'The crate is somewhere behind your stall there. Move along now -- I do not have all day.''There you are! Thank you, ${PLAYER} -- that customer was growing restless. I will get the order to her. I just need to find a bag....'Within the Barracks in Emax Dûl, the enemy has amassed equipment it can use for its army. We must seek out the equipment while it's vulnerable and destroy it.While fighting off any guards within, destroy any caches of spears and bows that you might find.Destroy bows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy spears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Mádathal the Deathward, the defender of the barracks.Defeat Mádathal the Deathward, the defender of the barracks'With Mádathal the Deathward defeated, and various weapons destroyed, you have helped our efforts within Emax Dûl. Thank you.'Girhâzi has decided it is time to go on the offensive and has ordered an assault on the Ordâkhai camp of Khetsok.Hamper the Ordâkhai efforts in Ambarûl by defeating soldiers and destroying their provisions in Khetsok.Defeat Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Ordâkhai provisions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Let us make our way back to Iridír.'You were tripped up by a sneaky hobbit in the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall event several times.You should try harder to avoid food stolen by the sneaky hobbit in the Hard Tack at Thorin's Hall event.Your mission is to sabotage siege engines that have been discovered in a nearby Ekhamâti camp and eliminate any soldiers that try and stop you.Your mission is to sabotage siege engines that have been discovered in a nearby Ekhamâti camp and eliminate any soldiers that try and stop you.Defeat Ekhamâti sorcerers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ekhamâti bowman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ekhamâti warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sabotage Ekhamâti catapults (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kósikul arrived to defend the camp! Defeat him!Defeat Kósikul'Great work destroying those siege engines. Let us return to Iridír.'Your mission is to travel north to Thalat Tîr to thin the numbers of vicious spiders in the area as well as bring back samples of their venom for the Sul Madásh scholars.Your mission is to travel north to Thalat Tîr to thin the numbers of vicious spiders in the area as well as bring back samples of their venom for the Sul Madásh scholars.Defeat spiders in Thalat Tîr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather venom (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to travel north to Thalat Tîr to thin the numbers of vicious spiders in the area as well as bring back samples of their venom for the Sul Madásh scholars.Defeat the blight-matron!'Fewer spiders around is good news for us all. You have done well to gather the venom needed. Return to Sul Madásh to the scholars so they can make good use of it.'The Blogmal clan are healers, understanding the way of fungus and poultices that close wounds. They also know the power of words inspirational and terrifying. Service to their clan is a boon to healers more than any other.You may seek the blessing of the Blogmal clan. All you need do is renounce all other clans.Speak with the Blogmal emissary'Why serve when you can collect debts? You will keep them upright and they will honour you for your efforts. Steel your nerve with the potent brew and serve our clan so that you may continue to serve.''Know the way of fungus of the fury that dwells in words. Of the fear that the words can inspire and the strength of insects in the eyes and ears of your enemy. Learn of the Blogmal. Serve the Blogmal.'The Temámir of Jiret-menêsh want to help the people who are being held prisoner by the Ordâkhai at Kôth Rau.Prisoners are held in cages throughout Kôth Rau. You should free them and defeat the Ordâkhai soldiers you encounter.Free prisoners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have freed the prisoners and defeated many soldiers of Ordâkh. You should return to Damudûr, the dark cleft at the base of the mountain.Return to the entrance of Damudûr at the mountain's baseYou have freed the prisoners and defeated many soldiers of Ordâkh, earning the attention of an Utûgi champion, Kulgath the Ruiner.Defeat Kulgath the Ruiner'Did you see how big that Orc was? It is good I got here in time to help you with him!

'Truly, I did. You were just too focused to notice. I do not fault you; you fought admirably. We should return to Jiret-menêsh with all haste, though. I do not wish to face another such Orc!'Bounder Boffin has his hands full with the rowdy party-going at the Farmers Faire.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>Party-goers can be found all over the Farmers Faire market area in Bywater during the festival.

You should accuse drunkards of drunken and disorderly behaviour to keep the party in line.Accuse drunkards of disorderly conduct (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Leave sober party-goers alone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bounder Boffin is in Bywater in the Shire.

You should speak with Bounder Boffin, and let him know that the party is under control.Speak with Bounder Boffin'${PLAYER}, hello! Are you keeping out of trouble at the Farmers Faire? Of course you are -- you wouldn't sink to the level of these dreadfully misbehaved party-goers.

'If you're looking for something to do, would you help me make rounds about the Faire? Some folk have had too much to drink, and must be reprimanded for bad behaviour and being a public nuisance!''Just, ah...keep watchful for signs of the disorderly conduct. The drunk ones should make their presence known sooner or later.''My thanks to you, ${PLAYER}; you are a great help! We Bounders are always a bit overworked. Why, I couldn't even take my afternoon nap yesterday!'Agatha Greendale wants you to collect the unopened letters that have recently been seen floating around the town. She believes that someone may be distributing them.Agatha Greendale has asked that you collect the letters being left along the streets of Bree and return them to her.Collect discarded letters from the streets of Bree (${NUMBER}/10)Having collected several discarded letters, you should return them to Agatha Greendale at the lodge at the end of road heading west from the South Gate of Bree.'I am glad that Graeme took my request seriously.

'We have been noticing a number of unopened letters being left along the thoroughfares throughout Bree. While letter carriers sometimes lose their post, the abundance of these letters and their appearance with the arrival of many drifters from the south and beyond gives us pause.

'We are busy with other matters, and had asked the Mayor to find someone to collect them for us. It appears you are the person for the job.'Agatha opens one of the letters and scans it quickly.

'Perhaps this is not a cause for concern after all. Still, better always to be safe and sure of matters such as these. The skies have grown darker as of late.

'Thank you, friend. I will ensure that Graeme is informed of your efforts.'Barliman Butterbur asks that you help clean up the city streets by clearing away any litter you may find strewn about.Barliman Butterbur has asked that you make your way through Bree-town looking for and removing any litter that you may find.Clean up all the litter you find around Bree-town (${NUMBER}/??)You have cleared up a good amount of litter around Bree. Return to Barliman Butterbur at the Prancing Pony and let him know of all you have done.Return to Barliman Butterbur at the Prancing Pony'Mayor Tenderlarch sent you, eh?

'Well this is auspicious. Just this morning I was ruminating with one of my regulars about these drifters milling about. They are good for a pint... or four, but their habits are of Wild Men, leaving all manner of dross strewn about the town streets.

'My constitutionals about the town have become an assault on my senses. It is good to see that Graeme asked for assistance.

'Since you offered, take a stroll of your own through the city, and clean up the litter you find.''I can tell by the grit under your nails that you have done an honest day's work. Fine work indeed. I will send a runner on to Graeme and let him know that I am pleased with your efforts. Thank you, friend.

'Keeping our town presentable is a community effort.'A local farmer outside Urmâkh has asked for help rounding up his escaped chickens.Speak with the farmer Mushêndu.Speak with the farmer MushênduRecover Mushêndu's escaped chickens.Recover the first escaped chickenRecover the second escaped chickenRecover the third escaped chickenRecover the fourth escaped chickenSpeak with Mushêndu outside the chicken pen.Speak with MushênduSpeak with Mushêndu outside the chicken pen.Speak with MushênduFind the scout.Find the scout'I'm glad you were able to help Mushêndu. I've been dispatched to bring you back to Urmâkh, there are other matters there that require your attention.''Thank you. Others talk of improving Urmâkh, but you're actually doing something about it. Thanks for your finding all my chickens and getting them back safely, it is quite a relief.''Hashtal-gûr, friend. I'm so glad they finally sent someone. These legs are not as spry and fresh as they once were. Hard to get up and down these hills. My chickens have escaped again. Only thing they seem to have a talent for. Juicier worms on the other side of the fence, must be. They are damned fools though, there are jackals that prowl these hills. Few things are as good a meal for those beasts as a chicken.

'Would you round them up before any harm can befall them?'Having met the emissaries of the clans, you must now make a decision. What clan shall you represent in the conflict of the Ettenmoors?The time has come to choose your clan allegiance. All you need do is speak with one of the emissaries and choose to represent them on the field of battle.Choose a clan and receive their blessing'This choice is an important one, for certain. But as the master has deemed, you can freely choose what clan you shall represent in the battle for a time.

'You should feel free to approach whichever tribe you choose without fear that you must always represent that clan. No, little worm, you can freely change your allegiances the same as you choose your diet for a day.'

She offers you a weak smile.

'Simply choose an emissary and accept their blessing. If you decide later that you dislike the benefits that their clan provides I am certain that they will abide by the master's law and allow you to freely choose your clan affiliation for now.

'Was that word too big for you? You seem to be staring at me more slack-jawed than usual. Perhaps, you should go make your choice.'The rot from Adagím is spreading. It threatens to bring blight to Kighân. Cut the restless trees down and burn the blight in the Moulder-grove.Defeat Huorns in the afflicted Moulder-grove and set aflame their saplings.Defeat Huorns in the Moulder-grove (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn strange saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat Totâkhri, the Rotted Root.Find and defeat Totâkhri, the Rotted Root'This grove makes me despair. I long for it to be lush and green again, may it return to health soon.'Complete Leaf-walkerComplete Side-stepComplete Perplexing RiddleComplete Long-distance FlingComplete Serious DemeanorComplete Make a MockeryComplete A Natural ExtensionComplete Strange DevicesComplete Spirited SongComplete the quest A Thief in the NightComplete Cruel OddsComplete Bleeding is BetterComplete the The Way of the MaelstromComplete The Way of the FulcrumComplete Lightning BladeComplete At Home on the WavesYour mission is to travel to Hordírid to the north-west to stop the dangerous Huorns and to cleanse the corrupted trees in the area.Your mission is to travel to Hordírid to the north-west to stop the dangerous Huorns and to cleanse the corrupted trees in the area.Cleanse corrupted trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Huorns in Hordírid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to travel to Hordírid to the north-west to stop the dangerous Huorns and to cleanse the corrupted trees in the area.Defeat the vicious Adagím Huorn'It saddens me that we must attack the forest in this way, but it must be done to slow the infection. You have done well. Let us return to Sul Madásh.'Your mission is to investigate the area where there have been many reports of brigands and put a stop to them and their leader, Ulâmul the Talon.Your mission is to investigate the area where there have been many reports of brigands and put a stop to them and their leader, Ulâmul the Talon.Discover attack locations (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat brigands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ulâmul the Talon has arrived. Defeat him!Defeat Ulâmul the Talon'You have done well, ${PLAYER}, to make these roads safe again by putting an end to the terrors Ulâmul the Talon and his companions have caused. Let us return to Iridír.'Many brazen hobbits have been well fed by your clumsy ineptitude. For this ignoble honour, you shall be known as a clod forever more.You should try much harder to avoid food stolen by the sneaky hobbit in the Hard Tack at Thorin's Hall event.The Combe lumberyard hosts a contest of strength, dexterity, and fortitude to help crown the winner of a coveted forester competition!You have chosen to compete in a competition to help determine the best forester in all of Chetwood - right now. Speak to the judge to let them know that you are ready to compete.Register for the competition with the judge<rgb=#FF0000>Failure: Fail to register with the judge</rgb>Now that you are registered for the event, you will need to wait at the Chetwood lumberyard for other competitors to join the event.Wait for others to register for the competitionAll the entrants are present and the judge is preparing to start the event. Wait for her to say 'go'.Wait for the judge to say goYou first need to collect an axe so that you can chop wood and then cure skins. Hurry now.Collect a forester's axe from the competition tableChetwood Forester Contest must not be recruitingLog piles along Old Bauman's hovel are set up for harvesting. Take your axe and collect five stacks of unrefined wood from the piles there.Collect stacks of unrefined wood (${NUMBER}/5)Chetwood Forester Contest must not be recruitingMake your way to the competition table beneath the tree in the centre of the camp and refine wood with the forester's axe.Chetwood Forester Contest must not be recruitingYou refined the wood, successfully. Now, collect hides from the bear carcasses behind Bauman's hovel.Collect unrefined skins from the bear carcasses behind Bauman's hovel (${NUMBER}/5)Chetwood Forester Contest must not be recruitingWith the skins collected, it is time to move on to the curing them. Make your way to the stone wall on the far side of the camp and cure skins at the hide stretchers.Chetwood Forester Contest must not be recruitingWith the hides completed, you now need to make your way to the bench beside the house and sample three brews from local taverns.Sample three beverages from local taverns (${NUMBER}/3)Chetwood Forester Contest must not be recruitingWith those tasty beverages consumed and sloshing in your stomach, the real test begins. Collect a caber.Collect a caber to carry for the eventChetwood Forester Contest must not be recruitingCarry the caber through the first set of markers in the Chetwood lumberyard.Pass through the first markersDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the second markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the third markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the fourth markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the fifth markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the sixth markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the seventh markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the eight markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the ninth markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the tenth markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the eleventh markers with the caberDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the next set of red markers.Pass through the twelfth markers with the cabersDo not drop the caberCarry the caber to the final blue markers to complete the race.Do not drop the caberReturn to the judge and speak to them about your efforts in the event.Return to the judge to claim your prize'Hullo there, have you come to compete in the contest?' 

Wilkin smiles broadly. 

'What contest, you ask? The one to determine who the finest forester in the Chetwood is, of course! Naturally, you will need have the forester profession to compete.' 

'Aldith and I thought it would be a fine way to settle the matter of who is best, seeing as how you foresters always seem to be arguing about such over a pint of ale. 

'To properly settle the matter with deeds instead of just boasts, it must be a contest of the strength, the dexterity, and even the fortitude of the competing foresters. And then there has to be prizes for the winners and those that compete, as would be expected. 

'If you think you are up to the challenge, or at least take a liking to the prizes, just tell me so! Then you will want to see Aldith to register, and in a short time we can get started.''We are very excited to offer these competitions. I am sure that my father and Old Bauman will see the merit in this idea. Thank you for thinking about participating.''Another contestant?

'It warms my heart to see so many seeking the noble profession of forestry. I have entered you in my log.'

She chuckles.

'Now, let's see who else wants to register. Stay close by, and I will let you know when it is time to begin.''Hmm, allow me a moment to look these over.'

She pauses.

'These are acceptable. Now, make your way behind my father's home and skin the bears there. When you have collected five skins go and tan them, then bring me the resulting items.''Yes, yes, it appears that you are at least nominally skilled with a skinning knife and hide stretcher. On to the next part of the competition: the feat of fortitude and strength!'

She flashes a broad smile.

'Sample beverages from the table beside my father's home and then collect a caber. Carry the caber through the red flags around the camp and finish at the blue flags!

'The first one through shall be declared the winner!''Well done, ${PLAYER}. I am very impressed with your prowess, and you should be, too. You are welcome to return any time and entertain the masses.''An effort for the ages, ${PLAYER}. We will remember your efforts here today and speak of them in this lumberyard for a good long time to come. Take this justly earned reward. You have made yourself and all foresters proud this day!'Due to extremely hot weather conditions at the summer festival, you have been asked to find a creative way to cool off the overheated patrons.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends.</rgb>A jug of water can be found near Tansy Tighfield at the Party Tree.

You should collect the jug of water.Collect the jug of cool waterOverheated patrons can be found throughout Hobbiton.

You should use the water creatively to help cool off overheated patrons.Tansy Tighfield can be found at the party tree in Hobbiton.

You should speak with Tansy Tighfield.Return to Tansy Tighfield'This is a mighty hot summer, ${PLAYER}. Many of the patrons don't seem to be enjoying the festival as much this year, due to this miserable heat.

'Can you think of a way to cool them off? If only we had a fountain in Hobbiton!''You... you spit on the patrons? That certainly wasn't what I had in mind. Though if they seemed to enjoy it, I guess it'll do! Thank you, I think.'Cinaid wants you to visit a humiliated Uruk in Grothum. His hope is that the Uruk will find a way to help your sapling. Go to him and ask for his guidance.Make your way to Grothum and speak with Taskmaster Bárzqhosh. Ask him for his design for making your sapling grow.Speak with Bárzqhosh at Grothum for adviceBárzqhosh provided a very strange answer. Go to the plains along the Hoardale where the Thistledown Grazers roam and collect their dung. Use it in the soil to grow your sapling.'In Grothum, seek out Taskmaster Bárzqhosh. His recent failure can be amended by allowing him to find another solution to our development of your sapling. Ask him for his design for making your creature grow.''Go to the plains where the Thistledown Grazes roam. Gather their scat. Crops grow well when fed, and the soil enriched by aurochs droppings grows best.''What is this? Surely, this is some kind of joke. Does Bárzqhosh expect us to farm like the Hill-men?

'Oh, no. Now I understand.'

Cinaid laughs.

'It is a joke. A well-played joke by the Taskmaster. He has some wit.'Goblins are natural allies of the forces of Angmar. The encampment of Grothum far to the north-east, houses such goblins. Go there and ask what you can do to assist.Make your way to Grothum and speak with the leader Bok to learn how the goblins would go about perverting the natural order that would grow this sapling.Speak with Bok at GrothumGo into the Ettenmoors and hunt down any of the Free Folk guards there. They will likely carry oil that can be used to poison the roots of the sapling. Replace water with oil and watch the sapling become rancid.'We have our methods for corrupting and the goblins have theirs. Let us ask their leader at Grothum for assistance. Go to Bok, and ask him how they would befoul a creature of nature. I am certain that there is some nefarious means that the goblin leader will devise.''A sapling will grow into a vindictive tree if you poison its roots... oil!

'You will find that the Free People carry it on them. Find them. Kill them. Get their oil and soak the roots of the sapling. The flesh of the tree will grow putrid. Poison will course through its veins.

'It will be a creature of ruin, and you will be its master.''Nefarious... cunning... there is much to like of the twisted minds possessed by the goblins. It is good they are our allies.'Cinaid is unsure that they can help, but he wants to find some dark humour in the development of your sapling. He directed you to seek out the assistance of trolls.Make your way to Grothum and ask Tyrant Bûrzgoth for guidance on how to corrupt the sapling.Speak with Tyrant Bûrzgoth at GrothumBûrzgoth suggested killing bears for their haunches and feeding them to your to your sapling... not a terrible idea from a troll.Collect Morningthaw haunches (${NUMBER}/7)Bûrzgoth suggested killing bears for their haunches and feeding them to your to your sapling... not a terrible idea from a troll.'Time for fun. Seek out Tyrant Bûrzgoth at Grothum and ask the troll how it would corrupt a sapling. This should be amusing.''Bears.

'Haunches.

'Feed. Make enemy.

'Take to Cinaid.''Bûrzgoth suggested this? Maybe I misjudged the troll's capacity for thought and reason.

'This will serve us well, indeed.'Cinaid learned from scouts that the Free People are attempting to get clean water from the Hoardale River. He assumes that this is to feed saplings that they discovered. His orders are clear, befoul the river!Cinaid sent you into the Ettenmoors to target locations along the Hoardale where the Free Folk are looking to collect pure water. You are to befoul the water with poison to thwart the Free People's designs.The water is poisoned and any collected here will surely not assist in the pure growth of anything that it feeds. Return to Cinaid at Gramsfoot and tell him of your success.'Our scouts see them at the river-banks of the Hoardale. My scouts see them in the day and in the night. We shall counter their attempts to breed a wholesome thing and poison the water they seek to use.'

He grins an evil grin.

'Take this and disperse it into the water along the banks where I have marked them.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. I shall see that you are commended for these efforts. If we cannot breach the walls of the enemy fortress to claim what saplings they discovered, then we shall destroy them with their own efforts to grow and cultivate this flora.'Cinaid ordered you to find dwarves, cut their beards from their chins and return them to him to feed to your sapling.Cinaid directed you to collect dwarf-beards to use in creating a painful growth process for your sapling so that it will learn the scent of the dwarf and associate it with the pain of its adolescent growth.'Dwarf beards lack flesh that will feed, but the coarse hair can be used to twist and deform your sapling, making the creature suffer at the hands of the bearded creatures. They will come to know the smell of the enemy and associate their painful growth with dwarf-kind. Its animosity will grow and further its corrupt spirit. It will be poisoned against another of the Free Peoples... all due to your contributions.''These will do nicely. Look how thick the hair is. It shall bind the limbs and twist the heart of this little creature. It shall be pliable to our whims and machination. We will make it ours.'Cinaid wants you to eliminate creatures of nature that the Free People have suddenly found an interest in so they are deprived of whatever material the creatures possess.Cinaid suggested you go to Hithlad and destroy creatures of nature there. Slaughter potential would-be allies to your sapling.Slaughter Leafcull bog-lurkers (${NUMBER}/10)With the lurkers defeated, you should return to Cinaid and tell them of your efforts.Speak with Cinaid at Gramsfoot'Neglect your sapling this day. Instead focus on the creatures that would be its ally. The lurkers on the woods of Hithlad. Hunt them and eradicate them.''You will see the wisdom in this attack. The natural order must be broken wherever it attempts to assert itself.'Cinaid identified the Free People attempting to acquire something from the cave-claws native to the Ettenmoors. He wants you to stop their ability to collect anything from them.Make your way into the Isendeep Mine or Arador's End and decimate the cave-claws there.Kill Frostfell cave-claws (${NUMBER}/10)Now that the cave-claws are defeated, return to Cinaid at Gramsfoot.Speak with Cinaid at Gramsfoot'Cave-claws are drawing the attention of the Free-folk. We do not know why, but if they want them we should deny them access. Go into the Isendeep or Arador's End and deny the Free People that which they covet.''You have done well in denying the free people access to their desires. We shall fight them at every turn. They do so deserve to fall.'Cinaid identified another new target of the Free People and desires that you stop them from being able to collect the bounties that they need.Make your way to the waters surrounding Tol Ascarnen and kill the nerbyg present to ensure that their natural presence is diminished and cannot call to your sapling.Kill nerbyg near Tol Ascarnen (${NUMBER}/10)Now that the nerbyg he wanted dead are removed, return to Cinaid at Gramsfoot and inform them of the news.Speak with Cinaid at Gramsfoot'The nerbyg dwelling around Tol Ascarnen are a natural ally of the sapling, or so we think. Let us thin their number and ensure that they can never ally with your new pet. As an additional bonus, it seems that the Free People also have an interest in these creatures. Denying them what they need is always a benefit.''You have done well. The Free People are stopped. This will be rewarded.'To corrupt the sapling, the Angmarim leadership devises a terrible way to nurture a bloodlust within the sapling.Cinaid asked you to collect legs of men to mash into the soil that feeds your sapling. Getting the taste for the blood of Men will defile the sapling.'Let us provide the right impetus for corruption. Legs of the Free Men will prove a potent mash to force through the soil. Go into the Ettenmoors and claim men. Slaughter them and acquire their legs so that we may mash them into the soil and feed the roots of the sapling from their blood.''You are commended. We will grind these legs into meat that will mix with the soil and feed the sapling. It will grow fond of the taste and become a potent ally.'Your discovery of this small sapling intrigues leadership. Something about this little creature drives a sinister desire in the Angmarim. You have been instructed to speak with others who may understand what you found.Make your way to Dâr-gazag and speak with corruptor Gavran. Ask them about corrupting the sapling you discovered.Speak with Gavran at Dâr-gazagReturn to Gramsfoot and find the Corruptor, Cinaid. They will tutor you in the best manner to despoil the sapling you found.'What have you found?'

The Angmarim looks the sapling over.

'This appears sentient. Perhaps more sentient than you.

'It certainly is aware that we are here and that is odd for a plant. Not unheard of, of course. There are agents of our Lord everywhere.

'It seems that you have stumbled upon a unique gift. You will be responsible for its malevolent growth.

'For now, speak with the other Angmarim who are here in the Ettenmoors for more advice on how to twist this creature's heart.''This is a good find, ${PLAYER}. We can easily warp this little thing to our whims, desires, and goals.'

Gavran grins evilly.

'You are charged with overseeing its fall to fell corruption. Return to Gramsfoot and speak with Cinaid so that he may provide you with better direction on how to distort this creature.''This specimen would entice the leaders in Sant Lhoer from their work. Fortune smiles, then, that I am here to guide you in the corrupting of such a fine creature. We will work together to turn this creature to the shadow.'Cinaid orders you to collect the ears of Elves to broaden the bloodthirst that your sapling will have.Cinaid directed you to slaughter Elves in the Ettenmoors and carve off their ears so that the strips can be added to the soil that feeds your sapling.'Go into the Ettenmoors and slaughter Elves. Carve the ears from their skulls and return them to me so that I can flay them into strips that will be used to fertilize the soil for growing your sapling. In time, the sapling will learn to covet the flavour of an Elf.''Your work is efficient and cruel. The malice with which you carry out your tasks will transfer to your sapling, and you will breed it into a vile creature that is sworn to our host.'Cinaid knows that the eagles to the east are defenders of the land and friends to nature. To make them a natural enemy for your sapling will be a great boon.Head to the east, in the shadow of the mountain that houses the Isendeep Mine, and hunt the eagles there for their feathers.'To the east, in the shadow of the Isendeep Mine, there are eagles that soar and defend the land.

'There, where Arador fell, you should travel and gather the feathers of those terrible creatures. We will use the quills as lances to stab the flesh of your sapling. It will learn that the feathers cause it pain and animosity will seep into its heart. In time, it will learn to attack the eagles and their allies on sight.''We shall use these quills to stab your pet, drive it mad and cause it pain so that it knows who the enemy is.'Cinaid knows that the taste of little folk flesh will further madden your sapling. He orders you to make your way to Hoarhallow to collect toes to feed your sapling.Make your way south to Hoarhallow and gather toes from the Little Folk there that you may feed the succulent flesh to your sapling.Collect hobbit-feet (${NUMBER}/7)Deliver the delectable feet to Cinaid at Gramsfoot.'Let us talk of the Little Folk of Hoarhallow a moment. Have you tasted their flesh? I have. It is succulent. When we gather their toes and grind them into pulp we will mix the flesh into the soil of your sapling and like all the other Free Folk, the sapling will know their taste. It will learn that their flesh is its sustenance and it will hunt them with impunity. Think of that, ${PLAYER}.''Plump and...'

Cinaid licks a severed toe.

'Delicious. Your sapling will appreciate this gift.'The Ordâkhai launched an attack, capturing the floating bridge at Wrackwade. The Dumûri have asked for your help to overcome their defenders and regain possession of the river-crossing.As you secure sections of the Wrackwade, raise Ambarûli banners to lay claim to them.Raise Ambarûli banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have reclaimed the span of the Wrackwade in the name of Ambarûl, and now the Ordâkhai have put forth their champion to challenge you. You should defeat their champion.Defeat Obonákh'It is always a joy to watch you fight. We appreciate what you have done for us this day. Come, let us return to Iridír.'Many kites have crash-landed all over Hobbiton, and must be picked up.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends.</rgb>Crashed kites can be found throughout Hobbiton.

You should collect the crashed kites so that other festival patrons may enjoy them.Recover crashed kites (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lila Roper can be found at the party tree in Hobbiton.

You should bring Lila Roper the crashed kites.Bring the crashed kites to Lila Roper‘The kites are a delightful addition to the Festival, but there have been a number of incidents of crashes. It seems that folks aren't terribly deft at kite-flying in these parts.

'Would you be so good as to search Hobbiton for crashed kites and return them to me?’'Thank you! It would have been such a shame if these went missing. Now more patrons can enjoy them during the Lithe Days!'Faranil admits that all her tireless work and study has given her little insight into the true nature of the sapling you discovered. She believes that it is time to seek aid outside of the Ettenmoors.Faranil directed you to tell the tale of how you discovered and claimed the sapling to Elrond at the Last Homely House in Rivendell. She hopes that the Lord of Rivendell may know something of the sapling you found.Speak with Elrond at the Last Homely HouseElrond could no more explain your discovery of the sapling than could Faranil. He insisted that you continue your efforts. He believes that you may be working toward healing the Ettenmoors in some fashion.Return to Faranil at Glân Vraig with your news'My friend. We have worked tirelessly for quite some time, and sadly, I must admit that with all of my knowledge I am left with as many questions as I have answers.'

Faranil looks at the pot where the sapling grows.

'We know that the sapling is native here to the Ettenmoors and that the land itself is helping it become strong. I am still loath to bring soil from elsewhere to nurture the sapling because I do not know enough. But I am limited in my knowledge and I think it is time to reach beyond these lands into the halls of my home at Rivendell.

'Elrond knows much of our history and stores more of it within the libraries of the Last Homely House. Please, take your tale to him and learn what he might know and then return to me.'Elrond listens to your tale intently. Then he looks about him and when he speaks, it is as if he conjures the very trees that surround Rivendell.

'Your tale, friend, is one of interest and wonder. A sapling that stirs at your passage is a thing of which I have not heard since the Great Forest covered nearly all of Middle-earth. It is a rare thing these days. This portent and your involvement in it, must have greater meaning than any have yet discovered.'

Elrond pauses and then shakes his head.

'Yet, friend, there is nothing more I can offer you or the patron who assists you in the Ettenmoors.'

Sensing your disappointment, he continues.

'Do not despair.

'This is a good omen. Perhaps the land is healing, though the battle still persists. Go with that knowledge, and the hope that the tomorrow you make for the sapling you have found will be one of bright light.''I hoped that we would learn more, but Elrond is correct.'

She stiffens and smiles.

'We should not despair.

'Your discovery does have meaning, even if we have not yet determined what that meaning is.

'Onward friend.'Faranil wants to unlock the mysteries of the sapling and believes that there might be one in the Lone-lands who knows something. His name is Radagast, and as a guardian of nature this does seem to be something of which he might know a thing or two.Faranil, seeking more information on the sapling that you are raising, directed you to Ost Guruth, an outpost in the Lone-lands, where Radagast the Brown has been seen. She bid you visit him and share your tale of discovering and nurturing the sapling.Speak with Radagast at Ost GuruthRadagast suggested that you are helping to grow a noble creatures by your efforts and advised that you should continue on the path that you are set upon.'Your continued efforts should not be empty. My frustration with my own limitations grows, but I believe that there is one to whom we can turn for assistance.'

She offers a light tilt of her head.

'Last I heard, Radagast the Brown, who is a staunch ally of nature, is in a tower in the Lone-lands within a settlement called Ost Guruth.

'I would have you visit him to explain your find and our actions thus far. He might provide his insight to us.

'Perhaps this master of the natural world can explain what it is that we are seeing.'Radagast nods his head when your tale is done.

'I know of what you speak, the woodland is home to many such oddities. Oddities, no, that is the wrong word. Wonders. That is the word. Wonders that should be celebrated.

'You found a child. You are nurturing the child. I cannot say what the child will become, but it is clear that you discovered something that recognized, in you, a purity which it sought. So, it signaled to you, and you responded. A noble thing. A wondrous thing.

'You must continue your effort and know that your influence over the sapling will only grow. What you do for your newly found progeny will help it grow into a noble creature. It will not do so on its own. Too often the corruption of the land seeps through the roots and spoils the good in such things.

'I recall, in a swamp, far from here.... well, not so far, but far enough that I cannot simply walk there now, there was such a creature poisoned, corrupted, withered from its true purpose by a vileness that pervaded all that surrounded it. I wondered. "What would you become were you not so befouled?" It could not answer, of course, given how forsaken it was from nature. But, I hoped it would say a splendid creature that would give as it had received.

'Alas, it was not to be. You have another choice, ${PLAYER}. Do not spoil it. See your effort through and remain as true to the end as you were at the start.''I am in awe at this insight. Could it be that he speaks of the huorns? Have you rescued a sapling huorn? I agree with the Brown Wizard, friend. We should keep the path.'Faranil believes that something has changed with the sapling and it is time to look for another piece of guidance. She bids you visit the Old Forest and speak to the River-maid who dwells there. Her name is Goldberry.Faranil carefully packed the young sapling into a pot and gave it to you with instructions to take the sapling into the Old Forest to speak with the River-maiden Goldberry.Speak with Goldberry at her spring in the Old ForestGoldberry directed your to meet with her again at Tom Bombadil's house deep within the Old Forest.Speak with Tom Bombadil at his home in the Old ForestTom hinted that you need bring the sapling to visit Old Man Willow, as something there will help the sapling grow into what it is meant to be.Nurture your sapling at Old Man WillowHaving done all you were told it is now time to return the sapling to Faranil in the Ettenmoors as Tom suggested.'Our efforts yield results, my friend. The sapling stirred. I believe it sprouted another leaf.

'Yet, I fear that my understanding of how this came to be and what it might yet become is limited. I think it is time that we seek the assistance of another who may know more of what this is.'

Faranil pauses.

'In the Old Forest, it is said, there is a woman known as a River Daughter. Her name, as I know it, is Goldberry.'

Faranil picks up the sapling and hands it to you in a well-packed pot.

'Here, friend. Take the sapling into the Old Forest and seek Goldberry at her spring. Ask her if she knows anything about the little sapling.'Goldberry smiles after hearing your tale.

'It is a wonder what you have discovered.

'The Wizard is correct. You are bound to this little creature in the same way that my Spring is tied to the Old Forest.'

She looks at the sapling with curiosity.

'I see that it struggles to grow as swiftly as it desires. Not because it is corrupt or poisoned, you have seen that it would not suffer such a fate.

'No, it is in need of a succor that it likely cannot get in the harsh climes of the Ettenmoors. It is good that you came to me, ${PLAYER}.

'I do know how to help, but we have need to speak with Tom before you tread where you must. Meet at our home, deep within this wood.''Hey Dol Derry Dol! You seek a gift.

'Not for you. For the child you carry on your being.'

Tom winks and chuckles.

'I tell you now that the gift you need comes from the Old Man most foul and mean. He will lull you to sleep if you linger too long... but linger you must!

'Linger there to further the trust and the bond, between the two of you who are so close.

'For the food of the forest that the Willow consumes is the same that will aid in the growth of your little child.

'Do not tarry long, lest the Old Man's will bring low the joy that your child has within!''Be one your way. Your cause is a noble one.''Something is different. I can see it in the bark and the leaves. I trust that the River-maiden led you where you needed to be. Now, all we can do is all we have been doing, friend. Let us continue with our efforts.'Faranil has pieced together enough understanding to send you to a friend who she believes will see the sapling in a completely different light and understanding.Faranil believes that it is time to speak with the Ent, Quickbough, about the sapling you have found. Though she knows the risk is that she will give the Ent false hope with this discovery.Travel to Evendim and seek out QuickboughYou spoke with Quickbough and it seems the Ent is given a new hope with your sapling. Return to the Ettenmoors and Faranil to tell them what occurred.'There is something happening with the sapling, I think, friend. There is someone else with whom we must speak.'

Faranil looks somewhat melancholy.

'Seeking them out is a step that I must admit, I fear. Their sorrow is the sorrow of their entire kind.

'I only hope that they understand that this is not a sign of anything more than a new hope. I can only hope that we will give them a different type of hope and not a measure of false one.

'In a copse of trees, on the far side of Lake Evendim there is an Ent named Quickbough. Go to them. Tell them what you have found and all that we have learned.'Quickbough stares, for what seems like several minutes, at the sapling. Suddenly, the sapling wiggles and Quickbough's eyes go wide.

'Hroom, throom, shoom.

'Not an Enting, no.

'Still... we will weep for the loss we suffer.

'But this... hroom...

'This little one... is... hope for a future...

'And you... throom... thrumm... humm...

'Have... made this... possible...'

You are not sure, but it appears that Quickbough's eye well with tears.

'Thank you... little one.

'Thrumm....''The Ents suffer a heavy loss. A sadness for what they have lost. Perhaps, this gift you discovered is a gift of a different kind. Perhaps it is the last gift left for the Ents. A hope that when they slumber at last their world will persist, though different. ${PLAYER}, you are doing much to heal our world. We are indebted to you.'After the second downfall of Angmar, the Witch-king of Angmar's realm of old was left all but abandoned. Alas, the remnants of the Iron Crown have crept forth from the shadows and returned to the fortress-city of Carn Dûm, seeking to wield a lost artifact of the Witch-king of Angmar to seize dominion over the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.After the second downfall of Angmar, the Witch-king of Angmar's realm of old was left all but abandoned. Alas, the remnants of the Iron Crown have crept forth from the shadows and returned to the fortress-city of Carn Dûm, seeking to wield a lost artifact of the Witch-king of Angmar to seize dominion over the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.Complete 'Deeds of Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens'Complete 'Deeds of Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary'Complete 'Deeds of Sagroth, Lair of Vermin'Complete 'Deeds of Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel'So returned the Nazgûl, and with their coming the Dark Lord’s power grew. Sauron unveiled his might through their dreadful voices, which cried words of wrath and terror. Even the boldest quailed and cowered as the Wraiths passed – or yet stood unmoving, their weapons falling from hands gone cold as they yielded to thoughts of darkness, fear, and death.Defeat the Grim SouthronDefeat the Forsaken ReaverDefeat the Gloom of NurnDefeat the Black Blade of LebenninDefeat the Bane of RhûnDefeat the High Sorcerer of HaradDefeat the Woe of KhandDefeat the Cursed RiderDefeat the Witch-kingOnce he was a great king in lands far to the east, accustomed to rule and unwilling to bend the knee to any other. But then came a giver of gifts and a promiser of power, and upon accepting these lures, the great king changed. No longer did he rule his lands with mercy, and neither did he remain in his own kingdom. He became Rhûn's bane, and by that name came he to be known as the Bane of Rhûn, and elsewhere.Defeat the Bane of RhûnIn later days, the Black Blade of Lebennin was oft-seen stalking among the hills and forests of Western Gondor, striking fear into the hearts of Men with both deadly countenance and fearsome sword. For those few who did not flee, his words poured like honey into their unwilling ears and drove them to terrible acts of evil. This may have proved his worst and most effective weapon.Defeat the Black Blade of LebenninHe moved at speed across the battlefield, running down the warriors who dared stand against him, fewer as the siege went on. He was the Cursed Rider, and the sound of his approach turned even courageous blood to water. In later years he would command armies from within the walls of Dol Guldur, but during the Second Age he preferred to fight from the back of his black steed, alone.Defeat the Cursed RiderFrom the distant south he came, bringing fear and fire to every coast he spied with his glass. His was a reign of blood, and he drew it from all who lived in sight and scent of the Sea. Was that the reason Sauron gave to him the ring Khânto, which is Pain-giver? With the power of it, the Forsaken Reaver could not be stopped, and his laughter carried inland on fell winds; he was among Sauron's swiftest servants, and the cruelest.Defeat the Forsaken ReaverNone can say what ship bore him hither to Middle-earth before Númenor was lost, but once he accepted Sauron's gift he could no longer be counted among the Men of that land. He dwelt in Thaurband, a fortress in southern Mordor, not far from the inland Sea. It was from that keep that the fear of him spread, giving him a new title to replace the name he no longer needed. He became the Gloom of Núrn, though he did not stay there, and roved far and wide at Sauron's command.Defeat the Gloom of NurnFew among the living ever heard him speak, but his visage was well-known, and feared. They called him the Grim Southron, and while Men quailed at his approach during the Second Age, during the Third the legend of his malice had only grown. In later days it was he that Lhaereth the Stained followed in secret to Dol Guldur, where she discovered Sauron and helped him recover, for a price. Did the Dark Lord deal out reward or punishment for his Nazgûl's lapse? But that was much later. During the Second Age, the Grim Southron was known only to be patient, loyal, and silent.Defeat the Grim SouthronA number of Summer Festival patrons are suffering in the intense summer heat.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>Heat Waves can be found in the area near the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should defeat Heat Waves.Defeat heat waves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tansy Tighfield is at the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should return to Tansy Tighfield.Speak with Tansy Tighfield'Oh dear. It is terribly hot today, is it not? I worry that the good patrons of the festival will succumb to the heat! Would you be so kind as to banish any bursts of heat that you see hanging around? The warmth is too much to endure.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! I can feel the drop in the heat already. I am sure I shall receive fewer complaints now.'They called him the High Sorcerer of Harad, but for most of those who fought against Sauron it was just a name. He rarely left the dungeon fastnesses of Mordor, for he delighted in the working of foul rituals and the mastery of fell magic, and gave his thought to little else. But when the Dark Lord saw fit to send him forth, Men and Elves knew to give him a wide berth, or suffer. It was Mêbat he wore, the Mirth-eater, and wherever he went there was an end to laughter, and only the onset of grief.Defeat the High Sorcerer of HaradGreatest and most feared of the Nine, the Witch-king stalked the battlefield but rarely, leaving the fortresses of Mordor only at Sauron's most pressing command. In later years the Lord of the Nazgûl would raise from nothing the Land of Angmar, wielding it in furtherance of the Dark Lord's aim to destroy the northern kingdom of Arnor, but at the close of the Second Age that was still far off in the mists of Time. During the Siege of Barad-dûr, the Witch-king could be found testing the weaknesses of the armies arrayed against his master, seeking the most valuable prize of all: information.Defeat the Witch-kingHe was the Woe of Khand, and with the blessing of Sauron he strode across the unconquered lands and claimed them for the Dark Lord. The ring gifted to him was called Adâsh, and many were the foes it made, many the proud warriors he brought low. He found great joy in the bringing of war, and always had done so, but with the power given to him by Sauron, the Woe of Khand became ever more deadly, more relentless, and more unforgiving.Defeat the Woe of KhandYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell, and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.Your mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.Speak with ArvunathYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.Defend Arvunath from the attacking OrcsYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.Defend Arvunath from the attacking OrcsYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.Defend Arvunath from the attacking OrcsYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.Defend Arvunath from the attacking Orcs'Arvunath is safe thanks to you, ${CLASS}. She can continue her research in peace for now.'Collect materials from the wilds of the Ettenmoors. Your forces will construct a door that will seal the upper level off from the enemy.Head into the Ettenmoors and collect the materials that are needed to construct a door that will seal the upper levels of Lugazag away from the enemy.'Listen here! We may have taken the tower, but the Free People are relentless. They will return, and we best defend the top of the tower so that we can hold this location. Get out into the wilds and get me the materials that I need to build a sturdy gate that will keep them Free Peoples out!''I am almost impressed. Now, the fun begins. I will see that the door is built and we will slaughter the free folk here at the pinnacle of Lugazag!'Orders are to collect items from around the Ettenmoors so that a gate can be constructed to keep the Free People out of Lugazag. Best get to it.Head out into the Ettenmoors and collect the materials needed to construct the gate that will seal the front of Lugazag tower.'Do you think I am going to return to Gramsfoot without having done all I can to defend this tower? No! I need you to go get the material we need to seal up the front of this tower and keep those Free People from breaching!''Quick work and efficient too. I will make sure to report that to the War-tyrant. No, I don't need your name.'You are ordered to acquire materials needed to build a gate that will defend the exterior of Tírith Rhaw.Make your way into the wilds of the Ettenmoors and collect the materials needed to construct the external gate.'We cannot rest with simply taking this tower. We must defend it. So get your scrawny arse out into the wild and get the materials we need to build a gate to keep the Free People out of the tower!''Well, well, seems we do have some maggots what is good at taking orders. You shall avoid the lash for this effort. But, don't think that this makes you anything more than a maggot, maggot.'Now that you have control of the tower of Lugazag, you must build a door to defend the exterior of the tower.Collect materials to build a gate to seal off the entrance of Lugazag. All the materials needed can be found in the wilds of the Ettenmoors.'Capturing this tower is a great accomplishment, but we will lose it if we do not post a defence. Go into the Ettenmoors and gather materials so that we may build a gate to stop the enemy from entering the tower.''This will strengthen our position and slow the enemy from taking this tower again. We will construct the gate immediately.

'Thank you for your assistance.'Now that you have control of the tower of Tírith Rhaw, you must build a door to defend the exterior of the tower.Collect materials to build a gate to seal off the entrance of Tírith Rhaw. All the materials needed can be found in the wilds of the Ettenmoors.'We have captured Tírith Rhaw and now must see to its defence. If you provide the materials, we can build the front gate quickly and deter the enemy from advancing within the tower. Make haste ${PLAYER}, lest the enemy return and drive us out too quickly.''We will put these materials to good use. The gate will hold against the enemy and we shall redouble efforts to strengthen it further.

'Thank you for your assistance.'It has been strongly recommended that you acquire materials needed to build a gate that will defend the interior of Tiriíth Rhaw.Make your way into the wilds of the Ettenmoors and collect the materials needed to construct the internal gate.'The tower is ours! Those Free People will take it back unless we act. Get out into the wilds and get what we need to build a door to seal off the top of the tower. Then we can slaughter the Free Folk at our own pace.''Impressive, maggot. It looks as though you really want to advance in our army. Good work. Don't rest though, the Free People will return.'Collect materials to build a gate that will prevent the enemy from breaching the upper level at the tower of Lugazag.Collect materials to build a door that will defend the upper level of Lugazag. All the materials needed can be found in the wilds of the Ettenmoors.'We cannot rest. The enemy will return to take the tower and we must defend the upper levels. Make your way into the Ettenmoors and collect the materials needed to construct the interior door.''These are good materials and will build a sturdy gate. We will put these to use immediately.

'Thank you.'Now that you have control of the tower of Tírith Rhaw, you must build a door to defend the upper level of the tower.Collect materials to build a gate to seal off the upper level of Tírith Rhaw. All the materials needed can be found in the wilds of the Ettenmoors.'We have captured Tírith Rhaw. Let us not rest here. Let us build a defence at the entry to the tower's heart so we might stop the enemy advance. For this, I will need items gathered from here in the Ettenmoors. Should you collect these and return them to me, I will see the gate is built.''This is enough to craft a sturdy door. We will set about building the door as quickly as we can.

'Thank you for your assistance.'You are directed back into the wilds of the Ettenmoors to collect material needed to reinforce the gate at Lugazag.Head into the Ettenmoors and collect the materials that are needed to reinforce the gate at Lugazag.'You done good so far. The enemy is foolish enough to keep throwing bodies at the walls and the gate. If we do not reinforce the gate, they may break through. That would make the war-tyrant angry. We do not want the war-tyrant angry, yes?

'So you are going back out into the wilderness to get more of what we need to make the gate sturdy. Sturdy like the war-tyrant himself. Got it?

'Go!''You did good following the request I made. Now I will hold up my end of the bargain and strengthen the gate. We will hold this tower away from the enemy!'You are directed back into the wilds of the Ettenmoors to collect material needed to reinforce the gate at Tírith Rhaw.Head into the Ettenmoors and collect the materials that are needed to reinforce the gate at Tírith Rhaw.'Listen up, whelp! The Free People will not relent. They will return with rams and forces to retake this tower. We must be prepared.

'Go back into the wilds and get more material to reinforce the gate we have built. We will not let this tower fall back into the hands of the enemy!''Good work. With this we can make the gate stronger. It will not survive forever, but we stand a better chance because of your effort.

'Take this, you deserve it.'With Lugazag captured and the gate built, you are asked to turn your attention to upgrading the gate for greater defence.Help to further reinforce the stronghold at Lugazag by collecting materials to reinforce the gate. You will find all you need throughout the Ettenmoors.'We have done well to capture the tower of Lugazag and built a gate to defend the location, but the enemy is relentless and will return. To strengthen our position we must do what we can to reinforce the gate.

'Make your way back into the wilds of the Ettenmoors, collect the wood and iron we need to reinforce the gate here.''I will see that the door is reinforced with this delivery. We will hold this location and press our advantage here in the Ettenmoors.

'Thank you for your continued efforts in this harsh land.'With Tírith Rhaw captured and the gate built, you are asked to turn your attention to upgrading the gate for greater defence.Help to further reinforce the stronghold at Tírith Rhaw by collecting materials to reinforce the gate. You will find all you need throughout the Ettenmoors.'We will hold this tower, though the effort will not be easy. You have done well to help construct the gate here at Tírith Rhaw, but we must reinforce the gate.

'Make your way back into the wilds of the Ettenmoors, collect the wood and iron we need to reinforce the gate here.''Yes, this delivery will help us to strengthen the gate below. You are to be commended for your further assistance to us in this war effort in the Ettenmoors.'Orcs drive south along a tributary to the south of Maurûsh along the river. They intend to poison it, and you must stop them.Your mission is to travel to the river near Maurûsh and stop the Orcs there from poisoning the tributary.Destroy poison spreaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'You have saved the river from being poisoned by the Orcs. We should return to Ub Nishir.'A posting from Tavu, an ally in the village of Galtrev in Dunland, requesting assistance with making deliveries throughout the town.Find your way to Galtrev and seek out Tavu. There is something that they need done, but the cryptic posting did not explain what that was.Speak with Tavu in the village of GaltrevCollect spears from the smith's pavilion near the lowest entrance of Galtrev and deliver them to the upper training ground.Collect and deliver the spears to the upper training ground in GaltrevCollect the swords from the upper training grounds of Galtrev and deliver them to the smith's pavilion at the lowest entrance.Collect the swords and deliver them to the smith's pavilionWith all the deliveries completed, return to Tavu in Galtrev and let him know the work is done.Return to Tavu in Galtrev with news of your successPost:

Plea for assistance. Report to me at Galtrev to offer your services.

- Tavu'I am grateful that you answered my request, and I owe you an apology for its rather cryptic nature. Had I openly declared, "I require aid in carrying weapons to be sharpened and replaced," I fear few would have troubled themselves to answer.

'Our numbers grow with each passing day as we prepare for the battles ahead. Yet our recruits are rightly occupied with their training, and the more humble work of carrying dulled blades down to the smiths remains undone. Our children are not yet strong enough to bear the weight of the barrels, and so we must look to others for aid.

'But you are here now, and the task should not take long.''We are most pleased that you have lent us your aid. Though the work may seem small, do not think it without worth. The aid you provided will be felt when our blades meet the enemy upon the field of battle.

'Small deeds may serve great purposes, friend.

'You have our thanks.'Gaergoth's misguided followers must be purged in order to re-establish control for Mordirith. Descend into the depths, put a whipping on these misguided heretics and bring them back into line.Uglash wants you to descend into The Delving of Frór to teach the misguided forces back under the control of Mordirith and Angmar.Defeat the neutral enemies in The Delving of Frór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You reminded the forces patrolling the depths of The Delving of Frór who the real master of Angmar is, whether the lesson will take or not is unknown. You should return to Uglash and let him know of your efforts.Return to Uglash and inform him of your efforts'There are those that know how to follow orders and those that gets confused when they are being yelled at by something bigger than them. Seems the things dwelling in the dark of The Delving of Frór have forgotten who stands at the top of the chain of command. Mordirith speaks for us here in the north.

'We would do well to remind the things in those depths that they should be following him. Right?''You done as I told you. If they are foolish enough to deny their ruler we will keep up the beatings until they come back to heel.

'For now, you deserve something for your effort.'The minions in The Delving of Frór are too numerous and appear to grow with every passing moment. Captain-General Tordúr has asked that you help to cull the denizens of the deep.Tordúr has asked that you venture into The Delving of Frór to cull the growing horde that assembles beneath Gaergoth's banner.Defeat the neutral enemies in The Delving of Frór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You culled the forces loyal to Gaergoth within The Delving of Frór. You should return to the Captain-General within the safety of Glân Vraig.Return to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig'Too many foes roam through The Delving of Frór, and they continue to flock to Gaergoth's banner. We must stem their insurgence and halt their growth before they become an inexorable tide that sweeps over the Ettenmoors, and spills into the free lands beyond.''You have done well, friend. We will not relent in our defence of this land, no matter the foe, and no matter the shadows wherein they hide.

'You are rewarded for your assistance.'Captain-General Tordúr requests assistance in destroying the master of The Delving of Frór, Gaergoth.Tordúr has asked that you enter the depths of The Delving of Frór to face and defeat the rogmul, Gaergoth.Defeat Gaergoth in his arena within The Delving of FrórGaergoth has fallen, but you know that he will reform. For now, you should return to Captain-General Tordúr to be recognized for your efforts.Return to Captain-General Tordúr and inform him of your efforts'Let us turn our attention to the true leader in The Delving of Frór. Enter the depths, confront the creature at his lair deep within The Delving of Frór, and end his reign.

'Come back to me when you have completed the task.''We shall use this time to bolster our strength and renew our resolve. Your efforts here will not be forgotten.'Access to Gaergoth's lair has been regained, and the forces of the enemy descend into the depths to claim treasures for their own purpose. Go forth and slaughter the enemy.Uglash has directed you to enter the Delving of Frór and slaughter all the Free Folk you find.Slaughter Free-folk in The Delving of Frór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})With a good number of the Free Folk defeated in the Delving of Frór, it is time to return to Uglash to claim your rewards.Return to Uglash at Gramsfoot with news of your victory'We got word that Gaergoth's been moving through the Ettendeep again, and the Free Peoples are heading there in droves to get whatever treasures that turncoat's collected. Well, I says, and the boss says, they don't deserve nothing. Get down there and slaughter the free folk you find. 

'I'll reward you handsomely for the effort.''Good work, you sniveling wretch. I could smell blood all over you as you approached. I told you, you'd be rewarded and so you shall.'Access to Gaergoth's lair has been regained, and the forces of the enemy descend into the depths to claim treasures for their own purpose. Go forth and slaughter the enemy.Captain-General Tordúr asked you to enter the Delving of Frór and defeat all the forces of Angmar you find.Defeat Angmar's forces in the Delving of Frór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You fought the forces of Angmar in the depths of The Delving of Frór. Many fell to your combat prowess. Return to Captain-General Tordúr with news of your success.Return to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig with news of your victory'The pathways beneath the Ettenmoors stir with new malevolent energy. Gaergoth returns, and with him the threat of a second force of enemies to stalk the over land. His arrival has sparked the forces of Angmar to venture below and claim whatever terrible prizes the creature has obtained in its absence.

'We require your arms, your cunning, and your strength. We must keep our enemy at bay, lest they gain an upper hand here in the Ettenmoors. Venture to the depths of The Delving of Frór and defeat the forces of Angmar.''Our enemy is relentless, and so we must be, too. 

'We recognize you for your efforts against the enemy.'Uglash sets his sight on Gaergoth, wanting to take down the lord of The Delving of Frór once and for all.Uglash wants you to enter The Delving of Frór and defeat Gaergoth, freeing the other denizens from the control of the Rogmul.Defeat Gaergoth in his arena within The Delving of FrórGaergoth has fallen, but you know that he will reform. For now, you should return to Uglash to claim your reward.Return to Uglash and inform him of your efforts'Let us turn our attention to the true leader in The Delving of Frór. Get down there and put that overzealous Rogmul in its place.

'Come back to me only when you have completed the task.''Good. Good. We will use this moment to enforce the will of Mordirith and bring the misbegotten back beneath the banner of Angmar!

'Reward, a reward for a - currently - worthy warrior.'Gaergoth has empowered some of the forces within the depths of The Delving of Frór with greater power. You have been tasked with defeating these more powerful foes.Tordúr has asked that you enter The Delving of Frór to defeat the commanders Gaergoth has empowered.Defeat Nemesis bosses in The Delving of Frór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Archnemesis bosses in The Delving of Frór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The leaders of The Delving of Frór will not soon forget the pain of your blade. Return to Captain-General Tordúr and inform him of your victory.'Power courses through the ancient enemy, Gaergoth, and it shares its power with those that flock to him.

'Word has reached us of the Dead rising and taking mantles of command alongside the merrevail from the north. We must end these leaders and diminish the strength that Gaergoth bestows upon them.''The commanders are vanquished, and though more will rise to take their place, we have dealt a blow against the forces in The Delving of Frór.

'We shall not retreat from our efforts, the Free Folk will endure.'Gaergoth's misguided followers include a small host of subordinates who hold sway over their lesser followers. These supposed leaders should be dealt with accordingly.Uglash wants you to enter The Delving of Frór and defeat leaders of the disparate forces in the depths. He believes it is their influence depriving the lesser beings of their allegiance to Mordirith and Angmar.Defeat Archnemesis bosses in The Delving of Frór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Nemesis bosses in The Delving of Frór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The leaders of The Delving of Frór will not soon forget the pain of your lash. Return to Uglash and inform him of your victory.'Like I said before about leadership and following the chain of command. Some's good at it, and others, well....

'Take for instance those that lead the different fiends that dwell in the dark below. These so-called leaders, nothing more than subordinates to Gaergoth, force their will upon their lesser recruits and keep them from coming back into our open and oh so forgiving chains.'

He offers a toothy smile.

'You sees where I'm going. And you'll be going to to do as I please. Purge these sycophants and return to me with good news, or not at all.''Ho ho, there's beatings and then there is delivering a really powerful beating. I think you done the latter.

