You should stand with Celebrimbor against the Enemy.Defend Caras Gelebren from the Enemy'You must go! Flee by secret ways, lead the others north, and do not look back!''It is as we feared—the Enemy walks among his servants at last. I am told that he still guises himself in the form of Antheron, but the evil in his heart struggles to conceal itself upon his visage.

'Sauron has ceased his attack for but a moment, but it will not be long before his forces are upon us again.

'Defend against the forces of the Enemy and keep them from breaching the inner gates of Caras Gelebren. Fall back if you must, for we cannot bear the loss of any more of our warriors. In the meantime, I shall prepare our final defences within the walls.

'If the time should come that the Enemy himself breaches the city, we shall make our stand there—upon the very steps of the House of the Mírdain!''We have held them at the gates thus far, but I do not think it will last. The Enemy knows we have no escape—he toys with us!

'Yet a cornered foe is not one with which to be trifled. It will be as Lord Celebrimbor said. We will make our stand together before the House of the Mírdain and cast the Enemy from Eregion!

'You must tell Lord Celebrimbor that we cannot hold the gates for much longer. Do not worry for me! I'll follow as soon as I am able, and we will stand together before the end!

'Go!''Alas for Caras Gelebren! Alas for the Mírdain! Alas that it should come to this!

'I do not doubt Faeldor's words: the gates will not hold. We must defend the House from the forces of the Enemy. Sauron must not find that which he seeks!

'As soon as the other warriors have fallen back, we'll stand to—''We have stood fast in the face of the Enemy, but this respite will not last.

'Sauron's forces have encircled Caras Gelebren, and try as they might, the armies of Gil-galad and Elrond have not yet been able to pierce them and come to our aid.

'I weep for all those we have lost, and I pray that their sacrifices were not in vain.'Orcs have set up camp near the Span of Nâmbadir. You are tasked with sabotaging their weapons and defeating any who get in your way.Destroy Orkish weapons racks and defeat Orcs in Tharháth, near the Span of Nâmbadir.Destroy Orkish weapons racks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orcs in Tharháth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Investigate the noise coming from the back of the camp.Investigate the back of the campDefeat the Utûgi Devastator.Defeat the Utûgi Devastator'We should get you back to Urmâkh. Come, we must spread the good news of your victory here.'You must acquire or use the bauble that allows you summon a miniature version of the Bane of Rhûn.Acquire the Effigy of The Bane of Rhûn orUse the skill: The Effigy of the Bane of RhûnYou must acquire or use the bauble that allows you summon a miniature version of the Black Blade of Lebennin.Acquire the Effigy of The Black Blade of Lebennin orUse the skill: The Effigy of the Black Blade of LebenninYou must acquire or use the bauble that allows you summon a miniature version of the Cursed Rider.Acquire the Effigy of The Cursed Rider orUse the skill: The Effigy of the Cursed RiderYou must acquire or use the bauble that allows you summon a miniature version of the Forsaken Reaver.Acquire the Effigy of The Forsaken Reaver orUse the skill: The Effigy of the Forsaken ReaverYou must acquire or use the bauble that allows you summon a miniature version of the Gloom of Nurn.Acquire the Effigy of The Gloom of Nurn orUse the skill: The Effigy of the Gloom of NurnYou must acquire or use the bauble that allows you summon a miniature version of the Grim Southron.Acquire the Effigy of The Grim Southron orUse the skill: The Effigy of the Grim SouthronYou must acquire or use the bauble that allows you summon a miniature version of the High Sorcerer of Harad.Acquire the Effigy of The High Sorcerer of Harad orUse the skill: The Effig