Free the final Zajâni noble prisoner in the Hall of Lajór.Free the final Zajâni noble prisoner'This is a good day for all of Zajâna. These nobles owe you their lives, and we owe you a debt of gratitude. Let us return to Jôrlar with news of this victory.'Goblins have taken over the hills of Glúkroz, raiding along the Great Road and killing any locals they find. Luckily they have brought the source of their own destruction. Set alight their explosives.Defeat goblins and destroy catapults and cauldrons in Glúkroz.Defeat goblins in Glúkroz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy goblin cauldrons in Glúkroz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy goblin catapults in Glúkroz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat Korutásh, leader of the goblins in Glúkroz.Defeat Korutásh in Glúkroz'Sen Chatâk and all of Kighân is in your debt. Those goblin raiding parties threatened travellers, caravans, and villagers all along the western half of Kighân. Let's get back to Zajâna and tell Jôrlar of your triumph.'Girhâzi has given the order to clear the Ordâkhai out of Omboha, their camp to the north.Defeat the Ordâkhai and burn their tents to run them out of Omboha.Defeat Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Ordâkhai tents (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many Ordâkhai and burned their tents. An Ordâkhai champion has come forth to challenge you. You should answer his challenge.Defeat Bodhóri'I am glad you are on our side! Come, let us return to Iridír.'You have come to the ruins of Nan Dhelu, where the emergence of the Dead from within the ruins prevents the Eglain from reclaiming the treasures they need.Cwendreda believes the War-singers carry the valuable treasures the Eglain need for trading. You should defeat them and search their remains for the valuables.Collect valuables from defeated War-singers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Master of Nan Dhelu is a fearsome wight that must be banished from the realm of the living. You should seek him out and defeat him.'Just knowing that the creature has been defeated brings a wisp of hope into my heart. You have done much to aid the Eglain this day, ${PLAYER}. These valuables will earn us a great deal of supplies from the traders in Bree-land.'Whatever the reason, you allowed these lazy prospectors in Ukhbab-gairu to cause you to drop ore more times than a dwarf cares to count. Your failures caused the forge fires to fail.You should try much harder to avoid getting tripped up by the Lazy Prospectors in the Hard Tack at Thorin's Hall event.Crebain have been stealing helms and hats from the good citizens of Urmâkh. A local scout has tracked them to Ghât Okho. You are to recover the headwear from these brazen winged thieves.Recovery headwear at Ghât Okho and fight off crebain.Recover stolen helms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat crebain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'That's quite the bounty of helms you've recovered. I wonder what the crebain planned to do with them all? Perhaps they just enjoy the way they catch the light.'Will Whitfoot, Mayor of Michel Delving, is said to be the fattest hobbit in the Westfarthing (and possibly beyond).

