'Will you dare to be glorious?'War-tyrant Akúlhun directs you to wade into the fray and slaughter the Free People. The more you kill, the greater your reward will be. Be warned, all will know that you are on a rampage.Scour the Ettenmoors for the enemies of Angmar and eliminate them where they are found. Slaughter for the glory of Angmar!Slaughter the Free People (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scour the Ettenmoors for the enemies of Angmar and eliminate them where they are found. Slaughter for the glory of Angmar!Slaughter the Free People (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scour the Ettenmoors for the enemies of Angmar and eliminate them where they are found. Slaughter for the glory of Angmar!Slaughter the Free People (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scour the Ettenmoors for the enemies of Angmar and eliminate them where they are found. Slaughter for the glory of Angmar!Slaughter the Free People (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scour the Ettenmoors for the enemies of Angmar and eliminate them where they are found. Slaughter for the glory of Angmar!Slaughter the Free People (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Our overlord demands blood. I would stride forth and slaughter the Free Folk were Malavin not watching me like a craban.

'You, on the other hand, can make your way into the field and slaughter them for me. Succeed and I will see a portion of my strength transferred to you for a time.

'Slaughter them. Slaughter them all!'War-tyrant Akúlhun commands you to find glory-seeking Free People and destroy them! He promises a reward for those who take the enemy down.Find a Free Person who is seeking glory across the Ettenmoors and slay them in the name of Angmar!

<rgb=#00FF00>Only Glory Seeking Free People Players count toward the advance of this quest.</rgb>Find and defeat a glory-seeking Free Person'These fools think they drive us from the field of battle? Never!

'Go forth, gather your numbers and find these fools wherever they may be. Slaughter them outright and you will be justly rewarded!'

<rgb=#00FF00>This quest will fail if there are no longer Glory Seeking Free People Players in the Ettenmoors.</rgb>You did some folks a good turn back at Yule-time, and it seems they haven't forgotten your kindness.Nora Strawley is in the Beggar's Alley in Bree.

You should speak with Nora Strawley to see what Daley Utteridge has sent to you.Talk to Nora Strawley in Bree to receive your gift${PLAYER}, I hope you remember me, for I will never forget your kindness. Ever since you helped Gareth Rust and myself, our town has been thriving. The mayor has been in no position to do us any harm again, and we are all much better off... and happy and healthy. No one is left without a home or without bread and meat for supper.

At the time, I could not thank you properly, but my wife and I have come into some money, and we wanted to spend some of it on you. Your goodness will never leave our thoughts!

I have mailed your gift to a friend in Bree, who will be happy to give it to you. You need only pick it up, and it is yours.

Sincerely,
Daley Utteridge of Winter-home'Ah, so you are the famous ${CLASS} who helped the Utteridges! They have sent a package for you. Here you are!'You chose to assist the cooks and prospectors of Thorin's Hall. How well will you perform?Aid the cooks and prospectors in Thorin's Hall as they endeavour to make hard tack for an upcoming expedition. Haul ore, catch fish, collect items from the nearby larder, or undertake any other available tasks to earn commendations.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier I (${NUMBER}/5)Aid the cooks and prospectors in Thorin's Hall as they endeavour to make hard tack for an upcoming expedition. Haul ore, catch fish, collect items from the nearby larder, or undertake any other available tasks to earn commendations.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier II (${NUMBER}/5)Aid the cooks and prospectors in Thorin's Hall as they endeavour to make hard tack for an upcoming expedition. Haul ore, catch fish, collect items from the nearby larder, or undertake any other available tasks to earn commendations.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier III (${NUMBER}/10)You provided an enormous contribution to the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall event and should visit the coordinator for your final reward.Speak to the Thorin's Hall Event Coordinator'If you are neither a cook nor a prospector, or you are just looking to lend a helping hand to the community here, then we have jobs for you to do.

'You can haul ore, you can catch fish, you can fetch items from the larder, or even keep an eye on that pesky hobbit over there. I will see you earn proper commendation for each task you complete while the cooks make their hard tack.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Accepting this quest will lock you out of accepting the Cook or Prospector Quests in the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall Event.</rgb>"'Masterful performance. Please accept this token of our gratitude. Our cooks and prospectors also thank you for your contributions!'Cooks making dishes to help the creation of the hard tack need fish to make the heartiest dishes and snacks. Fish them up at the pond in the cavern.Fish up the tasty fish in the pond in the cavern.Collect fish for the cooks helping the community (${NUMBER}/5)You caught ten fish from the pond in the cavern. You should deliver those to a fish barrel near the cooks making dishes to help those helping to make hard tack.'While the cooks who make hard tack ply their trade, I oversee the creation of the foods that help to speed the process of carrying and collecting all the materials we need to craft the hard tack.

'There are very tasty fish swimming in a pond within this cavern. With a little spice they can become a hearty dish or two for those helping in the creation of hard tack.

'Collect some and deliver them to the fish barrels.'Cooking large amounts of hard tack takes a full community effort. As a cook, you are well-suited to assist the dwarves.Aid the community of Thorin's Hall to inspire, hearten, and strengthen those assisting the cooks as they craft hard tack for an expedition. You will need to execute special recipes and deliver your creations for everyone involved.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier I (${NUMBER}/5)Aid the community of Thorin's Hall to inspire, hearten, and strengthen those assisting the cooks as they craft hard tack for an expedition. You will need to execute special recipes and deliver your creations for everyone involved.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier II (${NUMBER}/5)Aid the community of Thorin's Hall to inspire, hearten, and strengthen those assisting the cooks as they craft hard tack for an expedition. You will need to execute special recipes and deliver your creations for everyone involved.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier III (${NUMBER}/5)Aid the community of Thorin's Hall to inspire, hearten, and strengthen those assisting the cooks as they craft hard tack for an expedition. You will need to execute special recipes and deliver your creations for everyone involved.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier IV (${NUMBER}/5)Your assistance in feeding and slaking the thirst of those assisting the cooks to craft hard tack is complete. You exceeded expectations and should visit the coordinator to receive your final reward.Speak with the Coordinator at the Thorin's Hall event space'We do not need cooks to make the hard tack for the expedition. The best cooks in Thorin's Hall are engaged in the effort to make the hard tack. You can, however, assist everyone in their duties by making food that inspires, heartens, and strengthens all those assisting in the effort.

'We offer greater rewards for greater assistance.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Accepting this quest will lock you out of accepting the Assist or Prospector Quests in the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall Event.</rgb>""Magnificent cooking, friend. You deserve many thanks for assisting us in crafting the hard tack in the ovens above. Please, take this reward for your efforts."The dwarves tending the flames to cook a large amount of hard tack require ever-burning ore to keep the flames hot enough.Make your way through the tunnels and caverns to discover a vein of ever-burning ore to prospect.'We need ever-burning ore to keep the fires hot enough to cook the hard tack.

'You will need a discerning eye to find the ore. Some veins are rich, some poor, all the ore will help. Travel through the tunnels and find a proper location.'Sneaky hobbits are threatening to eat all the food needed to keep a steady delivery of ever-burning ore on track. You are tasked with sating their hunger to keep them from interfering in the event.To keep the sneaky hobbits from interfering with the stoking of the furnace, you were asked to feed them a little too much spice in their mushrooms. Collect mushrooms and spice from the larder.Collect a mushroom crate from the larderCollect spice from the larderYou sprinkle the spices onto the mushrooms and shake them around, concealing the additive. Deliver the crate to a sneaky hobbit.'Be on the look-out for pesky little sneaky hobbits. They keep swiping food from the service area and we simply do not have enough guards to keep track of them all.

'We might have a solution to slowing their interference down.

'An overload of spice! Enough will turn their stomachs for a while. We just need to deliver it to them in a manner they may find tasty. We will need mushrooms and spice from the larder.''Oh these look very tasty and smell delicious! You saved me some trouble!'Harvest the laden nodes to find ever-burning ore and keep the cook-fires of Thorin's Hall burning.Prospect laden ever-burning ore nodes to release a harvestable chunk of the ore.Prospect a laden ever-burning node'Prospecting nodes for ever-burning ore is more meticulous than just hacking away at metal veins.

'The volatile nature of the ore makes an errant swing of the pickaxe into an explosive event.

'Laden nodes yield the most ore in moderate, small, and large-sized pieces but are the slowest to unearth.

'Go forth and get that ore.'Ever-burning ore is needed to keep the cook-fires of Thorin's Hall active. Collect a large chunk of ore and deliver it to an ore cart.Collect a large chunk of harvested ever-burning ore and deliver it to a mine-cart in the area of the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall event.Deliver a large piece of ever-burning ore to a mine-cart<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid the lazy prospectors</rgb>'Freeing the ever-burning ore from nearby veins is only half the effort needed. Ever-burning ore is not only volatile but also heavy.

'You can possibly carry one large chunk of ever-burning ore. It will burn the longest, but it will also greatly weigh you down.

'Collect a large chunk of ore and deliver it to an ore-cart in Ukhbab-gairu.'Ever-burning ore is needed to keep the cook-fires of Thorin's Hall active. Collect the medium-sized ore and deliver it to an ore cart.Collect a medium-sized chunk of harvested ever-burning ore and deliver them to an ore cart in the area of the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall event.Collect and deliver a medium-sized chunk of ever-burning ore to an ore cart<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid the lazy prospectors</rgb>Collect another medium-sized chunks of harvested ever-burning ore and deliver them to an ore cart in the area of the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall event.Collect and deliver a medium-sized chunk of ever-burning ore to a mine-cart<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid the lazy prospectors</rgb>'Freeing the ever-burning ore from nearby veins is only half the effort needed. Ever-burning ore is not only volatile but also heavy.

'You can carry fewer of the medium-sized chunks of ever-burning ore, but they burn longer. They will also greatly weigh you down.

'Collect enough of the medium-sized chunks of ore and deliver it to an ore-cart in Ukhbab-gairu.'Mushrooms from within the cave are needed to make the dishes that help the crafting of hard tack along. Collect a crate from the larder or a bundle from the surrounding cave.Collect mushrooms from the caves where the dwarves of Thorin's Hall are making Hard Tack or collect a crate from the nearby larder and deliver the items to the cook station in the main area.Collect deep mushrooms from around the cave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect a crate of mushrooms from the larderDeliver the mushrooms you gathered to the cook's station in the main area.'You're neither cook nor prospector, but still you can help the dwarves of Thorin's Hall. Excellent. Excellent!

'Mushrooms! The cooks need mushrooms. Fetch a crate from the larder or gather them up from around the cave and deliver them to the cook station in the main room.

'Hurry, now!'Sluggard miners are more trouble than aid during the event. Fortunately, a quick bite of a mushroom from here in the deep will give them a little zeal.Make your way into the larder and collect a crate of mushrooms, then deliver the mushrooms to one of the sluggard miners milling about in the cavern below.Deliver a snack to a lazy prospector<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid sneaky hobbits</rgb>'There are Men here to help from the surface. I have found them incapable of focus or vim.

'I know we can inspire them with a little bit of mushroom from here in the cavern.

'Head to the larder and collect a crate of mushrooms. Deliver it to one of the sluggard miners and watch how fast he works.'Cooking large amounts of hard tack takes a full community effort. As a prospector, you are well-suited to assist the dwarfs and reap the rewards for your assistance.Aid the cooks of Thorin's Hall to keep the cook-fires burning while they make hard tack for an expedition under the mountains.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier I (${NUMBER}/5)Aid the cooks of Thorin's Hall to keep the cook-fires burning while they make hard tack for an expedition under the mountains.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier II (${NUMBER}/5)Aid the cooks of Thorin's Hall to keep the cook-fires burning while they make hard tack for an expedition under the mountains.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier III (${NUMBER}/5)Aid the cooks of Thorin's Hall to keep the cook-fires burning while they make hard tack for an expedition under the mountains.Earn Thorin's Hall Commendations - Tier IV (${NUMBER}/5)You exceeded expectations and performed feats of near perfection. You should visit the coordinator and speak to them for final acknowledgment.Speak with the Coordinator at the Thorin's Hall event space'Greetings! I can tell by the callouses on your hands and the definition of your arms you swing a pickaxe. Your arrival is most fortuitous. We are making hard tack. We are making a large batch to assist in an expedition of dwarves delving deeper into the mountains.

'We need able bodies to find the ever-burning ore in these halls to keep the cook-fires burning. There is much to do and you will be rewarded for your efforts.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Accepting this quest will lock you out of accepting the Assist or Cook Quests in the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall Event.</rgb>"'An amazing accomplishment. Your support and interaction with the community allowed the cooks to succeed in creating enough hard tack to support our expedition for several days.

'Please accept this reward for your effort.'Harvest the rich nodes to find ever-burning ore and keep the cook-fires of Thorin's Hall burning.Prospect rich ever-burning ore nodes to release harvestable chunks of the ore.Prospect a rich ever-burning node'The process of prospecting nodes for ever-burning ore is more meticulous than just hacking away at metal veins.

'The volatile nature of the ore makes an errant swing of the pickaxe into an explosive event.

'Rich nodes yield more ore in moderately sized pieces but are slower to unearth.

'Go forth and get that ore.'Sluggard miners are more trouble than aid during the event. Fortunately, their laziness is exacerbated by a flagon of ale.Make your way to the larder, collect a flagon of ale and deliver it to a sluggard miner to set them to sleep for a while. This will make the halls safer for transporting ever-burning ore.Collect a flagon of ale from the larderAvoid sneaky hobbits'Ho friend! We need to help the prospectors stay away from those lazy sluggards milling about the halls. These men are supposed to be learning a craft, instead they drift aimlessly through the caverns unaware of their surroundings, causing the hard workers to drop the precious and volatile ever-burning ore.

'We can mitigate their impact on deliveries by making a delivery of our own.

'A good flagon of ale will set them to sleep.''These sluggard miners say they want to learn and help, then they do nothing. Their antics will get someone injured. Surely they impede the work of those diligently engaged in keeping the furnace fired!

'Fortunately, a good flagon of ale from the larder will set them to slumber for a time.

'Since you are not capable with a pick or an oven you can run some ale to this sluggards.'Ever-burning ore is needed to keep the cook-fires of Thorin's Hall active. Collect the small ore and deliver it to an ore cart.Collect small chunks of harvested ever-burning ore and deliver it to an ore cart inside of the event space for Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall.Deliver a small chunk of ever-burning ore to a mine-cart<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid the lazy prospectors</rgb>Collect another small chunk of harvested ever-burning ore and deliver it to an ore cart inside of the event space for Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall.Deliver a small chunk of ever-burning ore to a mine-cart<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid the lazy prospectors</rgb>Collect one more small chunk of harvested ever-burning ore and deliver it to an ore cart inside of the event space for Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall.Deliver a small chunk of ever-burning ore to a mine-cart<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid the lazy prospectors</rgb>'Freeing the ever-burning ore from nearby veins is only half the effort needed. Ever-burning ore is not only volatile but also heavy.

'You can carry more of the small chunks of ever-burning ore, but they burn more quickly. They will also weigh you down.

'Collect enough of the small ore and deliver it to an ore-cart in Ukhbab-gairu.'A brew that gives a burst of focus and energy is a necessity in times like these. Try your hand at delivering this brew.Collect the ingredients needed to craft the Thorin's Hall Brew from the nearby mushrooms, keg, and spice rack.Collect an ale ingredient from the nearby kegCollect a mushroom ingredient from the mushroom crateCollect a spice ingredient from the spice rackCraft the Thorin's Brew beverage, then deliver it to a brew table to help all the workers perform at their peak.Craft Thorin's Hall BrewYou made Thorin's Hall Brew. Complete your brew in the oven and the deliver it to a brew table. Be careful to avoid sneaky hobbits.<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid sneaky hobbits</rgb>Complete the brew in the oven and deliver it to the tablePlace the brew onto the brew table.'Ho there! The grand chefs of Thorin's Hall intend on making enough hard tack to feed an expedition.

'To speed their efforts, prospectors will supply ever-burning ore from here in the depths to the furnace firing the ovens above. We cooks down here have an important role.

'We make brew, snacks, and a meal that helps everyone here in the depths perform better, faster, stronger! If you are willing to help out, we will see you rewarded well!'A meal providing exceptional leg strength and swiftness is a necessity in times like these. Try your hand at delivering this meal.Collect the ingredients needed to craft the Thorin's Hall Brew from the nearby fish barrel, mushrooms crate, and spice rack.Collect the fish ingredient from the fish barrelCollect the mushroom ingredient from the mushroom crateCollect the spice craft ingredient from the spice rackCreate a Thorin's Hall Hearty Meal then deliver it to a meal table to help all the workers perform at their peak.You made a Thorin's Hall Hearty Meal. Complete the meal in the oven and deliver it to a meal table.Complete the meal in the oven then deliver it to the table<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid sneaky hobbits</rgb>Place the Thorin's Hall Hearty Meal onto a meal table.'Swift and sturdy legs! That is what we need down here in the depths.

'No doubt you noticed that the air this deep is stifling. Makes moving like walking through a running river. We have an answer for this problem. A Thorin's Hall Hearty Meal!

'Collect up the mushrooms, fish, and spice. Then craft the meal and deliver it to the table for meals.'A snack providing a boost to speed is a necessity in times like these. Try your hand at delivering this snack.Collect the ingredients needed to craft the Thorin's Hall Brew from the nearby mushroom crate and spice rack.Collect craft ingredients from the spice rackCollect mushroom ingredients from the mushroom crateCraft a Thorin's Hall Mushroom Snack then deliver it to a snack table to help all the workers perform at their peak.Craft a Thorin's Hall Mushroom SnackYou made a Thorin's Hall Mushroom Snack. Complete the snack in an oven and deliver it to a snack table. Avoid sneaky hobbits.<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid sneaky hobbits</rgb>Complete the snack in the oven and deliver it to the tableDeliver the Thorin's Hall Snack to a snack table.'The grand chefs above call for the crafting of hard tack, and I am here to see the workers here thrive in their efforts.

'Prospectors and labourers hauling ever-burning ore need some extra strength while they do the back-breaking work. We will make them a hearty meal to strengthen them and lessen their burden as they do so.

'Collect mushrooms, fish, and spice to make the hearty meal and deliver it to the tables.'Everything needs a little special dwarf-spice when you are making hard tack. Cooks need this for their supporting dishes.Cooks making dishes that help to speed movement, grant strength, and hasten actions while the dwarves make hard tack require spice from the larder. Collect the spice from the larder and deliver it to a spice rack in the main room.Collect a jar of spice from the larderYou collected the jar of spice from the larder. Now place the jar of spice on the spice rack near where the cooks making snacks, drinks, and meals are cooking.'While the cooks who make hard tack ply their trade, I oversee the creation of the foods that help to speed the process of carrying and collecting all the materials we need to craft the hard tack.

'The larder contains spice used to flavour snacks and hearty dishes. Collect those spices and deliver them here to ease the process of making dishes to aid participants.'Harvest the weaker nodes to find ever-burning ore and keep the cook-fires of Thorin's Hall burning.Prospect weak ever-burning ore nodes of ever-burning to release harvestable chunks of the ore.Prospect a weak ever-burning node'Prospecting nodes for ever-burning ore is more meticulous than just hacking away at metal veins.

'The volatile nature of the ore makes an errant swing of the pickaxe into an explosive event.

'Weaker nodes yield less ore in smaller pieces but are faster to unearth.

'Go forth and get that ore.'Crafting the hard tack used by dwarf explorers is a community effort. To participate in the event you need to learn three recipes. Fortunately, these are easily learned.Speak with Ingúl Ovestoke near the ovens in Ukhbab-gairu to learn the recipes needed to participate in the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall event.'If you are willing to assist us in our efforts to craft hard tack, then I shall teach you the recipes necessary for our endeavour here.

'Speak with me again and I will explain.''There are three distinct recipes we craft in support of making hard tack.

'The first is a brew to slake the thirst of all participants that helps to focus and speed along the difficult task of mining the ever-burning ore.

'The second is a snack that puts a spring in your step and gives you extra speed as you traverse the Great Vault.

'The last recipe is a dish that provides strength when lifting and hauling heavy objects.

'Learn these recipes.'The Dumûri have learned the Ordâkhai in Eshadûr have restocked their supply of black powder.Search Eshadûr for explosive black powder, and destroy any containers of the substance you find.Destroy powder barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Keeping black powder out of Ordâkhai hands is important for our survival. Thank you.'A posting from the Mayor of Bree-town, Graeme Tenderlarch, requests assistance with keeping the town clean and clear for its residents.Make your way to Bree-town Hall and speak with Mayor Graeme Tenderlarch about the work he needs done around the town.Speak with Graeme Tenderlarch at the Bree-town HallSpeak with Barliman Butterbur and Agatha Greendale. They have requested assistance from the mayor. Barliman is the proprietor of The Prancing Pony, and Agatha can be found at the lodge at the end of the road heading west near the South Gate of Bree.Assist Barliman Butterbur with his request to Mayor TenderlarchAssist Agatha Greendale with her request to Mayor TenderlarchHaving completed the requests put forward by Barliman Butterbur and Agatha Greendale, you are ready to return to Graeme Tenderlarch and inform him of your success.Speak with Mayor Graeme Tenderlarch in Bree-town HallPost:

Needed, a friendly and diligent worker to assist with cleaning up Bree-town. Inquiries should be made with Mayor Graeme Tenderlarch at the Bree-town Hall.'Thank you for responding to my request.

'I must confess that we were not prepared for the amount of visitors we have received coming from the south and surrounding hamlets. While many of the local business owners are pleased with the increased patronage, they are equally displeased with the state of our streets.

'Not all the visitors share the same courtesy of keeping our city streets clear of unsightly refuse.

'Complaints have been mounting and I needed to find someone willing to assist. Now; here you are.'

He smiles.

'If you are willing, seek out Barliman Butterbur, proprietor of the Prancing Pony, and Agatha Greendale, a representative of the Men of Bree, at their lodge at the end of the western road near the South Gate.

'Their needs are the most pressing, at the moment.''Thanks to you, I can cross the requests of Barliman and Agatha off of my ever-growing list.

'I only wish I had more to offer you, beyond thanks, and a meager amount of coin.'You've chased many a chicken in your day, and few have played the game better than you.You must earn All-star with the Chicken Chasing League of EriadorYou are amongst the greatest to have ever played Hobnanigans.You must earn Hall of Famer with the Chicken Chasing League of EriadorAny Hobnanigans team would be excited to have you on it.You must earn Major Leaguer with the Chicken Chasing League of EriadorYou've got the basics down, but there's still a lot to learn.You must earn Minor Leaguer with the Chicken Chasing League of EriadorIt's a game about a chicken and a stick, right?You must earn Rookie with the Chicken Chasing League of EriadorHelp Lolo with the collection of honeycombs within the bear deans of Combe.Collect the honeycombs Lolo asked you to recover from the bear dens.Collect honeycomb from the beehives (${NUMBER}/8)Find the scout near the entrance of the ruins.Find the scout near the ruin entrance'Let's return to the cross-roads.'Tansy Tighfield asked you to deliver a block of ice to the frozen sweet-cream vendor in Bywater. Make sure to avoid obstacles!

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends.</rgb>The ice block for delivery to Bywater can be found at the Party Tree.

You should carry the ice to the frozen sweet-cream stand in Bywater.Deliver the ice block to the frozen sweet-cream standBluet Goldworthy is at her vendor stall in Bywater.

You should speak with Bluet Goldworthy.Speak with Bluet Goldworthy'Have you visited the stand in Bywater selling frozen sweet-cream? It is such a lovely treat, but the vendor is constantly requiring more fresh ice from our covered stockpile here in Hobbiton, for it would melt if we brought it all to Bywater at once.

'The only thing to do is carry it one block at a time each day. It's too heavy for me, but you look strong. Would you be willing to take it?

'Just be sure to watch out for obstacles. People move slowly and get in the way, and it will be hard to see around the ice….''Thank you! I have been out of ice for a bit now, and all of these folks are waiting for their frozen sweet-cream. Now I can get back to work.'The Ordâkhai torturer Dokhára is holding several Ambarûli people prisoner in Eshadûr.Rescue the prisoners being held in Eshadûr and save them from the Ordâkhai torturer Dokhára.You have rescued the prisoners being held in Eshadûr. Now you must face the Ordâkhai torturer Dokhára.Defeat Dokhára on the path towards the Entrance'I'm glad you were able to help Mushendu. I've been dispatched to bring you back to Urmâkh, there are other matters there that require your attention.'You find yourself inside The Forsaken Inn at midnight. The innkeeper has asked that you investigate the source of the wailing noises coming from the cellar.Patrons have already begun complaining of the noises in the cellar. Explore the area and see if you can uncover the source of the noises.Investigate the source of the wailing noisesThe book-shelf was hiding a secret passage leading down into the earth below the Inn. You should explore this cavern and see if you can locate who or what is making those noises.Explore the depths below The Forsaken InnYou have found a suspicious-looking man reading a book and staring at the glowing, rune-marked door in front of him. Who is this man, and why is he down here? You had best ask him.Talk to the suspicious manUmín, the man you met in these caverns, has agreed to assist you in your exploration of this place. You must use his expertise to make your way deeper into the caverns.Continue to explore the cavernsYou have discovered what appears to be a burial chamber. Perhaps Umín could shed some light on this place.Bring Umín to the burial chamberUmín has been crushed by the cave-in. You must press on without him. You are on your own now, so be always on guard.Press onwards through the cavernsIt is Umín. Alive and well, it seems... too well even. It appears that he has gained an almost supernatural strength in his absence. He wears a red, glowing necklace around his neck. He is also a bit angry with you... you will have to defeat him if you want to survive.Defeat UmínThe spinning blade-trap has knocked the necklace from Umín's neck, and it lies glowing on the floor. Umín himself lies crumpled on the floor. Why did he attack you?

Speak with him and allow him to explain....Talk to UmínEscape the shipIt wasn't Umín at all that was trying to kill you. It was the spirt inhabiting the necklace. It was controlling him, making him do its bidding. You must destroy the spirit, lest it escapes from the place and wreaks havoc upon Middle-earth.Defeat the Spirit of the NecklaceIt is over. The spirit has been defeated. Speak with Umín and explain your victory.Talk to Umín'It... was controlling me... my thoughts, my actions. I could see its purpose. It wants nothing less than the destruction of us all.

'Quickly! You must leave this place before it comes back. It isn't through with us yet! Just leave me here... I was the one who desired the necklace above all, and I shall be the one to destroy it!

'You have no time to lose! Cross to the other side of the ship and leave through that cave there!''Is it truly over? I am sorry for all the pain I have caused. I was blinded by the necklace before I even set eyes upon it.... It consumed my thoughts and my life. It is the reason I pursued this endeavour in the first place. Now that the spirit has been destroyed, it has no meaning to me. What shall I do with myself?

'Just leave me here with my thoughts....'Aragorn's skill at healing will be put to the test in the Houses of Healing.Aragorn is by Faramir's bedside in the Houses of Healing.Talk to AragornAragorn is by Faramir's bedside in the Houses of Healing.Remain alert in the event you are neededFaramir has recovered, and now Aragorn goes to see if Éowyn's condition has improved.Follow Aragorn to Éowyn's bedsideAragorn is by Éowyn's bedside in the Houses of Healing.Remain alert in the event you are neededAragorn has gone to Merry's bedside to see if his work has aided the hobbit's recovery.Walk to Merry's bedsideAragorn is by Merry's bedside in the Houses of Healing.Remain alert in the event you are neededMerry is still in bed, but he seems to be recovering.Talk to Merry'Thank you for all your help, ${PLAYER}. We have done much good here, and there is more to do before I can rest. But I am glad that some of the evils that befell us upon Pelennor have been remedied.''Let us see if Faramir's condition has improved, ${PLAYER}.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! Do you remember when we crept to see Théoden's war-council in the Drúadan Forest? It feels to me as if that was years and years ago, but it cannot have been. I have been caught in a terrible dream, but already the memory of it is fading.

'I think supper will be just the thing, and afterwards perhaps a pipe. No, not a pipe. I don't think I will ever smoke again. Théoden was sorry he would not be able to speak of herb-lore with me, smoking our pipes in comfort and peace. I will never be able to smoke without thinking of him.'The War-tyrant seems displeased that emissaries from Carn Dûm arrived and made their way into the war tent. His demeanor is more grim than usual, and he has instructed you to make your way to the Angmarim sorceress who now resides in the tent within the confines of Gramsfoot.War-tyrant Akúlhun directed you to the war tent to speak with an Angmarim sorceress there named Malavin. Apparently she is here to assist, inspect, or guide the war effort. Whatever her purpose, it does not sit well with the War-tyrant.Malavin instructed you to speak to each of the emissaries representing the clans of Carn Dûm and beyond. They have blessings that they will seek to bestow upon you, provided you will serve in their name.Speak with the emissariesHaving spoken to all the emissaries it is time to return to Malavin for further instruction.'Just what I need. A sorceress come from the north to tell me how the fight goes. Oh, she has the ear of the steward, but the arms are here, in the Ettenmoors. We've been fighting while they've been locked away in castles and steel barricades. What do they know about battling these people?'

It is a question that requires no answer.

'Bah... leadership back in Carn Dûm is looking for a new way to off these pesky Free Folk. So we got some new tricks available, meat. Each clan, and even the dirty dogs and sticky little spiders got their own emissaries here to help you new gits out. Oh and those southron Uruks too... talk to one of them and they'll give you a taste of what the leaders are thinking... don't get used to it though, maggot. These truces can only last so long....

'But first, they want me to send every maggot with snot dripping on their face up the hill to talk with her. Well... so be it. Better you go talk to her than me. She calls herself Malavin.'

There is a short pause.

'If you get a chance, accidentally spit on her for me, would you?''Orders is orders. You need to talk to the Priestess first.''Talk with the skinny witch, then you can talk to me.''Abide by the council's will and speak with Malavin.''Seek she who speaks for the lord of Carn Dûm. Our brood will wait our turn.''Sharkey's orders are clear, we let the woman speak... for now.''Far be it from the Krahjarn to deny protocol. What, you think we're all war hungry tyrants like Akúlhun?'

He smirks.

'We are... some of us just hide it better. Talk with Malavin. That is the command. We will abide.''The pack is eager to hunt. The human is a barrier to our victory. Speak with her quick and then return to me.''Another veteran of the way, or are you a new recruit? Honestly, I cannot tell the difference between a seasoned warrior and a whelp fresh from the pens or egg. I do, however, know a thing or two about obedience and seeing that orders are carried out.'

She smirks wryly.

'Mordirith is displeased with the efforts here and organized an effort to entice you... warriors... with gifts. Each of the Orc clans, the Scara-pack, and Brood of Shelob send emissaries to entreat. He even allowed the White Hand at this table. Perhaps, in time there will be more. For now, it is these few.'

She pauses a moment to look you over.

'It appears that the steward of Carn Dûm is correct in his assessment. You are all in dire need of help. I invite you then to speak with the emissaries here in Gramsfoot. Learn what they offer you and choose their blessing. Each has been ordered, for now, to entreat with all of you, provide for you until the council of our lord is complete.

'Run along now and learn from each of the emissaries here and then return to me.''Off with you until you have spoken to each of the emissaries. Return to me when you are done. I shall instruct you further.''I am Fathrug, and you look like you are ready to tear the flesh off a man. That is all we ask. Find the Men. Flay the Men. Leave their carcasses littering the earth to turn the grass bloody. The Tarkrîp clan will strengthen your skills, help you stay in the fight longer. You'll be rather brutal about your business of hacking and rending the enemy, and while we won't teach you how to dodge a really nasty sword blow, we'll teach you to shrug it off and keep going.

'The Tarkrîp clan prizes scrappy warriors above all else, willing to strike at the enemy relentlessly!''You look soft, maggot. I should know the Ongbúrz are the heartiest clan in all of Angmar. We are not afraid of battle. We thrive in it. We revel in the clash of hammers, axes, and all the tools those bearded bastards bring against us. We know little fear. Our prowess in in our staying power.

'If you want to swing your blade wildly without thought about tomorrow, go talk with the Tarkrîp or the dogs. If you want to stand tall above all the others then take our blessing into battle. Toughness like ours should never be underestimated.''Come closer. Smell that? Mushrooms. Slime. Herbs. Poultices. The trappings of healers. Oh, yes, the other clans will tell you that they are the most stalwart, or furious, or violent, or sinister, but we are the force that keeps them standing. We are the strength behind them all.'

He chuckles.

'Half the pain that they don't feel is because of our stinking sludges and fungal brews. We know how to pound a spike into a missing arm if things go terribly ill, too. Sometimes the victim even survives long enough to make it more permanent.

'The others will tell you tales, but it is we that let them keep tongues wagging. Without us, they'd all be face down in the dirt. Stand with us. Stand with the Blogmal Clan.''She is born of the first enemy of Elves. She feeds her brood well and gives them all they need to spread the faith of the Dark Lord. Gifts that sting deeply, secretly, and brutally. Her poison courses to seep into the flesh and twist it to the darkness where she dwells.'

The queen chitters.

'She burns the victims from within so they sting, sting, sting, longer and more painfully. She is the corruption that seeds the earth with malicious intent. She is mother to her brood. Join with her and earn the gift to inflict suffering most profound.''Sharkey orders us north to help figh, so we come. We see why these clans fail. Too unbalanced. Too dedicated to destruction, or defence. Too dedicated to mysticism or the darkness.'

He shakes his head.

'No temperance leads to a quick end. Learning the field of battle, discerning the weakness and strengths of your enemy provides a clearer path to victory. It is an even path we walk. It is the teaching of our master that we prize. The method to strike hard, the method to stand tall, the method to withstand a strike and turn a blade.

'I would lead the White Hand against any of these other clans and leave them in shambles. Join us and you will see what I mean.''The Krahjarn are born to lead. We remember the wars against the first. We recall the first lash against our backs and how to revisit that on our lessers. We know what it means to lead, to oversee the battle, to watch the flow of a fight, when to inspire and when to instill fear.'

He snarls.

'We know what makes a maggot a maggot and how to make a whelp a warrior. Stand alongside us, whelp and we'll make you a warrior yet.''The Scara know the hunt, the strength of a sudden strike, the panic you instill from the shadow, and the tastiest, easiest places to tear flesh from bone. We teach the pack the way and it is for the warg or any to do the rest.'

He shakes his fur.

'We need only brutality and cruelty to bring down our targets quickly and as painfully as possible. Our pack can teach you, but you must do the rest. We waste time by standing still. Choose us and run free.''Well done, I am amazed you had the attention span necessary to speak with them all. There may be hope for you yet. Now to the matter at hand. Choose. Choose a clan to represent while you fight for Angmar.

'All will welcome you. Freely shirk your allegiance like you have done your duty for so long. Drink of their blessing until you find a home that is welcoming to you. They are ordered to show no malice toward each other for now. This truce may not hold forever.

'Mordirith wants to see these Free Folk brought low, so the clans were convened to find the strongest among you and then to determine the best way to eliminate the forces here. Align yourself. That is all you need to do.'

She smiles deviously.

'Do your best to prove to the master what clans should remain here in the Ettenmoors fighting and slaughtering the Free Folk.'Assist the hunters dealing with acquiring meat, pelts, and bones from the herds of mammoth. Be wary of the Gauredain.Take down a herd of mammoth and be wary of the Gauredain who have encircled the herd.Collect mammoth bones from fresh kills (${NUMBER}/9)Collect mammoth meat from fresh kills (${NUMBER}/9)Collect mammoth pelts from fresh kills (${NUMBER}/9)Defeat terrible winter-tusks (${NUMBER}/3)Return to large stone where you arrived and find the scout.Return to the stone where you arrived to find the scout'Let us return to the Lossoth encampment.'Kergrim to the far north-west in Tûkurdul near Ashâgir ransacked a shipment from the west. They took the driver and the contents of his haul with them. Save the driver and recover his supplies.Your mission is to travel to Tûkurdul and recover supplies that got ransacked and save the driver if you can. Of course you should slay any kergrim you see in the area for good measure.Defeat kergrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ransacked supplies gathered (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Hello, friend! I am glad you were able to recover the supplies, though it is sad to hear about the driver. Let us return to Ub Nishir.'Maginard Foxbolt knows there are cave-claws causing trouble in Staddle and has some ideas of his own on how to deal with them.Maginard wants you to kick any thieving cave-claws you find inside the tunnel under Staddle. To do so safely, you must have a sturdy pair of kicking boots. Maginard told you of a nearby crate of such boots in the Staddle village centre.Get a pair of Claw Kickin' Boots from the crateMaginard wants you to kick any cave-claws you find inside the tunnel to the south-east of the Staddle village centre. Use your Claw Kickin' Boots to send the beasts flying.Kick thieving cave-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Everyone's going on about the thieving shrews, but there's not enough talk about the thieving cave-claws if you ask me. Of course, those worthless constables do nothing. I grew up out in the Shire proper, and the Bounders would never allow such things to happen, I tell you. No indeed, they would give those thieving cave-claws a swift kick that they wouldn't soon forget!

'If you're planning on going into that shrew-tunnel and you see a cave-claw, that's what you ought to do. Kick them so hard they'll think Bullroarer Took himself did it, and they won't come back, I promise you that!

'You'll want some sturdy boots, though. Cave-claws are right pointy. As a matter of fact, there's a crate of such boots just over yonder. Help yourself, most folk here don't want them.'

Maginard chuckles and wiggles his hairy toes.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>This crate contains sturdy boots of various sizes, perfect for kicking cave-claws. Maginard suggested you take a pair for yourself.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must slot the boots as a skill. To do so, drag the 'Claw Kickin' Boots' item from your inventory to your skill bar. You then use the skill on Thieving Cave-claws to advance the quest.</rgb>Scorpions near Dûlagig have been expanding their reach and are growing more aggressive in their attacks. Cull their number before they become an even great threat to Urmâkh.Defeat scorpions and destroy their burrows to cull their number.Set ablaze scorpion burrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat scorpions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat Tamâhu, the dread-scorpion.Defeat Tamâhu, the dread-scorpionFind the dread-scorpion Tamâhu'These scorpions make my skin crawl. I'm glad you were able to thin their number. Let's get back to Urmâkh to report the good news!'The Krahjarn clan boasts the strength and wisdom of leading from behind. Their skill with ranged weaponry and leadership, they claim, is unmatched. Accepting their blessing will turn your focus toward battling at a distance. Speak with their emissary to gain the Blessing of the Krahjarn.You may seek the blessing of the Krahjarn clan. All you need do is renounce all other clans.Speak with the Krahjarn emissary'Why stand at the front and face your enemy so close? Why smell them when they are not on your plate as your dinner? Why mingle with the lesser clans when you can rule over them? We are the Krahjarn. We are the leaders. We are the warriors who know best how to survive and command.''It is good you understand that command is better than servitude and so, you shall have our blessing.

'Take heed, warrior. You are no longer a maggot, though some may still say so. You are Krahjarn. You are better. You are smarter. You will not stride forward and fight when the distance is your greater ally.'Bob's daughter, Lalia, has gone missing, and Bob fears she may have gone off in search of the "Last Prince," a character in one of the tales Barliman Butterbur tells to travellers.Lalia was expected to be between the Northern Barrow and the Dead Spire where "The Last Prince" was said to be entombed, and that is exactly where you found her. You should approach the crying child.Approach LaliaYou found Lalia between the Northern Barrow and the Dead Spire as expected. You should talk to the crying child.Talk to LaliaLalia has asked you to help her get back to Bree safely. In addition, she has asked for your help finding the cloak she dropped somewhere on the Barrow-downs. You must protect her as she searches for her cloak, then leaves the Barrow-downs.Escort Lalia to safety'What a relief! It seems I know my daughter well. She actually <i>had</i> gone after that "Last Prince" of hers. Well, maybe she's learned her lesson and won't be so foolish in the future. I know I will certainly never come here again.

'I do hope I can survive her tweens. Maybe then she'll get some hobbit-sense. Maybe....''I came here to find "The Last Prince," like Mr. Butterbur talks about in his stories. I was going to find him, and then be with him forever and be his princess! But he wasn't here to be found! There's just all these skeletons and bones and walking dead! It isn't nice to go misleading young hobbits like that!

'When you are ready to go, could you help me get back home to Bree? I couldn't leave before, but now with a strong warrior like you here, I'm sure you can get me home safely!

'Oh, and I lost my cloak. I simply must find it or dad will yell at me something terrible!'Your mission is to travel to the Ekhamâti camp, defeat the dôla, and rob them of their gold in order to supply Mizâdi's forces.Your mission is to travel to the Ekhamâti camp, defeat the dôla, and rob them of their gold in order to supply Mizâdi's forces.Steal gold from Ekhamâti camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat OmurtókoDefeat KhisóntoDefeat PurombóroEscape the camp before reinforcements arrive!Escape the camp before reinforcements arrive'Quickly! We should return to Setokúli before reinforcements arrive.'Camelia Buttonbloom is beside herself with grief for a group of brave hobbits who entered the shrew-tunnel and have yet to return.Camelia has asked you to find the lost hobbits and return them to the surface. Or at least what is left of them.Find lost hobbits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found all four lost hobbits and given them directions back to the tunnel entrance. You should return to Camelia Buttonbloom just outside of the cave, south-east of the Staddle village centre.Talk to Camelia Buttonbloom'Going in the tunnel, are you? Be warned, others have gone in before you and have not returned! I fear they are lost forever, my poor, dear lost hobbits! If you find them... or what is left of them, please return them to us. They are so brave and do not deserve such a fate!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Bless me, you found them alive and well! They have already gone off to grab a pint somewhere, one of them said. What a relief! Surely you got there just in time to save them from the dangers within. You have my gratitude.'Many of the vendors have not returned from their break yet, and the market is crowded with impatient customers awaiting their goods.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>Customers of the Farmers Market are lining up at the vendor stall.

You should help fill as many orders as you can before your shift is over.Help as many customers as you can during your shift'Where are those simpletons? The other sellers have disappeared, surely to go off and enjoy the Faire. I will have their hides if they dare to show their faces after all these hours!

'I'm short of hands, ${PLAYER}, as you can surely see. Would you be so kind as to help me? There are many orders to be filled.''Please, don't waste any more time! See how the patrons clamour for our attention? Talk to them, not me!'Hunt bears to collect their meat to fill the hunter's larder.Hunt around the bear den and collect game meat that can be cured by the hunters.Collect game meat from bears (${NUMBER}/12)Defeat bears (${NUMBER}/12)Return to the stone near where you arrived and find the scout.Return to the scout near the stone where you arrived'Let us return to the lodge.'You have been tasked with repelling a pack of worms encroaching on Kidzul-kâlah.Your mission is to repel a pack of worms encroaching on Kidzul-kâlah.Defeat worms at Kidzul-kâlah (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Well done, ${PLAYER}! That ought to keep them at bay for a while! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'A note from Postmaster Proudfoot referencing the need for help within the Michel Delving Post Office.Make your way to Michel Delving and speak with Postmaster Proudfoot about the assistance that he requires at the Michel Delving Post Office.Speak with Postmaster Proudfoot at the Michel Delving Post OfficeSpeak with Postmaster Proudfoot to be let into the Post Office where you will be put to work sorting, stuffing, and preparing the post for delivery.Complete Mission: A Day at the Michel Delving PostReturn to Postmaster Proudfoot outside the Michel Delving post office and check in on how your day at the post went.Speak with Postmaster Proudfoot outside the Michel Delving Post OfficePost:

Help needed to sort post and stuff satchels for delivery. If you are willing, visit Postmaster Proudfoot outside the Michel Delving Post Office.

- Postmaster Proudfoot'Busy, busy, busy, friend.

'We post workers pride ourselves on delivering and keeping The Shire informed of goings on via the mail. Recently, an abundance of letters and dearth of workers has us barely making our scheduled rounds.

'I put out a call, and here you are.

'I need you to organize the post, stuff satchels, and move the full satchels where they belong.''So, friend, did you feel the pride that swells within the chest of every post worker in The Shire?

'We could always use another set of hands and eyes to help out around here. It is an art all its own, and you have better than many.

'If you are ever looking to join our ranks, please do not hesitate to return and submit a proper application with me.'A lovely day for pitching in on the farm without the fear of anything untoward happening at all.Close shrew burrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Repel craban invaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and speak with the Scout'See what a relaxing life you could lead? Oh dear. I did not expect this. Well, let us head back.'A hobbit farm is a happy place… usually. This farm, however, is seeing its fair share of trouble, and the owners are looking for some help in dealing with the nastiness that plagues their once happy plot.An odd request to help out on a nearby farm in Lhunach. Speak to the mission giver to head down to the farm and help.Complete the Mission: A Day on the FarmAfter an eventful day on the farm, it is time to return to the mission giver who asked you to go and help the famers with their work.'I have an interesting request. It seems a farmer nearby is having all manner of trouble with their crops. He needs a proper hand in gathering, protecting, and tending to everything on their property. Any chance you might be looking for a little work?''Not exactly work for an adventurer such as you eh, ${PLAYER}? Maybe this is the kind of thing that will bring you a measure of rest and recreation. What do you say, ready to work on the farm?''Was it as lovely as I expected it would be working on the farm? No? Well it seems that adventure has a way of finding you does it not, ${PLAYER}?'Yarikh is here in Evendim. Find him and recover the haversack for the mariner.You steel yourself for the challenge ahead. You can hear voices, boisterously cheering for the spoils they recovered.Defeat Corsairs in the ruins (${NUMBER}/12)Searching deeper within the ruins you hear Yarikh's voice speaking with his last lieutenant, Hilâma. Find them and confront them.Defeat HilâmaDefeat YarikhThe villains are gone. You have closed the circle of vengeance that began the mariner's tale many years ago. Collect his haversack and return to him.Collect the haversackReturn to the entrance and to Falnavar.Return to the entrance of the tombMake your way to the mariner.You have been tasked with rescuing dwarf scouts from the clutches of the hobgoblins.Find and free the captured dwarf scouts in Vorkodar.Free the first captured scoutFree the second captured scoutFree the third captured scoutFree the fourth captured scout'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'None have feasted on the remains of Scatha's larder with such fervour as a foul worm known to the dwarves as Stúrkvith the Bloated.Your mission is to defeat the gluttonous rock-worm, Stúrkvith the Bloated, who now dwells in Scatha's Larder.Defeat Stúrkvith the Bloated'You've done well to put that beast down, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'The Ordâkhai deserters paid handsomely for assistance to escape, but your efforts have them cornered.The bandits never intended to join the full Ordâkhai forces to the north. They were paid great sums of stolen riches to protect the escape of many Ordâkhai deserters. Your efforts thwarted the escape of many, and those left behind can now face justice.Defeat the deserters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy the makeshift Ordâkhai camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The deserters are defeated and the remnants of their encampment are destroyed. Find Mizâdi's scout to return to the encampment.Find Mizâdi's scout'No remnant of their atrocities remain. The curs deserved no other fate. Come, let us return.'Your mission is to travel to Shegdush and gather food for the people of Iridír from the chickens and boars in the area.Your mission is to travel to Shegdush and gather eggs and thin the numbers of chickens and boars in the area.

Speak to Setokúli to travel.Complete Mission: A Hearty MealYour mission is to travel to Shegdush and gather eggs and thin the numbers of chickens and boars in the area. Return with the scout to Setokúli with this report.'Good to see you ${PLAYER}. We are in need of some eggs here in Iridír to produce a much desired meal.

'Can you travel to Shegdush and collect as many eggs as you find? Please also thin the numbers of chickens and boars in the area before it becomes a danger to others.'Your mission is to travel to Shegdush and gather food for the people of Iridír from the chickens and boars in the area.'Wonderful! The eggs you have managed to gather will be put to great use for the meal. Please accept this reward for your troubles.'You have been tasked with thwarting a group of stone-giants within the rocky slopes of Câr Bronach.You should destroy worm nests, boulder piles, and sour the giants' soup.Destroy boulder piles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy worm nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sour the giants' soup (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to the entrance of the dungeon.You should return to the entrance of the dungeon'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the stone-giants sent running, Câr Bronach should remain safe for now. Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'The mariner begins his tale at the beginning; within the confines of a small inn in the port city of Pelargir.The time was mid-autumn in the harbour town of Pelargir. I arrived only a moment before my friend. As he entered, he approached and we spoke.Speak with the marinerI made my way toward the bar, not noticing yet that the inn was bereft of clients, something that should have alerted me to the curious nature of the night. Along the way, a posting caught my eye....Read the posterThe poster was meant to entice the reader to the sea, to service, on some it had that effect. On others...Speak with the marinerWe made our way to the bar and took up the flagons....Speak with the marinerI raised my flagon and awaited the same of my friend. Our toast, however, was only the beginning of a harrowing event....Drink with the marinerFor in the back of the inn, Corsairs had set to plunder. Killing the innkeep after he dared ask them for payment for the drinks we now consumed....Speak with the MarinerThere were no more words between us. The Corsairs drew blades and we fought. It were not luck that brought us through....Defeat Corsair cutthroats (${NUMBER}/6)Was it in the commotion that the captain appeared? It was unclear. I only know that after the fight was done, there they were....Speak with the CaptainThe Captain's words lingered with me as I rejoined my friend.Return to the Mariner'I did not expect any of this tonight, my friend. Perhaps, come the morning I may visit this ship and speak with this captain. I have never been so exhilarated.''Another night of libations to clear the dirt from our throats. This life, my friend, is lacking. How I yearn for something beyond the dust of the road, or the fires of a smith shop.

'Where is adventure and wonder?'

He pauses, looking sullen.

'Youth is wasted on wonder, when in our most fruitful years we are tied to the land, then to a partner, and then to children. What nonsense. That life is not for me. I want more.

'I want wonder! I want every day to forgo the rote mechanics of life and be new and inspiring. I want to never know what lay on the other side of the horizon.

'Alas, I am but me. You are but you. And we, together, are merely labourers with only a few coppers between us to seek our wonder at the bottom of a mug.

'Come, let us enjoy the night before I grow too grim.'Gondor expects...

and Gondor must not, and will not, be disappointed.

Recruits wanted to serve on the seas against the threat out of the South.
Pay, food, glory, and honour await those who would serve the people of Gondor.

Make your mark at the Nenglor in Pelargir harbour.'For the people of Gondor, yes. I see the merit in that, but our stewards are degenerate and never leave the safety of Minas Tirith. When was it they last set foot outside the white city?'

He scoffs and looks toward the bar.

'The innkeep must have known of our arrival. Come, my friend, let us toast to our lives... as they are and ever shall be.''Maybe I am too hasty to dismiss that offer. After all, there is something to serving the people of Gondor and not the corrupt leaders who reach into our pockets for coin or extract their price in blood.

'Is it then, that I fear my strength would be wasted not on hoisting sails but on spreading pitch to patch the leaks?

'Would we, perhaps, learn better the skills of swordsman, so that we are not skewered on the blade of some Corsair? Or, would we be a sacrifice in early battle so our captain could gain advantage and keep our coin?

'I think, I fear that I would be under the heel of a terrible captain who wants only glory and naught the thing they try to sell in that post.

'Listen to me ramble. I am sorry, friend. I fear I am in a grim state this night. Let us lighten the mood. A toast to kinship, and to friends who travel the road that rises to meet us on our journey.'The sound of plunderers echoed in the tavern. The flagons were not meant for us, after all.

'We best be prepared to draw weapons, friend. They are from Umbar and the very Corsairs that threaten Gondor.''You fight well. You should consider joining my crew. You just saw firsthand the menace that Umbar presents.

'Come down to the harbour on the morrow and speak with me.'You have been tasked with stopping the Tarkrîp Orcs before they collapse the mines of Writhenset.Use the summoning horn at the beginning of the tunnel to summon Radhril to your side.Pick up the summoning hornYou should talk to Radhril.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Use the Call Radhril skill and talk to RadhrilYou should destroy bombs and powder crates.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Destroy bombs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy powder crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to the mine entrance.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Return to the mine entrance'I commend your efforts, ${PLAYER}! Come, let us return and report our success to the Free Peoples.''It is of the utmost importance that we destroy every bomb and case of black powder that we find within these tunnels. We can not let these Orcs collapse the mine. Now then, there is much to be done.'You have been tasked with searching for signs of a dwarf-presence in the distant snow-fields.Investigate dwarf-made tools left in the snow.Investigate lost tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find written evidence of the previous dwarves.Recover lost journal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! A whole expedition lost in the snow, eh? You'll have to show that Journal to Ausma when we get back!'Your mission is to travel to Maurûsh and attack the Orcs before they can regroup and regain their strength.Your mission is to travel to Maurûsh and attack the Orcs before they can regain their strength.

Speak to Ashâmi to travel.Complete Mission: A Moment of HopeYou have successfully weakened the Orcs in Maurûsh. Return with the scout to Ashâmi with this report.'${PLAYER}, we must take this chance while we have it. The Orcs in Maurûsh are weakened and I ask that you go and attack before they can regain their strength.''${PLAYER}, your task is to travel to Maurûsh and attack the Orcs before they can regain their strength.''I am glad to hear that the forces at Maurûsh remain weakened. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Within the ruined walls of Kêr Bréin, the cold-drakes of the Frost-horde have laid a new clutch of eggs.Your mission is to destroy cold-drake eggs at Kêr Bréin.Destroy cold-drake eggs at Kêr Bréin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'That will show the Frost-horde, ${PLAYER}! Let us report your success to Hórin!'Your mission is to reach the Ekhamâti camp where they are holding prisoners and free any you can. Then put an end to the executioner before he can harm any more people.Your mission is to reach the Ekhamâti camp where they are holding prisoners and free any that you can. Then put an end to the executioner before he can harm any more people.

Speak to Setokúli to travel.Complete Mission: A Personal PleaYour mission is to reach the Ekhamâti camp where they are holding prisoners and free any that you can. Then put an end to the executioner before he can harm any more people.'There is an urgent matter that is in need of your skills, ${CLASS}.

'We have discovered a camp where prisoners are being held awaiting execution. I beg of you to go there now and save as many as you can. Be sure to put an end to the executioner himself to stop his terror.'Your mission is to reach the Ekhamâti camp where they are holding prisoners and free any that you can. Then put an end to the executioner before he can harm any more people.'Your return is most welcome, and the prisoners you freed are being tended to now. They owe you their lives.

'I thank you for your help and for stopping the executioner from doing any further harm to our people.'Locate and destroy the rotting food stores held by the brigands in Gaervarad.Destroy unsecured food barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'This is not the way that Men should live. Glad to know that you are here to help. Let us return to our settlement.'Brigands in Gaervarad stockpile their wares in open containers without properly curing or cooking the food before storing. This practice will lead to disease if it is not halted. While dealing with the brigand's unsafe food storage practices, you'll also be able to cull their number down as an added benefit.Speak with the mission giver and make your way to the ruins of Gaervarad to destroy the spoiling supplies held there by the brigands.Complete Mission: A Plague of MenAfter entering the ruins, dispatching a number of enemies, and destroying a good number of the rotting barrels of food, you should return to the mission giver and tell them of your success.Return to the mission giver and tell them of your success'Hail ${PLAYER}, there is a matter of importance as great as the arrival of invaders from the south. It appears that the brigands inhabiting the ruins of Gaervarad are not the most sanitary lot. Worse still, the provisions they have stolen from farmsteads and trappers in the region waste away in makeshift storage not suitable for... well... swine.

'Now, I know that this seems a meager task, but the foodstuff there is wont to spread disease if it is not destroyed. If you are willing to undertake the effort, we are willing to reward you for entering those ruins and destroying a good number of their food stores.

'What's more, you'll surely encounter a few of those ruffians when you are there, and thinning their number will only bolster the surrounding area. What say you?''Remember ${PLAYER}, the goal is to destroy the festering and foetid food that the brigands are hoarding, but thinning their number is an added benefit.''It is a shame that we needed to destroy the food. There are many here and in these lands that would be better served by getting that food for their tables. Alas, the greed and evil of some Men is simply too much to overcome.

'You have done well in helping us with this, ${PLAYER}.'Your mission is to steal weapons from within a nearby Ekhamâti camp and defeat as many soldiers as you can. You must make it out before reinforcements arrive.Your mission is to steal weapons from within a nearby Ekhamâti camp and defeat as many soldiers as you can. You must make it out before reinforcements arrive.

Speak to Setokúli to travel.Complete Mission: A Surfeit of WeaponsYour mission is to steal weapons from within a nearby Ekhamâti camp and defeat as many soldiers as you can. You must make it out before reinforcements arrive.'${PLAYER}, there is an Ekhamâti camp in Khûd Zagin where their soldiers appear to be stockpiling weapons.

'We are in need of your help to steal as many of their weapon caches as possible to hinder their attacks. I ask that you defeat any soldiers you run into during your time there as well.'Your mission is to steal weapons from within a nearby Ekhamâti camp and defeat as many soldiers as you can. You must make it out before reinforcements arrive.'You have done well to take the weapons from the hands of the Ekhamâti. We will put these to good use.'Intended to feed the war effort for as long as necessary in Elderslade, a massive cache of Orkish provisions has been found in Bekâr-zarakh.Your mission is to destroy the cache of Orkish provisions stored in Bekâr-zarakh.Destroy Orkish provisions in Bekâr-zarakh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})After destroying the cache of Orkish provisions stored in Bekâr-zarakh, a furious Orc has blocked your escape and challenged you. You must defeat Goglugúth.Defeat Goglugúth'That ought to slow them down a bit, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with collecting the abandoned supplies scattered throughout Stramvárth.Recover supplies.Recover supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! That is the last of the salvageable supplies. Let us return and report your success!'Reports reached the village that there are trees walking around the hillside. This cannot be so, and you have been drafted to investigate.Discover the walking trees and eliminate them (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and speak with a Scout'Wood-trolls? What are they? Creeping creatures! We need to return to the village and warn them!'Something unnatural moves through the woods in the Stoor-vales. Hobbit scouts ask for assistance in discovering what is happening to the forest surrounding their homes.Something is lurking in the woods in the Stoor-vales and hobbit scouts want someone to look into what it is. Speak with the mission giver at Clegur to assist.Complete the Mission: Aberrations of NatureThere were wood trolls lurking in the woods and ruins. This is not a good development and you should let the mission giver know.As you approach you hear the hobbit mutter, 'this simply does not make any sense…' They look up at you.

'Sorry, I was just reading a report from the woods not far from here where one of the villagers said they saw a twisted tree stand straight up and tear the bark off another tree nearby. It must be someone who had a little too much at the tavern and went wandering... right?'

A brief few seconds of thought and they continue, 'Then again, mayhap there is something going on. Would you be willing to look into this?''I am not certain what you will encounter there, friend. I only know what my neighbours have been saying. They tell me that the trees are walking and moving of their own accord. That cannot be a good thing, can it?''Trolls!? D-did you say, trolls? Indeed! This is terrifying news. We are not equipped to deal with trolls. Best it was you out there, I would not have been so successful.'You have been tasked with defending the bridge builders of the Hadhodiant from a potential ambush.Take your post upon the bridge.Take your post upon the bridgeKeep your post and defend the bridge builders of the Hadhodiant.Keep your post and defend the bridge builders<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the bridge unguarded</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow the bridge workers to be defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'Your mission is to travel to Sar-kidul and take the fight to the Orcs.Your mission is to travel to Sar-kidul and take the fight to the Orcs.

Speak to Ashâmi to travel.Complete Mission: All Out BattleYou have successfully eliminated Orcs in Sar-kidul. Return with the scout to Ashâmi with this report.'${PLAYER} I am glad you are here. I would request that you travel to Sar-kidul and take the fight to the Orcs. They have grown weak at the camp and now is the time to strike!''${PLAYER}, your task is to travel to Sar-kidul and take the fight to the Orcs.''I have heard of your victory over Madmurúk and the Orcs in Sar-kidul, ${PLAYER}. You have done well.'Watch-towers in the brigand encampment provide them a greater visibility over the approaching land. A large force cannot approach, but a small number can, and you have been drafted to remove their threat.Place black powder under watch-towers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and speak with the scout'Seeing those watch-towers burn gives us some hope to drive them out of this fort. You have done well. Let us return.'Watch-towers at the brigand encampment in Swanfleet provide a distinct advantage to the forces there. There is a desire to undermine their use by turning the tools of the enemy against them.Removing the enemy's ability to see over long distances will give an advantage to attackers making their way against the forces of brigands. You should visit the mission giver in Lhan Garan to begin your assault.Complete the Mission: Among the Watch-towersAfter some effort you were able to neutralize the watch-towers and some of the enemy stationed at the encampment. Return to Lhan Garan and tell the mission giver of your success.'When an enemy can see you coming from a great distance it puts you at a disadvantage. When that enemy is entrenched that disadvantage is even greater. At the brigand encampment, we have both issues at once.

'The brigands there built tall watch-towers that give them a clear view of the surrounding wilds. Any offensive that might be launched against them is immediately at a disadvantage. We also know that the brigands employ a volatile powder of some kind that we may be able to use in our favour.

'If we reposition some of that powder at the foot of the watch-towers we may be able to destroy them and take back the advantage. Are you willing to assist?''The advantage that the watch-towers provide is great. We cannot amass a force that will challenge them without them knowing that we are there. But, if you are willing to infiltrate, perhaps you will be able to sneak in and provide us the cover we need to begin a counter assault.''We shall watch them more closely and when the time is right, we will organize an assault of our own. We best plan as they will likely restore the watch-towers quickly.'After the War of the Dwarves and Orcs was ended, Orcs returned to Gundabad and laid claim to the countless dwarf-made weapons left abandoned in its halls. Many are now held as trophies by the Orcs of Bekâr-zarakh.Your mission is to reclaim dwarf-made weapons held as trophies by the Orcs in Bekâr-zarakh.Collect dwarf-made weapons at Bekâr-zarakh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'You've done well to reclaim what was taken from us, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with defending the fortress of Skarháld from a Frost-horde assault.Defeat the Frost-horde assault.Defeat the Frost-horde assault'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the Frost-horde assault defeated, let us return and report your success!'You have been tasked with dispatching the Orc archers defending Shathur-munzu.Defeat the Orc archers outside Shathur-munzu.Defeat Gundabad black-arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with surveying the ruins of Stormwall.Survey Stormwall.Survey Stormwall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Have you finished surveying Stormwall, ${PLAYER}? Then let us report back to Hórin!'Far above the battlefield, the ballistae of Ashmâr-zarakh keep silent watch over all that would seek to breach the gates of Gundabad.Your mission is to destroy ballistae in Ashmâr-zarakh.Destroy ballistae 