AL})Defeat poisonous wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy warg cages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to the entrance of dungeon.Return to the entrance of the dungeon'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the Angmarim warg pens properly disrupted, let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'Brigands moved into the ruins of Nímbarth. You have been tasked with driving them out of the ruins.Kill half-orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Slay the half-orc captainFind the Scout'Seemed a simple effort for you. Nice to know you fight alongside us. Let us return to the encampment.'Brigands set roost in the ruins at Nímbarth. They are not welcome. You are asked to make your way there to defeat their leader and thin their numbers.At the ruins of Nímbarth, a band of ruffians and brigands assaults the populace and lays waste to the beauty of the once great ruins. You are tasked with going forth and eliminating the brigand leader and their followers.Complete the Mission: Brigands in NímbarthAfter defeating the brigands, you should return to the mission giver and tell them of your success so that you may receive your well-earned rewards.Return to the mission giver'A word if I may. There are ruins called Nímbarth not far from here that are overrun by brigands. We would like to see them removed so that we might find some solace whilst travelling near the ruins. Too often these aggressive Men harry our folk and cause irreparable damage to the populace. Will you help us?''Be wary, for though they are a broadly disorganized group, they still pose a threat. I will send a scout to watch your progress.''Another victory for you, friend. We are all indebted for every effort you undertake. To say that we are grateful is an understatement. We owe you much. We hope this shall suffice.'You have been tasked with defeating the spider menace within the mines of Writhenset.Use the summoning horn at the beginning of the tunnel to summon Radhril to your side.Pick up the summoning hornYou should talk to Radhril.

