'Snítha, ${PLAYER} has a point -- you've always been the more numbers-minded of us two. Why not partner with me? We'd both get to focus on what we enjoy most, and we'd be able to leave this all behind. Everything that father tried to push on us.''Reckon the two of us will be alright without a mediator for the time being. Not that I don't appreciate what you've done! This just... finally feels like a conversation I can handle.'You have been tasked with recording the etchings of buried dwarves.Record etchings from the dwarf-sarcophagi in Atkat-darag, and defeat the tomb-robbers.Investigate sarcophagi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat tomb-robbers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to the entrance of the tomb.Return to the entrance of the tomb'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let's get those etchings back to camp!'You have been tasked with defeating the stone-claws who burrow too close to the Hadhodiant.Clear the stone-claw menace from the Hadhodiant.Destroy stone-claw burrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Clear the stone-claw menace from the Hadhodiant (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'You have been tasked with thwarting Angmarim bat-keepers in Gundabad.Defeat Angmarim bat-keepers, destroy their vile draughts, and free the fledgling bats.Destroy vile draughts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Free fledgling bats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Angmarim bat-keepers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to the entrance of dungeon.Return to the entrance of the dungeon'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the Angmarim bat-keepers defeated, let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'Having scaled the ruins of Caranost, you find yourself near the Orc command. Fight through the defenders within the ruins and engage the leader of the tribe that makes the ruin their home. This will surely break the Orcs' will and drive them back into hiding.Defeat Orcs at the Caranost Command Post (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat KrovlutFind the Scout'The Orcs seem undeterred though their leader falls in battle. Is there more to this infestation? Quickly return to Baglan and tell them what you learned here.'Deeper still in the ruins of Caranost, rumour spreads of a powerful Orc warrior leading the forces there. Go forth and defeat this White Hand Orc for the defence of the Free People.Enter the ruins of Caranost and scour the command area for the leader of the Orc forces there. Scouts say that it bears the symbol of the White Hand. This should make identifying the true enemy easier.Complete the Mission: Caranost Command PostWith your victory over the White Hand Orc leader secured, you should return to the mission giver and inform them of the victory. There is sure to be a reward for your efforts.Return to the mission giver and tell them of your victory'Caranost remains under the control of the Orcs and worse, it seems, they are bolstered now by a force of the White Hand. Or, perhaps, just led by one. The White Hand began appearing not long ago, but the forces bearing the symbol are well-armed and vicious. Will you venture back into Caranost and seek the destruction of this savage Orc leader?''The Orcs within the ruins of Caranost are vile and are led by a fearsome foe. You would do well to use caution as you search the ruins for their leader.''It is good to know that our scouts are reliable and observant. It is better to know that your strength of arms does not waver. You are truly a value to our efforts, ${PLAYER}. Please, take your rewards with the gratitude and thanks with which it is given.'Once a bastion of the Kingdom of Cardolan, the ruins of Caranost now teem with vile Orcs. Here in the courtyard at the foot of the grand steps, the savage Orcs established a small outpost to thwart would-be heroes from rooting them out of the ruins. You are here to see that this foothold does not last.Clear the Orcs out of the courtyard at Caranost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'Another victory. Let us return to Andrath and tell them the good news.'A grueling battle still brews within the ruins of Caranost. The Free forces press their advantage and look to take control of the courtyard at the foot of the grand steps that lead deeper into the ruins.Speak with the mission giver and let them know that you are prepared to make your way to the courtyard at the foot of Caranost. There you will face off against the slavering Orc horde.Complete the Mission: Caranost CourtyardWith the courtyard cleared, you must now return to the mission giver and let them know of your success.'${PLAYER}, there is a hope that if we can score a victory at the foot of Caranost, we can further our efforts to drive the Orcs from the ruin. If you are willing, we would task you with an assault on the courtyard there. Drive out all of the enemy and we should be able to strike deeper still into the heart of the enemy forces.''Fight well, ${PLAYER}. I expect that you will be as victorious as you ever are when we ask so much of you.''I heard that the battle was fierce, and that in the end the number of dead Orcs was great. You are a valued defender, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps, with the efforts shown by you and others we will yet retake the old homes of Men in these lands.'You have been tasked with rescuing miners from the partially collapsed cave of Mesem-gairu.Enter the cavern.Enter the cavernRescue the miners and defuse the powder kegs before the cave collapses completely!Rescue the miners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defuse powder kegs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Exit the cavern after rescuing the miners and defusing the powder kegs!<rgb=#FF0000>Rescue the miners and defuse the powder kegs before the cave collapses completely!</rgb>'We thank you for the rescue. One minute, we were mining crystals, and the next, the cavern shook and starting collapsing all around us. It would seem that goblins had entered the caverns before us, and lined the tunnels with hidden powder kegs. I am just glad that only a couple of the powder kegs detonated!'Time for change. Change of the leader of those pesky Hobbits in Hoarhallow. Time to get the mayor. Get him good!Slaughter Hobbits to Draw out the MayorHunt Down Mayor Wat Mudbottom'I saw it all, ${PLAYER}. The little Hobbit running around all trying to stay alive. You done good. We'll all eat well tonight. Get back to Gramsfoot and get your rewards.'Although the Dwarves of Gabilshathûr are no longer trapped beyond the Rammas Deluon, its miners face new challenges as the creatures of Angmar reclaim the fallen realm.Your mission is to aid the dwarves of Gabilshathûr in repelling an infestation of blade-beaks.Seal blade-beak burrows at Gabilshathûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to aid the dwarves of Gabilshathûr in repelling an infestation of blade-beaks.Rally to the centre of GabilshathûrYour mission is to aid the dwarves of Gabilshathûr in repelling an infestation of blade-beaks.Defeat the massive blade-beak'That ought to keep them at bay for a time, ${PLAYER}! Let us return!'Your mission is to travel to Hordírid to the north-west to stop the dangerous Huorns and to cleanse the corrupted trees in the area.Your mission is to travel to Hordírid to the north-west to stop the dangerous Huorns and to cleanse the corrupted trees in the area.

