You should talk to her.Talk to GolwenThe lilting notes of the flute carry themselves above the ocean breeze.Golwen gives one wayward glance towards the shoreline before dragging her eyes back to the earth.

'I... I will be fine. I will not let my fear stop me from paying my respects to Rikháwi.

'When she was buried at sea, I was unable to attend. I had still been recovering from my injuries; the shock hadn't quite worn off, either. I don't believe I fully understood Rikháwi had died until many days later. I could not say good-bye to her then, but I can say it now.

'Let us construct a cairn for her from the stones here.''Many thanks, and for the flowers as well. She would have liked them.'

Golwen takes a deep, steadying breath.'Well, it is done. I still do not know if peace will find me, but maybe it is possible now. One painful memory does not unravel the many happy ones I shared with Rikháwi. It was a long and arduous journey that led me to this understanding, but I am here now.

