You should talk to Golwen.Talk to Golwen'I will return one day. I must.'The corners of Golwen's mouth lift ever-so-slightly as she gazes upon the ship.

'I have worked onboard this ship for many years. I hope to continue doing so for many years to come.

'There is the captain. Come, I will introduce you.''As for your share of the work, there are barrels to be unloaded onto the pier, and stains to be wiped from the deck.'

He studies you with keen eyes.

'Unless Golwen has become adept at keeping secrets from the rest of us, I assume the two of you did not meet until very recently. I didn't expect her to make a friend on land so soon, though it is comforting to know she can change. I wonder....'

He shakes his head.

'Forgive my rambling. This is the time for work, not idle chatter. I'll leave you to it.'Golwen unfurls a part of the sail to show off her handiwork: a collection of careful patches and stitches spanning the fabric, ensuring the sail's continued function for future voyages.

'The captain understands the value of honest labour. Talk to him now, and he will let me return to the crew.'He sighs.

'Golwen misunderstands. I am not worried about her capabilities, but rather, the state of her mind. She has begun thinking of herself only in terms of her usefulness to the ship and its functions. I had hoped that sending her away would force her to reconsider, but it seems my actions have only made things worse. She needs time to heal, away from the sea.

'She has no loved ones left on land. She will not listen to her fellow crew-mates, and even I cannot seem to stop her. Yet I wonder, ${PLAYER}, if an outsider like you can.

'If you intend to be her friend, then I charge you with this duty: see to it that she spends some time simply living.''Orders must be clear and concise -- do this, fix that. An order to rest makes no sense. Ugh! Nevertheless, it is an order that I must follow; the question is how. Without the ship, I have nothing to do, and nowhere to go.

'Your efforts to persuade the captain may have been unsuccessful, but I am grateful all the same.

