You should eat them with Golwen.Eat the omelettes with GolwenYou should talk to Golwen.Talk to GolwenThe two of you spend the rest of the meal eating in silence.'Since we went out to sea, I have been craving omelettes. Eggs do not keep well on voyages and chickens do not survive for long, so it is a strictly land-only dish for me.

'I hope you are better at cooking than I am. The life of a sailor does not demand anything beyond "edible."

'First...'

She sighs at the sight of the bustling market-place.

'Please procure eggs from the grocer. I will make space for us to cook at the Artisans' Quarter to the north-east.''I hope that grocer did not cause too much trouble. Haggling is... not my strong suit. You have my gratitude for shouldering that burden. Allow me to crack the eggs.'

Golwen gets to work. She falls into a rhythm of expertly cracking two eggs at a time -- a comfortable rhythm that she seems quite familiar with. In this fleeting moment, her usually-creased brow has relaxed.'Now then, how long should we leave the omelettes over the fire?'Golwen thoughtfully chews a bite and swallows.

'I am... pleased we were able to do this together. It has been quite some time since I last cooked these myself. More than a year, in fact.

'I'd kept this tradition with a friend, to signal the end of one voyage and the start of another. Obviously, this is no longer the case.'

