Wanted: Assistance with the procurement of honeycombs from a difficult position outside of Bree. If interested, speak with Lolo Wendingway at the cross-roads of Staddle, Combe, and Bree.

- Lolo'Well met! I must confess, I had little hope that my notice would draw much patronage, being as vague as it was. Yet it gladdens me to see that there remain folk in these days who are willing to lend aid to another.

'Now, to the matter. I have a friend who seeks to begin a modest enterprise in the keeping of bees for honey. I told her there was no finer place to seek such sweetness than the bear dens nearby; and, for reasons of my own, I may have spoken somewhat too boldly of my ability to gather samples of honeycomb for her.

'Thus have I found myself in a rather uncomfortable position. My first efforts served only to stir the bears to wrath, and I must admit, with some shame, that I fled.

'It is my hope that you may prevail where I, alas, did not.''You have succeeded? Somehow I knew that you would. You bear the look of one well able to meet whatever perils may arise. I shall see to it that these honeycombs find their way safely to my friend. She will be most pleased with me—and, I trust, no less pleased than I am with you.

'I thank you most heartily for your aid. Would that I had more to offer you, my friend.''Have a care among the bears. I fear my taunts have done naught but rouse their wrath beyond its wont. They are sorely stirred, and seem most eager to defend the honeycomb that both they and I covet.'A terrible pack of Wargs dwells within the shadows of Valdhellir, posing a continued threat to the war effort.Your mission is to collect hides from the Wargs in Valdhellir.Collect hides from the Wargs in Valdhellir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'You've done well, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with defeating the Huorns in Grazadh-gropor.Defeat the corrupted Huorns in Grazadh-gropor.Defeat corrupted Huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'You have been tasked with defeating the Gate of Gath Uior from allies of the Iron Crown.Secure the Gate of Gath Uior.Secure the Gate of Gath UiorRepair the broken barricades.Repair the broken barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to the Elven defences.Return to the Elven defences'I thank you for coming to our aid. Since the Rangers departed, we have been able to hold the Gate of Gath Uior. Recently it has been difficult with the Iron Crown renewing their efforts to expand out from Angmar. You have assisted us and that assistance will not be forgotten. May your travels be swift and safe, my friend.'The Ordâkhai forces are proving relentless in their attempt to recover the scorpions they lost. You are asked to further diminish their ability to recover the scorpions by sabotaging their containers.Your efforts to slow the Ordâkhai incursion toward the overrun town west of their settlement has proven difficult. Mizâdi's scouts wish to change tactics. Sabotage the materials the Ordâkhai would use to contain and transport the scorpions.Sabotage a well-built crate (${NUMBER}/6)Sabotage a well-built cage (${NUMBER}/6)With the crates and cages sabotaged, you are ready to return to the encampment. Search for Mizâdi's scout near where you arrived and return to safety.Find Mizâdi's scout'When they attempt to collect the scorpions, they will be met with the same outcome as before. The boxes and cages will fail. Let us return to the camp.'You have been asked to help identify infiltrators in the town of Herne. You are to ask for details on joining Sharkey's ranks and determine how many in the town might be aligned with the enemy out of the south.Find your way to the scout'It's good to know that not every new visitor in the town is aligned with the enemy. Still, there is more work to be done. Let us return.'Speak with suspicious-looking villagers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Herne saw a fair bit of trouble recently, and the arrival of suspicious new folk has the town on edge. Scouts are concerned that the town is in danger from outside and hope that someone with your reputation might be willing to assist.Speak with the mission giver and alert them that you are prepared to visit Herne at night to discuss the intent of the suspicious folk lurking about the town square.Complete the Mission: InfiltrationYou have discovered that there are nefarious elements mixing in with other refugees making their way to Herne. You must return to the mission giver and tell them of this development.'What I am about to ask you, ${PLAYER}, is something that pains me to do.

'The township of Herne could be in danger. Recently, many folks who are not known in the town have been arriving from other areas, likely because of the encroaching Men and Uruks from the south.

'The mayor and other townsfolk are concerned that there might be a certain element trying to infiltrate the town. Now, it is possible that this is just a bit of alarmist reaction, but we cannot be too sure.

'What we are asking is that you approach any of these newcomers and determine their intentions in the town. Can you help?''I dislike using subterfuge to find these miscreants, but it seems that we might do best to employ their own tactics against them. Speak with those out and about at night and ask them if they serve Sharkey, when they expose their allegiance bring them to justice.''Your efforts have made Herne safer, ${PLAYER}. Sadly, it seems that Herne will need to be very cautious about the possibility of infiltration for some time to come. This concern is not yours, but that of the town's leadership.

'They will be warned and counseled.

'Thank you for this assistance.'Brilliant gem-stones illuminate the Crystal Tunnels beneath Skarháld, but beware, for foes lurk in the shadows.You have been tasked with collecting pure beryl in the Crystal Tunnels beneath Skarháld.Collect pure beryl in the Crystal Tunnels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Very good, ${PLAYER}! This beryl shall serve us well in the days to come. Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'Wargs make the hills their home and collect an impressive number of bones. It is unclear if the bones belong to the free folk or other victims. Regardless, the threat from these beasts is too great to let them remain.Defeat GorgostDefeat BrogmarshDefeat RauzghukDefeat wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'Wargs are always nasty business and when they are as powerful as those were, terrible days, friend. Let us return to our base.'Along the hilltops in Swanfleet there is a group of dens where vicious wargs bed down, feast, and terrorize the populace. You are tasked with the grim duty of hunting down the warg matrons that keep the rest of the pack in line.You are asked to make your way into the hills to find three warg matrons who lead a pack of the vile beasts there. Speak with the mission giver in Lhan Garan to begin this mission.Complete the Mission: Into the PitsThe warg matrons were present in the pit and they were fearsome. You were victorious. Return to the mission giver in Lhan Garan and tell them of the success.'Grim news, ${PLAYER}. Wargs in the hills surrounding the town grow more aggressive, and it seems that there are leaders, or at the very least, tenders who drive their murderous attacks. Our scouts know the location of these feral things, but they show a strength unnatural that terrifies most of our unseasoned warriors.

'Would you help? There are three wargs in those hills that we believe are the leaders. Each with distinctive markings that set them apart from the rest. They should be easy to identify.

'Slaying, on the other hand... well, that is the difficulty is it not?''A word of warning before you go: avoid the pointy fangs and sharp claws. They will rend and tear your flesh if they pierce your armour.

'Good luck, ${PLAYER}.''With the matrons eliminated, the remainder of the pack should be far easier to handle. Still, these beasts are far more fearsome than a pack of wolves, and where they roam, Orcs and uruks are sure to follow. Thank you for your efforts, ${PLAYER}.'You have been tasked with defeating the half-orc forces gathered at the entrances to the mines of Writhenset.Use the summoning horn outside the East-delf to summon Radhril to your side.Pick up the summoning hornYou should talk to Radhril.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Use the Call Radhril skill and talk to RadhrilYou should defeat half-orc overseers and destroy mining supplies and mining carts.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Defeat the half-orc overseer (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy mining supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy mining carts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to the small cabin near the East-delf.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Return to the small cabin near the East-delf'I commend your efforts, ${PLAYER}! Come, let us return and report our success to the Free Peoples.''These half-orcs do not just guard the entrances to the mines. This is a mining operation as well. First, we should find and defeat the overseers of this mining operation. I am sure there will be one stationed at each Delf. We should also destroy what tools they have brought to excavate the mine. I am ready when you are.'After traversing the Redhorn Pass, a growing band of goblins seeks to capture Kidzul-kâlah and set siege to the Vales of Anduin.You have been tasked with repelling the goblin invasion at Kidzul-kâlah and sealing the Redhorn Pass.Find a way to seal the Redhorn Pass and stop the goblin invasion'You've done well, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'Ordâkhai and Utûgi carrying wood, tools, and leading workers to a patch of flat land not far from the great river to the south must be investigated to understand what threat they may pose to Mizâdi's forces in the Hatokáli Fells.Find the Ordâkhai and Utûgi work-site to the west. Examine the tools they brought with them and record your findings before delivering them to back to the scouts.Record your findings about the toolsYou have recorded information about the tools in your journal. Now destroy the wooden planks so they cannot be used.Destroy the wooden planks (${NUMBER}/6)The planks are destroyed and the tools documented. Find Mizâdi's scout to return to the encampment.Find Mizâdi's scout'Interesting... these are ship-building materials. Let us return to camp with this information.'A notice from Ora asking for interested hunters to help to stock larders in Forochel.Find your way to the main encampment of the Lossoth in Forochel and speak with Ora.Speak with Ora at the main Lossoth Camp in ForochelComplete the mission: It's Always Winter in Forochel.Complete Mission: It's Always Winter in ForochelReturn to Ora and let her know that her hunters have received your support and that you recovered the much needed supplies.Return to Ora at Pynti-peldot in ForochelPost:

Our hunters require aid with stocking our larders as a potent chill covers our land. Those interested should report to me at our main encampment in Forochel.

- Ora'It is high sun, and yet another day passes beneath the cold sky. Our larders grow bare, while our enemies creep ever closer.

'Our hunters had cornered a small herd of mammoths, intending to take them for their meat, pelts, and bones. We would waste nothing. The meat would fill our bellies, the pelts would keep out the cold, and the bones would become tools, weapons, stakes, and poles for our tents.

'But the Gauredain came upon them with their great war-beasts. They use the mammoths to breed beasts of terrible size for battle, and so our hunt was broken.

'I turn now to those who come from beyond our lands for aid.

'If you are willing, help us fill our stores once more.''You have proven yourself an ally to us.

'With this food, we shall endure the long nights with full bellies. With these pelts, we shall make warm clothing and cover our tents against the bitter wind. The bones will serve us as weapons, stakes, and poles for our shelters.

'In these lands, nothing can be wasted.

'The cold takes all that is left unused.''Our hunters drove the herd between two great stones and were ready to set upon them when the Gauredain arrived with their war-beasts. Be wary of those beasts, for they are strong and bred for war. But gather what we need: the meat, the pelts, and the bones.'The Wargs of Elderslade keep numerous skulls of the slain as grisly trophies in Valdhellir.Your mission is to destroy collections of grisly trophies kept by the Wargs in Valdhellir.Destroy collections of grisly trophies in Valdhellir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Come, ${PLAYER}! Let us leave this dreadful place and report your success to Hórin!'A number of Jorthkyn have been found living in the ruins in Sedgemead. There have been reports of wargs making the ruins their home for some time, but if the wargs serve the Jorthkyn as their masters, the combination could prove deadly.Defeat Jorthkyn in the ruins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Wargs in the ruins (${NUMBER}/8)Find the Scout'Wargs alone are dangerous enough. With Jorthkyn as well, we could have faced an overwhelming force. Let us return and tell the mission giver of your efforts against them.'A number of Jorthkyn have been found living in the ruins in Sedgemead. There have been reports of wargs making the ruins their home for some time, but if the wargs serve the Jorthkyn as their masters, the combination could prove deadly.At ruins within Sedgemead there are Jorthkyn taking wargs as their servants. There is a growing fear that they will become another menace arrayed against the settlers in the region, and you are tasked with eliminating them.Complete the Mission: Jorthkyn and HoundsYou overcame the Jorthkyn attack at the ruins in Sedgemead and should now return to the mission giver and let them know of your efforts.'Jorthkyn! Can you believe this? There are Jorthkyn in the ruins at Sedgemead. We face Orcs, half-men, brigands, the dead and worse. Now we add Jorthkyn to the foes arrayed against us. What is worse, you might ask, they are in warg camps. We need to drive them out lest they ally with or train the wargs. Are you willing to assist?''Be wary. Jorthkyn are very large and will attack you ferociously. We cannot let them train the wargs to be their allies.''You are a marvel. We ask so much of you adventurers because we are so few in number and you always reply with such alacrity. We are grateful for your assistance.'You have been tasked with defeating ice-giants and recovering stolen treasures.You should defeat ice-giants and recover stolen treasures.Recover stolen treasures (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should regroup near the entrance to the cave.Regroup near the entrance to the chamber'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'Far to the north of Annâk-khurfu lies Rathad Caul, the Narrow Way, a treacherous passage into Câr Bronach. There, those still loyal to the Iron Crown guard the approach to the last bastions of Angmar.Your mission is to defeat the Dourhand gate-keeper guarding Rathad Caul and tear down the banner of the Iron Crown.Defeat servants of the Iron Crown at Rathad Caul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to defeat the Dourhand gate-keeper guarding Rathad Caul and tear down the banner of the Iron Crown.Summon and defeat the Dourhand gate-keeperYour mission is to defeat the Dourhand gate-keeper guarding Rathad Caul and tear down the banner of the Iron Crown.Destroy the banner of the Iron Crown'The realm of Angmar clings to life, ${PLAYER}, but they will not prevail! Let us return!'Your mission is to travel to Tûkurdul and recover what you can from the ransacked shipment as well as save the driver from the kergrim.Your mission is to travel to Tûkurdul and recover what you can from the ransacked shipment as well as save the driver from the kergrim.

Speak with Raphûz to travel.Complete Mission: Kergrim on the RoadYou have successfully recovered the ransacked supplies in Tûkurdul! Return with the scout to Raphûz with this report.'Good to see you ${PLAYER}. Kergrim to the far north-west in Tûkurdul, near Ashâgir, ransacked a shipment from the west. They took the driver and the contents of his haul with them. I ask of you that you save the driver and recover his supplies if you can. As well as slay any kergim who cross your path.''${PLAYER}, your task is to travel to Tûkurdul and recover what you can from the ransacked shipment, and if they are alive, bring the driver back safely.''You have my thanks for recovering what supplies you could. They will be of use here in Ub Nishir.

'Sad to hear about the driver's fate, I am sorry you were unable to save him.'You have been tasked with defeating a large deep-claw and destroying its burrow in Gundabad.You should destroy stone-claw burrows.Destroy stone-claw burrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should defeat Amshaz the Vast.Defeat Amshaz the Vast'Well done, ${PLAYER}! You have defeated Amshaz the Vast! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'You have been tasked with destroying fell sarcophagi and burning the remains of fallen Angmarim.You should destroy fell sarcophagi and burn the remains of fallen Angmarim.Destroy fell sarcophagi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn the remains of fallen Angmarim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should regroup near the entrance to the cave.Regroup near the entrance to the cave'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'It is time for a change. A change in leadership at Horahallow. The masters of Gramsfoot desire that you make your way into the Hobbit village and coax out the leader of the Hobbits there. Then pout him to the blade, claw, or whatever will end his days.Ordered by the taskmaster at Gramsfoot, you are to make your way to Hoarhallow and find a way to draw out the Mayor of the village and then put him to the sword.Complete the Mission: Leadership ChangeYou drew the Mayor out of hiding. You also are pretty sure that you took him down. Best return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.Return to Uglash at Gramsfoot'The time has come for new leadership. Before you celebrate, the new leadership is among the Hobbits in Hoarhallow. Leaders here think that we can put an end to that little fellow. So we are sending you, not our best to deal with the little menace. You will get your just rewards when the job is done.''You best get moving. The mayor down in Hoarhallow is not just going to off himself. The leadership wants this done. Get moving!''No, you did get him down, but those damned rangers and free folk came by and saved him just before he was good and gone. No reason to fret. There is always tomorrow.'A great leader amongst the Uruk from the White Hand was severely injured in an attack at Caras Geleden. You have been sent to finish the creature.Defeat the injured White Hand war-leaderDefeat melee Uruk-hai of the White Hand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat ranged White Hand Uruks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'Our scouts could not have been wrong. The Uruk was injured. What fell magic restored it after it was so grievously wounded? Come, let us return with this news.'After a counter assault by the Uruks at Caras Gelebren, scouts learned that one of the Uruk leaders was injured in the fray. They have set you to finding the leader and finishing the work started in the previous battle.After a failed raid on an encampment outside of Caras Gelebren, an Uruk leader was reportedly injured to point of near death. This development provides an opportunity for you to strike a vital blow.Complete the Mission: Leadership DirectionThe Uruk leader was not injured, he was more powerful than any of the other Uruks in the encampment. It appears that the information from the scouts was wrong or that there was something else at play with the war-leader.'Fortune smiles on us, ${PLAYER}. A recent attack by the Uruks has cost them dearly as one of their leaders was reported to take an arrow in the knee. With an injury like that they will never adventure again. Now is our chance to strike.

'Head back into their camp, find the leader and finish the work already begun.''We have an advantage and we must take it. Please make haste, ${PLAYER}. If we can cleave the head from this force of Uruks, surely we will drive them from these lands.''How is it possible that our scouts were wrong? The enemy should have been near death. I wonder if there is something nefarious seeping into our scouting ranks. We will need to look into this.'You have been tasked with destroying the brigand blockade within the mines of Writhenset.Use the summoning horn at the beginning of the tunnel to summon Radhril to your side.Pick up the summoning hornYou should talk to Radhril.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Use the Call Radhril skill and talk to RadhrilYou should retrieve stolen supplies and find a way to unlock the barricades.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Retrieve stolen goods (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Unlock the first barricadeUnlock the second barricadeUnlock the third barricadeYou should defeat the ruffian captain.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Defeat the ruffian captain'I commend your efforts, ${PLAYER}! Come, let us return and report our success to the Free Peoples.''I see, it looks as if the brigands have barred and locked themselves into the mines. This poses a more difficult task then I had envisioned. I am sure there is a way to unlock these gates. One of these brigands must hold a key. While we are here, we should also retrieve some of the goods that the brigands have stolen.'Your mission is to travel to the Ekhamâti camp, defeat the dôla and rob them of their gold in order to supply Mizâdi's forces.Your mission is to travel to the Ekhamâti camp, defeat the dôla, and rob them of their gold in order to supply Mizâdi's forces.

Speak to Setokúli to travel.Complete Mission: Looting the SuppliesYour mission is to travel to the Ekhamâti camp, defeat the dôla, and rob them of their gold in order to supply Mizâdi's forces.'Good to see you, ${CLASS}. Our scouts have discovered an Ekhamâti camp in Khûd Zagin and they appear to have an abundance of gold stored there. I ask that you travel to the camp and take as much gold as you can find so we can put it to better use supplying Mizâdi's forces.

'There have also been reports of brutal dôla in the camp by the names of Omurtóko, Khisónto, and Purombóro. I ask that you put an end to them while you are there.'Your mission is to travel to the Ekhamâti camp, defeat the dôla, and rob them of their gold in order to supply Mizâdi's forces.'I am glad for your return, ${CLASS}. This gold will do so much good in helping Mizâdi! I thank you! And putting a stop to those dôla will also be great news for our soldiers who have heard the stories of their cruelty.'Deep in the Grey Mountains, the hobgoblins launch a plot to free their mistress….Use the summoning horn at the cave entrance to summon Hórin to your side.Pick up the Summoning HornYou should talk to Hórin.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Hórin is missing, and the Call Hórin skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Use the skill Call Hórin and talk to HórinDefeat hobgoblins in Akûl-lagam with Hórin.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Hórin is missing, and the Call Hórin skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Defeat hobgoblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the hobgoblin leaderA door of unnatural ice blocks your path.

You should talk to Hórin.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Hórin is missing, and the Call Hórin skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Talk to HórinHórin believes hobgoblin frost-callers are causing the ice to block your path.

You should find and defeat the hobgoblin frost-callers.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Hórin is missing, and the Call Hórin skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Defeat hobgoblin frost-callers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})With the ice door dispelled, you should now be able to progress deeper into Akûl-lagam.

You should find and defeat the hobgoblin leader, Thrugdar the Slaughterer.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Hórin is missing, and the Call Hórin skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Defeat Thrugdar the SlaughtererThe hobgoblins have been defeated.

You should talk to Hórin.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Hórin is missing, and the Call Hórin skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Talk to Hórin'Well done, ${PLAYER}! Let us return to Annâk-khurfu!''This is the place. I must be honest, ${PLAYER}. After our failed assault on the Anvil, I am eager to be avenged upon the Frost-horde and their lackeys for the attack on Skarháld. And most of all, we must do everything we can to prevent Hrímil from being released. If she attacked our army during the battle, it would be catastrophic!'

He pauses as he is lost in his own thoughts. You can tell his experience in the Anvil still weighs heavily on him. He notices you staring at him and becomes flustered.

'D- Do not think me a coward, ${PLAYER}! I am more than willing to face that dragon again! And one day, we will have to, to end her reign over these mountains for good. I just don't want that day to be today! Come on, let's get to work.''This door is no natural thing, ${PLAYER}. I have seen this before! Those hobgoblins are summoning an unearthly cold with their dark magic to block our path. We will have to defeat them to progress further!''This uncanny cold.... We were just in time, ${PLAYER}. I swear I can almost hear that cursed dragon on the other side of this wall.

'If we're done, let's go. I have no desire to stand here freezing!'You have been tasked with dispatching a powerful hobgoblin in Vorkodar.Find and defeat Frost-caller Túgost.

He can be found in Vorkodar.Defeat Frost-caller Túgost'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'A notice from Thrasi, a hunter in Ered Luin, asks for assistance in stocking the hunter's larder.Travel to Thrasi's Lodge in Ered Luin and ask him how you may help.Speak with Thrasi at his lodge in Ered LuinComplete the mission: Many in Need.Complete Mission: Many in NeedReturn to Thrasi at his lodge and provide him the meat you collected.Speak with Thrasi at his lodge in Ered LuinPost:

Those with a hunter's heart can find me at my lodge in Ered Luin. We have need of game meat to cure and stock our larder. Visit me if you can assist.

- Thrasi'Thank you for answering my notice. There are many mouths to feed hereabouts, and too few strong arms to gather what is needed. I sent out word for hunters such as yourself to aid us in bringing in meat that may be cured and stored.

'If you are willing, I can guide you to the bear camp we have chosen for this work.''I trust the hunt was as lively as it was successful. You have seen to it that our larder will be well stocked for many days to come.

'I will set about curing this meat at once. You have my thanks again, friend.''Do not underestimate the bears, friend. They are stronger than they look, though their meat, when properly cured, is a delicacy fit for a king under the mountain.'With a new ship, the vengeful captain set out in search of Yarikh....I looked my friend over and asked if they could continue....We scoured the beach, slaughtering with impunity. None could withstand our vengeance or our blades....Defeat the Corsair crew (${NUMBER}/16)At last, Yarikh came into view. Two of his lieutenants flanked him near a serviceable launch they were trying to get into the sea. We wasted no time to engage.Find YarikhDefeat AkhâtYarikh's boat slipped out of sight as my blade wet itself on Akhât's corpse. Behind me, I heard a gasp and sputter for air... my friend.Make your way to your friend's side'Do not worry after me...

'I would have followed you to the end of the world. My friend... my-'

The last word is cut short as the man perishes on the sand.'Aye, I am able, though not hardy. Let us not let my injury allow them to escape again.'

He groans.

'Press onward.'You are tasked with entering the ruins outside of Mossward to eliminate the remaining pack-leader from the pair that lead the wolves there. Since the death of her mate, the wolf-matron in the ruins has been aggressive and so has her pack.Defeat the wolf-matronDefeat wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'With the wolf-matron eliminated there will be a time of peace. The wolves will eventually choose new leaders. Let us return.'Hunters, recently asked to assist in culling the wolves in the nearby ruins, eliminated one half of the pair who kept the wolves away from the populace of the town. Something has changed in the surviving pack-leader and she now seems to be testing the resolve of the townsfolk nearby. You are tasked with finishing the job the hunters began by eliminating the female pack-leader before she finds a new mate.What may be an error in judgement has raised the ire of a pack of nearby wolves with only one pack-leader now in charge. Speak with the mission giver to make your way to the ruins to finish the work of hunters.Complete the Mission: Mother of WolvesWith both the pack-leaders now eliminated, the wolves should be quieter for a time whilst they fight amongst themselves to determine their new order. Return to the mission giver and tell them you succeeded.'We often think it necessary to take action when maybe we ought not have. This report may be one of those times.

'Hunters were tasked with thinning a large pack of wolves in a nearby ruin. In their zeal, the hunters managed to kill one of the pack-leaders, the male. 

'Normally, this would allow the lesser wolves to fall on one another for a time until new pack-leaders rise, but the wolves in the ruins followed a breeding pair and the she-wolf has grown aggressive in her mate's absence.

'Our task is clear, we must eliminate the wolf matron before she drives the pack into attacking the village and does irreparable harm to the populace.''A new set of pack-leaders will rise to take their place, but for the moment, we will have respite from their attacks. I wonder though why the aggression was so great. There must be something stirring these creature more than normal.''Our own folly has wrought this end. A shame that the wolves cannot be more like faithful hounds, but it seems this is their nature. So we must do now, what we must.'One evening, on shore leave, the mariner and the captain had conversation about dreams and desires....We sat in a simple study, each enjoying a smoke and spoke at length about our goals....Speak with the captainOften he would be like this, jovial and open, a warm companion. I listened quietly and drew on my pipe....Smoke with the captainWhen it was my turn to speak he listened intently and responded....Speak with the captain'The night grows old, my friend. Let us rest while we can, we launch at dawn's first light. Let us see, together, what that new day holds for us.''When I was a boy, I was a ruffian. I fit in nowhere, much like you have confided of your early days.

'Ah, but when I found the sea. There, on the waves, was freedom. There, beneath the endless blanket of the sky was life. There was no substitute for what it offered, no greater joy.

'Dawn wakes over the horizon, drawing all from their slumber. The rocking of the waves give way to the bustle and commotion of boots on the deck, the promise of a new day, new adventure, new wealth and new shores... something new at every turn. There is no course that is set but the one you make.

'That is the life I covet and seek.''All noble pursuits, young one. And in time, you shall see them come to pass.

'For now, my friend, we should both be content in the knowledge that we are friends. We have fought and bled together. We have saved people in Gondor and beyond and we safe-guard their future by our very actions.

'Ours is a noble pursuit. We should never think otherwise.

'On the morrow we sail again into the Bay of Belfalas. Let us hope that our quarry, this Yarikh makes his presence known that we might finally end his reign of terror on the good people of our land.'Your mission is to travel to Tir Katar and put an end to the caracals who have been preying on nearby travellers and help any survivors you can find.Your mission is to travel to Tir Katar and put an end to the caracals who have been preying on nearby travellers and help any survivors you can find.

Speak to Setokúli to travel.Complete Mission: Natural PreyYou have successfully put an end to the caracals in Tir Katar as well as rescued any survivors! Return with the scout to Setokúli with this report.'Greetings, ${CLASS}. Caracals have been preying on travellers near Tir Katar. I ask that you go there and put an end to these beasts to prevent further troubles.

'Please keep a look out for any survivors as well and help them if you can.''${CLASS}, your mission is to travel to Tir Katar and put an end to the caracals who have been preying on nearby travellers and help any survivors you can find.''I thank you. The roads in the area are safe again, and I can not find the words to say how grateful the families of the survivors are to see them return home safely.'You have been tasked with clearing out the cold-worm nesting grounds at the ruins of Stormwall.Destroy cold-worm nests.Destroy cold-worm nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the nests destroyed, let us return and report your success to Hórin!'Your mission is to travel to the west of Sul Madásh to the Lair of the Shadlúgai and gather crocodile hides.Your mission is to travel to the west of Sul Madásh to the Lair of the Shadlúgai and gather crocodile hides.

Speak to Várudar to travel.Complete Mission: New Hides to TanYour mission is to travel to the west of Sul Madásh to the Lair of the Shadlúgai and gather crocodile hides.Return to Várudar in Sul Madásh'Our scouts are in need of new armour, and the crocodiles found in the Lair of the Shadlúgai provide the finest hides. The crafters here have requested some be gathered.''Our scouts are in need of new armour, and the crocodiles found in the Lair of the Shadlúgai provide the finest hides. The crafters here have requested some be gathered.''You have returned and with the hides!

'I am glad to hear you were able to defeat such a beast as well. You have made travelling through the marshes safer for us all.

'I thank you for your help, my friend.'There is a thought that if the leaders of the Southron Men are eliminated then the rest will fall into disarray. Make your way to the encampment.Defeat the brigand-captainDefeat brigand lieutenants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat brigands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'Now we shall wait and see if these brigands fall in on one another. Let us return.'Recently, the scouts of Swanfleet learned that there are a small number of leaders charged with the training of the Men at a large brigand encampment. If they are removed, infighting may result and provide an opening for a counter attack.A change in leadership could throw the Southron Men in the area into disarray. The mission giver at Lhan Garan will have a scout lead you to the camp to remove the leadership.Complete the Mission: Not as Many HeadsThe leaders of the brigands are defeated. You should now return to the mission giver in Lhan Garan and tell them of your victory.'My scouts report that there are leaders among the brigands who train them in the arts of battle. We had thought most of the Men coming from the south were brutes or brigands out to make a living as highwaymen. Now, we are not so certain.

'Yes, given the size of the encampment, we knew that something was amiss, but we did not understand the organization of the force until now.

'Knowing what we know now, there is a grim answer and call that was made. We want to eliminate these leaders and break the will of these brigands. Perhaps it will provide us the change to strike at them before they become more of a threat.''A great effort and battle well fought. You have well earned your rewards, ${PLAYER}.''We hope that by eliminating the leaders we can weaken the resolve of the men from the South. Perhaps they will scatter without leadership. At least, we hope that they will fall to in-fighting and disarray providing us a slight advantage over the enemy.'Your mission is to rid Sul Madásh of its rat problem. They are growing in numbers and becoming a problem for the settlement. The rats must be stopped and their nests destroyed.Your mission is to rid Sul Madásh of its rat problem. They are growing in numbers and becoming a problem for the settlement. The rats must be stopped and their nests destroyed.

Speak to Várudar to travel.Complete Mission: Oh, RatsYou have successfully pushed the rats out of Sul Madásh and destroyed their nests. That should stop them from overrunning the settlement for now.Return to Várudar in Sul Madásh'Sul Madásh has a problem with the vermin outside our borders.

'The rats are becoming more of a problem as the blight spreads. The people here are in need of someone to stop the rats and destroy their nests to prevent them from becoming more of a nuisance.''${CLASS}, Your mission is to rid Sul Madásh of its rat problem. They are growing in numbers and becoming a problem for the settlement. The rats must be stopped and their nests destroyed.''My friend, we thank you for dealing with the rats.

'I know the vermin will return in time, but for now we have one fewer thing to worry about here in Sul Madásh.'Your mission is to travel to Ab-dâna and defeat Orcs you find there to recover any order they may have.Your mission is to travel to Ab-dâna and eliminate Orcs you find there to recover any orders they have so that Ashâmi can discover who is sending them.

Speak to Ashâmi to travel.Complete Mission: Orders from the HighestYou have successfully eliminated Orcs within Ab-dâna and recovered the orders they have been receiving. Return with the scout to Ashâmi with this report.'Good to see you my friend. There are Orcs in Ab-dâna that are getting orders from something beyond them. We need you to eliminate these Orcs and recover the orders.''${PLAYER}, your task is to travel to Ab-dâna and eliminate Orcs you find there to recover any orders they have so that we can discover who is sending them.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. I am glad you were able to recover what you could from the Orcs, we will take the time to uncover who is sending them.

'You have my thanks.'You have been tasked with retrieving valuable ore from Sundergrót.Find and collect valuable ore inside Sundergrót.Mine valuable ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'Just an ordinary night in a quiet hobbit township. What could possibly go wrong?Find and speak with a scout'I did not expect that this would happen. We never see brigands this close to our town. Let us return.'Clegur is a relatively safe village. Still, the inhabitants are on edge with the recent events in Swanfleet and welcome the assistance of someone willing to watch over the village at night.The request is a simple one: patrol through the pathways that make up the township of Clegur at night. Speak with the mission giver to assist.Complete the Mission: Patrol the TownshipYour patrol was not as uneventful as everyone presumed. It appears that the Men from the south are intent on invading every corner of Swanfleet if they can. Alert the mission giver.'Ah, ${PLAYER}, a word for a moment if I may.

'Many villagers are concerned about what is happening all around us and were wondering if you might help put their minds at ease a bit.

'Nights are a little uneasy recently, and we just do not have enough Bounders to keep up with patrols. Would you be willing to help us keep watch?''Honestly, ${PLAYER}, I think it will be an uneventful night and that the townsfolk are grousing, just to grouse. Still, if you are willing to go on patrol it will put minds at ease.''It seems that the fears expressed by the townsfolk were warranted. I am glad that we employed you to patrol our streets. We need to double our own guard to ensure that our streets remain safe.'Your mission is to travel to the Gorge of Woe and defeat the Hive-matron and her corrupted Urâshi wasps before they can spread throughout Urash Dâr.Your mission is to travel to the Gorge of Woe and defeat the hive-matron and her corrupted Urâshi wasps before they can spread throughout Urash Dâr.

Speak with Raphûz to travel.Complete Mission: Perversion of NatureYou have successfully slain the hive-matron and prevented the corrupted wasps from spreading in Urash Dâr! Return with the scout to Raphûz with this report.'Greetings, ${CLASS}. A hive-matron and her hive within the Gorge of Woe are altered by the corruption seeping across the land. They must be destroyed.''${CLASS}, your task is to travel to the Gorge of Woe and defeat the hive-matron and her corrupted Urâshi wasps before they can spread throughout Urash Dâr.''I have heard of your success, ${PLAYER}. You have done well to stop the hive-matron and her swarm of corrupted wasps before they could cause more harm.'Your mission is to travel to Pits of Chortáth in the south-west and help the scouts of Sâr Marsag make the paths safer to travel by thinning the pack of jackals in the area.Your mission is to travel to Pits of Chortáth in the south-west and help the scouts of Sâr Marsag make the paths safer to travel by thinning the pack of jackals in the area.

Speak to Várudar to travel.Complete Mission: Prowling ScavengersYou have successfully thinned the number of jackals in the Pits of Chortáth and helped the scouts of Sâr Marsag.Return to Várudar in Sul Madásh'The scouts of Sâr Marsag to the south-west of here have requested help with the jackals in the Pits of Chortáth. They are preying on travellers and making their lives difficult in the camp.

'Please travel there and help out by thinning the pack.''The scouts of Sâr Marsag to the south-west of here have requested help with the jackals in the Pits of Chortáth. They are preying on travellers and making their lives difficult in the camp.''You return from the Pits of Chortáth.

'My scouts have told me you have succeeded in your task and even felled a fearsome jackal that attacked you!

'You have our thanks, friend.'Your mission is to gather mushrooms that have not been infected by the Pale Blight so that the gardeners of Sul Madásh can grow them safely within the settlement.The gardeners of Sul Madásh have asked for assistance in gathering mushrooms in the nearby bog that are untainted by the Pale Blight, so that they can grow them safely within the settlement.

Speak to Várudar to travel.Complete Mission: Questionable MorelsYou have successfully gathered unblighted mushrooms from the bog outside of Sul Madásh. Bring them to the gardeners so they can begin growing more.Return to Várudar in Sul Madásh'Hello, my friend. The gardeners here in Sul Madásh have a request that requires the help of someone such as yourself.

'They ask for someone to gather mushrooms that are untouched by the Pale Blight and return them here, so that they can grow them safely within the settlement. They do not wish lose them to the infection in the land.

'Some red, green, and pale ones should suffice.''The gardeners of Sul Madásh have asked for assistance in gathering mushrooms in the nearby bog that are untainted by the Pale Blight, so that they can grow them safely within the settlement.''You return and with the mushrooms.

'Thank you friend, the gardeners here will make great use of these and preserve them well.'You have been tasked with retrieving ice that is bolstered by frost grims.Collect ice clusters created by luring frost grims to highlighted areas.Collect ice (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Its far too cold in here for my liking! Let's head back!'You have been tasked with defending the fortress of Skarháld from a Gundabad raiding party.Push back raiders to the western gate of Skarháld.Push back raiders to the western gate of SkarháldDefend Skarháld from the Gundabad raiding party.Defend Skarháld from the Gundabad raiding party'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the Gundabad raiding party defeated, let us return and report your success!'A notice from Refr Quicksilver requests assistance in proving the lineage of the builders of Iorvinas.Find Refr Quicksilver at the cave entrance in the central Lone-lands. He stands watch there. Ask him what he means by getting your hands dirty.Speak with Refr Quicksilver at the cave entrance in the central Lone-landsComplete the mission: Reclaiming Iorvinas.Complete Mission: Reclaiming IorvinasReturn the rubbings you collected to Refr Quicksilver.Speak with Refr Quicksilver at the cave entrance in the central Lone-landsPost:

Requesting the aid of an experienced adventurer willing to get their hands a little dirty. Seek me out near the entrance to our home of old in the Lone-lands.

- Refr Quicksilver'Iorvinas was a home of my people in ages past; I know it, deep in my bones, and I mean to prove it.

'My duties hold me here, but I sent others to scout the depths below. They found rune-stones within, marked with the signs of the builders.

'I need you to enter Iorvinas, take rubbings of those stones, and bring them back to me. There is, however, one small trouble: Orcs. The ruins are crawling with them, so keep your wits about you as you pass through the halls.'He studies the rubbings for a long moment.

'A bit more incomplete than I had hoped. Still, I must share these with my brother. In truth, this mark bears the look of a family sigil, or something near to it.

'This is a fine first effort, my friend. You have my thanks for all you have done.''The stones are there; of that I am certain. My kin built those halls, and with your help, friend, I shall have proof enough to silence any who doubt it. Go well, and keep your weapon-hand ready.'You have been tasked with reclaiming the dwarf-ruins of Zarkul-sulûn.The enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Erebor.Claim the first encampment for EreborThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Erebor.Claim the second encampment for EreborThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Erebor.Claim the third encampment for EreborThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Erebor.Claim the final encampment for Erebor'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With Zarkul-sulûn reclaimed, let us return and report your success to Ausma!'You have been tasked with reclaiming the old watch-post of Bizar-atrâd.Reclaim Bizar-atrâd.Plant banners as you reclaim Bizar-atrâd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with repairing a series of forges within an ancient forge-hall in Gundabad.You should repair the forges while fending off frost grims and cold-drakesDefeat frost grims (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Repair forges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat cold-drakes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to the forge entrance.Return to the forge entrance'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with recovering dwarf-caches from Kidzul-kâlah before the Dourhands can lay claim to them.You have been tasked with recovering dwarf-caches from Kidzul-kâlah before the Dourhands can lay claim to them.Collect dwarf-caches in Kidzul-kâlah (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Excellent, ${PLAYER}! It is good we did not let such relics be claimed by the Dourhands. Let us return to Ausma!'A note requests aid with driving a wedge between the White Hand and Dunlendings in Eregion.Report to Tinúriel in Eregion and see what you can do to assist her.Speak with Tinúriel at the encampment in EregionComplete the mission: Removing Their Foothold.Complete Mission: Removing Their FootholdReturn to Tinúriel and report on your success.Speak with Tinúriel in Echad Dúnann in EregionPost:

Assistance required. Forces of the Dunlending are attempting to establish a foothold for the White Hand in Eregion. Visit me in Eregion to assist with this issue.

- Tinúriel'These lands hold many memories for the Elves. We remember when they were the seat of our people and the dwelling-place of our king. Now, much lies in ruin, and what once was has passed into memory. We cannot return to the days from which we came.

'Yet we may still have a hand in shaping what these lands shall become. It is for this that I ask your aid.

'Men from the South press farther into these lands at the bidding of the cruel master of the White Hand. If we are swift, we may yet halt their advance before they gain a stronger foothold.''You have returned, and with you comes word of victory.

'If I seem overly pleased by this news, forgive me. It is only that I remember too well the hurts I suffered in these lands, and the sorrow that lingers here for those of us who have seen their former glory.

'We must remain vigilant in these lands. They may never again become what they were in the Elder Days of the Elves, but that does not mean all hope is lost.

'There may yet be a brighter future here; for those who come after us.''You must drive the Dunlendings from this small fort and destroy whatever signs might lead the White Hand to this place. Leave them no trail by which they might find their way here again.

'Be relentless. This is an enemy not to be underestimated.'As the War of Three Peaks drew near its end, the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ suffered a sudden, terrible setback. Before the final effort is made to breach the gates of Gundabad, the dwarves must resist falling to despair and overcome their doubts.Your mission is to raise the spirits of disheartened soldiers of the Gabil'akkâ at Zarkul-sulûn and help them to overcome thoughts of despair.Help dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ overcome thoughts of despair (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Thank you, ${PLAYER}! We are not beaten yet!'A posting from the Elf maiden, Brethilwen, requesting assistance with removing goblins from her vineyard. She also desires the recovery of grapes and a cask from the vineyard, to ensure that she can restore production.Make your way to the outskirts of Limael's Vineyard in Ered Luin and speak with the vintner, Brethilwen.Speak with Brethilwen near Limael's Vineyard in Ered LuinComplete the mission: Restoring the Vineyard.Complete Mission: Restoring the VineyardReturn to Brethilwen near the vineyard in Ered Luin.Speak with Brethilwen near the vineyard in Ered LuinPost:

My vineyard has too long been overrun by goblins, and the time has come to reclaim it and start a proper distillation of my wine once again. If you are willing to aid me, seek me out near my vineyard in Ered Luin.

- Brethilwen, the vintner'I am pleased that you have answered my request for aid. My time here draws ever nearer to its end, and it is my wish to restore the vineyard before I depart, that I may leave it in the capable hands of another.

'I have long cherished the art of winemaking, and I believe my grapes yield a wine of rich and robust flavour. Alas, the goblins who have taken to my vineyard and winery seem to share my appreciation for them. They are many, and cruel besides, and none have yet been able to drive them away for long enough to restore my work.

'I would ask that you gather samples of my grapes and recover a cask of wine for me. While you are there, it would also be most helpful if you could see to these troublesome goblins and remind them that my vineyard is no place for them.

'It would ease my heart greatly to see the vines tended once more, before I take my leave.''You have done me a great service, my friend. The grapes yet retain their flavour and that distinctive tartness which gives my wine its character.

'With your aid, and my own resolve, I shall restore my vineyard and winery to their former grace. The work will be long, perhaps, but I have never been one to surrender easily to adversity.

'I am truly pleased that you answered my plea. Your kindness shall not be forgotten.''I require ten samples of my grapes, that I may be certain they remain sound and worthy of the vine. There is also a particular cask I desire to have recovered. It was the first barrel in which I ever aged my wine. Should you find it, I would be most grateful if you would return it to me.'You have been tasked with destroying the Angmarim ritual at Dûn Traikh.You should disrupt the Angmarim ritual at Dûn Traikh.Destroy ritual obelisks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat fell spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should regroup near the north gate of Dûn Traikh.Regroup near the north gate of Dûn Traikh'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'Your mission is to travel to Lhámuth and gather Pale Blight samples from the bog-lurkers there for the scholars of Sul Madásh.Your mission is to travel to Lhámuth and gather Pale Blight samples from the bog-lurkers there for the scholars of Sul Madásh.

Speak to Várudar to travel.Complete Mission: Sampling the Bog-lurkersYou have successfully gathered Pale Blight samples from the bog-lurkers in Lhámuth. Bring them to the scholars of Sul Madásh for them to study.Return to Várudar in Sul Madásh'Greetings, ${CLASS}. The scholars here in Sul Madásh have submitted a request for an adventurer such as yourself to travel west to Lhámuth. The marshes there have become overrun by bog-lurkers and the scholars desire to study how the Pale Blight has affected the creatures.

'Gather samples from their carapaces. But be careful, as our scouts have spotted wood-trolls lumbering in the area as well.''The marshes in Lhámuth have become overrun with bog-lurkers. Scholars here in Sul Madásh would like you to gather samples of the Pale Blight from them to study.''Welcome back, ${CLASS}. I see you have gathered the samples for which the scholars have asked.

'You have our thanks as we fight back this blight in Adagím.'Deep within Wyrmsgráf, the remains of countless dwarves lay strewn through Scatha's larder of old.Your mission is to recover the scavenged remains of dwarves that met their ends in Scatha's Larder.Recover dwarf-remains from Scatha's Larder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'I am certain the descendants of those you recovered offer their truest gratitude, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'Your mission is to hunt jackals in Khazâda and burn the remains of the poor victims they have defiled.Your mission is to travel to Khazâda and thin the numbers of jackals in the area as well as burn the corpses of slain travellers that have been defiled by the beasts.

Speak with Raphûz to travel.Complete Mission: Scavengers of Our FallenYou have successfully slain jackals and burned the remains in Khazâda! Return with the scout to Raphûz with this report.'${CLASS}, we are in need of your help. Jackals in Khazâda have been causing much trouble for the people of Urash Dâr. The coalition asks that you go and thin out their numbers and if you can, please burn the remains of the people who have sadly fallen prey to the beasts before they can defile their bodies further.''${CLASS}, your task is to travel to Khazâda and thin the numbers of jackals in the area as well as burn the corpses of slain travellers that have been defiled by the beasts.''Thank you, friend. The paths will be safer with fewer of those beasts around.

'I am grateful you were able to put the bodies to rest as well. The families will sleep better knowing their loved ones are no longer being defiled by those jackals.'A massive encampment of brigands threatens the region, and there is a growing fear that the organized forces are soon to attack. You are directed to find any plans that might be in the encampment.Collect plans (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat brigands at the encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and speak with the scout'Excellent work, let us return so you may collect your reward.'In a large brigand encampment, Southron Men gather in large numbers digging trenches, raising stake-walls and tents, and planning a terrible attack on the people of Swanfleet. It is unclear what their overall objectives are, but the scouts in the area want to learn more.Men from the south are a great threat to the populace and specifically to Mossward. You are asked to enter their encampment and seek any secret plans they may have.Complete the Mission: Secrets and PlansYou collected the plans and handed them to the scout who arrived to lead you away from the camp. You should return to the mission giver in Mossward to tell them what you learned.'I will tell you this, ${PLAYER}. Something terrible is amiss in these lands. Since riders pushed through here in the dead of night not long ago, there has been all manner of ill-fortuned and foul-mannered folk pouring in from the south.

'None are worse than the Southron Men making a large encampment. We know that they are planning something and need to know what it is.

'Great tents in their encampment are used for meeting between the leaders. It is possible, our scouts believe, that they are formulating some plan for an attack. We want to learn what they are planning so that we may thwart their efforts.

'Are you willing to help?''These plans are more well-developed than expected. It is hard to believe that bands of brigands could be this organized. I fear that this setback will not hold them long, ${PLAYER}. Still, you have done well to prepare us for the future.''The encampment of Southron Men is very large and teeming with brigands with only fell deeds on their minds. We need to find out what they intend and quickly. Please be swift, ${PLAYER}.'You have been tasked with mining ore from the Frostdelf in the halls of Thikil-gundu.Mine the Frostdelf.Mine the Frostdelf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Investigate the noise coming from the Depths of Akhatâr.Investigate the noise coming from the Depths of Akhatâr'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'Despite the failure of the Iron Garrison, the dwarves will not allow the Orcs of Khazad-dûm to spill forth into Azanulbizar, the Dimrill Dale.Your mission is to secure the Redhorn Pass.Secure the first encampment on the Redhorn PassYour mission is to secure the Redhorn Pass.Secure the second encampment on the Redhorn PassYour mission is to secure the Redhorn Pass.Secure the third encampment on the Redhorn PassYour mission is to secure the Redhorn Pass.Secure the final encampment on the Redhorn Pass'Well done, ${PLAYER}! We need not fear that the Redhorn Pass will be overrun this day! Let us return!'You have been tasked with defeating the Servants of Throkhâr and destroying their nameless shrines deep within Gundabad.You should defeat Servants of Throkhâr and destroy their nameless shrines.Destroy nameless shrines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Servants of Throkhâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should defeat Uknad, She Who Feeds.Defeat Uknad, She Who Feeds'Well done, ${PLAYER}. Let us not dwell here any longer. This place is unsettling. We should return and report your success to Hórin.'Something is lurking among the ruins along the banks of the Greyflood, and you have been asked to investigate.Investigate the apparitions along the bank of the Greyflood.Investigate along the banks of the GreyfloodApproach the scout to return to camp.Approach the scout to return to camp'Let us return to Hithriel.'At the outskirts of Caranost, a brave group holds a line against an onslaught of Orcs pouring across the bridge from the ruins. The latest assault threatens to break the resolve of the warriors at Sírlond. It falls to you to bolster them as they come under assault.Defeat the occupying forces at SírlondDefeat the occupying forces at SírlondFind the scout'A fight for the ages! We have won this day. Return anon to Baglan and tell them of your victory here at Sírlond.'Orcs from the forces within the ruins of Caranost crossed the bridge and forced the outpost defenders out of Sírlond. You were asked to drive the enemy out of the outpost.Speak with the mission giver when you are ready to travel to Sírlond and retake the outpost from the Orc menace.Complete the Mission: Siege of SírlondYour mission was a success, you should return to the mission giver and tell them of your success.Return to the mission giver and tell them of your success'${PLAYER}, reports from the outpost at Sírlond are dire. Orcs stationed at the ancient fortress of Caranost crossed the bridge and forced the defenders to flee. They need assistance driving the Orc forces out of the encampment so they can return and continue the effort to remove the menace from the ruin. If you are willing to undertake this effort, speak with me again.''Use caution ${PLAYER}, the Orcs are growing more fearsome and aggressive as each day passes. I expect that there will be a good number of the enemy within the outpost.''The defences of Sírlond hold for now thanks to you. It is likely only a matter of time before the Orcs muster enough strength to force their way back into the foothold. We must remain diligent in our efforts to drive them out of Caranost.'You have been tasked with protecting the Elves left to guard the entrance to The Rift.Defend the watch-tower.Defend the watch-towerClear the enemy encampment below the watch-tower.Clear the enemy encampment below the watch-tower'I thank you for coming to our aid. Since the Rangers departed, we have been able to hold the entrance to The Rift. Recently it has been difficult with the Iron Crown renewing their efforts to expand out from Angmar. You have assisted us and that assistance will not be forgotten. May your travels be swift and safe, my friend.'Uruks besiege ruins across the land and an organized attack is too dangerous given the forces available in the region. A task to help reduce the threat falls to you.Destroy White Hand siege towers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy White Hand catapults (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the scout'Thinning out the number of Uruks crawling through the hills is a great service to our people. Let us return now to safer lands.'At a hill-fort, constructed by the Uruk of the White Hand, massive siege weapons threaten to prolong the occupation of the land. Destroying the weapons will weaken the Uruks and potentially give the people of the region a chance to battle back against the invaders.You are to go to the Uruk encampment, destroy the siege equipment they have, and make ready for war.Complete the Mission: Siege-breakingNow that you have destroyed the siege weaponry at the Uruk encampment, you should return to the mission giver and tell them of your victory.'When reports began of Uruks coming from the south, we were unprepared. Uruks appeared quickly and built their hill-fort with an alacrity that we had never seen. Now, they build massive machines meant only for destruction and we must do what we can to destroy them before they can be used against us. Go to their encampment and destroy the siege weapons they have built so that we can slow down their war effort.''I do not envy you this task, ${PLAYER}. I am, however, grateful that you will do this for us. Be safe and swift.''With their siege weaponry destroyed, the Uruks will not be able to assault us at so great a range. We thank you for all you have done, ${PLAYER}.'Within the ruins ahead there are said to be great relics of the Elven past. You are to retrieve as many as you can for the Elven patron funding the expedition.Acquire Elven relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eliminate the Uruk-hai in the ruins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'I am pleased you found these items. The scattered remnants of our heritage are precious to us all. Let us return.'In ancient Elven ruins, Uruks are set to despoil not only the ruins, but also to remove or destroy the remnants of an ancient past. An enterprising individual asked the scouts of Swanfleet to hire folk to sift through the detritus in the ruins for anything of value expecting that some Elf-nobles may pay for a piece of their history.A rescue mission, not of the living, but of the historical items of the Elves. Speak with the mission giver to go to the ruins and retrieve the ancient bits of Elven history from the White Hand Uruks.Complete the Mission: Sifting Through TimeYou retrieved the relics and handed them to the scout who arrived to lead you out. Return to the mission giver and tell them of your efforts.'This is an odd request, ${PLAYER}, but suffice it to say, not everything we ask you to do is simply for the good of the effort. Sometimes, there are folk who are helping to arm us and fund our efforts to defend the lands who ask something peculiar of us. This is one of those times.

'A patron has asked for help in collecting anything of value from the crumbling Elven ruins. If you find some, I will have a scout meet you and collect the goods for our patron once you are done.''Elven relics of ages past, you see? Yes, our patron is an Elf in this case and we are obliged to assist them -- provided you are willing to assist us.''Our patron will be pleased that you succeeded in recovering the items they requested. It is our hope that this recompense pleases you as well.'Elven relics lost in the ruins are to be reclaimed so that the heritage of the once proud people can be preserved.Destroy White Hand banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eliminate Uruk invaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'Our patron will be pleased with this effort. Come, let us get these back to where they belong.'Once a great home of the Elves, the ruins of Caras Gelebren are now despoiled by the arrival of Uruk of the White Hand. There is now an effort underway to push the Uruks out.You are to make your way into the ruins of Caras Gelebren, tear down the banners of the White Hand and slay as many Uruk-hai as you find. Speak with the mission giver to undertake this mission.Complete the Mission: Signs and SigilsYou found a good number of Uruk-hai in the ruins and destroys the banners you found. Return now to receive your rewards.Speak with the mission giver'Uruks in the ruins of Caras Gelebren, this will not do. Our request here is a simple one, go to the ruin, drive them out, and tear down their banners.

'We know that this cannot be done simply, but at least thin their number. They are numerous and strong, but with enough effort we may wrest the ruins from their control.''It seems such a simple request, but Uruks are monstrous creatures of both size and temperament. You would do best to be on guard as you venture among them, ${PLAYER}.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. It is good to know that there are still stout warriors like you willing to aid us. The Uruk-hai know the retribution that will come to them for every affront they raise against us.'You have been tasked with dispatching one of the sons of the warg chieftain, Ránulur.Find and defeat Maukhuk, son of Ránulur.

He can be found inside Shathur-munzu.Defeat Maukhuk, son of Ránulur'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'Despite the failure of the Iron Garrison, the dwarves will not allow the Orcs of Khazad-dûm to spill forth into Azanulbizar, the Dimrill Dale.Your mission is to defeat Orcs in the Dimrill Dale and plant banners of the Gabil'akkâ upon them.Plant banners on defeated Orcs in the Dimrill Dale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'We cannot let the Orcs forget that Khazad-dûm belongs to Durin's Folk, ${PLAYER}! Let us return!'The filthy little Hobbits in Hoarhallow gorge themselves on food. This makes them hearty and more fit than they ought be. The leaders of Gramsfoot believe that they can starve the little plump creatures by stealing their food.Ordered by the taskmaster at Gramsfoot, you are to make your way to Hoarhallow and steal the feed sacks that the Hobbits keep laying around.Complete the Mission: Starve them OutHaving stolen a good number of the feedbags you should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot and claim your reward.Return to Uglash at Gramsfoot'Listen here, you worthless wretch. The masters here in camp have decided to cut the food supply for those filthy Hobbits in Hoarhallow. We need you to go there and steal as many of the feed bags as you can. The masters of the lash here think that without food the Hobbits will wither away.

'No back talk or thinking for yourself now. Just do as you are told.''Go steal the food from the hobbits, maybe it will make them thinner. Though I prefer them plump. They are better eating that way.''I see you have stolen their food. Guess we wait and see if the wisdom of the leaders means that the number of those pesky little cretins is lowered. Not that I have much faith in this effort. You earned your keep. Here...'Fool Hobbits won't simply die in large numbers. No, these little foes are hardy and made so by their abundant consumption of food. The masters of Gramsfoot have a plan to weaken the foe and it involves their food supply.Steal Hobbit Feed Sacks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Look at all that stuff. None of it meat, but it would do in a pinch. These Hobbits eat anything. Get back to Gramsfoot, Uglash will be waiting.'You have been tasked with defeating Frost-horde drake emissaries and destroying Angmarim coffers.You should defeat Frost-horde drake emissaries and destroy Angmarim coffers found throughout the area.Defeat Frost-horde drake emissaries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Angmarim coffers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should regroup at the bottom of the stairs where the mission began.You should regroup at the bottom of the stairs where the mission began'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'Precarious steps lead up into Caranost. There upon are Orcs who mean to throw you from the ruin into the arms of the slavering allies below. Fight through their number and clear the steps of their threat.Further into the ruins of Caranost you find more Orcs. In order to assist the Free Peoples, you must continue to drive them out and reach the top of the stairs at Caranost.Reach the small encampment at the top of Caranost's stairsFind the Scout'Fighting on steps is too dangerous for me. I am glad you kept your footing. Let us return to the camp.'Scaling the stairs at Caranost will prove a difficult endeavour. The Orc forces there are entrenched, but there is a need to infiltrate the ruin and continue efforts to drive the Orcs out.Tell the mission giver that you wish to take the fight up the stairs of Caranost to drive the Orc enemy from the ruin.Complete the Mission: Steps of CaranostYou have taken the steps and can return to the mission giver with news of your victory.'Battling through the precarious stairways is not something that I envy. I will understand if this ask is too great even for you. Still, Caranost can be scaled and the enemy can be driven from within if we persevere. Are you willing to fight up the ruins and take the stairs of the great structure of Men?''I send you with all haste and well-wishes. You will need it to keep your footing on the precarious climb to the top of Caranost.''I did not doubt that you would return victorious. I am, however, impressed with the alacrity with which you met the task. Surely the resistance there must have been overwhelmed by your superior strength and cunning. Well fought, ${PLAYER}. Well fought.'You have been tasked with retrieving the sulphurous secretions of gredbyg.Collect grodbog mucous, and extract grodbog poison glands within the grodbog hive.Collect grodbog mucous (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Extract poison glands from gredbyg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to the entrance of the hive.Return to the entrance of the hive'Great work, ${PLAYER}! The more explosives the better, I always say. Now let's get out of this disgusting place!'A grim darkness rises in the ruins of Gorthad. You were asked to set forth and discover what evil stirs in the accursed ruins.Discover the evil within the ruins and destroy it.Discover and destroy the source of evil in the ruinsFind the Scout'This bodes ill, ${PLAYER}. We should return to our settlement and inform the others. If gaunt-men be about, then trouble is surely brewing in these lands.'The post is late from the Shire and the news is that something has the post-carrier spooked and unwilling to make the crossing. You have been sent to investigate.Escort the post-worker across the Ford'Now that the Ford is safe, the post can be delivered without fear. Let us return.''Merry me, it sure is good to deliver the post again. You have my thanks!'Sarn Ford teems with unnatural energy since the passing of a stranger cloaked in black. A hobbit mail deliverer from the Shire asked for assistance in getting their deliveries across the Ford.The post coming out of the Shire proper has slowed to a crawl because of something that has upset the deliverer responsible for crossing the ford. You are asked to speak with the mission giver to investigate.Complete the Mission: Stirring at Sarn FordSomething was stirred in the wake of riders crossing the ford. You assisted the post-person in crossing the ford and now normal delivery resumes. Return to the mission giver and inform them of what transpired.'Well met, ${PLAYER}. Do not be surprised, we scouts know about you and all you have done. We talk. Do not worry, nearly all the discussion is good!

'In fact, we think that you are the right person for this request from a post-deliverer out of the Shire. It appears that San Ford is no longer as safe as it was in days past. Something happened there and there are now reports of evil spirits stalking any who cross.

'This post-worker needs to pass over the Ford and asked if there was any way that we might be able to help in their protection. That is where you come in, my friend.''The post is an important way for all of us to stay connected, and I daresay that this latest interruption is setting a good many of us on edge. If you are willing to help, I know that there are many minds that will be put at ease.''Living water, you say? Deary me this is not good to hear. Mayhap we will need to set up nightly patrols along the Ford. For now, we have you to thank for the return of our beloved Post.'A post from Bruilos in Evendim asks for assistance with the recovery of weapons and supplies stolen by the Angmarim.Make your way to High King's Crossing in Evendim to speak with Bruilos.Speak with Bruilos in High King's Crossing in EvendimComplete the mission: Stolen Weapons and Supplies.Complete Mission: Stolen Weapons and SuppliesReturn to Bruilos at High King's Crossing in Evendim.Speak with Bruilos at High King's Crossing in EvendimPost:

A recent attack near the Way of Kings resulted in our small band losing a number of weapons and supplies to the Angmarim forces there. If you can assist in the recovery effort please report to the great statue and seek me out.

- Bruilos'I am pleased that my message has been found by one of such noble sort. In these days, scoundrels may take many forms, and danger is never far from the road.

'It was so that our porters were set upon by such bandits when they drew too near the Way of Kings. There, the transports were attacked by Angmarim. Though the porters escaped with their lives, they were forced to abandon their cargo—arms and provisions meant for our small encampment.

'We have neither the strength nor the numbers to assault the tomb where the stolen goods were taken, but perhaps you may fare better than we. If you are willing, of course.''You have returned and with you, all that was lost!

'I am most pleased that you happened upon my note, and more grateful still that you have returned from your venture unscathed.

'There is much hardship in these lands, and more than enough folk willing to do harm. It is good to know, then, that there is still courage and decency to be found in this world.

'You have my thanks, friend. You have done a good deed for us all.''Eight swords and eight axes were lost, and I fear they may now be in the hands of those knaves. Six crates of supplies were taken as well, containing salves, food, and other necessities for those who dwell here.

'If you are able to recover what was lost, return to me when the task is done.'You have been tasked with defeating the dreaded two-headed troll Stûg-and-Zar.You should defeat the fearsome troll Stûg-and-Zar.Defeat Stûg-and-ZarYou should regroup near the entrance to the cave.Regroup near the entrance to the cave'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'Your attempt to thwart the collusion between the bandits and the Ordâkhai forces seems to have failed, and an expeditionary force of bandits heads north.Hatokáli bandits prepare to leave their encampment to journey northward, likely to bolster the ranks of the Ordâkhai warriors in the north. You must stop their advance.Defeat Hatokáli sharp-shooters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Hatokáli brutes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy the bandit barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You destroyed the barricades built by the bandits, and assailed their position. Confront the overseer.Confront the Hatokáliri overseerThe overseer, knowing he is defeated, begs you to stop and listen to him.Speak with the bandit overseerThe bandit overseer said that the treasure was not worth dying for and asked that you retrieve the price paid from within his camp.Collect the stolen treasure from the campYou have the treasure and information that needs to be given to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.Find Mizâdi's scout along the road to the north'We must bring this news to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.''You will pay for the men you cost me!''I am bested. My life is not worth the tithe the Ordâkhai paid.'

He winces.

'Many of them have lost their faith and wish to flee across the river. They paid a handsome sum in treasure for access to our crossing, but I will not give my life to protect them.

'More are meant to arrive within the day. I know only that they said they would come from the east.

'Go within our camp. Recover the treasure they paid. I will not keep it if a blood tithe be levied against us for having it.''The Ordâkhai were not recruiting the bandits, but instead were looking for a way across the river. This bodes well, my friend.'Your mission is to travel to Zikrum-dûl to defeat the apothecaries and their leader as well as destroy their workstations.Your mission is to travel to Zikrum-dûl to defeat the apothecaries and their leader, as well as destroy their workstations.

Speak to Ashâmi to travel.Complete Mission: Stop the ProductionYou have successfully eliminated Samûku and the apothecaries as well as destroyed their workstations. Return with the scout to Ashâmi with this report.'Greetings ${PLAYER}. The apothecaries of Zikrum-dûl are converting poison they gather from usan-kûni. You need to travel there and destroy their workstations and defeat their leader, Samûku.''${PLAYER}, your task is to travel to Zikrum-dûl to defeat the apothecaries and their leader Samûku, as well as destroy their workstations.''Good to see you ${PLAYER}. I have heard of your success in Zikrum-dûl. Urash Dâr will be safer with those apothecaries no longer crafting their poisons.You have been tasked with defeating snow-beasts that have been driven into the cavern and destroying their food source.You should defeat snow-beasts and destroy slop barrels within the cavern.Defeat snow-beasts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy slop barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should regroup near the entrance to the cave.Regroup near the entrance to the cave'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'A posting from an Earth-kin calling for help in learning why their 'once-brothers' have become plagued by corruption.Make your way to the Earth-kin camp in Ram Dúath and seek out Chief Tuokki to ask how you can help.Speak with Chief Tuokki at the Earth-kin camp in Ram DúathComplete the mission: Studying Corruption.Complete Mission: Studying CorruptionReturn to Chief Tuokki at the Earth-kin camp in Ram Dúath, provide the samples you collected, and tell him of the large cave-claw you faced.Speak with Chief Tuokki at the Earth-kin camp in Ram DúathPost:

My pain grows with the loss of my once-brothers. They have turned ill-tempered and smell of foul earth. They are tainted by the land and more. We have need of help.

- Chief Tuokki'Our once-brothers who till the earth with stone beaks grow sick in this land. They cry out for help, but we know little of the thing that makes our once-brothers ill.

'We cannot spare many of our number to aid them. So I turned to a way that is strange to us. Many have come here, like you, and helped us before.

'Would you help us, and our once-brothers?''I can see from the marks upon their flesh that our once-brothers suffer greatly. We must speak with our own people and use what skills we have. Perhaps then we will find a way to take away their pain.

'You have done all I asked, and more. For this, we call you friend. You have helped our once-brothers, and you have helped us.

'For this, we give you our thanks.''There is a creeping sickness in them. It goes into skin, into muscle, into bone. We must look at their flesh and study it, so that we may find a way to make them well again. We think, but we do not know, that a beast crawls among them and carries the rot.'Your mission is to cause a disturbance in a cave that is known for its spiders, but is now being occupied by Ekhamâti soldiers. Extinguish the soldiers' fires and sound their alarms to bring the spiders down on them.Your mission is to cause a disturbance in a cave that is known for its spiders, but is now being occupied by Ekhamâti soldiers. Extinguish the soldiers' fires and sound their alarms to bring the spiders down on them.

Speak to Setokúli to travel.Complete Mission: Succulent SoldiersYour mission is to cause a disturbance in a cave that is known for its spiders, but is now being occupied by Ekhamâti soldiers. Extinguish the soldiers' fires and sound their alarms to bring the spiders down on them.'${PLAYER}, we have located Ekhamâti soldiers who have begun to occupy a nearby cave.

'Fortunately this cave is well known to our people to be the home to dangerous spiders. I ask that you travel there and cause a disruption. If you extinguish the soldiers' fires and then sound their alarms within their camps, the spiders should do our work for us. You will need to make your escape quickly to ensure you are far from there before reinforcements arrive.'Your mission is to cause a disturbance in a cave that is known for its spiders, but is now being occupied by Ekhamâti soldiers. Extinguish the soldiers' fires and sound their alarms to bring the spiders down on them.'I am glad to see you return safely. You have done well to disrupt the Ekhamâti camp. Take this for your troubles.'You have been tasked with defeating the Hill Giant, Svalfang, in the Wildwood.Use the summoning horn at the east side of the hill to summon Radhril to your side.Pick up the summoning hornYou should talk to Radhril.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Use the Call Radhril skill and talk to RadhrilYou should find Svalfang.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Find SvalfangYou should defeat Svalfang.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Defeat Svalfang'I commend your efforts, ${PLAYER}! Come, let us return and report our success to the Free Peoples.''Let us proceed with caution. We do not yet know why Svalfang wanders through the Wildwood.'A posting from Longo Burrow in Tuckborough requests some assistance on his farm.Find Longo Burrow at his farm in Tuckborough and ask him how you can help.Speak with Longo Burrow at his farm in TuckboroughComplete the mission: Tend and Defend Crops.Complete Mission: Tend and Defend CropsReturn to Longo Burrow with your collection of beans and pipe-weed, and tell him that the shrew burrows have been closed.Speak with Longo Burrow at his farmPost:

My farm-hands are all feeling ill as of late, and I cannot tend to everything my farm needs. I am looking for assistance from those able to do some light farm work in Tuckborough.

- Longo Burrow'I had thought I would lose a good portion of my crops—and perhaps my livelihood besides—until you came along. My farm-hands all took ill at once, the poor fellows. A terrible happenstance for them, and no small trouble for me.

'But now that you are here, and looking fit enough to lend a hand, I daresay we may yet come through this in good order.''It is shaping up to be a wonderful harvest, after all! I shall begin bundling the beans as soon as we have finished with the niceties, and I will set the pipe-weed leaves to drying directly after. If all goes well, I may have the finest tobacco I have ever grown!

'I have you to thank for much of it, my friend. I—and my poor farm-hands—are most grateful that you have taken up the work while they are laid low. You have done us a fine turn indeed.''My beans are ripe upon the vines and need gathering so that I may bundle up the bushels and send them off to market. And, if you can believe it, the new pipe-weed I have been growing is coming along splendidly. I should like to have the leaves gathered and dried, that I might see how they smoke.

'Oh, and there are meddlesome shrews making their way onto the hill. If you could do something about those as well, it would save the crop from being nibbled to ruin.'At a ruin outside of the nearby village there is a terror growing among the turtles. The matron who watches over the clutch has grown increasingly aggressive and, sadly, must be put down.Defeat the turtle-matronDefeat dread-turtle young (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and speak with a Scout'Sad times that it came to this. We are grateful for your effort. Let us head back.'Turtles are not often something that hobbits fear greatly, but there is one in the ruins that causes them to tremble. The scouts from Glyn Helyg asked you for assistance in removing the menace from their midst.A rather large turtle is threatening the hobbit-folk fishing and dredging in the nearby swamp-land. Speak to the mission giver to help them out with this problem.Complete the Mission: Terrible Turtle TroubleHaving dispatched the turtle and her brood, you should now return to the mission giver and let them know of your deeds.'Hullo there friend. Would you be willing to help us with a rather large, small problem we have? It is not the kind of problem that we usually have in these parts. You see, there is a terrapin of unusual size living in the ruins at the edge of the murky water not far from here.

'Normally she leaves us well enough alone, but recently her little ones have been snapping up all the fish and even snapping at some of our folk.

'We know it seems cruel, but if we do not do something soon, we might start running low on food to feed our families. Sometimes we need to push back a little on nature. I am afraid that this is one of those times.''A pity that such a gentle creature is so incensed. We do not know what else to do. Please, do your best to be quick about this. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''There was no other way than this. I am glad that you handled this so quickly, friend. Here, you deserve this for such unselfish work.'Seek out the Orc commander in the tower of Tharbad and defeat him.Defeat the Orkish commander of Tharbad TowerDefeat the Orc commander of Tharbad TowerApproach the scout to return to camp.Approach the scout to return to camp'Let us return to Hithriel.'A particularly brutal Orc captain has made the old tower of Tharbad his base of operations.

The mission giver has asked you to clear the courtyard approaching the tower of defenders to open the way for an attack on the tower itself.Clear the tower courtyard of defenders.Clear the tower courtyard of defendersApproach the scout to return to camp.Approach the scout to return to camp'Let us return to Hithriel.'Approach the accursed flame and extinguish it.Approach the accursed flame and extinguish it to banish the spirits.Douse the accursed flameApproach the scout to return to camp.Approach the scout to return to camp'Let us return to Hithriel.'Gorgar the Ruthless has been tracked to Goblin-town. Will you find and defeat him in time?Use the summoning horn at the cave entrance to summon Hórin and Ausma to your side.Pick up the Summoning HornYou have arrived in Goblin-town with Hórin and Ausma.

You should talk to Ausma.

If you become separated, the summoning horn at the cave entrance to summon Hórin and Ausma to your side.Use the Call Dwarves skill and talk to AusmaFind Gorgar the Ruthless somewhere in Goblin-town.

