If you become separated, the summoning horn at the cave entrance to summon Hórin and Ausma to your side.Talk to Ausma'Let us return to Annâk-khurfu and report these events to Glóin!''Gorgar is in here somewhere, and should have a few of his own Orcs with him, but we don't know much else. We should be careful. Oh, and watch out for goblins. They're sneaky, and we could be swarmed by them very quickly. They don't call it Goblin-town for nothing.''That's him over there, and what must be the new Great Goblin. Huh. This must be what Orcs consider "diplomacy". A locked gate stands in our way, and I don't see another way through. Here, take these and see if you can get it open.'

She hands you her lockpicks.

'I know my dirty tricks have been rubbing off on you, don't deny it. Hórin and I will keep watch. Once this gate is open, we attack!'Ausma is clearly angry. Her fists are tightly clenched, teeth bared beneath her mustache. She takes a moment to breathe and calm down.

'Damn that Gorgar! I swear, I will have his head yet! Let's get moving. We need to report this to Glóin.'Hunting for the items lost by the mariner when he came to shore you happened upon massive footprints. They lead you here to a cave to face the beast within.Confront and defeat the beast.Defeat the beast: ModrankThe beast falls to your mighty attacks, but the haversack mentioned by the mariner is nowhere to be found. There is a commotion near the entrance.Return to the entrance of the caveThe tomb-robber is dead. Get back to the mariner.You have been tasked with dispatching a powerful beast in Misthallow.Find and defeat Frálnath.Find and defeat FrálnathDefeat Bergelmir.Defeat Bergelmir'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'A posting from Pete Shadetree asks for an adventurer to help recover his lost tools.Make your way to Bree-town speak with Pete Shadetree at his forge near the West Gate.Speak with Pete Shadetree at his forge near the Bree West GateComplete Mission: The Blacksmith's Lost ToolsAssist Pete ShadetreeReturn to Pete Shadetree with his tools. You will find him at his forge near the West Gate of Bree.Speak with Pete Shadetree at his forge near the Bree West GatePost:

Needed, an adventurer with a will of steel. I recently lent some tools to prospectors from the south. The ruffians returned without my tools, but with a tale too tall to regale in this post. Seek me out at my forge in Bree-town if you can assist.

- Pete Shadetree'Ah, you saw my notice. Thank you.

'There have been a good many folk coming into Bree as of late, and I have been busier than ever. I made a decision, which appears now a bad one, and some of my tools have gone missing in a place too dangerous for me to enter.'

He sighs.

'You see, the folk to whom I lent my tools made their way into the Barrow of Taradan to the south-west. When they encountered something terrifying there, they buried my tools and ran.

'I need those tools recovered, if you are willing to take up my cause.''Oh, thank you!

'I really thought I could trust them, but it turns out they were fools, and worse, cowards.

'Here, my friend, as a small thanks for your efforts.'A posting from Pete Shadetree asks for an adventurer to help recover his lost tools.Make your way to Bree-town speak with Pete Shadetree at his forge near the West Gate.Speak with Pete Shadetree at his forge near the Bree West GateComplete the mission: The Blacksmith's Lost Tools.Complete Mission: The Blacksmith's Lost ToolsReturn to Pete Shadetree with his tools. You will find him at his forge near the West Gate of Bree.Speak with Pete Shadetree at his forge near the Bree West GatePost:

Needed: an adventurer with a will of steel. I recently lent some tools to prospectors from the south. The ruffians returned without my tools and with a tale too tall to regale in this post. Seek me out at my forge in Bree-town if you can assist.

- Pete Shadetree'Ah! You saw my notice. Thank you kindly.

'There have been a good many folk coming into Bree of late, and I have been busier than ever. I made a decision—one that seems rather foolish now—and, as a result, some of my tools have gone missing in a place far too dangerous for the likes of me.'

He sighs heavily.

'You see, the folk to whom I lent my tools made their way to a barrow away to the south-west. There, they encountered something that frightened them badly enough to flee. In their haste, they buried my tools and ran, leaving them behind.

'I need those tools recovered, if you are willing to take up my cause.''You have recovered my tools! I scarcely believed I should see them again.

'I truly thought I could trust those folk, but they took my good will and repaid it by proving me a fool. I shall be more careful with whom I lend my things in the future.

'You, however, are an honest and good sort. I am most grateful for the trouble you have taken on my behalf.

'I shall endeavour to be less of a fool—and rather more diligent in my choices—from this day forward.''If my need were not so great, I should never have trusted them with such a thing. But there you have it. I am in rather a bind, and I fear I have little choice but to ask for your help.

'Please, make haste. I have need of those tools, and I would dearly like to have them back.'Your mission is to infiltrate the Ekhamâti camp, steal their torches, spill hog's blood, and eliminate their dôla all to spread the fear of the Blood Spectre.Your mission is to infiltrate the Ekhamâti camp, steal their torches, spill hog's blood, and eliminate their dôla all to spread the fear of the Blood Spectre.

Speak to Setokúli to travel.Complete Mission: The Blood SpectreYour mission is to infiltrate the Ekhamâti camp, steal their torches, spill hog's blood, and eliminate their dôla all to spread the fear of the Blood Spectre.'I have a task for you, ${CLASS}. The Ordâkhai are a fearful people and many of them have heard a story since they were children of a blood-stained spectre who steals the life right from the Men of the south when they sleep. We believe you can be that spectre to them, to ignite their fears.

'I ask that you travel to their camp to steal their torches and spill this hog's blood around to give the impression of the spectre. Then eliminate the dôla in the camp to spread the fear. You should try and avoid any guards while you are there to ensure the story will be believed, but do not hesitate to defeat any who happen to discover your presence.'Your mission is to infiltrate the Ekhamâti camp, steal their torches, spill hog's blood, and eliminate their dôla all to spread the fear of the Blood Spectre.'Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. That should stoke the fires and spread fear throughout their ranks. Take this as a token of gratitude for what you have accomplished this day.'You have been tasked with destroying the Angmarim ritual at Shakal-atrâd.Destroy the ritual obelisks.Destroy the ritual obelisks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the ritual stopped, let us return and report your success!'You have been tasked with thwarting the ghastly presence at Shakal-atrâd.Clear out the ghastly presence within the ruins of Shakal-atrâd.Clear out the ghastly presence'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the ruins cleared, let us return and report your success!'You have been tasked with destroying the source of the Taurogrim corruption that has spread over Óinsbridge.Find Glymlauf.Find GlymlaufDefeat the Taurog corruptors.Defeat Taurog corruptors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Glymlauf.Defeat Glymlauf'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'Forcing the Orcs back across the bridge at Caranost will provide the small band of defenders at the outskirts of the ruins some respite. Make your way across the bridge and drive the foe back.Reach the opposite side of the Bridge to CaranostFind the Scout'Their numbers seemed endless. You are truly a hero. Quickly let us return to the mission giver and tell them all you have done.'In an effort to drive the Orcs back out of Sírlond and out of Caranost, you were recruited to battle across the bridge that links the outpost and the ruin. If you are successful, the hope is that you can establish a foothold on the other side of the ancient bridge.Speak with the mission giver and have them escort you to the Bridge of Caranost where you will attempt to drive the Orcs back into the ruin.Complete the Mission: The Bridge to CaranostYour success at forging across the bridge affords the encampment at Sírlond a welcome respite. Return to the mission giver with this report.'Well met again, ${PLAYER}. We have more news from the fortress of Caranost. The Orcs there send expeditionary forces across the bridge with increasing frequency. Sírlond asks for our assistance in pushing across the bridge in an effort to not only drive the foe back but also to start a counter offensive. Are you willing to make the charge across the bridge?''Your objective is clear, ${PLAYER}, make your way across the bridge defeating whatever the foe throws at you as you battle across. The hopes of Sírlond rest upon your able shoulders.''A message-raven arrived just ahead of you, ${PLAYER}. You are victorious again. Sírlond is appreciative and the Free People rejoice in this victory. Thank you for your efforts.'You have been tasked with dispatching the wargs inside Shathur-munzu.Defeat the wargs inside Shathur-munzu.Defeat Wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'Mizâdi's scouts, after you recovered the orders, infiltrated the ranks of the Ordâkhai and determined that they are organizing crates to collect the scorpions that escaped into the village west of their encampment.Find and destroy the crates at the area before the cross-roads. The Ordâkhai intend to use the crates to store and deliver the scorpions from the nearby town.Burn the empty crates (${NUMBER}/10)Find Mizâdi's scout.Find Mizâdi's scout'We will see if this action stops the action of the Ordâkhai, or simply slows their advance.'You have been tasked with dispatching the worms in the Clutch-hollow.Enter the Clutch-hollow and defeat the worms within.Defeat worms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'With their escape craft destroyed, the remaining Ordâkhai and Utûgi forces are stuck on the northern shore of the river. The time is right to crush them once and for all.Mizâdi's forces want you to show no mercy. Hunt down the stragglers who wanted to escape to the south and grant them an ending fitting of such a terrible enemy.Defeat the remaining Utûgi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the remaining Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You returned to the shore and found a small number of stragglers. After a quick foray into the marsh you emerged victorious. Now to find Mizâdi's scout and return to the encampment.Find Mizâdi's scout'The enemy is defeated, and they shall not rejoin their brethren to the south. We have earned this victory, my friend. Let us return.'You have been tasked with defeating ukhrâsh and plugging leaks in Gundabad.You should defeat ukhrâsh and plug leaks.Plug leaks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat ukhrâsh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should defeat the ukhrash matron.Defeat the ukhrash matron'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With all the ukhrâsh defeated, let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'You have been tasked with collecting gears and redirecting the flow of water within the dwarf-made waterways of Shalakâm.You should redirect the flow of the water and collect any gears that you find.Redirect the water (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect gears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to the entrance of the dungeon.You should return to the entrance of the dungeon'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With all the water redirected, let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with removing the bats who have descended upon the dwarf-ruins of Zarkul-sulûn.Pick up a torch and burn bushes to clear bats.Burn bushes to clear bats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Pick up a torch to burn the bushes'Great work, ${PLAYER}! I hope those bats do not return! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'You have been tasked with exploring a recently uncovered dwarf-vault in Gundabad.Find a way out of the dwarf-vault.Find a way out of the dwarf-vaultDefeat the Orcs!Defeat the Orcs!'Well done, ${PLAYER}! You defeated that vile Orc, Lúrthrok the Grasping! I was worried when you became trapped in the vault. I am glad you are all right! Come, let us return to Hórin and report your success!'Where has Bilbo Baggins gone?Celeblír waits for you to help him search for Bilbo.Talk to CeleblírElrond is waiting to speak with you outside in Rivendell.Talk to Elrond outside the Last Homely HouseElrond suggested that you consult Arwen, Elladan, Elrohir, and Glorfindel about Bilbo's whereabouts.Talk to Arwen across the bridge to the northTalk to Elrohir outside the entrance to the Last Homely HouseTalk to Glorfindel to the southElrond has come to the front of the Last Homely House to hear if anyone has seen Bilbo Baggins today.Talk to Elrond outside the Last Homely House'I thought for certain we would find Bilbo by now!''This way, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps someone has seen Bilbo in the past few minutes, while we have been discussing his absence. That would be worthy of laughter indeed!''Go on, ${PLAYER}. Be not shy!''What is it, my friend? You may speak freely, even should Celeblír fear to do so!'

You tell Elrond that you have not seen Bilbo Baggins around Rivendell for some time, and wonder at the hobbit's absence. Elrond frowns, puzzled.

'I have not seen him today. I have only just come from my library, and he has taken to walking in the valley of late. Perhaps my daughter or one of my sons has seen him outside? Speak with them and with Glorfindel, if you should happen across him. It may be they have seen Mr. Baggins and your worries, and those of Celeblír, are unfounded.''Bilbo Baggins? I have not seen him today, but my thoughts have been elsewhere. On this day I might have walked right by him without noticing him!

'Or perhaps not. He has always been quick with a greeting and a smile whenever our paths have crossed; I would have seen him. I think you will not find him up the hill, for I just came from there.

'On cool days such as this he is most often seated in the house, composing songs and melodies by the fire. If he is not to be found within, you may discover him walking the lanes of Imladris, admiring the trees and the flowers. I am sorry to be of so little help. Perhaps someone else has seen him.''Word travels quickly, friend. I know for whom you search.

'My brother has gone inside to see if Bilbo fell asleep in the Hall of Fire again, or if he lost track of the time while working in his quarters. Elladan should soon return to tell us which of these proved the answer to Bilbo's disappearance.''Is it true that Bilbo Baggins has gone missing?'

You tell Glorfindel that you have not given up on the search, and Bilbo may yet turn up somewhere in Rivendell. The Elf-lord nods.

'That is the most likely outcome, but I would advise you to remember the hobbit about whom we speak. Bilbo is more susceptible to adventure's call than most of his kind.

'I will search for him as well.''None have seen Bilbo Baggins within the house or in the vale since yesterday, ${PLAYER}. Some of my folk believe he may have found a quiet, sunny place in which to write, or perhaps has fallen asleep somewhere among the trees and will awake rested, refreshed, and bemused at the worry for him.

'But we may need to consider another possibility. You know of the secret company that recently departed Imladris. It was decided in council that Bilbo should not become a part of that fellowship, but now I wonder if something might have driven the hobbit to follow after them.

'We cannot discount that possibility, friend. Our hobbit may not be in complete control of his feet or his sense of duty, and both of these might send him in pursuit of that secret company. I do not believe it is so, but neither should we dismiss it out of hand.'Having found Bilbo Baggins within the dungeons of Goblin-town, you must now return him safely to the surface!Your rescue of Bilbo Baggins from Goblin-town will not be complete until you have returned him safely to the surface!Talk to Bilbo Baggins in the depths of Goblin-townBilbo has asked to speak to you before dealing again with Bauglám Fork-tongue.Talk to Bilbo in Goblin-townBauglám Fork-tongue seems strangely confident about facing you in single combat.Talk to Bauglám Fork-tongueBauglám Fork-tongue seems especially pleased with himself.Defeat Bauglám Fork-tongue in single combatBauglám Fork-tongue has chosen the troll Thukafak to face you in single combat.Defeat Thukafak in single combatYou defeated Bauglám Fork-tongue's champion. Will he now agree to the terms of the contest?Remain alert for further trouble'Let's get out of here before he changes his mind!''Let us hurry to the surface, ${PLAYER}! I have seen more than enough of Goblin-town to last a lifetime, or even two!'Bilbo lowers his voice and speaks to you in little more than a whisper.

'When I was walking in the mountains, I was captured by a party of goblins, and they started hauling me to their camp. We had gone no more than a hundred feet or so when a second patrol of the creatures came up, led by this fellow. Now, I wouldn't say I'm an expert on goblin-kind, but I have had enough run-ins with them to know that they love gold more than anything. So I had to think fast, and... well, I told them I had been an adventurer in my younger days, and I had hidden sacks of gold in the mountains.

'The goblins fought among themselves for the right to my treasure, just as I thought they would! This fellow won the contest right quickly, before I could get away, and the next thing I knew I was locked in that cell here in Goblin-town! I couldn't tell them the truth, of course: that there were no sacks of gold. When I adventured with the dwarves I did end up with two small chests of silver and of gold, but that was a long time ago and they were never as large as the rumours around the Hill would put them!'

Bilbo claps his hands together. 'I think I've got it!' he says. 'You'll get us out of this, ${PLAYER}, trust me!''Single combat seems fair to me. No one can intervene. This will be a test of strength, one-on-one, and everyone here agrees this is fair, yes?'

Bauglám Fork-tongue stares at you, his lip curled in a sneer.

'There is no backing out now, ${RACE}. Are you prepared to fight?'Have the scouts from Rivendell spotted Bilbo Baggins on the high moor outside the valley?No one remains at the camp-site of the Elf-scouts in the high moor. Their duties have likely taken them down the slope to the south-west.Descend the slope south-west of their camp-site to find the Elf-scoutsRinghul scouts down the slope to the north-west of Canaddal's position.Find Ringhul down the slope to the north-westCanaddal and Ringhul have both returned to their camp-site and now discuss the troubling question of Bilbo's disappearance.Listen to Canaddal and Ringhul discuss the situation'I hope you find Bilbo Baggins, friend. We will keep looking for him as well, and send word if we find any sign of his passage.''What brings you here, ${PLAYER}? Wait... did you hear that sound?'

Canaddal peers around at the wind-blown expanse.

'Your mission here will have to wait, friend. We have been having difficulties with wild creatures all day, and it seems sunset's arrival will only bring further troubles! Help me fight them off and then I will hear your news.''What did you say? Bilbo Baggins has gone missing? Are you certain he has not merely fallen asleep in a warm corner somewhere within the Last Homely House?'

You tell Ringhul that none have seen Bilbo since yesterday, and as night approaches the folk of Rivendell grow more concerned at his absence.

'Yes, that is troubling. Let us return to my camp and discuss the situation with Canaddal.'Did Bilbo venture into Giant Valley, and if he did, did he emerge again unharmed?If Bilbo strayed into Giant Valley, there may yet be a friendly face willing to help recover him.Talk to Arifael inside Giant ValleyYou should conceal yourself behind the hide-covered dwelling just north of Arifael, and quickly!Hide in the dwelling just north of Arifael, and quickly!Mendorn has arrived and is none-too-pleased to see Arifael.Remain in hiding and listen to the conversation of the giants<rgb=#FF0000>Do not be seen by Mendorn</rgb>Mendorn is prepared for combat.Talk to Mendorn<rgb=#FF0000>Arifael must not be defeated!</rgb>Arifael is satisfied that Bilbo never came here.Talk to Arifael'Return to Elves. Tell them Bilbo did not come this way. He must have gone somewhere else.

'Now so must you.''This dangerous place, little ${RACE}. If you say hobbit come to Giant Valley, hobbit in big danger. Not all his kin friendly as Arifael.

'But I will bring you to giant-dwellings in Stonemere. Maybe save little hobbit, if not too late.''I will squash you into jelly, tiny pest, and then do the same to your pet! He may look like giant, but he not actual giant.

'On the inside, he small like you!''Have I seen anything else of your size or smaller here in the valley? No, to my disappointment! I would have squashed anything like that into jelly!''We put Mendorn into his place, and there he will stay! It will be some time before he dares fight with us again.

'I do not think he has seen your friend. Your Bilbo did not come this way.'If Bilbo did not travel south, perhaps he journeyed north. His old adventuring friend Glóin may have seen him.If Bilbo wandered north instead of south, Glóin may have seen his old adventuring companion.Talk to Glóin at his camp in the Misty MountainsWere those shouts in the distance? You and Glóin should <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for the disturbance!<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> into the distance and learn of the disturbanceScouts are returning to Glóin's camp with haste. What has happened?Learn what has caused the hasty return of Glóin's scoutsGlóin needs your help to defend his camp.Talk to Glóin and prepare for the onslaughtGlóin is outside his camp in the Misty Mountains.Talk to Glóin'I hope Bilbo has not gotten himself in real trouble!''What brings you to the mountains, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Glóin that no one in Rivendell has seen Bilbo Baggins today, and the Elves have started to worry that something may have happened to the old hobbit. Glóin looks at you with surprise.

'Bilbo? Missing?''Will you stand with us, ${PLAYER}? My Longbeards are a worthy fighting force, but this fell storm sounds unnatural, and we can use whatever help you might give to us! A horde of snow-beasts? Let us hope my scouts exaggerate!''Ah, yes, Bilbo.

'As I was saying, we spoke this morning around ten o'clock. We spoke about this and that, and then he bid me farewell and left the camp. I thought at the time that he turned right and made his way back to Rivendell, but... now I am not certain of it. Are you sure none have seen him in the valley?

'Well, if he turned left instead, he would have climbed the slope, leaving Rivendell behind. And with that spirit of the storm loose and causing trouble, it could be Mr. Baggins lost his way....

'I don't like this, ${PLAYER}. If only I had noticed which way he turned when he left! It seemed like such an ordinary visit, I thought nothing of it.'If Glóin is right, Bilbo Baggins may have ventured north into the Misty Mountains instead of returning to Rivendell.If Bilbo did come this way, some of his tracks may have survived being covered by the recent snows.Examine the tracks in the snow to the northMore of Bilbo's tracks may lie to the north, hopefully not covered by the recent snows.Defeat the goblins and journey north in search of more tracksA small camp-fire to the north-east of the tracks may conceal some sign of Bilbo.Search the camp-site to the north-east for sign of BilboPerhaps Bilbo evaded the goblins at the camp-fire and journeyed further north. You should search for more tracks in the wide-open space at the top of the slope.Defeat goblins and journey north in search of more tracksA goblin-camp to the north-east lies directly in the path of the last tracks you found. What was Bilbo thinking?Investigate the goblin-camp to the north-eastA dying goblin lies among the slain. Did he see Bilbo?Talk to the dying goblin in the camp of the slain'Dead goblins and wargs, but no sign of Bilbo? We need to find him, and quickly!''You... you're lookin' for that halfling... aren't you?'

The goblin coughs, spluttering and choking on his own blood.

'You're too late! My wargs found 'im... by rights he should belong to me... but look around! Sorrog and Bauglám squabbled over the spoils... claimed the halfling for... themselves....'

He closes his eyes, near to death. You demand that he tell you where Bilbo was taken, and before he dies he mumbles a single word.

'No....' he mutters, and dies laughing.The goblins must have taken Bilbo to the mountainside encampment of Pinnath Fenui.You should clear all the goblins and wargs from Pinnath Fenui to ensure none attack you from behind while you confront their leader at the top of the camp.Defeat all the goblins and wargs in Pinnath Fenui before confronting their leader at the top of the campSorrog Crows-eye is not pleased.Listen to Sorrog Crows-eye and learn what happened to BilboYou have a choice: either to slay Sorrog Crows-eye or to spare his life.

To spare him, ensure that you have him selected and then use the <rgb=#00FF00>No</rgb> emote.
To slay him... you know what to do.Things have gone from bad to worse: Bilbo is not held captive in Pinnath Fenui, but in Goblin-town!Wait for Celeblír to arriveCeleblír has arrived, and waits to hear what you learned about Bilbo's whereabouts.'We cannot leave Bilbo in Goblin-town. We must do something!''We cannot leave Bilbo in Goblin-town. We must do something!''Bilbo has been taken to Goblin-town? This is an unlucky turn, ${PLAYER}!

'Goblin-town! I can hardly believe this ill fortune!''Bilbo has been taken to Goblin-town? This is an unlucky turn, ${PLAYER}!

'Let us hope they show the same mercy to our hobbit that you showed that goblin!'Bilbo has been taken to Goblin-town, and now Celeblír has a plan for getting inside.Celeblír plans to cause a distraction that will let you access Goblin-town's main gate.Talk to CeleblírCeleblír will distract the goblins, drawing them away from the entrance to Goblin-town. You must avoid detection by the goblins until he lures them away!Remain hidden while Celeblír leads the goblins awayThe goblins will surely have hidden a spare key to the gate somewhere outside Goblin-town.With the spare key in your possession, you can now unlock the gate to Goblin-town.Celeblír has returned, and without his goblin-pursuers.Wait for Celeblír to arrive'Now that you have unlocked the gate, we should be able to rescue Bilbo!''Follow me, ${PLAYER}, and stay close. You'll need some way to open the main gate to Goblin-town, but you won't be able to search for such a thing while there are goblins outside.'Goblin-town will be full of the creatures, but if you act quickly you might be able to slow them down by locking the gates to other parts of the city.By locking gates to other parts of Goblin-town, you can keep under control the number of goblins with which you must contend.

<rgb=#FF0000>Stay on the upper level! If you fall to the lower levels you will be swiftly defeated.</rgb>The Guardian of the Jails has arrived, and he is not pleased to see you.

<rgb=#FF0000>Stay on the upper level! If you fall to the lower levels you will be swiftly defeated.</rgb>Talk to the Guardian of the Jails<rgb=#FF0000>Do not fall down to the lower level!</rgb>Now that it is (relatively) safe, Celeblír has arrived.Wait for Celeblír to arrive'You have done well to hinder the goblins, but even so we cannot hope for Bilbo to be unguarded. We must act quickly!''If you think you're saving your little friend, you're more stupid than you look! No one escapes from Goblin-town!'You are very near to rescuing Bilbo from Goblin-town, you can sense it!Bilbo must be held captive in the dungeons of Goblin-town.Find Bilbo in the dungeons of Goblin-townBilbo is held captive in a cell in the dungeons of Goblin-town.Listen to the discussion between Bilbo and his captorRukzot and his minions stand between you and Bilbo's freedom!Defeat Rukzot the Vicious and his minionsNow that you have the key to Bilbo's cell, you can free him from his captivity.Unlock the door to Bilbo's cellYou have freed Bilbo from his cell, but this is only the first step to the hobbit's freedom.Talk to Bilbo in the dungeons of Goblin-town'We should be off while we can, ${PLAYER}! Let us not tarry within Goblin-town any longer than we must!''Well done indeed, ${PLAYER}! I never doubted that you would best him, and best him you have!

