You should let the twins discuss their findings, or lack thereof.Listen to the twins' conversation'There's nothing else that can be done here. We should continue moving.''Other scouts already told me about the insects swarming the Bruinen, but I've never seen such an infestation before!

'Elrohir and I agreed to see how many we could each defeat before meeting downstream. Since he's already gotten a head start, perhaps we could work together. Surely that doesn't count as cheating!''It seems the swarm found the Black Riders' mounts. I count only three steeds, however -- the river may have carried the rest further.

'Go, find Elrohir in the fens and see if he requires aid. I shall stay behind to make sure the Riders did not escape into the woods.

'Oh, and let him know how many insects we defeated. I'm sure he was no match for us!''Elladan convinced you to help him with our little competition, didn't he? I kept track at first, but...' Elrohir gestures to the nearby horse corpses with a sigh. 'What I found -- or rather, what I didn't find -- troubled me.'

'Three horses upstream, five here... that makes eight of the nine mounts accounted for. I scoured every part of the woods for the Riders, but to no avail. If any of them linger in the Trollshaws, they have made themselves scarce.

'Hold on, what's that in the water? Is that a cloak?'The Great Eagle your party has been following has inexplicably disappeared.You should talk to Elrohir.Talk to ElrohirSomething's not right.

