You should examine the footprints.Examine the large footprintsYou should talk to Elrohir to see what he's discovered.Talk to ElrohirWhatever creature created these footprints may be dangerous.

You should follow Elrohir and help him track it down.Follow ElrohirYou and Elrohir have tracked down the drake matron.

Defeating it would make the area safer for travellers passing through Eregion.Defeat the drakesThe drake matron has been defeated.

You should talk to Elrohir.Talk to ElrohirYou and Elrohir have returned to Pembar to find Elladan waiting with the Great Eagle Gwaihir.

You should talk to Gwaihir.Talk to GwaihirYou should listen to the twins' discussion about Gwaihir's report.Listen to the twins' discussion'We should rest here and gather our strength before continuing. We have yet to embark on the most difficult part of our journey.''${PLAYER}, I'm certain the Eagle noticed our presence and flew here, but I don't see him. Do you?'

Elrohir surveys the area outside the ruins and frowns.'Whatever killed these boars was an even match in size for our friend.' Elrohir holds up a feather that is certainly too large to belong to any normal bird. 'It seems I wasn't wrong about his location after all. He must have left the area once he realized he had intruded on something's territory.

'Of course, I doubt that creature, whatever it is, was an even match in power. After all, the Eagles are a more than capable folk. But this creature may be dangerous to anyone travelling through this area, and that does not bode well for our errand.

'Let's track it down.''That drake matron commanded a most fearsome brood! It'll be safer here now, though I fear that will change.

'We ought to head back to Pembar; Elladan must be wondering where we are.''Greetings. You have my thanks for defeating the drakes. I had no desire to involve myself with them, seeing as how they do not threaten me or my kin, but they did not care for my presence. At least I may now deliver my message more easily.

'We have not discovered any sign of the Black Riders, nor any other tidings of the Enemy's servants. However, wolves gather along the banks of the Anduin in great numbers. What this indicates, I cannot say I know.'The Redhorn is not kind to any soul, person or beast. Raging blizzards and the biting cold stand in your way, daring you to continue.Your party has paused to take a break from the snow, but it's time to move on.

Elladan has something to say to you.Talk to ElladanYou should follow the twins through the pass.Follow the twinsFrost grims have separated Elrohir from you and Elladan.

