<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Regroup near Sutwarden'I commend your efforts, ${PLAYER}! Come, let us return and report our success to the Free Peoples.''We approach the steps of Sutwarden. Let us move swiftly through the tower ruins, destroying their banners and defeating every foe we encounter.'A post from Bombard Foxtail of the Mathom Society requesting assistance with recovering mathoms from the Dourhands.Find Brombard Foxtail outside of the Mathom-house in Michel Delving and ask him how you can provide assistance.Speak with Brombard Foxtail at the Mathom-house in Michel DelvingComplete the mission: The Missing Mathoms.Complete Mission: The Missing MathomsReturn to Brombard Foxtail with the mathoms and the news that the Dourhands have been dealt a blow.Speak with Brombard Foxtail at the Mathom-housePost:

Brigands and thieves stole several mathoms from our collection and we are in need of assistance in their recovery. If you can spare some aid, please visit me at the Mathom-house in Michel Delving.

- Brombard Foxtail'A terrible calamity has befallen us here at the Mathom Society, and I scarcely know where to begin!

'With mathoms being delivered and discovered all across the land, we have hardly had a moment to organize them, catalogue them, and put them properly away. Why, they have been piling up faster than we can keep track of them!

'And now, to make matters worse, it appears that our latest deliveries have been pilfered by a band of Dourhand brigands, intent - apparently - on making the lives of decent Shire-folk as miserable as possible.

'The Bounders, bless them, are far too busy with the mundane doings of the Shire to go chasing after thieves on our behalf. And so, in a moment of desperation, I posted my request for aid.

'And now, here you are.''All eighteen recovered, and a proper lesson taught besides! You truly are a good soul.

'We shall see to it that these are put in order and safely stored. If only we could persuade a few more good folk to join the Society and lend a hand with the cumbersome business of sorting, storing, and displaying the multitudes of mathoms we are forever collecting, perhaps such a calamity might not befall us again!

'It is a great deal of work, you know, keeping track of so many perfectly wondrous things.''Here you are, indeed! Willing, able, and ready to teach those Dourhands a proper lesson in what comes of thievery!

'I can direct you to the very place the scoundrels are hiding. I would ask that, while you are about it, you recover the mathoms they have stolen from us. There are eighteen in all.

'Eighteen! A dreadful number to have gone missing, if you ask me.'You have been tasked with recovering stolen treasure, hidden within Shakal-atrâd.Find the stolen treasure within the ruins of Shakal-atrâd.Find the stolen treasure within the ruins of Shakal-atrâd'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With the treasure recovered, let us return and report your success!'The crew of Nenglor encounters Yarikh ashore again, and this time prepares an assault to end the Corsair's time on the sea for good.We made our way to shore in the cover of darkness. The Corsairs were unaware of our approach....Speak with the captainDown the shoreline toward the flickering camp-fires and torches we moved. In the night, the shadows danced around the tents. Captives held outside the tents and nary a defender could be seen. It was an ambush....As the battle fell quiet, a scream came from where we placed our launch; followed by the sound of fire on the sea and the screams of men and women going into the deep....Return to the captain where you landed'What have I done?

'I have failed them all. I have lost my ship. I have lost it all....''No alarm. No warning. No soul watching over their only means of escape to their ship. We shall not make the same mistake as we did before.

'Leave their boats. The prize is the captain of these curs and him alone.

'Move swift into their camp, free the prisoners that they have captured and put an end to them.

'Go, swiftly.'After returning to Pelargir, the surviving members of the crew set about recovering and rebuilding.Our visit to the port was fraught with difficulty. Pelargir was hospitable and our faces recognizable from our saving some members of the city some time before. We got on with our business at hand....Speak with the captainSomething felt different. The jovial nature was gone. There was a curtness in the voice and the manner was prescriptive. I should have known that something had changed. I set out about my tasks....Collect the mapCollect the foul-smelling barrelPost recruitment letters (${NUMBER}/10)With the hold filled and a new crew coming aboard we were prepared for our next adventure. If only...Find the captain'If all is now at the ready, then we should set about final preparations. Yes, it is time to seek our vengeance and bring those curs to heel.''I have set most of the crew to their tasks, but there are some duties that must be handled by the only individual I truly trust.

'I have secured the assistance of a map maker who confided that they can provide a passage where we must go. I will require this of you. You will find the map stashed among a sheaf of papers near an empty stall near the dock across from our ship's bow.

'Second, there is the matter of some illicit materials formerly owned by the Corsairs who raided this city some time hence. I will have it procured by no other. It should be under the watchful eye of a healer, no less, along the alley near the opposite dock. Collect this and bring it to me.

'Last, we need new blood on the ship and that can only mean we post our letters throughout the immediate area. Take these and post them where it seems the will best be seen.

'Away now, there is much left to do.'Spiders toil in the shadow of the Old Forest and entrap any living thing they can find. These corrupt creatures are a menace and must be stopped, but worse, folk have gone missing and might be food for the creatures if we cannot free them. Search the woods for any potential captives that the spiders may have.Free spider victims in the Nettinglade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Make your way back to the entrance of the missionFind the scout at the mission entrance'That could have been a frightful end for some. Fortune smiles that you were here to assist, ${PLAYER}. Let us return.'It has come to your attention that some folks from surrounding areas near the Old Forest have gone missing. The only visible evidence of their disappearance is the presence of cobwebs and stretches of disturbed ground before reaching the tree line. It is possible that spiders are responsible for the abductions. You are tasked with investigating the disappearances.At the outskirts of the Old Forest free folk and others have gone missing. Evidence suggests that they are being dragged into the Old Forest by spiders. You are tasked with a mission to rescue as many as you can.Complete the Mission: The NettingladeAfter successfully freeing those trapped by the spiders, it is now time to return to the mission giver and provide a report.Speak with the mission giver'This is a stranger one, ${PLAYER}. Along the Old Forest there are reports of folk going missing. Visual evidence suggests that there are spiders collecting poor unsuspecting travellers or would-be adventurers wandering too close to their nests within the dark wood. The reports of the missing vary from Men to hobbits and some scouts have reported hearing that brigands and half-orcs have gone missing too. If you are willing, we will reward you for looking into the goings on in the Old Forest.''Be cautious, ${PLAYER}. The forest teems with life and some of it more malevolent than spiders. I do not want to have to send a party looking for you.''Good to see you return, ${PLAYER}. I had feared that if you were lost in the forest that we may never find you. It is no surprise that the spiders grow more brazen. The woods have long fallen from a place of mischief and wonder to one now of malevolence and dark spirits. I hear tell that there is a man who dwells within, but I think that is a tale for another time. Thank you for your effort.'You have been tasked with finding a great treasure in Sundergrót.Locate and find a way to open the treasure in Sundergrót.Locate the dwarf-treasureFind the ancient keyFind the old keyClaim the dwarf-treasure in Sundergrót.Claim the dwarf-treasure'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with destroying the Taurogrim corruption that has spread over Óinsbridge.Destroy the Taurogrim corruption at Óinsbridge.Destroy Taurog corruption (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Taurog-dens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'Amon Firn is occupied by half-orcs. Their leader must be somewhere amongst the ruins. Defeat him!Defeat the half-orc captain.Defeat the half-orc captainFind the Scout'Well done, ${PLAYER}! You have defeated the half-orc captain!'Brigands have overrun Gaervarad. You are tasked with defeating every last enemy amongst the ruins.Speak with the mission giver to travel to Gaervarad.Complete the Mission: The Ruins of GaervaradReturn to the mission giver and let him know you have defeated the brigands.Return to Hithriel and tell him the brigands are defeated'Brigands have overrun the ruins of Gaervarad, ${PLAYER}. We must defeat them!''Be careful ${PLAYER}, brigands occupy those ruins.''You have done well ${PLAYER}, as agreed, you are deserving of payment. Take this and know that we are grateful for all you have done.'Brigands have overrun Gaervarad. You are tasked with defeating every last enemy amongst the ruins.Defeat brigandsDefeat brigands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'Well done, ${PLAYER}! You have defeated the brigands!'You have been tasked with rescuing Skóthi from the clutches of an Iron Crown ritual.Find and rescue Skóthi.Find SkóthiStop the ritual.Stop the ritual<rgb=#FF0000>Stop the ritual before Skóthi is sacrificed</rgb>Rescue Skóthi.Rescue Skóthi'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Skóthi is safe and sound. Let us return and report your success!'At last, the master of the forces attempting to retake the village and scorpions has been revealed. The time is at hand to remove the Ordâkhai dôlo leading this effort.Your procurement of the orders was translated and the identity of the dôlo in charge of the effort revealed. You must make your way to the village and thwart the machinations of the dôlo, before he corrals and recovers the scorpions.Defeat Khómabekh DôloThe dôlo is defeated. The threat to Mizâdi's forces is diminished, for now. Return to the scout and the encampment to share the news.Find Mizâdi's scout'We should return to our camp. I believe there has been enough violence this day.'The scouts have discovered a secret underground supply line between Goblin-town and Gundabad. Ausma thinks this is a good opportunity to damage Gorgar's forces.Use the summoning horn at the beginning of the tunnel to summon Ausma to your side.Pick up the Summoning HornYou should talk to Ausma.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Ausma is missing, and the Call Ausma skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Use the Call Ausma skill and talk to AusmaYou should destroy supply carts throughout Fauthshúg with the bombs Ausma gave you.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Ausma is missing, and the Call Ausma skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Destroy supply carts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Foreman StrakhfutYou should talk to Ausma.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Ausma is missing, and the Call Ausma skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Talk to AusmaAusma has said she has an idea, and that you should stand back. You should watch this play out.Witness Ausma's "idea"'Well done, ${PLAYER}! Let us return to the Annâk-khurfu!''This is surely the right tunnel. The goblins must have dug into this old Longbeard mine and found it leads straight to Gundabad. We're lucky we didn't have to walk the whole way! Now that we have found the supply train, it's time to do some damage. These fools... they thought we would not notice them moving supplies underground and did not assign many guards to protect the caravan, but we are dwarves! We are just as at home under the mountains as they are. They will regret their mistake!

'We need to find the foreman in charge here and defeat him. I assume he will be near the front. Here, take these.'

She pulls out a satchel and hands it to you. Ausma grins mischievously as you peer inside to see a number of small explosives.

'I might have learned a few tricks during my time in Mordor. One of those should be enough to take out each of those carts. Destroy the supplies as we move. If we succeed here, we may be able to prevent them from supplying Gundabad for weeks! Let's move!''Look what they've done to this place! Damn filthy Orcs. I have an idea. We can destroy this foul defacement of dwarf art and remove this tunnel as a supply route to Gundabad all at once.

'You should probably stand back.'At sea once again, the mariner spends time within the captain's chamber listening to a disconcerting speech.With the new crew aboard not having yet earned their sea-legs, they did not notice what was happening. My time at sea gave me insight beyond theirs and I knew that with the travelling of the sun we were headed to the south... and Umbar.Speak with the captainAching. The pain swelling within. The strain at the loss of the first Nenglor. All those lost. Every waking moment the thoughts of the crew crept in, and every night in dreams their voices echoed from the sea....Attempt to calm the captainSpeak with the captainSomething had broken within, I did my best to wrest control of the madness seeping in.Calm the captain againSpeak with the captainTry as h- as I may, the anger would not come under control. Listening, I heard the true resentment.Speak with the captainSorrow took hold, and there were only tears. Were they loud enough to drown out the cries?Approach the captain'I let the tears speak in that moment.''Confronting me away from the crew was smart, friend.'

There is an undertone of menace to the word "friend."

'I knew you would recognize the portents in the sky. This new crew, so trusting...

'I ask you, would they have sailed with me had I not promised them wealth? Did they know I gave away one crew already? That the brigand we now chase across the sea has dismantled me so that I seek only his destruction to fill the void that now fills the space where once my heart had been?

'Nay, friend.'

Less menacing this time.'Do not tell me to be calm!'

He spits vehemently.

'What I need from you is strength! I need your strength of spirit and arm. You alone understand the terror wrought upon the first Nenglor... what we lost.

'I will not be pitied. I will have my vengeance for those who were wronged. I will pursue this quarry like the dog he is until the very end of the world if I must.

'I will not be deterred. I will not be dissuaded by reason, or ridicule!

'There is only one payment that will sate me, and it is blood!''I know my mind. I do....'

The captain calmed down.

'This map, containing only four points - four spokes - is but thin parchment and yet, mightier than the halyard that hoists our sails to drive us to our quarry.

'Out there, beyond the depths that swallowed my brethren whole and drove them down into the deep, there is an enemy in need of reckoning and by the stars above, I will set right the course of history.

'Should we be complacent, instead? Should we not revisit upon this enemy the same sentence they passed on Men and Women earning their wage?'

He shakes his head violently.The captain sighs deeply.

'It is not madness that consumes me, it is grief. It is humiliation. Twice this scoundrel evades my capture. And the last...'

He cuts himself short and offers a sob.

'So many dead. So many under my command.'In the deepest shadows of Valdhellir lies the domain of Drauglok, the mighty pack-leader of the den and one of the eldest Wargs in the Slade.Your mission is to defeat the terrible Warg, Drauglok, in Valdhellir.Defeat Drauglok'Well done, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'From within Kêr Bréin, a powerful hobgoblin leads the raids on Skarháld and keeps watch on the newly-laid eggs of the Frost-horde.Your mission is to defeat the powerful hobgoblin, Rukhnúl, at Kêr Bréin.Defeat Rukhnúl'You've done well, ${PLAYER}! Let us report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with defeating the Angmarim sorceress and retrieving an ancient text Tûr Ágal.Defeat Calaminag.Defeat CalaminagRetrieve the ancient text.Retrieve the ancient text'Well done, ${PLAYER}! Not only is Calaminag defeated, but the text Hórin seeks has been recovered as well. Let us return and report your success!'You have been tasked with defeating the Taurogrim in Grazadh-gropor.Defeat the Taurogrim in Grazadh-gropor.Defeat Taurogrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'Haudh Nírui has been overrun by grave-robbing goblins. If we defeat their leader we may be able to scare them off for now.You should defeat the Blogmal gang-leader.Defeat the Blogmal gang-leaderFind the Scout'Well done, ${PLAYER}! You have defeated the Blogmal gang-leader!'You have been tasked with defeating the wardens of Caivád Sâr.Defeat the wardens of Caivád Sâr.Defeat SengaDefeat AvlaithDefeat Tárlakh'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'Led by a terrible hobgoblin, the forces of Gundabad have invaded the Keep of Tharrazhâr. You have been charged with repelling their attack and securing Skarháld.The gate to the throne-room of Tharrazhâr has been sealed by the forces of Gundabad and the mechanism to open it is missing a piece. You should find the missing piece of the gate mechanism.Find the missing piece of the gate mechanismYou have found the missing piece of the gate mechanism, and you should now use the gate mechanism to open the gate to the throne-room of Tharrazhâr.You have cleared a path to the hobgoblin leading the forces of Gundabad in the Keep of Tharrazhâr. You should defeat Graznúl.Defeat Graznúl'You fought with valour, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and bring word of your victory to Hórin!'After a long patrol in the open waters of the Bay of Belfalas, the crew of the Nenglor happened upon a Corsair raiding party anchored at Tolfalas.We made our way to shore with the intent of beaching the Corsairs there. I remember how the sea air smelled as we rowed ashore....Speak with the CaptainMy orders were clear, find the launches, scuttle them and return forthwith. It was a take not without danger, but the risk was clear....Scuttle Corsair launch boats (${NUMBER}/4)With the boats scuttled, there was no retreat back to sea for the Corsairs. I sensed a chance for true glory and forged ahead to find Yarikh and his crew....Find and defeat Yarikh and his crew (${NUMBER}/24)The Corsair's ruse worked too well. While we came ashore they assaulted the Nenglor. I returned to the spot where we landed and stared at our launches retreating to the Corsair's vessel....Return to where you landed'They were too numerous, ${PLAYER}.'

The captain looked out on the longboat retreating toward the Corsair's ship.

'There will be time for redemption. There will be time for vengeance.''Keep your courage, ${PLAYER}, we have the enemy where want them. Along this shore are their launches. If we move swiftly we can strand them here and send word back to the capital that there is a crew of Corsairs stuck on Tolfalas.

'Make your way along the shore and scuttle the launches you find. I will stay here and await your return.'Gond Orchal has been corrupted by a gaunt-lord who is raising Wights from the various tombs. This evil must be defeated.A gaunt-lord is corrupting Gond Orchal. Clear the tombs of Wights and defeat this evil.Find and defeat the gaunt-lord corrupting Gond OrchalDefeat Gond Orchal Wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Scout'Well done, ${PLAYER}! You have defeated the gaunt-lord!'You have been tasked with investigating a fire in the Wildwood, then quickly returning to town.Use the summoning horn west of Trestlebridge to summon Radhril to your side.Pick up the summoning hornYou should talk to Radhril.

