'We require your help in intercepting these waggons so that we can salvage any valuables and provide them to Mizâdi's forces.'Your mission is to intercept a caravan of waggons filled with supplies and weapons, defeat and soldiers guarding it, and turn over the caravan to Mizâdi's forces.'I am glad to see you.

'I have heard of your success. The supplies you secured from the caravan will help greatly in our war efforts. Thank you.'You have been tasked with destroying the mark of the Iron Crown that inhabits the tower of Caivád Sâr.Destroy the Iron Crown standards and lesser watching stones found within the tower of Caivád Sâr.Destroy Iron Crown standards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the lesser watching stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#00FF00>Challenge</rgb> the spirits of the watching stones'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'All of your efforts have not stemmed the advance of the Ordâkhai, who are intent on recovering the scorpions from the town near the cross-roads south of Emax Dûl.Mizâdi's scouts learned that a new courier reached the encampment near the cross-roads. They believe the purpose, the method of recovery, and the leader spear-heading this effort are contained in the orders. You have been asked to recover the orders.Collect the orders from the Ordâkhai bóroYou have collected the orders. Find the scout and deliver the orders to them.'We should not waste time, friend. We must return to the camp.'The scout reads the orders.

'It is clearer now. There is a dôlo among these forces intent on succeeding where another has failed. Their ambition is great, as is their resolve.'You have been tasked with destroying the unhatched eggs in the the Clutch-hollow.Enter the Clutch-hollow and destroy the worm eggs within.Destroy worm eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin'Prince Ingór has declared that the Hall of Vérnozal needs to be cleaned up to suit the needs of the Zhélruka Clan.Defeat bats.Defeat mountain bats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat rats.Defeat cave rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat gredbyg.Defeat scavenging gredbyg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat cave-claws.Defeat mountain stone-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Zóva at the entrance of Vérnozal.Return to Zóva at the entrance of Vérnozal'Well done! That looks the last of the beasts, lurking within these halls. Prince Ingór will be pleased! Let us retire for the night and get some well deserved rest.'Prince Ingór has declared a Zhélruka Clan feast to commemorate their new Mountain-home.Join the feast!Join the feast!Eat some food!Eat some food (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Drink some drinks!Drink some drinks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Listen to Prince Ingór.Listen to Prince Ingór'Welcome one and all, to Gundabad, the home of the Zhélruka.'Prince Ingór has declared that the newly forged Zhélruka swords must be properly tested before they can be gifted to the Longbeards.Fight your way through the Orc encampment.Fight your way through the Orc encampmentSummon and defeat the Orc Captain.Summon and confront the Gundabad Pit-lord'Good work! I would say every one of those Zhélruka blades held their own in combat. We should return to Vérnozal and inform Prince Ingór of our success on this day!'The group of Longbeard explorers is in trouble and Prince Ingór wishes for the Zhélruka Clan to come to their aid.Rescue the trapped Longbeards.Rescue the first trapped LongbeardRescue the second trapped LongbeardRescue the third trapped LongbeardRescue the fourth trapped LongbeardClear fallen rocks as you search for trapped explorers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Regroup with the rescued Longbeards.Regroup with the rescued Longbeards'We thank you, brave ${CLASS}. Without your assistance we would certainly be done for. I believe I speak for all of us when I say that we are ready to return to safer dwellings whenever you are!'Prince Ingór has declared that the Hall of Vérnozal needs to be further decorated to suit the needs of the Zhélruka clan.Mine crystals.Mine crystals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the ukhrash matron that has appeared.Defeat the ukhrash matron'Good work obtaining those crystals! Those menacing ukhrâsh were no match for you! Prince Ingór will be pleased with your efforts! Come let us return to the Hall of Vérnozal with crystals in hand.'Zóva, Prince Ingór's advisor, has devised a plan to further disrupt the Orkish factions within Gundabad.Work to sabotage both the Orc encampment and the hobgoblin encampment.Take weapons from the Orc encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy provisions at the Orc encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Take totems from the hobgoblin encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy supplies at the hobgoblin encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Continue work to sabotage both the Orc encampment and the hobgoblin encampment.Return to Zóva.Return to ZóvaWait with Zóva and see if your plan works.Wait with Zóva and see if your plan works'Good work! With the Orcs and hobgoblins fighting amongst each other once more, reclaiming Gundabad has become an easier task! Let us return to Prince Ingór and inform him of our success on this day.'A group of visiting Dourhands has become very disruptive.Talk to the Dourhand guests.Talk to the Dourhand guestsPolish the Dourhand axes.Polish the Dourhand axes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to the Dourhands.Talk to the DourhandsFetch ales for the Dourhands.Fetch ales for the Dourhands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring ales to the Dourhand guests.Dance with the Dourhands.Talk to the Dourhands.Talk to the DourhandsFetch the Dourhands some food.Fetch the Dourhands some food (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the food to the Dourhands.Witness the events transpire.Witness the events transpireFight the angry Dourhands!Fight the angry Dourhands!Talk to Prince Ingór.Talk to Prince Ingór'Did these Dourhands come to test my resolve?! I have not the time for such fools when the fate of my peoples still hangs upon my decisions each day.''Ah, what a nice hall you and the Zhélruka have! We heard about the rules here. You have to greet us as kin and make us feel most welcome! I say then, give us a proper welcoming!

'We've been travelling for so long. Look at our axes! They are as dull as an unfavourable ${RACE}. Give our axes a polish, will you?''Hmm, these are much sharper, yes! We feel a little more welcome.

'Now, what of some drink? We have been travelling for so long, we are all parched! Our throats are dry as the Brown Lands! Bring us some ales, will you?''Ah, these ales quench our thirst indeed! Now then, it is so quiet in here. Where is the liveliness? Come, dance with us as we drink some more!''All this drinking and dancing has made us hungry! Bring us some food or I will start complaining loudly about how unwelcoming you are to great dwarf explorers!''Bah, you call this food?!'

The Dourhand looks about and speaks very loudly.

'The Zhélruka seem to know nothing about cooking a proper meal! I've eaten better food at a goblin's camp!''It would be too easy to cut down each one of these sad excuses for a dwarf. If you were not a trusted ally, ${PLAYER}, there would be blood on this floor today. Remember that, Dourhands.

'Now go! Leave Vérnozal and never come back! If I see you again, I will not hesitate to raise my sword. Heed my word as Prince Ingór, of the Zhélruka.'Prince Ingór wishes to hunt the great frost-drake, Svalnath, and to bring great honour to the Zhélruka clan.Use the summoning horn at the beginning of the mission to summon Prince Ingór to your side.Pick up the summoning hornYou should talk to Prince Ingór.

