<rgb=#FF0000>If Prince Ingór is missing, and the Call Prince Ingór skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Defeat Svalnath<rgb=#FF0000>Prince Ingór must survive</rgb>'Ah ha! Svalnath, the beast is no more! Let us take its head and mount it upon the walls of Vérnozal so that all will know the might and the great deeds of the Zhélruka!''Svalnath is near. Come, this way!'Charged by the masters of Gramsfoot you are told to go to Hoarhallow and kill the Hobbits there for a feast. Goblins from Grothum will come along and scoop up the bodies that you leave behind.Slaughter the Hobbits for Dinner (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Killed them good you did. We'll gather 'em up and bring them to Uglash. I'll have the boys clear a path for you back to Gramsfoot.'After some years passed, secrets become known and the mariner's story picks up the trail of Yarikh.The information proved true, and I found myself within a yawning maw of a cavern. All throughout the sound of men and women shuffling goods and coin. Could retribution be at hand?Defeat the Corsairs in the cavern (${NUMBER}/10)Collect the treasure chestWith the spoils in hand, I made my way back to the entrance....Return to the captain at the cavern entrance'Aye, this will do. Come, let us return to the city so that we can continue.'You have been tasked with assisting Rangvald with training dwarves for war.Spar with the first Longbeard.Spar with the first LongbeardSpar with the second Longbeard.Spar with the second LongbeardSpar with the third Longbeard.Spar with the third LongbeardSpar with the fourth Longbeard.Spar with the fourth LongbeardSpar with the fifth Longbeard.Spar with the fifth LongbeardSpar with the sixth Longbeard.Spar with the sixth Longbeard'Great work, ${PLAYER}! You have helped train these soldiers well! I now know this will be a battle that we will win!''I've been practicing!''I'm ready!''Do not hold back. I want to put on a good show for the commander and get promoted!''Ha, let us spar!''Let's see what you've got, ${CLASS}.''Ha, do not worry! I will go easy on you!'Despite the failure of the Iron Garrison, the dwarves will not allow the Orcs of Khazad-dûm to spill forth into Azanulbizar, the Dimrill Dale.Your mission is to recover trinkets stolen from the Dwarves of the Iron Garrison.Defeat the Pûlpum Stone-keeperCollect dwarf-trinkets stolen from the Iron Garrison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'It can hardly repay what was taken from the Iron Garrison, ${PLAYER}, but it will have to do for today! Let us return!'After reclaiming Gabilazan from the Dourhands and their foul allies, the Dwarves of Durin's Folk must now contend with the other inhabitants of the Misty Mountains.Your mission is to repel the meddlesome stone-giant troubling the dwarves at Gabilazan.Defeat invading snow-beasts at Gabilazan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fend off the vicious cold at Gabilazan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to repel the meddlesome stone-giant troubling the dwarves at Gabilazan.Your mission is to repel the meddlesome stone-giant troubling the dwarves at Gabilazan.Secure the gate at Gabilazan'I've a feeling that pesky giant will be back again, ${PLAYER}, but you have done well! Let us return!'You have been tasked with crippling the efforts of the Gundabad Orcs who have taken hold of the old armoury in Thikil-gundu.Destroy weapons barrels and weapons racks guarded by Gundabad Orcs in the Steel Keep.Destroy weapons barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy weapons racks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'A notice posted by Paladin Took calls for aid against a growing threat along The Shire's borders.Make your way to The Great Smials in Tuckborough to speak with Mayor Paladin Took about the growing threat on the borders of The Shire.Speak with Paladin Took within the Great Smials at TuckboroughComplete the mission: Trouble Near the Border.Complete the mission: Trouble Near the BorderReturn to Paladin Took at the Great Smials and tell him of your victory over the goblin horde.Speak with Paladin Took at The Great Smials in TuckboroughPost:

Required, adventurous type with weapons and gumption to charge headlong into enemy forces and root them out of The Shire. If compelled by these words, seek me out at the The Great Smials in Tuckborough.

- Paladin Took'Your coming is most fortunate, friend.

'The Bounders bring word of goblins seen in greater numbers about the Greenfields. I will not suffer such foul folk to creep into the Shire; else the townships shall beset me from dawn till dusk, clamouring that I rid them of the menace.

'Rather than send many Bounders to scour the fields and hedgerows for these goblins, I have looked beyond our borders and sought stout-hearted adventurers, such as yourself, to take up this charge.'

He smiles with no small measure of pride.

'For one such as you, it should prove a simple enough task.''I knew you were the very one for this undertaking.

'You have spared me no small measure of needless vexation. Yet, to speak plainly, my friend, my concern over the goblins grows with each passing day.

'They have ever been a nuisance, it is true, but now their boldness waxes. If they walk openly upon the Greenfields, how long shall it be before they press beyond the bounds and into the Shire itself?'

A heavy silence falls.

'But that is a thought for another day. This day belongs to me—and to you as well, of course, my friend!''Quickly now. The sooner you return, the sooner shall my mind be set at ease, knowing that the threat is contained—and, moreover, that I shall not be beset by a bevy of displeased hobbits. Go then, clear out the cavern, and let no goblin escape your mighty vengeance.'You have been tasked with guarding Trader's Wharf from potential threats.Use the summoning horn at Trader's Wharf to summon Radhril to your side.Pick up the summoning hornYou should talk to Radhril.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Use the Call Radhril skill and talk to RadhrilYou should get into position to defend Trader's Wharf.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Get into position to defend Trader's Wharf!You should defend Trader's Wharf from the attackers.

<rgb=#FF0000>If Radhril is missing, and the Call Radhril skill is not available, try using the /pet release command.</rgb>Defeat the attackersDefend Trader's Wharf!'I commend your efforts, ${PLAYER}! Come, let us return and report our success to the Free Peoples.''Do you hear that? The footsteps of Men approach. Our time of rest is at its end. Let us prepare ourselves for combat, ${PLAYER}. The footsteps grow louder now. I hear them from all sides, converging on the docks.'Explore further along the Greyflood and find the source of the apparitions that haunt it.Explore further along the Greyflood and find the source of the apparitions that haunt it.Discover the source of the Greyflood apparitionsApproach the scout to return to camp.Approach the scout to return to camp'During your battle, I spied an ominous green flame guttering in the ruins along the river's edge - perhaps it has something to do with these spirits? Let us return to Hithriel and prepare for our next step.'You have been tasked with defeating the two-headed troll, Brog-and-Glûk, at Zarkul-sulûn.Find and defeat Brog-and-Glûk.Find and defeat Brog-and-Glûk'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With Brog-and-Glûk defeated, let us return and report your success to Ausma!'You have been tasked with collecting uncovered treasures from within the ruins of Stormwall.Collect uncovered treasure.Collect uncovered treasure (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! You have found quite a lot of treasure! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with defeating the trolls in Sundergrót.Defeat the troll crushers in Sundergrót.Defeat troll crushers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Hórin!'A notice posted by Idhrien at a camp in Enedwaith requests assistance with dealings in a terrible prison.Find your way to the Ranger's camp at Fordirith in Enedwaith and speak with Idhrien to determine what it is she desires.Speak with Idhrien at Fordirith in EnedwaithComplete the mission: Unfortunate Circumstances.Complete Mission: Unfortunate CircumstancesReturn to Idhrien at her camp in Enedwaith and inform her of your victory.Speak with Idhrien at the Echad Dagoras in EnedwaithPost:

My request is for a stalwart combatant to ensure that those unjustly imprisoned, or worse, receive the justice they deserve. Seek me at our encampment at Fordirith in Enedwaith.

- Idhrien'Grant me a moment to speak of the cause behind my request. We know of a place where grievous wrongs are wrought, and it is for those who have suffered there that I make this plea.

'Prisoners, whether warriors taken in battle or hapless folk ensnared by ill fortune, are brought to a jail nearby and there tormented, or worse. Of three who perished within those walls we have knowledge, yet their bodies could not be reclaimed.

'I seek one with courage enough to enter that den of sorrow, shatter the manacles that might yet bind others, and commit to flame those who paid the final price. Will you do this deed for me?''Then it is done. To those who could no longer defend themselves, you have brought a final rest. For those who might yet be taken, you have weakened the chains that await them.

'When all this is ended, we shall cast down that place in full. Until that day, this small solace must suffice.''Be wary, for the jailors will not freely abandon their stronghold. Guards will remain, and you may deal with them as need requires. My wish is that their cruel means of binding be destroyed, and that the bodies of the dead be burned with honour. A provisioner, a warrior, and an archer, I know, met their end within.

'Go with care.'You have been tasked with clearing trolls from a hall within Gundabad.You should uproot the trolls from a hall within Gundabad.Destroy stone-troll statues (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Gundabad siege-trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should defeat Ghámgur Tremblestone.Defeat Ghámgur TremblestoneYou should regroup near the entrance to the cave.Regroup near the entrance to the cave'Well done, ${PLAYER}! With the vile Ghámgur Tremblestone defeated, we should return to to Scout-master Ausma and report our success!'You have been tasked with clearing out ice walls within the ruins of Stormwall.Destroy ice walls.Destroy ice walls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Secure Stormwall'Great work, ${PLAYER}! With those ice walls gone, let us return and report your success to Hórin!'You have been tasked with destroying watch-towers outside the Goblin-gate.Destroy the watch-towers outside the Goblin-gate.Destroy goblin watch-towers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Scout-master Ausma!'Continuing to act on the information you recovered, Mizâdi's scouts ask you to destroy the makeshift camp the Ordâkhai are building to the west of their encampment near the cross-roads south of Emax Dûl.Scouts ask that you destroy the tents and makeshift encampment the Ordâkhai have established beneath their large encampment in the crags south-east of Emax Dûl.Burn Ordâkhai tents (${NUMBER}/6)With the tents burned, you have surely set the Ordâkhai advance back. Find Mizâdi's scout, and return to the the encampment.Find Mizâdi's scout'The Ordâkhai have lost a day's worth of effort. Surely they will stop their advance and intent. Let us return to Kusâg.'Once a great larder used by Scatha the Worm, a recently-discovered chasm in Wyrmsgráf now serves as the proving grounds for young dragon-kind in Elderslade.Your mission is to defeat many of the dragon-kind dwelling in Scatha's Larder.Defeat dragon-kind in Scatha's Larder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Well done, ${PLAYER}! Let us return and report your success to Ausma!'A recent attack by the Frost-horde has threatened to overrun the dwarves keeping watch at Grálinvarth.Your mission is to repel the Frost-horde attackers and aid the wounded dwarves keeping watch at Grálinvarth.Your mission is to repel the Frost-horde attackers and aid the wounded dwarves keeping watch at Grálinvarth.Completed?Your mission is to repel the Frost-horde attackers and aid the wounded dwarves keeping watch at Grálinvarth.Defeat the spawn of Athramóth'You arrived not a moment too soon, ${PLAYER}! Let us report your success to Ausma!'You have been tasked with protecting a large geode in Gundabad from dwarf-wight miners.Protecting the large geode from dwarf-wight miners.Destroy the Angmarim wards to halt the dwarf-wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow the geode to be destroyed</rgb>'Great work, ${PLAYER}! You were able to protect the geode from the Angmarim necromancy! Let us return to Hórin and report of your success!'With the major threat of the Utûgi and Ordâkhai eliminated, it is time to return and free those pressed into labour for these enemies.Mizâdi's scouts will not leave the people of Mûr Ghala to suffer at the hands of the Utûgi or Ordâkhai. They have asked you to return and free the workers from their plight.Free the captive labourers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You freed a large number of builders and workers. They will take refuge with Mizâdi. You should find Mizâdi's scout and return to the encampment.Find Mizâdi's scout'We have done a great deed here. Let us return to the safety of the camp.'By the breath of Hrímil Frost-heart, the gates of Gundabad were sealed shut. If the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ intend to enter the sacred mountain, they shall first have to overcome the towering wall of ice that separates them from their prize.Your mission is to repel the Frost-horde and attempt to breach the ice sealing the gates of Mount Gundabad.Attempt to breach the ice sealing Mount Gundabad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the Frost-horde at Mount Gundabad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'You have done enough for now, ${PLAYER}! Let us leave this place before the Frost-horde overruns us!'Caracals in Tir Katar have been preying on travellers in the area. Drive them out of the area and try to find any survivors.Your mission is to travel to Tir Katar and put an end to the caracals who have been preying on nearby travellers and help any survivors you can find.Find missing citizen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Khûdi caracals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat the Khûdi caracal matron, Amangísu, in Tir Katar.Defeat Amangísu'Greetings! You made the roads safer and defeated the matron. Come, we should return to Iridír.'Your mission is to travel to the west of Sul Madásh to the Lair of the Shadlúgai and gather crocodile hides.Your mission is to travel to the west of Sul Madásh to the Lair of the Shadlúgai and gather crocodile hides.Gather crocodile hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Adagím crocodiles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to travel to the west of Sul Madásh to the Lair of the Shadlúgai and gather crocodile hides.Defeat the hulking crocodile'You have gathered the hides needed, ${CLASS}! Let us return to Sul Madásh.'You were tripped up by a Lazy Prospector in the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall Event a few times.You should try to avoid getting tripped up by the Lazy Prospectors in the Hard Tack at Thorin's Hall Event.Your mission is to rid Sul Madásh of its rat problem. They are growing in number and becoming a problem for the settlement. The rats must be stopped and their nests destroyed.Your mission is to rid Sul Madásh of its rat problem. They are growing in number and becoming a problem for the settlement. The rats must be stopped and their nests destroyed.Destroy rat nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat rats in Sul Madásh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to rid Sul Madásh of its rat problem. They are growing in number and becoming a problem for the settlement. The rats must be stopped and their nests destroyed.Defeat the monstrous rat'Good riddance to those vermin plaguing our home! Though... I am certain they will be back in time. Report back to Sul Madásh.'The warriors of the Ongbúrz clan are some of the toughest fighters in the army of Angmar. They prize the ability to withstand deadly blows more readily than their lessers. Accepting their blessing will make you into a powerful bruiser with great staying power. Speak with their emissary to gain the Blessing of the Ongbúrz.You may seek the blessing of the Ongbúrz clan. All you need do is renounce all other clans.Speak with the Ongbúrz emissary'You understand now how pathetic the other clans are. Nothing more than bluster. We are the bruisers. The strong of body, the unyielding. Let me tear away that stench they call a gift, and then I shall give you a true blessing.''Yes... forsake the others and stand with us, with strength, with power, and with victory assured.

'Stand tall. Stand firm. Stand with the might and armour of the Ongbúrz. Accept our blessing and fight with a body of stone and iron.'You have arrived at Bleakrift in Midgewater Pass. Here you should find War-master Uzorr, Candaith's bow, and other items stolen by the Orcs encamped here.Candaith's pursuit of an Orc-company turned deadly when he was discovered, and in his haste to escape, he lost his bow to the Orcs. Search among the Orc-encampment at Bleakrift for anything else that may be of worth to the people of the Lone-lands, and defeat the chief of the Orc-thieves, War-master Uzorr.Recover Candaith's bowCollect battered lockboxes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat War-master Uzorr'Thank you, my friend. This bow will yet slay many Orcs before its time is ended. I thank you for its happy return. Defeating Uzorr has weakened their position, and without their commander, the rest of the Orcs here will be helpless. I will see to it that these stolen items are retuned to the people who make these lands their home.'Orcs are getting orders from something beyond them. You are to hunt through their camp at Ab-dâna, eliminate the enemy, and recover orders.Your mission is to travel to Ab-dâna and eliminate Orcs you find there to recover any orders they have so that Ashâmi can discover who is sending them.Defeat Orcs in Ab-dâna (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Recover Orc orders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'You have done well eliminating the Orcs and recovering their orders! We should return to Ub Nishir.'The brigands in Ambarûl have become bold and are attacking Iridír.As you clear areas of Iridír from attackers, raise the control point banner to signal the Dumûri.Secure the Eastern Entrance of IridírAs you clear areas of Iridír from attackers, raise the control point banner to signal the Dumûri.Secure the Western Banner in IridírAs you clear areas of Iridír from attackers, raise the control point banner to signal the Dumûri.Secure the Northern Banner in Iridír'I'm glad you were able to help secure this town. I've been dispatched to bring you back to Urmâkh, there are other matters there that require your attention.'You were tripped up by a sneaky hobbit in the Hard Tack of Thorin's Hall event.You should try to avoid getting tripped up by the sneaky hobbit in the Hard Tack at Thorin's Hall event.A massive wasp and her hive in the Gorge of Woe are altered by the corruption seeping across the land. They must be destroyed.Your mission is to travel to the Gorge of Woe and stop the hive-matron and her corrupted Urâshi wasps from spreading.Defeat Urâshi wasps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat the hive-matron in the Gorge of Woe.Find and defeat the hive-matron'The hive-matron and her corrupted wasps are no more! Let us return to Ub Nishir with the news.'A posting from a warrior named Irminric in Bree, the request is cryptic, at best.Make your way to Bree-town and speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Irminric.Speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Irminric at the South Gate of BreeFind and speak with the Elf Gonediad in Rivendell and enquire about the gift he is to give Sergeant-at-Arms IrminricSpeak with Gonediad at the Spire of Meeting in RivendellGonediad asked you to collect a pouch of seeds from Tordúril and a sword design from Hemeldir north-west of the Spire of Meeting before returning the items to Irminric with a message of kinship.Collect seeds from TordúrilCollect the blacksmith notes from HemeldirYou have collected the seeds and notes from Tordúril and Helemdir, respectively. You should return these to Gonediad and let him know.With his message and gifts in your possession, it is now time to make Gonediad's delivery to Irminric. Return to Bree and deliver the news and items to Sergeant-at-Arms Irminric.Post:

Needed: someone to assist a friend in fulfilling a promise. Visit me at my post at the South Gate of Bree for more information.

- Sergeant-at-Arms Irminric'Hello, and thank you for responding to my notice.

'I have a friend, Gonediad, he is an Elven scholar with whom I bonded over stories and battles in the Ettenmoors. He told me he is preparing to leave, and never return. He has offered me a gift, but I cannot leave my post, and I was hoping to have someone help me.

'He said he wished to give me a design for an Elven sword and seeds from the trees of his home in Rivendell.'

He looks at you excitedly.

'Have you ever seen Rivendell? I was there, only for a few moments, but the trees and the land... hidden away as it is... well...'

He sighs.

'Can you seek out my friend and collect the gift he has offered me?''Gonediad's devotion to the man and to his position are both admirable. I have done as he asked and collected several samples of the seeds that make this valley beautiful and lush.

'Take them with you and see that they are delivered to Gonediad so that he may pass them on to his friend.''Ah yes, Gonediad mentioned this to me.'

He reaches into his robe.

'I hope I have not over-explained the methods used. I would hate to confuse the Man who wishes to learn this craft. Please, return this to Gonediad and tell him that I have done my best to detail the materials, direction, and methods used to craft this sword.''Irminiric, yes. He is a good man, and I did recently send him a letter at Glân Vraig. Lainedhal must have realized he was sent back to Bree for recruitment and sent the letter on there.

'Sadly, I will not be able to see him when I do depart, as my journey will not take me near his home. I had hoped to see him at Glân Vraig, alas, there are other plans now, it seems.'

He taps his foot.

'Tordúril, a woodworker here in Rivendell, has been gathering the seeds I planned to gift Irminric. And Hemeldir, the master of the forge will have the sword design. You will find them to the north-west of the Spire of Meeting.

'When you have acquired them, return to my friend at Bree and tell him that I will ever remember his stories, his ferocity, and the nights we bled together against our common foe in the Ettenmoors.''You have returned, and with the seeds and notes I have requested.

'My friend Irminric will be very pleased, I hope. I shall miss the lad. His tales were bold and entertaining for a Man. His sword arm strong, as well.

'Please, when you return to him, tell him I shall keep close his stories, and spread the tale of his bravery and prowess among those with whom I find my rest in the West. His deeds will live on, eternally.'

He offers a wry smile as he returns the items to you.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'After listening to the words Gonediad asked you to share, Irminric stifles a tear.

'He is a true friend. I shall miss our talks, and I shall ever be in his debt for giving me these gifts.

'Please, take this -- and thank you for all you have done for me.'Acquire Promotion Points (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Acquire Promotion Points (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have been tasked with protecting the Khâlbina from threats on her route to Halrax. You were below deck for a moment when you heard shouting from above. You've been boarded by Corsairs!You have been tasked with protecting the Khâlbina from threats on her route to Jax Phanâl. You were below deck for a moment when you heard shouting from above. You've been boarded by Corsairs!Defeat Corsairs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tend to wounded crew-members (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat Captain Belizâm the Bitter.Defeat Captain Belizâm the Bitter at the ship's helm'Wow! What good fortune for the crew that you were on board to repel those Corsairs! I've been instructed to bring you back to Umbar Baharbêl via Jax Phanâl, there on the coast. There are other pressing matters for which you are needed.'Your mission is to travel to Pits of Chortáth in the south-west and help the scouts of Sâr Marsag make the paths safer to travel by thinning the pack of jackals in the area.Your mission is to travel to Pits of Chortáth in the south-west and help the scouts of Sâr Marsag make the paths safer to travel by thinning the pack of jackals in the area.Defeat jackals in the Pits of Chortáth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to travel to Pits of Chortáth in the south-west and help the scouts of Sâr Marsag make the paths safer to travel by thinning the pack of jackals in the area.Defeat the pack-leader'The lands near Sâr Marsag will now be safer from these scavengers. We should return to Sul Madásh.'Your mission is to gather mushrooms that have not been infected by the Pale Blight so that the gardeners of Sul Madásh can grow them safely within the settlement.Your mission is to gather mushrooms that have not been infected by the Pale Blight so that the gardeners of Sul Madásh can grow them safely within the settlement.Gather red mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather green mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather pale mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to gather mushrooms that have not been infected by the Pale Blight so that the gardeners of Sul Madásh can grow them safely within the settlement.'Good work! The gardeners will be pleased. We should return to Sul Madásh.'Complete many quests in Misthallow.Complete many quests in Misthallow.Complete quests in MisthallowComplete many quests in the Floodfells.Complete many quests in the Floodfells.Complete many quests in the FloodfellsEnter Iorvinas and take rubbings from the dwarf rune-stones in an effort to prove the lineage of the builders.Find the dwarf rune-stones within Iorvinas and take rubbings of the glyphs carved on them. This will help prove the lineage of the builders. Be wary of the Orcs defending the halls.Collect rune-stone rubbings (${NUMBER}/6)Find the scout near the entrance.Return to the entrance and find the scout'Let use return to the surface.'The Barkhûshim took with them historical artifacts and scrolls when they fled Kûr Anzar. You are tasked with recovering these artifacts and defeating any Barkhûshim who move to stop you.Defeat All-seeing cultists and recover historical artifacts and documents.Recover stolen historical scrolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Recover stolen historical artifacts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat All-seeing cultists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search for the Barkhûshim leader Katrakhi Mâta near the centre of Dûl Zidur.Search for the Barkhûshim leader Katrakhi Mâta near the centre of Dûl ZidurDefeat Katrakhi Mâta!'Wow, look at all those scrolls. Zuhûl will be ecstatic when he sees this! There is so much history here that you've preserved.'Defeat the Dunlendings intent on joining the ranks of the White Hand and destroy the White Hand banners where you find them.Defeat the Dunlending forces at this fort and destroy the White Hand banners.Destroy White Hand banners (${NUMBER}/5)Defeat the Dunlending forces (${NUMBER}/20)Return to the stone near where you entered and find the scout.Return to the stone where you entered to find the scout'Let us return to Echad Dúnann.'A band of Ordâkhai have invaded Gha Nêkha and are attacking the locals.Defeat the Ordâkhai bullying the people of Gha Nêkha.Defeat Ordâkhai soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have reclaimed Gha Nêkha for the people. The Ordâkhai captain has come forth to challenge you. You should answer his challenge.Defeat Upóha'Today you have saved the people of Gha Nêkha. Well, most of them anyway. Come, let us return to Iridír.'Avorthal, the Elf-prince of Celondim, has been captured by goblins and handed over to wicked Dourhand dwarves. He has been moved from the Dourhand encampment to the port-city of Kheledûl, where he will soon be taken aboard a ship destined northward and beyond all hope of rescue.The Dourhands control the port-city of Kheledûl, where Avorthal will soon be taken aboard a ship destined northward. This Dourhand stronghold is also where boxes of treasure stolen from the Longbeards by the Dourhands are stored.Defeat Dourhands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect treasure-boxes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected the treasure-boxes and eliminated many of Kheledûl's Dourhand occupants. Now you must get to the Irestone, the ship preparing to take Avorthal to an unknown port in the north.Locate the IrestoneAvorthal is on the deck of the Irestone, still docked at Kheledûl. You should free Avorthal.Free AvorthalAvorthal is being held on the Irestone, the ship docked at the port-city of Kheledûl.

Unless you free him tonight, the Irestone will carry Avorthal far from rescue and doom Ered Luin to war between dwarves and Elves.Defend Avorthal'We must hurry, ${PLAYER}. Skorgrím has assembled an army of goblins within Rath Teraig. I fear that the goblin-army will not long remain within that narrow pass.

'We must return now.''You are here to free me? Skorgrím Dourhand has raised a goblin army in the cleft of Rath Teraig, and unless we stop him, he will sweep through all the free lands!

'There is no time to waste, my friend. We will need to defeat the Captain and his crew if we are to escape from Kheledûl with our lives and bring word of the danger which grows stronger within Rath Teraig!

'The Captain will soon return. Quickly, untie my hands! We need to escape from here!'Thieving shrews have stolen Corbo Tunnelly's vegetables.Corbo has asked you to recover some of his vegetables should you happen to find yourself in the shrew-tunnel located south-east of the Staddle village centre in Bree-land.Recover Corbo's vegetables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have rescued a dozen of Corbo's stolen vegetables from the shrew-tunnel beneath Staddle's farmland. You should return them to him at the Staddle village centre in Bree-land.'Ooh, I am done for. Those thieving shrews have stolen every single bit of my produce, if you can believe it. And those constables and watchers are of no help at all!

'Habbo thinks the shrews took them into that tunnel that just opened up to the south-east. If you... happen to find yourself inside that tunnel and see my vegetables, please bring some of them back!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Splendid! My lovely vegetables! Thank goodness you came along, friend.'Collect grape samples from the vines and recover a cask for Brethilwen.You must collect grapes and a cask for Brethilwen, but watch for goblins in the area!Collect grapes from the vineyard (${NUMBER}/10)Collect the wine caskReturn to the entrance of the vineyard to find the scout.Return to the vineyard entrance to find the scout'Let us return to Brethilwen.'Experience the fellowship version of the Retake Weathertop instance.Experience the fellowship version of the Retake Weathertop instance.Experience the fellowship version of the Retake Weathertop instanceCompletedCompletedExperience the fellowship version of the Retake Weathertop instance.Experience the fellowship version of the Retake Weathertop instance.You may now experience the fellowship version of the Retake Weathertop instance when ever you wish.Experience the solo version of the Retake Weathertop instance.Experience the solo version of the Retake Weathertop instance.Experience the solo version of the Retake Weathertop instanceCompletedCompletedExperience the solo version of the Retake Weathertop instance.Experience the solo version of the Retake Weathertop instance.You may now experience the solo version of the Retake Weathertop instance when ever you wish.A drunkard at the fair was scolded by a Bounder, and has been reduced to drinking by himself in hiding. He wants revenge on the Bounders who so cruelly discouraged his behaviour.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>There seems to be a beer right in the hand of the drunkard.

The drunkard encourages you to help yourself to some beer to commiserate with the woes of the drunkards of the Faire.Drink a beer to commiserate with the poor harangued drunkardBounders can be found throughout the Farmers Faire in Bywater.

You should avoid the Bounders while drunk...and also take a little revenge upon them for being so hard on the folks who love to drink during festivals.Throw rotten vegetables at the fun-spoiling Bounders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Don't let the Bounders spot you!Now that you have assailed the Bounders with a little sweet revenge, you should return to the drunkard.

The drunkard is near the Green Dragon Inn in Bywater during the Farmers Faire.Return to the drunkard with news of your success against the Bounders'Those Bounders are so mean! Accusing me, poor innocent me, of drunkorderly and disconduct...it cannot be borne!

'You...you'll have a drunk with me, won't you, ${PLAYER}? Stick it to those nasty Bounders, eh, ${PLAYER}?''Ha ha! Well done, ${PLAYER}...you bowed them shounders!

'Hey, now...who drank my beer?'Têsegi is worried for a caravan that is heading eastward to Zajâna and has asked you to check on them.The caravan is on the road ahead, to the south-east.Search for the caravanThe caravan is under attack by bandits! You should defeat the bandits and defend the caravan.Defend the caravanYou have defended the caravan by defeating the bandits and have now attracted the attention of their leader, Shubâza.Defeat Shubâza, the bandits' leaderYou have defended the caravan by defeating the bandits as well as their leader, but now a mûmak attacks! You should defeat the enraged mûmak.Defeat the enraged mûmak'Zigêt! I am glad to find you alive and well. I got here as fast as I could. Sadly, it seems I missed all of the action!

'What were bandits doing with a mûmak, anyway? That is very strange.

'Anyway, we are very near to Kighân. I am sure the caravan will be fine. I have forgotten something important in Jiret-menêsh and must hurry back. Come along!'The Emax Dûl guard barracks may still hold a store of valuable weapons.The Emax Dûl guard barracks still house many entrenched forces that pose a threat to the ongoing resistance. Enter into the barracks, destroy any fortifications, and rout the forces within.Destroy barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Seek out and defeat Udupóla BóroDefeat Udupóla Bóro'You were to able secure the barracks and defeat Udupóla Bóro. This brings my people hope.'Your mission is to travel to Lhámuth and gather Pale Blight samples from the bog-lurkers there for the scholars of Sul Madásh.Your mission is to travel to Lhámuth and gather Pale Blight samples from the bog-lurkers there for the scholars of Sul Madásh.Gather Pale Blight samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your mission is to travel to Lhámuth and gather Pale Blight samples from the bog-lurkers there for the scholars of Sul Madásh.Defeat the enraged Adagím thicket'That should be plenty of samples for the scholars. Let us return to Sul Madásh.'Thieving shrews have stolen Habbo Greenwort's apples.Habbo has asked you to venture into the shrew-tunnel and save his apples from their uncertain fate. The tunnel entrance is south-east of the Staddle village centre in Bree-land.Recover Habbo's apples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected a dozen of Habbo's apples. You should return them to him in the Staddle village centre in Bree-land.'Misery and woe! My apples!

'I brought my crop of apples to the village centre for the Farmers Faire, and as you can see, I now have nothing, and nothing to show for it! It seems that thieving shrews came in the night and stole them all! Some townsfolk discovered the entrance to a large shrew-tunnel, and that is surely where they came from.

'They can't possibly have eaten all those apples in one night though, they must be hoarding them. If you are interested in helping me, you could go into their tunnel and bring back my apples!

'Please, save my apples!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Bless me, you've saved some of my apples! I knew they couldn't have so quickly eaten all of them.

'Thank you, friend!'From the shadow they strike. Silent in their approach and deadly in their skill. The Scara-pack takes any who would strike swiftly and massacre their foes.You may seek the blessing of the Scara-pack. All you need do is renounce all other clans.Speak with the Scara-pack emissary'You reek of another clan. This will not due. If you wish to fight and slaughter on the field of battle, then there is only the Scara-pack. Stand with us. Know victory. Slake your thirst of blood.''Stick to the shadow if you will. Strike fiercely and without mercy - it is the way of the pack. We grant you our boon so that you may strike fear and death in the hearts of our enemy.'Jackals in the furrows scavenge from the dead. It is their nature, but the defiling of fallen allies the coalition cannot abide.Your mission is to travel to Khazâda and thin the numbers of jackals in the area as well as burn the corpses of slain travellers that have been defiled by the beasts.Defeat jackals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn defiled bodies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Great work here. Those jackals were causing a lot of trouble. Let us return to Ub Nishir.'The All-seeing are assaulting Kûr Anzar!  Destroy their makeshift fortifications and repel the invading Barkhûshim forces.Destroy fortifications and defeat the All-seeing forces.Defeat All-seeing cultists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy All-seeing fortifications (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat Usóhi, leader of the invading BarkhûshimFind and defeat Usóhi, leader of the invading BarkhûshimDefeat Usóhi, leader of the invading BarkhûshimDefeat Usóhi, leader of the invading Barkhûshim'Kûr Anzar is in your debt. Now that the battle is won, you are wanted back in Urmâkh.'A ship carrying weapons and supplies has broken up and the cargo is washing ashore in the Shield Isles. Collect the salvageable supplies to keep them out of the hands of the Heirs of Castamir.Collect the salvageable supplies washed up on the beach to keep them out of the hands of the Heirs of Castamir.Collect supply crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Heirsworn Corsairs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to your boat with the supplies you collected.Return to your boat with the suppliesYou must defeat the Heirsworn Captain in order to get back to your boat.Defeat the Heirsworn Captain'Have you defeated them, ${PLAYER}? That was close! Come, let us return to Umbar Baharbêl!'A posting from Dorongúr Whitehorn asks for assistance in a personal task.Make your way to Duillond and find Dorongúr on the rise overlooking the river among the smiths.Speak with Dorongúr Whitethorn among the smiths in DuillondDorongûr has asked that you speak with Elves in Duillond and Celondim to collect packets of seeds for a gift he is making for a friend. He does not want his friend to know about the gift.Speak with Nathronwen at Duillond and collect her seed pouchSpeak with Isferon in Duillond and collect his seed pouchSpeak with Ialadir in Celondim and collect his seed pouchSpeak with Gwaloth in Celondim and collect her seed pouchSpeak with Raindis in Celondim and collect her seed pouchReturn to Dorongúr among the smiths at Duillond and deliver him the seeds you collected.Post:

I request the assistance of a person of discretion for a task that is near to my heart. If you are interested, please visit me at Duillond.

- Dorongúr Whitehorn'Mae govannen, and I thank you for answering my request. Be assured, friend, there is no shadowed purpose in it. I seek only to fashion a surprise for one dear to me; were I to be seen, the gift would lose much of its grace.

'I would ask you to gather seed pouches from Nathronwen and Isferon here in Duillond, and likewise from Ialadir, Gwaloth, and Raindis in Celondim.

'Nathronwen may be found beyond the bridge to the south, and Isferon keeps watch over the river to the north-west.

'Ialadir watches over the farm-lands of Celondim. Gwaloth keeps vigil near the crafters in the upper hills, and Raindis stands watch above the northern docks.

'Gather their seed pouches and return to me.''Each of my friends is pure of heart and has given freely. These seeds shall bloom, and in their flowering may they strengthen my friend's resolve.

'His grief is deep, and too long has he dwelt upon what more he might have done to save his beloved from so untimely an end.

'These seeds may yet bring healing, for they were gathered from many gardens and bear the flowers and herbs that his beloved held most fair.

'For this, I thank you, friend.''Dorongúr's love for his friends is rooted deep in the grief he bore from Edhelion. Loss has shaped him in ways that few among us can fully understand.

'Take these, and may the seeds of my garden help restore the heart of the one he seeks to strengthen anew.''Dorongúr's request is born of deep love for one of our kin.

'His compassion has moved my heart, and with all haste I have gathered seeds for the garden of remembrance. Take them, I beg you, and tell Dorongúr that his kindness is a light by which others may be guided.''It gladdens me to know that Dorongúr's request is being fulfilled. His heart is noble, and his purpose no less so; gladly do I offer seeds for the remembrance garden he would make.

'Take this pouch, then, and bear it back to him, that his wish may come to flower.''I am glad to give these seeds to Dorongúr. May the garden he tends bring solace to his friend, for loss lies heavy upon the hearts of our kind.''Gladly will I aid Dorongúr in the making of his remembrance garden. I believe his friend will be both surprised and comforted to know that such devotion has been given on his behalf.

'Go now with haste, and see that these are delivered safely.'Zhurmat and his fearsome mount - the horrible two-headed troll Groz-and-Ulk - have begun to amass forces for use against the Gabil'akkâ in the valley below. Óli has asked for your assistance in routing the forces outside Bagûd-mekhem, the Gate of Wind.Óli has asked for your assistance in retaking Bagûd-mekhem.Speak with ÓliSecure the eastern and western gate controlsDefeat Azbauz and MaugrushDefeat ShatarkhaDefeat Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk and secure the Gate of WindsDefeat Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk'Recently there has a been a good deal of activity just North of this position. We have had reports of troops gathering near a little known entrance called Bagûd-mekhem, the Gate of Wind. These troops are being led by a goblin war-drummer known as Zhurmat with his fearsome mount: a horrible two-headed troll named Groz-and-Ulk. We fear that if this force pushes southward, it could risk the Gabil'akkâ below.

