hrews (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy shrew nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have shoo'd away the shrews and destroyed their nests as Nila Brambleberry requested. You should return to her just outside the cave entrance, south-east of the Staddle village centre.Talk to Nila Brambleberry'These thieving shrews are just the worst! Stealing the food of innocent hobbits! They really shouldn't be allowed to get away with such things! Someone should do something about it. 

'Though... I couldn't bear it if you stomped on them or something horrible like that. They're kind of cute, in their own way, don't you think? If you're going in there, just... shoo them away or something. Destroy their nests, and surely they will move on and go somewhere else.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Did you kindly shoo them away? Yes? And destroyed their nests as well? Excellent! I think they will have learned their lesson!'The Temámir of Jiret-menêsh want to know what has caused the dead to rise in the crypts of Gadim-ûn.You have come to the Crypts of Gadim-ûn to search for a sign of what may have caused the dead to rise in An Shêru. You should start by searching to the east.Search to the eastYou have found a corrupted corpse surrounded by a green radiance and the sound of a tormented voice. Perhaps you should sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.Soothe the anguished deadAfter finding a corrupted corpse, you were able to dispel the foul voice in the air with a lighthearted song. You should continue east and search the crypts for anything else notable.Search for another clue further eastYou have found another corrupted corpse. You should sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers, as you did last time.Soothe the anguished deadAfter finding two corrupted corpses, you were able to dispel the foul voice in the air with a lighthearted song. You should travel south and continue searching the crypts.Search for another sign to the southYou have discovered a third corrupted corpse. You should again sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.Soothe the anguished deadYou have now found three corrupted corpses, each surrounded by a green radiance and the sound of a tormented voice. Each time, you were able to dispel the foul voice with a lighthearted song. You should travel west and continue searching the crypts.Search for another clue to the westYou have found yet another corrupted corpse. You should again sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.Soothe the anguished dead'Fear not, ${PLAYER}, I am here to help! The mission is complete? Oh well, let 