<rgb=#00ff00> Speak with Cinaid again to claim your Supreme Bundle Rewards.</rgb>'Very well, use these well and prove your value to the army.'The workers at the quarry in Scary have broken into a hidden chamber containing a nest of spiders, and the creatures have now overrun the whole quarry.The spiders can be found all throughout the quarry and at the cave they swarmed from, cut into the cliff-face by Scary.Defeat Greenfields biters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Greenfields tree-weavers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated most, if not all, of the spiders in the quarry, but the most important spider to dispose of yet remains. You should find and defeat the Greenfields Queen.Defeat the Greenfields Queen'Thank you, ${PLAYER}! The spiders are showing no sign of leaving, but your efforts in the quarry surely won't hurt either!

'Still, I wonder if I should move to Budgeford? I've always gotten along well with the Bolgers... better than I have with spiders, at any rate!'Though there is nothing Constable Tanglerush can do personally to help the hobbits of Staddle with their current problem, she feels for them and has offered you a reward for helping them in her stead.Constable Tanglerush suggests talking to some of the hobbits around Staddle and seeing if there is anything you can do to help them with their current woes.Complete Quest: Shooing ShrewsComplete Quest: Saving the ApplesComplete Quest: Rescuing the VegetablesComplete Quest: Lost HobbitsComplete Quest: Vanished ValuablesComplete Quest: Kick Out the Cave-clawsYou have done what you can to help the hobbits of Staddle. You should return to Constable Tanglerush for the reward she promised.Talk to Constable Tanglerush in Staddle'I am not permitted to help the folk here with their rodent problem, but I still hate to see them all so upset.

'If you want to help them, you should talk to some of the hobbits around the village and see what can be done. I would be grateful if you did. If you manage to help them, return to me when you are done, and I will give you what reward I am able.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'So the hobbit-folk feel the day has been saved? Thank you so much for bringing them some relief. Here is a reward, as promised.

'Come back tomorrow, if you are able, as it seems likely that the raiders will return, at least during the harvest season.'Humbert Thornburrow has come from Staddle in search of stout-hearted individuals to help his village in their time of need.Humbert claims that Staddle is under attack and has asked you to go there and help the village. You should go there and ask one of the constables what is going on. Staddle is in Bree-land, just south-east of Bree-town.Talk to Constable Tanglerush in Staddle'Oh dear me, I'm having such trouble finding enough folk willing to help!'

The hobbit wrings his hands and is clearly in distress.

'My apologies, I should introduce myself. I am Humbert Thornburrow, and I've travelled here all the way from Staddle, searching for someone to aid us! We are under attack! Our food stores are almost empty, and if something isn't done soon, Staddle is done for!

'You look like the heroical sort. Would you be willing to travel there and help us? Staddle is just south-east of Bree-town. Hurry, before it's too late!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Under attack!? Does Staddle look under attack to you? It is certainly not, and if it were, the watchers and constables would handle the matter.

'Though... I must say the hobbits here are in quite a fuss. Apparently, some shrews got into their pantries and robbed them blind. Some are also saying they're missing personal items, but why would shrews take something they can't eat?

'Anyway, they have been asking us to do something about it, but my superiors maintain that pest control is not our duty.'Recover the weapons and supplies taken from the Rangers of Evendim by the Angmarim.Enter the tomb and find the stolen Ranger supplies carried and guarded by the Angmarim.Collect stolen axes from the Angmarim (${NUMBER}/8)Collect stolen swords from the Angmarim (${NUMBER}/8)Collect stolen supplies (${NUMBER}/6)Return to the tomb entrance and speak with the scout.Return to the entrance to find the scout'Let us return to the Rangers.'Collect samples of harathar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Hail, wanderer! I did not expect to see travellers so deep into the wastes, but I am pleased to meet you all the same. I thought myself alone with those creeping desert-wights skulking about. I am a mason by trade, you see, and am struggling to reach a most particular group of harathar, as the wights keep blocking my path. I feel at my wit's end. Might you be willing to procure several samples of the stone?''If you are wondering what harathar looks like, it is a gleaming, smooth stone of a bright green-blue hue. Most striking, and it stands out on the landscape of the sun-baked Khûd. The wights seem drawn to it, but to what end, I have yet to divine.''What flawless harathar you have chipped for me! You have an eye for quality. My current apprentice could not have sourced half as impressive a sampling as you. I would ask if you wished to replace him, but you seem the adventuring sort; thus I will simply thank you.'Brigand apothecaries are converting poison from usan-kûni. You need to destroy their workstations and defeat the apothecaries and their leader.Your mission is to travel to Zikrum-dûl to defeat the apothecaries and their leader, as well as destroy their workstations.Defeat Urâshi apothecaries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy apothecary supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat Samûku in Zikrum-dûl.Find and defeat Samûku'Good job defeating the apothecaries and stopping their production of poisons! Let us return to Ub Nishir.'The man begins to weave his tale and you listen so that in his final moments he will not be alone.Speak with the stowaway and listen well to his tale. This is the beginning of his life at sea.Complete the mission: Call of the SeaSpeak with the stowaway and allow him to finish recounting the events of that night long ago.'It is kind of you to stay. I shall do my best to be brief, out of necessity and thoughtfulness. Yet, I must start at the beginning for my tale to make sense.

'I spent my earliest years in Lossarnach, along the Erui. That stretch of river led to the mighty Anduin and it was there, at the river's edge, that my love of water grew. My dearest friend and I set out to seek a life as merchants, heading south along the Anduin towards Pelargir. Life has a way of twisting your desires and we soon found ourselves labourers and dockhands.

'It was there that I met the Captain.'

He stares longingly at the water.

'It is there my life changed.''It was in a small tavern...''When morning came, I stood in front of the Captain and pledged an oath to serve Gondor and the Steward Denethor who sat in our King's stead.'

He manages a smile remembering this long distant honour.

'I left my life on the land with nothing but my haversack, the clothes on my back, and a sword worn thin from being sharpened too many times over.'The stowaway's tale continues with details of his first tour.The mariner's tale continues with details of an assault on the river-port town of Pelargir.Complete the mission: Attack on PelargirThe mariner wishes to speak with you to provide the conclusion to this chapter.'It was on my first tour, at Pelargir, that we met Yarikh for the first time.

'Our ship was moored at the dockyard, after a short trip into the Bay of Belfalas. While we supped at the barracks the Corsair's ship crept up the river and dropped their raiders in the western part of the city.

'They intended to capture and enslave the populace. They did not expect to encounter us. Being defenders of Gondor, we pressed ourselves into action.''The harbour at...''In that battle against Yarikh, we knew that we would lose.'

He shakes his head, as if still in disbelief.

'I am still unsure why they fled that night. Yet, they did, and that spurred the captain to scour the seas for years to come.'Falnavar wishes to tell you of the events that helped to map the course of his life.The mariner's tale is to continue as he reminisces about the attack on the Corsairs they found at the shores of Tolfalas.Complete Mission: The Tolfalas ShoreKnowing now how the battle on the shore transpired, you should speak with the mariner.'Our patrols on the water took us west into the Bay of Belfalas. Sometimes into the Great Sea. We never ventured far enough south to threaten Umbar, but the Corsairs from the south would trespass into Gondorian water often.'

He stares beyond you to the sky.

'Once we spied a ship moored off the coast of Tolfalas with its sails drawn down. We recognized it at once as Yarikh's ship. Our captain set us to task as we made our way to intercept the Corsair crew on the island....''We thought we had them; we did. But the cunning Corsairs used weapons we had ne'er seen to shatter the shore and cover their escape in our longboats.'

A dark look spreads across Falnavar's face.

'The Captain was vexed and vowed to bring the Corsair marauder to justice.''We cornered them....'There is more to Falnavar's tale and he would like to share it with you. He speaks fondly of his past.There is more still to the mariner's tale. He bids you listen to the story of how he and the captain became fast friends.Complete Mission: My Bosom FriendAfter hearing how the captain and the mariner grew close it is time to speak with the mariner once again.'Our time ashore, always brief, allowed for little adventure. I did not desire adventure in those days; only camaraderie. The Captain - who had taken a liking to me only a few years ago in a tavern - and I became dearest friends….''Our future was not set, but I knew I had earned the respect of a man whom I greatly respected. When we set back to sail, I was named his second.''It was a cool night...'A turn in the events of their lives, the Captain and Falnavar face long odds against Yarikh and his crew.There is something more to the mariner's tale as his countenance falls grim.Complete Mission: The NenglorYou know the fate of that night and the incident that befell the captain and the mariner. Return to the mariner to hear more.'It was on a routine patrol at the tip of Andrast where we next encountered Yarikh and his ship again, anchored, with a launch of smaller boats along the shore. He had captured villagers in an earlier raid and we were to free the prisoners.

'The Captain devised a plan to keep our men aboard our vessel to attack the Corsair ship while we made our way to the shore to deal with the captain and crew.'

He sighs.

'If only we had known....''We saved the prisoners and dispatched the enemy on the shore. But the crew Yarikh left ashore was no true fighting force. They were a decoy; a trap set by Yarikh. We had fallen into the trap and our ship, Nenglor, and all her crew was the price we paid for our hubris.''We set our launches in the sea...'Falnavar and the captain make a trek back to Pelargir after losing their ship, but not all is well when they arrive.After a harsh reprimand for the loss of their ship, the captain set about building the Nenglor anew.Complete Mission: The Nenglor RebornWith the Nenglor rebuilt, the mariner's tale seems to be taking a different turn.'Bound to land, we started our journey back toward Anfalas to report. Those we rescued were burdensome, but duty bound us to protect them, and so we did. The wilder lands of Anfalas proved a challenge, but we made our way to the nearest port and reported in to the authorities.

'We received a reprimand and were forced to return to Pelargir to aid in the construction of our new ship.''We set sail only a few months after being shore-bound. I noticed it then, a change in the captain.''We set about rebuilding...'Falnavar recognizes that the change in the Captain is greater than he anticipated, and the crew is now in danger.Listen to the tale that the mariner tells, something clearly went amiss after the Nenglor was rebuilt.Complete Mission: The SermonThe captain seemed to become unhinged, in a fashion. Return to the mariner now and hear their thoughts.'Back on the sea we set sail south. To my protestation, the Captain pressed us beyond South Gondor. When we crossed past the River Harnen, we spoke in private about his intent….''I feared for my friend. I feared for our crew. More, I feared for the safety of our land if the Captain's obsession continued. If that storm had not blown in and damaged our sails... we would have started a war.''We were in strange waters...'Falnavar recalls the events after the near crossing into Umbar's waters and what harsh punishment was levied against the captain.Anger in his voice, the mariner continue his tale. Listen further.Complete Mission: To Plot RevengeYou understand the intent now of the raid, and the mariner will continue his tale.'After five years of service to the land of Gondor, my time at sea was at an end, so too The Captain's. It were not because I wanted to give up the sea. Stripped of our commission for violation of orders and resigned to a miserable life on the land.

'A crew-member spoke with other vessels and informed them of our near approach to Umbar. Villains.'

The man draws in a laboured breath.

'After that, I was lost.'

A wry smile spread on his face.

'Until, I met the captain again a few years later. Back in Pelargir; at an inn. I worked there on the docks and he said he had come looking for me.

'He told me he'd discovered the whereabouts of a Corsair ship's treasure in the hills nearby. He asked me to join him in raiding the hideout to claim the treasure.''The Captain and I returned to Pelargir with enough coin to retire, comfortably, anywhere we wanted. But something greater drove him than the desire for the coin. As we sat in the tavern he confided his new desire; to sail after Yarikh and his crew. To bring them to justice on our terms.''We set out for...'Falnavar's tale takes a different turn as he describes the pursuit of Yarikh, Hilâma, and Akhât, the Corsairs who had ruined their noble life at sea.The tale continues with the pursuit of the Corsair seemingly drawing to an end.Complete Mission: MarkedTragedy befell the mariner, but the tale feels strange, something in the telling is... inconsistent.'A new ship!

'The treasure-hunting provided enough for a ship and a crew. We sailed from Pelargir and caught sight of Yarikh entering Belegaer.

'We pursued him west, until a squall blew both our vessels back toward us, Andrast, and the place where our fates had changed.'

An excited look of wonder glints in his eye.

'Our ships collided, and our battle was fierce. Fire burned the ships to ash beneath our feet and we fell into the unforgiving sea only to wash ashore near the place where we had freed the prisoners but lost our first ship years earlier. This time... was... different....''The captain died there on the shores of the Bay of Belfalas.

'The captain, my captain, my friend. The water did not claim him as he hoped.'

He shakes his head forlornly.

'It was a blade of the enemy he pursued for years, an obsession that cost him his life and me… it nearly cost me my sanity.''We had them cornered and surprised...'Falnavar's tales shifts again, this time to the years after the defeat of the Corsair crew who brought an end to the Captain.A slip of the tongue? It is unclear, but the mariner's tale continues on.Complete Mission: The BeastThe beast is defeated, but a mystery is revealed. Return to the mariner and tell him what you discovered.'He -- The Captain gave me gifts; precious to me. I kept them with me at all times since his death, now, here at my own - I seem to have lost them. Do you have the heart to find them? To find what I have lost? So that I might have them in my death where the water has claimed me and not a tyrant's blade?''It cannot be. I saw him slain with my own eyes and now...

'My friend, I have failed you. We can no longer fight. Look at us.''The beast is near here. Go now.'Falnavar's state is deteriorating and his last wish is that you take the vengeance that he can no longer claim.The last request? Perhaps. Speak with the mariner to go to the place where Yarikh is, and defeat the Corsair villain, once and for all.Complete Mission: A Final VengeanceReturn to the mariner and speak with him to inform him that the deed is complete.Speak with FalnavarFalnavar's death is tragic, but there is a final note that he provided you.Read the note you collected from Falnavar'Go...

'Find that cur, Yarikh and put a final end to the misery he has caused. See him pay for the--'

He coughs madly, winces, and regains himself.

'Make him pay for the pain he wrought upon my brethren... my crews... my people.

'Fulfil this wish; the final wish of a dying man.'Falnavar is gone.

In his hand, he holds a crumpled note written on the back of the old recruitment poster.To you, who listened to my tale, I give you my haversack; provided that you retrieved it from Yarikh and his crew.

As you likely now know, I am the Captain in my tale. My obsessions led me here - not the call of water. I came to avenge the death of the boy I recruited and befriended and loved as a son. The horror and pain of his loss and the death of my crews is ended.

You have given peace and a final kindness to one who likely did not deserve such.

I go to my final rest with a mind at ease; a desire fulfilled, the scent of salt in my nose, and the sound of the babbling river to send me to my dreams.

Thank you, stranger.

Falnavar'Go now and find Yarikh. Bring me the haversack he stole.'Captain Aranhir's directions led you to search for goods lost in his wreck. What you did not expect to find was a wounded man along the shores of the great river. The man has a tale to tell.The old man is injured gravely and it seems that there is no hope to close his wounds. His request is simple, stay and listen to his tale so that he is not forgotten. Will you see this through?Speak with the manFalnavar paused, but it seems there is more he has to say. Ask him to continue.Speak with FalnavarFalnavar paused again. Perhaps you should see if there is more that he wishes to tell you.Speak with FalnavarContinue listening to Falnavar's tale.Continue speaking with Falnavar'Hoi there, friend,' the man winces as he speaks. 'I should have known better; and not done what I done.'

He manages a weak smile through the pain.

'Alas, the call of the waves and the way of water made me a fool, it seems, for the last time.'

He coughs.

'Could you... spare a moment for a stranger... to hear the tale of his life... so that someone might know of me and so I may not just end up as some corpse washed ashore the mighty Brandywine?''Call me Falnavar. In my youth, long ago now, I had no love for land or leisure.

'I was a tough and brutish lad who spent more time with ruffians than I ought. Minas Tirith, while only a league or so away from my home in Lossarnach, was a place of waste in my eyes.

'The steward saw fit to keep up his city while the outer lands fell to ruin and despair. There was no escape for a boy like myself that was not on the water.'

He looks to the river nearby.'Apologies.'

He coughs hard, clearing his throat.

'I was always taken by the flow of water and the River Erui provided me the only measure of joy I knew in my youth. My friends and I would build rafts from driftwood or barrels, and tumbled down the waters toward the mighty Anduin.

'It was harmless fun. We would make a trip, steal a ride on a cart heading back toward Lossarnach, or just steal a horse outright and sell it to the farrier who would sell it again.

'A scoundrel, I was, in with a crowd of others with like-minds and desires: to leave the land and sail the sea beneath the stars above.''Yes, yes... I'm seeing it all so clearly now. I do not want to miss a thing.'

He closes his eyes a moment and then speaks hoarsely.

'Near my fifteenth summer I decided that I would travel away from Lossarnach. My mother and father protested. They desired I remain in our hovel tilling soil for the magistrates who ran our village from afar.

'I did not care for the nobles. What had they offered me and mine? But, the people! The people who grew crops, made swords, and kept the promise of tomorrow alive. I cared for them.

'"A paradox of beliefs," my father would say.''I left my hamlet and found another, not far to the south where I worked under the employ of a farrier, a smith, a tailor... I was searching for my place; you see?

'I did not find it while tending fields, or hammering iron. I did not find it in careful study, or stitching cloth. It was only when I looked heavenward, toward the stars and heard the waters that my heart sang and was free.

'There is a tale of sailors long ago who settled the lands of Gondor. I know little of the truth to those tales, but I know that I was born with a sailor's heart.

'And that is where my tale truly begins.'Aid the Earth-kin by collecting samples from the cave-claws and defeating the monstrous beast that now lives among them.Collect samples of corrupt flesh from the cave-claws and defeat the monstrous beast that now dwells among them.Collect samples of corrupted flesh from cave-claws (${NUMBER}/12)Destroy the behemoth cave-clawReturn to the camp entrance to find the scout.Return to camp entrance to find the scout'Let us return to the Earth-kin at Ram Dúath.'Your mission is to cause a disturbance in a cave that is known for its spiders, but is now being occupied by Ekhamâti soldiers. Extinguish the soldiers' fires and sound their alarms to bring the spiders down on them.Your mission is to cause a disturbance in a cave that is known for its spiders, but is now being occupied by Ekhamâti soldiers. Extinguish the soldiers' fires and sound their alarms to bring the spiders down on them.Sound alarms at camps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Extinguish braziers at camps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have brought the spiders down on the soldiers. Escape before the reinforcements arrive!Escape the cave before reinforcements arrive!Sabragêsh is blocking your escape! Defeat her before reinforcements arrive.Defeat Sabragêsh'Quickly! We must return to Iridír before reinforcements arrive. You have done well here.'This quest rewards you for your purchase of the Enhanced Rivendell Supporter Pack.Enjoy your reward for being a supporter.Obtain the supporter pack bestowal objectAs a supporter, you are to receive a reward for your contribution. By accepting this quest, you will receive an amount of LotRO Points commensurate with your purchase.This quest rewards you for your purchase of the Luxuriant Rivendell Supporter Pack.Enjoy your reward for being a supporter.Obtain the supporter pack bestowal objectAs a supporter, you are to receive a reward for your contribution. By accepting this quest, you will receive an amount of LotRO Points commensurate with your purchase.This quest rewards you for your purchase of the Simple Rivendell Supporter Pack.Enjoy your reward for being a supporter.Obtain the supporter pack bestowal objectAs a supporter, you are to receive a reward for your contribution. By accepting this quest, you will receive an amount of LotRO Points commensurate with your purchase.The Trakrîp clan offers warriors devoted to its cause strength of arms and increased damage. Accepting their blessing will make you into a power bruiser. Speak with their emissary to gain the Blessing of the Tarkrîp.You may seek the blessing of the Tarkrîp clan. All you need do is renounce all other clans.Speak with the Tarkrîp emissary'You tire of servitude without strength. You see now the error of your choice. It is only with the Tarkrîp that a promise of belly full of man-flesh can be achieved. Join with us. Accept our blessing and fight without equal.''You have chosen well. 

