You should run to the chicken farm and return with a basket of fresh eggs before the time runs out.Collect the basket of eggs (eat pie for a burst of energy)Sperling Took, the supplier of the Farmers Faire, can be found in Bywater.

You should return to Bywater as quickly as you can, taking bites of the pie to help you along if you find yourself needing a burst of energy.'Oh dear, oh dear...! No more eggs? Can this be? Quickly, ${PLAYER} -- head to Sandson's Farm to find another basket for the market and bring it back as quickly as you can.

'Here...take this pie. It uses my great grand-mother's secret recipe, and it is said to lend you incredible speed when you take a bite of it. Hurry now. Do not tarry!''Hurry, ${PLAYER}! This is not the time to dilly-dally so!''Hurray, ${PLAYER}! You are the hero of the Farmers Faire!'The robbers in Kidu-bâla have stolen many valuables from the Beltáni and other travellers. The valuables should be reclaimed and returned to their rightful owners.Locate the whereabouts of the treasure that has been stashed within this cavern.Locate the double-locked chestGather keys spread throughout the cavern.Gather keys for double-locked chest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to the double-locked chest.Return to the double-locked chestSurvive the ambush in the cavernDefeat the ambushDefeat Ruhíshi the BounteousDefeat Ruhíshi the BounteousWith the ambush defeated, unlock the double-locked chest and gather the goods.Unlock the double-locked chest and gather the goods'With the goods reclaimed and returned to their rightful owners, our people shall be safe. Thank you.'Make your way through the cave and defeat all of the goblins you find.Make your way through the cave and defeat all of the goblins that you find.Defeat goblins in the cave (${NUMBER}/24)Find the scout at the entrance of the goblin's cave.Find the scout at the entrance to the cave'Let us return to Tuckborough.'A posting from Everard Holebourne of Overhill asks for assistance with making deliveries to the inns around The Shire.Make your way to Overhill and seek out Everard Holebourne.Speak with Everard Holebourne at OverhillFind the cart accident north-east of Overhill and collect the Blagrove's Brown keg and deliver it to the Bird and Baby Inn, or Collect the Toad's Tongue keg and deliver it to the Floating Log Inn, or collect the Green Dragon's Breath Ale keg and deliver it to The Green Dragon Inn, or collect the Old Withywindle keg and deliver it to the Golden Perch Inn.Collect and deliver Blagrove's Brown to the Bird and Baby InnCollect the Toad's Tongue Ale and deliver it to The Floating Log InnCollect and deliver the keg of Green Dragon's Breath Ale to the The Green Dragon InnCollect and deliver the keg of Old Withywindle to the Golden Perch InnWith all the deliveries completed, return to Everard Holebourne at Overhill and give him the splendid news.Return to Everard Holebourne with news of your successPost:

Needed: a person with patience and a sturdy back to help collect and deliver kegs of ale and beer to the inns of The Shire.

- Everard Holebourne'Oh, thank you kindly for answering my call. I am in a most dreadful pickle.

'I was on my way back from Brockenborings when my road was suddenly barred by spiders—great, creeping things, if you can believe it. My poor pony took fright, slipped her harness, and in the commotion all but turned my cart about.

'The fright of it drove the spiders off for a time, but I could do little more than haul the kegs down from the cart before my courage quite failed me. They remain there still, away to the north-east.

'I am sorely in need of a stout-hearted soul to gather up those kegs and see my deliveries completed.

'Each one is plainly marked and must be delivered with all due haste, if you would be so kind.''You truly pulled my toes from the flames, friend, and I am most grateful to you for it.

'I only hope the spiders will have the good sense to remain in the woods where they belong, henceforth. My poor pony shall be sore for a week, I fear, after all the exertion she has put forth.

'And, that is saying nothing of the state of my cart!

'Still, my chief trouble is put right for the moment, and that is thanks entirely to you. I shall not soon forget your kindness.'The War-tyrant seems displeased that emissaries from Carn Dûm arrived and made their way into the war tent. His demeanour is more grim than usual, and he has instructed you to make your way to the Angmarim sorceress who now resides in the tent at the within the confines of Gramsfoot.War-tyrant Akúlhun directed you to the war tent to speak with an Angmarim sorceress there named Malavin. Apparently she is here to assist, inspect, or guide the war effort. Whatever her purpose, it does not sit well with the War-tyrant.Malavin instructed you to speak to each of the emissaries representing the clans of Carn Dûm and beyond. They have blessings that they will seek to bestow upon you, provided you will serve in their name.Speak with the emissariesHaving spoken to all the emissaries it is time to return to Malavin for further instruction.'Listen here. A sorceress come from the north to tell me how the fight goes. Oh, she has the ear of the steward, but the arms are here, in the Ettenmoors. We've been fighting while they've been locked away in castles and steel barricades. What do they know about battling these people?'

It is a question expecting no answer.

'Bah... leadership back in Carn Dûm is looking for a new way to off these pesky Free Folk. So we got some new tricks available, meat. Each clan, and even the dirty dogs and sticky little spiders got their own emissaries here to help you new gits out. Oh and those southron Uruks too... talk to one of them and they'll give you a taste of what the leaders are thinking... don't get used to it though, maggot. These truces can only last so long....

'But first, they want me to send every maggot with snot dripping on their face up the hill to talk with her. Well... so be it. Better you go talk to her than me. She calls herself, Malavin.'

There is a short pause.

'If you get a chance, accidentally spit on her for me, would you?''Orders is orders. You need to talk to the Priestess first.''Talk with the skinny witch, then you can talk to me.''Abide by the council's will and speak with Malavin.''Seek she who speaks for the lord of Carn Dûm. Our brood will wait our turn.''Sharkey's orders are clear, we let the woman speak... for now.''Far be it from the Krahjarn to deny protocol. What, you think we're all war hungry tyrants like Akúlhun?'

He smirks.

'We are... some of us just hide it better. Talk with Malavin. That is the command. We will abide.''The pack is eager to hunt. The human is a barrier to our victory. Speak with her quick and then return to me.''Another veteran of the way? Or are you a new recruit? Honestly, I cannot tell the difference between a seasoned warrior and a whelp fresh from the pens or egg. I do, however know a thing or two about obedience and seeing that orders are carried out.'

She smirks wryly.

'Mordirith is displeased with the efforts here and organized an effort to entice you... warriors... with gifts. Each of the Orc clans, the Scara-pack, and Brood of Shelob send emissaries to entreat. He even allowed the White Hand at this table. Perhaps, in time there will be more. For now, it is these few.'

She pauses a moment to look you over.

'It appears that the steward of Carn Dûm is correct in his assessment. You are all in dire need of help. I invite you then to speak with the emissaries here in Gramsfoot. Learn what they offer you and choose their blessing. Each has been ordered, for now, to entreat with all of you. Provide for your until the council of our lord is complete.

'Run along now, and learn from each of the emissaries here and then return to me.''Off with you until you have spoken to each of the emissaries. Return to me when you are done. I shall instruct you further.''I am Fathrug, and you look like you are ready to tear the flesh off a man. That is all we ask. Find the Men. Flay the Men. Leave their carcasses littering the earth to turn the grass bloody. The Tarkrîp clan will strengthen your skills, help you stay in the fight longer. You'll be rather brutal about your business of hacking and rending the enemy, and while we won't teach you how to dodge a really nasty sword blow, we'll teach you to shrug it off and keep going.

'The Tarkrîp clan prizes scrappy warriors above all else, willing to strike at the enemy relentlessly!''You look soft, maggot. I should know the Ongbúrz are the heartiest clan in all of Angmar. We are not afraid of battle. We thrive in it. We revel in the clash of hammers, axes, and all the tools those bearded bastards bring against us. We know little fear. Our prowess is in our staying power.

'If you want to swing your blade wildly without thought about tomorrow, go talk with the Tarkrîp or the dogs. If you want to stand tall above all the others then take our blessing into battle. Toughness like ours should never be underestimated.''Come closer. Smell that? Mushrooms. Slime. Herbs. Poultices. The trappings of healers. Oh, yes, the other clans will tell you that they are the most stalwart, or furious, or violent, or sinister, but we are the force that keeps them standing. We are the strength behind them all.'

He chuckles.

'Half the pain that they don't feel is because of our stinking sludges and fungal brews. We know how to pound a spike into a missing arm if things go terribly ill, too. Sometimes the victim even survives long enough to make it more permanent.

'The others will tell you tales, but it is we that let them keep tongues wagging. Without us, they'd all be face down in the dirt. Stand with us. Stand with the Blogmal Clan.''She is born of the first enemy of Elves. She feeds her brood well and gives them all they need to spread the faith of the Dark Lord. Gifts that sting deeply, secretly, and brutally. Her poison courses to seep into the flesh and twist it to the darkness where she dwells.'

The queen chitters.

'She burns the victims from within so they sting, sting, sting, longer and more painfully. She is the corruption that seeds the earth with malicious intent. She is mother to her brood. Join with her and earn the gift to inflict suffering most profound.''Sharkey orders us north to help fight. So we come. We see why these clans fail. Too unbalanced. Too dedicated to destruction, or defence. Too dedicated to mysticism or the darkness.'

He shakes his head.

'No temperance leads to a quick end. Learning the field of battle. Discerning the weakness and strengths of your enemy provides a clearer path to victory. It is an even path we walk. It is the teaching of our master that we prize. The method to strike hard. The method to stand tall. The method to withstand a strike and turn a blade.

'I would lead the White Hand against any of these other clans and leave them in shambles. Join us and you will see what I mean.''The Krahjarn are born to lead. We remember the wars against the first. We recall the first lash against our backs and how to revisit that on our lessers. We know what it means to lead. To oversee the battle. To watch the flow of a fight. When to inspire and when to instill fear.'

He snarls.

'We know what makes a maggot a maggot and how to make a whelp a warrior. Stand alongside us, whelp and we'll make you a warrior yet.''The Scara know the hunt. The strength of sudden strike. The panic you instill from the shadow and tastiest, easiest places to tear flesh from bone. We teach the pack the way and it is for the warg or any to do the rest.'

He shakes his fur.

'We heed only brutality and cruelty to bring down our targets quickly and as painfully as possible. Our pack can teach you, but you must do the rest. We waste time by standing still. Choose us and run free.''Well done, I am amazed you had the attention span necessary to speak with them all. There may be hope for you yet. Now to the matter at hand. Choose. Choose a clan to represent while you fight for Angmar.

'All will welcome you. Freely shirk your allegiance like you have done your duty for so long. Drink of their blessing until you find a home that is welcoming to you. They are ordered to show no malice toward each other for now. This truce may not hold forever.

'Mordirith wants to see these Free Folk brought low. So the clans were convened to find the strongest among you in order to determine the best way to eliminate the forces here. Align yourself. That is all you need do.'

She smiles deviously.

'And when you tire of their boon, simply visit another to take their blessing in the first's stead. For the moment, it is simple. It shall not be forever. So do your best to prove to the master what clans should remain here in the Ettenmoors fighting and slaughtering the Free Folk.'Having met the emissaries of the clans, you must now make a decision. What clan shall you represent in the conflict of the Ettenmoors?The time has come to choose your clan allegiance. All you need do is speak with one of the emissaries and choose to represent them on the field of battle.Choose a clan and receive their blessingWith your choice of clan made, you should return to the emissary, Malavan and speak with her.'This choice is an important one, for certain. But as the master has deemed, you can freely choose what clan you shall represent in the battle for a time.

'You should feel free to approach whichever tribe you choose without fear that you must always represent that clan. No, little worm, you can freely change your allegiances the same as you choose your diet for a day.'

She offers you a weak smile.

'Simply choose an emissary and accept their blessing. If you decide later that you dislike the benefits that their clan provides I am certain that they will abide by the master's law and allow you to freely choose your clan affiliation for now.

'Was that word too big for you? You seem to be staring at me more slack-jawed than usual. Perhaps, you should go make your choice.''I do not care for the choice you made, only that you made one.'Destroy the manacles and burn the dead.Delve into the waterfall prison, destroy any manacles you find, and burn the dead.Destroy iron manacles (${NUMBER}/8)Burn the unfortunate provisionerBurn the unfortunate warriorBurn the unfortunate archerReturn to the entrance of the cavern to find the scout.Return to the entrance and find the scout'Let us return to Fordirith.'A group of day travellers has disappeared near Zahûmakh and haven't been seen in several days. Explore Zahûmakh and look for signs of the travellers.Investigate Zahûmakh for signs of the travellers.Investigate the marsh of Zahûmakh for signs of the travellersAid the travellers, grab their packs, and fight off any marsh-striders who get in your way.Aid wounded travellers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Recover traveller's packs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat marsh-striders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Make your way out of Zahûmakh.Make your way out of ZahûmakhDefeat Luhum-gêna, queen of the marsh.'The travellers have all made it to safety. That was quick work you made of those marsh-striders! Come, let's get you back to Urmâkh and out of this damp.'Fredegunda Cutt has discovered that many hobbits throughout the village have had items stolen from them.Fredegunda believes cave-claw burglars have stolen each of the missing items and maintains that the items could all be found inside the tunnel to the south-east of the village centre.Find Ponto Underhill's shovelFind Sarabeth Lowbanks's bookFind Ferdibrand Took's pipeFind Ethelinda Burr's teapotFind Ferumbras Attereeve's lucky tankardFind Pell Stoneleaf's whittling knifeInside the tunnel, you have found each of the items Fredegunda Cutt believed you would. You should return each of the items to their owners in the village of Staddle.You have returned the stolen items to their respective owners. You should return to Fredegunda Cutt in Staddle and tell her what happened.Talk to Fredegunda Cutt'Listen here, I have heard that someone has stolen Ferdibrand Took's pipe, and old Ethelinda Burr's teapot has gone missing. How do you lose a whole teapot? While I was trying to listen in on Ethelinda, I heard Sarabeth Lowbanks say she couldn't find her book! Also, I was having a chat with Himloc Grouse, and he said Ferumbras Attereeve's favourite tankard has gone missing.

'Now I know what you're going to say, "Never trust a Grouse!" but I believe he spoke true. And then, as if that isn't enough, I was doing a little shopping at Staddle Arms, just browsing, you know, and I heard Pell Stoneleaf say that his favourite whittling knife has disappeared. Whittling knives don't just grow legs and walk away, as they say.

'And on top of everything else, Gammy Boggs, who is very reliable, I must say, told me that Ponto Underhill can't get his work done because he says his shovel was stolen! She, of course, thinks it's quite possible he is just saying that so he can take a break and go fishing, but I think it was stolen indeed. I mean, look at all the other things that have been stolen.

'Now, I don't know if you are acquainted with old Maginard Foxbolt, but he says he has seen cave-claws roaming about at night. Cave-claws, if you can believe it! Well, I told him, mark my words, those cave-claws are burglars, without any doubt.

'I warrant that if you went into that queer tunnel, you would find all of these missing items along with a company of cave-claw burglars!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Humph! I told everyone so. I knew all along, of course, that my deduction was correct. Now good day to you, I must be off. I heard that Longo Daegmund is having trouble at home and mean to learn what happened.''Dear me, you've found my shovel! I'll... I'll go fishing later. Thank you for returning this.''You've found my book! Wonderful, now I can get back to work. Thank you! Now, where did I leave my auger?''My pipe! Bless me, thank you! I have others mind you, but this one smokes the best. You have my thanks, friend!''My teapot! And not a chip on it. Such a very fine teapot it is. Thank you for returning it.''My precious tankard! Ah, look at how she shines. And how very much beer she holds. Many thanks, friend!''Hooray! My jolly old whittling knife! Where did you find it? Stolen by cave-claws you say? How did they not cut themselves? I keep this knife razor sharp. How odd!'The Temámir of Jiret-menêsh want to know if any relics of Lâkindar of old remain within the Quelling-house.You have come to Lâkindar in search of relics from the mine's once-glorious past. The search would be easier if there were fewer wights about.Defeat Dwarf-wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect relics of Lâkindar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected what relics you could find in Lâkindar and spotted something strange. You should look into it.Investigate the room at the end of the hallYou have collected what relics you could find in Lâkindar and have spotted a strange stone tomb. You should examine it.Examine the tombAfter collecting what relics you could find in Lâkindar, you spotted a strange stone tomb and awoke its resident.Defeat the fell Temámir wight'Ah, ${PLAYER}! There you are! 

'I do not like this place. I feel somewhat ill at ease. Thankfully, I have already cleared a path so we can leave with all haste. We must only follow the path you took to get here, and we will be back in Jiret-menêsh before you know it!'The White Hand boasts that they are balanced in their approach to warfare. Serving their master, Sharkey, they claim that they will give you resilience and strength in the wars to come.You may accept the blessing of the White Hand. Renounce the other clans and choose to stand with the White Hand.Speak with the White Hand emissary'Sharkey wants allies who know that there is no winning without balance. You would do well to leave the others behind and join with the White Hand. We shall be the victors in this war and the others will serve us in the end.''We accept your request.

'We offer only what you need to survive. An approach to battle that awards strength of arms and armour. You will receive the benefit of our teaching and our will.'Carolyn Goodnough is pleased that you have come to visit Winter-home. She told you there is fun to be had all throughout Winter-home, even outside of the town.

She recommends you talk to Virgil Greenfield out in the field. He has been building snowmen to fill out the Yule cheer of Winter-home and would love help making more of them.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Virgil Greenfield would like to teach you the simple pleasures of building a snowman.  Speak to him for guidance.'Hello again! I hope you enjoyed that short tour of our fine town and all of the festivities we have to offer this year! We're so happy to have you here, and we're always looking for ways to make our celebration even more exciting.

'Virgil Greenfield is working hard to bring a little more Yule cheer to Winter-home in the form of snowmen. There's certainly enough snow for every one of our patrons, so why don't you take a quick walk out there? You can make your very own snowman, and I'm sure Virgil would love the help!''Hello again, have you talked to Virgil yet?''Ah, hello! The mayor's wife sent you, did she?

'Welcome again to Winter-home, traveller. As you can see, I spend my days here working as an artist of sorts. Too often, people overlook the simple joys of life, such as building a snowman.

'If you'd ever like to try your hand at building your own, I'll be here to guide you. After all, with some help, I'll be able to fill out this field in no time at all!'There is no shortage of adventure out there for a curious and wandering hobbit. What has Bilbo Baggins gotten up to now?Your mission is to find Bilbo Baggins. Speak to Celeblír to begin your search!Complete 'Mission: The Further Adventures of Bilbo Baggins, Chapter 1'Celeblír is west of the Last Homely House, near the Town Crier.Talk to Celeblír<rgb=#00FF00>This Further Adventure begins on January 12, 3019, and after 'Foreword: The Fellowship Departs.'</rgb>

'Might you spare me a moment of your time, ${PLAYER}? It is almost certainly nothing, but I should not care to face the master of the house if it turns out otherwise.

'I understand you know Bilbo Baggins? Yes, the hobbit currently in residence here at the Last Homely House, guest of Lord Elrond and welcomed by all. I had a question for him of great importance, but when I sought for him I could find no sign of him in any of his usual haunts. That is quite unusual.

'Will you accept this mission, then? I need you to find him for me!''No one has seen Bilbo since the morning? I felt certain we would solve the mystery by now, ${PLAYER}, but all we have managed to do is double my worries! Has something happened to him after all?''You will help me search for our missing hobbit? Good, good! Again, I am sure it is nothing. But if it is not nothing...

'Well, if it is not nothing, it is sure to mean trouble.'Lord Elrond has given his sons a secret errand that will take them to Lothlórien. You are to accompany them.Elladan is waiting for you outside of Elrond's Library.Talk to Elladan outside of Elrond's LibraryYou should talk to Elladan outside of Elrond's Library to begin your search of the Bruinen.Complete 'Mission: The Further Adventures of Elladan & Elrohir, Chapter 1'Your search of the Bruinen has taken you to Echad Candelleth.

You should talk to Elrohir.Talk to Elrohir<rgb=#00FF00>This Further Adventure begins on October 3018, before 'Book 4, Chapter 1: Where is the Horse and the Rider?' Be aware that you may find yourself travelling through more dangerous areas of Middle-earth throughout this adventure.</rgb>

'${PLAYER}, I have an undertaking that I believe you would be suited for. Servants of the Enemy, under the guise of riders in black, recently tried to cross the Bruinen. The river's waters swept them away at my command. Perhaps they no longer threaten Imladris, but we cannot be certain.

'Scouts have been sent out to determine whether the Black Riders truly fell at the Ford. My sons will soon set out to do the same, but I have also entrusted them with an errand of their own. I would ask that you travel with them to Lothlórien to meet with their grandmother, Lady Galadriel. Though I cannot fully reveal the purpose of their errand, I trust that the three of you will keep each other safe.

'Elladan waits for you outside. May your search bear fruit.''I'm sure we've kept Elrohir waiting for long enough.''Hail, ${PLAYER}! Elrohir has gone ahead to search the Bruinen, but he wished to pass on his greetings as well.

'We're to travel south to Eregion, then through the Redhorn Pass into Lothlórien. Make any preparations you may require; we have a long trek ahead of us.''I have faith that the waters of the Bruinen dealt the Riders a devastating blow. However, the less certain we are of the Riders' fates, the more worried my heart grows.

'Tracking the movements of the Enemy is of the utmost importance for our errand. After everything that's happened, I find our lack of information unsettling.'There is no shortage of adventure out there for a curious and wandering hobbit. What has Bilbo Baggins gotten up to now?Your mission is to find Bilbo Baggins. Speak to Celeblír to continue the search!Complete 'Mission: The Further Adventures of Bilbo Baggins, Chapter 2'Celeblír is west of the Last Homely House, near the Town Crier.Talk to Celeblír'I am especially worried about something Elrond said to us. You know of the company that departed Imladris on the twenty-fifth of December, as do I. Do you think it possible that Bilbo set out from Imladris in pursuit of them?

'You may know more of their mission than I do, but I know enough to see the danger in it for our dear friend Bilbo! What madness could have compelled him to follow them?

'We must find him before he does something even more foolish!''I hope Bilbo would know better than to hide from the scouts! I have always found him to be most friendly and personable, quick to laugh and eager to smile. He seemed to enjoy the peace and comfort of Imladris, and spent many restful days in quiet conversation with me and the others of the house.

'Why would he leave now?''Scouts of Imladris watch the high moor. It may be one of them has seen Bilbo's passage in pursuit of that secret company. Go, ${PLAYER}, and with haste!'The Great Eagles may have discovered important information for the twins' errand.Elrohir has sighted a Great Eagle flying towards Eregion.

You should talk to Elrohir at Echad Candelleth in the Trollshaws to continue your journey.Complete 'Mission: The Further Adventures of Elladan & Elrohir, Chapter 2'You and the twins have made it to Echad Eregion.

Elladan has something to say to you.Talk to Elladan'Our many questions may be answered soon; I spied one of the Great Eagles flying south-east. Perhaps they bear fresh news.

'We shall set out for Eregion once you're ready.''Watch the skies, ${PLAYER}. I will do the same.''${PLAYER} -- I'm sorry I did not thank you earlier for helping Elrohir at Pembar. I needed time to gather my thoughts.

'When the two of you left, I found myself pacing around out of nervousness. Perhaps it's the gravity of the errand we've been entrusted with. Or does my worry stem from everything else that's happening?

'The forces at play have long since been set in motion. There is much we don't have control over, but I tell myself we are doing what we can. I have to believe that.'There is no shortage of adventure out there for a curious and wandering hobbit. What has Bilbo Baggins gotten up to now?Your mission is to find Bilbo Baggins. Speak to Celeblír to continue the search!Complete 'Mission: The Further Adventures of Bilbo Baggins, Chapter 3'Celeblír is west of the Last Homely House, near the Town Crier.Talk to Celeblír'Canaddal and Ringhul would have seen him if he travelled the High Moor, would they not? Unless...

'I have heard that hobbits can make themselves very difficult to notice when the mood strikes. Indeed, Bilbo himself told me this! What if he strayed from the path in order to avoid the notice of our scouts? Where might he have ended up?''It was good of Arifael to help us, and my mind is put somewhat at ease by the news that Bilbo did not end up in Giant Valley.

'But if not there, then where?''Do you think he might have strayed near Giant Valley? I hope not, but we cannot strike that place from the list of sites to which he might have ventured... not without checking it first!

'It is fortunate for us that we have a friend in that valley, ${PLAYER}.'The mountain's wrath may make the Redhorn Pass the most dangerous leg of your adventure.The twins' chosen route into Lórien crosses through the Redhorn Pass.

You should talk to Elladan at Echad Eregion in Eregion to continue your journey.Complete 'Mission: The Further Adventures of Elladan & Elrohir, Chapter 3'After the unnerving trek through the Redhorn Pass, your party has made it safely to the Dimrill Dale.

You should talk to Elrohir to see how he's doing.Talk to Elrohir'It's best not to tarry here any longer. The Redhorn Pass can be treacherous during the warmest of months, and we are fast approaching winter.

'Be on the look-out for Orcs most of all; they plague the mountain and have waylaid many an unfortunate traveller.''Once you are ready, we shall depart.''${PLAYER}, I am sorry. My desperation for answers clouded my judgement. The Bruinen must have left the Black Riders severely weakened; even if the last horse had survived, it would not have been able to carry its owner far. Perhaps they have vanished from the North, like Elladan said.

'I do not wish to dwell on what happened in the Redhorn Pass but... the cloaked figure eluded you too, didn't it? I suppose we'll never know who or what that truly was. To tell the truth, I am in no rush to find out myself.'There is no shortage of adventure out there for a curious and wandering hobbit. What has Bilbo Baggins gotten up to now?Your mission is to find Bilbo Baggins. Speak to Celeblír to continue the search!Complete 'Mission: The Further Adventures of Bilbo Baggins, Chapter 4'Celeblír is west of the Last Homely House, near the Town Crier.Talk to Celeblír'We have found no sign that Bilbo travelled south. That is a relief, for it appears Elrond's concern may not be warranted. Our hobbit may not have followed in the footsteps of that secret company.

'If he did not travel south... did he journey north?''At last we are making some progress, ${PLAYER}, and may have picked up Bilbo's trail! But where does that trail lead?''I understand a party of dwarves has made camp along the path that winds into the Misty Mountains. Perhaps they caught sight of our missing hobbit?'Though you have almost reached your destination, danger may still lurk nearby.Elrohir is worried about the news Gwaihir brought regarding the wolves along the Anduin.

