<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Blagrove's Brown can be purchased at The Bird and Baby Inn, in Michel Delving.

You should buy some Blagrove's Brown for delivery to Harigar Mudbottom, who waits in Oatbarton.Collect Blagrove's Brown from the Bird and BabyThe Bird and Baby Inn is in Michel Delving. Harigar Mudbottom is in Oatbarton.

Harigar Mudbottom told you of the horror he experienced when he realized he had never had a "Blagrove's Brown" from the Bird and Baby. Since he lied and told others that he had, he has asked you, in the strictest of confidence, to fetch him a mug of the ale so that he can truly say he has had a sip of every ale, wine, and spirit that can be found west of the Misty Mountains.'I have here a list of requests to assist Inn League members in need, stranded away from home without the support of their beer-loving brethren. It seems they miss their favourite drinks, or in some cases they've never even tasted them!

'Here's a funny story, though I'm not supposed to be spreading it around: Harigar Mudbottom, one of our most vocal enthusiasts, hasn't tried Michel Delving's own Blagrove's Brown yet! It is here on my checklist, waiting to be checked, and my checklist is never checked unless a drink is duly drunk!

'You should bring him some of Blagrove's Brown so he can finish up. Oh, and...you don't need to tell him that I told you his whole story.''Another Outsider passing through? Well, usually I don't cotton much to Outsiders, but in this case an Outsider is exactly who I need. Now, what I'm about to tell you cannot be repeated to anyone!

'You see, I've made a bit of a name for myself as being an expert on ales, wines, and the like. And one night, I got to boasting and said there was no need for me to take up the Inn League Challenge, as I'd already drunk every type of spirit that could be found west of the Misty Mountains. Then someone asked if I had drunk a "Blagrove's Brown" from the Bird and Baby, and...and to my horror I realized I never had!

'Can you believe it? Me, living all my life in the Shire, and I had never drunk an ale found right in Michel Delving! What's worse is I lied, aye, I lied and said I had! Now I can't show my face down there and enjoy what might be the finest ale in all the Shire! I can't live like that! Could you fetch me a bit of that ale?''Blagrove's Brown can be found in The Bird and Baby Inn in Michel Delving. I would head that way, if I were you.''What a pickle I am in!''Do you have it? Good! Quick now, no one is looking. Give me that mug. I'll take this back into the house and drink it there.

'My thanks for doing this for me. Now I can hold my head up high and truly say that I've completed the Inn League Challenge. I really drank every spirit there is to be found west of the Misty Mountains!'You have been tasked with delivering unpleasant things to Inn League Members in need of assistance, something only a terrible ${CLASS} would do.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>The Ivy Bush is in Hobbiton in the Shire.

You should speak with the tavern keep at The Ivy Bush and collect some Whitebranch. This will be used as a decoy Blagrove's Brown.Collect fake Blagrove's Brown from The Ivy Bush in HobbitonHarigar Mudbottom is in Oatbarton, the northern-most town in the Shire.

You should bring the fake Blagrove's Brown, secretly Whitebranch, to Harigar Mudbottom.'I've received a different sort of orders from Jónar, the head of this here society. He hates the Inn League so much that he has assigned me a rather different task than my Inn League neighbour there. Shh, he mustn't hear us!

'I heard my friend from the Inn League there mention a foolish fellow named Harigar Mudbottom, stuck in a pickle up in Oatbarton. He wishes to drink Blagrove's Brown because he has not yet completed the Inn League Challenge.

'I can think of something even better. A drink of a different colour will serve to amuse us: Whitebranch, from The Ivy Bush in Hobbiton. If you bring that to Harigar, he will continue his boasting, but everyone will know that he never sampled Blagrove Brown. They are as different as apples and potatoes!''The Ivy Bush is in Hobbiton. You will find your decoy beverage there.''Whitebranch, you say? One moment...I shall have it ready directly.''Is that the Blagrove's Brown? Give it here; I will drink it right now, and then boast to all of its delightful taste, for I have heard wonderful things about it.'

Harigar takes a long drink, and lowers the mug at last.

