You should speak with Hamfast Gamgee, otherwise known as the Gaffer, to see if Bilbo or Frodo left him any clues as to the whereabouts of a key to the secret cellar.Talk to Gaffer Gamgee on Bagshot Row'You'll never believe this, ${PLAYER}! I decided a new oven was needed to begin preparations for the next festival. The labourers went to dig a pit into the side of the Hill, and lo! We all heard a shovel scrape against some wood, and before I knew what happened, a door was dug out!

'The door is locked now, but I'll wager it is a forgotten cellar of Bag End. Bag End is just above it, you see. Do you think that's where Mad Baggins kept his treasures? I suppose we can only guess...for Lobelia owns Bag End now.

'If you think she'll be letting anyone else dig around for Old Bilbo's treasure, then you go right ahead and ask her; be my guest! I won't be risking it...but it is terribly exciting, all the same!''Speak with Lobelia if you're really curious about that door. I don't know which is more frightening -- a cellar hidden away for fifty years, or Lobelia Sackville-Baggins.''Are you here about that door as well? You listen here: that mad fool of a Baggins never said anything about a secret cellar, and neither did that awful nephew of his, Frodo. I could not be more angry!

'I've scoured the whole burrow and not found a thing that could be used as a key to a hidden larder. They meant all along to leave Bag End to me with none of its proper fixings.

'If you want to see so much as a doorknob inside that cellar, you must find me that key! That gardener down on Bagshot Row surely knows something, but he won't speak a word to me. You look like a big, ominous sort; you ought to wrangle the truth out of him!''I loathe those Bagginses. Loathe, I tell you!''I'll wager Lobelia sent you to inquire after that new door going to the Baggins' lovely burrow. If you ask me, the whole affair smells of trouble. I tell my young ones, and I'll tell you too: best to mind your own matters, and no harm will come of aught.'Daley Utteridge has a great deal of good will towards the very poor in Winter-home, but sadly nothing to give. You are moved by his plight.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>The beggars can be found throughout town, and you can earn Yule Festival Tokens by participating in events at Winter-home.

Inspired by Daley Utteridge's wish to be more charitable with what little he has, you should collect many Yule Festival Tokens to gift to beggars who have nothing.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will consume 5 Yule Festival Tokens.</rgb>Daley Utteridge is in the workers' area in Winter-home.

You should return to Daley Utteridge and tell him of your kindness to the beggars. You gave them your hard-earned rewards!Tell Daley Utteridge that he inspired you to give away your hard-earned tokens'${PLAYER} has come back to visit! That is enough to brighten my day, for it needs brightening. As I walked to work this morning, I passed the good people of our town who are even worse off than myself. I had nothing to give them. It is the same every morning and every night.

'I count myself very lucky for what I have, but...my life would be better yet if I had the ability to give. All of my wages go to feeding my children and to paying the taxes on our home.

'If only there was something I could do! Perhaps Mayor Goodnough will give us more wages soon, and then I will be able to share my good fortune with the less fortunate.' 

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will consume 5 Yule Festival Tokens.</rgb>'I don't go a day without thinking often of those who are hungrier than I. My belly complains often, but at least I have bread to eat, meagre as it is. If only I had bread to spare....''Can it be? Are...are you giving these to me? I don't know what to say!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This will consume 1 Yule Festival Token.</rgb>'Pardon me -- surely...surely you're not giving this to me! Oh, generous ${CLASS}! You are too good!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This will consume 1 Yule Festival Token.</rgb>'Gracious me! You are so very kind, ${PLAYER}. I am amazed by your goodness, my dear ${RACE}.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This will consume 1 Yule Festival Token.</rgb>'All this, for me? What have I done to deserve such a gesture? I do not know what it is, but I will endeavour to do it again! Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This will consume 1 Yule Festival Token.</rgb>'What charity! What kindess! I haven't been on the receiving end of such generosity in many a long day. I will remember this, good ${RACE}.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This will consume 1 Yule Festival Token.</rgb>'${PLAYER}! Did you give the beggars your hard-earned rewards? That was too generous of you -- you worked hard for those!

