You have only false wine to give Lendasil... red wine, actually. You should bring it to her at once.'I've received a different sort of orders from Jónar, the head of this here society. He hates the Inn League so much that he has assigned me a rather different task than my Inn League neighbour there. Shh, he mustn't hear us!

'There is an Elf-lady by the name of Lendasil who tarries about in the Ruins of Edhelion, very near to Thorin's Hall, my home. She wishes to taste of Rivendell's own white wine, called Dorwinion White, but we shall all have a laugh at her expense when we deliver her the red version instead!

'Nonsensical as it may seem, it is all worth it in Jónar's eyes. Red wine instead of white! Lendasil will be so perplexed, and we shall all have a laugh upon your return.''Sogadan is the Vintner of Rivendell, and he can give you Dorwinion Red. Upon its delivery, you shall tell Lendasil that it is white wine and see what she thinks.''You seek Dorwinion Red? You are wise to do so; it is a fine wine indeed. Subtle, complex... rather like me, actually.''I see that you are come from Rivendell at last, and you have brought me the lovely wine I longed to taste. I shall sip it now.'

