'Simply gather a blue stick from the field and get ready to begin. Hurry, hurry -- only the first six people to join the Steel Beaks can play this round.  The game will start when all twelve sticks have been taken!'Hughbert Larch has gotten wind of a village that holds a yearly festival celebrating the blooming of daffodils.Hughbert cannot visit Clegur himself because he has too much work, and has given you a map to the town so you can go there if you choose. You should use the Map to Clegur in your inventory.Use the Map to ClegurHughbert cannot visit Clegur himself because he has too much work, and has given you a map to the town so you can go there if you choose.Travel to ClegurAs you arrived in Clegur with the help of the map given to you by Hughbert, a hobbit waved to you. You should go talk to her.Talk to Athra Devister'Well met, friend! The springtime flowers are so lovely, are they not? I'm a gardener by trade, and the happy blooms of spring fill my heart with so much joy. It's my misfortune, though, that as a gardener, I am often too busy in this season to truly enjoy it!

'I've heard of a place to the south that has a yearly celebration of the blooming of daffodils! That sounds like a reason for celebration if I have ever heard of one! But alas, there is too much work here to be done, and I cannot travel to see it myself. It's in a place called Clegur, away to the south, and east of old Cardolan.

'In fact, I have a map showing the way. You may have it if you think you might like to go. Someone should, it sounds wonderful!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Welcome to Daffodil Days, traveller! Have ye visited us before?'Athra Devister is grateful for your help with the Daffodil Days celebration and wants to give you a special gift.Athra wants you take her pot of daffodil bulbs as a reward for your contributions to the festival. You should take the pot of daffodil bulbs near Athra Devister in Clegur.Collect the daffodil bulbsAthra has given you daffodil bulbs as a reward for your contributions to the festival. You should think about what to do with them.<rgb=#FF0000>Think</rgb> about what to do with the bulbsYou remembered Hughbert Larch, the man from Bree who wanted to come to the Daffodil Days festival, but couldn't. You should find him at the Bree-land festival grounds and give the bulbs to him as a gift.'I can't begin to tell ye how much help ye've been for the past week. I had so many worries goin' into this years festival, I was gettin' crushed by 'em, I was! And then ye come along, all proper helpful, takin' much of the load off. I wanted to give ye a special gift. I have a pot of daffodil bulbs, and Old Gammer told me once that it's good luck to give plants as gifts, it is. So ye can go ahead and take 'em and do whatever ye want with 'em. They're yours now, they are. Thank ye for all yer help.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Hello again ${PLAYER}!

'You went to Clegur for Daffodil Days? Did you truly?'

You tell Hughbert of your time spent in Clegur.

'How delightful! I hope I can go there myself someday. Maybe next year.'

You give the daffodil bulbs to Hughbert to cheer him up.

'For me!? Really? I'm dumbfounded! What an incredible gift! Thank you, ${PLAYER}, thank you indeed! You have made my day. I will make sure they are well cared for!'The boot-maker for the Shrew Stomping event needs more wood for the special soles of the boots.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cherry wood branches can be found in the fields south of Duillond along the road to Celondim, probably near the bases of trees.

You should collect cherry wood for the reinforcement of the soles in the Shrew-stomping boots.Collect cherry wood branches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Deluraw can be found in Duillond near the ovens.

You should bring the cherry wood branches you collected to Deluraw.'I'm nearly out of the cherry wood I use for the most important part of the boots...the sole! The sole is fortified with this gentle, moderately dense, strong wood.

'It is the perfect -- yes, perfect -- wood for knocking out a pesky, oversized shrew without really hurting it. Elves do not like to hurt creatures, you see. Well, I suppose shrews tempt us to use violence more than most animals of the wild, but we have come up with a fair compromise.

'Cherry branches grow around clusters of trees in the pastures along the road to Duillond. I am sure there will be plenty of branches on the ground to replenish today's supply.''Elves would never harm shrews. Never. We wouldn't even consider such a gruesome ideas. Shrews are good, fine creatures.''These are just the branches I need! Many thanks, ${PLAYER}. This will ensure that the shrews are given just the right amount of dissuasion against their terrible behaviour.'You were able to stop Lobelia's plan to keep all the best Yule-feast food for herself.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Gaffer Gamgee is outside his hole on Bagshot Row at the foot of the Hill.

You should tell Gaffer Gamgee about Lobelia's folied plans.'Well it seems your little plan worked!  Fiddlesticks!  

'Another party ruined, no thanks to you. Why don't you go tell your good friend Hamfast what you've done here? No doubt he put you up to all this, what with his precious Marigold being sent up here to embarrass me so.''So that Lobelia was planning on keeping all the best food for herself and her own? I'm glad that you were able to set things to rights, and so are the rest of the folk here in Hobbiton.

'We only thought it proper to get you something. Lobelia was right, in a way: we don't have much in the way of spare proffer, but we share what we can, especially for those who have given us as much as you!

'We would like you to have this Yule-tree. It's a transplant -- my nephew Halfast brought it down from the Northfarthing. We were going to plant it in the yard, but seeing as how you helped us so...well, Marigold thought it would be best if you took it for your house.'There is a hedge-maze in the Horse-fields at the Spring Planting in Bree, and Sorrel North-took wants you to talk to her sister Buttercup before you partake in the aimless adventure.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Buttercup North-took is at the Festival Grounds in Bree, enjoying the hedge-maze on the Horse-fields.

You should make your way to the maze to give Sorrel's regards to her sister Buttercup.Talk to Buttercup North-took at the Horse-fields in Bree'Hi! You there, young ${RACE}! Have you seen the hedge maze yet? Half the attendants of the Feast of the Greenfields seem to have gone off to the maze in Bree. If you find yourself there this spring, you must talk to my dear sister Buttercup, who went on a great journey to see the hedges. She has always been most fond of foliage.

'It sounds like there is a great deal of fun to be had on the Horse-fields this year. I know you'll find yourself there before the festival is done with -- you must give my regards to Buttercup while she is there!''The Hedge-maze is in Bree, in the Horse-fields.''Hello there! So you come directly from my sister Sorrel, do you? It is a shame that she did not come herself to see the maze; unfortunately, the distance from Tookland to Bree is very great, and she has not quite the love of greenery that I possess. Nonetheless, I am glad you are here.'There is much to do during the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt.There is much to do in Eriador during the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt.Complete Eriador year one Trifles cardComplete Eriador year one Tales cardComplete Eriador year one Travels cardComplete Eriador year two Trifles cardComplete Eriador year two Tales cardComplete Eriador year three Tales cardComplete Eriador year three Travels cardComplete Eriador year four Trifles cardComplete Eriador year four Tales cardComplete Eriador year four Travels cardComplete Eriador year five Tales cardComplete Eriador year five Travels cardComplete Eriador year six Tales cardComplete Eriador year seven Travels cardComplete Eriador year eight Tales cardComplete Eriador year eight Travels cardComplete Eriador year nine Tales cardComplete Eriador year nine Travels cardComplete Eriador year ten Tales cardComplete Eriador year eleven Trifles cardComplete Eriador year eleven Tales cardComplete Eriador year eleven Travels cardThere is much to do during the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt.There is much to do during the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt.Complete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year OneComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year TwoComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year ThreeComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year FourComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year FiveComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year SixComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year SevenComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year EightComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year NineComplete The Anniversary Scavenger Hunt -- Year TenMeneldir says that the Uruk attack on Mossward is a sign that you cannot avoid the dangers that encroach upon Swanfleet. You have become part of a larger world.Eleri stands over the dead bodies of the Uruk raiders, considering the events of the attack.Talk to Eleri about the mark of the White HandMeneldir wears a worried expression.Talk to Meneldir'What meaning might this mark possess? ${PLAYER}, will you ask Eleri if she has seen this symbol before today?''Has Eleri seen this symbol before?''The White Hand? No, I have not seen this symbol before... and that troubles me. What new danger might it signify?''No, I have not seen this symbol before.''For now we should help the folk of Mossward recover from this attack. I trust you will lend your aid? You have become embroiled in this, just as I have. If it is a life of adventure you seek, I assure you that you seem to have found it... or it has found you!

