You have collected the writing-quill, phial of ink, and parchment. You should deliver them to Frodo at the wedding banquet in Merethrond.Frodo is deciding where to begin his tale of adventure.Wait for Frodo to decide how to start his tale of adventureFrodo Baggins can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).

After delivering a quill, ink, and parchment to Frodo Baggins, he appears to have found himself unable to write. You should talk to Frodo.Talk to Frodo'Good evening to you, ${PLAYER}! How have you been enjoying the banquet?

'To my mind, it is hard to recall a more pleasant night in recent memory.'

Frodo shifts in his seat.

'Even so, I have been thinking on all that has happened since I left the Shire. I was wondering what Uncle Bilbo would make of all this business, and that has given me an idea. Uncle Bilbo kept a diary, so why shouldn't I write of my own adventures?

'Could you find me a quill and a phial of ink? Oh, and a few sheets of parchment!''I must say, even such a grand feast makes me long for the comforts of the Shire.

'Did you find what I asked for? Oh good, good. I do hope it wasn't too much trouble, ${PLAYER}!

'Now... where to begin?''I suppose I should just enjoy the banquet tonight, shouldn't I?

'I thought I'd so much to say, but the words just will not come to me right now.

'Thank you all the same, ${PLAYER}. I hope you enjoy the rest of the banquet, and I will be sure to tell you when I finish my tale!'With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits a dwarf of the proud line of Durin's Folk -- Gimli, son of Glóin.

