Gimli has asked you to speak to Galadriel on his behalf and see if she might wish to visit the Glittering Caves or return to Minas Tirith once the city gates are repaired.Talk to GaladrielGimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).

Although seemingly flattered, Galadriel has politely declined Gimli's invitation. However, Galadriel did impart that she knows their paths shall cross once again.Talk to Gimli'Aye, have you ever seen such beauty?'

Gimli glances around at Merethrond, seemingly in awe of the Gondorian craft-skill needed for its construction.

'Fine, indeed, especially for the hands of Men. But what of the hands of dwarves? What of MY hands? You see, it has set my mind on the future!

'Drink with me, ${PLAYER}, and let me tell you of what I seek to do!''Now, listen to me.

'No dwarf of good repute would allow a flagon of ale - even one so fine, mind you - to speak on his behalf!

'Ha! Tonight that is what you are for, ${PLAYER}!

'Do you see the Lady Galadriel sitting at the wedding-table? Her radiance knows no equal! I have cherished the gift she granted to me since we parted in Lothlórien, and I would grant her one in return.

'I ask only that the Lady Galadriel one day visit the Glittering Caves. It shall be years before my work is finished, but that is not so long a time by the reckoning of Elves.

'Will you do this for me, ${PLAYER}?'As you tell Galadriel of Gimli's plans for the coming days and offer an invitation on his behalf, she begins to chuckle softly.

'You may tell Gimli that I have not forgotten the manner of our meeting in Lothlórien, nor have I forgotten the manner of our parting. A gift given freely need not be repaid.

'Although I must decline Gimli's invitation, do not think that I do so in unkindness. I look now to the West for that is where my future leads me. Yet, I know that our paths shall cross once more ere the end.

'Do not let your hearts be troubled in times of such joy. Much still remains to be seen!''What had the Lady Galadriel to say, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Gimli of Galadriel's words. When you mention that Galadriel knows their paths shall cross once again, a smile spreads across Gimli's face.

'There will be time enough tomorrow to talk of days to come, I think! For tonight, let us be merry!With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. At the head of the table beside Queen Arwen Undómiel, sits the King of Gondor and of the High King of the Reunited Kingdom  -- King Aragorn II Elessar.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Unquieted tables can be found throughout Merethrond.

King Aragorn II Elessar has asked you to quiet tables in Merethrond that he might offer a toast.Quiet tables in Merethrond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})King Aragorn II Elessar can be found in Merethrond.

You have quieted all of the tables in the main hall of Merethrond. You should return to King Aragorn II Elessar.Talk to King Aragorn II Elessar'What more could I ask of one who has done so much?'

King Aragorn II Elessar smiles at you.

'My words fail me, ${PLAYER}. To be united with my love at last brings me greater joy than I thought knowable by Men. Even so, I must address my people and my honoured guests. Such is the duty of a King!

'I would offer a toast to all in attendance this night. Would you quiet the tables that I might speak?''Allow me to offer a toast, my friend. Be seated if you wish.

'You have my thanks and those of the High Queen.'With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits an Elf of Eryn Lasgalen -- Legolas, son of Thranduil.

