You have collected Merry's pipe-weed and should now return it to him.'Hello, ${PLAYER}! Not getting tired so soon, are you?

'I know just the thing to liven up this banquet! I... just don't quite recall where I left it.

'Back when we were at Isengard, I packed away a bit of the Longbottom Leaf we found in the stores. After all, it's not like Saruman was going to use it stuck up in his tower!

'Anyway, I can't remember if I left my pipe-weed near the baths in the Great Guest-house, by some of the horses in the High Stables, or over by the prow of Minas Tirith. It's got to be one of those!

'If you go find it, I'd be happy to share it with you. Why, I'd be glad to share every last bit of it tonight!''It was quite the ceremony, wasn't it? Nothing like a Shire wedding, mind you.

'Have you found the pipe-weed?''${PLAYER}!

'You're not by chance looking for Master Meriadoc's pipe-weed, are you?

'He gave it to me for safe-keeping before the ceremony, but it has been quite a busy day! If you'd like to bring it to him, I set it near the bottom of the stairs down to the kitchens.

'Oh, and may I help you with anything else? No? Very good!''You found it? Oh, wonderful!

'Well, I can't speak for anyone else, but I hope this banquet never ends!'With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits one of the Wise -- Mithrandir, the Wizard known beyond the lands of Gondor as Gandalf the White.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'On the Line of Kings' and the 'Chronicle of Arnor' can be found in Mithrandir's guest-chamber in the High Guest-house.

Mithrandir has asked you to collect two tomes from his guest-chamber in the High Guest-house and return them to him in Merethrond.Collect 'On the Line of Kings' in the High Guest-houseCollect the 'Chronicle of Arnor' in the High Guest-houseMithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).

You have found the tomes that Mithrandir requested and should now deliver them to him at the wedding banquet.Mithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).

Mithrandir has not revealed why he needed the tomes from his guest-chamber. You should wait and see if he will soon reveal their purpose.Talk to MithrandirMithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).

Mithrandir seems prepared to discuss the purpose of the tomes he requested from his guest-chamber. You should talk to Mithrandir.Talk to Mithrandir'Ah, and how are you enjoying this fine banquet? Quite a bit, I hope, for I most certainly am!

'Although...'

Mithrandir pauses and looks to the ends of the table.

'I must confess that in my haste to take my seat here in Merethrond, I seem to have forgotten something in my guest-chamber. If it were of little import, I am certain it could wait until after the banquet. Unfortunately, it cannot.

'In my keeping, there are two tomes from the Houses of Lore. The first is a treatise on the line of Kings in Gondor, and the other is a chronicle of the Northern Kingdom.

'Will you fetch them for me?''You've found them?'

Mithrandir glances to his right and looks at Frodo and Samwise.

'Yes, yes. These will do.''Ah yes, ${PLAYER}. I suppose I owe you an explanation as to why I requested these particular tomes.

'You see...'

Mithrandir gestures to Frodo and Samwise and hands them the tomes. Frodo and Sam place the tomes on their seats, and hop back onto them. Mithrandir smiles at you.

'Need I explain further?

