Lendasil has asked you to collect a glass of Dorwinion White for her from the vintner Sogadan in the Rivendell. Once you have the wine, bring it back to her at Refuge of Edhelion.'I have here a list of requests to assist Inn League members in need, stranded away from home without the support of their beer-loving brethren. It seems they miss their favourite drinks, or in some cases they've never even tasted them!

'Take Lendasil, for example. She is in Edhelion, and craves a taste of wine from her own home. Dorwinion White, if my sources are correct.

'Sogadan in Rivendell is the fellow that sells it. He is a vintner there. Make sure you buy the white, not the red!''Greetings to you. I see that you are a member of the halflings' "Inn League" as well. Some find them a frivolous people, but it is good to find some pleasures in this Middle-earth, especially when confronted with ruins such as these.

'Soon I will leave Middle-earth behind, and yet I have decided to complete their Inn League's Challenge. It affords me a wonderful opportunity to taste all that will be lost to me when I leave these lands behind. Yet it seems I have neglected to drink one of the finest wines in Middle-earth: Dorwinion White. Sadly, beyond journeying to Dorwinion itself, this can only be found in Rivendell.

'Would you obtain this wine for me? I fear I cannot leave my contemplation at Edhelion. Sogadan, the vintner, is a friend of mine and will likely have what I desire.''You'd best hurry over to Rivendell to collect that wine. Dorwinion White is the ticket. Not red!''Dorwinion White reminds me of the Falls of Imladris, clear as water. It is a perfect wine.''Ah, you have brought the wine. What a lovely colour...truly a great wine. Perhaps there are superior wines in the West...but sometimes I wonder if that is true.

