Which bottle am I?'Did you really make it all the way through based on solving the riddles? Well done, ${PLAYER}! You are far cleverer than I; that much is certain.'While wandering through the woods of the Ettenmoors you discovered a sapling shaking in the soil. Odd, that a little sapling would move while you drew near. You investigate.Search the Ettenmoors for the tremor that stirred the earth, collect it and return it to Faranil at Glân Vraig.Find the source of the tremor Faranil feltThis was unexpected. Try once more to collect the sapling. Faranil, in Glân Vraig, wants to study the trembling little sapling.Collect and deliver the sapling to Faranil at Glân VraigHaving delivered the sapling to Faranil, you should now speak with the horticulturist to see what she may know of this little sapling.Speak with Faranil at Glân Vraig'Mae Govannen. I am Faranil, a tender of gardens and trees. You would rightly ask why one such as I would enlist to defend this accursed place, and I will tell you.

'After centuries in Rivendell, a tremor in the earth stirred my heart to action and drew me over the pass to this place. Lainedhal affords me a plot to study, learn, and seek what calls to my heart, but he cannot spare soldiers to defend me across these lands.

'I know that something awaits us beyond the gates of Glân Vraig, something wonderful and new, but I dare not make the journey.

'I wonder, friend, will you?

'I do not know what has awoken, but you will know when you see it.''I wonder what this could mean. Surely there is healing happening in these lands. I think we shall need to investigate further. When you are prepared speak with me about this little gift. We shall embark on an adventure together, I think.'Scouts throughout the Ettenmoors discovered saplings shaking in the soil. Cinaid, the corruptor at Gramsfoot bade you investigate these little saplings and bring him a sample.Find a sapling described by Cinaid, rip it out of the ground, and deliver it to Cinaid at Gramsfoot.It squealed or squeaked. You heard it. Get the sapling back to Gramsfoot.Get the sapling out of the ground!Deliver the sapling to Cinaid at GramsfootYou delivered the stubborn little sapling to the Corruptor Cinaid. Time to find out what this little creature might really be.Speak with Cinaid at Gramsfoot about your findCinaid half-hisses as he speaks.

'Words from scouts, something stirs across the Ettenmoors. Little sprigs of trees that shiver and shake in the morning dew. Unlike other saplings, they respond to our presence and the presence of the accursed so-called Free People.

'These saplings are an omen, and I intended to decipher what their presence means.

'I charge you to collect a specimen for me. Deliver it here, and we will study it together.

'Mordirith's grace be with you.''I cannot say what you have brought me. Not yet. We have need to study and present this creature to others. I do believe I have an understanding of what it may be, and if my supposition is correct, this is a find that will make Angmar's alchemists very happy.'

A grim smirk displays on the man's ashen face.

