Sew a guild-pattern robe.Execute the recipe for a guild-pattern robe'Robes are perhaps the most misunderstood form of 'armour' we see. Freedom of movement, protection against the elements and foes, pockets! Robes are highly functional. I'm sure you can produce a beautiful set.''Robes are perhaps the most misunderstood form of 'armour' we see. Freedom of movement, protection against the elements and foes, pockets! Robes are highly functional. I'm sure you can produce a beautiful set.''Warm, functional, just the right amount of flair. I adore it!''Warm, functional, just the right amount of flair. I adore it!'Frodo Baggins is looking for an adventurer to help in a birthday surprise for his uncle Bilbo! Travel to Rivendell to find out how you can be of assistance.Frodo can be found in Rivendell, inside The Last Homely House.

The birthday of Frodo and Bilbo Baggins is upon us!  Frodo is looking for an adventurer to assist him with a birthday surprise for his uncle Bilbo.Travel to Rivendell and speak with Frodo BagginsFrodo can be found in Rivendell, inside The Last Homely House.

The birthday of Frodo and Bilbo Baggins is upon us!  Frodo is looking for an adventurer to assist him with a birthday surprise for his uncle Bilbo.Speak to Frodo Baggins in The Last Homely House in RivendellWith Frodo and Bilbo Baggins' birthdays close at hand, Frodo is looking for an adventurer to assist him with a surprise for his uncle Bilbo.  Travel to Rivendell to assist Frodo with his plans.'Hello!  Ah, you're here to assist with my birthday surprise for uncle Bilbo?'A young hobbit child has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to the child's story.Speak to the child'Scuse me?  What's that you're asking about?  Oh yes! I know lots of stories about Bilbo!  My mum tells me them some nights when I can't get to sleep.''My mum tells me stories about mister Bilbo some nights when I can't get to sleep. My favourites are the ones about the Lonely Mountain, with the dragon and the treasure!

'I'd like a dragon I think, but only a nice one, not a nasty one.  My good dragon would live with me and bring us shiny things to play with, and I'd fly him around in the sky!  Dragons are terrible clever you know, and so mine would tell me stories and teach me things that only dragons know!

'But, you know, I keep thinking about that poor mountain.  Why, it's even called the Lonely Mountain, and that was when it still had a dragon friend of its own.   But since Bilbo scared off the dragon I bet that mountain is even lonelier.  I feel so bad for it some nights I just cry into my plush sheep, Petunia.

'But then I thought about nice Mister Bilbo and I bet he feels the same way! I bet he went back to that poor mountain to keep it company!  If I were him, I'd bring it another dragon, but a nice one this time to keep it company for years and years and years! I bet that's just what he did!'Tell the stories you've collected to Bilbo Baggins for his amusement.Tell Bilbo about Frodo's request.Speak to Bilbo BagginsTell Bilbo the stories you collected.Tell Bilbo the stories you've collectedBilbo is delighted with your stories and would like to reward you for your time.Speak to Bilbo Baggins'I imagine those stories have someone waiting for them! Off you go now.''Why hello, ${PLAYER}! Many salutations I'm sure. And what has brought you here to me on this fine day?''Stories? From the Shire? And all of them about me? I can't wait to hear them! Please tell me your tales.''Oh, oh dear! Oh my! They are even better than I thought! The imagination of hobbits truly knows no bounds. The Lonely Mountain? Holly Hornblowers' pies? A caped crusader even?! Oh gracious and goodness me.

'You have made this old hobbit very happy, and brought me belly laughs such as I have not known for a while. Elves, for all their charms, have a more esoteric form of humour. I've missed the stories hobbits tell!

'Take this with my thanks. Clearly you have a knack for recording and telling tales. I hope you keep that up during your adventures, as I sense you will have a great many stories to tell!'Bogo Chubb has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Bogo Chubb's story.Speak to Bogo Chubb'Bilbo Baggins you're asking about, eh?  Most folks think he's off gallivanting goodness knows where, but I've got quite a different story to tell you if you'll listen.''So, you're wondering what Bilbo's been up to since he disappeared, eh?  Well, as it happens I heard that he's not in some far off land at all, he's still right here, in the Shire!

'That whole party business was an elaborate ruse to set people talking and rumouring and thinking that he's in some far-off land, having more adventures.  That was just Bilbo's way of creating a distraction while he crept away to hide in plain sight!

'Folks say that at night you can sometimes see him, clothed in black, face hidden behind a dark mask with an even darker cape all flapping and flowing behind him, riding along the roads of the Shire.  He's turned vigilante, protecting us all from bandits and goblins and anything else nasty trying to creep into our towns!

'Bilbo's managed to stay out of sight so well due to his hidden hobbit-holes all over the Shire.  They were built in secret and paid for by his fortune, and he roams between these, never spending too much time in any one spot, always listening and waiting for danger to appear!'Dudo Chubb has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Dudo Chubb's story.Speak to Dudo Chubb'Oh, collecting stories about Bilbo 'Big-shot' Baggins, eh?  More than enough of those to go around to be sure.  

'Luckily for you, I happen to know the truth of the matter of that odd disappearing act he pulled at his party, yes I do!''As I was saying, here's what happened at that birthday party of Bilbo's.

'You see, when he was on his adventures, he met up with a pile of dwarves! Yes dwarves! Anybody who knows anything knows that some of them dwarves got mighty peculiar after losing their home in the mountains far off all that long time ago.

'Since then, stories say, some of them been known to be a roaming band doing nearly anything to squeak by, and that would breed loose morals if you ask me! Assuming they ever had any to start with, can't ever be sure with people not of the Shire, no you cannot!

'I heard that one of these dwarves helped Bilbo dig a complex of tunnels under Bag End, and he simply popped down into these at an opportune moment!  Goodness only knows what he's been up to since, but you can bet it's something no respectable hobbit would be caught doing!'Frodo Baggins requests that you travel to the Shire to collect the stories hobbits are telling about his uncle Bilbo's mysterious disappearance and current whereabouts and adventures.Gaffer Gamgee is located just south of the party tree and north-west of the Bywater Bridge.

Frodo has asked that you collect the stories being told by the hobbits of the Shire about his uncle Bilbo.  He's suggested that you speak to Gaffer Gamgee to learn which hobbits have the best stories to tell.Speak to Gaffer Gamgee in Hobbiton-Bywater'${PLAYER}, I'm glad you're here.  I am in need of an adventurer such as yourself to help with a birthday surprise for my uncle Bilbo. 

'When Bilbo decided to resettle in Rivendell, he did it in typical fashion as you may have heard - with a bang and a flash, disappearing right during his own birthday party!

'In that moment, Bilbo instantly became the subject of many a tall tale, and increasingly exaggerated legend.  I know he'd be amused to no end to hear these stories, but I myself can't go collect them.   The next time you're in the Shire, could you do this for me?  

'Were I you, I'd start at the Gaffer.  He hears most everything worth hearing and he will surely know who you should talk to in order to obtain the very best tales.''Why hello!  Frodo's sent you to talk to me then?  What's that young fry up to now?'Gaffer Gamgee is sure to know which hobbits have the best stories to tell of Bilbo's disappearance and his adventures and whereabouts since then.Speak to the Gaffer to obtain his list of hobbits likely to have stories worth collecting.Speak to the GafferRead the Gaffer's Note.Read the Gaffer's NoteSpeak to the Gaffer, he probably knows who you should talk to first.Speak to the GafferFollow this road from the Gaffer's out to the east and then turn south.  Ted's standing just south of the Bywater Bridge.

Speak to Ted Sandyman to hear the first of the stories about Bilbo and his adventures.Listen to Ted Sandyman's storyListen to the remainder of the hobbits' stories.Listen to Robin Smallburrow's storyListen to Dudo Chubb's storyListen to Lobelia Sackville-Baggins' storyListen to the Storyteller's taleListen to Hal Hornblower's storyListen to Bogo Chubb's storyListen to Lotho Sackville-Baggins' storyListen to the child's storyListen to Hereward Loamsdown's storyListen to Holly Hornblower's storyListen to Postman Grubb's storyAll the hobbits have been spoken to.  You should check in with the Gaffer once more.Return to Gaffer Gamgee'So you're here to collect stories about Bilbo Baggins, are you?  Heard that I would know who to talk to?  Naturally, you're correct.  Give me a moment and I'll write you down a list of likely hobbits to speak to.

'Mind you, you'll need to catch them at just the right time. If they don't seem to have a story for you, check back on them in a while.  If you want to hear every story, you'll need to have some perseverance!''Right then, here's that list.  You'll want to give it a quick look to make sure you can read my handwriting.''That note makes sense then?

'Were I you, I'd probably start by talking to Ted Sandyman.   Just follow this road out to the east and then turn south.  Ted's standing just south of the Bywater Bridge.

'I know Ted's got time now, so he'll be happy to share his story.  Just remember that not every hobbit on that list will have a story to share whenever you please!  Just check back on them from time to time, you'll catch them at a good time soon enough I'm sure.''You managed to speak to all the hobbits on my list then? Wonderful!

'If that's given you what you need, off with you then.  Time to take these stories to their final recipient!'Hal Hornblower has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Hal Hornblower's story.Speak to Hal Hornblower'Bilbo, eh?  Now, folks will tell you any nonsense about what happened to Bilbo at his birthday party, but what's the fun in that?  It was all smoke and mirrors anyway, if you ask me.  

'The real story is in what happened after!  Which, as it happens, I know all about.''Now, I keep my ears to the ground I do, and I can tell you with complete confidence that Bilbo went on back to the Elves!  He always told such stories about them the likes of which you wouldn't believe.

'They say that an Elf Queen has been teaching him to grow the biggest taters a person could ever hope to see.  Leave it to Bilbo to go all the way off to the Elves to gain knowledge just so he can steal the first prize ribbon from Farmer Maggot at one of these Farmers Faires!

'Some folks would just try harder in their own garden plot, but Bilbo just couldn't never do anything the easy way when he could have an adventure instead. I imagine he'll be back any day to wipe that smug smirk off of Farmer Maggot and break his sixty-year winning streak.'Hereward Loamsdown has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Hereward Loamsdown's story.Speak to Hereward Loamsdown'Ah! You're collecting stories about Bilbo Baggins?  I know a grand of one for ya, that fellow's been some places and seen some things, yes he most certainly has!''I heard that Bilbo got up to a whole mess of adventures after his party, but you're wondering what he's up to now, yes?

'Well I'll tell you that I heard that in the end, he ran into some of those big folk what ride horses all the time… what 're they called… the Riders of Ronald?  Roger? No, nearly there... tip of my tongue… Rohan!  That's it!  I hear he's got himself a war-pony and that they taught him to be a proper horse-master and all! 

'Rides in the company of, drat it, what's the feller's name… Theon...no… Theorem, ach, that's not it either.. hang it all, give me a minute… Théoden!  That's the chappy!  Our Bilbo's right there, riding in that company of Big Folk, with banners streaming and horses whinnying, all across those big plains of grass tall enough to hide a hobbit, or so I hear!'Holly Hornblower has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Holly Hornblower's story.Speak to Holly Hornblower'What's that?  Oh, you're wondering where Bilbo is now?  Turns out you've asked the right hobbit!''I'll have you know that I have it on excellent authority that on his travels Bilbo met a whopping massive bear!  Yes, a proper large bear, not like the little ones what den around in these parts.  And what did Bilbo do?

'No, don't be silly, the bear didn't eat him in one gulp!  Imagine the indigestion with all those brass buttons!

'Now, Bilbo might not be a proper hobbit, but a hobbit still he is, and that means he was carrying any number of delicious things the like of which that bear had never smelled or tasted before.  With those, clever Bilbo tamed that bear, indeed he did!   And that's not the end, no not at all! Just getting to the best part, if you believe it.

'Radagast the Brown, you've heard of him yes? Keeper of animals they say and  proper wizard in his own right, well, Radagast heard about Bilbo and the bear and he was so impressed that he trained old Bilbo to be a Lore-master!

'Neither jestin’ nor jokin’ am I, that's right, the first Hobbit Lore-master is our Bilbo, and he rides around now on his great bear, accompanying Radagast all over the lands!'Lobelia Sackville-Baggins has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Lobelia Sackville-Baggins' story.Speak to Lobelia Sackville-Baggins'Ooh, all anyone talks about around here is Bilbo Baggins!  But, as it happens, yes I do know quite a juicy bit of information that I don't mind sharing with a person such as yourself.''Listen up now and you might learn something worth knowing.  Earlier that day, the day of the party, that is,  I'll have you know that I saw Bilbo sampling a good many of Holly Hornblower's pies!

'They always look delectable but I swear she uses 'secret ingredients' that would put off even the staunchest eater! Not that I'm jealous, mind.  My pies always come in second and I have an easy mind knowing they are made of only the finest fruits, not any new nonsense I hear tell of, not like SOME people I know of and if that's good enough for me well... pardon me, what was I saying?  Right! Mr. Bilbo.

'As I was saying, I've heard that Holly was experimenting with sneaking in ground up mushrooms, pinched from Farmer Maggot's field!  If you listen to the young fry around these parts who've snuck into his field and eaten some, you know they have some awful queer effects!

'So, if you want to know what I think, and you clearly do as you're asking me, well, I think eating those pies up and disappeared Bilbo!  Good thing that odd Gandalf was around to cover it up with a poof of smoke and save us all the scandal, although some might think that there could have been an important lesson to be learned had he not.'Lotho Sackville-Baggins has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Lotho Sackville-Baggins' story.Speak to Lotho Sackville-Baggins'Oh, you're wondering what Mad Baggins has been up to?  Hah!  He was all cleverness and no sense, if you ask me.  I know a right amusing story of what mischief he's gotten himself into, I surely do.''Well now, last I heard is that old Baggins had completely squandered his fortune, although I never myself believed it was half as big as folks said, so it wouldn't be that hard to lose now would it?

'But as I was saying, with his fortune gone I hear he went to one of those big folk towns and got himself the finest fake beard that the remainder of his money could buy.  Now now, don't start laughing yet, you ain't heard the rest of it, and you remember what I said about him being too clever without much sense?

'Well! Fake beard obtained, he went to live with the dwarves!  Yes! Dwarves! Snuck right in there with them in their caves and their digging.  Dwarves aren't too smart from what I've heard and those caves gotta be mighty shadowy and smoky from the torches, don't you think?

'Figure with his beard he can hide and work right alongside them, all the while slowly building up a new fortune of pocketed gems and fine metals!  I bet he'll be back again lording his adventures and supposed fortunes over us all once more.'Postman Grubb has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Postman Grubb's story.Speak to Postman Grubb'Looking for stories about Bilbo, are you now?  Well as Postman, I know most people and hear most things.  I can certainly spare the time to tell you a tale.''So you're wanting to know where Bilbo has got himself off to?  Well if you ask around these parts folks will tell you all kinds of nonsense.  He got kidnapped or is flying his own dragon or is leading a fighting tribe of spiders!

'The gullibility of hobbits is sometimes not to be believed.  They'll latch onto any story they hear, and the more exotic the better! Can you imagine Bilbo doing any of those things at his age?  Gracious, he's a unique sort of hobbit but he's got limits!

'I can see you're the sensible sort, so I'll tell you the real truth – Bilbo's always had a terrible fondness for Elves.  Downright unsettling if you ask me, but he was never one to hold with convention.  Anyway, he decided to spend the rest of his days with them, invited by the Elvish leaders and all!

'He's spent his declining years living with them and enjoying their hospitality, all while writing his memoirs in the form of a one act play “Where There's Smaug, There's Fire.” I hear that the Buckland Benefit of the Benevolent Bucket Brigade Brotherhood for the Bruised and Burned has exclusive rights for the opening!'Ted Sandyman has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Shirrif Robin Smallburrow's story.Speak to Robin Smallburrow'What's that you're asking about now?  Old Mr. Bilbo you say?  Why certainly I know what happened at his birthday party!  

'Listen up and I'll tell you the true facts of the matter.''Bilbo Baggins was something of an eccentric around these parts.  His adventures created enough stories that  you can still hear new ones every day! Why, I was just recently talking to my niece's cousin's sister-in-law's nephew the other day and he said that he knew what really happened at that funny birthday party!

'All the folks in these parts attended it, but what with the food and the drink and the dancing and all the youngsters underfoot, only a few folks really witnessed the actual disappearing act!

'My niece's sister's cousins... aw you get the picture, the lad I was talking with, he says that he saw that Wizard Gandalf pop old Mr. Bilbo into a giant sack! Just visible through the fog he said, and Mr. Bilbo squirming and wriggling like anything!  Then they just vanished into thin air!

'Goodness knows what happened to the poor chap after that, but honestly! With the stories folks tell about his adventures and associates and goings on, what other end can a hobbit expect than a sticky one?'The local Storyteller has agreed to share a tale about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to the storyteller's tale.Speak to the storyteller'Bilbo Baggins could single-handedly keep me in business for years to come the way folks around here swap stories about him.  I'll gladly tell you my own personal thoughts on why he disappeared from his birthday party though.''Some around here weren't sure about him, but I miss dear Bilbo. He always had such an air of mystery about him, which is saying something since the only air most hobbits have about them is one of pipe-weed and their last meal.

'Bilbo was refreshing he was - shook us all up some and that's a good thing, no doubt.  We need some rousing out of our usual routine!  Not all of us have the constitution to be explorers, so it's a precious commodity indeed when we get a hobbit with real stories to tell.

'Anyhow, I hear that Bilbo was getting bored, and can you blame him?  So when Gandalf was setting off his lovely fireworks, Bilbo grabbed onto one and off he went!  Soared off into the skies in a trail of sparks!  Now shake your head if you like, but I think that Bilbo Baggins could do just nearly anything he put his mind to, and I'm not changing my story!

'Oh, I'd love to know where he landed and what mischief he's gotten up to since then.  I surely do hope he returns home again or I might just explode in a starburst myself from curiosity!'Ted Sandyman has agreed to share a story about Bilbo Baggins and his adventures.Listen to Ted Sandyman's story.Speak to Ted Sandyman'Surely I'll tell you a tale of Bilbo Baggins and the disappearing act he pulled at his birthday party all those years ago.  Just lend me your ear for a moment.''Well now, what I heard is that Bilbo had just about had it on his birthday! So many people, all of them bickering and squawking and trying to sneak into Bag End and look for treasure!  Anyone would grow weary and want to be done with it.

'Bilbo was always an... unconventional hobbit, so what I heard tell is that he decided to give everyone a good scare and sneak away!  Went to go enjoy himself where all his family wasn't, and went 'round to all the taverns and inns trying their brew!

'Now, from what I hear tell, no one's quite sure what really happened after that, but my brother's son's friend's cousin works down at The Green Dragon, and he swears he shipped off a barrel that was heavier than the others the next day, and that it rolled funny like something was in it. Didn't think to question it until after the fact!

'My guess is that Bilbo enjoyed himself a bit too much, found himself in a cozy barrel... and got shipped off!  Goodness only knows where he is now. I wonder what interesting brews he's gotten to try in far-flung lands?'You have earned the Bane of Aglarond title.You have earned the Bane of Anduin title.You have earned the Bane of Arkenstone title.You have earned the Bane of Belegaer title.You have earned the Bane of Brandywine title.You have earned the Bane of Crickhollow title.You have earned the Bane of Dwarrowdelf title.You have earned the Bane of Eldar title.You have earned the Bane of Estel title.You have earned the Bane of Evernight title.You have earned the Bane of Firefoot title.You have earned the Bane of Fornost title.You have earned the Bane of Gilrain title.You have earned the Bane of Gladden title.You have earned the Bane of Gwaihir title.You have earned the Bane of Imladris title.You have earned the Bane of Landroval title.You have earned the Bane of Laurelin title.You have earned the Bane of Maiar title.You have earned the Bane of Meneldor title.You have earned the Bane of Mirkwood title.You have earned the Bane of Morthond title.You have earned the Bane of Nimrodel title.You have earned the Bane of Riddermark title.You have earned the Bane of Silverlode title.You have earned the Bane of Sirannon title.You have earned the Bane of Snowbourn title.Determined to cast the Iron Crown out of Angmar, the Hill-men and their allies set siege upon the great fortress-city of Carn Dûm.Determined to cast the Iron Crown out of Angmar, the Hill-men and their allies set siege upon the great fortress-city of Carn Dûm.Complete 'Challenger of the Iron Crown (Weekly)'Determined to cast the Iron Crown out of Angmar, the Hill-men and their allies set siege upon the great fortress-city of Carn Dûm.Determined to cast the Iron Crown out of Angmar, the Hill-men and their allies set siege upon 