Whether they mean to do so or not varies...People seem to find your words and actions quite puzzling.Frodo Baggins and his cousin Bilbo -- though he calls him Uncle -- share the same birthday, but have been unable to celebrate together for seventeen years.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Bilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House at Rivendell.

Frodo Baggins has asked that you deliver a belated birthday present to Bilbo.Frodo Baggins is in Bilbo's room on the ground floor of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.

Bilbo Baggins has asked that you bring Frodo a birthday present in return.Bilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.

Frodo Baggins has asked you to thank Bilbo for his gift.'Hello there, I was wondering if you might be able to spare a moment. My Uncle Bilbo and I share a birthday, September the Twenty-second, and I have celebrated it by holding a small gathering in his honour every year since he left Bag End. Even though the day has passed, I thought it would be nice to get the old rascal something for our birthday anyway.

'It is a small gift, but I was hoping that you could bring it to him. He wouldn't take a present from me now -- he would say, "It isn't right, Frodo my lad, what with it being past our birthday and all," but perhaps he wouldn't turn down the gift if it was delivered by someone else.

'Would you do this for me?''Have you found my dear cousin yet, ${PLAYER}? It is important that you do so before our birthday is over.''What is this now? A present from Frodo for our Birthday? Well, isn't that curious, for I was planning on giving young Frodo a present of my own! It has been a tradition of mine ever since I arrived here in Rivendell to give out presents on my birthday to the Elves. They don't much understand the custom, but they always accept the gifts graciously. Wonderful folk, the Elves.

'I always set aside a present for Frodo and have in fact been carrying it around for a few days now! I would more than likely forgotten about it had you not reminded me.

'Take my present to him, if you would; he is often troubled, and it may brighten his mood.''I certainly hope Frodo enjoys my gift.''Bilbo accepted the present after all? Well, that did go better than I expected!

'And what's this? A present for me, from Bilbo? He is always full of surprises.

'Go back and tell him thank you very much, and that I will come to visit him later.''Let Uncle Bilbo know that I appreciate his gift.''Ah, he did enjoy the gift, splendid! And here I go, having you carry off presents for others without thought of yourself. A wonderful ${RACE} if I ever knew one!

'I believe I have something here for you. It isn't much, just a trinket. A small toy really. Why, I remember the day I was giving these out at my eleventy-first birthday not seventeen years ago...but I am going on with old tales again.

'Thank you for your help, ${PLAYER}.'Mosco Smallburrow claims he hooked the biggest fish he'd ever encountered, but in being dragged bodily from one edge of the pond to the other, he lost his fishing gear and other belongings along the way. Alas that the fish escaped!

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Mosco's missing goods are scattered around the Pond and the area nearby. If you read the note he gave you, perhaps there will be clues to the exact whereabouts of his gear.

You should collect Mosco's missing goods and return them to him.Find Mosco's lucky baitFind Mosco's fishing poleFind Mosco's hoeFind Mosco's cloakFind Mosco's elevenses mealMosco Smallburrow is at the Bywater Pond, waiting for you to return with his found belongings.

You should return Mosco's belongings to him.'You will never, ever believe what happened to me today. I wrote it all down as soon as I recovered, just to make sure I captured every detail. Are you ready to hear this? Good.

'I caught a giant fish. So giant that it would not fit in my burrow if I were to bring it home for dinner.

'Don't believe me, do you? Well, he dragged me all over, and I lost everything I own! How do you explain that, eh? Speaking of, I would appreciate it very much if you could help me find all of my belongings. Here is the story of my day -- perhaps it will give you clues to where my gear has got to.''Don't believe me, eh? Just wait til you see how far and wide my things were scattered while I was wrestling with the fish. It's all there in the note I gave you.''Did you see how far that great giant fish threw me with all of my belongings? Surely you believe me now. I'm going to try to catch that beast, if it's the last thing I do!'Many are those who seek true love -- few are those who find it.There are those who seem to find you quite attractive!Collect berries for the hungry cave-claw.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>You should collect berries in the Treasure Field for the hungry cave-claw.This cave-claw looks hungry. You should collect berries for it.The hungry cave-claw looks less hungry.You have acquired a lovely collection of beetles.You have acquired a lovely collection of beetles.Call the Blue Beetle to your sideCall the Green Beetle to your sideCall the Red Beetle to your sideThere's no achievement so great as catching a big, heavy old fish. Catching too many puny fish, however, makes one question one's abilities as a fisherman.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Fish (both big and small) can be caught at the Fishing Hole in Bywater.

You should try to catch many big fish without catching many small fish. Too many small fish will cause your luck to fail!Catch big fish (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Don't catch little fish (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bollo Bolger is near the Fishing Hole in Bywater.

You should speak with Bollo Bolger and show him the large, impressive fish you caught.Speak with Bollo Bolger'I do love to fish! Who doesn't? It's a fascinating sport, riveting, with all of that nasty competition. Why, just the other day I caught an enormous fish, while those around me who were partaking in the event could catch naught but little fish.

'The jealous looks they gave me were as savoury as a stack of Mushroom Pies.

'What sort of fisherman are you, ${PLAYER}? Do you catch big fish, or are you more inclined to catch puny, stunted, useless little things?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The outcome of this quest is based on luck, and is not affected by fishing skill.</rgb>'I am excited to see if you'll be giving or receiving jealous glances from your neighbours, ${PLAYER}.''Hey! You must be cheating. Those fish are even bigger than the ones I caught. What's your secret? Worm bait? Sandwich bait? Come on, out with it!

'Pooh. I see how it'll be. Well, I shall gladly challenge you again tomorrow. Someday, my luck will be better than yours....'Bilbo left a letter to the inhabitants of his beloved Shire in the hands of Hamfast Gamgee, affectionately known by neighbours as the Gaffer.

