You should bring Bilbo's parting letter to Lobelia, for it may give some insight into the locked cellar of Bag End.Lobelia Sackville-Baggins is up at Bag End, north of the Party Tree upon the Hill.

You should talk to Lobelia about Bilbo's letter.Prod Lobelia for informationLobelia is taking too long to read the letter. You should prod her for information.Prod Lobelia for informationLobelia is taking too long to read the letter. You should prod her for information.Prod Lobelia for informationLobelia is taking too long to read the letter. You should prod her for information.Prod Lobelia for information'Still here, are you? Well, I suppose if you are of an inquisitive nature like Mr. Bilbo himself, I'll let you in on something he said to me afore he disappeared forever.

'Old Bilbo, he said (with a sparkle in his eye) that his adventure would continue on even after he was long gone. That was Mr. Baggins, for you.

'Well, I'll not get in your way. Help yourself to look over his last letter for us, which my son Sam read to me. It has some particular instructions regarding that Sackville-Baggins....''You want to bring this letter to Lobelia, eh? Be my guest. It won't do a whit of good sitting here with me, you know.''If you're looking for that old weasel Lobelia, she's a few steps north of here. You can surely find her at Bag End, quarrelling about anything she can think of.''What is that envelope you have there? Give it here at once! I am sure Bilbo meant for the successor of Bag End to have it, and not that fool old gardener. Indeed no; I don't believe he even knows how to read.''I'm reading the letter. Leave me be! How is a hobbit to concentrate with annoying folk badgering them all day?

