Rodwen has asked to meet you outside the throne room, and away from listening ears. For what purpose does the expert wedding-planner seek this secret meeting?Talk to Rodwen up some stairs north of the Tower of Ecthelion, beyond a doorway spanned by a flower garland, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)'${PLAYER}, my friend! I am pleased you could return to my city in time of peace, with war safely behind us! We cannot lower our guard overmuch, it is true, but Mithrandir and the Council of Gondor both assure me that the threat of further war is at a low ebb, for now. My mind therefore turns from martial matters to those of the heart, for a day long prepared is nearly upon us. As you well know, Arwen my betrothed travels even now to Minas Tirith, where we shall be wedded before all of Gondor, and she will be the queen of my kingdom.

'Long have we waited for this day! It is very important to me and to my love that the ceremony be conducted properly, but my knowledge of such matters is not sufficient. Mithrandir insists that he has an understanding of the rituals, but some members of the Council questioned the depth of his knowledge concerning the customs of Gondor. The Council therefore selected a number of Gondorian representatives to decorate the city and make ready the ceremony. The woman responsible for the wedding ceremony is named Rodwen, and I would ask you to lend her your able assistance, if you have the time and the inclination.

'Arwen will be here soon with her household, and I want all the preparations to be made before she arrives.''The Council selected a Gondorian representative to make ready the ceremony and other preparations. Her name is Rodwen, and I would ask you to lend her your able assistance, if you have the time and the inclination.

'Arwen will be here soon with her household, and I want all the preparations to be made before she arrives.''Yes, hello. ${PLAYER}, is it? Hmmm... I see. You are to help me make ready the wedding ceremony? I assure you, we have things well in hand....'

Rodwen appears visibly nervous, and seems to be having some trouble meeting your gaze.

'Let us meet somewhere to discuss the preparations, ${PLAYER}. There is no point in disturbing the king with such details. Surely... surely you agree? Let us find a quiet spot to discuss them. If you leave the Tower of Ecthelion and turn north, you will see a doorway spanned by a garland of flowers. Slip past that garland and climb the steps to the wall... and that is where I will meet you.''Let us meet somewhere to discuss the preparations, ${PLAYER}. There is no point in disturbing the king with such details. Surely... surely you agree? Let us find a quiet spot to discuss them. If you leave the Tower of Ecthelion and turn north, you will see a doorway spanned by a garland of flowers. Slip past that garland and climb the steps to the wall... and that is where I will meet you.''I know you, ${PLAYER}. I have heard of your many heroic deeds, and word of your adventures has spread throughout the land. Is it true you can read the truth in someone's face despite their words? It is true, isn't it?'

Rodwen's face is pale, and you need no special ability to determine how nervous she is in your presence.

'Then I will just tell you, for you are sure to find it out anyway! I was an adventurer-for-hire, a champion of Gondor. My friends and I sought to earn coin by lending our swords and our skills to folk in need, but... we weren't very good at it. Our guardian Drafli was more brave than sensible, our minstrel Cuilinn never did learn the value of silence when enemies were about, and I have waylaid my sword at inopportune moments... more than once, I confess it! When the war ended, we decided it was best for all if we were to leave the adventuring life behind us. Cuilinn took up farming, the dear fellow, but it was a short-lived experiment and he has left that behind too; it did not suit him either.

'So we all came to settle within the White City, and through a series of misunderstandings and some ill-advised boasting my friends and I caught the attention of the Council of Gondor. The next thing I know, our lore-master Isteron is speaking before those noble lords and ladies, insisting that we are expert wedding-planners all! What do I know about weddings? Little enough! So we have stumbled our way into something of a real adventure, ${PLAYER}, and if we cannot perfect this wedding ceremony we will be in real trouble! Will you help us?'Rodwen asked you to help her with the final preparations for the Great Wedding, and out of respect for the bride and the groom you have agreed to do what you can.Isteron is outside the Tower of Ecthelion, in the Plaza of the Fountain, in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).

Rodwen gave you some letters of introduction authorizing you to act on her behalf, and directed you to deliver them to her friend and ally Isteron.Two of the helpful hobbits that helped Isteron with some of the wedding preparations are relaxing nearby: Frodo Baggins and Samwise Gamgee!Find the helpful hobbits south of the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Two of the helpful hobbits that helped Isteron with some of the wedding preparations are relaxing nearby: Frodo Baggins and Samwise Gamgee!Talk to Frodo Baggins in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Talk to Samwise Gamgee in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Frodo and Sam suggested that you follow the smell of pipe-smoke to find Merry and Pippin.

Frodo and Sam provided some very helpful advice to Rodwen's wedding-planning friends, but Merry and Pippin seemed very amused about something, which strikes young Master Samwise as perhaps a troubling sign.Follow the smell of pipe-smoke to the south-west in order to find Merry and PippinFrodo and Sam suggested that you follow the smell of pipe-smoke to find Merry and Pippin.

Frodo and Sam provided some very helpful advice to Rodwen's wedding-planning friends, but Merry and Pippin seemed very amused about something, which strikes young Master Samwise as perhaps a troubling sign.Follow the smell of pipe-smoke to the south-east in order to find Merry and PippinMerry is atop the wall south-east of the Plaza of the Fountain in Minas Tirith (Midsummer), very pleased with some recent mischief.Talk to Meriadoc Brandybuck in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Pippin is atop the wall south-east of the Plaza of the Fountain in Minas Tirith (Midsummer), very pleased with some recent mischief.Talk to Peregrin Took in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Merry and Pippin, quite delighted with themselves, have caused some mischief. You should find Cúfaron at the base of the ramp from the Seventh Circle, in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer), and see if it is too late to undo their handiwork.Examine the fruit of the hobbit's mischief at the base of the ramp from the Seventh Circle, in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Legolas stands by the pile of blue decorations, and despite his solemn expression you can tell he is also rather amused at the hobbits' prank.Talk to Legolas in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Cúfaron is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).Talk to Cúfaron in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)'What a relief it is to hear you will help us! Every wedding should be perfect, of course, but the weight of responsibility for this particular wedding is even greater, for all the eyes of the kingdom will be upon it! It means a great deal to me that you will not betray our secret. With your help, it should not matter that my friends and I know so little about such preparations! Already I have sent them throughout the city to get whatever help they can.

'Here, ${PLAYER}, I have penned some letters of introduction authorizing you to work on my behalf in all wedding-related matters. Bring these to our lore-master Isteron and he will tell you how best you can help us. You should find him outside the Tower of Ecthelion, in the Plaza of the Fountain.''Bring those letters to our lore-master Isteron and he will tell you how best you can help us. You should find him outside the Tower of Ecthelion, in the Plaza of the Fountain.''Ah, you are here to help plan for the Great Wedding? There is so much still to be done, but do not let that frighten you away! I have often found that the largest tasks are the most rewarding, just so long as you do not give up before you are begun!'

You ask Isteron if he needs any help researching wedding customs, and he blinks at you, the smile frozen on his face.

'Oh no, I gave up on that,' he replies. 'Cúfaron and I did learn some interesting tidbits from a number of hobbits over there, but I did not find their advice very promising. Their hobbit-traditions felt very quaint to me, not at all appropriate for such a grand wedding as this must be, but you are welcome to consult with them, if you like. They are to the south of the Tower of Ecthelion, I believe.''You are welcome to consult with the hobbits who helped me, if you like. I believe they are to the south of the Tower of Ecthelion.''You are welcome to consult with the hobbits who helped me, if you like. I believe they are to the south of the Tower of Ecthelion.''${PLAYER}! How nice to see you during a time of celebration and not during time of war!'

You tell Frodo that you are helping Rodwen and her companions with the preparations for the Great Wedding, and he nods thoughtfully.

'That is very good of you. Aragorn is dear to me, and I want his wedding to be all for which he and his bride might hope. Are Rodwen and her companions up for such a challenge? I have spoken with a number of them now, and in each of these planners I admit to you I have recognized something.'

He smiles knowingly.

'They are in over their heads, just as I was during the Quest of the Ring! Just as were we all. Well, that turned out all right, in the end. So too might the wedding ceremony! If there is anything we can do, ${PLAYER}, let us know and we will help.''There has been a lot of wedding chatter in the air, ${PLAYER}, and I'll have you know it's not the easiest thing for this Gamgee to talk about! Take that Isteron fellow. He spoke on and on about how grand this wedding should be, and how it'll be talked about for years and years, and maybe that's so, but I can't help but wonder if that's not the most important thing. Maybe I'm just a hobbit, with hobbit-ideas, but it seems to me that the wedding should be just as Arwen and Strider want it to be. Does it matter what the kingdom thinks of it, or for how long it's talked about?'

Sam falls silent and sniffs the air.

'Actually, now that I'm thinking about it, Mister Frodo and I weren't the only hobbits who spoke to the wedding planners. Merry and Pippin talked to them too, and when they finished they went off laughing, looking very pleased with themselves about something. It might be worth looking into, ${PLAYER}. Those two are always causing trouble of some kind or another, and if you follow the smell of their pipe-smoke, could be you'll get to the bottom of it!''Sam is right. The more amused with themselves our friends are, the more trouble they are likely to cause! I do think they have probably settled down somewhere to have a smoke and review the mischief they might have caused.''If you ask me, I'd wager those two are having a smoke and laughing at their mischief! Follow the smell of their pipes, ${PLAYER}, to the south-west!''Sam is right. The more amused with themselves our friends are, the more trouble they are likely to cause! I do think they have probably settled down somewhere to have a smoke and review the mischief they might have caused.''If you ask me, I'd wager those two are having a smoke and laughing at their mischief! Follow the smell of their pipes, ${PLAYER}, to the south-west!''Good day to you, ${PLAYER}! Why don't you stay awhile and have a smoke, there's room for all! What's on your mind, friend?'

You ask Merry and Pippin about the preparations for the upcoming wedding, and they share a conspiratorial look before doubling-over with laughter. When Merry has once again caught his breath, he apologizes and tries to answer your question.

'It's going to be a real sight to see, ${PLAYER}! It seemed to us that those wedding planners might not have actually been to a real wedding before, and you know Pip and I have been to plenty. We're real experts on the subject, you might say, so we gave Cúfaron a detailed account of the most important Shire wedding-traditions. It was the right thing to do, wasn't it, Pip? How did they go again?''We're real experts on the subject, you might say, so we gave Cúfaron a detailed account of the most important Shire wedding-traditions. It was the right thing to do, wasn't it, Pip? How did they go again?''Well, Merry, everyone knows that in a Shire wedding you've got to follow the traditions. There are four elements that must be present if the ceremony is to be a success. The bride needs to carry or wear something old, right? And then she should pair it with something new, which represents the new life she's starting with her husband...'

Merry nods solemnly, which causes Pippin to break out into laughter again before resuming.

'...and then she needs something borrowed as well, maybe a garment or a cloth or a small pocket item of some kind, and then, most important of all... everything has to be blue!'

The two hobbits start laughing again, and through their gales of laughter you can just make out gasps of 'everything blue! All the decorations, everything, they've got to be blue!''Something old, something new, something borrowed... and everything blue!

'I think he was going to collect everything in the Sixth Circle, ${PLAYER}, right by the base of the ramp from the Seventh!''Something old, something new, something borrowed, everything blue!''Not everyone is as familiar with our hobbits as we are, ${PLAYER}.'Legolas speaks solemnly, but the son of Thranduil cannot completely mask his amusement.

'Not everyone is as familiar with hobbits as we are, ${PLAYER}. Am I right to suggest that this must be the doing of a certain Brandybuck and Took of our acquaintance?'A faint smile flits across the Elf's face as he contemplates the pile of decorations, but he says nothing more.'Those hobbits weren't really wedding experts at all, were they?' he asks, staring wearily at the pile of blue decorations gathered from all around the city.

'Not really experts at all. There's a lot of that going around these days.'Cúfaron is trying to sort out the good advice he received from Merry and Pippin from the bad. He hopes their words concerning 'Gandalf's fireworks' can be believed.Mithrandir is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).

Cúfaron is hopeful that some of Merry and Pippin's chatter may have had a kernel of truth, and he wants you to find the wizard of whose fireworks they spoke.Talk to Mithrandir in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Mithrandir told you he has assembled quite a stock of fireworks during the days following the end of the war, and he keeps them in a crate in his quarters in the High Guest-house, located in the Seventh Circle.Find Gandalf's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer)The crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle.

Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!Take fireworks out of the crateThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle.

Mithrandir did not specify which of the fireworks to bring to him. Better take everything out of the crate, just to be safe!Take more fireworks out of the crateThe crate of fireworks is in Mithrandir's quarters in the High Guest-house in the Seventh Circle.

