You can acquire these quests from the Umbar Woodworker's Guild Leader in the Umbar Baharbêl craft guild hall.Complete Umbar Woodworker's Guild daily orders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You completed many Umbar woodworker requests.CompletedComplete daily quotas for the Umbar Woodworker's Guild.You have completed many Umbar Woodworker deliveries!Breakfast is the most important meal of the day -- and you believe in starting the day right.Eggs and OnionsComplete Hobbit BreakfastDelicious Crispy BaconHobbiton OmeletBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance to the Men of Bree.'Would you like to level up your rep with the Men of Bree?''Alright, soon the Men of Bree will consider you an Acquaintance. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Men of Bree.'Would you like to level up your rep with the Men of Bree?''Alright, soon you will be a Friend of the Men of Bree. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Men of Bree.'Would you like to level up your rep with the Men of Bree?''Alright, soon you will be an Ally of the Men of Bree. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred to the Men of Bree.'Would you like to level up your rep with the Men of Bree?''Alright, soon you will be Kindred to the Men of Bree. Ready?'Explore Bree-land and locate Chicken Stones.Enter session play.Enter session play.Explore Bree-land and locate Chicken Stones.Discover The Prancing Pony Chicken StoneDiscover the Old Forest Chicken StoneDiscover the Othrongroth Chicken StoneSpeak with creatures in Bree-landEnter session play as a chicken.Enter session playTravel to Bree-land and speak with the cow, the horse, the grey squirrel, Wink the cat, and Sniken the Neekerbreeker.Speak with the cowSpeak with the grey squirrelSpeak with Wink the catSpeak with SnikenSpeak with the horse'Would like one of these delectable mice, rooster? You do not eat rodents? Oh my, how uncouth! No wonder the wolves wish to eat you.''It is true, I have become weary of training these flea-ridden horses of Bree-land and would welcome a fight. But my master has not called me to battle, and so I will not come.''They will perish, I tell you! We cannot allow the red squirrels to continue in this world. They are weak! Are you with me?''Oh, I wish these fool hobbits would just bring me a ramp. At least then I could be off of this roof!''Get me out of this cage, chicken! I cannot take anymore of this madman's ravings!'Defeat many brigands in Swanfleet.Defeat many brigands in Swanfleet.Defeat many brigands in SwanfleetDefeat many brigands in Swanfleet.Defeat many brigands in Swanfleet.Defeat many brigands in SwanfleetYou ate several of Keteph's crab on barley sandwiches.Eat Keteph's Crab on BarleyA dwarf called Brútha the Wayward has approached you with a proposition regarding her toy-making business.If you've decided to accept Brútha the Wayward's request, you should talk to her at your home.Talk to Brútha the Wayward'Hello, hello, my friend! I'm seeking someplace to practice my woodworking and start my toy-making business. Would you be willing to help me? I'd be happy to pay you, of course.

'What do you say?''And so begins our partnership. You won't regret this, I promise!'Brútha looks towards the future.You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 10'You should talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.Talk to Brútha'${PLAYER}, hello, hello! Care to join me on a walk?

'Snítha's been asking plenty of questions about trees. My knowledge lies with the wood, not the entire tree. But I thought, why not gather some seeds to grow together? Then I'll learn more about the materials I work with.''Let's go!''${PLAYER}, I was able to finish my carving. Hold on -- '

After rummaging around in her pockets for a bit, Brútha pulls out a small, wooden bird.

'Take it. It's for you.' She grins her toothy grin. 'We dwarves have long memories, and I won't forget that you gave me what I needed: someone to believe in me, and a bit of space to do what I wanted to do. Not even my home had either of those things. If it weren't for you, Snítha and I would still be fighting, I'm sure.

'Thank you again. From the bottom of my heart.'Finding herself fresh out of wood for whittling, Brútha has invited you on an outing to collect more.You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.

Speak with Brútha at your home.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 2'You should talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.Talk to Brútha'Hello, hello! I was about to collect some more wood. For whittling, that is. After all, I won't be able to get my business started without more examples of my work.

'Join me?''This will be fun!''Can't talk right now. I finally have the wood I need and too many ideas!'Brútha is ready to spread the word about her business -- and you're just the right person to help her.You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.

Speak with Brútha at your home.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 3'You should talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.Talk to Brútha'${PLAYER}, just the person I was looking for! I've created enough toys to show examples of my wares; now I've got to spread the word...'

She grimaces, and her beard droops to follow the movement.

'This calls for a day in town. I'd appreciate the help, if you'd be so kind to come along.'Brútha sighs heavily as the two of you prepare to leave.'Nothing to do but to wait. Everything we've done has to pay off eventually, right?'With skill, help, and a little luck, Brútha has secured her first patron.You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.

Speak with Brútha at your home.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 4'You should talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.Talk to Brútha'${PLAYER}, ${PLAYER}! One of the townsfolk has asked me to craft a toy for her daughter! She's invited me to their home to discuss the matter.

'Would you come with me? It's just that -- well I don't know what will happen! This is my first time doing something like this, starting a project for coin.

'I can tell her you're... er... my business associate?''Let's be off, quickly!''I can scarcely believe my luck. No need to go collecting wood in the forest anymore -- I've got a steady supply! Well, I'll still go out to the forest to collect pieces, on occasion. It's something I enjoy doing very much.

'Before this all started, if you'd told me I'd have folks helping me and buying my crafts, I wouldn't have believed you. This almost feels like a real business now.'A surprising opportunity may have fallen into Brútha's lap, though who is this potential partner?You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.

Speak with Brútha at your home.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 5'You should talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.Try and talk to Brútha'${PLAYER}, someone's reached out to discuss a potential arrangement! Though, they weren't very forthcoming with details, only that they'd like to meet in-person at the Burnwater House.

'You'll come, won't you? Whatever we discuss might be draining -- well, no, it will be. It'd be good to have a friendly face in the room.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Brútha remains uncharacteristically reticent.

You leave her to her thoughts.Brútha had promised to tell you everything, and she's not one to take friends for granted.You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.

Speak with Brútha at your home.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 6'You should talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.Talk to BrúthaBrútha gives you a half-hearted wave in greeting.

'Spare a moment, ${PLAYER}?

'I wanted to tell you about my family. It's a dour topic, so I thought we'd go and feed some birds while we're at it. The birdseed's ready; just let me know when you'd like to go.''I hope those birds are hungry!''Well, I've spent enough time complaining. Time to get back to carving -- that toy for Astrith won't finish itself!'Though Brútha is ready to deliver Astrith's toy, Aslaug's reaction may colour the whole visit.You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 7'You should talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.Talk to Brútha'${PLAYER}, I've just put the finishing touches on Astrith's toy. Er... would you come with me to deliver it? I'm not sure how her mother will react.''I hope Aslaug won't be too angry with me...''Now that was a satisfying project, but I hope the next one isn't as complicated. Not that I had any trouble with the actual woodworking -- I meant dealing with people. We can be so difficult, can't we?'Every endeavour worth doing has its downsides, and Brútha knows that better than most.You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 8'You should talk to Brútha.Try and talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.'As much as I hate to admit it, there haven't been many patrons lately. We'll have to go back to town. To do what we did last time, I mean.

'Well, at least I'll have you for company. That's not so bad!''Let's get to work.'Even after leaving the Burnwater House, Brútha keeps to herself.To Brútha's surprise, Snítha has reached out to talk.You should talk to Brútha to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Brútha the Wayward, Chapter 9'You should talk to Brútha near the stable-master in Lake-town or at your home.Talk to Brútha'Snítha wrote. She wants to meet back at the Burnwater House. For a chat, that is. About...' 

Brútha gestures vaguely around her. 

'Everything.

'Nothing's going to change, you already know that. But as long as I drag this out, Snítha will continue to hound me.${PLAYER}, you'll step in if things get bad, won't you? Well, not if, but when.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I'll need all the help I can get.''I had a pleasant conversation with my sister. This isn't a dream, is it? I hope it isn't; I tried very hard to be nice to her. Hah, only joking.

'I just... didn't think this could ever happen. But it has, somehow -- thanks to you!

'Maybe things can get better between us.'Merkhâma is interested in having sand-castles built on the beaches of Furtherholm.You have accepted a commission to construct four sand-castles on the beach to add to the festive atmosphere.Build sand-castles on the beach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have fulfilled your obligation to build sand-castles on Furtherholm's beaches. You should return to Merkhâma outside of The Cracked Flagon to get your reward.Talk to Merkhâma'Tell me, my friend, have you ever heard of a sand-castle? Aye, it sounds strange to construct a fortress of just sand, but this is only for show, not protection. I have sailed many seas, they are real, I have seen them. Imagine if it were for tiny people yea tall.'

The woman holds two fingers about an inch apart and looks at you through them.

'If you want more of that coin for bartering, build me four castles of sand on beaches where other visitors will see them. It will add to the festive mood, I think.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'You are a very capable castle builder! Your method is flawless. Unfortunately, such fortresses rarely withstand the tides, and they all will likely need to be rebuilt tomorrow.'The most popular part of the Shire's Spring Festival is the consumption of large quantities of beer, especially Bullroarer's Brew.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>The Greenfields are north of Brockenborings in the Shire.

Sigismond North-took has asked that you collect clover used for making Bullroarer's Brew.Collect clover  (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sigismond North-took is in Brockenborings, south of the Greenfields.

You should bring the clover you collected to Sigismond North-took.'Welcome! Are you here to pay your respects to the Bullroarer? Bandobras 'Bullroarer' Took...he is my ancestor, you know, and the greatest hero of the Shire. A long time ago, an army of goblins invaded the Shire...goblins, of all things!  

'Well, the Bullroarer, he wouldn't stand for it, no sir. He gathered all the Tooks and other brave hobbits he could muster and rode out on his horse against them. You heard me right, ${PLAYER}, a horse, a full-growed horse! The Bullroarer was four-foot-five, as the family records tell, and could ride a horse just like the Big Folk.

'Every spring we honour his memory by holding The Feast of the Greenfields. We usually place tankards of Bullroarer's Brew, Bandobras's favourite drink around his statue, but so many folk have come out this season that we are completely out of clover, one of the main ingredients. You wouldn't be able to go out and get us more clover, would you, my good ${RACE}? The clover only grows on the Greenfields, north of Brockenborings.''This is my favourite holiday!''You gathered the clover we need? Excellent! We should have more Bullroarer's Brew in no time!'Sigismond North-took has invited you to participate in the Bullroarer's Challenge in Brockenborings.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>The Challenge Field is located just east of Brockenborings.

To participate in the Bullroarer's Challenge, Tobias Brockhouse told you to stand on the starting platform, pick up your official Bullroarer's Challenge brew tankard, toast to Bandobras's health, and make it across the fence to the other platform, where Belgo is standing, before time runs out.Toast to Bandobras's HealthDo not fall off the fenceSigismond North-took is in Brockenborings.

Speak with Sigismond North-took to claim your prize.'Sigismond North-took sent you to participate in the Bullroarer's Challenge, did he?

'The game's origin dates back to Bandobras Took himself. Every morning, it is said, he would run atop the fences of the Great Smials to stay in shape and hone his reflexes.

'Simply stand on the starting platform, pick up your official Bullroarer's Challenge brew tankard, toast to Bandobras's health, and make it across the fence to the other platform, where Belgo is standing, before time runs out. Good luck, ${PLAYER}!''Good luck to you!''You did it! I never doubted you for a moment, ${PLAYER}! You have truly honoured the spirit of Bandobras Took.'Sigismond North-took has invited you to participate in the Bullroarer's Challenge in Brockenborings.

