ekObtain a Map of Nud-melekObtain a map of the Foundations of StoneObtain a map of the Redhorn LodesObtain a Map of ZirakzigilObtain a map of the Flaming DeepsObtain a map of the Grand StairMany stray cats have made the Furtherholm harbour their home. What should be done about them?Maghôrdo is unsure of what to do about the cats. He has asked for your opinion - should they stay or should they go?Complete Quest: Yes to CatsComplete Quest: No to CatsMaghôrdo asked for your opinion on what should be done about Furtherholm's cats. You made a decision and acted accordingly. You should report to Maghôrdo at Furtherholm's harbour, near the waterfall.Talk to Maghôrdo'${PLAYER}, you may have noticed many cats about the harbour. I am not sure what to do about them. Among my people, cats are believed to bring good luck. No Umbari dromund would dare sail without one. To do so would bring bad fortune to any voyage!

'But it seems that among our visitors, not everyone appreciates cats as they should. Some people have complained, calling them pests, and one man claims they make him sneeze!

'My friend, you are a visitor. What say you? Should they stay or should they go?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Ah, you return for your reward!

'Do you think that was the correct decision, ${PLAYER}? Anyway, I do not doubt that the same choice will have to be made again tomorrow. Cats are inevitable.'Many stray cats have made the Furtherholm harbour their home, and you think they should go.Maghôrdo has asked you to visit each cat in Furtherholm's harbour area and shoo them away.Shoo the scruffy catShoo the slinky catShoo the skinny catShoo the smelly catShoo the sleepy catShoo the sassy catYou have shoo'd away each cat in Furtherholm's harbour. You should report to Maghôrdo at Furtherholm's harbour, near the waterfall.Return to Maghôrdo'You think the cats should go? I hate to admit it, but I think you are correct. It would be for the best. The Captain charged me with making this island as agreeable as possible for visitors, and if visitors object to the cats then it is my duty to see them gone.

'Just shooing them away from the harbour would do. ${PLAYER}, I do not wish to do this thing myself. If you do this in my stead, I will compensate you.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Many stray cats have made the Furtherholm harbour their home, and you think they should stay.Maghôrdo has asked you to visit each cat in Furtherholms harbour area and give them a bite to eat.Feed the scruffy catFeed the slinky catFeed the skinny catFeed the smelly catFeed the sleepy catFeed the sassy catYou have given each cat in Furtherholm's harbour area a bite to eat. You should report to Maghôrdo at Furtherholm's harbour, near the waterfall.Return to Maghôrdo'You think the cats should stay? I am relieved to hear it! Removing them may invite disaster to strike!

'Besides, you cannot always make everyone happy. I have also heard of places rife with cats that travellers visit specifically to see them! I would visit such a place myself, ${PLAYER}.

'Now that I think of it, I will reward you if you go around the harbour and give a tidbit to each cat, to ensure they stay. Everyone knows if you feed a cat, they will always return.'

