Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.Talk to Prince Ingór'Bah! Look at this hall! I know we just moved in, but it is still a mess! How are we supposed to welcome travellers from near and far when Vérnozal is still filled with dust and debris? Visitors from nearby will take one look and return to where they came from, and visitors from far away will curse us for our lack of hospitality!

'${PLAYER}, you must assist the Zhélruka and remove the broken crates and piles of debris from Vérnozal.''${PLAYER}, you must assist the Zhélruka and remove the broken crates and piles of debris from Vérnozal.''Good work! The hall is more welcoming already, and visitors will not be immediately consumed with disgust! That is an improvement. Now then, what else does Vérnozal need? Hmm....

'It is a bit dim in here. Now that we would not be illuminating broken crates and dusty corners, we should brighten it up! Collect some coal in Vérnozal and add it to the braziers for me.''Ah, you are right, it is a bit dim in here. We should brighten it up! Collect some coal in Vérnozal and add it to the braziers for me.''Ah, you are right, it is a bit dim in here. We should brighten it up! Collect some coal in Vérnozal and add it to the braziers for me.''Yes, this is quite a bit better! Now, what else is missing? Hmm....

'Ah, there is nothing in this hall that welcomes travellers and notifies them that this hall belongs to the mighty Zhélruka Clan!

'A banner or two should suffice! Take these Zhélruka Clan banners and hang them in Vérnozal.''Ah yes, this hall proudly proclaims that it belongs to the Zhélruka now.

'What is that? You believe that raising Zhélruka banners may not be the most welcoming of sights for a newly-arrived traveller? The Zhélruka symbol is a symbol of honour!'

Prince Ingór takes a moment to regain his composure.

'Hmm, I suppose if Gundabad is to be our home, then the Zhélruka must acknowledge that it is to be a home for others as well. I do have one Longbeard banner here. Take it and hang it somewhere prominent. It will do for now.''Look how welcoming that one Longbeard banner makes the hall feel! Are you sure it helps?

'I am very welcoming, with or without a banner, but if you think the banner is important, I will see that it stays. Now that we have made the hall of Vérnozal more inviting, perhaps you should put some of your other skills to use and assist Ausma and Hórin with a mission.''Thank you for assisting Ausma and Hórin with a mission. You have done much today. Still, more remains to be done. For now I will think on how we can make Vérnozal more inviting to all.'You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.

