Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.Talk to Prince Ingór'${PLAYER}, I must speak with you. There are rumours in the hall that a group of Longbeard explorers has gone missing while excavating a perilous cavern. Apparently one of the old tunnels gave way and the dwarves did not return. I believe they might be trapped, but still alive. We must search for them and assist the Longbeards!''Quickly now, we must hurry! If they remain alive, those Longbeards may not have much longer!''Ah, you have returned! I have heard of your success and the safe return of the Longbeard explorers! You have done well to strengthen the bond between all the dwarves in Gundabad.

'I believe we can do more, however! Let us send those explorers a gift to show that the Zhélruka are just as pleased as any Longbeard at their safe return. Some ales, bread, and draughts should do nicely! We can present this package to the Longbeard emissary before he departs.''The care package has been delivered? Good, good! You have done well today, my friend.''Let us send those explorers a gift to show that the Zhélruka are just as pleased as any Longbeard at their safe return. Some ales, bread, and draughts should do nicely! We can present this package to the Longbeard emissary before he departs.''Let us send those explorers a gift to show that the Zhélruka are just as pleased as any Longbeard at their safe return. Some ales, bread, and draughts should do nicely! We can present this package to the Longbeard emissary before he departs.''Ah, thank you for this care package. I am sure that the Longbeards you rescued will be honoured to receive such a gift! My personal thanks for all that you have done, ${CLASS}.'You have pledged to lend your aid and your adventuring skills to the Zhélruka and to fight on their behalf in Gundabad.Vérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset.

