You have gathered the charms and flowers. Return to Thorían.Talk to ThoríanConstruct the handfasting cordsCelairel is south of Duillond.

Bring the handfasting cords to Celairel.'Demand is high this year for handfasting cords. My usual artisan has already passed into the West. Any help you could provide would be much appreciated.

'Make your way up the hill to Central Duillond and speak with the master tailor, Thorían. She should have a box of cords for me.''Wedding cords? Ai, I knew I was forgetting something! You’ll have to pardon me, I’ve been awake for many days working on wedding garments. Everyone always waits until the last moment to put in their orders!

'Listen, if you could help me out, it’d be wonderful. You look like you’ve sliced up a thing or two in your time. Brethilas has a shipment of silk bolts I ordered. If you could collect the bolt from his store, you can use the table here to cut it into strips.''These ribbons look exquisite. Ah, my silk merchant always has the finest fabrics. I was right to think you to be good with a blade. Ah, not so fast!

'The cords still need some work. You’ll have to visit the metalsmith, Dringlaer, for charms, and we’ll need fresh flowers to braid into them as well. We haven't the time to send you to Lothlórien for elanor, but Duillond has its fair share of lovely offerings. When you have the charms and blossoms, return to me and I shall teach you how to braid them all together.''Charms? I do indeed have Thorían's order. Always one of my favourite things to work on. Finely detailed treasures, these. Symbols of eternal love and devotion. It’s nice to be working on something other than armour and blades for a bit.''Great! These charms look amazing. He always does such detailed work. Right, let’s get these made up.'

She takes a few strands and shows you how to braid the silk ribbons, charms and flowers together.

'Go ahead and use that table again. I’ve made room for you there. When you’re done, you can bring them straight to Celairel.''Thanks for your help. Come back tomorrow. I'll probably have more for you to do.'To ensure that the sapling is not recovered and that it twists to the will of Angmar, Cinaid wishes you to eliminate the Free People to ensure that their search for the sapling is for naught.Cinaid wants you to make your way into the Ettenmoors and eliminate the Free Folk that wander there looking to assist the saplings. Slaughter them all!Find and slaughter free-folk (${NUMBER}/15)With a good number of free-folk slain, you should return to Gramsfoot and inform Cinaid of your efforts.'The discovery of these shivering little saplings drives the Free Folk and our army into the field of battle. We search for signs of these creatures. We tread where we want and will crush the enemy to collect what we desire. Find the enemy. Stop them from maintaining the natural order.''Go to the Ettenmoors and seek out the Free-folk there. Slaughter all that you find.''Your success against the enemy is known to the War-tyrant! We will find these saplings. We will breed an army of corrupt nature that will eradicate the Free Folk!'Ailward Chubb is confused as to why four dwarves have recently left the Inn League without so much as a word. He does not know it, but you harassed them on behalf of the Ale Association. You should make reparations if you wish to do your duty to the Inn League.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Óli is at Thorin's Hall, Kópur is at Noglond, Grímar is at Gondamon, and Herluf is in Needlehole.

You must make reparations for your unkind behaviour towards the four dwarves who abandoned the Inn League at your behest.Help regain Óli's trustHelp regain Kópur's trustHelp regain Grímar's trustHelp regain Herluf's trustAilward Chubb is at the Party Tree in Hobbiton.

You should return to Ailward Chubb where he can restore his records of the dwarves being members of the Inn League, not the Ale Association.Talk to Ailward Chubb at the Party Tree'I was checking my records the other day, and it seems we've actually lost some members! I can't understand why four dwarves would up and leave without so much as a word.

'There are rumours of a dwarf society called the Ale Association. I wonder if they had anything to do with it.

'If you could do some investigating for me and, you know, find out what may have gone wrong with those dwarves, that would be wonderful. You should encourage them to re-join the Inn League! I cannot fathom the need for two drink-appreciation societies....''I still can't imagine why those dwarves would leave. They seemed so excited to join us!''Well done! How odd, that someone would harass them until they abandoned their friends in the Inn League. Who would do such a mean thing?

'Ah well. I guess we'll never know.'Ailward Chubb is confused as to why four dwarves have recently left the Inn League without so much as a word. He does not know it, but you harassed them on behalf of the Ale Association. You should make reparations if you wish to do your duty to the Inn League.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Lóthinn is in the cellar of Thorin's Hall, selling various healing goods and potions that improve morale.

You should see if Lóthinn has any sugared honeysuckle, for it was rumoured that he occasionally carried some in his inventory.See if Lóthinn has any sugared honeysuckleGamall the cook is in the Maker's Hall, inside of Thorin's Hall.

You should speak with Gamall to see if he might be able to give you the sugared honeysuckle he bought.See if Gamall has any sugared honeysuckleHeikki Goldwatcher is in the main Hall of Thorin's Hall.

You should speak with Heikki Goldwatcher, for he was the one that re-bought the sugared honeysuckle from Gamall the cook.See if Heikki Goldwatcher has the sugared honeysuckleDwalin is in Thorin's Hall, standing at the end of the Hall.

You should see if Dwalin still has the sugared honeysuckle candies, given to him by a dwarf who hoped to earn his favour.See if Dwalin has the sugared honeysuckleLaufar is in the cellar of Thorin's Hall, standing with Óli.

You should bring the sugared honeysuckle to Laufar as a gesture of reparation for your cruel behaviour to Óli.'You again! I saw everything! Óli will not speak to you now because you were so mean to him before. He has been moping ever since, poor fellow.

'But the Inn League sent you this time? You will have your work cut out for you if you wish to win him back. I'll give you a tip: my good friend Óli has a sweet tooth, and his favourite candy is sugared honeysuckle.

'I know that Lóthinn occasionally gets orders of honeysuckle candies in his inventory. You should talk to him, and see if you can make a present of them to poor old Óli.''You should try to find sugared honeysuckle for dear old Óli. He is very sad, and they might cheer him up enough for him to listen to you again.''Sadly, I do not have any sugared honeysuckle at this time. It is a rare treat, and the last jar was bought from me not long ago, by Gamall the cook, who said he wanted to use them in a special recipe.

'You could see if Gamall has used them yet.''The sugared honeysuckle? No, I do not have it anymore. I... used it in a recipe. Where is the finished dish? All right, you caught me! I did not cook with it. I merely gave it away and took credit for the recipe. Heikki Goldwatcher bought them from me. He wanted something home-made and sweet. Do not tell him!''Yes, I bought the sugared honeysuckle, and for quite the price too! Gamall's dishes are not cheap. But I wanted to give a special gift to Dwalin. I think he will look favourably upon me when it is time for promotions, you see. And who doesn't love candy?''Sugared honeysuckle? Yes, I have it. Hate the stuff. If you want it, it's yours! I was going to throw it away.''I can't believe it! How did you manage to find sugared honeysuckle at this time of year? I will give this to Óli for you. I'm sure he can be persuaded to join the friendly hobbits of the Inn League once again.'Ailward Chubb is confused as to why four dwarves have recently left the Inn League without so much as a word. He does not know it, but you harassed them on behalf of the Ale Association. You should make reparations if you wish to do your duty to the Inn League.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Kópur is in Noglond, and his friend Karli is with him.

You should <rgb=#FF0000>perform silly tricks</rgb> for Kópur to make him warm up to you again. Karli might have suggestions as to how best to cheer him up.Try to cheer up KópurKópur is in Noglond, and his friend Karli is with him.

You should <rgb=#FF0000>perform silly tricks</rgb> for Kópur to make him warm up to you again. Karli might have suggestions as to how best to cheer him up.Try to cheer up KópurKópur is in Noglond, and his friend Karli is with him.

You should <rgb=#FF0000>perform silly tricks</rgb> for Kópur to make him warm up to you again. Karli might have suggestions as to how best to cheer him up.Try to cheer up KópurKópur is in Noglond, and his friend Karli is with him.

You should <rgb=#FF0000>perform silly tricks</rgb> for Kópur to make him warm up to you again. Karli might have suggestions as to how best to cheer him up.Try to cheer up KópurKarli is in Noglond.

You should speak with Karli now that you have successfully cheered up his friend Kópur.Talk to Karli at Noglond'Kópur will not speak with you at this time. It will take a lot of persuading to convince him not to hate you for your cruel behaviour towards him, you know. You made him very, very sad.

'If you come on behalf of the Inn League, I will tell you how to rouse him, if you wish. I like the Inn League, but I do not care for the Ale Association. Apparently you have seen the folly of your ways and come back to the better society.

'If you want Kópur to rally his spirits, you have to try to amuse him a bit. Poke him, make him laugh, amuse him as best you can. See if you can get a chuckle out of him.''Do you know how to <rgb=#FF0000>stand upside-down?</rgb> Kópur is usually impressed by such tricks. You could try that on him.''Why don't you give him a little <rgb=#FF0000>jab with your finger?</rgb> He is known to be very ticklish. Go ahead, give him a nudge.''How strange that he hasn't come out of his sour mood yet! Maybe he wants to hear <rgb=#FF0000>that you have seen the error of your ways.</rgb> A good, heartfelt apology goes a long way.''Terrible! He is as stubborn a mule as I ever met. I would have forgiven you ages ago. He probably wants you to <rgb=#FF0000>get him flowers and take him out for dinner, for goodness sake.</rgb> I swear, it is easier to <rgb=#FF0000>woo wilful ladies</rgb> than it is to shake this fellow out of his baleful mood.''You've done it! I forgot to mention that Kópur just melts when folks pay special attention to him. Your flirting did the trick. Why, he is so cheerful now that I do believe he has all but completely forgotten the nasty business with the Ale Association. Well done, well done.'Ailward Chubb is confused as to why four dwarves have recently left the Inn League without so much as a word. He does not know it, but you harassed them on behalf of the Ale Association. You should make reparations if you wish to do your duty to the Inn League.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Ingredients for a hand-crafted card can be found inside of Gondamon and in the wilds just outside the dwarf-waypost.

You should collect scrap paper, gold-dust from an ore-deposit, and sap from a pine tree which will serve as glue.Collect shavings of gold-dust from an ore-depositCollect sap from a pine treeCollect scrap paperA good, sturdy crafting table can be found in Gondamon.

You should use the crafting table to assemble the glitter, glue, and paper into a nice card for Grímar.Grímar and Ísólfur are waiting in Gondamon.

You should deliver Grímar's cheer-up card to Ísólfur.'Why, hello. You're that mean ${RACE} that hurt my poor friend Grímar's feelings. Are you back to spread the nasty message of the Ale Association?

'No, I see that you represent the Inn League this time. Odd, but I am glad for it. Grímar is very shaken by how abominably you treated him, but I think he would like some encouragement to join with the hobbits' society again.

'All right. I've decided you're trustworthy again. But Grímar gets awfully stuck in his bad moods. Hmm...I know what will cheer him up! A nice hand-made card -- something creative. Do you think you could do that for him?''I'm sure you can find all of the materials for a hand-crafted card around Gondamon, if you know where to look.''Look, Grímar! A hand-crafted card, just for you! See how it sparkles? It is made with real gold!'

Ísólfur turns his attention back to you.

'I do believe he likes it, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for coming to cheer him up. He hasn't been the same dwarf since that day you chastised him so harshly.'Ailward Chubb is confused as to why four dwarves have recently left the Inn League without so much as a word. He does not know it, but you harassed them on behalf of the Ale Association. You should make reparations if you wish to do your duty to the Inn League.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Pretty flowers can be found along the banks of the river north of Needlehole.

You should collect pretty flowers to present to Herluf.Collect pretty flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Herluf and Jafet are in Needlehole, in the Shire.

You should bring the flower-arrangement you collected to Jafet.'Poor old Herluf. He has been in a sad state ever since the last time you came by. I am glad you came back to make things right again.

'I believe a good handful of pretty wildflowers will do the trick. Flowers that grow around here are especially lovely, and I think they will cheer his heart and make him a happy dwarf again.

'The flowers grow along the riverbanks to the north of Needlehole, and you should see them if you follow the road that leads up to the Elf-lands.''I am sure some bright flowers from the riverbank will cheer Herluf in no time.''Flowers! Look, Herluf! Aren't they lovely?'This will increase your reputation with the Cook Craft Guild.Speak to Hob Longbottom.'Speak to me again to max out your reputation with the Cook Craft Guild.''Congrats, you can cook tasty things now.'This will increase your reputation with the Jeweller Craft Guild.Speak to Hob Longbottom.'Speak to me again to max out your reputation with the Jeweller Craft Guild.''Congrats, you can make really shiny rings now.'This will increase your reputation with the Metalsmith Craft Guild.Speak to Hob Longbottom.'Speak to me again to max out your reputation with the Metalsmith Craft Guild.''Congrats, you can make really metally swords now.'This will increase your reputation with the Scholar Craft Guild.Speak to Hob Longbottom.'Speak to me again to max out your reputation with the Scholar Craft Guild.''Congrats, you can make books with really good looking letters now.'This will increase your reputation with the Tailor Craft Guild.Speak to Hob Longbottom.'Speak to me again to max out your reputation with the Tailor Craft Guild.''Congrats, you can make shoes with tassels now.'This will increase your reputation with the Weaponsmith Craft Guild.Speak to Hob Longbottom.'Speak to me again to max out your reputation with the Weaponsmith Craft Guild.''Congrats, you can make swords with gems on the hilt now.'This will increase your reputation with the Woodworker Craft Guild.Speak to Hob Longbottom.'Speak to me again to max out your reputation with the Woodworker Craft Guild.''Congrats, you can whittle like nobody's business now.'Talk to the profession trainer again to complete this quest.Completing this quest will grant you Umbar proficiency and Umbar mastery in the Cook profession.

