'Artisans can no longer execute their recipes at ordinary forges; instead, they must use the superior forge, like this one beside me.

'Before granting you access to artisan recipes, I want to make sure you are truly proficient as an expert. I would like you to execute two recipes and deliver the goods you make to folk who have need of it. They will tell me if what you make is evidence that you have achieved true proficiency as an expert.''Bring the steel helm to Egil Oldbeard and the steel gloves to Tandri Greyhammer.''Ah, a helm! And a fine one at that. Did you truly make this yourself? It is the last piece of armour I need to complete my set. I do believe all the other guards in the hall will be envious!''Ah, these are the finest-looking steel gloves I have seen in a long while. Molda was not wrong when he told me of your promise as a metalsmith. I will tell him I was very impressed with the finished product.''This helm is a wonderful piece of workmanship!''These gloves will do nicely!''Ah, ${PLAYER}! I see you have returned from a successful mission! Tandri and Egil spoke to me of how impressed they were, and with their high praise, I am impressed as well. We dwarves are not easy to please when it comes to matters of the forge.'You have been sent to an expert crafting vendor to have your own expertise appraised before moving on to artisanship.The crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel.

