You should craft the two recipes required by Fladdan for your growth as a Tailor.Execute the recipe for a cotton cloakExecute the recipe for sturdy leather armourPeople in need of the tailored items you have sewn can be found throughout Esteldín.

You should bring your sewn goods to the townsfolk of Esteldín.Fladdan can be found in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín.

You should speak with Fladdan and tell him of the successful deliveries of the goods you made.Talk to Fladdan in the Esteldín Crafting Hall'You have been sent to me at an important time in your journey as a crafter, ${PLAYER}. As I'm sure you've noticed, you are very close to becoming an artisan tailor.

'Artisans can no longer execute their recipes at ordinary workbenches; instead, they must use the superior workbench, like this one beside me.

'Before granting you access to artisan recipes, I want to make sure you are truly proficient as an expert. I would like you to execute two recipes and deliver the goods you make to folks who have need of it. They will tell me if what you make is evidence that you have achieved true proficiency as an expert.''Bring the cotton cloak to Eón and the sturdy leather armour to Herondan.''A cloak...of the softest cotton! Thank you, kind tailor. I have naught, but this cloak will keep out the chill. That is a gift beyond measure.''A fine piece of leather armour! I have some need of this, as you see. It does look a little small, though....

'No matter! A tight-fitting shirt always shows me at my best.''This armour is just what I needed.''Many thanks for the cloak...it shall keep me warm on cold nights.''I have heard high praises of you from those who received your gifts. You have impressed me, ${PLAYER}. I believe you are ready to advance as an artisan.'You have been sent to an expert crafting vendor to have your own expertise appraised before moving on to Artisanship.The crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel.

You should craft the two recipes required by Fladdan for your growth as a Tailor.Execute the recipe for a cotton cloakExecute the recipe for sturdy leather armourPeople in need of the tailored items you have sewn can be found throughout Esteldín.

You should bring your sewn goods to the townsfolk of Esteldín.Fladdan can be found in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín.

You should speak with Fladdan and tell him of the successful deliveries of the goods you made.Talk to Fladdan in the Esteldín Crafting Hall'You have been sent to me at an important time in your journey as a crafter, ${PLAYER}. As I'm sure you've noticed, you are very close to becoming an artisan tailor.

'Artisans can no longer execute their recipes at ordinary workbenches; instead, they must use the superior workbench, like this one beside me.

'Before granting you access to artisan recipes, I want to make sure you are truly proficient as an expert. I would like you to execute two recipes and deliver the goods you make to folks who have need of it. They will tell me if what you make is evidence that you have achieved true proficiency as an expert.''You need to craft a cotton cloak and sturdy leather armour.''A cloak...of the softest cotton! Thank you, kind tailor. I have naught, but this cloak will keep out the chill. That is a gift beyond measure.''A fine piece of leather armour! I have some need of this, as you see. It does look a little small, though....

'No matter! A tight-fitting shirt always shows me at my best.''This armour is just what I needed.''Many thanks for the cloak...it shall keep me warm on cold nights.''I have heard high praises of you from those who received your gifts. You have impressed me, ${PLAYER}. I believe you are ready to advance as an artisan.'You have been sent to an expert crafting vendor to have your own expertise appraised before moving on to artisanship.The crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel.

You should craft the two recipes required by Thithrandi for your growth as a weaponsmith.Execute the recipe for the bright steel greatswordExecute the recipe for a bright steel daggerDwarves who wish to receive the goods you made can be found throughout Thorin's Hall.

You should bring the weapons and components you forged to the interested dwarves in Thorin's Hall.Thithrandi can be found in the Maker's Hall in Thorin's Hall.

You should return to Thithrandi with the news that your weaponsmithy abilities were admired by the dwarves of Thorin's Hall.Return to Thithrandi in the Maker's Hall'You have been sent to me at an important time in your journey as a crafter, ${PLAYER}. As I'm sure you've noticed, you are very close to becoming an artisan weaponsmith.

'Artisans can no longer execute their recipes at ordinary forges; instead, they must use the superior forge, like this one beside me.

'Before granting you access to artisan recipes, I want to make sure you are truly proficient as an expert. I would like you to execute two recipes and deliver the goods you make to folk who have need of it. They will tell me if what you make is evidence that you have achieved true proficiency as an expert.''You must bring the bright steel greatsword to Hagan and the bright steel dagger to Albryc Longfoot.''I am, as you know, something of an expert myself on the craftsmanship of greatswords. This, ${PLAYER}, is a fine piece indeed. I am glad Thithrandi recommended you bring this to me; such craftsmanship is not often seen, even in Thorin's Hall.''This is as fine a dagger as I've seen in many a long year. Your skills in weaponsmithy seem to be rising fast. Thithrandi has spoken highly of you, but I did not believe that a busy ${CLASS} like yourself could truly have time for crafting at this level. Well done, ${PLAYER}...I was wrong about you!''This is an exquisite dagger!''This greatsword is a magnificent piece of work!''I've heard high praises of your weaponsmithy abilities from the dwarves! You have impressed me, ${PLAYER}. I believe you are ready to advance as an artisan.'You have been sent to an expert crafting vendor to have your own expertise appraised before moving on to artisanship.The crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel.

You should craft the two recipes required by Thithrandi for your growth as a weaponsmith.Execute the recipe for the bright steel greatswordExecute the recipe for a bright steel daggerDwarves who wish to receive the goods you made can be found throughout Thorin's Hall.

You should bring the weapons and components you forged to the interested dwarves in Thorin's Hall.Thithrandi can be found in the Forging Hall in Thorin's Hall.

You should return to Thithrandi with the news that your weaponsmithy abilities were admired by the dwarves of Thorin's Hall.Return to Thithrandi in the Forging Hall'You have been sent to me at an important time in your journey as a crafter, ${PLAYER}. As I'm sure you've noticed, you are very close to becoming an artisan weaponsmith.

'Artisans can no longer execute their recipes at ordinary forges; instead, they must use the superior forge, like this one beside me.

'Before granting you access to artisan recipes, I want to make sure you are truly proficient as an expert. I would like you to execute two recipes and deliver the goods you make to folk who have need of it. They will tell me if what you make is evidence that you have achieved true proficiency as an expert.''You must bring the bright steel greatsword to Hagan and the bright steel dagger to Albryc Longfoot.''I am, as you know, something of an expert myself on the crafstmanship of greatswords. This, ${PLAYER}, is a fine piece indeed. I am glad Thithrandi recommended you bring this to me; such craftsmanship is not often seen, even in Thorin's Hall.''This is as fine a dagger as I've seen in many a long year. Your skills in weaponsmithy seem to be rising fast. Thithrandi has spoken highly of you, but I did not believe that a busy ${CLASS} like yourself could truly have time for crafting at this level. Well done, ${PLAYER}...I was wrong about you!''This is an exquisite dagger!''This greatsword is a magnificent piece of work!''I've heard high praises of your weaponsmithy abilities from the dwarves! You have impressed me, ${PLAYER}. I believe you are ready to advance as an artisan.'You have been sent to an expert crafting vendor to have your own expertise appraised before moving on to artisanship.The crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel.

You should craft the two recipes required by Tadhrien for your growth as a woodworker.Execute the recipe for a yew spearExecute the recipe for a yew bowYour goods can be delivered to various people around Esteldín.

Many folks around Esteldín have taken an interest in your woodworking skills.Tadhrien is in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín.

You should speak with Tadhrien and tell her of your successful deliveries.Talk to Tadhrien in Esteldín'You have been sent to me at an important time in your journey as a crafter, ${PLAYER}. As I'm sure you've noticed, you are very close to becoming an artisan woodworker.

'Artisans can no longer execute their recipes at ordinary workbenches; instead, they must use the superior workbench, like this one beside me.

'Before granting you access to artisan recipes, I want to make sure you are truly proficient as an expert. I would like you to execute two recipes and deliver the goods you make to folks who have need of it. They will tell me if what you make is evidence that you have achieved true proficiency as an expert.''You need to craft a yew spear and yew bow.''You need to bring the yew spear to Rhona and the yew bow to Eón.''This is a good hunting spear! I have very little, and the Rangers have shared much with me since I came here, but I wish to hunt and contribute on my own. I thank you for this gift, ${PLAYER}. Such weapons cannot often be found where I am from.''This is a finely-crafted bow, ${PLAYER}, executed with a great deal of skill. Tadhrien did not exaggerate your talent. Thank you for this gift!''Thank you for this bow!''This is a wonderfuly-wrought spear!''I have heard much praise of your skill from Rhona and Eón. They were all very impressed with your work, and I am now sufficiently impressed as well. I believe you are ready to advance as an artisan.'You have been sent to an expert crafting vendor to have your own expertise appraised before moving on to artisanship.The crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel.

You should craft the two recipes required by Tadhrien for your growth as a woodworker.Execute the recipe for a yew spearExecute the recipe for a yew bowYour goods can be delivered to various people around Esteldín.

Many folks around Esteldín have taken an interest in your woodworking skills.Tadhrien is in the Crafting Hall in Esteldín.

You should speak with Tadhrien and tell her of your successful deliveries.Talk to Tadhrien in Esteldín'You have been sent to me at an important time in your journey as a crafter, ${PLAYER}. As I'm sure you've noticed, you are very close to becoming an artisan woodworker.

'Artisans can no longer execute their recipes at ordinary workbenches; instead, they must use the superior workbench, like this one beside me.

'Before granting you access to artisan recipes, I want to make sure you are truly proficient as an expert. I would like you to execute two recipes and deliver the goods you make to folks who have need of it. They will tell me if what you make is evidence that you have achieved true proficiency as an expert.''You need to craft a yew spear and yew bow.''You need to bring the yew spear to Rhona and the yew bow to Eón.''This is a good hunting spear! I have very little, and the Rangers have shared much with me since I came here, but I wish to hunt and contribute on my own. I thank you for this gift, ${PLAYER}. Such weapons cannot often be found where I am from.''This is a finely-crafted bow, ${PLAYER}, executed with a great deal of skill. Tadhrien did not exaggerate your talent. Thank you for this gift!''Thank you for this bow!''This is a wonderfuly-wrought spear!''I have heard much praise of your skill from Rhona and Eón. They were very impressed with your work, and I am now sufficiently impressed as well. I believe you are ready to advance as an artisan.'Concerned that the sapling is not drawing enough from the soil, Faranil asked you to make your way into the Ettenmoors to find soil that has been macerated by the cave-claws.Faranil asked that you make your way to the north-west to seek out cave-claws that move the earth with their mandibles. She believes that you can collect earth from within their maws that will be better for your sapling.'My friend, I expect that this request will be a surprising one. You see, as I watch the sapling I see that it does not sup as well as I would expect from the earth, soil, and water we provide to it. This makes me wonder if the  earth itself, here in the Ettenmoors, is too corrupt. Though, it cannot be, as this little sapling is uncorrupted. I still do not believe that we should introduce the sapling to anything outside of the Ettenmoors, so I have this new request of you.

'The cave dwelling crawlers in the Isendeep mine and scattered throughout Arador's End often consume the very earth as they dig. These nuisances are more vermin than assistance, but we may still gain strength from them. Will you go forth and collect lumps of earth from them?''This is welcome, friend. I will begin the process of enhancing the soil so that we may see the strength of the little sapling improve.'Faranil believes that your sapling is looking as though something made it sad. She wants you to seek out some advice on how you might brighten the mood of your little sapling.Make your way to Hoarhallow, talk to Emerald Twospade and ask her how she heartens the plants that she tends.Speak with Emerald Twospade in HoarhallowEmerald told you the secret is to sing to the plant. Return to Glân Vraig and sing to your sapling.Emerald Twospade advises that you should sing to your sapling'I have been studying the little sapling all day. Look upon it, friend. Does it seem... sad?

'I wonder... would you make your way to Emerald Twospade in Hoarhallow and ask her how she rouses plants that seem in such a state?''Please, ask Emerald for her advice. She can be found in Hoarhallow.''When I tend to my plants, I sing. It seems to me that they sway along with my voice. I would think that such an act would do the same for your problem, friend.'You discovered a sapling that reacted to your presence growing in the Ettenmoors. Being curious, you collected the little sapling, took it to the safety of Glân Vraig, and delivered it to Faranil, a horticulturist from Rivendell.Make your way north to Ost Ringdyr and speak with Emissary Pip Diggins of Hoarhallow. He may have knowledge of the sapling that you discovered.Travel to Ost Ringdyr and speak with Emissary Pip DigginsMake your way from Ost Ringdyr to Hoarhallow far to the south-west. There, find and speak with Marigold Winterdown, Ned Claybrick, and Emerald Twospade about the sapling.Speak with Ned ClaybrickSpeak with Emerald TwospadeSpeak with Marigold WinterdownAfter speaking with the residents of Hoarhallow, it is clear that they have never seen a sapling like you have found. They have seen the vile Huorns that make the woods their home near their village of Hoarhallow. Return to the cultivator and explain what you learned.'This is a peculiar find. I cannot say I have seen anything like this little sapling in all of my long years.

'I wonder...'

The Elf pauses.

'There is an emissary at Ost Ringdyr north of here who comes from the village of hobbits, Hoarhallow. Perhaps he or his kin have seen something like this before. Can you visit him and learn what you can?''The emissary from Hoarhallow, Pip Diggins, is at Ost Ringdyr to the north of Glân Vraig. You can travel there, in relative safety, if you take the hidden path just to the north of the quartermaster.''An unattended sapling in the wildlands of the Ettenmoors. Deary me.

'I will tell you this, my friend. I have heard tell of angry trees that roam the woods just outside of Hoarhallow, but I've fortune enough to never have run afoul of one of the creatures. I believe there are one or two from my town who have witnessed such things, and they may know something. Make your way to them at Hoarhallow in the distant south-west.

'If you seek out Emerald Twospade, Ned Claybrick, and Marigold Winterdown, they may be able to tell you more of the creature of which you speak.''I have not seen a sapling that trembled when I walked near. Trees do not move when I go near them... but there are fell things in those woods. They are not trees, but have the look of them. They are vile creatures.''A shivering sapling? Reacting to you as you moved? I may have heard stories when I was young about trees as such, but I have always thought them tales to make children stay away from the woods. I should like to see such a thing in my day, I think.''A sapling you say?

'I cannot say in my wandering that I have seen such a thing, but I have seen the terrors that dwell in the woods. Horrible walking trees and roots that try to drag you beneath the ground.

'Best stay away from them. May be best to leave that sapling - could be one of theirs.''Curious. We shall need to care for this little sapling and see what becomes of it. I feel that there is a reason you made this discovery, ${PLAYER}. We should remain diligent. Perhaps I can learn something more of this curious little creature.'Faranil believes that the sapling is in need of a direct source of sunlight. She believes that Golloval, the eagle that watches the Ettenmoors can assist.Head toward the Isendeep mine, and in the shadow of the entrance find the Eagle Golloval. Ask the eagle if he might know how to enhance the mood of the sapling kept at Glân Vraig.Speak with Golloval in the shadow of the Isendeep MineGolloval needs a glass bauble to capture a ray of the sun. He tasked you with trying to collect one from the goblins in Grothum, the Warg dens in the west, or the amongst the spiders in the craggy stones - far to the west.You received the infused bauble from Golloval and were advised to return the bauble to the cultivator at Glân Vraig.'I am watching the progress on your little find, my friend. It seems, sad somehow. I wonder.

'There are eagles in the wild, here in the Ettenmoors, that make the hostile lands their home. There is one, Golloval, that dwells in the shadow of the Isendeep Mine. He has long been a friend to my people and I would ask that you speak to him and see if there is a way that he might lend a gift to our fledgling here.''As with any tree, the nurturing rays of the sun must touch its leaves so that it can know the warmth and grow. I can help, in a small way by flying high into the sky to capture a golden ray in a bauble of sorts, but I need such a bauble. You can help me collect one.

'I know that the goblins nearby in the village of Grothum often pick up curiosities. They may have the glass I need.

'If not them, then the wargs to the west may have stashed a bauble near their dens.

'Lastly, if not among the goblins or Wargs, seek out the vile spiders at the foot of the mountains far to the west.

'Do not give up hope, one of them will have the clear glass ball I need.''This shall do nicely. I will head skyward and then return. Wait here.''The sun shines so brightly within this bauble. Golloval is truly a prince of the eagles. He will one day rise with the great eagles I think. For now, let us shine this upon your sapling and see the change it brings.'Faranil wants to further nurturing your sapling. She asks that you make your way into Ettenmoors along the banks of the Hoarwell, where the aurochs roam, to collect their manure.Make your way to the plains surrounding the Hoardale and collect the manure from the piles lift behind by the Thistledown Aurochs there.'We must further nurture the soil in which we have your sapling. This is a task I do not envy. The wild Thistledown Aurochs make the plains south and north of the Hoardale their home. As they wander, they leave behind their manure, which is rich with nutrients that help all plants grow.''I will see that the soil is further enriched. Though this is a foul business it is all for the health and growth of the sapling.'After studying your sapling for some time, Faranil seeks the aid of the Hobbits of Hoarhallow for more insight into how to care for the sapling.Make your way to Hoarhallow and ask Ned Claybrick if he ever thinks that plants he tends seem inquisitive.Ask Ned Claybrick at Hoarhallow if his plants are inquisitiveNed suggested that he speaks to his plants but he has never listened to them. Maybe there is something to what he said. Return to Glân Vraig and give it a try.Talk to your saplingYou talked to the sapling, but nothing seemed to change. Perhaps you should try listening.Listen to your saplingThough you heard nothing when listening to the sapling, it did seem that something stirred in the little plant. Let Faranil know.Speak with Faranil at Glân Vraig'Friend, I have been watching the sapling with great wonder recently. I think, the more I study it, the more I think it is studying me, as well. But... this cannot be.

'Could you speak with Ned Claybrick and ask him for his expertise? He tends crops in Hoarhallow and may be able to offer some insight.''Make your way to Hoarhallow and seek out Ned Claybrick. Perhaps he will know something of the actions of this sapling.''Inquisitive plants? No, I cannot say that I have ever thought that the plants I tend are listening or care much for what I do. Though, to be honest, my friend, I do speak with my plants. Though I have never listened to my plants.''Talking to and listening to the sapling? I often speak with the natural world, but all I have heard was the rustling of leaves. Perhaps we all should listen more... perhaps there is something being said after all.'Faranil believes that your sapling is especially happy today. She asked that you visit Marigold Winterdown at Hoarhallow for more insight.Journey to Hoarhallow and ask Marigold Winterdown if she knows of a way to brighten a flower or plant even further.Make your way to Hoarhallow and speak with Marigold WinterdownMarigold told you to dance with plants and they will dance with you. Return to Glân Vraig and dance with your sapling.Dance with your sapling'It seems today that the sapling has perked up, as if the world is brighter. I think that this is a good thing, friend. But, I wonder too, what could we do to make this an even brighter time for the sapling? Perhaps a friend in Hoarhallow might offer insight.''A bright flower made brighter?'

She thinks.

'I dance, ${PLAYER}. I dance among the flowers and they dance with me. It is a simple thing, I think, but they feel brighter and happier when I dance among them. Perhaps you should do the same.'Spiders living in the craggy stones in the farthest reach of the Ettenmoors will one day pose a threat to the forest in the southern part of the Ettenmoors unless their numbers are controlled.Faranil wants to eliminate the threat of the spiders that roam the Ettenmoors. The Cragstone brood is found far to the west. Make your way to them and cull the brood.Defeat Cragstone Spiders (${NUMBER}/14)Return to Faranil at Glân Vraig and tell her that you have done what she asked, and that a great number of the Cragstone brood died this day.Return to Glân Vraig and speak with Faranil'Spiders are corruption. They are the enemy of all nature.

'Let us break from tending the sapling and focus on ridding the world of this terrible enemy, so that it cannot harm nature more than it already does lest, one day, they threaten every forest, even the home that we will make for your sapling.''The Cragstone brood dwells deep in the shadow of the mountains to the west. Go there, thin their number as they are an affront to all nature.''Your efforts will help preserve nature for all, my friend. We shall help to make the Ettenmoors safe for future generations.'Faranil fears that the enmity of the wolves will threaten your sapling as they threaten the fauna in the forest. She begs that you thin out their number.Faranil wants to help secure the future of the forests in the Ettenmoors by culling the Darktide wolves from the woods.Defeat Darktide wolves (${NUMBER}/14)With your effort to thin the numbers in the Darktide pack complete, you should return to Faranil and let her know of your efforts.'It is not for neglect, rather it is because I know the enmity and danger that exists should we not address the enemies that would bring harm to the forest. Your sapling is growing and will one day need to be returned to the place where it was found. But, friend, there are enemies in these lands beyond the forces out of the north.''The Darktide wolves make the southern forests of the Ettenmoors their home. You will find them roaming throughout Hithlad. Go there and thin their number, please.''Though this may seem a truly selfish request, friend, it is for the better future we wish for all.'After tending to your sapling, Faranil believes that the sapling needs some pure water from the Hoarwell to aid in its cultivation.Make your way to the Hoardale River, specifically around Tol Ascarnen, and collect filtered soil from within the bellies of the nerbyg that make the banks their home.'Greetings again, ${PLAYER}. I have been watching the sapling with great interest today. I believe that the nutrients it is receiving from the soil here are out of balance. It is not surprising. The battle that plagues this land harms nearly every part of nature. I believe that there is a way to aid the sapling, but it will require some effort if you are willing.

'The nerbyg near the fortress of Tol Ascarnen use soil to aid in digesting their food. If you would collect filtered-earth from within their bellies, we may bring balance to the soil for your sapling.''Most excellent work. I will begin working this filtered soil with the earth and perhaps we will see the benefits start to assist the growth of your little sapling.'Faranil believes that one of the keys to growing your sapling well is the water that it consumes. She provided a map of the purest locations along the Hoarwell River and sent you with phials to collect the water.Faranil marked your map with many locations within the Ettenmoors where you can collect some of the purest water that the Hoarwell provides. She then gave you phials, asking that they be filled at locations she marked for you.You collected the phials of pure water from the Hoardale. Return them to Faranil at Glân Vraig.'It is important that we nurture this little sapling. We should be careful to only provide for it from the natural habitat where it was found. I believe, to strengthen its roots, we should provide it with water from the natural springs found within the Ettenmoors. I have collected flasks that you can use to can fill with water from the springs and rivers around the Ettenmoors.

'If you are able and willing to continue nurturing your find, I will mark your map with the locations where you should collect the water. Return to me when you have the specimens and we will strengthen the roots of this fledgling creature.''This is perfect, my friend. I shall introduce the water to the sapling and help aid in strengthening its roots. In time, we will see the fruits of your labour.'Faranil fears that there may be other saplings in the woods of the Ettenmoors and that the enemy would hunt for them and destroy them if they found them. She tasked you with finding the enemy and defeating them.Faranil suggested you make your way into the Ettenmoors and defeat the enemy that would pervert nature and destroy other saplings that may be growing in the wild.Defeat the forces of Angmar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Having completed your efforts against the enemies of nature, you should return to Faranil and tell her of your victory.Return to Glân Vraig and speak with Faranil'Since the discovery of this sapling, the enemy scours the land in search of the same signs that we seek. They tread without thought and would bring ruin to all you are working toward. Find them, my friend. Stop them from destroying the natural order.''Our battles here in the Ettenmoors are a necessity. It saddens us all that there is still war in the world. One day, there may be peace.

'Until that day, it is good to know that there are hearty warriors, like you, to fight for what is good and decent.'Faranil learned that a goblin in Grothum, Bok, is assisting the servants of Angmar in corrupting a sapling of their own. You were tasked with eliminating the goblin.Head north and west of Glân Vraig. On the east side of the Ettendeep in Arador's end find and defeat the goblin leader Bok, in the village of Grothum and then return to Faranil.Defeat Bok, the goblin leader at GrothumBok is defeated. Return to Faranil at her post in Glân Vraig and inform her of your success.'Friend, to the north and west of here at the eastern entrance to Arador's End there is a village of goblins. Word arrives that their leader, Bok, assists the servants of Angmar is befouling a sapling of their own.

'We must deny their illicit machinations and defeat this goblin lest he provide deeper details in corrupting the pure thing.

'Will you please go to Grothum and defeat the goblin leader, Bok?''You will find Bok in the goblin village of Grothum. The village lies on the eastern side of the Ettendeep Mine in Arador's End. Find him and defeat him before he imparts his knowledge to the enemy.''The goblins are a terrible creature of darkness, and they would pervert the true nature of the world if they could. It is good there are heroes like you to defend that which cannot yet defend itself.

'Be well and rewarded, friend.'Faranil believes that the sapling is stirring from all of your efforts. Continue your efforts over the course of several days to see what bounty may come.Faranil asked that you return to her each day to see what new effort might strengthen your sapling. She is located in Glân Vraig, the foothold of the Free People in the Ettenmoors.'My friend, something has happened. The sapling stirred.'

A smile spreads across the Faranil's face.

'We are witness to something I have never seen and we should rejoice... but, my friend, we should not rest! For while the sapling stirred, it rests again, and though I watch it intently, I do not know what next to do.

'Will you return to me each day and see if there is more that can be done to help cultivate your sapling?''Your efforts yield results, friend. The sapling grows in strength daily and weekly. We should keep up our efforts while I continue my study.

'There is something very unique about this little sapling, and we will discover the secret of how it came to be, together.

'For now, we must be patient and true to the endeavour at hand.'Burglars cannot rely on strength and power to defeat their enemies -- but a severely bleeding wound will often do the trick.Cunning WoundStrike with Cunning AttackBurglars cannot rely on strength and power to defeat their enemies -- but a severely bleeding wound will often do the trick.Cunning WoundStrike with Cunning AttackYou earned the Cuts Down Trees title.Obligatory Text.Athra Devister is standing by to greet visitors who come to Clegur for their annual Daffodil Days celebration.Athra Devister, the organizer of Clegur's Daffodil Days festival, has promised you a reward if you lend a hand with the festival while you're here.Complete Quest: The Gift of SpringComplete Quest: Family FeastComplete Quest: Stretched Too ThinComplete Quest: Musicians' MisfortuneComplete Quest: Well-watered BloomsComplete Quest: Promoting PieComplete Quest: Flower EnvyComplete Quest: Springtime's ColoursYou have helped many people around Clegur during Daffodil Days. You should return to Athra Devister near the stables and let her know.Talk to Athra Devister'Hullo there, friend. Welcome to Clegur! Proper lovely day fer a festival, isn't it?

'I'm Athra, planner of this here little party. But mind ye, if somethin's amiss, 'tisn't my fault. Can't be expected to do everythin' now, can I? I'm only one hobbit.

'In fact, if ye see things that need doin' and ye lend us a hand, that would be right kind of ye. I'll see to it that ye get a tidy little something fer your time, eh?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Oh, look at you, love! Helpin' all about town. I'm proper grateful, I am. 'Tisn't an easy task, I have. Ye can plan as much as ye want, but somethin' will always go awry. All ye can do is try to be ready for it and deal with it as ye can.

