<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Troublesome hobbits can be found around the Shire.

A sneaky hobbit has asked you to deliver deceptive invitations to her troublesome neighbours.The sneaky hobbit can be found near the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should let the sneaky hobbit know that you have delivered all of the invitations.'Ah, yes, you will do perfectly. Listen, if you could do me a favour I would really appreciate it! We have a wedding planned and… well, let’s say that the bride would really appreciate it if some of our more troublesome neighbours were not in attendance.

'I have a stack of invitations here whose information might be a bit… misleading, if you catch my drift. If you could deliver these to our good neighbours, I know the bride would really appreciate it!''What’s this? An invitation? Of course I’ll be there!''I knew my invitation got lost by the post! I shall have to get a new dress, and shoes!''Well it’s about time! Oh I do so hope they’ll have meat pies.''Finally! Can you believe I thought I wasn’t invited?!''Ah hah! My wife will finally stop asking after this now.''Hmmm. This had best be better than the last party they threw. Can you believe they made us all leave after only two days?!''Well it is about time! If you will excuse me, I have to show this to my sister. Imagine thinking I wasn't invited.''Hah! I knew Lobelia was wrong about them not inviting me! Wait 'till I show her this!''Haha! Excellent. The bride will be most pleased and my larders will not be as strained as the last wedding. What a disaster that was! Thank you for your help, friend! Oh, uh... I would invite you to the wedding also, however, I'm sure you are quite too busy to attend. Good day to you!'Thrice you have stood up on the side of Erebor for Durin's Day, and saw what the sun revealed when it touched the dwarf-wrought stone.Observe Durin's Day before the old secret door up on the side of Mount Erebor a third time in a row.Read the runes upon the stoneComplete deeds in Cardolan.Complete deeds in Cardolan.Complete Quests of CardolanComplete Explorer of CardolanComplete Slayer of CardolanOnce the seat of the Witch-king of Angmar, the dread citadel of Gwathrenost casts a long shadow upon the city of Carn Dûm. All but abandoned after the Steward of Angmar was deposed, the remnants of the Iron Crown have crept forth from the shadows, seeking to master a lost artifact of the Witch-king and reclaim dominion of Angmar.Once the seat of the Witch-king of Angmar, the dread citadel of Gwathrenost casts a long shadow upon the city of Carn Dûm. All but abandoned after the Steward of Angmar was deposed, the remnants of the Iron Crown have crept forth from the shadows, seeking to master a lost artifact of the Witch-king and reclaim dominion of Angmar.Complete Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel -- Tier 1Complete Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel -- Tier 2Complete Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel -- Tier 3Complete Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel -- Foe of the Iron CrownComplete Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel -- Foe of the Orc-realmComplete Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel -- Shadows of the PastMany dangerous creatures have called the sewers of Carn Dûm home. Some have remained rumours, nothing more. Others, however, may be of interest to the scattered remnants of the Iron Crown.Complete Sagroth, Lair of Vermin -- Tier 1Complete Sagroth, Lair of Vermin -- Tier 2Complete Sagroth, Lair of Vermin -- Tier 3Complete Sagroth, Lair of Vermin -- Slayer of AngmarimComplete Sagroth, Lair of Vermin -- The Seekers of SagrothSant Lhoer, known as the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm, is a dank place teeming with deadly plants, trees, and flowers, the likes of which have rarely or never been seen before in Middle-earth. Beyond the foetid, beryl-green waters which flow through Sant Lhoer, rise immense glass structures, including Bâr Heledh, the Glass House. It is here that the sorceress Oganuin plies her craft, experimenting upon creatures, plants, and people alike. To what end, and for what purpose? One can only assume the darkest of designs.Complete Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens -- Tier 1Complete Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens -- Tier 2Complete Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens -- Tier 3Complete Slayer of Sant LhoerComplete Plants of the Poison GardensUnbeknownst to the Men of Cardolan, Sarch Vorn, an ancient temple of the Edain, has long served as the resting place of a malevolent spirit of the Elder Days known only as Hithrengor, the Grey Fear. Roused by the return of the Witch-king of Angmar, the Grey Fear has awoken from its slumber to once again spread terror and death across the ravaged lands of Cardolan.Complete Sarch Vorn, the Black Grave -- Tier 1Complete Sarch Vorn, the Black Grave -- Tier 2Complete Sarch Vorn, the Black Grave -- Tier 3Complete Sarch Vorn, the Black Grave -- Slayer of the Barrow-wightsComplete deeds in Swanfleet.Complete deeds in Swanfleet.Complete Quests of SwanfleetComplete Explorer of SwanfleetComplete Slayer of SwanfleetIn the depths of Thaurisgar, countless foul and twisted experiments roam the shadows--the terrible legacy of Aniochán the Harrower. Before the fall of Carn Dûm, Aniochán worked tirelessly to outdo his rivals and win the favour of the Steward of Angmar. Chief among his tools in shaping his fell creations was a curious ichor known only as the Bile of Ifrinn. Thought to be lost after a disastrous experiment claimed Aniochán's life, now this foetid and vile substance is in danger of being let loose into the world.Complete Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary -- Tier 1Complete Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary -- Tier 2Complete Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary -- Tier 3Complete Slayer of ThaurisgarComplete Alchemy of ThaurisgarYou have been granted a discount at all Lothlórien vendors.Your heroic deeds shall never be forgotten.By completing this quest, you will receive a Delvings barter currency allowance.'Get barter currency for Delvings!''Ride back here like a bunny if you need more!'The Elves of Rivendell watch the Last Bridge from the Lone-lands into the Trollshaws.Scouts from Rivendell are likely encamped near the Last Bridge between the Lone-lands and the Trollshaws.

