is yearly Egg Scramble event...can you collect all the plain-coloured eggs?Acquire and use a blue eggAcquire and use a green eggAcquire and use an orange eggAcquire and use a red eggAcquire and use a purple eggFarmer Sandson has opened his yearly Egg Scramble event...can you collect all the spotted eggs?Acquire and use a green and yellow spotted eggAcquire and use an orange and red spotted eggAcquire and use a purple and blue spotted eggAcquire and use a blue and red spotted eggAcquire and use a yellow and blue spotted eggFarmer Sandson has opened his yearly Egg Scramble event...can you collect all the striped eggs?Acquire and use a blue and white striped eggAcquire and use a yellow and red striped eggAcquire and use a pink and purple striped eggAcquire and use an orange and purple striped eggAcquire and use a red and green striped eggFarmer Sandson has opened his yearly Egg Scramble event...can you collect the rare golden egg?Acquire and use a golden eggTalk to Ransroth.Speak to Ransroth'Talk to me to increase your reputation with the  Gabil'akkâ.''20,000 Reputation with the  Gabil'akkâ, coming right up!'Talk to Ransroth.Speak to Ransroth'Talk to me to increase your reputation with the March on Gundabad.''20,000 Reputation with the March on Gundabad, coming right up!'The Minas Tirith wedding planner Merilien seeks special lighting for her events.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>You can find emerald fireflies in the Midgewater Marshes from gloaming till dawn.

You should collect fireflies for the wedding planner in Minas Tirith.Catch emerald fireflies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The wedding planner Merilien is located on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith.

Return to Minas Tirith with the firefly-filled lanterns.Talk to MerilienThe Merry Swan is on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should place emerald firefly lanterns about the stage in the Merry Swan.'Green is the colour of growth, abundance, and... fertility! A flickering emerald glow will add enchantment and signify prosperity on my customer's special day.

'Fireflies prefer watery places and tall grasses. Those of the emerald variety, however, can only be found in Bree, in the Midgewater Marshes. You'll want to wear your mud stomping boots, for sure.

'Fill these lanterns for me with the little darlings, would you? And do come right back, they needn't be kept trapped for longer than is necessary.''Ah, look at that glow! It's like catching a bit of spring, isn't it? These will do, just fine. Good work, now begone. The stench of the marshes clings to you and I don't want anyone to pass by and think that reek is me.

'Take these with you and place them about the stage in the Merry Swan.'An Elf named Emmathron has asked for your assistance with helping him draw beautiful landscapes.If you've decided to accept Emmathron's request, you should talk to him at your home.Talk to Emmathron'Hail, adventurer. Have you come across many scenic views during your travels?

'Ah, let me explain before I get ahead of myself. I'm an artist, and I'm hoping to illustrate some landscapes. Except... I fear I am no adventurer, and I'm sure I'd find myself in some tricky situation out in the wilds alone.

'If you would not mind leading me to these sites, I would be happy to reward you.''I'm pleased that you accepted my offer! I shall let you know once I am ready to start an illustration -- or when inspiration strikes. Whichever comes first.'An artist's work is never complete.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 10'You should talk to Emmathron in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'I've been drawing so much lately that I've reduced my wax-pens to mere stubs! And as luck would have it, I've run out of materials and need to collect more.

'A rather good excuse to spend the day outside, don't you think? Would you care to join me?''Ever onwards, friend.'${PLAYER}, I wanted to gift this to you.'

Emmathron presents a piece of paper to you. On it is his recreated drawing of the turtle. The turtle appears just as serene as she did in that moment, unbothered by your presences and content to simply sit. A moment plucked out of time and placed onto paper.

'I used the same wax-pens from my first attempt. The colours shall fade eventually, I know that now. But I choose to see that as a measure of our friendship -- the more faded its colours, the longer our friendship will have been. Then I will draw something new for you.' Emmathron laughs, rubbing the back of his neck. 'It sounds like a silly hope, but may it come true regardless.'Emmathron has invited you to join him in collecting materials for his wax-pens.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 2'You should talk to Emmathron in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'Good day, ${PLAYER}. I'll need to collect some materials for my wax-pens. If I'm not mistaken, I know of a good location that holds the materials I seek.

'Would you like to join me?''Wonderful. I very much look forward to seeing what we can find.''I'll get to work straightaway on turning these into wax-pens. It's a rather lengthy and complicated process, but I enjoy it nevertheless.

'At least I can be certain that I'll produce a functional wax-pen by the end of it. Art is a different beast altogether.'With his wax-pens at the ready, Emmathron seeks to complete his first landscape drawing.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 3'You should talk to Emmathron in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'${PLAYER}, I believe I'm ready to illustrate a landscape now. Have you a place in mind? I shall prepare for the journey ahead and follow your lead.''Excellent! I shall gather my things.''I refuse to let this failure deter me from trying again. No matter how long it takes, I must create something worthwhile.

'But first, I shall have to adjust something about my methods....'A change in method may be needed in order for Emmathron to complete a drawing to his standards.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 4'You should talk to Emmathron in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'There is no use putting this off any longer -- I do not have eternity to wait for inspiration! What should our next destination be, ${PLAYER}?

'For this attempt, I would like to spend some time there first, then return later to draw the scenery. Perhaps that way, the drawing shall come more naturally to me.'

He frowns.

'Perhaps.''Surely the outcome will be different this time.''Forgive me for my dour state, ${PLAYER}; many invaluable moments had been preserved on those pages. My mind knows they are lost, but my heart insists it cannot be so.

'Please leave me -- I would prefer solitude for now.'Despite the setbacks, something still drives Emmathron to complete this second drawing.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 5'You should talk to Emmathron in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'I cannot wallow in despair forever; I must start illustrating the landscape that you chose for me. We shall see how I fare this time... though I do not have high hopes for myself.''I must get to work.''${PLAYER}, about what you said to me earlier... I shall have to ruminate further on whether to give Melur my drawing. It is quite a... delicate situation, and I do not wish to ruin things between us.'Your words have pushed Emmathron to act. Whether his gift will be accepted is up to his friend, Melur.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 6'You should talk to Emmathron near the stable-master in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'${PLAYER}, I have decided that it is time to give Melur my drawing. Despite its unsatisfactory quality, it's the only drawing I've managed to finish. I doubt I would do better with another attempt. No, I know I wouldn't. I need to accept that.

'Would you come with me to Melur's home? I do not believe this is something I can do alone.''I shall lead the way.''Perhaps I shouldn't have seen Melur at all tonight... my presence must have caused undue stress on his health.

'Leave me to my thoughts, ${PLAYER}. You do not deserve my misery.'Melur has invited you and Emmathron to an afternoon of gardening.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 7'You should talk to Emmathron near the stable-master in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'${PLAYER}, Melur has invited us over for some gardening. Have you any idea why he would invite me?'

When you explain that Melur truly wants to see him again, Emmathron hesitates, wringing some of the fabric on his clothes.

'I did not think that would be the case... but if you say so.''One moment, while I... prepare myself... for Melur's inevitable wrath.''I drew something I liked. I drew something I liked! Some aspects could have been drawn a little better, but -- oh, does perfection matter? I drew something and did not want to immediately set it ablaze. I had almost forgotten what that feels like.

'I had almost forgotten what it was like to spend time with Melur, too. I shunned his company for so many months. But you've shown me that it's not too late to change -- that I can still fix things between us.'With renewed inspiration and determination, Emmathron finally sets out to finish his gift for Melur.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 8'You should talk to Emmathron in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'${PLAYER}, would you accompany me to the site of the first landscape again? It may be worth recreating the drawing I discarded outside Melur's house.

'Realizing that I haven't lost my artistic touch yet has been refreshing; I am eager to draw whatever I can. And... well, I would be remiss to not give Melur a gift after this whole ordeal.''May this attempt fare better than the last.''While I would prefer to rush over and give Melur my drawing right this moment, I do not wish to come by unannounced. He deserves a proper apology along with my gift.

'Finding the right time for that conversation shouldn't take long -- and rest assured, I shall not avoid this forever.'The time has come for Emmathron to deliver his gift and apology to Melur.You should talk to Emmathron to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Emmathron, Chapter 9'You should talk to Emmathron near the stable-master in Idhobel or at your home.Talk to Emmathron'${PLAYER}, I am ready to deliver my painting and apology. I should have done this long ago, but better to do it late than not at all.

'Would you like to come with me? I could go alone, but I believe Melur rather enjoys your company. As do I.''Your company is much appreciated.''That went... much better than I think I deserved, ${PLAYER}. But if Melur deemed my apology acceptable, then the past is in the past.

'He has many years ahead of him still, and I do not plan on wasting a single one.'Basil Wyndham fell asleep after stealing away to engage in some festival fun, allowing the kegs in the town centre to run perilously low.

