<rgb=#FF0000>After accepting this quest, you can complete it to gain a map to the Party Tree in the Shire, where you can join the Festival. </rgb>The Fall Festival is in full swing! Join the hobbits in the Shire to begin your festivities.

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will grant you a map to the Party Tree, where you can join the festival. </rgb>Rosentyl Flutch, a busy mother of five, wants to make a traditional soup but lacks ingredients.Rosentyl has asked you to get the ingredients she needs to make cawl. The butcher, Cunedda Moltgig, should have some lamb for her. You should go into Clegur's butcher shop and talk to Cunedda.Talk to Cunedda MoltgigClegur's butcher, Cunedda Moltgig, has indicated that you can take the meat reserved for Rosentyl from the table inside the butcher shop.Collect a package of lamb meatRosentyl has asked you to get the ingredients she needs to make cawl. Gloron Magimrud, at the farm atop the hill in Clegur, should have some vegetables for her.Talk to Gloron MagimrudGloron Magimrud has said you can take some of the potatoes and carrots from his harvest, beside him in Clegur's fields.Collect carrotsCollect potatoesRosentyl has asked you to get the ingredients she needs to make cawl. She said you can talk to the provisioner's assistant about getting some leeks. You should talk to Bortho Bishel, in front of the Boat and Basket tavern.Talk to Bortho Bishel, the Provisioner's AssistantBortho Bishel, the Provisioner's Assistant, has said that you can take some leeks from the crate on the waggon beside the Provisioner.Collect leeksYou have collected all of the ingredients Rosentyl Flutch needs to make cawl. You should bring them to her in front of her home in Clegur.'Do ye fancy the daffodils? They're all right if ye ask me, but my favourite part of the festival is the feastin'. Ye can't have a Daffodil Days without cawl. 'Tis a simple and hearty soup with meat that melts in yer mouth and tender root vegetables that are sweet as sugar.

'I need to get a pot goin', but I haven't got the ingredients. Naturally, my children are nowhere to be seen. An irksome lot, they are! If ye want to be of some help to a busy mam, would you pick up some groceries for me?

'Cunedda the butcher should have some lamb for me. Gloron up the hill has the carrots and potatoes, and I'll need some leeks from the provisioner. Just talk to her assistant and he'll get them for you.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Hullo! Lamb for Rosentyl Flutch? It's over by there, on the table. Help yerself, I'm proper overwhelmed with orders. She's already paid, she has, so take it and be on yer way.''Ach, I forgot to pack somthin' up for Rosey. I knew I was forgettin' somthin'. There's some taters and some carrots right here. Go on and grab a few of each for Rose. Don't ye worry, she'll be good for it, she will.''Leeks? We have proper crates of 'em! Ye'll find 'em on the back of the waggon over by there. Go on and take some. I'll add 'em to Mrs. Flutch's tab.''Back already? There's lovely, look at those taters! It was proper good of ye to help me, it was. I would invite ye to supper, but do ye have any idea how hard it is to keep five children fed? Proper hobbit appetites, they have!'Talk to Ransroth to gain rep.Speak with Ransroth'Speak with me to gain rep with the Ents of Fangorn.''"Acquaintance" with the Ents of Fangorn with a side of wasabi, coming right up!'Talk to Ransroth to gain rep.Speak with Ransroth'Speak with me to gain rep with the Ents of Fangorn.''"Friend" with the Ents of Fangorn with a side of wasabi, coming right up!'Talk to Ransroth to gain rep.Speak with Ransroth'Speak with me to gain rep with the Ents of Fangorn.''"Ally" with the Ents of Fangorn with a side of wasabi, coming right up!'Talk to Ransroth to gain rep.Speak with Ransroth'Speak with me to gain rep with the Ents of Fangorn.''"Kindred" with the Ents of Fangorn with a side of wasabi, coming right up!'The annual Farmers Faire is in town for the harvest! Each day you may claim a few tickets for free to try out some of the events offered in the Faire.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>A Festival Announcer can be found in the centre of Bywater during the Farmers Faire festival.

You should speak with her to claim your free Festival Tickets!Claim your tickets to the Farmers Faire'Each day we offer a few tickets to Faire-goers to sample the games we have available - try out Maggot's Mushrooms over at the Bamfurlongs, or the Egg Scramble down at Farmer Sandson's place!

<rgb=#00FF00>Note: If you would like to purchase additional tickets, they'll be available from the LOTRO Store via the hobbits who run the games!</rgb>''Here are your tickets, ${PLAYER}! Have fun and enjoy the Faire!'The young hobbits of the Shire have long held a tradition of sneaking into Farmer Maggot's fields to make off with the succulent mushrooms that grow in the shade of the grain rows. Farmer Maggot does not take kindly to these trespassers, and each year around the harvest season, he unleashes his three dogs, Fang, Grip, and Wolf, into the fields to chase off any ne'er-do-well hobbits. This year a small group of enterprising hobbits has organized these raids into an unofficial 'event' of the Farmers Faire, forming groups to try to make off with the wild mushrooms.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>'You should head into the field shortly. We will be trying to find some of those delicious mushrooms growing out there...but be careful: once Farmer Maggot notices us out in the field, he will surely sic those dogs of his on us. You need to stay away from them!

'Come back here once you've eaten your fill of mushrooms.'Wait for the game to beginGather at least five mushrooms.Devour mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Avoid Maggot's dogsYou have succeeded in devouring five of Maggot's mushrooms...eat as many more as you can before the game is over!Gather more mushroomsAvoid Maggot's dogsTalk to Osbert Puddifoot to receive your tokens for winning the Mushroom Hunt.Talk to Osbert Puddifoot'Hoy there, ${PLAYER}! We're about to send in the next group of raiders into Farmer Maggot's fields. Be careful, though...our activities this year have Grip, Fang, and Wolf in a regular frenzy. You will need to get those mushrooms quickly before they catch your scent.

'Oh, but watch what you eat...several of our participants have reported some pretty strange effects from some of the rarer varieties of mushroom this year.''Wow! You ran circles around Farmer Maggot's dogs. I hope you left some mushrooms for everyone else!'Wymarc Grubb is overseeing the annual Egg Scramble, where hobbits and visitors, young and old alike, scramble about after Farmer Sandson's chickens, hoping to gather up eggs laid in panic. It seems that Sandson's special chicken feed may have had some unusual ingredients this year though, because some of the eggs his chickens are laying have decidedly strange hues. Still, perhaps egg collectors will see some value in them?

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>Sandson's Egg Scramble will begin shortly. Your goal is to collect at least five white eggs -- but you can earn additional tokens by collecting extra eggs... and especially for collecting the rare coloured eggs!

Wait in the chicken yard until Wymarc Grubb declares the game underway.Wait for the game to beginGather five white eggs as quickly as you can.Collect white eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have succeeded in gathering five white eggs -- get as many more as you can before the game is over.

You should try to grab any festive eggs that you spot.Gather more eggsTalk to Wymarc Grubb to receive your tokens for winning the Egg Scramble.Talk to Wymarc Grubb'Hey there, ${PLAYER}! Have you come to take part in Sandson's Egg Scramble? Well here are the rules: Just remain in the chicken yard here. When the event begins, Sandson's finest chickens will come out of their coops and start laying eggs! They tend to become a bit perturbed what with all the folk about, so they'll run about a lot, and things can get a bit confusing.

'If you can collect five white eggs before I call time, you'll win a bonus in Faire tokens!  Also, opening the eggs will also grant additional tokens whether you win or lose.

'Oh, I should mention that some mischief-maker seems to have slipped some unusual ingredients into the chickens' feed, and we've been getting some rather, er, unusual eggs now and again. Seems that there are collectors that value them though, so while they won't count towards the Egg Scramble, you may want to grab them nonetheless.''You've got quick feet and steady hands, ${PLAYER}! Congratulations on winning Sandson's Egg Scramble!

'Please come play again...and keep an eye out for any festive eggs you see out there. I hear that there are collectors with an eye for such things.'The leader of the Cook's Guild has asked to see what your Nine Star Pie looks like—or tastes like!The crafting recipes you must create can be found in your crafting panel.

