<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Speak to Gredlan Mugwort.Speak to Gredlan Mugwort'Avery needs help when it comes to collecting flowers but he's rather particular about who he lets aid him. He wants to know that person has secured a place for the flowers to go. Let me know if you're interested in a ticket that will prove to him we've spoken.''Present this ticket to Avery and he'll know you've found a buyer for the flowers.'By completing this quest, you can select any type of available festival tokens.'Do you want a lot of festival tokens? I sure hope so, since I have a lot to give!''Come back here to celebrate some more!'Collect a skulk of foxes.Collect a skulk of foxes.Call the Ithilien Fox to your sideCall the Red Fox to your sideCall the Brown Fox to your sideCall the Sleek Fox to your sideBarliman Butterbur, proprietor of the Prancing Pony, has found himself pleasantly overwhelmed during Bree's celebration of Midsummer.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Drunken revellers and forsaken mugs can be found throughout the Prancing Pony in Bree.

Barliman has asked you to coax drunken revellers off the tables before they can kick more of his crockery into the corners of the Prancing Pony. He has also asked you to gather any mugs abandoned by drunken revellers in unusual spots in the inn.Find and retrieve abandoned mugs in the Prancing Pony (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Coax drunken revellers off tables in the Prancing Pony (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Deliver the mugs to Barliman Butterbur at the entrance to the inn.'Hello and welcome to the Prancing Pony!

'Have you come to join in Bree-town's celebration of Midsummer? You would certainly not be the first, I must tell you. It has so often been my duty to alert adventurers like yourself to the needs of others, but I must confess that today, it is I who must ask something of you. You see... even with Bob and Nob about to help me, I was woefully unprepared for how many customers Midsummer would bring to Bree-town!

'Before you join in the festivities and find yourself as merry as some of my patrons, could you do me a favour? Some of the patrons have taken a bit too much to drink and have found themselves atop my tables. Normally, such practices do not bother me, but they've begun to damage my crockery and I've no time to step out to speak to them myself. Also, Nob informed me that they've taken to leaving their mugs in the strangest of places about the Pony.

'Find as many mugs as you can and coax the most drunken of the revellers down off my tables, would you? But do not be too harsh with them!''They left the mugs where?! Goodness me, I don't think I'd ever have found them. Not in a crowd like this!

'I do hope none of the patrons were upset by my request. The folk come to celebrate Midsummer seem a good-natured sort, but I would not be much of an inn-keeper if there were no inn left to keep!

'You have been a great help, ${PLAYER}. Can I offer you something?'Virgil Greenfield needs help filling out the snowman field outside of Winter-home. He has directed you to try your hand at crafting one of his snowmen.

