You should return to Flobert Chubb at once.Show Flobert Chubb what incredible luck you had'I have just the challenge for you, ${PLAYER}. I hope you like a good gamble.

'You have an excellent opportunity to fish up all the lovely fish you want, and those fish will naturally earn you admiration in the Fisherman Faction, as well as the fine rewards that go with it.

'However, one bad fish can spoil it all. Just one fish, and it's all over for the day. Your luck is done. That fish may be elusive at first, but the more you fish, the more likely you are to pull up that ominous fish that nobody wants....

'Best of luck to you! You'll need it.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The outcome of this quest is based on luck, and is not affected by fishing skill.</rgb>'Nobody likes bad fish. Bad fish spoil everything.''I...I can't believe it. Do you know how low the odds are of catching so many good fish in a row, and avoiding the bad fish? As more fish are caught, it gets harder and harder to win.

'You're the best Fisher-${RACE} ever, ${PLAYER}!'The shoe-maker of Duillond is having some trouble wresting supplies for linens from the hoarding weaver.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Tanathron is in Duillond, near the ovens and the Boot-maker.

You should speak with Tanathron about procuring flax fibre for linen shrew-stomping boots.Speak with TanathronFlax grows in the grasses along the road to Celondim that leads south from Duillond.

You should collect stalks of flax so that Tanathron's precarious supply can remain perfectly balanced.Collect flax plants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tanathron, the weaver, is in Duillond near the ovens.

You should bring the flax plants to Tanathron to refurbish his dwindling supply.Deluraw stands near the ovens in Duillond.

You should bring the desired flax fibres to Deluraw, for they are apparently very difficult to come by.'This is getting absurd. Tanathron over there, that weaver -- yes, the one glaring my way -- simply will not give me fibres for the linen I need for the special boots.

'My supplies are running low, and he is a key supplier, but he refuses to help me! It is because his own supply of flax is running low, and he hoards his ingredients so that his stock never depletes.

'I am afraid I've gone and made him angry with my demands. Perhaps you can reason with him; please try, ${PLAYER}.''He is an absurd Elf if I've ever met one, that Tanathron. So greedy with his ingredients! See how he glares at me?''What? So I like having a balanced supply of ingredient and product. What of it? If I have no ingredients, tomorrow I shall have no product. I do not think it is unreasonable for me to demand ingredients if I am going to generously give of my finite supply.

'If you want your own ingredients for your own endeavours, you will have to collect ingredients for me first. Flax plants grow along the road to Celondim. You'll be able to see the pale blue flowers amongst the grasses.''Good. Now we can proceed with our arrangement. At least someone around here can be reasonable, AHEM!

'Here are some flax fibres.''Splendid, ${PLAYER}! Your patience and politeness did wonders here, I see. 

'Tanathron is a stubborn fool who has no business being in this trade, but it is what it is, and I should learn to make do.

'Unfortunately, I have a sad feeling that I will go through the same thing all over again tomorrow, when my supplies run low again.'The people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...The people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...Defeat the Easterlings in the clearingThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...Defend the clearing from the Easterling assaultThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...The people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...Defeat the Easterlings in the clearingThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...Defend the clearing from the Easterling assaultA florist in Minas Tirith needs help finding her wayward daughter.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>The florist's daughter was sent to the First Circle of Minas Tirith to gather flowers.

You should look for the florist's daughter.Find the florist's daughterFlowers can be found in the gardens and green spaces of the First Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should collect flowers for the florist's daughter.Collect summer blossoms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The florist's daughter can be found on the First Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should bring the flowers to the florist's daughter.Return to the florist's daughterThe florist's daughter's blanket is on the First Circle of Minas Tirith.

Assemble the flowers into crowns on the blanket.The florist is on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith.

Bring the floral crowns to the florist.'Welcome, friend! I heard you shall be assisting us during the festivities. Glad I am, to hear this!

'I sent my daughter down to the First Circle to gather flowers, which I planned to weave into floral crowns. She is a good lass, but does tend to get distracted. If you find yourself down there, would you be so kind as to look for her?''Oh, hello! Have you come to play with us?'

You tell her of her mother’s concerns. The young girl gasps with almost theatrical drama.

'Oh no! I totally forgot about the flowers! Will… will you help me gather them? It will go twice as quickly with you by my side! That is, if you have the time.''I was right! You found twice as much as me! You can use the blankets to put down your flowers. Uhm, I know you have already done so much for me, however… if we weave these into crowns for mother, it will make her smile so much!

'And maybe she will not be upset that I got distracted…. Oh, and when you are done, could you tell her I am going to eat with father for dinner? Thank you!''Ah, you're back! She got you to make them for her, didn't she?'

You give her the message from her daughter.

'Hmph. Dinner with her father? Well, that will save me some time tonight. Honestly, that child will do whatever she needs to in order to shirk her duties. At least she chose someone crafty for her chores. These look marvellous, friend. Thank you for your help!'Naffa Blodven has come to Daffodil Days from Mossward to purchase the best daffodil bulbs in Eriador, but the Stoors of Clegur say they aren't for sale.Naffa has asked you to talk to Welduth Lhush, a Stoor reputed to have the best daffodils and the festival, and ask her if you can trade for some bulbs.Talk to Welduth LhushWelduth agreed to trade some daffodil bulbs in exchange for Gloron Magimrud's secret to growing carrots. You should talk to Gloron Magimrud in the farming fields of Clegur.Talk to Gloron MagimrudGloron has told you that he will give you the secret to his high-quality carrots if you get a daffodil banner and place it by the barn. You should talk to Clegur's Mayor, Malmadog Torlan, to see if you can get another banner.Talk to Malmadog TorlanMayor Malmadog has given you a daffodil banner. You should place it in the ground in front of the large barn by Clegur's farming fields.You have placed a daffodil banner in front of the barn, as Gloron Magimrud asked. You should talk to Gloron, still in the fields.Talk to Gloron MagimrudGloron Magimrud has shared his secret to growing good carrots with you. You should return to Welduth Lhush in front of her home in Clegur and tell her.Talk to Welduth LhushWelduth Lhush has relented and said you can take the pot of her prized daffodil bulbs to her left. You should collect the bulbs so you can give them to Naffa Blodven.Collect the prized daffodil bulbsYou have gotten some daffodil bulbs from Welduth Lhush. You should bring them to Naffa Blodven near Clegur's stable-master.'It's good to see a fellow traveller. I came here from Mossward, to the west of here. A travelling trader told me that this is where I should come to get the finest daffodil bulbs in Eriador. They are indeed quite beautiful, but these Stoors say they aren't for sale!

'Gardening is only a hobby for me, but I don't want to have come here for nothing. Welduth Lhush over there is said to have the finest daffodils, but I think I may have already earned her ire. Would you mind talking to her, and asking if she would sell or trade for some of her prized bulbs?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Ach, another stranger tryin' to get their grubby hands on my bulbs? As I told the other one, I'm not in the business of sellin'.'

You ask her if there is anything she would trade. She sighs and thinks about it for a moment before answering.

'Well, to tell ya truly, yes. I've always envied Gloron's carrots. Proper carrots, they are! Large, but not woody, and they roast so sweet...'

She gazes off into the distance for a moment, thinking about carrots.

'Yes, if ye can get Gloron's secret to growin' such fine carrots, I'll give ye some of my daffodil bulbs. But good luck to ye! He holds his secrets close, he does. Ye'll likely have better luck pryin' a coney out of a wolf's jaws.''Welduth covets my carrot secrets, does she?'

Gloron laughs.

'Why, she's never bothered to ask! If she did, she would find that I would tell her freely, I would. But since ye're doin' tradin', I'll make ye' a trade as well.

'I seen those tidy daffodil banners stuck about the village, and I find myself wonderin' why I didn't get one. It's not really fair, is it? I'm only sayin'.

'If ye get me one of those banners and stick it in over by the barn, I'll give ye the 'secret'.''Another banner? Ach, here, take it. I never wanted the things in the first place.''There's lovely! That's a good banner, it is!

'Well, ye kept up yer end of the bargain, so here's my 'secret'. Everyone knows ye must have loose soil for 'em to get big, but most folks give 'em too much fertilizer. If ye fertilize 'em, yer carrot gets big and leafy up top, but the root stays small. Don't fertilize 'em at all, I say.

'I don't know about flowers, but most vegetables need to struggle a bit. It's the struggle that gives 'em proper character. A lot like people, eh?''The secret is to not fertilize them? Are ye pullin' my leg? That Gloron is a shrewd one, he is. Probably havin' a laugh, takin' me for a fool.

'Still, I believe ye that that's what he said, so ye did yer part. Ye can have the pot of bulbs to my left. Take it, and be gone with ye.''Bless me, you got them! I'm as surprised as I am grateful! It's nothing personal, but I didn't expect you to succeed. Thank you!'Old tales tell of eight Entwives who passed from the south into the Old Forest, never to be seen again. Could they be true?Find the flowers marking the passing of the eight Entwives within the Old Forest.You have found the flower of Rhosthon. It is believed that she was once an Entwife who stood with vigilance over her gardens. None could approach without her knowledge, and those with evil intent would feel her gaze upon them and flee.

She passed into the Old Forest many long years ago and became part of the forest, granting her keen senses to the trees and creatures herein that evil might not approach unseen, for those were dark days and few places remained that were untouched by the power of Sauron.

The flowers are said to mark the place where she disappeared into the forest and seem to have been tended by someone.You have discovered the flower of Neldorlas, an Entwife of old. It was she who was foremost in the arts of nurturing the young, that they might achieve their potential in the fullness of time.

Not one seed did she plant, nor youthful mind touch that did not come to fruition, unless it was struck down by unfortunate fate. Such was her understanding of the arts of cultivation and teaching.

As with her sisters, she chose to become a part of the Old Forest, that it might endure the encroachment of darkness and evil throughout the years. So the folk tales say, anyway.The flower you found marks the place where the Entwife Dorollin passed into the Old Forest, perhaps forever.

She was among the largest of her kind, taller than any other, for the essence of all that grows was at the core of her nature. Her gardens were sprawling places wrapped in great vines, and enormous trees cast their shade upon acres of fertile ground.

She gave herself to the Old Forest to ensure that it would grow great enough to protect itself from the incursion of evil such as Orcs and thoughtless Men.

Some folk say that one day they will awaken and emerge from the forest - but no one knows when that might be.You discovered Cordofoneth's flower -- said to be one of eight Entwife sisters. Among her kin, she held most dear her affection for all living things.

It was this affection that she lent the Old Forest when she passed into its depths long ago, that all manner of living things might find shelter within its bounds. The flower you have found marks the place where she entered the forest, and she has not been seen since.

Alas, the Old Forest has oft been harmed by Men or intruded upon by darker powers, and so it is said that her heart lies muted, and she sleeps more deeply than her sisters. Perhaps she is awaiting the day when this world might become a place of lighter moods and the love of life is not so easily betrayed by axe or fire.You have discoverd the flower of Lenhwest. She was believed to be an Entwife known for her unquenchable passions. She could love as no other, but fury and despair were also her constant companions.

Amongst her sisters, she was the first to give herself to the forest, swept by her own emotions to ensure its survival during the trials of those dark years. Her presence is strongly felt in these woods still.

It is for fear of Lenhwest's tempestuous anger that folk walk with care in the Old Forest, for many believe that if her heart turns against you, it is unlikely you will ever emerge from it again!You have found Silloth's flower. She was said to have been a wonderous spirit - her heart was unbowed even during the ancient war that drove the Entwife sisters here, for mirth and frivolity ever followed in her wake, and her gardens were believed to be places where even the weariest of mortals could bring themselves to smile and laugh.

Among the Elves she was particularly beloved, and of those who remember her they fear they may never again hear the sound of her laughter beneath the boughs of ancient trees.The flower of Braiglad is seen as a warning by superstitious folk who would dare the depths of the Old Forest. She was an Entwife unusual amongst her sisters, for she was a wild and capricious being. Her gardens were populated by untamed beasts, and even the most delicate flowers within them were adorned with sharp thorns.

Braiglad rarely spoke with mortals, preferring the wild places of the forest, and in time she gave herself to the forest to protect it from the dark powers.

There are those who say her spirit is strongest when aroused by wild and dangerous times such as these.The tale of Merillif's flower often brings tears to those who hear it. Of the eight Entwives who came to the Old Forest, she was the most beautiful and the most beloved of all.

Her gardens shone with a brilliance of colour that even the finest artisans of the Firstborn would regard with envy. Her jewels were said to be the petals of flowers, and while they would last but a short season -- unlike the gems of the Noldor which are forever -- their beauty far surpassed that of any object carved of stone or crystal. This passing beauty was such that it endured no greed, and so the vanity of evil hearts could neither possess nor endure it.

Those who are fond of the story say that she will awaken some day when beauty can again be shared amongst all the creatures of Arda without fear of despoilment or jealous vanity.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. You have seen an unusual breed of flower that grows within the depths of the Old Forest? Their origins are most unusual.

'As the old tale goes, eight Entwives came into this forest from the distant south many years ago and took shelter here beneath the boughs of the Old Forest. But darkness was everywhere in the lands in those times, and Tom thought it wise that the sisters should pass into the heart of the forest where no evil might reach.

'The flowers I speak of mark the places where each of the Entwives disappeared into the weave of the forest, and it is possible to understand their nature in those places.

'Only Tom knows when or if they will ever awaken from their slumber, and he will not tell even me!'Vinca Pott wants to decorate tables at the Party Tree with smelly flowers, but she'll need some outside help to complete the job.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Gather some foul flowers from Vinca's basket.

Vinca wants you to "decorate" a couple of tables around the Party Tree with her flowers.Gather foul flowers from Vinca's basketVinca is targeting two tables around the Party Tree, specifically the ones with empty vases.

You should place your flowers in the vases while avoiding Caltha's helpers.Carry the flowers to the tables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF0000>You must not be spotted by Caltha's helpers</rgb>The tables now have bouquets of smelly flowers thanks to your efforts.

Vinca will want to hear about your deed.'Hullo! Come to enjoy the party too? Well, my friends and I think it could use a little more excitement!

'We wanted to decorate the tables with smelly flowers, but everyone always has their eyes on us. On account of our previous "misdeeds", I'd wager. But I'm sure you're an upstanding ${RACE}! No need to worry about people spying on you.

'The two tables you'll be looking for have empty vases. Just watch out for Caltha Goodchild's helpers. They've got the eyes of hawks.

'Grab some flowers from my basket when you're ready!''Job well done! Caltha and her helpers will catch wind of what we've accomplished, but don't worry -- they may suspect my friends and me, but they won't suspect you at all.

'We should do this again some other time! But one last thing: if anyone asks you, pretend we never met.'A quick hand can oft mean the difference between victory and defeat.Use FlurryGeorge feels that help must be found from beyond the Shire to defend against the invading wolves.George is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should speak with George.The fox is along the Stock road. Old Sally often wanders into the hills east of Tuckborough, east of Sandson's Farm. Fang, Grip, and Wolf patrol Bamfurlong, far to the east of Sandson's Farm and south along the Brandywine River.

George has asked you to speak with the creatures of the Shire. You should seek out and speak with the fox, Old Sally, Fang, Grip, and Wolf in the Shire.'I'm a pig, you fool rooster! Can't you see I'm in enough trouble as it is, what with all these nasty shrews about? Sometimes I wish that I was a pony.''What do you want? Protect your coop against wolves? I have my own farm to protect and no time for others.

'My but you would make a nice snack. Be on your way, rooster.''Shooing off a few wolves is mighty tempting, but I've too much work to do here. Besides, what if the wolves come here?''Ho there, rooster! You aren't one of ours! What are you doing here? Trying to steal some of our hens for your coop?

'Wolves? We haven't any wolves around here, but if they show their shaggy faces at Bamfurlong, you can be sure we'll deal with them.''I thank you for your bravery, my fellow rooster, but I fear that it may not have been enough to save many of us from a terrible fate. While you were away, I had time to think over the circumstances and consider our options. If we do nothing, our numbers will surely dwindle. A similar doom befell Dora Brownlock's coop, and I fear ours is not far off.  

'I cannot leave the coop; I have too many responsibilities with half of the coop under my supervision. I will set this task upon you: travel out into the world, even beyond the borders of the Shire. Speak with other animals you encounter and see if you can find anyone willing to help us in our plight.

'You should begin by seeking out animals here in the Shire.''Now what is this? First three hobbits sleeping in the forest, and now a chicken?

'You want me to help protect your coop from wolves? My friend, I would sooner eat you, particularly since chicken is very high among my dietary choices.

'However, seeing as you were brave enough to speak with me in the first place, I will forego my lunch for now.''You must speak with the other animals of the Shire! Evil is coming...I am sure of it!'George feels that help must be found from beyond the Shire to defend against the invading wolves.The horse is at Hengstacer. The grey squirrel can be found on an island in the southern part of Nen Harn. Wink the cat may be found in Bree. Sniken can be found in the south-east part of the Midgewater Marshes, in Roderick Neeker-friend's camp, on a hill above the Goblinhole Ruins. The cow can be found in Newbury in Buckland.

George has asked you to speak with the creatures of Bree-land. You should seek out and speak with the horse, the grey squirrel, Wink the cat, Sniken, and the cow in Bree-land.'Oh, please! My dear rooster, we have much more important things to do, such as napping. Besides, we must keep our mistress's house clear of mice and rats. We haven't time to run all the way to the Shire!''Who art thou, rooster? I am a noble steed of Rohan. Thy troubles are beneath my hooves.

'Even were I of a mind to lend thee aid, I have not long been in this place and know not of this land called the Shire. Begone, bird, for I have naught to do with thee.''Wolves? Ha! We fear no wolves! They will not withstand our onslaught. They will be the next to fall!

'After we destroy the helpless red squirrels, we shall conquer the wolves, and then the world! No one can stop us!''Oh dear! I found such lovely grass here, but I can't seem to find my way back off the roof of this hobbit-hole. Do you see a path?

'My dear rooster, how can I help you when I am stuck here? If I could find a way down, I might speak with my bull...wolves are too vicious for me.''I am trapped in a cage out in the middle of the Midgewater Marshes, and you want me to help you? I think you have it backwards, rooster. I am the one in need of help.

'This Man here is more than a bit mad! If he throws any more of those dreadful dead midges in this cage, I think my carapace is going to split!'George feels that help must be found from beyond the Shire to defend against the invading wolves.The lynx-mother is at Thrasi's Lodge in Ered Luin, north of Celondim and Duillond.

George has asked you to speak to the creatures of Ered Luin. You should seek out and speak with the lynx-mother.'You wish for me to protect a chicken coop? Until I was wounded, I fed my cub by stealing chickens.

'Well, I would rather steal them, than chase them, so begone with you.'George feels that help must be found from beyond the Shire to defend against the invading wolves.George has asked you to speak to the creatures of Evendim. You should seek out and speak with Longbough, the Ent in Evendim.'Hoom, hrom! Well now, wolves you say? Despicable creatures, and cruel. But the Shire is too far away.

'I have my own forest and my own troubles to attend. I am sorry, but I cannot help you.'George feels that help must be found from beyond the Shire to defend against the invading wolves.Radagast the Brown may be found in the tower at Ost Guruth.

George has asked you to speak to the creatures of the Lone-lands. You should seek out and speak with Radagast the Brown in the Lone-lands.'Greetings, my little rooster-friend! What is this? Your coops are threatened by wolves?

'Wolves are among the most craven of the Dark Lord's servants, and this proves them even more so. Unfortunately, the troubles here are much greater, with effects more far-reaching, than those which trouble the Shire.

'I am sorry, but I cannot leave the Eglain just yet.'George feels that help must be found from beyond the Shire to defend against the invading wolves.The aurochs yearling can be found amidst the small herd to the south-east of Gatson's farm.

George has asked you to speak with the creatures of the North Downs. You should seek out and speak with the aurochs yearling in the North Downs.'Are you here to help me? I'm lost and cannot find my way. Do you know where my mother is?

'The Shire? My mother is in the Shire? Oh, you want me to protect your coops from wolves. No, I couldn't do that. The wolves would eat me.'George feels that help must be found from beyond the Shire to defend against the invading wolves.Roheryn can be found at the stables in Rivendell.

George has asked you to speak with the creatures of the Trollshaws. You should seek out and speak with Roheryn in the Trollshaws.'I am the steed of Aragorn son of Arathorn, Chieftain of the Dúnedain of the North. What have I to do with chickens?

'I wait here for my master's call, when we will assail the hosts of Mordor. I cannot help thee in the Shire.'Cooks provide for the masses of Umbar Baharbêl, and you are doing your part to help.Complete requests from the Umbar Cook's Guild.

