<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>The mayor stands in the centre of Winter-home, overseeing the events of the Yule Festival.

You should speak with the mayor and find out what he wants from you, though it sounds like he has a sleazy scheme brewing.Find out what the mayor wants from youGareth Rust is in the workers' area in Winter-home, toiling unhappily with his fellow workers.

You should try to get some dirt on Gareth Rust, as his negativity makes him a candidate for being let go.Convince Gareth Rust to confide in youDaley Utteridge stands near Gareth Rust in the workers' area.

You should see if Daley Utteridge will trust you enough to speak of the workers' unhappiness to an outsider.Try to convince Daley Utteridge to confide in you (outsider though you are)Daley Utteridge is in the workers' area of Winter-home.

You should try to persuade Daley Utteridge to tell you more so that the mayor will have the information he seeks.

<rgb=#FF0000>To perform an emote, select your target and type the required emote in your chat window. (Example: '/cheer')</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Talk</rgb> to Daley Utteridge -- maybe he will talk backDaley Utteridge is in the workers' area of Winter-home.

You should try to persuade Daley Utteridge to tell you more so that the mayor will have the information he seeks.

<rgb=#FF0000>To perform an emote, select your target and type the required emote in your chat window. (Example: "/cheer")</rgb>Offer comfort and <rgb=#FF0000>pat</rgb> Daley Utteridge on the headDaley Utteridge is in the workers' area of Winter-home.

You should try to persuade Daley Utteridge to tell you more so that the mayor will have the information he seeks.

<rgb=#FF0000>To perform an emote, select your target and type the required emote in your chat window. (Example: '/cheer')</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Sigh</rgb> your sympathy at Daley UtteridgeDaley Utteridge is in the workers' area of Winter-home.

You should speak with Daley Utteridge and see if he will share the information that the mayor seeks.See if Daley Utteridge will tell you anything usefulThe mayor is in the centre of town among the festival patrons.

You should tell Mayor Goodnough what Daley Utteridge told you concerning Gareth Rust and the record of unsavoury transactions that now lies in his hands.Tell Mayor Goodnough everything you learned from Daley UtteridgeThe mayor wishes for you to meet the two workers in the woods south-east of town.

When you are ready, you should go to the woods and summon the mayor and the workers using the town's Summoning Horn.Use the summoning horn to call the mayor and protect him from the workers' wrathMayor Goodnough is in Winter-home in Frostbluff, awaiting news of your success in the Festival Square.

You should speak with the mayor now that you have helped to save his reputation and return the stolen records to him.'I'll give you the short of it: the mayor is feeling a little suspicious of the workers and wants someone to spy on them to see what's afoot. What you make of this is for you to decide, but I would talk to the mayor if I were you. See if what he has to say is to your liking.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: The rewards for both of these mutually-exclusive quests are UNIQUE to each quest. Please choose your quest carefully!</rgb>'Don't look to me for advice, ${PLAYER}. It's not my role to choose, or help you choose. You must look inside yourself and do what you think is right, for yourself or for others.''${PLAYER}, I hear you're interested in some fine clothing. You have good taste! If you help me, I'll see that you're wearing the finest style that Winter-home has to offer.

'I need your help, you see. When I came into my mayorship, I ignorantly put town money into unstable investments. I let go many workers, but the town is still in trouble. That's why the festival is here -- to raise money! 

'I keep promising them that the festival will help the town, which will let them have their normal wages back. But first I must use the festival profits to get out of my own debt. A southerner told me that there is a very promising investment to be made in a war that seems to be brewing in faraway lands.

'Sadly, the festival didn't raise enough for me to invest properly, so I need to cut back on the workforce again. Can you get some dirt on any disloyal workers? I hear that they trust you....''Oh, if it isn't the mayor's particular friend! I'm surprised he hasn't adopted you as part of the Goodnough family. That's right -- I saw you talking at length with the mayor.

'I've nothing to say to you. Now, if you'll excuse me, I have work to do.''Ah, ${PLAYER}. I am terribly sorry for the way my friend Gareth just spoke to you. He is very unhappy, you see. Many folks are, and it troubles my heart.

'Nay, don't listen to my ramblings. It is just the heaviness of winter that troubles me. I do not wish to burden you while you're visiting our town. Please, go back and enjoy the festivities!''I appreciate your sympathy, ${PLAYER}. I think talking to you might help to ease my mind, for I can see that you have a good soul.

'You see, my friend Gareth recently found a stray paper after Guard Frostway from the town vault came to make his nightly collection for the store-house. Gareth kept the fallen record, though I told him he should return it to Guard Frostway, and he read its contents.

'I am sure he must be mistaken, but he claims that the mayor has made some very unsavoury investments of the town's money, and that is why we work as hard as we do, for so little, and why so many folks are out of work.

'I couldn't believe it, ${PLAYER}. I am sure Gareth read it wrong. He is angry though...I do not know what he means to do.''Gareth Rust found my records? And Daley Utteridge told you, a visitor, all about it? Surely he means to blackmail me. It seems you caught them just in time, for it looks as though they meant to expose me in front of everyone. Well, they will both be sorry!

'One more favour, if you please, ${PLAYER}. I would ask you to meet me outside of town for some unpleasant business regarding this little issue you've uncovered.

'There is a summons-horn in the woods. Use it when you're ready, and I'll come to you. I'll send word to the workers to heed the call as well. I'm afraid there shall be a bit of a confrontation....''I knew we were wrong to ever trust you, ${PLAYER}! What is the mayor giving you for your troubles? How many loaves of bread could be bought with your reward, eh?''Ha! You showed them, ${PLAYER}! That was well done. Now I'll surely have enough money for this new investment, thanks to what I'll save from having to pay those two ingrates.

'As promised, here is your lavish reward. I appreciate everything you've done here!'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is your last chance to choose another path, and the other set of rewards.</rgb>Ermentrude Haybank, the Maze-master of Wistmead, asks of you to gather some of the amazing decorative gourds that grow within the wheat-walls.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>The Wistmead wheat maze can be found in the Wistmead Harvest Festival space.

Ermentrude Haybank has tasked you with gathering decorative gourds.Pick ripe gourds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Wistmead wheat maze can be found in the Wistmead Harvest Festival space.

You should bring the gourds to Ermentrude Haybank at the wheat maze entrance.'There are some truly wondrous gourds growing in the old wheat field. Gather some so that we may decorate!''How wonderful! Look at all these decorative gourds!''It is decorative gourd season!'Khâtaphos needs more people willing to travel Middle-earth to spread the word about Furtherholm and attract more guests.Captain Khâtaphos has made a list of places he would like someone to visit and promote Furtherholm. You should pick a location to go to.At Khâtaphos' request, you have gone to a location on his list and successfully promoted Furtherholm. You should return to him inside The Cracked Flagon to claim your reward.Talk to Khâtaphos in Furtherholm'Tell me, ${PLAYER}, would you be interested in helping me? Unfortunately, this undertaking would have you leave the island again. But I have no doubt you can find your way back! It may also have you travelling to far-off lands, some of which may be a difficult journey. The more experienced a traveller you are, the easier it should be, I think.

'What I need is more people like Ikhajât, going out into the world and finding others who might want to visit Furtherholm. Someone to help spread the word that this is a wonderful place to visit and all are welcome here!

'I have some specific places in mind where you could go to find people who might need a holiday in a warm and friendly place that has many good wines! In fact, I have made a list! Would you like to see it?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you return to me! I hear that you were successful and brought us another visitor to the island. That is wonderful! I knew I could count on you! Here is a reward for your trouble.'Khâtaphos needs people willing to travel Middle-earth all throughout Midsummer to spread the word about Furtherholm and attract more guests.Complete the quest Gathering Guests (Daily) seven times during the Midsummer Festival.Complete Gathering Guests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'I need more people like Ikhajât, going out into the world and finding others who might want to visit Furtherholm. Someone to help spread the word that this is a wonderful place to visit and all are welcome here!

'Do this seven times, and you will be well rewarded.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Men of Bree who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Bree and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Bree-town for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in Bree-townYou have found potential visitors in Bree. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'I have heard that right in the middle of Eriador is a city that answers to no king. It sits along an important trade route and is surrounded by green lands, but it does not sound like it is as prosperous as I should think. Perhaps these people could learn how to better profit from trade by meeting our fine Umbari merchants!

'Go to this "Bree-town" and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation to visit us in Zír Aktar. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Bree and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Elves of Ered Luin who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Celondim in Ered Luin and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Celondim for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in CelondimYou have found potential visitors in Celondim. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'I have the joy of meeting many people, and from these people, I learn many things. A Longbeard that I am pleased to call my friend told me of his home, Ered Luin, the Blue Mountains. There he says dwell Elves! I do not think my friend would lie to me, as fantastic as it sounds.

'He gave me the name of a village, Celondim, situated upon a mighty river. Go to this Celondim and see if there is an Elf who might cheerfully accept an invitation to visit us in Zír Aktar. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Celondim in Ered Luin and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Men of Dale who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Dale and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Dale for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in DaleYou have found potential visitors in Dale. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'During my time at sea, we ah... confiscated kegs of a biscuit called "Dale-men's Cram" on more than one occasion. I cannot say much for the taste, but they are quite hearty and can sustain men at sea for some time. It begs the question, though, who are these Men of Dale, and do they not know of flavoured foods? We can introduce them to many spices!

'This Dale must be somewhere north along the great river you call the Anduin. Go there and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to this Dale and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Rohirrim of Edoras who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Edoras in the Kingstead of West Rohan and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Edoras for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in EdorasYou have found potential visitors in Edoras. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'The barbarians of Rohan are no friend to the Umbari. But... neither should I consider them enemies any longer. Most especially if some wealthy horse-lord wants to spend his coin here! Who am I to deny them such an opportunity?

'Go to Edoras and there find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation to visit us here in Zír Aktar. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Edoras in the Kingstead of West Rohan and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Dunlendings of Galtrev who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Galtev in Dunland and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Galtrev for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in GaltrevYou have found potential visitors in Galtrev. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'Just north of the Gap of Rohan there is an untamed land called Dunland. It is said to be inhabited by equally untamed hillmen who paint their faces and wear naught but animal skins! I imagine they rarely leave their own lands, but maybe if someone gave them a little nudge, it may do them well to visit other places!

'Go to their largest village, Galtrev, and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Galtrev in Dunland and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the dwarves at the Hall of Vérnozal who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to the Hall of Vérnozal in Gundabad and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around the Hall of Vérnozal for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in the Hall of VérnozalYou have found potential visitors in the Hall of Vérnozal. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'Rumours among the Temámir dwarves speak of a great victory for the Zhélruka, who have retaken their rightful place as rulers of the Grey Mountains. They say Prince Ingór now rules in Gundabad. If this is true, the Zhélruka must be ready for a holiday, eh?

'Go to the Hall of Vérnozal in Gundabad, and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation to visit us in Zír Aktar. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to the Hall of Vérnozal in Gundabad and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the residents of Herne who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Herne in Cardolan and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Herne for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in HerneYou have found potential visitors in Herne. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'I have seen a map of the land that was once the old northern Kingdom of Cardolan. I spoke to a learned man who asked, "What happened to the Men of Anor and Cardolan?", and I can tell you what I think - they are still there! Or rather, their descendants are. If they themselves were still there, that would be ghastly.

'Go to this village called Herne. It has a good location for trade, so I expect there will be a thriving community there. Find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation to Furtherholm. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Herne in Cardolan and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Gondorian residents of Minas Tirith who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Minas Tirith (Midsummer) in Gondor and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Minas Tirith (Midsummer) for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)You have found potential visitors in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'Gondor, our age-old enemies.... Do you know what is strange? I was raised to hate Gondor and its people. They and their ancestors from Númenor have caused much suffering in these lands. And yet, when I meet someone from Gondor and talk to them face-to-face, it turns out they are much like us! I do not like what their Kingdom has done, but I find it hard to blame the average citizen of Gondor for these things.

'Go to Minas Tirith and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation to our beautiful island. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a visit, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us. Or... more poor, I suppose.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Minas Tirith (Midsummer) in Gondor and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the hobbits of Nobottle who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Nobottle in Yondershire and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Nobottle for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in NobottleYou have found potential visitors in Nobottle. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'Are you familiar with halflings? Hobbits, I am told they call themselves. Small folk with hairy feet. Perhaps it is just legend, but I heard they are quite merry, particularly when food and drink is around! I say they sound like wonderful company and I would love to see such jolly folk among our visitors.

'I have heard a tale of a halfling village called Nobottle in the land of Yondershire where it may be possible to find a young hobbit or two willing to travel. Especially if you tempt them with exotic foods and wine! Find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation to Furtherholm. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Nobottle in Yondershire and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Eglain of Ost Guruth who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Ost Guruth for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in Ost GuruthYou have found potential visitors in Ost Guruth. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'To the east of Bree-land, there is a desolate wilderness known as the Lone-lands. There lives a people called the Eglain. I have read they choose to live among ruins instead of cities or villages, rejecting the life of more cultured people in favour of the freedom of the wilderness. I would like to meet such Men! It is akin to choosing a life at sea instead of the comforts of Umbar Baharbêl.

'I hear many of them can be found in Ost Guruth, a ruin along the Great East Road. Go there and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Lossoth of Forochel who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Sûri-kylä in Forochel and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Sûri-kylä for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in Sûri-kyläYou have found potential visitors in Sûri-kylä. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'In the far northern lands of Eriador, there lies an icy wasteland called Forochel. There lives a people I have read about called 'Lossoth' that live in the cold snow. I think they could do with some sun and sand, don't you?

'Go to their largest village, Sûri-kylä, and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Sûri-kylä in Forochel and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some revellers at The Party Tree who might be interested in a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with locating The Party Tree and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around The Party Tree for potential visitors.Find potential visitors at The Party TreeYou have found potential visitors at The Party Tree. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'${PLAYER}, you know that in general I prefer facts over fantasy, but there is one legend in particular that intrigues me. It tells of an enchanted tree where people gather from miles around, and beneath its boughs, they dance, drink, and feast. "The Party Tree", they call it. A rather plain name, I should say, but at least it is descriptive.

'My friend, I charge you with a quest. A quest unlike any other. Go forth and search every corner of Middle-earth until you find this "Party Tree". When you find it... if you find it, see if you can convince one of the revellers to accept an invitation to join us here at Zír Aktar. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, begin your quest to seek out The Party Tree and find someone there to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the dwarves in Moria's Twenty-first Hall who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to the Twenty-first Hall inside the Mines of Moria and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around the Twenty-first Hall for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in the Twenty-first HallYou have found potential visitors in the Twenty-first Hall. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'They say that the Longbeard Dwarves have returned to their ancestral home of Moria, and that it has been a difficult and dangerous undertaking. Perhaps after such a trial, a brave and hearty dwarf could use a holiday?

'Go to The Twenty-first Hall inside the Mines of Moria and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation to our little island. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to the Twenty-first Hall in Moria and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Khâtaphos believes that there may be some among the Men of Trestlebridge who could use a tropical holiday.You have been tasked with travelling to Trestlebridge in the North Downs and finding a potential visitor who might accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival. You should look around Trestlebridge for potential visitors.Find potential visitors in TrestlebridgeYou have found potential visitors in Trestlebridge. You should choose one who is most likely to accept an invitation to visit Furtherholm for the Midsummer Festival and invite them.Invite someone to visit Furtherholm<rgb=#FF0000>Do not bother people (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>'A guest who claims to be a Bree-lander has asked a favour of me. She tells me that north of Bree-town, there is a village called Trestlebridge that has seen many attacks from Orc hordes, and a good part of the town has been lost to fire. She is enjoying her stay and has asked me to extend an invitation to the people of Trestlebridge, who could certainly do with a relaxing holiday!

'Go to this Trestlebridge and find someone who might cheerfully accept an invitation to Zír Aktar. Mind that you do not bother too many people who would not be open to such a journey, or people will think you a pest and grow to have a poor opinion of us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'When you are ready, go to Trestlebridge in the North Downs and find someone to invite to visit us in Furtherholm.'Your dual nature is no stranger to you, but transforming in the heat of battle is a bit more complicated.Enter Bear FormBy completing this quest, you will receive a Gift-giver's Brands allowance.'Do you want a lot of Gift-giver's Brands? I sure hope so, since you wanted me to talk more about this!''Rove back here if you need more!'Roger Hazeltwig desires to spread the joy of the celebration to his friend, Gail Catchpole.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Gail Catchpole is in Combe.

Roger Hazeltwig has asked you to deliver a lovely bracelet to Gail Catchpole, in the hopes that the gift will brighten her mood.'Hail, friend! I hope you are enjoying the festival.

'You wouldn't happen to be on your way to Combe, would you? You see, my friend Gail lives there now, and she recently lost many of her belongings in the tragedy that befell Archet. I wanted to give this bracelet to her as a gift, in the hope that it would raise her spirits in these troubling times.

'Would you be so kind as to take this to her?''Have you found Gail in Combe yet? Just head east out of Bree, then take the road north at the fork.''Hello there!

'Oh, what is this? You have something for me? How beautiful!'Dudo Chubb wishes to spread the cheer of the celebration to Ormr, a dwarf acquaintance of his in Ered Luin.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Ormr is at Frérin's Court, near Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin.

Dudo Chubb would like you to bring a shield to the Dwarf Ormr.'The festival is a great time for gift-giving, and I have the perfect idea for a fantastic tribute!

'I have this large shield here, much too big for a hobbit, but I have heard of a dwarf in the Blue Mountains named Ormr who is especially fond of shields like this one. He could put it to much better use than any Bounder here... would you be so kind as to take this to him in Frérin's Court?''Ormr can be found working in Frérin's Count, right outside of Thorin's Hall. For the most direct route, may I suggest visiting the stable-master in Michel Delving?''Ormr at your service and your family's.

'My, that is a fine shield... a strong shield, indeed! I shall pass this on to my son. He could put this to use in protecting our land. Cheers to you and yours!'Ormr wishes to spread the cheer of the celebration to Runulf, the innkeeper in Thorin's Hall.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Runulf is at his inn in the cellar of Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin.

Ormr has tasked you with taking a lucky goat's horn to Runulf, the innkeeper in Thorin's Hall.'Do you believe in items that are lucky? Many travellers and adventurers do. Certain kinds of items in particular are said to grant luck to their owners. I don't believe in such things, but many do, including Runulf the Thorin's Hall innkeeper.

'I have the perfect festival gift for Runulf: a decorative goat's horn. I would like you to take it to him. Some dwarves believe that a goat's horn will bring good fortune to whomever possesses it.''Are you lost, friend? Just head into Thorin's Hall, to the north of here. Head to the back and go down into the cellar, you will find Runulf keeping the inn there.''Welcome. Can I interest you in a pint?

'Ah, this is a gift for me? Well, I'm feeling quite lucky already! Blessings to you, kind ${RACE}.'Esmerelda Burrows wants to spread the cheer of celebration to her friend, Dudo Chubb.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Dudo Chubb is in Hobbiton in the Shire.

Esmerelda Burrows would like you to deliver a gift to her friend Dudo Chubb.'It's good that you are here: I have a small errand that needs doing.

'Do you know my friend Dudo Chubb? He works in Bywater, doing odd jobs and carpentry. He was complaining that his tools were not fit for use, so I want him to have this new hammer as a festival gift. The best gift is a practical gift, I always say!

'Would you mind paying him a visit and bringing him this new hammer? I'm sure he will be surprised.''Do you know the way to Hobbiton? It's to the east, a bit north of Tuckborough. Dudo is usually out and about, working on some task or another.''Quite a day, isn't it? What can I help you with?

'You say Esmerelda sent you? Oh my, what a fine hammer that is! My work will be much easier without having to use this old, rusty piece of junk....'Runulf wishes to spread the cheer of the celebration to his friend, Roger Hazeltwig.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Roger Hazeltwig is near the Boar-fountain in Bree.

Runulf has requested that you take a pint of his special brew of ale to Roger Hazeltwig.'A festival is always a great time for a drink. Oh! That reminds me, I have a request of you.

'I brewed up a special batch of my annual festival ale recently, but I'm down to only a few pints left. Would you take this pint of ale to my friend Roger Hazeltwig in Bree? He usually stops by for a taste, but he hasn't been able to visit in quite some time.

'Give him my regards... and a merry festival to you both!''If you're looking for Roger, you can find him in the town of Bree, by the famous Boar-fountain. Give him my regards when you see him.''Greetings.

'Ah, I see what you have there. With a colour and aroma like that, this can only have come from my friend Runulf! You have my deepest thanks for bringing this to me.'Gail Catchpole would like you to bring her delicious pastries to Constable Underhill.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Constable Underhill is outside the training hall in Combe.

Gail Catchpole would like you to bring her delicious pastries to Constable Underhill.'A merry festival to you! 

'They say that the festival is a time for cheer and for doing good deeds towards others. Would you be willing to assist me in this endeavour?

'Over by the inn, outside the training hall, you will find Constable Underhill. He was kind to me when I first moved to Combe, and as repayment, I have baked him some delicious pastries. Would you take them to him?''Head south-east from here and go up the stone stairs. You should find Constable Underhill standing outside of the training hall.''Good day to you.

'Oh! Something smells delicious! Working always makes me so hungry....'Constable Underhill desires to spread the cheer of the celebration to his friend Esmerelda Burrows.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Esmerelda Burrows is at The Bird and Baby Inn in Michel Delving in the Shire.

Constable Underhill has tasked you with bringing a small, wooden carving to his friend Esmerelda Burrows in Michel Delving.'Oh, how I miss my old friends in the Shire. I just recently purchased this wooden carving, which reminds me of my friend Esmerelda Burrows in Michel Delving. 

'Esmerelda always loved wooden carvings like this one. Maybe you could bring this one to her? I'm sure it would bring a smile to her face!

'Could you let her know that I sent this and that I wish her well? If you are looking for her, she is often found relaxing at The Bird and Baby Inn.''Esmerelda spends a lot of time at The Bird and Baby Inn in Michel Delving. I would consider speaking to the stable-master and going on horseback, if I were you.''Constable Underhill sent you? It's been ages since... oh! Is that a carving? For me?

'What a funny squirrel carving. Oh, this makes me so happy!'You have completed your collection of goat mounts.You have completed your collection of goat mounts.Mount the Prized Nimble Redhorn-goatMount the Prized Tame Redhorn-goatMount the Treasure Laden GoatMount the Nimble Black GoatMount the Wild Mountain-goatMount the Prized Thorin's Hall GoatMount the Prized Ale Association GoatMount the Harvest-brew GoatMount the Windfells GoatYou have completed your collection of goat mounts.You have completed your collection of goat mounts.Mount the Prized Nimble Redhorn-goatMount the Prized Tame Redhorn-goatMount the Treasure Laden GoatMount the Nimble Black GoatMount the Wild Mountain-goatMount the Prized Thorin's Hall GoatMount the Prized Ale Association GoatMount the Harvest-brew GoatMount the Windfells GoatDefeat many goblins in Cardolan.Defeat many goblins in Cardolan.Defeat many goblins in CardolanDefeat many goblins in Cardolan.Defeat many goblins in Cardolan.Defeat many goblins in CardolanMelilot Hayward, a Summer Festival patron, has lost her entire picnic lunch over the course of the day, and is very hungry.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Melilot's missing things can be found not far from the Party Tree. She has given you a note with some record of where her day led her.

