You should bring Melilot's picnic items back to her.'Hello, you there! Could you please pause a moment to help a hobbit in need? I came here today to enjoy the festival, but I've lost all the food I brought with me!

'Here, have this note; I've scribbled down everything I can remember about my day. Will you please help me find my missing meals?

'They shouldn't be far... I just don't know how I could have lost it all! I must have been thinking about other things, I suppose. I am awfully hungry.''I'm sure I didn't wander far... though it was rather a busy day. Who's to say? I've already forgotten everything. It's a good thing I remembered to jot down my progress on that note I gave you.''Oh, joy! You are a real hero, ${PLAYER}. There should be songs written about you. Perhaps I will try to make a song myself, right after I sit down and finally get to enjoy my picnic. And, of course, after I've had my nap.'By completing this quest, you will receive a gold allowance.'I hate to see a high level character struggling to find two golds to rub together. I have an allowance for you, but just like the allowance you got as a kid, this is only a once a week thing, so spend it wisely!''Remember, this allowance is only available once a week, so spend it wisely!'A Woman named Golwen has asked you to help persuade her captain that she remains fit for work.If you've decided to accept Golwen's request, you should talk to her at your home.Talk to Golwen'You -- you are a stranger. That is exactly what I need. My crew-mates have been insufferable with their pity.

'My captain has ordered me to stay onshore and away from our ship for reasons I cannot ascertain. The man has my respect, but I disagree with his judgement here.

'Evaluate my abilities. Persuade him that I am capable of continuing this work.'

<rgb=#00FF00>This neighbour's story begins after the War of the Ring.</rgb>'Thank you. With your help, I will be back on the ship swiftly.'Golwen sets out to deliver a long-awaited farewell.You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 10'You should talk to Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Talk to Golwen'${PLAYER}, please come with me to the beach again. Rikháwi deserves a proper farewell from me, and I would appreciate your company.'She exhales and squares her shoulders. 

'Onwards.'Golwen greets you with a small wince.

'My leg is not pleased with the trip to the beach, but it is a small price to pay for what we managed to do.'

She smiles.

'I could not have done this without you, ${PLAYER}.'With mended clothes for her crew-mates in tow, Golwen seeks to prove her usefulness to her captain.You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 2'You should talk to Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Talk to Golwen'${PLAYER}. I have mended clothes to deliver to my crew-mates. Rarely will a crew complete a voyage without damaging their clothing; thus the responsibility of mending falls to me.

'I will need you to carry this sack of clothes. I have a... leg injury.'

This admission forces its way out through gritted teeth.

'This injury enjoys making itself known at the most inopportune of times. Maybe to irritate me.

'When you are ready, we will set out.''Well?''That is one task complete, though more needs to be done if I am to persuade the captain. Unfortunately, my leg will require some rest first.

'Once I find more work to do, I will let you know.'Golwen is determined to rejoin the crew -- even if it takes disobeying her captain's orders.You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 3'You should talk to Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Talk to Golwen'${PLAYER}, I have found an opportunity for the both of us -- there remains unfinished tasks onboard the ship. Maintaining the ship's condition remains an important duty, even while docked. If you are interested, we could split whatever tasks are left, as well as the coin.

'The captain may have forbidden me from working, but surely he cannot be upset about the extra help. With luck, my actions and your words will persuade him that I am fit to return.''When you are ready.''You are the only person I know outside of the crew, ${PLAYER}, and I do not wish to continue facing my crew-mates' pity. Unfortunately, it appears you are stuck with me for the time being.

'But how to follow the captain's orders... I must ruminate on this further.'Left with more free time than she knows what to do with, Golwen has decided to try cooking for fun.You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 4'You should try and talk to Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Try and talk to Golwen'${PLAYER}, I was about to spend some time cooking. For... fun. It is not related to work.

'I would not say no to your help.''Follow me; I know of a place we can use.'Golwen makes no effort to reveal what sort of unspoken past currently occupies her thoughts, only giving you a single absent-minded nod of acknowledgement.

You leave her to those memories.In her continuing efforts to follow her captain's orders, Golwen has invited you to join her on a walk.You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 5'You should talk to Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Talk to Golwen'${PLAYER}, I was about to embark on a walk with no particular destination in mind. Yes, I am trying to take the captain's words to heart. If you would like to join me, I would welcome your company.''Whenever you are ready.''I had thought such aimless activities did not suit me, but our walk was rather.... relaxing. The captain's words may have held a wisdom that I could not grasp at the time.

'Yet, I wonder how long I must continue doing such things before I can return to the ship.'Though reluctant, Golwen has decided to join her crew-mates for a concert -- just this once.You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 6'You should talk to Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Talk to GolwenYou find Golwen's face fixed in a contemplative frown.

'${PLAYER}. My crew-mates have invited me yet again to perform with them at the tavern. I am reluctant to participate, but they have invited me countless times. Maybe it would be good to oblige their requests. At least once.

'They would welcome you as well, I am sure.''We should begin to make our way over, lest we arrive late.''My absence must have disappointed my crew-mates, but they will understand once I explain what happened. I will join them for a performance some other day. I swear.'For one who has known nothing but the sea, the pull of the tides is too much to ignore.You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 7'You should talk to Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Talk to Golwen'${PLAYER}, I confess that I miss the ocean -- which sounds ridiculous, considering the amount of time we have spent near it. But I miss it all the same.

'I have been making plans to camp on a beach for a night. Mind you, it will be a crude camp -- simple bed-rolls and nothing more. If that does not sound objectionable, you are welcome to accompany me.''I have packed my things and am ready, whenever you are.''For once, it was... comforting to have someone by my side. Thank you.'What better way to spend a day than with friends?You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 8'You should talk to Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Talk to Golwen'${PLAYER}, I have invited my crew-mates for an afternoon of fishing. Having your company on the beach reminded me... it has been far too long since I last spent time with any of them.

'I hope you can accompany us.''Simply come as you are. They will have spare fishing rods for the both of us.''Before they left, my crew-mates requested that you join us on future fishing excursions.'

An amused huff escapes Golwen.

'Well... I would not protest your presence.'A solo no longer.You should talk to Golwen to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Golwen, Chapter 9'You should check on Golwen near the stable-master in Dol Amroth (King's Gondor) or at your home.Check on Golwen'${PLAYER}. Tonight is the night of the performance.

'Let us go to the tavern early, if we can. I may require some time to steel myself.'Golwen barely acknowledges you; she directs all of her attention towards fiddling nervously with her flute.Golwen quietly hums a snippet of the song to herself.The hobbits' preferred drink during the Yule Festival has always been a stout, strong cider, heated and mulled to the perfect temperature and taste.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Apples can be found at Appledore's Orchard, west of the Party Tree.

