Samfast will be pleased to get his hands on the apples you collected so that he can begin making cider for the Yule celebration.'Every Yule, I make a special blend of my cider: a mix of cinnamon, sugar, and a few other spices I am not inclined to share with any old stranger. It has become a tradition within my family that we share a toast of this cider to remember the year that was and to look forward to the year that will be.

'Unfortunately, I fear my family may be disappointed this year. I have run out of apples to press for the cider. I had so much other planning to do, it simply slipped my mind.

'I don't suppose you would be willing to fetch me some apples? I don't need many. You can find them to the west, at Appledore's Orchard.''Those apples aren't for eating, mind you! They're for the cider. If I catch you eating one, you'll be sorry!''These apples will do perfectly. I and my family thank you, ${PLAYER}. This Yule will be as great as last...and hopefully moreso!'There are few hobbits who do not know the tale of Bandobras Took's triumph over the goblin, Golfimbul.Goblin-gourds can be found throughout Wistmead.

