<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>The garden lies on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith, to the north-west of the entryway between the Second and Third Circles. The statue of Steward Egalmoth keeps watch over the garden.

Lebadar has asked you to pull out the weeds and water the bushes there.Water bushes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Pull out weeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lebadar waits for you on the Second Circle, at the base of the entrance to the Third.

You should assure him that the garden has been tended.Return to Lebadar'Have you ever seen anything like this before? I daresay this is the first time in all of my long years that my people have experienced such joy.

'Still, there is work to be done. Several gardens in Minas Tirith are under my responsibility, but I have been having a harder time tending to them. So many people around the city! My old legs can no longer carry me as well as they used to. But I do not wish to let my plants waste away; they have survived troubled times.

'If you could help me, the garden that holds the statue of Steward Egalmoth on the Third Circle requires attention. Weeds have sprung out of the earth and the bushes need watering.''Thank you for aiding a silly old man and his plants today, kind stranger. I think my people will appreciate the reminder that as long as nature continues to grow, good still exists in the world.'You earned the Hacks All Day title.Obligatory text.A hobbit named Haldo Rushbank needs a home away from home in order to solve a mystery, and he's requested your help.If you've decided to accept Haldo Rushbank's request, you should talk to him at your home.Talk to Haldo Rushbank'Pardon me, do you travel often? Oh, good, good. I've got a... shall we say, "mystery" that needs solving, if you wouldn't mind helping me.

'In order to do this, I'll need to stay someplace away from my family. They can't know what I'm up to, but their curiosity ought to be sated for now. I gave them a long story about a very ill friend, you see.

'This must all sound rather strange to you, but please, consider my request.''Thank you for agreeing to my request. There are some items relevant to the mystery that you ought to look at -- cherished belongings that I dare not bring out of my family's smial. Knowing my family, it may be a while before I can find a time when nobody's home. But I shall let you know.'The moment of truth has arrived.You should talk to Haldo to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 10'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'It's almost time for our dinner party!

'I wonder if the dish will finally taste like grandmother's. It may be wiser of me to brace myself for disappointment, but we've made such great strides already. This has to be it... right?''We ought to leave soon, so that we can welcome Gisti when he arrives.''Venturing out into the unknown doesn't seem so scary anymore, now that I know Grandmother was out there too. Her recipe sat in the dark for so many years before I finally found the courage to begin investigating it.

'Often I've wondered what she would've felt if she could see me now. There was so much about her that I didn't know, and there still is. But of this, I am certain: she lived her life how she wanted, in spite of her family and her circumstances. And I hope to follow in her footsteps.'Haldo's nervousness over travelling might prove to be a thorn in his side.You should talk to Haldo to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 2'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'Prior to this entire undertaking, I never travelled out of the Shire before. Not many hobbits want to leave, me included. But this mystery may take me far and wide, and I'll need to brace myself for the reality of travelling with just one other person.

'Perhaps a walk around the outskirts of the Shire shall do me some good. It'll be close enough to home that I won't panic, but far enough that it'll all seem strange still.

'What do you think?''Well, here goes nothing.''That was no good, no good at all. What am I to do? I can't let my fear of bears stop me from travelling.

'I shall simply have to try again! Not -- not right this second. Maybe later. I'll, er, let you know.'The best way to conquer your fears is to try again.You should talk to Haldo to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 3'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'Well, I've twiddled my thumbs for long enough. As much as I want to just stay put, I won't get anything done by sitting here.

'I'd like to stay just outside of the Shire again, but... could we try someplace less bear-infested, perhaps?''At least, one can hope there is someplace less bear-infested...''I feared those bandits would be able to hear how loudly my heart was beating then!

'I'm not certain this has made me any more eager to start travelling, but at least I know I'll be safe with you.'Haldo has invited you to his family's smial to finally discuss the mystery at hand.You should talk to Haldo to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 4'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'${PLAYER}, I'm ready to discuss the mystery I need help with. Will you come with me to my family's smial? Of course, I've ensured they won't be there.''At least, I hope they won't be...''Once I make preparations for the journey ahead, we can set out. The trek can't be too difficult, can it?'Haldo has resolved to journey north into Gondamon, though whether he's happy about that is another story.You should talk to Haldo to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 5'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'Shall we begin our trip to... what was it called, Gondamon? I'm ready. Erm, well, "ready" may not be the best word... I'm still bracing myself... but that's beside the point!''Please let it be a quick and safe journey....''I cannot stop thinking about what Heming said. My grandmother was a gentle and proper sort -- almost respectable by Shire standards, if it weren't for her adventurous streak.

'As much as I would like to dismiss Heming, he's right; few hobbits go that way. How can two very different truths about my grandmother simultaneously exist?

'I wish she'd told me about her travels. I wish I knew the truth.'Could the ingredients collected near Gondamon be the answer to Haldo's mystery?You should talk to Haldo to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 6'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'${PLAYER}, I'd like to return home and try the ingredients we collected near Gondamon. Of course, any kitchen would suit my needs, but I want to work in the kitchen that my grandmother used. Something about that just feels right.

'Rest assured, I've made sure that nobody's home again; they should all be planning my cousin's birthday party. And the enormity of that task will certainly occupy them for hours.''Shall we?''That was much too close!

'We're getting closer to our answer, but not close enough. I'll have to consider our next step... which I'm afraid may require more travelling.'A memory shared, a burden lifted.Haldo wants to share a memory with you.

You should talk to him.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 7'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'${PLAYER}, there is something I wanted to tell you. Something that I think you ought to know, since I've trusted you with this mystery. None of what I'm about to recount will shed further light on anything, but I... I wanted to share this memory. As a friend.''Thank you for indulging me.'Haldo clears his throat.

'A-As for our next steps, we ought to visit... Thorin's Hall, was it? I hate to admit this, but Heming in Gondamon may have been telling the truth about my grandmother. Maybe she went further north as well. No, not maybe -- I'm certain she did.

'I shall need a while to brace myself. Gondamon's frost was not kind to me, and I fear the weather around Thorin's Hall may not be an improvement.'Gondamon did not hold all of the answers Haldo sought, but Thorin's Hall may.You should talk to Haldo to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 8'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'Time to begin our journey to Thorin's Hall. I did not want to go so far from home, but there's no other way to finish the recipe. If I must be brave, then I'll try my best.

'Once we arrive, I propose that we try some food -- we might find some answers that way.''We ought to start moving, lest my doubt creeps in!''Well, I suppose I can call our trip to Thorin's Hall a success. And Gisti... he seems to have truly known grandmother in a way that I never did. To finally have a connection to this part of her I did not know... is it strange to feel so much happiness, sadness, and envy all at once?

'As much as I wish we could have collected some stingóst immediately, it's best that we wait until Gisti is ready. Given how long it's been since he last went hiking, he may require some time to prepare.'Haldo follows in his grandmother's footsteps.You should talk to Haldo to begin your outing.Complete 'Mission: Haldo Rushbank, Chapter 9'You should talk to Haldo near the stable-master in Michel Delving or at your home.Talk to Haldo'Gisti has sent word! He's made preparations to take us to the place where he and Grandmother would gather stingóst.

'Gondamon has its bracing chill and Thorin's Hall has its frigid ice, but I'll be brave. Yes. I must be.''Well, what are we waiting for?''Do you think stingóst is the final ingredient we've been searching for? Even if it isn't, something tells me we're *very* close.

'To think the old dwarf was overjoyed to be invited to a home so far from his own...' Haldo shakes his head. 'Meanwhile, it took a years-old mystery to make me step foot out of the Shire!

'I must make some preparations, of course. For instance, I'll have to tell my family that I invited a friend of Grandmother's. The rumours and gossip won't be pleasant, but I'll not let them continue pretending she never existed.

'Besides, I've had enough of sneaking around.'Defeat many half-orcs in Cardolan.Defeat many half-orcs in Cardolan.Defeat many half-orcs in CardolanDefeat many half-orcs in Cardolan.Defeat many half-orcs in Cardolan.Defeat many half-orcs in CardolanYou earned the Hangs in Taverns title.Obligatory text.<rgb=#00e4ff>Received Expansion Pack Collector's Edition gifts for logging in during our 15th Anniversary.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>Receive Collector's Edition Expansion Pack gifts for logging in and reaching level 2 during our 15th Anniversary.</rgb>Play to level 2 during our 15th Anniversary CelebrationThe Summer Festival is upon us! It is time to enjoy the longest days of the year, the warmth of the sun, and the peak of the mid-year harvest.The Summer Festival has come to Middle-earth to spread its gaiety and warmth to each and every patron.Enjoy the summer festivities while they lastThe world is filled with those who are less well off than ourselves.You are often harassed by the poor and destitute.The magic of the voice is a delicate thing, easily disturbed by failures of harmony or rhythm.Use Ballads or CodasThe magic of the voice is a delicate thing, easily disturbed by failures of harmony or rhythm.Use Ballads or CodasYou have waited a long time, but now it is finally harvesting season!

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>Amabel Redfern is near the Party Tree in Hobbiton.

You should speak to Amabel Redfern again to receive your black mushroom transplant.'It has been a long season, but it looks as if your spores have finally grown! I took the liberty of tending to the field while you were away.... I have been growing mushrooms of my own alongside the ones that you planted in the spring.

'I have been trying to perfect my family's mushroom-growing techniques for a number of years, and it seems that I was unsuccessful once again. But look at me going on! Patience is the virtue that I have been advocating to you, and now it seems that I am in need of it the most!

'Your mushrooms grew hearty and strong, and you should be well rewarded for your farming prowess! While I won't give up my family recipe just yet, please take this black mushroom transplant. You can place it in your own garden and tend to it there. Who knows, maybe you will find the secrets that I have long been searching for!''Here are the black mushrooms that you planted in the spring. Do be careful with them. It would be a shame if you damaged them.'Harvestmath brings yet another bountiful farming season to a close as the leaves begin to turn gold and the days grow short and cool.The long summer has come to an end, and a beautiful autumn settles in over Middle-earth. The air grows crisper and cooler daily, and the sun retires earlier with each passing week.Enjoy the autumn festivities while they lastOrdâkhai and Utûgi forced labourers to carry wood and tools southward on the road from Emax Dûl. Their intent is unclear, and Mizâdi's scouts have asked for your assistance.Mizâdi's scouts were discovered, but not before they saw the Utûgi and Ordâkhai head west off the south road from Emax Dûl. You have been asked to finish the work they would have done.Complete the mission: Investigative Efforts of the HatokáliriYou reported back that the wood was treated to withstand the rigors of waves and water, and the tools are meant for a shipwright's hands. The scouts are planning to cause a distraction to draw the Utûgi and Ordâkhai away from the captives.Complete the mission: Drive the Enemy AwayMizâdi's scouts were not able to free the labourers before the Utûgi returned. Kusâg asked that you return to the site and release the workers.Complete the mission: Workers ReleasedYou defeated the enemy and rescued their captives. You should return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp to ensure that all you rescued are safe and counted.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'Despite their best effort, my scouts were discovered by the Utûgi and Ordâkhai as they followed them south. They watched as they left the southern road just north of where brigands have built shelter. They could not catalogue what they carried with them.

'I ask that you find where they went. Examine the wood and tools they brought with them and record what you discover. I will have my scouts keep a distance and collect your findings, if you are willing.''Once we better understand what the Utûgi and Ordâkhai mean to do with the labourers, wood, and tools, we can plan our strategy to remove them without threatening the lives of their captives.''My scouts will let you draw the Utûgi and Ordâkhai away from the captives. We will save their captives, and disrupt whatever devious plans they have. Be resolute, friend.''A victory, but hollow. My scouts drew many of the Utûgi gaolers from the labourers they watch, but not all. We must return once more to release the workers from their bonds.''As ever, you are a gracious hero, my friend.

'We are speaking with the labourers you rescued, and learning there is more we can still do. We are certain to have need of your service again soon, ${PLAYER}.'Ordâkhai and Utûgi forced labourers to carry wood and tools southward on the road from Emax Dûl. Their intent is unclear, and Mizâdi's scouts have asked for your assistance.After being rescued, the labourers explained they built a few boats, and the enemy is using them to ferry their numbers in retreat across the river and into the jungle. This presents an opportunity to strand the enemy and visit righteous judgement on them.Complete the mission: Deny Their EscapeThe boats burn on the riverside, and the scout who retrieved you suggested they found the remaining camp of Ordâkhai and Utûgi on the north side of the river. Kusâg sent you to finish off the stragglers.Complete the mission: The Final AssaultThe enemy has been defeated and the scout advised that you return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'The labourers explained that a few boats were constructed and that the surviving members of the Utûgi and Ordâkhai have been ferrying themselves across the river. They intended to leave the labourers on the north side of the river.

'We should strand the enemies we can, and visit righteous judgement upon them.''Find and burn the boats. Let us deny the enemy an escape route.''Do not show mercy to the enemy. They showed no quarter to the labourers they captured. We will show them none in return.''This is a true victory, ${PLAYER}.

'We saved many lives. We defeated many enemies and denied them a chance to regroup further to the south.'

She pauses.

'I see the look on your face, and I will admit, I have my own thoughts. This may have been a distraction for something else, or someone.

'For now, my friend, let us share in the joy of the lives we saved, and those we may still save.'Scouts in the west believe they have seen collusion beginning between the Ordâkhai in the north and the bandits in the south. These two forces must not be allowed to unite.Scouts have tracked messages being exchanged between the Ordâkhai from the crags west of Mizâdi's camp and the Hatokáli bandits encamped on the river's edge at the terminus of the south road from Emax Dûl. Mizâdi's forces cannot afford these forces allying with one another.Complete the mission: Emissaries from the OrdâkhaiThough you did all you could, it appears that emissaries have previously made contact with the Hatokáli bandits. Return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp to determine further action.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'The scourge of the Ordâkhai continues, and it seems that they are not done with their machination in the west. Scouts have been tracking emissaries making their way from the crag hills in the north to the Hatokáli bandit camp located at the water's edge in the south.

'I fear these forces may be on the verge of unifying. We cannot have these forces allying.

'Will you help us to put a stop their potential unification?''You may not find the emissaries on the main road. My scouts have warned they are moving silently, under the cover of shadow and off of the beaten road to avoid detection. Find them all, and deny them new allies.''We cannot know how long they have been exchanging messages and information. We do know that the flow of information is now interrupted. We should prepare for the worst, I fear.

'We will, of course be ready should there be movement from the bandits.'Scouts in the west believe they have seen collusion beginning between the Ordâkhai in the north and the bandits in the south. These two forces must not be allowed to unite.At the bandit camp at the terminus of the road south of Emax Dûl, the bandits appear to be gathering in force. This can only mean an alliance is being considered between the bandits and the Ordâkhai. It must be severed quickly.Complete the mission: Stop the Hatokáli Bandit AdvanceAmong the bandits you discovered riches and wealth given to them by Ordâkhai deserters, paying for passage across the makeshift ferry at the bandit camp. Your action foiled the plot, and recovered the stolen wealth, but the Ordâkhai deserters still remain.Complete the mission: A Harsh TruthYou defeated the last of the Ordâkhai deserters. You should return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp to alert her to your victory.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'Our efforts to contain the Ordâkhai have failed. They reached the bandits, and it seems the bandits are convinced to march north to join the Ordâkhai encampment.'

She shakes her head.

'This cannot happen. We must put an end to this uprising now, before our nearest foes grow even stronger.

'Please ${PLAYER}, help us end this alliance before it can be forged.''You will find that the bandits have left the relative safety of their camp, beginning to expand northward. They construct new barricades, and extend the reach of the towers. We cannot afford to have such a force combine with the Ordâkhai. We must be swift and final in this assault.''${PLAYER}, I do not wish you to think me overly cruel.'

She pauses, looking over the camp.

'I, too, question sometimes if my motivation is borne of justice or vengeance. It can be hard to discern.

'The oppression levied upon our people by the Ordâkhai was severe. Now, in the light borne by Mizâdi, we may have a future where we are free. The thought of our oppressors returning from the south one day-'

She shakes her head.

'It is justice for the years they have stolen... the pilfered wealth... the death they wrought... justice.''We cannot allow the Ordâkhai to escape. Their crimes are too numerous and heinous for them to escape justice. My scouts discovered they are camped not far from the bandit encampment. Our time to strike is now.'The Ordâkhai erred badly, and sprung a terrible trap upon themselves in the area south of Emax Dûl. Now an ambitious captain seems set on recovering the lost cargo and setting the trap anew.Mizâdi's scouts are being cautious to deter any potential Ordâkhai footholds from being established any further within Hatokáli. You have been asked to stop a plot to retake the town lost when the Ordâkhai lost control of the scorpions.Complete the mission: Discovering IntentYour caution in retrieving the orders from the courier at the Ordâkhai encampment affords Mizâdi's forces an opportunity they had not expected; infiltration. You must not waste this opportunity to further hamper the Ordâkhai forces.Complete the mission: The Crates Are Empty...Mizâdi's infiltrator escaped while you destroyed the crates the Ordâkhai brought to their makeshift camp. As they fled, they saw that the Ordâkhai were not deterred. In fact, they returned from the crags with tents to make a more formidable forward camp.Complete the mission: Weaken Their PositionYou destroyed the tents the Ordâkhai meant to use as shelter in the coming night. Perhaps this will be enough to stop their advance. You should return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp and speak with her.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'${PLAYER}, since our arrival, my task has been watching the roads and tracking the movements of the Ordâkhai throughout the Hatokáli Fells.

'My scouts are relentless in their duty, and have sent reports from the west, south of Emax Dûl, and between the forsaken town infested by scorpions, and the craggy rise where the Ordâkhai are entrenched.

'Something brews among the Ordâkhai. What, is unclear. We need assistance in learning the secrets they keep.''We must be cautious in how we approach this, my friend. Be secret, be swift, eliminate only the courier, so that we might gain better insight through subterfuge.''We shall not waste this good fortune afforded to us. The Ordâkhai would recapture the scorpions that overran the village west of their cragged camp. Even now they move crates and cages that will carry the scorpions to places we would occupy. We must destroy them and slow their plans.''It seems that there is a greater force driving the Ordâkhai than fear and fire can dissuade. So it is that we must use greater force ourselves. Will you return to their location and destroy their tents? We will not let them find comfort and rest if they dare pursue their goals.''You have done well this day. My scouts will watch the cross-road, and with luck, and your strength of arms and cunning, we shall see them press their position no further.

'Go now, friend. Enjoy a well-earned respite from battle and these necessary distractions. I am certain that tomorrow will hold more for you and me to do.

'Thank you.'The Ordâkhai erred badly, and sprung a terrible trap upon themselves in the area south of Emax Dûl. Now, an ambitious captain seems set on recovering the lost cargo and setting the trap anew.Mizâdi's scouts tracked the movements of the Ordâkhai of the crag overnight as they descended to the cross-roads south of Emax Dûl. A small force was left behind to defend cages and crates. With some clever activity, you may be able to sabotage these materials.Complete the mission: Inexorable EffortsYour success at sabotaging the containers to store and transport the scorpions may be for naught.

Mizâdi's scouts report movement from the crag brings cat-handlers making their way to the cross-roads. By some means, these handlers and their cats can herd and control the scorpions. They must be stopped.Complete the mission: Handling the HandlersDespite your efforts, the Ordâkhai are still driven to recover the scorpions from the overrun village. A new set of orders, delivered whilst you were dealing with the cat-handlers, must be recovered to learn what the Ordâkhai intend, who leads them, and why their resolve is so strong.Complete the mission: The Who, What, and WhyAfter delivering the orders you recovered to the scout, you were directed to return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp and speak with her.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. Our victory over the enemy yesterday is short-lived. My scouts report that under the cover of night, the Ordâkhai descended from the crags and set up at the cross-roads of the road south of Emax Dûl. If their intent were not so nefarious I may admire their resolve. Instead, I must ask you once again to aid us against this foe.

'They are proving to be a most grueling enemy.''Use your cunning again, my friend. But ensure that the crates and cages that would keep safe the scorpions are made brittle and easily broken.''You are a treasured ally, friend. One I fear we must rely on again, and so soon after your return.

'Scouts reported movement coming from the crags. Ordâkhai with cats, capable of taming the scorpions, if only for a time are making their way toward the cross-roads.

'They must not be allowed to join their brethren there.''I wish to thank you for your continued assistance, and beg of your skill-at-arms, once again. While you fought back the cat-handlers, a courier snuck around the battlefield and made their way to the cross-roads. They delivered new orders to the combatants there.

'We must learn what is in those orders.''We now know the name of the Ordâkhai who is driving the effort to recover the scorpions, Khómabekh Dólo. We also know they desire to recover the scorpions to deliver them against Mizâdi's forces. The who, the what, and the why.

'We are spread too thinly to have discovered this without you, ${PLAYER}. Again, we are in your debt.

'I shall draft plans to deal with Khómabekh. Return to me on the morrow.'The Ordâkhai erred badly, and sprung a terrible trap upon themselves in the area south of Emax Dûl. Now, an ambitious captain seems set on recovering the lost cargo and setting the trap anew.Khómabekh Dólo is making his final approach to the overrun village. You have been asked to face him, defeat him, and put an end to the threat he poses.Complete the mission: The Scorpion StingAfter defeating Khómabekh Dólo, Mizâdi's scout to the south arrived. They asked that you make your way back to speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'${PLAYER}, my plans were perfect, and then another group of Ordâkhai, accompanied by Utûgi, passed further to the south. I had need to reposition my scouts in the west to track their progress and now must ask the unthinkable of you.

'Khómabekh Dólo will shortly arrive and press his position. Should he succeed and recover the scorpions, we will need to dedicate more resources to tracking him and others.

'I have need of your assistance again.''Khómabekh Dólo will travel with at least two others. He will fight fiercely, and without abandon. Use your wits, steel your nerve. Be safe.''I have learned of your victory over Khómabekh Dólo. It is fortuitous news, as my scouts from the south bring me ill-tidings. News of Utûgi and Ordâkhai warriors dragging wood and tools southward, driving bound labourers ahead of them.

'I fear the success you achieved this day will be overshadowed by the continuing tide of woe that covers this land.

'For now, my friend, rest. I shall give news tomorrow on what more I learn.'With the threats diminished in the west, Mizâdi's scouts turn their attention to a looming threat in the south-east.Within the walls of the fortress to the south-east, a threat looms. The siege-leader who means to build the machines of war to launch an assault against Mizâdi's mountain camp. You have an opportunity to bring an end to this campaign.Complete the quest: Ending the Siege-lordThough the battle was fraught, you were victorious over the siege-lord. Return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'At last, ${PLAYER}, we have a name and location on the siege-master who would force the Mûrai into servitude and bring war machines to bear against our forces.

'We will make this a fitting end.''Find this villain and take him down, ${PLAYER}. We will have victory and know a moment of peace when this is done.''My scouts reported to me that you were victorious. The cur was put down, as he should have been.

'We will remain diligent, as there are certain to be other upstarts and warriors that we must contain.'

She smiles.

'We have a true victory, ${PLAYER}. We have this victory because of you; for this I, and the scouts who work to see a brighter future for our people and our lands, are grateful.'With the threats diminished in the west, Mizâdi's scouts turn their attention to a looming threat in the south-east.Ordâkhai in the south-east continue to forge an offensive against Mizâdi's forces. A bold effort by the Ordâkhai endangers the camp as siege machinery is being prepared on the rocky outcroppings to the south-east of Mizâdi's camp. You have been asked to assist.Complete the mission: Before the Bombardment BeginsWith the materials to craft the weapons destroyed, Kusâg is told that more citizens of Mûr Ghala are captive within the fortress to the south-east. You are asked to intervene.Complete the mission: A Harsh PunishmentYou freed the captive builders and saved them from a horrific fate. You discovered, however, a chain of overseers; cruel men who would visit terrible harm upon the captives. The scouts wish justice for those harmed by these wretches.Complete the mission: End the OversightThe overseers are removed. Return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'As one flank weakens, another grows in strength.

'Our efforts in the west reduced the threat posed by the Ordâkhai encamped there, but my scouts here in the east and the south have reported disturbing activity within striking distance of this encampment.

'Siege weaponry materials have been moved from a fort the Ordâkhai control to the south to rocky outcroppings to our south-east. If they are able to assemble these weapons, we would be under immediate bombardment.

'We cannot let them build those machines of war.''Beyond the battlefield where our numbers fight for control of this land, you will see the shadow of a fallen ruin occupied by Orcs. In that shadow, the Ordâkhai aim to make the flat and weathered stone a wall of siege weaponry to drive us from this camp. We will not let that happen.''We have spoken to the survivors you rescued and they tell us that there are more still held against their will. My scouts will find them.

'There is more yet to do, ${PLAYER}. Now, however, we rest.''They treat the people who cannot fight, or will not fight, as cattle... forcing them to build the machines of war. We will remove the yoke about their necks and free them from their oppressors.''Again, the matter of vengeance or justice rises. Still, my friend, I think it is justice we bring when we punish those who visited such terrible harm on the innocent.'With the threats diminished in the west, Mizâdi's scouts turn their attention to a looming threat in the south-east.Another opportunity to do right by those oppressed by the hand of the Ordâkhai arises. Far to the east, where the river grows rapid and the bridge that crossed that river is crumbled, Ordâkhai overseers drive captive workers to harvest wood for the machine of war.Complete the quest: Harvester's FlightYou have defeated the overseers and rescued the labourers who toiled in the shadow of the fallen bridge. Return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.Speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp'We discovered that the last large group of captives has been toiling at the river's edge, beneath the broken bridge in the shadow of the great water works.

'We have a chance to both eliminate their captors and rescue more Mûrai, if we can catch them off guard.

'My scouts will clear the roads, allowing you to assault the captors and free those harvesting wood in the shadow of the bridge and water works.''We will continue our efforts until all of Mûr Ghala is free. Let us take the fight to the enemy and free those who we can.''There are murmurs from those you recently freed that a powerful leader rises in the ranks of the Ordâkhai. Perhaps we can catch them, and hopefully end the oppression and more, the war.

'My scouts will keep searching, ${PLAYER}.'Helegrod was once an outpost of the great dwarf-realm of the Misty Mountains known to most as Moria. This wing now serves as the tomb of the dragon Thorog.Who knows what treasures remain in the hoard of the great beast Thorog.Complete Thorog DefeatedHelegrod was once an outpost of the great dwarf-realm of the Misty Mountains known to most as Moria. This wing is now home to a brood of drakes descended from the great dragon Thorog.Grisgart, a Man of Angmar serving at Helegrod, acts as the master of the drakes, bending them to the will of the Iron Crown.Complete Challenge: GrisgartComplete Drake-wranglerComplete Keep Them from HatchingComplete Fangs for NothingHelegrod was once an outpost of the great dwarf-realm of the Misty Mountains known to most as Moria. Giants under the influence of Skorgrím Dourhand and the Angmarim now call this wing of the dwarf-hold home.The mighty Storvâgûn leads his people in the fastness of Helegrod, holding the fortress against the Free Peoples.Complete Giants in the Service of AngmarComplete Giant-slayerComplete Beasts of SnowComplete Challenge: StorvâgûnHelegrod was once an outpost of the great dwarf-realm of the Misty Mountains known to most as Moria. Great spiders now infest many portions of the ancient dwarf-hold.The evil spider-queen Zaudru is one of the strongest of the spawn of Shelob, spawn of Ungoliant.Complete An Evil Place, Crawling with SpidersComplete Zaudru's BroodComplete Spider SquasherComplete Challenge: ZaudruAccess to the courtyard and Thorog is controlled by three guardians. They must all be vanquished before the master of Helegrod may be approached.Defeat Storvâgûn and claim the Giant WingDefeat Zaudru and claim the Spider WingDefeat Grisgart and claim the Drake WingSome people just like to help out.You often lend a helping hand.Many are the needs during the Farmers Faire.Be helpful during the Farmers Faire.Complete To Bamfurlong: Restocking the Mushroom TentComplete To the Appledores: Restocking the Apple StallComplete To Budgeford: Restocking the BaconComplete To Cotton's Farm: Restocking the CabbagesComplete To Sandson's Farm: Restocking the EggsComplete To Longo Burrows' Farm: Restocking the PipeweedComplete To the Tookland Beehives: Restocking the HoneyComplete To Northcotton Farm: Restocking the WineIn this time of strife, even a minstrel cannot travel the roads unarmed.Smite enemies with Herald's StrikeIn this time of strife, even a minstrel cannot travel the roads unarmed.Strike enemies with Healer's Strike, Hero's Strike, or Dissonant StrikeRegister your heritage with the notary.Elf notaries can be found in Duillond or Rivendell.'Where is it that you come from?''Where is it that you come from?''Where is it that you come from?''Ah... Beleriand.

