<rgb=#FF0000>ADVICE: You should equip your best weapon before attempting to engage in combat.</rgb>'You're a bolder hobbit than I! Well done, ${PLAYER}. Let's press on!''We're close now, ${PLAYER}! Odo's farm will get us safe to the road, and from there we can get to the nearest town... hopefully without encountering any spiders, or worse.''Come, ${PLAYER}! I can see that you have a brave spirit, but it is time to flee. The Baggins they captured is not the Baggins being hunted.

'The brigands will not follow us when they learn of their error, but it would be wise to be far away from here.

'My companion is outside, helping to rescue your friends. Let us join them!''Stay close to me this night, ${PLAYER}... we must get Amdir to safety. It is to Archet that we must flee!

'Bounder Boffin, you should go back to the Shire. Its bounds must be kept safe. Celandine, Mundo -- come with me. I worry for Mundo's safety when all the wicked folk west of the Greenway are searching for "Baggins". Alas that my true charge must wait!'Midsummer's Day has arrived, and with it the Great Wedding of King Elessar and Arwen Undómiel.The procession is underway, and King Aragorn Elessar II is waiting for you to walk down the aisle to him, where he has a few words for you.Walk down the aisle and speak to AragornYour place, from where you will have a fine view of the ceremony, is next to Meriadoc Brandybuck on the southern side of the aisle.Stand next to Merry on the southern side of the aisleThe processional continues while the Elves take their places atop the prow.Wait for the Elves to take their places as the processional continuesMithrandir has some words of welcome for the folk assembled atop the pier.Listen to Mithrandir's words of welcomeMithrandir has called for a moment of silence to remember those who did not live to see this day.<rgb=#00FF00>Mourn</rgb> to remember those who did not live to see this dayMithrandir wishes to speak some additional words of remembrance.Listen to Mithrandir's additional words of remembranceSome honoured guests have asked to speak some words at the ceremony.Listen to the speeches by honoured guestsSam has finished reciting his poem, and the assembled crowd cheers for the embarrassed hobbit.<rgb=#00FF00>Cheer</rgb> for SamThe speeches concluded, Mithrandir continues the wedding ceremony.Watch as Mithrandir continues the ceremonyThe time has come for King Elessar and Arwen Undómiel to exchange their vows, in view of the assembled masses.Witness the marriage of King Elessar and Arwen UndómielMithrandir's fireworks are as impressive as ever, and the celebration will continue long into the night.Mithrandir's fireworks signal an end to the ceremony, but only the start of the celebration'Mithrandir never fails to impress, does he not?

'But I understand the ceremony is merely the beginning of the festivities this night? I hope to see you later, my friend.'Aragorn smiles at you.

'I am pleased you could be here, ${PLAYER}, on this day of joy. Take your place beside Merry, my friend.'You are having a most peculiar dream.You are held in the grip of a peculiar dream.You are asleep, and experiencing a most peculiar dream...You are held in the grip of a dream.You are asleep and dreaming.As the Rangers led the halflings through Ithilien, they spoke freely and prepared an ill-fated ambush for a company of Haradrim.Mablung recalls standing at the halflings' camp-site.

Mablung is telling you more of the tale of the halflings in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Listen to Mablung's taleMablung recalls guarding the halflings and speaking to them of their plans.

Mablung is telling you more of the tale of the halflings in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Listen to Mablung's taleMablung recalls the Southrons breaking through the trap.

Mablung is telling you more of the tale of the halflings in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Listen to Mablung's taleMablung recalls the wild Mûmak and the aftermath of the battle.

Mablung is telling you more of the tale of the halflings in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Listen to Mablung's tale'That is all I have to tell, my friend.'For untold centuries, the humble folk known to themselves as the Holbytlan have lived peaceful lives among the hidden dells of Misthallow. Now, one of their number seeks to leave the safety of Lyndelby in search of adventure....Your good friend Valaric Túcca can hardly believe that you have made the decision to leave.Talk to your friend Valaric Túcca among the peaceful homes of the HolbytlanMeet with Heldric Túcca outside his home in Lyndelby as the sun rises on the day you have decided to leave.Meet with Heldric Túcca as the sun risesGrandmother Madelgard Túcca is waiting to speak with you as the sun rises on a beautiful day over the hidden Holbytlan village of Lyndelby.Talk to Grandmother Madelgard TúccaGrandmother Maddy asked you to say good-bye to some of the early risers of Lyndelby.Talk to Ogiva Túcca down the hillTalk to Vilihad on the path to the southTalk to Erma Túcca near the base of the hillYou have noticed Odger Túcca further down the path to the south-east, and should tell him about your plans.Talk to Odger Túcca further along the path to the south-eastOdger Túcca's best friend, his pet frog Croaker, has disappeared.Wait for Croaker to reveal where he has goneOdger Túcca's best friend, his pet frog Croaker, has disappeared, but you heard his croaking near the rocks to the south-west.Look for Croaker near the rocks to the south-westGoblins have snuck into the town of Lyndelby and now threaten your friends and family!Protect your friends and family from the goblinsThe Eagle Fanglind has long protected the Holbytlan from any who find their hidden valley, and today has been no different.Talk to Fanglind, one of the Great Eagles who protects your peopleFanglind has recommended that you search the satchel dropped by the goblins and equip one of the weapons you find within. Afterwards, he wants to talk to you some more.Search the goblin's satchel for a weapon to equip, and then talk to FanglindGrandmother Maddy stares at you with sadness, but with hope in her eyes as well.Talk to Grandmother MaddyGrandmother Maddy has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb> to your friends and family, and then to begin your grand adventure.<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> to your friends and family, the good Holbytlan of Lyndelby, and begin your grand adventureYour adventure begins, and you vow to do as Grandmother Maddy requested: to help anyone who has need of it.Your journey demands that you help folk who need itThe man is strangely-dressed but seems friendly, and any foe of goblins or Orc-kind is a friend to the Holbytlan.Talk to Meneldir and complete the quest 'A Larger World''I cannot believe you have truly decided to leave us, ${PLAYER}! I know we have spoken about this possibility for many years, but... well, I must admit I always thought I would be the first of the Holbytlan in living memory to leave this hidden vale, and the first to return!'

You tell Valaric that he is welcome to accompany you, and to his credit and his surprise he almost considers it. Then he shakes his head.

'Oh, no,' he stammers at last. 'It is a big world out there, they say, and I do not think I am quite ready to see it. But you are the tallest of us, and grew for the longest. If any of us have the courage to leave Misthallow, I believe you are the one!''So what has gotten my Heldric all in a bother, ${PLAYER}? And I have not seen Valaric this excited since... well, since Gísla accidentally doubled the recipe for her famous pie-fillings, but to speak honestly that was quite a day for all of us.'

You tell Grandmother Maddy that the time has finally arrived for you to leave Lyndelby, see the wider world, and have an adventure. She nods silently, and taps you on the nose.

'It was bound to happen sooner or later, dear ${PLAYER}. You have always been different, in your own way: more outgoing than the rest of us, and more curious about what lies beyond the mist-shrouded dells. And taller, too! The blood of the ancient Holbytlan is very strong in you, I have always said it! Haven't I, Heldric? Oh, he has stopped listening to me. That old goat!''You are up early today, ${PLAYER}. Are you planning to...'

Ogiva's cheerful words trail away into nothing, and her amiable expression is replaced with one of shock.

'This is the day! I knew it! I told Vilihad you were finally going to go and set out on your wanderings, and sure enough I was right! I did not know it would be this morning, perhaps, not exactly, but I have known for awhile that you were planning for just such a journey. That is terribly exciting, ${PLAYER}. You'll go and make us proud, see if you don't!''Today is the big day, then? Ogiva has been telling me you are soon to set out on some adventure or another, but I figured it wasn't really our business. I can't imagine leaving Lyndelby, but I suppose every one of us is different, after all.

'You be careful out there beyond Misthallow, ${PLAYER}. Who knows what dangers you might run into? The shrews are always getting into my crops and spoiling my lettuce, and I expect there are larger and more dangerous creatures out in the wide world. GIANT shrews, I wouldn't doubt it!''I just cannot believe you are leaving us, ${PLAYER}!'

Erma wipes away a tear and makes you promise that you will return after you have had your fill of adventure. You tell her you are certain to return to Lyndelby when you can, after you have seen what lies beyond the distant ridges on the horizon.

'The mountains are awfully tall to be climbed by one of the Holbytlan,' she says. 'I know Valaric says our people went that way, once, but he says a lot of things. Maybe you'll be the first of us to see what lies on the other side of them? If that's true, you be sure to come back and tell us all about it!''You are leaving Lyndelby in search of adventure? Good-bye then, ${PLAYER}. I will see you when you return, and...

'Oh! You should say good-bye to Croaker, too! He is simply the best frog-friend anyone's ever had, you know he is! You definitely need to say good-bye to Croaker, too. It will be some time before you come back, after all.''I saw the goblins from high above, ${PLAYER}, but I saw something else as well: I saw you bidding farewell to your folk, and I knew your mind. I have known what you intended for several weeks now, and have kept watch upon your steps. I hope you do not mind.

'I will continue to safe-guard your folk, as I have for all the years I have known you. But you will need to be properly-equipped if you are to survive the adventures that await you! You do not have the mighty talons of my kind, after all, though you are unusually tall and strong... for one of your folk. You are still very small when compared to the Great Eagles, and to the other peoples you will encounter beyond the ridges that surround your village.

'These goblins were thieves, and their leader possessed a bag of weapons. Perhaps you should avail yourself of this equipment; the goblin has no claim upon it, and its former owner cannot make use of it any longer, but in your hands it may yet do some good.''Do not forget to equip your new weapon, ${PLAYER}. I will not be able to protect you when you leave Misthallow, and you will need to rely upon your skills and the equipment you are able to find if you are to survive the challenges ahead of you.

'It is a dangerous world out there. Are you certain this is the life you have chosen? Most of your kind do not leave their homes, choosing to remain near the land of their birth.''I will not ask for you to stay, ${PLAYER}. I see that your mind is made.'

Grandmother Maddy smiles at you, and fondly tugs upon your ear.

'Now listen to me, dear one, because this is important and I will not repeat myself. You are to keep your eyes on the road ahead of you, and you will not worry about us; we have Fanglind and the other Eagles to keep watch over us, and Lyndelby will be fine while you are gone. But remember this: we are only letting you go so you can bring help to the folk you find out in that wide and dangerous world. You are to make yourself useful, ${PLAYER}! There are people out there who will need your help, and you should help them. I think that is the calling that draws you away from us, and it is only so you can answer it that I will permit you to go.

'Are we agreed? Then <rgb=#00FF00>wave</rgb> to us all and be off on your grand adventure, ${PLAYER}! And remember what I said!'Thorin and Company are preparing to leave from the Blue Mountains for the ancestral home of Thorin's folk, the Lonely Mountain. You are but a simple miner, but the wizard Gandalf has asked for your assistance.A wizened old man stands before you as you go on your way to the Silver Deep Mine.

You should walk towards him.Approach the old man who stands near <rgb=#00FF00>(Move forward by pressing W)</rgb>The wizard Gandalf the Grey, advisor of Thorin Oakenshield, wishes to have a word with you. As Thorin is the master of these halls, you think it best to listen.Talk to the wizard <rgb=#00FF00>(Right-click on Gandalf to interact)</rgb>You should accompany Gandalf, for he is a respected advisor of Thorin's.Walk with Gandalf and listen to him for a bit <rgb=#00FF00>(Move forward by pressing W; A and D to turn)</rgb>Walk with Gandalf while he wishes to have you near him.Follow Gandalf and listen to his musingsGormr Doursmith has been appointed Steward of Thorin's Halls while Thorin is away. Now that Thorin and Gandalf have departed, you should speak with Gormr to hear his instructions.Talk to Gormr, the new Steward of Thorin's HallA satchel full of equipment lies near the entrance to the Silver Deep Mine.

You should loot the satchel to equip what you will need for the day's work.Collect your equipment from the satchel near the door <rgb=#00FF00>(Right-click on glowing items to loot)</rgb>A satchel full of equipment lies near the entrance to the Silver Deep Mine. You should loot the satchel to equip what you will need for the day's work.Collect your equipment from the satchel near the door <rgb=#00FF00>(Right-click on glowing items to loot)</rgb>After you collected your weapon, a great quaking shook the very mountain above you. Gimli son of Glóin and Gormr are startled.Talk to Gimli to find out what to doGimli wishes for you to prove your strength before he allows you to follow him into the mine to rescue the workers. You never know what evils may appear when the mountains tremble.Spar with Gimli to practice your skill in battle <rgb=#00FF00>Be sure to equip your weapon</rgb>The entrance to the Silver Deep Mine stands before you.

Gimli wishes to meet you inside the unstable mine, where you will help him get the miners out. You should walk into the doorway.Ask Gimli what to do nextThe miners can be found throughout the mine, hard at work.

A quaking of the earth has troubled Gormr, the new leader. He and Gimli want this mine clear so that nobody gets hurt.Talk to Foreman OturFollow Foreman Otur to get help for Gimli.

While you were trying to call Tvistur to Thorin's ceremony, he broke through a wall, unleashing a troll. The troll slew him, then chased after Gimli. You should follow Otur and see how you can get help for Gimli.Talk to Foreman OturThe new tunnel excavated by Tvistur now yawns before you.

You should go down the tunnel to try to head off the troll as it pursues Gimli.Follow the tunnel opened by Tvistur to try to get to GimliYou seem to have uncovered some old ruins, apparently from ancient Elf-structures. A body lies among them.Examine the corpse in the Elf-ruinsFight your way deeper into the Silver Deep to help Gimli.

As you followed Otur, he discovered that the door that led to the bridge had been damaged by the troll's attacks. He asked you to go and help Gimli while he went off to get more help.Defeat cave-claws as you make your way to Gimli and the troll (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have made your way to Gimli. Help him, if you can!Search for GimliGandalf the Grey, a wizard accompanying Thorin's Company, saved Gimli from the troll.Talk to GandalfGandalf the Grey, a wizard accompanying Thorin's Company, saved Gimli from the troll.Talk to Gandalf<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The files you need to continue your adventures in Middle-earth should finish downloading shortly. Thank you for your patience!</rgb>'You found the body of a dwarf, did you? Do you hear that, Gormr? I wonder if ${PLAYER} has come upon Skorgrím, lying under the collapsed ruins where he was smitten by an Elf-warrior named Talagan.

'But that is a matter for years long passed. My business is with Thorin today. Gormr may look into the grave of his ancestor while he is Steward of this land in Thorin's absence.''You there! You are a miner here, are you not? Tell me your name then, my good Dwarf.

'${PLAYER}...a fine name. I am Gandalf, if you do not know me. I am also Gandalf if you DO know me...Gandalf the Grey.

'Now, will you humour an old man and walk with me for a spell? I am quite tired and could use the company.''He doesn't listen, and so I will have to give things a little nudge. You see, we need another party member for the company that departs for the Lonely Mountain. Thirteen won't do.''We've got to clear out all these miners. A shaking tunnel is never a good sign, and we could even feel it outside!

'Quickly, ${PLAYER}! You take this passage straight ahead, and I'll go off into the side passage.''All right, young one...you have dilly-dallied long enough. You ought to get back to work now. Hasn't your foreman given you enough to do?''I hope this is not an ill omen for my father's journey with Thorin.''Have you equipped your weapon yet, ${PLAYER}? Quickly now -- practice with me before you go into the mine. You never know what evils may appear when the mountains tremble!' 

<rgb=#00FF00>ACCESSING YOUR INVENTORY: Press 'i' to open your inventory to see the weapon or left-click on the bag icons on the bottom of your screen.</rgb>

<rgb=#00FF00>EQUIPPING YOUR WEAPON: Right-click on the weapon in your inventory to equip it. This will replace the flimsy weapon you currently have equipped.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>ADVICE: You should equip your best weapon before attempting to engage in combat.</rgb>'So we have the order to clear out? Good -- if I didn't know better, I'd think there was a troll romping around in the mountain.

'There is one miner left down this way. Let's go fetch him.''We must be quick. I don't know how long Gimli can keep that troll busy before the beast overpowers him.

'Follow me!'While travelling through the Chetwood, you were waylaid by brigands and taken captive. You now find yourself in a cell, searching for a means of escape.You awake in a holding pen in a brigand camp. A grim-looking man -- a Ranger, Strider -- is standing before you. As you groggily stand up, his urgent voice reaches your ears.Leave your cell and approach your rescuer <rgb=#00FF00>(Use W to move forward)</rgb>A satchel is on the floor near your rescuer.

Strider told you to search the satchel for any weapons and collect its contents, for you will need to defend yourself during this daring escape.Search the satchel for weapons <rgb=#00FF00>(Right-click the satchel to loot it)</rgb>Strider has bested the brigand guards, but he warns there are more enemies ahead.

The Ranger wants you to practice combat by sparring with him to ensure that you are able to protect yourself during the escape.Speak with Strider <rgb=#00FF00>(Right-click Strider to talk)</rgb>Now that you have practiced combat, speak with Strider and find out what to do next.Speak with StriderStrider has left the jailhouse and entered the yard. He is waiting for you there.Follow Strider outsideNow that you have left the jailhouse, speak with Stider and find out where to go next.Speak with StriderCelandine Brandybuck is being held ahead in the brigand camp.

Strider wishes you to rescue the hobbits, starting with Celandine, while he goes off in search of signs of Mordor (whose presence is startlingly near.) You will need to defeat any brigands you come upon while searching for the hobbits.Defeat Celandine's captors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Celandine is being held in a cage against the wall of the enclosure.

You have defeated Celandine's captors, but you have not found Mundo Sackville-Baggins. Celandine may be able to tell you where Mundo is being held.Mundo Sackville-Baggins is being held in the yard beyond the gate of Celandine's holding pen.

Celandine's distraction was a success. Only one brigand remains behind to guard Mundo. You should get rid of him quickly.Defeat Mundo's captorMundo is tied to a post in the yard.

Despite the defeat of his captor, Mundo Sackville-Baggins appears particularly displeased. You should encourage him to join you.Speak with Mundo Sackville-BagginsStrider and Amdir await you and the hobbits at the main gate.

You have freed both of the missing hobbits, but you have not yet escaped the camp.Find Strider and AmdirAmdir lies just beyond the main gate.

The Ranger Amdir was struck down by the Black Rider before Strider could drive him off. You should ask Strider what to do, for the situation is now dire.Strider waits near the main gate.

Amdir is gravely wounded. Strider will best know what to do to help his friend.Talk to StriderStrider waits near the main gate.

Amdir is gravely wounded. Strider will best know what to do to help his friend.Talk to Strider'Well done. Your skill in battle is most impressive! Now, listen closely: I will need your help getting out of here. When we leave this jailhouse, the real battle will begin.''Alas, I am too late. Amdir has been pierced with a morgul-blade; this does not bode well. We need to leave this place at once. Archet is nearby and will serve as a good resting place while Amdir recovers. Quickly, follow me!''Here we part for a time, ${PLAYER}. You should free the two innocent hobbits also being held captive here: Celandine Brandybuck and Mundo Sackville-Baggins.

'I must search for signs of the servant of Mordor and learn what I can of his connexion to the Blackwolds. Amdir, my fellow Ranger, is making a safe path for us -- he will be waiting for us at the main gate.

'Free Celandine first. It is Mundo they want alive, for they have mistaken him for someone more valuable. When you have both hobbits safe, seek Amdir near the main gate. Then we make for Archet, where we will find safety.'<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The files you need to continue your adventures in Middle-earth should finish downloading shortly. Thank you for your patience!</rgb>'Thank you, thank you, thank you! I was starting to worry that this little misadventure would be the end of me! These brigands are appalling folk.'

'My friend Mundo is nearby, I think. We must save him as well! The brigands have been saying terrible things!

'We'll need a distraction...and I know just what to do!''Good...the hobbits are...are out of danger. I am glad.

'Do not...concern yourself with me. The greatest danger...has passed. The Nazgûl fear those who wield fire....''It's about time! Was I expected to...to rescue myself?

'Come on, you big clodpole! Get me out of here before those ruffians return. They want to sell me off like a sack of potatoes!''Arm yourself with what weapons you find while I fend off these brigands!'

<rgb=#00FF00>ITEM INTERACTION: To loot the satchel, use your mouse to left-click on the item twice, or right click on the item once.</rgb>'You are not the only prisoner here, friend. My fellow Amdir and I have come to rescue a hobbit, but it turns out he is not the hobbit we have been tracking.

'This escape will be dangerous for us all, for I know that a great evil lurks here. I have heard of its movements, and I can feel its presence. Do you know how to fight? You should practice with me to get a feel for that weapon.'

