To start fighting Talagan, <rgb=#00ff00>right mouse-click</rgb> on him to initiate your standard attack. To use your <rgb=#ffff00>Abilities</rgb> either <rgb=#00ff00>left mouse-click</rgb> on the <rgb=#ffff00>Action Buttons</rgb> on your <rgb=#ffff00>Quick Slots Bar</rgb> (found at the bottom of the screen) or by pressing the associated <rgb=#ffff00>Hotkey</rgb>.

Defeat Talagan to advance.Talk to your master, Talagan SilvertongueA great thunder has shaken the library. Speak with Elrond to find out what you should do.Talk to ElrondTalagan Silvertongue has told you that he would like you to make your way to the courtyard of Edhelion and help defend it from further attack.Talk to Talagan Silvertongue outside of the libraryFollow Edhelben as he directs you to the courtyard of Edhelion.

You master Talagan Silvertongue has told you that he would like you to make your way to the courtyard of Edhelion and help defend it from further attack.Follow EdhelbenFight your way to the courtyard of Edhelion.Defeat Dourhand invaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Now that you have reached the courtyard of Edhelion, follow Dorongúr Whitethorn into it.Follow Dorongúr WhitethornSpeak with Dorongúr Whitethorn.Talk to DorongúrFollow Elrond and Dorongúr Whitethorn to the entrance to the halls of Edhelion.

Soon after you entered the courtyard of Edhelion, the Dourhands broke down the gate. Skorgrím and a party of dwarves ran towards the entrance to Edhelion's halls.Follow Elrond and Dorongúr WhitethornSpeak with Elrond.Talk to ElrondYou beloved master Talagan has sacrificed himself to ensure that the relics of Edhelion did not fall into the hands of Skorgrím.

You should now speak with Elrond about all that has transpiredTalk to Elrond<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The files you need to continue your adventures in Middle-earth should finish downloading shortly. Thank you for your patience!</rgb>'Alas, ${PLAYER}...you have lost your beloved master. You may blame me for his death -- I could have saved him, but he bade me go to you instead. Talagan was brave to spare your young life.

'Edhelion is ruined now...Talagan was not the only Elf to die today. Skorgrím will trouble us no more, and the relics are safely buried, but it was such a needless battle!

'Edhelion will fade....''You cannot tarry here any longer, ${PLAYER}. Skorgrím's forces are upon us, and I fear they make straight for this library!

'He seeks the relics of Edhelion, though I do not know what a dwarf could want with them. These relics were once coveted by a Gaunt-lord of old. I think the fool believes he can become immortal if he acquires them.''Good -- you are better armed. Your master Talagan wishes to see you before you venture out into the fray. But do hurry! This place is not safe for you.'

<rgb=#00FF00>ACCESSING YOUR INVENTORY: Press 'i' to open your inventory to see the weapon or left-click on the bag icons on the bottom of your screen.</rgb>

<rgb=#00FF00>EQUIPPING YOUR WEAPON: Right-click on the weapon in your inventory to equip it. This will replace the flimsy weapon you currently have equipped.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>ADVICE: You should equip your best weapon before attempting to engage in combat.</rgb>'There is no time to waste, ${PLAYER}. Go outside with Talagan and see what can be done to stop Skorgrím from advancing. The Dourhands cannot be allowed to take the Gaunt-lord's relics; I have vowed to keep them safe.

'I will hide the relics, then I will join Talagan in protecting the library. Be safe, young ${CLASS}.''Go, ${PLAYER}! This is where the storm will converge. Edhelben is down below -- he will let you through the gate to protect what is left of this refuge.''Those Dourhands were everywhere! I honestly did not think we would survive, but Dorongúr had the sense to bar the doors to the courtyard. With the courtyard as our final redoubt, we were able to push the Dourhand dwarves back.

'I know though that if the courtyard falls, all of Edhelion may go with it. You must help in the defence of the courtyard. Go up the stairs to the west and travel along until you come to the back gate. Once there, Dorongúr should let you in.

'Be careful; a few of the invaders may still be about.''Good, young ${PLAYER}, you are whole. Do not worry about me, I will be fine. It is but a minor wound. Once I bind it, I will make my way into the courtyard to help as I may. But do not wait on me: go to the courtyard now and help in its defence until Elrond arrives.

'This gate is barred, for fear the other gates will not hold, but the back entrance may be open. Go up the stairs to the west and travel along until you come to the back gate. Once there, Dorongúr will let you in.

'Be careful, though: there may still be a few stragglers left behind.''Those in the courtyard will need your help until Elrond returns. The main gates are barred, so you should travel to the west and go up the stairs. From there, travel along to the back entrance. Hopefully, someone will let you in.

'Be careful, though...there may still be a few stragglers left behind that you may have to deal with.''I fear for Edhelion. How much more can we withstand? And I hear that Skorgrím has not even shown himself yet...which means the worst is yet to come.''${PLAYER}, my dear student! I wish I could let you stay safe within these walls, but Elrond tells me that Skorgrím makes straight for this library.

'You must survive the battle outside, I am afraid. I worry for you! Duel with me one last time, my friend, and show me that you are ready. It will ease my heart!'The ceremony may be over, but the festivities continue! The great wedding-feast will last well into the night, with the noise of celebration continuing nearly until dawn.Merethien, the Master Foodmonger of Minas Tirith, has some questions for Merry and Pippin concerning what qualifies as a 'banquet' at their home, the distant Shire. Furthermore, she is pleased to have an excuse to leave Ioreth's chatter and Galathir's lecture behind her.Talk to MerethienMerethien wants to know if Merry and Pippin are satisfied that the wedding-feast she has helped to prepare can compare with the banquets they described in the Shire.Talk to MerryPippin wants to return to his own table for a bit, and wishes for you and Merry to follow him.Follow Pippin back to his tableBeregond and his family sit at Pippin's table with a number of Gondorian nobles.Talk to BeregondThrymm Red-beard has obtained a captive audience, and is regaling them with tales of his adventures.Talk to Thrymm Red-beardThrymm Red-beard has obtained a captive audience, and is regaling them with tales of his adventures.Listen (again) to Thrymm's tale of his exploitsPrince Imrahil was given a message for you.Talk to Prince ImrahilPrince Imrahil told you a wine steward working at the wedding-feast wanted you to meet with him downstairs.Talk to the wine steward downstairsThe wine steward gave you some fine bottles of Gondor's finest to use as a peace offering with the 'rough sorts' gathering outside.

You have been tasked with leaving Merethrond by the front doors and confronting the group of rough sorts the wine steward described.Go outside and confront the 'rough sorts' described by the wine stewardThe Grey Company has gathered to celebrate the wedding of their chieftain, and to honour the great deeds done on his behalf.Listen to the words of the Grey CompanyThe Grey Company has gathered to celebrate the wedding of their chieftain, and to honour the great deeds done on his behalf.Talk to RadanirTalk to CulangYou should return to the wedding-feast, which will likely soon be winding down.Go back inside Merethrond and rejoin the wedding-feastThe wine steward is being regaled with tales of Thrymm's heroics, and he wishes to speak with you.Talk to the wine stewardThe wedding-feast continues into the night and you should speak with King Elessar before the festivities conclude.Talk to King Elessar upstairs, on the western side of the feast-hallPrince Faramir of Ithilien is at the head table in Merethrond.Talk to Prince Faramir of IthilienSamwise Gamgee is at the head table in Merethrond.Talk to Samwise GamgeeA loud disturbance has caused a commotion on the western side of the feast-hall.Investigate the disturbance on the western side of the feast-hallKing Elessar wishes to speak with you.Talk to King Elessar'Thank you for rescuing me, ${PLAYER}. I intend no disrespect for any of the fine folk at my table, for they are all worthies of Gondor in their own ways... but some of them can be most tiring.

'Come with me, my helpful friend. I see the hobbits with whom I spoke right over there.''What do you think, Pip? What would old Flourdumpling have to say about the courses on offer here? Oh yes, Merethien, I think this wedding-feast can stand quite comfortably alongside the very finest of Shire banquets!''${PLAYER}, it is my pleasure to introduce you to my wife Gilithel, and I believe you have already met our son Bergil. He was quite the trouble-maker in Minas Tirith, running through the lower tiers with his friends, and he has found new ways to cause mischief in Ithilien. But he is a good lad, and at his age I was much the same.

'I must confess to you I did not think I would be welcomed back to the city for the King's wedding, but word was sent to Lord Faramir, and we could not refuse.''And so, with our horses refreshed, we crossed the Mering-stream and rode hard through the Beacon Hills. We were so close, but not yet close enough: we were beset by Orcs and Variags near Amon Dîn! We broke through the line of Variags, but they did not pursue us. I think now I know the reason: they knew the road ahead would be held against us!'

Thrymm pauses in his tale, seeming to see you for the first time.

'Oh, ${PLAYER}, pull up a seat! I was just telling these fine folk of Gondor about some of my recent adventures!''One of the wine stewards came by earlier, before our friend from Rohan launched into his... full-throated... tales of bravery. This steward asked if we would do him the kindness of delivering you to him if you chanced to come by our table.

'He said he would be downstairs, ${PLAYER}. Now that I have executed this charge, perhaps I will learn what else my daughter would hear of the new king of Rohan, and why the speaking of his name brings such a blush to her cheeks....''Ah, there you are, ${PLAYER}! I am pleased the Prince of Dol Amroth gave you my message, for it is urgent and I did not know where else I might turn. There is something of a problem, you see, and I need you to ensure it does not get any worse!

'Some rough sorts have gathered outside. I am afraid they might intend to disrupt the wedding-feast in some way. They were asking for you!

'Here, take these bottles of wine out to them. It could be that an offering of peace will send them happily on their way. And if not, well... your deeds are well-known, and such rough sorts as these may take one look at you and decide it would be best for them to go elsewhere!''Who can say when we will all be once again together, ${PLAYER}? Each of us has business elsewhere: some in the north, some here in the south. It would have been a shame not to mark the occasion. Is that so unusual? We all feel a kinship with each other, borne of our shared duty; it is strange to me that we must now separate.

'Lothrandir wishes to return to Forochel, the land of the Snowmen, so I will travel with him part of the way with some others of the company. Techeron will reside once again in Evendim, but on the way we will pay a visit to Saeradan and learn the tale of his own return to Eriador with our fallen brothers. Idhrien and Langlas plan to stay for awhile at Esteldín with Mincham. Angwedh has not yet decided where he will travel, just that his road lies to the north. If he has a place in mind, he has not shared it with us; I think the wilderness calls to him.'

Radanir smirks at you.

'Do you know what calls to me? The food of the north-lands! The food at this feast is too richly-made, too covered in sauces, too soft, and there's too much of it. There isn't anything to sink your teeth into, ${PLAYER}. Give me the crusty bread and old cheese of the Forsaken Inn, a day's ride east of Bree... that is all I need.''The Grey Company rode from Eriador to aid the chieftain of the Dúnedain, and now many of us will return to our homes; but not all. We all have our own reasons, for the king has not set a bond upon us that we do not choose for ourselves.

'But there remains the question: what shall be done about the land that lies on Gondor's doorstep? Mordor lies there, the Black Land, and who knows what sorceries of the Witch-king may lurk within the Morgul Vale. I will help my king to combat these evils, and so too will Dagoras, and Faeron, and Mithrendan.

'Others of the Grey Company may decide to do the same... but they must choose for themselves. We have done what we intended, but I wager that some may discover they wish to do more. Gondor awaits an era of peace... but it will not arrive without we who are willing to fight for it.''I played my part as well as I could, ${PLAYER}! Were your friends able to surprise you?'

The wine steward glances at Thrymm Red-beard, whose long-winded description of past glories has shown no sign of cessation; indeed, he may have started anew.

'Perhaps you can go back upstairs and see if my services are needed? I am sure there must be a need for more wine... there simply must....''I hope you are enjoying yourself, ${PLAYER}. I confess to you that much of tonight has passed by with dizzying speed, but it is a joyful motion and I would trade it for nothing else.

'Might I ask a favour of you? Earlier I spoke with Faramir about a matter of some importance, and I am interested to learn if he has come to a decision. Would you speak with him and determine if this be so?''It is a pleasure to speak with you, my friend. I saw you earlier, when our Halfling friends ran by the table on their way to do some mischief... it was a spirited chase, and brought a smile to my lips; that has been rare enough in the days since... well, in the past few days.'

Faramir falls silent, and you take the opportunity to ask if he has considered the topic about which King Elessar inquired. Faramir studies you quietly.

'He told you not the subject of our discussion? He is more subtle than I expected, or perhaps it is the hand of his Queen that makes him so! Ah, ${PLAYER}, you are a friend, so I will speak freely.

'The king knows that my heart has been captured by the Lady Éowyn of Rohan. She returned to the Riddermark in the company of her brother while they prepare for the funeral of Théoden, and while she has been gone my heart has been in darkness! Ever she occupies my thoughts, and I know I will never again feel happiness or joy while we are apart. I dare not hope she feels the same, and would not! For I would wish her no unhappiness.''I expect Grimbeorn and his animals will enliven Merethrond for a time. Good! It will give us a brief respite from all this celebration!

'Arwen and I would like to speak to you, ${PLAYER}, in a more quiet setting. Let us find one.''Dear me! I am pleased that Prince Faramir has made up his mind, but to be completely honest with you, ${PLAYER}, I had not quite gotten around to the advice I intended to give to him!

'Still, all is well when it ends well... which it will, if Lady Éowyn agrees to his proposal. If she does not, I fear the reputation of hobbit-wisdom may suffer in Ithilien and Gondor! Oh dear!'After a day of hard labour in Barad-dûr, you return to the dungeons for a brief reprieve. However, a sudden series of tremors has roused you from your rest.Lethi can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

You have woken from a short rest to find the other Stout-axes in your cell awake as well.Talk to LethiYour rations can be found on a chunk of rubble near your bunk in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

Awoken by tremors and unlikely to find more rest, Lethi has suggested that you finish your rations before cultists of the Order of the Eye return to the dungeons.Finish your rationsYour emptied plate of rations can be found near your bunk in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

You should add it to the pile of plates near the gate to your cell.Collect your plateVaski can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

After setting your plate down, Vaski has called you over. You should talk to Vaski.Talk to VaskiVaski can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

Vaski has heard several disquieting rumours in the Dark Tower and wishes to share them with you.Tell Vaski <rgb=#FF00FF>no</rgb> and ask him to share what he heardLethi and Vaski can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

Eager to share rumours while the Order of the Eye is absent, Vaski desires to tell you of what he has heard.Listen to Vaski and LethiLethi can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

Frustrated with Vaski's recklessness, Lethi has put an end to the conversation.Talk to LethiYour bunk can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

After a tense exchange between Lethi and Vaski, Lethi has suggested that you all try to rest in your bunks before dawn.You are trying to rest.Try to restNúluzagar can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

You brief rest was interrupted by the harsh voice of the cultist, Núluzagar. You should hearken to Núluzagar before his patience wears thin.Talk to Núluzagar'It's early yet. Even for Him.'

Lethi glances upward.

'It's been going on nigh an hour now, I reckon. I s'pose it's a fool's hope to think we'll get any more rest before dawn.

'You've still got a bit of your rations left, ${PLAYER}. You should eat while you can.''I don't know how you can eat that... even the rats taste better.'

Vaski peers out into the dungeon-halls of Barad-dûr.

'Ah, but I don't think either of us will have to eat like Orcs for much longer. There have been rumblings, you know....

'You have heard, haven't you?''Is that all then, Vaski? Nothing else for the Order to hear?'

Vaski begins to open his mouth, but after noticing the stern look on Lethi's face, he decides to remain silent.

'I thought as much.'Núluzagar stares at you impassively.Sticks and stones may break my bones, but words will never hurt me...that is unless they are part of some spell -- those can sting.People often signal their disdain for you.While great size and strength can be intimidating, attitude can also take you a long way.You seem to be rather intimidating.After rescuing you from the Blackwold brigands and a mysterious Black Rider, the Ranger Amdir brought you to the village of Archet in the Chetwood, east of Bree-town. The town, under threat of attack, prepares a defence against the Blackwolds.Amdir may be found resting on the ground near the centre of Archet, outside The Mad Badger Inn.

The Ranger Amdir has spread word that he wishes to speak with you.'Oh, hello there! You are the one who came with that Ranger, Amdir, the other night, aren't you? What a tale he told of your adventure. You must be quite brave!

'Oh, don't mind my blather! I think Amdir wanted to speak with you. Last I saw him, he was resting on the ground just south of here, around the corner of the big building there.

'He looked awfully pale. That hurt he took must be worse than it looked.''Gracious, just look where they want me to stay! This is nothing like home. And they say I can't go home until those Blackwold fellows are dealt with. This is outrageous!

'Well, I don't need you hanging about now, bothering me. Go talk to that Amdir fellow. He's sitting just south of here.

'I've no interest in sharing my troubles with the likes of you. Now leave me be!''That Amdir fellow who brought you in has been asking for you. He's outside The Mad Badger Inn, near the centre of town.''I've got nothing to tell you. I just want out of this village! I tell you, this whole affair has been an insult!

'If you want to talk to someone, go see that Amdir fellow.''Ah, ${PLAYER}. It is good to see you whole and hale. You proved yourself quite the hero, leading the hobbits and me here to Archet last evening. I must confess that I do not recall much of the journey.

'Nay, do not concern yourself with my injuries; though they appear grave, I have taken worse. My only fear is that the blade may have been poisoned, but young Celandine is seeing to my needs.

'There is a matter that needs immediate attention, one that I cannot undertake. Captain Brackenbrook, the founder of the garrison here in Archet, suffers my presence only because of my injuries. Few in Bree-land trust Rangers.'Strider will rest easy if Archet is made aware of the imminent threat from the Blackwolds, but the leader of the town's garrison, Captain Brackenbrook, is distrustful of the dangerous-looking Rangers. He simply will not heed Strider's warning.Captain Brackenbrook is in the town of Archet, near The Mad Badger Inn.

You should speak with Captain Brackenbrook on Strider's behalf and try to convince him to heed the Blackwold threat.Talk to Captain Brackenbrook in ArchetThe townsfolk of Archet are standing around the town, the presence of Ranger guests having drawn their attention.

You should speak to the townsfolk to see if anyone else is on your side and not Brackenbrook's.See if Kate Henseed will believe your warningSee if Peg Pruner will believe your warningSee if Constable Thistlewool will believe your warningStrider is in the town of Archet, awaiting word.

You should speak with Strider and tell him of Captain Brackenbrook's folly.Tell Strider that the people of Archet do not believe you'Perhaps you can help, ${PLAYER}. The people of Archet will be in great danger when the Blackwolds execute the plan we witnessed last night. The Captain here, a Man named Brackenbrook, does not like my look, and will not heed my warnings.

'Pray, speak to him on my behalf, and see if you can rouse him!

'Every moment I spend here is a moment in which my true charge plunges blindly nearer to unfathomable peril! The Black Rider you saw last night seeks a Baggins, and our friend Mundo is not the one.''I am worried for Amdir and worried for Archet, but I must find the real Mr. Baggins before the Black Riders do. Brackenbrook is a fool to risk the doom of his people on his dislike for my looks!''Did you wander in here last night with those Rangers? I do not like the look of those fellows one bit, but I let them stay on account of the pale one's wounds.

'You say the Blackwolds mean to attack us, but I do not believe it, not without proof. Those brigands have always been about -- they are an unruly lot, but not murderous.

'I'll not be attacking them without good reason. If you must, talk to folks around town and get their opinions. If they are on your side, I'll consider the Ranger's warning.''Argue all you like! I won't be attacking innocent people without reason, brigands or no. And I think you'll find my townsfolk agree with me.''If Captain Brackenbrook says we're safe, then we're safe. He's always done a fine job at protecting our village! Why would the Blackwold wanderers suddenly attack us now?''I see that your friend is wounded, and I hope it was not the Blackwolds that did it to him....

'I truly trust Captain Brackenbrook, for he has always kept us safe since he took charge of Archet. I won't argue with the captain, but I will help the injured fellow in any way that I can.''You think the Blackwolds mean to attack us? Don't be absurd! They harbour no love for us, but they haven't a leader, and they fight more among themselves than they do with outsiders.

'They couldn't raid a squirrel nest, let alone our town!''Alas for peaceful folk everywhere! It is an enormous task to convince them that evil people with evil intentions will commit evil deeds.

'It seems that I cannot leave yet. Amdir needs my help, and I have pressing work to do in Archet to get these people ready for the impending storm. If you help me, perhaps I can leave before tonight.'Elladan, one of Elrond's sons, has come to Edhelion to investigate a disturbing dream that troubled his father.The Elves of Elrond's Company can be found around the Edhelion Watch.

You should seek out Elves with ideas on where to start investigating the dream.Seek Merethen's insight on the riddle of Elrond's dreamThe Elves of Elrond's Company can be found around the Edhelion Watch.

You should seek out Elves with ideas on where to start investigating the dream.Seek Dorollas' insight on the riddle of Elrond's dreamElladan waits on the road to Edhelion.

You should speak with Elladan of what you learned from Merethen and Dorollas.Talk to Elladan'My father is great among the Wise, and his dreams and foretellings do not often stray from the mark. These are the words he imparted to me:

  "Blood-red footsteps
  Upon snow coloured black,
  Where the Dour King walks 
  to take back his throne
  and finish what was begun."

'I am no riddle-master, but some of the Elves of my company have skill in solving such things.

'Come, let us speak with the riddle-masters Merethen and Dorollas, for Dorollas bade us come here. Hopefully they know where to start looking.''I was the one who led the party here, for I believe the Dour King is none other than Skorgrím, king of the Dourhands of old.

'There is only one problem with my logic: Skorgrím has been dead for many long years. He died here, when he tried to raid Edhelion for Elven relics that he believed would ensure his immortality.

'I hope I have not led the party astray, but my heart tells me Skorgrím is part of this story.''Mae govannen -- I am here to help solve the riddle that is Elrond's dream.

'Look yonder, ${PLAYER}. Thorin's Hall belches smoke and soot, and the white snow of the mountain is black ere it touches the floor of the valley.

'"Upon snow coloured black...." What do you think? It is rather literal for a riddle.''Dorollas led us here because he believes that Skorgrím is the Dour King in my father's dream? Had I known, I would never have let this party be led here. Skorgrím is dead; my father watched him die!

'But Merethen believes she has found a piece of the puzzle -- the black snow, dirtied from the Dourhands' slovenly stewardship of these halls.

'I will permit the investigation to continue, but I am very skeptical and disappointed in Dorollas's judgement.''You should return to Elladan.''Perhaps Dorollas will have more insight.''Merethen and Dorollas are both here at the Edhelion Watch. You should seek them among the Elves of this company.'A party of Longbeards and a party of Elves have returned to Thorin's Hall after a long absence from both. Nos Grimsong of the dwarves has come to offer his aid to the Elves and to find out why they have returned at this time.Elladan, a son of Elrond Halfelven, stands not far from Nos Grimsong.

You should speak with Elladan to learn on what errand the Elves of Rivendell have ventured so far into Ered Luin.Talk to Elladan son of Elrond'Here we are, as Dwalin bade, standing among this party of Elves who arrived when we did. But now what? Who should we talk to?

'That fellow over there, the dark-haired one, looks to be the leader of this company. Dwalin sent us to find out why they are here, and if we may be of any assistance to them.

'You are the more courteous dwarf, ${PLAYER}. Go on -- speak to that tall fellow! Do you think he speaks Westron?''Please speak with that tall Elf on Dwalin's behalf! He stands just there, beneath that gate facing the ruins.''Interesting! We have followed the signs of my father's dream to this place, and the dwarves have followed the signs of trouble here as well.

'I wonder if the two quests are not unrelated, ${PLAYER}. What do you think?

'Well, let us begin our investigation, now that we are all here. Elrohir, my brother, has already gone out to scout the lands. Dwalin, though a dwarf, is a friend to Rivendell. We will lend him what help we can.'After being away for centuries, you  return to the refuge of Edhelion, along with the sons of Elrond and Dorongúr Whitethorn.Dorongúr Whitethorn is at the bottom of the steps within the ruins of Edhelion, beyond the gate.

Dorongúr Whitethorn wishes to speak to you about a matter of great importance.Talk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion'Welcome, ${PLAYER}. I know it has been many, many years since you last laid eyes upon Edhelion. I know the pain you feel upon seeing it as it is, for I too was here when Edhelion fell. It is hard to bear knowing what has become of it and harder to hold back the anger such a sight stirs in my breast....

'There are more important matters, though, to which we must attend. Dorongúr Whitethorn is here and wishes to speak with you. He awaits you  at the bottom of the stairs to the south.''Dorongúr awaits you at the bottom of the stairs to the south.''Ah, it is good to see you once more, ${PLAYER}. Master Elrond is concerned that some great evil is about to be committed here, though he could not see clearly what it is. I would like your help in discovering the nature of the evil.

'Before we delve into this mystery, it would be wise to reflect upon the events of the past. Perhaps they can guide us in the present...and the future. You should seek the counsel of another ${CLASS}, I think, and learn to better your skills.'After many years of absence, a party of Longbeards has returned to the Blue Mountains and Thorin's Hall.Nos Grimsong can be found in the north-west corner of Frerin's Court.

Bolli instructed you to lend your aid to Nos Grimsong.Talk to Nos Grimsong in Frerin's Court'It's hard to see the old place a mess like this. You would think with all the tribute the Dourhands have been withholding, they could keep the place neat and tidy. Bah, ill-mannered louts is what they are. But there I go running my mouth off again.

'Nos Grimsong over there has been handling our efforts to clean up trouble with the local wildlife. Go see if he has any tasks you can help with.

'Be sure to come back to me later, though; I'll have more work for you after you have gotten your beard wet.''Well met, ${PLAYER}. Aye, I have work for you. It is good that Bolli sent you.''You should go talk to Nos Grimsong. He is just over there, in the north-west corner of Frerin's Court.'With the help of the Ranger Strider and his friend Amdir, you have escaped death at the hands of a group of brigands called the Blackwolds.

You are now in the peaceful village of Archet, and you have witnessed evidence that this town is at great risk of an attack from the very Blackwolds that held you captive.Amdir, very pale and wounded, is sitting in Archet near The Mad Badger Inn.

You should check on Amdir, for he was stabbed last night while helping to rescue you and the two hobbits from the Blackwolds.See for yourself how Amdir faresStrider kneels beside his friend Amdir, near The Mad Badger Inn in the village of Archet.

You should speak with Strider, for Amdir implied that Strider's need is the more pressing.Learn why Strider is torn'You are awake, ${PLAYER}! Thank goodness. You were exhausted after what happened last night, but that Ranger got us all safe to Archet in the end.

'I am terribly worried for his friend! Amdir looks so very ill. You can check on him if you like; he is just over there, to the west of where I am standing. Do you see him there, across the lane?''Did you wander in with those Rangers and halflings in the middle of the night as well? I hope you'll not be bringing any trouble with you. That wound looks suspicious to me!''That poor dear Ranger... he was so brave last night! I do hope that Strider can help him. I don't have any experience with such violent wounds.''I haven't had breakfast yet! This is intolerable. First kidnapped and now starved... I do not like Big Folk one bit!''So you are awake at last, ${PLAYER}? You earned your rest, for you fought bravely last night. As for myself, I found no peace in slumber.

'The blade of the Black Rider pierced only my shoulder, though not deeply. I am chilled, but it is no matter....

'Thank you for your concern, but it is Strider for whom I fear! He is charged with a great task, but he tarries for my sake, and for Archet's.''Look not to me, but to Strider. It is he who is in need of your help this day.''Hail, ${PLAYER}. Amdir is right -- I am torn asunder! I do not wish to leave him in this state, and Archet must be warned that the Blackwolds mean to raid the town, but I should be seeking a different Baggins right now!'Cooking is an especially important profession -- ask any hobbit -- that can take a significant amount of time to master. Every true cook starts with the basics, and this introduction to the fine art of cooking will provide you with everything that you need to become a true master of the pot and pan.

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Be careful! You will need to complete the correct recipes and deliver the correct items outlined in this quest.

You will need to execute the cup of spring barley flour and hard biscuit recipes and deliver the hard biscuit. Failing to do so will force you to obtain new raw materials or to restart the quest after a 24-hour delay.</rgb>You should speak with the Novice Cook to learn more about cooking and set yourself on a path to good eating.The Novice Cook provided you with a <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> full of ingredients that you can use to execute the hard biscuit recipe. Open the <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> to get the ingredients.

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Ingredients for Cooks are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the farming profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.</rgb>The Novice Cook provided you with the ingredients necessary to create hard biscuits. First, however, you must prepare one of the most important ingredients: a <rgb=#FF00FF00>cup of spring barley flour</rgb>.Using the ingredients you received, craft a <rgb=#FF00FF00>cup of spring barley flour</rgb>The cup of spring barley flour is complete, and you are now ready to make the <rgb=#FF00FF00>hard biscuit</rgb>, as instructed by the Novice Cook.Using the ingredients you have obtained, cook a <rgb=#FF00FF00>hard biscuit</rgb>The recipe is complete. <rgb=#FF00FF00>Do not eat or sell the hard biscuit!</rgb> It is time to show your handiwork to the Novice Cook.'It looks as though you have strayed a little ways from home, ${RACE}, and you want to learn to cook up some tasty meals?

'I'd prefer swinging a hammer, but if you prefer a pan, who I am to judge?

'Speak with Islífur near the oven. He has offered to teach all the newest cooks the basics.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'You are far from home, ${RACE}. We will honour your request and help you as you learn the art of cooking.

'Speak with Faengamil near the oven here at the Terrace. She will provide you with the necessary guidance that you need to learn more of the cooking profession.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'Well then, you wish to set out on a career of being a cook. Let me tell you, ${RACE}, I find it admirable whenever I see folk like yourself trying your hand at such a noble craft.

'Granted, we hobbits are the finest cooks in all the land, but we are certainly not above teaching our craft to those willing to learn.

'Over by the oven there is Petunia Greenhand. She has offered to teach anyone new to cooking the very basics as part of her training to become a true expert at her craft.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'Well, look at you... I do not often see your folk here, and when I do, I always find it a bit queer. Well, hobbits less so because of the hill.

'Oh, I am sorry, you wish to know more of cooking? It just so happens that there is a fine cook near the oven by the name of Esilia Diggerly. She has offered to teach those new to the profession the basics of the art. Speak with her, and I am certain that she will help you.

'Good day, ${RACE}.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'You should speak with the novice trainer for your chosen profession.''You should speak with the novice trainer for your chosen profession.''You should speak with the novice trainer for your chosen profession.''You should speak with the novice trainer for your chosen profession.''Well look here, another would-be cook. I am pleased to meet you and looking forward to helping you get started.

'If I go too fast, or you need help at any point, you can ask me questions about cooking, and I will do my best to provide you with clear direction. The first and most important step is having the proper ingredients.

'I set aside a few for new cooks like yourself. Take this <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> and let us begin.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Cook vendors sell ingredients and recipes that are a vital part of any Cook's training and continued work.</rgb>'If you are looking for guidance in cooking, then I am prepared to offer you direction.

'If my methods are too fast, feel free to speak with me again, and I will answer any questions that you may have. I will do my best to provide you with clear direction. The first and most important step is having the proper ingredients.

'I have kept some of these ingredients aside for purpose of providing to new cooks. Take this <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> and let us begin.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Cook vendors sell ingredients and recipes that are a vital part of any Cook's training and continued work.</rgb>'Hullo, there! I hear that you are interested in learning the ways of a cook. If so, you have come to the right place.

'I will try not to move too quickly for you, but if I do, speak with me again to ask more pointed questions.

'I almost forgot the most important thing for every new cook -- ingredients. Everything you need to make hard biscuits is inside this <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb>.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Cook vendors sell ingredients and recipes that are a vital part of any Cook's training and continued work.</rgb>'Grab your <rgb=#FF00FF00>cooking tools</rgb> and make sure you have them equipped, then open the <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> of ingredients that I gave you and make your way to the oven.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Ingredients for Cooks are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the farming profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.</rgb>'To make the biscuits you will need to open the <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> of ingredients that I provided to you. Equip your <rgb=#FF00FF00>cooking tools</rgb> and head to the oven to begin cooking.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Ingredients for Cooks are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the farming profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.</rgb>'Just open up that <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> full of ingredients that I gave you, and you can start making the hard biscuit over by the oven. Make sure to equip your <rgb=#FF00FF00>cooking tools!</rgb>'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Ingredients for Cooks are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the farming profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.</rgb>'Making the flour should be simple. Grind down the barley and sift it a few times to filter out the impurities, and it should be ready for baking.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI.

Select the cooking tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe.

