Remember: in order to execute a recipe, you must be near the proper facility. Cooking typically requires an oven or camp-fire.</rgb>Using the ingredients you have obtained, cook a <rgb=#FF00FF00>hard biscuit</rgb> at an <rgb=#FF00FF00>oven</rgb>The recipe is complete. <rgb=#FF00FF00>Do not eat or sell the hard biscuit!</rgb> It is time to show your handiwork to the Novice Cook.'If you wish to know more of cooking, you should find Culhuc by the oven. He is one of the more experienced cooks in Lhan Garan despite his youth, and is teaching the craft to all who show interest.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'Go speak with the Novice Cook in Lhan Garan.''You wish to master the art of cooking? Then you and I share something in common. I was but an apprentice when I left Brundir. A promising one! But an apprentice nonetheless. I'll teach you what I know, and we can grow and learn together.

'Here, take this <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb>. It has everything you need to make a simple hard biscuit.

'Open that up, and you can use the <rgb=#FF00FF00>oven</rgb> to make the hard biscuit recipe. Make sure to equip your <rgb=#FF00FF00>cooking tools!</rgb>'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Cook vendors sell ingredients and recipes that are a vital part of any Cook's training and continued work.</rgb>'Open up that <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> full of ingredients that I gave you, and you can use the <rgb=#FF00FF00>oven</rgb> to make the hard biscuit recipe. Make sure to equip your <rgb=#FF00FF00>cooking tools!</rgb>'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Ingredients for Cooks are normally purchased from vendors or traded from players with the farming profession. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.</rgb>'Making flour is a simple process, if not a labour-intensive one. Mill the barley and sift it, running any pieces that are too big back through the mill until it is a mostly uniform consistency.'

