The supplier provided you with a <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> full of ingredients that you can use to execute the prospector recipe. Open the <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> to get the ingredients.The Chief Supplier provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a <rgb=#FF00FF00>copper ingot</rgb>.

<rgb=#FF00FF00>To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI.

Select the Prospecting tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe.

Remember: in order to execute a recipe you must be near the proper facility. Prospecting requires a forge.</rgb>Using the ingredients you received, craft a <rgb=#FF00FF00>copper ingot</rgb> at a <rgb=#FF00FF00>forge</rgb>The recipe is complete. <rgb=#FF00FF00>Do not sell the copper ingot!</rgb> It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the chief supplier.'If you wish to know more of prospecting, speak with the chief supplier here in Lhan Garan.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'You should speak with the chief supplier at once.''So you'd like to learn about prospecting? It can be a lucrative profession if you're willing to put in the effort.

'I'll walk you through the basics. If at any point you get confused, speak to me and I'll explain things again.

'I almost forgot the most important thing for every new prospector -- ingredients. Everything you need is inside this <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb>.

'Open it up, ensure your <rgb=#FF00FF00>prospector's pickaxe</rgb> is equipped, then make your way to the <rgb=#FF00FF00>forge</rgb>.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Suppliers provide the secondary ingredients necessary for Prospectors to refine the materials that they collect. As this is a collection profession there are no additional recipes to purchase as all are learned as you advance.</rgb>'First, ensure your <rgb=#FF00FF00>prospector's pickaxe</rgb> is equipped, then open the <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> of ingredients that I gave you and make your way to the <rgb=#FF00FF00>forge</rgb>.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Ingredients for prospectors are found in chests, gathered from ore-nodes, and purchased from suppliers. You can also find ingredients in the Auction Hall.</rgb>'Good work, so far. Get your hands back to work and refine that <rgb=#FF00FF00>copper ingot</rgb>.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>To open your crafting panel, you can use the 'T' key or click on the crafting button (it looks like a hammer and anvil) in the lower left part of your UI.

Select the Prospecting tab in the craft UI and find the proper recipe.

Remember: in order to execute a recipe you must be near the proper facility. Prospecting requires a forge.</rgb>'Let me see what you have done.'

She examines the item closely.

'The copper ingot appears to have been refined without a hint of impurity.

'Well done. Weaponsmiths and armoursmiths would be happy to forge something from work as good as this. You have the makings of a fine prospector.'Scholars study the ancient and not-so-ancient past to divine the secrets that were kept there. They can craft many wondrous treasures by learning of the past that can result in potions, oils, and scrolls which can enhance you and your fellows.

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Be careful! You will need to complete the correct recipes and deliver the correct items outlined in this quest.

You will need to execute the minor scholar lore recipe and deliver the minor scholar lore scroll. Failing to do so will force you to obtain new raw materials or to restart the quest after a 24-hour delay.</rgb>You should speak with the novice scholar to learn more about scholarship.The novice scholar provided you with a <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> full of ingredients that you can use to execute the scroll of minor scholar lore recipe. Open the <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> to get the ingredients.

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Ingredients for Scholars are normally purchased from vendors found near ruins, inside chests, or sometimes upon sentient enemies. You can also find ingredients on the Auction Hall.</rgb>The novice scholar provided you with the ingredients necessary to create a scroll of minor scholar lore.Using the ingredients you received, craft a <rgb=#FF00FF00>scroll of minor scholar lore</rgb>The recipe is complete. <rgb=#FF00FF00>Do not sell the scroll of minor scholar lore!</rgb> It is time to show your handiwork to your mentor, the novice scholar.'It looks as though you have strayed a little ways from home, ${RACE}, and you want to learn about scholarship?

'It seems, then, that you have come to the right place.

'You want to speak with Makan here in the Craft Hall. He will be able to set you upon the path of scholarship.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'You are far from home, ${RACE}. We will honour your request and help you as you learn the art of scholarship.

'Thavroniel, here in the Crafting Terrace, is an apprentice in the profession of scholarship. If you are looking for guidance, I am certain that she will be willing to assist you with the fundamentals of the craft.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'You will find Hildibras Took near the workbench here in the Crafting Area.

'He is knowledgeable in the art of scholarship and is awaiting the arrival of new would-be scholars.

'Speak with him if you are interested in learning and practicing the scholarship profession.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'Well, look at you. I do not often see your folk here, and when I do, I always find it a bit queer. Well, hobbits less so because of the hill.

'Oh, I am sorry, you wish to know more of scholarship? It just so happens that there is a fine scholar in this very hall, still learning, but taking to the art very quickly. Her name is Anna Bullrush, and you will find her by the workbench in the larger room.

'Good day, ${RACE}.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You must make sure to have room in your inventory for this quest.</rgb>'You should speak with the scholar trainer at once!''You should speak with the scholar trainer at once!''You should speak with the scholar trainer at once!''You should speak with the scholar trainer at once!''Well, look here... another would-be scholar. I am pleased to meet you and looking forward to helping you get started.

'If I go too fast or you need help at any point, you can ask me questions about scholarship, and I will do my best to provide you with clear direction. The first and most important step is having the proper ingredients.

'I set aside a few for new scholars like yourself. Take this <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> and let us begin.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Scholar vendors sell ingredients and recipes that are a vital part of any Scholar's training and continued work.</rgb>'If you are looking for guidance in scholarship, then I am prepared to offer you direction.

'If my methods are too fast, feel free to speak to me again, and I will answer any questions that you may have. I will do my best to provide you with clear direction. The first and most important step is having the proper ingredients.

'I have kept some of these ingredients aside for purpose of providing to new scholars. Take this <rgb=#FF00FF00>crate</rgb> and let us begin.'

<rgb=#FF00FF00>Scholar vendors sell ingredients and recipes that are a vital part of any Scholar's training and continued work.</rgb>'Hullo, there. I hear that you are interested in learning the ways of scholar. If so, you have come to the right place.

