'Please, take up your carving tools and help us supply all that is demanded.''Most excellent. These bows will be put to good use by guards all around Umbar.'Talk to Ransroth to gain rep.Speak with Ransroth'Speak with me to gain rep with the Eglain.''"Acquaintance" with the Eglain with a side of wasabi, coming right up!'Talk to Ransroth to gain rep.Speak with Ransroth'Speak with me to gain rep with the Eglain.''"Friend" with the Eglain with a side of wasabi, coming right up!'Talk to Ransroth to gain rep.Speak with Ransroth'Speak with me to gain rep with the Eglain.''"Ally" with the Eglain with a side of wasabi, coming right up!'Talk to Ransroth to gain rep.Speak with Ransroth'Speak with me to gain rep with the Eglain.''"Kindred" with the Eglain with a side of wasabi, coming right up!'Explore the Lone-lands and locate Chicken Stones.Enter session play.Enter session play.Explore The Lone-lands and locate Chicken Stones.Discover the Weathertop Chicken StoneDiscover the Last Bridge Chicken StoneDiscover The Forsaken Inn Chicken StoneSpeak with the creatures of the Lone-lands.Enter session play as a chicken.Enter session playTravel to the Lone-lands and speak with Radagast the Brown.Speak with Radagast the Brown'Alas, friend rooster, you have made a dire choice. The wide world is no place for one such as yourself. You should return to your coop.'Skalli has repeatedly tried to guess the race winners and sadly has not had a great deal of luck. He has lost more than his guesses, however; due to many tantrums, he has lost all of his belongings as well.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Skalli's items have been flung all over the race area. You should consult the note he gave you for hints as to where the missing belongings might be.

You should collect all of Skalli's missing items and return them to him.Find Skalli's shieldFind Skalli's spearFind Skalli's mugFind Skalli's mining pickFind Skalli's lucky jewelSkalli can be found at the Summer Festival Keg Race, likely still kicking the same waggon and cursing his luck (and festivals).

You should bring Skalli his found belongings and attempt to cheer him up.'I'm so angry I could shout!'

The dwarf kicks vigourously at a nearby waggon.

'I keep playing the races. Every time I select the dwarf I think should win, and every time -- without fail -- that dwarf LOSES! What sort of terrible idea for a festival was this? I HATE FESTIVALS!

'To make matters worse, every time I lose, I fly into a blind rage and seem to throw something off into the distance. While it feels wonderful, I often realize that the item I flung was my own. Will you please help me find my missing goods? Here is a brief detail of how I spent my day thus far.''What? I gave you a list! What more do you want?''My things! Spear, shield, mug... everything! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Now I can get back to my sulking without needing to worry about my missing goods.'Percy Bywood has lost the invitations he intended to send out to inform everyone of the anniversary festival.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>The envelopes are scattered around Bree.

Percy Bywood has asked you to look inside envelopes scattered around town return to him any invitations you find.Open envelopes you find to collect invitations (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Percy Bywood is near the Boar-fountain in Bree.

You should return the invitations you found to Percy Bywood.'Hail, friend. Might I ask a favour of you?

'I was put in charge of sending out invitations to the residents of Bree, to let them know of the festival events underway. Maybe you received one yourself? Well, I was about to send out another stack of envelopes when a strong wind came along and blew them all away! Can you collect the invitations around town for me?''Look around Bree for envelopes that have blown away. They couldn't have gone far....''Thank you for the invitations, ${PLAYER}.

'That was nearly a disaster, but now we can get the word out about the festival!'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Galadhrim.'Would you like some rep with the Galadhrim?''Alright, soon the Galadhrim will consider you an Acquaintance. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Galadhrim.'Would you like some rep with the Galadhrim?''Alright, soon you will be a Friend of the Galadhrim. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Galadhrim.'Would you like some rep with the Galadhrim?''Alright, soon you will be an Ally of the Galadhrim. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred of the Galadhrim.'Would you like some rep with the Galadhrim?''Alright, soon you will be Kindred of the Galadhrim. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will receive a Lothlórien barter currency allowance.'Get barter currency for Lothlórien!''Ride back here like a bunny if you need more!'A romance stricken young man needs help impressing his poetry-loving lady friend.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Wayward verses can be found around the Houses of Lore in Minas Tirith.

You should collect wayward verses for the hopeful poet.Catch wayward verses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Colladan is located in the Houses of Lore in Minas Tirith.

Bring the wayward verses to Colladan.'What? Sleep overtook me again?! Oh, hello. I wonder if you’ve seen… well, this is rather embarrassing. I have been collecting bits of poetry and romantic verse… for, uhm, inspiration. Yes, that’s it. I need a poem to read for a performance at which my beloved… well, my eventual beloved, Lírveril, will be present. She loves poetry and attends the annual show here in Minas Tirith every year.

'I collected some of the best verses from the old masters of the craft, and was in the process of organizing them into the best love poem that has ever existed! Or, I had been, that is. You see, I seem to have dozed off, during which time some dotard opened a nearby window!

'All my hours of hard work, my years of longing, my very careful copying of the very best love poems - ah, that is, gathering inspiration. All of it! Ruined by one nap! Say, have you a few moments to help me find those pages, friend? I could make it worth your while! How far could they have even gotten? I was asleep a mere… well, best to get started!

'Oh, my thanks, my thanks! I will look around the desk here if you will search the rest of the library.''It's a bit stuffy in here, do you not agree?'

The young woman looks up towards where Colladan is with a smirk, then returns to reading her book.'Were you able to find the verses? Ah, thank you, thank you! I must get back to compiling, er, writing the words with which I will win Lírveril's love!'The love-sick Avery Crabapple has fallen for a woman whom he has been admiring from afar around Bree-town.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Marigolds can be found near the stone circle outside Michel Delving, violets near the stone circle beyond the Bree West-gate, and primroses near the stone circle above Celondim.

Realizing that he cannot muster the courage to speak to the lady of his affections face-to-face, Avery Crabapple has requested help from you to gather a combination of flowers from all corners of Eriador.'Greetings, friend! I was wondering if you could help me, as I am in a precarious position. I have found that my affections for a particular woman have grown into something I can no longer ignore. She is the beautious flower amongst the weeds. She walks in my dreams and the sound of her voice is a melodious tone that bards could sing about for the ages. Of course, there is a slight bump in the road. I have not actually spoken to her. I simply cannot muster the courage to approach the lovely woman, as I have only watched her from afar walking around town. What would I say? I fear I would only make a terrible first impression.

'This is where my request comes in, for I have a brilliant plan to woo the woman of my dreams. Please, would you go and collect three types of flowers from all over Eriador... only the best for my sweet lady. Bring them back to me, and I will create the most beautiful bouquet a lady could want. I only need three varieties of flower for the bouquet. I will need a Marigold, a Violet, and a Primrose.

'Marigolds can be found near the stone circle outside Michel Delving, violets near the stone circle beyond the Bree West-gate, and primroses near the stone-circle outside Celondim in the Blue Mountains. Take care and return as quickly as you can!''Excellent! You have managed to find the perfect blooms to help make the perfect bouquet for my sweet lady. You have a wonderful eye for flowers!

'I truly appreciate all your help in finding these rare flowers. I will go ahead and create a beautiful bouquet worthy of the woman of my dreams. I am confident that this is the way to her heart!'You have earned the Loyal Servant of Sauron title.Perched high in the hills overlooking Imladris, the Elves of Rivendell welcome all seeking home and hearth to settle among the blazing leaves and babbling waters of the Trollshaws.The entrance to homestead glens of Imladris can be found south of the stables of Rivendell. Hirthamel has suggested you explore the hills and hollows, and perhaps consider residing there yourself.Visit the entrance to the neighbourhoodVisit the dell commonsVisit a Simple CottageVisit a VillaVisit a Grand VillaFind a good view of the ValleyFind a view of the TrollshawsYou should return to Hirthamel to share what you have seenReturn to Hirthamel'Mae-govannen, friend. I hail from the humble glen of Imladris. I'm sure you've journeyed far and your feet are no doubt tired. I would beg you find a seat and succour in the Vale - though perhaps you are not so tired yet that you might take in the sights of our fair dell first.

'I know the Men of Bree thrive in the bustle of dense markets and close-knit buildings nearly atop each other. I find that I myself prefer a more tranquil place to call home - which is why I find this valley so appealing. Though in fairness, it is the only place I've called home. Perhaps you are of a kindred heart?''Hello, my friend! I trust that our fine vale was a pleasant walk for you. There is room space a plenty, if you are as enamoured of it as I.

'You'll find no finer place to set your hearth, hang your hat, and enjoy the sunrise and sunset with a hearty draught of your choice.'A group of mischevious young hobbits organizes a yearly secret raid of Farmer Maggot's fields, seeking to snatch wild mushrooms that grow among the grain -- and each year Farmer Maggot sets his dogs loose in the field to chase them off -- can you prove your worth as a mushroom-hunter?Earn victories in Maggot's Mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A group of mischevious young hobbits organizes a yearly secret raid of Farmer Maggot's fields, seeking to snatch wild mushrooms that grow among the grain...and each year Farmer Maggot sets his dogs loose in the field to chase them off. Can you prove your worth as a veteran mushroom-hunter?Earn victories in Maggot's Mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Taunting an opponent can cause them to act irrationally. Use this to your advantage.Use the skills:
