You should return to Gareth Rust and find out if he saw your excellent firework display.'Back again? Maybe I spoke unjustly the first time we met. Mayor Goodnough's wish to please folk like you is the reason folk like me go hungry this winter. But you don't seem like a bad sort, despite the Mayor seeming to like you.

'If you want to earn yet more favour with me and my fellows here, you surely won't object to playing a little prank on the Mayor for the sport of the real townsfolk.

'The mayor has some fireworks stored near the festival area, and he's intent on saving them for just the right moment. If you set them off where they are, you'll ruin the show (at least for him.) While the patrons are distracted, you should pinch Frostbluff Coins from their pockets! I can think of better uses for those coins....''If you can pick the pockets of those silly distracted patrons, I'll have a great deal of respect for you, ${PLAYER}. Money is wasted on folk like them!''That was quite a display, ${PLAYER}! And judging from how close they were, I'll warrant you sent the mayor into a fit and disrupted things rather nicely!

'Well done, well done. Here, you should keep half of what you managed to collect. These coins here will be enough to spread out among my friends so that they won't go hungry tonight!'The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has requested your assistance in completing a series of missions on their behalf.Seek out and complete several missions to assist the Gabil'akkâ.Complete missions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Seek out and speak to Elóf regarding your completion of several missions.Speak to Elóf'We have need of your assistance in completing a series of missions for the on-going war effort.

'The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has been making headway towards Gundabad, but our troops are spread too thin to accomplish all that is needed to be done.

'Seek out and complete several of these missions to assist our efforts.''We wish to thank you for your hard work towards the war effort. Your good deeds shall help secure our foothold into Gundabad itself!'Your ability to write between the lines confounds your foes.Use any Words of Grace skillsYour ability to write between the lines confounds your foes.Use any Words of Grace skillsAchieve 130th level playing through as a Warden on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Warden.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a WardenAchieve 130th level playing through as a Captain on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Captain.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a CaptainOf the magicks that can be wielded by Man or Elf, the hearts of beasts are among the most closely tied to the visible world, and so there are many who strive to master them.Use Sign of the Wild: ProtectionOf the magicks that can be wielded by Man or Elf, the hearts of beasts are among the most closely tied to the visible world, and so there are many who strive to master them.Summon a companion.Achieve 130th level playing through as a Champion on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Champion.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a ChampionAchieve 130th level playing through as a Hunter on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Hunter.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a HunterAchieve 130th level playing through as a Beorning on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Beorning.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a BeorningAchieve 130th level playing through as a Brawler on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Brawler.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a BrawlerAchieve 130th level playing through as a Rune-keeper on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Rune-keeper.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Rune-keeperAchieve 130th level playing through as a Lore-master on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Lore-master.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Lore-masterAchieve 130th level playing through as a Burglar on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Burglar.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a BurglarAchieve 130th level playing through as a Guardian on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Guardian.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a GuardianAchieve 130th level playing through as a Minstrel on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Minstrel.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a MinstrelAchieve 130th level playing through as a Mariner on Fearless difficulty.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a Mariner.Achieve 130th level playing through on Fearless difficulty or higher as a MarinerEven a lore-master will occasionally find himself face-to-face with the enemy. At times like these, a sturdy oaken staff may take on a simpler and most vital role.Use Staff-strike against your foesEven a lore-master will occasionally find himself face-to-face with the enemy. At times like these, a sturdy oaken staff may take on a simpler and most vital role.Use Staff-strike against your foesThe rural foothills of Rohan are in need of pioneers and tree-friends. Seleflad has suggested you might take the opportunity to purchase your own home in Rohan.Seleflad can be found at Edoras or the Eastfold Homesteads.

You should talk to Seleflad.Talk to Seleflad'Good ${RACE}, you seem a well-travelled one, I dare say! You have just moved into the Homesteads of the Eastfold, have you not? If you are looking for a home with a slow pace to life, you have come to the right place. Still, we pride ourselves on keeping the neighbourhood both clean and friendly. I hope that you will join us in building a brighter community, my friend!''Good, good! I have many things that need doing. If we all pitch in, they will be done in no time at all!'The majestic plains of Rohan are in need of farmers and horse-friends. Burginda has suggested you might take the opportunity to purchase your own home in Rohan.Burginda can be found at Edoras or the Kingstead Households.

You should talk to Burginda.Talk to Burginda'Good ${RACE}, you seem a well-travelled one, I dare say! You have just moved into the Households of the Kingstead, have you not? If you are looking for a home with a slow pace to life, you have come to the right place. Still, we pride ourselves on keeping the neighbourhood both clean and friendly. I hope that you will join us building a brighter community, my friend!''Good, good! I have many things that need doing. If we all pitch in, they will be done in no time at all!'By completing this quest, you will receive a Minas Tirith endgame allowance.'Do you want to win the Minas Tirith endgame in now time? I sure hope so, since you wanted me to talk more about this!''Ride back here like a bunny if you need more!'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Malledhrim.'Would you like to level up with the Malledhrim?''Alright, soon the Malledhrim will consider you an Acquaintance. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Malledhrim.'Would you like to level up with the Malledhrim?''Alright, soon you will be a Friend of the Malledhrim. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Malledhrim.'Would you like to level up with the Malledhrim?''Alright, soon you will be an Ally of the Malledhrim. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred to the Malledhrim.'Would you like to level up with the Malledhrim?''Alright, soon you will be Kindred to the Malledhrim. Ready?'Saelthaliel found that she was missing several of her friends when she came out of the maze. She has been waiting patiently for them for several days now, but there is no sign that they will come out any time soon.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Saelthaliel's Elf-friends can probably be found wandering throughout the maze. The maze is in the Horse-fields of Bree, north of Bree-town.

You should speak to each Elf and encourage them to move a little faster towards getting to the exit of the maze.Saelthaliel is standing just outside the entrance to the hedge maze, waiting for word of her friends.

You should tell Saelthaliel of all that passed inside the maze.Talk to Saelthaliel outside the maze in the Horse-fields'I am glad you have come. I could use some assistance, if you please. You might wonder why I am standing all alone at a festive springtime event, but I am actually waiting for my friends. I have been waiting for some days now.

'We all entered the maze together, as a group, but sometime during the course of things we became separated, and only I came out. I have been waiting for them all these days since!

'Do you think you could go into the maze and remind them that we must soon be away back to our own Ethuilwereth celebration? I would go in again, but I am afraid that I will miss them once again, and we could be here even longer if they go back to look for me! I am beginning to regret our decision to come here....''We Elves do not notice the turning of the days. Saelthaliel's concern is unfounded; I am not lost, but enjoying the fresh foliage.

'I suppose it matters not. I will leave now. Where is the exit? I do not ask because I do not know. I just want to make sure that you know how to get out.''Saelthaliel is too hasty. But I suppose she is correct; I will come. I will...follow you for a while, if you don't mind.''Are you lost? I can see that you are. You needn't be ashamed. Just follow my path, and I will lead us both back to Saelthaliel in time.''The door? Oh, I am sure I must have passed it a hundred times and paid it no heed. I could find it again in a moment if I so desired.

'I stay only because I worry if you can get out yourself. I will watch which direction you go, to make sure you go the right way....''Saelthaliel is waiting? I had almost forgotten her. I find this maze most inhabitable. I am not sure I have a mind to leave just yet.

'Pray tell, though -- where is the door? I ask merely out of curiosity, should I ever want to find it. I am not sure that time will come, but just the same...it will be good to know it is there.''I am sorry, my mind was elsewhere. I have been looking for the exit for days! I have never been good at this sort of thing -- every leaf is distracting. Will you lead me out?''You spoke to all of them, and yet still they tarry! I do not know how I will ever get them out. I am beginning to think that bringing them along was not the most prudent idea....'Calendui of Duillond wishes to hear an account of Bree's Spring Planting event, but his fellows who travelled there have not yet returned. He wishes to receive word from Saelthaliel, the leader of the company, that all is well in Bree-land.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Saelthaliel and the Elves with her should be at the Festival Grounds in Bree, in the Horse-fields to the north of Bree-town.

Calendui has asked you to speak with Saelthaliel to remind her not to tarry too long at Bree's Spring Planting, lest she miss the Ethuilwereth celebration altogether.Talk to Saelthaliel at the Horse-fields in Bree'Mae govannen, traveller. Welcome to the celebration of Ethuilwereth in Duillond. I hope you will enjoy the wonders that the spring season has to offer before you, too, wander off to the Spring Planting in Bree-land. The hedge maze there is drawing many of my kindred thither.

'A company of Elves, led by clear-headed Saelthaliel, went to the Spring Planting many days ago to observe the green walls on the Horse-fields. I have not heard from them since, and I truly did not expect that they would be away so long.

'If you find yourself at the festival grounds in Bree, please look for Saelthaliel or any of her company. Remind her that Ethuilwereth will not go on forever, and that she and her company should hasten back if they wish to enjoy it before it has passed away until the next turn of the seasons.''Saelthaliel can hopefully be found at the Hedge Maze in Bree's Horsefields. I hope no harm has come to her.''I am not at all surprised that Calendui has sent you to me. Our stay has been overlong indeed, but perhaps you will be able to help me.'The dwarf Gísi was supposed to be back from the Spring Planting in Bree several days ago, and Mákr desires to find out what has become of him.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Gísi is at the Festival Grounds in Bree, near the hedge-maze on the Horse-fields.

You should bring Mákr's message to Gísi before the festival days come to a close for the season.Talk to Gísi at the Horse-fields in Bree'Are you enjoying the Springfest? It is a fine time of year! But my friend Gísi, who loves this festival most, is nowhere to be found. He travelled to the Spring Planting of Bree many days ago to try his luck in the hedge-maze there, but I've heard not a word from him since.

'If you go to the maze, could you look for him? I know that he would not wish to miss the festival of the dwarves. I am worried that some strange fate has befallen him.

'Just...try not to get lost among the greens yourself before you speak to Gísi.''You should go to Bree, traveller! You will find the Hedge Maze in the Horse-fields.''The Springfest! Goodness -- do you know I had nearly forgotten all about it? Because -- pardon me, my eyes; they will not stop tearing for all the laughing I do these days! Oh, if only you could see! The mirth! I may not go back for many days yet.'You have been tasked with repelling a pack of worms encroaching on Kidzul-kâlah.Your mission is to repel a pack of worms encroaching on Kidzul-kâlah.

You should talk to Ausma and travel to Kidzul-kâlah.Complete 'Mission: A Chill on the Gladdenmere'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Ausma for your reward.Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have reported a recent rise in the population of worms in the hills to the east of Kidzul-kâlah. It seems they have grown more bold as of late and have made several attempts to breach the walls of the old fortress. I do not know if they mean to nest in Kidzul-kâlah, but the Longbeards will not abide another work of dwarves stolen by dragon-kind!

'You are to travel to Kidzul-kâlah and thin the numbers of these encroaching worms. For the Gabil'akkâ!'Nestled in the foothills of the Misty Mountains, the dwarf-keep of Kidzul-kâlah lies half-sunken in the Gladdenmere. Meanwhile, a pack of worms has encroached on the old dwarf-keep….

Your mission is to repel a pack of worms encroaching on Kidzul-kâlah.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'A single worm is little trouble, but if that pack had made its way into Kidzul-kâlah, I fear it would not be long before the Goldencleft was overrun with dragon-kind. We shall have to remain vigilant!'Your mission is to go to Jâr Obadal, set alight the spiders' webs and cull their number.Your mission is to travel to Jâr Obadal and set alight the spiders' webbed burrows and cull their number.

Speak to Jôrlar to travel.Complete Mission: A Cleansing FireYou have defeated the spiders and destroyed their nests. Return with the scout to Jôrlar in Zajâna with this report.Speak with Jôrlar in Zajâna'It is not Men alone that threaten Kighân. The spiders to the east snatch and claw at passersby, harassing the many caravans set along the Great Road. They and their dread brood-mother - the one we call Jûkhtar the Ravenous. The spiders have set up their vile lair in Jâr Obadal, in the dusty caves east of Zajâna.

'Please, go there and set fire to their network of webs, and cull their number - so that travellers can again feel safe both on the road to Zajâna and throughout Kighân.''Your mission is clear, ${PLAYER}. Defeat the spiders and set their burrows ablaze.''You are a miracle worker! I can scarcely believe that you defeated Jûkhtar and ended the threat of her brood. We shall make a ballad of your deeds this night!'You have been tasked with taking the fight to Ghasaphâr and his Corsairs. Root them out of Kan Skûrja on the Cape of Umbar.Your mission is to take the fight to Ghasaphâr and his Corsairs. Root them out of their settlement in Kan Skûrja on the Cape of Umbar.

Speak to Malthak to travel.Complete Mission: A Cut AboveYou have successfully defeated Ghasaphâr and the Corsairs! Return to the mission giver.'Well met again, ${PLAYER}. We have need for some assistance for our merchant ships. They are being attacked by Corsairs while delivering food and supplies to our settlements on the Cape of Umbar. We believe these attacks are coordinated by a Corsair captain, Ghasaphâr, who makes his camp in Kan Skûrja on the Cape of Umbar. Please, go there and root out these Corsairs, so that our merchant vessels can once again pass safely into and out of the Cape. Defeat Ghasaphâr and the scoundrels who follow him.''Your objective is clear, ${PLAYER}. Root out Ghasaphâr and his Corsair crew. Put a stop to their pillaging of innocent Umbari merchant ships and the loss of innocent Umbari lives.''I am glad Ghasaphâr will no longer run rampant. All the hands on our merchant fleet will sleep easier tonight because of you. Thank you for all you've done.'You have been tasked with obtaining a great treasure cache in Bakhjâd in the Shield Isles before anyone else.Your mission is to travel to Bakhjâd and obtain a great stolen treasure cache by whatever means necessary.

Speak to Deshra to travel.Complete Mission: A Dark TreasureYou have successfully defeated the Corsairs and the Dead and recovered the cache! Return to the mission giver with this report.'Always a pleasure, ${PLAYER}. We just got some exciting information. We have a credible report as to the location of a cache of riches stolen by freebooters from one of our merchant ships. Unfortunately, this report points us to Bakhjâd, in the Shield Isles. It's quite a dangerous place to go, but we could really use that stolen coin to help us rebuild Umbar. Will you help us recover it, for the good of Umbar?''Your objective is clear, ${PLAYER}, recover that treasure cache at all cost. Don't let anyone or anything get in the way of that.''I am touched beyond words. This will do much to repair the wounds and scars carved into our city. Thank you for your bravery, and your honesty in bringing this much coin to us.'You have been tasked with rescuing dwarf scouts from the clutches of the hobgoblins.Your mission is to find and free the captured scouts in Vorkodar.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Vorkodar.Complete Mission: A Frosty ReceptionThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'I received word that my scouts have located a den of hobgoblins deep in the mountains, but four of the scouts never returned. I suspect they have been captured. I need you to infiltrate Vorkodar and rescue them before they are executed, or worse!''Thank Drasa you arrived when you did! My scouts all arrived in one piece. Good work, ${PLAYER}.'Several scouts keeping watch on the hobgoblin's den failed to report back. They must be rescued before it is too late!

Your mission is to find and free the captured scouts in Vorkodar.Ulfar has learned that Olwir plans to capture a Stone-troll that stalks Rushock Bog and deliver it as a gift to the Dourhands in the north.You have been asked to enter Olwir's camp and foil his plans to capture a Stone-toll and deliver it to Skorgrím as a gift.Complete Mission: A Gift for the NorthYou have stopped Olwir's plans and defeated the Stone-troll. You should talk to Ulfar and then give your report to the Hooded Stranger.Talk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony'In the Shire village of Needlehole, a dwarf, Ulfar, has uncovered a plot to capture a Stone-troll and give it as a gift to the resurrected Skorgrím Dourhand in the north. Their plan must not be allowed to proceed. Fortunately, Ulfar has learned where Olwir and his dwarves are camping, north of Rushock Bog. Go there and stop Olwir from achieving his goal.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Are you ready to travel to Olwir's camp? We must foil his plans, and if he has captured a troll, it must be slain!''I hear the day has been saved! Well done. Skorgrím will have to do without a troll. Here is your well-deserved reward.'None have feasted on the remains of Scatha's larder with such fervour as a foul worm known to the dwarves as Stúrkvith the Bloated.Your mission is to defeat the gluttonous rock-worm, Stúrkvith the Bloated, who now dwells in Scatha's Larder.

You should talk to Ausma and travel to Scatha's Larder.Complete 'Mission: A Glutton in the Larder'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Ausma for your reward.Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have returned from Wyrmsgráf with troubling news. A worm of considerable size has taken refuge deep within Scatha's larder and has begun to feed on the unwary... even those of its own kind. The Longbeards have seen fit to call it Stúrkvith the Bloated, and I think it a name well-earned.

'You are to travel to Scatha's larder in Wyrmsgráf and see that Stúrkvith grows no larger! For the Gabil'akkâ!'Deep within Wyrmsgráf, there lies a great larder which once belonged to Scatha the Worm. Rumours have spread of a gluttonous rock-worm dwelling among the bones of Scatha's long-devoured prey.

Your mission is to defeat the gluttonous rock-worm, Stúrkvith the Bloated, who now dwells in Scatha's Larder.'Well done, ${PLAYER}.

'That gluttonous beast must have spent too many years accustomed to feasting on easier prey than you!'You have been tasked with thwarting a group of stone-giants within the rocky slopes of Câr Bronach.Your mission is to thwart a group of stone-giants within the rocky slopes of Câr Bronach.

Speak to Ausma to travel.Complete Mission: A Large ProblemThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from Câr Bronach. A group of stone-giants are causing problems upon the peaks of Gundabad! We must do what we can to stop these giants and send them on their way.

'If their caves are ruined and their food spoiled, then perhaps they will leave these mountains for good!''Maddened stone-giants take to their dwellings in the rocky slopes of Câr Bronach, and where they walk, only trouble will follow….

'Your mission is to thwart a group of stone-giants within the rocky slopes of Câr Bronach.''Well done! With those stone-giants defeated, Câr Bronach is once again safe. Perhaps it is time to for more dwarves to start scouting the slopes of Gundbad. Just as the city within, the whole mountain must be protected.'On a remote Shield Isle, a distinguished Umbari scholar lost his priceless research when he was attacked by large beetles. Recover the research and take the fight to these vile creatures.On the northern Shield Isle Ghax-hophra, a distinguished Umbari scholar lost his priceless research when he was attacked by large beetles. Your mission is to recover the research and destroy these creatures' nests.

Speak to Malthak to travel.Complete Mission: A Life's WorkYou have successfully recovered the research and defeated the Ghax-hophra brood! Return with the Umbari scout to Malthak with this report.Speak with Malthak'Always good to see you, ${PLAYER}. One of Umbar's most distinguished scholars just returned from a research trip to the Shield Isles. Unfortunately for him, it was not a productive trip. Far from it. Seems he was harried by great beetles on one of the northernmost Shield Isles, Ghax-hophra. He was so afraid he left his notebooks, which contain a lifetime of research into Umbari life and culture.

'For his sake and ours, we need to get those pages back. Will you venture out into the Shield Isles and retrieve his research? While you're there, destroy the nests of those vile creatures, that they may not harm others.''Your objective is clear, ${PLAYER}, recover the research at all costs. If you aren't able to return with that research, a great deal of Umbari culture could be lost forever.''Future generations will have you to thank for preserving our knowledge about our past. Thank you for your bravery in securing these tomes.'You have been tasked with stopping the Tarkrîp Orcs before they collapse the mines of Writhenset.Your mission is to stop the Tarkrîp Orcs before they collapse the mines of Writhenset.

Speak to Radhril.Complete Mission: A Looming CollapseThe mission is complete!

Speak to Radhril for your reward!Talk to Radhril'Would you accompany me on a mission, ${CLASS}?

'The Free Peoples in the Wildwood have reported a group of Tarkrîp Orcs who head to the mines of Writhenset with bombs and black powder in tow. It would seem these foes seek to collapse the mines.

'If the mines of Writhenset are to ever again be safe, this group of Orcs must be removed.'A group of Tarkrîp Orcs seeks to collapse the mines of Writhenset!

Your mission is to stop the Tarkrîp Orcs before they collapse the mines of Writhenset.'We have done well, ${CLASS}. With the mines of Writhenset once again secure, the Free Peoples will now be able to continue with their efforts beneath the Wildwood.'You have been tasked with searching for signs of a dwarf-presence in the snow-fields.Your mission is to find evidence of the dwarf expedition in the snow-fields.

Speak to Ausma to travel to the snow-fields.Complete Mission: A Lost ExpeditionThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'Oh good, you’re here, ${PLAYER}.

'It's been brought to my attention recently that we weren't the first dwarves to explore the frozen expanses around here. Apparently there was a dwarf expedition into the snow-fields for an unknown purpose many years ago. The dwarves that went on the expedition never returned, so whatever information they may have gleaned has been lost to the drifts of snow.

'I beseech you; could you follow in their footsteps and see if you can recover any of their belongings now frozen in ice? Any information may prove useful to our efforts. Just beware of the freezing cold out there.'There seem to be remnants of a lost expedition scattered throughout the snow-fields.

Your mission is to investigate these areas and retrieve any lost equipment.'Well done! This journal should provide insight as to what happened to the dwarves that were here before, and can help us prepare against the cold climate.'Address the huorn problem on the Cape by paring their number back.Your mission is to address the huorn problem on the Cape by paring their number back.

Speak to Deshra to travel.Complete Mission: A Natural DisasterYou have successfully defeated the huorn threat! Return to the mission giver with this report.'Well met again, ${PLAYER}. We have some troubling news from the Cape. A group of territorial huorns has been expanding there, destroying property and lives alike, both peasants and nobles on the road to Umbar. Please, take the fight to them and trim their branches back.''Your objective is clear, ${PLAYER}, pare back the huorn menace on the Cape. Too many innocents have already lost their lives from their pillaging attacks.''Thank you for addressing the threat. It warms my heart to know that our citizens can move along the Cape without fear. Thank you for your valiant deeds.'Within the ruined walls of Kêr Bréin, the cold-drakes of the Frost-horde have laid a new clutch of eggs.Your mission is to destroy cold-drake eggs at Kêr Bréin.

You should talk to Hórin and travel to Kêr Bréin.Complete 'Mission: A New Clutch'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have returned from Kêr Bréin. In addition to being used as a base of attack against our forces in Ered Mithrin, the cold-drakes of the Frost-horde have transformed Kêr Bréin into a crude nursery for a new clutch of their eggs. Unless these eggs are destroyed, we shall soon have to contend with an even greater threat... and greater numbers of dragon-kind!

'You are to travel to Kêr Bréin and destroy the eggs of the Frost-horde. For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!'Although it once served as a camp of the Ungoledain, Kêr Bréin has fallen to the Frost-horde. There, the cold-drakes of Ered Mithrin lay their eggs within its ruined walls.

Your mission is to destroy cold-drake eggs at Kêr Bréin.'It is done?

'Wonderful! If the Frost-horde cannot bolster their numbers, our victory is assured!'Goblins stole a rare wine from the vintner, Brethilwen, and are currently occupying Limael's Vineyard in Ered Luin.There are goblins throughout Limael's Vineyard and they have stolen a rare wine. You have been asked to recover the bottles that the goblins have not yet drunk or destroyed. There are also still some late-season grapes on the vines. Collecting enough of them would allow Brethilwen to vinify one more cask of wine.Complete Mission: A Rare VintageYou have recovered as much of the rare wine as you were able and even collected enough grapes for Brethilwen to make one more cask of wine this season.Talk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony'Goblins despoil Limael's Vineyard, and recently a party of the wretched creatures broke into an old wine-cellar and stole a number of flasks of a rare and ancient vintage. No doubt the evil creatures have already drunk or destroyed most of the wine, but if you can recover any of the bottles from the goblins in this area, Master-vintner Brethilwen would be in your debt.

'Brethilwen also tells me this was a very generous season and many of the vines are still laden with grapes. Were you to gather the grapes from the vines that are still hale and hearty enough, Brethilwen will see to it that one more cask is filled with the finest of wines.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'If you are ready, there is no time to lose. The goblins are likely drinking all the good wine as we speak!''Excellent job, saving the wine. Your reward is well deserved. Cheers!'Intended to feed the war effort for as long as necessary in Elderslade, a massive cache of Orkish provisions has been found in Bekâr-zarakh.Your mission is to destroy the cache of Orkish provisions stored in Bekâr-zarakh.

You should talk to Hórin and travel to Bekâr-zarakh.Complete 'Mission: A Taste For Battle'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have just returned from Bekâr-zarakh with news that the Orcs have begun to store a great supply of provisions within the tower's walls. With the skirmishes in Elderslade growing more frequent, many of the Orcs who muster in Bekâr-zarakh have been sent to battle. Our warriors face them in the field, but that allows us a rare opportunity to strike within Gorgar's defences.

'You are to travel to Bekâr-zarakh and destroy the Orcs' provisions at once. Hunger alone will not slay these Orcs, but it will make it all the easier for our axes! For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!'High in the tower of Bekar-zarakh, the Orcs of Gundabad prepare for war. Stored there to feed the war effort, many Orkish provisions have been left poorly-guarded….

Your mission is to destroy the cache of Orkish provisions stored in Bekâr-zarakh.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'Without so much foul food to stuff themselves with, the Orcs of Gundabad shall prove little challenge to defeat on the battlefield.'Your mission is to aid in harvesting crabs in Zamarzîr and to fight off any crabs or beasts that get in your way.Your mission is to aid in harvesting crabs in Zamarzîr and to fight off any crabs or beasts that get in your way.

Speak to Malthak to travel.Complete Mission: A Taste for CrabYou have successfully harvested the crabs and defeated the greater cast-mother! Return with the Umbari scout to the mission giver with this report.'Well met again, ${PLAYER}. There is a new chef in Umbar, and he has been entertaining all of Umbar with his delicious crab creations. Now Umbar is running low on crab-meat! This may not seem like an emergency, but I can assure you it is. There are bountiful supplies of crabs on Zamarzîr in the Shield Isles, but large ferocious crabs have been sabotaging our traps and fighting off the workers. Please, aid the harvest on Zamarzîr in the Shield Isles.''Your mission is clear, ${PLAYER}, to aid in harvesting the crabs in Zamarzîr and to fight off any crabs or beasts that get in your way.''Thank you for this. It may seem silly, but it's the little things that keep us going, our hearts strong and our will determined...

'And I just love crab.'Your mission is to infiltrate the Halls of Lajór and retrieve a book titled "The Farings of Kábuzar", separated into two volumes. This tome is of great historical significance to the Zajâni, but has been stolen by the Jewelled Council.Your mission is to travel to the Halls of Lajór in Zajâna and retrieve a stolen book of great historical significance, "The Farings of Kábuzar."

Speak to Jôrlar to travel.Complete Mission: A Treasure in BlueYou have retrieved the book, "The Farings of Kábuzar." Return with the scout to Jôrlar in Zajâna with this report.Speak with Jôrlar in Zajâna'We have a problem, outsider. The Pohâni, our learned class of scholars and sages, have just informed me that one of our oldest and most important texts, "The Farings of Kábuzar," has been stolen.

'The Jewelled Council raided the Kalmakhíla last night, and stole many books. They have burned them in the past, seeing these stored learnings as sacrilegious and profane. We cannot allow this text to be burned.

'Will you go to the Halls of Lajór and retrieve this book before the Jewelled Council has a chance to figure out what they have in their possession and destroy it?''This book is truly irreplaceable. Do whatever you must to ensure the Jewelled Council does not destroy it.''You have it? Praise be. The Pohâni were beside themselves this morning when they thought it lost forever. You have my gratitude - and theirs - for returning this, my friend.'You have been tasked with collecting the abandoned supplies scattered throughout Stramvárth.Your mission is to collect the abandoned supplies scattered throughout Stramvárth.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Stramvárth.Complete Mission: Abandoned SuppliesThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts were passing by the abandoned ruins of Stramvárth in the Floodfells, where they noticed some supplies, just left there! We should return at once and gather any of the supplies that have yet to spoil.'Within the old ruins of Stramvárth lie abandoned supplies from various Orcs and goblins who have camped there….

Your mission is to collect the abandoned supplies scattered throughout Stramvárth.'Well done! With these supplies, the war effort will continue! It is important to keep everyone fed and healthy in our quest to reclaim Gundabad.'You have been tasked with defending the bridge builders of the Hadhodiant from a potential ambush.Your mission is to defend the bridge builders of the Hadhodiant.

Speak to Ausma to travel to the Hadhodiant.Complete Mission: Aiding the Bridge BuildersThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'We are in the midst of repairing the Hadhodiant in the Vales of Anduin. Our Beorning allies have sent word that a band of drakes heads south towards the bridge!

'We must protect the bridge builders and the work they have accomplished on the Hadhodiant!'An ambush could threathen the bridge builders, who work to repair to the Hadhodiant….

Your mission is to defend the bridge builders of the Hadhodiant.'Well done! I thank you for halting the attack and saving the bridge builders! Now we will finish repairing the Hadhodiant so that trade and movement will be swifter between the Vales of Anduin and the Misty Mountains!'At the behest of King Thorin Stonehelm, the Kharum-ubnâr have enlisted the aid of skilled adventurers to secure distant dwarf-holds and ensure the success of Prince Durin and the Gabil'akkâ in the forthcoming reclamation of Mount Gundabad.Vorthur Smokebreath can be found at Akrâz-zahar, in Erebor.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath and complete missions for the Kharum-ubnâr.Complete missions for the Kharum-ubnâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Vorthur Smokebreath can be found at Akrâz-zahar, in Erebor.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath.Talk to Vorthur Smokebreath'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I am in need of your assistance in completing a number of missions as part of our efforts to bolster Prince Durin and the Gabil'akkâ in their preparations and ensure the welfare of our brethren at distant dwarf-holds. We must be well-prepared when the time comes to reclaim Mount Gundabad at last!

'Would you assist me and the Kharum-ubnâr by completing several of these missions?''I thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. We of the Kharum-ubnâr cannot be everywhere, but you have done much to aid us.

'Hail Thorin Stonehelm, King Under the Mountain! Glory to Durin's Folk!'After the War of the Dwarves and Orcs was ended, Orcs returned to Gundabad and laid claim to the countless dwarf-made weapons left abandoned in its halls. Many are now held as trophies by the Orcs of Bekâr-zarakh.Your mission is to reclaim dwarf-made weapons held as trophies by the Orcs in Bekâr-zarakh.

You should talk to Hórin and travel to Bekâr-zarakh.Complete 'Mission: An Agelong Theft'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have just returned from Bekâr-zarakh. It seems the Orcs of Gundabad keep countless weapons of the dwarves as trophies within that tower. If the weapon one of my scouts recovered is of any indication, many may have been forged before Gundabad first fell in the Second Age. It is of great importance that these weapons are not allowed to remain in the hands of the Orcs. They are unworthy to bear them!

'You are to travel to Bekâr-zarakh and relieve the Orcs of these ill-gotten weapons. For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!'High in the tower of Bekar-zarakh, the Orcs of Gundabad prepare for war. In their keeping are weapons of dwarf-make, stolen long ago in the sack of Gundabad….

Your mission is to reclaim dwarf-made weapons held as trophies by the Orcs in Bekâr-zarakh.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'I shall send these to our greatest smiths and scholars that they might be identified and returned to their rightful owner's kin.'You have been tasked with defending the fortress of Skarháld from a Frost-horde assault.Your mission is to defend the fortress of Skarháld from a Frost-horde assault.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Skarháld.Complete Mission: An Assault of FrostThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have reported a band of drakes, flying towards Skarháld! I am certain the frost drakes will assault our fortress in Ered Mithrim! We must depart for Skarháld immediately and assist in thwarting this assault!'The fortress of Skarháld is under attack! The Frost-horde has launched an assault from parts unknown in Ered Mithrin in hopes to drive the dwarves away….

Your mission is to defend the fortress of Skarháld from a Frost-horde assault.'Well done! With the drake assault defeated, Skarháld is once again safe! The last thing we need is our greatest fortress of Ered Mithin in ruin!'Your mission is to sabotage the Ordâkhai siege engines under construction at Ghât Lor and defeat any Ordâkhai who move to stop you.Your mission is to sabotage the Ordâkhai siege engines under construction at Ghât Lor and defeat any Ordâkhai who move to stop you.

Speak to Udlanu to travel.Complete Mission: An Explosive AssaultYou have destroyed all the siege engines! Return with the scout to Udlanu in Urmâkh with this report.Speak with Udlanu in Urmâkh'Our attention has been so focused on the Barkhûshim - it seems the Ordâkhai to the south have slipped below our notice. One of our scouts just returned from their encampment at Ghât Lor. They are constructing siege weapons - we believe to assault us, either at Kûr Anzar or Urmâkh. Either way, we need to act first, and quickly.

'You are tasked with going to Ghât Lor and sabotaging these siege weapons. Destroy them before they can ever be used against the innocent peoples of Imhûlar. Defeat any Ordâkhai who try to stop you.''Your mission is simple, ${PLAYER}. Sabotage the Ordâkhai siege weapons and don't let any Ordâkhai warriors stop you.''That is excellent news. Thank you for destroying their engines of war. Without them, they can do little to attack our cities. I can assure you, we will be keeping a close watch on the Ordâkhai from now on.'Protect the Khâlbina and her crew from dangers while sailing to Jax Phanâl on the Cape of Umbar.Your mission is to protect the merchant ship Khâlbina on its trip to Jax Phanâl.

Speak to Deshra to travel.Complete Mission: An Infestation of CrabsYou have successfully defeated the crabs and protected the Khâlbina! Return with the Umbari scout to the mission giver with this report.Speak with Deshra'Well met again, ${PLAYER}. The Khâlbina is one of our finest merchant ships. She is sailing to Jax Phanâl on the morrow. There are rumours of huge beasts, giant crabs, and who knows what else, clamouring aboard ships near Jax Phanâl. These are simple merchant vessels, and their crews are not used to defending themselves from such beasts. Would you protect the Khâlbina and her crew on this perilous journey?''Your objective is clear, ${PLAYER}, protect the Khâlbina at all cost. The hopes of the Khâlbina and her crew rest upon your able shoulders.''Well that is quite the tale. I am so glad you were there to take on those dreadful beasts and ensure the crew's safety. Thank you for your valiant deeds.'There are reports of disappearances from Sormedân and some say that a suspicious figure fled into the Blade-horn. Investigate the Blade-horn for any sign of the culprit.Your mission is to investigate Bâdrasag, the Blade-horn, for any sign of a suspicious man who may be making it his refuge.

Speak to Jôrlar to travel.Complete Mission: An Ordinary ManYou have defeated the ordinary-looking man. Return with the scout to Jôrlar in Zajâna with this report.Speak with Jôrlar in Zajâna'A series of disappearances have shaken the small village of Sormedân.

'I know not whether it was beast or man, but something is hunting those in Sormedân. Several villagers stated that they saw a suspicious man near Bâdrasag, the Blade-horn. There are many stories about the Blade-horn, some of them may even be true. But it would be a good hiding spot for someone trying to lay low.

'Would you investigate the Blade-horn, and determine if someone there really is responsible for these disappearances? All of Sormedân would appreciate your efforts.''I hope you find nothing, and that these missing people stumble out of the woods, having lost their way. But I do not think that is the case. Keep your wits and your eyes sharp, there is great danger in Bâdrasag.''He seemed unassuming? Yet was that strong? I know not what that means, but I am grateful that he is no more. The people of Sormedân have much to thank you for.'Your mission is to investigate reports of a strange man who appears to live with the zizani in the ponds of Charganpâta.Your mission is to journey to the ponds of Charganpâta and investigate claims of theft by a strange man living among the zizani.

Speak to Jôrlar to travel.Complete Mission: Another Man's TreasureYou have gathered the stolen possessions and defeated Zâwakhar. Return with the scout to Jôrlar in Zajâna with your report.Speak with Jôrlar in Zajâna'We have received troubling reports from the north, near the ponds of Charganpâta.

'Locals say a man is living out there among the zizani in the swamp, breaking into their homes as they sleep and stealing their things before absconding back to Charganpâta.

'This is alarming, not least because Charganpâta is quite hostile to all but the zizani. Could you investigate these claims, and if they are true, try to speak sense into this man?''I hope these claims are unfounded, and that you find nothing. Nevertheless, take care. One does not live among the zizani for one's health - you may find trouble in pursuit of this man.''A hoardsman? I can scarcely believe it. Still, we will make sure all these possessions return to the people he stole from. I hesitate to call these valuables - but they will be returned.

'Thank you for seeing this matter through to its end.'You have been tasked with dispatching the Orc archers defending Shathur-munzu.Your mission is to defeat the Orc archers outside Shathur-munzu.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Shathur-munzu.Complete Mission: Archers at the GateThe mission is complete.

Speak to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

