'My scouts have come back from the High Pass. They report that they could not get to the Misty Mountains as an icy blockade constructed by the Frost-horde stands in their way! They fear the blockade will put an end to any dwarves seeking to join our efforts from over the Misty Mountains.

'I need you to destroy this blockade so that the High Pass can remain clear!'Upon the High Pass, the Frost-horde has blocked the mountain path….

Your mission is to destroy the icy blockade upon the High Pass.'Well done! With the blockade destroyed, we can continue scouting the mountains surrounding the High Pass. The last thing we need is more drakes in these mountains!'The Temámir of Jiret-menêsh want to help the people who are being held prisoner by the Ordâkhai at Kôth Rau.Your mission is to go to Kôth Rau and free the prisoners the Ordâkhai are holding there.

Talk to Têsegi when you are ready to travel.Complete Mission: Bound for TormentYou have completed your mission of setting the tents and banners at Onabóha on fire. Return with the Temámir scout to report your success.Talk to Têsegi Jiret-menêsh'The Ordâkhai at Kôth Rau are holding prisoners that are likely to be tortured for some unknown reason. Most of them are traders captured while coming or going from Zajâna. If we are to take our place as the stewards of An Shêru, it is our duty to free them from captivity.''Your mission is to go to Kôth Rau and free the prisoners the Ordâkhai are holding there.''They are free? This is joyous news indeed! We know not why these people were captured for torture, but we do not need to know the reason why to know that the Ordâkhai are doing wrong.'Feared by Orcs and dwarves alike, Ushgoth the Mighty leads the forces of Gundabad who dwell in Bekâr-zarakh.Your mission is to defeat Ushgoth the Mighty, the captain of the Orcs in Bekâr-zarakh.

You should talk to Hórin and travel to Bekâr-zarakh.Complete 'Mission: Breaking Bekâr-zarakh'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have just returned with urgent news. One of Gorgar's most trusted lieutenants, Ushgoth the Mighty, has been granted command of the Orcs in Bekâr-zarakh. With many of them still patrolling Elderslade, now is our chance to deal a blow to Gorgar himself!

'You are to travel to Bekâr-zarakh and see that Ushgoth is defeated. Let the Orcs of Gundabad tremble in fear! For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!'High in the tower of Bekar-zarakh, the Orcs of Gundabad prepare for war. Among them, Ushgoth the Mighty makes ready to enact his plans on the battlefield….

Your mission is to defeat Ushgoth the Mighty, the captain of the Orcs in Bekâr-zarakh.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'It seems Ushgoth wasn't so mighty after all, eh?'You have been tasked with defeating the Angmarim Warg-breeders in Gundabad.Your mission is to defeat the Angmarim Warg-breeders in Gundabad.

Speak to Ausma to travel.Complete Mission: Breeders of BeastsThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have returned from Cútaig. It seems the most vicious Wargs in Gundabad are being bred in those passages. The time has come to seek out the Angmarim Warg-breeders there and drive them off.'Within the halls of Cútaig, the most vicious Wargs of Gundabad are bred. There, even the most skilled of hunters must tread with care lest they become the hunted….

Your mission is to defeat the Angmarim Warg-breeders in Gundabad.'You have done well, ${PLAYER}. The fewer Wargs in Gundabad, the better!

'With the Warg-breeders defeated, the Angmarim will know that we are not to be underestimated!'You have been tasked with defeating the spider menace within the mines of Writhenset.Your mission is to defeat the spider menace within the mines of Writhenset.

Speak to Radhril.Complete Mission: Brooding in the DepthsThe mission is complete!

Speak to Radhril for your reward!Talk to Radhril'Would you accompany me on a mission, ${CLASS}?

'The Free Peoples in the Wildwood have reported hearing the scuttling legs of spiders in and around the mines of Writhenset. There could be a brood within the tunnels.

'If the mines of Writhenset are to ever again be safe, we should investigate this possible spider menace.'Within the depths of the mines of Writhenset, a brood of spiders grows restless.

Your mission is to defeat the spider menace within the mines of Writhenset.'We have done well, ${CLASS}. With the spider brood diminished, the mines of Writhenset are now much more safe for the Free Peoples. We should be on the look-out, however. The spiders could just as easily return in greater numbers.'You have been tasked with recording the etchings of buried dwarves.Your mission is to record etchings of the deceased dwarves in the excavated tomb.

Speak to Horin to travel to Atkat-daragComplete Mission: Buried, but Not ForgottenThe mission is complete!

Speak to Horin for your reward!Talk to Horin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Our scouts have made an incredible new discovery. Upon our recent excavation of an ancestral dwarf-tomb, it would appear that some of the stones are still in such good condition, they actually have the names and dates of the dwarves buried there!

'This is an important discovery, as so much about Gundabad's history was lost to the ages. Do you think you could go and copy down any legible names and dates written on the sarcophagi down there? Oh, and be careful. Our scouts reported hearing strange noises while they were down there....''Ancient dwarf-sarcophagi seem to still hold names and dates of the deceased.

'Your mission is to record these etchings safely, and return to Horin.''Well done! Thanks to you we can start piecing together more of the history of the dwarves and Gundabad.'You have been tasked with defeating the stone-claws who burrow too close to the Hadhodiant.Your mission is to clear the stone-claw menace from the Hadhodiant.

Speak to Ausma to travel to the Hadhodiant.Complete Mission: Burrowers by the HadhodiantThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'We seek to repair the Hadhodiant in the Vales of Anduin. It would seem there have been many sightings of stone-claws near the bridge, however. These pesky creatures are known for digging and burrowing. If they dig too much around the Hadhodiant, they might just collapse the entire structure!

'We must be rid of these stone-claws before the bridge building can continue.'Pesky stone-claws have been seen recently, digging around the Hadhodiant….

Your mission is to clear the stone-claw menace from the Hadhodiant.'Well done! I thank you for ridding us of those pesky stone-claws! Now we will finish repairing the Hadhodiant so that trade and movement will be swifter between the Vales of Anduin and the Misty Mountains!'You have been tasked with thwarting Angmarim bat-keepers in Gundabad.Your mission is to thwart Angmarim bat-keepers in Gundabad.

Speak to Ausma to travel.Complete Mission: Captive WingsThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have returned from an Angmarim keep in the mountains of Gundabad. There they have spotted a group of Angmarim who breed and train bats. Their vile tactics can not stand! We must return to the keep, defeat the bat-keepers, and put an end to their nefarious breeding!''Upon the peaks of Gundabad, the Angmarim breed bats for nefarious purposes….

'Your mission is to thwart Angmarim bat-keepers in Gundabad.''Well done! With the bat-keepers defeated, we now have one less thing to worry about when traversing the dark caverns of Gundabad! I would recant the others if the list were not so long!'You have been tasked with rescuing miners from the partially collapsed cave of Mesem-gairu.Your mission is to rescue miners from the partially collapsed cave of Mesem-gairu.

Speak to Ausma to travel.Complete Mission: Cave In!The mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have sent urgent word from the caverns of Mesem-gairu. While some miners were excavating, the caverns partially collapsed! These dwarves are expert miners. I believe that our enemies may have planned to collapse the caverns with our miners inside. Let us hope the miners have survived.

'You are to travel to Mesem-gairu at once. We must rescue the trapped miners!''Within the glittering caverns of Mesem-gairu lies a treasure trove of crystals, wanted by many….

'Your mission is to rescue miners from the partially collapsed cave of Mesem-gairu.''Well done!

'I am glad that you were able to rescue the miners. It would seem that the miners agree with my theory as well. We must be more careful in Gundabad, for many foes still lurk in its shadows!'Your mission is to help a local farmer outside Urmâkh round up his escaped chickens.Your mission is to help a local farmer outside Urmâkh round up his escaped chickens.

Speak to Udlanu to travel.Complete Mission: Chickens Home to RoostYou have helped Mushêndu recover his lost chickens! Return with the scout to Urmâkh with this report.Speak with Udlanu in Urmâkh'A local farmer, Mushêndu, just came to us, alarmed. His chickens are loose again, and he wants our assistance in getting them back. He lives on the hill outside Urmâkh. Unfortunately jackals prowl those hills, so it is quite dangerous, both for him and the chickens. Would you be able to assist him?''Your mission is to help Mushêndu recover his missing chickens.''Thank you for helping Mushêndu. I'm glad no harm befell him or his chickens.'Your mission is to venture to the Moulder-grove and prevent the blight from spreading further.Your mission is to go to the Moulder-grove. Bring peace to the restless trees and set fire to their progeny, that they may not spread further into Kighân.

Speak to Jôrlar to travel.Complete Mission: Chopping the WoodsYou have defeated the restless trees and scorched their venturous growths. Return with the scout to Jôrlar in Zajâna with this report.Speak with Jôrlar in Zajâna'Although our troubles are many, those who find their way from Adagím have it worse. There is a sickness there, one that threatens to take hold here in Kighân.

'We cannot allow that. Already it has found a toe-hold in northern Kighân, a place locals call the Moulder-grove. There as in Adagím the trees are restless and violent, and the plants twisted and strange. We cannot save Adagím - but we can contain its evil.

'Please, seek out the strange and twisted plants in the Moulder-grove, and set torch to their progeny. It is the only way we can be sure this affliction does not spread and take over Kighân as well.''Sometimes the only proper answer to a problem is a good flame. May fortune guide you, and bring you swiftly back to Zajâna.''You set fire to them? It heartens me to hear it. We shall be rid of this blight yet, if not by salves or miracles then by flame. Thank you, friend.'Although the Dwarves of Gabilshathûr are no longer trapped beyond the Rammas Deluon, its miners face new challenges as the creatures of Angmar reclaim the fallen realm.Your mission is to aid the Dwarves of Gabilshathûr in repelling an infestation of blade-beaks.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath and travel to Gabilshathûr.Complete 'Mission: Claws of Gabilshathûr'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath at Akrâz-zahar.Talk to Vorthur Smokebreath'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'I have received an urgent message from the dwarves at Gabilshathûr. It seems that even though they are no longer troubled by Orcs and the Men of Angmar, the blade-beaks that have long dwelled in the region have grown a bit more numerous and much more dangerous than they anticipated! Burrows have been cropping up in the centre of Gabilshathûr for several days now, and if they are not soon sealed, it is feared the blade-beaks will overrun the settlement.

'You are to travel to Gabilshathûr and aid the dwarves there in sealing these burrows!'Although the Dwarves of Gabilshathûr are no longer trapped beyond the Rammas Deluon, its miners face new challenges as the creatures of Angmar reclaim the fallen realm.

Your mission is to aid the Dwarves of Gabilshathûr in repelling an infestation of blade-beaks.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'I suppose if it is not one thing, it's another. Angmar is not the most hospitable land, even for the hardiest of dwarves!'You have been tasked with recovering precious ore and clearing a path through the cave.Your mission is to recover precious ore and clear a path through the cave-claw cave.

Speak to Ausma to travel to cave-claw cave.Complete Mission: Clearing a PathThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from one of the caverns that weaves throughout Gundabad and report findings of precious resources. However, several passageways are blocked and need to be cleared before we can send additional miners.

'Enter the mine, obtain samples of the ore in the area, and destroy any debris that blocks passage in the cavern!''Amongst the twisting caves that surround Gundabad, several passageways that lead to needed raw ore have been blocked by rubble. These precious resources are needed for the recovery effort.

'Your mission is to retrieve precious ore and clear a path so other miners can continue the work.''Well done! With the cavern cleared of debris and resources gathered, the foundation has been laid for our work in Gundabad!'You have been tasked with collapsing the old mining tunnels that the Dourhands have been using to dig further into Glimmerdeep.Your mission is to collapse the old mining tunnels in Glimmerdeep.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Glimmerdeep.Complete Mission: Collapsing the Old PathsThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the Glimmerdeep. They have found the old mine overrun with Dourhands! Those dwarves were seen digging in some of the old and unsafe tunnels!

'We must put a stop to their mining efforts and collapse those old tunnel entrances until a time when we can properly and safely survey them!'Dourhands have found the Glimmerdeep and seek to mine what they can from its depths….

Your mission is to collapse the old mining tunnels in Glimmerdeep.'Well done! With those tunnels collapsed, the Dourhands should stop searching for riches in Glimmerdeep. We should look to resume our mining efforts there once all the Dourhands have vacated the mines.'The Ordâkhai have gained ground, capturing the floating bridge at Wrackwade. The Dumûri have asked for your help to overcome their defenders and regain possession of the river-crossing.Your mission is to help the Dumûri counterattack and regain control of the Wrackwade. As you secure sections of the bridge, raise Ambarûli banners to lay claim to them.

Talk to Khâdamul when you are ready for battle.Complete Mission: Counterattack at WrackwadeThe counterattack is successful! You have helped the Dumûri regain control of the Wrackwade. Return with Khâdamul to report your victory.Speak with Khâdamul in Iridír'The Ordâkhai have attacked, capturing the floating bridge at Wrackwade! We have stopped their advance and there is a break in the fighting. Now is the time for a counterattack! We could use your help to overcome their defenders and regain possession of the river-crossing. As you secure sections of the bridge, raise Ambarûli banners to lay claim to them.''Your mission is to help the Dumûri regain control of the Wrackwade.''Thank you for helping the Dumûri regain control of the Wrackwade. As the only river-crossing in Ambarûl, it is vital to keep the bridge under our control.'You have been tasked with carefully mining crystals within Mesem-gairu.Your mission is to carefully mine crystals within Mesem-gairu and bring them back to Horin.

Speak to Horin to travel to Mesem-gairu.Complete Mission: Crystal ConundrumThe mission is complete!

Speak to Horin for your reward!Talk to Horin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'So it seems we've stumbled into a cavern full of crystals upon one of our recent delves into the ground. Our scouts are calling it Mesem-gairu, and its apparent that this cave is abundant with gems.

'I would ask if you could retrieve some of these crystals for further inspection and perhaps even further use in our endeavours. But do so carefully, we aren't sure what, if any, creatures may also be drawn to these crystals.'A large amount of crystals have been found within a new cavern named Mesem-gairu.

Your mission is to collect a sample of these crystals, and defend yourself against any creatures that may dwell down there.'Well done! I hope you weren't too overwhelmed down there! Thanks to you we can start finding a use for these new crystals!'You have been tasked to seek out and destroy the corrupted crystals and defeat the corrupted pack-leader Ramshar.Your mission is to destroy corrupted crystals in the cavern, and seek out the warg pack-leader.

Speak to Ausma to travel to the warg-infested cavern.Complete Mission: Culling the RotThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from one of the caverns within the mountain. They were exploring a cavern and found several strange crystals that were warped and changed. The scouts fled as they heard a series of howls approach the cave.  As they fled the area, they saw a powerful warg pack-leader lead wolves to the cavern.

