Your mission is to collect hides from the Wargs in Valdhellir.'You have done well, ${PLAYER}.

'These hides will serve as a stern reminder to the Wargs of Elderslade that we are not to be underestimated!'You have been tasked with defeating the Huorn in Grazadh-gropor.Your mission is to defeat the corrupted Huorns in Grazadh-gropor.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Grazadh-gropor.Complete Mission: Idols of CorruptionThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Do you know of the Taurogrim? They are fearsome wood-trolls native to Mirkwood, or Eryn Lasgalen as the Elves have renamed it. My scouts have seen some peculiar activity among the trees in Misthallow. They have seen the Taurogrim corrupting the Huorns into foul monstrosities, and then worshipping them as idols to some dark deity. I don't like this, ${PLAYER}. Who knows what evil plans they have for these corrupted Huorns? I task you with entering Grazadh-gropor and defeating them!''Thank you for putting a stop to whatever foul magics were afoot in Grazadh-gropor. The Elves can call the forest whatever they want, but it still seems like Mirkwood to me!'The wood-trolls known as the Taurogrim still haunt much of Eryn Lasgalen. Deep in Grazadh-gropor, they spread their corruption among the trees….

Your mission is to defeat the corrupted Huorns in Grazadh-gropor.The Ordâkhai torturer Dokhára is holding several Ambarûli people prisoner in Eshadûr.Your mission is to rescue the prisoners being held in Eshadûr and save them from the Ordâkhai torturer Dokhára.

Talk to Khâdamul when you are ready to get underway.Complete Mission: In Need of RescueYou have freed the prisoners in Eshadûr and defeated Dokhára! Return with Khâdamul to report your success.Speak with Khâdamul in Iridír'${PLAYER}, your help is needed in Eshadûr. We have received word that the Ordâkhai captured several people and took them to their stronghold. A witness reports seeing Dokhára with them. He is greatly feared by the Ambarûli and is known for torturing his prisoners. Quickly, you must get to Eshadûr and rescue these people!''Your mission is to rescue the prisoners being held in Eshadûr and save them from the Ordâkhai torturer Dokhára.''Thank you for rescuing the prisoners in Eshadûr. It is a relief that Dokhára did not get much time with them.'You have been tasked with defending the Gate of Gath Uior from allies of the Iron Crown.Your mission is to defend the Gate of Gath Uior from allies of the Iron Crown.

Speak to Hórin to travel.Complete Mission: In the TrenchesThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the Iron Pass where they have received a plea for assistance. It would seem a small band of Elves still hold the Gate of Gath Uior in Angmar. My scouts were told not to stray too far afield. Instead, they reported back to me immediately about the Elves. I believe if you leave now, you will still be able to offer this small band of Elves the assistance they require.

'The Rift is but one of the paths that can lead to Gundabad from Angmar. It is important that we protect Gundabad from further attacks by the Iron Crown!''In the far eastern edges of Angmar lies The Rift. The passage through the mountains there is one of few that the Iron Crown has taken to the slopes of Gundabad….

'Your mission is to defend the Gate of Gath Uior from allies of the Iron Crown.''Well done! With the Gate of Gath Uior still under guard, may we experience fewer troubles out of Angmar!'Brilliant gem-stones illuminate the Crystal Tunnels beneath Skarháld, but beware, for foes lurk in the shadows.You have been tasked with mining pure beryl from the Crystal Tunnels beneath Skarháld.

You should talk to Hórin to travel to Skarháld.Complete 'Mission: Into the Crystal Tunnels'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'The Gabil'akkâ has need for a new supply of pure beryl. We thought we had carried enough when we first journeyed from Skarháld, but such are the demands of war!

'You must travel to Skarháld and mine more pure beryl from the Crystal Tunnels! For the Gabil'akkâ!'A remnant of the lost Dwarf-kingdom of Grárik, Skarháld has long-endured both the harsh climes of Ered Mithrin and the wrath of dragon-kind. Beneath the Keep of Tharrazhâr lie tunnels of most beautiful crystal, but that is not all that lurks within….

Your mission is to mine pure beryl from the Crystal Tunnels beneath Skarháld.'This beryl shall do nicely, ${PLAYER}!

'And it is even better that it has not fallen in the hands of goblins!'You have been tasked with defeating the half-orc forces gathered at the entrances to the mines of Writhenset.Your mission is to defeat the half-orc forces gathered at the entrances to the mines of Writhenset.

Speak to Radhril.Complete Mission: Invaders on the DelfThe mission is complete!

Speak to Radhril for your reward!Talk to Radhril'Would you accompany me on a mission, ${CLASS}?

'The Free Peoples in the Wildwood have reported that the mines of Writhenset have been taken over by a group of half-orcs. It would seem they have the entrances to the mines completely guarded.

'If the mines of Writhenset are to ever again be safe, this group of half-orcs must be removed.'The entrances to the mines of Writhenset have been seized by half-orc intruders!

Your mission is to defeat the half-orc forces gathered at the entrances to the mines of Writhenset.'We have done well, ${CLASS}. With the half-orc mining operation defeated, the mines of Writhenset will soon enough be safe. I am sure the Free Peoples are thankful for our efforts.'After traversing the Redhorn Pass, a growing band of goblins seeks to capture Kidzul-kâlah and set siege to the Vales of Anduin.Your mission is to repel the goblin invasion at Kidzul-kâlah and seal the Redhorn Pass.

You should talk to Ausma and travel to Kidzul-kâlah.Complete 'Mission: Invasion at the Redhorn Pass'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Ausma for your reward.Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have sent urgent word from Kidzul-kâlah. It seems a band of goblins out of Eregion has made its way through the Redhorn Pass to the Vales of Anduin. A few goblins do not worry me, but I am told this force grows larger with every passing hour.

'You are to travel to Kidzul-kâlah at once. If you cannot find another way to stop this invasion, I have been given the authority to order you to seal the Redhorn Pass.

'Let us hope it does not come to that, but do what must be done! For the Gabil'akkâ!'Nestled in the foothills of the Misty Mountains, the dwarf-keep of Kidzul-kâlah lies half-sunken in the Gladdenmere. However, the Redhorn Pass lies open to friends and foes alike….

Your mission is to repel the goblin invasion at Kidzul-kâlah and seal the Redhorn Pass.'You have done well, ${PLAYER}!

'It is regrettable that the Redhorn Pass needed to be sealed. However, once this conflict is ended, we shall see it open once more!'The Wargs of Elderslade keep numerous skulls of the slain as grisly trophies in Valdhellir.Your mission is to destroy collections of grisly trophies kept by the Wargs in Valdhellir.

You should talk to Hórin and travel to Valdhellir.Complete 'Mission: Jaws of the Dead'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have returned from Valdhellir with troubling news. It appears these Wargs are more canny than we expected! In addition to devouring those unlucky enough to cross their paths, they also keep grisly trophies in the darkened passages of Valdhellir. It is an insult to the slain and I will not allow it to stand!

'You are to travel to Valdhellir and destroy these trophies at once! For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!'Within Valdhellir, the most vicious Wargs of Elderslade dwell in darkness surrounded by countless skulls and other grisly trophies.

Your mission is to destroy collections of grisly trophies kept by the Wargs in Valdhellir.'It is done then? Good.

'You have my thanks for destroying those terrible trophies, ${PLAYER}.'You have been tasked with defeating ice-giants and recovering stolen treasures.Your mission is to defeat ice-giants and recover stolen treasures.

Speak to Hórin to travel to the ice-giant enclave.Complete Missions: Just Beyond ReachThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from one of the caverns that weaves throughout Gundabad. Ice-giants have stolen several treasures from within Gundabad and secured them behind a series of gates.

'Defeat ice-giants and recover treasures stolen from the depths of Gundabad!'Amongst the halls of Gundabad, countless treasures await to be reclaimed. Ice-giants have breached one of the treasure halls and made off with our valuables.

Your mission is to recover the stolen treasures and punish the ice-giants for their actions.'Well done! With the stolen treasures reclaimed, we will have additional resources for our great effort!'Far to the north of Annâk-khurfu lies Rathad Caul, the Narrow Way, a treacherous passage into Câr Bronach. There, those still loyal to the Iron Crown guard the approach to the last bastions of Angmar.Your mission is to defeat the Dourhand gate-keeper guarding Rathad Caul and tear down the banner of the Iron Crown.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath and travel to Rathad Caul.Complete 'Mission: Keepers of the Narrow Way'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath at Akrâz-zahar.Talk to Vorthur Smokebreath'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Our scouts have reported a recent rise in activity to the north. It seems a remnant of the Iron Crown has taken refuge in the lands of Câr Bronach, and they have set a watch at Rathad Caul, the Narrow Way. Although the Gabil'akkâ must remain focused on the reclamation of Gundabad, we cannot allow the Iron Crown to keep a foothold so near to the mountain.

'You are to travel to Rathad Caul at once! Defeat the gate-keeper and tear down the banner of the Iron Crown!'Far to the north of Annâk-khurfu lies Rathad Caul, the Narrow Way, a treacherous passage into Câr Bronach. There, those still loyal to the Iron Crown guard the approach to the last bastions of Angmar.

Your mission is to defeat the Dourhand gate-keeper guarding Rathad Caul and tear down the banner of the Iron Crown.'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}!

'Once the gates of Gundabad are opened and we have staked our claim upon the mountain, the time shall come to explore Câr Bronach. Of that, I am certain!'Your mission is to go to Dûlagig, seal the scorpion burrows with fire and cull their number.Your mission is to go to Dûlagig, seal the scorpion burrows with fire and cull their number.

Speak to Udlanu to travel.Complete Mission: Kill It with FireYou have defeated the scorpions and destroyed their burrows. Return with the scout to Udlanu in Urmâkh with this report.Speak with Udlanu in Urmâkh'There is danger to the west, ${PLAYER}. Scorpions from Dûlagig have been expanding outward, harassing many local travellers. They are a danger to all the people of Urmâkh. These scorpions need to be culled, their numbers reduced. We require your help. Please, destroy their burrows, set them ablaze, and cull any scorpions you find.''Your mission is clear, ${PLAYER}. Defeat the scorpions and set their burrows ablaze.''Those scorpions were quite the threat to the people of Urmâkh. Thank you for ending their threat.'You have been tasked with defeating a large deep-claw and destroying its burrow in Gundabad.Your mission is to defeat Amshaz the Vast and destroy its burrow in Gundabad.

Speak to Ausma to travel.Complete Mission: King of ClawsThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the caverns of Ronglagam. Not only are the caverns overrun with stone-claws and deep-claws, a very large deep-claw has taken refuge there as well! My scouts have named the beast, Amshaz the Vast.

'We cannot let the stone-claws and Amshaz the Vast to burrow in Ronglagam. It lies under the very foundation of the Steepset!''Stone-claws and deep-claws have taken over the caverns of Ronglagam, as the great deep-claw Amshaz the Vast slumbers within….

'Your mission is to defeat a large deep-claw and destroy its burrow in Gundabad.''Well done! With Amshaz and the stone-claws defeated, and their burrow abandoned, the foundation of Steepset is once again safe. We must stay vigilant, for many other creatures may try to move into the caverns of Ronglagam!'Bob's daughter, Lalia, has gone missing, and Bob fears she may have gone off in search of the "Last Prince," a character in one of the tales Barliman Butterbur tells to travellers.According to Butterbur's tale, the barrow of the Last Prince lies between Northern Barrows and The Dead Spire, near a large standing stone. You have been asked to search the Barrow-downs for his missing daughter, who may have gone there in search of the fabled "Last Prince."Complete Mission: Lalia's Safe PassageYou have delivered Lalia safely out of the Barrow-downs despite her efforts to walk unwittingly into every wight in the fog-drenched hills.Talk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony'Lalia, a young hobbit lass, has gone missing. She is the daughter of Bob who is employed here at the Prancing Pony. She was very taken by Barliman's tales of "The Last Prince", who's barrow is in the Barrow-downs, purportedly between the Northern Barrow and the Dead Spire. If you are stouthearted enough to help look for her and bring her home, that is where you should begin your search.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Are you ready to brave the mists of the Barrow-downs? The hapless little one will likely be among the barrows much longer than she ever intended if she is not found soon.''It seems you successfully saved Lalia from the wights... and herself. She is with her father and is now resting, but I can offer you gratitude and a reward on their behalf.'You have been tasked with destroying fell sarcophagi and burning the remains of fallen Angmarim.Your mission is to destroy several corrupted sarcophagi and burn the corpses of the Angmarim scattered throughout.

Speak to Hórin to travel to barrows.Complete Mission: Lay to RestThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from one of the barrows within Gundabad. Deep within the barrow, several of the sarcophagi have been twisted, and foul creatures have begun to come forth. Additionally, the remains of several Angmarim littered the area.

'Enter the barrows, destroy the corrupted sarcophagi and destroy the remains of the foul invaders!''Amongst the barrows in the depths Gundabad, the spirits of our forefathers are being disturbed.

'Your mission is to destroy fell sarcophagi and burn the corpses of the Angmarim.''Well done! With the deed done, our ancestors can find rest in Gundabad!'You have been tasked with destroying the brigand blockade within the mines of Writhenset.Your mission is to destroy the brigand blockade within the mines of Writhenset.

Speak to Radhril.Complete Mission: Locked DownThe mission is complete!

Speak to Radhril for your reward!Talk to Radhril'Would you accompany me on a mission, ${CLASS}?

'The Free Peoples in the Wildwood have reported a group of brigands who have barricaded themselves in the mines of Writhenset. It would seem these deviant Men have all but fled from the Wildwood.

'If the mines of Writhenset are to ever again be safe, this group of brigands must be removed.'A group of brigands has locked themselves in the mines of Writhenset in a last ditch effort to control their foothold in the Wildwood.

Your mission is to destroy the brigand blockade within the mines of Writhenset.'We have done well, ${CLASS}. With nowhere else to take refuge in the Wildwood, this group of brigands will certainly disperse. The mines of Writhenset will soon enough be safe for the Free Peoples, thanks to our efforts.'Deep in the Grey Mountains, the hobgoblins launch a plot to free their mistress....You have been assigned another important mission!

Report to Ausma in Annâk-khurfu to learn the details.Talk to AusmaHórin has announced that he knows what the hobgoblins are planning.

You should talk to Hórin in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to HórinYour mission is to investigate Akûl-lagam with Hórin.

Talk to Hórin to travel to Akûl-lagam.Complete Mission: Loyalty of the Frost-boundThe mission is complete!

You should talk to Hórin in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to HórinThe mission is complete!

You should talk to Glóin in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to Glóin'${PLAYER}, for your proven heroism, I grant you the rank of Uzkhas of the Gabil'akkâ! I trust you will continue this fine work until the war is won.

'I have another important mission for you. Ausma's scouts have learned of a hobgoblin operation deep in the Grey Mountains. I will allow her to fill you in on the details. Good luck!''Hello, ${PLAYER}. Here for the hobgoblins? This is what I have learned so far:

'We have discovered a hidden cave entrance in the Grey Mountains, on the eastern slopes of Thrumfall. The scouts report hobgoblin and Orc activity inside, but they could not get close enough to see what they were up to. Something about "swarms of vicious worms". They could, however, hear the sounds of digging, or mining, and while I don't know what those Orcs are up to I agree that it warrants investigation.'Deep in the Grey Mountains, the hobgoblins launch a plot to free their mistress....

Your mission is to investigate Akûl-lagam with Hórin.'I am glad to be back indoors, ${PLAYER}! That place had an unnatural chill, just like the Anvil. They must have been close to their goal. It is good we arrived when we did, or they might have succeeded in releasing the dragon!

'I will make sure some scouts are posted near the entrance to that cave, in case some hobgoblin gets the bright idea to try to resume their operations. But, to be honest, I have a feeling deep in my bones that we fight the inevitable. You had best be ready to fight her when the time comes, ${PLAYER}. I know I will be.''Is everything all right, ${PLAYER}? Hórin looks deathly serious.'

You tell Glóin of Hórin's concern about Hrímil Frost-heart.

'Aye, having such a powerful foe so near concerns me as well. Dragons and other evils slumbering in unknown places deep in the mountains have long caused anxiety for the Longbeards. I am almost ashamed that none of my clan could have joined Hórin on his expedition into the Anvil, but our soldiers had not yet come to Skarháld, and we had only just recovered Dori from the clutches of the drakes. What good would a few old dwarves have done storming into the den of an elder dragon? Hórin has proven he is one of the bravest among us for rushing to stop Karazgar's plot with so few at his side.

'We must carry on as dwarves have done for centuries: keep your eyes on your goal, and take your battles one at a time. I will speak with Prince Durin about ways of defeating that dragon once and for all, but first, we have a war to win!''Aye, I overheard your conversation. It seems perfectly obvious to me what those drake-loving hobgoblins are up to! Digging east towards Winterstith can only mean one thing: They are trying to dig their way into the Anvil! We cannot allow them to free Hrímil Frost-heart or the rest of her Frost-horde! I don't know about you, but I think we have enough to deal with right now without the addition of a ferocious elder dragon!

'Let's go clear out that cave before it's too late. Yes, you heard me. I'm going with you!'You have been tasked with dispatching a powerful hobgoblin in Vorkodar.Your mission is to find and defeat Frost-caller Túgost.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Vorkodar.Complete Mission: Magic of the Frost-boundThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'We have located a powerful hobgoblin in a cave in Elderslade. He appears to be one of their leaders, and a zealous follower of the dragon Hrímil Frost-heart. It is in our best interest to ambush him while he is in his den, before he can add his magic to the Orc army. I leave dispatching him to you!''Well done! The hobgoblins are a formidable enemy, and when this battle finally comes to a head, I will be glad to have one less foul dragon-mage on the field!'The fearsome hobgoblins have sworn themselves to the Frost-horde, and gained terrible power in return….

Your mission is to find and defeat Frost-caller Túgost, the hobgoblin zealot, inside Vorkodar.You have been tasked with clearing out the cold-worm nesting grounds at the ruins of Stormwall.Your mission is to clear out the cold-worm nesting grounds at the ruins of Stormwall.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Stormwall.Complete Mission: Nests of IceThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from Stormwall. They have found the ruins overrun with cold-worms and their nests! Had my scouts more time, they would have destroyed some of the nests. We must return to properly rid these beasts from this place.

'We can not allow any of the Frost-horde to claim a hold in Ered Mithrin!'Within the ruins of Stormwall, cold-worms have begun nesting in the vacant lair of Etterfang….

Your mission is to clear out the cold-worm nesting grounds at the ruins of Stormwall.'Well done! With many of the nests destroyed and cold-worms defeated, we should be able to regain a hold on Stormwall soon enough. You have done well!'Candaith's pursuit of an Orc-company turned deadly when he was discovered, and in his haste to escape, he lost his bow to the Orcs. Led by a War-master named Uzorr, the Orcs also possess goods that would be of use to the people of the Lone-lands.You have been asked to enter the Orc encampment at Bleakrift and recover Candaith's bow as well as any other stolen goods. Before leaving, you should defeat their leader, War-master Uzorr.Complete Mission: Orc-thievesYou have recovered Candaith's bow along with the other stolen goods and defeated the Orcs' leader, War-master Uzorr. You should talk to Candaith and then give your report to the Hooded Stranger.Talk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony'My kinsman, Candaith, has been parted from his bow after crossing paths with a band of Orcs led by a War-master called Uzorr. One of War-master Uzorr's archers has surely taken it for his own. Go to their encampment at Bleakrift, within Midgewater Pass, and recover Candaith's weapon.

'While you are there, be on the look-out for lockboxes or anything that has the appearance of value that the Orcs may have stolen. These items should be returned to the people of the Lone-lands. You should also find and defeat War-master Uzorr and put an end to his activities in the region.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Are you ready to enter Bleakrift? War-master Uzorr and his band of thieves should be stopped, and the stolen goods returned to their rightful owners.''Candaith tells me that he is in possession of his bow once again, and the other wrongs have been righted. You have earned this reward, my friend.'You have been tasked with retrieving valuable ore from Sundergrót.Your mission is to retrieve ore from Sundergrót.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Sundergrót,Complete Mission: Ore OverflowingThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Are you familiar with Sundergrót, the abandoned mines in the Floodfells? It's been overrun by goblins, but it is still rich with ore! I know you're brave enough to handle this, so I am tasking you with infiltrating Sundergrót and retrieving as much ore as you can carry. It will be made into armour and weapons vital to the war effort!''Well done! This ore will be made into weapons and armour befitting our grand army! Be proud of your contribution, ${PLAYER}!'The abandoned mines of Sundergrót still hold valuable ore and treasures, ripe for the taking. However, the goblin intruders stand in your way….

Your mission is to retrieve valuable ore from Sundergrót.The brigands in Ambarûl have become bold and are attacking Iridír.Your mission is to help the Dumûri defend Iridír from pillaging brigands. Raise the control point banner when each area has been cleared of attackers.

Talk to Khâdamul when you are ready to defend Iridír.Complete Mission: Outlaws in IridírYou have helped the Dumûri defend Iridír from pillaging brigands! Return with Khâdamul to discuss your success.Speak with Khâdamul in Iridír'Brigands and outlaws have gone unchecked in Ambarûl for too long. They have now become so brazen that they are preparing to pillage Iridír! Stand by our side and help the Dumûri repel this attack.''Your mission is to help the Dumûri defend Iridír.''Thank you for helping us with the defence of Iridír. I hope the outlaws have learned a lesson they will not soon forget.'You have been tasked with protecting the merchant ship Khâlbina on its trip to Halrax in the Shield Isles.Your mission is to protect the merchant ship Khâlbina on its trip to Jax Phanâl.

Speak to Malthak to travel.Complete Mission: Protecting the Sea LanesYou have successfully defeated the Corsairs! Return with the Umbari scout to the mission giver with this report.'Well met again, ${PLAYER}. We have need of assistance for our merchant ships. We have been attacked by freebooters several times in our ongoing efforts to get food and supplies to help support Halrax in the Shield Isles. The Khâlbina is ready to set sail later today for a run to the Isles. Would you go aboard and protect her during this journey? Halrax is counting on those supplies.''Your objective is clear, ${PLAYER}, protect the Khâlbina at all cost. The hopes of the Khâlbina and her crew rest upon your able shoulders.''Well that is quite the tale. I am so glad you were there to take on those Corsairs and ensure the crew's safety. Thank you for your valiant deeds.'You have been tasked with retrieving ice that is bolstered by frost grims.Your mission is to have frost grims super-freeze ice, collect it, and retrieve it.

Speak to Horin to travel to Kallamdâm.Complete Mission: Raging FrostThe mission is complete!

Speak to Horin for your reward!Talk to Horin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'There's a great frozen hall that was explored recently called Kallamdâm. It's frigid and uninviting, and home to many a monster. Specifically, the frost grim.

'I believe when a frost grim persists near ice long enough, it can chill the ice to a super-cold state. I want you to test this theory, and lead frost grims to a frozen area, let them hang around, and then harvest any ice they super-freeze.''Apparently, when frost grims persist around ice for a short period, they can super-freeze it.

'Your mission is to test this theory within Kallamdâm by leading frost grims to cold spots, and collecting any ice they super-freeze.''Well done! Looks like our theory was correct after all. Well I'm sure we can find some use for all of this super-frozen ice. Thank you for your help!'You have been tasked with defending the fortress of Skarháld from a Gundabad raiding party.Your mission is to defend the fortress of Skarháld from a Gundabad raiding party.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Skarháld.Complete Mission: Raiders From GundabadThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have reported that a raiding party from Gundabad marches towards Skarháld! I am certain the large raiding party seeks to attack our fortress in Ered Mithrin! We must depart for Skarháld immediately and assist in thwarting this raiding party!'A raiding party from Gundabad has been spotted approaching the fortress of Skarháld, in Ered Mithrin. No different than all other Gundabad raiding parties, this one seeks to slay all in their path….

Your mission is to defend the fortress of Skarháld from a Gundabad raiding party.'Well done! With the raiding party defeated, Skarháld is once again safe! The last thing we need is our greatest fortress of Ered Mithrin in ruin!'You have been tasked with reclaiming the dwarf-ruins of Zarkul-sulûn.Your mission is to reclaim the dwarf-ruins of Zarkul-sulûn.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Zarkul-sulûn.Complete Mission: Reclaiming the Torrent-spiresThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from Zarkul-sulûn. Trolls have completely taken over the Torrent-spires! This can not stand! We must return to Zarkul-sulûn and reclaim the ruins!'Upon the dwarf-ruins of Zarkul-sulûn, a band of trolls has claimed the Torrent-spires….

Your mission is to reclaim the dwarf-ruins of Zarkul-sulûn.'Well done! With Zarkul-sulûn reclaimed, we may soon gain a greater foothold in Elderslade. We will make it to Gundabad soon enough!'You have been tasked with reclaiming the old watch-post of Bizar-atrâd.Your mission is to reclaim Bizar-atrâd.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Bizar-atrâd.Complete Mission: Reclaiming the Vale-watchThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Scouts bring word of the Vale-watch. It is under control of the hobgoblins! These Frost-bound seek to control one of the best vantage points in all of the Grey Mountains.

'We must reclaim the Vale-watch!'The watch-post of Bizar-atrâd, in the Grey Mountains, has been taken over by Frost-bound Hobgoblins….

Your mission is to reclaim Bizar-atrâd.'Well done! With Bizar-atrâd reclaimed, we can once again establish a post upon the Vale-watch. It is in our best interest to do so!'Your mission is to travel to Dûl Zidur and secure precious historical artifacts before the Barkhûshim can destroy them.Your mission is to travel to Dûl Zidur and secure precious historical artifacts and scrolls before the Barkhûshim can destroy them.

Speak to Udlanu to travel.Complete Mission: Recovering the PastYou have recovered the artifacts! Return with the scout to Udlanu in Urmâkh with this report.Speak with Udlanu in Urmâkh'A local scholar, Zuhûl, has alerted us to a cache of historical artifacts and scrolls he believes the Barkhûshim stole away when they fled Kûr Anzar. We know from our spies that the Barkhûshim remnant is quartered in Dûl Zidur, to the east. The Barkhûshim hold no love for history, and destroy anything not related to their fallen lord. They burned much of our written history in Kûr Anzar, and we have no reason to believe they won't destroy this cache as well.

'Those artifacts hold great significance for all Shagâni. They reveal our history, our culture, and provide important lessons for us, mistakes we should not repeat. Please, go to Dûl Zidur and secure these precious pieces of our history. Defeat any All-seeing who try to stop you. We are counting on you.''Your mission is clear, ${PLAYER}. You are to go to Dûl Zidur, recover the historical artifacts and scrolls, and defeat any Barkhûshim who move to stop you.''I am grateful, and I know Zuhûl will be as well. I had thought these artifacts lost forever. We will take excellent care of them, I can assure you of that. Thank you for your bravery in beating back the Barkhûshim.'You have been tasked with repairing a series of forges within an ancient forge in Gundabad.Your mission is to repair several forges and secure the area.

Speak to Hórin to travel to the forge.Complete Mission: Reforging the FutureThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have discovered an ancient and powerful forge within the halls of Gundabad. They have located several forges that could be essential to our bid to reclaim this place. However, these forges are being protected by several powerful creatures.

'Enter the forge, repair the forges found throughout the area, and defeat cold-drakes and frost grims to secure the area!''Amongst the halls of Gundabad, there lies an ancient forge that, if secured, could turn the tide of battle within these halls.

'Your mission is to repair several forges and secure the area.''Well done! With the forges repaired and the area secured, the foundation has been laid for our work in Gundabad!'You have been tasked with recovering dwarf-caches from Kidzul-kâlah before the Dourhands can lay claim to them.Your mission is to recover dwarf-caches from Kidzul-kâlah before the Dourhands can lay claim to them.

You should talk to Ausma and travel to Kidzul-kâlah.Complete 'Mission: Relics of the Goldencleft'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Ausma for your reward.Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have sent urgent word from Kidzul-kâlah. While our eyes have been turned toward Gundabad, it seems the Dourhands have taken to pillaging in the wake of the Gabil'akkâ. From what I am told, they seek to claim what few relics remain in its halls.

'You are to travel to Kidzul-kâlah and stop the Dourhands from stealing its relics. Instead, claim them on behalf of the Gabil'akkâ, and I shall see that they are looked after by more honourable dwarves!'Nestled in the foothills of the Misty Mountains, the dwarf-keep of Kidzul-kâlah lies half-sunken in the Gladdenmere. With the eyes of the dwarves elsewhere, the Dourhands have come to steal priceless relics long ago left behind....

Your mission is to recover dwarf-caches from Kidzul-kâlah before the Dourhands can lay claim to them.'Thank you, ${PLAYER}! I shall see that these relics are kept well-guarded.

'Like many of the Longbeards, I thought we had seen the last of the Dourhands. Alas, it was not to be!'A band of Ordâkhai have invaded Gha Nêkha and are harassing the locals.Your mission is to help the people of Gha Nêkha by forcibly removing the Ordâkhai soldiers there.

Talk to Khâdamul when you are ready to travel to Gha Nêkha.Complete Mission: Rescue at Gha NêkhaYou have saved the people of Gha Nêkha! Return with the Dumûri scout to report your success.Speak with Khâdamul in Iridír'We have received urgent news that a band of Ordâkhai have invaded Gha Nêkha and are attacking and bullying the locals. We are unable to send a Dumûri force to that area, but perhaps you are capable of handling the situation?''Your mission is to remove the Ordâkhai soldiers from Gha Nêkha.''Thank you for helping the people of Gha Nêkha. It is unlikely they would have stood up to the Ordâkhai on their own.'Avorthal, the Elf-prince of Celondim, has been captured by goblins and handed over to wicked Dourhand dwarves. He has been moved from the Dourhand encampment to the port-city of Kheledûl, where he will soon be taken aboard a ship destined northward and beyond all hope of rescue.You have been asked to rescue Avorthal, Elf-prince of Celondim, from the clutches of the Dourhands. While in the port-city of Kheledûl, you should also recover boxes of treasure stolen from the Longbeards by the Dourhands.Complete Mission: Rescue by MoonlightYou have successfully rescued Avorthal and recovered the boxes of treasure stolen from the Longbeards by the Dourhands.Talk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony'It is good you are here, friend. Help is needed urgently in Ered Luin. Avorthal, son of Cardavor, the Lord of Celondim is the prisoner of Dourhand dwarves. It appears they plan to take him north by ship, destined for an unknown port. The ship expected to transport him is called the "Irestone" and is moored in the port-city of Kheledûl.

'While you are in Kheledûl, the Dourhands possess many treasures stolen from the Longbeards during the years of their occupation in Thorin's Halls. Were you to recover these treasure-boxes for them, Durin's Folk would be forever grateful.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'You must not delay, ${PLAYER}. Avorthal needs to be rescued from the Dourhands before they can set sail.''You have done a great service for both the Elves and the dwarves of Ered Luin. And a greater service for Avorthal! Thank you for all that you have done.'As the War of Three Peaks drew near its end, the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ suffered a sudden, terrible setback. Before the final effort is made to breach the gates of Gundabad, the dwarves must resist falling to despair and overcome their doubts.Your mission is to raise the spirits of disheartened soldiers of the Gabil'akkâ at Zarkul-sulûn and help them to overcome thoughts of despair.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath and travel to Zarkul-sulûn.Complete 'Mission: Respite in Zarkul-sulûn'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath at Akrâz-zahar.Talk to Vorthur Smokebreath'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'After Hrímil Frost-heart sealed the gates of Mount Gundabad, the victory we sought was stolen from us! Prince Durin has handled himself in the manner of his station, but I know he feels this setback as keenly as any other dwarf. Some of the soldiers at Zarkul-sulûn have begun to doubt in our cause and they might soon fall to despair. You are a storied ${CLASS}, so I am told. Will you speak to them on behalf of the Prince?

'Travel to Zarkul-sulûn and do what you can to ease the minds of our soldiers.'As the War of Three Peaks drew near its end, the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ suffered a sudden, terrible setback. Before the final effort is made to breach the gates of Gundabad, the dwarves must resist falling to despair and overcome their doubts.

Your mission is to raise the spirits of disheartened soldiers of the Gabil'akkâ at Zarkul-sulûn and help them to overcome thoughts of despair.'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.

'Hrímil may have slowed us down, but victory will still be ours!'You have been tasked with destroying the Angmarim ritual at Dûn Traikh.Your mission is to destroy the Angmarim ritual at Dûn Traikh.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Dûn Traikh.Complete Mission: Ritual of SacrificeThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from Dûn Traikh. They have seen a terrible ritual taking place within the Angmarim fortress. Had my scouts more time, they would have disrupted the Angmarim there. Instead, they came across three fell spirits that prevented them from getting closer.

'Dûn Traikh is a deadly fortress and is not a place to tread lightly!''Far from Angmar, upon the Gates of Gundabad, the Iron Crown keep watch over Elderslade as they seek to hold on to power in Gundabad….

'Your mission is to destroy the Angmarim ritual at Dûn Traikh.''Well done! With the ritual destroyed, we should be able to launch another assault against Dûn Traikh soon enough!'Têsegi is worried for a caravan that is heading eastward to Zajâna and has asked you to check on them.Your mission is to go eastward on the road to Zajâna and see to the safety of a trade caravan travelling that road.

Talk to Têsegi when you are ready to travel.Complete Mission: Robbers on the RoadYou have completed your mission of ensuring the safety of the caravan. Return with the Temámir scout to report your success.Talk to Têsegi Jiret-menêsh'The roads through An Shêru are fraught with dangers of all kinds. A trade caravan left Jiret-menêsh bound for Zajâna, and I worry for them. They only had two guards! That is hardly enough to fend off animal attacks, much less the robbers that prey upon the unprepared.

'Would you mind checking the road eastward? I feel that they are more likely than not to run afoul of robbers on the road.''Your mission is to go eastward on the road to Zajâna and see to the safety of a trade caravan travelling that road.''I heard there was a run-in with some robbers? I am glad you were able to get there in time! Lives were saved, and the caravan has made it safely to Kighân. Thank you for all of your help.'The Emax Dûl guard barracks still house many entrenched forces that pose a threat to the ongoing resistance.  Enter into the barracks, destroy any fortifications, and rout the forces within.Your mission is to enter into the guard barracks, destroy any of the barricades found within, and defeat their captain.Complete Mission: Routing ReinforcementsYou have secured the needed weapons for our resistance.Speak with Shâpar in Ahaba'We have cornered an Ordâkhai leader on the western side of Emax Dûl, but they are attempting to fortify their position. Our scouts tell me they have constructed barricades to deter our advance, and are attempting to rally their forces for counter attack.

'We have an opportunity to take them by surprise, and pull this counter assault by the root. If you are willing to accompany me, we two can put an end to this upstart before they rise.''Your mission is to enter into the guard barracks, destroy any of the barricades found within, and defeat their captain.''Thank you for securing the barracks and giving us access to a wide array of weaponry.'Deep within Wyrmsgráf, the remains of countless dwarves lay strewn through Scatha's larder of old.Your mission is to recover the scavenged remains of dwarves that met their ends in Scatha's Larder.

You should talk to Ausma and travel to Scatha's Larder.Complete 'Mission: Scatha's Legacy'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Ausma for your reward.Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have just returned from Wyrmsgráf. Among the countless bones and dead in Scatha's larder, they discovered the mouldering remains of several dwarves. From what I have been told, I can only surmise that they long ago fell victim to Scatha the Worm, but that is no place for the bones of a dwarf to rest!

'You are to travel to Scatha's larder in Wyrmsgráf and reclaim the bones of fallen dwarves! Let them be laid to rest among the honoured dead!'Deep within Wyrmsgráf, there lies a great larder which once belonged to Scatha the Worm. Long lost to the Dwarves of the North, the time has come to reclaim the remains of their ancestors from Scatha.

Your mission is to recover the scavenged remains of dwarves that met their ends in Scatha's Larder.'You have my truest thanks, ${PLAYER}.

'Too long have these dwarves been kept by the dragons of Ered Mithrin. May they at last come to rest among the bones of their own kin.'You have been tasked with mining ore from the Frostdelf in the halls of Thikil-gundu.Your mission is to mine the Frostdelf.

Speak to Hórin to travel to the Frostdelf.Complete Mission: Secrets of the FrostdelfThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the Steel Keep. They have found a gap in the walls which leads to the Frostdelf. Had my scouts more time, they would have mined the cavern and gathered mineral samples. We must return to properly survey the abandoned passage.

'The Frostdelf is but unexplored and could still be rich in minerals!'Within the halls of Thikil-gundu, hidden riches await excavation from the darkest corners….

Your mission is to mine the Frostdelf.'Well done! With these samples, we should be able to assess the Frostdelf for a future mining expedition. We may need to better clear the cavern of those strange drakes first though!'The Barkhûshim are attacking Kûr Anzar! Your mission is to destroy their makeshift fortifications and repel them from Kûr Anzar.The Barkhûshim are attacking Kûr Anzar! Your mission is to destroy their makeshift fortifications and repel them from the lower ward of Kûr Anzar.

Speak to Udlanu to travel.Complete Mission: Securing Kûr AnzarYou have successfully repelled the assault by the vile Barkhûshim! Return with the scout to Udlanu in Urmâkh with this report.Speak with Udlanu in Urmâkh'Our scouts just sent word - we are being attacked! Kûr Anzar is under assault from All-seeing forces eager to reclaim her. We must go at once to Kûr Anzar's aid. For the Queen!''Quickly! We must aid Kûr Anzar in her hour of need!''Thank you for your valour on the battlefield this day. Kûr Anzar and all of Renewed Hamât owes you a debt for all you did to repel the Barkhûshim invaders.'Scouts have reported that a ship carrying weapons and supplies destined for the Heirs of Castamir has recently sunk, and the cargo is washing ashore in the Shield Isles. You have been tasked with collecting the salvageable supplies to keep them out of the hands of the Heirs of Castamir.A ship carrying weapons and supplies has been destroyed on the rocks in the Shield Isles and the cargo is washing ashore. Collect the salvageable supplies to keep them out of the hands of the Heirs of Castamir.

Speak to Malthak to travel.Complete Mission: Securing SalvageYou have collected the salvageable supplies and dealt with the Heirs of Castamir. Return to Malthak in the Bloody Eagle Tavern to report your success.Talk to Malthak'${PLAYER}, a scout has reported that a ship carrying weapons and supplies destined for the Heirs of Castamir has fallen victim to Shedax Khîn, the Grinding Jaws. The ship has broken up, and the cargo is washing ashore. Hurry to Zîrar Tarka and collect the salvageable supplies before the Heirs can recover it. We do not want these items falling into their hands.''Hurry, ${PLAYER}. You must keep the supplies out of enemy hands. We do not want the Heirs of Castamir to be better equipped than they already are. Go to the Shield Isles and collect the salvageable supplies before they do.''Many thanks ${PLAYER}! You have done the good people of Umbar a great service. We have the supplies and the Heirs do not! You also taught them a lesson they will not soon forget.'Despite the failure of the Iron Garrison, the dwarves will not allow the Orcs of Khazad-dûm to spill forth into Azanulbizar, the Dimrill Dale.Your mission is to secure the Redhorn Pass.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath and travel to the Dimrill Dale.Complete 'Mission: Securing the Redhorn'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath at Akrâz-zahar.Talk to Vorthur Smokebreath'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Our scouts in the Dimrill Dale have discovered a small band of Orcs and goblins camped upon the Redhorn Pass. I do not know if they mean to join with Gorgar and his ilk in Gundabad or simply harry the folk of the vales, but we cannot allow them to overrun the pass!

'You are to travel to the Dimrill Dale and secure the Redhorn Pass!'Despite the failure of the Iron Garrison, the dwarves will not allow the Orcs of Khazad-dûm to spill forth into Azanulbizar, the Dimrill Dale.

Your mission is to secure the Redhorn Pass.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'I am pleased that the Redhorn Pass will remain clear of foes as we prepared to march on Gundabad once more!'You have been tasked with defeating the Servants of Throkhâr and destroying their nameless shrines deep within Gundabad.Your mission is to defeat the Servants of Throkhâr and destroy their nameless shrines deep within Gundabad.

Speak to Hórin to travel.Complete Mission: Servants of ThrokhârThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have recently explored some of the deeper recesses of Gundabad. There they have encountered a series of tunnels connecting Gundabad to the realm of the nameless things. While the nameless under Gundabad are not near the numbers plaguing Moria, they too must be dealt with. Who can say what unspeakable things are down there?

'You are to travel to this nameless shrine and destroy what lurks deep under the mountain. For Gundabad!''Deep under the Three Peaks of Gundabad, nameless things have constructed a shrine to Throkhâr The Hunger, their lord….

'Your mission is to defeat the Servants of Throkhâr and destroy their nameless shrines deep within Gundabad.''It is done?

'I am glad. The Frost-horde is numerous, and our victory is not assured if ye must also contest with great enemies below us as well!'Something is lurking among the ruins along the banks of the Greyflood, and you have been asked to investigate.Speak with the mission giver and let them know that you are ready to investigate the ruins along the banks of the Greyflood.Complete the Mission: Shadows in the GreyfloodWith your mission in the ruins successful, you should return to the mission giver and tell them of your findings.Return to Hithriel and tell him of your findings'There's something sinister lurking upon the banks of the Greyflood. A scout reported strange flickering fires among the drowned ruins at the edge of the marshes, and dark apparitions beneath the water's surface. If my fears are true, then some dark magic has taken hold in that place, possibly through some artifice of the Enemy.'

'See if you can find these apparitions, and gain some sense of the foe that lurks here.''Be careful ${PLAYER}. We cannot be certain what lurks in those waters.''You have done well ${PLAYER}. As agreed, you are deserving of payment. Take this and know that we are grateful for all you have done.'You have been tasked with investigating what happened in the Shedax Khîn in the Shield Isles, and to rescue any trapped sailors.Your mission is to investigate what happened in the Shedax Khîn in the Shield Isles, and rescue any trapped sailors.

Speak to Deshra to travel.Complete Mission: Ship of WraithsYou have defeated the dead and rescued the prisoners! Return with the Umbari scout to the mission giver with this report.'Always good to see you, ${PLAYER}. We have just received a disturbing report. A prominent Umbari noble has vanished during a routine trip to Shedax Khîn in the Shield Isles, near an isle where it's rumoured the dead walk freely. Please, we need your help. Investigate and rescue any trapped sailors.''Your objective is clear, ${PLAYER}, investigate what happened in the Shedax Khîn in the Shield Isles, and rescue any trapped sailors. The hopes of the vanished crew rest with you.''Well that is quite the story. I am so glad you were there to take on the dead and ensure the crew's safety. Thank you for everything you've done.'You have been tasked with protecting the Elves left to guard the entrance to The Rift.Your mission is to protect the Elves left to guard the entrance to The Rift.

Speak to Hórin to travel.Complete Mission: Siege of the RiftThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the Iron Pass where they have received a plea for assistance. It would seem a small band of Elves still hold on to a watch-tower overlooking The Rift in Angmar. My scouts were told not to stray too far afield. Instead, they reported back to me immediately about the Elves. I believe if you leave now, you will still be able to offer this small band of Elves the assistance they require.

'The Rift is but one of the paths that can lead to Gundabad from Angmar. It is important that we protect Gundabad from further attacks by the Iron Crown!''In the far eastern edges of Angmar lies The Rift. The passage through the mountains there is one of few that the Iron Crown has taken to the slopes of Gundabad….

'Your mission is to protect the Elves left to guard the entrance to The Rift.''Well done! With The Rift still under guard, may we experience fewer troubles out of Angmar!'You have been tasked with dispatching Maukhuk, one of the sons of the warg chieftain, Ránulur.Your mission is to find and defeat Maukhuk, a fearsome warg pack-leader.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Shathur-munzu.Complete Mission: Son of the ChieftainThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Shathur-munzu, the abandoned fort in Duskenvale, had been quiet since the departure of the warg chieftain, but the scouts have reported seeing wargs hunting in the forest nearby. Some of the prints they have found suggest a large pack-leader may be inside; perhaps a son of Ránulur himself! We cannot allow the wargs to regain a foothold to the south!''Well done! Though the great prize of Gundabad stands in front of us, we must remember to also protect our rear!'The Orcs and Wargs have returned to Shathur-munzu, attempting to set up a new base south of the warfront….

Your mission is to find and defeat Maukhuk, a fearsome warg pack-leader.The Temámir of Jiret-menêsh want to know what has caused the dead to rise in the crypts of Gadim-ûn.Your mission is to search the Crypts of Gadim-ûn for the source of the evil that has caused the dead to rise.

Talk to Têsegi when you are ready to travel.Complete Mission: Song of RestYou have determined the source of the evil that has caused the dead to rise in the Crypts of Gadim-ûn. Return with the Temámir scout to report your success.Talk to Têsegi Jiret-menêsh'The Jatsakóri of Gadim-ûn grow worried about the Dead that walk the halls beneath their lair. We want to send someone capable and unafraid into the crypts to look for the source of what is causing them to rise. Would you go there and look for a sign of what evil dwells within?''Your mission is to search the Crypts of Gadim-ûn for the source of the evil that has caused the dead to rise.''A ghostly voice called the Ishími causes the dead to rise? I have never heard this voice myself, and I am glad for it! Thank you for venturing into such a foul place, ${PLAYER}, you are worthy of your reputation.'The workers at the quarry in Scary have broken into a hidden chamber containing a nest of spiders, and the creatures have now overrun the whole quarry.Monstrous spiders have taken over the quarry in Scary. You have been asked to help deal with the problem before the spiders have the chance to move on the town.Complete Mission: Spiders in the QuarryYou have defeated the spiders that flooded into the Scary quarry. You should talk to the Hooded Stranger about your reward.Talk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony'Workers at a quarry in the Shire broke through into a hidden chamber and released a swarm of spiders. The hobbits in Scary are rather concerned about this turn of events, and I can't blame them. Would you be willing to go to the quarry and help the residents of Scary? The infestation must be contained before the spiders move from the quarry into Scary itself.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'I doubt the hobbits of Shire will be able to handle such foes on their own. If you are ready for a fight, there is no time to lose!''I am pleased to hear that you successfully dealt with the spiders in the quarry! It would not surprise me if they were to return, but you've done what you can for now.'Despite the failure of the Iron Garrison, the dwarves will not allow the Orcs of Khazad-dûm to spill forth into Azanulbizar, the Dimrill Dale.Your mission is to defeat Orcs in the Dimrill Dale and plant banners of the Gabil'akkâ upon them.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath and travel to the Dimrill Dale.Complete 'Mission: Standards of Khazad-dûm'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath at Akrâz-zahar.Talk to Vorthur Smokebreath'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Our scouts have sighted a greater number of Orcs patrolling beyond the East-gate and down into the Dimrill Dale. We fight this day for Gundabad, but the time will soon come to return to Khazad-dûm and drive every last Orc from its halls! That is the promise of the Kharum-ubnâr!

'You are to travel to the Dimrill Dale at once and plant our banners upon every Orc you slay!'Despite the failure of the Iron Garrison, the dwarves will not allow the Orcs of Khazad-dûm to spill forth into Azanulbizar, the Dimrill Dale.

Your mission is to defeat Orcs in the Dimrill Dale and plant banners of the Gabil'akkâ upon them.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'There is only one sort of message an Orc will understand, and you have delivered it!'You have been tasked with defeating Frost-horde drake emissaries and destroying Angmarim coffers.You have been tasked with defeating Frost-horde drake emissaries and destroying Angmarim coffers.

Speak to Ausma to travel to the Drearspire.Complete Mission: Stepping into the DrearspireThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the towers known as the Drearspire. Several drakes were sighted in the area, and the Angmarim were seen transporting several treasure-laden coffers.

'Climb the tower, defeat Frost-horde drake emissaries and destroy Angmarim coffers!''Frost-horde drake emissaries have begun to claim the Drearspire as their own. Angmarim have also been seen with overflowing coffers following the arrival of these foul creatures.

'Your mission is to defeat Frost-horde drake emissaries and destroy Angmarim coffers.''Well done! With the drakes defeated and the coffers destroyed, the foundation has been laid for our work in Gundabad!'You have been tasked with retrieving the sulphurous secretions of gredbyg.Your mission is to retrieve grodbog mucous and poison glands from within the grodbog hive.

Speak to Ausma to travel to the grodbog hive.Complete Mission: Sting Like a GrodbogThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'Oh ${PLAYER}, you're back.

'We’ve been having a bit of a problem getting into some of the more resilient parts of the mountain recently. The blasting supplies we’ve brought over don’t seem to be cutting it against the frozen rock.

'However… one of our scouts has reported a rather large grodbog hive nearby. As you may not know, even though they are venomous, gredbyg secrete a nasty-smelling mucous that’s a great component for making explosives. You see what I’m getting at here? If you could infiltrate the hive and steal some of their mucous and glands, I would be very grateful!''Apparently gredbyg secrete both a sulphurous mucous and have powerful poison glands that can be repurposed into blasting jelly.

'Your mission is to explore the grodbog hive and extract these resources.''Well done! With a bit of dwarf-muscle, we can use these nasty-smelling secretions to make even stronger blasting jelly.'Reports have reached the scouts across Cardolan of evil rising from the ruins in south Gorthad, and you have been asked to investigate.Speak with the mission giver and let them know that you are ready to investigate the ruins.Complete the Mission: Stirring of SpiritsWith your mission in the ruins successful, you should return to the mission giver and tell them of your findings.Return to the mission giver and tell them of your findings'Fell news from the southern ruins of Gorthad, ${PLAYER}. Those with the will to travel and ability to resist the beckoning of the ghostly lights speak of spirits menacing the ruins.

'Many of those who venture by these ruins in the night are never seen again. If you are willing, then we shall see you paid for your efforts there.

'What say you, ${PLAYER}?''Be careful ${PLAYER}, there is an evil in those ruins that must be destroyed.''What manner of ill-tidings is this? Gaunt-men stirring the sleeping dead from their slumber in order to terrorize the countryside. We must be diligent in our efforts, or more citizens will be lost to the darkness spreading hereabout.

'You have done well ${PLAYER}, as agreed, you are deserving of payment. Take this and know that we are grateful for all you have done.'You have been tasked with defeating the dreaded two-headed troll Stûg-and-Zar.You have been tasked with defeating the dreaded two-headed troll Stûg-and-Zar.

