Talk to Têsegi when you are ready to travel.Complete Mission: The Flames of ResistanceYou have completed your mission of setting the tents and banners at Onabóha on fire. Return with the Temámir scout to report your success.Talk to Têsegi Jiret-menêsh'The Ordâkhai encampment at Onabóha is too close to Jiret-menêsh. We need to do something to drive them out. Perhaps if you went there and set their tents aflame, they might go elsewhere. Burning their banners would make a strong statement also, don't you think?''Your mission is to go to Onabóha and set the Ordâkhai tents and banners on fire.''The deed is done? Thank you! Even if it does not cause them to withdraw, it will thwart whatever it is they aim to do there.'You have been tasked with defeating ukhrâsh and plugging leaks in Gundabad.Your mission is to defeat ukhrâsh and plug leaks in Gundabad.

Speak to Ausma to travel.Complete Mission: The Flooded DepthsThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Some workers have just returned from Shalakâm where they were to make repairs to the tunnels, and it seems they only narrowly escaped a horde of ukhrâsh! It does not surprise me that beasts would roam the ancient, flooded waterways of Gundabad. What surprises me is the shear number of these beasts!

'You are to travel to Shalakâm, clear the waterways of the ukhrâsh, and help with the repairs! For Gundabad!''Within Shalakâm, the ancient waterways of Gundabad, the ukhrâsh have roamed unchecked. Their years of clawing and digging threaten to collapse the ancient tunnels….

'Your mission is to defeat ukhrâsh and plug leaks in Gundabad.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}!

'With the ukhrash horde defeated and repairs to the waterways underway, I hope to see the old tunnels restored and safe again soon. If the ukhrâsh return, we will be ready for them!'You have been tasked with collecting gears and redirecting the flow of water within the dwarf-made waterways of Shalakâm.Your mission is to collect gears and redirect the flow water within the dwarf-made waterways of Shalakâm.

