'To the west of Urmâkh is a place known as Shakhdag. There you will find many boar, both healthy and afflicted. Please, bring back boar slabs from the healthy boar, and cull the diseased boar from the sounder, for the good of them all.''Your mission is clear, ${PLAYER}, to acquire healthy boar slabs and cull any diseased boar you encounter.''Wow, that is quite the bounty. Our chef will be overjoyed. Thank you for culling the sounder, it is important we keep the forests safe for our people. And, most importantly, you brought back so much boar. Truth be told, bacon just makes me happy.'You have been tasked with finding a great treasure somewhere in Goblin-town.Your mission is to find a great treasure somewhere in Goblin-town.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Goblin-town.Complete Mission: The Great Goblin's TreasureThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'The scouts keeping watch on Goblin-town have returned with interesting news. There is rumour circulating among the goblins of their king's lost treasure. It seems when the previous Great Goblin was dispatched by the Great Eagle, the knowledge of where this treasure was hidden died with him! Hah! Well his loss is our gain! Get in there and find it!''What once was lost has now been found! Quite the haul, even for goblins! Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. I will make sure this is added to the war coffers and put to good use.'Goblin-town has long been a thorn in the side of the free peoples in Rhovanion. Once again, the goblin horde inside stirs….

Your mission is to find the Great Goblin's treasure somewhere in Goblin-town.After a bloody battle, Gorgar's forces have overrun Grálinvarth. They must be defeated before the forces of Gundabad can gain a significant foothold deep within the territory of the dwarves.Your mission is to defeat the Hand of Gorgar and reclaim Grálinvarth.

You should talk to Ausma and travel to Grálinvarth.Complete 'Mission: The Hand of Gorgar'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Ausma for your reward.Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have brought grave news from Grálinvarth. Gorgar's forces have seized our watch-post for their own and slain our warriors to the last. I am told that one of the Hands of Gorgar, Gorgar's most vicious enforcers, led the attack at Grálinvarth.

'You are to travel to Grálinvarth and deliver the vengeance of the Gabil'akkâ. Slay Gorgar's forces to the last and reclaim what was taken from us! For the Gabil'akkâ!'Rising into the Grey Mountains above the Greylin, Grálinvarth overlooks Elderslade. After a bloody battle, Gorgar's forces have overrun the foothold and gained a significant foothold deep within the territory of the dwarves.

Your mission is to defeat the Hand of Gorgar and reclaim Grálinvarth.'I am glad you have returned no worse for the wear, ${PLAYER}.

'The Hands of Gorgar are mighty, indeed, but it seems even they prove no match for you. You have my thanks!'A Dourhand expedition has descended into the newly-drained depths of Kidzul-kâlah, seeking to claim its riches for their own.Your mission is to defeat Rúnar Wolfstooth and put an end to the Dourhand expedition into the depths of Kidzul-kâlah.

You should talk to Ausma and travel to Kidzul-kâlah.Complete 'Mission: The Heart of Kidzul-kâlah'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Ausma for your reward.Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have sent urgent word from Kidzul-kâlah. From what I am told, the lower reaches of its mines were long ago flooded by the waters of the Gladdenmere. By some providence, the waters have receded and in so doing, it exposed countless deposits of gold and silver. It seems a company of Dourhands led by one called Rúnar Wolfstooth has descended into the depths of Kidzul-kâlah to claim the veins for themselves. This cannot be allowed to pass!

'You are to travel to Kidzul-kâlah at once and put a stop to Rúnar Wolfstooth's plans. For the Gabil'akkâ!'Nestled in the foothills of the Misty Mountains, the dwarf-keep of Kidzul-kâlah lies half-sunken in the Gladdenmere. Deep in its newly-drained depths, the Dourhands seek to mine the veins of the Goldencleft....

Your mission is to defeat Rúnar Wolfstooth and put an end to the Dourhand expedition into the depths of Kidzul-kâlah.'You have done well, ${PLAYER}!

'Those Dourhands are truly a dishonourable sort. To delve the earth without fear for any danger is a coward's way!'You have been tasked with thwarting a group of Dourhand treasure hunters at High Sundergrót.Your mission is to thwart a group of Dourhand treasure hunters at High Sundergrót.

Speak to Hórin to travel to High Sundergrót.Complete Mission: The High DigThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from High Sundergrót. The old ruins run amok with Dourhands! Those dwarves have no sense of honour and will cause nothing but trouble. We must put a stop to their treasure seeking efforts.

'If the Dourhands have nowhere to seek treasure, then perhaps they will leave these mountains for good!'Dourhands have found High Sundergrót and seek what treasures they can find from the old dwarf ruins….

Your mission is to thwart a group of Dourhand treasure hunters at High Sundergrót.'Well done! With those Dourhands defeated, High Sundergrót is once again safe. Perhaps it is time to plead for more dwarves to guard the old ruins, for High Sundergrót is a place rich in dwarf-history and must be protected.'You have been tasked with hunting for meats to feed the war efforts.Your mission is to hunt in the wilds and gather meat.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Misthallow.Complete Mission: The Hunting GroundsThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'The effort that we all have provided takes its strain on our provisions. I worry that our stores will be empty soon! We must head to the wilds of Misthallow and hunt the beasts there for meat!'Meat is needed to feed those in the war efforts….

Your mission is to hunt in the wilds and gather meat.'Well done! With these meats, we will prevail and not starve!'Rescue the trapped dwarf-miners (and their treasure) before the cave permanently collapses!Your mission is to rescue the trapped dwarf-miners (and their treasure) before the cave permanently collapses!

Speak to Deshra to travel.Complete Mission: The Ill-fated CaveYou have rescued the trapped miners and successfully escaped the cave! Return to the mission giver with this report.'It's always good to see you, ${PLAYER}. I have an urgent mission this time. We have just gotten word from one of the Temámir Dwarves that a number of their miners has been trapped in a cave outside Rakhatâb, on the Cape of Umbar. Locals call it the Jid Phêsi, the cavern of whispers. There are reports they found a treasure of great beauty and cost. If you are able, please rescue both the dwarves and this treasure. Please, there is no time to lose! Rescue them before the cave further collapses!''${PLAYER}, please, rescue the trapped miners! And if you can, whatever treasure they were excavating. Quickly, there's not a moment to lose!''That is a beautiful piece. I am glad you were able to rescue it, it will aid in the rebuilding efforts. What? Oh yes, the miners too, of course. I'm so glad they made it out with their lives.'We still know little about the Tarsâri, those who call themselves the Tasked Ones. Investigate the Blade-horn and return with what knowledge you have gathered about the Tarsâri.Your mission is to investigate Bâdrasag, the Blade-horn, for information about the Tarsâri, those who call themselves the Tasked Ones.

Speak to Jôrlar to travel.Complete Mission: The Knife's SecretYou have explored the Blade-horn and found several texts detailing the history of the Tarsâri, though some information is missing. Return with the scout to Jôrlar in Zajâna with this report.Speak with Jôrlar in Zajâna'There is still much we do not know about the Tarsâri, those who call themselves Tasked Ones.

'They operate in secret here in Zajâna, and control much from the shadows. The Doorwards have asked me to gather more information about them.

'Rumours say that the Blade-horn in the north is one of their haunts. Please, investigate the Blade-horn, and return with what information you find. They have operated for too long in the shadows, but we must bring light to the Tarsâri, or it could be our backs they stab next.''Explore the Blade-horn, but keep a wary eye. These Tarsâri are likely to jealously guard their secrets.''A missing book, eh? Still, this is more than we knew this morning about the Tarsâri. I will see this is given to the Master of Secrets straight away.'After escaping the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu, some of the surviving Ghâshfra found their way to Mount Gundabad where their mastery of flame has established them as powerful allies of Gorgar the Ruthless.Your mission is to defeat Draupush, one of the Ghâshfra in service to Gorgar the Ruthless.

You should talk to Hórin and travel to Ashmâr-zarakh.Complete 'Mission: The Last Embers of Nûrz Ghâshu'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have just returned from Ashmâr-zarakh with troubling news. It seems Gorgar has allowed some strange Orcs into his ranks, chief among them one of the Ghâshfra clan of Angmar. If the stories I heard of the Ghâshfra bear any truth, we have much to fear from this alliance.

'You must go to Ashmâr-zarakh and find the Orc known as Draupush. Defeat him and douse the last embers of Nûrz Ghâshu! For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!'In the armoury of Ashmâr-zarakh, the Orcs of Gundabad make ready their weapons of war. Rumours speak of an Orc of Angmar drawn into Gorgar's service….

Your mission is to defeat Draupush, one of the Ghâshfra in service to Gorgar the Ruthless.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'I have heard tales of the Ghâshfra of Angmar, but you have faced them in battle and lived to tell the tale. Let us hope Gorgar does not hide so many other surprises within Gundabad!'You have been tasked with finding a way into a recently uncovered dwarf-vault in Gundabad.Your mission is to find a way into a recently uncovered dwarf-vault in Gundabad.

Speak to Hórin to travel.Complete Mission: The Lost VaultThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have just recently uncovered a lost treasure vault. The ancient treasure hoard is sealed and untouched. What puzzles the dwarves who discovered it is there seems to be no way to open the vault.

'I ask you to travel to the vault of Agbash-khalt and find a way to open the vault. We cannot allow Agbash-khalt to be discovered and plundered by anyone else! For Gundabad!'Behold! The vault of Agbash-khalt, sealed and hidden to all those who have occupied Gundabad, has now finally revealed itself to the Zhélruka Dwarves….

Your mission is to find a way into a recently uncovered dwarf-vault in Gundabad.'The vault has been opened?! With our scouts guarding Agbash-khalt, we will soon find out what treasures lie within!

'You have done well, ${PLAYER}.'Prince Durin knows the forces of the dwarves are outnumbered by the Orcs, but Scout-master Ausma needs to know more.Speak to Scout-master Ausma in the War Room on the upper floor Annâk-khurfu.Talk to AusmaYour mission is to scout the main gates of Gundabad with Ausma.

Talk to Ausma in Annâk-khurfu to enter this mission.Complete Mission: The Main GatesYour mission has been completed.

You should talk to Ausma in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to AusmaTalk to Glóin'I hope you are ready, ${PLAYER}, because I will be putting you to work right away! Your first mission will be to scout the main gates of Gundabad itself, but do not worry. I will not be sending you alone. Go and speak with our Scout-master, Ausma. She will be accompanying you into enemy territory.''A pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}. I am Ausma of the Stout-axe clan. The Longbeard prince has named me Scout-master of his army. This was a wise decision, I think, for I possess some skills that the Longbeards and Zhélruka do not. A harsh life in Mordor required those of my clan to learn how to evade the notice of our captors, and of course...'

In a flash, there is a dagger inches from your throat. Ausma grins, and hides the dagger away again.

'...how to conceal our weapons and strike without warning. You may think that is not an "honourable" way to fight, and maybe you are correct, but slaves do not have such luxury. To my people, there was only survival, and the use of such skills proved necessary. If the prince would like me to use my skills to remove the foul Orcs from such a sacred site of his people, I am happy to oblige. And you, ${PLAYER}, will help me in this. Let us begin.'

She points to Gundabad on the large map on the table in front of you.

'Our prize is heavily fortified and swarming with Orcs, trolls, and wargs of all kinds. We will wait until night, slip past their patrols, and see it with our own eyes. The first step of any strategy? The gathering of intelligence. We depart at dusk.'The gates of Gundabad are heavily fortified. Only by approaching with stealth will you remain unseen....

Your mission is to scout the main gates of Gundabad with Ausma.'I will leave you to report our findings to Commander Glóin. It seems the prince's fears about our enemy's strength were well-founded. I will begin planning scouting missions with Hórin, representative of the Zhélruka clan. I hope you are prepared for the amount of work ahead of us!'You tell Glóin of the massive Orc presence and fortifications at the gates of Gundabad.

'It is as we feared. This promises to be not a simple clash, but a lengthy siege! We must make preparations to prevent an overwhelming defeat on the battlefield and to keep the Orcs from holing up inside the mountains and waiting us out! I ask that you do your part to advance our War Effort. Work with Ausma and Hórin, and slowly, but surely, we will win this war!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete Missions to advance the War Effort!</rgb>The War of the Three Peaks will not be truly over until Gorgar the Ruthless has been defeated.You have been assigned another important mission!

Report to Ausma in Annâk-khurfu to learn the details.Talk to AusmaYour mission is to infiltrate Bekâr-zarakh with Ausma and find Gorgar's location.

Talk to Ausma to travel to Bekâr-zarakh.Complete Mission: The Marked TargetThe mission is complete!

You should talk to Ausma in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to AusmaThe mission is complete!

You should talk to Glóin in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to Glóin'${PLAYER}, you have shown your worth to our cause. I grant you the rank of Fabarâl of the Gabil'akkâ! This is the highest rank I am able to give as your commander. Thank you for all you have done.

'Your efforts have significantly weakened the Orc forces, but we will not have won this war until Gorgar the Ruthless himself lies dead. You may be aware that Ausma has certain... talents... that will aid us in this endeavour. Report to her at once!''There you are, ${PLAYER}. The time to cut the head off this snake has finally come!'

She whips out her dagger, and mimes slicing the head off an Orc, cackling gleefully.

'The prince has given me permission to plan the assassination of our nemesis, Gorgar the Ruthless. Without the son of Bolg, the Orcs and their allies will quickly fall to in-fighting as they try to determine who next gets to be in charge. During the chaos, we can easily mop them up and take our prize: Gundabad!

'But first, we need to find him. We will infiltrate this tower outside Gundabad's main gates.'

She points to a tower on the map, just outside the keep.

'We believe this is where they plan their troop deployments. If Gorgar intends to leave the mountain for any reason, they will deploy a number of guards to keep him safe. And he WILL leave at some point. If Orcs are to be kept in line, they need to see their chieftain in the flesh from time to time. I bet if we snoop around this tower, we will learn when and where Gorgar will next appear. Let me know when you're ready to head out.'To end this war, Gorgar the Ruthless must be defeated. But first, he must be found….

Your mission is to infiltrate Bekâr-zarakh with Ausma and find Gorgar's location.Ausma greets you with a grin.

'We know now where Gorgar is heading next: Goblin-town! I'll prepare a plan of attack, and have the scouts watch the Goblin-gate. When he arrives, we will strike!''I have heard your mission was a success! Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. When next I call upon you, it will be to enter Goblin-town with Ausma and defeat Gorgar the Ruthless. Prepare yourself!'You have been tasked with dispatching a powerful drake in the Clutch-hollow.Your mission is to find and defeat Askónd, Matron of the Hatchery.

Speak to Ausma to travel to the the Clutch-hollow.Complete Mission: The Matron of the HatcheryThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the Wyrmsgráf. They have found what they believe to be a hatchery, where the worms raise their young. They could not get too close, however. It appears the hatchery is protected by a vicious fire-breathing drake! They call her Askónd, the Matron. They barely avoided her wrath and made it out alive!

'We cannot let those eggs hatch! I need you to defeat this Matron of Worms, so my scouts can continue exploring, and so we can dispatch those eggs!''Well done! With the matron defeated, we can press deeper in the Wyrmsgráf and can take care of those eggs! The last thing we need is more worms and drakes in these mountains!'Deep in the Wyrmsgráf, what remains of Scatha's brood makes their den....

Your mission is to infiltrate the Clutch-hollow and defeat Askónd, Matron of the Hatchery.You have been tasked with dispatching a powerful drake in the High Pass.Your mission is to defeat the vile drake matron who guards the High Pass.

Speak to Ausma to travel to the High Pass.Complete Mission: The Matron of the High PassThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the High Pass. They could not get to the Misty Mountains, however. It appears the High Pass is protected by a vicious frost-drake! They call her Slátra. They barely avoided her wrath and made it out alive!

'I need you to defeat this vile frost-drake, so that we can continue scouting the mountains.'Upon the High Pass, a terrible frost drake guards the mountain path….

Your mission is to defeat the vile drake matron who guards the High Pass.'Well done! With the matron defeated, we can continue scouting the mountains surrounding the High Pass. The last thing we need is more drakes in these mountains!'You have been tasked with dispatching a powerful drake who has blockaded the entrance to Thikil-gundu.Your mission is to defeat the frost matron who has blockaded the entrance to the Steel Keep.

Speak to Hórin to travel to the Steel Keep.Complete Mission: The Matron of the KeepThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from the Steel Keep. As they left the ruins behind, a vicious frost-drake Matron blocked the entrance! There is no other way into the Steel Keep! I need you to defeat this Matron, so that we can continue exploring the ruins of Thikil-gundu.'The entrance to Thikil-gundu has been blockaded by a terrible frost drake and her spawn….

Your mission is to defeat the frost matron who has blockaded the entrance to the Steel Keep.'Well done! With the matron defeated, we can return to the Steel Keep, and continue exploring the ruins! We were lucky that my scouts did not get trapped within the walls of Thikil-gundu.'You have been tasked with removing the enemies encamped at the tower ruins of Sutwarden.Your mission is to remove the enemies encamped at the tower ruins of Sutwarden.

Speak to Radhril.Complete Mission: The Menace of SutwardenThe mission is complete!

Speak to Radhril for your reward!Talk to Radhril'Would you accompany me on a mission, ${CLASS}?

'The Free Peoples in the Wildwood have been unable to regain control of the watch-tower ruins of Sutwarden. Those who control the tower have a vantage point to view all of the Wildwood and the Bree-fields.

'If the Wildwood and the Bree-fields are to ever again be safe, the tower of Sutwarden must be reclaimed.'The old Arnorian watch-tower of Sutwarden has attracted many foes of the Free Peoples, who wish to spy upon the Bree-fields.

Your mission is to remove the enemies encamped at the tower ruins of Sutwarden.'We have done well, ${CLASS}. With Sutwarden once again under control of the Free Peoples, both the Bree-fields and the Wildwood are much safer. I am certain the Free Peoples will thank us for our efforts.'You have been tasked with recovering stolen treasure, hidden within Shakal-atrâd.Your mission is to recover stolen treasure, hidden within Shakal-atrâd.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Shakal-atrâd.Complete Mission: The Missing TreasureThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'We have recently excavated lost dwarf-treasure from ruins near Gundabad! While on route here, the treasure was stolen! We believe those who stole the treasure may have hid in the old watch-post of Shakal-atrâd. We must recover that treasure, as it does not contain only valuables, it may contain lost history!'Treasures have been stolen! It is suspected that the items were brought to Shakal-atrâd, in Elderslade, and hidden in the depths of the old watch-tower….

Your mission is to recover stolen treasure, hidden within Shakal-atrâd.'Well done! With the treasure recovered, our lore-masters can study its contents! Perhaps it will shed some light on gaps in Gundabad's history.'The Orcs of Nan Wathren are planning an attack on the Elven village of Lin Giliath, which has yet to recover from an attack by stone-trolls.You have been asked to go to the Orc camp in Nan Wathren and do what you can to disrupt the plans of Drukordh, their Uruk leader who intends to attack the Elven village Lin Giliath while it is vulnerable.Complete Mission: The Orcs of Nan WathrenYour strike on the Orcs of Nan Wathren has successfully brought an end to their plans to raid the Elven village of Lin Giliath. You should talk to Candaith and then give your report to the Hooded Stranger.Talk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony'The Elf-lord Gildor Inglorion of the House of Finrod begs your aid, ${PLAYER}. He is worried for Lin Giliath, a small Elven village in the North Downs, has recently weathered an attack by stone-trolls that has left them short on food and supplies. They have yet to recover and have recently learned that Orcs in Nan Wathren will soon move against them. 

'Scouts report that these Orcs are being led by a great Uruk of Angmar named Drukordh. Perhaps if this Uruk were slain, Lin Giliath would be spared further ruin.

'Were you to strike at Nan Wathren, defeat Drukordh, and dishearten the Orcs there, their plans to further harm Lin Giliath would be undermined.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Have you readied yourself for a fight? Drukordh and the Orcs of Nan Wathren will not go down easily, but their attack on Lin Giliath must be thwarted.''Your actions have done much to protect the Elves at Lin Giliath from further attacks, and likely spared Trestlebridge from their wrath as well. You have truly made a difference for the people of the North Downs.'You have been tasked with finding a great treasure in Sundergrót.Your mission is to find the dwarf-treasure in Sundergrót.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Sundergrót,Complete Mission: The Riches of SundergrótThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'The abandoned mine, Sundergrót, lies to the south of here, in the Floodfells. We have discovered references in some old records of some kind of hidden treasure inside. What kind of dwarf would I be if I ignored a treasure in waiting? Find it, and bring it back here. It will help fund the war effort!'Hórin's eyes gleam as he looks over the treasure.

'Ah, what a sight! It brings a tear to my eye. I will make sure this wealth is added to our war coffers and put to good use. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'The abandoned mines of Sundergrót still hold valuable ore and treasures, ripe for the taking. However, the goblin intruders stand in your way….

Your mission is to find the dwarf-treasure hidden somewhere in Sundergrót.You have been tasked with destroying the Taurogrim corruption that has spread over Óinsbridge.Your mission is to destroy the Taurogrim corruption at Óinsbridge.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Óinsbridge.Complete Mission: The Roots of DecayThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from Óinsbridge. They have found the bridge to be overrun by the Taurogrim. The Taurogrim continue to be pushed from the Mirkwood and have begun taking lands such as the Thornholt!

'We cannot let the Taurogrim corruption to spread over Óinsbridge. We need the bridge to send supplies from Skarháld to Elderslade!'The Taurogrim have taken over Óinsbridge as their corruption spreads out past the Thornholt….

Your mission is to destroy the Taurogrim corruption at Óinsbridge.'Well done! With much of the Taurogrim corruption reduced upon the bridge, we should be able to retake Óinsbridge, and resume sending supplies! I just hope the Taurogrim do not try this fool's errand again!'Amon Firn is occupied by half-orcs. Their leader must be somewhere amongst the ruins. Defeat him!Search Amon Firn for the half-orc captain and defeat him. Speak with the mission giver when you are ready to travel.Complete the Mission: The Ruins of Amon FirnReturn to the mission giver and tell him you defeated the half-orc captain.Return to Baglan and tell him the captain is defeated'Amon Firn is occupied by a half-orc captain and his gang. They are disturbing the spirits in the area. We must defeat this leader and as many half-orcs as we can.''Be careful in the ruins of Amon Firn, ${PLAYER}.''You have done well ${PLAYER}, as agreed, you are deserving of payment. Take this and know that we are grateful for all you have done.'You have been tasked with rescuing Skóthi from the clutches of an Iron Crown ritual.Your mission is to rescue Skóthi from the tower of Caivád Sâr.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Caivád Sâr.Complete Mission: The Sacrificial TowerThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'All but one of my scouts have come back from Caivád Sâr. They have found a fortress of Angmarim there. Skóthi, did not return! They believe that Skóthi is being held captive in the fortress of Caivád Sâr.

'We must attempt a rescue!'Far from Angmar, the last stronghold of the Iron Crown keeps watch over Elderslade for the forces of Gundabad….

Your mission is to rescue Skóthi from the tower of Caivád Sâr.'Well done! I am glad to see Skóthi again! We now know to be extra careful around the fortress of Caivád Sâr, if we are to venture there again.'To win the war, you must prevent the Orcs from fortifying Gundabad for a siege.Scout-master Ausma has the details on your next assignment.

You should talk to her in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to AusmaYour mission is to stop the supply trains in the secret tunnel between Goblin-town and Gundabad.

Talk to Ausma in Annâk-khurfu to begin.Complete Mission: The Secret Supply LineThe mission is complete!

You should talk to Ausma in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to AusmaThe mission is complete!

You should talk to Glóin in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to Glóin'${PLAYER}, for your contribution to the war effort, I hereby grant you the rank of Dumul within the Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves.

'You have helped us tremendously, but this war is far from over! It is time to hit them where it really hurts: their supply lines! Report to Scout-master Ausma at once. She will fill you in on our plans.''There you are, ${PLAYER}. Commander Glóin has charged us with a pressing task. My scouts have discovered a secret tunnel in the Misty Mountains, connecting Goblin-town and Gundabad. We believe they are using it to move supplies into Gundabad to prepare it for a siege. If they still believe we do not know of these supply trains, they may not be heavily guarded. This is the time to strike!

'We will move out when you are ready, but don't take too long or we will miss this opportunity!'Deep in the Misty Mountains, the Orcs and goblins use a secret tunnel to move supplies between Goblin-town and Gundabad....

Your mission is to stop the supply trains in the secret tunnel between Goblin-town and Gundabad.'You do fine work, ${PLAYER}. We have surely set the Orcs back weeks in their efforts to prepare Gundabad for a long siege. You should inform Commander Glóin of our success.'You inform Glóin of the destroyed supply train and blocked tunnel.

'Good to hear, though I am not surprised! I assigned this important mission to you because I knew you would succeed! The Orcs will sorely miss those supplies, but we must keep up the pressure to prevent Gorgar from gaining the upper hand.

'Something about this troubles me, however. It was my understanding that Gundabad lost control of Goblin-town with the death of the Hobgoblin Warlord, Shárnakh. Does this mean a new Great Goblin has come to power, and he has opened diplomatic channels with Gorgar? I will send some scouts to look into the matter. Meanwhile, keep up the fight! This war is far from over!'In the deepest shadows of Valdhellir lies the domain of Drauglok, the mighty pack-leader of the den and one of the eldest Wargs in the Slade.Your mission is to defeat the terrible Warg, Drauglok, in Valdhellir.

You should talk to Hórin and travel to Valdhellir.Complete 'Mission: The Shadow of Valdhellir'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have just returned from Valdhellir, and it seems they only narrowly escaped a particularly keen Warg known to these Longbeards as Drauglok. It does not surprise me that these Longbeards did not put an end to such a threat, but now the task must fall to you. Drauglok can not be allowed to harry our forces any longer, and we cannot risk another ambush in the night.

'You are to travel to Valdhellir and put an end to Drauglok. For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!'Within Valdhellir, the most vicious Wargs of Elderslade dwell in darkness. Drauglok, the leader of this terrible pack, poses a great threat to the Dwarves of Durin's Folk.

Your mission is to defeat the terrible Warg, Drauglok, in Valdhellir.'Excellent work, ${PLAYER}!

'With Drauglok defeated, I hope it will be some time before those Wargs again dare to creep from Valdhellir.'From within Kêr Bréin, a powerful hobgoblin leads the raids on Skarháld and keeps watch on the newly-laid eggs of the Frost-horde.Your mission is to defeat the powerful hobgoblin, Rukhnúl, at Kêr Bréin.

You should talk to Hórin and travel to Kêr Bréin.Complete 'Mission: The Snows of Kêr Bréin'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Hórin for your reward.Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have returned from Kêr Bréin with troubling news. As we feared, the Frost-horde has overtaken the ruins and has begun to use it as a means to launch attacks on our forces in Ered Mithrin. We have learned that the leader of these forces is a hobgoblin frost-caller known as Rukhnúl.

'You are to travel to Kêr Bréin and put a stop to Rukhnúl before the Frost-horde can regain a stronger foothold in Ered Mithrin. Go! For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!'Although it once served as a camp of the Ungoledain, Kêr Bréin has fallen to the Frost-horde. From within its ruined walls, a powerful hobgoblin leads the raids on Skarháld and keeps watch on the newly-laid eggs of the Frost-horde.

Your mission is to defeat the powerful hobgoblin, Rukhnúl, at Kêr Bréin.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'With Rukhnúl vanquished, we need not fear continued attacks from the Frost-horde in Ered Mithrin.'You have been tasked with defeating the Angmarim sorceress and retrieving an ancient text.Your mission is to defeat the Angmarim sorceress and retrieve an ancient text from Tûr Ágal.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Tûr Ágal.Complete Mission: The Sorceress of Tûr ÁgalThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have returned from Tûr Ágal. An Angmarim sorceress has taken refuge within the top of the tower there. This can not stand! We must return to Tûr Ágal and put a stop to what ever this vile Calaminag has planned! If the reports are indeed true, Calaminag is another student of shadowy Galachán.''Within the walls of Tûr Ágal, in Elderslade, an Angmarim sorceress has overtaken the tower for unknown and nefarious purposes….

'Your mission is to defeat the Angmarim sorceress and retrieve an ancient text from Tûr Ágal.''Well done! With Calaminag defeated, Tûr Ágal should no longer be a threat to the Dwarves of Gundabad. If we are to keep the road to Gundabad clear, Tûr Ágal must remain clear of foes. I do hope this book with assist us in dealing with all the damage caused by Galachán's other student, Brágha Fellwinder.'Your mission is to go to Medân Makhai, harvest deposits of honey, recover the farmers' abandoned tools and defeat the aggressive new queen.Your mission is go to Medân Makhai, recover the stockpiled honey, retrieve the abandoned farmers' tools, and defeat the aggressive new queen.

Speak to Jôrlar to travel.Complete Mission: The Sweetest RewardYou have harvested the forsaken honey, recovered the farmers' tools and defeated the pretender queen.

Return with the scout to Jôrlar in Zajâna with this report.Speak with Jôrlar in Zajâna'The farmers of Sormedan recently came to us with an urgent matter. They can no longer harvest honey from the caves of Medân Makhai. Many here in Zajâna depend on them for the harvest. The farmers tell a strange tale.

'They say that recently a new dark queen installed herself, defeating and exiling the former queen. The farmers found the queen, injured and broken, not far from the caves, and were able to nurse her back to good health. However, they are not warriors - they cannot contend with this new queen or her warrior acolytes.

'Please, help them. They are not warrior folk like yourself. Defeat this new queen and harvest the stockpiled honey, so that the farmers may work with the bees as partners once more.''We are relying on you. Defeat this new dark queen, that our relationship with the bees may be healed and returned to the fruitful partnership that it once was.''It warms my heart to hear it! The farmers will be happy to be able to return to Medân Makhai, and all of Zajâna will be heartened that the supply of honey is once more flowing, a delicious amber river.'Your mission is to journey to the cave of Khatzâla and search for any sign of the missing travellers.Your mission is to explore the cave of Khatzâla for any sign of the missing travellers.

Speak to Jôrlar to travel.Complete Mission: The Talon's ClutchYou have escaped with your life from the giant, monstrous chicken. Return with the scout to Jôrlar in Zajâna with this report.Speak with Jôrlar in Zajâna'There are many dangerous places in Kighân. The cave of Khatzâla is not supposed to be one of them.

'Many visited the cave for its natural beauty, and it was a favourite of wanderers and sight-seers alike. Recently, however, scoundrels and common thieves have begun making it their home.

'A group of travellers from Zajâna were exploring the caves about a week ago. Several of their families came to the Doorwards and expressed concern that their family members had not returned. I fear the brigands there may have roughed them up - or worse.

'Would you explore Khatzâla for any sign of the travellers?''Explore the caves, and if you run into any brigands there, give them no quarter!''A giant chicken? Yes, I think I see one as well.

'That is quite the story - some might say unbelievable, even.'You have been tasked with defeating the Taurogrim in Grazadh-gropor.Your mission is to defeat the Taurogrim in Grazadh-gropor.

Speak to Ausma to travel to Grazadh-gropor.Complete Mission: The Taurogrim AllianceThe mission is complete!

Speak to Ausma for your reward!Talk to Ausma'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Do you know of the Taurogrim? They are fearsome wood-trolls native to Mirkwood, or Eryn Lasgalen as the Elves have renamed it. My scouts have seen a band of Orcs entering one of their lairs, Grazadh-gropor, in Misthallow. I fear this may be Gorgar sending emissaries to rouse the Taurogrim to war! We must not allow this to happen! I task you with entering Grazadh-gropor and defeating the Taurogrim you find there!''Well done! The Men of the Vales will be glad to know they need not fear an ambush from the forest while a war rages in the north, and we dwarves need not fear the Taurogrim's foul magic on the battlefield!'The wood-trolls known as the Taurogrim still haunt much of Eryn Lasgalen. If Gorgar rouses them to battle, they will pose a great threat….

Your mission is to defeat the Taurogrim in Grazadh-gropor.Haudh Nírui has been overrun by grave-robbing goblins. If we defeat their leader we may be able to scare them off for now.Speak with the mission giver. Travel to Haudh Nírui and search for the Blogmal gang-leader. Defeat it and as many goblins as you can to drive them out of the tomb.Complete the Mission: The Tearful TombWith your mission in the ruins successful, you should return to the mission giver and tell him you have defeated the Blogmal gang-leader.Return to the mission giver and tell him you have defeated the Blogmal gang-leader'Somewhere in the depths of Haudh Nírui, the Blogmal gang-leader commands his minions to rob and defile the tombs within. Defeating this menace might be enough to scare off the goblins temporarily.''Be careful in the depths of Haudh Nírui, ${PLAYER}.''You have done well ${PLAYER}, as agreed, you are deserving of payment. Take this and know that we are grateful for all you have done.'You have been tasked with defeating the wardens of Caivád Sâr.Your mission is to defeat the wardens of Caivád Sâr.

