Your mission is to infiltrate the Clutch-hollow and destroy the worm eggs within.Umbari Corsairs are stealing artifacts from the Ambarûli side of Telperiën's Wall.Your mission is to stop thieving Corsairs from stealing artifacts from the ruins of Telperiën's Wall, by any means necessary.

Talk to Khâdamul when you are ready to travel.Complete Mission: Thieves of AntiquityYou have dealt with the thieving Corsairs stealing artifacts from the ruins of Telperiën's Wall. Return with the Dumûri scout to report your success.Talk to Khâdamul in Iridír'A villager was out foraging near Telperiën's Wall and reported seeing Umbari strangers digging for artifacts. These items of antiquity belong to the people of Ambarûl. It is not a free-for-all for outsiders to come and take these things and sell them in foreign lands. Go there and put a stop to this theft by any means necessary.''Your mission is to stop thieving Corsairs from stealing artifacts from the ruins of Telperiën's Wall.''Thank you for stopping these thieves from stealing that which belongs to all of our people.'Robb Thornley has been rescued from the Orcs, battered and beaten, but he is not satisfied with rescue. He wants retribution, particularly against the Orc they call the Red Reaver.You have been given the dangerous task of entering the Tarkrîp encampment and delivering Thornely's revenge upon the Orcs there.Complete Mission: Thornley's RevengeYou have successfully dealt with the Tarkrîp Orcs and the Red Reaver. You should talk to Rose Thornley and then give your report to the Hooded Stranger.Talk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony'A local farmer, Robb Thornley, was recently captured and tortured by a tribe of Orcs from the north, called Tarkrîps. Thornley is now safely back home recovering from his ordeal, but his wife Rose tells us Robb cannot sleep at night, knowing these Orcs are still out there. He must have his revenge on the Tarkrîps and one called the Red Reaver. Would you be the one who can put them to heel?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Tell me when you are ready to deliver Thornley's revenge. Doing this will help more than just the Thornley family sleep at night.''You have done well, my friend. Robb Thornley will finally get some rest, and there are fewer Tarkrîp Orcs to worry the people of Bree-land.'You have been tasked with assisting Rangvald with training dwarves for war at Skarháld.Your mission is to assist Rangvald with training dwarves for war at Skarháld.

