You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath at Akrâz-zahar.Talk to Vorthur Smokebreath'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'After slaying a few unwary Orcs, our scouts in the Dimrill Dale discovered the Orcs of Moria are carrying trinkets belonging to the Dwarves of the Iron Garrison. This is a grave insult, and it will not be borne by me - or any other proud dwarf for that matter!

'You are to travel to the Dimrill Dale and recover these trinkets from the Orcs of Moria!'Despite the failure of the Iron Garrison, the dwarves will not allow the Orcs of Khazad-dûm to spill forth into Azanulbizar, the Dimrill Dale.

Your mission is to recover trinkets stolen from the Dwarves of the Iron Garrison.'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.

'Many dwarves were lost when the Iron Garrison was driven from Moria, and I will not let their efforts... or their sacrifices be forgotten. I shall see that these are returned to their kin at once!'After reclaiming Gabilazan from the Dourhands and their foul allies, the Dwarves of Durin's Folk must now contend with the other inhabitants of the Misty Mountains.Your mission is to repel the meddlesome stone-giant troubling the dwarves at Gabilazan.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath and travel to Gabilazan.Complete 'Mission: Trouble at the High Crag'You have completed your mission.

You should talk to Vorthur Smokebreath at Akrâz-zahar.Talk to Vorthur Smokebreath'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'I have received word that my kinsfolk in the Misty Mountains are dealing with a most unusual problem. It seems another stone-giant down from Iorbar's Peak has taken to propping open the gates of Gabilazan. It seems like some sort of queer game played by the giant and its kind, and though I do not believe it means my folk any real harm, it's letting all sorts of foul beasts and weather in!

'You are to travel to Gabilazan and do what you must to drive off that stone-giant!'After reclaiming Gabilazan from the Dourhands and their foul allies, the Dwarves of Durin's Folk must now contend with the other inhabitants of the Misty Mountains.

Your mission is to repel the meddlesome stone-giant troubling the dwarves at Gabilazan.'Very good, ${PLAYER}!

'Let us hope that giant leaves them alone... at least for a few days!'You have been tasked with crippling the efforts of the Gundabad Orcs who have taken hold of the old armoury in Thikil-gundu.Your mission is to destroy weapon stockpiles guarded by Gundabad Orcs in the Steel Keep.

