Your mission is to guard Trader's Wharf from potential threats.'We have done well, ${CLASS}. With Trader's Wharf still standing from the brigand assault, the League of the Axe will certainly be thankful of our efforts.'The waters of the Greyflood are haunted by tormented spirits. Hithriel believes they must be bound there by some power, which he has sent you to discover.Speak with the mission giver when you are ready to continue your investigation of the Greyflood.Speak with the mission giverHaving discovered a possible source of the disturbance of the Greyflood, you need to return to the mission giver to let him know what you have found.Return to Hithriel and tell him of your findings'So there are indeed troubled spirits in the waters of the Greyflood. What calls them forth? What has bound them to that place? Search further if you can. If some fell power has taken hold there, you must discover it.''Continue your investigation of the Greyflood. Something must be there to draw so many spirits to those waters.''I see. This flame you describe seems deeply foreboding. I do not know who kindled it, or how long it has burned there, but it seems that it draws evil spirits to it, from the depths of the Greyflood.

'It cannot be allowed to burn any longer.'You have been tasked with defeating the two-headed troll, Brog-and-Glûk, at Zarkul-sulûn.Your mission is to defeat the two-headed troll, Brog-and-Glûk, at Zarkul-sulûn.

