'My scouts have returned from Hadnul-zahar. There within the old dwarf halls, trolls have taken hold and protect it as their own. This can not stand! We must return to Hadnul-zahar and show these trolls that Gundabad belongs to the dwarves!''Within the old halls of Hadnul-zahar, in Gundabad, trolls now hold a hall that is essential to our cause….

'Your mission is to uproot the trolls within the hall in Gundabad.''Well done! With the dreadful Ghámgur Tremblestone defeated, and the trolls driven back, the old halls of Hadnul-zahar are once again safe. If we are to reclaim Gundabad, we must find and oust all that oppose us!'Your mission is to investigate Zahûmakh and attempt to find the travellers who vanished.Your mission is to investigate Zahûmakh and attempt to find the travellers who vanished.

Speak to Udlanu to travel.Complete Mission: Vanished in ZahûmakhYou have successfully aided the wounded travellers and fought off the marsh-striders! Return with the scout to Udlanu in Urmâkh with this report.Speak with Udlanu'Hashtal-gûr, ${PLAYER}. A group of travellers set out from Urmâkh to the south to investigate the marsh of Zahûmakh. Now several of their family members have come to us, asking us to locate them, as it's been several days since they've been seen. We had hoped to send several warriors, but the Ordâkhai demand our full attention. Can you investigate this claim? It's probably just a twisted ankle that is slowing their return, but we cannot rule out something more dangerous.

'Please, go to Zahûmakh and search for these travellers or clues to their whereabouts. It would be a great kindness to their families for any news.''Your mission is simple, ${PLAYER}, to journey to Zahûmakh and search for signs of the missing travellers. Good fortune to you!''You found them? That is excellent news. Thank you for your bravery, staving off those marsh-striders. You seem no worse for the fight, if a bit... pungent.'The Temámir of Jiret-menêsh want to know if any relics of Lâkindar of old remain within the Quelling-house.Your mission is to go to the Quelling-house and look for any vestiges of Lâkindar's happier past that can be brought to Jiret-menêsh.

Talk to Têsegi when you are ready to travel.Complete Mission: Vestiges of LâkindarYou have completed your mission of finding vestiges of Lâkindar of old and have brought them back to Jiret-menêsh. Return with the Temámir scout to report your success.Talk to Têsegi in Jiret-menêsh'Before the coming of Men to An Shêru, Lâkindar was wealthy and prosperous. Even those dwarves who were alive before the Din of Stone never saw Lâkindar at the height of its glory.

'I understand that it is a dangerous place to explore, but I cannot help but wonder if there is anything left of Lâkindar's happier past that can be found and brought to Jiret-menêsh? Even something as minor as slag would bring joy to the Temámir whose forefathers hailed from that mine.''Your mission is to go to the Quelling-house and look for any vestiges of Lâkindar's happier past that can be brought to Jiret-menêsh.''It gladdens me to see that you have safely returned to us! I hope to never set foot in that accursed place myself. Did you find anything?

'Oh, look at that.  These are shards of obsidian glass. It cannot be found on the surface of An Shêru. They may have come from trade, but it is more likely that it is from Lâkindar's mines. Though fragile, obsidian blades can be made to have a sharper edge than any steel is capable of. Some crafters also use it as you might use a jewel to decorate jewellery or weapons.

'Thank you for bringing these to us! I will see that families to whom it would mean the most receive these shards. We are honoured to have someone such as yourself helping us.'You have been tasked with clearing out ice walls within the ruins of Stormwall.Your mission is to clear out ice walls within the ruins of Stormwall.

Speak to Hórin to travel to Stormwall.Complete Mission: Wall of IceThe mission is complete!

Speak to Hórin for your reward!Talk to Hórin'I have a new mission for you, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have come back from Stormwall. They have found the old ruins partially encased in ice! Unfortunately, the group was running short on time and supplies, else they would have begun to chisel through the ice. We must return to properly clean up site.

'This can only be the work of the Frost-horde and for that, it can not stand!'Within the ruins of Stormwall, cold-worms have begun building icy walls within the vacant lair of Etterfang….

Your mission is to clear out ice walls within the ruins of Stormwall.'Well done! That should send a message that Stormwall does not belong to the Frost-horde! We may need to return to Stormwall often, to keep our hold upon the ruins. I fear the Frost-horde will return sooner than later!'You have been tasked with destroying watch-towers outside the Goblin-gate.Your mission is to destroy the watch-towers on the path to the Goblin-gate.

