You should deliver the materials to him.'Well met, friend! Some of the greybeards wish to create gifts for their spouses. But at their age, they can no longer venture out to gather materials, and we are busy with our own tasks. Still, they remain stubborn in their pride and refuse to ask others for help.

'Such love is a rare thing, especially among us dwarves, and I wish to see them happy. They only need silver, sapphires, and sand from the Silverdeep Mine, as well as bones from nearby wildlife. Not evil creatures, mind you; I doubt the greybeards would appreciate that.''You return! Thank you, friend -- it will do these greybeards well to finally smile, and you have given them reason to do so. Even if they do not admit it outright.'By completing this quest, you will receive a Morgul Crests allowance.'Do you want a lot of Morgul Crests? Om nom nom! I got ya covered partner.''I stay here if you need more! Om nom nom!'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Iron Garrison Guards.'Would you like to level up with the Iron Garrison Guards?''Alright, soon the Iron Garrison Guards will consider you an Acquaintance. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Iron Garrison Guards.'Would you like to level up with the Iron Garrison Guards?''Alright, soon you will be a Friend of the Iron Garrison Guards. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Iron Garrison Guards.'Would you like to level up with the Iron Garrison Guards?''Alright, soon you will be an Ally of the Iron Garrison Guards. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred of the Iron Garrison Guards.'Would you like to level up with the Iron Garrison Guards?''Alright, soon you will be Kindred of the Iron Garrison Guards. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Iron Garrison Miners.'Would you like to level up your rep with the Iron Garrison Miners?''Alright, soon the Iron Garrison Miners will consider you an Acquaintance. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Iron Garrison Miners.'Would you like to level up your rep with the Iron Garrison Miners?''Ready to be a Friend of the Iron Garrison Miners?'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Iron Garrison Miners.'Would you like to level up your rep with the Iron Garrison Miners?''Alright, soon you will be an Ally of the Iron Garrison Miners. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred to the Iron Garrison Miners.'Would you like to level up your rep with the Iron Garrison Miners?''Alright, soon you will be Kindred to the Iron Garrison Miners. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will receive a Moria Daily Challenge token allowance.'I am Rock's prettier cousin from Moria! I have tokens from the daily challenges in Moria instances. Do you want some?''Trust me, there's many more where this came from. Come on back if you need them!'By completing this quest, you will receive a Moria Elf-stone allowance.'I am Rock's prettier cousin from Moria! I have Elf-stones from instances in Moria. Do you want some?''Trust me, there's many more where this came from. Come on back if you need them!'By completing this quest, you will receive a Moria platinum token allowance.'I am Rock's prettier cousin from Moria! I have platinum tokens from Moria instances. Do you want some? Have them!''Trust me, there's many more where this came from. Come on back if you need them!'By completing this quest, you will receive an allowance of Motes, Embers and Figments.'Dust in the wind...''Everything is dust in the wind...'This quest will grant you some experience in mounted combat.Speak with Avon.Speak with Avon'Do you seek training in the ways of mounted-combat? I was about to go home but I suppose I could help you first.''Receive this experience in the ways of mounted combat.'Hungry beggars can often get too close to the Festival area in Winter-home, which is a strict violation of the Mayor's rules to keep the Yule Celebration pleasant for all.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>The beggars can be found in the streets throughout town, and since the Mayor finds them unsightly, Guard Kember has asked you to make them leave.

You should remove beggars from the streets about town so that the Festival patrons won't be upset by them.Tell Barrett Nowell to move offTell Ted Ives to move offTell Regina Judson to move offTell Jack Judson to move offTell Bill Hyde to move offGuard Kember is near the gate of Winter-home.

You should return to Guard Kember and tell him that the beggars have been successfully moved away from the eyes of the town.Return to Guard Kember'Oh, we can't have this. No indeed, the mayor's instructions were incredibly clear. Those beggars need to move off. I don't care where they go, but we can't have the good patrons and patronesses seeing them like this.

'The mayor wants this town to look pristine and happy and clean as long as the Yule Festivities go on. Those beggars must get off the streets at once and clear out.

'Are you looking for something to do between festival games? I'll give you a nice reward if you clear out those beggars. I have my hands full with my other guard duties right now.''If you please, ${PLAYER}, just get those beggars moving along to somewhere else. Wherever will do, as long as they're keeping out of sight and out of trouble.''You want me to leave, but...Guard Kember just told me to leave a few hours ago, so I did, and this is where I ended up. Where should I go now?'

You don't know where Barrett Nowell should move to, but you repeat your assurance that Guard Kember wants him to move regardless.

'All right, then. I suppose I'll just have to amble along somewhere else. And then Guard Kember or you or the Mayor or someone will tell me that's no good either. Then I'll amble elsewhere. I'm sure we beggars make a good sport for the rich folk.''I'll go, I'll go. Though I think it's abominable bad the way you rich folks treat us beggars. Just who do you think made us this way? The world ain't made of coins, you know. When one class gets all the coins, another gets none.''But...What does the mayor want? I would love nothing more than to disappear and stop inconveniencing the rich folk, believe me. But I am a person, flesh and blood, and I can't just disappear like a wisp of cloud on a windy day.''I know begging ain't becoming of a man, but...but these are hard times for my sister and me. We are very hungry, you see. So...seeing as there's lots of new folk about, I thought perhaps a good-willing patron could spare me some kindness, that I might get a bit of bread during the Festival.

'I see that I'm not wanted. I'll go find another haunt, and I'll stay out of sight. I am mightily sorry if I've displeased any of you good patrons.''Alas, I'm caught! Please, good ${RACE}...please, it be very cold. I shan't stay long. I only sneaked over here to be near the warmth of the town square. It has been too long since any real warmth flowed in my blood.

You give Bill Hyde a hard look, and convey Guard Kember's orders.

'Yes...yes. I see how I might be upsetting the patrons. I'm dreadful sorry. I'll be going....''I don't see any beggars loitering about now. Whatever you said to them seemed to do the trick! 

'As promised, here's a reward for the favour you did me. Now the mayor will be pleased, which means that I will be pleased, and that is always just how I want it!'To show true loyalty to the racing dwarves, you must select each of them as your favoured contestant many times and win.To show true loyalty to the racing dwarves, you must select each of them as your favoured contestant many times and win..Select Kolmar's Credulity and win (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Select Leg it, Lar and win (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Select Signar's Swift Step and win (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Select Ottó the Outstanding and win (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})To show true loyalty to the racing hobbits, you must select each of them as your favoured contestant many times and win.To show true loyalty to the racing hobbits, you must select each of them as your favoured contestant many times and win.Select Dashing Daffodilly and win (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Select Bustle with Burdy and win (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Select Gladdy's Gait and win (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Select Mudric's Momentum and win (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Durin has written you a message of thanks.Durin has written you a message containing his thanks and a number of other musings.Complete 'The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves'Some folks just cannot seem to behave themselves.You are often taken to task for your actions.When neighbours work together, the Rohan Eastfold Homesteads will shine bright as the beacons.Fresh pies can be found in the Rohan Eastfold Homesteads.

You should gather the pies.Gather pies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Deliver the pies to the doorsteps of your neighbors within the Rohan Eastfold Homesteads.Deliver pies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'One of our neighbours just baked some fresh pies for us! I think we should deliver them to some of our other neighbours. What a wonderful surprise to find a fresh pie on your doorstep in the morning!'Samwise Gamgee knows a little something about adventure. He will happily help you on your own merry adventures and see that you are capable of feeding yourself on the way.Samwise Gamgee, aside from being a great adventurer on his own, wants to help you with your own adventures. Speak with him and he will reward you with a gift of sorts; as any good hobbit would.See what Sam has for you'What I learned in all my travels is that you never know where you might find your next meal. Let me see if there is anything extra in my pack that you might use to make a meal in a time of need.'

Sam searches through his pack.

'It may not look like much. Trust me, ${PLAYER}, in a time of need, you will be happy you have this.''Taters are good for boiling, mashing, sticking in a stew.

'Carrots are always good. Cooked or raw, it really does not matter.

'Mushrooms... I had friends get into some mighty trouble over mushrooms.

'Onions are best for bringing out flavour in most any dish.

'A pinch of allspice is always welcome.

'Blueberries, elderberries, or blackberries are some of the finest foods for travelling on a long journey.

'One thing about fish; never eat them raw or wriggling. Upset your stomach, they will.'You have received an order to fill a delivery to a member of the Inn League who has been stranded away from the festival this season.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Limael's Vintage can be purchased in Celondim in Ered Luin.

You should collect Limael's Vintage from a Vintner in Celondim.Collect Limael's Vintage from CelondimWesley Hopwood is at Thornley's Work-site in Bree-land, far to the east of Ered Luin.

Wesley Hopwood has told you that he will never be able to travel to Celondim in Ered Luin to find the "Limael's Vintage" he needs to complete the Inn League's Challenge. He has asked you to collect some of the wine for him.'I have here a list of requests to assist Inn League members in need, stranded away from home with the support of their beer-loving brethren. It seems they miss their favourite drinks, or in some cases they've never even tasted them!

'There is a good fellow at Thornley's Worksite by the name of Wesley Hopwood. He apparently mopes day in and day out since the year he was able to get away and join us for some festival adventuring. He dearly wishes to begin the Challenge.

'Let's see here...ah yes. The first brew he needs to sample is none other than Limael's Vintage, and that can be found in Ered Luin, in a pretty Elf-port called Celondim. Have you been there? It is lovely. My travels brought me there once for this very same reason. You should bring some Limael's Vintage to Wesley Hopwood.''Huh? Oh, good day to you. Sorry, I've been a bit lost in my own thoughts. Thinking about great kingdoms and adventuring kings...but you know, I don't know why I torment myself like that. It's not like I'll ever get to see such great things. I'll be stuck here forever, working on these homes.

'Farthest I ever been from here is the Shire, and all I did there was join their silly little Inn League. Guess I thought it would be nice to be part of something big, but now all I know is that I'm going to fail their Challenge. The first spirit I'm supposed to drink is a bit of wine called "Limael's Vintage," but it's only found all the way out in a vineyard just west of Celondim in Ered Luin.

'Hmm, you look like a bit of a traveller. Would you help out a poor soul and get me a bit of Limael's Vintage? I'd hate to fail at this Challenge, not sure I could live with myself....''It's Limael's Vintage you want, in Celondim. I'm sure there is a vintner there who can help you.''Have you had a chance to get me a bit of "Limael's Vintage" from Celondim in Ered Luin? I don't know if I'll ever be able to entirely complete the Challenge, but it would be nice to at least get a start.''What's that? Is that it? Is that Limael's Vintage? It looks amazing...it's an Elf-wine, isn't it? I...I never thought I'd see such a thing in all my life!

'You've done me a great favour, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps...no, there is no perhaps about it! I will definitely complete the Challenge now. I will travel all over Eriador. And perhaps some day I will see those great kingdoms and adventuring kings I've dreamed about!'You have been tasked with delivering unpleasant things to Inn League Members in need of assistance, something only a terrible ${CLASS} would do.

