Óli has requested Beakbreaker Ale, but the Ale Association plans to trick him by delivering 1404 Vintage Reserve instead. You should speak to Barmy Rootknot at The Green Dragon and collect the incorrect wine.Collect fake Beakbreaker Ale from The Green DragonÓli is at Hrimbarg in the Misty Mountains, waiting for Beakbreaker Ale.

You should deliver the fake Beakbreaker Ale, actually 1404 Vintage Reserve wine, to Óli before you run out of time.'I've received a different sort of orders from Jónar, the head of this here society. He hates the Inn League so much that he has assigned me a rather different task than my Inn League neighbour there. Shh, he mustn't hear us!

'Atli harbours a preference for the Beakbreaker Ale of The Comb and Wattle Inn... that is not even dwarf-made! His cousin Óli wishes to sample it on Atli's recommendation, but we will make sure that he does not consider Atli's preference to be sound.

'Instead of Beakbreaker, we will be delivering a wine from the Shire itself. 1404 Vintage Reserve is a fine wine from the Green Dragon, to be sure, and a good clear one, but if it is disguised as an ale, it will be highly offensive to Óli's palate.''Switching ale with wine! Óli will be so delightfully confounded by our trick.''Welcome to The Green Dragon, my dear ${RACE}. Count yourself lucky to be tasting the finest wine in all the Shire! It will cheer you on your travels.''Is this the very Beakbreaker Ale recommended by my cousin Atli? I can scarcely believe my eyes. Let me taste that.'

Óli takes a long drink from the wine flask.

'Plah! Ptoo! That is the sweetest ale I've ever tasted. It's barely fit to be called an ale! They should really warn folk before giving out that stuff. I had no idea Atli was so foolish about his taste in beer! I do not think Men quite know how to correctly brew beers. I believe I will stick with dwarf-beer from now on.'Achieve 50th level playing through as a Champion on Adventurous difficulty or higher.Achieve 50th level playing through on Adventurous difficulty or higher as a Champion.Achieve 50th level playing through on Adventurous difficulty or higher as a ChampionYou stood up on the side of Erebor for Durin's Day, and saw what the sun revealed when it touched the dwarf-wrought stone.Observe Durin's Day before the old secret door up on the side of Mount Erebor.Read the runes upon the stoneYou have earned the Of Aglarond title.You have earned the Of Anduin title.You have earned the Of Arkenstone title.You have earned the Of Belegaer title.You have earned the Of Brandywine title.You have earned the Of Crickhollow title.You have earned the Of Dwarrowdelf title.You have earned the Of Eldar title.You have earned the Of Elendilmir title.You have earned the Of Elendilmir title.You have earned the Of Estel title.You have earned the Of Evernight title.You have earned the Of Firefoot title.You have earned the Of Fornost title.You have earned the Of Gilrain title.You have earned the Of Gladden title.You have earned the Of Gwaihir title.You have earned the Of Imladris title.You have earned the Of Landroval title.You have earned the Of Laurelin title.You have earned the Of Maiar title.You have earned the Of Meneldor title.You have earned the Of Mirkwood title.You have earned the Of Morthond title.You have earned the Of Nimrodel title.You have earned the Of Riddermark title.You have earned the Of Silverlode title.You have earned the Of Sirannon title.You have earned the Of Snowbourn title.You have earned the Of Vanyar title.You have earned the Of Vilya title.You have earned the Of Windfola title.You have earned the Of Withywindle title.Merkhâma has asked you to search for visitors around Furtherholm's harbour and southern beach who are in need of help.There appears to be someone in need of help on the small beach beside the harbour.Talk to the thirsty beachgoerThe thirsty beachgoer has asked you to get a drink from inside The Cracked Flagon.Find a refreshing beverage inside The Cracked FlagonYou have gotten a refreshing beverage from inside The Cracked Flagon. You should bring it to the thirsty beachgoer on the small beach near the harbour.There may be someone else in the harbour area that needs help.Talk to the relaxing holidayerThe relaxing holidayer has asked you to go into her room in The Cracked Flagon to find her book and bring it to her.Find the relaxing holidayer's bookYou have found the relaxing holidayer's book, "A Memory of Mûmakil". You should bring it to her at her bench in the harbour area.There may be someone on the southern beach that needs help.Talk to the unsettled sightseerThe unsettled sightseer has asked you for a cushion to sit on. The Cracked Flagon probably has something.Find a cushion for the unsettled sightseerYou have found a cushion for the unsettled sightseer. You should bring it to him on the southern beach.There appears to be someone else on the southern beach who needs help. You should talk to them.Talk to the hopeful suitorThe hopeful suitor has requested a picnic basket of food. You should head back to The Cracked Flagon and see what you can find.Find a picnic basketThe hopeful suitor has requested a picnic basket of food. You have a basket, now you must fill it. Sâghlem, the cook at The Cracked Flagon can probably help you.The hopeful suitor has requested a picnic basket of food. You brought an empty basket to Sâghlem, the cook at The Cracked Flagon, who filled it for you.Pick up the filled basketThe hopeful suitor has requested a picnic basket of food. You brought an empty basket to Sâghlem, the cook at The Cracked Flagon, who filled it for you. You should bring the filled basket to the hopeful suitor on the southern beach.It seems there is another person on the southern beach who needs help. You should talk to them.Talk to the queer merrymakerThe queer merrymaker has requested that you bury him in the sand.Bury the queer merrymaker in the sandThe queer merrymaker has requested that you bury him in the sand even more than you already have.Bury the queer merrymaker some moreYou have buried the queer merrymaker in the sand and don't see anyone else in need of help. You should return to Merkhâma outside of The Cracked Flagon to get your reward.Talk to Merkhâma'${PLAYER}, I can see that there are some visitors who might need assistance, but I am not to leave my current post. Would you mind taking a walk around the harbour area and the southern beach and helping anyone who needs it? Assist them with whatever you can, and I will pay you for your time.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'My goodness, I am absolutely parched! It is important to consume many beverages whilst taking in the beach, you know.

'Be a dear and run over to the tavern and get me a refreshing beverage. Something strong, if you catch my meaning.''Oh yes, do give that here. This is just what I needed. Now go, you are blocking my view.''Fair winds to you, what is it that you need? Oh, you come to ask if I need anything? Now that I think about it, I would love to be reading my book right now, but I left it in my room at the inn. I am afraid that if I leave here to go get it, someone will steal my seat on this bench!

'Would you mind going into The Cracked Flagon and getting my book? I left it on the side table, next to the bed.''You found it! Thank you so much. I have been eager to read what happens next. Clear skies and swift sails to you, my friend.''Bless me, you nearly gave a fright!

'Do I need anything? Well... if it's not too much trouble, I could use something to sit on. I'm enjoying the view very much, but this sand... I hate it. It's rough and irritating, and it gets everywhere. I think those folks over there with a blanket have the right idea. Could you perhaps bring me a cushion or some-such?''Ah! That will do perfectly! Thank you!''Greetings, my good ${RACE}. Since you appear to be assisting people, I wonder if you would do us a small favour.

'I daresay I did not plan our day well, as it would be a perfect day for a picnic, but alas, we do not have a picnic basket of food! If you would, nip on over to the tavern and fetch us a picnic, would you?''A picnic, you say? Oh, they appeared to be courting?'

The man chuckles as he takes the basket and begins to fill it.

'I have just the thing. A bottle of wine, some cured meats, a variety of cheeses, water biscuits, and a few figs. That should do them!''Oh ho, this is perfect, my friend. Thank you ever so much. And send my regards to Sâghlem.''Isn't this island such a magical place!?

'I heard that beachgoers have been known to enjoy themselves by burying each other in the sand! Buried in the sand, I say!? Well, I say to myself, I think I would quite like that! Only as the bury-ee I have no bury-er. But now you have come along!

'I charge you with the task of burying me in the sand!''Everyone has gotten the help they wanted? Thank you very much for helping them! And by them, I mean me.'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Defenders of Minas Tirith.'Hullo! Would you like to be an "Acquaintance" of the Defenders of Minas Tirith? Well look no further! Completion of this quest should do that just for you.

'If this sounds good to you, speak to me again!''Alright, soon the Defenders of Minas Tirith will consider you an Acquaintance. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Defenders of Minas Tirith.'Are you looking to become a "Friend" of  the Defenders of Minas Tirith? I can help you with that if you complete this quest!

'Speak to me again when you are ready.''Alright, soon you will be a Friend of the Defenders of Minas Tirith. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Defenders of Minas Tirith.'So you want to be an "Ally" of the Defenders of Minas Tirith? Allow me to help!

'Speak to me again when you are ready.''Alright, soon you will be an Ally of the Defenders of Minas Tirith. Ready?'By completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred to the Defenders of Minas Tirith.'Are you looking to be welcomed into the inner circle of Minas Tirith? I can help you with that and make you "Kindred" to the Defenders of Minas Tirith.

'If this sounds good to you, speak to me again!''Alright, soon you will be Kindred to the Defenders of Minas Tirith. Ready?'You discovered a small piece of parchment hidden away in a poorly hidden chest in Bilbo's Hidden Burrow. The letter made mention of a special request that has been carried out an a reward that might be waiting for the bearer of the writ.Deliver the letter to someone whom Bilbo would have trusted with an important secret. They will likely be very near the festival grounds, perhaps even part of the festival.

The writ speaks of a trustworthy sort with whom Bilbo struck a deal before he left the Shire. Apparently, there is a reward to be delivered to anyone not related to the Sackville-Bagginses.To whom it may concern,

Preparations of this magnitude require the confidence of very few folk and very few folk were trustworthy enough at the time that I penned this letter. The trustworthy lot were dear friends and so they have been instructed to provide the bearer of this writ, provided that the bearer is not of the Sackville-Baggins line, with a token of appreciation.

Treat the reward well and consider a spooky visit to my dear Lobelia from time to time.

Bilbo Baggins'Merry me! Could this be?'

She reads the note hastily.

'It is indeed. Mr. Bilbo gave us Hornblowers specific instruction to paint up horses and ponies once we found that his final trick for Lobelia was sprung. We did as he asked, and it seems that he would like you to have one of the precious beasts.

