<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Barliman Butterbur can be found at The Prancing Pony in Bree-town.

You should speak with Barliman Butterbur, for he sells Barliman's Best, which shall be brought to Alrek cleverly disguised as Forsaken Ale.Collect fake Forsaken Ale from the Prancing PonyAlrek is at Thrasi's Lodge in Ered Luin.

You should deliver the fake Forsaken Ale, actually Barliman's Best, to Alrek, for it will confuse him greatly.'I've received a different sort of orders from Jónar, the head of this here society. He hates the Inn League so much that he has assigned me a rather different task than my Inn League neighbour there. Shh, he mustn't hear us!

'One of our own dwarves, Alrek, is a traitor, and he loves the Inn League more than his own kind! The shameless fellow is at Thrasi's Lodge, waiting for a delivery of Forsaken Ale, with which he'll be completing the Inn League Challenge.

'I know what will throw him through a loop. He should be drinking only the best when expecting the worst, and that is Barliman's Best, of course. You should go to The Prancing Pony at once to collect Alrek's desired drink.''Have you travelled to The Prancing Pony yet? Your assignment will begin there.''You're here for the best of the best, are you? This is named after me because the Pony is the best of the best as well, and I warrant you'll never find a better inn.

'Where did that Nob get to this time? You must pardon me. I am always so busy, you see. No rest for the weary! I've a business to run!''Is that the Forsaken Ale? Give that here, my friend. I wish to complete the challenge straight away... but... I cannot bring myself to drink it. I have heard such terrible rumours.

'Thank you for bringing it. I may have changed my mind, though. I shall ponder it for a while....'You have received an order to fill a delivery to a member of the Inn League who has been stranded away from the festival this season.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Forsaken Ale can be purchased at The Forsaken Inn in the Lone-lands.

You should travel to The Forsaken Inn to purchase Forsaken Ale for Alrek, who waits at Thrasi's Lodge for some assistance.Collect Forsaken Ale from the Forsaken InnAlrek is at Thrasi's Lodge in Ered Luin, far to the west of the Lone-lands.

Alrek has asked you to collect a Forsaken Ale for him from Anlaf the Forlorn at The Forsaken Inn.'I have here a list of requests to assist Inn League members in need, stranded away from home without the support of their beer-loving brethren. It seems they miss their favourite drinks, or in some cases they've never even tasted them!

'Now, Alrek managed to find himself at Thrasi's Lodge quite unexpectedly after drinking quite a few of Barliman's Best in a row...far more than was necessary for the challenge, I daresay.

'Now he has only one drink left to complete his challenge, and that is the Forsaken Ale, from none other than The Forsaken Inn itself. I don't recommend that particular drink to anyone, but so it goes!''Ah, good day to you! At least I believe it is day...things are a bit blurry right now. There is only one you, right?

'Have you had the misfortune to embark upon the Inn League's Challenge yet? I did and have travelled long and far. Along the way, I have tasted many a fine spirit, but...I think I have tasted one too many! And the worst of it is that I was just one drink short of completing the Challenge! The last drink I need to sample is called "Forsaken Ale," and it can only be found far to the east at an inn called "The Forsaken Inn." The brewer is Anlaf, the inn's proprietor.

'It is much to ask of you, but could you bring me one of these Forsaken Ales? I would go myself, but...I am in no condition to ride right now!''You'll find Alrek's order of ale at The Forsaken Inn.''The last ale I need to finish the Challenge is "Forsaken Ale." It can only be found at The Forsaken Inn far to the east. Please bring me one...I would go there myself, but I am in no condition to ride right now!''You have done it? You made it all the way to The Forsaken Inn and back? My thanks! Now I can complete the Challenge!

'Let's see how this last brew tastes....'Barliman Butterbur had a letter to send you, but he misplaced it. One thing drives out another, after all! Now that he has remembered, he hopes his oversight will not cause trouble.Barliman Butterbur hopes his oversight will not cause trouble.Reach an experience level of 65Defeat many Orcs in Cardolan.Defeat many Orcs in Cardolan.Defeat many Orcs in CardolanDefeat many Orcs in Cardolan.Defeat many Orcs in Cardolan.Defeat many Orcs in CardolanWho needs elegance when you have unwieldy strength?Use the skill Overhand SmashUse the skill Overhand SmashBy completing this quest, you will receive the Tokens of Heroism and Hero's Marks barter currency allowances.'Get barter currency for Landscape Difficulty, The Paths of Valour!''Ride back here like a bunny if you need more!'Bullroarer's Brew is placed at the foot of the statue of the Bullroarer in Brockenborings as part of a ceremony of respect.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Gunderic Grubb is at The Golden Perch in Stock, south and east of Brockenborings.

Sigismond North-took told you to take the clover you collected to Gunderic Grubb.The statue of the Bullroarer is at the north edge of Brockenborings, north and west of Stock, overlooking the Greenfields.

You have been instructed to pay your respects to Bandobras Took by placing a tankard of Bullroarer's Brew near his statue.Sigismond North-took is in Brockenborings.

You have paid your respects to Bandobras Took. Now you should return to Sigismond North-took.Speak with Tobias Brockhouse just east of Brockenborings.'Now that we have the clover, it must be brewed! The only place in the whole Shire which makes Bullroarer's Brew is the Golden Perch. The original recipe was made by Bandobras himself and passed down from inn-keeper to inn-keeper at the Perch; they have been making it for over two hundred and fifty years!

'The clover is one of the main ingredients and also what gives it its green colour. Bring the clover you collected to Gunderic Grubb at the Golden Perch, and you should have some Bullroarer's Brew before the day is out.

'The Golden Perch is located in Stock. Hurry back as soon as you can with the Bullroarer's Brew.''You'll want to visit the famous Golden Perch, in Stock.''More clover! And just as we were running short. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You are doing the Bullroarer proud, you are!''I just received a fresh batch of Bullroarer's Brew from Gunderic Grubb. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.

'You have paid your respects...now for the Bullroarer's Challenge! You have heard of the Bullroarer's Challenge, haven't you? Every year the Took family hosts the Bullroarer's Challenge here in Brockenborings, some Hobbits like young Belgo practice all year for the event!

'Speak with Tobias Brockhouse, just east of Brockenborings. He will explain the rules to you. If you complete the Bullroarer's Challenge, return to me, and I will reward you with a special prize!''Hullo, friend, my name is Tobias Brockhouse, official Inn League Games-master; can I help you with something?'Explore enemy encampments and other dangerous places in Cardolan.Explore enemy encampments and other dangerous places in Cardolan.Explore Amon FirnExplore CaranostExplore Dol ErnilExplore GaervaradExplore Gond OrchalExplore Haudh NiruiExplore NímbarthExplore NettingladeExplore Sarch VornExplore EversteadExplore Hove FarmExplore TharbadExplore NagenstonesExplore WylvencloveExplore enemy encampments and other dangerous places in Swanfleet.Explore enemy encampments and other dangerous places in Swanfleet.Find the HowlingstonesFind RadlawFind FangsettleFind BloodhollowFind CobshollowFind SharmokalFind Caras GelebrenFind Tham LasgolFind Gwâl CrubanFind Tham CelechirA clever burglar can confuse opponents with odd challenges and riddles.Pose Riddles to your enemiesA clever burglar can confuse opponents with odd challenges and riddles.Pose Riddles to your enemiesThere are those who consider themselves knowledgable in the ways of magic or warfare. You, on the other hand, know a great deal about pies.Eat Mushroom Pies.Eat Steak and Kidney Pies.Eat Coney Pies.Eat Spiced Apple Pies.Eat Perfect Pies.Amabel Redfern's seeds will only reap their rewards when they are harvested many months from now. Simply plant them and wait for the crops to come to fruition during the Harvest Festival.

