'May your journey be swift and free of hardship, my friend. Namárië.'There are a number of things you will need to bring with you if you are to have a successful journey.Grimbeorn is outside his lodge, and can give you the supplies you will need to begin your journey.Talk to Grimbeorn and receive the supplies you will need for your journey'You will need to prepare for the journey, yes? It is a long way to Eriador, and you will need some supplies if you are to have success. Speak to Grimbeorn and he should give you what you will need.''I will give you what you will need for your journey. It is a long way across the mountains.'Arn Bulrush is concerned that the party-goers at this year's Spring Festival have become parched and will not enjoy his various activities unless their refreshments are refreshed.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>Jugs of spring wine can be found on the tables in the centre of the Festival Grounds.

Arn Bulrush asked you to deliver jugs of spring wine to tables on the outskirts of the Grounds.Pick up some wine for the north-east tableJugs of spring wine can be found on the tables in the centre of the Festival Grounds.

Arn Bulrush asked you to deliver jugs of spring wine to tables on the outskirts of the Grounds.Pick up some wine for the south-east tableJugs of spring wine can be found on the tables in the centre of the Festival Grounds.

Arn Bulrush asked you to deliver jugs of spring wine to tables on the outskirts of the Grounds.Pick up some wine for the south-west tableArn Bulrush is waiting to hear if your wine deliveries brought refreshment to the parched partygoers.Talk to Arn Bulrush at the Festival Grounds'I just walked around the Festival Grounds and do you know what I saw? Why, my disappointed eyes beheld parched party-goers everywhere I turned! No Spring Festival can be properly enjoyed without the delightful notes of a smooth spring wine! I have some Spring Leaves for you if you will pick up jugs of spring wine from the tables in the centre of the Festival Grounds and deliver them to tables on the outskirts, ${PLAYER}!''I can tell that your deliveries were met with much appreciation, ${PLAYER}! You earned these Spring Leaves, and at the same time put my mind at ease!

'Oh, I hope everyone is having a good time. When the party-goers find they are once again parched there will always be a need for someone willing to bring them what they need, so check back with me from time to time, my useful friend!'Ermentrude Haybank, the Maze-master of Wistmead, asks of you to shoo away pesky crows within the wheat-walls.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>The Wistmead wheat maze can be found in the Wistmead Harvest Festival space.

Ermentrude Haybank has tasked you with shooing away pesky crows.Shoo pesky crows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Wistmead wheat maze can be found in the Wistmead Harvest Festival space.

You should talk to Ermentrude Haybank at the wheat maze entrance.Talk to Ermentrude Haybank'Oh there are pesky crows all throughout the wheat field. Shoo them away if you are in there. With all their squawking, it sounds like they are laughing at us!''Thank you! I hope those pesky crows do not come back.'Maramam Bobbid has come to Clegur from Maur Tulhau to sell her pies, but the hobbits enjoying Daffodil Days are wary of the outsider.Maramam has offered to give you a free slice of her delicious pie if you hand out fliers to visiting hobbits scattered around Clegur.You have handed out all of the fliers Maramam gave you to advertise her pie. You should return to her near the stable-master in Clegur to receive your tasty reward.Talk to Maramam Bobbid'Hullo traveller! I've also come from a far away place, I have. All the way from Maur Tulhau! Ye may be thinkin', "She must really love daffodils, hey?" and while I do appreciate a nice flower, my true passion is pie!

'I make more pie than even a hobbit can eat herself, I do. So I've come to Clegur to sell some of my pie while there's a celebration on. It's not a business, mind ye, I'm just tryin' to fund more ingredients!

'But ach, it isn't goin' well. The folk here don't know who I am, and are proper suspicious of me, they are. I made these fliers to advertise my pie, but I can't leave my pie here to fend for itself while I hand them out.

'I'll make ye an offer, though. Hand out these fliers to visiting hobbits around the village, and when you're done, I'll give ye a slice for free.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Sales have picked up already, they have! Thank ye so much for the help. Here is the pie I promised ye, plus a little coin for yer pocket.'You have earned the Protagonist title.Obtain Title Writ - ProtagonistYou have earned the Protagonist title.Obtain Title Writ - ProtagonistComplete quests in Cardolan.Complete quests in Cardolan.Complete Tales of CardolanComplete Tales of Cardolan (Advanced)Complete Tales of Cardolan (Final)Complete quests in Swanfleet.Complete quests in Swanfleet.Complete Tales of SwanfleetComplete Tales of Swanfleet (Advanced)Complete Tales of Swanfleet (Final)Complete quests in Umbar Baharbêl.Complete quests in Umbar Baharbêl.Complete Tales of the Free CityComplete Tales of the Free City (Advanced)Complete Tales of the Free City (Final)Hunters who can release arrows the fastest tend to be the first to eat.Strike enemies with Quick ShotOne of your most dangerous attacks is a simple slash.Use SlashYou have received an order to fill a delivery to a member of the Inn League who has been stranded away from the festival this season.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Thistlebelly Brew can be purchased from The Ivy Bush in Hobbiton.

You should get some Thistlebelly Brew to deliver to Wald Mugwort.Collect Thistlebelly Brew from the Ivy Bush in HobbitonThe Ivy Bush is in the village of Hobbiton in the Shire, far to the west of the Lone-lands. Wald Mugwort is at Ost Haer in the Lone-lands, far to the east of the Shire.

Wald Mugwort, a Hobbit from Hobbiton, feels he needs a bit of a taste of home if he is to continue on his quest to complete the Inn League's Challenge. He has asked you to bring him a bit of "Thistlebelly's Brew" from the Ivy Bush in Hobbiton.'I have here a list of requests to assist Inn League members in need, stranded away from home without the support of their beer-loving brethren. It seems they miss their favourite drinks, or in some cases they've never even tasted them!

'My good friend Wald Mugwort is famous for pickling himself and then getting himself into a pickle. I believe he whisked himself off to the Lone-lands on an ill-advised drunken misadventure. I don't think he will be brave enough to return unless you get some Thistlebelly Brew in his belly.

'Thistlebelly Brew comes from The Ivy Bush. You should pick some up and bring this to Wald, who managed to find himself in some uncouth place called Ost Haer.''Oh dear, oh dear, I seem to have gotten myself into a pickle! Quite a pickle, indeed! I was such a fool thinking I could do this on my own, and now I am here all on my lonesome. Ah, but here you are, perhaps you can help!

'Oh goodness, I seem to have rattled on a bit there. I've had such a scare, so my wits are in tatters. You see, I am a hobbit from Hobbiton and a member of the Inn League. I was seeking to complete the League's Challenge and thought it would be a grand adventure, like old Mad Baggins'! But it would seem all I've done is get myself surrounded by all manner of evil creatures. However, if I had a bit of a taste of home, I could regain my courage and make it safely away from here!

'Could you bring me a bit of "Thistlebelly's Brew" from the Ivy Bush in Hobbiton? That should be all I need to set myself straight!''You'll want to start at The Ivy Bush, I imagine. It is a famous inn, in Hobbiton.''Please go to The Ivy Bush, and hurry! I need that beer....''Ah, a bit of "Thistlebelly's Brew," isn't it? Oh wonderful! Already, I can feel my lagging spirits picking up!

'With that beer in my belly, there will be no creature, great or small, that will put the fear into me. I will complete the League's Challenge yet!'You have been tasked with delivering unpleasant things to Inn League Members in need of assistance, something only a terrible ${CLASS} would do.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>The tavern keep is in the cellar of Thorin's Hall.

You should collect a small beer from Thorin's Hall's inn, and then deliver it to Wald Mugwort under the guise of Thistlebelly Brew.Collect fake Thistlebelly BrewWald Mugwort is at Ost Haer in the Lone-lands.

You should bring the fake Thistlebelly Brew to Wald Mugwort. You will trick him with this, for it is actually a small beer from Thorin's Hall.'I've received a different sort of orders from Jónar, the head of this here society. He hates the Inn League so much that he has assigned me a rather different task than my Inn League neighbour there. Shh, he mustn't hear us!

'A little hobbit named Wald Mugwort went on a wild adventure in pursuit of some Inn League exposure and has landed himself into a spot of trouble. He desires Thistlebelly Brew, a taste of home, in order to work up the courage to get himself out of there.

'Instead, we will deliver him a plain, ordinary beer. Just a beer, nothing more. And what is worse -- it will be from Thorin's Hall. It will be the dwarves that motivate him with their superior brewing skills, not little rascal hobbits.''Wald Mugwort will now feel the superiority of the dwarves' brewing skills! You must only fetch a beer from Thorin's Hall to advance this scheme.''Small beer? Is that all? Are you sure you don't want anything more exciting? Well, if you insist, here you go.''Thank you, thank you, thank you! I will drink it now!'

Wald Mugwort drinks deep of the Small Beer.

'I feel braver already! This is the best-tasting beer I've ever had, and I have had almost every beer west of the Lone-lands!'By completing this quest, you will receive racial traits for a high level character.'Hoom, hum. What are you, little one? Do not tell me, hasty creature. I will find out.

   Eldest of all, the elf-children;
   Dwarf the delver, dark are his houses;
   Ent the earthborn, old as mountains;
   Kin of Beorn, friend to nature....

'Hm, yes, that is you. Will you accept the gift of your peoples?'

