Using what remains of his research, find all the ingredients to make Bile of IfrinnScythespew is an odorous and viscous liquid. The phial which contains it is cool to the touch, but the vile substance is used to break down the toughest of flesh. The upper limits of its potency as a corrosive is untested and unknown.The crimson life essence of an adder has many uses in alchemy. In Thaurisgar, it is valuable for its numbing effects, but can be quite deadly if consumed. Ingestion of this substance can result in loss of vital functions. Research suggests it was mainly used as an anesthetic.The essence of a warg that has been reduced down to its base innate chemical structure by repeated cycles of steeping and simmering at low temperatures for long durations.The noxious liquid of festersweat, derived from fungus, is deadly on physical contact. This concentration has been fermented with other alchemical solutions for long periods of time to create alternative results from its various properties.Strickenseep is a highly toxic and deadly sap that is known to cause extreme paralysis and loss of vision. Its uses in alchemy is taboo. Its properties and effects are undesirable. However, when mixed with other substances, Aniochán the Harrower found that its effects and properties could be augmented to avoid the pitfalls of this sap when encountered alone.In the depths of Thaurisgar, countless foul and twisted experiments roam the shadows--the terrible legacy of Aniochán the Harrower. Before the fall of Carn Dûm, Aniochán worked tirelessly to outdo his rivals and win the favour of the Steward of Angmar. Chief among his tools in shaping his fell creations was a curious ichor known only as the Bile of Ifrinn. Thought to be lost after a disastrous experiment claimed Aniochán's life, now this foetid and vile substance is in danger of being let loose into the world.Complete Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary -- Tier 1In the depths of Thaurisgar, countless foul and twisted expe