You should talk to Waldo Rumble.Talk to Waldo Rumble'Welcome, welcome!

'If you're here for the Anniversary Festival, you have come to the right place! I'd recommend you look around and participate in many of the fun activities. Plenty to do!

'For those folks that participate in many of our activities, there might just be a reward in store for you, so get out there!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: this quest cannot be cancelled.</rgb>'Goodness, you certainly have given it your all this year! Thanks to all your hard work, the festival went off without a hitch!

'I hope to see you next year, when I'll have a whole new set of gifts ready for you!'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Event takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.  Come and join the festivities in Bree-town to help mark this milestone with fireworks and good-cheer!Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Event takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.  Come and join the festivities in Bree-town to help mark this milestone with fireworks and good-cheer!Complete to receive a map to Bree-town!Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Event takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.  Come and join the festivities in Bree-town and the Shire to help mark this milestone with fireworks and good-cheer!Complete to receive a map to Bree-town.Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Event takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.  Come and join the festivities in Bree-town to help mark this milestone with fireworks and good-cheer!Hurry and travel to Bree-town to experience this year's annual celebration. Hurry and join the festivities!Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Event takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>A spectacular fireworks display occurs every night on a hill above Bree-town. Winston Peartree, at the fireworks area near Bree's North-gate, will happily introduce you to the event and get you participating in it in no time.Speak to Winston Peartree at the fireworks area near Bree's North-gateVisit Sally Threshing at the Bree Festival Grounds race-track to learn about testing your skill at racing.   The Bree Festival Grounds are located between the Northern Bree Fields and Bree-town.Visit the site of the Bree race-trackThe Methel-stage, just south of Bywater in the Shire, is the location of a spectacular annual fireworks extravaganza.  Gandalf himself has donated fireworks for this event, which is hosted by the Hobbits of Bywater.  Help is needed to make this the largest spectacle it can be!Visit the Methel-stage in the ShireVisit  Carl Proudfoot at the Delving Fields race-track to learn about testing your skill at racing.   The Delving Fields are to the south-east of Michel Delving in the Shire.Visit the site of the Shire race-trackThe Thorin's Hall Festival Arena is host to the Battle for Glorious Beer.  Inside the arena, Gísli Strongclub will introduce you to the finer points of swinging a dwarf-club, and will tell you what is required if you choose to undergo the ultimate challenge of claiming the Glorious Beer for yourself.Visit the beer-fight arena in Thorin's HallThe Keepers of Gifts can be found in most of the major towns in Middle-earth during the Anniversary, with Angeline Greenpasture holding her post in Bree.

You should speak to Bree-land's Keeper of Gifts to receive a small token of appreciation.Speak with Angeline Greenpasture, the Keeper of Gifts in BreeHello there, good ${CLASS}!

You may have noticed that there is a special event is going on: our very own Anniversary! There are festivities taking place in many locations, perhaps you'd like to know the particulars?

While the event is under way, you will find that there is a beer-brawl in Thorin's Hall, fireworks shows in Bree and the Shire, horse-races at the Horse-fields and Delving fields, and a great number of tokens to be found all over the world. You may trade these tokens for special gifts and profit greatly from such simple tasks as fighting evil in Middle-earth.

Go and explore the different festivities, and be sure to return here at night to participate in our marvelous firework show!'Welcome to the show! Are you here to take in the sights, or maybe you would care to participate instead?

'There is nothing quite like the fireworks show we have here in Bree. We gather every night during the festival and set off quite the display! Feel free to join in the fun and be rewarded for your efforts. You won't regret it, friend.''Greetings! I am a Keeper of Gifts, and many like me can be found in the major towns throughout Middle-earth during the Anniversary celebration.

'As you defeat the forces of evil during this special time, you will find that your chances of acquiring special tokens will be quite good. When you have enough tokens, you may trade them in for gifts for a limited time!''Welcome, welcome! If you are a fan of fireworks, then you have come to the right place! This stage is home to the Shire's annual fireworks event, and no one does it better than we do.

'Gandalf the Grey has been kind enough to provide us with enough fireworks to have a spectacular show this year, but we need volunteers to help us set off all of the launchers. 

'Feel free to come celebrate with us as much as you would like... a new show starts every few minutes!''Welcome to the Festival Arena! This is where the Battle for Glorious Beer takes place. We have a fine brew this spring, and I am sure people will want to compete to win the limited supply.

'Come back often! This event runs every few minutes and is a wonderful way to blow off steam and acquire exciting rewards.''Hello there! Are you here to race? This is the Anniversary Run in the Shire, and you can race every day to win Anniversary tokens.''Greetings to you, ${CLASS}! Would you like to try your skill at racing? Come back every day to race, and you will not be sorry.'Sneaky hobbits from the Shire have left fun lists of things to do hanging from the Party Tree.Sneaky hobbits from the Shire have left fun lists of things to do hanging from the Party Tree.Waldo Rumble needs your assistanceEvery year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'I have an update regarding my request to be relieved, if you are curious. The Shire-wide Party Planning Committee has heard my case and the Chief Party Planners are considering what to do in the matter. 

'Only, while they stroke their chins and ponder, the number of cards up there has grown to staggering proportions! The old ones get under foot and the new ones make my head ache. What a mess!''The verdict from the Party Planning Committee is still out, I'm afraid. Important matters do take some time, you see. Here is another reward for your patience in this important matter.

'Do not snicker, it is important! My position and standing are on the line here!'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'Here we are again, friend! I must be honest with you; I have been looking forward to this all year! Quickly, go to the tree, and see what new adventure awaits you!''Three new lists this year! My, my, perhaps this will become a new tradition! I'm afraid there is nothing left to do now but wait until next year and await more from our mystery merrymaker! I wonder if they will ever reveal themselves?

'See you soon, and thanks again for all your help! Here's a final reward for being such a caring friend during all this ruckus. Take care!'

<rgb=#FFFF00>There will be no additional Scavenger Hunt cards this year, but the event will remain open for some time, so that remaining cards can be completed.</rgb>Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'My new suspicion is that adventuring trouble-maker, Bingo Boffin. He is behind all this. Of course I haven't a shred of evidence, but I feel sure that I am right!''Turns out Bingo Boffin has been busy reading about cooking at the Tuckborough library. Everyone saw him there. Well, I am fully dispirited now and ready to hand in the towel.'

'But no, I must persevere! The Party Planning Committee is counting on me, and trust me, friend, you do not want to disappoint the Party Planning Committee! Here, have another reward for all your help.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'Would you believe that I slept not a wink last night, standing watch over the tree to catch these miscreants in the act - and somehow missed them? Oh, how the Planning Committee mock me behind my back. I know they think me guilty. And what if I am? At night while walking in my sleep? Bah! What nonsense. 

'Do not mind me, friend. I am under-slept, that is all. You should take another of those lists off the tree and see where it leads you this time.''I don't suppose that YOU are the one leaving these notes? Ha ha! Just a meagre jest. Don't stop helping me out of this muddle. Unless it WAS you? No. I never thought it was, I assure you. Whoever it is has left more prizes here, so help yourself.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'I am bewildered, friend. There is no explaining it! The Committee still has not decided my case! They are torturing me, that is what this is. It is THEY who have - have perpetuated this travesty. Oh, ${PLAYER}, what if they cast me off? What if they no longer invite me to tea?

'I - I've got something in my eye. Go on and take another card. I will be myself by and by.''I am glad you are back, ${PLAYER}! There has been much discussion, and indeed, decision-making while you were out, and so, you see, the verdict is in.

'We - I mean the Committee, of course - have decided that the unexplained, unapproved, riddlesome work of mischief before you will be officially declared the Annual Anniversary Scavenger Hunt. Unable to best them, we have welcomed them in the door. The unknown perpetrators of the act shall be allowed to remain anonymous, so long as they continue to provide the workings of the festival according to proper Shire regulations each year.

'For me, I shall keep my post here at the Party Tree. This is good news, as party planning around the Party Tree is all I've ever really known, and I would like to keep it that way.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should talk to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'Ah! You have come in answer to my correspondence? I must apologize if it was a bit disjointed and rambled here and there. I have been in a terrible state. 

'The thing is, well, just look at the Party Tree! Overnight, some mischievous malefactor has covered it in all of that - all of that WHATEVER it is!

'And as I stated in my letter, don't ask me why, but the Party Planning Committee has decided I must have something to do with it, or that I am the one who should get to the bottom of it. Only I haven't the first idea where to begin. Will you help me, my good ${RACE}?

'Just go over and take one of those down and - and see if you can make heads or tails of it. I certainly can't. Are they lists? Or riddles? Get one of them well and fully worked out, and I think we'll be getting somewhere!''You've found every last thing written on the paper? My, but I hardly know what any of those are. You must be well-travelled, friend ${CLASS}! Seen far off locales like Archet or Bree, am I right?

'Well, if you can believe it, these malefactors have left some rewards behind as well. Snuck them right under the table right beside me! Do they expect me to play a part in this game? Bah. I do hate to see a good gift go to waste,  so... here, have this for helping me and being such a good sport about it all.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'Enough, is enough, ${PLAYER}. I have endured my share of nights disturbed by dreams of papers on ribbons, dangling from trees, of tearing my hair out puzzling over lists upon lists upon lists, of wondering - nay knowing how folks must snicker at me and this this this ridiculous prank behind my back!

'I have placed a request with the Party Planning Committee to be relieved of my post. Perhaps I can learn to help with the assembly of kites or the baking of pies. Really, anything to get away from this tree!''Alas the local Party Planning Committee has rejected my request. It looks as if I will need to plead my case in person at our next Shire-wide Party Planning Committee monthly meeting.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'Six cards, ${PLAYER}! I will confide to you that I felt certain five would be the end of it. Now I fear to think where it will lead us. Will there be an end?

'Between you and me, I would have run out of ideas at card two. And why shouldn't I? My hair stands on end to think of half the things written on those slips. Elves and Oliphaunts and what-have-you. For I have had the good sense to have stayed in my place and never left the Shire... unlike SOME I might mention. Oh my! Oh dear! I didn't mean you. You're not from here - and we Shire-folk are proud to welcome guests. Oh dear me, I've really put my foot in it now!''Oh bother, they left even more rewards, here you are.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Waldo Rumble for a reward!Waldo Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Waldo Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Waldo Rumble'Would you believe it? I certainly wouldn't if it weren't here in my hand. What I mean to say is, I received a letter today. Not dangled from the tree, mind you. Placed in my mail, like decent hobbit-folk do, only it seems to be from whomever was responsible for, you know, all of this. They wrote, and quite kindly, too, I might add, that this is the last week of new cards, though we are all welcome to continue solving them for some while yet. Then they say they'll be back next year with even more fun! 

'I must confess that in all the huffing and puffing and tearing out of my hair, I have actually - and despite all my better judgment - enjoyed myself. I hope you did as well!''Ah well, it seems the cards will be staying up for a bit longer, so if you missed any you thought might be worth your while, now would be a good time to complete them.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

