You should return hastily to Jónar to tell him the news of your success against the hobbits and their rival faction.Talk to Jónar at Thorin's Hall'I can't believe my first attempt at sabotage has been thwarted by the lazy, trusting natures of those silly hobbits. But this one cannot possibly go awry.

'Here's what you're going to do next. Listen closely: I want you to punch holes in those kegs they use to get their pathetic hobbit-beers out of. If you punch holes in them, they will drain everywhere and be empty for the next hobbit who comes along to use it.

'Just imagining the looks on their disappointed, doughy little faces puts a tear of joy in my eye. Now go, quickly, and drain those kegs! It is not a true waste when so much good comes of it...for me.''You have executed the perfect tragedy. Soon, the Inn League's supplies will be all but depleted, and the Ale Association shall reign in its place!''What do you want? Do you think those kegs will be any emptier if you stand here talking to me all day? These aren't the kegs you're looking for. Now, you'd best go about your business, and move along!'By completing a great number of tasks, you are earning a reputation as someone with a 'can do' attitude and tolerant spirit.Complete tasks throughout Middle-earthBillina is hungry for earthworms.Scratch at the ground to reveal earthworms in Farmer Sandson's field.Billina is in the yard at Sandson's Farm west of Sandson's Fields.

Now that you have collected some earthworms, you should speak with Billina.'Who might you be? I do not believe I have seen you in the hen-house before. Well, no matter.

'Are those earthworms you have for me? I simply will not eat anything but earthworms these days. I have not taken well to the new feed in the yard.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

