You should speak to Odilia Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Odilia Rumble'My new suspicion is that adventuring trouble-maker, Bingo Boffin. He is behind all this. Of course I haven't a shred of evidence, but I feel sure that I am right!''Turns out Bingo Boffin has been busy reading about cooking at the Tuckborough library. Everyone saw him there. Well, I am fully dispirited now and ready to hand in the towel.'

'But no, I must persevere! The Party Planning Committee is counting on me, and trust me, friend, you do not want to disappoint the Party Planning Committee! Here, have another reward for all your help.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#00FF00> This version of the quest includes only objectives found within Eriador and is available to players of all levels. </rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Odilia Rumble for a reward!Odilia Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Odilia Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Odilia Rumble'Would you believe that I slept not a wink last night, standing watch over the tree to catch these miscreants in the act - and somehow missed them? Oh, how the Planning Committee mock me behind my back. I know they think me guilty. And what if I am? At night while walking in my sleep? Bah! What nonsense. 

'Do not mind me, friend. I am under-slept, that is all. You should take another of those lists off the tree and see where it leads you this time.''I don't suppose that YOU are the one leaving these notes? Ha ha! Just a meagre jest. Don't stop helping me out of this muddle. Unless it WAS you? No. I never thought it was, I assure you. Whoever it is has left more prizes here, so help yourself.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#00FF00> This version of the quest includes only objectives found within Eriador and is available to players of all levels. </rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Odilia Rumble for a reward!Odilia Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Odilia Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Odilia Rumble'I am bewildered, friend. There is no explaining it! The Committee still has not decided my case! They are torturing me, that is what this is. It is THEY who have - have perpetuated this travesty. Oh, ${PLAYER}, what if they cast me off? What if they no longer invite me to tea?

'I - I've got something in my eye. Go on and take another card. I will be myself by and by.''I am glad you are back, ${PLAYER}! There has been much discussion, and indeed, decision-making while you were out, and so, you see, the verdict is in.

'We - I mean the Committee, of course - have decided that the unexplained, unapproved, riddlesome work of mischief before you will be officially declared the Annual Anniversary Scavenger Hunt. Unable to best them, we have welcomed them in the door. The unknown perpetrators of the act shall be allowed to remain anonymous, so long as they continue to provide the workings of the festival according to proper Shire regulations each year.

'For me, I shall keep my post here at the Party Tree. This is good news, as party planning around the Party Tree is all I've ever really known, and I would like to keep it that way.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#00FF00> This version of the quest includes only objectives found within Eriador and is available to players of all levels. </rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Odilia Rumble for a reward!Odilia Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should talk to Odilia Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Odilia Rumble'Ah! You have come in answer to my correspondence? I must apologize if it was a bit disjointed and rambled here and there. I have been in a terrible state. 

'The thing is, well, just look at the Party Tree! Overnight, some mischievous malefactor has covered it in all of that - all of that WHATEVER it is!

'And as I stated in my letter, don't ask me why, but the Party Planning Committee has decided I must have something to do with it, or that I am the one who should get to the bottom of it. Only I haven't the first idea where to begin. Will you help me, my good ${RACE}?

'Just go over and take one of those down and - and see if you can make heads or tails of it. I certainly can't. Are they lists? Or riddles? Get one of them well and fully worked out, and I think we'll be getting somewhere!''You've found every last thing written on the paper? My, but I hardly know what any of those are. You must be well-travelled, friend ${CLASS}! Seen far off locales like Archet or Bree, am I right?

'Well, if you can believe it, these malefactors have left some rewards behind as well. Snuck them right under the table right beside me! Do they expect me to play a part in this game? Bah. I do hate to see a good gift go to waste,  so... here, have this for helping me and being such a good sport about it all.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#00FF00> This version of the quest includes only objectives found within Eriador and is available to players of all levels. </rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Odilia Rumble for a reward!Odilia Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Odilia Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Odilia Rumble'Enough, is enough, ${PLAYER}. I have endured my share of nights disturbed by dreams of papers on ribbons, dangling from trees, of tearing my hair out puzzling over lists upon lists upon lists, of wondering - nay knowing how folks must snicker at me and this this this ridiculous prank behind my back!

'I have placed a request with the Party Planning Committee to be relieved of my post. Perhaps I can learn to help with the assembly of kites or the baking of pies. Really, anything to get away from this tree!''Alas the local Party Planning Committee has rejected my request. It looks as if I will need to plead my case in person at our next Shire-wide Party Planning Committee monthly meeting.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#00FF00> This version of the quest includes only objectives found within Eriador and is available to players of all levels. </rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Cards hang from the Party Tree. Each card contains a scavenger hunt to complete at your own pace. When you complete a scavenger hunt, bring the completed card to Odilia Rumble for a reward!Odilia Rumble can be found next to the Party Tree in the Shire.

You should speak to Odilia Rumble to receive your reward for completing a scavenger hunt card!Talk to Odilia Rumble'Six cards, ${PLAYER}! I will confide to you that I felt certain five would be the end of it. Now I fear to think where it will lead us. Will there be an end?

'Between you and me, I would have run out of ideas at card two. And why shouldn't I? My hair stands on end to think of half the things written on those slips. Elves and Oliphaunts and what-have-you. For I have had the good sense to have stayed in my place and never left the Shire... unlike SOME I might mention. Oh my! Oh dear! I didn't mean you. You're not from here - and we Shire-folk are proud to welcome guests. Oh dear me, I've really put my foot in it now!''Oh bother, they left even more rewards, here you are.'Every year in the spring, the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt takes place to celebrate a very special occasion.

<rgb=#00FF00> This version of the quest includes only objectives found within Eriador and is available to players of all levels. </rgb>

