'Take this mighty dwarf-club and prepare to swing it at your fellow competitors. Do not leave the arena, or you will be eliminated from the competition.

'Best of luck to you!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The mighty dwarf-club will appear in your inventory. You should quickslot it to participate in the fight. This item cannot be used outside of the arena's bounds.</rgb>'Now that you wield the mighty dwarf-club, you should enter the fight-arena and claim your prize! Stop at nothing, ${PLAYER}; do not let them deter you from your charge!''Well done, ${PLAYER}! You really gave them quite a good knock! For your impressive display of physical skill, I shall give you a deserving gift.'Chubanog's Gleemen are supposed to perform in the Boat and Basket, but their instruments have been stolen by troublesome tweens.You have been asked... in a way, to help the band recover their instruments. You should look around Clegur for musical instruments or suspicious activity.Find the luteFind the fiddleFind the bagpipesFind the bodhranFind the fluteYou have found the instruments belonging to Chubanog's Gleemen scattered around Clegur. You should return the instruments to their owners, waiting in front of the Boat and Basket tavern.Return the fiddle to the fiddlerReturn the bagpipes to the piperReturn the bodhran to the drummerReturn the flute to the flautistYou have found the instruments belonging to Chubanog's Gleemen scattered around Clegur. You should return the lute to the lutenist, waiting in front of the Boat and Basket tavern.Return the lute to the lutenist'Greetings, my fortunate friend! It would seem ye have travelled from afar to feast your eyes upon this fancy flower festival!

'Traditionally, I would tempt ye to visit the taproom tonight, but truly, a tragedy has transpired. We, Chubanog's Gleemen, are the victims of vile juveniles! 

'Alas, troublesome tweens have brought misfortune to this miserable mob of musicians. The very tools of our trade have been taken from us, and thus our performance in the proud public house of the Boat and Basket has been hindered.

'Would a friend of festivity come forth and find the absent objects of our occupation?

'Please?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>'Ah! My fiddle! The day is saved! My thanks, stranger!''Ye found my pipes! Jolly good thing ye did too, they cost a fortune. Thank ye!''Oh, look at that, ye found my bodhran, and not a scratch on it! I suppose I'll have to put my book away, now, eh?''What's that then, my flute? Ach, there's dirt in it. Thank ye anyway, I suppose a flute full of dirt is better than no flute at all. That sounds like some kind of wise sayin' don't it?''What a splendid sight to see rightness restored and to have instruments in hand! I herald ye a hero and will praise you in my performances at the Boat and Basket!'There is much to do during the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt.There is much to do during the Anniversary Scavenger Hunt.Complete year one Tales cardComplete year two Tales cardComplete year three Tales cardComplete year four Tales cardComplete year five Tales cardComplete year six Tales cardComplete year seven Tales cardComplete year eight Tales cardComplete year nine Tales cardComplete year ten Tales cardUnravel the Epic Story for Volume V: The Peace of Middle-earth.Complete 'Book 1: A Time of Celebration'The story continues in future updates!The ancient dwarf-realm of Khazad-dûm is called Moria, the Black Pit, by the Elves...never have you seen so many pits.Explore the depths of the pits of Moria -- the hard way.While the crevices that make up the Great Delving are not bottomless, they are more than deep enough to result in the swift demise of the careless delver.The most prominent feature of the Silvertine Lodes is the great shaft that descends into the earth in the centre of the dig.

If you were to drop a goblin into it, the screams would likely fade before it hit bottom.While Durin's Way does not feature the great abyssal cracks that are frequent in other parts of Moria, it still features dangerous ledges and falls for the unwary traveller.There is a dark pit in the Redhorn Lodes that the Orcs use as a refuse dump. One can only imagine what horrors lie down there by now....The area of Nud-melek lies riven with deadly chasms. The movements of the earth itself have badly damaged many of the works of the dwarves since they fled and left many of the paths dangerous to tread.The bridge of Khazad-dûm has fallen, and the great chasm it once spanned now poses a seemingly impassable obstacle to those seeking to escape through the eastern gates of Moria.The Men of Bree wish to help the hobbits in their annual fishing derby by allowing fishermen to catch fish from the pond by the farm.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>The fish pond is east of Andrath farm.

Will Hindmarsh has asked you to catch fish for the hobbits' Lithe Festival.Catch as many fish as you can in twenty minutes.'What a beautiful day! The flowers are in full bloom, the bees are buzzing about, all sorts of critters are running around, and the fish are at their peak! You should catch some for the Lithe Festival.

'I went last year and all they had were dwarf fish. It was terrible! Just simply too tough... couldn't chew a thing. Our fish are the best, from right here in Bree!

'The best fish can be found in this pond right here. I'm sure the farmers will let you fish here for some time.''You oughtn't tarry long here, ${PLAYER}, for your time is already running out! Good luck to you.'You found Edlothon before his company of Elves reached their destination, and he has chosen to humour this talk of blossoms, petals, and flowers.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the event it is associated with ends. </rgb>Edlothon has asked you to speak with the hobbits of Woodhall in an effort to learn if the legendary Anarlossë somehow survived the decline of the Northern Kingdom.Edlothon has come with you to the hobbit village of Woodhall, where you found some evidence of a flower resembling the legendary Anarlossë.Talk to Edlothon in the village of WoodhallMarjoram Woolgather wishes to speak with you and Edlothon.Talk to Marjoram Woolgather in the village of WoodhallMarjoram Woolgather told you that sun-flowers border a farm-field north of Woodhall.Find the sun-flowers in the field to the north of WoodhallEdlothon stands by a row of sun-flowers in a field not far from the hobbit village of Woodhall.Talk to Edlothon in the field near WoodhallHaerandel is at the Bree-land Festival Grounds.Talk to Haerandel at the Festival Grounds'You are certain you understood what this hobbit had to say? For love of my brother Haerandel I will humour you in this, even if it seems fanciful beyond all reason. There is a hobbit village just beneath us, and I understand it is called Woodhall by those who live there. Go to this village and speak with the hobbits, and learn if they possess such flowers as you describe.

'My mind is set, and springtime is the season of my departure. But I have not such haste that I cannot spare a moment to answer this one question of my brother. The journeys we shared in our youth remain dear to me, as does he. Go to Woodhall and put the matter to rest! I cannot delay very long, but I will give some moments to this exercise. It has left my thoughts astir!''The town of Woodhall is beneath us, friend. Speak to the hobbits within and learn what they have to say about the Anarlossë of yesteryear.''I do not know anything about... what did you call this flower? Anarlossë?''Hmm... sounds Elvish to me! No, I do not want anything to do with it!''There are flowers all around the Shire. Here in Woodhall we grow several varieties! I am sorry I cannot be of more help to you.''You should talk to Marjoram! She is always painting flowers and plants and animals, and she may have seen this Elf-flower you're seeking! She lives here in Woodhall.''Will you let me sit here in peace? I know only that I find flowers quite pretty to look at, but if you seek a deeper understanding than that I have nothing to offer you!''This mysterious flower does sound like a sun-flower to me. Not the purple sort, with the bright yellow centre, but the other variety! Marjoram is always painting that second kind, and if you want to know about them you should talk to her! She lives here in Woodhall.''You're looking for sun-flowers? Why, I finished painting another of them not yesterday! I leaned it against the wall right over there to dry. Inspect it and tell me what you think!''I am not a flower-expert, I am sorry. Delivering the mail is what I am best at, and just between you and me, these nosey hobbits make that much more difficult than I can take!''You ask about some Elf-flower and ignore the ones planted right in front of my home? How very rude! Good day to you!''Sun-flowers? I don't know anything about that. My apologies.''I do not know what to say, ${PLAYER}! If I did not know any better, I would say the artist painted this not from memory but from life! This depicts one of the Anarlossë, just as I remember! How can this be? Did one of my people paint this picture? How came it to be in this village of hobbits? They are longer-lived than Men, but not so long that any could have seen one of the Anarlossë and put paint to paper with such accuracy! The last of that breed died out long ago, and only one of my people could have painted this!''What does this hobbit have to say? Does she know the name of the Elf that painted this picture?''I always heard Elves were frightening and strange, but your friend here seems rather amusing instead! I assure you, no Elf painted this picture, but I will take that as a compliment of my artistry! Yes, I am the painter, and indeed I have painted a number of the plants and animals I have seen in the woods and fields throughout the Shire. I do not know the word he used to describe this flower, and have never heard it before; no doubt it is an Elvish word of some meaning and great significance, but we hobbits like to give things names that tell you everything you need to know. This painting is of a sun-flower, of course!

'There are many of them growing around the border of a farm-field north of Woodhall, if you'd like to see them for yourselves. And tell your Elf friend that I appreciate his kind words about my painting!''Sun-flowers border a farm-field just to the north, if you'd like to see them for yourselves. And tell your Elf friend that I appreciate his kind words about my painting!''A field bordered by such flowers as that depicted by this painting? Lead the way, ${PLAYER}, even if I scarce believe the words of this hobbit!''How can I put this into words, ${PLAYER}? My heart leaps at the sight! I feel as if I have stepped back in time, back to a day not when the Anarlossë struggled and failed, but to a day when they flourished. Haerandel and I walked together among these flowers, in kingdoms North and South, and our eyes lighted on the horizon and our minds danced upon the future it promised. I am brought back to those happy days, and the sorrows that followed in the wake of Sauron and his wars are forgotten to me. The promise of the sun-flowers was as bright as their petals, and so many journeys lay still ahead of us.

'Following the death of Anárion and the decline of Arnor, the Anarlossë died out in the wider world. And yet, somehow, a seedling must have come to this land. I can see it in my mind's eye, ${PLAYER}, borne aloft in springtime, carried on the breeze, until it came to rest within this sheltered land. That seed took root, and from it the line prospered, hidden from outside eyes. The Anarlossë survived.'

Edlothon gazes at the sun-flowers in silence.

'I was prepared to depart. My heart wept to leave my brother, but I knew I would see him again when he too sailed from these shores. But the sight of these flowers has restored in me a sensation I have not felt since our travels together, so long ago. How many other wonders might remain in Middle-earth? The wanderlust stirs in me again.

'I believed I could remain no longer, but now I think my brother and I might find joy in another journey within the bounds of Middle-earth, and then depart for the Undying Lands together, as once I thought we would. Can I ask you to convey this message to Haerandel for me? I will spend some time here in contemplation, and will join him soon.

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, for reminding me of what I once held dear. And not only that! I am grateful for one more thing: you have given back to me the hope of the unexpected, the unlooked-for wonders that might still remain around the next bend, or behind the next tree. You have given back to me the promise of sun-flowers, and that is something I have missed.''I think my brother and I might find joy in another journey within the bounds of Middle-earth, and then depart for the Undying Lands together, as once I thought we would. Can I ask you to convey this message to Haerandel for me? I will spend some time here in contemplation, and will join him soon.''You have returned, ${PLAYER}! Did you find my brother in time? And was there any truth to the rumour that some strain of the Anarlossë might remain within the Shire?'

You tell Haerandel about the sun-flowers and his brother's decision to remain in Middle-earth for now. He looks at you thoughtfully, and after a moment a smile lightens his features.

'I am conflicted, my friend. I did not mean to gainsay my brother's choice, for I know when he made it the decision was not easy, and he felt it strongly. I would not tell him otherwise, and I did not wish to make him stay.

'But when you went in search of him, when it seemed the Anarlossë might bloom still somewhere in the Shire, I confess I did wonder what I would say if he chose to stay. Could our journeying days come again? Where might we go?

'I have come up with just the right destination, ${PLAYER}! I will suggest to my brother that we let our wandering feet bring us to the south-lands. There is a so-called master of herbs in Minas Tirith that I would propose we visit. He is possessed of a number of misconceptions that Edlothon and I are well-prepared to correct! We two Elf-brothers will depart in springtime, emboldened by the breeze and a spring in our step, on another journey like those we took of old!

'Thank you for helping my brother and me, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps the sun will smile upon us and our paths will cross in some distant land. Until then, my friend, farewell!'Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Agarnaith.Discover the rarest bird in all of Agarnaith.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Angmar.Discover the rarest bird in all of Angmar.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Anórien.Discover the rarest bird in all of Anórien.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Belfalas.Discover the rarest bird in all of Belfalas.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Bree-land.Discover the rarest bird in all of Bree-land.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Cardolan.Discover the rarest bird in all of Cardolan.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Dunland.Discover the rarest bird in all of Dunland.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Enedwaith.Discover the rarest bird in all of Enedwaith.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Ered Luin.Discover the rarest bird in all of Ered Luin.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Eregion.Discover the rarest bird in all of Eregion.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Evendim.Discover the rarest bird in all of Evendim.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Fangorn.Discover the rarest bird in all of Fangorn.Your continued efforts and exploration led you to discover the rarest bird in all of Forochel.Discover the rarest bird in all of Forochel.Your 