You should speak with Nârud and inform him of your success.Talk to Nârud, the Shield Isles Race Marshal'Fair winds to you, my friend! Do you ride horses?

'In the fair land where I hail from, we take great pride in our breed of horses, highly valued not just for their speed and endurance, but also their courage and loyalty. We have a long history of grand competitions where riders display their animals and their skills, and I wanted to bring such an event to Zír Aktar's visitors.

'If you think you can handle one of our fine steeds, you are welcome to give our race course a try. I warn you though, only the most skilled of riders will be able to master such a tricky path in the amount of time we have allotted.

'The rules of the race are very simple -- race through each gate, and you must not fall off your steed before the time runs out. You will find obstacles and challenging terrain, but it is also a wonderful way to see the island. When you see two gates next to one another, you must choose which path to take, be it high or low. Each path has its own benefits and hinderances.

'Do you feel up for this challenge? Only the most spirited riders should even attempt such a feat! It is sure to be very dangerous, but you have an adventurous look to you.''You should hurry and mount your horse or you will fail the race!''Excellent riding, ${PLAYER}! I am very impressed. Take these tokens in reward of your achievement!'Billina is certain that a plague of wolves has come to the Shire and is stealing chickens.Billina is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

Billina wishes to speak with you.There are chicken coops at Brownlock's Farm on the road east and slightly north to Needlehole, Cotton's Farm to the east in Bywater, and Farmer Maggot's farm to the east and south along the Brandywine River.

Billina has asked you to warn the other chicken coops in the Shire about the threat of wolves.Visit Brownlock's coopVisit Maggot's coopVisit Cotton's coop'Why hello again. I was beginning to think you wouldn't come back after you brought me that nice present. I thought maybe you were taken by one of those terrible wolves.

'Time was when we didn't have to worry about wolves. There were so few and the farmer would always drive them off when they did try to sneak into the coop.  

'But more and more of us have been disappearing lately; I think that it may be wolf-mischief. We need a brave rooster such as yourself to go warn the other coops and find out exactly what is going on! There are coops at Brownlocks' Farm to the east and slightly north on the road to Needlehole, Cotton's Farm to the east in Bywater, and Bamfurlong far to the east and south along the river.''Wolves? Of course, I have seen the wolves! Have you looked around? Almost our entire coop has been taken!

'There have been some folk carrying off the survivors down to Waymeet, though.''What is that now? Wolves, no, of course not, not here in the Shire. I have heard rumours of them, yes, but they are just that, rumours.

'Chickens get to talking, you know, and can come up with wild, fanciful stories. The only Wolf on this farm is a dog! Of course, the farmer's dogs may be why we have no wolves. They are good protectors.''Wolves here, in the Shire? Wolves have not dared to venture in so far since the old times, or so legends tell.

'I don't rightly know what we could do about such an attack. If there is anything that we can do here, let us know. Give my regards to Billina.''You need to warn the other coops at Brownlock's Farm, Cotton's Farm, and Bamfurlong!'There is much to do during the Spring Festival! Participate often to earn wonderful gifts!

