'It is true. Hard to believe, I know. Could...could you please fetch me some more? I usually get mine in Celondim, where the Elves who tend the docks craft a fine strong thread.

'You are a good sort of ${RACE}, ${PLAYER}. Truly.''Oh...you're still here. Maybe you didn't hear me correctly: I am out of twine. Not wine. Not brine. Twine. Please get me some more.''Twine! Marvellous. I was beginning to wonder if you lost your way. Well, this should do for a short while, at least. My thanks, ${PLAYER}. You are more useful than you seem at first glance!'You ate the cheese!Eat Barrow-brieBy completing a great number of tasks, you are earning a reputation as someone with a 'can do' attitude and tolerant spirit.Complete tasks throughout Middle-earthPrince Durin of the Longbeards has declared his intention to re-take Gundabad for the dwarves. He needs heroes like you to win this war!(Optional) Report to a War Effort RecruiterYou are to report to Annâk-khurfu in the Elderslade. Mission Recruiter Stable-masters are available to deliver you there with haste.

Mission Recruiter Stable-masters can be found at Thorin's Gate, Gondamon, Bree-town, The Twenty-first Hall, Othrikar, Gabilshathûr, Glóin's Camp, Hrimbarg, Galtrev, The Dolven-view, Magh Ashtu, Járnfast, Erebor, and Minas Tirith (Midsummer).(Optional) Report to a War Effort RecruiterEnter Annâk-khurfu in the EldersladeSpeak to one of the guards in Annâk-khurfu for directions.Talk to one of the guards in Annâk-khurfuReport to Prince Durin in the War Room, on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.Talk to DurinReport to Commader Glóin in the War Room, on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.Talk to GlóinPrince Durin of the Longbeards has declared his intention to retake Gundabad for the dwarves! He needs heroes like you to aid in the war effort if there is any hope of succeeding against the Orc army.

If you wish to assist him, you should report to one of the War Effort Recruiters at dwarf settlements throughout Middle-earth. They will take you to Annâk-khurfu, Prince Durin's command centre in the Elderslade. War Effort Recruiters can be found at Thorin's Gate, Gondamon, Bree-town, The Twenty-first Hall, Othrikar, Gabilshathûr, Glóin's Camp, Hrimbarg, Galtrev, The Dolven-view, Magh Ashtu, Járnfast, Erebor, and Minas Tirith (Midsummer).'Hail, ${PLAYER}! Have you come to heed the summons to war? The Mission Recruiter Stable-masters' goats can take you to Prince Durin at Annâk-khurfu with much haste!''Welcome, adventurer! Our prince's call to war must have reached you! He will wish to speak with you at once. Proceed upstairs to the War Room with haste!''Welcome, ${PLAYER}. I am glad to have the assistance of brave adventurers such as you. There is much to do before the battle to come.

'We face a massive army of Orcs, trolls, wargs, goblins, and who knows what other foul creatures lurk in that mountain stronghold. Their leader is Gorgar the Ruthless, son of Bolg, and grandson of Azog. All dwarves know these names, for we faced those vile commanders in the last great War of Dwarves and Orcs.

'I have an army of Longbeards, Zhélruka, and even a few Stout-axes behind me, but I fear our enemies far outnumber us. We must be clever, and do what we can to weaken our foes before we engage them on the battlefield. Report to one of my commanders in charge of this war effort, the Longbeard hero Glóin. He will direct your efforts where they are needed most.''Greetings, ${PLAYER}. Have you come to lend aid to the war effort? Good, there is no time to delay!'The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has requested your assistance in completing a series of missions on their behalf.Seek out and push forward the war effort by completing 'The War Effort: Missions for the Cause' several times.Complete 'March on Gundabad: Missions for the Cause' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Seek out and speak to Elóf regarding your completion of several missions.Speak to Elóf'We have need of your assistance in completing a series of missions for the on-going war effort.

'The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has been making headway towards Gundabad, but their troops are spread too thin to accomplish all that is needed to be done.

'Seek out and complete several of these missions to assist our efforts.''We wish to thank you for your hard work towards the war effort. Your good deeds shall help secure our foothold into Gundabad itself!'Your contribution to the war effort has turned the tide in favour of the dwarves!The dwarves wish to thank you for your hard work!

You should talk to Ausma and Hórin in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to AusmaTalk to HórinPrince Durin wishes to reward you for your hard work.

You should talk to Durin in Annâk-khurfu.Talk to Durin'${PLAYER}, your efforts have done what we could only hope: you turned the tide of the war in our favour! We have confirmed that Gorgar's forces have all pulled back to defend Gundabad. The time for the final battle is soon upon us. The others wish to speak with you, and Prince Durin has said he plans to reward you for all your hard work. The Longbeards owe you a great debt, friend!''${PLAYER}, as reward for your efforts, I grant you the rank of Azghzabad, and name you Hero of Durin's Folk. You will have a place in my vanguard as we lead the attack on Gorgar's forces and reclaim Gundabad!

'I must sincerely thank you for your part in this campaign. The war has not yet been won, but because of your actions, we no longer face insurmountable odds. Battle is soon upon us, and I plan to lead this grand army of dwarves to victory!

'You are a great hero, ${PLAYER}, and must receive a hero's reward. Hail, ${PLAYER}, Hero of Durin's Folk!''I am not one for all this pomp and high praise, but I must admit, it has been a pleasure working with you, ${PLAYER}. May we fight side by side in the battle to come, and together see Gorgar dead at last!''${PLAYER}!'

The dwarf grabs your hand and gives it a hearty shake.

'We have done it! Gorgar's forces are on their last legs, and a great battle is upon us! I swell with pride just imagining it. Let us fight side by side when the time comes, and slay many Orcs together. We will reclaim Gundabad! For the Zhélruka!'By completing this quest, you will receive a Wastes endgame allowance.'Get endgame currency for the Wastes!''Ride back here like a bunny if you need more!'You have arrived in Winter-home, and Guard Kember has offered to give you a tour of the many sights to be seen.

