You should return to Mayor Goodnough now that you have finished your tour of Winter-home's many events.Return to Mayor Goodnough to finish your tour'Hello there! New to the Frostbluff, are you? Well, you've come at the finest time of year. I just hope you behave yourself, or else you'll be hearing from me!

'I'm sure you'll have a wonderful time, though. The mayor employs me to see to it that everyone keeps the peace so that you patrons can have the best possible experience during Yule.

'You should begin by speaking to Ona Kay who runs the Eating Contest. All good celebrations should start with a full belly of delicious food!''Speak with Ona Kay at the Eating Contest to begin your tour!''Good day to you! I'm Ona, the Announcer for the first station at the Eating Contest. There are many more stations, of course, and I hope you will be able to visit all of them before you get too full.

'What is a festival without wonderfully excessive amounts of food? I doubt you will find a bigger feast anywhere in Middle-earth than here in Winter-home.

'You should speak next to the mayor. The Festival is here thanks to his efforts, and he wishes to greet all of his guests personally.''Go ahead, my friend. Familiarize yourself with the activities of a fine Yule. You may want to speak with Mayor Goodnough first.''Hail, Travelling ${CLASS}! Welcome, welcome! And pray, tell all your friends to come visit as well! We have spared no expense for this Yule's festival.

'I am Winston Goodnough, the mayor of this town. Please, stay as long as you like! Try everything, taste everything!

'Why don't you go take a look at all the events? Come back and see me when you have explored.''You should speak with Mrs. Goodnough. She has had a great hand in putting together this year's festival!''Greetings, greetings. You are most welcome here, to be sure. I am Carolyn Goodnough, and my husband and I are very thrilled to have so many interested patrons and patronesses here at our Yule Celebration this year.

'I'll not take up any more of your time; you should continue your tour around our beautiful town.''Continue your tour of our beautiful town and the yule festivities!''Oh my goodness! I'm sorry, I'm only a servant. The Mayor surely doesn't need you to talk to me.

'I'll not take up any more of your time; but perhaps you'd like to see the games we have to offer? It's a bit of a walk, but you should go talk to Cecil Voller, the host of the Snowball Fight.

'Cecil is a ways north of the town, but I've heard that the snowball fights are well worth the trip.''You should speak with Cecil Voller at the Snowball Field... I must go now!''Ah, hello! I see you've trekked down to the Snowball Field during your tour of town! This is where folks come to throw freezing missiles at one another. 

'I hope you'll come back when you've finished your tour. The mayor is most particular about all patrons seeing all there is to see before they get distracted....''You should head to the theatre and speak with the representative of G.L.O.B.E.''Oh, hello! Are you interested in the theatre? We have quite a show that we're putting on this Yule, and we've travelled all the way from the Shire!

'Make sure you come back and see the show when you're finished with your tour of town. I know you won't be disappointed.

'Well, I am the last stop on your tour. You should return to the mayor. Do come back to see our wonderful show!''Be careful if you wander in to the south-west corner of town... there's unsavoury folk among the workers.''What do you want, O Revered Patron?  Have you come to show off your silver and gold and your fat belly?  Well, show away. We earn our meagre bread while you stuff your faces and play in the snow.

'You are not welcome in Winter-home, not to all of its residents. We slave so that the Mayor can be rich, and so that he can throw marvellous parties for you all. Begone! We are not welcome among you, and you are not welcome among us!''Perhaps Daley will speak with you, but I have no desire to.''Please, pardon my friend. It is a hard winter, and there is less money and bread to go around than usual. But that is no cause to be uncivil to the guests of this town.

'Life can be cruel here, as you can plainly see, but I count myself among the lucky. Those who cannot work go even colder and hungrier than we.

'I am sure you are more welcome among us than Gareth implied; we are a friendly folk. You are welcome to visit any time you wish. I hope you enjoy your time in our little town!''When you speak again with Mayor Goodnough, you shouldn't mention talking to me... it would not be to your benefit.''So, you've seen all of the events? We have a wonderful little town, do we not? Perfectly suited for all your festival needs. You don't need to waste any more time talking to me. Go enjoy! Eat! Play! Watch theatre!'Farmer Sandson is not looking. Now is your chance to escape.This may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.Travel to The CarrockThe Vales of Anduin is a lovely place.Find the BeorninghúsThis may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.Get to Lake Town!This may be a wonderful time to explore Middle-earth.Travel to Erebor, the Lonely MountainErebor is a lovely place.Sit on the throne under the mountainYou have earned the Thespian title.Obtain Title Writ - ThespianYou have earned the Thespian title by participating in the Yule Festival Play.To earn the title of Thespian, you must be chosen to perform all three roles in the Yule Festival play.Perform the Extra's role in the Yule Festival playPerform the Protagonist's role in the Yule Festival playPerform the Villian's role in the Yule Festival playBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of Thorin's Hall.'Hullo! Would you like to be an "Acquaintance" of Thorin's Hall? Well look no further! Completion of this quest should do just that for you.

