You should being the casks of ale to Merilien.'Wedding guests are a thirsty lot, and we shall serve nothing less than the city’s finest ales at our events. I have put in orders with the best taverns in the city for barrels of their choicest ales. Go and fetch them, if you would. It would save me a great deal of time.''Ah, you must be here for Merilien's order. The barrel is just over there next to the M- er, next to Oli, as the hobbit lords named her. Just look for the tusks! You can't miss it.''Hmmm? Oh yes, a cask of my finest! This is no Beren's Blood, I'll have you know! Merilien has much better taste of course. The barrel is just up there, with our other supplies.''You must be here for Merilien's order. Wouldn't do to be late for her now would it?'

The barkeep gives you a knowing wink.

'The cask you have come for is in the northern storeroom. Don't fall into the well, now, you hear?''Oh yes, I have her shipment. You shall find it downstairs, in the kitchen. Just... mind yourself down there. This establishment is a rougher place than I am used to.''Ah, excellent. Good work! While I am not fond of the brew myself, it is always in high demand for my events.'For a short while every year, rare flowers bloom throughout Middle-earth. Avery Crabapple has a need for your assistance during this special event.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Avery Crabapple is in the Market Square of Bree.

You should speak with Avery Crabapple, as you have been asked to help him with a very difficult task during the flower-blooming season.Speak with Avery Crabapple during the Flower-blooming Season'Why, what luck!  I've heard tell that Avery Crabapple, a man of Bree, is in need of some assistance. It's the annual week of flowers, when the loveliest local flowers bloom in Ered Luin, the Shire, and Bree.  Avery was looking for a person of some high regard to assist him. I think you are just the person! Go speak to him if you have the time. You'll find him in the Market Square in Bree.''Ah, Spring! The scent of flowers is in the air.  Why, they are at their most bountiful now out of all weeks of the year and are blooming all through Ered Luin, the Shire, and Bree. Avery Crabapple in Bree-town was looking for someone to help him out of a pickle, and I think you look just the sort!  Go speak to him if you have the time. You'll find him in the Market Square in Bree.''Why, how fortuitous! You appear to be just the person.  Avery Crabapple, a friend of mine in Bree, was looking for someone of your renown to help him.  Even the most stalwart of persons can get swept away in the springtime, especially with all the lovely flowers blooming.  The smell of flowers and romance is in the air!  Go speak to Avery if you have the time, you'll find him in the Market Square in Bree.''Avery is in Bree, somewhere in the Market Square.  I do hope you can help him!''You should speak to Avery. I'm sure you can find him in Bree's Market Square.''I hope you're able to help Avery out of his predicament! He should be found in the Market Square in Bree.''Are you the local hero, ${PLAYER}, of whom I've heard so much? I'm mightily glad you've made it in time for the Flower-blooming season! I have an urgent need for help, you see....'You have been roundly knocked about by your opponents.Is this the Spring Festival? Where is the maze?Successfully complete the Mightiest Blow -- Expert questEarn reputation with the People of Wildermore.Speak with Ransroth.Speak with Ransroth'I too wish to be better acquainted with the People of Wildermore.''Power to the People of Wildermore.'Earn reputation with the People of Wildermore.Speak with Ransroth.Speak with Ransroth'I too wish to be better acquainted with the People of Wildermore.''Power to the People of Wildermore.'Earn reputation with the People of Wildermore.Speak with Ransroth.Speak with Ransroth'I too wish to be better acquainted with the People of Wildermore.''Power to the People of Wildermore.'Earn reputation with the People of Wildermore.Speak with Ransroth.Speak with Ransroth'I too wish to be better acquainted with the People of Wildermore.''Power to the People of Wildermore.'Earn reputation with the Survivors of Wildermore.You should speak with Ransroth to continue.Speak with Ransroth'I too wish to be better acquainted with the Survivors of Wildermore.''For the Survivors of Wildermore!'Earn reputation with the Survivors of Wildermore.You should speak with Ransroth to continue.Speak with Ransroth'I too wish to be better acquainted with the Survivors of Wildermore.''For the Survivors of Wildermore!'Earn reputation with the Survivors of Wildermore.You should speak with Ransroth to continue.Speak with Ransroth'I too wish to be better acquainted with the Survivors of Wildermore.''For the Survivors of Wildermore!'Earn reputation with the Survivors of Wildermore.You should speak with Ransroth to continue.Speak with Ransroth'I too wish to be better acquainted with the Survivors of Wildermore.''For the Survivors of Wildermore!'By completing this quest, you will receive a Wildwood currency allowance.'Get barter currency for Wildwood!''Ride back here like a bunny if you need more!'You have completed your collection of Winter-time equines.You have completed your collection of Winter-time equines.Mount the Yule Festival HorseMount the Yule Festival Snow HorseMount the Yule Festival Glittering HorseMount the Yule Festival Frosty HorseMount the Yule Festival Snowy HorseYou have completed your collection of Winter-time equines.You have completed your collection of Winter-time equines.Mount the Yule Festival PonyMount the Yule Festival Snow PonyMount the Yule Festival Glittering PonyMount the Yule Festival Frosty PonyMount the Yule Festival Snowy PonyYour narratives combine the chill of a winter night and the turbulence of the fiercest storm.Use Fury of the Storm or Chill of Winter skillsYour narratives combine the chill of a winter night and the turbulence of the fiercest storm.Use Fury of Storm skillsSometimes you can't afford mistakes.Use Sure StrikeA beleaguered marriage-wright, Melthend, has asked you to bake some strawberry buns for an upcoming ceremony.The crafting recipe for the strawberry buns can be bartered for from the marriage-wright, Melthend.

