<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>You have been asked to inquire among the Hobbiton-folk for an explanation of Lobelia's post as Yule-planner.Sandyman's Mill is north of the bridge over the Water in Hobbiton.

Ted Sandyman's unusual behaviour might suggest a need to search Sandyman's Mill for anything out of the ordinary.Search Sandyman's Mill for anything out of the ordinaryWill Whitfoot is at the Town Hole in Michel Delving, far to the west of Hobbiton.

You should report your findings to Will Whitfoot, the Mayor of the Shire.'Why hullo there! I am guessing you have come about the rumours? Well, I am afraid they are true; Lobelia Sackville-Baggins is the official Yule-planner for the Hobbiton Yule-feast! It's dreadful, simply dreadful! She has already announced that we will be getting nothing more than harvest-vegetables at the feast. The gall of some folk!

'Lobelia also told us that we ought to end the festival early this year, what with all the roustabouts that have been coming in...says it isn't safe for decent folk to stay up late outdoors. Naught but vegetables and an early bed...what is a respectable hobbit to do?

'What's more, no one in Hobbiton is rightly sure how she came by the title. For years, old Mad Baggins held the position, and in turn Frodo Baggins took it after his disappearance. Something isn't right about the whole affair. Do you think you would be able to help us set things to rights?''It's bad enough that Lobelia has got her hands on old Mr. Bilbo's hole and has taken to threatening her neighbours and such, but now she has got herself made the official Yule-planner! She'll ruin the holiday, and that's no mistake.

'That Lotho of hers don't take truck with festive drinks and parties, and she loves that boy enough to make a mess of it all for him. What's a Yule-feast without a good mug, I asks? And what is all this nonsense about ending the feast early this year?

'It's bad business, ${PLAYER}. Mark my words, she'll ruin it for us all. Perhaps you could see about dealing with the problem on behalf of us Hobbiton-folk?''Have you heard? Old Lobelia Sackville-Baggins has gone and got herself made the official Yule-planner this year! It's dreadful, I says. Old Bilbo at least knew how to throw a particularly fine feast -- if a bit odd -- but Lobelia, now....

'She wants to serve vegetables and tea! Fine for a garden-party, but a Yule-feast? I daresay it's an outrage!

'It's that Lotho's doing, I'd lay odds. He needs a good lesson taught, but I guess no-one's got the courage. Perhaps you might talk to Old Flourdumpling, old Whitfoot the Mayor, about finding someone else?''After all her fuss about my pies, Lobelia was made the official Yule-planner. Now she wants to leave my pies out of the feast altogether! I'm not usually one to brag, but my pies are well thought of in Hobbiton, and I just don't think it fair that they should be left out...in favour of vegetables!

'Why I'm sure Opal Goodbody put her up to this outrage...she never did like me. Well, I can deal with her, but who is going to deal with Lobelia?

'Maybe you would find out how she managed to get her position and can find a way to do something about it? It would be a blessing to all of Hobbiton if you could!''I think it is just delightful that Lobelia was made the official Yule-planner this year! She has such a wise head on her shoulders. I know that Lotho has been out and about, spending large amounts of money...I'm sure it's going towards the feast!

'I'm sure all those rumours about Lobelia wanting vegetables and tea and an early bedtime for the feast is foolishness. Lobelia is a hobbit, after all...what else could a hobbit ask for than a wonderful feast?

'Well, I'm sure all those tom-fools begging Old Flourdumpling to remove Lobelia from her position are just jealous. You wouldn't happen to be one of them would you?''It's a sad day, my friend. Here I thought there would be orders going to and from Bag End with no end when Lobelia was made the Yule-planner, but there ain't been no mail at all; no letters, no provender, no gifts, no nothing.

'Well, Hobbiton will be bad off this year if Lobelia stays in her position. What's to become of the Yule-feast? It's a pity, it is.

'Hey, maybe you could look into her appointment? It smells a bit fishy to me...what with all the ruckus in the Southfarthing, and this Chief buying up land in the Northfarthing. It would be nice to have something to celebrate, and Lobelia being removed from her position would certainly be something to celebrate!''Old Lobelia has been pestering the Shirriffs about maintaining order during this year's Yule-feast. Who made her the boss anyway? Well, I suppose Mayor Whitfoot did, but that doesn't mean I have to like it.

'She wants all the inns closed during the feast this year and plans on having tea instead of beer! Can you believe it? Well, open or closed, I'll be sitting right here in The Ivy Bush come Yule.

'Maybe you would ask around and find out how exactly Lobelia managed to worm her way into Old Flourdumpling's good graces?''It's hard enough managing a stable in the Shire, but when I heard that Lobelia Sackville-Baggins was made the official Yule-planner this year, I almost climbed on one of my ponies and rode out of Hobbiton as quick as I could. It's a poor joke, if you ask me. What good can come of it?

'Lobelia has all the joy and capacity for pleasantry as a spoiled egg. It smells, I tell you, and the rumours of her plans for the feast smell worse.

'Perhaps you could look into her appointment? There has to be a mistake; I'm sure of it!''Shut me down for Yule, that's what she wants to do! Who? Why that Lobelia Sackville-Baggins! She was made official Yule-planner, if you can believe it!

'Why what's a feast without good cheer? And how do you get good cheer without an inn? It's a terrible mistake...it has to be!

'Maybe you would go find out the truth behind these rumours? It's madness, I tell you!''The Yule feast? Why my dad and I were personally invited by Lotho Sackville-Baggins, but why I would tell the likes of you anything more is beyond me.

'Now be off! I have important things to be doing up at the mill without the likes of you snooping about my business.''I'm sorry, but I haven't heard anything about how Lobelia came by the Yule-planner post.  

'Whatever shall we do? Yule will be ruined if Lobelia has her way!''Lobelia's post as Yule-planner? No, I haven't heard anything as to how she came by it.''Lobelia? I heard she was up to some mischief away in Michel Delving...I'm sure that's how she came by the position.''I haven't heard aught else save that we're all to eat our vegetables and get a proper nights rest. The cheek of it!''If you need any help looking for information, I might be able to help you after another pint or two.''I have heard a thing or two, but I am not one to spread rumours.

'But if you have to know, I heard she paid off Old Flourdumpling off in Michel Delving for the position.''Sorry, I haven't heard anything.''Lobelia took a pony-cart up to Michel Delving maybe a month ago, but that is all I know.''Lobelia has been coming and going on festival business, but I haven't heard how she came to the job.''The Yule-feast will be simply wonderful this year! The best that has been held for many a long season; leastwise, better than any that old fool Bilbo ever planned, that's for certain.''Be off! Can't you see we have a great deal of planning left to do before the Yule-feast?''Lobelia Sackville-Baggins is trying to cheat Hobbiton out of their Yule-feast? I would love to help, but I fear my hands are tied in this matter.

'Lobelia came not a month ago seeking the laws relating to local Hobbiton feasts. If I remember correctly the Hobbiton-law states: Whosoever resides in the Hill at Bag End shall be charged with the planning and coordination of all local feasts and festival-activities and shall preside over said feasts in the absence of the Mayor.

'This law being a holdover from when the Baggins family was the chief residence of the Hill. Because the law was not changed or a new planner appointed, there is simply nothing I can do.'Your trainer wants you to use your new skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.Use <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>on the training-dummy nearby. 

HINT:

Captains rely on their <rgb=#00ff00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put them into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb>. While in this state, Captains can use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>, an effective attack that deals a great deal of damage. Attack the <rgb=#ff0000>Training Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00FF00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put you into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb> and then attack the dummy with your <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>.Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Battle Shout</rgb> on the training-dummy, then strike it with your skill <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>The Captain Trainer is in the training grounds of Archet, very near the gate.

Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.Talk to the Captain Trainer in Archet'I welcome you to Archet, fellow Captain! I specialize in teaching warriors such as yourself useful skills and abilities. I presume you are here for just such a purpose, so here is a word of advice:

'Remember, a Captain does not best serve his companions by running recklessly into the fray. Nay, it is when he stands behind and directs the efforts of his fellows that he truly shines. There he can see weaknesses in his enemies or press his companions forwards and inspire them to victory.

'Show me your skill by using <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>.'

HINT:

Captains rely on their <rgb=#00ff00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put them into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb>. While in this state, Captains can use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>, an effective attack that deals a great deal of damage. Attack the <rgb=#ff0000>Training Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00FF00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put you into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb> and then attack the dummy with your <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>.'Strike the training-dummy with your new skill and return to me. We must make certain that you are prepared to stand against the dangers of Middle-earth.'

HINT:

Captains rely on their <rgb=#00ff00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put them into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb>. While in this state, Captains can use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>, an effective attack that deals a great deal of damage. Attack the <rgb=#ff0000>Training Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00FF00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put you into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb> and then attack the dummy with your <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!  As you grow, you will learn additional skills. Good luck!'Your trainer wants you to use your new skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.Speak with the trainer again and learn the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Shield Swipe</rgb>. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. 

<rgb=#00ff00>NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Guardian Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel, or double-click the skill, and you will successfully purchase the skill.</rgb>

HINT:

Guardians rely on <rgb=#ffff00>Reactive Skills</rgb> to deal damage and generate <rgb=#ff0000>Threat</rgb> against their enemies.  <rgb=#00ff00>Shield Swipe</rgb> requires that the Guardian <rgb=#ffff00>Block</rgb> an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill.  Head over to the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummies</rgb> to the north of the trainer and attack it until you successfully block one of their attacks.  If you're having trouble getting a block, try using <rgb=#00ff00>Guardian's Ward</rgb> to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks.  Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield Swipe</rgb> skill.  Strike the <rgb=#ff0000>Targeting Dummy</rgb> with <rgb=#00ff00>Shield Swipe</rgb>.Strike the training-dummy with Shield SwipeNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell her of your success.Talk to the Guardian Trainer in EdhelionDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion.

You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.Talk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion'Even in this fallen refuge there are threats which we must confront. Without the watchful eye and care of the Elves, Edhelion has become home to many unnatural creatures. You will need to know how to defend yourself and defeat these threats.

'You must learn skills from others, like myself. We can guide you through your training and help you become stronger.

'Learn the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Shield Swipe</rgb> from me and show me that my teaching has given you mastery by striking the training-dummy nearby.'

HINT:

Guardians rely on <rgb=#ffff00>Reactive Skills</rgb> to deal damage and generate <rgb=#ff0000>Threat</rgb> against their enemies.  <rgb=#00ff00>Shield Swipe</rgb> requires that the Guardian <rgb=#ffff00>Block</rgb> an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill.  Head over to the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummies</rgb> to the north of the trainer and attack it until you successfully block one of their attacks.  If you're having trouble getting a block, try using <rgb=#00ff00>Guardian's Ward</rgb> to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks.  Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield Swipe</rgb> skill.  Strike the <rgb=#ff0000>Targeting Dummy</rgb> with <rgb=#00ff00>Shield Swipe</rgb>.'I am pleased to know that you have completed your meditation and training. The road ahead is filled with many challenges, and we must all prepare ourselves for what is to come. I think that this lesson will be one that remains with you.''Yes, I sensed that you were well-prepared, ${PLAYER}. Remember, we must work to reclaim this land and while we have a tentative peace with the dwarves in the valley below, we cannot overlook the lessons of the past and the betrayal that came at their hands.

'Speak with Dorongúr and tell him that I believe you are ready.''Strike the training-dummy with your new skill, then return to me. We must make certain that you are prepared to stand against the dangers of Middle-earth.'

