HINT:

Guardians rely on <rgb=#ffff00>Reactive Skills</rgb> to deal damage and generate <rgb=#ff0000>Threat</rgb> against their enemies.  <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> requires that the Guardian <rgb=#ffff00>Block</rgb> an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill.  Head over to the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-dummies</rgb> to the north and attack one until you successfully block one of its attacks.  If you're having trouble getting a block, try using <rgb=#00ff00>Guardian's Ward</rgb> to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks.  Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> skill.  Strike the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-dummy</rgb> with <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb>.Strike the training-dummy with 'Shield-swipe'The Guardian Trainer is in the training ground in Archet.

Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell her of your success.Talk to the Guardian Trainer in Archet'I am here to help you learn how to use skills that will make you a more powerful Guardian. As you gain levels, more skills will become available to you.'

HINT: Guardians rely on <rgb=#ffff00>Reactive Skills</rgb> to deal damage and generate <rgb=#ff0000>Threat</rgb> against their enemies. <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> requires that the Guardian <rgb=#ffff00>Block</rgb> an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill. Head over to the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-dummies</rgb> to the north and attack one until you successfully block one of its attacks. If you're having trouble getting a block, try using <rgb=#00ff00>Guardian's Ward</rgb> to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks. Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> skill.  Strike the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-dummy</rgb> with <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb>.'Strike the training-dummy with your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> skill and return to me. We must make certain that you are prepared to stand against the dangers of Middle-earth.'

HINT:

Guardians rely on <rgb=#ffff00>Reactive Skills</rgb> to deal damage and generate <rgb=#ff0000>Threat</rgb> against their enemies.  <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> requires that the Guardian <rgb=#ffff00>Block</rgb> an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill.  Head over to the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-dummies</rgb> to the north and attack one until you successfully block one of its attacks.  If you're having trouble getting a block, try using <rgb=#00ff00>Guardian's Ward</rgb> to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks.  Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> skill.  Strike the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-dummy</rgb> with <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb>.'Well done, ${PLAYER}! As you grow as a ${CLASS}, you will find that there are many more powerful new skills in store for you. Good luck!'Your trainer wants you to use your new skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.HINT:

Minstrels use <rgb=#ffff00>Ballads</rgb> to attack their enemies, lightly heal their fellows and empower themselves. These skills operate on a rotating system that allows the minstrel to have three special buffs on themselves at any time. After the third buff is applied the next <rgb=#ffff00>Ballad</rgb> played will overwrite the first, then the second and so on.Use Major Ballad while in combat with the Training DummyThe Minstrel Trainer is in Archet, west of the training grounds.

Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.Talk to the Minstrel Trainer in Archet'A good day to you! I am pleased to find another Minstrel here in Archet. I should be happy to share what skills I have with you. First, though, I will give you some small advice, if you are willing to lend an ear to it.

'As you may already know, a Minstrel possesses a great power...the power to stir the spirit and raise hopes when all seems lost. When the spirit is roused, the body soon follows! A good Minstrel heals themselves and their fellows, staving off even the most dire wounds.

'Demonstrate your mastery by entering combat with the training-dummy nearby, then using the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Major Ballad</rgb>.'

HINT:

Minstrels use <rgb=#ffff00>Ballads</rgb> to attack their enemies, lightly heal their fellows and empower themselves. These skills operate on a rotating system that allows the minstrel to have three special buffs on themselves at any time. After the third buff is applied the next <rgb=#ffff00>Ballad</rgb> played will overwrite the first, then the second and so on.'Enter combat with the training-dummy and then use your new skill and return to me. We must make certain that you are prepared to stand against the dangers of Middle-earth.'

HINT:

Minstrels use <rgb=#ffff00>Ballads</rgb> to attack their enemies, lightly heal their fellows and empower themselves. These skills operate on a rotating system that allows the minstrel to have three special buffs on themselves at any time. After the third buff is applied the next <rgb=#ffff00>Ballad</rgb> played will overwrite the first, then the second and so on.'Well done, ${PLAYER}! Make sure you visit a trainer often as you advance in your role as a ${CLASS}. As you grow, you will find that trainers such as myself may have important tasks and bits of wisdom for you. Good luck!'Your trainer wants you to use your new skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.Speak with the trainer again and learn the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb>. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. 

<rgb=#00ff00>NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Warden Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel, or double-click the skill, and you will successfully purchase the skill.</rgb>

HINT:

Wardens use combinations of their basic skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Quick Thrust</rgb> and <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-Bash</rgb> to build more powerful <rgb=#ffff00>Gambit</rgb> attacks.  To use your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> skill, attack a <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00ff00>Quick Thrust</rgb> ability twice.  This should cause your <rgb=#00ff00>Gambit Default</rgb> skill to change into your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> skill.  Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> ability to strike a <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummy</rgb>.Use the skill Deft Strike on a training-dummyNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell him of your success.Talk to the Warden Trainer in EdhelionDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion.

You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.Talk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion'Even in this fallen refuge, there are threats that we must confront. Without the watchful eye and care of the Elves, Edhelion has become home to many unnatural creatures. You will need to know how to defend yourself and defeat these threats.

'You must learn skills from others, like myself. We can guide you through your training and help you become stronger.

'Learn the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> from me and show me that my teaching has given you mastery by striking the training-dummy nearby.'

HINT:

Wardens use combinations of their basic skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Quick Thrust</rgb> and <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-Bash</rgb> to build more powerful <rgb=#ffff00>Gambit</rgb> attacks.  To use your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> skill, attack a <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00ff00>Quick Thrust</rgb> ability twice.  This should cause your <rgb=#00ff00>Gambit Default</rgb> skill to change into your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> skill.  Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> ability to strike a <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummy</rgb>.'I am pleased to know that you have completed your meditation and training. The road ahead is filled with many challenges, and we must all prepare ourselves for what is to come. I think that this lesson will be one that remains with you.''Yes, I sensed that you were well-prepared, ${PLAYER}. Remember, we must work to reclaim this land, and while we have a tentative peace with the dwarves in the valley below, we cannot overlook the lessons of the past and the betrayal that came at their hands.

'Speak with Dorongúr and tell him that I believe you are ready.''Strike the training-dummy with your new skill and return to me. We must make certain that you are prepared to stand against the dangers of Middle-earth.'

HINT:

Wardens use combinations of their basic skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Quick Thrust</rgb> and <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-Bash</rgb> to build more powerful <rgb=#ffff00>Gambit</rgb> attacks.  To use your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> skill, attack a <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00ff00>Quick Thrust</rgb> ability twice.  This should cause your <rgb=#00ff00>Gambit Default</rgb> skill to change into your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> skill.  Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Deft Strike</rgb> ability to strike a <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummy</rgb>.'I will teach you more when you are ready to learn. For the moment, you should speak with Dorongúr.'Jon Brackenbrook, the son of the captain who organized Archet's garrison, feared the presence of a traitor within the garrison's ranks. The Ranger Amdir confirmed Jon's suspicions at the Blackwolds' camp.Captain Brackenbrook commands the garrison from The Mad Badger Inn to the south of Amdir.

Amdir fears that Captain Brackenbrook will not heed his tidings of the traitor Calder Cob, but hopes that if the news comes from you, he will listen.Amdir rests against the building north of The Mad Badger Inn.

Captain Brackenbrook was not willing to hear what you had to say about Calder Cob. Instead, he told you to tell Amdir to stay out of Archet's troubles, after suggesting you help the local farms fend off wolves.'As I believe I mentioned to you before, I came to Archet to learn what connexion the Blackwolds had to the Nazgûl. Here I met Jon Brackenbrook, Captain Brackenbrook's son. It was from him that I learned the location of the Blackwolds' camp and of Celandine and Mundo's capture.

'Jon and his father recently had a terrible falling out. Jon believed that a member of the Captain's garrison, Calder Cob, was in league with the Blackwold brigands. Before I came to you, I witnessed Cob and Éogan discussing a raid on the town. Jon's suspicions are correct, and his father must be warned.

'Captain Brackenbrook, like many, distrusts Rangers and will not heed anything I have to say. Perhaps, if the news comes from you, he will listen. He commands the garrison from The Mad Badger. The entrance is just to the south there, up those steps.''Captain Brackenbrook is set in his ways and will not heed my words. Nevertheless, he must be informed that Calder Cob is playing him the fool.''You are the one who brought the Ranger back to Archet? My son was foolish enough to befriend him and dared accuse one of my finest guards of betrayal.

'If you are here to tell me the same tale, I say be off with you. Calder Cob personally apprehended Otto, the leader of the Blackwolds. He is in the stocks now if you would like to see him. In the last week, he has captured two more brigands, so I will hear no more of this traitor nonsense.

'If you wish to aid Archet, take up arms and make your way to the sheep-farm to the south and west and help Dirk Mudbrick against the wolves that plague the farmers! And tell that Ranger friend of yours to mind his own concerns.''I have no time for nonsense. The Blackwolds are leaderless, and soon I'll have these townsfolk ready to assail the brigands' encampment. That will end their threat once and for all!''I had feared this may happen. Captain Brackenbrook is a good man, but set in his ways.

'Calder Cob has done his job too well. We will need to find another way to expose Cob's treachery.'Your trainer wants you to use your new skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.Enter Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Surprise Strike</rgb> skill against the nearby training dummy.

<rgb=#00ff00>HINT:

Burglars benefit greatly from <rgb=#ffff00>Critical Strikes</rgb> and <rgb=#ffff00>Devastating Blows</rgb>. Scoring such hits will allow them to use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Double-edged Strike</rgb>. In addition, many Burglar skills benefit from being in <rgb=#ffff00>Stealth</rgb>.

Try attacking a <rgb=#ff0000>training-dummy</rgb> from <rgb=#ffff00>Stealth</rgb> with <rgb=#ffff00>Surprise Strike</rgb> to inflict even more damage. </rgb>Strike the training-dummy with Surprise StrikeThe Burglar Trainer is in Archet, west of the training grounds.

Now that you have successfully used your Surprise Strike, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.Talk to the Burglar Trainer in Archet'So you want to learn the ways of the burglar? Well, I'm the trainer for you! I don't mind sharing a few tricks with you, but before I do, there's a bit of advice.

'Before getting into a fight, study your enemy's weaknesses, for they can often be used against him. Approaching a foe from Stealth allows many of your attacks to be more potent. Also, never forget that your enemy's greatest weakness is his mind, more often than not.

'Show me me you've learned my lessons. <rgb=#00ff00>Approach the Training-dummy nearby, and strike it with Surprise Strike.</rgb>'

<rgb=#00ff00>HINT:

Burglars benefit greatly from <rgb=#ffff00>Critical Strikes</rgb> and <rgb=#ffff00>Devastating Blows</rgb>. Scoring such hits will allow them to use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Double-edged Strike</rgb>. In addition, many Burglar skills benefit from being in <rgb=#ffff00>Stealth</rgb>.

Try attacking a <rgb=#ff0000>training-dummy</rgb> from <rgb=#ffff00>Stealth</rgb> with <rgb=#ffff00>Surprise Strike</rgb> to inflict even more damage. </rgb>'Strike the training-dummy with your new skill and return to me. We must make certain that you are prepared to properly wield a blade.'

<rgb=#00ff00>HINT:

Burglars benefit greatly from <rgb=#ffff00>Critical Strikes</rgb> and <rgb=#ffff00>Devastating Blows</rgb>. Scoring such hits will allow them to use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Double-edged Strike</rgb>. In addition, many Burglar skills benefit from being in <rgb=#ffff00>Stealth</rgb>.

Try attacking a <rgb=#ff0000>training-dummy</rgb> from <rgb=#ffff00>Stealth</rgb> with <rgb=#ffff00>Surprise Strike</rgb> to inflict even more damage. </rgb>'Well done, ${PLAYER}! As you grow, you will learn even more powerful new skills to use in battle. Good luck!'The Guards of the Silver Deep are a group of dwarf-guardians charged by Thorin to ensure that the Silver Deep remains undisturbed.Olin may be found to the west of Frerin's Court.

Bolli asked you to find Olin, one of the Guards of the Silver Deep, and learn what he knows about the situation at Thorin's Hall.Talk to Olin'Before we left for the Lonely Mountain, Thorin asked a few dwarves to stay behind and guard the Silver Deep. They were led by Olin, and it was he who was charged with sending reports to King Dáin. Nobody had heard from Olin in quite a while...long enough to make us worried.

'Olin just returned and is resting to the west of Frerin's Court. You should speak with him and see if you can learn what he's been up to.''Go west of Frerin's Court and learn from Olin what has transpired in our absence.''A friendly face at last! You must help me, for I've been poisoned...no doubt by one of those ruffianly Dourhands. I'm weak as a babe...too weak to get help for myself. But a cure is...is near. You must get it for me!

'I must rest now...so very tired. I would tell you more of the Dourhands but I haven't the strength....'Strider seeks your aid, but recognizes that your path will be fraught with danger. He wishes for you to learn from a ${CLASS} who can help hone your skills.Strider suggested you train further before coming to Archet's defence.Strider can be found outside The Mad Badger Inn in the centre of Archet.

Now that you have spoken to the more experienced ${CLASS},  you should return to Strider.Talk to Strider in Archet'There is much to do, and you are new to this world of danger. As long as you wish to help Archet, it is most important that you hone your skills as a ${CLASS}.

'I would like you to assist me, but I wish to make sure you are ready for the evil trials you will face.''You must speak to your ${CLASS} trainer now, near the gate of Archet.

'The trainers wish to see you demonstrate your skills as a warrior. You should not try to take on the brigand threat if you are not prepared for battle.''Have you learned some new tricks of the ${CLASS}? I can see that you have; you seem more confident now.

'You are about to take on a most perilous task. If we fail, I fear that ruin will come to more towns than Archet alone. The Black Rider has brought the influence of Angmar to our very doorstep, ${PLAYER}.

'So much is at stake this day! Are you ready to begin your great venture?'Elladan feels that you should sharpen your skills as a ${CLASS} before beginning your search.Class trainers can be found in major hubs throughout the world, but the nearest is in the Edhelion Watch, not far from Elladan.

You should speak with your trainer to see if they have anything for you to learn.Elladan waits on the road to Edhelion.

You should speak with Elladan and let him know that you are prepared to face whatever dangers lie in your path.Talk to Elladan'Whether Dorollas was right or wrong in leading us here, my heart warns me that danger is near, as is often the case with the wide world of late.

'Before getting started, everyone should be prepared. You are a ${CLASS}, as I can see plainly, but have you mastered your skills?

'I fear that you will be tested as a warrior in these harsh mountains. You should speak with your trainer to make sure you are ready for what lies ahead.''You will find the ${CLASS} trainer standing here at the Edhelion Watch.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. You have a true warrior's heart. Learning the ways of a ${CLASS} throughout your life is not an easy feat, but it is rewarding.'Your trainer wants you to use your skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.Use your skill <rgb=#00ff00>Thrust</rgb> on the training dummy nearby.Use your Thrust skill on the Training Dummy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Barton Halifax, the Mariner Trainer, is in Archet, west of the training grounds.

Now that you have successfully used your skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.Talk to Barton Halifax, the Mariner Trainer in Archet'I am ready to help you learn how to become a more effective Mariner. As you gain levels, more skills will be available for you to unleash upon your foes.

'Use your skill <rgb=#00ff00>Thrust</rgb> against a Training Dummy. You will find that certain skills move your Balance either towards the Fore or to the Aft, which will have various effects upon your combat ability!''Strike the training dummy with your skill and return to me. We must make certain that you are prepared to stand against the dangers of Middle-earth.''Well done, ${PLAYER}!  As you grow as a ${CLASS}, you will find that there are much more powerful new skills available for you. Good luck!'The eldest and wisest of the Elves spend their time contemplating the past in an effort to glean wisdom from it.The Elf ${CLASS} is in the ruins near Dorongúr Whitethorn.

Dorongúr suggested you speak to one of the Elves reflecting upon the events that happened in Edhelion so long ago. You must learn all you can from those who contemplate the past. Listen to their words and learn from their wisdom.'Many who have travelled with us are reflecting upon the events of so many years ago. You would benefit from spending time with them and doing the same.

'Hopefully you will not interrupt their contemplation for long, but such reflection may help us in the days to come. Return to me when you are finished. The insight you gain may be of aid in the days ahead.''You should speak with the ${CLASS} who has accompanied me here, ${PLAYER}.''It angers me to see what has become of Edhelion since we left. The Dourhands did much to dishonour us. Together we can reflect upon the path of the Champion. Then we shall be prepared to bring justice to these dwarves.

'The Champion does not hide at the back of the ranks. We stand on the front lines, shoulder-to-shoulder with our brethren. "A! Elbereth Gilthoniel! tol-ammen!" we cry, vowing to lay down our lives so that our fellows may live.

'Reflect upon these words, and together we can bring justice to this Middle-earth.''Ah, if only I were here in the dark days when Edhelion fell. Perhaps things would have been different? Alas, such thoughts do us no good. We are here to protect the future, not dream about the past...for both you and I chose the path of the Guardian.

'There is no glory in battle if it comes to naught. Guardians challenge and taunt our enemies, keeping our allies from harm and shielding them with our own steel and our own sinews. You will learn that even the fiercest enemy has a weakness. It is our calling to strike out against that weakness and save the day.

'May you never forget those that depend upon you, Guardian.''I never knew the fire of wrath until I set my eyes upon the ruins of Edhelion. Mourn for the past, but do not let anger cloud your mind and lead you from the path you follow.

'The Hunter must keep himself under control, lest his arrows fly wild. We are a special breed of warrior. While others depend upon strength of arms and furious emotions, we act with sure, swift strokes and keen-eyed precision. And should the enemy close in, we must strike fast and true.

'Keep your eyes sharp and your mind clear. I have faith in you.''With Edhelion but a shadow of its former glory, I fear that even the sweetest song will never again raise my spirits. Yet the soothing comfort of a silver voice and a gentle melody is exactly what is needed at this moment in time.

'The power to stir the spirit and raise hope...that is the greatest power of the Minstrel. Even when all seems lost, our voices strengthen the resolve of those around us. Hope in the face of despair, light in the face of darkness.

'We must use our gifts well, for only then can we hope to chase the shadow from Middle-earth.''Greetings. You are a fellow sage, yes? I am glad to see another walking the path of wisdom. Preserving the knowledge of the past is our sacred duty.

'I sense greatness in you, ${PLAYER}. There are dark clouds upon the horizon, and the shadow of doom. Some may call upon you to face this threat, one greater than any faced in your many years. But you are not alone. The birds and beasts of the land will aid you, as will the very land itself. Your knowledge of forgotten lore and remedies will be of great use to both you and your companions.

'A bright future awaits you. For now, I will share what knowledge I can to start you upon your path.''Has the sight of Edhelion darkened your heart, ${PLAYER}? Fear not, for I feel much the same. Although the rune-lore we possess is powerful, it alone cannot stand against such tireless and powerful foes as those we face. We will need to use our knowledge to aid our allies in the days ahead.

'Do not forget, though, that the runes we scribe can strike great fear into our enemies or strengthen our companions' resolve...but the two cannot easily be mixed. Also, do not forget the power of some inscriptions, as they can foretell what may yet happen. Such knowledge, although rare, is a powerful force for us to bring to bear.

'I think we both know what must be done if you wish to continue upon this road. Practice your rune-lore; combat evil and reward goodness. You cannot undo the tragedy of Edhelion, but with careful attention, you may become a great bane to the plans of the Enemy.''Mae govannen. I can tell that the sight of the destruction of Edhelion has darkened your spirit, ${PLAYER}. Do not lose hope, friend, for while the past cannot be changed, we may yet set matters right here.

'As Wardens, our knowledge of sword, spear, shield, and javelin may turn the tide. Also, do not forget that the insight we have into our enemies may lead to just the right combination of blows that may strike terror into their hearts or strengthen our own resolve for the battles ahead. Of course, battles are plentiful for we Wardens, as we always seek to draw the eye of the Enemy away from those who cannot defend themselves.

'I tell you nothing which you do not already know, ${PLAYER}. However, I tell you these things only so that you may know that you will stand before the challenges ahead and that you shall make a difference.'Nos Grimsong recommended that you sharpen your skills a bit before attempting to deal with any of the threats that abound in Ered Luin.The ${CLASS} trainer awaits you near the centre of Frerin's Court.

Nos Grimsong suggested that you spend some time training with the visiting ${CLASS}.Bolli can be found on the northern steps in the centre of Frerin's Court.

You should return to Bolli and see what else he might have in store for you.Talk to Bolli in Frerin's Court'You will need courage and skill to deal with the threats that abound in the Blue Mountains, ${PLAYER}.

'Fortunately, there is a ${CLASS} of some small skill here with us. You should spend some time with him and learn what you may. When he's finished with you, be sure to talk with Bolli again. He's been asking about your progress.

'You can find the ${CLASS} near the centre of Frerin's Court.''Excellent, ${PLAYER}, you look stronger already! Now, for your next task.''You should find your fellow ${CLASS} in Frerin's Court.

'Be sure to see Bolli when you've finished your training.''Return now to Bolli. He should see your progress.''Bolli will want to know how you are getting on, I am certain. You should return to him.''Why don't you go over and talk to Bolli. I am sure that he wants to know how you are getting on.''You learn pretty quickly. I think that Bolli would like to see that...why not return to him and let him know your training with me is complete?''You have learned what you can from me for the moment. Return to Bolli...he will guide you further in your studies.'Elladan entered Edhelion and found goblins digging away at the walls. He slew many of the foul creatures and drove the others and their boggart minions away.The corpses of the slain goblins lie to the east of Elladan, surrounding the pool there.

Elladan killed several goblins and wants you to search the dead for clues, while he remains at his post.Search dead goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elladan awaits you to the west of the pool.

Your search revealed that many of the goblins carried dwarf-made pick-axes. Elladan will be most interested in your find.'In my battle against the goblins, I managed to kill many before the rest retreated beyond the west gate of Edhelion. The goblins I slew lay about the small pool just east of here. While I keep watch for their companions to return, I would ask that you search the remains of the slain for clues as to why they are here.

'The pool lies beneath the trees to the east. Be wary, for it is home to foul slugs. Be quick now...we must learn what the goblins were up to!''Make your way to the small pool to the east and search the dead goblins for information. We must learn why they were here.''All of the goblins were carrying dwarf-made pick-axes? Most curious....

'I would understand one or two -- the spoils of some battle with the dwarves, perhaps -- but all of them? Nay, it cannot be only a coincidence. You must bring this information to Durin's Folk.'Your trainer wants you to use your new skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.Speak with the trainer again and learn the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Savage Strikes</rgb>. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. 

