HINT:

Wardens use combinations of their basic skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Quick Thrust</rgb> and <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-bash</rgb> to build more powerful <rgb=#ffff00>Gambit</rgb> attacks. To use your <rgb=#00ff00>Defensive Strike</rgb> skill, attack a <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-bash</rgb> ability twice. This should cause your <rgb=#00ff00>Gambit Default</rgb> skill to change into your <rgb=#00ff00>Defensive Strike</rgb> skill. Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Defensive Strike</rgb> ability to strike a <rgb=#ff0000>Training-Dummy</rgb>.'Well done, ${PLAYER}! Make sure you visit a trainer as you advance in your role as a ${CLASS}. As you grow, you will find that trainers such as myself have tasks for you, as well as the occasional bit of wisdom. Good luck!'The folk of Mossward could use your help to recover from the hurts done by the recent Uruk attack on their town.Injured residents of Mossward can be found lying on the ground nearby.

Meneldir gave you a supply of salves and bandages with which you can treat the wounds of injured residents of Mossward.Meneldir is by the east gate of Mossward, by the body of Madthrug.

Having treated the wounds of some of the residents of Mossward who were injured during the attack, you should return to Meneldir and see what he has learned.Madthrug, the leader of the Uruk raiding party, might hold some clue to his purpose for attacking Mossward.Retrieve the small item Madthrug holds in his handYou took a small scrap of parchment from the body of Madthrug. What secrets does it hold?Read the scrap of parchment you took from the body of MadthrugMeneldir waits for you to show him the scrap of parchment you recovered from the body of Madthrug.A noisy crowd of children has gathered to the north-west in Mossward. What has gotten them so excited?Investigate what has excited the children to the north-west, in MosswardIt appears that Tegwyn absconded with the cruel blade once wielded by Madthrug.

Tegwyn might hurt himself or someone else unless you are able to take the weapon from him.Talk to TegwynThe nearest defeat circle is located north of Mossward.

You have (reluctantly) agreed to teach Tegwyn some basic adventuring lessons, and what better place to begin than the local defeat circle?Find the defeat circle located to the north of MosswardTegwyn stands at the defeat circle outside Mossward.Talk to Tegwyn at the defeat circle outside MosswardThe blacksmith shop is located in Mossward, and is an important location for adventurers who seek to purchase new gear or repair their old equipment.Enter the blacksmith shop in Mossward and teach Tegwyn about its utilityTegwyn is inside the blacksmith shop in Mossward.Talk to Tegwyn inside the blacksmith shop in MosswardA training dummy located just outside the blacksmith shop in Mossward will satisfy Tegwyn's eagerness to engage in combat training.Find the training dummy located outside the blacksmith shop in MosswardTegwyn stands by the training dummy located in Mossward, eager to learn more about adventuring and combat.Talk to Tegwyn at the training dummy in Mossward'Some of Mossward's residents sustained injuries we cannot heal, and they are beyond our aid. We will mourn for them later, but now we must focus upon those we can still help.'

Meneldir hands you a small bundle of bandages and a pouch of bitter-smelling salve.

'This is the last of my supplies, but there is no reason to save them for another day. Bring these bandages and this salve to the injured residents nearby. It is my hope that their hurts will not prove serious, and these will ease the pain of their injuries.''Bring those bandages and that salve to the injured residents nearby. It is my hope that their hurts will not prove serious, and those supplies will ease the pain of their injuries.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. The people of Mossward sometimes look down upon the Rangers that were once my kin, but they do welcome their aid when it is offered! My former chieftain Strider may say the distrust of such folk does not bother him, but if that is true he is a better man than I am.'

A pained look crosses Meneldir's face.

'That is true for many reasons, ${PLAYER}. I have not called the Dúnedain my kin for some time now, but I would never question Strider's integrity or his courage.

'But look here. The Uruk that led this band has something in his hand. See if you can't wrest it from his grip.''Look here. The Uruk that led this band has something in his hand. See if you can't wrest it from his grip.''A scrap of parchment? You had better read it, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps it will tell us why this Uruk led his raiding party to Mossward.''Let's see if this parchment holds any clues for us.'

Meneldir briefly studies the crumpled parchment, but then he looks up, disappointed.

'I cannot read much of this. If this were an ordinary day, I would be grateful to have no reason to understand the Black Speech... but on this day it is a cause for frustration.

'Hold, ${PLAYER}. What has happened to this Uruk's blade? It did not fall far from his body, unless my eyes were somehow deceived.''I think we may have our answer, ${PLAYER}. If one of those children has taken the Uruk's sword, you had better get it back before the child does some harm with it.''Hah! Yah! Take that, villains!''What do you want, stranger? No, I'm not giving you this sword! It is so much better than the wooden sword I was using before! I found it, and it belongs to me now! My father says that when you're in a battle, you get to keep the spoils, and I stood up to those Uruks even when the town guard wouldn't! If anyone should get to keep that Uruk's blade, it's me!

'Well... wait a moment. You're an adventurer, right? If you promise to help train me in the adventuring arts, maybe I'll give you the sword. I'm not saying I will, you understand, I'm saying MAYBE. It'll depend on how good your training is!

'So what's my first lesson, stranger? What's the first thing I need to know to become an adventurer?''What's my first lesson, stranger? What's the first thing I need to know to become an adventurer?''Very funny.'You explain that adventuring is dangerous work, and sooner or later your morale is likely to run out. When that happens, you will find yourself at one of the many Defeat Circles scattered around the land.

'Very funny, stranger. I know that fighting is dangerous! That's why I will try not to fight enemies that look to be beyond my capabilities! But sometimes it's unavoidable, I suppose... and when that happens, if I'm defeated, I'll find myself at the nearest Defeat Circle to where I fell in battle?''What's my next adventuring lesson? And make it a good one!''Skardí spends more time fixing horseshoes than he does forging swords!''Skardí spends more time fixing horseshoes than he does forging swords! I mean no insult, Skardí, but it's true! What use does an adventurer have with a shop like this?'

You explain that as an adventurer engages in combat, equipped weapons and armour sustain durability damage, and folk such as Skardí Bendblade are able to repair them so you can keep using them. Additionally, shopkeepers throughout Middle-earth can sell an adventurer all sorts of items and equipment that will aid you on your journeys.

Skardí clears his throat and speaks up. 'That all costs coin, young Tegwyn, horseshoes and swords alike! But if that raid is a sign of things to come, I think the swords might become more in demand than they have been until now....''That's all well and good, but I want to hit something!''Now this is more like it!''Now this is more like it!'Tegwyn agreed to relinquish the Uruk sword if you are able to impress him with a demonstration of your combat ability.Tegwyn is waiting for you to demonstrate your combat ability by using <rgb=#00ff00>Wild Attack</rgb> on the training dummy.Use <rgb=#00ff00>Wild Attack</rgb> on the training dummyYou have demonstrated a basic Champion attack to Tegwyn. Will he relinquish the Uruk's blade to you, as he agreed?Talk to Tegwyn by the training dummyTegwyn is waiting for you to demonstrate your combat ability by using <rgb=#00ff00>Savage Strikes</rgb> on the training dummy.Use <rgb=#00ff00>Savage Strikes</rgb> on the training dummy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have demonstrated how to unleash a Champion's <rgb=#ffff00>Fervour</rgb> by using the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Savage Strikes</rgb>. Will Tegwyn relinquish the Uruk's blade to you, as he agreed?Talk to Tegwyn by the training dummyUse <rgb=#00ff00>Remorseless Strike</rgb>, <rgb=#00ff00>Sudden Defence</rgb>, or <rgb=#00ff00>Blade Storm</rgb> on the training dummyYou have fulfilled your end of the bargain. Will Tegwyn relinquish the Uruk's blade to you, as he agreed?Talk to Tegwyn by the training dummyMeneldir is by the east gate of Mossward.

Now that you have recovered the Uruk blade, you should bring it to Meneldir.'Well? I'm ready for you to show off your combat skills... and if you impress me, I'll give up this Uruk sword. It had better be a good demonstration, or the bargain is done!'

