After you choose a specialization, use <rgb=#00ff00>Dramatic Flourish</rgb>, <rgb=#00ff00>Feint</rgb>, or <rgb=#00ff00>Thrum of the Sea</rgb> on the training dummy.The lynx that prowl Thorin's Gate are too many for the land to support. They attack travellers and the thrushes, long-time friends of the dwarves.Lynx can be found in the wooded areas north or east of Frerin's Court and to the north of the Elf-camp.

 Nos Grimsong/Laergil asked you to defeat the Lynx found throughout Thorin's Gate and bring back their pelts.Collect lynx-pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the lynx-pelts you gathered back to Nos Grimsong at the Berghold/Laergil in the ruins of Edhelion.'The Dourhands do nothing to stem the growth of the lynx in this area. No surprise, to be honest. Despite their newfound ties to their cousins, the Longbeards, the Dourhands are the same dwarves that Skorgrím led against Edhelion centuries ago. We cannot expect them to be proper stewards of the land.

'Go into the wilds and cull the lynx population. You can find them in the wooded areas near the frozen lake down the road from here. You can also find them to the north.' 

'Return the pelts of the creatures to me. It would be a waste to leave the furs out on the snow, and I am sure Durin's Folk would appreciate them in the cold nights to come.''You will find the lynx prides out in the forested area around the frozen lake down the road from here. You might also find some to the north. Return with pelts and be careful.''You return victorious? Excellent, friend. Perhaps these pelts will garner us trade with the Longbeards of Ered Luin.'The lynx that prowl Thorin's Gate are too many for the land to support. They attack travellers and the thrushes, long-time friends of the dwarves.<rgb=#ffff00>Highland cubs</rgb> and <rgb=#ffff00>highland prowlers</rgb> can be found in the wooded areas north or east of Frerin's Court.

Nos Grimsong asked you to defeat the lynx found throughout Thorin's Gate and bring back their pelts.Collect lynx-pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nos Grimsong is in the north-west corner of Frerin's Court.

Bring the lynx-pelts you gathered back to Nos Grimsong.'Blast those Dourhands! They are supposed to be out hunting, but I see nary a one of them out there! There are too many lynx and not enough food to go around. Worse still, our friends the thrushes are falling prey to the beasts! We can't stand by and do nothing, so I'm asking you to go out on a hunting expedition for us.

'Kill a few of the <rgb=#ffff00>highland cubs</rgb> and <rgb=#ffff00>highland prowlers</rgb> nearby and keep them from doing more harm. Just east of Frerin's Court, I saw a pride of the beasts, and others here tell of still more to the north.

'Oh, and be sure to bring back the pelts! The nights out here are cold and long, and we could use some warm furs to keep away the chill.''What are you waiting for? Time to go a-hunting for lynx! And don't let the pelts go to waste. They're roaming the woods to the north or east of Frerin's Court.''Well done! These are fine pelts. Fine indeed. I'll send these down to the tanner at once.

'On behalf of both dwarf and thrush alike, I thank you kindly.'Bolli needs the fronds of the nestadalas-bush to purge himself of the poison the Dourhands gave him.Nestedelais can be found to the north-east of Frerin's Court.

Bolli mentioned that the leaves of the nestadalas-bush were necessary for his cure and asked you to gather some fronds for him.<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest has been restored for Legendary Servers!</rgb>

'I'll not last long if...if help cannot be found for me. Fortunately, I know of something which may be of aid. There are bushes which grow in the vale just north-east of Frerin's Court called nestadalas.

'Venture out north-east of Frerin's Court and gather up leaves from these bushes. They are said to have healing properties. They may well be my only chance.

'Now make haste and do not get lost!''Good, good. Just the smell of these leaves is helping to ease the pain. Now I will tell you what I know!'Your trainer wants you to use your new skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.Use <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>on the training dummy nearby.

HINT: Captains rely on their <rgb=#00ff00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put them into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb>. While in this state, Captains can use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>, an effective attack that deals a great deal of damage. Attack the <rgb=#ff0000>Training Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00FF00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put you into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb> and then attack the dummy with your <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>.Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Battle Shout</rgb> on the training dummy, then strike it with your skill <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>The Captain Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch.

Now that you have successfully used your Devastating Blow, you should return to your trainer and tell them of your success.Talk to the Captain Trainer at the Edhelion Watch'A fellow Captain, are you? Were our errand here not so urgent, there would be more time to spare for your training, but here is a word of advice:

'Unlike the brash Champion, a Captain does not best serve his companions by running recklessly into the fray. Nay, it is the Captain who stands behind and dutifully guides the efforts of his fellows that wins the day! Even so, the time may come when you must take up arms and wade into battle yourself—and that is no time to show weakness. With careful technique and precision, a Captain might land a Devastating Blow against even the mightiest foe!

'Show me your skill and deliver a <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb> to one of these training dummies. Do not hold back!'

HINT:

Captains rely on their <rgb=#00ff00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put them into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb>. While in this state, Captains can use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>, an effective attack that deals a great deal of damage. Attack the <rgb=#ff0000>Training Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00FF00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put you into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb> and then attack the dummy with your <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>.'You should strike the training dummy with the most Devastating Blow you can muster. Once you feel confident in your ability, return to me. We must make certain that you are prepared to stand against the dangers of Middle-earth!'

HINT:

Captains rely on their <rgb=#00ff00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put them into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb>. While in this state, Captains can use special skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>, an effective attack that deals a great deal of damage. Attack the <rgb=#ff0000>Training Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#00FF00>Battle Shout</rgb> to put you into a <rgb=#ffff00>Battle-Readied State</rgb> and then attack the dummy with your <rgb=#00ff00>Devastating Blow</rgb>.'Well done, ${PLAYER}!  As you continue to hone your skills, you will learn new techniques with which to bolster your allies and master the field of battle itself!

'If that is all, you should return to Elladan.'As you gain levels, you will learn new skills to help you develop into a more powerful Guardian.Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> skill on the Training-dummy nearby.

HINT:

Guardians rely on <rgb=#ffff00>Reactive Skills</rgb> to deal damage and generate <rgb=#ff0000>Threat</rgb> against their enemies.  <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> requires that the Guardian <rgb=#ffff00>Block</rgb> an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill. Head over to the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-dummies</rgb> to the north of the trainer and attack it until you successfully block one of their attacks. If you're having trouble getting a block, try using <rgb=#00ff00>Guardian's Ward</rgb> to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks. Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb> skill. Strike the <rgb=#ff0000>Training-dummy</rgb> with <rgb=#00ff00>Shield-swipe</rgb>.Strike the Training-dummy with 'Shield-swipe'The Guardian Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch.

