Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell her of your success.Talk to the Lore-master Trainer at the Edhelion Watch'Welcome, ${PLAYER}. It is good to meet another who walks the path of wisdom, and I will gladly share my insight with you.

'As you grow in knowledge and ability, you will find that you will have many allies to call upon in your struggles. The birds and creatures of the land will lend you their strength. Even the strength of the very earth can be drawn upon, or the light from the sky. But today, I speak of one of your most dangerous companions: tongues of fire raised by hotly-burning embers of flame!

'Demonstrate your mastery by setting alight this training dummy with the power of your burning embers!'Use the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Burning Embers</rgb> on the training-dummy nearby.'Good, ${PLAYER}! I think you will be an excellent Lore-master someday. You should return now to Elladan; I believe he wishes to begin the investigation.'Your trainer wants you to use your new skills to prove that you are ready to face the many dangers that exist in the world.HINT:

Minstrels use <rgb=#ffff00>Ballads</rgb> to attack their enemies, lightly heal their fellows and empower themselves. These skills operate on a rotating system that allows the minstrel to have three special buffs on themselves at any time. After the third buff is applied the next <rgb=#ffff00>Ballad</rgb> played will overwrite the first, then the second and so on.Learn the skill 'Major Ballad' and use it while in combat with a Training DummyThe Minstrel Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch.

Now that you have successfully used your skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.Talk to the Minstrel Trainer at the Edhelion Watch'A good day to you! I am pleased to find another Minstrel has accompanied us. I should be happy to share what skills I have with you. First, though, I will give you some small advice, if you are willing to lend an ear to it.

'As you may already know, a Minstrel possesses a great power...the power to stir the spirit and raise hopes when all seems lost. When the spirit is roused, the body soon follows! A good Minstrel heals themselves and their fellows, staving off even the most dire wounds.

'Demonstrate your mastery by entering combat with the training-dummy nearby, then using the skill <rgb=#00ff00>Major Ballad</rgb>.'


