Brawlers rely on <rgb=#ffff00>Mettle</rgb> to activate some of their skills such as <rgb=#00ff00>Overhand Smash</rgb>. Use your <rgb=#00ff00>Low Strike</rgb>or <rgb=#00ff00>Dextrous Hook</rgb> to build <rgb=#ffff00>3 Mettle</rgb> and then strike the <rgb=#ff0000>Training Dummy</rgb> with your <rgb=#ffff00>Overhand Smash</rgb> skill.'Good, ${PLAYER}! I think you will be an excellent Brawler someday. You should return now to Elladan; I believe he wishes to begin the investigation.'Now that you have thinned the lynx-population, Nos has asked you to deal with the wolves to the north-east.Wolves can be found by the frozen lake, north-east of Frerin's Court.

Nos Grimsong has asked you to thin the number of wolves in the region.Defeat Frost-wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Grizzled Frost-wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nos Grimsong is in the north-west corner of Frerin's Court.

You should return to Nos Grimsong for your reward.Talk to Nos Grimsong in Frerin's Court'Now that you've dealt with the lynx, we will need to thin the wolf population some to make sure that balance is preserved.

'Head to the north-east and hunt down some Frost-wolves. The evil creatures are no doubt spies of goblins.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. Through your efforts our home will be better for the future.

'Please take this along with my thanks as your reward.''Head to the north-east and hunt down some Frost-wolves. The evil creatures are no doubt spies of goblins.'The Witch-king of Angmar has come to the Dark Tower to seek new servants for the Dead City. You have been chosen.The Twisted Stair can be found beyond the halls leading out of the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

Zôreth has bidden you to present yourself to the Mouth of Sauron that you might serve in the Dead City.Ascend the Twisted Stair and present yourself to the Mouth of SauronLethi can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

Before you were able to reach the Twisted Stair, you encountered Lethi standing amid a slaughter of Men, Orcs, and Stout-axes. You should ask Lethi what has happened.Talk to Lethi'Many of your kind have been sent to the Black Pits. That is not your fate, but perhaps you may wish it were so!

'You are to leave the dungeons at once and present yourself to the Mouth of Sauron upon the highest steps of the Twisted Stair. The Witch-king of Angmar has come to Barad-dûr seeking stronger servants for the Dead City and your... unique heritage may be of use to the Lord of the Nazgûl.

'Relish this brief freedom to walk among the glorious works of Sauron the Great, dwarf, for your servitude is far from ended!''No... no, no, no.

'What have they done?!'Troublesome pests have burrowed into the foundations of the Dark Tower.You are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.Maggots and rats can be found throughout the dungeons of Barad-dûr.Defeat rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat maggots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.Constable Thistlewool is concerned for his friend Cal Sprigley, a farmer on the southern outskirts of Archet. Sprigley's farm is vulnerable to brigand attack.Cal Sprigley's farm can be found to the south of Bronwe's Folly.

Constable Thistlewool has asked you to go to Cal Sprigley's farm and convince Sprigley to bring his family to Archet, where they can be protected from the Blackwolds.Talk to Cal Sprigley'Ho, there, ${PLAYER}. I could use your help. I've a friend, Cal Sprigley, who has a farm outside Archet. With what I've heard about the Blackwolds' threatening attack against Archet, I'm worried that the brigands might bring harm to him and his folk.

'Would you mind speaking with him? You might be able to convince him to come here.

'Cal's farm lies to the south of Bronwe's Folly. Tell him it will be safer for him here in Archet. I only hope he listens to reason!''Well, it's nice to meet you, ${PLAYER}. I suppose Thistlewool is wanting me to bring the wife and workhands to town? Well, I'll tell you now: no brigands are going to run me off my land!

'No, don't look at me like that. We're safer right here than behind some rickety old walls!

'Now old Thistlewool's a good sort, and I appreciate him worrying about us, but nothing is going to run us off our land!''Cal Sprigley's farm is just south of Bronwe's Folly. Please go there and convince him to bring his household north.'The weapons and armour forged by the Stout-axes supply the garrisons that keep watch over the Black Land of Mordor.You are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.The Uruk garrison-captain can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.Deliver a barrel of armour to the Uruk garrison-captainDeliver a barrel of spears to the Uruk garrison-captainDeliver a barrel of swords to the Uruk garrison-captainYou are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.Since the abandonment of Edhelion, terrible creatures of unnatural ilk have found their way within the walls. In a tepid pool of water, a filthy creature has taken residence, and the Elves, intent on restoring the refuge of Edhelion, want your assistance in removing the vile things from the pool.Slugs infest a pool within the walls of Edhelion, east of Dorollas.

Dorollas has tasked you with cleaning the slugs from Edhelion so that healing may begin in the once-beautiful refuge of the Elves.Defeat slugs in Edhelion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dorollas is west of the pool in Edhelion, near Elladan.

You should return to Dorollas and tell him that you have successfully purged the vile slugs from the pool.Talk to Dorollas in Edhelion'Long have we waited to return to Edhelion, and now that we have, we find the ruins of our once-great home overrun by filth and vermin. I recall the vibrance of this place and wish to restore it to the glory it once held. 

'The pool, beneath the blighted trees to the east, was once a place where we could reflect in peace and feel the cool water and breeze off the mountains. Now, it is swelled with filth shed from the slugs which make it their home.

'Would you assist me and clean out the slugs from the pool?''These slugs are great unnatural creatures. They have grown to enormous size and have a sickly quality to them. We must destroy them to cleanse the pool of their filth.''It may seem a small deed, but from the many small deeds that shall be done in this place, we shall achieve the greatest goal. Edhelion will be restored through the efforts of all. No single Elf shall claim greater glory than any other.

'Beyond the gate of Edhelion, you will find Laergil and Orodlin, two of our brethren working to mend the division between the dwarves and Elves. Speak with them, if you have the chance.

'I am told that they have taken comfort in the outpost to the south, beyond the western gate of Edhelion.'Olin felt much better after taking a remedy made with Elven mushrooms. Free of pain, Olin told you of Gormr Doursmith, the dwarf who leads the Dourhands.Dwalin can be found in Frerin's Court, the central square of Thorin's Gate.

Olin revealed that Gormr Dourhand is in league with goblins and may have contributed to his poisoning.'Gormr Doursmith, the Dourhand steward, is responsible for the guards' deaths, and nearly mine as well! He's been seen having dealings with a strange red-robed man and...and...goblins! 

'Dwalin must know about this. Find him at Frerin's Court in the centre of town.''Fool Dourhands! But we'll need further evidence if we are going to prove they are going back to their old ways.''Dwalin must be told of Gormr's treachery. Find him at the centre of Frerin's Court.'Based on the evidence you collected, Captain Brackenbrook has ordered the capture of Calder Cob.  

Captain Brackenbrook wants you to head to the jails and glean what information you can from Calder Cob.Ned Pruner is in the jails to the east of Captain Brackenbrook's location.Speak with Ned Pruner'Thank you for your efforts in uncovering this mess thus far.  I would like to ask you to follow up on your investigation by looking in on the prisoner, Calder Cobb.

'Head to the jails, just to the east of this building and speak with Ned Pruner.  He'll be your point of contact.''Captain Brackenbrook sent you did he?''If you're having trouble finding Ned, just head across the way to the east when you exit this building.'Prepared and armed with new skills, you are tasked now with a battle against the vile creatures that blight and plague the trees of Edhelion.The insects may be found at the copse of trees north of Dorongúr Whitethorn, near the golden gate.

Dorongúr Whitethorn charged you with helping to reclaim the refuge of Edhelion by eliminating the insects that have made the nearby trees their home.Defeat insects near the trees of Edhelion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dorongúr Whitethorn is south of the trees.

With the insects defeated, you have proven yourself worthy to Dorongúr Whitethorn. You should return to him and tell him of your victory.Talk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion'Armed with new knowledge and a clear recollection of the past, I must ask you to assist us in our first strides to reclaim this fallen refuge. Nearby, just to the north, there is a copse of trees before a golden gate. These trees were once one of the grandest sights in all of Edhelion. Now, sadly, they are a ghost of their former selves. Barren and blighted, these trees remind us of our failure and the betrayal wrought upon us by the Dourhands. 

'Worse still, they have become home to foul and twisted insects. We must eliminate those insects lest they infest new plantings, and there may yet be a way to save the ailing trees.

'Go now and strike down the creatures plaguing the trees of Edhelion. Return to me when you have completed this task.''You are ready now to leave this place. Elrond has chosen another path for you, and I was here only to ensure that you were ready for the journey. I am confident now that you will prove everything we expect of you, ${PLAYER}.''You will find the insects near the copse of trees a short distance north of here. Destroy them, then return to me.'The traitor, Calder Cob, refuses to speak with the gullible jailor, Ned Pruner, until he has some bilberry cakes.Bilberry bushes grow near Blackwold's Roost, south-east of Archet.

Ned Pruner has asked you to gather enough bilberries to bake the cakes that Calder Cob demanded.Collect piles of bilberries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ned Pruner can be found at Archet's jail.

You collected the bilberries which Ned Pruner requested. You should return to Ned with the berries.'You're the one what helped discover that old Calder here was a traitor, ain't ye? Ye have me thanks for that, friend! I was just talking to my Peg about that. You're quite a hero!

'Calder here could probably tell us a lot about what them Blackwolds are planning, if only he'd talk. Thing is, he's refusing to talk until he gets some better food, and he wants bilberry cakes. But me Peg don't have no bilberries to make the cakes.

'Could you maybe go out and pick a few piles of bilberries from the bushes along the river south-east of town? Head south-east from Archet's gates and you you should spot it. If I could just get some cakes, maybe then Calder would talk!''I really need those berries if I'm going to get the cakes that'll loosen Calder's tongue. Bilberry bushes grow near Blackwold's Roost, south-east of Archet.

'You can get to the river if you head south-east from Archet's gates.''Those bilberries sure smell good! Too bad I have to feed 'em to a traitor.

'Well, I'm going to just step out for a moment and take them over to Peg. She'll get the cakes baked up and brought over. Then finally we'll get some information out of old Calder there!'The Ranger Amdir told you that he had asked Celandine Brandybuck to gather an herb called "athelas" to make a remedy for his wound, in case the blade was poisoned.Kingsfoil grows south of Archet, near some old ruins called Bronwe's Folly.

Celandine Brandybuck, too frightened to pass beyond the gates of Archet, has asked you to collect kingsfoil leaves for her, so that she can prepare the remedy Amdir asked her to make.Gather kingsfoil leaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Celandine Brandybuck can be found with Amdir outside The Mad Badger Inn in Archet.

You have gathered enough leaves for Amdir's remedy. You should return with them to Celandine Brandybuck.'Oh, hello! Thank you again for your help the other night. I shudder to think what might have happened if you hadn't freed me!

'While he's putting on a brave face, I am quite worried about Amdir's knife-wound. I asked how I could help, and he told me of some sort of remedy from the Old Kings involving some plant called "athelas." He said I might know it as kingsfoil, but I've always thought that was naught but a weed. He says that some grows outside of Archet, but I'm afraid of the wolves and Men that prowl out there.

'Amdir said the kingsfoil could be found south of Archet, near some old ruins the men call "Bronwe's Folly." After you gather some of the leaves, could you bring them back here to me?''Kingsfoil grows to the south, near some old ruins the men call Bronwe's Folly. You should hurry...Amdir doesn't look too well.''Thank you! I hope the draught Amdir told me of will help him. I wouldn't have thought such a small wound would have caused him so much pain!'Strider, worried for his wounded friend, has asked you to seek a herb called "Kingsfoil," which he believes will slow the poison of the evil knife that pierced Amdir.Captain Brackenbrook is near The Mad Badger Inn in the village of Archet.

You should ask the Captain if he knows of any kingsfoil plants nearby and also if he would like some assistance to earn his favour.Ask Captain Brackenbrook for directions and begin to try to earn his favourCalder Cob is at a farm outside of Archet, on the way to Bronwe's Folly as you take the road south from the town. Kingsfoil can be found at Bronwe's Folly.

You should speak with Calder Cob and see how you can assist him against the threat of attacking wolves before heading to the ruins to pick kingsfoil.Complete a quest for Calder Cob, Brackenbrook's most trusted soldierGather kingsfoil leaves to treat Amdir's wound (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Strider is in the town of Archet, awaiting your return with leaves and news of your efforts to get Brackenbrook to trust you.

You should bring Strider the kingsfoil and inform him of Calder Cob's treacherous behaviour.'Amdir, my poor old friend! A shadow has crept over him... the Black Rider that stabbed him is more fell than any creature you will meet in your travels!

'We have little time, and we must stretch what time we have by doing two things at once. Amdir needs medicine, ${PLAYER}, and quickly. Do you know of a plant called kingsfoil? It has great power to heal.

'You should ask Captain Brackenbrook if he knows of any that grows in these parts. Offer him assistance as well, if it does not take you far out of the way. We must begin to work on him, and perhaps he will look more kindly upon you after you do him a good deed.''Assist Captain Brackenbrook if you are able, but it is important that kingsfoil be brought back. Many deem it useless, but it is a powerful herb with many positive uses.''Kingsfoil, eh? 'Tis a nice leafy plant that grows around Bronwe's Folly, a ruin south of here. Help yourself to as much as you'd like; we've no use for it.

'And as for your offer of assistance, I will take you up on it! We are always in need of able hands, and you might as well earn your keep while you stay with us.

'My best man, Calder Cob, is having trouble with wolves of late. Perhaps you could help him on your way to do your gardening job for the Ranger.''Calder Cob is my best man in this town. If you help him, you shall earn your keep here. If he thinks favourably of you, I might be inclined to warm up to you, despite your choice of friends!''Assist Captain Brackenbrook if you are able, but it is important that kingsfoil be brought back to me. Many deem it useless, but it is a powerful herb with many positive uses.''Danger has found you much earlier than I predicted! It sounds like Calder Cob had it in for you before you even arrived.

'How did he know of you, if he was at his post? And how did that Blackwold know you were coming?

'Thank you for the risk you took to deliver the kingsfoil. I will think upon this riddle while I prepare a salve for Amdir.'Amdir has asked you to see to the defence of Archet by helping Captain Brackenbrook.Dirk Mudbrick defends a farm south and west out the front gate of Archet.

Amdir told you to speak with Dirk Mudbrick and offer him your services, as Captain Brackenbrook originally instructed you.Talk to Dirk MudbrickWolves can be found east and south of the farm and at Bronwe's Folly.

Dirk Mudbrick is charged with guarding the sheep-farm outside of Archet and is pleased to be receiving help from Captain Brackenbrook.Defeat wolves near Archet (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dirk Mudbrick can be found at the sheep-farm south and west from Archet.

You should return to Dirk Mudbrick with news of your success.Talk to Dirk Mudbrick'It appears you are prepared for battle, ${PLAYER}. You should make your way to the sheep farm south and west out of Archet's gate. Seek Dirk Mudbrick and tell him that you are there to assist him at the behest of Captain Brackenbrook.

'If the wolves are truly threatening the sheep, then we should do what we can to assist the people here in Archet.

'Also, if you have not spoken to her yet, Celandine Brandybuck could use your help. I have asked her to help me treat my wound as if it were poisoned and will need athelas, or "kingsfoil" as it is commonly known. Might I ask that you help her in this as well?''Leave the gate of Archet. Look for the sheep farm nor far from the entrance and speak with Dirk Mudbrick. He is a good, honest, man. Earn his trust and maybe he can help us.''Well now, what with the Captain paying no heed to the talk o' traitors, I guess ye be needing some work? There's more to do down Combe-way, but the roads are too dangerous for travelling.

'Well, far be it from me to refuse help. These wolves are proving bad. We've lost more sheep than I care to mention. And that's just about all I've got to guard, what with most folk already pulled within the walls o' the village.

'I need ye to clear out as many o' the wolves beyond the gates as ye can. The longer they're about, the bolder they'll get! Start your search south or east of the farm. If you're feeling particularly bold, I heard there's a large group of wolves at Bronwe's Folly to the south-east.''If Captain Brackenbrook wants you to help Archet by hunting wolves with Dirk Mudbrick, then do so. I will see what I can do to expose Calder Cob.

'You should find Mudbrick at the sheep-farm south and west outside Archet's gate.''The wolves are becoming a serious threat, thanks in no small part to the Blackwolds. I've heard there's a large pack of them at Bronwe's Folly.''Those wolves are getting closer every day. They have already slaughtered many of the sheep here and the remainder of the flock is dearly threatened. With your help maybe we can turn our attentions elsewhere.''I see the trophies of your hunt about you. You should return to Dirk Mudbrick and let him know of your success!''You're stouter than I thought. Well done with those wolves. There's much more to be done, though!

'The Captain won't see the true threat, though. I shouldn't say anymore... my mouth is why I was assigned to this place.'Captain Brackenbrook, worried about Otto the Brigand's mention of a Blackwold attack from the south of Archet, has asked you to travel to Cal Sprigley's farm to find proof of the brigands' intentions.Cal Sprigley can be found at his farm in the southernmost part of Archet.

You should speak with Cal Sprigley to assess the reality of the Blackwold threat.Talk to Cal Sprigley to assess the Blackwold threat in the south'Does Ned speak true of his prisoner? If so, we would be wise to investigate Otto's threat of trouble in the south. I'll not question Calder Cob's lifetime of loyalty if there is no truth to back it up.

'But if you and Ned are right in your suspicion, this will be a very bad situation for us.

'Cal Sprigley's farm is to the south of here, near the gate to the town of Combe. If aught is going on, he'll know!''A stranger, eh? If Brackenbrook sent you, I'll take you in. I'm afraid you're the best thing that's happened to us all day!''Cal Sprigley's farm is south of here, beyond Bronwë's Folly if you follow the road towards Combe. I hope Cal can set this mess straight....'After Calder Cob tried to have you ambushed by the Blackwolds, Strider wishes to prove beyond a doubt that he is an enemy to Archet.Otto the Brigand is being held in the stocks in the Archet Jailyard, across the lane from Strider and Amdir.

You should question Otto directly about Calder Cob and the Blackwolds' treachery; Captain Brackenbrook is not ready to be convinced by your words alone.Question Otto the Brigand about his ties to the BlackwoldsThe Archet jailor, a man named Ned Pruner, stands warily near Otto.

You should speak with Ned Pruner, for perhaps Otto had a loose tongue around his captor.Talk to the jailor about Otto's foreboding wordsCaptain Brackenbrook is in the town of Archet.

You should quickly tell Captain Brackenbrook about what Otto has said to you and to Ned Pruner, his jailor.Talk to Captain Brackenbrook'I cannot decide which is more dangerous right now: Calder Cob's treachery or the ignorance of Captain Brackenbrook!

'If Calder Cob is his best soldier, I know Brackenbrook will not believe that he tried to have you ambushed by a Blackwold.

'I did some asking around while you were gone, and there is a Blackwold brigand in the stocks, across the lane from here; he is being held for highway robbery. You should question him about Calder Cob.''Otto is a Blackwold, and he is being held in the stocks. You can find him across the lane from here, past where the hobbits are sitting. There you will find the Archet Jail.''Let me go! I'm a friend of Calder Cob's, and I'm innocent at that! This idiot jailor won't heed me.'

Otto quiets down as you tell him you know of Calder Cob's treachery.

'So you think you know the plan? Don't be smug; it's too late! By now, the gears of war be turning down in the south, and quick. Soon I'll be free, and you'll be the one in shackles... or worse.''I taste vengeance on the South Wind.''It is good to make your acquaintance, ${PLAYER}. I noticed you were questioning Otto... does that mean that his mutterings have been truthful?

'Yes, I do believe what you have come to Archet to tell. It is unprecedented, but all signs are showing that the Blackwolds mean to attack us. How is it that they have the means?

'If Brackenbrook does not believe you, you may tell him that I DO, for what it's worth.''You should repeat everything Otto said to Captain Brackenbrook. If any of it is true, it sounds like Archet is in for some real trouble.''That is a serious charge, ${PLAYER}. Calder Cob has been loyal to me and this town since he was a boy....'Goblins were discovered within Edhelion and Elladan fought many of them. He is troubled by what you discovered when you searched the bodies: each of the slain goblins carried dwarf-made pick-axes.Dwalin can be found in Frerin's Court, west of the Silver Deep. Boggarts line the way out of Edhelion.

Elladan has instructed you to take the dwarf-made picks to Dwalin and tell him of the goblins in the Silver Deep. He also suggested you slay some boggarts and learn if they, too, carry the picks.'There is a party of Longbeards that has recently come from Erebor. Their leader, Dwalin, was a member of Thorin's Company, which journeyed forth long ago on the Quest of Erebor, and he is a friend of my father's.

'You will find Dwalin standing at Frerin's Court, west of here within the vale. You will need to make your way down the mountainside and across the dwarf-paths to reach him. Bring him the picks and tell him of the goblins. 

'Should you find any of the boggart minions that were with these goblins, kill them and search for more of these dwarf-picks. If the boggarts also carry the dwarf-picks, then surely something is amiss, and Dwalin will wish to know this disturbing news.''Go speak with Dwalin. He will be found in Frerin's Court.''Greetings, good Elf! What's this? Pick-axes from the bodies of our enemies? I must say you are not the only one who has brought me such news. I think that the Dourhands are falling back to their old ways, but I cannot yet prove it. 

'You may have heard tales of Skorgrím, the leader of the Dourhands, and the fall of the Elf-refuge? You were there? Then you know more than I. Still, you may learn something yet.'The Blackwolds have sent spies to appraise the situation in Archet, which has become a cause of concern for Dirk Mudbrick.Blackwold spies may be found to the south-east of the sheep-farm, between the farm and Bronwe's Folly.

Dirk Mudbrick wants to discover what the Blackwold spies have learned. He has asked you to confront one of the spies and recover any orders or messages he might be carrying.Defeat a Blackwold spy and search himDirk Mudbrick can be found at the sheep-farm south and west of Archet.

Dirk Mudbrick will be anxious to read the orders you found on the Blackwold spy. You should bring them to him as quickly as possible.Captain Brackenbrook can be found inside The Mad Badger Inn, north of the Archet gate.

Dirk Mudbrick sent you to Captain Brackenbrook with the orders you found on the Blackwold Spies.'Well, since I already opened my mouth, I guess I should explain myself a little. I mentioned to the Captain that the Blackwolds seemed a bit stronger than we'd been told, and that we ought to listen to Jon and spy out their camp. If we'd done that, we might have stopped them from grabbing them two hobbits.

'Now, when I says this, the Captain re-assigns me from gate-duty to watching these sheep here. I see brigands making their way through the woods here and there, and I can't help thinking that they are trying to get a good look at us.

'We need to know what they've learned and what they're up to. If ye can, confront one of their spies and see what ye can discover. Bring me any orders or messages ye find. I swear I saw some of their spies sneaking about to the south-east, between here and Bronwe's Folly.''The Blackwold spies are hiding between here and Bronwe's Folly, to the south-east. They must be dealt with!''Did ye read this, ${PLAYER}? It was just like Jon said! Calder... Calder was in league with the Blackwolds!

'Jon was right. He warned us about Calder, but the Captain paid him no mind. Calder used the Captain's stubbornness against him and turned him on his own son!

'There must be some devilry at work here! Calder will see the inside of our jail before the day is over! Quickly, take these orders to Captain Brackenbrook and show him what you've found.''Quickly now, bring that letter to Captain Brackenbrook at The Mad Badger. He needs to know about Calder before he learns more secrets to take to the Blackwolds. Hopefully, we're not too late.''Jon was right. I've been a fool. My son warned me against Calder Cob, but I paid him no mind. Calder has always been an able and trustworthy man.

'All the while, he was driving me towards training rather than confronting the brigands. How much information do the brigands have? How much time do we have to prepare? I must get word to my son.

'But first, Calder must pay for this affront!'Strider would like you to earn the favour of Captain Brackenbrook if you can, so you find yourself offering your aid to a loyal soldier named Calder Cob.Wolves can be found near Archet, and seem to be most concentrated around Bronwe's Folly.

Calder Cob, a trusted soldier of Captain Brackenbrook, has asked you to look into Archet's wolf problem.Defeat wolves around Bronwe's Folly (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search atop Bronwe's Folly for the source of the wolvesYou found a strange banner atop the ruins at Bronwe's Folly.

You should take a closer look at this banner....Use the Blackwold Banner to summon the offender <rgb=#ffff00>(Do not leave the platform)</rgb>Calder Cob stands at the farm just down the road from Archet.

Before you go back to Strider, you should ask him why he tried to have you ambushed by Blackwolds.Ask Calder Cob why he set you up to be ambushed'Well well, if it isn't the rumour-monger! I've heard all about you, ${PLAYER}.

'As you can see for yourself, there aren't no brigands causing problems. It's the wolves that threaten us lately. They seem to have gathered around Bronwe's Folly, especially about the top of the ruins.

'Brackenbrook sent you to assist me, and assist me you shall. I would like you to look into this wolf problem we are having.''It's always interesting when a stranger comes into town squawking about nonsense. Such folk don't always meet happy ends.''H-how is it that you stand before me? A weakling like you defeated the Wolf-master? Bah! I would kill you myself if that fool Dirk Mudbrick weren't watching.

'No matter. I do not fear exposure. Brackenbrook will never believe you. He thinks I have served him loyally since I was but a lad, the old fool.

'Tell Brackenbrook whatever you like. But Archet WILL fall, and I'll make out with more gold than you can fathom! And you... you will die with the rest, if you do not make yourself scarce before tonight.'If Skorgrím is indeed the source of Elrond's disturbing premonition, the site of his final deeds should be examined.The ruins of Edhelion are north-east along the road from where Elladan stands.

You should enter the ruins of Edhelion and seek the place where Skorgrím fell.Talk to Dorniel about her memories of EdhelionThe ruins of Edhelion are north-east along the road from where Elladan stands.

You should enter the ruins of Edhelion and seek the place where Skorgrím fell.Talk to Naithriel about her memories of EdhelionThe ruins of Edhelion are north-east along the road from where Elladan stands.

You should enter the ruins of Edhelion and seek the place where Skorgrím fell.Talk to Dorongur about his memory of Skorgrím's death'I will give Dorollas' theory a chance, since we are here. Merethen is not unconvinced either. We should investigate the ruins of Edhelion, the place where Skorgrím fell, to ensure that he is still dead.

'The Elves watched him die, so if Skorgrím's grave is undisturbed, then the mystery will be even greater.''The ruins are north-east along the road from here. Seek the place where Skorgrím met his doom.''I am lucky to be alive after the injuries I bore the day Edhelion fell. I...I do not think I have the will to go back into that place.

'It is only a shadow of its former glory now. Only pain remains.''You should speak with Naithriel.''I was here when Edhelion fell. I was a healer, but my strength in mending was not enough to mend the hurts caused by Skorgrím and his Dourhand warriors.

'I cannot return here without great sadness in my heart. It was such a needless war! He sought immortality in the relics we kept here, but found only death.''You should speak with Dorongúr Whitethorn.''It was across this bridge that brave Talagan brought the library's walls down upon Skorgrím and himself, thus putting an end to Skorgrím's lust for immortality. The walls smote them both as they crumbled.

'But that is a strange flower, one that I have never seen before. Is it familiar to you, ${RACE}?'The body of Skorgrím was last seen several years ago by dwarf-miners in the Silver Deep Mine, where the ruined cellars of Edhelion were found for the first time since its fall.The Silver Deep Mine is west of the ruins of Edhelion, at the bottom of the stair-path leading down the Mountain.

You should follow the stairs down and enter the Silver Deep Mine to search for Skorgrím's body once again.Defeat pests as you seek Skorgrím's body (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The place where Skorgrím's body was discovered deep in the mine, where the sun touches the old ruined cellars of Edhelion.

You should seek Skorgrím's body once more to ensure that it does not walk as it did in Elrond's dream.Find the site where Skorgrím's body was foundYou have found the site of Skorgrím's body, but...the body is nowhere to be found. Instead, red flowers are in its place.

You should pick up one of the fell red flowers to bring to Elladan.Collect one of the strange, red flowersElladan awaits your return at the Edhelion Watch.

You should return to Elladan with the flower you collected from the site of Skorgrím's grave.'I have been told Skorgrím's body was discovered by Thorin's folk back when he inhabited this land, before his death.

'The dwarf-miners dug into the mountain and exposed the ruined cellars of Edhelion, and that is where the corpse lay perfectly preserved -- in the Silver Deep Mine.

'When Talagan brought the library down upon them both, they fell to their grave below. You could search for Skorgrím's body where last it was seen, if you seek it still. For my part, I have no wish to look upon Skorgrím again.'''The Silver Deep Mine is west of here, down the stairs that lead down the mountain-side. Inside that mine was where Skorgrím's body was discovered.''That is a vile, little flower, and one I have not seen before. You say it grew where Skorgrím died, and where his body lay in death for all these years? Such magic is not common with dwarves....

'His body has been moved, though we do not know where. It seems that the flowers follow him in death. Perhaps they will lead to his new grave.'Within the dungeons of Barad-dûr, a foul larder feeds the many thralls of the Dark Lord.You are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.Sullied plates can be found throughout the dungeons of Barad-dûr.Collect sullied plates in the dungeons of Barad-dûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A washing-tub can be found in the Foul Larder in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.Clean the plates in the Foul Larder's washing-tubThe cleaned plates can be found in the Foul Larder in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.You are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.The Stout-axes are forced to serve as the metalsmiths of the Dark Lord in the dungeons of the Dark Tower.You are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.Crude iron bars can be found at Anghnúl, the Forge of Torment.Collect crude iron bars at Anghnúl, the Forge of TormentForges can be found at Anghnúl, the Forge of Torment.Heat the iron bars in one of the forges at AnghnúlAnvils can be found at Anghnúl, the Forge of Torment.Hammer the iron bar into the shape of an Orkish bladeGrindstones can be found at Anghnúl, the Forge of Torment.Hone the Orkish blade on a grindstoneForges can be found at Anghnúl, the Forge of Torment.Heat the Orkish blade in one of the forges at AnghnúlA tub can be found at Anghnúl, the Forge of Torment.Quench and temper the blade in a tub at AnghnúlA rack can be found at Anghnúl, the Forge of Torment.You are fated to labour in service to the Dark Lord.With your help, Ned Pruner has managed to interrogate the prisoner, Calder Cob.

Ned has asked you to present your findings to Captain Brackenbrook.Ned Pruner has asked you to report your findings to Captain Brackenbrook.Speak with Captain Brackenbrook'You've been an immense help, ${PLAYER_NAME}.

Would you be so kind as to report our findings to Captain Brackenbrook?

