<rgb=#00FF00>This is a tutorial quest for accessing the web store.</rgb>Talk to Skardi Bendblade in his shop.'If you plan to continue helping Mossward, I'd happily part with a steed should you desire one.'

<rgb=#00FF00>NOTE: Accepting and completing this quest can only be done once on each server. If you logout before completing this quest, it will be removed from your quest log and you will need to accept it again. This will grant you access to a tutorial quest to introduce you to the LOTRO Store.</rgb>'Very good!'You assisted Dwalin and the sons of Elrond against the evil forces stirring in Thorin's Gate, and these efforts have not gone unnoticed. The Lord of the Longbeards sent you a missive which he hopes will bring you favour.Deliver the letter of thanks to Laenin the Glade Watcher in Celondim.

Dwalin, the Lord of the Longbeards, sent you a letter of thanks for your efforts against Ivar the Bloodhand. His hope is that this letter will earn you some measure of reward from the Elves or Dwarves.The letter reads:

Be it known that I, Dwalin, Lord of the Longbeards of the Blue Mountains and Steward of Thorin's Hall, write this on behalf of ${PLAYER}. I fought alongside ${PLAYER} to stop a dangerous and unearthly ritual from taking place -- the resurrection of Skorgrím, king of the Dourhands of old, by the Gaunt-lord Ivar the Bloodhand.

Should it be within your power, please give ${PLAYER} some measure of welcome and thanks for all that was done.

Dwalin
Lord of the Longbeards of the Blue Mountains
Steward of Thorin's Hall'

Apparently Dwalin remembers well the travels you and he had together. Seek out Laenin at Celondim or Bogi Deepdelver to see what this letter will yield.'Your name is well known, ${PLAYER}. It is not often that a hero of your stature visits me. I will honour you as Lord Dwalin honours you. Please accept these as a token of welcome in these lands.

'Speak with me again and look among my wares. You may find something there to your liking, and I will gladly barter for what you desire.''Lord Dwalin deems that we give you thanks and I honour his request. Take these and speak with me again. I will share with you what we can offer.

'It may not be much, but it is certain that these will help an adventurer such as you.'Your assistance against the bandits who burned and raided Archet is worthy of much merit from the people of the Shire and Bree-land. Jon Brackenbrook has seen that you are given some measure of favour.Deliver the letter of thanks to Constable Thistlewool in Archet or Postman Newbuck in Little Delving.

Jon Brackenbrook has written a letter on your behalf thanking you for your assistance with the Blackwold brigands who recently assaulted and destroyed much of Archet. He hopes that you will gain some measure of thanks from others.The letter reads:

'Be it known that I, Jon Brackenbrook, overseeing the rebuilding of Archet, write this on behalf of ${PLAYER}. I fought alongside ${PLAYER} in an attempt to thwart the Blackwold brigands and their Angmarim masters.

Should it be within your power, give ${PLAYER}, some measure of welcome and thanks for all that they have done.

Jon Brackenbrook


Apparently, Jon Brackenbrook wishes you well in your future endeavours.'I heard what you did. Mundo will never admit to it but what you did with the tall folk will be talked about behind your back for years! To think, you helped save not only two hobbits from the Shire, but a whole town.

'Merry me, you must have a little Baggins in you. Here, take these and then look through my wares. You may find something there to your liking, adventurer!''I remember your face and your actions. You are a hero to us all.

'I will do what I can, though we do not have much to offer at the moment. Take these and then speak with me again to see what else I can offer you.'Halli has asked you to help him improve his brother's reputation in the guard by having his tarnished armour polished.Brúni Stonehelm can be found among the armour merchants of Thorin's Hall, where the canal runs through the mountain.

Halli asks you to take his brother's armour to Brúni Stonehelm.In return for polishing Halli's armour, Brúni asks you to collect the damaged armour from the guards at Noglond, the way-station south of Thorin's Hall.Brúni is by the armour merchants in Thorin's Hall.

You should take the armour you collected to Brúni to be mended.Halli is in Frerin's Court, south of Thorin's Hall.

Brúni has given you Halli's armour, cleaned and polished, to return to its owner.'Hello there, friend. I was just thinking of all the things I've got to do and me here on duty.

'I've got my brother's armour to get polished. He'd do it himself, if he had a mind to, but I'm afraid Kalli does not have our family's sense of duty. He'll never earn his commander's respect; always being late, never diligent in his duties, always wearing his old, worn armour and filthy uniform.

'Perhaps you could be of some service to an old warrior. Could you bring this armour up to Brúni Stonehelm and have him polish it for me? Brúni's stands among the armour merchants of Thorin's Hall, where the canal runs through the mountain.''Have you not brought the armour to Brúni yet? Do not tarry; Kalli will need his armour shined bright to impress the commander!''What's this? I know that armour! That's Halli's, unless I miss my guess. I haven't the time to polish his armour again. I'm far too busy!

'I was supposed to go down to Noglond, the way-station to the south, and pick up the guards' damaged armour. No, I have no time to clean Halli's armour today. You will just have to leave it here, and I will see if I can get to it before next week. Unless... you can go down to Noglond and retrieve the guards' armour for me.''Have you not brought the armour to Brúni yet? He's in the western hall with the other smiths, and Kalli will need his armour shined bright to impress the commander!''The Noglond guards have got more damaged armour than that, and it's not going to drag itself up the mountain! If I have to go down there and get it I'll not be able to polish Halli's armour.''Brúni's got someone else to do his errands for him again, eh? Very well, here's my other armour. You might want to check with Olafr, too. His armour was torn up bad a few days back in a scuffle with some goblins.''I've been waiting for Brúni to come down. We expected him the other day, but as usual, he put us off again! I've got a dent in my armour a hand and a half long. Poxy goblin would have cut me from shoulder to belly if not for that hunk of metal!''I don't blame Brúni for not coming out of his nice warm forge up at Thorin's Halls. That's where I'd stay if I were him, not trapessing out here in the cold.''Have you not brought the armour to Brúni yet? He's in the merchant's area of Thorin's Hall, and Kalli will need his armour shined bright to impress the commander!''Be sure to tell Brúni to replace that strap on the left side of my armour. He should have plenty of time up there at the forge.''There you are. What's taken you so long? Let me see these.... Thorin's beard! Have they been wrestling oliphaunts? I could forge two suits of armour in the time it will take me to hammer this out.'

The dwarf-smith looks up at you. 'Oh yes, here is the armour you wanted shined.''That's a handsome suit of armour, but it's not mine. If you're still running errands for Brúni, you'll want to ask him who that armour belongs to.''I'd be surprised if Durin himself could fix my armour up nice as the set you've got there. You must have me mixed up with someone else. Check with Brúni at the forge to see who that armour belongs to.''Halli's going to want his armour back right away. Best you take it to him now. He's usually on duty down by the gate to the courtyard.''Aye, that's just the thing. Kalli will look sharp as an axe in this. The commander's sure to notice him now!'Alla has been issued a second dare by the Mossward bully, and she needs your help once again.Alla has given you five minutes to reach the spot in question along the road in view of Tharbad.Make it to the marked spot along the road to Tharbad without running out of time<rgb=#FF0000>Do not run out of time before reaching the correct location</rgb>Alla is by a haystack in north-eastern Mossward. You only have five minutes for the return journey!Return to Alla in north-eastern Mossward without running out of time<rgb=#FF0000>Do not run out of time before reaching the correct location</rgb>Alla is by a haystack in north-eastern Mossward.Talk to Alla in north-eastern Mossward'I really appreciate your help with that, ${PLAYER}. When I go to complete that dare, now I know how to do it, and that it's possible, and that's going to make a big difference.

'But you are not going to believe this. The bully has issued a SECOND dare! He must know I am well-prepared to finish the first one, so he's already made up this second one. Will you help me with this one too? I simply must know if this is possible.

'The same rules are at play this time as there were for the first time: five minutes out there, and five minutes back. I'll mark the spot on your map, as I did before. This time you're going within view of the flooded city of Tharbad!''Remember, you only have five minutes to reach the spot I marked on your map! Hurry, hurry, hurry!''Hurry, hurry!''Welcome back! I am less surprised this time, for you have proven quite capable of finishing these dares! Now I know this one is also possible, and when I do it I will have less to fear, even though the grown-ups always say getting so near to Tharbad is dangerous.

'So, what did you see when you got to that location? Anything notable?'

You tell her that there was a shovel standing in the dirt, but its owner was nowhere to be seen.

'Very interesting, all right. Thank you once again! That is the last of the Mossward bully's dares, so I won't be needing your help anymore. But you have been most helpful, and I appreciate it!'Cal Sprigley's farm has been overrun by spiders. The farmer and his wife fled to Archet, leaving their belongings behind.Cal Sprigley can be found north of the ruins of The Mad Badger Inn in Archet.

After spiders attacked his farm, Cal Sprigley and his wife fled to the safety of Archet. Atli Spider-bane has asked you to speak with the farmer.Talk to Cal Sprigley in ArchetCal Sprigley's farm is south of Bronwe's Folly.

Cal Sprigley has asked you to go to his farm and recover his strongbox, seed sack, and bow. With these things, he might be able to make a fresh start.Collect Sprigley's seed bagCollect Sprigley's strongboxCollect Sprigley's bowCal Sprigley and his wife await you north of the ruins of The Mad Badger Inn in Archet.

Cal and Holly Sprigley are waiting in Archet for the possessions you recovered from their spider-infested farm. You should return to them at once.'Don't worry about me, ${PLAYER}. It's just a minor wound I got in the fighting.

'Now that the Brackenbrooks, father and son, have driven the Blackwolds away from Archet, perhaps these folk can get to living their lives as they once did. Word has reached me, though, that there's a new threat to be dealt with.

'A nearby farm has been overrun with spiders, and the folk there have retreated to Archet. My injury prevents me from dealing with the pests, but you have proven yourself a capable warrior and should have no trouble. Look for the farmer here in Archet. You may know him already... his name is Cal Sprigley.''Sprigley and his wife fled to Archet with what little he could carry from his farm. The spiders must have come upon them suddenly.''There we were, ready to stand our ground against them Blackwold villains, when these monstrous spiders come pouring up from the cellar in the middle of the night. It seems hardly fair!

'Still, if the Spider-bane sent you, it could be you'll be able to help us out. Our farm is due south of Bronwe's Folly. If you can recover my seed bag from the pens and my strongbox from the storage shed, we could make a new start of it. Oh, and my father's bow as well! Poor Henry was trying to kill some of the spiders with it. He was a good hand, but the spiders made quick work of the lad.

'Hurry back, if you can... though with all the spiders around my farm, I don't see how you will.''I am sure you will be of great help to Sprigley. Spiders are no friends of Men and must be dealt with severely if they are to be dealt with at all.''My farm is to the south of Bronwe's Folly, down the second eastward trail from the south road. The place is much changed now -- a wretched nest of spiders.''The spiders came up from the cellar in the night, and we had barely enough time to escape! Many of the farmhands weren't so lucky. We saw poor Henry trying to fight off the spiders in the side yard with Cal's bow.

'If you can recover that bow, our seed bag from the livestock pens, and my strongbox near the storage shed, we'll be mighty grateful.''You should bring Sprigley his belongings at once. Such possessions are nearly as important to a farmer as my axe is to me.''I hope you can drive those horrible spiders off our land for good! We're decent, law-abiding folk and shouldn't have to put up with such troubles!''This is everything we asked for, all right: my seed bag, strongbox, and my father's trusty bow! I can't thank you enough, ${PLAYER}, and I must beg your pardon for treating you so poorly earlier.

'Had I known what was to become of my farm, I would have heeded your advice and retreated to Archet at once, saving ourselves a great deal of trouble... and poor Henry his life.

'Still, I am glad we can make a new start. Tell the Spider-bane he has my thanks as well for sending you to us.'Cledd asked you to defeat the warg that has come to command the nearby wolf pack.There is a Warg at Howlingstones.

Find and defeat the Warg.Defeat the Warg at the HowlingstonesTrack the Warg deeper into the HowlingstonesFollow the tracks southInspect the slain deer and prepare for a fightCledd can be found near the eastern gate of Mossward.

Talk to Cledd.Talk to Cledd'Look there, friend. The ruins to the east have long been home to a pack of wolves. They have always been content to leave us alone, and we were all too happy to return the favour. Something seems to have upset this unspoken pact. The wolves have grown aggressive. I dared to venture close to the ruins and eyed a great beast known as a warg among their number.

'I didn't think it to be real at first. Wargs are monsters we tell the children about to get them to behave!

'We have our hands full with rebuilding Mossward and recovering from the attack. We lack the strength to fight this beast. If you were to slay the warg, you would spare both ourselves and the wolves from needless conflict.''I'm glad to see you return safely and victorious! With any luck, the wolves will return to their usual selves before too long, though it may take some time. There is something foul in the air, and I fear our troubles are not entirely over. Still, I think the people of Mossward can breathe a bit easier now, in no small part thanks to your heroics.''Howlingstones is south-east of here. I spied the Warg amongst the wolves. Check near the husk of the giant tree. If it's not there, perhaps you'll have to search deeper....'Complete 10 quests in Ered Luin.Complete 10 Ered Luin quests.Complete quests in Ered LuinWith winter coming soon, Bevan knows the store-houses of Mossward need to be stocked with salted and preserved boar-meat.Mosshide boars dwell near the Old South Road, and will prove a good source of the boar-steaks for which Bevan asked.Collect boar-meat from Mosshide boars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bevan is at the north gate of Mossward, waiting for you to return with boar-meat.'But such musings will have to wait, for winter is approaching and autumn doesn't last. If the store-houses are not stocked with salted and preserved boar-meat by the time the nights turn cold, Mossward will go hungry. Unless the Uruks come back, I suppose! No, don't tell anyone I said that. It is not funny.

'But we always have need of boar-meat, and we are fortunate that many such creatures dwell nearby. If you return to me with fine cuts of boar-steak, all of Mossward will toast your name when winter comes.''We always have need of boar-meat, and we are fortunate that many such creatures dwell nearby. If you return to me with fine cuts of boar-steak, all of Mossward will toast your name when winter comes.''Very good, ${PLAYER}, very good! I will see this boar-meat is salted and preserved, and it should help carry Mossward through some of the coldest winter months, when belts must be tightened and plates seem lightest. I am glad this task, at least, proved helpful for the town!

'Aye, I have abandoned my idea of using those craban feathers. A number of uses? My wife said the number might as well have been zero after she tried the pillow I made from them. "Bevan, you fool!" she said to me, "It takes more than eight feathers to make a pillow, and anyone who tries it with craban feathers, of all things, deserves the crimp it would leave in his neck!"

'I suppose the good ideas that spring up in autumn... well, they fall when winter comes. I'd rather deal with the threat of Uruk war-bands loose in the Swanfleet than present my wife with another one of my brand-new ideas! I think I'll stick to guarding the town from now on... it's less damaging to my morale!'Éogar can always use more help on his farm, and today he needs the hay for the horse's bedding replaced.The hay-piles can be found at Hengstacer Farm, in the field north of the stables.Collect fresh hay in the north field (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Billy, Bobby, Lizzie, and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first. They must be cared for in the right order.

Éogar's old hay-fork is well worn and can be used on the dirty hay only so often before it breaks.Replace the bedding of the first horseBilly, Bobby, Lizzie, and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first. They must be cared for in the right order.

Éogar's old hay-fork is well worn and can be used on the dirty hay only so often before it breaks.Replace the bedding of the second horseBilly, Bobby, Lizzie, and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first. They must be cared for in the right order.

Éogar's old hay-fork is well worn and can be used on the dirty hay only so often before it breaks.Replace the bedding of the third horseBilly, Bobby, Lizzie, and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first. They must be cared for in the right order.

Éogar's old hay-fork is well worn and can be used on the dirty hay only so often before it breaks.Replace the bedding of the fourth horseÉogar may be found at Hengstacer Farm in the Horse-fields of Bree-land.Talk to Éogar and inform him the bedding has been replaced'Are you occupied? A stable-help ran by on his way to finish an errand and told me the bedding in the new horse's stable needs to be replaced, and as soon as possible. Unfortunately, Billy, Bobby, Lizzie, and Henry -- as the stable-hands have named them -- are finicky about who gets attention first, as they have a bit of a pecking order. We need to be careful to care for them in the right order, as we must not upset them too much.

'It seems the stable-help has taken all the good hay-forks, and all I have left are old and brittle ones. You will only be able to use these old hay-forks on the dirty hay so many times before they will break, at which point you will have to come see me again for another.''Thank you for taking care of the horses' bedding for me!'For too long, Boar-kind has plagued the land. In your efforts, you have shown a desire to drive them from Middle-earth.Danger presses upon Bree-land from all sides, foreshadowing the ascension of a great darkness. You are called to stand against the Shadow. Your efforts on behalf of Bree-land will be rewarded.Undertake quests in Bree-land.Complete quests within Bree-landMany bands of brigands roam the wilds of Bree-land, waylaying travellers and bullying the inhabitants of Bree and the towns surrounding it. It is up to you to counter the threat the brigands pose to the inhabitants of Bree-land.Defeat brigands in Bree-landDefeat brigands in the Shire.Defeat brigands in the ShireMany bands of brigands roam the wilds of Bree-land, waylaying travellers and bullying the inhabitants of Bree and the towns surrounding it. It is up to you to counter the threat the brigands pose to the inhabitants of Bree-land.Defeat brigands in Bree-landDefeat many brigands in the Shire.Defeat brigands in the ShireBuilder Earur provided directions to one who can assist you, should you desire to take on a profession.You should find a Master of Apprentices willing to take on pupils in Combe.

Builder Earur directed you to a crafting master in Combe. He mentioned that the master can be found by following the left path once you enter Combe centre.Speak with the Master of Apprentices'If you ever want to take up a trade yourself, then you'll need some guidance on the matters. I'd offer my services but Archet needs my skills more now friend; I hope you understand. I can point you toward one who can give you the assistance that you seek, however.

'You'll want to head south out of Archet and towards the centre of Combe. When the road splits in Combe centre follow the road to the left and make your way part way up the hill. You'll see a master of crafts there who is always willing, ready, and able to take on apprentices.

'Be safe friend and once again, thank you for all you've done for Archet. You're the reason that we've a town to still work on repairing after all.''Greetings, traveller. If you are looking to take on a profession, I am willing to train you. I have spent my life learning the fundamentals of all crafts. You will never see me hoist a weapon, save to assess its quality.'Alf Goodcliff thinks you could be a crafter of some skill and suggested you visit his friend Emerald Borings at the Craft-fair on the south side of Michel Delving.Emerald Borings is at the Michel Delving Craft-fair, south-west of the statue in the town centre, past the stables, and along the first leftward turning.

Alf Goodcliff suggested you speak with his friend Emerald Borings if you are interested in pursuing a crafting profession.'Have you already been to the Michel Delving Craft-fair? You should definitely go, if you haven't already! There's a workbench, a forge, and even an oven just waiting to be used!

'If you think you have crafting in your heart, you should visit my friend Emerald Borings at the Craft-fair -- she's always happy to help someone get started making useful and pretty things.

'Pass east through Little Delving, and then follow the path south into Michel Delving. Take the south-west path from the statue of Marcho and Blanco in the town centre, and pass the stables on your right. Take the next left turn to reach the Craft Fair. Emerald will be happy to help you out!''Pass east through Little Delving, and then follow the path south into Michel Delving. Take the south-west path from the statue of Marcho and Blanco in the town centre and pass the stables on your right. Take the next left turn to reach the Craft-fair.

'Emerald will be happy to help you out!''Alf sent you to me? Good, good! We need more good folk with an interest in making useful and pretty things! Speak with the Mistress of Apprentices, and she can help you choose professions in which to specialize. Choose your professions with care, because you will expend a great deal of time and energy improving your skills.

'Once the Mistress of Apprentices has welcomed you to your chosen professions, be sure to speak with a Supplier who can sell you the tools of your trade -- every profession has its own tools, so be not over-shy with your coinpurse! The novices will be happy to sell you any recipes you might wish to have, though I can tell you now that you will already know how to make a thing or two.

'Equip the crafting tools you plan on using and find an appropriate facility -- Michel Delving has a forge, workbench, and oven available for your use -- and begin practising your skills! You will advance in your chosen professions as you practice and seek out the teachings of others in the field. I hope you will become a skilled crafter, ${PLAYER}, and that it will bring profit to you and to the Shire! I will give you a few coins to get you started. Use them wisely, and consider them an investment in your future as a skilled crafter!'For centuries the Mearas have freely roamed the plains of Rohan, only bowing before the kings and princes of the Rohirrim.The horse appears to be staring off into the distance, as if he now knows where he needs to go.Check on the horse from CombeTalk to Éogar in the Horsefields'The horse is acting strange as of late. He keeps staring to the south-east, always focused there. It's as if something is out there waiting for him, and he knows it.''So, he is eager to return to his herd? It warms my heart to hear he received his calling. I hope to see him one day returned to his true home.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Completing this quest will grant the Favour of the Mearas skill.</rgb>  

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: The skill from this quest can only be used while mounted on a war-steed in the fields of Rohan.</rgb>The horse stamps at the ground and looks anxious to be free of his stall, out running free....

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will not be able to leave the region the character starts in, as this character and will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>Without knowing where we have come from, we cannot possibly know where we are going.

Éogar, master of Hengstacer Farm, will look for help around the farm and for someone to help train the new arrival once per day.Horses have memories longer than most Men....Complete Bedbugs BiteComplete Herding to the North DownsComplete The Horsefields DerbyComplete Feed for the HorsesComplete Worse for WearComplete Every Last DropComplete Herding to the TrollshawsComplete Herding to the Lone-landsComplete Proof of TrustThe stable-helper wants you to assist the new horse in settling into its new stall in the Combe horse stables.The new horse in the Combe stables needs some help settling into his new stall.Fill the water-bucketEnsure the food-trough has grainInspect the horse's beddingThe newly arrived horse in Combe may be found in his new stall.

The horse is strange to Combe and is still uneasy in his new environment. <rgb=#FF0000>Pat</rgb> the horse to comfort him.<rgb=#FF0000>Pat</rgb> the horse to comfort him in his new stallThe stable-helper is near the stables of Combe.Talk to the stable-helper'An unusual horse arrived in the stable here down at the end, but I have no time to help him settle into his new stall. I need to tend to these other horses or the stable-master will have my head! Would you please help me tend to the horse's stall and make sure he has everything he needs?

'For new horses, I usually check the bedding for freshness and the trough for grain. Make sure he has plenty of water, too!''Thank you for your help! That horse looks more comfortable in the new stall already, and appears to be pretty well taken care of now. You may have acquired a new friend in this horse; he seems to have taken a liking to you.'Éogar can always use more help on his farm, and today he desperately needs help filling the horses' water buckets.The trick is, Billy, Bobby, Lizzie and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first, so we need to be careful to do them in the right order. They can be found in their stalls centred around the well here at the horse farm.Collect a bucket of well waterThe trick is, Billy, Bobby, Lizzie and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first, so we need to be careful to do them in the right order. They can be found in their stalls centred around the well here at the horse farm.Collect a bucket of well waterThe trick is, Billy, Bobby, Lizzie and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first, so we need to be careful to do them in the right order. They can be found in their stalls centred around the well here at the horse farm.Collect a bucket of well waterThe trick is, Billy, Bobby, Lizzie and Henry are finicky about who gets attention first, so we need to be careful to do them in the right order. They can be found in their stalls centred around the well here at the horse farm.Collect a bucket of well waterÉogar is awaiting your return near the stables of the horse farm.Return to Éogar at Hengstacer Farm'Hey, you there! Do you have a free moment? I could use some help filling the water in the horses' buckets. The trick is, Billy, Bobby, Lizzie and Henry are finicky about who gets filled up first, as they have a bit of a pecking order. 

'They are a little funny about who gets attention first, so we need to be careful to do them in the right order. We can't upset them too much.

'If you spill too many buckets of water we'll have to cut you off from using the well for a while. We can't risk the well running dry, so we can't be too wasteful!''Thank you! The horses seem much happier now.'The stone beneath Thorin's Gate is honeycombed by cave-claw burrows. If the damage continues, the entire area could be weakened enough to collapse on itself.Cave-claws are found along the hill-side west of Edhelion, scattered near the entrance and within the Silver-deep.

Orodlin asked you to defeat cave-claws found throughout Thorin's Gate and deliver the message that you have to Bogi at Frerin's Court.Defeat cave-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bogi can be found in the centre of Thorin's Gate at Frerin's Court west of Edhelion in the centre of the valley.'The cave-claws are destroying the land with their rampant digging. Without some way to reduce their numbers, I fear the ground will collapse beneath our feet. Even the Dourhands are aware of the menace, but the sluggards have done nothing.

'Bogi, a Longbeard Dwarf at Frerin's Court, asked that I organize efforts to thin the number of cave-claws to help prevent further damage.

'You will find the cave-claws along the hillside west of the ruins of Edhelion, surrounding and within the Silver Deep at the base of the hill. When you have done this task, seek Bogi at Frerin's Court in the centre of Thorin's Gate, to the west.''We cannot undo the damage wrought by the cave-claws, but their future impact on the caverns will be minimal. Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for all you have done.''The mindless beasts dig and dig without a care for the damage they do. Someone must kill the cave-claws before they do any more damage.'Éogar can always use more help on his farm, and today he needs help feeding the horses.There are many bags and sacks of grain spread around the main buildings of Hengstacer Farm.Find grain in the area (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Éogar is found by the stables of the horse-farm.Return to Éogar with the grain'The horses are sounding hungry, and I have been told their troughs are running empty. I need to have a stable-hand feed the horses very shortly, or they may get agitated, but the helpers are busy at the moment! Can you please help me start on the task and gather the grain? As soon as you get back with it, a helper should be available to feed them.

'There are many bags and sacks of grain around the farm; some might be empty, but there should be enough full ones. Hurry back with the grain!''Well done! We should be stocked for a little while now. Thank you for your help!'Horses can be trained and respond to different tones of voice or signals.The horse can be found out in the Horse-fields.Tell Éogar what happened'The new horse that came here with you from Combe looks anxious, and you should spend some time with him. Head out into the Horse-fields and see what you can do.''Well done! The horse just got back before you, and he is looking much more comfortable.'Refkell is incredibly proud of his last catch and wishes to show it off to his friend.Noglond is south of Thorin's Hall, south and east of the Vale of Thrain, along the road to the Low Lands.

Refkell has asked that you visit Nokki and tell him of his latest catch.Talk to Nokki'At your service, ${CLASS}. Now that you have learned the ways of the fisherman, perhaps you could aid me in delivering a message to an old friend.

'I wish to inform Nokki of my latest catch, the largest I have ever seen and I daresay the largest ever caught in Ered Luin! It was enormous, I tell you -- nearly a stone in weight! A pity that I don't have proof of my catch, for after I had the beast in my bucket it made a mighty leap and escaped back into the channel.

'Go to Noglond and speak with Nokki. Tell him of my catch and see if he has caught any bigger.''Another fish-tale from Refkell? You are the third person this week to come from him with stories of a giant catch that managed to slip through his fingers.

'But never mind that. If you are in need of fishing supplies you will find no greater store of equipment to suit your needs anywhere else.''Have you told Nokki my tale? He is at Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall, along the road to the Low Lands.'The Stable-helper wants you to help the newly-arrived horse to settle into his new stall at the Combe stables.The food for the food-trough can be found around the stable area.Find grain in the area (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The grain can be placed in the food-trough inside the new horse's stall.Return the grain to the troughThis food-trough looks empty. There seems to be a decent supply of grain in the area. Search the containers for grain to put in the food-trough.Frostmantle is a great aurochs-bull that dwells in Thorin's Gate. The beast is surly and ill-tempered, charging any dwarf that dares cross its path.Frostmantle roams the area by the old obelisk in hills west of Frerin's Court.

Slay the aurochs called "Frostmantle" and bring back one of its horns to Bolli as proof of your victory.<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest has been restored for Legendary Servers!</rgb>

'If you know the aurochs, you know what a menace they can be when something raises their ire. One of them is a brute of a particular and foul disposition, a beast Durin's Folk call Frostmantle.

'We can't get close to Frostmantle without him charging, and it's getting too dangerous to leave alone. I fear that someone's bound to get trampled, gored or worse! What say you go and kill the brute? Return with one of its horns and I'll see to it that you're rewarded.

'You'll find it wandering to the west of Frerin's Court here, by the old obelisk.''Ah, you have done it. That'll keep the area a bit safer, eh?

'Good job!'Wenna is concerned that her husband Geralt recently lost one of his favourite boots, and she wants you to find it, if you can.Wenna told you her husband lost his favourite boot on the edge of the Wadewater, to the north of Mossward.Find Geralt's missing boot somewhere on the edge of the Wadewater, to the north of MosswardA mysterious object in the mud on the edge of the Wadewater could be Geralt's missing boot.Search the pile of mud on the edge of the WadewaterWenna is outside her home in south-east Mossward.Bring Geralt's favourite boot to his wife Wenna in south-east MosswardWenna's husband Geralt is by the north gate of Mossward.'You are an adventurer? My husband was once like you, but he gave it up to settle down and have a family, and never looked back! But I do have need of an adventurer today, if you're interested in helping me. My husband has lost a boot!

'Oh, it's not just any boot. It's his favourite, and it would be a shame to discard the remaining one just because he misplaced its mate. He lost it walking out by the edge of the Wadewater, to the north, and upon getting stuck in the mud it just came free of his foot! If you can find it and bring it back to me I would really appreciate it.''My husband lost his favourite boot walking out by the edge of the Wadewater, to the north, and upon getting stuck in the mud it just came free of his foot! If you can find it and bring it back to me I would really appreciate it.''My husband lost his favourite boot walking out by the edge of the Wadewater, to the north, and upon getting stuck in the mud it just came free of his foot! If you can find it and bring it back to me I would really appreciate it.''You found it! He is going to be so happy, ${PLAYER}!

'You should bring it to him! He used to be an adventurer, you know, and he travelled far and wide helping folk with their problems. Sometimes I think he fills the head of our boy Tegwyn with too many tales of his old adventures, but maybe if he hears about some of yours it will satisfy his appetite for the things.

'I think Geralt is by the north gate, wearing his old leather shoes.''My husband Geralt is probably by the north gate of Mossward, wearing his old leather shoes. He will be so pleased to see his favourite boot returned to him!''What is... what is this?'

You hand his favourite boot to him, and Geralt stares at you with open-mouthed astonishment.

'Why have you brought me this? I thought I was rid of it!'Defeat goblins in the Shire.Defeat goblins in the ShireDefeat goblins in Ered Luin.Defeat goblins in Ered LuinDefeat many goblins in the Shire.Defeat goblins in the ShireDefeat many goblins in Ered Luin.Defeat goblins in Ered LuinDefeat harvest-flies in the Shire.Defeat harvest-flies in the ShireDefeat many harvest-flies in the Shire.Defeat harvest-flies in the ShireDefeat hendrevail in Ered Luin.Defeat hendrevail in Ered LuinDefeat many hendrevail in Ered Luin.Defeat hendrevail in Ered LuinYou received a letter from the owner of Hengstacer Farms, a stable that provides beasts of burden for the lands of Bree. The owner invited you to his farm to possibly acquire a beast of burden that you can call your very own.You should make your way to Hengstacer farms and speak with the owner Éogar.

From the West-gate of Bree travel north along the Greenway until you pass Thornley's Farm on your left and an old ruined fort on your right. There is a thin trail, beaten by the hooves of Hengstacer horses and ponies that leads up the hill beside those ruins. Follow that trail to the east and north, and you will find your way to Hengstacer Farms.Talk to Éogar at Hengstacer FarmsDirections to Hengstacer Farms:

From the West-gate of Bree, travel north along the Greenway until you pass Thornley's Farm on your left and an old ruined fort on your right. There is a thin trail, beaten by the hooves of Hengstacer horses and ponies that leads up the hill beside those ruins. Follow that trail to the east and north, and you will find your way to Hengstacer Farms.'My letter found you then? Excellent news, and even more excellent that you are here. 

'I am Éogar, master of horses here at Hengstacer Farms, and I will tell you that there are no finer horses in all of Bree-land. I supply my horses to all stables far and wide...there are none better save for those of my homeland Rohan. 

'You have already used one of my horses, so you are aware of how good they are, but now I wonder. Are you willing to own such a fine specimen...I wonder?'

<rgb=#00FF00>If you wish to own a mount you can visit the LOTRO Store and purchase the Riding Skill. At level 20, subscribers can return to Hengstacer Farms and unlock this skill through an in-game quest. Free Accounts must purchase the Riding Skill on the LOTRO Store in order to use mount skills in the game.</rgb>The horse from Combe followed you here, and seems content to stay put for the time being...The horse from Combe is on the far side of Hengstacer Farm's main stable area from Éogar.Check on the horse from Combe'The horse from Combe looks restless and needs to be taken out for a daily run. Could you go check on him?'The horse stamps at the ground and looks anxious to be free of his stall, and out running free...

'<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will not be able to leave the region the character starts in, as this character and will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>'The horse from Combe followed you to Hengstacer Farm and seems content to stay there for the time being....The horse from Combe is on the far side of Hengstacer Farm's main stable area.Check on the horse from Combe'The horse from Combe looks restless and needs to be taken out for a daily run. Could you go check on him?'The horse stamps at the ground and looks anxious to be free of his stall and out running free...

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly NPC. You will not be able to leave the region the character starts in, and this character will attain a set of skills unique to it.</rgb>The Horse from Combe followed you here, and seems pretty content to stay here for the time being...The Horse from Combe is on the far side of the horse farm's main stable area from Éogar.Check on the Horse from Combe'The horse from Combe looks restless and needs to be taken out for a daily run. Could you go check on him?'The horse paws at the ground and looks anxious to be free of his stall, and out running free...

'<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will not be able to leave the region the character starts in, as this character and will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>'The Stable-helper wants you to help the newly-arrived horse to settle into his new stall at the Combe stables.The hay-piles can be found around the stables and up the road towards Bree-town and Staddle.Collect fresh hay (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The horse-bedding can be found inside the horse's stall.Replace the horse's beddingThis bedding looks like it's been here forever, probably from the previous tenant in this stall. It's awfully dirty and should certainly be replaced at once. Collect some freshly-cut hay stacks to replace this bedding.An unusual horse you met in Combe seems to have bonded to you. Perhaps you were meant to help him in some way?An unusual horse you met in Combe seems to have bonded to you. Perhaps you were meant to help him in some way?Complete activities with the horseTo truly become a respected member of the Inn League, you must sample all the local beers, ales and wines found throughout Eriador. Seek out all of these beverages to earn the respect of the League.Drink a mug of Blagrove's BrownDrink a glass of Old WinyardsDrink a glass of Limael's VintageDrink a mug of Beakbreaker AleDrink a mug of Toad's Tongue AleDrink a mug of Forsaken AleChoke down a mug of SwillDrink a mug of Forsaken CiderDrink a mug of Old WithywindleDrink a glass of Brandy WineDrink a mug of Green Dragon's Breath AleDrink a glass of 1404 Vintage ReserveDrink a mug of Thistlebelly BrewDrink a glass of WhitebranchDrink a mug of Wooly-foot StoutDrink a mug of Barliman's BestDrink a glass of Blind Troll StoutDrink a mug of Moor-boar BeerDrink a mug of Stars of Old CiderDrink a glass of IsenwineDrink a glass of Dorwinion RedDrink a glass of Dorwinion WhiteDrink a glass of Bombur's Beard LagerIt wasn't easy, but you have passed the grueling Inn League Initiation.Complete the Inn League InitiationAt Dwalin's behest, you have entered Thorin's Halls to confront Gormr about his part in the theft of Hen-heledh.You have accompanied Dwalin into the throne room  of Thorin's Halls. You should speak to him before you confront Gormr.Instead of confronting Gormr, you found him surrounded by Goblins! With the distraction you provided, he was able to escape, but Marrec sent goblins to attack you. You must defend yourself.You have defeated the goblins, but Dwalin has fallen. You should attend to him.Dwalin instructs you to follow after Marrec and stop him from stealing Hen-heledh from Gormr.Follow after MarrecYou have found Gormr, mortally wounded by Marrec. You should speak to him while he yet lives.Marrec has stolen the Seeing-glass from Gormr. He must not escape Thorin's Halls with Hen-heledh.Follow after MarrecMarrec has struck Dwalin down, leaving only you to prevent his escape.Confront MarrecWith Marrec dead and Hen-heledh safe, you should attend to Dwalin.Dwalin informs Mathi Stouthand, who has just entered, that you would tell him the tale of your battle with Marrec.While you were speaking to Mathi, the Lady Arwen entered and began tending Dwalin's wounds. You should speak to her to see how Dwalin fares.'Blah!''Blah!''Blah!''Blah!''Blah!''Blah!'The Dourhand dwarves hope to restore their long-dead leader, Skorgrím, to life. Alongside Dwalin, you have travelled to the tomb delved by the Dourhands for Skorgrím to put an end to their plans.Accompany and defend Dwalin as you make your way into Skorgrím's tomb.Talk to DwalinFollow Dwalin to see if you can stop the resurrection.Talk to DwalinContinue to defend Dwalin as you near your goal: the place where the ritual to restore Skorgrím is being performed!Talk to DwalinHaving fleed the halls, speak with Dwalin one more time.Talk to Dwalin'Are you ready to leave these halls, friend? I, for one, will be glad to put them behind me!''Can you sense it, ${PLAYER}? There's evil in the air here! The last time I felt something like this was when I was crossing through Mirkwood all those years ago. We'll need to keep our wits sharp in here!

'Elrohir and the others are here to help, but we shouldn't delay too long, or we may miss our chance to stop whatever evil is happening here. We must go now! Are you ready?''I fear what Gormr has done. We may be too late, but Ivar is too powerful for us to storm the tomb directly. He will stop us if we try. We will need to find another way around.

'Elladan and Elrohir will go see if they can find an alternate path. We will head up these stairs and see if we can sneak around the side. Let's hurry!''We need to get out of here! We have made a significant blow to the Dourhands, even if we could not stop the ritual from taking place. Skorgrím will have to be dealt with another day.

'Quickly now, we must flee. Whatever Ivar has done, the place is coming down around us!''Ah, even though we did not stop the Dourhands' plans, we have done well this day, ${PLAYER}. At the end of the day, Thorin's Hall shall be free of the Dourhands, and all will know they are dwarves of no account.

'I wonder, though, when will we see the effects of this day and the return of Skorgrím? I will be glad to have you in Thorin's Hall as one of my good and sturdy dwarves.

'Now, let us leave these halls behind us!'Archet is under attack. Jon Brackenbrook and the other hunters have decided to enter the town from the East Gate. You must go forward and learn the fate of Mundo, Celandine, Amdir, and Captain Brackenbrook.You stand outside the breach in Archet's east wall, due west of the Hunter's Lodge.

You must prevent the Blackwolds from capturing Archet.Talk to Jon BrackenbrookNed Pruner is grievously wounded and requires assistance.Talk to Ned PrunerFind a way to get to the centre of Archet and find Amdir.

After you defeated the prisoners, Ned Pruner told you that the Blackwold brigands had attempted to invade Archet at last, and that Amdir helped to defend the Inn. Amdir can be found somewhere ahead; you should aid him in the defence of The Mad Badger Inn.

After Ned died, his poor wife Peg came to attend to his body.Talk to Jon BrackenbrookThe Archet market square is blocked, and Jon Brackenbrook is worried that you are too late. He wants to press on.Talk to Jon BrackenbrookYou were too late to save the crafters' area, but it may not be too late to save all of Archet.Talk to Jon BrackenbrookProtect Archet by defeating the Blackwolds' invasion.

Amdir was rendered powerless by the morgul-wound he suffered from the Nazgûl, and now it is up to you to save Archet from the Blackwolds.Defeat the Blackwolds and their leaderWith Archet saved, you should speak with Jon Brackenbrook.Talk to Jon Brackenbrook'What tragedy has befallen us this night! But we defeated the Blackwold menace. I think it will be long ere they grow so bold again, with or without the help of the evil masters from Angmar.''There is not much time to lose. Already the town burns! We have only a short time to rest here before they see that we have broken through the East Wall. I fear we are less safe by the moment....''Amdir... Amdir's close by. He escaped the slaughter at the Badger. You have to help him... defend the Badger...!

'Those Blackwolds want the hobbit... and the Captain. I... I saw something in the flames... go after them! You must save them...!''You need to find a way to the Badger. The Blackwolds are attacking every corner of town. Quickly, go find Amdir and end these Blackwolds! Leave me with my poor Ned....''Calder Cob's and Otto's treachery were just the beginning of this battle, I fear. We must find a way to The Mad Badger Inn. Peg has left us a way into the marketplace. Perhaps there is a way in through there! Follow me!''The marketplace is safe for now, but we must press on! If we tarry too long, we will lose all of Archet!  

'We must find another way into the centre of town!''You have fared well, my friend, but all might be lost nonetheless. We have protected the market square and the crafters' area. Already The Mad Badger burns. Perhaps my father is still alive but... I hold little hope.

'Follow Atli and me! We will defend what is left of this town to the death, if we must.''This is a sad day indeed. Archet is burned, my father is dead, and the Ranger was taken by evil Men, if Men they can be called.  

Now, all we can do is wait for the flames to die down. Then... with luck, we may begin to rebuild our poor town.'Dwalin has asked you to travel with him and join the sons of Elrond in Skorgrím's Tomb. The evil stirred by the Dourhands must be quelled before the heinous resurrection of Skorgrím can take place.Dwalin asked you to travel with him to Skorgrím's tomb and put an end to the Dourhands' mad schemes. 

You should speak with him again when you are ready to leave.Talk to DwalinDwalin asked you to travel with him to Skorgrím's tomb and put an end to the Dourhands' mad schemes. 

You should speak with him again when you are ready to leave.Talk to DwalinSkógi wishes to speak with you.

Two years have passed since the events in Skorgrím's tomb, but you have remained in the Blue Mountains to help the Longbeards reclaim their halls./Eilian wishes to speak with you.

Two years have passed since the events in Skorgrím's tomb, but you have remained in Ered Luin to help protect the Refuge of Duillond.Talk to SkógiTalk to Eilian'We cannot allow the Dourhands to resurrect their king with such foul sorcery, ${PLAYER}. They have poisoned the mountains and soiled the lands of Thorin. Gormr's fall to corruption is unforgiveable!

'Come, let us journey to the tomb. The sons of Elrond are waiting. We will make a great stand against the Dourhands, and they will think twice before falling to greed again!'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed in a Fellowship.</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The files you need to continue your adventures in Middle-earth should finish downloading shortly. Thank you for your patience!</rgb>'${PLAYER}! It's about time. There's an important task that you need to attend to, so pay attention!''Greetings, ${PLAYER}. The sights of Celondim are a wonder to behold, are they not?

'I must intrude upon your reflection, though, with an important matter.''The tomb's entrance lies in a deep crag east of here. I don't know what to expect once we get inside, so stay on your guard and be ready for anything.

'Are you ready to travel to the tomb?'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest is the final quest in the Introduction. If you have any other quests underway you should complete them now, as those quests will no longer be available after the Introduction is completed.</rgb>Dwalin, a loyal friend of the late Thorin Oakenshield, has come to assert Thorin's reign once again, but many of the dwarves in his party have fallen ill.The dwarves of Dwalin's party came over the fields to the west of Frerin's Court when they arrived.

You should begin your search by following the road west to see if there is any evidence for the source of the plague that afflicts the dwarves.Examine patches of strange soil along the river (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect samples from sick bears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dwalin awaits word in Frerin's Court, east of the river where you examined the soil.

You should speak with Dwalin in Frerin's Court and let him know that the river itself seems poisoned by some sickly rot.'Look, look! All of these dwarves are sick -- dying, I think! I cannot do another thing until I figure out what we can do to help them.

'I don't even know what happened to make them ill. How can I hope to cure them if I don't know how they came by this plague?

'Those foul Dourhands have really let this place crumble. Thorin would be livid if he could see it now! Full of poison and death.''Please hurry, ${PLAYER}! Search wherever you can. These lads may not last another day....''The soil along the river is foul, you say? So you think that the water that flows from the clean mountain springs is tainted by a putrid rot?

'And these bears -- look! The meat is rotted, even though they are fresh-killed. This must be what is taking hold of the dwarves in my party....

'Many of my dwarves stopped at the river to fill their flasks. No wonder they are sick! What can we do?'Putrid water flows from the Blue Mountains' spring from above Thorin's Hall, poisoning all creatures unfortunate enough to drink from it.The mountain-path is north-west of Frerin's Court in Ered Luin.

You should climb the mountain path and find the source of the befouled waters and fend off any guards of the corruption along the way.Defeat guards of the mountain path (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Explore the mountainside for the source of the poisonElrohir of Rivendell, the other son of Elrond, stands outside the entrance to a cave on the mountain path.

You should speak with Elrohir of your errand for Dwalin and Elladan.Talk to Elrohir, the brother of Elladan'Mountain springs are always the purest of water, especially in these parts. Something must be causing the water to run foul.

'Will you explore the source of the river? Perhaps there will be evidence as to what caused the vile plague, because now we don't even know what it is that's making my poor dwarves sick.

'If we can make the river run clean again, I have hope for the animals and the snows here as well. Maybe Thorin's Hall won't be lost to sickness.''The dwarves with Dwalin drank from the river-water below, you say? That is ill tidings! The creatures here are transformed by plague and look as if they will die very soon.

'I came this way to scout for signs of my father's dream, but the grim dwarves here have kept me from getting much farther. Something evil stirs in that cave...can you feel it?''Explore the source of the mountain's spring, ${PLAYER}. You should walk up the mountain-path north-west of here and see what has tainted the water's source.'The Blackwold-plans you collected reveal that the brigands, guided by the evil forces of Angmar, mean to attack under the cover of shadow by the Old East Path, which is overrun by spiders.Atli Spider-bane stands outside the Hunter's Lodge.

You should speak with Atli Spider-bane and learn what you can about the Old East Path.Talk to Atli Spider-bane about the Old East PathThe Old East Path cuts into the large hill west of the Hunting Lodge.

You should explore the Old East Path to see how it can be used to get an advantage over the Blackwolds when they attack.Defeat spiders on the Old East Path (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})See if the wall is still intactJon Brackenbrook is at the Hunter's Lodge in the north-east corner of Archet.

You should tell Jon Brackenbrook of the dead end and the slaughtered Blackwold scout at the end of the Old East Path.Return to Jon Brackenbrook with the hopeful news'What an excellent find, ${PLAYER}. These folk from Angmar sound like evil foes, but at least we know what we are up against....

'The plans also show a map that points to the Old East Path, which is just near here. We all avoid that path save for Atli Spider-bane, a visitor from east of the Misty Mountains.

'Speak with Atli and learn what he can tell you about the path. We can use the path to our advantage if we manage to successfully scout it.''Aye, I know all about the Old East Path. There are spiders everywhere! When you kill one, another takes its place.

'If we are to make use of the path at all, we should fight our way through and ensure that it is still blocked at the walls of Archet.

'The spiders will do some work for us against the Blackwolds. And what the spiders don't deal with, we shall come from afore and behind with our axes and our blades, and we will fall upon them like a mighty cave coming down!''That is good news! A dead end at the end of the path will work in our favour! The brigands will be slowed, and they will have the spiders at their heels, and the hunters will come from behind while the soldiers attack at the head!

'I will go to Archet to rally them and ready them for the storm that awaits them tonight.''Keep your wits about you, ${CLASS}. Spiders are deadly foes.''I think Atli's knowledge of the layout of the Old East Path will help us form a plan.'Gormr's words and hints have brought you nothing but uneasiness, and there is a tension in the air. It is time to seek Dwalin and see if the Elves and Longbeards may be united in their purposes.Dwalin is in Frerin's Court, in the very centre of the Thorin's Gate area.

Now would be a good time to consult Dwalin on Gormr's strange behaviour and sinister hints.Talk to Dwalin and tell him of Gormr's plans for the ritual'Would you like to be here to witness the Ritual of Commemoration of our fallen king? As Steward of these halls, I welcome you to celebrate with us. It will not be long now...in fact, I believe the preparations begin tonight.

'What say you, ${PLAYER}? Think on it, if you will. Return to me when you have decided. Just be sure you make the right decision! Ha ho ho.

'Run along now, friend. I've no more time for you. It will be a busy day for all my folk.''Does this mean you will be joining the Dourhands in the ritual tonight? No? Don't think too long, ${RACE}. My patience wears ever thinner as I grow older.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! Thank goodness you're back! Nos Grimsong sent me word that you were finding out what you could from the Elves that settled up near the ruins.

'You spoke to Gormr as well? The traitor -- Skorgrím is not the king of Thorin's Hall! This place belongs to Thorin's line! I have too much on my plate for the nonsense of the Dourhands and their strange rituals.

'Look, ${PLAYER}! Since you went away, the dwarves of our party fell ill!'The barrow-dwelling dogs called "barghests" have taken over the lands in Thorin's Gate, implying the presence of much death nearby....Barghests can be found in the sooty snow-fields around Frerin's Court.

You should defeat barghests, for they are a sign of an unnatural death in this valley that was once hale and fair.Defeat barghests in the snow-fields around Frerin's Court (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Unnarr is in Frerin's Court, standing among the other members of Dwalin's party.

You should speak with Unnarr and tell him of your success in driving off the evil barrow-hounds in Thorin's Gate.Talk to Unnarr in Frerin's Court'Have you seen the barrow-hounds nearby, ${PLAYER}? The others think they are just bleak, wild dogs, but I know better. These are no mere dogs -- they are barghests!

'In my travels some years ago, I once happened upon the most forsaken place I have ever seen. Dread filled me, and my voice died, and all was cold. The dogs there were the very same as these black, mournful beasts, with their eyes full of death.

'Why have they come to replace the lynx and wild aurochs-herds that roamed here in Thorin's day? It does not make any sense. They must be driven off!''Those dogs are a bad sign for any land. To see them in the fields around Frerin's Court fills my heart with dread.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}! Those dogs chill my heart. You did a good deed for these lands by driving them back. Perhaps some day the lynx and aurochs will be able to return to these parts. Some day.

'I wonder why the wretched dogs settled here to begin with....'The Elves told Dwalin that Elrohir, son of Elrond, entered the Mirkstone Tunnels near Thorin's Hall to discover more about the plans of the Dourhands.Elrohir may be found somewhere in the Mirkstone Tunnels. The entrance to the Tunnels lies at the bottom of the Axe-head Path, north-west of Frerin's Court.

Elrohir, son of Elrond, entered the Mirkstone Tunnels to search for answers to the mystery of why the Dourhands have allied themselves with goblins. Dwalin asked you to meet with Elrohir to see what he may have learned.Dwalin can be found in Frerin's Court, south-east of the Mirkstone Tunnels.

Elrohir gave you a letter to take to Dwalin.'I consulted with the Elves while you were away and learned that Elrohir, one of the sons of Elrond, is exploring the Mirkstone Tunnels to the north-west of here.

'He intends to learn more about the Dourhand's plans, and I want you to be there when he does! The entrance to the Mirkstone Tunnels can be found at the bottom of the Axe-head Path, north-west of here.

'The Dourhands have much to answer for!''Elrohir should be in the Mirkstone Tunnels, if the Elves words are true, and I've no reason to think they aren't!

'The entrance to the tunnels lies at the bottom of the Axe-head path, north-west of here.''Welcome, Master Dwarf. I presume you come at the behest of Dwalin? I have found some intriguing information here in the cave. At a camp-site near here, I found a letter.

'It was penned by a man called Marrec, and I sense something foul is afoot. He speaks of a dark master and a plan to return the dead leader of the Dourhands to life. For this, the Dourhands would pledge their loyalty to Angmar!

'It is imperative that Marrec and his master be stopped. The letter speaks of a tomb... I believe I know where it may be found, so I am going to go there, but I would like you to return the letter to Dwalin. Tell him that the Elves and dwarves must unite to drive the Dourhands from Ered Luin!''Return this letter to Dwalin. We must put an end to the Dourhand's plans!''This is madness! Restoring a dwarf to life? The lore of my people has always told that certain dwarves are returned to us, but deliberately restoring one to life? It is not possible! There is no power in Middle-earth that can do so.

'I think that there is something far more sinister at work here. I have heard that necromancers once sent fell spirits into the Dead to stir them....

'We must stop the Dourhands and their new allies before it's too late. I will tell my dwarves to band together with the Elves, but I cannot just stand here as Elrohir goes into that tomb alone. We must follow... I fear for him.'Jon Brackenbrook has sent you into the Blackwold's Roost, the heart of the shadow over Archet, in hopes that you can uncover their plan of attack.The Blackwold's Roost can be found south of the Hunting Lodge.

You should defeat brigands to thin their ranks and gather information about their exact plans for the raid on Archet.Defeat brigands to thin their ranks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather information about the intended Blackwold raidJon Brackenbrook is mustering his strength in the Hunter's Lodge, in the north-east corner of Archet.

You should return to Jon Brackenbrook with the Blackwold-plans you have collected.'Calder Cob has shown his true colours at last! I knew him to be evil-hearted, but my father is too trusting. He does not like to think ill of people. His blindness wounded me, but he is a good man.

'So, to answer your question: yes, I will come to Archet's aid, I and my fellows. I am a hunter and a skilled warrior, trained by my father and Captain, and I would rather die than sit idly by while foul brigands crash upon a decent peoples.

'Let us see what there is to see before the storm is upon us. While I gather my warriors and my weapons, you should sneak into the Blackwold's Roost and uncover their plan of attack for tonight.'The Blackwold's Roost is south of here, across the lake. You should be able to find plans if you venture around. Just be prepared to fight as you go!''Good work, ${PLAYER}, and fast too! This will be a great boon to Archet! Now we will be able to counter their efforts with the proper strategy.'Elrohir has asked you to seek a herb within the caves of the Mirkstone Tunnels, as he believes the mountain will try in its own way to purge itself of the encroaching poisons.It is possible that healing herbs may be found inside the cave behind Elrohir.

You should search the cave for herbs that grow to help to purge the poisons from the Mirkstone Tunnels.Collect healing herbs from the Mirkstone Tunnels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There is surely a reason for the Dead to have encroached upon these parts, and this cave seems to be the source.

You should search the cave for the heart of the problems at Thorin's Gate.Examine the cave for what might be causing the blight of Ered LuinElrohir is outside the Mirkstone Tunnels, guarding the entrance from the bloodthirsty Dourhands.

You should bring the herbs to Elrohir and tell him what you witnessed inside the caves.'I believe there may be hope for the sick dwarves, ${PLAYER}. When poisons seep into the land, oftentimes the land will strive to heal itself, much as our own bodies will fight infection. If you explore inside the mountain, you might find just such an event.

'I believe that medicinal plants will grow inside, and those will help to cure the dwarves. But the source of the poison itself is yet to be discovered... though I have my suspicions.

'I feel a powerful chill when I stand near this entrance to the mountain. I will stand guard here while you explore the cave.''I'll stand guard here, ${PLAYER}. Go into the caves behind me and look for any wholesome-looking plants that grow.''Ah, you have collected pure herbs! You will be a hero to those dwarves, ${PLAYER}. Tell me of what you saw in the cave while I mix a salve to help the sick.'You have had a long day, and a hunter in the Hunter's Lodge thinks you should get some rest.A hunter has offered you a bedroll in the Hunter's Lodge you can use to rest.Use the bedroll in the Hunter's Lodge to get some restYou had a most curious dream, and should share it with the hunter in the Hunter's Lodge.Tell the hunter about your curious dream'You have had a long day, friend, and more dangers await! You should take some rest. There is a bedroll just over there you can use. I will wake you if anything happens.'The bedroll is more comfortable than you expected, or perhaps you are more tired than you realized. You close your eyes, and before long you are lost in dreams....'That sounds a most curious dream! I never have dreams like that, friend. I would not wish to have such!'You have had a long day, and a miner thinks you should get some rest.A miner has offered you a bedroll you can use to rest.Use the bedroll to get some restYou had a most curious dream, and should share it with the miner who recommended you rest.Tell the miner about your curious dream'You have had a long day, and more dangers await! You should take some rest. There is a bedroll just over there you can use. I will wake you if anything happens.'The bedroll is more comfortable than you expected, or perhaps you are more tired than you realized. You close your eyes, and before long you are lost in dreams....'That sounds a most curious dream! I never have dreams like that. I would not wish to have such!'Your efforts to ready Archet for the impending Blackwold attack have come to fruition. Now the preparations are complete, and the time has come to fight.Jon Brackenbrook is at the Hunting Lodge, east of Archet.

Jon Brackenbrook is waiting for you to join his company.Talk to Jon BrackenbrookJon Brackenbrook is at the Hunting Lodge, east of Archet.

Jon Brackenbrook is waiting for you to join his company.Talk to Jon BrackenbrookJon Brackenbrook wishes to speak with you.

After the assault on Archet, Jon Brackenbrook returned to the town to assist and rebuild, taking up his father's legacy.'/'Mundo Sackville-Baggins wishes to speak with you.

After the assault on Archet, you helped Mundo Sackville-Baggins and Celandine Brandybuck on their return trip to the Shire.'Talk to Jon BrackenbrookTalk to Mundo Sackville-Baggins'Quickly! Calder Cob is making his move against Archet, and wicked men of Angmar are lending him and the Blackwolds strength. We must go to the town's defence at once! Return to me when you are prepared.''The loss of my father is a painful one, but my pain is no greater than any other here in Archet. The people of Archet regard you as a hero, and I agree with them, ${PLAYER}. Without your quick thinking we would have lost more lives.

'You were the one who faced down the evil Men and drove them and many of the Blackwolds from the woods surrounding our town. We owe you much.

'It is good to know that the grim dark growing across the land will have such fierce adversaries as yourself.'<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The files you need to continue your adventures in Middle-earth should finish downloading shortly. Thank you for your patience!</rgb>'You'll never see me outside the bounds of the Shire again. Some Bagginses may enjoy an uncomfortable adventure, but not I. 

'To think that I had to rely on Big Folk to pull me from the grips of others.

'You didn't help much with the way you marched us back to the Shire either, ${PLAYER}.''Are you ready to go? Very well....'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest is the final quest in the Introduction. If you have any other quests underway you should complete them now, as those quests will no longer be available after the Introduction is completed.</rgb>Before Dwalin and the Longbeards can hope to join the Elves in stopping Gormr from allowing the fell spirits to corrupt Ered Luin for good, the poisoned dwarves must be cured of their terrible sickness.Dwalin stands by his sick dwarves in Frerin's Court, below the Mirkstone Tunnels.

You should bring Elrohir's remedy to Dwalin and tell him of the dire warnings of the fell spirit you encountered in the cave.Talk to Dwalin in Frerin's CourtThe sick dwarves are in Frerin's Court, huddled on the ground and dying from the poisonous spring from which they drank.

You should administer Elrohir's draught to the sick dwarves.Administer Elrohir's draught to BogiThe sick dwarves are in Frerin's Court, huddled on the ground and dying from the poisonous spring from which they drank.

You should administer Elrohir's draughte to the sick dwarves.Administer Elrohir's draught to SelurThe sick dwarves are in Frerin's Court, huddled on the ground and dying from the poisonous spring from which they drank.

You should administer Elrohir's draught to the sick dwarves.Administer Elrohir's draught to OlinThe sick dwarves are in Frerin's Court, huddled on the ground and dying from the poisonous spring from which they drank.

You should administer Elrohir's draught to the sick dwarves.Administer Elrohir's draught to Mathi StouthandDwalin is in Frerin's Court at Thorin's Gate.

You should speak with Dwalin about how to proceed now that his dwarves have received a remedy.Tell Dwalin that there is now hope for the dwarves of his party'These leaves can be crushed to make a powerful remedy. Do you smell the clear sap? It is the blood of the mountain, striving to cleanse itself of corruption.

'Take this phial, ${PLAYER}... I have drained enough sap to save those dwarves. If we can rally them in time, our two parties should be able to rid Ered Luin of the horrible fate that awaits it.

'I will not stand idly by while these fair, clean lands are poisoned with death! Go well, my friend. Hopefully, I will see you again when we meet to put a stop to this madness.''Go quickly to Dwalin, friend ${CLASS}! There is not much time. The only hope for saving this land is to stop Gormr from going through with his plans for tonight's ritual.''Can this be? By what miracle do you return with a draught to cure my poor dwarves? You are a valuable friend to have, ${PLAYER}!

'Please, don't let me get in your way. Go ahead and give that remedy to the sick dwarves.''Bring the remedy to my folk.''Bring the remedy to my folk.''Bring the remedy to my folk.''Bring the remedy to my folk.''Now that there is hope for the sick among my company, we can deal with the more pressing matter at hand. What is this nonsense about Gormr wishing to raise Skorgrím from the dead?

'Dead is dead, in my opinion. You can't bring someone back! It sounds like Gormr has gotten some bad ideas in his head, and Ered Luin has become corrupted in his hands. We'll take it back, ${PLAYER}!'Choose a vocation with the Mistress of Apprentices in order to unlock Introductory crafting quests. Complete three introductory crafting quests.'I can teach you about the trades, yes. Speak with me, and I'll help you get started on your crafting journey.''Ask me about any of the six widely recognized vocations. Then, tell me which vocation you'd like to pursue, and I will direct you to individual profession trainers who will help you craft your first items. Complete the work they set before you, and I'll consider your initiation into the trades complete.'You have found a mysterious coin inlaid with ithildín. This rare metal was made by the Elves from mithril long ago. The image of the Doors of Durin, the doors that guarded the West Gate of Moria, is found on one side of the coin, while the other has the image of a hammer and anvil, the signs of Durin.Bring your ithildín coin to one of the following people to receive a reward.

• Jon Brackenbrook in Archet
• Dwalin in Thorin's Hall
• Mayor Will Whitfoot in Michel Delving
• Barliman Butterbur in Bree-town
• Cardavor in CelondimYou are not sure where this coin came from, but it seems to be a relic from Khazad-dûm, called Moria by the Elves. There are many who would be interested in such a relic and would likely provide you with a great reward!

<rgb=#FF0000>Bring this coin to any of the following people to receive your reward:
• Jon Brackenbrook in Archet
• Dwalin in Thorin's Hall
• Mayor Will Whitfoot in Michel Delving
• Barliman Butterbur in Bree-town
• Cardavor in Celondim</rgb>'What do you have here? A coin of some sort? Doesn't look like much... and what's this, some sort of doors on the back? What a queer coin you've brought me!

'I suppose it is worth something, although surely not much. Perhaps Keeper Foxtail would like to put it on display in the Mathom House.

'Yes, that should be fine. Here, choose something that you feel is appropriate for a coin such as this.''A dwarf-coin of some sort, is it not? I have heard of such things, but I never thought to see one. Where did you come across it?

'I would gladly give you something in trade for this coin. Choose what you would like, and we shall finish our trade.''A dwarf-coin of some sort, is it not? I have heard of such things, but I never thought to see one. Where did you come across it?

'I would gladly give you something in trade for this coin. Choose what you would like, and we shall finish our trade.''I cannot believe it! It is an ithildín coin! It is said that many were minted to commemorate the friendship of the Elves of Hollin and the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm. Most were lost... where did you come across such a treasure?

'Please, friend, trade this coin with me. I have many things to offer in trade. Choose something you think appropriate!''I cannot believe it! It is an ithildín coin! It is said that many were minted to commemorate the friendship of the Elves of Hollin and the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm. Most were lost... where did you come across such a treasure?

'Please, friend, trade this coin with me. I have many things to offer in trade. Choose something you think appropriate!''Barliman Butterbur at your service, friend! That's quite a strange coin you've got there! Looks like a dwarf-coin of some sort... I've seen a few from guests, mind you, but not one like this. Not sure even what it's made of!

'Well, not sure I would take it for a meal or a room, but it probably has some value to someone... if only as something interesting to talk over!

'I will offer you a trade. I've a number of things travellers have left behind. You can trade this coin for one of those. How's that sound?''Hail, friend. I see you have found an ithildín coin. These coins were minted by the Dwarves of Moria in the days of their friendship with the Elves of Eregion. See here, engraved here are the Doors of Durin, which were inlaid with this same metal.

'Most of these coins were lost when Moria fell into darkness. If you would have it, I would like to keep this coin. It can serve as a good reminder in these dark times of the fellowship that can exist between dwarves and Elves.

'However, I would not ask you to go away empty-handed. Choose something you find acceptable, and we shall make our exchange.''I cannot believe it! It is an ithildín coin! It is said that many were minted to commemorate the friendship of the Elves of Hollin and the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm. Most were lost... where did you come across such a treasure?

'Please, friend, trade this coin with me. I have many things to offer in trade. Choose something you think appropriate!'You have found a mysterious coin inlaid with ithildín. This rare metal was made by the Elves from mithril long ago. The image of the Doors of Durin, the doors that guarded the West Gate of Moria, is found on one side of the coin, while the other has the image of a hammer and anvil, the signs of Durin.Bring your ithildín coin to one of the following people to receive a reward.

• Jon Brackenbrook in Archet
• Dwalin in Thorin's Hall
• Mayor Will Whitfoot in Michel Delving
• Barliman Butterbur in Bree-town
• Cardavor in CelondimYou are not sure where this coin came from, but it seems to be a relic from Khazad-dûm, called Moria by the Elves. There are many who would be interested in such a relic and would likely provide you with a great reward!

