'Please, friend, trade this coin with me. I have many things to offer in trade. Choose something you think appropriate!'Rhedyn asks you to bring a little repast to each watch-tower along the wall.Deliver food to the watch-towers along Mossward's defensive wall.Deliver food and drink to DerisDeliver food and drink to ErylDeliver food and drink to Lhian and CleddDeliver food and drink to GwionYou should tell Rhedyn that you have completed your deliveries.

Talk to Rhedyn.Talk to Rhedyn'Excuse me! Could I bother you to help me make some deliveries?

'More of us are volunteering for shifts up on the watch-towers. The new folks forget to pack a lunch. Would you mind bringing these sandwiches and canteens to whoever's on watch?''Ooooh lunch? That's wonderful! Uuff my tummy was beginning to growl like an angry cat. I volunteered to take the noon to sundown shift thinking "Oh well I'll just have a big lunch and look forward to a large supper. I won't need a snack." But let me tell you, standin' around for hours with nothing to look at but the grass has a strange way of building up an appetite.

'Oh but don't let me keep you with my blabbering. Off you go now, and tell the baker she's lovely and thoughtful. Thanks to both of you!''Mutton? Oooh I love mutton! Mutton mutton hmm hmm like a button...

'Oh! You're still here! You uh, didn't hear me... singing a song about mutton did you? I'm not used to uh, standing around here doing nothing all day. I sing about little things I see to keep myself occupied.

'...

'Please don't tell anyone.''Hmm? A lunch delivery? Ah for the new folk who forget to bring food and drink. Well, an experienced watcher like myself remembered to bring her own.'

Lhian gives you a wink and pats a satchel at her hip.

'Unless... is that chicken, mushroom, and onion? With rosemary?'

Lhian opens her satchel.

'Give it here, friend.'Gwion takes a long swig from the canteen before speaking.

'I packed salted pork for food. I forgot to bring anything to drink, and it wouldn't do for me to leave my post to fetch something. Thanks for the water, friend, and pass my thanks to the baker too.''Thanks for helping out. These are hard times for Mossward, but if we support each other we'll get through it, right?'Now that you have dealt with the local wildlife, Nos Grimsong has asked you to help with restocking supplies for Frerin's Court.The minerals can be found in the Silver Deep, east of the frozen lake to the east of Frerin's Court.

Nos Grimsong has asked you to gather minerals for him.Gather minerals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nos Grimsong is in Frerin's Court, west of the Silver Deep.

You should return to Nos Grimsong for your reward.'Well done, ${PLAYER}. Now that you have dealt with the local wildlife, I don't suppose you could help us restock our supplies?

'Follow the road east out of Frerin's Court around the lake to the east and to the Silver Deep. Inside are several veins of minerals that we need to craft our weapons. Head inside, gather the minerals, and bring the ore back to me.

'Be careful, but be quick!''Follow the road east out of Frerin's Court around the lake to the east and to the Silver Deep. Inside are several veins of minerals that we need to craft our weapons. Head inside, gather the minerals, and bring the ore back to me.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. This ore should last us for a short time, at least.

'Take this reward, along with my thanks, for all your efforts.'Lalfor has lost some of his most precious writings and belongings while watching Nedhrien dance.

<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>Lalfor has given you a list of his missing things to remind you exactly what they are.

Lalfor would like you to find his missing things while he remains close to the Festival of Enedhin for...research purposes.Lalfor is waiting for you at the festival in Duillond.

Lalfor will be pleased to have all his missing items returned to him.'Excuse me, good ${RACE}, perhaps you could help me. I came here today to see Nedhrien. Today is the day that I will profess my feelings for her. But in all of my excitement -- and dare I say nervousness -- I seem to have dropped all of my poems and gifts for her.

'Could you find them for me? And please hurry, while I still have the nerve to do as my heart tells me I must. Here is a list of all the things I need.''I am simply at a loss; I cannot find my missing things anywhere.''Ah, thank you! You have kept a young Elf's heart whole today and that is no small thing. The world itself would have shattered if I had missed this opportunity.

'For your efforts, here is a festival coin.

'Thank you! I must now speak with her!'The Midgewater Marshes are home to the Neekerbreekers, a variety of annoying insect that has recently become hostile, following the passage of Black Riders from the East. You are called to halt the plague of Neekerbreekers.Defeat Neekerbreekers in Bree-landThe Midgewater Marshes are home to the Neekerbreekers, a variety of annoying insect that has recently become hostile, following the passage of Black Riders from the East. You are called to halt the plague of Neekerbreekers.Defeat Neekerbreekers in Bree-landYou received a mail asking you to help the stable workers in Combe handle a new and unusual horse that just arrived.Combe is located south of Archet and east of Bree-town in Bree.Seek out the Stable-help in Combe'The stables in Combe have been unusually busy lately with many travellers coming in and out of the city. I haven't seen this many visitors in a long time, and it's keeping us busy at the stables in trying to keep our horses in good health. Not only visitors are coming by these days either, for just this morning a new horse arrived that looks nothing like any horse I've ever seen!

'Can you come to the stables in Combe and help us tend to this new horse? Combe is located just south of Archet and east of Bree-town in Bree.''Thank goodness you've arrived, and just in time!'An exasperated daughter seeks help finding her father who has been known to down two too many cups of wine.Sioned has asked you to look for her father, a hobbit affectionately known as Ol' Tipsy Gil.

Gil can be found around Glyn Helyg.Search for Ol' GilYou found an empty wine bottle, so Tipsy Gil may be close by!

Keep searching for him in Glyn Helyg.Continue searching for GilYou managed to find Gil, but he's too drunk to make it home for dinner. He has asked you to bring him some water to help him sober up.

You should fill the wine bottle you found with water from the nearby fountain.With a full bottle of fresh water in hand, you are ready to help sober up Ol' Tipsy Gil.

Gil is in Glyn Helyg.You should let Sioned know that her father is on the way to recovery and will be around for dinner soon.

Sioned is in Glyn Helyg.Talk to Sioned'Excuse me, have you seen my father? You wouldn't have missed him. Most likely falling over himself drunk? No? Well, if you would be so kind as to keep an eye out for him, I would be quite grateful.''Wah? Whosh there? Twins? Wait, now theresh jush one of you. Oh my daughter shent you? Well, you tell her...'

He pauses, thinking very hard.

'What wash I shaying? Oh, right, Sshioned shent you. Ish it time for shupper already? Well, I can't sheem to walk. Maybe a ship of water will help. Go fesh me a ship of water, will you?''Mmm, wha? You shwoke me from a great dream. Did you bring me a ship of ale? Water?!! Oh fine, give it here.'

He takes a long draw of water from the bottle and then several deep breaths. After a few long moments, his eyes clear and he blinks up at you.

'Very well, very well. I am getting very weller indeed. I just need a bit more time. Go on and tell Sioned that I will be along shortly. I just need a few more minutes and a few more sips. Of water, that is. I wouldn't be missing her cooking for the world.''Soberin' up is 'e? The taters will have gone cold, but at least he's on his way. Thank you for your help!'Cal Sprigley is concerned about a particularly dangerous and aggressive boar living near a watering hole just east of his farm.Old Bloodtusk's den, which is built in a rotten, old tree stump, lies east of Sprigley's Farm.

Cal Sprigley has asked you to dispose of Old Bloodtusk before the boar can bring harm to anyone else.Cal Sprigley awaits your return.

At Cal Sprigley's request, you hunted and slew the great boar Old Bloodtusk. You should return to the farmer with news of your success.Talk to Cal Sprigley at his farmTalk to Cal Sprigley at his farm<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest has been restored for Legendary Servers!</rgb>

'While we seem to have made it through the worst with the Blackwolds, there is still one threat that my farmhands and I can't seem to silence. 

'There is a great, vicious boar that lives somewhere to the east of my farm. His den is built in an old, rotting tree stump. Folks call him Old Bloodtusk, but I call him a nuisance! Always rooting for food near my hedge. He once broke through the hedge and gored a farmhand in my field.

'With all that is going on, it may seem a bit foolish, but that boar isn't right and is better dead than alive.'<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest has been restored for Legendary Servers!</rgb>

'While we seem to have made it through the worst with the Blackwolds, there is still one threat that my farmhands and I can't seem to silence. 

'There is a great, vicious boar that lives somewhere to the east of my farm. His den is built in an old, rotting tree stump. Folks call him Old Bloodtusk, but I call him a nuisance! Always rooting for food near my hedge. He once broke through the hedge and gored a farmhand in my field.

'With all that is going on, it may seem a bit foolish, but that boar isn't right and is better dead than alive.''Old Bloodtusk's den is south-east of Bronwe's Folly and east of my farm. If you kill the boar, I'll be sure to treat you right for your service.''Old Bloodtusk's den is south-east of Bronwe's Folly and east of my farm. If you kill the boar, I'll be sure to treat you right for your service.''When all this finally is over, I will have one less worry on my farm thanks to you, ${PLAYER}.

'That boar was a menace to a great lot of the farmers in the area. Without him, we might get our farmlands flourishing again!''When all this finally is over, I will have one less worry on my farm thanks to you, ${PLAYER}.

'That boar was a menace to a great lot of the farmers in the area. Without him, we might get our farmlands flourishing again!'Estmar Bolger has accidentally lost the notes pertaining to his family business.Misty Bolger is north and east of Michel Delving in the town of Bywater.

Estmar Bolger has asked that you visit his sister, Misty Bolger, and find out how many fish she caught last week.Talk to Misty Bolger'Hullo there, ${PLAYER}. How do you do this fine day? I'm in an awful spot of trouble; perhaps you can assist me?

'It is my sister, Misty Bolger, you see. She is the muscle of the family, while I am the brains. It is she who goes out each day and fishes our daily catch, and I keep track of the sales and teach young fishermen the trade.

'It seems that last night my notes were used as a napkin for a simply delectable fish medley.  Those notes had the totals and sales of our fish for the last week! Could you please go and see my sister in Bywater and ask her if she recalls the number of fish that she caught last week?''Used the notes as a napkin -- what will he do next? I am out here fishing every day for our keep, and he can't even keep track of his own notes!

'It is a good thing that I always keep records of my own. This isn't the first time Estmar has accidentally had his notes go missing.

'I will send another copy to him right away! Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''Have you visited my sister yet? She is east and north of Michel Delving in the town of Bywater.'The Masters and Mistresses of Apprentices, representing the many Craft Guilds of Middle-earth, have invited you to speak with them about the many professions that they teach.You received a letter from the Crafting Guilds of Middle-earth inviting you to visit one of their apprentice trainers. You should seek out Jill Brushwood at the Craft Hall in Combe/Blossom Proudfoot at the Crafting Area in Michel Delving/Golphedinir at the Crafter's Terrace in Celondim/Loftur in the Crafting Hall at Thorin's Gate or Morór at the Maker's Hall in Thorin's Hall.,

The Crafting Guilds of Middle-earth thank you for all that you have done for the Free Peoples and would like to extend an invitation to speak with our representative, Jill Brushwood, at the Craft Hall in the village of Combe/Blossom Proudfoot at the Crafting Area in Michel Delving/Loftur in the Crafting Hall at Thorin's Gate or Morór at the Maker's Hall in Thorin's Hall/Golphedinir at the Crafter's Terrace in Celondim.

We acknowledge your ability as a combatant and invite you to try your hand at a less violent form of work, craftsmanship. You will find that Jill Brushwood is an able teacher/Blossom Proudfoot is an able teacher/Loftur and Morór are able teachers/Golphedinir is an able teacher who can introduce you to pursuits ranging from cooking to scholarly to smithy and everything in between.

Sincerely,

The Crafting Guilds of Middle-earth'It seems that you are a little ways from home, ${RACE}. No matter.

'I am here to provide you with information and assistance in becoming a crafter, a very important role for many of the folk in Middle-earth.''It seems that you are a little ways from home, ${RACE}. No matter.

