<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.</rgb>Return to the masterThe master is found overlooking the fields on his hill, just north of the eighth gate.  

<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.</rgb>Complete'These are my fields, and if you wish to stay here for a while, you must pass my test. Any horse that can pull his weight can make it around the eastern track in less than five minutes. I need to make sure every horse in my herd can pull his weight. There will be no weak links in my chain.'He looks at you proudly. You seem to have proven to him that you are not a weak link after all.'Stuff...'A horse in Ost Guruth is seeking an audience with you.Find the horse in Ost GuruthJourney into the Trollshaws and find a horse in Thorenhad.Journey into the Trollshaws and find a horse in Thorenhad.Roheryn is found at the stables in Rivendell.Talk to Roheryn at the Rivendell stablesThe sounds and smell of war would scare away most horses, but you are drawn to it like a moth to a flame. You seek an audience with a horse that is accustomed to conflict in hope that it may shed some light on your purpose....You are drawn to Esteldín by a notion of some conflict there, and you feel connected to that purpose somehow. You seek a horse that can inform you about the tactics and strategies of war as a steed.

<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.</rgb>Find a Ranger's horse in EsteldínTerrible horse-traps are being used by the enemy and can be found in the passes toward Dol Dínen.

<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.</rgb>Destroy horse-trapsDefeat Ongbúrz horse-trappers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Ranger's horse can be found back in Esteldín.

<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.</rgb>Talk to the Ranger's horse at Esteldín'What brought you to a place like this? This is not a place for any creature in his right mind, for I am on the edge of war, with the smoke of many fires filling the air.

'The Enemy has turned his attention to steeds of late; he uses traps to tear or break our legs. These wicked mechanisms must be destroyed, but be careful, for they will likely be guarded. Once a steed is snared, enemies try to ambush the rider before the horse can break free.

'You look like you can handle yourself better than most horses I have ever seen. Please help us destroy the horse-traps and their makers!''The Rangers here, and we steeds especially, thank you for destroying the traps that our enemies laid for us. You have had a taste of war, and it looks as though it did not break your spirit. You are made of strong stuff, friend...and I hope to see you again before long.'Your nostrils flare at a scent of evil on the air. You feel compelled to find the source, excited to face whatever it is you discover...You are drawn to a source of evil detected in the Trollshaws by your keen senses.

