<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to the horsefields.</rgb>Destroy a scrap of black armourDestroy a scrap of black clothThe trophies left behind by the fallen black steed and its rider have been destroyed.

With your rage satisfied, curiosity has crept in. What could have killed this steed, and where was its rider going?Examine the fallen black steed once moreA powerful force left a mysterious energy about the black steed's corpse, like a receeding wave would leave small pools of water to linger in the sand.

The black steed did not make it far after suffering an injury so great. The source of such a power must exist somewhere in the Trollshaws.Find the source of that which drove the black steed awayYou found the source of evil that drew you here. This was once a horse bred to serve the forces of Sauron. There are many horses in the service of the Enemy, but this creature was the steed of a Nazgûl, one of the Nine.

The scent of evil here fuels a fire you have never felt before, and you know this horse is an arch-enemy. Its death is bittersweet; you would prefer to have done battle with it yourself.

The enemy left fragments of armour and strips of cloak behind. Destroying the trophies of evil will satisfy your anger at the existence of such a creature. Search the area and destroy the trophies of this fallen enemy.Destroying the trophies left behind by the enemy quenched your rage, for now. A powerful force was involved in driving this creature away, and it was injured badly to meet its doom at this spot.

You could not sense it before because the stench of evil filled your nostrils. Upon returning to the corpse, you feel the other energy, somehow different.

It lingers as a receding wave would leave small pools of water upon the sand. What could have done this to such a powerful creature? You must find the source of this energy.The steeds of the Horsefields mentioned a mysterious horse with a wizard that has a particular affinity for animals, both residing in the Lone-lands.There is a horse in Ost Guruth that you feel compelled to seek out.

<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to the Horsefields.</rgb>Head to Ost Guruth and find a horse thereThe rare herb sought by Radagast's horse only grows in places of high elevation.  The only place high enough for miles around Ost Guruth is the summit of Weathertop.

<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to the Horsefields.</rgb>Find herbs on the summit of weathertopDefeat ambushing crebain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Radagast's horse is found in Ost Guruth.

<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to the horsefields.</rgb>Take the herbs back to Radagast's horse'Lately I have been desiring a rare herb that I haven't tasted in ages. I used to only find it in very high places, but not where it's too cold. I believe it might be found on the highest summit in these lands, at the top of Weathertop. Could you head there and kindly gather a few herbs for me if you happen to find them?

'My master and I used to travel quite often, and I grew a fondness for this herb. It has been ages since he has taken me very far beyond this ruin. Maybe some day soon we will roam Middle-earth again as we used to.''Thank you for appeasing my appetite of herbs that I have sorely missed! My master has been busy with the important events unfolding here, but he will be happy to be reminded of our travels together when he sees these herbs. These are exactly what I was looking for; I cannot thank you enough.

'You may or may not know this already, but there seems to be something special about you. My master and I have travelled to a lot of places in Middle-earth over the ages, and I have met many horses in my travels. Rarely have I encountered a steed of your spirit, or such an air of authority as yours....'There are many villainous monsters roaming the Shire, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many brigands in the ShireSlay many goblins in the ShireSlay many harvest-flies in the ShireSlay many slugs in the ShireSlay many spiders in the ShireSlay many wolves in the ShireDefeat slugs in the Shire.Defeat slugs in the ShireDefeat many slugs in the Shire.Defeat slugs in the ShireStrange, monstrous spiders have crept into Bree-land from the dark corners of Mirkwood, beyond the Misty Mountains in the east. Your courage will be tested against the spider infestation spreading through the forests and marshes of Bree-land.Defeat spiders in Bree-landDefeat spiders in the Shire.Defeat spiders in the ShireStrange, monstrous spiders have crept into Bree-land from the dark corners of Mirkwood, beyond the Misty Mountains in the east. Your courage will be tested against the spider infestation spreading through the forests and marshes of Bree-land.Defeat spiders in Bree-landDefeat many spiders in the Shire.Defeat spiders in the ShireHolly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Wydo Boffin of Little Delving had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Wydo Boffin has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Wydo Boffin's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'Don't get any ideas about snitching that pie of mine. It's from Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton. Do you know how hard it is to get one of her pies? Why I've been waiting for days! That pie shall be the highlight of my dinner party tonight!'

'What? What? Bad berries? Why I would not have believed it. Goodness, can you imagine my embarrassment had I served that? Take it away, take it back to Holly. Her home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

'And make sure she bakes me a new one quickly! I have guests coming over!''Gracious, I won't get another pie from Holly with you standing about here. Take it back to her in Hobbiton immediately!'When Ann Granger, a member of Captain Brackenbrook's garrison, was run off of her land by the Blackwolds, she lost a satchel containing things that were valuable to her.Blackwolds' Roost lies in the ruins south of the Hunter's Lodge.

Ann Granger has asked you to go to Blackwolds' Roost and recover her stolen satchel.'Good day, pleasure to meet you. You know, I heard a bit about your adventures, and it got me wondering if you might do me a favour.

'You see, I was chased off my farm by those Blackwolds a while back, and in my flight, I dropped my satchel, which contained some valuables. Well, as I looked back, I saw one of those brigands pick it up!

'I joined up with the guard when I made it to Archet, but now I'm stuck watching this lodge and can't get back what's mine! I'd be most grateful if you could go to Blackwolds' Roost to the south of here and get my satchel back!''You found my satchel! I didn't think I'd ever see this thing again. Thank you!'An inhabitant of Swanfleet has posted a task to collect small wings.You have accepted a task to acquire small wings.Wanted: Small wings from the invasive crebain troubling the folk of Swanfleet. Suitable reward offered upon delivery!Wanted: Small wings from the invasive crebain troubling the folk of Swanfleet. Suitable reward offered upon delivery!You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Henry Oakeshott has prepared a shipment of supplies for Joy Bloomer, a local fisherwoman, and needs someone to deliver a message to her.Joy Bloomer is in Staddle, east of Bree.

Henry Oakeshott has asked that you speak with his business partner, Joy Bloomer, and assure her that her shipment will arrive soon.Talk to Joy Bloomer'Hail, ${PLAYER}. Now that you have learned the subtleties of fishing, perhaps you could aid me in a small task?

'I have a business arrangement with a fisherwoman, Joy Bloomer, in Staddle. She often brings up choice cuts of fish, as well as a number of oddities that she finds while fishing in the rivers and lakes of Bree-land. I, for my part, send her business and keep her supplied with items that she cannot acquire in Staddle.

'Bring her news that her latest shipment has been sent. You will find Joy Bloomer east of here, in the town of Staddle. You will arrive on foot well before her shipment reaches her, and I would give her the peace of mind knowing she will soon have her supplies.''Ah, word of my supplies! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I have been expecting this delivery for some time now.

'And what of yourself? It seems that you have the look of a fisherman about you. Henry Oakeshott has always sent me the finest fishermen, and I, in turn, have supplied them with only the finest gear. If you are looking for fishing supplies, you need look no further than Joy Bloomer!''Have you brought Joy Bloomer word of her supplies? Please hurry along and tell her, she is east of Bree in the town of Staddle if you have forgotten.'Seren asks you to help soothe the animals.Nervous animals can be found in the pen near Mossward's eastern gate.

Seren has asked you to calm some of the nervous animals in Mossward.Calm the nervous goatCalm the anxious chickenCalm the perturbed cowTalk to Seren'These poor creatures are still recovering from the shock of what happened the other day. We all are, really. They could use a little attention, but alas I cannot pet all the animals at once, but such attention often helps to calm their nerves.

'Could you take a little time out of your day to reassure some of these critters?''Just give some of the animals some pets. If you're gentle and kind, they'll take to you.''Wasn't that lovely? They seem more at ease already. I find that taking care of the critters is just as soothing for the critters as it is for the caretaker. Wouldn't you agree?

'Next, I could use some help cleaning up their droppings.... Wait! Where are you going!?'Jon Brackenbrook is eager to help his father in the defence of Archet, but time is still needed to fully prepare the defences.Blackwolds' Roost lies among the ruins south of the Hunter's Lodge.

Jon Brackenbrook has asked you to provide a distraction by engaging the brigands at their encampment, Blackwolds' Roost.Defeat brigands at Blackwolds' Roost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Jon Brackenbrook can be found in the Hunter's Lodge, east of Archet, north of Blackwolds' Roost.

You engaged the Blackwolds as Jon Brackenbrook requested, but only time will tell if your efforts were enough. You should return to Jon with your report.<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest has been restored for Legendary Servers!</rgb>

'If Archet is to survive the Blackwolds' attack, they must have time to better prepare their defences. We must give them that time.

'The Blackwolds have established an encampment among the ruins to the south, which some call "Blackwolds' Roost." While you go there and distract the Blackwolds, my hunters and I will help my father prepare for their attack.

'Quickly now, we haven't any time to spare!''Hurry, travel to Blackwolds' Roost in the ruins south of the lodge. Defeat what brigands you find and return here.

'Hopefully your raid will provide us the time we need to better prepare for the assault that Éogan has planned.''Good, you've returned. We were too late. The Blackwolds are moving against Archet. We will need to defend the town now!'A child of Mossward has been dared by the town bully to make a dangerous run, and she wants to make sure it's possible before she makes the attempt.Alla has given you five minutes to reach the spot in question on the edge of the Wadewater, north of Mossward.Make it to the marked spot on the edge of the Wadewater without running out of time<rgb=#FF0000>Do not run out of time before reaching the correct location</rgb>Alla is by a haystack in north-eastern Mossward. You only have five minutes for the return journey!Return to Alla in north-eastern Mossward without running out of time<rgb=#FF0000>Do not run out of time before reaching the correct location</rgb>Alla is by a haystack in north-eastern Mossward.Talk to Alla in north-eastern Mossward'You look pretty tough to me. You're not scared of anything, are you?

'Maybe you can help me, then. The Mossward town bully has dared me to run to a certain spot north of town, right on the very edge of the Wadewater, and then come back... all in ten minutes! Now I'm not afraid, but I want to be certain it's possible. So what do you say to using no more than five minutes to run out there, and then five minutes to run back? That way I'll know it can be done before I make the attempt.

'Here, I'll mark it on your map. It's right here.''Time is a-wasting! If you cannot reach that spot on the edge of the Wadewater within five minutes, how am I supposed to do it?''Hurry up!''You made it! I have to admit that I was not sure you would be able to go out there and come back in time... but you did!

'So, did you see anything when you got out there?'

You tell her that there was a basket with a ball of string inside it beside the Wadewater, which seemed rather strange.

'I see, yes. That is peculiar. Thank you for your help.'Adan Rhuvyg has been up to secret shenanigans.Adan Rhuvyg has asked you to meet him atop the nearby cliffs.

The cliffs are north of the town of Lintrev.Talk to Adan by the cliffsAdan Rhuvyg has suggested you enjoy the view from the cliffs of Lintrev.You should talk to Adan about the view.

Adan is atop the cliffs of Lintrev.Tell Adan what you sawAdan has asked you to find materials with which to make a kite.

Kite materials can be found throughout Lintrev.Collect the kite fabricCollect a spool of ropeCollect a fallen branchYou should bring the kite materials to Adan.

Adan is around Lintrev.'Have you been to the edge of the nearby cliffs yet? If not, you have got to take in the view. If you like, I will meet you over there and show you the best look-out spot!''Oh hullo! I see you managed to gather all of the things I needed for the kite. Well, ahem, you took too long and I got hungry and… I suppose I will have to put off flying for today. Eirlys baked an incredible apple pie for me and it would be rude to let it go cold. I might try flying tomorrow, we'll see.

'Maybe from a nearby hill, instead of…'

He looks up to the cliffs and swallows.

'…up so high.''Ah, you made it! Come, come, look over yonder! Is it not marvellous! On clear days you can see all the way to Tharbad! Right, maybe not, but is it not still a wonder? Go on ahead and take a look!''Impressive, no? Anyhow - you may be wondering why I asked you for the bird wings and why there's a rock tied to my favourite handkerchief. You see…'

He pauses dramatically, lowering his voice to a whisper.

'I am going to be the first hobbit to fly like a bird! I have been experimenting and studying things that fly. Birds, handkerchiefs that aren't weighed down by rocks… those sorts of things. My experiments have not quite garnered the results I was hoping for, but I have a new plan that is sure to work!

'Here is where you come in. I need you to gather some materials for me. If I go about doing it myself, there will be no end of questions and interruptions! I need the straightest branch you can find, rope, and the purple canvas that's hanging on one of the houses at the base of the southern cliffs.

'We are going to build a larger kite than anyone has ever seen before, and then I am going to leap from this edge like an eagle, and soar over Stoor-vales! You just wait and see!'Explore the history of the Dúnedain Rangers of the North.Discover clues about the history of the Dúnedain scattered throughout the Arnorian ruins in Bree-land.The worn but noble visage engraved on the statue you discovered belongs to Aranarth, the first Chieftain of the Dúnedain after the fall of Arthedain.

The statue was probably created some time after the wars that destroyed the old Kingdom, most likely by the Rangers who hold Aranarth in great reverence.

It was in good repair suggesting that they tend to it to this day. The memories of the Dúnedain are long, and their respect for the dead borders on obsession at times.The runes you found seemed to be very old indeed, and in style of ancient Arnorian script that few would readily recognize in these times. While you made out only a little of it, the inscription is likely an oath of fealty taken by Dúnedain to their lords.

The Men of those days put great store in ceremony and oaths, and believed that to break one would bring a terrible curse upon the oathbreaker.

Few Men put much store in ritual and ceremony these days -- save for the Rangers of the North, who are rumoured to have descended from those very Dúnedain who once ruled Arnor. Perhaps they are the ones who have protected the inscription from the wear of time?The cairn is rather unlike many that the Men of old built, but you recalled a tale of an old battle...

In the time after the fall of Arnor and the defeat of Angmar by the host of Gondor, few men remained in the north. Those who remained loyal to the old kings banded together under the first Chieftain of the Dúnedain and became the forebears of the Rangers who walk these lands today, or so it is rumoured.

In those days there were still evil Men and worse who walked these lands and there was a battle few Men alive today remember. Though the Dúnedain were victorious, their numbers dwindled. The cairn you have found is most likely the resting place of the men who died in that battle, built hurriedly and in secret.You found a carving with an old Arnorian symbol upon it. It appeared to be the crest of the ancient kingdom of Arthedain.

The ruins of that kingdom stretch for miles to the south-west and north. Bree-town itself was built upon a cross-roads between Arthedain and its sister kingdom Cardolan to the south. Once they were all one great kingdom, stretching all across the north, but the folly of Men first sundered them, then set them against each other until one after another they fell over the long years of the Third Age.

There are some folk who still remember the tales of Arthedain, but you suspect that the crest may be of particular importance to the Rangers, for it is said that they are descended from that bloodline.The strange altar you found appeared to be Arnorian in origin, with signs that some gathering or ritual had taken place there recently.

You've heard rumours that Rangers here in the north occasionally gather for a ceremony to declare the coming of age of one of their number, where they induct the young man or woman into their ranks by way of an oath to the old kingdoms.You found an old obelisk out among the Arnorian ruins, seemingly newer than the ruins themselves, with the names of many Men carved upon it. Your only guess is that it must be some sort of memorial.

The design and the style of the names you saw there suggest that it was built by the Dúnedain, and given their reverence for their ancestors there is every reason to believe that it may be a memorial for their fallen.

Some of the names seemed to have been added recently, suggesting that the Rangers are somehow involved....The horse from Combe followed you here, and seems content to stay put for the time being....The Horse from Combe is on the far side of the horse farm's main stable area from Éogar.Check on the horse from Combe'The horse from Combe seems restless, and likely needs to be taken out for a daily run. Could you go check on him?'The horse stamps at the ground and looks anxious to be free of his stall, and out running free...

'<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will not be able to leave the region the character starts in, as this character and will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>'Bevan, town guard of Mossward, has heard that children of the village have been giving each other increasingly-dangerous dares and challenges, and is hopeful you might be able to do something about it.Mossward has several provisioners, but one of them is usually outside their store-house on the west side of the town square.Alla is by the haystack on the north-east side of Mossward.Talk to Alla by the north-east side of MosswardDai must be somewhere in Mossward, and with his cheese-filled pockets he is likely to be in real trouble from the town's rodent population.Find Dai in Mossward and talk to himAlla is by the haystack on the north-east side of Mossward.Talk to Alla by the north-east side of Mossward'I have heard rumour that the children of Mossward have been giving each other increasingly-dangerous dares and challenges, and I am worried that these may get out-of-hand, if they have not already! None of the town guards will be able to learn anything... you know how children are... but perhaps an outsider will be able to learn something?

'Several children lingered outside the provisioners' store-house a few minutes ago, and it could be one of the provisioners overheard some of their talk? We need to get to the bottom of this before someone gets hurt, ${PLAYER}.''Several children lingered outside the provisioners' store-house a few minutes ago, and it could be one of the provisioners overheard some of their talk? We need to get to the bottom of this before someone gets hurt, ${PLAYER}.''A group of children? Aye, I saw them. They were hoping to get their hands on as much cheese as possible, which seemed a little odd to me. I did not give them as much as they requested, but I thought one small block from the store-house each would be fine.

'Those kids have been through a lot, what with the Uruk raid on Mossward, and I have seen few problems that could not be helped with cheese!''A group of children? Aye, I saw them. They were hoping to get their hands on as much cheese as possible, which seemed a little odd to me. I did not give them as much as they requested, but I thought one small block from the store-house each would be fine.

'Those kids have been through a lot, what with the Uruk raid on Mossward, and I have seen few problems that could not be helped with cheese!''The children gave no reason they wanted cheese. Does anyone really need a reason?''The children gave no reason they wanted cheese. Does anyone really need a reason?''What are you doing here, ${PLAYER}? I thought you would have left Mossward by now. You had better get going, I think. So long!'

You stand your ground and ask Alla why the children of Mossward needed so much cheese from the store-house. Her eyes grow wide and a panicked expression crosses her face.

'We aren't in trouble, are we? It's just that we finally managed to turn the tables on the town bully, and you helped us do it! If we're in trouble, I think you should be also... it's only fair!

'You see, there's a boy named Dai, and he's always challenging us to these dares, and if we don't complete them then we look like cowards! He's always asking me to run to places very fast, see an item he left there, and then come back to town, and if I don't describe the right item he'll know I didn't do it!'

You point out to the girl that she didn't complete any of the dares, since she got the information from you instead, but that Dai apparently did go to each of those places first to leave the items.

'I feel like this just means I'm very smart, ${PLAYER}, wouldn't you say? But because we completed those last two dares... don't argue with me, it still counts... then Dai has to fill his pockets with cheese and walk through Mossward.'

You ask the girl if she has considered that she might be the town bully after all, and she tips her head to one side, considering it.

'Huh. No, I don't think so. But I'll think it over.''I don't know where Dai is, but he has to be somewhere in Mossward.''Rats! There's rats everywhere! They were following me until I gave them the slip!''Is it true that Dai was almost eaten by rats? That's really amazing, ${PLAYER}. Good job saving him, I suppose. Still, now he's got a really exciting tale to tell. Did he keep the cheese, or did he have to give it back to the provisioners?

'I have been thinking it over while you were gone, and I think maybe we won't challenge each other to any more dares for awhile. For awhile, I said! I am not saying never, so don't think you're stopping us if we think of a really good one.

'Good-bye for now, ${PLAYER}.'Satisfy the needs of the Shire-folk.Complete quests within the ShireIt is time for the pie-eating contest at the Bree-fields fair-ground. Come one, come all, and enjoy the fare.Eat six pies within the allotted amount of time.Eat five more pies within the allotted amount of time.Eat four more pies within the allotted amount of time.Eat three more pies within the allotted amount of time.Eat two more pies within the allotted amount of time.Eat one more within the allotted amount of time.Stuffed and sticky with pie, you should now speak to the Pie-man.'Are you here for the pie-eating contest? Wonderful! I'll explain the rules...

'The goal is to eat any six of the pies there on the table. Big ones or small ones, it makes no difference to me! But be sure you let me know you are finished before the time expires.

'Are you ready to start?''Well done, friend! You sure put away those pies, and just in the nick of time!

'As a winner of the pie-eating contest, you're welcome to claim your prize. Of course, you also have a wonderful title to go along with it: Pie-Eating Champion!''Go on and eat! You're lagging behind!''Stuffed already? You've barely begun!''Good, good...almost half-way done!''Oh dear, you look a bit flushed. Are you feeling ill?''This is quite disturbing to watch, let me assure you!''You're almost done! Don't bother chewing, just finish it!'After a journey of many miles, you have come at last to the town of Archet. Aragorn was recently seen travelling in the vicinity of this sleepy town.Jon Brackenbrook is in front of the wreckage of the Mad Badger Tavern, in the burned village of Archet.

Letty Foxtail has told you to speak to Jon Brackenbrook about the whereabouts of Aragorn, who left the town of Archet shortly before it was attacked by the Blackwold brigands. Jon is in charge of rebuilding the town now that his father has died.Talk to Jon Brackenbrook in front of the wreckage of the tavern, in the town of Archet'I must say, you are a tall one! From where have you come and what are you called? ${PLAYER}? That is quite an unusual name. What business brings you to Archet? We have our own share of troubles, and have little need for outsiders to bring theirs.'

You tell the woman that you have travelled from afar seeking the Ranger Aragorn. She thinks for a moment, and then shakes her head.

'He was here, it is true, but he has gone. He left just before the Blackwold brigands launched their attack on our town, reducing it to this state. We could have used him in the defence. To speak the truth, we could have used you as well, had you arrived a little earlier. You look to be a strong one.

'I do not know where the Ranger has gone now, but Jon Brackenbrook might know. He has assumed command of the rebuilding process, now that  his father has perished. You will find him in front of the wreckage of the tavern, I imagine. I saw him there earlier.''The Ranger Aragorn was here, it is true, but he left before the Blackwold attack. I do not know where he went, but Jon Brackenbrook may know. Jon is in charge of rebuilding the town now that his father has died.''Well, I must say I never expected to see one of your kind in these parts! You are of the line of Beorn, are you not? Your stature and demeanor seem unmistakable to me. I have never met any of your family until today, but I have heard tell of your people from Rangers and other wild folk.'

You tell Jon Brackenbrook why you have come to Archet, and he nods.

'Yes, Aragorn was here, though he goes by the name Strider in these parts. He left with some haste, but I heard from others he was loath to do so, and wished to stay and help us with our troubles. He made for the town of Bree, unless I have heard wrong.

'But stay, my tall friend! Do not hurry away just yet. You come to us in our darkest hour, when the Blackwold brigands have burned our town and slain many of our friends. My own father perished in the night, struck down by the Blackwolds and their hateful allies from the north... from Angmar. I know you wish to seek out Aragorn, but if you truly share his ideals you will spare a moment here and there to help people who need it. The experience will make you stronger, and together we may prevent other towns from being burned in the name of evil. Think on it, ${PLAYER}.'As the shadow of Mordor lengthens across Middle-earth, the Enemy orders the release of a mysterious prisoner, sparking in-fighting and revolt in Barad-dûr.Lethi can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr.

The Stout-axes have begun to revolt within the Dark Tower. You should talk to Lethi.Talk to LethiDwalin can be found in Thorin's Hall.

You have spent many months helping to undo the damage wrought upon Thorin's Halls by the Dourhands. You should speak to Dwalin.Talk to Dwalin in Thorin's Hall'It's begun.'

Lethi looks around at the scattered bodies of Orcs, Men, and Stout-axes.

'Before I realized what was happening, Vaski and the others slew the Men of the Order and fled out of the dungeons. I wanted no part in this plot, but it's going to be worse for us if we stay here much longer! Perhaps we'll be able to hide in Udûn... but escape Mordor? I do not think so!

'It doesn't matter where we go, but we have to get out of here! I know the way to the gates of the Dark Tower, but I'll need your help.

'What will it be?''Ah, ${PLAYER}. It is good to see you on such a fine day!

'You have helped us for many months to restore Thorin's Hall, and I hope you now feel welcome among us. I have not forgotten the manner of our meeting, nor the grim events that preceded it. There is unease in the air, and I fear we have not seen the last of Skorgrím Dourhand nor the shadows of Angmar that guide him.

'There is still much to be done in Thorin's Hall, but when the time comes, I give you leave to seek your own adventure. Evil does not stoop to disguise itself any longer, and the Free Peoples will have need of aid... especially from a dwarf like you, ${PLAYER}.'

'It is time, I think, for you to venture back into the world.''It's now or never, ${PLAYER}!'Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel have devised a daring plan: to cross the river Anduin and attack the fortress of Dol Guldur in the depths of Mirkwood.It is time to execute Lord Celeborn's daring plan: an attack upon the fortress of Dol Guldur, in the depths of Southern Mirkwood.Begin the Siege of MirkwoodAchieve 5th level without falling in battle!Survive for as long as possible without being defeated!Achieve 5th level without falling in battle!Healer Iach asks you to pick more Kingsfoil. Unfortunately, it happens to be in the wolves' habitat.Kingsfoil can be found at the Howlingstones south-east of Mossward.

Collect kingsfoil.Collect kingsfoil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iach can be found near the eastern gate of Mossward.

Return to Iach.'This kingsfoil herb works wonders! I'm grateful that Meneldir shared his knowledge with us, though I wish he didn't wait until a crisis to do so. In any case, we need more if we hope to continue treating the injured with such efficacy.

'Now that I know what it looks like, I realize that kingsfoil grows aplenty in the Howlingstones to the south-east. I'd be grateful if you could gather more. Just... watch out for the wolves. I hear they are ill-tempered as of late.''Thank you. With this I should have more than enough to continue tending to the injured, perhaps with a little extra in case an emergency comes to pass....'The Dunlendings of Lhan Garan need help preparing for the coming winter.

A Dunlending you encountered in Mossward told you about their settlement of Lhan Garan. Go there and meet their leader, Talfryn.Talfryn is at Lhan Garan in Swanfleet.

Talk to Talfryn.Talk to Talfryn in Lhan Garan'Well met, adventurer. On behalf of the people of Lhan Garan, I thank you for all that you've done for our new neighbours here in Mossward. I wish we had been able to fight alongside them, but we weren't aware of the attack until after it was repelled. Still, we will be sure to help them rebuild.

'You've never heard of Lhan Garan you say? I would expect not, as we only recently built it! As such, if you have settled your matters in Mossward, I would invite you to visit us north of here along the Wadewater. We had to leave much behind when we left Dunland, and winter approaches quickly. Speak to our leader Talfryn. I'm sure he'll have plenty of work for an adventurer.''Lhan Garan is our home astride the Wadewater, due north-west of here. Together with the folk of Mossward we built a simple dirt road between our communities.''Our envoy to Mossward sent you our way? Good! Good. If you're looking for work you've come to the right place. Our community is a new one, and there's too much to do.'You have received a message from Pethelen, an Elf of Imladris, asking for you to see him at once about some urgent matter.A new story begins!Welcome to Volume III: Allies of the King!The Stable-helper wants you to help the newly-arrived horse to settle into his new stall at the Combe stables.The well for water can be found in the centre of Combe, near the horse's stall.Collect a bucket of well-waterThis water-bucket looks empty and needs to be filled. Grab a bucket of water from the nearby well to fill the bucket and provide the horse with water.Cunedda Moltgig needs the weekly meat orders for the villagers of Clegur.The weekly meat orders for Cunedda Moltgig can be found outside the homes of his neighbours in the village of Clegur.Collect weekly meat orders from outside houses in Clegur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cunedda Moltgig is inside his shop in the village of Clegur.Mayor Malmadog Torlan is outside his house in the south of Clegur.Talk to Mayor Malmadog Torlan in ClegurCunedda Moltgig is inside his shop in the village of Clegur.Talk to Cunedda Moltgig in his shop'What day is it? Are you sure? That can't be right!

'You see, I collect orders from my neighbours so I know what cuts of meat they wish to purchase for the next week, but I am already behind and cannot now spare the time! Do you think you could walk around Clegur and pick up the orders for me? They should be posted outside my neighbours' homes, although sometimes the wind picks them up and causes some mischief.

'You'll have my thanks if you do this. It shouldn't take you long!''Do you think you could walk around Clegur and pick up the orders for me? They should be posted outside my neighbours' homes, although sometimes the wind picks them up and causes some mischief.

'You'll have my thanks if you do this. It shouldn't take you long!''Good, good, very good.

'Wait... where is the order for Mayor Malmadog? Ah, sometimes he forgets to post his order, but that doesn't mean he'll understand if I don't send the steaks to him that he expects!

'You'd better talk to the mayor in person. Then run back here and let me know what he wants.''Sometimes the mayor forgets to post his order, but that doesn't mean he'll understand if I don't send the steaks to him that he expects!

'You'd better talk to Mayor Malmadog in person. Then run back here and let me know what he wants.''Cunedda wants to know what meat I wish to order for the next week? Surely he must know by now that I expect to have a standing order: beef, chicken, and pork, with plenty of each! Malmadog loves them all!'

The mayor notices your expression and gives a hearty laugh.

'I do enjoy them all, but I speak not only of myself. My very good boy here shares my name and my appetite: we are both Malmadogs.

'Now, you run along and tell Cunedda that I want the same order as last week, and mayors shouldn't need to be consulted on this every seven days! I am very busy, after all.''Now, you run along and tell Cunedda that I want the same order as last week, and mayors shouldn't need to be consulted on this every seven days! I am very busy, after all.''So what does the mayor want for his meat delivery next week? The same as last time?

'It's always the same, you know, but if I don't ask him he complains that I didn't! I think the mayor just likes the attention. He always says he's very busy, but he's always just standing out there on his porch with his dog, taking in the sun.

'One of these days I should take a holiday. Maybe I could be mayor, and then I'd have more than enough time to relax!'Defeat wolves within the Shire.Defeat wolves within the ShireDefeat wolves in Ered Luin.Defeat wolves in Ered LuinSlay many wolves within the Shire.Defeat wolves within the ShireDefeat many wolves in Ered Luin.Defeat wolves in Ered LuinPeony Grubb has received word from her friend Dora Brownlock, a chicken farmer in Waymeet, that wolves have invaded the Shire and are threatening the town.Dora Brownlock is at the centre of Waymeet, north-east of Michel Delving.

Peony Grubb has asked you to help her friend Dora with the wolves that have taken over her farm.'I've received a most distressing letter! My good friend Dora -- she's a chicken farmer near Waymeet -- has written to say that a pack of wolves has invaded the Shire and driven her from her farm! She's staying in Waymeet for the time being, but the sooner she can get her farm back, the better!

'Can you help? Just take the north-east road right to the centre of Waymeet. You just tell Dora Brownlock that I've sent you to help with her wolf problem.

'Wolves in the Shire! What's going on in the world these days?''Peony sent you to help me, ${PLAYER}? She's a sweet lady, and a good friend! I'm glad to have your help.

'Yes, the wolves came slavering near to Waymeet recently and seemed to head straight for my farm! It was all I could do to escape to Waymeet without them noticing me!''Dora Brownlock is a good friend of mine, so you'd best hurry to Waymeet, if you don't want your superiors to hear of this. Wolves! I can hardly believe it! In this day and age!'The stable-helper found out the horse needs a set of horseshoes made, and asked you to look into having the blacksmiths of Bree help make some.A blacksmith in Bree-town should be able to help us make a new set of horseshoes.Find a blacksmith in Bree-town to help youThe items needed by the blacksmith to forge new horseshoes can be found around the forge area.Find an old horseshoeObtain crates of nails (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Obtain scrap metal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Matt Haywood can be found at his forge near the Western gate of Bree-town, and is ready to help make the horseshoes.Bring the items to Matt Haywood in Bree-townThe stable-helper in Combe will be happy to receive the horseshoes for the newly arrived horse.Bring the horseshoes to the stable-helper in Combe'The horse's stall looks satisfactory for the time being, but it would seem this horse arrived with no horseshoes. I managed to check the hooves without getting kicked, and they're doing fine for now. Soon, though, he will need a set of shoes made. Please head to Bree-town and talk to the blacksmiths to see if one is available to make a set of horseshoes for us.''Sorry, I can't help you make horseshoes at the moment. A few new orders just came in.''I'm helping Flint here with his new order. You'll need to find another blacksmith to help you with these horseshoes. You may want to try Matt over there.''Ah you need some horseshoes made? Sure, I can make those for you. Do me a favour, and grab the items I need while I put the finishing touches on this item.

'I'll need you to find me an old horseshoe as a template for scale of the new ones, some scrap metal and a few crates of nails.''These are just what I needed to make the horseshoes. Give me a moment and I'll have these for you.''Thank you for taking the time to head into Bree-town and seeing this request through. The horse will appreciate this set of shoes! The stable-master is the only one here trained in replacing shoes, so I'll give these to him right away.'Éogar has recently increased the number of horses housed at the farm, and his stock of horseshoes has been depleted of late. He could use some help replenishing the stock of shoes.The blacksmiths of Bree-town can be found near the West-gate.Find a blacksmith to help fill the horseshoe orderAll of the items required by the blacksmith should be found here in Bree-town. The old horseshoe should be in the fields across the street. The scrap-metal can usually be found among the trash in Beggar's Alley, and the crates of nails should be in the Market Square.Find an old horseshoeObtain crates of horseshoe nails (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Obtain scrap-metal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Flint is near the Bree-town's West-gate, always busy shaping iron at his forge.

Flint is prepared to make the horseshoes once you can bring the supplies he required back to him.Bring the items to Flint Oakhewer in Bree-townÉogar can be found at his farm in the Horsefields of Bree.Return to Éogar with the horseshoes'Our stock of horseshoes on the farm has run out! We need someone to help us replenish the stock by running down to Bree-town to find a blacksmith who can fill an order quickly.

'Would you be so good as to bring some new shoes for my horses?''Sorry, I'm busy with new orders from Combe and can't help you with Éogar's request.''I am really busy with an order that I need to finish as soon as possible.''Certainly I can help you with Éogar's request, as I just finished my previous orders. To help you make them, I'm going to need an old horseshoe, some nails for the shoes, and some scrap-metal. Please bring these items back to me, and I'll make them right away.

'All of the items I require should be found here in Bree-town. The old horseshoe should be close by, probably in the fields across the street. The scrap-metal can usually be found among the trash in Beggar's Alley, and the crates of nails should be in the Market Square.''Ah! These are exactly what I require. This iron isn't the greatest quality, but it will do. I'll finish these for you as soon as I can.''Thank you for returning with these horseshoes! Horses seem to be arriving almost hourly these days, and I wasn't sure what I was going to do. These will come to good use, and I am sure the animals here appreciate your help as much as I do.'A fissure has opened in the great dwarf-canal leading down from Thorin's Hall, threatening to flood the Vale of Thráin.Enter Thorin's Hall to the north, then go west to the Hall of Merchants.

Tindr gave you some mortar with which to repair the cracks in the canal walls.Tindr is in the courtyard outside Thorin's Hall.

The fissure was sealed. You should return to Tindr with news of your success.'Hurry! Take the mortar and make the repairs before the fissures expand. It's only a matter of time before the wall is breached.''That's one less task to concern me. Perhaps that will fix the problems with the water supply they've been reporting down at Noglond, the way-station in the Vale.''The canal is leaking into the tunnels beneath the Hall of Merchants. Hurry and patch the fractures!'The discovery of a goblin-crafted collar about the neck of the wolves in the valley of Nen Hilith sparks serious concern amongst the Elves. Quick action will be necessary and those with the ability to do something about the menace must be informed.Hurry back to Celondim and speak with Laenin the Glade-watcher.

Your discovery of a wolf-collar hewn by goblin crafters has proven a frightening occurrence to the glade wardens. You have been charged with bringing this news to their leader in the Elf-port of Celondim.Talk to Laenin the Glade-watcher at Celondim'We cannot let another moment pass without informing others of the arrival of the goblins. Perhaps Lord Dorongúr's protection is weakening as we make our way to the shores to depart -- or perhaps the Enemy grows stronger faster than we expect.

'Regardless, ${PLAYER}, we must send word back to Celondim and my superior there. Quickly, return to Laenin the Glade-watcher at Celondim and tell him of what you have found.

'You will find Laenin at the docks in Celondim north-east of this vale.''Hurry back to Laenin and report what we have found here. He is at Celondim to the south-east.''This discovery is worrisome. I will see that this information is passed along to Lord Dorongúr at Duillond.

'We never would have learned of this if not for you, ${PLAYER}. We are in your debt.'Postmaster Proudfoot of Michel Delving has asked you to deliver a satchel to Waymeet.Postman Twofoot can be found north-west of the cross-roads in Waymeet, north-east of Michel Delving.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Twofoot in Waymeet as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty!Collect the satchel from Postmaster Proudfoot's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'If the reputation of the Quick Post service is to be restored, you simply must help with my deliveries! There on the table you will find a satchel that must be delivered to Postman Twofoot in Waymeet as quickly as possible. Would you mind taking it to him?

'Postman Twofoot can be found north-west of the cross-roads in Waymeet. Don't dilly-dally!

'The Quick Post service has fallen on hard times in the past few months, and we must double efforts and halve our problems -- the mail must be delivered, not only ON time but with PLENTY of time! Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty and don't let the satchel get wet! The ink will run and be no good to anybody!''The satchel for Waymeet is over there on the table. Pick it up and take it to Postman Twofoot -- you'll find him north-west of the main crossing in Waymeet. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty and don't let the satchel get wet!'You discovered a crude, iron collar on the neck of a wolf in the vale of Nen Hilith. It is possible that the collar may give insight to the trouble that has arisen there.Ovorlas is at the Elf-camp on the northern edge of Nen Hilith.

You should bring the collar to Ovorlas and see if it means anything to him.Looking closely at this crude collar, you can see that this is not the handiwork of Elves or dwarves. 

Perhaps Ovorlas will be able to discern some measure of insight from the collar. You should deliver it to him at the Elf-camp on the northern edge of Nen Hilith.'I know this handiwork. It is the handiwork of goblins. We must inform the others in Celondim. If the goblins have grown this aggressive, then we must do what we can to drive them back from our homes.'Your collection of wood within the vale of Nen Hilith proved valuable to the Elves. Glavrolnen would like you to take the wood to the cooper, Bregedúr, in Celondim.Deliver the cask wood to Bregedúr at the crafting tier at Celondim.

Collecting the wood was half of the journey. Now you must deliver the material to the craftsman who shall make the cask for Elven wine.'Now that you have collected the wood I would ask one more favour from you, friend.

'The cooper in Celondim, Bregedúr, needs the wood to craft his casks. I would ask that you seek him out at the highest levels of Celondim on the tiers of the crafters north-east of this location. Deliver the wood to him that he may build a proper cask.''You will find Bregedúr amongst the crafters on the crafting tier within Celondim.''More wood? Excellent, I have been kept busy enough to think I may soon need assistants.

'You have my thanks for this delivery, ${PLAYER}. This wood will serve nicely as a cask for fine Elven wine.'Mibrethil has suggested that you speak with his friend Gwaloth at a terrace overlooking the harbour of Celondim where useful and comely goods are made.Gwaloth is on a terrace overlooking Celondim, located south of the top of the stairs that wind up the hillside around which the city is constructed.

The Elf Mibrethil suggested that you speak with his friend Gwaloth if you are interested in learning a crafting trade.Talk to Gwaloth'Welcome to Falathlorn, ${PLAYER}. You can see the harbour-city of Celondim up the hill to the north-east, and the refuge of Duillond is further to the north.

'But I can see that you have a desire to fashion goods, to practice your ability to create things of substance and use. It is my recommendation that you visit my friend Gwaloth at the terrace overlooking Celondim, where many useful and comely goods are fashioned. Go up the hill to the north-east into the city and follow the path to the left as it winds up the hillside. Atop the stairs, follow the path southward to the terrace.

'Gwaloth will be pleased to help you learn how to begin your journey as a craftsman.''Gwaloth is on a terrace overlooking Celondim where many useful things are made. Go down the hill to the north-east into Celondim, then climb the winding stair on your left as it rises along the hillside. Atop the stair, take the southern path to the terrace and introduce yourself to Gwaloth. She will gladly aid you in choosing crafting professions.''Mibrethil sent you to me? You must be interested in learning a crafting trade, then? Wonderful! Ered Luin will be better for your efforts, my friend! Speak with the Master of Apprentices on this terrace, for he can help you choose professions in which to specialize.

'Once the Master of Apprentices has welcomed you to your chosen professions, be sure to speak with a supplier. She can sell you the tools of your trade -- every profession has its own tools, so be not over-shy with your coinpurse! The novices will be happy to sell you any recipes you might wish to have, though I can tell you now that you will already know how to make a thing or two.

'Equip the crafting tools you plan on using and find an appropriate facility -- Celondim has a forge, workbench, and oven available for your use -- and begin practising your skills! You will advance in your chosen professions as you practice and seek out the teachings of others in the field. I hope you will become a skilled crafter, ${PLAYER}, and that it will bring joy to you and profit to Ered Luin!'Raindis of Celondim has asked you to bring her some minor woodworking-lore that she can apply to the preparation of timbers used in the construction of the White Ships.Raindis is at Celondim, in Ered Luin.

Raindis has asked if you would collect some minor woodworking-lore from a scholar so she can see if any improvements might be made to the wood that is used as the timber for the White Ships.'It is my privilege to aid with the construction of the White Ships that bring the Eldar into the West, but I have wondered of late if there was any improvement, even of small value, that might be made to the wood we use for that purpose.

'If you know a scholar of some skill, I would appreciate any minor woodworking-lore you might be able to acquire.

'Thank you for your assistance. I have one or two small relics I can give to you for your trouble.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}, this minor woodworking-lore is just what I had in mind. I will spend some time in contemplation of it to see if there are any lessons I can draw from within its pages. Take these small items with my gratitude.'Bogi Deepdelver has asked you to speak with his friend Egil Oldbeard in Thorin's Hall about contributing to the state of crafting in the Blue Mountains.Egil Oldbeard is in the Maker's Hall, inside Thorin's Hall, east of the entrance chamber.

Bogi Deepdelver suggested that you speak with his friend Egil Oldbeard, who has greeted fledgling crafters in the Blue Mountains for more than one hundred years.'Our struggles against the Dourhands and the goblins continue with great vigour, ${PLAYER}, but we must also do what we can to better the craftsmanship of the goods created within the Blue Mountains!

'My friend Egil Oldbeard has greeted fledgling crafters for the past hundred and thirty years...it keeps him young, he says! You should speak with him in the Maker's Hall if you are interested in turning your eye towards the fashioning of goods or equipment.

'Go north up the steps into Thorin's Hall proper. Once inside, walk north past the great statue and pass into the next hall. Turn to the east when you are halfway across the floor and you will descend some more steps into the Maker's Hall. Old Egil will be pleased to speak with you!''Egil Oldbeard is in the Maker's Hall, which is the wing on your right as you pass the big statue in the entrance of Thorin's Hall. Just go up the stairs there and inside the Hall -- you'll find it!

'He enjoys talking with prospective craftsmen and setting their feet on the path.''Bogi sent you to me, I see. Good, good! It is always an honour to help guide fledgling crafters as they take the first steps of their art! Listen carefully, for my words are borne of experience! Look for the Master of Apprentices in the Maker's Hall...he walks about, supervising the goings-on. He can help you choose professions in which to specialize. Choose your professions with care, because you will expend a great deal of time and energy improving your skills!

'Once the Master of Apprentices has welcomed you to your chosen profession, be sure to speak with a Supplier, such as the one that stays in the Maker's Hall. He can sell you the tools of your trade -- every profession has its own tools, so be not over-shy with your coinpurse! The novices will be happy to sell you any recipes you might wish to have, though I can tell you now that you will already know how to make a thing or two.

'Equip the crafting tools you plan on using and find an appropriate facility -- the Maker's Hall has a forge, workbench, and oven available for your use -- and begin practising your skills! You will advance in your chosen professions as you practice and seek out the teachings of others in the field. I hope you will become a skilled crafter, ${PLAYER}, and that it will bring profit to you and to the Blue Mountains! I will give you a few coins to get you started. Use them wisely and consider them an investment in your future as a skilled crafter!'Constable Thistlewool is troubled by the disease spreading through the boars in the wake of the destruction wrought on Archet. The boars must be destroyed before they infect the other wildlife and eradicate the diminished food supply in Archet.Diseased boars roam the lands to the south and east of Archet's gate.

Constable Thistlewool thinks that the best way to end the disease afflicting the local boars is to slay those already infected.Defeat diseased Bristlehides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Constable Thistlewool can be found near the ruins of The Mad Badger Inn in Archet.

Constable Thistlewool will wish to hear of your success.'Ah, a fine day to you! It's good to see the backs of the Blackwolds broken and peace settling over Archet once more. Now we can concern ourselves with less dire problems!

'Actually, you might be able to help with one of those problems, if you are interested. There seems to be an illness spreading among the local boars. And a terrible affliction it must be, for the beasts are more hostile than normal!

'We really must put an end to this illness, and the only way is to slay those afflicted. Would you do this?''Ah, you've taken care of the poor, blighted creatures. Every boar that has caught that foul plague will, in the end, have to be destroyed, but the few you've dealt with will slow the spread of the plague.

'Thank you!''Are you looking for those diseased boars? They should be roaming south and east of the gate.

'It may seem a bit harsh, slaying the beasts without any concern for their meat, but the spread of that illness is to slay those afflicted. It is a sad duty, but one that must be done!'Due to his bad leg, Farmer Sandson cannot deliver the eggs Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton is waiting for.Holly Hornblower's house is in Hobbiton, behind The Ivy Bush.

Pick up the egg basket and carry it to Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton. Be careful that the rooster doesn't see you with the eggs, as he will let out a call that will upset the hens.Collect the egg basketAvoid roostersFarmer Sandson is at his farm, west of Waymeet.

Holly Hornblower was grateful for the eggs. You should return to Farmer Sandson and let him know the eggs were delivered without incident.'My thanks again for gathering the eggs, but I need to ask another favour, if you can spare me the time.

'One of the cooks waiting on these eggs is Holly Hornblower, and I'd hate to disappoint her... she makes the most wonderful pies. I've put some of the eggs in the basket next to me, so if you could take the basket up to Holly, I'd appreciate it.

'Holly lives up the road to the east in Hobbiton, behind The Ivy Bush. Please be quick about delivering them, if you would. And again, be careful that the rooster don't see you with 'em. He'll let out a call that'll upset the whole flock if he catches sight of you!''Them eggs for Holly are right there in that basket. Take it to her in Hobbiton, if you would. She lives just behind The Ivy Bush.

'I need to ask you to be quick though, as Holly is waiting on them eggs for her pies. And be careful that the rooster don't see you. If he catches sight of you, he'll call out and upset the hens!''Thanks again for those eggs. I just used my last one in my latest batch of pie crust. Not sure what I would have done if ye hadn't come by!

'And please thank Farmer Sandson for the eggs. His chickens produce some of the largest and best eggs in all the Shire! His farm is west of Waymeet.''Ah, good! I'm glad old Holly got her eggs. Now she can be making those pies everyone loves.

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, but I wonder if you'd be up for one last delivery?'The rooster, George, seems extremely agitated about something.George is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should find out what is wrong with the rooster, George.Examine GeorgeGeorge is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should check on the rooster, George.Examine GeorgeWald Sandson is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should return to Wald Sandson and report your success.'Wouldn't you know, as soon as you calmed down Billina, George started to act all queer. I'm not sure what has gotten into my dad's chickens, but it seems he only trusts you to calm them.

'If you would, go and see what is wrong with George. He is a very important rooster...he always warns me when wolves are prowling about.'George flaps his wings excitedly. It seems he sees something approaching.'George does seem a bit more peaceful, though with all the wolves around, I don't know if he will ever unruffle his feathers.

'You should go and see if you can calm him down a bit more, if you have the time that is.'George flaps his wings and scratches at the ground. It seems that he is trying to communicate something.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>'I wonder what's got into George?'The rooster, George, seems extremely agitated about something.George is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should find out what is wrong with the rooster, George.Examine GeorgeGeorge is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should check on the rooster, George.Examine George'George still seems agitated.'George flaps his wings excitedly. It seems he sees something approaching.George flaps his wings and scratches at the ground. It seems that he is trying to communicate something.

