<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>Having had a taste of freedom, you desire more.You think that perhaps it is time to escape Farmer Sandson's coop.Examine GeorgeGeorge flaps his wings wildly.George seems incredibly agitated about something. Perhaps you should try and find out what it is.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>Geralt has complicated feelings about the life that missing boot represented, and he is hopeful you might be able to help him resolve the situation.Geralt hoped you might ask villagers in the Stoor village of Clegur if they might like his once-loved but now least-favourite boot.Find a hobbit in the village of Clegur who might be interested in Geralt's bootBriallen Wynbuch in the village of Clegur is interested in Geralt's old boot.Wenna is outside her home in south-east Mossward.Geralt is by the north gate of Mossward.Talk to Geralt by the north gate of Mossward'It is true, ${PLAYER}, that boot was one half of a pair that was dearest to my heart: they were my adventuring boots! They represent a life that I gave up to settle down with my wife Wenna, and now I only want to relive those days by telling tales of my exploits to my son Teg. Now these boots are my least-favourite, for they remind me of those days, and sometimes the memory is painful. I thought I would "lose" one of them; better that than have Wenna think I regret the choice I made to settle down!

'But here it is again, and it seems I will never be free of it! Did I not bring it far enough away? That must be it. Perhaps you could bring this boot further afield? Why not show it to one of the villagers in the Stoor-vales? That is pretty far away, and one of the residents of Clegur might be able to find a use for such an old, well-worn boot as this.''Did I not bring that boot far enough away to be rid of it for good? That must be it. Perhaps you could bring this boot further afield? Why not show it to one of the villagers in the Stoor-vales? That is pretty far away, and one of the residents of Clegur might be able to find a use for such an old, well-worn boot as this.''Perhaps one of the villagers of Clegur will have some interest in that boot? That is pretty far away.''That is an interesting artifact you carry! It must have quite a story, I imagine!'

You tell Briallen Wynbuch about Geralt's complicated feelings about the boot, and about Wenna's belief that it remains her husband's favourite.

'Well, unlike some folk of other villages in the Stoor-vales, I believe that it is always best to be honest... but if you can't manage that, for one reason or another, then perhaps a compassionate solution is second best!'

Briallen produces a pretty flower from somewhere about her person, scoops up a handful of earth, and puts both inside the well-worn boot.

'You bring this back to our former adventurer's wife, and tell her that her husband asked for the Stoors to craft this delightful little planter. Perhaps it isn't the most honest of solutions... but I think in this way everyone might be made happy, and that is pretty good too, wouldn't you say?''You bring that back to our former adventurer's wife, and tell her that her husband asked for the Stoors to craft this delightful little planter. Perhaps it isn't the most honest of solutions... but I think in this way everyone might be made happy, and that is pretty good too, wouldn't you say?''What is this?'

Wenna takes the old boot with the flower sticking out of it, a huge smile lighting up her face.

'What a beautiful gift! Oh, my Geralt! What a dear man he is, and so thoughtful for him to give up his favourite boot for this delightful little planter! This is the finest anniversary gift I could have imagined! Do you know I had believed he'd forgotten?

'I simply must have Skardí fashion a replacement boot in this exact style for my dear Geralt. Thank you again, ${PLAYER}. Our family is in your debt, for so many reasons!''You have been such a help to our family, ${PLAYER}!''How did it go? Did you manage to get rid of that boot?'

You tell Geralt about Briallen Wynbuch's solution to the problem, and he thinks it over.

'Well, I never would have thought of that. The boot remains in my home, a reminder to me of my adventuring days, but without the connotation that I regretted my choice to settle down? And to my wife it is a thoughtful present, a gift that ably demonstrates my commitment to the family? Miss Wynbuch is quite clever; let us hope she continues to use her skills for good and not for ill!

'Wait... did you say "anniversary?" I am fortunate indeed you came to Mossward, ${PLAYER}. I had quite forgotten that was coming up!

'That was a close one, my friend. Thanks again.'Ormr's son Gísli was recently assigned to his first post at Noglond, the way-station in the Vale of Thráin. The dwarf wants to prepare his son's favourite meal to show him he is thinking about him.Cave-claws can be found in the old mine east of Thorin's Hall. Ormr is on the road south from Thorin's Hall to Noglond.

Ormr has asked you to collect the last ingredient he needs to prepare Gísli's favourite meal: cave-claw legs.Gísli is at Noglond, south of Thorin's Halls.

Ormr finished preparing the stew for his son and asked you to deliver it to Gísli for him.'Welcome and well met! I could use your help, if you have a moment. I've a bit of a problem -- nothing terrible, mind you, but difficult for this old dwarf. You see, it's my son, Gísli. He's a good fellow and all, but he is young and doesn't have the experience of his elders. He has just received his first post, down at Noglond in the Vale of Thráin.

'I want to send Gísli his favourite meal so he knows I'm thinking about him, but I don't have the most important ingredient: Cave-claw legs! If you can bring me a batch, I just know Gísli will be pleased! You can find cave-claws in the old mine east of Thorin's Halls.

'You've not had a good meal, until you've tasted my stew!''I am at your service, ${PLAYER}! I'll just add these to the stew... give me a few minutes.

'There we are! Could you take this meal to Gísli? You can find him south of here at Noglond, the way-station in the Vale of Thráin. Just follow the road south!

'Gísli will be pleased, I am sure.''You should hurry if you're going to get that meal to Gísli before it gets cold. He is posted at Noglond, the way-station in the Vale of Thráin, south down the road.''Not again! This is the third meal my father has sent me in as many days! When will he realize I'm a grown dwarf, and not a child to be coddled and fretted over?

'Ah, you're not to blame. Thank you for the food. Maybe someday my father will realize I'm not the thin-bearded dwarf of sixty he remembers.'Rollo Newbuck has been asked to play Hiders and Seekers with his friends, Daisy and Polo Brockhouse, but their unimaginative hiding places have made him lose interest in the game.Polo Brockhouse is hiding behind the carved wooden statue of Marcho and Blanco in the centre of Michel Delving. His sister Daisy is hiding south-east of the carving, in the bushes to the right of Peony Grubb's home.

Rollo Newbuck is playing Hiders and Seekers with his friends, but they always hide in the same places, and he is tired of pretending to be surprised every time he finds them.Find Polo BrockhouseFind Daisy BrockhouseRollo Newbuck is north of the carved statue of Marcho and Blanco at the centre of Michel Delving, within the circle of hedges that surround Town Hole.

Rollo is waiting to hear that you found Polo and Daisy Brockhouse.'Hello there! You wouldn't mind helping me out with a game of Hiders and Seekers, would you? You see, my friends Daisy and Polo have convinced me to play, even though they always hide in the same places! It isn't nearly as much fun when your friends are so unimaginative, as I'm sure you realize.

'It would be fantastic if you could round them up for me. I'll give you a coin or two if you help me out, but I don't know how many more times I can pretend to be surprised that Daisy is hiding in the bushes next to Peony Grubb's home, or that Polo is crouched behind the carved statue of Marcho and Blanco.

'You'll find the statue carved on a large tree stump just south of here, and I'm sure that Polo Brockhouse is hiding right by it. South-east of the statue, there's a small hill with several hobbit-houses behind a wooden fence -- Daisy thinks the bushes to the right of Peony Grubb's house are a clever place to hide. Find my friends for me, and next time I'll try and tell them I don't feel like playing Hiders and Seekers!''Polo is probably hiding behind the carved statue of Marcho and Blanco to the south of here, and his sister Daisy is always hiding south-east of there, among the bushes next to Peony Grubb's home.''Ha ha! Rollo sent you to find me, did he? It always takes him so long to find us. Just between you and me, I don't think he's very good at Hiders and Seekers.

'I'll stay here and think about where I can hide for our next game!''Rollo sent you to look for me? Oh, he always gives up so easily. I'm not sure that you can do that in a game of Hiders and Seekers -- I'm pretty sure it's against the rules. If you don't find the Hiders yourself, you aren't much of a Seeker, are you?

'Anyway, I'll wait here until Rollo finds everyone else. This is a great hiding spot, isn't it?''I'll stay here until Rollo has found everyone else. I'm not convinced that you're allowed to designate someone else to be Seeker, but I guess I'll allow it since Rollo isn't very good at the game.''You found Daisy already? That's very good! She always chooses good hiding-places, like up near Peony Grubb's home. That's a great spot, although it isn't as good as some of mine, like right here in the shadow of Marcho and Blanco!''Thanks for your help, ${PLAYER}! Hiders and Seekers is not much fun when your friends always hide in the same places. I don't think it's a game they're very good at.

'Wait a minute... you say that Daisy mentioned hiding until I found "everyone else?" That's strange. I thought Polo was the only other hobbit I was supposed to be looking for! They mentioned maybe getting Odo to play, but I didn't think they'd actually do it....

'Here are the coins I promised you, but it sounds like your work as Seeker might not be done yet, ${PLAYER}!'Laenin the Glade-watcher plans to leave Middle-earth, but he would see the sanctity and the beauty of the forests surrounding Celondim preserved. Recent events have driven a large number of foul insects into the wood, and Laenin fears that the trees may suffer disease as a result.Sickle-flies may be found in the forests west and south-west of Celondim.

Laenin the Glade-watcher informed you that he is recruiting those willing to help save the surrounding nature from an infestation of sickle-flies.Defeat vale-flies surrounding Celondim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ovorlas is at the Elf-camp in Nen Hilith, south-west of Celondim.

You have defeated many sickle-flies, as Laenin asked, and should now seek out Ovorlas.Talk to Ovorlas at Nen Hilith'Our time is closing in this land. Soon we will be but legend and memory to the mortals who will remain upon these shores. While we are still here, however, we must do what we can to ensure that these lands remain safe and beautiful. 

'The preservation of the land is why I have come to the port of Celondim. My brethren and I have been looking into recent events in a glade to the north. I am here to enlist any willing to go there and assist us in discovering the source of an infestation of sickle-flies among the trees to the west and south-west of the port.

'If you are willing, remove the threat of the sickle-flies from the trees and report to Ovorlas at Nen Hilith to the south-west.''You will find Ovorlas to the south-west, in the area we call Nen Hilith. Speak with him and assist him however you may, after you have removed the threat the sickle-flies pose to the surrounding wood.''You will find Ovorlas to the south-west, in the area we call Nen Hilith. Speak with him and assist him however you may, after you have removed the threat the sickle-flies pose to the surrounding wood.''Mae govannen! Laenin had you fighting back the sickle-flies? Good. It has become necessary to drive them out of the forest, lest they kill the trees.

'Your aid will be welcome here, ${PLAYER}, for there is much to do.'Farmer Sandson has hurt his leg and cannot tend to his chickens or their nests.The chicken nests are around Farmer Sandson's yard.

Farmer Sandson has asked you to gather some eggs from his chicken nests, but warned you to stay away from the rooster. If he sees you while you are gathering the eggs, they will call out and upset the other chickens. Furthermore, you are sure to drop the eggs you've collected!Collect eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Avoid the roosterFarmer Sandson is at his farm, west of Waymeet.

You managed to gather enough eggs without being noticed by the rooster. You should take them back to Farmer Sandson.'Good day to you, young lady/fellow. Seems I'm in a spot of trouble, and I wonder if you could help me?

'You see, I've got a couple of cooks who're waiting on eggs from my chickens, but the problem is I've gone and hurt my leg. It's nothing serious, but I can't get out there and gather the eggs them cooks need. Now I don't want to disappoint them, so I was wondering if you could make the rounds and check the nests for eggs?

'The nests are just out in the yard. Four or so eggs should be enough. A bit of warning though, don't let the rooster see you gathering eggs. If he does, he'll let out a call that'll get all the hens upset, and worse -- you're sure to be so surprised that you'll drop the eggs you collected!''Just go on out there and search the nests for eggs. Shouldn't be too hard to find enough of them.

'Remember, don't let the rooster see you, or he'll get the whole flock upset, and the hens won't be laying for days! Worse still, he crows so suddenly that it can startle someone something fierce -- you might drop the eggs!''Good, you've found the eggs!

'Now, if you are still able to help, I've more work for you. With my leg ailing me, I couldn't possibly deliver them!'The folk of Clegur and the other villages in the Stoor-vales have heard tell of the excitement at Mossward, and could use your help to prepare themselves for any further attacks.Malmadog Torlan, the mayor of Clegur, can be found outside his house to the south of the stable-master.

You have been asked to inform the mayor of Clegur about the worrisome happenings beyond the Stoor-vales.Talk to Malmadog Torlan outside his house to the south of the Clegur stable-masterChoice cuts of meat from the beasts prowling the Stoor-vales can be used to feed the folk of Clegur as winter approaches.Collect choice cuts of meat from beasts in the Stoor-vales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cunedda Moltgig, the butcher of Clegur, can be found in his shop to the south-east of the pond in Clegur.

You collected some choice cuts of meat and should bring them to the butcher in Clegur.Meneldir has come to the village of Clegur, in the Stoor-vales.Talk to Meneldir outside the butcher shop in ClegurGlyn Helyg and Lintrev are both located north-east of Clegur, in the Stoor-vales.

Meneldir asked you to check in with folk in the other Stoor villages to learn if the recent troubles have affected them in any way, or if the Uruks had eyes only for Mossward.Find a helpful villager in Glyn Helyg to tell you of recent events in the Stoor-valesFind a helpful villager in Lintrev to tell you of recent events in the Stoor-valesMalmadog Torlan, the mayor of Clegur, is located outside his house on the southern slope of the village.

You have checked in with the other villages of the Stoor-vales and should report now to the mayor of Clegur.Talk to Malmadog Torlan in the village of ClegurA hunter has returned to Clegur with most interesting tidings!Talk to Flam Helur in the village of Clegur'The mayor must be told of this, even if the very idea is preposterous. It's not that I don't believe you, it's just that folk here have lived peacefully for so long! We keep to ourselves, and we like it that way.

'Climb up the path to the south and tell the mayor what you told me. Malmadog will know what to do about this, if anything must be done!''Climb up the path to the south and tell the mayor what you told me. Malmadog will know what to do about this, if anything must be done!''What's that? Goblins and Uruks? Ordinarily I would say you were spinning tall tales and send you on your way without supper, but there was a good deal of excitement in the night a few hours past, and some of the hunters we sent out never came back!

'I am worried about them, but I am even more concerned that without the meat they were supposed to bring back, our food stocks will be thinner than planned. You don't need me to tell you that autumn can turn to winter quite unexpectedly, no matter how pleasant the mornings or afternoons might seem, and he who does not plan for the night will find himself hungry by morning!

'I will consider what you have told me, but I will consider it more quickly if you bring back some choice cuts of meat from the beasts of the Stoor-vales! Bring them to Cunedda Moltgig, our butcher, at his shop down the hill.''I will consider what you have told me, but I will consider it more quickly if you bring back some choice cuts of meat from the beasts of the Stoor-vales! Bring them to Cunedda Moltgig, our butcher, at his shop down the hill.''Ah, these cuts are choice indeed! Well-done, my friend. I will get to salting and preserving these meats right away. You are always welcome to help out in the Stoor-vales, and I will tell my neighbours what a help you've been today. They might not appreciate it immediately, but they will when winter comes and their bellies are full rather than empty!''It sounds like someone outside is calling for you. You'd better see what he wants!''I should have warned you that the folk in Swanfleet will often put you to work, ${PLAYER}... it comes with the territory, you might say.

'So the mayor of Clegur is waiting for the overdue return of some of his hunters? I hope they did not run afoul of a raiding party like the one that attacked Mossward. I will take a look around and see what I can discover. Perhaps you can check in on the situation in the other two villages in the Stoor-vales? Someone in Glyn Helyg or Lintrev may have seen something.''The mayor of Clegur is waiting for the overdue return of some of his hunters? I hope they did not run afoul of a raiding party like the one that attacked Mossward. I will take a look around and see what I can discover. Perhaps you can check in on the situation in the other two villages in the Stoor-vales? Someone in Glyn Helyg or Lintrev may have seen something.''Goblins and Uruks? Oh, you must be mistaken! Any such creatures around here would be the talk of the town for months and months, if not years! Someone would have said something if such villains as that were prowling about!

'We Stoors are a rough-and-tumble folk, friend. We're not a-feared of much, and that's the way it should be. We don't frighten easily, unlike some others I might name! But I shan't, for we also believe in being polite!'

Dervel lowers his voice. 'Not like the Stoors of Lintrev! But you didn't hear that from me.''Uruks and goblins? You cannot be serious! The Stoor-vales are peaceful, and the quiet is only occasionally disturbed by the howling of wolves and the carrying-on of our neighbours in Glyn Helyg, of which I assure you we do NOT approve!

'But you did not hear that from me! We're like one big happy family in the Stoor-vales, and all three villages get along quite famously.'

Nerys lowers her voice.

'But if I was pressed to put the villages in a sort of order, I would place Lintrev at the top, followed by Clegur, and it would be Glyn Helyg that brought up the rear! Still, I would not wish goblins or Uruks upon any of my fellow Stoors! Not really.''Well, it seems these are strange days indeed, ${PLAYER}. I will not say you were right, but... well, let it be known that mayors are never to be embarrassed, especially not in their own village, and the word of an outsider must always be judged with a grain or two of salt.

'This is all to say: one of the hunters has returned, and his tale is most peculiar! You had better hear it from him!''There are Uruks about, stranger! Me and Drusi Begwyl were out in the brush, lying in wait for one of the boars of the Stoor-vales to stray within reach of our bows, when we saw one of the vile creatures lurking about. Well, we changed our choice of target right then and there! Not for eating, you understand, perish the thought!

'But we caught him! We caught ourselves an Uruk, and now we need to decide what to do with him!'Athal is now concered about Avorthal as he missed not only the meeting with his friend, but is late to visit his father, Cardavor. Before causing greater worry to Cardavor, Athal has asked that you search for signs of Avorthal at his favourite spots within the vale of Nen Hilith.Avorthal may be meditating beneath the white trees in Nen Hilith. The trees are found in the vale to the south-west.

Athal explained that Avorthal enjoys the quiet of the vale of Nen Hilith. He suggested that you search beneath the white trees for either the Elf or his pack.Find Avorthal or Avorthal's PackYou discovered a leather satchel near the body of a slain goblin. It is unclear if this is Avorthal's pack. You should bring it to Athal at the camp on the north edge of Nen Hilith.

Athal explained that Avorthal enjoys the quiet of the vale of Nen Hilith. He suggested that you search beneath the white trees for either the Elf or his pack.Cardavor is at Celondim north-east of the vale of Nen Hilith. Deliver the pack to him there.

You went to Nen Hilith and there found the dwarf Athal waiting for his friend Avorthal. After a short disucssion you went into Nen Hilith to search for the missing Elf and discovered his pack alongside a fallen goblin.'It is not like Avorthal to be late -- at least not without sending word -- nor to put aside his usual habits. Still, he has spent much time in contemplation in recent days.

'When Avorthal desires solitude for quiet thought, he spends much time beneath the white trees in this vale. Perhaps he is amongst them now, unbeknownst to anyone. Would you go there and find him? I would of course, but I shall not defy the will of the Elves.

'Make your way into the vale of Nen Hilith and search for any signs of Avorthal. I pray you find him hale and hardy, but if not, perhaps you will find some sign of him -- even just his pack.''Avorthal has always been fond of sitting in the shade of the white trees in this valley. He says they bring him a calm unlike any he has known. Perhaps you will find him there.''This is Avorthal's pack, I am certain. I fear that something untoward has befallen my friend. Please, take this to Cardavor and tell him that I will do whatever I can to help find my friend -- his son.''You must return to Avorthal's father, Cardavor, quickly. He must know that some ill has befallen his son.''This is Avorthal's satchel, I am certain of it! Do you see this pattern on the side? Avorthal stitched that himself long ago.

'You bring me fell tidings, ${PLAYER}. You are sure there were no other signs of Avorthal? Some sign that my son might have been hiding nearby, safe from wolves or other dangers but too far away to reclaim his satchel?

'Nay, that is a weak hope, and I must not trust to it. Some foe has brought down my son, my Avorthal. That is the only answer.'Unnarr believes the caved-in passage through which the burglars gained access to the treasury leads to the Silver Deep.The other side of the caved-in passage is somewhere in the Silver Deep, the mine in the north-east corner of the valley.

Unnarr has asked you to search the Silver Deep for the other side of the caved-in passage through which the burglars were able to reach the treasury, perhaps finding some sign of their passing.Search the Silver DeepUnnarr is at Frerin's Court.

You discovered a dead Dourhand by the caved-in passage leading into the treasury, but did not find any of the stolen gold. Unnarr is waiting for your report and should be shown the Dourhand insignia on the sword you found.'Judging from the location of the treasury, I would say the burglars dug their passage from the Silver Deep, and that points to goblins. Goblins crawled into that mine shortly after that unpleasant business two years ago, and we haven't had much success driving them out.

'I want you to enter the Silver Deep and look for the other side of the cave-in. You might find some of the stolen gold or one of our burglars trapped on the other side. Bring me whatever you find.

'The entrance to the Silver Deep is in the north-eastern corner of the valley, at the end of a gully.''The Silver Deep is at the back of a gully in the north-east corner of the valley. Watch out for goblins. Bring whatever you find there back to me, and we can decide what should be done next.''What is this? You found this Dourhand sword at the other end of the cave-in? This is not good, ${PLAYER}. Bad enough that our treasury has been burgled, but worse still that it was burgled by Dourhands!'Unnarr cannot believe that the Dourhands have returned to Thorin's Halls and managed to steal Longbeard gold right from under his nose.Dwalin is in the throne room of Thorin's Halls, north of the main square.

Unnarr has given you the unhappy task of telling Dwalin that the Dourhands have made off with some Longbeard gold.'Dwalin is not going to be happy, ${PLAYER}. There are troubles with Dourhands elsewhere in the Blue Mountains, but we thought they were out of Thorin's Hall forever. And to steal Longbeard gold from the treasury? Unbelievable!

'You had better head north into Thorin's Hall and show Dwalin the Dourhand sword-hilt you recovered from the Silver Deep. You will find him in the Throne Room at the north end of the Hall.

'Burglars and Dourhands be bothered! What did I do to deserve this, I ask you?''You will find Dwalin in the Throne Room inside Thorin's Halls, to the north. Tell him that the Dourhands have returned, and they have burgled Longbeard gold from the treasury! I don't know if he will believe it, but you do have the Dourhand sword-hilt to prove it.''Coming from anyone else, ${PLAYER}, I would not believe these grim tidings, but you seem to be an honourable ${RACE}.

'I too thought the Dourhands were gone from Thorin's Halls for good, but it seems they still had designs on our gold. We will teach them a hard lesson, ${PLAYER}, and they will rue the day they sneaked back into Thorin's Halls like the brigands they are!

'We will discover where they have taken the stolen gold, ${PLAYER}, and then we will deal with them. I swear this by Durin's beard!'Unnarr, Captain of the Guard at Frerin's Court, was informed that one of the armouries had been left unguarded.The unguarded Arming-cave is located near to the large statue of Thorin that looks out over the valley from the north-west of Frerin's Court.

Unnarr has asked you to learn what became of Vitharr, the guard assigned to the presently unguarded Arming-cave.Unnarr, the Captain of the Guard, can be found at Frerin's Court.

You found the missing guard, Vitharr, inside the Arming-cave, practically unconscious. Vitharr asked you to return to Unnarr and report that someone had assaulted him from behind and looted the Arming-cave.'The news I have received is most unsettling, ${PLAYER}. One of the armouries has been left unguarded! Vitharr has been a stalwart and dependable guard until now, but he has apparently abandoned his post! Outrageous!

'I want you to investigate the unguarded treasury and confirm that Vitharr is not there. If anything is missing, I'll have his armour! He was next in line for commendation, but after this he won't see any praise for thirty years!

'The Arming-cave is to the north-west, very near to the great statue of Thorin carved in the mountain. Go there and look for Vitharr.''Vitharr will be cleaning the grime off the canal for the next thirty years if he has abandoned his post! Search the unguarded Arming-cave for him, then report back to me! The Arming-cave is to the north-west, very near to the great statue of Thorin in the side of the mountain.''Oooh, what happened? What am I doing inside the Arming-cave? I was standing guard just outside the door, like I always do, and then...'

'Ah, my head! Someone must have clubbed me and dragged me inside while they robbed the Arming-cave bare! This is terrible!

'That caved-in passage must be how they got in. Someone spent a long time digging that tunnel, I'd wager. Hurry back to Captain Unnarr and tell him what happened. Tell him also that it won't happen again! I'm sure it won't help matters, but please tell him that I wasn't sleeping at my post. I don't know how this could have happened... and on my shift!''Quickly, now. Back to the captain. He must be told what happened here.''We've been burgled? This is outrageous! There was a lot of valuable gold and weapons in that cave, and we won't be replacing it any time soon. There's hardly an ounce of anything but stone and iron in these mountains!

'That caved-in passage might provide the clue we need to catch these burglars, ${PLAYER}. They won't have gone far. They might be trapped beneath the rubble, and more importantly, the gold might be there too! I'll have some dwarves begin clearing it away. It will be a good first assignment for Vitharr... give him time to think about how dirty the canal can get.

'For you, ${PLAYER}, I have a more urgent task.'Cardavor, an Elf of Celondim, received a message from his son Avorthal saying that he was coming down from Duillond to visit; however, Avorthal is late, and Cardavor is concerned.The dwarf, Athal, who Avorthal considers a friend, has to come to the vale of Nen Hilith to speak with Avorthal. Athal is likely waiting for Avorthal at the camp to the south-west near Nen Hilith.

Cardavor hopes that his son was only delayed by a visit with his dwarf-friend Athal at the vale of Nen Hilith. He has asked you to journey south-west to find him.Speak to Athal at the Elf camp near Nen Hilith'I have heard that you are well-travelled... perhaps you have seen my son Avorthal on your journeys? I received a message from him saying that he was coming from Duillond to visit, but he has not yet arrived. That is most unlike him.

'In his journeys here, he oft speaks with the travellers along the road and visits the vale of Nen Hilith with a friend of his, a dwarf named Athal. Athal watches the road and helps the few dwarf-travellers who come to Celondim. Perhaps Avorthal is speaking to him now and has simply forgotten the time. Would you seek him?

'Head across the woods south-west of Celondim to the vale of Nen Hilith, there is a small camp of Elves there. If you do not find Avorthal there, perhaps you will find Athal. If so, speak to Athal and see what news he may have of Avorthal.''Athal should be at the camp near Nen Hilith, it was he who last knew the whereabouts of my son. Perhaps he has some news.''Nay, I am still here waiting for Avorthal. He requested I meet him here at the vale of Nen Hilith and has yet to arrive.

'I meant to enter the vale myself, but the Elves bade me not enter and being that Avorthal is not here to speak for me I dare not risk angering them.

'I am sorry that I cannot be more help to you or Lord Cardavor.'George seems much calmer than before.  You should speak with Wald Sandson.Wald Sandson is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should return to Wald Sandson and report your success.'George looks much calmer than when you first examined him.''You did fine work, ${PLAYER}. I think you calmed George and Billina down as well as any could have hoped.  

'It's funny, though...those two have been acting up more ever since that new rooster started darting in and out of the farm. Dad thinks I should try to catch it. I couldn't tell you why, but I don't feel that it's doing any harm.

'For all your hard work my ma thought you would like to have this cloak. It ain't much, but until these chickens calm down for good and start laying eggs like they used to, it's the most we could afford.'Nerys Trafferth is worried that rampant shrews will eat all the apples in her orchard.The orchard to the north of Nerys Trafferth's home is full of shrews to be shooed.Shoo the shrews in the orchard north of Nerys Trafferth's house (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There is no end to the shrews in the orchard.The shrews are gone... but only for nowNerys Trafferth is outside her house in Lintrev.Talk to Nerys Trafferth in LintrevNerys asked you to place the apple basket a good distance down the hill north of her orchard.Nerys Trafferth is outside her house in Lintrev.Talk to Nerys Trafferth in Lintrev'There are a lot of shrews in my orchard, just north of here, and I'm afraid the little pests will eat all my apples! Do you think you could shoo them away? I'd really appreciate it.''My orchard is just to the north, and it is full of shrews that must be shooed away from my apples!''Hmm... thank you for your efforts, but those shrews are sure to be back. They just love my apples so very much!

'I have had an idea. Perhaps an offering of peace will show the shrews I am a friend, and friends don't sneak into a friend's orchard and nibble bites out of her livelihood!

'I have filled up a basket with apples. Bring it up to my orchard, but keep walking north. There's a sloping hill north of my orchard, and if you set the basket down near the bottom of the hill, perhaps it will attract the shrews and keep them satisfied. It is worth a try, wouldn't you say?''Bring that basket up to my orchard, but keep walking north. There's a sloping hill north of my orchard, and if you set the basket down near the bottom of the hill, perhaps it will attract the shrews and keep them satisfied. It is worth a try, wouldn't you say?''You did it? You did it!

'Do you think this was their plan all along? That's very shrewd of them, ${PLAYER}. Now they have plenty of apples, and they don't even need to steal them! Oh, I suppose I cannot be too grumpy about it. There's no denying that my apple trees are the finest in all the Stoor-vales... even the shrews think so!

'You did good work today, and I thank you for it. And I know the shrews do, as well!'Atli Spider-bane asked one of Jon Brackenbrook's hunters to clear out some of the spiders which have overrun the Old East Path, but he has yet to return.The Old East Path is west of the hunter's lodge.

Suspecting that Jon Brackenbrook's hunter went off for an ale instead of the duty he was hired for, Atli asked you to go in and clear out the spiders. He also mentioned that you ought to search for the missing hunter, while you were out there.Defeat spiders at the Old East Path (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search for the missing hunterAtli Spider-bane can be found out front of the hunter's lodge.

While clearing the spiders from the Old East Path, you found the first hunter Atli had sent out, slain by the spiders. In the hunter's hand was Atli's axe, but it was broken during battle. You should return to Atli with the ill news.'Aye, you might do. Interested in some work? See, I sent one of Jon Brackenbrook's hunters to clear out some spiders that have overrun the Old East Path west of here, but he's not returned.

'Fool probably went off to get an ale at the Mad Badger instead of doing what I asked! And he took my best axe, at that. Since the rascal's not done his job, I'll need you to go out to the Old East Path and clear those filthy spiders away from it.

'You ought to search for that hunter while you're there, in case he's actually trying to do his duty and gotten himself into a pickle. Not that I'm too worried about him, but I want that axe back!'The puncture marks on the neck of the hunter reveal that he fell victim to the poison of the spiders on the Old East Path. In his hand, you see the axe Atli Spider-bane spoke of. You take the axe from his hand.'Spiders are filthy creatures, and evil. They've choked up the Old East Path leading from Archet and need to be removed.''The poor fellow...is dead? And I spoke so ill of him. I'll never forgive myself! Those spiders will pay, I tell you!'Holly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Gerd Whitfoot of Bywater had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Gerd Whitfoot has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, since Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Gerd Whitfoot's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'Ah, so you're back. And you're here about the pie, aren't you? I thought so! I knew something was wrong with the pie when you brought it by.

'Bad berries, right? Don't be so surprised. I've eaten more than enough pies in my life to know when something is off in one of them! Holly probably got her berries from the Rushock Bog, and they've been having more than a few problems with the berries lately.

'Anyway, go ahead and take the pie back to Holly. And tell the poor thing not to rush about getting me another. I'll tell the guests I ate the last one, and they'll just have to wait for another! Holly's home is just north of the Hobbiton main square.''The pie is over there on the table. Go ahead and take it back to Holly in Hobbiton. And remember to tell her not to be in a big rush to bake me another. As long as I'm about, The Green Dragon will be asking for her pies!'Holly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Opal Goodbody of Hobbiton had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Opal Goodbody has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Opal Goodbody's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'Back again, are you? What did Holly say about that pie you brought me? The berries are bad, aren't they? I simply have no time for this sort of trouble! Lobelia has been after me for days to get the desserts set for the party, and when I finally get a pie from Holly... it's spoiled!

'Take that terrible pie back to Holly Hornblower. And tell her that I want another pie immediately! Her home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

'Now off with you! I can tolerate no further delay!''Don't just stand there! Take that horrible pie back to Holly Hornblower. And let her know that if I don't get another pie soon, I will be most unhappy!'A fissure has opened in the great dwarf-canal leading down from Thorin's Hall, threatening to flood the Vale of Thráin.Tindr is in the courtyard in front of Thorin's Hall. Sand is in the Rockbelly Pit south-east of Frerin's Court in a place called Winterheight. Gypsum and small stones can be found in the Mirkstone Tunnels above Frerin's Court to the north-west.

Tindr, the Master Builder of Thorin's Hall, has asked you to collect various ingredients for a mortar with which to repair a leak in the canal wall.'I am Tindr, Master Builder of Thorin's Hall. The great canal, for which I am responsible, has recently fissured. The crack has not yet become a serious threat, but it is only a matter of time, and I haven't any builders available to assist with its repairs. Could you help me seal the fissure?

'I need to mix a mortar to seal the crack but our stores are barren. I will need stone and gypsum from the new Mirkstone Tunnels and sand from the Rockbelly Pit. The Mirkstone Tunnels are above the great statue of Thorin to the north-west. Fool goblins dug another entrance after we closed off the original with the Arming Cave. The Rockbelly Pit is to the south-east in the Winterheight.

'If we do not seal the crack soon, it may break, flooding the Vale of Thráin below.''It will just take me a moment to make the mortar. You learn a few tricks when you've done this as long as I have.

'There we are! Now take this mortar to the fissures in the canal walls in the Hall of Merchants inside the western parts of Thorin's Hall.'An inhabitant of Swanfleet has posted a task to collect torn furs.You have accepted a task to acquire torn furs.Wanted: Torn furs of all kinds from the beasts of Swanfleet. Suitable reward offered upon delivery!Wanted: Torn furs of all kinds from the beasts of Swanfleet. Suitable reward offered upon delivery!You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Wald Sandson told you that Billina, Farmer Sandson's best hen, has stopped laying eggs, and that Farmer Sandson is considering butchering her if she does not start laying again.Billina is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

Wald Sandson has asked you to see if you can discover what is wrong with Billina.Examine BillinaWald Sandson can be found on Sandson's Farm, north and east of Michel Delving.

Now that you have learned what ailed Billina, you should talk to Wald Sandson again.'Do you see that chicken over there, the big one? She is the queen of the hen house, and dad's favourite, Billina.

'Billina used to be the best egg-layer in the whole of the Westfarthing, but the other day she just up and stopped laying eggs all together. Dad says if she doesn't start laying eggs soon she is going to end up as supper. I know she can still lay eggs, and I would hate to see her on my dinner plate, no matter how fat she is.

'You were so helpful with returning those eggs, I am sure you will be able to figure out what is wrong with Billina, ${PLAYER}.''So Billina was just hungry for some earthworms? Well, I am glad that you figured out what was wrong with her. Now she will be safe from dad's cooking pot.

'That chicken is an odd one; if she takes to you, she will show you exactly what is bothering her. Why I'd wager she would talk if she knew how!'Billina looks up at you, and then begins to peck at the ground. It looks like she is trying to show you something....

'<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will not be able to leave the Shire as this character and will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>''Have you figured out what's bothering Billina?'Bávor is an artificer tasked with repairing the great lock which opens access to the fabled Vault of the Mountain.The first missing gear is in a cave in the Winterheight, south-east of Thorin's Hall.

Bávor has asked you to help reassemble the dwarf-built device which opens the Vault.Find the first gearBávor is in Thorin's Hall.

Bávor will be pleased to see you have acquired the first gear.'Greetings! I wonder if you could lend me a hand? I have been trying to repair this device, which opens access to the old Vault of the Mountain, but some key pieces, ancient gears, were removed and scattered long ago to prevent the Dourhands getting their grubby hands on the vault treasure.

'Now that we have finally ousted the Dourhands from Thorin's Hall, it is time to open the Vault, but first this device must be repaired. Old Sindri Winchmaster, the artificer who made this, had skill far beyond mine, so I'll need the actual pieces that were lost to have any hope of getting it to work again.

'They say the first missing gear was hidden somewhere in an old cave in the Winterheight, up the path south-east from Thorin's Hall. You will probably find it in a chest somewhere in the cave. There's a trick to the chest, by the way, you have to press in at the corners to open it....''They say the first missing gear was hidden somewhere in an old cave in the Winterheight, up the path south-east from Thorin's Hall. You will probably find it in a chest somewhere in the cave. There's a trick to the chest, by the way, you have to press in at the corners to open it....''Ha! This looks like the gear! It goes here... or maybe here....

'No matter. I will work it out given time, I am sure of it!'Having had a taste of freedom, you desire more.You think that perhaps it is time to escape Farmer Sandson's coop.Examine GeorgeGeorge flaps his wings wildly.George seems incredibly agitated about something and flaps his wings wildly.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>Flosi, an elderly dwarf-prospector, lost his pick while digging in an old cave infested by cave-claws.The cave is south-east of Thorin's Hall, in the Winterheights.

Certain that he was nearing a vein of gold before being driven out of the cave, Flosi asked you to retrieve his pick-axe, as well as clear some of the cave-claws from the cave.Find Flosi's lost pick-axeDefeat cave-claws in cave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Flosi is on the stairs in front of the main gate to Thorin's Hall.

You should return the pick-axe to Flosi and let the old prospector know it should be safe for him to return to the cave.'Can you keep a secret? I was exploring an old cave over yonder, when I was attacked by one of those vicious cave-claws. In the fight, I accidentally left my pick-axe behind.

'Could you go and get my pick for me... and while you're at it, kill off a few of those cave-claws, so I can continue my digging in peace.

'The cave is to the south-east in the Winterheights. Hurry now! I think I was nearing a vein of gold when they drove me out!''My pick-axe must still be in the old cave south-east in the Winterheights.''Ah, there she is! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. But I've sad news... a friend of mine told me that cave's been tapped dry. There's naught but fool's gold in there.

'But don't you worry... I'll find my claim one of these days!'Dervel Crintach has entered into a wager, and he wants to involve you in it.Dervel Crintach challenged you to reach, before time runs out, the water-wheel located at the bottom of the ravine in which Glyn Helyg is built.Reach the water-wheel located at the bottom of the ravine before time runs outAddo Benchuth is waiting to speak with you about your accomplishment.Talk to Addo Benchuth by the water-wheel'I have entered into a wager with old Addo Benchuth, who lives down at the bottom of the ravine in which Glyn Helyg is built. The wager is this: that a newcomer to the town can't get down to the water-wheel, far below us, in less than two minutes.

'Will you help me with this wager? It's a long way down, and the bridges can be confusing, so you'll need to be clever. But don't take the quickest way down... you don't want to break your bones, after all!

'Are you ready? Good fortune to you!''You'd better hurry, friend. The water-wheel is a long way below us!''You made it down here in less than two minutes? Incredible! Dervel said it would be impossible!

'Aye, he wagered me that a newcomer wouldn't be able to make it, and everyone who fails helps to fill his pockets. Finally, someone was able to do it!

'I guess that means I should reward you for this accomplishment. Oh, it's no bother. It's worth it to me just to see the look on Dervel's face when I tell him you actually made it!'Billina the hen seems to be upset, you should try and find out what is wrong with her.Billina is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should try to find out what is wrong with Billina. She is quite an intelligent chicken.Examine BillinaBillina is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should check on Billina.Examine BillinaWald Sandson is in the yard at Sandson's Farm.

You should return to Wald Sandson and tell him of your success.'Billina is eating again but she still looks upset.  You did as good a job as could be asked getting her to eat again, do you think you could calm her too?

'Pa doesn't like me fussing with Billina, says I get her too excitable.  He has taken a liking to you though.  Maybe he would even hire you on as a  farmhand if you had a mind for it, I could use the extra help.'Billina looks slightly less agitated than before, but she looks as if she is waiting for something.'Billina looks much calmer ${PLAYER}, thank you!

'By the way, did you happen to see an odd rooster on the farm?  I thought I saw one, but I never got a good look at it.'Billina ruffles her feathers and begins to make sharp clucking sounds. It seems that she is worried about something.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player friendly npc. You will not be able to leave the Shire as this character and will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>'I just don't understand what is making Billina upset!'Rollo Newbuck has learned that Odo Pipes is also playing Hiders and Seekers, but Rollo doesn't know where the hobbit is hiding.Odo Pipes is hiding somewhere in Michel Delving.

Rollo Newbuck has sent you to find Odo Pipes, rumoured to be the best Hider in the Shire. Odo is hiding somewhere in Michel Delving. Rollo thinks that Daisy or Polo, in their usual hiding-places, might have some clue to Odo's location.Find Odo PipesRollo Newbuck is east of The Bird and Baby Inn, within the stone wall around Town Hole.

Rollo is waiting to hear that you have found Odo Pipes and his hiding-place.'This is serious, ${PLAYER}. I thought I was only playing Hiders and Seekers with Polo and Daisy, but it sounds like they talked to Odo Pipes and convinced him to play as well. You'd think they might have mentioned that to me!

'At any rate, Odo has a reputation for being the best Hider in all the Shire -- at least as good as old Bilbo was in his day, or so it's said among folk in The Bird and Baby. I don't know if it's true, but I do know that, unlike Daisy and Polo, Odo Pipes is sure to have a capital hiding-place, the very best!

'I'll have more coins for you if you can find him, ${PLAYER}. He'll be hiding somewhere in Michel Delving, so don't wander too far. You might want to talk to Polo and Daisy again -- they might be able to tell you where he could be hiding.''You found me! Very well-done, very well-done indeed! Next time I'll need to choose a better hiding-place, I suppose. I thought this one was perfect!

'You should return to Rollo and tell him that he knows how to choose good Seekers!''You found Odo Pipes? Excellent! He was on top of The Bird and Baby Inn the whole time?

'He must have some Tookish blood in him. You'd never get me up there, I can tell you that!

'Here are the coins I promised you, ${PLAYER}, and take my thanks as well! If they ever get me to play Hiders and Seekers again, I'll be sure to let you know -- that way you can give me a stern talking-to and ask me what I was thinking!''You and Rollo haven't found Odo Pipes yet? It doesn't surprise me -- he's always been the best Hider in the Shire, you know.

'I don't know where his favourite hiding-places are, though. He really likes to climb things -- trees, fences, buildings. If you're looking for Odo Pipes, you probably should be looking in the sky!''Odo Pipes used to work here in The Bird and Baby -- in fact, he and I were responsible for rolling out the barrels when they were called for, and rolling them back when they were emptied.

'One time, he helped me climb up onto the roof to fix a leak up there. That was a very rainy Spring, and the rain was like to flood us out if the hole wasn't patched up!

'He was a good fellow, that Odo. After awhile he decided he didn't want to roll barrels anymore, and he moved on. I'm not sure what he's up to these days.''Rollo is in the square outside Town Hole, within the encircling hedges. Let him know that you found my hiding-place, and he's sure to be impressed!''Odo Pipes is the best Hider in the Shire -- I don't mind telling you that he's even better at the game than I am!

'I don't know where he's hiding, but I do know that he worked for a while stacking barrels at the Bird and Baby, just to the north. Maybe he mentioned his favourite hiding-places to someone in there?''You need to find Odo Pipes for me, ${PLAYER} -- he's sure to have found a really great hiding-place somewhere in Michel Delving!'Having had a taste of freedom, you desire more.You think that perhaps it is time to escape Farmer Sandson's coop.Examine GeorgeGeorge flaps his wings wildly.George seems incredibly agitated about something and flaps his wings wildly.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly NPC. You will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>Trouble arose at Nen Hilith when wolves made their way into the valley. Workers gathering the fallen wood of the vale were driven out, and the sickle-flies, mostly a nuisance, fled the vale and infested the nearby wood. Glade-wardens have come to the vale of Nen Hilith to attempt to discern the cause of the disturbance.Glavrolnen and Helhathel are at the Elf-camp in Nen Hilith.

Ovorlas is pleased at your arrival and has set you to earning the favour of his assistants, Glavrolnen and Helhathel, in the vale of Nen Hilith.Earn Helhathel's favourEarn Glavrolnen's favourOvorlas is at the Elf-camp in Nen Hilith.

Now that you have earned the favour of Glavrolnen and Helhathel, you should return to Ovorlas.Talk to Ovorlas at Nen Hilith'Your arrival heralds a time of hope. We have yet to discern what caused the wolves to empty into this valley. Perhaps with your assistance, we will soon learn the reasons behind the invasion.

'The two other glade-wardens here, Glavrolnen and Helhathel, will explain the tasks that I set before them. See to their requests and earn their favour, and you shall have mine.''You have done well here, ${PLAYER}. We will keep vigil here at Nen Hilith. I think now you are needed elsewhere.

'We shall not soon forget all you have done for us here at Celondim.''My assistants will tell you what they need to accomplish. When you have earned their favour, return to me.'Wald Sandson took a basket of eggs from his father's prize hens, but later discovered they had chicks in them.Farmer Sandson's prize hens are in yard at Sandson's farm.

Wald Sandson has asked you to return the eggs for him, so that he will not get caught. You need to place the eggs back in the order they were taken, starting with the first.Place the first egg in the proper nestFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in the yard of Sandson's Farm.

Place the second egg in the proper nest.Place the second egg in the proper nestFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in the yard of Sandson's Farm.

Place the third egg in the proper nest.Place the third egg in the proper nestFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in the yard of Sandson's Farm.

Place the fourth egg in the proper nest.Place the fourth egg in the proper nestFarmer Sandson's prize hens are in the yard of Sandson's Farm.

Place the fifth egg in the proper nest.Place the fifth egg in the proper nestWald Sandson can be found at Sandson's Farm, north and east of Michel Delving.

Having replaced all the eggs, you should return and speak with Wald Sandson.'Hullo there! I have gotten myself into a heap of trouble; do you think you can help me? I snuck in and took a basket of eggs when dad wasn't looking... he is very particular about his prized hens and doesn't let me tend them. I just wanted a snack by the river with my friends is all.

'Well, after I snuck out the eggs I realized that they had chicks in them! Dad has been trying to get his prized hens to lay eggs for longer than I can remember; it must be the new rooster he got from Budgeford. I can't go back and return the eggs, but maybe you can! Dad hurt his leg and has so many travellers running about fetching eggs, you would be able to sneak in and replace the ones I took.

'I got so flustered trying to get away with the eggs that I forgot which hen I took them from. I put the eggs in the basket in the order I took them, so all you need to do is figure out what order the hens lay them in. 

'I was able to sneak out a page from my dad's journal -- he can write you know, taught me all my letters -- though I can't make out up from down with his notes. Maybe you will have more luck? 

'Be careful placing the eggs back in the nests... those hens know what eggs are their own and will roll out any that aren't theirs, then you'll have to start over.''Have you figured out which hen laid first?''Have you figured out which hen laid first?''Have you figured out which hen laid first?''Have you figured out which hen laid first?''Have you figured out which hen laid first?''You got all the eggs matched up with their hens? I can't thank you enough, ${PLAYER}!'Wolves have found their way into the peaceful valley of Nen Hilith and have upset the balance of nature there.Wolves can be found in Nen Hilith, south-west of the Elf-camp.

Helhathel has asked you to defeat wolves in Nen Hilith in order to restore balance in the valley.Defeat wolves in Nen Hilith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Helhathel at the Elf-camp, north-west of the wolf-haunts.

You successfully defeated a number of wolves within the valley of Nen Hilith and should return to Helhathel with your report.Talk to Helhathel in Nen Hilith'Mae govannen, ${CLASS}. I overheard your discussion with Ovorlas and hope that you are willing to assist us. This vale was once a place of inspiring beauty where we could come and commune with nature. It has fallen far from those days since the incursion of these wolves.

'It is unclear where the wolves came from or why they chose to dwell in this valley, but it is clear that they must be removed to ensure that nature can return to its balance.

'Enter the valley and destroy the wolves to ensure the future of the valley. Return to me when you have completed this task, and you will have earned my favour.''You will find the wolves dwell and hunt throughout Nen Hilith to the south-west. Be cautious and return to me when you have defeated many of the wolves.''Nature calls once again from the vale, I can feel it course through my being. We cannot rest on this virtue, but you have brought hope where there was sorrow, ${PLAYER}. You have earned my favour.'The vintner Brethilwen desires to provide enough wine to last the final voyages from the Grey Havens to the Uttermost West, but needs wood for casks.Wood may be found in the valley of Nen Hilith, south-west of the Elf-camp.

Glavrolnen has asked you to bring him several pieces of strong wood.Glavrolnen can be found at the Elf-camp in Nen Hilith, north-east of the wood-piles.

Searching through the wood-piles, you were able to identify five good pieces of wood with which a sturdy cask can be built. You should now return to Glavrolnen'Our efforts here are to recover the land from this new threat, that is clear. We are also here at the behest of our kinsmen. 

'In Celondim, there is a vinter who wants only to make a final offering to store enough wine to survive our journey to the west. I have offered to recover enough wood to build such a cask.

'You will need to search the wood in this vale for wood that has not been spoiled by the sickle-flies or the wolves. Return to me when you have collected enough sturdy pieces of wood, and I will grant you my favour.''You will find the wood scattered throughout the vale of Nen Hilith to the south-west, but only some of the wood is strong enough to be used for making wine-casks.''Yes, this wood will certainly do. This should please the cooper and the vintner both. The White Ships will certainly now be supplied with the finest wine from Ered Luin.'A weary mother has her hands full making a meal for her five children.Rosentyl Flutch has asked you to let her children know that it is time to eat.

Rosentyl's children can be found around Clegur.Rosentyl is in Clegur.

You should let Rosentyl know that you have told all of her children to come enjoy the meal she has cooked.Return to Rosentyl'If ye're coming 'round looking for food, I haven't any for ye. No offence meant, but with five ravenous children there's not a bite left over for a stranger. But say, I could offer ye some coin if ye could help me out.

'The children are afield playing and gathering or whatever it is they do that gets them covered with mud, burrs, and smelling like a dunghill. Will ye let them know 'tis time for a meal?''Food's ready? All right! I will head back right away!''Oh, hullo. Yes, I suppose I can head home to sup.''Who are you? What? Food already? Splendid!''Finally! It's been hours since I last ate!''Time to eat? Oh, I suppose I shouldn’t have had all those berries. …eh! There's always room for more.''The children are all on their way? Lovely! A fine job you did! I do no' suppose ye would set aside yer adventuring ways for that of a nanny, eh? Hah hah, nor would I.

'Well, ye have me thanks!'Vicious hendrevail plague the Vale of Thráin, making travel through the Vale unsafe.The road runs northwards from Noglond through the Vale of Thráin to Thorin's Halls.

Ketill has asked you to patrol along the road through the Vale of Thráin and cull the numbers of hendrevail. He also mentioned that hendrevail could be found in large numbers south of the river to the south of Noglond.Defeat hendrevail in the Vale of Thráin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ketill is in Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall.

You should return to Ketill and report the results of your patrol.Talk to Ketill at Noglond'Hendrevail have grown to alarming numbers over the past year and now the roads from Thorin's Hall all the way to Gondamon are unsafe.

'${PLAYER}, if you would lend your aid once more patrol the roads north and south from Noglond and hunt down any hendrevail you may find.

'Recent travellers through our outpost say they've seen large numbers of hendrevail across the river to our south. If you're looking for the source of their numbers, that's as likely to be it as not.''There are still hendrevail plaguing the roads. Continue your hunt for the birds and return to me when you have culled their numbers.''Thank you for helping keep the ways clear. If it's not too much to ask, please don't tell anyone that I needed help.'Goblins stole a rare wine from the vintner, Brethilwen.There are goblins throughout Limael's Vineyard, north-west of Celondim. Brethilwen is at an old ruin overlooking the vineyard to the east.

Brethilwen has asked you to recover wine flasks of a rare and ancient vintage from the goblins who stole them.'My friend, I wonder if I can ask you to undertake a task for me? It is bad enough that the goblins despoil Limael's Vineyard, but recently a party of the wretched creatures broke into an old wine-cellar and stole a number of flasks of a rare and ancient vintage.

'No doubt the evil creatures have already drunk or destroyed most of the wine, but if you can recover any of the bottles from the goblins in this area, I would be deeply in your debt.

'You can find the goblins throughout Limael's Vineyard. I would not venture beyond into the Rath Teraig, however, as the goblins there are rather more dangerous.''Ah very good! You have done all that I could ask. Thank you for your efforts. Those wicked creatures will learn better than to raid my wine-cellars in the future!'Ted Pickthorn has found himself near penniless and in desperate straits. Rumour of his father's stolen wealth has brought him some hope, however.The Hanging Tree sits along the river-bank south of Constable Wren's post, south-east of Combe.

Ted Pickthorn's father was once a robber in the Chetwood and had purportedly garnered a significant amount of wealth. Ted believes his father's ill-gotten gains are buried at the foot of the Hanging Tree. The tree is supposed to be marked with an X.Find the Hanging TreeAlthough there is no way to tell which stump was once the Hanging Tree, it would not hurt to dig near a few of the stumps in search of the treasure.Ted Pickthorn can be found on the east side of Combe.

Ted Pickthorn sent you to retrieve his father's loot from beneath the Hanging Tree, but you discovered that the tree, among others, was chopped down by the woodcutters of Combe. You dug at several places on the field, but found no sign of Pickthorn's buried treasure.'Me old dad was a robber some years back and got his hands on a good deal o' riches, as I hear it. Constable caught him, but afore he was hanged, me dad told me where he buried his loot! I never needed it afore now, so I was content to let it stay buried. But I figure it's time to get my hands on "wealth enough to keep you warm and shod," as me dear old dad called it. Can you take this pick-axe and dig the treasure up?

'Just take the road east from Combe to Constable Wren's post up by the guard-house. Climb over the hill on the right and walk down to the river-bank, where the Hanging Tree grows -- it'll have an X carved into it.

'You'll be helping me make a new start of things, and you'll have me everlasting thanks!''There are many other trees around the Hanging Tree. There were more hangings in those days, and they didn't want children seeing too much, so the surrounding trees helped to hide the robber-hangings from young eyes.

'Take the road east out of Combe, and at Constable Wren's post, head south. The Hanging Tree is on the downward slope of the hill south of the guard-house, on the bank of the river. You'll know it by the X carved into it.''All the trees are cut down? Maybe the X is still there. Please see if you can find a tree with the mark. Perhaps we'll get lucky and find my dad's treasure!''What? They chopped down the Hanging Tree? And ye dug at all the trees with an X? This is terrible! How will I ever find me dad's buried treasure now?'Postman Newbuck of Little Delving has asked you to deliver a satchel to Michel Delving.Postmaster Proudfoot can be found in Michel Delving, near Town Hole. The square outside Town Hole is surrounded by a stone wall.

Deliver the satchel to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty!Collect the satchel from Postman Newbuck's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'Oh, hullo! Are you passing through? Would you perhaps be heading down to Michel Delving? You see, I have a satchel that must be delivered to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving. The reputation of the Quick Post service isn't what it once was, and I really want gentlehobbits throughout the Shire to once again trust in the speedy delivery of their mail.

'Would you mind taking it from the table over there and delivering it to Postmaster Proudfoot? He can be found in the square outside Town Hole -- just look for the stone wall.

'Please deliver it to him as quickly as you can, for he won't be happy with me if I get it to him late! Oh, and let no busybodies bother you as you deliver the mail. Come rain, come shine, come nosey hobbits, a postman must deliver the mail on time!''The satchel for Michel Delving is over there on the table. Take it to Postmaster Proudfoot as quickly as possible! And remember, let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty! The Quick Post must go through!'Postman Twofoot of Waymeet has asked you to deliver a satchel to Needlehole.Postman Redsmith can be found in the centre of Needlehole.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Redsmith in Needlehole as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty, and keep the satchel away from water!Collect the satchel from Postman Twofoot's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'The Quick Post service has really fallen behind -- there is always so much mail to deliver, and some to every town in the Shire, that even with a team of dedicated carriers, we still can't deliver everything as speedily as Postmaster Proudfoot would like!

'If you'd like to help out, you'll be more than welcome! There on the table you will find a satchel of mail for Postman Redsmith in Needlehole. Would you mind taking it to him? You'll find him right in the centre of Needlehole, to the north-west of Waymeet and beyond the Rushock Bog.

'Watch out for nosey hobbits, for they will delay you and prevent your delivery. Don't let the satchel get wet! The Rushock Bog is a damp place, so stay to the road if you can!''The satchel for Needlehole is over there on the table. Take it to Postman Redsmith as quickly as possible! Let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty, and keep the satchel dry!'Vicious bears have grown numerous and bold north of Noglond along the road through the Vale of Thráin, making travel through the Vale unsafe.Hunter's Notch can be found north of Noglond.

Ketill has asked you to hunt bears in Hunter's Notch and cull their numbers.Defeat bears in the Vale of Thráin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ketill is in Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall.

You should return to Ketill and report the results of your patrol.'There was a time when our hunters kept the number of bears in check, but alas, the beasts have grown numerous in recent years. It's shameful, really, that we have let the wild overrun our paths. As long as dwarves dwell here, the ways should be safe.

'If you want to be of help, patrol north from Noglond to Hunter's Notch and clear out any of the beasts you find.

'With your help, we will make the road safe once more.''There are still wild and savage bears plaguing the roads. Continue your hunt for the beasts and return to me when you've managed to cull their numbers.''Thank you for your help with the bears. Thanks to you the road will be safe once more.'The shrew population near Michel Delving has increased tremendously recently, and Ruby Primstone wants the Bounders to do something about it.There are shrew burrows to the east of Michel Delving, beyond the Delving Fields.

Ruby Primstone is upset by the ruination of the greenery caused by the shrews and wants you to close up some of their burrows.Close shrew burrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ruby Primstone is in Michel Delving, at her home south-east of the statue of Marcho and Blanco in the centre of town.

Ruby will be pleased to hear that you have closed some of the shrew burrows near the town.'You're just the sort I was hoping would come along -- a Bounder!

'My brother up in Brockenborings is a Bounder, so ordinarily I would ask him for help with this, but Brockenborings is such a long way from here, and I really want to get this problem taken care of as soon as possible.

'There's a terrible infestation of shrews to the east of here, beyond the Delving Fields, and they're burrowing deep into the soil and ruining the greenery! If you can find some of their burrows and close them up, that should keep the filthy little beasts from straying near to the town. It's your duty to help me with this, Bounder!''Thank you for your help, Bounder ${PLAYER}! That should discourage the shrews from burrowing near the town, for a while at least.''There are shrew burrows to the east, beyond the Delving Fields. They need to be closed before the beasts tunnel any closer to the town!'Following the burning of Archet, Edward Carver and his brother Roderick are hoping to encourage all those with potential to take up crafting professions for the good of the Free Peoples.Roderick Carver is by the Craft Hall in Combe, south of Archet. The left path from the Combe town centre climbs up the hill past the Craft Hall.

Edward Carver wants you to speak to his brother Roderick about taking up a crafting profession.'I look at you, ${PLAYER}, and I see a blank canvas, an uncarved block of wood, an untempered blade, an unread book... any number of things that have the potential for greatness, but are still waiting for that potential to be realized.

'I look around at my home, and I see wreckage, a memory of the comfort that this town once had. It can have that peace and comfort again, ${PLAYER}, if those like you will rise to the challenge! Skilled hands must be kept busy if they are to improve in their craft!

'My brother Roderick stands near the Craft Hall in Combe, south of Archet. From the Combe town centre, take the left path as it climbs up the hill. You'll see my brother part of the way up the hill. Tell him that you wish to learn a crafter's profession. The towns of Bree-land can only benefit from the application of your skills!''Speak to my brother Roderick in Combe, to the south if you're interested in learning a profession, ${PLAYER}. When you arrive in the town centre, take the left path as it climbs partway up the hill, and you should see him right away.''My brother sent you, eh? As well he should! The business up in Archet is unfortunate, but it serves to remind us of the importance of skilled crafters. It will take a great deal of labour to rebuild Archet and supply the people of Bree-land with everything they need to prosper.

'The Mistress of Apprentices to my left can help you choose professions in which to specialize. Choose your professions with care, because you will expend a great deal of time and energy improving your skills!

'Once the Mistress of Apprentices has welcomed you to your chosen professions, be sure to speak with the Provisioner within the Craft Hall. She can sell you the tools of your trade -- every profession has its own, so be not overshy with your coinpurse! The novices will be happy to sell you any recipes you might wish to have, though I can tell you now that you will already know how to make a thing or two.

'Equip the crafting tools you plan on using and find an appropriate facility -- the Craft Hall has a forge, workbench, and oven available for your use -- and begin practising your skills! You will advance in your chosen professions as you practise and seek out the teachings of others in the field. I hope you will become a skilled crafter, ${PLAYER}, and that it will bring profit to you and to the Bree-land.'Grímkell, the commander at Noglond, sent one of his guards, Vífill, to cut some firewood and is concerned because Vífill has failed to return.Vífill is somewhere in the firewood grove down the road west of Noglond.

Grímkell has asked you to go out and search for Vífill.Find VífillGrímkell is at Noglond, east of the firewood grove.

Vífill tells you to inform Grímkell of the presence of goblins in the firewood grove.'You there! I sent Vífill to cut a quarter-cord of firewood for Noglond, but he hasn't come back. See if you can find him.

'Just follow the road to the west. There's a clearing out that way where we gather our wood.

'Be wary though... who knows what's delayed Vífill.''Vífill still hasn't returned from the firewood grove just up the road.''Ha! Well met! I was wondering when Grímkell would send someone. I was in the clearing, cutting wood for Noglond, when goblins fell on me from the shadows of the trees.

'I managed to kill two and wounded the last, enough to drive it off, but was wounded myself in the fight. The foul creature ran off to the south. Tell Grímkell what happened and to send help!''I'll be fine... leave me. Grímkell must be told about the goblins immediately!''Goblins, here in Vale of Thráin? Nay, that's not likely. Surely not!'Complete 20 Ered Luin quests.Complete Ally of Ered Luin.Complete 20 Ered Luin quests.Complete quests in Ered LuinGaffer Gamgee was dismissed from his duties as the gardener of Bag End by the Sackville-Bagginses. Before his dismissal, he was in the midst of gathering apples from the orchard but never had a chance to finish.The Bag End apple orchard is just to the west of Bag End.

Gaffer Gamgee has asked you to do a little gardening on his behalf by gathering the fallen apples from Bag End's orchard, certain that the Sackville-Bagginses will not chase off a Bounder.Gather fallen apples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gaffer Gamgee is outside his home on Bagshot Row at the foot of the Hill in Hobbiton.

You should bring Gaffer Gamgee the apples you were able to salvage from the apple piles.'You're new, aren't you? There's work what needs doing, but I can't do it myself. I should be gardening over at Bag End, but Mr. Lotho now, he says he and his ma don't need my services no more! Me, as worked the land for Mr. Bilbo and Mr. Frodo!

'The apples in that there orchard are going to rot there on the ground unless someone gathers them. Why don't you head over and see if any are still good?

'Those Sackville-Bagginses mightn't want common folk like me on their land, but there's naught they can do, eh? The orchard is just up the hill to the north-west.''If you have the time to spare, Bounder, I'd appreciate you gathering   some of the apples in the orchard to the west of Bag End. I didn't have a chance to bring them in and I fear they'll be rotten in no time.

'If Mr. Bilbo or Mr. Frodo were here and could see what Lotho and his mum have done to the place...well, it's good for their hearts they can't, I tell you true!''That Lotho won't be the ruin of Bag End so long as I've something to say about it!

'Thank'ee for your kind help, ${PLAYER}!'Cal Sprigley's farm has been overrun by spiders for no apparent reason, leaving Cal and Holly homeless in Archet.Atli Spider-bane can be found just north of Cal Sprigley.

Cal Sprigley suggested that you speak with Atli Spider-bane about the spiders at his farm and how to be rid of them.Talk to Atli Spider-bane in ArchetThe entrance to the cave the hunters blocked off lies in the ruins due east of Archet.

Atli told you that he sent his cousin Bali to check the caves, but he has not yet returned. If you find him, he may have the answer to what has disturbed the spiders.Search for BaliThe missing pages of Bali's journal must be somewhere within the caves. The spiders may have taken the missing pages and webbed them into their cocoons.

You have found Bali's corpse and his journal, but the journal is missing several pages. You need to find the pages before returning to Atli.Atli Spider-bane can be found at the north end of Archet.

Atli Spider-bane will want to know what you discovered among the pages of Bali's journal.'Them spiders have et my workhands and driven me and Holly out of our home. There's got to be some way to get 'em off our land!

'I would think that Atli Spider-bane might know more about spiders than I do. Perhaps you should go speak with him again.

'We can't return home until those awful things are gone!''Them spiders came up through my shed on the far end of the farm, but you should speak with Atli before going there again. He'll know more about what to do, I'm sure.''Good, you have returned! It seems there is much more going on here than I first thought. While you were away, my cousin Bali arrived, and I sent him to search some caves in the ruins outside the east wall of Archet. A few of the hunters had dropped a huge stone in front of the cave, and I wanted him to ensure the stone remained. He has not yet returned, and I am worried.

'Now, from what you told me of Sprigley's troubles, the spiders came up through the cellar in his shed. Perhaps seeing the cave blocked off, they tunnelled up through there.

'We won't know for certain, though, until you find Bali. Hopefully he'll have some answers.''Go find Bali quickly before something terrible happens! I sent him to the caves in the ruins due east of here.''I don't think I can help you. Atli's cousin must be around that cave somewhere.'You search Bali's corpse and find a journal with several pages missing. The journal text reads:

'I would not believe it, but the spiders have pushed the cave mouth clear! I have entered the cave, and the spiders reacted to me instantly, as if drawn to me. I am unsure why. I spent my day carefully searching near the entrance only and found several corpses bound into cocoons. These spiders seem to wrap everything up into their cocoons! I will write more tomorrow when I go further into the cave.'

Perhaps it would be best to enter the cave to see if you can find the rest of the journal pages before returning to Atli.'Bali... dead? This is... impossible! And the spiders have pushed the cave open? You must enter the cave and search for the rest of his journal.

'We must avenge Bali, and that journal may hold the knowledge that will help us do that!''I cannot believe it. Bali... gone. He must be avenged! And this journal tells me what is behind this: a spider-queen from the Blue Mountains. She and her brood must have followed me from Thorin's Halls.

'Know this! Even if I am slain, she will never leave this place... she has found easy prey here. We must destroy her, or Archet shall become a new abode for the queen and her spawn.'Brethilwen, the Master-vintner of Celondim, believes there are enough grapes left on the vine for one last cask of wine.The fertile vines grow around a lake in a sheltered valley west along the stone path beneath Brethilwen. You will need to be wary of the goblins.

Brethilwen has asked you to pick the remaining grapes from Limael's Vineyard.Pick the grape clusters from the vines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Brethilwen is in Celondim, south-east of Limael's Vineyard.

You should return to Brethilwen with your harvest.'By this time of the year, most of the grapes have been picked and the wine already bottled. This was a very generous season, however, and many of the vines are still laden with grapes. I would welcome your assistance. Wine-making is not easy work, but performing this task will certainly add to your appreciation of the wine you drink.

'Harder still when nasty goblins find their way into the fields and drive you off. I think though you might be sturdy enough to aid me.

'If you would, gather the grapes from the vines still hale and hearty enough and I will see that this cask is filled with the finest this vale has to offer.

'The vineyard is below us and further to the west along the stone path. Be careful of the goblins -- they are particularly nasty.''Six large clusters of grapes from this season's ripe vines should be enough. Any less than that, and I could not in good conscience bottle them.''Very good, ${PLAYER}. Years from now, your efforts today will bring great joy to many. Hard work brings satisfaction, not just in wine-making but in all things.'You raided the goblin encampment in the Vale of Thráin and slew their chieftain, but the threat still looms over the peoples of Ered Luin.Bolli is at Gondamon, east of Noglond.

Grímkell has asked you to take the goblin fetish to Bolli, the Captain of the Guard at Gondamon, and warn him of the threat the goblins pose.'It is unthinkable that these goblins managed to sneak into the Vale of Thráin under my very beard. Well, there's nothing to do about it now but prepare for the worst.

'I need you to take the fetish you found to Bolli, the Captain of the Guard in Gondamon to the east. He must know of the goblin's incursion from the valley into Vale of Thráin.

'I've no doubt this is a sign of a larger threat.''That fetish must be brought to Gondamon with all haste. Proof of the goblin threat must be seen by the Captain of the Guard himself.''You carry with you a fetish of the Blue Crag goblin tribes. It's clear that the vile creatures are on the move and intend to launch an offensive against the Vale of Thráin. Troubling news, to be sure.

'We must crush the goblin forces before they become an even greater threat. Their presence in the Vale is a festering blight on the land and if we don't stop it now, it will spread like a shadow across the land.'Óláfr needs help dealing with the lynx in Thrain's Vale.Lynx can be found throughout the Vale of Thráin, but Óláfr suggested heading north to the Thrushstones.

Óláfr has asked you to secure the safety of the road leading through the Vale of Thráin by hunting the lynx that dwell there.Defeat lynx in the Vale of Thrain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Óláfr is at Noglond in Thrain's Vale, south along the road from the Thrushstones.

Óláfr should be pleased to hear of your success.Talk to Óláfr at Noglond'The lynx that roam the hills in the Vale of Thrain have become bold with hunger in recent months. There have even been reports of them attacking unwary travellers! I have the unwelcome task of dealing with these beasts, but there are too many for me to handle alone.

'Grimkell has ordered me to take care of the problem, but I could use your help. We must teach the beasts to fear the bite of metal again and keep to four-legged game.

'Head to the north, along the road back to Thorin's Hall. Look to the west side of the road, near the Thrushstones, and you will find lynx in great numbers.''Please help me out by hunting the lynx in the area.''Good work with those vicious cats. Perhaps now lone travellers will have less to fear in this land. Grimkell will be pleased, for a change.'Grímkell scoffed at Vífill's story of goblins in the Vale of Thráin, blaming Vífill's injury instead upon his own clumsiness.Vífill said there were goblins south of his camp.

Grímkell told you he would only be convinced of Vífill's tale if you could bring him an authentic goblin fetish.'I don't doubt Vífill made up his story of goblins after hitting himself with his own axe!

'Oh? You think he told the truth? Not likely! But if you're so sure he's met up with goblins, maybe you can go find them.

'The goblins of the Blue Mountains sometimes carry these little things, fetishes I guess you might call them. Bring me one of their fetishes, and maybe I'll lend Vífill's tale my ear.''What? He doesn't believe me? Well that beard-chewing...! Forget I said that. He's a good commander, just a bit contrary at times.

'I suppose that you'd best go find one of those fetishes Grímkell wants. There are goblins to the south of my camp and a bit to the west.''What's this? Oh...

'I must beg your pardon. It seems you and Vífill were right. Let's see now. Goblins in the Vale?'Flam Helur, one of the Stoor hunters of Clegur, has agreed to bring you to the Uruk he and his partner Drusi captured.Flam Helur has agreed to lead you and Meneldir to the Uruk he and his partner captured.Talk to Flam Helur<rgb=#FF0000>Both Meneldir and Flam Helur must survive</rgb>Drusi Begwyl stands guard over her captive, and wants to ask you something.Talk to Drusi BegwylDrusi's captive sneers at you.Talk to the captive UrukMeneldir and the Stoors seek to learn what has brought Ushdul and the other Uruks to Swanfleet.Remain alert and learn what brought Ushdul and the Uruks to SwanfleetMeneldir stands ready to fight whatever new danger approaches.Talk to Meneldir<rgb=#FF0000>Both Meneldir and Flam Helur must survive</rgb>You have prevented the rescue of Ushdul by the Uruks.Return to the captive Uruk and remain on your guardUshdul is dying, pierced by arrows fired by his supposed rescuers.Talk to the dying UshdulUshdul lies dying. He has demanded you listen to his final words.Hear Ushdul's dying words'Saruman? Why would he speak the name of the White Wizard?

'What did he mean by that?''It's not far now... just a quick jog up the hill.

'Sorry about the chill in the air, friends! But we're almost there.''Did you see those boars? They ran right past here, and I would have loosed some arrows at them but I did not want to take my attention off the captive!

'They were big, though! There'd have been meat enough on those bones to prepare quite a few boar-meat steaks for the folk of Clegur. Tell me that you saw them, and that Flam was quick enough with his bow or his knife to get them!'

You assure Drusi that the boar-meat can be brought back to the village when you are done here... but perhaps there are more pressing matters at hand?

'More pressing?' she asks. 'I suppose, but still: those boars really were something, and it would be a shame to let so many potential dinners escape without at least trying!''When I get free of these rats, I'll make you pay! You'll wish you never crossed Ushdul!

'You have no idea what's coming for you, for all of you!''I think these newcomers must be here to rescue our captive, ${PLAYER}.

'Let us show them they have erred, and badly! We will not let him go without a fight!''This changes... nothing! You will die... even more painfully than I!'

Ushdul visibly gathers his strength, hatred flaring in his eyes.

'Hear me, all of you! Hear the words of Ushdul!'In order for you to help the Hobbits of the Shire, you will need to join the Bounders of the Watch.Second Shirriff Bunce can be found outside Town Hole in Michel Delving. Town Hole is in a walled enclosure on the north side of town.

You should speak to the Second Shirriff of the Shire Watch, Bodo Bunce, in Michel Delving, if you wish to join the Bounders.'I don't know you, though I've heard your name. If you're interested in helping out around here, you should talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. He can normally be found near Town Hole.''I don't know you. If you was a Bounder, maybe people around here would welcome you more. You should go speak to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce out near Town Hole in Michel Delving.''Plenty of problems around here for a Bounder to solve, but not for some stranger I don't know. If you want to help out, you should speak with Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. His offices are near Town Hole.''There are lots of strangers about these days. We need more Bounders! If you want to help out, you should talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. He can usually be found near Town Hole.''There's tell you're one what helps those in need. Well, if you want to help us Shire-folk, you'll have to join the Bounders. Most hobbits are friendly enough, but suspicious of strangers. As a Bounder, they'll trust you. At least a bit, anyway.

'If you want to join the Watch as a Bounder, you'll have to speak to the Second Shirriff. He's the only one who can sign you up. You'll find him in Michel Delving, near Town Hole.

'Second Shirriff Bunce is respected by most folk, so if he says you're a right sort, they'll listen.''We can use more Bounders. If you want to help, speak to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. He can be found near Town Hole.''We can use more Bounders. If you want to help, speak to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. He can be found near Town Hole.''Why, hullo there! I must say, we've been getting more than our share of strangers through this town, dwarves and other queer lot. Most folk will be polite enough, if you keep to yourself.

'I suppose though that if you spoke to Second Shirriff Bunce -- he's captain of the Watch -- and he made you a Bounder, you might find a better welcome. Yes, yes, that would do it. The Shirriff can be found somewhere about in Michel Delving.

'Good day to you!''I don't know you, and I don't trust folks I don't know. If you was a Bounder, maybe I'd give you a little more time. You want to be a Bounder, speak to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. You can find him near Town Hole.''Oh! Do you want to become a Bounder? I hear they need more people. You might want to speak to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving! Bodo doesn't often go far from Town Hole.''Well now, I don't know you, but I do know you're no Bounder. Maybe you should speak to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce at his offices near Town Hole in Michel Delving.''I hear the Bounders need more people. You might want to talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce near Town Hole in Michel Delving.''If you want to help us Shire-folk, you'll have to join the Bounders. You should go over to Michel Delving and talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. He'll be near Town Hole, I'm sure.''You there, get off my land! I've had enough trouble with strangers trapessing over my land without so much as a 'Hallo!'

'If you've a problem, go see Bodo Bunce, the Second Shirriff over in Michel Delving. You'll find him near Town Hole.

'Now off with you!''You maybe ought to go over to Michel Delving to talk to Shirriff Bodo Bunce. I hear he needs more Bounders real bad. His offices are near Town Hole.''Things ain't right here these days. Maybe getting more Bounders would help. If you don't have anything better to do, maybe you should go over to Michel Delving to talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. He'll be near Town Hole, like as not.''Eh, what're you doing about here? Strange folk aren't too welcome in Hobbiton! I suppose you won't do no harm, though. You've a friendlier look about you than some others I've seen. I suppose you could stay, but you'll have to speak to Second Shirriff Bunce about that.

'Bunce is nigh on the captain of the Bounders, although old Flourdumpling might tell you different! You'll find him near Town Hole in Michel Delving. That's away west of here.

'Now, I've work to do. Gardens don't tend themselves, you know!''Eh? Who are you? I want no strangers shadowing my doorstep. I'm not old Mad Baggins looking for an adventure! If you want to be walking about, bothering the folk here, you'll have to get permission from Second Shirriff Bunce.

'He's Captain of the Watch out by Town Hole in Michel Delving, west of here. He might even have a use for you as a Bounder.

'Now off with you!''I hear that Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce over in Michel Delving needs new Bounders. Maybe you should head over there to talk to him! His offices are near Town Hole.''I think you should go talk to Bodo Bunce, the Second Shirriff over in Michel Delving. I hear he needs folks to sign up as Bounders, and you look like you might do for the job. You can find him near Town Hole.''We need more Bounders, we do. You should go over to Michel Delving to talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. His offices are near Town Hole.''Ow! My ankle. No, no, you can't help me right now. If you want to do me a favour, though, go over to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce at his offices near Town Hole in Michel Delving. I hear he could use more Bounders.''I hear that Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce is hiring anyone at all as a Bounder. Hobbits, Big Folk, anyone! You should go over to Michel Delving to talk to him about that. You can usually find him near Town Hole.''You want to help out in the Shire? You ought to talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. I hear he needs new Bounders to sign up right away. You can find him at his offices near Town Hole.''Oh, bother those bears! What? Oh, well... if you want to help out around here, you should become a Bounder. We can sure use more of them! You should talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving if you want to join up. His offices are near Town Hole.''I think you look like Bounder material! You should go over to Michel Delving to talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce about a job. You will probably find him near Town Hole.''If you're wanting to travel freely about the Shire, you'll want to talk to the Second Shirriff, Bodo Bunce. See, folk here in the Shire, they don't take to strangers much. Lot of queer folk trapessing through here recently. Now though, if Bunce lets you join the Bounders, well then I'll wager you'd find a warmer welcome!

'You can find Bunce near Town Hole in Michel Delving. That's a ways west of here.

'Good luck to you, stranger.''I've heard that Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving needs folks to sign up as Bounders. Maybe you should go talk to him? You can find him near Town Hole.''Hello there! Have you heard that the Bounders are expanding? Not just their belts, mind you! You should go talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving if you're interested. His offices are near Town Hole.''Hello there, stranger. If you want to help out around the Shire, you should become a Bounder. Go talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving if you're interested. You can usually find him near Town Hole.''You should go talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce over in Michel Delving. I hear he needs some new Bounders. You can find him near Town Hole.''We can use some help around here, but not from strangers. If you want to help out around the Shire, you should talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving about becoming a Bounder. You can usually find him near Town Hole.''Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce over in Michel Delving has put out the call for more Bounders. Seems to me you might want to head over there and join up. The Watch-office over there is near Town Hole.''If you're interested in helping out around here as a Bounder, you should talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. His offices are near Town Hole.''Have you heard that the Bounders are looking for new people? Maybe you should head over to Michel Delving to talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce about the job. His offices are near Town Hole.''You might want to go over to Michel Delving to talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. I hear he's hiring new Bounders! You can find him near Town Hole.''If you want to help out in the Shire, you should become a Bounder! Speak with Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce over at his offices near Town Hole in Michel Delving.''Budgeford needs more Bounders! You should talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce over in Michel Delving about signing up for the job. You can find Bunce near Town Hole.''Who are you? I don't know you. You should join the Bounders first if you want to help out around the Shire. Speak with Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce over in Michel Delving if you're interested. You can find him near Town Hole.''I am sorry, I cannot grant an audience to just any stranger. I must admit there is a favourable look to you, so you may be welcome in the Shire. However, I would want to leave that decision in the hands of the Second Shirriff, Bodo Bunce. In fact, he may allow you to become a Bounder of the Watch, although that would be most unusual.

'Shirriff Bunce can be found in Michel Delving to the west. I recommend you speak with him as soon as possible.

'Farewell.''Well, I never. You're a stranger, aren't you? If you want to get by in the Shire, you should join the Bounders. Go over quick to Michel Delving and talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. You'll find him near Town Hole.''Are you a stranger around here? You must be. Take my advice and join the Bounders. Go over to Michel Delving and talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce, why don't you? His offices are near Town Hole.''Oh my, another stranger. You should go over to see Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. His offices are near Town Hole.''Who are you, anyways? I don't recall your face. Maybe you should head over to Michel Delving to talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. I hear he's looking for more Bounders, and you look like you might be good at that job. Bunce can be found near Town Hole.''Hullo there. You're new around here, aren't you? Maybe you should join the Bounders if you'll be staying a while. I hear that Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving is looking for more people. You can find him near Town Hole.''Now what would you be doing about here? Must admit though, you have a friendly look about you, so you probably won't do any harm. Still, folk around here will be distrustful of you, unless you talk to Second Shirriff Bunce. He's captain of the Watch. If you're looking for work, he may even let you join the Bounders.

'Second Shirrif Bunce has his offices out at Town Hole in Michel Delving. That's in the Westfarthing.

'If you join the Bounders, folk won't likely be so distrustful of you. Might even ask you for help with a few things. And trust me, that'll keep you busier than you like!''Well now, look at you. Do you want to help out around the Shire? You should go over to Michel Delving and talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce, so's you can become a Bounder. He can be found near Town Hole.''Hullo there, what's a body like you doing about in Hobbiton? Oh well, you don't look of a mind to do much harm, now do you?

'Still, most folk won't have a thing to do with you, not unless you talk to Second Shirriff Bunce down in Michel Delving. He's in charge of the Watch. In fact, he may let you join as a Bounder, although that would be odd.

'As a Bounder though, most folk won't be so suspicious of you.''No, I don't know you. Thought I did, but I don't. Say! Maybe you should go talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce over in Michel Delving. I hear he's trying to hire more Bounders, and maybe you'll do for that job. His offices are near Town Hole.''You should go over to see Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce in Michel Delving. I hear he's hiring Bounders like mad! You might find him near Town Hole.''Have you heard about the Bounders? They're hiring lots of new folks. Maybe you should join? If you want to, go over to Michel Delving and talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. His offices are near Town Hole.''Goodness gracious, another stranger! Do you want to become a Bounder, too? You should go over to Michel Delving to speak with Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. You can usually find him around Town Hole.''Who's this? I got no time dealing with some stranger walking about and disturbing the peace. Got enough problems as it is with those cursed spiders!

'Talk to Second Shirriff Bunce in Michel Delving; he's captain of the Watch. He's oft looking for Bounders to help in keeping the peace. If he feels comfortable trusting you, then maybe I'll have some work for you.

'But for now, be off with you!''What? Who are you, again? Oh, oh, I see. You might want to go over to Michel Delving and talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce. I hear he's hiring lots of new Bounders. His offices are near Town Hole.''Who's this now? I can't be disturbed by some stranger. If you are looking for work from folk around here, talk to Second Shirriff Bunce over there. He assists me with the Watch, making sure the Bounders make their rounds, keeping out undesirable folk and the like.

'Now you don't seem like a bad lot, so I suppose he might let you join the Watch as a Bounder.''If you are looking for Second Shirriff Bunce, you'll find him in Michel Delving.''If you still want to help the Shire, you will need to become a Bounder, and only Second Shirriff Bunce in Michel Delving can grant you that.''My uncle, Second Shirriff Bunce, could use your help, if you are still willing. You can find him in Michel Delving.''So you were sent my way, were you? Of course, we usually only accept hobbits -- Shire-folk, you understand -- but these are not usual times, I'm afraid, and we can use any hob... er, any person of good will we can find.

'Help out as many Shire-folk as you can, and you'll rise through the ranks. All who would protect the people of the Shire are welcome! We hobbits are a peaceful folk, and our cares may seem of small importance to others -- the delivery of the mail, the tasting of fine foods, the lighting of fireworks -- but do not be misled. Our peaceful ways are threatened, and danger can be found in the unlikeliest places.

'Aid the Shire-folk with their daily concerns, but if you travel to more distant villages, such as Needlehole, Overhill, or Brockenborings... bring a weapon with you, Bounder. Life is dangerous on the borders of the Shire, and the further you get from Michel Delving and Hobbiton, the more likely you are to see trouble.'You've slain a most peculiar-looking marsh-fly queen.The Hunter's Lodge is to the east of Archet.

You should take the carcass of the marsh-fly queen to the Hunter's Lodge to see if anyone has more information for you.<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest has been restored for Legendary Servers!</rgb>

The markings on this marsh-fly queen are unlike any you have heard of before. Surely, someone at the Hunter's Lodge would care to see it.'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This is a most peculiar find!'Opal Goodbody, who is helping organize Lobelia's upcoming party, has been bothering Holly Hornblower to deliver a pie for the party.Opal Goodbody is at the Party Field, north of Hobbiton and south of Bag End.

When you returned from delivering a pie to The Green Dragon, Holly Hornblower had another delivery task waiting for you: she has asked you to take the pie she baked for Lobelia Sackville-Baggins's birthday party to Opal Goodbody at the Party Field in Hobbiton, south of Bag End and north of the town proper. Make sure that no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, or they will be pestering Holly for a slice!Pick up the pieAvoid hungry hobbitsHolly Hornblower can be found north of the main square of Hobbiton and south of the Party Field.

When you delivered the pie to Opal Goodbody, she tasted it and found that it tasted awful. She demanded a new one from Holly Hornblower. You should return to Holly at once.'Lobelia Sackville-Baggins has been fussing and bothering everyone about this party of hers for a while now, but evidently that wasn't enough for her, so she's brought on another hobbit, Opal Goodbody, to help her.

'Poor Opal has been so harried by Lobelia that she's snapping at everyone. She's been after me for a pie, but being not too fond of Lobelia, I've put it off. But I couldn't put it off any longer, so today I made the pie she's been after.

'The pie is cooling on the table over there. Take it up to Opal at the Party Field, but remember: even though this pie is for Lobelia, it must be hot when ye deliver it! Keep it away from those hungry hobbits... I don't want them pestering me!''The pie for Lobelia's party is over there on the table. Pick it up and deliver it to Opal Goodbody out on the Party Field. And be quick about it, my pies must be delivered hot!

'Don't forget to not let any hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as I don't want them pestering me for a slice!''Why are you still standing here? Go tell Holly that her pie tasted foul! I demand a new one!''What? My pie tasted foul? Of all the rude things to say! Here, let me taste this one I'm working on now....

'These berries are bad! Oh no, oh no! Do you know how many pies I've made with these berries?'

'I simply must get to making new pies for all those people. I haven't the time to talk right now, but I'm glad ye found this out for me. Oh, and if ye come across any of the pies I sent out, please bring them to me. Tell them that I will bake them a fresh pie as soon as I can. I simply can't allow people to eat bad pies!'Earur wishes to aid the people of Archet and believes that there are enough supplies to begin the rebuilding process. To ensure that supplies do not dwindle too quickly he directed you to visit Taylor Green at the Combe Lumber Yard.Tell Taylor Green at the Lumber Mill in Combe that Builder Earur needs more wood in Archet.

Builder Earur mentioned that Archet would need more wood to completely rebuild. He asked you to visit the Combe Lumber Yard and tell Taylor Green that Archet needs more wood.'Supplies here in Archet are limited and will certainly not suffice to repair the damage wrought upon the village. Now that I have my tools, I will be able to begin shoring the fences and repairing the buildings where I can.

'Archet will need more lumber if it is to recover completely from this attack. If you find yourself in Combe, to the south, seek out Taylor Green and let him know that I will need another order of wood from the lumber yard.

'If you've not been there before, listen well. The Combe Lumber Yard can be found by following the road south. Pass through the gate toward Combe and follow the road east up the hill. It will bend softly to the north east towards the Chetwood. There, in a soft dip before the North Chetwood you should find Taylor Green.''Archet's woes did not escape us here in Combe, and it's good what Earur is doing, no doubt in that. But the evil of the Blackwold has spread and now rests in the same wood where we need to collect the wood for Archet.

'I will see that we do what we can, but as you can see, we've troubles of our own.''Hurry along now. I'll get to work on what I can, but the lumber will not last long. Find Taylor Green at the Lumber yard east and north from the centre of Combe.'Bregedúr, at the Craftsman's Plaza in Celondim, asked that you deliver a cask meant for storing wine to his friend Brethilwen at Limael's Vineyard.You will find Brethilwen to the north and west at the outskirts of Limael's Vineyard. Make your way along the roadway heading north-west out of Celondim and follow the small path along the river to the west to find her.

Bregedúr, the local cooper at Celondim, asked you to deliver a cask to his friend Brethilwen at Limael's Vineyard.'${CLASS}, if you would take a moment, I have a request of you. A dear friend to me, Brethilwen, spends her days tending the grapes at Limael's Vineyard to the north and west. She sent word to me not long ago that she required a cask for a special wine she wanted to present upon the White Ships.

'I have crafted a cask for her, but need someone to take it to her since the preparations for our departure keep me very busy.

'Would you take the cask to her? You will find her to the north and west at Limael's Vineyard.''You will find Brethilwen at Limael's Vineyard to the north and west of Celondim. Follow the road north-west and shortly after the river seek the small path leading to the west. You will find her along that road.''I only wish that this thoughtful gift from Bregedúr did not arrive during such dire times. With the situation at the Vineyard, I fear that the cask may go empty for our journey.'Holly Hornblower's pies are in exceeding demand, and she does not have time to deliver them all.Gerd Whitfoot is at The Green Dragon Inn in Bywater.

Holly Hornblower has asked you to deliver a pie to Gerd Whitfoot at The Green Dragon in Bywater. She warned you to not allow any hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, or they will come by pestering her for a slice, and she has no time for that.Pick up the pie from the tableAvoid hungry hobbitsHolly Hornblower can be found north of Hobbiton's main square, behind The Ivy Bush.

You should return to Holly Hornblower and let her know that the pie has been delivered.'Ah, just who I wanted to see. I've got something very important for the likes of you!

'I'm up to my ears in people wanting my pies. Now I'm not complaining -- it's good that people love my pies -- but I've not the time to deliver them! Right now I've got one that simply has to be taken to The Green Dragon. Would you take it there?

'The pie is cooling on the table over there. Take it to Gerd Whitfoot, south-east of here in Bywater, and be quick about it! I'm known for delivering hot pies, and if it cools too much, I won't get paid! Also, don't let any hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, or they'll be over here pestering me for a slice, and I don't have time for that either!''The pie for The Green Dragon is cooling over there by the table. Take it to Gerd Whitfoot at The Green Dragon in Bywater, to the south-east.

'Be quick about it, my pies must be delivered piping hot! And don't let any hungry hobbits catch a whiff, or they'll be pestering me for a slice!''Thanks again for that pie, although it smells a bit... off, somehow. Oh well, I'm sure it'll be delicious. Please give my thanks to Holly!''Smelled a bit off, he says? That Gerd Whitfoot couldn't smell a pig farm if he was in the middle of it!

'Anyway, there's another pie that needs to be delivered, and the one waiting for this pie isn't quite so friendly as Gerd over in Bywater!'While hunting for game for the village, some of the Stoor hunters captured an Uruk.Meneldir is in the village of Clegur, in the Stoor-vales.

The Ranger's opinion is obvious: he wants the two of you to follow the Stoor hunter back to the captive Uruk.Talk to Meneldir and follow Flam back to the captive UrukMalmadog Torlan, the Mayor of Clegur, is pleased that you helped his folk.Talk to Malmadog Torlan in the village of Clegur'I left Drusi behind so I could ask Mayor Torlan what to do, but if you and this Ranger are up to it, I could lead the two of you back to the prisoner. It's not that far.

'What do you say?''We had better follow him to his captive, ${PLAYER}, and quickly! The Stoors are a hardy folk, but I fear the harm an Uruk warrior might do, though he be their captive.''What do you say? Should I lead the two of you back to the Uruk we captured? I'm sure Drusi can handle herself, but the sooner we leave, the better!''Thank you for aiding my folk, ${PLAYER}. It reflects well upon you that you were willing to help the people of the Stoor-vales in this, and it reflects well upon me that I called upon your assistance. That's the mark of a good mayor, you know: selecting the right person for the job at hand!

'I have had little to do with Wizards, but I can tell from your friend's expression that these tidings of Saruman can mean nothing good. Perhaps this gift will help speed you on your way to combat this new and unpleasant development.'If it is true that Saruman commands the loyalties of the Uruks that have come to Swanfleet, there may indeed be dark days ahead for Middle-earth.Meneldir stands by the mayor in the village of Clegur, in the Stoor-vales.Talk to Meneldir in the village of ClegurMeneldir desires to return to Mossward to speak with the townspeople there, and he recommended you do the same.Return to the town square of MosswardCadogan addresses the crowd.Talk to Cadogan in the Mossward town squareCadogan asked you to carry a barrel of swords from within Skardí Bendblade's shop to the town square so the folk of Mossward can be armed against further intrusion by the Uruks.Pick up a barrel of swords inside the Mossward blacksmith shopMeneldir is to the north-west, trying to get your attention.Talk to Meneldir north-west of the town square, in MosswardMeneldir wishes to discuss what he knows of the Wizards that walk in Middle-earth.Hear what Meneldir knows of Saruman the WizardHear what Meneldir knows of Radagast the WizardHear what Meneldir knows of Gandalf the WizardMeneldir is north-west of the town square, in Mossward.Talk to Meneldir north-west of the town square, in Mossward'Why does your Ranger friend just stand there, like a lump on a log? Speak up, man. What has gotten into him?''I do not know much of Wizards. That has always been for the best, and if they choose to send Uruks to ravage our lands it is seeming a better choice day after day!''I cannot believe this, ${PLAYER}. Can it be true that Saruman commanded these Uruks to attack the folk of Swanfleet? Why would the Wizard wish to do harm to the folk of Mossward? He has ever been a watchful protector of Middle-earth! What can have changed?

'It must be a lie. There can be no other explanation. Let us return to Mossward and see how the people there fare in our absence. I... I cannot believe Saruman is capable of such treachery. There must be something else to blame for the Orc-presence in these lands.''We should return to Mossward. I need time to think about this.''We must make ready!''We won't be caught off-guard again! If goblins and Uruks seek to raid our village again, we will make them pay a heavy price for it!

'Skardí Bendblade has been working to supply us with arms and armour, ${PLAYER}, so we will be prepared if another raiding party comes to Mossward. Will you bring us another barrel of the weapons he has fashioned for us? I will then distribute them to the people of the village.''Skardí Bendblade has been working to supply us with arms and armour, ${PLAYER}, so we will be prepared if another raiding party comes to Mossward. Will you bring us another barrel of the weapons he has fashioned for us? I will then distribute them to the people of the village.''Aye, there's another barrel of weapons for the folk of Mossward. You can come behind the counter to pick it up... just don't touch anything else!''Cadogan means well, and the folk of Mossward will fight to defend their homes from goblins and Uruks and anything else that threatens them... but against Wizards I do not think they will have a very high chance of survival.

'I will tell you what I know of the Three Wizards, ${PLAYER}, and I will let you judge our chances.''I will tell you what I know of the Three Wizards that walk in Middle-earth. It is not very much, I confess it.'Meneldir sighs heavily.

'I have always understood Saruman the White to be the most learned of the Wizards, and the greatest of their order. It is said he was sent here by the Powers to guide and instruct those who dwell within Middle-earth. At Isengard he lives, in a great tower built by the Númenóreans. Orthanc, it is called, and I have heard it contains a trove of knowledge and learning unmatched by that of any king or scholar.

'Can it be that Saruman no longer seeks to protect the Free Peoples of Middle-earth? I cannot believe this is so.'Meneldir rubs his temple, deep in thought.

'Of all the Three Wizards, I have only met this one in person: Radagast the Brown, a master of shapes and hues and friend to all good-hearted beasts and birds. He wanders the wild places, secret lands known only to creatures of fur and feather... and I suppose known to some of my kin among the Dúnedain, as well.

'He seemed a jovial chap to me, when I met him. I cannot believe he would turn against us.'Meneldir shakes his head.

'I know little about Gandalf the Grey. They say he walks the land with the aid of an old walking-stick, pipe-smoke curling about the tall hat he wears, but I have never seen him. I believe he must keep to himself, choosing not to become involved in the matters of the day.

'My former chieftain Strider knew him, and believed him to be a kindly soul. I have never known my chieftain to judge someone wrongly, and if he had it was not his fault but another's.

'Still, I would not have believed any of the Wizards could become corrupted, either....''I don't know, ${PLAYER}.

'If the aims of the Three Wizards have changed, if they have been corrupted by evil, all of the Free Peoples of Middle-earth may be endangered.'Dwalin's mood has lightened somewhat now that he knows where the Dourhands took the stolen gold. Plans have been put in motion to recover the gold.Rothgar is at Noglond, the way-station far to the south along the road that runs through the Vale of Thráin.

Dwalin has asked you to work with Rothgar, a loyal Longbeard, to recover the stolen gold from the Dourhand thieves.'Well, Dourhands are no better than goblins, anyway, so it should not be too difficult to retrieve the gold!

'A Longbeard by the name of Rothgar is at Noglond, the way-station to the south. He is very loyal to Dáin and has kept an eye on doings within the Vale of Thráin. Follow the road south to Noglond and ask him about the old Dourhand city in the mountains that edge the Vale. Once you have learned what Rothgar knows about the place, make your way inside and retrieve the stolen Longbeard gold!

'You can trust Rothgar to return the gold to me once you have recovered it. He is a Longbeard I would trust with my life...and my wealth!''Welcome to Noglond, friend ${CLASS}! You might not know it, but this way-station has a storied history nearly as rich as Thorin's Halls itself! I would be honoured to tell you of....

'Oh, I see. You are here on business from Dwalin? You will never find a truer Longbeard than our Steward, and Thorin's Halls are maintained with the dignity that befits our glorious....

'Ah, yes, your pardon. What was it you were wanting, friend?''Noglond is down in the Vale of Thráin. Just follow the road south from Thorin's Halls. Rothgar is a loyal Longbeard and should be able to tell you much about the old Dourhand city where the stolen gold has been hidden.'Mundo Sackville-Baggins is furious about his treatment at the hands of the Blackwold brigands and demands compensation from Mayor Will Whitfoot for his inconvenience.Mayor Will Whitfoot is in Michel Delving, just outside Town Hole. Town Hole is on your left, surrounded by hedges, as you enter Michel Delving from the north.

Mundo Sackville-Baggins has written a letter of complaint to the Mayor and has asked you to deliver it.'This is outrageous, ${PLAYER}! I will not be satisfied until I receive compensation for my treatment at the hands of those Blackwolds. I have been most ill-used, and it is more than any hobbit would stand!

'A Sackville-Baggins should be able to travel throughout the Shire and even into Bree-land, if he wishes it, without danger of being abducted! And when a Sackville-Baggins is promised gold, he had better receive some gold when the whole thing is done with -- it is only fair!

'I wrote this letter while you were off looking for Jon Brackenbrook. It doesn't include the business with the brigands burning Archet or that Ranger becoming so queer, but it's sure to be enough for old Flourdumpling. Take my letter to Mayor Will Whitfoot in Michel Delving. He'll be just outside Town Hole, which will be to your left, surrounded by hedges, when you enter town.''You deliver my letter to Mayor Whitfoot in Michel Delving, ${PLAYER}, and I won't forget the favour! He'll be outside Town Hole, which is to your left as you enter the town. It's surrounded by hedges, so you shouldn't have any trouble finding it.''What's this? Oh dear. A letter from a Sackville-Baggins is not something you want to see.

'He's holding me personally accountable for his troubles in Bree-land? I wasn't even there! I've never even been outside the Shire! And now I'm supposed to pay "just compensation" to his family? But he took no harm and was in Archet of his own accord!

'You don't happen to know why I wanted to be Mayor, do you? Because I seem to have forgotten.'From all appearances, goblins waylaid Avorthal in Tham Gelair, leaving no trace of him but his satchel.Pampraush and his minions are in Limael's Vineyard, north-west of Celondim.

The apparent death of Avorthal has enraged Cardavor against the goblins. He has asked you to seek out a band of goblins led by a creature named Pampraush and slay them all in Avorthal's name.Cardavor is at Celondim, the harbour south-east of Limael's Vineyard.

You sought out the goblin Pampraush and his minions as Cardavor requested, but learned from Pampraush that Avorthal may still be alive as a prisoner of dwarves. Cardavor should be told at once.'The goblins have slain my son, ${PLAYER}, and for that we will sweep them from Ered Luin! No goblin will take as much as three steps into these lands before we are there to greet him with swordblade or arrowhead!

'Go forth and slay goblins wherever you find them and cry aloud the name of Avorthal. I would have the foul creatures know whose doom has come upon them!

'While you were gone, word came to me that Limael's Vineyard has been defiled by goblins led by a vile creature called Pampraush. Seek out Pampraush and his minions and slay them in the name of Avorthal! Limael's Vineyard lies north-west of Celondim.''Limael's Vineyard is to the north-west of Celondim, on the high-ground above the harbour. I will not be satisfied until you have avenged my son's death.''What is this? Pampraush said that my son still lives? Avorthal was not slain? My heart wants to believe... but believe the words of a goblin? Still, I cannot fathom why he would tell you this if it were not so.

'But if Avorthal is alive, then his capture does not bode well. I fear he will not live long while imprisoned by those outcast dwarves. They are no better than the goblins!'According to Geitir, the waterflow from the canal has been staunched for several days, and the builders have not replied to his message requesting assistance.The canal can be found south of Noglond, flowing down from Thorin's Halls.

Geitir asks you to investigate the flow of the canal to Noglond and learn the cause of the problem.Discover the source of the canal's waterflow problemThere are thickets blocking the canal between Noglond and Thorin's Halls.

Now that you have discovered the problem in the canal, you should clear away enough of the thickets to allow the water to flow more freely. There may be several patches of thickets along the canal.Clear away the thickets clogging the canal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Geitir is at Noglond to the north of the canal, south of Thorin's Halls.

You should return to Geitir with news of your success.'The water has not been flowing down to Noglond for several days. I sent a message back to the Halls, but I've not received a reply from the builders. I'm not about to send one of my boys to do builder's work, and I can't have them trapessing to the river every time we need water.

'Would you look into it? The canal runs all the way down the mountain from Thorin's Halls and to Gondamon below. The problem must be up-river from here.

'The above-ground part of the canal, the place that may be blocked, is south and west of here. Just take the road south to the bridge and look underneath it. Follow the canal all the way up to the big gate if you have to, just find the problem!''Have you found the source of the problem?''Aye, it would be a great help if you would clear away the thickets clogging the canal.''Done already? Good work! We could use someone like you on the guard... better than these layabouts. Can I interest you in signing up? Oh, the pay's not that good, and you'll find yourself in some cold, out-of-the-way post like this, but it's a living. No? I thought not....

'Ah well, thanks for your work, anyway.'Wolves have invaded the Shire, and some of them chased Dora Brownlock from her farm and have begun to feed on her chickens.Dora's chickens are at her farm north of Waymeet, at the end of the first stone path on the right off the main road.

You went to Waymeet to help Dora Brownlock at the behest of Peony Grubb. Dora has in turn asked you to rescue her chickens from her farm, which has been overrun by the wolves.Collect Dora's chickens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dora Brownlock is at the centre of Waymeet.

Dora Brownlock will be pleased to have her chickens returned to her, safe from the threat of the wolves prowling about her farm. You should return to her at once.'When the wolves chased me off my farm, I didn't have enough time to collect my babies! My poor darlings... what was that? My chickens, of course! If those wolves have gotten hold of them, I just don't know what I'll do!

'You can save them for me, ${PLAYER}, I know you can! Follow the road north up the hill and out of Waymeet, then take the first stone path to your right. You'll see a sign for my farm at the correct crossing.

'Quickly! You must save my little darlings!''You simply must rescue my babies from the wolves! You'll find my poor dears at my farm, to the north of Waymeet. Please hurry!''You saved my chickens! Thank you so much! I don't know what I would have done if the wolves had gotten my darling Rosy, or my precious Georgie, or my lovely Dottie!

'Someone needs to do something about these wolves, and I think that someone is you, ${PLAYER}!'Brethilwen wishes to thank Bregedúr for his kindness.Bregedúr spends his time at the crafters' market in Celondim.

Brethilwen crushed the grapes you collected into a fine wine and sent them on to her friend Bregedúr in Celondim.'All filled and ready for delivery. I would like to thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}, as I would not have been able to see this last bit of harvest along without you.

'This cask is meant for another; however, I should like to see it sent along to my friend Bregedúr. It was he who sent it to me, after all... why should he not have the finest wine of the valley?

'If you would, take this back to him at Celondim. Follow the path to the east and turn towards the south-east across the bridge. You will find him at the crafters' market.''Take the cask to Bregedúr at the crafters' market in Celondim, south of here.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}, and thank my friend Brethilwen for knowing my intentions. I understand that Brethilwen was beset by goblins and that you fought many off to obtain this spirit. Know that it was for a worthy cause.'Fenton Marshley is concerned about the recent boom in the local marsh-fly population.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest will be cancelled if you complete or skip 'Intro: The Assault on Archet'.</rgb>Marsh-flies can be found near the lake east of Archet.

Fenton Marshley has asked you to hunt down the marsh-flies that plague Archet.Defeat marsh-flies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fenton Marshley is near the Hunter's Lodge, east of Archet.

You should return to Fenton Marshley for your reward.Talk to Fenton Marshley at the Hunter's Lodge<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest has been restored for Legendary Servers!</rgb>

'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. I've lived in Archet all my life and have hunted game throughout the forests since I was strong enough to wield a bow; but never before have I seen the marsh-flies grown to such a menace as they have now.

'There is clearly something wrong here and isn't simply wild growth.

'If you could kill some of the pests I would reward you for your efforts. And, ${PLAYER}, if you could find further information for me I would be indebted to you.''You'll find the flies make their nests and pestering grounds just surrounding the lake near the lodge.''Ah good, you have returned...and with tales of success no doubt!  

'Here then, take this as your reward.  Good luck in your adventures, ${PLAYER}.'Holly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Hugo Broadbelt of Michel Delving had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Hugo Broadbelt has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Hugo Broadbelt's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'Hands off that pie there! That's going to be part of my dinner tonight. Been looking forwards to eating it all day. You aren't getting a slice of it!

'Eh? Spoiled berries? I don't want none of that. Take that pie back to Holly in Hobbiton. Her home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

'Guess I'll have to wait a bit longer to have that pie with my dinner, eh?''Take that pie back to Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton. Can't believe I've been looking forwards to eating that all day, only to find it's gone bad!'Holly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Iris Chubb of Needlehole had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Iris Chubb has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Iris Chubb's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'Good day to you. I see you've noticed my pie over there. It's from Holly Hornblower, and I can hardly wait to eat it. I've been tempted to sneak a slice, but my husband would never forgive me if I did!

'What did you say? Goodness me, bad berries? How terrible. I'm glad now I didn't sneak a slice! Please take the pie back to Holly in Hobbiton. Her home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

'And let her know that when she gets a chance, I'd like another pie.''Goodness, I still can't believe that Holly's pie was made with bad berries. Well, nothing to be done about it now, I suppose. Please take the pie back to Holly in Hobbiton, if you don't mind.'Carlo Blagrove, innkeeper of The Bird and Baby, is entering the Four Farthings Brewing-moot.The Great Smials are in Tuckborough, to the east of Michel Delving. The Bird and Baby Inn is in Michel Delving, to the west of Tuckborough.

Carlo Blagrove has asked you to search the Great Smials for a recipe he thinks his great-grandfather might have hidden there.'Hallo there! Haven't seen you here before! Sit down, take a mug of my Blagrove's Brown! Good stuff, ain't it? Best you ever had? No? Ah well. You see, I've been entering the All-Farthing Brewing Moot every year like clockwork for nigh on fifty years now, and not one prize to my name!

'But this time, I think I got the smell of a best in show. See, I just heard that my old great-granddad -- a Took he was -- who ran the Bird and Baby in his day, won the Moot-prize most every year he entered! They say his Brown was the best ever, but it seems the recipe died with him, because the Bird just hasn't been able to compete since those days. I'm thinking he might have written down his recipe somewhere. If it would be anywhere, it would be in the Great Smials over in Tuckborough to the east of Michel Delving.

'I wonder... would you mind maybe going over there and take a look? If you find that old recipe, I'll give you the first taste of the new brew!''Ah yes! Here it is! What's this? A bit of honey? Special malt? Yes! That's the ticket! This will be our secret!

'In the meantime, here, have some of the old stuff on the house. It might not win any prizes, but it still goes down easy, don't it?'Tindr hopes the repairs to the canal in Thorin's Hall has restored the flow of water to Noglond, the way-station in the Vale of Thráin.Geitir is in Noglond, south on the road from Thorin's Halls.

Tindr has asked you to speak with Geitir in Noglond to learn if the flow of water in the canal has returned to normal.'I've got some complaints from Noglond, down in the Vale of Thráin to the south, that the canal hasn't been flowing the way it should. Hopefully that repair you made to the leak has solved that problem, as well.

'Could you go down to Noglond and talk to Geitir about the problem? He can tell you if the canal is back to normal. Just follow the road south as it curves through the Vale of Thráin, and you will eventually come upon Noglond.

'With the Dourhands stirring up trouble, we are so short on workhands.''Has the waterflow been restored? I should say not. It's just a trickle, really, when it should be a torrent!''Have you not been to Noglond yet?'Continue meeting the needs of the Shire-folk.Complete quests within the ShireBávor is an artificer tasked with repairing the great lock which opens access to the fabled Vault of the Mountain.The chest containing the second gear can be found on the south side of the goblin-infested ruins in the Vale of Thráin, south of Thorin's Halls and west of Noglond.

Bávor discovered the location of the second gear and has sent you to search for it, while he repairs the first gear.Find the missing second gearBávor is in Thorin's Hall.

Bávor will be pleased to begin working with the second gear.'That first gear has seen better days, but it's not beyond repair. I'll get to work on that, while you look for the second gear.

'According to the old records, the second gear was hidden in a chest in some old ruins to the south in the Vale of Thráin. The ruins are on the west side of the vale, off the road and across the Vale from Noglond. The records indicate that the chest is on the south side of the ruins.

'One thing you should be aware of, though, is that goblins have overrun those ruins. Be careful.''According to the old records, the second gear was hidden in a chest in some old ruins to the south in the Vale of Thráin. The ruins are on the west side of the vale, off the road and across the Vale from Noglond. The records indicate that the chest is on the south side of the ruins.''Aye! This is it! Wait... does this actually fit anywhere? How about here? Ah, I'll work it out eventually. For now, we must find the other gears!'Grímkell thinks the goblins have occupied a large ruin, a former Dourhand city, to the south-west of Noglond.The Blue-crag Chieftain is at the large goblin camp in ruins to the south-west of Noglond. 

Embarrassed by his previous skepticism, Grímkell has asked you to raid the goblins in their camp and slay their chieftain. He suggested you take allies.Defeat goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grímkell is in Noglond, north-east of the goblin encampment.

You should return to Grímkell with news of your victory.'I think I know what's going on. There are some sprawling old ruins just south-west of here. I think the goblins have occupied those ruins.

'I'd be sorry to have to send a message up to Thorin's Halls or off to Gondamon for help. I guess I'd feel like Vífill must have. They would laugh and leave it lie.

'I wonder if you and some friends, perhaps, could deal with these goblins? If you could raid their camp in those ruins and defeat their chieftain, I wouldn't have to ask for help from elsewhere. I'd gather some allies, though -- the camp is likely to be well-guarded.''Ha! Good work. I'm sorry I ever doubted Vífill, but who would have known that goblins would actually dare to enter the Vale of Thráin?''Search the goblin-camp in the ruins to the south-west for the Blue Crag Chieftain and put him out of our misery.'Wolves overran Dora Brownlock's farm and present a threat to Waymeet and the surrounding communities.The wolf den is off the road north of Dora Brownlock's farm and Waymeet.

Dora Brownlock is grateful that you rescued her chickens from the wolves, but she is afraid to go home until she is sure that the wolves will no longer trouble her. She has asked you to go to the wolf den and put an end to the threat.Defeat wolves at wolf den (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dora Brownlock is at the centre of Waymeet.

Dora Brownlock will be pleased to hear that you have done something about the wolves threatening the area.'I don't know that I can go home until I know those wolves are gone for good! What if they come for my babies again?

'You were so brave to rescue my little darlings... I'm sure you could do something about the wolves. The awful beasts that attacked my farm came from the north... there must be a wolf den somewhere among the hills north of my farm!

'Oh, please do hurry! I really would like to go home soon.''If you're looking for the wolf-den, you want to head back to the road -- the den is on the other side of the road from my camp. I've been watching them, trying to learn which of the wolves is their leader.''The wolf-den is somewhere north of my farm, ${PLAYER}! I simply can't return home while they are still wandering around.''You haven't taken care of the wolf problem around Waymeet for my friend Dora yet? You'd best get started on that!''Thank you for your efforts, ${PLAYER}! We won't need to fear these wolves now that you've killed their leader!

'What? You didn't see their leader at the wolf den? He won't be an ordinary pack-leader, that's for sure. The real leader of the wolves must be in hiding. Until we do something about the chief wolf, no one in the area will be safe!'Pervinca Took made the mistake of helping her cousins Isembard and Imbert play a trick on the aged Adelard Took. Pervinca sneaked off with the chapter he wrote for the Yearbook of Tuckborough, and Isembard hid it.Pervinca thought her cousins Isembard and Imbert Took could be found near the Great Willow east of the Great Smials in Tuckborough.

Pervinca asked you to find her cousins Isembard and Imbert, who went to retrieve Adelard's chapter of the Yearbook, and see what is taking him so long.Speak to Isembard TookBring Adelard's chapter back to Pervinca Took in the Great Smials.

Having survived Isembard's grand idea for getting the satchel with Adelard's chapter down from the tree, you finally have the chapter in hand to bring back to Pervinca.'I need your help! I made a terrible mistake and listened to Isembard and Imbert, my fool cousins. You see, old Adelard is always lecturing us young Tooks on the history of the family, and well, it does get tiring. My cousins decided to play a trick on him and convinced me to sneak away with the latest chapter Adelard wrote for the Yearbook of Tuckborough.

'Now I'm worried about the trouble I'm going to get into! Isembard, though, went out to get the chapter from where he hid it, but hasn't returned yet!

'I think he said he hid it in a tall tree east of the Great Smials in Tuckborough. Could you go there and see what is taking him so long?''Oh, good day to you! Are you here about that chapter of Adelard's as well? Best be talking to Isembard, he's the smarter of us two! I'm just here to lend him a hand, if I can.''Isembard and Imbert should be near that big willow east of the Great Smials in Tuckborough. Please hurry, I don't know how long it'll be until Adelard discovers that his chapter is missing!''What? Pervinca sent a Bounder out here? She is such a worrier! There's nothing to fear, old Imbert and me will have that chapter of Adelard's in two shakes.

'See, we hid the chapter in a satchel in the tree, but the branch we climbed up on broke off. We have been here scratching our heads on how to get it down... but you just gave me a grand idea!''I thought that satchel would never fall from that tree. But, fortunately, old Isembard's plan worked. I always said he was the smarter of the two of us, and this just proved it again!''See, I told you we'd have that satchel out of the tree quick enough! You'd best take it to Pervinca.

'Still, I wish we had hung on to it a bit longer... we're sure to hear another of old Adelard's speeches now.''Good, you've found it! Now to sneak this back into the library before Adelard notices it's gone missing. My thanks! You've saved me from a host of troubles!'If the Uruks newly-arrived in Swanfleet are truly in the employ of the Wizard Saruman, you must learn what you can of their purpose and why he sent them to this land.Tegwyn has overheard much of your conversation concerning Saruman and the Uruks.Talk to Tegwyn in the alley between buildings in MosswardMeneldir is in an alley between buildings in Mossward.Talk to Meneldir in the alley between buildings in MosswardThe road runs north-east past Mossward and on into Enedwaith. Did the Uruks come from that direction?Search for a sign of the Uruks where the road enters Swanfleet from EnedwaithThe bodies of Uruks lie on the road where it enters Swanfleet from Enedwaith.Examine one of the dead Uruks along the roadMeneldir will want to examine the weapons carried by these Uruks.Collect fallen Uruk swords along the road from Enedwaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Meneldir is in the Mossward town square, waiting for you to return with news of the border with Enedwaith.Bring the Uruk swords to Meneldir in the Mossward town squareSkardí Bendblade will be interested in the Uruk swords you recovered.

Skardí is always hard at work in his Mossward shop.'This much we know for certain: the Uruks that have come to Swanfleet believe they do so at Saruman's command. That means the White Wizard cannot be trusted.'

Meneldir falls silent.

'We are being observed, ${PLAYER}. Someone listens to our conversation.''We are being observed, ${PLAYER}. Someone listens to our conversation.''What? I didn't hear anything I wasn't supposed to hear! You told me that an adventurer is supposed to remain watchful for the needs of all good folk, and how can I do that if I don't keep my eyes and ears open?

'All right, maybe you didn't say EXACTLY that, but I'm sure it's true all the same! If a Wizard is sending goblins and Uruks to attack Mossward, shouldn't we know about it?'

You tell Tegwyn that the best way he can help the people of his village is to keep their spirits up and to help them prepare the defences.

'Sure. I'll do what I can, but I'll have you know I expect to be given more dangerous quests in the days ahead! I am an adventurer now, after all, and you and Meneldir are going to need all the help you can get, especially if we're up against Wizards and their lackeys!''I expect to be given more dangerous quests in the days ahead! I am an adventurer now, after all, and you and Meneldir are going to need all the help you can get, especially if we're up against Wizards and their lackeys!''I think you handled that pretty well, my friend... better than I would have, at any rate. I have never had much patience for children.

'I plan to search further afield for some clue to Saruman's purpose: why would he send goblins and Uruks to attack Mossward? I can't understand it.

'Will you travel to the east, where the road from Enedwaith enters Swanfleet? The raiding party may have come from there, and left behind some trace of their passage. I will see you again when we have both returned.''Will you travel to the east, where the road from Enedwaith enters Swanfleet? The raiding party may have come from there, and left behind some trace of their passage. I will see you again when we have both returned.''Will you travel to the east, where the road from Enedwaith enters Swanfleet? The raiding party may have come from there, and left behind some trace of their passage. I will see you again when we have both returned.''Will you travel to the east, where the road from Enedwaith enters Swanfleet? The raiding party may have come from there, and left behind some trace of their passage. I will see you again when we have both returned.''You bring interesting tidings, ${PLAYER}. It sounds to me as if the Uruks quarrelled among themselves after they arrived in Swanfleet. But for what purpose? The warband may have been much larger when it travelled from Enedwaith, and divided into two or more raiding parties when it crossed into Swanfleet. Perhaps the decision to attack Mossward was made not by the Wizard but by the Uruks themselves? It is curious.

'As for the swords you collected, perhaps Skardí can melt them down and put them to better use than their former bearers.''Bring the swords you collected inside to Skardí. He should be able to melt them down and put them to better use than their former bearers.''More Uruk blades? I didn't ask for these, ${PLAYER}.

'Well, Meneldir is right, I suppose. I'll melt them down and turn them into arms for the defence of Mossward. No one will want to use them as they are now, but metal is metal, in my experience.'Danger presses upon Bree-land from all sides, foreshadowing the ascension of a great darkness. You are called to stand against the Shadow. Your continued efforts on behalf of Bree-land will be rewarded.Complete additional quests in Bree-land.Complete quests within Bree-landBuilder Earur has asked you to recover the tools he lost when a mad boar overturned his cart on the road south of Archet.Builder Earur's cart was overturned south of Archet, near the gate to Combe. Builder Earur is in Archet, north of the overturned cart.

Builder Earur has asked you to recover the toolbox he left in the wreckage of his cart, overturned by a mad boar south of Archet.'Working with wood has always been my trade, so I thought to put my hands to the rebuilding of Archet. I had loaded up my tools and set out, when suddenly this mad boar came out of nowhere and overturned my cart!

'It was all my son Borin and I could do to make it here to Archet, and we had to leave the tools in the wreckage of the cart! If you head south to the gate that leads to Combe, you might be able to recover my toolbox. I'd really appreciate it, and the folk of Archet are sure to be better for it as well -- the sooner I can get started, the sooner this town will be back to the way it was!

'Watch out for that boar, though. You might be able to get my toolbox without attracting his attention, but you'd need more luck than I have to manage it!''You have my thanks, ${PLAYER} -- now Borin and I can get to work rebuilding this town. Take these coins for your trouble.'Postman Took of Tuckborough has asked you to deliver a satchel to Hobbiton.Postman Grubb can be found west of the centre of Hobbiton, north of Tuckborough.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Grubb in Hobbiton as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty and don't let the satchel get wet!Collect the satchel from Postman Took's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'There's been talk that Postmaster Proudfoot is trying to speed up delivery times for the Quick Post service, but I'm really swamped with mail and haven't been able to hit the times he wants.

'Lobelia's Birthday is fast-approaching, though curiously enough very few pieces of mail are postmarked for Bag End. Instead, there's mail going everywhere else! I think hobbits throughout Tuckborough are writing to their friends to complain about Lobelia's new presents proposal, if you ask me.

'There on the table you will find a satchel of mail to be delivered to Postman Grubb in Hobbiton for sorting. He can be found west of the centre of Hobbiton, to the north, if you're interested. Watch out for nosey hobbits and don't let the mail get wet!''The satchel for Hobbiton is over there on the table. Take it to Postman Grubb as quickly as possible! And remember, let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty!'Postman Redsmith of Needlehole has asked you to deliver a satchel to Michel Delving.Postmaster Proudfoot can be found in Michel Delving, near Town Hole. Town Hole is surrounded by hedges.

Deliver the satchel to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty and don't let the satchel get wet!Collect the satchel from Postman Redsmith's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'The dwarves here don't understand the importance of the Quick Post service and insist that letters and packages can be delivered whenever it is most convenient. That is preposterous, of course! Imagine if Postmaster Proudfoot allowed us that degree of laziness!

'Speaking of the Postmaster, I have a bundle of mail that needs to go to Michel Delving. If you are going that way, I'd appreciate if you dropped it off with Postmaster Proudfoot by Town Hole. Town Hole is surrounded by hedges, if you haven't visited it before.

'Go at once and let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty! You'll have a long walk ahead of you, especially if you head south to Waymeet and then cut west across the fields to Michel Delving. Keep the satchel dry, even when travelling through Rushock Bog!''The satchel for Michel Delving is over there on the table. Take it to Postmaster Proudfoot by Town Hole and let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty!'Postmaster Proudfoot of Michel Delving has asked you to deliver a satchel to Tuckborough.Postman Took can be found at the centre of Tuckborough.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Took in Tuckborough as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty, and keep the satchel dry!Collect the satchel from Postmaster Proudfoot's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'I've received word that you delivered that package to Postman Twofoot at Waymeet in a timely manner -- he was very impressed, and I must tell you that I am as well!

'The Quick Post service is becoming respectable again! Speedy deliveries, mail that you can count on... this is a happy day for this old postmaster!

'If you'd still like to help out, well, there's always work to be done! There on the table you will find a satchel for Postman Took at the centre of Tuckborough. You know how this works now, my friend -- avoid nosey hobbits, keep the satchel dry, and make haste! The Quick Post service will set new standards for speedy delivery of the mail!''The satchel for Tuckborough is over there on the table. Take it to Postman Took as quickly as possible, and let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty! With your help, the Quick Post service will once again live up to its name!'Gwenfor Mellion is concerned for the wild land surrounding Glyn Helyg.Gwenfor Mellion tells you the plants are wilting, and a shadow looming over the wild in the forest to the south-east.

The forest she speaks of can be found south-east of Glyn Helyg. You can follow the road out of the village.Investigate the corrupted plantGwenfor awaits your report. Gwenfor can be found in Glyn Helyg.Talk to GwenforGwenfor Mellion wants you to go deeper into the forest and confirm her suspicions.

Continue further down the path to the south-east across the bridge. A faint shadow lingers around still waters.Venture deeper into the forestThe shadow has revealed itself.Defeat the corrupted beastThe corruption deeper in the forest has gone on to affect even the beasts.

You should tell Gwenfor in Glyn Helyg immediately.Talk to GwenforNuddo Sutchic can be found in Lintrev to the north.

Gwenfor has asked you to share your findings with them.'Could you spare a moment? A strange shadow lingers in the wild... I have observed its effects for quite some time now. The plants are wilting and the crop does not survive until the harvest.

'This shadow spreads and harms everything it touches. Since you happened to survive the journey here, I'm hoping that you might take a look around and try to gather more information for me.''That is troubling to see. It is as I feared. The corruption has begun to take hold. I've never travelled as deep as you have. The corruption on this plant looks even more severe.

'You should travel deeper into the forest. If my suspicions are correct, we may find a more potent corruption exists.''The shadow touches the beasts of the land now? It is more dire than I thought. First the plants and now the animals. If we allow this corruption to go unabated, it could cause a great strife in the Stoor-vales.

'My friend in Lintrev has told me similar stories. In fact, he speaks of black riders passing through. I suspect he could tell you more. Go to Lintrev and find Nuddo Sutchic. Regale them of what has transpired and give them this sample of coltsfoot.

'Lintrev is north of here. Just follow the road east out of Glyn Helyg.''The corruption on this coltsfoot plant is troubling indeed. You say Gwenfor sent you?

'She was right. This might explain the recent unrest in Cobshollow. Ever since the black riders passed through, the situation here in the Stoor-vales grows more and more bleak. Our very way of life is being threatened.'Coruwen has noticed the corruption of the surrounding plant life. Help her drive it back.Coruwen has asked you to travel to Cobshollow to the south of Lintrev to collect samples of corrupted plant life.Collect corrupted coltsfoot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect corrupted feldwort (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Coruwen awaits your return with the plant samples in LintrevTalk to CoruwenCoruwen has asked you to grind the corrupted samples into a powder.

Coruwen's mortar and pestle can be found nearby, next to her work table in Lintrev.Coruwen instructs you on how to mix the ingredients in the mixing bowl by her work table in Lintrev.Talk to CoruwenCoruwen has asked you to mix the samples in with the ingredients she has prepared.

The mixing bowl can be found near Coruwen in Lintrev.Mix the ingredients in the bowlThe cleansing draught seems to be complete. Bring it to Coruwen in Lintrev.Talk to CoruwenCoruwen has asked you to spread the cleansing draught along a running water source.

She has suggested a waterfall to the south of Lintrev that runs into the Wadewater. The people of Stoor-vales often use this watering spot. You should look for their items.The cleansing solution has been poured into a water source that runs into the Wadewater. This should help with the shadow's corruption for now.

Coruwen can be found in Lintrev. You should tell her the deed is done.Talk to Coruwen'Are you the one who helped Nuddo? We have both been working tirelessly to combat the spread. I found myself here in the Stoor-vales in my travels through Eregion. It was this very shadow that led me here, and that has kept me here.

'If you could help me, perhaps I could create a draught that could ease the pain on the land. I will first need samples of the blighted plant life. The corruption is strongest in the dark nest Cobshollow.

'Travel to Cobshollow and find samples of the corrupted plant life... but be cautious! What lurks within is dark and twisted.''I had anticipated a further progressed corruption, but these plants have transformed into something else entirely. We must act quickly if we are to fight this corruption.

'You will find my mortar and pestle by my work table. Take the samples and grind them into a workable powder.''Good. Next you need to take the ground powder and incorporate it into the mixing bowl. I have gathered several ingredients in the mixing bowl already. My work table is nearby.

'Take the samples and mix them with the ingredients I have prepared.'Coruwen examines the draught with an approving look.

'You have done well. This draught should be enough to stave off the corruption for now.

'You will need to find a suitable area to spread the draught. A source of running water should prove effective in spreading the remedy throughout the land.

'Take this phial and find a waterfall. There should be one to the south of Lintrev that runs into the Wadewater that the people of the Stoor-vales often visit to clean their things. That should be quite effective.''This should help in warding off the shadow's corruption for now. But I fear it may not be enough. Nonetheless, this gives us more time to come up with a permanent solution.

'We have done all we can with what we have. That is all anyone can hope for. I hope that whatever looms out there spreading this shadow will soon meet its end.'Woodcutters from Combe moving further into the Chetwood in search of quality lumber are seeking protection from the local wildlife.The wolf-den is set in the cliff wall north-east of the lumber camp.

Woodcutter Taylor Green is concerned that the wolves roaming the woods to the north-east may be a threat to the woodcutters and has asked you to cull their numbers.Defeat wolves at the wolf-den (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Woodcutter Taylor Green waits at the lumber camp to the south-west, north of the guard-house.

As Woodcutter Green requested, you put the fear of Men into the wolves of the Chetwood. He will be pleased to hear of your success.'Combe has always relied on this lumber camp for her livelihood, and now the people of Archet will be relying on us to supply the wood to rebuild their town, I expect. There's no shortage of work, that much is certain!

'We'll need to start taking down some of the trees to the north-east, along the cliffs, but there's a wolf-den up that way that endangers our workers!

'Could you deal with those wolves for me? It's not safe to chop down trees near there, and I'm afraid we might lose some of our best loggers. Follow the cliff wall. You'll see the wolves, or they'll see you.''You took care of the wolves! That will make harvesting the trees by that den much safer. Rebuilding the burned buildings in Archet will require more wood than we have, and that's only one village!

'I don't think the Blackwolds have the numbers to try anything funny around Combe, but there's still Staddle. Too many raids, and we'll need to cut down the whole Chetwood to make the repairs!''The wolf-den is north-east of here. Just follow the bend of the cliff wall, and you'll see it. It's not far.'Due to his bad leg, Farmer Sandson cannot deliver the eggs Gammer Tunnelly in Tuckborough is waiting for.Gammer Tunnelly can be found in the centre of Tuckborough.

When you returned from delivering the eggs to Holly Hornblower, he asked you to make another delivery to Gammer Tunnelly in Tuckborough. Be careful that the rooster doesn't see you with the eggs, as he will let out a call that will upset the hens.Pickup the egg basketAvoid the roosterGammer Tunnelly was grateful for the eggs. You should return to Farmer Sandson and let him know the eggs were delivered without incident.'My thanks again for taking that last batch of eggs to Holly in Hobbiton, but I've got another cook waiting on some eggs, if you've got the time to deliver them!

'Gammer Tunnelly in Tuckborough is a fine lady... misses her grandson terribly though. If you could deliver the basket of eggs right there to her, I'd really appreciate it!

'Remember, don't let the rooster see you. I can't have the hens all upset by him and not laying!''Go ahead and grab that basket of eggs there. There should be enough in there for Gammer Tunnelly.''Oh, thank you again for bringing me those eggs. Please give my thanks to Farmer Sandson and let him know I hope his leg heals soon!''Gammer Tunnelly is such a sweet, old hobbit. I'm glad she got the eggs. You have my thanks again, ${PLAYER}. When my leg gets better, maybe I can do a favour for you, eh?'Explore the old places left behind by the Elves as they abandoned Edhelion and moved further south to Duillond.NOT USEDThe ruins of Nen Hilith speak of more peaceful times when the Elves dwelt by the lake and contemplated the world that was. Now, evil wolves stalk the ruins, casting a dark shadow over the beautiful memory of the place.In the days when Tham Gelair stood whole, it was a place of celebration and ceremony for the Elves of Ered Luin. Now it is a wretched ruin, a shattered memory of better days.Limael's Vineyard was once the chief source of wine-grapes for the Elves of Ered Luin, but goblins have since taken over the once-peaceful vale. Nevertheless, the Elves still harvest the grapes when they ripen, as well as the trespassing goblins.Dol Ringwest was once a place of great beauty, home to many Elves. Now it is a decayed and broken ruin.This tower overlooking the Lhûn once guarded docks where ships would carry wood and wine from Edhelion to Mithlond. Now it has been abandoned to the wild.A while ago, Esilia Took had made plans with her cousin, Gerebert, to share a meal, but he has not shown up. As Gerebert is not one to miss a meal, Esilia is terribly concerned.Gerebert Took's house is west of Tuckborough, at the end of the road.

Esilia has asked you to go to Gerebert Took's house and learn why he is late for dinner.Search for Gerebert TookThe inside of Gerebert Took's home is empty and unused. You should search the house for some information that will explain where Gerebert has gone.Search Gerebert Took's homeEsilia Took can be found near the centre of Tuckborough.

As you entered Gerebert Took's bedroom, you spotted a journal on a table on the other side of the room. It may contain clues as to where Gerebert has gotten off to. You should take it to Esilia Took.Read Gerebert's journal'Oh, hello there. I'm sorry I'm not more friendly today, but I'm a bit concerned about my cousin, Gerebert.

'You see, a while ago I wrote in my calendar that Gerebert and I were to share supper. Today was the day, but Gerebert hasn't shown up. My cousin isn't one to miss a meal, so I'm more than a little troubled.

'Would you mind going over to his house and see what is taking him so long? I would go, but I've got a pot on the stove right now. His house is west of Tuckborough -- just follow the road west out of the town proper and you'll see it.''Gerebert's house is west of Tuckborough, at the end of the road and just down the hill.

'If he's not there, feel free to go on in, he won't mind. When you find him, tell him he shouldn't have taken so long, I was getting concerned!''Gerebert's house was empty? Here, let me take a look at that journal of his. I'm sure he'll be all manner of embarassed to know I've read his journal, but I think it's important we know where he's gotten off to!'The ruins of Gwâl Cruban are no place to wander into unprepared. The turtles who have made it their home have sharp beaks and sharper tempers.Gwendrian has asked you to look for her companion in Gwâl Cruban.

Gwâl Cruban is in northern Swanfleet.Look for InnathronYou found Innathron in Gwâl Cruban, however, he has managed to get his foot stuck in a small sink hole.

You should try to free Innathron.You should try to free Innathron's footInnathron is waiting to thank you for freeing him.

Innathron is in Gwâl Cruban, in northern Swanfleet.Speak to Innathron'Mae govannen. Over the water, a bit away from here, is Gwâl Cruban, home to vicious turtles whose beaks are strong enough to bite through - well, I shudder to think on it. My companion, Innathron, wandered that way yesterday to look at the ruins and has yet to return. Please keep watch for him, if you are heading that way.''Well met, ${CLASS}. You are just in time. I am afraid that I have gotten my foot trapped here. I have managed to fend off the turtles thus far, but help is appreciated.''Freed! I can make my way back to Echad Terthas on my own now. I thank you for your assistance.'Thinglaer, an Elf lingering at Celondim, seeks to restore a few of the old Elven places before he departs for the Grey Havens.Tham Gelair lies to the west of Celondim.

Thinglaer has asked you to go to the ruins of Tham Gelair and slay some of the foul creatures there.Defeat foul creatures in Tham Gelair (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tham Gelair is west of Celondim.

Thinglaer has asked you to place his token within the Elf-ruins west of Celondim.Thinglaer is at Celondim, east of Tham Gelair.

You should return to Thinglaer and let him know that you have done as he asked.'This is a beautiful land, is it not? I wandered it often in my youth -- but places that were once fair have long since fallen into decay. Some of the older ruins have even become habitations for foul creatures that gnaw at the edges of our lands.

'My brothers and I have set to ourselves the task of cleansing a few of these places before we leave. To this end, I have in my possession a token given to me by Elrond Halfelven long ago. It is imbued with a light that creatures of evil find painful to bear.

'The ruins of Tham Gelair west of Celondim have become infested with foul creatures. If you could slay any you find within, and then place this token there, its light should keep them from slinking back in the night.''Your news gladdens my heart, ${PLAYER}, and I am eager to walk among the ruins as I once did, with the sky over my head and the sun on my face. The cool shadows cast by the walls will no longer be a reminder of the Shadow in the East, but of respite and restoration.''You must purge the fell beasts from the land.'Lolo Wendingway mentioned that Bree-town is a-flutter with rumours of shadows growing and refugees pouring in from the south. He told you to seek out Second-watcher Heathstraw if you were looking to continue your assistance of Bree-land.Second-watcher Heathstraw can be found near the Boar Fountain in the centre of the Market Square in Bree-town.

Lolo Wendingway mentioned that Second-watcher Heathstraw may have some knowledge of people needing things done throughout Bree.'You've been a big help to me, ${PLAYER}. Something about you tells me you could be a great help to many. If you are looking to further your charitable nature, you may want to speak with Second-watcher Heathstraw in Bree-town.

'Heathstraw is very much in the know of problems facing Bree. What with the refugees coming from the south and all the whispers of the rising dark, I think he's got a fair share of details to keep track of, poor fellow.

'You can find him through the Staddle-gate of Bree standing near the Boar Fountain in the Market Square.''Lolo? Used to come here often, he did. Good stout little fellow, good barker and good seller he is. Strange for a hobbit it's true, but then again they say that most hobbits living 'round here is queer.

'His information is correct though, Bree's seen its share of new blood recently, and not all have been of your quality.

'If you need work, I am certain that I can find you something.'Esilia Took discovered from her cousin's journal that Gerebert was dared to hide on the waggon of a local pipeweed farmer, Longo Burrow, as it went east. She is becoming more concerned, as the entry in the journal was written some time ago, and Longo Burrow's farm is not that far away.Longo Burrow is at his farm on the Stock Road, east out of Tuckborough.

Upset greatly by her cousin's disappearance, Esilia Took has asked you to speak with Longo Burrow to learn if he has seen Gerebert.'Oh dear. Well, it seems Gerebert may have gotten himself into a bit of a pickle. The last entry in his journal says that our fool cousin Pippin dared him to hide on one of Longo Burrow's waggons going east. The strangest thing is that this was written some time ago -- Pippin has been away in Hobbiton -- and Longo's farm isn't that far away.

'Hmm, perhaps you should speak with Longo to see if he's seen Gerebert. Longo's farm is on the Stock Road east out of Tuckborough.

'The more I think about this, the more concerned I get for poor Gerebert!''What? You come a-calling about some fool Took? Well. I might have seen him, but I ain't going to tell you what I've seen for nothing. No, you're going to have to do me a favour first!''Have you found Gerebert yet? Oh please find him!'Hal Hornblower wants dirty filth. Hal can be found near the stable in the centre of Hobbiton.You have accepted a task to acquire dirty filth for the Bounders of the Shire. They have deputized Hal Hornblower to collect the items near the stables in Hobbiton.Wanted: Dirty filth from insects and spiders infesting the Shire. Bounders are looking for proof of those who are assisting them in keeping the Shire safe. Deliver the filth to Hal Hornblower at Hobbiton centre.Wanted: Dirty filth from insects and spiders infesting the Shire.'Not certain what the Bounders are going to do with all this, but I will keep collecting it so long as they need the proof.

'Thank you, kindly.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Hal Hornblower wants matted fur. Hal can be found near the stable in the centre of Hobbiton.You have accepted a task to acquire matted fur for the bounders of the Shire. They have deputized Hal Hornblower to collect the items near the stables in Hobbiton.Wanted: Matted fur from the beasts prowling the Shire. Bounders are looking for proof of those who are assisting them in keeping the Shire safe. Deliver the furs to Hal Hornblower at Hobbiton centre.Wanted: Matted fur from the beasts prowling the Shire.'These appear to be the furs that the Bounders wanted. So many strange creatures making their way about the Shire these days.

'Thank you, kindly.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Shirriff Smallburrow believes you should become acquainted with the other Shirriffs and Bounders.Bounder Chubb can be found on duty near the road leading into Needlehole, due north of Michel Delving, north-west of Hobbiton.

Shirriff Smallburrow has asked you to travel to Needlehole and offer your services to Bounder Chubb.'Welcome to Hobbiton, ${PLAYER}. It's always nice to see new folk, and I think it's important to strengthen the bonds of friendship. I think you should call on Bounder Chubb in Needlehole and see if he has any work that needs doing. Needlehole has become such a busy place that it may require its own Shirriff soon!

'Needlehole is due north of Michel Delving, some distance past Little Delving, north-west of here. Don't be surprised if you find some dwarves there -- Needlehole is on the road to Ered Luin, and we've had more dwarf-traders coming through that way of late. 

'You'll probably find Bounder Chubb on duty near the entrance to town.''Please stop by Needlehole and introduce yourself to Bounder Chubb. Needlehole is north-west of Hobbiton, beyond Michel Delving and on the edge of the Rushock Bog.''Robin Smallburrow sent you? Hullo then. We may have a few things for you to do around here.

'These dwarves are mostly fine, steady, law-abiding folk, if a bit touchy at times, but some of them... well, let's just say a few of these dwarves are not good neighbours at all. Not at all!'Lolo Wendingway mentioned that the people of Staddle are dealing with some peculiar goings-on and told you to visit Watcher Redweed for more information.Watcher Redweed can be found in Staddle centre.

Lolo Wendingway advised you to seek out Watcher Redweed to help out with troubles brewing in the surrounding areas.'Staddle is a tranquil place, or normally so. Recently however, the guards and constables have been fearful of the Midgewater Marsh and the tall-folk moving into ruins in the south. 

'If you continue following the road to the south, you'll find Staddle centre. Talk to Watcher Redweed there and tell them that I sent you on to help!''Hullo there! You've come from Lolo, have you?

'You've come to the right place then friend. There is much happening around Staddle that needs attention and there are too few guards and constables to reach them all.'Mason Thorne's ledger revealed the location of the old Hanging Tree. Now you can search for Ted Pickthorn's treasure.The south-easternmost stump in the stump-field -- the one closest to Staddle Falls -- was once the Hanging Tree.

After reading through the ledger you recovered for him, Mason Thorne was able to point you to the location of the Hanging Tree.Ted Pickthorn is on the east side of Combe.

Following Thorne's instructions, you found the stump of the Hanging Tree. You dug up something buried beneath the stump, but it is not what Ted Pickthorn had led you to believe. His father's treasure appears to be a pair of old boots.'Let me just... hmmm... find the right page. Ah! Here we go. I see, I see. So, you stand in the field of stumps and... hmmm... take this many paces... and then that many strides... of course! I remember! The Hanging Tree was the south-easternmost tree in that bunch. It was standing there closest to the Staddle Falls!

'Now just... hmmm... go back to that stump-field, and you'll find that thing you wanted. What was it you wanted, again? You were digging for something, right? Here, take this pick-axe, it'll make it easier to dig. Least I could do, you finding my ledger and all!''You found out which stump was the Hanging Tree? Well, what're you standing here for? Go dig up me dad's treasure and bring it back here!''I gave you what... hmmm... you wanted to know, didn't I? You should go find... hmmm... whatever it was.''Did you find what you... hmmm... wanted? It looks from your face like you... hmmm... did. Good for you!''Wh-what are these? These boots were buried beneath the Hanging Tree? My dad was a villain to the end! "Wealth enough to keep you warm and shod." Shod, indeed!

'Wait... there's something rattling around inside the heel of this one.' Taking a knife from his pocket, Ted slices into the heel, and gold pieces tumble out into his waiting palm.

'Well, I'll be! My dear old dad told me true! "Wealth enough to keep you warm and shod," indeed! You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}! With this money, I'll be able to get a new start. I'll do better than my dear old dad, you wait and see!'A stranger to Archet spoke with Jon Brackenbrook seeking heroes.Lizbeth Honeymeade is the proprietor of The Comb and Wattle Inn in Combe, south of Archet.

Jon Brackenbrook said you were to meet the grim stranger in Combe. He recommended that you speak with the innkeeper, Lizbeth Honeymeade, who can tell you what room the stranger is staying in.Toradan's room is at the end of the hall at the top of the stairs across the common room.

You have come to The Comb and Wattle Inn, as instructed, and spoken to the proprietor. Lizbeth Honeymeade told you that the man who sent you the message, Toradan, is waiting for you in his room.'The man who came through the village -- he reminded me of Strider in his behaviour -- said he was looking for "the Hero of Archet." I can only assume that he spoke of you!

'He said the matter was most urgent, and that if I saw you, I was to direct you to The Comb and Wattle Inn, where he will be waiting for you. The Comb and Wattle is in the centre of Combe to the south.

'He seemed most grim to me. I would travel to Combe immediately and speak with the innkeeper, Lizbeth Honeymeade. She should know where to find this man.''Lizbeth runs a fine establishment in Combe. Head there now and speak with her.''Oh my. Look here, a real live hero! It's not often we get such respectable folk through here.

'My, how my tongue runs on! Toradan told me to send you upstairs to his room as soon as you arrived. The stairs are across the room there, and Toradan's is the door at the end of the hall. He said you shouldn't delay none.''Keep it quiet that I have one of them Northmen here. The Comb and Wattle is normally a nice place.''The Hero of Archet, I suppose? I am pleased to finally meet you. I am sorry for the cryptic summons, but I dared not betray my whereabouts to just anyone.

'There is much we need to discuss. Will you hear me?'The stranger that summoned you was a kinsman of Amdir who is seeking the missing Ranger.Constable Underhill can be found outside The Comb and Wattle Inn in Combe.

Toradan has asked you to speak with Constable Underhill to learn ways of finding the Blackwolds' hideout. He is certain Amdir will be found among them.Many of the scattered Blackwolds dwell in the hills east of Combe.

Following Toradan's advice, you spoke with Constable Underhill about the Blackwold brigands. The hobbit constable suggests that you search amongst the camp-fires of the Blackwolds to the east of Combe for one of the brigand agent's letters.Search a Blackwold recruit's packConstable Underhill awaits your return near Combe centre, outside The Comb and Wattle Inn.

Searching through a pack found near a small encampment of Blackwolds, you found a letter from the Blackwold agent. You should return to Constable Underhill with the letter.'Thank you for your aid, ${PLAYER}. My kindred and I were driven from the Bounds of the Shire by the Nazgûl of Mordor. They pursued us eastward and slew many of us. It was my goal to join Amdir, but I have heard rumour of his fate in Archet. They say he was stabbed with a morgul-knife and led off by some evil Men -- the ones who lent the Blackwolds aid. There are few left now with power over such wounds, and those that I know of dwell some distance from here. We must find Amdir, and quickly, if we are to save him.

'He is likely being held by the Blackwolds somewhere in the Chetwood. We must find a way to enter their lair and free him, but first we must find them. Speak with Constable Underhill... he may be of help. You can usually find him outside, near The Comb and Wattle.

'Once you have learned of the Blackwolds' lair and believe you can gain entry, return to me. Hurry, before it is too late.''You should speak with Constable Underhill near The Comb and Wattle. He may have some thoughts on how to discover the Blackwolds' hideout.''Toradan sent you, did he? It's good to have the Hero of Archet on our side!' The hobbit lowers his voice. 'There's still a Blackwold agent in town. We think he's trying to rebuild the band from among the local ruffians and bullies. We need proof, though. A letter or parchment would do, if it came from the agent himself.

'Many of the brigands hole up in the Chetwood. Follow the road east, until you come to the guard-house, where Constable Wren is stationed. From there, head north and look for the brigands' watch-fires scattered through the wood. Search their packs for signs of their summons.

'Let me know right away if you find anything... we need to know what they're up to!''The Blackwolds have taken up residence in the Chetwood to the east. You had best begin your search there.''The Blackwolds have taken up residence north of the guard-house, east of Combe. You will most likely find them there.''Hallo! What's this? Ellie Cutleaf! Well, I should have guessed. She's smart and disreputable, by all accounts... and she's just the sort who might lead us to the Blackwold agent.

'She won't lead you to this Amdir fellow, I don't think, but it's a start. We must gain access to the leader somehow. He'll have the answers we seek.'Mundo Sackville-Baggins has demanded that Mayor Whitfoot pay compensation to his family for Mundo's recent bad experiences, and the mayor is at a loss as to what to do.Lobelia Sackville-Baggins is at Bag End, north of Hobbiton.

Mayor Whitfoot has decided to take a stand and refuse Mundo Sackville-Baggins' demand for compensation, but a sudden lack of time has required him to send you to break the news to Mundo's aunt, Lobelia.'I've thought about Mundo's demand that I pay compensation for his ill treatment in Bree-land, ${PLAYER}, and I'm not going to do it! We simply can't afford to pay money to satisfy a single hobbit for an experience that was his own fault to begin with.

'The Sackville-Bagginses have never liked me, either. I think it was one of them that started calling me "Flourdumpling" after the roof of Town Hole gave way and buried me in chalk, you know. I don't mind when the Shirriffs call me that, but from the Sackville-Bagginses it is just too much.

'The time has come to take a stand! I will not be bullied by the Sackville-Bagginses any longer -- they can't push me around, and I don't mind telling them that! Well, actually I'm a little busy. Run along to Bag End, north of Hobbiton, and tell Lobelia that for me, will you?''Aunt Lobelia lives at Bag End, north of Hobbiton. You can deliver any payment from the Mayor to her, and she'll hold onto it for me.''What do you want? I don't like talking to Bounders -- or whatever you are -- if I can help it. Useless, the whole bunch of you!''I'm not afraid of the Sackville-Bagginses, not one bit! I'm just... very busy, all of a sudden. You go tell Lobelia that I'm not going to give her anything for Mundo's troubles. She lives at Bag End, north of Hobbiton.''I heard about the troubles my nephew Mundo went through in Bree-land. I assume you're here with Old Flourdumpling's coin-purse, to repay us for Mundo's hardship?

'You're not? What is this nonsense? Whitfoot doesn't have an ounce of sense in that fat head of his! It doesn't surprise me that he didn't have the courage to come tell me this himself, but he'll regret it! I'll go to Michel Delving to see him personally and tell him in no uncertain terms what I think of him!

'What use is he as Mayor, anyway? And what use are the Bounders, for that matter? My nephew has gone through so much, and he was barely outside the Bounds!'Dwalin wants to know where the Dourhands went with the stolen gold and wonders if the thrushes of the Vale of Thráin might have seen something.Noglond can be found far to the south of Thorin's Hall. The stable-master Wíli can be found in the west end of Frerin's Court.

Dwalin wants you to seek out Nos Grimsong, one of his loyal retainers and a friend to the thrushes of the Vale of Thráin. If the thrushes saw the Dourhand burglars, Nos will have heard about it. Dwalin instructed you to take a horse from Frerin's court to the outpost of Noglond. Once there you are to speak to Rothgar.Talk to Wíli to the West of Frerin's CourtWíli is in the west end of Frerin's Court.

Wíli told you to travel to Noglond by way of one of his horses and to speak with Rothgar when you arrive there.Talk to Rothgar in NoglondNos Grimsong is at the Thrushstones, north-west of Noglond.

Rothgar told you seek Nos Grimsong and see if he has heard anything from the thrushes about the Dourhands robbing the dwarf-treasury.Find Nos GrimsongRothgar is in Noglond, to the south-east.

Nos Grimsong wrote down what he learned from the thrushes about the movements of the Dourhands in recent days and gave you his notes to take to Rothgar.'We need to find out where the Dourhand burglars took the gold they stole from our treasury, ${PLAYER}, and I believe I know just how to do it. The thrushes of the Vale of Thráin have long served as the eyes of Durin's Folk in the air. If the Dourhands tried moving the stolen gold from Thorin's Hall, as they must have, one of the thrushes would surely have seen them.

'Nos Grimsong is a friend of the thrushes who has long been loyal to the Lonely Mountain, and he understands their language. Nos was last appointed to duty at the outpost of Noglond to the south.

'To get to Noglond, speak with the stable-master, Wíli, to the west of Frerin's Court. Tell him you want a steed to take you to Noglond and he'll take care of the rest. When you get to Noglond, look for Rothgar. He'll be your point of contact for the time being.''Head south to Frerin's Court and speak with Wíli about getting a horse to Noglond.  When you get there speak with Rothgar, he should know where Nos is.''Well met, ${PLAYER}. If ever you need to travel at speed you should come to visit me or whomever the closest stable-master happens to be.

'So Dwalin sent you to me to purchase passage to Noglond, did he?  Well it's a good thing he did considering how far away Noglond is. Simply speak with me about renting a horse, and you'll be able to purchase safe passage at speed on one of my fine mounts.

'When you get there be sure to look for Rothgar, I expect he'll have some tasks for you.''So Dwalin sent you to me to purchase passage to Noglond, did he? Well it's a good thing he did considering how far away Noglond is. Simply speak with me about renting a horse, and you'll be able to purchase safe passage at speed on one of my fine mounts.

'When you get there be sure to look for Rothgar, I expect he'll have some tasks for you.''Welcome to Noglond, friend ${CLASS}! You might not know it, but this way-station has a storied history nearly as rich as Thorin's Halls itself! I would be honoured to tell you of...

'Oh, I see. You are here on business from Dwalin? You will never find a truer Longbeard than our Steward, and Thorin's Halls are maintained with the dignity that befits our glorious...

'Ah, yes, your pardon. What was it you were wanting, friend? Of course... Nos came through here just hours ago. When he left he mentioned heading to the Thrushstones. Follow the road north back to Thorin's Hall, and it will turn sharply to the west. Continue to follow the road until it bends to the north again. Continue west from there, and you'll find the Thrushstones.''Nos came through here just hours ago. When he left he mentioned heading to the Thrushstones.

'Follow the road north back to Thorin's Hall, and it will turn sharply to the west. Continue to follow the road until it bends to the north again. Continue west from there, and you'll find the Thrushstones.''You're here about the Dourhands sneaking out of Thorin's Halls, aren't you? The thrushes told me all about it, and I wrote it down to show Dwalin. Here, I'll give you my...

'Oh no! Lynx! Quick, help me fight them off! They're always hungry for thrushes!''Head back to Rothgar in Noglond and give him my note. He'll know what to do next.''Dwalin was right to count on Nos Grimsong and his friends among the thrushes! These notes confirm that the Dourhands brought their stolen gold in secret down into the Vale of Thráin, but the thrushes insist that they then returned to their old stronghold in the mountains that border the Vale. I thought that old city was infested with goblins now.

'There were goblins in the Silver Deep, as well, and the Dourhands seem to have passed untroubled. There is something strange going on here, ${PLAYER}, though you probably don't need me to tell you that.'Money that had been set aside to refurbish Town Hole in Michel Delving has gone missing, presumably stolen.Griffo Boffin may be found at his home near the centre of Needlehole, to the north of Michel Delving. The easiest road to Needlehole runs north from Waymeet, the cross-roads east of Michel Delving.

Mayor Whitfoot's assistant has asked you to investigate the disappearance of the money that was set aside for refurbishing Town Hole in Michel Delving.Talk to Griffo BoffinThe dwarves came out of the Rushock Bog to the east, between Needlehole and Overhill. Their camp is somewhere nearby, behind tall wooden bulwarks.

You spoke with Griffo Boffin about the missing money, as Assistant Fallohide requested, and discovered that ruffian dwarves may have stolen it. Griffo asked that you seek out the dwarves' camp, retrieve the money bag, and bring it to Assistant Fallohide in Michel Delving.Collect the money bagYou found the missing money, so now it should be delivered to Assistant Fallohide in Michel Delving.'Mayor Whitfoot set aside some money to refurbish Town Hole in Michel Delving, but it seems the carpenters haven't received it, and they won't work unless they are paid. One of the Mayor's other assistants, Griffo Boffin, was supposed to make sure the carpenters received the money. He hasn't shown up for work, though, and I'm worried that something has happened to him.

'He lives up in Needlehole, far to the north and beyond the Rushock Bog. Please visit Griffo, make sure he's all right, and then return here with the missing money. Griffo lives near the centre of Needlehole. The best way to get there is to head east to Waymeet, then follow the road north and west through Rushock Bog until you reach Needlehole.

'I would do it myself, but I'm responsible for making sure the Mayor's image remains untarnished, and... well, with Mayor Whitfoot, that's a job that takes more hours than there are in a day!''See if you can find Griffo, and learn what became of the money he was supposed to take to the carpenters. His home is in Needlehole, and can be most easily reached by travelling east to Waymeet and then north and west along the road through the Rushock Bog.''I know what you are thinking -- that I stole the money -- but I didn't! I was taking the money on a short cut across the bog to Overhill where the carpenters are working today, and these ragged-looking dwarves came running down at me from the north!

'They had axes and looked like they meant to use them, so I don't mind saying I ran as fast as I could back to town. But I dropped the bag with the money along the way and turned my ankle, too. I was just trying to come up with some way to tell the Mayor the bad news when you showed up.

'I think those dwarves came out of the Rushock Bog east of here, about halfway to Overhill. I expect the bag is in their camp -- you'll know it by the large wooden bulwarks that protect it. If you can recover the bag of money, please bring it back to Assistant Fallohide with my apologies.''Please find the bag of money and bring it back to Assistant Fallohide in Michel Delving. The ruffian dwarves surely have it in their camp, somewhere in the bog to the east, between Needlehole and Overhill. You'll know their camp by the large bulwarks which defend it.''Wonderful! I'm so happy you found the bag. Please bring it back to Assistant Fallohide in Michel Delving.''Oh, thank you! I'm so glad that Griffo is all right. A terrible thing, but it's worked out in the end. I'll make sure the carpenters get their money, and with no short cuts through the bog this time!'After discovering a letter on the brigand supervisor at Old Bauman's farm, you delivered it to Constable Sageford to discover the identity of "R.F." is Rurik Fennel a locksmith in Combe.Rurik Fennel, a local locksmith, lives on the road that runs south past The Comb and Wattle Inn in Combe.

Constable Sageford wants you to confront Rurik Fennel of the coincidences surrounding the Blackwold brigands and his name and initials appearing on their crates and letters they carry.Talk to Rurik Fennel in CombeConstable Sageford awaits news of Rurik's involvement near the centre of Combe.

Rurik Fennel appears to have been an unwitting and bullied pawn of the Blackwold.Talk to Constable Sageford in Combe'Rurik is a locksmith here in Combe. You should show him that receipt and ask him why the brigands appear to be common patrons of his.

'It seems odd that Rurik would be involved, he's a quiet man who keeps to himself mostly. Still we need to investigate every lead carefully.

'You should find him outside his home on the road that runs south past The Comb and Wattle Inn.''Make your way down the road that runs south past The Comb and Wattle Inn and confront Rurik about the letter and the strongbox you found.''Yes, my name is Rurik. Yes, I'm a locksmith. What is this about? One of my strongboxes -- recovered from a brigand? -- and a letter? I see....

'I had hoped that I saw the last of the Blackwolds. You must understand, I did not willingly help them. My business is keeping things locked away, so I do not often ask questions of my customers. I filled an order for twenty strongboxes and upon completion was visited by the Blackwolds. One -- a tough fellow -- took my master key and threatened my life if I talked. One of the others with him called him Applewood.

'Please, tell the Constable that any aid was unwilling, and I only stayed silent because I feared for my life.''Please tell Constable Sageford that I did not aid the brigands purposefully. I do not know who Applewood is, but he has the master key to the strongboxes.''While this doesn't help us get this box open and the valuables returned, it does speak well of Rurik. I feel badly that he felt as though we could not protect him... but with what happened to Archet, I understand his hesitation.

'Let me think a moment on the name he gave us. Scouts are coming and going at all times... one may have mentioned seeing this Applewood.'Holly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Edilina Proudfoot of Tuckborough had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Edilina Proudfoot has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Edilina Proudfoot's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'Well hullo there, what can I do for you today? A slice of pie, perhaps? It's from Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton. She bakes a fine pie! I could learn a thing or two from her!

'Spoiled berries? Well, I was right... I could learn something from Holly. Always taste your berries before you bake them into a pie! Poor thing, she must be terribly embarrassed! Well, here, take that pie back to her. Her home is north of the main square of Hobbiton.

'Tell the dear thing to take her time baking me a new one.''Holly's pie, the one with the bad berries, is over there on the table. Go ahead and take it back to her in Hobbiton.'Bingo Boffin lives a peaceful life in his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, but he is lonely and wants something more from his days.The market of Michel Delving is south of Bingo's hobbit-hole.

Bingo Boffin has decided to throw a dinner-party for his neighbours in order to relieve some of his loneliness, and wants you to assess the available food at the market. He hopes it will inspire him on the matter of what courses to serve at his party.Bingo Boffin is outside his hobbit-hole north of the Michel Delving market, on the other side of the Town Hole.

You have assessed a number of foods at the market in Michel Delving, and should now report back to Bingo Boffin.Return to Bingo and give him your reportThe library in the Great Smials is in the town of Tuckborough, east of Michel Delving.

Uninspired by your report of the delicious food for sale at the market, Bingo thinks that perhaps a cookbook will give him the inspiration he needs.Travel to the library in the Great Smials, in Tuckborough, and speak to the librarian thereDonnamira Took, the librarian in the Great Smials, has recommended a cookbook from the shelf behind her.Check out one of the fine cookbooks behind Donnamira TookBingo is outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, just north of the the Town Hole.

You have checked out a fine cookbook from the library in the Great Smials and should bring it to Bingo.The Mathom-house of Michel Delving is on a hill south-west of Bingo Boffin's hobbit-hole.

Bingo has asked you to bring the map that fell out of the library's cookbook to the Mathom-house in Michel Delving. He does not want it.Bingo has run up the hill to the Mathom-house at break-neck speed, and is now exhausted. What could he want?Bingo has asked to meet you once again outside his hobbit-hole to the north-east of the Mathom-house, north of the Town Hole.

Bingo has been inspired by the hand-drawn map he found, but not to host a dinner-party. Instead, he wants to go on an adventure!Talk to Bingo Boffin outside his hobbit-hole'A pleasant day to you, friend. If you have a moment or two to spare, do you think I might trouble you for a spell? My name is Bingo, of the Delving-field Boffins, and it is so rare for me to see new folk on the path that runs by my hole. It is a pleasure to meet you!

'I have been feeling a mite lonely these days, you see, and could use a festive occasion on the horizon to put a spring in my step and to occupy my thoughts. Perhaps a dinner-party would do the trick? Yes, that sounds capital! I will invite my neighbours, and you as well, of course!

'Could you run down to the Michel Delving market and assess some of the produce on display? Tell me what foods look particularly delicious, and that may give me the spark of inspiration for a course or three to serve at my party!

'The market is to the south of my hobbit-hole.''Could you run down to the Michel Delving market and assess some of the produce on display? Tell me what foods look particularly delicious, and that may give me the spark of inspiration for a course or three to serve at my party!

'The market is south of my hobbit-hole.''Well? Did any of the food at the market capture your fancy, ${PLAYER}?'

Bingo listens to your report that everything looked delicious.

'That is both a wonderful thing and a pity, because it makes it very difficult to decide what to serve at my party! I need more than just an account of the ingredients, I suppose. I need a cookbook!

'There is a library in the Great Smials at Tuckborough. Would you mind terribly a quick trip to the library to check out a cookbook on my behalf? Perhaps leafing through such a book will give me a good idea of what to serve.''There is a library in the Great Smials at Tuckborough. Would you mind terribly a quick trip to the library to check out a cookbook on my behalf? Perhaps leafing through such a book will give me a good idea of what to serve.''Yes? Can I help you find something in particular?'

You tell Donnamira that you're looking for a cookbook suitable for preparing fine meals for dinner-parties, and her face lights up.

'Very good, very good! There is no day that cannot be brightened with a tasty meal shared by friends. Any of the fine cookbooks on this shelf behind me will suffice, I warrant!''There is no day that cannot be brightened with a tasty meal shared by friends. Any of the fine cookbooks on this shelf behind me will suffice, I warrant!''You are all set, my book-loving friend! Thank you for your patronage, and support your local library!''This looks like just the thing, ${PLAYER}, thank you!'

Bingo takes the cookbook from you and begins to leaf through it when a folded parchment falls out from between the pages. The curious hobbit picks it up and unfolds it.

'What's this? Why, it's a map! Someone left a map in this cookbook, ${PLAYER}. Barrow-downs... Weather Hills... Stone-trolls' Glade... look at these little pictures, my friend! Do you think these are real places?

'Bah! I cannot let my mind wander to these places! I have a party to plan! Bring this map to the Mathom-house, ${PLAYER}! I do not need it, and I do not want it!''I cannot let my mind wander to these places! I have a party to plan! Bring this map to the Mathom-house, ${PLAYER}! I do not need it, and I do not want it!''You have an unloved and unwanted object with no place else to go, but cannot bear to throw it away? Hand it over, and I will make sure it joins other mathoms of its type in my keeping.'

Brombard extends his hand to receive the map, but then something catches his eye and he pauses.

'Perhaps I spoke too hastily! It appears that there is a claimant for this mathom after all, and he has run here at great speed to recover it!''Most folk who bring things to the Mathom-house are not so eager to keep them! Perhaps Bingo is an exception to the rule. I have never seen Master Boffin run so hard before, and it has quite taken the breeze from his pipes!''I changed my mind, ${PLAYER}, I changed my mind! I do not want that map to gather dust inside the mathom-house! I want to learn more about the places it depicts!

'I want to wander the Weather Hills, walking-stick in hand! I want to cross the Last Bridge, and see what lies beyond! I want to see Rivendell... are there really Elves there?

'I will keep the map, ${PLAYER}, and I will use it to design my adventure! Let us return to my hobbit-hole and make some plans, my inspiring friend!''I will keep the map, ${PLAYER}, and I will use it to plan my adventure! Let us return to my hobbit-hole and make some plans, my inspiring friend!''Ah, it will take me some time to recover from that exercise. I have never run so quickly in all my days, ${PLAYER}! And yet, I am more excited than ever before. An adventure! It will be just the thing! But it will take some preparations, to be sure. I will need your help to get ready for this journey!'

<rgb=#00FF00>Look for Bert Bartleby near the Michel Delving stables to exchange Bingo Badges for rewards.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Training for the Journey' (Recommended Level: 9)</rgb>Adelard Took has sent word that a copy of the Founding Writ, the document that established the Bounds of the Shire, has been discovered. The original document was given to the Fallohide brothers, Marcho and Blanco, by the old King.Adelard Took can be found in the Great Smials in Tuckborough.

Brombard Foxtail, the Keeper of the Mathom-house heard rumour of Adelard Took's find and asked you to try and obtain the copy of the Founding Writ from Adelard.Belco Brockhouse can be found north of Tuckborough town centre, up the hill and on the right of the path.

To his embarassment, Adelard Took revealed that he doesn't have the Founding Writ. A local farmer, Belco Brockhouse, is the one who found the Writ, but he refuses to hand it over to Adelard until someone helps him around his farm.'Ah, yes, good day to you. I was wondering if you could do me a favour?

'I have just received word that Adelard Took has found a copy of the original writ penned by the old King. This writ granted the Fallohide brothers, Marcho and Blanco, the lands that became the Shire. It is a most exceptional find! True, I already have a copy of the document, but it is in very poor shape. If this copy is in better condition, it would be a marvelous addition to the Mathom-house!

'Would you go to Tookland and speak to Adelard about this find? I believe you can find him in the Great Smials in Tuckborough.''Oh dear! You are here for the Founding Writ? Please don't let Paladin know, but I don't have it!

'A local farmer, Belco Brockhouse, has it, and he won't give it up. His home is north of here, up the hill and to the right of the path, and he says he won't give up the Writ until he gets a hand with his crops. Honestly! At my age, I can't help with farm labour!

'I'm sorry to say that if you want the Writ, you'll have to speak to him and perhaps lend a hand. The cheek of some hobbits!''Aye, I've got that piece o' parchment Adelard's wanting. I found it among my Mum's things, and I don't mind it going off to the Mathom-house -- I'd rather it go there than into that Adelard's collection -- but there's a few problems I need help with.

'See, my fences need mending, my pig has run off, and I need some feed from Hobbiton. If you help me with those tasks, I'll give you the Writ. Fair to you?''Belco Brockhouse is the one who has the Writ. Go speak with him about it, up the hill to the north...but be prepared to help him with his farm!''Do please be quick about acquiring that copy of the Founding Writ. I'm anxious to get a look at such a find! Speak with Adelard Took in the Great Smials in Tuckborough...he is the one who sent me word of this.''Do please be quick about acquiring that copy of the Founding Writ. I'm anxious to get a look at such a find! Speak with Adelard Took in the Great Smials in Tuckborough...he is the one who sent me word of this.'Ted Pickthorn was greatly distressed when you told him the Hanging Tree and all the trees surrounding it had been chopped down.Mason Thorne is at the lumber-camp, north and east of the guard-house.

Ted Pickthorn asked you to speak with Mason Thorne, the foreman at the Combe lumber-camp. He may recall which tree had been the Hanging Tree.Talk to Mason Thorne at the Combe lumber-campMason Thorne awaits you at the lumber-camp that lies east and north of Combe, south of the Chetwood.

Thorne sent you to retrieve his ledger from the Blackwold brigands encamped along the road. You should return the ledger to him at once.'Maybe the woodcutters at the lumber-camp up east of here remember which tree was the Hanging Tree! ${PLAYER}, you've got to have a word with Mason Thorne, the Man in charge there. He just has to remember which o' the stumps used to be the Hanging Tree. He just has to!

'The lumber-camp is along the road, north o' the Big House. Please, I need that money to make a new start for meself.''You tell those woodcutters at the lumber-camp that they can't go around chopping down trees willy-nilly like that!

'I realize that the people of Combe depend on the sale of that wood to get by, but this is me dad's legacy we're talking about! How am I ever going to find it now without digging holes up and down the Chetwood?''The Hanging Tree? Oh, I remember seeing a few... hmm... hangings in my day. I... hmmm... do believe I wrote the site o' the Hanging Tree down in my ledger. I write down all the things I want to remember. So I can just look it up in....

'Well... hmmm... bless me! I think I dropped my ledger in the woods not far from here. Yes, I remember! We were surprised by some o' those Blackwolds, and I dropped my ledger on the road. I'd wager a captain o' those brigands picked it up!

'There are quite a few camp-fires to the north and east, along the forested road. You might find my ledger on one o' them Blackwolds! Bring it back here... hmmm... and I'll look up that thing you wanted to know about. A tree, was it?''You say the site o' the Hanging Tree is inside Mason's ledger? Good, good! I'd love to see that ledger, uh, well... truth is, I can't read. Once you've got the ledger, you best get old Thorne to look it up.''Ah, you found my ledger! Now I can find that... hmmm... thing you wanted!'Dora Brownlock thinks an admirer of hers has gone to try and kill the exiled leader of the wolves near Waymeet.Jolly Smallburrow may be after the wolf that was seen across the road from the wolf-den, north of Dora Brownlock's farm.

Dora Brownlock is worried that her neighbour, Jolly Smallburrow, may be in trouble and has asked you to find him.Find Jolly SmallburrowDora Brownlock is at the centre of Waymeet.

Dora will be pleased to know that you have rescued Jolly Smallburrow and defeated the scarred leader of the wolves that have been harassing her farm and town.'There's been rumour of a scarred, old wolf spotted away from the rest of the pack -- in fact, across the road from the wolf-den north of my farm. I don't know what might have happened, but I think it's fair to say that this old wolf must be their leader, exiled for some reason.

'Now, I think I've done something terribly foolish, ${PLAYER}! My neighbour, Jolly Smallburrow, is a true gentlehobbit, and I suspect he's something of an admirer of mine. Unfortunately, I mentioned this wolf business to him, and he swore to take care of it!

'If you don't mind, would you please find Jolly before the wolf does? I'll feel terrible if something happens to him!''Jolly means well, but he's always trying to find ways to impress me. I hope you find him before that dreadful wolf does!''Dora was worried about me? Truly? Perhaps she does have feelings for me! Well, to tell you the truth, I was a little worried myself about what would happen once that wolf showed its muzzle around here.

'I felt sure my bucket of boar meat would lure the beast out of hiding, too. Ah, well. Maybe I didn't get smelly-enough boar meat....

'I'll clean this up, and we can go talk to Dora together....''You rescued Jolly, ${PLAYER}, and thank goodness! I knew there wouldn't be an old wolf that could do you in, though I'm sure the same can't be said for poor, well-meaning Mr. Smallburrow.

'I have not yet decided whether to take him up on his dinner invitation. Yes, he ran straight here to ask before you even returned!'Dorri wants dirty wings. Dorri can be found standing at the west gate of Gondamon.You have accepted a task to acquire dirty wings. You are to deliver them to Dorri at the western gate of Gondamon to earn favour with Thorin's Hall.Wanted: Dirty wings from the hendrevail and bats found in Ered Luin. Collect them and deliver them to Dorri at Gondamon to earn favour with Thorin's Hall.Wanted: Dirty wings from the hendrevail and bats found in Ered Luin.'Hendrevail work with the Dourhands, vile creatures, and bats are nothing more than flying vermin.

'Your efforts will echo through the halls.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Dorri wants dull beaks. Dorri can be found standing at the west gate of Gondamon.You have accepted a task to acquire dull beaks. You are to deliver them to Dorri at the western gate of Gondamon to earn favour with Thorin's Hall.Wanted: Dull beaks from the hendrevail in Ered Luin. Collect them and deliver them to Dorri at Gondamon to earn favour with Thorin's Hall.Wanted: Dull beaks from the hendrevail in Ered Luin.'Good riddance to these creatures...too many of them around for us to feel comfortable.

'Your efforts will echo through the halls.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The ruins of Gwâl Cruban are overrun with vicious turtles.Gwendrian has asked you to thin the number of turtles at Gwâl Cruban.

Gwâl Cruban is in northern Swanfleet.Defeat dread-turtles at Gwâl Cruban (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Gwendrian know that you have thinned out the dread-turtles at Gwâl Cruban.

Gwendrian is at Echad Terthas.Return to Gwendrian'I am usually loath to harm wildlife, but the dread-turtles of Gwâl Cruban have overbred and are straining the local resources. If you reduce their numbers, I shall reward you.''I thank you for your attention to this task. It is no easy feat to defeat a dread-turtle. You have my thanks!'Mal Begbeam once dreamed of exploring the land but has since settled down with a family of his own.

He laments that he had never chanced a view at the floating village in the sky.Clegur can be found south-east of Mossward past the Howlingstones.

You should ask Leri Grudd about the floating village.Talk to Leri GruddLeri Grudd has given you exact instructions on where the parcel was buried.

Find the parcel in the ruffian camp north of Clegur and return it to her.Find Leri Grudd's family parcelYou found Leri's parcel. You should take it back to Leri Grudd and confirm its authenticity.Talk to Leri GruddCranog Dambryn wanders along the banks of the river north-east of Clegur.

You should find them if you want to find Glyn Helyg.Talk to Cranog DambrynThe ruffian camp Radlaw can be found north of Clegur.

Cranog Dambryn has asked you to teach them a lesson.Defeat ruffians in Radlaw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You managed to create some chaos inside Radlaw.

You should talk to Cranog.Talk to Cranog DambrynCranog has told you to look for trail markers he left that lead to Glyn Helyg.Locate the first trail markerCranog has told you to look for trail markers in order to locate Glyn Helyg.Locate the second trail markerCranog has told you to look for trail markers in order to locate Glyn Helyg.Locate the third trail markerCranog has told you to look for trail markers in order to locate Glyn Helyg.Locate the fourth trail markerYou have found Glyn Helyg. You should deliver Leri's parcel to her cousin Gwenfor.'Have you been to the Stoor-vales? I was once a traveller. But I met my wife here and chose family. I never made it out that far.

'I've heard fascinating tales from my friend, of a floating village overlooking the river. I would have loved to witness this place.

'If you'd like to see it for yourself, you can talk to my friend Leri Grudd.

'You'll find her south-east of here past the Howlingstones in a town called Clegur.''A floating village you say? Well, I did say that to Mal last we spoke I suppose. The village is called Glyn Helyg. It is where I was raised. You can imagine it, floating in the sky and all, being quite an ordeal to get there, mind ya. I could help you find it. But I am in need of help.

'There is a small parcel. Sentimental, really. Hidden and buried to keep the ruffians away from it. Problem is, the ruffians decided to set up their home where we buried it!

'If you have it in ya, might you retrieve this parcel from them and return it to my family in Glyn Helyg?''That's the one! Thank you for retrieving this for me. The brigands have been pestering us folk for a while and I feared our family might lose it. Please deliver this to my cousin Gwenfor in Glyn Helyg.

'Now, the way to Glyn Helyg is very rough. I cannot personally show you the way. But I have an acquaintance that could. Follow the road east across the river and speak to Cranog Dambryn.

'They wander along the banks close to a watermill looking for odd trinkets.''Looking for Glyn Helyg, are ya? You and everyone else. The ruffians out of Radlaw have been causing all kinds of chaos for the Stoor-vales. How do I know you are not one of them?

'Tell you what. If you can stir up some trouble in Radlaw and perhaps teach a few of those ruffians a thing or two, I will show you the way to Glyn Helyg.

'Sound like a deal?''Word travels fast in the Stoor-vales. Ruffians are in a panic in response to your actions.

'All right. I'll tell you how to find Glyn Helyg. You know the road you took to get here? Follow it north.

'I have left trail markers along the way for you to find the secret entrance to Glyn Helyg. They will point you in the right direction.

'If you follow the trail markers precisely, you should be able to find Glyn Helyg.''Ah, Leri sent you? Judging by your face, I'd say you are quite disappointed.

'This is indeed Glyn Helyg. And no, it is not a floating village. I'm going to have to give Leri what for!

'Ever since they left to go on their adventures, they've been spreadin' all kinds of fantastical rumours about this place. Tellin' all manner of folk that our humble town floats in the sky overlooking the river.

'You are not the first to appear to me with such despair. But enough about them. Thank you for deliverin' the parcel.

'It's quite important to our family.'Calengil wants you to destroy the goblin, Durglup, at Dol Ringwest. He believes this goblin is the leader of the forces there and thus responsible for the desecration of the ruins.Dol Ringwest lies to the west of Duillond.

Calengil wishes to drive the evil out of the ruins of Dol Ringwest. He has asked you to make your way to the ruins and seek out the goblin's leader, Durglup.Defeat DurglupCalengil is at Duillond, east of Dol Ringwest.

Durglup proved a challenge for which you were well prepared. He no longer taints the ruins of Dol Ringwest. You should return to Calengil at once.Talk to Calengil at Duillond'My duty to this land will not be complete until the terror that brought ruin here is ousted. Your efforts thus far have been in earnest and proved that you too desire to see the land restored and cleansed of the evil wrought hereon. 

'While in the ruins, I would ask that you seek out the leader of the goblins there, Durglup. He is a particularly nasty goblin and should not be underestimated.

'You will find this creature within the confines of Dol Ringwest, to the west of Duillond. Return to me when the beast is slain.''It is good to know that the threat posed by this creature is no more. I thank you for your efforts there.

'I will ever recall your deeds this day, ${PLAYER}.''Durglup is a terribly cruel creature  willing to lash out at his own brethren. He is a potent servant and needs to be destroyed.'Belco Brockhouse found a copy of the Founding Writ of the Shire, but will not give it up until he has received some services in return.The sack of feed can be found on the Grange north of Hobbiton. Once you have picked up the feed, bring them back to Belco in Tuckborough.

Belco has told you that his pig, Old Sally, has a ravenous appetite, and that he needs more feed if he is to satisfy her. He has instructed you to go to the Grange and pick up a sack of feed.Pick up the sack of feed'So my pig, old Sally, when she ain't running loose all over the countryside, eats, and eats like you wouldn't believe. Goes through a sack o' feed in no time! Never seen a pig with an appetite like hers.

'I need you to go to the Grange up in Hobbiton and fetch me a sack o' feed. Don't worry about talking to Ted Sandyman there to pay for them... I told him someone was going to come by and get them later today.

'Now, if you want that writ, you'd best be hurrying along! Head north across the Bywater Bridge in Hobbiton, and you'll see the Grange right there to your left.''Old Sally has no use for this writ, but I know that you do! Go fetch the sack o' feed that I'm due from the Grange, and then we can talk some more. Head north through Hobbiton to the Bywater Bridge, and you'll see the Grange right there on your left.'After helping him out around the farm, Belco Brockhouse has finally given you the copy of the Founding Writ of the Shire he found among his mother's things.Brombard Foxtail is at the Mathom-house in Michel Delving.

Belco Brockhouse, satisifed with your services, exhorted you to take his copy of the Founding Writ directly to Keeper Brombard Foxtail. He has no desire to see it end up in the hands of Adelard Took.'Aye, I suppose you've done enough for me, although I am going to miss the extra help around the farm here. And Old Sally seems to have taken a liking to you, although that could just be because you brought her feed!

'Here's that copy of the writ I found in my mum's things. Take it over to Keeper Foxtail at the Mathom-house in Michel Delving.

'And make sure you don't let that Adelard Took have it, I don't want it near his collection!''Marvelous, you have the Writ! Thank you for your work. Now, if you don't mind, please give it to Brombard Foxtail with my regards!''What you doing hanging about here? Anxious for more work? If not, be off with you. Take that Writ to Keeper Foxtail in Michel Delving.''Excellent, so this is it! Let me take a look at it....

'Yes, interesting, interesting. Wonderful! It is a complete copy of the Writ and is in a bit better condition than the one already in the Mathom-house. Thank you for your efforts. I trust it wasn't too difficult to acquire, was it?'Constable Sageford has learned that the Blackwold brigands have been trying to support themselves by working a farm they seized deep in the Chetwood to the east of Combe.Old Bauman's farm is deep in the Chetwood, at the end of the eastward path.

Constable Sageford believes that if you confront the Blackwolds' leader at Old Bauman's farm, you might be able to recover some of the valuables the Blackwolds have stolen.Search for valuablesConstable Sageford can be found near town-centre in Combe, with his fellow constables.

Sageford sent you to confront the leader of the Blackwolds at Old Bauman's farm. You found a receipt signed by a 'Rurik' on the Blackwold's body. Constable Sageford will want to know about this.'After the initial raids, when folk began fleeing for villages like Archet and Staddle, the Blackwolds found they could no longer rely only upon raids to support themselves. They seized Old Bauman's farm and began tilling the soil, though badly and without care for the land.

'The brigands at the farm must be under the supervision of some Blackwold leader, else they would fall to laziness. If you confront the Blackwolds' leader at the farm, you might be able to recover some of the valuables they have stolen. Old Bauman's farm is deep in the Chetwood, at the end of the eastward path.

'I would appreciate it if you could at least try. There are many folk who would benefit from the recovery of this treasure.''The farms north-east of Combe are sure to be under the watchful eye of some important Blackwold!''What is this?

'Rurik? There's a Rurik Fennel living here in Combe. He's a... a locksmith! But why would he be aiding the Blackwolds, ${PLAYER}? Rurik's house is south-west of here, just behind The Comb and Wattle.

'You had best have a talk with Rurik. I will be very interested to know why he's been locking boxes for the Blackwolds. Very interested, indeed.'Most adventurers get their start from humble beginnings, and few can see at the beginning how grand their adventure might become.Tegwyn has been bothering Skardí Bendblade all morning, and the blacksmith wants you to do something about him.Talk to Tegwyn inside the Mossward blacksmith shopSkardí Bendblade asked you to collect boar tusks, craban talons, and potential whetstones he might put to various uses for the town.Collect boar tusks along the Old South Road (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect craban talons along the Old South Road (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect potential whetstones along the Old South Road (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Skardí Bendblade is waiting in his shop in Mossward for the items you collected.Skardí Bendblade told you that Tegwyn never returned to his home, and you should check the perimeter of the town for the missing boy.You should tell one of the nearby town guards that Tegwyn is missing from Mossward.Talk to Merion by the east gate of Mossward'I could use a number of items to restock my supplies while you continue looking into the matter of the raiding-party, ${PLAYER}: sharp stones, boar tusks, and craban talons.

'And do you think you could do something about Tegwyn? He's been bothering me with questions since this morning, and I need to get this work done!''I need sharp stones, boar tusks, and craban talons to restock my supplies. But first, can you do something about Tegwyn? He's been bothering me with questions since this morning, and I need to get this work done!''I'm ready for a more important adventuring task, ${PLAYER}! What can I do to help the village? Can I come with you?'

Reluctant to send the boy into danger, you ask that he patrol the outer palisade of Mossward.

'All right. I guess I can do that. Maybe I can accompany you later?''I'll patrol the palisades, but maybe later on I can accompany you?''Thank you for these items, ${PLAYER}, but I'll have you know this: I am quite cross with you! All I want is to be left in peace, free to do my work, but folk are constantly barging in here, interrupting me and slowing down my work. That boy's mother was just here, Wenna, and she says he hasn't returned home.

'The last I heard, you sent him to scout the edge of town, so you get to go looking for him! You send him back to his parents before they come bothering me again, will you?''The last I heard, you sent him to scout the edge of town, so you get to go looking for him! You send him back to his parents before they come bothering me again, will you?''The last I heard, you sent him to scout the edge of town, so you get to go looking for him! You send him back to his parents before they come bothering me again, will you?''Tegwyn is missing? It would not be the first time the boy has gone looking for trouble... but with Uruks and goblins about, he might have gotten in over his head this time.'Defeat brigands in Ered Luin.Defeat brigands in Ered LuinDefeat many brigands in Ered Luin.Defeat brigands in Ered LuinSince Lobelia Sackville-Baggins paid to acquire the ingredients for her fireworks, Hyacinth Took has recruited you to help her gather them.The dwarf-merchant Onar is in the hamlet of Needlehole in the north-west corner of Rushock Bog.

Hyacinth only needs brimstone and iron filings to get to work on Lobelia Sackville-Baggins' fireworks. She suggested you could obtain them from Onar, a dwarf-merchant.Hyacinth Took is in Tuckborough, near the Great Smials.

Hyacinth Took sent you to Needlehole to acquire brimstone and iron filings from the dwarf-merchant Onar. Onar made a quick and fair trade and has sent you back to Hyacinth with her parcels.Lobelia Sackville-Baggins is at her home at Bag End in Hobbiton.

With your help, Hyacinth Took now has all she needs to begin work on Lobelia Sackville-Baggins' fireworks. She told you to return to Lobelia and let her know the fireworks will be done in three months.'You're too willing, ${PLAYER}! First wolves, and now a bear? You should be more firm with these folk and make them take care of their own problems for once.

'All right. Now last, but not least, I'll need some brimstone and iron filings. You can't find brimstone around here, so I always go to the dwarves for that stuff. They can also provide the filings cheaper than any of the local smiths, so we'll take care of two problems at once, this time.

'Please head over to Needlehole and talk to the dwarf-merchant Onar. I've dealt with him in the past, and I imagine he'll be able to give us what we need.''Three months! Three months! That won't do! Won't do at all! My birthday is in two months! Do you understand? Two!''Ho! So little Hyacinth wants some more makings for her pretty lights! Wants to be a Wizard, does she? Ha!

'Well it just so happens I have some brimstone and filings to sell -- at a very reasonable price too, I might add. Tell all your friends, very easy terms....

'What? Don't just stand there like a ninny with your mouth open like that. Were you thinking I'd send you on a quest or something for such simple things? Here, take these parcels, and good day to you!''Please go to Needlehole to pick up the brimstone and iron filings from Onar.''You'd best tell Lobelia that all the ingredients have been purchased, and her fireworks will be ready in three months.''You seem surprised, friend, but you shouldn't be. If a dwarf says he can provide a particular kind of good, you can count on him to provide it! Bring the brimstone and the iron filings to Hyacinth Took in Tuckborough as soon as you are able.''Well, well, that wasn't that hard was it? And you stood your ground with him! 

'I'll get started on these fireworks right away! Tell the old crow I should have all she needs in just three months!'Postman Boffin of Overhill has asked you to deliver a satchel to Bywater.Postman Cotton can be found north-east of The Green Dragon in Bywater, far to the south of Overhill.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Cotton in Bywater as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty and keep the mail satchel dry!Collect the satchel from Postman Boffin's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'It's important that the Quick Post service recover its old reputation for speed and service, and you can certainly help with that!

'There on the table is a satchel for Postman Cotton in Bywater, and you could really help me out by delivering it. Postman Cotton can be found north-east of The Green Dragon in Bywater. Do not let yourself be distracted by Cotton's location near The Green Dragon! The mail must be delivered quickly and without any side-trips for thirsty mail carriers!

'Avoid nosey hobbits, for they will stall you and make your delivery impossible! Keep the satchel dry, as well -- wet mail is no good for anybody!''The satchel for Bywater is over there on the table. Take it to Postman Cotton as quickly as possible! Avoid nosey hobbits and keep both yourself and the mail satchel dry -- and that includes of the beer at The Green Dragon!'Postman Grubb of Hobbiton has asked you to deliver a satchel to Overhill.Postman Boffin can be found in the centre of Overhill, far to the north of Hobbiton.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Boffin in Overhill as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty, and do not let the mail satchel get wet!Collect the satchel from Postman Grubb's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'I have received a great many complaints lately concerning the amount of time it takes the Quick Post service to deliver packages and mail. Admittedly, most of those complaints have come from Lobelia Sackville-Baggins and her son Lotho, but some respectable hobbits have complained as well. We need to do something about this, certainly!

'If you'd like to help out, there on the table you will find a satchel for delivery to Postman Boffin in Overhill. Overhill is a good distance north of here, nestled in the Bindbole Wood, and Postman Boffin should be right in the centre of town.

'Look out for nosey hobbits, for they will delay you and keep you from delivering the mail on time, and don't let the mail satchel get wet! If the ink on the letters runs, the good hobbits of Overhill are sure to be upset with us.''The satchel for Overhill is over there on the table. Take it to Postman Boffin in the centre of Overhill, and let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty!'Lobelia insists on fireworks for her birthday party. The only possible way to get them in time for her party is to recover the fireworks stolen from Hyacinth Took.Shirriff Robin Smallburrow can be found inside the Ivy Bush in the centre of Hobbiton.

Since it will be three months before Hyacinth Took can have more fireworks ready for Lobelia Sackville-Baggins, a month too late for her party, Lobelia instructed you to speak with Robin Smallburrow about recovering Hyacinth's stolen fireworks.The Thain can be found at the Great Smials in Tuckborough, south of Hobbiton.

Lobelia Sackville-Baggins sent you to speak with Robin Smallburrow about Hyacinth Took's stolen fireworks, but Shirriff Smallburrow told you the matter was outside of his jurisdiction. He suggested you speak with Paladin Took, Thain of the Shire.'I must have those fireworks in time for my birthday party. One way or another, by hook or by crook, I will have them, I tell you!

'Ah! Hyacinth said her fireworks were stolen, didn't she? Well, then, the answer is simple. All you have to do is get them back from the thieves! Talk to Shirriff Smallburrow here in Hobbiton, and I'm sure he will set you right on the path if you can pull him away from his mug!

'After all, that is what Bounders and Shirriffs --or whatever you are -- are supposed to do, isn't it? Catch thieves and ruffians and recover stolen properties for upstanding citizens like myself? It certainly is! Now be off!''Don't just stand there gaping like a ninnyhammer! Go speak with Shirriff Smallburrow at the Ivy Bush!''You've got my sympathy about dealing with Lobelia, but I'm happy to say this matter is completely out of my hands. Fortunately for me, there's nothing I can do about fireworks stolen in Tuckborough -- I only deal with matters arising near Hobbiton!

'You should go talk to the Thain, Paladin Took, at the Great Smials in Tuckborough. I'm sure he'll be able to direct you.''So the Shirriff told you to go to the Thain? Why ask me what to do? Go to the Thain!''I think you should go talk to the Thain about the stolen fireworks. He'll be at the Great Smials in Tuckborough, to the south.''I do remember the incident. Hyacinth told me about it, naturally.

'The local Bounders have been unable to recover the lost fireworks. But since you bring it to my mind, I think I may have a task for you... a dangerous one too, I might add.'Thinglaer's brother Calengil also seeks to restore the ancient Elf-ruins within Ered Luin and requires your aid.Calengil can be found in the Elf-refuge of Duillond to the north.

Thinglaer has asked you to seek out his brother Calengil and lend him what aid you may.'My brother Calengil is staying at Duillond, our refuge to the north. Like me, he also strives to restore the old places to their pristine state and may need your help.

'Follow the road to the high ground above Celondim, then make your way north through a gap in the hills to reach the refuge.''So, Thinglaer has succeeded in driving the darkness back from Tham Gelair with your aid? I too have such a task before me -- but, alas, I have no trinket from Rivendell to aid me.

'I do know much of the herbs of these lands however and can mix a draught that should serve to purify the nearby ruins -- will you lend me your aid in this endeavour?''My brother Calengil resides in Duillond to the north. He could use your aid with his own tasks, I believe.'Since Lobelia Sackville-Baggins paid to acquire the ingredients for her fireworks, Hyacinth Took has recruited you to help her gather them.Hart Holeman is at his home in the centre of Overhill.

Hyacinth Took appreciated the saltpetre you brought back with you, though she chided you for letting Cam Puddifoot talk you into hunting wolves for him. Now she has asked you to speak with Hart Holeman about the charcoal she needs.'You really shouldn't have let Cam bully you into hunting those wolves for him. That's work for the Shirriffs! Well, thank you for the saltpetre.

'Now I need some charcoal. Please go to Overhill and talk to Hart Holeman. He and some other wood-cutters gather timber from Bindbole Wood and sometimes cook charcoal for sale. You can find him at his home in the centre of Overhill.

'Mind you don't let him bully you like Cam did.''Charcoal is it? Yes, we do have some for sale. I'll be happy to prepare a parcel for young Hyacinth. But there's one thing you can do for me first....''Please go talk to Hart Holeman in Overhill to get the charcoal I need.'Calengil has asked you to collect some herbs for him as part of a draught he is creating to cleanse a dark taint from the ruins near Duillond.The herbs can be found along the riverside beneath Duillond. 

Calengil has asked you to retrieve the herbs that he needs to complete the cleansing draught.Collect damp fragrant herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Calengil is at Duillond, north of Celondim.

You should return the herbs you collected to Calengil.'You have decided to help me? Excellent. There is a draught I know the making of that should cleanse the taint from the ruins of Dol Ringwest. I have most of the ingredients I need, but there is one remaining herb -- a fragrant herb that grows on the shores of the river, running north to south below Duillond.

'Tis a simple matter to gather it, and I would do so myself, but the brewing is at a delicate stage right now, and I must keep a close eye upon it. Would you gather the herbs I need, ${PLAYER}?''You will find that the herb grows on the shores of the river below Duillond running north to south.''Ah! There, just in time. The last step of the process is to add the herbs you have collected for me. After that it simply needs to steep for a few minutes, and the draught will be complete.'Calengil has prepared his draught and has offered you the honour of cleansing Dol Ringwest. The draught will in time encourage the growth of great vines that will entwine the ruins, tearing them down and returning them to pristine nature.Dol Ringwest is west of Duillond.

Calengil bade you pour the cleansing draught upon the ground at the base of two towers that remain standing in the ruins of Dol Ringwest.Calengil is in Duillond, east of Dol Ringwest.

You should return to Calengil and inform him that your task in the ruins of Dol Ringwest is complete.'The draught is ready -- all that remains is for it to be sprinkled upon the grounds within the ruins of Dol Ringwest. It will encourage and speed the growth of the natural vines that one often finds in such places -- so much so that by the end of the next spring the ruins will be buried in a great mass of them. In but a short time, they will reduce the ruins to naught but rubble, returning them to pristine nature once again.

'To you I offer the honour of this task, for I find now that I cannot bring myself to destroy the place that I once loved so, even in its decrepit state. Pour the draught onto the ground beneath the two towers that remain standing amongst the ruins.

'Time and the forces of nature will do the deed with no further help from us.''Dol Ringwest can be found to the west. Take the draught to the towers there.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. It pains me that I shall never again walk among the spires, which I remember from my youth, but better this than to leave Middle-earth with the knowledge that they are a home for creatures of darkness.'Nothing you have done for Adelard Took has appeared to have any effect whatsoever on the "ghost" in Adelard's library.The ghost's presence is strongest in the far corner of Adelard's library, near the small book-shelf.

After all else failed, Adelard Took has asked you to enter his library and confront the ghost of the Old Took.Confront the Old Took's ghostAdelard Took is outside the library in the Great Smials.

In confronting the "ghost" in Adelard Took's library, you discovered that it was nothing more than a squirrel hiding behind the book-case. You should tell Adelard that it is safe to return to his library.'I am simply at my wit's end! Nothing we have done has appeased the Old Took's ghost. I can think of nothing else to do. I will never have my library back. What to do, what to do....

'Wait... no, it's too terrible to ask! But I must have my library back. You have done so much for me already, but could I ask you to muster up your courage and face the Old Took's ghost yourself?

'With great caution, enter my library and perhaps -- since you have done so much to try and appease him -- the Old Took will grant you an audience. His presence seems to be strongest in the far corner of the room, by my small book-shelf. Do please be careful!''Please, my friend, confront the ghost of the Old Took in my library. Perhaps you can appease him!'As you near the shelf, it starts to shake and shiver. Something is hiding behind the book-shelf!'A squirrel? It was nothing more than a... a foul, grey squirrel? Oh my, this is embarrassing. What will others think if they hear about this?

'Oh, I know what they'll say! They'll say I'm as mad as old Bilbo. Dear, oh dear! Would it be too much to ask of you not to report this incident?

'I will be most pleased to put this business behind me! And to think of all the trouble I put you through. I am so sorry to have been such a bother!'Filibert Bolger told you that his cow, Daffodil, has gone missing, and he suspects that a dwarf named Olwir stole her.Troll's Knoll is in Rushock Bog, south-east of Needlehole.

Filibert suspects that Olwir took Daffodil out into Rushock Bog somewhere. He suggested you start searching at Troll's Knoll.Find DaffodilAs you searched Troll's Knoll on behalf of Filibert Bolger, you came across the corpse of a cow. A closer examination of the cow should reveal if it is Filibert's cow, Daffodil.Examine the cowFilibert Bolger can be found in Needlehole, north of Troll's Knoll.

In your examination of the dead cow you found atop Troll's Knoll, you came across a bell. Perhaps Filibert Bolger will be able to tell from the bell whether the cow you found was his Daffodil.'Gracious me, am I glad to see you! You see, my cow Daffodil, she's gone missing, and I suspect some foul play!

'Yesterday, a dwarf came by my farm. Olwir was his name, and he wanted to buy my Daffodil. Well, I couldn't sell her... she's the only cow I got. He didn't seem to take that well. I think he may have come back and stolen her!

'Now, I don't know where he might have taken her, but I do remember that his boots were caked in mud. I'll wager he was out tromping about in Rushock Bog! Maybe that's where he took her! Start looking at Troll's Knoll, south-east of here.''I am sure it was that dwarf, Olwir, who took my Daffodil! You've got to bring her back, if you can.

'If I were you, I would start searching atop Troll's Knoll. It's about the highest point in the Bog. From there, you might be able to spy something that'll lead you to my Daffodil!''You found a dead cow on top of Troll's Knoll? Oh, I'm hoping against hope that it isn't my Daffodil.

'If you could, please, take a closer look at that poor animal. If you find anything on it, bring it to me. Perhaps I can tell from what you find if it was my Daffodil or not.'This poor cow looks like it was attacked and partially eaten by a large beast of some kind. Around its neck you find a bronze bell.'Oh, aye, this is my Daffodil's bell. What could have attacked her so horribly, and why did that dwarf take her? Poor Daffodil, poor, poor thing....

'Someone needs to pay for this! Please, you need to do something.'There is much to do while travelling through the lands of Ered Luin.Complete Explorer of Ered Luin deedComplete Hero of Ered Luin deedComplete Slayer of Ered Luin deedGoblins defile the sanctity of a once sacred area of Ered Luin. Bregar wishes to see the goblins there purged so that sanctity may one day return.Make your way to the ruins of Dol Ringwest, west of Duillond, and purge the goblins who have infested them.

Bregar wants to see the sanctity of the ruins returned and asked you to destroy the goblins who dwell within the ruins of Dol Ringwest.Defeat Blue-crag goblins at Dol Ringwest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bregar is at Duillond, east of Dol Ringwest.

Goblins infested the ruins of Dol Ringwest, and you did your best to drive the creatures forth from there.Talk to Bregar at Duillond'Ancient battles were fought at the ruins of Dol Ringwest, and we had thought the evil purged. Now, goblins toil within the ruins and desecrate the memory of the place.

'I would ask that you do your best to clear the goblins from these ruins. It will ease my heart and perhaps aid my brother Toronn to leave in peace.

'You will find the goblins in residence of Dol Ringwest to the west of Duillond. Please, make your way there and drive these foul creatures from the ruins.''The memory of that place will always be one of melancholy. Knowing that the goblins have been purged restores a small amount of hope to me, ${PLAYER}.

'You have brought a timely resolution with regard to Dol Ringwest, and I thank you for this.''You will find the foul goblins within the ruins at Dol Ringwest, west of Duillond.'Bruner Stoutthrush, a disreputable seeming gentleman from Bree, has decided to do a good deed for the refugees from the Blackwold attacks.The brigands can be found in a large camp in the Yellow Tree Ruins, south of Staddle; but it may be that some others in the Chetwood also carry stolen items.

Whether as an act of beneficence or complete self-interest, Stoutthrush has asked you to collect stolen heirlooms from the brigands and bring them to him at Bree's Combe-gate.'Ah, what troubled times we live in. Brigands have been raiding people's homes in Archet, Staddle, and Combe. Deplorable! Some of the poor folk have made their way here to Bree and told me their sad tales.

'Now I'd like nothing more than to help them but I'm just not made for adventures. Why don't you track down these villains and bring the stolen family heirlooms to me. Then I can return them to the rightful owners, the poor wretches. Just think of the looks on their faces!

'I hear there are brigands encamped in the Yellow Tree Ruins, south of Staddle; but it may be that some others in the Chetwood are also carrying stolen items.''Ah, you've found them! That was a kind deed. Now, let's just hope that I can find the poor people from whom these treasured things were stolen.'Adelard Took's library in the Great Smial is being troubled by a "spirit", which he believes is the ghost of the Old Took.Bears can be found in the woods east of Tuckborough.

Adelard believes the ghost of the Old Took is upset by the troubles darkening the Shire of late, especially the recent aggressiveness of the bears. He has asked you to bring him a few bear pelts to prove to the Old Took that all is well in hand.'Oh thank goodness! I am in the sorriest of straits, but I must make you swear to tell no one else of my troubles. If others were to hear of it, there would surely be a panic in Tuckborough!

'My library is haunted! As difficult as it may be to believe, I think it is the ghost of the Old Took! I think the troubles darkening the Shire of late have disturbed him, like those bears over to the east of here... they were never so aggressive in his day!

'Wait, perhaps that is it! The Old Took was known for slaying a great bear in his time. If you could bring me the pelts of a few bears, maybe it will ease his spirit. It will show the Shire is still safe!''Oh good, you've found the pelts! Now I'll just have to put them in the library, and the Old Took's ghost will be calmed, I'm sure of it. He'll go back to his rest, and I'll get my library back.

'Thank you!'Bregedúr promised a cask of the finest vintage to Dolengyl, an Elf at the refuge of Duillond.The Elf-refuge of Duillond lies on the north road by the river.

Bregedúr has asked you to deliver a bottle of last year's vintage to his friend Dolengyl.'Before you leave, ${PLAYER}, I have one more boon to ask of you. I promised a bottle of last year's vintage to a friend at Duillond to the north, and my labours kept me too busy to fulfil that pledge. I hope this has not inconvenienced her.

'Could you deliver this bottle to Dolengyl for me? The refuge lies on the road that follows the river north beyond Limael's Vineyard.

'If you reach the dwarf-port of Kheledûl, you have travelled too far north. Perhaps you should make use of the horse from here to Duillond.''You are looking for Dolengyl of Duillond. The refuge is on the river, yes, but it is a far distance north of here. You want to head north across the tributary and past Limael's Vineyard. You would be wise to use the horse to reach Duillond.''Splendid! I must admit that I wondered if perhaps Bregedúr would come through on his promise. I should have known that he would not forget a friend.

'Ah, this vintage has the promise of ageing nicely. Perhaps in some thirty years, it will have aged sufficiently. You have my thanks.'Leecher Cartwell has ordered some supplies from Bruner Stoutthrush, who has in turn run out of stock.Hodric Bracegirdle lives on the forest side of Brandy Hall in Buckland.

The hobbit Hoderic Bracegirdle supplies Stoutthrush with the healing salve he sells to Leecher Cartwell.Collect a crate of oily salve from Hodric BracegirdleBruner Stoutthrush does business at the Combe-gate in Bree.

Hodric, not entirely happily, gave you the crate Bruner requested. You should bring it to Stoutthrush straight away.'Leecher Cartwell in Combe has been wasting his healing stores on any rabble or riff-raff that wander through his door. Now, he expects me to fill his stores! It will cost him more than a few pennies this time, I can tell you that!

'Travel over to Brandy Hall in Buckland and speak with a good-for-naught hobbit there by the name of Hodric Bracegirdle. Get a crate of that oily salve he makes and bring it back to me.

'That salve should satisfy the leech.''What's that? Oh, that villain Stoutthrush! He's been demanding one thing or another of me ever since I lost that wager to him.

'I suppose I can spare some salve. I'll have to make more soon or I'll run out.''Where have you been? Cartwell might have found another supply of salve by now.'Farmer Polo Proudfoot has had trouble with bears raiding his beehives and killing his bees.Farmer Proudfoot closed his hives to protect his bees from marauding honey-bears, but they cannot be kept closed or harm will still come to his bees. He has asked you to fend off any bears that are drawn to the honey.Protect Polo and fight off all the bearsNow that you've driven off the bears, talk to Polo Proudfoot again for your reward.'Hallo there! I wonder if you can help me out for a few minutes. I've had problems with bears from the hills nearby raiding my beehives for honey. I need someone who isn't afraid of bears to fend them off and protect the hives.

'My hives are right over there. The bears have killed the bees in all the hives except the middle one. I have it closed right now to protect the bees, but they'll be in trouble soon if the hives aren't opened. If you'll help me, I'll open the hive, and I'm sure the bears will soon return.''Ha! That was a sight to see! You did a good job with those bears, and you deserve a reward for your work!'Postman Cotton is delighted that you are helping the Quick Post service regain its reputation for speedy delivery of the mail and wants you to bring word of your efforts to Postman Oddfoot of Frogmorton, who has been rather depressed of late.Postman Oddfoot is in Frogmorton, east of Bywater.

Postman Cotton is concerned for his friend Oddfoot and wants you to bring word of your efforts to revitalize the Quick Post service in hopes that it will cheer him up.'The Quick Post service will surely live up to its name again if we continue at this rate, ${PLAYER}! There is something you can help me with, and maybe that will...

'Oh, don't start towards the mail satchels just yet! I'm actually on top of the deliveries for today and don't need you to take any of these anywhere. No, what I want you to do is to bring word to Postman Oddfoot in Frogmorton about our efforts to improve the speed at which we deliver the mail. He's been rather depressed lately -- hobbits in Frogmorton are not shy about expressing their complaints, and Oddfoot has always been one to take things rather to heart.

'Frogmorton is east of Bywater. Tell Oddfoot that we're repairing the reputation of the Quick Post service and offer him whatever help you can.''Frogmorton is to the east of Bywater, and you'll find Postman Oddfoot near the centre of town. To hear him talk, it sounds like you could just follow the trail of complaining hobbits! Cheer him up and help him with any deliveries he might need to make, if you have the time.''Hello there. I'm the postman for Frogmorton. I'm sorry for any inconvenience the Quick Post service may have caused you....

'What's that? You're not here to complain? Oh. Oh, I see. That's nice. Yes, I'm glad we haven't disappointed you today. I get so many complaints, you know. It does get to a hobbit, after a while.

'You say that Postman Cotton is trying to revitalize the Quick Post service and make it what it used to be? Even with all the letters that get sent these days? That's incredible news! If we can recapture our old reputation, maybe we won't need to spend so much time answering complaints!'Longo Burrows was of no help in discovering what has become of Gerebert Took, but Esilia thought of someone else you could speak with.Rollo Boffin is in Woodhall, east of Tuckborough on the Stock Road.

Since Longo Burrows was unhelpful in learning Gerebert's location, Esilia asked you to speak with Rollo Boffin. Since Rollo oversees much of the pipe-weed that passes through Woodhall, and Gerebert hid on a waggon carrying leaf that was travelling to the east, he may know something about Gerebert.'You see, I just had a thought about who else we could ask. My cousin Alda is married to Rollo Boffin in Woodhall. Some didn't consider it a wise marriage, myself included, but they seem happy enough.

'That, though, is neither here nor there. The importance of Woodhall is that much of the pipeweed from Tookland passes through there for other points in the Shire. Rollo happens to oversee much of that pipeweed.

'Perhaps, since Gerebert hid on a leaf-waggon travelling east, Rollo may know something of him. I must say, the less you discover, the more anxious about him I become! Rollo lives in Woodhall, east of Tuckborough on the Stock Road.''Esilia sent you my way, did she? Well, what a surprise! She didn't seem too fond of me after I married my Alda, but I suppose time heals all wounds, as they say.

'So you are looking for a hobbit who hid on one of Longo Burrow's leaf-waggons are you? Gerebert Took was the name? Well, it's funny you mention that, as I'm missing something myself, and I think they may be related.''Rollo Boffin is in Woodhall, which is east of Tuckborough on the Stock Road. He might know what happened to Gerebert, since Rollo has many dealings with the leaf-waggons that pass by Woodhall.'Toronn wants to leave Middle-earth and journey into the West to the Undying Lands, but will not leave as long as his brother, Bregar, refuses to leave.Bregar is at Duillond, north of Celondim.

Toronn has asked you to try to convince Bregar to accompany him into the West.'Long have my brother and I dwelt upon these shores and much have we seen in that time. Now the time has come for us to leave this place and sail into the West.

'My brother, however, does not see clearly and wishes to remain here. We have always dwelt together, and I could not consider a day in my life without his company and counsel. He is the cord which binds me to this Middle-earth. While he is of a mind to remain, I am forced to wait for him.

'If you would, go to Duillond and see if you can convince Bregar to join me here at Celondim. It is time we begin our journey. The refuge is north along the road.''My brother wishes to leave Middle-earth, but I believe it is time for us to stand our ground against the Shadow growing in the East. With your help, perhaps, Toronn will see reason.

'This Middle-earth which we love will soon face great peril, and we are bound to defend it. I cannot yet sail West.''Please persuade Bregar that he must leave this place, no matter his feelings towards it.'Lobelia Sackville-Baggins is planning a birthday party for herself grand enough to outshine that of Bilbo Baggins several years before. She wants fireworks worthy of her efforts.Hyacinth Took is in Tuckborough, west of the Great Smials.

Lobelia Sackville-Baggins has heard that Hyacinth Took knows the art of making fireworks and asked that you place an order for her biggest and brightest.Lobelia Sackville-Baggins is at her home at Bag End in Hobbiton.

Lobelia Sackville-Baggins sent you to order fireworks from Hyacinth Took, but Hyacinth informed you that she was out of both fireworks and the materials to make them. She told you to return to Hobbiton and make sure Lobelia will be expected to pay for the materials, if she still wants fireworks.Hyacinth Took is west of the Great Smials in Tuckborough.

Hyacinth Took sent you back to Lobelia Sackville-Baggins to request payment for the ingredients to make her fireworks. Lobelia reluctantly agreed and gave you a coinpurse to take back to Hyacinth.'You there! Yes, I mean you. Come over here. I've work for you.

'I simply must have fireworks for my birthday party. More and brighter than that mad Bilbo ever had! I hear that Hyacinth Took over in Tuckborough has learned to make them, no doubt from that queer Gandalf fellow. You go over there and tell her I want a dozen large crates of her best fireworks! She lives west of the Great Smials.

'Of course, I'll pay you if you insist. What a nuisance. I thought Bounders -- or whatever you are -- were supposed to do for us Shire-folk out of duty.''Well? I'm not paying you to stand around, you know. Hurry over to that Hyacinth Took and get those fireworks! She lives in Tuckborough, west of the Great Smials!''Oh really? Fireworks for Lobelia Sackville-Baggins, is it? I'm almost happy to be able to tell you that I'm out of both fireworks and the ingredients to make them. The truth is, I made up a whole batch recently, but it was stolen! And the Bounders haven't been much help getting it back, begging your pardon.

'If Lobelia really wants fireworks for her party, there will be a lot of purchases she has to make. There's charcoal, saltpetre, brimstone, and iron filings to buy, among other things. So you go back to Lobelia and make sure she's willing to pay for all this.

'If she still wants them, come back here, and I'll lay out all the things you need to do.''Lobelia probably won't want to pay for the ingredients. I'm not sorry none, either. You go tell her that, up in Bag End.''Pay for the ingredients? Why! I never...!

'Oh, I suppose I must, if all her stock was stolen. Here, take these coins to that Took. These had better be the best fireworks the Shire has ever seen!''Mind you, don't even think about stealing any of those coins. I have my eye on you, and I'll keep an eye on that Took, too! Find her at her home west of the Great Smials, in Tuckborough.''So, the old crow actually paid? I'm astonished. She must really want these fireworks.

'Well, I'll see what I can do.'Hal Hornblower wants light carapaces. Hal can be found near the stable in the centre of Hobbiton.You have accepted a task to acquire light carapaces for the bounders of the Shire. They have deputized Hal Hornblower to collect the items near the stables in Hobbiton.Wanted: Light carapaces from insects and spiders infesting the Shire. Bounders are looking for proof of those who are assisting them in keeping the Shire safe. Deliver the items to Hal Hornblower at Hobbiton centre.Wanted: Light carapaces from insects and spiders infesting the Shire.'These look like they came from some nasty creatures. Looks like you are really helping out.

'Thank you, kindly.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Hal Hornblower wants matted skins. Hal can be found near the stable in the centre of Hobbiton.You have accepted a task to acquire matted skins for the Bounders of the Shire. They have deputized Hal Hornblower to collect the items near the stables in Hobbiton.Wanted: Matted skins from the beasts overrunning the Shire. Bounders are looking for proof of those who are assisting them in keeping the Shire safe. Deliver the items to Hal Hornblower at Hobbiton centre.Wanted: Matted skins from the beasts overrunning the Shire.'Oh goodness, what is that? It's all stiff and leathery. I guess this is what the Bounders wanted.

'Thank you, kindly.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Gail Catchpole's father perished in the flames of The Mad Badger Inn, and many of their belongings were stolen by the Blackwold brigands.Constable Wren can be found at the guard-house on the hill east of Combe.

Gail wants to find the brigands who stole her dead father's favourite fishing pole and retrieve it. She has sent you to ask Constable Wren for information about the brigands and where they might have taken her stolen goods.The main encampment of the Blackwolds is in the Chetwood, north of the guard-house.

Constable Wren suggested that the brigand who looted the fishing pole belonging to Gail Catchpole's dead father may be near the watering hole beneath the Blackwold main encampment.'I'm sorry, my mind is miles away. I didn't see you there. Did you help fight off the brigands? My dad did, he... he....' Gail chokes back a sob.

'During the Blackwolds' raid on Archet, someone broke into our house and stole many of our things. I don't care about most of them, but they took my dad's favourite fishing pole! I don't care if I get anything else back, but he wouldn't have wanted some filthy brigand to have it.

'Now that I've moved here to Combe, I've been meaning to ask Constable Wren if she could track down that fishing pole for me. Could you ask her if she has any idea where it might have been taken? She'll be at the guard-house on the hill east of Combe.''I just know Constable Wren will have some idea where the brigand who stole my father's fishing pole has gone! She's usually out in front of the guard-house on the hill east of Combe. Please talk to her.''I have heard that many of the Blackwold brigands, after looting Archet, fled into the Chetwood. It seems that the Blackwold leaders are angry. They feel that the raid might have been more successful if their followers had been less focused on filling their pockets and more on acting together.

'The main encampment is east down the road and then deep into the northern woods. I suspect that many of the Blackwolds can be found within that camp.

'Mayhaps if you search in that area, you might find Gail's lost fishing pole.''Gail will be pleased, I am sure, if you recovered her father's fishing pole.''You've found it! Oh, thank you, thank you!

'I've been thinking that the pole should be given to the waters of my dad's favourite fishing hole: the pond near the Hunter's Lodge in Archet. I think he'd like that.

'Thank you... thank you again!'The Blackwold brigands seized Old Bauman's farm during the early days of their uprising.Old Bauman's farm lies far to the east of Combe, beyond the brigand camps in the Chetwood, at the end of the eastward path. Old Bauman is at the logging camp, south of the Chetwood, east of Combe.

Old Bauman lost his farm to the Blackwolds when they retreated from Archet, and he would like you to go there and retrieve his Sally's chain for him.'Have you heard that Archet gave them Blackwold villains what-for? Kicked 'em right out, they did, and good on 'em! If little old Archet can manage it, I say Combe can do one better, and sweep them Blackwolds out o' the Chetwood for good!

'Now I lost my Sally's chain when them brigands took over my farm. She's been gone for many a year, but that chain always did bring me comfort. One o' them Blackwolds probably picked it up, and I want it back! Farm's far to the east -- just follow the road past all them brigand campfires.

'Eh, what's that? No, it's a chain, not a necklace. What a queer question.''You found my Sally's chain and showed those Blackwold villains a thing or two, I don't doubt it! A lifetime o' thanks, ${PLAYER}!

'Ah, Sally was a good hound. We'd go hunting in the fall, and she could sniff out a coney from what seemed near a mile! It's good to have her chain back. It's all I've got left o' her, now.

'Take these coins for your trouble, ${PLAYER}, with my thanks.'Belco Brockhouse found a copy of the Founding Writ of the Shire, but will not give it up until he has received some services in return.Belco Brockhouse's pig, Old Sally, may be found near the big willow south-east of Belco's farm.

Belco has asked you to find his pig, Old Sally, and bring her back to his barn. He warned you that she spooks easily, and if she gets too scared, she may run away.Find Old SallyBelco Brockhouse can be found south of the Tuckborough town centre.

You should speak with Belco Brockhouse and let him know that you led his pig, Old Sally, back to his barn.'My pig, Old Sally, has run off again. Sometimes I think that pig is more trouble than she's worth. Always running off, eating like a horse and scared o' her own shadow! If I weren't so fond o' her, I would have made sausage out of her years ago!

'Usually when she runs off, it's down to the woods south-east o' here, by the big willow. If you find her, approach her carefully and bring her back to the barn here.

'Be careful though, she spooks easily, so if she sees anything while you are bringing her back, she might run off, and this time for good!''Ah, good, the old girl is back. She's a nuisance at times, that one, but in the end I suppose I'm too fond of her to do much else with 'er.

'Thanks for doing that, but I suppose I owe the real thanks to that Writ I found, don't I?''If you are wanting that Writ, you need to find my pig, Old Sally. When she runs off, she's usually found to the south-east o' here, not far from the big willow.

'Now approach her carefully, she's rather skittish. And make sure no critters get too close to her, she's likely to spook. And if she gets too spooked, she may run away for good!'The pig cautiously snorts your hand, but seems satisfied that you mean her no harm. She looks like she is ready to return to Belco's barn.With the thickets removed from the canal, the waterflow has been restored to Noglond in the Vale of Thráin.Otkell is in Gondamon, east down the road from Noglond, and south at the first crossing.

Geitir has asked you to inform Otkell in Gondamon about the restoration of the canal.'This canal water is used down in Gondamon in the Low-lands as well as here in the Vale of Thráin. You should go down there and make sure they know we removed the blockage up here.

'Travel down the road to the east, then turn south at the first crossing and Gondamon will be right there. You will want to talk to old Otkell.

'Their cisterns must be nearly dry down there, what with the blockage as bad as it was!''You restored the waterflow? Why it's not flowing nearly enough at all! You may have cleared out some problems over at Noglond, but there must be something else blocking the flow around here.''Gondamon is easy to find. Just take the road east, then turn south at the first crossing.'Bruner Stoutthrush, a merchant in Bree, has asked you to deliver an order to two of his customers.Roger Hawkling can be found at Adso Haybank's camp along the Great East Road, west of Bree, north of the Old Forest.

Stoutthrush wants you to bring the cask of pipe-weed to Roger Hawkling.'There's a pair of fine gentlemen, Mr. Larkspur and Mr. Hawkling, what have taken up residence at Adso Haybank's camp, along the Great East Road north of the Old Forest.

'Yes, sir, fine gentlemen indeed! Hunters of game, great and small. Last time they were through here, Mr. Hawkling asked me to procure them a bit of pipe-weed.

'If you'd be so kind, deliver this cask to them with all due haste. I'm sure Mr. Hawkling will tip you if you're quick about it.''So, that ill-favoured fellow, Stoutthrush, finally came through with our pipe-weed. Looks like I owe you for that wager, Larkspur!'Posco Burrows is concerned that his uncle, Filbert Burrows, has gone deep into the Chetwood to 'have a word' with the Blackwold brigands and wants to make sure he has not gotten himself into trouble.Filbert Burrows should be somewhere along the road east of Combe heading towards the Chetwood.

Posco Burrows has asked you to look for his uncle, Filbert, and make sure he is unharmed.Cole Sickleleaf is at the ruins between the main Blackwold encampment and Skunkwood's Farm.

You found Posco Burrow's uncle, Filbert, sitting on a stump at the cross-roads in the Chetwood. He wants you to collect a handkerchief taken by Cole Sickleleaf.Filbert Burrows is waiting at the cross-roads in the Chetwood.

You should return Filbert Burrow's handkerchief to him and convince him to leave the area.Posco Burrows is waiting for you at the Lumber Camp by Combe.

Filbert Burrows, determined to remain where he is until the Blackwolds relent, has asked you to return to Combe to tell his nephew, Posco Burrows, that he is fine.'My Uncle Filbert and I were having tea and discussing the state of things in Bree-land -- about how the folk in Archet showed the Blackwold brigands a thing or two -- when Uncle Filbert stood up and said, "Someone ought do something about these villains. I'm going to give them a piece of my mind." And then he left, without even finishing his tea!

'Up the road in the woods east of this camp, past the brigands' watch-fires, there's some ruins where the Blackwolds are holed up. Uncle Filbert has probably gone there to have a word with them. Though I don't think he will make the full journey, he's not as young as he once was.

'If he has, he's likely got himself into trouble. I dare go no further to search for him, but could you go look for him and make sure he's all right?''Uncle Filbert is probably sitting on a stump or rock right now! I would wager he never made it by the split in the road!''Finally, someone respectable! I was beginning to think no one out here in the woods had any manners! I simply couldn't stand by any longer while the Blackwolds have their way in the Chetwood! I marched right in and told them just what I think of their sort.

'They laughed me right out of their camp! "Go back to Hobbiton, little boy!" they said to me! I've never been spoke to like this, never! I wanted to leave, something in that big ruin is just a bit off, I say!

'One ruffian, Cole Sickleleaf -- he used to be a nice boy -- took my handkerchief. Could you bring it back to me? He ran off to the ruins all the way to the east, between the frightening ruins to the north and that Skunkwood's farm.''Have you got my handkerchief yet?''You, at least, have some decency. I thank you very much for returning my handkerchief and bid you a good day, as civilized folk are wont to do!

'I'm going to stay here and keep an eye on these impolite troublemakers. Maybe it's the Tookish blood I get from my mother's side of the family, but it'll take more than insults to send me back to town unsatisfied! Perhaps my presence here will remind these ruffians what it means to live in Bree-land!

'If you can tell my nephew, Posco, that I'm fine, I'd appreciate it. Good day!''I'm going to keep an eye on these Blackwold villains. I don't trust 'em one bit! You go back to the Lumber Camp by Combe and tell my nephew Posco that everything's fine, and I'll be back soon.''It's good to hear that Uncle Filbert is all right. He always says that I'll develop good hobbit-sense when I get older, but if he's any example, I'm not sure I will!

'Thank you for looking in on him, ${PLAYER}.'Rothgar is concerned about the ominous words you heard from the Dourhand burglar and feels Mathi Stouthand, Lord of Gondamon, should be told that trouble is brewing.Mathi Stouthand can be found on the upper levels of Gondamon, along the road east of Noglond.

Rothgar has asked you to deliver word to Mathi Stouthand that the goblins and the Dourhands are planning some new treachery, while he delivers the stolen gold back to Dwalin.'That Dourhand burglar said that his folk paid the goblins well to steal a prince? I don't know what that means, but it can't be good!

'Mathi Stouthand became the chief of Gondamon, the great watch-post of the Low-lands, shortly after the Dourhands were driven from Thorin's Hall. If there is a war brewing, Mathi needs to be warned so he can begin the preparations.

'Follow the road east to Gondamon. There, I expect you'll find Mathi on the upper levels. Travel with great haste, ${PLAYER}! I would quicken your feet with a tale of great deeds, but I see that there is no time to spare!''Mathi Stouthand is the Lord of Gondamon and must be given warning that the goblins and the Dourhands are up to something. War could be brewing, and the forces of Gondamon will need to be prepared!

'Follow the road east to the fortress. I am sure you will find Mathi on the upper levels!''You could not have arrived with this news at a better time, ${PLAYER}. An Elf-prince has gone missing, and the Elves are convinced that we abducted him and refuse to believe otherwise! We have learned where their prince is being held... an encampment of Dourhands to the north-east.

'Your information tells us a great deal about his fate, and I hope it is enough. The Elves have sent an emissary to Gondamon, and she insists that we rescue this Avorthal as a sign of our goodwill. A sign of our goodwill! As if the Longbeards need to prove anything!

'I have always considered myself an even-tempered dwarf, but this emissary has gone too far. We need someone who is neither dwarf nor Elf to organize this rescue. I do not want to be responsible for an outbreak of war in the Blue Mountains.'The goblin Pampraush let slip the knowledge that Avorthal was not slain, but handed over to wicked dwarves. Cardavor was further embittered by this news and is prepared to declare open war against the dwarves of Ered Luin to reclaim his son.Dorongúr Whitethorn can be found at the refuge of Duillond, north of Celondim.

While Cardavor is relieved that Avorthal still lives, he is prepared to wage war upon all the Dwarves of Ered Luin to rescue his son. He has asked you to inform Dorongúr Whitethorn of Avorthal's captivity in hopes that Dorongúr will muster a force to reclaim the Elf-prince.'You have done so much for me already, ${PLAYER}, but there is still much that must be done if my son is to be restored. We have not had dealings with the dwarves for a very long time, and those are not pleasant memories.

'My people have had poor relations with the dwarves for years, and now there is news that one of them has aligned with some Ancient Evil? Dwarves are scheming and self-serving, not to be trusted!

'We must gather our strength to lay siege to the dwarves of Ered Luin and rescue Avorthal from their clutches, but only Dorongúr Whitethorn, the Master of Duillond has the authority to muster such a force. Bring him the news of my son, that he is alive, but a prisoner. We must strike at the dwarves before it is too late!

'Speak with Toronn at the stable before you go. He will hasten you upon your journey.''There is little time to spare, ${PLAYER}! The wretched dwarves may not keep Avorthal alive for long. Go to Master Dorongúr at Duillond, to the north, and tell him that he must assemble a force of Elves to move against the dwarves at once!

'Speak with Toronn about a horse to Duillond.''Cardavor was wise to send you to me. You should take a horse to the sanctuary at Duillond. They are swift and can cover distances more swiftly than our own feet. Speak with the stable master and he will see you carried on the back of a swift horse.

'Move quickly, Avorthal's life is in the balance.''Your news is troubling, ${PLAYER}. For dwarves to work peacefully with goblins is unusual enough, but to conspire in the abduction of an Elf-prince seems foolhardy, even for them.

'I will not call our warriors to arms just yet. Cardavor is full of anger, which is to be expected, but as Master of Duillond it is my duty to exercise restraint.

'If the dwarves have indeed taken Avorthal, we will fall upon them with such fury that the mountains shall shake at our passing; but this could also be a trick of the goblins. They would have much to gain from a war between Elves and dwarves.'Rothgar told you about the old Dourhand city to the west of Noglond, but does not know why the Dourhands would bring the stolen gold into it -- the city was overrun by goblins two years earlier.The old Dourhand city lies to the west of Noglond, up a flight of steps carved into the mountains.

Rothgar has confirmed the existence of an old stronghold of the Dourhands, now goblin-infested, near Noglond. If the thrushes are correct, the Dourhands brought the stolen gold into the city.Find stolen Longbeard goldRothgar is at Noglond, east of the old Dourhand city, along the road that runs through the Vale of Thráin.

You have recovered the stolen gold and should return it to Rothgar for delivery, as Dwalin instructed.'The thrushes saw the Dourhands carrying this stolen gold into the old Dourhand city to the west? That is very peculiar. You see, it has been infested with goblins for the past two years!

'I don't know why the Dourhands would bring the gold into a goblin-held city, even if they once called it home. Most peculiar. It reminds me of the tale of...

'I am sorry. You want to head west to the old Dourhand city and search it for the stolen Longbeard gold, I expect. It won't be easy, but I'll be waiting to hear of your exploits! Head west of Noglond and look for the stairs carved into the mountainside... and watch out for the goblins!''The old Dourhand city where the dwarves brought the stolen Longbeard gold is to the west of Noglond. Just look for the stairs carved into the mountainside. You'll want to watch out for goblins, of course.''Well done, ${PLAYER}, well done indeed! I will deliver this gold to Dwalin at Thorin's Halls, but it sounds to me like you have a more urgent errand to undertake!'Maida Woodwright had an argument with her son Covell, and she has not seen him since. The Blackwold activity in the area has made her nervous, and she is seeking news of him.Constable Wren is at the guard-house, east of Combe.

Maida Woodwright has asked that you speak with Constable Wren regarding the whereabouts of her son, Covell.Covell may be found at one of the Blackwold camps north and east of the Combe lumber camp.

Maida Woodwright sent you to speak with Constable Wren, who suggested that Covell joined the Blackwolds and would likely be found near one of their camps in the Chetwood.Talk to Covell WoodwrightConstable Wren patrols near the guard-house on the hill south of the lumber camp and east of Combe.

You discovered Covell Woodwright on the path leading through the Chetwood, and he attacked you. Though you defeated him, he escaped deeper into the woods. Constable Wren will want to hear of your encounter with the brigand.Maida Woodwright is back in Combe.

Maida Woodwright must be told that her son Covell has joined the Blackwold brigands.'Pardon me, do you think I could take up some o' your time? I haven't had any word o' me son Covell since this brigand nonsense began, and I'm mighty scared that he got caught up in some trouble.

'We lived in Archet till recently, but we had an argument -- I'm sure ye know how boys are -- and Covell left all in a huff. He said he would make his own way, down in Combe, and that's the last I heard o' him. Now that I've come to Combe, I hear he's gone east!

'If ye don't mind, could ye talk to Constable Wren for me? She watches the road east out o' Combe, and maybe she's seen Covell pass.''I hope Covell didn't get into any trouble! Constable Wren may have seen him pass. She watches the road east out of Combe.''Looking for Covell Woodwright, are you? I've heard something about the boy, but I can't say his mother is going to like it.

'He's joined up with the Blackwolds. He hadn't been in Combe for long when they took him, either. He tried finding work around town, but he didn't have the stamina for hard labour.

'If you can talk to him, you might convince him to give up his new line of "work," but I doubt it. I wager you'll find him east of Combe, in the Chetwood. Just follow the path from the lumber camp north and east... you're sure to come across a Blackwold camp or two up there.''Covell Woodwright is probably with his Blackwold friends in the Chetwood, east of here. It could be that you will convince him to give up his lawless ways, but I rather doubt it.''Joined up with them Blackwolds? What's a mother to do! I hope ye can find him and convince him to give up them thieving ways!''What's that? Me mother sent you to find me?

'I... I don't care! I've never been good at anything in my life, but now I've found something I can do and do right good! You're going to regret coming into Blackwold territory!''I do hope Covell hasn't gotten into any trouble. Constable Wren at the guard-house on the hill east of Combe might know something.''You fought with Covell Woodwright, but he escaped? Well, his sort will not be able to flee forever. I feel the time of the Blackwold brigands is coming to an end.

'It seems I was right, and he will never give up his lawlessness. His mother will not be pleased to hear it.''It will not be easy, but you must tell Maida that her son has joined the Blackwold brigands. She should know the truth.''What? Covell has joined those villains in truth? I refuse to believe it! He's a good boy, even if he has a temper. He's a Woodwright, through and through, and would never do such a thing! Ye shouldn't say such horrible things, and to an old woman!

'Ah, what am I saying? I knew the boy had landed hisself in a spot o' trouble. Thank ye... thank ye at the least for finding him.'Belco Brockhouse found a copy of the Founding Writ of the Shire, but will not give it up until he has received some services in return.Field stones can be found south of Longo Burrow's farm near the big willow. Belco lives north-west of the willow, on the upper slopes of Tuckborough.

Belco Brockhouse's fences need mending, and he has asked you to gather stones from the field for him to use in patching them.'You see them coneys running all over my garden there? Since all them holes appeared in my stone fences, I can't keep the devils out. I've been wanting to gather up some new field stones to patch them up, but haven't found the time yet to do it.

'There's a great big willow down the hill and to the south-east, directly south of Longo Burrow's farm -- you can find many stones o' different sizes down there. Bring me a variety o' them, if you would. Never know what I'll need to patch the fences!

'Hurry along now, or I'll be giving the Writ to the coneys!''These stones will do nicely for my fences. Never thought I'd find the time to gather them up, but it seems things are changing a bit for me since finding that old Writ!'With the passing of Black Riders from the East, the disease-bearing sickle-flies of the Midgewater Marshes have begun to breed more rapidly, threatening to spread contagion among the inhabitants of Bree-land. You are tasked with ending the threat of the sickle-flies' plague.Defeat sickle-flies in Bree-landWith the passing of Black Riders from the East, the disease-bearing sickle-flies of the Midgewater Marshes have begun to breed more rapidly, threatening to spread contagion among the inhabitants of Bree-land. You are tasked with ending the threat of the sickle-flies' plague.Defeat sickle-flies in Bree-landThere are many villainous monsters roaming Ered Luin, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many brigands in Ered LuinSlay many goblins in Ered LuinSlay many hendrevail in Ered LuinSlay many spiders in Ered LuinSlay many wolves in Ered LuinAn ancient spider-queen has pursued Atli Spider-bane to Archet and invaded Cal Sprigley's farm.Sprigley's farm is south of Bronwe's Folly. One entrance to the spider tunnels lies through the cellar of Sprigley's shed, while the other is through the cave mouth due west of the Hunter's Lodge.

To prevent Iornaith's brood from overrunning Archet, Atli Spider-bane has asked you to find and slay the spider-queen. Atli suggests searching the spider caves beneath Sprigley's farm for a secret entrance into the Iornaith's lair.Defeat IornaithAtli Spider-bane can be found at the north end of Archet, west of the spider-cave, north-west of Sprigley's farm.

You should take news of Iornaith's defeat to Atli Spider-bane.Talk to Atli Spider-bane in Archet'This spider-queen -- Iornaith by name -- and her ways are known to me. She will have hidden herself in Sprigley's house and blocked all the entrances, save one.

'If you search the tunnels below the house, I would wager you will find a hidden passage leading to Iornaith's lair. The vile thing must be slain, or Archet will be overrun by her brood.

'Would that I were hale and could heft an axe! But that time has passed. Now, the mantle of Spider-bane must pass to you, if you'll have it. I wish you well in facing her.''This spider is clever. Seek the entrance to her lair beneath Sprigley's farm. And beware her fangs! Though I ruined her eyes, she is ancient and full of malice.''"Many seeds did the Dread-weaver sow throughout our mountains...."

'Because of you, another of those seeds has passed from the world.

'I owe you a great debt... for Iornaith's death and for my life. Accept this reward, and with it, the friendship of Atli Spider-bane!'You slew a spider-queen that invaded the caves beneath Archet.Atli Spider-bane is in Archet.

You fought and defeated Iornaith, a spider of great power, while searching the tunnels west of Archet. Knowing that the dwarf, Atli, is often referred to as the Spider-bane, you should bring proof of your deeds back to Archet to show to the dwarf.Talk to Atli Spider-bane in ArchetThis brood-queen is far more fearsome than any spider you have come across before and seems to be manipulating many of the events around Archet.

The dwarf Atli is known as the Spider-bane. He would likely want to see proof of this creature's demise.'This spider-queen -- Iornaith by name -- and her ways are known to me.  

'You have done the people of this town many great services, this one not the least of all. Were she allowed to endure, it is likely all the peoples of Bree-land might have suffered her spawn.

'Take a quick perusal of these items I have. You have earned your pick of them.'Defeat spiders in Ered Luin.Defeat spiders in Ered LuinDefeat many Spiders in Ered Luin.Defeat spiders in Ered LuinHolly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to retrieve them before they are eaten. Sapphira Bolger of Budgeford had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Sapphira Bolger has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Sapphira Bolger's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'Oh, I see you are interested in that pie. It was baked by Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton! Usually they smell delicious, but that one smells a bit strange, for some reason.

'Ah, spoiled berries... so that's why it smells a bit funny. Thank you for telling me, friend! Would you mind taking the pie back to Holly in Hobbiton? I certainly don't want a pie baked with bad berries! Her home is north of the main square in Hobbiton.

'Oh, and tell Holly to not work herself to death. Poor thing works night and day making those pies of hers!''Go ahead and take that pie there to Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton. Poor thing, she was making quite a name for herself with those pies of hers. If anyone eats those spoiled pies, her reputation may be ruined!'Holly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Myrtle Oddfoot of Frogmorton had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Myrtle Oddfoot has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Myrtle Oddfoot's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'I see you are looking at that pie there. It's from Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton -- she makes such wonderful pies, you know. It is a special treat for my husband tonight. I suppose, though, I could spare a slice, if you would like one.

'What did you say? Bad berries? How horrible! Please, take it away! Take it back to Holly! Her home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

'Oh dear, tonight's dinner is ruined. Please tell her to hurry and bake another!''Oh dear, please do hurry! Take that pie back to Holly Hornblower in Hobbiton. I do hope she has another pie for me soon...dinner will be ruined without a pie!'Holly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Primrose Proudfoot of Stock had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the main square of Hobbiton.

Primrose Proudfoot has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Primrose Proudfoot's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'What can I help you with today, Bounder? A piece of pie, perhaps? It is a fine looking pie, isn't it? I have to say, it does smell a bit off, though....

'Bad berries, is it? I told you it smelled a bit off. Well, I suppose you should take it back to Holly in Hobbiton. Her home is north of the main square of Hobbiton.

'Oh, and tell her that I don't have any hard feelings about it. Mistakes happen!''If you are looking for that pie to take back to Holly in Hobbiton, it's just over there on the table.'Holly Hornblower of Hobbiton baked pies using spoiled berries and has asked you to bring any of the bad pies you find back to her. Daisy Hornblower of Woodhall had one such pie.Holly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

Daisy Hornblower has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers.Collect Daisy Hornblower's pieAvoid hungry hobbits'Good day to you! Are you hungry? Could I offer you a bit of pie, perhaps? It was baked by my sister, Holly Hornblower, of Hobbiton. She's a wonderful cook!

'Bad berries? Oh, that poor thing! She's been fraying at the edges dealing with all the people wanting her pies. She should learn to say, "No" when people come about asking for one. Well I suppose you should take that pie there back to her in Hobbiton. Her home is north of the Hobbiton main square.

'Tell her she needs to rest some!''Poor Holly's pie is over there on the table. Go ahead and take it back to her in Hobbiton.'An inhabitant of Swanfleet has posted a task to collect broken sword sheaths.You have accepted a task to acquire broken sword sheaths.Wanted: Broken sword sheaths from brigands and other disreputable folk in Swanfleet. Suitable reward offered upon delivery!Wanted: Broken sword sheaths from brigands and other disreputable folk in Swanfleet. Suitable reward offered upon delivery!You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.An inhabitant of Swanfleet has posted a task to collect light carapaces.You have accepted a task to acquire light carapaces.Wanted: Light carapaces from the spiders, sickle-flies, bog-lurkers, and Neekerbreekers of Swanfleet. Suitable reward offered upon delivery!Wanted: Light carapaces from the spiders, sickle-flies, bog-lurkers, and Neekerbreekers of Swanfleet. Suitable reward offered upon delivery!You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.While searching Troll's Knoll for Filibert Bolger's cow Daffodil, you came across the poor creature, dead. She was the apparent victim of some sort of large beast. Filibert blames the dwarf, Olwir, for both stealing the cow and leaving her out in the bog.Bounder Chubb can be found on the south side of Needlehole.

Filibert Bolger, angered by the death of his cow, has asked you to speak with Bounder Chubb about the incident.'That Olwir has to pay for stealing my Daffodil and for leaving her out in the bog to be killed like that.

'The dwarves who pass through Needlehole may not pay any mind to ordinary hobbits, but I reckon they'll listen to a Bounder of the Watch! You go tell Bounder Chubb about this, and maybe you two can keep that dwarf from getting away with this!

'Bounder Chubb is on the south side of Needlehole. Tell him about my poor Daffodil and do something about this Olwir!''What? Filibert's cow is dead, and he suspects a dwarf? This is outrageous!

'Most of the dwarves who pass through here are an agreeable lot, but lately there's been more than a few rascals about. I don't know this Olwir, but it wouldn't surprise me if he was one of that bad lot.

'The problem is I can't go off accusing dwarves of being thieves without proof. That would upset the whole lot, and we'd probably never find the one responsible. What to do....''Please go speak to Bounder Chubb here in Needlehole. He needs to do something about what happened to my poor Daffodil!'A big black bear has decided to make Hart Holeman's woodpile its home, causing Hart no end of trouble.Hart Holeman's wood pile is to the north, beyond the wall and a small logging camp.

Hart Holeman is willing to provide the charcoal Hyacinth Took requested, but first he wants you to drive off a big black bear that has made his wood pile its home.Hart Holeman is at his home in the centre of Overhill.

Hart Holeman had asked you to deal with the big black bear that had taken up residence in his wood pile, while he put together a parcel of charcoal for Hyacinth Took. He will be pleased to learn that the bear will no longer trouble him.Hyacinth Took is in Tuckborough near the Great Smials.

While you were away, dealing with the big black bear at Hart Holeman's wood pile, Hart was busy putting together a parcel of charcoal for you to take back to Hyacinth Took.'This is my problem. There's a lot of bears in the north woods. Usually, I have no trouble with them. You just stay out of their way, and they'll stay out of yours, so to speak. But I have a big wood pile I've spent some time gathering, and a really big black bear has decided it's the perfect place for him and his kind to live.

'The big black bear is very dangerous, and I can't get near my wood pile anymore. If you can help me out by getting rid of it so I can get at my wood, I'll be happy to make up a parcel of charcoal for your friend Hyacinth.

'My wood pile is almost due north of here, past the wall and a small logging camp. You'll probably find that black bear right on top of it.''Please get rid of that big black bear! It's right by my wood pile, directly north of here, I expect!''You killed him? I don't generally hold with hunting our local bears just to be rid of them, but that big black bear was dangerous, let me tell you!

'Here, take this parcel of charcoal back to young Hyacinth, with my courtesy and respect.''You should bring that charcoal down to Hyacinth, now that you've got it. She lives in Tuckborough, east of the Great Smials, if I remember right.''Ah, this will do nicely. I hope old Hart didn't give you a difficult time?

'Well now, we should be about our next bit of business....'According to Filibert Bolger, his cow, Daffodil, was stolen by a dwarf named Olwir; however, Bounder Chubb hesitates to accuse a dwarf of cow-theft without evidence.Ulfar is at the dwarf buildings north of Needlehole.

In order to avoid angering the dwarves with accusations of theft, Bounder Chubb told you to obtain the aid of the dwarves through their overseer, Ulfar. Chubb believes that Ulfar might be able to point out any potential thieves among his folk.The dwarf-hunters prowl the northern and eastern sections of Rushock Bog. The bog lies to the south-east of Needlehole.

When you told Ulfar the tale of Filibert's cow, and Olwir's involvement, he wasn't surprised. A number of dwarves of low character have been passing through Needlehole lately, and Olwir seemed to be the worst of them. Ulfar has asked you to acquire letters from the dwarf-hunters that he suspects of working for Olwir.'I've got it! There's a dwarf by the name of Ulfar, with whom I've had some dealings in the past. He might be of some help. I think he's a sort of overseer for the dwarves, or some such.

'In fact, just the other day there was a bit of a tussle between two of his folk, and Ulfar waded in and broke it up. The other dwarves seemed to respect him, so he might know something about his people here that will be of use to us.

'You should be able to find Ulfar up among the dwarf buildings north of Needlehole. Tell him what you told me, and hopefully he'll be able to help us.''Aye, it doesn't surprise me that Olwir is involved in this. A number of dwarves passing through lately are of low character, and he's the worst!

'I wish I could tell you where he was, but I've not seen him about for a few days. Those other dwarves might've seen him. In fact, just the other day, I saw a bunch of them crowding around a parchment of some sort. I didn't catch what they were talking about, but I did hear Olwir's name mentioned.

'That parchment could have been their orders. If you could go out to Rushock Bog and acquire a few of those letters from the dwarf-hunters out there, we might learn what Olwir is up to.''The dwarf Ulfar seems to be an overseer or some such over the dwarves in Needlehole. You should speak to him among the dwarf-buildings on the north side of town and see if he can help.''So Ulfar suspects this Olwir leads those rascally dwarves? Well they did seem a bit organized, so it wouldn't surprise me at all.

'Perhaps if you can find those orders Ulfar spoke of on one of the dwarf hunters or trappers, you might find out where Olwir is, and he can be made to pay for his crime!''Aye, good, you've found them. As I told you, that bunch is up to no good! Now, hand the letters over, I'd like to look over them....

'The fools! These orders you found weren't written by Olwir. Some dwarf named Skorgrím promises riches if Olwir can deliver -- I hardly believe it -- a Stone-troll! I've paid no mind to the old wives' tales of such creatures in the Bog, but Olwir must have listened and promised one as a gift.

'I cannot imagine what a dwarf would want with such a vile creature, but it can't be for any good purpose.'Ponto Hopsbloom, innkeeper of The Floating Log in Frogmorton, is entering the Four Farthings Brewing-moot.Frog Hops grow in the marsh north of Frogmorton. The Floating Log Inn is in Frogmorton, south of the Frogmoors.

Ponto Hopsbloom has asked you to pick some Frog Hops for his famous beer.'Welcome to The Floating Log! I'm sure you'll be wanting a draught of my Toad's Tongue brew, won't you? Say, you're that one what's been helping folks around here, aren't you? Maybe you can help me out some too.

'You see, the Four Farthings Brewing-moot is coming up, and I want to win this year! So I'm going to need some of our famous hops from the fens here, Frog Hops we call 'em.

'Well, anyways, these hops grow around the Frog Marsh just north of here. I'm not sure what it is, but them old toads get mean when you pick the hops. Now I'm not one for warts you know, so I wonder if you'd be so kind as to pick a peck of Frog Hops for me? I'd be much obliged....''That's the frog hops you've got there all right! I hope the toads didn't bite! Of course, they ain't got no teeth, but they can lip you pretty fierce.'Gerd Whitfoot, innkeeper of The Green Dragon in Bywater, is entering the Four Farthings Brewing-moot.The lost barrel is somewhere north-west of Overhill. The Green Dragon Inn is in Bywater, south-east of Overhill.

Barmy Rootknot, the assistant innkeeper at The Green Dragon Inn, has sent you off in search of a lost brandy-barrel.'Well, I suppose you'd like a mug of our justly famous Green Dragon's Breath beer? Well we've plenty and to spare! But say, I've heard of you around the Shire. They say you're good at solving problems! Well, I've got a little problem of my own.

'The annual Four Farthings Brewing-moot is coming up, and old Gerd wants to enter some of our special reserve in the judging. But the thing of it is, for the special Gerd uses old barrels from Ered Luin that the dwarves used for brandy. Every year, a dwarf-merchant he knows delivers a barrel. This year, though, it seems that the poor fellow was waylaid by huge beastly spiders near Overhill, and in his hurry to get away, he lost the barrel from his waggon.

'I wonder if you can head up to Overhill and look to the north-west of town for the barrel? It would mean a lot to Gerd to enter the judging with his best beer!''Yes! That's it! This year Gerd will win for sure! Please, accept a mug on the house!'In tidying up his library, Adelard Took came across a rocket from the Old Took's last Midsummer's Eve party. He sent it off to the Mathom-house in Michel Delving, but he thinks that might have upset the Old Took's ghost.Brombard Foxtail is at the Mathom-house in Michel Delving, far west of Tuckborough.

Adelard Took asked you to travel to the Mathom-house in Michel Delving and ask Keeper Foxtail for the fireworks rocket he had sent there.The Methel-stage is on the southern side of the road heading west out of Bywater.

Adelard Took had asked you to fire the rocket off at the Methel-stage in Bywater in hopes that the sight of this last rocket will appease the Old Took's ghost.Adelard Took can be found at the Great Smials in Tuckborough.

You should return to Adelard Took and let him know that you have done as he asked.'The ghost is still in my library! When will it leave me alone? You know, all this started when I was doing a bit of tidying up in there, sending a few things off to the Mathom-house, and such....

'I stumbled across an old rocket from the Old Took's last Midsummer's Eve party. Gandalf the Grey and he were great friends, you know, and Gandalf would bring the most splendid fireworks! Perhaps I upset the Old Took's ghost when I sent that rocket off to the Mathom-house? It could be that he wants to see it fired off!

'If we could get the rocket back and fire it, that might appease his ghost. Could you speak with Keeper Brombard Foxtail in Michel Delving and get it? The Mathom-house is up on a hill, north-west of the centre of Michel Delving. Once you have the crackers, could you fire them off at the Methel-stage in Bywater?''You need to travel to Michel Delving, to the Mathom-house, to retrieve the rocket that I sent there. I think that is what upset the Old Took's ghost!

'If you can get that rocket and fire it off at the Methel-stage in Bywater, that might appease the ghost!''Good day to you. So Adelard is looking for the rocket that he sent here?

'Well, yes I have it. In fact, I haven't had the chance to do anything with it yet, actually. A moment please....

'Ah, here you are! Be careful... although it is quite old, I would wager that since it was made by Gandalf the Grey it is still potent!''Wonderful, you've gotten the rocket from the Mathom-house. Now, please travel to the Methel-stage in Bywater and fire it off.

'I'll wager seeing that will appease the Old Took's ghost, and he'll leave my library in peace!''Other than that fireworks rocket I gave you, I don't think Adelard has sent anything else over to the Mathom-house recently, at least nothing of note.

'If he is looking for something else, please let me know!''Other than that fireworks rocket I gave you, I don't think Adelard has sent anything else over to the Mathom-house recently, at least nothing of note.

'If he is looking for something else, please let me know!''Oh, I can tell by the smell of your clothes that you fired off the rocket. Wonderful!

'Surely this will appease the Old Took's ghost. I'm going to go check in the library right now and make sure. I have a good feeling about this though, I'm sure this has appeased his ghost!'Meet the needs of a very large number of Shire-folk.Complete quests within the ShireWith the ghost still troubling his library, Adelard has come up with another idea on how to appease the Old Took: food. The Old Took was known for his love of spiced boar ribs, and he thinks that if he presents a plate of the ribs to the ghost in the library, he will return to his rest.Edilina Proudfoot's hole is east of the Great Smials.

Adelard sent you to ask his niece, Edilina Proudfoot, to prepare a plate of spiced boar ribs to appease the ghost of the Old Took, but warned you not to tell her the reason. He does not want to start a panic.Boars can be found in the hills east of Tuckborough. Edilina Proudfoot's home is just east of Tuckborough.

Edilina Proudfoot said she could make the spiced boar-ribs that Adelard wants to appease the ghost of the Old Took, but lacks the actual ribs. She asked you to bring her some ribs from the boars in the hills beyond Tuckborough.Adelard Took is waiting at the Great Smials in Tuckborough.

After gathering the ribs Edilina Proudfoot needed, she cooked up a plate of spiced boar-ribs for you to give to Adelard Took. You should bring them to Adelard, so he can use them to try and appease the Old Took's ghost.'Oh dear! The ghost is still troubling my library. In fact, the moment I took a step in, it raised such a racket that it gave me a terrible fright! I'm so a-flutter that I don't think I will be able to eat supper.

'Wait! Food! Like most hobbits, the Old Took had an affection for his vittles, especially spiced boar-ribs. I admit, I have a fondness for them myself. Perhaps if we prepare a plate of ribs for him, we can appease his ghost.

'Go speak with my niece, Edilina Proudfoot. Her hole is just east of the Great Smials and she is a marvelous cook. Don't tell her why we need the ribs, I don't want to start a panic!''Oh, how is dear old Uncle Adelard? I don't see him nearly enough any more!

'So he wants some spiced boar-ribs, does he? Well I have the spices, but I lack the ribs. They are rather important to the dish, are they not? Ha!

'But don't you worry, there are plenty of boars roaming the hills east of Tuckborough. If you bring me some ribs, I will make the dish Uncle Adelard is after!''Please go speak with my niece, Edilina Proudfoot, here in Tuckborough. She's a marvelous cook and should be able to prepare a plate of boar-ribs for us. Then I can present them to the ghost in my library and appease the Old Took!''Oh dear, Edilina needs ribs before she can make the dish for the Old Took's ghost?

'Dear, oh dear. Well, there are plenty of boars roaming the hills east of Tuckbrough. You should be able to get the ribs you need from them. Please hurry though, I'm not sure how long I can stand this ghost in my library!''You've got the ribs for Adelard, Bounder ${PLAYER}. Please give them to him in the Great Smials, with my regards!''Good, you've brought the ribs. Let me prepare them for you....

'Here you go. Tell Uncle Adelard to enjoy them, but if he eats too many he'll have to add a notch or two to his belt!''Ah, good, you have the ribs. And they do smell delicious! Edilina is quite the cook, isn't she?

'Well, I will place these in the library and hopefully they will appease the Old Took's ghost. Then I'll have some peace again!'Mat Harfoot told you that one of the members of his "Vigilance Committee", Violet Underhill, has gone missing.Bamfurlong, Maggot's farm, is south along the river road, in the Marish.

Mat Harfoot has asked you to look for Violet Underhill and suggested you speak first with old Farmer Maggot.'The Bounders haven't been able to keep the peace as well as they used to, no offence intended, so we've organized our own little group. We call it, well, the Vigilance Committee.

'A few of us have been looking into strange doings, like that Black Rider that's been seen round about and other Outsiders who've come to the Shire lately. The thing is, one of our members has gone missing. Violet Underhill was going to look into some reports of strangers in the south of the Marish, but she hasn't come back, and I'm getting worried. I wonder if you can go down there and look for her?

'It may be that Farmer Maggot has seen her. He knows what's what around there. His farm, Bamfurlong, is south down the river road, in the Marish.''Violet Underhill? Yes, indeed, I told that young lady what I'm going to tell you, and what I'd have told the Bounders days ago, if I had any sense.

'Some ruffians have come into the Shire not far west of here. Brigands, more than likely. My son Hammy here can tell you more about them, too. We'd both like to see them gone from the Shire.'

'I told that young lady that their camp was no place for her to be poking her nose, but I guess from what you say that she didn't listen. I should have told someone about 'em, but I figured her to have more hobbit-sense.''Please talk to Farmer Maggot about our missing Violet. His farm, Bamfurlong, is south along the river. If anyone will know where she is, he will.'Dorri wants matted feathers. Dorri can be found standing at the west gate of Gondamon.You have accepted a task to acquire matted feathers. You are to deliver them to Dorri at the western gate of Gondamon to earn favour with Thorin's Hall.Wanted: Matted feathers from the hendrevail in Ered Luin. Collect them and deliver them to Dorri at Gondamon to earn favour with Thorin's Hall.Wanted: Matted feathers from the hendrevail in Ered Luin.'Now, these are crusty looking things...not much use of these other than knowing that the Dourhands cannot call on these allies any longer.

'Your efforts will echo through the halls.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Dorri wants matted furs. Dorri can be found standing at the west gate of Gondamon.You have accepted a task to acquire matted furs. You are to deliver them to Dorri at the western gate of Gondamon to earn favour with Thorin's Hall.Wanted: Matted furs from the beasts in Ered Luin. Collect them and deliver them to Dorri at Gondamon to earn favour with Thorin's Hall.Wanted: Matted furs from the beasts in Ered Luin.'Furs can be used from everything from boot liners to rugs. You can never have enough fur.

'Your efforts will echo through the halls.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Bingo is excited to begin his journey, but he knows that he'll need to train for the adventure before he departs.Gaffer Gamgee lives at 3 Bagshot Row, part of the way up the Hill in Hobbiton, north-east of Bingo's hobbit-hole.

Bingo has asked you to consult with Gaffer Gamgee and learn if the hobbit learned anything about adventuring from Bilbo Baggins.Talk to Gaffer Gamgee on Bagshot Row, in HobbitonThe orchard at Appledores is up the side of the Hill, north-west of Bagshot Row.

Gaffer Gamgee has recommended that you pick up some of the fallen apples in the orchard at Appledores to give Bingo a good start on supplies for his journey.Pick up fallen apples in the orchard at Appledores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gaffer Gamgee is waiting for you to return from the Appledores with apples for Bingo.Return to Gaffer Gamgee at Bagshot RowBingo is outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, just north of the Town Hole.

You have a selection of fine apples from the Appledores in Hobbiton to give to Bingo.The Bird and Baby Inn is to the south-west of Bingo's hobbit-hole, in Michel Delving.

Bingo cannot stand apples, and has asked you to bring them to the Bird and Baby Inn and leave them by the counter inside. Someone will eat them.Esmerelda Burrows has gotten your attention inside the Bird and Baby Inn, and wishes to speak with you about something.Talk to Esmerelda Burrows in the Bird and Baby InnBingo is at his home north-east of the Bird and Baby Inn.

You have left the basket of apples in the Bird and Baby Inn, but in the process Esmerelda Burrows managed to discover that Bingo is planning a journey.Talk to Bingo outside his hobbit-hole in Michel DelvingBingo asked you to meet him at the Stocktower south of the town of Stock. He plans to climb the tower in order to build up the physical prowess he will need for his journey.Talk to Bingo by the Stocktower, south of the town of StockBingo tried to climb the Stocktower, and has given up. He says he will meet you in the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock, to continue his training.Talk to Bingo in the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock'I can hardly wait to begin my journey, ${PLAYER}, but I know there is much to be done before I depart. I need to train for the adventure if I am to have success on the road! I will need knowledge, and supplies, and physical strength, and... and...'

Bingo shudders.

'There is one more thing I will need, but let us not speak of that now. There is enough to do to get ready without beginning with that most perilous of tasks!

'But first: knowledge! You know, old Gaffer Gamgee up Hobbiton way was the gardener for Bilbo Baggins for many years, and it could be that he was privy to old Bilbo's secrets. He might have given the Gaffer some adventuring advice! Make your way to Bagshot Row in Hobbiton and see if the Gaffer has any sound advice for a hobbit starting out on a journey!''You know, old Gaffer Gamgee up Hobbiton way was the gardener for Bilbo Baggins for many years, and it could be that he was privy to old Bilbo's secrets. He might have given the Gaffer some adventuring advice! Make your way to Bagshot Row in Hobbiton and see if the Gaffer has any sound advice for a hobbit starting out on a journey!''What's that? You say Bingo Boffin wants to go on an adventure? Here I thought the Delving-field Boffins were respectable sorts!'

The Gaffer hems and haws for a moment.

'You tell young Bingo the only advice I have for hobbits thinking of leaving the Shire is this: 'don't!' Naught but trouble ever came of a journey. Mr. Bilbo was as well-spoken a hobbit as you could hope to meet, but I'm afeared he mixed up with some downright odd folk abroad. Poor fellow.

'I have no further advice for Mr. Boffin, but I do know that he'll be wanting for foodstuffs on his journey. If you run up to the Appledores on the side of the Hill and pick up some of the fallen apples, I daresay his stomach will be satisfied, even if his head will not! Good day to you!''I do know that Mr. Boffin will be wanting for foodstuffs on his journey. If you run up to the Appledores on the side of the Hill and pick up some of the fallen apples, I daresay his stomach will be satisfied, even if his head will not! Good day to you!''This looks to be a fine batch of apples, and should give Mr. Boffin a good start for his journey.

'I don't mind telling you that when the apples run out, I hope he turns around and heads for home! The wild is no place for a hobbit.''This looks to be a fine batch of apples, and should give Mr. Boffin a good start for his journey. I don't mind telling you that when the apples run out, I hope he turns around and heads for home! The wild is no place for a hobbit.''What's that? The Gaffer gave you some supplies for my journey? That was very thoughtful of him. I must be certain to write a note of thanks. He is... truly... a gentle...'

Bingo trails off as he sees what you carry.

'Apples? Oh my. I cannot STAND apples! I am sure those are fine specimens, ${PLAYER}, but I simply cannot abide the wormy things!

'I will not take even the smallest bite! Bring that basket into the Bird and Baby Inn and leave it by the counter, if you would, my friend. Someone will eat those apples, but that someone absolutely, positively, will not be me!''Bring that basket of apples into the Bird and Baby Inn and leave it by the counter, if you would, my friend. Someone will eat those apples, but that someone absolutely, positively, will not be me!''You didn't ignore Esmerelda inside the Bird and Baby Inn, did you? Oh, you shouldn't have done that. We'll never hear the end of it! You'd better go back and find out what she wanted.''You there! Who do you think you are, leaving those apples there? Are they for anyone to take? Where did they come from?'

You are forced to tell Esmerelda that they were a gift for Bingo, but he did not want them.

'Bingo Boffin? Whose birthday was it? And wouldn't his friends know he doesn't like the things? What's that? They were a gift from old Ham Gamgee? A going-away gift?'

Esmerelda's eyes have gained a conspiratorial shine, and you excuse yourself as politely as you can manage.'So Bingo Boffin is going on a journey? What has gotten into that hobbit?''You're back, and without the apples! Lovely. I am certain someone will enjoy them. Meanwhile, I bought some supplies from Petunia Greenhand, and should have enough food to last for a good while. But why the long face, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Bingo that Esmerelda Burrows managed to learn of Bingo's upcoming departure, despite the fact that you barely said a word about it.

'Well, there's nothing to be done, I suppose. If Esmerelda knows, all of Michel Delving will know by the morrow, and the rest of the Shire will be buzzing by next week! It can't be helped.

'The next area in which I must train is physical strength, and I know just how to do it. I will climb the Stocktower! Meet me at the base of the tower, south of the town of Stock, and we can climb the Stocktower together!''The next area in which I must train is physical strength, and I know just how to do it. I will climb the Stocktower! Meet me at the base of the tower, south of the town of Stock, and we can climb the Stocktower together!''Huff! Puff! Oh, ${PLAYER}, this was... a bad idea!'

Bingo's face is beet-red, and he is doubled over with exhaustion.

'I say... who knew... this tower was... huff... puff... so tall! I am not going to... go any higher... Hoo! I know a better... a better way....

'Meet me in... in the Golden Perch... ${PLAYER}. It's back in... in the town of Stock....''Who knew... this tower was... huff... puff... so tall! I am not going to... go any higher.... Hoo! I know a better... a better way....

'Meet me in... in the Golden Perch... ${PLAYER}. It's back in... in the town of Stock....''Ah, now this is the best way to build up these arm muscles, my friend: lifting a mug of hearty ale to my lips! I already feel much more prepared for my journey!

'So we have gotten a little advice about adventuring, I purchased some of the supplies I will need, and I have done a little exercise to get in shape for the journey. There is just one more area in which I need to train... but we'll get to that in a little while!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Sink or Swim' (Recommended Level: 10)</rgb>Now that the Blackwold brigands have been largely pushed out of Archet, Constable Sageford wants to redistribute their stolen goods to those who suffered at their hands.The Blackwolds have many camps along the road east and north of Combe. Constable Sageford is in Combe.

Constable Sageford wants you to recover a brigand lockbox from one of the watch-fires in the Chetwood. Its contents can then be used to reimburse those who lost property to the Blackwold.'The Blackwold brigands are on the run, no question about it. They're trying to regroup at camps throughout the Chetwood, but they suffered a real defeat at Archet.

'The brigands fled their old encampment up by Archet carrying a large lockbox, which they brought to one of their smaller camps in the Chetwood, north-east of Combe. If we can get our hands on that lockbox, its contents could be used to help those who lost property to the Blackwolds. There are a number of watch-fires along the road, so you'll need to find the right one.

'These villains have a great many debts to repay, ${PLAYER}. If you can return with the lockbox, the folk around here will be better for it.''Ah, you have returned with the brigands' lockbox! Now let me see what's inside, and we can sell the valuables to support the survivors of the Blackwold raids throughout the area.

'Locked! I should have guessed as much. Well, until we can find the key, we won't have any luck with this. There seem to be some initials carved in the lock: "R.F." Most unusual.'Toronn desires to leave Middle-earth, while Bregar, his brother, believes they should remain.The broken sword is upon a stone cairn in the ruins of Dol Ringwest which lie west of Duillond.

Bregar has asked you to search the ruins of Dol Ringwest for the stone cairn and the broken sword it holds, which you should return to Bregar.Search the cairn for the broken swordBregar awaits your return in Duillond, east of the ruins of Dol Ringwest.

You recovered a broken sword from a burial cairn in the Elf-ruins of Dol Ringwest.'Toronn must know that while I remain behind, I will ever be with him. To do this, I will need your aid. So much of this land has been our shelter and teacher and our memories are filled with moments of joy and laughter because of this land.

'I think, perhaps, my brother will appreciate this well enough to see me on my journey as he begins his own. In the ruins of Dol Ringwest, there lies a sword upon a stone cairn, borne once by a Dúnadan we fought beside in defence of our homeland. I may be able to remind my brother of our duty to Middle-earth.

'My duties here will not allow me to leave, but I hope you will see the need I have to seal this rift between my brother and me. Will you help me?''Seek the broken sword at Dol Ringwest, west of here. It is very important!''This blade means much, broken and dulled as it may be. Alas, the passage of time does little to dull my memories of that battle.

'Perhaps I have underestimated the importance of brothers.'You have proven to be a Bounder of great merit.Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce is by Town Hole in Michel Delving.

You have been told to bring word of the many good deeds you have performed for the Shire-folk to Bodo Bunce.'You have done a lot of good for a lot of folk, Bounder ${PLAYER}. Report back to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce by Town Hole in Michel Delving and tell him of your deeds!''I have heard of all the good you have done, ${PLAYER}. You truly are an excellent Bounder and deserve the thanks of all Shire-folk!

'We don't go in for uniforms, but I must say that you've earned another feather in your cap. Take it with my thanks!''Talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce by Town Hole in Michel Delving. He'll be very pleased to hear of all the good you have done!'You have proven to be a Bounder of great merit.Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce is by Town Hole in Michel Delving.

You have been told to bring word of the many good deeds you have performed for the Shire-folk to Bodo Bunce.'You have done a lot of good for a lot of folk, Bounder ${PLAYER}. Report back to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce by Town Hole in Michel Delving and tell him of your deeds!''I have heard of all the good you have done, ${PLAYER}. You truly are an excellent Bounder and deserve the thanks of all Shire-folk!

'We don't go in for uniforms, but I must say that you've earned another feather in your cap. Take it with my thanks!''Talk to Second Shirriff Bodo Bunce by Town Hole in Michel Delving. He'll be very pleased to hear of all the good you have done!'Eluna would like you to help folks around Lhan Garan.Eluna asked you to help folks around Lhan Garan.

Help people around Lhan Garan.Aid CulhucAid Madog and Teilo GwyniadAid MargetYou have helped several people around town.

It is time to return to Eluna in Lhan Garan.Talk to Eluna'I'm still trying to sort out why the Draig-lûth are here. When we left to settle Lhan Garan it was certainly a source of tension, but Talfryn secured the promise we'd be left alone. Let me look into this. Don't worry, I promise I'll keep safe.

'Until I have news, could you help some folks around town?''You have an uncanny knack for good timing, friend. I have news.'What might seem like an uncontrolled, chaotic, thrashing attack to an outsider is actually a very deliberate, chaotic, thrashing attack.Use Thrash - Tier 3When a Captain calls for aid, they will never be alone.Summon your HeraldsThe Champion is afraid of none and welcomes any foe who accepts their challenge.Use Champion's ChallengeWith the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the surviving members of the Fellowship of the Ring and their dear friends have gathered in Merethrond for a grand banquet to commemorate the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must have the repeatable quest 'A Long-awaited Banquet, A Celebration Without End' underway to advance this Deed.</rgb>With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the surviving members of the Fellowship of the Ring and their dear friends have gathered in Merethrond for a banquet to commemorate the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must have the repeatable quest 'A Long-awaited Banquet, A Celebration Without End' underway to advance this Deed.</rgb>Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- Frodo Baggins'Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- Samwise Gamgee'Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- Meriadoc Brandybuck'Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- Peregrin Took'Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- Gimli'Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- Legolas'Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- Faramir'Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- Mithrandir'Complete 'A Long-awaited Banquet -- King Aragorn II Elessar'The journal you brought back to Wilimar Bolger was missing many of its leaves, thanks to being shaken and torn by some wild beasts.Wolves can be found east of Budgeford.

Without the missing leaves, it will be impossible to determine who shot the arrow in Wilimar Bolger's door, nor why. Wilimar suspects that wolves tore the journal apart and has asked you to try to recover the leaves from them.'Oh dear, this isn't good, not good at all. Many of the leaves of the journal are missing, as if it were shaken and torn by a beast. Look here, see the teeth marks?

'Goodness, those teeth marks might be from a wolf! I wonder if some of the beasts took the pages, perhaps to line their dens? Yes, yes, I know it sounds strange, but I've heard a tale or two of them doing such things.

'If you could, slay a few of the wolves east of here and see if they have any of the journal leaves. I seem to be missing about three leaves all told. Once I have all the pages, I should be able to see what the author of the journal was up to!''Marvelous, you've found them all. Thank you! Now to see what this means....

'Goodness, this is interesting... and distressing! I will need a moment more to read this, but it would appear the author of this journal was a man named "Callum." And the tale it tells is an astonishing one!

'As hard as it is to believe, it would seem a distant ancestor of mine slew one of his in a great battle! And, oh dear... he means to revenge himself upon me....'What a perfect evening for a fireworks celebration!Talk to Gandalf the Grey.Talk to Gandalf the GreyPick up fireworks crates from the cart.Pick up fireworks crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Set up the fireworks display at the first launch location.Set up the fireworks display at the first launch locationThwart nosey hobbits<rgb=#FF0000>The volunteer must finish their task!</rgb>Pick up more fireworks crates from the cart.Pick up more fireworks crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Set up the fireworks display at the second launch location.Set up the fireworks display at the second launch location<rgb=#FF0000>The volunteer must finish their task!</rgb>Pick up even more fireworks crates from the cart.Pick up even more fireworks crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Set up the fireworks display at the final launch location.Set up the fireworks display at the final launch location<rgb=#FF0000>The volunteer must finish their task!</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Do not let all of the finale fireworks launch early!</rgb>Talk to Gandalf the Grey to launch the fireworks display.Talk to Gandalf the Grey to launch the fireworks display'A wonderous celebration indeed.''Greetings, ${PLAYER}. I am glad you have come to assist with this evening's fireworks display.

'The display will be well attended, for many have come to Bree Town to view tonight's marvellous celebration. We must not disappoint them! Let us now carefully set up the fireworks display. We must be both careful and quick, for the sun is setting.

'Do not worry, you will not be alone in your endeavours this evening. I have requested additional assistance from our many friends. Now then, let us begin.''Well done, well done indeed! Now, let the celebration commence!'A fireworks show a day - how best to celebrate the occasion!Complete 'A Flurry of Fireworks'.Complete 'A Flurry of Fireworks''A moment, ${PLAYER}. I am trusting you with this evening's celebration. If this marvelous display goes without trouble, I will give you an extra reward. What do you say?'From the orders you found, Ulfar has learned that Olwir plans to capture a Stone-troll that stalks Rushock Bog and deliver it as a gift to the Dourhands in the north. The cow he stole from Filibert was bait to trap the creature.Olwir's camp is in the northern reaches of Rushock Bog.

Ulfar has decided that Olwir's plan must be put to an end and has asked you to gather a party of warriors to accompany him to the camp. Once there, he plans to inflitrate the camp and slay any Stone-troll Olwir's dwarves may have captured.Speak to UlfarUlfar is back in Needlehole.

Having succeeded in your quest, you should return to Ulfar to tell him what happened.'Who would have thought the theft of a cow would uncover a plot such as this? We must foil Olwir's plans, and if he has captured a troll, we must slay it!

'Fortunately, I have learned where Olwir and his dwarves are camping. They can be found in the north of Rushock Bog. However, getting into the camp and slaying this Stone-troll, if they have one, will not be easy. We will need help.

'Gather a party of warriors -- if there are any to be found in this land -- then return here. Make sure to gather sturdy warriors, for the battle ahead will not be easy.''Well done. You certainly deserve this reward.''Are you ready to leave?

'Make sure your party is ready as well, as we'll surely need their help to slay this Stone-troll.'Gerebert Took's journal revealed that Gerebert had accepted a dare to hide in one of Longo Burrow's leaf-waggons. Esilia Took asked you to help search for her cousin.The bear dens are to the south of Longo Burrow's farm.

Esilia Took asked you to speak with Longo Burrow about her cousin Gerebert. Longo demanded that you perform a favour for him before he would talk. He told you that his leaf was in high demand, but that his current crop wasn't ready for harvesting yet. He instructed you to retrieve a barrel of pipe-weed that he hid in a bear den during the winter.Esilia Took can be found in the centre of Tuckborough.

Longo Burrow agreed to tell you what he knew of Gerebert in exchange for a barrel of leaf he hid in a bear den. On bringing it back, though, Longo revealed that he didn't know anything about Gerebert. You should return to Esilia Took and let her know.'Afore I tell you where that fool Took you're looking for is, I want you to do something for me. See, my pipe-weed is known throughout the Shire, and a bit beyond, and that means I've got lots o' folk coming to me asking for leaf.

'Well, my current crop isn't quite ready for harvesting yet, but I'm a smart hobbit, you see. Back when the bears were sleeping in the winter, I hid a barrel o' leaf out in one o' their dens, for just such a rainy day.

'Go to the bear dens south of here and find that barrel o' leaf. When you bring it back, I'll tell you what I know o' that Took.''All right, you found the leaf. Give it here. Now, I'll keep my end o' the bargain now. This Took you're looking for... Gerebert was his name, eh? And he hid in one of my leaf-waggons?

'Well, I haven't seen him. Eh? I didn't say I'd actually seen this Took of yours. I just said I'd tell you what I know. And that's all I know! Now off with you!''What are you still standing about here for? I told you what I know of that Took you were looking for... it just so happened what I knew was nothing!

'Now off with you!''Oh, how terrible! That Longo is a rude sort. I'm so sorry that he tricked you like that. The next time I see him, I shall have words with him!

'Now, back to the matter of Gerebert. I think I may have just had a thought on who else we might be able to ask, if you are still willing to go out and look for him.'Culhuc would like for you to taste his newest dish.Culhuc is in Lhan Garan, near the oven along the water-front path.

Sample the roast next to Culhuc in Lhan Garan.Taste the roast avancCulhuc is waiting to hear your thoughts about his dish.

Talk to Culhuc in Lhan Garan.Talk to Culhuc'I prepared a simple roast for you! You did, after all, procure the meat for me. I'd be curious to hear your thoughts on the dish.''Tasty but a little tough to chew? I thought so too. I'm sure my next attempt will yield better results. I'm glad I asked you to gather so much meat!'A humble merchant needs help rescuing his friends from Radlaw.Radlaw can be found to the north of Clegur. The humble merchant has asked you to free his friends.Free captured hobbits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The hobbits have been released. The humble merchant should hear about this.Talk to the humble merchant in Clegur'Do ye have a moment? I am but a humble merchant. I have travelled through these lands selling stock for a time now. But my livelihood has been taken from me.

'Ever since the bandits and ruffians moved into Radlaw, I haven't been able to conduct business! Ye see, they send a few at a time once in a moon to rouse the village. Shake us up for coin. They offer us what they call "protection."

'But ever since they arrived, business hasn't been the same. I couldn't pay their tribute and now my friends have been captured.

'They are being held in Radlaw as collateral. Could you please help free them? They're all I've got!''I am eternally grateful for all you've done. My friends are home and safe. I just hope we will sooner rather than later be rid of those ruffians. My business cannot succeed here if they continue bleeding this town dry of its labours.

'I might have to move on from here to keep my friends safe.'You must complete the full eating contest several times.You must complete the full eating contest several times.Finish all courses in the Eating ContestWith training, the blade becomes a natural extension of the arm.Use offensive Swordplay skillsUse offensive Swordplay skillsThe Bree Postmaster can grant Honorary Postman's Badges to individuals he deems trustworthy.Speak to the Bree Postmaster to request a Postman's Badge, in order to assist with finding the lost invitations.Talk to the Bree Postmaster'Hail, ${PLAYER}. Are you here to help with the festival invitations?'

'Any person who handles mail in Bree must have a Postman's Badge, or face the consequences of the law. I can authorize trustworthy individuals by bestowing them with an honourary badge, but only with the agreement that it will be used for helping Percy in his current situation. Can I trust you in this?''You seem trustworthy enough. Do not make me regret this decision, or I will send the Constable after you!

'By my authority, I will grant you the temporary status of Honourary Postman. Show Percy the badge and let him know that you are willing to help.'Marget asked you to check on her friends.Marget has asked you to check on her friends in Lhan Garan.

Talk to Murig and Deryn.Talk to MurigTalk to DerynMarget is waiting to hear from you about how her friends are faring.

Talk to Marget in Lhan Garan.Talk to Marget'Ever since we got back, Murig and Deryn have been rather withdrawn. Could you check on them for me?

'No no, I'm not worried about them or anything. I simply, er, want to make sure they will be ready for whatever tasks lie ahead.''Come to check on me? That's kind of you. I needed to get my mind off things, so I thought I'd come fish with my grandfather. I'll admit that recent events have unsettled me. I never thought I would have to apply my training skills to fighting my own people.

'As much as I appreciate your concern, I'd like to be alone for a while.''Ah, ${PLAYER}, if you came to try my famous bread I'm afraid you arrived too early. I'm still mixing the dough, as you can see. You know, making tinctures and poultices is not so different from baking. The right ingredients in the right proportions, treated with just the right touch, will yield something marvellous. I even use the same mixing bowl for both tasks!

'That was a joke.''They have thrown themselves into their hobbies? Good. It's better than having to watch them sulk.

'Me? Do I have something to take my mind off this? Are you telling me I should get a hobby?'The hobbits are celebrating the Lithe Festival. To aid them in their celebration, the Dwarves of Thorin's Hall are letting you catch and bring them fish.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>Fish can be caught in the river running through Thorin's Hall.

Láfi has given you some time to catch fish for the Lithe Festival.Catch as many fish as you can in twenty minutes'We dwarves have the greatest fish in all of Eriador. The river that runs through this great hall makes them powerful swimmers, which means lots of meat.

'You won't find a finer fish anywhere. I suppose we can be civil and share some of ours for the Lithe Festival in the Shire, but you've got to catch them yourself.''You don't have much time, ${PLAYER}! You should look to the water, not to me, if you wish to succeed. Good luck to you.'Farmer Polo Proudfoot needs new bee queens to replace the ones killed by bears. Before you can go hunting wild hives, you'll need to get a salve to protect yourself from bee stings.Gammer Boffin is in Overhill, some considerable distance north of Tuckborough, on the other side of Hobbiton.

Before you can collect new queen-bees for Farmer Proudfoot, you will need to obtain the means to protect yourself from the stings of the wild bees. Proudfoot told you to get a special balm from Gammer Boffin.Toads can be found in Rushock Bog, west of Overhill, beyond Hobbiton, and also in the marsh just north of Frogmorton. Gammer Boffin is in Overhill, a town nestled in the Bindbole Wood.

Before you can hunt new queens for Farmer Proudfoot's hives, he sent you to Gammer Boffin to get some salve to protect you from the stings of the wild bees; however, Gammer Boffin does not have all the ingredients she needs to prepare the salve. She has asked you to collect some toad-stones for the salve.'Sorry to say, but I got more bee problems. You saved the one hive, but the queens in the others were killed by the bears, and I need new ones. But it isn't that simple.

'First of all, the wild hives are off in the woods to the south... that's right, where all them bears live in the first place. Second thing -- and we'll deal with it first -- those wild bees don't take kindly to being moved, so you'll need to protect yourself from their stings. Now Gammer Boffin up in Overhill, she's got some kind of balm that will protect you from stings, so you just go and get some of that salve from her.

'Overhill is almost due north of here, the other side of Hobbiton, so it's a ways off. Hurry back... I need those queens!''Please talk to Gammer Boffin in Overhill about a salve for bee-stings.''Eh, what's that? Knees? You skinned your knee? Oh! Bees!

'Yes, yes, I can make a salve against stings. But I'll need some ingredients first. Find me four toad-stones from any of the toads around the Shire. Mind you, not all toads have got 'em. Eh? Where to find 'em? Well, one place is the bog. Look in the west side of Rushock Bog, west of here, beyond Hobbiton. Or if you like, you can find plenty of toads in the marsh just north of Frogmorton.

'Don't look so funny. The salve's no good without toad-stones!''Please, do what the Gammer asks to get that bee-sting salve. Rushock Bog? The Frogmoors near Frogmorton? Toads, you need some toads!''Toad-stones! Such a terrible trouble to get them. Salve would be easier to make if not for the hunting, eh?'Call upon the power of lightning to strike your foes.Use Lightning StrikeLinda Bolger of Budgeford is worried about a pack of wolves that have invaded the Shire and fears her pig farm will soon be attacked.Milo Bolger is at a farm east of Budgeford, keeping an eye on the wolves in the nearby ruins.

Linda Bolger came to Budgeford looking for someone to help with the wolf problem. She has asked you to speak with her husband, Milo.The wolves can be found east of Milo and Linda Bolger's farm, among the ruins.

Linda Bolger sent you to speak with her husband, Milo, in regards to the wolves that have entered the Shire. Milo asked you to thin the pack before they can become a greater threat.Defeat wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Milo Bolger is keeping an eye on the wolves east of Budgeford.

Milo will be pleased to hear that you have reduced the number of wolves the Hobbits of Budgeford will need to deal with.'Things are not good in Budgeford, ${PLAYER}. A pack of wolves has made its way into the Shire, and there's talk that there might be more on the way. I'm worried that my farm will soon be attacked, but more than that -- all Shire-folk are threatened by the presence of these wolves. 

'And I saw... well, it's probably not important. Nevermind.

'Anyway, I came into town looking for help, but you should go talk with my husband, Milo, back at our farm. Just head up the hill and cut east across the fields until you see our farm. Milo will probably be out behind the house, keeping an eye on the nearby ruins where the wolves have holed up.''My husband, Milo, is at our farm, up the hill and east of Budgeford, keeping an eye on the wolves. I know he'd appreciate your help.''Any help is welcome, ${PLAYER}, and I think we're going to need it. We Hobbits of Budgeford aren't well-suited to dealing with wolves, and the thought of wolves again in the Shire is enough to freeze my blood as solid as the Brandywine during the Fell Winter.

'If you can thin the pack a bit, we might have a better chance of keeping them away from the town. You'll find them in those ruins out east of our farm.

'I hope you can manage it, friend -- there are a lot of pigs and hobbits in Budgeford, and I'm afraid these wolves would love to have either or both for dinner!''Wolves have invaded the Marish! I hope you can do something about them.''The wolves here are a real threat to not only Budgeford, but the rest of the Shire as well! The more of these evil beasts you can kill off, the better!''My husband Milo will want to hear about your success! He should still be at our farm, east of Budgeford.''Very good, ${PLAYER}, very good! You have been a tremendous help. There's something queer about these wolves, and I've only begun to fill in the pieces.'You have run all over the Shire helping to return spoiled pies to Holly Hornblower -- no small feat!Holly Hornblower is north of the main square of Hobbiton.

Holly has decided to give you one of her pie recipes and is waiting to speak with you.'You are a true friend, ${PLAYER}, and thanks to you, my business is saved! If you'll give me a moment, I'll dig out one of my recipes for you.

'Now, where did I leave it?''Here you are, ${PLAYER}! For your hard work, I've decided to give you one of my pie recipes -- be sure not to use spoiled berries!

'And if you have any stomach left for pies after all the pie-adventures you have now had, I'd like you to have one of them as well!

'Thanks again for your hard work, ${PLAYER}, Pie-runner!'You have run all over the Shire helping to return spoiled pies to Holly Hornblower -- no small feat!Holly Hornblower is north of the main square of Hobbiton.

