'Thanks again for your hard work, ${PLAYER}, Pie-runner!'Talfryn told you about several people who need help around Lhan Garan.Talfryn asked you to help a few key people in and around Lhan Garan.

Help Eluna, Madog, and Undeg.Complete 'Dealing with Bloodhollow'Complete 'Introduction to Crafting'Complete 'Learning to Fish in Lhan Garan''Our home of Lhan Garan is only recently settled. We left Brundir, or Dunland as you would know it, mere months ago, and we had to leave much behind in our departure. The nearby communities of Mossward and the hobbit villages have been very generous to us, for which I am grateful, but there is more to be done if we are to safely greet the coming winter.

'Find Madog and Teilo Gwyniad fishing by the water. They could use your help catching fish to be salted and smoked for the winter.

'Look for Undeg. She is coordinating our tradesfolk and can help you take up a crafting profession such as weaponsmithing or cooking. Head north-west along the path by the water. She'll be with other crafters and the community oven.

'Eluna here is training many of our new scouts, and as much as she may deny it, she could use a helping hand, as we all do from time to time.'Jónar, a sinister and surly resident of Thorin's Hall, has grown increasingly sour towards the success of the Inn League.The Inn League Tasting is taking place in Frerin's Court, in the southern outdoor courtyard of Thorin's Hall. You may only speak with the recruiter when she is not distracted by her duties.

You should go to the Inn League Tasting and see what you can do to sabotage it. Jónar has expressed that he does not want any more dwarves joining the Inn League while he still draws breath!Talk to Laurel Sackville in Frerin's CourtThe tasting table is in Frerin's Court, just to the south of Thorin's Hall.

You should wait for Laurel Sackville, the Inn League Recruiter, to wander away.Hide behind the nearby kegs until Laurel Sackville wanders awayThe tasting table is in Frerin's Court, just to the south of Thorin's Hall.

You should add swill to the tasting samples between rounds of tasting. Surely no one will notice....Add swill to Inn League samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Do not let Laurel Sackville see your mischiefThe tasting has begun!

You must watch the carnage unfold, for Jónar will wish to hear of your success.Watch the events of the tasting unfoldDo not leave the tasting areaJónar awaits word of your deeds in the inn at Thorin's Hall.

You should tell Jónar of your cruel, wonderful success against the Inn League Tasting recruiter.'Nincompoops and ninnyhammers, how I loathe the Inn League! The vermin have infested Thorin's Hall, spilling all the way out into fair Frerin's Court. They are having an Inn League tasting today to try to recruit more members!

'You must get to Frerin's Court immediately, ${PLAYER}, before they are finished setting up, and make sure this event goes terribly. There will be no more dwarves joining the Inn League...not on my watch, at least!

'Go outdoors to Frerin's Court and stop that beer-tasting immediately! Here...take this swill from the Forsaken Inn. Do something useful for once! I don't care what.''If you are here for a tasting, another round will begin shortly! Please sit down and make yourself comfortable until we begin.

'Tastings occur every few minutes.''Can I help you, o greatest of time-wasters? Do dilly-dally a little longer; I insist!''Ha ha ha ha! Oh, ha ha! Ho ho ho! Oh my goodness, pardon me. My eyes...how they sting with tears of delight!

'Do not speak! Let me savour this moment.'You have unlocked the neighbour Brútha the Wayward. The Gift Maker can give you her welcoming housing decoration.Speak with the gift maker to accept his kind offer.'You would like to welcome Brútha the Wayward to your housing neighbourhood?

