<rgb=#FF0000>You can access Anniversary Celebration Instances from the Instance Join panel.</rgb>Áskell, at Gondamon, told you that one of Gellir's company left a brother of his own behind. Sigurdór, the brother left behind, has gone to Kheledúl seeking his own vengeance. Áskell asked that you seek him out as the port has been overrun and it's dockmaster deposed to a tower on the outskirts of the port.Sigurdór is at a tower along the road to Kheledúl east of Gondamon.

Áskell directed you to find and stop Sigurdór, a hot-headed young dwarf, from committing a terrible folly.Talk to Sigurdór near Kheledúl'Though my brother is avenged, I fear that in my sorrow I spoke too plainly to a younger dwarf who now risks his own life to avenge his own brother, a member of Gellir's company.

'The dwarf, Sigurdór, went towards Kheledûl to avenge his brother, but likely is at a tower on the outskirts of the port with the deposed dockmaster, Svanr. Follow the road east beyond Thrasi's cabin, towards the shore, and keep an eye out for Sigurdór.

'I pray you are not too late to stop his folly.''You must hurry to Kheledûl to stop Sigurdór from doing something rash. Kheledûl lies to the east of here.''Áskell told me not to go, but I would hear nothing of his warning. My brother Arndór was not much older than myself, and I felt I must avenge him. I failed.

'The Dourhands are too rooted within that port for one dwarf, more miner than warrior, to dislodge. You, though, you are a hale and hearty warrior, else you would not be here....'Learn to quickly regain your footing.Use the skill Sea LegsListen to all twelve of the hobbits' stories about Bilbo Baggins' adventures.Listen to all twelve of the hobbit's stories about Bilbo Baggins' adventures.Complete Baggins' Birthday - Ted Sandyman's StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Shirrif Robin Smallburrow's StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Dudo Chubb's StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Lobelia Sackville-Baggins' StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Storyteller's TaleComplete Baggins' Birthday - Hal Hornblower's StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Bogo Chubb's StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Lotho Sackville-Baggins' StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - a Child's StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Hereward Loamsdown's StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Holly Hornblower's StoryComplete Baggins' Birthday - Postman Grubb's StoryReading further in the journal, Wilimar has begun to sympathize with Callum, the Hillman who swore to kill him. Learning of Callum's hard-fought life in a realm far in the north, he has decided to aid Callum and help him with the wound he suffered from the wild boar.Prickly broom grows along the water, south-east of Budgeford.

Wilimar has decided to provide Callum with bandages for his wound, but to aid in his healing, he wants to soak the bandages in an unguent made from prickly broom leaves. He has asked you to gather these leaves for him.Collect prickly broom leaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wilimar Bolger can be found near his hole on the north-west side of Budgeford.

Wilimar has decided to provide Callum with bandages for his wound, but to aid in his healing, he wants to soak the bandages in an unguent made from prickly broom leaves. He has asked you to gather these leaves for him.Callum's camp is on the far west side of the Frogmoors, west of Budgeford.

With the prickly broom leaves you gathered, Wilimar was able to prepare an unguent in which to soak the bandages. In addition to giving the bandages to Callum, Wilimar has asked you to tell Callum that he holds no malice against him and hopes he will do the same.'He may not accept charity from me, his "sworn enemy," but I think I should try to help this Callum all the same.

'This wound of his, from the boar, most likely needs to be bandaged. To ward off infection and help the wound to heal, we should soak the bandages in an unguent of... let's see, what would be best?

'Prickly broom, I think. I already have the bandages, but I don't have the broom leaves. Could I ask you to help me once more and gather some prickly broom leaves from the bushes south-east of Budgeford, near to the water?''There should be plenty of prickly broom bushes south-east of Budgeford, near the water. Gather me some leaves from them, so that I can make the unguent I need for Callum's bandages.''Ah, you have the leaves, please let me have them. This will only take a moment....

'Please take these bandages to Callum at his camp-site on the far west side of the Frogmoors. Tell him he should change the bandages daily. There are enough here for seven days. Hopefully that will be enough to help him heal.

'Also, let him know that I hold no malice against him... and ask that he do the same for me!''Please take those bandages to Callum. Hopefully they will help him heal, and perhaps he will lose his malice towards me! His camp is west of here, near the far western edge of the Frogmoors.''Bandages? From the little man? I... and this is not treachery of some sort? I... I am not sure what to say. I have hated this mark against my family for so long, I thought it would finally be erased if the little man was dead... but these are not the actions of an enemy....

'Should my anger be aimed at those who forced my ancestor into battle? Or should I lay the blame upon Fate and leave my anger behind? I have much to think upon.

'I thank you. This Wilimar has nothing to fear from me.'The Lore-master is friend to beast and bird and may call upon their aid.Use Sign of the Wild: RageThe Beorninghús needs a beautiful bouquet of flowers!Gather all the flowers required to make the perfect bouquet of flowers for the Beorninghús.Collect Lossarnach flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Give the flowers to Grimbeorn's dogs.'My wife, Gírta, would like me to return to the Beorninghús with some of Lossarnach's finest flowers. If you would pick some for me and give the flowers to my dogs, I will give you an extra reward. What do you say?''Woof!''Ruff!''Yipp!''Woof woof!'It is time to pollinate the meadows!Talk to Grimbeorn.Talk to GrimbeornSee if the bees are ready to go.See if the bees are ready to goPollinate the first field of flowersPollinate the first field of flowers<rgb=#FF0000>Grimbeorn's bees must finish their task!</rgb>See if the bees are ready to continue.See if the bees are ready to continuePollinate the second field of flowers.Pollinate the second field of flowers<rgb=#FF0000>Grimbeorn's bees must finish their task!</rgb>See if the bees are ready to continue.See if the bees are ready to continuePollinate the Lossarnach great-lilies.Pollinate the Lossarnach great-lilies<rgb=#FF0000>Grimbeorn's bees must finish their task!</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>At least one Lossarnach great-lily must survive!</rgb>See if the bees are ready to return to Grimbeorn.See if the bees are ready to return to GrimbeornEscort the bees back to Grimbeorn.Escort the bees back to Grimbeorn'What took you so long? Did you stop and smell each and every flower? Ha, just some Beorning humour my friend! I am glad you have returned my bees to me!'

Grimbeorn turns to his bees.

'Bees! Did you have a grand meal?! I am sure you did!''Well here we are. Why did I agree to lend my bees and aid Gondor with pollinating the fields of Lossarnach? Well my trusted ${RACE}, Gondor has conquered many foes that might one day threaten the safety of my Vale! It is the least I could do!

'Yes, I have called upon you to accompany me because I know not the lands of Lossarnach. How do I guide my bees upon lands that I do not know? You however know these lands. That is why you shall guide my bees for me. Do not worry! All you have do to is make sure that my bees do no stray far afield and that no harm comes to them. That should be quite easy! This is just a woods filled with flowers after all!''Buzz buzz!''Buzz!''Buzz!''Buzz buzz!'A daily frolic - spring is simply grand!Complete 'Bee's Big Business'.Complete 'Bee's Big Business''Hmm, if you bring all my bees back to me well fed, I will give you an extra reward. What do you say?'The waterfalls in and around the sleepy town of Clegur may hide secrets.Drudwen has asked you to explore the waterfalls in and around Clegur.

Clegur is in the south-west of Swanfleet.Explore the waterfall behind the bridgeExplore the south-eastern waterfallExplore the eastern waterfallExplore the north-eastern waterfallExplore the north-western waterfallExplore the southern waterfallYou should report back to Drudwen with the pottery and news of the skeleton you found behind the waterfalls.

Drudwen is in the town of Clegur, in southern Swanfleet.'Hullo there. You look like the adventurous sort! Just the type of person I need. Have you noticed all the waterfalls around Clegur? I am endlessly curious about what might be behind them!

'Unfortunately, I cannot swim. Can you swim? Maybe you could explore the falls for me and tell me what you find?''Goodness, you are soaked! But you did not drown - good work! And what have you there?'

You hand over the broken vase.

'Well would you look at that! How old is this, I wonder? And you found a skeleton too? Oh, I cannot wait to tell all of my friends about the discoveries that I... er, that is, that we... have made! Thank you!'Constable Sageford remembered that a scout mentioned hearing a Blackwold recruit heeding orders from Sergeant Applewood near the Blackwold main encampment.Applewood has been seen entering the Blackwold's main encampment in the northernmost part of the Chetwood.

After learning that Rurik was guilty only of fear, Sageford recalled the name Rurik provided as being a Brigand within the main encampent of the Blackwold in the Chetwood. Sageford wants you to seek Applewood out and obtain the key he stole from Rurik.Find Rurik's master-key (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Constable Sageford can be found near the centre of Combe.

Having found and defeated Applewood, you took the key back from him. Now you should return to Constable Sageford.'Ah yes! I remember. A scout returned a few hours ago and mentioned that there was an Applewood giving orders to the recruits. He then headed towards the Blackwold's main encampment in the ruins in the north most part of the Chetwood.

'If Applewood has the key, then we should set about getting it from him to aid those who have suffered so greatly at the Blackwold's hands. Be careful, ${PLAYER}, reports from near those ruins tell of a great sense of dread and dismay. You will need to be cautious if you are to attempt to find Applewood and obtain the key.

'When you find the key return to me, and we shall see what good news we shall bring to the people of Archet and Combe.''If you can find Applewood within the Blackwold's main encampment, you should be able to recover Rurik's key, and then we can begin to restore the people's hope here in Combe and Archet.''You found it! Excellent work, and I can say that we are pleased that there is one less Blackwold to worry about, as well.

'Now, ${PLAYER}, we can find what the brigands hid away within this chest.
You have done a wonderful job, friend, and deserve this reward.'There is much to be learned from seeing a foe's reaction to an open wound, and you consider yourself a scholar.Use skills which apply bleedsAbove all, a Guardian must be where they are needed and quickly, for your companions are not so sturdy as you.Block enemy attacksFood, drink, companionship -- for the Champion, all of these are second to the joys of battle...drink is a very close second though.Land Critical Hits using Wild AttackMerion told you that children of the village are forbidden from venturing into the Wadewater... which makes it very likely to have been Tegwyn's destination.The Dunlending village of Lhan Garan is north-east of Mossward, on the eastern side of the Wadewater. It would be a good place to start looking for Tegwyn.Visit Lhan Garan on the eastern edge of the Wadewater and learn if there was any sign of TegwynMeneldir has come to Lhan Garan on the Wadewater's edge.Talk to Meneldir at Lhan GaranAvanc in the Wadewater would be a real danger to Tegwyn. Defeating any of them you encounter can only help in your rescue efforts.Defeat avanc in the Wadewater (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Meneldir is in the middle of the Wadewater, west of Fangsettle.Talk to Meneldir in the middle of the Wadewater, west of FangsettleMeneldir asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for Tegwyn.<rgb=#00FF00>Listen</rgb> for TegwynMeneldir is in the middle of the Wadewater, west of Fangsettle.Talk to Meneldir in the Wadewater, west of FangsettleMeneldir suggested you continue the search for Tegwyn further to the west.Search for Tegwyn further to the west in the WadewaterYou found a worn wooden sword abandoned in the mud of the Wadewater.Examine the abandoned wooden swordMeneldir has joined you in the Wadewater by an abandoned wooden sword.Talk to Meneldir by the abandoned wooden sword in the WadewaterMeneldir asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for Tegwyn.<rgb=#00FF00>Listen</rgb> for TegwynYou heard a faint voice calling for you to the north-west in the Wadewater. Is it Tegwyn?Search for Tegwyn to the north-west in the WadewaterYou found Tegwyn in the Wadewater, safe and sound.Talk to Tegwyn in the north-western reaches of the Wadewater'You say the boy might have found Uruk tracks leading north? If he goes that way he is likely to blunder into the Wadewater. Children of the village are forbidden from going there, but I will not seek to tell you that it has prevented the more adventurous sorts from exploring that marsh. If Tegwyn tried tracking the Uruks there... well, there are plenty of dangers in the Wadewater to begin with, let alone our recent troubles!

'You should follow the road north-east to the Dunlending town of Lhan Garan. It sits on the eastern side of the Wadewater, and their scouts may have seen the boy. Perhaps he went to speak with the Dunlending villagers there, and is even now enjoying their hospitality or their tales? We should not leap to judgement too soon; he may be in no danger at all.''You should follow the road north-east to the Dunlending town of Lhan Garan. It sits on the eastern side of the Wadewater, and their scouts may have seen the boy. Perhaps he went to speak with the Dunlending villagers there, and is even now enjoying their hospitality or their tales? We should not leap to judgement too soon; he may be in no danger at all.''Hello there.''I heard Tegwyn has gone missing, ${PLAYER}. With Uruks in Swanfleet, I felt it wisest to begin the search as soon as possible.

'That said, if he has truly made for the Wadewater, I think Uruks may be the least of his problems. The footing there is unsteady, and like any marshland the depth of the pools may be deceptive. There are creatures in the Wadewater that would love nothing more than to make a supper of anyone who strays too near their domain. The most dangerous of these are the avanc, and we should hunt them as we seek the boy.''There are creatures in the Wadewater that would love nothing more than to make a supper of anyone who strays too near their domain. The most dangerous of these are the avanc, and we should hunt them as we seek the boy.''No sign of Tegwyn? I have seen nothing either. I was trained in the art of tracking, but this marshland has put my skills to the test.

'Let us <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for some sound of the boy. We must use all of our senses on this hunt.''Let us <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for some sound of the boy. We must use all of our senses on this hunt.''Nothing.

'Let us continue our search further to the west.''This does seem to be Tegwyn's sword....

'That is not a good sign, ${PLAYER}. Let us <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> once again, and hope this time we hear something. He may not have much time left.''Let us <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> once again, and hope this time we hear something. He may not have much time left.''Is that Tegwyn? Someone calls out to the north-west!''Here I am!''I'm here... I'm here, ${PLAYER}!

'Your adventuring lessons were not complete! You didn't mention how cold and damp it would be, or how often things would be trying to kill me! I stayed away from the avanc, because I'm no fool, but even the turtles here tried to snap at me!

'Still... it was quite an adventure, for my very first! If you're planning to scold me, you can forget about it... because I learned something important! I know where the Uruks are going!'The Bracing Attack is an important tool used by Champions who must fight alone and outnumbered.Strike enemies with Bracing AttackPostman Smallburrow of Stock has asked you to deliver a satchel to Budgeford.Postman Bolger can be found on the east side of Budgeford, north of the pig pens.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Bolger in Budgeford as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty, and keep the mail satchel from getting wet!Collect the satchel from Postman Smallburrow's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'I have always done my duty as a postman to the best of my ability, but hobbits send so many letters! Sometimes it is quite overwhelming!

'If you'd like to ease some of my workload a little, you'll find a satchel full of mail there on the table that must be delivered to Postman Bolger in Budgeford as quickly as possible. Would you mind taking it to him? Postman Bolger can be found on the east side of Budgeford, north of the pig pens.

'If you get seen by nosey hobbits, you won't be able to deliver the mail as quickly as it must be done for the reputation of the Quick Post service to be upheld, so don't stop to chat! And keep the satchel from getting wet -- Budgeford is a muddy place, and we don't want to soil the mail with it.''The satchel for Budgeford is over there on the table. Take it to Postman Bolger as quickly as possible! Remember, let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty and stay away from water!'Postman Spinner of Woodhall has asked you to deliver a satchel to Stock.Postman Smallburrow can be found north-east of Stock, very near the Brandywine Bridge.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Smallburrow near the Brandywine Bridge as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty and don't let the mail satchel get wet!Collect the satchel from Postman Spinner's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'With your help, the Quick Post service can once again have a reputation for speed and quality of delivery, ${PLAYER}! If you are willing, you can help me with something right now!

'There on the table you will find a mail satchel to be delivered to Postman Smallburrow, north-east of the town of Stock. It's just up the Stock Road, east of here, and shouldn't be too much trouble. I would go myself, but there's a shipment of leaf due in any minute now and I need to be here to send out the receipts.

'You'll find Postman Smallburrow north-east of the town, quite near the Brandywine Bridge. Don't delay, and avoid nosey hobbits! They will impede your delivery with their questions and chatter! Don't let the mail satchel get wet, either!''The mail satchel is over there on the table. Take it to Postman Smallburrow near the Brandywine Bridge as quickly as possible, and let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty! You'll find him north-east of Stock!'Postman Oddfoot of Frogmorton has asked you to deliver a mail satchel to Woodhall.Postman Spinner can be found in the centre of Woodhall.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Spinner in Woodhall as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty, and do not let the satchel get wet!Collect the satchel from Postman Oddfoot's tableAvoid nosey hobbits'With your help ${PLAYER}, I believe the Quick Post service will once again be the respected establishment it used to be!

'We must act quickly! There's a mail satchel on the table there that must go to Postman Spinner in Woodhall as soon as possible, and you're just the one to do it!

'Woodhall is quite the walk from Frogmorton -- there isn't a direct route, so you might need to head out to Budgeford or Stock to find the road there. Good luck, and watch out for nosey hobbits! And steer clear of water, for it won't do to hand Postman Spinner a soaked pile of mail!''The satchel for Woodhall is over there on the table. Take it to Postman Spinner as quickly as possible, and let no nosey hobbits interfere in your duty!'Champions prefer to fight their enemies face-to-face, so that they may look their foes in the eye as they fall.Strike with Wild AttackChampions prefer to fight their enemies face-to-face, so that they may look their foes in the eye as they fall.Strike with Wild AttackIn times of war, soldiers must rally to symbols of hope and valour if they are to prove victorious when badly outnumbered.Summon your Herald of HopeLeaders who would inspire their troops to acts of great valour must lead from the front, where their example can be seen by all those who follow them.Summon your Herald of WarCaptains carry forth banners to inspire and rally their troops. Each carries their own meaning and history and those who follow them strive to honour those tales.Summon your Herald of VictoryComplete both Cat Conundrum quests during the Midsummer Festival.Complete Cat Conundrum: Yes to Cats and Cat Conundrum: No to Cats during the Midsummer Festival.Complete Cat Conundrum: Yes to CatsComplete Cat Conundrum: No to CatsOdovacar Bolger has sent you to pursue the so-called Black Rider who has been stalking his pig sties by night.The "Black Rider" was seen in Cam Puddifoot's fields, east of Budgeford. 

Odovacar Bolger told you that one of his neighbours, Cam Puddifoot, reported the Black Rider on his land, being chased by wolves. Odovacar has asked you to go look for the horseless "Rider".Look for signs of the "Black Rider"Odovacar Bolger is at his home up the hill in the centre of Budgeford.

Odovacar Bolger sent you to search Puddifoot's fields for signs of the Black Rider, but all you found was a ruined black cloak. You should bring the cloak back to Odovacar.'Cam Puddifoot just told me that one of his hands spotted that so-called Black Rider heading off to the east -- on foot, mind you. No horse in sight, not even a pony.

'Cam says he was seen running through some fields of his, being chased by some wolves. It's bad enough we have to deal with unwanted nuisances like these "Black Riders", but now we have to worry about wolves, too?

'If this fellow gets himself eaten by wolves, I'll never know what's going on here, so you'd best do something about it. Head off to Cam Puddifoot's fields, east of Budgeford, and look for any signs of that "Black Rider".''I want you to find that black-robed chap and get to the bottom of this, ${PLAYER}. He was seen being chased by wolves through Cam Puddifoot's fields, east of Budgeford.''Ha! That's a hobbit-sized cloak all right. It must have got snagged when he was running away.

'Don't worry about losing his trail. We'll soon have him!'Bothersome birds have become a nuisance in the fields of Lintrev.Adan Rhuvyg has asked you to collect craban wings from the gardens of Lintrev.

Lintrev is in the Stoor-vales.Collect craban wings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the craban wings to Adan Rhuvyg.

Adan is in Lintrev.'Oh, hullo! You're new here, aren’t you! You have that adventuring air about you, and folk such as yourself always seem to be looking for jobs to do for some extra coin. Well I have coin and job both, if you are willing!

'The gardens are plagued by bothersome crow-like birds. They're very odd looking, they eat all the seed, and they peck at your toes if you try to shoo them away! Do away with the pests, but bring me their wings? I wish to study them in detail.''You return! Most excellent! The farmers will be glad you have helped in their fields, and everyone's toes will be safer now.'Master the art of trap-setting to be able to deploy them no matter the distractions.Complete Sturdy TrapsUse your Set Trap or Set Snare skillsVery few keep their eyes down to look for a tripwire, and if they do, they'll never see you coming.Use your Tripwire skillWith practice, you can kindle flame from fragments faster and with less effort.Strike with Fiery RidiculeWith practice, you can kindle flame from fragments faster and with less effort.Strike with Fiery RidiculeImprove the effect your touch can have upon your foe.Strike with Shocking TouchImprove the effect your touch can have upon your foe.Strike with Shocking TouchThere is no point in going into a fight if you always run out of breath just as things are getting good.Use Catch a BreathThere is no point in going into a fight if you always run out of breath just as things are getting good.Use Catch a BreathCrocus Stonybanks is trying to assemble some camp-fire materials so she can go camping with her friends.Crocus Stonybanks is in Overhill.

Crocus has asked you to bring her two rowan camp-fire kits so she can go camping with her friends.'Hello there! Do you mind helping me with something?

'I'm going to go camping with my friends in the Bindbole Wood, and we want to be sure we have everything all set. I still need two rowan camp-fire kits, though.

'Can you bring them for me? I'll give you some coins and other useful things for them, all right?''Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}! This is just what we need!

'Here are your coins and a few odds and ends, as I promised. Camping is so exciting, isn't it? I wouldn't want to do it outside of the Shire, though, that's for certain!'The jeweller Guleneth has asked you to bring him polished agates he can use in the pieces he makes.Guleneth is at Celondim in Ered Luin.

Jeweller Guleneth has asked you to acquire three polished agates that he can use to complete some of the pieces he has left unfinished.'I am a jeweller by interest and by trade, and I have a great many pieces in various states of completion. I could finish many of these pieces, but I am missing the gems needed for the final settings.

'If you know a jeweller with a ready supply, I will give you some coins for bringing to me three polished agates of suitable quality.

'Your assistance will be greatly appreciated, for I have already neglected these pieces for too long and am eager to complete them. I have one or two items that may be useful to you, and would happily trade them to you in exchange for the agates I need.''These polished agates are just the sort for which I have been waiting, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for them!

'Take these coins and items with my well-wishes, for now I can finish the pieces I have kept too long undone!

'Perhaps when this affair is finished, I shall find a place on one of the White Ships and sail away into the West. I will need to think on it.'Geoffrey Fuller has a real problem with the splinters he gets daily from working at the Combe lumber-camp.Geoffrey Fuller is in the village of Combe.

Geoffrey is sick to death of the splinters he encounters every day during his work at the lumber-camp and has asked if you can bring him some padded gloves. A tailor should be able to make the gloves.'I work up at the lumber-camp most days, and I'll tell you this: I'm always getting splinters. I hate it! These tiny little pieces of wood are always flying up from the wood as we cut it, and they get their revenge through annoyance! Small annoyances, to be sure, but after a full day of it, you'd be sick to death of the things, and I've been working there going on three weeks now!

'And that's not all! The axes we use have wooden handles, and if you don't get splinters from gripping those things, then I'm a dwarf! I'm just about at the end of my wits!

'If you know a tailor of even small skill, I could do with a pair of padded gloves. I'll pay you for the trouble, of course, with coins and a few materials, and I'll be in your debt!''You've brought me some padded gloves, haven't you? Let me see them!

'Ah, these are just the thing, ${PLAYER}! I'd like to see the splinters from my axe-hilt get through these! Or rather, I wouldn't!

'These things aren't much, but I hope you can use them for something as useful as these gloves you have given me!'The Elf Laegon has taken to practising his bow-making, and he often wants for materials.Laegon is at Celondim, in Ered Luin.

Laegon has asked if you could bring him three rowan bowstaves he can use to refine his bow-bending techniques.'Are you a woodworker? I have taken to practising my bow-bending, and I always have need of rowan wood with which to refine my technique.

'If you can bring to me three rowan bowstaves, I will appreciate it and give to you some coins and materials.''These will serve wonderfully well, my friend. I thank you for them and will resume my practice at once!

'I hope these coins and materials are of use to you.'Gagi Cloudbrow tried to make himself some bronze leggings, but the event has been described as something of a disaster.Gagi Cloudbrow is west of Frerin's Court.

Gagi Cloudbrow has asked you to procure for him some bronze leggings, because the pair he tried to make for himself turned out poorly, and in no way resembled the leggings for which he was trying.'I don't know what the problem is, stranger. My father was a metalworker, and my father's father was a metalworker, but I do not seem to have inherited their skill with hammer and anvil. I do not know where it could have gone, for I have no brothers, but that skill certainly has avoided me!

'You see, I decided it was time to make a new pair of bronze leggings for myself, but I did something wrong with the heat of the fire and my hammer-blows and ended up with something more akin to a belt. A belt fused in on itself, with something like a sleeve on one end. I can't wear that! And I wouldn't wear it even if I could figure out how exactly to try it on!

'If you know a metalworker of even small skill, I'll pay you for some bronze leggings. I'll give you my leftover materials as well! And don't tell anyone about my... mishap... if you don't mind.''These will do very well, ${PLAYER}! I don't understand how mine could have turned out so very differently, because these seem easy enough to make. I just don't understand.

'Here are the coins and materials I promised you. Take with them my thanks!'Solvi Scrollbearer is certain that better use could be made of the resources found outside Gondamon and wants your help in acquiring information to support this idea.Solvi Scrollbearer is at Gondamon, on the low-lands of Ered Luin.

Solvi Scrollbearer asked you to have a scholar prepare some minor metalsmithing-lore and some minor woodworking-lore for him to examine.'If we are to defeat the goblins of Rath Teraig and the sneaking Dourhands that even now remain in the hidden corners of the Blue Mountains, we'll need to make better use of the resources we have available.

'The wild lands around Gondamon are a bounty of such resources, but if we don't make full use of them, we might as well be giving them to the goblins!

'If you know a scholar of some skill, I would have him prepare for me some minor metalsmithing-lore and some minor woodworking-lore. Armed with these, I can surely prepare a plan for better using what we have. I will pay you for your efforts, of course.''Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}! Now I must engross myself in study and take what lessons from these I can!

'Here is your payment, as I promised.'Marigold Twospade has asked you to bring her some minor tailoring-lore so she can learn the trade.Marigold Twospade is in Michel Delving.

Marigold asked you to bring her some minor tailoring-lore so she can get a start on learning the trade, even though no one will teach her.'I'm trying to learn how to sew and knit and make clothing out of leather and cloth and fabric, but no one is willing to teach me! It's so very maddening!

'If you happen to obtain any minor tailoring-lore, could you give it to me? If no one will teach me, how am I supposed to learn?

'I found a few old tablets in the South Fields that I'd be willing to give you if you helped me out, and maybe I could find one or two other useful things as well!''This will be just the thing, ${PLAYER}! I'll study this and become the best tailor in all the Shire -- you just wait and see!

'I've been saving up to buy something like this, so I'll give the coins to you instead, and these other things!'Odo Mudbottom is distraught that his favourite eating-place, The Floating Log, is currently undergoing repairs to its roof.Odo Mudbottom is in Frogmorton.

Odo refuses to eat at The Floating Log while the repairs on the roof are underway, but he still wants his customary mushroom pies.'I've eaten at The Floating Log almost every night for the past twenty years, but now they're working on the roof, and if you try and eat there you get plaster falling into your dishes!

'I refuse to eat there while the repairs are going on. I mean, honestly! I have my standards, and for mushroom pies I demand they be plaster-free! Is that too much to ask? I think not!

'If you know a worthy cook, I'd pay you for two mushroom pies, with coins and goods. I still need to eat, you know!''These pies look delicious! Thank you, ${PLAYER} -- maybe I don't need The Floating Log after all!

'Take these coins and other small items with my good wishes!'Ned Diggins has gone and eaten the pie crust you brought him as a replacement for the earlier crust he devoured, and now he is in a real pickle.Ned Diggins is in Michel Delving.

Ned Diggins is waiting for you to return with a pie crust he can use to replace the one he ate that was to replace the one he ate, before his wife discovers it missing.'I seem to have eaten the pie crust you brought me, ${PLAYER}.

'Do you think you could bring me another one? I'm sorry to be a bother, but I just can't help myself! I have another half-dozen eggs to give you if you'll help me! How can you refuse that?''I'm not even going to look at this one, ${PLAYER}!

'Take these coins, eggs, and other small items, and my deepest apologies for troubling you over this! Twice!'Nefi Gemcutter has broken the setting of a necklace he once fashioned and desires a replacement.Nefi Gemcutter is along the road that approaches Thorin's Hall.

Nefi Gemcutter has asked you to bring him a glittering copper necklace to replace one he made during his own time as a jeweller.'I was a jeweller of no small skill some time ago, and though I have now put down my tools, the pieces I fashioned during my youth are still precious to me.

'It is thus with sadness that I report to you that one of the necklaces I crafted but a few years ago has lost its setting! It has been too long for me to fashion a replacement, but if you know a jeweller who could do so, I would appreciate it.

'Bring me a glittering copper necklace, and I will pay you a fair sum. I have a few small items as well, including some leftover gemstones, with which I would be willing to part.''You have done as I asked and brought to me a glittering copper necklace. I thank you for it and give to you these coins and materials!

'I must admit, however, that this necklace does not seem as special to me as the one that I crafted with my own hands. Perhaps I will come to appreciate this one, but I had not expected to feel this way. That's a little strange, isn't it?

'Thank you for it, friend. I am sure I will feel differently in the morning.'Efi Plateshaper is eager to outfit the dwarves guarding the barricade to Rath Teraig and asked for your help collecting the necessary pieces of armour.Efi Plateshaper is at Gondamon, in the Low-lands of Ered Luin.

Efi Plateshaper asked you to bring him bronze gloves and a bronze helm with which he can outfit the defenders of the barricade at Rath Teraig.'Goblins infest the narrow reaches of Rath Teraig, and stout-hearted dwarves keep the southern barricade against them. Their armour will fail before their spirits do, ${PLAYER}, so we must do for them what we can!

'If you can ask a metalsmith to fashion bronze gloves and a bronze helm, then bring them to me, I will see that the staunch defenders of the barricade receive them.

'You will be paid for your trouble, of course, in coin and other small things, though given the importance of this task no one would presume to ask for payment.''Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}. Take these coins and other items. I insist, even though the knowledge of the good you are doing for the defenders should be enough.'Ingi Steambeard has been hard at work fashioning armour for the dwarves that defend Gondamon, and now he is ready to eat.Ingi Steambeard is at Gondamon, in the Low-lands of Ered Luin.

Ingi Steambeard is hungry and wants you to bring him two servings of roast pork and two hard biscuits with which to feed his appetite.'I have been assembling armour for the guards of this city for what seems like days, and I have developed an appetite! I don't have time to prepare dinner. If you can bring me something, I'll give you some coins and materials for the favour!

'I don't want just anything, though. Bring me some roast pork and two hard biscuits.

'Actually, make that two servings of roast pork! Just one won't be enough to keep me going!''This food looks delicious, ${PLAYER}! Thank you very much, and here is your payment!'Gríss Stonesmasher would like to teach some of his students how to forge weapons out of bronze and wants you to bring him some of the pieces.Gríss Stonesmasher is in the Forging Hall inside Thorin's Hall.

Gríss Stonesmasher asked you to bring him two bronze blades and two bronze hilts for him to use as examples for some of his weaponsmithy pupils.'Hello there! Do you have an ear to lend a teacher of weaponsmithy? I am glad to hear it, for time is precious and should not be wasted in dull conversation!

'I have need of several examples of bronze craftwork I can use to teach some pupils of mine the art of weaponsmithing. I have other demands on my time and cannot spend it preparing the examples.

'If you bring me two bronze blades and two bronze hilts, I will give you some coins for the favour, and a few leftover materials I do not plan on using.''These will do, I suppose. Here are the coins and materials I promised you. My pupils should be able to learn one lesson or another from studying these blades and hilts.'The Combe lumber-camp is in need of supplies with which its workers can increase the production of useable timber.Ember Hayes is at the Combe lumber-camp.

Ember has said she would pay you for a rowan hammer and three rowan hafts, if you could bring them to her. A woodworker should be able to make these items.'Hello there, do you have a moment? I'm sorry to bother you, but I thought I would ask this of you, just in case you know something about woodworking.

'Mason Thorne has charged me with purchasing supplies for the camp here, but I've had a difficult time finding woodworkers willing to sell me some of the supplies we need.

'If you don't mind, could you bring me some supplies made of rowan wood? A rowan hammer and some rowan hafts would be perfect. I'd really appreciate it, and I'd pay you for them, of course, with coins and some odds and ends!''You have the items crafted from rowan wood I requested? Thank you so much! These look to be just what Mason wanted me to procure for the lumber-camp. I'll pay you, just as we agreed. Here you go.'Ned Diggins has gone and eaten the pie crust his wife was planning on filling with delicious pie, and now he needs a replacement in a hurry!Ned Diggins is in Michel Delving.

Ned Diggins is waiting for you to return with a pie crust he can use to replace the one he ate, before his wife discovers it missing.'You've got to help me, ${PLAYER}! While my wife was out, I went and ate the pie crust she had baked...I couldn't help myself! I know that if I had waited, it would be filled with some delicious filling and be even better, but I've always been partial to the way my wife bakes the crust.

'Do you know any cooks? I need a replacement pie crust, and fast! If my wife gets back and sees the crust missing, why...she might not make another!

'I'll give you some coins and, and... half a dozen eggs if you can do this for me, ${PLAYER} -- now, quickly! Go get me a pie crust! I might have some other things lying about that I can give you as well!''You've got the pie crust there? Excellent, superb, wonderful! Here, hand it over!

'Yes, this will do perfectly! My wife will never know the difference, and she'll go ahead with her plan to fill it with something delicious: fruit filling, meat filling, who knows what she'll choose? I can't wait! Here is the reward I promised you, and my thanks for your trouble.

'This crust does look delicious. Maybe just a nibble...that won't hurt anything....'Leighton Howard has asked you to obtain some weapons of bronze with which he can defend his family.Leighton Howard is in the town of Combe, in Bree-land.

Leighton has asked you to obtain a bronze axe and two bronze blades for him, because the local weaponsmiths are charging too much for him to pay, and he needs them to protect his family.'These are dangerous times. Those Blackwold villains are roving through the Chetwood, nearly unchecked! Yes, they suffered a defeat at Archet, but you could just as well call that a defeat for the people who live there! It'll be a long time before the town is rebuilt!

'I need to defend my family from those brigands, and I don't think the constables are up to the task. They mean well, but I trust the strength of my arms more than any well-meaning constable.

'Trouble is, the smiths are tasked with too many duties and their prices are far too high! If you have any connexions, or a weaponsmith that holds you in friendship, I'd pay you reasonable rates for a bronze axe and two bronze blades, and throw in a few sundries as well. The axe will serve me until I can replace the blades of my own sword and my son's with whatever you can bring me. Hurry now! The Chetwood is full of those villainous Blackwolds!''You've got a good heart, ${PLAYER}, and I know my whole family thanks you: my wife Kate, my son Nate, and my daughters Piper and Pepper.

'I give you these coins and a few odds and ends for your trouble, and I will get to replacing the blades of my old weapons with these new ones you have brought to me.'To better twist chance in your favour, you must first master the art of piling victory on top of success.Achieve a critical hit with any skill unlocked by a critical hitTo better twist chance in your favour, you must first master the art of piling victory on top of success.Achieve a critical hit with any skill unlocked by a critical hitNuddo has witnessed the shadow's presence in the surrounding area.Nuddo tells you that the spiders have begun attacking ever since the shadow strode through the land. Cobshollow can be found to the south-west. You can take the road heading south out of Lintrev and across the bridge.

Travel to Cobshollow and contain the spider infestation.Defeat spiders in Cobshollow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nuddo should hear about the growing infestation. Nuddo Sutchic is waiting in Lintrev.Talk to NuddoNuddo Sutchic has tasked you with finding and defeating the corrupted spider queen.

Travel back to Cobshollow to the south-west and find the queen.Defeat the corrupted spider queenYou defeated the corrupted spider queen.

You should tell Nuddo in Lintrev the good news.Talk to Nuddo Sutchic'Thank you for sharing your story with me. I have witnessed the crossing of black riders through these parts and a veil of shadow along with them.

'It has had a terrible effect on the land. All the spiders of Cobshollow have come to chaos. I have been working together with my friend Coruwen to deal with the shadow's corruptive force.''So the infestation has gotten worse? If left unchecked, these spiders could multiply and endanger all of the Stoor-vales. It is bad enough with ailing crop and aggressive animals. All that won't matter if this whole land is overrun by this infestation.

'You must find the spider queen taken by the shadow and defeat them.''Thank you for defeating the spider queen. That should slow their proliferation into the Stoor-vales for now.

'But this is just the beginning. We must find a more permanent solution to driving back the shadow. We have some room to breathe yet.'Do not allow your foe to think of any target but yourself.Strike with Warden's Taunt, Warden's Aim, or Warden's ScornDo not allow your foe to think of any target but yourself.Strike with Warden's Taunt or Warden's AimEluna wants to introduce you to her pupils.Marget, Deryn, and Murig can be found near the Warg den known as Bloodhollow.

Help each of the students with their task.Complete the quest 'Melee in Bloodhollow'Complete the quest 'Morbid Botany'Complete the quest 'Securing Water'You have aided each of the scout-warriors in training, and should return to their encampment.

Talk to Deryn.Talk to DerynYou have aided each of the scout-warriors in training, and should return to their encampment.

Talk to Deryn.Talk to Deryn'I have three pupils: Marget, Deryn, and Murig. They're great students with lots of potential. While I am their teacher, they're old enough to take on responsibilities of their own. I would like for you to help each of them with a task they are working on. I think it will be helpful for them to play the teacher for once.

'Deryn is this clever fellow right next to me. Marget is over by Bloodhollow proper. Last I saw she was taking a little break after felling a few of the beasts. Murig is downhill by the river.

'Hmm? What will I be doing? I have had a long week. I might go nap. Have you had to look after three children in the wilderness for a week straight? That'll exhaust anyone.''${PLAYER}, I take it you finished the task Eluna set before you? Speaking of our dear instructor, have you seen her at all as you've been aiding us? She should have long since returned to us by now. She may be an unconventional teacher, but she is an excellent scout-warrior. I grow concerned at her unexplained absence.'There is much to do while travelling through the lands of the Shire.Complete Explorer of the Shire deedComplete The Life of a Bounder (final) deedComplete Slayer of the Shire deedComplete Restoring the Quick Post deedComplete No Place for Spoiled Pies deedComplete Shire Brew-master deedThe elements of nature can be truly understood by few and to those few alone will they lend their power.Use your Lore Skills against enemiesThe elements of nature can be truly understood by few and to those few alone will they lend their power.Use your Lore Skills against enemiesAn errant arrow has run astray of an angry avanc.Delyth Saethur has asked you to recover her missing arrow.

The arrow went missing in Clegur.Search for the missing arrowWhile searching for Delyth Saethur's missing arrow, you have come across large, reptilian footprints. You should follow the footprints and confront the creature who stole the arrow.Follow the tracksYou should bring the arrow to Delyth Saethur.

Delyth is in Clegur.Bring the arrow to DelythYou managed to recover Delyth's arrow, but it's a bit worse for the wear. She has asked you to rinse it off in the nearby river.

The river is located next to Clegur.You should bring the cleansed arrow to Delyth.

Delyth is in Clegur.'Oh, hullo there! My name is Delyth Saethur. I wonder if you might help me. I was practicing with my bow when one of my shots went a bit wide of the target. I went after it, but some large creature seems to have made off with it, judging by the footprints.

'If you are heading down by the river, and you see my arrow, or find the large creature, would you bring it back? The arrow, I mean, not the large creature.''Hullo, hullo! Do you have it? You found my arrow!'

She reaches out then recoils.

