Talk to Culhuc.Talk to Culhuc'As you know, there's a risk we may not have enough food to last winter. There's a healthy population of avanc out in the Wadewater. I'm sure if cooked properly, they might taste good. How are your butchering skills?''Good! This gives me plenty to experiment with.'While the Elves were long known as masters of lore, the Dúnedain of old were very near their equals in many arts.Use Signs of Power or Battle to improve your skill.Use Wizard's Frost, Fire, or SparkImprovisation is a vital skill for any performer.Change StancesIncrease your vigour and find greater well-springs of spirit within yourself.Use Healing SkillsIncrease your vigour and find greater well-springs of spirit within yourself.Use Healing SkillsThe armies of Saruman are on the march.The armies of Saruman are on the march!Reach Level 10 to unlock Epic BattlesThe armies of Saruman approach the Hornburg, and Aragorn wishes to help his companions prepare for the epic battle soon to be joined.Aragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Talk to Aragorn and learn about Epic BattlesAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Listen to Aragorn and his companions discuss the coming battleAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Talk to the Officer and learn about CommandersAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Talk to Legolas and learn about Approaching EnemiesAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Listen to Legolas and his companions discuss the effectiveness of dealing with enemies at rangeAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Talk to the Engineer and learn about Siege EquipmentAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Talk to Aragorn and learn about Battle RolesAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Talk to the Engineer and learn about the Engineer RoleTalk to the Officer and learn about the Officer RoleTalk to the Vanguard and learn about the Vanguard RoleAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Talk to Aragorn and learn about MeritAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Listen to Aragorn and his companions discuss Merit and medalsAragorn stands before the walls of the Hornburg, discussing what your friends should expect in the coming battles.Talk to Gimli when you are done learning about Epic Battles for now'I believe I know enough for now, ${PLAYER}. I hope you feel the same! This land will not give in to Saruman's designs without a fight!''Saruman's armies will soon be here, ${PLAYER}, but I fear that my companions do not know what to expect. <rgb=#FFFF00><b>An Epic Battle is not like the engagements we have faced to this point</b></rgb>, and I want to ensure that our friends are ready.''Selecting the Commander will highlight all of the soldiers under his command.

'During battle, by <rgb=#FFFF00><b>speaking with someone 'Awaiting Orders,' like a Commander,</b></rgb> you can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>change the tactics of a group of soldiers</b></rgb>. 

'Some options are available at the outset, such as <rgb=#FFFF00><b>healing the soldiers</b></rgb> over time and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>increasing their damage output</b></rgb>.

'Other options become available  <rgb=#FFFF00><b>by spending points in the Officer Battle Role</b></rgb>.''We have fought large numbers of enemies before, but never so many foes as this! There will <rgb=#FFFF00><b>simply be too many enemies</b></rgb> for one hero to dispatch alone.

'We must <rgb=#FFFF00><b>use other methods</b></rgb> against them if we are to survive.''If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>excel at building, upgrading, and firing siege equipment</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Engineer Battle Role</b></rgb>.

'Engineers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>build siege equipment and other devices more quickly</b></rgb>. They also have more options for <rgb=#FFFF00><b>upgrading and repairing</b></rgb> such devices, and can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>place traps</b></rgb> to hinder the enemy.

'Engineers can also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>disable enemy traps</b></rgb>.''If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>excel at issuing orders to Commanders</b></rgb> and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>provide useful buffs to your allies</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Officer Battle Role</b></rgb>.

'Officers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>issue more effective orders to Commanders</b></rgb>. They also have more commands at their disposal, and can make a group of soldiers <rgb=#FFFF00><b>focus on particular targets</b></rgb> or <rgb=#FFFF00><b>change their weapons</b></rgb>.

Officers can command soldiers to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>shelter from incoming catapult shells or arrows</b></rgb>.

'Additionally, Officers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>plant banners that aid nearby Engineers and Vanguards</b></rgb>.''If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>stand toe-to-toe with enemy forces</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Vanguard Battle Role</b></rgb>.

'Vanguards <rgb=#FFFF00><b>unlock powerful attacks by earning Killstreaks</b></rgb>, defeating many enemies in succession. They also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>receive benefits by dealing and receiving damage</b></rgb>, and can also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>run faster</b></rgb> than other heroes.

'A Vanguard is happiest when <rgb=#FFFF00><b>engaging in close-quarters combat</b></rgb>.''I would count mere survival of the battle a success, given the foes arrayed before us, but <rgb=#FFFF00><b>the truest victory is one in which we overcome all the challenges</b></rgb> the battle brings.

'As a battle ebbs and flows, we may be presented with <rgb=#FFFF00><b>optional side objectives</b></rgb>.

'These are <rgb=#FFFF00><b>not necessary for victory, but completing them successfully will add to the Merit we earn</b></rgb> in the battle: the measure of our victory.''<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Enemies will march in formations</b></rgb> toward us. When a formation reaches our position, enemies will engage in close combat. We should <rgb=#FFFF00><b>use siege equipment to lessen their numbers first</b></rgb>, before that happens!

'<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Anyone can build and use basic siege equipment</b></rgb>.

'Other options become available <rgb=#FFFF00><b>by spending points in the Engineer Battle Role</b></rgb>.

'If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>excel at building, upgrading, and firing siege equipment</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Engineer Battle Role</b></rgb>.

'Engineers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>build siege equipment and other devices more quickly</b></rgb>. They also have more options for <rgb=#FFFF00><b>upgrading and repairing</b></rgb> such devices, and can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>place traps</b></rgb> to hinder the enemy.

'Engineers can also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>disable enemy traps</b></rgb>.''Selecting the Commander will highlight all of the soldiers under his command.

'During battle, by <rgb=#FFFF00><b>speaking with someone 'Awaiting Orders,' like a Commander,</b></rgb> you can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>change the tactics of a group of soldiers</b></rgb>. 

'Some options are available at the outset, such as <rgb=#FFFF00><b>healing the soldiers</b></rgb> over time and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>increasing their damage output</b></rgb>.

'Other options become available  <rgb=#FFFF00><b>by spending points in the Officer Battle Role</b></rgb>.

'If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>excel at issuing orders to Commanders</b></rgb> and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>provide useful buffs to your allies</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Officer Battle Role</b></rgb>.

'Officers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>issue more effective orders to Commanders</b></rgb>. They have more commands at their disposal, and can make a group of soldiers <rgb=#FFFF00><b>focus on particular targets</b></rgb> or <rgb=#FFFF00><b>change their weapons</b></rgb>.

'Officers can also command soldiers to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>shelter from incoming catapult shells or arrows</b></rgb>.

'Additionally, Officers can <rgb=#FFFF00><b>plant banners that aid nearby Engineers and Vanguards</b></rgb>.''If you want to <rgb=#FFFF00><b>stand toe-to-toe with enemy forces</b></rgb>, you should focus on the <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Vanguard Battle Role</b></rgb>.

'Vanguards <rgb=#FFFF00><b>unlock powerful attacks by earning Killstreaks</b></rgb>, defeating many enemies in succession. They also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>receive benefits by dealing and receiving damage</b></rgb>, and can also <rgb=#FFFF00><b>run faster</b></rgb> than other heroes.

'A Vanguard is happiest when <rgb=#FFFF00><b>engaging in close-quarters combat</b></rgb>.''We have fought large numbers of enemies before, but never so many foes as this! There will <rgb=#FFFF00><b>simply be too many enemies</b></rgb> for one hero to dispatch alone. We must <rgb=#FFFF00><b>use other methods</b></rgb> against them if we are to survive.''Saruman's armies will soon be here, ${PLAYER}, but I fear that my companions do not know what to expect. <rgb=#FFFF00><b>An Epic Battle is not like the engagements we have faced to this point</b></rgb>, and I want to ensure that our friends are ready.

'I would count mere survival of the battle a success, given the foes arrayed before us, but <rgb=#FFFF00><b>the truest victory is one in which we overcome all the challenges</b></rgb> the battle brings. As a battle ebbs and flows, we may be presented with <rgb=#FFFF00><b>optional secondary objectives</b></rgb>. These are <rgb=#FFFF00><b>not necessary for victory, but completing them successfully will add to the Merit we earn</b></rgb> in the battle: the measure of our victory.''It is very complicated, but I believe I understand what Aragorn has said to us. We will do well, ${PLAYER}, I am certain of it!''<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Enemies will march in formations</b></rgb> towards us. When a formation reaches our position, enemies will engage in close combat. We should <rgb=#FFFF00><b>use siege equipment to lessen their numbers first</b></rgb>, before that happens!

'<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Anyone can build and use basic siege equipment</b></rgb>.

'Other options become available <rgb=#FFFF00><b>by spending points in the Engineer Battle Role</b></rgb>.''There are three different Battle Roles in which you can specialize, ${PLAYER}. These Roles are <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Engineer</b></rgb>, <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Vanguard</b></rgb>, and <rgb=#FFFF00><b>Officer</b></rgb>.

'By performing well during battle, you will <rgb=#FFFF00><b>earn points you can spend on these Roles in the Promotions Panel</b></rgb>, becoming more effective at your chosen specialization.

'Speak with each of the representatives here to learn what each Battle Role has to offer.'Sigurdór, at the tower outside of Kheledúl, has asked you to avenge his brother where he cannot.Kheledûl lies below the tower where Sigurdór waits.

Sigurdór asked you to make your way to Kheledúl to exact vengeance on the Dourhand dwarves for his slain brother.Defeat Dourhands at Kheledúl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sigurdór is at the tower outside Kheledúl.

You exacted vengeance upon the murderous Dourhand dwarves responsible for slaying Sigurdór's brother, Arndór. Now you should return to Sigurdór.Talk to Sigurdór'I did attempt to fight my way through the port in search of the leader, to no avail. His cowardice keeps him well hidden and his lackeys gave my legs a good beating. Were it not for Svanr, I likely would have fallen to them as well.

'I failed to avenge Arndór. I am not fit for another foray, but you have helped Askell, and I hope that you will help me.

'Below us, in the valley to the east, lay the port of Kheledúl and therein the Dourhands. Will you go there and strike down a goodly number of the forces there so I might be able to give my brother the vengeance that he deserves?''My brother may not know that this has been done, but I do and this will give me leave to rest at night. I am ever in your debt, ${PLAYER}.

'I will miss my brother, but I will know that his death is avenged and that the Dourhands are weakened now to a point where we Longbeards may drive them, finally, from our lands.''Carry out my vengeance, ${PLAYER}! The Dourhands of Kheledûl must pay for their affrontery.'Explore the settlements held by the Dwarves, the old places left behind by the Elves, and the strongholds of the Dourhand brigands.Explore the Dourhand StrongholdsExplore the places of the DwarvesExplore the Elf-ruins of Ered LuinExplore Rath TeraigEluna asked you to speak with the people of Lhan Garan.Eluna has asked you to say farewell to her students before you leave.

Talk to Murig, Deryn, and Marget.Talk to MurigTalk to DerynEluna is waiting for you.

Talk to Eluna.Talk to Eluna'Before you go, say good-bye to the children, please.'Murig smiles warmly as you approach.

'You had no obligation to us, yet you continued to put yourself in harm's way at every turn. Thank you.

'The others and I will keep Lhan Garan safe. It will be here should you ever choose to come visit.''Farewell, ${PLAYER}. You have been a boon to us, and a genuine pleasure to get to know.

'Be safe on your travels.'

He thrusts a small parcel of bread into your hands.Marget's attention is on Ardhun. It's only when you get close does she seem to remember the world around her.

'Say, traveller, you saw how she fought, right? How do you think I would measure up against her?'

Marget smiles at you, and there is a hint of danger and mischief in her eyes.

'About as well as I'd measure up against you, I suspect.

'I hear you are to leave us soon. I hope the rest of your adventures are at least half as exciting as the one we shared.

'Come visit us again. And bring bread. Deryn's tastes like medicine, somehow.''Hello, traveller.

'I'm sad to see you leave, but more than that, I'm grateful for your acquaintance in the first place. These past months have been quite the trial for all of us. Setting down roots in a foreign land, away from everything we call familiar, it's not easy. It makes every kindness feel more meaningful.

'Ardhun? Well, she's stuck with us now. In a selfish way, I'm glad she is. I much prefer her being here with me, even if she's going to sulk her way through the entire winter.

'Be kind to yourself out there.'Eldo Swatmidge is a successful farmer, but he is lonely. He has sought your help to woo his neighbour, the Widow Froghorn.The Widow Froghorn's farm is on the road west and south of Eldo Swatmidge's farm.

Eldo Swatmidge asked you to collect the produce that Asphodel Froghorn means to sell.Collect produce from Asphodel FroghornHimloc Grouse can usually be found in the town square of Staddle, west of the Widow Froghorn's farm.

Asphodel seems to think highly of you and has asked you to sell some of her produce to Himloc Grouse, the trader.Widow Froghorn's farm is east of Staddle.

Asphodel Froghorn is waiting for the payment you received from Himloc Grouse for the sale of her vegetables.'Asphodel keeps her farm going by selling her goods at the Farmer's Market. I made a deal with Himloc Grouse to pay double what others pay for her fresh vegetables.

'Could you go to her farm, collect the produce she means to sell, and deliver it to Himloc? Be sure to return the money to her when you are done.''You go take Asphodel's produce to Himloc Grouse in town... and don't forget to mention my kind treatment of my dogs!''Eldo didn't send a layabout, did he?

'And he's kind to his dogs? How about that?

'Since you've already proven yourself so useful, why not take this into Staddle and sell it to Himloc Grouse? He'll be in the town square, most likely. Maybe then we can continue our discussion of Eldo Swatmidge's good qualities, of which I am sure you will tell me there are many.''If you are going to volunteer your labour, you might as well take my produce to Himloc Grouse.''I told you that you had impressed her! It sounds like we're making progress, yes it does!

'Oh, by the way, I told old Himloc that when he buys produce from Asphodel, he should pay double what he normally would, and I'd pay him the difference. I figured you should know -- don't be surprised when you talk to him!''So you've got some produce for sale from the Widow Froghorn, do you? Well, I'll be taking it... and here's the payment.

'And before you start thinking I've gone soft in the head, that's double what I usually pay. Eldo Swatmidge and I have a standing agreement, on account of he asked me to pay double for any of the Widow's produce, then he gives me the difference. It's true what they say: a hobbit in love don't have no hobbit-sense at all!

'You bring that payment back to the Widow Froghorn and don't mention the agreement I've got with Swatmidge. That's part of the whole arrangement.''Old Himloc kept up his end of the bargain? Good, good! Well, take that money on to Asphodel now and be sure to mention my good hobbit-sense!''You go take that payment back to the Widow Froghorn... but don't you tell her why I paid so much!''This seems like a bit much. Are you sure Himloc gave you the right amount? No, don't tell me. I have a feeling Eldo Swatmidge might have something to do with Himloc's generosity.'Odovacar Bolger is certain the mystery of the trespasser in black will soon be resolved.Odovacar Bolger has lent you the services of his hound, Veronica, to track down the mysterious "Black Rider". He told you to follow Veronica wherever she lead, and she would find the trespasser.Follow Veronica to the "Black Rider"Greta Fallohide is in Budgeford.

Veronica has led you to Greta Fallohide. Could she be the mysterious "Black Rider?"Fogo Fallohide can be found at The Golden Perch in Stock, south-east of Budgeford.

Odovacar's Bolger's hound, Veronica, led you to Greta Fallohide, who told you she made the cloak for her nephew, Fogo. Fogo Fallohide is very likely the "Black Rider". You should seek him out.Odovacar Bolger can be found at his home in the centre of Budgeford north of his pig sties.

You should return to Odovacar Bolger and let him know what you learned about the "Black Rider."'Never fear! My hound, Veronica, will track down that "Black Rider" with just a sniff of his cloak. She's the best hunter in the Four Farthings! Maggot can talk up his Grip, Fang, and Wolf all he likes, but I'll stake Veronica against the pack of 'em!

'You just follow Veronica wherever she leads, and you'll see! She'll find that trespasser!''I want you to find out who has been masquerading around my sties!'Veronica snuffles at the cloak, sniffs the air for a moment, and then yips excitedly.'Do you know yet who has been masquerading around my sties?''What? What Black Rider? Me? Of all the absurd...! Oh, this black cloak... yes, I have seen it before. I sewed it!

'I sewed that cloak for my good-for-nothing nephew, Fogo. Little thanks I got from him, too. If you want to speak with him, he's likely at The Golden Perch in Stock, cadging drinks.

'I wondered what that cloak was for. He acted so mysterious about it. I'll take it back, thank you very much, and you go have a word with Fogo.''You go talk to my good-for-nothing nephew, Fogo, and ask him what he's been up to. You're sure to find him cadging drinks at The Golden Perch, down Stock way.''One of those Fallohides is behind the fright? Which one?''Ah well, I guess you've found out my little secret. We thought it would be so much fun!

'See, I met this fellow a few days ago, while I was drinking, called himself "The Chief" he did. He said he was an old friend of Odo's, wanted to play a little joke on him. Told me to get a black cloak and gave me some money to haunt Odovacar's farm by night.

'Well now! Surely you don't think I meant any harm! I never! That Chief fellow? I haven't seen him since, come to think of it. At least I got some spare money for beer out of it. Oh, yes... I promise not to do it again. Those wolves almost got me! I won't be running around at night anymore, that's for sure!''You go tell old Odovacar that I didn't mean any harm by it -- I just thought it would be a funny joke! Odo's probably at his house in the centre of Budgeford, north of his pig sties.''Shame on Fogo for scaring Mr. Bolger's pigs!''I suppose it wouldn't be right to report that fool to the Shirriffs. But I wonder who this "Chief" might be, and why would he want to play this terrible joke on me? You don't suppose... that Lotho... no!

'Well, there's no way to prove anything I guess, but if Lotho wants to buy my farm, he'll have a long wait, let me tell you! It will take a lot more than this little "joke" before I let go of my land!

'Thank you kindly, for all your work. You may just have saved me from doing something very foolish. Please accept this small reward for your work.'Warriors must have courage to do battle, and in battle it is your sworn duty to ensure they have it.Use Words of CourageWarriors must have courage to do battle, and in battle it is your sworn duty to ensure they have it.Use Words of CourageGafí, the provisioner of Gondamon, has asked for your help building up their winter stores.Bears can be found in the wilds around Gondamon, especially to the north.

Gafí has asked you to bring in bear-meat to help fill Gondamon's stores for the coming months.'Our huntsmen are skilled, but this year's hunt has proven particularly difficult, what with the cold and the wretched Dourhands. I have found myself short of supplies for the coming winter.

'You can help us by bringing in some bear-meat. There are plenty of bears in the wilds around Gondamon, especially to the north.

