Otho thinks that the Shirriffs should be made aware of the danger the spiders may pose and has asked you to speak with Robin Smallburrow, the Shirriff in Hobbiton.There may be spiders in the Bindbole Wood, north and north-west of Overhill.

Otho Broadbelt sent you to speak with Robin Smallburrow about the spiders, but the Hobbiton Shirriff had already received reports about the creatures in Bindbole Wood. Shirriff Smallburrow has asked you to kill as many of the spiders as you can, but also to find their nest.Defeat spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the spiders' nestRobin Smallburrow can be found in the Ivy Bush in the centre of Hobbiton.

Shirriff Smallburrow sent you to deal with the spider threat in Bindbole Wood and to discover the location of their nest. You should report back to Robin Smallburrow with news of your success.'I hate to make more work for you, but it seems that the spiders infesting my waggon have run off somewhere. If they grow and breed, they may become a threat elsewhere in the Shire.

'I think you should report this to the Shirriff in Hobbiton, Robin Smallburrow, and see what he thinks should be done. Robin Smallburrow can usually be found at The Ivy Bush Inn in Hobbiton town centre.

'The last thing the Shire needs is an infestation of spiders nearly as big as a hobbit!''Please talk to Shirriff Robin Smallburrow in Hobbiton. I'm worried about all the spiders you didn't find.''Otho Broadbelt was right to be concerned. I've already had reports of dangerous spiders seen in the Bindbole Wood, north and north-west of Overhill. I think I'm going to send you to look into this problem.

'Try to kill as many of the spiders as you can, but also explore the north end of the woods and see if you can find their nest.

'Folk say these are monstrously large spiders, so I'd be careful if I were you.''It's good that the Shirriff knows what happened. I hope you can deal with all those spiders.''We've got to do something about this spider problem. Search for their nests in the Bindbole Wood, north and north-west of Overhill.''I wish I could help you with those spiders, but I'm a merchant, not a warrior.''Good job! Now all we have to do is find a way to get past the webs tangling up the spider nest.'Complete all four firefly lantern quests twice.Complete the Ruby, Sapphire, Emerald, and Amethyst Firefly Lanterns questsComplete 'Ruby Firefly Lanterns' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Complete 'Amethyst Firefly Lanterns' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Complete 'Emerald Firefly Lanterns' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Complete 'Sapphire Firefly Lanterns' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Being able to gain focus in the midst of chaos is a true art that few can master.Use the skill FocusWithout the advantage of strength, you must rely on speed and agility. If you are fast enough, you might be able to finish a conflict with a single strike.Use the Aim skillYou find it considerably more difficult to maintain proper pitch when some goblin is attempting to tickle your ribs with a short sword.Evade enemy attacksComplete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earth to unlock more unique seasonal rewards.Complete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earth to unlock the ability to purchase additional seasonal rewards from Feredis.Complete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earthComplete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earth to unlock even more unique seasonal rewards.Complete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earth to unlock the ability to purchase additional seasonal rewards from Feredis.Complete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earthComplete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earth to unlock unique seasonal rewards.Complete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earth to unlock the ability to purchase additional seasonal rewards from Feredis.Complete Midsummer quests in Minas Tirith, Furtherholm, and across Middle-earthYou found the fabled "walking tree" that Gammer Boffin told you about, and it appears to be entrapped by the spiders.Gammer Boffin's draught is almost spent, but there appears to be just enough left to help weaken the webs binding the tree.Free the walking treeShirriff Robin Smallburrow is in the Ivy Bush in the centre of Hobbiton.

With the aid of Gammer Boffin's draught, you cleared the way to the nest and managed to rescue a walking tree, while dealing with the spiders. Shirriff Smallburrow will want to hear your tale.The tree shudders, attempting to tear itself loose from the webs that bind it. Perhaps there is a way you could help it clear the webs away.The tree rips itself free from its remaining bonds. Alerted by the commotion, more spiders appear from the nearby foliage.'Quite a tale you tell! Sounds more like one of those stories about the Old Forest than something we'd find in the Westfarthing!

'I think we'll need to be wary of stray spiders in the area for quite some time, but it sounds like you've taken care of the worst of them... though you needn't have made up all that about a walking tree!

'Well done, anyhow.'The time has come for you to venture beyond the borders of the Shire and to find your fortune in the town of Bree.Travel east along the road to Bree.

The Bounder suggested you might find your fortune in the town of Bree. Speak to the Mayor once you arrive.'Feeling a bit cooped up here in the Shire, eh? I say you should go to Bree, where the Men dwell. There's bound to be work for an enterprising sort like yourself. 

'Head east along the road and you'll reach the gates of Bree before you know it. Stay to the road, mind you. The Bounders don't stray far from the Shire.

'When you reach Bree-town, speak to the Mayor. He's a friendly fellow and might find a use for your talents.''From the Shire, you say? Well, friend, that's quite a journey. As for work, hmmm. Speak to me again when you've rested. You must be terribly tired.''You should go to Bree, east along the Great East Road, and speak with its mayor, Graeme Tenderlarch.'Defeat all the frosty beasts who threaten Winterhome.Defeat all the frosty beasts who threaten Winterhome.Defeat the frosty mountain bullDefeat the frosty mountain bearDefeat the frosty sabre-toothDefeat the frosty snow-beastDefeat the frosty winter wargDefeat the frosty frost-wormGreylond Bottomley told you a little of the Mathom Society and its efforts to build the Mathom House's collection, particularly with gifts given in return for kindness, selflessness, or aid rendered the giver.Greylond Bottomley is at the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire.

Greylond Bottomley has asked you to bring him any mathoms that you receive as gifts as you travel throughout the Shire.'Hullo there, my young ${RACE}, have you come to have a look around, or perhaps you're looking to make a donation to our worthy Mathom House? We accept all sorts of mathoms you know, it's amazing the odds and ends that Hobbits young and old have managed to collect and what you can see here runs the whole gamut! If you ask me, this old museum says more about us Hobbits than any book or story could hope to tell.

Right now we're looking for mathoms that have been given as gifts for some kindness or aid rendered. The stories behind such objects are of great interest to us, regardless of what the mathom itself might be. Anything you could bring us along those lines would be a fine gesture indeed.''What's that there? You received this mathom as a gift from one of our fellow hobbits? Ah, this is a fine thing indeed, an ancient tradition -- well, as old as any of them I know of at any rate. You're sure you have no need for it? Fine, fine then, I'll happily take it and see if I can find a suitable place for it in our collection!'Your deeds in the Second Age are known to the Elves of Middle-earth.Your deeds in the Second Age are known to the Elves of Middle-earth.Prove your skill in the Battle of DagorladConstant vigilance is needed to protect oneself in battle. A moment's forgetfulness can be the end of you.Strike enemies with Guardian's WardConstant vigilance is needed to protect oneself in battle. A moment's forgetfulness can be the end of you.Strike enemies with Guardian's WardAlthough Dwalin and the other Longbeards have permitted you to remain in Thorin's Hall, you have still to earn their friendship.You must earn Friend standing with the Dwarves of Thorin's HallComplete each Gathering Guests quest during the Midsummer Festival.Complete each of Captain Khâtaphos's Gathering Guests quests during the Midsummer Festival.Complete Gathering Guests: Bree-townComplete Gathering Guests: CelondimComplete Gathering Guests: DaleComplete Gathering Guests: EdorasComplete Gathering Guests: GaltrevComplete Gathering Guests: Hall of VérnozalComplete Gathering Guests: HerneComplete Gathering Guests: Minas Tirith (Midsummer)Complete Gathering Guests: NobottleComplete Gathering Guests: Ost GuruthComplete Gathering Guests: Sûri-kyläComplete Gathering Guests: The Party TreeComplete Gathering Guests: The Twenty-first HallComplete Gathering Guests: TrestlebridgeWhen facing large numbers of enemies the role of the Hunter goes from that of deadly artist to a bringer of terror from the skies.Strike enemies with Rain of ArrowsA Guardian is talented at drawing the attention of his enemies away from his friends.Use Vexing BlowAmong the most respected forms of learning is that of healing. Every Lore-master should strive to understand this fundamental art.Heal your fellows with Knowledge of CuresAmong the most respected forms of learning is that of healing. Every Lore-master should strive to understand this fundamental art.Heal your fellows with Knowledge of CuresThough reclusive, Beornings are natural leaders when called to action.Use HeartenIt is rumoured that Beorning honey-cakes are so delicious, even Elves try to replicate the recipe.Bake honey-cakesHunters are often renowned for their ability to see what is hidden and follow signs that few others are even aware of.Use Tracking skillsHunters are often renowned for their ability to see what is hidden and follow signs that few others are even aware of.Use Tracking skillsGive a helping hand to all fireworks celebration volunteers!Give a helping hand to all fireworks celebration volunteers!Assist LagorlamAssist AnurandirAssist FlíkAssist PengailAssist MachanAssist Gwin CurhononAssist LaliaAssist Robb ThornleyComplete 30 Ered Luin quests.Complete Defender of Ered Luin.Complete 30 Ered Luin quests.Complete quests in Ered LuinYou must complete a number of quests for the people of Winter-home during the Yule Festival.You must complete a number of quests for the people of Winter-home during the Yule Festival.Complete quests in Winter-home for the Yule FestivalAccording to Milo Bolger, the wolves in the ruins were heard fighting among themselves one night. When the fighting ended, a large number of wolves ran through Budgeford, but did no harm to anyone.Linda Bolger is in Budgeford, on the road furthest down the hill.

Milo Bolger told you that his wife, Linda, had been caught outside when the wolves ran through Budgeford. He told you to go speak with her to learn more.The Yale-height is a far distance south-east of Budgeford, beyond Stock Road, not far north-east of Woodhall. The hill is marked by three pillars atop its pinnacle.

Milo Bolger asked you to speak with his wife, Linda, about the strange encounter she had with the wolves in the middle of Budgeford. Linda did not have much more to reveal, other than to ask you to investigate the Yale-height, where she saw a large and evil-looking wolf digging in the soil on the night the wolves ran through Budgeford.Search the Yale-heightLinda Bolger is in Budgeford, on the road furthest down the hill.

Linda Bolger sent you to investigate the Yale-height, where she claimed to have seen a great, evil-looking wolf digging in the ground. During your search you discovered a strange, rune-inscribed collar. You should take the collar to Linda and see if it means anything to her.'A few nights agone, we heard a great ruckus. There were wolves fighting among themselves out at the old ruins! Nary a hobbit dared stray out of their holes all night. Soon after the racket died down, a good number of wolves charged through the town -- right down the middle of the street, if you believe it -- and disappeared off to the west.

'My wife, Linda, was caught outside when the wolves came through. None of them so much as looked at her! If you go back to Budgeford and talk to Linda, she might be able to figure out what's going on. The town's just west of here.

'These wolves have got me worried something terrible... someone's likely to get et!''My wife, Linda, was in Budgeford when the wolves ran through. She'd be the best one to talk to about that.''Milo told you about the wolves passing through Budgeford? I thought he might. Well, I was a short way out of town when I saw a huge wolf standing on a hilltop. It seemed to be digging in the soil of the hill with its great paws. Then it leaped down the hill and was gone.

'I started on my way home as fast as I could, but as I neared the edge of Budgeford, at least a dozen wolves came running right through the middle of town! I thought I was done for, but they just ran on, like I wasn't there at all!

'I think it might have something to do with the wolf I saw on the hilltop. It was the Yale-height, I'm sure of it. That's to the south-east of here, way down across Stock Road, not far north-east of Woodhall. The wolf was standing by the three pillars atop the hill. You might find something there.''I saw that evil-looking wolf digging in the soil on a hilltop near here. You should see if you can discover what it was doing! The Yale-height is south-east of Budgeford, only a short distance north-east of Woodhall.''My wife, Linda, saw something strange out on a hilltop the night the wolves ran through Budgeford. The Yale-height is south-east of Budgeford.''You found something on the hilltop? You should go tell my wife, Linda, in Budgeford at once!''You found this in the dirt on that hilltop? This is a collar, ${PLAYER}! Who could possibly be strong enough to put a collar on a wolf like the one I saw that night, much less want to? And how strong must the wolf have been to remove it?

'I can't read the letters that are inscribed on the collar, but they sure look unpleasant to me.'Thrasi's lynx and her cub were reunited thanks to your efforts but they are getting hungry, and Thrasi is still nursing his ankle.There are traps for small game scattered not far to the east and west of Thrasi's lodge.

Thrasi asked you to either hunt and kill a live rabbit, or to check his traps and bring back a rabbit carcass for the lynx-mother and her cub.Bring the rabbit carcass to Thrasi at Thrasi's Lodge.'The cub is hungry, but he is too young to hunt his own food. His mother is still all scratched up and in no position to hunt either. Let's see... the only meat I have here at the lodge is either dried or smoked. I think they both could use some fresh, raw meat.

'Could I ask you for another favour? I wonder if you can find a rabbit carcass for them to eat? If you have trouble hunting a live rabbit, I have a string of rabbit traps scattered in the woods not far to the east and west of the lodge. I'd appreciate it if you would check the traps and bring back a plump rabbit.

'I'd hate to see mother and cub go without food.''I have laid traps all over the place to the east and west of the lodge... surely one of them has caught a rabbit!''This'll do for now, but we can't keep hand-feeding the things, or they'll lose that wild streak that makes them good hunters.'Be a herald of your opponent's defeat.Complete Herald's HammerUse Herald's StrikeBe a herald of your opponent's defeat.Strike enemies with Healer's Strike, Hero's Strike, or Dissonant StrikePractice your attacks which cause bleeding in your foes.Strike with Cleave or RendYou have travelled with Ulfar to the outskirts of the dwarf camp in the Rushock Bog. There you hope to put an end to the dwarf Olwir's plan to capture a Stone-troll and give it as a gift to the dwarf Skorgrím in the north.Speak to Ulfar and then defend him as he delves deeper into the dwarf camp.Speak to UlfarUlfar has been wounded in the battle. Speak to him to see what he would have you do.Speak to UlfarUlfar has told you to continue on, deeper into the dwarf camp, without him and slay the Stone-troll, if you find one.

Ulfar was wounded in the fighting and was unable to continue on with you. He told you though that the Stone-troll must be slain, and to be on the watch for Olwir, as he will surely try to stop you from slaying the beast.Slay the Stone-trollWith the Stone-troll and Olwir dead, return to the wounded Ulfar and tell him what happened.Speak to Ulfar'Are you ready to depart?''All right, now be careful. We've got to get into this camp and slay the Stone-troll they may have captured.

'Also, when we get into the camp, be on the watch for that Olwir. He won't be too pleased to see us trying to slay his "gift."''Aye, I guess I've been away from battle for too long. The wound is painful, but not mortal. It will keep me from being much help, though.

'You must continue without me and slay the Stone-troll, if they've captured one. And don't forget to be on the watch for Olwir, he will do his best to stop you!

'I'll stay behind and make sure none of these lot escape.''You have to go ahead and slay that Stone-troll. If they've captured him, he'll be somewhere deeper in the camp.''Well done! I got impatient waiting, so I had to see how you were doing, but it seems you did fine without me. That Stone-troll is slain, and it seems Olwir is as well. He paid a high price for his crime, stealing that cow from Filibert, didn't he? With him gone, these dwarves shouldn't trouble Rushock Bog much longer.

'As for Filibert, do not worry about him, I'll make sure he is given money to purchase a new cow.

'You have done well today, my friend. You have my thanks.'You set out with Eluna and her students to a high-stakes negotiation.Talk to Eluna before the negotiation begins.Talk to ElunaWait for Ardhun to arrive.Wait for Ardhun to arriveListen to Eluna and Ardhun's conversation.Listen to Eluna and Ardhun's conversation<rgb=#FF0000>Do not get too close to Eluna and Ardhun's conversation</rgb>Remain alert.Remain on guard as more Draig-lûth arriveYou should defend ElunaDefend ElunaThe fight is over.

Regroup with the others.Regroup with Eluna and her studentsEluna has survived the attempt on her life, thanks in no small part to your valour.

You should talk to Eluna.Talk to Eluna'Onwards, then.''I hope we can resolve this with words alone, but if not, I will count on you to fight. Stay hidden unless you are needed.''We return to Lhan Garan without delay. Ardhun will come with us. I will take responsibility for her.'In preparation for his journey, you have come down to the banks of the Brandywine to help Bingo learn to swim.Bingo is ready to learn to swim, and needs your advice.Talk to Bingo on the banks of the BrandywineBingo is ready to learn to swim, and needs your advice.Talk to Bingo on the banks of the BrandywineBingo is ready to learn to swim, and needs your advice.Talk to Bingo on the banks of the BrandywinePerhaps leading by example will help. If you swim across the river yourself, perhaps Bingo will find it within himself to do the same.Swim to the other side of the riverYou should return to Bingo and see if your demonstration helped him gain some confidence.Return to Bingo and see if your demonstration helpedBingo splashed around some in the water. It is possible there might have been a little swimming in there, but it is hard to say for certain.Talk to Bingo, but don't let him drip on you'I am drenched, but I am happy, my friend. Let us return to the Golden Perch and dry off!''Well, here we are, ${PLAYER}. Time for this hobbit to learn a new skill!''It occurs to me that I may have made a slight error in judgement, ${PLAYER}, and I have perhaps not dressed entirely appropriately for the... cold... frigid... waters...'

Bingo shivers.

'What do you think? Do you think perhaps I just need to warm myself up? Possibly get the blood flowing? That is a capital idea, my intelligent ${RACE} friend!''I am a bit warmer, but the water still looks cold and now I just feel tired!

'You think maybe this is just a bad spot? Maybe I should try another place on the bank? Good idea!''That was incredible, my friend! If you can do it, I certainly think I can do it as well!''I did it, ${PLAYER}! Did you see me? Your feat was pretty good, but I'm afraid my own may have shown you up some.

'Now that was a true display of swimming prowess, wouldn't you say?'Toradan sent you to Skunkwood's hideout to rescue Amdir and put an end to the Blackwolds' mischief.Speak to the Blackwold guard. If your ruse is successful, he should give you access to the hideout.

Toradan sent you to Skunkwood's hideout to rescue Amdir and put an end to the Blackwolds' mischief.Speak to the Blackwold guardSkunkwood resides somewhere within the hideout.

You have tricked your way into the Blackwolds' hideout. Now you must find Skunkwood and speak with him to learn the whereabouts of Amdir.Talk to William SkunkwoodAmdir lies in the dungeons at the far end of the Blackwold hideout.

Skunkwood told you that Amdir was locked away and that what was happening to him seemed unnatural. You should find Amdir quickly.Search for AmdirYou have discovered Amdir and found that he has partially transformed into a wraith. He stopped raving at the sight of you, so perhaps there is still some hope for him.Talk to AmdirAn old woman in the back of the cell that held Amdir called to you for help. You should help her escape.

Whatever is happening to Amdir, it has driven him completely mad, and he is far more powerful than he first seemed. His deafening scream momentarily stunned you and threw open his cell door.Speak with the old prisonerTry to help Toradan defeat Amdir.

As neared the entrance of the Blackwold Hideout, you encountered Toradan and Amdir.Aid ToradanAfter helping Sara Oakheart out of the Blackwold hideout, Toradan entered and saw what had become of Amdir. Seeing his kinsman too far gone to help, Toradan attempted to slay him, but was instead himself stricken down.

You should speak with Toradan before he perishes.Speak to ToradanToradan spoke about Amdir trying to kill the other Rangers and asked you to speak with Constable Underhill about a message he sent to someone named Tanglerush.

Before leaving the hideout, however, you should speak to Sara Oakheart again to see if she needs any further help.Talk to Sara OakheartThe Blackwold guard stares up at you from beneath a furrowed brow. He spits onto the ground and studies your face for a few seconds before giving you a wry and sinister smile.'Ah, so you're the one I've heard so much about from Ellie. We lost a lot of good men in Archet, and I'll be glad to have you in the fold.

'You say you've heard about that Ranger? I have to tell you, what is happening to that fellow is plain unnatural. Éogan tells me he'll be a great boon to us, but for now he's just a raving madman.

'I don't mind letting you go take a peek in on him. He's down in the dungeon at the far end of the cavern. My guard there will let you pass.''The wound... it is so cold....

'The voice... the voice speaks to me. Commands me. Tells me things. Tells me about the end of all things...the beginning of new things. It calls me...it calls me to service....

'I must do what it says... must follow.... I serve... I must serve the Dark Lord....''Oh, thank you for coming to save me, young one! I have been held captive here for a long time! I have seen many things, and if you would be so kind as to help me out of this dungeon, I would be able to tell you a bit of what happened to your friend Amdir.'Toradan coughs up blood. 'Amdir is... beyond saving now. You must warn... my kindred....'

'Mundol is in the Mustering Cave of the Rangers. He... help him....

'Go to Underhill... ask him if... if Tanglerush delivered my message....''Goodness me, what a terrible sight for these old eyes! The blade that stung Amdir has done its work, and I fear he's nothing more than a servant of the Enemy now. You should try and stop him, if you can.

'And don't worry about me. Now that I'm free of that awful cell, I'll be fine. And I've got my stick back. Don't know what I'd have done without it.'Moving silently is easy -- moving silently and quickly? That is a challenge....Leaf-walkerUse your Sneak skillMoving silently is easy -- moving silently and quickly? That is a challenge....Leaf-walkerUse your Sneak skillMadog has asked you to demonstrate your skills at fishing.Madog asked you to catch a fish while standing near the Hobby Master in Lhan Garan.

Catch a fish.Stand near the Hobby Master in Lhan Garan and catch a fish'Another amateur angler come to help us shore up our food supplies for the winter. Well met, I'm Madog and this fella to my side is Teilo. We're in charge of filling up those racks of drying fish you passed by. If you want to help us, catch three small fish off the dock here. You have to do it on the dock here where we can watch your technique, ok?

'If you need to learn the basics, talk to this self professed 'Hobby Master' next to me. He'll teach you the basics and set you up with a basic fishing rod.''Talk to the nearby 'Hobby Master' to learn the basics and get a free basic fishing rod. Then, while you're standing next to him, catch a fish so he can observe that you have the right.''Not bad! Not good either, but not bad, especially for a beginner. You have some natural talent.'Rhawn Torlan has lost their favourite spot to look over the Wadewater.Rhawn needs help finding their lost tome. It should be in Radlaw in a location overlooking the Wadewater.Find Rhawn's bookDefeat ruffians in Radlaw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found Rhawn Torlan's lost tome.

You should bring it back to Rhawn Torlan in Clegur.Talk to Rhawn Torlan'Hello there! Don't mind me. I've only lost the best spot to read my books. I used to look upon the Wadewater's still current and reflect leisurely, until those ruffians in Radlaw moved in.

'Now, I have been resigned to reading under this post. Actually, I was wondering if you could help me? I had to leave my spot in a hurry and I lost one of my favourite books in the shuffle.

'Could you perhaps find it for me? Oh, and if you don't mind... teach those ruffians a lesson while you're at it.

'Radlaw is to the north. It should be easy to find, as it neighbours the Wadewater.''Ah yes! That's the one! The Path of the Light! This is quite a rare book and I'm so grateful that you were able to find it.

'Are you perhaps familiar with this story? It's a tale of mighty warriors from beyond the twinkling night sky vanquishing evil where it hides. They wield blades of dazzling light. It's rather far-fetched, but the adventures these warriors go on is quite fascinating!

'Perhaps not. It's not a story just anyone reads. Again, a rare legend.'The songs of life are quite draining, and only the most experienced minstrels can use them for long.Use your Healing and Motivation SkillsThe songs of life are quite draining, and only the most experienced minstrels can use them for long.Use your Healing and Motivation SkillsMany creatures of evil and darkness do not fare well before the beauty and light of music.Use Minor BalladMany creatures of evil and darkness do not fare well before the beauty and light of music.Use Minor BalladWith a lightweight blade, you may strike as quick as lightning.Use the skill FlickPolo Proudfoot needs new queens for his hives to replace the ones killed by the honey-bears.Farmer Proudfoot is guarding his hives in the meadow south-east of Tuckborough. The wild beehives you are looking for are in a bear-infested area further south-east past the meadow. 

Farmer Proudfoot sent you to Gammer Boffin in Overhill to obtain some balm to keep off the bees, so you can collect a hive for him. Gammer Boffin warned you that the salve will not last long, so you will need to collect the hive as soon as possible and take it to Polo Proudfoot.Find a wild hive before the salve driesPolo Proudfoot would like to take a moment to thank you for your efforts.'I've got the salve ready for you, my dear, whenever you're ready for it. But remember, it will only last a few minutes before it wears off, so you'd best hurry back and find a hive for Farmer Proudfoot!

'I expect you will find beehives in the woods south-east of Tuckborough. Find a big one for Polo and take it to him at his meadow nearby.

'Now, if you're carrying a delicate beehive around, you may not be able to fight off any bears or such that may be drawn to the hive, so tread carefully!''That new hive will do nicely. I'll just give the bees a while to get used to their new home.

'In the meantime, please take this reward -- you deserve it!''You'd better hurry and find one of those wild beehives before that salve you've got dries out. Look to the south-east, among all the bears, and be careful!''You'd best be finding a new hive for Polo!'If you think about it, throwing a random piece of junk at an enemy is like a long-distance punch.Use the skill Hurl ObjectUse the skill Hurl ObjectRollo Boffin, who oversees the leaf-waggons that come through Woodhall, mentioned that one of Longo Burrow's waggons did go missing a while ago and thinks that perhaps it is related to the disappearance of Gerebert Took.Longo's waggon may be at the Stock Road clearing due west of Woodhall, by the Wellbridge.

Rollo Boffin did not have any information specifically about Gerebert Took, but now wonders if Gerebert's disappearance and the disappearance of Longo Burrow's waggon are somehow connected. He has asked you to go search a clearing just off the Stock Road for any sign of the missing waggon.Search for Longo's missing waggonRollo Boffin can be found in the centre of Woodhall.

At the Stock Road clearing, you found an abandoned waggon. Your examination of the waggon revealed that it once carried pipe-weed, but all the pipe-weed was removed and carried off to the south.'I was expecting one of Longo Burrow's waggons to arrive a while ago, but the fool thing never showed up. I sent a message over to Longo, but he never answered. At the time, I supposed he had never sent the waggon or wasn't worried about it, but now you've got me wondering.

'There is a clearing north of the Stock Road where waggons occasionally stop. It's due west of Woodhall, right by the Wellbridge. Maybe there you'll find some sign of Longo's waggon or this Gerebert Took you're looking for.

'I'll have to look further into this matter. I always did think it strange that Longo didn't seem too concerned about his missing waggon.''Very curious. You say that this abandoned waggon had a wheel that was smaller than the others? That sounds like one of Longo's waggons, all right. I warned him that it wasn't safe, but he wouldn't listen to me.

'Well I suppose the only way to find out what became of that leaf, and perhaps Gerebert Took, is to follow the trail of leaf to the south.''A few waggons on their way to Woodhall stop over at the clearing on the north side of the Stock Road, near the Wellbridge. It might be a good place to search for that waggon of Longo's, if indeed it is missing. It's due west of Woodhall.'Defeat all the pesky critters who agitate Grimbeorn's bees.Defeat all the pesky critters who agitate Grimbeorn's bees.Defeat the Hateful HornetDefeat the Mischievous Midge-cloudDefeat the Nagging NeekerbreekerDefeat the Terrorizing ToadDefeat the Worrying WaspDefeat RockEverard Holebourne lost his venison and his favourite sling-stone to a marauding bear.The bear den is north of Overhill, located on the slopes above the Bolestones.

