Milo Hornblower has asked you to subdue the wild toad he has named Lobelia.Milo Hornblower is waiting by The Floating Log in Frogmorton.

You should let Milo know of your success in capturing Lobelia the Toad.'That Lobelia Sackville-Baggins has been telling everyone that she doesn't think she should give out presents at her birthday party, that she thinks it more reasonable that she should be receiving them. She needs learning, so I've been raising this toad to give her as a present. I've named the toad Lobelia, and she's proved quite as ornery as the original, if you take my meaning -- in fact she's grown to be quite enormous!

'Well, my Lobelia slipped loose today. She's too big and tough for me to deal with when she's upset, so I need someone to calm her down. Funny, though, she seems afraid of the other toads, so you might have to clear out a number of the toads in the marsh before Lobelia will show herself.

'If she does come out, she'll probably be directly north of the The Floating Log -- that section of the marsh is more familiar to her, I think, and she'll probably return there.''You certainly taught her a lesson! I wonder if I'll be able to keep Lobelia the Toad caged long enough to teach the real Lobelia a lesson as well. We'll see.

'Thanks for your help!''Lobelia the Toad won't come out if there are lots of other toads around, ${PLAYER}, so you'll want to clear out some of the toads that are currently lurking in the Frogmoors.'You are a fierce fighter who knows there is always room for improvement.Use SlashHal Hornblower wants bent claws. Hal can be found near the stable in the centre of Hobbiton.You have accepted a task to acquire bent claws for the bounders of the Shire. They have deputized Hal Hornblower to collect the items near the stables in Hobbiton.Wanted: Bent claws from the toads surrounding Frogmorton in the Shire. Bounders are looking for proof of those who are assisting them in keeping the Shire safe. Deliver the items to Hal Hornblower at Hobbiton centre.Wanted: Bent claws from the toads surrounding Frogmorton in the Shire.'Did you happen to see Lobelia when you were getting these. Oh mercy, not of the Sackville-Bagginses... the toad! Oh never you mind now, I'll be uninvited from her party for certain if anyone overheard that conversation.

