art of Kidzul-kâlah'Complete 'Mission: The Roots of Decay'Complete 'Mission: The Branches of Corruption'Complete 'Mission: The Bloody Ritual'Complete 'Mission: The Bloody Ruins'Complete 'Mission: The Missing Treasure'Complete 'Mission: An Assault of Frost'Complete 'Mission: Raiders from Gundabad'Complete 'Mission: Training For Glory'Complete 'Mission: The Throne of Tharrazhâr'Complete 'Mission: Into the Crystal Tunnels'Complete 'Mission: Secrets of the Frostdelf'Complete 'Mission: Halls of the Dead'Complete 'Mission: Trouble in the Armoury'Complete 'Mission: The Matron of the Keep'Complete 'Mission: Goblins at Stramvárth'Complete 'Mission: Abandoned Supplies'Complete 'Mission: Ore Overflowing'Complete 'Mission: The Goblins for Gorgar'Complete 'Mission: Under Command of Trolls'Complete 'Mission: The Riches of Sundergrót'Complete 'Mission: Hunting the Hunters'Complete 'Mission: Jaws of the Dead'Complete 'Mission: The Shadow of Valdhellir'Complete 'Mission: Well-fed in Wyrmsgráf'Complete 'Mission: Scatha's Legacy'Complete 'Mission: A Glutton in the Larder'Complete 'Mission: The Matron of the Hatchery'Complete 'Mission: The Den of Worms'Complete 'Mission: The Worm Hatchery'Complete 'Mission: Magic of the Frost-bound'Complete 'Mission: A Frosty Reception'Complete 'Mission: Den of the Frostbound'Complete 'Mission: Son of the Chieftain'Complete 'Mission: The Chieftain's Pack'Complete 'Mission: The Gate Captain'Complete 'Mission: Archers at the Gate'Complete 'Mission: Nests of Ice'Complete 'Mission: Area of Interest'Complete 'Mission: Wall of Ice'Complete 'Mission: Uncovered Treasures'Complete 'Mission: Two Heads are Deadlier'Complete 'Mission: Reclaiming the Torrent-spires'Complete 'Mission: The Fluttering Fires'Deryn wants you to gather some unique plants in order to study their properties.The purple flowers of amethyst nightshade can be found to the north-east of Deryn, in Bloodhollow.

Deryn has asked you to gather amethyst nightshade in Bloodhollow.Collect amethyst nightshade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Deryn can be found among his peers to the south-west of Bloodhollow.

You have collected enough amethyst nightshade to satisfy Deryn's needs. You should return to Deryn.'Duvodiad, hello. My name is Deryn, a warrior-scout in training. My specialty lies in the study of plants, especially those with... peculiar properties.

'I have a slightly morbid request to make of you. The Wargs to the east have um... piled the bones of their victims in a rather dramatic fashion. You'll note that some of these bone piles have vines with purple flowers growing from them. Could you pluck some for me? 

'Oh and you should know, I asked Marget to gather some and she made the incredible discovery that this plant is poisonous to the touch. Perhaps... wear gloves.''The flowers I require can be found in the Warg den to the north-east. I hear it referred to as "Bloodhollow", a needlessly dramatic name if you ask me. Just look for the piles of bones with plants growing from them. Hard to miss, really.''Ah yes, the flowers I asked for.'

Deryn indicates a mortar for depositing the flowers.

'You must be curious about what I plan to do with these. Perhaps I'll concoct some vile poison with which to threaten our new neighbours? Don't be silly. Many poisonous plants have incredible medicinal properties if ingested in the correct quantities. Though born of death, perhaps these flowers could do much for the living.

'Hmm? Will I ask you to ingest any? And deprive Marget the opportunity to prove she's one of the toughest warriors in our people's storied history? I could never do that to such a dear friend.'Constable Sageford believes there may be a second lockbox in the Blackwold's main camp in northern Chetwood.The main Blackwold camp is in the ruins of northern Chetwood, just east of Combe.

Constable Sageford has asked you to search the Blackwold camp for another strongbox.Collect Blackwold strongboxConstable Sageford can be found near Combe town-centre.

Sageford sent you to the Blackwold Headquarters to find another strongbox. You should return to Sageford with the news of your success.'I was talking to one of the other constables shortly before you returned, and it seems that he learned that some of the Blackwolds were keeping even more valuables in their main camp in the ruins of northern Chetwood.

'With any luck, you might find a strongbox that's not locked. It's worth trying, anyway. There are so many people who need money to rebuild, and who better to take it from than the ones that stole it in the first place?''The Blackwolds are holed up in the ruins of northern Chetwood. If you can find another lockbox -- and it is unlocked -- we can distribute the valuables to the suffering people of the Chetwood.''You found a strongbox! And... this one is locked as well. And do you see these scratches, right here on the lock? "R.F." just like on the other one.

'We need to get these strongboxes open, ${PLAYER}.'Thrasi has given you some thistle-mead to feed to the mother lynx, hopefully to help heal her injuries.The mother lynx is at Thrasi's cabin.

Thrasi asked you to feed the thistle-mead to the mother lynx.Thrasi is at the hunter's lodge to the north.

The mother lynx seems to be completely healed, yet she has returned to Thrasi's side.'All right, here you go. Try feeding some of this thistle-mead to the mother lynx. No sneaking sips for yourself, mind you!''That mead should fix her up right!'The mother lynx sniffs tentatively at the fragrant mead, then quickly laps it all up.'See? Thistle-mead! Good for what ails you... if you're a cat, that is!

'Hmm. She seems to like me... doesn't want to run off anyway. I could use a hunting partner, and her cub's taken a shine to me as well.

'Thanks for all your help, friend. In a few years, this cub'll be old enough to join me on hunts with his mother. Hendrevail beware!'Sing to the North Wind, bringing it down upon your foes.Call the North WindCall the North WindEllie Cutleaf, a resident of Combe, is mentioned by name in the letter you found in the Blackwold recruit's pack.Ellie Cutleaf's house lies in the north-west corner of Combe, on the banks of the pond.

After discovering the identity of the Blackwold agent, Constable Underhill asked you to enter the ranks of the Blackwolds by speaking with Ellie Cutleaf and doing whatever she asks of you.Skunkwood's farm can be found by following the road east up the hill and then north into the Chetwood. Follow the road east through the woods and towards the northern end of the Midgewater Marshes.

Constable Underhill ordered you to try and insinuate yourself into the Blackwolds' good graces by doing tasks for their agent, Ellie Cutleaf. However, Ellie admitted her involvement and her desire to leave that part of her life behind. She has asked you for help righting her wrongs.Defeat Skunkwood's den-motherEllie Cutleaf's house lies in the north-west corner of Combe, on the banks of the pond.

Ellie Cutleaf asked you to slay the den-mother she bred with a Warg for Jagger Jack, the wolf-keeper of the Blackwolds. You should return to her with news of your success.'Now here's an idea. Ellie is looking for new blood, so why not help her out? You could mask yourself as a ruffian and offer to join the Blackwolds. Gain her confidence, and we might find out where the Blackwold leaders are hiding! Of course, it would be dangerous! Do you think you're up to the task?

'Ellie's house is in the north-west corner of town, by the pond. There are some large cages nearby -- she breeds dogs, I think.

'Go and speak with her... and remember, you're a brigand!''Go to Ellie Cutwood and try to pass yourself off as a brigand. If you succeed, she may betray the location of the Blackwolds' new leader.''Not another one! I'd thought I'd gotten all o' those letters back. You'd be better served just going home. You don't want to join up with the Blackwolds.

'I listened to Skunkwood, their leader, and helped them breed some wolves. I admit, I did it for the promise o' riches, but I regret it. Jagger Jack is their head wolf-master, and he had me breed a local wolf with one o' them Wargs. When they took me into their camp, deep within the Chetwood, I got afeared right quick. There's something not right there. I've done something terrible, ${PLAYER}, and I need help getting out.

'The den-mother I helped them breed is kept at Skunkwood's farm in the north Chetwood. She needs to be killed before her next litter is born, else her pups'll do worse damage to the Chetwood and the folk here.''Ellie wants out does she? We may be able to help her then. If she's willing to help us defeat the Blackwolds, then I see no reason not to help her.

'Just remember, ${PLAYER}, she once worked with the Blackwolds.''I've done a terrible thing and need to fix it before it goes further than it has. Follow the road east from Combe, up the hill, and then north into the Chetwood. Stay on the path to the east, and you'll reach Skunkwood's farm. Find the den-mother there and make sure she can't whelp no more o' them vile wolves.''Ellie wants out does she? We may be able to help her then. If she's willing to help us defeat the Blackwolds, then I see no reason not to help her.

'Just remember, ${PLAYER}, she once worked with the Blackwolds.''I'm glad that you were able to defeat the Den-mother before she bore any more of those half-Wargs.

'Now there's just Skunkwood to deal with. He spends most of his time in the Blackwold hideout these days. There are dark-skinned men who sometimes attend him, clearly not from these parts, and that Jagger Jack fellow.'According to Ellie, someone named Jagger Jack trains the wolves deep within the Blackwold Hideout. She met him when she was brought there and felt very ill at ease in the area.Leecher Cartwell's house overlooks Combe on the road south towards Bree.

Ellie Cutleaf has instructed you to acquire some poison from Cartwell, the local leech, to use against the Jagger Jack's wolves.There are beehives behind the abandoned house south of Combe. Red berries grow in patches in the valley behind the house. Blackwort root grows near a wolf-den north-east of the Combe lumber camp.

Leecher Cartwell has agreed to make the poison Ellie requested, but needs your assistance gathering the ingredients.Collect honeyCollect blackwort roots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect red berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cartwell's house is on a low cliff in the south-west corner of Combe.

Your search for Cartwell's herbs and honey took you into danger, but your efforts were fruitful. You should return at once to Cartwell with the ingredients.Ellie Cutleaf's home is in the north-west corner of Combe, on the banks of the pond.

After a short distilling process, Cartwell handed you a sweet-smelling phial. He assured you that the poison would kill the wolves threatening the Chetwood and the inhabitants of Combe, then sent you back to Ellie Cutleaf.'When Skunkwood took me to the Blackwold's encampment in the Chetwood, I met Jagger Jack. Jack is training the wolves for the Blackwolds. He keeps most o' them deep in the ruins in the north parts of the woods.

'If we're going to put a stop to the Blackwolds, then we may need to do a little mischief o' our own. I'm not wont to do this, mind you, but we need to stop them wolves before they're used against Combe.

'Leecher Cartwell can help us and will. Talk to him at his house, up on the cliff south of Combe centre. Tell him that I need a poison to kill the wolves.''Ellie got herself in trouble, did she? I've been near the wood of late to gather herbs and such. Something has the animals there stirred up, for certain.

'If this will help make things right between Ellie and the Combe-folk, I will help. I think I know just the thing. I'll need fresh honey, blackwort root, and several red berries.

'There are beehives behind the abandoned house, south of Combe. The berries grow in patches in a valley just over the hill behind the house. Blackwort root is found near the wolf-den in the north Chetwood.''She aims to kill the wolves with poison? It appears that Ellie truly wishes to atone for the harm she wrought. Something must have frightened her good at that camp.''Better we don't speak too often. If Ellie is found to be working with us, we may endanger her. I'd rather not see her harmed if she truly wishes to make amends.''Better we don't speak too often. If Ellie is found to be working with us, we may endanger her. I'd rather not see her harmed if she truly wishes to make amends.''Better we don't speak too often. If Ellie is found to be working with us, we may endanger her. I'd rather not see her harmed if she truly wishes to make amends.''I wish to make amends for my folly. First, you will need to consult with Leecher Cartwell. He will know how best to deal with this threat.''What are ye doing here, hanging about? Please hurry!''What are ye doing here, hanging about? Please hurry!''Fresh honey, blackwort root, and red berries. That is all I need to make the poison.''Take the poison to Ellie. Tell her that I truly hope she finds her way through this. She is a good woman, but sometimes easily misled.''Ah! There you are, it will be just a moment, and I'll have the poison for you....

'Be careful with this. It'll not hurt you or I, nor even the little folk -- except perhaps to make us mildly ill -- but the normal woodland creatures would suffer terribly if you don't use caution.

'You should return to Ellie and let her know that the poison is ready.''You have the poison from Cartwell?

'I trust Cartwell. Now that we have the poison, we may be ready to strike at the Blackwolds in their Chetwood home.'Since the Dourhands were driven out of Thorin's Halls, they have harried the hunters of the Blue Mountain Dwarves.The Dourhand brigands can be found to the north of Gondamon.

Orlygr has asked you to deal with the Dourhand brigands which have been harrying the hunters of Gondamon.Defeat Dourhand warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat sturdy Dourhands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Orlygr is at Gondamon to the south of the Dourhand-encampment.

You should return to Orlygr and report your success against the Dourhand brigands.Talk to Orlygr at Gondamon'The hunters who have been plying the forests north of Gondamon have come to me with stories of being threatened or even attacked by those backstabbing Dourhand brigands.

'If you're of a mind to lend us a hand, you could head out there and deal with the treacherous thin-beards! They need to learn not to meddle with the hunters of Gondamon!

'The Dourhands have built a small camp to the north of here, in the hills somewhere. You will find plenty of heads to break there, I'd warrant.''You should be able to find those brigands in a camp in the hills to the north. They mostly stay holed up in there like rats in their warren.''Ah good. That should teach the Dourhands a little lesson. You have done us a fair favour, ${PLAYER}, and helped ensure that Gondamon remains secure over the coming winter months. 

'Let me see if I can find some suitable reward for you.'Eldo Swatmidge is a successful farmer, but he is lonely. He has sought your help to woo his neighbour, the Widow Froghorn.There are bears south of the Widow Froghorn's farm.

Eldo wants to show Asphodel that he is willing to see to her protection. He has asked you to drive the bears away from her farm.Defeat bears near Widow Froghorn's farm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Asphodel Froghorn is at her farm.

