Asphodel Froghorn was pleased to learn that Eldo is both thoughtful and caring, but she still asked you to tell Eldo Swatmidge that her answer was still no.Talk to Eldo Swatmidge at his farm'Asphodel mentioned in her letter that there are bears wandering closer and closer to her farm. Maybe this is a clue that she needs some help with them.

'Would you make your way into the woods south of her farm and drive the bears away? This might show her that I am willing to see to her safety and show how caring I can be.

'When you're done, tell her!''You haven't gotten worn out already, have you?''Sent you again, did he? That Eldo Swatmidge is certainly persistent. I'll give him that, at least.

'He's honest, too? I'm glad you shared that information, ${PLAYER}, because it's certainly important. Or perhaps it isn't.

'Tell him that I appreciate the help around here, but my answer is still no.''Eldo is surely persistent, and he seems to have a very good heart.''Still no...? She is fickle, to be sure, but she's the finest lady in Staddle.

'Well, regardless, I think you made another fine impression. You're doing wonderfully, ${PLAYER}.'A sound defence is often more important than an explosive offence.Parry enemy attacksExplore the dark valley of Rath Teraig.NOT USEDThe Northern Barricade of Rath Teraig is held by stalwart dwarf-warriors posted out of Gondamon. Since the resurgence of the goblins in Ered Luin some years ago, the dwarves have fought to keep them bottled up in Rath Teraig to prevent them from spilling out into the vales and forests beyond.The Southern Barricade guards the way to the Grey Havens to the south-west. It was sealed off by the dwarves some years ago as the goblins swarmed out to overrun Rath Teraig and now lies abandoned and impassable, making the trek of the Elves travelling to the Havens a long and arduous journey as they must use passes far to the south.The goblins have fortified the canyon of Tum Agor, preparing for an assault against the barricades, trapping them within Rath Teraig.The goblins trapped within Rath Teraig have established a camp upon Amon Thanc, from where they can view the dwarf-barricades.The goblins of Rath Teraig have established their largest camp here in the Crookdell. This is where they plan their raids against the dwarf-barricades.A fierce bellow braces you for coming conflict and fills your heart with wrath.Loose Ferocious RoarPractice assuming an aggressive stance and learn how to make it stronger still.Use OverpowerStudy how encouraging words may sometimes yield very great changes in the hearts of your fellows.Use Words of Courage or Rallying CryNow that you have scouted the bridges of Glyn Helyg, work can be done to repair those that have suffered rot and weather-wear.Ponta Gochelgar has asked you to cut down trees from which to make planks to repair the bridges.

