Talk to Murig.'You must be the adventurer that Instructor Eluna told me about. Yes I know I was to report back already but I have yet to complete my work. My task is to find a reliable source of water for our scouting party. With such a great river near us, I thought this would be simple. The presence of Bloodhollow nearby complicates things. I’m concerned that its proximity may contaminate the water somehow. I'm working on a concoction that Deryn taught me to make. When added to water, it can help determine if it is safe to drink or not. Could you collect samples of water for me?'

'The first sample should be from the river-bank near Bloodhollow.
'The second sample should be from farther down river from Bloodhollow.
'The third sample should be from farther still down river from Bloodhollow. You get the idea.''What timing! I just finished making the concoction.'

Murig arranges the samples of water you collected into three separate basins of water. He then hands you three balls of a curious substance.

'Add one lump of the erm, paste, to each basin. Let us observe the results.''Clearly, the soil of Bloodhollow has some effect on the water. For now, I will be sure to collect water from further downriver to make sure it is fit for myself and my comrades. Perhaps when Marget's bloody work is complete, the waters around Bloodhollow will become more palatable.

'I will return to our encampment shortly! Thank you for your aid.'Since Lobelia Sackville-Baggins paid to acquire the ingredients for her fireworks, Hyacinth Took has recruited you to help her gather them.Cam Puddifoot is at his home in the middle of Budgeford.

The first ingredient Hyacinth Took has sent you after is saltpetre. She suggested you visit her friend Cam Puddifoot, a pig-farmer in Budgeford.'Well, if the old crow is willing to pay, then I suppose I'll have to oblige her.

'First, I'll send you out after saltpetre. My friend Cam Puddifoot, the pig-farmer in Budgeford, can usually supply some. He's got the biggest manure-pits in the whole Shire!

'Cam will let me know when he needs payment, so you'll not need to carry coin with you. He hardly has use for saltpetre.''Saltpetre? I got mounds of it. But I tell you what, I got other problems, too.

'Long as you're here, I'm going to ask you to take care of 'em for me before I send that saltpetre over to Hyacinth's place.''Please go to Budgeford and ask my friend Cam Puddifoot for the saltpetre I need.'Not every battle can be an amusing free-for-all.Use Get SeriousPresent your foe with your shield...to his face.Strike with Shield-bash, Behind the Shield, or Shield-blastPresent your foe with your shield...to his face.Strike with Shield-bash or Behind the ShieldWhen Orcs are raining arrows down upon you, you had best have a spring in your step.Evade enemy attacksWhen Orcs are raining arrows down upon you, you had best have a spring in your step.Evade enemy attacksBingo has decided that he needs to master one more skill before his journey begins. He must learn to swim.Bingo is in the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock. He is waiting for you to speak with him when you are ready to practice the art of swimming.Talk to Bingo in the Golden Perch Inn and travel with him to practice swimmingBingo is in the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock.Talk to Bingo Boffin inside the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock'I have knowledge, supplies, and strength, ${PLAYER}, and they will serve me well on my journey. But there is one more thing I must master before my adventure begins, and it is not something that comes naturally to hobbits. I must learn to swim!

'Have you seen the number of rivers on this map? Whoever drew this map must have been quite fond of the things, because there are squiggly lines and little ponds all over the place! There is nothing for it, ${PLAYER}. I must become a master of the waterways!

'Speak to me when you are ready, and we will go down to the Brandywine and practice!''All right, ${PLAYER}. I am as ready as I will ever be! Let us walk down to the Brandywine and practice being fish!''I think that went fairly well, ${PLAYER}. You might not have had a great look at it, but I'd say I mastered the art of swimming remarkably quickly.'

Bingo seems to be looking everywhere but at your face.

'Just for fun, though, I think I'll avoid rivers while on my journey. Dry land makes for a more interesting trip, I'd say, and it would be a shame to take the easy way and float across every river that squiggles its way across my path. You understand, I'm sure.'

