<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will need to train fishing in order to participate in this quest line. A Fishing Hobby Trainer stands in Bywater next to Neddie Grubb.</rgb>Above all, a Guardian must be where they are needed and quickly, for your companions are not so sturdy as you.Evade enemy attacksAbove all, a Guardian must be where they are needed and quickly, for your companions are not so sturdy as you.Evade enemy attacksSome consider Treats or Trickery an outing; some, a preoccupation; others, a way of life.Complete Treats or Trickery for the majority of the Harvest Festival.Complete Treats or Trickery many times (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have sampled wide and eaten deep of the Harvest Festival treats, but can you truly say you know each of them as well as the back of your own teeth?Complete Treats or Trickery: Second HelpingsComplete Treats or Trickery: Second HelpingsYou should consume a large number of every type of treat that can be gathered from Treats or Trickery doormats: apple goblins, honey-bears, liquorice twists, Midgewater marshmallows, jam tarts, mint turtles, mad Baggins' gold, and Ent-bark.Eat apple goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eat honey-bears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eat liquorice twists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eat Midgewater marshmallows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eat jam tarts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eat mint turtles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eat some mad Baggins' gold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eat some Ent-bark (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You promised Begonia Grubb you would put on a costume and join in Treats or Trickery. And so you have.Complete one excursion of Treats or Trickery.Complete Treats or TrickeryYou donned the costume and went from door to neighbourhood door. But have you tasted each kind of treat?You should try one of each type of treat that can be gathered from Treats or Trickery doormats: apple goblins, honey-bears, liquorice twists, Midgewater marshmallows, jam tarts, mint turtles, mad Baggins' gold, and Ent-bark.Try an apple goblinTry a honey-bearTry a liquorice twistTry a Midgewater marshmallowTry a jam tartTry a mint turtleTry some mad Baggins' goldTry some Ent-barkYou have tasted every type of treat that could be gathered from a doormat during Harvest Festival once, to be sure, but have you made yourself truly sick on them?Complete Treats or Trickery: Just a TasteComplete Treats or Trickery: Just a TasteYou should consume a large number of the Treats or Trickery treats, to say that you truly know them well.Consume many treats  (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You promised Begonia Grubb you would put on a costume and join in Treats or Trickery. But is once really enough?Complete a week's worth of Treats or Trickery.Complete a week's worth of Treats or Trickery (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})So what if it is an old trick? The old tricks are the best tricks.Use Dust in the EyesSo what if it is an old trick? The old tricks are the best tricks.Use TricksNo matter what tricks your opponent may deploy, fight on.Use Ignore PainIt is said that minstrels who can maintain the most difficult keys can cause disorienting pain to their foes.Land Critical hits with Piercing CryIt is said that minstrels who can maintain the most difficult keys can cause disorienting pain to their foes.Land Critical hits with Piercing CryThe spider nest you discovered is blocked from reach by a mass of monstrous webs, too strong to cut through.Gammer Boffin can be found at her home at the centre of Overhill.

Shirriff Smallburrow has sent you to Overhill to speak with Gammer Boffin, an old hobbit with a great knowledge of herb-lore. Robin believes she might know of something to help clear the spider-webs away.Slugs can be found in Rushock Bog, west of Overhill. Gammer Boffin is at her home in the middle of Overhill.

Robin Smallburrow was sure that Gammer Boffin would know of some mixture that might help remove the webs blocking the spider-nest in Bindbole Wood. You went to Overhill and spoke with Gammer, who sent you to collect six drams of slug-slime.'Now we have to find a way through the webs that are blocking the spider-nest you found. Those webs are too tough and sticky to cut through, and we can't burn them without setting the whole wood afire.

'Fortunately, I think I know who can help us. Gammer Boffin up in Overhill is a wise, old lady who knows all kinds of things about herbs and such. I think she'll be able to brew up something to help us deal with those webs. Her home is in the middle of Overhill.

'Perhaps with old Gammer's help, we'll be able to deal with the spider-nest in the woods.''Please speak with Gammer Boffin in Overhill about the spider-webs. I'm not sure who else to turn to.''Eh, what's that? Speak up, speak up! Oh... spider-webs, is it, my dear? Such a nuisance they are, sticking to everything you try to get rid of them with.

'But old Gammer has the answer, my dear! I'll need half a dozen drams of slug-slime first, though, and then I'll fix you right up, for sure! Eh? Slugs? Well, I'd look in the bog if I was you, dear. Rushock Bog, you know... it's to the west of Overhill. You can't miss it!

'When you have enough slime, bring it back to me, and old Gammer will take care of everything else.''Please do what the Gammer asks so we can deal with that spider-nest. Slugs in the Rushock Bog? Do whatever it takes!''Nasty stuff, isn't it? But that's what we'll use to get through those webs! It will take me but a moment to mix this up for you!'Sometimes courage and motivation just aren't enough, you need to dig deep for that little bit extra.Crit or Devastate with Words of Courage or Rallying CryYour enemies would be wise to not judge a book by its cover and to not underestimate a Rune-keeper.Use Mending Verse, Sustaining Bolt, or Smouldering WrathA small flowering plant found in Wadewater can make a quite delicious meal. If one can gather the rushes without falling astray of the ferocious turtles who call the area home.Lindeth has asked you to bring her back any flowering rushes that you might find in Wadewater.

Wadewater is in northern Swanfleet.Collect flowering rushes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the flowering rushes to Lindeth.

Lindeth is in Echad Terthas.Return to Lindeth'Well met! Are you heading west? If so, I have a boon to ask of you.

'Along the banks of the land masses in Wadewater grows a plant known to some as the flowering rush. The plant is edible, and I admit that my craving for it has brought me all this way!

'I was sent back here with my tail between my legs, however. The dread-turtles are too fierce and have a taste for the rushes as well! Please, if you are in that area, would you bring me back any of the rushes that you might find?''Ah, you are most welcome back! I see the turtles were not too much for you to handle. I am looking forward to cooking these rushes up right away. You have my thanks.'Eldo Swatmidge is a successful farmer, but he is lonely. He has sought your help to woo his neighbour, the Widow Froghorn.Eldo Swatmidge's farm is up the road to the north and east of the Widow Froghorn's farm.

Asphodel Froghorn stated she would allow Eldo to court her, if he was willing to sell his dog. You should return to Eldo Swatmidge with the widow's terms.Talk to Eldo Swatmidge at his farmThe Widow Froghorn's farm is on the road west and south of Eldo Swatmidge's farm.

Eldo Swatmidge cannot sell Wanetta even though he cares so much for Asphodel Froghorn. He has asked you to deliver his message to the Widow.Talk to Asphodel Froghorn at her farmEldo Swatmidge's farm is up the road north and east of the Widow Froghorn's farm.

Asphodel Froghorn found Eldo's loyalty so endearing that she is willing to put up with sniffles and sneezing. You should return to Eldo Swatmidge with the good news.Talk to Eldo Swatmidge at his farm'I am surprised at how earnest Eldo seems to be! Perhaps I shall give him a chance. A courtship could be just the thing to brighten my days.

'Tell him that I'll consider his courting me, but he'll need to sell his dog, Wanetta. I always come down with the sneezes whenever I am around dogs of her breed, and it is really unbearable.

'Hurry back with his answer! Oh, I'm all a-flutter like a little hobbit-girl!''Oh, I'm so excited! Please hurry and tell Mr. Swatmidge so he can make arrangements to sell that dog of his. I can't wait!''Sell Wanetta? I... I can't. I've had Wanetta here since she was a pup. She's given me litter after litter of good, strong pups. She's my prized dog! I can't sell her! If she was a hobbit and I was a dog, she wouldn't sell me, I know it!

'If that is what Asphodel wants... tell her I can't. I can't do it. Looks like I won't ever be courting the Widow Froghorn. Please don't think me ungrateful for what you've done, but I just can't lose my Wanetta.''I hope she understands, but I just can't sell my Wanetta. I just can't!''What? He won't sell that dog? Now... now I want him courting me even more! What loyalty, and not even to a person!

'You were right all along, ${PLAYER}. Eldo Swatmidge might not be the most well-dressed hobbit in Staddle, or even the most well-spoken, but he's a good, hard-working, loyal fellow.

'Maybe someday there will be a cure for the sneezes I get around that breed of dog, and then not even Wanetta will keep me from my Eldo! Please go tell him at once, ${PLAYER}.''Eldo's loyalty, generosity, kindness, and caring make him a fine suitor, I think!''Really!'

Eldo looks to Wanetta, 'Did you hear that Wanetta? Asphodel said yes!'

'${PLAYER}, I don't know if this is thanks enough for what you've done for me! Take this and know that I'll be everything I promised Asphodel and more!'Dorri has asked for your help building their winter stores.Wolves can be found in the wilds around Gondamon, especially to the west.

Dorri has asked you to hunt the wolves that menace the wilds around Gondamon and obtain pelts he can use to make blankets and winter clothing.'The wind coming down from the mountains makes my bones ache year-round, but even the younger sentries feel the chill when the days grow short. 

'We could use more pelts to make blankets and clothing in preparation for the coming winter. There is no shortage of wolves prowling in the wilds, especially to the west. I expect you will have no difficulty obtaining some furs for me.

'Wolves are vile creatures, but at least their fur is warm.''The Dwarves of Gondamon will be grateful for these pelts when winter arrives, ${PLAYER}. Thank you.'Gammer Boffin has prepared an unpleasant draught from slug-slime that should allow you to pass through the webs protecting the spider-lair in Bindbole Woods.The spider-nest is to the north-west of Overhill town centre, past the wall and the lumber-yard.

Shirriff Smallburrow sent you to Gammer Boffin in Overhill to obtain something to dissolve the spider-webs blocking the way to the nest. Gammer warned you that the mixture dries quickly, so you must hurry. She also mentioned a nursery story about a walking tree in Bindbole Wood that might serve as an ally... if it even exists.Get past the webs in Lob's GroveThe walking tree, if it exists, probably can be found somewhere in the spider nest.

You were able to clear the way to the nest using Gammer Boffin's draught. She also mentioned a nursery story about a walking tree in the wood that might help to deal with the spiders, though she warned it might be dangerous to you as well.Find the walking tree'There we go, my dear. This draught should get you through those spider-webs! But you must hurry! It dries out quickly.

'Oh, there's one more thing. I've heard nursery stories about a walking tree in Bindbole Wood, like them in the Old Forest. It might be asleep, if it is even there at all, and it might be dangerous to things on two-legs, like they say the Old Forest is, but I doubt it will take kindly to all those nasty spiders either.

'Now off with you before that draught dries, or you'll never get through the webs!''You must hurry if you want to clear those webs, or the draught will dry out! Head north through Bindbole Wood until you find the spider-nest. If your way is blocked by thick webs, you should be able make it through now!''That draught worked, didn't it, dear? Did you find that old walking-tree? Sometimes those old nursery stories have some truth to them.'The walking tree shudders when you touch it. Tiny spiders are crawling all over it, their webs veiling its bark. It looks like the walking tree is in some distress.Culhuc would like you to forage where the avanc nest in the Wadewater.Avanc eggs can be found in the Wadewater.

Collect avanc eggs.Collect avanc eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Culhuc is tending the community oven in Lhan Garan.

Talk to Culhuc.'I'd love to get my hands on some avanc eggs, but I'm better at fighting people than I am beasts. It's a hip thing, bending is hard on me. There's a big population of avanc out in the Wadewater.

'Hmm? How many? Well they are big eggs, so six.''Head west into the Wadewater to find the avanc and their nests.''Ah, the eggs I asked for. You did wash them in the water before bringing them here, right?'

Before you can answer, he takes hold of one of the eggs and you watch his smile morph into a deep frown.

'No bother. I'll just... wash this egg, and my hands, and just please set them down on the ground and give me a moment.

'Thank you, I suppose.'The safety of the small village of Lintrev is dependent upon its residents leaving no trace of their whereabouts for their unsavoury neighbours to find.Heleth Bach has asked you to smooth over and hide any tracks that she may have left behind down by the river.

The river is north-west of Lintrev, in southern Swanfleet.Hide hobbit prints (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Heleth know that you have hidden her tracks.

Heleth Bach is in Lintrev.Return to Heleth'Oh, hullo there. I am Heleth. Have you been down to the river? I was there earlier today, but the scariest big folk I have ever seen came thundering down the road! I dove for the bushes then rushed back here as quickly as I could.

'Alas, I forgot to hide my tracks! If you go down to the river, will you scuff over my footprints if you see them? Mayor Dringarth insists that we leave no trace of ourselves where the scary big folk can see them, but I am too afrighted to go back down myself.''Hullo, hullo! Have you done it? Oh, marvellous! I would not have slept a wink had I thought those nasty big folk from up the road would have found us. Why, I have had such an upset tummy that I have not eaten in at least an hour!'Eldo Swatmidge is a successful farmer, but he is lonely. He has sought your help to woo his neighbour, the Widow Froghorn.Asphodel's pipe-weed field is located by her home, directly to the west of her wheat-field.

The Widow Froghorn has asked you to harvest some of the ripe pipe-weed from her field.Eldo Swatmidge's farm is up the road to the north and east of the Widow Froghorn's farm.

After collecting pipeweed for Asphodel, she handed you a note and told you to deliver it to Eldo without reading the contents.'I must beg your pardon, but it's been a bit of a trial since I lost my Bodo. If you're here to lend a hand, I won't stop you.

'The pipe-weed is ready for harvest, so if you're still intent on helping out, you can bring it in. It's right there, on the other side of my wheat-field.

'But you should know that I'll not change my mind about old Eldo Swatmidge.''Any good news, friend? Will the widow let me court her?''I see you've harvested quite a bundle of pipe-weed. You have my thanks -- a helping hand is appreciated, no matter where it comes from.

'You say Eldo is a good, solid hobbit? You would say that, I suppose, being in his employ.'

Asphodel takes the pipe-weed and hands you a folded, sealed note. 'Take this back to your good, solid friend. And don't read it!''Now, mind you, my mind has not been changed about old Eldo... and you can let him know that!''You're back! How did it go?

'What's this? Refused again! Well... I'm not going to give up! If you go back and tell her some more of my good qualities, I'm sure she'll reconsider. I'm sure of it!

'Did you mention how hard-working I am? I'm an honest fellow, and good to my dogs. They say you can judge the worth of a hobbit by how he treats his dogs, and I treat mine like royalty! You go help her out around the farm some more, and be sure to mention that. Like royalty!'Eldo Swatmidge is a successful farmer, but he is lonely. He has sought your help to woo his neighbour, the Widow Froghorn.The Widow Froghorn's farm is west and south of Eldo Swatmidge's farm.

Eldo has asked you to help out around Asphodel Froghorn's farm, taking the opportunity to put in a few good words for him.Talk to Asphodel Froghorn at her farm'This is a fine farm, wouldn't you say? Yes, life has been kind to me. My only regret is that I haven't anyone to share it with!

'I think you might be able to help me, if you're of a mind. The Widow Froghorn lives up the hill to the west, and she's a fine lady, but she won't hear of me courting her. I've been sending letters to her for a while now, asking her to tea, to the dance, to watch o'er my dog... but she refuses every time!

'Now, Widow Froghorn -- Asphodel is her right name -- is always needing help around her farm. Maybe if you lend her a hand, saying a kind word about me now and then, she'll change her mind! Go west up the hill, then turn south by the fence at the top. Her farm is at the cross-roads.''Asphodel's farm is west of here, closer to Staddle. Go up the hill to the west and turn south at the fence on the top. Don't forget to put in a good word for me every chance you get!''Who might you be? Another farmhand Eldo sent to help me? I don't need his help, thank you very much and good day to you!

'No matter how many times I tell him "no," he just won't give up. I swear, there's only one thing he loves, and it's those dogs he raises! If it doesn't bark or have a tail to wag, he doesn't know the first thing about it!'Food, drink, companionship -- for the Champion, all of these are second to the joys of battle...drink is a very close second though.Land Critical Hits using Wild AttackBlade-storm is one of the Champion's most impressive attacks, causing considerable havoc upon the field of battle.Strike enemies with Blade-stormBlade-storm is one of the Champion's most impressive attacks, causing considerable havoc upon the field of battle.Use Blade-Storm, Remorseless Strike or Sudden DefenceWinter Seasonal Instances have arrived! Play Winter Seasonal Instances during the Yule Festival.Winter Seasonal Instances have arrived! Play Winter Seasonal Instances during the Yule Festival.

