'Oswin Leek is a renowned guardian in Bree-land, and he may be able to guide your further training. Look for him at the North-gate of the town of Bree, east of the Shire.''We share a bond, ${PLAYER}, that few others can know. Wherever there is battle, you will find us there. Wherever there is hardship, we will stand against it. Wherever good people are threatened, we stand before them with shield in hand or blade at the ready, and do not stand down until it is safe once more.

'We are guardians of the people, Elf, Man, hobbit, and dwarf, and we must be strong in their defence.

'Oswin Leek is a renowned guardian in Bree-land, and he may be able to guide your further training. Look for him at the North-gate of the town of Bree, far to the west along the Road, and pay heed to his words.''I welcome you to Bree, Guardian ${PLAYER}, but I confess I do not have the time to spare in idle conversation -- there are brigands about, and though they have suffered some measure of defeat of late, they are still on the Bree-fields and within the Andrath, and their recent losses only stir them to boldness.

'Unless I am very much mistaken, you surely seek every opportunity to strengthen yourself. Well, I have many such opportunities available! Indeed, the brigands seem eager to present them to us! The worthy farmers of Bree-land are hard put to it, though, and we must protect their lands and their lives whenever either are threatened.

'I will set out to deal with brigand attacks to the north, but I need you elsewhere. Burle Pierson lives on a farm to the south of Bree-town, and he has reported several raids on his land. Each time he has fought them off, but he says they always return with more men, and soon he will be unable to resist them. Help him defend his farm, ${PLAYER}, and the training will surely be of use to you.''The light in your eye tells me that you have aided Burle Pierson with the defence of his farm, ${PLAYER}, and I am glad to hear it! It is a guardian's lot to put himself between danger and those who need protecting.

'Always remember that every battle makes you tougher, ${PLAYER}. Even now, your arm is stronger and your senses keener than when last I saw you. Train often, and you will find your ability to fend off attacks increasing. Indeed, that is already the case!

'Go forth, Guardian ${PLAYER}, and protect the good peoples of Middle-earth from the dangers they face. It is your lot to do so.''You'll find Burle Pierson's farm to the south of the town of Bree, rather near to the Andrath. Speak to him and help him fight off the brigands that often raid his land.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''Look for Oswin Leek at the North-gate of the town of Bree. He is a mighty guardian and may be able to help you hone your skills.''You go tell Oswin Leek what a help you were to me. He's usually at the North-gate of Bree.''You are a guardian, ${PLAYER}? I am glad to hear it, for the brigands have been a constant threat to me and mine, and I don't know how much longer I can fight them off!

'Let us walk about my property and keep watch for any of the brigands that might have designs on my land. They said they would be back with great numbers, and I fear they will keep their oath!'Dangerous lands and terrible monsters make for grand tales, but an experienced minstrel knows that a room full of skeptical listeners can be the most frightening chamber of all.Piper Prescott, a renowned minstrel, is often within the common room of The Prancing Pony, in the town of Bree.

