Lethi is pressing on to the gates of Barad-dûr. You should follow him.Follow LethiThe pale creature can be found in Barad-dûr.

Despite appearing to be dead, the pale creature has scrambled to its feet and attacked Lethi. You should defend him and drive off the creature.Lethi can be found in Barad-dûr.

After repelling the pale creature that attacked him, Lethi is shaken. You should talk to Lethi before pressing on to the gates of Barad-dûr.Talk to LethiLethi has travelled into the shadowed halls of Barad-dûr.

You should follow Lethi and press on to the gates of Barad-dûr.Follow LethiLethi can be found Barad-dûr.

Lethi is standing next to a brazier in Barad-dûr. You should talk to Lethi.Talk to LethiLethi can be found in Barad-dûr.

Lethi is pressing on toward the gates of Barad-dûr. You should follow him.Follow LethiThe slain Orc-captain can be found just ahead of Lethi in Barad-dûr.

After spying a slain Orc-captain, Lethi has urged you to disguise yourself in its armour so that you might fool the inhabitants of Mordor. You should disguise yourself.Disguise yourself as an Orc-captainLethi can be found in Barad-dûr.

You have disguised yourself as an Orc-captain, which may be of help in escaping the Land of Mordor. You should talk to Lethi.Talk to LethiThe path to the gates of Barad-dûr is just ahead of you.

Lethi has asked you to peer around the corner and see if the path out of Barad-dûr is clear.Lethi can be found in Barad-dûr.

You discovered the uruk, Ushgrat, guarding the gates of Barad-dûr. Worse still, he appears to have subdued Vaski. You should talk to Lethi.Talk to LethiAfter foiling Vaski's escape, Ushgrat is keeping watch before the gates of Barad-dûr.

