Are you sure you want to continue?There are many villainous monsters roaming the Lone-lands, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many bog-lurkers in the Lone-landsSlay many crebain in the Lone-landsSlay many gaunt-men in the Lone-landsSlay many goblins in the Lone-landsSlay many Orcs in the Lone-landsSlay many spiders in the Lone-landsSlay many trolls in the Lone-landsSlay many Wargs in the Lone-landsYou rescued Robb Thornley from the Orcs, battered and beaten, but he is not satisfied with rescue. He wants retribution.The Red Reaver is in the Orc-stockade on the western side of the Greenway, north of Thornley's farm.

On behalf of her husband, Rose Thornley has offered you a reward if you would go to the stockade and slay the Red Reaver.Defeat the Red ReaverThornley's farm is south along the Greenway from the Orc-stockade.

You should return to Thornley's farm at once to tell Rose of your victory and claim your reward.Talk to Rose Thornley at Thornley's Farm'Robb is resting now and recovering nicely, thanks to you, but he asks another favour of you.

'He said he can't sleep, thinking about those accursed Orcs what ambushed him up the Greenway. When he was captured, he said a large Orc came over to torment him from a camp to the west from where he was being held, the one behind a wooden stockade. He says the other Orcs called this monster the Red Reaver. Robb says he must have his revenge on the Red Reaver and will be glad to give you what coins he can spare if you can put him to heel.

'Now, I can't say as I like all this bloodshed, and it sounds right dangerous to me, but if you'll show that horrible monster who tortured Robb a thing or two, I guess you surely do deserve a reward.''Robb will be so happy to hear you've done away with that beast of an Orc! And I'll thank you too for making the Greenway a safer place. Please accept this reward from both of us.''Have you done away with the Red Reaver yet?'Strewn throughout the lore you discovered in previous efforts for Tobold Leafcutter were stories of a great Cardolan treasure. He believes that two brothers, warriors of Arnor, fought and recovered the treasure and brought it to the Northern Barrow.You may find a chest resting at the Northern Barrow, the northernmost barrow of the Barrow-downs. Tobold Leafcutter waits for you between the Old Forest and Barrow-downs.

Tobold Leafcutter has asked you to search the Northern Barrow for more lore. He hopes that lore from the Men of Cardolan may have survived the long years since the Great Plague in a chest. If you find such lore, you should bring it to Tobold.'It seems that this may not be the first time that such terror has plagued these lands. The bits of parchment you recovered lead me to believe that two brothers fought to recover a great treasure of Cardolan and brought it here to the northern Barrow-downs.

'The lore-fragments you brought me mention a fortress named Ost Gorthad. The Men of Cardolan took many of those who fell sick to the Plague there. The ruins of that fortress still stand today in the south! It is from here that a terror rose and cursed the brothers for their theft.

'If you are willing, you may seek the treasure or the history of that treasure at the Northern Barrow, not far from here to the east. Perhaps we can learn more about these Men and how to stave this evil from spreading beyond the bounds of the Barrow-downs.''Ah, you found something! Many of the pages are missing, but perhaps I can glean something from those which remain.

'Ah! This is almost too terrible to read. The author, a Man of Cardolan, tells how those few of Cardolan who remained died in a Great Plague, borne along by dark clouds from the East. Soon after, fell spirits swept down from the North. The man writes of tormenting dreams that followed, dreams of a place called Angmar. Soon after, the Dead walked the land once more. In the last entry, the man writes that he fears that he too will succumb to the Plague, but that his body will never know rest.

'How I wish I had remained ignorant of those cursed lands, yet now I find I must know more. If you ever find more pages of this journal, bring them to me. Perhaps in this knowledge, a defence against these fell spirits can be learned.'After encountering the elusive huorn, Drindolf, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Stoors of Swanfleet.Addo Benchuth can be found at Glyn Helyg in Swanfleet.

You have acquired a trophy from an elusive foe in Swanfleet. You should deliver it to Addo Benchuth, a trophy-hunter and purveyor of odd things in Swanfleet.Deliver Drindolf's heartwood to Addo Benchuth in SwanfleetAfter encountering and defeating the elusive huorn, Drindolf, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Stoors of Swanfleet.

As you inspect Drindolf's heartwood, you take note of the many rings within it. It is marked in a few spots with a strange blight, which appear to have begun to devour Drindolf from within. Perhaps this was the cause of the huorn's unusual hostility, but it is likely you will never know for certain.

You should bring this trophy to Addo Benchuth, a trophy-hunter and purveyor of odd things in Swanfleet.'Oh, hullo! What's that there? May I see it?'

As Addo Benchuth inspects Drindolf's heartwood, he makes a note of the blight you noticed within its rings.

'It's unfortunate that one of those ancient creatures should take ill. For my part, I can do my best to honour its memory by preserving its heartwood. It'll take some time, but I'll remove the blight and reshape the heartwood. What it will become I cannot say for certain, but it will be something I cherish for each day of my life—and that is a promise!

'If you find anything else of this sort, please bring it here and I'll see that you're compensated for your efforts. Thank you, friend!'Defeat wights in the Lone-lands.Defeat wights in the Lone-landsDefeat many wights in the Lone-lands.Defeat wights in the Lone-landsRangers, watching movements of enemies from the north and south, are concerned over the appearance of a foe they have long fought in the north.Saeradan is at his cabin, south of the Old Greenway Fort.

Andreg instructed you to return to Saeradan with news of your success.Talk to Saeradan at his cabin'While we did not capture Ferny, we did stop the threat for the moment. This will please Saeradan, and we should make haste to inform him of this success.

'Return to his cottage, south along the Greenway on the east side of the road, and tell him what you have accomplished.''While catching the coward, Ferny, and presenting him to Grimbriar would have established greater acceptance between us, I am pleased to know that the Orcs have been stifled for the moment.

'Still, we cannot be certain that we have stopped their efforts altogether, and I must ask you to continue your efforts for the moment.''Return to Saeradan's cabin, south along the Greenway on the east side of the road, and tell him what you have accomplished.'Bingo has agreed to carry the gift for Angelica so the rest of you can meet up outside her new home.Dinodas and the other Boffins agreed to meet you outside Angelica's new home in Nobottle, on Honeymead Lane.Meet up with the Boffins outside Angelica's new home on Honeymead LaneDinodas stands outside Angelica's new home on Honeymead Lane, very pleased with himself.Talk to Dinodas Boffin on Honeymead LanePrisca Boffin and many of her children gather on Honeymead Lane to welcome Angelica to her new home.Talk to Prisca Boffin on Honeymead LaneBingo Boffin stands on Honeymead Lane with his cousin Prisca and some of her children.Talk to Bingo Boffin on Honeymead LaneAngelica Boffin is delighted to see that you and so much of her family has come to Nobottle to welcome her to her new home.Talk to Angelica Boffin outside her new homeDinodas stands alone outside 9 Honeymead Lane.Talk to Dinodas outside 9 Honeymead Lane'All right, ${PLAYER}, you go ahead with Dino to Nobottle while I find something I can use to wrap this present. I'll bring it along shortly, but we shouldn't keep Angelica waiting.''You go ahead with Dino to Nobottle while I find something I can use to wrap this present. I'll bring it along shortly, but we shouldn't keep Angelica waiting.''Onward, ${PLAYER}, to 9 Honeymead Lane. My sister Angelica will be so pleased!''Here we are, ${PLAYER}. Angelica has done quite well for herself, hasn't she?

'When it comes time for me to find a place of my own, I think I will look for something a little smaller. It seems to me that having so many rooms might invite, well, ghosts! Who needs all those empty rooms, just ripe for haunting? I tell you I do not, but perhaps Angelica isn't worried about that sort of thing. Let's hope she doesn't regret it!

'It is a nice hobbit-burrow, though, I'll say that for her. She knows how to pick them!''There's my mother, and Griffo and Esmeralda too.''${PLAYER}! This is a pleasant surprise! Are you here for my daughter Angelica's house-warming party? You must be, surely!

'I see that some of my children have already arrived. I hope the rest are on their way... sometimes it is hard to keep them on a schedule, the dear ones.

'But this is Angelica's day and I want nothing to spoil it for her!''Welcome, Bingo, welcome. We shall be quite a merry gathering! I hope there is room enough for all of us inside!''Found the place with no trouble, I see, very good.

'And here is the gift for Angelica, perfectly-wrapped, from all her Boffin relatives and from ${PLAYER} too!''There she is!''Oh, hooray, ${PLAYER}! I didn't know you were going to come to my party! I know it's just a small hobbit-burrow, but it's all mine. I think it is quite cozy!

'Come inside, everyone! I hope there will be room!''Uh... ${PLAYER}?

'I think I... might have made a mistake.'Dinodas has come up with a plan to fix his mistake.Dinodas has his eye set on a side window through which you might be able to secretly gain access to 8 Honeymead Lane in order to steal back the gift.Scout a side window to 8 Honeymead LaneThere are so many nosey hobbits around that you will need to stack crates outside the side entrance if you are to hide your caper from their view.Take a crate from the stack outside the Fox and Fiddle, in NobottleThere are so many nosey hobbits around that you will need to stack crates outside the side entrance if you are to hide your caper from their view.Take a crate from the stack outside the Fox and Fiddle, in NobottleThere are so many nosey hobbits around that you will need to stack crates outside the side entrance if you are to hide your caper from their view.Take a crate from the stack outside the Fox and Fiddle, in NobottleDinodas Boffin is ready to begin the risky caper.Talk to Dinodas Boffin on Honeymead Lane and conduct his risky caperDinodas is beaming with pride and relief after the successful execution of the caper.Celebrate your successful caper?Camellia Boffin has discovered you! How much does she know about the recently-concluded caper?Talk to Camellia Boffin beside 8 Honeymead Lane'We'll need to sneak inside and steal back the gift before Angelica is able to open it. It's not "stealing," ${PLAYER}, not exactly! It isn't really her property until she opens it, is it? No, of course not. Anyone would say so! And it's only barely burglary. It's for the best, trust me!

'Now go see if there's a window we might use to get inside without being seen.''Go see if there's a window we might use to get inside without being seen.''That entrance will work, but we'll need a stack of crates to block the view of it from all the nosey hobbits hereabout. I saw a stack of crates outside the Fox and Fiddle tavern, here in Nobottle. That should work!''That entrance will work, but we'll need a stack of crates to block the view of it from all the nosey hobbits hereabout. I saw a stack of crates outside the Fox and Fiddle tavern, here in Nobottle. That should work!''That entrance will work, but we'll need a stack of crates to block the view of it from all the nosey hobbits hereabout. I saw a stack of crates outside the Fox and Fiddle tavern, here in Nobottle. That should work!''No time to waste, ${PLAYER}! Let's get that present back!''Perfect, ${PLAYER}, well-done! That could not have gone more smoothly! Now Angelica need never discover the tiny mistake I made concerning her house-warming present. Never has there been a more finely-executed caper!''Oh no!''Dinodas! What are you whispering about? Why have you stolen back our house-warming present for Angelica? You were so proud of that painting of her new home!'

Camellia gasps, and her expression turns scandalous.

'You had that Elf paint the wrong house! And now you've embroiled me in your silly conspiracy too! Dinodas! How could you?'Writs are always effective, sometimes more than others.Critically hit with any WritAfter trying to escape the wicked designs of Skorgrím Dourhand by fleeing Ered Luin, Erfith and his kin were ensnared by the goblins at Lhúngobel.Lhúngobel can be found along the River Lune in the north-western reaches of Yondershire.

Erfith has asked you to free his companions that were captured by the goblins at Lhúngobel. Dourhands can be found in the ruins of Lhúngobel.Erfith can be found on a hill just off the road near the border of Ered Luin in Yondershire.

You have successfully freed several of Erfith's kin from the goblins at Lhúngobel. You should talk to Erfith.Talk to Erfith'Something horrid has taken hold of my kinsfolk. I do not even recognize them anymore!

'A few of my companions and I resolved to strike out on our own after Skorgrím departed Ered Luin, but it wasn't long before our kinsfolk sent the goblins after us! It was Glúmir, a wicked champion of my people, who issued that order, but it matters not. The goblins pursued us across the Lune to Lhúngobel and I only narrowly escaped.

'The goblins have my companions. It won't be long before they drag them back to Glúmir and the others still loyal to Skorgrím!

'Won't you help me?''I hardly know what to say...

'After all we have done, you owe us nothing and yet you have lent us your aid. You have my truest thanks, ${PLAYER}.

'My companions and I will not trouble the folk of Ered Luin ever again. I promise it!'After dealing with both the Chief and Sharkey, Mal Ragwood finds himself caught between two different leaders—and he likes neither of them.A captured Bounder can be found somewhere in Taerhad.

In the hopes that it will draw out Sharkey's lieutenant, Mal Ragwood has asked you to free a captured Bounder from the half-orcs at Taerhad.Find the captured Bounder in TaerhadThe captured Bounder can be found atop Taerhad in Yondershire.

You have found the captured Bounder at Taerhad. You should attempt to free him and also keep watch for any sign of Sharkey's lieutenant.Free the captured Bounder at Taerhad
Defeat Sharkey's LieutenantBounder Hawkwort can be found at Taerhad in Yondershire.

You have defeated Sharkey's lieutenant. You should talk to Bounder Hawkwort and aid in freeing him from the half-orcs at Taerhad.Talk to Bounder Hawkwort at TaerhadBounder Hawkwort can be found inside the Roaring Bull in Long Cleeve in Yondershire.

After freeing Bounder Hawkwort from the half-orcs at Taerhad, he has asked you to meet him at the Roaring Bull. You should talk to Bounder Hawkwort.Talk to Bounder Hawkwort in the Roaring Bull'What's your business with me? Make it quick or be on your way!'

You introduce yourself and ask why he's not with the other ruffians in Yondershire.

'Bah! I've no quarrel with you. Not yet, anyway. The name's Mal Ragwood, and it used to mean something around here! Not after the little Chief and Sharkey started meddling in things, though....'

Mal Ragwood spits on the ground.

'Some of my boys say they've even seen one of Sharkey's men giving out medallions to folks who fall in line. If that's all it takes to win their loyalty, good riddance!

'Anyway, Sharkey's got a lieutenant up in Taerhad, and I hear he's caught himself one of those feather-capped halflings. Rumour has it he even has a taste for them. I wouldn't put it past those half-orcs—a nasty lot they are! Now, I don't particularly care what happens to that one, but if someone were to drive Sharkey's lieutenant off... well, that would be a different story, wouldn't it?

'If you're wanting to help the halfling anyway, why not do me a favour?''Oh, erm, thank you! I was just planning to wait for nightfall, but I s'pose that works, too.'

Bounder Hawkwort notices a look of confusion on your face.

'What do I mean? Oh, I just don't think those half-orcs gave much thought to the size of this cage is all. Why, I can fit right through the bars! See?'

Bounder Hawkwort swiftly squeezes himself between two bars of the cage and is free of his imprisonment.

'You've done a fine job driving that fellow off, though. As for me, I'm done with my watch, so it's back to Long Cleeve. And I'll be needing a new hat, it seems. All in a day's work!

'What say you meet me in the Roaring Bull?''Ah, ${PLAYER}. It is good to see you!

'I must thank you again for dispatching that cruel half-orc, friend. I've heard quite enough talk about this Sharkey fellow to know that anyone who's caught up with him is bad news! Between that and all this business about that meddling Lotho and some fellow called the "Chief", I've a feeling I'll need to keep a close watch on things this year.'

Bounder Hawkwort looks around the bustling tavern and begins to smile.

'But those are problems for tomorrow, I think. Tonight, I'll enjoy some of Bullroarer's Best—and you should, too!'Postman Grubb of Nobottle has begun to suspect that someone is interfering with the Quick Post—tampering with the mail and hindering its delivery to the inhabitants of Yondershire.The Quick Post can be found in Nobottle.

After becoming suspicious that someone is tampering with the mail coming into Yondershire, Postman Grubb has asked you to meet him inside the Quick Post of Nobottle. You should meet Postman Grubb inside the Quick Post.Meet Postman Grubb inside the Quick Post in NobottlePostman Grubb can be found inside the Quick Post in Nobottle.

After becoming suspicious that someone is tampering with the mail coming into Yondershire, Postman Grubb has asked you to meet him inside the Quick Post in Nobottle. You should talk to Postman Grubb inside the Quick Post.Talk to Postman Grubb in the Quick Post in NobottleLetters and parcels can be found throughout the Quick Post in Nobottle.

Postman Grubb has asked you to examine letters and parcels delivered from the Shire.Postman Grubb can be found inside the Quick Post in Nobottle.

After examining letters and parcels delivered from the Shire, you have found evidence of tampering and a curious sort of signature. You should report to Postman Grubb inside the Quick Post in Nobottle.Talk to Postman Grubb in the Quick Post in Nobottle'Oh, hullo!

'If you have a complaint to file against the Quick Post, I do ask that you submit it in writing and deliver it to my assistant, Ebbo. We are aware of a number of issues involving delayed or lost mail that some hobbits have reported over the past few weeks. Rest assured, the Quick Post will get to the bottom of it!

'With that out of the way, who are you? How can I help you today?'

You introduce yourself to Postman Grubb and ask what's happening at the Quick Post.

'Pleased to meet you, ${PLAYER}. I'm Walto Grubb, and I've been a postman going on twelve years. I'd say it's my calling, if you believe in such things! As for what's going on with the Quick Post, I wish I could tell you. Like I said, the mail's been turning up late or not at all, and the folk in Yondershire aren't too happy about it. I don't know if the Postmaster's been trying something new or altering routes, but I don't think that's it.'

Postman Grubb looks around and lowers his voice.

'Between you and me, I think someone's been tampering with the mail. If you're of a mind to help me sort this out, meet me inside the Quick Post.''I must apologize for the mess, ${PLAYER}.

'You see, we're a bit backed up here in Nobottle with letters and parcels due to be delivered to the Hithershire. Most folks down in Michel Delving, Hobbiton, and the like just call it the Shire, but it seems a bit odd to me, but I digress. We've had a few postmen come up from the Hithershire with small deliveries, but none of them are taking as much as they ought to to deliver back to the rest of the Shire. It's almost like they're trying to slow the whole thing down. For goodness' sake, we've had a parcel due for Stock sitting here for over a month!

'Ebbo received a delivery from the Quick Post of Waymeet this morning, and as usual, it was very light. Unfortunately, after I inspected the letters and parcels, I only became more suspicious that someone's been deliberately tampering with the mail.

'Why don't you head up front and take a look at them, ${PLAYER}? I am curious to know what you make of their condition!''What do you think, ${PLAYER}? What did you make of those letters and parcels? Are my concerns ill-founded?'

You tell Postman Grubb that unless many, many hobbits have coincidentally forgotten to add postscripts until after sealing their letters, you must conclude that there are obvious signs of tampering on all of the recent deliveries at the Quick Post in Nobottle.

'I knew it!'A fast and simple attack may allow your efforts to be spent elsewhere.Strike with Precise BlowA fast and simple attack may allow your efforts to be spent elsewhere.Strike with Precise BlowThe Elf, Avorthal, and the dwarf, Athal, keep a close watch on Ered Luin and the surrounding lands.Athal and Erfith can be found on a hill just off the road near the border of Ered Luin in Yondershire.

Avorthal has asked you to aid Athal and the Dourhand, Erfith, in routing the goblins that have crossed into the Yondershire.Help Athal with 'The Bounty-hunter of Lhúngobel'Help Erfith with 'A Deal Gone Wrong'Avorthal can be found on a hill just off the road near the border of Ered Luin in Yondershire.

You have aided Avorthal and Athal in routing the goblins that crossed the River Lune, freed Erfith's peace-seeking companions, and learned of the Dourhands' plot to rally their wicked allies to the ancient keep of Sarnúr. You should talk to Avorthal.Talk to Avorthal'Hail! Have you been sent by the Bounders of this land?

'I am Avorthal, and my companion over there with the axe is Athal. We do not often travel beyond the lands of Ered Luin, but this is a matter of some urgency. You see, not long ago, our two peoples nearly came to war over a dispute engineered by Skorgrím Dourhand and his ilk. My father, Cardavor, was injured in the fighting and Skorgrím fled Ered Luin, but other threats still remain.

'Alas, I am afraid my companion and I have not come here on a happy errand. Goblins were spotted crossing the River Lune into the ruins of Lhúngobel and it is possible they mean to interfere in the affairs of the Shire. In addition, we have captured a Dourhand, but he bears no weapon against us and begs our aid.

'It is an unusual matter, I admit. Will you speak to this Dourhand and aid my companion and I in ridding the Shire of these goblins?''Even though Skorgrím threatened the life of my father, I would not think to seek vengeance upon all the Dourhands. It is pity they deserve—not my wrath. A darkness has ensnared their people, and it wears the face of their lord of old!

'For our part, Athal and I will continue to keep watch on Ered Luin. If the Dourhands have truly returned to Sarnúr, I have no doubt that we will call upon you again. As for the goblins, we will rout them to the very last!

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'Despite the Yule season, brave adventurers are still needed to complete missions across Middle-earth.Missions can be completed across Middle-earth.

You should complete any mission.Complete a mission (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mara Sandydowns can be found near the entrance to Winter-home.

You have completed a mission during the Yule Festival. You should talk to Mara Sandydowns.'We love that you've come to visit Frostbluff, but there's more to Yule than this lovely little town. Why don't you bring some Yule cheer to folks in need of aid across Middle-earth?''Spread some Yule cheer, have you? Well done, friend.'A letter arrived, and in it you found a note from the people of Trestlebridge, north of Bree-land along the Greenway.Trestlebridge can be found north of Bree along the Greenway. Make your way there and speak with the folk who make the beleaguered town their home.

The letter requested that you make your way to Trestlebridge to talk to the people there.${CLASS},

Trestlebridge is in a terrible state. We are besieged by Orcs at our northern and southern borders and are sending out general calls to any that we feel may be able to assist us. 

Please, if you find that you are near our borders, come and talk to us.'So many are missing. So much is lost. If only there were someone willing to aid us, I am certain that the people of Trestlebridge would do what they could to show their thanks.''What supplies we have are rationed and threatened every night and day by the Orcs. We need to drive them out, but the number of able bodies grows fewer each day.

'What will become of us here in Trestlebridge?''Hullo, are you here to help? So many have gone missing or have wandered out to seek help, and fewer still have returned. Every night, it seems that the Orcs grow more aggressive and threaten us more.

'Trestlebridge could use a hero.''Well met, friend. As you can see, Trestlebridge has seen better days. Nellie is doing what she can to keep order, but the Orcs press their advantage more every day.

'If you speak with others, they will surely tell you the same as I. We could certainly use your help.''There are folk here not willing to lie down and lose their land. I am one!

'Still, the Orcs are a plague like none we have ever seen, and without aid there may be no land left to claim.'You have helped Tangwen to brew a delicious-smelling tea in the hopes of bringing some comfort to the people of Herne.Tangwen has asked you to bring tea to residents of Herne who are taking refuge in the Crossway Inn.

Herne is in central Cardolan.You should bring the hawkwort flowers and lavender to Tangwen. 

Tangwen is in Herne in western Cardolan.'It smells so wonderful in here, does it not? Let's spread this lovely feeling to the rest of Herne. Here, take the tea, and bring it to villagers who may be in need.''Tea? Does it have honey in it? I only like tea with honey in it. Hmm, that does smell good, though. I guess I could try some.''Is this one of Tangwen's teas? Ah, she is always looking out for us. What a lovely lady. You have my thanks! May we all find rest and peace soon.''Tea from Tangwen? Why thank you. Not much will alleviate my fears until those black riders are found and dealt with, though.''What is this now? Tea? Relax?! This is not the time for relaxing. Take your herbs and meddling elsewhere.''A tea from the town healer? Ahh, that smells incredible. It reminds me of something mother used to make to help me sleep. Thank you, my friend. I will have to pay my respects to Tangwen soon.''I would much rather have wine. Brandy Wine from the Golden Perch, such as is imported for festivals. I do not suppose you will have been to the Golden Perch. You do not look like you get over to Stock much.''Welcome back! Why, you still have tea left? I am surprised, but not sad that there will be more left for us to enjoy!

'Thank you for your help, ${PLAYER}! It was a small thing, but I hope it brings peace and comfort to those we helped.'Hoping to put an end to the upstart "Chief Shirriff" and the conspiracy to seize control of the Quick Post, Mayor Will Whitfoot has authorized Postmaster Proudfoot to take drastic measures to restore service to Yondershire.Postmaster Proudfoot can be found outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.

Mayor Will Whitfoot has authorized Postmaster Proudfoot to alter the route to Nobottle. It now begins in Michel Delving, passes through Little Delving, and follows the road northward into Yondershire. You should inform Postmaster Proudfoot of the Mayor's decision.Talk to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel DelvingOnyx Nethercot can be found inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.

Postmaster Proudfoot has asked you to collect the satchels for Yondershire from Onyx Nethercot inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.Collect the satchels from Onyx Nethercot inside the Quick Post in Michel DelvingOnyx Nethercot can be found inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.

Postmaster Proudfoot has asked you to collect the satchels for Yondershire from Onyx Nethercot inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. You should talk to Onyx Nethercot.Talk to Onyx Nethercot in the Quick Post in Michel DelvingThe revised route to Nobottle begins in Michel Delving, continues into Little Delving, and follows the road northward into Yondershire.

The satchel of mail for Yondershire can be found on Postmaster Proudfoot's table outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. You should carry the satchel to Postman Grubb in Nobottle.Collect the satchel from Postmaster Proudfoot's tablePostman Grubb can be found outside the Quick Post in Nobottle, in Yondershire.

You have successfully delivered the latest mail to Yondershire and outwitted the so-called "Chief Shirriff" in his efforts to seize control of the Quick Post. You should talk to Postman Grubb.Talk to Postman Grubb in Nobottle'I have made up my mind, ${PLAYER}.

'I'd like you to inform Postmaster Proudfoot that I'm officially authorizing him to alter the route to Nobottle. It is my recommendation that the new route ought to pass through Little Delving into the Yondershire, even though I expect the folk dwelling there will give me an earful for it. Nevertheless, it's like my grandfather used to say: if trouble is standing in your way, better to walk around it!

'As for that so-called "Chief Shirriff", let us hope this is the last we hear of him. I certainly do!''What did the Mayor have to say, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Postmaster Proudfoot that Mayor Will Whitfoot has authorized him to alter the route to Nobottle in an effort to undermine the plans of the would-be "Chief Shirriff" and safe-guard the Quick Post. You inform him that the new route is to pass through Little Delving into the Yondershire and continue northward until Nobottle.

'It isn't perfect, but if it means the mail will reach Yondershire, it'll have to do. However, unless the Mayor is prepared to act against this upstart, I fear it will not be enough. For my part, I'll be keeping a much closer eye on the goings-on at the Quick Post. As you know, the Quick Post has many offices across the Shire. Who can say that "Chief" hasn't already found useful friends in some of them?

'That is a matter for me to resolve, ${PLAYER}. As for you, I would have you oversee the very first run of the new route to Nobottle! I believe Onyx has been preparing the satchels inside the Quick Post, so just speak to her when you're ready to set out.''Hullo, ${PLAYER}! How are you? What can I help you with?'

You ask Onyx Nethercot if the satchels for Yondershire are prepared and inform her that the Postmaster has asked you to run a new route to Nobottle on behalf of the Quick Post.

'Oh! So that's what all that business was about! I... overheard you talking to the Postmaster. I didn't mean to, of course, it's just these windows are awfully thin!

'While you were talking to the Mayor, I put all the mail for Yondershire into a bigger satchel and set it just outside on the table beside the Postmaster. With so many things pulling at his attention today, Hugo must not have seen me! It's all there, though, and ready to be delivered.

'Don't let me keep you, ${PLAYER}. The folk of Yondershire have waited long enough for their mail!''My goodness, ${PLAYER}! Is that all the mail out of the Hithershire?'

Postman Grubb takes the satchel, sets it down on his table, and peers into it. After a moment, a smile spreads across his face.

'Why, this'll keep me busy for days! I cannot thank you enough, ${PLAYER}, but tell me, were you and the Postmaster able to unmask the culprit behind the tampering and delays? What happened?'

You tell Postman Grubb of the self-styled "Chief Shirriff" who has been gathering support in the Shire and employing some of the Bounders to unlawfully confiscate the mail. You tell the Postman that Mayor Will Whitfoot has drawn up a new route to Nobottle by way of Little Delving and that service to Yondershire has been restored. In addition, you inform him that Postmaster Proudfoot intends to remain vigilant against further attempts to disrupt the Quick Post.

'From all the talk I've heard around Nobottle, it almost sounds like that Lotho fellow out of Hobbiton. I don't think he's got the mind for a plot like that, though!

'I must thank you again, ${PLAYER}. The Quick Post owes you a great debt!'With net and pie in hand, Diamond is ready to enact her Grand Plan and set a trap for her prey!Adamanda North-took has everything she needs for her Grand Plan!Adamanda is in Yondershire.

You should speak with Adamanda North-took.Speak to Adamanda'The time has come for me to reveal my Grand Plan!

'There is a lynx in the area, harassing the sheep and making trouble for any who approach the nearby hill. We are going to trap him, my friend! Then, I shall charm my way into his heart until he agrees to be my steed and steadfast companion! My ancestor, the great Bandobras Took, rode a horse into battle! I shall follow in his footsteps with my new lynx steed! The Bullroarer club will go to war once more, and goblins and Orcs alike shall tremble before the might of the Yondershire!

'Right! Let us get to it then. Look for a good place for our net, my friend.''Let us trap this lynx!''My mother is right. There are more immediate things I can be doing to help out and gain the respect of the Hobbits of Yondershire.

'In any case, thank you for your help with this! I know exactly what we need to do next.'The Orcs occupying Tharbad have been attacking travellers and destroying or stealing their goods. Turn around is fair play, as they say.Melia has asked you to destroy caches of Orc weapons in Tharbad.

Tharbad is in southern Cardolan.Destroy Orkish weapon caches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Melia know that you have enacted her revenge upon the Orcs.

Melia is at Stonecrop Encampment, north-east of Tharbad.Return to Melia'I am so angry that our trip to Tharbad has been ruined by those awful Orcs! I wish I could walk right into their camps and destroy things of theirs, just like they did to us a few nights ago! But I am no match for them, alas.

'You, however, could enact my revenge, could you not? If you come across any of their stashes of weapons, destroy them! Hahah! That will teach them!''You return! Tell me all about it! Were they angry?'

She laughs with delight as you recount your deeds, then presses coins into your hands.Now that everything has been (hopefully) resolved and the Boffins have all returned, it is time for Angelica's house-warming party to properly begin!Prisca Boffin is in 8 Honeymead Lane, and she is ready for the house-warming party to properly begin.Talk to Prisca Boffin inside 8 Honeymead Lane and attend her daughter's house-warming partyBingo Boffin is outside Angelica's new home on Honeymead Lane.Talk to Bingo Boffin on Honeymead Lane'The party is back on, and with my children returned it will take no time at all to make Angelica's new home ready for the festivities.''You are ready to help us prepare, ${PLAYER}?''I think that turned out to be a fairly satisfying house-warming party, ${PLAYER}, wouldn't you say? And it seems Dinodas inflicted no lasting damage.'

You adopt an innocent expression and ask Bingo what he means by that.

'Ha ha! You are free to keep your secret, my friend, but this hobbit sees more than you might credit him! Aye, I am quite a perceptive fellow, and it is little use to keep things from me... for I will unravel any mystery in no time at all! I discerned the mishap my cousin caused very early on, and knew that the painting must certainly be of the wrong hobbit-home. Who do you think told Camellia where you and Dinodas might be found, fresh after your present-purloining caper? She is as sharp as a tack, you know, and I thought your little conspiracy could use a bit more in the way of smarts. No offence, ${PLAYER}!

'Did you think I ran into Magetha Grubb entirely by accident, or that I did not suggest that she bring her entire menagerie to the party? I have had rather a lot of experience managing the assorted difficulties the Boffins sometimes cause for themselves, and in point of fact I have caused mischief enough myself, as it turns out!'

Bingo laughs brightly, and claps you on the back.

'Oh, one more thing, my friend. I have come into possession of an easel, and I think you should have it. This belonged to an artist I met on the road shortly before I arrived in Yondershire, and when I spoke with him he revealed that not only had he encountered a relative of mine, he had painted a hobbit-house for him! He told me he had no more need for the easel and I could have it. Well, I am more skilled with words than with pictures, so I did not intend to keep it. You can have it instead, ${PLAYER}.

'And yes, because you have figured it out: he told me the address that Dinodas had given him and I knew at once it was the wrong one, and determined to pull this prank on my cousin. So perhaps I am not quite as perceptive as I led you to believe, but still it was a good jest, and I think it all turned out all right in the end.

'Thank you for all your help making this happen, ${PLAYER}. I do believe it was a very Boffin house-warming, and I would have wanted nothing else!'Bingo Boffin has come to Yondershire to welcome his first cousin Angelica (once removed) to her new home in Nobottle.Camellia Boffin and her siblings should have reached Tighfield by now.Meet up with Camellia Boffin and her siblings in TighfieldCamellia Boffin is in Tighfield, but some of her siblings have wandered off (as they often do).Talk to Camellia Boffin in TighfieldMarigold might be getting into some trouble in Tham Amothir to the west, especially if there are half-orcs among the ruins.Marigold might be getting into some trouble in Tham Amothir to the west, especially if there are half-orcs among the ruins.Marigold Boffin is near the ruins of Tham Amothir.Talk to Marigold Boffin near Tham AmothirAccording to Marigold, her brother Dinodas intended to visit with a friend of his at Gamwich.Find Dinodas Boffin in GamwichDinodas Boffin is in Gamwich, and he is very pleased to see you.Talk to Dinodas Boffin in GamwichThe Boffin siblings plan to all meet back up at Tighfield, and would be happy for you to join them.Meet up with the Boffins back in TighfieldBingo is in Tighfield with some of his cousins (once removed).Talk to Bingo Boffin in TighfieldBingo is excited to see the house-warming present that Dinodas came up with.Talk to Dinodas Boffin and see the house-warming presentDinodas arranged for an Elf-painter passing through the Shire to paint Angelica's new home.Examine the painting of Angelica's new homeBingo is very impressed with the painting Dinodas obtained for Angelica.Talk to Bingo Boffin in Tighfield'Well hullo there, ${PLAYER}! This is a pleasant surprise!

'I am on my way to Yondershire to welcome my cousin Prisca's daughter Angelica to her new home! She's not in her tweens anymore, you see, and has purchased a home in Nobottle. They grow up so fast, don't they?

'Prisca and her other children are planning a house-warming party for Angelica, and I am certain you would be welcome as well! Some of Prisca's brood made the trip a few days ago; they intended to find a suitable present to give their sister. Ah... perhaps don't tell Prisca I said that. She dislikes when I refer to her children as a brood. She broods on it, you know?'

Bingo chuckles to himself.

'I should remember to write that down. Anyway... if you're in a festive sort of mood, I'm supposed to meet up with my cousins in the centre of Tighfield. It's to the north-west of here, in Yondershire.''If you're in a festive sort of mood, I'm supposed to meet up with my cousins in the centre of Tighfield. It's to the north-west of here, in Yondershire.''Oh, hello there.''Welcome, ${PLAYER}! Have you come to Yondershire for Angelica's house-warming party? How lovely! I have had my hands full keeping Dinodas and Marigold out of trouble, but mother entrusted me with the task and I will not let her down.'

You ask Camellia where her brother and sister have gone, and a look of sudden panic crosses her face.

'Wha-? They were here a minute ago! I took my eyes off them for just a moment, and they vanished? That is so typical, ${PLAYER}. Can you track them down for me? Marigold had been talking about seeing the Elf ruins to the west of here, but where Dinodas might have gone is a mystery to me. Maybe Marigold will know? She had better!''Can you track down my wayward brother and sister for me? Marigold had been talking about seeing the Elf ruins to the west of here, but where Dinodas might have gone is a mystery to me. Maybe Marigold will know? She had better!''Can you track down my wayward brother and sister for me? Marigold had been talking about seeing the Elf ruins to the west of here, but where Dinodas might have gone is a mystery to me. Maybe Marigold will know? She had better!''Well hello there, ${PLAYER}! Your adventures have brought you to Yondershire? My own taste for adventure has also led my feet here, and it is a good thing, too: these half-orcs would only grow in strength until they might threaten the safety of the Yonder-hobbits, and we can't have that. Did you know my sister Angelica has become one of them? A Yonder-hobbit, I mean; not a half-orc.

'It's true! She's a resident of Nobottle now. We're all here to welcome her to her new home.'

You ask Marigold if she knows where Dinodas might have gone, and she smiles brightly.

'Dinodas gave Camellia the slip, eh? Good for him! Maybe we'll make an adventurer of him after all, ${PLAYER}! Or perhaps not. I'm pretty sure he just wanted to go to Gamwich to show off the house-warming gift he commissioned for Angelica to some friends of his. You'll probably find him there.''I'm pretty sure Dinodas just wanted to go to Gamwich to show off the house-warming gift he commissioned for Angelica to some friends of his. You'll probably find him there.''Hullo there, ${PLAYER}.''${PLAYER}! You are here in Yondershire for Angelica's house-warming party? Oh, you are going to be impressed with the present I found for her. And they all said I wouldn't be able to find anything she'd like!

'Let's go back to Camellia in Tighfield. She and cousin Bingo are going to be so impressed with my gift! "You've come through again, Dinodas!" they'll say! You see if they don't, ${PLAYER}, you see if they don't!''Let's go back to Camellia in Tighfield. She and cousin Bingo are going to be so impressed with my gift! "You've come through again, Dinodas!" they'll say! You see if they don't, ${PLAYER}, you see if they don't!''You're back!''Welcome back!

'So what's this house-warming gift you found, Dino? I hope it's something Angelica will really like!''Well, I'm ready to see this present, Dino! What did you come up with?''Prepare to be amazed, everyone!

'On my way here I encountered an Elf on his way to the Grey Havens. He was travelling westward and my road lay to the north, but we walked together for a little while and spoke of many things. He was a painter, it seems, and though he possessed humility more befitting a hobbit than an Elf, I could tell he must have no small skill in the art. It became clear to me as well that he was dawdling; he seemed in no real hurry to reach the Havens at the end of his road.

'"Perhaps you wouldn't mind painting something for me?" I asked him, and he said it had been many years since he had last painted a subject of hobbit-style. "How many years?" I asked, and he would not say. You know how Elves can be. At any rate, I thought this would be just the thing to give to Angelica: a painting of her new house!

'And here it is!''It is lovely, isn't it? And you all thought I would not find anything suitable!''I have to say, Dino, this painting is incredible! We are fortunate you encountered that Elf when you did, for I am certain Angelica is going to love this gift!

'I did not doubt you for a moment, cousin!'Addie Wheatley, an impoverished, elderly woman afraid for her sons, Amlach and Malin, went into the Barrow-downs in search of her treasure-seeking sons.There is a place immediately upon entering that some mistake for the Dead Man's Perch.

Addie Wheatley said that her son Amlach was going to set up camp at the Dead Man's Perch, but was not there when she and her guides arrived. She fears that Amlach became lost in the southern Barrow-downs while searching for his brother, Malin.Search for AmlachAddie Wheatley awaits your return among the relative safety offered by the guides at the Dead Man's Perch.

You have found Addie Wheatley's son, Amlach, dead within the grave-stones in the southern Barrow-downs. In his hand, you found that he was grasping a tattered journal. You should bring the journal back to Addie, as she will want to know the fate of her sons.'Oh, what a fine, strong person you are. You remind me of my own poor sons. They've been gone for some time now, and I've heard nary a word from them.

'You see, it started with my son, Malin. He was sure there were treasures out in the Barrow-downs for the taking and left seeking his fortune. After a few days passed, and he didn't come back, I sent his brother, Amlach, out after him, and I've not heard from him either!

'Now I've ventured here with these others after my sons. Amlach said he'd camp at the Dead Man's Perch on the eastern cliffs, but he was not here when we arrived. The others here think he's gone further south. Can you go and look for him?''I simply must know what happened to my sons. My guides say that there are grey ruins in the south, sometimes mistaken for the Dead Man's Perch, perhaps my son Amlach is there. Please hurry!''You have returned with Malin's journal! He never let it out of his sight. What evil fate has befallen my sons?

'Amlach... dead? Malin... you must return and search for Malin, ${PLAYER}!'Gangur Farwend has stopped in Herne for a short time only, but if the rocks are interesting he might be convinced to stay longer.Gangur Farwend asked to meet you west of the town of Herne, where he wished to study some of the curious red rocks to be found there.Talk to Gangur Farwend west of the town of HerneChunks of red rock can be found among the craggy outcroppings west of the town of Herne.Collect chunks of red rock west of Herne (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gangur Farwend is waiting west of Herne for you to show him the chunks of rock you collected.'Are you a traveller, as I am? Interesting.

'I am journeying south to the White Mountains to see the dwarf-halls there, but I heard from someone on the road that the rocks of this place have a red sheen to them, and it put me in mind of the Iron Hills. I thought I would see them for myself, and if there is valuable ore to be found here, perhaps I will delay my southward journey and stay awhile.

'If you meet me west of town, I would appreciate both the company and the help!''I am journeying south to the White Mountains to see the dwarf-halls there, but I heard from someone on the road that the rocks of this place have a red sheen to them, and it put me in mind of the Iron Hills. I thought I would see them for myself, and if there is valuable ore to be found here, perhaps I will delay my southward journey and stay awhile.

'If you meet me west of town, I would appreciate both the company and the help!''Aye, these rocks do indeed have a red sheen to them! But the real value lies within, I warrant.

'Will you help me gather up chunks of red rock for closer study?''Will you help me gather up chunks of red rock for closer study?''Ah, yes, these rocks are notable! Now, these were all pretty near the surface, and the working of wind and rain caused them to slough from the larger crags. There could well be valuable ore buried a little deeper!

'I may have to stay here in Ruddymore a little longer, after all. My journey will have to wait, even though the town of Herne seems glum and gloomy. Why are the most valuable materials never to be found in places of cheer?

'You have helped me, friend. Take this reward and my thanks!'You have been tasked with catching the most elusive of quarry: a toy boot?Fish for the lost boot in the nearby pond.Fish for the tiny waterlogged bootMaggo Bunce is near the pond south-east of Nobottle.

Deliver the boot to Maggo Bunce.Maggo Bunce holds up a tattered old doll and draws your attention to its missing boot.

'Excuse me, but my friend Mr. Pondfoot here lost one of his shoes in the pond. Could you fish it up for him? He says he’ll reward you handsomely for your efforts.

'I think I see it glowing down in the water!''Thank you!'

Maggo takes the still soggy boot and works it onto their doll’s foot.

'Mr. Pondfoot says he found this magic stone. He can’t tell you what it does, only that you’ll know what to do when the time is right.'With the mail for Yondershire under the watch of Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving, you prepare to conduct a test of the Quick Post's route to Nobottle according to the Postmaster's instructions.The route to Nobottle begins at Waymeet, continues into Needlehole, and passes through the Rushock Gate into Yondershire.

You have prepared a satchel containing Postmaster Proudfoot's letter to be taken on the Quick Post's route to Nobottle. You should pick up the 'filled' satchel from Postman Twofoot's table and carry it along the route to Nobottle by way of the Rushock Gate.Collect the 'filled' satchel from Postman Twofoot's table<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid nosey hobbits</rgb>Bounder Dogberry can be found at the Rushock Gate, just to the north-west of Needlehole in the Shire.

While attempting to complete the route to Nobottle, you have been stopped by Bounder Dogberry at the Rushock Gate. You should talk to Bounder Dogberry.Talk to Bounder Dogberry at the Rushock GateBounder Dogberry can be found at the Rushock Gate, just to the north-west of Needlehole in the Shire.

Bounder Dogberry has demanded to inspect the contents of the satchel you are carrying to Nobottle. You should wait for Bounder Dogberry to finish his inspection.Wait for Bounder Dogberry to finish his inspectionBounder Dogberry can be found at the Rushock Gate, just to the north-west of Needlehole in the Shire.

Bounder Dogberry has laid claim to Postmaster Proudfoot's letter and the satchel. You should talk to Bounder Dogberry.Talk to Bounder Dogberry at the Rushock GatePostmaster Proudfoot can be found outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.

The Postmaster's letter was confiscated by Bounder Dogberry on behalf of the Chief Shirriff. You should return to Postmaster Proudfoot and tell him what has happened.Talk to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel DelvingMayor Will Whitfoot can be found outside the Town Hole, in Michel Delving.

After learning that someone claiming to be the "Chief Shirriff" has been interfering with the Quick Post, Postmaster Proudfoot has insisted that you speak to Mayor Will Whitfoot. You should talk to Mayor Will Whitfoot.Talk to Mayor Will Whitfoot in Michel Delving'If Postmaster Proudfoot wants you to run the usual route to Nobottle, you'll have to follow the road north through the bog to Needlehole and then continue north-west to the Rushock Gate. Once you pass through the gate, you'll be on the road to Nobottle. Postman Grubb is always about at the Quick Post, so he should be easy to spot. Ah, right, you've already met!

'It's a bit of a journey, but it's a simple enough route. Oh, and keep an eye out for nosey hobbits!

'Best of luck to you, ${PLAYER}. I hope the Postmaster is able to sort this out!''Deliver that satchel to Nobottle on the usual route through the Rushock Gate like the Postmaster asked and we'll get to the bottom of this, ${PLAYER}.

'Do be careful not to let any nosey folk trouble you on your journey—time is of the essence, after all. Oh, and don't let that satchel get wet!''Haven't you heard, postman? There's new rules! By order of the Chief Shirriff, all mail is subject to inspection prior to delivery—especially to the Yondershire!

'Hand that satchel over, and I'll decide if it's worth the Chief's time.''Like I expected... the Chief hasn't seen to this one yet. No mark, no delivery! Just one letter, though? I might as well bring it to the Chief, even if it's just a bunch of prattle.'

Bounder Dogberry furrows his brow and a sneer forms at the corner of his mouth.

'Don't you worry, I'll make sure the Quick Post gets their satchel back.''You're back sooner than I expected, ${PLAYER}. What happened?'

You tell Postmaster Proudfoot about the Bounder you encountered at the Rushock Gate. You inform him that the someone titled "Chief Shirriff" has been issuing new orders to the Bounders demanding inspection of the mail and interfering with the Quick Post.

'Chief Shirriff?! Why, there's no such thing! I'd sooner call myself "Lord of the Post"! There's a First Shirriff, yes, but he's never been the sort for more rules. In fact, he spends most of his time puttering about in the Town Hole as far as I can tell. No, this is some upstart meddling in things he knows nothing about!

'Dogberry, was it? You tell the Mayor what that Bounder said to you and have him set things right for the Quick Post!''Yes? May I help you with something?'

You inform Mayor Will Whitfoot of Postmaster Proudfoot's concerns and of the so-called "Chief Shirriff" interfering with the Quick Post. You tell him that the Postmaster has insisted that service to Yondershire be restored and free of any unlawful inspections.

'Why, there's no such title! Ah, the Postmaster said that too, did he? I wonder if this has anything to do with that upstart in Hobbiton... a terrible nuisance, that one!

'If you would allow me a moment to think, I believe I can resolve this matter to the satisfaction of the Postmaster.'Ancient dead have arisen within the Great Barrow.Ancient Barrow-wights can be found within the Maze Wing of the Great Barrow.Defeat ancient Barrow-wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The ancient corpses within the Maze wing of the Great Barrow should be met with flame, lest they rise again.The ancient corpses can be found throughout the Maze wing of the Great Barrow.Set flame to the wrapped ancient corpses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Adamanda North-took's Grand Plan is nearly ready to be put into action. There is but one missing piece... of the pie.Yonderboars and fallen apples can be found below the apple trees about the northern farm in Tighfield.

Rosalinda North-took has asked you to collect Yonderboar meat and fallen apples.Collect Yonderboar haunches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect fallen apples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Finola is in Nobottle.

You should bring the Yonderboar meat and apples to Finola Whortleberry.Talk to Finola WhortleberryFinola and her oven are located in Nobottle.

Finola has asked you to use her oven to bake an apple and Yonderboar pie.Diamond North-took can be found in Nobottle.

Bring the pie to Diamond.'I bet you are wondering what we are going to trap in this net. I shall tell you! Not yet, however. Firstly, we need to set this trap with the best bait possible - one of Finola Whortleberry's meat pies!

'Now then, everyone knows the best pies are Finola Whortleberry's wild boar and apple pies. I need to check in with our local Bounders, so while I do that, go on ahead and get some Yonderboar meat and some apples. You can pick up some fallen apples near the trees around the big farm in Tighfield. Yonderboar also like the fallen apples, so they might be near the farm too! Bring the meat and apples to Finola Whortleberry and then meet me up the road with pie in hand.''Greetings! Another pie for Diamond? Oh, she wants a Yonderboar pie, does she? Very good, very good! Let's get to work! You can use my oven and I will add in my secret spice mix!''I could smell that pie from a mile away! So too shall our prey! Good work, friend!'When a Hunter faces many foes, the only answer is a great many arrows.Earn the Hail of Arrows traitStrike enemies with Rain of ArrowsChampions are students of battle and become adept at controlling the ebb and flow of each conflict.Use Ebbing Ire or Rising IreChampions are students of battle and become adept at controlling the ebb and flow of each conflict.Use Ebbing Ire, Battle Frenzy, or Second WindStay on your toes and keep your wits about you.Use Slip FreeDefeat many of the Harbingers of the Dead during Skirmish Assault: Ill Omens.Defeat many Harbingers of the Dead during Skirmish Assault: Ill OmensDefeat many of the Harbingers of the Dead during Skirmish Assault: Ill Omens.Defeat many Harbingers of the Dead during Skirmish Assault: Ill OmensIt has long been a legend among the Bree-folk that great treasure still remains buried in the barrows of the Barrow-downs, but there are few among them with the courage to seek it.Barrows are scattered across the Northern and Southern Barrow-downs. Tad Leafcutter is at the Bree Hunting Lodge in Bree-town, east of the Barrow-downs.

Tad Leafcutter has asked you to enter the various barrows within the Barrow-downs and recover some of the Barrow-treasures which lie there.'Greetings ${PLAYER}. I have been very interested in the doings here at the hunting lodge. It seems the only place here in Bree where people would even think about heading up to the old Barrow-downs. Well, there I go talking before explaining. You see, I am quite interested in the place -- the Barrow-downs that is. Ancient cities, old kings, and treasure beyond imagining! My dad, Newbold, has told me such wonderful stories. It seems somehow he got quite a few pieces of old histories out of the Downs, though he never would tell me how.

'I have tasked every hunter who frequents this lodge to travel to the Barrow-downs and retrieve some of the Barrow-treasure, but it seems that none of them have the nerve. As for those Rangers, they aren't ones to be pushed, if you get my meaning. I have heard talk that the treasures within the underground barrows are some of the finest. One of the hunters goes on and on about removing the treasure and breaking some curse laid on it... all a bunch of nonsense if you ask me.

'If you would travel to the Barrow-downs, venture into the underground barrows and retrieve some of the old Barrow-treasures, you would be held in high regard, I'm sure.''You have done it! Look here, ${PLAYER} wasn't scared to go up into those old hills, ha!

'Don't mind the other hunters, they are all superstitious fools. They think the Barrow-downs are haunted, can you believe it!'Defeat many Battle-swine in Skirmishes.

