Meregrot North-took has asked you to gather wild strawberries and forest mushrooms.Collect wild strawberries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect forest mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Meregrot is sitting by the river, south-east of Long Cleeve.

You should bring the mushrooms and strawberries to Meregrot.Return to MeregrotMeregrot is sitting by the river, south-east of Long Cleeve.

Meregrot North-took has asked you to place the mushrooms and strawberries in the picnic basket on the blanket beside her.Meregrot is sitting by the river south-east of Long Cleeve.

You should talk to Meregrot.Talk to MeregrotThe basket is beside Meregrot, south-east of Long Cleeve.

Meregrot North-took has asked you to pick up the picnic basket on the blanket beside her and bring it to her daughter, Rosalinda.Pick up the picnic basketRosalinda North-took can be found in Long Cleeve.

Meregrot has asked you to bring the picnic basket to her daughter Rosalinda.'Isn't it nice to simply sit by the water and take a moment away from all the hustle and bustle? My daughter Rosa certainly could use a break. She tries to take too much on herself. Say, if you are not too busy yourself, perhaps you could do me a favour?

'Rosa probably already has dinner planned, but it would not hurt for me to bring something home to contribute to the fare. Would you gather some ingredients for me? Rosa loves wild strawberries. Too tart for me, by far, but the girl can not get enough. I prefer a hearty, nutty mushroom! You can find the strawberries growing wild along certain paths, and the mushrooms are all over the forest bed.''Welcome back, welcome back! Ahhh, I can smell those mushrooms from here! Perfect timing. I just finished eating and the picnic basket is empty - a perfect place for those strawberries and mushrooms.''My daughter takes too much on herself. I keep telling her one of my most important rules: Many hobbits make for light work.

'Rosa needs to learn how to delegate her duties more! Spread around what needs doing. Like I do! On that note, why don't you take that basket back to her? I think having you deliver it to her will help make my point.''Oh, hello again. Thank you for returning the basket - why, it is full of mushrooms and strawberries! How did she find the time?'

You pass along Meregrot's words of wisdom.

'Ah yes, mother was always good at getting others to help her. I do not want to burden anyone, especially when I have a daughter who is perfectly capable of assisting me.'Fredegar Bolger plans to dispute the official marking of the bounds with Lotho Sackville-Baggins.Lotho Sackville-Baggins can be found in eastern Yondershire, outside of Needlehole.

You should travel towards Needlehole with Fredegar Bolger.Find Lotho Sackville-Baggins between Needlehole and YondershireLotho Sackville-Baggins can be found in eastern Yondershire, outside of Needlehole.

You should talk to Lotho Sackville-Baggins.Talk to Lotho Sackville-Baggins outside of NeedleholeFredegar Bolger can be found in eastern Yondershire, outside of Needlehole.

You should talk to Fredegar Bolger.Talk to Fredegar BolgerA secret Yonder-watch store-house can be found in the woods between Gamwich and Long Cleeve.

Fredegar Bolger has asked you to regroup at the secret Yonder-watch store-house.Regroup at the secret Yonder-watch store-houseA secret Yonder-watch store-house can be found in the woods between Gamwich and Long Cleeve.

You should talk to Fredegar Bolger at the Yonder-watch store-house.Talk to Fredegar Bolger at the secret hideout'It is good that you came back when you did, because this matter has become more urgent. The Yonder-watch has informed me that the hobbit seeking to change the bounds has been spotted near Needlehole! He is a sour fellow named Lotho Sackville-Baggins. Do you know him?

'Let us find him and see if he will abandon this misguided campaign of his.''Hullo, what's this you have here?'

Lotho scowls at you.

'Do you think waving this list of names in my face is going to change my mind? The old bounds worked fine, back when the Westfarthing and Northfarthing ended where they should! Who needs Yondershire to be a part of the Shire? Not I, and not anyone, leastways not any good solid hobbits!

'You peculiar folk... listen up! We need to change the bounds so we can keep the Shire proper safe. Either you move, or you're not in the Shire anymore. It's that simple.

'There's no point trying to discuss it, and your Yonder-watch hasn't got any say in the matter. In fact, I'm sending my own personal Bounders into the Yondershire to make sure nobody tries tampering with the proper bounds. Ha!''I won't let you get away with this, Lotho!'

Fredegar takes a deep breath and calms down slightly before speaking to you in a hushed tone.

'${PLAYER}, I have a plan. There is a Yonder-watch store-house not far from here, and it's become something of a secret hideout for me and my friends. Meet me there as soon as you are able!'

Fredegar turns back to Lotho.

'Until next time, Lotho. You haven't seen the last of us!''You made it! That Lotho has never been much for discussion, and he's only gotten worse with age.

'Unfortunately for him, we've only gotten smarter and more serious, haven't we?'Defeat many bloated mireworms in Skirmishes.
