This deed will only be advanced by Lieutenants that do not appear grey to your character, they must be around the same level as you are.Defeat Blood-rooks in SkirmishesDinodas Boffin has ruined his sister Angelica's house-warming party (with your assistance), but now his mother Prisca demands that you help him set things right.Bingo is in Tighfield, and Dinodas believes he might have seen where the other Boffin children went.Talk to Bingo Boffin in TighfieldFosco Boffin apparently went in search of Elf-boats on the western rivers of Yondershire.Find Fosco BoffinFosco Boffin has found a hobbit-boat in one of the rivers of Yondershire.Talk to Fosco Boffin by the riversideFosco told you that Marigold headed north in the direction of Lhúngobel, seeking enemies to slay.Fosco told you that Marigold headed north in the direction of Lhúngobel, seeking enemies to slay.Bingo Boffin has followed you to Lhúngobel.Talk to Bingo Boffin at LhúngobelBingo heard rumours of a dancing competition happening at Long Cleeve, and thinks that seems a likely place to find Esmeralda.Find Esmeralda at the dancing competition at Long CleeveEsmeralda Boffin is dancing at Long Cleeve.Talk to Esmeralda Boffin at Long CleeveEsmeralda will not return to Nobottle until you perform in her dancing competition. You had better <rgb=#00FF00>dance</rgb>!Esmeralda will not return to Nobottle until you perform in her dancing competition. You had better <rgb=#00FF00>dance</rgb>!Esmeralda Boffin is at Long Cleeve, dancing.Talk to Esmeralda at Long CleeveEsmeralda saw Marigold heading north in the direction of Bâr Faroth.Find Marigold Boffin at the ruins of Bâr FarothNárnaz the Smiter encountered a deadly hobbit-adventurer at Bâr Faroth, to his sorrow.Talk to Nárnaz the Smiter near Bâr FarothBingo Boffin has arrived at Bâr Faroth.Talk to Bingo Boffin at Bâr FarothMarigold Boffin went ahead to the Old Links to stop the planned goblin-mischief.Berilac slept through the commotion on the Old Links.Talk to Berilac on the Old LinksBerilac dreamed of a delicious smell wafting from Northcotton Farm, in the east: just the sort of odour to attract the attention of his hungry sibling Griffo.Find Griffo BoffinGriffo Boffin stands by a waggon bearing food from Northcotton Farm.Talk to Griffo BoffinNow that you have found all of his brothers and sisters, you should return to Dinodas outside 8 Honeymead Lane, in Nobottle.Talk to Dinodas outside 8 Honeymead Lane'There's nothing for it, ${PLAYER}: we have to track down the rest of my siblings and get them to come back before my mother loses her temper. Trust me! She's a little cross at the moment, but you'll see much worse if we don't hurry!

'You should check first with my cousin Bingo. He's something of an adventurer, it turns out, and might have seen where everyone went. I think he went back to Tighfield.''You should check first with my cousin Bingo. He's something of an adventurer, it turns out, and might have seen where everyone went. I think he went back to Tighfield.''Hullo, hullo, ${PLAYER}! You're looking for cousin Prisca's children? Well, I've seen one! Young Fosco told me the party was delayed, and he intended to spy an Elf-boat or two on one of the western rivers. That's the direction you want to look.

'I'll catch up with you after I'm done with my shopping. I'm in the market for some rope, you see. Can never have enough rope, when you're adventuring! I will see you later, friend!''Young Fosco told me the party was delayed, and he intended to spy an Elf-boat or two on one of the western rivers. That's the direction you want to look.

'I'll catch up with you after I'm done with my shopping. I'm in the market for some rope, you see. Can never have enough rope, when you're adventuring! I will see you later, friend!''Will you look at that!''I went in search of Elf-boats, ${PLAYER}... but I found a hobbit-boat instead! It seems the Yonder-hobbits aren't as afraid of boating as the folk back home. Are these... are these my people?

'I bumped into my sister Marigold a short ways back, but she didn't come here with me. She said she was going to investigate the ruins to the north of here. That's very much like our Marigold, if you don't know. She's always looking for adventure. If you find goblins you'll likely find my sister!

'I have a few more questions for this fellow about his boat, but once I've asked them I'll come back for Angelica's party. Worry not! I won't be long.''I bumped into my sister Marigold a short ways back, but she didn't come here with me. She said she was going to investigate the ruins to the north of here. That's very much like our Marigold, if you don't know. She's always looking for adventure. If you find goblins you'll likely find my sister!

'I have a few more questions for this fellow about his boat, but once I've asked them I'll come back for Angelica's party. Worry not! I won't be long.''No sign of Marigold yet? I'm sure she's fine: she's a chip off the old block, as they say! Of all my first-removed cousins, she seems most able to take care of herself. Prisca would say I have been a bad influence, but I say that's the very best kind!

'I think I might have found a clue to the location of another of the Boffin children, ${PLAYER}. There is apparently a dancing competition underway at Long Cleeve. If that does not sound like music to Esmeralda's ears, I know of nothing else that would!

'To Long Cleeve, my good ${RACE}!''I think I might have found a clue to the location of another of the Boffin children, ${PLAYER}. There is apparently a dancing competition underway at Long Cleeve. If that does not sound like music to Esmeralda's ears, I know of nothing else that would!

'To Long Cleeve, my good ${RACE}!''Hullo there!''Are you here to join in the dancing competition, ${PLAYER}? When I arrived, I discovered to my dismay that there was nothing going on! There was nary a toe-tap, no sign of an arm-flourish, neither a twirl nor a whirl! So I started my own.

'I will return to Nobottle, of course. But not until you participate in the dance, ${PLAYER}!''I will return to Nobottle, of course. But not until you participate in the dance, ${PLAYER}!''Keep dancing, ${PLAYER}! Mix it up!''Good job, ${PLAYER}! I am impressed!

'Anyway, you're looking for Marigold? She came this way and I asked if she wanted to join my dancing competition, but she declined. Apparently she was pursuing a band of goblins, although with my sister it can sometimes be hard to tell if what she says is true or if she's imagining some mad adventure. Either way, she ran off to the north, so you can look for her in that direction.

'I will return to Nobottle in a few moments. Let me just get a few more dance-steps in!''You'll never get me alive!''I never knew these folk to fight so fiercely before! Curse these Shire-folk!'

Nárnaz the Smiter coughs, the blood pooling beneath his torn armour.

'It won't matter, in the long run: the rest of my boys have already gone south-east, and they'll make the rules for a NEW sport! They're gonna repay those hobbits for the invention of Golfimbul-clubbing, you wait and see! This new sport will use the same clubs and can be played on the same fields... but the heads that roll won't belong to goblins! Ha ha ha!''That sounds bad, ${PLAYER}. We'd better hurry south-east! Marigold might have run into trouble on the Old Links!''Hullo there, ${PLAYER}! My brother Berilac is sleeping peacefully... but he doesn't know there are goblins about! We'd better protect him.'Berilac yawns and stretches sleepily.

'Ah, hello there, ${PLAYER}. I just had the most lovely and peaceful dream. There was a delicious smell wafting through Yondershire from the east. Actually, I can still smell it! What a convincing dream, to have left its imprint in this fashion!

'Now that I am rested, I will go see if Angelica's party is ready to begin. You're looking for Griffo? Perhaps you should follow the delicious smell of food... he probably would do so, if his nostrils detected it!''Now that I am rested, I will go see if Angelica's party is ready to begin. You're looking for Griffo? Perhaps you should follow the delicious smell of food to the east... he probably would do so, if his nostrils detected it!''Greetings!''Are you here to sample some food from Northcotton Farm? The waggon-driver kindly let me try some of the vegetables, and I am pleased to report that they are perfectly fresh and of the finest quality! Well, then I just had to try some of this fresh-baked bread, and there was a basket of apples just waiting to be sampled....

'I suppose Angelica's party is nearly ready to begin? Then I will return to Nobottle, and perhaps when I get there I shall fill up my corners. My sister will surely have set out the snacks by then!''I will return to Nobottle.''You did it: you found all my wayward brothers and sisters! You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'A shade found wandering in the Barrow-downs -- meaning no ill, it seems -- felt the pull of its brother and struggles to appease whatever force has returned to awaken them.The shade does not know precisely where the Bone Man may be found, other than that he lies somewhere in the south Barrow-downs.

The shade spoke of the Bones of a man of Cardolan returned to life and of the oath he and his brother made.Defeat the Bone ManThe shade wanders through the northern Barrow-downs.

You should return to the shade and let him know that the Bone Man has been defeated and the shades freed.Talk to the Wandering Shade'In the south he rose
from an earthen grave.
Once flesh and whole
now bones, depraved,
by spirits seeking a home.

'A man of Bone 
slept 'neath Cardolan stone.
Rising once, struck low,
by oathed brothers
now sundered twain.

'Brothers, cursed,
return again 
to face this foe
from whom they stole.
For deeds most noble
in intent.

'Whilst evil walks
so too will we.

'Seek you he,
beyond the border
south towards stone
the land of Cardolan
his Bones there still roam.''Hear you this brother?
Hear you absolution?
Rest now, brother, 
rest as we were
as we shall be.''A Man of Bone,
from 'neath Cardolan stone.
Seek him now to lift this curse,
e're we Brothers wander ever more.''Bone Man? Barrow-downs? I know nothing of such things, nor do I care to! But I want rid of that accursed shade in the alley.

'Talk to Newbold Leafcutter. He's a scholar of such dark and mysterious things. He went gallivanting off to the Barrow-downs.''Ah, the Bone Man! Yes, indeed, I have heard tales of this fell creature, though I know not if they be legend or truth.

'I have heard that he sometimes stalks the night in the heights of Ost Gorthad, a ruined fortress in the south-east corner of the Barrow-downs. If this be a true telling, though, I would fear to venture to that place, as it is said that the Bone Man is a terrible evil.'Meneldir is not entirely convinced that Boromir is trustworthy: should the four of you travel together from Tharbad?Boromir, his tale completed, studies the faces of your companions. Meneldir stares back impassively.Talk to MeneldirMeneldir has asked to speak with you some distance from the others, just to the north-east of the camp-site.Join Meneldir a short distance away from the others, to the north-eastMeneldir wishes to speak with you about his concerns about Boromir, the Captain of Gondor.Talk to Meneldir to the north-east, away from your other companionsBoromir remains at the camp-fire near the northern bank of the Gwathló.

Meneldir gave you a worn map of Old Cardolan to show to Boromir and to Egfrith.Show the map to Boromir at the camp-siteEgfrith remains at the camp-fire near the northern bank of the Gwathló.

Meneldir gave you a worn map of Old Cardolan to show to Boromir and to Egfrith.Show the map to Egfrith at the camp-siteMeneldir has come back to the camp-site.Meneldir suggested that you scout the countryside outside Tharbad from a number of locations within the city, and defeat the foes you encounter there, to make safe your passage through the flooded city.Defeat foes within Tharbad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Meneldir and the others planned to meet with you on the road north of Tharbad.Talk to Meneldir on the road just north of Tharbad'That is my tale. You have no doubt heard more exciting stories than this, and were I to speak of our mighty efforts in Gondor's defence you would hear one such! But time is wasting.''That is the tale of my journey to the north, such as it has been to this day.''Could I speak with you alone for a moment, ${PLAYER}?

'Let us just walk to the north-east, right over there.''Let us just walk to the north-east, right over there.''I do not know if we can trust this Captain of Gondor, ${PLAYER}. Remember the words of Bregoleth! She told us to guard our trust with care, for even seeming allies could harbour treachery in their hearts. Neither do I exclude Egfrith from this warning! But Boromir rode right by Isengard on his way north, and even admitted that he spoke with Saruman! How can we trust his conversation with the White Wizard was as he described? We cannot.

'I think we should keep what we know of the White Hand to ourselves, for now, just in case Boromir has fallen under the sway of the traitor wizard. We can travel together, at least until we reach Bree-land and the Dúnedain, but we should keep an eye on both of our companions. Bregoleth believed we stood on the very precipice of danger, and I think she spoke true.

'Here, take this map of Cardolan. Show it to the others and see what they recommend for our course.''Show that map to the others and see what they recommend for our course.''You have decided we should travel together? I believed your friend would suggest we should not, but I find the idea agreeable, for now. Should my own course not align with yours, I will depart, and without hard feeling.'

Boromir unfolds the map of Old Cardolan and studies it briefly before handing it back to you.

'My own journey's end lies in a hidden dale, ${PLAYER}, further north than this map tells. Perhaps Meneldir will unveil a second map when we draw nearer to the Bree-land, and that one will mark my destination. But perhaps not: my father said the dale was hidden.''My own journey's end lies in a hidden dale, further north than this map tells. Perhaps Meneldir will unveil a second map when we draw nearer to the Bree-land, and that one will mark my destination. But perhaps not: my father said the dale was hidden.''It pleases me to hear that Meneldir will not turn away the Captain of Gondor, for the Men of that land are warriors strong and true, and in past days they have been hardy friends of Rohan, and we of them.'

Egfrith unfolds the map of Cardolan and wrinkles her nose.

'These names are unfamiliar to me, ${PLAYER}, so different from those of my own land. I cannot begin to understand how to speak some of these places aloud. Boromir is not the only one of us who is far from their homeland.

'I will follow Meneldir until we find the Rangers of the North, for Rohan lies withering while I am away, and if I cannot return with the thing I seek I fear the kingdom will die.''We will travel together.''Then our paths lie together, for a time.''Then we are agreed? Our road leads north, and that means we must pass through the city and travel north along the Greenway towards Bree-land.

'We should defeat more of the creatures that lie between us and the northern walls of the city, and I suggest we scout the gaps in the encircling wall at several locations before we leave Tharbad behind us. Once that is accomplished, we can meet up just north of the city to plan our further course.''We should defeat more of the creatures that lie between us and the northern walls of the city, and I suggest we scout the gaps in the encircling wall at several locations before we leave Tharbad behind us. Once that is accomplished, we can meet up just north of the city to plan our further course.''And that is Tharbad behind us, ${PLAYER}. If the crossing of the Greyflood proves the worst experience of our journey, I will count us fortunate. I fear it will not be so, though it is likely to be the wettest. Did Tegwyn dislike the damp and cold of the Wadewater? He is fortunate he had no need to cross the Greyflood, and under the watchful eye of his parents it will be many years before he might.

'But now we must turn our eyes to our own road. Cardolan awaits, and within its bounds we will find my friend Narndir, who will know the location of the chieftain of the Dúnedain. Then will Egfrith's purpose be attained, and our own as well. Perhaps then Boromir can be set on the proper course, and you and I will dine at the Prancing Pony before we part.

'But we are not there yet. We must take one step at a time, lest we trip upon our own feet.'Barghests can be found throughout the southern Barrow-downs. Their glowing eyes can be turned in for a bounty and crafting materials.Barghests can be found within the southern Barrow-downs,

Some barghests can chill a being with but a gaze. Edith Sweetrose, at Dead Man's Perch, has offered to provide you a reward for collecting barghest-eyes taken from the southern-dwelling barghests.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'Many believe that the strength of the barghests lay in their howl. While it is true their howls are dangerous, the power of their eyes is equally dangerous. With but a gaze they have been known to strike a deep fear into their victims that can kill them.

'I would ask you to seek out barghests and collect their eyes. I will pay you handsomely for this bounty.''These will do well. I am unclear what the power truly is behind these eyes, but I know that I have seen the ill that these creatures can bring about.

'You have earned this reward well.'Sage Hayseed is looking for bear-hides to sell to the rug makers of Bree.Bears can be found throughout the northern Bree-fields.

Sage Hayseed has asked you to collect bear-hides from the bears in the northern Bree-fields and surrounding areas and return them to her. She has offered to pay you a fair price for this effort.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'Aside from boars, I was also hunting bears in an effort to collect massive hides that could be turned into rugs, wall hangings and blankets if need be.

'I will pay you handsomely for your assistance in collecting these for me.''These will do nicely and surely satisfy the order which I have. Thank you for all that you have done thus far, friend.'Cardolan, once the ruling kingdom in the area of the southern Barrow-downs, left behind many relics. The creatures of the southern Barrow-downs likely carry some of these relics if one looks for them.Any of the creatures in the southern Barrow-downs may carry trinkets and relics from the kingdom of Cardolan.

Edith Sweetrose will trade crafting materials for any relics of Cardolan you may find.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'The relics of Cardolan can fetch a nifty price from the well-to-do in Bree-town. Since we are here, I thought I might offer you a little deal. 

'If you collect these relics over the course of your travel, I will trade you materials that may be of great use to you.

'Is this acceptable?''These will sell nicely, and I owe you much. Here, this should be a fair trade and if you find otherwise, you know where I can be found.'Sage Hayseed asked that you collect perfect tusks from boars througout the northern Bree-fields to help her with the orders she is out there to fill.Boars can be found in the northernmost Bree-fields.

Sage Hayseed has asked you to hunt boars for their tusks and return the tusks to her at the camp near the lakes in the north Bree-fields.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'I came to the north to find tusks, a prized item for hunters throughout Bree. The tusks that I seek sit aside antlers within establishments to hang cloaks and overcoats upon. I have been tasked with collecting a good many of these, but the number of Orcs in the area, frankly, gives me pause to venture too far from our camp.

'You seem a bit more hardy than I, and I am willing to pay you for collecting the tusks which I need. Are you willing to help me?''These are perfect!

'I owe you a great deal, friend. Here, please take these and know that you have helped me greatly.'Walt Whitrose is collecting turtle shells to furnish to the Blacksmiths of Bree. Turtle-shells can be used as a good form for creating shields.Turtles can be found surrounding the lakes and other bodies of water in the northern Bree-fields.

Walt Whitrose would like you to collect turtle-shells and return back to him behind the stones near the falls where the gorge meets the lakes. 

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'Greetings, traveller. It seems as though you found yourself far away from the safety of Bree, which means that you are probably like myself and my friend here: adventurous spirits. We'd be out and about more if it weren't for those Orcs to the west. As it is, the safety of our camp seems to be more important than the money we could make by filling our bounties.

'Of course, if you are willing to assist us, we have some materials that we would happily part with should you want to help us. 

'I am looking for turtle-shells to furnish the blacksmiths of Bree who often use them to create forms to fashion their shields from. You can find turtles all around the lake area here in northern Bree.''These will do nicely. Now tell me, which of these fine rewards would you like to claim for your efforts?'There is a bounty out for the skulls of the wights which wander the southern Barrow-downs.Wights can be found throughout the southern Barrow-downs.

The guide, Edith Sweetrose, prizes wight-skulls and will pay you for them. She is camped at the Dead Man's Perch, where the northern Barrow-downs meet the southern Barrow-downs.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'It is not usual that we are in such a position. We have come here before with no danger present save the rats, crawlers, or the occasional barghest. This, however, is most peculiar.

'I am certain that the people of Bree-land can benefit from the removal of these terrifying foes, these wights, so I will offer you something of a bounty for their defeat.

'Defeat the walking dead here and return their skulls to me. I will reward you well for these endeavours.''Yes, this proves a good many victories. You have done a great service to the people of Bree-land this day.'The town of Trestlebridge is threatened by the Enemy and needs help from afar.Trestlebridge is to the north, along the route called the Greenway. 

Speak to Guardsman Otley in Trestlebridge and learn how you can help with the town's defence.'Have you heard about Trestlebridge to the north? Its location makes it a tempting target for Orc raiders and brigands. I'm sure your help in its defence would be most appreciated.

'Gather your belongings and travel north to Trestlebridge. The Greenway is the most expeditious path, and the most well-trod. Keep to it and you should be safe.

'When you arrive, seek out Guardsman Otley. He'll point you in the right direction.''Bree-town sent you, eh? It's good to know that our messengers arrived safe and sound. And now that you're here, well it's good to have another sword-arm for the cause.'Complete 'A Mission to Bring Good Cheer'.Complete 'A Mission to Bring Good Cheer'.Complete 'A Mission to Bring Good Cheer' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The evil spider Gwigon has made its lair amongst the twisting barrow of Taradan, and there her brood multiplies. They seek to ensnare any living thing foolish enough to wander in amongst the bones and dust of long-fallen princes.Defeat Barrow-spiders in the barrow of TaradanThe evil spider Gwigon has made her lair among the twisting barrow of Taradan, and there her brood multiplies. They seek to ensnare any living thing foolish enough to wander in among the bones and dust of long-fallen princes.Defeat Barrow-spiders in the barrow of TaradanDefeat many brood-queens in Skirmishes.
