You should talk to Fredegar Bolger.Talk to Fredegar in NobottleHobbits upset and disgruntled for various reasons can be found in villages throughout Yondershire.

Fredegar has asked you to collect signatures from upset hobbits in each village.Fredegar Bolger can be found in the village of Nobottle.

You should bring the list of signatures to Fredegar Bolger.The young hobbit speaks to the small crowd that gathers around him.

'They say the Bounders protect the bounds? Why is that? That is because everything within the bounds is our home! We are hobbits, are we not? We will decide where the bounds are and where the bounds are not!'

The young hobbit turns his attention to you.

'You there! You look like you could use some more convincing. Speak to these hobbits gathered around. They will tell you I speak only the truth!''Now that you have spoken to these fine hobbits, you must see that I speak the truth! My name is Fredegar, and I have but one concern: the state of the bounds!

'There has been something upsetting going on in the Shire. I can't say any more than that, but you will have to take my word for it. There are frightening folk about, and...'

Fredegar shivers.

'The less said of that, the better. But I have also seen a number of ruffians moving about, and we can surely do something about them! Can I ask you to persuade some ruffians to turn tail and return to their homes outside the Shire? I know they have taken up residence in the ruins of Ost Lagorath to the north, but you might also find them prowling about elsewhere in the Yondershire.''Fredegar speaks the truth. I have seen a ruffian or two cross the bounds of southern Yondershire. We have got to do something!''Fredegar is worried about Yondershire, and I believe him. We live a peaceful life but lately I've seen more and more troublemakers about!''He is such a good storyteller. I could listen to him talk about the bounds all day!

'Did you know the bounds of the Shire used to be different from the current bounds? I have seen the maps! Hubo Clayhanger has a book containing such maps in his collection! Now, what was the name of that author? It was someone familiar, but I can't remember why....''I don't have proof, but I think some of the stone walls that mark the old bounds are being moved! One day the old wall was intact, and the next? Why, it was missing a stone or two! Someone is up to something!''Listen to the tales told by ${PLAYER}, the ${CLASS} who has defeated many ruffians in Yondershire!

'So that's one thing settled, and I thank you for handling it. On to my second concern: someone is seeking to change the bounds, removing Yondershire from the Shire itself! This is unacceptable.

'Here, ${PLAYER}. Take this signature list and collect as many signatures as you can. We'll prove to the guilty party that the folk of Yondershire will not stand for his meddling!''This is a fine and lengthy list of signatures! You have done well!'The Dúnedain of Cardolan have posted a task to collect blackened furs.You have accepted a task to acquire blackened furs.Wanted: Blackened furs from the beasts of Cardolan, in especial those of Wargs. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Wanted: Blackened furs from the beasts of Cardolan, in especial those of Wargs. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Dúnedain of Cardolan have posted a task to collect dusky ears.You have accepted a task to acquire dusky ears.Wanted: Dusky ears from lynx, aurochs, and Wargs in Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Wanted: Dusky ears from lynx, aurochs, and Wargs in Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Barrow-downs were once a haven of the Rangers of Cardolan. They fell long ago and became of place of terror beneath the shadow of the Witch-king of Angmar.Barrows lie scattered across the Northern and Southern Barrow-downs. Anglinn is at the Bree Hunting Lodge in Bree-town, east of the Barrow-downs.

The Ranger Anglinn has asked you to banish the wights beneath the Northern and Southern Barrow-downs and bring him trinkets of ancient Cardolan which they might be carrying.'I have heard your name whispered before in these streets. I know who you are, and I know your intentions, so I will not waste your time. You have perhaps heard of Black Riders who came through town, causing geese to scream and dogs to howl? Well, they are more than just Men in black cloaks, and they are a far greater danger than any of these simple folk know.

'The Riders have awoken something, something that should have remained sleeping. You have no doubt heard at least a part of the tale of the fall of Cardolan? It was a nation divided by war and decimated by a Plague borne on winds out of Mordor, their remains inhabited with the servants of the Witch-king! The awakened spirits have heard their master's call once more, and I fear for the safety of Bree. I have been tasked to guard it at all costs.

'What I ask of you is to enter one of the barrows and put to rest the bones that still dwell within. Once the barrow housed a great ruler of Cardolan, now it is known as Haudh Iarchith, and Men shiver to hear its name whispered. Enter into Haudh Iarchith and put to rest those that wander its halls. Some of the wights might carry trinkets of Cardolan. Bring them to me as proof of your deeds, and you will earn great respect among the hunters of Bree who would not dare to enter those halls of madness.''I did not doubt that you would finish the task, ${PLAYER}. It is well that you have returned, however, for your strength will be needed sooner than you think.'Brogadan is an ancient warrior joined with the fires Angmar used to raze this ancient fortess.Find Brogadan, Wraith of Fire, in the third tower of Fornost.Approach BrogadanBrogadan, Wraith of Fire, is master over flames.Allow the room to be engulfed in fireDo not defeat BrogadanBrogadan, Wraith of Fire, is ready to meet his final end.Defeat BrogadanRemmenaeg is an ancient warrior joined with the lingering evil essence of the Witch-king of Angmar.Remmenaeg is in the final tower of Fornost.Approach RemmenaegRemmenaeg must be defeated without lighting the braziers too many times.Defeat RemmenaegDo not light too many braziers (${VALUE}/7)Rhavalmeldir is an ancient warrior joined with the crumbling walls and defences of the ancient fortress.Rhavameldir awaits you at the top of the second tower in Fornost.Locate RhavameldirRhavameldir must be shown his place.Defeat RhavameldirDo not defeat any of Rhavameldir's minionsRhavameldir's minions must now be destroyed.Defeat Rhavameldir's minions.Megoriath is an ancient warrior joined with the corrupted brack now flooding the lower ramparts of Fornost.The wraith is waiting at the end of the water tower.Find Megoriath, the Wraith of WaterMegoriath, the Wraith of Water, is awaiting you.Defeat MegoriathDo not fall into the waterDefeat many Chaos-fiends in Skirmishes.
