This deed will only be advanced by Lieutenants that do not appear grey to your character, they must be around the same level as you are.Defeat Death-mongers in SkirmishesDefeat many Death-mongers in Skirmishes.
This deed will only be advanced by Lieutenants that do not appear grey to your character, they must be around the same level as you are.Defeat Death-mongers in SkirmishesAn ancient scroll contains what may be essential information which Rhiangar desperately wants to obtain. The ability to decipher its contents are beyond her, however.Rhiangar has asked you to bring the scroll to Melynis Bragreg.

Melynis is among the caravans south of Andrath, in northern Cardolan.Melynis has suggested that you speak with Gerwyn while she works on deciphering the scroll.

Gerwyn is located in the caravan in northern Cardolan.'How exciting and frustrating at the same time! I feel like this scroll certainly holds the answer. I cannot read it, but I know someone who can!

'Across the Greenway, near the northern border to Andrath, a caravan of travellers has circled up near the road. I travelled with them for some of the way from Bree, but they had a wheel crack and needed to stop, so I went on alone. Among their number is a scholar - one of the little people called hobbits! She will know how to read this! Let's bring the scroll to Melynis!''Oh, hullo. I am Guffo Bragreg, Melynis' husband. Melynis warned me this trip would be an adventure. I should have hidden under the bed, but I could not let her go off into danger without me.

'How I wish we were comfortably settled by our fireplace, a cup of warm milk in my hand and no ghosts anywhere around! What a miserable land this is! But look at Melynis! Even broken down on the side of the road, she is still cheerful. Look at her smile! Ah, she is truly my favourite person.''Hullo there! Rhiangar tells me you have a scroll that you cannot read? I may indeed be able to help with that. Let's have a look, shall we?

'I learned how to read the old tongue for my studies. I have been tracing my family history and exploring my lineage! Rhiangar and I met in Bree and she told me there are hobbits living in Swanfleet who visit Herne! I aim to meet some of these hobbits in the hopes that they might be able to fill in some blanks on my family tree.

'Ah yes, I can read this, but it will take me some time to decipher it. In the meanwhile, there are some in our camp who could use your help. Why not speak with Gerwyn while I work on this?''Well met. I am Gerwyn, and yes, we could certainly use your help.'Complete many deeds in Yondershire.Complete many deeds in Yondershire.Complete: Sites of YondershireComplete: Quests of YondershireComplete: Slayer of YondershireThe Hunter depends on precision and focus above all other things, but few realize the endurance it takes to pull back that arrow as well, and fatigue quickly clouds one's vision.Use Intent ConcentrationDeep wounds are deadly wounds. Many a warrior survives the battle, but not the night that follows.Land blows using Brutal StrikesDeep wounds are deadly wounds. Many a warrior survives the battle, but not the night that follows.Critically Hit enemies with Rend, Brutal Strikes or Bracing AttackCaras Gelebren, the Silver Bastion, was once the capital of Tham Mírdain and the jewel of Eregion. Alas, it was brought to ruin long ago when Sauron, seeking to lay claim to the Rings of Power, gathered his vast armies and destroyed all of Eregion.Caras Gelebren, the Silver Bastion, was once the capital of Tham Mírdain and the jewel of Eregion. Alas, it was brought to ruin long ago when Sauron, seeking to lay claim to the Rings of Power, gathered his vast armies and destroyed all of Eregion.Complete 'Doom of Caras Gelebren -- Raid'Weighed down by her duties, Rosalinda North-took is unable to bring a meal to her elderly mother, Meregrot.The picnic basket is beside Rosalinda North-took in Long Cleeve.

Rosalinda has asked you to bring a picnic basket to her mother Meregrot.Pick up the picnic basketMeregrot is sitting by the river, south-east of Long Cleeve.

Rosalinda has asked you to bring a basket of food to her mother, Meregrot.Bring the basket to MeregrotMeregrot is sitting by the river, south-east of Long Cleeve.

Meregrot North-took has asked you to place the picnic basket on the blanket beside her.'While you are exploring, might I ask a favour of you? I recently took over the position of Reeve from my mother, Meregrot. I do not know how she ever kept up with all the requests, concerns, and troubles of Yondershire! I am up to an Elf's ears with things to do.

'If you have the time, would you bring the basket next to me to my mother? She is usually sitting by the river this time of day, and she is certain to be famished by now. Why, I think it has been at least two hours since our last meal.''Well hello, my dear ${RACE}. Rosa sent you, has she? Ah, she is a good girl. Here then, you can set the basket down right here beside me.'

She smiles and pats a spot on the blanket.Rosalinda North-took, Reeve of Yondershire, has too much work and too few hands to help. Her daughter Adamanda should be assisting her, but is nowhere to be found. Perhaps the local townsfolk have some clue as to where the errant hobbit may be found.Hobbits who may know where Adamanda is can found around Nobottle and Long Cleeve.

You should ask if anyone knows where Adamanda North-took is.Ask about Adamanda's whereaboutsAdamanda North-took can be found in Yondershire.

You should look for Adamanda North-took.'Bounders on our borders, goblins in the gardens, shrews in Yondershire, and my daughter is nowhere to be found... as usual!

'Adamanda should have been back by now, as we had plans for a dinner this evening. I have too much work to go chasing that girl down, but perhaps you could locate her? When you do, please give her this letter. She is probably off pretending to be a Ranger somewhere. You should ask around and see if anyone has seen her.''Hey! Watch your step! You nearly trampled all over the tracks that I am following!'

She straightens and looks you up and down.

'Well now, and just who might you be? ${PLAYER}, is it? And my mother sent you with a letter for me? Well, give it here then.''Adamanda? Oh, you mean Diamond! No, I am sorry. I have not seen her for a few hours. I have my hands full here.''Diamond? She came by earlier today for a small meat pie, but I have not seen her for some while.''Adamanda? No, sorry. I have not seen my darling Diamond since second breakfast this morning.''Diamond? Oh yes, I saw her. She was hunting across the river, outside of town to the north-east.''Diamond? I have not seen her today, no.'With her obligations for the afternoon cancelled, Adamanda North-took is free to focus on enacting her Grand Plan.Anson Roper can be found in Tighfield.

Adamanda North-took has asked you to collect some rope from Anson Roper.Talk to Anson RoperFlax can be found growing in the farms of northern Tighfield.

Anson Roper has asked you to collect flax.Collect flax (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Anson Roper can be found in Tighfield.

You should bring the flax to Anson Roper.Fallen wood can be found in the forests around Tighfield.

Anson Roper has asked you to collect a fine piece of fallen wood.Collect a fine piece of woodAnson Roper can be found in Tighfield.

You should bring the fine piece of wood to Anson.The rope is next to Anson in Tighfield.

You should pick up the rope.Pick up the ropeAdamanda is near Nobottle.

You should bring the rope to Adamanda.'You bring fortuitous news, my new friend! The foolish dinner my mother insisted upon has been cancelled! I suppose we can thank good ol' Pip for whatever prank he's off pulling. I am glad to know he is as keen on the machinations of our parents as myself. Which is to say, not at all.

'This leaves me free for the rest of the day to get on with my Grand Plan! Say, you seem to be rather accomplished and useful. Perhaps you could aid me in my endeavour? Excellent!

'We need a few things to make this happen, one of which is a spool of rope from Anson. You head over to Tighfield and collect that from Anson while I gather some of the other supplies.''Rope, is it? Well, you have come to the right place, but this is sadly the wrong time. It will take me some time to get your order together. If you want the rope today, I will need you to take on some of the tasks I had planned for myself or I shall fall behind in my work.

'You still want the rope? Very well. Firstly, my supply of flax is low for today and my next delivery is not until the morrow. Go gather some flax from the fields north of here.''Yes, yes, this will do! You did a fine job of harvesting the flax. If you ever give up this adventuring life of yours, you could make a fine farmer!

'Now then, some animal wandered onto the rope walk and chewed up my top and other wooden items I use to make rope. The top is a piece of wood with grooves cut into it, you see. It is essential for weaving strands of yarn into rope, and you had best believe it will not produce the same quality with the grooves all chewed up.

'Go into the forest and find some freshly fallen wood, will you? No need to cut anything down. We had a beast of a storm come through a few nights back. Knocked down all manner of trees that were otherwise healthy. Find a fine piece of wood for me that is not too dried out, rotted, or fragile. Bring me that and I will trade you for the rope.''Ah, you return! Why yes, this is a fine piece of wood indeed. Very well, you have fulfilled my requests and helped me out a great deal. I thank you! Here is the rope Diamond requested.''Welcome back, friend. My, you look like you have been busy! What took you so long?'

You explain the tasks Anson had you complete. Adamanda guffaws.

'He made you do what?! That Anson is the laziest hobbit I know. I paid for that rope last week. Brought down a fine buck that I traded to him, and he has you running around doing a full day's work.'

She laughs again, shaking her head and wiping tears from the corners of her eyes.Dinodas might have made something of a mistake, and he needs your help to fix it.Griffo, Esmeralda, and Marigold have all gone inside 8 Honeymead Lane.

Dinodas, frantic with worry, has tasked you with scattering his siblings to the wind in order to delay the opening of Angelica's house-warming present.Talk to Griffo Boffin inside 8 Honeymead LaneTalk to Esmeralda Boffin inside 8 Honeymead LaneTalk to Marigold Boffin inside 8 Honeymead LanePrisca has a question for you. She is currently inside 8 Honeymead Lane, waiting for the house-warming party to begin.Talk to Prisca Boffin inside 8 Honeymead LaneAngelica is suddenly distraught! She stands inside her new home, 8 Honeymead Lane, but has been upset by something.Talk to Angelica Boffin inside 8 Honeymead LaneAngelica has asked you to go outside and find out if her siblings plan to come right back for her party.Go outside and see if Angelica's siblings plan to come right backDinodas is being pestered by nosey hobbits of Yondershire.Tell the nosey hobbits not to bother Dinodas (0/3)Dinodas is being pestered by nosey hobbits of Yondershire.Tell the nosey hobbits not to bother Dinodas (1/3)Dinodas is being pestered by nosey hobbits of Yondershire.Tell the nosey hobbits not to bother Dinodas (2/3)The nosey hobbits leave... for now.Make sure the nosey hobbits leave Dinodas aloneDinodas is grateful that you got the nosey hobbits to leave him alone.Talk to Dinodas Boffin on Honeymead Lane'I think I got the address of Angelica's new house wrong, ${PLAYER}! I would have sworn up and down that my mother told me the address was 9 Honeymead Lane, but it seems like my sister actually purchased the burrow at 8 Honeymead Lane! This is a disaster!

'Why, you ask? It's because I told the painterly Elf I met to paint THIS house, and not THAT one! Angelica is going to open our house-warming gift and see the mistake at once! When she unwraps that present and sees a painting of her neighbour's house... she'll be aghast! I haven't arranged for the BEST house-warming gift of all time... I have arranged for the WORST!

'You have to help me delay the opening of the presents, ${PLAYER}. March right in to Angelica's burrow and scatter my siblings to the winds. It shouldn't be that hard, because it happens more than you might expect! Just tell Griffo that there's a free lunch being offered somewhere, tell Esmeralda there's a very competitive dancing competition happening, and let Marigold know there could be goblins or something dangerous lurking just over the horizon. It's no use trying to get Camellia to run out... she always follows the rules. Even so, three of my siblings scattered is sure to delay the party long enough for us to figure out what to do! Hurry, hurry! There's no time to waste!''You have to help me delay the opening of the presents, ${PLAYER}. March right in to Angelica's burrow and scatter my siblings to the winds. It shouldn't be that hard, because it happens more than you might expect! Just tell Griffo that there's a free lunch being offered somewhere, tell Esmeralda there's a very competitive dancing competition happening, and let Marigold know there could be goblins or something dangerous lurking just over the horizon. That's sure to do it! Then we should have enough time to figure out what to do about this mistake. Hurry, hurry! There's no time to waste!''With so many siblings, it is rare for me to have a day just about me, ${PLAYER}! I am very pleased you are here to share it with me!''Do you think Angelica will set out some food pretty soon? It won't be much of a party without snacks!'

You tell Griffo that you aren't sure about the food situation here, but the markets of Yondershire are likely well-stocked by the farms of both the Westfarthing and the Northfarthing.

'Yes... there probably is quite a variety to be found...' Griffo muses.'This burrow is nice and cozy, or it will be after we help my sister finish decorating! You don't think she's done already, do you? Oh my.'

You ask Esmeralda if she has entered into any dancing competitions lately.

'No, not really. Back home they stopped holding them as often when I kept winning, you know. I considered wearing a disguise, but all the cloaks I tried on kept getting tangled up in my feet and it wasn't the same.

'But now that you mention it, I wonder if there are any dancing competitions up here in Yondershire? They wouldn't know me up here...'

Esmeralda trails away, deep in thought.You open your mouth to suggest that Marigold leave the party in search of adventure, but before you can say anything she interrupts you.

'I think there might be goblins up here,' she says, and you nod in agreement.

'Someone should do something...' she says, her eyes drifting to the door.'Hmm... I wonder...?''Hmm... let me think...''Yes, someone should do something...''Have the rest of my boys yet arrived, ${PLAYER}? Fosco and Berilac should have gotten here by now. I hope they did not get distracted by sights along the road... or that Berilac did not find a sunny place in which to nap!

'Do you think you could -''Angelica, what is wrong?''Mother, they've done it again! They've all run off, and this was supposed to be my big day, and now they're going to spoil it... like they always do!

'${PLAYER}! Can you go outside and see if they're going to come back? This was supposed to be a party for me, and now my siblings just run off with nary a good-bye or a single wishing well?'

Angelica stamps her foot on the floor.

'They are always doing this, ${PLAYER}. It's worse than herding cats... because that is a joy, and this is NOT!''${PLAYER}! Help!''Can you go outside and see if they're going to come back?''${PLAYER}! Help!''${PLAYER}! Help!''${PLAYER}! Help!''Thank you for that, ${PLAYER}. I always heard the Yonder-hobbits were peculiar and stand-offish, but these folk seem to have a thirst for news... especially when they can see a fellow is in distress and wants nothing to do with them!

'I do have some good news, however! I saw Berilac and Fosco coming up the road, and I told them the party had been delayed for a few hours and they should find somewhere to wait. That should buy the two of us enough time to resolve this difficult situation!'Certain postures will force enemies to fight with greater caution, limiting their ability to attack.Use Disable against an enemyHenepa Twistknot needs help with a culinary conundrum.Wolf-weed can be found along the wood's edge north of Tighfield.

