You should deliver your brews to each of the four taverns in Yondershire.Receive a token of gratitude from each tavern-keep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Delivered brews!Completed'Hullo there! Correct me if I'm wrong, but you seem to be the sort who enjoys a good brew! You're in good company here, friend! Now, let me ask you a question: have you ever fancied brewing up a good beer yourself? I find if you engage in the process you'll have a greater appreciation for every bottle you enjoy, and wouldn't that be quite a nice reward?

'I will be happy to teach you the way of it, for I am Bloda Hopblossom, the head brew-master of Nobottle, and mine is the finest beer in the Westfarthing... don't let anyone tell you differently! This may be one of the younger settlements in the Shire, as things are reckoned, but Nobottle is still centuries old by now... plenty of time for us to master brewing!

'Now listen to the many steps of brewing a beer of which you can be proud!''Good work! Now the barley needs to be malted. Look for the malting container here on the farm.''The barley is right here at the farm. Make sure to pick only the stalks that are ripe and ready!''You are getting there! I love your enthusiasm! Make sure to use that enthusiasm when mashing the barley! That is the next step!''Now my favourite step, boiling the brew! I like the aroma it brings to the air!''The next step is to ferment the brew. This is an important step, though not the most exciting.''While you are waiting for the brew to ferment, you should collect some empty bottles. There are a few on the farm but we also have an arrangement with The Fox and Fiddle to make use of their empty bottles as well. We will need them all for the next step!''Ah, you are back! I believe the brew has fermented enough. Now the brew is complete and we are ready to fill all these empty bottles with delicious beer!''Now that's a beer of which you can be proud! Delightful! Note the sense of accomplishment you now feel, and let it float your steps as you walk around Yondershire.'

Brewmaster Bloda Hopblossom grins at you.

'Aye, you'll have some walking to do, friend! You can't keep this brew all to yourself! You need to get it into the hands of our patrons! Visit every drinking establishment in Yondershire and bring the brew to our waiting customers... you'll get to see a lot of happy faces as you make these deliveries!''Hullo there! I am glad to see you! I was almost out of Nobottle brew! Have a drink to quench your thirst. You earned it!''Good, good! You can leave those beers with me. That drink is for you: a token of thanks for making this delivery.''Hullo! Ah, I see Brewmaster Bloda Hopblossom has put you to work. It's been awhile since she's had to make a delivery herself!

'Have a drink before you leave. No sense crafting a batch and not having a taste!''I was wondering when someone would come around. I am nearly out of drink! You saved this establishment, and no mistake! Please make sure to have a token of my gratitude before you leave.'You have learned a great deal about the brewing of Yondershire beer from Brewmaster Bloda Hopblossom and completed her deliveries to each of the grateful tavern-keeps. Revellers of Yondershire will no doubt sing your praises this evening, as they enjoy a mug or two of Nobottle's finest!Salga Greengrass has asked you to explore the village of Nobottle, then seek the nearby settlement of Long Cleeve.Nobottle can be found in eastern Yondershire.

Salga Greengrass has asked you to explore the village of Nobottle.Visit The Fox and Fiddle in NobottleFind Fredegar BolgerVisit Nobottle's village centreVisit Nobottle FarmThe village of Long Cleeve can be found north of Nobottle in Yondershire.

You should travel to Long Cleeve and talk to Rosalinda North-took.Talk to Rosalinda North-took in Long CleeveThe village of Long Cleeve can be found north of Nobottle in Yondershire.

Rosalinda North-took has asked you to explore the village of Long Cleeve.Visit the Long Cleeve gazeboVisit Long Cleeve's village centreVisit The Roaring Bull in Long Cleeve'Welcome to the village of Nobottle. I am Salga Greengrass of the Yonder-watch! We here at Nobottle welcome both friends and strangers alike, despite what you may have been told. Farmers, brewers, writers, and all sorts of folk reside here in Nobottle, and we are proud of them all. We even have some guests at the moment, such as that Fredegar Bolger, a hobbit from away on whom I have been keeping my eye! Perhaps you can do the same?

'While you are here, I recommend exploring our lively village and seeing the sights: the village centre, Nobottle Farm, and the Fox and Fiddle, the finest tavern in all of Yondershire! When you are done, feel free to make the journey to the village of Long Cleeve. Once there you can meet Rosa, the newest Reeve! She took over for her mother, you see, who was Reeve before....

'Ah, do not let me talk your ears off! Get to sightseeing!''Welcome to Yondershire! Make yourself at home here in Long Cleeve. There is much to do and see here. Have you any other business to discuss? What news have you from Nobottle?

'Salga Greengrass sent you to see the sights of Nobottle, and claimed they were the most interesting to be seen anywhere? Well, that claim has little substance! No tour is complete without seeing what Long Cleeve has on offer: the village centre, the lovely gazebo, and the Roaring Bull, the finest tavern in all of Yondershire!'A letter from a place bordering the Lone-lands and Bree-land arrived with a request for aid.The Forsaken Inn is along the Great East Road leading out of the South-gate in Bree. If you travel for a goodly while, you will find the inn on the north side of the road there.

Find The Forsaken Inn and speak with the patrons there.${CLASS},

There is a ramshackle inn on the borders of Bree-land and the Lone-lands that has suffered much in recent weeks. If you find yourself travelling along the roads east of Bree, mayhaps you could stop in and speak with the people in the inn.'I have run this inn for more years than I can count, and I can say without question that this is the most unrest ever I have seen. I have been trying to get word to Bree-land, but I have heard nothing. I am beginning to wonder if help will ever come.''Some come to these lands because they are shunned, others to simply pass through. Some folks, like me, are here at the behest of others with nothing more than profit on the mind.

'Which ilk are you?''My people have long lived in these lands. Never have we seen the evil that swells now in the heart of the land. I have said too much. You are an outsider, and until you earn our trust, there is little more I can say.''The larder is nearly empty, the blankets befouled, and we've covered the floor in straw to hide the damage. This place needs help, ${CLASS}.''So many travellers have been stranded here because of goblin-attacks. We could sure use some help.'Frothard Took has asked you to explore the hamlet of Tighfield, then seek the nearby settlement of Gamwich.Tighfield can be found in central Yondershire.

