Saeradan revealed that Orcs calling themselves Uruk-hai have come north to spy out the land and discover why their northern cousins are moving southward. He asked you to return quickly to Candaith and warn him of the danger.'The letter you discovered within the Bleakrift is also written in the Black Speech -- we need to know the orders contained within each of these letters. I am not a student of the tongue, but there is one of my kind who is.

'Out of Bree, north along the Greenway and east of the road, there is a cabin where Rangers gather. Saeradan often keeps vigil there; he is a friend of mine, and he may know enough of the cruel sigils to make sense of at least some portion of these orders.

'Travel to Bree-town. From the West-gate of Bree travel north along the Greenway until you spy the Ranger cabin among the trees east of the road. The cabin is quite near to Thornley's Work Site. Find Saeradan and ask him to translate these orders. May haste speed your errand!''You must not delay! Return to Candaith in the Lone-lands! If these Uruk-hai now occupy the ruins atop Amon Sûl, he is in grave danger.''Make haste! The quickest way to Saeradan's cabin is through the town of Bree. Once you have arrived at the town, follow the Greenway north and look for his cabin east of the road. Thornley's Work Site is very close by.''What brings you on such a long journey, ${PLAYER}? Candaith, you say? It is long since I have spoken to him. Let me see these letters he sends. The Black Speech is harsh and cruel, and it pains me some to have need of it. Still, this is why I have made it my study: to have knowledge of it at need.

'These letters bring ill tidings, ${PLAYER}. An Orc of the South-lands, Rigûl by name, has been tasked with learning what has caused a great movement of Orcs out of the North. Rigûl and his fellows call themselves "Uruk-hai" and are using the ruins atop Amon Sûl as a centre for their activities.

'Return to Candaith with all haste and warn him. He may be in more terrible danger than he is aware!''Dark is the news you bring from Saeradan. We must prepare. If Amon Sûl is threatened, then all of the Lone-lands are in danger.

