You have found Onyx Nethercot, an associate postman, at work inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. You should talk to Onyx Nethercot.Talk to Onyx Nethercot in the Quick Post in Michel DelvingThe ledger can be found on the counter inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.

At Postmaster Proudfoot's request, Onyx Nethercot has produced the Quick Post's ledger for your perusal. You should examine the ledger and compare its records against those of Postman Grubb's account.Examine the ledger in the Quick Post in Michel DelvingOnyx Nethercot can be found inside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.

After examining the Quick Post's ledger, you have discovered a troubling discrepancy between Postman Grubb's account and the records of the Quick Post of Michel Delving. You should speak to Onyx Nethercot.Talk to Onyx Nethercot in the Quick Post in Michel DelvingPostmaster Proudfoot can be found outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving.

After discovering a troubling discrepancy in the Quick Post's ledger, Onyx Nethercot has asked you to speak to Postmaster Proudfoot. You should speak to Postmaster Proudfoot.'I knew it, ${PLAYER}.

'If Postmaster Proudfoot had caught wind of this, he'd have already put a stop to it. After all the work he's put in to maintain the good reputation of the Quick Post, there's no chance he'd let some sort of conspiracy drag it into the mud. I have to inform the Postmaster at once!'

Postman Grubb takes out a blank piece of parchment and inks a quill. He begins writing, periodically glancing to his ledger.

'Now, ${PLAYER}, I hope you don't mind, but I need to ask you to deliver this to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving. In case something should happen to this letter, commit it to your memory that Nobottle has received thirty-three pieces of mail from the Hithershire in the past month. The Postmaster will have his own records on hand, and I would urge him to compare them against my own.'

Postman Grubb finishes writing, seals the letter, and hands it to you.

'I'm counting on you, ${PLAYER}. There is something afoot in the Shire!''Hullo there! What's this now?'

You hand Postman Grubb's letter to Postmaster Proudfoot. He unseals it, begins reading, and after a long moment, his eyes widen.

'Well, I don't like the sound of this at all. To my knowledge, the Quick Post has not altered our service to Nobottle, or Yondershire, for that matter! And we certainly would not make a habit of failing to make deliveries entirely!

'To his credit, Walto has provided a detailed record of the comings and goings at the Quick Post in Nobottle. One of my associates, Onyx Nethercot, has taken to maintaining the ledger, and I assure you, our records are current and accurate. A careful comparison between Walto's records and the ledger should tell us everything we need to know.

'You'll find Onyx behind the counter inside the Quick Post. Tell her to bring out the ledger and see if everything is in accord!''Oh, hullo! What brings you to the Quick Post today?'

You introduce yourself and tell Onyx that Postmaster Proudfoot has asked to see the ledger to compare it to Postman Grubb's records.

'Oh dear me, has some sort of mistake been made? Just a moment....'

Onyx leans down, produces a heavy ledger from under the counter, and examines its spine. After a moment, Onyx sets it down on the counter with a muffled thud.

'Here you go, ${PLAYER}. Take all the time you need!''A discrepancy?! I can't believe such a thing happened on my watch!'

Onyx pauses for a moment and composes herself.

'Fifty-eight pieces of mail sent out but only thirty-three actually making it to the Yondershire? That just doesn't make any sense. And besides, no one's ever lost that much on their routes—not since 'ere the days of Ned Harfoot!

'Here, ${PLAYER}, show the ledger to the Postmaster and see what he makes of it. If there's trouble with the Quick Post, it's not happening here in Michel Delving!''Ah, you've brought the ledger. Were you able to find what we were looking for?'

You tell Postmaster Proudfoot that you found clear discrepancies between the records of Michel Delving and Nobottle. He shakes his head solemnly.

'I'll have to thank Miss Nethercot for keeping such neat records. To be quite honest, that has never been a strength of mine. If it's all the same to you, I'd still like to examine it myself.'

You hand the ledger to Postmaster Proudfoot. He leaves through it, pausing in a few places and tracing along the page with his finger. After a short while, he snaps the ledger shut.

'It's as you said, ${PLAYER}. A discrepancy of twenty-five pieces of mail....'Edith Sweetrose believes that there may be a way to bring the old woman, Addie Wheatley, some solace. She believes that deep within the ruins of Ost Gorthad there may be treasure worthy of what the woman's sons were searching for, but it is only legend.The treasure is rumoured in the protection of a wight Lord at the deepest point of Ost Gorthad. Addie Wheatley is at the Dead Man's Perch in the Barrow-downs.

Edith Sweetrose wants you to search for the treasure of Cardolan to ease Addie Wheatley's pain over losing her two sons.'Addie deserves better than the news that you were forced to deliver her. I would ask, if you are willing, that you attempt to finish what her sons could not.

'Addie is poor... we took her along thinking that we could do a good service only to end up here in this tragedy. Her sons came here to try and change her fortune, only to meet their end. I am certain they were searching for the rumoured treasures of Cardolan.

'I have oft heard the tales myself of treasure held deep within the ruins of Ost Gorthad. If there is any truth to this, then the treasure lies at the deepest parts of Ost Gorthad in the hands of a terrifying creature.''It pains me deeply to see the hurt on Addie's face. Will you not help her by recovering the lost treasure so that her pain may be reduced?''What is this? The treasure that my sons sought? Given over in kindness by yourself and my guides? 

'I cannot... this, this is what my sons sought, a way to see that their mother would not die penniless. I shall keep this, keep it always in memory of their sacrifice.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Every creature has its weak spots -- eyes, throat, spleen, something -- you just need to figure out what they are.Use Counter DefenceEvery creature has its weak spots -- eyes, throat, spleen, something -- you just need to figure out what they are.Use Reveal WeaknessThere's an inn by the road from Ost Guruth where you can find food and shelter and perhaps employment.The Forsaken Inn can be found along the road to the west.

Go to the Forsaken Inn and talk to Candac Brightwood.'There is a place where you can find shelter for the night. The innkeeper is an old man now, and the locals are a stern and morose lot, but the beds are warm, and the wine is cold. 

'Travel west along the east-west road that brought you here. The Forsaken Inn is by that road.

'I know a man called Candac who might be found at the Inn. If you happen to go there, bid him greetings from Frideric.''Frideric is in good health, then? I am glad to hear that. He and his kin have been through much turmoil in recent months.''If you find yourself at The Forsaken Inn, pass on my greetings to Candac.'Defeat many pale trappers in Skirmishes.
