You should let Diamond know about the Men you defeated.Talk to Adamanda'I am glad that my daughter is starting to take things more seriously. Perhaps I have your influence to thank for that, along with my words to her earlier, of course.

'Since I am assuming you are out doing her work for her and will see her again soon, I bid you take this report to her. It came to me by way of our local Bounders, and its contents trouble me. Please ask my daughter to look into the situation.''A report from the Bounders? Do give it here and let's see what they have found.'

She reads over the report, her brow furrowing.

'This is not good. The report states that strange Men have been seen along the walls that border our lands. We should go and have a look for ourselves and see what is going on. Why, with your help we can cover twice as much ground! Meet me at the wall west of Tighfield.''Welcome back! How did you do?'

You tell her about the bandits.

'What! I should have picked that way instead. All I found was a suspicious lump of cloth. Turned out to be the old farmer's cloak. He was happy to have it back, at least.

'Well, my friend. We have done many a brave thing together today! Thank you for all of your help, and especially for helping me refocus my efforts for Yondershire. I will not be Reeve for some time, but all of today's wandering around showed me how much help I can be to townsfolk. Perhaps one day I will wander outside of the wall and along the dusty roads, but for now, there is plenty for me to do here.

'Thank you again, my friend!''You head that way and I'll head this way. Let us meet back here once we have scouted the wall.'In the heat of battle, pain is to be ignored. You can lick your wounds when your foe has fallen.Use Ignore the PainThere are many different kinds of poison in Middle-earth. Knowing how to cure them is a life long task.Use Purge PoisonAgatha Greendale told you of several fell creatures which haunt the barrows of Haudh Iarchith, Gwantham, Goetham, and Haudh Nogbenn.Haudh Iarchith, Gwantham, Goetham, and Haudh Nogbenn are located in the southern Barrow-downs.

