Saeloril is near Nímbarth in Cardolan.Return to Saeloril'The missive you recovered is troubling. The Orcs in Tharbad have noticed Stonecrop's group and are calling for reinforcements. They mean to attack soon! I think we can use this to our advantage. Here's where you come in. Again.

'I have rewritten the orders to say that we are not a threat and to ignore our presence. A few of the other missives now have wording that I am sure will stir chaos and confusion, with the goal of having those at Nímbarth start to question the Orcs at Tharbad.

'It won’t hold them off for long, but possibly long enough for us to plan our next moves! Go to Nímbarth and plant these orders where someone in charge may discover them.''You return! Thank you for what you have done here. You have given the people of Cardolan more of a fighting chance, to be sure!'Remaining balanced in combat is key.Use the skill Re-centre.Use the skill Re-centre.The runed doors beneath the Forsaken Inn display a random assortment of riddles. Are you clever enough to solve them all?You or a member of your party must solve each riddle inscription at least once.Solve riddle inscription 01Solve riddle inscription 02Solve riddle inscription 03Solve riddle inscription 04Solve riddle inscription 05Solve riddle inscription 06Solve riddle inscription 07Solve riddle inscription 08Solve riddle inscription 09Solve riddle inscription 10Solve riddle inscription 11Solve riddle inscription 12Solve riddle inscription 13Solve riddle inscription 14Solve riddle inscription 15Solve riddle inscription 16Solve riddle inscription 17Solve riddle inscription 18Solve riddle inscription 19Solve riddle inscription 20Solve riddle inscription 21Solve riddle inscription 22Solve riddle inscription 23Solve riddle inscription 24Solve riddle inscription 25Solve riddle inscription 26Solve riddle inscription 27Solve riddle inscription 28Solve riddle inscription 29Solve riddle inscription 30Solve riddle inscription 31Solve riddle inscription 32Solve riddle inscription 33Solve riddle inscription 34Solve riddle inscription 35Solve riddle inscription 36Solve riddle inscription 37Solve riddle inscription 38Solve riddle inscription 39Solve riddle inscription 40Solve riddle inscription 41Solve riddle inscription 42Solve riddle inscription 43Solve riddle inscription 44Solve riddle inscription 45Solve riddle inscription 46Solve riddle inscription 47Solve riddle inscription 48Solve riddle inscription 49Solve riddle inscription 50Solve riddle inscription 51Solve riddle inscription 52Solve riddle inscription 53Solve riddle inscription 54Solve riddle inscription 55Solve riddle inscription 56Solve riddle inscription 57Solve riddle inscription 58Solve riddle inscription 59Solve riddle inscription 60Solve riddle inscription 61Solve riddle inscription 62Solve riddle inscription 63Solve riddle inscription 64Solve riddle inscription 65Solve riddle inscription 66Solve riddle inscription 67Solve riddle inscription 68Solve riddle inscription 69Solve riddle inscription 70Solve riddle inscription 71Solve riddle inscription 72Solve riddle inscription 73Solve riddle inscription 74Solve riddle inscription 75Solve riddle inscription 76Solve riddle inscription 77Solve riddle inscription 78Solve riddle inscription 79Solve riddle inscription 80Solve riddle inscription 81Solve riddle inscription 82Solve riddle inscription 83Having started at an advanced level, you are being asked to assist Candaith in Weathertop. Ride there via Saeradan's horse and learn the secrets of Middle-earth.To earn this deed, you must start a level 20 character and complete the horse-ride to Weathertop.Enter the world as a level 20 characterTo earn this deed, you must start a level 20 character and complete the horse-ride to Weathertop.Odd-looking folk have been riding between Tharbad and Nímbarth. Getting your hands on their correspondences could help those who are trying to settle peacefully in the area.Burl Stonecrop has asked you locate his missing scout Saeloril, near Nímbarth.

Nímbarth is located in south-east Cardolan.Search for SaelorilSaeloril has asked you to defeat riders from Nímbarth and bring back the orders they are carrying.

Riders can be found in Nímbarth.Collect orders from ridersYou have recovered orders destined for Tharbad from the riders of Nímbarth! You should bring the orders they were carrying to Saeloril.

Saeloril is near Nímbarth, in southern Cardolan.'I had heard that Cardolan was a wilder land than Bree, but to see it for myself has been eye opening. To the north lie the ruins of Nímbarth. Judging by the walls that are left, it seems to have once been a fortress. Now, however, a rank-looking lot of Men, though I hesitate to call them such, occupies the ruins.

'One of our group, Saeloril, headed that way some hours ago to scout the situation. That she has yet to return is causing me some concern. If you head up to Nímbarth, please find Saeloril. I do not like the look of the men that have taken up in those ruins.''Hold! Stay where you are!

'Hmm, you do not seem to be like the men I have seen occupying Nímbarth. Burl sent you, did he? I am indeed Saeloril. I have not yet returned because I have been seeing riders coming and going from the fortress at all hours. They must be the means by which orders are delivered to the Orcs in Tharbad.

'You look like you can handle yourself! If you come across one of these riders, take them down and bring me any correspondences you find.''Found some, did you? Well then, let's have 'em here.'Investigating the Old Forest may require the help of Marigold Boffin, a bold adventurer.Hob Hayward has asked you to find Marigold Boffin before venturing into the Old Forest.

You can find her just outside of Newbury, by the river's shore.Talk to MarigoldMarigold has offered to guide you through the forest to investigate what has been agitating the wildlife.

You should let her know when you're ready to depart.Talk to MarigoldMarigold has taken you to see Tom Bombadil, who may know more about the situation in the forest.

Tom can be found in and around his house.Talk to Tom Bombadil'Something strange is at work here, no doubt about it. It won't be easy for us Bounders to get to the bottom of this; our numbers are stretched thin enough as it is. If you're able to investigate, we'd welcome the help.

'Before you go, talk to Marigold Boffin. I'd wager she's just outside of Newbury, by the river's shore. She seems to know the forest more than most folk around here.''So the Bounders need our help? Well, I reckon I know where to start our search!

'I saw the strangest creatures mucking about in the forest. They were very tall -- tree-like, almost, but not quite. Tough and fierce-looking, too. All the animals stayed away from them. Whatever those tree-creatures are up to, it can't be good.

'I'll show you where I saw them. Let me know when you're ready!''At least we won't be spending another second stuck in Buckland!'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'A fellow tall, a cruel sword, the wicked Dead a-calling? By my boots, both I've spied close by Old Man Willow! A scar, a blight on forest green: the trolls, they spread their mischief there.

'But stay awhile! To other paths you may turn and yet be safe. Old Tom must be a-going, to gather lilies for his Goldberry.'Postman Mapledore of Gamwich has asked you to deliver a satchel to Tighfield.Postman Mapledore can be found in Gamwich, in Yondershire.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Hartclover in Tighfield as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits or those surly Bounders interfere with your duty!Collect the satchel from Postman Mapledore's table<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid the Chief's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid Lotho's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid nosey hobbits</rgb>'Hullo, do you have some time to spare today?

'If you would lend me a hand, I need to have this satchel of mail delivered to Tighfield as soon as possible. Follow the road south as it bends east and you'll pass through Tighfield. Postman Hartclover ought to be at the Quick Post just past the Elbow's Bend. A fine tavern, indeed, but best enjoyed when not carrying mail for the Quick Post!

'When you're ready, the satchel is on the table right over there. For your sake, don't get caught up in chatter with the folk around Tighfield. Rumours are flying right now that there's some surly Bounders about out of Hithershire, but I don't think there's any truth to it.

'Oh, and tell Postman Hartclover that I received his note and have spoken to the involved parties about shipping cuts of meat in standard envelopes. It will not happen again.

'Do not let me keep you! The Quick Post must carry on!''The satchel for Tighfield is over there on the table. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty!

'Oh, and don't let the satchel get wet. It would be easy enough to have a new one made here in Gamwich, but there's no doubt that the Postmaster would hear about it!'Postman North-took of Long Cleeve has asked you to deliver a satchel to Nobottle.Postman North-took can be found in Long Cleeve, in Yondershire.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Grubb in Nobottle as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits or those surly Bounders interfere with your duty!Collect the satchel from Postman North-took's table<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid the Chief's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid Lotho's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid nosey hobbits</rgb>'If you're of a mind to help the Quick Post, I need to get a satchel of mail to Nobottle as soon as possible. If you follow the road south, you'll end up in Nobottle—sooner or later anyway. Postman Grubb can be found outside the Quick Post just up the hillside off the west side of the road.

'Keep your wits about you in Nobottle. There's a lot of folk there, and they've a love for gossip. And to their minds, it is vital that a busy postman hears every last bit of it! Fine folk, I'm sure, but a bit talkative for my taste.

'Oh, and before you go, I overheard a Bounder from Hithershire making trouble at the arch the other day. Some business about wanting to see Reeve Rosa without an invitation. Don't tell anyone I said this, but you ought to keep your distance from the Bounders if you don't recognize them.

'Anyway, the satchel's right over on the table. Deliver it to Nobottle as quickly as you can!''The satchel for Nobottle is right over there on the table. Let no nosey hobbits or those surly Bounders out of Hithershire interfere with your duty!

'Oh, and don't let the satchel get wet. I'll have to use it again, after all!'Postman Grubb of Nobottle has asked you to deliver a satchel to Long Cleeve.Postman Grubb can be found in Nobottle, in Yondershire.

Deliver the satchel to Postman North-took in Long Cleeve as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits or those surly Bounders interfere with your duty!Collect the satchel from Postman Grubb's table<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid the Chief's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid Lotho's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid nosey hobbits</rgb>'For years now, I have done my duty as a postman to the best of my ability, but as of late, I have found it quite overwhelming!

'It pains me to ask, but would you help me to handle this workload? I've many deliveries to make today, and I do not know if I can finish them all before sundown. And what would folk think of the Quick Post then?

'If you'd help me to get some of this mail delivered to Long Cleeve, I will see to it that you are properly compensated. Provided, of course, that the task is done to the standards of the Quick Post: No stopping to chat with nosey folk, and no swimming—at least not while you're holding one of my satchels! Also, I'm told that some queer Bounders have been coming out of Hithershire and bothering our folk. They seem an unsavoury lot, and if I were you, I'd avoid them. The Mayor or the First Shirriff ought to have a word with them, I think. Nothing doing with attitudes like that!

'If you've never been to Long Cleeve, all you need to do is follow the road to the north. Once you pass under the stone arch into Long Cleeve, you'll find Postman North-took at the Quick Post to the east of the road—you can't miss him! Best get to it!''The satchel for Long Cleeve is over there on the table. Remember that so long as you are carrying it, you are a representative of the Quick Post!Postman Grubb of Nobottle has asked you to deliver a satchel to Tighfield.Postman Grubb can be found in Nobottle, in Yondershire.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Hartclover in Tighfield as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits or those surly Bounders interfere with your duty!Collect the satchel from next to Postman Grubb<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid the Chief's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid Lotho's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid nosey hobbits</rgb>'Oh, one more thing....

'If you'd also help me to get a satchel of this mail delivered to Postman Hartclover in Tighfield, I will see to it that you are properly compensated. If you've never been to Tighfield, simply follow the road west and you'll pass through the centre of the village. Postman Hartclover is at the Quick Post just along the road in Tighfield. If you find yourself at the Elbow's Bend, you've gone too far.

'Don't delay, and avoid nosey hobbits! And do inform Postman Hartclover that if another hobbit attempts to pay their postage with hemp, I will be issuing a complaint to the Postmaster!''The satchel for Tighfield is over there on the table. Let no nosey hobbits interfere with your duty!'Postman Hartclover of Tighfield has asked you to deliver a satchel to Gamwich.Postman Hartclover can be found in Tighfield, in Yondershire.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Mapledore in Gamwich as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits or those surly Bounders interfere with your duty!Collect the satchel from Postman Hartclover's table<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid the Chief's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid Lotho's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid nosey hobbits</rgb>'As I said, I have many deliveries from Gamwich to manage today, and though it will only make more work for me, I do need someone to run the route to Gamwich on behalf of the Quick Post.

'If you would be willing to ease my workload, I need a satchel of mail to be delivered to Gamwich. If you follow the road west out of Tighfield and continue north at the fork, you'll find your way to Gamwich. You'll find Postman Mapledore at the Quick Post in Gamwich. It's not far into the village, and the Postman keeps a stable near the Quick Post, so that ought to catch your eye!

'And keep a look-out for nosey hobbits! You're best off avoiding them if you can—they make our routes take three times as long as they ought to!''The satchel for Gamwich is over there on the table. Let no nosey hobbits or those rumoured Bounders out of Hithershire interfere with your duty!

'Oh, and don't let the satchel get wet!'Postman Hartclover of Tighfield has asked you to deliver a satchel to Nobottle.Postman Hartclover can be found in Tighfield, in Yondershire.

Deliver the satchel to Postman Grubb in Nobottle as quickly as possible. Let no nosey hobbits or those surly Bounders interfere with your duty!Collect the satchel from Postman Hartclover's table<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid the Chief's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid Lotho's Bounders</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Avoid nosey hobbits</rgb>'Hullo there, would you care to lend the Quick Post a hand? You look a trustworthy sort, and to be honest, I've not many options left.

'I have many deliveries from Gamwich to manage today, and I'll suspect it'll be near sundown before I can even begin to run my usual routes.

'If you would help me, I need to get a satchel of mail to Nobottle. Just follow the road east, and you're bound to find your way to Nobottle. You'll find Postman Grubb at the Quick Post in Nobottle, just up the hillside off the west side of the road. If you ask me, the Postman can be a bit of a prissy fellow, but he means well.

'Keep to the route and avoid any nosey hobbits along the way. If you don't spot them first, they'll be sure to spot you!

'I've also heard tell that there's some mean-spirited Bounders about in Yondershire, but I don't know about that. Seems like just a rumour to me!''The satchel for Nobottle is over there on the table. Let no nosey hobbits or those rumoured Bounders out of Hithershire interfere with your duty!

