You should bring the golf clubs to Frothard Took.'I am a little embarrassed, ${PLAYER}, but perhaps you can help me with something?

'I have always kept my Bounder supplies within a small shed, and never thought I needed to worry that someone might break in... but that very thing has happened! And I know the identities of the culprits!'

Frothard turns a bright pink.

'It's shrews, ${PLAYER}. They burrowed right under the wall of my shed and made a terrible mess. Worse still, they ran off with an important map of mine, and they have likely torn it all to pieces by now! Can you find all the pieces of the map and return them to me so I can put it back together?''You found every scrap of the map! Wonderful!

'You see, this map holds the location of a treasure that I buried for safekeeping many years ago! It was so many years ago that I have, er, rather forgotten what the treasure was, but with the map restored I will be able to dig it up and find out!

'It had to be something valuable... why else would I have drawn a map? Follow the map and dig up the treasure, ${PLAYER}! I am very curious to learn what I thought to hide!''Ah! Of course! I remember now!

'I buried my golf clubs to keep them safe while Foxden Heath was being tidied up and restored so it could serve as a golfing course once again!'

You ask why he buried the clubs instead of keeping them safe in his shed, and he laughs.

'Are you quite mad? I can't keep them in there: the shrews are always getting into that shed!'

'Hobbits,' you think to yourself.Aggressive sickle-flies who love to feast upon valuable reeds are plaguing the ponds near Herne.Aerona has asked you to reduce the number of sickle-flies buzzing about the ponds and waterways east of Herne.

Herne is in western Cardolan.Defeat reed-munching sickle-flies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Aerona know that fewer sickle-flies will trouble the reeds of the ponds near Herne.

Aerona is in Herne.Return to Aerona'Well met! I am Aerona, basket weaver of Herne. If you are looking to make some coin, I am looking for some help. East of Herne are various bodies of water from which I often go to gather reeds with which to make my baskets. Of late, the reeds have been decimated by sickle-flies! Well, by their larva...'

She shudders saying the word.

