You should return to Broderic Willowmeade with news of your success.Talk to Broderic Willowmeade in Bree'Deep within Haudh Methernil, the Barrow of Ringdor, and the Barrow of Taradan, there are said to be three creatures that haunt its depths. The first creature is a horrible spider named Gwigon. The second is a darkwater by the name of Umnen. Lastly is the kergrim named Marrow.

'If you are able to defeat one of these creatures, return to me, and I will spread word of your valour to all of the people of Bree-town.

'Haudh Methernil, the Barrow of Ringdor, and the Barrow of Taradan are scattered across the northern Barrow-downs.''Hunt down the evil things which dwell within Haudh Methernil, the Barrow of Ringdor, and the Barrow of Taradan and lay them to rest.''You have done us all a great service by your deeds... your name will be spoken fondly throughout Bree.

'It will take me some time to spread word of your deeds. If you travel again to Haudh Methernil, The Barrow of Ringdor, The Barrow of Taradan, Hautham, and Haudh Taenthod, seek me out, as I may have another task for you to accomplish.'Many would call Guardians fatalistic. Perhaps they should try holding a bridge alone against countless Orcs?Use Guardian's PledgeMany would call Guardians fatalistic. Perhaps they should try holding a bridge alone against countless Orcs?Use Guardian's Pledge, Protection, or Protection by the SwordOddvarr's pack was recovered, but he is no better off. The notes he wrote down are missing, and he suspects that some Orcs made off with them.Tarkrîp Orcs from around Cirith Nûr, west to north-west of Oddvarr in the North Bree-fields, have stolen Oddvarr's precious notes. Oddvarr can be found south-east of Hengstacer Farm near the ruins.

Oddvarr's notes are missing, and he suspects the Tarkrîp Orcs ran off with them. One of the Orcs must have them, if you can only find which one.'This is not good! In fact, it is downright terrible! All my work... gone! Just like that, quick as you please. Drat and double-drat!

'My notes are missing, and I'm absolutely certain that I placed them in my pack. There was a band of Tarkrîp Orcs from around Cirith Nûr, west to north-west of here in the North Bree-fields, come sniffing around the ruins. That's why I left my pack behind in such a hurry.

'I'm in no shape to take on Orcs. I'm an explorer, not a warrior. Those notes mean everything to me. Could you please find them and return them to me?''Orcs! I hate Orcs. Why would they run off with my notes like that? I'll tell you why... just to get my beard in a snarl, I would say!

'Now that my notes are safe, I can continue my research. Lofar will be pleased to know that my work continues unabated.'Burl Stonecrop's expedition to Tharbad has been thwarted by the Orcs who have made the ruins their home.Burl Stonecrop has asked you retrieve stolen supplies from the Orcs in Tharbad.

Tharbad is in southern Cardolan.Recover stolen supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the recovered supplies to Burl Stonecrop.

Burl is near Tharbad, in southern Cardolan.'Greetings, fellow traveller. My name is Burl Stonecrop. My companions and I have been tasked with travelling the Greenway and investigating whether or not there would be any benefit in rebuilding a settlement here in Cardolan.

'Predictably, on our first night here at Tharbad we were attacked! The ruins are full of vicious Orcs who stole our supplies before we could fend them off. We will probably be heading back up to Bree, but without our supplies, the trip home is impossible. However, you look like someone who could stand up to those Orcs! If you retrieve our supplies, I will compensate you!''You have done it! I have higher hopes now for our endeavours.'Merruth has put his plan with the boar meat into action, with troubling results!Merruth has asked you to talk to his sister, Maeriel, to see what can be done about the diseased Wargs.

Maeriel is in Sedgemead, in Cardolan.Talk to MaerielMerruth's sister, Maeriel, has instructed you to defeat the diseased Wargs before their illness can spread to anything else.

Diseased Wargs can be found in Sedgemead.Defeat diseased wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Maeriel know you have defeated many of the diseased Wargs.

Maeriel is in Sedgemead, in Cardolan.Talk to Maeriel'Well, it seems like the plan did not go quite as planned. That is – we  put a good dent into the boar population. So that went well! But, well... you see, then I may have used the meat you brought me to poison the nearby Wargs.

'The poisoned meat did weaken the Wargs with the illness, just as planned! However, uhm, it has come to my attention that the Wargs are made of a bit sterner stuff and the illness is not quite having the desired effect.

'While it has slowed the ghastly things down a bit, the Wargs are not succumbing as expected. If you could see your way to helping me again, talk to my sister Maeriel. She always knows what to do and is more than happy to tell you to do it! She will certainly have a plan. I see her across the water a ways, but I am loath to confess what I have done. She is so mean! That is, she probably will not be mean to you. Probably.''Thank you, stranger. I am sorry you had to clean up my brother's mess. Perhaps this will help him learn not to try to cut corners.''Careful, stranger. Some fool placed diseased meat here.'

As you tell her of Merruth's plan, her face grows more and more troubled.

'My brother's laziness has reached a new bound. The Wargs are sick, as he intended. However, fast though the illness has spread to them, it is not killing them as quickly. The creatures are now spreading the disease to the wildlife around them.

'If you come across any diseased Wargs, put them down. They are a danger to us and to all those around them!'You have accompanied the Rangers Saeradan and Amlan to confront the witch Gwyllion, called the Old Woman of the Mountain by the Dunlending locals, at her home atop Methedras, a great mountain overlooking the vale of Nan Curunír and Isengard.Saeradan waits to speak with you on the path leading up Methedras.Talk to SaeradanTake control of the gate to the outer courtyard of Gwyllion's homestead.Capture the outer courtyard gateWith the gate to the outer courtyard in your control, it is now time to break the enemy's hold on the outer courtyard and win through to the gate to the inner courtyard and Gwyllion's hut.Capture the inner courtyard gateThe gate to the inner courtyard gate has been secured. Now the inner courtyard and Gwyllion's hut beyond may be assaulted.Capture Gwyllion's hutThe courtyard has fallen. Now all that remains is to defeat the leader of the assault and break the siege.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: The Boar-clan mystics will counter the buffs Gwyllion has placed on her servants, but will not fight.</rgb>Defeat Gwyllion and Echrud at the entrance to Gwyllion's hut and claim the final control pointSpeak with Saeradan.Talk to Saeradan'In the Windfells of Enedwaith, we first encountered the hag Gwyllion. There she was using her evil powers to summon fell spirits in the forms of druggavar, cuthraul, and cûn annûn to build an army of ancient evil to the aid of Saruman. Then in the Gravenwood below, we hindered her efforts to create a host of wights.

'Long have we hounded this Old Woman of the Mountain, and now we have her cornered. It is our duty to remain here and try to hinder her efforts. If she should succeed, all manner of foul demons shall come to the aid of Saruman against Rohan.

'The Boar-clan of Dunland understands that this is not to the benefit of their people and have sent mystics to try and counter the Old Woman's spells should she try to turn them against us.

'${PLAYER}, go forward and claim the gate to the outer courtyard of her abode. Amlan and I will stay with the Boar-clan mystics until the point is secure. Go now, and may the Valar protect you!''I confess I had not even imagined that the Old Woman of the Mountain had power enough to summon such a horde of devils to her aid. It is well that she has been defeated.

'Well done, ${PLAYER}, my friend through many dangers.''I fear this struggle is not over, ${PLAYER}. We have defeated Gwyllion here, but who knows what other allies Saruman may still have?

'Let us return to our camp.'The dwelling place of Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, lies atop Methedras, overlooking Isengard. The witch has allied herself with Saruman the White and seeks to bring a great army of ancient evil down upon the Rohirrim.Defeat all of Gwyllion's lieutenants in the Storm on Methedras Skirmish.Defeat RhodriDefeat BudantDefeat Maru BreninDefeat GarzogDefeat CaurDefeat HelechúlDefeat NúrvorDefeat DomborDefeat DaeharnYou have only one shot when ambushing an opponent -- make it count!Strike from ShadowsLand Critical blows from hiding with skills that benefit from stealthYou have only one shot when ambushing an opponent -- make it count!Strike from ShadowsLand Critical blows with skills that benefit from stealthLet loose the cry of war and see your enemy's resolve erode.Strike with War-cryLet loose the cry of war and see your enemy's resolve erode.Strike with War-cryUnfortunately, the old tales are filled with incidents of foolhardy minstrels finding themselves riddled with arrows as they bravely sing their last upon the field of battle.Use Song of SoothingUnfortunately, the old tales are filled with incidents of foolhardy minstrels finding themselves riddled with arrows as they bravely sing their last upon the field of battle.Use Anthem of ProwessMany Lore-masters choose to forsake the garish magics of thunderous fire and glamour, for they may bring the wrath of the Enemy quickly upon them.Use Blinding Flash against your enemiesMany Lore-masters choose to forsake the garish magics of thunderous fire and glamour, for they may bring the wrath of the Enemy quickly upon them.Use Blinding Flash against your enemiesTad Leafcutter has asked for adventurers throughout Bree to come and speak with him.Tad Leafcutter can be found outside the Bree Hunting Lodge west of the South-gate of Bree.

Tad Leafcutter has asked that adventurers in Bree come and speak with him.'Hello there. You look like just the type Tad has been looking for. Young Leafcutter has been seeking adventurers throughout Bree and has asked me to send them his way when I see them.

'If you would, go and visit Tad Leafcutter. He should be west of the South-gate here in Bree.  Make sure you tell him I sent you; I don't get paid if they don't get sent by me.''Thomas Thistlewool sent you? Yes, yes, I will make sure he receives his coin, I have something much more important to discuss with you.'Maeriel needs word of the diseased boars and aggressive Wargs brought to her fellow Ranger.Maeriel has asked you to talk to her fellow Ranger, Calargyl about what you all saw and did here in Sedgemead.

Calargyl is near Amon Firn, in north-eastern Cardolan.Talk to Calargyl'You have shown yourself to be far more dependable than my brother, so I wonder if I can entrust you with another task. I was meant to meet with my fellow Ranger, Calargyl, at Amon Firn, but I daren't leave Merruth unattended.

'Would you bring Calargyl word of what we saw here? The diseased boars and the encroaching Warg presence is unsettling. Some darkness has swept through Cardolan, I am sure of it.''Greetings! I am indeed Calargyl. So, Maeriel was left once more to clean up her brother's mess? I am not surprised by that, but the rest of the news you bring is quite troubling. I have myself witnessed strange things indeed.'Defeat many Tempests of Flame in Skirmishes.
This deed will only be advanced by Lieutenants that do not appear grey to your character, they must be around the same level as you are.Defeat Tempests of Flame in SkirmishesDefeat many Tempests of Flame in Skirmishes.
This deed will only be advanced by Lieutenants that do not appear grey to your character, they must be around the same level as you are.Defeat Tempests of Flame in SkirmishesWingard Puddifoot needs help gathering ingredients.Gather some herbs along the river east of Gamwich. Bring them to Wingard Puddifoot back in town.Collect Gamwich herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wingard Puddifoot can be found back in Gamwich.

Return to Wingard Puddifoot.Wingard is scanning the texts you recovered when she suddenly bursts into off-key song and clumsy dance.

'O-Oh! Assistant! You're still here!

...


'You didn't see or hear any of that.

...

'Ahem.

'Assistant! I have made the most incredible finding. A shrub that grows in this area was actually used as a culinary herb. 
I will gather a small amount on my way back to Gamwich and make some test dishes. I would ask you to pick a greater amount and bring them to me in Gamwich.'Wingard accepts the bundle of herbs from you, plucks one from the bundle, and rubs the leaf between her thumb and forefinger. The aroma that seizes your attention is bitter and vegetal, but it quickly gives way to a profound sweetness backed by a gentle peppery note. And just as quickly, the scent is gone.

'The test dishes I made were abject failures. Just horrid and... and gunky, if that's even a word. But the aroma is so arresting isn't it? Perhaps this wasn't used in the food itself, but as an aroma to appreciate before or after the meal. Maybe there are techniques that can properly draw out this herb's flavour.'

Wingard grips the bundle of herbs the way a child grips a new toy.

'Assistant, I am sad to say that this is the end of our partnership. At least for now. If my research yields a famous new dish, I'll be sure to credit you for your contribution. Perhaps I'll find a way to work your name into the name of the dish.

'How did you spell your name again? ${PLAYER}?

'Hmm.... In any case, thank you again, and I hope to see you around.'Believing Erfith's claim that the goblins were sent to hunt fleeing Dourhands, Athal has asked you to confront and defeat the leader of the goblins at Lhúngobel.Lhúngobel can be found along the River Lune in the north-western reaches of Yondershire.

Athal has asked you to travel to Lhúngobel to confront and defeat whichever goblin is now leading them. You should search for some sign of the goblins' leader at Lhúngobel.Find some sign of the goblins' leader at LhúngobelA banner of Angmar can be found in the ruins of Lhúngobel in the north-western reaches of Yondershire.

You have discovered a crude banner of Angmar among the goblins at Lhúngobel. You should examine the banner and continue your search for the goblins' leader at Lhúngobel.Examine the banner of AngmarAthal can be found on a hill just off the road near the border of Ered Luin in Yondershire.

You have defeated the goblins' leader, Faltúrz, but a plot between Angmar and the Dourhands loyal to Skorgrím has been revealed. You should talk to Athal.Talk to Athal'Ah, I see you have already met my companion. I am Athal and I am at your service!

'You see, Avorthal and I were mistaken. This Dourhand, Erfith, tells me that he and his kin fled Ered Luin under the cover of night a few days ago. If the goblins have any ill intentions for the Shire, it appears that is secondary to their true task: to capture and retrieve deserters. But retrieve them and bring them where? The Dourhands were routed at Rath Teraig, and Ered Luin has not been troubled by their kind in recent days. It does not sit well with me!

'I would ask that you travel to Lhúngobel. If you can find whoever leads these goblins, defeat them and learn what you can of their plans!''A banner of Angmar? I do not like the sound of that, ${PLAYER}. That old kingdom fell long ago... and for good reason!

'And you say that the goblins' leader spoke of Sarnúr? I know of it. It was once a city of the Dourhands, but it has laid abandoned for many years. If the Dourhands who still remain loyal to Skorgrím have taken refuge in its halls, it is possible they still plot against the Elves and dwarves of Ered Luin.

'If it were not for Erfith, I doubt we would have known until it was too late. Perhaps there are still some among his kin who have not lost their sense of honour!

'I thank you for your aid, ${PLAYER}. It seems we shall have to remain vigilant in the days to come!'Being light on your feet means better positioning for both attack and defence.Use Quick Feint.Melynis has completed her deciphering of the ancient scroll you found in the base of the statue of Luilloth.Melynis has given the deciphered scroll to Rhiangar, who is waiting to speak with you.

Rhiangar is among the circled caravans, in northern Cardolan.Talk to RhiangarRhiangar has suggested that you read the deciphered scroll which is on a bench next to her in the caravan south of Andrath. You should talk to Rhiangar when you are done.Read the deciphered scrollRhiangar is waiting to speak with you among the circled caravans, in northern Cardolan.Talk to Rhiangar'Hullo, hullo! What a fascinating scroll you and Rhiangar brought me. This Luilloth was an incredible person! A princess who fought for her people and who seems to have been much loved. Her tale reads like a spook story one might tell around a fire late at night, though. Gave me the shivers straight through and I was standing in the sun!

'In any case, I wrote out what the scroll says and gave it to Rhiangar. She is waiting to talk to you. Oh, and ${PLAYER} - if you do decide to follow in Luilloth's footsteps, be careful.''Oh, ${PLAYER}. We have found something incredible! The scroll tells of Luilloth's final days. Such a tragic story, too. My heart is nearly broken reading of her adventures and doom.

'You can read what Melynis deciphered, but here is the long and short of it - Luilloth and her family were fighting against risen spirits too, just as I had expected. Sadly, she lost her son and her husband to the horrors that rose up across Cardolan. She went to the forest nearby to seek guidance from an old woman who lived among its trees! I do not know what guidance she got, because Luilloth vanished soon afterwards. However, her people revered her as a hero, because whatever happened to her - the spirits went back to their graves and troubled Cardolan no more.

'Go on ahead and read the deciphered scroll for yourself, if you like. Then we shall speak of what I think must be done next.'The scroll is a testament to Princess-regent Luilloth of Dol Ernil, and praises her character and deeds:

"In those days, a fog rolled over the land, from whence emerged a plague of the Dead who slew all before them. Most fearsome of these was a wraith-like figure known as Hithrengor, the Grey Fear, who terrorized Dol Ernil. Luilloth brought her young son Ostir to Fornost for his protection while her husband, Prince Ostecthel, hunted down the source of the evil.

Prince Ostecthel strode into the fog a mighty warrior in his prime... only to later stumble out looking as though he had aged decades. With gasping words he revealed that the evil had been banished and that the land was safe once more. Aggrieved but proud, Luilloth returned and served as princess-regent until Ostir came of age. The people loved her, for she was good and kind, and ruled wisely.

But Ostecthel's words were soon proven wrong! The great evil was not gone, for it returned in Cardolan's darkest hour. Called away to the defence of Amon Sûl, Prince Ostir rode north with much of his household. In his absence, the Grey Fear attacked once more, and Ostir returned to find Dol Ernil merely a ruined shell, its people scattered or slaughtered, and Luilloth nowhere to be found.

"Once more, the Dead rose and ravaged Cardolan, while Ostir and his few remaining knights fell back, retreating north. Is it not known where Luilloth had been, but tales say that when Ostir and his army did not return, she set out to aid them. She found only her son's loyal canine howling among the Downs, and Luilloth knew then that Ostir was dead, for Astoryn would never leave his master's side.

"Luilloth vowed to put an end to the torments and ravages visited upon the land and her family. She and Astoryn went north to seek guidance, following whispers of some great power that dwelt beneath the sinister boughs of the forest. She was never seen again, but the ravening Dead quieted soon after and vanished back into the mists.

"The fate of Princess Luilloth is unknown, but those she left behind built this statue in honour of her sacrifice."'My heart breaks for Luilloth, losing so many as well as having her kingdom ravaged.'Long ago, the Elves of Tham Mírdain led by Celebrimbor wrought great works, but when they were deceived by the Enemy, ruin befell them.Tarandir can be found upon the ruins of an old watch-tower at Caras Gelebren in Swanfleet.

You have found a lone Elf in ornate armour standing among the ruins of Caras Gelebren. The Elf, Tarandir, has offered to tell you the tale of the doom of Caras Gelebren.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must complete the Skirmish: Doom of Caras Gelebren. If you have not yet completed the Skirmish Tutorial, you must first visit any Skirmish Camp and speak to the Skirmish Captain. Skirmish Camps can be found throughout Middle-earth in locations such as Bree, Thorin's Gate, Ost Guruth, and Rivendell.</rgb>Hear Tarandir's tale and complete 'Doom of Caras Gelebren'Tarandir can be found upon the ruins of an old watch-tower at Caras Gelebren in Swanfleet.

You have heard Tarandir's tale of the doom of Caras Gelebren. You should speak to Tarandir.Talk to TarandirThe ruins of the House of the Mírdain can be found at the easternmost point of Caras Gelebren.

Tarandir has asked you to stand before the ruins of the House of the Mírdain and listen that you might honour the memory of his people. You should find the ruins of the House of the Mírdain and listen to honour the memory of the Mírdain.Tarandir can be found upon the ruins of an old watch-tower at Caras Gelebren in Swanfleet.

You have done as Tarandir asked and listened before the ruins of the House of the Mírdain. You should return to Tarandir.Talk to Tarandir'Hail, traveller. What has brought you to this place?'

You introduce yourself and tell the Elf of your adventures in Swanfleet.

'I am Tarandir, of the Mírdain, and I have come to Caras Gelebren on a last pilgrimage before I depart Middle-earth. Know you the history of this place? It stood in peace for many years, both before and after its destruction, but now Orc-kind roams it once more. It pains my heart to see it so, that these evils might remain after I depart.

'I was here when it fell long ago, ${PLAYER}, and though it is a sorrowful tale, I would share it with you.

'Will you hear it, friend?'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must complete the Skirmish: Doom of Caras Gelebren. If you have not yet completed the Skirmish Tutorial, you must first visit any Skirmish Camp and speak to the Skirmish Captain. Skirmish Camps can be found throughout Middle-earth in locations such as Bree, Thorin's Gate, Ost Guruth, and Rivendell.</rgb>'And that is the end of the tale, ${PLAYER}. Although I did not see him fall, Faeldor was lost. My brother held the gates of Caras Gelebren against the Enemy for as long as he could... and I wish I could tell him how proud I was of him in that moment. But there is never time, is there? Even for the Eldar...

'Although the war continued on for years, I and the other survivors of my kin found refuge at Imladris. In time, what we were faded away, and it was as if the Mírdain were not to be named as such among the Elves—that the stain of the Enemy could not be scoured from our hands.'

Tarandir shakes his head.

'Might I ask something of you?

'Travel up into the city, stand before the ruins of the House of the Mírdain, and listen. That is all I ask.''You heard nothing, yes?

'That is a great sorrow, and one made no less painful with the passage of time. Once you would have heard the songs of anvils and chisels, and those of laughter and friendship, but no more. All that remains of Caras Gelebren... of Tham Mírdain... of old Mirobel are ruins and dreadful memories.

'When I soon depart this realm, will I be healed of these wounds? I cannot say for certain, but I fear the answer—for neither seems befitting, either as gift or punishment.'

Tarandir pauses. His gaze falls upon the ruins of the lower city of Caras Gelebren. After a long moment, he turns to you.

'I thank you for hearing my tale, ${PLAYER}. It has done my spirit well to tell it one last time in Middle-earth.

'Oh, but one more thing... a word of warning, if you would hear it. The Enemy's hand, though maimed, may still seek to shape the days to come in Middle-earth.

'Be watchful of the evils in this world, my friend.'You met an old dwarf named Oddvarr who seems a bit absent-minded. He is an explorer of some renown... or at least he says he is.Oddvarr asked you to search the ruins to the north.

Oddvarr set his pack down somewhere in the area and cannot seem to remember where.Search the ruins for Oddvarr's packOddvarr awaits you to the south of the ruins.

You found Oddvarr's pack in the old ruins to the north.Retrieve Oddvarr's packOddvarr is by the haystacks south of the ruins where you found the pack.

You found Oddvarr's pack containing his much-needed provisions.'My name is Oddvarr of the Blue Mountains, and I'm here in Bree-land on very important business. The only problem is I misplaced my pack.

'Now, I'm to investigate the old dwarf-ruins that are rumoured to exist here. I'm sure there are important discoveries to be made, and I'm the one to do it! I'm a famous explorer, you see.  

'But I digress! If you could help me find that pack, I would be indebted to you. You start looking over yonder north, and I'll search this area and to the south. If you find anything, meet me back here!''Ah, there's my old pack! Thank you so much for returning it to me. I would be in a world of hurt if my notes....

'What? My notes are missing! Curse those Orcs! They must have thought they were valuable.'As goblins continue to encroach upon Bâr Faroth, an unexpected ally emerges in the fight to drive them out of the Yondershire.You have discovered the remains of a slain goblin outside the long-abandoned Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.Examine the slain goblinThe Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth can be found in the northern reaches of the Yondershire.

After discovering a slain goblin outside the Hunters' Hall, you suspect that someone is acting against the goblins at Bâr Faroth. You should investigate the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.Enter the Hunters' Hall at Bâr FarothThe Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth can be found in the northern reaches of the Yondershire.

After entering the Hunter's Hall, you have discovered the light of a camp-fire. You should investigate the camp-site inside the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.Explore the camp-site inside the Hunters' Hall at Bâr FarothAnthandir can be found in the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.

After entering the Hunter's Hall, you have discovered a Ranger of the North, Anthandir, and his faithful companion dwelling in the old ruins. You should talk to Anthandir and learn of his purpose at Bâr Faroth.Talk to Anthandir in the Hunters' Hall at Bâr FarothIdeal trap locations can be found throughout Bâr Faroth. Anthandir has marked your map with the locations of several Rangers' caches at Bâr Faroth.

Anthandir has requested your aid in laying traps for the encroaching goblins at Bâr Faroth. In addition, he has tasked you with retrieving several Rangers' caches from the ruins before they are discovered by the goblins.Lay traps for the goblins at Bâr Faroth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Retrieve Rangers' caches at Bâr Faroth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Anthandir can be found in the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.

You have set traps for the goblins and retrieved several Ranger caches as Anthandir requested. You should deliver the caches to Anthandir at the Hunters' Hall at Bâr Faroth.While exploring Bâr Faroth, you have discovered the remains of a slain goblin outside the ruins of the old Hunters' Hall. It seems that few goblins have dared to draw too near to its doors, but it remains unclear why they have become so fearful of it.

You should enter the ruins of the Hunters' Hall and attempt to discover who has been acting against the goblins at Bâr Faroth.'I heard you coming, ${RACE}. If I did not deem you a friend, you would not stand before me.

'Tell me, did Halros send you? I will tell you the same thing I told the others he sent. It is not the place of the Dúnedain to intervene in the affairs of the halflings. Who are you and what business do you have in the Shire?'

You introduce yourself and inform Anthandir that many threats have come to the Yondershire.

'It is true that I have kept watch for many years and that the dangers facing the Shire have seldom grown so dire, but my duty is to protect these lands. Why now should I involve myself when the halflings act against their own? When lesser men come unbidden to these lands, seeking for stolen fortunes? Should not the halflings prove their own mettle?'

You tell Anthandir that the hobbits may face their own challenges, but the presence of the goblins poses a unique threat.

'Indeed, they have complicated my long vigil at Bâr Faroth. I have repelled them as best I can, but I fear I will soon have to seek new refuge.

'If you insist upon aiding me, I would ask that you set traps within Bâr Faroth and retrieve my caches. The goblins arrived so swiftly that I could not recover them before they built their encampment atop them. Here, I will mark your map.

'You have given me much to consider. Do as I have asked, and I will hear your words.''I must admit I doubted your resolve, ${PLAYER}.

'I thought Halros a fool when he ingratiated himself to the halflings. It was our duty to protect these lands, not befriend its peoples. Perhaps I have misjudged my charge....'

Anthandir pauses and for the briefest moment, a pained look washes across his face.

'When the time is right, I will reveal myself to the halflings in the village they call Long Cleeve. For too long, they have caught only glimpses of me and Thorvellon. They think that my companion is some terrible Gnasher, some beast in the night, but we have protected these lands—vigilant and unseen. Yet, there is a shadow that rises in the east, and it grows in strength with each passing hour. If we do not stand together, then we shall die alone. Perhaps now it is best that they know of me, that they might call upon me in times of dire need.

'Go, friend, and aid those that you can. I ask only one thing: do not speak of me to Halros. Old wounds are best left forgotten.'Umín seems to be possessed by that necklace he is wearing. You must remove that necklace from him at all costs.Save Umín from the necklace's holdSave Umín from the necklace's holdWith the amount of animals that Prunella Goldworthy has volunteered to care for, she has lost sight of one particularly ornery goose!The goose is loose and was last seen in the village of Long Cleeve.

