You should talk to Prunella Goldworthy.Talk to Prunella Goldworthy'We're missing a particularly troublesome goose, on whom I usually need to keep a close eye. Needless to say, I have not had an eye to spare of late, as you can attest!

'Now I fear the goose is loose and getting up to mischief somewhere in the village. This is... well, it's not the first time this has happened! Take care as you go, ${PLAYER}, this goose is a tricky one!''That was the most excitement I have seen in several days, and you just missed all the fun! That goose ran in here, knocked down every bottle in its path, and ran out... just as you arrived!

'I do appreciate you cleaning up the bottles for me. Now good luck catching that silly goose!''Thank you for helping me up. Did you see that goose? One minute I am minding my own business, taking home some fresh vegetables from the market. The very next minute, this horrible goose comes along, knocks me down, and pilfers all my beautiful cabbages!

'You must get back my cabbages!''Oh thank you for retrieving my cabbages, for by rescuing them you have saved me as well! How so, you ask? Well, cabbage stew is my wife's favourite meal and I promised to make it for her... for today is our wedding anniversary!

'I don't think she would have believed that I was robbed by a goose, let alone three geese. I am in your debt.''You say there were three geese unleashed upon my neighbours, and not simply one loose goose?'

Prunella rubs her chin.

'That does explain why my goose was so tricksy. It was always able to cause the most surprising amount of mischief. Three times the normal amount, it seems!

'Who can say where those geese might have wandered off to now? Perhaps we will see them again one day. Thank you for all your help! Now I think I should find out if the farmer that entrusted me with that goose in the first place knew the full story of the silly creature....'Beneath The Forsaken Inn stretches an expanse of natural caverns. It seems that people lived here at one time. One such person, the apparent leader of the group, left behind a journal. Who were these people, and what were they doing here? Collect all the pages and discover for yourself.

Note: Not all journal pages can be found in Tier 1 difficulty.Captain Rabghul has not made it easy to locate the pages of his journal. He has left some of them in hidden areas where only a well-balanced party may venture.Locate page 1Locate page 2Locate page 3Locate page 4Locate page 5Edhan is exhausted from the work he has already done, and wonders if you will help him with the rest of it.The crates that were intended for Crossway House were left along the east road out of Herne, and Edhan asked you to carry them to the storage room inside the inn.Pick up one of the crates by the eastern road out of HerneThe crates that were intended for Crossway House were left along the east road out of Herne, and Edhan asked you to carry them to the storage room inside the inn.Pick up the remaining crate by the eastern road out of HerneEdhan is just outside the back door of Crossway House.Talk to Edhan outside Crossway House'I am exhausted, friend. I work for Maddoc in Crossway House, and it is my job to carry crates and supplies into the tavern whenever they are delivered. But the waggon-driver from Bree-land just departed, and he refused to leave the crates any nearer than the very outskirts of Herne! He said there's a bad feeling about the town today, and he didn't want to stay here any longer than was strictly necessary!

'He did the least amount of effort, but I have already done more than I should! Do you think you could bring the last two crates inside Crossway House, and set them down in the storage room with the fireplace? I would really appreciate resting my arms for a moment, friend, and I wouldn't forget it.

'The last two crates are right where the eastern road leaves Herne.''Do you think you could bring the last two crates inside Crossway House, and set them down in the storage room with the fireplace? I would really appreciate resting my arms for a moment, friend, and I wouldn't forget it.

