'My father’s bedroom is on the second floor, but in his condition, there is no way he can manage stairs. Will you disassemble his bed and reassemble it in his library downstairs? He will complain, I am sure, but I can tell by the bedroll that he has already been spending nights down here, thankfully.''Thank you so much! I know he has a hard time admitting when he needs help, but I think that in the end he will be grateful.'The necklace by itself is just a necklace, but the spirit surrounding it makes it special. This spirit will stop at nothing to escape its prison and find a new host. You must put it to rest once and for all.Destroy the Spirit of the NecklaceThe Yonder-watch will need supplies if they are to put a stop to Lotho's foolish plans.Yonder-watch supplies can be found at the secret store-hole in the woods between Gamwich and Long Cleeve.

