'I will find you there later, once I have completed a few more of my preparations. My plan is still coming together, but when it does it will be something else... trust me!''Thank you for these supplies. I confess that I was suspicious of Mr. Bolger when he arrived, but he has proven to be a good friend to the Yonder-watch.

'While I have you here, would you mind assisting me with an urgent matter? Some Man named Harry Goatleaf is lurking about near here. I was hoping you might confront him and send him on his way.''You want to move along, stranger. Stand in my way and you'll be sorry!''Harry Goatleaf? How many of these Men have come to Yondershire? Perhaps they are in league with Lotho after all. How can a hobbit, even one like Lotho, stoop to such lows as this? Still, it seems he has done just that, and now it's up to us to stop him and his cronies.

