Return to Tílsa Hardstep.Talk to Tílsa Hardstep'Judging by your outfit you must be a person of discerning taste. Perhaps you're the right person to help me! I'm in town visiting a friend. This'll be my first time being a guest in her home, and I'd like to bring a gift for her, a "mathom" as they say 'round these parts. Problem is, I can't decide what to give her. I'm petrified of giving a lackluster gift. Could I bother you to ask around town, see what folks think make for a good mathom?''Interesting... cooking utensils, small things, and things that are... red? A third of that information is very useful.

'You know my friend is a brewer, maybe a wooden spoon would make a good gift. Oh and you know what? I'm no stranger to whittling. Perhaps I could make it for her myself. Is it proper to whittle a wooden spoon? I suppose I'll find out!

'Thank you for helping me. I feel so relieved to have a direction to go in.''What do I like in a mathom, you ask? The smaller the better! When you have as many friends and relations as I do, a lot of mathoms find their way into your home. I like to keep things tidy, so smaller mathoms mean they take up less space, which means I am less bothered!''What makes for a good mathom? Well, anything I suppose. If I receive a mathom I don't like, I simply pass it along to someone else! Personally, though, I like receiving a mathom suited to my hobbies. Best mathoms I ever received are a hammer, a bundle of cheesecloth, and a short sword.'

...

'For three separate hobbies, of course.

'Why do you ask? Are you offering? If so a new wooden spoon would be great. I lost my old one during what I choose to call a 'grain mashing incident'.''Red. I like red things.'Practice the art of casting your vision forwards, and you shall be able to do it with greater frequency.Use Visions and Foretellings skillsPractice the art of casting your vision forwards, and you shall be able to do it with greater frequency.Use the skills "Do Not Fall This Day" and "Scribe a New Ending"With routes extending into the Yondershire, the Quick Post must maintain its good reputation.The Quick Post service is responsible for more than a dozen mail routes throughout the Shire. If its good name is to be maintained, you will need to help deliver mail at each of its routes and ensure that the routes between Hithershire and Yondershire remain in service.Aid Postman Grubb and complete 'A Route Over Yonder'Service Nobottle to Long Cleeve RouteService Nobottle to Tighfield RouteService Gamwich to Tighfield RouteService Long Cleeve to Nobottle RouteService Tighfield to Gamwich RouteService Tighfield to Nobottle RoutePostmaster Proudfoot is in Michel Delving, near the Town Hole.

Thanks to your efforts, a conspiracy to subvert the Quick Post was thwarted and it has maintained its reputation for speedy delivery of the mail both in Hithershire and Yondershire. Postmaster Proudfoot will be delighted to hear of all you have done.Talk to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving'Delightful news, ${PLAYER}! With your help, we've been able to keep our branches in Yondershire in working order and ensure that the Quick Post remains a respected institution in the Shire.

'If Postman Grubb and our very own Onyx had not discovered the discrepancy when they did, I fear irreparable damage would have been done to the reputation of the Quick Post. Although I remain suspicious that this self-styled "Chief Shirriff" will again attempt to subvert the Quick Post, I have ordered my postmen to keep a vigilant eye on their routes and report any misconduct—even from one of the Bounders!

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. If your propensity for adventure should ever wane, there is a place for you here at the Quick Post.'Gandalf the Grey is troubled by recent stirrings in the East. He wonders what has become of his allies and enemies of the past.Master Elrond is at the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

