This deed will only be advanced by Lieutenants that do not appear grey to your character, they must be around the same level as you are.Frideric the Elder tribesman of the Eglain is under threat of attack by the Orc hordes.Head down the Greenway from Trestlebridge and then east along the east-west road.

Go to Ost Guruth and talk to Frideric the Elder.'I thank you for all you've done for us. Without your help this town would be a smouldering ruin and all of us would be killed or captured by the Orcs.

'There's a settlement to the south-east called Ost Guruth. A brave elder called Frideric and his people, the Eglain make it their home. They too know the horrors of the Orcs.

'If you are able to help them as you did us, Frideric would reward you. Find him and wish him well from the good folk of Trestlebridge.''The folk down in the Lone-lands -- the Eglain, I think they call themselves -- are a strange lot. They don't take to living in cities very well.''You are the one who helped battle the Orcs at the Trestlespan? Then perhaps you can be of use to the Eglain....'Defeat many troll Wound-takers in Skirmishes.
This deed will only be advanced by Lieutenants that do not appear grey to your character, they must be around the same level as you are.Defeat troll Wound-takers in SkirmishesDefeat many more troll Wound-takers in Skirmishes.
This deed will only be advanced by Lieutenants that do not appear grey to your character, they must be around the same level as you are.Defeat troll Wound-takers in SkirmishesAfter encountering the elusive boar, Turch, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Gaerion can be found at Sírlond in Cardolan.

You have acquired a trophy from an elusive foe in Cardolan. You should deliver it to Gaerion, a trophy-hunter and lore-keeper of the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Deliver Turch's tusks to Gaerion in CardolanAfter encountering and defeating the elusive boar, Turch, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Dúnedain of Cardolan.

As you inspect Turch's tusks, you are impressed by their condition. At their points, they are as sharp as needles, and despite Turch's age, they show far less wear than those of the other boars in Cardolan. Perhaps Turch was so imposing that he did not often deign to fight his own battles, but judging by your encounter, this was not for lack of skill in combat.

You should bring this trophy to Gaerion, a trophy-hunter and lore-keeper of the Dúnedain of Cardolan.'Welcome, traveller. Have you found something new?'

As Gaerion inspects Turch's tusks, he carefully touches the tip of one of the tusks with his finger. Even with a soft touch, he pricks himself, drawing a small amount of blood. He winces slightly, but then his face warms to a smile.

'A mighty beast, even in death. These tusks will make a fine trophy, indeed.

'I shall see that they are well-preserved. You have my thanks!'Tuckborough is the chief village of Tookland and home to the Thain of the Shire. Goblins and half-orcs seek to capture it in the name of Sharkey, the brigand chieftain troubling Bree-land and the Shire.The first step to breaking the siege on the Great Smials is to reclaim the south and west sides of the hill.Free the southern hillsideFree the western hillsideFree Hyacinth's entrancewayWith the south and west sides in your control, it is now time to break the enemy's hold on the eastern hillside.Free the eastern hillsideFree Edilina's entrancewayThe hillsides have been claimed for the Free Peoples. Now the courtyard has opened and may be assaulted.Free the courtyard of the Great SmialsThe courtyard has fallen. Now all that remains is to defeat the leader of the assault and break the siege.Defeat the half-orc at the doorway to the Great Smials and claim the Great Smials'The Tooks will remember your patronage and aid for many generations to come.'The Great Smials are the capitol of the Shire, the home of the Thain, Paladin Took. Brigands and goblins in the service of Saruman the White seek to capture the Great Smials and throw down the Tooks.The Great Smials are besieged.Stop Ghâshfog from digging into the Great SmialsStop Murbarash from burning hobbit holesStop Fíthrokh from eating chickensDefeat Oldroot at the Great WillowDefeat Big Fright on the hillside.Few of your foes are foolish enough to take to the field of battle without armour, but every armour has its flaws.Strike enemies with Penetrating ShotFew of your foes are foolish enough to take to the field of battle without armour, but every armour has its flaws.Critically hit enemies with Penetrating ShotYou never know when you may run across a brigand of some repute.Complete optional encounters in the Bree Offensive Tutorial Skirmish.Defeat Reginald CutweedThe inhabitants of Bree have spent the occupation holed up within The Prancing Pony. Angered at their uprising, the brigand have decided to burn them out....Second-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to discuss his plan with you.Talk to Second-watcher HeathstrawWill and Tom are outside of The Prancing Pony. They want to help you upgrade your soldier by allowing you to purchase and slot a role trait enabling him to be a warrior.Purchase the Warrior Role Trait from Will, then talk to Tom to slot it, then use your skill to call forth your WarriorSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to discuss a few final details with you.Talk to Second-watcher HeathstrawThe enemy is attacking The Prancing Pony. Aid Second-watcher Heathstraw in defending it.Defeat the first assaultSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to speak with you.Talk to Second-watcher HeathstrawThe enemy is attacking The Prancing Pony. Aid Second-watcher Heathstraw in defending it.Defeat the second assaultSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to speak with you.Talk to Second-watcher HeathstrawThe enemy is launching their final attack at The Prancing Pony. Help Second-watcher Heathstraw defend it.Defeat the final assault and DríthlorzSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to speak with you about today's success.Talk to Second-watcher Heathstraw'I am glad to see that you have returned, friend. We have made it here to The Prancing Pony in your absence and have been holding it, but I fear we won't last much longer. The brigands are coming at us with a vengeance which I cannot match. I am glad to have you by my side once more.''Oftentimes during Skirmishes such as these, you will find you have other allies, such as myself, aiding you in your battle. In some cases, if those allies fall, you will lose the Skirmish.''We often know little about the enemy's forces or where exactly they may come from. From scouting, I know that we are facing brigands, half-orcs, and wolves of varying skill and strength. But I do not know what combination of those might come at us at any point. Stay on your guard and be prepared to alter your defence at any moment to best defend against the enemy's assaults.''That Orc was one of the lieutenants I was speaking of. You did well to defeat it.''Bree is safe! You have done us a great service by aiding the cause. I could have held for a short time, but that half-orc with Bill Ferny and Harry Goatleaf surely would have done me in had I been alone. I thank you greatly for your aid.''There are a great number and variety of rewards attainable by helping the Free Peoples fight against the Enemy.''I thank you again for your help in freeing Bree. It will be long before what you have done is forgotten.''It is important to be sure that your soldier is properly trained for the role you wish him to fulfill. Make sure to pay attention to the other members of your fellowship, their abilities, and which soldiers they will be calling forth.''Making sure your soldier is trained to complement your own abilities and those of your fellowship is crucial to overcoming the challenges each Skirmish with the enemy presents.''When you were taking the South-gate, you moved through and took the enemy's bastions, claiming them for your own. Here, we are defending The Prancing Pony and the bastions we have claimed, while the enemy comes to us and attempts to take them for their own.''You can always purchase rewards and train your Soldier at any of the Skirmish Camps throughout the world.'While the Rangers of the North were distracted in the South, brigands and ruffians took an opportunity to wrest control of Bree....Second-watcher Heathstraw is at his camp just outside of Bree's South-gate. He is waiting for you to report in.Talk to Second-watcher HeathstrawThe horn is on a crate next to Second-watcher Heathstraw. You will need to use it in order to learn how to call forth a Soldier into the battle.Use the horn to learn how to call a SoldierThe Soldier skill is in your Skill Panel under the Skirmish section. You will need to use this skill to summon a Soldier to aid you.Use your new skill to call forth a SoldierSecond-watcher Heathstraw is at his camp just outside the South-gate of Bree. He wishes to discuss his plan for retaking the town with you.Talk to Second-watcher HeathstrawThe South-gate is just north of Second-watcher Heathstraw's camp. You will need to clear all of the enemies from around the banner in order to claim it.Take control of Bree's South-gateThe banner is at the South-gate of Bree. In order to claim this Control Point you need to use the banner.Use the banner to claim the South-gateThe Auction House is north of the South-gate of Bree. The enemies must be cleared and the banner used to take this point.Take control of Bree's Auction HouseBill Ferny's house is east of the Auction House. Dríthlorz and his allies must be defeated and the banner used in order to reclaim this part of Bree.Take control of Bill Ferny's house and defeat DríthlorzSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside of Bill Ferny's house. He wishes to discuss your victory with you.Report your success to Second-watcher Heathstraw'I did not think help would get here this quickly, but I am grateful to see that it has. I am afraid the situation is currently not very good. Brigands, let in by Bill Ferny and Harry Goatleaf, have taken over much of Bree.''Your Soldier is a powerful ally in the fight against the encroaching darkness. He will aid you greatly in your battles against the Enemy.''You have done much good work here today, ${PLAYER}. There is more to do, but for today, let us rest and tend our wounds.''Use the horn, and it will teach you how to call forth a Soldier to join you in your Skirmish against the enemy.''Use the skill the horn taught you to call forth a Soldier of the Free Peoples. You will not survive storming the gates of Bree alone.''The South-gate must be taken first. If it is not in our control, we cannot hope to push further into Bree.''Oftentimes, the enemy will not be pleased about losing a location of importance. Be wary...they may launch a counterassault to try and regain it.''The leaders of the enemy's forces are often cunning and powerful creatures. They should not be regarded lightly.''Go and rest. You have done much good for the world today. More will be needed tomorrow, but for tonight, enjoy the respite.'With a fresh bundle of rope in hand, thanks entirely to you having been duped into trading for it, Adamanda is ready for the next stage of her Grand Plan.Ramsa Twelling can be found in Gamwich.

Adamanda North-took has asked you to bring the rope to Ramsa Twelling and have her weave it into a net.Fresh honey can be found in hives near Ramsa's dwelling in Gamwich.

Ramsa Twelling has asked you to collect honey from her hives.Collect honeyPello can be found in the Brimful Quiver, in Gamwich.

You should bring the honey to Pello Hartstongue and exchange it for a bottle of mead.The bottle of mead can be found in the Brimful Quiver, in Gamwich.

Pello has given you permission to collect a bottle of mead from the back room.Collect the bottle of meadRamsa is in Gamwich.

You should bring the mead to Ramsa Twelling.The net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich.

Ramsa has asked for your assistance finishing the knots for the net she is making for Adamanda.Add knots to the net (0/80)The net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich.

Ramsa has asked for your assistance finishing the knots for the net she is making for Adamanda.Add knots to the net (1/80)The net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich.

Ramsa has asked for your assistance finishing the knots for the net she is making for Adamanda.Add knots to the net (2/80)The net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich.

Ramsa has asked for your assistance finishing the knots for the net she is making for Adamanda.Add knots to the net (3/80)Ramsa is in Gamwich.

You should talk to Ramsa.Talk to RamsaThe net is hanging next to Ramsa in Gamwich.

You should collect the net and bring it to Adamanda.Collect the completed netAdamanda North-took can be found near Nobottle.

You should bring the net to Adamanda.Adamanda's laughter fades to a chuckle and she clears her throat, trying to hide her smile.

'Now that we have the rope, we can move on to the next step in my Grand Plan! We need a net! Take the rope to Ramsa Twelling in Gamwich and have her make us a net, will you? I am going to follow these tracks a ways and will meet you further along their trail.''Hello to you, my fine ${RACE}. This is very nice rope and will make an excellent net. Tell Diamond I shall have it for her by mid-day on the morrow.'

You explain that you need it sooner.

'Well that's too bad for you, now isn't it? I have tasks what need doing today and haven't the time for net weaving.

'Although... how comfortable are you with bees? My hives are full of the sweetest honey but not always the sweetest bees. If you take some honey over to Pello at the Brimful Quiver, I could work on the net for Diamond. Mind you don't upset the bees, though. They are quick to anger a' times.''Welcome, friend! What can I get for you today? Ah, you have come for Ramsa's mead is it? I thought you looked sweet!

'Let's have the honey then, and you may collect her bottle from the room behind me.''Well now, you made your way back here far sooner than I expected! The net is not done yet, but look what I have found! A helper!'

She beams at you pointedly.

'Come now, here is the knot you want to use. With the both of us tying, this will be finished in no time!''Well, well! Your first few knots were making me a bit nervous, but you seem to get the hang of it as you went on! Good for you! If you ever want to give up this wandering life of yours, I could see you taking up work as an Apprentice Net Weaver! Go on ahead and take the net to Diamond, and good hunting!''Oh. You return. You were gone for so long that I forgot you were even doing something for me.'

She glances up at the sky. 

'You are lucky, you know. To be able to travel so far and to see so many things. To make your own future.'

Adamanda is silent a moment and then sighs, and smiles brightly at you.

'Now then! Where is this net that took you so long to procure? We have Grand Plans to enact!'Foes might expect a Beorning to be slow and lumbering, but you are as quick as you are strong.Parry or Evade enemy attacksThe Bounders find themselves perplexed over the sudden aggression of the Old Forest wildlife.The road to the Bonfire Glade lies just beyond the Old Forest Tunnel on the eastern border of Buckland.

Shirriff Hob Hayward has asked you to set up jars of foul-smelling brew along the road to ward off aggressive wildlife.Place jars along the road to the Bonfire Glade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Shirriff Hob Hayward is guarding the Buckland Gate in Buckland.

You should let him know that you've set up the jars in the Old Forest.'Hoy there, stranger! I'll warn you right now, you ought to stay away from the Old Forest. The beasts there are all riled up -- they've even gone and attacked hobbits near the Old Forest Tunnel.

'But... hold on, you seem like the adventuring sort. Think you could lend us a hand? Us Bounders came up with a brew of sorts that'll dissuade most things from approaching. All you need to do is set up these jars along the road to the Bonfire Glade.

'It'll take a while for the smell to set in, so don't drop your guard in the forest! And... don't breathe in too deeply.''Wolves attacked you on the way to the Bonfire Glade? I'd wager they were as panicked as the other animals we've seen.

'At any rate... I can't say it'll be pleasant venturing into the forest for the time being, but better safe than sorry.'Defeat many Venomous Blood-arrows in Skirmishes.

