'Remember, we must defeat the leaders of this war-band if we are to discourage them. Use the torches you find on the unlit pyres along the path. They may draw the attention of nearby Orcs.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}, better than I, it appears. Uruk-hai and Orcs nearly bested me and my wounds run deep.

'But you must not concern yourself with me now. Beyond that gate is the Uruk who leads this force. Pass through the gate and defeat him. We cannot allow these Orcs to have a hold in the north.''My wounds are grievous, but I shall recover. Come, we shall return to my camp.'Reginard has been found. Now it's time to find his belongings.You should free Reginard from his bindings.Free Reginard from his bindingsReginard has asked you to find his pack, which must be somewhere in Lhúngobel.Find Reginard's packYou have found Reginard's pack with most of its contents ruined.

You should retrieve his pack for him.Retrieve Reginard's packReginard is waiting for you outside of Lhúngobel.

You should return to him with his pack and what remains of his belongings.Reginard has invited you to meet up with him back at his camp-site.

His camp-site is in the marsh south of Lhúngobel.Return to Reginard's camp-site in the marshYou have found Reginard back at his camp-site.

You should talk to him.Talk to Reginard'I can get out just fine once you untie me, but you've got to search for my pack! It has my lucky four-leaf clover. As long as I have my clover, everything will be fine.

'The goblins dragged my pack off to who knows where -- though I suspect they didn't take it very far!

'I'll wait for you outside the ruins.'Reginard's face falls when he weighs the pack in his hands.

'I suppose the goblins weren't very fond of my things. It's just a few spice containers left....

'Wait. Wh -- where's my lucky clover? I can't go back without it! That clover was a gift from -- from -- '

He takes several deep, shaky breaths to steady himself.

'Not much I can do about this, right? Can't comb the entire place for a single clover. This... this will just be a minor setback in my adventure! Yes, that's it.

'Why don't I cook you a meal back at camp? It's only proper after everything you did! I'll meet you there -- I need to take this walk alone.''Oh, hello. I collected kindling on the way here but erm, I tripped and dropped most of it into the river....'Guardsman Otley, in Trestlebridge, is awaiting delivery of broken wooden spears at the war-torn town of Trestlebridge.You have been tasked with collecting broken wooden spears from the Orcs found deep in the valley to the east of Trestlebridge. You can deliver the items to Guardsman Otley at Trestlebridge.Wanted: Broken wooden spears found on the Orcs deep in the valley to the east of Trestlebridge. Deliver the items to Guardsman Otley in the town of Trestlebridge.Wanted: Broken wooden spears found on the Orcs deep in the valley to the east of Trestlebridge.'We'll drive these Orcs away from our land and take back all the North Downs. These spears will serve as a rallying cry to gather our forces to drive the Orcs back. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Guardsman Otley, in Trestlebridge, is awaiting delivery of tough sword sheaths.You have been tasked with collecting tough sword sheaths from intelligent enemies far to the north. You can deliver the items to Guardsman Otley at Trestlebridge.Wanted: Tough sword sheaths from intelligent enemies to the north. Deliver the items to Guardsman Otley in the town of Trestlebridge.Wanted: Tough sword sheaths from intelligent enemies to the north.'We will be able to refit these for our weapons quickly. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Eilian Good-heart came to Gaervarad to give the brigands a piece of her mind, but she has admitted that perhaps it might be too dangerous for her.Two brigand leaders of ill repute can be found within Gaervarad: Idwal and Emrys Redclaw.Defeat Idwal Redclaw in GaervaradDefeat Emrys Redclaw in GaervaradEilian Good-heart waits to hear of your successes outside Gaervarad.Talk to Eilian Good-heart outside Gaervarad'Hello there, adventurer! I trust that is what you are, yes? Very good! I am not an adventurer, you see, but a citizen concerned with an issue I have noticed of late: the increase of bad-tempered ruffians that threaten the peace and safety of these lands!

'You may call me Missus Good-heart, if it please you, and I may call you... what? ${PLAYER}? It is a pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}. I came here to give these brigands a piece of my mind, but now that I have arrived I think perhaps I was a bit over-zealous. There are two ruffians in particular that have caused a great deal of trouble back home. They are the Redclaw brothers, Idwal and Emrys, and their crimes are too numerous to recount! Let us just say that "Redclaw" is not just a family name, but a description of the sort of villainy of which they are most fond!

'They are dangerous, and they are somewhere within this structure! If you can put an end to their murdering, I will have a reward for you. And you will also have the appreciation of my entire village!''There are two ruffians in particular that have caused a great deal of trouble back home. They are the Redclaw brothers, Idwal and Emrys, and their crimes are too numerous to recount! Let us just say that "Redclaw" is not just a family name, but a description of the sort of villainy of which they are most fond!

'They are dangerous, and they are somewhere within this structure! If you can put an end to their murdering, I will have a reward for you. And you will also have the appreciation of my entire village!''Idwal and Emrys are no more? Very well done, ${PLAYER}! You have my thanks, and when I report to my village that the Redclaw brothers have paid for their crimes, you will have the appreciation of an entire village!

'Good day to you, my adventuring friend! I cannot imagine our paths will cross again, but if they do I will know that fate smiles upon me, and I should expect good fortune for all the rest of the day!'Rothavron is concerned about more than just the passage of the terrible Riders.Brigands have been massing to the south, at Gaervarad in Ruddymore, and Rothavron does not want the villains to be unopposed.Defeat brigands at Gaervarad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rothavron is at Sarn Ford.Talk to Rothavron at Sarn Ford'Before Sarn Ford was attacked by the terrible riders in black, we received word that brigands were gathering at Gaervarad, to the south, and we planned to dispatch a force of Rangers to deal with them. Brigands! Such foes seem so trivial now!

'But no, I speak rashly. They are still a danger to the folk who live in these lands, though my people's concerns seem more pressing in the aftermath of the attack some days gone! There is never just one thing, is there?

'Will you go to Gaervarad and deal with the massing of the brigands? If one danger is ignored, that will be the one that overmasters us, or so says my worried heart.''Will you go to Gaervarad and deal with the massing of the brigands? If one danger is ignored, that will be the one that overmasters us, or so says my worried heart.''You have done well to oppose the brigands massing at Gaervarad. I must remember that one frightening experience does not eliminate the other dangers against which we must stand! That is easier said than it is done, friend.

'Thank you for helping the people I am sworn to defend.'Gurthern believes that the missing child may have followed one of the elhudan, the glowing wisp-like orbs, into the fogs near Calarphel.Gurthern will meet you where he last saw the elhudan to search for the missing child. He waits for you by a pond in Tyrn Gorthad.

You should speak with Gurthern.Talk to GurthernGurthern believes that the missing child may have followed one of the elhudan, the glowing wisp-like orbs, into the wilderness of Tyrn Gorthad.

You should look for the elhudan that Gurthern saw around this area.Search for the missing childSpeak to the wailing womanAfter following the elhudan, you found the missing child unharmed. The wailing woman fled up the hill, while the child fled towards Gurthern.

You should return to Gurthern and share what you found.Return to Gurthern'Your words are troubling. Leader Talfryn sent me here to look into rumours of dark tidings that were reaching us in Lhan Garan. Some fell-wind has swept across Swanfleet and Cardolan. The dead stir in their barrows, and Orcs are crawling over the ruined fortresses and forts.

'You say the young girl mentioned glowing balls of light? With the unrest around the barrows, the elhudan have also risen. I have seen their flickering lights at dusk, near Calarphel. Perhaps you will find some answers there.

'I will show you where I saw them, but I dare not go close myself. North of Herne is a small pond, around which the elhudan have been gathering in numbers. Meet me there.''Well, here we are! The ruins across the pond are where I saw the elhudan gathering. I can see their fell glow from here. Walk carefully! I will wait for you here.''You did it! Cai made it back to me safely.'The truth emerges.You should tell Watcyn the truth about Rendal's past.Watcyn has pleaded for you and Rendal to help him.

You should talk to Rendal and decide on what to do.Talk to RendalRendal plans to attack the captains in Gaervarad. You should meet with him there.

Gaervarad is located to the south-west of Sírlond.Find Rendal near GaervaradYou have found Rendal near Gaervarad.

You should talk to him to discuss what to do next.Talk to Rendal'Watcyn's suspicions are not unfounded; I used to be a Ranger, but I've long since severed my ties. They are too disconnected from the people they seek to protect. Distrust is to be expected when you shroud your movements and intentions.

'Yes, the irony is not lost on me. I feared that the truth would have put Watcyn on edge, but... he deserves the truth. Alas, my presence clearly causes him some anxiety. Would you be willing to tell him in my stead?

'I'll apologize to him myself -- should he allow it.''Huh... maybe Rendal isn't so bad after all. I guess it's time I told my story, too.

'There's a reason why I was in Caranost -- I've heard rumours about valuable relics there. I'll need every bit of money I can get to flee whatever mess is brewing down south.

'Not to mention the mess that's brewing here. The captains in Gaervarad are searching for me, and every other deserter out there, to force us into some wizard's service.

'All I want is a safe place to lay my head down at night. Nobody would be able -- or even willing -- to help someone like me. Except you and Rendal... I know I've already asked a lot from you. But please.''These captains would force Watcyn into a war he does not want to fight. Then I'll strike them first!

'Gaervarad lies to the south-west. It's quite the trek, but I'll do everything I can. After all, Watcyn is under my protection.

'You are under no obligation to aid me, but... if you wish to, I'll meet you there.''${PLAYER}, I'm glad you came. I've been watching the camp for some time.

'What kind of misfortunes led these people here, I wonder? To commit such acts of warmongering, to fuel their hunger for power?

'One way or another, we are all trying to survive. A shame it must be this way.'The ruffian Elgar Crowfoot has been taking Imbert's potatoes and threatening Gamwich. This will not stand!Elgar Crowfoot is holed up in Ost Lagorath to the north-east.

You should find the stolen potatoes there.Find the stolen potatoes in Ost LagorathIf you defeat Elgar Crowfoot, the rest of the ruffians won't return to threaten Gamwich.

You should steal back the stolen potatoes to lure him out.Take the stolen potatoes and defeat Elgar CrowfootYou have defeated Elgar Crowfoot and reclaimed the stolen potatoes.

You should return to Adro outside of Gamwich.'I don't know a thing about fighting, but you look like you do. If you could defeat Elgar, you'd scare off his friends from ever approaching Gamwich! And I wouldn't have to steal any more food from my neighbours!

'Elgar is holed up in Ost Lagorath to the north-east. Maybe you could draw him out by stealing back the remaining potatoes.''You're back! I'll take those potatoes back to Imbert. After all, I've got some apologies to make.'What could be causing Imbert's potatoes to sprout?Imbert has asked you to solve the mystery of why his potatoes are sprouting.

You should examine the potato sacks in his yard.The potatoes in the first two sacks you checked haven't sprouted at all.

Maybe you should check one last potato sack....Check one last sackOne of Imbert's potato sacks is indeed filled with sprouted potatoes. You also found a trail of potatoes leading away from Imbert's house.

You should follow the trail.Follow the potato trailThe potato trail ends right at the feet of a hobbit waiting outside Gamwich.

You should question this suspicious hobbit.Talk to Adro'Hey! Why are you snooping around? Trying to ruin my potatoes again? Why, I ought to --

'You don't know what I'm talking about? Hm... I admit, I may have been a bit hasty. Sorry. It's just that all of my potatoes have sprouted, and it's too early for them to sprout! Something's not right!

'I'm no good at solving mysteries, but if you are, feel free to investigate the sacks over there.''Eep! I'm sorry, I'm sorry! I didn't want to steal those potatoes, honest!

'Some ruffians caught me eavesdropping and one of them -- Elgar Crowfoot -- threatened me. I'd heard they were running low on supplies, so I offered to bring food to them if they'd let me go.

'Stealing from Imbert was easy enough; I just filled his potato sack with sprouted ones so he wouldn't notice until it was too late. But I knew I'd get found out in the end.'Nathan Hodges, at Amon Raith, awaits the collection and delivery of broken wood spears.You have accepted a task to deliver broken wood spears to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith in the North Downs. You can find broken wood spears from the Orcs and shades north of Amon Raith.Wanted: Broken wood spears from the Orcs and shades north of Amon Raith. Deliver the items to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith.Wanted: Broken wood spears from the Orcs and shades north of Amon Raith.'This calms me a little. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Nathan Hodges, at Amon Raith, awaits the collection and delivery of coarse furs.You have accepted a task to deliver coarse furs to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith in the North Downs. You can find the coarse furs on the beasts to the north of the ruin of Amon Raith.Wanted: Coarse furs from beasts to the north of Amon Raith. Deliver the items to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith.Wanted: Coarse furs from beasts to the north of Amon Raith.'I will make certain that Agnes puts these to good use. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of coarse fur to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect coarse fur from the beasts in the area surrounding Esteldín to the west. Once collected, you are to deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Coarse fur from the beasts to the west of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Coarse fur from the beasts to the west of Esteldín.'We will put these to good use. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of large filth to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect the large filth from spiders in the area surrounding Esteldín to the west. Once collected you are to deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Large filth from the spiders to the west of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Large filth from the spiders to the west of Esteldín.'Knowing that the number of these creatures has been diminished is a welcome thought. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Candaith saw a company of Orcs climbing to the summit of Weathertop, preparing fortifications and barricades as they went. The Orcs have foul plans for the hill and must be defeated before they work some great mischief.Candaith is at his camp at the north-west foot of Weathertop in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree.

You have been asked to assist him in driving a company of Orcs from Weathertop. He told you to gather allies and return to him when you are prepared.Talk to Candaith and retake WeathertopCandaith is at his camp at the north-west foot of Weathertop.

Candaith is waiting to discuss with you the strange events that occurred atop Amon Sûl.Talk to Candaith'My stalwart companion Candaith requires your aid in the Lone-lands to the east! A band of ruthless and well-organized Orcs have snuck into those lands under cover of night and claimed the prominence of Amon Sûl -- called Weathertop by most in this age -- from which they command a view of all the lands and roads below.

'They cannot be allowed to hold that place, for they will be a deadly threat to any travellers in the region. You must meet with Candaith and do battle with the Orcs and reclaim Weathertop!

'You may find Candaith at his camp at the foot of Weathertop, along the north-west edge of the great hill.''Do not concern yourself with the Orcs that remain. This far removed from the south-lands, they will dwindle and become only a small danger to travellers through the Lone-lands.

'We have won a pivotal battle, my friend. You have earned some rest, I think, for the great threat posed by these Orcs is now finished!''If you are prepared, I will lead the way. We must be swift, else the Orcs may succeed at whatever foul mischief they have planned!'Tyrn Gorthad is haunted by elhudan, wisps that seem to enjoy luring away children and leading travellers astray.Gurthern has asked you to reduce the number of elhudan in Tyrn Gorthad.

Tyrn Gorthad is located in north-western Cardolan.Defeat luring glooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Gurthern know that you have defeated many luring glooms.

Gurthern is in Tyrn Gorthad in north-western Cardolan.Return to Gurthern'I encourage you to do what you can to reduce the numbers of these luring glooms, ${PLAYER}. Let no more children be led astray.

'Be careful, though, ${PLAYER}. Do not follow the elhudan too closely, as they love to lure folk into swamps, pits, and deadly pools.''Good work. May they trouble none again.'A hobbit by the name of Reginard left Tighfield and hasn't returned. Where has he gone?The hobbit Reginard has gone missing.

You might find clues to his whereabouts at his camp-site in the marsh west of Tighfield.Find Reginard's camp-site in the marshYou have found Reginard's camp-site, but not him.

You should examine the footprints at the camp-site.Examine the footprintsGoblins may have captured Reginard and taken him to Lhúngobel.

You should try to find him there.Find Reginard at LhúngobelThe goblins have held Reginard captive in Lhúngobel.

You should talk to him.Talk to Reginard'Have you got the time to help us search for a missing hobbit? Reginard is his name; he ventured out of Tighfield a day ago and hasn't returned. I'm rather concerned; the poor fellow has a reputation for being unlucky. There was a time when Reginard wasn't as plagued by misfortune but... well, that's not my story to tell.

'He was headed towards a camp-site in the marsh to the west. I'm sure he can handle the local wildlife just fine, but goblins are another story. There are quite a few of them in the ruins to the north-west. I do hope he hasn't run into them....'Most of these footprints must have been made by goblins, but one set may have belonged to a hobbit. You find no signs of a struggle.
 
Perhaps it would be best to continue your investigation at Lhúngobel to the north.'I didn't think anyone would come this far north to rescue me! The goblins ambushed me and took my pack. Didn't think it would be very smart to try fighting back... so here I am.'Thornegil fears the terrible evil that crossed into the Shire will endanger the hobbits, and she wants you to check on them.Andy Brockhouse is the housing broker of Michel Delving, and can be found north-west of Sarn Ford, by the Delving Fields.Cross the river north-west of Sarn Ford and talk to Andy Brockhouse in the ShireThornegil is at the crossing of Sarn Ford, south-east of the Shire.Talk to Thornegil at Sarn Ford'My people have long protected the borders of the Shire from the dangers of the wild world, but I have never seen such evil as that which scattered my people a few days gone. Dreadful riders in black left many among the Rangers injured or dead, and some of their number passed into the Shire... I know not how many.

'Will you cross the river and see how fare the folk of the Shire? The terrible creatures rode us down, and I fear to think what they might do to the peaceful folk across the river. Look for Andy Brockhouse and see if he still lives; he keeps watch outside some of the neighbourhoods that lie near Michel Delving.''Will you cross the river and see how fare the folk of the Shire? The terrible creatures rode us down, and I fear to think what they might do to the peaceful folk across the river. Look for Andy Brockhouse and see if he still lives; he keeps watch outside some of the neighbourhoods that lie near Michel Delving.''Black Riders? No, I haven't seen anything like that. Did you take a knock on the head? This is the Shire, and these are peaceful days! If anyone had seen a great big group of Big Folk on horses, all galloping together, someone would have said something!

'Now, it is true that sometimes a hobbit will see something that frightens him when he's out for a nighttime stroll, but nine times out of every ten the shadow that seemed to conceal something scary will turn out to be a fallen log in the road, or a deer frozen among the trees... and that more frightened of him than he of it!

'I appreciate the concern, but we hobbits know how to handle our own business. You go back to whoever sent you here in such a hurry, and you tell them all is fine in the Shire.''I appreciate the concern, but we hobbits know how to handle our own business. You go back to whoever sent you here in such a hurry, and you tell them all is fine in the Shire.''The hobbits do not report seeing anything untoward? This does not lighten my worries, ${PLAYER}, for it means whoever commands the terrible riders does so with a purpose beyond only killing. He must have had the riders separate, so as not to attract attention. But what do they seek if it is not open battle they desire?

'I am glad that Andy and his folk still live, but I do not know what to make of the creatures that broke our lines and scattered my people. Aye, I say creatures: in the misty night they looked like men to my eyes, but my heart says they are something else, and evil.

'Be wary as you travel these lands. Some of the creatures went into the Shire, but I think some of them remained here to trouble the Rangers, and keep us from opposing them.'After encountering the elusive aurochs, Tarangarn, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Gaerion can be found at Sírlond in Cardolan.

You have acquired a trophy from an elusive foe in Cardolan. You should deliver it to Gaerion, a trophy-hunter and lore-keeper of the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Deliver Tarangarn's horns to Gaerion in CardolanAfter encountering and defeating the elusive aurochs, Tarangarn, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Dúnedain of Cardolan.

As you inspect Tarangarn's horns, you take note of their startlingly-intact points, especially coming from an aurochs of Tarangarn's age. It is rumoured that certain folk in the North have been said to wear them as a sort of armour, but you can hardly imagine bearing such a burden upon your shoulders.

You should bring this trophy to Gaerion, a trophy-hunter and lore-keeper of the Dúnedain of Cardolan.'Hail, traveller. What do you have there?'

Gaerion inspects Tarangarn's horns closely, studying various markings and wear upon them.

'This is a fascinating find, friend. If you would be willing to part with it, I can offer you my gratitude... and some coin, of course.

'I shall see that it is well-preserved among our keepings—and that is a promise. You have my thanks!'A man named Watcyn has found himself in strange circumstances.Rendal has asked you to help him gather athelas.

Athelas grows around the pool near Sírlond, to the east.Collect athelas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected enough athelas.

You should return to Rendal in Sírlond.Return to Rendal in in SírlondRendal hasn't returned, but the injured man he was tending to -- Watcyn -- wishes to speak to you.Watcyn has asked you to rifle through Rendal's belongings, which are lying next to the tent.Examine Rendal's mapsExamine Rendal's weaponsRendal's belongings have given you a better idea of what kind of person he is.

You should tell Watcyn.Talk to Watcyn'Hail, traveller. Do you know of athelas? Kingsfoil, I mean. The weed?

'I found this man -- Watcyn -- injured in Caranost. I need to stay a bit longer to keep an eye on him, but once his condition has steadied, I'll go looking for athelas.

'We could work together to gather more -- if you don't mind, that is. There should be athelas growing around the pool nearby, just to the east.''Oi, you're the ${CLASS} Rendal mentioned, yeah? He's still gone. Said you and him were picking kingsfoil. What's a weed got to do with my wounds?

'Never mind, I haven't got a mind for healing and the like. Just give it here, and I'll make sure Rendal receives it.

'That man's a strange one; he carried me out of Caranost and still hasn't asked for a reward. What kind of person would venture into an Orc-infested ruin and -- erm, you're asking how I ended up there myself? The Orcs, of course!

'What I mean to say is, there's got to be a catch to Rendal's kindness. Come on, aren't you just a bit curious? His belongings are just lying over there, next to the tent!

'I'd go digging around myself, but -- ' Watcyn winces. 'Well, you get the idea.''Maps and weapons.... No ordinary traveller would go around seeking danger. D'you think he's one of them Rangers?

'They're too mysterious for my liking. Always avoiding other folks, coming and going to do who-knows-what. 'Course I don't like them.'Watcyn needs all the help he can get.Let Rendal know when you're ready to enter Gaervarad.

He waits for you outside.Talk to RendalRendal believes that defeating a few captains will cause them to have second doubts about hunting down deserters.

You should defeat captains around Gaervarad.Defeat Gaervarad captains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Use the whistle to summon Rendal to your sideYou have defeated enough captains.

You should speak with Rendal. Use the whistle in Gaervarad to summon Rendal to your side.Use the whistle in Gaervarad to summon Rendal'There must be several of these captains walking around, but defeating just a few will send enough of a message. Between the two of us, that shouldn't be too difficult.

'I'll let you decide how you want to approach this. When you are ready, let me know.''A new start for Watcyn is now possible. I only hope he realizes that there is more to life than just survival -- perhaps with my help, if he is willing.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You have a good heart; don't let the world take that away.''Whether or not you need my aid -- should you use this whistle, I'll be there.'Gadaric Munce desires that vengeance be visited upon the goblins who drove his people from the ruins of Minas Eriol.Goblins can be found in the ruins of Minas Eriol, south-east of The Forsaken Inn.

Goblins slaughtered many of the Eglain, and Gadaric Munce wants to revisit these losses upon the evil creatures. He bade you go to the ruins where the attack took place and defeat any goblins you find there.Defeat White Hand Guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat White Hand Spear-throwers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat White Hand ThrasherGadaric Munce is at The Forsaken Inn.

You found your prey within the ruins and dispatched them, avenging those of the Eglain slain at the hands of the goblins. Gadaric Munce will wish to hear of your victory.Talk to Gadaric Munce'Our people suffered an attack that cost many lives, and who knows how many more will be dead of starvation before the year is spent? The goblins must pay for this foul treachery.

'You carry yourself as one familiar with battle. Would you go to the ruins of Minas Eriol, south-east of this inn and destroy the goblins you find there? The Eglain deserve vengeance.''Thank you, ${RACE}. Terror spreads into our homes, and we are powerless to stand against these foes. We are not warriors, but gatherers and craftsmen.

'Many of our tribe are old, sick, or very young; not all are as capable as my brother and I. We were sent to search the Lone-lands for aid. The Ranger to the north is of no use to us. He sits and watches the Orcs and their crebain even as goblins slay my people here in the south.

'You have done much to earn my trust, and I shall speak well of you to my brother.''Savage killers, the goblins slay without conscience and dig through the ruins, disturbing the rest of the dead. They must be destroyed. Make haste and drive them from Minas Eriol, south-east of this inn, I beg you.'Defeat Wargs in the North Downs.Defeat Wargs in the North DownsDefeat many Wargs in the North Downs.Defeat Wargs in the North DownsSuspicious of Rendal, Watcyn now looks to you for help.Watcyn's lost belongings should be scattered around the stairs in Caranost, west of Sírlond.You have reclaimed Watcyn's belongings -- or, at least, whatever was left.

You should return to Watcyn in Sírlond.Watcyn has asked you to split some of his coin between you and Rendal.

Rendal has returned to Sírlond by now.'Well, I've got something to ask of you. I'll be honest, I don't have anything to give you in return -- yet. And I can't promise it'll be much. But I lost everything in Caranost while I was fleeing from the Orcs. They put up a good chase, so I kept dropping my things 'til I had nothing left to weigh me down.

'Could you retrieve what you can for me? I'd rather not rely on Rendal more than I need to.

'All I remember is running down those stairs west of here, before the Orcs caught up with me.''Oh... that's all that's left, then? Well, I'll figure something out.

'Here -- take this coin, and split it between you and Rendal. I still don't trust him much, but the two of you are the only folks who have ever shown me a bit of kindness.''No. I've already told Watcyn, I do not require a reward, coin or otherwise.

'By the way, ${PLAYER}, do you know why my belongings have been rummaged through?'

As you explain what happened, Rendal's frown softens.

'I see. Then this situation is my fault entirely, for I was not forthright about my identity.'The hunters from Bree, camped within the Midgewater Pass, asked you to take word south to The Forsaken Inn to alert the owner of the Inn that they will no longer need their rooms.Head south to the border of the Midgewater Marsh and the Lone-lands and seek out the owner of The Forsaken Inn, inform him that the hunters no longer need their rooms.

Sam Thistlebur asked that you make your way to The Forsaken Inn to tell the innkeeper that he no longer needs to save their rooms for them.Talk to Anlaf the Forlorn at the Forsaken Inn'This may seem a strange request, but it is one that I feel necessary.

'There is an inn on the border of the Midgewater Marsh and the Lone-lands, The Forsaken Inn. It is operated by a man named Anlaf. He was holding rooms for us as we meant to stay there for a few days before returning to Bree.

'With all that has happened, it is clear that we will not be making the journey south over the hills to visit the inn. Could you make your way there and let the innkeeper know that we will not be coming?''Sam Thistlebur? I do not recall the name. Of course there have been more folk passing through here than normal. Usually, there are very few pressing toward the east or coming from that way. Those dark shadows have caused this land to stir in ways I had not seen through most of my life.

'Their rooms are freed. Ha!''Anlaf is a queer sort, not the happiest fellow I have ever met. Still, he runs an adequate establishment and Leiva is one of the finest women I have ever met. Could you let them know that we will no longer need the rooms at The Forsaken Inn.'You have discovered an old map-page of some apparent historic significance upon an Orc slain in the Tarkrîp Assault Camp.Old map-pages can be found on Orcs in the Tarkrîp Assault Camp.

You should collect map-pages, for they look to be of some historic significance.Collect old map-pages from Tarkrîp OrcsOld map-pages can be found on Orcs in the Tarkrîp Assault Camp.

