These will surely be better off back in the hands of the people of Trestlebridge, rather than in the claws of the scheming Orcs.Aggy Digweed recalls a great explosion in town, and that no guards but herself were roused by the sound.A clue to the great boom heard in Trestlebridge may be found somewhere in town.

Aggy Digweed has asked you to search for the source of the mayhem that ruined Trestlebridge the previous night.Search Trestlebridge for the cause of the explosion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Captain Trotter can be found in Trestlebridge.

You should bring the powder you found to Captain Trotter.Bring the powder to Captain Trotter'I dare not abandon my guard post to investigate the carnage, but would you like to help? You could search the town and figure out how this could have happened.

'The explosion was deafening; why did no one wake? What caused this mayhem? I have never heard a thing like it in all my life....''What's this, then? Incendiary powder of some sort... how strange! Who would do such a thing?'Talbot Hinton claims he was not remiss in his guard duties the night of the attack, and that someone may have drugged him and the other guards.Orc encampments can be found to the north-east of Trestlebridge.

You should search Orc encampments for signs that the guards of Trestlebridge were drugged before the attack, proving Talbot's innocence.Talbot Hinton can be found in Trestlebridge.

At the Orc camps north of Trestlebridge, you were able to find cauldrons of a vile liquid, and collect some of the contents.Bring the sleeping draught to Talbot Hinton'Someone to hear me out at last! Yes, I was on guard duty the night of the blasts... but I did not fall asleep! Well, I did, but I cannot remember anything about it. It is almost like I was drugged.

'I only remember waking up to Aggy shaking me, fires roaring all around us. We all slept through the thunderous blasts. How do you explain that?

'But Captain Trotter will hear none of it....''You found something to prove that we were drugged? That is wonderful, ${PLAYER}! You must show the captain at once, so that he can set me free!'The ancient Dead have arisen within the Great Barrow.Accursed fell spirits can be found within the Flooded Wing of the Great Barrow.Defeat accursed fell spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Searching the Orc camp, you were able to find a wheel for Mattie Woodruff's cart. Although the wheel is a bit small, he thinks it should work well enough to get the cart and a load of lumber back to Trestlebridge.Elsie Woodruff is in Trestlebridge.

While Mattie and Noll fix the cart and load it with the lumber they've collected, Mattie asked you to go back to Trestlebridge and tell his wife that he's safe.'All right, while Noll here and I put this wheel on the cart, there's one last thing I'd ask you to do. Go back to Elsie in Trestlebridge and tell her that all's well here.

'Once the cart is fixed, Noll and I are going to take down a couple more trees and then bring our load down to the town. Of course, we couldn't have done that without your help! Thanks for that!

'Now hurry... won't do to stand around here waiting for Orcs!''I think we'll be fine here. Noll and I should be able to get this wheel on without too many problems.

'All I'd ask of you is to go back down to Trestlebridge and tell Elsie that we're all right!''Mattie and Noll are safe and sound? Oh, bless you! Bless you! That's the best news I've heard in many a day. I was fearing the worst, but I'm glad to hear my worries were for naught!

'I just hope they hurry up and get back to Trestlebridge! I don't think I'll get a bit of rest until I see them back.'Naerandir has told you he knows the story of Othrongroth, the Great Barrow, but that the reality of the place as it exists now must be masked beneath the splendour of legend, lest cautious fear grows into terror.The Great Barrow is at the crest of the hill beyond the small encampment. The first key fragment is guarded by two wights in the Great Barrow maze. The second key fragment is held by a Gaunt-lord elsewhere in the Great Barrow.

Naerandir asked you to enter the Great Barrow, Orthongroth to rid the tomb of evil. He provided you with a book to aid you on your adventure.

<rgb=#FF0000>The first half of the key is found in the Great Barrow -- Maze instance space, while the second half is found in the Great Barrow -- Thadur instance space.</rgb>A forge lay before a great door within the Barrows. It is here that the key will need to be reforged. It will take no skill, but certainly time, to reforge the key.

Consult Naerandir's book should you ever become confused about how to reforge the key.Refer to Naeradir's Book for help'Greetings, traveller! I came to these barrows to investigate a tale...do you wish to hear it? Have you heard of Othrongroth, the Great Barrow? It lies just at the crest of this hill, a place of dread in Bree-land.

'But it was not always so and perhaps need not remain so. Evil things stir in the Barrow-downs and threaten to turn cautious fear into abject terror. Perhaps you might be interested in restoring the peace of the Barrow-downs? In return, I will place you within my tale of this Great Barrow.

'You will need only a few things to venture deep within these halls to end the evil stirring in its heart. First, you will need friends, and a good many, for the enemies risen now within those halls are greater by far than any who walk these lands. The next are resolve and courage, for the fear these creatures will cast upon you is a thing of legend. The last are my notes...they will let you know what next to do.'Beyond the tunnels, heavy with mist and dust, down decrepit stairs built in an age before our own lay a door. The door leads to the final resting place of a great leader of Men, long dead, and a powerful shell claimed by the forces loyal to the Witch-king.

It was for safe keeping that the tinkers made the key before his tomb. A great door, replicated several times, to seal the dead beyond the reach of evil. Evil, it seems, proved too potent for mere metal to overcome. Yet something of power must remain for the key is split asunder in a way that reforging requries no tinker skills, one to be made whole at the forge where it was made.

Seek this forge at the foot of those decrepit stairs, in a pit before the great door.'Destroying the evil that lay within the Great Barrow will not prove easy. See that you keep your wits about you and your friends near.''Destroying the evil that lay within the Great Barrow will not prove easy. See that you keep your wits about you and your friends near.'Having obtained the two fragments of the key, you will need to seek the forge.

You will not need the skill to forge weapons, tools, or armour. The key desires to be remade again as it was meant to see that the Dead remained in slumber. Yet the Dead within will do what they can to see that the key is never remade.

When the hammer strikes the anvil your test will begin...pray to the Valar that you have brought friends who are true and stout enough to see you through.The ancient Dead have arisen within the Great Barrow.Ancient braziers can be found within the Flooded Wing of the Great Barrow.

You need to light the ancient braziers of the Great Barrow.Light the ancient braziers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The ancient Dead have arisen within the Great Barrow.Barrow-wights can be found within the Flooded Wing of the Great Barrow.Defeat Ancient Barrow-wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Barrow-wight Bowmen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elsie Woodruff was charged with acquiring the supplies needed to maintain Trestlebridge's barricades, but is now having trouble finding the supplies she needs.The stolen supplies can be found in the Orc camps to the north-east.

Elsie told you that the outlying farmers were supposed to be bringing some of the supplies she needs -- specifically a barrel of nails, a crate of hammers, and a crate of saws -- but their farms were overrun and their goods stolen. She has asked you to go to the Orc camps north along the Greenway and gather the supplies the Orcs scattered.'You there, I need your help! Our poor town is under threat of another attack from those foul Orcs. All of us are doing our part to help Trestlebridge survive, and I'm charged with getting supplies to maintain the barricades.

'The problem is that the outlying farmers were supposed to be bringing some of the supplies we need, only their farms were overrun by Orcs. They barely escaped and the Orcs scattered their goods. I would send for supplies from the south, but Orcs block that route as well. We need those stolen supplies!

'The three things we need are the barrel of nails they were carrying, a crate of hammers, and a crate of saws. The Orcs should have them at their camps to the north-east.''Oh wonderful, you've found the supplies! Thank you!

'There is something else though that I would have you do, if you would....'Halbarad of the Dúnedain organizes the recovery of the Rangers charged with defending Sarn Ford in the aftermath of the attack some days earlier.Rangers charged with the defence of Sarn Ford can use your assistance. Halbarad also requested that you recover a few caches of supplies from nearby, with which the Dúnedain will be able to restock Sarn Ford.Talk to Galasebdir to the north-east of Sarn FordTalk to Nethúr to the south-east of Sarn FordCollect Ranger caches not far from Sarn Ford (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Meneldir is at Sarn Ford, where he is helping his kin recover from the recent attack.Talk to Meneldir at Sarn FordThe earth has been kicked up at several locations near Sarn Ford, and Meneldir thinks you should examine some of those piles of dirt. He has a suspicion that the black riders left something behind, as they did at Herne.Meneldir's hunch proved accurate: the black riders left a token behind, and it likely drew the wights to Sarn Ford in the days following their attack.Halbarad is overseeing the recovery of the Dúnedain following the black riders' attack on Sarn Ford.

You retrieved a number of Ranger caches and should bring them to Halbarad.'You say you have a warning for me, Meneldir? Deliver it, then, and be away. We are still recovering from an attack upon the ford that left us scattered and in disarray, and I cannot spare much time for those who break their oaths.

'But I might have some use for your companion. ${PLAYER}, I ask you to aid the defenders of Sarn Ford and gather nearby Ranger caches; they were set aside to provide sustenance and supplies in the event they were needed, and in the aftermath of the attack they surely are!''${PLAYER}, I ask you to aid the defenders of Sarn Ford and gather nearby Ranger caches; they were set aside to provide sustenance and supplies in the event they were needed, and in the aftermath of the attack they surely are!''Ever since the terrible wraiths attacked the ford, we have endured the onslaught of the Dead. They rise and press the attack, and though we defeat them, always they return!''Ever since those terrible riders attacked Sarn Ford, we have heard the howls of wolves from nearby Ruddymore. Something has stirred them to frenzy, and they continually test our defences along the outskirts, as they never have before.''I have given Halbarad our warning, and though he does not wish to believe it, he says he has seen creatures bearing the White Hand in recent days. He thought they were led by one of their own kind, but our tidings have made him doubt.

'I have been thinking about something else, ${PLAYER}. Do you remember the token we found buried at Herne? What if the riders left a similar device behind here as well? I think we should look for one.''Do you remember the token we found buried at Herne? What if the riders left a similar device behind here as well? I think we should look for one.''I thought so. These creatures have a knack for stirring nearby creatures to madness, and for leaving disorder in their wake. Perhaps our removal of this token will slow the onslaught of the Dead upon the defenders here.''It seems I know what I am talking about, does it not?''Thank you for bringing back these caches of supplies. If it is true that Saruman and the other Wizards have turned against us...'

Halbarad shakes his head.

'It is not that I distrust your word, , but Meneldir broke his oath to the Dúnedain, and that is a matter of great shame for us. Not just for him, but for all of us. Is it not the failing of an entire village when one of its own is found wanting?

'But such is our need that I cannot turn even Meneldir away, as was my first instinct! The Rangers are scattered and in disarray, and I need every man! Aye, and every woman too/That goes for you too.'Grateful for the assistance you provided, Halbarad has agreed to tell you what befell at Sarn Ford just days past.Halbarad is at Sarn Ford.

Halbarad has agreed to tell you what befell the Rangers at Sarn Ford just days past.Talk to Halbarad and hear what befell the RangersHalbarad is at Sarn Ford.Talk to Halbarad at Sarn Ford'I will tell you what happened in the attack, ${PLAYER}, and then I have a task for you and Meneldir to accomplish. Evils walk the land, and I can deny none who are willing to help us fight them.''Night had fallen on the twenty-second of September when our courage was tested...''The number of the terrible wraiths was nine, ${PLAYER}, though not all those who defended Sarn Ford knew what that meant as I did. We defied those Black Riders for as long as we could, but that is not an evil against which any man, or any woman, can be expected to stand for long. I do not judge any who ran, or any who hid themselves; those of the Riders who did not pass into the Shire pursued the Dúnedain they found into the wild.

'There are still Rangers in the Shire, and I know they will do what they must to save the hobbits from these Black Riders. But more of my kin were scattered across Cardolan by those of the Riders that did not cross the Brandywine, and we will need their strength in the days ahead, if they still live.

'That is what I need from you and from Meneldir. I need you to track down survivors of the attack and learn how they fared in the days since my people were scattered like leaves in the wind. This will not cure Meneldir's shame, or restore his broken oath, but it may reveal the nature of his heart. If he bears any love for his former kin, let him show it by aiding them now!

'You, ${PLAYER}, are free to do as you will, but know that it will be of great help to the Dúnedain if you aid us in this, and I will not forget it.'When some of the Eglain fled from the goblins, they attempted to flee through the spider-infested valley beneath Minas Eriol. Many did not reach safety, and Hunulf wishes to burn their bodies, lest they suffer greater atrocities from the spiders.The corpses of the Eglain who failed to escape the spiders lie in the gorge beneath Minas Eriol.

Hunulf Munce asked that you burn the corpses of the slain Eglain beneath Minas Eriol.Hunulf Munce is at his encampment on the far eastern side of Minas Eriol.

You found several of the slain Eglain and burned their bodies. You should now return to Hunulf.Talk to Hunulf Munce'When the goblins came into Minas Eriol there was panic. Many ran towards the savages, and others fled through the valley beneath the ruins, hoping to escape the spears and sharp teeth of the goblins, only to fall prey to the spiders beneath.

'Those that entered the valley and did not emerge must be burned. It is only fair to save their bodies from the terror that awaits them. If you are willing, I will ask that you burn the corpses of the fallen.

'You will find the entrance to the valley north and to the west at the front of Minas Eriol, or over the bridge and through the goblins to the west.''The lost will not be forgotten. The goblins have wrought much pain upon my people, but not as much as others. The spiders in these lands are filled with true malice and an intelligence unseen.

'Your efforts give my mind some measure of ease. Thank you.''You can enter the spider's vale through the northern entrance, through the goblin-infested ruins west over the bridge, or through the eastern corridor to the north of the ruin-entrance there. Please, see that the dead are given proper rites.'The Dúnedain of Cardolan have posted a task to collect broken wood spears.You have accepted a task to acquire broken wood spears.Wanted: Broken wood spears from the goblins, half-orcs, and Orcs who trouble the folk of Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Wanted: Broken wood spears from the goblins, half-orcs, and Orcs who trouble the folk of Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Dúnedain of Cardolan have posted a task to collect coarse skins.You have accepted a task to acquire coarse skins.Wanted: Coarse skins from the beasts of Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Wanted: Coarse skins from the beasts of Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Dúnedain of Cardolan have posted a task to collect tough sword sheaths.You have accepted a task to acquire tough sword sheaths.Wanted: Tough sword sheaths from brigands and half-orcs in Cardolan. In addition, those who dare to brave Tyrn Gorthad might also recover these from barrow-wights. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Wanted: Tough sword sheaths from brigands and half-orcs in Cardolan. In addition, those who dare to brave Tyrn Gorthad might also recover these from barrow-wights. 