You should return to Naerandir and tell him that Sambrog is slain.Return to Naeradir outside of the Great Barrow'You have reforged the key! This step was necessary to complete your story and your foray into this terrible place. Now, you must return to the deepest parts of the Great Barrow and defeat Sambrog, the ancient wight-lord who makes the Barrow his home.''A better story I never could have composed. The tale of the hero, ${PLAYER}, who braved the greatest of challenges in Bree-land, who found glory and riches and fame.

'And so, my friend, you have lived the tale of Othrongroth. A great evil has been banished, and terror is laid to rest behind the cloak of heroic deeds.  

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Take this as a small reward.'Elsie Woodruff told you that her husband, Mattie, and her brother, Noll, left Trestlebridge in search of trees to fell for the barricades.Mattie Woodruff and Noll Tobbit should be found somewhere along the Greenway north out of Trestlebridge.

Elsie told you that she hasn't heard from either her husband Mattie or Noll Tobbit, her brother, since they left and asked you to look for them.'You see, the other thing needed for the barricades is wood. In the past we would fell trees in the Nan Wathren when we needed lumber, but now the Orcs lurk there.

'We were so desperate for lumber that my husband, Mattie, and my brother, Noll Tobbit, risked leaving Trestlebridge and went north along the Greenway proper in search of trees to fell. It has been too long since I've heard from them, and I'm worried something terrible has happened.

'Would you search north along the Greenway for them? I can't bear to think that something bad might have happened to them.''Mattie and Noll said they were going north along the Greenway, so hopefully you'll find them there! I'm so worried something terrible has happened to them!''So Elsie sent you? Well I'm glad for it!

'Well, we did run afoul of them Orcs... fortunate to have escaped with our lives, we are! But our cart here... well, it didn't get off quite as well, as you can see!

'No matter how many trees we fell, if we don't have our cart fixed we can't bring 'em back to Trestlebridge!'Naerandir's book explains the steps to cleanse the horrors of the Great Barrow.The forge lies within the Great Barrow.

Naerandir instructed you to remake the Barrow-key anew at the forge of Othrongroth.'I know that I promised you the story of the Great Barrow, but your tale has not yet ended. We need to finish the final chapter.

'Take these key-fragments into the Great Barrow and find the forge within. The key will require no skill to remake...only time, and that time will require the efforts of others to see that you live.'Aggy Digweed heard rumour of a man that was likely a half-orc slinking around Trestlebridge the night of the blast.The half-orc rumoured to have been in Trestlebridge can likely be found in the Orc camp north-east of Trestlebridge.

You should search for anyone matching Aggy Digweed's description.Search for the half-orc who planted the powderAggy Digweed is in Trestlebridge.

You should return to Aggy Digweed with news of your victory against Lugbas.Return to Aggy Digweed'The question remains as to how the suspicious powder got into town at all. We have many travellers here, being on the Greenway... and I did hear rumours of an ugly, mean-looking man that came through last night.

'I didn't see him myself, but he made a few folks uneasy. He was already gone when I went to look for him.

'Folks say he looked more than a little Orkish. Have you ever heard of such a thing?''You defeated the ugly brute? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We will have to be less welcoming to travellers, now, I'm afraid.

'If such a man could come unhindered and wreak such havoc, then we will never be safe. Orcs creep ever closer to our gates. These are dangerous times, my friend.'Three Elves journeying towards the Grey Havens came to the Barrow-downs after sensing the source of great corruption welling within the Great Barrow. Their sojourn into Bree-land will not end until they help cleanse the land of an ancient corruption before passing into the West.Othrongroth, the Great Barrow, is up the hill from the small encampment in the southern Barrow-downs. The fell spirits can be found within Othrongroth behind a door displaying a skull.

As one last favour before leaving Middle-earth, Aradia and her companions would like to help cleanse the Shadow of Angmar from the Barrow-downs. She has asked you to enter Othrongroth and send the fell spirits which dwell there back to their master.Defeat fell spirits in the Great Barrow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aradia is camped outside the Great Barrow.

You should return to Aradia with news of your success against the fell spirits of the Great Barrow.Talk to Aradia outside the Great Barrow'The Age of the Elves is over, ${PLAYER}, and now the time has come for us to pass into the West. But ere we come at last to the Grey Havens beyond the land of the halflings, we wish to do what little we can to help against the Shadow that is once again rising in the East.

'Long ago, the Witch-king of Angmar sent many fell spirits out of Angmar and Rhudaur to turn the Barrow-downs into a place of terror, and we sense that they are again stirring. We fear that more of these spirits have come with the intent of increasing their master's horde in Bree-land. We would have you enter the Great Barrow and send these spirits back to their master. The spirits will likely be found behind a door displaying a skull.

'Othrongroth, the Great Barrow, is a terrible dread place. You should not enter Othrongroth alone, for it is a dark and dangerous place. Take those you can trust.''Go forth with the blessing of the Elves and drive forth the enemies of the Free Peoples from Othrongroth and restore the Barrow-downs to the peace it once knew!''You have done well, ${PLAYER}; nevertheless, we shall sojourn here a short while longer to see that evil does not come to the simple folk of this land.'Halbarad has agreed to tell you of the night Sarn Ford was attacked.Halbarad weaves a tale of dread.Talk to Halbarad and hear his taleHalbarad weaves a tale of dread.Hear Halbarad's tale'My own heart was seized by a terrible foreboding, but I had the duty of command and would not abandon it. I want you to know this, ${PLAYER}, before I tell you the events that followed: these men and women that stood with me on that night... there was not a single drop of cowardice among them.

'But we had no idea what we would face on that night.'Hunulf Munce told you of many valuable treasures lost in the webs of the spiders beneath Minas Eriol.Beneath the ruins of Minas Eriol, to the west of Hunulf's encampment, lay a den of spiders. Many goods and valuables, necessary for the Eglain's continued livelihood have gone missing within.

Hunulf asked you to make your way into the dangerous valley beneath the goblin infested ruin of Minas Eriol. He warned that spiders there are in possession of many Eglan-treasures that must be recovered for his people.'Over the years, as we have studied and collected the items left in these ruins, we have earned a living for our people. Many of the goods that will help to purchase much needed items for our folk have been lost in the spiders' lairs over the years.

'If you are already entering the valley to assist us with the spiders, then I would ask that you take the time to reclaim these valuable treasures for us. You will likely find them wrapped in thick webbing, scattered throughout the valley floor.

'Cut through the webbing and find the valuable items and return them to me.''These treasures do not appear to be more than old tarnished coins, but they are valuable to many collectors. Customers from Bree will often purchase them from us by bartering food or other goods for these coins. Any soul diligent enough to search through these ruins will sooner or later stumble upon many of these coins.

'The Half-orcs in the north scour the ruins even now in such an effort.'Thousands of years ago, a princess put the dead to rest and saved the realm. Along the way, however, she lost everything.Rhiangar Nevit has asked you to listen to her tale of Luilloth.

Rhiangar can be found in Crossway House, the inn of Herne.Talk to Rhiangar to hear her tale of LuillothRhiangar Nevit has asked you to meet her near Dol Ernil.

Dol Ernil is in north-western Cardolan.Meet Rhiangar Nevit near Dol ErnilRhiangar Nevit has asked you to find a statue of Luilloth in Dol Ernil and to examine its base for clues.

The statue of Luilloth is in Dol Ernil.Search for the statue of LuillothUpon examining the statue of Luilloth you discovered an ancient scroll! You should bring the scroll to Rhiangar.

Rhiangar is by the roadside, near Dol Ernil.'My father was the main reason I returned, but he is correct in that I would have come back on my own now as well. I have been doing research into an ancient ruler of this land, Luilloth. Long ago, she served as princess-regent when her son was too young to take the throne. Luilloth was beloved by her people, and under her rule the land prospered.

'Cardolan was once a great and powerful place, with princes and princesses, knights and guild masters! Now, it is ruins, spirits, and dangerous creatures. The wild has taken back the rolling hills, the once great walls of fortresses are overgrown and being reclaimed by the Old Forest.

'Will you listen to my tale of Luilloth?''Luilloth was princess-regent of Cardolan thousands of years ago. She was known for her bravery, and for the kindness and wisdom with which she ruled while acting as regent until her son came of age. Not much of her story remains, however, but my mother told me tales of her when I was young. You see, my mother had travelled up to Dol Ernil before I was born. There, she read an inscription on the base of an ancient statue that said that Luilloth banished a scourge of wraiths that plagued the land.

'Father has shooed me away, and it turns out there is not much I can do here at the moment. I cannot safely travel within Dol Ernil, but I must know what is on the base of the statue! Perhaps it can help us understand what is happening now in Cardolan. Please! Let us go to Dol Ernil! I shall have to wait by the road where it's safer, but you could easily search for the statue!''Thank you for meeting me here! The statue of Luilloth is said to be among these ruins. I dare not tread there myself, but you are certainly capable and will be in far less danger, I am sure. Please look for the statue!''You return! I am glad to see you again, friend. What have you there?'

She takes the scroll from your outstretched hand and unrolls it carefully.

'This is incredible. Absolutely incredible. I can read some of it, but most of the words are so old, and I cannot make them out or decipher them. I recognize Luilloth's name, though! This scroll is about her, I am sure of it!'Gadaric, feeling that your efforts have been honest and true, believes you may be able to assist his brother Hunulf.Hunulf Munce is at the camp on the eastern side of Minas Eriol.

Gadaric Munce sent you to speak with his brother Hunulf.Talk to Hunulf Munce'Thus far you have proven true to your word. My judgment, however, is often clouded by my passion, and for this reason, I will send you on to my brother. He will know whether you are true of intent.

'You will find him by following the roadway east to where it begins to rise. There is a vale to the south that will lead to the back side of Minas Eriol. He is encamped there with others.

'Pass his test... perhaps you will earn our trust and earn passage to speak with one who knows much of what transpires now in these lands.''Seek out my brother, Hunulf, encamped at the east edge of Minas Eriol. You should follow the road eastward until it climbs steeply. Follow the path through the valley south of the road, then continue east towards the encampment.

'Speak with Hunulf. He will know how to better test you.''Gadaric sent you on to me? This is good news. My brother sought vengeance, it is true, and I swear to you just. We lost many when the goblins came here.

'Many are gone and still lost to us... it is good that you are here and willing to aid us.'Constable Bram Ashleaf, satisfied with your assistance, has another task for you.Deputy Osmann is at the camp on the east side of Minas Eriol.

Constable Bram Ashleaf sent you to aid his deputy. He thinks that you will be able to see that the deputy keeps his charges safe and also assist him in his various tasks.Talk to Deputy Osmann'You handled yourself very well against the Orcs, swine, and wolves. I think that you may be able to assist my Deputy.

'He headed out to the camp on the far eastern side of Minas Eriol. He is watching over one of the workers there and the brother of that ornery fellow, Gadaric.

'If you are interested in helping him out with the tasks I put before him, seek him at the camp on the far eastern edge of Minas Eriol.''Finding the camp may be a bit difficult. You need to head east along the road until it climbs steeply as it passes by Weathertop. When that happens follow the southern vale and wrap down toward the south and east. You should find it hidden up on a rise near the eastern entrance to Minas Eriol.''Bram sent me help?

'He sent me here to watch over this hobbit -- Old Mugwort -- who is proving to be far more difficult to watch than I like. He also wanted me to make certain that this fellow Hunulf was kept safe.

'Then I receive a message from him that he wants all these other problems handled and... well, thankfully you are here now.'The residents of Trestlebridge are all very shaken by the explosions and fires of the previous evening. Guards were nowhere to be found during the commotion -- all but Aggy Digweed, who showed a keen presence of mind during the attack.Aggy Digweed is at the Trestlespan on the northern edge of town.

According to Captain Trotter, Aggy Digweed was the only guard who may be able to shed light on the unfortunate circumstances that have befallen Trestlebridge.Find and speak with Aggy Digweed'I have half a mind to lock up every last guard in this sorry excuse for a town, after they let this catastrophe take place. Look at our town! People burned out of their homes, ash falling like snow....

'Aggy Digweed was the only one who kept her mind during this attack. If not for her, we would all be dead. Nobody even remembers what happened -- just Aggy, running to and fro trying to rouse everyone!

'I'll see that Talbot Hinton hanged for letting this happen! Mark my words.''Captain Trotter is very preoccupied with punishing those who slept through the attack, but I am much more concerned about what may happen if we let down our guard again.

'I have not slept in two days, but I will not abandon my post here. Would you be willing to help me?'The guides of Bree admit now that they should have been more cautious. Bob Redthistle believes now that they must do their part to destroy the fell creatures rising, as legend once told, throughout the Barrow-downs.The Great Barrow is at the southern end of the Barrow-downs.

Bob Redthistle has asked you to enter the Great Barrow and keep more wights from getting out. He recommended that you take friends with you.Defeat wights in the Great Barrow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bob Redthistle awaits your return at Dead Man's Perch, between the north and south Barrow-downs.

You should return to Bob Redthistle and let him know that you have destroyed many wights within the Great Barrow.Talk to Bob Redthistle at Dead Man's Perch'You've done good work dealing with those old wights, but I'll be honest with you, ${PLAYER}... these are creatures of legend! And the legend runs deeper than these mounds can provide.

'The Great Barrow, called Othrongroth long ago, has always been a place that few are brave enough to face, because of the legends of the powerful beings that once walked there. With the return of these legendary creatures throughout the Barrow-downs, I can only assume that more have risen within the Great Barrow. Othrongroth lies towards the southern end of the Barrow-downs.

'Stout or not, I'd not go it alone, if I were you. That Great Barrow is sure to be a bad place. Maybe you should take some friends?''Have you turned those Barrow-wights aside?''You are a valiant ${RACE}, my friend. You have succeeded where many would fail... truthfully, I would never dare.

'Thank you greatly for your help.  I believe that Bree is safer for your actions.'Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of broken wood spears to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect broken wood spears from the Orcs in the area surrounding Esteldín to the west. Once collected, you are to deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Broken wood spears from the Orcs to the west of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Broken wood spears from the Orcs to the west of Esteldín.'Good work, there are fewer of them capable of harming the people of the North Downs. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Nathan Hodges, at Amon Raith, awaits the collection and delivery of coarse skins.You have accepted a task to deliver coarse skins to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith in the North Downs. You can find the coarse skins from the beasts to the north of the ruin of Amon Raith.Wanted: Coarse skins from beasts to the north of Amon Raith. Deliver the items to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith.Wanted: Coarse skins from beasts to the north of Amon Raith.'I can make good use of these. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of tough carapaces to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect tough carapaces from the spiders in the area surrounding Esteldín to the west. Once collected, you are to deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Tough carapaces from the spiders to the west of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Tough carapaces from the spiders to the west of Esteldín.'We will find a use for these items. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Nathan Hodges, at Amon Raith, awaits the collection and delivery of tough sword sheaths.You have accepted a task to deliver tough sword sheaths to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith in the North Downs. You can find tough sword sheaths on Orcs north of Amon Raith.Wanted: Tough sword sheaths from the Orcs north of Amon Raith. Deliver the items to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith.Wanted: Tough sword sheaths from the Orcs north of Amon Raith.'This will certainly relieve us all of some of our fears. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Mattie Woodruff and Noll Tobbit did run into Orcs, but managed to escape unharmed. Their cart however was not as fortunate and needs a new wheel if they are going to use it to haul lumber back to Trestlebridge.The broken waggons were dragged off by the Orcs to their camp outside of Nan Wathren.

Some of the farmers, while escaping from the Orcs, were waylaid and their waggons were ruined. Mattie hopes that among the wreckage of the farmers' waggons you will find a wheel that he can use to fix his cart.'If we don't get a wheel for this cart, this lumber ain't going anywhere. I'd send you to Trestlebridge, but I doubt they'd have anything to spare. Every little bit there is precious.

'But there's some hope yet. See, there were some farmers escaping to Trestlebridge and their waggons got overrun by them Orcs. Well, their supplies were stolen and their carts broke up, but there might be a wheel from one of their carts that we can salvage.

'I don't think they dragged the carts into Nan Wathren, so I think you'll find the remains of them carts in that Orc camp straight east of here. If we're going to find a wheel to salvage, it'll be there, I'd wager!''Aye, you found one! This one looks like it'll work! It's a bit smaller than the other wheels, so the ride will be a bit rougher. But as long as we get this lumber to Trestlebridge, it won't matter how rough the ride is!'The ancient Dead have arisen within the Great Barrow.Sambrog can be found in the greatest depths of the Great Barrow.Defeat SambrogShades of oathbreakers, cursed to remain after life has fled, haunt the Fields of Fornost. They are deadly in their hatred of all things that live and breathe.Shades can be found in the western Fields of Fornost.

You should defeat shades in the Fields of Fornost.Defeat shades in the western Fields of Fornost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many shades in the western Fields of Fornost.CompletedShades of oathbreakers, cursed to remain after life has fled, haunt the Fields of Fornost. They are deadly in their hatred of all things that live and breathe.You have defeated many shades in the western Fields of Fornost.Haerandir wants you to help collect needed supplies to restock the camp of his sister and her husband.Boars and lynxes of the South Downs can provide the supplies for which Haerandir has asked.Collect meat from the boars of the South Downs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect hides from the lynx of the South Downs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Haerandir is outside Haudh Nirui, on the South Downs.Bring the boar-meat and lynx hides to Haerandir outside Haudh NiruiSirvellon is at Sírlond, east of Caranost proper.'My sister Maedhril married an Elf of Imladris. His name is Sirvellon, and he led an expedition south; even now the two of them have made camp near the abandoned city of Caranost. Their camp is called Sírlond.

'Theirs is a young love, only seven hundred years by my count, and sometimes I think they are blinded to the others' faults. Sirvellon is a fine Elf, but he is more short-sighted than my sister, and I fear he is so focused upon the Orcs that he will not obtain sufficient provision to keep the camp going.

'Perhaps you will help me obtain boar-meat and lynx hides from beasts here in the South Downs? Then we can send them along to Sirvellon and Maedhril, and I will worry less about them.''Perhaps you will help me obtain boar-meat and lynx hides from beasts here in the South Downs? Then we can send them along to Sirvellon and Maedhril, and I will worry less about them.''Yes, these will do nicely! This meat and these hides will help Sirvellon and Maedhril restock the provisions I am certain they failed to prepare.

'Bring them to Sirvellon at Sírlond with my regards, and tell him too that I maintain my watch upon the Blogmal goblins that creep in the South Downs. Sírlond is east of Caranost proper, to the south-west of here.''Bring that boar-meat and those hides to Sirvellon at Sírlond with my regards, and tell him too that I maintain my watch upon the Blogmal goblins that creep in the South Downs. Sírlond is east of Caranost proper, to the south-west of here.''These supplies are from Haerandir? They are welcome... but with reservation.

'My wife's brother is always doing this. "Sirvellon, I think you should do this," he says, and "Sirvellon, why did you not think of this?" If I had known the ways of her brother when I fell in love with my Maedhril... but no, it would change nothing. She has all of my love, and always will.

'It was her idea to send him scouting for goblins when the three of us came south, and it was very wise. Trust Haerandir to annoy me, even from afar! But the supplies are welcome. He is right on this point: our provisions are beginning to run out.'

Sirvellon sighs.

'And that is the worst annoyance of all, is it not? That my wife's brother was right once again!

'Are you married, ${PLAYER}? If you are not, heed well my advice: discover if your intended spouse has any siblings... and do so in advance!'Talbot has asked you to show the sleeping-draught you found to Captain Trotter.Captain Trotter can be found in Trestlebridge.

Talbot Hinton asked you to show Captain Trotter the strange potion brewed by the Orcs near Nan Wathren.Talbot Hinton is in the stocks in Trestlebridge.

You should free Talbot Hinton from his bonds, for his innocence is proven.Free Talbot Hinton from the stocksTalbot Hinton is in Trestlebridge.

You should speak with Talbot Hinton.Speak with Talbot HintonCaptain Trotter can be found in Trestlebridge.

You should speak with Captain Trotter once more.Return to Captain Trotter'Please, show the sleeping-draught to Captain Trotter. Then he will know I was not remiss in my duties.

'We have been sabotaged!'Captain Trotter listens to your explanation, and takes a deep sniff from the potion flask.

'The Orcs brewed this, did they? This is not good for us. It appears they have taken to using sabotage when their raids have been dashed against our defences at the Trestlespan.

'I suppose Talbot may be freed from his bonds. But the guards must be on the alert for any suspicious travellers from this point on. It is a sad day for Trestlebridge....''I cannot thank you enough for your help, good ${PLAYER}! I do not know if you have ever been thrown in the stocks... but I can tell you, it is not a comfortable experience.

'I do think Captain Trotter was ready to hang me for what happened. You have likely saved my life, my friend.''Humph, well then. I'm glad that debacle is over with. Perhaps now we can focus on more pressing issues....'Aggy Digweed has asked you to ensure that no more of the suspicious black-fire can find its way into Trestlebridge.Aggy Digweed is at the entrance to the Trestlespan at the northern edge of Trestlebridge.

You should speak with Aggy Digweed.Speak with Aggy DigweedOrc encampments have been spotted north-east of Trestlebridge.

You should investigate the Orc-camps for signs of the black-fire, and carefully destroy any that you find.Find the black-fire at the first encampmentFind the black-fire at the second encampmentFind the black-fire at the third encampmentAggy Digweed can be found in Trestlebridge.

You should return to Aggy Digweed with the news that you destroyed all the remaining crates of incendiary powder that you could find.Return to Aggy DigweedCaptain Trotter is in Trestlebridge.

You should speak with Captain Trotter.Return to Captain Trotter'Flaming powder! I like this not at all. I want to know how it came here, but more than that, I want to ensure that it never comes here again.

'Speak with Aggy at the span, and see if she knows anything of this... this... black-fire stuff! I have never seen anything like it.''So much... was it all destined for us? Or perhaps they were planning it to bring it along to Bree once we were all dead.

'Evil surrounds us, ${PLAYER}. This is a bad time, mark my words. I've never seen Orcs dare to come so close, or interfere with our lives other than scare travellers on the road. I've never seen such great numbers of them.

'You'll be wanting to tell Captain Trotter all about this.''Captain Trotter is right to be afraid of this... black-fire. It must be the Orcs that have been cropping up near here of late, to the north-east near the pass of Nan Wathren. Surely they have wrought some fell magic, and are using it to bring down our town and choke off the Greenway!

'We cannot let them, ${PLAYER}. They failed to destroy us once, so we must assume that they will try again. You cannot let them!''So the Orcs were behind it all, eh? But how did they come in, if nobody saw them?

'Hopefully you have ensured that they won't be back to the same mischief any time soon, which will give us time to rebuild, but there are still mysteries to be solved. How did they sneak the stuff in?'Haerandir is filled with disgust when he considers the Blogmal now inhabiting Haudh Nirui.Goblins now creep within Haudh Nirui, and Haerandir wants you to defeat as many of the creatures as you can.Defeat goblins at Haudh Nirui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Haerandir is outside Haudh Nirui.Talk to Haerandir outside Haudh Nirui'Goblins are like a flowering weed, friend: whenever we uproot them in one place, after a time we discover they have spread to another! Those of the Blogmal tribe are particularly troublesome, and it is of no real surprise to me that they have appeared here on the South Downs. They creep now among the ruins of Haudh Nirui, to the north-east.

'Will you help me end the threat posed by these Blogmal goblins? You will be doing the folk who live nearby a good service, for such creatures never stay where they begin, and a goblin-raid can be a frightening thing.''Will you help me end the threat posed by the Blogmal goblins that creep in Haudh Nirui, to the north-east? You will be doing the folk who live nearby a good service, for such creatures never stay where they begin, and a goblin-raid can be a frightening thing.''That was very good work, ${PLAYER}. The Blogmal will fear to speak your name from now on, I imagine. I am glad to have met you, for any foe of goblins is a friend of mine!'Long ago the towers of Caranost fell, but long was their proud vigilance.Though now crumbling, the towers of Caranost once watched over the land for miles and miles.Discover the lost towers of CaranostYou should discover the crumbling towers of Caranost.

Caranost is in western Cardolan.Discover the eastern towerDiscover the south-western towerDiscover the central towerDiscover the north-western towerLong ago the towers of Caranost fell, but long was their proud vigilance.Since no sign has been found of the potion-master who made the powerful sleeping draught, Captain Trotter has asked you to extend your search into a more dangerous territory: Nan Wathren.Nan Wathren lies to the north-east of Trestlebridge.

You should head to the pass of Nan Wathren to search for the source of Trestlebridge's troubles.Find and enter the dangerous pass of Nan WathrenYou have explored the edge of Nan Wathren.Completed'I wonder, ${PLAYER} -- did you even find the brewer of the foul potion while you explored the Orc-encampments?'

You tell Captain Trotter that you had no such luck.

'Ah. That is dire news indeed, for it means that the enemy's influence stretches further than I ever thought. I have a troubling notion that Nan Wathren has fallen to Orcs.

'The pass of Nan Wathren is a dangerous place in the best of times. If you wish to help Trestlebridge once and for all, you must wipe out the Orc presence from Nan Wathren.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Nan Wathren is a dangerous area. It would be wise to travel there in the company of a fellowship.</rgb>You have come to the edge of Nan Wathren.

You may enter if you wish, but it will be a dangerous path.Fell and foul barghests have taken to wandering the Fields of Fornost. They follow the dead, and they leave death in their wakes.Barghests can be found in the western Fields of Fornost.

You should defeat barghests in the Fields of Fornost.Defeat barghests in the western Fields of Fornost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many barghests in the western Fields of Fornost.CompletedFell and foul barghests have taken to wandering the Fields of Fornost. They follow the dead, and they leave death in their wakes.You have defeated many barghests in the western Fields of Fornost.A number of Tarkrîp Orcs have established encampments along the roads near Trestlebridge and the Greenway, posing a dire threat to the peoples of the western North Downs.Orcs can be found at their encampments just north-east of Trestlebridge.

You should defeat the Tarkrîp Orcs at their encampments.Defeat Tarkrîp Orcs at their encampmentsOrcs can be found at their encampments just north-east of Trestlebridge.

You should defeat the Tarkrîp Orcs at their encampments.Defeat Tarkrîp pickets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Tarkrîp raiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have cleared the Tarkrîp encampments threatening Trestlebridge.CompletedA number of Tarkrîp Orcs have established encampments along the roads near Trestlebridge and the Greenway, posing a dire threat to the peoples of the western North Downs.You have cleared the Tarkrîp encampments threatening Trestlebridge. The people of the North Downs are safer... for a time.The next step of Bingo's journey takes him to the town of Bree, where hobbits and Big Folk live together on the Bree hill.The town of Bree is to the east along the road from Newbury.

Bingo is ready to continue his journey, and wants to walk with you to the West Gate of the town of Bree.Travel to the West Gate of the town of BreeBingo has made a new friend at the West Gate of the town of Bree.Talk to Bingo at the West Gate of BreeMilo Goodbody is at the West Gate of Bree.

Bingo has made a new friend, a Bree-hobbit named Milo Goodbody, and you should speak with him.Talk to Milo Goodbody at the West Gate of BreeYou and Bingo have been invited to partake in the merriment at the Prancing Pony, and should speak to its proprietor, Barliman Butterbur.Talk to Barliman Butterbur inside the Prancing PonyBingo and Milo have made themselves at home inside the common room of the Prancing Pony.Talk to Bingo in the Prancing PonyBingo has invited you to eat, drink, and sing in the common room of the Prancing Pony.Sample some food from the large platters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Drink mugs of ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo is enjoying his stay in the common room of the Prancing Pony.Talk to Bingo in the Prancing PonyBingo has invited you to eat, drink, and sing in the common room of the Prancing Pony.Sample some food from the small platters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Drink mugs of ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo is enjoying his time in the common room of the Prancing Pony.Talk to Bingo in the Prancing PonyBarliman Butterbur is the proprietor of the Prancing Pony, and Bingo gave you his money-purse to ensure that he is well-paid for the hospitality.Milo Goodbody seeks to get your attention in the Prancing Pony.Talk to Milo Goodbody in the Prancing PonyBingo has asked you to join him on the table and dance!Barliman Butterbur is in the Prancing Pony, and your recent dancing exploits have convinced you that perhaps he deserves a few more of Bingo's coins.Milo Goodbody is waiting to speak with you in the Prancing Pony.Talk to Milo Goodbody in the Prancing PonyMilo told you that Bingo went outside to get some air, and might be sleeping in one of the haystacks in the stables near the Prancing Pony.Find Bingo somewhere outside the Prancing PonyThe Forsaken Inn is in the Lone-lands, east of Bree.

Bingo has decided that it would be best to continue his journey before spending any more time in revelry in the Prancing Pony.Travel to the Forsaken Inn, in the Lone-landsBingo is inside the unwelcoming common room of the Forsaken Inn, in the Lone-lands.Talk to Bingo in the Forsaken Inn'That was a nice visit after all, ${PLAYER}. Prisca eventually forgave me for whatever part I may have played in Marigold's decision to become a hero instead of a stay-at-home hobbit, and I enjoyed spending time with my many cousins. I jotted down their names in the margins of my manuscript so I do not forget them. Once again I marvel at how Prisca keeps track of them all!

'My feet are ready to once again set forth on the road! I consulted the map, and it seems the town of Bree should be our next stop. Let us walk to the west-gate of that town and take in the sights for a short time only, and then we will continue into the Lone-lands... and further adventure!''I will meet you at the West Gate of the town of Bree. I am ready for our journey to continue!''This is a much bigger town than I was expecting!''Always a pleasure to meet new folk!''Welcome to Bree, my new friends!''I have never been to Bree before, but I always heard there was something peculiar about the hobbits who lived here. This Milo fellow seems to be perfectly friendly, though! He has invited us to the Prancing Pony for a brief welcome in the main room, and I have gladly accepted. It is good to make new friends!''Milo has invited us to the Prancing Pony for a brief welcome in the main room, and I have gladly accepted. It is good to make new friends!''Welcome, welcome! I was just talking to Bingo here, and he was telling me about this journey of his. What an extraordinary fellow! It is only right that he experience the finest tavern in all of the Bree-land, wouldn't you say?

'You'll find the Pony just up the hill, and I think it would be a fine opportunity for some rest and merriment. After all, Bingo's adventure will soon take him into the wild, and there will be few opportunities for such revelry! Speak to old Barliman inside the Pony, and he will ensure we are provided with aught we might need.''The Prancing Pony is just up the hill, and it is a place of much merriment, with fine food and drink and many good folk, both Big and Little. Speak to Barliman and he will make sure to take care of us!''I will see you inside the Prancing Pony, ${PLAYER}!''Welcome to the Prancing Pony, friend! Make yourself comfortable, and do not be shy! Mister Boffin has already found a table in the main room, and told me to expect you.

'Please let me know if there is anything I can get you, and enjoy the food and the drink and the company!''Mister Boffin and Mister Goodbody are already in the common room. They did not wait for you to begin eating and drinking, but they said you would be along shortly so I thought nothing of it!''Ah, there you are! What a fine place this is, ${PLAYER}! Have some food and have some drink, and sing a song or three! There is plenty of each, and we should all add to the din with our melodies!

'Milo has been telling me some of this town's history, and he says that Bree was founded by hobbits before even the Shire! I do not know if that is so, but he certainly believes it. He is a good fellow, but I think he is wrong on this subject. I do not know where hobbits come from, but there are so many of us in the Shire, compared to Bree, that I think we must be the older.

'Eat, drink, and sing, my friend! This is no time for arguing, even if Milo is mistaken about his history!''Eat, drink, and sing, my friend! This is no time for arguing, even if Milo is mistaken about his history!''Magnificent, my friend! Your singing voice is quite something, and I am impressed at your ability to put away so much food and drink in so short a time! It is nothing compared to my own facility for such, of course, but still impressive!

'Are you slowing down? Unacceptable! More food, more drink, and more song! We must not insult the proprietor of this fine establishment!''Ah, what a remarkable singing voice! It seems you are becoming even more talented as our stay wears on, ${PLAYER}!

'Here, let me give you my money-purse. Can you be sure that Barliman receives sufficient coin to pay for our food and drink? We are a boisterous group, and it is only fair that he be well-compensated for his hospitality!

'While you see to that, I must tell Milo something. What was it? Something about hobbits, I remember that much! But what was it? It will come back to me, I am sure of it.''I gave you my money-purse. Can you be sure that Barliman receives sufficient coin to pay for our food and drink? We are a boisterous group, and it is only fair that he be well-compensated for his hospitality!'You give Barliman some coins from Bingo's money-purse and he accepts them graciously.

'Oh, thank you very much, that's more than generous. It is an honour and a pleasure to serve such fine folk as yourself and Mister Bingo, and Mister Goodbody is a regular patron, of course. Your party has been most good-natured. Often times I need to get people down from dancing on the tables, kicking crockery everywhere, but you have been fine customers indeed!''It is an honour and a pleasure to serve such fine folk as yourself and Mister Bingo, and Mister Goodbody is a regular patron, of course. Your party has been most good-natured. Often times I need to get people down from dancing on the tables, kicking crockery everywhere, but you have been fine customers indeed!''There you are! Bingo was asking around for you. He wants you to join him on the table and <rgb=#FF0000>dance</rgb>! There really was no arguing with him! You'll have to do it!''You and Bingo are good sports, ${PLAYER}! You are welcome in Bree anytime!''What's this? More coins? Ah, thank you, thank you! This is really not necessary.'

Barliman looks around conspiratorially.

'Your dancing was not THAT bad, ${PLAYER}! Ha! Ha! I mean no disrespect, of course, and thank you once again for yours and Mister Boffin's generosity!''Thank you once again for yours and Mister Boffin's generosity!''Bingo said he was feeling poorly, and he went outside to get some air. I expect you will find him sleeping in a haystack near the stables outside the Pony. I have woken up in those animal pens more than once, I can tell you!

'You should make sure he is feeling all right, ${PLAYER}.''Bingo said he wanted to get some air. I expect he is sleeping in one of the haystacks in the stables outside!''Oh my, ${PLAYER}... I do not feel very well. This may have been a poor idea!'

Bingo shakes his head groggily.

'I enjoyed making some new friends, but I must confess that this is not the most auspicious beginning for our journey! I think it is best that we leave the town of Bree and its renowned Pony behind us, or this is as far as my adventure will take me!

'According to the map, there is another tavern just inside the Lone-lands, to the east. Let us travel to that tavern and find rooms for the night. No more merriment, for now! That has proved even more dangerous to my journey than the Barrow-downs!''According to the map, there is another tavern just inside the Lone-lands, to the east. Let us travel to that tavern and find rooms for the night. No more merriment, for now! That has proved even more dangerous to my journey than the Barrow-downs!''Will you look at this place, ${PLAYER}?''I cannot imagine a more different common room than that of the Prancing Pony, ${PLAYER}! This one is oppressive and unwelcoming, for certain! It may be just as well, for the revelry and merriment of Bree's renowned Pony threatened to stall my journey there for good!'

<rgb=#00FF00>Bert Bartleby has arrived outside Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'The Last Treasure' (Recommended Level: 26)</rgb>A number of crates lie scattered throughout the Orc encampment north-east of Trestlebridge, likely looted from the town.Stolen crates from Trestlebridge lie scattered throughout the large Orc encampment north-east of Trestlebridge.

You should search the creates and collect treasure.The pages of the Founders Book have been scattered by the Orcs near Trestlebridge.

You should collect all of the missing pages from the Founder's Book.Collect all the missing pages from the Founder's BookMarla Shelton is back in Trestlebridge.

You have found the Founder's Book and should bring it back to Marla Shelton.A number of crates lie scattered throughout the Orc encampment north-east of Trestlebridge, likely looted from the town.

You should search the crates and collect anything that should be returned to the devastated town.'The Founder's Book! I never thought to see it again. It is in rough shape, but I think you found most of the torn out pages.

'I'm sure I can repair it. Thank you, ${PLAYER}! I had given it up for lost.'Defeat Trolls in the Lone-lands.Defeat Trolls in the Lone-landsDefeat many Trolls in the Lone-lands.Defeat Trolls in the Lone-landsAfter encountering the elusive Orc, Borhashat, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Gaerion can be found at Sírlond in Cardolan.

You have acquired a trophy from an elusive foe in Cardolan. You should deliver it to Gaerion, a trophy-hunter and lore-keeper of the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Deliver Borhashat's quiver to Gaerion in CardolanAfter encountering and defeating the elusive Orc, Borhashat, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Dúnedain of Cardolan.

As you inspect Borhashat's quiver, you take note of dark stains at the base of the quiver. Did Borhashat revel in plucking the arrows from his freshly-slain prey? Are the Orcs' foul poisons so corrosive that they might seep through leather itself? No matter the truth of it, it is good that Borhashat will no longer trouble the folk of Cardolan.

You should bring this trophy to Gaerion, a trophy-hunter and lore-keeper of the Dúnedain of Cardolan.'Hail, friend. What have you found?'

Gaerion inspects Borhashat's quiver closely, taking care not to touch the stained portion of it with his bare hands. He pulls a long, black arrow from the quiver and its tip drips with some vile poison. After a moment, he carefully lowers the arrow back into the quiver.

'If this is the quiver of the Orc I suspect, you have done the Dúnedain a great service this day. I cannot say for certain, but I believe he was of the Tarkrîp clan. They delight in the slaying of Men and have troubled my kin and I every time our paths have crossed.

'To my mind, there is little that strikes fear into the hearts of Orcs, but perhaps this quiver will help us to ward them away from our encampments. Thank you, friend!'A number of cruel crebain have settled in alongside the Tarkrîp Orcs, waiting to feast upon the corpses of Men when the Orcs have had their say.Cruel-beaks can be found in and around the Tarkrîp Orc encampments north of Trestlebridge.

You should defeat a number of these cruel crebain.Defeat cruel-beaks near Trestlebridge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of the invading crebain.CompletedA number of cruel crebain have settled in alongside the Tarkrîp Orcs, waiting to feast upon the corpses of Men when the Orcs have had their say.

These merciless birds should be driven off, for they fill you with an unpleasant sense of foreboding.You have defeated a number of the invading crebain.Spiders in the valley beneath Minas Eriol have preyed upon the Eglain for a long time.Spiders can be found in the valley beneath Minas Eriol, north-west of the Eglain over-look.

Hunulf Munce believes that you can take the eyes from the Moor-web spiders beneath Minas Eriol, depriving them of their strength.'Long has evil flourished in the dark places of the world, and creatures spawned in those shadows come forth to trouble the Eglain.

'Spiders, a kind which we call vile-fang and shadow-weaver, make their home in the valley beneath the ruins of Minas Eriol, north-west from this camp. Their staring eyes ensnare all who gaze upon them. Pluck out their eyes and you remove their power.

'If you are willing to face them, I would ask that you find the spiders beneath Minas Eriol and take their eyes from them, black as pitch and crimson as blood.''You have proven a great friend to my people, ${PLAYER}. I will keep these for now.

'My brother and I were sent to the west in search of assistance. The Eglain are in grave danger and need more assistance than our kin can provide. Already there is one who visits us, following Black Riders out of the west, but even he has been given pause upon seeing the red waters of the swamp near our home.

'We face a danger greater than the Orcs, goblins, and evil dwarves together. I will leave the rest for my elders to explain. You have earned this reward, friend.'A harried graverobber begs for assistance in lifting a potentially deadly curse... again.Arnail has asked you to return a stolen necklace to a barrow near Dol Ernil.

Dol Ernil is in north-western Cardolan.You should let Nan Mabli know that you have returned the stolen necklace to the barrows.

Nan Mabli is near the barrows south of Dol Ernil.Return to Nan Mabli'Oh, uhm, hello there. Well, I need your help again.'

Nan Mabli says, 'That's right he does! This layabout lied to you, didn’t he?'

She nudges her grandson with her boot. He groans and nods vigorously.

'I, uhm, forgot to give you one of the items I… borrowed from the tombs. I tried to return it, I really did! But, well, the spirits within are so riled up that I can't enter the tomb to return it.

'Here! Take it! I never want to see it again!''Blue eyes, like the sapphire of the necklace. I see them in my dreams. I see them when I close my eyes! She is always watching me. Always.''You're back! Excellent. I do not hear the excessive moaning and groaning that was coming from the tombs, so it seems you were successful. Thank you for putting the spirits back to rest. I hope that my grandson has learned his lesson.'In Annunlos lay a ruin, long abandoned by the Eglain. Picked clean and having only the depths of the ruin unexplored, the Eglain left the tombs beneath the ruin be, as is their custom. However, the ruin now teems with life again as dwarves, in league with Orcs, scour the ruin for treasures in the depths.The Dourhands can be found within the ruins of Thandobel, south of Refr Quicksilver.

The Dourhand dwarves have forsaken their ties to their brethren by consorting with Orcs. Refr Quicksilver has asked you to bring vengeance upon the Dourhands in the name of the Free Peoples and to bring him a trophy of their axes.Collect Dourhand axes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Refr Quicksilver waits for you at the entrance to the cave, south of the Great East Road in the Lone-lands, north of Thandobel.

You should return to Refr Quicksilver with news of your victory against the Dourhands and bring him the axes you took as trophies.'This dwarf is not one to brook betrayal, and I know now that the Dourhands are betrayers to all the Free Peoples. Consorting with Orcs is deserving of only one punishment.

'I'll not say that I am pleased by this situation, ${PLAYER}, nor will I look an opportunity side-long when it stares me in the face. Dwarves or not, these Dourhands need to be dealt with, and you seem to be more than suitable to the cause.

'I have a request of you, then. Return to Thandobel and wreak vengeance upon the Dourhands in the name of all the Free Peoples. But let us see something good come out of this evil. Bring me the axes of the Dourhands, for metal is not evil, and dwarf-metal can be used to the benefit of us all!''Bring me those axes, ${PLAYER}!''Ha! Fine iron indeed. Not as comely as other weapons but still made by dwarf-hands and crafted with care. I shall smelt the ill deeds from these weapons and craft them newly into arms and armour for all to use.

'Do not see shame in what you have done, but gain strength from the knowledge that you have done your part to stop the spread of evil.'The disturbed tomb in this clearing seemed to shimmer briefly with an odd eeriness. Perhaps it was only a trick of the light, but you should investigate more closely.The strange tomb can be found north-west of Mincham's Camp, in the Fields of Fornost.

You should investigate the strange tomb.Investigate the strange tombThe strange tomb can be found north-west of Mincham's Camp, in the Fields of Fornost.

You should investigate the strange tomb.Investigate the strange tombYou have dispersed Morrafn's fell light from this haunted place.CompletedThe disturbed tomb in this clearing seemed to shimmer briefly with an odd eeriness. Perhaps it was only a trick of the light, but you should investigate more closely.You have dispersed Morrafn's fell light from this haunted place.Passage through the Lone-lands has become difficult with the arrival of goblins. Worse still are their pets, the fearsome Wargs who roam the plains and attack unwary travellers.Lynx can be found throughout Nain Enidh -- the central Lone-lands -- north and north-east of the encampment at the east edge of Minas Eriol.

Old Mugwort believes he has come up with a way to drive goblins and Wargs from the Lone-lands, but he needs you to collect lynx-meat first.'The folk at The Forsaken Inn are not the wealthiest sort here, friend. We barely make our lives comfortable, and the goblins overrunning the eastward stretch of road have turned the inn into a lonelier place than ever. If you've time to offer, there's work to be done!

'Our fortune is about to change, though -- I've devised a way to make the road safe! Kill the creature at the top, and the rest will turn aside! 

'I need some help making this work. If you're willing, head north or north-east into the brush and get me some lynx-meat. Everyone knows that dog-like things eat cat-like things. Get just enough meat to make a meal for a Warg or two! What's wrong? Lynx are deadly creatures when angry, and their meat will serve my purposes nicely. Don't you want to end the threat of goblins and Wargs? Then get out there and hunt some lynx! No excuses! We'll be killing two lynx or Wargs with one stone! Ha ha ha!''This one is a bit tough and this one a bit tender. Hmm... no matter, they'll all go into the grinder nonetheless! A pinch of sickle-fly eyes, a dollop of gooey crawler-flesh. Really tasty things, crawlers.

'This will take me a while, I'm afraid.'Amarion has asked you to offer assistance and company to Orthonn, a Ranger tasked with manning a lonely post in the wilds of Annúndir.Orthonn can be found at his encampment just over the river in Annúndir, not far from the road.

You should find and speak with Orthonn.Find and speak with Orthonn'What a help you have been to us, ${PLAYER}! I imagine that with the Wargs driven off, we can put this area back to right.

'I must ask one last thing of you. My friend, Orthonn, watches over Annúndir from a lonely post. Very few folk come his way. Would you check to make sure that he fares well, and offer him news of the western Downs while you are there?''Hail, stranger! Ah, Amarion sent you? What news from Amon Raith?'A report of the activity at Amon Firn must be brought to the Ranger Taeras.Calargyl has asked you to bring a report to Taeras of what occurred at Amon Firn.

Taeras is at the Scurloc Farm, in north-eastern Cardolan.Talk to TaerasTaeras has suggested that you speak with Edrud Scurloc.

Edrud is at the Scurloc Farm, in north-eastern Cardolan.Talk to Edrud'You have acted admirably in the defence of Cardolan, but I would impose a boon upon you, if you are willing. I need to make a report of the activity that we have seen here, but I also do not think it is time yet to give up my post.

'Will you bring word of what you saw and did here to my companion Taeras? He has gone on ahead to a farm that is west of here, chasing troubling rumours.''Well met. I am indeed Taeras. You may give me Calargyl's report.'

You tell Taeras what transpired at Amon Firn.

'Troubling times these are, but glad I am that we have one such as yourself to aid us. You have come at a fortuitous time to this farmstead as well. I came after hearing rumours of goblins and displaced farmers. We Rangers do what we can to shield these folk from outside intrusions, but our number are few and the enemies are many.

'Go and speak with the Scurloc and Hove families, if you have not yet already done so. They definitely could use your help.''Who are you?! What do you want? We might be missing folk, but I won't let you take what's left!

'Oh, you're not here to steal anything? I suppose you don't look like a goblin.'

She takes a shuddering breath and her shoulders slump.

'Aye, I am Edrud Scurloc. If you've come to help, you're just in time.'In the shadow of Amon Sûl, at the edge of Nain Enidh, lays an Arnorian ruin. Those ruins afforded the Eglain a wealth of material to trade with collectors in Bree-land... until the arrival of half-breeds from the South.Naerost lies just east of Amon Sûl, north of Hunulf Munce.

Hunulf Munce has asked you to seek out and slay the hirelings who guard the relics packed for shipment and return as many of the relics as you can to the Eglain.Collect stolen crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat half-orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hunulf awaits your return at the east edge of Minas Eriol, near the bridge over the gorge.

You should return with the recovered relics to Hunulf Munce.'Many lost their lives when the half-orcs raided Naerost. Since then, we have struggled greatly. Most recently, as you likely know, we lost the ruin to goblins forced through the mountains in the north. 

'Yet the half-orcs came first, and they slaughtered our people, stole our livelihood, and began despoiling the ruin. We do not know why, but we know they have collected many relics within the ruins and have packed them for delivery to the South.

'If you are willing, I would ask you to enter Naerost and seek the hirelings who guard the relics and slay them. Bring back any of the relics you find.''The half-orcs are vile creatures, the result of breeding between Man and Orc. They are a blight in these lands and the world at large. Their murderous and thieving nature requires some manner of retaliation, even if the hour of its coming is late.''We will ensure that none of these relics were taken from the tombs of the men who perished within the ruins in ages past. If they are not, they will be used to feed and clothe our people. If they prove to be stolen from tombs, they will be buried once more to honour the fallen.

'You have proven yourself a brave and honourable warrior, ${PLAYER}, and your aid is valued by the Eglain.'Burglars throughout Eriador consider themselves members of a secret club, an exclusive brotherhood of those who practice the art of stealth.A burglar named Ponto is somewhere in Oatbarton, the hobbit-village on the very northern border of the Shire, almost in Evendim.

