You have encounted Achassoth, a terrifying being in the Fields of Fornost. This ghostly entity has grown in bloodlust from having pulled the life from the lands around it.'Come closer, warm creature. Closer.'You have defeated one of the chief forces of evil in the Fields of Fornost, bloodthirsty Achassoth, killer of Men.Candaith's investigation into the whereabouts of Radagast the Brown led him to the discovery that he is under the protection of the Eglain. He has spoken well of you to one of their members, Gadaric Munce, but warned that they would not provide the location of the Lore-master in Brown without assurance that you have good intentions.Ride Candaith's horse or make your way on foot to The Forsaken Inn on the border of the Midgewater Marsh and the Lone-lands along the Great East Road.

Candaith thanked you for your assistance and warned that the Eglain must be made to understand that your intentions are just before they will allow you an audience with Radagast the Brown.Talk to Gadaric Munce at The Forsaken InnFind a member of the Eglain and ask him for the whereabouts of Radagast the Brown.

You have worked long and hard to obtain the trust of the Eglain. Now, you must ask them the whereabouts of Radagast the Brown.Find and speak with a member of the Eglain in The Forsaken Inn or their camp in Nain Enidh'I managed to track Radagast south and there met friends, the Eglain, who make some ruins here in the Lone-lands their home. They are a solitary and quiet people, having shunned societal obligation for a simple life eked out here. The few that do venture towards the more civilized areas of the world are still different than most you will ever meet.

'Because of this nature, they are truly wary of anyone who wishes to traffick with them or their allies, and it seems that Radagast has enlisted their aid, not only now, but at some time in the distant past. I fear that you will need to earn the right to speak with Radagast.

'I have done what part I can. My horse will take you south and west to The Forsaken Inn. There, you should seek an audience with Gadaric Munce. He will know your name. Be safe, ${PLAYER}.''You have toiled long, and we are grateful for all you have done. You appear to have the best intentions towards our people. For this, we will grant you the request you ask.''Candaith is a good man who has taken a chance by giving us his word that you can be trusted. For his sake, and our continued friendship with him, I hope that you are worth the risk.

'We are a simple people who wish to remain apart from society, but there are efforts that all must undertake to survive, and we will ask you for assistance to prove that you are worthy.''You may use my horse or walk to The Forsaken Inn. It is located south-west from here on the border of the Midgewater Marsh and the Lone-lands along the Great East Road. You must speak with Gadaric Munce and begin earning the trust of the Eglain.'Halbarad has charged you with rendering aid to those of his kin who were scattered across the South Downs following the attack on Sarn Ford by the Black Riders.Meneldir is at Sarn Ford.

Meneldir is eager to set forth in search of his scattered kin.Talk to Meneldir at Sarn FordElves camp east of the river near Caranost.

Meneldir believes that some of the scattered Rangers likely made their way for one of the Elf-camps across the river from Caranost.Search for scattered Rangers at an Elf-camp across the riverHandarod rallies the Rangers at Sírlond, an Elf-camp across the river from Caranost, the old capital of Cardolan.Talk to Handarod at SírlondDangerous foes stalk the South Downs, making it difficult for scattered kinfolk of the Ranger Handarod to make it to Sírlond. He has asked you to do what you can to help.Defeat foes in the South Downs that endanger the scattered Rangers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ranger Handarod is at Sírlond, waiting for word of your success in the South Downs.Talk to Handarod at SírlondHandarod believes other Rangers gather at Scurloc Farm, to the north-east.Find the Rangers that made for Scurloc Farm, to the north-east of CaranostRanger Malenfang watches over Scurloc Farm, in the South Downs.Talk to Malenfang at Scurloc Farm'Many of my kin were scattered across the South Downs in the wake of the attack, and I fear at least four of the Black Riders may harry the Rangers among the hills. Save the Dúnedain you can, help them recover from their injuries, and restore what safety you can to the South Downs.

'If you see the wraiths... hide, if you can, but run, if you must. There is a power and an evil about them I have never seen before.''Save the Dúnedain you can, help them recover from their injuries, and restore what safety you can to the South Downs. If you see the wraiths... hide, if you can, but run, if you must. There is a power and an evil about them I have never seen before.''Any search of the South Downs should begin near Caranost, ${PLAYER}. It commands a view of the surrounding lands, and I believe any Rangers seeking to return from their escape will make for it.

'When last I walked the rolling hills of the South Downs, there were Elves camped east of the river, just on the other side of Caranost. Let us begin our search there.''When last I walked the rolling hills of the South Downs, there were Elves camped east of the river, just on the other side of Caranost. Let us begin our search there.''Hail!''It is good to see friendly faces after the days we have had! Rangers assemble here to recover from their wounds, and so far we have remained beneath notice of the terrible shadows that chased us from Sarn Ford. We are the lucky ones... not all of my friends have been so fortunate.

'If you can thin the numbers of our foes in the surrounding areas, other Rangers may be able to make it here to Sírlond.''If you can thin the numbers of our foes in the surrounding areas, other Rangers may be able to make it here to Sírlond.''I am grateful for your help, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps more of my kin will be able to make it here to Sírlond, thanks to your efforts.

'Word has reached me of another gathering-place of the Dúnedain, at Scurloc Farm to the north-east. I would ask you to travel there and lend them similar aid, for the betterment of us all. Those wraiths remain abroad, and they have slain many of my friends already.'Malenfang nods as you approach.'Handarod sent you to us? I am glad he still lives... too many of my folk were scattered into the wild by the attack of the terrible Riders, and some were slain even as they ran. Those who survived made for this farm, and there must be other safe havens, as well.

'Safe, did I say? No place is safe! I have not seen any sign of the Riders for two days, but there are Orcs and half-orcs gathering in the South Downs, and they are ever a threat.'The Ranger Malenfang has learned enough of the activity of his foes in the South Downs to be worried.Half-orcs can be found near Amon Firn, in the South Downs.

Malenfang has asked you to search for any orders the half-orcs might be carrying.Defeat half-orcs at Amon Firn and find any orders they might be carryingYou should read the scrap of parchment you found on the half-orc's body.Read the half-orc ordersMalenfang is at Scurloc Farm, waiting to see any of the half-orc orders you might have recovered.Malenfang believes that you might find more information about the shared purpose of the half-orcs and the goblins at the ruins of Haudh Nirui, north-west of Amon Firn.Search Haudh Nirui for scraps of orders to the goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The orders you recovered have been torn to scraps by the goblins of Haudh Nirui, and will need to be properly sorted and reconstructed before they can be read.The table at Scurloc Farm will serve as a good place to sort the scraps of the orders you recovered.Sort the papers on the table at Scurloc FarmThe table at Scurloc Farm will serve as a good place to sort the scraps of the orders you recovered.Sort the papers on the table at Scurloc FarmThe table at Scurloc Farm will serve as a good place to sort the scraps of the orders you recovered.Sort the papers on the table at Scurloc FarmYou have reassembled the scraps of the orders to the half-orcs and goblins of the South Downs, putting them into a readable form that seems to make sense.Examine the reconstructed orders on the table at Scurloc FarmMeneldir has arrived, and will want to see the orders you reconstructed.Talk to Meneldir at Scurloc Farm about what you have learned'Half-orcs gather around the base of Amon Firn, the Deadmount, a place of ill omen to the east, and some of them have dared venture near to this farm. I suspect they may hold orders that guide their movements.

'Find these orders, if they exist, and return to me with what you find. When we know what they seek to achieve, and how their movements align with those of the Black Riders that attacked us, we will be better able to oppose them.''Half-orcs gather around the base of Amon Firn, the Deadmount, a place of ill omen to the east, and some of them have dared venture near to this farm. I suspect they may hold orders that guide their movements.

'Find these orders, if they exist, and return to me with what you find. When we know what they seek to achieve, and how their movements align with those of the Black Riders that attacked us, we will be better able to oppose them.''You found some orders on a half-orc? You should read them and see what we can learn of their plans in this area.''Half-orcs working with goblins? It sounds as if neither side is very happy about it, but I cannot tell from this what their overall scheme might be, or for whom they toil. A half-orc held the quill that penned these orders, I believe, not one of those terrible Riders... but for whom did the half-orc write them?

'If the author of these orders is to be believed, we might learn more from the goblins that dwell at the ruins north-west of Amon Firn. Haudh Nirui, those are called. Let us hope the goblins are as careless with their own orders as the half-orcs believe them to be!''If the author of these orders is to be believed, we might learn more from the goblins that dwell at the ruins north-west of Amon Firn. Haudh Nirui, those are called. Let us hope the goblins are as careless with their own orders as the half-orcs believe them to be!''Good luck to you as you sort through all those papers, ${PLAYER}. I will wait for your summary!''Good luck to you as you sort through all those papers, ${PLAYER}. I will wait for your summary!''Good luck to you as you sort through all those papers, ${PLAYER}. I will wait for your summary!''Good luck to you as you sort through all those papers, ${PLAYER}. I will wait for your summary!''You have sorted through all the papers? Well, what do they say?''Let that be a lesson to you goblins, then: the big ones have ways of dealing with treachery, and if you work against their goals, what happened to the last batch can happen to you and yours, as well! You'll be told what you need to know when you have need of it, and not before. The Dark Lord will repay us for our service; why else would the very Wisest throw their lot in with him, even as we have done?

'The dwarves will be easily-manipulated. They will follow Skorgrím wherever he leads them... no matter who leads Skorgrím. I trust the gaunt-lord can do this, and that should be enough for you lot. The attack will come from both directions: down from the Blue Mountains, and up the Greenway from across the old barrows. Even now the Witch-king works to raise the spirits of the Dead. With the aid of the Grey Fear, none will stand against him, or against us. It was the Fear that laid waste to the old kingdom that once stood here, and see what little of that remains!

'The shadow rises in Angmar, but it needs time to gather its strength. Not much time... but time all the same. That's what we're for, my gang and you lot. Just don't get in the way of the Riders, or the Grey Fear... no one would save you then, and you wouldn't want them to... you would just yearn for death. What the Fear would do to you doesn't bear thinking about.

'So you stay out of their way. These are the Dark Lord's most valued servants. You and me are just worms to such as them, and worms can get squashed, if they haven't got brains enough to get clear. We'll be called on when we're needed.''I don't like the sound of that, ${PLAYER}. Not only do servants of the White Hand move openly in Swanfleet, but in Cardolan and beyond there are other powers at work: the Witch-king and the Black Riders, goblins and half-orcs making common cause, and now a dwarf-rebellion led by someone named Skorgrím? Judging from his name he is no Longbeard, but if he leads an army out of the Blue Mountains we will be hard-pressed to deal with him, no matter who he might be.

'But there's something else, too. These orders speak of something called "the Grey Fear." That is a familiar title, but I cannot remember why, and that worries me.'Maedhril has a plan to deal with the Orc-archers, and it involves both your help and a very large fire.Maedhril asked you to defeat Caranost scouts and retrieve their bows.Collect Orc-bows from Caranost scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The tower overlooking the bridge at Caranost holds a large bonfire at which Maedhril wanted you to burn the Orc-bows.Maedhril is at Sírlond, east of Caranost proper.Talk to Maedhril at Sírlond'The Orc-scouts that prowl throughout Caranost carry bows with which they have proven quite deadly. Defeat these scouts and gather up their bows. Then climb to the tower from which you could spy on Sírlond, and burn the bows in the fire the Orcs built.

'I will watch for the smoke of the burning, and so I will know when the Orcs have received the message. What message? Simply this, my helpful messenger: that their archers will not be allowed to strike us from afar.''The Orc-scouts that prowl throughout Caranost carry bows with which they have proven quite deadly. Defeat these scouts and gather up their bows. Then climb to the tower from which you could spy on Sírlond, and burn the bows in the fire the Orcs built.

'I will watch for the smoke of the burning, and so I will know when the Orcs have received the message. What message? Simply this, my helpful messenger: that their archers will not be allowed to strike us from afar.''The Orc-scouts that prowl throughout Caranost carry bows with which they have proven quite deadly. Defeat these scouts and gather up their bows. Then climb to the tower from which you could spy on Sírlond, and burn the bows in the fire the Orcs built.

'I will watch for the smoke of the burning, and so I will know when the Orcs have received the message. What message? Simply this, my helpful messenger: that their archers will not be allowed to strike us from afar.''I saw the smoke, ${PLAYER}. Let that be a message to them.

'You have my thanks, and those of my husband as well. We have been here for several days, but this is the first that I feel we may be turning the tide against the Orcs that dwell in Caranost.'Caranost is full of Orcs, and the Elves at Sirvellon's camp-site are eager to do something about it.Caranost warriors can be found west of Sírlond, throughout the city.Defeat Caranost warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sirvellon is at his camp of Sírlond, east of Caranost proper.Talk to Sirvellon at Sírlond'If you come in peace and bear a helpful heart, then I welcome you to Sírlond. My wife Maedhril and I established this camp here among the ruins of Caranost to combat the evils that threaten the old city and the surrounding lands, and our numbers have only grown in recent days. Rangers fled here following an attack upon the river-crossing to the west, and others were drawn hither by the light of our fire. I welcome all as I welcomed you.

'To the west, a long bridge leads into Caranost proper, where Orcs dwell in great number. If you wish to help us, you will take up arms against their warriors. Many of those who shelter here bear injuries that prevent them from bringing the fight to the Orcs, but I see that you are no stranger to combat, and do it well.''To the west, a long bridge leads into Caranost proper, where Orcs dwell in great number. If you wish to help us, you will take up arms against their warriors. Many of those who shelter here bear injuries that prevent them from bringing the fight to the Orcs, but I see that you are no stranger to combat, and do it well.''I heard the fighting from here, ${PLAYER}, and I know the Orcs now count fewer warriors among their number. You have my thanks.'The Dúnedain of Cardolan have posted a task to collect piles of dim dust.You have accepted a task to acquire piles of dim dust.Wanted: Piles of dim dust from the Dead who have returned to trouble the lands of Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Wanted: Piles of dim dust from the Dead who have returned to trouble the lands of Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Dúnedain of Cardolan have posted a task to collect tough carapaces.You have accepted a task to acquire tough carapaces.Wanted: Tough carapaces from spiders, crawlers, and other loathsome insects of Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.Wanted: Tough carapaces from spiders, crawlers, and other loathsome insects of Cardolan. Those who deliver these trophies will receive modest compensation from the Dúnedain of Cardolan.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Fences all over Nathan Hodges' Farm have been broken by the marauding Wargs.Broken fence-pieces can be found at Nathan Hodges' Farm in the northern Lone-lands, near Annúndir.

