You should dig and see if there is anything worth finding buried in this strange ground.The digging was dangerous work in disturbed and sullied earth, but you uncovered some valuables just the same. You are richer for your troubles.In Annunlos lays a ruin, long abandoned by the Eglain. Picked clean and having only the depths of the ruin unexplored, the Eglain left the places beneath the ruin be, as is their custom. However, the ruin now teems with life again as dwarves, presumably in league with Orcs, scour for treasures in the depths.The ruins of Thandobel lie to the south of Refr Quicksilver in Annunlos.

Refr Quicksilver expressed a desire to learn what kind of dwarves would deign to work alongside Orcs and has asked you to go to the ruins of Thandobel and capture one of their banners.'I sometimes think I ought never have left the mountains and the home of my ancestors, but I sought after a life of adventure. After too many years looking, I found myself lost and then found again here amongst the Eglain.

'I have been here a long time now and consider myself one of them, but there are remnants of my own heritage that never stray, friend, and those remnants get stirred in times like these.

'I hear rumour of dwarves working with Orcs to despoil the tombs beneath the ruins of Thandobel to the south. I wish to know what kind of dwarf would tolerate Orcs, much less deign to work alongside them. Go to Thandobel and bring me one of their banners.''I know this blazon. My father told me of a revolt and battle long ago against a host of the Elves in Ered Luin. Skorgrím, a leader of the Dourhands, to whom this blazon belongs, led the assault and drove the Dourhands to near destruction.

'Buried beneath the mountains was he, by the quick actions of the Elves' leader, who sacrificed himself to deny Skorgrím victory.

'Dourhands in league with Orcs... grim news indeed, and there is no doubt of what must come next.'The Hove family farm is up in flames after an attack by ferocious goblins!Erina has asked you to put out fires at the Hove family farm. You should look for a bucket at Scurloc farm with which to fill with water in order to douse the flames.

Scurloc farm is in northern Cardolan.Find an empty bucketYou found an empty bucket, but now you need to fill it with water.

You should find the pond at the Hove family farm, in northern Cardolan.Armed with a bucket of water, you are now ready to douse the flames burning at the Hove family farm.

The farm is in northern Cardolan.Douse fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Erina know that you have put out many of the fires at Hove Farm.

Erina is at Sculoc Farm, in northern Cardolan.'Who are you? Are you here to help? Oh, please say yes!

'Terrible goblins raided our farm! I want to go home, but they are still there and I can see the smoke from here! Please, please, please can you please put out the fires? Oooh, it is all going to burn if you do not! You must help!

'We have a beautiful pond where you could fill a bucket and use it to put out the fires!''You did it? Oh, thank you thank you! I hope we can go home soon!'While you hunted the Wargs of Nain Enidh, Mugwort prepared a special meal for their leader. All that remains to ease passage along the Great East Road is to draw this leader out of hiding and into battle.The stone table where you should pour Mugwort's gruel is at the end of a southward path near a signpost on the road through Nain Enidh.

Old Mugwort asked you to take the special gruel he prepared to an ancient stone near the lair of the Wargs. The stench of it should draw forth their leader.Summon and defeat ShadepawOld Mugwort is at the camp on the east side of Minas Eriol.

After drawing Shadepaw's pack into the open, you defeated the Warg-leader. Old Mugwort will want to hear of your victory.'Once you have finished this last errand, the Wargs will no longer be a threat to travellers along the Great East Road.

'There is a signpost on the road through Nain Enidh, and a path near this signpost winds southwards. Of course, that is northward from here. If you follow the path as it slopes into a mild depression to the south-west, you will arrive at a stone structure, like an ancient table or a flat section of ruin. Bring the gruel I have prepared to that table and pour some of it onto the stone.

'I am certain that the leader will come running to the food, thinking it the cooking of some foolish ${RACE}! When you have slain the creature, come back here.''This stew should draw out the leader of those foul Wargs. Place it on the stone table like I asked.''We did it! You watch, those Wargs'll think twice about chasing down anyone now that you've slain their leader.

'We'll be heroes at The Forsaken Inn. You'll see!

'I owe you, friend. Here, take one of these for all that you've done!'Mincham has offered to introduce you to his two strange companions.Colbert the Mad is at Mincham's Camp at the south-west edge of the Fields of Fornost.

You should introduce yourself to Colbert the Mad.Introduce yourself to Colbert the MadMincham is at Mincham's Camp at the south-west edge of the Fields of Fornost.

You should speak with Mincham.Speak with MinchamIdhremmin is at Mincham's Camp at the south-west edge of the Fields of Fornost.

You should introduce yourself to Idhremmin.Introduce yourself to Idhremmin'I am Mincham, a Ranger of the North, and ever a protector of these lands. My duty bids me to keep watch over the Fields of Fornost, for they have grown dark and evil. Wise folk do not come near this place.

'Allow me to introduce my companion, Colbert the Mad (so he likes to call himself); he wandered out of the field one day and sat himself down at my fire. It was some time ago, and he has not left.'The man fixes you with a hard stare, lines of amusement etched into his pale skin.

'Yes, I am Colbert the Mad. I came out of Fornost and lived to tell the tale. I remember no time before, but I walked the dark fields and saw many things.

'You are ${PLAYER} the Mad. Yes, mad, mad, mad, to come to this place. There are ghosts, yes, and evil spirits, but more terrible than any are the bears!''And there is Idhremmin, our vigilant look-out. He speaks but rarely and smiles not at all, but his watchful presence eases my fears and lets me sleep better at night, so I do not begrudge him his silence.

'I believe he came from Meluinen far to the south-east, but I do not know what brought him hither.'Idhremmin peers at you calmly but does not speak.

After a moment of uncomfortable staring, he looks away and seems to listen intently to some distant sound only he can hear.Frideric the Elder at Ost Guruth desires flawed goo from the spiders found throughout the central and eastern Lone-lands.You accepted a task from Frideric the Elder to acquire flawed goo from the insects in the central and eastern Lone-lands. You can find Frideric the Elder within Ost Guruth.Wanted: Flawed goo from the insects and spiders in the central Lone-lands. Bring the goo to Frideric the Elder at Ost Guruth.Wanted: Flawed goo from the insects and spiders in the central Lone-lands.'A strange request, yes, but there are scholars among us who can discern how to better protect our people from the toxins within these creatures.

'Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Frideric the Elder at Ost Guruth desires ruffled feathers from the crebain found throughout the central and eastern Lone-lands.You accepted a task from Frideric the Elder to acquire ruffled feathers from the crebain in the central and eastern Lone-lands. You can find Frideric the Elder within Ost Guruth.Wanted: Ruffled feathers from the gore-crows. Bring the feathers to Frideric the Elder at Ost Guruth.Wanted: Ruffled feathers from the gore-crows.'More symbols of courage for my beleaguered people. You are proving yourself a valued ally.

'Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Thaliollang in the Elf-ruin of Meluinen at Lin Giliath requires the return of coarse skin.You are on a task to collect coarse skin from the beasts and toads found in Meluinen and to deliver them to Thaliollang. Thaliollang can be found at Lin Giliath, the Elf-ruins of Meluinen.Needed: Coarse skin from the beasts and toads within Meluinen. Deliver the items to Thaliollang at Lin Giliath.Needed: Coarse skin from the beasts and toads within Meluinen.'Thank you for this, it will make for interesting study.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Thaliollang in the Elf-ruin of Meluinen at Lin Giliath requires the return of tough carapaces.You are on a task to collect tough carapaces from bog-lurkers and insects found in Meluinen and to deliver them to Thaliollang. Thaliollang can be found at Lin Giliath, the Elf-ruins of Meluinen.Needed: Tough carapaces from the insects and bog-lurkers within Meluinen. Deliver the items to Thaliollang at Lin Giliath.Needed: Tough carapaces from the insects and bog-lurkers within Meluinen.'These will serve my purpose well, thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Thaliollang in the Elf-ruin of Meluinen at Lin Giliath requires the return of tough sword sheaths.You are on a task to collect Tough Sword Sheaths from Orcs plaguing Meluinen and to deliver them to Thaliollang. Thaliollang can be found at Lin Giliath, the Elf-ruins of Meluinen.Needed: Tough sword sheaths from the Orcs plaguing Meluinen. Deliver the items to Thaliollang at Lin Giliath.Needed: Tough sword sheaths from the Orcs plaguing Meluinen.'It is good to see that you are willing to stand against the Orcs. We are grateful for your assistance.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.In Annunlos lays a ruin, long abandoned by the Eglain. Picked clean and having only the depths of the ruin unexplored, the Eglain left the tombs beneath the ruin be, as is their custom. However, the ruin now teems with life again as dwarves, in league with Orcs, scour for treasures in the depths.The overseer of the Dourhands may be found within the ruins of Mithrenost, south of Refr Quicklsilver.

Refr Quicksilver has asked to seek out and defeat the overseer of the Dourhands at Mithrenost, in hopes that his followers will turn from their evil ways. He asked you to bring him evidence of the overseer's defeat.'Somewhere in Mithrenost, there is a dwarf who oversees the labours of the Dourhands. Though the Dourhands have gone against their nature by consorting with Orcs, all hope for them may not be lost.

'Find the overseer of the Dourhands and defeat him. His defeat may break the resolve of his followers, and they may well turn from the dark path upon which they tread. Bring me evidence of the overseer's downfall, and I will hold you honoured for your efforts on behalf of the Eglain.

'The overseer will be savvy and strong... be wary if you hope to defeat him.''Hunulf and Gadaric did well with choosing you. A fine upstanding sort you turned out to be.

'Though it pains me to know that my brethren have fallen so far, I am pleased to have gained the kinship you offer, ${PLAYER}.

'I took a certain liberty with some of the metal of the axes you collected and crafted this fine piece for you. You can do with it as you will. You have earned it.'Throughout the history of Middle-earth, there have been Men who have shunned the rule of Kings and forsaken their own heritage. Far too often they fall under the sway of the Dark Lord, who plays upon their distrust of the great Kingdoms, threatens them with hidden force, or sways them with false riches and power. However, there are some Men who freely offer themselves into his service and swear unerring loyalty to the Dark Lord.Defeat cultists sworn to the Dark LordMorgoth, Sauron, the Witch-king of Angmar, the terrible Gaunt-lords... all possess the sorcerous power to infuse the remains of the dead with fell spirits in service to the Enemy. Rumour speaks of haunted vales in the realm of Angmar inhabited almost wholly by these spirits and the fell wights they produce....Defeat wightsEver since the earliest records, history has been rife with stories of betrayal and tragedy. The rebellion of the Dourhands is just the latest chapter in this long and sorrowful litany. It is time to bring that chapter to an end....Defeat Dourhand dwarvesIt is uncertain what goblins think of Elves, as they are rarely willing to speak on the matter, save from the opposite end of a sharp implement. Are they at all aware of their distant ancestry, when they once lived among the Free Peoples? Do they hate the Elves because they are told to by their Dark Lord -- or is it because they remember something from long ago and strive to destroy you out of jealous hatred for your place in the light?Defeat goblinsFear spreads throughout the ranks of goblins. Far and wide, they whisper in hushed tones of the wrath of the line of Beorn.Defeat goblinsOrcs and goblins are neither cowards nor weaklings, but their oft-unfocused strength and determination is of little use against a foe they cannot find—or a foe they cannot even be certain truly exists! Legends and stories persist among them of the River Hobbits of Misthallow, but there is little time to speak of such trifles in the service of the Enemy.Defeat goblins and OrcsThe stories say that back in old Bullroarer's time, the arrival of Golfimbul's goblins were presaged by an invasion of wolves much like the one people are seeing these days. That cannot be a good sign.Defeat wolvesMany are the tales of the wood-demons of the North, who spread like a festering disease through the Greenwood of old. Rumours tell that others alike to their kind have appeared in lands far beyond the bounds of Mirkwood and the Wells of Langflood, and many among the River Hobbits of Misthallow now believe that nature itself is being corrupted by some unseen hand.Defeat wood-trollsGaelm has told you that you can exchange your Bree-horse for another.Gaelm is at the Hengstacer Farm, north of the Bree Festival Grounds.

Gaelm suggested that you take a moment to consider whether or not you want to exchange your horse. If you decided that you do want to exchange your horse, you should speak to Gaelm again.'Greetings, I am Gaelm, son of Éogar.

'Have you chosen a horse for yourself instead of a pony? While Bree-horses are much more gentle than others, a horse would still not suit one of your stature. I can take your horse back and provide you with a pony instead, if you wish.

'I would ask that you be careful with your choice this time, though. My father already looks down on these Bree-steeds... I would not wish him to think those that ride them have addled wits.''Greetings, I am Gaelm, son of Éogar.

'Have you chosen a horse for yourself instead of a pony? While Bree-horses are much more gentle than others, a horse would still not suit one of your stature. I can take your horse back and provide you with a pony instead, if you wish.

'I would ask that you be careful with your choice this time, though. My father already looks down on these Bree-steeds... I would not wish him to think those that ride them have addled wits.''So you do wish to return your Bree-horse? Then so be it.'Gaelm has told you that you can exchange your Bree-pony for another.Gaelm is at the Hengstacer Farm, north of the Bree Festival Grounds.

If you wish to trade in your pony for a horse, you should speak again with Gaelm.'Greetings, I am Gaelm, son of Éogar.

Have you chosen a pony for yourself instead of a horse? A Bree-pony would buckle under the load of someone of your stature! You must exchange it for a Bree-horse.

I would ask that you be careful though in your choice this time. My father already looks down on these Bree-steeds...I would not wish him to think those that ride them have addled wits.''Greetings, I am Gaelm, son of Éogar.

Have you chosen a pony for yourself instead of a horse? A Bree-pony would buckle under the load of someone of your stature! You must exchange it for a Bree-horse.

I would ask that you be careful though in your chose this time. My father already looks down on these Bree-steeds...I would not wish him to think those that ride them have addled wits.''Good! You wish to return your poor Bree-pony to me. Thank you!'Driven from his land and wounded by rampaging goblins, Cendrew Hove seeks a way to give back to his hosts.Cendrew Hove has asked you retrieve his woodworking tools from his farm.

The Hove family farm is in Cardolan.Search for the woodworking toolsYou found the farmer's toolbox, but it was empty. You suspect that the goblins who have infiltrated the farm carried off the tools. You should defeat goblins at the Hove farm and recover the stolen tools.

The Hove farm is located in north-central Cardolan.Recover stolen tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the woodworking tools back to Cendrew Hove.

Cendrew is at the Scurloc farm in north-eastern Cardolan.'Greetings. I am Cendrew Hove. I heard Edrud talking to you about our farm. If you are going that way, I would also beg a boon of you. I hurt my back during the raid on our farm, so I'm not able to help out here as much as I'd usually have done. If I'm going to be stuck off my feet, I can still be useful, but not without my woodworking tools.

'Please - if you do go to our farm, will you look for my tools? I left them near the house.''My tools! You found them! Now I can start to pitch in around here. Thank you, friend, thank you! For everything you have done!'You have become a friend to the Eglain—Men who have shunned accepted society, choosing the meagre life that the Lone-lands will support. Although they dwell in less-hospitable lands than the Wells of Langflood, their way of life and their friendship with Radagast the Brown has led you to consider them kindred spirits of the River Hobbits of Misthallow.You must earn Friend standing with the EglainGoblins have settled in among the tombs of Haudh Narui.Taeras has asked you to clear the tombs of Haudh Narui of goblins.

Haudh Narui is located in north-eastern Cardolan.Defeat goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Taeras know that you have defeated goblins in Haudh Narui.

Taeras is at Scurloc Farm.Return to Taeras'To the north lie the ruins of Haudh Nirui. My ancestors' ancestors rest there in ancient stone sarcophagi, but recently the tombs have been overrun by goblins. I implore you to do what you can to lessen their numbers, that the dead may sleep more soundly.''May those wretched creatures be driven from this land for good!'You have encounted Gurthagar, a terrifying presence in the Fields of Fornost....Gurthagar can be found in the eastern Fields of Fornost, near Amon Amrûn.

You should defeat Gurthagar, for this being has sapped the life from the Fields of Fornost.Defeat GurthagarGurthagar can be found in the eastern Fields of Fornost, near Amon Amrûn.

You should defeat Gurthagar, for this being has sapped the life from the Fields of Fornost.Defeat GurthagarYou have defeated one of the chief forces of evil in the Fields of Fornost.CompletedA great shuddering dread chills you to your bones.

You have encounted Gurthagar, a terrifying presence in the Fields of Fornost. This ghostly being is strong from having pulled the life from the lands around it.'Ahhh... a life, whole and hale. Let me devour you. I will drain all that you have, all that you are.'You have defeated Gurthagar, one of the chief forces of evil in the Fields of Fornost.In the shadow of Amon Sûl, at the edge of Nain Enidh, lay an Arnorian ruin. Those ruins afforded the Eglain of Ost Guruth a wealth of material to trade with collectors in Bree-land... until the arrival of half-breeds from the South.The ruins of Naerost are just east of Weathertop, north of Hunulf's camp.

A year ago, half-orcs wrested the ruins of Naerost from the Eglain, causing the Eglain to lose a valuable source of trade-goods. Hunulf asked you to return to ruins to sift through the relics there to recover the trade-goods they lost.'A year ago, we lost a rich ruin to Men from the South... at least we thought they were Men. They bore the manner, height, and look of Men but were nearly as savage as the Orc-folk we learned they were descended from.

'Naerost, north of here, in the eastern shadow of the great hill of Weathertop, fell to the half-breeds and our trade was lost with it. If we could recover some of those goods, we might restore trade with the west and some more hope for Eglain.

'Will you help us sift through the ruins for our goods?''Worthy finds, ${PLAYER}. These will fetch enough food for many families in Ost Guruth. You are becoming a true friend to the Eglain.

'So many perished when the half-breeds approached from the south, it is painful to recall. For now, know that you have done a great good for us all.'You have been asked to search the Fields of Fornost for signs of Olnathron.Colbert the Mad is at Mincham's Camp in the southern Fields of Fornost, in the north-western North Downs.Ask Colbert if he knows of any place where Olnathron might be hidingOlnathron could be hiding anywhere throughout the western Fields of Fornost.

Mincham has asked you to investigate suspicious sites that might lead to Olnathron.Find and explore the strange piles of earthSearch for the deathly lightsSearch for graves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mincham is at his camp in the southern Fields of Fornost.

You should speak with Mincham.Return to Mincham to tell of what you saw'This poor girl! She is from a farm not far from here, but the fell spirit Olnathron seems to have tricked her into coming.

'My duty does not allow me to pursue the villains of Fornost, unless they are unwise enough to venture south of where we stand, into the North Downs. I must stay here... but you are bound by no such oath.

'Of everyone, Colbert the Mad knows the most about Fornost and its many fell landmarks. Maybe he will have an inkling of where Olnathron would likely be hiding.''You want to search the Fields of Fornost? You cannot walk the steps I walked without going a tad mad.

'I came from the north and the west, and I saw piles of dirt with bones sticking out, with treasure glinting from within. I saw lights that called me to my death, and I saw graves wherever I looked.'You tell Mincham of the wights who spoke of Olnathron and Tham Lorn, the waking of Morrafn, light of death, and newly disturbed graves.

'If your tale is true, Olnathron has likely retreated to Tham Lorn, but her power has not waned....

