<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Do not retreat from combat.</rgb>Defeat the Harbinger of the Dead in "Trouble in Tuckborough"One of the Harbingers of the Dead, a terrible omen of death and decay, has come to this place.Defeat the Harbinger of the Dead in "Trouble in Tuckborough".Defeat the Harbinger of the Dead in "Trouble in Tuckborough (Tier 3)"You have come to Dwaling with Ponto Oats in order to deal with the brigands that have taken the town.Ponto Oats is standing on the road that leads down to Dwaling.

Ponto is waiting to speak with you about your upcoming "retrieval".The club for which you are seeking is on the ground by the sleeping brigands near Pearlina Gamgee's house in Dwaling.

Ponto is waiting for you to retrieve the club from near the sleeping brigands in Dwaling.Find the clubPonto Oats is on the slope at the northern edge of Dwaling.

Ponto is waiting to hear about your retrieval of the club.'The village of Dwaling is just down the slope, ${PLAYER}, and it is full of brigands. One of the Chief's Men wields a deadly club; without this weapon, I warrant he would not be a match for even a single ${RACE}!

'Some of the brigands remain on guard, but many of the villains are sleeping by the fires near Pearlina Gamgee's house. Sneak up to those sleeping; their leader's club is likely on the ground by his resting place.

'Seize the club and return to me, ${PLAYER}! But do not engage in battle! If you are seen by even one of the Chief's Men, our task ends in failure!''You did it, ${PLAYER}! We'll make an Expert Treasure Hunter out of you yet! You must give me details of the recovery while we return to Oatbarton.''Many of the brigands are sleeping by the fires near Pearlina Gamgee's house, down the slope in Dwaling. Sneak up to them and look for the club; seize it and bring it back to me, but do not engage in battle! If you are seen, our task ends in failure!''Let us be off, friend ${PLAYER}! I look forward to the tale of your deeds this night!'Nidgyl in Bree-town told you of a ruthless band of half-orcs that has inhabited the ruins of Naerost in the Lone-lands.Naerost lies to the east of Weathertop in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree.

Nidgyl has asked you to assault the ruins of Naerost and defeat the villianous half-orc Hontimûrz. He suggested that you take allies with you.Defeat HontimûrzNidgyl is in Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the west of Naerost.

You should return to Nidgyl and tell him of Hontimûrz' defeat.Talk to Nidgyl'${PLAYER}, should you find yourself in the hills east of Weathertop, there is a particular half-orc by the name of Hontimûrz who has been making quite a nuisance of himself in that region. It has even reached my ears that he may be in the service of some ally of the Enemy.

'In any case, I -- and many others  would like to see his evil put to an end. Perhaps you would go against him? He has set up a camp in the ruins of Naerost.

'I should warn you however, he is said to be an accomplished warrior, and he is often surrounded by fellow brigands who will defend him... you would do well to take allies with you.''You have defeated Hontimûrz? You have earned my praise, ${PLAYER}! That is one less trouble I need worry about in these dark days.'The wailing woman's own lost child may be the key to freeing her from the grief that has her spiraling into madness.Grethron believes that Annaethel's son may yet live. You should look for signs of Mellanion in Caranost, in central Cardolan.Search for signs of MellanionThe blanket you found is definitely of Elven weave. Could it have belonged to the missing Elf-child? You should continue to look for signs of Mellanion in Caranost, in central Cardolan.Continue to look for signs of MellanionThe hobby horse looks like it's been chewed on, but hopefully its owner has not been! Keep looking for signs of Mellanion in Caranost, in central Cardolan.Continue looking for signs of MellanionMellanion managed to hide from his captors, but he needs help making his escape. He wants you to ignite the crate of black powder he spotted in the tower above the stairs.

The tower is in Caranost.Ignite the black powder crateWith the Orcs distracted, Mellanion was able to make his escape! You should check to be sure he made it back to Sírlond.

Sírlond is in central Cardolan.Grethron wants you to give the hobby horse back to Mellanion.

Mellanion is in Sírlond, thanks to you.'We have been here at Sírlond looking into the situation with the Orcs and, more recently, the restless dead. Though I encouraged her to leave him at home, Annaethel insisted on bringing her youngling, Mellanion. The child went missing during an Orc attack. Annaethel was convinced he survived, but after a few days of not finding him she took the loss very deeply.

'Annaethel's grief could not be lightened, and with it came a madness I have never seen before. She took to wandering away from our camp, and vanished one night. I have been searching for her and Mellanion ever since, and I am overjoyed that you have found her! My heart trembles, however, thinking that she has lured away someone else's child.

'I fear for Annaethel's safety, but even more for that of her child. I dare hope that he yet lives, but if that is true, he is a captive of the Orcs who dwell throughout Caranost. Due to their numbers, I am unable to penetrate the crumbled city, but perhaps you will succeed where I have failed! Please, look for signs of Mellanion.''Hail, hail and well met indeed! Are you come from Sírlond? What a relief!

'I have been stuck down here for days! I managed to slip away from my captors and hide down here, but they're looking for me and patrol above incessantly. I feared I would never escape, but now you are here!

'I can make my own way out of here, but I need a distraction. When I was leading them on a chase a few days ago, I saw a curious crate in the tower above these steps. I believe that lighting that box with fire will create a fantastic explosion! If you do that, the patrolling guards will be distracted long enough for me to make my escape. Will you help me?''Well met again, my new friend! Mellanion has returned and brought word of your deeds! There are not enough words to thank you for what you have done! Additionally, while you were gone, a scout came back with news of Annaethel! She was found in the ruins south of here, but ran off when approached.

'I see you found the boy's hobby horse also. I think we can use this to help us get through to his mother!

'Give the toy back to Mellanion. I have an idea.''Hail again! This time under much better circumstances. Thank you for my rescue, and for bringing me back my horse, chewed though he seems to be. We would have both been gnawed upon much more, were it not for your help.'Nidgyl is concerned with the half-orcs who have been spotted marauding through the Nain Enidh region of the Lone-lands, making travel into the east nearly impossible.Half-orcs can be found throughout the Nain Enidh region of the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree.

Nidgyl has asked you to defeat the half-orcs marauding in the Lone-lands.Defeat half-orcs in Nain Enidh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nidgyl is at Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the west of Nain Enidh.

You should return to Nidgyl of Bree-town and tell him of your battles against the half-orcs of Nain Enidh.Talk to Nidgyl'My kinsmen often have need to travel into the Trollshaws to carry information to and from Rivendell, but of late that passage has become hazardous, as the roads are frequently watched by bands of half-orc marauders -- particularly in the region of Nain Enidh in the Lone-lands.

'I need you to foray into Nain Enidh and defeat as many of these half-orcs as possible to free up the passage into the east; otherwise, we will likely be caught unaware when the Enemy makes its next move in the east.''You have struck a telling blow against the half-orcs of Nain Enidh. My kinsmen have been able to reach Rivendell with considerably fewer unpleasant incidents, thanks to your efforts on our behalf.'You have encountered Naethír, a terrifying presence in the Fields of Fornost....Naethír can be found in the central Fields of Fornost, north of the road leading west towards Evendim.

You should defeat Naethír, for this being has sapped the warmth from the Fields of Fornost.Defeat NaethírNaethír can be found in the central Fields of Fornost, north of the road leading west towards Evendim.

You should defeat Naethír, for this being has sapped the warmth from the Fields of Fornost.Defeat NaethírYou have defeated one of the chief forces of evil in the Fields of Fornost.CompletedYou feel a terrible chill, and realize that a great and old evil presence is near.

You have encounted Naethír, a terrifying presence in the Fields of Fornost. This ghostly being has gained power from having pulled the life from the lands around it.'Come closer, warm creature. Closer.'You have defeated one of the chief forces of evil in the Fields of Fornost, Naethír, who drains the warmth from Men.Nathan Hodges and his wife were driven from their farmstead by an attack by Wargs. They have asked you to see if it's safe for them to return.Nathan Hodges' Farm can be found east along the road from Amon Raith in the North Downs.

You should go to Nathan Hodges' Farm and ensure that it is free of Wargs.Defeat Wargs at Nathan Hodges' Farm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nathan Hodges is at Amon Raith.

You should tell Nathan Hodges that his farm is now safe from the Wargs.Tell Nathan Hodges the farm has been cleared of Wargs'Our poor farm, overrun by Wargs! We fled this way, and this kind Ranger vowed to protect us from the dangers coming out of Annúndir.

'I dare not go back. What if the Wargs linger there? It is east along the road. I would dearly love to return soon. We have a livelihood to make there.''You cleared out the rest of the Wargs that were hanging about? Thank you, ${PLAYER}! You're a real hero! We'll go back soon, and try to rebuild.'The North Downs were once the home to the capitol of the North Kingdom. Now it lies in ruin, inviting the return of Angmar.Complete quests within North DownsAs the goblins descended on the Eglain in Minas Eriol, the tribe left something very important behind, hidden in the deepest ruins.The goblins of Minas Eriol are in possession of the statue.

Hunulf directed you to seek out the greatest discovery made by the Eglain, a statue dredged from the swamps of the Lone-lands.'${PLAYER}, if you have time, I would ask for assistance in a manner of great importance. As the goblins tore through our ranks, we salvaged one find and hid it deep within the ruins of Minas Eriol, at a place called Ost Laden. It is a statue, retrieved from marshy swamp-land, and we hoped to keep it safe from harm, but a recent visitor to Ost Guruth made mention that the statue lay at the heart of problems facing us.

'If you are willing, we need to collect this statue. You will find it in the goblin camps that now lie furthest east in ruins of Minas Eriol, across the bridge to the west. I fear the goblins may have already found it, so search any goblins you may slay there.

'When you have found the statue, return it to me.''You see the beauty of this statue now. I have not seen such beauty among Man or Elf. Aric, another of our number claims that she is a maiden separated from her sisters.

'I do not know if the tales woven by our stone-speaker are true, but I know that this statue shows a female of beauty unseen in the world. I thank you for making this recovery.'Nidgyl told you that the Orcs assaulting Trestlebridge have been using poisoned arrows to slay the defenders there.Nan Wathren lies to the north-east of Trestlebridge in the North Downs, far to the north of Bree.

Nidgyl has asked you to slay the Tarkrîp Defiler who has been creating the poisons used by the Orcs attacking Trestlebridge.Defeat the Tarkrîp DefilerNidgyl is at Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the south of Nan Wathren and Trestlebridge.

You should return to Nidgyl and tell him that the Tarkrîp Defiler is dead.Talk to Nidgyl'Ill-tidings, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs have mounted an assault on the town of Trestlebridge to the North. While their first attack has been repelled, they are continuing to harass the defenders while they bring more reinforcements from the east.

'Worst of all, the raiders who assault the town have been using poisoned arrows -- even the smallest nick can cause raging fevers which put down a strong warrior for days. If they can weaken Trestlebridge's defence enough, the next major attack will overrun the town.

'I need you to find the Orc responsible for creating these evil poisons -- find the Tarkrîp Defiler who has hidden in the valleys of Nan Wathren, north-east of Trestlebridge, and slay him.''You have slain the defiler? Excellent. Now the soldiers of Trestlebridge need not fear a painful death from any nick or scratch as they do battle.'Old Mugwort believes that if the Wargs are angered, they will send forth their leader.Wargs can be found off the Great East Road on the far side of Nain Enidh, in the vicinity of Ost Cyrn.

Old Mugwort thinks that if you anger enough Wargs, they will call forth their leader.Defeat Wargs in Nain Enidh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Old Mugwort is at the camp on the eastern edge of Minas Eriol.

The Wargs are surely angry now, given your exploits in Nain Enidh, and Old Mugwort should be informed of your success.Talk to Old Mugwort'It's going to take awhile before the special meal I am preparing will be ready. What should I have you do in the meantime?

'Ah, I have it! Wargs are mean-tempered sorts of beast, and they're smarter than your everyday wolf... stronger too. That means that they can get angry, and if they can get angry, they can make mistakes!

'The logic of that all works out, I'm sure of it! Now, you listen well: go east! Go to the far side of Nain Enidh and search the wilderlands off the road near Ost Cyrn for Wargs; defeat all those you find! Let's get them good and angry, and their leader is sure to come forth, hungry to taste some flesh!''Go into Nain Enidh, far to the east, and slay Wargs. Get them nice and angry! We don't want them wandering all over the Great East Road after all. Let's send that message to their leader!''So you defeated a good number of Wargs? You've a hand for this, that much is certain!

'I finished my cooking too, I think. Maybe not quite yet, but I'm sure this will draw out their leader, or leaders, and then....

'Then you'll defeat them and make the road safe for travellers, that's what, and we'll have more guests at the inn!'Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of coarse skin to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect coarse skin from the beasts in the area surrounding Esteldín to the west. Once collected, you are to deliver the items to Frerrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Coarse skin from the beasts to the west of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Coarse skin from the beasts to the west of Esteldín.'We will find a use for these items. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Nathan Hodges, at Amon Raith, awaits the collection and delivery of dim dust.You have accepted a task to deliver dim dust to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith in the North Downs. You can find dim dust on shades north-west of Amon Raith.Wanted: Dim dust from the shades north-west of Amon Raith. Deliver the items to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith.Wanted: Dim dust from the shades north-west of Amon Raith.'I am certain that the elf will be pleased with this collection. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of flawed goo to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect flawed goo from the spiders in the area surrounding Esteldín to the west. Once collected, you are to deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: flawed goo from the spiders to the west of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: flawed goo from the spiders to the west of Esteldín.'I will ensure that this is put to good use, thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Nathan Hodges, at Amon Raith, awaits the collection and delivery of glossy essence.You have accepted a task to deliver glossy essence to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith in the North Downs. You can find glossy essence on shades north-west of Amon Raith.Wanted: Glossy essence from the shades north-west of Amon Raith. Deliver the items to Nathan Hodges at Amon Raith.Wanted: Glossy essence from the shades north-west of Amon Raith.'I am certain that the Elf will be pleased with this collection. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Goblins of Nan Wathren have been found to be in possession of valuable Elvish relics pillaged from the refuge of Meluinen.Relics of Meluinen can be found on goblins and in caches in central Nan Wathren, in the southern North Downs.

You should collect the stolen relics of Meluinen, so that they may someday be returned.

<rgb=#FF0000>Small Fellowship Recommended.</rgb>Defeat goblins in Nan Wathren (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Relics of Meluinen can be found on goblins and in caches in central Nan Wathren, in the southern North Downs.

You should collect the stolen relics of Meluinen, so that they may someday be returned.Collect Relics of Meluinen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of goblins from Nan Wathren.CompletedGoblins of Nan Wathren have been found to be in possession of valuable Elvish relics pillaged from an unknown place called Meluinen.

You should gather relics from the goblins and their hidden caches, in hope that they may someday be restored to Meluinen.

<rgb=#FF0000>Small Fellowship Recommended.</rgb>You have defeated a number of goblins from Nan Wathren, and reclaimed the relics of ancient Meluinen. You have honoured the memory of the Elves who once roamed these lands.The Eglain are requesting that crafters proficient with woodworking deliver fishing-rods to them at their encampment in the ruins of Ost Guruth. The Eglain hope to be able to utilize the fishing-rods to provide for their people from the small number of ponds throughout the Lone-lands.Craft and deliver the fishing-rod to Léoflac at the Ost Guruth encampment.

The Eglain have asked that fishing-rods be crafted and delivered to assist them in their efforts to survive in the harsh climate of the Lone-lands.Attention woodworkers,

We, the Eglain, require a number of fishing-rods to outfit our people with the ability to fish the few ponds throughout the Lone-lands. We will also use these rods to fish the great river in the east. If you are capable of crafting such items, we would be greatly appreciative. Please, deliver the fishing-rods to Léoflac at the Ost Guruth encampment.'Yes, this fishing-rod is of good quality. We will see it distributed to our people, and given time, will send them to the ponds to fish for much-needed food. 

'Thank you for doing this.'Spiders often poison members of the Eglain, and they wish to better control the spider-population near their home and the dig-sites throughout the Lone-lands. To accomplish this, they are requesting that scholars make them foe-finder bow-chants.Craft eight copies of Bow Chant: Minor Foe-finder and deliver them to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth.

The Eglain, in an effort to better prepare their provisioners for the dangers posed by the spiders of the Lone-lands, request the creation and collection of foe-finder bow-chants.Attention scholars,

We hope to secure enough foe-finder bow-chants to make our providers formidable against the spiders' threat. If you can craft these items, we ask that you to deliver these items to Léoflac at our encampment at Ost Guruth.'These will aid us greatly. The spiders will be fearful of our provisioners now that they will be better prepared.

'Thank you for doing this.'Throwing hatchets are a way that the Eglain can procure the game needed to feed the many mouths among them. They have asked that weaponsmiths assist them by crafting throwing hatchets to achieve this goal.Craft three Gondorian throwing hatchets and deliver them to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth.

Gondorian throwing hatchets will be used to assist the Eglan-provisioners in providing enough food for the entirety of their people.Attention weaponsmiths,

We can use throwing hatchets to augment and assist our provisioners in providing enough game to feed the Eglan-people. If you can craft these items, please deliver some to Léoflac at our encampment at Ost Guruth.'These throwing hatchets will do nicely. With them, we will be able to hunt effectively throughout the Lone-lands and be able to feed all our people.

'Thank you for doing this.'Living in a section of land teeming with disease, the Eglain have put out a general call for cooks to make hearty onion soup so they may hearten themselves against the growing threat of disease.Craft two servings of hearty onion soup and deliver them to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth.

The Eglain, in an effort to stave off the spread of disease, have asked for cooks to make them hearty onion soup.Attention cooks,

There is much disease in these grim times, spread by the coming of the evil forces which have come here. We need assistance to ensure the continued health of our people. If you can cook hearty onion soup, please deliver some to Léoflac at our encampment at Ost Guruth.'This smells delicious. I wish to thank you for preparing this. If you have more, please deliver it to us. Disease is sure to begin spreading soon now that we must remain in this close proximity.

'Thank you for doing this.'The Eglain have lost most of their cloth and leather goods in recent weeks, and they have asked tailors to craft various items so they might begin restoring the trade that serves as the lifeblood of their community.Craft a heavy cotton cloak and deliver it to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth.

To restore their cloth trade, the Eglain require a good number of heavy cotton cloaks.Attention tailors,

Recent weeks have seen the destruction of much of our cloth and leather goods. Because of this, we need to restock in order to restore our trade business. If you can craft these items, please deliver some to Léoflac at our encampment at Ost Guruth.'This cloak was crafted with much quality and care. With a few more of these, we may once again trade with other people and be left alone to our own devices once more.

'Thank you for doing this.'Spiders are a great danger to the Eglain. They have thus put out a request to jewellers to create ruby rings of willpower that they might distribute to their people in an effort to defend them from the spider's wrath. The rings will make Eglan bodies healthier and give them strength against the spiders found throughout the Lone-lands.Craft a ruby ring of willpower and deliver it to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth.

Defending their people from the spiders of the Lone-lands is one goal of the Eglain. If they can find crafters able to create ruby rings of willpower, they believe that they can protect a good number of their people.Attention jewellers,

There is a great danger to our people that comes from the terrifying fangs of the spiders found throughout the Lone-lands. We require ruby rings of willpower, which have a quality that strengthens the wearer's body. If you can craft these items, please deliver some to Léoflac at our encampment at Ost Guruth.'This is beautiful. I will be certain to see that our people receive the rings. It is likely that they will protect them from the spiders and perhaps prevent needless death.

'Thank you for doing this.'Since the invasion of their land, the Eglain have lost many materials and tools necessary to sift through the ruins of the Lone-lands. They have put out a general call to collect mining picks and forester axes that will assist them in performing these tasks.Craft and deliver tools of the expert explorer to Léoflac at the Ost Guruth encampment.

The Eglain have asked that tools of the expert explorer be crafted and delivered to assist them in their efforts to survive in the harsh climate of the lone-lands.Attention metalsmiths,

Since the arrival of these enemies all throughout the Lone-lands, we have lost many tools, lives, and materials that assist us in our survival here. We require mining-picks and forester axes to help us collect the important trinkets that we trade for provisions. If you are capable of crafting such items, we would be greatly appreciative. Please, deliver these tools to Léoflac at the Ost Guruth encampment.'Yes, this tool is of good quality. It will assist us in replenishing our diminished supplies once the threats to this land are removed.

'Thank you for doing this.'When goblins overran the Hove farm, Tomur Scurloc and his sons rushed over to drive them out! The farmer and his sons have not returned, however, and his wife fears the worst.Edrud Scurloc has asked you to rescue her husband and sons, who went to the Hove farm to fight goblins.

The Hove farm is in north-eastern Cardolan.Rescue TomurRescue CleddRescue TomRescue ArwelYou have managed to free all of the Scurloc men. You should return to Edrud and let her know they're all safe.

Edrud is at the Scurloc farmstead, in north-eastern Cardolan.Return to Edrud'A band of goblins took over the Hove farm across the way, to the north-west. My husband Tomur and our sons went to do something about it, but they have not yet returned and I am worried.

'I'm pretty handy with a hay-fork, but I can't take on those horrid goblins. And besides, I have the Hoves here to look over. But you look formidable! Please, rescue my husband and sons from those foul creatures!''Thank you for rescuing me and my boys. I cannot believe that goblins have come this far south!''I nearly was out of my bonds, but I guess it's good that you came by when you did.''Thank you for the rescue. I was right about to faint from how bad my guards stank.''I never seen anyone fight like you do. Maybe if I train as a warrior, I'll be able to protect my family better.''Welcome back! You did it! You really did it! I didn't think you could, but I am more than happy to be proven wrong! Thanks are in order, I suppose.'The ancient guardians of Amon Amrûn have awoken, pouring out of the tombs in a blind rage.Enraged shades can be found roaming Amon Amrûn in the eastern Fields of Fornost.

You should defeat shades that patrol the surface of the ruined tombs.Defeat enraged shades at Amon AmrûnEnraged shades can be found roaming Amon Amrûn in the eastern Fields of Fornost.

