Hunulf Munce is concerned that the half-orcs are servants of a greater power, perhaps even Mordor. He has asked you to enter Naerost and defeat their leader and his guards in hopes that the rest will flee.Defeat HontimûrzDefeat Hontimûrz's guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hunulf Munce awaits your return at his camp on the east side of Minas Eriol, south of Naerost.

Though the half-orcs did not flee, their leader and his guards have been defeated. You should return to Hunulf Munce with the news.Talk to Hunulf Munce'Your efforts on behalf of the Eglain are noble, my friend, but I deem our peril is greater than first we thought. These half-breeds bear a standard with the mark of a white hand? Ordinary brigands and ruffians do not bear such charges. The mark of the White Hand tells me they serve a greater master.

'Whatever their purpose, such creatures cannot be allowed to take a foothold in the North. They do not belong here. If you can enter Naerost and slay Hontimûrz, their leader, and his guards, perhaps the rest will flee.

'Hontimûrz became known to us when he sent us gifts of the dead with his crudely-scrawled threats. I think, that you are here to avenge that disservice and restore more faith to the Eglain.''I will spare the grim details of the delivery made to us by Hontimûrz. Know only that the depravation of these creatures proves that they are not Men. They are something wholly bestial and destructive. We have longed for a chance at revenge, and it seems that your arrival may herald a chance to seek that revenge.''Ah, so the half-breeds will not run? No matter... the grip of the White Hand is loosened. I think that they will not trouble us again thanks to you.

'Your efforts on behalf of the Eglain will not be forgotten, ${PLAYER}.'Gaelm has told you that in exchange for doing tasks for the Stable-masters of Bree, he will grant you the boon of being able to ride one of his steeds. Although lacking the power and stamina of his father's horses, Gaelm's horses are more tame and easier to ride.The sack of grain is near the silo on Hengstacer's Farm, east of Gaelm.

Gaelm has instructed you to pick up a sack of grain near the silo at Hengstacer Farm and bring it to Bill Rosewood, the Stable-master near the West-gate of Bree.Pick up a sack of grainBill Rosewood is at the stables near the West-gate of Bree, to the south of the Hengstacer Farm.

You should speak with Bill Rosewood at his stable.The Boar Fountain is south of The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree.

Bill Rosewood has asked you to draw water from the Boar Fountain in Bree and use it to muck out one of his stalls by the West-gate of Bree.Draw water from the Boar FountainBill Rosewood is at the stable near the South-gate of Bree.

You mucked out one of Bill Rosewood's stalls, but he mentioned that Bert Goldenleaf, who maintains the stalls by the South-gate of Bree, may need the same service. You should speak with Bill Rosewood again before you leave.The Boar Fountain is south of The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree. Bert Goldenleaf is at the stable near Bree's South-gate.

Bill Rosewood told you to draw some water from the Boar Fountain in Bree and use it to muck out one of Bert Goldenleaf's stalls.Draw water from the Boar FountainBert Goldenleaf is at his stable near the South-gate of Bree.

