<rgb=#FF0000>Fellowship Recommended.</rgb>You have defeated the defiler responsible for brewing the sleeping draught that led to the catastrophe at Trestlebridge.Maedhril is worried that the Orcs have a good line of sight to her husband's camp-site of Sírlond from the heights of Caranost.The tower about which Maedhril is concerned is to the west across the bridge from Sírlond.Maedhril is at Sírlond, east of Caranost proper.Talk to Maedhril at Sírlond'My husband is dear to me, but he sees only that which is directly in front of him. "We must put an end to the Orc warriors, Maedhril," he tells me, "for their swords are deadly and sharp." He is not wrong in this, but I am more concerned about the arrows of their scouts, for they can strike us from much further away.

'Will you cross to Caranost proper and find the stairs that climb just beyond the bridge? There is a fire burning atop one of the towers, and I want to learn if the Orc-archers can strike at this camp from the parapet. Go there and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> in our direction. I want to hear what can be seen from that location.''Will you cross to Caranost proper and find the stairs that climb just beyond the bridge? There is a fire burning atop one of the towers, and I want to learn if the Orc-archers can strike at this camp from the parapet. Go there and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> in our direction. I want to hear what can be seen from that location.''You could see Sírlond from that location? That is what I feared, ${PLAYER}.

'My husband Sirvellon is always thinking of swords and axes, and things that are up close. It falls to me to take the longer view.'Mincham believes that Olnathron can be found in some ancient ruins in the western Fields of Fornost.Tham Lorn, in the western Fields of Fornost, can be reached by taking the horse from Mincham's Camp.

You should travel to Tham Lorn to confront Olnathron once and for all.Take the horse from Mincham's Camp to Tham LornOlnathron can be found to the west of the graves of his wife and child.

Fearing for the strength of his will, Mincham has asked you to find and confront the fell spirit who has taken his wife's semblance.Confront the fell spirit OlnathronMincham awaits you at his camp.

Mincham will be relieved to learn that the fell spirit Olnathron has been sent back to the abyss.Return to Mincham'I believe Olnathron is at Tham Lorn, some ruins in the western fields. I have heard dark rumours about that place of late, and it could well be the source of the evil stirrings in Fornost.

'My horse will take you there if you wish to go. You must be careful. You are a seasoned warrior, but this place is truly evil.''The Dúnedain cannot withstand the might of the dead, and neither can you. You will all die, and this land will be covered in our fell shadows.''Ah, my friend. I know you have been victorious. A shadow that has darkened my thoughts has vanished.

'You have the gratitude of the Rangers.'Amidst the ruins of Dol Ernil, the restless Dead shuffle across crumbling stone.Medi has asked you to defeat gaunt-men at Dol Ernil.

Dol Ernil is in northern Cardolan.Defeat blight-callers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat war-mongers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat blight priests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Medi know that there are far fewer gaunt-men to haunt her dreams.

Medi is at Gerwyn's convoy.Return to Medi'Well met, traveller. When we tried to pass below Dol Ernil, we were attacked on the road by an evil most foul. I must admit that I am terrified and have not slept a moment since that night. I see them when I close my eyes - gaunt-men with their horrifying countenances.

'Please, send them back to the grave, that I may sleep again!''You return! Tell me, were you able to vanquish them?'

You inform her that you did.

'Oh thank you. Thank you! Perhaps I will sleep at last.'Goblins have driven the Hove family from their farm and have taken over!Bethan Hove has asked you to defeat the goblins that have taken over her family's farm.

The Hove family farm is in northern Cardolan.Defeat goblins at Hove Farm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Lukglob'Oh, hello. I am Bethan Hove. Did you come here from the west? Have you been to our farm too, I wonder? The Scurlocs have been so kind to us. They took us in when a wretched band of goblins drove us off our land! The fiends killed our cows and ate all of our food. Poor Nelly. She was such a good cow, too!

'We do not have much, but if you happen to go back in that direction, give those goblins a taste of their own medicine. I would be so grateful! You will find our farm west of here.'The goblins of Minas Eriol are led by a terrible creature named Nishrûk.The goblin's leader, Nishrûk, dwells in a goblin-fort built among the ruins south-east of The Forsaken Inn.

Deputy Osmann has asked you to slay Nishrûk, the leader of the goblins troubling The Forsaken Inn.Defeat NishrûkDeputy Osmann awaits you across the bridge at the eastern edge of the ruins at Minas Eriol.

You entered the ruins and defeated Nishrûk, as Deputy Osmann requested. You should return to him with news of your success.Talk to Deputy Osmann'Goblins swept in from the north and overran the ruins in the south, then were pressed into service by the strange Orcs in the north. Their leader, a cunning little runt called Nishrûk, hides in the ruins west of this encampment in the darkest reaches of Minas Eriol.

'Bram sent me here to see that the leader was destroyed and that these fine folk were watched over properly. Now, I know that the encampment is deep beyond the ruins to the west in an area that looks truly infested by goblins. 

'Go to that section of the ruins of Minas Eriol and kill Nishrûk. I'll have a reward for you when the deed is done.''Bram put too much faith in me, I fear. I am not a stout enough warrior to go wading through the number of goblins perched to the west. Better to leave that to folk like you. Hardy and hale folk who crave adventure.''Heroes come from unlikely places. You've done very well, ${PLAYER}. Were I braver, I would have waded into those goblins on my own.

'While we may have dealt a blow against the goblins here in the west, it's unlikely that the tribe will scatter to the wind. They're well organized for goblins, almost as if there is a purpose to their actions. Something tells me that the Lone-lands is in for bad times... well, worse than usual.

'We'll survive -- we always do -- and thanks to you, we may be able to handle the goblins near our Inn. I promised you a gift. This was mine when I was still young enough to use it... I pass it now to you. May it treat you as well as it did me.'Brigands along the road through Andrath are waylaying travellers.Gerwyn has asked you to defeat bandits who chased them out of Andrath.

The bandits are south of Andrath, in northern Cardolan.Defeat Greenway raiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Greenway knaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Greenway bowmen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should tell Gerwyn that you defeated a number of Greenway bandits.

Gerwyn is in the circle of caravans, in northern Cardolan.Return to Gerwyn'Well met, fellow traveller. I see that you are also not from these lands. We came down the Greenway from Bree, and I should have known our luck had been too good for too long. We were attacked by brigands as we passed through Andrath, and in the hurry to get away from them, we had a waggon wheel crack. We circled up here for repairs, but I am worried the ruffians will follow us, or attack others on the road.

'You seem capable and eager. There's coin in it for you, if you deal with them for us.''You return victorious! Most excellent! I know these roads are no longer travelled as they once were, but perhaps we have saved some lives today, and I am grateful we won't have to worry about having them at our backs.'The Grimfens are in the south-east extent of the Lone-lands. Travellers have avoided this place for as long as any can remember -- and for good reason.Explore the Grimfens.Ost Haer was a fortress of Arthedain set against the might of Rhudaur's Garth Agarwen in ancient days, now fallen into ruin and decay, home to the shades of Oath-breakers sworn to defeat the Red-maid of Agamaur.Nindor was another fortification of Arthedain, overrun by the Hillmen of Rhudaur in the wars with Angmar. Wights summoned by the Gaunt-lords of Morgoth now haunt the ruins.Rhiangar is convinced answers can be found by speaking with an ancient hag who resides in the gloomy Old Forest.Rhiangar has asked you to look for the hag of the Old Forest.

The Old Forest is in north-western Cardolan.Find the hag of the Old ForestHenbran has asked you to bring her fish from the river.

The river is located near Sarch Vorn, next to the Old Forest.Catch fish (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the fish you have caught to Henbran Amon.

Henbran is in the Old Forest, in north-western Cardolan.'Luilloth was a hero, just as I always suspected! It sounds like she found some method of dispelling the dead that were plaguing Cardolan in her day, but there is no mention of what that method might have been.

'The section about the forest is intriguing! I grew up hearing rumours of a hag of the Old Forest who has haunted its wood for hundreds of years! We need to talk to this hag! Perhaps she was the one Luilloth met with beneath the trees. Obviously, I cannot accompany you, but I implore you to search for the hag of the woods! She could hold the key to us understanding how to banish the risen dead!''Oh, hello there. Hag of the Old Forest? Oh dear, are they still calling us that? Hoo hoo. Well, you probably are looking for my sister, Henbran. She is over the hill north some, then go through the woods a bit more.''Who are you?! Have you been sent by Blue Cloak? Ah, no. I see you are just some hapless adventurer.'

You begin to explain that you are actually looking for her, but she holds up her hand and interrupts you.

'Stop right there. I do not want to hear your story. I have too much to do! I am naught but a poor old woman, living alone in the dark forest. Usually the man in the blue cloak comes by with a basket of food, but he has not been by for days. I do not know who he is, but hoo, did I become dependent upon the fish he brought!

'Well now, I have an idea! You seem to want something from me, though I am but a poor old woman, who has nothing. Nothing! Where was I? Oh yes, you want something from me, and I want this week's fish. Go get me some fish from the nearby river. Then I will hear your tale. If not, then good day to you!''You again? Oh, but you seem to have fish with you this time! Excellent! I will take those, then we may talk.'Orcs have entered the North Downs from the north. The farmers of the region fled south, except old Gatson, who is determined to hold his land against the Orcs.Orthonn may be found at the ruins of Ost Lagoros, north-west of Gatson's farm by the river.

Farmer Gatson told you that he has been helping the Rangers with provisions for many years and now expects them to help him protect his farm. He has sent you to speak with the Ranger he delivers the food to, a man named Orthonn.Gatson awaits you at his farm to the east of Ost Lagoros.

Orthonn admitted that Gatson had provisioned them often, but told you that the Rangers did not have the numbers to defend the farms of the North Downs. He asked you to return to Gatson and exhort the farmer and his workhands to flee at once.'Hullo there. Maybe you can help me out. We're in a bit of a bind here. This is the last farm in the North Downs -- all of the other landowners have been run off their places by the Orcs.

'I don't mind saying that the Orcs who've moved into the area are more than I can handle on my own. I've made ties with a few of them Rangers and been helping provision them for a good many years. It's about time they did me a good turn for it.

'Now, I don't know where he goes with it, but I take their goods to a Ranger who camps out near those old ruins to the north-west of my farm. Ost Lagoros is what they call it, I think. The fellow's name is Orthonn.''Us that are still here will cleave to Master Gatson no matter what may come, even if Orcs be the end of us.''Please go to Orthonn out in those old ruins and get me some help defending my farm against the Orcs!''Gatson? He has not fled south as he was told? Aye, he has aided us with provisions on many an occasion, but he has always been paid in either coin or goods.

'When we learned that a great host of Orcs was amassing in the North, preparing to march upon Eriador, we sent messages to all the farmers of the North Downs, warning them to flee south. My kindred have not the numbers to defend these farmers from the Orc army.

'Gatson's farm stands in the path of Angmar's army. Return to him, if you will, and exhort him and his hands to leave at once. His farm is not defensible.''I cannot help Gatson...he was warned to leave the North Downs, and leave he must.''Orthonn won't help? But I can't leave! Those Orcs will come through here and burn everything! My family has had this farm since time out of mind, and I'll not be the one to let it all go to ruin.

'The farmhands that haven't fled...Gilmar and those other fools will stick with me to the end if I stay. What can I do?'Colbert the Mad has followed you to Amon Amrûn, where something happened to make him lose his mind after he stirred up the furious shades from their tomb while attempting to rob it.Amon Amrûn is in the eastern Fields of Fornost in the North Downs.

You should search Amon Amrûn for signs of what happened to cause Colbert to go mad.Find the heirloom chest and return it to its tombColbert awaits you at his overlook south of Amon Amrûn.

You should speak with Colbert.Tell Colbert the Mad that the stirred shades have returned to restYou ask Colbert the Mad what happened here after he attempted to rob the graves of Amon Amrûn.

'Two went in and one came out. But I never came out, not really. The shades that stirred as we cradled the loot, they stir now in my mind, always.

'I can never leave Amon Amrûn. Like the shades. Soon I'll be no more than a wandering ghost, just like them.''My head... it is a little clearer now. The fog is receding. How strange.

'Do you know, it wasn't very wise for my brother or I to come here and start robbing random tombs. We are professional treasure-hunters, but we separated from the rest of the group a few weeks back. We were seeking the riches of old Fornost.

'I wonder if the others are still encamped where we left them....'In the days of King Arvedui, last king at Fornost, a company of the king's men betrayed their oaths to Arthedain, allowing Fornost to fall to the armies of Angmar. Arvedui cursed these men to never know rest until they had fulfilled their oaths.The shade of the Oath-breaker captain can be found north-east of Mincham's camp, in some scattered ruins by the walls of Fornost.

Mincham has asked you to find the shade of the Oath-breaker captain and recall him and his followers to their ancient duty.Talk to the shade of the Oath-breaker captainMincham awaits you at his camp.

The Oath-breaker captain told you that he and his followers had sworn a new allegiance to someone named Amarthiel. Mincham may know what this means.Talk to Mincham'In the days of the war against Angmar a thousand years ago, a group of King Arvedui's men forsook his call to arms. Arvedui cursed these men, saying they should know no rest until they fulfilled their duty. To this day, they have walked the Fields of Fornost, tormented by their failings.

'The time has come for these shades to be free at last. Assemble your allies and seek out the Oath-breaker captain. He can be found beneath the very walls of Fornost, north-east of here by some old, broken ruins of Arthedain.

'Beware, though; his was a fell fate, and he may not be friendly to those who remind him of his foresworn oaths.''It is our duty to offer the shades of Men freedom from their curse and call them to fight against Angmar... even more so in that these Men are our own kindred.''What? Who dares to interrupt my ancient vigil?

'You fool! How dare you remind me of our pathetic oaths to the craven Arvedui! We have sworn new oaths now!

'We follow Amarthiel, and soon we will sweep aside all the living fools of the North!''Alas! I regret sending you on this foolhardy task. I had expected the shade to be of an ill mind, but not to go so far as to attack you! It seems that the Oath-breakers now serve the Enemy in thought and deed.

'Amarthiel... it seems I have heard that name before. I should not speak of such things now, but these are indeed dark tidings you bring!'Orcs have taken over the canyons of Nan Wathren, and should be driven out.Orcs can be found in Nan Wathren, in the southern North Downs.

