Sarch Vorn is in northern Cardolan.Search for cluesYou have found an old necklace on the weather-worn skeleton of a woman. You suspect Rhiangar would be interested in this item.

You should bring the necklace to her in Herne.'I do not know what you may find in Sarch Vorn, but I wonder if I could ask you to look for any clues that my mother may have gone that way. I suspect that like us, she was following in Luilloth's footsteps.

'I do not know what you might find, but anything at all would be of interest to me. I am returning to Herne. The stew must need stirring by now. You carry much hope with you, and I will keep hope in my heart that I will see you again.''What have you got there? Oh... where did you...'

You tell her of the skeleton you found near Sarch Vorn.

'But this... this was my mother's necklace.'

She is silent for a time, her hand closing around the tarnished necklace. Then she looks up at you with a sad smile.

'Thank you. I suppose knowing what happened means that I can close the door to my heart that I left open, hoping she would one day return. I think I always knew, though, that she would not.'The standing stones of Tyrn Gorthad are covered with a slow-spreading lichen.Hafren has asked you to collect lichen from standing stones.

Standing stones can be found in Tyrn Gorthad.Collect lichen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the lichen you collected to Hafren.

Hafren is at Gerwyn's convoy, in northern Cardolan.'One of our scouts came back with reports of great circles of standing stones on the other side of the hill across the road.

'If you happen to find yourself among them, would you look out for a green-grey lichen that may be growing on their surfaces? It has healing powers, and it also slowly destroys the stones. Gently scrape it away and bring it back here for a reward!''I thank you. You have helped to save the lives of my companions and lengthened the lives of the stones as well.'An odd people calling themselves the Earth-kin have been discovered in the eastern North Downs. Seek out their villages and learn more of them, and whether they be friend or foe.NOT USEDIt seems that the Earth-kin hunters of Rusfold are friendly enough, if rather odd. They speak of others of their kind to the east however, who have fallen under the sway of Angmar.It seems that this village and others have fallen under the sway of Angmar. The Earth-kin are fighting amongst themselves -- to the amusment of the lords of Angmar, no doubt.Kar Lak is a camp of Earth-kin that has fallen under the yoke of Angmar. If they would listen to reason perhaps they could be freed, but they do not seem to be in a mood to talk.Hidden deep within the Ram Dúath you have discoverd this camp of the Earth-kin. Trapped from their home in the south of Angmar by the forces of the Angmarim, their lot does not seem to be a happy one, as they have been turned against one another by the lies of Angmar.Idhremmin has heard a strange voice wafting from the Fields of Fornost, and you have decided to investigate.Idhremmin is at Mincham's Camp in the North Downs, at the south-west edge of the Fields of Fornost.

