'He speaks very little, but of one thing I am certain: whatever draws his attention, he fears it. He will not venture into the Fields of Fornost to seek it.''Tra-lily-la, tra-la! Oh! But it is long since I had someone to sing and dance with me. Come, sing! Tra-lily, tra-la....'You ask Idhremmin what he hears, but he does not respond. His expression is slightly annoyed, as if you have interrupted him in something important.You tell Idhremmin that you have heard the strange voice, and he looks at you sharply. His words come haltingly, as if the Common Speech is strange to him.

'You hear the twisted song. Great evil lies beyond the light of this fire. Do you seek death? If not, stay, and listen from afar.''You did well. Not many would have survived such an encounter, let alone drive off the fell spirit without harming the girl.'The missing child, Cai, has been recovered safely, but the wailing Elf-woman is still on the run! She must be found before she lures any other children into danger.Gurthern has suggested you speak with the Elves who are camped at Sírlond, across the river from Caranost.

