<rgb=#FF0000>Fellowship recommended.</rgb>'I... I cannot believe it. Truly, ${PLAYER}... you were able to enter that pass and leave again with your life intact? It is incredible. You have halted what would have been certain war for our people. You have saved the good folk of Trestlebridge, saved their homes and livelihoods.

'I cannot thank you enough!'Many old treasures from before the days of Fornost's downfall still remain in the Fields of Fornost.Amon Amrûn is in the eastern Fields of Fornost.

Colbert the Mad wants you to investigate Amon Amrûn, for he claimed there was a great deal of treasure there, but he was afraid to claim it.Investigate Amon AmrûnAmon Amrûn is in the eastern Fields of Fornost.

The shades of Amon Amrûn seem to be disturbed because their ancient tomb has been robbed.Search for signs of looters at Amon AmrûnSomeone is watching you from a hill just south of Amon Amrûn.

You should confront the person who followed you here.Speak with the person who followed you here'I went many, many places in the Fields of Fornost. I came from a group of treasure hunters, you know, but they are still within. I went to Amon Amrûn and heard the call of death.

'I sought treasure there, but I could not withstand the presence there. It is far to the east. Will you seek your own death? Mad, mad, mad.''Who disturbs Amon Amrûn? More thieves to unearth our treasure? Have a taste of death, thief!''Clever, to have found me out! The Brothers Colbert, Adventurers, that's who we were afore we adventured here. The Brothers Colbert, Grave Robbers, afore we robbed the wrong grave. The Brothers Colbert, making a fine living, before Amon Amrûn.

'Now it is just one Colbert, Colbert the Mad.'

