'If you would gain such a boon, travel to the Eglain encampment, which lies in the Lone-lands, and speak to Radagast there.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''If you wish to gain insight from Radagast the Brown, you should travel to his tower the Eglain camp in Agamaur.''Greetings, friend. You have come seeking more knowledge about the creatures of nature? Perhaps I can help you, but first you must prove to be a true friend of the wild.'When Gondranc of Esteldín was journeying north from Rivendell, he had promised a man of Trestlebridge that he would assist them by providing armour for use against the Orcs.Asikko is at the Earth-kin camp, found by skirting the hills northward from the eastern entrance to Esteldín.

In order to fulfil his obligation to Trestlebridge, Gondranc has asked you to obtain a book of leatherworking lore promised to him by Asikko, chieftain of the Earth-kin.Talk to Asikko'Your efforts are well known amongst all here in Esteldín, ${PLAYER}. I am hopeful that you will assist me with a small task.

'Long ago, when I journeyed abroad, I taught Asikko, the chieftain of the Earth-kin the Westron letters. In return, he offered to write me a book describing their leatherworking methods. I need this book to fulfil a promise I made to a man in Trestlebridge as I came north from Rivendell in the guise of a common leatherworker. I promised to make for his people armour suitable for use against the Orcs.

'Will you go to Asikko and ask for the book? The Earth-kin are encamped north-east of here. Just skirt the hills northward from the eastern entrance to Esteldín.''Asikko is honourable and trustworthy. I know that he will not abandon his promise.''Ha, you come for my book! I had not thought on those days for long and long.

'Are you Gondranc? No... you are not he. You must forgive me, but it is difficult to know. You little folk look so much alike to the Suuri-lehmä, and my mind is on the pain of my own people.'The Rangers of Esteldín are in need of supplies.Hillborn woad and hillborn orchanet grow on the hills of eastern Nan Amlug and Rhunenlad.

Elúr has asked you to collect some hillborn woad and hillborn orchanet for Esteldín.Collect hillborn woad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect hillborn orchanet (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The orchanet and woad you collected can be brought to Nethúr in Esteldín.Bring the dye-plants to Nethúr in Esteldín'The Rangers of Esteldín have always kept woad and orchanet close at hand for the dyeing of banners, and I passed much on my way here. Sadly, it would not be practical to bring these on my scouting mission.

'If you pick some for Esteldín, they will be most pleased.''Woad and orchanet! How thoughtful of you to bring these to us, ${PLAYER}.'Ragnarr Hornsounder went to live among the Earth-kin, but a recent betrayal has made the Earth-kin distrustful.The aurochs skull can be found in the Warg territory to the north-east of the Earth-kin camp.

In order to regain the trust of the Earth-kin, Ragnarr Hornsounder has asked you to collect an aurochs skull from the totem in the hills of eastern Nan Amlug and return it to him at the Earth-kin camp. A group of Wargs currently roam this territory.'The Jorthkyn have always been a mystery of sorts; helping my people without asking for payment. I came here to live among them so that our people could know each other better.

'This group is all that remains of a hunting party from beyond the Ram Dúath. After crossing the pass, their First Hunter turned on them, throwing the party into chaos.

'I am still a stranger and not fully trusted, especially after this recent betrayal. I will need to gain their trust again. I understand their tribal totem is the aurochs. When the First Hunter's group turned, they took one of the totem skulls. I have seen a totem shrine among the hills north-east from here. Collect this skull for me so that I might win the trust of the tribe.''This is good, you have done fine but... well, I might have made a mistake....'Radagast wants to learn what drew a creature such as Ivar to the Red Swamp. He thinks that something could be learned from one of the Eglain.Aric is south of Ost Guruth, beyond Talath Gaun, down in Harloeg.

Radagast spoke of a Man named Aric the Stone-speaker. Aric may be able to tell you the history of the Red Swamp.Talk to Aric the Stone-speaker in Harloeg'This land was the site of many battles in the past. Some say the swamp takes its name from the blood of fallen Men that stains the earth red. But my knowledge of the swamp's history is limited.

'I do know of a Man named Aric, a wise Man of the Eglain, though only by reputation. He is a Stone-speaker, a scholar who studies the stones and collects knowledge from their markings. Aric knows much of the local lore.

'Travel to him and ask for his help. He currently dwells south of here, beyond Talath Gaun, down in Harloeg. He may provide us with the knowledge we seek.''Find Aric the Stone-speaker. We do not have the luxury of time.''I know much about these lands, yes. Do you know from whence my knowledge stems?

'The dead hold secrets... great secrets, terrible secrets. Secrets they clutch to their chests like fire on a winter's day. Memories keep their hearts warm, you see? No, perhaps you do not see.

'But you shall. Oh yes, I believe you shall.'While investigating the source of the Wights of the Red Swamp, Radagast sent you to a man named Aric the Stone-speaker. Aric hinted that the dead might hold the answers you seek.Emelin haunts the area called Ost Haer.

Aric spoke of a shade called Emelin. If you can prove your worth to the shade, he might give you the information you desire.Talk to EmelinEmelin haunts the area called Ost Haer.

Emelin has tasked you with defeating the apparitions of his dead warriors. Succeed, and he will help you. Fail, and you may perish.Talk to Emelin at Ost Haer'You can learn many things from the Dead. But there is one troublesome shade called Emelin that resists all attempts at communication. Perhaps you may succeed where I have not.

'Emelin is... difficult. He is bound by pride and deems the living beneath contempt. If you can prove yourself to him, this might grant you enough status in his eyes that he will lend you aid.

'Beware when you speak to him. He will try and win your trust with pleasant words, then send you off to your doom. You will find him at the ruins of Ost Haer.''Emelin is a tricky fellow and keeps his secrets well.''Thou drawest breath and yet thou dost wish to speak with me? Thou art not like the man Aric. He is stone-wise and knows the secrets of this land. But even he I despise for his warm flesh and bright-eyed stare.

'Wisdom will be thine if thou art proven worthy. Dost thou dare to face my warriors? If thou art the victor, then I shall help thee upon thy quest.

'Fail, and thou shalt not see the light of another day....''Thou art alive still to draw breath, though ragged and coarse it be. Rest thyself and hearken unto me.

'Terrible deeds I have done in the name of the kings of old. While evil corrupted this land, my men and I stood by and did nothing, ignoring our charge. Now the Red Maid serves Angmar... something we swore to prevent. Iarwain Ben-adar cursed us to live as half-dead, such was our failure.

'Dost thou understand? I will help thee in order to break my curse, but thou must do more to secure my aid.'An enterprising and perhaps delusional member of the Eglain plans on creating strange food dishes to assist in the shortage that the Eglain face almost regularly.Crawlers can be found throughout the swamp of Harloeg. Glaednoth is located at Ost Haer in the southern most reaches of Harloeg.

Glaednoth has asked you to collect meat from the crawlers of Harloeg.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'Have you seen them scurrying on their little legs with their bellies scraping the ground? Yes, they have a hard shell, but I wager that beneath the shell there is soft meat, succulent and ready for a basting of herbs and spices to bring out the finer flavours lingering within!

'I aim to prove that we can live on more than what we can trade for with Bree-land, and I need some aid doing so. 

'You will find crawlers all throughout the swamp here in Harloeg. Kill them and bring me the meat within their little shells so that I might test out the viability of a meal of the crunchy little crawlers.''Why these are not succulent at all... they are rather crunchy actually. I wonder how to cook this? I shall have to find a way....

'I must give you what I offered. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'An enterprising and perhaps delusional member of the Eglain plans on creating strange food dishes to assist in the shortage that the Eglain face almost regularly.Sickle-flies can be found throughout the swamp of Harloeg. Glaednoth is located at Ost Haer in the southernmost reaches of Harloeg.

Glaednoth has asked you to collect gizzards from the sickle-flies of Harloeg.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'I have slapped a good number of those sickle-flies and seen their insides.

'It looks to me that with the proper preparation you could mix together a tasty pudding from what they have within them. If you find yourself out on the fen and cornered by these creatures will you collect their gizzards?

'I think that I shall make a fine pudding from them.''Yes! These are definitely soft enough and bear the consistency I desire.

'I must give you what I offered. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'An enterprising and perhaps delusional member of the Eglain plans on creating strange food dishes to assist in the shortage that the Eglain face almost regularly.Soggy mushrooms can be found in the ruins west of Ost Haer. Glaednoth can be found within the ruins of Ost Haer in the southern stretch of Harloeg.

Glaednoth asked you to search for soggy mushrooms so he might try to make an interesting meal from them.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.</rgb>'I have no doubt that the mushrooms within the ruins to the west will be delectable.

'They have all the characteristics of a tasty dish but they need harvesting. Aric has been clear that he thinks I will find trouble if I go there, but he told me that offering up these shiny gems may find me some assistance.

'All I want is ten of the mushrooms from the ruins to the west so that I might mix together a wonderful dish I shall call soggy mushroom mash. Would you be willing to help?''What is that stench? Is that you? No? The mushrooms?

'Oh goodness, well this will take a great deal of spices to cover, but who is to say that this will make the meal any less filling?

'Thank you for this.'Istuienn seeks your aid with a matter of some importance.Istuienn is in Esteldín.

You should speak with Istuienn.Speak with IstuiennAsikko, chieftain of the Suuri-lehmä, can be found at the Earth-kin camp located along the hills north of the eastern entrance to Esteldín.

Istuienn asked you for a favour; she gave you a letter and sent you to find Asikko, the chieftain of the Earth-kin still loyal to the defence of Ram Dúath.'I hear that Istuienn is looking for aid with a task. Will you speak with her, ${PLAYER}? She can generally be found further within Esteldín.''Perhaps Asikko will declare an alliance with us once you have delivered that letter.''You see that we raise no weapons against you, ${RACE}. We are peaceful and wish to remain that way.

'I see that the Men have chosen to honour our oath. This pleases me. We shall honour our oaths as well and await the return of our stolen weapons.

'We shall not rest until our brethren return to our ways or are removed. Such betrayal cannot be allowed.''I have a favour to ask of you.

'Just east from Esteldín and to the north along the base of the hills surrounding this hidden fort, you will find an Earth-kin camp. The denizens there are of the Suuri-lehmä tribe, our friends. We must make sure they know of our efforts on their behalf.

'Will you take this letter to Asikko, their chieftain? It may be that he will openly declare an alliance with my people, which can only serve to strengthen our position in the North Downs.'Within the ruins of Dol Vaeg, Northrim collects the last few items needed for Stanric's defence. Soon the Eglain hope to be prepared for the worst, a prolonged battle against encroaching darkness.The Last Bridge lies at the eastern end of the Great East Road.

Northrim gave you an empty, cured bladder and asked you to collect water from the Hoarwell on the northern side of the Last Bridge.Northrim awaits your return with clean water at Dol Vaeg, west of the Last Bridge.

You made your way to the Hoarwell's edge and collected water from the banks. You should return at once to Northrim.'Before you leave, ${PLAYER}, I would ask one other small task, left over from the last folk who stopped to aid us here.

'We have some bladders already cleaned and ready for water. I ask that you make your way along the Great East Road to the Last Bridge and fill this bladder with water from Mitheithel, the Hoarwell.

'The Bridge has stood through many ages, and we have found that the water taken from the northern end of the bridge is best. Draw the water, then return to me.''Fill the bladder at the water's edge on the north side of the Last Bridge, then return here.''We have water now to fill our barrels. I am grateful for all that you have done for my people. Here, ${PLAYER}, take this and know the gratitude of all the Eglain of Ost Guruth.'The Earth-kin once believed the hides of the Wargs to be utterly useless, but have recently discovered a way to cure them.Both dire Wargs and harrow weed can be found in the eastern plains of Nan Amlug.

In order to make armour for the Suuri-lehmä, Mauno has asked you to gather hides from dire Wargs and some harrow weed.Collect dire Warg hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect harrow weed (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mauno is at the camp of the Suuri-lehmä.

You have gathered enough Warg hides and the harrow weed that Mauno needs to cure them. You should take them to Mauno as soon as possible.'We long thought the fur of Wargs useless. It rots too quickly as they die. But we have found that it may be cured with a simple mixture of harrow weed, a bitter plant that grows in the plains nearby.

'If you bring me hides from dire Wargs and some harrow weed, I may be able to fashion armour from it. The Wargs wander the plains in the east.

'The dark hides of the dire Wargs might make armour that will let us hide more easily from the Rauta-lehmä and the Angmarim.''Bring me harrow weed and Warg hides, and I will make you armour.''Ah, you have brought all that I sent you for. Good.

'Now I shall fashion for you something of worth from these vile beasts who have caused us so much anguish.'Eriac the Strong, at the Eglain-camp in Agamaur, desires broken short bows from the intelligent foes found in Agamaur.You accepted a task from Eriac the Strong to acquire broken short bows from the intelligent foes within Agamaur. You can find Eriac the Strong within the Eglain-camp at Agamaur.Wanted: Broken short bows from the intelligent foes in Agamaur. Bring them to Eriac the Strong at the Eglain-camp in Agamaur.Wanted: Broken short bows from the intelligent foes in Agamaur.'They will go with the trophies they earned in their final battle, thanks to you.

'Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Elsa the Bold, at the Eglain-camp in Agamaur, desires crooked branches from the twisted creatures of nature found in Agamaur.You accepted a task from Elsa the Bold to acquire crooked branches from the creatures of nature within the swamp of Agamaur. You can find Elsa the Bold within the Eglain-camp in Agamaur.Wanted: Crooked branches from the twisted creatures of nature in Agamaur. Bring them to Elsa the Bold at the Eglain-camp at Agamaur.Wanted: Crooked branches from the twisted creatures of nature in Agamaur.'This is a painful effort, but one that must be done.

'Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Eriac the Strong, at the Eglain-camp at Agamaur, desires decrepit finger bones from the Dead found in Agamaur.You accepted a task from Eriac the Strong to acquire decrepit finger bones from the Dead within Agamaur. You can find Eriac the Strong within the Eglain-camp in Agamaur.Wanted: decrepit finger bones from the Dead in Agamaur. Bring them to Eriac the Strong at the Eglain-camp in Agamaur.Wanted: decrepit finger bones from the Dead in Agamaur.'These bones will not rise again, though I have no doubt that the Gaunt-lord Ivar has more bones at his disposal.

'Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Dragons were bred long ages ago to break the power of the Elves in the North -- and in this they succeeded with their vast power and cunning, acting as a deadly spearhead of the Enemy's armies that none could stand against. Like Elves, Dragons have never been numerous, and their savage demeanor means that few of their offspring ever reach adulthood. Their numbers have also dwindled in Middle-earth -- but recently many of the lesser drakes have been unleashed from Angmar, which is worrisome indeed, for if these lesser beasts have reappeared, can the Dragons be far behind? Regardless of the danger, these creatures must be destroyed!Defeat drakesOf all the powers of the Enemy, the goblins are the only ones to have openly assaulted the Shire. They were defeated by Bullroarer Took many years ago -- but now the descendants of Golfimbul have again been seen near the bounds of your fair land, as well as many other places in the North. Hobbits have been called to take up arms again, and the Bounders have redoubled their training, lest they be caught unawares by these savage creatures.Defeat goblinsThe dwarves have always held the advantage over the goblins in terms of skill in battle as well as quality of weapons, armour, and fortifications. The goblins, however, have always held the advantage in numbers -- a rather vast advantage.Defeat goblinsFor many years there have been tribes of Men who have shunned the rule of Kings and the life of great cities and towns. While some of these might be called allies by the Men of Gondor or Rohan, far too often they fall under the sway of the Enemy, who plays upon their distrust of the great Kingdoms, or threatens them with hidden force, or sways them with false riches and power. Thus it has been that the Kingdoms of Middle-earth have often found themselves at war with the folk of the Hills when the Enemy rises -- and this age seems no exception.Defeat Hillmen and DunlendingsOrcs are clever, skilled, and brutal in combat. They do not however, anticipate their enemy changing into a massive bear and mauling them.Defeat OrcsUnlike the goblins, the Orcs have been raised with a martial outlook and form the backbone of the Enemy's armies. They are neither cowards nor weaklings -- though they cannot hope to match the martial prowess of the Elves -- but their numbers and war industry are vast when motivated by their shadowy lords.Defeat OrcsWhere have these horrors come from? What ever happened to nice little garden spiders eating flies and all that? These days your idea of a spider starts at about two feet across and goes up from there -- hardly the kind of thing you would expect to encounter in the cozy Shire, yet now they seem to be common in all the forests of Eriador. It is enough to make even the most staid and placid hobbit sit up and take notice that things are getting rather queer these days.Defeat spidersThese creatures have taken root in the once pure woods of Middle-earth. You have made some progress in clearing them out.Defeat spidersTrolls are a particularly deadly threat to the dwarves. Capable of smashing the strongest fortifications and thriving in the dark underground domains where the sun poses no danger, they have often been used to spearhead major assaults against the dwarf-kingdoms.Defeat trollsWargs are sometimes used by goblins as mounts to extend the range of their attacks against villages and settlements, for goblins are loth to strike further than they can march in a single night and still return to the dark safety of their caves before morning comes.Defeat WargsEsteldín employs a number of scouts who cast their eyes far beyond the walls of the refuge.Melthindir, a watcher of Esteldín, can be found at the eastern entrance to Esteldín.

You should offer your aid to Melthindir.Offer assistance to Melthindir'You have helped us enough, little friend, and you have the thanks of our tribe. I know that the Men-folk, these Rangers, must need your help again. I see them looking out with their watchful eyes.''You have come to aid me? That is well! I have many fears tugging at my mind today.'The unexpected invasion of the Orcs from the North has caught the Rangers of Esteldín unprepared, with many of their kindred abroad in other lands. This new threat has forced them to recall as many of their kind as they can and to arm themselves for war.The Rangers' supply troves are hidden throughout eastern Nan Amlug and Rhunenlad.

In preparation for war, Melthindir is tasked with recovering the stores of weapons and supplies his predecessor hid. He has asked you to search Nan Amlug and Rhunenlad for these hidden stores. He only knows that these troves are hidden by rocks and trees.'The Orcs' invasion from the North has caught the Rangers of the North unprepared. Many of our kindred are abroad in other lands, preparing a defence against the Shadow in the East, and our eyes were not turned northwards.

'This army that has come down from Angmar is too great for our forces in the North Downs to defeat without support, yet we must still prepare for the fighting that is to come.

'My predecessor stored many weapons and supplies throughout eastern Nan Amlug and Rhunenlad, but I do not know exactly where. I need you to seek out these troves and bring them to me. The thing that I do know is that these troves were all hidden near rocks and trees. This will not be an easy search without proper guidance, but in these dark times every resource we can gather will be of great help to us.''It will take some work to make many of these weapons usable, but they are better than hoes and hay-forks. We shall set about the repairs at once.

'I trust that your search was not too difficult. We must be resolute and fight back against these Orcs before the North Downs are lost. They must not be allowed to invade Bree-land, or many innocents will be killed and all the North may fall.'For many ages, the Earth-kin protected the pass through Ram Dúath from Angmar, but since the betrayal of the Suuri-lehmä tribe by First Hunter Jarkko and his followers, the Earth-kin have themselves become trapped in the North Downs.The Earth-kin of the Rauta-lehmä faction are encamped east of Esteldín in Nan Amlug.

You should show the traitorous Rauta-lehmä that they have chosen the wrong side in the coming war.Defeat Rauta-lehmä Warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Rauta-lehmä Hunters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated the Earth-kin of the Rauta-lehmä in the eastern section of Nan Amlug.CompletedFor many ages, the Earth-kin protected the pass through Ram Dúath from Angmar, but since the betrayal of the Suuri-lehmä tribe by First Hunter Jarkko and his followers, the Earth-kin have themselves become trapped in the North Downs.

You should defeat the Rauta-lehmä, as the traitors call themselves. Show them that their betrayal is known and will not be brooked.You have defeated a number of the Rauta-lehmä in eastern Nan Amlug.You have encountered a number of interesting herbs in your travels. These should be collected as you make your way through the lands, and brought to the Ranger Orthonn.Periwinkle can be found among rock outcroppings atop the hills of Nan Amlug, near Othrikar. Meadowsweet can be found in south facing tree roots in the spider-camp south of Esteldín. Butterbur can be found growing along the waters edge in the fens near the Elf-refuge of Lin Giliath in Meluinen.

You should gather herbs for Orthonn.Collect meadowsweet (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect periwinkle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect butterbur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Orthonn is in Kingsfell, north of Gatson's Farm.

You should bring the herbs you gathered to Orthonn.Bring the herbs to OrthonnYou have encountered a number of interesting herbs in your travels. These should be collected as you make your way through the lands, and brought to the Ranger Orthonn.'Ah, what a pleasant surprise! I do have a great fondness for herb-lore. Thank you for this gift, ${PLAYER}.'When First Hunter Jarkko betrayed the Suuri-lehmä, he left with the totem of the tribe's hunter; the skull of the Great Aurochs -- the namesake of the Suuri-lehmä. You brought a totem skull to Ragnarr, but it appears that it is not sufficient.The skull of The Great Aurochs is being held in the lands of the Rauta-lehmä, eastward across Nan Amlug.

In order to prove his benign intent to the Earth-kin, Ragnarr Hornsounder has asked you to retrieve the stolen skull of The Great Aurochs from the Rauta-lehmä.Collect the skull of the Great AurochsRagnarr Hornsounder is at the camp of the Suuri-lehmä, west of the Rauta-lehmä camp.

You should return the skull of the Great Aurochs to Ragnarr Hornsounder.'I seem to have misunderstood the Jorthkyn. The skull that was taken by the First Hunter was not just any aurochs skull, but the skull of the Great Aurochs -- the namesake of their tribe, Suuri-lehmä.

'This skull has been a symbol of the tribe's hunters for generations. If you could retrieve this totem it would prove my purpose is pure and without ill intent.

'Go to the camps of the traitorous Jorthkyn -- the Rauta-lehmä -- eastward across the Nan Amlug. That is where the skull of The Great Aurochs has been taken. Look for a place of reverence or altar, for even these lowly curs could not have abandoned all they once held dear. The skull will be difficult to carry.''Have you not found the skull yet? I'm very sorry about the last incident. I promise, if you do this for me, I'll not ask another favour of you.''The gift of their returned totem will surely win the trust of the Jorthkyn! My thanks to you.'Hillmen from Angmar followed the Orc army through Ram Dúath into the North Downs and established an encampment near the head of the pass. These Hillmen serve to keep open the passage from Angmar.The Hillmen are encamped near the mouth of the eastern entrance to Ram Dúath, north-east of Esteldín.

You should collect brooches from the Hillmen, so that the composition of their forces may be determined.Collect brooches from Hillmen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Melthindir stands outside of Esteldín, looking out onto eastern Nan Amlug.

You should return to Melthindir with the brooches you collected.Return to Melthindir'The Hillmen encamped at the eastern entrance of the Ram Dúath pass have me concerned.

'These are men who long ago foreswore their allegiance to Angmar, after the Witch-king was defeated, and have never united beneath a single banner since. That they should now serve under the banner of Angmar is troubling, but that they should guard the pass into Angmar is alarming.

'Before we can know best how to deal with them, we need to know their strength. These Hillmen often wear brooches by which they distinguish one another. Collect these brooches, so that I may determine what is the composition of their ranks.''There is no doubt then that they have brought forces who are well-armed if these are the most plentiful of the inhabitants of their encampment. This bodes ill for our chances to push through the eastern section of Ram Dúath.

'We will need to redouble our efforts against the Angmarim if we are to make a strong attack against them in the north. Thank you, friend.'Elder Tahvo has asked you to prove yourself by defeating many Wargs on his turf.Warg packs prowl the hills of eastern Nan Amlug, befouling the land of the Rauta-lehmä.

