You should find out if Radagast the Brown has anything else for you to do.'There is another in need of rescuing -- a turtle, trapped at the edge of the Circle of Blood by the dead who should not walk.

'A turtle can be a difficult creature to draw, but he will respond to a true lore-master's greeting. Try your voice with him, and bring him here.''Ah, you have done well, but there is more still to do.'The townsfolk in Oatbarton await the delivery of heavy carapaces to Ponto Oats at the centre of the town.You have been tasked with collecting and delivering heavy carapaces from the insects and spiders north of Oatbarton. You are to deliver the items to Ponto Oats at the centre of the town of Oatbarton.Wanted: Heavy carapaces from the insects and spiders north of Oatbarton. You can make the delivery to Ponto Oats at Oatbarton centre.Wanted: Heavy carapaces from the insects and spiders north of Oatbarton.'I am certain that we will be able to find a use for these.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The townsfolk in Oatbarton await the delivery of soft skin to Ponto Oats at the centre of the town.You have been tasked with collecting and delivering soft skin from the lizard-like creatures north of Oatbarton. You are to deliver the items to Ponto Oats at the centre of the town of Oatbarton.Wanted: Soft skin from the lizard-like creatures north of Oatbarton. You can make the delivery to Ponto Oats at Oatbarton centre.Wanted: Soft skin from the lizard-like creatures north of Oatbarton.'How strange, the skin is softer than it appears beneath the scales. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Elder Tahvo has asked if you may impress him by delivering him meat from sturdy, tough-to-kill aurochs.The aurochs herds roam the foothills and plains of eastern Nan Amlug.

Elder Tahvo has asked you to impress him by hunting aurochs for their meat.'I like you, little warrior. I wish to see some of your skill. Wargs are little creatures, much like you. The aurochs, they are more like us. Big, difficult to kill.

'If you can bring us the meat of the aurochs, the Suuri-lehmä will hold you in high esteem indeed.''Ah, delicious aurochs-meat! Such a little creature to bring down such a great creature. I am impressed, yes. You did well, little friend.'The Rangers of the North muster their forces within their hidden refuge of Esteldín, preparing to turn back the tide of the Iron Crown.Complete 75 North Downs quests.Complete quests within North DownsWith the migration of Orcs and goblins to the western Lone-lands, the Eglain attempted to rekindle old trade relations with an Elf from Rivendell to the east. However, they encountered great, lumbering beasts upon the Road and dared not continue forwards.Galrîp leads the trolls at Harloeg, south and east of the Tornstones.

Kekkonen made it clear that killing the leader of the trolls would be a great boon. He mentioned that the creature wanders through the woods of Harloeg.Defeat GalrîpKekkonen and the other Earth-kin are at the Tornstones, north and east of Harloeg and south of Ost Guruth.

You should return to Kekkonen and tell him of your success.Talk to Kekkonen at the Tornstones'We left our homes in the hills and stone caves of the north as the trolls stirred and took back the land. In our haste, we easily could have overlooked the leader of their tribe, but we were cautious enough to hear his name and see his look.

'He is large and thick at the legs, bearing the look of a warrior and the strength of many. He is called Galrîp, and he is the leader of the trolls in Harloeg. What a gift it would be to know that he was defeated.

'A gift worthy of lasting peace, it would be. He will wander through the swamps of the south. He will hide among the trees and his brethren and be difficult to face.''You will find this great terror in the woods of Harloeg, south and east of the Tornstones.''It is done then. While our homes are lost, the creature responsible for our exile is no more, and we can find peace here in these lands. The Wargs and Orcs will prove more a nuisance than a danger.

'They are meagre creatures compared to the mighty trolls.'With the migration of Orcs and goblins to the western Lone-lands, the Eglain attempted to rekindle old trade relations with an Elf from Rivendell to the east. However, they encountered great, lumbering beasts upon the road and dared not continue forwards.Stones bearing the historical markings of the Earth-kin may be found on the trolls in the woods bordering Harloeg.

Kekkonen at the Tornstones desires to collect and maintain the history of his people. He dispatched you to fight the trolls of Harloeg to collect the stolen stones bearing the Earth-kin's history.'In our home northward, we wrote histories upon stone. When the trolls came, we abandoned our home and writing and now have little of the memories of our ancestors. The trolls now sift through our old homes and steal that history.

'We have no knowledge of why, we know only that they now carry our histories upon them.

'Will you search them in the shade of the forest on the east edge of Harloeg? Take back our past and return it to us?''Yes, ${PLAYER}, this is the history of my people written upon the stone. You have done us a great service, and it is clear that the little folk to the north chose you well.

