Mauno, the chief hunter of the Suuri-lehmä, asked you to drive off the packs of Wargs which have been slaughtering the aurochs. There are many Wargs, but your efforts should make them more manageable. You should return to Mauno with news of your success.'You seek to help the Earth-kin? Wargs come from the northern hills in great packs. They slaughter the lehmä herds -- what you call aurochs -- for no reason, leaving carcasses rotting in the sun, uneaten.

'The lehmä are our food. With the herds gone, we will starve! There are too many Wargs for our hunters to slay.

'You will hunt them? Drive the packs from our herds, or this winter is our last!''Little one, will you hunt the dire Wargs which threaten my people?''Many Wargs have you slain. Good! Some remain, but our hunters can keep them at bay.

'The herds are thinned. The winter will be lean this year, but the Earth-kin shall endure. Thank you, little one.'With the migration of Orcs and goblins to the western Lone-lands, the Eglain attempted to rekindle old trade relations with an Elf from Rivendell to the east. However, they encountered great, lumbering beasts upon the road and dared not continue forwards.The trolls dwell in a place called Harloeg, far to the south-east of the Tornstones.

Trolls pursued the Earth-kin from the Ettenmoors far to the north-east and have taken residence in the far south-east corner of the Grimfens in the southern Lone-lands. Kekkonen, the Earth-kin chieftain, asked you to assist his people by destroying the trolls which pursued the fragile remnants of his people into the Lone-lands.Defeat trolls in Harloeg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Earth-kin encampment is near the Tornstones, far to the north-west of Harloeg, south of the Great East Road.

Return to the Earth-kin camp near the Tornstones and speak with Kekkonen. He waits to hear how you fared against the Trolls in the Grimfens.'We are pursued by our past from our home in the north and east. We fled as the darkness rose around us and came here to find peace. But peace will not come to us, not while the enemy follows us south. We stay here now, away from the forest and bog, ever in the sun to shield ourselves from darkness. At night, the trolls will roam free.

'If we could confront the darkness and defeat it, we could, perhaps, make friends of others who wish not to succumb to the shadow of evil. You have helped the tribe who wishes our friendship... perhaps you would help the Jorthkyn, too?

'Would you fight the trolls for us, make them go away? They hide in the bog, far to the south and east of here, at a place that Elf-folk call Harloeg. You are very tiny... but you should be fine on your own.''We are pursued, though we have gone far from our home.''You are possessed of strength beyond what I believed of such little people. You have earned our trust and given us hope. We honour you, and we give you our thanks and more.'Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of bumpy scales to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect bumpy scales from the worms and drakes in the area surrounding Esteldín to the north. Once collected, you are to deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Bumpy scales from the worms and drakes north of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Bumpy scales from the worms and drakes north of Esteldín.'I will begin bundling these together now, thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of soft skin to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect soft skin from the beasts in the area surrounding Esteldín to the east and south. Once collected, you are to deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Soft skin from the beasts south and east of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Soft skin from the beasts south and east of Esteldín.'We will do what we can to keep everyone in clothing and shoes. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Ferrif, a Ranger, has asked for a collection of sticky filth to be delivered to him at the Ranger's home at Esteldín.You have accepted a task to collect sticky filth from the spiders in the area surrounding Esteldín to the north and east. Once collected, you are to deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Sticky filth from the spiders north and east of Esteldín. Deliver the items to Ferrif within Esteldín.Wanted: Sticky filth from the spiders north and east of Esteldín.'This will be used in a manner to help our people, thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The two Earth-kin clans in the North Downs have begun to find themselves at war with one another. The peaceful Suuri-lehmä are now at odds with the war-mongering Rauta-lehmä.The stolen weapons may be found on hostile Rauta-lehmä Earth-kin in Nan Amlug, east of Rusfold.

You should recover stolen weapons from the hostile Earth-kin, and return them to Iivari at Rusfold.Collect Earth-kin weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iivari is at Rusfold.

You should bring the recovered weapons to Iivari.Return the Earth-kin weapons to Iivari'We have lost much with our brethren's betrayal. They took from us. They stole from us.

'The Earth-kin of the Rauta-lehmä take weapons from the fallen. Go there and take these weapons back. They belong to us.''You give heart to the Earth-kin, to return these to us. Thank you, small creature. We are allies.'Orcs stormed out of the Ram Dúath and swept across the North Downs. After their passage, Hillmen out of Angmar came through the pass and encamped beyond the cliff faces and treacherous paths.The Hillman-encampment is north-east of Esteldín. The pass is west of the Hillman-encampment, north-west of an outcropping of spiny rocks.

Melthindir has asked you to scout the Hillman-encampment and the pass through which the Hillmen approached to determine the severity of the threat they pose, so that the Rangers can plan a defence against them.Scout the Hillman camp at the Eastern Ram DúathScout the pass through the Western Ram DúathMelthindir awaits your report at Esteldín.

Angmarim forces have sent a small company of Hillmen to the south-east entrance of Ram Dúath. At the south-west entrance of Ram Dúath, you discovered evidence of many worms and drakes. You should return to Melthindir with your report.Return to Melthindir'${PLAYER}, I have need of your assistance. As you are aware, Orcs attacked the North Downs in force, driving farmers from their homes and burning the lands to the south-east. While our attention was turned to the Orcs, we did not notice the Hillmen who came after.

'I look to Dol Dínen as the primary threat against our lands, but we are spread so thinly in the North Downs that we cannot fully determine the threat the Hillmen of Angmar pose.

'I need you to scout the Hillman-encampment to the north-east for us. From that camp, head west until you find an outcropping of strange spiny rocks. The pass continues to the north-west of these rocks. I need to know what you find at both places.''It is a relief to know that the Angmarim forces are not as great as I had feared. Also, while I had known the valley in the west to be home to worms, I did not know that drakes had come there as well.

'You have done us a great service this day, ${PLAYER}.

'There is much yet to be done before we are prepared to deal with the threat from Angmar.'Holger Tanner is the survivor of a party of merchants ambushed by spiders in the Kingsfell. The merchants were carrying a valuable pouch of gems, which the spiders dragged off with one of the bodies.The lost pouch of gems is somewhere in the area called the Snares, south of Esteldín.

Holger Tanner, a merchant who escaped an attack by spiders, has asked you to recover his companions' missing pouch of gems from the spiders' lair.Collect the gem pouchHolger Tanner is at Esteldín.

Holger Tanner, a merchant who escaped an attack by spiders, has asked you to recover his companions' missing pouch of gems.'Oh, stranger, perhaps you will hear my sad story. I was a member of a group of merchants who were crossing the North Downs when we encountered a party of marauding Orcs.

'We fled from them, but did not escape tragedy. We encamped not far south of here, in a place I later learned was called the Snares, and with good reason. As we slept, our camp was raided by spiders! Only I escaped and was rescued by these Rangers.

'One of my companions was bearing a pouch of valuable gems on his person, which we were taking to Othrikar for trade. I do not doubt that it was still on his body when the spiders dragged him off. Could you go to the spider-lair and retrieve it? Without it, I will be destitute. The lair is to the south of here.''I am grateful to these Rangers and all for saving my life, but I need those gems back!''Indeed, these are the gems! Thank you so much for your help. I must give you a small reward for your courage!'Special weapons are being forged in the eastern camps for the Rauta-lehmä by the Hillmen of Angmar, who journey down from the mouth of the Ram Dúath.The Hillmen armourers are encamped south-east of the Ram Dúath.

