You should defeat the Hillmen armourers at their camp, for they pose a great threat to the free peoples of the North Downs.You succeeded in defeating the Hillmen armourers from Angmar who came to strengthen the Rauta-lehmä.Frideric directed you to Cwendreda, located at the ruins of Dol Vaeg. The woman is there watching, tracking, and attempting to stave off the spread of the Dead from within the ruins of Nan Dhelu.Make your way to the ruins of Dol Vaeg and speak with Cwendreda. The ruins are east and north of the Great East Road on a high hill.

Frideric the Elder, in an effort to further garner your help for the Eglain, sent you to Dol Vaeg to assist Cwendreda.Talk to Cwendreda at Dol Vaeg'A moment of your time, ${PLAYER}, but know that the task I will ask of you will take more than moments and set you on a course for true danger.

'Some time back, before the darkness spread from the east and north, we witnessed the arrival of the Dead at Nan Dhelu. We have often stayed afar of that place as something there always set unease upon us. Now, though, the evil emanating spreads fear throughout the people.

'I dispatched one of our strongest kinswomen to watch the ruins... she is there now with her companion who is there at the behest of Stanric. Should you wish to aid us further, make your way to the ruin of Dol Vaeg, east along the road and north to the highest hill, and assist her.''Head east along the road and search for the highest hill in the north. Dol Vaeg is there.''Frideric is a strong leader and wise. I have learned much just by watching the comings and goings within the ruins. I know that there is wealth to be gained from within that place as well.

'If you are here to help, then I will gratefully accept any help you offer.'The Ranger Gondranc sent you to the Earth-kin camp to collect a book of leatherworking lore from Asikko, the Earth-kin's chieftain. However, when you arrived at the Earth-kin camp, Asikko told you the book had been stolen.Asikko's book is hidden somewhere in the camp of the traitorous Rauta-lehmä faction in Nan Amlug, east of the camp of the Suuri-lehmä.

Asikko is hesitant to go himself to retrieve the book of lore from the Rauta-lehmä for fear of provoking war too soon. Instead, he has asked you to retrieve the book for him.Gondranc awaits your return at Esteldín.

You successfully recovered Asikko's book from the camp of the Rauta-lehmä. The Earth-kin chieftain has asked you to deliver it to Gondanc, fulfilling his promise to the Ranger.'My people's pride binds us. I do not wish to raise arms against my brethren, but I have been forced to do so. I will fight them when the time comes, though it does not please me. I am also bound by honour, and that honour must be satisfied, even in the face of the First Hunter's betrayal.

'I know only names, not faces. The name I know is Gondranc, a man who knows well the crafting of leather and tanned hides. I promised to share with him the secrets of our art in return for the letters he once taught me.

'I wrote a book for the man before the betrayal, but it is lost now to the Rauta-lehmä in the east. I dare not go there yet. Will you go to the camp of the traitors and find this book for me?''In a time past, I would ask my brethren for the book, and it would be given freely. Since the arrival of the Men of the North, my brethren have changed. They have forsaken their oaths and follow the Men without thinking of the damage they do to the land. It is sad that the book had to be taken from them with war and death, but honour says it must be so.

'Take this book to little Gondranc and tell him honour is satisfied. May he use its knowledge well.''You have my book, now bring it to my little friend Gondranc!''Ah, my thanks to Asikko for his courtesy and to you for your assistance. With this lore, I will be able to craft the best possible armour I may for the people of Trestlebridge.'Handaron has told you that Halbarad requires the aid of a band of warriors to help bolster the defence of Trestlebridge against an assault by the Orcs.Halbarad is at Esteldín in the North Downs.

Handarod has asked you to speak with Halbarad and lend him your aid in defending Trestlebridge. The townsfolk will not be able to defend against the Orcs alone. Handarod suggested that you take allies with you.Talk to HalbaradNellie Boskins can be found in Trestlebridge.

At Halbarad's side, you helped defend Trestlebridge from the Orcs that sought to destroy it. At the conclusion of the battle, Nellie Boskins asked to speak with you.Talk to Nellie Boskins'I have received urgent messages from Trestlebridge -- it seems that the town has again come under attack by the vicious Ongbúrz Orcs and needs reinforcement swiftly, lest it fall into the hands of the Enemy.

'That town remains the linch-pin of our defence of Bree-land beyond -- should the Orcs break through in great numbers, it will not be in our power to keep them at bay any longer, and matters will become dark indeed.

'So gather your allies quickly and then go to Halbarad, who will organize your place in the defence.''I must apologize to you, for I fear my behaviour towards you was nearly unforgiveable. I see now that the constant Orc-attacks were nothing compared to what Angmar could bring to bear on this small town.

'You and the Ranger Halbarad have risked your lives to save my people. I am in your debt.''Are you prepared for the battle ahead? It will be a difficult one, and we will need all the warriors you can gather.

'Are you ready to leave now?'The ruins of Nan Dhelu have often given the Eglain ill feelings, but the arrival or emergence of the Dead from within the ruins has them even more fearful. A brave warrior, Cwendreda, was sent to watch and learn about the ruins, and her tasks now fall to you as terror begins to grow from within these once great halls.The Master of the Ruins wanders within the ruins of Nan Dhelu, north of Dol Vaeg.

Cwendreda warned you to be cautious while searching Nan Dhelu for the Master of the Ruins and offered you a reward should you defeat the monster.Defeat the Master of the RuinsCwendreda is at Dol Vaeg.

Cwendreda awaits your return and the news that the Master of the Ruins has been defeated.Talk to Cwendreda at Dol Vaeg'Though I bear a great deal of pride, I can admit that I know fear, and no greater fear has come over me as seeing the Master of the Ruins. It roams Nan Dhelu with a skeletal wight at its side at all times and is itself a creature of extreme terror.

'Should you happen upon this creature, I would advise running. If you stay and fight and emerge victorious, tell me and I may offer you a reward.

'The Master of the Ruins wanders throughout the ruins and is never in one place too long.''Just knowing that the creature has been defeated brings a wisp of hope into my heart. You have done much to aid the Eglain this day, ${PLAYER}, and have done much to earn this.

'Thank you for all that you continue to do for my people.''Be careful, ${PLAYER}. The Master of the Ruins is the most fearsome creature I have ever seen. Be wary as you wander through the ruins of Nan Dehlu.'The spiders of the Snares in Kingsfell have covered this little valley in sticky webs, creating a dangerous potential trap for any unlucky enough to stumble into this place. It would be unwise to linger here any longer than necessary.Spiders can be found in the Snares, south of Esteldín in the Kingsfell.

You should defeat spiders as quickly as you can, before the time runs out.Defeat spiders in the Snares before the time runs out (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have swiftly defeated a number of the Kingsfell spiders in the Snares, helping to make the area near Esteldín safer and free of the influence of evil.CompletedThe spiders of the Snares in Kingsfell have covered this little valley in sticky webs, creating a dangerous potential trap for any unlucky enough to stumble into this place. It would be unwise to linger here any longer than necessary.

You should defeat a number of spiders as quickly as you can.You have swiftly defeated a number of the Kingsfell spiders in the Snares, helping to make the area near Esteldín safer and free of the influence of evil.Frideric has sent you to Aric, the Stone-speaker of the Eglain, in Harloeg.Find Aric by travelling south across the Great East Road and beyond Talath Gaun. Venture into Harloeg, as far south into the swamp as you can journey into the ruins there.

Frideric has sent you to speak with Aric, the Stone-speaker.'There is a man you should speak with. He is named Aric, but we also call him the Stone-speaker. He is a wise man of the Eglain. He is currently keeping vigil at a place inhabited by the cursed shades of Men. You may find much to learn from Aric and the dead men of Harloeg.

'Find Aric by travelling south across the Great East Road and beyond Talath Gaun. Venture into Harloeg, as far south into the swamp as you can journey, and you will discover the Stone-speaker in the ancient ruins there.

'The shades there are not like the old wives' tales you might hear of ghosts... they seem to have no ill intent.''You should go speak with Aric in the Harloeg.''If Frideric sends you, then I bid you welcome.

'You will find this a strange place. The shades of the long-suffering dead walk in these ruins, but have no fear... they will do you no harm. Indeed, they may be able to teach you much of this land.'With the discovery of the grimoire, more of Luilloth's final steps have been revealed.Henbran has suggested that you look for a mysterious woman down by the river's edge.

The river's edge is in the Old Forest.Find the mysterious womanGoldberry told you that dust blossoms prefer to grow in near old ruins and elevated parts of the Old Forest.Collect dust blossoms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the dust blossoms to Goldberry.

Goldberry is by the river, in the Old Forest.Bring the blossoms to GoldberryGoldberry has instructed you to place the dust blooms in the water at the river's edge.

The river is in the Old Forest.You should talk to Goldberry.

Goldberry is by the river, in the Old Forest.Talk to GoldberryYou should tell Rhiangar that Henbran's family grimoire and Goldberry traced Luilloth's pursuit of the Grey Fear to Sarch Vorn.

Rhiangar is at the circled caravans, south of Andrath.Return to Rhiangar'It took me a little while to find the passage about Luilloth, but here it is. It says here that the lady came looking for help finding the source of power that was compelling the dead to walk. My ancestor and Luilloth worked out the location for the Grey Fear. Ah yes, I remember tales of this evil being. Let me see...'

She pauses, reading.

'Yes, here it is. My ancestor Darogandes urged Luilloth to gather forces, but Luilloth went on her own to... I cannot quite make it out... but wait, this passage here I do not remember. Darogandes wrote that Luilloth first went to seek council from another. Hmm, I think I know of whom she speaks.

'There is one who walks this forest even more powerful than myself. Her memory is long, and she will know where Luilloth next went. You will find her by the river-side, if you follow the path just right. You shall know her by her shining hair, and, perhaps if you are lucky, by her song on the wind.''${PLAYER}! You return! I was growing worried, you were gone for so long.'

You tell her what you discovered.

'The woman you met sounds fascinating! And Sarch Vorn?! I have heard the name, but have never been. It was a haunted place even before the rest of Cardolan's dead stirred again.''Welcome! You must be a friend to young Henbran to have found me thus. I am Goldberry, and both the shadows in your eyes and the murmur of the river tell me dark tidings have brought you here.'

You explain your search for Luilloth and for a way to put the unquiet dead back to rest.

'Glad I am to hear that you are challenging the Grey Fear! Though my heart knows sorrow once more too, to hear dear Luilloth's name spoken. I spoke with her indeed, long ago and very near this same spot. She came to me for aid as you yourself now do! I gave her what protections I could, and I hold hope that they provided an advantage in her final hours. For, though she vanished, so too did the dead trickle back into their barrows!

'To you I will give the same boon, but you must follow in her footsteps to procure it! Deep in the forest, behind the tangled webs of the deadly weavers, grow dust blossoms, the scent of which bolsters the heart against dread. Bring me five blooms from the ruins at the centre of the forest, that you may to go to battle with your heart girded.''Welcome back! Oh dear, you have some webbing in your hair. You have found the dust blossoms? Wonderful! Now then, place the blooms in the water here - and be sure to stay close by!''Go with cheer and walk more lightly, for day will always follow night. May this small thing help you do great deeds.'Hillmen from Angmar followed the Orc army through Ram Dúath into the North Downs and established an encampment near the head of the pass. These Hillmen serve to keep open the passage from Angmar.The food stores, weapons, and shields can be found in the northern part of the Hillmen's camp, north-east of Esteldín.

You should destroy the food stores, weapons, and shields of the Hillmen, affecting their ability to effectively wage war.Destroy Hillman weapons rack (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Hillman shield rack (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Hillman food crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You found and destroyed the weapons, armour, and food stores of the Hillmen in an effort to slow their progress and ability to field a true army. You have done the Rangers of Esteldín a great service.CompletedThe Rangers of Esteldín are ill-prepared to deal with such a force from Ram Dúath, for the Hillmen are well-armed and outfitted.

You should find and destroy their weapons, shields, and food stores. This may slow the Hillmen advance long enough to prevent them from mounting a sufficent attack.You found and destroyed the weapons, armour, and food stores of the Hillmen in an effort to slow their progress and ability to field a true army. You have done the Rangers of Esteldín a great service.Foul Wargs prowl the North Downs, hunting for those who would oppose their masters. Their presence threatens the security of Esteldín.There are Wargs in the areas west and south of Esteldín.

In order to protect the secrecy of Esteldín, Dagoras has asked you to hunt down and slay as many Wargs as you can.Defeat Wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagoras is at Esteldín.

Dagoras, the Ranger Watch-captain, asked you to hunt the Wargs of the North Downs in order to protect the location of Esteldín. You should return to him with word of your success.'We've had reports that Wargs are moving into the area around Esteldín. While we are not yet prepared to move against the Enemy in the North Downs, we can't have these foul beasts spying on us here.

'We need you to hunt these creatures down and slay them. It should not be difficult to find the Wargs, for they prowl to the west and south, hunting for those of us who dare to oppose Angmar.

'If they learn the whereabouts of Esteldín, the Orcs will be able to sweep down upon us, and our line will be ended. You must hurry before they find us.''Wargs are the forward scouts of the Enemy... if they discover Esteldín, the armies of Angmar will descend upon us, and we will fall.''Well done! If only there were more of us in Esteldín, we Rangers could deal with such creatures ourselves, but all our attention is, by necessity, consumed by the Orc army. Your work is allowing us to gather our forces to deal with the greater threat.'Despite a small supply of arms and armour, Stanric of the Eglain is attempting to organize at least a meagre defence against the wild and dangerous beasts and other enemies which stalk the ruins the Eglain call their homes.Northrim is at the Eglan-encampment at Dol Vaeg overlooking Haragmar and Nan Dhelu.

Stanric sent you to Northrim to complete further tasks necessary to prepare the Eglain for the grim future ahead of them.Talk to Northrim at Dol VaegBoars may be found eastwards along the Great East Road, which lies to the south of Ost Guruth.

Northrim dispatched you to collect boar-haunches and stomachs to help the Eglain fill their winter stores.'We had a pen of boars once, poached now by Orcs and spiders in the west and south. Frideric means to make peace and asks such a meagre price to find that peace. Our stores will not hold long, and we need meat and water soon, or we will face famine.

'In the east, north of the road, you will find Dol Vaeg and a small encampment of our people. Find and speak with Northrim at this camp and assist him with his tasks. We must be well-prepared for this new future.''Stanric is a good man, and his words are true. We must prepare for the dark future ahead. As my companion, Cwendreda, will tell you, the ruins of Nan Dhelu have grown darker than ever we have seen.

'My task is mundane, but necessary. We require water-bladders and food as moving a large number of people from one location to another may take longer than we have to find new sources of fresh water and food.

'To make these bladders and feed our people, we will need a creature untouched by corruption. The boars in these eastern stretches will suffice. There are many boars east along the road but a handful of burrows can be found where the hills rise on the north and south sides of the road.''You will find Northrim and his companion, Cwendreda, at Dol Vaeg, a small, overgrown ruin west of Ost Guruth. They are there watching the ruins of Nan Dhelu and Haragmar. Speak with Northrim and assist him as you can.''The bellies will be cleaned and the meat will be cured and salted. I will be able to fill our water barrels and feed my people.

'You have my thanks, friend.'A burglar hones his skill by thieving items of little worth, but these excursions are mere dalliances when the fate of the Free Peoples is at stake.Palma Brownlock is waiting for you at The Forsaken Inn in the Lone-lands, just off the Great East Road.

