'Slade makes his home at Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands, if you wish to answer his call.''Word of your deeds has travelled far, ${PLAYER}, and you have become much sought-after by those who have need of such a champion! I have heard it said that Slade Ransford, himself a champion of no small skill, wants to meet with you to discuss a mission of some urgency.

'Slade makes his home at Ost Guruth, the Ruin-hold in the Lone-lands, if you wish to answer his call.''Welcome, ${PLAYER}. I heard of your victories in Bree-land and rejoiced in particular that you slew Morley the Fierce. A truer name for him would be "Morley the False!" He had long been a foe of my family, and I am glad that you put an end to his villainy.

'It is with confidence that I then ask for your help, ${PLAYER}, for I know you to be a true champion. A band of Orcs have come to the ruins of Ost Cyrn, not far from here, and I know that together we can drive them out. These lands may be wilderness, but every yard of land we allow the Orcs to take brings them one yard closer to Bree-town, and the lands of good folk!

'The leader of these Orcs has the vile name Mosal-ruk, and he, like others of his kind, will not resist a challenge issued from a true champion. Let us journey together to Ost Cyrn, ${PLAYER}, defeat Mosal-ruk's war-band, and put an end to his designs on the Lone-lands!''Your victories over Morley, Zhurpukh, and Fair Sherman were not accidental, ${PLAYER} -- you are a mighty champion indeed, and you have proved it sevenfold this day! The defeat of Mosal-ruk is already being spoken of by the minstrels I have seen, and that tale is sure to grow in the telling!''Are you ready to depart? I know that we can defeat Mosal-ruk and his war-band, and the minstrels will sing of our valour when we return victorious...probably.

'Are you ready to go?'

