'The pigs didn't get out. They had the chance to, but that would have meant they'd have to stop just lying around. But things have been dry since the storm, and their wallow is more dust and dirt than mud.

'Everyone loves to see a pig roll around in the mud, almost as much as the pigs love to do it. There's a bucket near the pond nearby. Use it and bring a few pailfuls over to the pen to get it nice and wet and muddy.''Just bring the full buckets over to the pig-pen.''I can hear the happy grunting from here!'A mysterious relic appeared outside the Peake's abandoned farmhouse in the North Downs.Ted Farmer is outside the cottage he was dwelling in with his brother Burt, staring at the frightening relic someone placed there as the cottage burned.Talk to Ted FarmerBefore the burned cottage stands an evil-looking relic. Staring at the relic, your blood boils, though you can identify no good reason for it. You shake your head, and the feeling passes.'As if Burt and I have not suffered enough at the hands of the Orcs, now we have to deal with someone setting our home afire? If we had the means, my brother and I would go somewhere, but where else could we go? We were living in this cottage because there is nowhere else to go!'A hobbit penned a message that reached you. In it, the hobbit requested that brave souls make their way to the town of Oatbarton, north of the Brockenborings and bordering Evendim.Oatbarton is north of Brockenborings in the Shire. You will need to follow the path through the Greenfields to reach the town and seek out Hal Gamgee.

