'And this time, I hope you are more sure of your choice. Choosing a pony should not be something done lightly!'Explore the ruins of forts and towers that once guarded the roads, the ancient ruin of Amon Sûl or more commonly known as Weathertop, and the stronghold of corruption and evil that is Garth Agarwen.Explore Garth AgarwenExplore the GrimfensExplore the defences of the Lone-landsExplore WeathertopExplore the lone winding road through the Trollshaws, but be wary as it is not well-guarded from the dangers of the wild.Explore the Road to RivendellExplore the Ruins of the TrollshawsExplore the Wilds of Tâl BruinenThe Huorns of the North Trollshaws have become corrupted by some dark power and have begun working in concert with Wood-trolls and other servants of the Enemy.Huorns can be found in the Gladdalf, in the North Trollshaws.

Thoroniel has asked you and your companions to put down the Huorns of the North Trollshaws.Defeat Huorns in the North Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thoroniel is posted to the south and west of the Gladdalf in the North Trollshaws.

You should return to Thoroniel and let her know that you have done as she has asked.Talk to Thoroniel'There are more threats in the North Trollshaws than just spiders, ${PLAYER}. Far to the north and east of here is a marsh we call the Gladdalf. Here, Wood-trolls have appeared, dangerous servants of the Enemy. As well, creatures known as Huorns dwell here, which legend tells are related to the Onodrim of old.

'Alas, these Huorns, though always somewhat wild, have been corrupted by some dark power, and they have begun to work in concert with the Wood-trolls. I do not believe that there is any hope left for them.

'If you and your companions would journey to the Gladdalf, the poor creatures there should be put to rest. Will you do this?''Thank you, ${PLAYER}...it is tragic that these poor creatures had to be destroyed, but it is sometimes the way of things when shadows grow.'It is strange that cave-claws have swarmed out of their caves into the open sunlight. Perhaps something has stirred them into a feeding frenzy.Cave-claws can be found throughout the South Trollshaws, but especially Ost Dúrgonn, north of the road and Barachen's camp.

You should cull the numbers of the cave-claws in the South Trollshaws, as they present a threat to travel in their current frenzied state.Defeat cave-claws in the South TrollshawsCave-claws can be found throughout the South Trollshaws, but especially Ost Dúrgonn, north of the road and Barachen's camp.

You should cull the numbers of the cave-claws in the South Trollshaws, as they present a threat to travel in their current frenzied state.Defeat cave-claws in the South Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many cave-claws in the south Trollshaws.CompletedCave-claws can be found throughout the South Trollshaws, but especially Ost Dúrgonn, north of the road and Barachen's camp.

You should cull the numbers of the cave-claws in the South Trollshaws, as they present a threat to travel in their current frenzied state.You have slain many cave-claws in the South Trollshaws and once again made the road safe for travellers.Thoroniel has been keeping an eye on the activity of the spiders in the North Trollshaws and has become alarmed at the recent surge in their number.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is intended for a full fellowship.</rgb>Spiders have made their home in the Wovenvales of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp.

Thoroniel has asked you to defeat spiders in the Wovenvales, advising you to bring allies.Defeat spiders in the Wovenvales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thoroniel is in the North Trollshaws, just south of the Wovenvales in the north-west corner.

Thoroniel is waiting to hear that you have defeated the spiders which stalk the Wovenvales.Talk to Thoroniel'You have arrived at just the right moment, ${PLAYER} -- any later and the spiders of the Wovenvales might have spilled forth from their valley and forced me to retreat. Once the creatures escape the valley, there will be little to stand between them and the rest of the Trollshaws. Imladris would become the only beacon in the darkness, though this may already be the case.

'These spiders are a particularly dangerous breed, or I would have already journeyed into the valley to face them myself, but I cannot face them alone. If you would, gather any allies you might have, ${PLAYER}, and cleanse the Wovenvales of this filth.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is intended for a full fellowship.</rgb>'You have done well, ${PLAYER}, but this is only the beginning! Your tale of valour against the spiders of the Wovenvales has encouraged me, but it also contains news that gives me pause. There are more spiders within the Wovenvales than I suspected.

'And yet I believe this may prove a great help to us. If I am correct in my guess, we may be able to turn these great numbers to our advantage. We must find out if this is so, and quickly!'The Rangers of Esteldín are hunting a fugitive by the name of Jabe Grimshaw, who slew one of their comrades during his escape.The Rangers believe Jabe Grimshaw can be found in the ruins of Barad Rath in Evendim, far to the west of Esteldín.

Handarod has asked you to seek out the brigand Jabe Grimshaw and defeat him.Defeat Jabe GrimshawHandarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the east of Evendim.

You should return to Handarod and tell him of Jabe Grimshaw's defeat.Talk to Handarod'Two weeks ago one of our Rangers captured a prominent brigand-leader by the name of Jabe Grimshaw, who we believed might be working in league with agents of Angmar.

'However, before he could be questioned, he escaped, killing his captor in the process, and fled into Evendim.

'If you would hunt down this villain, we would be indebted to you for avenging our fallen comrade. We believe he has taken refuge in the ruins of Barad Rath, far to the west.''So, you have found and defeated Grimshaw? Excellent. The Rangers are too few in number to let the murder of one of our kin pass unavenged.'Éogar, the owner of Hengstacer has asked for your help in delivering a fresh steed to Bree.The stable-master can be found near the West-gate in Bree-town, south of Hengstacer.

Éogar has asked that you ride a fresh steed out to the stable-master in Bree-town.Éogar, son of Hadorgar, is located at Hengstacer, north of Bree.

Return to Éogar and inform him that you delivered the horse to the Bree stable-master.'Who are you and what do you want at Hengstacer, ${CLASS}?  I have no doubt you have used the services of a stable-master...many of the skilled and trustworthy ones use my steeds to carry travellers such as you. The swiftest horses and ponies have all been foaled here in Hengstacer...there are none swifter of hoof west of the Mountains.

'From your raiment I can tell that you are a traveller...I know the hardships of the long roads between here and the Westfold but that is a story for a later time. If you are looking to learn how to ride a steed, I can teach you, but learning the skills is not an easy task. I have to deliver a fresh steed to the stable-master near the West-gate of Bree-town, but my grooms are busy with other tasks. You can start your training by bringing this Blonde Sorrel steed to the stable-master.

'After you deliver her safely, return to me, and we can discuss your training further.'

<rgb=#FFFF00>Right-Clicking on the 'Mount' vitals display gives you the option to dismount your steed but will also cancel the quest.</rgb>'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, there are many more travellers down this way than the Bree-folk are used to. The stable-master there has almost been buried with requests for horses. If you are not too sore from that ride I have another task for you.''You should get that horse to Bree at once...my good name is at stake!''Hurry on back to Hengstacer and thank Éogar for the fresh Steed!'Éogar, the owner of Hengstacer, has asked for your help delivering a fresh steed to Michel Delving.The stable-master can be found in Michel Delving in the Shire, far to the west of Bree.

Éogar has asked that you ride a fresh steed out to the stable-master in Michel Delving.Éogar, son of Hadorgar, is located at Hengstacer, north of Bree, far to the east of the Shire.

You should return to Éogar and inform him that you delivered the horse to the Michel Delving stable-master.'You did a fine job with that steed. It looks like the horse trusted you well enough. You also made it back more quickly than I expected. Men in my country...they would not believe a ${RACE} such as yourself could have done it so quickly!

'Now that you have proven that you can handle a steed I have another task for you...it will teach you endurance and holding your mount to its course. There is a stable-master in the land of the holbytla away to the west -- Michel Delving I believe they call it. The stable-master there is in need of a fresh Chestnut steed as well. Bring him his horse, and you will prove that you can hold to your saddle on a long journey!

'Hurry now! You have a long ride ahead of you.  When you return, we shall see about continuing your training.'

<rgb=#FFFF00>Right-Clicking on the 'Mount' vitals display gives you the option to dismount your steed but will also cancel the quest.</rgb>'You returned! I thought you might have been thrown from the saddle or lost.  Your determination is strong...I have no doubt that you will make a fine rider.''Now that the steed has arrived I can finally sit down for a proper meal.'Éogar, the owner of Hengstacer, has asked for your help delivering a fresh steed to Othrikar.The stable-master is at the dwarf-mines of Othrikar in the North Downs, far to the north and east of Bree-land.

Éogar has asked that you ride a fresh steed out to the stable-master in Othrikar.Éogar, son of Hadorgar, is located at Hengstacer north of Bree.

You should return to Éogar and inform him that you delivered the horse to the Othrikar stable-master.'There is one last task I would have you do before I ask you to prove your true quality.

'The stable-master at the dwarf-mines of Othrikar is an old friend of mine. We met along the road when I left the Riddermark after the king's health failed. I had promised I would send him out a fresh steed as soon as I could find a spare rider. I think you now have skill enough to lead your mount through greater perils than the lands of the holbytla. I am a man of my word and this Bay steed must be sent out at once. Before I can give you your final test, I will need you to travel into the North Downs and deliver it.

'Be careful...the road is long, and there are more dangers than loose stones and roots hidden in the hills of the North Downs.'

<rgb=#FFFF00>Right-Clicking on the 'Mount' vitals display gives you the option to dismount your steed but will also cancel the quest.</rgb>'Well done, ${PLAYER}, that was the last of the horses that I needed to deliver. I hope you did not encounter many difficulties on your journey.''You're a fine rider to make it all this way so quickly, hurry back to Éogar with my thanks.'Garth Agarwen lies in the north-east hills of the Lone-lands. Once a great fortress of the ancient kingdoms, rumours say that it has become a stronghold of corruption and evil.Explore Garth Agarwen.The Circle of Blood is a vile marsh in Haragmar, formed by the corruption overflowing from Agamaur in the north.Nan Dhelu was once a beautiful valley before the corruption of Agamaur flooded the land. Now it is home to vile creatures of Morgoth who live only to breed terror.This gate opens into the courtyard of Garth Agarwen, once a fortress of the evil Rhudaur, now the ruined palace of the Red-maid of Agamaur.This gate leads into the inner sanctuaries of the Red-maid and the vile and corrupted creatures who serve her.This crypt is the resting place and throne of the Gaunt-lord Ivar the Bloodhand, Lord of War, necromancer in service to Angmar.This is the sanctum of the Red-maid of Agamaur, a River-maiden corrupted by the blood spilled in her waters during the wars between Angmar and the North Kingdom.Defeat giants in the Trollshaws.Defeat giants in the TrollshawsPoppy Seaton is distressed by the fact that goblins have taken up residence so near to Ost Forod and wants something done about them.Goblins have made a camp at Tûm Fuin, north of Ost Forod in Tyrn Fornech.

Poppy Seaton has asked you to do something about the goblins that have taken up residence at Tûm Fuin.Defeat goblins at Tûm Fuin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Poppy Seaton is at Ost Forod, the old watch-post in the hills of Tyrn Fornech, south of Tûm Fuin.

You have defeated many goblins and should now return to Poppy with news of your victory.'You might have heard mention of this around town already, but if you haven't: there are goblins at Tûm Fuin, a hollow a short distance north of Ost Forod!

'We have enough problems with the Wargs and tomb-robbers stirring up trouble in Tyrn Fornech; we don't need goblins and boggarts as well!

'I have set aside some coins for any adventurer able enough to do something about the goblins. Are you such an adventurer, ${PLAYER}? If so, you'll have no trouble journeying north to Tûm Fuin and defeating the goblins there!''Tûm Fuin sounds dreadful, ${PLAYER}! I am glad you were able to defeat some of the goblins there, but I don't know if the hollow will ever be the pretty place that once it was. The corruption the goblins have wrought sounds severe.

'Take this reward, ${PLAYER}, and let us both wish for the day that Tûm Fuin will be restored.''The goblins are at Tûm Fuin, ${PLAYER}, a hollow to the north of Ost Forod, among the hills of Tyrn Fornech. It is to the north-east of the Duskencleft, if you have ever been to that pass between the hills.'Bear-hides make for warm winter blankets, keeping the wind from chilling your bones.Nan Orngon is south-east of Ost Forod.

Rowena Parker asked you to venture to Nan Orngon and bring back several bear hides to be turned into blankets.Collect bear-hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ost Forod is west of Nan Orngon.

Rowena Parker will want to begin turning the hides into blankets.'The winter cold will chill you to your core if you are not ready for it. It is especially dangerous at night, when one does not awaken from the bitter cold. Blankets are very important if you wish to wake in the morning.

'We had plenty to go around last year, but it seems the robbers are not just pilfering tombs these days. A store-house was emptied just last week, and we are now short of blankets.

'Bear-hide is the ideal material for making new ones. It is thick and with brushing will be made soft. Plus, there are plenty of bears just south-east of here, at a place we call Nan Orngon.''Fortunately, we have enough time before the winds come for me to make real blankets should you get the hides soon.''These are perfect. Nice and large with only small nicks and tears. I can make enough blankets to keep us all warm for the entire winter with these.'Baldwin Foxtail told you that a honey-roasted chicken is always the centerpiece of the Mathom Society dinner, but the Master Chef has been too busy to prepare one.Baldwin Foxtail is at the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire.

Baldwin Foxtail has asked you to bring him a honey-roasted chicken for the cooks of the Mathom Society.'The centerpiece for every good Mathom Society dinner is a honey-roasted chicken. My mouth is watering just thinking about it!

'Our Master Chef has been tasked with cataloguing all mathoms smaller than a pie tin...a pie tin! I have no idea if he will be able to finish cooking the chicken for our next dinner in time.

'Without a honey roasted-chicken, we simply cannot hold our meeting. Please, ${PLAYER}, help us find a honey-roasted chicken in time for our meeting.''Is that...? It is! A honey-roasted chicken! You have saved the Mathom Society dinner, ${PLAYER}. You have my most sincere thanks.'There are many threats to the north Ost Forod agreed to deal with in the pact with the Rangers of Tinnudir. It is time they be dealt with.There are several threats that must be addressed for Ost Forod to uphold its end of the pact.Assist Clark Standish againAssist Ballard Wilmer againAssist Rowena Parker againAssist Poppy Seaton againBasil Gummidge is at Ost Forod.

Basil will be pleased to hear Ost Forod has upheld its end of the pact with Tinnudir.Talk to Basil Gummidge at Ost Forod'You have shown the Rangers are serious in restoring the pact between us. It is now time that we step up here and honour our end of the agreement.

'We said we would watch over Evendim from the north, guard the trade routes with Forochel, and ensure the enemies of the Rangers did not enter from those lands. They have entered and are already here, that much we cannot change, but we can drive them back out.

'Speak with my associates around town, the same who you helped prepare for the winter. They have each been tasked with scouting a threat. They will know more about what to do next.''The north is secured, and we can honestly say we have now done our part. We are not yet done, though. The years of hardship created another problem, which it is time to finally address.''It is high time we started working with the Rangers instead of against them.'Let the calls of battle echo from the hills and mountains in a great clamour.Use Melody of Battle, Echoes of Battle or Timeless Echoes of BattleLet the calls of battle echo from the hills and mountains in a great clamour.Use Melody of Battle, Echoes of Battle or Timeless Echoes of BattleCuthbert Sprunt has placed a bounty on your head, and you have decided to challenge him to single combat to have it removed.Basil Gummidge has travelled with you to the Sparring Circle of Ost Forod.

Basil Gummidge is waiting to speak with you inside the Sparring Circle.Talk to Basil GummidgeYou are engaged in single combat with Cuthbert Sprunt in the Sparring Circle.

Basil Gummidge is overseeing the combat to ensure that Cuthbert does not cheat.Defeat Cuthbert SpruntCuthbert Sprunt has revealed his true colours and has called upon his cronies for aid.

Basil Gummidge has leapt to your defence, and with his aid, you must defeat the enemy.Defeat Cuthbert SpruntBasil Gummidge is in the Sparring Circle of Ost Forod.

You and Basil Gummidge have successfully overcome Cuthbert Sprunt's treachery. You should speak with Basil at once.Talk to Basil Gummidge'Ready to go? I certainly am. This was some good exercise, though, and I'm glad we've both come through it all right!''Cuthbert Sprunt isn't here yet, ${PLAYER}, so there's still time to change your mind. Sprunt is a dangerous foe, but you shouldn't have any trouble...assuming he plays fair.''Good luck, ${PLAYER}! I'm cheering for you!''Fight on, ${PLAYER}! Do not give up, for I stand with you!''Yeah, yeah, you're tough, all right. Would want you for my band if you weren't such a stickler for "proper!"''I'll shape up from now on! My villainous ways are behind me!''I'm through with villainy! You won't be seeing me again, I assure you!''I'm done with this band, you'll see! I'm leaving my villainy behind me!''I knew that Sprunt planned on cheating, I just knew it! It's a good thing I was here, ${PLAYER}, but all's well that ends well, I always say. Or at least, I'm saying it now!

'Let me know when you're ready to return. We taught this villain a lesson, that much is certain, and I daresay his cronies won't be causing you any more trouble.'Dry logs can be found around Nan Orngon. The bears root them up when they dig for grubs.Nan Orngon is east of Ost Forod.

Poppy Seaton has asked you to venture to Nan Orngon and collect dried logs.Collect dry logs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Poppy Seaton is at Ost Forod, west of Nan Orngon.

Poppy Seaton will be pleased to see all of the wood you collected.'Blankets are not the only things that keep you warm in the winter. A good, roaring fire is just as important to have. To keep it going, you need wood, though... lots of it and plenty dry.

'Our stores are low this winter. With folks leaving to join the tomb-robbers, we have fewer honest people left to do the work necessary to get ready for the winter. We have had to focus everyone on food. The fire-wood pile has stayed very short.

'The best wood is out near Nan Orngon. The bears root it up while they are digging for grubs. It is dry, but burns for a long time. If you could gather up a bunch of branches, it would be very helpful.''If we do not have wood for the fires, the winter will end up being very short for most of us.''We will still need to gather more wood in order to make it through the winter, but it is nice to see the wood-pile grow for the first time in a long time.'Calenglad has asked you to help his fellow Rangers at Tinnudir. Once they are satisfied with the assistance you provide, he will consider your proposal again.The Rangers Astiul, Forchon, and Naethmunn are at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim.

Calenglad has asked you to render your aid to three of his brethren. When they are satisfied that you are true of heart and do not harbour plans to plunder the tombs of the Dúnedain, he will consider your errand again.Earn Astiul's trustEarn Forchon's trustEarn Naethmunn's trustCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim.

You have satisfied his brethren of your true heart and should now return to Calenglad to ask him again for aid in acquiring the Silithar for Aragorn.'You put me in a difficult situation, ${PLAYER}. I cannot in good conscience help you without first administering a test of your character, but if you are indeed sent by Aragorn, any delay is an affront to my lord.

'I will not make this decision alone. Render your aid to the rest of my brethren, to Astiul, Forchon, and Naethmunn. Once they are satisfied that you are indeed of good character and do not have villainous motives, I will consider your petition once more.

'You will find my fellow Rangers here at Tinnudir. If, however, you prove false, I will have you cast into the lake with any of your robber-friends that I catch!''I have heard from my brethren, ${PLAYER}, and they are satisfied that you are who you say you are. I apologize for my mistrust, but you cannot be too careful of strangers in these dark days, no matter whose letters they claim to carry.

'I will help you acquire the Silithar for my lord Aragorn, but the power to do so does not lie with me. I must journey to speak with Gwindeth, and I think it best that I alone make that journey.''You will find Astiul, Forchon, and Naethmunn here on Tinnudir. Give them your aid, and once they are all satisfied with your actions, I will reconsider your petition.'Greylond Bottomley told you a little of the Mathom Society and its efforts to build the Mathom House's collection.Greylond Bottomley is at the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire.

Greylond Bottomley has asked you to bring him any mathoms that you gather during your travels.

<rgb=#FF0000> Mathoms drop off of Men, Dwarves, Orc-kind, Troll-kind, and the Dead of level 35 - 45 throughout the world.</rgb>'Hullo there, my young ${RACE}. Have you come to learn about the Mathom Society? I know quite a bit, as I have been a member for over four years now! Come closer...my eyesight is not as good as it once was; I turn one hundred this year, you know.

'Five years ago, a group of hobbits began to take a close interest in the Mathom House and the recovery of mathoms across the Shire. We have the most splendid meetings and discuss all sorts of things: where we would be likely to find mathoms, who holds private collections of mathoms from which we could borrow, or even what differentiates a mathom from a non-mathom! Most of the meetings occur over dinner, and we have begun to get quite a turnout. Why, just last week Baldwin Foxtail proposed to add to the main floor to increase the number we could fit at the table. Who would have thought so many hobbits were interested in history?

'Though we have some wonderful plans, we have not actually begun the process of going out and collecting the mathoms. That is where youngsters such as yourself come in! If you happen across any mathoms in your travels be sure to bring them back here so they can be organized and catalogued. It would be a pity to lose any more mathoms. A good deal of our collection has been diminished ever since old Bilbo took some of our most interesting pieces with him when he went and got himself killed, or lost -- you know, I don't rightly remember what happened to the old fool now that I think about it....''You have returned with some mathoms? Oh, Brombard will be overjoyed! I will put these down into storage right away. If they ever get put on display, I will make sure your name is added to the plaque that accompanies them.'In order to dry and cure before the winter cold hits, elk-meat must be gathered now.Elk can be found wandering the hills north and east of Ost Forod.

Ballard Wilmer asked you to gather elk-meat so he can dry and cure it for the winter.Collect elk-haunches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ballard Wilmer is at Ost Forod.

Ballard Wilmer will be eager to begin drying and curing the elk-meat.'It is time to build up our foodstuffs and prepare for the coming cold. Elk-meat takes time to dry and cure... it is not done overnight, and it must be done before the cold-snap hits. It cannot cure if it is frozen.

'That means it must be gathered now so it has enough time that we will be able to enjoy it later. There are few things that warm a belly more than a spiced, dried piece of elk-meat on a frozen winter night.

'Head into the hills... you will find the elk roaming about them. Bring back enough haunches that we will be able to get a few weeks of meals from them.''I would ask you to get bear-meat, but the bear-meat is better fresh. At this point, it is too fatty to dry well.''These are very nice haunches. Looks like the elk had plenty of plants to feed upon this fall.'Hithlim has asked that you speak with Greylond Bottomley outside the Mathom House in Michel Delving.Greylond Bottomley can be found outside the Mathom House in Michel Delving.

Hithlim has asked that you speak with Greylond Bottomley to find out what the Mathom Society is up to.Talk to Greylond Bottomley at the Mathom House'One of the many duties of the Rangers of Esteldín is to watch over a place known as the Shire. I recently received word that the Hobbits of Michel Delving, calling themselves the Mathom Society, have begun asking traders and merchants for a variety of...interesting items.

'If you would, travel to the Shire and find out exactly what this Mathom Society is up to. I have heard that a hobbit named Greylond Bottomley has been taking the orders. You should seek him out.''You were sent to help us locate mathoms? How wonderful, I am sure we can put you to work right away.''You should journey to the Shire and speak with Greylond Bottomley at the Mathom House.'Rowena Parker is concerned at the increasing boldness of the tomb-robbers that creep among the hills of Tyrn Fornech.Tomb-robbers can be found among the hills north and west of Ost Forod, in Tyrn Fornech.

Rowena Parker has asked you to defeat the experienced tomb-robbers that prowl the hills of Tyrn Fornech.Rowena Parker is at Ost Forod, the old watch-post in Tyrn Fornech.

You have defeated many experienced tomb-robbers in Tyrn Fornech and should return to Rowena with the tale of your success.Talk to Rowena Parker in Ost Forod'The hills of Tyrn Fornech are the refuge of several different tomb-robber bands, ${PLAYER}, and each of them is becoming increasingly bold.

'If you are sure enough in your abilities, perhaps you could venture north and west of Ost Forod into the hills to confront some of these outlaws? The tomb-robbers that prowl throughout Tyrn Fornech are tougher than those who inhabit Parth Aduial; these are veteran robbers and scouts who have adapted to a harsher life in the hills.

'You'll find veterans and scouts throughout Tyrn Fornech, ${PLAYER}, and if you don't... they'll find you.''You'll find the tomb-robbers throughout Tyrn Fornech, ${PLAYER}. Defeat these villains, and these lands will be made safer.''Thank you for this news, ${PLAYER}. There will always be tomb-robbers in these lands, but perhaps you have helped lessen their numbers or influence somewhat. Take this reward with my thanks.'There are many varieties of elk which dwell in the Trollshaws, which would provide sufficient provender for the Elves who patrol the Southern Trollshaws.There are elk dwelling in the Southern Trollshaws.

While you are here, you should collect venison for Barachen and the Elves who patrol the Southern Trollshaws.Collect venison from the elk of the Southern TrollshawsThere are elk dwelling in the Southern Trollshaws.

While you are here, you should collect venison for Barachen and the Elves who patrol the Southern Trollshaws.Collect venison from the elk of the Southern Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Barachen is encamped in the Southern Trollshaws.

You should bring the venison you collected to Barachen in the Southern Trollshaws.There are elk dwelling in the Southern Trollshaws.

While you are here, you should collect venison for Barachen and the Elves who patrol the Southern Trollshaws.'It was good of you to bring this venison to us. We have had little time for hunting.'Handarod is concerned with the bands of tomb-robbers who creep throughout the Fields of Evendim and the eastern region of the Twilight Hills in Evendim.Tomb-robbers can be found throughout the eastern and north-easten regions of Evendim, far to the west of Esteldín.

Handarod has asked you to defeat tomb-robbers in Evendim.Defeat tomb-robbers in the Fields of Evendim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Handarod is at Esteldín, far to the east of Evendim.

You should return to Handarod and tell him of your battles with the tomb-robbers.Talk to Handarod'Our brothers in Evendim are planning some kind of offensive to re-take the city of Annúminas, but they know that this will leave them too short-handed to deal with the near-constant raids by the bands of tomb-robbers who wander the Fields of Evendim and the eastern Twilight Hills.

'They have asked me to send what warriors I can spare to help hunt down these bands of brigands and make sure that they cannot interfere with the efforts of the Wardens over the next month or so.''The Wardens of Annúminas have asked me to thank you for your efforts in fighting off the tomb-robbers in Evendim, and so I do, ${PLAYER}. May your blade continue to shine brightly in the face of darkness.'You have slain many spiders and poisoned many of their egg-sacs, but that will not be enough to defeat the spiders of the Wovenvales.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest is intended for a full fellowship.</rgb>The queen of the Trapdoor brood can be found somewhere deep within the Wovenvales, in the north-west of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp.

To put an end to the spider-threat, you should defeat the queen of the Trapdoor-brood, which has brought the two broods together.Defeat the Trapdoor queenThe queen of the Trapdoor brood can be found somewhere deep within the Wovenvales, in the north-west of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp.

To put an end to the spider-threat, you should defeat the queen of the Trapdoor-brood, which has brought the two broods together.Defeat the Trapdoor queenThoroniel is encamped south of the Wovenvales.

Thoroniel will be pleased to hear that you have defeated the Trapdoor queen.Talk to ThoronielThe queen of the Trapdoor brood can be found somewhere deep within the Wovenvales, in the north-west of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp.

To put an end to the spider-threat, you should defeat the queen of the Trapdoor-brood, which has brought the two broods together.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest is intended for a full fellowship.</rgb>'You have had better fortune than I, ${PLAYER}, for I was unable to find the queen of the Flesh-gnawer brood. I believe there was a struggle between the two broods -- for what reason I do not know -- and the queen of the Flesh-gnawer spiders was cast out, or perhaps she was the victor, and the Trapdoor queen was left behind to face you in defeat. I do not know. It is a mystery, and one that I cannot resolve to my satisfaction.

'Our task here is half-completed, but we must be satisfied with this small victory for the time being. We have halted the threat, and that must be enough.'Radagast instructed you to pour the pure water into the sanctum of the Red-maid's fortress, Garth Agarwen.The Red-maid is in her sanctum within her fortress of Garth Agarwen.

Dannasen instructed you to obey Radagast and take the pure water to the Red-maid's sanctum. Once there, he told you that you would have to defeat the Red-maid, and when the waters of her pool go still, to pour the water in.Dannasen is at the Eglan-camp in Agamaur.

You should return to Dannasen and tell him that you poured the pure water into the Red-maid's Sanctum.'Thou must now enter the stronghold of the Red-maid at Garth Agarwen, as the Wizard instructed thee. Her sanctum is guarded beyond the walls of the mighty fortress. Men of Rhudaur still walk through the remains of their ancient home in service to the Red-maid and the Gaunt-lord Ivar.

'Thou must find thy way into her sanctum, call her by some means, and then defeat her. She will fall into the water, and the water will become still.

'When this happens add the pure water graced by a River-daughter's love to the pool. There are centuries of corruption and hatred layered upon the Red-maid, but we must begin somewhere. May the Valar go with thee, ${PLAYER}, for they have abandoned us.''The task before thee is daunting, but it must be done to stem the tide of the Red-maid's corruption. Thou must go and confront the Red-maid, driving her back beneath her waters. Once thou hast done so, use the waters of the phial given to thee by Radagast and help restore the purity of the waters, if but for a little while.''Our work has only begun... our oath shall hold until the Red-maid is reclaimed. Thou hast started us along the path to her redemption, and one day, we shall undo Angmar's evil. Thou hast given great hope to those who art hopeless.

'Evil draws its hand tightly over the land, and not only here in the swamp where it has plied its machinations through centuries. Beware of where thou travel... thy light shines strong and evil will strive to snuff it out.

'Thank thee, friend ${PLAYER}. Thank thee for all that thou hast done.'Radagast the Brown was reminded of a legend about rings that were given to the leaders of the Hill-men to signify their service to Angmar. These rings gave them power over their lessers, but exacted their very lives from them, making their bodies vessels for wight-spirits.Wights can be found in Garth Agarwen in the north of Agamaur. Radagast can be found at Barad Dhorn in the Eglan-camp.

Radagast the Brown has asked you to enter Garth Agarwen and discover if the legendary rings exist. If they do, he wishes them brought to him so that they may be destroyed.'${PLAYER}, I have a tale to share with you. It is of warriors who served Rhudaur at this very place, and the fate they shared. It is a story, nothing more, but one that may have merit.

'When Rhudaur pledged to serve Angmar it is said that some were gifted rings that gave them command over their lessers. These rings, borne by the most powerful leaders signified their stations, but came with a terrible price. Each of them perished and were replaced by wight-spirits.

'Likely, it is naught more than a nursery tale, but if it is not, then the power of those rings must be removed. Seek out these rings, if they exist, and bring them to me so that they may be destroyed. The wight-leaders will bear them.''I can only assume that the tales are true. You have done a great service this day, ${PLAYER}. I will see that these are destroyed, before more harm can come of them.'The tomb-robbers are killing elk and bear for food, cutting into the supply Ost Forod will need to survive the coming winter.Tomb-robbers can be found in the hills north and east of Ost Forod.

Clark Standish asked you to venture into the hills around Ost Forod and defeat several tomb-robbers to protect the town's winter food-supply.Defeat tomb-robbers around Ost Forod (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Clark Standish is at Ost Forod.

Clark Standish will be pleased to know that the tomb-robbers have several fewer mouths to feed.Talk to Clark Standish at Ost Forod'The winters here are colder and harsher than the rest of Evendim. We do not have the lake to warm us, and the winds blow straight through the mountain passes from Forochel. It is difficult to prepare for everything we need.

'Often during the winter, we run hunting parties out to find whatever elk or bear are still foraging about. I worry that this year we will not find any. There are more tomb-robbers camped in the hills than I remember from any year before, and they will all want to eat.

'Head out into the hills west of here and encourage some of these tomb-robbers to move on. They will be bad for this winter, and we simply cannot afford them taking the food sources we will desperately need.''They chose the path they wanted to walk, each and every one of them. They took greed and fortune over an honest living. Those of us who remain here, who have suffered but remained just, will now have the food we need.''Denying the tomb-robbers the source of their provisions seems a heartless thing to do, but they have chosen their path.'These lands once were the eastern extent of the old kingdom of Rhudaur. They have lain in ruins for many long years now and most are inhabited only by wild beasts -- or horrid creatures that have crawled more recently out of the depths of Angmar.Explore the ancient ruins of the Trollshaws.Of the larger spiders in Middle-earth, it seems that some have descended from a particularly dark and evil brood. Among these creatures, it is not unheard of for them to possess a cunning intelligence and even the power to speak in the languages of Men. It is rumoured that one such creature has made this ancient ruin its lair.Built as an outlaying watch-tower of Nan Tornaeth to the north, Ost Thondol once stood watch over the approaches to the Ford of Bruinen.A fortress was constructed in Nan Tornaeth long ago. It was built as a series of strong watchtowers in these high hills, connected by elegant spans.

Minas Ciliant was the north-western corner of these towers.Ost Chall was once the main keep of the tower fortress built into the hills of Nan Tornaeth. Now it lies in ruins like all the other remnants of the old kingdom here in the Trollshaws.The tower of Amon Varadh was named after the high hill upon which it was constructed, providing a commanding view of the surrounding valleys.This is another of the towers built upon the hills of Nan Tornaeth and combined into a fortress that once provided a commanding presence for the old kingdom here in the Trollshaws.

All of this has lain in ruin for as long as any Man can remember, and only the Elves can speak of its ancient glory.Barad Glamgil overlooks the southern approach into Nan Tornaeth, as well as a dramatic waterfall which cascades into deep pools at the base of the hills below the tower.Ost Dúrgonn was constructed by the ancient Kingdom of Arnor to stand guard over the main crossing into the Trollshaws and thus deny it to invaders from the East -- however, the greater threat proved to be from the North, and this fortress fell into misuse and eventual ruin as wars raged elsewhere.Alphlanc is watching the road as it runs over the Last Bridge for any sign that servants of the Enemy might slip into -- or out of -- the Trollshaws.The Elves placed a white marker stone along the road to guide friends towards Barachen's camp.

Alphlanc told you to seek a white marker stone eastward along the road.Find the Elves' markerBarachen is at his camp east of the Last Bridge, on a hill south of the road.

Alphlanc asked you to bring word to Barachen that no evil has entered the Trollshaws while she has been watching the Last Bridge, though neither has any left.Talk to Barachen'I bid you welcome, friend, but must give you a word of caution: servants of the Enemy passed across the Last Bridge and swept into the Trollshaws no less than two months ago, pursuing a small company. They were hindered at the Ford of Bruinen, and the good people were brought to safety, but... not all of the evil ones were accounted for.

'Barachen maintains a camp to the east, on a hill south of the road. Bring him this message from me, if you are going that way: "No agents of evil have entered the Trollshaws by the Last Bridge, but so too have none left it. Whatever evil lurks among the ruins of old Rhudaur... remains there.

'I thank you for this, friend. Tread with care and follow the road east until you find the marker we placed to guide friends to Barachen's camp. It is difficult to miss, for it is white, unlike the stone of these hills.''This Elf, Barachen, has agreed to help me with the troubles I have encountered here in the Trollshaws. If you are of a mind to, you could lend him a hand.''If you are looking for Barachen's camp, you will find it to the south. Leave the road and follow the slope to the right as it winds up the side of those cliffs.''Barachen has a camp not far to the east, on a hill south of the road. Follow the road until you see the marker we placed to guide friends to Barachen's camp.

'Bring him word that the road over the Last Bridge remains clear, though the evil that crept into the Trollshaws seems to remain here.''You bring word from Alphlanc? I am gladdened that she has not encountered any evil creatures, but it is clear to the Wise that an unseen evil is often the worst.

'Still, I am glad of your tidings. If you are willing to help us watch the wilderness for signs of evil, you would be doing us a great service.'Many scouts were dispatched across the Trollshaws to keep watch for signs of evil at the behest of Elladan and Elrohir, the sons of Elrond.Narlinn and Fimgris are encamped along the road, east of Barachen's camp.

Barachen is impressed by your skill and determination and has asked you to lend your aid to the sons of Elrond, who keep watch over the Trollshaws from their camp near the Bruinen Gorges. He told you that Narlinn and Fimgris would be able to direct you to Thorenhad, where the sons of Elrond reside.Talk to Narlinn'You have been a boon to those of us assigned to watch the Trollshaws, ${PLAYER}. Recovering the stones stolen from Heithur's couriers was no small task, but you did so without complaint. I know that Heithur is pleased with your service, and I add my voice to his. You have our thanks.

'If you are of a mind to continue lending your aid, I would have you introduce yourself to Elladan and Elrohir, the sons of Elrond. They have established a camp in the ruins of Thorenhad, east of here and to the north in the Bruinen Gorges, and I know your services would be appreciated. Thorenhad is set atop a hill north of the bear-dens of the Bruinen Gorges.

'If you follow the road eastward, you will find the encampment of Narlinn and Fimgris. They will be able to direct you to Thorenhad.''You come from Barachen, seeking to help Elladan and Elrohir? I am glad of it, but I would ask you to help me first, if you have a moment....'There exists a pact between the Suuri-lehmä and the Dwarves of Othrikar, that each would provide aid to the other.Quartermaster Orgrin is at Othrikar, north-west of Rusfold.

Iivari has asked you to perform one final task for him: he wishes you to deliver a satchel of herbs to Orgrin, the provisioner at Othrikar, as fulfillment of a pact between Earth-kin and dwarves.'You have aided us well ${PLAYER}. The time for battle is very near now.

'One last thing I ask -- take this to Othrikar, the dwarf-mines north-west of here, and give it to Quartermaster Orgrin. This satchel contains many healing herbs we collected as part of our pact with the dwarves there, who will also aid us.

'Be well. We may not meet again.''Take the herbs to Othrikar. The dwarves will have need of them.''Eh, what is this? Ah, the herbs promised by the Jorthkyn. Thank you for bringing them!

'They are strange allies, are they not? But these times are dangerous, and any force we can raise to halt the advance of Angmar is welcome.

'The Jorthkyn seem to have an odd affinity for plants, though they do not raise crops... I am not sure where they learned such lore but it is of great value to us now. Many of us shall doubtless be wounded in the battles to come, and the poultices that can be made from these herbs are potent for healing.'The Master Chef is also the Mathom Society's clerk. He has been so busy that he will be unable to prepare the Society's next dinner.Baldwin Foxtail is at the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire.

Baldwin Foxtail has asked you to bring him some seasoned beef with cauliflower for the cooks of the Mathom Society.'Hullo there, my name is Baldwin Foxtail son of Brombard Foxtail...he's the keeper of the Mathom House, you know. I am one of the more important members of the Mathom Society; I am in charge of overseeing the collection of the delectable menu items for our extravagant Mathom Society dinners, as well as the labeling and cleaning of several of the more significant sections of the Mathom House storage collection.

'We have run into a bit of trouble, what with all the adventurers coming in with new mathoms, I have never seen so many in all my life! Old Greylond seems to fix all of us to get the mathoms sorted and organized before he thinks about the dinner menu, quite silly if you ask me. 

'Our Master Chef has been locked up in the cellar of the Mathom House for so long now that I am worried he may have forgotten how to cook! I am worried even more that he will not have time to cook up his specialty, seasoned beef with cauliflower, in time for our next Mathom Society dinner.

'We can't hold the dinner without something to serve! Do you think you would be able to find us some seasoned beef with cauliflower? You would be doing the Mathom Society quite a service.''You found us some seasoned beef with cauliflower? You have saved me! I can not thank you enough, ${PLAYER}.'There are many villainous monsters roaming the Misty Mountains, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many bears in the Misty MountainsSlay many snow-beasts in the Misty MountainsSlay many Wargs in the Misty MountainsSlay many worms in the Misty MountainsThe winter in Ost Forod is long and dangerous. Winter winds blow strong from Forochel to the north.Several townsfolk around Ost Forod have work that needs to be done before the winter arrives.

Basil Gummidge told you that before they do what the Rangers want, several of the town's needs must be addressed first.Assist Clark StandishAssist Ballard WilmerAssist Rowena ParkerAssist Poppy SeatonBasil Gummidge is at Ost Forod.

Basil Gummidge will be pleased to hear Ost Forod is stocked and prepared for a long winter.Talk to Basil Gummidge at Ost Forod'So, the Rangers suddenly want to honour their end of our old arrangement? Funny how as soon as things start to go bad for them, they seek out help, yet deny it to others who have needed it for so long. Still, the fact that you are here shows a small step has been taken. Let us see how serious they really are.

'Before we get to anything dealing with what they want, we have to make sure we are well-prepared for the winter. The storms will be coming soon, and our supplies of nearly everything have gotten very low.

'If you are serious about restoring this pact, we start with our needs. Go see several of the townsfolk, and they will direct you to what those are.''The townsfolk have spoken well of you. I believe I may have been too harsh before...your intentions seem genuine enough. Perhaps it is our time to step up now.''If I hear back good things about your work, maybe we will talk about what we can do for the Rangers.'The Mathom Society is short on their store of strawberry dessert-wine and have not had time to make more.Baldwin Foxtail is at the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire.

Baldwin Foxtail has asked you to bring him five bottles of strawberry dessert-wine for the cooks of the Mathom Society.'The members of the Mathom Society do their best thinking when they have a full stomach. Most of our ideas do not come to us until after we have finished with the Mathom Society dinners that accompany every Mathom Society meeting.

'We have had a problem finding enough strawberries for our strawberry dessert-wine. One of the main tasks of the Mathom Society members was to go on a weekly strawberry-picking in order to make enough strawberry dessert-wine, but with all of the work we have been tasked with, I doubt we will be able to find enough in time for our next meeting.

'If you are looking for a task, bring us five bottles of strawberry dessert-wine. It would be awful if we did not have something to sip after dinner. Why, I doubt any planning would get done at all without it!''Those look like fine bottles. I will make sure to sample these bottles personally to ensure that they meet the strict Mathom Society standards.'The Ranger Culang has learned of a great treasure buried long ago by a Dúnadan-landholder and wants it recovered before it is found by tomb-robbers.The treasure may lie beneath another stone marker, somewhere in Evendim, if this riddle is to be believed:

  "From this beach, you can see Rantost,
   A short swim across the water."

You should examine the marker when you find it for some clue to the location of the treasure.Find the solution to the riddleThe inscription on this stone marker is barely legible, but these words can just be made out:

  "From this beach, you can see Rantost,
   A short swim across the water."

This new riddle may reveal the true location of the treasure.The inscription on this stone marker is barely legible, but these words can just be made out:

  "From this beach, you can see Rantost,
   A short swim across the water."

This new riddle may reveal the true location of the treasure.'Another riddle? You are jesting! How does this one go?

  "From this beach, you can see Rantost,
   A short swim across the water."

'Rantost is an island to the north of Tinnudir, claimed now by tomb-robbers. Look for a beach on the mainland from which you can see Rantost, and I would wager you might find the treasure!'The stone marker is surrounded by signs of digging; if it once marked the location of the treasure, it has surely been found.

The marker bears an inscription, all but worn away by the passage of time.Torogethir wishes to show the robbers at Ost Heryn mercy and perhaps show them the error of their ways by relieving them of the shade-captain Miluidir.Miluidir is at Ost Heryn, south-west along the road from Torogethir's camp.

Torogethir has asked you to drive forth the shade of Miluidir at the ruins of Ost Heryn.Defeat Miluidir before dawnTorogethir is at his camp, north-east of Ost Heryn.

You should return to Torogethir with news of your success.'Do you hear those terrible cries rising from Ost Heryn? It is this way every evening, for the robbers who have made those ruins their home are plagued by the shade of one of the Oathbreakers, one who was once a captain of Men, Miluidir.

'While some would say the robbers have earned what they deserve for their greed, I cannot help but feel that something should be done. Perhaps those robbers can someday be redeemed.

'Would you travel to those ruins and find Miluidir and defeat him? It would be but a brief reprieve, for none but a higher Power can banish him from this world. Be warned though, Miluidir must be defeated before dawn, or he will hide once more and plague the robbers again upon the morrow.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps by seeing your noble efforts on their behalf, some of the robbers will see the error of their ways. At least hope still remains for them.'Basil Gummidge is worried that you may have done too good a job at claiming the bounties posted in Ost Forod, and that you have made a number of enemies.There is a poster on the wall by the stairs near Basil Gummidge in Ost Forod.

Basil Gummidge has directed your attention to a poster on the wall near him, asking you to read it, then bring it to him.Read the poster near Basil GummidgeBasil Gummidge is in Ost Forod.

You have found a wanted poster placing a bounty on your head at the behest of one Cuthbert Sprunt.Basil Gummidge is in Ost Forod.

Basil Gummidge, the arbiter of Ost Forod, has agreed to ensure that Cuthbert Sprunt does not cheat when you challenge him to single combat. Basil is waiting to speak with you so you can travel together to the Sparring Circle.Talk to Basil Gummidge and travel to the Sparring CircleBasil Gummidge is in Ost Forod.

You have defeated Cuthbert Sprunt, despite his underhanded attempts to cheat at the competition, and should now speak with Basil Gummidge about the victory.'There's been a troubling development, ${PLAYER}, and it's best that you hear it from me before seeing it for yourself. You've done a lot of good for this town by claiming the bounties on some of the villains hereabouts, and it wouldn't be right for me to let you walk into trouble without warning.

'Someone's been putting up posters. I've been taking them down wherever I come across them, but I kept one up on the wall over there so you could have a look. Go read it and take it down, and then we can have a talk about what can be done.

'The poster is just over there on the wall, by the stairs.'The poster is written in a messy scrawl, but the words leap off the parchment at you:

'For the death of ${PLAYER}, ${CLASS} of no account, Cuthbert Sprunt offers two gold pieces. This ${RACE} has come to Evendim and caused nothing but trouble. Just ask Mrs. Idden where her boy Andy is, or the widow Tripper why her son Will is missing a brother!'

Beneath a brief but unflattering description of you, an angry hand has scrawled something else:

'If you think you've been wronged in this, ${PLAYER}, "bounty-hunter," then you come talk to Mr. Sprunt at the Sparring Circle. We'll sort it out, fair-like.''Well-fought, ${PLAYER}, well-fought indeed! Sprunt will not dare face you again, and his band is well-warned now of your skill!

'They know now what I have known for some time: ${PLAYER} is a bounty-hunter, not the bounty!''The poster is right over there on the wall by the stairs, ${PLAYER}. Go bring it back here, and we can decide what to do about it.''Are you ready to travel to the Sparring Circle and confront Cuthbert Sprunt? He won't dare cheat while I'm there, and I'm confident you can defeat him and make him take down these ridiculous posters!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'You see why I'm concerned, ${PLAYER}? I know this Cuthbert Sprunt, a villain of the lowest measure, and the sum he's offering for your head is enough to have even the good folk of Ost Forod thinking twice, and there are plenty here who need only think on it once! You're a marked ${RACE} now, my friend -- the bounty-hunter becomes the bounty!

'You want to fight this, don't you? You want to best Sprunt in single combat? If you can show that you're tougher than he is, I expect there will be few willing to claim the bounty. I'll stand by you, ${PLAYER}.

'Talk to me when you're ready, and we can see what he has in store at the Sparring Circle. He won't turn down a challenge, I expect, but I'll watch him closely to ensure that he doesn't cheat.'Thoroniel believes that the Wovenvales are infested with two different broods of spider, and she has formed a plan to deal with both of them.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is intended for a full fellowship.</rgb>Two broods of spider make their home in the Wovenvales of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp.

Thoroniel has asked you to collect fangs from the two different spider-broods in the North Trollshaws.Collect trapdoor spider-fangs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect flesh-gnawer spider-fangs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'It appears that we are dealing not with one brood of spiders, ${PLAYER}, but with two! I do not know for what purpose these two broods have formed an alliance within the Wovenvales, but I can guess at it -- to prepare for an assault upon the rest of the Trollshaws.

'If these creatures do indeed belong to separate broods, then I propose that the venom of one may be deadly to the other. If this is so, we may be able to turn their own weapons against them and destroy each of the deadly broods! These spiders cannot be allowed to remain here.

'If you are prepared for another adventure, ${PLAYER}, I ask you to journey once more into the Wovenvales. Defeat spiders of each brood and retrieve their fangs. There may be enough venom within them to poison their egg sacs.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is intended for a full fellowship.</rgb>Naethmunn has asked you to lend your aid to the Ranger Pantescal, defending the ruins of House Brumbar in Parth Aduial.The remains of House Brumbar are in Parth Aduial, north-east of Tinnudir. Naethmunn told you to cross the bridge to the mainland and then follow the shoreline north until you see the few walls that remain of House Brumbar.

Naethmunn has asked you to lend your aid to Pantescal, currently planning the defence of an important Dúnedain site against a crowd of boggarts.Talk to PantescalNaethmunn is at the Ranger camp on Tinnudir, in Evendim, south-west of House Brumbar.

You defended House Brumbar from the band of boggarts that threatened it and should now return to Naethmunn with the tale of your success.'While you were confronting Jabe Grimshaw in Tyrn Fornech, a Ranger named Pantescal sent word of many boggarts advancing towards the ruins of House Brumbar. Brumbar was a Dúnedain line of no small importance before the abandonment of Annúminas, and we must keep the grounds of that ancient manor safe from treasure-seekers, though the buildings are mostly gone.

'Pantescal did not seem overly-concerned about this band of boggarts, but I would be put more at ease if you stood with him. The creatures are cowardly, but in great numbers even the weakest of foes can pose a threat.

'The ruins of House Brumbar are north and east of Tinnudir, in Parth Aduial. Cross the bridge to the mainland and follow the shore northward. Brumbar is little more than crumbling walls now, but we can not allow the boggarts to befoul its memory.''You will find House Brumbar north-east of Tinnudir, in Parth Aduial. Cross the bridge to the mainland and follow the shoreline north until you find Pantescal, and help him defend the site from the boggart-band!''Naethmunn has sent you to me? I do not think I will have need of your assistance, but I know better than to refuse help earnestly offered!

'These boggarts are weak, but their great numbers give them courage. This courage is misplaced, for we will turn them aside from House Brumbar with ease!

'Make yourself ready!''You have returned, ${PLAYER}! I must applaud you and apologize at the same time!

'I still did not believe you were trustworthy. These are dark days, and the Dúnedain cannot afford to trust so easily. But you have proven yourself to me many times over!

'I will tell Calenglad that your errand must not be hindered. Do not think less of me! The Dúnedain have not survived through the long years by having an abundance of trust.'Broderic Willowmeade, a man of Bree-town has bade you seek out Imyl in the Last Homely House of Rivendell, and offer aid to her if you may.Speak with Imyl of Rivendell.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}, have you travelled to fair Rivendell? I have had business there on occasion in the past, but lately a friend of mine by the name of Imyl sent warning to me that I should no longer travel through the Trollshaws, for fear that I should fall victim to bands of roving hill-men who have come down from the north in the last year or so.

'I count myself a friend of the fair Elves of Rivendell, and if matters have come to this, I fear that they may be in some peril. Should you find your way to Rivendell, seek out Imyl of the Last Homely House, and aid her, if you may. I would be most grateful.''Broderic sent you here? To aid us?

'What a dear, foolish man he is. I doubt there is much that you can do to aid us, for our borders are tested by the shadow at every turn. However, if you are determined to lend us aid, then I will gratefully accept your help.''You should speak with Imyl at the Elf-haven of Rivendell.'Corcur, descendants of the Hill-men of Rhudaur, have encamped at the ruins of Minas Agor in the South Trollshaws.Corcur are encamped at the ruins of Minas Agor in the South Trollshaws.

While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should deal with the Corcur encamped there.Defeat Corcur in the South Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Corcur are encamped at the ruins of Minas Agor in the South Trollshaws.

While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should deal with the Corcur encamped there.The lone winding road through the Trollshaws leads to the last bastion of civilization for a great many leagues. Travellers must take great care while exploring this road however, for it is not well-guarded from the dangers of the wild.Explore stuff.Beyond this bridge the domain of Men ends. While the Lone-lands have long been left desolate and rarely-travelled, the lands beyond are altogether wild and untamed. Only the well-seasoned wanderer or skilled adventurer would brave the Trollshaws alone.At the behest of the sons of Elrond, Barachen the Elf established a small camp in the southern Trollshaws from which to watch for threats on the road to Rivendell. The Elves Alphlanc and Rochwen, bound to him by friendship rather than command, assist Barachen with his duties and work to keep the road free from danger.This is the only crossing of the River Bruinen until it joins with the mighty Greyflood far to the south and west. The waters seem calm and placid here, but the signs along either bank suggest that the river overflows its course with great violence from time to time.The southern passage into Rivendell is called the Gates of Imladris and establishes a clear bastion of civilization and safety in an otherwise wild land. Nevertheless, the Elves of Rivendell guard this approach carefully, and it is not entirely safe for travellers to approach unannounced -- those who pass this way with ill intent in their hearts are rarely seen or heard from again.The dwarves of Heithur Ironfist's company have fallen upon some misfortune near the Last Bridge, and the stones they were transporting to Glóin in Rivendell were lost.Cave-claws infest the ruins of Ost Dúrgonn, north of the road and Barachen's camp.

Heithur Ironfist believes that the cave-claws of Ost Dúrgonn might have carried away the stones that his company was bringing to Glóin and perhaps swarmed in such strength as to defeat the dwarves.Search Ost Dúrgonn for the stolen stonesHeithur Ironfist is at Barachen's camp, east of the Last Bridge and south of the road, on a sloping hill in the shadow of tall cliffs.

You have learned from Tóki Whitebeard that the stones his company was transporting have been stolen by trolls, apparently aided by the monstrous cave-claw you defeated.Talk to Tóki Whitebeard'Clearly, misfortune befell my companions. My dwarves may be lost now, but the stones they were escorting can be recovered from whomever or whatever has stolen them. This we must do, ${PLAYER}.

'As I was returning from Glóin's camp to meet my companions, I saw a large number of cave-claws along the road, especially to the north of the road. Barachen tells me that the ruins of Ost Dúrgonn lie near there as well... the old fortress of Rhudaur would attract creatures such as cave-claws, for the vermin devour stone. It may be that whatever frenzy has drawn them out of their caves has also driven them to attack armed caravans. Alas, the stolen stones would be just such a prize as might cause the cave-claws to swarm so.

'Would you investigate Ost Dúrgonn for any signs of the stones? As with many beasts, often the pack-leader keeps the choicest morsels, and these stones would certainly be that. Perhaps they yet survive within their foul den.''Are you... here to help? Be careful, friend! A mighty cave-claw has slain... the rest of my....'

The dwarf shudders with exhaustion.

'This monstrous cave-claw... attacked us... after the trolls stole... the stones we... were bearing....''Many... thanks, good ${RACE}. I do not think... I could have held out... any longer.

'You say that Heithur Ironfist... has taken refuge with an... Elf to the south of here? I... will go to him... then, when I have rested a moment. Please... track down the trolls who... stole the stones. They led us here... but I believe their camp... is further east along the road....'The wild boars of the South Trollshaws have become numerous and dangerous, oft attacking travellers upon the road.There are boars dwelling in the South Trollshaws.

While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should cull the number of boars, perhaps lessening the threat they present to travellers upon the road.Defeat boars in the South Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are boars dwelling in the South Trollshaws.

While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should cull the number of boars, perhaps lessening the threat they present to travellers upon the road.Tóki Whitebeard told you that trolls stole the stones his company was bearing.The Stone-trolls are encamped on a trail north of the road, further east from the Last Bridge.

Tóki Whitebeard asked you to hunt down the trolls who stole the stones and recover the dwarves' treasure.Search for the stolen stones among the Stone-trollsThe Stone-trolls are encamped on a trail north of the road, further east from the Last Bridge.

Tóki Whitebeard asked you to hunt down the trolls who stole the stones and recover the treasure.Search for stolen stones among the Stone-trolls of the TrollshawsHeithur Ironfist is at Barachen's camp, south of the road, westward from the Stone-troll camp.

You should bring the stolen stones to Heithur Ironfist at once.The Stone-trolls are encamped on a trail north of the road, further east from the Last Bridge.

Tóki Whitebeard asked you to hunt down the trolls who stole the stones and recover the treasure.'You have recovered the stones from the Stone-trolls! You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, and more besides -- you have the thanks too of Lord Glóin of the Lonely Mountain!

'Take this reward and bear it in memory of the good that you have done for me and my master!'Arohir of Esteldín has bade you seek the camp of Tinnudir along the eastern shore of Lake Evendim, and once there to speak with Cannuion.Cannuion is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir, in Evendim, to the west of the North Downs.

Arohir has sent you to speak with Cannuion in Evendim.'Have you heard of the Wardens of Annúminas? They are a branch of our order who guard the ancient tombs and ruins which mark the long-ago abandoned capital of Arnor.

'News has come to me that they stand hard-pressed, as bandits and refugees from the North Downs have begun to loot the old tombs in increasing numbers, and darker rumours of the presence of Angmarim agents who seek entrance into the ancient city itself.

'Travel to the camp of Tinnudir and you will find Cannuion, who will be most grateful for any aid you can render.''You have been sent by Arohir? Good, we have great need of trustworthy warriors to help us against the growing threat of robbers and the like that have grown up in recent months here - for we are few, and it threatens to overwhelm us.''Speak with Cannuion at Tinnudír on the banks of Lake Evendim, ${PLAYER}.'The broods of the Wovenvales may be vulnerable to each other's venom.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest is intended for a full fellowship.</rgb>Egg-sacs of both the Trapdoor and Flesh-gnawer broods may be found in the Wovenvales, in the north-west corner of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp.

You should use the fangs you collected to envenom the egg-sacs of the Wovenvale spiders.Envenom the spiders' egg-sacsEgg-sacs of both the Trapdoor and Flesh-gnawer broods may be found in the Wovenvales, in the north-west corner of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp.

You should use the fangs you collected to envenom the egg-sacs of the Wovenvale spiders.Egg-sacs of both the Trapdoor and Flesh-gnawer broods may be found in the Wovenvales, in the north-west corner of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp.

You should use the fangs you collected to envenom the egg-sacs of the Wovenvale spiders.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest is intended for a full fellowship.</rgb>Naethmunn has asked you to defeat Jabe Grimshaw, a leader among the tomb-robbers who often plans their activities from high atop Barad Rath, an overlook in Tyrn Fornech.Jabe Grimshaw plans his band's attacks from atop Barad Rath, a flat stone overlook atop the tall hills of Tyrn Fornech, north-east of Tinnudir and north of Tham Ornen.

Ranger Naethmunn has asked you to find and defeat Jabe Grimshaw, leader of a band of tomb-robbers that has plagued the Rangers of Evendim for a long time.Naethmunn is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim, south-west of Barad Rath.

You should report your victory over Jabe Grimshaw to Naethmunn.'Calenglad is a wise Ranger who has seen many summers, and I trust his judgement as my own. If he is not convinced of your honesty, I remain unconvinced as well.

'North of Tinnudir, in Tyrn Fornech, an ancient stone overlook stands watch atop one of the tallest hills. Jabe Grimshaw, leader to one of the robber-bands that has caused us so much trouble, plans his band's activities from its heights.

'If you seek to prove yourself to me and Calenglad, you will put an end to Jabe Grimshaw. You will find Barad Rath, the flat stone platform atop the tall hills of Tyrn Fornech, north-east of Tinnudir and north of Tham Ornen. You will find Jabe there as well.''Barad Rath is atop one of the tallest hills of Tyrn Fornech, north-east of Tinnudir and north of Tham Ornen. You will find Jabe Grimshaw there, planning the activities of his robber-gang.''Grimshaw is no more? This is excellent news, ${PLAYER}, and I begin to believe your tale.

'It is not yet enough, I am afraid, but perhaps you are telling the truth. If you succeed at my next errand I will be free of doubt!'Stone-trolls have come down from the Misty Mountains in large number to the South Trollshaws.There are Stone-trolls encamped north of the main road in the South Trollshaws.

While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should deal with the Stone-trolls encamped there.Defeat Stone-trolls in the South Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are Stone-trolls encamped north of the main road in the South Trollshaws.

While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should deal with the Stone-trolls encamped there.After spending some time with you, the Elves of Rivendell are prepared to welcome you into the inner halls of Imlad Gelair.Imlad Gelair is located to the south-east of The Last Homely House, below the Falls of Imladris.

You have been instructed to speak with Atharbain in Imlad Gelair.'${PLAYER}, it has become clear that your loyalties stand firmly with our House. The Elves of Rivendell are grateful for your service, and already a few of our bards take up their quills, prepared to spread the knowledge of your deeds in harmonious melodies.

'After some discussion, the Defenders of Imlad Gelair were instructed to welcome you to our sanctuary high upon the hills, overlooking The Last Homely House.

'You will find Imlad Gelair to the south, across the Falls of Imladris at the end of a low road which leads west. When you arrive, speak with Atharbain. She will be expecting you.''You have found favour with my people and should go at once to Imlad Gelair.''We are pleased to have you among us, ${PLAYER}.  You are welcome to make use of any services we can provide.'Anhebir has sent you to the Last Bridge in hopes of providing aid to the scout, Alphlanc.Alphlanc makes her camp at the head of the Last Bridge between the Lone-lands and the Trollshaws, far to the west of Rivendell.

Anhebir has sent you to lend what aid you may to the Elf Alphlanc in the western Trollshaws.Talk to Alphlanc'Greetings, friend, and welcome to Imladris. Are you here at the behest of the Rangers? Perhaps you would aid us in patrolling these lands.

'One of our scouts, Alphlanc, guards the Last Bridge from the Lone-lands into the Trollshaws. You should speak with her and learn how you might aid her.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: You will travel to the Last Bridge immediately when you accept this quest.</rgb>'You were sent by Anhebir? If so, you are welcome here indeed. There is much to be done.'Elf-scouts are encamped at Thorenhad, charged with patrolling the Trollshaws for signs of evil.Thorenhad is a ruin atop a hill north of the bear-dens of the Bruinen Gorges. It is to the east of Barachen's camp, and some distance west of Rivendell.

Anhebir has sent you to Thorenhad, to report to Elrond's son, Elrohir.'I do not believe you have been told yet of Thorenhad. Elrond has sent scouts there to patrol the wilds of the Trollshaws and to search out the evil that lurks in those old hills.

'I am sure you would be welcomed there, for the Trollshaws are a broad land, and our people too few. Seek out Elrond's son Elrohir and say that I have sent you to support him.

'Thorenhad is a ruin atop a hill north of the bear-dens of the Bruinen Gorges. It is to the east of Barachen's camp and some distance west of here.''Please, seek out Elrohir at Thorenhad.''You are welcome to join our company, ${PLAYER}. My brother and I have done our best, but there is more still to be done if we are to keep this land safe from servants of the Enemy.'Cannuion told you of the terrible threat the Angmarim and tomb-raiders pose to the Rangers of Evendim.Tomb-raiders can be found throughout Evendim. Cannuion is at Tinnudir.

Cannuion has asked you to collect the tomb-raiders' sashes of allegiance and bring them to him.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. You have arrived at a difficult time... we have been stretched terribly thin by the incursions of the Angmarim into our lands and by the number of lawless brigands that have been stirred up by the gathering clouds of war.

'It is against the latter which I hope you can aid us. The bands of tomb-raiders have become so bold of late that they have taken to wearing sashes of allegiance to their various unsavoury leaders. I would have you bring me these sashes as proof of their defeat.

'If you can do this for us, then I will see to it that your name is regarded well among the Wardens of Annúminas.''Your actions speak well of your skill and bravery. Would that I could reward you more handsomely for your efforts, but our resources are drawn thin, and our thanks must suffice for the time being.'The Elf Barachen and his friends have learned that a company of dwarves bound for Rivendell may have fallen to misfortune.A boar herd can be found in the South Trollshaws, at a place called Lavanim, west of Barachen's camp.

Barachen asked you to search for the missing dwarves among the boars of the South Trollshaws.Search for evidence of the dwarves' locationA boar herd can be found in the South Trollshaws, at a place called Lavanim, west of Barachen's camp.

Barachen asked you to search for the missing dwarves among the boars to the west of his camp. Perhaps you may find more evidence upon the boars of Lavanim.Search for evidence of the dwarf-company upon the boars of LavanimBarachen is at his camp in the South Trollshaws, south of the road and in the shadow of tall cliffs.

Barachen is waiting to hear whether you found any sign of the missing dwarves among the boars of the Trollshaws.'Our dwarf-friend here has requested my assistance with a matter of some urgency, and we should do what we can to help him. He was part of a company of dwarves that was commanded to bring certain relics from Thorin's Hall to the dwarf Glóin, currently staying in Rivendell.

'Heithur Ironfist travelled ahead to notify his lord that the dwarves would soon arrive, but after the passage of some days, he grew worried. The company never arrived at Rivendell, and Heithur has now come back along the road seeking them. Alas, the grounds along the road from the Last Bridge have been trampled by a herd of wild boars and any tracks are illegible.

'It may be that if you search among the herd to the west, at a place in the wood that we call Lavanim, you may find some clues as to the whereabouts of the dwarves. It may even be that they paused to hunt for meat.''I am uncertain what this cloth portends. It is not of Elf-make, but I cannot say whether it is of dwarf-make or not. Heithur's company may yet live, though I have little hope of it.'Stone-trolls have come down out of the Ettenmoors to settle in the North Trollshaws.Stone-trolls can be found at the ruins of Ost Belegram, south-west of Thoroniel's encampment.

Thoroniel has asked you and your companions to deal with the Stone-trolls of the North Trollshaws.Defeat Stone-trolls in the North Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thoroniel is posted north-east of Ost Belegram, in the North Trollshaws.

You should return to Thoroniel and let her know that you have done as she has asked.Talk to Thoroniel'There are more threats in the North Trollshaws than just spiders, ${PLAYER}. Stone-trolls have come down out of the Ettenmoors to settle here in the North Trollshaws. I have seen them encamped in large number at the ruins of Ost Belegram to the south-west of here.

'If you and your companions could deal with them ere they become a threat to the rest of the Trollshaws, I would be grateful.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Trolls are a creature we shall not brook in our lands, though they seem to be more numerous than ever before.'Heithur Ironfist is concerned about his missing dwarves, but he is especially worried about their cargo of historically-significant stones from Thorin's Hall bound for Glóin, and he wants them recovered.Alphlanc is at the Last Bridge on the western edge of the Trollshaws, where the road passes into the Lone-lands.

Barachen has asked you to speak again with Alphlanc at the Last Bridge to see if she has learned anything of the missing dwarves.Talk to AlphlancThe Last Bridge supports the road as it winds west out of the Trollshaws and passes into the Lone-lands.

Alphlanc has asked you to search the area immediately around the Last Bridge closely for some sign of the missing dwarves.Search the area around the Last BridgeA smashed crate lies at the foot of the Last Bridge, on the water's edge.

You have located a smashed crate by the Last Bridge that appears to be of dwarf-make. You should investigate further.Search the shattered dwarf-crateAlphlanc is at the Last Bridge on the western edge of the Trollshaws, where the road passes into the Lone-lands.

You should tell Alphlanc what you have found.Talk to AlphlancHeithur Ironfist is at Barachen's camp, east of the Last Bridge, on a sloping hill in the shadow of the southern cliffs.

Alphlanc believes that Heithur will want to hear about your discovery of a shattered dwarf-crate at the base of the Last Bridge, emptied of its contents, for it means that Heithur's company met with an unfortunate fate.Talk to Heithur Ironfist'Heithur Ironfist told me about the missing dwarves while you were away, ${PLAYER}. Glóin of the Lonely Mountain requested the delivery of some stones of historical value from Thorin's Hall as a sign of good faith for the Elves of Rivendell -- he is visiting Imladris on a mission of some importance -- and Heithur is worried that Glóin will be made a laughing-stock without such gifts.

'He is mistaken, of course. Master Elrond treats all with respect and honour and has no need for such baubles. I have told Heithur he need not worry on that account, but he does not listen.

'Perhaps the dwarves were surprised before they had come very far into the Trollshaws. Return to the Last Bridge and speak with Alphlanc... perhaps she has seen some sign of their passing.''Greetings once more, ${PLAYER}. Alas, I have seen no sign of these dwarves you are searching for. Is Heithur Ironfist certain that they came this way? If so, it was before Rochwen and I arrived.

'Perhaps you should search the area around the bridge very carefully. Some evidence of trouble might have been missed, or well-hidden by whatever evil fate befell the dwarves.''Examine the area around the Last Bridge carefully, friend, and you might find some sign of the dwarves for whom you are searching.'The crate has been smashed open and its contents removed. Whatever it once contained has been stolen by parties unknown.'You have found the crate my dwarves were bringing with them? I had hoped that you might return with the stones, but it sounds from your tale that someone else has already made off with them.

'This is inexcusable! We must find them, ${PLAYER}, or Lord Glóin will be made a laughing-stock!''You found a shattered crate of dwarf-make? Then it seems your dwarves did pass this way, ere Rochwen and I arrived. You should return to Heithur Ironfist and let him know of your discovery, for it would seem that the dwarves were not fortunate in their encounters.'Robin Dunkley is concerned by the presence of relics stolen from Annúminas in Ost Forod and wants you to return them to their rightful caretakers, the Rangers of Tinnudir.The chest of stolen relics is among the tents on the highest level of Ost Forod, north of Robin Dunkley.

Robin Dunkley has asked you to find a chest of stolen relics and carry it to Ranger Astiul in Tinnudir, avoiding the eyes of the unfriendly Men of Ost Forod.Collect chest of relicsAvoid being seen by unfriendly menAstiul is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim.

Robin Dunkley asked you to speak with Astiul after delivering the chest of stolen relics.Robin Dunkley is in Ost Forod, north-east of Tinnudir.

Ranger Astiul has asked you to return to Robin Dunkley with his thanks for the delivery of the stolen relics.'Life is hard in Tyrn Fornech, ${PLAYER}, and some of the folk who live here at Ost Forod have begun dealing with the robbers in order to better their fortunes. It pains me to say this, but even now in Ost Forod you can find relics stolen from Annúminas.

'We should return these relics to the Rangers of Tinnudir, ${PLAYER} -- it's the right thing to do! You can find a chest full of stolen artifacts among the tents on the highest level of Ost Forod, north of here. Please understand that the folk of Ost Forod who trade with the robbers are not bad people; their desperation makes them unfriendly and more willing to compromise their values, but I do not want you to hurt them.

'Carry the chest to the Ranger Astiul in Tinnudir, to the south-west, and avoid the unfriendly men of Ost Forod! They will find other means of sustaining themselves if this easy, but reprehensible, road is closed to them. Be sure to speak with Astiul when you have delivered the chest.''The chest of stolen relics is north of here, among the tents on the highest level of Ost Forod. Carry it to Astiul in Tinnudir, to the south-west, but avoid the gaze of the unfriendly Men of Ost Forod! They are not evil, and I would not have you hurt them, so if they see you the game will be up!

'Be sure to speak with Astiul when you have delivered the chest.''You didn't speak to Astiul after delivering the chest of stolen relics? Please go talk to him! I want him to know where from where the chest came!''Robin sent you to bring that chest of stolen relics, then? Very good, very good! He is an old man and can be crotchety at times, but his heart is in the right place. He has long been a good friend to the Dúnedain.

'Return to him with my thanks, and I will see about returning these artifacts to their proper places.''Robin Dunkley lives in Ost Forod, the remains of the great fortress that once watched the northern road. His people dwell there and maintain the watch, though some have turned to villainy, dealing and trading with the tomb-robbers of Evendim.

'Robin has always been a good friend to the Dúnedain, and you should continue to render him your aid. It is what Calenglad wants for you.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. I trust that you have delivered the chest of stolen relics to Astiul? Excellent.

'But enough dilly-dallying! I have great news!'Cave-claws have come out of their dens in the mountains, seeking stone to devour in the lowlands of the South Trollshaws.There are cave-claws infesting the South Trollshaws.

While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should cull the number of cave-claws infesting the ruins and low-lands.Defeat cave-claws in the South Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are cave-claws infesting the South Trollshaws.

While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should cull the number of cave-claws infesting the ruins and low-lands.It is odd that Stone-trolls would risk the sunlight, as direct exposure would cause them to return to the stone from which they were made.Stone-trolls can be found north of the road, eastward from the Last Bridge and Barachen's camp.

You should dispatch the Stone-trolls which have come down from the mountains, for their migration into the Trollshaws poses a danger to all who pass that way.Defeat Stone-trolls in the South TrollshawsStone-trolls can be found north of the road, eastward from the Last Bridge and Barachen's camp.

You should dispatch the Stone-trolls which have come down from the mountains, for their migration into the Trollshaws poses a danger to all who pass that way.Defeat Stone-trolls in the South Trollshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many Stone-trolls in the South Trollshaws.CompletedStone-trolls can be found north of the road, eastward from the Last Bridge and Barachen's camp.

You should dispatch the Stone-trolls which have come down from the mountains, for their migration into the Trollshaws poses a danger to all who pass that way.You have defeated many Stone-trolls in the South Trollshaws and have made the road safe for travel once more.The Wardens of Annúminas signify their leadership with a special token, the Warden's Sceptre.Cannasgam is at Tinnudir in Evendim.

Cannasgam has asked you to forge a Warden's Sceptre and bring it to her.'Among the Wardens of Annúminas, we traditionally signify the authority of our leadership via the Warden's Sceptre. Alas, tradition also dictates the inclusion of a rather rare ore in its construction.

'If you can forge for us such a sceptre, the Wardens would be greatly obliged to you.''Aye, that is a Warden's Sceptre, and elegantly forged as well! My thanks to you and your kin, good ${PLAYER}.'Parr Chopley, an out-of-place hobbit at Ost Forod, awaits the delivery of fine skin at the haven outpost of Ost Forod in Evendim.You have accepted a task to collect the fine skin from the beasts surrounding the haven outpost of Ost Forod in Evendim. You are to deliver the items to Parr Chopley, a hobbit, living in the settlement.Wanted: Fine skin from the beasts surrounding the haven of Ost Forod. Deliver the items to Parr Chopley at the centre of the fortress.Wanted: Fine skin from the beasts surrounding the haven of Ost Forod.'This will help us very nicely, thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Parr Chopley, an out-of-place hobbit at Ost Forod, awaits the delivery of new sword sheaths at the haven outpost of Ost Forod in Evendim.You have accepted a task to collect the new sword sheaths from the goblins or tomb-robbers surrounding the haven outpost of Ost Forod in Evendim. You are to deliver the items to Parr Chopley, a hobbit, living in the settlement.Wanted: New sword sheaths from goblins or tomb-robbers threatening the areas surrounding the haven of Ost Forod. Deliver the items to Parr Chopley at the centre of the fortress.Wanted: New sword sheaths from goblins or tomb-robbers threatening the areas surrounding the haven of Ost Forod.'It looks as though you showed this bunch a thing or two.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Eustoma Muddybanks told you that the Mathom Society did not have many pieces of display quality on-hand.Eustoma Muddybanks is in the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire.

Eustoma Muddybanks has asked you bring her some well-kept mathoms.

<rgb=#FF0000> Well-kept Mathoms drop off of Men, Dwarves, Orc-kind, Troll-kind, and the Dead of level 35 - 45 throughout the world.</rgb>'We have been busy as bees these last few days organizing the Mathom Society members and finding storage for all the new mathoms that have been pouring in. Soon enough, we may be forced to use the old storage tunnels. We have never had this much activity before, and I think it is too much for some of the younger hobbits. I overheard some grumblings from young Baldwin outside over finding a honey-roasted chicken for the next Mathom Society meeting when he should have been labeling mathoms! Some of these young hobbits seem more interested in the meeting dinner-menu than the wonderful new mathoms.

'Anyhow, we have found that many of the mathoms are not in very good condition. I don't know what has happened to many of them -- to tell the truth I don't know what most of them do or did! What I do know is that they are not of display quality. What would we have to show of all our hard work if we have no display pieces?

'If you come across any well-kept mathoms, be sure to take extra care when delivering them to us. The more intact they are, the better. And do try to at least wipe them clean before you drop them off...some of them have had some very queer things on them.''A well-kept mathom! I will get it to the Master Chef right away; he is so good at cataloguing the smaller mathoms, you know.'Parr Chopley has decided that he will make do with some delicious bear-steaks instead, since Evendim seems to have a striking absence of boars.Bears roam the hills of Tyrn Fornech and can especially be found at Nan Orngon, east of Ost Forod.

Parr Chopley has asked you to bring him choice cuts of bear-meat from the bears that roam Tyrn Fornech.Parr Chopley is in the old watch-post of Ost Forod, in the hills of Tyrn Fornech, west of Nan Orngon.

You have collected several choice cuts of bear-meat and should bring them to Parr Chopley.'Well, we must not let life's day-to-day upsets get to us, ${PLAYER}. There may not be boars in Evendim, but they say there are a great number of bears throughout the hills of Tyrn Fornech, and especially at Nan Orngon to the east.

'Bear-steaks, while still delicious, are certainly no match for a sizzling boar-steak. My friend Ronald Dwale once went on at great length about the similarities between those two words, you know, "boar" and "bear," but I must confess that I do not share his same love for words. Words are often an inconvenience and get in the way when you are trying to express yourself... to get to the real meat of an idea, if you will.

'The meat in question here, for example, is certainly a choice cut of bear-meat! Bring me back several cuts, and I will share them with some of my neighbours. There will be a bit of coin in it for you, as well, and we can mourn the absence of boar over a delicious bear-steak. How does that sound?''There are bears all over Tyrn Fornech, ${PLAYER}, but you'll find them especially at Nan Orngon, to the east of Ost Forod. Bring me choice cuts of bear-meat, and we can drown our sadness at the absence of boars in Evendim.''You have brought the bear-meat? Good, good! I'll just prepare it, and we'll have a grand old time. Still, it's a shame this isn't boar-meat. You can make a really delicious steak out of boar-meat, if you know what to do.

'Still, I don't mean to sound ungrateful! Bear-meat is still quite good, and to tell you the truth, people here at Ost Forod don't have it quite as easy as my folk in Oatbarton. I'll call over some of these folk and share these steaks with them -- it's only right!

'Thanks again, ${PLAYER}. Keep an eye out for boars!'Arrod has prepared a necklace for the Elf-maid Narlinn with whom he is smitten.Narlinn is at Thorenhad, the camp of the sons of Elrond located among the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear dens.

Arrod has asked you to deliver the necklace to Narlinn, the Elf-maid who is the object of his devotion.Arrod is at his vantage point high above the Bruinen Gorges, by an old set of ruins.

Narlinn has refused Arrod's gift and has sent you to return it to him.'There, I have finished the necklace, ${PLAYER}. If you will bring this to Narlinn, I will be in your debt! You will find her at Thorenhad, the camp of the sons of Elrond located north-west of here, north of the bear dens.

'Narlinn believes that the maiden for whom I have been sighing is Faimir of Rivendell. She is lovely, and for a time I thought I loved her, but my time here in the wild has taught me that Narlinn is the one for whom my heart sings.

'Bring her this necklace with my fondest affection! I will stay here and continue my duties, though I will look forward to rejoining Narlinn in peace when the dark times against which we must guard have passed.''Narlinn? Why do you ask me about her? She is off at Thorenhad with Elladan and Elrohir, I think.

'My Arrod is also there, I think. He has been so thoughtful and admiring of me lately, as to inspire envy from the other maidens.''Thorenhad is west of here, and north of the bear dens of the Bruinen Gorges. Bring my necklace to Narlinn with my affection!''What? This necklace is from Arrod? You must be confused -- he is interested only in Faimir of Rivendell. He has told me this himself!

'You are well-meaning, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot take this. Return with this to Arrod, and tell him that you did not understand his charge.

'I will not hear anymore of this. I do not wish to embarrass you or Arrod any further. You have brought this beautiful necklace to the wrong Elf-maid!''That necklace is very shoddily-made, ${PLAYER}. I do not want it.

'I am sure its maker is most ashamed of his hasty craftsmanship.''Arrod is scouting the Bruinen Gorges, and I am worried that by thinking always of Faimir, he pays no heed to his own safety or to his duty! Return this necklace to him, for there has been some mistake. He did not mean for you to bring it to me.''What? Why do you still have the necklace, ${PLAYER}? Do not tell me that Narlinn refused it!

'I see...I have become a victim of my own subtleties, my friend! So good was my performance that Narlinn believes that Faimir truly is the Elf-maiden for whom I have been sighing!

'I have a solution, ${PLAYER}. I will maintain my watch here, ever-vigilant and meet Narlinn personally when my duty here is done. I will then explain my true feelings to her! I should not have given you this task at all. This task is for Arrod of Rivendell, and Arrod of Rivendell alone!'Robin Dunkley has told you that the people of Ost Forod are worried about one of their own, a hunter named Nat Rapkins, who has not returned from a hunt in the eastern Emyn Uial.Nat Rapkins crossed the Even-rills at the northern tip of the lake, north-west of Ost Forod, and never returned. Robin Dunkley wants you to search along the edge of the lake near the Even-rills for the missing hunter.

Robin Dunkley heard a dreadful howling along the shore at night and is worried that Nat Rapkins might have fallen to some evil beast. He wants you to try and find the lost hunter.Find Nat RapkinsRobin Dunkley is in Ost Forod, south-east of the Even-rills, in Tyrn Fornech in Evendim.

Nat Rapkins spoke of the Gauredain with his dying breath and gave you his pack to return to Ost Forod. You should bring it to Robin Dunkley.'A hunter by the name of Nat Rapkins often travels far to the north-west, crossing the cold waters of the Even-rills that feed into the lake, and conducts his hunts in Emyn Uial. Nat is a woodsman of no small skill and should have returned by now. His family is overcome with concern.

'I did not want to say anything to them about it, but I heard a terrible howling along the shore last evening. It had been driven from my mind with all of our doings against the tomb-robbers, but now I wonder if those dreadful howls had something to do with poor Nat.

'If you would journey north-west to the northernmost tip of the lake and cross the Even-rills there to search for Nat Rapkins, I would greatly appreciate it. He has been gone for far too long, and I fear what end he may have found. He is sure to have remained in sight of the lake, if that was within his power, so do not stray too far from it.''If old Nat is in trouble, you'll find him somewhere near the Even-rills at the northern reach of the lake. Head north-west of Ost Forod and cross the waters at its northern reach, but beware of whatever evil made that terrible howling -- it froze my blood cold to hear it.''You there... I... attacked by Gauredain! Terrible creatures....

'Take my pack... bring it... Ost Forod....''I was afraid you would return with such news, ${PLAYER}. Nat was a good hunter, well-liked by the people here, and will be missed. I will return the pack to his family and give them these sad tidings.

'You say he spoke of the Gauredain? Yes, I feared as much. They have always been a danger to those who find themselves in Emyn Uial, but it has been many years since last they proved so bold. Something must be done, ${PLAYER}.'Unable to leave her post, Narlinn is concerned for her friend, Arrod, whom she has not heard from in days.Arrod is encamped in the Bruinen Gorges, upon the cliff overlooking the road eastward from Narlinn's camp. Narlinn told you to seek the white marker stone pointing towards the road north to Thorenhad, then take the road and turn aside to the right of the path and circle back to the cliff.

Narlinn has not received any reports from her friend Arrod in days and has asked you to seek him out and learn if he is well.Find the white marker stone indicating the path to ThorenhadArrod is encamped in the Bruinen Gorges, upon the cliff overlooking the road eastward from Narlinn's camp. Narlinn told you to seek the white marker stone pointing towards the road north to Thorenhad, then take the road and turn aside to the right of the path and circle back to the cliff.

Narlinn has not received any reports from her friend Arrod in days and has asked you to seek him out and learn if he is well.Talk to ArrodThe hendroval made its nest among the rocks to the east of Arrod's post.

Fearing for his bird, Caledhroval, Arrod has asked you to search the nest of the hendroval he saw for any evidence of what it might have brought back from its hunt.Search hendroval-nestArrod is encamped in the Bruinen Gorges, upon the cliff overlooking the eastward road, west of the hendroval-nest.

You should bring the feather you found to Arrod.'My friend Arrod watches from the heights above the road, guarding the path to Thorenhad. Fimgris and I have seen trolls wandering towards that path in the night, and I fear for Arrod's safety. He is a skilful archer, surely able to defend against a single troll, but against more? I do not think that even Arrod would survive the encounter.

'Normally, Arrod would send his companion Calendhroval to provide us with regular reports, but I have seen naught of the bird in days. Neither Fimgris nor I can leave our post... would you seek out Arrod and learn if he is well? You need but travel a small distance east to the white marker stone and take the road north. Leave the road to the right as soon as you may and circle back upon the cliff. You should find him among the ruins there.''Alas, it is as I feared! This feather could belong to none but Caledhroval. I do not believe his death was simply the result of a predator seeking food. It was the work of the Enemy.

'There have been trolls about at night -- I have barely managed to stay hidden at times -- and I have no doubt there are other foul servants of the Enemy in these woods. We must know what evils have come to these lands....''Narlinn sent you? I am not surprised. I have been unable to send her any reports for several days, for my friend and companion Caledhroval, whom I usually dispatch with messages, has been missing.

'I sent Calendhroval out to scout the Gorges a few days ago, and he never returned. I did, however, sight a hendroval returning to its nest not far from here. I fear the worst, for I saw that the bird bore something in its talons. It may have simply been a rodent, but I doubt it. Hendrevail are oft used by the Enemy as spies, and I think it more likely that Caledhroval fell prey to the creature.

'I cannot leave my post to investigate... would you do so in my stead? I must know if Caledhroval still lives. The nest was on the other side of those rocks to the east.'The Elf Fimgris has noticed the wolves of the Bruinen Gorges have been acting queer and wonders what could have put such rage and fear into their eyes.The wolves of the Bruinen Gorges stalk the vale between the main road and Thorenhad. Fimgris told you to follow the road east to the white marker stone, then turn north.

Fimgris has asked you to defeat some of the crazed wolves of the Bruinen Gorges in hopes that you might discover what has disturbed them.Find the white marker stone indicating the path to ThorenhadThe wolves of the Bruinen Gorges stalk the vale between the main road and Thorenhad. Fimgris told you to follow the road east to the white marker stone, then turn north.

Fimgris has asked you to defeat some of the crazed wolves of the Bruinen Gorges in hopes that you might discover what has disturbed them.Defeat wolves in the Bruinen Gorges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'There have been worrisome signs for the past few months that something has not been right in the Trollshaws -- trolls coming down from the mountains, servants of the Enemy upon the road -- but even the beasts of the wood are troubled in ways that I cannot explain. Wolves have long dwelt in the Trollshaws, and though evil by nature, they have generally kept to themselves. Now, however, they have become bold and dangerous. I daresay, I have seen fear in their eyes the like I have never seen.

'It is true that servants of the Enemy pursued a small company along the road not more than two months ago, but the wolves have become more unruly in recent days, and I cannot determine the reason.

'If you would, hunt the wolves of the Gorges in the vale between here and Thorenhad. Perhaps you may find some evidence of what has disturbed them. Follow this road eastward until you find the white marker stone. There, take the road north and begin your hunt.'The Rangers at Tinnudir will want to speak with you about Rantost, the tomb-robbers, and what comes next.Orchalwë is at Tinnudir, south of Rantost.

Orchalwë wants to speak with you about what is next for Evendim.Talk to Orchalwë at Tinnudir'We have done good work here, and I am happy to be able to return home and get back to real work. The few Rangers I spoke with before they left were very cordial. They were excited about getting these relics back to Tinnudir but were also looking forward to a more open beneficial relationship with Ost Forod...something we will certainly welcome.

'The Rangers told me Orchalwë at Tinnudir wanted to speak with you. I believe it is to thank you for your help and aid, but suspect there will be more to do.''The tomb-robbers will threaten our history no more. I thank you greatly for your work to stop them. I know we sent you initially to repair the pact with Ost Forod, but to have you -- and them -- go above and beyond and deliver us Rantost. Words cannot express my gratitude.''You should speak with Orchalwë at Tinnudir.'You found an interesting scroll fragment. By itself it is illegible, but perhaps in combination with other fragments, the original scroll can be restored.Brigands and robbers can be found in many places around Lake Evendim.

Brigands and tomb-robbers in Evendim most likely hold the remaining fragments of the scroll you found.Collect faded scroll-fragments (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect worn scroll-fragments (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tinnudir, an island west of Emyn Uial, may have a lore-master who can help you reassemble the scroll.

You found all the scroll-fragments; now all you have to do is put them together.The old trove is hidden beneath a stone marker, north-east of Tinnudír in the ruins of Barad Rath.

Culang helped to reconstruct the old scroll and told you the good news: not only does it give directions to an old treasure, but the treasure is one that can be honourably recovered, since there is no record of the original owners.Recover the treasure from the old troveCulang can be found back at Tinnudir.

You found no great treasure; it appears that the old trove had been looted long ago. But you did recover an old book: a chronicle of the Battle of Fornost. Perhaps Culang would find it of interest, along with the scroll he restored for you.This scroll fragment looks interesting, but it is illegible by itself. Perhaps in combination with other fragments, the original document can be restored.'An interesting find. I have always enjoyed puzzles such as this. Let us see. This one goes here... ah, a simple matter. All done! Let us learn what it says.

'Remarkable! Evendim abounds with tales of old treasure, most of them completely false. But this scroll... this is an account of a man -- an adventurer shall we say, to be polite to the dead -- who scavenged the Fields of Fornost long ago, after the Witch-king's great defeat. It seems this fellow hid his finds not far away.

'From your point of view, this treasure is a legitimate trove -- there should be no reason that anyone could not honourably recover it if they happened to find its location. If you wish to find this trove, according to the scroll, it lies hidden beneath a stone marker in Barad Rath, ruins that lie to the north-east of here.''Have you recovered the trove yet?''Alas! I am sorry you found no great treasure. That trove must have been looted long ago. But in truth, an old book like this is a treasure to me, though I suppose the robbers must have found it worthless.

'I have little to offer to sweeten your bitter loss, but I will give you what I can for the book and the scroll.'Robin Dunkley, encouraged by your retrieval of the broken statuary carried by the ill-fated robbers that ran afoul of bears at Nan Orngon, has charged you with recovering more of its pieces.Tomb-robbers in Tyrn Fornech may be carrying small statue pieces, and larger pieces can likely be found in their camp on Rantost, the island west of Ost Forod.

Robin Dunkley has been inspired by the broken statuary you recovered with the dream of remaking the complete statue and wants you to recover the pieces of it.Robin Dunkley is at Ost Forod, east of Rantost, in Tyrn Fornech in Evendim.

You have recovered many pieces of statuary, and now you should bring them to Robin Dunkley to see if they belong to the statue he seeks to repair.'I expect that the robbers that prowl Tyrn Fornech are carrying more pieces of this broken statue, ${PLAYER}. If you can recover more of these fragments, I might be able to reassemble it. Wouldn't that be something? I expect Calenglad and the rest of the Rangers would be so pleased!

'Look for robbers among the hills of Tyrn Fornech and take statue pieces from them, ${PLAYER}. You'll most likely find only small pieces on these robbers, but one or two might carry larger pieces. The villains have also established a camp of sorts to the west, on the island of Rantost in the lake; you might find larger pieces of the statue there.

'Return to me with any statue pieces you can recover, and I'll see if I can remake it.''The tomb-robbers that prowl Tyrn Fornech may be carrying small pieces of the statue, and their camp on Rantost, the island to the west, might hold larger pieces. One or two robbers might have large pieces as well.

'If you can recover enough pieces, I might be able to remake the statue! Wouldn't that be something?''Very good, ${PLAYER}, very good indeed! It doesn't look like all of these belong to the statue I'm trying to put back together, but I think enough of them do that I can make a good start of it.

'Do you know, I think this might be a statue of Elendil? I wonder where once it stood? Perhaps it shall stand there again some day!

'There is troubling talk around Ost Forod, my friend. Stay, and I will tell you of it.'While hunting the bears of the Bruinen Gorges, you obtained a hide of unusual toughness. The beast from which it came was strong and hardy, possessed of thick fur and even thicker hide.An armourer of sufficient skill likely dwells in the hidden valley of Rivendell, far to the east of the Bruinen Gorges, across the Ford of Bruinen and beyond.

It will take an armourer of great skill to craft armour worthy of the beast from which this perfect hide came.Never have you seen such a magnificent hide. The fur is thick and lush, unblemished by burrs or tangles. The blows that dispatched its former owner were well-enough aimed that the useable portion of the hide is unmarred. 

An armourer of sufficient skill might make this hide into formidable armour. An Elf in Rivendell likely possesses both the skill and the desire to do this for you.'This hide is truly magnificent, ${PLAYER}, and you are equally so to have bested the mighty creature from which it came!

'I would be honoured to craft fine armour from this hide, friend ${RACE}. Wear it with pride, and at no cost -- the honour of working with such fine materials is payment enough!'Mountain-bears dwelling in the Bruinen Gorges would provide plenty of pelts which the dwarves could use to make blankets.There are mountain-bears dwelling in the Bruinen Gorges, in the Trollshaws.

While you are in the Bruinen Gorges, you should hunt bears for pelts.Collect pelts from the bears of the Bruinen GorgesThere are mountain-bears dwelling in the Bruinen Gorges, in the Trollshaws.

While you are in the Bruinen Gorges, you should hunt bears for pelts.Collect pelts from the bears of the Bruinen Gorges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are dwarves encamped with the Elves at Thorenhad in the Bruinen Gorges.

You should bring the pelts you collected to one of the dwarves encamped at Thorenhad.There are mountain-bears dwelling in the Bruinen Gorges, in the Trollshaws.

While you are in the Bruinen Gorges, you should hunt bears for pelts.'It was good of you to bring these pelts to us. These Elves may not feel the cold, but our old bones most certainly do!'The isle of Rantost is where the tomb-robbers have made their central camp. A great deal of history is being kept there.Crates and barrels are spread around Rantost.

Leighton Kipps has asked you to count the packed crates and barrels around Rantost.Search the crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search the barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Leighton Kipps is camped at the south-east corner of Rantost.

Leighton Kipps will want to know how many crates and barrels there are so he can relay the information to the Rangers.Talk to Leighton Kipps at Rantost'The tomb-robbers store all of the relics they bring here. They sort them and, depending on their value, place the more valuable items in crates and the less valuable items in barrels. 

'The crates are kept deeper within the camp, in more guarded locations. The barrels are strewn about here and there. They are still valuable, but the crates are the most valuable.

'I have not been able to get a count of how many crates and barrels there are around the island. The Rangers will need to know how many there are so they can prepare accordingly. Please get their number for me.''Good! This will tell the Rangers how many men to bring and how much they will be carrying back.''The Rangers will need to change their preparations and strength of their force based on this count, so do not miss any.'Wolves may be attracted to the Bruinen Gorges by the presence of the elk which dwell there.There are elk dwelling in the Bruinen Gorges in the Trollshaws.

The wolves which trouble the Bruinen Gorges might be deterred if the number of the elk were thinned, leaving them with little prey.Defeat elk in the Bruinen Gorges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are elk dwelling in the Bruinen Gorges in the Trollshaws.

The wolves which trouble the Bruinen Gorges might be deterred if the number of the elk were thinned, leaving them with little prey.The Elves at Thorenhad desire a delivery of extremely sharp claws to be made to them.You have accepted a task to collect extremely sharp claws from the creeping things in the areas surrounding Thorenhad. The items are to be delivered to a collection box. There is a collection box at Thorenhad in the Trollshaws.Wanted: Extremely sharp claws from the creeping things surrounding Thorenhad. All items should be delivered to the collection box at the outpost in the Trollshaws.Wanted: Extremely sharp claws from the creeping things surrounding Thorenhad.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Hendrevail, often used as spies by the Enemy, have begun to appear in the Bruinen Gorges.Hendrevail can be found in the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws.

While you are in the Bruinen Gorges, you should deal with the hendrevail which have begun to appear there.Defeat hendrevail in the Bruinen Gorges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hendrevail can be found in the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws.

While you are in the Bruinen Gorges, you should deal with the hendrevail which have begun to appear there.Erchiel is ready to move forward with the final stages of the plan Lithuifin helped her devise.Erchiel has asked you to modify a series of Gauradan-markers into Wards of Doom to prevent the Gauredain from crossing into the Eavespires.

The Gauradan-markers are along the river to the north of the Eavespires.Place false wards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return and tell Erchiel that you have finished placing the wards.

Erchiel is at the Eavespires, south of the river.'Now then, as a warrior of some renown, I am all too accustomed to doing battle, and always I contend with and offer the threat of death. Against such mean foes as goblins and Orcs, this threat itself is often sufficient to break their spirits and send them back into the darkness unless they are driven by powerful masters -- but not so with the Gauredain.

'As Lithuifin has reminded me, Men such as they who are still free of spirit and pride often place greater value upon the unseen and unfelt worlds than they do upon their own lives. The wards were the clue, and it is this that we shall play upon to keep our respective camps safely separated. You may have noticed a number of Gauradan-markers along the shore of the river just north of here. Those mark the current boundaries of the Gauredain's territory -- at least as they see it. But they do not in any way prevent them from crossing further into our stretch of the forest. That we shall now change.

'I have changed the wards you brought me and added a few flourishes. If you add these to the boundary markers, they will no longer represent mere territorial boundaries, but Wards of Doom to the Gauredain, a warning that any who cross put their very spirits into absolute peril. The Gauredain may not respect our swords and bows, but this they shall not lightly ignore.''This final task should be quite simple. The markers you seek can be found along the northern bank of the river that runs by the Eavespires.''Ah, well done, my friend. That should greatly reduce the threat of the Gauredain for the time being.

'That line of wards will neither prevent their crossing indefinitely, nor will it stop some of their most insistent or brave hunters from intruding, but I will deal with those as I must. What it will do is prevent open war from erupting between their tribe and those of us here in the Eavespires, and that is enough for now.

'You have my deepest gratitude, and though I have no more tasks for you, you may wish to speak with Lithuifin or Longbough and see if either of them requires your aid.'The Eavespires is a small camp on the north-western shore of Lake Evendim.Talk to Longbough at the Eavespires'The oath with Ost Forod has been resworn, and we stand stronger today because of that. It is a great burden off of my shoulders to have those wrongs now stand righted.

'Now we turn our attention to the western shore and to a friend we have had far longer than Ost Forod. A friend who stands at the end of his time and weeps for the state of the land.

'Use the boat and venture across to the Eavespires. Speak with Longbough once you arrive. Let him know the Rangers will do whatever they can to soothe his pains.''While we can restore the ruins, the lake and forest will not heal without Longbough.''You say a Ranger sent you? He is wise to know the lake and forest are in pain.'Arrod's bird-companion, Caledhroval, was seriously wounded by a hendroval and carried back to the scavengers' nest near Arrod's post.The bear-den lies off the road to the north-west of Arrod's camp, in the shadow of Thorenhad.

Arrod asked you to search the bear-den for evidence of what transpired between Caledhroval and the hendroval.Find the bear-den beneath ThorenhadThe bear-den lies off the road to the north-west of Arrod's camp, in the shadow of Thorenhad.

Arrod asked you to search the bear-den for evidence of what transpired between Caledhroval and the hendroval.Search for evidence at the bear-denArrod is encamped in the Bruinen Gorges, upon the cliff overlooking the eastward road, south-east of the bear-den.

You should bring Caledhroval to Arrod at once, so that the Elf may tend to his friend's wounds.'I saw the hendroval come from the north-west, ${PLAYER}. There is a den of bears there in the shadow of Thorenhad. It may be that the hendroval was spying upon Elladan and Elrohir, and Caledhroval discovered it....

'If that is indeed where Caledhroval fell, there might still be some evidence present to suggest exactly what happened. Would you go to the bear-den and search for this evidence? You need only follow the road northward to the den.''Caledhroval! My friend lives!

'Thank you for bringing him to me...I will tend to his wounds. However, I know for certain now that the hendroval was indeed a spy.'Erchiel, an Elf living in Eavespires, has asked you to enter the lands of the Gauredain to the north and collect some relics from their encampments there that she might better understand the threat as they intrude further south into the forests.Erchiel has asked you to collect various relics from the camps of the Gauredain.

The Gauradan camps lie in the hills to the north of the Eavespires.Collect Gauradan-basketCollect Gauradan-spearCollect a Gauradan-wardYou should return to Erchiel with the Gauredain relics.

She can be found at the Eavespires, south of the Gauradan encampments.'Greetings, traveller. It is not often that we receive visitors here, so far from the open roads, but you are welcome to stay a little while if you wish. Take care around Longbough, however. He is a bit short-tempered for an Onod and has little trust for the folk of Eriador. In fact, if you would gain his trust, then there is a small matter with which you might aid us.

'An unusual tribe of Men called the Gauredain have recently come down from the mountains to the north and have begun to hunt these lands. Thus far they seem little more than savages, but they are hostile to most whom they meet, and I have no intention of allowing them to disturb us here in the Eavespires. Nevertheless, my husband Lithuifin frowns on unnecessary slaughter; therefore, I wish to learn more about the Gauredain before I take further steps to drive them away -- but it falls to me to maintain the watch upon this grove, and I have little time for such expeditions.

'If you could surreptitiously gather a few relics from their encampments in the hills north of here and bring them to me, I might learn a good deal more about them, for I have dealt with a great many tribes of Men and others in my years, and many of their customs and symbols are familiar to me.''Hoom! Hom! I would not tarry here over-long, Little One. These forests are wild places, and since the fall of the old kingdoms, they are not for the likes of you.''I see that Erchiel has convinced you to help her deal with the Gauredain who have intruded on these forests. That is well, for they have become a growing problem of late.

'Please take care, however: my dear Erchiel's methods can sometimes be a bit... harsh.''Bring me those relics, ${PLAYER}, that I may have a trophy of this my foe.''Ta-rum! What you do with the trinkets of the Gauredain is of little interest to me. The affairs of Men in this age are of no import here.''These relics are crude, but revealing. I believe that Erchiel asked you to retrieve these, did she not?

'She has never been known for her sense of patience, so I would take them to her right away were I you.''Ah, I see you have returned with the relics of the Gauredain. Excellent.

'They are crude as I expected, but they also show more sinister signs -- some of the work is influenced by the customs of Orcs and goblins! The relationship is distant, and perhaps they have had no dealings with each other for some considerable time, but it does not bode well for our chances of coming to a reasoned understanding with them, I am afraid.

'Lithuifin's tender temperaments aside, I fear that our next course may best be one of decisive action -- hopefully he will not be too upset with me.'Folk tales have long spoken of werewolves stalking the night -- but now that you have met the Gauredain, you suspect you know more of the truth of these tales. If they are Men, then they are only barely so. They are greater than most Men in stature, yet hunched over and using only primitive tools and speech and often dressing in the skins of wolves.Defeat Gauredain in EvendimIf the Gauredain were known to the ancient Kings of Arnor, few tales survive to this day that speak of them. More likely it seems that these savage Men wandered down into Evendim from the far north from Forochel.Defeat Gauredain in EvendimGlorfindel has heard that his former comrade Erchiel has taken up residence in a glade by Lake Evendim.Culang is at Tinnudir, an island off the east shore of Lake Evendim, west of the North Downs.

Glorfindel has asked you to seek out his old battle-companion Erchiel who is said to be living near Lake Evendim. He has sent you first to speak to the Ranger Culang at Tinnudir, for it may be that he knows where she can be found.Erchiel may be found in a glade on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim, by a stream that empties into the lake.

Culang received you warmly but confessed he had not heard the name Erchiel before. He suggested it may be that she can be found in or near a strange glade on the west shore of Lake Evendim, but he warned you that the area is very dangerous.'Well met! I know you to be a great traveller, and it occurs to me that I might be able to make use of your road-lore. Long ago, an Elf-warrior named Erchiel was one of my company. She was a doughty fighter and a boon companion. But since I had heard nothing from her in recent years, I had supposed she had sailed over the Sea and departed Middle-earth.

'Yet now comes word from a traveller that she is living in a glade near Lake Evendim. If you would be so kind, I will send you to her with my greetings and with an invitation to come to Rivendell now that Middle-earth is once again threatened by the Enemy.

'If you accept this task, I will send you first to the Ranger lore-master Culang at Tinnudir, an island just off the eastern shore of Lake Evendim. Since before the fall of Sauron, Evendim has been the domain of Men, not of Elves, so not only is it a courtesy to call on him first, but it may be that he knows just where Erchiel can be found.''Please seek out Culang at Tinnudir, as it may be he knows where Erchiel may be found.''You come from Lord Glorfindel himself? Well then, you are welcome here -- it is a great honour to receive a messenger from such a renowned Elf!

'Erchiel, you say? I know not that name. There are few Elves who come to these lands, and those are mostly travellers, not residents. Still, it may be....

'I have heard tell of an uncanny glade across the lake, on the north-west shore. That shore is dangerous these days, but they say the glade itself is different. If an Elf lives anywhere around the lake, it would be in or near that glade. Go if you will... but be wary!''You should speak with Erchiel, across the lake.''Glorfindel... It is an age and more since last I saw his face. You bring back many memories....

'I have fought many battles for my kindred, yet long ago I laid aside my sword, and that was no idle choice. Even Glorfindel's words will not sway my resolve.

'I thank you for your kindness in bearing Glorfindel's invitation, but I think I will not go to Imladris.'Crawlers have begun to burrow up from the earth, notorious for feeding upon the corpses of the dead and spreading disease.There are crawlers infesting the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws.

While you are in the Bruinen Gorges, you should cull the number of crawlers, hopefully reducing the risk of disease.Defeat crawlers in the Bruinen Gorges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are crawlers infesting the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws.

While you are in the Bruinen Gorges, you should cull the number of crawlers, hopefully reducing the risk of disease.You have been encouraged to learn the lay of the lands around Lake Nenuial, so you may better find your way around its shores.Horace Roxhythe hid one of his arrow-heads somewhere in Evendim. He crossed from the island of Tinnudir to the mainland on the stone bridge.

You have been challenged to follow Horace's trail and recover the arrow-head he hid somewhere in Evendim to prove you are ready for his teachings.Horace Roxhythe is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir.

You have found the arrow-head that Horace hid in Evendim and should return it to him so he will recognize your skill as a hunter.'Welcome to Tinnudir, ${PLAYER}. I can show you secret paths by which you can lead your fellowship here quickly, but you must prove to me that you are worthy to be taught such skills. You must know for what to look.

'I have hidden one of my arrow-heads somewhere in Evendim. If you can pick up my trail and follow the signs, you will be able to recover the arrow-head and prove to me that you are ready. If not, well...perhaps another hunter will succeed where you fail.

'I will tell you this: I crossed the bridge from Tinnudir to the mainland. So you will want to begin your search for my trail there.''I crossed to the mainland by bridge, but from there you will need to pick up my trail, if you are to find the arrow-head I have hidden somewhere in Evendim.'Peering closely at the soil, you find a scratched arrow-head partially embedded in the dirt. This must be Horace's arrow-head.There are tracks here in the soil, but you cannot tell what made them, or how long ago they were made. It is not likely that Horace came this way.The trail here is muddled and confused. That Horace came this way is unmistakeable to your skilled eye, but you cannot discern in what direction he left this place.The marks in the dirt leave no question: the trail here leads south-east.There is little question to your keen eye that Horace's trail here bends south-west.'Yes, this is my arrow-head! See these scratches here? I carved my initials there so I would be able to recognize it. A number of burglars have tried to pass themselves off as hunters, and I needed some way to catch imitations.

'I will teach you secret paths through Evendim, ${PLAYER}, so you will be able to lead your fellowship to Tinnudir with utmost speed.'Erchiel has asked you to defeat several of the Gauredain in order to frighten them and keep them from exploring further south.Erchiel has asked you to defeat a number of Gauredain in order to instill in them a healthy fear of the forests.

The Gauredain she speaks of can be found in the forests north of the river that passes by the Eavespires.Defeat Gauredain tribesmen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Gauredain gorge-stalkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat a Gauradan soothsayerErchiel is at the Eavespires on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim.

You should return and tell Erchiel of your forays against the Gauredain.'I am afraid that speaking with the Gauredain is unlikely to buy us anything -- they are very nearly feral creatures, and the influence of the Orcs means they are unlikely to look upon Elves such as myself kindly at all.

'If they discover us here there is every likelihood that they will attempt to drive us out -- and while neither Longbough nor I would allow it, to have such bloodshed occur on our very doorstep would wound Lithuifin deeply, and I would not wish to involve him so.

'I would ask you to hunt down some small number of their hunters and warriors that have wandered south of the river -- not so many as to cause them grievous hurt, but enough to warn them that these lands are not theirs, nor are they welcome here. It would also be best if you could find one of their leaders, for such tribes are often deeply superstitious and the loss of such a leader can set them aback greatly in fear.''Hoom, ta-room! It is of no matter to me if you wish to do battle with the Men of the Wood, nor do I care which of you are victorious -- so long as you do not bring your troubles here into these quiet glades!''Erchiel has asked you to do battle with the Gauredain, hasn't she?

'I am afraid that she is too old and set in her ways to accept counsel in such matters from such as I unless she comes to me for such advice.

'Erchiel was born in long ages past where the long wars against the Enemy made skill at war paramount -- and she does not easily forget those ways when she feels that our place here may be threatened. Even when there may be a better way.''You will not have to search far for the Gauredain that roam these forests.

'I fear it is only a matter of time now before they discover us here at the Eavespires, unless you can deter them from coming south of the river.''Hom! Hoom! Take care that you do not bring your petty battles here, Little One.''So, you have done battle with the Gauredain who now invade these forests, but I can see in your eyes that the outcome was not what you and my dear Erchiel had hoped for -- that the Gauredain remain undeterred.

'She is no fool, however, and I rather expect she will seek a more effective course soon enough.''It seems you have fought well against the Gauredain, but from your descriptions of their savagery I realize that I have been hasty and foolish myself....

'Forgive me. I have fought a great many battles and lost many things I have cared for and become something of a creature of habit. The way of the sword comes to my hand and thoughts as readily as breathing, and I fear it may always be so. I have misjudged the Gauredain -- they are feral and brutal perhaps, but unlike the craven Orcs and goblins, it seems they are yet unbowed and carry a great pride with them -- they will not be cowed by such an assault.

'I will consult with Lithuifin on the matter, for he is gentler and in his own manner a more clever Elf than I, and certainly his mind is less clouded with thoughts of glory long lost. We will speak again shortly when I have had more time to consider our next course of action.'The Rangers have come to Rantost to cast out the tomb-robbers and reclaim the stolen relics.Rangers have taken up position at three camps on the island of Rantost. 

Defend the Rangers from attacks by tomb-robbers and their allies.Speak to Eliot Bencroft'Are you ready to meet back up at our camp? Speak to me when you are prepared to leave.''I do not yet wish to reveal myself to the tomb-robbers as being the spy! Do not think less of me for remaining here, in hiding! You should hasten to help the Rangers around the island. I believe they have set up camps around the three sites at which you found stockpiled relics.

'One stockpile is right here, one is in the centre of the ruins, and one is on the west side of the ruins. The tomb-robbers will likely assault the Rangers at all three sites!'You defeated the hendroval, but saw few trolls, though they may be holed up in their cave.The entrance to the troll-cave is north-east of Arrod's camp.

You should scout inside the cave, as there are few trolls outside during the light of day.Scout inside the troll-caveThe entrance to the troll-cave is north-east of Arrod's camp.

You should scout inside the cave, as there are few trolls outside during the light of day.Scout inside the troll-caveArrod is at his camp on the cliff south-west of the troll-cave.

You should return to Arrod with tidings of your discovery in the troll-cave.Talk to ArrodThe entrance to the troll-cave is north-east of Arrod's camp.

You should scout inside the cave, as there do not seem to be too many trolls outside.'Cave-trolls? I have not heard of such venturing so far from Moria....

'This is dire news, indeed.'Arrod was pleased with the feather you brought him and has been inspired by it to craft a necklace for Narlinn.A perfect lily grows somewhere along the Bruinen east of Arrod's post.

Arrod has asked you to bring him a perfect lily of exquisite beauty. No other kind will do.Find the perfect lilyArrod is watching the road through the Bruinen Gorges from his vantage point near a set of hilltop ruins, west of the Bruinen.

Arrod will be delighted to see that you have found a lily of exquisite beauty.'I have decided to craft a necklace for my Elf-maid, ${PLAYER}, and though the feather you brought me is a fine addition, it is not yet enough.

'Lilies grow along the banks of the Loudwater, the Bruinen to the east, and any of them would be pretty enough for an Elf-swain to give his love. Mine is no ordinary love, ${PLAYER}, and these white lilies will not be enough!

'Only a mauve lily of unsurpassing beauty will be lovely enough for my Elf-maid. Look for one somewhere along the Bruinen, and carefully -- lilies of such a shade are exceedingly rare!''A mauve lily of unsurpassing loveliness is a rare thing and is only found along the Bruinen. Look with care! None of the white ones will do!''Such beauty! This lily will do nicely, ${PLAYER}. You have my thanks, of course, and they are most heartfelt!

'It will just be a moment. Narlinn will cherish this necklace and recognize the depth of my affection for her!'Kelsey West has told you something of Ost Forod, an old watch-post in Tyrn Fornech that has become settled by the hardened Men of Evendim.Basil Gummidge is in Ost Forod, located in Tyrn Fornech along the road that runs north of the cross-roads in Parth Aduial, north-east of Tinnudir.

Kelsey West has asked you to travel to Ost Forod to speak with Basil Gummidge and offer your help to the people there.'I have come to this camp to enlist the aid of the Rangers with the problems that face my people, but these men seem so distrustful!

'It's almost as if they think Ost Forod is full of tomb-robbers! Certainly times are hard, and some of my people have turned to plunder, but there are far more decent people at my home than the unsavoury types these Rangers fear.

'Will you come to Ost Forod? There are some rewarding bounties posted, and an adventurer of your skills could well find yourself gainfully employed in no time! Just cross the bridge back to the mainland and then follow the road to the cross-roads. Once you reach it, take the northward road up into Tyrn Fornech, and you'll see Ost Forod in no time! One of the arbiters, Basil Gummidge, will be pleased to see you.''To reach Ost Forod, cross back onto the mainland and take the northern road from the cross-roads in Parth Aduial. Look for Basil Gummidge and offer your services, my friend! There are good people in Ost Forod, and they need your help!''Kelsey finally found someone to help us, I see. The Rangers are good men, to be sure, but they are distrustful and seem to believe that the people of Ost Forod have all given in to the lure of tomb-robbing. That is ridiculous, of course.

'Calenglad trusts Robin Dunkley, to be sure, but there are more good Men in Ost Forod than our Robin!'The Elf-scout Pothlorn was wounded in an encounter with Stone-trolls while scouting Ost Thondol.The ruins of Ost Thondol can be found atop the hill, north-west of Pothlorn.

Pothlorn asked you to search the ruins of Ost Thondol for the evil he sensed during his battle with the Stone-trolls.Search Ost Thondol for the source of the evil Pothlorn sensedThe worm-wight is in the ruins of Ost Thondol, north-west of Pothlorn's hiding place.

You should attempt to destroy the worm-wight, which appears to be leading the trolls of Ost Thondol.Defeat the worm-wightPothlorn is hiding among the rocks at the base of the hill, south-east of Ost Thondol.

You should return to Pothlorn and let him know what you discovered within Ost Thondol.Talk to PothlornElladan is at Thorenhad, north-west of Pothlorn's hiding place.

Pothlorn told you to return to Elladan and tell him what you discovered.Talk to Elladan'There were many wolves on the path, and they became ever more maddened the nearer I came to Ost Thondol, which lies on the height right above me. They would not pass the foot of the hill, however, so I pressed on... only to encounter Stone-trolls in the ruins above.

'I sensed something else there, as well, but I know not what it was, for the trolls were too many for me, and I was forced to retreat. They were nearly my death.

'If you wish to be of true aid to Elladan and Elrohir, head up the hill to Ost Thondol and seek the source of the evil here. Whatever it is, even the wolves fear it....''What? A wight in the form of a worm? This is an evil omen indeed. A wight is not empowered of itself, but filled with a spirit of evil, placed there by an even greater evil. You must return to Elladan at once and tell him what you found here. I will come when I am able.''A worm-wight? That explains the uneasiness many of us have felt here for the last few weeks. Pothlorn is right... a greater evil had to have placed the creature at Ost Thondol. The first to come to mind would be the Black Captain, but he was thrown down in the Bruinen and sent horseless back to his master.

'Nevertheless, we must find the master of the worm-wight at all costs. My brother Elrohir sent a scout into Nan Tornaeth, where some worms dwell. You should speak with Elrohir.'The Even-rills are a series of pools and waterfalls through which meltwater from Forochel runs before entering the lake of Evendim.Gauradan-pouches can be found at their camp in the Even-rills, north-east of the Eavespires.

Remmenylf asked you to bring him several of the pouches the Gauredain have in their camp.Collect Gauradan-pouches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Remmenylf can be found at the Eavespires, south-west of the Even-rills.

Remmenylf will want to examine the Gauradan shaman pouches you recovered.'We do not know how long the Gauredain have been encamped within the pools of the Even-rills. They might have already done great damage to the lake. We must know what they are doing there.

'The Gauredain believe in nature and its abilities and powers, though they do not understand whence these powers derive. While we use the virtues instilled therein by the Valar for good and healing, they use it for more nefarious purposes. They should have gathered up several pouches of herbs and plants they are using within the pools.

'Find and bring me these pouches. I may be able to determine what exactly they are poisoning the lake with, and if need be, may be able to concoct a cure.''Take as many pouches as you can from the Gauredain... they may contain different combinations of herbs.''It will take me some time to study these, and if fortune is with us, we will not need to use what I learn.'Robin Dunkley has shared his delight at the misfortune of a band of tomb-robbers with you and wants you to recover any artifacts they might have been transporting.A group of tomb-robbers ran afoul of the bears at Nan Orngon, east of Ost Forod in Tyrn Fornech.

Robin Dunkley has asked you to find the bodies of the tomb-robbers at Nan Orngon and recover any artifacts they might have stolen.Reclaim stolen relic from a tomb-robber corpseRobin Dunkley is at Ost Forod, west of Nan Orngon, in Tyrn Fornech.

You have recovered a piece of broken statuary from a robber that ran into some trouble with bears at Nan Orngon. Robin Dunkley asked you to return any relics you find to him at Ost Forod.'While you were gone, I heard that a group of robbers transporting relics from the islands ran into a spot of trouble with the bears of Tyrn Fornech. Isn't that wonderful?

'Apparently, they had hoped to give Tinnudir a wide berth and had circled far to the east in a great loop, but they went too far and stumbled upon the bears at Nan Orngon. What luck: bad for them but good for us, ${PLAYER}!

'Head east of Ost Forod to Nan Orngon and search the bodies for the relics the robbers brought with them. Bears don't care about such things, so I figure they won't mind if we return them to the Rangers! Use caution while at Nan Orngon, friend -- bears do not discriminate between true-hearted friends of the Dúnedain and villainous tomb-robbers!''Some tomb-robbers ran into trouble with bears at Nan Orngon, to the east. Isn't that wonderful?

'Go to Nan Orngon and recover any artifacts they might have been transporting. The bears don't need them, after all, and we can return them to their rightful places.''This statuary is very interesting, ${PLAYER}, and very old. I wonder how many pieces of this statue have already been claimed by robbers?

'If we can assemble the complete statue, I know that Calenglad and the other Rangers would be pleased!'The Even-rills are a series of pools and waterfalls that meltwater from Forochel runs through before entering the lake of Evendim.The Elves at the Eavespires have several things to help purify the Even-rills.

Longbough has asked you to work with the Elves to rid the Even-rills of the Gauredain.Aid Lithuifin at the Even-rillsAid Remmenylf at the Even-rillsAid Erchiel at the Even-rillsLongbough at the Eavespires.

