'The rowboats are mostly along a small channel that runs through the centre of the island. There may be one or two on the far side, however. Burn them all.''Now we know all the relics will stay here on Rantost until we are ready to take them.''Without the boats to get here or remove relics, Rantost will be ripe for the Rangers to pluck.'The isle of Rantost is where the tomb-robbers have made their central camp. A great deal of history is being kept there.Rantost is north-west of Ost Forod.

Basil sent you to meet with several spies he has among the tomb-robber camp on the isle of Rantost.Talk to Eliot Bencroft at Rantost'We have now both honoured our sides of the pact, after ignoring it so long. It feels good to have that relationship restored. I hope that in the future we can build and make it grow and flourish.

'I am prepared to take a large step towards that. I know where the tomb-robbers make their primary camp. It is a small island at the north end of the lake called Rantost. Many of the relics they have pilfered are kept there until they can find buyers for them. I imagine the history they are keeping there is immense and invaluable to the Rangers.

'Months ago, I sent three of my men to join the tomb-robbers. They are now on the isle of Rantost, still working for me. I am now willing to use them and have them expose themselves and challenge Rantost for the Rangers. Seek them out, and they will tell you what to do next.''I'm doing nothing suspicious, just standing around waiting for the next boat. Wait, what's your name? Who sent you? Basil, you say? Then it is time we got to work.''If Evendim is to be restored to glory, the tomb-robbers must be stopped.'The Even-rills are a series of pools and waterfalls through which meltwater from Forochel runs before entering Lake Evendim.The pool is at the peak of the Even-rills, north-east of the Eavespires.

Erchiel asked you to venture to the topmost pool of the Even-rills and pour some Ent-tears within it to purify the waters.Erchiel is at the Eavespires, south-west of the Even-rills.

Erchiel will be pleased to hear the tears have purified the water.Talk to Erchiel at the Eavespires'It used to be a rare sight to see Longbough weep. In the many years I have been here with him, it happened once, maybe twice, per year... usually when a sapling he knew got snapped in a storm.

'Over these past few months, it has happened more frequently. The pain Evendim is feeling is slowly killing him. While these tears are created from pain and evil, they are a great force for life and good.

'Take this vial... it contains a few tears which I gathered last week. Pour them into the pool at the top of the Even-rills. The waters will be purified and restored.''I do not know how the tears can hold this much virtue, but much about our friend here is a mystery.''The water glowed lightly, then felt cool against your legs? I believe that means it worked and whatever damage may have been done by the Gauredain should fade from the lake.'The isle of Rantost is where the tomb-robbers have made their central camp. A great deal of history is being kept there.There are several things to be done around Rantost to disturb the tomb-robbers operations.Aid Eliot Bencroft in RantostAid Leighton Kipps in RantostAid Wal Simpkins in RantostEliot Bencroft is at the south-east corner of Rantost.

Eliot Bencroft will want to hear that Rantost has been weakened to the point of being open to a larger assault.Talk to Eliot Bencroft at Rantost'The tomb-robbers are far more organized than we have previously thought, and Rantost is the hive of their villainy. Everything they plunder from the tombs and crypts of Evendim comes through here.

'We have been watching for a while, and each of us comes up with a way to hinder their efforts. If we can curtail them enough, we may allow the Rangers an opportunity to strike. This would let them end the tomb-robbers, recover their relics, and strengthen the restored friendship between Ost Forod and Tinnudir.

'Speak with my associates here for what we feel needs to be done. The list is not long, but it should make a heavy impact.''Chaos reigns within the camp. It seems the time is ripe to launch the true offensive.''Once we have the tomb-robbers rattled, we will be able to signal the Rangers to come with a larger force.'The discovery of the cave-trolls near Thorenhad and the Shadow-wolf elder has brought great concern to Narlinn and Fimgris.Elladan and Elrohir are at Thorenhad, east and north of Narlinn's camp. The ruins may be found by following the road eastward to the white marker stone and taking the northward path to the bluff.

Narlinn has asked you to bring news of the trolls and the Shadow-wolf to Elladan and Elrohir, the sons of Elrond.'The sons of Elrond must know of your discoveries here in the Bruinen Gorges, for the threat both creatures present cannot be ignored. The servants of the Enemy are encamped upon our doorstep!

'Alas, neither Fimgris nor I may leave our post here. Will you bring word of these evils to Elladan and Elrohir? They are encamped in the ruins of Thorenhad. Just follow the road east to the white marker stone, then take the northern path until you come to Thorenhad. The ruins are set atop the bluff overlooking the bear-den.''Narlinn was right to send you to us. The evils you describe cannot be allowed to remain upon the threshold of Imladris. Elladan and I shall see that word comes to our father.

'For now, we have some tasks with which you may aid us....''Narlinn was right to send you to us. The evils you describe cannot be allowed to remain upon the threshold of Imladris. Elrohir and I shall see that word comes to our father.

'For now, we have some tasks with which you may aid us....'Tomb-robbers are threatening the peace of Evendim, despoiling the ancient sites of the Dúnedain.Tomb-robbers have established a camp on Rantost, an island north of Tinnudir on Lake Nenuial.

Eliot Bencroft wants you to defeat a few tomb-robbers.Eliot Bencroft is at the south-east corner of Rantost.

Eliot Bencroft will be pleased to hear the island has been thinned.Talk to Eliot Bencroft on Rantost'I have been monitoring the patterns of the tomb-robbers here. When they come, when they go, who is here and when. There are patterns in everything. In Rantost, the patterns run deep. 

