Erchiel will want to know the first tasks are complete.'The men from the north, who dress like wolves, are not like the Rangers from the east. They worship the land, but then use it to create evil and darkness. They are a foul breed of Man, one I do not trust.

'They have begun coming further south, even to the edges of this grove. This causes me great worry.''With those things done, it is now time to draw the line.''Men dressed as wolves defiling the forest...'After learning that Arrod's bird was, in fact, alive -- though wounded -- you returned to Arrod, bringing Caledhroval with you.The troll-cave lies to the north-east of Arrod's camp.

Arrod asked you to scout the entrance to the troll-cave, which Caledhroval discovered, and and see what you can learn about their strength.Scout the troll-cave in the Bruinen GorgesThe hendroval can be found near the entrance to the troll-cave in the Bruinen Gorges, north-east of Arrod's camp.

You should deal with the hendroval before it can warn the trolls.Defeat the spying hendroval'As I tended Caledhroval's wounds, he told me of what he learned upon his patrol. The situation is more dire than it seems.

'That trolls have begun to come down from the Misty Mountains has long been known, but we thought it only a few. However, it appears that there is an entire cave of them not too far from here. After spotting the cave, Caledhroval thought to warn Elladan and Elrohir, but was intercepted by the hendroval... apparently an agent of the trolls.

'Unfortunately, Caledhroval is not clear about the enemy's number. Would you scout the cave entrance and learn what the strength of the trolls' number is? The cave lies to the north-east. I shall await your return.'Remmenylf has suggested a solution to Erchiel regarding the Gauredain that seems rather less violent than other possible approaches.Remmenylf has asked you to steal a number of the wards that are scattered around the Gauradan-encampments.

The Gauradan-encampments are north of the Eavespires.Gather Gauradan-wards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Remmenylf is at the Eavespires, south of the Gauradan-encampments.

You should bring the Gauradan-wards you collected to Remmenylf.'I have devised a plan to deal with the Gauredain and have proposed it to Erchiel. She agrees on this course of action.

'As for this plan, we -- and by that, I am afraid I mean you -- shall steal several of the wards that the Gauredain have scattered about their encampments. These wards are simple tribal symbols, commonly used to keep evil spirits at bay by superstitious cultures. That is not to say that such spirits do not occasionally roam the world in one form or another -- but I am afraid a simple chunk of wood would do little to deter them.

'In any case, I need you to gather several of these and bring them to me, then we can embark on the rather more clever part of this plan.''Bring me the wards of the Gauredain.''Good, you have done exactly as I asked. I hope the Gauredain were not too much trouble?

'In any case, now we have what we need to begin setting our final plan into motion, which Erchiel will describe to you....'The Even-rills are a series of pools and waterfalls that meltwater from Forochel runs through before entering the lake of Evendim.The Even-rills are north-east of the Eavespires.

Lithuifin asked you to head to the Even-rills and defeat the Gauredain there.Defeat Gauredain at the Even-rills (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lithuifin is at the Eavespires, south-west of the Even-rills.

Lithuifin will want to hear the Guaredain have been driven out of the Even-rills.Talk to Lithuifin at the Eavespires'So, Longbough has sensed that the Even-rills are threatened? He has never been wrong, so even though I have not seen what he feels, I trust this threat to be real.

'The enemy is likely the Gauredain, Men from the North, the cold wastes of Forochel. They dabble in dark alchemy and evil magic, things that turn nature into abominations.

'Clear out the camp they have at the Even-rills. If even a few remain, then more will come.''The Even-rills supply all the water this lake holds. If they are made foul, the entire lake will become fouled as well.''So, as you defeated the Gauredain, they began to scatter and flee? Good! They will think twice before returning to that place.'The Elf-scouts Narlinn and Fimgris sent you to warn the sons of Elrond of impending danger to Rivendell, and they in turn recruited you to their service.Pothlorn was scouting the path which leads north and east through the Gorges to Ost Thondol.

Elladan asked you to search for the missing Elf-scout, Pothlorn, and learn whether or not he still lives.Find Pothlorn'${PLAYER}, the agitation of the wolves was not new to us, though the cause of their madness was certainly unknown until you came. Indeed, we sent another of our Elves, Pothlorn, to scout the path to the ruins of Ost Thondol. Wolves were seen in that direction as well, and we wished to know how widespread their roaming had become. Alas, we have had no word from Pothlorn.

'Would you search for Pothlorn along that path and learn if he still lives? It may be that some ill has befallen him... and even then, we wish to know of his fate.

'That path begins just to the east and travels into the northern Gorges, swinging eastward away from Nan Tornaeth.''Ah, a ${RACE}... it is well for me that you have come, but perhaps not for yourself. This place is unsafe....'You discovered that the trolls encamped in the nearby cave are not Stone-trolls, but Cave-trolls...a much greater threat.Narlinn is at her encampment, west along the main road from Arrod's camp.

Arrod bade you take word of your discovery within the troll-cave to Narlinn.Talk to Narlinn'Elladan and Elrohir must be warned of your discovery; however, they are well-guarded at Thorenhad. I am more immediately concerned with Narlinn and Fimgris, who are encamped on the road, without any defence against such creatures.

'Return to Narlinn with due haste and tell her of your discovery. She will decide whether to return herself to Thorenhad or send you in her stead. To reach her encampment, return to the main road and head west.''I am relieved that Arrod is well and that Caledhroval has been recovered, but the tidings you bring are dire. Cave-trolls? In the Bruinen Gorges?

'I shall have to consider our best course....'You found a rune-marked collar upon one of the bears and were nearly overcome with a chilling sensation.The source of the chill seems to come from the south-west part of Nan Tornaeth.

You should investigate the source of the chilling sensation.Investigate the source of the chilling sensationThe source of the chill seems to come from the south-west part of Nan Tornaeth, not far from Calenthon's camp.

You should investigate the source of the chilling sensation.Investigate the source of the chilling sensationThe bear-wight is laired in the south-west part of Nan Tornaeth, not far from Calenthon's camp.

You should defeat the bear-wight, perhaps freeing the other bears from its madness.Defeat the bear-wightCalenthon is at his camp in Nan Tornaeth, north-east from the bear-wight's lair.

You should return to Calenthon and tell him of your victory over the bear-wight.The source of the chill seems to come from the south-west part of Nan Tornaeth.

You should investigate the source of the chilling sensation.'I cannot say that I am surprised, given your previous encounters, that you found a wight behind the madness of the bears; however, we are no closer to learning what power is behind the raising of these foul wights.

'I should not say that we are not any closer, for these runes upon the collar are in a mode once used in the kingdom of Rhudaur. The Corcur, a remnant from the old kingdom who took refuge in Angmar long ago, have returned and have established an encampment in the ruins above. They seek to reclaim Rhudaur and make it a great power once more, but they have become little more than wild men... I cannot see how they could have the power to raise wights.

'Nevertheless, I sent my companion, Malloval, to scout their encampment, but he has not returned....'Many scouts were dispatched across the Trollshaws to keep watch for signs of evil, and the sons of Elrond want to know if anything has been found.Worms can be found in Nan Tornaeth on the path to Calenthon's camp, which can be reached by following the northward path to Ost Thondol and taking the north-west trail at the first fork. Elrohir said to look for the white marker stone at the head of the path.

Elrohir suggested you defeat a number of worms on your way to speak with Calenthon, hoping you might find some clue as to the identity of the evil which has stirred them to madness.Defeat worms in Nan Tornaeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Seek the white stone marking the correct trailCalenthon is at his camp, which can be reached by following the northward path to Ost Thondol and taking the north-west trail at the fork.

Elrohir suggested you enlist the aid of Calenthon in finding the evil which has stirred up the worms of Nan Tornaeth.Talk to Calenthon'Elladan is right. Nan Tornaeth is the most logical place to begin searching for the master of the worm-wight. Many worms dwell in those Gorges. I sent Calenthon and Malloval to scout Nan Tornaeth... they may be able to help you discover the source of this evil.

'Calenthon's encampment can be reached by taking the path that leads to Ost Thondol; however, when you reach the first fork, take the north-west path instead. Look for the white marker stone at the head of the path.

'Along the way, you might want to dispose of some of the worms... you might find some evidence of the evil which has stirred them to unrest.''You have come from Thorenhad? I would have sent word to Elrohir, but I do not yet understand the nature of the evil I have discovered here. Will you lend me your aid?'The dark cloud over the western shores of Lake Evendim has been lifted and Longbough's spirits are high.Orchalwë is at Tinnudir.

Orchalwë will be pleased to hear the western shores of Evendim are safe.Talk to Orchalwë at Tinnudir'Hoom, it seems you are more like the Men who wear green than the tall Elves or wolf-wearing ones. I like the ones who wear green. They are my friends.

'Let the Rangers know that I am no longer tired. I am full of energy and will not rest until the west of their lake is filled with peaceful nature again.''Ents are very curious creatures indeed...so ancient, yet we know so little. I am glad you had the pleasure of not only meeting Longbough, but of aiding him. In the dark times to come, the Ents could prove to be very valuable allies.

'Now, it is time to turn our attention to the south and the city of my ancestors.''Hoom, another little one as a friend. More conversations like this, and I may forget how to speak treeish....'Lithuifin the Elf is concerned with the giants which have been ruining the forest.The encampment of the giants is at Amon Môth, south and west of the Eavespires.

Lithuifin has asked you to pour his draught into the giants' stew.Lithuifin is at the Eavespires, north and east of Amon Môth.

You should return to Lithuifin with your report.Talk to Lithuifin at the Eavespires'The giants tend to gather each day for a large meal somewhere near the southern end of their encampment where they have placed an enormous stew-pot.

'Your goal is simplicity itself -- make your way quietly to the pot in their midst and slip this into their meal, then escape before you are stepped on.

'If you can manage to stay nearby, you may find the events to follow amusing.''They have long believed these woods to be haunted, and now I believe they will take this opportunity to leave them.''This meal should be memorable to the giants....'The camp within the Way of Kings is watching over the tombs of the Rangers' ancestral rulers.Nimbellas is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings, south of Tinnudir.Talk to Nimbellas at the Way of Kings camp'You have done much for us, and it feels unfair to ask for more, but I must. The tomb-robbers we drove from Rantost fled to the south and are now threatening our hold within the Way of Kings. The Way of Kings is where the ancient rulers of my people are buried. Those that watched over Annúminas and Evendim from on high now sleep below. Their memories are to be cherished and thought of often, but their tombs are not to be disturbed.

'I have also heard rumours and whispers of another force amongst the ruins. I believe you have encountered them already within the estates to the east of here. I fear we have little time to determine their motives and defeat them before it will be too late.

'Head south to the Way of Kings and meet up with Nimbellas at his camp and see what you can do to help.''There is much work to be done, and if we are to succeed, it must be done quickly.''Go south and see what aid you can provide.'Your tale of evil wolves and worm-wights reminded Calenthon strongly of the madness of the bears in Nan Tornaeth.Maddened bears stalk the passes and valleys of Nan Tornaeth, especially to the south and south-west.

Calenthon asked you to hunt the maddened bears of Nan Tornaeth and search them for clues which might reveal the source of their madness.Hunt the bears of Nan Tornaeth for clues to the source of their madnessYou have found a rune-marked collar amongst the maddened bears.Completed'The tale you tell of the wolves at Drauglad and in the Bruinen Gorges reminds me much of the madness I have seen among the bears here in Nan Tornaeth. Perhaps you encountered some of the beasts as you journeyed here?

'Hunt the mad bears of these hills and see if you can find any clues as to the cause of their madness...though I have little doubt the source is related to the evil which called forth the creatures you encountered before. There are many bears to the south and south-west. I would start there.'As you examine the collar, you are nearly overwhelmed by a chilling sensation which seems to emanate from the south-west part of Nan Tornaeth, not far from Calenthon's camp.The giants camping on the western shores of the lake are new to Evendim.The Elves have ideas on how to help ease Longbough's pain.Aid Erchiel at Amon MôthAid Lithuifin at Amon MôthAid Remmenylf at Amon MôthLithuifin is at the Eavespires.

Lithuifin has a plan to drive off the giants for good.Talk to Lithuifin at the Eavespires'Hoom-hom... the men dressed in wolf-skins are of no concern anymore, so says the silky-haired ones. I believe them, hoom. The trees of the mountain they are atop no longer call to me... they have returned to slumber.

'The trees to the south, though, hom, scream out in agony. They call for help. Big men, giant men, nearly as tall as Longbough, hoom, rip the trees from the ground. I can feel their agony.''Men in green, Elf-folk, Men dressed as wolves, giant Men... there are nearly as many types of Man as there are trees.''All of the preparations are ready. Now, we drive them off for good.'Servants of the Enemy pursued Frodo Baggins to the Bruinen, and though the hobbit and his friends were saved and the fell creatures defeated by the power of Elrond, not all of the Nazgûl have been accounted for.Elladan is at his camp of Thorenhad on the north-western slope of the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear-dens.

Lord Elrond has asked you to lend your assistance to his sons Elladan and Elrohir, currently seeking the missing Nazgûl.'Welcome to Imladris, ${PLAYER}. It is good that you have come. Rest well, but not too deeply or too long! We have need of adventuring folk, for there is evil beyond the vale.

'Not more than two months ago, a hobbit by the name of Frodo Baggins and his companions were pursued to the Ford of Bruinen by servants of the Enemy. I speak of the Nine, the Nazgûl, fell creatures in the service of Sauron, and though the Bruinen fell upon them at my command, we have found the steeds of only eight. One of the Riders is unaccounted for.

'My sons set forth with scouts bound to them by friendship to seek this missing Rider. I ask that you speak with Elladan at their camp of Thorenhad, among the Bruinen Gorges, and lend your aid to the search. We must learn where this Nazgûl has gone, and most importantly, his designs.''My sons have established a camp, Thorenhad, on the northern reaches of the Bruinen Gorges. Seek them north of the bear-dens and lend your assistance to Elladan in this matter.''My father has sent you to aid us? It is good that you have come, for we have made an unsettling discovery. It seems likely the missing Rider is still somewhere within the wilderness of the Trollshaws.'Elladan was pleased that you found the horse of the missing Rider, but will not be satisfied until he knows its master's fate.Lord Glorfindel can be found in Imladris, far to the east of Thorenhad, contemplating the waterfalls by the Last Homely House.

Elladan has asked you to consult with the Elf-lord Glorfindel about the missing Rider.The Ford of Bruinen is to the west of Imladris, at the bottom of the steeply-climbing slopes.

Lord Glorfindel has given you a beryl and has asked you to test its powers by holding it aloft on the banks of the Bruinen.Lord Glorfindel is in Imladris, high above the Bruinen and to the east, by the waterfall outside the Last Homely House.

Glorfindel is waiting to speak with you upon your return from the Ford of Bruinen.'We know more than we did, ${PLAYER}, but we do not yet know what we must, for the safety of all those who live or journey in this region: the whereabouts of the missing Nazgûl. His steed was our greatest ally in this search, for while he could remove his cloak and remain nearly unseen, his horse was a mortal creature and its physical trail could be followed. With the creature now dead, either from exhaustion or at his master's hand, our ability to track the Nazgûl is lessened.

'Lessened but not gone, perhaps. I would ask you to return to Imladris and to consult with Lord Glorfindel, for he is accounted very wise and may have some strategem we have not yet tested. He keeps close counsel with my father and with Mithrandir, and often contemplates near the falling water by my father's house.

'He may be able to help us find this missing Nazgûl.''Look for Glorfindel in Imladris, near the waterfalls by my father's house. He is often wont to contemplate the falling water and is counted among the Wise.''You are welcome to Imladris, ${PLAYER}. These are times of trouble, but for now, at least, the curtain of shadow is held back and we meet in peace.

'You bring grievous tidings from Elladan, but they are not entirely unlooked-for. I feared that not all of the Nazgûl were claimed by the Bruinen. This stray servant of the Enemy will leave a mark on the wilderness -- he may have already done so -- and we can use it to track him.

'I give you my beryl, and ask you to hold it aloft at the Ford of Bruinen. Return to me once you have done so, and we will speak further.''The Ford of Bruinen is to the west of Imladris, at the bottom of steeply-sloping hills. It is where the Nazgûl were halted by Lord Elrond's power of command over those waters, and it is where you must hold aloft the beryl I gave you.

'We shall speak more upon your return.''You have returned, ${PLAYER}. Did you notice any change in the beryl I gave you when you arrived at the Ford?

'The beryl began to glow? That is what I expected, and I am glad it was so for it shall be our means of locating the Nazgûl that remains hidden within the wilderness.

'The Nine, servants of the Enemy and shadows beneath his greater shadow, are creatures of such evil that the land cannot bear their presence. This beryl will glow in places where they have been. It will allow us to follow the missing Rider's trail.'Lord Glorfindel gave you a beryl which glows when it is brought into places where great evil has left its mark.Elladan is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear-dens.

Lord Glorfindel has sent you back to Elladan with a beryl, an Elf-stone that glows when it comes near places on which great evil has left its mark.'I do not often travel into the wild, though I will do so when the need is great, as the Ranger Aragorn or his small friend Frodo Baggins could tell you. The sons of Elrond are better-suited for directing your search for the missing Nazgûl.

'I leave my beryl in your care for the time being and ask you to return with it to Elladan at his camp of Thorenhad. He will know where you should bring it to follow the traces of the Nazgûl.

'Go with speed and with clarity of vision! The beryl will help you to find this stray servant of the Enemy, but what will you do when you find him, I wonder?''Elladan's camp of Thorenhad is located among the Bruinen Gorges, west of Imladris and north of the bear-dens. Bring him the beryl and my good wishes, and I hope that each will give the sons of Elrond what they need to seek out this evil.''The words of Lord Glorfindel are most wise, and his gift of this beryl brings me hope that we may be able to regain the trail of this missing Nazgûl. You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, but now I must determine where we are to bring the beryl in order to reveal the Nazgûl's location!'Aragorn has asked that you speak with Elrond concerning a matter of gravest import for Rivendell.Elrond waits in the library on the upper floor of his house.

Aragorn asked that you present yourself to Elrond, the master of the Last Homely House.'Welcome to Rivendell, where you will find the Last Homely House east of the Sea, ${PLAYER}. The road to Imladris is not as forgiving as once it was, and I commend you for your efforts.

'I hope the waters of the Ford have calmed since our passage; we left them in turmoil. I fear the cause of these troubles is not yet concluded.

'Lord Elrond is the master of the house here; he should be given news of your arrival. You will find him in his library on the upper floor of the Last Homely House, to the north-east.''Elrond will be most interested to hear of your journey, ${PLAYER}. Speak to him in his library on the upper floor of his house, to the north-east.''The path you took to my doorstep has been perilous, ${PLAYER}, and its dangers all too common in these dark days. If you will consent to lend us your aid, it will not be the least of your challenges.'Complete additional quests within the Trollshaws.Complete quests within the TrollshawsThe Elves at Thorenhad desire a delivery of ridged finger-bones to be delivered to them.You have accepted a task to collect ridged finger-bones from the Dead in the areas surrounding Thorenhad. The items are to be delivered to the collection box at the outpost.Wanted: Ridged finger-bones from the Dead surrounding Thorenhad. All items should be delivered to the collection box at the outpost in the Trollshaws.Wanted: Ridged finger-bones from the Dead surrounding Thorenhad.The Elves at Thorenhad thank you for your efforts.The Elves at Thorenhad desire a delivery of silky filth to be made to them.You have accepted a task to collect silky filth from the spiders in the areas surrounding Thorenhad. The items are to be delivered to a collection box. There is a collection box at Thorenhad in the Trollshaws.Wanted: Silky filth from the spiders surrounding Thorenhad. The items are to be delivered to a collection box. There is a collection box at Thorenhad in the Trollshaws.Wanted: Silky filth from the spiders surrounding Thorenhad.The Elves at Thorenhad thank you for your efforts.Remmenylf the Elf is concerned with the giants which have been ruining the forest.The stone-giant chieftain is at Amon Môth, south and west of the Eavespires.

Remmenylf has asked you to defeat the stone-giant chieftain of Amon Môth.Defeat the stone-giant chieftainRemmenylf resides in the Eavespires, east and north of Amon Môth.

You should return to Remmenylf and tell him of the chieftain's defeat.Talk to Remmenylf at the Eavespires'I fear things have gone awry and taken a rather dangerous turn. It seems that a stone-giant of some actual cunning and intelligence has arisen to leadership among the giants of Amon Môth, and I cannot ignore such an ominous portent.

'Giants are very powerful creatures and dangerous at the best of times, but they are fractious and chaotic, and it is quite rare for a strong leader to arise among them. The consequences of such are usually disastrous, for few forces can stand against an organized war-band of giants. Even Erchiel and Longbough would likely find themselves overmatched, should it come to that.

'In this instance, I am afraid this newly arisen leader must not be allowed to strengthen his control over the giants, or they might easily overwhelm these forests. Alas, it is not within my power to defeat him, and Erchiel and Lithuifin must stand guard over the Eavespires... might you defeat him for me?''It is time for these giants' chieftain to fall....''That was well done! Please forgive me for asking such of you. Erchiel and Lithuifin have striven for many years to avoid the conflict and strife of the world at large, but in these years, it presses ever closer, and I fear that they may find themselves called away to fight in yet another war.

'Erchiel has already fought her share, ${PLAYER}. I have seen it in her face as the dreams of ages past intrude upon her slumber and crease her beautiful brow with worry and care. I have seen the ancient fire alight in her eyes when it seems that danger may be upon us yet again.

'I would have her see no more of those dreams, if it lies within my power, and I thank you greatly for your aid. May the world show you kindness in your travels.'Ferrod has asked you to bring his greetings to the Elves staying at Eavespires.Eavespires is on the opposite side of Lake Nenuial from Tinnudir; you were told to cross the Even-rills at the northernmost tip of the lake and continue to follow the shore as it curves westward, until you arrive at a stream that feeds into the lake.

Ferrod has asked you to bring his greetings to the Elves currently staying at Eavespires.'Are you thinking of travelling to the far side of the lake, ${PLAYER}? That is a long journey!

'If your travels take you to the far side of Nenuial, I ask that you bring my greetings to any Elves that stay at Eavespires -- I heard that some of that kindred have come to the glade, and I wish them to be welcome in Evendim.

'Cross to the mainland, and follow the shore of the lake in a great loop north and then west. You will cross the Even-rills at the northern tip of the lake; continue to follow the lake shore until you see a stream that feeds into Nenuial. Near that place you will find Eavespires. You will find Elves there, and even greater mysteries, if the stories are to be believed.''Hello, friend. My name is Lithuifin, and it is my pleasure to welcome you to Eavespires. I return Ferrod's greetings with good cheer, and hope you will find comfort and safety at the end of your road!''Hail, ${PLAYER}. I return Ferrod's welcome to these lands with my own, for Elves passed through this place even before his oldest ancestors! But I am glad to see you on this side of Nenuial, and I hope you will not find sorrow in these lands.'Lithuifin the Elf is concerned with the giants which have been ruining the forest.The berries can be found south of the Eavespires and east of Amon Môth.

Lithuifin has asked you to collect some colourful berries and bring them to him.Collect colourful berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lithuifin resides at the Eavespires, east and north of Amon Môth, along the shoreline of Lake Evendim.

You should bring the berries you collected to Lithuifin.'I must beg your pardon, for we have forgotten to mention how we keep the giants convinced that this forest is haunted. It is easier than you might assume.

'I need you to collect some berries from the bushes that grow in this part of the forest -- they are quite sweet, but I suggest that you not sample them, lest you find yourself led far astray by their effects. The taste may be flavourful, but they are more intoxicating than the stoutest of dwarf-ales.

'Bring me several handfuls, and I will prepare a fine treat for the giants. They can be found south of the Eavespires and east of Amon Môth.''You were unable to find the berries? They grew quite plentifully in the forests just a short distance south of here.''These seem fresh and vibrant and should do quite nicely. Allow me a few minutes to prepare a batch. Giants have a constitution to match their great size, and this is one of the few draughts that can have any real effect on them.

'Just wait and you shall see what I mean!'Longbough believes that some evil power may be twisting the wood to dark ends, perhaps the Wood-trolls that have begun to appear in Evendim. Roused to anger, the Ent is ready to take action.The Twisted Grove lies to the south-west of the Eavespires.

Angered by the wanton ruin inflicted upon his grove, Longbough has asked you to defeat the wood-trolls infesting the Twisted Grove.Defeat Barkskin wood-trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Rotting wood-trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Heart-rot is at the Twisted Grove, which lies south-west of the Eavespires.

As well as driving the wood-trolls from his grove, Erchiel also asked you to find and defeat their leader, Heart-rot, in hopes that the remnant will flee.Find and defeat Heart-rotErchiel is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim.

You should return to the Eavespires and tell Erchiel of your battle with Heart-rot.'Something seems to be amiss on the edge of the forest, well to the south of here. A party of wood-trolls -- led by one called 'Heart-rot' -- has dwelled there for some time, but now their power seems to be growing and threatens to twist the forest around them to evil and hatred.

'Seek out these trolls and winnow their numbers. If you can slay enough of them, then Heart-rot should be driven to confront you, and you may destroy him, thus removing the source of this trouble.''Have you been to the Twisted Grove yet? It fills me with a foreboding I have not known for many years.''Unfortunately, it seems that there is more to this Heart-rot than we had first imagined. Whatever power lies in the Twisted Grove, its roots run deeper than we had suspected.'Longbough has joined you in the battle to destroy both Heart-rot and the Huorn known as the Twisted Heart.You should speak with Longbough and aid him against the Twisted Heart.Speak with LongboughYou should speak with Longbough.'Well fought, Little One! Hoom! The Twisted Heart has been uprooted, and Heart-rot destroyed. Their corruption will spread no further.''Eventually this grove will return to what it was, but the healing shall take time.

Let us be quit of this dark place, shall we?''Ta-rum! We have much work to do here. Follow me!'During your rescue of Malloval, you discovered that the Corcur are in league with wights, but learned nothing else.Hillmen of Rhudaur may be found throughout the ruins of Nan Tornaeth, especially across the bridge of Thoriant.

The Hillmen of Rhudaur have some foul connexion to the wights that stalk the ruins of Nan Tornaeth, and you should search among them for some token which might reveal their mutual master.Collect a token from the Hillmen of RhudaurHillmen of Rhudaur may be found throughout the ruins of Nan Tornaeth, especially across the bridge of Thoriant.

The Hillmen of Rhudaur have some foul connexion to the wights that stalk the ruins of Nan Tornaeth, and you should search among them for some token which might reveal their mutual master.Collect a token from the Hillmen of RhudaurYou found the emblem of the gaunt-man Gúrdring and should hunt for the evil creature before his power becomes too great.Hillmen of Rhudaur may be found throughout the ruins of Nan Tornaeth, especially across the bridge of Thoriant.

The Hillmen of Rhudaur have some foul connexion to the wights that stalk the ruins of Nan Tornaeth, and you should search among them for some token which might reveal their mutual master.This emblem bears markings belonging to a gaunt-man named Gúrdring. The vile creature must be found and destroyed.Erchiel the Elf is concerned with the giants which have been ruining the forest.Amon Môth is located to the west and south of the Eavespires, and the cairn Erchiel mentioned is somewhere on the northern outskirts of their camp.

Erchiel has asked you to prove your cunning by stealing a lucky stone from one of the giants of Amon Môth.Steal a lucky stoneErchiel can be found at the Eavespires, east and north of Amon Môth, near the shoreline of Lake Evendim.

You should bring the lucky stone back to Erchiel.'There is a band of Hill-giants who have taken up residence at the western edge of the forest. Nasty brutes they are and taken to smashing trees and tromping the undergrowth in such a fashion that it makes Longbough's knots itch just to consider it.

'Now, I myself prefer battles of trickery to those of the blade when dealing with fellows thrice my height and one-tenth my wit, and so I suggest this plan to you: for some years now I have instilled a fear of wood-spirits and sprites in the giants -- nay, there are none such, at least not hereabouts, but the giants do not know that. Flickering lights in the distant woods, the unexplained disappearance of important things, strange and unearthly sounds -- all the sort of things you might use to scare children and keep them from wandering into a dangerous wood. The giants are little wiser than children themselves and much the same ploy keeps them out of this forest... usually.

'The giants have been growing bolder again of late -- perhaps you could... raise the spirits once more? I happen to know that one of the giants that guards the outskirts of their encampment has a cherished lucky stone he keeps near his person -- a rock of no true value, I would wager. See if you can snatch it away when his attention is elsewhere. There is a small rock cairn I left nearby to help provide a means of distraction. Be sure to move quickly and stay unnoticed, or you will likely be stepped on.''No luck yet?

'As I recall, the giant in question stands guard near the northern outskirts of Amon Môth. There should be a small cairn of stones nearby to mark the place.

'Do be careful. The giants are not terribly bright, but they are quite strong.''You have returned and with the giant's keepsake no less! Well done, indeed.

'Now that you have proven yourself up to the task, I have a somewhat more complicated duty for you.'Tham Laegamon is a ruin that overlooks the Way of Kings and the entrance to the city of Annúminas.Tham Laegamon is to the south-west of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam asked you to venture to Tham Laegamon and gather longbows from the tomb-robbers there.Collect longbows from Tham Laegamon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rodlam is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam will want to see the longbows you collected from Tham Laegamon.'Like the tomb-robbers in Tham Sarch, those camping in Tham Laegamon are also alerting Angmar to our activities, but in a different manner.

'These have longbows with which they fire burning arrows at us. That allows them to track us in the night and eliminates stealth as a tactic for us, thus it has caused us many difficulties.

'I would like you to take the longbows from them. If we cannot freely move throughout the Way of Kings, we cannot proceed... and we must proceed.''If we can at least move around during the night, we can begin to make some progress in the Way of Kings.''Now we can burn these and give the Enemy a fire to watch for a night.'You found an emblem the like of which you have only seen once...in Agamaur, upon the Gaunt-lord Ivar.The gaunt-man Gúrdring is likely encamped in the deepest parts of Nan Tornaeth's ruins.

You found the emblem of the gaunt-man Gúrdring and should hunt for the evil creature before his power becomes too great.Defeat GúrdringThe gaunt-man Gúrdring is likely encamped in the deepest parts of Nan Tornaeth's ruins.

You found the emblem of the gaunt-man Gúrdring and should hunt for the evil creature before his power becomes too great.Defeat GúrdringDefeat wights in Nan Tornaeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Calenthon is within Nan Tornaeth, far to the west of Ost Brandras.

Calenthon will be pleased to know that you have slain the gaunt-man Gúrdring.Talk to CalenthonThe gaunt-man Gúrdring is likely encamped in the deepest parts of Nan Tornaeth's ruins.

You found the emblem of the gaunt-man Gúrdring and should hunt for the evil creature before his power becomes too great.'A gaunt-man, you say? It is well that Gúrdring was defeated, and the wights he commanded pushed back. Just such an evil as that might have posed a true threat to Rivendell.

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'Tham Sarch is an ancient ruin that overlooks Lake Evendim from the hills above the southern shore.Mirrors can be found on tomb-robbers at Tham Sarch, north-east of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir asked you to recover mirrors from the tomb-robbers in Tham Sarch.Collect mirrors from tomb-robbers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nethrandir is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir will want to examine the mirrors you collected.'Tham Sarch has not been a site of much importance before this week. Earlier in the week, the tomb-robbers occupied it and began looting it. While the looting angers me, they are presenting a larger issue which we must deal with.

'Whenever we move, I see glints of light from the hillside. We know the Angmarim and the tomb-robbers have an accord, so they must be signalling them as to our actions.

'This is something we cannot allow to continue. We must hinder their ability to signal each other about our every move. Head to Tham Sarch and collect the mirrors the tomb-robbers there are using to alert the Angmarim.''If we do not remove their ability to signal the Angmarim, we may as well return to Tinnudir.''These are exactly what I expected. They may look small to you, but catch the glint of the sun just right, and you can signal someone from a great distance.'Stone-trolls have moved into Nan Tornaeth, settling in the ruins high above.There are Stone-trolls encamped at the ruins of Barad Glamgil in Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws.

While in Nan Tornaeth, you should drive out the Stone-trolls which have settled there.Defeat Stone-trolls in Nan Tornaeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are Stone-trolls encamped at the ruins of Barad Glamgil in Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws.

While in Nan Tornaeth, you should drive out the Stone-trolls which have settled there.The maddened bears of Nan Tornaeth are beyond hope, thanks to the wights which have risen in the hills.There are bears dwelling in Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws.

While in Nan Tornaeth, you should put down the maddened bears which dwell there, ending their suffering.Defeat bears in Nan Tornaeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are bears dwelling in Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws.

While in Nan Tornaeth, you should put down the maddened bears which dwell there, ending their suffering.You discovered the presence of a gaunt-man within the ruins of Nan Tornaeth and dispatched it, securing the northern reaches of the Trollshaws.Elrohir is at Thorenhad, which can be reached by following the trail east and south from Calenthon's camp.

Calenthon suggested that you bring a report to Elrohir at Thorenhad.Talk to Elrohir'You should return to Thorenhad and tell Elrohir of your discoveries -- and victories -- here in Nan Tornaeth. Though you have laid to rest the greatest threat, there is much to do here, and I deem Elrohir may wish to send more Elves to my aid.

'You need but return down the trail east and south. Farewell, ${PLAYER}.''You found and defeated a gaunt-man in Nan Tornaeth? I am concerned that such a creature could pass so close to Imladris without being detected. Nevertheless, you deserve our thanks for ridding the world of its presence.

'My father will need to know of this....'Tham Laegamon is a ruin that overlooks the Way of Kings and the entrance to the city of Annúminas.Tham Laegamon is to the south-west of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam asked you to venture to Tham Laegamon and defeat the tomb-robbers there.Defeat tomb-robbers at Tham Laegamon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rodlam is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam will be pleased to hear the tomb-robbers at Tham Laegamon have been defeated.Talk to Rodlam'Up on the hill above us, if you travel to the west, you will find the ruins of Tham Laegamon. This was the rulers' retreat during the days of the North Kingdom. They would go there, stare down upon their city, the lake, and their ancestors and ponder the future.

'Now, a foul presence occupies the ruins, and while they look down upon all the same things, their purpose is dark and evil. Tomb-robbers have come to fill those ruins. They are ransacking more from it each and every day.

'The robbers must be stopped. There are not many more beyond these few here in the hills. If we draw the final line here, I believe Evendim may have a future free of them.''There are a few more within the Way of Kings itself, but hopefully we shall soon be rid of the tomb-robbers entirely.''I thought we had won the day when you drove the robbers from Rantost, yet it seems the battle is not quite over.'Tham Sarch is an ancient ruin that overlooks Lake Evendim from the hills above the southern shore.Tham Sarch is in the hills south-west of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir asked you to venture to Tham Sarch and defeat the tomb-robbers you find there.Defeat tomb-robbers at Tham Sarch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nethrandir is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir will be pleased to hear that the tomb-robbers have been cleared from Tham Sarch.Talk to Nethrandir'Some people go through life never changing, always repeating the same mistakes and errors time and time again. It seems the tomb-robbers here in Evendim are no different.

'After Rantost, the few that remained and fled had a choice to make: a defining moment in their lives. They could have returned to Ost Forod and started to live honourable lives again. Most sailed south instead.

'They have come here, made bargains with an enemy they cannot fathom, and have returned to their old ways. While they use Tham Sarch to signal the Angmarim below, they are also stripping it bare. They have had their chances and moments and defied them all. They have been judged, and it is time they accept their sentence.''So it is done? Good. It may seem as if I am overly harsh, but if you continue to reject good time and time again, can you be anything but evil?''We have tolerated the tomb-robbers for too long. They have had their chances for redemption.'Arthobel sits high upon the hills above the Way of Kings. Were the robbers to find their way in, it would provide a very strategic viewpoint.Arthobel is south-west of the Ranger-encampment in the Way of Kings.

Maladan asked you to scout the ruins of Arthobel to see if the tomb-robbers are actively using it.Maladan is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Maladan will be pleased to hear the tomb-robbers have not gained access to Arthobel.Talk to Maladan'I have been watching the robbers as they have moved about the hills above us. They seem to focus on two primary ruins, Tham Sarch and Tham Laegamon. I know from my days as a child playing in those hills of a third ruin: Arthobel.

'The tower that stands there would make for a very strategic position. You could clearly see over the Way of Kings below you, watch the waters of the Baranduin to the south-east, and on a clear day, see Tinnudir.

'Last I remember, the heavy doors to that place were sealed tight, and none had been within in many years. I ask you to venture to the south-west, up into the hills, to the entrance and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> around to see if you notice any recent activity there.''So they have not yet found a way in either? That plays to our advantage.''I believe Arthobel was once lived in by an ancient relative of mine, but the records to prove it are long since lost.'Longbough believes that some evil power may be twisting the wood to dark ends.The Twisted Grove lies south-west of the Eavespires.

Lithuifin has asked you to seek evidence of the power which has corrupted the Twisted Grove. He asked you to collect rotted limbs and bring them to him.Collect rotted limbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lithuifin is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim.

You should bring the rotted limbs you have collected to Lithuifin.'We must learn more about the power which has corrupted the Twisted Grove and now seeps into the surrounding forest. It is dark and evil, but we know nothing of its source.

'Head to the Twisted Grove and gather any sickened or dead plants you may find. From them, I may be able to determine what it is that we truly face.''Take care as you explore the Twisted Grove. It has become a dark place with a vile hatred of all living things, and we must learn whence this blight has sprung.''You have brought me the fallen limbs from the trees of the grove? These should offer me some greater insight into what power now infects that dark place.'The Twisted Grove has a pool of water beneath it that feeds the roots of the trees and Wood-trolls there.The Twisted Grove is south-west of the Eavespires.

Remmenylf asked you to go to the Twisted Grove and pour the Ent's tear into the pool beneath it.Remmenylf is at the Eavespires, north-east of the Twisted Grove.

Remmenylf will be dismayed to hear that the Ent's tears did not purify the waters.Talk to Remmenylf at the Eavespires'Beneath the Twisted Grove is a pool of water. From this source, the trees and Wood-trolls' roots bring in their nutrients...and also their corruption. The waters of that pool are foul and poisoned.

'I have collected a few more of Longbough's tears and believe that they may purify this pool like they did the Gauradan-tainted one. 

'Head within the Twisted Grove and pour this into the waters below.''It did not work, you say? The evil that is concentrated there must be ancient and foul to resist Longbough.''If this works, the Wood-trolls should become trees and return to sleep.'Robin Dunkley has asked you to defeat the Gauredain of Emyn Uial and return with their weapons.The Gauredain prowl the hills and forests of Emyn Uial, north-west of Ost Forod.

Robin Dunkley desires revenge for the death of Nat Rapkins and wants you to defeat the evil men that slew him. He has also asked you to bring him some of the Gauredain's unusual weapons.Robin Dunkley is in Ost Forod, in Tyrn Fornech of Evendim, south-east of Emyn Uial.

You have defeated a number of the Gauredain that slew Nat Rapkins and collected some of their unusual weapons. Robin Dunkley will be pleased to hear the tale.'I do not know what made the Gauredain choose the life they lead, whether it be fascination with the form of the wolf or some other reason, but I do know that they have become entirely evil. These men wear wolf-skin cloaks and bedeck themselves with ornaments fashioned from bloody teeth and fangs, and it is said they move with unbelievable speed and attack with strength beyond that of a normal man.

'Nat must be avenged, ${PLAYER}, and the Gauredain taught not to attack the people who live around the lake. Journey north-west into Emyn Uial and defeat some of these evil Men. Return to me some of their weapons as well, that I may destroy them.''The Gauredain prowl the hills and forests of Emyn Uial, to the north-west. Defeat these evil men in memory of Nat Rapkins and bring me the unusual weapons they carry.''These claws fill me with dread, ${PLAYER}. The Gauredain are cruel indeed to hunt their own kin with these, for kin we are, despite the beast-hides they wear and the blood-thirst they possess. I hope that Nat has found peace, and I thank you for avenging his memory.

'I have nearly finished remaking the statue of Elendil from the pieces you brought to me, ${PLAYER}. I do not have all of the missing fragments, but some other adventurers are helping me search the camps of the tomb-robbers for the pieces that remain.

'But that is not what I must speak with you about. I have received word from Calenglad! He has returned from his meeting with the Blue Lady of Nenuial!'The Corcur, descendants of Hill-men of Rhudaur, have come down out of Angmar, seeking to reclaim their lands of old at the bidding of the Dark Lord.Corcur have begun to invade Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws.

While in Nan Tornaeth, you should drive out the Corcur who have come to the Trollshaws to reclaim their lands of old.Defeat Corcur in Nan Tornaeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Corcur have begun to invade Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws.

While in Nan Tornaeth, you should drive out the Corcur who have come to the Trollshaws to reclaim their lands of old.The tomb-robbers have fled to the hills above the Way of Kings. From them, they alert the forces of Angmar, their new allies, as to the actions of the Rangers.The crypts line the Way of Kings leading into Annúminas.

Before the Rangers can move to investigate the state of the crypts within the Way of Kings, they must secure the hills from the remaining tomb-robbers. Nimbellas has asked you to do this.Help Maladan scout ArthobelAid Nethrandir with the robbers of Tham SarchAid Nethrandir with the mirrors of Tham SarchAid Rodlam with the robbers of Tham LaegamonAid Rodlam with the longbows of Tham LaegamonNimbellas is at the Ranger-camp along the Way of Kings.

The hills have been cleared of threats. You should return at once to Nimbellas.Talk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings'I am glad to finally get some aid. We have been trying to do all that we can down here, but with every move we make, our enemies are already there waiting for us. I have discovered why, but we just have not had the numbers to do anything about it. Not long after you freed Rantost, several boats landed on the shore here. I watched a meeting between the newly-arrived tomb-robbers and the forces of Angmar. Afterwards, the robbers headed up into the hills, and the Angmarim resumed their search.

'I can only fathom that an accord was struck. The tomb-robbers would spy for Angmar and report on our movements from above. In return, Angmar would give the robbers any relics from the city that they did not want.

'If we are to move forward into the Way of Kings, the ancient burial ground of our ancestors' rulers, our actions must be shrouded to the Enemy. For that to happen, we must empty the hills and claim them for ourselves.''The hills have been cleared, and we are prepared to venture into the Way of Kings more boldly.''Once we secure the hills, the real work can begin.'Calenthon has sent his falcon Malloval to scout the Rhudaur ruins in Nan Tornaeth a long while ago, but Malloval has not returned.The slope south of Calenthon would be an ideal location at which to blow the whistle he gave you to summon Malloval.

Calenthon gave you a whistle with which to summon his falcon, Malloval.The ruins are above Calenthon's camp, which can be reached by taking the path north and east from Calenthon's camp.

After using Calenthon's whistle, you heard a falcon cry above the ruins near the bridge of Thoniant in Nan Tornaeth.Locate MallovalThe presence of wights and Corcur together suggests that the Hill-men are in league with whoever or whatever has raised the Dead. One of the Hill-men may bear an emblem or sigil indicating whom they serve....'If you have not already surmised, Malloval is a falcon, swift of wing and keen of eye. I sent him to learn what he could of the Corcur's strength and plans, but he has not returned.

'I use this whistle to summon him when he is flying afar amid the peaks and valleys...take it and climb the hill to the south. Blow the whistle from its sloping side, and Malloval should come to you, or at the very least answer your call with one of his own. If the latter, go to him, for it is likely he is beset by danger!

'Be wary, for the Corcur are dangerous in great number!'The falcon has been wounded by an arrow and hops about restlessly. He must be defended from his foes, or he will surely perish.The presence of wights and Corcur together suggests that the Hill-men are in league with whoever or whatever has raised the Dead. One of the Hill-men may bear an emblem or sigil indicating whom they serve....Longbough believes that some evil power may be twisting the wood to dark ends.Longbough is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim.

Longbough asked you to accompany him against the Twisted Heart.Accompany Longbough against the Twisted HeartLongbough is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim.

You should speak again with Longbough.Talk to Longbough at the Eavespires'Hoom! From the blighted branches you brought to us, I have divined much. There was once an ancient tree in the southern forest whom I was once well acquainted with, but after the destruction wrought upon the forest during the wars long ago, it became withdrawn and would speak with me no more...even though my own despair at the acts of Men was nearly as great.

'Now it seems that the Wood-trolls -- particularly this one called Heart-rot -- have whispered long to the Huorn in its slumber and re-awakened it under their thrall. Its heart is now black and twisted with their malice, and it will suffer no living thing of flesh in its domain. Hom! Ta-room! Were that all that had transpired, I would pay it less heed, for the Twisted Heart's folly is its own, but now its roots run deep and far, ever grasping and twisting the trees that they touch, and the Wood-trolls will follow in its wake. I cannot allow the Twisted Heart to warp the entire forest to its will. We must stand against it and fell both it and the vile troll that has corrupted it.

'Be careful, for the Twisted Heart's power has grown fell, and I fear it will be all we can do to face it in the place of its greatest strength, but we have no choice! Ta-rum! Hoom! Speak with me again when you are ready to leave.'Hoom! Hom! It has been ever so long since my blood has run with such heat and fervour! That was well fought, Little One! Indeed while I have little love for axes and swords, I had forgotten the enjoyable haste of battle. Ta-room! Even now though, I feel the anger of the forest subsiding as the Twisted Heart's influence fades. Soon some measure of peace shall return here, I think.

'Ta-rum! My thanks to you, Little One, your aid was most welcome. Please forgive my rudeness when first we met.'Hom! The forest seethes with anger as the power of the Twisted Heart grows, and while I fear we have little time, haste will lead only to disaster.

'Ta-room! Ta-rum! Are you fully prepared for what lies ahead? Be certain, for we face death should we falter.'The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of sleek fur.Collection boxes for this task can be found at the camps within the Misty Mountains.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Sleek fur from the beasts in the area of the Bruinen Source.  

The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of sleek fur.Wanted: Sleek fur from the beasts in the area of the Bruinen Source.This collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of toughened carapaces.Collection boxes for this task can be found at the camps within the Misty Mountains.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Toughened carapaces from the snow-lurkers throughout the Bruinen Source. 

The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of toughened carapaces.Wanted: Toughened carapaces from the snow-lurkers throughout the Bruinen Source.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Spring Standish is concerned about the lack of trade with the Snowmen of Forochel ever since tomb-robbers seized the gate at Cirith Rhîw.The captain of a robber-band maintains control of the road leading to the gate at Cirith Rhîw, north of Ost Forod.

Spring Standish has asked you to defeat a tomb-robber captain at Cirith Rhîw, in hopes that the rest of his band will disperse.Defeat tomb-robber captain at Cirith RhîwSpring Standish is at Ost Forod, the old watch-post in the hills of Tyrn Fornech, south of Cirith Rhîw.

You have defeated the tomb-robber captain at Cirith Rhîw and should return to Spring with news of your victory.'At the end of the northern road, at Cirith Rhîw, there stands a gate. For years, my family has brought goods that way to trade with the Snowmen of Forochel, but recently, a tomb-robber band has made passage nearly impossible.

'If you are a brave adventurer and true, you would surely be able to defeat the captain of that robber-band and recover any trade goods they have stolen.

'Just follow the road north through Tyrn Fornech until you come within sight of the gate at Cirith Rhîw. You should be careful, for the robber-band has held the road for a long time.''It will be some time before trade with Forochel resumes, but you have taken a step on that road for all of us now, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for it!''The tomb-robber captain and his cronies currently hold the road near the gate at Cirith Rhîw, and trade with Forochel is impossible. I hope you will be able to defeat him!'The Twisted Grove was once a place of respite and peace.The Elves of the Eavespires have some plans for the Twisted Grove.Aid Erchiel at The Twisted GroveAid Lithuifin in The Twisted GroveAid Remmenylf in The Twisted GroveLongbough is at the Eavespires.

Longbough will want to hear that the evil at the Twisted Grove is more powerful than previously thought.Talk to Longbough at the Eavespires'With the big people gone and the branches cleared, I can finally see the forest floor and what is poisoning the roots of all of us. The Twisted Grove, once a place that I called home, has become foul and corrupted.

'The trees there now live and move, but not as Ents or Huorns, they have been twisted into Wood-trolls, dangerous abominations of nature.

'I know not what has caused this all to happen, what has driven my woods to be against me.''Hoom, this is most concerning, and perhaps beyond our grasp to save.''If the evil within the Twisted Grove spreads, all of Evendim will be shrouded beneath darkness.'Crawlers infesting the gullies and cliffs of Nan Tornaeth are drawn to the rotting flesh of the wights which have arisen there.There are crawlers infesting Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws.

While in Nan Tornaeth, you should purge as many of the foul flesh-eating crawlers infesting the ruins as you can.Defeat crawlers in Nan Tornaeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are crawlers infesting Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws.

While in Nan Tornaeth, you should purge as many of the foul flesh-eating crawlers infesting the ruins as you can.Calenglad sent word to Robin Dunkley that he has returned from his journey to meet with Gwindeth and wants to speak with you.Calenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, south-west of Ost Forod, in Evendim.

The Ranger Calenglad has sent word that he wishes to speak with you.'Calenglad wants you to return to him at once so he may tell you of his meeting with the Blue Lady. Do not delay, ${PLAYER}!

'You have been a great help to me and have done much good for the people of Ost Forod. I hope to see you again, but for now you should return to Tinnudir and speak with Calenglad!''I am glad to see you again, ${PLAYER}, and to know that you have not been idle while I journeyed. Robin spoke of the aid you rendered, and I believe that the people of Ost Forod are better for your service.

'I have spoken with Gwindeth about acquiring the Silithar for Aragorn, but she is not satisfied with what I have told her of you. She wants to meet you herself.''What are you waiting for, ${PLAYER}? Calenglad waits for you at Tinnudir, to the south-west!'Bainthir has been charged with keeping the road through Tâl Bruinen clear.The road runs north of Echad Candelleth and south through Tâl Bruinen.

The road that runs through Tâl Bruinen often becomes choked with brambles and treacherous stones and is threatened by glen-bucks. Bainthir has offered you a reward if you can help him with his duty of keeping the road clear.Clear brambles from road (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Clear treacherous stones from road (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat great glen-bucks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bainthir is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen.

You have helped clear the road which runs through Tâl Bruinen of many hazards and should return now to Bainthir for your reward.Talk to Bainthir'The road that passes through Tâl Bruinen is little more than a dirt path for most of its length, but it is still used by travellers who pass south heading for Hollin and must be kept in usable condition.

'I have been charged by Lord Elrond with keeping the road clear, but it is a time-consuming duty, and I am often at a loss to keep it free of hazards.

'The path runs north of Echad Candelleth and south towards Hollin and often becomes choked with brambles and treacherous stones. Furthermore, the glen-bucks often stray near to the road and threaten travellers. If you can clear the road of these hindrances, I will reward you for your time.''Thank you for your service, ${PLAYER}. It is of great importance to Master Elrond that the road remain clear, especially in recent days.

'I cannot speak more on this subject, but know that you receive this reward with my thanks and with those of Master Elrond as well.'Nora Strawley has given you unexpected, but joyful, tidings: her husband survived his encounter with the Gauredain.Tongannel is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen in the Trollshaws, far to the east of Bree.

Nora Strawley has given you the happy news that the body you found was not her husband -- for he survived his ordeal and made it safely back to Bree -- and has asked you to bring one of the wooden figurines to Tongannel as a sign of friendship.'Don't be ridiculous! My husband is fine -- in fact, he's inside the house right now, resting from his ordeal! You see, when those wolf-men attacked the waggon, he wasted no time at all: he broke open the crate of figurines and started throwing them at them. While they were distracted, he crept by them down the path and escaped into the woods! He got turned around, or he would have stopped at Echad Candelleth to see the Elf Tongannel again, but he was already nearly to the Last Bridge when he regained his bearings. He came home, bemoaning the loss of the figurines, and I put him right to bed to rest.

'But you have recovered the figurines he meant to sell! He'll be so pleased. I think I will forbid him from making another such journey, however -- we will sell them here in Bree, and that will be more than enough. Though I must say, it is too bad that about the poor man you found... whoever he was he should not have died so.

'Here, take one of these figurines back to Tongannel. I know that Tim will be touched by her thoughtfulness, and he will want her to keep this as a token of her friendship with the Strawleys.''My heart is filled with joy at your tidings, ${PLAYER}! I will treasure this figurine, and think of the Strawleys whenever I look upon it!

'Take this reward with my good wishes, though it is nowhere near the happiness you have brought to me with this news!'You were unable to save the craftsman Tim Strawley from the ravaging of the Gauredain, but managed to recover his stolen figurines and bring them to Tongannel.Nora Strawley lives somewhere in the town of Bree, far to the west of the Trollshaws.

Tongannel has asked you to bring the wooden figurines to Nora Strawley in the hope that she will be able to sell them and make enough coin to live on for a time.'Ah, ${PLAYER}, I see that you remain here still. Perhaps you may help me again.

'You recovered the wooden figurines that were stolen from Tim Strawley's waggon, ${PLAYER}, and I would that they be brought to his widow, Nora. It is my hope that she will be able to sell them...perhaps not for as much as Tim hoped to receive south of the mountains, but enough for her to live on for a time, I think.

'The Strawleys made their home in the town of Bree, but beyond that I do not know where you will find her. I will not hold you to this task, for the journey is long, but if you choose to do this, bring Mrs. Strawley my best wishes, as well, and tell her of my sorrow.''These are my husband's figurines; I would know them anywhere!

'How did you come by them? And why the sorrowful face?'Gwindeth told you that two statues of Elendil stood on the islands of Tyl Ruinen: one corrupted by the salamanders and the other lost.Two statues of Elendil once stood on the south-east and south-west shores of Tyl Ruinen, but one statue has been corrupted by salamanders and the other statue is missing, perhaps recovered by the treasure-hunters of Ost Forod. The Eavespires are far to the north and east of Rushingdale.

Gwindeth wants you to restore two statues of Elendil on Tyl Ruinen. Some Elves at the Eavespires may be able to prepare a cleansing draught for the corrupted statue. Gwindeth does not know where the missing statue may have ended up or in what condition it may be.Complete Quest: The Corrupted StatueComplete Quest: The Lost StatueThe Blue Lady is in Gwindethrond, behind the waterfall at Rushingdale in western Emyn Uial, south-west of Tyl Ruinen.

You have restored the two statues of Elendil on Tyl Ruinen, as Gwindeth requested, and should return to her with the news.'Did you see the statues of noble Elendil that stand upon Tyl Ruinen, Messenger? One of them has been corrupted by the vile salamanders, tainted with dread ichor, and the other has been removed from its pedestal -- the statue itself has been lost.

'If you can restore both of the statues, I may be able to more readily judge your worth and the worthiness of Aragorn son of Arathorn. When both statues of mighty Elendil once more stand untroubled on the south-west and south-east shores of Tyl Ruinen, I will speak with you again on this matter.

'You will need a cleansing draught of some kind to restore the statue the salamanders have ruined. Elves have come to the Eavespires, far to the north and east of Rushingdale, where a stream flows into the lake; they may prepare such a draught for you. I do not know where you may find the missing statue. Perhaps the scavengers of Ost Forod have seized it.''Two statues of noble Elendil once stood on the main island of Tyl Ruinen, to the north-east, at its south-west and south-east corners. One has been corrupted by the salamanders and the other has been lost to time, but if you restore both statues, I will speak with you again.

'Elves at the Eavespires, far to the north and east of Rushingdale where a stream empties into the lake, may be able to prepare a cleansing draught for one of the statues. I do not know what has happened to the other statue; you will need to find it on your own.''You have restored both statues of fair Elendil, Messenger? I am pleased with your doings. Perhaps Aragorn son of Arathorn chose well when he sent you to me with his request. Calenglad spoke well of you, and he has always been true.

'I was always a friend to the kings of old, and I will not betray the trust they placed in me or the respect they bore me.

'There is one final test, Messenger. If you are able to meet my last request, I will allow you access to the tomb of Elendil and the Silithar. Surely the Lord of the Dúnedain has prepared you for this test. If he has not, it must be that he has learned nothing since last I saw him, and I will not surrender the Silithar to you.'Calenglad spoke with Gwindeth about acquiring the Silithar for Aragorn, but she refused to agree without first meeting you.The Blue Lady lives at Gwindethrond, a cave behind the waterfall at Rushingdale in the hills of western Emyn Uial on the far side of the lake, west and slightly south of Tinnudir and Tyl Ruinen.

Calenglad has arranged a meeting with Gwindeth and warned you to speak to her with respect and honesty. Only Gwindeth can grant you access to the Silithar needed by Aragorn.'Gwindeth has agreed to speak with you, ${PLAYER}, but do not misunderstand: she will only allow us to recover the Silithar if she believes that you are worthy of her trust and that Aragorn is ready for the burden that awaits him. She did not hesitate to rebuke him when he and I encountered her almost sixty years ago; I have no doubt that she would do so again, if it was in her mind.

'Speak to her with respect and do not seek to hide anything from her! The Blue Lady has lived in these lands for years uncounted, and she had patience only for the kings of Annúminas. It is said that Elendil consulted her often on various matters, and she grieved his passing.

'She lives at Gwindethrond, a cave in Western Emyn Uial, behind a clear waterfall that pours from the heights and feeds a shady pool at Rushingdale. You will need to circle the lake, for the pool is tucked among the hills on the far side of Nenuial. It will be a long journey, for Rushingdale is on the far side of Nenuial, west and slightly south even of Tinnudir and Tyl Ruinen.''You are the messenger from Aragorn son of Arathorn, Lord of the Dúnedain? You speak with his voice, and he shall be judged by yours, messenger, for he chose you as his agent.

'If there is much of Elendil in him, I do not doubt that Aragorn son of Arathorn will be found worthy. If there is not, the Silithar will remain where it has lain for centuries.''The Blue Lady lives at Gwindethrond, a cave behind the waterfall at Rushingdale in western Emyn Uial, on the far side of the lake, west and slightly south even of Tinnudir. Only she can grant you access to the Silithar.'After your defeat of the gaunt-man Gúrdring in Nan Tornaeth, Elrohir told you of Echad Candelleth, an Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen, and suggested that you lend its keepers your aid.Echad Candelleth sits atop a hill in Tâl Bruinen, south-east of Thorenhad. Elrohir told you to head east along the main road to the Bruinen, where you will find another white marker stone.

Elrohir told you to go to Echad Candelleth and aid Candelleth's company, while he and Elladan inform their father of the threats you discovered in Nan Tornaeth.Seek the white marker stone indicating the path to Tâl BruinenEchad Candelleth sits atop a hill in Tâl Bruinen, south-east of Thorenhad. Elrohir told you to take dirt path south as it climbs the hills above the western bank of the river. He advised that you to pay close attention to the path, as it is covered in brush and crossed by streams, but said that you might find a scout somewhere along its length to guide you to the encampment.

Elrohir has asked you to help the Elves at Echad Candelleth with their charge of keeping Tâl Bruinen free from danger.Talk to an Elf-scout in Tâl BruinenNestael is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen, just over the south-east hill from Haradir's post.

Haradir told you to introduce yourself to Nestael at Echad Candelleth, and she would let you know what aid you might lend.Talk to Nestael'My brother and I will see to it that our father is notified of the threats in Nan Tornaeth, for there is more yet to be done in the wilds. The Trollshaws are dangerous, as you have seen, ${PLAYER}, and it takes the labour of many Elves to keep the wild at bay.

'South along the river, you will find the wooded hills of Tâl Bruinen. Echad Candelleth stands high atop one of the hills there. Travel east until you see the river, and you will find yet another white marker stone. Follow the dirt path to the south that climbs the hills above the western bank of the Bruinen. After you pass into Tâl Bruinen, keep a close watch on the path, for the wilderness encroaches upon it, and it may be difficult to make out. The land, too, is damp, and the path may be crossed by several quick-flowing streams.

'I am certain that Candelleth will have dispatched a scout to guide friends to her encampment. Lend whatever aid you may to Candelleth and her company.''Greetings, traveller! If you are looking for Echad Candelleth, you have nearly found it! You simply need to climb the slope to the south-east. As you crest the hill, you will see the encampment among the ruins.

'Introduce yourself to Nestael, and she will tell you of these lands and what you might do to help.''It is a pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}, for we have much need of aid! Tâl Bruinen has become a place of great danger: Gauredain from the far north have found their way here and have established a camp in the south-west, the Dâg Taushakhu in the depths of Eryn Singor urge the Wood-trolls to greater and greater malevolence, and the rock-worms of Cirith Ulunn threaten travellers in these lands.

'A number of hunters have come here as well, and we grant them what hospitality we may. Treat them with kindness, for they are our guests. Furthermore, servants of Angmar have come to Tâl Bruinen. They have focused their attention on the small ruins to be found throughout the woods, but I know not what they seek.'Wéthorm has sent you back to Indor with the improved toad stew, and insists that you deliver his compliments to the hunter for improving upon the original recipe.Indor is at the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen.

Wéthorm has returned the toad stew to you and asked you to give his compliments to Indor on its improvement.'Most delicious! Indor has truly improved upon my original recipe. I cannot place the ingredient, but there is a whiskery sort of quality to it that makes the dish truly amazing.

'Return to him with my compliments, ${PLAYER}! You might tell him, as well, to put less stock in the words of others.''I cannot place what ingredients Indor added to the toad stew, but whatever they were, they only served to improve its flavour!

'Indor is still at the Elf-camp of Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen? If you pass by that way, be sure to return the rest of the toad stew to him with my compliments on its improvement.''You have returned, ${PLAYER}! Describe to me the look on Wéthorm's face when he bit into my "improved" toad stew!

'What? He liked it? That is odd. Do you think I stumbled upon some culinary secret, ${PLAYER}? Maybe adding the crawler mandibles and legs did something to the body of the stew? Maybe in combination with the toad parts, they worked some magic in the flavour? This could be quite the discovery!'

Indor excitedly scoops a big spoonful of the Improved Toad Stew and takes a tremendous bite. His grin quickly fades to a scowl.

'By my eyes, he tricked me again! Wéthorm, you scoundrel! This is even worse than the original stew! You know, ${PLAYER}, maybe Wéthorm has a point. I will try and be less trusting from now on. I will not hold it against you, and I am sure I can dig up something with which to reward you. No, no, do not look so panicked! I was not planning on giving you the toad stew!'Garbert has devised a plan for catching the sneaking creature.Garbert is at his cottage south of Echad Candelleth, at a fork in the river Bruinen.

You should speak with Garbert when you are ready to carry out his plan to capture the creature.Talk to Garbert and carry out his plan to capture the creatureGarbert is at his cottage south of Echad Candelleth, at a fork in the river Bruinen.

You should speak with Garbert regarding the creature.Talk to GarbertWistan is at his camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen, north of Garbert's cottage.

Garbert suggested that you bring Wistan's arrows back to him.'If we place these fish beneath the open window of my cottage, I reckon we might surprise him when he returns to try for the cradle again. Little will it know that Afanen will have Whelan safely away.

'Let me know when you are ready to go, ${PLAYER}, and we can prepare. I'm no hunter, so I sent word to a friend of mine, a hunter named Adwold, to lend a hand. He'll meet us later.''Are you ready to go? Let us prepare the trap to catch this creature.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Arrows, but no hart? Did I miss?

'Ah! I was beaten to the carcass by a creeping beast. It is the height of humiliation.

'I suppose we should be thankful that the fisherman and his wife were unharmed.''I have never seen such a creature! Are you sure it won't return?

'Nevertheless, I shall remain wary, until I am certain myself. You have my thanks, though.

'You should probably take those arrows back to your hunter friend.'At Tongannel's behest, you travelled south towards the Hollin Ridge, searching for the craftsman Tim Strawley. You found his waggon in ruins, an empty and broken crate, and other signs that he was attacked.The Gauredain make their home in the south-western hills of Tâl Bruinen, south of Eryn Singor.

From the wreckage, it appears that perhaps the mysterious Gauredain Nestael mentioned when you first arrived at Echad Candelleth might be responsible for the attack. You should search for their encampment and rescue Tim Strawley, if he still lives, and recover his goods.Rescue Tim Strawley and recover his goodsThe Gauredain make their home in the south-western hills of Tâl Bruinen, south of Eryn Singor.

From the wreckage, it appears that perhaps the mysterious Gauredain Nestael mentioned when you first arrived at Echad Candelleth might be responsible for the attack. You should search for their encampment and rescue Tim Strawley, if he still lives, and recover his goods.Recover wooden figurines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find Tim StrawleyTongannel is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen, north of Echad Gauradan.

You have recovered Tim Strawley's wooden figurines from the Gauredain who stole them, but Strawley himself was slain. You should return the goods to Tongannel.The Gauredain make their home in the south-western hills of Tâl Bruinen, south of Eryn Singor.

From the wreckage, it appears that perhaps the mysterious Gauredain Nestael mentioned when you first arrived at Echad Candelleth might be responsible for the attack. You should search for their encampment and rescue Tim Strawley, if they have taken him captive, and recover his goods.'Thank you for this, ${PLAYER}. I am glad that you have recovered Tim Strawley's figurines from the Gauredain, though I would that you could have saved him from their ravaging.'Each of the rulers of Annúminas had a unique ring given to him by the Blue Lady.Haudh Arantar is to the south of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir asked you to go venture within Haudh Arantar and find Arantar's ring before Angmar does.Find Arantar's ringNethrandir is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir will be eager to see you found Arantar's ring.'Upon taking the throne, each of the rulers of Annúminas was given a ring by the Blue Lady. This signified their right to rule and also identified them to others from outside the kingdom.

'It has long been rumoured that these rings also had some form of extra power. Not like the Rings of Power themselves, mind you, but something else.

'I believe Arantar's ring may still be in his tomb, and that is what Angmar is desperately searching for. See if you can find it first.''We must find that ring before Angmar does!''Yes, this indeed is Arantar's ring. I will see it gets sent to Tinnudir immediately.'Garbert's grandparents were driven from their village many years ago by three marauding trolls, and Garbert wants to learn what became of the villains.The trolls that terrorized the village that Garbert's grandparents once lived in probably met their end somewhere within the wilderness of the Trollshaws. Garbert lives in a cottage along the banks of the river in Tâl Bruinen.

Garbert has asked you to find the location where the three trolls of which he spoke met their end and to learn the story of their undoing.Find someone who knows the fate of Bert, Tom, and BillFind Bert, Tom, and BillGarbert lives at his cottage in Tâl Bruinen, on the banks of the river.

You have learned what befell the trolls Bert, Tom, and Bill, and have visited the glade where they were turned to stone. You should return to Garbert with the news.'Many years ago, my grandparents lived in a quiet village not far from here. It was a peaceful place, and they were very happy, but one day three monstrous Stone-trolls came to the village and caused great destruction. My grandparents fled, and eventually my grandfather built this cottage here on the bank of the Bruinen. His son lived in the cottage with them, and I was later born here.

'I grew up and took a wife, and my parents left me the cottage when they passed on; Afanen and I have lived here ever since. I have always wondered whatever happened to those three trolls: Bert, Tom, and Bill they were called, and the names send shivers down my spine even today!

'I'm sure they must have come to a bad end, being trolls, but if you can find where they ended up and learn the tale of their undoing, I'd be very glad to hear it!''If you are looking for the one who defeated Bert, Tom, and Bill, three trolls who ought to have spent more time thinking and less time bickering, you have found him!

'But the tale should be told by another; look for burglar Bilbo in the Hall of Fire to tell you the tale. He knows it most intimately, and if he perhaps downplays his own part in the events, it is only to his credit.''The trolls probably met their end somewhere within the Trollshaws. I do not know who might know the tale of their undoing, but if you can find someone who does, I would appreciate it.''Garbert is always going on about the trolls that ran his grandparents out of their village. If you can find where the trolls ended up and learn the story of their undoing as well, maybe he will finally stop talking about it!''Bert, Tom, and Bill, you said? My goodness! Yes, yes, I know of them, and more than that; they invited me to dinner once! Well, I say "invited," but that's not quite true. You might say I invited myself, but hoping to pick a troll's purse is not as easy as you'd expect, and if caught in the act you might very well be cooked!

'I was there with the dwarves, you see, and when I didn't come back from my little bit of burglary, the dwarves came to see what had happened. Soon enough, the trolls had bagged them all, and a debate had begun concerning how best to cook us and eat us! Well, Gandalf turned up, as he does when most needed, and sure enough the trolls had spent so long bickering that they were quite turned to stone at sun-up! So that's what happened. I've written it all down in my book, but to have lived it is a much different experience than to read about it!

'If you want to visit old Bert, Tom, and Bill, you'll find them in the wilderness of the Trollshaws, off the road.''I'll not forget Bert, Tom, and Bill in all my days!''This Bilbo sounds like a great hero, does he not? I wonder what else he has written in his book?''Ah, so that is what happened to those old trolls. I am glad to have heard the story, ${PLAYER}, and thank you for the news! It is good to know that old Bert, Tom, and Bill came to an unhappy end after what they did to my grandparents' village.

'You have my thanks for the tale, and I will give you this as well!'Indor has decided to reciprocate Wéthorm's bad humour with an ill joke of his own.Crawlers can be found all throughout Tâl Bruinen.

Indor has asked you to collect several pieces from the crawlers of Tâl Bruinen so he can have his revenge upon the dwarf who played a trick on him.Collect bristly crawler legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect slimy crawler mandibles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Indor is at the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen.

You have collected the crawler bits for which Indor asked and should now bring them to him, so he can add them to the stew he is preparing.The grinding stone is near the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth.

Indor has asked you to grind the various crawler bits you recovered into mush on a nearby grinding stone.Indor is at the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen.

You have ground the crawler pieces you collected into mush and should now bring the mush to Indor so he can add it to the stew.Wéthorm is at Thorenhad, in the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws, north of the bear-dens.

Indor has sent you to Wéthorm with his toad stew, and has asked you to pay close attention to the dwarf's reaction to his first bite. Indor wishes to savour his revenge on the dwarf who tricked him into tasting the unpleasant toad stew.'That Wéthorm has been having a bit of fun at my expense, if you ask me! Well, we will have some sport as well and see how he likes it!

'I will need your help, ${PLAYER}. I am going to "improve" the toad stew by adding crawler bits to it, and then I will have you bring it to Wéthorm. Tell him that I made some improvements to the stew, and it is even better now! Oh, we will have the last laugh with this one, my dear ${RACE}!

'Gather some crawler legs and mandibles and bring them back to me, and we will set my plan in motion! You will find crawlers all throughout Tâl Bruinen, ${PLAYER}, so start hunting!''There are crawlers all over Tâl Bruinen, ${PLAYER}, but they especially like damp places. Bring me some of their bristly legs and slimy mandibles and we will teach that Wéthorm a lesson!''Very good, ${PLAYER}! These legs and mandibles are very unappealing and will be just the thing!

'Do me a favour and grind them into mush on that grinding stone, will you?''The grinding stone is right there, ${PLAYER}. Grind all the crawler pieces into mush, and then I can add them to the stew! We will teach Wéthorm to play tricks on us!''This will do nicely, ${PLAYER}. It looks terrible, and it smells worse! It is perfect!

'Now, take this toad stew and bring it to the Dwarf Wéthorm at Thorenhad. Tell him that I made some additions to the stew to make it taste even better, and I wanted to share it with him. And be sure to get a good look at his face when he takes a bite -- I want you to describe it to me, leaving nothing out! We will have the last laugh, we will!

'Thorenhad is north of here, in the Trollshaws, along the Bruinen Gorges. Wéthorm said he was going to visit one of his kinsmen there for a while, and I am sure he is still there.''Wéthorm is staying at Thorenhad, north of here in the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws, north of the bear-dens. Pay close attention to his first bite of my toad stew, because I want to savour my revenge!''Hello, ${PLAYER}. Wéthorm at your service and your family's! Ah, you are a friend of Indor! He is a good Man, if a little too trusting in these dangerous times. He would do well to learn that lesson early.'

Wéthorm takes a tremendous bite of the toad stew, and his face lights up. He takes a second bite, and then a third, before handing the bowl back to you.The Ranger Culang has learned of a great treasure buried long ago by a Dúnadan-landholder and wants it recovered before it is found by tomb-robbers.The treasure may lie beneath another stone marker, somewhere in Evendim, if this riddle is to be believed:

  "High atop Dol Haedír, beyond the Gloaming Falls,
   Wolf-kin men will guard my last."

You should examine the marker when you find it for some clue to the location of the treasure.Find the solution to the riddleThe inscription on this stone marker is barely legible, but these words can just be made out:

  "High atop Dol Haedír, beyond the Gloaming Falls,
   Wolf-kin men will guard my last."

This new riddle may reveal the true location of the treasure.The stone marker is surrounded by signs of digging; if it once marked the location of the treasure, it has surely been found.

The marker bears an inscription, all but worn away by the passage of time.'Again, ${PLAYER}? I am amazed at both your persistence and that of the departed landholder! How does this latest riddle go?

  "High atop Dol Haedír, beyond the Gloaming Falls,
   Wolf-kin men will guard my last."

'I have heard of Dol Haedír, ${PLAYER}, but it has a foul reputation. It lies far to the north-west of Lake Nenuial, and from this riddle I gather the Gloaming Falls must be somewhere near the summit.'Elladan and Elrohir have had an unfruitful search for the missing Rider, but the brothers have finally uncovered some traces of his passing.The hoofprints were discovered far south of the road, and the sons of Elrond believe that the missing Rider might be hiding in the ruins of Minas Agor, located within the narrow channels of the South Trollshaws.

Elladan has asked you to follow the Nazgûl into the South Trollshaws.

<rgb=#FF0000>The Elf-stone can be used to allow for you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.</rgb>Find some sign of the missing NazgûlThe corpse of a black horse lies in the ruins of Minas Agor, located among the narrow channels of the South Trollshaws.

You should remove the bridle from the horse's corpse and return with it to Elladan.

<rgb=#FF0000>The Elf-stone can be used to allow for you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.</rgb>Remove bridle from the black horse's corpseElladan is at Thorenhad, located among the Bruinen Gorges, north of a bear-den.

Elladan will be both pleased and troubled to see the bridle of the black horse, for it means that the missing Rider is still somewhere within the Trollshaws.'Shortly after Frodo Baggins and his company came to Rivendell, my father sent us to search for signs of the Nazgûl, the Nine Riders of the Enemy. We found the bodies of eight horses downstream, but of the last there was no sign. We searched further, but still found nothing.

'We travelled far afield, into lands to the south, and still found no sign of the fleeing Rider. Only on our return journey did we find something: hoofprints in the South Trollshaws, far south of the road. There are many narrow valleys in that region -- the Nazgûl might lie there, sheltered from prying eyes, waiting for his time to strike.

'Journey far south of the road in the South Trollshaws, ${PLAYER}, and seek out the missing Rider. The ruins within those narrow channels have a fell reputation. Minas Agor that place was called of old, and the Nazgûl may have sought it out for that reason.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant to completed while grouped, but can be attempted solo. The stone you receive upon bestowal can be used for a short term buff that will enable you to benefit from the inspiration buff while in a fellowship smaller than five.</rgb>'We discovered hoofprints leading into the narrow valleys far south of the road through the South Trollshaws. The ruins of Minas Agor are located within those channels and have a fell name. The missing Rider may be sheltering within those crumbling walls.''The black steed of the Nazgûl is dead, within the ruins of Minas Agor? We must be certain, ${PLAYER} -- return to the ruins and remove the horse's bridle. Only then can we be certain of what you have seen.''Great tragedy befell the dwellers of Minas Agor long ago, and the place has never recovered from the memory of what happened there. If it is now a refuge for the missing Nazgûl, it appears its fate has not much changed.

'You will find the ruins south of the Great East Road that runs through the South Trollshaws, amidst the narrow valleys of that place.''You have found the black horse of the Nazgûl? Quickly, ${PLAYER} -- return to Minas Agor and bring us the bridle of the steed. We must know for certain.''You must tell Elladan these grim tidings at once. I confess that a shadow has fallen over my heart, for these lands that I love are endangered by the very presence of the Nazgûl. Would that he had been caught within the Bruinen with the rest of his fell brethren!''Your tale begins to fill in this puzzle for me, ${PLAYER}, and I think I now see what has happened.

'Caught between the remainder of Frodo's company and the raging of the Bruinen, the Nine were forced into the torrent -- but one escaped in the chaos. Near death, his steed bore him through hidden channels into some place where, nearly formless, he gathered his strength.

'His horse he abandoned, and he vanished into the wild. Without his cloak he would be all but invisible to us -- a malice on the wind. If he takes it onto himself again, it is only to give shape to his strength. It means he has survived the ordeal unharmed and will surely strike at us again. We are running out of time, ${PLAYER}.'Elladan has determined that the missing Rider may be hiding in one of the many caves that dot the crags of the Trollshaws and wants you to search several of them with Glorfindel's beryl.Elladan gave you his notes containing the locations of the troll-caves.

Elladan wants you to search three troll-caves with Glorfindel's beryl.

<rgb=#FF0000>Using the Shimmering Elf-stone allows you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.</rgb>Elladan is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear-dens.

Elladan is waiting to hear what Glorfindel's beryl revealed: that the missing Nazgûl was never in any of the caves you searched.'I have given some thought to our riddle, ${PLAYER}, and while I do not know if this is the answer, my heart tells me that we must exhaust this course before we can be sure it is fruitless.

'Many caves dot the wilderness of the Trollshaws, home to the creatures that give this place its name. The missing Nazgûl suffered some grievous hurt when caught between the fires of Glorfindel and the Ranger Aragorn and the waters of Bruinen, and he must have escaped to some secluded corner of the wild to regain his strength; I believe he fled to one of the troll-caves.

'I will write down the names and locations of three caves. Descend into the deepest chamber of each and hold Glorfindel's beryl aloft. We must learn if the Nazgûl hid within one of these caves in order to pick up his trail. Bring allies to these caves, for the trolls that lurk within are dangerous. Here are my notes, ${PLAYER}.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Using the Shimmering Elf-stone allows you to access the inspiration buff while solo or in a smaller fellowship.</rgb>'I gave you my notes on the troll-caves you should search, ${PLAYER}. Descend to the deepest chamber within the caves Torogrod, Nurath, and Thingroth and hold aloft Glorfindel's beryl.''You are seeking the cave of Thingroth? I do not know if it bears that name, but there is a troll cave to the east -- I passed by it as I sought the Wovenvales.''You have done as I asked, ${PLAYER}, and for that I am grateful. Nay, do not frown so! Had you not searched the caves, we could never be sure that the Nazgûl was not hiding within, waiting for his time to strike anew. Now we have eliminated some of his possible hiding-places, and for that we should be pleased.

'I will take Glorfindel's beryl and return it to him. For you, I have another avenue of inquiry, and it could be this one will bear fruit.'Because of their decreasing numbers, the Rangers of the North must occasionally hire Men from Ost Forod to watch over their ancient tombs.Alfred Whitley can be found in Men Erain, south of Tinnudir across the lake. Following the shore road north and east into Men Erain, Whitley's camp can be found on the hillside up some carved stone steps.

The Ranger Helechír has asked you to bring supplies to a man by the name of Alfred Whitley in Men Erain.Bring the supplies to Alfred WhitleyAlfred Whitley is missing from his watch-post in Men Erain, but the journal that remains among his things may hold some clue to his whereabouts.

You found Alfred Whitley's watch-post, but there was no sign of Whitley himself. His journal may hold some clue as to his fate.Collect journal from Alfred Whitley's campHelechír is on an island a little south-west of Men Erain.

You found the journal of a Ranger on a pilgrimage to his family's ancestral holdings near Annúminas. According to his journal, he suspected he was being followed. Helechír will be most interested to hear of this.'Stay a moment, for I would speak with you. My people are much concerned with the protection of the ancient Dúnedain heritage of Annúminas and the surrounding lands, but we are stretched thin. We have on occasion hired some of the more adventurous folk of Ost Forod, to the north-east, to help protect the old manors and crypts from despoiling.

'One such worthy, by the name of Alfred Whitley, keeps watch over some of the tombs of Men Erain. If you would, please take these supplies to him. Return to the mainland and follow the shore road north and east into Men Erain. Shortly after reaching that place, the burial ground for many of the ancient kings of my people, you will see steps carved into the hillside. Climb the steps to Alfred Whitley's camp.

'He has been away for some time and is surely running short of provisions; return to me when you have given him these supplies, and I will reward you for the trouble.''Please bring those supplies to Alfred Whitley. He has probably run low of provisions, and will have need of them before long. Return to the mainland and follow the shore road north and east into Men Erain, until you see the steps carved in the hillside that climb up to Whitley's camp.''Alfred Whitley was not at his watch-post? That is very strange.

'Please return to his camp and look for some sign of what happened to him -- perhaps he left his journal behind? Whitley was a good friend and true. We must learn what has happened to him.

'The watch-post is to the north and east, in Men Erain. Look for the steps carved into the hillside a short distance into Men Erain and search Whitley's watch-post for anything that might help.''You found a journal, ${PLAYER}? Allow me to read it, and perhaps it will shed some light on the fate of Alfred Whitley.

'This is terrible news! I must now believe that not only Whitley, but my kinsman Iorthrenar as well, were attacked and slain by tomb-robbers! Both now lie in shallow graves.'Gwindeth wants you to prove yourself worthy of recovering the Silithar by fighting the salamanders of Tyl Ruinen.The islands of Tyl Ruinen are located north-east of Rushingdale, near the middle of the lake, in Evendim.

Gwindeth has asked you to defeat the corrupted salamanders you find on Tyl Ruinen.Defeat salamanders on Tyl Ruinen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Blue Lady is in Gwindethrond, behind the waterfall at Rushingdale in western Emyn Uial, south-west of Tyl Ruinen.

Gwindeth is waiting to hear that you have dealt a blow to the salamanders of Tyl Ruinen.'Before he went away to his doom, Elendil often spoke with me beside Nenuial; we would walk among the reeds and speak of his kingdom, and he treated me with grace and respect. It is for the memory of great Elendil that I maintain the lake and protect the relics of his line.

'At the behest of Amlaith, the last king to sit enthroned in Annúminas, I permitted the waters of Nenuial to wash over the walls of the city, and the treasures of proud Elendil now sleep soundly in the watery half-light. The adamant you seek, the Silithar that passed from Gil-galad to Elendil and his line through the safe-keeping of Círdan the Shipwright, cannot be reclaimed without my permission. It was the will of Amlaith that the Silithar be kept safe, even from those of Elendil's line, for fear that its light would be wasted unduly or the stone taken by the Enemy.

'The islands of Tyl Ruinen have been overrun by salamanders, corrupted beasts that singe the grasses and taint the waters of Nenuial. Swim north-east to Tyl Ruinen in the centre of the lake and defeat the salamanders you find there. Perhaps when you return, I will have proof of the worthiness of Aragorn son of Arathorn through his messenger.''You have defeated some of the salamanders that lurk now on Tyl Ruinen? There are many who would do such a thing, when asked. Why should this prove yourself worthy of what you seek or prove that Aragorn has grown since last I saw him?''The islands of Tyl Ruinen are to the north-east, in the middle of the lake. Defeat the salamanders that have corrupted them, and I may be able to judge your worth, Messenger.'The Hillmen at Aughaire have requested a collection of broken halberds to be delivered to Raith.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver broken halberds from the Orcs and Angmarim surrounding Aughaire to Raith, a Hillman within the settlement.Wanted: Broken halberds from Orcs and Angmarim in the lands surrounding Aughaire. Deliver the items to Raith at Aughaire in the south-western reaches of Angmar.Wanted: Broken halberds from Orcs and Angmarim in the lands surrounding Aughaire.'They ruled over our people too long and took everything from us. This will bring hope to many that the oppressive yoke can be cast aside. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Hillmen at Aughaire have requested a collection of huge filth to be delivered to Raith.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver huge filth from insects and spiders surrounding Aughaire to Raith, a Hillman within the settlement.Wanted: Huge filth from insects and spiders from the lands surrounding Aughaire. Deliver the items to Raith at Aughaire in the south-western reaches of Angmar.Wanted: Huge filth from insects and spiders from the lands surrounding Aughaire.'We will use this well. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Hillmen at Aughaire have requested a collection of lethal sharp claws to be delivered to Raith.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver lethal sharp claws from cave-claws surrounding Aughaire to Raith, a Hillman within the settlement.Wanted: lethal sharp claws from cave-claws to the south of Aughaire. Deliver the items to Raith at Aughaire in the south-western reaches of Angmar.Wanted: lethal sharp claws from cave-claws to the south of Aughaire.'These can be fashioned into many weapons. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Foul toads infest the waterways of Tâl Bruinen.There are toads infesting the waterways of Tâl Bruinen, in the Trollshaws.

While in Tâl Bruinen, you should purge the waterways of the foul toads.Defeat toads in Tâl Bruinen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are toads infesting the waterways of Tâl Bruinen, in the Trollshaws.

While in Tâl Bruinen, you should purge the waterways of the foul toads.Tongannel has had an uneasy feeling for the last few days and hopes it does not bode ill for the traveller from Bree whom she befriended.Tim Strawley drove his waggon south of Echad Candelleth along the road heading for Hollin, which crosses a small ford east of Garbert's cottage and climbs towards the Hollin Ridge.

Tongannel has asked you to follow the road south and search for any sign of Tim Strawley to allay her fears for his safety.'My heart has been ill at ease for the last few days, ${PLAYER}, and I hope that you can put my fears to rest. A traveller from Bree by the name of Tim Strawley came to Echad Candelleth on his way south; a craftsman he was, and he bore wooden figurines of exquisite quality that he hoped to sell in far-off markets. He desired to raise enough money to support his young wife, Nora, and he was enthusiastic about his prospects.

'But the road is rarely-travelled, and a worry has been growing in the back of my mind ever since he left the camp. If it is not too much to ask, could you take the road south towards Hollin and check to see that he has not come into trouble? I am certain that all is well, but I would be more at ease if you would do this for me.

'The road to Hollin runs south of Echad Candelleth and crosses the Bruinen at a small ford east of Garbert's cottage, where it rises steadily until reaching the Hollin Ridge.'There is much to do while travelling through the lands of the Trollshaws.Complete Explorer of the Trollshaws deedComplete Deeds in the Wilderness (Final) deedComplete Slayer of the Trollshaws deedThe once-great city of Annúminas is now occupied by a large and powerful enemy force.The eastern gate of Annúminas is to the south of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nimbellas asked you to scout the eastern gate of Annúminas.Scout the eastern gate to AnnúminasNimbellas is at the Ranger-camp within the Way of Kings.

Nimbellas will be dismayed to hear about the strength of Angmar's encampment at the eastern gate of Annúminas.Talk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings'Eventually, once we have the tombs here secured, we will be working to try to link up with the Rangers that are standing firm within the city of Annúminas to the west. We cannot risk such a mission without a better understanding of the enemy forces between our camp here and the camp established at Echad Garthadir.

'Out here, we have space to move, and once we are within the city, we can use rooftops and alleyways to traverse unseen. The sticking point is the eastern gate to the city. We will have to pass through that, unless we are to go by boat, which is likely a deadlier proposition.

'Head south of here until the path brings you to the city. From a distance, observe the eastern gate, then report back what forces may be there.''That many you say? This presents a dilemma I must ponder for a while.''We cannot move unless we have full knowledge of the tactical situation.'The Elves at Thorenhad desire a delivery of broken longswords to be delivered to them.You have accepted a task to collect broken longswords from the evil men and trolls in the areas surrounding Thorenhad. The items are to be delivered to a collection box. There is a collection box at Thorenhad in the Trollshaws.Wanted: Broken longswords from the evil Men and Trolls surrounding Thorenhad. The items are to be delivered to a collection box. There is a collection box at Thorenhad in the Trollshaws.Wanted: Broken longswords from the evil Men and Trolls surrounding Thorenhad.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Elves at Thorenhad desire a delivery of hardened carapaces to be made to them.You have accepted a task to collect hardened carapaces from the spiders and insects in the areas surrounding Thorenhad. The items are to be delivered to a collection box. There is a collection box at Thorenhad in the Trollshaws.Wanted: Hardened carapaces from the spiders and insects surrounding Thorenhad. All items should be delivered to a collection box.Wanted: Hardened carapaces from the spiders and insects surrounding Thorenhad.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Some can fall to the Shadow, but these dwarves have allied themselves with the Enemy by choice.Defeat DourhandsDuring their thralldom in Barad-dûr, the Stout-axes were held to be lesser than even the lowliest Orc. Even as the Stout-axes endured the cruelty of the Enemy's servants, the old hatreds between dwarves and Orcs were not forgotten.Defeat OrcsWithin Haudh Eärendur rests the last King of the North who managed to hold together the House of Elendil.Haudh Eärendur is within the Way of Kings, west of the Rangers' camp.

Nimbellas has asked you to take rubbings of engravings from the tombs within Haudh Eärendur.Collect rubbings within Haudh Eärendur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nimbellas is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nimbellas will be eager to examine the rubbings you collected.Talk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings'Alas, the tale of the North Kingdom is one of tragedy. Eärendur son of Elendur was the last King of Arnor, before his sons splintered the North Kingdom into the realms of Arthedain, Cardolan, and Rhudaur. Unfortunately, much lore of those final days was lost with him.

'He rests still in his tomb, Haudh Eärendur, and with him, we believe, some fragments of the knowledge of the last days of Arnor. Would you perhaps venture into the tomb and take rubbings of any engravings you might find there?

'Be wary, for I do not doubt that enemies, beasts, or the elements have invaded that tomb, as they have so many others here.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. These rubbings will help us piece together an important part of our history.''I am sure much knowledge of the last days of Arnor has been lost in Haudh Eärendur for lo these many ages.'Echad Garthadir, the Rangers' encampment within Annúminas, is under constant assault.Echad Garthadir lies some distance from the Way of Kings, within Annúminas.

The Rangers have sent you to lend aid to Echad Garthadir.Talk to Adadhrond at Echad Garthadir'I have just received word that our encampment in Annúminas is under heavy and near constant assault. Echad Garthadir is our one foothold in the city itself, and we cannot afford to lose it.

'I believe that we can handle what is left to do here within the tombs. Please, journey to Echad Garthadir and join the fight there!''Welcome to the centre of the conflict, ${PLAYER}. If tomb-robbers or Gauredain gave you trouble in the past, I would advise you leave now. The battles here are for true warriors.''I do not know the horrors you will find once you get to Echad Garthadir, so steel yourself for anything!'Kergrim, creatures from the depths of the waters and tombs, have begun to spread into the Way of Kings.Defeat kergrim in the Way of Kings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rodlam is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam will be pleased to hear a number of kergrim have been defeated.Talk to Rodlam in the Way of Kings'The depths, both of the lake and the tombs, contain many things we do not yet understand. These creatures now roaming the Way of Kings are one such example of that.

'We call them kergrim, but are not sure what they are, other than that they feed upon the remains of the dead. I do not know if they are lizard, twisted men, or something else, something more ancient and foul. What I do know, is they are very territorial and hostile, and they stand between us and the tombs.

'They must be cleared out if we are to advance further. Head into the Way of Kings and defeat several of them so we can advance.''Good! Perhaps that will get us a little more room to explore within the area.''Eventually, we may learn what these beasts are, but for now all I need to know is that they will kill if given the chance.'The Way of Kings is dotted with tombs and crypts holding the remains of the former kings and rulers of the ancient city of Annúminas.Crypts and tombs line the pathway from the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings west to the city of Annúminas.

Maladan asked you to scout the entrances to several tombs and crypts within the Way of Kings.Scout Haudh EärendurScout Haudh ElendurScout Haudh ValandurScout Haudh ElendilScout Haudh TarondorScout Haudh EldacarScout Haudh TarcilScout Haudh ArantarMaladan is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Maladan will want to know the state of the tombs and crypts within the Way of Kings.Talk to Maladan in the Way of Kings'The path between here and the great city was once one of grandeur and unrivalled beauty. Tombs, crypts, and monuments to those who had ruled the North Kingdom lined the road. You were flooded with a sense of honour, justice, wisdom, and valour.

'It pains me to look out and see what has become of them. Some destroyed, some empty, robbed of everything but the stones themselves, some swallowed up by the lake. It is not the end that men of that stature deserve.

'We have not yet taken an accounting of the state of each of the tombs. While you are venturing within the Way of Kings, could you stop by each of them and let me know how time has treated them?''I wish to know the state of the tombs along the Way of Kings.''So, four are being used, one lies destroyed, one is dormant, and Elendil has retained its majesty. We will have to do something about the four that are open... and quickly I fear.'You found what seems to be the footprint of a giant on the high ridge above the western bank of the Bruinen.There are likely other footprints near the first one you found, on the ridge above the western bank of the river in the southern area of Tâl Bruinen.

You found a giant footprint in Tâl Bruinen, and should look for more.Examine enormous footprintsThere are likely other footprints near the others you found, on the ridge above the western bank of the river in the southern area of Tâl Bruinen.

You found some giant footprints in Tâl Bruinen, and should look for more.Examine enormous footprintsCandelleth is at her encampment, Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen.

You found the Elf-brooch in the footprint of a giant that must have come down from the mountains into Tâl Bruinen and should seek to return it to its owner. Perhaps Candelleth will know to whom it belongs.This deep impression appears to be the footprint of a giant. But where did he come from, and to where did he go?

There may be more footprints nearby that can tell the tale.Close examination of this footprint reveals a brooch of Elf-make embedded in the mud at the bottom of the crater.

If you can, you should try to return the brooch to its owner.'Indeed I know to whom this belongs. There is a marchwarden posted upon the High Moor who was once a scout of mine. His name is Ringhul. I recall that he lost it while patrolling the river.'You and Garbert are prepared to set in motion the fisherman's plan to catch the sneaking creature that haunts Tâl Bruinen.Garbert has already prepared some of the trap, but he still needs your help.Talk to GarbertAdwold is waiting for you to place the fish beneath the window.

Adwold has shown you the perfect place to leave the bait for your trap: beneath the large window on the side of Garbert's cottage.Place fish beneath the windowAdwold is preparing to lie in wait for the creature to appear.

You and Adwold must steel yourselves for the springing of the trap.Talk to AdwoldAdwold is hiding behind the makeshift cover Garbert constructed by his cottage.

What was that sound? Adwold is certain he heard something -- could it be the creature?Talk to AdwoldThe sneaking creature has come again to Garbert's cottage, and you and Adwold are ready to spring the trap.

Adwold has told you to wait for his signal before jumping out at the creature and trying to seize it.Grab the creature at Adwold's signalThe sneaking creature is escaping through Tâl Bruinen, and you must follow it if you can.Chase the sneaking creature through Tâl BruinenThe sneaking creature is escaping through Tâl Bruinen, and you must follow it if you can.Chase the sneaking creature through Tâl BruinenThe sneaking creature is escaping through Tâl Bruinen, and you must follow it if you can.Chase the sneaking creature through Tâl BruinenThe sneaking creature is escaping through Tâl Bruinen, and you must follow it if you can.Chase the sneaking creature through Tâl BruinenThe sneaking creature is escaping through Tâl Bruinen, and you must follow it if you can.Chase the sneaking creature through Tâl BruinenYou have lost the creature, but encountered an Orc that seems to have been charged with tracking its movements: this is Udulug, of whom the creature spoke.

Udulug must be defeated.Defeat UdulugAdwold has managed to catch up to you despite suffering a leg injury during the chase.

Adwold is waiting to hear the results of the chase.Talk to Adwold'Are you ready to go?''We are going to trap this creature, ${PLAYER}, I can feel it! It will surely come back to the cottage tonight, and we will be waiting!

'I have already made most of the preparations. We only await Adwold!''This will be a perfect place to lie in wait, ${PLAYER}. Keep your eyes open, for the creature will be back sometime tonight, or so Garbert believes!''There's something out there, ${PLAYER}...I think our creature is nearby!

'There it is again: a soft splashing! He is coming from the water!

'I will give you the signal to jump out and try to grab him -- we want him to be in the middle of eating the fish, so wait for my signal before revealing yourself!''It is a shame that you lost him, but you do not have the experience in tracking that I do, so that is to be expected. You did your best, ${PLAYER}, and I appreciate it.

'I think we gave that creature enough of a fright that he will not be troubling Garbert or Afanen or their child again, and is that not what matters, after all?

'Good work with the Orc, by the by! If it was not for my leg, I would have helped you out with him, of a certainty! I wonder why this Udulug was out here, and what his connexion to our creature might have been? Very strange. Probably it was nothing important.'Haudh Valandur has become home to a group of kergrim, foul creatures of unknown origin.Haudh Valandur is within the Way of Kings, west of the Ranger-camp.

Maladan asked you to go to Haudh Valandur and defeat the kergrim found within.Defeat kergrim in Haudh Valandur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maladan is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Maladan will be pleased to hear that you survived the kergrim of Haudh Valandur.Talk to Maladan in the Way of Kings'When we came here, we thought the only trouble that we would have in these tombs would be a few robbers and then making sure the walls did not come down upon us. 

'No-one foresaw the kergrim, whatever they are. All I know is that they are vicious carrion feeders that will sooner kill you than look at you.

'A group of them have taken to living within Haudh Valandur. That is a problem I need you to rectify.''So it is safe to venture within then?''I have no words of advice beyond strike them first and strike them hard.'The Kergrim are yet another mystery of the lands of Evendim. The Rangers seem to believe that they are a distant cousin of the snow-beasts that range throughout the Misty Mountains, but none can say why they would be here -- or what power has twisted them into these hideous shapes. The implication is that the hand of the Enemy is at work here, somehow, but there is no clear evidence of his power here, otherwise.Defeat Kergrim in EvendimMany of the foul Kergrim appear to have infested the valley in which the tombs of the ancient Dúnedain kings can be found. No doubt the Rangers of the North are enraged by the potential desecration of their ancestors' tombs by these beasts, but they can spare few men to root them out.Defeat Kergrim in EvendimThe denizens of the Way of Kings have ancient keys that may open some of the crypts and tombs within.Collect keys within the Way of Kings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maladan is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Maladan will want to examine the keys you collected.'In a short time, we will want to begin exploring the tombs in this area... seeing the shape they are in, who is within them, driving out those who now occupy them, and recovering precious relics.

'We cannot do that if we cannot get inside them, though. I sent a request to Tinnudir, but none of the keys to these crypts were found within the keep there. Our copies have been lost to history.

'I have seen many of the denizens of the Way of Kings entering and leaving the tombs, however, and believe some must have keys they are using. Go out and collect a handful of them and let us see where we can explore.''If we want to discover the fate of our rulers, we must have the keys to open the crypts and tombs.''I will compare these against our records and see where you may have just gained access to.'The forces of Angmar have erected several monuments around the city of Annúminas.Monuments of Angmar are spread throughout the ruins of Annúminas.

Orchalwë asked you to find several Monuments of Angmar throughout the ruins and hang flags of the Rangers from them.Display Ranger-flags from the monuments of Angmar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Orchalwë will want to speak with you about the monuments of Angmar.Talk to Orchalwë'Annúminas is our city. The ruins and buildings were built by my forebears, and they are monuments to our history, memories of the glory of the past. 

'The Angmarim not only dare to occupy what is ours, they defile it with foul monuments to their false king. It is a slap in the face of every Dúnadan that those stones stand within our city.

'We cannot hope to tear the monuments down...they are too large and we are too few. In the time it would take us to destroy them, they would have us surrounded with more warriors than we could possibly defeat. No, the answer is subtler.

'We will take the monuments and claim them for ourselves. There are six spread throughout the city. Once we find them, I will protect you while you fly a flag of the Rangers from it. We will turn their monument into ours.''While their monuments may still stand, they now spread our message and stand as symbols for the Rangers of Evendim. They may come, but we shall stay.'The Ranger Culang has learned of a great treasure buried long ago by a Dúnadan-landholder and wants it recovered before it is found by tomb-robbers.The treasure may lie beneath another stone marker, somewhere in Evendim, if this riddle is to be believed:

  "On the western shore of mighty Lake Nenuial,
   Stone paths run to the water from a flat clearing."

You should examine the marker when you find it for some clue to the location of the treasure.The inscription on this stone marker is barely legible, but these words can just be made out:

  "On the western shore of mighty Lake Nenuial,
   Stone paths run to the water from a flat clearing."

This new riddle may reveal the true location of the treasure.'Another riddle? This is beginning to border on the ridiculous, ${PLAYER}! How does this one go?

  "On the western shore of mighty Lake Nenuial
   Stone paths run to the water from a flat clearing."

'This sounds rather vague, friend -- the western shore is vast. I suppose you can travel to the far shore and keep an eye open for the stone paths it mentions.'The stone marker is surrounded by signs of digging; if it once marked the location of the treasure, it has surely been found.

The marker bears an inscription, all but worn away by the passage of time.'You are a friend to the Rangers? Happy tidings! Here we were thinking we lacked the numbers to send those tomb-robbers packing, but with your help we should be able to manage it!

'Let's get 'em, boys! Teach 'em to leave the relics of the past good and buried!'Nethúr told you that veteran Orcs carry special medallions which signify their achievements.Orcs can be found in Dol Dínen, south-east of Esteldín, in the North Downs. Nethúr is at Esteldín.

Nethúr asked you to collect Orc battle-medallions and bring them to her.'So, ${PLAYER}, are you ready to face the Orcs in all their strength? Many have marched down now through the passes of the Ram Dúath, and their main encampment lies south-east of here in Dol Dínen, where they prepare to strike down into the heart of Eriador. We have not nearly the numbers needed to face them in force, but we sortie forth and skirmish against them daily in an effort to slow their advance and weaken them before the inevitable battles to follow.

'Those among the Orcs who have faced and survived battles are awarded battle-medallions. If we can defeat these veterans, the resolve of the greater force will be weakened, and there is some hope that they might be held at bay.

'Bring me Orc battle-medallions as proof of your strength and valour, and we shall support your efforts in any way we can.''Well done! You have fought long and hard against the Orcs of Dol Dínen. We thank you for your stalwart efforts and shall find some way to reward you as our meagre supplies allow.'The ruins of Annúminas have fallen to the forces of Angmar.Orchalwë has decided to join the fight and help to reclaim Annúminas.

If you become separated from Orchalwë, you can use the smoke signal he gave you to call him to you.Aid Orchalwë with Untoward AggressionAid Orchalwë with Monuments of AngmarAid Orchalwë with Drowning at the DocksOrchalwë will want to discuss all that has happened.Adadhrond is at Echad Garthadir in Annúminas.

Adadhrond will want a report of how things went with Orchalwë.Talk to Adadhrond'There is much work to do here in order to reclaim the city -- more than we may be able to do -- but we shall still try. At the least, we may preserve some of what is here.

'Orchalwë has come with us to Annúminas. There is much anger within him. I do not trust his judgement to let him go out into the city on his own. I fear he may place himself into a situation he cannot survive.

'I ask you to accompany him. There is much he will want to do, and I believe his goals to be true. Make sure his means of achieving them do not allow him to fall to the darkness.

'Orchalwë will find you when you use this smoke signal. Work with him to reclaim our city.''I do not know if we will ever have the force to retake the city. We may have to simply wait for Angmar to find whatever they want and leave on their own. Hopefully, we can prevent too much damage to the city until that day comes. I thank you for all of your help.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Advancing this quest will no longer allow you to summon Orchalwë and will cancel any quests bestowed by him that are currently underway.</rgb>'We have worked very hard to clear these ruins, and I am quite pleased with our work. There is still much to do, but I feel we will accomplish our goal.'An important Angmarim leader has been seen within Haudh Eldacar.Haudh Eldacar is to the south-west of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam asked you to obtain orders from the commander at Haudh Eldacar.Collect orders from the Angmarim leader at Haudh EldacarRodlam is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam will be eager to begin deciphering the orders you found.'We still do not have a grasp onto why Angmar has come here... and why now? There must be a reason that eludes us.

'One step we can take to try to figure it out is to see if we can get our hands on the orders one of their leaders carries. I have seen one of them near the entrance to Haudh Eldacar. I believe he is leading the searching there.

'Find him within and recover the orders from him, then bring them back here, and maybe we can begin to unravel this mystery.''Those orders might help us discover what is going on here.''I cannot understand much of this but I can make out a name... Amarthiel. Does that mean anything to you?'The last of the tomb-robbers are within the Way of Kings, stripping bare the final resting place of many of the ancient city's rulers.Tomb-robbers can be found within the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir asked you to defeat tomb-robbers within the Way of Kings.Defeat tomb-robbers in the Way of Kings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nethrandir is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir will be pleased to hear that many tomb-robbers have been defeated.Talk to Nethrandir in the Way of Kings'We are close to having finally driven the tomb-robbers from Evendim entirely. There is a small group of them working within the Way of Kings. This was part of their agreement with Angmar. Now that their brethren in the hills are gone, I doubt that Angmar will be eager to protect them.

'If we can thin their numbers, the remainder may flee Evendim for good. Let them run to the barrows of Angmar or the Shire and deal with the guardians there, creatures far more frightening than you and I.''This is good. I sense this business with the tomb-robbers is about to come to its final blow.''Their numbers dwindle, and soon their menace will be gone from our shores.'There are many varieties of elk which dwell in the Trollshaws, which would provide sufficient provender for the hunters loitering at Echad Candelleth.There are elk dwelling in Tâl Bruinen.

While you are here, you should collect venison for the hunters loitering at Echad Candelleth.Collect venison from the elk of Tâl BruinenThere are elk dwelling in Tâl Bruinen.

While you are here, you should collect venison for the hunters loitering at Echad Candelleth.Collect venison from the elk of Tâl Bruinen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are hunters at Echad Candelleth in Tâl Bruinen.

You should bring the venison you collected to one of the hunters in Tâl Bruinen.There are elk dwelling in Tâl Bruinen.

While you are here, you should collect venison for the hunters loitering at Echad Candelleth.'It was good of you to bring this venison to us. It has been too dangerous for hunting, and the Elves only give us cram.'You tracked the creature which devoured the white hart to a fisherman's cottage along the river, and warned the fisherman's wife of the lurking danger.Garbert is at his cottage south of Echad Candelleth, at a fork in the river Bruinen.

Afanen told you to speak with her husband, Garbert, if you are willing to help them drive off the creature and protect their infant son.Talk to GarbertGarbert's fishing nets are placed throughout the waters that flow through Tâl Bruinen.

Garbert has given you permission to check his nets for fish, but has cautioned you that not every net will have fish in it.Garbert is at his cottage south of Echad Candelleth, at a fork in the river Bruinen.

You have collected the day's catch for Garbert and should now bring the fish to him.'Little Whelan is fine, but what if that monster comes back? Mayhaps chance was kind to us and brought us a great hunter? If you wish to help us, you should speak with my husband Garbert.''That is the truth of it, friend -- we cannot leave the house while that creature is still out there. I want it caught as much or more than you do, and I know Afanen feels the same, but I cannot risk leaving the cottage unguarded.

'Here is my suggestion, though: go to my nets and collect this morning's catch, bring it to me, and I will help you set a trap for the creature. It seems the monster has a taste for fish! I have nets strung all over the waters that run through Tâl Bruinen.

'Not every net will be fortunate enough to have snared some fish. That is the lot of the fisherman, my friend: find what you may.''This should be enough, ${PLAYER}. This creature will enjoy these fish, maybe, and then enjoy nothing ever again!'Techeron has asked you to craft sashes for the Rangers of Esteldín to bestow upon their deputies and followers as they wage battle against the forces of Angmar.

Turn in Rangers' sashes to Techeron to improve your standing with the Rangers of Esteldín.Techeron is at Esteldín in the North Downs.

Techeron has asked you to craft a number of Rangers' sashes for the youth of his kindred and bring them to him.'Are you not a tailor of some skill, ${PLAYER}? If so, we have a task in which you might aid us. For many ages, it has been our practice to send those of our kindred who are coming of age on pilgrimages to notable places of our forefathers. The war against Angmar has forced us to change this.

'Here in Esteldín, we give our youths special sashes to signify their coming of age, but supplies of fabric and those with the skill to craft any quantity of them have been short. Most cloth has gone for bandages.

'If you could weave a few of these sashes for us, we would be quite grateful.''You have brought more Rangers' sashes? Very good. We have a need, for we have a number of youths on the cusp of adulthood -- I only wish that more of them could survive their first battles with the Orcs....'Angmar has taken an interest in Haudh Arantar.Haudh Arantar is south of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir asked you to go to Haudh Arantar and defeat the Angmarim within.Defeat Angmarim in Haudh Arantar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nethrandir is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nethrandir will be pleased to hear Angmar has been sent a clear message.Talk to Nethrandir in the Way of Kings'We know little about the reign of Arantar. I have been in his tomb before... a modest place indeed. He was clearly of some importance and must have done something of worth, but that knowledge has been lost to us.

'However, like all the Kings of the North, he wielded a ring gifted to him by the Blue Lady. Legend has it that some virtue resides within the ring, though of no power as significant as the Rings of Power. Nevertheless, it is the prize for which the Angmarim search, I am certain of it.

'Head to Haudh Arantar and drive the Angmarim out. Let them know that they have a formidable foe to deal with, and the tomb-robbers will protect them no longer.''Angmar shall feel our wrath and know that we do not mean to allow them free rein within our homeland.''They will soon learn to fear our approach, thanks to you.'The last of the tomb-robbers are attempting to gain whatever of value they can from Haudh Eärendur before they flee Evendim.Haudh Eärendur is within the Way of Kings, west of the Ranger-camp.

Nimbellas asked you to venture to Haudh Eärendur and defeat the tomb-robbers within.Defeat tomb-robbers in Haudh Eärendur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nimbellas is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nimbellas will be pleased to hear that the tomb-robbers have been defeated.Talk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings'The tomb-robbers have found the place where they will make their final stand. Within the tomb of Haudh Eärendur, they now scramble to take whatever they can. Once they have enough, they will leave Evendim never to return.

'Once you enter, they will have nowhere to go, and we can end this once and for all... on our terms. None shall go unpunished for the acts they have committed against our ancestors.

'Head to Haudh Eärendur and defeat whatever tomb-robbers you find within. End this today, ${PLAYER}.''With this final blow, the tomb-robbers of Evendim will be no more.''That is one threat we shall never have to worry about again.'An infestation of foul crawlers is destroying the roots of healthy vegetation in Tâl Bruinen.There are crawlers infesting Tâl Bruinen, in the Trollshaws.

While in Tâl Bruinen, you should purge as many of the foul crawlers destroying the vegetation there as you can.Defeat crawlers in Tâl Bruinen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are crawlers infesting Tâl Bruinen, in the Trollshaws.

While in Tâl Bruinen, you should purge as many of the foul crawlers destroying the vegetation there as you can.Several tombs and crypts within the Way of Kings have been opened.There is much to do within the open tombs of the Way of Kings.Aid Nimbellas with Robbers of Haudh EärendurAid Nimbellas with Entombed of Haudh EärendurAid Maladan with Kergrim of Haudh ValandurAid Maladan with Valandur's SceptreAid Nethrandir with Ransackers of Haudh ArantarAid Nethrandir with Arantar's RingAid Rodlam with Searchers of Haudh EldacarAid Rodlam with Orders of the Iron CrownNimbellas is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Nimbellas will want to discuss the work done within the open crypts in the Way of Kings.Talk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings'With the threats thinned, the crypts scouted, and these keys in hand, we are ready to venture into the tombs within the Way of Kings. 

'We will focus on the four you discovered to be opened: Haudh Eärendur, Haudh Valandur, Haudh Arantar, and Haudh Eldacar.

'We have each spent some time researching these crypts and reviewing our notes from what we have seen while posted here. There is much to do.''You have done much to help us preserve these tombs and crypts, ${PLAYER}. If the rulers below still lived, I know they would honour and praise you.''Will you lend us your aid?'From the heights of Cirith Ulunn, you saw the rock-worm Sarnemil fleeing to the south along the course of the Bruinen.Sarnemil is at Torech Ullug, south of Echad Candelleth and on the eastern bank of the river by the rapids that flow out of Tâl Bruinen.

You have defeated Sarlug and many Rock-worms, but Sarnemil escaped; however, you saw her flee to the south along the course of the Bruinen. You should return down the slopes to the Bruinen and search southward along the banks for her lair.Defeat SarnemilSarnemil is at Torech Ullug, south of Echad Candelleth and on the eastern bank of the river by the rapids that flow out of Tâl Bruinen.

You have defeated Sarlug and many Rock-worms, but Sarnemil escaped; however, you saw her flee to the south along the course of the Bruinen. You should return down the slopes to the Bruinen and search southward along the banks for her lair.Defeat SarnemilDaervellas is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen, north of Torech Ullug.

You have defeated Sarnemil and ended the threat of her offspring. You should now return to Daervellas with this news.Talk to DaervellasSarnemil is at Torech Ullug, south of Echad Candelleth and on the eastern bank of the river by the rapids that flow out of Tâl Bruinen.

You have defeated Sarlug and many Rock-worms, but Sarnemil escaped; however, you saw her flee to the south along the course of the Bruinen. You should return down the slopes to the Bruinen and search southward along the banks for her lair.'I am pleased at your return, ${PLAYER}! I do not have much, but for the slayer of Sarlug and Sarnemil, I will offer you what I may. Tâl Bruinen is safer for your efforts, and I am glad that it is so.'Angmar has taken an interest in Haudh Eldacar.Haudh Eldacar is south-west of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam asked you to venture within Haudh Eldacar and defeat the Angmarim within.Defeat Angmarim in Haudh Eldacar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rodlam is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Rodlam will want to know that you defeated many Angmarim in Haudh Eldacar.Talk to Rodlam in the Way of Kings'Unlike Haudh Arantar, where the Angmarim are just ransacking and destroying the crypt, the searching at Haudh Eldacar seems to be much more methodical. Very little has been removed thus far.

'Whatever they are looking for there must be of great importance to their purpose here in Annúminas.

'We must delay them while we discover what their goal is. If you were to drive out the party currently searching within, it would buy us valuable time.''I do not yet know their ultimate purpose, but I know that we have set it back, if only ever so slightly.''You must delay them while we search for the reason they are here.'There are many villainous monsters roaming the Trollshaws, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many crawlers in the TrollshawsSlay many giants in the TrollshawsSlay many trolls in the TrollshawsSlay many wights in the TrollshawsSlay many wolves in the TrollshawsSlay many worms in the TrollshawsWhile searching the ruins at Echad Gauradan for Tim Strawley and his stolen figurines, you discovered that there are ritualists among them possessed of some sorcerous power.Gauradan-ritualists can be found at Echad Gaurdan, south of Echad Candelleth.

You should defeat the Gauradan-ritualists, removing the threat they pose to those who dwell in Tâl Bruinen.Defeat Gauradan-ritualistsGauradan-ritualists can be found at Echad Gaurdan, south of Echad Candelleth.

