The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of sleek skin.Wanted: Sleek skin from the beasts in the area of the Bruinen Source.This collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.Indor is very excited to try a recipe that the Dwarf Wéthorm gave to him, but he does not have the necessary ingredients.Toads can be found along the river-banks in Tâl Bruinen.

Indor has asked you to help him collect the various ingredients he needs to make toad stew, a recipe given to him by the Dwarf Wéthorm. He reminded you that only the green river-toads will provide tongues and legs of sufficient quality.Collect slimy toad legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect rough toad tongues (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Indor is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen.

You have collected many bits of toad with which Indor plans to make toad stew. You should bring them to him.There is a grinding stone right next to the camp-fire by Indor, at Echad Candelleth.

Indor is waiting for you to grind the ingredients for toad stew into a mush.Indor is at the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen.

You have ground the toad pieces into mush and should now give them to Indor so he can add the finishing touches to the toad stew.'It's no secret that I consider myself something of a skilled cook, ${PLAYER}. Folk are always giving me new recipes to try, and I spend more time preparing delicious new dishes than I do hunting! You need to follow your own path, that's what I always say.

'I spoke for a while with a very nice dwarf named Wéthorm as he passed through Tâl Bruinen on his way north. He told me he had a delicious recipe for Toad Stew, and after a little bit of coaxing, he agreed to share it with me!

'Would you help me gather the ingredients for it? I still need some toad tongues and legs. You will find toads all along the rivers that run through Tâl Bruinen, I wager. I understand that the green river-toads have the tastiest legs and tongues! Don't come back here with legs and tongues from the red ones. Wéthorm was most specific on that point!''You should be able to find toads all along the river-banks within Tâl Bruinen, ${PLAYER}. I will share the toad stew with you when it is done, so be quick with collecting the ingredients! They hunt in packs, these toads of Tâl Bruinen, but only the green river-toads are tasty enough for me to use!''Very good, ${PLAYER}! I see that you have collected the ingredients I need to make toad stew!

'If you will grind them up on that stone right over there, I would be much obliged.''The grinding stone is right there, ${PLAYER}. Just grind up those toad legs and tongues into mush, and I will add them to the rest of the stew.''Thank you, thank you, ${PLAYER}! Now I will just stir this mush into the rest of the stew, and... it is done!'

Indor takes a big bite of the stew and chews contentedly for a moment. Then an expression of disgust crosses his face, and he spits out his mouthful.

'This is disgusting, ${PLAYER}! It is not at all as delicious as that dwarf claimed!'Orchalwë's rage against the forces of Angmar is seeped in a deep and painful history.Angmarim can be found within the bounds of the city of Annúminas.

Orchalwë is desperate to defeat the Angmarim in Annúminas.Defeat Angmarim in Annuminas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Gertheryg in Annúminas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Orchalwë wants to speak to you.Talk to Orchalwë'Unlike the estates in the hills which you cleared for us earlier, Annúminas holds a special place for me. This is where my ancestors lived their lives.

'They shopped in the markets on these streets, worked in these buildings, fished from this harbour. They danced in the halls of Ost Elendil, swam in the waters of Glinghant, mourned in chambers of Haudh Valandil.

'Now, everything they stood for, what they strived their entire lives to build, the good they brought into this world and nurtured, I fear is now nothing more than the flicker of a dying flame.

'I for one will no longer stand by and watch as Angmar destroys all that I love. It is time that I draw my sword and join this battle.''Though it is tempered slightly, my wrath is not yet sated.'Valandur, a king of Annúminas, was known for his sceptre.Haudh Valandur is to the west of the Ranger-camp within the Way of Kings.

Maladan asked you to venture within the tomb of Haudh Valandur and return a sceptre held by a kergrim within.Collect the sceptre from the kergrim within Haudh ValandurMaladan is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings.

Maladan will be eager to receive Valandur's sceptre.'Valandur was one of the kings who ruled over Annúminas during its glory years. He was a wise and just man, and he was known to his people by his sceptre.

'As he judged a case or complaint, he would carefully ponder the words that were being said. To maintain order, only those holding his sceptre were allowed to speak. When he had made a decision, the sceptre would shine with a white light.

'We had thought this sceptre lost to history, but recently I have seen a kergrim stalking around Haudh Valandur holding it. I believe he makes his nest within the tomb. We must have Valandur's sceptre returned to us!''We must have this sceptre returned to us.''This sceptre is amazing! It is difficult to believe that after all these years it is still intact.'Cerys is concerned about the Stone-trolls that wander into Tâl Bruinen during the night.Stone-trolls sometimes wander out of the north into Tâl Bruinen by night.

The hunter Cerys has asked you to defeat the Stone-trolls that come into Tâl Bruinen at night.Defeat Stone-trolls in Tâl Bruinen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cerys is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen.

You have defeated a number of wandering Stone-trolls and should report of your victory to Cerys.Talk to Cerys'Greetings, ${CLASS}. I've a bit of a problem. I hunt many creatures which come out at night, but alas, it has become too dangerous. Stone-trolls have begun coming down from the mountains at night and wander the paths below.

'I haven't the skill nor knowledge to deal with trolls. You look to be a sturdy adventurer, perhaps with some experience with trolls...would you mind hunting a few? Perhaps then, they'll stay in their mountain haunts.''The woods of Tâl Bruinen can be dangerous and frightening when the moon is hidden among the clouds, but your deeds this night have made the area more safe for unwary travellers. I thank you, friend!'Eirieniel, a Ranger of Evendim located within Annúminas, awaits a delivery of broken halberds at the camp there.You have accepted a task to collect broken halberds from the Angmarim infesting the city of Annúminas and deliver them to Eirieniel at the Ranger-camp within the city.Wanted: Broken halberds from the Angmarim infesting the ruined city of Annúminas. Deliver the items to Eirieniel at the Ranger-camp within Annúminas.Wanted: Broken halberds from the Angmarim infesting the ruined city of Annúminas.'We will drive these evil men from our city. This is proof that it will come to be.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Eirieniel, a Ranger of Evendim located within Annúminas, awaits a delivery of studded sword sheaths at the camp there.You have accepted a task to collect studded sword sheaths from the Angmarim infesting the city of Annúminas and deliver them to Eirieniel at the Ranger-camp within the city.Wanted: studded sword sheaths from the Angmarim infesting the ruined city of Annúminas. Deliver the items to Eirieniel at the Ranger-camp within Annúminas.Wanted: studded sword sheaths from the Angmarim infesting the ruined city of Annúminas.'We will drive these evil men from our city. This is proof that it will come to be.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Defeat Wargs in the Misty Mountains.Defeat Wargs in the Misty MountainsDefeat many Wargs in the Misty Mountains.Defeat Wargs in the Misty MountainsYou 