'Til once more I am needed.Find the answer to Lindir's riddle somewhere in RivendellLindir is with Bilbo in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House.

Boromir has given you a token that provides the answer to Lindir's riddle and told you to bring it to Lindir.'While you were gone, Lindir told me that he has come up with something interesting for our game. Apparently, he found a new riddle on the back of some old parchment out of Gondor.

'You should speak with him at once... I am curious to know his riddle!''Parchment can be difficult to find at times in the world of Men, so I am not all that surprised to find a riddle scrawled on the back of some old chronicles of Gondor. Perhaps some young scribe of the Tower had too much time on his hands....

'It just so happens that the answer can be found somewhere in Rivendell:

'Breath is needed
Warning heeded
Some will arrive
With sword and knife
My work is completed
'Til once more I am needed''What is this? A game? Ha! I see, a riddle out of Gondor is it? Well, you have come to the right man, indeed! 

'Nay, I fear I cannot give you my horn even for a minute -- for a horn is indeed the answer -- because it is my trust and duty to bear it, but I will give you something that should suffice.

'This is the badge of my rank, as the Steward's heir. As you can see it shows a horn above the White Tree of Gondor. I daresay that Elf-loremaster will be satisfied with this token.''Excellent! You have found the answer. I will see that this badge is returned to Boromir.

'Well-played. I trust the fact the item was not just laying on a shelf was no obstacle?'Bilbo has asked you to help out in a riddle-game he is playing with Lindir:

I often hold your hand,
But I have no hands wherewith to hold.
I often sleep in summer,
But I do my best when it grows cold.
I often lose my mate,
But I feel no sorrow, if truth be told.Lindir is standing with Bilbo in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House.

Bilbo has asked you to speak with Lindir about the riddle he presented to the old hobbit.Talk to LindirThe answer to Lindir's riddle lies somewhere in the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Lindir awaits your return in the Hall of Fire.

Lindir is waiting for you to bring him the answer to his riddle.'Hello there, friend ${CLASS}. I wonder if you could help out an old hobbit who is not as spry as he used to be? Lindir and I are playing a friendly riddle-game. Here is his latest:

'I often hold your hand,
But I have no hands wherewith to hold.
I often sleep in summer,
But I do my best when it grows cold.
I often lose my mate,
But I feel no sorrow, if truth be told.

'If truth be told, I'm quite stumped! Speak with Lindir about it -- it could be he has forgotten an important line or two.''I thought for once I would try one of the homely riddles that Bilbo loves so well, rather than an involved mystery of Elf-lore. And so it seems that with his mind in the clouds of Sindarin poetry, our friend here cannot solve old-fashioned riddles of the hobbit-kind!

'But I will give you the hint I gave Bilbo. The answer to this riddle can be found here in the Last Homely House. Just find the answer and bring it here to solve the riddle.''Ha! Well done. The answer fits like a glove, does it not?'Bilbo has a riddle of his own for you to solve:

A long beard I have of bristly hair,
But no chin or cheek on which to bear.
Many hands hold me, with ne'er a caress,
Yet I'm e'er the first to clean up a mess.Bilbo is standing with Lindir in the Hall of Fire.

Lindir told you that it was Bilbo's turn to present a riddle and that you should speak with him.Talk to BilboThe solution to Bilbo's riddle is somewhere in the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Bilbo awaits your return in the Hall of Fire.

Bilbo is waiting for you to bring him the item that solves his riddle.'It seems that we have an expert riddler here!

'It is Bilbo's turn to present a riddle... you should speak with him and learn what he will pose to me.''Lindir out-foxed me! I was rummaging through all my small stock of Elf-lore searching for some poem or tale to fit his verse, but I should have been thinking of more prosaic things, after all. I wonder if he can answer my next little puzzle, though!

'I would like to offer one of my poems on Elven lore, but I dread Lindir's gentle laughter more than a goblin's sword! So I will follow his lead and make another homely riddle, one that I am sure you can solve by finding another item here in the Last Homely House. Here it is:

'A long beard I have of bristly hair,
But no chin or cheek on which to bear.
Many hands hold me, with ne'er a caress,
Yet I'm e'er the first to clean up a mess.''And what could be more homely than a simple besom broom? Even Elves have to clean up from time to time, it seems!'Glorfindel does not know where lies Celebrían's legacy for Arwen, but he has given you some advice which may help you to find it.The lost Elf-vault is somewhere in the Trollshaws in the vicinity of Rivendell, probably on the High Moor. Glorfindel awaits your return outside the house of Elrond, by the waterfall.

Glorfindel told you to seek the vault on the High Moor and advised you to place a hand upon a rock beside the entrance of the Elf-vault and to recite the verses of the riddle. Celebrían's legacy for Arwen, a white jewel, should be somewhere within the vault.Elrond is in the library of Rivendell.

Glorfindel asked you to bring Arwen's legacy to Elrond.'I said that I do not know where the vault containing Celebrían's legacy lies, but it may be that I can help you to gain entrance when it is found.

'The riddle itself is the key to the vault. If in your travels near Imladris you find a sealed vault, those words may offer you passage within. There should be a rock in front of the entrance. Place your hand upon the rock and recite the verse.

'I would be surprised if the jewel is in the vale of Imladris itself as these carefully tended gardens and groves are too often frequented by the Elves for a vault to be easily hidden. I have no doubt it is close by, not far from Imladris... perhaps on the High Moor.''Yes, indeed, this is the jewel itself... Celebrían's legacy. Please bring it to Elrond, as it is his duty to give it to his daughter.''To think that the vault has remained sealed for so long past its time! Even those counted among the Wise can be foolhardy, it seems!

'But I must thank you for your perseverance, Master of Riddles. You seek the truth in all things, even though it brings you into darkness -- your skill and cunning bring you back out into the light again.'A final riddle that bears on Elrond's House in Rivendell is yet to be solved.Bilbo is standing with Lindir in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House.

Lindir told you to speak with Bilbo to learn the unsolved riddle.Talk to BilboElrond is in his library in the Last Homely House.

Bilbo believes Elrond may know more about the riddle.

The jewel of the moon,
Enshrined in the water,
From mother to daughter
Is given a boon.

Ships sail to the west,
Forgetting all sorrow,
Landfall on the morrow,
The isles of the blest.Talk to ElrondGlorfindel is outside the house of Elrond, by the waterfall.

Elrond has directed you to speak to Glorfindel about the riddle.

The jewel of the moon,
Enshrined in the water,
From mother to daughter
Is given a boon.

Ships sail to the west,
Forgetting all sorrow,
Landfall on the morrow,
The isles of the blest.Talk to Glorfindel'You have proven yourself an expert riddle-solver. Bilbo and I have, of late, been contemplating a riddle of the most interesting sort -- one for which no answer is yet known. This riddle seems to bear upon the lineage of the House of Elrond itself and may be of great import if it is solved.

'For once, we cannot say for sure that the answer truly lies in Imladris, but it is certain that the riddle is concerned with Rivendell more than with any other place.

'Bilbo can tell you more, but I think for the full story of this riddle you will have to speak with others as well.''Well, this was written by Elrond's wife, Celebrían, who long ago sailed into the West. Just before she departed Middle-earth, she inscribed these words. The verse was probably not meant as a riddle, but its meaning is nevertheless hidden, even to her own family. I hope you will excuse my poor translation into Westron. The riddle goes like this:

'The jewel of the moon,
Enshrined in the water,
From mother to daughter
Is given a boon.

'Ships sail to the west,
Forgetting all sorrow,
Landfall on the morrow,
The isles of the blest.

'It may be that Master Elrond will be able to tell you something more about these words. It would be splendid if the riddle could be solved after all these years, and even more wonderful if some lost legacy could be found and delivered to Lady Arwen.''Those old words...alas, I had hoped not to have those evil days recalled to me. But I know that Lindir must mean well. Indeed, if there was some legacy of her mother I could give to Arwen, I would do so gladly.

'But the meaning of the words is a mystery to me, and those who might once have known have been gone for long years.

'I wonder at it, since this has come to my mind after so long a space. Glorfindel was present at the time these words were written. I have never thought to speak with him on this subject. Seek him by the falling water outside my house and ask him the meaning of the old words.''A riddle? A mystery? Had but Elrond inquired of me, I could have unravelled these last sad words of his wife long ago.

'There was a splendid white gem, a very jewel of the moon as the verse says, which long ago was hidden away in a secret vault. This is Celebrían's legacy that was meant to go to Arwen. Even I do not know where this vault was hidden, but I am sure it could not have been far from Imladris.'The southern Trollshaws are dominated by the Wilds of Tâl Bruinen. Few even amongst the Elves live here now, and the forested hills have become heavily overgrown and inhabited mostly by wild beasts that pose a constant danger to travellers and the few who try to eke out an existence in these undisciplined lands.Explore the wild extents of the southern Trollshaws.Though worms can be found scattered in other areas of the Trollshaws, the breed here has grown particularly deadly and numerous. Indeed, the aggressive hunting instincts of these vicious beasts do a great deal to dissuade those few explorers and settlers who might otherwise take up their livelihoods in the Wilds of Tal Bruinen.The ruin of Echad Candelleth is believed by scholars to have once been a centre of art and learning in the ancient kingdom of Rhudaur, before it fell beneath the corrupt sway of Angmar and was destroyed in wars with its neighbours after which even its original name was lost.

Now it simply acts as a makeshift camp for those hardy souls brave enough to explore the surrounding wilds.Though it is a wonder to behold, travellers who allow themselves to be lulled by the natural beauty of Eryn Singor rarely emerge from its treacherous ravines.

A host of deadly Wood-trolls have taken up residence within, and delight in descending upon unwary hunters and explorers and tearing them limb from limb.While civilized men long ago quit these hills, a tribe of wild men have recently taken up residence here, seemingly at home amongst the dangerous beasts and natural hazards of the region.

Alas, they are of a savage disposition and display an obvious hatred of those who intrude upon their territory from more civilized lands.It is said that there is a nesting area for the numerous worms who infest Tal Bruinen, and it would seem that you have stumbled upon it here at Torech Ullug.

Take care! The mothers of nesting worms are known for their particulary vicious disposition, as well as a ravenous appetite for fresh meat to feed to their young.What are these strange ruins? They seem to be of ancient Cardolan origins, but the Elves of Rivendell seem hesitant to speak of them at all. Some strange mystery surrounds them, and it may be that the only answers can be found within...The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of Huge Wings.Collection boxes for this task can be found at the camps within the Misty Mountains.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Huge wings from the birds found throughout the Bruinen Source. 

The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of huge wings.Wanted: Huge wings from the birds found throughout the Bruinen Source.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of studded sword sheaths.Collection boxes for this task can be found at the camps within the Misty Mountains.

