The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of studded sword sheaths.Wanted: Studded sword sheaths from the Men and goblins throughout the Bruinen Source.This collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.Dannassel has told you of a number of supply stores hidden throughout the city in times of peace.Stores of supplies are hidden in out-of-the-way locations throughout Annúminas.

Dannassel has asked you to search for supply stores hidden throughout the city and to bring their contents to her. She warned you that Angmarim patrols may have already discovered and looted some of the stores.Collect supplies from hidden stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dannassel is at Echad Garthadir, the Ranger-encampment in the heart of Annúminas.

You have recovered some of the supplies from the stores hidden throughout Annúminas and should bring them to Dannassel.'${PLAYER}, we are in a difficult position. The Angmarim have been unable to force us from Echad Garthadir thus far, but every assault taxes our strength more than the last. We cannot hold out forever, despite Badhordam's efforts to resupply and Fainneleg's cunning strategies.

'Long ago, the Dúnedain hid a number of supply stores of weapons and armour throughout the city, against the fear that some enemy might attempt to take and hold Annúminas. If you can find some of these hidden stores and return to me with their contents, we will be able to replace our damaged equipment and better continue the fight with the Angmarim in the city.

'I do not know the locations of these hidden stores, but if you search in out-of-the-way locations within Annúminas, you will surely find them. It is possible that the Angmarim will have come across some of the stores and looted them.''There should be supply stores of weapons and armour hidden throughout the city. If you can find them and bring them to me, we will be better able to replace some of our damaged equipment and continue the fight against the Angmarim. Be warned that some of the stores may have been looted by the enemy.''You have done very well, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for searching for these stores! They had to be well-hidden for them not to have fallen into the hands of the enemy, so I know you have been particularly wise to have found them.

'Fainneleg will be pleased that we can replace some of our damaged equipment. With these supplies, the fight against the Angmarim here in Annúminas can continue for some days yet!'A terrible Gorthorog stands on the terrace of Tyl Annûn, overlooking the whole of Lake Evendim.The Titan of Tyl Annûn must fall.Defeat the Titan of Tyl AnnûnOrchalwë will want to speak of the battle with the Titan of Tyl Annûn.Talk to Orchalwë'Do you see the creature ahead? He is a terrible Gorthorog, among the strongest they have in their force here. I have seen that one defeat at least a dozen Rangers.

'We call him the Titan of Tyl Annûn, he never steps foot off this island. He stands there and makes us fear coming here.

'It is time to put his reign of terror to an end. Let us defeat the beast.''The abomination has fallen and Tyl Annûn is a little safer. There are still many more to deal with, but now I tread here with more confidence.'Helechír is worried that other Dùnedain ruins in Men Erain may also come under attack.Sid Waring's camp is encamped with Helechír.

Helechír has asked you to warn a man named Sid Waring of the possibility of attack by tomb-robbers.Talk to Sid WaringSome of the stolen relics are on an island next to Sid Waring's camp; others were carried to another island camp to the south in Men Erain. Helechír is at Sid Waring's camp.

Sid Waring has been wounded, but he remains hale enough to tell you he was attacked by men he knew out of Ost Forod. He mentioned a leader called Brychan the Bold and asked you to recover the relics that were stolen from the ruin he was hired to protect.'Alas, that a kinsman and a loyal friend should come to the end of their lives in the ancestral lands of the Dúnedain!

'Alfred Whitley was a good sort, and many of the men that live now in Ost Forod are of his kind -- honest and dependable. And yet, there are some in Ost Forod who stoop to scavenging and robbing the unguarded ruins of Evendim. But to slay one of their kinsmen? This is treachery most foul, ${PLAYER}.

'I ask you to warn some other of the watchers of this danger. Sid Waring is a friend to the Dúnedain and keeps watch from this very camp-site.''Warn Sid Waring of the impending attack... I do not know how much longer I will remain here.''Ah... who are you? You come from Helechír, then? A bit late, friend, but perhaps not too late. I was just attacked by men I know not far from here, neighbours out of Ost Forod who have been driven to evil under the orders of Brychan the Bold.

'These were men I grew up with, kin even, mad for the wealth they say lies hidden in these old ruins! The robbers that attacked me fear no reprisal; you can hear them, even now, digging away on the island just over there! Teach them a lesson, friend, and recover some of the relics they stole! They may have carried some of the relics to another island camp a bit more to the south.

'Go to their camps here in Men Erain, recover the stolen relics and bring them back to Helechír. Tell them there that at least Sid Waring has not forgotten his loyalty, or the oaths he swore.''Find the stolen relics on the island just over there, and on an island further to the south, and bring them to Helechír here at this camp, friend!''It is good to know that the relics the tomb-robbers stole have been recovered. And now we know the name of one of the leaders of this gang!

'We must move swiftly to protect the remaining ruins, ${PLAYER}.'The lynx of the High Moor have become feral, posing a threat to those who come seeking refuge in Rivendell.Lynx dwell upon the High Moor in the Trollshaws.

Canaddal has asked you to cull the number of lynx, securing safe travel through the High Moor once again.Defeat lynx upon the High Moor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Canaddal is encamped on the High Moor in the Trollshaws.

You should return to Canaddal and tell him that you have done as he asked.Talk to Canaddal'${PLAYER}, while I am most concerned with provisioning and outfitting our visitors, I am troubled by something else. The lynx which dwell upon the High Moor have become feral -- no doubt due to the shadow rising in the East. Unfortunately, they pose a great threat to those who journey to Rivendell seeking refuge.

'Would you mind hunting the lynx for me? If their number is culled, then they may, perhaps, be less apt to attack travellers.''The lynx remain a threat, for they are stealthy and cunning. Nevertheless, I thank you.'When the stars of the night sky reflected off the waters here, the Rangers would throw coins in and make wishes.The coins beneath the waters are wishes that never got a chance to be fulfilled.Collect coins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Orchalwë will want to take the coins you collected.'In the days of old, women and children would come here on clear nights. The stars reflect off the waters below and look as if you could reach out and grab them. The mothers would give their children coins to make a wish and throw to the waters, sending their hopes and dreams out among the stars.

'The river was supposed to carry the coins down to the lake, where the legend said the Blue Lady would gather them up. Those wishes she found worthy would be fulfilled.

'I can see several coins that are still in these waters, never having made it...wishes that never had a chance to be fulfilled. Gather those coins up for me, and I shall see that they make it to the lake.''I will take these and bring them down to the waters. I will add a coin of my own and wish that all the hopes and dreams these coins hold be fulfilled, then I shall cast them into the waters.'You received a letter from your trainer in Bree-town asking for you to return to her. Apparently, there is something that she wishes to teach you.Albra Lowbanks sent you a letter requesting that you visit her in the training hall in Bree.

