Brom Hawksbeard'The fine art of brawling isn't just about punching the other fellow, you know: you need to know how hard to hit him, and where!

'These books should help you, as they helped me. And I'll sell them to you for a very nice discount!'You received a letter from Mick Maidenhair, a seasoned Mariner of Bree-town.Mick Maidenhair sent you a letter requesting that you visit him in the Dwarrow-ward, in Bree-town.

Deliver the letter to Mick Maidenhair. He can be found in the Dwarrow-ward, in Bree-town.${PLAYER},

It has been many years since I last heard tell of a Mariner of your skill, but even the most seasoned of us can be made a fool by the Sea. If you wish to learn the finer techniques of the Mariner, come and speak with me in the Dwarrow-ward of Bree-town.

Mick Maidenhair'Yes? Ah, my letter. It is good to meet you at last, ${PLAYER}!

'It is true enough that many lessons can be only learned upon the deck of a ship, but even so, there is much to be gained by studying the accounts of the great Mariners of the world with your feet firmly planted on the ground! I have several books in my keeping that might be of use to a Mariner such as yourself. Perhaps they will help you, as they have helped me over the years. If you wish to study them further, I'll offer them to you for a fair price.

'You might need the knowledge they contain when you least expect it!'Scholar Deluros has reassembled an ancient vase from the fragments you retrieved in the Misty Mountains, and seeks to teach Glorenglir a further lesson.Glorenglir is in Rivendell, and a table nearby would be a suitable place to set the vase you have been given.

Scholar Deluros has asked you to place the vase he reassembled on the table near Glorenglir, observe her reactions, then return to him.Scholar Deluros is in the library of Elrond's House in Rivendell.

Deluros is waiting to hear if Glorenglir recognized the vase he reassembled.'We have been very fortunate, ${PLAYER}, for some of those fragments were indeed once part of this vase. I have repaired it as best I can, and the beauty it once had has returned in some measure!

'I have another task for you, ${PLAYER}. There are tables throughout Rivendell on which pieces of art and history are sometimes placed for contemplation. Bring this vase to a table near Glorenglir. If she recognizes it as being the sum of the fragments you earlier uncovered for her, I shall agree to further her instruction as a scholar and give her leave to study some of the more valuable artifacts kept here at Imladris.

'If she does not recognize the vase, she will have received my final lesson. Place the vase on the table, observe her reactions, then return to me, and we will speak further.''Glorenglir is in Imladris. Go to her and place the vase I have reassembled on a table by her location. Gauge her reaction to it and return to me.''Hello, ${PLAYER}. Any word yet from Master Deluros?''That vase has a small measure of beauty, ${PLAYER}. Is it from Lord Elrond's collection?

'Have you forgotten to tell Master Deluros of my inspiration concerning the snow-lurkers, ${PLAYER}? You will find him in the library of the House of Lord Elrond!''It does not surprise me that Glorenglir failed to recognize the vase, ${PLAYER}, even though she had some part in restoring it.

'I thank you for your assistance, and I hope the lesson of Glorenglir will stay with you! Be not so eager to advance that you fail to experience the moment, ${PLAYER}, in life and in all things.'Maervellon thinks he finally knows where his talisman is. He certainly doesn't act like any Ranger you've met before....The half-orcs of Thelgarth are sure to have Maervellon's lucky talisman. Sure they are.Defeat half-orcs in Thelgarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maervellon remains outside the fortress of Thelgarth, in the Angle.Talk to Maervellon outside Thelgarth'${PLAYER}, just the adventurer for whom I was looking! How have been your travels in these wild lands, with which I am well-accustomed? Mine have been rather fruitless I'm afraid... until now, that is! I have journeyed hither and yon, and now my searching has revealed just who stole my precious talisman! The half-orcs who reside now in the fortress of Thelgarth, atop this very hill!

'What's that? I did not mention half-orcs before now? I am certain I did. You must have misunderstood me when I spoke of half of the foe-men arrayed before me being Orcs. An honest mistake. I forgive you.

'You have helped me so much to this point, I am sure you want to finish this, my friend! Climb up to Thelgarth and defeat as many half-orcs as it takes to find my lucky talisman!

'You'll help me see this through to the end, won't you?''That was quite a feat! So tell me, friend, which villain was it who pocketed my lucky talisman?'

You shake your head and hold up empty hands.

'Wh-what? But... that's impossible. Are you sure you bested the right ones?

'B-but that can't be, that necklace was given to me by some very important people... I can't have lost it....

'Listen, my friend, I suppose it is time you knew the truth. I am no Ranger. I merely wish I was as heroic and courageous as they are. I am but a humble traveller on whom the Rangers took pity. I looked up to them so much! I wanted to do everything just like they can! They looked after me for a few weeks, and during that time they gave to me that talisman as a way to keep that dream alive. I thought one of the brigands that attacked me might have taken it but in reality... I might have dropped it. I spun a yarn to save my pride. I am sorry, friend.'

So defeated, Maervellon slumps to the ground. As he does so, something startles him and he rises once more to his feet. Reaching into his back pocket, he pulls out an oddly shaped necklace. His face turns crimson.

'Oh! Er... ${PLAYER}, th-this is the talisman for which I was searching! It was... in my pocket the whole time? Oh, I am such a fool... to think I imagined a tale so dangerous, I myself believed it to be true.... Don't think too badly of me, ${PLAYER}. I was very distraught!

'But nonetheless, you helped me on this craban hunt the whole way. And though it proved rather unnecessary, it was not a thankless task. I will do my best to live up to the Rangers I so admire, and I think that may begin with the purchase of trousers with frontward facing pockets!

'Thank you for all your help, ${PLAYER}, and uh, sorry for all the trouble!'It seems that this Ranger is a bit more scatterbrained than you thought, now believing the wargs made off with his talisman.Wargs can be found among the old burrows of Glynafon, in the Angle.Defeat wargs in the Angle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maervellon is near the old hobbit-burrows of Glynafon, in the Angle.Talk to Maervellon at Glynafon'Well if it isn't ${PLAYER}! How have you been, friend? I have some exciting news! While seeking more Orcs to find my lucky talisman, I remembered something: it wasn't the Orcs that took it!'

You ask him if he sustained a knock on the head during his brawl with whatever foes he fought.

'Ah, you jest, my new friend, but Rangers like me often do battle with whatever enemies cross our path: and in my case it was both brigands and Orcs, as I told you before. No, not together, not at the same time, but one after the other. I swear it.

'But I am pretty certain the brigands did not take my talisman, for they were frightened of the Orcs and would not remain in their presence for any period of time, I imagine. But you know who DID remain by the side of the Orcs? Wargs, of course!

'The Orcs I fought were warg-riders, and they must've stashed my talisman inside one of the supply pouches borne by their horrible steeds! So you see, all we have to do is find the warg that carries my talisman! There are lots of them around here, ${PLAYER}. You should check it out! You'd be helping a Ranger, and that counts for a lot in the wild, doesn't it?''Ah, ${PLAYER}, I hope you had better luck than I....'

You shake your head.

'Ah, well.' He curses under his breath before turning back to you.

'I suppose I'll just have to think of something else. There is a great fortress on the southernmost promontory of this land; perhaps I will check there. Should we run into each other again I hope to report that I found the talisman! Farewell.'It seems that a Ranger has somehow lost something very important to him.Slay Orcs within the Angle and keep an eye out for the lost talisman.Defeat Orcs in the Angle and keep an eye out for Maervellon's talisman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Maervellon outside the ruins of Eitheldir.Talk to Maervellon outside Eitheldir'Oh, you startled me! Well-met traveller, I am Maervellon, Ranger of these wood-lands. But I ask that you keep your voice low, for I am tracking down a voracious band of thieves. I trailed the brigands to this ruin, but now I see there are mostly Orcs here....'

The Ranger peers nervously about.

'There have been a few Orc raids through these woods of late, and recently we brawled a good while. Fear not, for I survived with nary a scratch, but those blasted thieves made off with my lucky talisman! It is a charm we Rangers keep for good luck while on the hunt.'

You ask him if he fought with Orcs or with brigands and he peers into the distance.

'Oh, you know... both, really. There were quite a lot of them. This might go a lot faster if you were to aid me in this endeavour. You do look capable enough. All I need is my talisman, you can keep any other treasure we find! So, what do you say? Care to help me retrieve my lucky charm and slay some Orcs?''You're back! Any luck?'

You shake your head. His expression breaks for a moment, but he quickly regains his smile.

'Ah, same results on my end, I'm afraid. Oh well, I'm sure it will turn up. I could've sworn... ah, no matter.

'Thank you for your help all the same, ${PLAYER}. I will think on this, and perhaps wander the area further south-east, beyond the old hobbit-burrows. That is the life of a Ranger, is it not? Until we meet again.'The League of the Axe no longer considers you an outsider, instead they welcome you as an ally against the enemies and repression that they face.You must earn Ally standing with the League of the AxeThe Woodcutter's Brotherhood now know to call upon you in times of strife, and they consider you a skilled ally.You must earn Ally standing with the Woodcutter's BrotherhoodThe ending of this tale is yours to determine.Use Scribe a New EndingThough passage into the Angle is complicated by the rivers that border it, the Elves of Rivendell are concerned by the increased presence of the Enemy's servants.Tham Lumren is in the north-east Angle.

