You should speak to Thalathril.Speak to Thalathril'Between Elladan's note and your accomplishments here, I am willing to trust you with a task, if you are willing. Take this report to Thalathril. She is at Tham Lumren, a camp in the north-eastern part of this land. Your assistance in this will mean that I can continue my watch here, yet still provide her with the information she needs. It is highly probable that she could use your help as well.''Daro! Who comes so boldly to Tham Lumren?'

You show the guard the report.

'Elladan trusts you, it seems, as does Merileg, but our eyes are on you, stranger. You may pass. You will find Thalathril near the large tent.''Who are you? I do not recognize you.'

You hand her the report, which she looks over.

'I see. It would be false of me to say that your assistance was not welcome at this time. We can use your help here, stranger.'Build your sprinting stamina with focused training.Use SprintBuild your sprinting stamina with focused training.Use SprintOst Elendil, beyond the bridge of Ariant, was once the high seat of the kings of Annúminas. No longer -- after lying abandoned for a terribly long count of years, it is now held by the evil that came out of Angmar.

Of Amarthiel's lieutenants, the Black Númenórean named Balhest is surely the most cruel. He it is that sits in Ost Elendil and holds it against us behind an army of fell spirits and Angmarim sworn to him.

Balhest must be defeated if we are to retake the city, ${PLAYER}. If it can be done, it must be. The Dúnedain cannot fight this foe alone. If I am not here when you return, bring this news to Captain-General Daerdan at Echad Garthadir, for he will be most pleased at your success!Balhest, one of Amarthiel's mightiest Black Númenórean lieutenants, is in Ost Elendil.

Legrindavor has asked you to put an end to Balhest so that Ost Elendil might be reclaimed.Defeat BalhestOnora and her husband Rúdhan need somewhere more sheltered to rest.Onora has asked you to investigate the rocks to the north-west in search of food to forage.Find food for Onora and Rúdhan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A fresh bear carcass could supply plenty of food for Onora and Rúdhan during their recovery.Collect some meat from the fresh bear carcassHead back to Onora and tell her about the shelter.'Rúdhan's injury is worse than we thought. We might need to stay here longer than I expected.

'But there is always food to be found in the wild, if you know where to look. There should be some berry bushes somewhere nearby, perhaps among the rocks to the north-west. Now, such a bounty will attract wild beasts, but that should be no real danger for such as you, should it? We heard the growling of what sounded like a large bear shortly before we made it to this river... but perhaps it has already moved on.

'We would both greatly appreciate any food you can bring back to us: berries, meat, or vegetables. When my husband's strength has returned we will move on.''A bear, and a troll? These wilds are very dangerous, it seems! But you bested these threats and returned with food, and for that you have the thanks of both Onora and Rúdhan!'Glóin thinks that the dwarves may be overstaying their welcome at Rivendell and wishes to renew his guest-gift to Elrond.There may be great white bears to the east and south of Glóin's camp. There may be brown bears north of Glóin's camp.

