In the north, through the Ram Dúath, there is an encampment of Hillmen who have been free of Angmar's sway for years. My leader has trained some of these men, but we are in need of aid.

Seek me out at Aughaire, the encampment on the northern edge of the Ram Dúath. I am in a tent among a circle of stones.

Corunir'I am glad to see you.

'You should make your way among the people here. They will not shy from you. There is much that needs doing here and they will be grateful for any aid. This place is in dire need, friend.'Train to perform your heroic tales with less effort but equal effect.Recite any taleLead with the fist, and the rest will follow.Strike with Surety of Death, Resolution, or Spear of VirtueLead with the fist, and the rest will follow.Strike with Surety of Death, Resolution, or Spear of VirtueThe Ford of Bruinen is the last bastion of security leading to the hidden vale of Rivendell.Complete all encounters at the Ford of Bruinen.Defeat ZanúrzDefeat KunquinDefeat DurkúfSupply the archersDefeat BruidagnirYou have earned the trust of the League of the Axe -- even their friendship -- and they now treat you far differently than any other outsider.You must earn Friend standing with the League of the AxeThe Woodcutter's Brotherhood has grown to count you among its friends.You must earn Friend standing with the Woodcutter's BrotherhoodAn elderly couple uncovers ancient secrets and threats on the road to join their son.The road to Tornhad is in the western Angle.

