Elladan has asked you to see how fares the elderly couple headed to Tornhad.Talk to the elderly coupleOst Waeren is near the road south of Eitheldir.

Waltney Maythorn has asked you to investigate the ruins of Ost Waeren.Defeat Ost Waeren ravagers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Waltney and Garan Maythorn are located near Ost Waeren.

You should let Waltney and Garan know that the ravagers have been defeated.Return to the elderly couple'I have another task for you, if you are willing. A couple, most advanced in age as far as Men go, passed through my camp recently. The Maythorns are on their way down to meet their son, a Ranger living in Tornhad. The couple refused to turn back, and I was unable to offer them an escort. If you happen to be travelling that way, please look for them and give what help you may. The roads south are dangerous, and the elders are not the sort who can protect themselves against the threats of the Angle.''Greetings fellow traveller! Oh, Elladan sent you, did he? Hmph. I knew he would not be able to let us alone. We do not need help! Well, that is, we did not need help until a few moments ago.'

He sighs, wringing his hands.

'I am Waltney Maythorn the Second and this is the wife, Garan Maythorn. We are travelling south to meet our son, Waltney the Third, and his family in Tornhad. Trouble is, you see, there is something not of this world on the road ahead, or my horse is pink. Perhaps, if you happen to be going that way anyhow, you could see whether the road is clear? I would do it myself, of course, but my knee is not what it used to be.''Elladan told us this place was called Ost Waeren. The stones of these ruins hold memories. Echoes of those who walked beneath now fallen arches, who slept within the crumbled walls, and who perished in the many battles this land has seen. I will be more than happy to be pressing on.''You return! You have my thanks for your assistance, friend! We can press on to Tornhad now!'Glinghant was once the most beautiful place in all of Annúminas -- no small feat given the splendor of the ancient city at its height. Descriptions of the pools and gardens of Glinghant hold a special place in the hearts of my people. Even after the long years of decay, you could see the memory of its beauty.

The coming of Amarthiel and her legions to Annúminas is cause itself for sorrow, but of all the harm they have caused to this city, their possession and despoiling of Glinghant stirs me most to rage. I would cast them out of this place and restore the splendour it had of old, even should the rest of Annúminas fall. In that, I am not joined by most of my kindred, but such is my horror at the spoiling of Glinghant.

Amarthiel has many servants, but to Glinghant she has sent the darkwater: foul spirits of corruption led by a grisly demon called Nengon. If you should venture beyond the gate into the terraced steps of Glinghant, I would account you highly should you defeat Nengon and his corrupting brethren.Nengon and his darkwater brethren are within the pools and gardens of Glinghant, beyond the court of Clorhir.

Harthadril has asked that you enter Glinghant and defeat the darkwater that have despoiled its beauty.Defeat NengonJónar, a sinister and surly resident of Thorin's Hall, has grown increasingly sour towards the success of the Inn League.Nathalan can be found in Angmar. Wesley Hopwood is in Bree-land. Alrek is in Ered Luin. Lendasil may be found in Ered Luin. Harigar Mudbottom is in Evendim. Lófi is in Forochel.

The spiteful dwarf Jónar has asked you to deliver fake versions of the Inn League members' requests all over Middle-earth.'We have stolen their recipes, emptied their kegs, and harried those who wished to join them. Now we shall attack the very core of the Inn League -- the members themselves!

'There are travellers all across Middle-earth, clamouring for the beers, ales, and wines that they could not bring with them. How do I know this? Never you mind! I have my sources, and they are trustier than you!

'Now there is but one thing left to do, and then my sabotage will be complete, and the Ale Association is sure to be a success! I have gathered many drinks and poured them all into tankards, and now I give them to you. Deliver them to each requestor! Do not let on that I have poured the wrong beverage into each glass. Ha, ha! Ha, ha, ha! They will hate the Inn League after they have tasted what I have given them.''Take a taste of that swill, ${RACE}. Do you think it will be as foul as the original? Ho, ho, ho, ha, ha, ha! Ha... ha, ha!''Have you brought me Swill for the Inn League Challenge? Excellent; now give it here. I expect it to be truly despicable.'

Nathalan takes a deep drink from the odious-looking mug of fake swill, which is actually the delicious Shire Spice Ale in disguise. He seems momentarily confused.

'Disgusting! Foul stuff -- I think. Come to think of it, that was not what I expected. Oh my! It has a rather pleasant after-taste. Hmm.''Is that Limael's Vintage? What a fortunate turn of events! Let us give this a taste.'

Wesley Hopwood sniffs the glass, and then sips it, swirling the wine around before swallowing it.

'Delicious! Now that is a fine wine, though... it tastes a bit familiar. Hmm.''Ah, the Forsaken Ale! This will make up for all the calamities of the Inn League Challenge, no matter how unsavoury the taste.'

Alrek holds his nose and drains the mug quickly, making a face despite the smoothness of Barliman's Best.

'Plhaugh! Pleh! Splah! Foul stuff. No, wait... that is not bad. It was actually rather good. Now I am confused -- everyone told me it was very bad. Why would they lie? Am I losing my knack for tasting? Hmm....''Dorwinion White! It cannot be! It... it is red? How odd. A red-coloured white wine. Hmm.'

Lendasil takes a sip, but shakes her head sadly.'Ah, the Blagrove's Brown from my humble home! When I drink this, I shall be able to show my face again, and I will boast to all of the delightful flavours of this classic ale. It is a little whiter in colour and odour than I expected, but that is all right. Hmm....

'Thank you, friend. I will enjoy this, and stand upon the table-tops in Michel Delving to tell tales of this fine brew.'

Harigar looks happily at the Whitebranch, which he thinks is Blagrove Brown, and drinks it all.'Moor-boar Beer! Now we can finish the Inn League's Challenge. I shall drink this batch before it freezes.'

Lófi takes a hearty gulp of the beer and raises an eyebrow. Little does he know that he just drank Toad's Tongue Ale, and not Moor-boar Beer at all.

'It does not remind me so much of boar, in the end. It is a little slimy. Warty, too, if a beer can be warty. Not that I mind it... but it is strange, nonetheless. Hmm.'You are more than just a champion for the people of Middle Earth, you are a true hero.Hit enemies with True HeroicsMalthenor is concerned about the bears that prowl the mountains and wants you to fight against them.Bears are found throughout the Misty Mountains: near the Bruinen Source, by the High Crags, north of Glóin's Camp, and close to the Giant Halls.

Malthenor has asked you to defeat bears throughout the mountains to lessen the threat they pose to potential travellers.Defeat bears in the Misty Mountains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Malthenor is located in Glóin's camp.

Malthenor will be pleased to hear that you have defeated many bears throughout the mountains.'The snowbeasts are a threat near the source of the Bruinen, but they have not spread throughout the mountains as much as other creatures. It is easier to guide travellers past them in a way that is impossible with the more widespread threats.

'This is not true of the bears that prowl the slopes, not only near the source of the Bruinen, but also further east among the high crags beneath Pinnath Fenui and as far south as the Giant Halls around Iorbar.

'If you can defeat many of the bears in these areas, the slopes will be made safer for travellers. Watch yourself as you hunt the bears of these regions, for they may surprise you with their numbers and their savagery.''Bears can be found throughout the Misty Mountains. Defeat as many as possible to ensure the travellers along the road will be made a good deal safer.''You have become a true foe of the savage bears that prowl the mountains, ${PLAYER}, and I am glad of it! Every beast that is slain makes the wild country safer for those who must journey there.'Glóin sent a letter requesting your presence at his encampment north of Rivendell in the Misty Mountains.Glóin's camp is west off of the road that leads up and north out of Rivendell. Seek him out and speak with him.

Glóin sent a request for you to come and visit him at his encampment in the Misty Mountains.Talk to Glóin at his camp in the Misty Mountains${CLASS},

I have headed north into the Misty Mountains to seek old remembrance and find a bit of sport. Others have come with me, and our camp can be found to the west of the path that leads north out of Rivendell.

Seek me out, if you will.

Glóin'Look here: an adventurous soul,

'Good to see you. Look about you: many a dwarf here, and all with something or other to do. I never thought that seeing these mountains would restore such vigour in me, but I feel better already.

'If you are looking for work, we have it, I promise you this.'With practice, the right comeback may no longer require a mind set only to mischief.Strike with Clever RetortHaldúr has informed you that Garbert has fallen on hard times and could use some business.Garbert is at his cottage in Tâl Bruinen, south and west of Rivendell.

Haldúr has asked that you visit Garbert and purchase fishing supplies from him because of his injuries.Talk to Garbert'Now that you have learned the ways of the fisherman you will be needing supplies. Though the Elves of Rivendell excel in the craft, a Man of the Trollshaws -- Garbert by name -- has fallen on difficult times.

'Garbert was injured, as Men so commonly are, and cannot travel. His sale of fish and fishing supplies has been much diminished, and I worry for him and his family. He is very skilled in matters of the rivers and waters for a Man; his prowess almost reaches that of Elrond's folk.

'If you wish to find supplies, I would ask that you visit Garbert. He should be at his cottage in Tâl Bruinen, south of here, near to the river.''Why, hello there! It is unusual to see a fellow fisherman this far down the Loudwater, what with the times being what they are these days.

'You say the Elves sent you? I have had dealings with some of their folk, but I did not know that they thought so highly of me to send me business in my need!''Have you visited Garbert? His cottage is south and west of Rivendell along the Bruinen in Tâl Bruinen.'Handarod is concerned with the snow-beasts which have been attacking Glóin's camp up in the Bruinen Source regions of the Misty Mountains.Snow-beasts may be found throughout the Bruinen Source regions of the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell, far to the south and east of the North Downs.

Handarod has asked you to defeat snow-beasts in the Bruinen Source regions.Defeat snow-beasts in the Bruinen Source (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Handarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the west and north of the Misty Mountains.

You should return to Handarod and tell him of your snow-beast hunt.Talk to Handarod'I have received an urgent message from the dwarf Glóin, who has maintained a watch-post up in the western regions of the Misty Mountains, above the passages to Rivendell.

'He claims that the local population of snow-beasts -- normally reclusive, though still dangerous beasts -- have recently launched relentless attacks upon him and his companions.

'Glóin has asked that I send someone skilled in battle to help hunt down these beasts and frighten them away from his camp.''I hear that your snow-beast hunt went well. Glóin's latest messenger asked me to commend you for your efforts on behalf of him and his kin. Well done, ${PLAYER}.'Deflect and evade the enemy's attacks.Parry or Evade enemy attacksYou have heard that there may be a more complete form of the sign you uncovered previously.Strike with Sign of Power: CommandKnowledge of the natural world has given you subtle influence over its natural fluctuations, but there is deeper knowledge still to be gleaned through study.Strike with Storm-loreKnowledge of the natural world has given you subtle influence over its natural fluctuations, but there is deeper knowledge still to be gleaned through study.Strike with Storm-lore or Lightning StrikeThe darkwater that have occupied Glinghant are vile, corrupting creatures sent by Amarthiel for the purpose of despoiling the beauty of its pools and gardens. The beauty it had of old is lost, and the water's taint now spreads through the city. I fear that the corruption will soon spread to Lake Nenuial if something is not done!

It was not an easy matter, but I spoke with Gwindeth, the Blue Lady of Nenuial, and acquired a phial of clean water with which we may be able to purify the pools of Glinghant. The phial does not contain much, so we must not waste it, but if it might be poured into the pools on each of Glinghant's three terraces, we might be able to purify the waters and thus lessen the corruption of the darkwater.

The entrance of Glinghant is here at the court of Clorhir. Pour some water from this phial into the pools on each terrace of Glinghant and return to me when you have done so. We may still be able to cleanse away some of this evil, ${PLAYER}! If I am not available when you return, please speak with Captain-General Daerdan, at Echad Garthadir, here in the city.The entrance to Glinghant is located in the court of Clorhir, in Annúminas. Glinghant consists of several terraces, and every terrace supports a pool of water.

You should pour some water from the phial of clean water she gave you into each of the terrace pools in Glinghant.Find the pool on the second terraceThe Elf-smiths of Elrond have begun to reforge Narsil, the blade that was broken, an heirloom of Elendil's line.Aragorn is waiting to speak with you just outside the forges of Rivendell.

Elf-smiths are reforging Narsil, the blade that was broken.At the forges of Rivendell, the Elf-smiths of Elrond are hard at work remaking the sword of the kings.

Elf-smiths have begun the work of reforging Narsil.Witness the reforging of NarsilAragorn is at the forges of Rivendell.

Aragorn wishes to speak with you.'Are you ready, ${PLAYER}? The air tonight feels full of promise, and I have resolved to leave any doubts I have behind me. For Narsil to be reforged this night feels unreal to me, as if I will wake in the House of Elrond and find this has all been a dream.''I can hardly believe that Narsil has been remade, but the feel of Andúril in my hand quells all my doubt! This night has been long in coming, ${PLAYER}, and I marvel at it!''Let us return to the House of Elrond. Many are the friends that wait within, and I would show them Andúril that they may know what has been done this night.''I know that Aragorn has long hoped this night would come and feared that it would not. At last, the sword has been reforged!'You have journeyed into the Tomb of Elendil in search of the Silithar needed to reforge Narsil.Idella Crypt-breaker is somewhere within the depths of the tomb of Elendil.

Calenglad was right -- Idella Crypt-breaker's gang of tomb-robbers has taken advantage of the newly-lowered waters to plumb the depths of the tomb for treasure. She must be stopped.Gwindeth has come to the Tomb of Elendil, and is waiting to speak with you in its deepest chamber.

You have dispatched Idella Crypt-breaker, but there is no sign of the Silithar.The Silithar is somewhere in the caverns beneath the tomb of Elendil.

You did not find the Silithar in the final chamber of the tomb of Elendil -- it must have been carried somewhere by the retreating waters.Find the SilitharGwindeth is now in the cave beneath the tomb of Elendil.

