'Spiders make silk. We need silk. You kill spiders, take their silk, then we give you the Orcs' shiny metal.

'We have much shiny metal taken from Orcs. Little people like shiny things, yes?''Good silk. Here is the shiny metal.'No matter how well-placed the strike, there is always room for improvement.Strike with Well-placed StrikeDefeat the Dead within Annúminas.Defeat the Dead within AnnúminasDefeat the Dead within Annúminas.Defeat the Dead within AnnúminasRenew yourself in the midst of battle.Use Bracing RoarMaster drawing greater strength from the courage you share with your fellows.Use the Muster Courage skillStrike fear into the heart of your enemies and learn what it is that makes them flee.Strike with Bard's Arrow or Cry of the PredatorMaster the call to arms and the empowerment of your shield-brother.Use the To Arms skillMaster the call to arms and the empowerment of your shield-brother.Use the To Arms skillYou are able to convey epic meaning through fewer words.Use Epic for the AgesElrohir is concerned the safety of the Angle might be threatened.The small camp-site at Gaerond is located south of the Trollshaws, in the northern reaches of the Angle.Journey to the camp-site at Gaerond, in the Angle of MitheithelElladan has come to Gaerond, in the Angle.Talk to Elladan at Gaerond'A good distance to the south, nestled between the Loudwater and Hoarwell rivers, there is a wooded and rock-studded land known to those who dwell there as the Angle of Mitheithel.

'Will you venture there and learn if all is well in that place? The Angle has a tumultuous history, and I would not have those days return if they might be prevented by safe-guarding its people.''Will you venture south to the Angle and learn if all is well? That land has a tumultuous history, and I would not have those days return if they might be prevented by safe-guarding its people.''My brother was right to ask us to come here, ${PLAYER}. I cannot long stay, but what I have seen reveals that the land is unsettled. Something stirs in the wild.

'The land between the rivers is not densely populated, but the folk here must be protected. Can I ask you to do this?'Waltney and Garan Maythorn are nearing Tornhad, but is their son, Waltney Maythorn III, ready for their arrival?Waltney Maythorn III is in Tornhad.

