You should bring the fresh meat to Thorn.Return to Waltney Maythorn III'You have done much for us, but I wonder if you could spare the time for another task. Tornhad is not far away, but with Waltney jumping at every shadow he thinks might be a shade, our going will still be delayed. If you happen to find your way to the town, please let our son Waltney Junior know that we are very nearly there. I would not want him to worry.''Well met! Yes, I am Waltney Maythorn III. I go by Thorn, however.'

You tell him of his parents' impending arrival.

'What?! My parents are coming here? Today?! Those old fools! I told them to stay in Bree where it was safe! Oh dear. This is terrible! I must excuse myself. My home is nowhere near ready to accommodate those two nitpickers. If my mother were to arrive and see my hole-ridden socks hanging by the fire I should never hear the end of it!

'I thank you for helping them cross the Angle. What a nightmare this is! Say, would you be up for assisting me? I must rush off to my house and do what cleaning I may, and my larder is emptier than if I had had hobbit guests! If you were to hunt a bit for me and bring back some boar meat, I would really appreciate it!''Oh hello! Please tell me you have something I can serve for dinner? Oh my. This is better than I could have done myself by far! Thank you so much! I still have much to do before my home is ready for my parents, but at least dinner is possible now! Well, if you will excuse me, I have much yet to do.'Defeat beasts in Urugarth.Defeat beasts in UrugarthDefeat beasts in Urugarth.Defeat beasts in UrugarthYou have returned the last of the Silithair to Aragorn, and now the time has come for Narsil to be reforged.Aragorn is in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House.

The Elf-smiths of Imladris will reforge the blade that was broken, and Aragorn is waiting to walk with you to the forges where it will be done.Talk to Aragorn in Rivendell and travel to the forgesAragorn is in one of the guest rooms along the road that winds up the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris.

Andúril, Flame of the West, has been forged from the shards of Narsil, and Aragorn is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Aragorn in Rivendell'The time has come, ${PLAYER} -- Narsil will be reforged.

'Will you accompany me to the forges? The work will take some time, but I would have you there at Andúril's making. Speak with me when your affairs are in order, and we can walk there together.''Let us walk to the forges, ${PLAYER}. It will be some time before the sword is completed, and we can take in the air while the Elf-smiths of Elrond work their craft.''My heart tells me that Gandalf speaks true, ${PLAYER}: it will take more than a sword, even a sword as well-crafted and with such lineage as Andúril, to fight the will of the Enemy. But I know this as well: we will do what we must, no matter the cost! We will stand opposed to all who threaten the safety of Middle-earth and will not rest until the Enemy is laid low and my people restored to safety and to plenty.

'You are wondering why I did not tell you what it was that Gwindeth was seeking? That is hardly a riddle, ${PLAYER}! When I journeyed with Calenglad to claim the Silithar those long years ago, Gwindeth turned me aside with the rebuke that I was not yet ready for the sword to be reforged; indeed, I was not. How might events have been different if I had retrieved it at that young age? How might events have changed if Amlaith had taken it with him to Fornost?

'We cannot see the ends of every road, ${PLAYER}. I withheld that information from you, for I believed that if the time was truly ripe, if Narsil was supposed to now be reforged, you would know for what Gwindeth asked without my telling you. It seems that on this matter, at least, I have been proven correct. Rejoice, ${PLAYER}! Dark days may lie ahead, but we will face them now with the light of Andúril before us and friends at our backs!'Explore the ruins of the ancient city of Annúminas.NOT USEDYou have discovered Gwaelband in Annúminas.You have discovered Gaerannon in Annúminas.You have discovered Echad Garthadir in Annúminas.You have discovered Menelband in Annúminas.You have discovered Clorhir in Annúminas.You have discovered Tirband in Annúminas.You have discovered Ariant in Annúminas.You have discovered Minathranc in Annúminas.Cedivor Hedgerow, renowned historian and artifact expert, seeks protection while he delves into the crumbling halls of Glynafon.The abandoned burrows of Glynafon are in the eastern Angle.

You should explore the abandoned burrows and bring anything of interest back to Cedivor.Search the abandoned burrowsCedivor Hedgerow is outside of Glynafon, in the eastern Angle.

You should bring the stone to Cedivor.Show the stone to CedivorNarnien is located in Gaerond, in the northern Angle.

You should tell Narnien that you have found a strange artifact.Bring the stone to Narnien'Hello there! Why, you look exactly like the sort of help I need! I am Cedivor Hedgerow, grand historian and artifact expert!'

He pauses, waiting for a reaction from you.

'You... have not heard of me? Well, I suppose someone like you does not keep up with this sort of thing. Too busy tramping all over the countryside being a hero and having adventures? Exactly the person I have been seeking. You see, I am exploring the ruins that dot the hills and forests of the Angle, but I need assistance in these dangerous lands.

'I can not enter the Warg dens, but I suspect there are ancient dwellings buried in these hills. A place that was called Glynafon! If you find anything of interest within and bring it to me, I shall reward you greatly!''Perhaps the poison was a bit much. The Wargs did my work for me. Oh my! You are still here?'

Cedivor coughs and looks uncomfortable.'Welcome back! Have you found something interesting?'

You hand her the stone.

'Fascinating! This is a Gwelumir, a weather-stone. It sadly has lost most of its function, but when it was first created, it would have indicated what the weather is in a certain area. They were an experiment that had been considered a failure, as one could easily look to the skies to count clouds. You say you found this in an ancient smial? What a perfect use for such a device! It must have been gifted to an Elf-friend long ago. Thank you for bringing it to me! I look forward to studying its properties.''What have you found there, my friend? How interesting! Did you find anything of import on his… uh, their body?'

You show him the stone. A queer gleam flashes across his eyes.

'How strange this object is! I should keep it! Ah, for my research. Well now, I think we can leave. Whatever killed Ragnal may still be down here.'

'How do you know his name?' you ask, readying your weapon.

'What? His… ah, well, no need to look so violent! Fine, fine. I'm no historian. But what do you care? Oh. I see you care very much. Here! Take the blasted thing. I do not need to die for a rock.'The Black Númenórean that sits in Ost Elendil is named Balhest. He is a powerful foe, but he is not the only evil that resides now in that place. We have learned that the passage into the throne room where Balhest commands his forces is guarded by the Cargûl known as Guloth. If you are to defeat Balhest, you will first need to do something about Guloth.

He possesses some terrible power over creatures of shadow, drawing strength out of the darkness with which he commands them to his will. You must somehow sever Guloth's ability to strengthen the fell spirits under his command.

Ost Elendil lies across the bridge of Ariant. Go there only if you are able and willing to face not only Balhest, lieutenant of Amarthiel, but also Guloth the Cargûl. If the battle has drawn me elsewhere by the time you return, report of your victory to Captain-General Daerdan at Echad Garthadir, the Ranger-encampment here in the city.The Cargûl Guloth is inside Ost Elendil, beyond the bridge of Ariant on the highest level of Annúminas.

Legrindavor has warned you that Balhest is defended by a fearsome Cargûl, Guloth by name, who wields power over creatures of shadow.Lehmä-koti is a small Earth-kin camp just over the border of Angmar.Lehmä-koti lies far to the east of Tinnudir, beyond Ram Dúath.

The Rangers have sent you to Lehmä-koti to speak with the Earth-kin.Talk to the Earth-kin at Lehmä-koti'When I stayed in Esteldín, I made friends with a group of Earth-kin that lived not far from the refuge. They were holding out valiantly against the oppression of Angmar. Seeing what we have gone through here, I think of them and wonder if they are well.

'I would like you to go and find out. If they are, I am sure there is work to be done there. Their camp is north of Esteldín, just beyond the Ram Dúath.''Angmar pushes against us hard. There is much help we could use.''Go now and speak with the Earth-kin of Lehmä-koti.'The Rangers of Esteldín have told you of a troll named Shataz, who is attempting to raise a raid against Rivendell.The troll Shataz was last seen by an Elvish scout on the slopes east of Orod Laden in the Misty Mountains, far to the south and east of the North Downs.

Handarod has asked you to find the troll Shataz and defeat him.Defeat ShatazHandarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the west and north of the Misty Mountains.

You should return to Handarod and tell him of Shataz' defeat.Talk to Handarod'The Elves of Rivendell have spoken to me recently of a particular problem which they had thought long ago dealt with.

'It seems there was once a troll in the lower regions of Bruinen, of particular strength and cunning, who strove to stir the trolls of the Trollshaws to band together in war against Rivendell. The Elves learned of this and hunted Shataz down, eventually driving him up into the Misty Mountains -- but they were unable to capture or kill him.

'Now it seems that Shataz lives up there still, and a scout discovered him once again attempting to raise a band of trolls to raid Rivendell itself from the region of Orod Laden. This is a distraction that Elrond can ill-afford at this time, and so I would have you take a small band of skilled warriors up into the Misty Mountains to do away with this troublesome creature. You should take allies with you if you plan to find this creature.''I have received a message from the Wardens telling me of your heroic efforts in support of their cause. I thank you for taking such risks on their behalf and ours.'The Ford of Bruinen is the last bulwark leading into the hidden vale of Rivendell. Orcs in the service of Angmar lay siege at the Ford, seeking to break through the defences of Imladris.Elrohir and Elladan, sons of Elrond, are prepared to stand against the army of the Enemy attempting to cross the Bruinen. Elrohir is awaiting your arrival.Talk to Elrohir at the Ford of BruinenThe first assault has been launched. The Ford and the sons of Elrond must be defended.Push back the first assaultThe second assault has been launched. The Enemy shows no signs of slowing.Push back the second assaultThe third assault has been launched. The Enemy appears to be wavering in morale and decreasing in number.Push back the third assaultThe fourth assault has been launched. The Enemy's forces are dwindling quickly and are nearly at their end.Push back the fourth assaultThe final assault begins as the leader of the Enemy's forces enters the battle. Defeat him, and the invasion will be thwartedFend off the final assault'The drums have stopped, ${PLAYER}. The assault will come any moment now. Prepare yourself.''The Ford remains ours, and Rivendell shall be free from any assault, at least for this day. This was a good victory, one the Enemy's forces will not soon recover from.'Waltney and Garan Maythorn's progress is halted once more by a ghost-like spectre.The ghostly figure can be found near the road south of Eitheldir in the western Angle.

