You should let Waltney and Garan know that the brigand pretending to be a ghost has been defeated.Return to the elderly couple'Well, look here! My very favourite ${CLASS}! Your timing is most fortuitous once again. Another one of those wretched spirits is pestering good folks like ourselves. I stepped off of the road for barely an instant and it swept towards me most frightfully!

'I was just regrouping and getting prepared to send it packing, but now that you are here... well, youth before beauty. We would be much obliged if you could see to its defeat.''My son told me that the ruins are full of treasure! Lost relics of kings and queens who did battle here and fell, spewing curses so potent that none dared to strip them of their goods. They just left them where they fell, and let the birds and wolves see to the bodies.'

Garan shudders.

'I do not believe in curses, but I think we shall continue on our way regardless.''You return! Is the ghost defeated?'

You tell him about the relic hunters.

'So the cur was trying to scare people away from where they were digging by pretending to be a ghost? Well, he certainly fooled me!

'You have my thanks, friend! I would have seen to it myself were I a few decades younger. We are grateful to you! We haven’t much, but please, take this for your trouble. We will be on our way to Tornhad once more, all thanks to you!'In order to cross the Misty Mountains, travellers have long had to traverse high and trecherous passes, often choked with snow, knife-like winds, and other more aggressive hazards. Seek out these passes and learn the secret ways of the mountains.Explore stuff.Cirith Imladris acts as the lone gateway between the Valley of Rivendell and the high passes of the Misty Mountains. Once there was fair trade along this route between the dwarf-realms of the mountains and the Elves of Rivendell, but the dwarves were driven out long ago by goblins, and many other hazards have returned to make travel up through this region difficult indeed. For the most part, the Elves keep watch over Cirith Imladris, and few pass beyond its upper reaches into the Misty Mountains.The difficult yet unassuming pass of Whitcleft turned out to be the downfall of one of the larger dwarf-realms within the northern reaches of the Misty Mountains. Believing that the goblins to the north would resolutely struggle to find or dig secret tunnels into their well-defended mines to attack, the dwarves to the south neglected the defence of this pass.

A particularly cunning goblin chieftain led a horde of his people through the pass of Whitcleft in the deep of winter, forcing them to dig their way through at a terrible cost in lives -- but using this approach he came upon the dwarves from the surface unexpectedly and trapped them underground through the long months that followed, driving most to their death through starvation or futile attempts to escape the siege.

So many goblins froze during the siege that they too were decimated by it, but Durin's Folk were never able to return to their lost stronghold.Rakhâs-bizar has never been well-travelled by the Free Peoples of Middle-earth. For time immemorial, giants have lived in the peaks and valleys to the south, and only those rare few who might call them friends, or who wish to test their mettle against a truly powerful and capricious foe might have reason to travel there. Not many of the latter return.Angmar is attempting to use dark powers to call forth a blizzard to freeze Evendim.The first canyon is ahead. To proceed forward, you must claim it.Take the first canyonThe second canyon is ahead. To proceed forward, you must claim it.Take the second canyonThe third canyon is ahead. To proceed forward, you must claim it.Take the third canyonThe Angmarim Sorceror is performing his ritual in the cave ahead. He must be stopped if Evendim is to be saved.Defeat the Angmarim sorcerer and claim the caveAngmar is attempting to send a blizzard from the frozen lands of Forochel down into the waters of Evendim.Complete all encounters at the Icy Crevasse.Defeat MíthalagosDefeat Kôkas-jokuDefeat Lapa-kitaDefeat CoflúgDefeat CrantokDefeat TúgarchDefeat Veri-torviDefeat MahtiOst Elendil, the great palace of the kings of old, is on the island beyond the bridge of Ariant. At its base is the entrance to Haudh Valandil, the tomb of Valandil son of Isildur. I fear that the tomb, long-undisturbed, has become the home to great evils: both of Angmar's design and otherwise.

Have you seen the vile creatures known as Kergrim? They are believed to be some relative of the cave-claw, but more prone to disease and the desecration of hallowed places.

Some of these beasts have come to Haudh Valandil, and they must be cleared from the tomb, especially their brute of a leader: Shingrinder, he is called, and he is vile. You will do this, ${PLAYER}, if you honour the ancient places of the Dúnedain, and you will return to me with news of your success. If I have been drawn elsewhere, report instead to Captain-General Daerdan at Echad Garthadir, the Ranger-encampment here in the city.Kergrim stalk Haudh Valandil, the tomb on the island beyond the bridge of Ariant, in Annúminas.

Glangilith has asked you to defeat the kergrim that stalk the depths of Haudh Valandil, including their leader Shingrinder.Defeat kergrim in Haudh Valandil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat ShingrinderYou have recovered the last of the Silithair, shining adamants crafted by Elves of the house of Fëanor in days of old. It must be used to reforge the blade that was broken.Aragorn is in one of the guest rooms of the House of Elrond in Rivendell.

Calenglad has given you the Silithar to bring to Aragorn. Its light will be used to remake the blade that was broken.'By reclaiming the last of the Silithair, you have done what Aragorn sent you here to do, ${PLAYER}, and along the way you made yourself a great help to all of us that live along the shores of Lake Nenuial. I am sorry to see you go.

'But go you must, for Narsil is to be reforged! Return at once to Rivendell, far to the east, and deliver the Silithar to Aragorn! The time has come at last for the blade that was broken to be remade!''I am sorry to see you go, ${PLAYER}, but go you must! Aragorn awaits the Silithar!''The son of Arathorn has learned much since I confronted him those many years ago. He will become a great leader, if the battles to come do not cut his life short.

'Deliver unto him the Silithar, for it is of his line, and he has passed my test.''You return from out of the wild, ${PLAYER}, and my heart rejoices to see you! Unless my eyes are very much mistaken, you have passed the challenges of Gwindeth and return bearing the last of the Silithair!'The Angle has been home to countless battles over the long years. What lost treasures lie beneath the earth of Haudh Erthaid, the Tomb of Kingdoms?Collect an ancient artifact.Collect an ancient Angle artifactAncient artifacts can be found in Ost Waeren and Tham Lumren.

The Elf Narnien had asked you to search for ancient artifacts.Collect ancient artifacts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Narnien is in Gaerond, in the northern Angle.

You should bring the ancient artifacts to Narnien.What lost treasures lie beneath the earth of Haudh Erthaid, the Tomb of Kingdoms?'What interesting things you have brought me! I look forward to learning what I can about them. Thank you for keeping them out of the hands of those who would not appreciate them for their history and artistry. You have my thanks.'The fragments you retrieved from the snow-lurkers of the Misty Mountains are of interest to the scholar Deluros, though Glorenglir missed their significance.Snow-lurkers can be found near the source of the Bruinen and drifts of snow in the area may also hold the jagged relic fragments sought by Deluros.

Scholar Deluros has asked you to collect jagged relic fragments from near the source of the Bruinen so he may reassemble the vase so readily dismissed by Glorenglir.Scholar Deluros is in the library of the House of Elrond in Rivendell.

You have retrieved some jagged relic fragments. Perhaps Deluros can use them to reassemble the ancient vase.'Glorenglir has not understood the significance of these fragments, ${PLAYER}, but I do. These are shards from what must once have been a beautiful vase, crafted long ago by some lord of the Eldar.

'If you can retrieve more fragments of this vase, it might be possible to reassemble it. Its former glory might have been lost to carelessness or necessity, but history leaves us with one certainty -- though broken, something once fair can be made beautiful again through care and good will.

'Return to the source of the Bruinen and search the drifts there for more fragments. The remaining pieces are sure to be most jagged. Whether you dig them out of the drifts yourself or rely on Glorenglir's snow-lurkers, I leave to you. Be warned, however, that the chance of finding the remaining fragments will likely be quite low.''If you can retrieve jagged relic fragments from the same area to which Glorenglir sent you, I may be able to reassemble this ancient vase.

'You may find these jagged fragments on snow-lurkers, as you did before, but I do not have as much confidence in this as Glorenglir does. Rather, I would have you search the snowdrifts near the source of the Bruinen, north of Rivendell in the Misty Mountains, to find these fragments.''While you were away, ${PLAYER}, I was able to partially reassemble the vase. It is a thing of beauty, even incomplete! I wonder at its maker, and the circumstances that brought it to lie abandoned in pieces beneath the snow of the mountains.

'I see you have brought some jagged fragments back with you! I will see if any of them belong to this vase.'Glóin is dealing with multiple issues in the Misty Mountains and could use aid.Glóin has camped out in the Misty Mountains and is trying to deal with the threats present there.

Glóin can be found at his camp in the south-west of the Misty Mountains.Speak to Glóin in the Misty Mountains'There is much to do in the Misty Mountains to the North. The giants have begun to wander and there are goblins throughout the fields. I fear our northern border is no longer safe ${PLAYER}. An old friend of the Elves, Glóin, has a camp to the north of here, in the south-western area of the Misty Mountains.

'Find Glóin in the Misty Mountains and see what you can do to aid him.''There is much to do here, friend. I am glad you are here to aid our cause.'Defeat Orcs in Urugarth.Defeat Orcs in UrugarthDefeat many Orcs in Urugarth.Defeat Orcs in UrugarthThe quality of your shot must not strain your bow. The strain on your target is another matter altogether.Achieve critical hits with Merciful ShotThe quality of your shot must not strain your bow. The strain on your target is another matter altogether.Achieve critical hits with Merciful Shot or Huntsman's ShotPerched high above the River Hoarwell lie the ruins of Eitheldir. Once a stronghold of the Noldor, its arched domes now play host to a new influx of Orcs and brigands who fight over these lands. But Elven eyes keep watch here still, and the scout Merileg waits, crouched in shadows on the road below.Eitheldir is in the northern Angle.

You should defeat enemies in Eitheldir.Defeat enemies at Eitheldir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Eitheldir's captainMerileg is located on the road to Eitheldir, in the northern Angle.

You should return to Merileg.Return to Merileg'You stand below the ruins of Eitheldir, stranger. Once a great stronghold of my people, it now lies rotting and crumbled. Servants of the Enemy have infiltrated those once-formidable walls and sullied the grounds. You seek to aid our cause? Do what you may to thin their ranks, and I shall reward you greatly. Keep an eye out for their captain as well. I have heard tell he is a nasty brute.''Those scum sully this place with their presence.''I commend you, stranger. With your help, the Enemy will gain no stronger foothold in these lands. Here is what I promised you.'Knowledge of the natural world has given you subtle influence over its natural fluctuations, but there is deeper knowledge still to be gleaned through study.Strike with Fire-loreKnowledge of the natural world has given you subtle influence over its natural fluctuations, but there is deeper knowledge still to be gleaned through study.Strike with Fire and Frost Lore or Wizard's FireKnowledge of the natural world has given you subtle influence over its natural fluctuations, but there is deeper knowledge still to be gleaned through study.Strike with Frost-loreKnowledge of the natural world has given you subtle influence over its natural fluctuations, but there is deeper knowledge still to be gleaned through study.Strike with Fire and Frost Lore or Wizard's FrostGwindeth has agreed to lower the flood-waters in the tomb of Elendil so that you can recover the Silithar for Aragorn.Calenglad is at the Ranger-camp on Tinnudir, in Evendim.

Calenglad is waiting to speak with you about travelling to the tomb of Elendil to reclaim the Silithar for Aragorn.Talk to Calenglad and travel to the tomb of ElendilCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on Tinnudir, in Evendim.

Calenglad is waiting for you to speak with him about your adventures in the tomb of Elendil.'Gwindeth has agreed to lower the flood-waters in the tomb of Elendil? I am filled with amazement, ${PLAYER}, that you were able to accomplish such a wonder! I do not know what you will find in the freshly-unflooded portion of the tomb -- it might be best to bring allies with you.

'I fear that the tomb-robbers that prowl Evendim will take advantage of Gwindeth's decision; long have the waters prevented them from gaining access to the lowest levels of Elendil's tomb. Now that this barrier will be gone, the robbers will rush to seize what treasures they may. One such band is led by Idella Crypt-breaker, a notorious robber, and she will not remain idle with the promise of riches unclaimed.

'Gather allies and speak to me when you are ready to journey to the tomb, and I will show you inside. Confront Idella if you find her within the tomb and reclaim the Silithar for Lord Aragorn!''You have emerged from the darkness, ${PLAYER}, and have truly made an old man glad to see this happy day. The light of Narsil shall be kindled once again!

'Gwindeth appeared shortly before your return and gave to me the Silithar; to see such a wonder return from out of the mists of history fills me with amazement!''Are you ready to journey to the tomb of Elendil, ${PLAYER}? I hope you have gathered allies, for Idella Crypt-breaker is sure to be making her way into the deepest chambers with the rest of her band!''You did well in the watery half-light of the tomb of great Elendil, ${PLAYER}. I am pleased to know you, and the Lord of the Dúnedain is fortunate indeed to have such a friend!'The Ent Longbough believes that some evil power may be twisting the wood to dark ends.Longbough is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim.

Handarod has asked you to speak with the Ent Longbough and assist him against the Wood-trolls of Evendim.Accompany Longbough against the Twisted HeartLongbough is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim.

You should speak again with Longbough.Talk to Longbough'I have received a strange message from our allies in Evendim. It seems that far to the West in the forests of Evendim there lies a grove where one an Ent has taken up residence in his search for the Entwives. Through his Elf-friends he has sent forth a call for aid against a dark menace in the forests there -- some corruption of the wood by a band of Wood-trolls and a Huorn that has fallen under their sway.

'I need you to gather a strong following of your companions and make this journey into the western woods, so that this threat may be eliminated before it spreads its corruption further.

'Speak with Longbough the Ent when you are ready to begin your assault.''Have you gathered your allies? Hom! The forest seethes with anger as the power of the Twisted Heart grows, and while I fear we have little time, haste will lead only to disaster.

'Ta-room! Ta-rum! Are you fully prepared for what lies ahead? Be certain, for we face death should we falter.'Hoom! Hom! It has been ever so long since my blood has run with such heat and fervour! That was well fought, Little One! Indeed while I have little love for axes and swords, I had forgotten the enjoyable haste of battle. Ta-room!

'Even now though, I feel the anger of the forest subsiding as the Twisted Heart's influence fades. Soon some measure of peace shall return here, I think.

'Ta-rum! My thanks to you, little one. Your aid was most welcome. Please forgive my rudeness when first we met.The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of extremely sharp beaks.Collection boxes for this task can be found at the camps within the Misty Mountains.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Extremely sharp beaks from the birds found throughout the Bruinen Source. 

The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of extremely sharp beaks.Wanted: Extremely sharp beaks from the birds found throughout the Bruinen Source.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of huge heartwood.Collection boxes for this task can be found at the camps within the Misty Mountains.

