The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of huge heartwood.Wanted: Huge heartwood from the snow-lurkers throughout the Bruinen Source.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Cultivate a threatening demeanor and practice the imposing art of putting your shield into your enemy's face.Strike with BashPractice your weapon-recovering strike; it could save your life...or a friend's.Strike with Hedge or Improved HedgePractice your weapon-recovering strike; it could save your life...or a friend's.Use Riposte, Ferocious Strikes, or Raging BladeIt is said that love makes fools of us all... but perhaps it does so for some more than others.Hal has tasked you with collecting strange mushrooms within the forested lands of the Angle.Collect strange mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hal Twayblade is beside the road north of Glynafon, in the Angle.Hal needs healing herbs: the very ones he was sent to recover.Collect healing herbs, and steer clear of strange mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Hal with the healing herbs you gathered.'You there! You look more than capable of handling yourself in these woods. Could I perhaps propose a favour?

'My name is Hal Twayblade, and I have been tasked by a beautiful Elf-woman to collect herbs so she may prepare a number of useful medicinal remedies. However, I seem to be having some trouble recalling anything beyond her delicate features, her lovely tresses...'

Hal drifts away into his reverie. At last he seems to remember your presence.

'There was something else: she did say that a strange breed of mushroom grew in these parts, but I have seen neither stem nor cap of it! I want to get back to her as soon as possible, and I have yet to find any of these mushrooms she mentioned. The two of us will be able to cover more ground. Please say you will help me!''You're back already? Did you have any luck?'

You hand the mushrooms to Hal and he wrinkles his nose at the foul odour emanating from them.

'These are great! They look exactly how the healer described! ...I think.

'Now, she said you could ingest these raw and they would have potent healing properties! Let me just take a big bite to be sure....'

It does not take long before his face turns pallid and green.

'O-on second thought... did she want me to stay AWAY from these mushrooms? I was rather distracted, and perhaps did not pay close enough attention.... Oh dear....

'Do you think you could do me one more favour? The herbs she sent me to recover may be my only hope! Can you seek them out? And stay away from those mushrooms!''Ah, th-thanks... these must be the herbs I need... just have to....'

He crushes them up in his hands before popping them into his mouth. After a short time he stands up straighter.

'Ah that should do the trick, at least for the time being. I guess I didn't really pay enough attention when that lovely Elf-maiden told me about the herbs of the forest....

'Still! You managed to do everything I asked and helped stave off a self-induced stomach-ache. For that I am grateful! I will do my best to remember what the healer said and find some herbs of my own before heading back. Thanks for your help!'Show your enemies all the different ways you can be dangerous.Use Bard's Arrow, Rain of Arrows, or Blood ArrowHandarod is concerned for the safety of the Wardens of Annúminas, who struggle to secure the ruined home of their forebears.The Even-rills lie in Evendim, far to the west of the North Downs, on the northern end of Lake Evendim.

Handarod has asked you to scout the area around the Even-rills, one of the two major sources of water coming into Lake Evendim from the north.Scout the Even-rillsThe Eave-mere lies in Evendim, far to the west of the North Downs, on the western side of Lake Evendim.

Handarod has asked you to scout the Eave-mere, a small lake that feeds down into the much larger Lake Evendim.Scout the Eave-mereTollobel lies in Evendim, far to the west of the North Downs, in the south-west reaches of Lake Evendim.

Handarod has asked you to scout the island of Tollobel. It could make an ideal location for the Angmarim to strike from should their hold on the city of Annúminas be weakened.Scout TollobelHandarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the east of Evendim.

You should report to Handarod and tell him what you have found along the shores of Lake Evendim.Talk to Handarod'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. Urgent news has come to my attention, and I could use your aid.

'Our bretheren in Evendim are preparing an offensive to break the foul occupation of Annúminas, but these preparations have left them with no scouts to spare in patrolling the far side of Lake Evendim -- that is where you come in.

'Up until now, there has been little evidence of the Angmarim or their Orc-soldiers in that area of Evendim, but we need to know if they have constructed any outposts there, lest they catch the Wardens by surprise. I want you to scout the far side of the lake and make sure that there is no sign of the Angmarim there.''Well done. The presence of the Gauredain in Evendim is disturbing, but knowing that neither Angmarim nor Orc yet occupies the far shores of the lake is a relief. Thank you for your efforts.'Amongst the ruins of Tham Lumren, ghostly spectres cling to ancient artifacts.Glatharn is located in Tham Lumren.

Thalathril has suggested you offer your assistance to Glatharn.Talk to GlatharnTwisted spirits can be found at Tham Lumren, in the north-east Angle.

Glatharn has asked you to collect twisted armbands from twisted spirits.Collect twisted armbands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glatharn is located in Tham Lumren.

You should bring the twisted armbands to Glatharn.Twisted rotroot can be found along the banks of the rivers that border the Angle.

Glatharn has asked you to collect a bouquet of twisted rotroot.Collect twisted rotroot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glatharn is located in Tham Lumren.

You should bring the twisted rotroot flowers to Glatharn.Return to GlatharnThe pyre is in Tham Lumren, in the eastern Angle.

Glatharn has asked you to add the twisted rotroot and armbands to the pyre.Glatharn is located in Tham Lumren.

You should talk to Glatharn.Return to Glatharn'At present, I personally do not require your aid. However, Glatharn mentioned that he wanted to talk to me about something. Go see if you are able to lend assistance, that I might continue my work.''Mae govannen! I am indeed Glatharn. I heard tell that you might be interested in offering assistance to our cause. I have a… slightly odd request. We are camped near the ruins of Tham Lumren. As with the rest of Haudh Erthaid, Tham Lumren has played host to countless battles. Many of which saw Elves and Men meet their demise. For some of those folk, a physical death was not enough to send their spirits onwards, and they lurk among the ruins, attacking blindly, and imagining that their last battle still rages.

'I have identified certain artifacts that I believe are tethering these troubled shades – twisted, golden armbands that they wore in life. Thalathril will not grant me leave to assist these confused soldiers, but you have the freedom to do so. Please, go and collect armbands from the shades.''Ah, you return! I knew you were more than a match for those poor spirits. Come, let me see what you bring.'

You hand him an armband.

'Yes, it is as I thought. I think I know how we can help these warriors. The rivers that surround the Angle often ran red after the battles that were fought here. So much loss and violence has twisted some of the plants that grow in this area. On their banks, you will find twisted rotroot. Collect a bouquet of their flowers and bring it here.''In other lands, these flowers grow tall and proud. Here in the Angle, they grow twisted by the memories of violence and strife.

'I have prepared a pyre using an incantation for purifying and letting go. Here, take the armbands. Add them to the fire with the bouquet you gathered. May the hearts of the warriors find peace, and may the twisted flowers unfurl and bloom again.''Did you feel it, ${PLAYER}? Like a warm summer wind, and that sweet scent! I believe we have done it, friend. We are a small step closer to healing this land and granting peace to troubled souls.'There exist secret techniques that will change the way you fight.Use any Capstone skill as The Fulcrum or The MaelstromMany relics have been lost to the snows of the Misty Mountains, buried beneath the drifts by the winds and by time.Snow-lurkers climb the drifts near the source of the Bruinen in the Misty Mountains north of Rivendell.

As the creatures make their way through the snow, shards of pottery and old relics become tangled in their root-like legs. Collect relic fragments from snow lurkers in the Misty Mountains.Collect relic-fragmentsSnow-lurkers climb the drifts near the source of the Bruinen in the Misty Mountains north of Rivendell.

As the creatures make their way through the snow, shards of pottery and old relics become tangled in their root-like legs. Collect relic fragments from snow lurkers in the Misty Mountains.Collect relic-fragments (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glorenglir is interested in investigating these relic fragments collected from the Misty Mountains.

Glorenglir may be found in Rivendell.As the snow-lurkers make their way through the snow, shards of pottery and old relics become tangled in their root-like legs. If enough were gathered, these items may have interest to some of the scholars in Rivendell.

Collect relic-fragments from the snow-lurkers in the Misty Mountains.'Snow lurkers climb the slopes near the source of Loudwater, north of Imladris in the Misty Mountains. Master Deluros has asked me to search for relic fragments among the drifts, but the snow lurkers unknowingly collect the pieces for me! Be careful if you decide to help me, for the lurkers will attack you on sight.''You actually found relic fragments on the snow-lurkers? I can hardly believe it, ${PLAYER}!

'I suspected that such fragments would become entangled in the legs of the snow-lurkers, but I had never observed that behaviour myself. My musings have been proven true by your efforts!

'I am pleased as well that you collected these old fragments, but there is no shortage of those in Imladris, and I am more excited that my musings were correct! I thank you, ${PLAYER}!'Brychan the Bold is behind some of the attacks on the defenders of the tombs of Evendim, and Helechír wants him defeated.Brychan the Bold is at his home in Ost Forod, north-east of Tinnudir. Helechír told you to return to the mainland and follow the road north of the cross-roads of Canadiach until you reach Ost Forod.

Helechír has asked you to confront Brychan the Bold about the many crimes his gang of tomb-robbers have committed.Confront Brychan the BoldHelechír is on a little island off of Men Erain.

You taught Brychan the Bold a hard lesson, and he fled into his home. Helechír is waiting to hear the tale of your confrontation with the leader of the robber-gang.'The time has come to strike a decisive blow against the tomb-robbers of Evendim, ${PLAYER}, and you are just the ${RACE} to do it!

'Sid Waring mentioned a man named "Brychan the Bold." I believe he is the leader of a powerful gang of tomb-robbers, the same gang that murdered Alfred Whitley and my kinsman Iorthrenar, injured Sid Waring and stole the relics he guarded, and attacked both you and Glirion high atop the peaks above Men Erain.

'Brychan has a home in Ost Forod, to the north-east of Tinnudir. Return to the mainland and follow the road north from the cross-roads of Canadiach until you arrive at Ost Forod. Look for Brychan the Bold and confront him!''You must bring Brychan the Bold to justice! Journey to his home in Ost Forod, north-east of Tinnudir, and confront him about his crimes!''I do as I please, stranger, and I'll keep on doing it! These lands belong to me and mine, not some filthy descendants of long-forgotten kings!

'My blade will teach you not to bother me!''It sounds like you taught Brychan a lesson, ${PLAYER}. I hope it stays with him.

'I wish that Evendim was not such a wild place. Of old, even after the fading of the Dúnedain, it was a place of peace, but the troubles of the world have come to disturb even these lands.

'Even so, you have served us well! There are other robber-gangs, but it is to be hoped that the men who followed Brychan will rethink, perhaps, the trust they placed in the strength of their leader. You again have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'Use the defeat of your foe to fuel your attack against the next.Use Second WindYour efforts within Annúminas have not gone unnoticed by the Rangers. Because of your unceasing aid in the defence of the City of the Kings, they have bestowed upon you the title of Warden.Vighar Roadwalker, a dwarf at the High Crag camp, wants to post signs warning travellers away from dangerous locations in the mountains.Evil Men have established themselves in a keep to the north-west of the High Crag camp.

Vighar Roadwalker has given you a sign to post just outside the entrance of the keep occupied by evil Men in the north-western Misty Mountains.Vighar Roadwalker is at the High Crag camp, east of Glóin's camp.

Vighar will be pleased to hear that you have posted the sign he gave you in front of the keep occupied by evil Rhudaurans.'Would you say you are skilled with hammer and nail, friend? It doesn't really matter, but it would be a help if you were. Some of my kin have been looking to get the trade passing through the mountains again, and I'm doing my part to help.

'The trouble is that the mountains are dangerous even in summer, and during winter only a fool would expect to come through without incident. And there are threats in the mountains beyond the cold and the snows -- goblins and worse!

'There's an old keep far to the north, and evil Men have overtaken it for their own purposes. It's a ways north of the road, but I don't want any dwarves to get turned about in a storm and happen upon it unawares. I'd appreciate it if you could post this warning sign I've made in front of the slope leading up to the keep. There's already a suitable post at the base of the slope -- just affix the sign to it and hurry back. Head north along the road, and then turn north-west to travel into the northern source. It's quite a ways, so be prepared for a good hike!''Evil Men have occupied a keep far to the north, across a snow-covered field beyond the road as it makes its turn east. Post the sign I gave you in front of their keep, to warn travellers of the danger that place may pose to them.

'It's quite a ways north of the road, so be ready for a good walk.''You have returned, ${PLAYER}! I trust that you have posted my sign? I am glad to hear it, for now I have another!'The Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Complete Weathering the Storm -- Small FellowshipComplete Weathering the Storm -- FellowshipComplete Weathering the Storm -- RaidThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive in the Barrow-downs for five minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for ten minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutes at levelThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive in the Barrow-downs for five minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for ten minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutes at levelThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive for five minutes at levelSurvive for ten minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes at levelSurvive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutes at levelTravellers have long told tales of the mighty and capricious giants that inhabit the cold peaks of the Misty Mountains. You must seek out their places for yourself however, for there are few who have seen them left to tell you the way.Explore stuff.In giantish terms, the Lornstone would likely be described as a quaint villa or summer cottage. As far as anyone else is concerned, it's a grim pile of stone with a commanding overlook of the valleys that wind below, providing an excellent vantage for its inhabitants to bowl great rocks upon whatever interlopers are foolish enough to wander this far into the Mountains.Whatever explorer gave Greybough End its name must have been desperately homesick and thinking of greener lands and happier times. Despite the name, there is nothing whatsoever comforting about these massive granite slabs piled here like children's blocks. The fact that it serves as lair to the massive brutes who constructed it only adds to the irony of its comfortingly familiar name.The Giant's Needle is simply a massive stone spire erected by the Giants of the Misty Mountains. No purpose has ever been found for it, nor is its construction all that remarkable given the size of its builders.

What is perhaps most remarkable about the Giant's Spire is that none of the giants has ever gotten around to knocking it down just for fun. It is this that leads scholars to believe that it does indeed have some meaning or purpose, but even the wise cannot guess at what that might be.Iorbar is a massive, desolate settlement within which the Giants of the Misty Mountains gather from time to time. While Iorbar is not a fortress in any true sense of the word, its sheer size and great stone structures make it a formidable redoubt, and its massive inhabitants make it even more so.

Even at the height of their strength within the Misty Mountains, Durin's Folk never made open war against the giants, nor attempted to drive them from Iorbar despite the occasional raids and harrasment of travellers; instead, an uneasy truce reigned for many long years until the dwarves were finally driven out of the mountains by goblins.Gabilazan was one of two fortresses built by Durin's Folk in the northern reaches of the Misty Mountains, beneath which stretched extensive mines. Alas, these settlements were always challenged by the goblins which infested the range. After the fall of Helegrod to the north to a maurauding Dragon and its spawn, Gabilazan was eventually isolated, besieged and overrun by goblins during the waning rule of the Longbeards.

These days the goblins have abandoned the fortress to ruin and in their stead an odd alliance of giants and the traitorous Dourhands have made it their home.You are adept at knowing and calling on the Winds.Use Wind Shanties.Glorfindel has asked you to deliver a letter from Aragorn to the Rangers of Tornhad.You should look for a Ranger outside of Tornhad who is keeping watch, to whom you should deliver the letter. Tornhad is in the southern region of the Angle of Mitheithel.Find the Ranger keeping watch outside of TornhadYou have found the Ranger Calithil, who is keeping watch outside of Tornhad. You should talk to him and give him the letter.'${PLAYER}, since I need not continue down this road, would you do me the favour of delivering something for me? I carry a sealed letter from Aragorn to the Rangers in Tornhad. When he is unable to speak with them in person, he sometimes sends them information or instructions this way. Can I trust you with this task?

'As you travel overland, you are quite likely to encounter a Ranger outside of the village keeping watch.... If you can spot him, that is!'

Glorfindel laughs and you think you can almost hear the ringing of clear bells in his voice.

'The Ranger keeping watch will make certain it gets into the right hands. If you do this for me, I will be free to scout the east.''Hoy there, what business have you?'

You tell the Ranger that you are delivering a letter from Aragorn on behalf of Glorfindel, and the Ranger straightens up.

'Yes, I see,' he says, taking the letter. He scrutinizes it and then tucks it away.

The Ranger leans against the wall again and gives you a curt nod.

'Thank you, friend. I appreciate that it is unopened. Many thanks on behalf of the Dúnedain.'Ivoreth has realized that they are not safe at her chosen camp, and has asked you to stave off the wolves and lynxes that lurk nearby while she and Barhador prepare to depart.Wolves and lynxes threaten the safety of Ivoreth and Barhador. They can be found on the hill just north of their camp in the Angle of Mitheithel.Defeat wolves in the Angle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat lynx in the Angle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have held off the wolves and lynxes and should return to Ivoreth at her camp in the Angle of Mitheithel to see how she fares.Return to Ivoreth at her camp'Oh, ${PLAYER}... I fear I have chosen a terrible place to rest! There are wolves and lynxes all about us! I really should have known better. Please, if you are truly a friend, would you stave them off while I put away the food and get Barhador ready to travel once more? I am competent with a blade and will keep watch here as I can while we make ready.

'I saw them there, up this hill to the north of us.''Thank you, ${PLAYER} for buying us some time. I will not forget your kindness. We are almost ready to go on our way.'Ivoreth, the mother of the Ranger Halbarad, travels to Tham Lumren and is stopped along the road for rest and a meal. She has asked you to join them and forage for some wild carrots so that there is enough food for everyone.Wild carrots grow on a hill to the south of Ivoreth's location in the Angle of Mitheithel. Collect wild carrots to join Ivoreth for a meal.Forage for wild carrots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected wild carrots to share a meal with Ivoreth. You should return to her at her camp in the Angle of Mitheithel.'Welcome, traveller. What brings you to the Angle?'

You tell her that you are here at the request of your friend, Elladan, and she smiles at you.

'A friend of Elladan is a friend of mine. Come, join us at the fire. Have you eaten? I am Ivoreth, and my brave guardian is Barhador. We are on an errand to Tham Lumren to trade with the Elves for supplies and stopped here to take a rest and have a bite to eat. Would you join us? It's important to keep your strength up when the land is full of dangers.

'Have you come from the north? I would be thankful for any news from that point of the earth. It is my son Halbarad's duty to safe-guard the north.'

You tell her briefly of your adventures and what news you are able.

'Is that so!? Well, now you must join us for a meal, but I am not sure we have enough to feed another. Go forage up some carrots, would you? They grow wild on a hill to the south, not far from here.''Ah, ${PLAYER}, you return! Let us see the carrots.'

She takes the vegetables from you.

