 items should be made to Othran at the base of the hilltop outpost.'These will serve our purpose well.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Hillmen at Aughaire have requested a collection of huge ears to be delivered to Raith.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver huge ears from beasts surrounding Aughaire to Raith, a Hillman within the settlement.Wanted: Huge ears from the beasts surrounding Aughaire. Deliver the items to Raith at Aughaire in the south-western reaches of Angmar.Wanted: Huge ears from the beasts surrounding Aughaire.'These will ornament our items well. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The hunters at Tyrn Lhuig expect a delivery of huge filth to be made to Othran, one of their number at the bottom of their hillside outpost.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver huge filth from the insects surrounding Tyrn Lhuig to Othran at the bottom of the hillside outpost.Wanted: Huge filth from the insects surrounding Tyrn Lhuig. Delivery of the items should be made to Othran at the base of the hilltop outpost.'These will serve our purpose well.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Hillmen at Aughaire have requested a collection of huge goo to be delivered to Raith.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver huge goo from insects and spiders surrounding Aughaire to Raith, a Hillman within the settlement.Wanted: Huge goo from the insects and spiders from the lands surrounding Aughaire. Deliver the items to Raith at Aughaire in the south-western reaches of Angmar.Wanted: Huge goo from the insects and spiders from the lands surrounding Aughaire.'We will ensure that this is used to help our people. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The hunters at Tyrn Lhuig expect a delivery of lethal sharp claws to be made to Othran, one of their number at the bottom of their hillside outpost.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver lethal sharp claws from the turtles surrounding Tyrn Lhuig to Othran at the bottom of the hillside outpost.Wanted: Lethal sharp claws from the turtles surrounding Tyrn Lhuig. Delivery of the items should be made to Othran at the base of the hilltop outpost.'These will serve our purpose well.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The hunters at Tyrn Lhuig expect a delivery of pure black skin to be made to Othran, one of their number at the bottom of their hillside outpost.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver pure black skin from the worms surrounding Tyrn Lhuig to Othran at the bottom of the hillside outpost.Wanted: Pure black skin from the worms surrounding Tyrn Lhuig. Delivery of the items should be made to Othran at the base of the hilltop outpost.'These will serve our purpose well.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.There is much to do while travelling through the lands of Angmar.Complete Explorer of Angmar deedComplete Marching into Shadow (Final) deedComplete Slayer of Angmar deedThere is much to do while travelling through the lands of Forochel.Complete Explorer of Forochel deedComplete Forochel Pioneer deedComplete Slayer of Forochel deedComplete The Lost Fellowship deedYoung Barhador made it clear that he would prefer to eat fish instead of vegetables and asked if you could catch some fish for you all to enjoy with your meal.Catch three fish from the stream just south of where Barhador is camped in the Angle of Mitheithel.Find the fishing spot Barhador describedCatch three fresh fish at Barhador's recommended fishing spot in the Angle of Mitheithel.Catch fresh fish (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Barhador at his camp in the Angle of Mitheithel with the three fresh fish you caught.'Gross! I don't want carrots! If I am to grow big and strong I need more than vegetables! My mother says vegetables do make you big and strong, but I am not so sure.

'Do you like fish? There is a very good fishing spot just across the road to the south, you know. Do you know how to catch one? Catch us each a fish, would you? Ivoreth won't me out of her sight. Please? I would be ever so grateful.''Oh, look at that! These are wonderful! Thank you greatly. They are so much better than carrots.'Bainthir, an Elf at the camp of Echad Candelleth, is awaiting a delivery of grey goo.You have accepted a task to collect grey goo from the insects surrounding Echad Candelleth. You are to deliver the items to Bainthir at the camp.Wanted: A collection of grey goo from the insects surrounding Echad Candelleth. All items should be delivered to Bainthir at the camp.Wanted: A collection of grey goo from the insects surrounding Echad Candelleth.'Know that this will be used well. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Bainthir, an Elf at the camp of Echad Candelleth, is awaiting a delivery of smooth scales.You have accepted a task to collect smooth scales from the worms surrounding Echad Candelleth. You are to deliver the items to Bainthir at the camp.Wanted: A collection of smooth scales from the worms surrounding Echad Candelleth. All items should be delivered to Bainthir at the camp.Wanted: A collection of smooth scales from the worms surrounding Echad Candelleth.'It is good to know that these have been destroyed. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.According to the records Larus Sharpshard was given by Heikki Goldwatcher, the strongbox you recovered is missing some of its contents.Goblins carrying dwarf-gold ingots can likely be found on the Pinnath Fenui, the ridges east of the source of the Bruinen, in the Misty Mountains.

Larus Sharpshard is outraged that goblins have pilfered from the strongbox you recovered and has demanded that you retrieve all of the stolen ingots.Larus Sharpshard is located at a camp north of High Crag.

Larus Sharpshard will be delighted that you have recovered the stolen ingots from the goblins of the Misty Mountains.'Those despicable goblins must have stolen some of the dwarf-gold ingots from this strongbox, ${PLAYER}! According to the records given me by Heikki Goldwatcher, the strongbox is missing twelve ingots!

'This is unforgiveable! To think that the gold of his ancestors has been pilfered by goblins is more than any dwarf could bear.

'The goblins have camps in the mountains somewhere to the north and east, ${PLAYER}. Find the creatures and slay them until you recover the missing ingots! Look especially on the ridges of Pinnath Fenui, east of the source of the Bruinen, for I have heard that many goblin-fires have been spotted that way.''Those goblins will be made to pay, ${PLAYER}. Look for their camps east of the source of the Bruinen, and recover all of the stolen dwarf-gold ingots from their filthy fingers.''Perfect, ${PLAYER}, perfect! This should do it! Now all of the ingots are accounted for, and Heikki Goldwatcher will be happy to know that we have recovered the treasure mentioned in his records.

'Yes, according to Heikki's records we've got everything... needed....

'Oh no, what's this?'Explorer the brutal wilderness of Forochel.Explore the Battle for ForochelExplore the Ancient Stones of ForochelAmong many other things, Barhador has asked you to pick some tart berries while you are out gathering the other things to eat.Pick tart berries that grow to the west of where Barhador is camped in the Angle of Mitheithel.Pick tart berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Barhador at his camp in the Angle of Mitheithel with the berries you picked.'Do you like my shield? Uncle Candaith says it's from Dunland. Have you ever been to Dunland? Where are you from? Did you say you know Halbarad? Do you know Uncle Candaith? He is very brave and strong.'

The lad assails you with questions and doesn't allow you to answer any of them.

'I am going to be a Ranger just like him! I will slay Orcs and goblins and have a bow and a blade of my own. I will travel all over Eriador and do good things for people, but they will never know. It is our way. Who are you, anyway?

'My name is Barhador. Are you going to get some more food and join us? We don't have anything for dessert! Do you like berries? Some berries grow west of here that are both sweet and tart and make your face do this.'

The boy puckers his lips and raises his eyebrows as far as they can go.

'We went past them earlier but Ivoreth said we couldn't stop yet. If you're going foraging, can you get us some of them? They are very good, I promise!''So many berries! This is excellent. You are truly a good ${RACE}, ${PLAYER}.'The Earth-kin are fond of a certain kind of tuber that grows in the gorges in the east side of Ram Dúath in the Duvairë -- the places now frequented by the Orkish-army and merrevail.The root vegetables grow in the gorges on the east side of Ram Dúath in the Duvairë.

Eetu has asked you to gather vegetables for the Earth-kin of the Suuri-lehmä.'Listen, little one. You are brave to come here and help us. Maybe if you are fighting Orcs and flying bat-women anyway, you will do us another service? We eat the fruits of the earth -- root vegetables -- that grow in the gorges to the east, the old little people call it Duvairë. But now the Orcs and flying bat-women make it hard for us to gather them. If you are there killing, maybe you can bring us some vegetables, too?''Very good! These will make a good stew. You have our thanks, little one.'Ivoreth is concerned for the safety of Barhador as they travel east to Tham Lumren and has asked you to scout the road ahead.Follow the road east toward Tham Lumren, to the sometimes dangerous road crossing described by Ivoreth while watching for threats that may hinder their travel.Continue further east down the road to Tham Lumren, watching for threats that may hinder the travel of Ivoreth and Barhador.Continue your search further east, to Tham LumrenYou have spotted the Elf-lord Glorfindel near the bridge to Tham Lumren, and he is hailing you. You should talk to Glorfindel.Talk to GlorfindelReturn to Ivoreth at her camp in the Angle of Mitheithel and let her know that the road ahead is clear.Return to Ivoreth at her camp'${PLAYER}, I would ask one last thing of you. It would not be necessary were I alone, but with a child in my company, the situation is different. I should have left him in Tornhad, but the lad is persuasive and loves hearing the songs of the Elves. If you would perform but one more act of kindness for us, I would ask you to scout the road ahead.

'There is a crossing to the east where this road meets another going to the south. Wargs have been spotted there before, and I would wish to ensure that they are not there now. Our destination of Tham Lumren is just a short way further east from there. Would you scout the road ahead and ensure that it is free of peril? When you return we will be on our way.''Hail, and well met ${PLAYER}. I have come recently from the House of Elrond and was told I may encounter you in Haudh Erthaid.'

His voice is musical and his eyes sparkle with a joy that fills your heart.

'It is good that you are here, as you may lighten my burdens! I am keeping watch for the Enemy along the roads surrounding Rivendell for the benefit of our mutual friends when they choose to depart.

'You are also making safe this road? I feel then that I need not repeat what you have already done, and may now take myself east of the Baranduin. Thank you, my friend!'You tell Ivoreth that the road is secure and that you encountered the Elf-lord Glorfindel just outside of Tham Lumren.

'Oh, this is excellent news! We will be safe indeed! Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for all you have done for us. May you be well on the rest of your journeys, even as dark times lie ahead.'There are many villainous monsters roaming Angmar, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many angmarim in AngmarSlay many Orcs in AngmarSlay many trolls in AngmarSlay many Uruks in AngmarSlay many Wargs in AngmarSlay many wights in AngmarSlay many worms in AngmarThe Earth-kin have been destroying the siege-engines of the Angmarim as they wheel them through Ram Dúath, but now they are too strongly guarded for the Earth-kin to reach.The war-engines -- siege towers and catapults -- of the Angmarim are in the eastern part of Ram Dúath.

Tuokki has asked you to help destroy the Angmarim siege-towers and catapults.Destroy catapults (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy siege-towers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Chief Tuokki is at the Suuri-lehmä camp in Ram Dúath.

You should return to Tuokki with word of your success.'The Men and Orcs of Angmar have been bringing great wheeled war-engines through Ram Dúath. At first, they often broke on their own. It took many tries before the stupid Orcs learned how to move these clumsy things safely through the pass.

'We thought, they are taking such pains, perhaps we can help them too. So we showed them the strength of stone and broke many of them ourselves, seeing as the evil ones seemed to want them in the South so badly.

'Now, though, they have learned again, and the war-engines are too well-guarded for us. But maybe you can fight through to them. These must be treasures for these evil folk, things they need to make war in the South. You can find them in the eastern pass.''It is good that those engines were broken. We would not want the Orcs to think they had easy lives!

'I know you fight the Orcs and Men of Angmar for your own reasons, but it is good that we can fight them together in Ram Dúath.''Destroy the war-engines and show the Orcs the strength of stone.'Discover each of the key battlegrounds for control of the Ice Bay of Forochel.NOT USEDForochel is dotted with many small hunting-camps, including Hylje-leiri, the Camp of the Seal.Karhu-leiri, the Camp of the Bear, is one of many Lossoth hunting-camps spread across Forochel.Pynti-leiri, the Camp of the Hunt, is one of the more popular hunting-camps of the Lossoth.Norsu-leiri, the Camp of the Mammoth, was established by the Lossoth as a place from which to hunt the native mammoths.The distracted Hal is once again looking for a different item than the one with which he was tasked.The flower Hal wants grows among the mounds of Glynafon, to the south.Find the warg-infested mounds of Glynafon where Hal saw the flowerWargs can be found prowling around Glynafon. Hal saw the flower he wanted among the old mounds there, but the wargs will make collecting it difficult.Defeat wargs around Glynafon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect the rare flowerHal is by the road north of Glynafon, waiting to hear of your success collecting the rare flower.'I can't go back just yet, I'm still searching for another... plant for my lovely Elf-maid! Yes, a rather rare plant at that. Worry not, I've already spotted it! There's just one problem... there seem to be rather a lot of Wargs around the area in which it is growing. Normally I'd just slip in and out, but I'm feeling a bit weak from those mushrooms earlier.'

'Since you seem so capable, do you think you could try and retrieve the flower for me? It's delicate and very beautiful, and I saw it growing among the mounds to the south. I know it's asking a lot... but I really need this plant before I head back. What do you say?''You made it back! Does that mean...?'

You show Hal the flower you picked among the old mounds.

'That's it! I'm sure it was dangerous, but it certainly paid off in the end. Now I can give this to my lovely Elf-maid and she is sure to be impressed! Smitten, even!

'Thank you for helping me, not once but twice! Or thrice? It is not every day someone will set aside their own tasks to help with someone else's! Good day to you, good day!'Glóin has sent several dwarves ahead to establish a small camp at the High Crag.Larus and Vighar are at a small camp in the High Crag, east of Glóin's camp.

Glóin asked you to find his friends Larus and Vighar at the High Crag camp and aid them.'There is much to do in the snowy hills to the north and east of us. A few of my friends, Larus and Vighar, have ventured to the east and set up a small camp in the High Crag. Seek them out and aid them however you can.''Glóin sent you over to help? Whenever you find your way back to him thank him for that. There is much to do here.'Defeat trolls in Urugarth.Defeat trolls in UrugarthDefeat trolls in Urugarth.Defeat trolls in UrugarthThe dwarves at Gabilshathûr await a delivery of broken great swords to be made to Avar.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver broken great swords from the Orcs surrounding Gabilshathûr to Avar at the dwarf-outpost.Wanted: Broken great swords from the Orcs surrounding Gabilshathûr. Delivery of the items should be made to Avar at the dwarf-outpost.Wanted: Broken great swords from the Orcs surrounding Gabilshathûr.'That serves them right! We'll melt this down and forge it right.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The dwarves of the Misty Mountains have requested a collection of Huge Ears.Collection boxes for this task can be found at the camps within the Misty Mountains.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Huge ears from the beasts in the area of the Bruinen Source. 

