You should talk to Cad Buckthorn.Talk to Cad Buckthorn'As you can see, the reconstruction efforts here in Trestlebridge have left the village in a bit of a mess. There are a lot of empty crates left all over the village.

'Would you mind picking up the empty crates and delivering them to the store house? If you assist us, then we will be able to load up the crates with more supplies and speed up our reconstruction efforts.''Thank you! This helps us a great deal! The Woodcutter's Brotherhood is grateful for your assistance, ${CLASS}.'The Council of the North is in need of a means to identify their warriors in the field.Hróar is at Gath Forthnír in Angmar.

Hróar has asked you to craft some Crests of Vigilance and bring them to him.'I have heard that you have some considerable skill in the craft of metalsmithing, ${PLAYER}. I would ask something of you, if you would aid the Council of the North in their battle against Angmar.

'There are certain intricate symbols that we use to identify our warriors in the field in order to reduce the risk of enemies infiltrating our ranks. Unfortunately, these Crests of Vigilance are in short supply, and we have little time for their crafting, given our pressing need to maintain weapons and armour.

'You can learn how they are made here in Gath Forthnír. If you can aid us in this simple task, the Council of the North will be indebted to you.''Ah, yes, these will do nicely! Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for your assistance.'Thornmane seeks your assistance cultivating the Wildwood's trees.Places to plant trees and to mark the wilderyew trees can be found in the southern Wildwood.

Thornmane has asked you to mark the wilderyew trees for culling and to plant the seeds of a less aggressive tree type.Mark wilderyew trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Plant seedlings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thornmane is in the southern Wildwood.

You should talk to Thornmane.Talk to Thornmane'It is good work that you have done here, Little One, hoom. As promised, I will teach you what trees your townsfolk may harvest. Beside me is a full-grown wilderyew, toom-haroom, and it should not be here. Perhaps a bird carried a seed to the Wildwood from far away lands. Perhaps the Orcs brought the seeds with them, unwittingly as is their way in most things. Either way, wilderyew trees will crowd out others around them and block out the sun. You may mark those you find for removal and use by the people of Trestlebridge.

'The seeds and saplings you gathered will not be ready for planting for some time yet. However, I have brought with me seeds for strong trees that are ready to be sown. Go forth, mark the wilderyew trees, and plant what you may, that the Wildwood grows strong once more.

'I shall continue south, for the trees there whisper enticing rumours of which I wish to learn more.''It is good work that you have done here, Little One, hoom. As promised, I will teach you what trees your townsfolk may harvest. Beside me is a full-grown wilderyew, toom-haroom, and it should not be here. Perhaps a bird carried a seed to the Wildwood from far away lands. Perhaps the Orcs brought the seeds with them, unwittingly as is their way in most things. Either way, wilderyew trees will crowd out others around them and block out the sun. You may mark those you find for removal and use by the people of Trestlebridge.

'The seeds and saplings you gathered will not be ready for planting for some time yet. However, I have brought with me seeds for strong trees that are ready to be sown. Go forth, mark the wilderyew trees, and plant what you may, that the Wildwood grows strong once more.

'I shall continue south, for the trees there whisper enticing rumours of which I wish to learn more.''Shepherding a forest is a balance of plant and cull. With your help, the Wildwood will flourish once more.'Defeat many of the Dead in the Angle.Defeat many of the Dead in the Angle.Defeat many of the Dead in the AngleDefeat many of the Dead in the Angle.Defeat many of the Dead in the Angle.Defeat many of the Dead in the AngleThere is much to do while adventuring in the Angle.There is much to do while adventuring in Deepscrave.Complete Explorer of the AngleComplete Quests of the AngleComplete Slayer of the AngleComplete many deeds in the Wildwood.Complete many deeds in the Wildwood.Complete: Explorer of the WildwoodComplete: Quests of the WildwoodComplete: Slayer of the WildwoodComplete: The League of the WildwoodThe Barrow-downs were once a stronghold of the Rangers of Cardolan, but after the destruction of the last remnant of Cardolan, the Witch-king sent fell spirits to stir the bones of the dead and make it a place of terror.Complete Defeating the Dead -- Small FellowshipComplete Defeating the Dead -- FellowshipComplete Defeating the Dead -- RaidThe Barrow-downs were once a stronghold of the Rangers of Cardolan, but after the destruction of the last remnant of Cardolan, the Witch-king sent fell spirits to stir the bones of the dead and make it a place of terror.Defeat fifty monsters in one Skirmish sessionDefeat one hundred monsters in one Skirmish sessionDefeat two hundred and fifty monsters in one Skirmish sessionThe Barrow-downs were once a stronghold of the Rangers of Cardolan, but after the destruction of the last remnant of Cardolan, the Witch-king sent fell spirits to stir the bones of the dead and make it a place of terror.Defeat fifty monsters in one Skirmish sessionDefeat one hundred monsters in one Skirmish sessionDefeat two hundred and fifty monsters in one Skirmish sessionThe Barrow-downs were once a stronghold of the Rangers of Cardolan, but after the destruction of the last remnant of Cardolan, the Witch-king sent fell spirits to stir the bones of the dead and make it a place of terror.Defeat fifty monsters in one Skirmish sessionDefeat one hundred monsters in one Skirmish sessionDefeat two hundred and fifty monsters in one Skirmish sessionGlóin is seeking news of one of his distant cousins who is trading in the land of Forochel.Forochel lies north of Evendim through Cirith Rhiw, north of Tyrn Fornech. You should start your search in the village of Kauppa-kohta.Talk to Leithólf'Have you heard of the land of Forochel? It lies north and far to the west of here and is an inhospitable place filled with grinding ice and strange peoples. Though I have never been there, one of my cousins, Leithólf, recently led a group of my people up to Forochel to seek their fortunes trading with the Lossoth.

'If you were to travel to those lands, I would ask you to seek out Leithólf and ensure that he is safe. I have not heard from him in many months, though that is his way, coming and going for long stretches of time without correspondence to his kin.

'He said that he would be taking his caravan to Kauppa-kohta. A strange sounding name for a town, isn't it? He said it lay north of the land of Evendim through Cirith Rhiw, the Gate to the North.''Have you started your journey to Forochel yet, ${PLAYER}? It lies north of Tyrn Fornech. Seek the town called Kauppa-kohta.''My cousin Glóin? I have not had word from him in many long months. It is good to know that he is well, though with my troubles here, I do not know when I would be able to travel back to visit him.'Having defeated the Warg pack-leader Blackfang and discovered the likely whereabouts of the missing Elvish hunter Glorwen, you now face the grim task of proceeding into the depths of Goblin-town itself to effect her rescue!Glóin is encamped outside the entrance to Goblin-town.

Nogmeldir has asked you to find Glóin and ask for aid finding Glorwen.Glorwen is imprisoned in Goblin-town.

Nogmeldir has asked you to find and rescue the scout Glorwen.'So, Blackfang revealed Glorwen's fate to you before he was himself torn to pieces by his own pack? I deem it a fitting fate for such a monster, but not for poor Glorwen!

'There is but one glimmer of hope that remains -- the hatred of the goblins for my people is such that they will not kill Glorwen if they can help it. They would much rather keep her in endless toil and torment until her will to live breaks and she either loses her mind or dies of her own accord.

'Luckily, Glorwen is no faint maiden to be easily broken by such as they, and thus we may have some time to effect her escape -- but I would not have her suffer a minute longer beneath at the tender mercies of the goblins!

'I have heard that Glóin, a dwarf yet still a friend, has set up a camp outside of Goblin-town. Find him and he will share with you what he knows of the depths and dungeons hidden beneath.''Hurry, ${PLAYER}! You must find Glorwen in Goblin-town before it is too late!''Leave me be! Touch me again, and I'll break your arm as I did the last of you filthy beasts who dared try it!'

'Oh! Forgive me! In this eternal darkness one does not come to expect a friendly face at the door...Who are you and how have you come to this hellish place?! Are you a fellow prisoner who has found a means of escape? Or a truly foolish ${RACE} who has come down here of your own accord?

'Never mind -- it matters not. All that matters now is that we free the others and find our escape from this deadly prison, before we meet our ends so far from the light of the stars.''They think an Elf is caught within the dungeons down beneath? Goblin-town has re-awoken and I fear there's more than just one trapped in those depths. I do not remember where the dungeons are within, it was a long time ago. It will be up to you to explore and find where they are being kept.'Your success against the Wargs of Forochel has brought you great respect from the Lossoth hunters. Valtteri seeks your aid one more time.The red-fang behemoth can be found among the dark rocky hills far to the south-west of Kauppa-kohta.

Valtteri has asked you to hunt down and defeat the red-fang behemoth, using a burning Lossoth token to frighten the beast.Defeat the red-fang behemothValtteri is in the northern part of Kauppa-kohta.

You should return to Valtteri and tell him of your victory against the red-fang behemoth.'The most vicious of the Surmâja, which some call the behemoth, waits for us among the rocks to the south-west. The beast has been made stronger by the Rauta-väki and has grown far too powerful for our hunters to defeat alone.

'Perhaps you can help us drive away or slay the beast. We will rub the Surmâja-fat you brought us on a token of the Lossoth and set it alight.  Place this token in the ground when the behemoth attacks. Hopefully the beast will become frightened, and you may attack it in its confusion.

'The behemoth is a terrible foe, and you should use caution when approaching it.''Use our fire token to drive the beast mad! You should find the behemoth in the hills to the south-west.''The beast is gone. Our traders will be able to pass this way freely, without fear of being tracked by servants of Angmar.

'We are grateful that you have walked with us, as the hirvi walks among the kettu.

'A gift has been prepared for you. May there be many paths to guide you.'The notes you discovered spoke of trolls being kept in the deep parts of Goblin-town, drumming to stir up the goblins and prepare them for battle. Glóin has tasked Vighar with organizing parties to enter the drum areas and kill the trolls and the leader of the lashers there to lessen the threat that they represent to the people west and east of the Misty Mountains.Goblin-town is to the north-east of Glóin's camp.

Vighar has asked you to find your way through the stronghold to the area where the troll-drummers are watched over by the lashers. Kill several of these goblins and their leader, Kaushar.Defeat KausharDefeat Goblin-town lashers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Vighar Roadwalker is at Glóin's camp just outside of Goblin-town.

Kaushar and the lashers used their trolls against you, but you were successful in defeating them. You should now return to Vighar with your report.Speak with Vighar at Glóin's camp outside of Goblin-town'Your discovery in Goblin-town has us all on edge around here, ${PLAYER}. Something terrible is amiss, and we must be vigilant against that growing darkness or face a terrible foe when they are organized.

'Glóin would like to see that this never comes to pass and has asked me to find those willing to face the strongest enemies within Goblin-town.

'The translation of the sheaf mentioned goblin-lashers keeping troll-drummers in line in the deep places of Goblin-town. We need you to go there, seek out these lashers, kill them and their leader, then return to us.''We do not know where the trolls and the goblin-lashers may be within the stronghold. We know only that the notes you recovered makes mention of them.''This news is bright indeed, friend! You are proving an invaluable asset to us.

'We are in your debt, and I personally thank you. I have no desire to face a host of trolls driven forward by cruel goblin masters.'Oghûk wants revenge on Kaushar, the goblin who imprisoned him for causing trouble with the troll-drums in the deep places of Goblin-town.Troll-drummers can be found in the deep places of Goblin-town.

Oghûk wants to exact vengeance on Kaushar, a goblin who mends the drums in the deep places of Goblin-town. He blames Kaushar for his imprisonment and wants to cause him suffering and pain. It is an unpleasant task, but Oghûk will not help you if you do not help him first.Oghûk is in his cell in the Goblin-town prison.

The troll-drummers were found in an area deep within Goblin-town. Watched over by goblin-taskmasters, you found the trolls and defeated them as requested.Return to Oghûk at his cell in the Goblin-town prison'Kaushar is to blame for this. I used to mend the drums in the place of the trolls, and Kaushar complained to Aklash who locked me away. Kaushar now mends the drums in my place.

'Kaushar must be punished for this. He is in the deep places where the trolls are. Go there and kill his drummers.

'While you're about your job, I'll figure out who has the key to my cell.''Kill Kaushar's trolls. This will make him angry and give me time to think where the key might be.''Ha! The sniveling worm! Kaushar is probably fuming about the loss of his trolls. You've done well, ${RACE}.'In the Wildwood roams an elk with a coat as black as pitch.Dúgar the Black Elk can be found in the southern Wildwood.

Linnet has asked you to defeat the Black Elk, Dúgar.Defeat Dúgar the Black ElkLinnet is located in the south-central Wildwood.

You should talk to Linnet Redholm.Talk to Linnet'Dúgar the Black Elk. His was one of the first tales to reach my ears. They say he roams the southern Wildwood, fleet of foot and fierce of horn.

'Think you are up to the task of defeating him? Others have tried and failed.''A fine beast and a fine victory! I never doubted you could do it, of course.'Explore the enemy encampments found within the Angle.Explore the enemy encampments found within the Angle.Explore EitheldirExplore GlynafonExplore Ost WaerenExplore ThelgarthThe leaders of the League of the Axe and the Woodcutter's Brotherhood look to work together to achieve their goals in the Wildwood.Aran Greenwith and Enid Nettlesting plan to meet in the centre of the Wildwood.

