You should talk to Aran Greenwith.Talk to Aran GreenwithYou should return to either Trestlebridge or Trader's Wharf.Return to Trader's WharfReturn to Trestlebridge'Now that the Woodcutter's Brotherhood has retained our foothold in the Wildwood and accomplished much, I believe it is time to discuss ownership of the Wildwood with the League of the Axe. Let us set a meeting between our groups upon neutral grounds within the Wildwood. There I hope we can discuss a peaceful solution to both our factions vying for the same resources.''Now that the League of the Axe has grown our foothold in the Wildwood and enriched each of our lives, I believe it is time to discuss ownership of the Wildwood with the Woodcutter's Brotherhood. Let us set a meeting between our groups upon neutral grounds within the Wildwood. There I hope we can discuss a solution to both our factions vying for the same resources.''Yes Aran, I think that we can work together to gather and preserve the wood's resources. The longevity of the Wildwood is important to the League of the Axe. Will the League of the Axe be welcome to trade and sell goods at Trestlebridge? Also, what do you think of my proposal concerning our two factions?''Enid, the League of the Axe is more than welcome in Trestlebridge. We shall set up a permanent trading post in town for you. Then it is settled, since we now share the same goals, let us combine our knowledge and resources and watch over the Wildwood together. Your proposal is sound. Henceforth we shall all be known as the League of the Wildwood!

'${PLAYER}, Enid and those of the League are good people. If we were not so busy with our own problems and difficulties that we faced in the Wildwood, perhaps we could have united in our causes sooner. A lesson learned, I suppose. I am glad that we have found a common ground on this day. The future of the Wildwood is indeed a bright one.'Defeat many evil Men in the Angle.Defeat many evil Men in the Angle.Defeat many evil Men in the AngleDefeat many evil Men in the Angle.Defeat many evil Men in the Angle.Defeat many evil Men in the AngleExplore the sites and ruins of the Angle.Explore the sites and ruins of the Angle.Complete Sites of the AngleComplete Enemies of the AngleExplore much of the Wildwood.Explore much of the Wildwood.Complete: Sites of the WildwoodComplete: Flowers of the WildwoodFaeron has been charged with recovering a number of Ranger caches in preparation for the next mission of the Dúnedain, but he insists upon making a game of it.The first Ranger cache is located north-east of Tornhad, beyond a still pond, nestled among the rocks west of the base of a swiftly-flowing waterfall.Reach the Ranger cache before FaeronFaeron stands smugly by the first Ranger cache.Talk to Faeron by the Ranger cacheThe second Ranger cache is located just to the north, across the river, nestled in a ditch near the western cliff's edge.Reach the Ranger cache before FaeronFaeron might approach at any moment, but if you can catch him in the act you will win the contest.Remain alert for Faeron's approach, and catch him in the act!Faeron thinks to sneak by your guard and collect the Ranger cache? Show him he cannot slip by you!Apprehend FaeronFaeron stands by the second cache, quite pleased with himself.Talk to Faeron by the Ranger cacheThe third Ranger cache is located on an island in the stream a short distance to the north-east.Collect the third Ranger cache on an island in the stream to the north-eastFaeron has not yet seen you. Now is your chance to surprise him!Surprise FaeronThe third Ranger cache is located on a small island in the middle of the stream.Collect the Ranger cacheThe Ranger Mithrendan is back at Tornhad.'For the Dúnedain of Tornhad life is a steady routine, always preparing for the next mission. It wears on you after awhile, ${PLAYER}. Will the day for which we constantly prepare ever arrive? Who can say? For my part I devise means of keeping myself entertained, without which I might go mad!

'Some of our number prepare for an eastward journey and have need of some caches that lie hidden throughout the Angle. Mithrendan has charged me with recovering three such caches, and I will do so, but what say you to this suggestion: Why not make this a contest?

'You shall go to the location of each cache, and if I can reach it before you do, or open the cache without you detecting my presence, I shall win! This will allow me to practice my skill at the art of stealth, Mithrendan will receive the supplies he needs, and you will test your perceptive ability. There are only winners here, ${PLAYER}. The first cache is north-east of Tornhad, beyond a still pond, nestled among the rocks west of the base of a swiftly-flowing waterfall. I look forward to besting you at this game!''You shall go to the location of each cache, and if I can reach it before you do, or open the cache without you detecting my presence, I shall win! This will allow me to practice my skill at the art of stealth, Mithrendan will receive the supplies he needs, and you will test your perceptive ability. There are only winners here, ${PLAYER}. The first cache is north-east of Tornhad, beyond a still pond, nestled among the rocks west of the base of a swiftly-flowing waterfall. I look forward to besting you at this game!''You're too late, ${PLAYER}. I win this round!''Looks like I win this round, ${PLAYER}. You will need to be quicker if you are to beat me to the next cache, or to see through my stealth!

'The next cache is just to the north, across the river, nestled in a ditch near the western cliff's edge. I wish you good fortune... you will need it!''The next cache is just to the north, across the river, nestled in a ditch near the western cliff's edge. I wish you good fortune... you will need it!''I am sorry for this deception, ${PLAYER}, but Faeron insisted that I help him in this.'

This is not Faeron at all but Helchon, young Ranger of Tornhad!'I am sorry about this, ${PLAYER}, but I could not deny Faeron his wish.''Young Helchon has not the years to deny his elders anything, which makes him a useful ally when I have need of outwitting one such as you at a friendly contest, ${PLAYER}.

'Ah, do not frown so! It is only a game, after all! How about we call off the contest, my good ${RACE}, in the interest of preserving our young friendship? You can find the last cache and bring it back to Mithrendan, and I will carry the first two back to him, heavy though they are. It is only fair, and I will not embarrass you further!

'The last cache is on an island in the stream a short distance to the north-east.''How about we call off the contest, my good ${RACE}, in the interest of preserving our young friendship? You can find the last cache and bring it back to Mithrendan, and I will carry the first two back to him, heavy though they are. It is only fair, and I will not embarrass you further!

'The last cache is located on an island in the stream a short distance to the north-east.''Wha-?'

Faeron jumps, startled at your approach, and when he sees it is you his face falls.

'Ah, you got me, ${PLAYER}. Yes, I told you I was not going to try to reach this cache, but I thought I might surprise you and win all three rounds. Very well, very well. But now you get to pick up this cache and bring it all the way back to Mithrendan. Enjoy your victory and your aching arms, then!'

Faeron smirks at you.

'Perhaps I am more skilled at stealth than I am at losing with grace, ${PLAYER}, but that is not a requirement of my duty. I thank you for the game.''Now you get to pick up this cache and bring it all the way back to Mithrendan. Enjoy your victory and your aching arms!''Thank you for the contents of this cache, ${PLAYER}. They will be of great use for the Dúnedain that travel soon eastward.

'I understand that you bested Faeron at one of his innumerable contests? I daresay it will do him some good to be overmatched from time to time! Few among the Dúnedain have the time or the patience to play at his games any longer. Still, he is a master of stealth and brings valuable skills to our people whenever he sets his mind to his duty.

'Thank you again for this, my friend.'Minda Heathertoes' pony and waggon have been located, but she still has a job to do: collecting ingredients for her master's feast.Feast ingredients can be found in the Wildwood.

Minda Heathertoes needs help gathering ingredients for a grand feast.Collect Wildwood moose meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Wildwood boar meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Wildwood bear meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collected Wildwood Huorn bark (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Complete Wildwood DelicacyMinda is in a camp in the southern Wildwood.

You should talk to Minda Heathertoes.Talk to Minda Heathertoes'We need meat from the game animals in Wildwood. Please bring me cuts of boar, moose, and bear.

'Also have I heard tell of terrible walking trees in these woods! My master insists that, and I do quote, 'Huorn are rotten to the core, but their bark produces the perfect flavour when smoking meat and fish!' If you come across any of these monstrous walking plants, please bring me their bark.

'Stomper and me are heading south. I have heard there is a merchant over this hill who has a supply of a special spice I require.''So many dishes, so many ingredients! My future as a chef is doomed if I return empty handed!''I do not know how I could do this without you, ${PLAYER}! Well, I could not do this without you at all. I would have to hang my head in shame and return a failure.

'I can cross off so many ingredients from my list now! You have saved the feast and my apprenticeship!'Someone has posted a task to collect feathers in the Wildwood.Feathers can be found on birds in the Wildwood.

