You should return to Grun Curldock with the fish you have collected.'We're not going to get much work done on an empty stomach. The League needs to eat! That's why I cast some nets into the Brandywine River. The river should provide us with some good food each day.

'Would you check on the nets for me? Collect any fish you find for me and League will be grateful.''Now that is a good haul! We'll not go hungry tonight! Thank you for assisting the League, ${CLASS}.'The Elves of Lothlórien now consider you a dear friend.You must earn Friend standing with the GaladhrimThe lords of Carn Dûm sent three of their servants to keep the people of Donnvail under control. If the mighty Gorthorog known as Fûshath the Beast is defeated, the grip of the shadow on the city might be loosened.Fûshath the Beast can often be found in the neighbourhood east of Una's allies.

Enan has tasked you with defeating Fûshath the Beast, the mighty Gorthorog enforcer.Enan is by Una's allies, in the city of Donnvail, west of the neighbourhood where Fûshath the Beast could once be found.

You should return to Enan with news of your victory.'Donnvail was a beautiful city once, proud and free; that must be why it attracted the eye of the Iron Crown. The lords of Carn Dûm sent three of their servants to keep the city beneath the yoke. All are powerful, but perhaps the Gorthorog known to us as Fûshath the Beast is the most terrifying.

'Fûshath the Beast is the enforcer for Muiráthakh, the Silent Judge, and he is a most frightening creature; he knows no mercy and must be given none.

'Find this terrible foe in the neighbourhood next to this one, through the eastward arch, and put an end to his menace. You will need many allies, for Fûshath the Beast is very strong and very dangerous.''Our fortunes must be changing, ${PLAYER}: Fûshath the Beast is defeated!

'You have done a great thing this day, my friend! Donnvail will be free once more, I can sense it!''We will be better able to strike against our oppressors if Fûshath the Beast is no longer among their ranks...or among the living.

'Look for him in the neighbourhood beyond the eastward arch.'A delicious sap can be found in the Wildwood, and the Woodcutter's Brotherhood looks to tap into this resource.Tree tappers can be found in the Wildwood.

You should gather sap from the tree tappers in the Wildwood.Gather sap from tree tappers in the Wildwood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cad Buckthorn can be found in Trestlebridge.

You should return to Cad Buckthorn with the sap you have collected.'There are many ways to assist Trestlebridge. One such task is harvesting the resources of the Wildwood so that the village has more to trade with and to offer passing travellers.

'One resource of the Wildwood is its delicious sap, found within some of the trees there. We have already tapped the trees that produce this sap and could use a volunteer to harvest it for us. Will you assist us? The Brotherhood will be grateful for your assistance.''I see that you've returned with the sap. This is a good amount indeed! I will take it from you and bring to someone in town that is proficient in cooking it and bringing out the great flavour within. The Brotherhood appreciates your assistance, ${CLASS}.'You should bring what news of the giants you uncover from journeying near the halls of the giants in the Misty Mountains.The Giants' Table is south of the pass of Rakhâs-bizar, east of the guarded pass of Gabilazan.Seek the Giants' Table in the Misty MountainsThe Giants' Table is south of the pass of Rakhâs-bizar, east of the guarded pass of Gabilazan.Find the Giants' TableYou found the Giants' Table, but the giants there attacked without warning. They have lost their respect for the old ways, and the Giants' Table is no longer a place of peaceful negotiation.You find yourself journeying near the halls of the giants in the Misty Mountains. Nearby is the Giants' Table, a place of parley in elder days.You found the Giants' Table, but the giants there attacked without warning. They have lost their respect for the old ways, and the Giants' Table is no longer a place of peaceful negotiation.The wargs of Gnawbone Pit should be defeated in order protect those within the Wildwood.Foes can be found at the Gnawbone Pit in the Wildwood.

You should defeat wargs at the Gnawbone Pit.Defeat wargs at the Gnawbone PitFoes can be found at the Gnawbone Pit in the Wildwood.

You should defeat wargs at the Gnawbone Pit.Defeat wargs at the Gnawbone Pit (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The warg dens of Gnawbone Pit are a dangerous place within the Wildwood. Defeating wargs here will assist in returning safety to the Wildwood.Few know the full extent of the depths of Goblin-town, and those who have experienced them most likely died therin as slaves to cruel goblin-overseers. The goblins themselves may not know all the ways, for the deepest passages extend far into the heart of the Misty Mountains where dark and unseen terrors lie, and the goblins will not brave these passages unless driven or enraged.EXPLORE STUFFThe War Steading serves as a large barracks for Goblin-town, where their soldiers and skirmishers gather and prepare for raids upon the villages to either side of the Mountains. Mostly, they descend through the passages to the east to fall upon the smaller and more weakly defended settlements of Men which border the Mirkwood, but on occasion, when their strength grows, they have been known to raid Elf-settlements on the edges of Rivendell's domain -- though these over-bold assaults generally turn out badly for the goblins, and few return.The Thundergrot is aptly named for the enormous booming sounds that echo through the surrounding caves and passages. This thunder is produced by massive drums carried by the Cave-trolls bred and enslaved by the goblins and employed when they raid larger settlements under cover of night.The stench and horror of the Slave Pens of Goblin-town are the subject of dark rumour among travellers who must brave the High Pass, for it is well-known that the goblins delight in taking such folk captive and dragging them down into the depths of the Mountains where they are pressed into cruel labour in the darkness, and few ever again see the light of day.Gollum's Cave is a dark, silent lake nestled down near the roots of the Misty Mountains, and it is said that even the goblins fear it greatly and rarely come here.

The famed hobbit-burglar Bilbo Baggins stumbled into this cave long ago, and there met the wretched creature Gollum. It is said he won his freedom through a Riddle-game, but there is rumour that he did not play fairly.The throne room of Goblin-town, the Den of the Great Goblin, is not a place where most travellers wish to find themselves. Possessed of an odd and unfair sense of justice, the goblins usually bring their captives before the Great Goblin to face his judgement rather than simply imprisoning or killing them. His judgement for presumptive crimes usually involves spying or tresspassing upon the goblin's domain.

Unfortunately for the hapless captives, the outcome of these encounters is fore-ordained, and the punishment for such infractions is always unpleasant -- and ultimately fatal.This sweltering cave houses the forges of Goblin-town, where cruel implements of war and torture are fashioned by over-clever smiths whose knowledge descends from ages ago when the Dark Lord taught them the arts of metalsmithy.The true origin of the ruins that can be found scattered in these caverns is unknown. It is clear that once the dwarves delved here and built their tunnels and mines, but this was lost and abandoned to the goblins so long ago that even among Durin's Folk there are few who remember the names of those who built it or how their story came to an end.The hatred between goblins and dwarves runs deep, and Glóin wants to go on the offensive against the goblins before their threat grows too great.The main gate into Goblin-town is to the north and east of Glóin's camp.

Glóin has instructed you to enter the main gate into Goblin-town and defeat many of the Overland Goblins near the entrance.Defeat goblins in and around Goblin-town (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Discover the main gate into Goblin-townGlóin is at his camp, just outside the entrance of Goblin-town.

Goblin-town teemed with goblins, and the forces within were ferocious and many. You steeled your nerve and struck against them, felling many as you pressed through the entrance of their terrible kingdom. Now you should return to Glóin with news of your success.Talk to Glóin at his camp outside Goblin-town'I first encountered the goblins of Goblin-town when I was with Thorin's Company on our quest to reclaim the Lonely Mountain. They had captured us and dragged us into their vile tunnels, cracking whips and singing terrible songs. We had our vengeance upon them at the Battle of Five Armies, but they simply returned to the Mountains and began gathering their strength again.

'Now with darkness rising everywhere, they have become a threat again...a threat we must hinder as quickly as possible. The entrance we were taken through was hidden, probably a postern gate. Ahead is their main gate. Enter it and wreak havoc among their number.''Be careful, ${PLAYER}. The goblins are treacherous creatures, and they will not hesitate to throw a bag over your head and drag you down to their prisons or mines!''So many goblins! You say that there were more than enough for your blades, and I have no reason to doubt your word. I fear that my friend Dwalin may be right. The Darkness reaching into the Blue Mountains may also be stretching here to the Misty Mountains.

'We must investigate further, I fear, and that means you must go back into the darkness of Goblin-town.'Those who dwell in Trestlebridge have gone through much hardship, and the Woodcutter's Brotherhood know that they can and must assist the village.A crate of cured meats can be found nearby in Trestlebridge.

You should retrieve the cured meats from the crate.Retrieve cured meats from the nearby crateChildren can be found around Trestlebridge.

You should deliver the cured meats to the children of Trestlebridge.Nessa Larch can be found in Trestlebridge.

You should talk to Nessa Larch.Talk to Nessa Larch'It is important that those who dwell in Trestlebridge trust the Woodcutter's Brotherhood. We are here to protect the village and make the village a better place, after all!

'With that said, I would like you to deliver these cured meats to the children of Trestlebridge. They are certainly deserving of sharing in the bounty. It makes the hard work that we have been putting into the Wildwood worth it!''Has all the cured meat been delivered? Very good, my friend. You have done well in assisting the Brotherhood, ${CLASS}.'The Gauredain believe that the grims are the wandering souls of those among their people who were cast out for their cowardice, damned to eternally wander the frozen snow-fields after they froze to death in the ice. Those few among the wise who know of these creatures, however, suspect that they are more likely fell spirits left wandering the northern wastes long after the fall of their ancient Dark Lord.Defeat grims in ForochelIf there is the slightest trace of a once-living spirit within the grim, it would seem that it is not enough to show any sign of compassion or mercy. At the slightest sign of warmth or life they strike, seemingly intent on snuffing it out in a howling assault of hail and hatred.Defeat grims in ForochelThe Lossoth's distrust of you stands in the way of further exploration of Forochel. Impressing Ora, one of the Lossoth-chieftains, may be the only way to continue your efforts in Forochel.Ora's son Kaj may be found near her, at the main lodge. Ora's best scout, Lauri, is near the southern gate of Pynti-peldot. Ora's Master of the Hunt, Niko, may be found at his camp, south-west along the road.

Ora told you that you must gain her trust by helping other Lossoth of her tribe. She suggested you start with her son Kaj, the scout Lauri, and Niko, her Master of the Hunt.Earn the trust of KajEarn the trust of NikoEarn the trust of LauriOra is at Pynti-peldot.

Having gained the trust of three of the Lossoth, you should return at once to Ora.Talk to Chief Ora'If you wish to explore our lands with impunity, you will have to earn that privilege; no Lumi-väki tribe nor any of our kin will so much as answer your queries if you have not been vouched for. And I warn you, not all of my kinsmen will be as welcoming as I. Be courteous, be wary, and be silent unless spoken to.

'I am open-minded, however. If I am given three reports of your worth, you will be granted the tolerance of the Lumi-väki. My son, Kaj, seeks aid in some endeavour or other. I have not the time to attend to it. You might begin with him; he is standing just to the east. And now that I think of it, Niko, our Master of the Hunt, has been looking more harried than usual lately; follow the road south-west and you can find him at his camp on the north side. He may not welcome your assistance, though; he does not think much of Sivullinen. Lauri, my best scout, may also need assistance. You can find him near the stable-master.''My people speak well of you, Sivullinen. You will find tolerance among the Lumi-väki.'Tales of a marvellous white stag who can be found in the Wildwood have reached the ears of Linnet Redholm.The white stag can be found in the south-western Wildwood.

Linnet has asked you to defeat Gwengorn the white stag.Defeat Gwengorn the white stagGwengorn has fled into the hills of the southern Wildwood.

You should pursue Gwengorn.Pursue the white stagGwengorn has led you to a sprung trap in the southern Wildwood.

You should examine the trap.Examine the net trapLinnet is located in the south-central Wildwood.

You should talk to Linnet Redholm.Talk to Linnet'The rumours that drew me here made mention of Gwengorn, a stag with a coat like snow and antlers that rise above the tree tops. I am less inclined to give credence to that last bit, but a white stag would be quite the catch!''He got away from you, did he? Sometimes this is the way of things. Perhaps I will come across him one day.

'It sounds like you did a good deed while you were out there as well. I suppose you got closer to Gwengorn than ever I was able.'Helchon is among the youngest of the Dúnedain sworn to Aragorn, and he is eager to prove his worthiness.Helchon's duty for the day requires him to patrol near the ruins of Thelgarth, to the south and high above Tornhad. He has agreed to meet you there.Talk to Helchon outside the ruins of Thelgarth, high above TornhadHis patrol completed, Helchon waits for you back outside Tornhad.Talk to Helchon in Tornhad'You are an adventurer, ${PLAYER}? It is a pleasure to meet you!

'My name is Helchon, and I am only lately-removed from childhood. Aye, it is true: I am very recently-sworn to the service of Aragorn, chieftain of the Dúnedain. It seems only a short time ago that I led a battalion of my fellows in and around Tornhad, delving into the hillside caves and exploring the woodlands without supervision... but we were only children. Now I am a man grown, and have taken the oath of the Rangers, and will die in service to Aragorn, if I must.

'I am eager to prove my worthiness, but for today I have been tasked with a simple duty: patrolling the bounds of Thelgarth. Perhaps you will accompany me, and tell me of your adventures? It will help pass the time, and I fear nothing so much as I fear boredom and tedium! Has all the magic and excitement gone from the world?

'I will meet you near Thelgarth.''Today I have been tasked with a simple duty: patrolling the bounds of Thelgarth. Perhaps you will accompany me, and tell me of your adventures? It will help pass the time, and I fear nothing so much as I fear boredom and tedium! Has all the magic and excitement gone from the world?

'I will meet you near Thelgarth.''Let us keep on the watch for foes, though I expect few dangers so near to Tornhad. I desire real excitement, like that told in stories of old! But so far it has not presented itself to me.''Thank you for helping me with my patrol, ${PLAYER}. I know that a Dúnadan must put his duty above a concern for glory, and that I will always do... but still I hunger for excitement! Am I wrong to hope that such greater adventures may lie just over the horizon?

'The Angle is my home, and it is dear to me, but I hope to range further afield. I told you of the hillside caves my friends and I explored as children? I know every tunnel and passage of them, not just from those explorations but from nights spent hiding in the dark when we feared Tornhad was threatened by foes seeking the eradication of the Dúnedain. I know why we did not stand and fight... but sometimes I wish we had.

'I will uphold my oath, without question. But it is my small hope that doing so will bring me to distant lands I have never seen, to face dangers that no man has faced, and when my duty is done to hear it said that I did well. Is that too much to ask? I hope not, my new friend. Thank you once more, and may we see each other again... far from here!'The hill of Helva's Edge is a good place to hunt wild game within the Wildwood.Beasts can be found at Helva's Edge in the Wildwood.

