You should clear the rubble to see what was in this section of the mine.Talk to Enid NettlestingEnid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf.

You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.Talk to Enid Nettlesting'You have done much for the League of the Axe since last we spoke, ${PLAYER}. How would you like to join a mining survey? Addy Rushtuft here is leading a survey expedition to Writhenset, in the Wildwood. Speak to her when you are ready and she will fill you in with the details.''Yes, I'm Addy Rushtuft. Are you here for the survey expedition? Good to hear! There's some nefarious folk at the East-delf and West-delf of Writhenset. Let's begin by making life in the Wildwood difficult for them. Destroying their supplies and mined stones should complete that task! Then we'll be able to get into the mines without a problem.''Great work, ${PLAYER}. Looks like we sent those scoundrels running! Now is our chance to enter the mines. I'd like you to challenge the foreman and overseer of Writhenset. I'm sure they deserve what's coming to them. While you're at it, why don't you weaken some of the support beams in there? That will send a message, all right!'

You are taken aback by Addy Rushtuft's words and see now that she is no more honourable than Nye Crowfoot. You agree to assist Addy but form your own plan as you continue to question the reputable nature of the League of the Axe.

'All right, ${PLAYER}, into the mines we go.''Ah, you are back from the mining survey. How did it go? I see, you were met with some hostility from brigands and Orcs. I am not surprised that they look to pillage the old mine.'

You ask about the League's intentions for the mine of Writhenset.

'Why we wish to make the mine safe once again and extract stone for trade. I hope that is acceptable to you.'

You now judge Enid of honourable character and relinquish the information you have been holding close about the less than reputable actions of Nye Crowfoot and Addy Rushtuft as well as the hidden tomb of Arnor.

'I see. I have had my suspicions about those two but did not have any proof to expel them from the League. I have been sending you on expeditions with them to monitor their actions in the Wildwood. I knew I judged your character as true and could trust you. We must now keep an even closer eye on Nye and Addy. Now as for this hidden tomb, the League of the Axe is not comprised of tomb-robbers. I have no interest in an old tomb. If we work in the mines however, we will proudly protect and preserve the tomb.'Bilbo Baggins has completed his book and would like to make certain that his memory of the important locations and events is correct.Dwalin is at Thorin's Hall far to the west, beyond the Shire. Glóin is at his camp north of Rivendell.

Bilbo Baggins would like to know if his dwarf-friends Dwalin and Glóin have any recollections which would make good additions to his book.Talk to Glóin in the Misty MountainsTalk to DwalinBilbo Baggins is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws, south of Glóin's camp and far to the east of Thorin's Hall.

Dwalin and Glóin both shared stories of their adventure in Goblin-town. Now you should return to Bilbo.Talk to Bilbo Baggins in Rivendell'All this talk about Goblin-town and my adventures with Thorin and company has brought back many memories. I was wondering if it wouldn't be too much a bother to have you visit my old friends. I have heard tell that Dwalin is at Thorin's Hall in the Blue Mountains, away west of the dear old Shire and that Glóin is encamped in the Misty Mountains, north from here.

'I wonder if they have any memories of Goblin-town which I could add to my book. Would you visit them and find out for me?

'I would go, but I pledged I had made my last journey. Well, my last journey for a long while anyway.''If you would, please speak with my old dwarf-friends about their memories of Goblin-town. Dwalin is at Thorin's Hall, Glóin at his camp in the Misty Mountains.''Bilbo has you researching Goblin-town? We had a terrible time there. I was sure the Great Goblin was going to make an end of us... but then Gandalf came along and saved the day.

'The fire went out, and all we could see was a towering column of smoke and sparks and Glamdring flashing blue in the dark. The Great Goblin fell dead, and his folk went all wild.

'We still might not have escaped that place, if it hadn't been daylight outside.''Bilbo Baggins? Old Burglar Baggins? There is a name I have not heard in many, many years.

'So he would like my impressions of Goblin-town? Well, they were not good, that is for certain. All the whips, the stench, the goblins, the wretched songs they sang... it was a dreadful ordeal altogether.

'And to make it worse, when Dori lost our burglar in those tunnels, and Gandalf demanded we go back for him... well, we nearly despaired. Then he appeared out of nowhere, alive! Oh, that was a strange day.''Good old Bilbo. I have never met a burglar his equal. We were lost in the great Mirkwood without him. And oh the surprise he gave us when we fled Goblin-town.

'I tell you friend, Bilbo Baggins is a magnificent burglar.''I remember well of what Bilbo speaks, and I would rather not enter that place again. Darkness stirs in these lands now, and we might yet need to fight our way back through those forsaken tunnels and ancient halls.

'Be cautious if it is Bilbo's charge to send you there.''So you were able to find Dwalin and Glóin? Oh, that is good.

'And Dwalin was impressed by my reappearance after escaping Goblin-town? Well, it never would have happened if I hadn't fallen into that dratted Gollum's cave and found... well, found my way out.

'It's a pity that Gollum-creature escaped the Elf-king's people.'Déornyd has lost his prized weapon, a sword belonging to his sister, who was a champion of great renown among the Eglain.Déornyd thinks his sister's sword is still in or around the ice canyons, south of Pynti-peldot.

Déornyd has asked you to find his sister's sword and return it to him.Recover GránungDéornyd is at Pynti-peldot, north of the ice canyons.

You have found Gránung and should now return it to Déornyd at Pynti-peldot.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! My name is Déornyd of the Eglain. Among my own people, I enjoy a certain renown -- though it is paltry indeed when compared to that of my sister. She was the reason I became a Champion: her courage was unshakeable, her voice commanding, and the flickering of her blades was like the shimmering dance of moonlight on the Red Swamp. She fell in battle against minions of the Enemy, and the world has been a little dimmer ever since.

'I took up her sword, which is named Gránung. I have wielded it as best I could in defence of justice, until recently, when I was travelling here from Taur Orthon through the ice canyons. I was ambushed by something -- all I saw was a flash of fur. Altti, a trapper, found me and brought me here, but without my sword!

'I believe it to be still in the canyons south of here. Please, I beg you, help me recover Gránung! My family's honour as well as my own are at stake.''Have you found it? You have not?

'The ice canyons are south of here; the road leads right to them. I think that is where Gránung must still be. I beg you, please find it!''Can it be?

'It is! Gránung, bright as she shone in the time of my ancestors!

'Blessings on you, ${PLAYER}. You have recovered that which was most precious to me.'The fearsome warg called Natsulm the Night-raider stalks those who venture too far into the Wildwood.Natsulm the Night-raider can be found in the Wildwood.

You should find Natsulm the Night-raider.Find Natsulm the Night-raiderNatsulm the Night-raider can be found in the Wildwood.

You should defeat Natsulm the Night-raider.Defeat Natsulm the Night-raiderThe fearsome warg called Natsulm the Night-raider stalks those who venture too far into the Wildwood. Defeating this fearsome beast will assist in returning safety to the Wildwood.Tongannel is seeking information about the origin of the Gauredain.Forochel lies north of Evendim through Cirith Rhiw, north of Tyrn Fornech. You should start your search in the village of Kauppa-kohta.

Tongannel has asked you to go into the frozen North and seek news of the Gauredain.Go to Kauppa-kohta in Forochel and learn of the Gauredain'I am quite worried about the threat from the North, these Gauredain of which we have seen so many in recent weeks.

'They are not native to this land, for though some believe that they are Men of Eriador gone wild, bereft of morals and virtue, I do not believe that to be true. I believe that these Gauredain come from the far land of Forochel.  There, the bitter ice has kept alive an ancient race of evil Men who have long been in the service of the Enemy.

'Travel to this land and see if what I speak is true. If it is so, then I fear that the Gauredain are a greater threat than we have anticipated.''Have you travelled to Forochel yet? That icy land lies north of Tyrn Fornech in Evendim. Search for someone in the village of Kauppa-kohta who might speak on this matter.''Gauredain? I do not know of such...ah! You mean the Susi-väki! Yes, the Susi-väki live on the western edge of the Ice Bay, though they do not trouble us this far south. We have more pressing issues than the Susi-väki here in Kauppa-kohta.'Barricades found at Norwarden should be destroyed in order weaken the defences of your foes within the Wildwood.Barricades can be found at Norwarden in the Wildwood.

