Bilbo Baggins would like you to help him correct the directions to Goblin-town that he has written in his book.Find the hidden entrance to Goblin-townBilbo Baggins is at the Last Homely House in Rivendell, south-west of Goblin-town.

Having completed the task Bilbo set you to, you should return to him at Rivendell.Talk to Bilbo Baggins at Rivendell'Well, hullo there! You seem a bit of an adventurous sort... perhaps you wouldn't mind helping out an old hobbit?

'You see, I have been writing a book about my travels with Thorin and his Company -- off to deal with Smaug and get Thorin's gold back -- and I am afraid I may have gotten confused on some details. My memory isn't what it used to be, and I am unsure of the directions to some of the places we visited.

'Perhaps you would help me? All you need to do is find the Back Door of Goblin-town... if you find the place, I have remembered them a-right. High in the mountains, along the stretch called the High Pass, we travelled and at night found a dry place in a cave midway up the mountain. You should find the entrance there. If not, well, try and find the correct directions for me, if you would be so kind.''Those directions I gave you should lead you straight to the doorstep of Goblin-town... I hope.''Oh, you found it! That is wonderful.

'Do you know, we found the doorstep quite by accident. We were camping there, taking refuge from a storm and some wayward boulders -- the giants were out playing catch, I suppose -- and were set upon by goblins!

'Gandalf the Grey blasted a few, but we were captured and dragged down to Goblin-town. From there, the tale only gets more exciting.'Aeglas used the stake you provided him to prepare a special surprise for the Orcs.The stake should be placed on a sturdy patch of earth in the place where the Orcs are gathered within Goblin-town.

Aeglas' plan is nearly complete. He believes that the items within the bag will drive the Orcs into a frenzy and set them upon the goblins of Goblin-town.Aeglas is in his cell within the Goblin-town prison.

After placing the Orc-head and pike in the gathering place, the Orcs grew enraged, but the goblins seemed prepared for their aggression and quickly put the matter to end. You should return to Aeglas with your report.Talk to Aeglas in the Goblin-town prison'We are ready to put this plan in motion. If we are successful, then the Orcs and goblins will fall upon one another, perhaps destroying any chance for Angmar to bring Goblin-town under their control.

'Take this sack and place the items within in a firm bit of earth. Make certain that the stake will stand freely. We need to make certain that the Orcs will see it.

'Return to me when you have done what I have asked.''Make your way to the place where the Orcs from Angmar are gathered and put the items within the sack in a sturdy patch of earth there. This should drive the Orcs into a frenzy against the goblins and set them upon one another.''They were prepared for this? It seems that the goblins are more cunning than I had anticipated. I think now it might be necessary to find my way out of this place. 

'I am not certain how, though. Perhaps Oghûk will know a way to get the key.'Someone has posted a task to heal critters who have been poisoned by careless Tarkrîp Orcs.Poisoned critters can be found in the Wildwood.

You should cure the poisoned critters.Cured poisoned critters in the Wildwood.CompletedThe bulletin notice reads:

'Urgent: Small critters in the Wildwood are being poisoned by the Tarkrîp Orcs! Please search the woods for these poisoned animals and cure them. We can not have these animals infecting larger game or being caught and eaten by us! You will be rewarded for your efforts.'You have successfully cured many of the poisoned critters found in the Wildwood. Your efforts to keep watch over the unspoiled beauty of the Wildwood will not go unnoticed by the Free Peoples at Trader's Wharf and Trestlebridge. You will certainly be rewarded for all that you have accomplished.Bilbo Baggins has completed his book and would like to make certain that his memory of the important locations and events is correct.Gandalf and Frodo are in Bilbo's room on the first floor of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.

Uncertain of the task he has set before you, Bilbo Baggins wants you to speak with his nephew, Frodo Baggins, and the Wizard Gandalf the Grey before setting forth on your journey.Talk to Gandalf in RivendellTalk to Frodo Baggins in RivendellBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House at Rivendell.

Gandalf and Frodo warned you of the dangers found in the cavern in the dark. You should return to Bilbo Baggins with their opinions.Talk to Bilbo Baggins'I would hate to ask this of you, ${PLAYER}, but there is another place I would like you to go. The way is quite dangerous, and I simply am not sure whether I should indeed ask it of you, but it is a very important place... it is really where this whole mess began.

'Deep within Goblin-town, there is a cave. I've mentioned it before, I'm sure. A wretched creature called Gollum once lived there. Gandalf says he is related to hobbits, but I just cannot imagine it.

'At any rate, I would like you to find that cave and get me proper directions, as I stumbled into it quite by accident during my adventure with Thorin and Company. But perhaps you should speak with Gandalf the Grey and my nephew Frodo... they might have some reservations about anyone going there.''You really should speak with Frodo and Gandalf before you leave. Let me know what they think of this adventure I have tasked you with. You'll find them in my room on the ground floor.''Bilbo wants you to go where? While Gollum no longer dwells within that cavern, it is by no means safe. You will have to pass through the ranks of goblins in Goblin-town.

'What did he tell you of his encounter with Gollum? Nothing? That is good, for it entails knowledge which you need not be made aware of.

'I cannot hinder you, if you believe yourself up to the task, but I warn against it.''Uncle Bilbo is a dear old hobbit, and he remembers his adventure fondly, but I do not think he even now understands exactly how terrible this whole thing is.

'Gollum is loose, and he is searching for... well, he is searching for something he once possessed. If you go to that place, hope he has not returned there himself.''I dread the place you speak of, though I have never been there myself. Bilbo's encounter there has laid on me a terrible burden and has brought me great woe.''Be cautious should you seek Gollum's cave, for the journey is long and perilous. The goblins will not likely let you pass unharmed.''Well then, you have returned, and that means you have spoken to my nephew and my friend Gandalf. They aren't keen on your going to Gollum's cave? Well, I suppose I can't blame them, but I simply must know what has become of that place and how to find it again.'The Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Complete Pride of Endurance -- Small FellowshipComplete Pride of Endurance -- FellowshipComplete Pride of Endurance -- RaidThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.The Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutesThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.The Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutesThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.The Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutesA hunter found the tables turned when he stumbled into a trap. Poachers will soon be returning for their prize.The poachers' camp can be found in the southern Wildwood.

The hunter has asked for your assistance in defeating the poachers who trapped him.Defeat half-orc poachers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The hunter can be found in the western Wildwood.

You should talk to the hunter you freed.Talk to the hunter'My am I lucky you happened by! It must have been hours since I got myself tangled up in this blasted net. Darn poachers!

'I fear whoever laid this trap will come back for me! I saw some strange looking men camped to the south-east of here. What if they return? I don't stand a chance! Oh, I never should have hunted the White Stag! Please, you must help me!''I cannot thank you enough, friend. I will make my way out of the Wildwood. No more will I trouble the beasts here.'Complete many quests in the Wildwood.Complete many quests in the Wildwood.Complete many quests in the WildwoodComplete many quests in the Angle.Complete many quests in the Angle.Complete quests in the AngleComplete many quests in the Wildwood.Complete many quests in the Wildwood.Complete: Quests in the WildwoodComplete: The League of the AxeComplete: The Woodcutter's BrotherhoodComplete: Missions: The WildwoodInformation received from the letters you recovered in Black Speech led Glóin to offer rewards for the defeat of Rakothúrz and Horm, a goblin-handler and a terrible Cave-troll found in the Great Goblin's throne room in Goblin-town.Goblin-town is to the north-east of Glóin's Camp and the throne room should lay straight through the many tunnels.

Tralli Gemfinder directed you to find and defeat the troll and goblin, Horm and Rakothúrz, within the Great Goblin's throne room.Tralli Gemfinder is at Glóin's camp in the Misty Mountains, outside the entrance to Goblin-town.

You should return to Tralli Gemfinder with news of your success.Talk to Tralli Gemfinder'All you have discovered will contribute to us keeping the Misty Mountains safer in the future. If our number was larger now, I have no doubt that Glóin would once again brave the depths of Goblin-town himself and destroy the goblins there. Alas, we are small in number, and there are greater threats to contain elsewhere. Let us be direct then....

'Glóin would like you to be watchful for the goblin and troll, Rakothúrz and Horm, within the Great Goblin's throne room. Lord Elrond mentioned that the forces of Angmar wanted to draw them into the conflict in the north and west, and if we can destroy them we may save the lives of countless allies.

'Search the throne room in Goblin-town for this troll and goblin, and after they are defeated, return to me. Goblin-town is to the north and east.''Seek out Rakothúrz and Horm within the throne room of Goblin-town.''Well done! A victory against such a terrible foe is surely a great thing.

'You have our thanks and should be content to know that you have saved the lives of many who would surely have suffered terrible fates at the hands of those foes.'The Rangers of Esteldín are in need of warm cloaks for the coming days.Techeron is at Esteldín, in the North Downs.

Techeron has asked you to weave some Rangers' cloaks for his kindred.'A fine day to you during dark times, ${PLAYER}.

I have a matter of craft for you. We have need of fine cloaks for the Rangers of Esteldín. They are something of a mark of pride, not to mention being remarkably useful to those who must live for long periods out among the forests and hills, but they suffer much wear, and our supplies of them are coming up short.

'If you could craft a few Rangers' cloaks for me, I and my kindred would be much obliged!''There we are, cloaks fit for men who must travel far and fast.

'My thanks to you, for every bit helps during this time of hardship.'Poachers have raided a wolf den and stolen the young cubs.Poachers can be found in the south-eastern Wildwood.

Linnet has asked you to rescue wolf cubs who have been captured by poachers.Release wolf cubs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Wildwood Cub Burglars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Linnet can be found in the south-central Wildwood.

You should return to Linnet.Return to Linnet'I came across a very angry wolf while you were gone and ended up spending a good deal of time up a tree so she wouldn't see me. I feared her rage was illness driven, but when I tracked her I found a camp of poachers with cages full of wolf cubs. I don't hold with poachers. They care not for the impact their hunting has on forests.

'I am a hunter, but I am no fighter. Will you release the wolf cubs and deal with the poachers? I will of course make sure you are compensated.''Well done! Wolves can be dangerous, but they are essential to the balance of the land. Without wolves, other creatures would grow too large in number, and soon deplete the resources available.'Orcs have been logging part of the Wildwood and must be stopped before they decimate the forest.Tarkríp tree-reavers and tree-burners can be found in the central Wildwood.

Thornmane has asked you to defeat the Orcs who are wreaking havoc upon the Wildwood's forest.Defeat Tarkríp tree-reavers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Tarkríp fire-starters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thornmane is in the southern Wildwood.

You should talk to Thornmane.Talk to Thornmane'Well, little one, I must say that I am impressed with your deeds, hoom. This part of the forest is already starting to look and feel better. There is still work to be done, however, hoom ta-room.

'The destruction I found as I passed through the Wildwood is quite troubling. I believed it to be the work of the Men of Trestlebridge, hummm. But while you were gone, I observed the twisted creatures responsible for felling and setting fire to the forest. You must stop the Orcs, ${PLAYER}, lest their burning and hewing devastate all of the Wildwood.''Well, little one, I must say that I am impressed with your deeds, hoom. This part of the forest is already starting to look and feel better. There is still work to be done, however, hoom ta-room.

'The destruction I found as I passed through the Wildwood is quite troubling. I believed it to be the work of the Men of Trestlebridge, hummm. But while you were gone, I observed the twisted creatures responsible for felling and setting fire to the forest. You must stop the Orcs, ${PLAYER}, lest their burning and hewing devastate all of the Wildwood.''Well, little one, I must say that I am impressed with your deeds, hoom. This part of the forest is already starting to look and feel better. There is still work to be done, however, hoom ta-room.

