You should talk to Mal Knapweed.Talk to Mal Knapweed'The League prides itself on the tools we wield. I'm sorry to say that some of the axes around here at Trader's Wharf have seen better days! If you'd like to assist us, I think there is something for you to do.

'There might be some whetstones nearby. They are indeed very good when used for sharpening axes and knives. Would you find some for us, then give these axes a good sharpen? The League will be grateful for your efforts.''Those axes look mighty sharp. Harvesting lumber is about to get a might easier! Thank you for assisting the League, ${CLASS}.'The Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Complete Simple Skill -- Small FellowshipComplete Simple Skill -- FellowshipComplete Simple Skill -- RaidThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive in the Barrow-downs for five minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for ten minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes without utilizing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive in the Barrow-downs for five minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for ten minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresThe Enemy in the Barrow-downs is relentless, throwing themselves at their foes without regard to their lives...for they have no life.Survive in the Barrow-downs for five minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for ten minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresSurvive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutes without performing any Fellowship ManouevresExplore the points of interests within the Angle.Explore the points of interests within the Angle.Explore Fernbrake CotExplore Tham LumrenExplore GaerondExplore Cuan-lûth RefugeExplore TornhadExplore the many interesting locations to be found within the Wildwood.Explore the many interesting locations to be found within the Wildwood.Explore Trader's WharfExplore WrithensetExplore the East-delfExplore the West-delfExplore Marl's CrossingExplore Hunter's LedgeExplore Helva's EdgeExplore Blomley SwardExplore the Old Bluff-houseExplore Overwine HallExplore NorwardenExplore SutwardenExplore CotfastExplore Gnawbone PitThe inhabitants of the Barrow-downs do not take kindly to visitors.A shade has appeared within the Barrow-downs. Speak with him to discover why he is here.Talk to the shadeThe Barrow-downs have unleashed their fury. Hold your position for as long as you can possibly stand.Survive for as long as possible'You should not have come here, and now you shall pay for your transgressions. The Dead do not forgive.'The Angle hosts a variety of dangerous creatures and enemies.The Angle plays host to a variety of dangerous creatures and enemies.Slay many beasts in the AngleSlay many of the Dead in the AngleSlay many evil Men in the AngleSlay many Orc-kind in the AngleDefeat many enemies in the Wildwood.Defeat many enemies in the Wildwood.Complete: Wildwood Brigand-slayer (Advanced)Complete: Wildwood Big Game Slayer (Advanced)Complete: Wildwood Orc-kind Slayer (Advanced)Complete: Wildwood Mission-slayer (Advanced)Lauri reported that one of his scouts, Ida, has been missing for some time and that there has been smoke recently seen in the sky near one of the Lossoth homesteads, west of Pynti-peldot.Ida's supply-encampment is to the south of Pynti-peldot, next to the road and near the entrance to the ice canyons.

Lauri has asked you to investigate Ida's supply-encampment and make sure she is not hurt.Check on Ida at the supply-encampment'Ora sent you? I suppose I could use some help. I have an injured scout here, so I dare not venture out of shouting range -- but another of my scouts, Ida, is very late in reporting back.

'Go check on her, if you wish to be of use -- she is at our supply encampment just south of here, along the road. There have also been reports of smoke being seen coming from a homestead, too... make sure everything is as it should be.

'And if she is all right, find out what has been keeping her!''What? Who are you? Lauri sent you to check on me? I am all right; I just took a few bruises.

'There is a homestead further west along the road, past the hill on which Pynti-peldot is built, that is being terrorized by a Gauradan. We do not see many of them in Itä-mâ.

'I barely made it back here to recuperate; I was trying to chase the invader off, and his accursed wolf flanked me....'Thornmane needs assistance gathering saplings and seeds to help restore the depleted Wildwood forest.Seeds and saplings to replenish the Wildwood can be found in central Wildwood.

Thornmane has asked you to gather seeds and saplings to help restore the forest.Collect acorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect pine-cones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thornmane is in the eastern Wildwood.

You should talk to Thornmane.Talk to Thornmane'The Orcs and brigands have done much to harm the forest here. A fine grove once stood where yonder town now squats. If you are of a mind to assist me once more, I would ask another boon of you. While you are trapessing throughout the Wildwood, keep your eyes open for seeds and young saplings, that we might heal some of the damage that has been done.''Ah yes, excellent work, my little friend. These seeds and saplings have much promise. You have given me hope for the Wildwood.'Not content to remain idle while in his cell, the Elf Aeglas has a plan to turn the tables against the goblins of Goblin-town.Stacks of bound posts lie in the main tunnels of Goblin-town.

Aeglas believes that he can turn the Orcs and goblins against one another, but his plan requires that you collect a sharp post for him.'I believe that we can use the information Glorwen has provided us to cause dissent among the goblins and Orcs. If we can sow the seed of rage within the Orcs here, we might cause the goblins and Orcs to fall upon one another.

'To accomplish this, we will need to do something truly dangerous. I need you to bring me a sharp post.

'When I was brought here, I remember passing many lashed and bound posts stacked together in the tunnels above. Cut one of the posts free and bring it to me.''This will do just fine. Give me one moment....'Anornaneth has observed an increased level of activity on the walls of Helegrod, the lost dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains, and is worried about what it might signify.Lord Elrond is in the library of his house in Rivendell.

Anornaneth has asked you to bring word of her fears concerning Helegrod to Elrond.'There is something going on in the mountains, my friend, and I fear what it might signify. Long has the dwarf-city of Helegrod stood empty, abandoned by the dwarves who made it, but cruel folk have come there of late, and I have seen evil Men on the walls.

'I fear the mischief they might do, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps I worry for naught, but this fear has been steadily growing on my mind and I can no longer dismiss it as needless.

'Tell Lord Elrond of my fears, friend. Perhaps he will have some insight that can put them to rest, but I cannot find any good that might come of Helegrod inhabited again.''I hope that my worries are baseless, ${PLAYER}, but I fear that they are not. Go to Lord Elrond in his library, and tell him that Helegrod is inhabited again, and not by dwarves.''Your news gives me pause, ${PLAYER}, for Anornaneth is not one to lightly give voice to such concerns. If Helegrod is indeed inhabited by creatures of evil, the darkness may be closer to Imladris than we had supposed.'The Shadowbark Huorns are defeated, but the darkness that twisted them is still a mystery.The Wicked Holm may be summoned by burning the shadow bark atop a hill in the south-western Wildwood.

Thornmane has asked you to defeat the Wicked Holm.Summon and defeat the Wicked HolmThornmane is located in southern Wildwood.

You should talk to Thornmane.'Hoom, hum. I have spoken with the trees and am troubled anew. They speak of poisoned roots, foul waters, and a silver-barked Huorn called, hummm, how to say it in your speech - the Wicked Holm. Take you this rotten bark and burn it on the hill nearby. I suspect the scent of the smoke will draw out the source of the poisoned shadows.

'Go carefully, my little friend, room-tum. To spread its violence through so many, and so far - I fear the Wicked Holm to be a powerful foe, indeed.''So you found the source, hum, hoom. You have done the Wildwood a favour on this day, little friend.

'I think I will stay here for a time and keep watch over these forests. You have done me a great favour as well, and I am willing to work with your Trestlebridge folk now.'The unpredictability of diversity can be a strength when building a force to be reckoned with.Complete Strength in Diversity -- Small FellowshipComplete Strength in Diversity -- FellowshipComplete Strength in Diversity -- RaidThe unpredictability of diversity can be a strength when building a force to be reckoned with.Survive in the Barrow-downs for five minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for ten minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutes with no duplicate classesThe unpredictability of diversity can be a strength when building a force to be reckoned with.Survive in the Barrow-downs for five minutes with at least one of each classSurvive in the Barrow-downs for ten minutes with at least one of each classSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes with at least one of each classSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes with at least one of each classSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes with at least one of each classSurvive in the Barrow-downs for thirty minutes with at least one of each classThe unpredictability of diversity can be a strength when building a force to be reckoned with.Survive in the Barrow-downs for five minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for ten minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for fifteen minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs for twenty-five minutes with no duplicate classesSurvive in the Barrow-downs f