Minda Heathertoes has asked you to go to Cotfast to gather supplies with which to repair her waggon.Collect sacks of nails (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect woodworking toolsCollect waggon wheels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect cut wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Minda is waiting at Trader's Warf.

You should talk to Minda Heathertoes.Talk to Minda Heathertoes'My dear ${RACE}! A better friend could no one ever ask for!

'Much have you assisted me, but if you would, I have one last request. Heavy are the crates of goods that you have helped me gather. My waggon, however, still lies shattered. The merchants here have told me that we can find the materials needed to build a new waggon in the nearby town of Cotfast.

'I would go myself, but alas, it is full of vicious individuals, and we both know how I'd fare. Please, my friend. Go to Cotfast and collect nails, woodworking tools, wheels, and cut wood. I shall await your return at Trader’s Warf!''You did it, ${PLAYER}! You ensured not only my continued employment, but every ingredient needed for the feast as well! This will be a grand day of celebration! A light of hope during these dark times!

'The League members here have offered to assist me in assembling a new waggon. I should be on the road home in no time. Thank you, a hundred times, thank you!'The Woodcutter's Brotherhood wishes to survey the Wildwood of Bree-land to identify both resources and threats that exist within the wooded hills.Aggy Digweed, Guardsman Otley, Giles Chadwick, and Nellie Boskins can all be found in Trestlebridge.

