You should talk to Aran Greenwith.Talk to Aran Greenwith'Do you know Supervisor Beecher, who maintains the Trestlespan? He is a trusted friend of the Woodcutter's Brotherhood and has been a great assistance in planning the restoration and reconstruction of Trestlebridge that we wish to undertake.

'It is concerning then, when Supervisor Beecher urgently calls upon the Brotherhood. I ask that you seek him out as soon as you are able. Assisting the townsfolk of Trestlebridge is all a part of our cause after all. I hope that the Trestlespan is not in any danger!''I am glad that Supervisor Beecher thoroughly inspects the Trestlespan each morning. Without his diligence, we would not have the great bridge over the chasm of Cirith Nûr. I fear the devious Orcs who planted the black powder thought their plan would remain hidden just long enough to enact terrible destruction upon our town. Returning the powder in force to the Orkish forces and those who enable them in the Wildwood was the correct course of action. You have done well, ${CLASS}.

'Now, I am happy to report that our reconstruction effort of Trestlebridge has begun. Why, have a look for yourself!''Ah, you must be with the Woodcutter's Brotherhood. We do not have much time. I woke up this morning to inspect the Trestlespan, as I do every morning. Look there at what I found! Do you see these hidden Orkish cannisters? Someone planted these here under cover of darkness just the other night! They look to be filled with black powder! I am just glad that they were not yet lit, or there would not be a Trestlespan here this morning!

'Find and remove all the black powder bombs around the Trestlespan for me, then safely dispose of them however you see fit. Quickly now, we do not know when those who planted the black powder will return!''Yes, thanks to your assistance we have already made great strides in our cause. Still, there is much more to be done in the Wildwood and in Trestlebridge.'You hunted the moose as Cenlieg requested, but the lore-master's bear-friend did not like the meat you had given it.The great elk can be found to the south-west of Kauppa-kohta.

Cenlieg has asked you to kill the great elk and bring its flank to him.Collect the Silvan thirty-point's flankCenlieg is at Kauppa-kohta, east from where you found the elk-buck.

You should return to Cenlieg with the elk-flank you collected.'It seems Linden's sensitive stomach is not as grateful as I am for your help. He is of the highest breed, you see, and must be fed lean, tender meat. I promise not to trouble you again, if you can only supply him with some suitable food.

'I have overheard the Lossoth -- wonderful people you know -- saying something about an immense elk-buck who keeps watch over the southern end of the forest. Surely his flanks would be strong and rich for Linden here.

'I think you will find him if you journey south-west into the start of the foothills, just beyond the southern shore.''Linden is quite particular, but if you can just bring him the lean meat he requires, we can be on our way.''Linden's spirits are finally picking up. It seems that after all this time, I should be packing to journey on with you instead of my fellows, but alas I must be on my way to meet them.

'I will prepare to take my leave, but I thank you heartily for your assistance, and I know Linden thanks you as well in his way.'The Corcur of the Misty Mountains fell under the sway of the Angmarim that now control Helegrod.Elladan is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges, west of Rivendell.

Lord Elrond has asked you to bring news of the Corcur now living within Helegrod under the power of Angmar to his son Elladan, who has fought long against them.'The Hillmen of Rhudaur splintered into many different factions after the fighting that broke the North Kingdom, and many lived still among the ruins scattered through the wilderness of the Trollshaws. Many of them tried the passage of the mountains but most were defeated by snow in the high places. Those that endured took the name Corcur and live still in hard places.

'Always they resented their long-ago defeat, searching forever for strong allies to help them reclaim what they had lost. In Angmar they found the ally they sought, and the Corcur now dwell within Helegrod in service to Angmar's will.

'My son Elladan has long fought the Corcur, and knows of their ways. Speak to him at his camp of Thorenhad, among the Bruinen Gorges to the west of Imladris.''My sons have established a camp, Thorenhad, among the Bruinen Gorges, west of Imladris. From there, they watch the wilderness of the Trollshaws for sign of the Enemy. Elladan will be greatly interested to hear of the Corcur that now inhabit Helegrod.''The Corcur have come to live within the walls of Helegrod? That is an evil place, and I do not doubt that the evil power within Angmar hopes to use these new allies for some mischief.

'We must put an end to their evil, ${PLAYER}.'Arohir of Esteldín has bade you seek the hidden camp of Gath Forthnír in the far north, somewhere east of the gates of Carn Dûm, and once there to speak with Annábla.Speak with Annábla of Gath Forthnír.'I have heard rumour that a hidden camp exists near unto the very gates of Carn Dûm in the far north where brave heroes gather to contest the power of Angmar itself.

'I cannot say precisely where Gath Forthnír -- as it is called -- lies, but should you find this place, speak with one called Annábla, and she will tell you more of their purpose.''You have been sent by Arohir, yes? It speaks highly to his confidence in you that he would tell you of our existence at all - and so I have high hopes that you may indeed be able to help us in our desperate cause.''You should speak with Annábla at Gath Forthnír in Angmar, ${PLAYER}.'Lord Elrond believes the dwarf Glóin should be warned of the evil that might hide within Helegrod, not far to the north of his camp in the Misty Mountains.Glóin is at his camp in the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell.

Lord Elrond asked you to warn Glóin of the threat rumoured to be growing within the walls of Helegrod.'Glóin and a company of dwarves from the Lonely Mountain have established a camp to the north, among the snows of the mountains. Tell him what you have told me, and I will devise some plan by which we can prepare to face whatever evil has come to Helegrod.

'Your news fills me with forboding, ${PLAYER}, for the tale of that place is a sad one, as hostile as the mountains in winter. Durin, the fifth to bear that name, came to a grim end within the walls of that keep, despite words out of Eregion concerning the axe he bore: "Darkness shall not fall upon Hadhodrond while the line of Durin bears Mírdanant in friendship with the Gwaith-i-Mírdain."

'Perhaps the strength of those words had waned during the many years since Mírdanant was gifted? I do not know. Glóin may tell some of the tale to you, if that is his mind. Go now with haste. I do not know how much time we may have to counter this threat. Helegrod inhabited again is a troubling matter.''Glóin may not wish to share with you the tale of Durin who met his end in Helegrod, but he must be told that evil stirs again within that place. Find him at his camp north of Rivendell, among the snows of the Misty Mountains.''It was good of Master Elrond to send you to me, ${PLAYER}, though the shadow growing within Helegrod is not news to my company. Indeed, I sent two of our number northward to scout the base of the Bitter Stair that wends up to the gates. They will see what is happening in Helegrod.

'Elrond spoke to you of the fifth Durin? It is true that he came to the end of his days in Helegrod, once-great city of my people. The dragon Thorog coveted the riches that lay within and assaulted the city, slaying dwarves beyond count. Durin took up Mírdanant, the axe given to his grandsire by the Elves of Eregion, and sought to defeat Thorog in battle. Words had been spoken of the axe at the time of its making, words that were thought to ensure the safety and power of its bearer. The words were false, for Durin died in battle with Thorog at the gates of Helegrod.

'That song is a sad one, and I find I am loath to relate it now to you.'Supplies found at the East-delf and the West-delf should be destroyed in order to lessen the strength of your foes within the Wildwood.Supply crates can be found at the East-delf and the West-delf in the Wildwood.

You should destroy supply crates at the East-delf and the West-delf.Destroy supply crates at the East-delf and West-delfSupply crates can be found at the East-delf and the West-delf in the Wildwood.

You should destroy supply crates at the East-delf and the West-delf.Destroy supply crates at the East-delf and West-delf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Foes of the Free Peoples are keeping supplies at the mine entrances of the East-delf and the West-delf within the Wildwood. Destroying these supplies should lessen the strength of foes here.Foes of the Free Peoples found at East-delf and the West-delf should be defeated in order protect those within the Wildwood.Foes can be found at the East-delf and West-delf in the Wildwood.

You should defeat foes at the East-delf and West-delf.Defeat foes at the East-delf and West-delfFoes can be found at the East-delf and West-delf in the Wildwood.

You should defeat foes at the East-delf and West-delf.Defeat foes at the East-delf and West-delf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Foes of the Free Peoples have claimed the mining entrances of the East-delf and the West-delf within the Wildwood. Defeating their numbers here will assist in returning safety to the Wildwood.After fighting the wolves back to the edges of the forest, the Lossoth are confident that the beasts can be prevented from doing more damage if the den-mother is slain.The den-mother may be found on an island near the lake's western shore.

Urho has asked you to seek out the den-mother of the wolf-pack and defeat her.Defeat the den-motherSanttu is at Kauppa-kohta, on the eastern shore of the lake.

Now that you have defeated the wolves' den-mother, you should return to Santtu with news of your victory.Talk to Santtu'Now that they are on the run, we must deliver one last strike at the susi. Many of the pack are the offspring of one susi, the den-mother who leads the pack through the forest.

'If the den-mother is slain, the susi will be scattered and confused...I do not think they will trouble us again for many winters. Will you do this thing for us?

'The den-mother protects her pack on an island to the west. When you have found her, slay her, then return to my captain, Santtu.''The den-mother is defeated? You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Though the Lumi-väki do not trust Sivullinen, we give them our respect when it is earned. Your actions will not go unheralded.''Deliver the final blow to these murdering susi! Kill the den-mother, then speak with Santtu.'Information received from the letters you recovered in Black Speech led Glóin to offer rewards for the defeat of the Uruk-emissary from Angmar.Bhoghad is in the Great Goblin's throne room in Goblin-town. Goblin-town lies to the north-east of Glóin's camp.

Tralli seemed pleased with all you have done for Glóin in the past and offered you a reward for hunting down and defeating the Uruk-emissary Bhoghad in Goblin-town.Tralli Gemfinder is at Glóin's camp in the Misty Mountains, to the south-west of the entrance to Goblin-town.

You entered the Great Goblin's throne room and found Bhoghad entreating with the goblins there. You defeated the Uruk and should now return with the news to Tralli Gemfinder.Talk to Tralli Gemfinder'You have done a great service for us all, ${PLAYER}. Glóin is right...you should be rewarded for your efforts now and in the future.

'If you find the emissary, Bhoghad, within the Great Goblin's throne room, defeat him and return to me with the news, and I will be certain to reward you.

'The throne room, from tales I have heard from Glóin himself, can be found at the end of a long tunnel. Of course, I have heard that the walls within Goblin-town cannot be trusted to remain closed or open.''It is best we keep the goblins of Goblin-town under control, rather than let them join with Angmar. Defeat the emissary before he succeeds in bringing the Misty Mountain goblins under Angmar's sway.''Find the Uruk Angmar sent to rile those goblins and put an end to him, ${PLAYER}.''Glóin will be pleased to know that you have completed this task.

'I would like to thank you on behalf of the dwarves for your efforts, ${PLAYER}.'Sigrun and Greip learned that the evil that has taken Helegrod is much worse than Glóin had suspected.Elrond is in his library in Rivendell.

Sigrun has asked you to return to Elrond with news of the extent of the threat lurking now within Helegrod.Talk to Elrond at Rivendell'Lord Glóin sent us to the Bitter Stair to scout Helegrod, for he thought some evil had come back to live there, but I do not think he suspected things to be this grave. The dragon Thorog reborn? No dwarf could have imagined such a terror!

'You must return to Elrond of Rivendell and tell him of the danger that lurks now on his very doorstep. His home may be hidden from prying eyes due to some Elf-craft, but few things are safe from dragon-fire, as the grandsires of the Men of Dale could tell you!

'Go now with haste, ${PLAYER}! Greip and I will continue our vigil here, and the Elves of Rivendell will need time to prepare some plan of their own.''Elrond must be told what is happening in Helegrod, ${PLAYER}. Tell him that the situation is more grave than we thought!''You have returned, ${PLAYER}, and your news is as I expected, for I sent some scouts of my own to investigate while you were away. Armed with this knowledge, we may now plan not only our defence, but our offence as well.

'The evil that hides behind the walls of Helegrod must be swept away. You must help both Elves and dwarves accomplish this charge, ${PLAYER}.'While most folks sensibly stay home and tend to fields and shops, some hardy adventurers are drawn to the most inhospitable and difficult places in Middle-earth. Few such places pose so great a challenge as the stretch of the Misty Mountains surrounding the region of the High Pass, which is fraught with hazards -- both natural and otherwise -- to test the most rugged individuals.EXPLORE STUFFCirith Daur was once one of the major passes that travellers used to enter the High Pass. Even at the best of times, it is torn by winds and storms and is treacherous to pass through. It often becomes completely impassable during the late seasons, blocking all access between communities on the eastern and western sides of the Misty Mountains.This small cave in the rocks of the High Pass offers apparent shelter for travellers in times of storm, but it was long ago discovered to be a concealed entrance into the burrows of Goblin-town below, from which goblins would emerge in the dark of night to kidnap those foolish enough to make camp here.

These days the crack sees little use as few even attempt the crossing any more, and the goblins more frequently emerge through the larger gate down below as they make ominous preparations for war.Dómstoll -- more often called the Giant's Throne in Westron -- is a great seat of massive stones that sits above the abandoned ruins of Starkhath and offers a domineering view of the surrounding region when it is not obscured by driving snow and mist.

Most of the giants left this place long ago, but rumours say that one, at least, still remains to watch over this lonely domain.The Erforgh Cleft is a massive jumble of rocks and frozen streams left behind by some great mass of ice in ages past. Now it offers some semblance of shelter from the most brutal mountain winds to a nomadic tribe of Gauredain who have made their home here.

Whether the Gauredain came here of their own accord or were directed here by the Enemy is uncertain, but their presence is troubling nonetheless.This complex of caves called the Writhenbores seems to be formed by a great mass of boulders, larger than even the giants could hope to lift. How they came to be this way is a mystery -- perhaps by the fall of an entire peak upon the mountainside below or some equally cataclysmic event.

The caves are oddly warmer than the wind-stripped slopes outside, possibly heated by a warm spring welling up from deep below the mountain. However, any traveller hoping to take shelter within would be strongly advised to look elsewhere, for this same warmth has drawn a large and deadly brood of worms into these caves, and to carelessly wander within is certain death.A group of travellers who passed this way many years ago described a place where giants capriciously tossed boulders across the pass for sport and amusement.

The giants appear to be gone now -- some say they were driven away when a new Great Goblin took the throne of Goblin-town and relations between the two races became intolerable. In time, tired of being tormented by their diminutive foes, the giants left this place and moved towards Iorbar to the south-west.

Only the massive stone slabs that they once used as shelter remain, echoing with the howls of the Wargs who now prowl among them.Founded before the city of Helegrod, Hrimbarg was once called 'The Crown of the Misty Mountains' by the dwarves who lived there, and they marked it as the highest dwelling of their people in all the world at that time.

Alas, it fell neither to goblins nor giants nor dragons or other wickedness -- but tales say it fell to a great storm that drove down upon the High Pass and did not relent for five long years, choking the passes with vast mountains of ice, even burying Hrimbarg itself beneath a deep, featureless blanket of snow.

When at last the storm relented and their fellows from Moria came north to relieve their brothers at Hrimbarg, not one dwarf was found alive, all having frozen or starved during the long years of isolation. It was decided thereafter that Hrimbarg should not be resettled, and it has stood empty for years beyond reckoning.Newly built since the ascension of the new Great Goblin of Goblin-town, the camp of Akûltot is set among rock ledges and spires that overlook the approach to the main gates of Goblin-town. Historically, the goblins of the Misty Mountains have eschewed the construction of camps in the inhospitable drifts and glaring light of the High Pass, and it is unsettling that they should choose to do so now.

The only likely explanation is that they are preparing to extend their grasp beyond the mountains in some fashion, which is surely ill news to those who live in the hills and forests below.After you recovered the master key from the goblin-torturer, Aeglas decided it is time to depart from Goblin-town.Aeglas must be protected as he attempts to lead Glorwen and Oghûk to safety. It falls to you to defend him along the way.Speak with AeglasGlóin is just outside the entrance to Goblin-town.

With your aid, Aeglas and Glorwen escaped to safety. Oghûk proved as treacherous as any goblin. You should report your victories to Glóin.Talk to Glóin at his camp outside of Goblin-town'My plan has not worked. The goblins were prepared, though I do not know how. It matters not though. Now that we have a key the time has come for us to leave this place, ${PLAYER}. We shall need to be cautious. Glorwen must be taken from here, and we will test the truth in Oghûk's words.

'Tell me when you are prepared, and we shall begin our escape.''Guard me, while I free the others. Stay close.''Aeglas has been freed and has returned to the field, you say? You have done well, ${PLAYER}.'Handarod told you of the trials of the dwarves at Glóin's camp in the Misty Mountains and of the plans to finally assault the ancient dwarf-hold of GabilazanHandarod has asked you to gather some allies and seek out the Dwarf Gimli. Gimli will accompany you to the dwarf-keep where the Nazgûl and Skorgrím may be hiding. Gimli is staying in one of the guest rooms along the road that winds up the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris.Speak to GimliGlóin is at his camp in the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell.

The Nazgûl left the dwarf-keep, commanding Skorgrím to slay you. Fortunately, you were able to defeat Skorgrím, but a fell spirit emerged from his corpse and cursed the Longbeards before vanishing. You should tell Glóin all that has transpired.Talk to Glóin'I have a dangerous task for you and your companions. The Dwarf Glóin has come into possession of a special key which will allow access to a passage that leads into the fortress of Skorgrím Dourhand.

'Glóin has bidden me send him a group of warriors who -- led by his son Gimli, who knows the secret ways of that place -- will put an end to Skorgrím's treachery once and for all.

'Seek out Gimli in one of the guest rooms on the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris when you have gathered your companions and are prepared to embark.''Greetings, ${PLAYER}. A glorious battle awaits us!

'Are you and your allies ready? My father has given me the Key-stone, so I am prepared. Let us go now into the Mountains to defeat Skorgrím and his Dourhands!''Speak to Gimli when your allies are ready, and he will lead you to the dwarf-keep.''That was a good fight, ${PLAYER}! Such exercise does not come along every day!''You bring tidings both joyous and dark, ${PLAYER}. The Dourhands are done! They will never hope to threaten the Longbeards again.

'While the news of the spirit that was driven from Skorgrím is unsettling, it is not as disturbing as the news of the Nazgûl's escape. What is worse, you tell me that he spoke of bringing Men to Helegrod. What he seeks in that old dwarf-hall is a mystery to me.

'Unfortunately, there is more that must be done if Rivendell is to be secured. Know, though, that I will give you whatever help I can.'Complete many quests for the League of the Axe.Complete many quests for the League of the Axe.Complete many quests for the League of the AxeThe League of the Axe is in need of assistance with efforts in the Wildwood of Bree-land.Complete factionless quests in the Wildwood to assist the League of the Axe.Complete quests in the Wildwood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Assisted the League of the Axe.Completed'The success of the League of the Axe is determined by each of its members, and we can ill-afford to be unprepared when the Wildwood is our only hope for a better life.

'Aid the League of the Axe in our hardships, and I shall see that your efforts are rewarded.'You have assisted the League of the Axe in their efforts throughout the Wildwood of Bree-land. All those in the League are thankful for your aid.There is much to do in assisting those in the Wildwood.There is much to do in assisting those in the Wildwood.Complete: Ally to the League of the AxeComplete: Kindred to the Woodcutter's BrotherhoodDescendants of Beorn have not traditionally left the skin-changer's home-land, but your journey has brought you to Eriador in defence of the Free Peoples. You should now go to meet your brother Sterkist, at the Spire of Meeting in Rivendell.Your journey continues in Eriador.Reach Level 45 as a BeorningSoltakh has arranged for the transfer of Gillë Andras, the Lord of the Western Marches, to Dûn Covád, where he can be faced on more even terms.Gillë Andras, the Lord of the Western Marches, can be found within the city of Dûn Covád, in the western foothills north of Fail-á-Khro.

Soltakh has asked you and your allies to defeat Gillë Andras, the Lord of the Western Marches.Soltakh is at Fail-á-Khro, north of Aughaire and south of Dûn Covád.

You have defeated Gillë Andras, the Lord of the Western Marches, and should now bring news of your triumph to Soltakh.'If the orders you have planted do their work, the leader of the armies that now threaten Fasach-falroid may be already doomed, ${PLAYER}, and not even know it! His name is Gillë Andras, and he is the Lord of the Western Marches.

'Even now, he is likely receiving his new orders: to travel to Dûn Covád with a small retinue to monitor the Orcs in that city under his command. He will be leaving the sturdy defences of his command in Donnvail and coming to the lesser defences of Dûn Covád. With your allies, you can make your way into Dûn Covád, north of here in the western hills, and defeat Gillë Andras apart from his lieutenants. As this plan ripens, Soltakh proves his worth! May Drostan be forgotten!

'Defeat the Lord of the Western Marches, ${PLAYER}. This blow will be a great strike for the Trév Gállorg, if you and your allies can see it done.''Our plan is fulfilled, ${PLAYER}, and you have brought great joy to Soltakh, "He Who Is Changed!"

'Already the memory of Drostan falls from me. We have done much good this day, friend ${RACE}, and I thank you for it.''Gillë Andras has likely been sent to Dûn Covád by now; if you strike quickly, you and your allies can face him without his defences!

'Dûn Covád is in the western foothills, north of Fail-á-Khro.'Helegdir has asked for your help in ensuring the safety of a group of individuals known as the Lost Fellowship.Forochel lies north of Evendim, through Cirith Rhiw, north of Tyrn Fornech. You should start your search in the town of Kauppa-kohta.

Helegdir asked you to seek out a member of a fellowship of adventurers who journeyed to Forochel, passing through Aughaire in Angmar.Talk to Cenlieg'We have had many strange travellers in these lands, though none as strange as the fellowship that recently passed through Aughaire, seeking for the land of Forochel. That land lies to the north and west of this land, though I have never seen the mountains of snow, nor frozen shores of the sea.

'They had an old map that claimed ancient dwarf-mines filled with treasure lay somewhere within the land of Forochel. If you were to travel to those lands, I would ask for you to seek out one of their company and lend them aid if you are able. They did not seem a very capable company, and it would ease my heart to know that a ${CLASS} such as yourself would look out for them.

'Forochel lies north of Evendim, through Cirith Rhiw, north of Tyrn Fornech. You should start your search in the village of Kauppa-kohta.''You were sent by Helegdir to ensure we were safe? Yes, yes, that is all well and good, but it is not my fault, you see. Those other fools got themselves lost. If I had my raven, things would be much different.''Have you found the lost fellowship yet? You should start your search in Kauppa-kohta. I heard them discussing that village as their first destination.'The Woodcutter's Brotherhood has agreed to help Trestlebridge bring a farmers' market to the centre of town.The market stalls of potential vendors have been set up in Trestlebridge.

You should inspect the produce of the farmers.The market stalls of potential vendors have been set up in Trestlebridge.

You should inspect the produce of the farmers.Inspect the final market stallThe market stalls of potential vendors have been set up in Trestlebridge.

You should talk to the farmer closest to the stall with the rancid fruit.Talk to the helpful vendorThe owner of the poisonous fruit ran out of town and towards the Wildwood.

You should follow in pursuit and try to catch up with this man.You should follow in pursuit of the fleeing vendorFind and follow the man's trailThe vendor can be found outside of Cotfast in the Wildwood.

You should confront the vendor.Confront the troublesome brigandAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge.

You should talk to Aran Greenwith.Talk to Aran GreenwithReconstruction work continues on Trestlebridge.

You should survey the reconstruction of Trestlebridge.Survey the reconstruction of TrestlebridgeAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge.

You should talk to Aran Greenwith.Talk to Aran Greenwith'I have some good news, ${PLAYER}. After a lot of hard work from the Woodcutter's Brotherhood and its members, Trestlebridge will soon have a monthly market day where farmers and traders will come to town, bringing their goods in tow.

'To keep the town safe, the Woodcutter's Brotherhood has been vetting each vendor. Today we are talking to some of the nearby farmers from the Bree-fields. Would you like to talk to the vendor for us?''Yes, there was a man standing behind the market stall there. He saw you inspecting the farmers' goods and started to get nervous. I only know this because I saw him pacing. Then he walked away until he was almost out of sight, whereupon he just started running. I think he was heading in the direction of the Bree-fields. I hope that helps. Glad you like my marmalades though!''Ha, have you come to Cotfast alone?! I'm telling you nothing, ${CLASS}! Gothtal has my back!''Now we have a name, Gothtal. We also know this Orc frequents the outpost of Cotfast in the Wildwood. An attempt to infiltrate our market in town is a brazen effort for this Gothtal. Has he become desperate? What is his plan? I hope to find out soon, ${PLAYER}.

'Why not take some time to admire the reconstruction efforts in Trestlebridge and I will think on our next course of action.''I have given some thought to our problems with Gothtal. For now, let us continue our efforts in the reconstruction of Trestlebridge and we will deal with this Gothtal when the time is right. There is still much to be done here in both Trestlebridge and the Wildwood.'Golhador has cautioned you about the great mammoths of the Misty Mountains, some of which seem to have become allies of the giants.Mammoths can be found throughout the Misty Mountains, but especially in areas where giants walk.

Golhador has expressed concern that the mammoths and the giants have formed an alliance and asked you to bring the silver tusk-rings worn by the mammoths for him to examine.Golhador is at the High Crag camp.

Golhador is waiting for you to return with tusk-rings that might illuminate the nature of the alliance between the mammoths and the giants of the Misty Mountains.'If you are climbing into the mountains, friend, take care to avoid the great mammoths. They are dangerous on all days, but of late the few travellers in this place have mentioned some unusual ornamentation on the mighty beasts -- great silver rings affixed to their dangerous tusks.

'There is only one race that could affix such rings and still live, and it is that of the giants. This alliance is one of ill omen, if alliance it be, and I am concerned not only for the House of Elrond but also for our dwarf friends, who have established a camp not far to the north.

'If by some fortune you are able to defeat some of the mammoths, bring me their tusk-rings for further study. We must learn how deep this alliance of great beasts and giants may go.''Mammoths never walk in great numbers, but they can be found near to the giants in many cases. If you can retrieve some of their tusk-rings, we may learn how strong this alliance may be.''You have done very well to bring me these tusk-rings, ${PLAYER}. They are most fearsome! It was a terrible giant indeed who affixed these rings, my friend. Let us hope he never approaches this place, or the camp of the dwarves to the west!'There is something amiss within the League of the Axe and tensions rise when a tomb of Arnor is discovered in the Wildwood.Chests with the personal belongings of Addy Rushtuft and Nye Crowfoot can be found at Trader's Wharf.

You should search the chests belonging to Addy Rushtuft and Nye Crowfoot.Search Addy's chest of personal belongingsSearch Nye's chest of personal belongingsEnid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf.

You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.Talk to Enid NettlestingEnid Nettlesting wishes to go to Writhenset to get to the bottom of things.

You should talk to Enid Nettlesting in Writhenset.Talk to Enid Nettlesting in WrithensetThe entrance to Haudh Eglan can be found in Writhenset.

You should enter Haudh Eglan.Enter the tombThe tomb-robbers can be found in Haudh Eglan.

You should defeat the tomb-robbers and recover what they have already pilfered.Defeat tomb-robbers and recover stolen relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Addy RushtuftDefeat Nye CrowfootThe ceremonial coffer can be found in Haudh Eglan.

You should return the relics to their proper place in the tomb.Enid Nettlesting can be found in Writhenset.

You should talk to Enid Nettlesting in Writhenset.Talk to Enid Nettlesting in WrithensetEnid Nettlesting wishes to return to Trader's Wharf.

You should talk to Enid Nettlesting at Trader's Wharf.Talk to Enid Nettlesting at Trader's Wharf'${PLAYER}. Nye and Addy have gone missing! A member of the League noticed the two speaking together in hushed tones and only moments later they fled Trader's Wharf without a word. I am not sure what they are up to but I'm revoking their membership to the League of the Axe, that much is certain!

'It looks like Nye and Addy were in a hurry. They didn't even take their personal belongings with them! Perhaps there might be some clues to their whereabouts among their possessions.''What's this?! They left their League sashes behind and you believe that they went to the hidden tomb in the mines of Writhenset?! Those deviants! Let us head to the mines and quickly. Perhaps we can stop them before they do something foolish and get themselves killed. The mines are not yet safe!''I fear Nye and Addy might be tomb-robbers, ${PLAYER}. Why else would they go against the League's wishes and enter this tomb? Tread with caution, my friend.''To think Nye and Addy used the League of the Axe as a means of finding and attempting to rob a tomb. I will never forgive them. We should return to Trader's Wharf.''I thank you, ${PLAYER}, for all you have done for the League of the Axe. To think that we were harbouring tomb-robbers in our midst! If Nye and Addy had succeeded, the League would continue to attract more unscrupulous individuals. Soon we would be nothing more than an unsavory group of brigands! No, we are more than that and always will be! The League of the Axe is about hard work, honesty, honour, and a love of the land. Thanks to you, the League will thrive here in the Wildwood.'Bilbo Baggins has completed his book and would like to make certain that his memory of the important locations and events is correct.Gollum's cave is deep within the tunnels of Goblin-town, beyond the central hall.

Bilbo Baggins provided you with some writing materials and sent you off to find Gollum's cave, with instruction to verify the details of his book regarding the cave.Bilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House at Rivendell, south of Goblin-town.

You found Gollum's cave in the depths of Goblin-town and discovered the creature's makeshift hut on an island in the lake. Once there, you wrote down what you saw. Now you should return to Bilbo Baggins.'Gollum and his cave are very important to my book, and so I simply must be sure of the details. I don't suppose you could find the old villain, could you? No, that would be quite out of the question, I'm sure.

'Anyway, I'm not sure how I managed to fall into one of the deepest caverns in Goblin-town, but if you could find it and make sure my recollections have not failed me, I would greatly appreciate it. There was a big lake in that cavern, that much I remember clearly.

'I know Gandalf and Frodo don't approve, but it would bring some joy to this old hobbit if you could manage this for me.''Gollum's cave lay somewhere deep in the belly of the Mountains. I only know that it was deeper than the main hall where we came upon the Great Goblin and where Gandalf saved us all from a terrible fate.

'I would be greatly pleased if you could find it again and verify the details in my book.''Well, this just goes to show you can only trust your memories so far. I had forgotten all about Gollum's hut... I never saw it up close, thank goodness, so I had no reason to be concerned with it.

'It looks like I will have some revisions to make to my book. Thank you very much!'The League of the Axe wishes to hunt the forests and mine the hills of the Wildwood of Bree-land, once the woods have been properly scouted.Blomley Sward, Helva's Edge, Hunter's Ledge, the East-delf, and the West-delf can all be found in the Wildwood.

You should collect ore samples and animal pelts from moose, wolves, bears, and boars, for the League of the Axe as you survey the Wildwood.Scout Blomley SwardScout Helva's EdgeScout Hunter's LedgeScout the East-delfScout the West-delfCollect ore samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect pelts from beasts in the Wildwood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf.

You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.Broken traps and dull pickaxes can be found at Trader's Wharf.

You should repair these items for the League of the Axe.Repair broken bear traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Repair broken fish traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sharpen dull pickaxes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf.

You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.Talk to Enid Nettlesting'While I find your words compelling, it is not for me to decide whether or not you join the League of the Axe. No, it is for your own skills and actions to decide. I will give you a test to prove yourself worthy of joining the League.

'Knowing the land is an important skill for our cause. I ask of you to scout the hunting grounds and mine entrances in the Wildwood. There is more, however. Extracting resources from these lands in a way that does not hurt the Wildwood is just as important to our prosperity and survival. I ask of you to return with both pelts and samples of ore that you deem worthy of trade.''I see that you have accomplished all that I have asked, and with good judgement and knowledge. Do you think you can join the League of the Axe now? No, for you still need to be tested on your skill and your work ethic. The League works as a family. We all take turns repairing our traps, as without them, there would be no League.

'I ask of you to repair the broken bear traps, fish traps, and sharpen pickaxes scattered around Trader's Wharf. If you accomplish all these tasks well, you will be a member of the League of the Axe. If you fail to repair any, you will only be welcome here to trade with us.''I am impressed by your skills and all which you have accomplished for us on this day. Welcome to the League of the Axe, ${PLAYER}. May you earn our trust in time and may we all prosper in the Wildwood.'Linnet Redholm sets a challenge to hunt the Wildwood's fiercest and rarest game.The great beasts can be found across the Wildwood. 

Linnet has asked you to defeat the White Stag Gwengorn, the Great Boar Brundurch, the Black Elk Dúgar, and the Silver Warg Lhudblath.Linnet can be found in the central Wildwood.

You should return to Linnet.Return to Linnet'Our friends here tell of mighty beasts that roam the Wildwood, some attacking all in their path with wanton abandon. I have tracked a few of them and feel confident their behaviour is not natural. Whatever sickness has driven these animals to such violence must not be spread to the rest of the forest.

'I came here seeking glory, but I am wise enough to know when I am outmatched. If you take down the sickened creatures, I will ensure the bards know your name.''Amazing work, friend. I might even admit that you are a better hunter than myself. ...One day.'The Wildwood is a lightly travelled wilderness, far beyond the Bree-fields, teeming with untapped resources.Aran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge and Enid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf.

You should talk to Aran Greenwith and Enid Nettlesting.Talk to Aran GreenwithTalk to Enid Nettlesting'Hail traveller, I am Aran Greenwith, leader of the Woodcutter's Brotherhood. What brings you to us, here in Trestlebridge? Have you come to assist our efforts in the Wildwood? I should say that we do not stake all the claim to this forest. So too does the League of the Axe, who reside upon the shores of the Brandywine.''I am Enid Nettlesting, leader of the League of the Axe, and who might you be? Have you come to Trader's Wharf to trade or do you think you have what it takes to be a member of the League? We have claimed much of the Wildwood, yet so has the Woodcutter's Brotherhood, who dwell at Trestlebridge.''The Woodcutter's Brotherhood is always on the look-out for new members to join our cause. What is it that we wish to accomplish? Why, the rebuilding of Trestlebridge! Yes, this village is quite important to us and it has seen much hardship and sorrow. We wish now to revitalize Trestlebridge and restore it to a thriving place of commerce and return it to a joyful community.

'What say you? Will you join the Woodcutter's Brotherhood and join our cause?''Do you think you are up for the task of becoming a member of the League of the Axe? I am not so sure. Tell me about the hardships you have faced in your life. Tell me about the difficulties you have had to deal with to make ends meet, be it no food at the table, or no bed for the night.

'We at the League have endured much. This is why we band together, to make a name for ourselves at our home, at Trader's Wharf.'Complete many quests for the Woodcutter's Brotherhood.Complete many quests for the Woodcutter's Brotherhood.Complete many quests for the Woodcutter's BrotherhoodThe Woodcutter's Brotherhood is in need of assistance with efforts in the Wildwood of Bree-land.Complete factionless quests in the Wildwood to assist the Woodcutter's Brotherhood.Complete quests in the Wildwood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Assisted the Woodcutter's Brotherhood.Completed'The success of the Woodcutter's Brotherhood is determined by each of its members, and we can ill-afford to be unprepared when the village of Trestlebridge depends upon us.'

'Aid the Woodcutter's Brotherhood in our tasks, and I shall see that your efforts are rewarded.'You have assisted the Woodcutter's Brotherhood in their efforts throughout the Wildwood of Bree-land. All those in the Brotherhood are thankful for your aid.Sigrun told you of Ormulf Worm-hunter, a dwarf at Othrikar renowned for his brave deeds against the worms and drakes that stalk the crevices of the North Downs.Ormulf Worm-hunter is at Othrikar, far to the west in the north-central North Downs.

Sigrun has seen from afar that the keep of Helegrod appears to be crawling with worms and drakes and has asked you to consult with Ormulf Worm-hunter about what must be done.'The keep of Helegrod has stood empty for years beyond count, ${PLAYER}, but now it has become home to worm and drake, a vile warren filled with many clutches of eggs and guarded by the watchful eyes of the great beasts.

'Few of the Corcur or Angmarim that we have spied from afar seem willing to brave the stronghold. Perhaps the fire-breath of the creatures keeps the Men at bay, or they are under some command not to disturb the beasts. One of the Angmarim, a man of great importance, seems to have no fear of the worms or drakes and passes often through the doors of the keep. It is curious.

'But we do not have the time to muse on such things! Ormulf Worm-hunter, a dwarf of Othrikar on the North Downs, should be told of the infestation of worms and drakes that lurk now within the keep of Helegrod. He will know how best to fight the creatures. Go with haste, and leave the mystery of the Angmarim worm-friend to Greip and myself!''Ormulf Worm-hunter is at Othrikar on the North Downs, ${PLAYER}. He will know what to do about the worms and drakes that slither now within Helegrod's inner keep!''Worms within Helegrod? Sigrun was right to send you to me, ${PLAYER}, for no one knows as much about fighting the fell creatures as I do!

'And I am worried about this Man of Angmar you mentioned. If he can pass safely among drakes and worms, he may hold a power far greater than anything I have yet faced. But the situation here on the Downs needs all my attention, and I cannot travel all the way to Helegrod! How I wish it were not so, but I gave my word that I would not abandon my post here, and a dwarf's word is stronger even than mithril bonds!

'I hope no ill comes of it, but there is nothing I can do. I will put it out of my mind. If you are willing to combat the threat of worms and drakes within Helegrod on my behalf, give me your word you will do so, and will not cower before such mysterious power as this Man seems to wield. If you are not prepared for such danger, I will waste no more of my breath upon you!'The dwarves at Gabilshathûr await a delivery of clean tails to be made to Avar.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver clean tails from the worms surrounding Gabilshathûr to Avar at the dwarf-outpost.Wanted: Clean tails from the worms surrounding Gabilshathûr. Delivery of the items should be made to Avar at the dwarf-outpost.Wanted: Clean tails from the worms surrounding Gabilshathûr.'Good to know that these things will not bother us any longer.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Forti, overseer of the dwarves of Forochel, awaits the delivery of clean tails at the dwarf-home of Zigilgund.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver clean tails from the worms surrounding Zigilgund in Forochel. The items are to be delivered to the dwarf-overseer Fotri encamped at the dwarf-home.Wanted: Clean tails from the worms surrounding the dwarf-home of Zigilgund. Deliver the items to Forti, overseer of the settlement.'It will take a while to cure these, so we had better get to the process. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Fotri, overseer of the dwarves of Forochel, awaits the delivery of gilded sword sheaths at the dwarf-home of Zigilgund.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver gilded sword sheaths from the Dourhands and Gauredain surrounding Zigilgund in Forochel. The items are to be delivered to the dwarf-overseer Fotri encamped at the dwarf-home.Wanted: Gilded sword sheaths from the Dourhands and Gauredain surrounding the dwarf-home of Zigilgund. Deliver the items to Fotri, overseer of the settlement.'Good to see that their number will dwindle. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Afwald, the provisioner at the dwarf-ruin of Hrimbarg, awaits the return of great ears.You have accepted a task to deliver great ears from the beasts found in the eastern reaches of the Misty Mountains to Afwald. Afwald can be found within the ruins at Hrimbarg, also found in the Misty Mountains.Wanted: Great ears from the beasts in the eastern reaches of the Misty Mountains. You can deliver these items to Afwald within the ruins at Hrimbarg in the Misty Mountains.Wanted: Great ears from the beasts in the eastern reaches of the Misty Mountains.'Supplies are supplies at the moment, thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The dwarves at Gabilshathûr await a delivery of great filth to be made to Avar.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver great filth from the insects surrounding Gabilshathûr and return it to Avar at the dwarf-outpost.Wanted: Great filth from the insects surrounding Gabilshathûr. Delivery of the items should be made to Avar at the dwarf-outpost.Wanted: Great filth from the insects surrounding Gabilshathûr.'This is disgusting, but it burns well, long and hot.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Afwald, the provisioner at the dwarf-ruin of Hrimbarg, awaits the return of great scales.You have accepted a task to deliver great scales from the worms found in the eastern reaches of the Misty Mountains to Afwald. Afwald can be found within the ruins at Hrimbarg, also found in the Misty Mountains.Wanted: Great scales from the worms in the eastern reaches of the Misty Mountains. You can deliver these items to Afwald within the ruins at Hrimbarg in the Misty Mountains.Wanted: Great scales from the worms in the eastern reaches of the Misty Mountains.'I am glad to see that you are making your way through these terrible creatures. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Fotri, overseer of the dwarves of Forochel, awaits the delivery of pure black skin at the dwarf-home of Zigilgund.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver pure black skin from the worms and beasts in the areas surrounding Zigilgund in Forochel. The items are to be delivered to the dwarf-overseer Fotri encamped at the dwarf-home.Wanted: Pure black skin from the beasts and worms surrounding the dwarf-home of Zigilgund. Deliver the items to Fotri, overseer of the settlement.'We will use this wisely. Thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The dwarves at Gabilshathûr await a delivery of razor sharp claws to be made to Avar.You have accepted a task to collect and deliver razor sharp claws from the worms surrounding Gabilshathûr and bring them to the dwarf Avar at the dwarf-outpost.Wanted: Razor sharp claws from the worms surrounding Gabilshathûr. Delivery of the items should be made to Avar at the dwarf-outpost.Wanted: Razor sharp claws from the worms surrounding Gabilshathûr.'These will work nicely, thank you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Thunder-lord, leader of the giants, has ordered his people to battle. If he can be defeated, this threat might fall with him.The Thunder-lord rules the giants from Iorbar, south and east of the Giants' Table in the Misty Mountains.

The Thunder-lord is the source of the giants' recent hostility, and he must be defeated before all the giants in the region heed his commands. You will need the aid of brave allies if you hope to defeat him.Stand upon the Giants' TableThe Thunder-lord rules the giants from Iorbar, south and east of the Giants' Table in the Misty Mountains.

The Thunder-lord is the source of the giants' recent hostility, and he must be defeated before all the giants in the region heed his commands. You will need the aid of brave allies if you hope to defeat him.Defeat the Thunder-lordGolhador is at the High Crag camp in the Misty Mountains, north-east of Rivendell.

You should return to Golhador and let him know that the Thunder-lord has been defeated.Talk to Golhador at the High Crag campThe giants at the Giants' Table mentioned the Thunder-lord, whom you can only assume is their leader. Perhaps if the Thunder-lord were defeated, the giants might turn from their wicked path.

It is likely that the Thunder-lord rules from the furthest reaches of Iorbar, south and east of the Giants' Table. You should be wary, for he must be a deadly opponent, and only a determined party of warriors could hope to defeat him.'You have defeated a mighty foe, ${PLAYER}, and have proven yourself worthy beyond any need, but I remain troubled. The Thunder-lord has planted an unease in my heart.

'Dark days are ahead, for all of Middle-earth. Remain wary, ${PLAYER}! I fear a terrible shadow has been cast upon the land from afar.'Golhador has identified the giants who have mastery over the mammoths of the Misty Mountains and has asked that you put an end to this dangerous alliance.The Giant's Needle is in the heart of the Giant Halls of the Misty Mountains, south-east of the dwarf-stronghold of Gabilazan.

Madfurr is east of the Giant's Needle, in a cleft of the rock. Sukdyr is north-east of the Giant's Needle, among the stony paths. Kulgurz is on the high slopes above the Giant's Needle.

Golhador the Elf has told you the locations of the powerful giant-champions responsible for taming the ferocious mammoths.Golhador is in the High Crag camp in the central Misty Mountains.

Golhador will be pleased to hear that you have defeated the mighty champions responsible for taming the ferocious mammoths.'It has taken exceptionally powerful giants to bend the will of the mammoths of the Misty Mountains. If these champions are defeated, we will not need to fear the alliance of giant and mammoth until more champions arise. Gather what allies you may, for these champions are truly mighty, even among the already-fearsome giants.

'The mammoths bear the signs of three giants. These champions have never treated with me, but I know their reputations. Madfurr is a master of unarmed warfare and lives in the cleft east of the Giant's Needle. Few dare pass near the stones he has set aside for his protection from the elements. Other giants are awe-struck by Sukdyr's skill with his great club -- look for him somewhere within the paths north-east of the Giant's Needle, among the rocky chasms.

'Kulgurz is the last, and of him I know less than the others. Beware his skill from afar! It is said that he can strike a mighty aurochs dead with a single toss from a distance of two miles. Kulgurz strides along the slopes high above the Giant's Needle, looking for trouble. May fortune smile upon you, ${PLAYER}. You will have need of it.

'Oh, the Giant's Needle itself? It is a natural black rock spire in a small bowl-like valley. You will find it in the heart of the Giant Halls of the Misty Mountains, some distance south-east of an old dwarf-stronghold called Gabilazan.''You have filled me with amazement, ${PLAYER}, and I marvel at your ability to best the giants' mighty champions!

'I have no doubt they will raise new champions against us, but you have purchased us some time, brave ${RACE}, and for that we of Imladris are grateful.'The League of the Axe uses traps to catch beasts for food and furs in the wilds of the Wildwood.Good trap locations can be found in the Wildwood.

You should place the traps you have been given in the Wildwood.Grun Curldock can be found at Trader's Wharf.

You should talk to Grun Curldock.Talk to Grun Curldock'The livelihood of the League depends upon trapping. It is important to keep the living things in the forest thriving, however. For that, we maintain a set number of traps in the Wildwood, no more.

'I can see that we have many traps here at Trader's Wharf that could be set in the Wildwood. Would you set them for us? The League will be grateful.''You have done as I asked? Very good. I thank you for assisting the League of the Axe, ${CLASS}.'The League of the Axe has spotted a group of ruffians camped upon the shores of the Wildwood and fear for the safety of Trader's Wharf.The ruffians' camp-site can be found north of Trader's Wharf.

You should find the ruffians' camp-site on the shores of the Wildwood.Find the ruffians' camp-siteThe ruffians' camp-site can be found north of Trader's Wharf.

