Baillindiel is waiting for you to return with the last set of components.'For a minstrel of such heart as you, ${PLAYER}, I will gladly fashion some truly remarkable equipment. The components I will need for its making will not be easily obtained, but I know that you will succeed.

'I will need you to bring me the items I will need. The first items I will need are furs from the snowbeasts of the Misty Mountains and brimstone-tinged armour-plates from the Tarkrîp goblins in Angmar.

'I will see you again, ${PLAYER}, and we will sing of your deeds when you return in triumph!''Snowbeasts are common on the slopes of the Misty Mountains. The goblins you seek serve the Tarkrîp Orcs of Mallenhad in Angmar.''I am glad to see your safe return, ${PLAYER}, and will make use of these components in the fashioning of your equipment.

'I hope that you have as much fortune obtaining the next set of components I need. The second set of materials I need are the eyes of worms, such as are found in Angmar, and the remains of wights found in Imlad Balchorth in Angmar.''Look for the worms in Gorothlad in Angmar and the wights in Imlad Balchorth.''My heart is joyful to see you return from the darkness, ${PLAYER}! One set of components remains, and I fear this will be your greatest challenge. But despair not! You will wear the equipment I make for you with greater satisfaction in memory of the triumph it will represent!

'I need you to bring me a horn from the Gorthorog Tarlûg, who resides in Carn Dûm. I also need a badge of rank from the goblins of Urugarth.''Seek the Gorthorog Tarlûg at Carn Dûm. Goblins guard the tower of Urugarth, also in Angmar.''You have returned from out of the darkness, ${PLAYER}, and my heart leaps to see you victorious! I will make use of these last components in the fashioning of your equipment.

'I give this to you with the deepest respect for your worthiness as a minstrel, ${PLAYER}. Use it well, and bring hope to the Free Peoples! These dark days will pass, and word of your deeds will be a pleasant memory by the hearth when peace comes again. It is with great joy that I call you friend.'Aelindil at Tornhad has agreed to help you fashion a piece of jewellery worthy of your reputation as a Mariner.Aelindil has asked you to bring him a number of hooked avanc-teeth and Torcadáll's spy-glass.

Torcadáll Wild-eye may be found in Thelgarth in the Angle of Mitheithel. Avanc can be found throughout the Angle of Mitheithel.Collect Torcadáll's spy-glassCollect hooked avanc-teeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.Spiders can found in Angmar and other dangerous places. Drakes and other dragon-kind can be found in Angmar and Moria.

Aelindil has asked you to bring him coiled spider spinnerets and unyielding drake scales.Collect coiled spider spinnerets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect unyielding drake scales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.Urro can be found at Carn Dûm in Angmar. Morthrâng can be found at Urugarth in Angmar.

Aelindil has asked you to bring him a medallion of passage and an emblem of ritual.Collect a medallion of passageCollect an emblem of ritualAelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.'A Mariner must always strive for balance! This is true upon the rivers and Seas of Middle-earth, and it is also true in the manner of one's appearance. Simple garb is oft of great use when undertaking duties upon a ship, but for a Mariner, the wearing of fine jewellery is a long-held tradition.

'Indeed, I can fashion you a suitable piece of jewellery that you might share in this proud tradition, but first, you must find the materials I seek.

'For your first task in this trial, I require two things, but one has need of further explanation. I have heard word that a Man of Angmar named Torcadáll Wild-eye has taken up with the brigands and half-orcs at Thelgarth. I do not know why he has come to the Angle of Mitheithel, but I fear it bodes ill, for it has been long since the realm of Angmar last troubled this land. He carries in his possession a curious object called a spy-glass, and it is said that it grants its wielder the sight of the Elves. I do not know if he means to sway new allies into the service of the Iron Crown or searches for some relic lost long ago in the war between Angmar and Arnor, but it matters not. I need not explain that Torcadáll is unwelcome in the Angle of Mitheithel, and his spy-glass could prove a great boon to the Dúnedain, so I ask that you retrieve it, my friend. In addition, I require a number of hooked avanc-teeth. That will be a simpler errand, surely, for they can be found throughout the Angle of Mitheithel.

'After you have finished this task, I must ask you to venture further afield, for the materials I shall need next cannot be found in the Angle of Mitheithel.''For your first task, I require two things, but one has need of further explanation. I have heard word that a Man of Angmar named Torcadáll Wild-eye has taken up with the brigands and half-orcs at Thelgarth. I do not know why he has come to the Angle of Mitheithel, but I fear it bodes ill, for it has been long since the realm of Angmar last troubled this land. He carries in his possession a curious object called a spy-glass, and it is said that it grants its wielder the sight of the Elves. I do not know if he means to sway new allies into the service of the Iron Crown or searches for some relic lost long ago in the war between Angmar and Arnor, but it matters not. I need not explain that Torcadáll is unwelcome in the Angle of Mitheithel, and his spy-glass could prove a great boon to the Dúnedain, so I ask that you retrieve it, my friend. In addition, I require a number of hooked avanc-teeth. That will be a simpler errand, surely, for they can be found throughout the Angle of Mitheithel.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}! I am glad to know that Torcadáll Wild-eye will no longer trouble the Dúnedain here in the Angle, and it pleases me that you were able to recover his spy-glass. What a curious tool! And do not worry, those avanc-teeth will still have a use in my design!

'For the next set of materials, I will need coiled spider spinnerets from spiders such as those found in Angmar and in other dangerous lands. I also require a number of unyielding drake scales from the dragon-kind of Angmar or the lost realm of Moria.''For the next set of materials, I will need coiled spider spinnerets from spiders such as those found in Angmar and in other dangerous lands. I also require a number of unyielding drake scales from the dragon-kind of Angmar or the lost realm of Moria.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Each of these materials will serve to adorn the jewellery I craft for you, but there are still two items I require and each of them will do much to prove your worthiness as a Mariner.

'For the final set of materials, you must collect an emblem of ritual from the Uruk, Morthrâng, who resides in the Orc-fortress of Urugarth, but that is not all, my friend. You must also bring me a medallion of passage from the Uruk, Urro, who dwells within the walls of Carn Dûm.

'Only then shall I count your task as finished!''For the final set of materials, you must collect an emblem of ritual from the Uruk, Morthrâng, who resides in the Orc-fortress of Urugarth, but that is not all, my friend. You must also bring me a medallion of passage from the Uruk, Urro, who dwells within the walls of Carn Dûm. Only then shall I count your task as finished!''I am most impressed, ${PLAYER}!

'You have performed admirably in the tasks I set before you, and no doubt can remain that you have proven your worthiness of this reward—both as a Mariner and as a protector of the Free Peoples of Middle-earth. Let this fine piece of jewellery serve as a reminder of your skill and ingenuity as a Mariner!'Isdi has agreed to fashion you a piece of equipment to reflect the depth of your knowledge.Grimgore roams Fasach-larran in Angmar. Corcur may be found near Helegrod in the Misty Mountains.

