Yrjänä informed you that another has come claiming Narchuil and seeking the aid of the Lossoth in finding it.Go with Yrjänä to meet your rivalYrjänä is in the Great Lodge of Sûri-kylä.

You should speak with Yrjänä regarding Mordrambor's threats.Talk to Yrjänä'You have gained the favour of the Lumi-väki, but you are not the only one to come seeking our help to find this ring. Why is it so important? No, do not speak of it... I fear it will only bring a black wind upon us.

'First came the Vanha-väki, Laerdan, and then came you, but another awaits an audience with me. He makes powerful claims... will you go with me to treat with him? You should know the claim he lays upon the ring.

'However, we will wait until you are prepared. When you are ready, speak with me again.''Are you ready to meet your opposition?''And so you have it ${RACE}. The servants of the Iron Crown stand against you. An end must be put to the evils of Angmar, but my people will not help you as long as this shadow looms over us.

'There is one, however, who may help you....'The Black Númenórean Mordrambor arrived at the Lossoth village demanding the loyalty of the Lossoth people, striking fear into their hearts.Saija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri.

Yrjänä instructed you to seek the wisdom of Saija in order to find Narchuil.Talk to SaijaThe body of the sea-monster Saija spoke of lies in the Ice-bay of Forochel, east of Kuru-leiri.

Saija directed you to seek Narchuil or news of it upon the body of a sea-monster which can be seen in the Ice-bay of Forochel.Seek the body of the sea-monster in the Ice-bay of ForochelArvedui haunts the wreckage of a great Elf-ship frozen in the Ice-bay of Forochel.

You have discovered the shade of Arvedui, the last king of Arthedain, haunting the wreckage of the Elf-ship which had come to rescue him so long ago. It may be that the shade will know the whereabouts of Narchuil.Talk to Arvedui'There is a näkijä, a seer, who dwells outside the village. She is powerful and does not fear the Lord of Storms. She may help you find your ring.

'You will find Saija at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri; that is on the western edge of the Ice Bay. She is haughty and proud, but you may find in her an ally against Mordrambor.

'Go, seek the wisdom of the ages.''Thou art not of the Lossoth, but are a ${RACE} from my lands of old. Why come ye into this terrible place?''You come from Yrjänä? I have no fear of the stone-dwellers from Angmar. They can do me no harm. I will share with you what wisdom I have.

'Long ago, a king from the South came into Forochel, seeking refuge from the Witch-king of Angmar. Arvedui was his right name, but we called him the Gaunt King, because he was frail from hiding in the ancient mines of the dwarves.

'The Gaunt King begged for aid from the Lossoth, which was given but hesitantly, for the Lossoth feared the wrath of the Witch-king. The Gaunt King stayed with the Lossoth until a great sea-monster appeared in the Ice-bay, bearing many Elves. We warned the Gaunt King not to go forth upon the back of the beast, but to wait for the summer, so that the power of the Witch-king would not be so strong. He would not listen, and the storms slew the beast.

'It is said that the body of the beast may yet be seen in the Ice-bay, north and east of here. It may be that you may find the knowledge you seek upon its corpse.''It is said that the body of the beast may yet be seen in the Ice-bay, north and east of here. It may be that you may find the knowledge you seek upon its corpse.''You will find Saija at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri; that is on the western edge of the Ice Bay. She is haughty and proud, but you may find in her an ally against Mordrambor.

'Go, seek the wisdom of the ages.'Upon finding the wreckage of the ship which came to carry King Arvedui back to the Grey Havens, you made an even more shocking discovery: the shade of Arvedui himself.The book of heraldry lies in the dwarf-mines where Arvedui and his people hid in Länsi-mâ.

Arvedui instructed you to find the book of heraldry that was abandoned deep in the old dwarf-mines and bring it to a Ranger encamped in Forochel.Find the book of heraldryThe Ranger is encamped at Sûri-kylä.

Now that you have found the book of heraldry as directed by Arvedui, you should take it to the Ranger the ancient king spoke of.Arevedui is in the wreckage of the Elf-ship, north along the Ice-bay in Talvi-mûri.

Having delivered the book, you should return to Arvedui for further guidance.Talk to Arvedui'Thou dost not belong in this place, but it matters not. Alas, so much evil has befallen this world. I remain here in penitence, for my own curse was brought down upon my head.

'In pride, I ignored the warnings of the Lossoth, for I wished to return to my kingdom. The storms of the Ice Bay brought ruin to the vessel and all aboard her, and in despair and wrath I cursed myself for my pride. Redemption does not lay beyond hope, however, and those who follow in my footsteps may yet bring me peace.

'In the dwarf-mines south in Länsi-mâ, where we first hid from the agents of the Witch-king, we were forced to abandon many things. One such item is a book of heraldry which details the lineage of my people. Go forth and find it, then bring it to the Dúnadan who watches these cold lands at Sûri-kylä. He will take it to his lord.''Thank thee, friend from the South. Thou hast earned me one step closer to redemption.

'Pride can be such a terrible thing. I desired out of pride to return to Fornost and caused the deaths of many Elves.

'Ah, but I speak of things that I should not dwell upon....''In the dwarf-mines south in Länsi-mâ, where we first hid from the agents of the Witch-king, we were forced to abandon many things. One such item is a book of heraldry which details the lineage of my people. Go forth and find it, then bring it to the Dúnadan who watches these cold lands at Sûri-kylä. He will take it to his lord.''Return now to the shade of Arvedui, by the wreckage of the ship that sought to bring him from this land!''What is this? A book of heraldry once belonging to Arvedui of Arthedain? Ai-oi! You say you have seen the spirit of Arvedui himself?

'I will take this at once to Rivendell, for this tale must be told to Elrond and Aragorn!'To gain the trust of Arvedui's restless spirit, you have performed a deed of kindness for him and delivered a lost tome to one of the descendants of his house.Saija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri.

Arvedui told you that the captain of the Elf-ship did not perish with his vessel and suggested that you seek the knowledge of Saija regarding the fate of Aearil and his crew.Talk to Saija'I may one day forgive my pride, but that day is not yet come.

'Long after the Thoroval perished, another ship came into the Ice Bay. It, too, was from Mithlond, and I can only assume it was seeking news of the Thoroval and its crew. That ship also perished, but the Elves attempted to flee its destruction. I do not believe they perished in the cold waters -- at least not all -- but I cannot say what their final fate was.

'Perhaps the seer of the Lossoth who sent thee to find the ship would know? Return to her and seek her guidance once more.''You found the body of the sea-monster? You found also the shade of the Gaunt King? This is most unexpected, but perhaps not as surprising as it might have been.''Long after the Thoroval perished, another ship came into the Ice Bay. It, too, was from Mithlond, and I can only assume it was seeking news of the Thoroval and its crew. That ship also perished, but the Elves attempted to flee its destruction. I do not believe they perished in the cold waters -- at least not all -- but I cannot say what their final fate was.

'Perhaps the seer of the Lossoth who sent thee to find the ship would know? Return to her and seek her guidance once more.'Not only did you find the wreckage of the Elf-ship which had borne King Arvedui from the shores of Forochel, but you found the shade of Arvedui himself.Saija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri.

Saija will tell you what you need to know, but wants you to perform two tasks for her.Saija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri.

Now that you have completed both of the tasks she set before you, you should speak again with Saija.Talk to Saija'As you have spoken with the Gaunt King, I will tell you what I have learned of his story, but first there are things you must do. My information does not come without a price.

'Speak to me when you are ready to hear the tasks I have for you.''You have earned the right to hear this tale which has been kept by my kindred, and is known only to them and to very few among the learned Wise. 

'When the great sea-monster came to take the Laiha-herra away, my people begged him not to mount upon it, for the Witch-king could send terrible storms to drown them all, but he would not listen. Surely, as the monster moved out into the great water, a most violent storm came from the north and caused the monster to be dashed upon the ice and slain.

'For many days, the storm raged, and all who were caught outside of the village perished in the deep snow and blinding ice-rain that poured from the sky. When it finally ended, we went in search of survivors, both of the Lumi-väki and of those who had gone out upon the sea-monster, but there were none.

'In the following year, another sea monster appeared, like unto the first, but it was slain ere it neared the land, and the Vanha-väki who rode upon it fled its ruin. Though we found many bodies frozen in the ice, the trail was lost at the mouth of a cave sealed by ice.'Saija has two tasks she requires of you before she imparts her knowledge.Ice-giants can be found south and west of Näky-kolo.

Saija has tasked you with defeating the Ice-giants that have come down from the mountains.  She also suggests pulling them onto hot springs to weaken them.Defeat Ice-giants  (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Saija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri.

Having defeated the Ice-giants, you should return at once to Saija.Talk to Saija'To the south and west, Ice-giants have come down from the mountains, threatening all who hunt in those lands. Go forth and meet them, drive them from the lands of the Lossoth. Such a deed will help to prove your loyalty.

'You may find them easier to deal with if you draw them to the hot springs that spout up within their camp. When you have completed this task, return to me for further instruction.''To the south and west, Ice-giants have come down from the mountains, threatening all who hunt in those lands. Go forth and meet them, drive them from the lands of the Lossoth. Such a deed will help to prove your loyalty.

'You may find them easier to deal with if you draw them to the hot springs that spout up within their camp. When you have completed this task, return to me for further instruction.''Only a ${RACE} of great valour would dare to face such mighty and terrible creatures. You have proved your prowess.'Saija has two tasks she requires of you before she imparts her knowledge.Ice-wights can be found above Näky-kolo south and west from Näky-kolo.

Saija has tasked you with banishing the ice-wights from the shores of Forochel.Defeat ice-wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Saija is at Näky-kolo.

Now that you have defeated many ice-wights, you should return to Saija as instructed.Talk to Saija'Upon the western shores of the Ice Bay, where the storms often rage the worst, dwell fell spirits sent from Angmar to trouble the Lossoth. The demons raise up terrible wights and make of it a place of great dread. Go forth and banish these creatures from the shores of Forochel.

'You will find them above this cave, south and west from its mouth and then north into the ruins. When you have fulfilled your task, return to me here.''Upon the western shores of the Ice Bay, where the storms often rage the worst, dwell fell spirits sent from Angmar to trouble the Lossoth. The demons raise up terrible wights and make of it a place of great dread. Go forth and banish these creatures from the shores of Forochel.

'You will find them above this cave, south and west from its mouth and then north into the ruins. When you have fulfilled your task, return to me here.''Your task was futile, for a mortal cannot eternally banish a spirit, but your courage in the face of such horror speaks well of you.'Saija disclosed to you the location of a cave where the Lossoth believe the captain of the second Elf-ship may have taken refuge after the ship was sunk.The Elf-captain or his belongings may remain within the cave.

Saija suggested you speak with her again to seek out the cave, and she would guide you there.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>Find NarchuilThe shade of Arvedui is at the Ruin of Thoroval north and east along the Ice Bay in Talvi-mûri.

Having recovered a ring-fragment from Aearil's belongings, you should seek out the shade of Arvedui and let him know the fate of his would-be rescuer and learn whether the fragment you found is indeed the lost half of Narchuil.'This cave lies within Talvi-mûri. It is a dangerous place, but I do not think you should fear to go there. I myself will guide you there when you are ready.

'If the Elf does not live, you will likely not find any remains beyond his clothing. If he bore this ring you seek, it should be among his belongings, if they remain.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'Are you ready to leave?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'The Elf-captain perished then? I will not grieve, for he escaped this Middle-earth to a land much greener, or so the Elves say.'Newbold Leafcutter directed you to the tomb of Maenadar the Craftsman, but you came too late to recover Celebrimbor's shaping tool.Eglamír is at Celondim in Ered Luin, far to the west of Bree-land.

Newbold Leafcutter suggested you return to Eglamír for more advice.Talk to Eglamír at Celondim'There is little else that I can help you with, ${PLAYER}. It's a pity that tool was stolen... I would have dearly loved to see it.

'Ah well, perhaps you should return to the Elf who sent you... Eglamír was it? He may have more words of wisdom for you.

'Celondim is far off, I understand... in the shadows of the Blue Mountains. You will want to start off soon.''I believe you mentioned you came here from Celondim...?''This is ill news, ${PLAYER}. With that tool, Angmar may do great harm in Eriador....'Newbold Leafcutter could help you no longer and suggested you return to Eglamír at Celondim.Yrjänä is at Sûri-kylä in Forochel, far to the east and north of Celondim.

Eglamír believes that Amarthiel's minions may be trying to find the lair of a dragon which may still dwell in Forochel, the hide from which may be used to repair the bellows of the forges at Mirobel. He suggests you go to the frozen north and speak with the Lossoth chieftain Yrjänä.Talk to Yrjänä at Sûri-kylä'It is tragic news that you bring from Bree-land. If I had to guess, I would say that Angmar is trying to rekindle the forges of Mirobel in Eregion...perhaps they plan to forge a new ring or repair an old one?

'Ah well, it is of no matter. There is much harm to be done if Angmar succeeds. However before they rekindle the forges, they will need to fix the great bellows. The bellows were originally made of a fine Elven leather that could withstand the test of time, but those are now rotted.

'Angmar could, however, replace the Elf-leather with dragon-hide. It is strong and durable. There is rumour that a dragon -- lesser though he might be -- once dwelled in the frozen wastes of Forochel. Go to Sûri-kylä and speak with their chieftain, Yrjänä. He may know more.''One of the Vanha-väki sent you to me? The last I remember seeing was the one named Laerdan, and he failed in his task.

'What does this Vanha-väki wish of the Lumi-väki?''Yrjänä dwells in the Lossoth village of Sûri-kylä in Forochel. He may be able to guide you to the dragon's lair.'Eglamír believes that the minions of Amarthiel may be seeking the hide of the Dragon of Forochel to repair the great bellows of Mirobel, the Ring-forges of Eregion, and sent you to learn of Bregmor for Yrjänä, the chieftain of Sûri-kylä.Bregmor's lair can be found far to the west of Sûri-kylä, south-east of Jotunstath.

Yrjänä told you that the dragon Bregmor once terrorized Forochel, but no longer. He also indicated that he would not spare his people to guide you to Bregmor's lair, leaving you to fend for yourself.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>Find and enter Bregmor's lairYrjänä is at Sûri-kylä, far to the east of Bregmor's lair.

You failed to stop Angmar from obtaining the hide of the dragon Bregmor and should now return to Yrjänä with your news.Talk to Yrjänä at Sûri-kylä'Your Vanha-väki sends you to find the lair of the great lohikârme, the creature called Bregmor? I know somewhat of him, though I have never seen him.

'It is told among the Lumi-väki that Bregmor was once the scourge of these cold lands. Many hunters tracked him, but none ever returned. It came to be that one day Bregmor ceased to hunt the Lumi-väki, and we saw no need to anger him further.

'If you wish to visit the lohikârme, you may do so yourself. You will find his lair far to the west, south-east of Jotunstath, the home of the Elukka, the Ice-giants as you call them.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'Bregmor was an evil creature, but it is sad still that such a great beast perished in such a lonely way.

'More troubling still is that the Rauta-väki succeeded in defiling the person of the lohikârme. And Mordrambor, why would he aid in this fashion? Is he not an enemy of Amarthiel, seeking her ring for himself? It is very strange and troubling.''I will not send my people to die for you. If you wish to see the lohikârme, go yourself.'You failed to stop the machinations of Angmar in Forochel, leaving the servants of Amarthiel free to rekindle the forges of Mirobel.Eglamír is at Celondim in Ered Luin, far to the south and west of Forochel.

Yrjänä told you to return to Eglamír with news of your failure.Talk to Eglamír at Celondim'You should return to your Vanha-väki, this Eglamír. I am sure he will want to know of your failure. Do not forget to tell of the involvement of Mordrambor. What it means, I do not know, but perhaps others will know what it foretells.

'I believe you said he dwells at the Vanha-väki place called Celondim, far to the south and west in the Blue Mountains. I would hurry there and speak with him.''Alas! There is little hope now that we may hinder Amarthiel from reforging Narchuil and bringing her armies to bear upon Eriador. Especially if this Lord of Umbar, this Mordrambor you spoke of, is aiding her once more!''It would be well for you to return to your Vanha-väki and confess your failure.'With hide from the dragon Bregmor and Celebrimbor's shaping tool, there is nothing more Eglamír knows of that Amarthiel will need to rekindle the forges of Eregion and reforge Narchuil.Elrond is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws, far to the east of Celondim.

Eglamír suggested that you bring news of your failure to Elrond at Rivendell.Talk to Elrond at Rivendell'There is no more aid I can give you. With the hide of Bregmor and Celebrimbor's shaping tool, there is naught to keep Angmar from rekindling the forges of Eregion and reforging Narchuil. You have failed, but think not too poorly of yourself... the chances were slim at best.

'You should return to Rivendell and bring this dire news to Elrond Halfelven. Perhaps he will know what to do now.

'Rivendell lies in the Trollshaws, far to the east in the shadow of the Misty Mountains.''Angmar is one step closer to claiming all of Eriador. You should return to Elrond at once!''So the Ring-forges will burn again. Amarthiel will reforge Narchuil and use it to lead her armies against Eriador. At her side will be Mordrambor, who appears to have sided with her once more.

'If this happens, the North will be crushed, and though Rivendell will stand, it will only be a matter of time before we, too, are overrun.

'We must put an end to Amarthiel's plans, once and for all.'With your defeats in Bree-land and Forochel, little remains now but to throw yourself at Amarthiel's forces in a vain attempt to put an end to her plans.Mirobel can be reached by travelling far to the south, into the land of Eregion.

Elrond instructed you to journey to Mirobel and do whatever you can to stop Amarthiel.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>Travel to Mirobel and try to stop AmarthielThe watch-captain Glorenthol is at Delossad in Tâl Bruinen.

You failed to stop Amarthiel, but she was at last defeated at the surprise return of Mordirith. Narchuil has fallen into the hands of the False King, but Amarthiel is now the prisoner of the Free Peoples. You should speak with the watch-captain Glorenthol.Talk to the watch-captainElrond is in his library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

The watch-captain has directed you to speak with Elrond regarding your mission to Mirobel.Talk to Elrond at Rivendell'One last hope remains, ${PLAYER}, and vain it may well be. You must travel to Mirobel and try to put an end to Amarthiel's plans there.

'You must hurry... it may already be too late, but there is a slender hope that she has not yet received the materials she needs to rekindle the forges of Eregion and reforge Narchuil.

'Mirobel is far to the south of Rivendell, in the land of Eregion. May the stars shine upon your road.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'Your stand against Amarthiel is the last hope for Eriador, unless the Company fulfils their task....

'You must travel to Mirobel in Eregion, far to the south, if you are to have any chance of stopping her.''Master Elrond awaits you in his library, ${PLAYER}. You should speak with him at once.''Master Elrond awaits you in his library... you should go there at once!''The shadow has not yet lifted -- not as long as Narchuil rests in the hands of Mordirith -- but you have scored at least one major victory for Eriador: Amarthiel has been captured.

'Alas, though, for the loss of Laerdan. He thought he could bring forth his daughter from Amarthiel... we must learn whether he succeeded.'Laerdan sent you to Filegnaneth to collect provisions for the journey to Eregion, but she does not have the fine clover honey she requires to make lembas, the waybread of the Elves.The expert cook is in Michel Delving in the Shire, far to the west of Rivendell. Filegnaneth is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws, far to the east of the Shire.

Filegnaneth has asked you to travel to the Shire and purchase fine clover honey from the expert cook there.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! Laerdan's journey is not unknown to me. I have gathered many provisions, but I lack the fine clover honey I need to prepare lembas, the waybread of the Elves.

'I am given to understand, however, that there is an expert cook in the Shire, the land of the halflings. Young Peregrin Took suggested I send someone to Michel Delving to find this cook, but the journey is far, and we are busy with many preparations.

'Perhaps you would undertake this task? Journey to Michel Delving in the Shire, far to the west of Rivendell, and purchase some fine clover honey, then return to me.''Yes, this will do nicely. A very rich gold and sweet from the comb.

'You may let Laerdan know that the lembas will be ready ere his journey begins.'Laerdan sent you to Gath Forthnír to reclaim his breastplate from the Ranger Golodir.Dolendath is located in Imlad Balchorth, south and west of Myrkworth.

Golodir suggested that you may find Laerdan's breastplate at Dolendath, the place where Golodir's army first took refuge in Angmar.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'Alas, I know not where Laerdan's breastplate may lie. I do not recall him wearing it when we came to Gath Forthnír.

'There is one place you may look, but it is a terrible and dangerous place. When we first passed Rammas Deluon, we took refuge at a place called Dolendath in Imlad Balchorth. When the Dead arose, we fled and left much behind. Perhaps Laerdan's breastplate was among those belongings.

'If you wish to search Dolendath, you will find the entrance in Imlad Balchorth, to the south and west of Myrkworth. But beware the Dead!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'I see you have found the breastplate, but it is in too poor condition to give to Laerdan now. Allow me to have one of the dwarves here repair it. I would consider it a gift to my friend.

'I will have it brought by one of our messengers to Esteldín and on to Rivendell.'Laerdan is preparing to make the journey to Eregion, but he needs your aid to finish his preparations.Filegnaneth is found in the Hall of Fire at Rivendell. Nat Collop is found in Tinnudír in Evendim, far to the west and north of the Trollshaws. Golodir is found in Gath Forthnír in Angmar, far to the north of the Trollshaws.

Laerdan asked you to perform several tasks on his behalf.Talk to Filegnaneth in RivendellTalk to Nat Collop at TinnudírTalk to Golodir at Gath ForthnírLaerdan is at the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

You should return at once to Laerdan with news of your successes, but also of the resulting delays.Elrond is in his library in the Last Homely House at Rivendell.

You should tell Elrond of Laerdan's note at once.Talk to Elrond in Rivendell'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! You have been of great help to me in the past, and now I have need of your aid once more. As you know, we will soon depart for Eregion, but there is much to be done before I leave.

'First, I would ask you to visit Filegnaneth in the Hall of Fire here at Rivendell and request provisions of her. Then, I would have you journey to the isle of Tinnudír in Evendim and ask Nat Collop to send my trusted steed Arel back to me. Lastly, I would ask you to venture to Gath Forthnír and ask Golodir to return my breastplate to me -- it has long been missing.

'When you have accomplished these tasks, return to me, and we will depart.''${PLAYER}, I must apologize, but I did not think you would understand. Your tasks were little more than a diversion.

'I have departed already from Rivendell and have taken with me the shards of Narchuil. I must return them to Narmeleth, or her mind will never be made whole.

'The love of my daughter, alas, must supersede all else. May the light of the stars shine upon your path.''Laerdan has taken the shards of Narchuil to Amarthiel? This is dread news, my friend. This development forces our hand....''You are not done yet? You must make haste!

'Filegnaneth is here in Rivendell, in the Fire Hall of Elrond's House, Nat Collop can be found at the stable at Tinnudír in Evendim, and Golodir remains at Gath Forthnír in Angmar.'Laerdan has asked you to speak with Nat Collop, a Man of Ost Forod who oversees the stable at Tinnudír, about sending his horse, Arel, to Rivendell.Thorin's Hall is in Ered Luin, far to the west and south of Evendim.

Nat Collop has asked you to speak with the expert metalsmith at Thorin's Hall and obtain some dwarf-steel cutlery moulds.'Well now, Laerdan sends you to bring his horse back to him? That'll be a mite difficult. You see, he badly needs new shoes, and I haven't the materials to finish them.

'Without some dwarf-steel cutlery moulds, there's not much more I can do. I hear there's an expert metalsmith at Thorin's Hall, out in the Blue Mountains way off to the west, who might have some, but I can't leave.

'Perhaps you would make the journey to Thorin's Hall and purchase a few of the moulds? I'm sure I could make it worth your while....''Well, these will do right nicely, ${PLAYER}! Where better to get dwarf-steel moulds than the dwarves?

'You tell Master Laerdan that I'll send a rider down with Arel as soon as the new shoes are finished.'You found a note left by Laerdan indicating that he has left Rivendell with the intent of bringing the shards of Narchuil to Amarthiel.Ladrochan, the stable-master, can be found in the stables of Rivendell, west of the Last Homely House.

Elrond has told you to speak with Ladrochan and learn how long ago Laerdan left Rivendell.Talk to Ladrochan at the stable in RivendellElrond is in his library in the Last Homely House of Rivendell, to the east of the stable.

Ladrochan told you that Laerdan had left Rivendell two days ago. You should return to Elrond with this news at once.Talk to Elrond in Rivendell'${PLAYER}, it seems that Amarthiel's tormentors succeeded in breaking Laerdan's mind. He has left Rivendell and seeks to bring the shards of Narchuil to Amarthiel in the vain hope of restoring her mind to Narmeleth.

'Time is of the essence! We must learn quickly how far ahead Laerdan has gone. We must try to overtake him before he can complete his purpose.

'Speak with Ladrochan, the stable-master, at the stables to the west of here. He will surely have seen Laerdan.''Hurry to Ladrochan and learn what you may of Laerdan's departure.''You seek news of Laerdan? He came to me two days ago seeking the use of a horse... he said that Master Elrond had given him leave to seek the traitorous Amarthiel....

'This was not the case? Please tell Lord Elrond immediately!''It appears I was remiss in giving Laerdan a mount... you should speak at once with Elrond!''The news becomes more dire with each passing moment. Alas for Laerdan.

'There is no time left to lose... we must act at once!'Elrond was dismayed by Laerdan's secret departure. Doubts have been cast now upon the honour of the Elf-lord, and Elrond desires to know the truth behind his disappearance.Laerdan's room is in the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

Elrond has asked you to search Laerdan's rooms for anything which might reveal Laerdan's full purpose.Elrond is in the library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

You found a journal in Laerdan's rooms. It may reveal Laerdan's plans.Examine Laerdan's journal'Your news is most distressing, ${PLAYER}. I fear Laerdan's will was broken under the torments of Amarthiel.

'You have my approval to search Laerdan's room for anything that reveals the full purpose of his departure. I fear there is little time, for if he brings the shards of Narchuil to Mirobel, Amarthiel is sure to be waiting there.

'Laerdan's room is in this very house. Go now and return when you have learned more.'This map has a route sketched across it from Rivendell south to Eregion, but it contains no other clues.This pack was evidently left behind intentionally, for it is terribly worn and would likely not have survived a long journey.You find a coil of rope which Laerdan had clearly intended to take with him, but apparently overlooked in his haste to leave.This journal contains many entries, but it lay open at one particular passage....'Search Laerdan's room and return when you have discovered his full purpose.'Have you found aught yet that reveals Laerdan's purpose?'While searching Laerdan's rooms, you discovered his journal, the passage he had read last marked clearly.You should read further into the journal... it may provide some clues as to Laerdan's purposes.Read Laerdan's journal further and experience 'Session: The Prisoner of Sammath Baul' or read the shortened account insteadWhile reading Laerdan's journal, you discover that Laerdan believes he saw his daughter Narmeleth there at Sammath Baul. This entry is quite disturbing....Finish reading the journalThe entry the journal was opened to detailed Laerdan's imprisonment at Sammath Baul and his torture at the hands of Amarthiel and her minions.You begin to read more about Laerdan's imprisonment and torture....While imprisoned within the fortress of Sammath Baul, Laerdan endures tortures of both body and mind. Deception will, as always, prove Amarthiel's closest ally: when she appears to the captive in the guise of his daughter Narmeleth, Laerdan relinquishes his deepest secret: the location of the second half of Narchuil. It remains hidden within Forochel, but if it were to be joined with the other half of the broken ring, it might be reforged.

'I could save you!' Laerdan swears to the villain wearing his daughter's guise, even as Amarthiel leaves the protection of her prisoner to the captain of Sammath Baul and her Bloodletters. Heroes of the Free People arrive to free Laerdan from captivity, though not from the trap in which Amarthiel has ensnared him....In his journal, Laerdan refers to his "visitation by Narmeleth" as an epiphany. He came to believe that he could free her by giving her Narchuil, the ring of Amarthiel.Laerdan's journal contained a horrid description of his imprisonment and torture at Sammath Baul.Elrond is found in the Library of the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

You should return at once to Elrond and tell him what you have learned.Talk to ElrondYou learn nothing more from Laerdan's journal than the details of his imprisonment and his encounters with Amarthiel and Narmeleth, real or imagined. Elrond may understand more of these things than you.'Alas! This is sorrowful and dreadful news you bring, ${PLAYER}. I now understand how Laerdan was broken. The evils of Angmar are truly great if they can turn a father's love for his daughter into a terrible weapon.

'This forebodes a greater evil still....'Elrond was alarmed by the journal entry you described, fearing the worst for Laerdan.Elrond is in his library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

Elrond wishes to speak with you regarding what he discovered in Laerdan's journal.Discuss with Elrond what fate may await Laerdan and experience 'Session: The Fate of Laerdan' or read the shortened account insteadElrond is in his library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

You discussed the fate of Laerdan with Elrond, coming to a dire conclusion.Talk to Elrond'I dread what is to come, ${PLAYER}. Laerdan's journal brings me great distress. I fear the deceptions of Amarthiel will bring Laerdan to a terrible end.

'Will you hear me?''From what you have told me, I believe Amarthiel has deceived Laerdan into bringing Narchuil to her. I fear he may be walking into a trap....'Believing that only Narchuil can restore the broken mind of his daughter Narmeleth, Laerdan travels to the old ring-forges of Eregion. When he arrives and is confronted with Amarthiel's deception, he fights bravely, but there is little hope and he is overwhelmed.

Now Amarthiel needs only reforge the broken halves of Narchuil using forbidden arts to accomplish her evil ends...'To think of Laerdan's fate grieves me, but we can dwell upon it no longer. Greater still is the threat Amarthiel will become if Narchuil should fall into her grasp.'Laerdan's journal brings more concerns upon Elrond than just the fate of Laerdan....Elrond spoke of an Elf named Eglamír who may dwell in Celondim in Ered Luin, far to the west of Rivendell and the Trollshaws.

Elrond has told you that Celebrimbor wisely did not record many of the details of Ring-craft in the lore of Eregion. However Elrond did find many references to an Elf named Eglamír who may know more.Search for Eglamír in Celondim'I have little doubt of the Enemy's intentions, though I do not know whether they will bear out. That is our one hope.

'There is much Ring-lore of Eregion remaining here in Rivendell, for I myself wrote it, and much has been brought here thanks to the efforts of many. Sadly, this lore reveals little that might tell us Angmar's plans.

'Fortunately, my study of the lore has revealed one clue, a name. This name is Eglamír, undoubtedly an Elf who was a trusted friend of Celebrimbor. He may have insights that will aid you. If he is still to be found in Middle-earth, he may be in Celondim. Many Elves visit there before heading further south to the Grey Havens. Travel there and, if you find him, see what aid he can be to you in your quest.''You seek knowledge of Ring-craft and the long ruined forges of Mirobel. I would turn you away if not for the fact Master Elrond sent you. He was a great friend of Celebrimbor, so I will lend what aid I may.''Find the Elf Eglamír that I spoke of. He may be of help to us. You may find him, or some knowledge of him, in Celondim.'In an effort to learn more of the Ring-lore of Eregion, Elrond sent you to Eglamír, an Elf of Eregion who dwells now at Celondim.Bree-town lies in Bree-land, far to the east of Ered Luin.

Eglamír would speak little of the Ring-lore of Eregion, but did tell you that the Ring-smith Celebrimbor gave a shaping tool to a Man of Bree-land. He suggests you find someone in Bree who might know the whereabouts of the Man's barrow.Newbold Leafcutter can be found at the Scholar's Stairs Archive in Bree-town.

You were advised to seek out Newbold Leafcutter to learn more regarding the whereabouts of Celebrimbor's shaping tool.Talk to Newbold Leafcutter'Of the Ring-lore of Eregion, I will speak little. It is dangerous knowledge learned from the Dark Lord and should not be explored further.

'However, I will tell you this: in the days of Eregion, our lord, Celebrimbor, gave to an Elf-friend, a Man of Bree-land, one of his shaping tools. I would expect that this tool was buried with him, as is the custom of Men.

'Surely you may find someone in Bree-town who might know the location of the barrow where the shaping tool lies. Perhaps someone at their Town Hall or a patron of the inn there, or even a member of their Watch.''Well now, what is it you wanted again? Oh, the Barrow-downs...why didn't you say so? That place has a bad name, if you don't mind me saying, and I would stay away from there.

'But if you're determined to know more about them, you should ask Newbold Leafcutter up at the Scholar's Stairs Archive.''What? You want to go to the Barrow-downs to find some kind of tool? Why, we've had enough trouble with spooks in this town.

'If you want to know about those old Barrows, you go bother Newbold Leafcutter up at the Scholar's Stairs Archive.''Greetings, ${PLAYER}! Do you seek yet more adventure in the Barrow-downs?''The Barrow-downs are a dark place, full of evil things. No matter what we do to try and cleanse them, the terror lingers. What can you do to banish something that is already dead?

'If you need to find a specific barrow, you had best ask Newbold Leafcutter, up at the Scholar's Stairs Archive.'Speak with the men of Bree and see if you might learn the location of the barrow I mentioned.'Eglamír sent you in search of someone with knowledge of the Barrow-downs and the shaping tool of Celebrimbor.The tomb of Maenadar can be found in the small barrow beside the entrance to Haudh Iarchith in the southern parts of the Barrow-downs.

Newbold Leafcutter told you that the shaping tool can be found in the tomb of Maenadar the Craftsman.Find the tomb of Maenadar the CraftsmanNewbold Leafcutter is at the Scholar's Stairs Archive in Bree-town.

You came too late to the tomb of Maenadar and found it despoiled. Angmar arrived first. You should return to Newbold Leafcutter to learn if he knows anything else.Talk to Newbold Leafcutter in Bree'So you seek knowledge of the shaping tool of Celebrimbor and Maenadar the Craftsman? I know the story well.

'Alas, the tool will not be easy to find, if it even still exists. It was buried with Maenadar in Haudh Iarchith, which has become infested with wights of the vilest sort.

'Haudh Iarchith lies in the southern part of the Barrow-downs, and Maenadar's tomb is found beside it in the cradle of a larger mound of the barrow. Be wary as you journey...the Dead do not take kindly to visitors.'The tomb of Maenadar the Craftsman has recently been disturbed and any relics which might have lain there have been removed....'That's too bad, ${PLAYER}. More and more foul travellers have been arriving here from the South, and it would be no wonder that some of them are grave-robbers.''The tomb you seek may be alongside the entrance to the barrows of Haudh Iarchith in the southern Barrow-downs.'Laerdan's hopes of using the sword and armour of Golodir to renew the Ranger's spirit were not in vain. The sight of the shining shield of Gondor and of his bright-burning sword, Dúnachar, kindled within Golodir a new fire... perhaps a dangerous one.Mordirith can be found within the throne room of Carn Dûm.

Golodir has asked you to join him as he returns to Carn Dûm to face Mordirith, the False King, Steward of Angmar.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>Speak to GolodirGolodir is at Gath Forthnír.

After defeating Mordirith and encountering the mysterious Sara Oakheart, you and Golodir travelled back to Gath Forthnír. You should speak with Golodir again.Talk to Golodir in Gath Forthnír'The time for vengeance is at hand. Despite the strength you have seen within Angmar's bosom, it is a strength which may falter quickly. Mordirith, the False King, is a creature of great power, but I believe he may be hindered, if not destroyed altogether.

'I will return to Carn Dûm and face Mordirith. It is time to cut the Iron Crown from the head of this serpent. I would ask that you stand with me!

'Together, we will pass into that vile city and face Mordirith in the throne room of Carn Dûm. Gather what companions and supplies you need, for the fight ahead will be terrible.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'The journey into Carn Dûm will be a difficult one, but Mordirith must be thrown down. Are you ready to travel?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'Mordirith has been weakened, though not destroyed. The way though is open for others to finally throw down this False King. I wish that it had been I who had driven that foul creature back into Shadow, but it is enough to have done what I have.

'I ask that if you do return to Carn Dûm, finish the work that we started, strike down Mordirith. Although a creature such as he cannot be entirely destroyed -- for he can simply recloak -- such a loss for him will be a great victory for the Free Peoples of Eriador.

'Still, there is more I would ask of you....'With Golodir's aid, you have greatly weakened Mordirith, the Steward of Angmar, and avenged the death of Lorniel.Aragorn is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House.

Golodir instructed you to take word of Mordirith's fall to his chieftain, Aragorn.Talk to Aragorn in Rivendell'This victory is an important one, though not as complete as I had at first hoped. However, even this victory will give us a brief reprieve from the onslaught of the Enemy. I would ask that news of our success be brought to my chieftain, Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

'You have met him then? He is at Rivendell? Go, then, to speak with my Lord Aragorn in one of the guest rooms along the road that winds up the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris, and tell him of our deeds here.''Aragorn must learn of our victory against the False King. Go to Rivendell and speak with him in one of the guest rooms along the road that winds up the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris.''So Golodir did not perish, and the Shadow of Angmar is, for the moment at least, weakened. I am of a mind that even if Mordirith does finally fall, he may someday return... or another Shadow of the Enemy will take his place.

'Still, your efforts were valiant and deserving of praise, ${PLAYER}. Your name will not be forgotten by the Dúnedain of the North.'Mordirith, the False King, has been defeated and sent back to Mordor houseless, but the mysterious Sara Oakheart stole the palantír Mordirith had in his possession. This greatly concerns Gandalf the Grey.Golodir is at Gath Forthnír in Angmar, far to the north of Rivendell.

Gandalf the Grey has instructed you to return to Gath Forthnír and help Golodir to search for Sara Oakheart and the missing palantír.Sara Oakheart is at Barad Gúlaran in Nan Gurth in Angmar. Barad Gúlaran is located in the centre of a series of bridges that surround it like the spokes of a waggon-wheel. Sara Oakheart was seen by the tower located at the most south-easterly of these bridges.

Sara Oakheart has been found outside Barad Gúlaran. Golodir has told you to be careful.'Ah, ${PLAYER}, I need to speak with you. I have heard of your adventures at Carn Dûm, and I am concerned. Besides your strange encounters with her during your travels, I have never heard of this Sara Oakheart, and I am troubled by her.

'There are few now in this age who have even heard of the palantíri, much less be concerned enough with them to steal them. Moreso, they have now become dangerous, for Sauron possesses the Ithil-stone, which he has certainly bent to his will.

'Return to Golodir at Gath Forthnír and help him search for Sara Oakheart and the palantír. I fear that only evil will come of these events.''Lend your aid to Golodir at Gath Forthnír. The valiant Ranger has a mighty task before him.''Gandalf sent you to help me search for Sara Oakheart and the missing palantír? Well, the search will be short, for one of my scouts has found her already: outside Barad Gúlaran, the place where the Witch-king studied his terrible arts. She has made no effort to conceal her whereabouts, but I can think of no reason this would be so.

'You will find Barad Gúlaran in the centre of Nan Gurth, an evil valley haunted by wights and other dread creatures. Barad Gúlaran is located in the centre of a series of bridges that surround it like the spokes of a waggon-wheel. Sara Oakheart was seen by the tower located at the most south-easterly of these bridges. Go and bring back the palantír.''Barad Gúlaran is located in Nan Gurth, in the centre of a series of bridges that surround it like the spokes of a waggon-wheel. Sara Oakheart was seen by the tower located at the most south-easterly of these bridges. Find her and retrieve the palantír.''Seek out Sara Oakheart outside Barad Gularan, ${PLAYER}. Barad Gúlaran is located in the centre of a series of bridges that surround it like the spokes of a waggon-wheel. Sara Oakheart was seen by the tower located at the most south-easterly of these bridges. Be careful! There is more to that old woman than meets the eye.''I am glad that you have come, ${PLAYER}. The time has come for us to discuss several things. You have been most helpful in many ways to me and my friends. We have much to talk about very soon.'You have found Sara Oakheart at Barad Gúlaran, the ancient retreat of the Witch-king of Angmar.Sara Oakheart has asked you to escort her into Barad Gúlaran.Help Sara Oakheart get to the heart of Barad GúlaranGolodir is at Gath Forthnír.

You should return to Golodir and tell him what happened at Barad Gúlaran.'Thank you for coming, ${PLAYER}. You have been such a great help to me during my travels. I know you have many questions. We will talk, but first I have one last favour to ask of you.

'I need your help getting to the heart of this place. I am afraid I will not be able to make it on my own. Please help me this one last time, and I promise you that I will answer anything you have to ask.

'This is an evil place, full of unspeakable horrors, but I will guide you true! I only ask for your protection.''This is foul news indeed. To think that Sara Oakheart was all along an agent of Angmar. If she is indeed the same Amarthiel of which only legends speak, then evil are the days to come.

'I must consider what you have learned....''Are you ready to help me, my friend?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>Golodir is concerned that Mordirith's Knights will be taken into Amarthiel's service.Your allies may be found in Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands, Esteldín in the North Downs, and in places familiar to every people -- Combe for hobbits, the race of Men, and Beornings, and Gondamon for dwarf and Elf-kind.

Golodir has asked you to return to three places where Sara Oakheart has been encountered in the past and speak with allies in those places.Golodir is at Gath Forthnír in Angmar.

You should return to Golodir and tell him the task is completed.Talk to Golodir'No one should ever read this.''The Knights of Mordirith must be stopped, ${PLAYER}. They have been sent abroad to who knows what mischief.''You have done the Free Peoples of Eriador a great service. Thank you.

'While you were gone, I spoke with Laerdan about Amarthiel, and it seems he is the one with whom you should speak. He knows much more about this woman than any other, it seems.

'We will speak more about this shortly.'Constable Underhill mentioned that there is a new threat in the Chetwood and that maybe it is the knight whom you seek.The Knight of Mordirith can be found near an evil idol in the Chetwood, north-east of Combe.

Constable Underhill told you how to find the threat in the Chetwood, which might be the knight you seek.Find the Knight of MordirithConstable Underhill is outside The Comb and Wattle in Combe, south-west of the knight's camp.

Having defeated the Knight of Mordirith, you return to Constable Underhill and let him know that the threat is ended.'Golodir? I have never heard of him, but he sounds like one of those Rangers, like Toradan. If he's anything like Toradan was, I don't see any reason to doubt him.

'Well I'm not sure about this knight that you speak of, but there is a new threat in the Chetwood, much more powerful than anything you've come across in the past. Perhaps he is the knight you seek.

'You can find him at his camp near the evil idol in the Chetwood. It is not hard to find, north-east of here.''Why do you come to trouble me, fool? I have many things to take care of for Mordirith....

'What? You have defeated the Steward and left his throne to Amarthiel? Prepare to die!''It was the knight you sought, and you have slain him? I am impressed. It is not often we get heroes of your ilk in these parts.

'Thank you for your help. Please tell your friend Golodir that your deed is done, and I will make sure we do something about that dreadful idol. It seems to attract an awful lot of attention.'Daervunn has warned you of a new threat to the north near the entrance to Ram Dúath and that maybe it is the Knight you seek.The Knight of Mordirith may be found near Ost Crithlanc, north-east of Esteldín.

Daervunn told you of a new threat in the north, which may be the Knight you seek.Find the Knight of MordirithDaervunn is at Esteldín, south of the mouth of Ram Dúath.

Having defeated the Knight of Mordirith, You should return to Daervunn and let him know of your success.Speak with Daervunn at Esteldin'Golodir sent you? That is well, for it means his spirit has been renewed.

'There are grave dangers about and many have spoken of a new evil from Angmar near the entrance to Ram Dúath. I am quite certain that this is the Knight you seek.

'Go to the entrance to Ram Dúath, and you will find him...but be wary, there are many Angmarim in that place. It will not be an easy path.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Golodir will be pleased with your success.

'I can now give my attention to sending more help to the North, now that you have made the way easier.

'Return to Golodir and let him know of your victory.''Mordirith cannot be stopped. Even if you think you have defeated him, he will never truly be dead. He was the King of the South in mortal life and will be King of the North as a wraith-lord.

'Mordirith's will lives on, which is more than I can say for you, you pathetic ${RACE}.'Mathi Stouthand has warned you of a new threat to the north of Gondamon and that maybe it is the Knight you seek.The Knight of Mordirith might be found north of Gondamon.

Mathi Stouthand suggested that the threat to the north of Gondamon may be the Knight you seek.Find the Knight of MordirithMathi Stouthand is at Gondamon, south of the Knight's camp.

Having defeated the Knight of Mordirith, you should return to Mathi Stouthand and let him know that you were successful.'Golodir? I'm not familiar with him, but the Rangers helped us achieve peace here, so I will gladly aid you in this.

'I think I may know where your man is hiding.  There have been many reports of new threats to the north of here. They are mostly rumours, but several of my patrols have not returned. Perhaps you could look into this problem for us?

'Report back to me if you are successful.''Why do you come to trouble me, fool?  I have many things to do here for Mordirith.

'What? You have defeated the Steward and left his throne to Amarthiel? Prepare to die!''So not only did you find your Knight, but you defeated him as well? I am impressed. Thank you for your efforts. It is not often we see such a powerful ${CLASS} grace these parts.

'Please tell your friend Golodir that you have done your part here at Gondamon.'Frideric the Elder has warned you of a new threat in the southern bogs and that maybe it is the Knight you seek.The Knight of Mordirith may be found somewhere within Harloeg, south and east of Ost Guruth.

Frideric the Elder suggested that you might find the Knight of Mordirith in the southern bog.Find the Knight of MordirithFrideric the Elder is at Ost Guruth, north and west of Harloeg.

Having defeated the Knight of Mordirith, you should return to Frideric the Elder and let him know of your success.'I have never heard of Golodir, but if he is a Ranger, as you say, then why should we give aid to him? The Rangers did not aid us when we had a need, and we were forced to rely upon the shades of Oathbreakers to win our freedom.

'Still, we have lost many good men exploring Harloeg these days. There is rumour that Angmar is involved, so my guess is that is the best place to search. Go to Harloeg and seek out your evil Knight.

'When you have purged this evil, return to me.''It is a shame that you have travelled this far only to be defeated. Mordirith's defeat means nothing. You have no idea what forces are at work in Eriador, and you will die without knowing.''Thank you for helping us. I feared to send more men to Harloeg, for my people are small in number.

'You have helped the people of Ost Guruth greatly, and from what you tell me, all the Free Peoples.

'Thank you again, friend ${PLAYER}.'Golodir was pleased with your success in the south, but is still concerned with Amarthiel and her possession of a palantír.Laerdan is on the other side of the cave at Gath Forthnír.

Golodir instructed you to speak with Laerdan to learn how you can help him track down Amarthiel.Calenglad is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir on the eastern shore of Lake Evendim.

Laerdan instructed you to go to the Ranger-camp in Evendim to speak with the Ranger Calenglad.'You have done well with very difficult tasks, but there is more yet to be accomplished. While you were gone, I spoke with Laerdan about Amarthiel and where she might be heading with the palantír. We need to find her quickly and put an end to her schemes. 

'However, Laerdan knows much more than I thought before. Go and speak with him and learn how you can help him find Amarthiel.''I am loath to confess that I know more of Amarthiel than perhaps any other living, yet still I knew nothing of her secrets as Sara Oakheart. She has become much more powerful than I had imagined...indeed, I had believed her dead since the Battle of Fornost.

'It matters not. She is alive, and my pursuit of her must continue. I believe that she is heading to Evendim. She has a palantír--I am guessing that of Osgiliath, the master of the south, thought lost in Anduin--and if she has any hope of staying in power, she will need to confer often with the Lidless Eye. She may also use the palantír to find Narchuil, that token of power she lost long ago.

'The only place left for her is Annúminas then, for it may be that the pedestal where once sat the palantír of Annúminas still stands. You should go to Evendim quickly and speak with Calenglad. He is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir on the eastern shore.

'It is my dearest hope that we will meet again on a happier day, ${PLAYER}.''Laerdan and Golodir sent you, did they? There must be more than we thought to the growing presence of the Angmarim then. I am glad then that they have sent a proven hero to help.''Go and speak with Laerdan. It is urgent that you find Amarthiel.''You must do as Laerdan says. Hurry, for I deem time is short.''Calenglad is in Evendim at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir. The camp is along the eastern shore of Lake Evendim, on an island there. Hurry!'Calenglad has informed you that there has been a recent growth in the number of Angmarim outside of Annúminas.Calenglad is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir on the eastern shore of Lake Evendim.

Speak with Calenglad when you are ready to leave for Annúminas.Discover Amarthiel's plans at AnnúminasCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir on the eastern shore of Lake Evendim.

You should speak with Calenglad again, now that you have discovered Amarthiel's plans.'The Angmarim presence in Annúminas is most disturbing, and hearing the news you brought me, I think that is the best place to search for Amarthiel. She cannot yet have gone too deep into the ruined city, and we cannot let her go any further.

'I will let you bring five of my men with you. Whatever you do, you must come back with information about her plans. This is most urgent for the Dúnedain and for Eriador. We cannot let the Lidless Eye have any more influence in this region.

'Speak with me again when you are ready to leave.''This is grave news indeed. I will send word to Elrond of Rivendell and to Golodir my kinsman. We need help, and quickly, if Mordor is so deeply involved.

'Thank you for your help with this and for dispatching one of Amarthiel's Black Númenórean lieutenants. We have made a strike, but unless we follow it up with one more sure, Amarthiel will surely recover from it and seek to crush us utterly.''Are you ready to search for Amarthiel? My men have been ordered to protect you no matter the cost.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>Aragorn believes that Gandalf should be informed of the mysterious Sara Oakheart's theft of the palantír.Gandalf is in Bilbo's room on the first floor of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.

Aragorn has sent you to speak with Gandalf.Talk to Gandalf in Rivendell'Gandalf the Grey, currently in Bilbo's room on the first floor of the Last Homely House here in Rivendell, should be informed of the actions of this Sara Oakheart.  You say you have encountered her several times before?  Most curious.

'The theft of a palantír is no small matter, ${PLAYER}.  Few have knowledge of them; fewer still can use them with purpose and accuracy.  If this Oakheart is one of those few, her designs on such a powerful item bode very ill.

'Go now, and speak with Gandalf.''Aragorn has sent you?

'What's this you say?  The palantír, stolen?'The Red-maid is lost -- or so it seems -- to the corruption wrought upon her land at the hands of Men. These men stand before her, ready to sacrifice themselves for the Red-maid, and they deserve this fate... and yet the nobility of your blood will be a greater reward for her. When these Men fall willingly before her, she will know the difference between those who help to strengthen, and those who seek to destroy.You have returned to Garth Agarwen to defeat Naruhel, the Red-maid.<rgb=#66b3ff>Daily Reward -- Tier 1</rgb>Learn to identify the turning point in a foe's strength and strike.Strike with Merciful StrikeLearn to identify the turning point in a foe's strength and strike.Strike with Merciful StrikeHunward will be pleased to instruct you in the finer points of brawling, but he insists that you will need better equipment if you are to unlock your potential in the punching arts.Hunward at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood has agreed to fashion you fine equipment suitable for a legendary Brawler, if you will bring him the materials he needs.Complete 'Implements of Striking' for HunwardComplete 'Articles of Durability' for HunwardHunward is at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.Talk to Hunward at Trader's Wharf'You're going to need better equipment if you are to fulfil your potential as a master of the fine art of punching things, my new friend! But heed my warning, for the materials I will need to fashion you such articles and implements as these may not be easy to acquire. If you are to become the most feared Brawler of all, I know you will have little difficulty finding them.

'And if you don't, then perhaps you were not intended to stand apart from all the other mid-level Brawlers in this land. You will engage in a tavern fight here, a back alley brawl there, and you will wonder what might have been. Always you will wonder if you could have been more.

'With my help, you can be. Think it over, ${PLAYER}.''If you are to become the most feared Brawler of all, I know you will have little difficulty finding them. And if you don't, then perhaps you were not intended to stand apart from all the other mid-level Brawlers in this land. You will engage in a tavern fight here, a back alley brawl there, and you will wonder what might have been. Always you will wonder if you could have been more.

'With my help, you can be. Think it over, ${PLAYER}.''Let me congratulate you on your achievements, ${PLAYER}, for you have truly come into your own, and your fists will surely be feared by all those with whom you brawl!'

You thank Hunward for the fine equipment he fashioned for you and for his kind words, and you ask him how he came to study the art of brawling. He laughs.

'You would have expected a Man of Rohan to prefer fighting astride a horse? It is true, most of my kin much prefer it, but I choose to model myself after the most legendary Brawler of all. You have heard of Helm Hammerhand, of course. Know you how he was given that epithet? When he was insulted by Freca, in whose veins ran Dunlendish blood, Helm commanded that he step outside, for brawls were not permitted in the king's house.

'Freca was filled with fear, and well he might have been, for Helm was a man large and strong, and none of Freca's men were near enough to aid him. But he saw that Helm bore no sword, having left it within the hall, and that eased his mind. It should not have done, for Helm's fists were deadlier than any sword. He smote Freca a single blow from his fist, and that was his mortal injury.

'Helm truly stands apart, ${PLAYER}, as a legendary Brawler. Let us do what we can to prove ourselves worthy of his memory!'You are a light shadow flitting against the moon, only seen when you wish to be, a soft breeze on the night air, soon past.Sterling Proudfoot is in Buckland, west of the town of Bree, in Bree-land.

You have been told to speak with Sterling Proudfoot, a skilled burglar who likely has much to share about your chosen career.Meet Sterling Proudfoot for further Burglar trainingSterling Proudfoot is in Buckland, west of the town of Bree, in Bree-land.

You have been told to speak with Sterling Proudfoot, a skilled burglar who likely has much to share about your chosen career.As a Burglar, you have achieved such renown as to receive a summons from Sterling Proudfoot of Buckland.

You should seek Sterling Proudfoot to receive further training in your class.'It's a pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}. Not many burglars reach our level of skill, you know. If you ask me, that's a good thing -- less competition for the best treasure!'Your banner brings the flame of hope to the hearts of good people, and your name is praised by those who follow you into battle against the evils of the shadow.Dawn Stockard is in the town of Archet, north of Bree, in Bree-land.

You have been told to speak with Dawn Stockard, a great captain, to learn what troubles her.Meet Dawn Stockard to receive more Captain trainingDawn Stockard is in the town of Archet, north of Bree, in Bree-land.

You have been told to speak with Dawn Stockard, a great captain, to learn what troubles her.As a Captain, you have achieved such renown as to receive a summons from Dawn Stockard of Archet.

You should seek Dawn Stockard to receive further training in your class.'I am pleased to make your acquaintance, ${PLAYER}, but I must tell you that rumours of my troubles are greatly exaggerated. Nothing weighs heavily upon my mind at the moment, and I wonder at those who believe I am occupied by worries. Indeed, the rebuilding of Archet proceeds apace, and hope returns to the people here with every passing day.'You discovered the corpse of a slain Redhorn-goat, which Hjór took as a good sign that his friend may yet live, for the corpse was expertly skinned.Thorlák entered the Redhorn Gate in search of Durin's Tower in the eastern parts of the pass, upon Zirakzigil.

Hjór hopes that Thorlák has found some shelter in the upper reaches of the Redhorn Gate.Find ThorlákHjór is in Echad Dúnann, south-west of the Redhorn Gate.

You should return to Hjór and inform him of Thorlák's death.Talk to Hjór at Echad Dúnann'If the goat was killed recently, there is still a chance that Thorlák made camp, but is unable to return. Caradhras the Cruel can entangle even the hardiest explorers if they are not prepared.

'Return to the Redhorn Gate and search its northern reaches. Thorlák's supplies would almost certainly be spent by now if he was forced to seek shelter on the hard face of Zirakzigil.

'I can only hope that Thorlák is having a merry time, sitting among the ancient treasures next to a warm fire in Durin's Tower....'The body of the dwarf is frozen, its last moments of life preserved by the cold.  It would appear that Thorlák met his end in the peaceful embrace of slumber.'Thorlák is dead? This is grievous news ${PLAYER}, for he was a close friend, as true of heart as any dwarf could ask, and as tough as stone.

'Alas that he died for a fool's hope, for Durin's Tower is lost to us forever.''Search for Thorlák among the highest reaches of the Redhorn Gate.'Behind the wights and fell spirits of Imlad Balchorth, there are even greater terrors.Gaunt-men can be found in western Imlad Balchorth, west of Myrkworth.

Sigar has asked you to destroy the Gaunt-men in Imlad Balchorth.Defeat Gaunt-men in Imlad Balchorth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sigar is at Myrkworth, east of Imlad Balchorth.

Having killed the Gaunt-men as asked, return to Sigar in Myrkworth and tell him the deed is done.'You are a brave soul, but this next task I ask of you is no small achievment and requires the staunchest of allies! The fell spirits and wights of Imlad Balchorth are terrible, but pale in comparison to their masters.

'I will need you to make your way to the far western depths of Imlad Balchorth and hunt the Gaunt-men. They are responsible for this raising of the Dead and must be stopped if we are to escape this horrid place!

'Go west with your fellows and destroy this menace, then return to me!''Impressive! You are a great ${CLASS}, indeed, to accomplish such deeds. They will sing songs of you one day, I am sure of it!

'Thank you so very much. Perhaps soon I can return to my home.''Go west and find the Gaunt-men and destroy them. Hurry...and bring your friends!'Strike at the wickedness in the hearts of your enemies. Or the legs, or stomach, or wherever they keep their wickedness.Use Helm's HammerTales of your daring have spread throughout the lands of Middle-earth, and you are known as a mighty champion in roadside inns everywhere.Gwesgylliel is at Lin Giliath in Meluinen in the North Downs.

You have been told that the Elf-maiden Gwesgylliel, herself a mighty champion, desires to speak with you.Meet Gwesgylliel for further Champion trainingGwesgylliel is at Lin Giliath in Meluinen in the North Downs.

You have been told that the Elf-maiden Gwesgylliel, herself a mighty champion, desires to speak with you.As a Champion, you have achieved such renown as to receive a summons from Gwesgylliel at Lin Giliath in Meluinen.

You should seek Gwesgylliel to receive further training in your class.'I am pleased to meet you at last, ${PLAYER}, for your deeds travel ahead of you and speak well of your good heart and your strong arm. Our actions bring hope to those who have none, and that is the greatest gift that can be given.'Defeat the champions of Barad Gúlaran.Defeat AfraigDefeat CoblaithDefeat Castellan WisdánDefeat ForvengwathDefeat MúlvuirëDefeat UdúnionDefeat the champions of Carn Dûm.Defeat UrroDefeat BarashalDefeat HelchgamDefeat the champions of Carn Dûm.Defeat SálvakhDefeat AzgothDefeat AvalgaithDefeat TárlakhDefeat the champions of Carn Dûm.Defeat TârlugDefeat MormozDefeat RodakhanDefeat GúrthulDefeat MordirithYou have received a weapon from the Elder Days, discovered by the dwarves in a hidden cache, and you must now delve for its secrets.Wafi is in the Forging Hall of Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin.

Hundi has told you to show your new weapon to Wafi in Thorin's Hall. Wafi will be able to help determine the intrinsic characteristics of the weapon.Rósar the Forge-master is in the Forging Hall in Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin. He has the skill to identify the mysterious weapon you have acquired.

Wafi has instructed you to have Rósar the Forge-master identify your weapon so that you may understand its strength and potential.Bring the weapon to the Forge-master to be identifiedNow that your weapon has been identified, you must equip it if you wish it to enhance its worth.Equip your new weaponWafi is in the Forging Hall of Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin.

Rósar the Forge-master has identified your weapon, and you should now show it to Wafi.Wafi is in the Forging Hall of Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin.

Wafi has asked you to slot one of the Relics to your weapon in order to further customise its abilities.Slot a Setting Relic in your weaponWafi is in the Forging Hall of Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin.

Wafi has asked you to slot one of the Relics you have to your weapon in order to further customise its abilities, and is now waiting to speak with you.Talk to Wafi'Weapons of this make may have a long and storied history, ${PLAYER}. Its tale grows ever with the felling of evil foes -- the more servants of evil this weapon cuts down, the more deadly it becomes.

'Only a skilful few can read the tale of a weapon from its craftsmanship. I send you to one who can further aid you: the dwarf Wafi, in Thorin's Hall in the distant land of Ered Luin.

'Seek out Wafi by the great fires of the Forging Hall in Thorin's Hall. He can assist you in finding one who has some skill in reading the lineage and power of a weapon such as this.''Wafi is in the Forging Hall of Thorin's Hall itself, in Ered Luin. It is a long way from here, but there are very few who can read the strengths of a weapon from its make, and Wafi is one.''You have come a long way to be here, ${PLAYER}. What business could bring a doughty ${CLASS} such as yourself all the way from Hollin to Thorin's Hall?'

Wafi looks at the weapon and whistles his astonishment.

'This is a relic of the Old Days, to be sure! I fear I cannot identify the lineage and strengths of this weapon for you; it is ancient beyond my reckoning, learned though I may be in these matters.

'However, my kinsman Rósar, the Forge-master, will surely have more to say than I, for his knowledge is vast and exceeds my own. Show him the weapon, and he will give you an assessment of its strength and potential.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Legendary Items must be Identified by a Forge-master before they can be used. The process reveals certain strengths the weapon may have.</rgb>'My kinsman Rósar, the Forge-master, can identify weapons of this sort that you acquire during your travels, revealing their secret strengths and their potential for growth.''You must equip your new weapon if you wish to see its worth increase.''Incredible, ${PLAYER}! This weapon is truly mighty, and you are fortunate to have come into possession of such a thing! However, it is not strong enough to stand against the creature of which you speak. A thousand curses on its foul hide for keeping the dwarves from Moria!

'I see that you have a number of Relics. You should apply one of them to your weapon to further customise its abilities! Once you have done so, speak to me again.'

<rgb=#FF0000>There are four different types of Relics that you can slot from the Legendary Item panel: Settings, Gems, Runes, and Crafted. A weapon can have one of each type slotted at any given time.</rgb>'You should slot one of the Relics you have into your weapon, ${PLAYER}. Slotting Relics allows you to further customise your weapon's abilities and strengths.'

<rgb=#FF0000>There are four different types of Relics that you can slot from the Legendary Item panel: Settings, Gems, Runes, and Crafted. A weapon can have one of each type slotted at any given time.</rgb>'A good choice, ${PLAYER}! You will acquire more Relics as you adventure, and should feel free to customise your weapon with the appropriate Relic for each situation.

'This weapon is still not strong enough to defeat the Watcher in the Water, friend ${CLASS}, but it might become so. I will tell you how this might be.'You have received a weapon from the Elder Days that the dwarves discovered in a hidden cache, and you must now delve for its secrets.Dithalion is by the forges in Rivendell.

Hundi bid you to show your new weapon to Dithalion, an Elf of Rivendell who will be able to help you make use of your weapon.Talk to Dithalion by the forges in RivendellDithalion is at the Forges of Rivendell.Talk to Dithalion by the forges in RivendellDithalion is at the Forges of Rivendell.

You have inscribed a tracery into your weapon and should now speak with Dithalion.Talk to Dithalion by the forges in Rivendell'Weapons of this make may have a long and storied history, ${PLAYER}. Its tale grows ever with the felling of evil foes -- the more servants of evil this weapon cuts down, the more deadly it becomes.

'Only a skilful few can read the tale of a weapon from its craftsmanship. I refer you to one who can further aid you: the Elf Dithalion by the forges in Rivendell. He is wise and learned in many things, including the study of ancient weapons.

'If Dithalion cannot help you, he will surely know another who can descry the lineage and powers in a weapon of this artistry.''Dithalion will be by the forges in Rivendell, ${PLAYER}. It is a long way, but he may be able to glean some knowledge from your new weapon that will be of use to us.''You have come a long way to be here, ${PLAYER}. What business could bring a valiant ${CLASS} such as yourself here to the Forges of Rivendell?'

Dithalion looks at the weapon and grows still, his eyes wide in wonderment.

'This is a relic of the Elder Days, my friend! Such a weapon has an unmatched potential to grow in power, its storied legend growing along with your own!'

<rgb=#00FF00>- Legendary Items can be enhanced in a number of ways as you adventure in Middle-earth:

- Their base stats will increase along with yours as you level.

- They can be slotted with a wide assortment of traceries, and those traceries can be further enhanced by runes.

- As you adventure, you will find traceries and runes throughout the world. You can also obtain them by spending Ancient Script at the Word-hoard of Gobetham, located in the Last Homely House.</rgb>'I see that you have been given some traceries. You should apply one of them to your weapon to further customize its abilities! Once you have done so, speak to me again.'

<rgb=#00FF00>- There are a variety of traceries that can be added to your legendary item.

- Among them are Heraldries, Words of Power, Words of Mastery, and Words of Craft.

- They are slotted onto your items in much the same way as Essences.</rgb>'A good choice, ${PLAYER}! Inscribing traceries onto your weapon will enhance your skills, and will often help turn the tide of battle.

'This weapon is still not strong enough to defeat the Watcher in the Water, friend ${CLASS}, but it might become so. I will tell you how this may come to pass.'Diathalon wishes to see your weapon reforged anew.Snár the Forge-master can be found by the Forges of Rivendell.

Your weapon possesses hidden potential that can be unlocked by reforging at a Forge-master. This process increases the weapon's damage and reveals a weapon's potential.Talk to Snár the Forge-master at the Forges of RivendellDithalion is by the Forges of Rivendell.

Now that you have reforged the weapon, you should return to Dithalion to demonstrate its development.Ráthwald is at the crumbling arch near the camp of Echad Dúnann in Eregion.

Your weapon has become powerful indeed, perhaps powerful enough to use in battle with the Watcher before the Doors of Durin.'This ancient weapon can be reforged at the hands of a Forge-master allowing its power to increase to match the skill of its wielder.

'Once reforged, it may possess the strength to face the creature that lurks within the Black Pool, ${PLAYER}. You should bring it to the Forge-master for reforging, and mayhap your newly-refurbished blade will at last best the flesh of the cruel Watcher.

'Take this weapon to Snár and he shall reforge it anew, and then perhaps we shall see its true potential.'

<rgb=#00FF00>- As your character level increases, your weapon may be brought to a Forge-master to be reforged. 

- Reforging your weapon increases its power and may unlock additional tracery slots.</rgb>'Bring your weapon to the Forge-master for reforging, ${PLAYER}! Only in this way shall we learn if it will now be hardy enough to best the creature of the Black Pool.''That is quite a weapon you have found! If you wish to reforge it and increase its potential, speak to me again and I will see that it is done!

'But know this, friend: the true strength of this weapon will come from the one who wields it! I believe you now have what you need to best the foes that stand arrayed against you!''Now you understand your weapon's potential? Yes, it can now bear Heraldry!

'You must return to Hollin at once and show Ráthwald, the dwarf at the crumbling arch near Echad Dúnann, that you wield a great weapon. Surely it will give the dwarves of his company newfound hope.

'Go at once, friend! I deem that weapon has come forth from the very fibres of legend for this purpose.''Go to the camp of Echad Dúnann in Eregion at once and speak to Ráthwald. He must see the weapon you now wield and the power that it may have against the creature of the Black Pool!''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. Did that weapon of the Elder Days prove worthwhile, or was it a fruitless chase?'

Ráthwald's eyes widen in surprise.

'This weapon has become even more powerful in your hands, ${PLAYER}! Surely now we have the strength to stand against the horror in that foetid pool!'Your new weapon has the potential for worth beyond measure, but you must yet wield it in battle.Wafi is in the Forging Hall of Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin, and Dithalion is by the Forges of Rivendell.

Now that you have fought many foes with your new weapon, you should return to either Wafi or Dithalion to demonstrate your progress.'Weapons of such worth improve as they are used, ${PLAYER}. Only when they are wielded in battle can they achieve the true measure of their greatness.

'Use it against worthy foes, and it will improve as your own skills advance. When it has achieved a high measure of worth, bring it to me or the learned Wafi in Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin, and one of us will advise you on what must be done next.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Legendary Items gain experience as you fight experience-granting enemies with them. When such a weapon receives enough experience, it gains a level.</rgb>'Weapons of such worth improve as they are used, ${PLAYER}. Only when they are wielded in battle can they achieve the true measure of their greatness.

'Equip the weapon and use it against worthy foes, and it will improve as you do. When it has achieved a high measure of worth, bring it to me or the learned Dithalion in Rivendell, and one of us will advise you on what must be done next.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Legendary Items gain experience as you fight experience-granting enemies with them. When such a weapon receives enough experience, it gains a level.</rgb>'You have done very well, ${PLAYER}! Your weapon has advanced to an impressive level indeed!''You have done very well, ${PLAYER}! Your weapon has advanced to an impressive level indeed!'You have become proficient with a lost weapon of the Elder Days, and the dwarves of Bósi's expedition are confident that you can now stand against the Watcher in the Water.Ráthwald is at the ruined arch near Echad Dúnann, in Eregion.

Now that you have a weapon strong enough to harm the Watcher in the Water, Ráthwald is waiting to bring you to Bósi.Talk to Ráthwald and travel to face the WatcherRáthwald is at the ruined arch near Echad Dúnann, in Eregion.

You have driven away the Watcher in the Water and the dwarves have entered Moria at last.'This weapon may be what we need to drive off the Watcher in the Water, ${PLAYER}, and allow the dwarves to enter Moria!

'Speak to me when you are ready and I will bring you to Bósi and Brogur. They will be pleased to see there is hope again at last!''Are you ready? I will bring you to Bósi so that he may be heartened by the mighty weapon that has returned from the depths of time. This may be the advantage we need to wreak vengeance upon the Watcher in the Water for the death of Bróin and the other lives it claimed that day.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'The rest of the dwarves have entered Moria in search of fortune, ${PLAYER}, and we have you to thank for it!'The dwarves have entered Moria at last, but their work has just begun. You will need to assist them in their struggle if they are to find any success in the forgotten halls of Khazad-dûm.Tulk is just inside the Doors of Durin that stand by the still pool where you did battle with the Watcher in the Water.

You have been told to speak with Tulk about the dwarves that have entered Moria.'Tulk is waiting to speak with you just inside the Doors of Durin. You remember him, do you not? He is pleased that you proved such a boon to the expedition and will be delighted to speak with you again.''Tulk is just inside the Doors of Durin, waiting to speak with you.

'The Black Pool is empty now, and it seems to be safe, though still foetid. Tulk will tell you how you may continue to assist the Iron Garrison when you arrive inside Moria.''${PLAYER}, hello! Here we are, inside Khazad-dûm at last! There is a great deal to be done at the several camps we are establishing here, and you can help us to succeed at the mighty task before us!

'Bósi asked me to reward you for your leadership before the Doors. Take this with his thanks, and those of the entire Iron Garrison!'You have offered your services to the expedition of dwarves that has come to Hollin to reclaim the halls of Khazad-dûm beneath the mountains.Spying crebain can be found along the banks of the dried-up Sirannon, south-east of the ruined gate in the area near the Walls of Moria.

Tulk has asked you to defeat the spying crebain along the banks of the Sirannon and to bring him their talons, which can be put to various uses.Defeat spying crebain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect jagged talons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tulk can be found east of the ruined gate in the area near the Walls of Moria.

The dwarf Tulk awaits your return with the talons you collected from the spying crebain along the Sirannon.'We had not been here long before it became clear that some power was keeping a watchful gaze on Hollin. Filthy crebain have appeared in great numbers, spying on our efforts and troubling the workers. I do not know to what purpose news of our efforts may be put, but their presence has made Bósi uneasy, and that is enough for me.

'To the south, you can see where the Sirannon once flowed, but it has dried up and the stream-bed is now empty. Walk along the banks, defeating any of the spying crebain you see there, and bring me their talons. We can put those vile birds' claws to various uses.

'More importantly, though, you will be hindering whatever fell plan the master of these spies may be brewing for my kinsmen.''Look to the south along the banks of the dried-up Sirannon if you wish to find the spying crebain that have caused us so much trouble, ${PLAYER}. I do not know whom these filthy birds serve, but I do not believe that their master can mean us any good.''Thank you for this, ${PLAYER} -- not only for the talons, but for defeating agents of whatever power believes that the dwarves have no business here in Hollin, or in Khazad-dûm.'Tulk has asked you to bring a report to Bósi, the leader of the expedition of dwarves. Bósi's kin have come to Hollin purposing to enter Moria.Bósi is overseeing some of the waggons along the road through Hollin, south-east from the Hollin Gate and then bending to the north-east.

Tulk has given you a report to bring to Bósi, one of the dwarves leading the expedition to Hollin.'I've written a report for you to bring to Bósi, ${PLAYER}. Show him this document and he will determine how best to utilise your assistance.

'You will find Bósi near some of the waggons beyond the rocky outcropping to the south-east. Just follow the road as it bends around the outcropping and turns north-east.''If you follow the road south-east as it bends around the rocky outcropping you see there, you will find Bósi by the waggons as the road turns north-east.

'Bring him the report I gave you. He will find something for you to do to aid in our efforts here.''Thank you for bringing me this, ${PLAYER}, and also for your efforts on our behalf. Our work here has been going more slowly than we expected.

'My cousin Brogur and I determined to seek Balin within Moria some months ago, but it took many weeks to assemble an expedition of dwarves willing to accompany us. We chose a roundabout way over the mountains so as to speak with Lord Glóin, a close friend of our fathers, about Khazad-dûm.

'His words were grim; I do not think he believes that our expedition will succeed. 'It has been too long without word,' he said to us, 'for Balin son of Fundin to live still within the Mines.' I am beginning to perceive the likelihood of his warning, ${PLAYER}.Bósi has asked you to help re-supply the workers attempting to unearth the Hollin Gate with lunches in order to keep their spirits high.Dwarf-workers can be found north of Bósi's encampment, all along the winding road that runs up to the Hollin Gate.

Bósi has asked you to deliver lunches to the dwarves charged with unearthing the rubble in front of the Hollin Gate, and to then report to Wárr.The dwarf Wárr is at the Hollin Gate, supervising the workers there.

Now that you have delivered the lunches to the dwarf-workers along the road to the Hollin Gate, you should speak with Wárr for further engagement.Bósi is overseeing some of the waggons near the banks of the dried-up Sirannon, south of the road that winds up to the Hollin Gate.

Wárr has asked you to deliver a supply of broken pick-axes to Bósi and to request replacements.'When we arrived at the Hollin Gate some days ago, we found the Doors of Durin sealed by rubble and debris. Our road seems poorly chosen now; I wonder if the Dimrill Gate on the eastern side of the mountains is open.

'Dwarves of our expedition have been working to unearth the Gate, but it is lean and hungry work. Bring them these lunches so that they may harbour strength for the labours ahead.

Travel north up the slope between the rocky walls and you will find workers resting all along the path to the Hollin Gate, and there are more along the edge of the water before the Doors. Speak with Wárr at the Gate when you have done this, and he will have further tasks for you.''You've come at just the right time, ${PLAYER}. We're really going through pick-axes up here, and if we break any more it will hinder our progress in digging out the Hollin Gate.

'Bring these broken pick-axes back to Lord Bósi, and tell him that we'll need some replacements, and quickly, if we are to continue making good progress.

'You will find him near the bank of the Sirannon, south of the winding road that ends here at the Gate.''You're going the wrong way, friend; these stairs are blocked at the top by a stagnant pool. If you're looking for the road up to the Doors of Durin, you want to turn around. Keep the grey stone of the cliffs on your right, and follow it back the way you came, towards my uncle Bósi.

'If you follow the line of cliffs, keeping them on your right, you will find the road that winds up to the Doors.''Bring those lunches to the workers along the road north of here that winds up to the Hollin Gate. They will need the sustenance to maintain their strength.''Thank you for delivering those lunches. You should now speak with Wárr, supervising the work at the Hollin Gate.''Bring those pick-axes to Lord Bósi and request some replacements, or we will  have to abandon the work here at the Hollin Gate until we can make more tools.''Ah, thank you for this. I was afraid I might waste away without something to eat soon!

'We'll have unearthed the Hollin Gate before too long, but it's not easy work. We work in shifts in order to get the job done as efficiently as possible.''Hello there, and thank you for this lunch. My stomach was just beginning to grumble.

'My kinsmen are wondering what it is we'll find within Khazad-dûm: Lord Balin, alive and well? Great riches of mithril? Countless Orcs and goblins?

'I suppose we'll see, but I'm hoping for the mithril.''You have my thanks for the lunch, but I will have to eat it when my shift is done.

'We'll be through this rubble in no time. 'Tis odd, though; my pick tells me that this debris hasn't yet settled. I'd wager a waggonful of Moria-silver that this collapse happened recently.''Ah, a prepared lunch! Lord Bósi is doing a fine job keeping us fed and rested. We will repay both him and Lord Brogur with all of our strength, and be through this rubble in no time!

'What will we find beyond this Gate, I wonder?''This lunch will be just the thing to refresh me after my long labour, and I thank you for it.

'We would not have followed just anyone here to Hollin and the darkness of Khazad-dûm. Lords Bósi and Brogur are young, true, but they are stout of heart and their fathers earned great renown as part of Thorin's Company. This could be our chance to achieve glory of the same kind.''Thank you for this lunch. I will eat it in a moment.

'There is something about this lake I do not like, but I cannot figure out what it is. It makes me uneasy.''Thank you for the lunch. You are truly courageous to help us thus...or have you not yet heard the tale of Durin's Bane?

'At any rate, you have my thanks!''Oh, I see. These pick-axes are broken, which means that unless we can get replacements to Wárr, all work on excavating the Hollin Gate will be suspended. We have to do something about this, ${PLAYER}, and quickly!'Bósi has tasked you with collecting the materials necessary for producing new pick-axes to replace the ones broken by the dwarves at the Hollin Gate.Thick branches can be found at the base of trees in the area around the Hollin Gate. Bori is likely talking to his friend Bróin at the stairs east of Bósi.

Bósi has asked you to collect thick branches with which to make sturdy pick-handles and to help his son Bori with the task of gathering sharpening stones.Help Bori with the task Bósi gave himBósi is west of the stairs leading up to the foetid lake in front of the Hollin Gate.

Bósi is waiting to speak with you now that sufficient materials for new pick-axes have been gathered.'We had no way of knowing the Gate would be in this state, ${PLAYER}, and didn't think to bring extra pick-axes with us. Still, this area has many stout trees which should provide ample strong branches, perfect for pick-handles. We'll sharpen the metal heads ourselves and attach them to the new handles.

'I sent my son Bori to collect stones upon which we could sharpen our axes, but he has yet to bring me any. Gather branches from the bases of trees and help my son collect sufficiently sharp stones, and return to me when you have done both. Bori is probably wasting time with his friend Bróin at the stairs east of here. Those two care more for the spinning of tales than they do for working!''It is very important that we have the branches needed to repair the pick-axes. How else can we remove the rubble that blocks the Doors of Durin?''You have my thanks once again, ${PLAYER}. All the materials have been gathered, and my dwarves will begin working on new pick-axes right away.'Bori was charged with gathering suitable stones upon which to sharpen the pick-axes for workers at the Hollin Gate.Stones can be found along the dry bed of the Sirannon, but not every stone is suitably sharp.

Bori is waiting for you to bring him enough stones to sharpen the pick-axes needed by the workers unearthing the Hollin Gate.Collect sharp Eregion stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bori is at the base of the stairs that lead up to the foetid lake in front of the Hollin Gate. Stones can be found along the dry bed of the Sirannon, but not every stone is suitably sharp.

Bori is waiting for you to bring him enough stones to sharpen the pick-axes required by the workers unearthing the Hollin Gate.'Hello, ${PLAYER}. Did father send you to oversee on the charge he gave me? To tell you the truth, it hasn't been going very well.

'I was supposed to find suitable stones for sharpening the pick-axes for the workers at Hollin Gate, and I did find two of them, but then I got a little distracted. My friend Bróin and I have been discussing the treasures we might find within Moria, you see, and I lost track of the time.

'I'll give you these two stones I already found, if you like. Find the rest of them for me and I won't forget it! I had some luck looking along the dry bed of the Sirannon, but not every stone there is suitably sharp.''Look for stones along the dry bed of the Sirannon, but know that not every stone will be sharp enough for my father's purpose.''Perfect! These stones are just what my father wanted me to collect, and will surely sharpen our pick-axes to a fine point indeed.

'Bróin and I cannot wait to get into Moria proper; that is where the real glory awaits! I don't mean to look down upon the work everyone is doing out here, but the real adventure is waiting in the depths. Dangers unmeasured, I'll not doubt, but treasure in equal score, and honour, and renown!

'You have my thanks for your assistance, ${PLAYER}.'Bósi thanked you for your part in gathering materials for the crafting of new pick-axes, and sent you to Brogur so you may lend your aid to his cousin.Bósi's cousin Brogur is somewhere along the road that winds up to the Hollin Gate, north of Bósi's position.

Bósi has asked you to lend your aid to his cousin Brogur while the pick-axes are being crafted.'Bori is a good lad, and will grow into a fine dwarf. I reckon his preference for tale-spinning over hard work will pass in time. My cousin Brogur and I were no different when we were his age.

'It will take some time to fashion pick-axes from the materials you have delivered. While my dwarves are working on that, I ask you to lend your aid to Brogur. If you truly wish to assist the dwarves, not a moment shall be idly spent!

'You will find my cousin north of here, somewhere along the road that winds up to the Hollin Gate. He is gruff, even for his line, but will welcome your help.''Brogur is stern like his father before him, but respects strength and friendship. He will welcome your aid.

'Look for him north of here, along the road that winds up to the Hollin Gate.''What did you say your name was? ${PLAYER}?

'Is that even a real name? You'll need to work especially hard to make up for that!'Brogur's son Bróin has asked for your help fighting off the dangerous Shadow-wargs that lurk beyond the Sirannon's banks.Shadow-wargs can be found south of the stairs that lead up to the pool in front of the Hollin Gate, on the other side of the Sirannon's dry river-bed.

Bróin has somehow managed to foist his task off on you, and now you have to face the shadow-wargs in his stead.Defeat shadow-wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bróin is at the base of the stairs that climb up to the foetid pool in front of the Hollin Gate, east of Bósi's location.

You have defeated many shadow-wargs and should return now to Bróin.Talk to Bróin'You're the traveller who helped Bori with gathering those stones, aren't you? I thought so -- I have an eye for faces, and never forget a name, especially one belonging to an adventurer! Of course, the more dangerous deeds you accomplish, the more memorable you'll be, ${PLAYER}!

'That's what I'm hoping to do, you know. Once we get inside Khazad-dûm, Bori and I will become great heroes, and stories of our adventures will be told all over the land. Years from now, 'The Glorious Tale of Bróin the Mighty' could inspire young dwarves just as the songs of Durin and of Thorin Oakenshield inspire Bori and me today!

'If you'd like to help me with the task my father gave me, though, I wouldn't turn it down. There are shadow-wargs to the south, across the bed of the dried-up Sirannon. Defeat some of the beasts for me, if you would; I've already slain one of them, but that's not really enough. May good fortune be with you, friend!''I really appreciate this, ${PLAYER}. Your battles with the dangerous shadow-wargs are sure to be an important part of your tale.

'You'll find them south of here, on the other side of the Sirannon's dry river-bed.''You have returned, ${PLAYER}, and in victory over the shadow-wargs! You truly are an adventurer of great worth, are you not?

'In all honesty, my battle with that shadow-warg wasn't exactly worthy of song; I was too frightened to do more than survive. I guess I'm not much of a hero. Is it in me to do great deeds? Will there ever be a song sung about me, or will my name be forgotten?

'You are most kind, ${PLAYER}. I hope I will soon have the chance to prove myself as you have done.'Brogur is concerned about the unusually aggressive behaviour of the wolves in the area and wants them handled.The cause of the wolves' fearsome behaviour may be found among their lairs, south of Brogur's location and across the Sirannon's dry river-bed. Brogur believes the cave Filgogân may hold some clue to the wolves' madness, in the far south-western corner of the area. Bróin can be seen talking to Bori at the base of the stairs that climb to the pool in front of the Hollin Gate.

Brogur has asked you to search for the cause of the shadow-wolves growing madness, and to help his son Bróin with a task. When you have done each of these things, he told you to speak with his cousin Bósi.Find the cause of the wolves' madnessHelp Bróin with the task Brogur gave himBósi is south of Brogur's location, in view of the stairs that lead up to the pool in front of the Hollin Gate.

You have learned something of the Shadow-wargs' madness and aided Bróin with his task, and have been asked to speak now with Bósi.'Some madness has seized the wolves of this area, driving the creatures into blind fury. They are far more aggressive than is usual for their kind, and I fear they may attack our expedition before long.

'Can you hear their shuddering voices on the wind? I sent my son Bróin to challenge these beasts of Shadow, but he has not returned. He is probably wasting time with my cousin's boy, wagging his tongue by the stairway yonder.

'Return to the Sirannon's dry river-bed and climb the opposite bank whence the fell clamour comes. There is a cave, Filgogân, in the far south-west there. It could be that you will find some explanation for the creatures' wrath within that cave. I fear you must help my son with his task, for he has not yet spoken with me about its successful completion! Talk to my cousin Bósi when you're finished.''My son Bróin is probably wasting time by the stairs, idling away the hours with ceaseless chatter. The source of the shadow-wolves' madness is likely south of here, across the dry river-bed of the Sirannon. Perhaps you will find some clue in the cave Filgogân, in the south-western corner of this area?''You say you found a burned wolf-corpse on the other side of the Sirannon? I do not have the answer to this mystery, ${PLAYER}.

'While you were helping my cousin, the new pick-axes were finished. They are of very high quality and will surely be of great help at the Hollin Gate.'The dwarves of Bósi and Brogur's expedition await the opening of the Doors of Durin.Bósi is waiting at his small camp to travel with you to the Doors of Durin.

Bósi's dwarves have repaired the pick-axes, and now he wants you to bring them to the workers with him.Talk to Bósi and travel to the Doors of DurinRáthwald is outside the arch near the camp of Echad Dúnan, in Eregion.

The dwarves have retreated in disarray from the Doors of Durin, and must now plan for the uncertain future.'Let me know when you are ready, ${PLAYER}, and we will walk together to the Doors of Durin. With these newly-repaired pick-axes, our dwarves will soon clear the way into Moria.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: Once you complete this chapter, the Expedition will move into Moria, and any Expedition quests that remain in your quest log will be cancelled. If you have any Expedition quests underway you should complete them now, as those quests will no longer be available after this chapter is completed.</rgb>'We are in full retreat, ${PLAYER} -- the beast of the pool is too much for our meagre weapons!

'If only we had some relic of the old days, we might stand a chance against the creature. The weapons of our Fathers were of a stronger and keener make, their craft forgotten; today's forge-skill is lesser.

'A cache of weapons was discovered in one of the caves near here shortly after we arrived. Perhaps one of those will stand worthy as a bane to this monster.''Are you ready to leave? Let me know, and we shall walk together to the Doors of Durin.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: Once you complete this chapter, the Expedition will move into Moria, and any Expedition quests that remain in your quest log will be cancelled. If you have any Expedition quests underway you should complete them now, as those quests will no longer be available after this chapter is completed.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>The dwarves are desperate for some means of defeating the Watcher that waits in the Black Pool before the Walls of Moria.Hundi is at Echad Dúnann, not far to the west of Ráthwald, in Eregion.

Ráthwald has asked you to speak to his friend Hundi, who aided in the recovery of a cache of weapons that may prove useful.'We dare not approach our old camp until we find some way to defeat the creature in the Black Pool, ${PLAYER}. I cannot let you pass.

'A number of dwarves of our expedition are resting at Echad Dúnann, just to the west. Speak to Hundi there; he was instrumental in uncovering the cache of weapons of which I spoke.''Hundi is at Echad Dúnann, the camp just to the west there. Speak to him about the cache of weapons his team recovered from one of the caves of Eregion.''Ráthwald is right, my friend. Without a truly magnificent weapon forged in the ways of Old, we cannot hope to so much as score the flesh of that ancient creature.

'But legends of the past sometimes turn up when least expected. My friends and I found a cache of ancient weapons not long after the Iron Garrison came to this place. Select one of these weapons, and it may be that your choice will help us clear the way into Moria of that terrible creature.

'Take too this tracery to engrave upon your weapon, for I know of one who can help you understand the uses of these ancient relics.'The dwarves are desperate for some means of defeating the Watcher that waits in the Black Pool before the Walls of Moria.Hundi is at Echad Dúnann, not far to the west of Ráthwald, in Eregion.

