Isdi is waiting for you to return with the last set of components.'I can make you a weapon befitting the wisdom of an accomplished lore-master such as yourself, ${PLAYER}. I surely need not tell you that the road to its completion will not be easy -- you are wise enough to know that will be the case.

'However, I must ask you to bring me the components that I will need for its making. Do not fear the difficult road, for that way lies satisfaction.

'First, I will need the staves of the Corcur, who are encamped near Helegrod in the Misty Mountains, and the rending-claw of the great bear Driftclaw who roams the land of the giants in the Misty Mountains.''Corcur may be found near Helegrod, ${PLAYER}, while the bear Driftclaw roams the land of the giants, both in the Misty Mountains.''I thank you for these components, ${PLAYER}, and am sure you will have little difficulty returning with the second set.

'Next, I will need the eyes of such worms as may be found in Forochel, Eregion, and the Misty Mountains. I will also need the putrid fingernails of the wights which roam Imlad Balchorth in Angmar.''Wights can be found among the tombs of Imlad Balchorth, in Angmar, while worms roam Forochel, Eregion, and the Misty Mountains.''These will do nicely, ${PLAYER}, and will improve the bite of the weapon I am making for you.

'One set of components remains, and these will be found within the very heart of the land of Angmar. Keep your wits about you, as I am sure you will, and you will have victory.

'I need you to seek out the uruk Morthrâng of Carn Dûm and obtain from him an Emblem of Ritual. Also at Carn Dûm, you should seek out the Man of Angmar known as Sálvakh and wrest from him his Rune of Evil Presence.''Now we come to it, ${PLAYER}. You may find both Morthrâng and Sálvakh at Carn Dûm in Angmar.''I am not surprised that you have returned victorious, ${PLAYER}, for I know you to be a lore-master of unsurpassed skill and knowledge.

'I bow to your wisdom and give to you this weapon. May it serve you well!'Aelindil at Tornhad has agreed to help you fashion a weapon worthy of your skill as a Mariner.Aelindil has asked you to collect Throghásh's cask of fire-oil at Eitheldir and also a number of steel water-flasks carried by half-orcs and brigands in the Angle of Mitheithel.Collect Throghásh's cask of fire-oilCollect steel water-flasks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.Bloated brimstone-leeches may be found in Eastern Malenhad and Duvuinen in Angmar. Dread-turtles may be found in Malenhad in Angmar.

Aelindil has asked you to bring him venomous dread turtle beaks and corrosive droplets.Collect venomous dread turtle beaks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect corrosive droplets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.Helchgam can be found at Carn Dûm in Angmar. Dafrim, Gríshakrum, and Kughûrz can all be found in Urugarth in Angmar.

Aelindil has asked you to bring him a bloodstained tally sick and the putrid slime of Helchgam.Collect the putrid slime of HelchgamCollect a bloodstained tally stickAelindil can be found at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.'I wonder, ${PLAYER}. Is not a weapon yet another tool of navigation? It is true enough that one can guide you to the end of conflict or conversation.

'I can fashion for you a fine weapon, one befitting a Mariner of your skill, but first, I will need you to bring me a number of materials. I must warn you, though. This shall be no simple task, my friend.

'For your first task in this trial, I shall require two materials. First, I will need a cask of the foul fire-oil carried by the Orc, Throghásh, who roams near the ruins of Eitheldir, and second, I have need of a number of the steel water-flasks carried by half-orcs and brigands here in the Angle of Mitheithel. Despite our best efforts, they have maintained an encampment in the ruins of Thelgarth, so it will not be difficult to find them.

'After you have brought those to me, I will task you to find materials that must be gathered further afield, in less hospitable lands.''For your first task in this trial, I shall require two materials. First, I will need a cask of the foul fire-oil carried by the Orc, Throghásh, who roams near the ruins of Eitheldir, and second, I have need of a number of the steel water-flasks carried by half-orcs and brigands here in the Angle of Mitheithel. Despite our best efforts, they have maintained an encampment in the ruins of Thelgarth, so it will not be difficult to find them.

'After you have brought those to me, I will task you to find materials that must be gathered further afield, in less hospitable lands.''Very good, ${PLAYER}. These will do nicely, but there is more to be done yet!

'For the next materials I require, you will need to travel to the lands of Angmar. I must ask you to gather several beaks from the venomous dread-turtles of Malenhad, and you must also bring me a collection of corrosive droplets from the brimstone-leeches that dwell amongst the befouled waters of Duvuinen.''For the next materials, you will need to travel to the lands of Angmar. I must ask you to gather several beaks from the venomous dread-turtles of Malenhad, and you must also bring me a collection of corrosive droplets from the brimstone-leeches that dwell amongst the befouled waters of Duvuinen.''Well done, my friend! Now, there are still two more items I require, and these shall be the most challenging of all.

'For each of these final materials, you must again travel to the land of Angmar—to Urugarth and Carn Dûm. For the first, you will need to seek out the fearsome Orcs known as Dafrim, Gríshakrum, and Kughûrz in Urugarth. Word of their cruelty and prowess in battle has spread among the Dúnedain, and it is said that they delight in tallying a count of those they have slain by carving a notch into crude sticks. If you can best them in combat, collect one of their bloodstained tally sticks and bring it to me in Tornhad.

'As for the second, that is a most dangerous task. It is said that the beast Helchgam can be found in the sewers beneath the dread city of Carn Dûm, but I am afraid there is only one way to procure the putrid slime of Helchgam, and that will mean putting an end to it.''For the final materials I need, you must again travel to the land of Angmar. Dafrim, Gríshakrum, and Kughûrz are fearsome Orcs of Urugarth. Word of their cruelty and prowess in battle has spread among the Dúnedain, and it is said that they delight in tallying a count of those they have slain by carving a notch into crude sticks. If you can best even one of them in combat, collect a bloodstained tally stick and bring it to me in Tornhad. It is said that Helchgam can be found in the sewers beneath the dread city of Carn Dûm, but I am afraid there is only one way to procure the putrid slime of Helchgam, and that will mean putting an end to it.''You return triumphant, ${PLAYER}!

'I bow to your skill, for none but the most seasoned Mariner could finish the many tasks I set before you, let alone overcome the dread-beast Helchgam in its foul cistern.

'You have proven yourself a most worthy Mariner, my friend, and so it is my honour to present you with this weapon. May it will serve you well in your journeys!'Baillindiel has agreed to help you craft a weapon that will help you fulfill your duties as a minstrel of great renown.Narglup roams Fasach-larran in Angmar. Rock-worms dwell in the Misty Mountains.

Baillindiel asked you to bring her chipped rock-worm fangs and the blunted tooth of the Warg Narglup.Collect Narglup's blunted toothCollect chipped rock-worm fangs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Baillindiel is at the Elf-harbour of Celondim, in Ered Luin.

Baillindiel is waiting for you to return with the first set of components.Brimstone-slugs can be found in Angmar. Wargs can be found in Angmar and Eregion. Bats can be found in Angmar and Moria.

Baillindiel asked you to bring her corrosive droplets, splintered Warg-claws, and grisly bat-talons.Collect corrosive droplets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect splintered Warg-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect grisly bat-talons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Baillindiel is at the Elf-harbour of Celondim, in Ered Luin.

Baillindiel is waiting for you to return with the second set of components.Morthrâng may be found in Urugarth. Mormoz and Azgoth dwell in Carn Dûm.

Baillindiel asked you to return with an Emblem of Ritual and a Rune of Winged Dominance.Collect Emblem of RitualCollect Rune of Winged DominanceBaillindiel is at the Elf-harbour of Celondim, in Ered Luin.

Baillindiel is waiting for you to return with the last set of components.'The way of the minstrel is not free of danger, ${PLAYER}, a truth that you have surely come to realize. To combat that danger, you need a weapon that you can rely on. I can fashion you such a weapon.

'As with all tales worth hearing, the tale of this weapon will be fraught with hardship and toil. You will look back upon the road you have walked, when all is done, and know that it was worth the journey, ${PLAYER}. Of this, I am certain.

'I must ask you to gather the items I will need to make this weapon and to give it the strength to counter our hated foes. The first set of components I will need includes the blunted tooth of the Warg Narglup, who ranges Fasach-larran in Angmar, and the fangs of the rock-worms of the Misty Mountains.''Look for the Warg Narglup in Angmar, ${PLAYER}, and the rock-worms in the Misty Mountains.''You have succeeded admirably to this point, ${PLAYER}. I will make use of these components in the fashioning of this weapon.

'I also have need of the corrosive droplets of the brimstone-slugs of Angmar, claws from Wargs, such as those in Angmar and Eregion, and talons of the bats which pervade Angmar and Moria.''I believe you will find everything I need in Angmar, though you may also find Warg-claws in Eregion and bat-talons in Moria.''I am glad to see you return, ${PLAYER}, and with the components I need if I am to make your weapon as strong as it deserves to be. I thank you.

'Your final task will be your most challenging and song-worthy! I need you to obtain for me an Emblem of Ritual from the uruk Morthrâng in Urugarth and a Rune of Winged Dominance from the merrevail Mormoz and Azgoth in Carn Dûm.''The uruk Morthrâng dwells within the walls of Urugarth, and the merrevail Mormoz and Azgoth can be found in Carn Dûm.''I am delighted at your return, ${PLAYER}! I know that the tale of your bravery and courage in the acquisition of these items must be a thrilling one! Allow me to make use of them in the fashioning of this weapon for you...and it is done.

'I give you this weapon with the certainty that it will serve you well and faithfully as you bring hope to the Free Peoples of Middle-earth. I count you among my friends, ${PLAYER}, and hope that you do the same.'Hunward at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood has agreed to fashion you a fine set weapons for your fists.Hunward has asked you to find toughened Huorn bark and Wildwood Orc knives from creatures in the Wildwood.Collect toughened Huorn bark (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Wildwood Orc knives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hunward is at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.Worms may be found in Forochel and Angmar. Dread-turtles may be found in Malenhad in Angmar.

Hunward asked you to bring him clouded worm eyes and venomous dread turtle beaks.Collect clouded worm eyes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect venomous dread turtle beaks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hunward is at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.Barashal may be found at Carn Dûm in Angmar. Gruglok is at Urugarth in Angmar.

Hunward asked you to bring him a crimson Gorthorog-horn and a Sigil of War.Collect crimson Gorthorog-hornCollect Sigil of WarHunward is at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.'Many are the folk who underestimate the might of a good Brawler. "Where is your sword or your spear?" they ask, only to learn we have no need of such weapons, to their sorrow.

'I will fashion you a fine set of battle-gauntlets, but I will need you to bring me a number of materials. Know that this will not be easy! I will use some of these items to craft your weapons, but others of them will be used to prove that you are deserving of such equipment! So it was for me, and so it will be for you.

'First I will need toughened Huorn bark from the Huorns that stalk the Wildwood, and Wildwood Orc knives from the Orcs in this land. Bring them to me and I will task you to find materials that must be gathered further afield, in more dangerous places.''First I will need toughened Huorn bark from the Huorns that stalk the Wildwood, and Wildwood Orc knives from the Orcs in this land. Bring them to me and I will task you to find materials that must be gathered further afield, in more dangerous places.''These will do nicely! The next materials I need you to gather will bring you further afield, to places of greater danger. I speak of the snowy wastes of Forochel, and of the dread land called Angmar.

'Bring me the clouded eyes of worms such as dwell in Forochel and Angmar. I will also need the beaks of the dread-turtles that crawl in Angmar alone. Beware their hard shells, and see that your punches find only the soft meat within!''Bring me the clouded eyes of worms such as dwell in Forochel and Angmar. I will also need the beaks of the dread-turtles that crawl in Angmar alone. Beware their hard shells, and see that your punches find only the soft meat within!''Well done, my friend! These materials are just what I sought. But there are two more items I will need, and you may find the collection of them most taxing!

'Barashal the Gorthorog and Gruglok of Urugarth are fearsome opponents. From Barashal, collect a crimson Gorthorog-horn. He is to be found at the dread city of Carn Dûm. You will gain from Gruglok at Urugarth a Sigil of War, if you are able to best him in combat.''Barashal the Gorthorog and Gruglok of Urugarth are fearsome opponents. From Barashal, collect a crimson Gorthorog-horn. He is to be found at the dread city of Carn Dûm. You will gain from Gruglok at Urugarth a Sigil of War, if you are able to best him in combat.''I never doubted you for a moment, ${PLAYER}! Well done indeed, and in return for your fine efforts I give to you these battle-gauntlets. May they serve you well wherever your adventures take you!

'Your opponents will come to fear each of your strikes, for they will be deadlier than ever before!'Fenton Marshley has agreed to help you fashion a weapon worthy of your great skill as a hunter. The tale of this weapon will be one of danger and evil, but from these hardships will come strength.Men of Angmar may be found in Fasach-falroid and near Malenhad in Angmar. Driftclaw may be found in the Misty Mountains, where the giants dwell.

Fenton Marshley asked you to bring him one of Driftclaw's razor-sharp claws and the corroded Iron Crown staves carried by the evil Men of Angmar.Collect Driftclaw's razor-sharp clawCollect corroded Iron Crown staves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fenton Marshley is at the Hunting Lodge east of Archet and north of Bree, in Bree-land.

You have collected the first set of components Fenton Marshley has asked you to bring him.Worms may be found in Forochel and Angmar. Dread-turtles may be found in Malenhad in Angmar. Wights roam Imlad Balchorth in Angmar.

Fenton asked you to bring him clouded worm-eyes, venomous dread-turtle beaks, and putrid fingernails.Collect clouded worm-eyes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect venomous dread-turtle beaks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect putrid fingernails (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fenton Marshley is at the Hunting Lodge east of Archet and north of Bree, in Bree-land.

