Dawn Stockard is waiting for you to return with the last set of components she needs for the weapon she will make for you.'I can make you a weapon that befits your impressive stature as a captain, ${PLAYER}, but I warn you that its making will be fraught with danger. As with all things of worth, the road to it will be hard and long, but you will surely look back on it with satisfaction.

'I need you to venture forth and bring me the materials needed to craft your weapon. The first items are some knives from the Snowreap goblins who dwell in the Misty Mountains and the jagged blade of the Orc Fakhthal, who commands the Orcs of Fasach-falroid in Angmar.

'Bring these items to me, and I will begin my work.''The Snowreap goblins dwell in the Misty Mountains, while Fakhthal commands the Orcs of Fasach-falroid in Angmar.''Look for spiders in Angmar and Helegrod in the Misty Mountains, worms in places like Forochel, the Misty Mountains, Sarnur in Ered Luin, and Eregion, and barghests at Fornost and Haudh Iarchith.''Dushkâl, Brízrip, and Thordragh may be found at Urugarth in Angmar, and uruks may be found at Carn Dûm, also in Angmar.''My heart is glad to see you again, ${PLAYER}, and to see that you have ended Fakhthal. His debt to me is now paid.

'The knives of the Snowreap are a valuable bounty, as well, and they will lend their bite to the weapon I make for you.

'These are but the first components I need, however. Next you should find for me worm-eyes such as those found in Forochel, the Misty Mountains, Sarnur in Ered Luin, or Eregion, spider-spinnarets from the spiders of Angmar and Helegrod in the Misty Mountains, and paws from the barghests of Fornost and Haudh Iarchith.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. I delight to see you return to Archet and with the components for which I asked!

'One set of components remains, and these will be the most dangerous for you to acquire. I need the teeth of a Gorthorog, which can be acquired from Dushkâl, Brízrip, or Thordragh in Urugarth, and a Medallion of Passage from the uruks guarding Carn Dûm.''You return from out of the darkness, ${PLAYER}, and I salute you for it! Take this weapon with my highest regards, for you are truly a mighty Captain of Men!'Continue your study of ancient signs and the power they represent.Strike with Sign of Battle: Wizard's FireContinue your study of ancient signs and the power they represent.Strike with Wizard's Frost, Fire, or SparkTrain yourself to diminish your appearance in the eyes of your foe.Use Song of SoothingSaija has promised to guide you in your search for Narchuil.Speak to Saija inside of Halla-kolo.Talk to SaijaSearch Halla-kolo for the ring Narchuil.Search for NarchuilProtect SaijaSearch Halla-kolo for the ring Narchuil.Search for Narchuil'We must hurry if we are to find your ring, ${PLAYER}.'Glorfindel has summoned you to a final council at which the fate of Narmeleth will be decided.Attend the final council.Attend the final councilSpeak with Glorfindel to return to Rivendell.Talk to Glorfindel'We must return to Rivendell, ${PLAYER}.''Are you ready to depart?'Calenglad has asked you to find Amarthiel and discover her plans. He has sent you to Annúminas with five Rangers to help fight off the Angmarim.Speak with the Ranger protector before you search for Amarthiel.Talk to the Ranger protector standing before youFind Amarthiel and discover her plans.Find and stop AmarthielYou must defeat the Black Númenórean.'We must return to Tinnudir, ${PLAYER}. I fear that Amarthiel has won this hour. We must plan our next move, and quickly, so her victory will be short-lived!''Hurry, they were ready for us. We must push through if we are to find Amarthiel before it is too late! Follow us!'You have learned that Laerdan was not slain and was kept in Barad Tironn for questioning.Enter Barad Tironn and speak to Forchon.Enter Barad Tironn and find Laerdan.Find LaerdanWait for Forchon in Barad Tironn'We must leave quickly before our presence is known, ${PLAYER}.''We have arrived safely, but I fear that the Enemy may be close upon our heels.'Workers of Bósi and Brogur's expedition have nearly unearthed the rubble blocking the Hollin Gate, and the time is nigh to enter Khazad-dûm.Bósi is standing on the slope that winds past the small dwarf-outpost in view of the still pool.

