The Hollin Gate is nearly opened, and the dwarves prepare to enter the mines.Wait for more dwarves to arriveBósi is on the edge of the pool outside the Hollin Gate, with the rest of the dwarves of his expedition.

The Hollin Gate is nearly opened, and the dwarves prepare to enter the mines, but something has made you uneasy.Talk to BósiSomething, or many somethings, are lurking in the waters of the pool!Remain on your guardThe small outpost is on the other side of the pool, where you defended Bósi from attacking shadow-wolves.

The dwarves are attempting to fight off the mysterious creature that lurks now outside the Walls of Moria. Bósi has ordered you to hurry to the small outpost to seek help for the desperate dwarves.Return to the small outpost and get helpBósi is at the small outpost where you fought the shadow-wolves, on the other side of the menacing pool.

The dwarves are in full retreat from the mysterious creature in the pool, and you should speak to Bósi before the expedition turns into a rout.Talk to Bósi'We will stop at the outpost here for a moment before continuing on to the gates, ${PLAYER}. We will need to establish a camp once we are inside the mines, and I want to ensure that everything is prepared.

'You still have the pick-axes, yes? Good. Follow me.''What is it, ${PLAYER}? You say you saw something stir out in the water? What was it?

'I don't see anything now. Are you sure you didn't imagine it?''You have been a great help to us in our work here in Hollin, ${PLAYER}, and I know that you will be a great boon once we are inside Khazad-dûm proper.

'I would hereby be honoured if you would bear a pick-axe and help us to clear away the remainder of this rubble that blocks the Doors of Durin. This is an historic opportunity, friend ${CLASS}, and it is my joy to offer it to you in return for the many services you have given us already.''Did you see how the flesh of that creature deflected our blows, ${PLAYER}? We need more than ordinary weapons if we wish to stand against the Watcher of the Black Pool!

'It waited in the depths, watching as we strove to open the doors, and struck just as we were most vulnerable. Curse its foul hide for taking Bróin, and many other fine dwarves beside!

'They will be avenged, but for now we must retreat. We cannot hope to enter the Doors while it lurks before them.''Those pick-axes will be a great help, ${PLAYER}, even if you took your time bringing them here. Our workers are almost through the rubble already!

'Don't worry about that; what's done is done. I'm more concerned with this pool -- there's something about it I don't like. It makes me feel uneasy.

'Some of my dwarves have been casting stones into the water, and I'd appreciate it if you could get them to stop. It makes me nervous.''Very good, ${PLAYER}. I appreciate your help. I understand that many of my dwarves are restless, but there's just something about that water I don't like. I will be relieved when the workers have finished removing the rubble from in front of the gate and we can leave this unpleasant shore.''The crate for the pick-axes is just to the south there, next to Lord Brogur. You can leave them there.''You'll find Wárr at the rubble blocking the Hollin Gate. Bring him the repaired pick-axes and tell him I will be along shortly.''This is hard work, to be sure, but years from now you will be pleased to remember the hand you had in opening the way to Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Help us to clear away some of the rubble blocking the Gate, and never will you forget your part in the great deeds that are to come.''We must retreat with what survivors remain. We will return to visit our vengeance upon the Watcher in the Black Pool!''Certain of the workers are casting stones into the pool, and I want you to tell them not to disturb the water. There's something about this pool that makes me uneasy.

'You think I am overreacting? Let us hope so.''I don't like this, ${PLAYER}; something is wrong. The air is too still and quiet.''Very good. These pick-axes look to be in good shape, and will be a great asset as we finish unearthing the last of this rubble.

'You can leave them in that crate to the south there, right next to Lord Brogur.'Listen to Narmeleth's story of how she became Amarthiel, Champion of Angmar.Narmeleth has asked you to come with her, as she has someone very special for you to meet.Follow NarmelethProtect NarmelethNarmeleth has asked you to come with her, as she has someone very special for you to meet.Follow NarmelethProtect NarmelethProtect LaerdanNarmeleth has asked you to come with her, as she has someone very special for you to meet.Follow NarmelethLothrandir, a Ranger of the North, has joined you in your quest to find a lost Arnorian treasure in Forochel. Your only hope of finding it may lie with the shade of Arvedui, last King of Arthedain.You have arrived at the shipwreck of the Thoroval.

You should talk to Lothrandir.Talk to LothrandirLothrandir is speaking with Arvedui at the shipwreck of the Thoroval.

You should listen to the conversation.Listen to the conversationThe Angmarim have launched an ambush!

You should defeat the Angmarim attackers!Defeat the AngmarimLothrandir is speaking with Arvedui at the shipwreck of the Thoroval.

You should listen to the conversation.Listen to the conversation'I believe we have a lead! Let us consider our next steps.''We have arrived. It is time to speak with King Arvedui.'You have entered Minas Maur in search of Prakhum, the emissary of Goblin-town.You must defeat Prakhum, the emissary of Goblin-town, in order to retrieve some of Golodir's equipment.Defeat PrakhumYou have entered Minas Angos in search of Laugi Goldentongue, the emissary of the Dourhands.You must defeat Laugi Goldentongue, the emissary of the Dourhands from the Blue Mountains, in order to retrieve some of Golodir's equipment.Defeat Laugi GoldentongueYou have entered Minas Agar in search of Karstíona, the emissary of the Trév Duvárdain.You must defeat Karstíona, the emissary of the Trév Duvárdain from western Angmar, in order to retrieve some of Golodir's equipment.Defeat KarstíonaYou have entered Minas Caul in search of Bâlak, the emissary of the White Hand.You must defeat Bâlak.Defeat BâlakHalf of Narchuil has been recovered, and you must attend a council called by Elrond to discuss the fate of the ring and to consider Laerdan's actions.Attend the Council of Narchuil.Attend the Council of Narchuil'The council can not continue without Laerdan. I will speak with you privately in my library ${PLAYER}.'Laerdan is being held captive in Sammath Baul.Enter Sammath Baul and find Laerdan.Find LaerdanLaerdan is nearly unconscious and wounded.  He must be taken to Rivendell to Elrond for you doubt that he will survive without his aid.You have travelled deep into Carn Dûm with Golodir, into the very fortress of the Witch-king himself. Here Golodir hopes to confront Mordirith and shatter the Iron Crown forever.Aid Golodir as you make your way deeper into the Castle of the Witch-king.Speak to GolodirWith the light of Dúnachar, Golodir has defeated Mordirith, although the villain escaped before he could be completely defeated. You should speak with Golodir to see what he would wish you to do.Talk to GolodirYou should speak with Golodir at once.Talk to Golodir'We should tarry here no longer. Are you prepared to leave? I will show you the secret ways out of Carn Dûm and back to Gath Forthnír.''It seems my long imprisonment in Carn Dûm has served us well. We have come far into the the Witch-king's keep unnoticed. It would be folly to think, though, that our fortune will hold. Already, Mordirith may be aware of our presence.

'Steel yourself for the battle ahead. I have few words of advice to offer you, other than to warn you that Mordirith is a master of trickery and illusion. He will try to break your resolve with his words. Do not let him! Keep to your hope and trust your companions.

'Shall we go now?''Mordirith the coward has escaped us... but did you notice that the blade of Dúnachar was still lodged within his breast? I wager the pain of that blade's light shall be a constant reminder of the evil he has committed.

'While my revenge is not yet complete, I would wager there will be others who will complete this task. For now, I can take solace in this fact...

'A moment, someone approaches!''What an unsettling end to our battle. I fear that there is much more to that old woman than what we see upon the surface.

'However, we cannot deal with that matter now. We should leave here before we are overrun with Angmarim or their servants!'Calenglad has decided to confront Mordrambor and learn if he knows anything about Narchuil.Calenglad is inside the keep on Tinnudir.

You have entered the keep on Tinnudir to confront Mordrambor, the imprisoned Black Númenórean.Calenglad is inside the keep on Tinnudir.

You and Calenglad have entered the keep on Tinnudir to confront Mordrambor, the imprisoned Black Númenórean.Confront Mordrambor with CalengladTadan is inside the room atop the stairs, where Mordrambor was being held prisoner.

The Black Númenórean has escaped from his prison, and there is no sign of his jailor.Find TadanCalenglad is inside the keep on Tinnudir.

Mordrambor has escaped, and in his wake, he has left the dead and the dying.'We must repair the damage done to the keep, but there can be no cure for some of these hurts.''Let us meet with Mordrambor, ${PLAYER}. We have much to say to him... and to hear, I expect.

'We will need to be on our guard. Let us learn from Laerdan's folly, and our own: even in captivity, a Black Númenórean may cause much trouble.''${PLAYER}... it was Tann Morgul. I kept meaning to bring it... to Calenglad... but....

'Mordrambor... his sorceries....''Mordrambor is gone, ${PLAYER}, and he leaves many of my people dead or dying. It seems that he wove cruel sorceries within the mind of his jailor: how often did Tadan resolve to bring Tann Morgul to me, only to have the matter slip from his memory? It is clear that this relic of evil gave to our prisoner some measure of the power he sought.

'Nay! Do not blame Tadan for this! Any of us could have done this. His was a dangerous duty, and he has come now to the end of his service. Weep for him, but do not lay the blame at his feet! It belongs with Angmar and its cruel servants alone.'Sara Oakheart has asked you to speak with her and would like you to follow her as she tells you her story.Follow Sara Oakheart into the heart of Barad Gúlaran.Talk to Sara OakheartFollow Sara Oakheart into the heart of Barad Gúlaran.Follow Sara Oakheart deeper into Barad Gúlaran'Thank you for helping me this one last time. I do not think I could make it on my own, being the frail old woman I am. You have done much for me -- more, perhaps, than you will ever know. I cannot begin to thank you for your services.

'Come let us see what can be found here. I do not think anyone will trouble us.'The last hope to defeat Mordirith, the False King of Angmar, is a final assault on him in his stronghold of Gador Gúlaran.Journey with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.Talk to NarmelethJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.Follow NarmelethJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.Talk to NarmelethJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.Defeat MordramborJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.Talk to NarmelethJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith.Talk to Narmeleth when you have readied yourselfSpeak to Narmeleth.

With the last of her strength, Narmeleth drove the broken blade into the chest of Mordirith. His crumpled form lies near the collapsed form of Narmeleth.Speak to NarmelethHer life spent defeating Mordirith, the lifeless form of Narmeleth lies before you. Her face, once wracked with guilt and sorrow, is now at peace.

You should now return to Gath Forthnír to let them know all that has transpired.'We must hurry, with Narchuil reforged it will not be long before all of Eriador is overrun.''Are you ready to continue, ${PLAYER}?''We must hasten if we are to take Mordirith unawares.''Let us end this, ${PLAYER}.''It is done... Mordirith's spirit is gone, thrown into the void... never to return... I fear, though, it has cost me what grace remained within me and my time here in this Middle-earth is ending....

'Nay... do not weep! I would gladly pay this price again. I now can leave these shores knowing that I have helped, in a small way, push back... the darkness I served for so very long. Soon, I will see my mother... my father....'You have travelled with Muildir to the ruins of Delossad to search for answers to the mystery of Narchuil's past.Muildir is hiding by the entrance of Delossad.

Muildir is waiting to speak with you before you investigate the ruins of Delossad.Talk to MuildirSome Angmarim have returned to the outskirts of Delossad to search the ruins.

Muildir has told you of the Angmarim that lurk outside Delossad and wants you to defeat them before you search inside.Defeat Angmarim at Delossad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Muildir is hiding by the entrance of Delossad.

