You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.Examine unusual items within DelossadYou have encountered Mordrambor within the depths of Delossad, and he has locked you within one of the cells where Amarthiel was imprisoned.

Muildir has come to your aid and will free you from the cell.'Let us leave this place. Memory hangs on its stones like a shroud and fills me with unease.''Hearken, ${PLAYER} -- many of the Angmarim that came to Tâl Bruinen are searching elsewhere, but some of them have returned to search the ruins.

'Defeat those that you find here and return to me before you search inside. I do not want them to see you opening the door.''Most of the Angmarim have gone to search other parts of Tâl Bruinen, but a few have returned here. Defeat them with caution, and then return to me. I do not want them to see you open the door.''Very good, ${PLAYER}. Your exploration of the ruins should now be uninterrupted. A word, though, before you try the door again, my friend: Delossad is an ancient place, and some memory of great evil hangs over its stones. I fear that something terrible came from there and would ask you to keep a clear head while you are inside.

'Examine anything that seems unusual, for I believe that the memory of whatever sorrow hangs about that place will make itself known to you. Learn what you can, but remain wary -- creatures of the dark are drawn to such places, and you may need to defend yourself from them.

'I will stay on guard out here, watching to ensure that no enemies enter Delossad while you are within.''Go now into the depths of Delossad and uncover what secrets you can, ${PLAYER}! I will keep watch out here to ensure that your search remains uninterrupted.''${PLAYER}, are you all right? The Black Númenórean appeared outside Delossad, and I only had a moment in which to hide myself. Were it any other opponent, I would have engaged him in battle, but I could not hope to defeat him without others of my kindred. He came to the door and passed inside, and I followed behind him in secret, hoping beyond hope that I might oppose him in the final need.

'I shudder to think what he might have done had he known I was there!

'Let us leave this place, friend. You can tell me what you have learned as we travel out of the shadows of this sad ruin!'You have come with Calenglad to Barad Rath to remember the Rangers slain during Mordrambor's escape from Tinnudir.Calenglad is on the slope by Barad Rath.

The Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to remember their fallen, and Calenglad is waiting to walk with you to the site.The Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.Take your place next to CuguminuialThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.Watch the building of the cairnThe Dúnedain are waiting for you to place the cap-stone on the cairn for Carchammadel.Place cap-stone on the cairn for CarchammadelThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.Watch the building of the cairnThe Dúnedain are waiting for you to place the cap-stone on the cairn for Colhamnir.Place cap-stone on the cairn for ColhamnirThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.Watch the building of the cairnThe Dúnedain are waiting for you to place the cap-stone on the cairn for Tadan.Place cap-stone on the cairn for TadanThe Dúnedain have come to Barad Rath to mourn the loss of their kin.Listen to CalengladFleet-wing brings a dreaded, but expected, message: Amarthiel's troops have begun passing through the Evendim Gate in search of Narchuil.Talk to Calenglad'Let us leave Barad Rath, ${PLAYER}. I hope one day to return here to the cairns of Tadan, Carchammadel, and Colhamnir and share with them news of our victory over Angmar and its treacherous regent.''The air is chill, and my heart is heavy with sorrow. All battles bring grief in their train, but beyond the veil of sadness lies the hope of victory.''Torogethir has done as he said he would, for this is his raven, Fleet-wing. Amarthiel's troops are leaving this land by the Evendim Gate.

'We must depart this place, ${PLAYER}. I thank you for attending my people, and for your part in the remembrance of our fallen kin.'Yrjänä told you where to find the lair of the dragon Bregmor, though he did not know whether the dragon still lived or not.Find the lair of the dragon Bregmor.Seek out and stop the Angmarim from obtaining the hide of BregmorDefeat the leader of the Angmarim force.Defeat YthelTadan and his fellow Rangers have come up with a plan to capture Mordrambor, one of Amarthiel's Black Númenórean lieutenants, as he travels from Haudh Elendil with an unusually small retinue.Ranger Tadan and his fellow Dúnedain are hiding at the end of the causeway to Haudh Elendil, waiting in ambush for Mordrambor to emerge.

Tadan needs you to lure Mordrambor into the Dúnedain ambush at the end of the causeway.Talk to TadanYou have been asked to bring Mordrambor back to the end of the causeway with the Rangers.Confront Mordrambor at the far end of the causewayRanger Tadan is at the end of the causeway in front of Haudh Elendil.

Tadan is waiting to speak with you, following the capture of Mordrambor.Talk to Tadan'Let us return to Tinnudir with our captive, then. Perhaps our fortunes are finally beginning to turn around!''Calenglad speaks highly of you, ${PLAYER}. If we are successful this night, he will speak more highly still!

'Mordrambor has entered the tomb of Elendil and will surely emerge in a moment with his servants. If we can retain the element of surprise, my brethren and I will be more than a match for him. Present yourself to this lieutenant of Amarthiel and lure him to this end of the causeway! We will fall upon him and take him prisoner, and then we shall see what this trusted servant of Amarthiel may be able to tell us.

'This foe is in no way weak, ${PLAYER}. You will be in danger as you lead Mordrambor to our position, and we will not be able to help you -- if we reveal ourselves too soon, all will be lost. Tell him something that will make him curious enough to follow... perhaps you have found a weapon that can destroy him. He will doubt such a weapon exists and will follow you willingly to disprove it. Luck be with you in this, ${PLAYER}.''Why should I not strike thee down, little ${RACE}?'

Mordrambor's mocking smile wavers slightly when you tell him you have brought a mighty artifact to the other end of the causeway, and it spells his doom. Almost immediately it returns.

'I admire thy courage, though it be foolish in the extreme! I will go with thee to this artifact, and give thee the death thou seemest to crave.''Well done, my friend, well done! Amarthiel will not be pleased with this turn at all.

'Let me know when you are ready to leave, and we shall return to Tinnudir with our captive.'The Ranger Faelbenn has asked you to help him defeat the Angmarim reinforcements crossing Rammas Deluon.Receive your orders from Faelbenn.Talk to FaelbennDefeat the Angmarim sorceresses and prevent the reinforcements from crossing Rammas Deluon.Defeat Angmarim sorceresses (${VALUE}/5)Quickly defeat the sorceressesPrevent bulwarks from fallingDefend FaelbennVictory is yours... you should speak again with Faelbenn at once.Talk to Faelbenn'There is no more for us to do here...let us leave.''We must hurry, ${PLAYER}! The Angmarim reinforcements are trying to cross the Rammas Deluon and are rallying near the various stones. Unfortunately we dare not cross the line of the stones, as there are foul Sorceresses supplicating the stones, making them more deadly than we have ever seen.

'However, it is not all dark. The sorceresses cannot maintain their state for very long and their resolve will falter. At those moments, you must strike and defeat those sorceresses!

'Do not forget though, if we are to maintain our blockade of the Rammas Deluon, our bulwarks must stand, so you must aid in their defence as well.''This was perhaps the greatest blow we have yet dealt to Angmar! It shows that they have become weakened, and it may soon be time for us to deal a final blow to them.'You have accompanied the Ranger Firingal to Aughaire to defend the village against the assaults of Mordirith's horde.Speak to Firingal regarding the defence of Aughaire.Talk to FiringalDefend Aughaire from Angmar's assault.Defend AughairePrevent Trév Gállorg defeats (${VALUE}/8)Defend all of the Aughaire bulwarksDefend FiringalYou should report back to Firingal.Talk to Firingal'Quickly now, we must return to Gath Forthnír and see if there we are needed elsewhere.''We must hurry, ${PLAYER}! Angmar's host is nearly here.

'We must protect all of the bulwarks of Aughaire, or we will be unable to defend the town. When the call rings out, move to help defend that bulwark. I will keep watch over the Gate of Aughaire, in case any sneak past our defences.

'Go now and defend the good people of Aughaire!''You fought gloriously, ${PLAYER}! We have defended Aughaire and routed the forces of Angmar. I feel the tide is turning against Mordirith!'The Ranger Tordoron has asked for your aid in assaulting the forces of Angmar in Rhunendin.Speak with Tordoron to receive your marching orders.Talk to TordoronClaim all of Angmar's encampments (${VALUE}/4)Quickly claim all the encampmentsDefend the Free Peoples' bulwarksDefend TordoronYou should speak with Tordoron regarding your victory.Talk to Tordoron'Let us leave this place, ${PLAYER}.''Are you prepared, ${PLAYER}? Good! Then let us away!

'We must claim all of Angmar's encampments or be forced to retreat.''We are victorious, ${PLAYER}! The scourge of Angmar is collapsing... it will not be long, I think, before the Iron Crown is defeated....'You have arrived near the ruins of Tham Mírdain, the Ring-forges of Eregion, where Amarthiel intends to reforge Narchuil. You must find the means to put an end to her plan.You must find Amarthiel before she can reforge Narchuil.Find Amarthiel somewhere within Tham MírdainYou have found Laerdan lying within the entrance to Tham Mírdain, gravely wounded. You should learn from him what happened.Laerdan instructed you to find and defeat the Gorthorog Strok, who bears the keys to Tham Mírdain.Defeat the doorwarden, StrokYou should use the keys you recovered from Strok to gain entry into Tham Mírdain.Enter Tham MírdainYou must find the ring-forges of Tham Mírdain.Find the ring-forges of Tham MírdainYou must confront Amarthiel at the ring-forges of Tham Mírdain.Confront AmarthielAmarthiel was interrupted by the arrival of the Black Númenórean Mordrambor. You should follow them to learn what new evil has arisen.Follow Amarthiel and MordramborAmarthiel pays you no mind, for her grief is all-consuming. Although she has suffered terribly at the hands of her former allies, she may yet pose a threat to the North. You must take her away as a prisoner of the Free Peoples and leave her to their mercy.'I was a fool to be deceived so easily by Amarthiel, and it has led to this. There is hope, however, for she left me alive. Perhaps if she can be hindered from reforging Narchuil, Narmeleth may be reclaimed.

'To enter into Tham Mírdain, you will need to defeat the Gorthorog who holds the keys to the forges. His name is Strok, and he is a mighty foe.

'Hurry, ${PLAYER}, there is little time to lose!'Although gravely wounded, Laerdan still breathes shallowly.Laerdan has foolishly listened to the words of Mordrambor and journeyed into Barad Tironn alone to challenge Amarthiel. Calenglad has asked you to steal the palantír from her and aid Laerdan if you can.The palantír is somewhere within Barad Tironn.

You must find the palantír and steal it before Amarthiel can use it to learn the location of Narchuil.Enter Barad Tironn and search for the palantírAmarthiel and the palantír are within Barad Tironn.

Laerdan has confronted Amarthiel, and now you are waiting for his command to seize the palantír and carry it from Barad Tironn.The palantír is on its pedestal deep within Barad Tironn.

Laerdan has given you the word: one of you must seize the palantír and carry it to Calenglad at the entrance of Barad Tironn! Hurry!Calenglad is at the entrance to Barad Tironn.

You must protect the carrier of the palantír and see it delivered to Calenglad at the entrance to Barad Tironn. Hurry!Deliver the palantír to Calenglad at the entrance to Barad Tironn'We have no time to waste, ${PLAYER}! I weep for Laerdan, but we must retrieve the palantír and remove it from Annúminas!

'Are you ready?''The palantír is somewhere within Barad Tironn, ${PLAYER}. My Men have managed to bring you this far, but we must hold the line -- you will need to find the palantír yourself.

'If you can assist Laerdan in any way once you are inside, I would ask you to do so, but retrieval of the palantír must come first. Once you have seized it, carry it back here to me with as much haste as you can manage -- if Amarthiel realizes what you have done, she will do everything in her power to keep you from escaping with it, so you must be quick!''${PLAYER}, why have you come here? This is not your fight -- I need to confront Amarthiel on my own, as I should have done long ago!

'The time is past, my friend. If I can hold Amarthiel's attention long enough, you will be able to seize the palantír. We will challenge her together, and perhaps she will not realize her peril. When I give you the word, you must seize the palantír and immediately run to the entrance of Barad Tironn -- do not delay! Bring it to Calenglad, and perhaps I will be able to set right my errors of old.

'May the Valar smile upon your endeavour and mine, ${PLAYER}. Let us go.'Elrond is concerned as to the plight of Laerdan at Tham Mírdain....Laerdan searches even now for his beloved daughter Narmeleth, seeking to bring her the shards of Narchuil and restore her mind.Find NarmelethLaerdan has been tricked. He must defend himself against the onslaught of Amarthiel, Champion of Angmar....Survive Amarthiel's onslaughtThe time has come to bid farewell to the Company as they set forth on their errand of secrecy.Frodo is on the porch of the House of Elrond, preparing to depart with the Company.

The folk of Elrond's house bid farewell to the Company as they prepare to depart.Members of the Company can be found in front of the House of Elrond, preparing to depart.

The folk of Elrond's house bid farewell to the Company as they prepare to depart.Boromir stands proudly before the House of Elrond, preparing to depart with the Company.

The folk of Elrond's house bid farewell to the Company as they prepare to depart.Gandalf is before the House of Elrond, preparing to depart with the Company.

The folk of Elrond's house bid farewell to the Company as they prepare to depart.Elrond is before his house, watching the Company depart.

The Company is now on their way into the wild on an errand of secrecy upon which rest the hopes of all the Free Peoples.'Let us go back inside, ${PLAYER}. There is nothing more we can do for them: the Company must now rely upon their own strength and wisdom.''Everything seems to be ready, ${PLAYER}, and we're about to leave. Hopefully, I will see you again once this is all done with!''Keep an eye upon these lands while we are away, my friend. Our errand is a dangerous one, but there will be danger behind us, too, and my footsteps will be easier if I know that ${PLAYER} remains behind to protect against them. My own journey will carry me far from here.''Samwise, you dunder-head! You've gone and forgotten to bring a bit of rope with you. I knew there was something you had forgot!

'Bill here will have too much to carry as it is, and I've lightened his load as much as I can.''This is it, ${PLAYER}. Wish us luck, and we'll be sure to come through all right. Leastways, we'll make sure to lend Frodo all the help we can, and do whatever Gandalf needs us to do.

'We'll see you when we get back, and that's a promise!''So begins a new journey. Let us go forth boldly, I say, rather than skulking from shadow to shadow, and let the Enemy quail at our coming!''The number of the Company has been chosen, ${PLAYER}, and any more would threaten the success of its mission.

'You have business remaining in Eriador, brave ${RACE}: defend its people from the lengthening shadows. If the errand of this Company fails, Eriador will have need of heroes before the final darkness.''It is done, and they are beyond my aid. For all of my wisdom, I cannot see the end of their road. May they come to it in safety and return to Rivendell in victory.'Yrjänä told you that the Angmarim have also come to Sûri-kylä, led by a Black Númenórean.Accompany Yrjänä to meet with the emissary of Angmar.Yrjänä and the Elders of the Lossoth are to meet with the emissary from Angmar.'Come, we must seek shelter from this storm.''Let us gather the Elders and meet with this emissary from Angmar.'Golodir told you that Laerdan's breastplate might be found in Dolendath, the place where his army first took refuge after passing Rammas Deluon.Search through Dolendath for some sign of Laerdan's breastplate.Search for Laerdan's breastplateA strange voice beckoned you forwards. Discover its source.Search for the source of the strange laughterYour search for the source of the strange laughter led you to a gaunt-man. This vile creature must be defeated.Defeat GoeolgúrWith the key of Agoroth in hand, the time has come to find the door to the hidden fortress, deep within the caves of ice.Arvedui and Lothrandir are conversing outside Sûri-kylä.

You should listen to the conversation.Listen to the conversationArvedui and Lothrandir are having a conversation outside Sûri-kylä.

You should talk to Lothrandir when they are finished.Talk to LothrandirArvedui and Lothrandir are talking.

You should listen to the conversation.Listen to the conversationArvedui is ready to show you the way to Agoroth.

Talk to Arvedui to travel to Jä-reitti.Speak to Arvedui to travel to Jä-reittiFrost grims block your path deeper into the ice caves.

You should defeat the frost grims.Defeat the frost grimsYou must be close now!

You should help Arvedui reveal the hidden door!

Say the password 'Dolen uin Belegoth' aloud to reveal the door.Say the password to reveal the door'The way is open. When you are ready, we shall enter.''I have been telling Arvedui of his heir, Aragorn, and his desire to reunite the kingdoms. Hearing such things seems to have lifted his spirits! I believe he blames himself for his death ending the line of Kings. Perhaps we are making progress on two fronts, ${PLAYER}! Did you acquire the key from the Lossoth?'

You tell Lothrandir and Arvedui that you acquired the key but promised to destroy the Oath-stone that the Lossoth believe is inside Agoroth. Lothrandir looks at you curiously.

'Quite a promise to exchange for something so valuable, ${PLAYER}! I truly hope we are able to keep it.''I will lead us to Agoroth.'The Elf Laerdan has been imprisoned in Sammath Baul, where he is kept under the watchful eye of the torturer Morven and her Angmarim bloodletters.Morven is in the chamber on the upper floor of Sammath Baul.

Morven is waiting to give you your instructions.Blood-leeches can be found throughout the tower of Sammath Baul.

Morven has asked you to eradicate the blood-leeches that infest the tower in preparation for Amarthiel's visit to Sammath Baul.Clear vermin from Sammath Baul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Morven is in the upper chamber of Sammath Baul.

You have cleared the blood-leeches from Sammath Baul, for the time being, and should report now to Morven on the top floor.Tarkrîp Orcs and Lozudurkh the Gorthorog can be found sleeping throughout Sammath Baul.

Morven has sent you to awaken Lozudurkh and all the sleeping Tarkrîp throughout the tower.Morven is on the upper floor of the tower.

You have awakened all the sleeping guards and should return now to Morven.Amarthiel is interrogating the Elf Laerdan on the upper floor of Sammath Baul.

You have been given the great honour of watching Amarthiel interrogate the Elf Laerdan.Wait for Amarthiel to finish her interrogationMorven is in the chamber on the upper floor of Sammath Baul.

Amarthiel has finished her interrogation, and Morven now wishes to speak with you.Laerdan is in a state of thrall in the chamber on the upper floor of Sammath Baul.

Morven has commanded you to bring Laerdan back to his cell.Return Laerdan to his cellLaerdan is in a state of thrall in the chamber on the upper floor of Sammath Baul.

Sammath Baul is under attack by allies of Laerdan, and Morven mobilizes her forces to the defence of the tower.Return Laerdan to his cell'I have an important assignment for you, Bloodletter; if you carry it out well, I might allow you your choice of the treasures from our latest captives. The Trév Gállorg may be poor, but sometimes they fashion things of great worth, and you might earn yourself a pretty bauble.

'I have received word that our Mistress will be coming to Sammath Baul to question the Elf Laerdan, and I want everything to run smoothly during her visit.

'The corpses in the tower have given rise to tremendous blood-leeches, and their filth and disease has been... distracting... for the rest of my servants. I want you to destroy the blood-leeches before the Mistress arrives.''If you delay any further, I will have you put to death, Bloodletter! Will you enjoy being bled by your fellows and thrown into a cell to rot out the last moments of your pitiful life?

'No? Then eliminate the blood-leeches from Sammath Baul and do it quickly! Our Mistress will be here soon!''These Trév Gállorg have been in Sammath Baul only a few days and already I tire of their wailing. Perhaps I will ask Morven if I may kill them.''Lozudurkh has done little but sleep ever since he was assigned here, the fool. His failure at Annúminas is well-known.

'I would gut him myself, but it seems the Mistress has something in mind for him. Why else would she name him Key-master of the tower, when countless of her servants are more deserving?''You are dealing with the blood-leeches? Pity. It is a pleasure to watch them feed on the corpses.

'Still, Morven's word is but one step removed from that of our Mistress; you are wise to obey.''Morven has been given free reign to do as she will in Sammath Baul. If she allows it, these Trév Gállorg will not see the light of morning! I can hear their screams in my head already. Beautiful.''That useless Gorthorog! Ask Morven if I can do away with Lozudurkh, will you? His stench is drawing the blood-leeches.''It is a shame that you had to destroy the blood-leeches, but they will be back. They breed from the corpses, you know.''You have cleared the tower of blood-leeches? You will go far, Bloodletter. Perhaps I will tell our Mistress of your dedication when she arrives.

'What? The Tarkrîp are all asleep, and Lozudurkh as well? I would never question our Mistress, but I do not understand why she would send such spineless sluggards to guard Sammath Baul. Surely the bloodletters under my command are sufficient?

'Awaken all of the sleeping Tarkrîp and that useless Gorthorog as well! If he is to be Key-master, he should be at his post outside the tower! Use your boot if necessary, Bloodletter.''I will not allow the Tarkrîp to spend this time in slumber! Awaken them all, and that worthless Gorthorog as well!''What is our Mistress thinking? Why assign Tarkrîp to this tower, instead of one of the more formidable tribes? Surely she has some plan.

'I do not know what it could be. Perhaps after I kill these prisoners, I will spend some time in contemplation of our Mistress's purposes.''The Tarkrîp are worthless. Sammath Baul was better protected before they arrived! What could the Mistress possibly have in mind?''The Tarkrîp need to learn discipline. We could teach them something of it, you and I. Bleed some of them and kill the rest. The ones that remain will be more... vigilant.''Maybe we will be lucky and Lozudurkh will not come back from his post.''Our Mistress has arrived, Bloodletter! Since you have been of such use, I grant you this boon: to watch her interrogation of the Elf Laerdan. Some few of your brothers have also been given this great honour, that they too may be rewarded.''You heard our Mistress! Allies of the Elf will soon arrive to bring him to freedom.

'Return him at once to his cell, Bloodletter. We will not give his friends the pleasure of seeing him alive.'The sharp bite of your weapon will have to prevail against the thick flesh of the Watcher's many arms.Bósi is on the slope that leads up to the pool before the Doors of Durin.

Bósi is waiting to wish you well against the Watcher in the Water. He is confident that the sharp bite of your weapon will prevail.Talk to BósiBósi sent some dwarves up to the pool to scout ahead for the beast.

Armed with your new weapon, you are ready to face the Watcher in the Water.Talk to Bósi's scoutThe Watcher in the Water lurks within the pool, casting its arms forth to attack you!

You must defeat the arms of the Watcher and drive it from the entrance to Moria.Drive off the Watcher in the WaterBrogur has come to the shore of the Black Pool, against his cousin's wishes.Talk to BrogurBrogur has challenged the Watcher in the Water, determined to avenge the death of his son.Protect Brogur from the Watcher in the WaterBósi and Brogur are on the edge of the pool.

The Watcher in the Water has been driven off, and you should now speak with Bósi and Brogur.Talk to BósiTalk to Brogur'We must return now to tell the rest of the expedition what you have accomplished, and that we may now pass into the Mines of Moria!''It's out there... the beast that killed my son. I will not rest until Bróin is avenged.''The foul creature that watches from within the depths of the pool will feel the sharp bite of your weapon and be afraid. Stride forth and teach it a lesson it will be long in forgetting!

'Do this not just for the sake of Khazad-dûm, but for the memory of Bróin, taken by that fell creature. My nephew deserved a better fate than to die in that thing's grasp.

'When you have driven off or slain the creature, we will be unopposed and may walk into Moria unhindered!

'One of my dwarves has gone ahead to scout for the beast. Look for him, and be watchful.''Look for my scout just up the slope, on the edge of the pool. He will tell you where he has seen the beast, that you may attack it with your new weapon.''There are ripples in the water, but I do not see the beast. Be on your guard, for it may attack without warning, as unlucky Bróin learned at his peril!''No longer will I cow to my grief, ${PLAYER}. Nay; I will avenge my son in battle, and woe to this creature that took him from me!''We have done it, ${PLAYER}! We have driven the Watcher from the Doors of Durin, and now the dwarves of our expedition may pass into the Mines of Moria! The weapons we found have proven the difference, friend -- yes, my dwarves have equipped themselves from the same cache, and the creature has learned to fear the sharp bite of the Iron Garrison!

'You have avenged my nephew Bróin as well, and all of the dwarves who have been lost to this creature. It retreats now through dark passages; may its writhing, reeking arms never trouble us again.''I cannot thank you enough for this, ${PLAYER}. Not only have you driven off the beast that kept us out of Moria, but you have avenged my son as well. I will never forget your great service to me, and will always be in your debt and at your service.

'Bróin spoke often of combat and great heroics; he would have marvelled at your battle with the fierce Watcher.'The ring Narchuil is being studied by the Enemy in Barad Dúrgul.Enter Barad Dúrgul and recover the ring Narchuil.Find the ring NarchuilYou have found Narucham, and it appears that he has been dead for some time now.  You should give him a proper burial and then return to Gwathryn.As a burglar, you know that you must take advantage of any opportunity that presents itself and revel in the moments when luck is on your side.Crit with a Critical Hit chain skillGlorfindel is troubled about recent events and the recollection of a greater evil in Angmar.Glorfindel is near the Bruinen in Rivendell.

Faimir suggests that you speak with Glorfindel and learn what it is that troubles him.Iorelen is at Iorelen's camp far to the north-east in Angmar.

Glorfindel requested that you seek Iorelen and learn whether he still lives.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. You have come at a most fortuitous time. Have you spoken to Lord Glorfindel? He seems troubled recently, but will not speak of it.

'You have become familiar with him, have you not? Perhaps he will reveal his concerns to you. If you are willing, go to him near the Bruinen and speak with him.''You should speak at once with Lord Glorfindel.''So you have spoken with Faimir? Her concern is kind, but there is nothing she can do.

'A friend of mine, Iorelen, journeyed into Angmar to the Rift, a place the servants of the Enemy call Nûrz Ghâshu. It is said that a great evil dwells there beneath the Mountains of Angmar, and he went to seek news of it. Glathlírel, another ally of mine, had gone there long ago and did not return, though it is said among the Wise that the evil there was contained.

'Perhaps you may be of help. You have ventured into Angmar, have you not? Perhaps you can make your way to Iorelen's camp far to the north east in the land of Angmar and learn of Glathlírel's fate.''I have heard rumour that Iorelen lives still and may be found far to the north and east, in Angmar.'Iorelen was once a member of my company. Will you find him and speak with him regarding the dangers at Núrz Ghâshu''Glorfindel sent you? Indeed, the Shadow of Angmar reaches even here to the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu. It is well that you have come, for we will need aid in turning back the Shadow.'The Trév Duvárdain have sent an emissary to Agar to treat with the minions of the Iron Crown.Minas Agar stands on the western side of Barad Gúlaran, south of Gath Forthnír.

You must travel to Barad Gúlaran and defeat Karstíona, the emissary of the Trév Duvárdain, inside Minas Agar.Brúnfair is in Gath Forthníir, north of Barad Gúlaran.

Having defeated Karstíona, you should return to Brúnfair and tell him of your success.'The text you recovered told of an alliance between Angmar and the Trév Duvárdain. I have done some research and learned that Domongart has sent an emissary to treat with Angmar. 

'You should investigate the matter. There have been many reports of Hillmen of the Trév Duvárdain near the tower of Minas Agar near Barad Gúlaran. We must stop this alliance from happening, no matter the cost.

'Defeat Karstíona, the emissary, then return to me. If you wish to enter Minas Agar, I suggest you take trustworthy allies.''Karstíona must be defeated and the alliance between the Iron Crown and the Hillmen sundered.''Of all alliances the Iron Crown could have forged, this was the most dire. If they lent greater support to the Trév Duvárdain, our efforts here would have been in vain.

'Well done!'Having discovered a pledge from the Dourhands, you must enter Minas Angos and defeat their emissary to stop an alliance between them and the Iron Crown.Minas Angos is a tower in Barad Gúlaran, south of Gath Forthnír.

You must travel to Barad Gúlaran and defeat Laugi Goldentongue, the emissary of the Dourhands, inside Minas Angos. Brúnfair suggested you take allies.Brúnfair is at Gath Forthnír, north of Barad Gúlaran.

Having defeated Laugi Goldentongue, you should return to Brúnfair and tell him of your victory.'The text you recovered told of an alliance between Angmar and the Dourhands. Our scouts tell us that an emissary of the Dourhands has come to treat with Angmar.

'You should investigate the matter. There have been many reports of dwarves near the tower of Minas Angos near Barad Gúlaran. We must stop this alliance from happening, no matter the cost.

'Defeat the emissary, Laugi Goldentongue, then return back to me when the deed is done. If you are to succeed, you should take allies.''Laugi Goldentongue must be defeated, else the Iron Crown and the Dourhands will forge a stronger alliance.''The downfall of the Dourhands' emissary will be sure to sever the alliance between these two evil powers. Well done, ${PLAYER}.'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Acquire the Legend of Angmar Title<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Complete Legendary Angmar: Carn DûmComplete Legendary Angmar: UrugarthComplete Legendary Angmar: The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Complete the Annúminas - Glinghant instance.<rgb=#00e4ff>Complete the Annúminas - Glinghant instance</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Complete the Annúminas - Haudh Valandil instance.<rgb=#00e4ff>Complete the Annúminas - Haudh Valandil instance</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Complete the Annúminas - Ost Elendil instance.<rgb=#00e4ff>Complete the Annúminas - Ost Elendil instance</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Defeat Udúnion.<rgb=#00e4ff>Defeat Udúnion</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Defeat Mordirith.<rgb=#00e4ff>Defeat Mordirith</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#FF00FF>Complete ten quests and instances to aid those in Angmar.

