You should seek Isdi to receive further training in your class.'I am pleased to meet you at last, ${PLAYER}. The years may be long, but they are full of joy for those who seek learning. The passing of the seasons cannot blunt the sharp mind eager for wisdom.'Become a master of your own will, and you will not so easily fall under the sway of others.Use Anthem of ComposureBecome a master of your own will, and you will not so easily fall under the sway of others.Use Anthem of ComposureYou earned this title during the Season of Malice Reward Track Season in Monster Play.You have proven yourself among the countless Mariners and Corsairs that sail the waters of Middle-earth, but now you are set on a new course: to test your skill and master the Sea itself, if you might.Aelindil can be found at Tornhad, in the Angle of Mitheithel.

You have received a letter from Aelindil, a Mariner of the Dúnedain, who wishes to speak with you.${PLAYER},

Word of your prowess has spread among the Dúnedain, and so, I have arranged for you an audience with a visiting Mariner of great experience and skill. However, you must first prove yourself worthy of his tutelage, and that will be no simple task. I await you at Tornhad in the Angle of Mitheithel.

Aelindil'I bid you welcome to Tornhad, ${PLAYER}. You have my letter, I presume?'

You hand Aelindil the letter you received, and he pockets it.

'You see, Tarneth wrote to me some days ago, and she had much to say of the aid you offered my kinsmen upon the shores of Lake Evendim. I thank you for the part you played in protecting the relics of Annúminas, my friend.

'I might be able to aid you in return, but that depends upon you!'Long ago, a servant pledged himself to the Witch-king's cause. His service lasts to this day, and his dark embrace on Barad Gúlaran brings terror into the hearts of those fighting to unseat Shadow in the North.Barad Gúlaran rises out of the centre of Nan Gurth, south and east of Gath Forthnír.

Uidon directed you to enter Barad Gúlaran in search of Castellan Wisdán. You are to slay him and return to Uidon for your reward.Gath Forthnír is north-west from Barad Gúlaran.

You entered Barad Gúlaran and after some time found and defeated the Castellan within his chambers. You should now return to Gath Forthnír, the hidden refuge in the north-east area of Angmar, and inform Uidon that you have defeated Castellan Wisdán.'We face many fell foes in this dark place. Though the strength of the Enemy is weakened, so, too, is it strengthened by the discovery of this great ruse. Now, we learn that the dark tower standing amidst the forces within the forsaken valley to our south teems with enemies long kindling flames from a place I shall not speak of.

'It falls to you, ${PLAYER}, to gather your allies and make an assault on Barad Gúlaran, to stand against the horrors awakened within that dark citadel. One horror, Wisdán, once a man in service to Angmar, sacrificed his life to watch over Barad Gúlaran. Lore-masters dispatched from Esteldín brought us all we know of him and Barad Gúlaran. Little is known beyond his service to the Witch-king and his close ties with the Shadow in the North. It is possible that he is a sorcerer, like a few others within Barad Gúlaran.

'He must be slain, ${PLAYER}, lest his darkness be used to spread evil towards the south to become the bane of all. Gather your allies together and enter Barad Gúlaran. Return to me when you have done the deed, and I will see that the Council's gifts are bestowed upon you.''A sign of hope in these dark times, ${PLAYER}. This news will hearten Halbarad and those who worry of our tenuous position here. You have earned a great deal of our respect and this reward.

'Take it and know that we are honoured by all you do to keep Evil from spreading to the south. We must endeavour onward.''Do not tarry, ${PLAYER}. Though the citadel of Barad Gúlaran has long lain in slumber, recent events will surely set the inhabitants within to their task. We must disrupt their intentions swiftly.'Your understanding of inference and connotation is improved by your foe's lack of understanding.Have your Battle skills resistedYou have aided in the search for the lost Ring-lore of Eregion.You have aided in the search for the lost Ring-lore of Eregion.Master the Way of the Fist.Strike with Exultation of Battle or DesolationMaster the Way of the Fist.Strike with Exultation of Battle or DesolationMaster the Way of the Shield.Strike with Shield Mastery, Celebration of Skill, or Dance of WarMaster the Way of the Shield.Strike with Shield Mastery, Celebration of Skill, or Dance of WarYour studies in the construction of tragedy can have tremendous impact upon your foes.Critical Hits with Fury of the Storm skillsYour studies in the construction of tragedy can have tremendous impact upon your foes.Critical Hits with Fury of the Storm skillsWithout aid, the Dunlendings at Porth Cadlus will be vulnerable to attack.Porth Cadlus is south and slightly west of Echad Dúnann, across Nan Sirannon.

