You should return to Ruidhriel and tell her what you found.Talk to Ruidhriel'Hail, stranger! It is good to see a friendly face in times such as these, but what brings you here?

'Rinneldor has sent aid as I had hoped! Caradhras is troubled; something has caused great unease upon his slopes. His winds are cold and biting, and I fear for any who have dared to tread upon him when he is in such a fey mood.

'I cannot leave my post, but perhaps you could travel to the mountain's lower slopes and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for signs of the Company? Travel north-east to the Redhorn Gate and look for any signs of them where the trees and snows meet.''An avalanche? We can only hope that the Company was not on the mountain when it happened.

'If they did brave the pass, no enemies will follow now. Thank you for your help, ${PLAYER}.''Travel north-east into the Redhorn Gate and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for signs of the Company where the snow and trees meet.'Ormulf Worm-hunter, impressed with your selflessness, has offered you a reward for slaying ice-drakes after all.Wegeir is somewhere within Thorin's Hall.

Ormulf Worm-hunter has been impressed by your selflessness and asked you to deliver a crate of pick-axes to Wegeir, who can give to you your reward.'I cannot keep my mirth hidden beneath my beard any longer -- you have passed my test, ${PLAYER}! I did not think to find one so selfless, but you have proven your worth to me! To slay so many ice-drakes, without hope for reward...you are an honourable ${RACE}, that much is certain!

'Unless...you assumed I would give you a reward anyway? Surely that isn't the case, is it?

'Bring this crate of pick-axes to Wegeir in Thorin's Hall. He will provide to you the reward of which I speak, and he will receive the pick-axes he is due. If I could leave Othrikar I would deliver them myself, but you know how it is. I left with him several choice items of mine, and any of them would be a suitable reward for you, my honourable ${RACE}!''You bring pick-axes from Ormulf? It is well past time, but I am glad to see them finally arrive.

'He gave word that his messenger should be given the choice of several items he left in my keeping. Here they are, and thank you for the delivery!'Find pages of the Plans of War scattered throughout Carn Dûm.Find pages of the Plans of War scattered throughout Carn Dûm and discover the machinations of the Enemy.Find pages of the Plans of War scattered throughout Carn Dûm and discover the machinationss of the Enemy.'This is one of many pages scribed by Mordirith detailing his machinations towards Eriador.''This is one of many pages scribed by Mordirith detailing his machinations towards Eriador.''This is one of many pages scribed by Mordirith detailing his machinations towards Eriador.''This is one of many pages scribed by Mordirith detailing his machinations towards Eriador.''This is one of many pages scribed by Mordirith detailing his machinations towards Eriador.''This is one of many pages scribed by Mordirith detailing his machinations towards Eriador.'Goblin-town has sent an emissary to Minas Maur to treat with Angmar.Minas Maur is one of the large towers of Barad Gúlaran, south of Gath Forthnír.

You must travel to Barad Gúlaran and defeat the emissary from Goblin-town inside Minas Maur. Brúfair suggested you take allies with you.Gath Forthnir is north of Barad Gúluran.

Having defeated Prakhum, return to Gath Forthnír and let Brúnfair know what you have done.'The text you recovered told of an alliance between Angmar and the goblins of Goblin-town.  Rumour has been told that Angmar and Goblin-town have had troubles entreating in the past. It is strange to find the goblins here. Perhaps this emissary is here without the knowledge of his leaders.

'You should investigate the matter. There have been many reports of goblins near the tower of Minas Maur near Barad Gúlaran. We must stop this alliance from happening, no matter the cost.

'Defeat the emissary and return to me when the deed is done. If you wish to succeed, you will likely want to take allies with you.''You must defeat the goblin Prakhum and stop the alliance between the Iron Crown and the goblins of the Misty Mountains.''You have helped the Free Peoples avoid the greatest of threats! An alliance between the goblins of the Misty Mountains and the Iron Crown would have been disastrous!'You must field your archer to practice his art in order to cultivate greater skill and precision.Call forth your archerYou must field your archer to practice his art in order to cultivate greater skill and precision.Call forth your archerThough you defeated the merrevail and the bats that plagued the Rangers of Gath Forthnír, Thoriel spoke of taking the fight to Carn Dûm and to the queen of the merrevail herself.Glyn is at a small camp on the eastern path to Carn Dûm.

Thoriel has sent you to Carn Dûm to deal with the queen of the merrevail, though she asked you to speak with Glyn on your way there.Azgoth dwells within Carn Dûm, the city of Angmar that lies to the west.

Glyn told you of the morroval-queen, a creature called Azgoth, that must be slain.Glyn is in Tármunn Súrsa, to the east of Carn Dûm, near the Gates of Carn Dûm.

You braved the city of Carn Dûm and defeated Azgoth. Glyn will want to hear of your feat.'Your courage and grace give us hope, ${PLAYER}. But as I told you, the threat is not yet vanquished.

'You must go to Carn Dûm, though you should speak with Glyn on the way. He is in a small look-out camp past the Gates of Carn Dûm.

'Speak with him quickly. We must attack before the merrevail return.''Seek Glyn upon the eastern path to Carn Dûm... he may know more about the evils that plague Angmar.''Your deeds precede you, friend, but I will speak plainly. The merrevail follow a queen, a most powerful creature called Azgoth.

'She is a terror most foul, with many minions at her beck and call. Azgoth nests within Carn Dûm, the great city of Angmar that lies to the west.

'It will not be an easy journey, and the city is well protected. Return to me when you have slain the mighty Azgoth.''You must defeat Azgoth, or she will lead her minions against us... and our numbers are dwindling daily.

'You must travel to Carn Dûm and find a way inside.''Azgoth is the terrible Queen of the Winged Host... do as Glyn instructed and defeat her!''Azgoth is no more? Glyn will wish to know of this.''You claim that Azgoth is no more, but how can this be? You are but one and succeeded where we could not!

'Ah, but I can see her black blood upon you and the fire in your eyes. Yes, you speak the truth. This is a great day, a day of celebration where we stood as one against the Enemy.'Rostoriel has asked for your aid in quelling rage of Caradhras.The Redhorn Gate is north-east of Echad Dúnann.

Rostoriel has asked you to search the highest reaches of the Redhorn Gate for clues to understand the mountain's anger.'The storms have not relented. The winds continue to howl, and I can hear anger in the voice of Caradhras, but not for the Elves or even the dwarves. There is something on the mountain that is causing his fury.

'It will be a dangerous task, but I would ask that you search as high into the pass as you dare and seek out the source of the mountain's anger.  Only by soothing the wrath of Caradhras will we be able to safely continue our search for signs of the Company.

'You should return to the Redhorn Gate, north-east of here, and search the highest reaches of the mountain-side.''A camp-fire? And so high into the pass!

'This must have been left by the Company, but did they brave the Redhorn Gate or were they forced off Caradhras by his fury...?'The drake-queen rules the wilds of Urugarth, spawning broods of drakelings that ravage the countryside.Urugarth lies to the west of Tármunn Sûrsa.

Gormal asked you to go to Urugarth and defeat the drake-queen who dwells there, advising you to attack her drakelings in order to draw her out. He also advised that you do not go alone.Defeat drake-queenTármunn Súrsa lies to the east of Urugarth.

You should return to Gormal and tell him of your success.'There is a great drake-queen which must be slain within Urugarth.

'She is a creature of fierce intelligence and will attempt to evade you. Turn your weapons against her young drakelings... that may goad her into action.

'The fortress of Urugarth lies to the west of here. Be cautious when you approach and do not go alone.''Go to Urugarth and slay the drake-queen.''The great drake-queen is no more? Then you are truly a ${CLASS} of renown. We shall sing of your deeds this night!'A powerful artifact awaits in the hidden fortress of Agoroth. You must reach it before the Witch-king's forces.The Lossoth chieftain Yrjänä can be found in the Great Lodge of Sûri-kylä.

You should ask Yrjänä if the Lossoth would be willing to trade for the key of Agoroth.Talk to Yrjänä in the Great Lodge of Sûri-kyläYrjänä has asked you to promise to find a way to destroy the Oath-stone in exchange for the key of Agoroth.

If you accept these terms, let Yrjänä know that you <rgb=#FF0000>agree</rgb>.<rgb=#FF0000>Agree</rgb> to Yrjänä's termsYou have agreed to destroy the Oath-stone in exchange for the key of Agoroth.

You should talk to Yrjänä in Sûri-kylä.Talk to YrjänäSalavahti can be found on the rise above Sûri-kylä.

You should talk to Salavahti.Talk to SalavahtiSalavahti has informed you that Lothrandir has returned to Sûri-kylä to meet you.

You should talk to Lothrandir.Talk to Lothrandir outside Sûri-kyläLothrandir and Arvedui are outside Sûri-kylä.

You should listen to their conversation in 'Instance: The Power of Oaths.'Complete 'Instance: The Power of Oaths'Arvedui has shown you and Lothrandir the hidden entrance to Agoroth in Jä-reitti.

You should talk to Lothrandir.Talk to Lothrandir in Jä-reitti'It is clear we do not have much time if we are to reach Agoroth's treasure before the Angmarim. You should go ahead to Sûri-kylä and ask the Lossoth council if they will barter for the key to Agoroth. They are an honourable folk, and will make fair trade for it. Meanwhile, I would like to speak with King Arvedui at length, giving him word of the last thousand years, and to hear tales of the Dúnedain of old.'', you return. The Lumi-väki did not expect to see you again after that business with the ring was finished. At least, not so soon. What do you want from Yrjänä?'

You explain that the Angmarim are searching for a treasure in the hidden fortress of Agoroth, and that you need the key Arvedui left with the Lossoth before his death if there is any hope of beating them to it.

'Yrjänä knows of what you speak. The Lumi-väki have kept this heirloom safe. But I ask, do you know the true significance of this item? It is more than a metal key to a metal door. The Lumi-väki know. My people have long memories.

'The songs tell of a time long ago, when the tall men came in suits of iron. They asked the Lumi-väki for peace, and to swear an oath before a great stone, blue as the sky on a clear day. The Lumi-väki swore to help the tall men fight their enemies, and in trade, we received weapons of forged metal to fight our ancient rivals, the Gauredain. A good trade, until the Iron Men went to war. Many Lumi-väki died in foreign lands, facing enemies that were not our own.

'Even still, the Lumi-väki kept our oath and the peace with the Iron Men and their descendants. One day, they came again to Sûri-kylä. They said the stone must be moved and hidden. There were other stones, with oaths made by other clans, that were taken, and corrupted. The Iron Men wished to build a new Stone-home here, in our lands. The Lumi-väki were hesitant. An enemy capable of corrupting such powerful magic is not an enemy to be made lightly. We knew who that enemy must be....

'But the Lumi-väki were compelled by their oath, and allowed the Iron Men to build their Stone-home here. We hid the way with our magic, for we knew if the stone was found and corrupted, the Lumi-väki would become bound to that evil.

'For many years, the Iron Men were left to their Stone-home. Rarely, one would come to Sûri-kylä to barter for supplies. Then came a foul wind carrying the scent of evil, followed by the worst storm in many generations. No more Iron Men came after that day, and we feared the stone must now be unprotected.

'This key... it will unlock the door to the Oath-stone. Of this Yrjänä is certain. It will be given in trade, but not for goods or currency, no... in return, Yrjänä asks that  makes her/his own oath. Promise to the Lumi-väki that you will protect the stone from Angmar, and promise Yrjänä that you will find a way to destroy the Oath-stone for good. The Lumi-väki wish to be be bound to no-one. We will give our allegiance to those deserving, and fight enemies we understand fully.

'Do you accept?'Yrjänä nods solemnly.

'A pact is made. Go to Salavahti and tell her that Yrjänä has given you Arvedui's key. She is the keeper of ancient things, and of stories from long ago. You will find her on the rise above the village.

'The Lumi-väki are relying on you, ${PLAYER}. Do not fail us.''What brings you to Salavahti, outsider?'

You tell Salavahti that Yrjänä has given you the right to take Arvedui's key. Her eyes widen.

'The Lumi-väki have held this key for many generations. We knew that one day someone would come for it, as they did for the ring of Arvedui. By Yrjänä's will, I offer it into your care.'

Salavahti turns from you, and whispers a prayer in the language of the Lossoth. She then begins humming a single tone, deep in her chest. This tone makes the tall stone spires around you vibrate, and the snow dance, unearthing a square cut-out in the rock you would never have been able to otherwise see. She lifts the square-shaped stone, exposing a hollow space, and stops humming. Inside rests an unassuming bundle of elk-hide, worn with age. Salavahti takes the bundle and unwraps it, revealing an intricately detailed metal key. You see that the key is quite large, and the seven-pointed star of Arnor serves as its handle. This must be the key of Agoroth. Salavahti holds the key toward you, allowing you to take it.

'Our business is concluded, outsider. May you do great things with this. The one known as Lothrandir has come to meet you. Salavahti sees much from this high place. You should go to him.'Surprisingly, Lothrandir has compelled Arvedui to accompany him to the Lossoth village. Lothrandir seems to be telling Arvedui a story, and has not noticed you approach.

You should listen in on their conversation.You approach and listen in on Lothrandir and Arvedui's conversation.'Arvedui has shown us the way to Agoroth. Now, we must prepare to venture inside. Let us hope we have arrived before the Angmarim!'Atli Spider-bane has, at long last, learned the location of his greatest foe, the cause of his deep hatred for the foul creatures.Zaudru has made her lair in the caverns beneath the old dwarf-city of Helegrod, in the Misty Mountains. Atli Spider-bane is in the town of Archet, in Bree-land.

Atli Spider-bane has told you the story of his encounter with Zaudru long years ago and has charged you with carrying out his vengeance.'The city of Helegrod has stood empty for long years, ${PLAYER}, but if wretched Zaudru has chosen as her lair the caverns beneath it, it will not remain so for long. Corcur, Angmarim, giant, or drake will not be able to stand against her, though each of them may believe Zaudru to be an ally. When her brood has grown to sufficient size, she will come forth, and woe to any who stand before her! Helegrod will have a new queen!

'Long years ago, I beheld Zaudru in all her bloated majesty, and it is a sight that will never fully leave my mind. My father and brothers and I had begun mining a decent vein when all about there came a great shaking. Rocks fell from above, and dust filled the air. We ran for the surface, but she was upon us before we had gone fifteen paces. The sound of her evil voice still fills me with dread, though I could not make out many of the words she spoke, save one: "Zaudru" she said, over and over, "Zaudru!" I stumbled into the sunlight, and as I turned back to the entrance of the mine, I saw her great, bloated mass moving through the dust, saw the glint of her small and angry eyes. Then the roof gave way and the entrance collapsed, sealing Zaudru behind a wall of stone. It was all that saved me from her.

'Of a dozen dwarves, only I and two of my brothers escaped her clutches that day. I swore vengeance upon Zaudru and took to hunting any of her kind that crossed my path. She must have followed secret paths through the stone, mile after mile, until she came at last to Helegrod. End her, ${PLAYER}. End her and bring me her crimson mandible. She had only one, but it will be the proof of my vengeance.''I have no words, ${PLAYER}. That Zaudru no longer lives brings me such joy as I cannot relate to you.

'I am forever at your service and your family's. Walk with honour, my friend, for you have slain Zaudru, most wretched of the spiders that creep beneath the mountains.''All who remember the story of mighty Durin and fierce Thorog know of Helegrod, ${PLAYER}, but I did not think to hear its name spoken aloud in my time. Though dwarves repaired the gates and tried to reclaim it after the passage of the dragon, it was not meant to be, and my father and his father before him assumed Helegrod would always stand empty.

'But word now comes to my ears of weaving beneath the city, weaving and the clicking of many legs. The Shadow-brood spiders that infest the caverns beneath Helegrod might stay there for years...any spider-hunter knows that the creatures prefer the darkness beneath the mountains to the light of the sun. But if the wretched creature that birthed these monstrosities turns her eyes towards the exit of her cave, towards the snow-covered slopes of the Misty Mountains....

'We cannot let this happen, ${PLAYER}. Despite the danger, you must descend into the caverns beneath Helegrod and defeat as many of the Shadow-brood as you can. Bring to me their venom, for the venom of one brood is often poisonous to others, and I might be able to make use of it against other of the vile creatures. Only mature spiders are likely to have the potent venom I require, and even then, it will be difficult to slay the spiders that carry it without spilling it.'The Shadow-brood spiders in the caverns beneath Helegrod possess the venom Atli Spider-bane is seeking. Atli is in the town of Archet, in Bree-land.

Atli Spider-bane has asked you to collect venom from the Shadow-brood of Helegrod.Collect Helegrod Shadow-brood Venom (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The snowy paths of Helegrod are filled with ancient snow-beasts.The snow-beasts must be cleared from the paths of Helegrod for any assault to succeed against the Enemy holed up in the ancient dwarf-hold.Defeat ancient snow-beasts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lunathron told you of a great, vile spider, Bogbereth, which hunts in Himbar.Bogbereth hunts in the north-east reaches of Himbar, west and then north of Gath Forthnír.

Lunathron cautioned you not to face Bogbereth with anything less than a fully-armed war-party. She must be defeated, lest she continues to spawn more of her foul brood.Gath Forthnír is in the eastern part of Himbar, south and east of Torech-i-Bogbereth.

Lunathron bade you destroy the great spider, Bogbereth. Now that she is no more, you can return to claim your victory.'This next task you cannot possibly succeed at alone, or even with a fellowship of your closest allies. Nay, you must assemble a war-party if you are to defeat Bogbereth. 

'No ordinary creature is she, Bogbereth, the Poison-queen of Himbar. You must strike swift and true against her, for her hide is as steel armour and her fangs are keen-edged daggers, dripping venom.

'Assemble your band of heroes and journey back to Torech-i-Bogbereth. You will find her there, unless she finds you first.''Have you assembled your war-band yet? Bogbereth will not fall without a fight, and despite your courage, you are no threat to her by yourself.''The great beast is fallen? Then her poisonous reign is ended. This has been another blow to the Iron Crown and the forces of Angmar, and we owe it all to you and your allies.'Grisgart and the drake-brood under his command present a terrible threat to Rivendell.Grisgart, a Man of Angmar, strives to maintain control over the drakes of Helegrod and must be defeated before he can bring his terrible army to bear upon Rivendell.Defeat Grisgart and his drake-brood'If countless drakes and worms now nest within the central keep of Helegrod, it seems the evil history of that place will be continued! It is an insult to the memory of Durin, slain in battle with great Thorog at the gates so many years ago!

'This cannot stand, ${PLAYER}. Journey to Helegrod and defeat the worms and drakes within the keep. I charge you with bringing to me their fangs!

'I have no reward for this task. The honour and sense of duty you possess must serve as reward enough! Do you answer my challenge? Then go to Helegrod, the ancient dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains, and retrieve the fangs of the evil creatures that now lurk within its central keep!'Worms and drakes have come to live within the central keep of Helegrod, the ancient dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains. Ormulf Worm-hunter is in Othrikar, in the North Downs.

Ormulf Worm-hunter has tasked you with retrieving fangs from the drakes and worms that nest within the central keep of Helegrod. He has refused to offer you a reward for this expedition, insisting that the honour of the deed will be reward enough.Collect Cruel Helegrod Fang (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The giant-chieftain Storvâgûn and his kin have fallen under the sway of Angmar and guard the passes into Helegrod.Storvâgûn, leader of the giants of Helegrod, has become corrupted by the forces of Angmar. His defeat will strike a terrible blow against the Iron Crown.Defeat Storvâgûn'Storvâgûn seized control of the cliffs above the old dwarf-city, and with riches from robed Men, he bought the loyalty of many giants!

'Some giants that were my friends, but no more! They are traitors now, slaves to the robed Men who pay Storvâgûn. They do not deserve to be called giants!

'If you have brave friends, go to the old dwarf-city and take away the riches Storvâgûn bribed the giants with! Giants record wealth on notched barter-sticks... take them away! Giants sold their loyalty to Storvâgûn and the robed Men... they do not deserve to keep them! I will burn the sticks when you bring them.'Giants in the service of Storvâgûn and his new masters can be found on the cliffs above Helegrod. Arifael is on Amon Nendir, south-west of Rivendell.

Arifael has asked you to take the notched barter-sticks on which the giants recorded the wealth paid to them by robed Men of Angmar away from them. When you bring him enough of the barter-sticks, he will burn them.Collect Helegrod barter-sticks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'So it seems the inner keep of Helegrod, an ancient dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains, is home to worms and drakes beyond count? It makes sense, though I had never thought about it before now!

'The keep there is the perfect spawning ground for the creatures, you see. Inside the central keep, newly-laid eggs will be protected from the cold winds of the mountains and can be tended by the drakes without fear of interference by snowbeasts or other creatures. I have never been to Helegrod, for it has stood empty since dwarves were unable to hold it even after the passing of Thorog, but I know what it must be like from many stories. Balconies on either side of the main halls, with short stairs climbing to different levels? Large rooms in the centre, with plenty of space for the great creatures to move about? The perfect spawning ground!

'If I could leave Othrikar, I would deal with the ice-hatchlings myself, but I gave my word I would stay. If you, however, will journey to Helegrod and defeat any of the newly-hatched creatures within the keep, honour will be yours!'The central keep of Helegrod is a spawning ground for ice-hatchlings.

Ormulf Worm-hunter has asked you to defeat the ice-hatchlings that are spawning within Helegrod's central keep.Gonediad of Rivendell is worried that Thorog will not long stay behind the walls of Helegrod.The dragon Thorog has been spotted behind the walls of Helegrod, Mírdanant still buried within his neck.

Gonediad of Rivendell has asked you to try and recover the axe of Durin, lost in ancient battle with Thorog at Helegrod.'If the rumour of Thorog's return is true, I fear that the old terrors will seize the people of Eriador. The dragon will not long stay behind the walls of Helegrod.

'And yet this forgotten terror may bring with it hope unlooked-for: Mírdanant, the axe of Durin, is said to remain still buried within the dragon's neck. If Thorog is defeated, the axe might yet be recovered. The fortunes of the dwarves may change for the better once Mírdanant is retrieved, and the words out of Eregion, as well as the friendship of the Gwaith-i-Mírdain with Durin's Folk, might still be proven true.

'I dare not hope that you and your allies could stand triumphant over the might of Thorog that was, for that hope is fleeting. And yet, if you are able to retrieve Mírdanant from the body of ancient Thorog, I know of one unhappy and untrusting dwarf, at least, who might be comforted by its return.''You have done the impossible, ${PLAYER}. Allow me the honour of examining Mírdanant. I never believed this hour would come, the axe of Durin returned from out of the darkness.'Lord Elrond has alerted you to the presence of three servants of Angmar in Helegrod.Grisgart, Adhargal, and Breosal keep the forces of evil under control behind the walls of Helegrod.

Lord Elrond has charged you with defeating the three Angmarim apparently keeping the evils within Helegrod under control and organized.Defeat BreosalDefeat AdhargalDefeat GrisgartMaster Elrond is in the library of Rivendell.

The three servants of Angmar within Helegrod have been defeated. Elrond should be told of your success.Talk to Elrond in the Last Homely House'The picture becomes clearer to me, ${PLAYER}, and I begin to understand what is happening behind the walls of Helegrod.

'Many evils have come to the dwarf-city: spiders, giants, drakes, the dragon Thorog himself... but undirected, each of these would be likely to fight with the others. The evil power that has come again to Angmar would not condone such in-fighting.

'The Iron Crown must have sent trusted servants out of Angmar and into the mountains, I guessed, to keep the evils within Helegrod mindful and under control. My guess has been rewarded, ${PLAYER}: scouts have reported the presence of three powerful Angmarim within the walls. Their names are known to me from the descriptions of my scouts: fierce Adhargal, cruel Grisgart, and unyielding Breosal. They must be defeated, ${PLAYER}, for perhaps then the uneasy alliance within Helegrod will fall apart, and the problem resolve itself.''Seek within Helegrod for the servants of Angmar, ${PLAYER}. If they are defeated, the evils within that ancient city may give in to their natures and fight among themselves.''You have done well to defeat the servants of Angmar behind the walls of Helegrod, ${PLAYER}. That Adhargal and Breosal were slain not by you or your allies, but by the forces of evil they sought to control, tells us much of the enemy we face.

'I thank you again, ${PLAYER}. The mountains are safer for your efforts.'Among the caves of Helegrod dwell the brood of the spider Zaudru.The Angmarim believe they control the spiders of Helegrod...they could not be more mistaken. The vile Zaudru is a force to be reckoned with by any.Defeat Zaudru and her broodArifael has told you the tale of Storvâgûn, the new leader of the giants above Helegrod.The giant Storvâgûn is on the cliffs above Helegrod, the ancient dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains. Arifael is on Amon Nendir, south-west of Rivendell.

Arifael has asked you to take Storvâgûn's emblem of loyalty away from him. Robed Men of Angmar gave the emblem to him in exchange for the service of the giants.'The giants left the dwarf-city alone for a long time, not interested in the empty halls. But Storvâgûn wants leadership, and he says the city belongs to the giants just as the mountains do!

'Robed Men spoke with Storvâgûn, and suddenly he has riches! He pledges loyalty to his new friends, offers them the service of all giants -- all giants, not just himself! When others complain and challenge Storvâgûn, he gives them new wealth! Now many giants have joined Storvâgûn above the old dwarf-city.

'He is no giant. He is a traitor to his people! If you are brave beyond your tiny stature, bring many friends and take Storvâgûn's emblem of loyalty to the robed Men away from him. He only has one. Look for him on cliffs above the old dwarf-city in mountains. I think his new friends mistake Storvâgûn's loyalty. He will betray them too, perhaps! But he betrayed giants first, and he must pay for it.''Storvâgûn is no more? You have the thanks of Arifael, tiny ${RACE}! There is no amount of wealth that will make Arifael forget his true loyalty: to giants, not to robed Men!

'You are strong indeed, and Storvâgûn now knows it! Robed Men know too, and quake in fear, I think!'Elladan has long fought the Corcur of the Trollshaws and the Misty Mountains, and fears their new allegiance to Angmar.The Corcur of Helegrod can be found within its walls, far north of Imladris in the Misty Mountains. Elladan is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges west of Rivendell.

Elladan has told you that each of the Corcur within Helegrod carry talismans from which they believe their strength comes. If enough of these talismans can be taken from their grasp, the will of the Corcur may be broken.'My brother and I have long fought the Corcur, ${PLAYER}, and the news that they have given their allegiance to Angmar and now hold the dwarf-city of Helegrod between their forces are unhappy tidings. They must be driven forth.

'The Corcur carry talismans from which they believe their strength and power comes... we must recover these talismans from the Corcur of Helegrod. They are fierce warriors, but they put such stock in these talismans that their will is broken when they are deprived of them.

'Bring me the talismans from the Corcur of Helegrod, and I will destroy them. Perhaps we can stem this tide before they are ready to sweep down from the mountains in battle!''You have done well, ${PLAYER}, and you have my thanks for this brave deed! I have fought the Corcur, and their ferocity is known to me. Without these talismans, their people will be demoralized. Perhaps they will no longer be the allies that Angmar hoped to have!'Elrohir is troubled by the presence of Angmarim in Helegrod, the old dwarf-city in the mountains north of Rivendell.Angmarim inside Helegrod, the old dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains, bear emblems that reveal their loyalties. Elrohir is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges west of Rivendell.

Elrohir has asked you to defeat Angmarim inside Helegrod and take from them the emblems they carry.'Elladan has told me of the Corcur in Helegrod, ${PLAYER}, and that they have likely sworn fealty to Angmar. This union can bring nothing but hardship to the people of the mountains and to my people in Imladris.

'We must combat the Angmarim before they can prepare their full strength. Helegrod was a city of riches before the dragon came, and even after Thorog was laid low, the dwarves could not reclaim it. I do not doubt that its deepest vaults still contain weapons and devices that might be turned to the service of evil.

'The Angmarim of Helegrod surely carry the signs of their servitude: emblems twisted into evil shape by foul craft. Bring these emblems to me and I will rid the world of them. We will strike a blow against Angmar and its latest fastness by depriving its people of their tokens.''You have done well this day, ${PLAYER}, and Angmar should now fear your name and the names of your allies!

'I will destroy these foul emblems. They set an uneasiness upon my mind, and I am loathe to bear them any longer. I cannot imagine how it must feel to always wear one of these, and proudly, but the Men of Angmar are fallen to darkness and their ways are not our own.

'I thank you again, my friend.''I know not how it has happened, ${PLAYER}, but Thorog has been returned to life through some foul craft! Sigrun and I have seen him, with our own eyes, perched atop the walls of Helegrod like an evil memory given hateful shape.

'So long as the beast lives, the honour of the dwarves is tarnished; both Durin and Mírdanant are lost and cannot rid us of this scourge.

'I do not know if you have allies to rival Durin's great company of old, but it will take many stout hearts to best evil Thorog. If he can be drawn from his perch atop Helegrod, you must do what you can to defeat him, or all the lands will be threatened.'The dragon Thorog has been seen atop the walls of Helegrod, in the Misty Mountains.

Greip and Sigrun have seen Thorog from their small camp north of the source of the Bruinen and have charged you with his defeat.'If the caverns beneath Helegrod are now home to wretched Zaudru, as it seems they must be, every day that passes must see the increase of her spawn. The hatchlings of Zaudru possess an unusually ravenous appetite, even for spiders, and will feast on anything that stumbles near. They have need of great amounts of flesh and blood if they are to grow to adult size.

'We must stop them before they do, ${PLAYER}, for Zaudru gives to her brood the strength and toughness that she herself possesses. Much easier to slay them as hatchlings, I tell you truly!

'The caverns beneath Helegrod are almost certainly riddled with cracks and crevices within which Zaudru's Shadow-brood hatchlings vie for dominance. Approach these holes and slay as many of the creatures as emerge into the light.'The caverns beneath Helegrod are riddled with cracks and crevices, home to Zaudru's hatchlings.

Atli Spider-bane has asked you to slay as many Shadow-brood hatchlings as you can find beneath Helegrod.<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Acquire the Rambling Rover TitleRansacking GathbúrzRansacking GathbúrzRansacking GathbúrzRansacking GathbúrzYour attacks are quick, numerous, and without mercy.Use Upshot, The One Trap, or Rapid FireIt is rumoured that there are many relics of the ancient days remaining in Sarnúr, which the Dourhands seek to recover.Glúmir can be found in Sarnúr, south of Thorin's Hall, reached through the ruins of Orodost.

Rútur has asked you to find the Dourhand Glúmir, defeat him, and recover any rune-shards you may find.Defeat Glúmir and recover the rune-shardsRútur is in Thorin's Hall, north of Sarnúr, just outside the Blue Stone Garrison.

You should bring the rune-shard to Rútur and tell him of Glúmir's defeat.'Within the depths of Sarnúr, a large company of cowardly Dourhands have fled and established a camp. Among them, a particularly foul brigand by the name of Glúmir has been attempting to gather relics of the ancient days. 

'If you travel to Sarnúr, would you seek out Glúmir, defeat him, and gather any rune-shards that he might possess?

'Sarnúr can be found south of Thorin's Hall, deep beyond the ruins of Orodost, which is located on the western mountains of Ered Luin.''Collect the rune-shards for me, ${PLAYER}...I will reward you as best I may.''Your deeds this day will be told to all who live within Thorin's Hall. 

'I will begin to study these rune-shards to determine the reason that Glúmir was gathering them. 

'If you are to travel again to Sarnúr, please come and find me, as I may ask you to recover more of these shards.'You have aided in the search for the lost Ring-lore of Eregion.You have aided in the search for the lost Ring-lore of Eregion.The Dourhands, after fleeing Thorin's Hall in defeat, took refuge in the ruins of one of their ancient cities, now called by the Elves Sarnúr.Dourhands can be found in Sarnúr, south of Thorin's Hall, reached through the ruins of Orodost.

Rútur has asked you to seek out the Dourhands of Sarnúr and defeat them.Defeat Dourhand excavators (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Dourhand blasters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rútur is in Thorin's Hall, north of Sarnúr, just outside the Blue Stone Garrison.

You should return to Rútur with news of your victory against the Dourhands of Sarnúr.Talk to Rútur in Thorin's Hall'The Dourhands have been driven from Thorin's Hall, ${PLAYER}, yet the vermin still infest these mountains. 

'Seek out the Dourhands that have taken refuge in the ruins of Sarnúr and defeat them, then return to me. If you travel to this place, be aware that many of the creatures within are protected against weapons not of our making.  

'Travel to Sarnúr, south of Thorin's Hall deep within the ruins of Orodost, which can be found along the western mountains of Ered Luin.''Thank you for seeking out the vile vermin and driving them back into the ruins. The Dwarves of Thorin's Hall are deeply indebted to you.

'If you journey into Sarnúr again, please seek me out, for I may have more tasks for you.''Stop the Dourhands, ${PLAYER}...they are a disgrace to all of dwarf-kind!'The secrets of rune-lore lie open to you. Meaning upon meaning lies within them, and their power sings in your blood.Dardúr is at Gondamon in Ered Luin.

You have been told to seek the wisdom of the rune-keeper Dardúr.Meet Dardúr for further Rune-keeper trainingDardúr is at Gondamon in Ered Luin.

You have been told to seek the wisdom of the rune-keeper Dardúr.Talk to Dardúr at GondamonAs a Rune-keeper, you have achieved such renown as to receive a summons from Dardúr of Gondamon.

You should seek Dardúr to receive further training in your class.'Welcome and well met, ${PLAYER}. I have heard of your cunning in the ways of the graven rune. Our sort are rare in Middle-earth, and I fear that soon we will pass away.'Whether they burn hot or fall in a rain of arrows, they will fall.Use Burn Hot, Rain of Thorns, or BarrageVast riches were granted to Storvâgûn by the Men of Angmar. Although many of his trinkets bear the corruption of the Witch-king of Angmar, brave adventurers might uncover the most valuable of Storvâgûn's riches.Storvâgûn can be encountered during the Yule Festival in Boss From The Vaults: Storvâgûn.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest can only be advanced on Tier 2 of Boss From The Vaults: Storvâgûn. In addition, this quest can only be completed once per Yule Festival.</rgb>Collect vile gold coins from Storvâgûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Verbena Greenhand can be found in Frostbluff.

You have collected a number of vile gold coins and you should now deliver them to Verbena Greenhand.'Hallo there! How are you enjoying the Yule Festival?

'Plenty of food and a bit of theatre... how grand! I wonder, though. I heard a curious tale from one of the patrons of Winter-home. Have you heard it as well?

'No? Well, it goes that there was once a greedy, old giant named Storvâgûn who lived above Helegrod. He was so greedy that he decided to speak for all of his friends and make a deal with some nasty Men from the North. Even worse, all his friends went along with it - except for one! That one, Arifael, was a better sort of giant... a friendly giant! So Arifael found some new friends and sent them to stop old Storvâgûn from being so selfish! And then they took all of his treasure!

'You know, saying that out loud... I think I have forgotten the lesson of the tale. But I am certain there is one!

'Anyway, rumour has it that old Storvâgûn returns to count his riches atop Helegrod during the Yule Festival. I'm not sure I believe it, but if it were true, I bet a brave adventurer like you could snatch a few coins out from under his nose!

'I'd make it worth your while, but if you go looking for his gold, don't blame me if you find him too!''Well, well! You look chilled to the marrow, my dear! I ought to have known better than to send you up to old Helegrod! Did you find any of old Storvâgûn's coins?

'So the tale was true! I knew it!

'I'm afraid I've no scarves or cloaks to offer you, but perhaps this will do?'Sergeant Tom has heard the tale of adventurers facing Naruhel the Red-maid and would like you to bring him evidence of your good deeds.Bloody gold coins can be earned by defeating Naruhel once per day during the Spring Festival in Boss From The Vaults: Naruhel.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest can only be advanced on Tier 3 of Boss From The Vaults: Naruhel. In addition, this quest can only be completed once per Spring Festival.</rgb>Collect bloody gold coins from Naruhel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sergeant Tom can be found at the festival grounds within the Horsefields in Bree-land.

You have collected a number of bloody golden coins, and you should now deliver them to Sergeant Tom.'Hello there! Enjoying the Spring Festival? Say, if you're feeling brave, I've got a job you would be perfect for!

'One day, I was enjoying a meal and a drink at the Prancing Pony, and I overhead a Minstrel spinning some tales. He told the story of a corrupted spring that lies deep within the Garth Agarwen, a fortress within the Lone-lands. It is said that a water-maid by the name of Naruhel resides deep within, and has fallen due to blood spilled in her waters during the wars between Angmar and the North Kingdom.

'Within the swamp, there are a series of golden coins that were given as a gift to the river-maiden. Sadly these coins, much like the creature herself, have become darkened by the blood throughout the area.

'As hope springs eternal, our hope is that you could cleanse this creature of the taint infecting the surrounding lands. If you bring me coins that bear her plight as proof of this deeds, I will reward you for your efforts!'You hold out the coins you have gathered. Sergeant Tom accepts them, nodding solemnly.

'These are surely the same coins that I heard tale of from the minstrel. Thank you, adventurer, for braving that terrible place in the hope to lend some aid to the people of the Lone-lands.

'Here, take this gift. It's the least I can do. Enjoy the rest of the Spring Festival!'You have aided in the search for the lost Ring-lore of Eregion.You have aided in the search for the lost Ring-lore of Eregion.The Brawler has unique talents and it would be a shame not to share them with the world.Use any "Share Innate Strength" skillDanger lurks within Barad Gúlaran and Uidon, an Elf dispatched to the north to support those sent there by the Council of Esteldín, wishes to examine the armour worn by the fell spirits within the citadel. You must smite the defenders and warriors within Barad Gúlaran to obtain the armour.Ancient armour wreathes terrifying creatures within Barad Gúlaran. Collect these items and return them to Uidon at the encampment in the north-eastern area of Angmar.

Uidon asked you to obtain samples of the armour worn by the defenders within Barad Gúlaran so he might learn a weakness to better defeat them. Make your way into Barad Gúlaran, with the assistance of others and collect the samples.'Within the walls of Barad Gúlaran you will find many enemies. One enemy in particular concerns me and intrigues me more than any other. I know we must destroy the keeper of Barad Gúlaran, but the servants who have walked the halls for ages intrigue me more.

'Clad in ancient iron, these spirits from the Shadow keep an eternal watch over the former home of the Witch-king.

'I wish to study the armour and determine how these creatures were able to manifest themselves in such a way. Perhaps there is a way we can defeat them without bringing forth our swords and arrows.

'Enter Barad Gúlaran and collect twelve pieces of the armour so I may sate my curiosity and discover a weakness to these creatures.''I am pleased to see that you are hale and whole, ${PLAYER}. I am pleased greater still that you acquired such fine specimens. I shall begin my research immediately.

'You have earned much thanks from myself and others, ${CLASS}. Accept this token, though it is a pittance compared to all you do it is what we can spare.'Taunt your foes without relent, for you know they would not spare you or your allies the blade.Strike with Shield-tauntEarn a name for yourself and improve the reliability of your most deadly attack.Strike with Heart SeekerEarn a name for yourself and improve the reliability of your most deadly attack.Strike with Heart-seekerRuidhriel has asked for your aid in confusing the events of the Burnt Tor.Charred wood can be found on the Burnt Tor, west of Ruidhriel.

Ruidhriel has asked that you gather charred wood for her to study in hopes of finding out what happened there.'A short while ago, as the Elves would recount it, a copse of ancient trees stood here, but it seems that strange deeds have taken place that I cannot yet explain.

'Something has happened upon the hilltop. I fear that the Company may have encountered a powerful enemy; even the smallest clue could bring disastrous news to our enemies.  

'You must go and collect some of the charred remains and bring them here for me to study. You will find the charred wood lying upon the ground throughout the Burnt Tor.''It is as I feared: this wood was not burned by natural means. A word of command was used to light the fire that kindled this wood.'Brúnfair, recently dispatched to the north, brings ill tidings and carries a heavy concern on his careworn shoulders. Recent events within the black citadel of Barad Gúlaran have forced him into action.

He has requested that you gather assistance from your fellows in seeking the destruction of a cabal of sorceresses who are attempting to see Amarthiel's will carried forth.Find the three Sorceresses within Barad Gúlaran and defeat them. If they are stopped, then there will be no others to carry out the will of Amarthiel.

Brúnfair asked you to search through the halls of Barad Gúlaran in search of the sorceresses left in charge of carrying out Amarthiel's will. Find them and destroy them.You have defeated the sorceresses within Barad Gúlaran. Return to Brúnfair at the Ranger encampment in the north-eastern section of Angmar and tell him of your success.

Searching through the halls of Barad Gúlaran you discovered and defeated the sorceresses responsible for carrying out the machinations of Amarthiel in Angmar.'We face a grave enemy in these lands, ${CLASS}. The work ahead of us is perilous, but we cannot falter.

'With the discovery of Amarthiel and her ties to Angmar, we have learned a great deal of the enemy we face. Within Barad Gúlaran we face a cabal of sorcerers who are trained in dark arts that threaten life.

'I must ask you for assistance. I require you to enter that accursed place in search of the three sorceresses who carry out the will of Amarthiel. End their plot before they succeed and return to me with news of your victory.''Quickly, now. We must crush this coven before it grows into a larger threat to all of Eriador.''This reprieve must be used to gain a stronger foothold here, friend. We shall not relent in our efforts to secure Angmar and crumble the swelling shadow here.

'You have played an instrumental part in forging a better future for Eriador and you are well-deserved of this reward. You have my thanks and the thanks of all who would remain free throughout Eriador.'A strong finish makes your words and melodies all the more potent.Score Critical Hits with CodasStand at Ost GaladhStand at Ost GaladhStand at Ost GaladhStand at Ost GaladhIf you can internalize the age old maxim, you may find the right location easier to arrive at and more effective than before.Use the Location is Everything skillYou have aided in the search for the lost Ring-lore of Eregion.You have aided in the search for the lost Ring-lore of Eregion.The Rangers have taken the court of Clorhir in front of the pools of Glinghant.Harthadril is at the Ranger-encampment in the court of Clorhir, in front of the entrance to the pools of Glinghant, on a higher level of the city.

Quartermaster Badhordam has asked you to carry a crate of supplies to Harthadril at the forward position of Clorhir. He recommended that you bring some strong allies to protect you while you are carrying the crate, for Angmarim will surely attempt to disrupt this attempt at resupply.Collect crate of suppliesQuartermaster Badhordam is at Echad Garthadir, the Ranger-encampment at the heart of Annúminas.

