'However, we are sure to lose this foothold if we cannot supply them! I want you to bring a crate of supplies to Harthadril at Clorhir. She will be grateful for the delivery. Just pick up one of the crates from this stack, and carry it to Harthadril.

'Return to me once you have done this, but be warned: you would best bring some strong allies to safe-guard you as you carry the crate. The Angmarim will try to prevent our resupply of Clorhir if they can.''Clorhir is on a higher level of the city, ${PLAYER}. Pick up a crate from the stack here and carry it to Harthadril.

'You should bring a few strong allies with you to protect you, because your hands will be full while you are carrying the crate.''I thank you for that, ${PLAYER}. We cannot hope to hold our forward positions, if we cannot keep them supplied, and we cannot deal with the threat of the darkwater that infest Glinghant if we lose control of Clorhir.'The Rangers at Annúminas need supplies to continue their fight there.Badhordam is at Echad Garthadir, the Ranger-encampment at the heart of Annúminas.

Cuguminuial has asked you to carry a crate of supplies to Badhordam, the quartermaster at Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas. She warned you not to get the crate wet and to bring friends who can protect you while you are carrying it. She is worried that unless the Dúnedain control the gate at the courtyard of Gwaelband, you might not be able to find a safe route to Echad Garthadir.Collect crate of suppliesBadhordam is at the Ranger-encampment of Echad Garthadir, in Annúminas.

You have delivered a crate of supplies from Tinnudir to Echad Garthadir and should now speak with Badhordam, the quartermaster of the camp.'It is all we can do to keep Fainneleg's encampment supplied, ${PLAYER}. His Rangers are hard-pressed at Echad Garthadir in the heart of Annúminas, and I fear that without fresh supplies, they will not be able to hold out much longer.

'Can I ask you to bring a crate of supplies to Badhordam, Fainneleg's quartermaster at Echad Garthadir? You will need some friends to guard you while you carry the crate, for fighting inside the city can be intense at times.

'The crate has many cracks and holes in the bottom -- do not get it wet, or its contents will be ruined! I hope the gate at the courtyard of Gwaelband is held by the Dúnedain; if it is not, I do not know how you will get the crate to Echad Garthadir.''Thank you for these supplies, ${PLAYER}. Cuguminuial is right -- these should allow us to keep fighting for a few more days.

'As we gain more footholds further in the city, we must keep them resupplied.''Do not get the crate wet, bring friends to protect you on your way, and hope that the Dúnedain still control the gate at Gwaelband; if we do not, I do not think you will be able to find a route to Echad Garthadir.

'It will not be easy, ${PLAYER}, but these supplies could spell the difference between victory and defeat for the Rangers under Fainneleg's command! Badhordam is his quartermaster, and will be very grateful for these supplies.'The Rangers have taken control of Tirband, the court in front of the great watch-tower on the highest level of the city.Legrindavor is at Tirband, the court on the highest level of the city, from which the great watch-tower looks out over Lake Nenuial.

