You should return to Authlanc and tell him of your success.Talk to Authlanc at Echad Dúnann'No doubt your gaze has been drawn to the peaks of Celebdil, Caradhras, and Fanuidhol, but there a great shadow often defeats my eyes. Great, dark clouds move against the wind, and they pass over the land in search of something.

'Flocks of black-winged crebain from Dunland have been circling the Redhorn Gate. It is clear that they are searching for the Company, and I fear that they may have news or have found some clue that we have not ourselves discovered.

'Travel north-east into the Redhorn Gate and defeat these spies of Saruman, then return to me.''Just before your return a great concourse of birds flew hastily from the Redhorn Gate. Let us hope that you set enough fear into their ranks to drive them from Eregion, though I doubt not that they will return to pick the bones of the fallen.''The crebain can be found in the Redhorn Gate north-east of Echad Dúnann.'Defeat the Dead in Barad Gúlaran.Defeat the Dead in Barad GúlaranDefeat the Dead in Barad Gúlaran.Defeat the Dead in Barad GúlaranBrom Hawksbeard has heard that another Brawler such as you was seen travelling through Bree-land, heading north.Brom Hawksbeard wrote to you, telling you to seek out a Rohirric Brawler by the name of Hunward. Hunward was seen heading for Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.${PLAYER},

Folk around Bree-town have been discussing a curious fellow who passed through town recently. Rohirric, they thought he was, name of Hunward, and he headed north in the direction of the Wildwood. I think he was a Brawler same as us, ${PLAYER}! You'd better go see if you can find him. Like as not he'll have some useful skills to impart!

I expect you'll find him at Trader's Wharf.

Brom Hawksbeard'Ah, you seek instruction in the finer points of brawling? That you know such things exist proves you are a Brawler like few others! Most think it as simple as punching first with your left hand and then with your right, but there is a great deal more to it than that, as you and I are both well aware!

'I am pleased to hear of your willingness to learn. Many underestimate the danger of a competent Brawler; sometimes, the deadliest punch is the first one you throw against such a foe!'The drake-queen rules the wilds of Urugarth, spawning broods of drakelings that ravage the countryside.The drake-queen and her brood of eggs lies in Urugarth to the west of Tármunn Sûrsa.

Esmë advised you to destroy the eggs of the drake-queen.Destroy drake-eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Esmë is at Tármunn Súrsa, east of Urugarth.

You should return to Esmë with news of your success.'Gormal tells me that you will attempt to slay the drake-queen. A noble quest, and I wish you good hunting, but killing the drake-queen will only bring temporary reprieve.

'If left unchecked, her brood of eggs will hatch, and one of her drakelings will grow to take her place. You should destroy her eggs and make sure that nothing exists to inherit her legacy as the Scourge of Urugarth.

'Continue on your quest to Urugarth. It lies to the west.''The eggs are destroyed? That is good. The young drakes are not as powerful as the queen, but they are just as vicious and evil.''Go into Urugarth and destroy the eggs of the drake-queen.'Iorelen was sent to the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu to investigate the activities of Angmar in the area and the existence of a deadly mushroom found there which could be used by the Enemy to create a terrible weapon. He is also seeking a race of giants of which he learned from Glorfindel at Rivendell.The Eldgang can be found deep within the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.

Iorelen has asked you to seek out signs of the Eldgang, the legendary Fire-giants of Nûrz Ghâshu.Iorelen is at Iorelen's Camp.

You should return to Iorelen with news of what you found within the Rift.'Master Elrond sent me here to the Rift, which is called Nûrz Ghâshu by the Enemy, to investigate rumours of forays therein by Angmar's forces. There are veins of valuable metals and a variety of deadly mushrooms which might be used to produce a terrible weapon for the Enemy.

'Lord Glorfindel told me, as well, of a legend of a race of giants which dwell deep in the heart of Nûrz Ghâshu. This legend greatly interests me, for it is said these giants, the Eldgang, are not of an evil bent and may help us to combat Angmar.

'Will you enter the Rift and seek out the Eldgang? If you find them, I will reward you according to your deeds.''I am interested in learning more of this Eldgang.''The Eldgang still dwell within the Rift? If they can be swayed to join in our fight, we could well defeat Angmar.

'Rivendell should be informed at once!'Once the seat of power from which the Witch-king's army marched upon the kingdom of Arnor, Carn Dûm now exists as the primary bastion of the Steadfast of Angmar.Once the seat of power from which the Witch-king's army marched upon the kingdom of Arnor, Carn Dûm now exists as the primary bastion of the Steadfast of Angmar.Amid the foul waters of Carn Dûm lies the slave-pens of the Trév Duvárdain. It is here that those who have challenged the might of the Steward of Angmar are pressed into his service against their will.The Gorthorog-captain Barashal commands his minions from this post within the eastern crags on the outskirts of Carn Dûm.The water you found in this place was a putrescent green, contaminated with the vile poisons of Carn Dûm.While Carn Dûm has many enemies, there are those that call it ally as well. Among them are the Hillmen of the Trév Duvárdain. This alliance has granted the Trév Duvárdain a district of their own within the city.It is from the Castle of Carn Dûm that the Witch-king of Angmar oversaw his domain, and it is from here that Mordirith, the Steward of Angmar, does the same.The Seat of the Witch-king is a well-appointed room adorned with vicious looking statues and ornaments. It was here that the Ranger Golodir confronted Moridirth in battle and forced retreat upon the Steward of Angmar.Looking south over the sprawl of Carn Dûm, this balcony affords the perfect location to survey the whole of the city.Because you have provided a great deal of assistance to the dwarves of Bósi and Brogur's expedition, they want to ensure that you know the story of Moria's fall before you help them further.Ráthwald is by the archway near the camp of Echad Dúnann in Eregion.

You have provided much assistance to the dwarves of the expedition, and should now return to Ráthwald to hear the tale of the fall of Moria.Ráthwald is by the archway near the camp of Echad Dúnann in Eregion.

Ráthwald has agreed to tell you the tale of the fall of Moria.Ráthwald is by the archway near the camp of Echad Dúnann in Eregion.

Ráthwald has told you the tale of the fall of Moria and is waiting to speak with you.'You have done us a great service already, friend, but there is something you should know about the Mines before you accompany the Iron Garrison into the mountains. Speak to me if you are willing to hear what I have to say.''You have been a tremendous help to us, ${PLAYER}, and have aided us with so many tasks! You have enabled the exploration of both the Brackwater and Filgogân for lost friends and hidden treasure, and have valiantly withstood the threats within.

'But the halls and caverns of Khazad-dûm may harbour even greater danger, and I want you to know what you will be getting into before you follow us past the Doors of Durin.

'Return to Ráthwald who stands guard by the camp of Echad Dúnann, and have him tell you the tale of the fall of Moria. He will speak of dark times, but you should know the story before you walk into the dark, even if it makes you think ill of Khazad-dûm -- though I hope it will not be so.''You have been a tremendous help to us, ${PLAYER}, and have aided us with so many tasks! You have helped us to explore both the Brackwater and Filgogân for lost friends and hidden treasure, and have stood tall against the threats within.

'But the halls and caverns of Khazad-dûm may hold even greater danger, and I want you to know what you will be getting into before you follow us past the Doors of Durin.

'Return to Ráthwald, on guard by the camp of Echad Dúnann, where the road passes beneath the old Elf-arch, and have him tell you the tale of the fall of Moria. They were dark times, but you should know the story, even if you have heard it before.''You have been a tremendous help to us, ${PLAYER}, and have aided us with so many tasks! You have helped us to explore both the Brackwater and Filgogân for lost friends and hidden treasure, and have stood tall against the threats within.

