'But the halls and caverns of Khazad-dûm may hold even greater danger, and I want you to know what you will be getting into before you follow us past the Doors of Durin.

'Return to Ráthwald, on guard by the camp of Echad Dúnann, where the road passes beneath the old Elf-arch, and have him tell you the tale of the fall of Moria. They were dark times, but you should know the story, even if you have heard it before.''You have already lent great service to our expedition, ${PLAYER}, and I do not wish to be held responsible if you come to a...bad sort of end. The history of Khazad-dûm is sad and grim, and it is Bósi's wish that all who lend their aid to our cause know what might await them inside the mines.

'I will tell you the story of the fall of Moria, if you will hear it, and give reasons why Khazad-dûm is called "Moria" by the Elves: "Black Pit."

'Listen well, and if you still wish to follow the dwarves into Moria, we can talk it over.''Though Náin and his kinsmen stood against the great evil that slew Durin, they did not stand long: Náin was killed by the shadow the following year and the dwarves were forced to abandon Khazad-dûm. Many of the Silvan Elves fled Lothlórien in terror of the nameless fear, flying southward and cursing the dwarves as they went.

'From time to time some brave dwarf has been known to seek those halls. Lord Balin is the most recent, but despite some encouraging reports shortly after his expedition arrived, we have not heard from him in many years, and begin to despair of finding him again.

'Bósi fears that he has perished, but it could be that Balin lives still within some deep hall. It is possible, but my thoughts are like to Bósi's. Thank you for listening to the tale, my friend. You see now how important this expedition is to my people.''Listen well, ${PLAYER}, and I will tell you the tale of the Fall of Moria.'Skygni wishes to tell you the tale of the fall of Moria so that you can better appreciate what the expedition has accomplished.Skygni is in the Twenty-first Hall in Moria.

Skygni has agreed to tell you the tale of the fall of Moria.Talk to Skygni and listen to the tale of the fall of MoriaSkygni is in the Twenty-first Hall in Moria.

Skygni has told you the tale of the fall of Moria and is waiting to speak with you.'I will tell you the story of the fall of Moria, if you will hear it. Perhaps one day your part in our expedition to reclaim this place will be an important narrative for a new tale, eh?

'I warn you thus: it is a sad story. Only now do we endeavour to give it a happier ending.''Though Náin and his kinsmen stood against the great evil that slew Durin, they did not stand long: Náin was killed by the shadow the following year and the dwarves were forced to abandon Khazad-dûm. Many of the Silvan Elves departed Lothlórien in anger and fear, flying southward and cursing the dwarves as they went.

'Thank you for listening to the tale, my friend. You see now the importance of this expedition to my people.''Listen well, ${PLAYER}, and I will tell you the tale of the Fall of Moria.'You have defeated Thaurlach and hold in your possession a broken link of the great chain which once held the Balrog in his prison.Elrond is at the Last Homely House in Rivendell, in the Trollshaws far to the south of Angmar.

You have defeated the Balrog Thaurlach and should inform Elrond Halfelven of your deeds.Glorfindel may be found outside the Last Homely House standing next to the Bruinen.

Elrond suggested you speak with Glorfindel about the defeat of Thaurlach, for the tale concerns him greatly.'This great broken link was once part of the great chain which bound the Balrog Thaurlach within his prison. You wonder if you should perhaps bring it and the news of the Balrog's defeat to Master Elrond in Rivendell.''Greetings, ${PLAYER}! What is this you say? You found the prison of the Balrog Thaurlach?

'It is well that you defeated him. Long ago was he chained, though he should have been destroyed. It was not in wisdom that he was spared.

'But that is a long tale, full of sorrow. You should speak with Glorfindel, for this concerns him greatly. You may find him outside standing next to the Bruinen above the falls.''Speak with Glorfindel and tell him of your victory against the Balrog Thaurlach.''Hail and well met, ${PLAYER}. I understand you wish to speak with me?'At some point you gained the attention of the Fashion Maven, who judged your appearance and found it lacking.Bring the Fashion Maven's scroll to an Outfitter to exchange it for the package left for you by the Maven. Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.This elegantly written scroll directs you to take it to an Outfitter, who will exchange it for a package left behind for you by the Fashion Maven. It goes on to say that Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.'Oh dear, I'm surprised you actually came to get the Fashion Maven's package for you. Few people can actually bear the shame her poor judgement brings! However, from looking at your appearance, I can tell you are not one who cares much what others think about them.

'Perhaps, after you have taken what the Maven left for you, you could make use of my shop? It certainly couldn't hurt!'At some point you gained the attention of the Fashion Maven, who judged your appearance and found you stunning, a paragon of fashion!Bring the Fashion Maven's scroll to an Outfitter to exchange it for the package left for you by the Maven. Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.This elegantly written scroll directs you to take it to an Outfitter, who will exchange it for a package left behind for you by the Fashion Maven. It goes on to say that Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.'My goodness, you are dressed well! I can see why the Fashion Maven judged you so well! There is little I can offer you to improve your appearance, other than the notice you so richly deserve for your wonderful taste!

'Thank you, ${PLAYER} for gracing my presence. You have shown me all that is possible with a well appointed appearance.'At some point you gained the attention of the Fashion Maven, who judged your appearance and found it lacking.Bring the Fashion Maven's scroll to an Outfitter to exchange it for the package left for you by the Maven. Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.This elegantly written scroll directs you to take it to an Outfitter, who will exchange it for a package left behind for you by the Fashion Maven. It goes on to say that Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.'Oh hello! You've received one of the Fashion Maven's scrolls have you? Well I can see why she judged your appearance to be... well, lacking. However, there is still hope for you, so please choose one of the gifts left behind for you by the Maven! Perhaps next time the Maven will judge you better, eh?'At some point you gained the attention of the Fashion Maven, who judged your appearance and found it lacking.Bring the Fashion Maven's scroll to an Outfitter to exchange it for the package left for you by the Maven. Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.This elegantly written scroll directs you to take it to an Outfitter, who will exchange it for a package left behind for you by the Fashion Maven. It goes on to say that Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.'Oh hello! You've received one of the Fashion Maven's scrolls have you? Well I can see why she judged your appearance to be... well, lacking. However, there is still hope for you, so please choose one of the gifts left behind for you by the Maven! Perhaps next time the Maven will judge you better, eh?'Your constant harassment of the Angmarim has not gone unnoticed. The Rangers wish to push the fight to the Gates of Carn Dûm itself and defeat the leader of the Angmarim in Himbar.Garthamendir guards the gates of Carn Dûm to the west.

Areneth warned you of the Cargûl and its terrible wrath. But killing the fell creature is the only way to break the Angmarim forces. He warned you not to face Garthamendir alone.Areneth is at Gath Forthnír, east of Carn Dûm.

Garthamendir was defeated and his forces shattered. You should return to Areneth with the news.'I know a way to take the fire from the Angmarim. But I must warn you that this is no mean feat. I cannot promise you will return from this battle.

'There is a creature that commands the Angmarim. The wraith Garthamendir, a Cargûl that guards the gate of Carn Dûm. It is the thing that spurs the Angmarim into battle, the thing they fear more than your steel or the arrows of my Rangers.

'Find the Cargûl at the gates of Carn Dûm to the west. Rest first and gather your strength. You will need all of it if you are to triumph. And go not alone!''Your courage inspires my men, ${PLAYER}. With the wraith defeated, the Angmarim scurry in search of a new leader. We will attack them while they are at their weakest.''Garthamendir will fall this day, I can feel it on the wind. Head to the Gates of Carn Dûm in the north-west corner of Himbar.'The Dunlendings remain in Eregion, despite their defeat, indicating the presence of a powerful leader.The Uruk Gâmzhurm can be found south and slightly west of Echad Dúnann, across Nan Sirannon.

You must use the horn of challenge to summon Gâmzhurm, the leader of the Dunlendings, and defeat him.Glavroleth is at Echad Dúnann, north and slightly east of Porth Cadlus.

You should return to Glavroleth with the news of Gâmzhurm's death.Talk to Glavroleth at Echad Dúnann'Though the Dunlendings were weakened by our assault, they have not departed from Eregion. Something else holds their will and drives their assaults.

'One of my scouts came upon one of the Dunlendings in the wilderness who had deserted their camp. He spoke of one of Saruman's Uruk-hai who commands the camp and drives the Dunlendings to madness.

'Return to Porth Cadlus and challenge this Uruk to single combat. If he is defeated, many of the Dunlendings will lay down arms and return to their homeland.''With their leader defeated, the Dunlendings will not continue their assault. You have our deepest thanks, ${PLAYER}.''You may find a horn at the Dunlending encampment which may be used to challenge the uruk.'Tortrygg is concerned with the invasion of Norbar by the Orcs.Narnûlubat and Zogtark can be found within Noruidor.

Tortrygg has asked to you to find and defeat two of the leaders of the Ghâshfra, Narnûlubat and Zogtark.Defeat NarnûlubatDefeat ZogtarkTortrygg is at the Eldgang camp within the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.

You should return to Tortrygg with news of your victory against Narnûlubat and Zogtark.'You are a friend to us, little one? Then hear me, Tortrygg of Norbar. Evil Fire-orcs came from the surface world to conquer us and unleash the Great Evil. They kill us, we kill them...it does not end.

'I ask you to help us end this war. Help us to drive back the Fire-Orcs. If you can slay Narnûlubat and Zogtark, two of the leaders of the Ghâshfra, the Fire-orcs, the others might leave.

'Will you help us? Narnûlubat and Zogtark may be found within Noruidor.''Evil things invade our home...help us to defeat them, ${PLAYER}.''You are a mighty warrior, little one. You are deserving of this reward, though I fear your success was not enough to drive away the Ghâshfra.'Defeat Angmarim in Barad Gúlaran.Defeat Angmarim in Barad GúlaranDefeat Angmarim in Barad Gúlaran.Defeat Angmarim in Barad GúlaranYou earned this title during the Season of the Nemesis Reward Track Season in Monster Play.Aragorn is concerned that his ancestor Arvedui lingers still in Middle-earth, haunting the wreck of the Thoroval.Elrond can be found in his library in the Last Homely House.

You should talk to Elrond.Talk to ElrondLothrandir can be found outside the village of Sûri-kylä in Forochel.

You should find Lothrandir and explain Elrond's request.Find Lothrandir in ForochelLothrandir is prepared to travel to the shipwreck of the Thoroval to meet Arvedui.

Speak with Lothrandir at Sûri-kylä to enter 'Instance: Dúnedain Past and Present'.Complete 'Instance: Dúnedain Past and Present'Lothrandir is with the shade of Arvedui at the shipwreck of the Thoroval.

You should talk to Lothrandir.Talk to Lothrandir'I would take a moment more of your time before you depart, ${PLAYER}.

'Though our mission to thwart the schemes of Amarthiel and Mordrambor must be our main focus, I sorrow that the shade of my ancestor lingers, burdened by great remorse. There must be something we can do to ease his spirit.

'Please, speak with Lord Elrond on my behalf. If anyone among the living knows what can be done, it will be him.''Back so soon, ${PLAYER}?'

You explain that Aragorn wishes to find some way to put the shade of Arvedui to rest, and sent you to Elrond for his help.

'We are in agreement. I knew King Arvedui in life. He deserves a better fate than to linger in the frozen wastes, tormented by his past. Relieving him of his burden will be no easy task, however.'

Elrond furrows his brow, deep in thought.

'Truthfully, I do not know how best to help him. In my experience, shades of Men often linger in the world because of something unfinished: an oath unfulfilled, an oath broken. Perhaps if you spend time with Arvedui, you will learn why he lingers, and find a way to relieve his burden. To that end, I have a request that might lead to salvation for the fallen king and also thwart the Enemy.'

Elrond motions to the book on the table, and opens it to a page marked with a piece of tasseled cloth. You see that it contains a list of many dated entries, logging something. The seven-pointed star of Arnor illustrates one of the pages.

'As you have seen, Angmar has committed many forces to Forochel, conscripting the local Gauredain into their ranks, sending more soldiers than necessary for the purpose we believed they possessed. They are searching for something, and I have finally found a clue as to what that might be. 

'This record recovered from Annúminas details significant troop movements from the years 500 to 600 of the Third Age. There, on that page, it states that a large contingent of soldiers and Prince Elendur himself moved an "item of great importance" from Ost Forod into the North. It does not declare what this item is, or where precisely it came to rest. I have a suspicion as to what it might be, and if I am correct, it is surely what the Angmarim seek in the frozen wilds of Forochel.

'First, I would ask you to seek the Ranger known as Lothrandir. I believe he is still among the Lossoth, and should you encounter the Angmarim in force, I fear you will have need of his sword-arm. Together, bring this information to Arvedui. As the King of Arthedain, he may know where this secret treasure was hidden by the Arnorians all those years ago.

'If fate is kind, you will find the treasure before the Angmarim can seize it for their dark masters. If it is kinder still, you will also find a way to put Arvedui's spirit to rest. I wish you luck, ${PLAYER}.''Hello, ${PLAYER}. What has brought you back to Forochel? Is everything well in Rivendell?'

You explain Elrond's request to find the missing Arnorian treasure before the Angmarim, and to try to put Arvedui's shade to rest.

'You bring tidings of high adventure, and it would be a great honour to assist you in finding a lost treasure of the Dúnedain, and to meet King Arvedui himself! We must not tarry here, then, if we are to find it before the Angmarim. Let us travel to the shipwreck of the Thoroval at once!''We will depart for the Thoroval when you are ready.''Lord Elrond's intuition was correct. King Arvedui was a valuable source of information, but the Angmarim are aware we seek Agoroth as well. How far do they lead us in this race?'Defeat Orc-kind in Carn Dûm.Defeat Orc-kind in Carn DûmDefeat Orc-kind in Carn Dûm.Defeat Orc-kind in Carn DûmThe caverns below The Forsaken Inn are filled with all manner of objects and dangers requiring the expertise of a wide range of classes.

