The seven swords must be given to the Seven Sentinels in the correct order before the vault will open.You have solved the puzzle of the seven sentinels, so now it is time to enter the vault and retrieve the treasure.'At last, the time has come to open the ancient vault! I believe each of these seven statues must be given the correct sword before the vault can be opened...but the tale is unfortunately a bit vague. I suppose we could try all the combinations, but that might take a long time. 

'I have made a copy of the relevant verses -- here, perhaps you can puzzle it all out.''You have done it! This chest contains treasures of past ages forged to fight the forces of darkness!

'After all of your effort and the danger you have seen, it is only right that you choose one of these items as your just reward. The rest will be sent to my brethren to distribute.'Unravel the the epic tale of the Shadows of Angmar.Unravel the the epic tale of the Shadows of Angmar.Book I - Stirrings in the DarknessBook II - The Red MaidBook III - The Council of the NorthBook IV - Chasing ShadowsBook V - The Last RefugeBook VI - The Fires in the NorthBook VII - The Hidden HopeBook VIII - The Scourge of the NorthUnravel the the epic tale of the Shadows of Angmar.Unravel the the epic tale of the Shadows of Angmar.Epic - Book IX: The Shores of EvendimEpic - Book X: The City of the KingsEpic - Book XI: Prisoner of the Free PeoplesEpic - Book XII: The Ashen WasteEpic - Book XIII: Doom of the Last-kingEpic - Book XIV: The Ring-forges of EregionEpic - Book XV: Daughter of StrifeDefeat slugs in Carn Dûm.Defeat slugs in Carn DûmYou earned this title during the Season of the Spirit's Scourge Reward Track Season in Monster Play.You slew many crebain in the Redhorn Gate, but Authlanc fears the birds are guided by a more immediate threat.Pizumu the Spy-master can be found north-east of Echad Dúnann, up the winding road that leads into the Redhorn Gate.

Authlanc has asked you to slay Saruman's spy-master.Defeat Pizumu the Spy-masterAuthlanc is in Echad Dúnann, south-west of the Redhorn Gate.

You should return to Authlanc and inform him of your success.Talk to Authlanc at Echad Dúnann'Though you dealt a mighty blow to the crebain, they still persist. Their black wings darken the sky day and night.

'I have spent many days contemplating the source of the crebain, for though daily more are seen flying to Eregion out of Dunland and Fangorn, not once have they been seen flying back.

'They must be reporting to someone in Eregion.  Go north and east, up the winding roads into the Redhorn Gate, and search out this spy-master.  Once he has been dealt with, maybe we will have some peace, and the skies will no longer bear the unceasing sound of crow-wings.''The spy-master is dead? We may all sleep easier without the fear of beating wings and sharp beaks.

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.''The spy-master should be north-east of Echad Dúnann, up the winding road that leads into the Redhorn Gate.'The slaves of Carn Dûm were set free, but Éa, a woman of the hillmen dwelling at Tármunn Súrsa, is still missing her husband.Carn Dûm lies far to the west of Tármunn Súrsa.

Éa begged you to find her missing husband, the hillman-warrior called Erscin.Find ErscinErscin is at Carn Dûm, far to the west of Gath Forthnír.

Erscin is waiting to speak with you again.Speak to ErscinÉa is at Tármunn Súrsa, east of Carn Dûm.

You found Erscin, alive and well, within Carn Dûm and returned him to safety. You should let Éa know the good tidings.'My husband remains in Carn Dûm. I know you have already done so much, but please... find it in your heart to help me once more.

'Erscin is strong of back and force of will. I cannot imagine that he fell to the Orcs, though perhaps he tried to escape and was killed. I cannot bear to imagine such things.

'If he lives, I fear he will not live long. I am sure that the Evil Ones will punish any slaves that remained behind. You must return to Carn Dûm and find him!''Please, return to Carn Dûm and find Erscin!''Thank you, stranger. Whoever you are, I can see that you are no Orc-friend. Let us depart this evil place. And please, whatever you do, do not awaken the gorthorog!''Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for rescuing me. I must return now to my wife. She will be worried that I have left her.

'You may continue on. I know the way from here. Be well, friend.''My dear husband has returned to me! Thank you, Southron, for all you have done!'You have recovered six of the seven swords, and Nethraw is most pleased.The Sword of the Vigil is somewhere in Nan Gurth.

Nethraw told you the last of the seven swords may be found in a deadly place called Nan Gurth. He again warned you that allies will be required to obtain the sword.Nethraw is back at the Fane of the Seven Sentinels, east of Gabilshathûr.

You should bring the Sword of the Vigil to Nethraw.'Finally, the last of the seven swords! This weapon is called the Sword of the Vigil, and it was borne by the leader of the Seven Sentinels, a knight who made his post in the most dangerous part of Angmar -- a place perhaps even more deadly than Carn Dûm itself!

'I speak of Nan Gurth, a place inhabited by terrible beasts and the most evil of foes. The tale tells not where in this dread place the sword can be found. Truly, I hesitate to ask you to go to such a terrible place, merely to satisfy my curiosity, and perhaps to uncover an ancient hoard. But too, it would be a shame to stop now, when we are so close!

'Certainly, as before, this quest is far too dangerous for a single adventurer to attempt alone.''I would never forgive myself if I sent you to your death! Please be careful.''The seven swords! Collected at last! I am trembling with excitement. But one small obstacle remains....'You found a bracelet of burnished gold, covered in grime and filth. The name "Dírdrë" was marked upon it.Tármunn Súrsa lies in the northern part of eastern Angmar.

You should go to Tármunn Súrsa and question its inhabitants about the bracelet you found.Wiping away a bit of the grime covering the bracelet, you discover an engraving that reads, "Dírdrë." It may be that someone at Tármunn Súrsa will recognize the bracelet or the name engraved upon it.'This is not of dwarf-make, I can tell you that much. Nor is it of Elf-craft. It's a bit primitive, I think. I can't say I know from whence it comes.''"Dírdrë" sounds like a Hillman name to me, but I can't tell you much else.''Yes, I can make out the name, but I do not recall meeting anyone of that name in this place. It is a Hillman's name. Perhaps one of those Hillmen who camp near Carn Dûm will know something about it.''Ah, this is a Hillman's bracelet, but I do not recognize the name written upon it. Perhaps one of the others will know of this "Dírdrë."''I know nothing of such baubles. Speak to one of the others if you are so interested in this bracelet!''A bracelet you found on one of the Nimwaith? Likely the creature found it or stole it from someone else. Other than that, I can tell you nothing about the bracelet. Some of the others in the camp may know more.''I have never seen a bracelet such as this. It seems a bit crude, but still beyond the skill of the Nimwaith. I cannot tell you more than that. I would speak to some of the others in the camp...they may be able to help you more.''I think this bracelet was made by the Hillmen. I have seen some of them wearing similar bracelets. Speak to one of them up near Carn Dûm to find out more.''What do you have there, a bracelet? Perhaps you can sell it to someone. I have not much to say about jewellery and other such baubles.''This bracelet looks to be of Hillman-make. You should speak to one of the Hillmen who camp up near Carn Dûm to see if they recognize it.''Ah, one of the Hillmen's bracelets. Speak with one of them up near Carn Dûm if you wish to learn more about it.''This bracelet looks to be of Hillman-make. You should speak to one of the Hillmen who camp near Carn Dûm to see if they recognize it.''What...? Where did you find this? This belonged to my Dírdrë. I thought it was lost forever when she was taken from me by the Angmarim. But that was so long ago....

'Thank you for finding it!'You discovered that half-orcs had ransacked the vestiges of a camp-site, taking something away with them.The half-orcs were seen to the east and a little south of Echad Eregion, almost due south of the Company's camp-site.

Golgallon told you to hunt down the half-orcs and recover whatever they took from the camp-site.Find half-orcs bearing the item from the Company's camp-siteGolgallon is at Echad Eregion, west and north of where you found Thlûk.

You should return to Golgallon with tidings of your encounter with Thlûk.Talk to Golgallon at Echad Eregion'You say you saw tracks leading southwards? These half-orcs clearly serve Saruman and are bearing their prize to Isengard.

'From what you say, they only have a single horse between them, so it is likely a pack-horse, rather than a mount. You should be able to catch them.

'Fortunately, our scouts saw such a pair of half-orcs to the east and a little south of here, almost due south of the camp-site. Hurry! You must recover whatever they took from the camp-site.''You must catch the half-orcs and recover whatever it is they took from the Company's camp-site. Such a pair of half-orcs was seen a distance to the east and a little south of here.''You are too late, ${CLASS}. My companion is already headed south with our prize... Sharkey will soon know everything he needs to find that precious thing he seeks. I am not about to let you hinder its delivery... die!''The second half-orc is alone now and headed south? That is troubling, for it means he may be using the horse as a mount.

'He has a strong enough lead, but perhaps there is yet time....'Defeat troll-kind in Carn Dûm.Defeat troll-kind in Carn Dûm.Defeat troll-kind in Carn Dûm.Defeat troll-kind in Carn DûmYou defeated many wolf-keepers at Barad Morlas, but Dornhador still has one more task for you.Nûkhud, Wolf-master is at Barad Morlas, south-west of Echad Eregion.

Dornhador has asked you to find and defeat Nûkhud, Wolf-master, the leader of the wolf-keepers at Barad Morlas.Defeat Nûkhud, Wolf-masterDornhador is at Echad Eregion, north-east of Barad Morlas.

You should return to Dornhador with tidings of Nûkhud's downfall.Talk to Dornhador at Echad Eregion'While your efforts against the wolf-keepers at Barad Morlas have certainly hindered the plans of the White Hand, they have not halted their search. They are driven by the chief of their keepers, a creature who goes by the name of Nûkhud, Wolf-master.

'I would have you return to Barad Morlas and defeat Nûkhud. His defeat should drive fear into the hearts of the half-orcs and their wolf allies.

'Nûkhud was last seen ranging beyond the ruins west of the bridge in Barad Morlas, south-west of here. Be careful, ${PLAYER}... he is certain to be a dangerous foe.''Nûkhud's defeat should drive terror into the hearts of the half-orcs at Barad Morlas. Go now and see to his demise.''Ha! Nûkhud's demise should give the half-orcs pause! Well done, ${PLAYER}.'The Ghâshfra, a breed of Fire-orcs from Angmar, have invaded the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.Orcs of the Ghâshfra can be found throughout the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.

Hyrrokkin has asked you to defeat the Ghâshfra which have invaded the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.Defeat Ghâshfra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Little one, you may be of help to the Eldgang. While we did not build this place, it is our home now, and it is threatened by the Ghâshfra from the surface world.

'There are many places in Nûrz Ghâshu where the Eldgang cannot go, for they are too small. Perhaps you would go into these holes and drive forth the Ghâshfra? Then we may have peace again.

'There are many Ghâshfra in Nûrz Ghâshu. They are like a plague.''Please destroy the violators of our home, ${PLAYER}.'You earned this title during the inaugural Monster Player Reward Season.You earned this title during the inaugural Monster Player Reward Season.You earned this title during the inaugural Monster Player Reward Season.You earned this title during the inaugural Monster Player Reward Season.You earned this title during the inaugural Monster Player Reward Season.You earned this title during the inaugural Monster Player Reward Season.You earned this title during the inaugural Monster Player Reward Season.You earned access to this title by actively participating in Season 6 of the Monster Player reward track.You earned this title during the inaugural Monster Player Reward Season.You have been called upon to do all that needs to be done to close the gates of Barad Gúlaran forever.Complete The Minions of WisdánComplete Lore of the EnemyComplete Champions of Barad GúlaranComplete The Dead That LiveComplete Allies of the EnemyHunt the Free People in Angmar. You may hunt for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Hunt in Angmar.Hunt in AngmarWelcome to the Ettenmoors! It is time to learn your way around. Follow your orders and prepare to meet the enemy outside of the encampment at Gramsfoot!You are directed to speak with War-tyrant Akulhún, the leader of the forces in Gramsfoot. He awaits you at the totems and bonfires down the hill near the exit into the Ettenmoors proper.'Pay attention, maggot! You are nothing! A speck. I don't know why Mordirith sent you here, other than to die like the rest! Ha! You need to make an impression or, at least an introduction. Make your way to the totems surrounded by bonfires. Find War-tyrant Akulhún and report in.

'Now, get out of my face. You sicken me.''You have just been hatched, broodling, but already you must play an important role. Mordirith sends you here to aid in the war against the Free Peoples. We have no time to waste. You must now get your feet wet. All of them.

'Seek out the War-tyrant Akulhún near the totems and bonfires. He is the ultimate leader in the Ettenmoors and will give you your orders!''Well... well... a new pup fresh from a litter in the mires of Angmar. Finally ready to wet your pelt with the blood of our enemies? Good, bare your teeth. Gird your loins. Your first task is to meet the War-tyrant. Akulhún stands before the totems near the bonfires. Make your way to him and report your arrival.

'Go now. Make the pack proud.''Welcome, mistress. Your presence in this war-torn land is welcome. The filth that fights in the Lord's name falters at every turn. Perhaps with our hand to guide them we will turn the tide and finally force our way south to discover the hidden Elven stronghold. Though it is beneath you, your first task is to meet with War-tyrant Akulhún. You will find him behind you shouting incessantly in the shadow of the totems. Be warned, he has a temper.''Here's a specimen ready for battle! Now, if only I could get the Lord of Angmar to recall the damned emissary he's sent here. Welcome to the front!'Solve all the riddles of Moria.Solve all the riddles of Moria.Solve all of Falgeirr Twisttongue's riddlesYou have delivered Golgallon's message to Rinneldor, who now has more tasks for you.Ruidhriel is encamped near the Burnt Tor, north-west of Echad Dúnann. Limlaer is encamped along the road, south-west of Echad Dúnann.

Rinneldor has asked you to speak with his scouts abroad, Ruidhriel and Limlaer, and aid them if you may.Help RuidhrielHelp LimlaerRinneldor is at Echad Dúnann, south-east of the Burnt Tor and north-east of Limlaer's post.

You should return to Rinneldor and report all that you have learned regarding the Company's movements.Talk to Rinneldor at Echad Dúnann'We have sent out scouts to determine what path the Company may have followed in order to cross Hithaeglir, the Misty Mountains. If what you say is true of the camp-sites you found, there may be other signs of their passing that will need to be hidden.

'There are only three paths that seem reasonable for their passage across the Mountains: through the pass of the Redhorn Gate, south through the Gap of Rohan... or beneath the Mountains through the halls of Moria. Speak with our scouts, Ruidhriel and Limlaer, and learn if they have noted aught of the Company's passing.

'Ruidhriel is encamped near a place to the north-west which we are calling the Burnt Tor, for something has scorched the earth there. Limlaer may be found along the road, south-west of here.''Go at once to Ruidhriel and Limlaer and learn what they may have found. Ruidhriel is encamped near the Burnt Tor to the north-west, while you may find Limlaer along the road, south-west of here.''So, the Company tried the Redhorn Gate, but was foiled by Caradhras itself. And no sign was found of their passing through the Gap of Rohan? The latter does not surprise me, for it would bring their burden very near to the traitor Saruman, and that would be disastrous.

'That leaves but one path then, and I fear it most....'You have taken shining heartwood of unusually high quality from one of the Wood-trolls of Eryn Singor and should find someone who can make use of it.A woodworker in Rivendell might be able to fashion something of great worth from the shining heartwood you found.

You should bring the shining heartwood to a woodworker in Rivendell.This heartwood was taken from one of the Wood-trolls of Eryn Singor and shines with an inner light.

A woodworker in nearby Rivendell might be able to fashion something of great worth from such a valuable find.'Where did you find this shining heartwood, ${PLAYER}? The Wood-trolls of Eryn Singor? It is of great quality, and from it I could fashion goods both useful and powerful!

'This is the least I can do for you, friend ${RACE}. Please take this with my thanks.'This quest grants several scrolls that are used to advance each of your virtues to your new level.

Make sure to select the virtue(s) to advance before consuming each scroll.You may complete this quest at any time.This scroll bestows the Virtues of the Valar quest, which will provide you with several scrolls to improve your Virtues.

You must be level 50 to accept this quest.Complete this quest to receive scrolls which will allow you to advance your Virtues to an appropriate tier for level 50.

<rgb=#FFFF00>Important: Make sure to select each virtue you wish to advance before using a virtue scroll!
 -> Open Traits Panel: 'j' 
 -> Select Tab: Virtue Traits
 -> Select Virtue</rgb>Your calls are capable of evoking the distant past.Invoke The Breaking of ThangorodrimYour spear-arm is strong and your heart is stout. With your like watching over the marches of Middle-earth, the forces of the Enemy shudder with dread.Hrotha is in Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands.

You have been told to speak with Hrotha, a Warden of great fame and skill.Meet Hrotha for further Warden trainingHrotha is in Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands.

You have been told to speak with Hrotha, a Warden of great fame and skill.Talk to Hrotha at Ost GuruthAs a Warden, you have achieved such renown as to receive a summons from Hrotha at Ost Guruth.

You should seek Hrotha to receive further training in your class.'So, ${PLAYER}, you think there are things I can teach you? Yes, I have heard of you. All of us who range the wilds of Eriador, be we Elf or Dúnadan or Eglan, have heard the tales. And yet you have sought me out, so what am I to do with you?

'I am no sage, hiding in some old broken skull of a keep, speaking riddles to all who cross my threshold, and you are not the first warrior to ask me my secrets.'Ruidhriel has asked you to help her defeat the shadow-wargs around the Burnt Tor.The shadow-wargs inhabit the Burnt Tor, west of Ruidhriel.

Ruidhriel has asked that you kill the Wargs that stalk the Burnt Tor.Defeat shadow-wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ruidhriel is east of the Burnt Tor.

You should return to Ruidhriel and tell her of your success.Talk to Ruidhriel'Some great evil has taken an interest in the Burnt Tor. At night, shining eyes peer at me from the hilltop and ominous howls echo throughout the valley.

'Maybe these Wargs know nothing of the Company and their task, but I would ask that you seek them out and destroy as many as you can. If they do have some malicious intent, then perhaps we can stop them before it is too late.

'The howling came from the Burnt Tor behind me. Please, ${PLAYER}, take care and return to me when the task is complete.''These Wargs have a fell air about them, ${PLAYER}. They have a dreadful presence.''These Wargs are an evil much greater than the spies of Saruman. I must consider what this means ${PLAYER}.'Handarod has told you that the Enemy holds the ring Narchuil at Barad Dúrgul. Though it is a minor essay in Ringcraft, it is dangerous nonetheless.Handarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs.

Handarod has bid you enter Barad Dúrgul and recover the ring Narchuil.Defeat GoeolgonGwathryn is at Tármunn Súrsa in Angmar.

You should report to Gwathryn at once.Report to Gwathryn'Though we have recovered Narchuil, Goeolgon yet lives, and is rebuilding his power in Barad Dúrgul. He thirsts for revenge and will soon bring his power to bear upon us if he is allowed to recover.

'Barad Dúrgul awaits, when you are ready to leave, come and speak with me again.''So, Handarod has sent you afield gain has he?

'I am not certain how Goeolgon was able to rebuild his strength again so quickly, but I thank you for your efforts to keep his evil in check.''Are you ready to enter Barad Dúrgul? We must destroy Goeolgon before he regains his strength!'Glavroleth is concerned that the White Hand is preparing an assault on Echad Mirobel.Echad Mirobel is west of Echad Dúnann, along the Nan Sirannon road.

You have been instructed to warn Echad Mirobel of the White Hand threat.Talk to Ornras at Echad Mirobel'The Uruk's words about an assault on Echad Mirobel worry me ${PLAYER}. Echad Mirobel does not have enough strength to resist an assault from even a part of Saruman's forces.

'We must warn Echad Mirobel that the White Hand is preparing to move against them. Travel west of Echad Dúnann along the Nan Sirannon road to Echad Mirobel and speak with Ornras. Let him know of the danger he now faces.''The White Hand prepares a force against Echad Mirobel?

'You bear ill news, but perhaps we have some time left to fortify our defences.''Echad Mirobel is west of Echad Dúnann, along the Nan Sirannon road.'At the behest of Hrotha, you must speak with Aragorn, son of Arathorn, to gain the great wisdom of the Wardens.Hrotha knows of a legendary warden who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.Complete A Warden's Second Best AllyComplete A Weapon of Might and GloryHrotha is in Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands.Aragorn can be found in Rivendell, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House.

Hrotha counselled you to speak with Aragorn, the Ranger also known as Strider.Talk to Aragorn at Rivendell'And to that, I will tell you as I have told the others: I know no secrets, or none that could be called wisdom. I trust my spear and my arm, my corselet and the strength of my heart. And perhaps that is the greatest lesson of our kind, to trust in yourself, the weapon you wield, and the armour you wear.

'Very well, then. That is where we shall begin, if you want. I will see you properly armed, and we will call that a kind of wisdom.''You must complete the tasks put before you.''You have proven yourself, ${PLAYER}. I doubted the tales folk told about you when first I heard them, but now I am sure they are all true...or as close to true as a minstrel can manage.

'Now it is time for you to seek out one who knows more than any of us of the skills of the Warden. He may not be one of us, but he has fought alongside us many times, for longer than I have been alive. Some in Bree call him Strider, but his true name is Aragorn son of Arathorn.

'Aragorn is a wanderer by nature, but great deeds are in the offing, and I think you should be able to find him where the Wise gather. Find him, ${PLAYER}, and give him my regards.''Aragorn has had many haunts, though his true home is the wild. Often he dwells among the Dúnedain of Esteldín, though he has not been seen there in many months, if the word I hear is true.

'Bree, too, has seen the back of him for some time, from what folk say. That fool Bill Ferny would not speak ill of him quite so much, if he thought "Strider" might return.

'If I were to guess, I would suspect him to be involved in all the goings-on at Rivendell. But if he is there, it is surely in secret, so tell no one.''We are well met, ${PLAYER}. I should be troubled that you have found me so easily in these times, but if you bear greetings from Hrotha, I know your intent cannot be ill. He is a great Warden, and if he thinks well of you, then I do as well, for he does not give his friendship lightly.

'Courage is the greatest virtue of our kind, ${PLAYER}. All else may fail us, but never our bravery. We are the bulwark between the darkness of the world and those who could not bear to behold it. Without stout hearts, even in the face of death, we cannot hope to prevail against our foes. So your spear may fail you, and yes, your habergeon as well, but your spirit must never flag. This is the greatest lesson I have learned, through all my long years and travels.

'This, then, is my word, ${PLAYER}: go always with valour, and always remember that you must protect all who need it.'Few dare to engage you in a war of words, and those who do, lose.Use Combustion, Concession and Rebuttal, or Bombastic InspirationThe threat of the furry worms has been growing in the wake of the Gauradan raids.Ice-worms can be found throughout Talvi-mûri.

Jyrki has asked you to defeat the furry worms that threaten the Lossoth encampments.Defeat ice-worms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Jyrki is at the hunter's way-post at the northern end of Talvi-mûri.

You should return to Jyrki with news of your success.'We grow weary. Soon the Gauredain will overtake this outpost.

'The furry worms have encroached upon our outposts. Defeat the creatures and teach them the error of their new boldness.''Track the furry worms and defeat them. They grow bold in the wake of the Gauredain raids.''You have defeated some of the ice-worms? The news gives me great pleasure.'While the Company did try the Redhorn Gate, they were forced to turn back. Neither was there any sign of their passing towards the Gap of Rohan, leaving but one direction open to Rinneldor's mind: Moria.Ruidhriel is encamped near the Burnt Tor, north-west of Echad Dúnann. Limlaer may be found along the road, south-west of Echad Dúnann.

Rinneldor has asked you to once again speak with Ruidhriel and Limlaer to learn what must be done to confuse the Company's trail.Help RuidhrielHelp LimlaerRinneldor is at Echad Dúnann, south-east of the Burnt Tor and north-east of Limlaer's post.

You should return to Rinneldor with news of your successes.Talk to Rinneldor at Echad Dúnann'So, ${PLAYER}, we now know whither the Company has gone. They have surely passed into the long dark of Moria. May the Valar guide their steps, for it is said Durin's Bane dwells there still... though none can say for certain, as no one in this age has ever laid eyes upon it.

'Here, then, is the last task appointed to us: we must confuse their trail, so that the Enemy cannot be prepared for their passage. Speak again with Ruidhriel and Limlaer... they will know what to do.

'If you have forgotten, Ruidhriel is encamped near the Burnt Tor to the north-west, while you may find Limlaer along the road to the south-west.''We must throw the Enemy off the trail of the Company. Speak with Ruidhriel and Limlaer and learn what they would have you do.''It is done, then. The safety of the Company is out of our hands. We must now turn our attention to our own roles in the coming War.

'You have the gratitude of the Free Peoples, ${PLAYER}.'Dagfinn has disappeared to explore the hall of Shemeldurj in the Great Delving.Dagfinn went off to explore Shemeldurj, an ancient hall of Moria.

You should seek Dagfinn at Shemeldurj to ease Túbi's fretting for his friend.Seek Dagfinn in ShemeldurjPiles of promising debris can be found around Shemeldurj.

You should root through several piles of promising debris to seek ancient treasure.Search piles of debris for any promising relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagfinn is in Shemeldurj in the north-west of the Great Delving, near Durin's Threshold.

You should tell Dagfinn that you found nothing promising anywhere in Shemeldurj.Tell Dagfinn that Shemeldurj appears to be as empty as it looksTúbi Thickfist is atop the great stair in Durin's Threshold in the west of the Great Delving.

You should return to Túbi Thickfist with news of Dagfinn's fruitless search.Return to Túbi Thickfist'Many of our expedition have pressed forward -- for better or worse -- but two were supposed to return, and they have not.

'Will you seek out Dagfinn? He made for Shemeldurj many hours ago and has not returned. You can find it by pressing east from here, then turning north at your first opportunity.''Oh! You startled me! I am sorry, I just cannot stop hunting. There must be treasure in this room, stowed away somewhere.

'My father gave me a map of this place, passed down from the time when the Longbeards inhabited Moria, and there were notes of great promise in this hall. I meant only to come in and explore, but... I cannot walk away when there is a hope of buried treasure!

'Will you help me look?'You explain that you rooted through many corners of Shemeldurj, but found nothing of promise, and perhaps it would be wise for everyone to return to Durin's Threshold.

'No! No, I cannot believe it. I've treasured that map all my life. I cannot accept that it would lead me here, only to find this hall empty!''That fool. Just because he treasured a map for a lifetime does not mean that the map was ever going to be accurate. Shemeldurj is likely as dry as a bone now. I hope he returns soon to take some rest.'Túbi Thickfist is curious about any relics that may linger in the Chamber of Deep Thought near Durin's Threshold.The Chamber of Deep Thought is east through the tunnel from Durin's Threshold, then south.

You should search the Chamber of Deep Thought for any relics of interest.Find the Chamber of Deep ThoughtThe cocoon is in the Chamber of Deep Thought in the west of the Great Delving.

You should search the cocoon for anything that might be of value to the dwarves.Examine the cocoonTúbi Thickfist is at the top of the stair of Durin's Threshold.

You should return to Túbi Thickfist with news of your search.Return to Túbi Thickfist'If you happen to pass the Chamber of Deep Thought while you search for my friends, would you mind investigating it? Such a place may hold many relics that would be invaluable to the dwarves.

'If anything catches your eye, feel free to investigate.''Alas! A spider, and nothing more? That is dire news. I have never even heard of a great spider that can glow translucent...I hope we do not discover any more of those!

'Well, at least you have cleared the chamber of evil. I will look on the bright side; perhaps we can begin to restore it now.''The Chamber of Deep Thought is east through the tunnel, then a southern turn will see you there in no time.'Wigfast heard a strangely long echoing shout to the north-east of Gazatmur, and wonders at what the sound could have been.The source of the echo can be found by following the stairs behind Wigfast's hiding place, and heading north-west from there to the upper levels.

You should search for the source of the echo.Find the source of the echoYou spot a rucksack in the north-east corner of the Great Delving, perched near a great rift in the path.

You should search the rucksack.Investigate the rucksack near the rift in the pathNear the rucksack is a book, a journal, with a dwarf's objectives written down.

You should complete the objectives intended by the dwarf who perished.Complete the first objective in the journalComplete the second objective in the journalSlagvi is in the Dolven-view in Moria's Great Delving.

You should tell Slagvi of all you encountered on the eastern side of the Great Delving.Talk to Slagvi in the Dolven-view'The strangest thing happened when you were away this last time, ${PLAYER}. I heard a very long echo... and it sounded rather like a dwarf-shout.

'The sound came from the north-east of here. Will you go explore? I should like to head back to the Dolven-view.''A very odd echo it was! Chilling, if truth be told. It could not have been too far from here.'This rucksack may indicate the source of the strange echo heard by Wigfast. It appears to have once been owned by a dwarf, but the dwarf is nowhere to be found.

Your strong suspicion is that he fell right through the perilous crack in the path. But what was he doing so far from any established hubs in Moria?'You have had some strange encounters, to be sure! White Hands and Uruks and goblins and rucksacks and deep rifts... better you than me, ${PLAYER}!

'Well, I am glad you've made it back safe and sound. Take your rest here at the Dolven-view, where the light is bright and the fire warm.'When these lands were held by our brethren, the land flourished in wonder and beauty. The library halls were brilliant and the greenery lush. Many believe that Elves love only nature, and that admiration is indeed strong, but it is not the only beauty we see in the world. Knowledge is beautiful also, and in the library at Tham Mírdain, much knowledge was kept.

When these lands fell to darkness the library was pillaged and many tomes within were stolen...or worse: destroyed. Yet it appears that the Enemy believes there may still be knowledge within the walls of Tham Mírdain. If this is true, we must do our part to reclaim the books for light, honour, and the memory of the Elves.

If you are undertaking the challenge of scouring the library for lost lore, I would ask that you seek to recover as many books as you can from within the ruins.The Library of Tham Mírdain is south and a little west of Echad Mirobel.

As you work towards cleansing the Library of Tham Mírdain, you should keep a watchful eye for any tomes which may still be intact.Collect books of Tham Mírdain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have discovered a message among the belongings of a man of Angmar, slain in battle.Make your way to the ruins at Echad Mirobel located in the south-western reaches of Eregion.

The message you found speaks of Angmar's desire to scour the remaining ruins for any remnant of power or knowledge that can be used to further strengthen their forces in the North. It mentions that an Uruk named Gûrsh has been placed in charge of the expedition.Opening the message reveals orders from a captain of Angmar:

'We are to dispatch forces to the Elf-lands of Eregion and there search among the ruins for any remnant of their bygone era. Outlying ruins are to be scoured but the main thrust of our forces will be upon the Ring-forge itself.

'Chieftain Gûrsh will be in charge of this expedition, a testament to the Orc's great assistance in our clandestine warfare. Serve him well.'

The message ends there. The Elves present at the Ring-forge may well want to know of this message. They can be found far to the south-west in the ruins known as Echad Mirobel.'My thanks, ${PLAYER}. We know that the Angmarim are further defiling the ruins of our past, but we now have greater information on what they seek and who leads them.

'This information will undoubtedly prove useful. We shall redouble our efforts in searching among the ruins here within Echad Mirobel.

'I wonder, though, if you would be interested in some other work involving the Angmarim....'Kambi, wounded by a goblin near Durin's Threshold, spoke of the ramblings of his attacker. Túbi Thickfist wants this tribe's camp found as soon as possible.The goblin-camp can be found through a crack in the wall above the eastern stair.

Túbi Thickfist has asked you to locate the goblin-camp.Find the goblin-tribeJarmárr is near the goblin camp of Snaga-maudhûl.

You have located the goblin-tribe and heard the voice the chieftain spoke of. You should speak with the dwarf near the road.Speak with the dwarf near the goblin camp of Snaga-maudhûl'According to Kambi, the chieftain said to go through the broken wall above the eastern stairs. We must see if this goblin-tribe does, in fact, lurk in the shadows. I also want to know more about this voice the chieftain was so fearful of.

'Head to the east through the crack and locate the tribe.''By Durin's beard! Someone has come to help me! I was cut off from the rest of my group venturing forward through this area, and I found myself here....''Before we do anything else, we must first find that goblin-tribe. According to Kambi it should be found through the broken wall above the eastern stairs.'The half-orcs at Târ Stazg were dismayed by the defeat of Akashpug, but were not driven off.The half-orc tents are at Târ Stazg, north-east of Echad Dúnann, along the mountains before the Redhorn Gate.

In order to drive the disorganized half-orcs from Eregion, Palanaer has tasked you with destroying their tents.Palanaer is in Echad Dúnann, south-west of Târ Stazg.

You should return to Palanaer and report your success.Talk to Palanaer'Though they are unmanned, Târ Stazg still presents a threat to Eregion. If we do not act quickly, they will rebuild their force and bring it to bear at Barad Morlas still.

'We must drive the half-orcs from Eregion... with fire if it must be so. Return to Târ Stazg and set ablaze the tents of the half-orcs. Without shelter and supplies, they will become easy prey for our scouts.

'The tents are spread throughout Târ Stazg, north-east of Echad Dúnann, along the mountains before the Redhorn Gate.''The half-orc tents are spread throughout Târ Stazg to the north-east.''The leaderless half-orcs will find it much harder to maintain their presence without shelter and supplies. You have done well, ${PLAYER}.'Swerthir is fascinated by the Vault of Durin to the south, but worries about separating from his party.The Vault of Durin lies directly south of the little encampment in Lamab-dûm, in the Great Delving.

You should find the Vault of Durin and see if it is as promising as its name sounds.Search for relics in the Vault of Durin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Swerthir is at the small dwarf-encampment in Lamab-dûm in the Great Delving.

You should return to Swerthir and tell him what you have learned about the current state of the Vault of Durin.Return to Swerthir in Lamab-dûm'According to my map, ${PLAYER}, the Vault of Durin lies directly south of here. The problem is that my party refuses to explore it. They wish to head straight to the Dolven-view and not veer off the path.

'I should dearly like to know what lies in the Vault, but I dare not separate from my group. Will you go look, my good ${RACE}?'Swerthir listens quietly while you explain the current state of the Vault of Durin, not only empty, but falling into ruin.

'That is sad news, ${PLAYER}. I imagine this is only the first of many such disappointments as we go through Moria. Perhaps it will never be restored fully, but...I would like to think that this expedition can forge a new mine. Different, but good.'It is time to press forward into Moria from the safety of Durin's Threshold.Túbi Thickfist is atop the great stairway of Durin's Threshold.

You should climb the stairs and find Túbi Thickfist.Find Túbi Thickfist at the top of the Stair'You have done much for us, and now I am sure you are eager to press on into the tunnels.

'Túbi Thickfist is at the top of the great stair just yonder, and I believe some dwarves under his supervision have already begun to press forward! If you are interested in doing the same, Túbi might have information that would be helpful for your journey.''Ah, I am glad someone with some skill as a warrior has come. I am afraid this tunnel quite unnerves me, ${PLAYER}.

'Some dwarves have already gone forth under my supervision, but they have not yet returned.''You can find Túbi atop the stairs, ${PLAYER}.'The food-stores of the goblins can be found in Gazatmur and provide the goblins with extended sustenance.Goblin food-stores can likely be found in Gazatmur in the eastern Great Delving.

You should destroy food-stores in Gazatmur to dismantle this camp as an established keep for the enemy.Destroy food-stores in Gazatmur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wigfast is perched just beyond Gazatmur in the Great Delving.

You should return to Wigfast.Return to Wigfast'I cannot understand how so many goblins can exist here, unless they have some great hoard of supplies stowed away in Gazatmur.

'If you encounter any food-stores, please do feel free to destroy them utterly. We ought to discourage the goblins from lengthening their stay in the Great Delving.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! That was a key step in dismantling their presence here. Now they will have to look elsewhere for food.''Gazatmur is just yonder, and I am almost positive there is a great amount of food amassed within.'Palanaer fears that half-orcs are not the only threat to Echad Mirobel.Echad Mirobel is west of Echad Dúnann along the Nan Sirannon road.

You have been asked to warn Echad Mirobel of the half-orc threat.Talk to Gelirwen at Echad Mirobel'Though the half-orcs are no longer a threat to Echad Dúnann, I fear that they may attempt an assault upon Echad Mirobel.

'Mirobel has long lain in ruin and is already nearly overrun; if even a part of the half-orc host of Târ Stazg joined in the assault, the Elves at Echad Mirobel may be overrun.

'Echad Mirobel lies west of Echad Dúnann, along the Nan Sirannon road. Go and warn Gelirwen. Render any aid that you may in their defence.''An assault from Târ Stazg? This is grim news indeed, ${CLASS}.

'Preparations must begin at once against such an assault.''Echad Mirobel is west of Echad Dúnann along the Nan Sirannon road.'Gamli the dwarf harbours fears that something might be hiding within his bedding.Gamli's bed is in the Durin's Threshold camp.

Gamli seems concerned that there might be something hiding in his bed.Examine Gamli's bedGamli is at the Durin's Threshold camp.

You should speak with Gamli regarding what you found in his bed.Talk to Gamli'Ho there, friend! You don't see anything... moving... in my bed, do you?

'My sleep has been quite disturbed of late by the feeling of something crawling across my skin. I refuse to lay beneath those blankets again until I am assured there is nothing alive within them.

'Take a look for me, ${PLAYER}. I dare not touch the blankets.''Don't you see those awful things crawling in my bed?''This is intolerable! Insects rustling around where I lay my head is quite unacceptable! It is not to be borne, I tell you!

'Where did those hideous little things come from? We have hardly been here a day, and already we are infested.

'I think now I shall need a thorough wash....'Narmeleth believes she knows the secret to Mordirith's weakness.Narmeleth is in her father's old room at Gath Forthnír in the northern reaches of Angmar.

Narmeleth has told you to speak with Golodir and find what has become of the broken blade of Dúnachar.Talk to Narmeleth at Gath ForthnírGolodir is in his room in Gath Forthnír.

Narmeleth has told you to speak with Golodir and find what has become of the broken blade of Dúnachar.'Narmeleth will have arrived by now. Go to her father's old room and see what she has to say about the situation here in Angmar. I hope you know what you're doing, ${PLAYER}, because I still have my reservations that she has truly forsaken her old ways.''Narmeleth has arrived at a plan to rid us of Mordirith? I am ready to hear it.''Thank you for speaking on my behalf, ${PLAYER}. From here we can set into motion the plan to defeat Mordirith at last.

'My father's final words revealed to me how Mordirith may be defeated. Though he has returned from Minas Morgul with great power, he still bears the scar of Golodir's blade, Dúnachar, that pierced him and sent him back to his foul master.

'If we were to bare this weapon before him, even in its broken state, the memory of his wound will be enough to make Mordirith falter.

'Speak to Golodir and find out what has become of the broken blade of Dúnachar.'Narmeleth believes that baring the shattered hilt of Dúnachar before Mordirith will weaken the False King's will.Lorniel's grave is on the northern slopes of Gorothlad, south of Nan Gurth in Angmar.

Golodir has given you the location of Dúnachar and has given you permission to retrieve it.Retrieve the broken hilt of DúnacharGolodir is at Gath Forthnír in the northern reaches of Angmar.

You should return to Golodir with the broken hilt of Dúnachar.Golodir listens to your account of Narmeleth's plan, and nods.

'I took the broken hilt of Dúnachar with me when I buried my dear Lorniel, and by her grave it lies still. After her death we carried her as far  as we dared under the cover of darkness; she rests atop a hill on the northern slopes of Gorothlad.

'If the blade of Dúnachar will aid you in your fight against Mordirith, I give you my leave to retrieve it.''Lorniel's grave is on the northern slopes of Gorothlad, south of Nan Gurth.''I trust the hilt was not too difficult to find?'Elrond shares your concerns about Amarthiel and has asked Lord Glorfindel to deal with the matter.Glorfindel can be found outside the Last Homely House to the south-east, looking out on the Falls of Imladris.

Elrond has asked you to speak with Glorfindel.Talk to Glorfindel in RivendellDelossad is south-west of Rivendell in Tâl Bruinen, east of Garbert's cottage.

Glorfindel has asked that you question Narmeleth in Delossad.Talk to Narmeleth at Delossad'I am concerned, ${PLAYER}, as I am sure you are, by the capture of Amarthiel. Though she has been stripped of Narchuil, she may still pose some threat to the unwary.

'It is no small choice, deciding the fate of Amarthiel. But there are other pressing matters; strange news has come in from my scouts in the south. I must concern myself with these things, as well as others, and I have tasked none less than the Elf-lord Glorfindel with the matter of Amarthiel. See what counsel he can give you, and maybe you can offer him some aid in rendering his judgement.

'You may find Lord Glorfindel outside of my house to the south-east.''I am surprised, ${PLAYER}. I had not thought that you would be the one who should choose to come and listen to a broken Elf-maiden's tale.''The matter of Amarthiel is grave indeed. It is a strange fate that Amarthiel, or Narmeleth as she now wishes to be called, is again imprisoned where she was once held for so long.  

'She must be questioned, and though Master Elrond has bidden me to address this matter at once, I still have many other duties to which to attend. I would ask you to go and speak with her; perhaps you may glean some information of use from Amarthiel.

'${PLAYER}, beware her words. This might again be some trickery on her part, though my heart counsels me that she speaks true.''Glorfindel can usually be found standing near the Falls of Imladris, south-east of my house.''Lord Glorfindel has asked you to question Amarthiel?

'Delossad is south-west of Rivendell, in Tâl Bruinen.''Delossad is south-west of Rivendell, in the region of the Trollshaws called Tâl Bruinen.'Narmeleth has turned from her evil ways and has offered her knowledge in aid of the Free Peoples.Esteldín is in the North Downs, a land north-west of the Trollshaws.

Narmeleth wishes for you to travel to Esteldín and warn Halbarad of the spy.Talk to Halbarad at Esteldín'Though few believe it, I have been freed from the evil that once ensnared me. It was as the lifting of a veil and a release from chains that held me for so long. I am no longer consumed by the ring, Narchuil, nor the desire for it.

'I have dire news -- a warning for those that would listen: As Amarthiel, I had heard whispers of a hidden city of the Dúnedain, Esteldín. I had sent out a master spy to divine its location, and by now they surely must have located it. 

'The Rangers must be warned of this threat; if the spy is able to infiltrate Esteldín, they will move a large force against it in secret. Travel to the North Downs and warn the leader of this camp against the treachery that I have sown.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Esteldín in the North Downs when you accept this quest.</rgb>'What brings you to Esteldín this day, ${PLAYER}?''I know only that Esteldín lies somewhere in the North Downs.'You must help prove that Narmeleth is telling the truth by questioning refugees from Angmar.The refugees are outside of the library, near the craft-hall, watching the Rangers train, and by the stable-master in Esteldín.

Halbarad is not convinced of Narmeleth's intentions, but has allowed you to question the Hillman-refugees from Angmar.Halbarad is in Esteldín in the North Downs.

You should return to Halbarad and inform him that one of the refugees is missing.Talk to Halbarad at Esteldín'A spy? Among us here in Esteldín? It seems unlikely that a spy would be able to penetrate our ranks, and even less likely given the source of this information....

'If you insist upon pursuing the matter, go and speak with the refugees that were recently rescued from Angmar. Doubtless you will find that they are simple herdsmen and farmers.

'Speak with the refugees outside of the library, near the craft-hall, watching my kinsmen train, and by the stable-master... though I see little wisdom in trusting the words of the enemy, ${PLAYER}.''I see little wisdom in trusting in the words of the enemy, ${PLAYER}, but you can find the refugees outside of the library, near the craft-hall, watching my kinsmen train, and by the stable-master.''A spy? Friend, I have seen many things, but no spy.''I have seen nothing strange since I left Angmar, ${CLASS}.''I would not even know how to recognize what you seek, ${CLASS}. I am but a simple farmer.''One of the refugees is missing?'Halbarad has asked that you find the missing refugee and bring her back to Esteldín.The missing refugee might be found in the eastern-most pass between the North Downs and Angmar.

Halbarad instructed you to search for signs of the missing refugee.Find the missing refugeeHalbarad is in Esteldín in the North Downs.

You should return to Halbarad and inform him that the refugee was a spy.Talk to Halbarad at Esteldín'Those whom we take under protection here in Esteldín are not allowed to depart without my leave under penalty of death. This is the law, and it has protected us and kept us hidden from our enemies.

'It is likely that this refugee is only returning to her homestead and that she is no spy, but she must still be brought to judgement for breaking the laws of Esteldín.

'Search the eastern-most pass into Angmar and bring back the refugee, be she spy or otherwise.''Alis was a spy! I am sorry for mistrusting your counsel, though doubtless even the Wise would not see aid of this nature coming unlooked-for from such an ally.''Search the eastern-most pass into Angmar for the missing refugee, ${PLAYER}.''Lay down your weapons and walk away, ${CLASS}. I will not be stopped!'Narmeleth's warning about the spy proved true and proved her good intentions to Halbarad.Narmeleth is at Delossad in Tâl Bruinen.

Halbarad has asked that you bring his thanks to Narmeleth for her aid in saving Esteldín.Talk to Narmeleth at Delossad'Esteldín remains hidden, and though I am glad that disaster was averted, I still do not wholly trust the counsel of Amarthiel... no, Narmeleth, who for so long brought strife and war upon us.

'She may still have a great store of information to offer our cause, so you may return to Delossad with my thanks, but be wary. I am not wholly convinced that she can be trusted in all matters and that this is not some grand scheme of the enemy.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Delossad in Tâl Bruinen when you accept this quest.</rgb>'I am glad that at least one of my wicked deeds has been amended. There are so many others whose weight I must bear for the rest of my days, however few those might be....''Delossad lies in Tâl Bruinen in the far south of the Trollshaws, south-east of the North Downs.'The truth of Narmeleth's warning has earned her some measure of trust.Narmeleth is being held prisoner in Delossad in southern Trollshaws.

You should speak with Narmeleth and hear the tale of her downfall.Hear Narmeleth's tale and experience 'Session: Daughter of Strife' or read the shortened account insteadDelossad is in the Trollshaws, south-west of Rivendell.

There Narmaleth wishes to speak with you.Talk to Narmeleth at Delossad'I am glad that you have returned, ${PLAYER}.

'I was not always as you have known me, for though I was doomed to failure, my heart's intentions were ever true. Alas that Shadows will corrupt even the noblest of goals. 
  
'I have much to tell, if you will hear me.''I have had much time to reflect: upon those whom I have hurt, upon the suffering inflicted at my behest, and my thoughts turn oft as well to my father who is lost.

'If you would but attend me, I will tell you of my downfall. It would please me to express the full tale to another ere it pass beyond recall.

'Will you hear me, ${PLAYER}?'During the Second Age, the Dark Lord comes to Eregion in fair guise to beguile the Elves with the promise of secret knowledge. He captivates Narmeleth, drawing her from the protection of her father Laerdan and Celebrimbor's people, and the seeds of her corruption are sown...'I was young and foolish, and Sauron taught me the secret arts of Ring-lore, and by that I was ensnared. With his aid, I forged a potent ring, powerful enough to sway the hearts and minds of those around me. Yet he regarded not in me the skill of a Ring-smith, but the prowess of a warrior, cruel and beautiful.

'But the violent losses of Narchuil and my father have purged me of the spell and the spirit that bound me to Sauron's will. I am truly free, though I have paid a bitter price indeed for my folly so many ages ago.

'I regret all the deeds I wrought under my spell of madness. Each death by my hand is a crushing weight that I will bear forever, even into the Undying West, if I am ever allowed into those hallowed halls.'Narmeleth told you the tragic tale of her fall and her transformation into Amarthiel, the Champion of Angmar.Glorfindel is in Rivendell, south-east of the House of Elrond.

Narmeleth has asked you to speak with Glorfindel on her behalf.Accompany Glorfindel to the final CouncilGlorfindel is in Rivendell by the Falls of Imladris, south-east of the House of Elrond.

You should return and speak with Glorfindel in Rivendell.Talk to Glorfindel'${PLAYER}, I wish to do some good in the fight against that evil which I created. Mordirith has recovered Narchuil, and doubtless he will seek to use its powers soon.

'Mordrambor is arrogant, but he has skill in the Dark Arts of the Enemy and is no less wicked than his master. He, too, remains a threat that I allowed to persist.

'I wish to aid in healing the hurts I have inflicted upon the world, even if by the least act. If you would but speak to Lord Glorfindel for me, I will accept my judgement, whatever it may be.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Rivendell in the Trollshaws when you accept this quest.</rgb>'By your word, ${PLAYER}, Narmeleth is allowed her freedom. Had it not been for your excellent reputation amongst my kindred, I would not have allowed for her departure.  

'But hear this ere you depart from my side: be wary and fastidiously watchful. Though my thoughts counsel me to trust that no treachery remains in Narmeleth, I perceive that the desire of Narchuil has not wholly left her.''Speak with Lord Glorfindel on my behalf...I wish to do at least some small good in penance for the vast evils I have inflicted upon this world.''One good deed does not erase all that was done by her as Amarthiel, no matter what name she calls herself now, but I will reflect upon all that you have told me.

'Master Elrond has asked that Narmeleth be judged, and I would have you accompany me while she is questioned.'Glorfindel's council moved to free Narmeleth from her prison and enlist her aid against Mordirith.Delossad is in the southern Trollshaws, south-west of Rivendell.

Narmeleth has asked to speak with you at once.Talk to Narmeleth at Delossad'Narmeleth has sent word that she desires to speak with you, ${PLAYER}. She wishes to begin preparations for the journey immediately, and asks for you to return to Delossad as quickly as you may.

'Pray do not forget my counsel, and be cautious when dealing with Narmeleth in the event that we are deceived. Revised though she may seem, one does not plunge one's hands so deeply into the realm of Shadow without finding them forever tarnished by its influence.

'I fear that your road hence will be fraught with peril, my friend, but I hope that you will find light in the darkness when all is done.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Delossad in Tâl Bruinen when you accept this quest.</rgb>'We must be quick if we hope to stop Mordirith. I know of one place only in which he could house his foul steed. Deep in Barad Gúlaran, Mordirith has a secret lair: Gador Gúlaran. The path thither is beset with danger, but perhaps we can catch Mordirith off his guard. He will not have foreseen that you would trust me enough to allow my passage to Angmar, and this distrust will be his undoing.

'Let us begin our final preparations.''Delossad is in the southern Trollshaws, south-west of Rivendell. You will find Narmeleth there.'Narmeleth is ready to begin her journey to Angmar.Gath Forthnír is in the north of Angmar, north-east of Imlad Balchorth.

Narmeleth is ready to travel to Gath Forthnír and speak with Golodir.Talk to Golodir at Gath Forthnír'We can now make the journey to Gath Forthnír in Angmar, where my father hid for so long, watching for my return. From Gath Forthnír, we will be able to form our plan of attack.

'You will have to go ahead and carry word to Golodir. I doubt that he will be eager to allow my admittance to Gath Forthnír, yet he is a good man. Speak to Golodir and ask him to let me enter, and I will follow if he allows it.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Gath Forthnír in Angmar when you accept this quest.</rgb>'Amarthiel? In Gath Forthnír? I forbid it! Should we also make rooms for Mordrambor and Mordirith? I will not have my enemies within the walls of the stronghold whose very doors have been defended by those whose blood she has spilled.

'Nay, perhaps I spoke too rashly.  I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. I remember the long years in which Laerdan sought to free his daughter from the evil that consumed her, even to his own doom. As a last favour to my dear friend, I will harbour Narmeleth in Gath Forthnír.''Gath Forthnír is in the north of Angmar, north-east of Imlad Balchorth.'You caught up with one of the half-orcs who ransacked the Company's camp-site, but the other had already continued southwards with their stolen prize.The remaining half-orc might be found along the northern banks of the dry Sirannon river-bed, south-east of Echad Eregion.

Golgallon suggests that there is a chance to stop the remaining half-orc when he stops to rest his horse.Retrieve what was taken from the Company's camp-siteQuickly find the thiefGolgallon is at Echad Eregion, north-west of the Sirannon.

You should bring the pot you found back to Golgallon.'Your return here is all that may stand in the way of success. But not all is yet lost.

'The remaining half-orc will likely ride hard for Isengard, but that will hinder him more than aid him... he will be forced to stop the sooner to rest his mount. That is when you will need to strike.

'From what you tell me, I would guess he would make for the Dunlending camp of Porth Cadlus, south of the Sirannon. The encampment lies to the south-east of here, but I would look first along the northern banks of the Sirannon, now dry... that is where he would most likely rest his horse.''The last half-orc must be stopped from fulfilling his mission, ${PLAYER}!''This was all you found upon the half-orc? We are fortunate that it was something so common and unremarkable!'Scouts reported seeing a strange uruk, and overheard the Orc-overseers under his command calling out "Chieftain Gûrsh" as he strode away toward the Library at Tham Mírdain. It appears that we have identified the leader of this war effort out of Angmar, and now we must do what we can to end this menace.

I would ask you to enter the Library at Tham Mírdain and challenge Gûrsh to a battle. If you can draw him out and defeat him, we will have effectively eliminated the leader of the northern forces.

We must be careful, however, not to attract the attention of the Orcs and Dunlendings from the South, for we do not have the strength to combat north and south should they suddenly join forces. The more stealthy we are, the better our chances to best all foes. Gather no more than two companions for this assault, for our hope is in secrecy. Before you make your assault, you should speak with Maegamiel.Chieftain Gûrsh, leader of the northern forces of Angmar, can be found in the Library at Tham Mírdain, just to the south-west of Echad Mirobel.

Ornras of Echad Mirobel has asked you to take a small band of fighters and unseat Chieftan Gûrsh, which will hopefully weaken the enemy presence from the north without drawing the attention of the south. Enemies have been scavenging the Library for forgotten history that might be useful to their cause.Defeat Chieftain GûrshDeep-claws roam the great Delving, especially naer the Dolven-view. These monstrous tunnellers make the deeps unstable.Deep-claws can be found in the Great Delving, especially on the east path from the Dolven-view.

You should defeat many deep-claws in the Great Delving, but it would be wise to focus your attention on the east path towards Zelem-melek.Defeat deep-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wafri is in the Dolven-view camp in the Great Delving.

You should speak with Wafri and tell him that you've defeated many deep-claws in the surrounding area.Return to Wafri in the Dolven-view'The first order of business: I have noticed a number of deep-claws roaming awfully near to the Dolven-view, haven't you? I think there is a great nest of them nearby.

'They are mild enough beasts, but their tunnelling cannot be borne. It is dangerous, and I think it is the very reason for all the pitfalls, collapses, and general rumblings in Moria.

'Let us lessen their numbers a bit. What do you say?''Hello again, ${PLAYER}. I am glad to see those deep-claws did not make slivers out of your hide! Well, you have done the dwarves of this expedition a good turn indeed.''Please, take out some of those deep-claws before they can collapse all of Moria. I fear they will be a persistent problem in your travels here.'The paths from the Dolven-view are clogged with debris and rubble, making travel difficult.The rock-fall that Sót has asked you to clear can be found in the eastern side of the Great Delving, south of the gate leading to the Lonely Span.

Sót, the librarian of the Dolven-view expedition, has asked you to aid him by clearing the road leading to the Lonely Span of debris and rubble.Clear rubble (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sót is at the Dolven-view camp, south-west of the Lonely Span.

The rubble from the rock-fall has been cleared out. You should return to Sót and let him know.Talk to Sót at the Dolven-view camp'Forgive me for asking, ${PLAYER}, but could you lend me a hand? I joined this expedition as a librarian, hoping to uncover the lost lore and mysteries of Khazad-dûm, but there is so much to be done around here that instead I've been assigned a list of labourious tasks to which I fear I am ill-suited!

'It appears that a recent rock-fall has littered the road between here and the Twenty-first Hall with rubble that makes travel difficult, and we need that stretch of the passage cleared if we are to continue to supply the Twenty-first Hall.

'The rock-fall occured in the eastern-most area of the Great Delving, along the path just south of the gate to the Lonely Span.''Excellent! With that path clear again, it will be much easier to deliver supplies to the Twenty-first Hall.''Keep working. We must get enough of the rubble clear that we can safely move supplies to our deeper encampments.'The Dunlendings scouring Eregion have been ordered to pillage anything they believe to be of merit to whomever is at the root of the White Hand activity. Though the forces are scattered amongst the ruins of Eregion, there are a good many who have been sent to a more specific location.Echad Mirobel is in the south-western stretches of Eregion.

You have found strange orders pertaining to the ransack of the School of Tham Mirdain, and a champion of the Dunlendings who will lead this assault on the lore-vault of the Elves. You should bring this message to Echad Mirobel, where someone will hopefully know what to make of it.The orders read thus:

'Scour the lands of Eregion. Leave no stone unturned. Go with your champion, Llygad, Blade of the Dunlending, into the School at Tham Mírdain and assist my Uruk-hai, and there you must obtain what knowledge you can and return it to me.'

And so the missive ends, brief but unmistakably clear. If there is still any knowledge to be gleaned from the wisdom of Tham Mirdain, the Elves of Echad Mirobel should be informed.'Our enemies to the south grow bold. We must endure so many foes in this land, but I think with your efforts these tasks will prove less painful than they have in the past. The arrival of this delivery does not weigh more heavily upon me, rather it inspires me to greater hope.

'We know now that the White Hand has intentions for the School at Tham Mírdain, so we can set a task to focus upon them. Thank you for showing me this message, ${PLAYER}. You have acted rightly.'Goblins have infested Gazatmur in alarming numbers and pose a great threat to the Dolven-view camp.Goblins can be found in Gazatmur, a large area in the east of the Great Delving.

You should defeat many goblins at Gazatmur to thin their numbers.Defeat goblins at Gazatmur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wigfast is at his hiding spot near Gazatmur, the goblin-encampment of the eastern Great Delving.

You should return to Wigfast now that you have thinned the goblins' ranks.Return to Wigfast at his hiding spot'Can you believe all of these goblins? You are a brave and skilled ${CLASS}, so it will be nothing to you to thin their numbers a bit. We have got to start somewhere.

'Be careful, friend. I do not like the looks of this place. The goblins seem more organized than usual.''That was a good start, ${PLAYER}! I thank you for your assistance in making these halls safer for our expedition.''There is something unusually bad about Gazatmur. I do not like the way the goblins seem so organized in their movements.'Wegil has given you directions to follow the road towards the new Dolven-view camp in the Great Delving.The road heads east from Wegil and makes towards the Dolven-view.

You should follow the road towards the Dolven-view and stop to speak with any dwarf-travellers you see along the way.Follow the road further into Moria'If you wish to go further into Moria, you will want to follow the road towards the Dolven-view. Perhaps you will encounter more dwarves along the way, and they can help you get there.

'If you see any dwarves cut off from the rest throughout your travels, please endeavour to assist them! I fear this is a more dangerous place than we anticipated upon our arrival.''Hail, traveller! Behold Lamab-dûm; beautiful, is it not? If you have time, we could use your assistance, for we are very curious about what lies near here.''Follow the road towards the east...and do look out for any travellers you see along the way!'The goblins encamped below the Dolven-view have become a great threat to the dwarves, driven by their overseers to greater violence than is usual for them.Goblin-overseers can be found in and around the encampment Gazatmur.

Slagvi told you that the goblin-overseers must be defeated if the goblin-encampment threatening the Dolven-view is to be destroyed.Defeat goblin-overseers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wigfast can be found at his hiding spot near Gazatmur in the Great Delving.

You should return to Wigfast and inform him that the goblins' overseers have been defeated.Return to Wigfast'Now that we have weakened the defences of the goblin-camp below, we may soon be in a position to launch a full assault against them.

'Go down there and see if you cannot defeat a few of the goblins' overseers. With the strongest goblins out of the way, the weaker ones will be unable to unite against us.

'Much depends upon your success, ${PLAYER}. Be careful!''Your courage knows no bounds, ${PLAYER}. We are nearly ready to strike at their camp.''With the overseers organizing the goblins down there, it's only a matter of time before they amass together to destroy us. See that they do not get the chance!'Goblins have made their home in Khazad-dûm like a swarm of ants, ever burrowing under the mountains and seeking the riches of the dwarves. To curb their growth would be a heroic deed, both in Moria and elsewhere in Middle-earth, for they are a dangerous nuisance wherever they reside.Defeat goblins in MoriaRáthulf grieves for the dwarves who lost their lives to the Watcher in the Water.Outside of the Hollin Gate lies a small graveyard where the fallen dwarves lie.

You should plant a banner at the graveyard just outside the Hollin Gate.Plant a banner at the grave of the fallen dwarvesRáthulf is at Durin's Threshold in Moria.

You should return to Ráthulf and tell him of your service to the fallen dwarves.Return to Ráthulf'Those poor dwarves! They met their doom before they could feast their eyes upon the splendour of Moria! Our victory over this gate is a bittersweet one for me.

'I would like to honour the fallen, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps you can plant a banner at their graves, so that we will all remember their bravery and sacrifice.''That was a good deed, ${PLAYER}! Thank you for honouring my stalwart friends. I hope they rest well in sight of the halls of their forefathers.''The graveyard is just outside, if you wish to pay your respects.'You have been encouraged to learn the hidden tracks and paths of Eregion so that you may travel there more quickly.Explore the Elf ruins and dens of the beasts found in Eregion.

Tinúriel told you that for you to learn the quickest route to Echad Dúnann in Eregion, you must explore the land and learn its hidden tracks and paths.Complete the deed "Dens of the Beasts"Complete the deed "The Ruins of Eregion"Tinúriel is at Echad Dúnann in Eregion.

Now that you have explored Eregion and become familiar with its ruins and the dens of the beasts here, you will be able to understand Tinúriel's instruction on the secret way to Echad Dúnann.Talk to Tinúriel at Echad Dúnann'Hail, ${PLAYER}. Have you seen much of the Eregion? It has much changed since Elves lived here, and there is little of the Elves left here. I have spent much time learning these changes, so that we can move quickly here to Echad Dúnann unseen by the eyes of the Enemy.

'If you would seek to learn these paths, I would share such knowledge with you. First, though, you must explore Eregion. Many of the landmarks and points I reference would be useless to you unless you saw them first with your own eyes.

'Go and explore Eregion. Once you have done so, return to me, and I shall share with you my knowledge of the secret way to Echad Dúnann.''I can see that you have not yet fully explored Eregion. You must do this first, otherwise my instruction on the hidden path to Echad Dúnann would be useless to you.''You have explored Eregion, ${PLAYER}? This is good. These lands are much changed, and there is little of the land that remembers the Elves. Even though we camp here now on an errand for Master Elrond, we soon will be gone, and I fear the land will forget us completely.

'However, those are matters for another day. For now, Elves walk these lands and our knowledge can hamper the efforts of the Enemy. Here, ${PLAYER}, take this guide and learn from it. Use such knowledge well.'You found a dropped dwarf-axe upon the road and are currently searching for the dwarf who wielded it.The owner of the axe will likely be somewhere in the tunnels near Durin's Threshold, towards the west of the Great Delving.

You should search for the owner of the axe.Find the owner of the dropped axeTúbi Thickfist is atop the stairs at Durin's Threshold.

Kambi told you of the goblin-chieftan's ramblings of his tribe and the voice he fears. He asked you to inform Túbi Thickfist as soon as possible.Talk to Túbi ThickfistThis axe is dwarf-make and looks to have been abandoned recently. Perhaps one of the dwarf expeditionaries has encountered trouble upon the road.

You should search nearby for the owner of this axe.'What Kambi says is disturbing. A goblin-tribe this close to the entrance bothers me. We cannot safely reclaim Moria with such an impending threat.

'I am curious as to the nature of this voice, as well. We must do what we can to locate their camp, for while Moria contains many unsleeping things that disappear into the darkness, goblins are not one of them.''I am a silly old fool for rushing in here without any help, but I thought this mad goblin was just up here by himself. Little did I know, the goblin is skilled at combat.

'He has spoken madness since then of a tribe lurking in the darkness. Somewhere near, led by a mysterious voice from the darkness. It is something he fears greatly.

'Do not worry about me...this leg is not as bad as it looks. Go and let Túbi know about the goblins and the voice. Those are far more troublesome than this nick on my leg.''Hurry up. Let Túbi know about the goblin-tribe and this mysterious voice. They are not going to simply go away and leave us alone.'Slagvi wishes to investigate failure of the water systems in the Great Delving, and he believes the source of the trouble is in the cooling chamber itself.A summoning horn stands at the front of the cooling chamber.

The summoning horn can be used to call Slagvi to your side.Use the summoning horn to call SlagviSlagvi is at your side in the cooling chamber.

You should speak with Slagvi.Talk to SlagviSlagvi wants the goblin-leader who has claimed the cooling chamber found and defeated.Find and defeat the Moria chieftainThe items to repair can be found at the back of the cooling chamber.Fix the jammed leverRepair the rusted gearRepair the stuck wheelTalk to Slagvi. You can summon him if you become separated.Talk to SlagviIt is time to exit the cooling chamber.Exit the cooling chamber'Ah, so here we are! What a marvellously constructed place this is. But... I fear there are enemies all around us. I will do my best to help you clear them out.''You did very well, my friend! Thank you for your help. I would not have been able to face so many goblins alone.'Spalvi Stout-heart has decided that there is no other way, and if you wish to find Bingo again you will need to follow the Iron Garrison into Moria.Spalvi has agreed to meet you just inside the entrance to the dwarf-kingdom of Moria once the Iron Garrison has opened the Doors of Durin at the Hollin Gate.Complete 'Volume II, Book 1: The Walls of Moria' by speaking to Ráthwald near Echad Dúnann and completing his quest chainSpalvi Stout-heart is in Durin's Threshold, just inside the western entrance to Moria.

Spalvi has decided that following the Iron Garrison into Moria is your best hope of finding Bingo Boffin.Talk to Spalvi in Durin's Threshold, in the Great Delving of MoriaKetill Map-maker is in the Dolven-view, located in the Great Delving of Moria.

Spalvi has heard that a dwarf with the Iron Garrison named Ketill is making maps of Khazad-dûm and might be able to help you find Bingo.Talk to Ketill Map-maker at the Dolven-view, in the Great DelvingKetill Map-maker has asked you to fight enemies in Gazatmur, east of the Dolven-view, until he is done working.Ketill Map-maker can be found perched on a wall overlooking Gazatmur, east of the Dolven-view.Talk to Ketill Map-maker overlooking Gazatmur, east of the Dolven-viewKetill Map-maker has asked you to fight enemies in Katûb-zahar, north-east of the Dolven-view, until he is done working.Ketill Map-maker can be found on the highest ledge in the middle of the library of Katûb-zahar, north-east of the Dolven-view.Talk to Ketill Map-maker on the highest ledge of Katûb-zaharSpalvi is in the Dolven-view, in the Great Delving of Moria.Talk to Spalvi at the Dolven-view, in the Great Delving'I had hoped we might not have to follow the Longbeards into Moria, ${PLAYER}. I may not be a Dourhand any longer, but the old resentments are not so easily swept away. Well, if they do not greet me with steel I will repay them with kindness, and not in kind!

'During our time here, I have learned that the Iron Garrison travelled south-east to the ruins of Echad Dúnann, outside the Hollin Gate. You should speak to the dwarves there and see if they have gained access to Khazad-dûm! If they already have done so, or once they do, I will meet up with you inside the entrance to the great dwarf-kingdom!''During our time here, I have learned that the Iron Garrison travelled south-east to the ruins of Echad Dúnann, outside the Hollin Gate. You should speak to the dwarves there and see if they have gained access to Khazad-dûm! If they already have done so, or once they do, I will meet up with you inside the entrance to the great dwarf-kingdom!''During our time here, I have learned that the Iron Garrison travelled south-east to the ruins of Echad Dúnann, outside the Hollin Gate. You should speak to the dwarves there and see if they have gained access to Khazad-dûm! If they already have done so, or once they do, I will meet up with you inside the entrance to the great dwarf-kingdom!''I cannot believe I stand here, ${PLAYER}, at the foot of the great steps within Khazad-dûm! The sight takes my breath away!'

Spalvi's good eye is bright with wonder.

'Skorgrím spoke of reclaiming the glory of the dwarves, but he always said it was the Elves that took it from us. I see now that our glory was not truly taken away, and that it was merely lost for a time. It remained here beneath the mountains for us to find once again!

'I cannot thank you and Bingo enough for crossing my path, ${PLAYER}, or I would never have seen these halls! Let us find our lost friend! The dwarves here speak of a map-maker named Ketill who works out of a place called the Dolven-view, to the east. He will know the ins and outs of exploring Khazad-dûm!''The dwarves here speak of a map-maker named Ketill who works out of a place called the Dolven-view, to the east. He will know the ins and outs of exploring Khazad-dûm!''Yes? You are interested in my maps? Perfect, perfect! It is always a pleasure to meet a fellow enthusiast! There is a great deal of craft involved with drawing accurate maps, and you would be surprised how few folk truly appreciate the effort!

'Just between you and me, I think the rest of the Iron Garrison would care more about my maps if I included the locations of precious veins and ore deposits on them, but those would be out of place on these maps! Perhaps I will make a second set of maps later on. But for now these maps are purely for rooms and chambers and tunnels and caves. As a maker of maps, it is important to know your focus, and to keep it narrow!

'I am focused on making maps, and therefore I am less capable in combat. Will you help me defeat enemies at the next location I need to map? While you fight, I will draw, and in that way we will be of great help to each other. Gazatmur is to the east of here!''Please do not bother me right now. I am busy working! If you keep defeating foes in Gazatmur this will take less time!''Are you willing to help me map the library of Katûb-zahar, to the north-east? Perfect!''Thank you very much, my helpful friend! I am sorry that took awhile, but making a map takes time and if you rush it you ruin it!

'The next location I was hoping to finish mapping is a library to the north-east of here called Katûb-zahar. Will you fight the enemies we find within while I work?''Please do not bother me right now. I am busy working! If you keep defeating foes here in Katûb-zahar this will take less time!''Finished! Thank you for your help! Now that I have some time to think, why don't you tell me what it is you are seeking within these halls?'

You tell Ketill an abbreviated version of the adventure that resulted in your separation from Bingo. The dwarf thinks for a moment.

'It is not out of the question to believe that he might have fallen into an underground river and been swept into Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Unlikely, perhaps, but it sounds as if this fellow might be rather unlikely himself! I will continue to study the maps I have available and let you know if I uncover any possible hiding-places for this hobbit of yours, my friend. It is the least I can do!''It is not out of the question to believe that your Bingo might have fallen into an underground river and been swept into Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Unlikely, perhaps, but it sounds as if this fellow might be rather unlikely himself! I will continue to study the maps I have available and let you know if I uncover any possible hiding-places for this hobbit of yours, my friend. It is the least I can do!''We have made a good start of it, my friend. Ketill Map-maker may come up with some idea of places we can search for Bingo, and I will make good the wrong I caused when I was a Dourhand. I am certain it is close!

'Willem Whisker did not stay here in the Dolven-view for long. He too is searching for Bingo! I know we will find our missing hobbit, and I trust that it will be soon!'

<rgb=#00FF00>Bert Bartleby has arrived at the Dolven-view, in the Great Delving of Moria.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Willem Takes the Lead' (Recommended Level: 53)</rgb>The paths to and from the Dolven-view are dark, but adjusting an ancient light-reflecting mirror has helped to light the way.Slagvi is at the Dolven-view camp in the Great Delving in Moria.

You should speak with Slagvi of the mirror you adjusted.Speak with Slagvi at the Dolven-viewAdjusting this mirror has helped the paths of the Dolven-view to be much better lit than they were previously. This will likely save many from falling or taking a wrong turn.'So you were the one that adjusted the light, were you? At first I thought there was a fire, and that we were about to be attacked, but then I realized that the light was a warm, gentle one. 

'I knew then that it came from one of the ancient mirrors I've heard so much about. I am only happy that I lived to see the beauty of the light system in Khazad-dûm.'You have discovered a strange growth unlike any you have seen in the Palace of Náin.Thórhall is at the small dwarf-encampment at Lamab-dûm.

You should tell Thórhall of the strange fungus you found in the Palace of Náin.Tell Thórhall of the fungus you sawThe Dolven-view camp is the central dwarf-hub in the Great Delving.

You should bring word of the strange fungus you marked to someone in the Dolven-view.Tell someone in the Dolven-view camp about the fungusWhat an odd-looking fungus this is....

It may be wise to report to the dwarves that strange flora seems to be creeping into Moria. There is something about the look of that fungus and the surrounding area that is strangely unnerving.'A fungus? That is no surprise, ${PLAYER}. Such things grow in damp places all over the earth.'

Thórhall listens as you explain that you are aware of the nature of fungus, but that this one was strange and new and gave you a sense of foreboding.

'Upon my word... you do look a little peaked. Perhaps you should bring this news to the Dolven-view camp. That is where we are headed as well.''You found an unusual fungus? I am not surprised. Well, fortunately it seems somewhat contained. Hopefully the Palace of Náin is the only place where it grows.

'In the meantime, I will make sure to warn my folk to steer clear of that place, in case this fungus is of a putrid nature.'A final award for achieving level 51 has been mailed to you by an unknown benefactor.Achieve level 51The bridge running beneath the Dwarf-lords' Gate contains a hidden waterway that once brought fresh water to the Dolven-view. According to the journal you found, the waterway was closed long ago.The bridge is very near the fallen rucksack and book of the dwarf who fell to his death.

You should throw the levers on the bridge to open the waterway running from the Dwarf-Lord's Gate to the Dolven-view.Throw levers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The bridge lies to the north of the Dolven-view.Wafri is at the Dolven-view camp, south of the bridge.

You should return to Wafri and inform him that, even though you threw all the levers, you did not hear any water flow through the ancient waterways.Talk to Wafri at the Dolven-view campThe journal indicates that there should be an old waterway running beneath the bridge north of here, through the Dwarf-lords' Gate. It should be providing water to the Dolven-view, but it appears to have been closed.

There should be a pair of levers on the bridge that can be thrown to open the old waterway, and the fallen dwarf seemed to want to do this very task. You should take over in his stead.'A journal of a fallen dwarf pointed you to the levers of the Dolven-view water sources? How strange! What a brave dwarf, and you were very good for making the effort on his behalf, whoever he was.

'It will be some time before we can spare a team of craftsmen to go down there and try to repair them. How sad that one should fall while pursuing a fruitless endeavour!'Angmarim scour Eregion in search of any remnants of the past that may further strengthen their forces. The small band of Elves found at Echad Mirobel wish to preserve the ruins as they are, and have asked you to assist them in this mission.The Angmarim can be found throughout Mirobel in southern Eregion, near the Elf-haven of Echad Mirobel.

You should seek out Angmarim in Mirobel and collect proof that they travel with Angmarim Iron. If the fears of Ornras are true, the tide could easily turn against the Elves with the forging of great weapons on the enemy's side.'To our great dismay, we have learned that the Angmarim have established an outpost amongst the ruins of Mirobel. Through the repeated efforts of valiant folk such as yourself, we have done well to thin their numbers and ease the threat they present. There are... other matters at hand, however... and these matters, while requiring the Angmarim to further establish themselves in these lands, could prove particularly dangerous if our efforts prove vain.

'To that end, I will dispatch you to Mirobel in search of a very rare iron found only on the borders of Angmar and Forochel. This iron, taken from deep within the core of the frozen mountains, can be worked into a terrible metal in the hands of a skilled artisan. Though I think it improbable that such an artisan is among our foes, I would rather err on the side of caution and ensure the safety of my people.

'Only the Angmarim would be allowed to carry this iron. Search among them for the iron. Return to me when you have proven my inkling right or wrong.''This is an unnerving discovery. None of our efforts have yielded any indication that there is an accomplished weaponsmith amongst the Angmarim camped here, yet still they carry the Angmarim Iron with them.

'We must remain diligent in our efforts to thwart these enemies, ${PLAYER}. Your work does not go unnoticed.'Pale-folk pillagers and blades, working under the lash of the Ongbúrz, are ransacking the Library of Tham Mírdain for anything of value.The Pale-folk pillagers and blades can be found throughout the Library of Tham Mirdaín.Defeat pale-folk pillagers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat pale-folk blades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Overmasters command the slave forces of Angmar. The Men we encounter in the ruins are too bold and brash to yield to the lash of an Overseer, so I do not think that these will be the slaves to which I refer. Nay, I think that there is something else digging under the Overmasters' watchful eyes.

Our scouts mentioned seeing the leaders entering the Library at Tham Mírdain. We can unseat them from this place if we keep our foray small -- no more than three, for, as before, we do not want to attract the attention of the southern enemies in this area. This is a frustrating way to go about things, but unless many reinforcements arrive unlooked for in these parts, we will have to continue to chip away at our foes.

I hope you can go through the Library in safety, friend. It will not be easy, but I have faith that you can do this. May the blessings of the Eldar keep you, ${PLAYER}.Ongbúrz Overmasters can be found in the Library at Tham Mírdain, just to the south-west of Echad Mirobel.

Hethugúr of Echad Mirobel has asked you to defeat Orc Overmasters at the Library, and to bring no more than a small handful of stout companions with you. The southern forces must not be alerted of your presence, so attacks against either side must be small and covert.Slay Ongbúrz Overmasters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You found some strange papers in the library of Katûb-zahar, and should bring them to a dwarf who may know more of them.Sót, the librarian of the Dolven-view camp, might know more about the papers you found. You should speak with him.Bring the strange runes to Sót at the Dolven-viewThese papers are full of runes you do not recognize translated into the Common Tongue. It means nothing to you, but the strange runes are of some interest, for they do not look to be any language that you recognize. The papers are signed "Falgeirr Twisttongue."'Hammer and tongs! These papers must date back to the time of Durin's rule! A very promising find, ${PLAYER}.

'Falgeirr Twisttongue was a famous riddle-master and tinkerer of words. These runes are utterly foreign to me...so I believe they may be a special language he made up! You should hang onto these papers, in case you see any of these runes in Moria. I have a feeling old Falgeirr left some puzzles to be solved!'Goblin-messengers have been busy running information to and fro about the movements of the newly-arrived dwarves in Moria.Goblin-messengers can be found running along Snaga-maudhûl, the goblin-camp on the west road in the Great Delving.

You should defeat the malicious messengers so that they will stop reporting the movements of the dwarves along the roads.Defeat goblin-messengers in Snaga-maudhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wegil is outside the back gate of Snaga-maudhûl.

You should speak with Wegil on your way eastwards through the Great Delving.Find Wegil on the other side of Snaga-maudhûl'I have been seeing a great deal of movement among the goblin-messengers at this camp. I do not like Snaga-maudhûl's nearness to Durin's Threshold, nor the road to the Dolven-view.

'They are watching all of our movements and running communications hither and thither! I fear that many dwarves using the roads here will lose their lives to this unhindered flow of malicious information.

'I am sure you wish to hasten eastwards, but if you could do me this favour as you pass through the camp, I would appreciate it!''Oh! Hello there! Did you just fight your way through Snaga-maudhûl? That is incredible!

'I am here to offer assistance on the road to those who may be waylaid by the goblins. It is nervous work indeed!''The goblin-messengers can be found inside of Snaga-maudhûl. There is the gate, just there.'Thórhall hopes to study the anatomy of gredbyg to learn more about them, so that they can be better combatted in the future.Gredbyg can be found in a hive in the Palace of Náin.

You have been asked to collect anatomical items of interest from the gredbyg for study.Collect grodbog scent-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thórhall is at the small dwarf-camp in Lamab-dûm in the Great Delving.

You should bring the scent-glands you have collected to Thórhall, so that he may study them.'I should like to learn about these odious insects while you're working on driving them off. Will you do me a great favour, and bring me anything out of the ordinary that can be found on their anatomy?

'I hope that studying the gredbyg will give us better tools to fight them.''Have you found anything of interest on those gredbyg yet?''Scent-glands, eh? Very interesting...I have not seen many creatures such as this in possession of glands of this nature.

'I have a theory, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps these can be used to lure whatever menace is at the centre of the infestation at the Palace of Náin, eh?'The goblins have established a large encampment in Gazatmur, which worries the dwarves at the Dolven-view.The goblin encampment lies below the Dolven-view at Gazatmur. Good vantage points for scouting can be found to the north and south of the encampment.

Slagvi has asked you to scout a large goblin encampment. He warned you to avoid being seen.Find Wigfast, the scout at Gazatmur'Well, ${PLAYER}, as you can see even from here, there is a large encampment of goblins down there in Gazatmur, off to the north-east a way. We haven't the forces to push them out of there now, but I would like you to get down there and join Wigfast, who has gone to scout the encampment.

'I am sure Wigfast could use help with assessing the situation down there. He is brave for going off to scout, but I do not think he will be of much use by himself.''Ah! Did Slagvi send you? Just in time -- I was about to try to venture in there and start lobbing off goblin-heads all by myself, though I am ill-equipped for such a venture!''Wigfast is a bold scout, but he will need your aid if he means to come back alive.'Jarmárr wants the newly discovered goblin-camp removed. Snaga-maudhûl is a threat to all who travel from the Hollin Gate into the rest of Moria.The goblin-camp lies in the tunnels beyond the crack above the eastern stair.

The dwarves want to end the goblins' reign over the tunnels below to ensure the safety and security of their foothold.Defeat Moria soldiers in Snaga-maudhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wegil is on the north-east side of Snaga-maudhûl, standing watch on the road.

You should find and speak with Wegil.Talk to Wegil on the north-east side of Snaga-maudhûl'I am glad a greater warrior than I is here to do some damage to these menacing little fiends. Their camp here utterly threatens all travel from Durin's Threshold to the Dolven-view and beyond.

'All dwarves who come into Moria will pass this way, and we cannot have Snaga-maudhûl looming beneath the roadway! On your way through, ${PLAYER}, please thin out this malicious nest of goblins.''Ho there! Are you hurt? No, I can see that you are not. But you seem to have hurt many goblins during your short stay in Snaga-maudhûl, and I'll thank you for that!

'I am here to assist travellers who may be hindered on the road as they pass that rotten goblin-camp, but since you seem to have waylaid them, I will help you on your way!''The goblins must be driven from Snaga-maudhûl if we are to reclaim Moria for the dwarves.'Some of the ancient archives of Durin's Folk are located within the Great Delving, or so says a journal you encountered on the road.The library called Katûb-zahar indicated by the journal is located north of Gazatmur, north-east of the Dolven-view.

You should search the ancient libraries of Khazad-dûm for the ancient tome.Find the ancient tomeSót is at the Dolven-view, south-west of Katûb-zahar.

You should bring the tome you found to Sót. He will be eager to peruse it.This journal page describes a hope to reach the old libraries of Khazad-dûm, known as Katûb-zahar. The dwarf who owned this book was seeking an old text within which is rumoured to detail the ancient methods of blending mithril with other metals, along with many other secrets of its proper forging.

It seems a worthy search. You should continue the fallen dwarf's quest.'You found a journal on the road with the objective of recovering this book? Amazing! But....

'Alas! The years and the foul vermin infesting Khazad-dûm have been most unkind... so many pages are ruined!

'No matter. With enough time, I'm sure I can piece it back together, even if it takes me years!'The Elves of Echad Mirobel have tracked Angmar's forces in Eregion to an ancient library.The Library of Tham Mírdain can be found in Mirobel, in the south-west region of Eregion.

Ornras of Echad Mirobel has asked you to find the entrance to an ancient library.Find the Library of Tham Mírdain'We have tracked the smiths' weapons to an ancient library near Mirobel, at Tham Mírdain. Venture forth and find this place. I am sure there are greater mysteries lying in wait within.''Find the Library of Tham Mírdain, ${PLAYER}...it is most urgent.'Grants completion of quest: Seeker of KnowledgeBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Seeker of Knowledge'Now, my little fellows, where be you a-going to, puffing like a bellows? What's the matter here then? Tell me what's your trouble!

'You need to play the instances? Naught worse that that, eh? That can soon be mended.''Well, my little fellows! You shall have your deeds completed!'An Uruk in the service of the White Hand has appeared in the goblin-camp at Gazatmur. Clearly, he plans to subdue the goblins to his will and drive them against the Dwarves of Dolven-view in great numbers.The White-hand Lieutenant can be found in Gazatmur, north-east of the Dolven-view.

You should defeat the White-hand Lieutenant.Defeat the White Hand lieutenantWigfast is at his hiding spot near the entry-way of Gazatmur.

You should seek out Wigfast and tell him of the White Hand corruption you discovered and quelled in one swoop.This goblin-shield bears a mark of the White Hand, a strange thing to find in Moria... or perhaps not strange. Surely a servant of the White Hand is nearby, responsible for stirring up evil in Gazatmur. If that servant is taken out, perhaps the goblin presence will be dispelled in the Great Delving.'White Hand mark, and an enemy Uruk leading it all? That is strange news, and I am not sure what to make of it, but it sounded like an altogether disagreeable affair. I am glad you put a stop to it, ${PLAYER}.'Athils is looking for assistance in getting an old forge in the North Wing up and running.Dull blades can be found on weapon-racks in the North Wing of Durin's Threshold.

You should collect several dull blades for restoration in the newly-lit forge.Collect dull blades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The forge of the North Wing can be found near Athils.

You should use the forge to restore the blades you collected.Use the forge to restore the blades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Athils is in the North Wing of Durin's Threshold, overseeing the work being done there.

You should bring the newly restored blades to Athils.'Ah, hello, ${PLAYER}! We are off to a rough start here, to be sure, but is this not an exciting time? Already we have excavated these most impressive forges.

'Would you like to help me set up shop? Be careful... the fires are hot. The Dwarves of Moria knew what they were about when they built these!''You can find the old dull blades strewn about the North Wing. You needn't look too far.''Ah, that is fine work, good ${RACE}! I can tell this was forged in Moria -- the improvement is remarkable already. I look forward to the work to be done here.'The goblins have built a series of platforms from which their archers can rain arrows upon any attackers bold enough to confront them.The goblin-platforms are near the goblin camp of Gazatmur in the Great Delving.

Wigfast has asked you to bring down a few of the goblin's archer-platforms with a simple hammer.Destroy goblin-platforms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wigfast is at his hiding spot outside Gazatmur in the great Delving.

You should return to Wigfast and let him know that you have destroyed the goblin archer-platforms as he requested.'The goblins of Gazatmur have stationed archers upon those platforms. Anyone who tries to attack them directly will be slaughtered. They will make the road perilous for those trying to move through the Great Delving. 

'The platforms are of typical goblin-make, from what I've seen: clever idea, but shoddy. There is a major pin at the base of the shaft that holds the platforms up: pop that out with one or two good whacks of your trusty hammer, and the whole thing comes right down.''Those archers are not going to stop shooting on their own. Go knock down a few of those platforms!''Good work, ${PLAYER}. They will put those platforms back up sooner or later, but in the meantime, our forays against the goblins will be a little more successful without all those arrows raining down upon us!'Several coin purses have gone missing from travellers who had encounters with the Snaga-maudhûl goblins.The goblin-thieves can be found in Snaga-maudhûl, in the western area of the Great Delving.

You should reclaim the coins of dwarf-travellers that have been stolen by the waylaying goblins.Reclaim the stolen coins of the dwarves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wegil can be found on the north-east side of Snaga-maudhûl in the Great Delving.

You should bring the coins you recovered to Wegil.'It seems as though anyone who encounters the goblins and manages to escape finds their coin purses much lighter than they were previously.

'In fact, my own coin purse is a bit lighter now. I would appreciate if you could go in there and take back the goods that were stolen from the innocent travellers passing through here.''The missing coins will surely be found on those goblins, or I'm no dwarf!''Well, look here! I always suspected those goblins were thieves and worse! Thank you for bringing these back to the side of the dwarves; I will make sure these coins find their way back to their owners.'Angmarim scour Eregion in search of any remnants of the past that may further strengthen their forces. The small band of Elves found at Echad Mirobel wish to preserve the ruins as they are and have asked you to assist them in this mission.A smith can be found in Mirobel, in the south-west region of Eregion.

Ornras of Echad Mirobel has asked you to defeat enemies in that region and hopefully find one who bears Angmar's Brand. A great smith hidden among the lesser enemies would explain why powerful and fell ore is carried by some of the leaders of this northern host.'I hate to do this, I must ask you to assuage my fears and return to Mirobel, and to the presence of the Angmarim there. You have done much already, but the hardships are never done when such foes are at hand.

'My heart warns me that there is a smith among the Angmarim capable of working with the iron you discovered. I would ask that you return to Mirobel and search many Angmarim there. You might very well find a smith bearing a Brand of Angmar. In fact, I expect that you will.

'I have seen these brands before and they denote a level of respect to the prowess of the smith who possesses the item. Only a great smith would carry one, and only a great smith would work with the fell ore you found. If you eliminate this smith, the bearer of the Brand, you may do more than you guess to hinder the dour work of this presence from the north.''Coupled with tidings we are receiving from scouts throughout Eregion and those very nearby, the proof of this smith is grave news. Still, I am heartened to know that he is dead, and can assist the enemy no more.'Your foray into Târ Stazg has had the opposite effect as intended: Târ Stazg is readying an assault against the Elves of Eregion.Akashpug is at Târ Stazg, north-east of Echad Dúnann, along the mountains before the Redhorn Gate.

Palanaer has instructed you to call forth Akashpug with the horn and defeat him.Palanaer is in Echad Dúnann, south-west of Târ Stazg.

You should return to Palanaer with news of Akashpug's defeat.Talk to Palanaer'Akashpug, the leader of Târ Stazg is no half-orc; he is  one of Saruman's Uruk-hai, and he is more cunning and cruel than any other of his kind I have encountered.  

'Already, he has brought up reinforcements from the South to replace those that were slain in our first assault on his camp. If we do not act quickly, he will soon be marching to Barad Morlas.

'Return to Târ Stazg, north-east of Echad Dúnann, along the mountains before the Redhorn Gate. Use the horn of challenge you find there to call him forth. If you are able to defeat him, the half-orcs will be thrown into disarray, and we will have time to prevent their march.''Târ Stazg is north-east of Echad Dúnann, along the mountains before the Redhorn Gate.''With Akashpug defeated, the half-orcs will be leaderless and unable to aid Barad Morlas.

'We must now take thought on how to drive the remaining half-orcs from Eregion.'The Cooling Chamber is an ancient structure used to collect, cool, and purify the hot steam from the forges below.Slagvi is at the Dolven-view camp.

Slagvi wishes to enter the Cooling Chamber in hopes to restore the Great Delving's natural water system to an operational state.Explore the cooling chamber with SlagviSlagvi is at the Dolven-view camp.

You should speak with Slagvi.Talk to Slagvi at the Dolven-view camp'${PLAYER}, I would like to know more about why the water systems of the Great Delving are not operational. I do not relish the idea of our expedition needing to rely upon imported water.

'There is a Cooling Chamber not far from here, and perhaps we should investigate it. I am not unfamiliar with such systems, so I believe I will be useful in trying to get the system working again.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This instance is intended for solo players, but can be completed with up to two people in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready to leave? I don't know what is going on inside the cooling chamber, but I know we must move quickly if we wish to find out.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This instance is intended for solo players, but can be completed with up to two people in a fellowship.</rgb>'Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}! I would not have been able to restore those systems by myself with so many goblins at hand. You have done much for the Dolven-view camp, but I believe we are ready to fend for ourselves. The Deep Descent awaits you!'Thórhall believes that the scent-glands you gathered may lure the hive-queen into revealing herself, allowing her to be slain.The grodbog-lair is in the Palace of Náin, north of Lamâb-dûm.

Thórhall asked you to take the scent-glands to the grodbog-hive and crush them. The resulting scent should draw forth the hive-queen.Thórhall is at the small dwarf-camp in Lamab-dûm, south of the Palace of Náin.

You should report back to Thórhall with news of your success.'What do you know, ${PLAYER}; I have had an idea! If you crush the scent-glands you gathered, an overwhelming scent will be released, and the gredbyg will rise up.

'The scent will undoubtedly draw the hive-queen from her hidden nest. If you can slay her, the entire hive will be greatly weakened... at least until they can raise a new queen. That should keep them out of our way for quite a while, and that is the best we can hope for.''Did my plan work, ${PLAYER}?

'What? You haven't tried it yet? Well, get to it! Better you than me.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}! With the grodbog hive-queen slain, the hive will be thrown into disarray, and their numbers will likewise diminish... at least until they can raise a new queen.'Thórhall is disturbed by the strange noises being emitted all around Lamab-dûm, and fears that the noise comes from the gredbyg that crawl all over.A swarm of gredbyg can likely be found in a hive in the Palance of Náin, north of Lamab-dûm in the Great Delving.

Thórhall wants you to kill off as many gredbyg as you can.Defeat gredbyg in the Palace of Náin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thórhall is at his camp in Lamab-dûm in the Great Delving.

You should return to Thórhall and tell him that the grodbog presence is somewhat lessened in the hive to the north.Return to Thórhall at Lamab-dûm'Strange sounds and strange creeping shadows surround us here... do you feel uneasy? I think it is coming from the north. There is a sickly light about that place.

'I have noticed a great increase in the gredbyg about this place. Perhaps it is their hive up yonder... will you go and thin their numbers? I will rest easier if I know there are less of them to crawl over me in my sleep!''Brrr! Those gredbyg do make me shiver!''Ah! A fine effort, ${PLAYER}. Would that this were the end of them! But I suppose I will have to settle for this valiant endeavour of yours. You have my thanks!'The dwarves of the Dolven-view wish to mark the Lonely Span as a passageway owned now by dwarves, and no other creature of Moria.The Lonely Span can be found by following the east path past the Cooling Chamber from the Dolven-view camp.

You should head to the Lonely Span and plant a banner of the dwarves there.Plant a banner to claim the Lonely Span for the dwarvesSót is in the Dolven-view in the Great Delving of Moria.

You should return to Sót now that the bridge to the Twenty-first Hall has been claimed by the dwarf-expedition.Return to Sót at the Dolven-view'Have you seen the Lonely Span yet? It is a bridge that connects the Great Delving to the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek, and it is a vital checkpoint in our expedition.

'If it is safe, you should plant a banner of the dwarves there. As long as it stands, we will know that the Lonely Span is held for the dwarves of Khazad-dûm!''Well done, ${PLAYER}! As long as that banner stands, the Lonely Span will be safe for the members of this expedition and all the Free Peoples who wish to use this road once more! It was a small task, but a meaningful one.'Wárr is most likely anxious for news of the rest of the dwarves from the expedition. A natural passage, great and winding, connects the Twenty-first Hall with the Chamber of the Cross-roads.Wárr is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, just north of the Twenty-first Hall, far to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

You must travel east from the Chamber of the Cross-roads through the great winding road leading to the Twenty-first Hall.Find the Western Gate of the Twenty-first HallWárr is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, north of the Twenty-first Hall, far to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Líkmund has asked you to speak with Wárr and relay what you know of recent events from the Chamber of the Cross-roads.'You've been a great help to us, ${PLAYER}, and if you haven't been that way yet, you may want to head east to the Twenty-first hall and see our encampment there. The Twenty-first hall was one of the greatest halls in all of Moria in it's day, and will soon be so again if we are successful!

'The hall can be reached most directly by the road that leads east from here -- you can reach it by the passage that leads south-east out of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. It is a wide road built in a winding natural passage through the rock. Luck is with us, for it seems the goblins make little use of it, and the way is as safe as any down here... as long as we can keep watch on it at any rate.

'When you reach the hall, find Wárr and tell him how we are doing over here; he is the supervisor of the Twenty-first Hall expedition, and he'll be eager for news. He'll probably be in the Chamber of Mazarbul, just off the passage to the north of the Twenty-first Hall.''You should let Wárr at the Twenty-first Hall know how our expedition fares.''What's this, then? Líkmund sends word from the western halls of Durin's Way, does he? Good. I am happy enough to hear he still lives, for these are deadly halls.

'I suppose you're here to lend a hand, and not just to see the sights I suppose, though they are fine enough for any!'Rinneldor has asked you to seek out Limlaer who stands watch near the southern border of Eregion.The tower is upon a hill, south-west of Limlaer, who stands near the road leading south-west from Echad Dúnann.

Limlaer has asked you to go to a nearby tower and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for signs of the Company's passing.Limlaer is south-west of Echad Dúnann, along the Nan Sirannon road.

You should report your findings to Limlaer.Talk to Limlaer'Mae govannen! You were sent by Rinneldor, were you not? I have been tasked with searching the southern borders of this land for signs of the Company's passing, but as of yet I have found nothing.

'Rinneldor believes that they may have passed this way, though any travelling near Nan Curunír would need to be wary...and none more than the Company!

'I bid you travel south-west and aid me in my search. You will find a tower just south-west of here atop a hill. It faces towards the Gap of Rohan. <rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> out from that hill and report anything you find.''You found naught? It is as I believed. Mithrandir would not be so foolish as to let himself become ensnared again by Saruman the White. The Company did not come this way.''The tower lies south-west, within sight of Limlaer. Find the hill and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for signs of the Company's passing.'Thórhall has encouraged you to head east to the Dolven-view camp, the central hub of the dwarves in the Great Delving.The Dolven-view camp lies east of Lamab-dûm, at a somewhat central cross-roads in the Great Delving.

You should follow the lit road as best you can to the Dolven-view.Talk to Slagvi at the Dolven-view'You have done all that is needed for our little camp, ${PLAYER}, and we appreciate your help! But I expect you are excited to delve further into Moria, as we are.

'The Dolven-view camp is the central camp of the dwarves in the Great Delving. I expect that several dwarves will have settled there, and established many useful town services.''Are you not excited to press further into Moria? We certainly are.''Greetings, my good ${RACE}, and welcome to the Dolven-view! 'Tis a fine view indeed -- or at least it would be were it not cluttered with the cook-fires of a goblin horde beneath us....

'No matter. We will defend the Dolven-view at all costs, and find some way to drive these vermin from our ancestral homes. Mark my words ${PLAYER}, this will once again be a city of wonder and beautiful to behold, though we give our lives to achieve it!'Thormóth, leader of the dwarf-expedition group that holds Durin's Threshold, has asked you to help his folk get settled after the ordeal at the gate.Gamli and Ráthulf are in Durin's Threshold. Athils is in the North Wing of Durin's Threshold: up the stairs, to the north, and then west.

Thormóth has asked you to speak with some of the dwarves who are having difficulty in settling Durin's Threshold.Assist GamliAssist RáthulfAssist AthilsThormóth is in Durin's Threshold.

Having lent a helping hand at this first expedition site, you should now return to its leader.Speak with Thormóth'Welcome to Moria, ${PLAYER}. You join us at a momentous time! I am the master of the expedition group here at Durin's Threshold. Other expedition groups have already moved further on into the depths of Khazad-dûm, hoping to find Balin's expedition of some years ago and learn of their fate.

'My fellow dwarves are having a difficult time settling in, for a number of reasons. If you could assist them, I would be most grateful.''You should speak with Gamli, Ráthulf, and Athils, here in Durin's Threshold.''Thank you for all that you've done, ${PLAYER}. We are certainly off to a better start here now.'You recovered the item taken from the Company's camp-site, which turned out to be naught but a cooking pot, but Golgallon fears other more revealing signs may have been left.Rinneldor is at Echad Dúnann, some distance to the south-east of Echad Eregion.

Golgallon has asked you to speak with Rinneldor regarding the movements of the Company and the discoveries you have made.Talk to Rinneldor at Echad Dúnann'Indeed, we were fortunate that all that the Company left behind was a cooking pot, but I fear for the carelessness of the halflings. I am not sure that they yet understand fully that their quest is not a mere stroll in the wilderness.

'Nevertheless, it is our lot to make sure the Enemy does not learn more of the Company or its quest. To this end, I would have you go to Echad Dúnann, some distance to the south-east of here, and speak with Rinneldor.

'Tell him all that has transpired and serve him as best you may.''Hurry now to Echad Dúnann and speak with Rinneldor. The encampment lies to the south-east.''Welcome to Echad Dúnann, ${PLAYER}. I welcome your news, though it troubles me as well.

'Stay a while... we have much to discuss.'Falgeirr Twisttongue, a dwarf with a penchant for riddles, left messages throughout Moria for those with the key to solving his strange runes and twisting words. You have just such a key.You should try and solve Falgeirr Twisttongue's riddle:

I can sizzle like bacon; I am made with an egg,
I have plenty of backbone, but lack a good leg,
I peel layers like onions, but still remain whole,
I can be long, like a flag-pole, yet fit in small holes.
What am I?

The solution to the riddle can be found somewhere in the Silvertine Lodes.Solve Twisttongue's RiddleYou have found a plaque bearing the strange runes of Falgeirr Twisttongue, author of the papers you found in Katûb-zahar. When translated, they read as follows:

I can sizzle like bacon; I am made with an egg,
I have plenty of backbone, but lack a good leg,
I peel layers like onions, but still remain whole,
I can be long, like a flag-pole, yet fit in small holes.
What am I?Stíling noted that the armour of the goblins at Gamil Filik is of unusual make and is concerned about its origin.Goblins can be found in Gamil Filik, south-east of the Deep Descent camp.

Stíling has asked you to collect several pieces of the goblins' armour for him to examine.Collect goblin armour-scraps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Stíling is at the outskirts of Gamil Filik.

You should bring the armour back to Stíling for his examination.'The make of the goblin-armour disturbs me, ${PLAYER}. It is finer than I would expect them to have -- and certainly to make themselves. If the goblins are being supplied with armour and equipment from elsewhere in Khazad-dûm, then I think we had best find out where that source is and remove it.

'However, I cannot be certain of my fears unless I have some of their armour to examine. For that purpose, I would have you collect some of that armour from the goblins while you're in Gamil Filik.''See if you can get me a few pieces of that goblin-armour; we must know whence it came.''Ah, I had feared this was the case. Upon a closer look, it is no mystery where this came from -- these suits incorporate old pieces of dwarf-metal and armour from long ago. The craftsmanship is so fine that even the vast span of years between has not destroyed it.

'Unfortunately, what time could not ruin, the foul hands of goblin-smiths have. Some of these pieces must have been re-beaten and re-worked a dozen times by now and worn by even more goblins over the years since they were looted from the fallen or from hidden armouries of old. I fear they are of no use to us now.

'They serve only as another reminder of the ancient tragedies that engulfed fair Khazad-dûm in darkness.'Narmeleth seeks to put a final end to Mordrambor and Mordirith.Gath Forthnír is in the northern reaches of Angmar.

Golodir told you to bring the hilt to Narmeleth in Gath Forthnír.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>Narmeleth is in Gath Forthnír in the northern reaches of Angmar.

Narmeleth told you to gather friends and speak with her again to begin the final assault.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>Assault Gador GúlaranGath Forthnír is in the northern reaches of Angmar.

You should speak with Golodir in Gath Forthnír.Talk to Golodir at Gath ForthnírRivendell is in the north-east corner of the Trollshaws.

Golodir sent you to speak with Glorfindel and bring him news of Mordirith's defeat.Talk to Glorfindel in RivendellElrond can be found in the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

Glorfindel told you to deliver your tidings to Master Elrond.Talk to Elrond in RivendellFailloth is in the courtyard of the Last Homely House in Rivendell.

Elrond told you to retrieve Laerdan's legacy from Failloth, the caretakers of Rivendell.Talk to Failloth in Rivendell'I thought I had seen this hilt for the last time. The very weight of it brings back memories both painful and heartening. Long and well it served me before it was shattered by the False King.

'Bring the hilt to Narmeleth. She has been preparing for the final assault and is awaiting your return.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'Narmeleth is awaiting you.''The hilt of Dúnachar! I trust it was not too difficult to find?

'Gather companions and speak to me again when you are ready to assail Gador Gúlaran. Time is wasting, and our road will be long and dangerous.''Are you ready to leave? Good... there is no more time to waste, and we have a long road before us.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.</rgb>'Narmeleth's death pains me, though it may seem strange to say such a thing after all the evil she once wrought. The fall of Mordirith is a hope beyond hope, and the destruction of Narchuil and Mordrambor will be a boon to our efforts in Angmar.

'Bring news of the fall of Mordirith to Rivendell, for it will ease the counsels of the many there who must still take thought for the north.''Have you brought your tidings to Glorfindel in Rivendell? He will wish to know of all that has passed since you were last in that place.''Ai! Mordirith has fallen! These are tidings indeed, though woven with tragedy, as are all things in these days of strife. Narmeleth was a valiant Elf, strong beyond the measure of the wise.

'Take word to Master Elrond. He should hear these words from one who witnessed the event!''Take word of Mordirith's defeat to Master Elrond in Rivendell, ${PLAYER}.''You will find Elrond in the library of the Last Homely House, ${PLAYER}.''The words of Glorfindel have shown their wisdom, by Narmeleth's hand or by none, though doubtless you played a great role in Mordirith's downfall as well, ${PLAYER}.

'Do not burden yourself with the oppression of grief. With Narmeleth's noble sacrifice, she has redeemed herself and earned a place among the greatest of our kind in the Undying West.

'Our foe in the north has finally been defeated. I deem that such an end has been put to him that he will trouble Middle-earth no longer; Eärnur can finally go to his long sleep.

'It seems that Laerdan has one last part to play in all of these events. While Failloth, one of the caretakers, was cleaning Laerdan's chambers, a parcel was found addressed to you, ${PLAYER}. It would seem that he left it for you before he left for Eregion.

'I have asked that the parcel remain in Failloth's keeping until your return to Imladris. Now that you are come, you should seek her and claim Laerdan's legacy.''Failloth, the caretaker, should be in the courtyard of my house. Seek her when you have a moment, ${PLAYER}.''You are ${PLAYER}, are you not?'Gufi is confident that the dwarves will be able to reclaim Moria quickly. He is eager to scout out potential mine-sites.The railway tunnel is directly west of Gufi's camp, and can be reached by following the track directly there.

Gufi has asked you to scout the tunnel into which the rails proceed.Scout dead-end passages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scout intact passages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Signposts can be found in the rail-tunnels of the Silvertine Lodes near the dead ends.

You should hang signs where the rails lead to dead ends.Post signs at the dead ends (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gufi is at the central encampment in the Silvertine Lodes.

You should return to Gufi with the results of your survey.Return to Gufi'Ah, greetings to you, good ${RACE}! I am Gufi, at your service. It is a great day to be a dwarf, I tell you, and I am privileged to see the retaking of Khazad-dûm in person!

'As we arrived here, I noticed the railway directly to the west. I sense that there are untapped mining prospects there, for the lodes of the Silvertine are the richest in veins in all of Moria, and likely in all of Middle-earth.

'Would you be so good as to scout prospective paths in the tunnels, and hang signs at any clear dead-ends so that we know where to start our search?''Dread, you say? Bah! A dwarf does not fear a little dreariness in a mine-shaft! According to you, that is the best and only road, and so that is where we will begin! I thank you for your report, ${PLAYER}, however nonsensical its delivery!''There is no point proceeding until we have had a chance to scout out our best prospects.'Stíling pointed out an ancient dead-fall in the mines, constructed by the Dwarves of Moria long ago, and suggested that it might be used to the advantage of the dwarves.The hidden passage is just near Stíling in the hall near Gamil Filik.

You should enter the hidden passage to sneak behind the goblin camp.Use the hidden passage near StílingThe dead-fall trap lies near the goblin-camp at Gamil Filik, south-east of the Deep Descent camp.

Stíling has asked you to find the dead-fall trap and arm it, then lure Pukhlor to his death beneath the rocks.Arm the trap and lure Pukhlor into itStíling is at his spot outside of Gamil Filik.

You should return to Stíling and let him know of Pukhlor's defeat.Return to Stíling (you may use the hidden passage)Thettmárr is in the Deep Descent camp, north of Gamil Filik.

You should return to Thettmárr and tell him of what you saw in the goblin-camp.Talk to Thettmárr at the Deep Descent'I explored this secret passage while you were distracting the goblins inside Gamil Filik, and I am quite pleased to report that it is safe. It brings us to a tunnel right near Pukhlor, who looks to be a terrifying foe, the likes of whom I had not anticipated.

'But there is good news: I thought I espied a loose bit of rock that would make a good trap for Pukhlor's downfall. If you sneak behind through this hidden passage, I think you will be able to get through and crush that villain by luring him to the trap.''So our goblin neighbours will likely not trouble us in the future? That is excellent news, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for helping Stíling at Gamil Filik.''So Pukhlor lies in a grave of stone. Hopefully that will remind the goblins to whom Khazad-dûm truly belongs.

'I do not care what evil lords support them, the very bones of Khazad-dûm stand against them.'The sinister dragonets of the Silvertine Lodes have picked off several dwarves running supplies between the dwarf-camps in the Silvertine Lodes and Water-works.Diseased dragonets can be found in the Old Silvertine City in the southern Silvertine Lodes.

You should slay many of the diseased dragonets.Kill dragonets in the Old Silvertine City (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Öndótt stands at the top of the stairwell in the Old Silvertine City.

You should return to Öndótt.Inform Öndótt that the dragonet population has been lessened'I have noticed some very evil-looking dragonets during my travels throughout the Silvertine Lodes, but with no sense of where their hive could be until I came here. I believe they have made their home in this old city here.

'If you slay them at their own hive, I believe we will be cutting off the entire population of the menaces throughout the entirety of the Silvertines. Will you help, ${PLAYER}?''I am deeply indebted to you! This will make a great difference, I think, for dwarves all over the Silvertine Lodes. You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.

'Has anyone ever told you how incredibly useful you seem to be?''I cannot abide those foul, disease-ridden dragonets in this ancient city!'Thettmár has asked you to find Stíling, who has gone off to scout the eastern roadways.Stíling is scouting the outskirts of Gamil Filik in the Silvertine Lodes, south and then slightly east of the Deep Descent.

You should speak with Stíling and offer your services against the goblin threat.Find Stíling at Gamil Filik'If you are looking for tasks, we have plenty of them, ${PLAYER}. The most pressing issue is probably that of our closest neighbours....

'Stíling, one of our miners, has sent back reports of a great goblin settlement too near here, unfortunately. The name of the place is Gamil Filik, and you can find Stíling there making an assessment of the threat.

'Head south from the Deep Descent and then take the east path at the cross-roads, and you should find Stíling there.''Stíling can be found near the goblin encampment of Gamil Filik, south and east of here.''Well met, good ${RACE}. As you see, I have discovered some very unfriendly neighbours to the Deep Descent....'The final exploration of the Silvertine Lodes involves following Öndótt to the old abandoned city in the southern Silvertine Lodes.Sori mentioned a hidden door along the southern passages of the Silvertine Lodes that would help you follow the dwarf Öndótt.

You should search the southern tunnel for the hidden door to the ancient dwarf-city.Find the hidden door in the southern passagesÖndótt can be found in the ancient and abandoned dwarf-city of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should find and speak with Öndótt.Find Öndótt in the ancient city of the Silvertine'I think we have done enough here to establish that mithril is not likely to be found in this part of the Silvertine Lodes. I may pack up and return to the Deep Descent, or Menem-berej. I have not yet decided.

'If you wish to continue your exploration, however, you should search for Öndótt. I hear he was making his way to the old dwarf-city that was rumoured to be in the south of the Silvertine Lodes. The only way to reach it was by a hidden door in a passage near here. Make your way to Öndótt, if you will, and then I believe you will have seen all there is to see in these parts.''I am afraid I cannot be more helpful. You must explore and seek the hidden door yourself!''Oh! Hello there, traveller. I did not expect anyone to come along with me, but my curiosity to behold this place could not be contained! Marvellous and surprising, is it not? The civilization in the Silvertine was once very great, I think. I should like to explore here!'Thalfar has set up a camp near the centre of the Silvertine Lodes and will likely need help with the mining endeavours there.Thalfar is at the central mining-camp of the Silvertine Lodes, south from the Deep Descent camp.

You should speak with Thalfar at his mining-camp.Talk to Thalfar at his mining-camp'A band of miners from the Deep Descent has pushed forth into the Silvertine Lodes to establish a small mining-camp in the centre of this area.

'You should seek Thalfar along the path towards Menem-berej and give him my regards! He will likely need your help getting things started.''Hail, traveller! Are you here to help us get our feet wet? Good! We can always use another pair of hands.'You found a dwarf from the Silvertine Lodes held prisoner in a goblin-camp.Flík is in the goblin-camp where you found him.

You should escort Flík to safety.Inform Flík that you are ready to goStyrr is in the Deep Descent camp.

You should return at once to Styrr and inform him that Flík has been found and rescued.Inform Styrr that Flík has been rescued'Hurry up and get me out of here! I wish I had never wanted to come out here. All I wanted to do was make my father proud, and now I am about to become goblin-stew! Stop dawdling and let us go!''I hate this place... get me back to the Deep Descent!''So you found Flík? And he was well? Not too badly hurt? That is very relieving news.

'Thank you! I am in your debt. Both the captain's son and my beard are safe, at least for another night.'Gufi believes that you are exaggerating the dangers you encountered during your scouting mission, and has asked you to scout a prospective mining site from Balin's time.A grim silence pervades the mine, interrupted only by the alien sounds of the Gredbyg. Discover what you can of Balin's mining expedition.Recover artifacts from Balin's expedition (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found the picks of Balin's miners, and naught else but danger.Since the dwarf-expedition entered Moria, there have been far too many encounters with goblins.Gathrok and his goblins are in Gamil Filik, south-east of the Deep Descent.

Stíling has asked you to defeat Gathrok, a goblin-chieftain, and weaken his forces.Defeat GathrokDefeat goblins in Gamil Filik (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Stíling is hiding just at the outskirts of Gamil Filik in the Silvertine Lodes.

You should return to Stíling and tell him that you were able to defeat Gathrok.Talk to Stíling'Well, ${PLAYER}, we have been lucky so far in that the goblins infesting Khazad-dûm seem to be terribly disorganized, with inept leaders.

'Nevertheless, we cannot relax our guard. If I read things rightly, there is one particular leader among the nearby goblin-tribe who has been bold enough to organize a raid against the Deep Descent, and I think it would be best if he doesn't live long enough to carry out his ploy.

'See if you cannot perhaps weaken the goblin-forces in Gamil Filik, and deal with their chieftain while you are at it.''So, Gathrok has fallen. That should set the goblins back again in their efforts to organize against us.''I think it would be best for all of us if the goblin Gathrok did not live too much longer....'Thalfar wants the lamps of the deep mine to be lit, which should help to drive away the enemies who have settled there and make the mining expedition safer for the dwarves.The lamps can be found on the long winding descent into the pit at the centre of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should descend the path and light the lamps as you go.Light lamps along the winding path (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thalfar can be found at the small mining camp near Menem-berej in the Silvertine Lodes.

You should return to Thalfar and tell him that the lamps are lit once more.Talk to Thalfar'There are many lamps set along the winding mining path that descends into the Silvertine Lodes, but it has been many years since they have been lit.

'Will you patrol the long descent and light the lamps as you go? The fires should help to drive away the enemies that have settled here, and help the dwarves to see as they work and explore.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. The lights will be a great boon to our efforts in the Silvertine Lodes!''The lights along the pit's path will be very helpful to the mining expedition.'Flík went out to deliver supplies to the Rotting Cellar and has not returned.Flík is probably in a camp not far from the road leading through the Silvertine Lodes.

The dwarf Flík has gone missing from the expedition, and you have been asked to find him, for he is the son of an important dwarf. If Flík cannot be found, Styrr will be in a great deal of trouble for allowing harm to come to him.Find Flík'This will be my head for sure. I was not supposed to send Flík out with any tasks, but he kept begging me.

'His father is leading one of the eastern parties of the expedition; if he knew I let his son go out there and he never came back, they would probably throw me down one of these fissures here!

'I will never be heard from again -- unless, of course, you could find him. You would be saving my beard if you managed it!''Who are you? Are you a friend? Did Styrr send you to find me? I hope so! I begged for this task, and now all I want is to be back safe in camp.''Have you found Flík yet?'The mineshaft near Sori is utterly infested with glow-worms, the innards of which can be used to make torches of a sort.Collect luminous goop (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sori can be found in the southern passage of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should return to Sori with the luminous goop you collected from the many glow-worms.Bring the luminous goop to Sori'Well, as you can see, the shaft just near me is utterly infested with those vile glow-worms. 

'Perhaps you can do me a good deed and smash the ugly crawlers, and while you are at it, collect some of the luminescent goop that gives them their eerie glow. I believe I can fashion some of that goo into a torch of sorts, which will light the way for me in this accursed dark.''Ah, lovely! Well...perhaps not lovely, but you know what I mean. I can smear this goop on anything, and it will provide a light for me as I wander in the dark. You have probably saved me from many a false step, ${PLAYER}!''Collect the luminous goo from those terrible glow-worms, if you would. I believe the vile stuff will be most useful to me.'Sori just received a notification that a miner by the name of Nykr has gone missing in the Silvertine Lodes, and many dwarves have begun to search for him.Nykr could be anywhere, but it is up to you and Sori to search in the southern tunnels, while the dwarves of other camps search near their own sites.

You should search for Nykr in the southern passages of the Silvertine Lodes.Search for NykrSori is on the platform in the southern tunnels of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should return to Sori with the news that Nykr has been found -- dead.Return to Sori with news of Nykr's death'I am glad you're back, ${PLAYER}! I have just received a message from Thettmárr at the Deep Descent: it would seem that Nykr, a miner from Menem-berej, has gone missing, and all of the dwarves of this area are now looking for him.

'Will you help, ${PLAYER}? He could easily have passed right under our noses in the dark. I know Nykr well -- what could he have been doing off by himself? The mines are not safe....''Nykr dead! That is a tragedy beyond bearing. Why, that fool; what could he have been about?

'I will send notice to the other camps to call off their search. Poor, foolish Nykr!''Why would Nykr just up and leave in such a strange manner? Something strange is afoot.'The dwarves of the Silvertine Lodes mining expedition have a universal hunger for the discovery of mithril, or true-silver in the common tongue.Ore veins can be found in the vicinity of the Deep Descent camp, and down into the passage reaching towards the Silvertine mines.

You should mine small ore veins in search for traces of mithril.Harvest ore-samples near the Deep Descent camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Styrr is at the Deep Descent camp in the Silvertine Lodes.

You should bring the ore you collected to Styrr in the Deep Descent.'You may wonder why we have come to this vast deep, ${PLAYER}, and scattered to the wind as we did.

'The Silvertine Lodes are famous for being the first and primary source of true-silver, or mithril as it is called by many. A large branch of miners have gathered for an expedition to search the Silvertine from head to toe, starting at the toes in its roots here.

'We have not had much chance to mine yet, as we are beset by dangers and missing dwarves and other mishaps. Would you care to do the honours of mining ore in the vicinity of the Deep Descent?''Ah, have you found any ore nodes yet? It would really gladden our hearts and give us a sense of purpose if you could show that mithril awaits us!''Ah! You're back, wonderful! Let me take a look at what you've collected.'

Styrr carefully examines each piece of ore closely by holding them up to his squinting eye, and rolling them gently in his fingers.

'No mithril yet. Just ordinary iron here, I believe. This is disappointing, but I am not surprised... nor shall I give up hope! There are many places yet to explore in the Silvertine Lodes!'The dwarves of the Silvertine Lodes mining expedition have a universal hunger for the discovery of mithril, or true-silver in the common tongue.Ore deposits can be found in the glow-worm infested mine-shaft near Sori.

You should collect ore from the deposits so that Sori may assess the likelihood of mithril being found in this area.Harvest ore from deposits in the mine-shaft (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sori is on a platform in the southern tunnels of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should return to Sori with the ore you collected.'The real reason I have come to this forsaken tunnel is to search for mithril along these dark, forgotten paths. Up where the glow-worms infest the mine-shaft, I believe there will be plenty of ore deposits to harvest. Will you bring me a sampling of what you collect?''Any sign of mithril yet?''Hello again, ${PLAYER}! Let us take a look, eh?'

Sori gently inspects each piece of ore you brought him, as carefully as Styrr did before him.

'Hm. No mithril that way. But perhaps in another spot nearby.'The dwarves of the Silvertine Lodes mining expedition have a universal hunger for the discovery of mithril, or true-silver in the common tongue.Ore-deposits can be found in the tunnel near Sori, and in the south-heading passage of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should search nearby for deposits of ore, and bring samples back to Sori for inspection.Harvest ore from deposits in the southern tunnel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sori is in the southern tunnel of the Silvertine Lodes, perched on a wooden platform.

You should bring the ore you gathered to Sori so that he may inspect it for mithril.'The mine-shaft may be fairly empty of good prospects, but perhaps the very tunnel around us may provide a better yield. Will you search the surrounding area once more, and again I will look at your harvest for signs of mithril.

'My heart yearns to see just the slenderest vein! The hope such a discovery would kindle in my folk is beyond description, ${PLAYER}.''How is your collection coming along? I would love to have a look when you've gathered enough of a sampling.'Sori again scrutinizes all of the ore you collected from the surrounding tunnels.

'Nothing. Alas! I will have to search more on my own, but my hopes are rather low right now. Regardless, you have my gratitude, ${PLAYER}. I am certain you did your best! Perhaps there is no true-silver left to uncover....'You have mined for traces of mithril in every corner of the Silvertine Lodes but this one, so you had better give it one last try.Ore deposits can be found along the rock-walls of the Old Silvertine City in the southern Silvertine Lodes.

You should collect ore from the mineral deposits along the walls.Harvest ore from mineral deposits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Öndótt is at the top of the stair in the Old Silvertine City.

You should bring the samples you gathered to Öndótt.'We have searched for mithril all over the Silvertine Lodes by mining mineral deposits, and found not a trace.

'I noticed some deposits along the walls here. I am sure they will come up dry as well, so I dare not get my hopes up. But, we had best finish what you started and take a look, don't you think?

'Bring me the ore-samples you collect, and I will look it over.''I have little hope, but we had best try one last time.''Well, let's have that ore. I will take a look.'

Öndótt looks at each piece of ore with a scrutinizing stare. Suddenly he jumps as if startled by a ghost.

'What -- I cannot believe it. ${PLAYER}... you have found mithril. It is a tiny trace, very small, but... by Durin's Beard, you have found it! And naturally the old city sits on a source. You must send word to the rest of the expedition, my friend! We will settle ere long!'Thalfar has asked you to patrol the huge mining platform of Menem-berej to the south.

He needs it cleared of creatures so that the miners can safely prospect for Mithril.Menem-berej is just south of the central miners' camp in the Silvertine Lodes.

You should clear the platform and its surrounding area of any dangerous creatures.Defeat enemies or creatures at Menem-berej (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thalfar is in the central mining camp the Silvertine Lodes.

You should return to Thalfar and inform him that the platform has been cleared, for now.Return to Thalfar'Forgive me for placing yet another burden upon you, but the miners have complained that the platform of Menem-berej is frequently overrun by goblins or other creatures, and they need it patrolled more frequently to keep such threats at bay while they prospect for Mithril.

'I won't have my miners picked off by goblin filth! I need you to go patrol that platform and clear it of creatures to ensure the miner's safety.''Thank you for your efforts ${PLAYER}. We're terribly short-handed here, given the threat of the goblins all around us.

'Whether or not those miners ever find anything, I rest easier knowing that they are safe.''Clear off that platform, if you would. I cannot have my miners getting hurt on Menem-berej.'The dwarf-mirrors of Khazad-dûm once illuminated the underground halls, but many of them have since fallen into disrepair or were knocked out of alignment.Thettmárr is in the Deep Descent.

You should tell Thettmárr of your continuing efforts towards making Khazad-dûm safe once more.Talk to Thettmárr at the Deep DescentSwivelling this mirror back into place should restore a little light to Khazad-dûm. Once finished, you should seek out the dwarf Thettmárr at the Deep Descent.'You are making Khazad-dûm just a little more habitable every day, ${PLAYER}. These mirrors will once again light our ancient home.'You solved the first riddle, which led to a plaque marked with a snake. Further within the room thus marked is a plaque inscribed with a riddle in Falgeirr's hand.Solve Twisttongue's riddle by choosing the correct chest:

At night, I come without being fetched.
By day, though lost, I am not gone.
All know me, but only the ocean heeds my call.Öndótt can be found in the Old Silvertine City in the Silvertine Lodes.

You should tell Öndótt that you solved an ancient riddle and uncovered a key.This plaque is inscribed with a riddle in Falgeirr's strange language.

At night, I come without being fetched.
By day, though lost, I am not gone.
All know me, but only the ocean heeds my call.'You are a riddle-master as well as a doughty ${CLASS}, eh, ${PLAYER}? That is most impressive! Let us see what you found here... a key?

'Interesting! I should hang onto this, if I were you. It might come in handy if you find any more of Twisttongue's riddling in Moria.'Sori, an explorer from the Deep Descent, apparently passed through the Menem-berej camp on his way south.Sori travelled south from Menem-berej, and should be found somewhere in the tunnel leading south through the Silvertine Lodes.

You should find Sori and offer him your assistance.Find Sori in the southern tunnels'You have helped us out a fair amount here at Menem-berej, ${PLAYER}. While you were exploring, an explorer named Sori passed through on his way south, and he asked for the assistance of anyone I could spare. I told him I would apply to you upon your return.

'Will you seek out Sori as you head southwards?''Ah, you must be the famous ${PLAYER} of whom I have heard so much praise spoken. They are singing of your valour from Hollin to the roots of the Silvertine! Stay a moment, and I am sure we can do some good work here.''Sori said he was heading south through the Silvertine Lodes.'Öndótt noticed a strange light coming from a far end of the Old Silvertine City, and wants you to find its source.The strange light came from the far end of the Old Silvertine City from where Öndótt stands.

You should find the source of the strange light.Öndótt is at the top of the stair in the Old Silvertine City.

You should return to Öndótt with the crystals you gathered.'I notice a strange light of many colours coming from the far end of this ancient city's edge, ${PLAYER}. What could it be? Will you go and take a look? I worry there is some goblin camp-fire perched near us, and the goblins are ready to spring!''What do you have there, ${PLAYER}? Ah! Were these fair crystals the source of the light I saw, and not a goblin-fire? That is wonderful! We can harvest those crystals for lamps in these desolate parts.'Now that you have done all you can for the dwarves in the Silvertine Lodes, Öndótt wants you to tell Thettmárr and the dwarves of the Deep Descent that mithril has been discovered at last.Öndótt's goat is beside Öndótt himself in the Old Silvertine City.

You should use the goat to return to the Deep Descent with haste and speak with Thettmárr.Use Öndótt's goat to travel north and speak with Thettmárr'You have done all that I could have hoped for here, ${PLAYER}, and now I must endeavour to send you to the Deep Descent camp and tell them the wonderful news: that mithril has been found at last!

'Do not tarry; in fact, you should take my goat! I will stay here and defend the work you did to make the Old Silvertine City safe for my folk. I am sure Thettmárr will wish to set up camp here straight away!''Quickly now! Take this goat, and make haste!''Mithril! What? You... you found a tiny vein of mithril in the Old Silvertine City? I cannot believe it, truly I cannot. That is wonderful news, ${PLAYER}! We will have to send reinforcements there. What a discovery, upon my beard!'Many crystals can be found within Moria, but this one seems different than the others. Darkened by time and appearing burned out, perhaps there is something to be learned from this crystal fallen from a Moria Orc.Falgir is at the Deep Descent.

You should bring the crystal you found to a dwarf who might know of such things.This crystal, discovered on one of Moria's Orc-kin, appears to be different than any other crystals found within Moria. You should bring it to someone who may know something about its origin.

Perhaps you could speak with Falgir at the Deep Descent. He may have some knowledge regarding a crystal of this sort.'A worthy find indeed. Though I am unclear of where this came from, I know from stories that there were many such crystals stored in a treasury that we are intent on finding.

'But... this could not be such a treasure as the vault is long forgotten and well hid. It is unlikely that Orcs could have found the entrance. Yet, what if they have?

'Suddenly, I fear that this discovery is more dire than I had thought, ${PLAYER}.'Thalfar would like to restore the gears of Menem-berej, a platform in the Silvertine Lodes that has been ransacked by the goblins.The gear-wheels are on the platform of Menem-berej in the centre of the Silvertine Lodes.

Thalfar asked you to repair the gears on the platform of Menem-berej.Repair gears on Menem-berej (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thalfar is at the camp at the centre of the Silvertine Lodes, overlooking Menem-berej.

You should return to Thalfar.Return to Thalfar'Our best hope of finding mithril in the Silvertine Lodes is to reclaim and repair the platform of Menem-berej, if you ask me.

'If you could begin by restoring the wheels on the platform, that would be most helpful, ${PLAYER}!''Ah, well done, my friend! We will have Menem-berej back in working order in no time.''The gears of old ought to be repaired before we can truly begin our mining expedition in this area.'Despite the dread you felt, Gufi wishes for you to explore an old mining site set upon by Balin's expedition.Gufi is at the Menem-berej encampment in the centre of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should speak with Gufi to travel to the prospective mining site.Talk to Gufi to travel to the mine-siteGufi is at the Menem-berej encampment in the centre of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should speak with Gufi about the survey-expedition.Talk to Gufi at Menem-berej'According to our maps and Balin's own records, there is a mining site along the tunnel where you began to fret for your safety.

'You should try to overcome your worry and see what you can find there of Balin's expedition. My hope is that there is great potential in that mine for our own dwarves!

'Do let me know what you find, ${PLAYER}. I am counting on you!''Very well then! You will see; we will be finding veins of mithril and clusters of gems in no time!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'By axe and sword, ${PLAYER}! You have my deepest apologies. I did not realize how bad things really were down here. We will need an entire garrison to clear these mines properly.'Thettmárr has asked you to check on the progress of the dwarf-expedition at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, in Durin's Way. Once there, you should speak with Líkmund.To reach the Chamber of the Cross-roads, head north from the Deep Descent to the Dolven-view camp. From the Dolven-view, follow your map and the main lit roadway towards the Chamber of the Cross-roads.Speak with Líkmund'You have done more than we could ever have hoped in the Silvertine Lodes, so it is time to send you back to the upper levels to help out in Durin's Way. You should make for the Chamber of the Cross-roads, which lies to the north of the Great Delving.

'Give my greetings to Líkmund when you get there, if he's still breathing.''Líkmund is with the expedition at the Chamber of the Cross-roads in Durin's Way. You should speak with him as soon as possible.''Thettmárr sent you to check up on us, did he? More like he sent you to check up on ME.

'I still owe him a hefty gambling debt from our last outing together, and I'm betting he wants to make sure I live long enough to make good on it.

'Well, we could use the extra hands anyway, so you're welcome to stay if you have a pair of them to lend to our efforts!'There is much work to be done for the Longbeards to reclaim their ancient home of Moria.The Deep Descent is along the south path from the Dolven-view, at the north edge of the Silvertine Lodes.

You should take the path south to discover the dwarf-hub at the Deep Descent.Talk to Thettmárr at the Deep Descent'Interested in taking a look at the true Mines of Moria now, are you? I can't blame you, for tales speak of their wonder and beauty!

'What I wouldn't give to have gone with the dwarves who went to the Silvertine Lodes... but I have a job here, and I mean to do it!

'Take the south path from the Dolven-view and you will find yourself at the Deep Descent in no time -- it is really quite close. You might be able to help the dwarves there quite as much as you helped us!''You should speak with Thettmárr at the Deep Descent encampment as soon as you feel ready to take your leave.''Welcome to the Deep Descent, ${PLAYER}! We miners have great hopes for the Silvertine Lodes.

'Are you here to look for ways to be of use? Never fret... there is more to be done here than we can handle!'Menacing deep-claws seem to have built a nest in the Old Silvertine City.The nest of deep-claws can be found in the Old Silvertine City in the southern Silvertine Lodes.

You should defeat deep-claws and clean up the nest area.Defeat deep-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy filthy nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Öndótt can be found at the top of the stair in the Old Silvertine City.

You should return to Öndótt and tell him that you have done as he asked.Talk to Öndótt'It would appear that we have another problematic inhabitant of this city. Deep-claws have made themselves quite the little nest here, and as long as they remain, the Old Silvertine City will be hopelessly polluted. They have uneven tempers, those beasts, and they weaken the foundations of Moria.

'You ought to go clear out that wretched nest, when you have spare time.''You got rid of those pesky deep-claws? Good, I am glad to hear it!''Go clear out that deep-claw nest when you get a chance, eh, ${PLAYER}?'A parcel has been found addressed to you in Laerdan's old room.You should read Laerdan's note before opening the parcel he left for you.

You spoke to Failloth in Rivendell and learned that Laerdan had left a note and a parcel behind for you in his room.Read Laerdan's noteFailloth is in the courtyard of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.

You have read Laerdan's note and should speak now to Failloth.'While performing the sombre task of cleaning Laerdan's chambers once and for all, I uncovered a note from Laerdan made out to you, ${PLAYER}, along with a parcel that he left behind. Master Elrond bade me hold these items in my keeping in hopes that you would return.''You should read the note from Laerdan I have given you, ${PLAYER}.''My heart goes out to Laerdan, ${PLAYER}; his was a sad story. I know, as does he, that you did everything for him that you could.

'This parcel is yours, as he wished it to be.'A parcel has been found addressed to you in Laerdan's old room.You should read Laerdan's note before opening the parcel he left for you.

You spoke to Failloth in Rivendell and learned that Laerdan had left a note and a parcel behind for you in his room.Read Laerdan's noteFailloth is in the courtyard of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.

You have read Laerdan's note and should speak now to Failloth.'While performing the sombre task of cleaning Laerdan's chambers once and for all, I uncovered a note from Laerdan made out to you, ${PLAYER}, along with a parcel that he left behind. Master Elrond bade me hold these items in my keeping in hopes that you would return.''You should read the note from Laerdan I have given you, ${PLAYER}.''My heart goes out to Laerdan, ${PLAYER}; his was a sad story. I know, as does he, that you did everything for him that you could.

'This parcel is yours, as he wished it to be.'One of Líkmund's dwarves has discovered a large band of goblins in the Hall of the High Stair in Durin's Way.The Hall of the High Stair can be found to the north of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Rink has asked you to defeat any goblin inhabitants in the Hall of the High Stair.Defeat goblins in the Hall of the High Stair (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rink is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, south of The Hall of the High Stair.

You have managed to overcome several of the goblins in combat, and Rink awaits word of your deed.Talk to Rink at the Chamber of the Cross-roads'The goblins are among the most ancient and bitter rivals of Durin's folk, and yet again they prove to be an obstacle in our path.

'The chamber to the north has become inhabited by goblins. If we ever hope to reclaim Durin's Way for those who made it great, then we must drive our old foe away. Find the Hall of the High Stair and confront any goblins you may find.''Durin's folk must regain control of Durin's Way! It is an utter insult to have these goblins defiling our halls and chambers.''You have dealt a blow to the goblins laying hold to the Hall, and this is a welcome first step in taking back the High Stair.

'We must continue to be vigilant against the goblins, for they will not easily retreat. I am most thankful for your help, you have given me great hope.'The creatures in Tharâkh Bazân keep tampering with the mirror there.Oxi is at Jazârgund, east of Tharâkh Bazân in Durin's Way.

Oxi will be pleased to hear the mirror has been re-aligned and is useful once more.Talk to Oxi at JazârgundThe mirror in Tharâkh Bazân has been rendered useless once more. It seems that the creatures there insist on moving it out of position.'So the mirror once again reflects light through the halls? That news lifts my spirits.'Búkk hopes to find a type of medicinal root, which he remembers from his youth. He suspects that the plant may be found near the pools of water in Tharâkh Bazân.Tharâkh Bazân can be found to the west of Búkk's camp in Durin's Way.

Búkk has asked you to look for a specific plant root which only grows near sources of fresh water. He believes it may be found among the streams of Tharâkh Bazân.Collect healthy mud-roots in Tharâkh Bazân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Búkk can be found at the small encampment at the eastern edge of Tharâkh Bazân.

You have collected several roots near water sources that seem to match Búkk's description of mud-roots. He awaits your return at the small encampment in Tharâkh Bazân.Return to Búkk with the healthy roots'When I was merely a lad, my grandfather taught me about a certain plant that had nourishing properties. He called this plant mud-root, as it only grew near the edges of fresh water. By boiling the roots of this plant, he could extract the oils within and create a brew that was hearty enough to rouse a sleeping dragon! Well, that is what he claimed. I doubt he ever saw a dragon. Nevertheless, the brew was strong and could be put to use in helping our sick and wounded recover more quickly.

'I have not seen such a plant in some time, but I am hopeful that it may be growing here in Tharâkh Bazân, as there are many pools and streams of fresh water to be found. If you come across any healthy roots growing near the water, please return them to me so that I may examine them.''These are exactly what I had hoped for, ${PLAYER}! Yes these are the mud-roots I remember from my youth. I had all but given up hope that I would see them again. You are well deserving of my praise.

'I will wait for you to take your leave before beginning the boiling process, the smell is quite horrible, and it often attracts the deep claws.... I wish you luck on your travels.'Goblins have burned the outpost that once stood at Gloku-ru, and now threaten to build their own fortifications in the same location.The goblin camp at Gloku-ru is south and slightly west of the entrance to Zirakzigil and the Door to the Clouds.

Kalman has asked you to defeat goblins that burned the encampment that once stood at Gloku-ru.Defeat goblins at Gloku-ru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tharâkh Bazân is north and east of Gloku-ru.

You have been asked to report to Gerwith at Tharâkh Bazân with your success at Gloku-ru.Talk to Gerwith at Tharâkh Bazân'Not all endeavours have gone well for us in Moria. One early settlement in Durin's Way was an outpost built by Gerwith, at Gloku-ru to the south. The encampment became overrun by goblins and was burned entirely, while only Gerwith and a few others managed to escape.

'The goblins threaten to fortify Gloku-ru and remain a persistent danger to us if we do not act against them. Head there and defeat as many of them as you can. Then report to Gerwith in Tharâkh Bazân, to the east, when it is done.''Gloku-ru is to the south, beyond Durin's crossroad, and slightly west. When you are finished, you can find Gerwith at Tharâkh Bazân to the east.''It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. I am glad to hear that the goblins have paid for what transpired at Gloku-ru. When I think back to that day, I can still feel the heat of the fire all around me....

'Well, your deeds have given me hope. Perhaps one day I will build a new outpost at Gloku-ru, and I will make it known that it was only possible thanks to your bravery.'The dwarves at Jazârgund are concerned about the presence of White Hand Uruks this deep into Moria.White Hand taskmasters can be found in Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm, east of Jazârgund.

Borgar fears the White Hand Uruks are wresting control of the Orcs and goblins of Moria. He wants to thin their ranks.Defeat White Hand Taskmasters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Borgar is at Jazârgund, west of Hadâd-dûm and Fehem-dûm.

Borgar will be pleased to know that the White Hand Uruks' numbers have been greatly reduced.Talk to Borgar at Jazârgund'I have heard reports of White Hand Uruks all over the Great Delving, but did not believe any had pressed this deep. I have seen them, taking hold of the halls to the west, and I fear what their purpose might be. I suspected their plan would be to enlist some of the goblin tribes to supplement their forces, but now I fear something more sinister.

'The ones I am particularly concerned with are the White Hand taskmasters. They seem to carry considerable influence among the Orcs of Khazad-dûm. I would ask you to defeat as many of them as you can... perhaps it will dishearten the others.''If the White Hand takes over Khazad-dûm, or allies with the forces here, then we will be but the first casualties of this war.''So most of their number has fallen... that is good. I dare say they will have a difficult time at recruiting any goblins without them.

'Until the White Hand has been driven from the halls, I will not be satisifed... but you have done your part, ${PLAYER}.'The merrevail use several perches as nests. Gúri believes that if they were destroyed, the colony would be crippled.The morroval-camp is located at Skoiruzg, far to the east of the Fanged Pit camp.

Gúri asked you to destroy the morroval-perches and defeat several morroval-slingers.Destroy nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat slingers in Skoiruzg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gúri is at the Fanged Pit camp, far to the west of Skoiruzg.

Gúri will be pleased to hear that the morroval-perches have been destroyed and the approach to the camp is free from the attacks of the slingers.Talk to Gúri at the Fanged Pit camp'Merrevail above ground take to the skies at night. In Khazad-dûm, however, they nest and sleep in several perches high above the caves, as though they were queer birds. If those perches were to fall, they would be forced to the ground, where we might meet them with our steel.

'The greatest collection of perches is in the furthest camp to the east, Skoiruzg. While you are assaulting their nests, take care of any slingers you come across. When we attack, we need to make sure we can get in close, and their ability to fight at range could pose problems.

'Hurry, ${PLAYER}. Much depends upon your success.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. Now the merrevail will be forced to the ground, where we are on even footing, and with fewer slingers, we can bring our axes to bear upon them without fear of darts. Now they have become the prey!

'Ha! I wonder what their queen will think of her slingers now that they've failed to protect their nesting areas! 

'Yes, their queen. It seems that they are ruled by one they call She-Who-Must-Be-Obeyed.''We must force the merrevail to the ground and ensure our approach will be unfettered.'Uruk-hai and Men of Dunland hold the School of Tham Mírdain, and there is little that we can do. I have heard that there are small forces making their way into the Library of Tham Mírdain to deal with the threat out of the north. I hope to do the same against the foes we face from the south.

The School at Tham Mírdain was once a place of learning where ideas were exchanged freely, and the Elves would discuss important matters and knowledge. It lays in ruins now, but the forces of White Hand think that there may still be something within those walls worth taking.

I would ask that any who wish to assist us enter the School at Tham Mírdain and purge the White Hand presence from within that forsaken place. You will find the entrance south-east of our station here.The School at Tham Mírdain is located to the south-east of Echad Mirobel.

Lefnuichen, an elf at Echad Mirobel, asked that you drive the White Hand out by force, for the uruks and Dunlendings have taken over the School that rightfully belongs to the Elves.Defeat White Hand archers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat White Hand leaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Dunlendings in the School at Tham Mírdain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gerwith needs the natural cave crystals that grow in Tharâkh Bazân to replace many of the light sources that have been destroyed across Moria.Crystals may be found in Tharâkh Bazân, west of Jazârgund in Durin's Way.

Gerwith has asked you to search for natural crystals in Tharâkh Bazân in order to replace ones that have been destroyed.Harvest naturally growing crystals from Tharâkh Bazân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gerwith is at the encampment on the eastern edge of Tharâkh Bazân.

Gerwith awaits your return with the glowing crystals that may be used as sources of light.Return the crystals to Gerwith in Tharâkh Bazân'The beauty of the gardens never ceases to amaze me. Many of the crystals that grow naturally here in Tharâkh Bazân  are used throughout Khazad-dûm as a source of light.

'In some locations, the merrevail have been destroying the crystals we have placed, in order to extinguish any visible light. Many of our corridors and halls have become darker than the blackest night.

'We must collect more crystals to replace the ones that have been destroyed. Search Tharâkh Bazân for naturally formed crystals, and I will make sure they are put to good use.''You have brought me quite the assortment of crystals, great work! We will use them to bring some of the warmth and beauty of these gardens into the dark corners where no other light can pierce.'Gelirwen informed me that a great leader -- nay, a champion -- of the Dunlending entered the School at Tham Mírdain to assist the Uruk-hai and Dunlending forces in their ransacking efforts. This leader of the Dunlendings will serve this purpose all too well if he is not stopped.

I would ask that you make your way south-east of Echad Mirobel, and break into the School at Tham Mírdain; there you should defeat Llygad the Blade. With their leader overthrown, perhaps we can rouse fear in the hearts of the Men of Dunland.

You may wish to bring friends with you, ${PLAYER}. This will be a dangerous venture, for there are many warriors within the school that stand between you and your quarry.Llygad the Blade leads the forces of Dunland from within the School at Tham Mírdain, the entrance of which is south-east of Echad Mirobel.

Faellion wishes for you to defeat the champion to dismay the Dunlending forces from their warmongering intentions.Kill Llygad the BladeBósi has established his command centre at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, a guard room once used for watching three passages that lead deeper into Moria.Gredbyg can be found throughout the Great Delving, to the south and west of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Bósi has asked you to eliminate the fierce gredbyg within the Great Delving. These insects are a threat to the safety of the dwarves.Defeat gredbyg within the Great Delving (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

You have defeated many of the gredbyg in the Great Delving, helping to make the area more safe for Bósi's dwarves.'We have established a presence within Moria, ${PLAYER}, and will stage further excursions into the depths from this room, the Chamber of the Cross-roads. This once served as a guard room for watching the three passages just to the south, but has been empty for many long years.

'Many creatures have thrived in the darkness during the long absence of the dwarves, especially the gredbyg, fierce and loathsome insects spawned from the deep.

'Seek out all varieties of gredbyg in the Western Levels, to the south and west of this chamber, and eliminate them. This will be the first small step in reclaiming the Great Delving for my people. There is much to be done before true progress is to be made.''Gredbyg can be found throughout the Great Delving and must be dealt with. Travel south and west of this chamber into the Great Delving, and eliminate any gredbyg that you find skittering along the way.''Good work! You are ever a friend at need, and I am at your service. You continue to impress me with your inextinguishable fervour towards our cause!'With a foothold established in the Twenty-first Hall, the Iron Garrison has begun the reclamation of the forgotten stock-houses, libraries, and mines of Moria. The lumber warehouse of Bult-kâr is one such location.The entrance to Bult-kâr lies within Mezer-serej.

Burkni has asked you to defeat the leader of the intruders within Bult-kâr.Defeat leader of the intruders within Bult-kârBurkni is at Mezer-serej.

With the defeat of their leader, the intruders within Bult-kâr have had their morale weakened. You should return to Burkni and tell him of your victory.Talk to Burkni at Mezer-serej'Greetings. I am Burkni of the Iron Garrision, tasked with the reclamation of Bult-kâr. Within, there lies a vast store of lumber which we could readily use to begin repairs across Khazad-dûm.

'Unfortunately, we cannot claim this store-house until the intruders within have been dealt with. Perhaps with your aid, we could strike terror into these intruders and drive them out.

'I am certain that these intruders have a leader, someone -- or something -- that holds sway over them. Quickly, enter Bult-kâr and dispatch the foe who commands the rest of those within.'

<rgb=#FF0000>The Iron Garrison has created a diversion, drawing the bulk of the intruders from the depths of Bult-kâr. They are permitting you access for one hour, during which time you may enter and exit Bult-kâr freely to complete the tasks bestown upon you.

However, after the hour has passed, the Iron Garrison can no longer guarantee your safety and thus will bar access until they can once again muster an offence to draw the enemy from Bult-kâr.</rgb>'What of your task? Do not waste any time... slay the one who leads the intruders within Bult-kâr!''Well done, well done.

'With the defeat of their leader, we have already observed disarray among the remaining intruders. The Iron Garrison should have no trouble reclaiming this store-house.'The Iron Garrison is striving to reclaim the long forgotten store-houses of Moria. Tasked by his superiors, Burkni is attempting the drive the intruders out of Bult-kâr. With his previous attempts to do so being unsuccessful, Burkni has turned to other adventurers within Moria to aid him in his task.The entrance to Bult-kâr lies within Mezer-serej.

Burkni has asked you to assist him in clearing Bult-kâr of the intruders within.Defeat intruders in Bult-kâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burkni can be found at Mezer-serej in the eastern halls of Zelem-melek.

You should return to Burkni to receive a reward for your efforts.Talk to Burkni at Mezer-serej'Hello, friend. We of the Iron Garrison have begun the work of reclaiming Moria from the foul creatures that now reside here.

'My task is to retake the warehouse Bult-kâr from the creatures that reside within. Alas, their great numbers makes it difficult to claim this store-house on my own. Perhaps you can help me with this task.''Have you completed your task yet? Please do so, then return to me when you have finished.''I never realized how numerous the intruders within Bult-kâr were! It is good to know that they were not too much for you to dispatch.

'Your efforts have helped greatly in furthering the goals of the Iron Garrision... and for that, you deserve a reward.'Weapons are not the only implement with a lineage. The Dwarves of Moria know that every job has the right tool and it is because of that they bent so much effort upon crafting the finest hand-axes. The intruders within Bult-kâr stand to ruin or steal these fine axes.The entrance to Bult-kâr lies within Mezer-serej.

Burkni is investigating rumours of implements of high lineage within the store-house of Bult-kâr. To that end, he has tasked you with entering the store-house and gathering dwarf hand-axes for him to study.'We of the Iron Garrision are not just simple guards or miners. We are, to an extent, scholars of our professions.

'We know of weapons and armour that bear great lineages. Our records show that there may even be other tools and implements that bear a high lineage as well.

'Reading these records, I am most interested in learning of these implements. I do not know if such things exist within Bult-kâr, but I would be interested in studying any tools you may find.''So your search has borne fruit has it? Thank you for this. The promise of finding a hand-axe of great lineage makes your efforts worthwhile!'Bósi has asked you to seek out three store-houses within the Great Delving of Moria and attempt to recover any surviving records or histories.The Chamber of Knowledge, the Chamber of Wisdom, and the Chamber of Deep Thought can all be found somewhere within the Great Delving of Moria.

Bósi has asked you to search three ancient store-houses of the Great Delving for pages, tablets, or tomes that will enlighten him about Old Days.Find and search the Chamber of KnowledgeFind and search the Chamber of WisdomFind and search the Chamber of Deep ThoughtBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving of Moria.

You have collected ancient records of Moria from three store-houses in the Great Delving and should bring them to Bósi.'The gredbyg were a dreadful hazard, and despite your efforts they will undoubtedly return in time, but we cannot spend overlong dealing with this minor threat. To wholly wipe them out would involve resources beyond what I can provide. We must turn now to other matters, and defend ourselves from the returning gredbyg wherever we must.

'What I truly desire above all else is a chance to look at records and histories from the Old Days. Who knows what secrets lie untold beneath the dust: pages, tablets, and tomes to be found throughout the caverns of Moria?

'There should be store-houses located within the Great Delving of Moria, and they are thus named: the Chamber of Knowledge, the Chamber of Wisdom, and the Chamber of Deep Thought. Find these store-houses within the Great Delving and search them all for records of the Old Days. Return to me when you have found something from each area.''The three store-houses of which I speak are called the Chamber of Knowledge, the Chamber of Wisdom, and the Chamber of Deep Thought. Look for them somewhere in the Great Delving of Moria, and bring me records or histories from each.''Excellent, ${PLAYER}! These records and histories are very old, and probably harbour many ancient secrets. They are sure to be tremendously valuable!'

Bósi examines each of the records in turn, and his face falls somewhat as he reads.

'Records of goods bought and sold, inventories of iron and other metals... these are of some interest, to be sure, but....'

Bósi trails off, and then brightens.

'Wait a moment, ${PLAYER}. You might have something here after all.'Bósi has discovered mention of a mighty axe made of mithril in one of the records you found and seeks to learn whether it might still be found.Bori is in a small room off the eastern side of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Bósi has given you back the dusty pages which hold clues to the location of Zigilburk, hoping that your delivery may raise his son's spirits.Katûb-zahar, the Word-hoard of Durin, is somewhere on the eastern side of the Great Delving, north of a large statue of Durin.

Bori told you that if you can find the place called Katûb-zahar, he may be able to discover the location of the mysterious mithril axe, Zigilburk.Find evidence of Katûb-zaharBori is in the Chamber of Command; it is the room up the eastern stairs in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern end of Durin's Way. It can be reached from the Great Delving.

You have located a plaque that marks the location of Katûb-zahar and should return to Bori with the news.'These pages mention something curious indeed, ${PLAYER}: an axe made entirely of mithril, light enough to be wielded one-handed but strong enough to fell any foe or rend any armour with a single sweep! Zigilburk, it was called, and it appears to have been forged in Durin's time by one called Ongli. Hm. I have not heard that name before. How can it be that one so skilled would not be remembered in legend?

'There is more to be learned on these pages. Could it be that Zigilburk might yet be found?

'My son Bori has been wracked by grief ever since Bróin was slain before the Doors of Durin. Bring him these pages and tell him of Zigilburk. It will do him well to have other thoughts upon which to brood. Go up the stairs on the eastern side of the chamber and through the door into the Chamber of Command; my son Bori is there, and Brogur also.''Go up the stairs on the eastern side of this chamber and through the door there. My son Bori is in the Chamber of Command with Brogur.''Alas that Bróin is not here, ${PLAYER}. This is just the sort of adventure he would have relished. Still, I may be able to help you, though my heart will not be in it.

'It seems that the dwarf who sought to forge Zigilburk relished his privacy, and by the grace of Durin he was given a secret forge at which to work. These pages do not reveal the location of the forge, but they do mention a trick of some sort that would open the door. The nature of this trick is lost, but these pages indicate that it was recorded at Katûb-zahar, the Word-hoard of Durin.

'Katûb-zahar was once supposed to be on the eastern side of the Great Delving, somewhere north of a great statue of Durin. I am sorry, but there is little else with which to guide you. Find the location and return to me, and perhaps I can unravel some more of the mystery.''Katûb-zahar, the Word-hoard of Durin, was somewhere on the eastern side of the Great Delving, north of a statue of Durin. Those are not the most helpful of directions, I know; there are many statues of Durin in Moria.''Katûb-zahar was somewhere on the eastern side of the Great Delving, north of a statue of Durin.

'Find some evidence of this place, the Word-hoard of Durin, and return it to me. Recovering the mithril axe mentioned in those pages, if it was ever in fact made, would be a tremendous feat!''You found the location of Katûb-zahar, the Word-hoard of Durin? I am deeply impressed. It is a shame that your report tells of a great infestation of deep-claws and cave-claws; I hope the beasts have not ruined too many of the records and histories kept in that place.

'It seems that Ongli, the great craftsman who may have forged Zigilburk, was very protective of his privacy. Durin granted him a secret forge at which to work: Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire. The way to Nâr-khelab was locked by means of some trick known only to a trusted few.

'These pages do not mention the location of Nâr-khelab, but they do say that the trick to opening the way was kept in Katûb-zahar. Now that you have found the Word-hoard of Durin, you can search for this trick.'Bori has told you of Nâr-khelab, the great forge at which the mithril axe, Zigilburk, may have been made. The way to the forge is blocked by some secret trick, lost to time.Katûb-zahar, the Word-hoard of Durin, is on the eastern side of the Great Delving, north of a large statue of Durin.

Bori has asked you to return to Katûb-zahar to search for some sign of the trick to opening the door to Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire.Defeat deep-claws or cave-claws in the Great Delving (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search Katûb-zahar for the secret to opening Nâr-khelabBori is in the Chamber of Command, the room up the eastern stairs in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

You have uncovered some pages that reveal information about Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire.'If we can find both the location of the Heart of Fire and the secret to opening its doors, it could be that Zigilburk will return to us from the darkness.

'I will ask the other dwarves of our expedition if they have come across any sign of Nâr-khelab. Perhaps someone has encountered some clue, though I am not hopeful.

'You must return to Katûb-zahar, the Word-hoard of Durin, and search for the secret to opening the door. The deep-claws you found will not make it easy, but you are strong enough to deal with them. Katûb-zahar is on the eastern side of the Great Delving, north of a large statue of Durin. Somewhere inside, among the deep-claw nests, you may find the secret to opening the Heart of Fire.''Return to Katûb-zahar on the eastern side of the Great Delving, north of a large statue of Durin, and search it for some sign of the secret that will open the way to the Heart of Fire.

'If we can find both the location of that ancient forge and the secret to opening its doors, it could be that Zigilburk will return to us from out of the darkness.''This looks very promising indeed, ${PLAYER}. Let me see what I can learn from these pages.

'Many of the words are faded, and the parchment is rotten.... Curse the deep-claws and cave-claws that nest now in Katûb-zahar!

'Use of this secret to opening the door seems to be... punishable by death... or imprisonment. Blacksmith Ongli could approve entry, as could Durin, of course.... I cannot make out the next line, but...ah, here we go.

'The door will be hidden until... the following steps are taken.... This word must be "Ongli," which means that he must be hailed as a master blacksmith, or congratulated for his fine works, or...saluted, I think. And then these words are to be spoken: "Bâb kanon zuhûk!"

'This is it, ${PLAYER}!'You have uncovered the secret to opening the door to Nâr-khelab, the forge where Zigilburk was made, but still do not know the location of the door.Brogur is in the Chamber of Command, up the eastern stairs within the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Bori has asked you to consult with his uncle Brogur about the Heart of Fire.'We now have the secret to opening the doors to the Heart of Fire, but not the location of the doors themselves! This is a frustrating turn.

'Speak to my uncle Brogur about this, if you would. He is busy, as usual, organizing our efforts here within Moria, but he may have some idea that has eluded our consideration.

'Brogur is wise and has a great store of knowledge in that old head of his. I would be very happy to have him giving thought to this adventure as well, for his input is certain to be valuable.''My uncle Brogur may be able to help us find the Heart of Fire. What use is the key when you can't find the door?''My nephew has told me of this wild goose chase, ${PLAYER}. How can we be certain that Nâr-khelab, this Heart of Fire, ever existed at all? We would have heard tales of such a forge, surely. And Zigilburk: an axe made entirely of mithril? Ludicrous. This would surely have been featured in many of our tales before now, as all dwarves would sing its praise until the end of time.

'You would have better luck catching a wild Redhorn Goat than you would finding this ridiculous forge. This "secret" to opening the door that you have recovered is nothing more than a mad dwarf's mutterings.'Based on what we know of the White Hand's movements in this area, I have discerned that there is an intelligent uruk-hai at the head of the enemy forces here in Eregion.

He is currently commanding the effort to scour the ruins of the School at Tham Mírdain to the south-east of Echad Mirobel. He is a fearsome warrior by all accounts, and his name is Commander Târsh. I would have you enter the School at Tham Mírdain and face down this clever uruk-hai.

It is said that his ego is large, and that he fancies himself a warrior without equal. Perhaps we can use this against him. Take no more than two others into the School, for we do not want to attract the attention of our northern enemies as well. We have our hands full enough with our more aggressive manoeuvres against those foes, and it would be grievous indeed if they were to join forces.Commander Târsh can be found in the School of Tham Mírdain, south-east of the Elf-refuge of Echad Mirobel. 

Commander Târsh, a pride-filled uruk-hai, leads the forces of the White Hand in an attempt to gain information of old from the School in which he has established his host. Gelirwen wishes you to enter the School and face down this brute with the aid of a small fellowship.Defeat Commander Târsh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hamall noticed several decaying columns in the caves around the Orc and goblin-camps. If they were to be damaged, the cave should come crashing down atop the enemy forces.The decaying columns can be found in the Orc-camps at Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm, east of Jazârgund.

Hamall noticed several decaying columns within the nearby Orc-camps. He assures you if they are damaged enough, everything will come crashing down and destroy the camps.Damage the decayed columns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hamall is at Jazârgund, west of Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm.

Hamall should know that none of the columns collapsed, and the cavern did not collapse.Talk to Hamall at Jazârgund'I just narrowly escaped from the Orcs to the east. They had me captive for an entire week, but I kept my eyes open and saw many useful things. It is time for you to make what I saw work to our benefit, ${PLAYER}.

'The camps are built within our ancient halls, but the Orcs have been careless. There are several columns that with a little work look like they would fail and bring the entire cavern crashing down upon the Orcs.

'The decaying columns are east of here, in the Orc-camps at Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm. All you should need to do to bring the cavern down upon the Orcs is pick away at the stone... then run!''Damage the columns, drop the rocks on the Orcs and goblins, and then we will attack!''The columns did not collapse? But surely, they must have. Did you push hard enough? Did you try striking them with hard steel?

'I suppose there was naught you could do... our stone-work is among the finest.

'Now I simply do not know what to do. It will not be long until the Orcs come again, and then I suspect they will not be interested in taking prisoners.'Oxi believes that your efforts have greatly improved matters in Durin's Way, since your arrival. He believes that victory is assured for the dwarves at Jazârgund, but that other locations  in Moria may need your assistance.Simbi is on duty in the Twenty-first Hall, south of Jazârgund. 

Simbi has sent a message to Oxi, asking to speak with you in the Twenty-first Hall.Speak to Simbi in the Twenty-first Hall'Your resolve has helped us to turn the tide, ${PLAYER}! When you first arrived, we were besieged by foes on all sides, but now... now we are the ones driving back our enemies! I daresay that our victory in reclaiming Durin's Way is all but assured, and you played no small part in that.

'There are other dwarves in Khazad-dûm that are in greater need than we are. Simbi in the Twenty-first hall has asked that we send you to him. Good luck to you my friend. We will not forget your bravery.''${PLAYER}! You are not a moment too late, I have been awaiting your arrival.

'Oxi says that things are going well in Durin's Way, but the same cannot be said for all of Khazad-dûm.'The dwarves at the Chamber of the Crossroads have gotten little sleep since arriving. The goblins nearby have been pounding on drums without respite, sending booming echoes throughout Durin's Way.The goblin-drummers are encamped in the Hall of the High Stair, north of the Chamber of the Crossroads.

Fostólf has asked you to destroy the goblin-drums so that he and his companions can get some sleep.Destroy the drums (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fostólf is at the Chamber of the Crossroads, south of the Hall of the High Stair.

All of the goblin drums have been silenced. Fostólf should be able to get some rest at last.Talk to Fostólf in the Chamber of the Crossroads'Forgive me, ${PLAYER}, for any rudeness. I am not permitted to leave my post here, but those incessant drums are driving me mad! I've not had any decent sleep since we arrived here.

'The band of goblins responsible for that din are encamped just north of here in the Hall of the High Stair. Could you do me a favour and silence those drummers?

'What I would not give to have just one night's peace!''Please destroy those confounded drums. They beat on and on without end...I cannot get a wink of sleep.''Thank you for your help, ${PLAYER}. I am very much looking forward to taking my nap in a while. It may seem like a small thing, but the better rested we are when the battle is joined, the more favourable towards us it will go.'Dwarf-scouts have spotted a handful of White Hand Uruks who have somehow slipped into Moria through unknown passages. They seem to be attempting to sway the goblin-tribes of Durin's Way into an alliance.The White Hand Uruks can be found among the goblins and Orcs inhabiting Durin's Way. One was seen at Ninknakh Faltor, north of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Another was seen at Gloku-ru to the north-east. The last was seen on the road to Jazârgund at Durin's Crossing, to the north and east.

Kalman has asked you to go forth and defeat the emissaries of the White Hand.Defeat the emissary in Ninknakh FaltorDefeat the emissary in Gloku-ruDefeat the emissary at Durin's CrossingKalman is at the Door to the Clouds in Durin's Way.

You should inform Kalman that the White Hand emissaries in Durin's Way have been defeated.Talk to Kalman at the entrance to Zirakzigil'The White Hand Uruks have me concerned, ${PLAYER}. They are attempting to sway the goblins into an alliance with the leaders of the White Hand army. While it is a fine thing for us when goblins fight each other, we cannot allow  them to gain a foothold here within the bounds of Khazad-dûm when they already control considerable forces without!

'I need you to hunt down and defeat the White Hand's emissaries before they are able to convince or intimidate the goblins here into joining him!

'My scouts spotted one in the goblin-camp of Ninknakh Faltor, another in Gloku-ru, and the third was at Durin's Crossing, between here and Jazârgund.''The White Hand must not be allowed to bring the goblins of Moria under its dominion!''So, that's the end of the emissaries of the White Hand... and good riddance. Our only hope against these odds is to keep the goblins disorganized and to encourage them to prey upon each other as much as they prey upon us.

'The last thing we need down here is for some strong leader to emerge and unite them against us!'You have entered Khazad-dûm at last, and the dwarves have begun to establish their camps within its dark passages.Bennt Sharp-eye is in the Dolven-view, far to the east of Durin's Threshold, in the Great Delving. Stíling is in the Deep Descent, among the Silvertine Lodes, south of the Dolven-view.

Tulk has asked you to provide assistance to the dwarves at Durin's Threshold, the Dolven-view, and the Deep Descent.Talk to Bennt Sharp-eye in the Dolven-viewTalk to Thettmárr in the Deep DescentBósi has established a command centre somewhere within Moria and is waiting to speak with you there.

The Dwarves of Moria will be able to guide you to Bósi's new command centre, a guard room with a strategic location somewhere within the mines.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, on Durin's Way'There is so much work to be done, ${PLAYER}, here and elsewhere in the Mines! This has been a great victory for the Iron Garrison, but this is only the beginning of our toils beneath the mountains.

'You must aid our people here at Durin's Threshold, and at our other encampments, if we are to have victory in Khazad-dûm.

'When you have performed some of the tasks here in Durin's Threshold, you should seek for the Dolven-view and for the Deep Descent. Speak to Bennt Sharp-eye at the Dolven-view, to the east of here, and to Thettmárr at the Deep Descent, among the Silvertine Lodes. They will have ways for you to assist the Iron Garrison.''When you have performed some of the tasks here in Durin's Threshold, you should seek for the Dolven-view and for the Deep Descent. Speak to Bennt Sharp-eye at the Dolven-view, to the east of here, and to Stíling at the Deep Descent, among the Silvertine Lodes. They will have ways for you to assist the Iron Garrison.''You should travel to the Dolven-view and the Deep Descent, ${PLAYER}, and continue to help the Iron Garrison. There is so much still to be done!''The Dolven-view and the Deep Descent are both to the east of here, ${PLAYER}. Climb up these steps and keep watch for other guides to show you the way to the other camps.''The road to the Dolven-view, and beyond it the Deep Descent? As you keep heading east, you will pass into a series of very dark caverns, lit only by some curious blue crystals.

'Follow this sloping path as it curves and descends, watching out for the gredbyg, vile insects that inhabit the darkness.

'Another guide of the Iron Garrison should be by a railing in the midst of the dark cavern.''Be cautious on this leg of your journey to the Dolven-view and to the Deep Descent, ${PLAYER}, because it is so dark.

'You want to travel north-east through the darkness, following the sloping paths as they descend to buildings made by the ancient dwarves.''Do you see the large structure to the east there? The camp known as the Dolven-view is built atop that large building. The road to the Deep Descent runs south from the Dolven-view, passing into the Silvertine Lodes.

'Wait! You cannot get atop the Dolven-view from here. Travel north, watching out for great fissures in the road, until you find another guide. He will show you the winding path up to the Dolven-view.''Do you see the paths to the east of here? If you take the southern path upward and follow the winding road at the top, you will come to the Dolven-view. The Deep Descent is among the Silvertine Lodes, south of the Dolven-view.

'Wait! Be careful! There is a great fissure in the road just to the east. You will need to step carefully around it.''This is not the path you want if you are looking to find the Dolven-view, and beyond it the Deep Descent. The path you want is that one, to the south. The winding road at its head will take you to the camp at the Dolven-view.''Welcome to the Dolven-view, ${PLAYER}. As you can see, the Iron Garrison is hard at work making everything ready for our resettlement of the Mines.

'Speak to the people here and help them with their tasks. We must see to our safety before we can push any further into Khazad-dûm.''I am glad you have come to the Deep Descent, ${PLAYER}. A ${CLASS} such as you should be able to help my people with many of the tasks that need doing here among the Silvertine Lodes. We are particularly plagued by the goblins of Gamil Filik!''When you are satisfied with the aid you have provided the dwarves here at the Dolven-view, you should speak to Bósi for more work. You will find him at the Three-fork Camp on Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. He has established a command centre in the Chamber of the Cross-roads.''When you are satisfied with the aid you have provided the dwarves here at the Deep Descent, you should speak to Bósi for more work. You will find him at the Three-fork Camp on Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. He has established a command centre in the Chamber of the Cross-roads.''You are looking for the Chamber of the Cross-roads, ${PLAYER}? You have quite a trek ahead of you, for Bósi's command centre is a good distance from here.

'You will want to look for Iron Garrison Guides like myself as you make your way to the Chamber of the Cross-roads; we will steer you a-right!

'Bósi's command centre is not far along Durin's Way, but Durin's Way is a long way to the east. Start your journey east and north by climbing these steps.''The road to the Chamber of the Cross-roads? As you keep heading east, you will pass into a series of very dark caverns, lit only by some curious blue crystals.

'Follow this sloping path as it curves and descends, watching out for the gredbyg, vile insects that inhabit the darkness.

'Another guide of the Iron Garrison should be by a railing in the midst of the dark cavern.''This may be the most difficult part of your passage to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, ${PLAYER}, because it is so dark.

'You want to travel north-east through the darkness, following the sloping paths as they descend to buildings made by the ancient dwarves.''You are looking for the Chamber of the Cross-roads? Well, you should start out by heading north from here.

'Wait! Hold on a moment! There's a great fissure in the floor just to the north! Be careful as you go -- you can skirt it on the left, but only if you pay attention and see it!''You are looking for the Chamber of the Cross-roads? You want to head east of here to the Palace of Náin. Watch out for the great fissure in the path, and make your way around it on the left!''You are getting nearer to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, ${PLAYER}. Climb this path and pass north through the Palace of Náin. Your road will then bend to the east, where you must be careful to jump across several fissures in the floor.

'After a short time, you will see a mighty bridge on your left; it travels north, through the Dwarf-lords' Gate.

'That is where you must go.''Do you see that reddish-glow to the north-west, ${PLAYER}? You must follow that passage if you are seeking the Chamber of the Cross-roads.''You have nearly come to Bósi's command centre, ${PLAYER}!

'Head east until you see stairs on your left. At the bottom of those stairs you will see another set of stairs on your right. You will then be at Manarbul, and the door to the Chamber of the Cross-roads will be to the north!''The Chamber of the Cross-roads? The entrance is just to the north there!''Welcome, ${PLAYER}, to the Chamber of the Cross-roads! This shall be my command centre for a time as we establish our presence here in Moria. We will busy ourselves with making ready to restore the mines and cities beneath the mountains.

'I will never forget the great deeds you have done on behalf of the Iron Garrison, and I eagerly await tales of your future achievements. I am ever at your service, and may your feet lead you well in the darkness of Khazad-dûm and beyond.'The merrevail have captured several fungus-infected Orcs and are keeping them in cages. The dwarves are worried the merrevail might discover how to turn the fungus into a weapon.The morroval-camp is at Tith-maudhûl, east of the Fanged Pit camp.

Bési asked you to free the infected Orcs from their cages and defeat any merrevail in the camp who might also be infected.Open cages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Morroval-slayers at Tith-maudhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bési is at the Fanged Pit camp west of Tith-maudhûl.

Bési will be pleased to know that you freed the infected Orcs from the cages and killed any merrevail that have been infected.Talk to Bési at the Fanged Pit camp'Orcs infested with fungus is bad enough news for us, but infected Orcs captured by merrevail is even worse. These creatures are canny, and I worry what they may be up to. If they can learn how to turn this fungus into a weapon, it will be many more centuries before dwarves rule these depths again.

'There is a camp, Tith-maudhûl, where I believe they have these Orcs locked up in cages. While the thought sickens me, free the Orcs from their prisons and defeat any merrevail in the area who might also be infected.

'I do not wish to think of the danger this situation poses to us all.''The camp has been destroyed? That is good news. We no longer have to fear the fungus being used against us by the merrevail.

'Another of my scouts mentioned overhearing one of the merrevail mention that their leader -- I don't know her name, but they called her She-Who-Must-Be-Obeyed -- had the idea of capturing Globsnaga goblins. Whoever she is, she's maliciously clever.''Hurry! Every moment we delay is a moment the merrevail have to make use of that fungus!'The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of barbed claws.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Barbed Claws

The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of barbed claws.Wanted: Barbed ClawsThis collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of charming sword sheaths.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Charming Sword Sheaths

The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of charming sword sheaths.Wanted: Charming Sword SheathsThis collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of creepy filth.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Creepy Filth

