You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Polished Scales

The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of polished scales.Wanted: Polished ScalesThis collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of polished sword sheaths.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Polished Sword Sheaths

The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of polished sword sheaths.Wanted: Polished Sword SheathsThis collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of spotted skins.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Spotted Skins

The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of spotted skins.Wanted: Spotted SkinsThis collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.Helgi Goblinbane's statue would not be complete without an arm to grip a great axe.The statue's arm is at Sulnul-dûm, east of Tharâkh Bazân.

You should collect the arm of Helgi Goblinbane's statue.Find the statue's armArnod is at Tharâkh Bazân, west of Sulnul-dûm.

Arnod will be delighted to hear you found the statue-piece.Talk to Arnod at Tharâkh BazânHelgi Goblinbane's statue would not be complete without an arm to grip a great axe.

The goblins of Durin's Way destroyed the statue, and its parts can be found scattered throughout Moria. A dwarf named Uxi endeavours to reassemble this statue.'Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. It would have been a pity if this piece had remained in the hands of the Enemy.

'I will send this over to Uxi right away, for his devotion to the statue of Helgi Goblinbane is legendary already.'You found a piece of armour. When you picked it up, bats attacked you.Sigdan is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, north of the Dolven-view.

Rambi told you to speak to his friend Sigdan about the armour you found.Talk to Sigdan at the Chamber of the Cross-roadsRambi is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads in Durin's Way.

Sigdan has given his evaluation of the scratches in the armour you found.Talk to Rambi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads'The armour you found is a beautiful piece of craftsmanship, ${PLAYER}. What interests me particularly are these gouges in it: look here, and here. I believe this was carried in a creature's claws.

'Attacked by bats? Well, I suppose... but why would a bat carry a piece of armour about? This is most peculiar.

'When inspecting finely crafted armour, there is one dwarf who I would count on beyond all others: Sigdan. Talk to him here in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, he may have some insight into this strange find.''Sigdan will likely know more about that armour. You can find him here in the Chamber of the Cross-roads.''Yes, I am Sigdan. Your servant, brave ${CLASS}. Why have you sought me out?'

Sigdan looks carefully at the claw marks in the armour.

'These scratches are too deep to have been caused by even the largest of bats. It would have taken something much stronger to have pierced armour this well made. That is really all I can say.''Sigdan doesn't think this was done by a bat, and neither do I. The bats fit into this in some way, but I have yet to figure out how.'Borgar has gotten word that more dwarves are being readied to support the encampment at Jazârgund.The cauldrons are to the east in Jundul-dûm.

Borgar has asked you to light several cauldrons along the road leading east from Jazârgund.Light the cauldrons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Borgar is at Jazârgund, west of Jundul-dûm.

Borgar will be pleased to hear that the reinforcements he requested will now be able to find their way.'Thank goodness you are here, ${PLAYER}. We are pressed to the limit. The Orcs here are being led by a vicious group of White Hand Uruks, whose knowledge and abilities have pressed us into a fight we cannot win with our current garrison.

'I sent word several days ago for help, but I am afraid they will not know the safest path to our camp. Here is a flint and some twigs. Light the cauldrons along the road to the east.

'When you have finished, return here to me.''Make sure all of those cauldrons are lit. I do not want our reinforcements getting lost in the dark.''I can see the light from the cauldrons myself. Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. Hopefully the reinforcements will arrive soon.

'In the meantime, there is plenty left for us to do while we are waiting.'Oxi has asked you to give aid to a group of dwarves attempting to hinder the merrevail in the Fanged Pit, on the eastern side of Durin's Way.Oxi's sack of provisions lies on the ground beside him, in Jazârgund.

Oxi has asked that you bring a sack of important provisions to the dwarf-outpost in the Fanged Pit.Collect the sack of provisions near Oxi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Folkath awaits the supplies at the camp in the Fanged Pit, at the end of the path east out of Jazârgund.

Oxi has asked you to take the important provisions he has collected to Folkath in the Fanged Pit.Talk to Folkath in the Fanged Pit'There are more threats in Moria than we originally guessed, my good ${RACE}. We have had your aid in dealing with the Uruk-hai and goblins here in Durin's Way, but an entirely new menace threatens to spread from the east; the merrevail, an ancient ally of Morgoth.

'A large tribe of merrevail have taken residence in the Fanged Pit. Folkath and some others have taken camp there in order to deal with this threat, but they are in sore need of supplies. I have prepared this sack of goods, take the provisions to Folkath if you are ready to help in his task.''Welcome, traveller. It is good to make your acquaintance, ${PLAYER}.

'Ah, I see you have brought supplies from Oxi! I was deeply worried that we might be cut off from Jazârgund, but appears you made it here safely. Many thanks to you.'Stirred by the tales of the dwarves' lost battle, Arnod wishes now to honour the memory of the fallen dwarves.There are three locations in Tharâkh Bazân, where Arnod wishes you to tell the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of the battles: a northern statue, a southern fountain, and a central statue.

Arnod wants you to honour the fallen dwarves of Moria by telling the story of the ancient lost battle at the monuments the dwarves built in Tharâkh Bazân.Arnod is at the eastern end of Tharâkh Bazân.

Arnod will want to know that you honoured the ancients by telling the story of their defeat.Talk to Arnod at Tharâkh Bazân'I want to restore the glory I believe we have lost in denying our history. It is time to tell the tales of past battles in Khazad-dûm. Not to my fellow dwarves, for they will not appreciate them; to truly honour those who have fallen, we must tell our tale to those figures of lore. Of course, this is not truly possible, but we may still honour their memory in another way.

'Go into the gardens and stand before the statues that rest at the centre, and to the north, and before the southern fountain. There, recount the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of the great battle.

'Those who fell died in battle and in honour. They should forever be remembered for their valour.''I feel we have done well today, ${PLAYER}. Our forebears would be proud. We have honoured them as we should have done long ago.''Go to Tharâkh Bazân and tell the story of the forgotten battle.'The dwarves at the Chamber of the Cross-roads need help establishing their presence there.Fostólf, Rink, and Gansi are in the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Líkmund suggested that you speak with Fostólf, Rink, and Gansi and learn what tasks they might have for you.Help FostólfHelp GansiHelp RinkLíkmund is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

You should return to Líkmund and tell him of your efforts on behalf of Fostólf, Rink, and Gansi.Talk to Líkmund at the Chamber of the Cross-roads'Welcome to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, ${PLAYER}. We are fairly busy here, as you can no doubt see, and could certainly use your help. Our encampment is a vital link in the supply-chain between Durin's Threshold and the Twenty-first Hall, far to the east. It is also nearly impossible for anything to get past us here without us spotting them, so it's very important that we not fail to hold this chamber against anything the goblins and Orcs can throw at us!

'If you are of a mind to help us out, you should speak with Fostólf, Rink, and Gansi over there... they have some rather important matters that need attending to, or so they tell me.

'I am sure I can find something for you to do, as well.''Help out Fostólf, Rink, and Gansi. No sense in wandering off into the darkness without some purpose... you will just be fresh meat in the goblin's next stew!''Thank you for helping us out, ${PLAYER}. Now that we are settled in this chamber, we can see to some other pressing matters!'The White Hand Uruk leader has established his camp in Durin's Way and is aligning the banners of several goblin and Orc-tribes under his rule.Zâhof can be found at Fehem-dûm, east from Jazârgund.

Zâhof is the leader of the White Hand Uruks in Moria. If he falls, Saruman's plans for the deeps fall with him.Defeat ZâhofZâhofs throne is in Fehem-dûm, east from Jazârgund.

Ión wishes to stir up strife between the Orcs of Moria and Mordor. He gave you a banner to plant upon the throne of the fallen White Hand Uruk.Ión is at Jazârgund, west from Fehem-dûm.

Ión will be pleased to hear Zâhof is dead and the Mordor-banner has been planted on his throne.Talk to Ión at Jazârgund'The White Hand Uruks here had one purpose: to take command of the Orcs and goblins of Khazad-dûm and turn them against the forces of Mordor. Why they were ordered to do that, I do not know, but their intentions are clear to me now. Now it is time to tip the balance. Before they have a chance to overwhelm us, I want to force them against each other.

'There is a powerful White Hand Uruk leader, Zâhof -- one who has united many of the goblin-tribes between here and the gate -- who now stands over Durin's Way, claiming it as his own. The time for his fall has come, and for Mordor to be given the responsibility for his demise.

'My scouts report that Zâhof reigns in Fehem-dûm. Find him, defeat him, and place this banner of Mordor upon his throne.''Zâhof has outlived his welcome in Khazad-dûm. It is time for him to fall... and for Mordor to take the blame.''Hurry up and place that banner on Zâhof's throne! Those loyal to him must believe that Mordor committed this act!''So Zâhof has finally fallen. With his fall, the rest of the White Hand's forces have begun fleeing from Khazad-dûm. With pressure from both the forces of Mordor and from Durin's Folk, they believe it is not a cause worth fighting for.

'This is a great victory for us indeed, but do not relax your vigilance yet. We have but lit a small flame... now begins the work of turning it into a raging fire.'The dwarves escorting a cart of supplies from Durin's Threshold were ambushed just west of Manarbul. The cart was destroyed, and the supply-crates stolen.The goblin-thieves were last seen fleeing north along the road towards Mudmulzarâk.

Gansi has asked you to recover the stolen supply-crates from the goblins who took them.Collect supply-crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gansi is at the Chamber of the Crossroads, south of Mudmulzarâk.

You have collected the supply crates stolen by the goblins and should bring them at once to Gansi.'Líkmund sent you to help me? Well, that is most fortuitous timing, good ${RACE}. I have just the task for one such as yourself.

'We are running dangerously low on supplies. I was bringing a cart over from Durin's Threshold, but we were ambushed outside Manarbul. We were driven back before reinforcements could arrive, and the goblins made off with our supplies!

'I would be greatly appreciative if you could hunt down those missing crates. It will be a lean week indeed before the next shipment otherwise, and we might even be forced to abandon this camp. The goblins fled north towards Mudmulzarâk.''Please recover those crates, ${PLAYER}. I doubt we will be able to maintain our post without those supplies.''This camp is of great importance to our expedition. From here, we can keep an eye on anything that tries to move between Durin's Way and the Great Delving in the south.

'Without these supplies, we might have been forced to abandon this vital watch-post!'Thálfi is in need of someone to map the Winding Way, the path between the Chamber of the Cross-roads and the Twenty-first Hall.The Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall.

Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.The Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall.

Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.The Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall.

Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.The Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall.

Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.The Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall.

Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.The Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall.

Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.Thálfi is to the west at the the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Thálfi is waiting for you to return with the map you have drawn of the Winding Way.Speak to Thálfi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads'There are few places in the world as large and mystifying as Khazad-dûm. With its wide chasms and twisting paths... it is easy to become disoriented! Because of this, I have been working hard on obtaining detailed maps of each hall and pathway we secure.

'Directly to the east you will find a passage known as the Winding Way. I had a beautiful map, detailing each section of the path, stretching all the way to the Twenty-first Hall... but some of the careless guards here placed their mugs of ale and various other liquids directly on top of it. They have utterly ruined it!

'I need a replacement and it must be accurate. Would you take this parchment and detail a new map for me, ${PLAYER}?''You drew this, ${PLAYER}? Why, this is even better than the original! I appreciate the detail you put in. Have you not considered a career in map-making?

'Whenever I travel the Winding Way, I will think of you. You have my thanks.'While Moria is most well-known as a mine, there is much more to it. It was home to a vast and ambitious culture of dwarves. They were warriors, crafters, and scholars. The knowledge the Dwarves of Moria had amassed is often overlooked when compared to the scale of their structural and prospecting achievements. Seeking to instill a sense of scholarly pursuit within the Iron Garrison, Darri has been dispatched to the library of Mekeb-faham to reclaim it and rediscover the lost lore within.The entrance to Mekeb-faham lies within Hadudbâb.

Darri has instructed you to enter Mekeb-faham and defeat the creature leading the intruders.Defeat the leader of the intruders in Mekeb-fahamDarri is at Hadudbâb.

You should return to Darri with news of your success.Talk to Darri at Hadudbâb'Greetings, traveller. I am Darri of the Iron Garrison. I have been sent here to evaluate the state of the library of Mekeb-faham and recover any lost knowledge that may yet be found there.

'I have had difficulty setting foot within the library, however. Something inside is organizing or influencing the rest. If its leadership is broken, the rest of those within should fall easily afterwards.

'Go. Enter Mekeb-faham and confront whatever passes for a leader inside. I don't care how you do it, short of setting the place ablaze.'

<rgb=#FF0000>The Iron Garrison has created a diversion, drawing the bulk of the intruders from the depths of Mekeb-faham. They are permitting you access for one hour, during which time you may enter and exit Mekeb-faham freely to complete the tasks bestown upon you. 

However, after the hour has passed, the Iron Garrison can no longer guarantee your safety and thus will bar access until they can once again muster an offence to draw the enemy from Mekeb-faham.</rgb>'Mekeb-faham will not reclaim itself! You must topple the leadership of the intruders within. Once you have done that, the rest will fall into disarray.''You have returned with the glow of victory about you. This is good.

'We will certainly have an easier time of it within Mekeb-faham now that the ranks of the Enemy are in disarray.'The Dwarves of Moria were renowned for their industry. Crafters and prospectors of exceptional talent, they would not have been able to maintain such efficiency were it not for the love of lore. Not all things written in Moria pertained to mining and building. Great tales of battle and epic poems were transcribed by the dwarves. Some of these can be found within the walls of Mekeb-faham along the tunnels of Durin's Way.The entrance to Mekeb-faham lies within Hadudbâb.

Darri has asked you to enter Mekeb-faham and collect any dwarf-prose you may find.'The Iron Garrison's chief interest in this place is the recovery of ancient strategem and tactics. Building plans, too, are of interest. But so far in my research, I have seen far too many of these and not enough in the vein of creative offerings. Does that sound queer to you? That there would be interest in prose coming from someone of the Iron Garrison?

'It isn't queer at all. Not all of us hunger for a swift and violent reclamation of Khazad-dûm. Some of us seek to revel in new discoveries and enjoy the art and prose of our long lost brethren.

'Mekeb-faham is a library. Within it, there are many records, but I am most interested in those that pertain to the art of words, not the art of war. If you journey into this library and happen across any prose-work, I would happily reward you in exchange for them.''The Dwarves of Khazad-dûm had an interesting sense of timing. While it is different from what I expected, I am still heartened to see the wealth of artistic writing you have found within Mekeb-faham.

'As I promised, here is your reward. It is not a fine copy of a great dwarf-playwright's works, but it is something you could find useful if you had enough of them.'Not even libraries are safe from the ravages of Orcs and beasts alike. Whether their interest in them be the pursuit of information or just a dry place to nest, the libraries of Moria risk an ugly degradation. Seeking to protect the literature and lineage of Moria, the Iron Garrison has sent a representative to Mekeb-faham to prevent it from falling into the hands of the enemy or becoming a breeding ground for all manner of foul beasts.The entrance to Mekeb-faham lies within Hadudbâb.

Darri has asked you to assist him in clearing Mekeb-faham of the vermin within.Defeat intruders in Mekeb-faham (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Darri can be found at Hadudbâb along the southern road in Durin's Way.

You should return to Darri to receive a reward for your efforts.Talk to Darri at Hadudbâb'Greetings, good adventurer. My name is Darri of the Iron Garrison. I was sent here by the Iron Garrison to safe-guard Mekeb-faham against the intrusion of Orcs and beasts alike. Unfortunately, I have arrived too late and something has already moved in.

'While I am a competent soldier, I have neither the skill nor the training to confront the numbers I fear reside within.

'But you look able enough to aid me in this effort. Were I to offer you a small reward, would you be willing to undertake the task of clearing out the intruders from within Mekeb-faham?''Have you completed your task yet? Please do so, then return to me when you have finished.''You certainly are a handy one to have around when skulls and shells need to be cracked, I will give you that!

'As I promised you, here is your compensation for your efforts. Now don't look at me like I've short-changed you. Given my own competency in combat, I am certain I will have additional opportunities to hire you in the future!'Líkmund has given you a message to bring to Listein at the Door to the Clouds, the entrance to Zirakzigil in Durin's Way.Listein can be found at the Door to the Clouds, the entrance to Zirakzigil in Durin's Way.

Líkmund has asked you to take a message to Listein that may contain information on the location of a lost artifact in Moria.Talk to Listein at the entrance to Zirakzigil'Durin's Way is home to precious few of the artifacts of our ancestors, many of which have been lost or destroyed by the goblins.

'Listein has been searching for these artifacts throughout Durin's Way, in the hopes of preserving the history of our craft. Take this message to him. It reveals the last known location of such an artifact, and I'm sure he will be thankful for it.''A message? I was not expecting any messages, what is this about?'

You deliver the message, and Listein looks it over.

'This artifact was not far from here at all! This is wonderful news, ${PLAYER}. With this information, I may be able to preserve another once lost artifact!''The Door to the Clouds is north and a bit east. It is a small outpost at the onset of the frigid Zirakzigil.'The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of barbed claws.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Barbed Claws

The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of barbed claws.Wanted: Barbed ClawsThis collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of charming sword sheaths.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Charming Sword Sheaths

The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of charming sword sheaths.Wanted: Charming Sword SheathsThis collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of creepy filth.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Creepy Filth

