You should bring the trophies you gathered to a collection box.Wanted: Spotted Skins

The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of spotted skins.Wanted: Spotted SkinsThis collection box is checked daily by the dwarves. Your collection is sure to reach the requesting party.If you are to enter the School at Tham Mírdain, I beseech you to seek out whatever remnants of the great knowledge held within you may find. There may be nothing remaining therein or there may be some scrap of knowledge that seems to be naught, but if there is even the least of scraps, the Enemy must not be allowed to obtain it.

What knowledge might remain in the School would be held within the main hall, where all would come to listen to the discourse presented by the greatest crafters of Eregion.

Seek out this knowledge and bring whatever you find there to me.The School at Tham Mírdain lies to the east, up a small incline from the northern slopes of Echad Mirobel.

Evil threatens to claim the lost knowledge of Eregion, and it falls to you to recover this knowledge before it is truly lost forever. Faellien has asked you to bring any scraps of knowledge you find back to Echad Mirobel.Collect scraps of knowledge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Forces loyal to Saruman have moved up from the south and begun to sift through the ruins of Eregion. News of their arrival reached Echad Mirobel; there, the small force of Elves employ the assistance of any willing to aid them in driving this foe from the Elf-lands.A symbol of the White Hand may be found among the enemies throughout the lands around Echad Mirobel.

Gelirwen wants to preserve the memory of the School at Tham Mírdain and save it from the befouling evil currently residing there. She will not risk lives without first knowing the enemies that are to be faced. She has asked you to obtain a symbol of the White Hand from among the enemies to help her learn about these foes.'At one time, the School at Tham Mírdain was a bastion of the free exchange of knowledge. Students of every art would gather in the courtyard or the great hall and there discuss history, crafts, arts and music. All manner of topics dear to the Elves would be shared among those scholars.

'When war darkened these lands, the knowledge prevailed in other areas of Middle-earth, but many scars of what transpired here remain upon the Elves. Now, the School is a reminder of the brighter days we once shared with our brethren.

'We cannot abide the arrival of the White Hand within its walls, and so we must do something to drive the Enemy out. Here in Mirobel, we have had signs and portents that a great leader drives the forces of the White Hand. I would ask that you search for them throughout Mirobel and search the enemies for a symbol of the White Hand... with that, I may be able to discern the identity and location of their leader.''Yes, this symbol is the one that I sought. I had seen glimpses ere you brought me this piece, but now I can study it closely. We have discerned that it belongs to one named Târsh, a commander of the forces of the White Hand.

'This symbol was the last piece I needed to know what we face. I am grateful to you for your generous deed, ${PLAYER}.'The dwarves at the Door to the Clouds are constantly on guard against the goblins, who vastly outnumber them. A goblin captain and his personal guards have been making things difficult for travellers between the Chamber of the Cross-roads and Zirakzigil.Captain Gomîg and his guards can be found in the northern passages west of the Door to the Clouds.

Hoping to clear the way to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, Siggir has asked you to defeat the captain of the goblins in western Durin's Way.Defeat goblin guards in Durin's Way (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Captain GomîgSiggir is at the Door to the Clouds.

You should return to the Door to the Clouds and inform Siggir that you have defeated Captain Gomîg and his guards.Talk to Siggir at the Door to the Clouds'Collecting supplies and scouting chambers is all well and good, but I've got something a little more dangerous in mind. Goblin-hunting!

'As you have surely noticed, nearly every room and corridor of Khazad-dûm is crawling with them, and those causing us grief here in Durin's Way seem to take orders from a single leader. We have all got to do our part to drive them out, and that includes you!

'Search to the west for the goblin captain, who goes by the name of Gomîg. He and his personal guard have been harassing any who travel unaware between the Chamber of the Cross-roads and our outpost here at the Door to the Clouds.''If you can cull a few of the captain's guards, he might be easier to deal with alone.''You have dealt with quite a few goblins in the last day or so, ${PLAYER}, and more importantly, you have rid us of Captain Gomîg. That should make it easier for us to move between the western part of Durin's Way for some time. 

'Not that they will stop coming after us. It is only a matter of time before a new captain rises, but we can use this opportunity to fortify our position before that happens!'Arnod has studied the ancient texts of Khazad-dûm, and would like you to deliver the tale to others.Búkk waits in Tharâkh Bazân for your return, awaiting any news of the battles from ancient lore.

Arnod has asked you to bring the tales to Búkk, so that he may know the conclusions of the ancient tales.Talk to Búkk in Tharâkh BazânBorgar may be found in Jazârgund, along the path east out of Tharâkh Bazân.

Búkk has asked you to bring the tale of the ancient battle to Borgar in Jazârgund, so that the story may be preserved for future generations.Talk to Borgar at Jazârgund'I have had ample time to study the pages you delivered to me, ${PLAYER}. Understanding these tales is simpler than I had imagined. The author describes the events in great detail and with incredible accuracy. The stories that are told within are tragic, but important to our history.

'You should have the honour of delivering the completed story to Búkk. He must surely wonder what has been found since you and he last spoke. Share with him the knowledge we have uncovered and give him my regards.''I have been eagerly awaiting your return, ${PLAYER}. What news from Arnod?

'Ah, this is outstanding! These pages recount one of the greatest battles of my forefathers in Khazad-dûm... and in such detail!  We have just as much to learn from the victories of old as we do our failure. There is no dishonour in defeat when all have fought bravely.

'These records are not safe here in Tharâkh Bazân. Take this tale to Borgar in Jazârgund, so that they may be preserved for future ages.''What tale is this you bring to me, ${PLAYER}? I know it not.'

Borgar looks carefully over the aged pages.

'Azog... this is a tale most grim. It is a sad moment in our history, but an important one as well. I had thought the pages of this tale were forever lost. I shall be sure to preserve these stories for Búkk, and for all our kin. Many thanks, brave ${CLASS}.'Moria still holds the secrets of the past, including tales of the dwarves' great defeats by the Orcs of Azog.Arnod is camped at Tharâkh Bazân in Durin's Way.

Búkk is interested in tales of the battles that the dwarves lost to the Orcs. He believes Moria still holds these secrets and that Arnod may know where to find them.Talk to Arnod at the gardens of Tharâkh BazânThe pages are located in the chambers to the north and south of Salab Nurjundul, west of Jazârgund.

Arnod believes the old tales are still in Moria.Collect records (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arnod is camped at Tharâkh Bazân, west from Jazârgund.

Arnod wants to help in understanding the history behind the tales you found.'When I was young, my father told me tales of the early days of Khazad-dûm. All of these stories ended abruptly, however, and no matter how many times I would ask, he would never tell me what happened next. I know now that the dark days were not spoken of.

'I fear by not talking about these defeats, about not even attempting to learn from them, we are dishonouring our forebears. I know Khazad-dûm keeps within it the tales of those lost battles.

'I sense that wise old Arnod may know where to look for record of these tales, but I dare not ask him myself. Perhaps you could ask him? Simply feign ignorance on the matter if he becomes angered.''So, you want to know about the battles of old? And not our victories? That sort of talk could get you in a lot of trouble around here, for those things simply are not discussed. But Búkk is a close friend, so I suppose I could help.

'Khazad-dûm, in fact, does still hold record of those days, though the goblins have strewn the pages all over, and what is left may be difficult to interpret without knowing more about the history of those days. Head east of here, into Salab Nurjundul, and explore the halls to the north and south. Return any pages you may find to me, so that I may help us to understand their meaning.''You may find the pages you seek at Salab Nurjundul, ${PLAYER}.''Speak with Arnod, over there. He should know where to find what I seek. Oh, and if you could, don't mention that I asked you to do this.''So, the great halls still hold record of the battles. I knew they did, and now I want to read them even more.''You found them, and the pages are all here! The complete tale of one of the great defeats of the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm, a priceless find!

'Allow me to study these pages a bit more before revealing their discovery to Búkk.'The spirits of the dwarves at Jazârgund have fallen very low, and many think that some cheerful songs would help improve their morale.The dwarf-bard's sheet music has been spread throughout the Orc-camps in Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm.

With the failure of his plan, Hamall wishes to raise the spirits of his fellow dwarves in Jazârgund. He believes collecting the songs of old lost by the maddened bard will help achieve this goal.Collect dwarf sheet-music (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hamall is at Jazârgund, west of Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm.

Hamall's spirits will be greatly raised by the ancient dwarf-songs you recovered.'If only the bard had not left. One night, he just seemed to lose his senses, started yelling into the darkness and went screaming from camp, throwing his music everywhere. I think the future would look much brighter, even down here, if we could just sing the songs of old once more.

'Perhaps if you could find the bard's music, we could use it to bolster the spirits of the dwarves here at Jazârgund... a light in the shadow, so to speak.

'The sheets of music will likely be spread throughout the Orc-camps at Fehem-dûm and Hadâd-dûm. It would be a dangerous venture... are you prepared for such a challenge?''I long for the songs of old. If only the bard had not fled into the dark.''The songs of old! You found them all. I thought when the bard fled, we had lost everything.

'How you managed to find these, I do not know, but we are deeply in your debt. This will do much to restore the morale here.'Something is stirring the bats up, causing concern for the dwarves in Moria.Kalman can be found at the small outpost found at the entrance to Zirakzigil in Durin's Way.Talk to Kalman at the Door to the CloudsThe entrance to the bats' cave lies south and east of Durin's Crossing.

Kalman has asked you to hunt down the bats that have infested Durin's Way.Find the bat-caveThe entrance to the bats' cave lies south and east of the entrance to Zirakzigil.

Kalman has asked you to hunt down the bats that have infested Durin's Way.Defeat bats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat morvul bat-handlers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kalman is at the outpost near the entrance to Zirakzigil in Durin's Way, north and west of the bats' cave.

You should return to Kalman with tidings of your success.Talk to Kalman at the entrance to Zirakzigil'Something has been stirring up the bats since we arrived. At first, I thought it was those goblins, but I spotted something else the other day... it looked a bit like one of those merrevail, but different in some way.

'I say we find out what it was and deal with those bats while we are about it! There is a small outpost north of here, the Door to the Clouds, near the entrance to Zirakzigil. Go there and speak with Kalman to find out what they know of the bats.''The entrance to Zirakzigil is some distance to the north and a bit east. When you feel the air become much cooler, you will know that you are near.''Rambi sent you to find out about the increase in bat activity? Yes, we have noticed this as well.

'The bats seem to dwell in a cave a bit south and east of here. I am unsure of what has roused them, but I would imagine that it might be found within that cave. Hunt as many of those winged menaces as you can, while you are there.''There's a cavern entrance that is rumoured to be swarming with bats. When you reach Durin's Crossing head south, then east at the first passage and you will be well on your way.''Welcome back. Was the hunting good? You saw a few of those creatures that have been stirring up the bats, have you? This does not bode well.'The merrevail haunting the tunnels of Khazad-dûm have stolen many letters from the dwarves who have fallen in battle in Durin's Way.Letters can be taken from merrevail looting the bodies of fallen dwarves in the halls of Durin's Way.

Listein has asked you to reclaim dwarf-letters before they are be taken away by merrevail.Collect dwarf-letters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Listein as at the Door to the Clouds, near the entrance to Zirakzigil.

You should bring the dwarf-letters back to Listein.'We have many traditions, ${PLAYER}, and this one is not the least. When we head into battle, we bring with us a letter. If we fall, that letter will be returned home by the survivors, if any remain.

'Many of us have come to Moria, and some of us have fallen...and now it appears that the merrevail have discovered these letters and have taken a perverse pleasure in keeping them as trophies of victory against us. The honour of our warriors and the peace of mind of their families demand that we recover these letters from the enemy whenever possible and return them to their rightful homes. Will you help us retrieve these letters?

'If you come upon one of our fallen in Durin's Way, search the body for their letter. Return any letters here to me before the merrevail can get to them.''Those letters must be found and brought back home. We owe the fallen that much at least.''You have retrieved the letters of the fallen? My thanks to you, ${PLAYER}.

'The messages contained herein will bring a sorrowful, but much needed close to the grieving of their families. I will see that they make their way safely to Durin's Threshold.'Uxi fears for a wonderful statue of Helgi Goblinbane, a dwarf of great renown once, whose name resonates among the goblins the way Azog's does among the dwarves.The statue base is in the courtyard hall just to the south-east of Uxi.

Uxi told you to examine the statue base so that you will be able to recognize its other pieces.Examine the statueUxi is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, north-west of the statue.

You should return to Uxi for more instruction.Talk to Uxi at the Chamber of the Cross-roads'Do you see that shattered statue just in the centre of the hall, friend ${RACE}? According to records and carvings we have found, it once depicted a brave dwarf by the name of Helgi Goblinbane.

'The goblins of Moria have been systematically smashing all images they can find of him -- I am not even sure that this isn't the last remnant of his legacy! It was nearly whole when I first arrived, but just recently a party of goblins reduced the statue to the state in which you now see it. They carried off the pieces, boasting that they would become objects of ridicule in goblin-camps throughout the Mines.

'If you are prepared for a dangerous and noble undertaking, go look closely at the statue's base, so that you will recognize its pieces when you go seeking them.''It is a pity that such a great work of art would be shattered so. Is there aught you can do to aid in its recovery?''So, do you think you can recognize the statue's pieces now, if you were to run into them elsewhere?

'I think the rest are in goblin and Orc-camps throughout Khazad-dûm. I would start by heading east to Jazârgund -- that's the direction in which the goblins who smashed the statue fled.'Krum, one of Líkmund's dwarves, has discovered a large band of goblins in Ninknakh Faltor at the westernmost end of Durin's Way.Krum can be found to the north of the Chamber of the Cross-roads, near Ninknakh Faltor.

Líkmund has asked you to speak with Krum regarding the goblin-camp he found and aid him as you may.Find and talk to KrumLíkmund is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, south of Ninknakh Faltor.

The camp at Ninknakh Faltor was indeed quite large and well-fortified, and you were only able to explore it in part. You should inform Líkmund of what you learned.Talk to Líkmund at the Chamber of the Cross-roads'One of my dwarves, Krum, has discovered a large goblin-camp in the westernmost chamber of Durin's Way, which the creatures call Ninknakh Faltor in their vile tongue. He has only scouted around the outskirts and has asked for help investigating more closely.

'I cannot spare any extra men for this, but if you would go and ensure his safety I would be grateful. You can find him near Ninknakh Faltor to the north of here.

'When you have learned more about this encampment, return to me.''The camp Krum found is large -- we will need to keep an eye on it, lest the goblins there launch a foray against us. That would make for a pitched battle indeed....''Líkmund sent you? I welcome your aid!

'The camp is just around the corner. It is large, but I am not yet sure how large it truly is.

'Let us find out!''So, the camp was larger than Krum first thought. It is good to know more about it.

'Fortunately, it lies off the main road to Jazârgund, and we can for the most part avoid it.'The Elves of Echad Mirobel have tracked Isengard's forces in Eregion to an ancient school.The School of Tham Mírdain can be found in Mirobel, in the south-west region of Eregion.

Gelriwen of Echad Mirobel has asked you to find the entrance to an ancient school.Find the School of Tham Mírdain'We have tracked the forces of Isengard and believe they are ransacking an ancient school, desperately searching for any knowledge related to the making of Rings of Power. We must find this school before them.''You must find the School at Tham Mírdain, ${PLAYER}!'Grants completion of quest: Student of the EnemyBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Student of the Enemy'Now, my little fellows, where be you a-going to, puffing like a bellows? What's the matter here then? Tell me what's your trouble!

'You need to play the instances? Naught worse that that, eh? That can soon be mended.''Well, my little fellows! You shall have your deeds completed!'Arnfinn ventured out from Tharâkh Bazân to gather information about Mazog and has yet to return.Arnfinn was last seen heading east towards Jazârgund.

Búkk fears for the safety of one of his friends, Arnfinn who was last seen venturing out to find information about Mazog and the Orcs of Moria.Búkk is at Tharâkh Bazân to the west of Jazârgund.

Búkk will be pleased to know that Arnfinn is safe.Talk to Búkk at Tharâkh Bazân'${PLAYER}, I fear there is trouble brewing. Arnfinn left several days ago, heading east towards Jazârgund. He said he was going out to search the nearby chambers, to learn anything he might about Mazog and the Orcs.

'He has yet to return, and I fear for his safety. Would you look for him? He was last seen heading towards some of the Orc infested areas to the east. I fear something may have happened to him... and that could lead the Orcs back here!''Please, find Arnfinn. We cannot afford to lose any more good dwarves, nor can we afford to alert the Orcs to our presence here.''Thank you for your help, friend. I was doing all I could to give us an advantage against the Orcs when I was set upon. The Orcs kept me trapped back here, taunting me with tales of Azog and the days of old, when the Orcs slew the dwarves in scores. I shudder to recall those days.

'Please, go back to Tharâkh Bazân and let Búkk know that I am unharmed, but will not yet be returning. The information we need may be found out here somewhere.''Speak with Búkk at the gardens of Tharâkh Bazân. Let him know of my gratitude to you.''So Arnfinn is safe? That lightens my heart, ${PLAYER}. He is a brave adventurer like you, but I worried he had taken an arrow in the back. I do not approve of him staying out there, but that decision is his to make... he is a reasonable dwarf.'The Redhorn Lodes have become a haven for beasts and Orc-kind alike since the fall of Moria. A variety of different tribes of Orcs fight for control over the precious ore found within the rock while also competing with insect and beast alike for territory to call their own. The Iron Garrison, seeking to reclaim the mine of Tumun-ghâr, has sent Alwar to the Redhorn Lodes to establish an effort to clear the intruders from the old dwarf-delving.The entrance to Tumun-ghâr lies within Gharâaf-fehem.

Alwar has asked you to assist him in clearing Tumun-ghâr of the vermin within.Defeat intruders within Tumun-ghâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Alwar can be found at Gharâf-fehem in the Redhorn Lodes.

You should return to Alwar to receive a reward for your efforts.Talk to Alwar at Gharâf-fehem'I have encountered many foes just to get shelter here in Gharâf-fehem. I was hopeful that the lack of resistance Hersir and I encountered in setting up camp here would be indicative of what was within the mine.

'Luck was, sadly, not with me in that. My hopes for an easy reclamation were dashed when I beheld the enemies lurking within Tumun-ghâr.

'They are many and varied. Could I convince you to provide me aid in expelling these intruders?''I feared you would not return when I sent you into Tumun-ghâr. The silence seemed to indicate your falling to those within the mine.

'But seeing you here now, unscathed and victorious, means that my fears were thankfully unfounded.

'Your aid in this matter is much appreciated.''Have you completed your task yet? Please do so, then return to me when you have finished.'The Redhorn Lodes have become a haven for beasts and Orc-kind alike since the fall of Moria. A variety of different tribes of Orcs fight for control over the precious ore found within the rock, while also competing with insect and beast alike for territory to call their own. The Iron Garrison has sent a small expedition into the Redhorn Lodes to recover a little known mine called Tumun-ghâr.The entrance to Tumun-ghâr lies within Gharâf-fehem.

Alwar has asked you to defeat the leader of the intruders within Tumun-ghâr.Defeat the leader of the intruders in Tumun-ghârAlwar is at Gharâf-fehem.

You should return to Alwar with news of your success.Talk to Alwar at Gharâf-fehem'The Redhorn Lodes are a frightening place to be in. Orcs to the left, deep-claws to the right, and gredbyg right in the middle!

'Were it not for my duty to the Iron Garrison, I would not even attempt to reclaim Tumun-ghâr. But to me, duty is everything, so here I am.

'In order to reclaim this mine, we will need to defeat the leadership of the intruders within. Defeat the enemy, be it Orc or beast, that leads the intruders within. Doing so should position us to more ably reclaim Tumun-ghâr in the name of the Iron Garrison.'

<rgb=#FF0000>The Iron Garrison has created a diversion, drawing the bulk of the intruders from the depths of Tumun-ghâr. They are permitting you access for one hour, during which time you may enter and exit Tumun-ghâr freely to complete the tasks bestown upon you. 

However, after the hour has passed, the Iron Garrison can no longer guarantee your safety and thus will bar access until they can once again muster an offence to draw the enemy from Tumun-ghâr.</rgb>'Do not waste time! Enter Tumun-ghâr and tear down whatever passes for a leader within.''You are quite efficient with a weapon, my friend. I could not have done the job better myself.

'With the intruders in disarray, we can further secure Tumun-ghâr. For your efforts, you deserve a token of the Iron Garrison's appreciation.

'What? Yes, I know -- it doesn't look like much. That is because...well...it isn't.'Though well-stocked initially, the efforts to reclaim Moria have spread the Iron Garrison thin. To supplement their ambition, the Iron Garrison seeks to repurpose tools and equipment scavenged from the ruins. Within Tumun-ghâr, the Iron Garrison works to collect the tools needed to support additional prospecting efforts across the entirety of Moria.The entrance to Tumun-ghâr lies within Gharâf-fehem.

Alwar has asked you to collect Miner's Tool-kits from within Tumun-ghâr.'Our purposes here at Tumun-ghâr are manifold. While it is most important for us to reclaim this mine in the name of the Iron Garrison, we also need to use it to bolster our supplies.

'While history warns us of the consequences of delving deeper than we should, we cannot simply be content to reclaim...we must expand! And to do that, we need equipment.

'What better place to find mining tools than a once-functioning mine?''While not many, these tool-kits will aid us in our future efforts across Khazad-dûm. Until the forges are stoked and the ore is flowing, we must make do with what was left behind.'You found an ornate chest-piece from a set of heavy armour, old but of superlative craftsmanship and raked with claw-marks, lying seemingly unattended. You may wish to find out more about it.You may wish to ask someone in the Chamber of the Cross-roads about the armour you found.Talk to Rambi at the Chamber of the Cross-roadsYou have found an ornate chest-piece from a set of heavy armour, old but of superlative craftsmanship and raked with claw-marks, lying seemingly unattended. You may wish to find out more about it.

Perhaps a dwarf in the Chamber of the Cross-roads will know more.'An ornate chest-piece, you say? Surrounded by bats... that is interesting.'Kalman has little idea what the mervyl are, but they sound to him like something his friend Búkk mentioned before leaving for Tharâkh Bazân.Búkk can be found in Tharâkh Bazân, the gardens to the east.

Kalman recommends that you speak with his friend Búkk about the mervyl.Talk to Búkk in Tharâkh BazânArnod can be found at the camp in Tharâkh Bazân, the gardens east of the Door to the Clouds.

Búkk recommends speaking with Arnod, who has studied the maps and history of Khazad-dûm, about where to begin searching for mervyl.Talk to Arnod in Tharâkh Bazân'I don't know what these creatures are, ${PLAYER} -- this is the first I've seen or heard of them, though perhaps they are related to the merrevail -- but I am certain that their presence here in Khazad-dûm bodes only ill.

'Perhaps Búkk may be of help to us. I seem to recall him mentioning something about these creatures, and I suspect that he may have encountered them again on his way to Tharâkh Bazân. Speak with Búkk and find out what information he may have.''Greetings, traveller. What brings you to Tharâkh Bazân?

'Mervyl, you say? Why yes, not long ago I read a report on these creatures that came from Jazârgund, to the east. They indicate a huge cavern at the eastern end of Durin's Way, crawling with merrevail and mervyl. Let us be thankful that we have not yet seen them in force, but be wary should you head east to that great pit where they are known to dwell.''So, you want to learn more about the accursed creatures known as mervyl?

'Well, I'm afraid I cannot say that I've learned much as of yet. The mervyl have remained mostly unseen as we explored Tharâkh Bazân, but I know of someone who may know where to look. Arnod has studied the maps and gathered knowledge of the many dark corners of Khazad-dûm. Obtain from him the knowledge of where the mervyl may reside in number.''Búkk saw something similar to the creatures you tell me about. You should speak with him at the Tharâkh Bazân.'Listein has asked you to recover a relic of ages past, in nearby Uflûmp-mur.Uflûmp-mur can be found at the small outpost found at the entrance to Zirakzigil in Durin's Way.

Listein has asked you to head east to Uflûmp-mur to find an ancient shield, so that he may learn what untold legends it holds.Find the ancient shield in Uflûmp-murThe Door to the Clouds is just west of Uflûmp-mur, at the entrance to Zirakzigil in Durin's Way.

You have found the ancient shield, and should return it to Listein for safe-keeping.Return the shield to Listein at the entrance to Zirakzigil'We must keep safe the artifacts of ages past, ${PLAYER}. Studying these relics gives insight to the untold legends of our forefathers, which might otherwise become lost.

'I have information that one such object, a mythical shield, was last seen in Uflûmp-mur, just a short distance east of The Door to the Clouds. The goblins would have a difficult time destroying such a sturdy shield, so I am hopeful it may still be found there.''Uflûmp-mur is just a short distance to the east. The goblins will have difficulty in destroying such a remarkable shield, but perhaps they will have discarded it nearby.''What a wonderful find this is, a true treasure of the dwarves. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. The safe-guarding of this shield will ensure that the legend of our craft does not fade from knowledge.'The morroval-queen has laid claim to one of the ancient mirrors of Khazad-dûm. If it were tampered with, she would surely respond with angry force.Bogrian's mirror is at Dâr-rukh, atop a tall Moria-mirror tower which overlooks the morroval-caverns to the east.

Folkath believes the time has come to strike against the morroval-queen. He knows she has an ancient mirror she values highly, and Folkath believes if you were to tamper with it, Bogrian will appear and attack.Folkath as at the camp on the western edge of the morroval-caverns.

Folkath will be pleased to hear that you wounded Bogrian and forced her to retreat from the battle.Talk to Folkath at the Fanged Pit camp'I have talked to the others here and gathered all the information you gave them. I believe, with the damage you have already done, we are prepared to strike against the queen of the merrevail.

'Our scouts tell me that she has one of the ancient mirrors of Khazad-dûm in her possession, and she values it very highly. I believe if you were to try to damage the mirror, she should quickly respond with force. That will be your opportunity to strike. Do not waste it.

'You will find it at the top of a tall tower, east of here.''So, Bogrian took the cowardly way out and fled after the battle. I am not much surprised. I sense she is far from through being a thorn in our side, but for now, at least, the victory is ours.''The queen of the merrevail will fall, and these caverns shall belong to Durin's Folk once more.'Folkath wants you to learn more about the mysterious creatures so connected to the bats.Gúri, Hadi,and Bési are all at the camp in the Fanged Pit.

Folkath wants you to help the dwarves of Durin's Way in their efforts against the merrevail.Aid HadiAid GúriAid BésiFolkath is at the Fanged Pit, east of Jazârgund.

Folkath will be interested to know what you learned from helping Hadi, Bési, and Gúri.Talk to Folkath at the Fanged Pit camp'The merrevail and mervyl are mysterious creatures. I know much about goblins and Orcs, but little of those with wings. What I do know is that they present a serious threat to us here in Durin's Way. These foul creatures call this entire cavern their territory, and I fear they are intent on expanding it.

'These merrevail cling to the safety of the darkness, and they have a bloodlust that makes them a most dangerous foe. If we are to be successful, we must know more about everything that goes on here. Speak to Hadi, Bési, and Gúri. They have each agreed to help, and have travelled with me here to the Fanged Pit.''So, from what the four of you have gathered, everything in the Fanged Pit revolves around the queen of the merrevail. 

'They all live and die by her order and command. It is decided then: the only option is to strike against her directly.''Do as the others wish. Without the information they will glean from your efforts, we cannot hope to stop these creatures.'The search for Bingo Boffin continues in the unmapped depths of Khazad-dûm.Ketill Map-maker said he would meet you in Tharâkh Bazân, along Durin's Way, to the north-east of the Dolven-view.Talk to Ketill Map-maker at Tharâkh Bazân, along Durin's WayA large lynx ran by Ketill Map-maker in Tharâkh Bazân, heading to the east. Could it be Willem Whisker?Find Willem Whisker somewhere in Tharâkh BazânSpalvi Stout-heart has come to the pool in Tharâkh Bazân.

Willem Whisker found a page from Bingo's manuscript and you should show it to Spalvi.Willem Whisker has run east from Tharâkh Bazân on the trail of some scent. Has he found Bingo's trail?Follow Willem Whisker east to the Stone Hall of JazârgundSpalvi is at the Stone Hall of Jazârgund, halfway along Durin's Way, in Moria.Talk to Spalvi at the Stone Hall of JazârgundWillem Whisker has run east from the Stone Hall of Jazârgund on the trail of some scent. Has he found Bingo's trail?Follow Willem Whisker east to the Fanged PitSpalvi has come to the Fanged Pit. Unlike Willem Whisker, he's not here to take a nap!Talk to Spalvi at the Fanged PitMerrevail can be found in the Fanged Pit at the eastern end of Durin's Way, and they gather near pools of water such as the pool of Khulturg.

Spalvi thinks you should make your way to the pool of Khulturg in the Fanged Pit, defeating merrevail to prove to the dwarves that you are a helpful sort.Defeat merrevail on your way to the pool of Khulturg, in the Fanged PitBingo sits by the edge of the pool of Khulturg, in the Fanged Pit, but something does not seem quite right.Talk to Bingo by the side of the pool of Khulturg, in the Fanged PitSpalvi Stout-heart is in the camp of dwarves at the Fanged Pit.

You have found Bingo Boffin, but it seems that he lost his memory during his time apart!Talk to Spalvi at the Fanged Pit'Ketill Map-maker told me he plans to begin mapping Durin's Way. He said he would meet you at the gardens of Tharâkh Bazân, to the north-east. Go to him and keep your eyes peeled for Bingo, ${PLAYER}!''Ketill Map-maker told me he plans to begin mapping Durin's Way. He said he would meet you at the gardens of Tharâkh Bazân, to the north-east. Go to him and keep your eyes peeled for Bingo, ${PLAYER}!''${PLAYER}! You will not believe what happened to me while I was setting up my map-making tools here!

'A large lynx came barreling up the slope and almost knocked me down! It was racing at quite a clip, and seemed to be chasing a piece of paper caught on one of the light breezes that rustles the trees of Tharâkh Bazân!

'The lynx raced off to the east! What do you think it means? Is this some frightening beast from the depths that has emerged from its vile den to threaten the Iron Garrison?''A large lynx came barreling up the slope and almost knocked me down! It was racing at quite a clip, and seemed to be chasing a piece of paper caught on one of the light breezes that rustles the trees of Tharâkh Bazân!

'The lynx raced off to the east! What do you think it means? Is this some frightening beast from the depths that has emerged from its vile den to threaten the Iron Garrison?'Willem is drenched, his fur matted against his skin as he swims in the chill waters of the pool. As you take a closer look, you see that he holds a wet piece of parchment in his powerful jaws and is trying to keep it above the water of the pool.

You gently retrieve the wet parchment from him, and he stares at you intently.Willem Whisker is soggy and soaked, but seems happy. Has he caught Bingo's scent?'Is this what I think it is? It certainly looks like it, ${PLAYER}! Bingo told me about the book he was writing of his journey, and here we hold a piece of it!

'Sweet vindication! If the manuscript is here in Khazad-dûm, then surely our hobbit must be as well! I think Willem Whisker must have caught Bingo's scent, and if we follow him faithfully we will find our lost hobbit!''Willem ran to the east! Has he caught Bingo's scent?''Oh, Willem. He was just hungry.''I thought Willem might have caught Bingo's scent, but he wasn't following our hobbit... he was following his stomach!

'Wait, I think he's about to run off again, ${PLAYER}! This time he must find Bingo for sure!''Willem ran off again! Do you think this time he has caught Bingo's scent?''Well, it seems as if Willem Whisker knows what he wants, but it brings us no closer to accomplishing our objective!

'The dwarves here come under frequent attacks by the merrevail that live in the pits to the east. They gather by the pools, and prevent any dwarves from getting close. Travel into the pit and defeat any merrevail that you see, making your way to the pool of Khulturg located in the north-east.

'Perhaps the knowledge that we are helping them will convince these dwarves to provide us some assistance, as well.''The dwarves here come under frequent attacks by the merrevail that live in the pits to the east. They gather by the pools, and prevent any dwarves from getting close. Travel into the pit and defeat any merrevail that you see, making your way to the pool of Khulturg located in the north-east.

'Perhaps the knowledge that we are helping them will convince these dwarves to provide us some assistance, as well.''Yes? Can I help you?''Hello there. Is this your cat? He does seem quite friendly, but I have never seen such a creature up close before.'

You ask Bingo if he is feeling all right, and the hobbit responds with a puzzled smile.

'It is nice of you to ask, but I must admit that I am a bit worried. I do not know exactly how I came to be sitting by the side of this lake. Are we underground? This is not like anywhere in the Shire that I have ever seen! This must be out by Scary, or Brockenborings.

'You keep calling me Bingo. Is that me? How odd! I can't quite get a handle on my name. Bingo Boffin, you say? It does not feel terribly familiar, but if you are a friend, I will take you at your word, and I thank you for filling me in!''What a peculiar place! Are we really in the Shire?''You found Bingo! What is it, ${PLAYER}? Why do you wear that expression?'

You tell Spalvi that something must have happened to Bingo after he became separated from you, for now he seems to have lost his memory.

'Really? That can happen? I would not mind if he simply forgot the part where I betrayed him to the Dourhands and locked him in a cage, but I suppose forgetting the rest is not acceptable, is it? A pity.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Bingo's Scattered Thoughts' (Recommended Level: 56)</rgb>The morroval-workshop has been busy making weapons of war. Hadi is tasked with putting an end to their labour.Erlar is waiting just outside the morroval-workshop, east from the Fanged Pit camp.

Hadi asked you to speak to Erlar and help him assault a morroval siege-weapon workshop. Erlar must survive!Talk to ErlarWith the workshop clear of merrevail, the nearby siege-weapon can be dealt with.

Hadi asked you to help Erlar assault a morroval siege-weapon workshop.Destroy the morroval siege-weaponHadi as at the Fanged Pit camp, west of the morroval siege-camp.

Hadi will want to know that your assault with Erlar was successful.Talk to Hadi at the camp in the Fanged Pit'Reports indicate that the merrevail are a larger threat than we initially thought. Like the great armies of the South, they have great siege-weaponry with which to wage war. This is disturbing news.

'If we are to succeed here, we must infiltrate their workshop and destroy those constructing the siege weapons. Erlar is waiting for you to help assault their camp. You will find him east of here, within morroval-territory, at the base of the siege-camp.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Erlar must survive.</rgb>'Erlar is waiting just outside the morroval-camp. I ask you to make haste, ${PLAYER}, lest he be caught before our strike can be delivered.''Hadi sent you? Good! I have made all the preparations and now is the perfect time.

'The merrevail have left the siege-workshop undefended. We can sneak in and catch them unawares. On your mark, the battle will be joined.''So, Erlar's plan worked. I admit, I initially had doubts, but he has a mind for such things.

'With those weapons out of commission, we can venture deeper into the morroval-camp without fear of reprisal.

'Erlar said that some of the mervyl were being chivvied along by their female counterparts with threats of "Bogrian's wrath" should they err. Whoever this Bogrian is, they fear her most sincerely.'Throughout Eregion there exist still several ancient Elf-forges where items of power were once crafted. The ruins of Pembar are one such site, one which Perimbant knows well.Perimbant has asked you to bring him an infused garnet to act as the heart of the spell that is to be woven into your weapon. Where such a gem may be obtained, he does not know.Perimbant can be found in Echad Dúnann, just west of the gates of Moria.

Perimbant has bidden you to speak with him when you are ready to travel to the ruins of Pembar to liberate it from the flight of drakes.Talk to Perimbant to travel to PembarPerimbant can be found in Echad Dúnann, west of the gates of Moria.

You should return to Perimbant to complete the enhancement of your weapon.'Indeed, I know of just the place to imbue such a quality as you seek. An ancient forge lies hidden among the ruins of Pembar, north-west of here. There is a small complication, I fear. A wing of Drakes from high Zirakzigil was seen flying in the direction of the ruins not a week ago. It is likely that they have brought their brood down into the hills to feed upon the carrion of battle.

'Alas, Pembar is of little enough value for us to risk trying to retake it now. If you need to reach that forge, I suggest you gather a few companions and see if you can dislodge the Drakes by your own cunning and skill.

'In any case, you will need an infused garnet if you wish to obtain the quality you seek there. Return to me when you have one and bring a couple of stalwart companions to aid you.''Are you ready to face the drakes I spoke of, ${PLAYER}? I have devised a simple plan for you, though I do not think it will be simple to carry out.

'The drakes have likely come down to feed their young. I suggest you hunt the smaller ones, both because they are weaker and because you are likely to force the leader of the flight to come to you if you slay enough of her young.

'Avoid the older ones as much as you can. They are considerably more dangerous, and if you can defeat the Wing-mother, then they will likely retreat back to Zirakzigil, having no reason to remain.''Ah! You were able to acquire an infused garnet. I will return the gem to you when you are ready to depart for Pembar.

'Speak to me again when you and your companions are ready.''Well fought, ${PLAYER}! The Wing-mother has fallen and Pembar is free of her brood!

'I trust you were able to make use of the forge while you were there?'The Water-works is a site of importance to the dwarves who wish to remain in Moria. Once such dwarf, Foreman Indrith, has made it a mission to repair the channel there.Foreman Indrith believes that you sheared a gear while trying to force the wheel housing in the Great Wheel to start turning once more. He believes another gear is located in the tunnels of the Great Wheel.Find a new gear in the tunnels of the Great WheelForeman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel, south-west of Hulwul-nefekh.'If we sheared a gear, and I believe that we did, we need to get a new one. During my time in the Great Wheel, I have explored many of the tunnels that feed these wheels.

'On one of my journeys, I spotted a gear in a room beside the tunnels. However, I thought nothing of it, and left it where it lay. I believe you will need to recover this gear before our work can continue.

'You can make your way deeper into the Great Wheel from The Drowned Deeps or through the gate across the way. Hurry!''Search the tunnels of the Great Wheel. I saw a gear lying about on one of my journeys... perhaps it still remains.''You have the gear? Wonderful!

'While you were gone, I heard the rumble of something great moving amid the Water-works. Whether our wheels begin to churn once more or some other force lurks nearby, I do not know....

'Maybe a little caution would not hurt, after all....'The Water-works is a site of importance to the dwarves who wish to remain in Moria. Once such dwarf, Foreman Indrith, has made it a mission to repair the channel there.Foreman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel.

Foreman Indrith wants to make certain that you are strong enough to assist him with turning the wheel. Perhaps you should <rgb=#FF0000>flex</rgb> for him.Show Foreman Indrith how strong you are by <rgb=#FF0000>flex</rgb>ingForeman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel.

Foreman Indrith has asked you to help turn the wheel.Step to the Wheel to aid Foreman IndrithForeman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel.

After showing the foreman that you were strong enough, of which he was dubious, the two of you attempted to turn the wheel behind him. A terrible noise was heard, and the foreman looked baffled.Talk to Foreman Indrith in the Wheel-house'With the number of toads and lizards reduced, we should get a better idea of what is clogging up the works. It is going to take some time to clean out the pipes, though.

'Well, that can wait for later. I have another task that I will need your help with. Of course, I first need to see if you are strong enough to help me.

'Roll up your sleeves and let me see how much muscle you have there.''Well, I have seen greater sinews on a chicken, but you will have to do. Come along, ${PLAYER}, let us see if we can get this wheel to move.''That was not right. I think that we sheared a gear, and our work cannot continue until we have a new one. Lucky for us, I believe I know where we can find one....''Come now, do not shy away from this. A simple <rgb=#FF0000>flex</rgb> is all I need to know if you are strong enough to help me.'Simbi is interested to hear from one of his friends, Aguti, about the progress of the expedition in the Water-works.Águti is at the Rotting Cellar camp in the Water-works, far south-west of the Twenty-first Hall.

Simbi has asked you to speak with Águti regarding the progress of the expedition in the Water-works.Talk to Águti at the Rotting Cellar camp'Do you have time enough to aid the expedition again? I would like you to speak with a friend of mine, Águti. He has travelled deeper into Moria with the expedition, and I have yet to hear back from him.

'You can find Águti down in the old Water-works in a place we call the Rotting Cellar, south-west of here, past the Silvertine Lodes.

'I'm given to understand that it isn't considered the most comfortable post....''Well met, ${PLAYER}. So, Simbi sent you down here did he? He must not like you very much then....

'No! No! 'Twas but a jest! It's just a bit damp down here but you get used to it -- as long as you can keep the mould out of your beard.

'I've been studying the creatures of Moria since I arrived here -- as much as I can without being devoured by them, at any rate -- and have learned a few things. If you would be willing to aid me, I'm sure we can uncover their secrets!''Go see Águti in the Rotting Cellar.'Kaldi wishes you to return to Simbi with news of the Watcher's return.Simbi is in the Twenty-first Hall, to the north-east of the Water-works.

Kaldi wishes you to bring word of the Watcher's return to the expedition.Talk to Simbi in the Twenty-first Hall'This is bad news, ${PLAYER}. The terrible beast that assailed us outside the West Gate has made its lair here amongst the Water-works.

'You must return to Simbi in the Twenty-first Hall at once, and inform him of our plight. We have had many successes here in the Water-works, but this terror could destroy everything we have worked for.

'I will inform Indrith and Ansurr of your passage. Go with haste!''Hurry, speak to Simbi in the Twenty-first Hall! We cannot allow the Watcher to slay more of our number!''What word do you bring? Will our great wheels churn once more?'

You relay your tale of what you have seen within the Water-works.

'No! How many more must fall before that beast troubles us no longer? This is... an unfortunate turn. We have not the numbers to make an assault on the beast yet, but perhaps in time we will. You and your allies may be able to deal a final blow against it, but I sense you are not yet prepared.

'The expedition must press on - the time for vengeance against this beast will come. For now, we must reclaim Zelem-melek.'The morroval-queen, Bogrian, has fled into hiding. Folkath and the others have begun investigating where she may next appear.Hadi resides in camp with Folkath at the west edge of the Fanged Pit.

Folkath recommends that you question Hadi about what he has learned of Bogrian's clan.Speak to Hadi to find out what he knowsSeek out the scouts at their habitual meeting-place, south of the entrance to Tith-maudhul, and try to overhear their conversation before you defeat them.Spy upon and defeat two scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Folkath is at the camp on the west edge of the Fanged Pit.

You should return to Folkath with news of your success.Talk to Folkath at his camp in the Fanged Pit'We have done our best to keep watch throughout this cavern, and have been learning more about Bogrian and her maidens. 

'Hadi overheard some of the merrevail talking, and a few key phrases piqued my interest. Will you speak to him and find out what he knows?''Their queen wants to flee to the Mirror-Halls in Zirakzigil? Durin's beard!''It is true that I overheard some of Bogrian's tribe speaking of her whereabouts, but before I could learn her location I was spotted and I fled. I have not the courage to go back. You will need to spy on some of her scouts, yourself, to find out what is truly going on.

'Head north out of camp, then bear east and hug the cliff-face. The scouts have a meeting-place just south of the entrance to Tith-maudhul. Once you've overheard a little of their conversation, defeat them -- the fewer scouts their queen has, the better for us!''Seek out Bogrian's scouts and learn what you may from them. The merrevail roost at the just north of our encampment.'You discovered a brooch of Lórien within the spiderwebs of the Water-works.Geirfast is in the Twenty-first Hall.

The brooch of Lórien you found is marked with the name Geirfast.Nestled among the webs of the glass-spiders you find a brooch. It features a green leaf veined with silver. The name Geirfast is engraved in the back. You find it odd that a brooch of Lothlórien bears the name of a dwarf.'Where did you find this? In a web in the Water-works, you say? This belonged to my great-great-great-grandfather whose name I now bear. Thank you for bringing this to me.'Brogur is skeptical that the Heart of Fire even exists, and wants you to at least do something about the goblin problem while you search for it.Goblins can be found among the Silvertine Lodes, south and below the Great Delving, and their maps can be found within Gamil Filik, the mine they have occupied.

Brogur asked you to slay goblins while you seek the Heart of Fire, and to keep an eye out for their maps; it is possible they discovered the forge and included it on their crude maps.Defeat goblins along the Silvertine Lodes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Brogur is in the Chamber of Command, up the eastern stairs in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

You have slain many goblins and collected their maps while searching for the Heart of Fire.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, just outside the Chamber of Command.

Brogur has not seen anything of use on the crude goblin-maps you found, but his cousin Bósi may have better fortune interpreting them.'You will always have my respect for what you did before the Doors of Durin, avenging my poor son with your excellent weapon, but I must be honest with you: I believe you are wasting your time. As long as you will be trapessing around in the dark looking for this flight-of-fancy forge, you might as well accomplish something worthwhile, ${PLAYER}.

'There seems to be a large goblin presence among the Silvertine Lodes, far to the south and below the Great Delving. As long as you are searching for this fabled Heart of Fire, you may as well slay goblins while you do it -- especially the ones that have moved into Gamil Filik, the Elder-mine. The goblins are many, and bringing an ally or two might be a good idea.

'In fact, why not steal some of their maps? They have long lived here in the darkness, and their crude maps may show the way to this mythical forge of yours, as well as being useful to those of us seeking paths that actually exist.''I do not think the Heart of Fire exists, ${PLAYER}. We would have heard of this legendary forge if it did. As long as you are searching for it, you may as well slay goblins along the Silvertine Lodes. They are many, and you may wish to bring an ally or two.

'Keep an eye out for their maps, if you must; perhaps they have found this imaginary forge of yours.''I cannot complain about this errand of yours, ${PLAYER}: you have slain many goblins despite your search for a forge that likely never existed.

'These crude goblin-maps tell me nothing I didn't already know: that goblins are filthy, disgusting creatures, and their maps are worthless.

'Show them to my cousin Bósi, though. Perhaps he has more patience than I and will tell you something useful.''Bósi has always been better at this sort of mind-work than I. Show him the maps and maybe he will have more to tell you. They look like crude and hideous scribbles to me. Goblins are wretched creatures, are they not?''The goblins have made their homes here in the darkness for a long time. These maps might have secrets to show us, however unsavoury they seem.'

Bósi peers at the maps for a long while, and then his face creases into a wide smile.

'I may have unravelled our riddle, ${PLAYER}! I do believe that we can discern the location of the Heart of Fire from these maps!'Bósi believes he has discovered the location of Nâr-khelab, the forge where the mithril axe Zigilburk was made.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, near the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving of Moria.

Bósi believes he has intuited the hidden entrance to Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire, and is waiting to travel there with you.Talk to Bósi and travel with him to find Nâr-khelabBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving of Moria.

With Bósi's help, you discovered the hidden entrance to Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire, and should now speak with him.'Look here, ${PLAYER}. The location of Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire, is on this crude goblin-map! Do you not see it?'

Bósi laughs, clearly enjoying the attention.

'Let me put it this way, my friend: we know that the door to the Heart of Fire is sealed; indeed, you discovered the trick to opening it within the Word-hoard of Durin. But the goblins cannot know this trick -- the pages that held the secret were disturbed by only deep-claws; if the goblins had found those pages and understood their significance, they would have certainly taken them.

'We are not looking for a room on this map, ${PLAYER}; we are looking for a stretch of undisturbed wall behind which such a room could lie hidden, and I have found just such a spot! Let me know when you are ready, and together we will travel to this place!''Are you ready, ${PLAYER}? If my guess is near the mark, we will soon find the Heart of Fire, and I will set the dwarves of my company to its mighty forges!

'And perhaps Zigilburk itself still remains within! Imagine: an axe made entirely of mithril. What a wonder!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'You fought bravely and well, ${PLAYER}, as I have come to expect, but more important is this: the secret forges of the Heart of Fire are now at the service of my people!

'It is a shame that we did not find Zigilburk itself within the Heart of Fire, but I was wrong to expect it: only rarely do weapons remain at the place of their making, for is it not their purpose to go forth into the world and find glory on the battlefield? Even so, this remains a great victory for my expedition.

'If you have the proficiency, the forges of Nâr-khelab are of course at your service.'Encouraged by their success within the mines, many of the dwarves have followed Brogur further east, to the Twenty-first Hall.Brogur is in the Chamber of Leadership, a small room off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.

Brogur has brought a company of dwarves further east into Moria, and has set up a new base of operations in the Chamber of Leadership, off the Twenty-first Hall.'We have had great successes here in Moria already, ${PLAYER}, and Brogur has gone eastward with many of our people seeking the Twenty-first Hall and the royal houses of Durin.

'I am worried by this haste. Yes, we have achieved a great victory with the discovery of the Heart of Fire, but I fear that Brogur will advance too far and get in over his head.

'Travel to the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek and warn my cousin against this move.''Welcome to the Chamber of Leadership, ${PLAYER}! From here I will lead my people to even greater glory in Moria!''Brogur will be in the Chamber of Leadership, a small room off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.'The water-wheels of Moria were once instrumental in powering and cooling the great fires of the ancient forges.The water-wheels can be found at The Great Wheel, south-west of the Hulwul-nefekh.

Ansurr challenged you to find a great water-wheel in the Water-works which is no longer working. Once found, he wants you to clear out some of the creatures nearby to secure it.Find the ancient water-wheelDefeat creatures at The Great Wheel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ansurr is in Hulwul-nefekh, north-east of The Great Wheel.

Ansurr will be pleased to hear you located and secured the water-wheel.Talk to Ansurr in Hulwul-nefekh'Have you heard a great creaking and churning in your travels of the Water-works? That sound is from one of the ancient water-wheels which once powered the great forges of Khazad-dûm. Without those wheels, the forges would overheat, and all the dwarves would have burned and met their end.

'However, not all of the wheels still work. The Great Wheel has long stood dormant, and it is time we renewed its churn. If you can, do us a favour and drive out some of the creatures in the area. If we are to refire the forges, we will need to control the wheels first.

'The water-wheels can be found by The Great Wheel, south-west of here.''So you found it? 

'Well, I am impressed. Many would have succumbed to the waters or the creatures of the deeps. Your help is greatly appreciated.''The water-wheels can be found to the south-west. If we are to rekindle the forges, the wheels must be under our control.'The materials originally used to craft the dwarf-lamps have long since been used up. More must be found if the halls of Moria are to shine once more.Glass-spiders can be found to the west of the Rotting Cellar, near The Lost Palace.

Thrand wishes to repair some of the dwarf-lamps smashed by the goblins and speculates that glass-spider legs will make the best replacements for the crystals.Collect glass-spider legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thrand is in the Rotting Cellar, east of The Lost Palace.

Thrand will be delighted to see the condition of the glass-spider legs you collected.'The goblins keep smashing the dwarf-lamps. Without them, we cannot safely find our way through the halls and move supplies between the camps we have established throughout Khazad-dûm.

'We either have to find more materials to craft more lamps or find a replacement. The latter may be easier, now that I think of it. I believe we can use bits of glass-spider legs to replace the crystals. In order to do this, though, I will need a great many of those legs.

'If you would, go out and hunt down some glass-spiders and bring me their legs. You can find a good many of the beasts to the west, near The Lost Palace.''I do not believe we can fix the dwarf-lamps without those glass-spider legs. Do not tarry any longer.''Yes, looking at these, they may do well for a shoddy replacement. Thank you for not breaking them into too many pieces.'The leeches infesting the Water-works have grown out of control and are preventing the dwarves from exploring further.Leeches swarm around goblin corpses just to the west of the Rotting Cellar.

Gyrgir would like you to find the corpses the leeches have been feasting upon and spread newt-toxin around them to kill the leeches.Gyrgir is in the Rotting Cellar in north-east Water-works.

Gyrgir will be pleased to hear the leeches will no longer pose a problem to the dwarves.Talk to Gyrgir at the Rotting Cellar'I am not going down to the banks again. Not after what those leeches did to my legs the last time. I have a solution that I believe will get rid of them, but I will not try it.

'If you want to go down to the water and pour this in, you may feel free to do so. There are four places that are particularly bad, all near dead goblins. Those corpses are probably their primary food-source, when they cannot find my legs.

'Head just to the west. You will find the leech-infested water just beneath the Rotting Cellar.''We cannot explore the waters with all those leeches. Take the solution to the places where they gather and pour it into the water.''So you spread it everywhere you saw leeches? Excellent. Hopefully soon it will be safe to explore once more.'Ancient mirrors once reflected light throughout the tunnels of Moria. One of them in the Water-works has been covered with a thick layer of fungus.The fungus-covered mirror can be found just outside the Chamber of Memory, south-east of Hulwul-nefekh.

Thrand believes the acid Ansurr crafted should destroy the fungus covering the mirror.Find the fungus-covered mirrorThe fungus-covered mirror can be found just outside the Chamber of Memory, south-east of Hulwul-nefekh.

Thrand believes the acid Ansurr crafted should destroy the fungus covering the mirror.Thrand is at Hulwul-nefekh in central Water-works.Talk to Thrand at Hulwul-nefekh'Greetings, ${PLAYER}!

'One of the dwarf-mirrors has been covered with the fungus infesting everything down here. No matter what I have tried, I have not been able to get rid of it. Ansurr has been experimenting with a variety of acid he claims he retrieved from the dragonets in the Silvertine Lodes... perhaps you could try using it to clean the mirror?

'The mirror is to the south, just outside the Chamber of Memory. If it works, return to me, but travel with care, the Orcs are lurking about! There is still more to be done!''Use the acid on the mirror. If Ansurr is correct, it should clear the fungus from it.''So, it cleared it away? Good. Interesting that the Orcs would be riled to defend it so.'Bogrian has fled to Zirakzigil with a detachment of her personal guards to search for the entrance to the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar.The passage to Zirakzigil lies west through the gardens, then north.

Folkath has instructed you to prevent Bogrian's expedition from bringing back any potentially valuable or dangerous trophies from the Balrog's remains.Defeat Bogrian's morroval-guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Bogrian's morvul-defilers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bogrian's banner is located among the merrevail detachment on Zirakzigil.

Bogrian may be called out of hiding by using the horns on her banner to summon her forth.Use the horn on Bogrian's banner to summon and defeat herOxi is at Jazârgund, south and east of the entrance to Zirakzigil.

Oxi is awaiting your return and hoping for your success.Talk to Oxi at Jazârgund'Bogrian, the morroval-queen called She-Who-Must-Be-Obeyed by her subjects, has fled with a small, but dangerous detachment of her personal morroval-guards and morvul-defilers to Zirakzigil. 

'It would seem that she has commanded them to guide her to the entrance of the great Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar, in the hopes of forging an alliance with the merrevail who reside there. We cannot allow that expedition to succeed.

'Best of luck, my brave ${RACE}. If you manage to stop Bogrian, report to Oxi at Jazârgund. Do you know the way to Zirakzigil? It is far to the west of here, beyond the gardens of Tharâkh Bazân -- it is quite some distance on foot, but I will allow you to use my goat to travel there quickly.''You have thwarted the will of the winged queen! For this great deed, I will ensure that your name is recorded alongside those of the brave dwarves who have distinguished themselves through their acts of valour here in Khazad-dûm.

'Please, accept my thanks and this reward.''You must think like your enemy, ${PLAYER}! If I have taught you nothing else, I hope you have learned that. What I mean is, these creatures will have taken the high ground, where they will be least vulnerable. I would begin my search at the peak and move down.

'You may use my goat to travel with haste to Zirakzigil, free of charge. May she carry you swiftly.'Gyrgir believes the fungus would rather live in the water than on the Orcs. He wants to study the infestation further.Globsnaga Orcs can be found on the banks near The Chamber of Dark Waters, south of the Rotting Cellar.

Gyrgir wants you to gather fungus-spores from several Globsnaga Orcs. He believes with them, he will be able to learn things important for creating an antidote.Collect fungus-spores from Globsnaga Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gyrgir is in Hulwul-nefekh, west of The Chamber of Dark Waters.

You defeated several Globsnaga Orcs and managed to gather enough fungus-spores for the dwarves to research. You should return to Gyrgir in Hulwul-nefekh and deliver the spores.'I have been talking with Ansurr and studying the cloth you brought back at the Rotting Cellar, and I have come to a conclusion. I believe the fungus would rather be in the water than living on the Orcs.

'The only reason it is on the Orcs is because it cannot get back to the water. If you could bring me back several spores from the infested Orcs, I can study them and learn more, perhaps even prove my theory.

'You can find these infested Orcs near The Chamber of Dark Waters to the east of here.''I believe the spores will unlock everything. I must have several to test my belief.''These are perfect, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for bringing these to me. I am sure they will prove useful.'A powerful lizard has been killing dwarf-messengers. Gyrgir wishes you to lure the lizard out and end him.The lizard-food can be found at The Drowned Deep, west of Hulwul-nefekh.

Gyrgir says that a powerful lizard, Stonecrest, often feeds on grodbog-corpses. He has crafted a powerful poison to sprinkle on the food. Once Stonecrest eats it, Gyrgir believes you may have a chance to defeat it.Gyrgir is in Hulwul-nefekh, east of The Drowned Deep.

Gyrgir will be pleased to know his poison worked and that Stonecrest will devour no more dwarves.'I have boiled down the slime and combined it with several herbs to make a potent powder. It smells very appetizing, but it is a powerful poison.

'Sprinkle it on the lizard-food in The Drowned Deep. At some point, Stonecrest should come looking to feast.

'When it has been weakened, you should be able to defeat it.''That lizard must be dealt with before he kills us all!''So the great lizard has fallen. My brothers are avenged....

'This news brings tears of joy to my eyes. Making sure our travel routes are clear and open is of vital importance, and this is one step in the right direction.'The dwarves of Hulwul-nefekh have many thoughts and ideas about how to best combat the fungus.Ansurr and the other dwarves are at Hulwul-nefekh in central Water-works.

Ansurr has asked you to assist the other dwarves with their ideas about how to defend against the vile growth.Help AnsurrHelp GyrgirHelp ThrandAnsurr is in Hulwul-nefekh in central Water-works.

You should return to Ansurr and inform him you have aided his companions with their ideas.Talk to Ansurr at Hulwul-nefekh'On our way here from the Rotting Cellar, we saw much of the fungus in the Water-works. We need to take swift action to ensure that we are not overwhelmed, and also, we must ensure that the Orcs do not maintain even a small foothold by our water-wheels.

'Speak with the others and do what you can to help them out with their plans. Meanwhile, I have another request of you.''Speak with the others. They have good ideas... but more importantly, they are interested in staying and fighting this accursed affliction.''I thank you for helping them all with their plans. I am sure some did more than others, but they have all proved valuable.

'I believe we are getting close to figuring out how to stop this foul fungus.'Foreman Indrith made his way into the Wheel-house within the Great Wheel of the Water-works. The dwarves of Hulwul-nefekh are concerned that he may need help there.Foreman Indrith is in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel, south-west of Hulwul-nefekh.

Ansurr suggested to seek out Foreman Indrith and aid him however you may.Talk to Foreman Indrith in the Wheel-house'If you are looking for more work in the area of the Great Wheel, I would suggest you find Foreman Indrith. He headed down there some time ago, and rumour has it that he is holed up there. Apparently, the fungus was not reason enough for him to abandon his charge.

'He may require your assistance. He'll probably be within the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel.''Ansurr sent you to aid me? You must be hearty to have made it through the creatures and the fungus. That is good to know, for I have work to do here, and if you are willing to labour hard, I am willing to set you to work.''You may find Foreman Indrith in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel, south-west of Hulwul-nefekh.'The water-wheel assembly in the Water-works is covered with fungus spores and slime.The water-wheel is located at the Great Wheel, south-west of Hulwul-nefekh.

The paddles above the wheel are covered with fungus and slime. For the great wheel to work once more, the paddles must function.Ansurr is at Hulwul-nefekh, north-east of the Great Wheel.

Ansurr will be pleased to know the fungus and slime has been removed from around the water wheel, and it is ready to run once more.Talk to Ansurr in Hulwul-nefekh'I have distilled and purified the acid from the glow-worms into something we can use to great effect. Take this and head back to the water-wheel assembly at The Great Wheel, ${PLAYER}.

'In that area, you will find many small paddles infested with fungus spores and the main paddle covered with slime. For the wheel to work once more, the fungus and slime must be removed.

'Return to me when you are done and tell me the results. It would be a pity if the wheels are damaged beyond repair.''The water-wheel is nearly ready to be restarted. I thank you greatly.

'I know it may seem like nothing, but that wheel is an important part of our efforts to restore the forges of Khazad-dûm.

'I can take it from here. Thank you again.''Without the water-wheel at full capacity, it matters not whether we take the rest of the Deeps.'The Water-works is a site of importance to the dwarves who wish to remain in Moria. One such dwarf, Foreman Indrith, has made it a mission to repair the channel there.Toads and lizards can be found within the Water-works surrounding the Great Wheel.

Foreman Indrith believes that the toads and lizards may be clogging the piping of the Water-works.Defeat toads in the Water-works (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat lizards in the Water-works (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Foreman Indrith can be found in the Wheel-house, beneath the Great Wheel.

You cleared a good many toads and lizards out from the Water-works surrounding the Great Wheel and should now return to Foreman Indrith to inform him of your work.Talk to Foreman Indrith in the Wheel-house'Well now, you can see that this place is in a state unfitting for a dwarf like myself: too many leaks and not enough production. Add to that all the toads and lizards skittering about and... well, I am sure you understand what I mean.

'I suspect that the toads and lizards are being pulled along with the currents and getting stuck in the pipes, gumming them up.

'Do me a favour and thin out their number here and in the Water-works surrounding the Great Wheel, then return to me. We will see if we can get these pipes working as they should.''We have to clear the pipes first, then we can think about getting the Water-works up and running. I already sent a dwarf ahead to examine the workings, but we must keep our attention here for the time being.

'Do your best to rid the area of lizards and toads, and when you think you killed enough, return to me, and we will see if we can get the wheels working correctly again.''Good, good. We can now see if the Great Wheel is ready to turn on its own once more, then set about fixing these leaks.'You must drive away the wing of drakes that have descended upon the Elf-ruins of Pembar from the peak of Zirakzigil. Should you succeed, you will have the blessings of the Elves to make use of the ancient forge within the ruins to empower the infused garnet you bear.Hunt down the younger drakes while avoiding their elder brethren.Defeat Wing-drake hatchlings (${VALUE}/20)Defeat Wing-drake yearlings (${VALUE}/10)The enraged Wing-mother has descended into the courtyard in the centre of the ruins. Confront and defeat her to drive the drakes from the ruins for good.Defeat Rimlúg the Wing-motherUse the ancient forge to empower your imbued garnet.Speak with Perimbant to return to Echad Dúnann.Talk to Perimbant'I daresay what few drakes remain of this flight will not stray far from the peaks of Zirakzigil for some time after this stinging defeat.''Are you ready to return to Echad Dúnann?'You and Bósi have come to a neglected corridor in the Western Deeps, hoping to find an entrance to Nâr-khelab, the Heart of Fire.Bósi is in the passage where he believes the doorway to the Heart of Fire may be found.Talk to BósiBósi is in the passage where he believes the doorway to the Heart of Fire may be found.

Bósi is waiting to speak with you about searching for the doorway.Talk to BósiBósi believes that by hailing or congratulating the memory of the dwarf who built the Heart of Fire, you will gain access to it.Bósi's guess was correct, and you have found the location of the Heart of Fire.Travel with Bósi into the Heart of FireBósi's guess was correct, and you have found the location of the Heart of Fire.Travel with Bósi into the Heart of FireBósi has asked you to investigate the Heart of Fire, looking for Zigilburk, the mithril axe.Search the forges on the leftSearch the forges on the rightSearch the forges in the centreBósi is in the Heart of Fire, looking out over the majestic hidden forges.Talk to Bósi'Thank you for your help with the goblins, and with the gredbyg before them!

'Let us now return to the Chamber of the Cross-roads to tell of our victory, and that the Heart of Fire has been unsealed!''I hope this adventure will not be in vain. To find the legendary forges of Nâr-khelab would work wonders on the hopes and efforts of my people. The chance that the mithril axe Zigilburk might lie within... I cannot describe what a boon that would be.

'Let us proceed, my friend. We are nearing the wall that might very well be hiding the door we seek.''If the Heart of Fire actually exists, I believe it must be behind this wall.

'What were the secret means of opening it that you recovered from Katûb-zahar, ${PLAYER}? Ah, yes! The great blacksmith Ongli desired not to be disturbed, not even by Durin himself, unless by ceremonial gestures of acknowledgement worthy of his station.

'You should <rgb=#FF0000>hail</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>congratulate</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>salute</rgb> him, ${PLAYER}. I hope that we have read the clues aright!''What were the secret means of opening it that you recovered from Katûb-zahar, ${PLAYER}? Ah, yes! The great blacksmith Ongli desired not to be disturbed, even by Durin himself, unless he was greeted with accolades befitting of his station.

'You should <rgb=#FF0000>hail</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>congratulate</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>salute</rgb> him, ${PLAYER}. I hope that we have read the clues aright!''The three mighty forges of Nâr-khelab fill me with awe, ${PLAYER}; I cannot yet bring myself to approach them. Allow me this moment to gaze humbly upon their majesty.

'If you would, please approach each of the three forges and look for the mithril axe Zigilburk. Dare I hope that it might still remain?''You did not find Zigilburk, ${PLAYER}? No, do not apologize -- I should not have let my hopes rise so. It has surely been many hundreds of years since the axe beheld the heat of these forges.

'Let us return to the Chamber of the Cross-roads and tell my people that the Heart of Fire has been found!'You were told of a long played-out mithril-mine within which an ancient smelting-forge lies. Within it, you should be able to lay the basis for the quality you seek. However, a vicious band of Orcs has enslaved their own goblin brethren to eke out the remining tailings from the mine, making it difficult to reach the forge.You must find enough fragments of mithril ore to make proper use of the smelting-forge for the quality. Hopefully, the goblin-slaves have managed to collect enough of the ore for your needs...though they are unlikely to part with it willingly.Collect mithril ore-fragments (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Mine-overseerUse the ancient forge and the mitrhil ore-fragments you have collected to empower your infused garnet.A disciplined war-band of Moria Orcs has taken up residence in one of the old armoury halls and is using it as a training hall in preparation for their next offensive against the dwarves. If you are to reach the old weapons forge within that hall and empower the infused garnet you carry, you shall have to win your way past the Orcs.You must defeat the Orkish recruits before they are prepared to launch their offensive against the dwarves and defeat the Uruk who is overseeing their training.Defeat Orkish recruits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the Uruk Battle-masterUse the ancient forge to empower your infused garnet.The Orcs have not attacked the dwarf-post at the Rotting Cellar in several days. Sylfa fears they are preparing a larger assault and wants you to press the attack while most of the dwarves at the Rotting Cellar advance westward to a new outpost.Orcs may be found in The Chamber of Dark Waters to the south of the Rotting Cellar.

Sylfa has asked you to make a pre-emptive attack against the Orcs while his fellows advance to the west.Defeat Orcs in The Chamber of Dark Waters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ansurr is in Hulwul-nefekh, west of The Chamber of Dark Waters.

You observed that the Orcs you defeated were different than those you had seen throughout Moria, with odd growths covering them. Ansurr should be made aware of this.Talk to Ansurr in Hulwul-nefekh'The Orc-attacks that have come lately have been terrible. We barely beat back the last one a few days ago, and then they suddenly stopped.

'I know we haven't killed them all... I can feel them at night, lurking beyond the torch-light. I fear they are preparing a final assault that will be the doom of us all. We cannot wait for the hammer-fall, ${PLAYER}. We must take the battle to them before they are ready and move from their attack.

'That is where you come in. I want you to take them unaware. Their encampment lies near The Chamber of Dark Waters to the south. While you press the attack, several of my men will move westward to a new outpost. When you have finished, meet Ansurr there.''Keep the Orcs at bay! We do not want to give them an inch with which to launch their own assault.''Thank you for holding them off, ${PLAYER}. You bought us enough time to make our way over here. It's not... ideal, but it will do for now.

'They were covered in some sort of fungus-growth, you say? That must be why they stopped attacking us. Something else attacked them... but what could it be? What could be down there?'The mirror located deep within the Water-works has been twisted and is no longer illuminating the flooded depths.Sylfa is in the Rotting Cellar, on the eastern edge of the Water-works.

Sylfa will be pleased to hear the mirror has been adjusted, and light shines throughout the Water-works, at least for today.Speak with Sylfa in the Rotting CellarYou stand before a mirror deep within the Water-works. It is used to illuminate these flooded depths, but has been twisted out of position. The creatures of the deeps loathe the light it reflects, but that very light is the greatest hope for the expedition. Perhaps shifting its angle will return much-needed light to the Water-works.'Excellent work. I can see the reflected light from here.

'There is much of Khazad-dûm buried beneath the waters here. Without that light, we would never be able to fully map and explore it.'Ansurr has traded arrows with the Orc Urbhrum for several weeks now. Neither have hit their targets, but he has enjoyed the challenge of their nightly duels. He has not seen an arrow for several days and fears his opponent has fallen to the fungus.By the flight of the arrows, Ansurr believes Urbhrum can be found amid the fungus-covered Orcs of the Water-works.

Ansurr has asked you to find and defeat Urbhrum near The Chamber of Dark Waters, east of Hulwul-nefekh.Find and defeat UrbhrumAnsurr is in Hulwul-nefekh, west of The Chamber of Dark Waters.

You should return to Ansurr and inform him of your victory against the infected Urbhrum.Talk to Ansurr at Hulwul-nefekh'Every night at the Rotting Cellar, I used to engage in battle with one of the Orcs of Moria. We would fire our arrows back and forth, listening for the twang of the bow string, searching for our enemy in the dark. It broke the monotony of guard duty, but a dangerous game it was. At rare times we traded taunts -- though we were each careful to move so as not to be discovered -- and I learned this creature's name is Urbhrum.

'Urbhrum had not loosed upon us for several days now, and I fear he has fallen to the fungus. These infected Orcs are unpredictable and dangerous. I do not know what drives them, but an Orc of Urbhrum's skill under the influence of the spore could be a terrible threat.

'Go to The Chamber of Dark Waters, east of here, and seek out Urbhrum. If he is to be found, destroy him, lest his arrows return.''I dare not think what evil Urbhrum may be capable of under the influence of that terrible fungus. Orcs are vile enough creatures to begin with!''The deed is done? That is well. Urbhrum was a dangerous opponent before, but I fear he would have become more so under the influence of the fungus.'Thrand believes the fungus forms into mushrooms growing on the lake. In his opinion, the Orcs must have eaten the mushrooms, and that is what caused them to become infected.Mushrooms can be found around the water's edge to the west of the Rotting Cellar.

Thrand thinks destroying the mushrooms will slow the spread of the fungus into the Orc-population.Destroy mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thrand is in Hulwul-nefekh in central Water-works.

You have destroyed many mushrooms and should now return to Thrand.Return to Thrand in Hulwul-nefekh'I have a fear, ${PLAYER}. We have been using some of the mushrooms around here for cooking with our meals, but I do not think all of them are safe.

'There are some mushrooms down near the water's edge, growing in that tepid pool of fungus. I believe the Orcs have eaten those, and that is what caused them to become infected.

'To deal with this threat -- at least to slow its spread -- I would ask you to go and destroy those mushrooms. While an Orc is still an enemy, it is an easier enemy to kill than one of these fungus-infested creatures.''Destroying those mushrooms should stop the spread of this fungus-infestation. You can find them at the water's edge to the west.''They are destroyed, and that is that. I am glad to know they looked different than the ones around here... we should not have anything to fear from what we have already eaten, but I might be a little more careful about which ones I cook from here on.'The Water-works is a site of importance to the dwarves who wish to remain in Moria. Once such dwarf, Foreman Indrith, has made it a mission to repair the channel there.Kaldi should be in the Vile Maw, west and a little north of the Great Wheel.

Foreman Indrith fears that he may have sent his worker and friend Kaldi to his death. He has sent you to a camp where he believes Kaldi should be.Talk to Kaldi at the entrance to the Vile Maw'I sent Kaldi off to the Vile Maw to open the doors of the channel in preparation for the work to be done there. I have not heard back from him, but I thought that maybe he was just dawdling. Now, I wonder.

'Please, ${PLAYER}, make your way to the Vile Maw, west and a little north of here, and see if Kaldi is still there. I would feel terrible if anything happened to him.

'If he needs help, give it to him!''It is good to know that Indrith is worried about me, though he need not be. Kaldi is no fool, my friend.''I sent Kaldi west to start preparations in the Vile Maw. I had thought it a good idea, but now I am not so certain. Please go and check if Kaldi is still alive and well.'The dwarves believe that they have created a mixture that will destroy the fungus-growth infesting the Orcs and allow them to be easily defeated.Kraibag is somewhere in the Water-works, near The Chamber of Dark Waters, south of the Rotting Cellar.

Ansurr told you to find Kraibag, the most powerful of the infested Orcs, and use the mixture the dwarves gave you on him to determine its effect.Use the mixture on KraibagKraibag is somewhere in the Water-works near The Chamber of Dark Waters, south of the Rotting Cellar.

The mixture appeared to have no effect on Kraibag. He must still be defeated to ensure the safety of the dwarves of the Water-works.Defeat KraibagAnsurr is at Hulwul-nefekh, west of The Chamber of Dark Waters.

Return to Ansurr at Hulwul-nefekh and inform him that even though the concoction they gave you did not work, in fact quite the opposite, you still defeated Kraibag.Talk to Ansurr at Hulwul-nefekh'So we have all discussed the work you did and the effects it has had and believe we have come up with a plan to stop the growth here, keeping it from spreading to the rest of Khazad-dûm.

'We have created a mixture we believe will remove the additional power the fungus-growth is giving the Orcs it has infested. Seek out Kraibag, the most powerful of the infested Orcs. Throw this in his face, and then see if piercing through the growth is easier.

'Do not worry... what could possibly go wrong? Return to me when you have tried this solution.''Find Kraibag and use the mixture on him. We must know if it works... I mean, of course it will work!''I am sure the mixture simply has a delayed effect. Find Kraibag again and kill him while he is still weakened!''So, the mixture only made Kraibag angry, you say? Then perhaps we used a little too much rhubarb. We will tweak it some more and then try again.

'I am confident that with the right balance of spice and punch, with the correct undertone of...'

Ansurr continues to ramble on about making what sounds more like a pie filling than a mixture to battle a fungus such as that infecting the Orcs.The Water-works is a site of importance to the dwarves who wish to remain in Moria. Once such dwarf, Foreman Indrith, has made it a mission to repair the channel there.Water samples can be drawn from the water's edge north-east from the entrance to the Vile Maw.

Kaldi said that since he heard the noises near the Vile Maw, he has not been down to the water. He asked you to make your way there to take a sample for him and provided you with an empty phial.Kaldi is at his little camp outside the Vile Maw.

You should bring the water sample you collected to Kaldi.'When I arrived at the Vile Maw and made my way to the doors, I stopped immediately as I began to push on them. I heard thrashing in the water and unintelligible screams from within. I knew then that there was something alive in there. I was not reared to be a fool, and so I came down here to think.

'While walking along the water's edge, I noticed ooze filtering out of the stone near the water where the drains would push the run-off from within. I came running back here and have not gone near the water since.

'You seem an adventurous sort. Perhaps you would care to take a sample of the water near the edge for me. You will not have to travel far... anywhere to the north-east of here should suffice.''I want to deliver the sample to Foreman Indrith at the Great Wheel. He will know well what to do with whatever we find, of that I am certain.

'Just go down to the water's edge anywhere around this little camp and scoop up some water.''Wonderful! Now there is only one thing left to do.'The Water-works is a site of importance to the dwarves who wish to remain in Moria. One such dwarf, Foreman Indrith, has made it a mission to repair the channel there.Foreman Indrith is at the Great Wheel to the east of the Vile Maw.

Kaldi handed the sample back to you and sent you to speak with Indrith about what is wrong with the water and to find out what should be done at the Vile Maw.Kaldi is at his camp outside the Vile Maw, west of the Great Wheel.

Foreman Indrith did not like what he saw within the water and sent you back to Kaldi with a special message.Talk to Kaldi at the Vile Maw'Now that we have the findings, we can send them on to someone who will know what we should do.

'Make your way east to the Great Wheel and speak with Foreman Indrith. He will be able to tell you if there is anything wrong with the water and how we can best deal with the situation.

'I am afraid something terrible is going on here.''This is grave indeed. It appears that we have found something after all.

'In fact, it seems as though we found the very thing we had hoped we would not find since facing it outside of Khazad-dûm.'

'We must persevere though, ${PLAYER}.''Hurry back to Kaldi and let him know what I have learned.''Hurry now, get that sample to Indrith at the Great Wheel to the east of here.''This is a sample of the water near the Vile Maw?'

He examines the fluid.

'Not good. There is something there, and I think that we need to be cautious about what we do. When you return to Kaldi, tell him that I said it is time for a final foray.

'You should head back to him now at his encampment outside the Vile Maw.'The ancient water-wheels are largely rusted and covered with fungus, impeding their movement.Glow-worms can be found to the north-west, in the Water-works.

Ansurr asked you to gather acid glands from glow-worms. With them, he can fashion an oil to restore the water-wheels.Collect acid-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ansurr is in Hulwul-nefekh, in central Water-works.

Ansurr will be pleased to see you have gathered all of the acid-glands he needs to create his oil.'The sound of the water through the wheels was once so great it nearly hurt to be here, now the water flows through them at barely a trickle. Time and fungus have assaulted the once-great wheels.

'They are decrepit, eaten away by rust and consumed by spores. To bring them to their full potential, they must be cleared of these banes. Search the Water-works and bring me the acid-glands of the glow-worms. Many of these worms have gathered to the north-west. With those glands, I can fashion an oil that will clear away these foul things.

'When you have accomplished this task, return here to me.''That acid will be strong enough to reverse the centuries of damage, I should think.''These will do fine. This will be just enough acid to make exactly what we need, and it looks like you did not get too much on yourself either.

'A fine job, ${PLAYER}.'Sylfa wants to know the extent and scope of the fungus-growth. He fears the water may be the cause of a strange fungus that is spreading through the Water-works.The water of the Water-works is west of the Rotting Cellar.

Sylfa told you to take the white cloth he gave you and dip it in the water of the Water-works.Sylfa is in the Rotting Cellar, east of the Water-works.

You dipped the white cloth strip in the water, and it turned green. You should return it to Sylfa at once.Welcome to the Rotting Cellar, but I would not become too comfortable here. There is a strange fungus spreading throughout these deeps, and it threatens the expedition's success. We are not certain whence it came, but I have a suspicion. I believe the fungus to be spreading through the water. We must know where this growth is coming from.

'Take this cloth strip and dip it in the waters below. If it changes colour, then things are indeed quite bad.

'Return to me with the results.''Hurry up and test that water. You do not want to end up like those Orcs, do you?''So it is in the water. That is disturbing indeed. But perhaps to our advantage.

'I must ponder this information further. Orcs are a tricky foe, but I have never had to fight a fungus-growth like this before.'Thrand has polished the glass-spider legs and prepared them to be placed inside the empty lamp-posts.The empty lamp-posts can be found all over Gabil-munz, south-west of the Rotting Cellar.

Thrand would like you to place the polished glass-spider legs inside the posts to repair them.Thrand is in the Rotting Cellar, north-east of Gabil-munz.

You should return to Thrand and inform him the glass-spider legs worked and the lamp-posts have been repaired.Talk to Thrand in the Rotting Cellar'I have polished up and tinkered with these glass-spider legs as much as I can. There is naught more I can do...either they will work, or we shall be wandering in the dark.

'Unfortunately, I have too much to do here, or I would repair the lamps myself. I will have to leave that task in your capable hands.

'The posts are all over Gabil-munz, south-west of here. Go out there and repair those lamp-posts, then return to me when you are done.''So, they worked! I never doubted my craftsmanship. Never had a doubt.''If those lamps are not repaired, we cannot safely run supplies between the camps.'Águti is curious as to the nature of the wildlife in the Water-works and is looking for someone to help him investigate.Toads, lizards, and spiders can be found all over the Water-works in Moria.

Águti wants to know more about the local wildlife. He asked you to gather samples of the toads, lizards, and spiders of the Water-works.Collect creature samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Águti can be found at the Rotting Cellar camp in the Water-works.

Águti will want to see the samples while they are still fresh, for he hopes to learn from them.'I am curious to know more about what lurks in the depths of the Water-works. I have identified three major forms of creature here: toads, lizards, and spiders -- all of them vile, creeping things.

'I want to know more about them, however, and how we might stem their growth. If you would bring me back some examples of the specimens, I should be able to determine who eats what, and perhaps I can find a way to pit them against each other.

'You can find these creatures all throughout the Water-works. I would like to see these vermin distracted from their appetite for my kinsmen.''Hurry up and bring back those samples. As soon as we can figure out what eats what, we can figure out what we need to kill to remove these creatures from the area.''These samples are exactly what I need to break the mysteries of the Water-works. With these, I can figure out the feeding hierarchy and determine the most effective creature for us to strike.'Águti has determined that the deep-toads are the linchpin to the food-chain in the Water-works.Deep-toads can be found all over the Water-works.

Águti believes that when the toads are killed, the lizards and spiders will fall upon each other for food.Defeat deep-toads (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Águti is in the Rotting Cellar.

Águti will be pleased to hear the deep-toad population has been thinned.Talk to Águti in the Rotting Cellar'I studied the samples you brought me and have determined how we can best thin out everything down here with one simple stroke. The deep-toads are the key to the survival of the lizards and spiders. To strike the deep-toads will be to strike their predators as well.

'How, you ask? The lizards are unaffected by the venom of the spiders, and so the spiders cannot weaken them, making them undesirable prey for the spiders. Also, the lizards have enough cunning to avoid the webs of the spiders. The toads, on the other hand, are nearly mindless in contrast; lizard and spider alike have little difficulty trapping and devouring the toads.

'If you remove the toads, the spiders and lizards will have no choice but to fall upon each other. Will you do this?''If we thin the toads, the rest will kill each other off. I am confident in this!''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. I have faith that soon the creatures in the Water-works will no longer be a threat, and we will be able to retake it with ease.'Mundgeirr knows of an ancient mithril mine containing a smelting forge where you may lay the foundation of the quality you seek to bestow upon your weapon. Unfortunately, a band of particularly savage Orcs has claimed the mine and enslaved their own goblin brethren to work the played-out veins in hope of coming up with a few poor scraps of mithril ore for their masters.Mundgeirr has asked you to bring him an infused garnet with which he may aid you in bestowing a quality upon your weapon. He does not know, however, where to find such a stone.Mundgeirr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria.

Mungeirr has bidden you to talk to him again when you are ready to seek out the forge, but warns you that a vicious band of Orcs and their goblin slaves have taken over the mithril mine.Talk to Mundgeirr to travel to the mithril mineMundgeirr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria.

You should return to Mundgeirr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.'If you are seeking to enhance the abilities of your weapon, there is one place where you are sure to lay the foundation for such a quality. There is an old mithril mine, played-out long ago, but within it was a fine forge with mighty spells laid upon it for the smelting of mithril ore!

'Of course, now the Orcs have it and have set their own goblin brethren to work as slaves trying to eke out a few last sorry bits of the poorest quality ore. I doubt they know anything about the forge itself -- or care in the least -- but you will have to fight your way through them if you want to make use of it.

'Before you dare the mine, however, you should bring me an infused garnet. Only with such a stone will you succeed in enhancing your weapon. I do not know where to find such stone, however.''If you are ready to go, I'm sure the Orcs are as ready as they are likely to be. If you are lucky they will be too busy digging and yelling at each other to notice you wandering through...but it will take quite a lot of luck, I'm afraid.

'Now don't forget, you may need a small bit of that mithril ore yourself if you are going to infuse that garnet properly, so you may need to borrow a bit from the Orcs along the way, if there is any to be had.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Ah! You were able to get your hands upon an infused garnet.

'It will take me some time to prepare the stone. When you are ready to leave for the mine, let me know, and I will return the stone to you.''Ho there! I see you are still in one piece. Excellent, and what's more, you have empowered the garnet! Well done, indeed.

'Let's have that stone, and we will see if we cannot bestow the quality you seek!'Fastarr knows of an ancient anvil where you may craft the heart of the quality you seek for your weapon, but scouts report that the ancient armoury in which it lies has recently been overrun by a well-organized force of Moria Orcs, who are even now training in preparation for their next assault to drive the dwarves from Moria.Fastarr has asked you to bring him an infused garnet with which he may be able to aid you in bestowing a quality upon your weapon. He does not, however, know where to find such a stone.Fastarr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria.

Fastarr has bidden you to speak with him again when you are ready to seek out the old armoury, but warns you that a well-organized band of Moria Orcs has taken control of the hall.Talk to Fastarr to travel to the old armouryFastarr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria.

You should return to Fastarr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.'A well-organized band of Orcs has recently overrun the hall containing the anvil you seek. If you are to reach the anvil, you will have a difficult fight on your hands.

'I can tell you how to reach the hall, but such a journey would be useless until you bring me an infused garnet. Without such a stone, you will not be able to bestow the quality you seek to place upon your weapon.

When you find such a stone, I will prepare it for you and tell you how to reach the ancient hall.''If my scouts are correct, it seems that a particularly brutal Uruk has brought his forces up from the deeper mines and overrun the hall containing the anvil you seek.  It will be no simple task to rout them from their work, but the sooner the better, for they are preparing an assault against us as we speak.

'Are you ready to face the Orcs? If so, then you should be off...time is wasting!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Ah! You have found an infused garnet at last! Now, you will need to bring that to the old armoury, but first I must prepare it.

'When you are ready to depart for the armoury, speak with me again.''So you have returned? Ah, and I see you have brought an empowered garnet. Then you were successful.

'Let us see if that stone will suffice for the quality you desire.'The toads of the Water-works are known to exude a slime that has befuddling qualities.Toads can be found all over the Water-works and to the east of the Great Wheel.

Gyrgir believes with some toad-slime he can create a solution to the lizard problem.Collect toad-slime (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gyrgir is in Hulwul-nefekh in central Water-works.

You should bring the toad-slime you collected to Gyrgir.'I know you are busy aiding Ansurr with the Wheel, but if you can spare a moment, I need aid of my own.

'There is a powerful lizard who keeps killing our messengers. But, I have a plan on how to get rid of him! The first part involves toad-slime.

'The slime off the toads here in the Water-works has powerful befuddling qualities. If you bring me some, I can turn it into a powder we can use against the lizards.''Without that slime we cannot hope to get rid of the lizards.''Excellent. Once I add a couple of spices from my stores, this will be exactly what we need.'You have discovered the torso of the statue of Helgi Goblinbane.Águti is at the Rotting Cellar to the north.

Águti will want to know you found a piece of the shattered statue.Talk to Águti in the Rotting CellarThis is a piece of the torso of the statue of Helgi Goblinbane that once stood outside of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

The goblins of Durin's Way destroyed the statue, and its parts can be found scattered throughout Moria. A dwarf named Uxi endeavours to reassemble this statue.'I have heard of the dwarf Uxi's endeavour to reassemble Helgi Goblinbane's great statue! So the statue's torso was nearly lost to the flooded depths? I am glad you came when you did.

