You should speak with Mögr.'Welcome, welcome! Is not the Twenty-first Hall the grandest sight in all of Khazad-dûm?

'We have encountered no dangers here whatsoever, and I take this to be a sign that the dwarves have won Zelem-melek. We have established a great foothold here, and you are just in time for the celebration.

'If you would be so kind, please distribute ale to the fine dwarves who have done such great work here. They have earned it!''Foreman Mögr has sent us ale? How thoughtful! If he is confident that this hall is secure, then so am I. Pour me a drink, ${CLASS}!''I do not need my wits about me for this easy post. Guard-duty in this hall is nothing -- not an enemy in sight!''Ale from Foreman Mögr? Now?

'Is it really so safe that I can drink ale while on watch? Well, I suppose if the foreman thinks it is, then there can be no harm in it.''Hm, well now. I was about to set to repairing the scaffolding, but I suppose that can wait, eh?

'Pour me a glass of that ale, friend.''Ale from Mögr, while I am tasked with repairs? Well, I suppose there can be no harm in it. What's the rush, anyhow?''Celebrations already! That is grand news. I was not aware that we had made such great strides here, but I will take this as a sign of success! Thank you, ${PLAYER}, and give the foreman my thanks as well.''By Durin's beard, what is Foreman Mögr about? No ale for me, thank you. I must stay sharp.

'Is that fool of a dwarf letting down his guard already? While it is true that there have been no intrusions upon our work here, and that we make great progress, I do not believe Zelem-melek is safe yet.''Phooh! Phooh! Reinn is clever, to be sure, but he always spoils everything with his zeal for over-caution.'Foreman Mögr, frustrated by Reinn's obstinance about the security of Zelem-melek, wishes to prove to you that the Twenty-first Hall is as safe as can be.The Twenty-first Hall is an enormous pillared hall covering northern Zelem-melek.

