'Thank you ${PLAYER}. This blow will leave them quite vulnerable.'Orcs infest the long, winding passages of Khazad-dûm, but a greater threat has arisen: the Globsnaga, Orcs infested by a vile fungus.Defeat Globsnaga in MoriaYou have defeated a great number of the Globsnaga, the fungus-infested Orcs of Moria, and still you remain standing, having resisted the disease that wreaths these foes. They must be destroyed to the last, for the plague they bear is a perilous invention of the Enemy.Defeat Globsnaga in MoriaYour tireless work against the goblins has been a great help to the dwarves of Moria, but it is oft said that where one falls, two will come forth to take its place. Goblins should be destroyed whenever they are encountered, for they are evil to the very core and spread evil wherever they go.Defeat goblins in MoriaGreat insects, the gredbyg, have been drawn to the vast dark of Moria like moths to a flame. They lurk in the gloom, ready at any time to ambush travellers unlucky enough to be caught at unawares upon the ever-turning paths.Defeat gredbyg in MoriaNow that some cleansing has been done against the vile insects of Moria, the effort must be ever maintained. Gredbyg do not ever truly leave a place, but their numbers should be quelled, lest the caves are overrun once more. To prevail against the gredbyg of Moria will be a tireless task.Defeat gredbyg in MoriaDefeat half-orcs in Eregion.Defeat half-orcs in EregionDefeat many half-orcs in Eregion.Defeat half-orcs in EregionYou found a missing piece from the statue of Helgi Goblinbane -- the top of his head.Simbi is in the Twenty-first Hall.

You have found a piece of the shattered statue of Helgi Goblinbane, and should bring it to a dwarf who will deliver it to Uxi.Bring the statue-piece to Simbi in the Twenty-first HallYou have discovered the top of the head from the statue of Helgi Goblinbane.'What's this now? The helm from a Helgi Goblinbane statue! Hammer and tongs, he was in many of my favourite stories when I was but a young dwarf! The Tale of Helgi's Hammer... Goblinbane's Gilded Helm... The Lay of the Goblin-rout... Helgi and the Maiden's Beard-ribbons! Ah, such fine tales!

'I have heard that Uxi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads endeavours to find and reassemble all of the pieces of the statue. I will have this delivered to him at once.'The dwarves of the Upper Levels expeditions will need a great deal of help in overcoming the obstacles that await them in the Mines of Moria. Your assistance will be welcome, for there is much work to be done if Khazad-dûm is to be hospitable once more.NOT USEDComplete quests in the Upper Levels of Moria.Complete quests in the Upper LevelsFollow the path of the Fellowship through Moria.NOT USEDThe threshold of the western gate of Khazad-dûm, it was here that Durin completed his legendary journey through the heart of the mountains and came once again into the light of the sun, having discovered the place that would become his people's home for ages to come.This ancient guard room controls the passages leading up into Durin's Way, as well as the ones east, towards the Twenty-first Hall. It is now occupied by part of the dwarf-expedition to reclaim Moria from the Orcs and goblins who now hold sway.The Twenty-first hall is among the largest in all of Khazad-dûm, and often regarded as the most famous. In times long past a great market stood here where the Dwarves of Moria and travellers from abroad would trade in fine goods from across much of Middle-earth. Fine woods and wine and foodstuffs would be exchanged for gold and priceless gems and finely wrought pieces of smith-craft. In truth nearly anything at all could be bought or sold within this very hall, though it is hard to imagine it to look upon it now.It is likely that the Chamber of Mazarbul once served some great ceremonial purpose in the old days of Moria; now it remains the tomb of Balin, son of Fundin and friend to old Bilbo, who, not so many years ago, led an expedition much like the current one to retake Moria and restore it to the glories of old.Find the Bridge of Khazad-dûm (west arch)Find the Bridge of Khazad-dûm (east arch)The First Hall was the original entrance to Khazad-dûm, where Durin first set foot in the caverns that would one day become the greatest city of the dwarves, and indeed the most enduring city of any people in the long history of Middle-earth, until at last it fell into ruin.Dómárr has discovered some unpleasant business in the Great Hall of Durin, and he believes that he can offer proof that Zelem-melek is extremely vulnerable.Dómárr and Reinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.Talk to DómárrDómárr and Reinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.Listen to Reinn and DómárrDómárr and Reinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.Talk to DómárrDómárr and Reinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.Listen to the dwarves' discussionDómárr can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.

You should speak with Dómárr.Talk to Dómárr'I should be glad to tell fellow travellers my tale of woe as I passed this way! You should heed my tale, and beware.''Here they are -- the evil Orcs of Gazatu-ru, worshipping the lord of Mordor! Be careful, now. Hide yourself well!''Good for Reinn! Perhaps now the Twenty-first Hall will be properly prepared to be a force to be reckoned with in Zelem-melek.

'It would be a travesty to lose the footing they have gained there, simply because the foreman is blind to the dangers.''Let us return to camp, ${PLAYER}. This is no place to linger about, and I must gather my thoughts. Perhaps something can be done about these Orcs.'You found an ancient map among the remains of Balin's Camp. It contains instructions for making a very strange and special torch.Dwarves can be found in the Twenty-first Hall, west of Balin's Camp.

