'Kafli was friends with many on this expedition, and they are stationed from the Hollin Gate to the ruins of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm. Will you honour Kafli's memory with them, by quaffing a good ale with each of them where they are staying at most of the major encampments of my people throughout the Mines?''Ho there, ${PLAYER}! Raise a glass to my fallen cousin!''Ah, I remember Kafli well. He will be missed... when we were but little dwarves together, I remember once he hid from me a gem I'd mined myself, with my own little pick, which I prized above all my other possessions, until I apologized to another child that I had insulted. I took years to fully forgive him....''O, what a grievous day! I am moved... I shall write an epic ode to the memory of Kafli!''Let us all salute Kafli! To the memory of the bravest dwarf I know!''Kafli died as he lived, brave and faithful to the lovely Finna. May all of us find in our lives the happiness theirs held!''I met him in passing several times. He was a good craftsman... he could hoist a tankard with the best of us.''Kafli's passing will be long mourned, and his life's story sung until I too pass, or may my beard be cut from my face.''Poor Finna! I pity the messenger who delivers this news. I don't suppose you're going to the Lonely Mountain...? No, that would have been too easy, I suppose. Ah, well. To Kafli! Let us hoist a tankard in his memory!''You did not know him as long as we, but you proved yourself a stouthearted friend to Kafli.

'It will be through the noble actions of people like yourself, willing to both fight for the future and respect the traditions of the past, that the glory of Khazad-dûm will once more be sung throughout the world!'The gredbyg were once confined to the edges of this cavern, but the hive has grown exponentially into the impressive size you see today. There must be a source of heat nearby that helps the gredbyg to grow their larvae and cocoons so quickly.You seek the heat source helping the grodbog hive to incubate their young so quickly. It is likely found on the far side of the grodbog hive.Find the heat source helping the grodbog hiveYou heard a noise when entering the Flaming Deeps from the Redhorn Lodes, coming from around the corner to the right.Check out the noise around the corner to the rightYou found the heat source helping the grodbog hive, and sadly there is nothing that can be done to stop it. The hive has been built in the perfect location in Moria, to benefit from the natural heat production of the mines.Check out the noise around the corner to the right'The hive formations in this cavern have never been this large, and must be incubating an immense population of gredbyg! They always lived in the nooks and crannies here, but recently their growth has downright exploded. You can see from here, the ceiling and walls are covered in cocoons and larvae! There must be a heat source helping to incubate all those eggs so quickly.

'Perhaps you could seek out this heat source? If we find out where the heat comes from, we may be able to do something about it.'The heat is coming from the boiling oil pools and lava pools in The Flaming Deeps. There is nothing that can be done to stop it from helping the grodbog hive incubate their young....

But there appears to be an injured dwarf hiding among the rocks up ahead. You should see if he needs help.The gredbyg outside the Orc-watch camp chitter and screech during the night, keeping the dwarves from sleeping.The gredbyg can be found to the south-west of the Orc-watch.

Kúli has asked you to defeat the gredbyg which are driving him mad with their chittering.Defeat gredbyg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kúli is alone at a camp far to the south-east of the Orc-watch, in a cavernous corridor between the Redhorn Lodes and the Flaming Deeps.

Kúli will be pleased to know the chittering gredbyg have been silenced.Talk to Kúli'That incessant chittering never seems to stop. I cannot get any sleep, no matter how many pillows I stack over my head. Please, for my sanity, make them stop.

'The gredbyg are most prolific to the south-west of here. Destroy them! I cannot abide the noise any longer!''Praise Durin, they are quieted. Thank you, for tonight I shall sleep in peace.''The infernal noise gets so loud you cannot even think.'The gredbyg in the grodbog hive in the southern tunnel of Redhorn Lodes chitter and screech. The number of voices can be heard for miles, and it's amazing that all of Moria doesn't buzz with the sound.The grodbog warriors can be found throughout the grodbog hive which takes up the entire cavernous corridor between the Redhorn Lodes and the Flaming Deeps.

The droning noise from thousands of gredbyg is heard throughout most of Moria, but it's so constant most are unaware of it.Defeat grodbog warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The imposing grodbog hive takes up the entire cavernous corridor between the Redhorn Lodes and the Flaming Deeps.

The droning is still painfully loud throughout the hive, but will be noticeably quieter in other parts of Moria.CompletedThe droning noise of thousands of gredbyg voices is enough to drive anyone mad. The incessant chittering never seems to stop. The voices need to be silenced. The largest gredbyg, the grodbog warriors, are responsible for the loudest of the chittering.The grodbog hive is quieter, for now, and the droning that remains is almost... tolerable.The newly infected spiders and Orcs seem to follow a new master once they're turned into their mutated forms. Chaos can be frightening, but when one sees order when they expect chaos, it can be even more terrifying.The leader of the infected Orcs should be among his minions to the south-east of Knakk's camp, as well as the Queen lurking among her brood to the east.Find a leader among the infected OrcsFind a leader among the infected spidersKnakk is camped on the elevated walkway in the north-east corner of Redhorn Lodes.Return to Knakk'The spiders and Orcs corrupted by the infesting fungus seem to change behaviour once turned. One would expect them to act chaotic and attack anything around them, even turn on each other in their confusion. However, once infested they seem to simply change allegiance, as if they immediately begin following new orders. Is something controlling them once they turn?

'Please explore the affected area and see if you can find a leader among newly infected spiders and Orcs.''It didn't take long for the organizers of this corruption to convert enough creatures for a small army. The fungus seems symbiotic in nature. It somehow allowed the leaders you killed to control them. This infecting fungus is extremely dangerous.

'I hope that's the last time we see those horrors come out of the Foundations of Stone!'The sad news of Nykr's passing must be delivered to his next of kin, a dwarf by the name of Kúli, who is studying spider behaviour.Kuli is at the Chittering Hole, south-east of the Orc-watch.

Róarr asked you to find Kúli at the Chittering Hole and deliver to him the news of Nykr's death.Talk to Kúli at the Chittering Hole'This will not be easy news to deliver to Nykr's next of kin. I would do so myself, but my duties here prevent me from leaving.

'I suppose you will have to do it! There is much honour in performing this duty.

'His cousin Kúli is, as Kafli mentioned, the only member of Nykr's kin that I can think of who came with us to the Mines. You will likely find him to the south-east, at the Chittering Hole, studying the creatures there.''Aye, friend ${CLASS}? How may I be of service?

'Nykr dead! Alas, that is a tragedy beyond bearing. He was friend to many, reliable, kind...it will not be easy to spread this sad news.''Kuli is out studying the creatures at the Chittering Hole.'The sad news of Kafli's passing must be delivered to his next of kin, a dwarf by the name of Kúli, who is camped near the grodbog hive and is seeking ore and riches in the southern caverns of the Redhorn Lodes.Knakk's goat is standing near Knakk.

Knakk's goat can take you safely to Kúli's camp near the grodbog hive in the southern cavern of the Redhorn Lodes.

Knakk asked you to find Kúli and deliver to him the news of Kafli's death and ask him to translate the ancient dwarf-text found within the locket.Take Knakk's goat to Kúli's camp to speak with him about the locket'This will not be easy news to deliver to Kafli's next of kin. His cousin Kúli is the only member of Kafli's family that I can think of who came with us to the Mines. You will likely find him to the south-west, searching for long-lost riches and ore-deposits. He may also be able to make out what this ancient text says inside the locket.

'Here, take my goat. He can take you safely to Kúli's camp in southern Redhorn Lodes.''Kafli's dead! Alas, that is a tragedy beyond bearing. He was friend to many, reliable, kind... it will not be easy to spread this sad news. We will send our condolences to Finna.

'Can I see that locket, which you said may have lead to his death? Aye, you and Knakk are right: there are ancient runes inscribed in here. It describes a dwarf mining company of old who found the original deposits of mithril. This says the mining company had a structure somewhere around here, but could it still exist?'The Moria Orcs have mined the Redhorn Lodes ever since the dwarves were wiped out of Moria. Recently, around the time the dwarves returned, so too did the White Hand Orcs. The White Hand aggressively wrestled a large territory from the Moria Orcs, and both are competing for control of the best mining location in all of Moria.Ore is being gathered by both tribes of Orcs in large quantities in the central area of the large Redhorn Lodes cavern.Recover ore from White-hand Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Recover ore from Moria Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the ore samples back to Róarr, camped at the bottom of the stairs on the way up to Orc-watch.Return to Róarr'Those blasted Orcs are stealing our ore! It's intolerable to see them stealing what should be ours. Dwarves found and built this mine first! 

'I wonder what they're finding in the veins they've tapped into? It's one thing if they're smelting forms of iron or steel, but another thing entirely if they've managed to find mithril! 

'Snatch ore from their dead Orc-fingers! It would be best to obtain ore from both tribes of Orcs to see what they've found.''Ok, good. Both of these samples are common iron found throughout Moria. They haven't found anything special, yet. But the good stuff is definitely here somewhere, I can feel it. My sense for mithril may be dulled by our long stay in Orc-watch, but it's not gone completely!'The mirror in the Redhorn Lodes is constantly being knocked out of alignment by the White Hand Orcs dominating the mine.Auti is camped just north of the grodbog hive, west of the mirror, in the southern cavern of Redhorn Lodes.

Auti will be pleased to hear that the mirror in the Redhorn Lodes has been re-aligned.Talk to Auti near the grodbog hiveThe mirror in the Redhorn Lodes, used to reflect the light and illuminate the mine, has been knocked out of alignment, likely by the Orcs who roam there. The dwarves will have difficulty exploring safely if they cannot see.'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for fixing the mirror. Now I can see, at least until those blasted Orcs knock it out of alignment again.'The Forgotten Treasury houses a good deal of wealth discovered or mined in Moria in the elder days. Seeing that these remnants of the past are maintained for the dwarves is a duty worth undertaking.The Forgotten Treasury is in Menem-berej, directly south of the Deep Descent. 

You should search the Orcs and any spoiled ruins for relics or coins of the Forgotten Treasury. Hafberg would prefer that you not unearth any that may still be lying about untouched.'If you are travelling into the Forgotten Treasury, as I expect you are, I would ask that you take the time to see that any relics or coins already taken out of the place are returned to us here. We would not like to disturb anything that is still intact within the treasury itself, but anything already spoiled by the Orcs should be returned to us here.

'Should you find anything befitting, I would ask that you collect these items from within the Treasury and return them here to me at the Deep Descent.

'The Forgotten Treasury lies to the south of here.''Ah, so many already taken. When we found the Forgotten Treasury upturned by the Orcs, some wanted to treat it as a tomb.

'I prefer that we be wise about preserving what we can of the past. Your efforts in this will help us do that.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Knakk and Kafli headed East when the dwarf-fellowship parted ways at the base of the stairs from Orc-watch. They deemed the Orcs only a bump in the road and that they could find a path through Orc-territory and make camp on the far side of the Redhorn Lodes.The two dwarves, Knakk and Kafli, should be found somewhere to the east, around or beyond the Orcs' territory.

You have been asked to find the dwarves Knakk and Kafli.Knakk must have kept going after Kafli fell to the Orcs, but probably is not far away. He surely would not have wanted to leave his friend behind....Find Knakk'Our fellowship from Orc-watch didn't make it far before parting ways. We camped here for a night, then arguments broke out about what we should do next with ranks of Orcs in the way. The two dwarves who headed to the southern caverns were well-prepared, but the two who headed east -- straight into the Orcs' territory -- have me concerned. Please, ${PLAYER}, can you look for them and make sure that they made it where they were going?

'They went straight into the middle of the Orcs' territory, believing there was a safe road between those Orc-tribes' encampments.'Clutched in this dwarf's cold, rigid hand is a beautifully hand-carved locket. After fiddling with it, you have come to realize that it is not a normal locket and will not easily open. This should be taken to this fallen dwarf's companion, who probably kept going without him and should be somewhere to the east.'Kafli and I tried to sneak past the Orcs... and we almost made it here! I think it was that necklace he was holding that gave him away. It was pretty shiny.

'I told him when we left the fellowship's camp that he should hide it in a pocket or something, but he refused, thinking something would snatch it from him while his hand was not on it. I cannot believe he lost his life for that thing.'Crystals have been discovered in Moria, bearing marks of the Forgotten Treasury, a sealed vault hiding a substantial amount of wealth. This discovery has piqued the interest of some dwarves who now wish to uncover the vault and save its contents from the pilfering Orcs.Skûm and Urauth were last seen near the Forgotten Treasury, south and south-east of the Deep Descent in Moria. 

Hafberg told you of the twin trolls, Skûm and Urauth, alike in every way, and how they terrorize the dwarves in the area. You were asked to defeat them should you find yourself facing them.Defeat SkûmDefeat UrauthHafberg is at the Deep Descent, north and north-west of the Forgotten Treasury.

After a long and difficult battle, you defeated the twin trolls to avenge the dwarves who fell to their cruelty.Return to Hafberg at the Deep Descent'You must be the ${RACE} that Falgir has been going on about. I suppose you do have the look of an adventurer, though you seem a little soft around the middle. Ha!

'He tells me you mean to enter the Forgotten Treasury to the south and south-east of the Deep Descent. If you do, I wanted to warn you about the troll-twins, Skûm and Urauth.

'They are quite alike in temperament, it is said. Some of our company have come across them at times, but few ever survive. Should you find yourself facing them, I will be greatly in your debt if you would deal with them once and for all. Our scouts last saw them in the area where the Forgotten Treasury was found, south and south-east of our location here in the Deep Descent.''This news brightens me with newfound hope. Still, I cannot forget all the pain that those two monsters have caused.

'You did well, though, ${PLAYER}. It appears that my hope was not misplaced at all.''Have you met the twin trolls yet, friend?'Ingifast believes that the White Hand Orcs can be frightened off if they are confronted with the remains of the previous expedition.The White Hand expedition was exploring the Claw Hollow, to the south-east of the Orc-watch.

Ingifast has instructed you to locate the remains of the previous expedition and bring them back in the bag he supplied.Collect White Hand armourCollect the tattered White Hand bannerCollect the White Hand leg-boneCollect the White Hand skullIngifast is at the Orc-watch, north-west of the Claw Hollow.

Ingifast will be eager to see the remains you collected of the previous White Hand expedition.'Those orders you took off that foul Orc have proven very interesting, ${PLAYER}. The signatory, this  person, does not seem to care whether or not the expedition sent previously is dead -- only whether they dared defect or desert.

'I think we can send these Orcs home, fearing the dark of the Mines! No, not fear of us...fear of those creatures in the higher levels, the merrevail.

'Look for the remains of that doomed expedition to the south-east, at the Claw Hollow. There should be bits and pieces left -- here, take this bag to keep them together and bring it back when you have found a few remnants that the other White Hand Orcs will be able to unmistakably recognize.''I suggest you start looking around the Claw Hollow, ${PLAYER}.''Ah, you have returned! May I see what you found?

'A skull, a leg-bone...I'm not sure this will be -- ah, a banner! That's more like it! And this armour...yes, wonderful finds, ${PLAYER}. This should be just right for the next step in my plan.'The eastern side of the Redhorn Lodes is infested with some kind of fungus, and the spiders are playing a role in it. The spread is occurring at an alarming rate....The fungal spiders are found in the north-east corner and eastern side of the Redhorn Lodes.Kill a globsnaga spiderThe fungal spiders are found in the north-east corner and eastern side of the Redhorn Lodes.Collect fungus samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Knakk is camped on the elevated walkway in the north-east corner of Redhorn Lodes.

Knakk will be happy to study the samples you've collected of the fungus. He will have to pull himself away from the locket puzzle to analyze it.Return to KnakkThe fungal spiders are spreading spores from their mutations. The fungus growing on them seems to have twisted these spiders into something quite different. It would be good to collect a few samples and bring them back to Knakk for further study.'I've made progress on this locket's puzzle, but I need to put it down and could use a distraction.

'Woh, this sample you brought me is unlike anything I've seen before. It's an aggressively growing fungus. I swear, this stuff could probably grow in or on anything. After seeing what this can do, I'm worried about my health by handling it, and will dispose of what you brought me. Be careful going back there, and spending much time around this stuff....'Crystals discovered in Moria, bearing marks of the Forgotten Treasury, have piqued the interest of some dwarves who now want to excavate the location and save its contents from the pilfering Orcs within Moria.Garthar is in the Deep Descent of Moria.

Falgir confided in you about the discovery of crystals thought long lost, now turning up all throughout Moria. He has asked you to speak with Garthar to see if he can shed some light on the matter.Talk to Garthar in the Deep DescentFalgir is in the Deep Descent in Moria.

Garthar told you a bit of history of the vaults in Moria, what they held and how he fears that one such vault is breached. He now wishes you to tell Falgir what you have learned.Talk to Falgir at the Deep Descent'A moment of your time if you would, friend.

'When first we entered this place, we had no intention of pushing as far as we did so quickly. Now that we have breached this far down into the depths and we see the horror of what transpired here, there are some discoveries that make many of us uncomfortable.

'It is bad enough to know that there are Orcs and goblins all about, but to think that they have breached some of our most hallowed and secret holds... gives one reason to hoist a hammer and crack some goblin-skulls. Still, we have orders and we must abide them, lest we endanger everything we attempt here.

'My friends Garthar and Hafberg are concerned about some discoveries we've been seeing as of late. Crystals, dull and black-looking -- more like glass than crystals -- have been turning up here and there, and we do not know what this signifies. Speak with my friend Garthar, if you would, and see what he knows.''Garthar is a knowledgeable fellow. He will have more to tell you about these crystals.''Aye, these crystals bear the mark of the great dwarf treasury long forgotten beneath this place. Mithril may well have been the true wealth of Moria, but it was not the only wealth we knew here. There were many riches to be harvested from these mines.

'Anything that was not mithril was taken to treasuries throughout Moria and there stored for safe-keeping. Complex puzzles guarded the treasure therein, and now they are well-hidden by the ingenuity of the dwarves.

'I also know that one of our treasuries was recently breached by enemies. Our orders bid us to stay here, surely for our own safety, but I have a good mind to disobey. Alas, I have no more news to share, but feel free to tell Falgir all that I have said.''I have no more to tell you. Return to Falgir; you must have seen him before. He is here in the Deep Descent.''Garthar thinks that the vault is breached, does he? Well then, that makes decisions more obvious, if you ask me.

'Are you still looking for a bit of work?'Crystals have been discovered in Moria, bearing marks of the Forgotten Treasury, a sealed vault hiding a substantial amount of wealth. This discovery has piqued the interest of some dwarves who now wish to uncover the vault and save its contents from the pilfering Orcs.The Forgotten Treasury lies to the south and south-east of the Deep Descent.

Falgir has asked that you kill Orcs and goblins between the Deep Descent and Forgotten Treasury to ready yourself for the task of liberating the vault. He also asked you to collect scraps of material from the Orcs and goblins.'If you are to enter the vault of the Forgotten Treasury, we must prepare you for what you are to face. It is located to the south and east of here, though more southerly than east.

'Between our hold and your destination are many Orcs. These Orcs are likely a smaller, stupider breed than the ones you will encounter inside the Treasury, for it would take cunning enemies to enter such a protected place.

'It would do you well to hunt the lesser Orcs for a short while; this will give me time to prepare you for the adventure. Head south-east and south of here and collect a bundle of scraps from these Orcs, then return to me when you have enough.''Good work! These certainly came from good strong Orcs, which means that you must be ready for the fight ahead. I will tell you all I know, then send you to speak with Garthar and Hafberg, for they, like myself, have tasks within the vault.'Nud-heden will never be recovered until the grodbog-queen is struck down.The grodbog-queen in Nud-heden is laying eggs and nurturing larvae. She is creating a swarm to protect herself, while she continues to breed unharmed.

You should defeat the grodbog-queen in Nud-heden.Defeat the grodbog-queenThe grodbog-queen in Nud-heden is laying eggs and nurturing larvae. She is creating a swarm to protect herself, while she continues to breed unharmed.

You should defeat the grodbog-queen in Nud-heden.Defeat the grodbog-queenThe grodbog-queen in Nud-heden is laying eggs and nurturing larvae. She is creating a swarm to protect herself, while she continues to breed unharmed.

You should defeat the grodbog-queen in Nud-heden.The grodbog-queen is defeatedWhile the grodbog-queen still lives, dwarves will never reclaim their honourable home of old. She must be struck down. Only then will this place be left in peace.Nud-heden now has a chance to be claimed by something other than gredbyg. Will dwarves once again call this home?

Khazad-dûm will not be restored to glory all at once, but stone-by-stone, it will shine once more.The remains you brought to Ingifast yielded some useful items to help him stage the next step in his plan.The crate is near the Chittering Hole, south-east of the Orc-watch.

Ingifast wants you to place the bag containing the remains of the previous White Hand expedition on a raised surface, such as a crate, near a patrol-route often used by White Hand scouts.Do not be seen by the White Hand scoutsIngifast is at the Orc-watch, north-west of the Chittering Hole.

Ingifast will be pleased to hear the evidence has been placed on the crate for the scout to find.Talk to Ingifast in the Orc-watch'The next step in my plan is a challenge. A White Hand scout has a patrol-route that runs along the edge of the Chittering Hole...they are distrusting of the insects there. There are a few crates near that place, and I want you to leave the evidence you collected on one of them -- the whole bag, yes...because it's more visible and off the ground, that's why!

'The important part is not to be seen! It's vital that the Orcs think one of the other scouts left it -- or better yet, play upon their superstitious nature. There are many things within the Mines that they view with near-worshipful fear.

'Head south-east to the Chittering Hole and find the crate. Place the bag upon it, and remember...do not kill the scout!''The plan progresses apace, thanks to you!''You will have to place the bag in plain sight, without being seen and without warning the White Hand Orcs through the deaths of their scouts.'The Orc-tribes compete for the vast riches of the Redhorn Lodes. Each tribe is likely to gather information about the other in order to gain the upper hand.The scouting report is hidden in each tribe's camp.

Each tribe has been scouting the other's defences, locations of strategic points, and general mining operations.Find the Moria tribe reportFind the White Hand tribe reportIngifast's camp is on the stairs near Orc-watch.

Ingifast will be pleased to see the reports that you have gathered.You found a report about the other Orc-tribe. This is a vital piece of information, as it is a good record of the strengths and weaknesses of their tribe. The Dwarves of Orc-watch will find this invaluable.'These scouting reports are mostly drawings and are very useful. This will surely help us dismantle the power struggle of these Orcs. 

'There are a few words written here that I cannot understand. I will bring these to Orc-watch or Twenty-first Hall to have someone familiar with Orkish text to translate for me.'The White Hand Orcs stormed into the Redhorn Lodes and ravaged the Moria Orcs enough to hold a larger territory in very little time. The long-standing Moria Orcs were content and unchallenged for some time, but this cannot fully explain why the White Hand had so much success against them.White Hand Orcs can be found in the northern region of the Redhorn Lodes.

Ingifast has asked you to collect a few pieces of White Hand Orc armour, to help determine why they are superior in their struggle with the Moria Orcs for sole control of the Redhorn's bountiful resources.Collect White Hand helms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Knakk is located on the elevated platform just north of the White Hand Orcs' encampment, on the road towards the Grand Stair.

Knakk will assess the helmets and send them back to Ingifast, who will be pleased to see all the White Hand helms that you claimed as trophies.'It's clear that the invading White Hand is stronger than the Orcs of Moria. I am not convinced that tactics alone are why they are so easily winning the struggle for the Redhorn Lodes. My sneaking suspicion is they have been taught better smithing techniques and may be winning an arms race with the Moria Orcs.

'We found out they are both collecting iron. But maybe the White Hand is able to refine the iron better, or possibly knows how to produce steel?

'Defeat White Hand Orcs to collect a few pieces of their armour. I would like to inspect their pieces for quality and make and see if my suspicions are correct.''These White Hand helms seem to be made of steel! But while the White Hand Orcs seem to have basic skills in steel-making, the helmets are not of very high quality. However, even low quality steel is far superior to the iron equipment the Moria Orcs have been making.

'I have never heard of Orcs working with steel before, so what could this mean? It raises a lot of questions about the White Hand....

'The White Hand's skill in smelting and smithing is impressive for Orcs. I'll send word of this news back to Ingifast as soon as I can.'You have helped Mögr in Zelem-melek, and he has received word that the Orc-watch in the Redhorn Lodes is in need of aid as well.Avar is in the Orc-watch in the Redhorn Lodes, a long ways from the Twenty-first Hall through the many winding passages of Zelem-melek.

Mögr has invited you to ride a goat to the Redhorn Lodes if the journey is too difficult on foot.Talk to Avar at the Orc-watch (a goat is available for travel, for the journey is difficult)'Had enough of Zelem-melek, have you? Well, you will always be welcome in the Twenty-first Hall, ${PLAYER}, for the services you did us.

'There is a goat waiting in the stable that already knows the way there, if you do not wish to take your chances on the road. It is a difficult journey to the Orc-watch....''Ah, greetings to you, ${RACE}. Welcome to the Orc-watch. We are certainly in need of aid, if that is why you are here.'What was so special about this locket that to make it worth dying for?The Orc Watch is the main Iron Garrison settlement in the Redhorn Lodes, located on the western side of that area.

There are many dwarves at the Orc-watch. Perhaps one of them knows why the recently deceased Nykr valued this little hand-made locket so highly.Clutched in this dwarf's cold, rigid hand is a beautifully hand-carved locket. After fiddling with it for a little while, its puzzle reveals itself, and it swivels open to show two tiny engravings: two bearded dwarf-faces.'I'm afraid I don't recognize that. Sorry.''That is a wonderful little trinket. 

'No, I can't help you; I've never seen it before.''Welcome, ${CLASS}! How may I...where on earth did you get that locket? Speak up!''I do not know what is so special about that locket, that Nykr would die for it. Perhaps someone at the Orc-watch will know.'You obtained a locket from Kafli, who had fallen to the Orcs. You brought this locket to his closest friend, Knakk, the fellow travelling with him.  Knakk is trying to determine what was so special about this locket to make it worth dying for.Knakk is camped close to the Grand Stair and is trying to figure out the puzzle of a locket which Kafli was holding when he died. 

He thinks the puzzle is finally solved, with a little help from a tool out of his nearby crate. He is eager to finally see what is inside and perhaps find an answer for why Kafli was so afraid to lose it.Collect Knakk's tools from his nearby crateKnakk is camped close to the Grand Stair and is trying to figure out the puzzle of a locket which Kafli was holding when he died. He seems to be very close to finally figuring out the locket's intriguing puzzle.

You should bring Knakk's tools to him.Return to Knakk to help him open the locket'While you have been busy with the corruption to the east, I have spent time figuring out the locket, and I think I have it. It is a curious puzzle, and I have never seen or heard of anything like this. I am really curious as to what is inside!

'The locket has sides that pop out when rubbed and pressed a certain way. I am holding it open but if I let go, I may have to start over, and it took a while to finesse the levers open. With a little help I may finally pop this open. Could you do me a favour and grab my tools from that crate over there?''Ah hah, that did the trick, and I finally got it open! What an interesting locket Kafli held onto....

'There are two inscriptions inside, one in Khuzdûl, and the other I cannot make out. It is much older than anything I have seen and in some form of ancient runic. The newer inscription is written to Kafli from his love, Finna Frostbeard. Finna is one of the premier carvers back home. She was Kafli's sweetheart, and their betrothal was made formal only shortly before he joined this expedition.'Gapi, a dwarf located at Anazârmekhem is organizing efforts to repair the bridges at the Cross-roads of Ash, and would like you to gather pieces of scaffold for him.Pieces of scaffold can be found in the tunnels east of Hadâd-mezer and Bhraf-ru, both south of Anazârmekhem.

You should collect pieces of scaffold for the repairs going on beneath the Cross-roads of Ash.Collect pieces of scaffold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gapi is at Anazârmekhem, located to the north-west of Hadâd-mezer.

You should bring the scaffold-pieces you gathered to Gapi.Wood is in short supply in Khazad-dûm, and the pieces of scaffold found around the Flaming Deeps could prove useful for the repair efforts being performed beneath The Cross-roads of Ash.

There should be a decent supply of pieces of scaffold found throughout the tunnels east of Hadâd-mezer.'Wood is in short supply in Khazad-dûm, and the scaffold-pieces found around the Flaming Deeps could prove useful for the repair efforts being performed beneath The Cross-roads of Ash.

'There should be a decent supply of scaffold-pieces found throughout the tunnels east of Hadâd-mezer.''This will do perfectly. There is enough wood to assist with the refurbishing efforts. I'll see to it that it arrives safely at The Cross-roads of Ash. Thank you very much.'Feggi recommended that you travel to Durin's Court in an attempt to warn Gúthi and his dwarves of the Ghâsh-hai threat, hopefully before they march into a stronghold teeming with Orcs.Gúthi can be found in Durin's Court, east from Feggi's camp in Ânghumu-ru, and then south through Hadâd-mezer. Unlit braziers can be found along the way.

You should make your way across the Flaming Deeps to Gúthi, lighting the braziers along the way.Discover Durin's CourtLight braziers as you make your way to Durin's Court (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gúthi can be found in Durin's Court in the south-eastern Flaming Deeps.

You should speak with Gúthi.Talk to Gúthi at Durin's Court'Gúthi and his dwarves made for Durin's Court to take the stronghold at Hurmulkezer, but now I fear for them. It may not be too late to warn them of the Ghâsh-hai threat.

'Along the way to Durin's Court, you will find several unlit braziers. They should be lit as a warning to the dwarves of the fire-wielding Orcs that menace these halls.

'Durin's Court can be found south-east of Ânghumu-ru. Have a safe journey, brave ${CLASS}!''Hail, stranger! You arrived just in time; we were about to strike at the Orcs in an attempt to take back Hurmulkezer, but it sounds as though this would go badly for us.

'If the Ghâsh-hai are truly as formidable as you say, we might need a new strategy.

'Instead of attacking head on, perhaps we should meet up with the dwarves at the Cross-roads of Ash. There is strength in numbers.'In order to repair the bridges in the Flaming Deeps, the dwarves need iron to forge braces and supports.Ghâsh-hai swords can be found on the Ghâsh-hai, roving throughout the Flaming Deeps.

Ulfied needs Ghâsh-hai swords to melt down so he will have the iron necessary to build repair struts for the bridges.Collect Ghâsh-hai swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ulfied is at The Cross-roads of Ash, in the south-west portion of the Flaming Deeps.

Ulfied will want to begin melting down the Ghâsh-hai swords as soon as possible.'I no longer have the iron I need to build the braces to support the failing bridges.

'The Ghâsh-hai have many iron weapons. If you were to collect some and bring them to me, I could melt them down and be able to make what we need. You can find the Ghâsh-hai roving all over the Flaming Deeps.''It will take many Ghâsh-hai swords, but it is the one source of iron that is abundant in these halls.''These swords will work perfectly. I will put them into the crucible, and they should be melted down in a short time.'You found a half-written scroll intended to be delivered to Anazârmekhem clutched in the hand of a slain dwarf. It would be wise to deliver this message yourself to warn the others of the formidable Ghâsh-hai.Anazârmekhem can be found north of Hadâd-mezer in the Flaming Deeps.

You should deliver the slain dwarf's message warning of the formidable Ghâsh-hai to Anazârmekhem.Bring the message to Hysing in AnazârmekhemYou found a half-written scroll intended to be delivered to Anazârmekhem clutched in the hand of a slain dwarf. It would be wise to deliver this message yourself to warn the others of the formidable Ghâsh-hai.

Anazârmekhem can be found north of Hadâd-mezer.'My goodness -- this is troubling news. If there were Ghâsh-hai reinforcements at Hadâd-mezer, I can only assume they are also at Ânghumu-ru and Hurmulkezer.

'We must warn the others before it is too late... assuming it is not already too late!'The Ghâsh-hai are led by the vicious Orc-commander Yûl, and his defeat would be a serious blow to the organization of the principal enemy threat in the Flaming Deeps.Yûl can be found on the highest floor of Hurmulkezer in the south-eastern Flaming Deeps, south of Durin's Court.

You should find and defeat Yûl.Defeat YûlYûl can be found on the highest floor of Hurmulkezer in the south-eastern Flaming Deeps, south of Durin's Court.

You should find and defeat Yûl.Defeat YûlYou have defeated Yûl, the leader of the Ghâsh-hai forces in Hurmulkezer.

While many Orcs still remain, they will founder without a leader.CompletedThe Ghâsh-hai are led by the vicious Orc-commander Yûl, and his defeat would be a serious blow to the organization of the principal enemy threat in the Flaming Deeps.

You should seek Yûl and defeat him; such a blow would break the spirit of the Orcs.You have defeated Yûl, the leader of the Ghâsh-hai forces in Hurmulkezer.

While many Orcs still remain, they will founder without a leader.The ancient forge located at Hurmulkezer must be shut down and the Orcs stopped before they have an opportunity to craft dangerous new weapons.Gúthi can be found at the Cross-roads of Ash in the western Flaming Deeps.

You should speak with Gúthi when you are ready to travel to the ancient forge of Hurmulkezer.Talk to GúthiGúthi is at the Cross-roads of Ash in the western Flaming Deeps.

Gúthi will be pleased to hear Dolpan was unable to finish crafting his weapon at the ancient forge.Talk to Gúthi at the Cross-roads of Ash'You must disable the ancient forge at Hurmulkezer before it is too late, ${PLAYER}. The Ghâsh-hai have been using it to craft flaming armour and deadly weapons, making them deadlier foes than ordinary Orcs.

'The forge rests high atop Hurmulkezer and is south-east of the Cross-roads of Ash. Talk to me when you are ready to travel there.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready to travel to the ancient forge?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Dolpan has fallen and the forge has been disabled, and no more flaming armour will come to the Ghâsh-hai. No deadly weapon will be forged. We all owe a debt of gratitude to you today, ${PLAYER}!

'We must remain vigilant, however. If we lower our defences now, we will be vulnerable once more.

'I ask your pardon, for I do not mean to speak as if we are on the doorstep of doom. For now, a small step has been taken towards the reclamation of Khazad-dûm once more, and even the smallest of victories deserve celebration.'Bori wants you to collect armour, weapons, and shields that can be repaired or melted down to equip the dwarves who execute his daring plan.Dented armour, broken blades, and cracked shields can be found on Orcs and within their camps throughout Zelem-melek and the Redhorn Lodes.

Bori needs to equip the two teams that will execute his strike on Stazgnâkh, and wants you to gather the materials that will allow him to do this.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek.

You have collected many pieces of the equipment for which Bori has asked, and should now bring them to him.'Even if my plan goes smoothly, both groups of dwarves will be in danger. Orcs of the White Hand are deadly, and there is sure to be fighting. We're low on equipment, though, and certainly lack the armour and weapons my two teams will require.

'If you can find dented armour, broken blades, and cracked shields on Orcs throughout Zelem-melek, the Redhorn Lodes, and within their camps, this equipment might be repaired; if they are too damaged, we could melt them down and use them to make new weapons and armour.

'In either case, I will be able to equip my teams with the weapons and armour victory will require.''Search throughout Zelem-melek and the Redhorn Lodes for the dented armour, broken blades, and cracked shields I can use in the execution of my plan.''These will do nicely, ${PLAYER}; just the sort of thing I need in order to equip the two teams we are assembling. Some of these pieces can be repaired, and the rest will be melted down to make new equipment.'Bori needs you to recruit some dwarves to fill the ranks of the two groups called for by his plan: the diversionary group and the attack group.The Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek is full of dwarves that Bori wants to recruit for his daring mission against the White Hand.

Bori needs to fill two groups with dwarves: a diversionary force and a main attack group.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.

You have attempted to recruit some dwarves for Bori's daring plan to drive the White Hand from Moria, but very few of the dwarves have volunteered.'I will need the help of the bravest dwarves of this company if my plan is to succeed, ${PLAYER}. One group will make a feint against the guarded junction on the Eastern Road, and I will lead the other against Stazgnâkh, the encampment of the White Hand.

'Speak with the dwarves in the Twenty-first Hall and recruit as many as you can for my mission. Bring to their minds visions of honour and of valour, for there will be both in great supply!

'Once the White Hand is driven from Moria, we will have peace beneath the mountains!''Wonderful! Have you found brave dwarves to execute my plan?'

Bori listens as you tell him of Stilling and Wíli, the volunteers you recruited. He waits expectantly for more, and then his face falls.

'That's all? Only two dwarves? How can this be, ${PLAYER}? That is barely enough for one group! Well, I am sure you did your best. I will manage somehow.''I have a great deal of respect for Bori, of course, but I have enough work to do without casting stones at a nest of hornets! This plan is ill-conceived, and unless Lords Bósi or Brogur order it themselves I will have no part of it.''Do not question my valour, ${CLASS}, but I will not follow young Bori to my death. Lord Brogur has already lost his son on this endeavour; unless someone wiser than Bori leads this assault on Stazgnâkh, I fear that Lord Bósi will lose his as well.''I will gladly volunteer for young Bori's mission. The sooner the White Hand is cast from Moria, the safer we will all be! Let none call Stilling coward!''I already have tasks to do, ${PLAYER}. I am sorry that I cannot help Bori with his mission, but I respect him for this undertaking!''I will follow my lord Bósi's son into battle, and gladly! The White Hand's time in Moria will soon be at an end!''What is this plan of Bori's? A diversionary strike? I am old-fashioned, and I do not appreciate such tactics; enemies should be challenged head-on.

'Even if this were more to my liking, I have too many tasks on my plate and not enough time in which to complete them all. It is a shame that I cannot fight alongside the young master.''Talk to the warriors in the Twenty-first Hall and recruit them for the two groups detailed in my plans, ${PLAYER}.'Brogur has told you that his nephew Bori has come up with a daring plan that might accelerate the successful reclamation of Khazad-dûm by the dwarves.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership, off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek, with Brogur.

Brogur has told you that his nephew Bori has devised a daring plan to strike a blow against the White Hand Orcs in Moria, and wants you to help him with his preparations.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership, off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.

You have helped Bori prepare for his daring strike on the White Hand, and should now report to him.'My nephew Bori has come up with a daring plan, ${PLAYER}. He conceived a diversionary strike against a certain hall in the Deeps to draw the Orcs of the White Hand from their camp; this way a second group could enter the camp and defeat its leader.

'It will be dangerous, for both groups, but it is a good plan. Imagine it: with one axe-blow, we will cut off the head of the White Hand presence in Moria! Bósi's fears will be assuaged in the face of such a victory.

'Will you help my nephew Bori with the preparations for this strike? He grieves still for Bróin, and feels that he must earn honour doubly: for himself, and for my slain son. If this strike is successful, he will have done so.''Thank you for helping me with the preparations, ${PLAYER}. I am almost ready, but...nay, it's nothing. I am ready.''Speak to my nephew Bori here and aid him with the preparations for his attack on the White Hand Orcs, ${PLAYER}.'Bori's plan calls for a diversionary strike on the Eastern Road to draw the main force of White Hand Orcs out of Stazgnâkh so another group of dwarves can eliminate the leader.The guarded junction on the Eastern Road is in Nud-melek, and the White Hand encampment of Stazgnâkh is located among the Redhorn Lodes.

Bori has asked you to investigate the guarded junction along the Eastern Road, and to collect barrels of black powder from the White Hand encampment of Stazgnâkh so you will become familiar with it.Find guarded junction on Eastern RoadBori is in the Chamber of Leadership, off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.

You have assessed the strength of the force at the guarded junction along the Eastern Road and found two entrances into Stazgnâkh, the White Hand encampment among the Redhorn Lodes.'One team of dwarves will lead a diversionary strike on an outpost on the Eastern Road in order to draw the main body of White Hand Orcs out of their camp, Stazgnâkh. At that time, a second group will stealthily enter Stazgnâkh and defeat the White Hand leader.

'I need information about these locations, ${PLAYER}: examine the strength of the force along the Eastern Road and become familiar with the layout of Stazgnâkh. I want you to collect barrels of black powder from within Stazgnâkh, and return them to me; we must deprive them of this dangerous weapon wherever we can! Investigate these locations and return to me with any information you discover.

'My father is always telling me that information is among a dwarf's mightiest weapons. How we wield the information you bring back will determine the success of my plan!''Stazgnâkh is located among the Redhorn Lodes. Search it for barrels of black powder, and spy also on the guarded junction on the Eastern Road.''You have done very well, ${PLAYER} -- the information you have brought will be of great value as we carry out my plan. Thank you, my friend!'The time has come for Bori to set into motion his daring plan to drive the White Hand from Moria.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek.

Bori is waiting for you to give the word, and he will then set his plan into motion.Talk to Bori and execute his daring plan to combat the White HandBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek.

Bori's plan has been successful, and you should now speak to him about it.Brogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek, with Bori.

Bori is worried about Ashpar's final words, and wants you to ask Brogur for advice.'When I give the word, Stilling and Wíli will set out for the guarded junction on the Eastern Road. Two hours after that, they will attack the outpost and attempt to convince the defenders that their force is of much larger size.

'Meanwhile, you and I will creep towards Stazgnâkh. If I am correct, the main force of White Hand Orcs will leave the camp to defend the guarded junction on the Eastern Road. We will then enter the camp and find the leader of the White Hand Orcs in Moria. Once he is dead, they will be leaderless and disorganized, and be of little threat to us!

'Speak with me when you are ready, ${PLAYER}. If only Bróin could see our moment of triumph!''My nephew need not be worried -- Ashpar was obviously making empty threats in an attempt to save his own life; I am proud of Bori for not giving in to the Orc's coercion.''We are victorious, and my heart is brimming with pride. We have left the White Hand leaderless and in disarray, just as I had hoped to do!

'Furthermore, Stilling and Wíli returned unharmed from their dangerous mission. These Orcs have underestimated the ingenuity of dwarves!

'Still, I wonder what Ashpar meant when he spoke of "the true power in Moria?" Perhaps my uncle can guess.''Speak to my uncle Brogur about Ashpar's last words. We have won a great victory today, but I am still a little worried by Ashpar's bravado.''Are you ready, ${PLAYER}? We shall leave for Stazgnâkh, and I will give the word to Stilling and Wíli that they should leave for the guarded outpost on the eastern road.

'We will drive the White Hand from Moria, friend; you will see!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>Brogur has asked you to tell Bósi of his son's victory over the White Hand in Moria.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads at the southern entrance of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

Brogur has asked you to bring Bósi news of his son's victory over Ashpar and the White Hand Orcs in Moria.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads'Do not worry about Ashpar's dying words. The Orc was trying to save himself, but it was too late for words to do the trick.

'I wish that my own son had lived to accompany Bori on this adventure. There was honour enough for all, and it would have done Bróin some good to be a part of such a victory.

'You should bring my cousin Bósi news of his son's valiant successes over the White Hand! Perhaps it will cheer him from his gloom.''Bósi will be pleased to hear of his son's victory over the White Hand! Return to the Chamber of the Cross-roads at the southern entrance of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving, and tell him of Bori's grand adventure.'Bósi listens keenly as you tell the story of his son's victory over Ashpar and the White Hand, but his eyes fill with tears when he hears of the Orc's last words. He masters himself before speaking, and his face is stern once again.

'You thought to bring me joy with this news of my son, ${PLAYER}, and I am sorry that it does not. I know this "Mazog" of whom you speak, for it is a name I have heard, and recently.

'The White Hand is not the greatest threat to the dwarves inside Moria, friend. Ashpar was telling my son the truth. We are in grave danger.'Bósi has finished reading the Book of Mazarbul, and is worried that the tale contained therein might also be the fate of his expedition.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads at the southern entrance of Durin's Way, north of the Western Levels.

Bósi is willing to tell you the story of the end of Balin's expedition, a tale he learned from the Book of Mazarbul.Talk to Bósi and experience 'Session: We Cannot Get Out' or read the shortened account insteadBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads at the southern entrance of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

You have listened to the sad fate of Balin's expedition, and should talk now to Bósi.'I have finished reading the Book of Mazarbul. The dwarves of Balin's expedition came to a terrible end indeed.

'I will tell you the story of their final days. It will cause me pain to speak of it, but I hope that revealing the truth about Balin's company will prevent this dire fate from befalling us as well.

'Speak to me when you are ready to hear the tale of that company.''I will tell you the tale of the last moments of Balin's expedition, ${PLAYER}, as they were recorded in the Book of Mazarbul.'After the death of Balin, his expedition to reclaim Khazad-dûm is imperiled by a seemingly endless onslaught of Orcs... and worse than Orcs. Something moves in the darkness of the Black Pit, an ancient creature of shadow and flame that drives all before it.

Trapped at last in the Chamber of Mazarbul, the dwarf-captain Ori records the final moments of the doomed expedition, lamenting that the dwarves cannot long stand against the evils arrayed against them. 'We cannot get out,' he writes. 'They are coming.''If there is hope to be found in the leaves of Mazarbul, ${PLAYER}, I could not see it.

'If we are to survive where Balin's dwarves did not, we will need to prepare for the coming storm. It may not be possible, but we will at least make a stand.'The black iron forged in the Flaming Deeps of Moria often has slight traces of truesilver in it. Though the precious metal is not recoverable, this odd alloy does have its uses for knowledgeable masters of lore and craft.Iron ingots and burnished worm-scales can be collected from the Orcs and worms inhabiting the Flaming Deeps.

Myndil has asked you to collect black iron and burnished worm-scales for him.Collect iron ingots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect burnished worm-scales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Myndil is at Anazârmekhem in the Flaming Deeps of Moria.

You should bring the iron and scales you collected to Myndil at once.'Ah, ${PLAYER}, it's good that you have come by... I have a proposition for you! Though most don't know it, the iron-lodes in this section of Khazad-dûm always had trace amounts of mithril in it. My forefather tried for over a hundred years to find some way to extract it, but never had any luck.

'I have other uses in mind for it, but I need some rather large quantities of the black iron that the Orcs have been using to forge their weapons in the Flaming Deeps. The Orcs often trade and barter the ingots among each other for other goods so they are easy enough to come across.

'Do you think you could get ahold of a good stack of them for me? Oh, it almost slipped my mind, but I also need a number of worm-scales as well. Worms are plentiful down here, so see if you can get me a few of their scales while you're about it, would you?''If you bring me the items I requested, I'll have an attractive reward for you!''Are these the items I asked you to gather? Excellent!

'Would that I could extract the mithril from them, but better dwarves than I have tried and failed. Nevertheless, the debased alloy itself should prove useful for my work.

'Now then, what can I offer you in return for your efforts? I have a few things that you might find most useful!'Unbeknownst to the dwarves, the Ghâsh-hai have sent reinforcements to bolster the Orc camps. Hopefully it is not too late to warn the dwarves.Ânghumu-ru is located to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.

You should travel towards Ânghumu-ru and search for Feggi there.Head towards Ânghumu-ruFeggi and his dwarves can likely be found in western Ânghumu-ru.

You should search for Feggi and his dwarves.Search for Feggi at Ânghumu-ru'Please make for Ânghumu-ru at once and warn Feggi and his dwarves about the danger. Hopefully it is not too late.

'Ânghumu-ru is south-west of Anazârmekhem. Be careful out there! The roads are dangerous.''Thank goodness! I was afraid we would meet our ends here, caught like rats in a trap.

'You were sent to warn us of the reinforcements, were you? Alas! We found that out on our own. Nonetheless, I am thankful you arrived when you did. It might not be too late to warn Gúthi!''We must discover why the Ghâsh-hai are helping their Orc brethren.'The dwarves believe they can trick the Ghâsh-hai into allying with the forces of Mordor by convincing them that Sauron is aware of their betrayal.The Ghâsh-hai altars can be found on the bridge-like structures surrounding The Cross-roads of Ash.

Gúthi believes the Ghâsh-hai can be convinced to join the forces of Mordor. He wants you to place several stones marked with the Great Eye on the altars near The Cross-roads of Ash.Place stones upon the altars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gúthi is located at the Cross-roads of Ash, in the south-west portion of The Flaming Deeps.'While we await information, we can still cause dissent and confusion within the ranks of the Orcs. If they came from Mordor as early emissaries into Khazad-dûm, it may be that they can be frightened into service once again.

'I have prepared several stones, each marked with the symbol of the Great Eye. Place them upon the altars found near The Cross-roads of Ash; when they see the symbol of the Eye burning upon their altars, they should rethink their allegiance.

'The altars are located on the bridge-like structures surrounding The Cross-roads of Ash.''All of the altars must bear the marks for them to believe that the Dark Lord has turned his Eye upon them.''The marks have been placed, and already I sense that allegiances are being questioned.

'While this is a big step towards victory, we still have much to do.'Geirfast has identified the small cave described in the map and will send the wondrous torch you have assembled to it while you find an ally or two.Geirfast is in the Twenty-first Hall.

You should speak with Geirfast again when you are prepared to travel to the strange cave.Talk to Geirfast at the Twenty-first HallGeirfast is at the Twenty-first Hall.

You should return to Geirfast and tell him of the strange map you saw projected on the wall by the light of the torch.Talk to Geirfast at the Twenty-first Hall'You have collected all the materials, and I have assembled the torch this map calls for -- now it is time to see what we shall do with it!

'A lit torch is a fit weapon against few creatures; I suggest you find an ally, perhaps two, in case you have to move around while the torch is lit. While you are looking for the help, I will just send a runner to bring the unlit torch into the cave described in the map.

'Speak to me again once you are ready to leave.''You are prepared to go? I hope you have some help...

'I sent that runner, as promised -- he returned to say that he was barely able to stick his head into the cave before he was blasted with a pygmy drake's fire-breath! He dropped the torch and legged it back here with some alacrity. So be ready!''Another map? Are you sure?

'My curiosity burns within me! Will you follow this strange story to the end?'The Orcs have taken over Ânghumu-ru and have been using the forges to craft weapons. If the forges are disabled, the Orcs' craft will be slowed.Forges can be found in Ânghumu-ru in the north-west quadrant of the Flaming Deeps.

You should disable the forges to hinder the weapon-craft of the Ghâsh-hai.Disable forges at Ânghumu-ruForges can be found in Ânghumu-ru in the north-west quadrant of the Flaming Deeps.

You should disable the forges to hinder the weapon-craft of the Ghâsh-hai.Disable forges at Ânghumu-ru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The forges of Ânghumu-ru are disabled, and the Orcs will now be hindered in their crafting of new weapons.CompletedThe Orcs have taken over Ânghumu-ru and have been using the forges to craft weapons. If the forges are disabled, the Orcs' craft will be slowed.The forges of Ânghumu-ru are disabled, and the Orcs will now be hindered in their crafting of new weapons.Though well-stocked initially, the efforts to reclaim Moria have spread the Iron Garrison thin. To supplement their ambition, the Iron Garrison seeks to repurpose tools and equipment scavenged from the ruins. In order to begin working the long abandoned mines once again, the Iron Garrison seeks to scavenge pick-axes from Fulz-zahar.The entrance to Fulz-zahar lies within Gharâf-fehem

Hersir has asked that you enter Fulz-zahar and collect pick-axes to aid in the re-establishment of the Mines of Moria.'As the Iron Garrison works to reclaim Khazad-dûm, we are also working to re-establish functioning mines. Our primary concern when we first entered was reclamation, and because of that, we did not come prepared for any sort of prospecting activities.

'To that end, we need to bolster our supply of mining equipment with what we can find here in Fulz-zahar. Primarily, we are looking for pick-axes.

'Scavenging is not an activity we are proud of, but we do what we must with our limited supply line.''While these are not the finest of pick-axes, they appear to be sturdy and functional, despite the many years of neglect.

'My thanks for your aid. These pick-axes are a small, but neccessary contribution to our intended re-establishment of mining efforts within Khazad-dûm.'The Redhorn Lodes have become a haven for beasts and Orc-kind alike since the fall of Moria. A variety of different tribes of Orcs fight for control over the precious ore found within the rock, while also competing with insect and beast alike for territory to call their own. The Iron Garrison, seeking to reclaim the mine of Fulz-zahar, has sent Hersir to the Redhorn Lodes to establish an effort to clear the intruders from the old dwarf-delving.The entrance to Fulz-zahar lies within Gharâf-fehem.

Hersir has asked you to assist him in clearing Fulz-zahar of the vermin within.Defeat intruders in Fulz-zahar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hersir is at Gharâf-fehem.

You should return to Hersir with news of your success.Talk to Hersir at Gharâf-fehem'Alwar and I have been tasked to establish a safe prospecting location here in the Redhorn Lodes. Our scouts discovered Gharâf-fehem and the two mines within it. As we arrived, we split our duties. My chief goal in this venture is now to empty Fulz-zahar of threats and re-establish it as a viable prospecting location.

'It seems, unfortunately, that we are not the only ones interested in Fulz-zahar and therefore must...convince...those within to leave. Being so close to the Orkish camps of the Redhorn Lodes, I am hard pressed to leave this post for fear of losing it to the vile creatures.

'Were I to offer you compensation, would you be willing to take up my task instead? Would you enter Fulz-zahar and clear it of the threat within?''Excellent work within Fulz-zahar. Even out here I could hear your efforts within.

'You have bought us time to explore the mine. I don't expect we will reclaim it immediately, as I am certain there are tunnels in there that we are unaware of through which other intruders may enter.

'If ever you are in need of work in the future, please stop by. I am certain we will be able to make use of you.''Have you completed your task yet? Please do so, then return to me when you have finished.'The Redhorn Lodes have become a haven for beasts and Orc-kind alike since the fall of Moria. A variety of different tribes of Orcs fight for control over the precious ore found within the rock, while also competing with insect and beast alike for territory to call their own. The Iron Garrison has sent a small expedition into the Redhorn Lodes to recover a little known mine called Fulz-zahar.The entrance to Fulz-zahar lies within Gharâf-fehem.

Hersir has asked you to defeat leader of the intruders within Fulz-zaharDefeat the leader of the intruders in Fulz-zaharHersir is at Gharâf-fehem.

You should return to Hersir at Gharâf-fehem in the Redhorn Lodes.Talk to Hersir at Gharâf-fehem'It seems that no matter where we go within Khazad-dûm, all we find are infested delvings or rubble. Even Fulz-zahar, a mine that is fairly well-hidden, does not escape incursion.

'If you have spoken with my companion Alwar, you will know that he favours a decisive strike at the leaders of the intruders within our mines. And in that, I agree with him.

'Deep within Fulz-zahar, I suspect there to be one such enemy, one who holds sway over the rest. Defeat that leader, and you will sow disarray among the rest!'

<rgb=#FF0000>The Iron Garrison has created a diversion, drawing the bulk of the intruders from the depths of Fulz-zahar. They are permitting you access for one hour, during which time you may enter and exit Fulz-zahar freely to complete the tasks bestown upon you. 

However, after the hour has passed, the Iron Garrison can no longer guarantee your safety and thus will bar access until they can once again muster an offence to draw the enemy from Fulz-zahar.</rgb>'Do not waste time! Enter Fulz-zahar and defeat whatever passes for a leader within.''I can already hear the unrest within Fulz-zahar. You have done well. It should be but a small task for us to now dispatch the remaining intruders.

'I would not feel right asking you to have undertaken this without some reward, so please accept this token.'Gúthi made for the Cross-roads of Ash to join his fellow dwarves and formulate a new plan to smash the presence of Ghâsh-hai in Flaming Deeps.The Cross-roads of Ash can be found by following the road west from Durin's Court. Gúthi's score-marks can be found along the way.

You should keep an eye out for Gúthi's score marks on the walls, which should help to guide you along the path to the Cross-roads of Ash.Gúthi is at The Cross-roads of Ash, in the south-west quadrant of the Flaming Deeps.

You should speak with Gúthi.Speak with Gúthi at The Cross-roads of AshGúthi went off to the Cross-roads of Ash to meet others to formulate a new plan to get rid of the Orc presence in Flaming Deeps. Go to the Cross-roads of Ash, which can be found to the north-west of Hurmulkezer and speak with Gúthi to hear the new plan.'We are still trying to gather additional information about the Ghâsh-hai movements and plans. As we know, they have been using the forges to craft weaponry, but there is something odd about their behaviour that we've been unable to puzzle out.

'In the meantime, I am glad you have joined us! We need all the strength we can get....'The fiery grims are nothing but a hindrance to the dwarf efforts, and their flames must be extinguished. Their hot orange glow should make them easy targets.Fiery grims can be found throughout the Flaming Deeps.

You should extinguish the Fiery Grims, for the dwarves do not love them.Defeat fiery grims in the Flaming Deeps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have extinguished the bright, roaming flames of the Fiery Grims that prowl the Flaming Deeps. The dwarves will rest easier knowing that their number is lessened.CompletedThe fiery grims are nothing but a hindrance to the dwarf efforts, and their flames must be extinguished. Their hot orange glow should make them easy targets.'I have seen these creatures moving throughout the Flaming Deeps, but do not know what they are. They appear almost as if the depths themselves have taken shape. There is a fell air about them. I fear they are an ancient evil, perhaps drawn here by Durin's Bane.

'If you encounter these strange beings on your journey through the Flaming Deeps, do not hesitate to extinguish them! We dwarves have no love for them.''I fear the grims are an ancient evil, perhaps drawn here by Durin's Bane.'You have extinguished the bright, roaming flames of the Fiery Grims that prowl the Flaming Deeps. The dwarves will rest easier knowing that their number is lessened.Auti received reports that behind the doors the gredbyg were guarding, they are raising their young.Gredbyg can be found within Nud-heden, in the Chittering Hole, south-east of the Orc-watch.

Auti wants you to slay the gredbyg who are nursing their young.Defeat gredbyg in Nud-heden (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Auti is at the Orc-watch, north-west of Nud-heden.

Auti will be pleased to hear that the gredbyg have been defeated and are no longer nursing their young.Talk to Auti at the Orc-watch'I knew I was right to try and foil those horrible creatures! You will never imagine what I recently overheard.

'The gredbyg are raising their young behind the doors they were guarding! Behind that door is a chamber we have named Nud-heden...it was once one of our nurseries. And nay, I am not overreacting! Don't you understand? They are raising their young where once we dwarves raised our young. It is revolting! May my beard wither if it does not stop, and soon!

'Return to Nud-heden, within the Chittering Hole, south-east of here. Venture inside and defeat any gredbyg you find within.''Dead, you say? Are you sure?

'Well, that's good. I will send someone else soon to ensure those blasted bugs do not try to occupy those spaces again!''You are wasting time!'The dwarves of the mining expedition have requested a collection of beautiful sword sheaths.Collection boxes for this task can be found in the major hubs of Moria.

