You should collect the statue-piece for Uxi's collection.Find the statue-pieceMarkthor is at The Cross-roads of Ash, west of Hurmulkezer.

Markthor will want to know the statue's shoulder is safe, so that it can be sent to Uxi for reassembling.Speak with Markthor at The Cross-roads of AshYou have discovered the shoulder of the Helgi Goblinbane statue in Hurmulkezer in the Flaming Deeps.

The goblins of Durin's Way destroyed the statue, and its parts can be found scattered throughout Moria. A dwarf named Uxi endeavours to reassemble this statue.'Ah! What an excellent find, ${PLAYER}. Many of us are very interested in Uxi's efforts to reassemble this particular statue. I will have this piece sent to him at once.'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, has invited you to recollect your experience exploring the Drowned Treasury.The Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'The Drowned Treasury.'

A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit the flooded depths of Ghân-gharâf.

<rgb=#FF0000>You can form a Fellowship to complete this quest with players currently on the original instance or on this Sage of Moria quest. All players will receive credit for completing the instance for their respective quests.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: It is suggested that you complete this quest while in a fellowship. Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge alone or with a smaller group.</rgb>Peer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Drowned Treasury'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria.

A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting your adventures in the Drowned Treasury.'You have done much for the Iron Garrison here in Moria, ${PLAYER}, and I know that you will do even more in the future. There is value in remembering deeds done, for they shape us and can affect successes to come.

'Do you remember the watery darkness of Ghân-gharâf? Into the depths with Bori you travelled, seeking the mithril axe Zigilburk; find it you did, and more beside: Bróin, taken from before the Doors of Durin!

'Peer into the Reflecting Pool and experience this memory anew, ${PLAYER}. You will find that recalling your past may do you some good in the present.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You can form a Fellowship to complete this quest with players currently on the original instance or on this Sage of Moria quest. All players will receive credit for completing the instance for their respective quests.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: It is suggested that you complete this quest while in a fellowship. Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge alone or with a smaller group.</rgb>'I am happy that you have revisited your past adventures seeking the Drowned Treasury, ${PLAYER}. Only by studying our past can we gain knowledge to aid our future.'New information has come to light that the Orcs have been after one forge in particular: the ancient forge of Hurmulkezer. They have used it to forge flaming armour, and have plans to craft a deadly new weapon as well....Regin can be found in the south-west corner of the Flaming Deeps, underneath and just south of the Cross-roads of Ash.

You should find and speak with Regin by taking the stairs down from the Cross-roads of Ash.Head beneath the Cross-roads of Ash bridgeRegin can be found in the south-west corner of the Flaming Deeps, underneath and just south of the Cross-roads of Ash.

You should find and speak with Regin.Talk to Regin below the southern bridge out of the Cross-roads of AshGúthi is at the Cross-roads of Ash, in the western Flaming Deeps.

You should return to Gúthi.Talk to Gúthi at the Cross-roads of Ash'The ancient forge at Hurmulkezer is responsible for all of this flaming armour we see on the Ghâsh-hai, and it would seem it is being used to forge great weapons as well.

'Go speak to Regin, the former care-taker for the forge, to find out how to stop the Orcs from using it.

'He can be found underneath and just south of the Cross-roads of Ash; he is working on reinforcing the bridges.''Go speak with Regin. The longer you delay, the better the chances the Orcs have of using the ancient forge against us.''Watch over Regin. The longer you delay, the more danger he is in.''The Orcs have control of the ancient forge? This cannot be! No wonder they are so strong and fell in these forsaken deeps.

'Thankfully, there is a way to stop them. I come from a long line of dwarves who passed down knowledge of the forge, and it happens that there is a failsafe in such an event. Take this Mithril tuning fork and sound it near the forge to shut it down.

'Be sharp, ${PLAYER} -- attackers are near!''There is a way to shut the forge down? We must see to that at once! The Orcs cannot be allowed to continue using it against us.'Gúthi has asked that the ancient forge of Hurmulkezer be disabled, so that the Orcs cannot continue to use it against the dwarves of the Flaming Deeps.High above Hurmulkezer, the ancient forge has been claimed by the Orcs.Disable the forgeDolpan was about to craft a weapon in the ancient forge when it was disabled. He must be defeated.Defeat DolpanGeirfast recommends bringing an ally or two along for the lighting and placing of the torch. 

He left the torch just inside the entrance of the cave described in the strange map, which contains esoteric instructions for its lighting.Bring the torch to wherever it needs to be, further within the little cave.Pick up the torchYou must destroy the fell spirits that have taken up residence in this chamber, as well as their master, if you are to reach the forge and complete the quality you seek.You must destroy the accursed armoursmiths, as well their wraith master, to dispel the evil they have woven about this ancient forge.Destroy accursed armourers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the Cargûl Forge-masterUse the ancient forge to empower your infused sapphire.You have travelled to an ancient forge where some of the finest weapons in Moria were once crafted, but a band of merrevail driven out of their own caverns have begun raiding it and making off with the tools and materials inside. You must defeat the merrevail and recover the stolen tools before they strip the forge bare if you wish to be able to empower the gem you carry.You must defeat the morroval-robbers and recover the tools they have taken from the forge. You must also prevent the fleeing scavengers from escaping the forge, lest they make off with too many important pieces of equipment.Collect stolen tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the morroval-mistressUse the ancient forge to empower your infused sapphire.The Elves have launched an attack to retake Barad Morlas from the Dunlendings who have invaded Eregion. While the initial attack was successful, a larger force of Dunlendings fell upon the Elves while they were caring for their wounded. Now trapped among the ruins and pinned under assaults from the Dunlendings' siege-engines, the Elves are in desperate need of aid.While the Elves are skilled warriors capable of easily fending off the Dunlendings' assaults, the siege-engines in the field have them pinned down and are dwindling their numbers. You must take to the field, find the siege-engines, and defeat their crews, buying respite for the Elven defenders.Defeat siege-weapon teams (${VALUE}/4)With his siege-engines out of commission and his assault faltering, the Dunlending commander is leading a final attack against the bridge. He must be stopped.Defeat the Dunlending commanderHaving defeated the Dunlendings and routed their forces, you may now use the ancient forge to empower your infused sapphire with the blessings of the Elves.Speak with Perimbant to return to Echad Dúnann.'I am sorry that I was unable to assist you during the battle. My thanks to you for saving my kinsmen!''Are you prepared to return to Echad Dúnann now?'You have come to Stazgnâkh with Bori to execute his daring plan: to sneak into the back of the encampment and slay the leader of the White Hand Orcs.Bori is waiting to speak with you concerning his plan.Talk to BoriBori is waiting for you to <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb> so he will know that you understand the signal.Bori has asked you to follow him into Stazgnâkh.Follow BoriBori is looking out into the darkness that surrounds Stazgnâkh and is waiting to speak with you.Talk to BoriThe building for which you should run is straight ahead of Bori's position, built into the side of the rock wall. Be sure to stay away from the patrolling Orcs, or your mission will end in failure.Bori is making his way deeper into Stazgnâkh.Wait for Bori to arriveThe mine cart tracks for which you should run are straight ahead of Bori's position, built above a gap in the rock wall. Be sure to stay away from the patrolling Orcs, or your mission will end in failure.Bori is making his way deeper into Stazgnâkh.Wait for Bori to arriveBori's plan is in full effect; it is now up to the valiant efforts of Wíli and Stilling to draw the main force of the Orcs out of the encampment.Wait for the Orcs to leave StazgnâkhBori is waiting beneath the mine cart tracks to speak with you about the main force of the Orcs.Talk to BoriThe platform for which you should run is straight ahead of Bori's position, built above a gap in the rock wall. Be sure to stay away from the patrolling Orcs, or your mission will end in failure.Bori is making his way deeper into Stazgnâkh.Wait for Bori to arriveThe scaffolding for which you should run is straight ahead of Bori's position; he wants you to wait for him in its shadow. Be sure to stay away from the patrolling Orcs, or your mission will end in failure.Bori is making his way deeper into Stazgnâkh.Wait for Bori to arriveThe time has come to shed all stealth; you and Bori are now deep enough into the camp that the leader of the White Hand Orcs is without the safety of his protectors!Talk to Bori'Here we are, ${PLAYER}. If we are able to defeat the leader of these White Hand Orcs, we should be able to drive them from Moria with little difficulty!

'But we must be cautious. I do not want to attract any attention until we are near the leader. We should not travel in a group, for we would then be too easy for the sentries to spot. No, we must travel single-file.

'You will go first, and then when the coast is clear, you will give me a signal so I can follow. Our signal will be a <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb>. Just <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb> to me when you feel I can run to you without getting seen. <rgb=#FF0000>Wave</rgb> for me now so I can see that you understand.''They did it! Wíli and Stilling have drawn the attention of the main body of the White Hand Orcs!

'Do you see the wooden platform straight ahead? Make a run for it, and once you are underneath it, <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb> for me to join you...that is, if the coast is clear.

'We must still proceed with caution! There are fewer Orcs now in Stazgnâkh, thanks to our heroic friends, but there are still watchful sentries.''Be careful. Do you see the patrolling Orcs? We cannot let them see us, or our mission will be a failure.

'We are making for the building built into the side of the rock wall there, straight ahead. It seems that the Orcs are paying it no mind, and we will be out of their view if we can make it there.

'Run there without getting too close to any Orcs. Once you have made it there, wave for me when the coast is clear, and I will run to the building. Make sure the Orcs will not see me, ${PLAYER}! Your vantage point will be better than mine.''Run for that wooden platform; do you see it, straight ahead of our position? When you are beneath it, <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb> for me to join you... but only if the coast is clear!''Do you see the scaffolding straight ahead of us? Run for its shadow, avoiding the patrolling Orcs. When you get there, and it is safe, <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb> for me to join you.''It is too dangerous for us to travel together. Instead, you will go ahead, and when you reach a safe location, you will <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb> so I will know to run there too.

'<rgb=#FF0000>Wave</rgb> for me now so I can see what the signal will look like.''The building straight ahead, built into the side of the rock wall, is where you should aim to go. Avoid getting too close to Orcs!

'When you make it to the building, <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb> to me when the coast is clear. Make sure it is safe and my route is empty of Orcs before you signal me!''Do you see straight ahead, where the mine cart tracks pass above that gap in the rock walls? That is where you should go, avoiding the patrols of Orcs.

'Once you are beneath the tracks and it is safe for me to join you, <rgb=#FF0000>wave</rgb> to me and I will come running.''We must watch and wait. It is up to Wíli and Stilling now. If they cannot draw the main force of the Orcs out of Stazgnâkh, we will be unable to proceed.''Let us return to the Chamber of Leadership, ${PLAYER}, singing the song of our victory as we go! Moria will be ours again, in no small part to our brave deeds today!''We have done it! From here we have but a short run to face the leader of the White Hand Orcs. The time for stealth is over. He cannot hide from us now!

'Let us put an end to him, my friend. Fear no sentries!'The year is 2994 of the Third Age, and Balin's expedition into Moria is reaching its grim fate. You are Ori, one of the dwarves charged with defending Moria after the death of Balin.Frár is waiting on the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.

Frár desperately needs your help if the Orcs are to be driven back!Talk to FrárLóni and Náli are on the eastern side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.

You have fought your way to the dwarves on the far side of the Bridge, and should speak to them about the dire situation.Talk to NáliTalk to LóniFrár, Lóni, and Náli have decided to make one last stand against the Orcs. You, Ori, will stand with them.Talk to FrárFrár is in the passage east of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.

Your stand against the Orcs has brought you and Frár to the passage east of the Bridge.Wait for Frár to decide what to doFrár is in the passage east of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.

Some great evil has come to Khazad-dûm, and the shadow of it has filled Frár with dread. He is waiting to speak with you.Talk to FrárThíli is on the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.

Frár has chosen to meet his fate, slowing the advance of whatever evils is yet in store for the dwarves so you may escape to the Twenty-first Hall with Thíli.Talk to ThíliThíli is in the Twenty-first Hall.

You and Thíli have escaped from the Orcs mustering at the Bridge of Khazad-dûm, but they are closing in around you.Talk to ThíliOne of the scouts you sent out days ago has returned to the Twenty-first Hall.Talk to OlgirThíli is in the Twenty-first Hall.

You are down to your last few dwarves, and all appears lost. Thíli is waiting to discuss the situation with you.Talk to ThíliAt your suggestion, the dwarves are retreating to the Chamber of Mazarbul, which may be more easily held against the approaching horde.Follow Thíli to the Chamber of MazarbulThíli is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, waiting to speak with you as the rest of the dwarves prepare the defences.Talk to ThíliThe Book of Mazarbul is on the tomb that was erected for Balin in the centre of the chamber.

Thíli has asked you to finish writing the account of the dwarves in the Book of Mazarbul.Finish writing the Book of MazarbulThe final assault on the dwarves has begun.Survive the Orc assaultMazog, a young Orc descended from Azog the Goblin, has led the assault on the dwarves and must be defeated.Defeat MazogThe Orcs are too many, and Mazog's forces close in to deliver the fatal blow.Stand against Mazog to the last'We have to get you out of here, Captain Ori! We must retreat to the Twenty-first Hall and hope that we can hold them off there!''We have to get you out of here, Captain Ori! We must retreat to the Twenty-first Hall and hope that we can hold them off there!''Were we wrong to come back to Khazad-dûm, Captain? With Balin slain, this endeavour seems ready to fall: the Orcs are too many!

'No, no! We will stand! I will die a dwarf! Let none call Lóni coward!''Things are not well, Captain! There is no end to the creatures -- for every Orc we cleave, two more spring from the darkness!

'Still, we are the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm! We will not let these Orcs drive us from the halls in which we have lived for years too few!''Now that it comes down to it, Captain, I grieve that our return to Moria has been so brief, and so full of sorrow. Was Balin wrong to lead us here, and to expect that whatever curse lay upon these halls had been lifted?

'It is too late now to ask such things, but I would not have this hopeful journey come to such an end, to be forgotten forever, to come to nothing.

'Captain Ori, I beg you: finish writing our account in the book where such things are recorded. There it is, on the tomb we erected for Lord Balin; it was begun by others, but I would have you finish it. I do not want our fate to be forgotten!''I was not certain you would still be alive, Captain Ori, but I rejoice to see you so. I wanted you here for our last defence. We are still waiting for word from the scouts you sent west, but so far there has been nothing.

'And now the Orcs have taken the bridge and the second hall, and close in on our position from all sides. We are certain to follow Frár and Lóni and Náli, my captain, even if we hold out for a little while.

'Hark! Who is that? Is that one of the scouts?''What can we do, Captain? We have no hope of standing against them here in the hall. They will overwhelm us with their vast numbers.'

Thíli listens to your plan, and his face hardens, his eyes stern and bright.

'You are right, Captain. We will retreat to the Chamber of Mazarbul, and make what stand we may! There we may last long enough to make them feel the sting of our axes and hearken our battle-cries!''My captain, I bring sad news! The pool has come all the way up to the wall at west gate; there is no hope of escape that way. Noble Óin's mission has ended, and in failure -- in surprise he was taken by the Watcher in the Water, and the weapon he bore availed him naught.

'The surrounding halls are filling with Orcs, Captain! It was all I could do to make it back here, but it has been for nothing!''Captain Ori, you have arrived at last! I feared we would be overwhelmed before you arrived, but with your strength we may yet push back the Orcs!

'O, that Balin were still alive! We have need of his leadership; against this horde of Orcs we must move with one mind, or we will not survive the fall of evening!

'I was cut off from Lóni and Náli during the last attack. We must join them on the far side of the Bridge, but many Orcs have crawled up from the pit and stand between here and there. We must defeat them before yet more arrive!''I do not like this, Captain. Some Shadow lies ahead. See how my hands tremble, and I have never quailed before any foe! A great evil waits down this passage, worse than all the evils we have seen this day. I...I do not think we can face this thing.

'We must retreat. We must fall back! We must escape across the Bridge!''We are decided, then? One last, glorious stand against the Orcs! I weep that none will sing of it, Captain Ori, but I am glad that I have such honourable and dependable dwarves by my side for its making.

'For Balin! For Khazad-dûm, and for the glory of the dwarves!'Nud-melek awaits! The last hall of Moria before reaching the sunlight of the Dimrill Dale stands before you on your road through Khazad-dûm.The dwarf Svanr can be found upon the western stair of Nud-melek, atop Khadar-zarâm.

You should speak with Svanr.Talk to Svanr in Nud-melek'You have done much for us, friend ${CLASS}, and we are grateful! But I see that you are anxious to continue your pilgrimage through Khazad-dûm.

'As a token of my gratitude, this goat here will take you to Nud-melek, and leave you at the stair atop Khadar-zarâm. Nud-melek is the last hall before reaching the sunlight of the Dale!''Hail, friend! What fortuitous timing; I see that you also seek to make your way through Nud-melek to the fair sunlight beyond. I do love company on my travels.''This goat will take you to Nud-melek, my friend.'All Orcs are lazy creatures, and the pyres of Hurmulkezer remain unlit from lack of upkeep. Lighting them will serve as a warning to the dwarves that enemies dwell in this hall.Hurmulkezer is located just south of Durin's Court, in the south-eastern Flaming Deeps.

You should light pyres in Hurmulkezer.Light warning flames in Hurmulkezer (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The pyres of Hurmulkezer are lit, providing a warning to the dwarves that the enemies currently claim this stronghold, and it would be deadly to enter unawares.Completed'I will head to the Cross-roads of Ash now, but I will ask you a favour, ${PLAYER}, before you follow.

'The pyres of Hurmulkezer are unlit, and without any dwarves guarding Durin's Court, they will not have proper warning that Hurmulkezer has been claimed by the Enemy. I would like you to go and light the pyres as warning to the dwarves.

'In the meantime, I will mark the walls that lead to the Cross-roads of Ash so you may find your way there easily.'The pyres of Hurmulkezer are lit, providing a warning to the dwarves that the enemies currently claim this stronghold, and it would be deadly to enter unawares.The Dwarves of Moria were renowned for their industry. Crafters and prospectors of exceptional talent, they would not have been able to maintain such efficiency were it not for the love of lore. Not all things written in Moria pertained to mining and building. Great tales of battle and epic poems were transcribed by the dwarves. Some of these can be found within the walls of Mekeb-farak along the tunnels of Durin's Way.The entrance to Mekeb-farak lies within Hadudbâb.

Orvar Steeleye has asked you to bring him any tales of adventure you may find in your own adventure within Mekeb-farak.'I have never much been one for anything beyond the sharpening of my axe and the cleaving of Orc-skulls. I remember as a lad, my mother reading to me grand tales of adventuresome dwarves. The challenges they undertook, the foes they fought...it was inspiring to me in my youth. It helped shape me into the dwarf I am now.

'Thinking about my past now hits me with a tinge of nostalgia. I wonder...do you suppose this library has anything in it like the tales I was told as a child? I shouldn't ask this of you but...should you happen across any of these tales while you are exploring Mekeb-farak, would you mind bringing them to me?

'I am a warrior at heart, but this discussion alone raises in me a desire to reread my childhood stories.''Aye! This does bring back memories! I don't remember this exact story but it reminds me much of the ones I was told in my youth.'While Moria is most well-known as a mine, there is much more to it. It was home to a vast and ambitious culture of dwarves. They were warriors, crafters, and scholars. The knowledge the Dwarves of Moria had amassed is often overlooked when compared to the scale of their structural and prospecting achievements. Seeking to instill a sense of scholarly pursuit within the Iron Garrison, Orvar Steeleye has been dispatched to the library of Mekeb-farak to reclaim it and rediscover the lost lore within.The entrance to Mekeb-farak lies within Hadudbâb.

Orvar Steeleye of the Iron Garrison is reluctant to abandon his post and his charge Darri in order to fulfill his duties. In light of this, he has tasked you with entering Mekeb-farak and defeating the leader of the intruders within its halls.Defeat the leader of the intruders in Mekeb-farakOrvar Steeleye is at Hadudbâb.

You should return to Orvar with news of your success.Talk to Orvar at Hadudbâb'When the Iron Garrison first ordered me to Mekeb-farak, I admit to a degree of resentment at the decision. I am a warrior, not a scholar. But, having done some cursory exploration of it, I now see that sending a warrior such as myself here was the correct choice.

'My instincts tell me that the creatures within Mekeb-farak are not a mere collection of random foes. They are led by something greater. A captain perhaps? Or at the very least some sort of intelligent beast.

'On occasion, I have seen Orcs walking this road and would hate to abandon my post or that helpless scholar Darri to their whims. It is for that reason alone that I cannot explore too deeply into Mekeb-farak. You, on the other hand, look to have some time on your hands and the fire in your heart to take up arms and slay the foe who leads the intruders.'

<rgb=#FF0000>The Iron Garrison has created a diversion, drawing the bulk of the intruders from the depths of Mekeb-farak. They are permitting you access for one hour, during which time you may enter and exit Mekeb-farak freely to complete the tasks bestown upon you. 

However, after the hour has passed, the Iron Garrison can no longer guarantee your safety and thus will bar access until they can once again muster an offence to draw the enemy from Mekeb-farak.</rgb>'Well done! You are a warrior after my own heart.

'I can hear the confusion caused by your actions. It will not be long now before we have claimed this library as ours once again!''Darri is no warrior and this camp cannot be abandoned. You must enter Mekeb-farak and defeat the one who leads the intruders inside.

'When you have done this, the intruders themselves will become disheartened, which will make it much easier for us to reclaim Mekeb-farak.'Not even libraries are safe from the ravages of Orcs and beasts alike. Whether their interest in them be the pursuit of information or just a dry place to nest, the libraries of Moria risk an ugly degradation. Seeking to protect the literature and lineage of Moria, the Iron Garrison has sent a representative to Mekeb-farak to prevent it from falling into the hands of the enemy or becoming a breeding ground for all manner of foul beasts.The entrance to Mekeb-farak lies within Hadudbâb.

