You should return to Fastarr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.'There is a forge I know of which may be used to craft the beginnings of the qualities you seek to bestow upon your weapon. Something evil and accursed has crept into the ancient forge, however, and I deem it too dangerous now to go there.

'However, you should not even consider looking for it if you haven't an infused sapphire. Such a stone is necessary to capture the power needed to imbue your weapon. If you can manage to find an infused sapphire, I will tell you the way to the forge....''Take care, ${PLAYER}. I know not what lies within the forges of our forefathers, but any who have dared approach the doors have spoken of a sense of unsettling dread from within. If you are ready, then steel your heart against evil and set forth.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Ah! So you have found an infused sapphire. This stone will do nicely, but once I have prepared it, you will need to take it to the ancient forge to complete the process.

'Let me know when you are ready, and I will tell you the way....''Well fought, ${PLAYER}! I know not what the wraith-slaves of Mordor have in mind claiming our forebears' forges for their evil crafts, but it is well that their task has failed.

'Now hand that empowered sapphire here and I'll see what needs to be done yet to bestow the qualities you seek.'Mundgeirr has told you of an ancient forge where some of the finest weapons in Moria were once crafted...but shortly after the dwarves rediscovered it, a band of merrevail driven out of their own caverns have begun raiding it and making off with the tools and materials inside.Mundgeirr has asked you to bring him an infused sapphire through which a quality may be placed upon your weapon. Unfortunately, Mundgeirr does not know exactly where to find such a sapphire.Mundgeirr can be found in the Dolven-view camp in Moria.

Mundgeirr has bidden you to seek out the forge he spoke of, but warns you that a desperate band of morroval-outcasts has taken control of the forge. You should speak with him when you are ready to leave.Speak with Mundgeirr to travel to the ancient forgeMundgeirr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria.

You should return to Mundgeirr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.'Aye, there is a forge of the quality you seek. We discovered it only recently, but shortly after we re-opened the halls, a band of desperate merrevail driven from the eastern caverns broke in and drove away my men.

'Since then, they have been wrecking and looting everything in sight. If you can get in there and stop them from escaping with those tools, then you should be able to make use of the forge to prepare your weapon as you desire.

'However, before we can even consider assaulting the merrevail, you need to bring me an infused sapphire. Speak with me again when you are ready to leave.''Time is passing swiftly...if you do not leave soon, those morroval-scavengers won't leave you so much as a pair of tongs to work with. Are you ready to go?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Ah, you managed to find an infused sapphire. Now you will need to bring this stone to the ancient forge I spoke of.''So, you managed to drive off those merrevail and restore the forge! Well done!

'Now that you have empowered the stone, I should be able to complete the process, and you will be able to bestow a quality upon your weapon!'Nud-heden will never be recovered until the grodbog-queen is struck down.The grodbog-queen is at Nud-heden, within the Chittering Hole, south-east of the Orc-watch.

Auti is convinced the grodbog-infestation will not be resolved until their queen is defeated.Defeat the grodbog-queenAuti is at the Orc-watch, north-west of Nud-heden.

Auti will be pleased to hear the grodbog-queen has been defeated and the insects have left Nud-heden.Talk to Auti at the Orc-watch'${PLAYER}, we have done much, but we have only delayed the inevitable. While the grodbog-queen still lives, these events can only repeat themselves. No, she must be struck down. That is the only way the insects will stop coming.

'Return to Nud-heden within the Chittering Hole, south-east of here. Venture within, find the grodbog-queen, and defeat her. Only then will we be left in peace.''I thank you, ${PLAYER}. Now we can begin to reclaim that structure and return it to what it once was. Khazad-dûm will not be restored to glory all at once, but stone-by-stone, it will shine once more.''Hurry! You must destroy grodbog-queen before she lays any more eggs.'The Elves of Rivendell have sent a small force of soldiers to retake the ruins of Barad Morlas from the Dunlendings of the south. Within these ruins lies one of the ancient forges where many items of power were made in the elder days.Perimbant has asked you to bring him an infused sapphire which may allow your weapon to be imbued with an Elven quality. Where you may find such a sapphire, the Elf does not know.Perimbant can be found at Echad Dúnann, west of the gates of Moria.

Perimbant has bidden you to speak with him when you are ready to travel to Barad Morlas, where a company of Elves has been entrapped by an army of Dunlendings from the south.Talk to Perimbant to travel to Barad MorlasPerimbant can be found at Echad Dúnann, west of the gates of Moria.

You should return to Perimbant to complete the enhancement of your weapon.'The forge hidden within the ruins of Barad Morlas in Eregion should prove suitable to imbue the quality you seek upon your weapon.

'Unfortunately, those ruins have been held for the past several weeks by a force of Dunlendings from the south. Luck is with you, however, for a company of my brethren have set forth recently to dislodge the Dunlendings from Barad Morlas and retake the lands that are rightfully ours.

'If you can bring me an imbued sapphire which you will need to obtain the quality you desire, then I shall dispatch you directly to Barad Morlas. By the time you arrive, the situation with the Dunlendings should be well in hand.''I fear I have received ill tidings from the Elves sent to assault Barad Morlas, ${PLAYER}. While their attack went as well as can be hoped, and the Dunlendings were routed without the loss of a single Elf, some injuries were inevitable.

'As my kindred settled down to treat their wounded and fortify Barad Morlas, a much larger Dunlending force has fallen upon them unexpectedly. The battle rages even now, and I do not know how it fares, but I can arrange for swift travel to their aid if you are prepared!

'If we can hold Barad Morlas against this assault with your help, then surely the Commander there would be more than happy to allow you the use of our forges.''Ah! You were able to acquire an infused sapphire. I will pack this among the supplies you will need for the battle at Barad Morlas.

'When you and your companions are ready to leave, speak with me again. I should have your supplies ready.''Tidings have reached me that you fought most valiantly in the siege of Barad Morlas and saved many an Elf. My thanks to you indeed, ${PLAYER}.

'Now let me aid you once more. I shall use this empowered sapphire to imbue an Elven quality upon your weapon, and we shall see what you may make of it.'The deep-worms of the Flaming Deeps have been reproducing at an alarming rate. The population of these creatures needs to be kept in check.The deep-worms keep their eggs at Tanunshush, north-west of The Cross-roads of Ash, north of The Burning Stair.

The population of deep-worms needs to be kept in check by destroying their eggs.Smash deep-worm eggs in Tanunshush (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ölfun is at the Cross-roads of Ash, south-east of Tanunshush.

Ölfun will want to know that you smashed many deep-worm eggs, contributing to lowering the population of deep-worms in the Flaming Deeps.Talk to Ölfun at the Cross-roads of Ash'The deep-worms have been reproducing at an alarming rate lately. We've finally narrowed down the location where they keep their eggs.

'They are kept at a place we call Tanunshush. Head north-west until you reach The Burning Stair, just before the Water-works. Tanunshush is just north of there.

'Smash several of their eggs so that we can help keep the population of deep-worms down in the Flaming Deeps.''It may not be the most noble act, but it is the only way we can keep the population of deep-worms down.''I apologize if that was unpleasant, but it truly was for the best.

'That will allow us dwarves to go about our business and not have to deal with so many deep-worms in the Flaming Deeps.'Celofa has tasked you with slaying the Orc Bidroi to further your advancement as a Burglar.The Orc Bidroi can be found on the bottom floor of the Second Hall where he fell from befuddlement. The Second Hall is north of the Foundations of Stone and east of Zelem-Melek.

Celofa looks forward to sharing some new skills as an advanced Burglar, but has first tasked you with a simple deed: to defeat the Orc Bidroi.Defeat BidroiCelofa can be found in the Shadowed Refuge in the northern reaches of the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

Now that you've defeated Bidroi, you should return to Celofa so that she may begin to teach you her advanced Burglar skills.Return to Celofa'I am glad you are here, ${PLAYER}; well met, indeed! For I'm Celofa, Mistress of Riddles. How I love riddling! I can see by the twinkle in your eye that you know just how I feel on this matter.

'I shall be happy to trade some riddlish skill with you, but first I have a more mundane task. Complete it, and the riddling will begin!

'There's a nasty Orc, Bidroi, down in the Eastern Deeps. He doesn't like riddles, that one. I seem to have upset him when I told him a terribly befuddling one, and he was so confused that he fell right down a set of stairs into a great hole, and had to shout and roar for his fellows to come and free him. He is not very happy now, and is rather a threat to the good people here, I'm afraid. Deal with him, and then return to me.''Before I continue your instruction, I want you to defeat Bidroi...you should find him in the lowest level of the Second Hall.''Splendid!  Now let us begin our game of riddles.'Celofa has given you a challenge to better learn the use of the riddle she gave you.The Sixteenth Hall is north from the Foundations of Stone just south of Sigin-tharâk, and that is where the curse-shouter Unur may be found.

Celofa wishes you to do what she could not: to summon Unur with your scroll and defeat him in fair combat. He will likely have companions, so you should be sure bring allies on this venture.Defeat Unur and his trollsThe great Burglar Celofa can be found in the Foundations of Stone.

Celofa awaits tidings of your adventure and looks forward to humbly teaching you all that she knows.'Now that you have that old riddle of mine, I suggest you go out and put it to good use. There's no better way to learn than by doing, I say. I've gathered what information I can from all these texts you've brought me, and I think I shall be able to give you a nice reward for this next bit of burglary I'll have you do. Don't you love a good challenge?

'There is a terrible enemy in the Sixteenth Hall, an Orc named Unur. He is a curse-shouter of no small skill, and he hates Burglars more than anything, for it may have come to pass that I plucked some valuables from under his nose and sneaked away unnoticed. He will answer a summons, but be wary and bring company with you! I'll warrant he'll have some friends too.

'I may have picked his pocket, but I hadn't the gall to face him down in a fair fight. If you can defeat him, you will prove a great Burglar indeed, and I will humbly teach you all that I know.''Unur is a foul creature... the likes of him cannot be allowed to roam free.''I am tremendously impressed with your skills as a Burglar, ${PLAYER}, and I do believe you have surpassed even myself in skill. I did not think anyone loved riddles more than I, but I see that you may be the greatest riddler I have ever met!

'Now, do take this reward. You have earned it, and no mistake!'Many dwarves have been slain by an Orc named Pukhal, a terrible warrior among the denizens of Moria.Pukhal can be found south and then west of Anazârmekhem in the north-western reaches of the Flaming Deeps.

Garnyd has tasked you with killing the Orc Pukhal.Defeat PukhalGarnyd is at Anazârmekhem, in the northern reaches of the Flaming Deeps.

You should return to Garnyd with news of your success.Talk to Garnyd at Anazârmekhem'Well met, ${PLAYER}. If Durin's Folk are to ever retake their ancient home of Moria they will need the support of captains like yourself. I can see that you are a captain of no small amount of experience. If  you would like to contribute further to the campaign here, I would ask of you a series of challenges.

'There is an Orc not far from here, in the north-western region of the Flaming Deeps. He is responsible for the deaths of more dwarves than any other single Orc I know of in this place.

'If you are up to it, your first task is to hunt down and kill this Orc, who calls himself Pukhal. Head south and then west from here into the Flaming Deeps and deal with Pukhal. Return to me if you succeed in this task.''Well done. You have eliminated a great threat to our campaign, and in the process, you have proven that your valour in battle will be enough to inspire those under your command.'Igash appeared to be different from other Orcs. An unearthly fire burned behind his eyes, and when he fell to your blade, something was left behind and this husk is now an item of some consternation.Narfi is at the Twenty-first Hall.

You discovered that Igash was something more than a typical Orc and are looking for some answers to newfound questions.Pálmar is at Anazârmekhem.

Narfi could give you very little information about the strange husk, but he thought that his agent, Pálmar -- posted in Anazármekhem -- may know something about the strange fire behind Igash's eyes.Talk to Pálmar at AnazârmekhemAll that is left of Igash is a dry and vile husk, as if the body was nothing more than a shell. You collected a small piece of this husk, which might be studied further. Perhaps you should deliver it to Narfi at the Twenty-first Hall.'I have never seen such a thing, but the fire you describe in this creature's eyes is as well-known to me as it is to Pálmar. My agent watching the Forges of Khazad-dûm says he has seen the same look within the eyes of the leader there.

'I wonder if there is something unseen happening with these Orcs, something more vile than the smell these beasts typically give off.

'Make your way to Pálmar and tell him what you found. Perhaps he can give you more insight to what this is and means.''You should speak with Pálmar at Anazârmekhem about Igash.''A strange fire? Aye, I know very well that look. Twice I have seen the master of the Forge and twice have I seen something in his eyes that was not right, as if something dwelled deep within the Uruk that was unnatural to his kind.

'I have spoken to others of this, and we fear that this is some new fell creature, perhaps born in the dark depths of Khazad-dûm. Or... perhaps something reborn. Regardless, they do not occupy positions of power other than the leadership of these locations. Kranklûk within the Forges is just another menace to be removed.'You received a letter from Bardag Hailhand, summoning able and willing Brawlers to join him at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.Bardag Hailhand is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, in Moria.Bardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.Punch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the soundBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.Punch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the soundBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.Punch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the soundBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.Punch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the soundBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.Punch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the soundBardag Hailhand is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, in Moria.Talk to Bardag Hailhand at the Shadowed RefugeThere are adventurers of all sorts lending their support to the Iron Garrison in Moria, but these Champions and Guardians and Hunters don't have what it takes. I need a good Brawler who knows a thing or two about fighting, and doesn't rely on swords or spears or arrows. Is that you? Come see me at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, if it is!

Bardag Hailhand, Brawler-of-Note'At last, a Brawler! You are just the sort for whom I have been looking, ${PLAYER}. These others just don't understand. When they think of brawling, they think of musclebound types smacking each other around in taverns or in alleys, but you and I know that a good brawl can break out anywhere, and involve anyone!

'To wit: I have discovered that certain rock formations in the Foundations of Stone, when struck, cause tremendous reverberations through these dark caverns. Creatures of great evil and power are drawn to these echoing sounds, and a mighty Brawler might use this opportunity to defeat them, rendering the caves less dangerous for those other adventurers who never learned to brawl!

'An islet north-east of the great underground lake contains several of these echoing deep-stones. Find them, punch them, and defeat whatever creatures answer your noisy challenges! This will be good for you, Brawler. I'd say five bouts should do it, and you might even learn something to help you advance in the fighting arts.''An islet north-east of the great underground lake contains several suitably echoing deep-stones. Find them, punch them, and defeat whatever creatures answer your noisy challenges! This will be good for you, Brawler. I'd say five bouts should do it, and you might even learn something to help you advance in the fighting arts.''An islet north-east of the great underground lake contains several suitably echoing deep-stones. Find them, punch them, and defeat whatever creatures answer your noisy challenges! This will be good for you, Brawler. I'd say five bouts should do it, and you might even learn something to help you advance in the fighting arts.''An islet north-east of the great underground lake contains several suitably echoing deep-stones. Find them, punch them, and defeat whatever creatures answer your noisy challenges! This will be good for you, Brawler. I'd say five bouts should do it, and you might even learn something to help you advance in the fighting arts.''An islet north-east of the great underground lake contains several suitably echoing deep-stones. Find them, punch them, and defeat whatever creatures answer your noisy challenges! This will be good for you, Brawler. I'd say five bouts should do it, and you might even learn something to help you advance in the fighting arts.''An islet north-east of the great underground lake contains several suitably echoing deep-stones. Find them, punch them, and defeat whatever creatures answer your noisy challenges! This will be good for you, Brawler. I'd say five bouts should do it, and you might even learn something to help you advance in the fighting arts.''You have returned, and in one piece! Well done, ${PLAYER}. Am I to understand that you defeated five opponents, and delivered such a drubbing to them that the echoes of it will remain a warning to all other foes in the Foundations of Stone? What foes did you defeat?'

You recount the list of your opponents, and with every name Bardag's eyes grow wider.

'I expected you to fight Orcs and trolls, but I must confess I did not anticipate that nameless creatures of such power would answer your challenge! Well-brawled, my friend! Such good fighting deserves a reward to match, though I know for the two of us a good brawl is reward enough!'Bingo is ready to say farewell to Moria and to continue his adventure on the other side of the mountains.Enemies can be found throughout Nud-melek, the eastern levels of Moria.

Bingo wanted you to defeat foes in Nud-melek as you make your way to the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.Defeat foes in Nud-melek, in Moria (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo wanted to meet you at the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm, in Nud-melek.Meet Bingo at the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûmBingo is at the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.Talk to Bingo on the west side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûmEnemies can be found throughout Nud-melek, the eastern levels of Moria.

Bingo wanted you to defeat foes in Nud-melek as you make your way to the exit of Moria.Defeat foes in Nud-melek, in Moria (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo is ready to see the sunlight once again, and wants to meet you in the Dimrill Dale.

The exit from Moria is east of the First Hall, in Nud-melek.Pass into Nanduhirion from the First Hall in Nud-melekBingo is outside the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion.Talk to Bingo outside the East-gate of Moria, in NanduhirionSpalvi has fallen behind, and stands by the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion.Talk to Spalvi outside the East-gate of Moria, in NanduhirionBingo is outside the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion.Talk to Bingo outside the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion'I think I am ready to say farewell to these caverns, ${PLAYER}. My memory has returned, but most of my time beneath the mountains is a cold, dark blur, and I am ready to see the sun once again! Perhaps if I were a dwarf I would feel differently about these halls, but I am a hobbit, and we like our burrows to be a bit more cozy and comfortable!

'Spalvi introduced me to a dwarf named Ketill, and he agreed to draw some illustrated maps for my book once my adventure is complete! What a fine fellow! He also provided a map of the eastern levels of Khazad-dûm we can use to find our way to the exit.

'I would like to repay Ketill Map-maker for these kindnesses, so let us defeat enemies in Nud-melek as we make our way to this point on the map: the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm. That sounds like it will be quite a sight, and we will also be helping to make the halls and passages safer for Ketill while he works.''Spalvi introduced me to a dwarf named Ketill, and he agreed to draw some illustrated maps for my book once my adventure is complete! What a fine fellow! He also provided a map of the eastern levels of Khazad-dûm we can use to find our way to the exit.

'I would like to repay Ketill Map-maker for these kindnesses, so let us defeat enemies in Nud-melek as we make our way to this point on the map: the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm. That sounds like it will be quite a sight, and we will also be helping to make the halls and passages safer for Ketill while he works.''Let us meet at the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm! I would like to see it!''Well now. This is a pickle.''Let us meet at the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm! I would like to see it!''I am beginning to have doubts about letting Ketill draw the maps for my book, ${PLAYER}. On the map he gave me, the bridge here is intact!

'Well, I suppose we will have to go around. The good news is we can defeat more of the enemies in Nud-melek that threaten the dwarves as we make our way to the exit.''I suppose we will have to go around. The good news is we can defeat more of the enemies in Nud-melek that threaten the dwarves as we make our way to the exit.''It is good to be out in the fresh air once again!''Ah, it is good to breathe fresh air once again! There is a certain majesty to the great halls of Khazad-dûm, no mistake, but anything larger than a hobbit-hole seems a bit much, if you ask me. I am glad to be outside again!

'But wait! Spalvi seems to have fallen behind. I wonder if everything is all right?''Spalvi seems to have fallen behind. I wonder if everything is all right?''I do not know how to say this, my friend, but I think the time has come for me to take my leave of our little band. I have enjoyed our adventures together, and am glad to have made right the wrong I caused you and Bingo. I have cast behind my old name and adopted a new one, and indeed I feel as if more has changed between the Stout-heart and the Dourhand than just the name!

'I wish to remain in Khazad-dûm and help the Iron Garrison with their work, if they will have me. I will not worry about Bingo, ${PLAYER}, for I know that you will be with him. I do have a word of warning, however: I have heard that Elves live on this side of the mountains. Use caution in your dealings with them! They are not to be trusted.

'Farewell, my friends! May we meet again at journey's end!''I am sorry to see Spalvi go, but I know he will be of great help to the dwarves in Moria. Now we should turn our faces to the future, and see what awaits us next on our journey!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'A Chapter About Elves' (Recommended Level: 60)</rgb>Pada has deciphered the musical text you acquired and transcribed it to a composition that you can now read and perform. In order to practise your newfound knowledge, Pada has tasked you with entering Skûmfil and facing down the deep-claw Cracktooth.Cracktooth is in Skûmfil in Moria, east of the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.

You should defeat and search the deep-claw named Cracktooth in Skûmfil, for it is likely that the last bit of text can be found upon that beast.Defeat Cracktooth in SkûmfilPada awaits your return at the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

You have defeated Cracktooth and recovered the lost text missing from the composition being compiled. The completed work should help you on your way to being a truly heroic Minstrel.'I have deciphered all I can from this text you recovered, ${PLAYER}, but there is still something missing. This composition is almost complete, yet it is so far from being the full song I know it should be!

'I want you take what I've written so far and head into Skûmfil east of here. While there, keep an eye out for the deep-claw Cracktooth. I believe it may be in posession of the remaining text, for deep-claws always seem to be gathering for their foul nests.

'Gather your friends and strength for this fight, for it shan't be easy. Your companions will look to you for inspiration, so you must be wilful and strong...but I will not tell you how to be a good Minstrel, for you know that well already! Return to me when you have found the scrap I seek, and you will then be ready for all that I have to teach you.''${PLAYER}, this is it! You have found and restored a lost piece of wonderful music, ancient beyond reckoning, but timeless too. Surely you appreciate what a great thing you have done, for music is woven into everything we know. There is even music in silence, if you listen closely.

'It has been a pleasure working with so great a Minstrel as yourself. I hope that my lesson is worth your troubles; indeed, you have taught and inspired me as well! I see now that you will stop at nothing to pursue a worthy cause, and here I had doubted that your will would prevail in this dark place.  

'You have restored hope to me, my friend, and I did not even know that my hope had failed. May your music ever bring you light when your feet take you down dark roads.'You received a letter from Byrski Hardprow, a dwarf of the Iron Garrison stationed in the Dimrill Dale.Byrski Hardprow sent you a letter requesting that you visit him in the Dimrill Dale.

Deliver the letter to Byrski Hardprow. He can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.${PLAYER},

I have heard many tales of your skill, and enough has been said of your efforts to help us reclaim the mines of Moria. I have need of a practised Mariner's assistance for an expedition onto the Mirrormere. If you wish to aid me, you can find me at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale, but beware the Orcs that lurk in Azanulbizar of old. Do not keep me waiting; I will set sail without you if I must!

Byrski Hardprow'Well, well! I had begun to worry you weren't coming, ${PLAYER}. Right then, I'll be taking that!'

You hand Byrski Hardprow the letter he sent you, and he crumples it into a ball before stuffing it into one of his pockets.

'If we're going to set out on the Mirrormere today, there's work to be done. I promised Brogur that I would see to this task, and I will not be made a liar!'Spear-wielding goblins threaten all who hope to descend the stair of Khadar-zarâm.Spear-wielding goblins can be found atop Khadar-zarâm.

You should collect spears from the lethal goblins.Collect spears from goblinsSpear-wielding goblins can be found atop Khadar-zarâm.

You should collect spears from the lethal goblins.Collect spears from goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have taken the weapons of the spear-throwing goblins of Khadar-zarâm, making the stair safer for those who wish to leave Moria through the eastern door.CompletedSpear-wielding goblins threaten all who hope to descend the stair of Khadar-zarâm. You should collect spears from the goblins that perch atop the stair, aiming their malice at passers-by hoping to leave Moria.You have taken the weapons of the spear-throwing goblins of Khadar-zarâm, making the stair safer for those who wish to leave Moria through the eastern door.The spider Gaelnath has stolen an ancient dwarf-make rune-stone.Gaelnath should be found in the Foundations of Stone, far to the east of Thorin's Hall.

Dwalin told you to recover the dwarf-make rune-stone from the spider Gaelnath and bring it to Márus.'Troubles abound in Ered Luin, but this not the least. Rumours abound of an ancient spider, Gaelnath, that has come into the possession of a particularly important dwarf-make rune-stone.  

'If you are up to the challenge, head back into the Foundations of Stone and look for Tunzelgund along the northern edge of its central region.  To the north of Tunzelgund you will find Gaelnath.

'I want you to get this rune-stone and take it back to Márus. He will know what to do with it.''You should seek Gaelnath in the Foundations of Stone in Moria.''What is that you have there, ${PLAYER}? Amazing! This is an ancient Rune of Restoration.'

Márus frowns as he looks over the rune-stone.

'It would seem that this stone has seen too much foul corruption in the dark of Khazad-dûm. We will have to do what we can to restore it to its former power.'Many rune-keepers seek the Rune of Restoration, but not all can accomplish their goals alone.Helegfan can be found in the Sixteenth Hall, at the south-eastern tip of Nud-Melek, just north of the Foundations of Stone.

Ríon has instructed you to aid your fellow rune-keepers with their final task upon the path to obtain a Rune of Restoration.Defeat HelegfanRíon is just outside of the Sixteenth Hall.

You should return to Ríon and inform him of your success.Talk to Ríon outside the Sixteenth Hall'Well met, ${CLASS}. It is fortunate for me that you have come along. I have a favour to ask of you if would spare a moment. My fellow rune-keepers and I have learned of a foul creature housed within the Sixteenth Hall: the frost-grim Helegfan.

'Many young rune-keepers are seeking this fell spirit, but I doubt any would succeed alone. They will need your help.  

'If you are willing, enter the Sixteenth Hall and aid a rune-keeper in this task. Return to me when you have succeeded, and I will reward you.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest can only be completed by helping a rune-keeper on its Legendary Trait quest "Secrets Long Forgotten."</rgb>'You should help a fellow Rune-keeper, ${PLAYER}.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. Now then, here is your reward.

'Durin's Folk everywhere owe you thanks for your efforts this day. You've done a great deed in the effort to reclaim the lost realm of Khazad-dûm.

'If you should ever come back this way, be sure to check with me before entering the Sixteenth Hall once again. There are likely to be other rune-keepers in the future who will need help facing their own challenges.'You notice a great number of strangely-glowing worms slithering about the feet of the stone trees in Nud-melek.Deep-crawlers can be found in the Second Hall of Nud-melek.

You should defeat deep-crawlers.Collect ichor from deep-crawlersIchor can be found on deep-crawlers in Nud-melek, on the eastern side of the Second Hall.

You should gather ichor from deep-crawlers.Collect deep-crawler ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected the valuable glowing ichor of several glow-worms, enough to coat a number of lamps.You notice a great number of strangely-glowing worms slithering about the feet of the stone trees in Nud-melek.

You should see if the worms' ichor contains any luminescent properties that will be useful to the dwarves of the expedition.You have collected the valuable glowing ichor of several glow-worms, enough to coat a number of lamps.Celofa thinks that the remaining text that pairs with the scroll you found earlier is in the posession of an Orc named Horngaz. The remaining text must be found in order for her appetite for riddles to be sated.Horngaz is somewhere within the Foundations of Stone.

Celofa has asked you to acquire the missing text from the Orc Horngaz.Find the missing textCelofa is in the Foundations of Stone.

You should return to Celofa with the scroll.'I am terribly perplexed by this deceptive scroll, friend Burglar. It teased me with hopes of learning a very great and mischievous riddle, but then played a trick on me by being incomplete from the start! 

'I think I know just where to hunt next for the missing text to this naughty scrap of lore. In the Foundations of Stone are many Orcs, most of whom have become infected with the unhappy fungus that plagues the area. One in particular, who goes by the name of Horngaz, has apparently gained his own appreciation of scrolls and books. Yes, an Orc who likes riddles -- a peculiar event, is it not?

'Find Horngaz, ${PLAYER}, and see if he has the missing text we seek. I shan't sleep a wink until I can find out the rest!''Have you found Horngaz yet? I am sure he can be found in the Foundations of Stone somewhere.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. Well done, indeed!'

Celofa immediately starts reading the text you brought her while absently handing you an old scroll.

'Here, you may take this.  I've learned all I can from it and I think you could make good use out of it.

'In fact, I know just the thing to help you learn how to use it.'As you entered Khadar-zarâm, you felt a great tremor underfoot....The source of the tremor can be found in Khadar-zarâm's goblin camp atop the stair.Find the source of the tremorThe source of the tremor can be found in Khadar-zarâm's goblin camp atop the stair.Find the source of the tremorYou have defeated the menace upon the stair.CompletedAs you entered Khadar-zarâm, you felt a great tremor underfoot....You have defeated the menace upon the stair.Svanr has suggested that you light the braziers at the feet of the dwarf-statues that line the Second Hall in Nud-melek.The summoning horn can be found near Svanr on the stairs of Khadar-zarâm.

You should summon Svanr to let him know when you are ready to depart.Use the summoning horn to call SvanrBraziers can be found at the feet of the dwarf-statues along the north edge of Nud-melek's Second Hall.

You should light the braziers as a tribute to the fine stone-work of Durin's day.Light braziers at the feet of the stone dwarves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Svanr can be summoned using the horn.

