You should bring the lore-fragments back to Winiel.'Well met, ${PLAYER}. It is good that you have come to me. I see in your eyes the hunger for knowledge that drove me to greater pursuits in ages long passed.

'Here in the Water-works, it is easy to find odd bits of dwarf-knowledge thought lost to the ages. If you are up to the task, I would have you gather some of these texts and bring them to me.  It is likely we will both end up learning a great deal together.

'Your search should focus upon the larger buildings in the Water-works as well as any large gatherings of foul creatures here. Return to me when you have found a significant amount of material for us to study.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. These will prove most valuable in the days to come.

'We must move on to your next task, for we have little time to lose.'Trolls are a formidable opponent, and in Moria, the trolls have had much time to develop thicker hides and worse tempers. It falls to Ossur to watch the comings and goings of the trolls and their handlers at the Grand Stair. In the time since he began watching, he has seen one troll that seemed more frightening and deadly than the others, and a throng of handlers who kept the savage troll at bay.The Grand Stair is north-east of the Orc-watch.

Ossur told you of seeing a great troll slumber under the soothing sound of drums and enter a terrible frenzy without them. He watched the goblins and an Uruk-handler carry the massive troll into the Grand Stair, and there it has remained.Defeat the BeastOssur is at the Orc-watch.

You defeated the Beast within the Grand Stair. It was a difficult battle, but you perservered. You should now return to Ossur.Talk to Ossur at the Orc-watch'In my earliest moments here at the Orc-watch, I knew that there were terrible things in the deep. I heard rumblings through the walls, and then one night, as I stood outside the Grand Stair to the north-east, I heard the drums. Giant drums carried by goblin-slaves pounded in a terrible rhythm by other goblin-slaves. All under the watch of an Uruk-handler armed with a sharp brand. The goblins also carried a massive litter, and on that litter slept a massive troll.

'Its chest heaved in time with the drum-beats, and I could see a massive scar on its chest. As I watched, one of the goblins lost its footing and slid into the depths below along with the drum on its back. The other goblins stopped drumming, and without warning, the troll leapt awake and began slaughtering the goblins. Only after a moment of poking and violence administered by the Uruk did the Beast quiet. The drumming began anew, and the troll fell back to slumber.

'Whether it is a gift or a weapon to be used against Igash, it must be destroyed. Enter the Grand Stair and find this beast. When you have accomplished this task, return to me.''An incredible success and effort, ${PLAYER}. I can only imagine that the battle was difficult, but you succeeded, and that is all that matters. 

'I tell you, never had I seen a troll with such terrible skill and power, and yet you have bested the Beast. You are truly a potent warrior.''I tell you, I have never seen such a display of destruction as was wrought by that Beast. You would do best to kill it fast or learn to use the drums.'Even the Elves recognize that wildlife unchecked can be as harmful to nature as wildlife slaughtered for no good reason.Defeat wild animals in LothlórienEven the Elves recognize that wildlife unchecked can be as harmful to nature as wildlife slaughtered for no good reason.Defeat beasts in LothlórienArmbeald has asked you to track the path of a missing dwarf-worker and bring back any evidence you find of his passage.The dwarf-worker was rumoured to have passed through the heart of the Redhorn Lodes, by the east to west mine cart track just north of the passage leading into the Flaming Deeps.

You should collect evidence of his passage and bring it to Armbeald, who wishes to see the progress of the dwarf's mission.Acquire evidence of dwarf-worker's passageArmbeald is at the Orc-watch in the Redhorn Lodes of Moria, north-west from where you found evidence of the dwarf's remains.

You should return to Armbeald with the skull you have found, which has been cleaned of all its flesh.'Here we come to it, ${PLAYER}. You wish to learn, and I am willing to teach you, if you can do what I ask.

'You have the look of an experienced enough woodsman and hunter. I know of a skill that will aid you greatly, but the path you must follow to attain it will not be easy. Sometimes it is more useful to track friend than foe, so let us start there. 

'One of the dwarf-workers of the expedition went out many days ago on a scouting mission that took him through the southern region of the Redhorn Lodes. You should search there for evidence of his passage, and see how he fares.''How terrible! I sought evidence, yes, but I had hoped it had not come to this. Let us examine the poor fellow's skull for clues as to what happened to him. If we can avenge him, that will suffice for your challenge!

'He was killed recently. Some teeth are missing, also. What shall we make of this?'Valthor considers pride in one's own abilities paramount to a champion.Dwalin's throne is in Thorin's Hall, far to the west of Moria.

