'The difference between a good champion and a great one is their renown. The peoples of Middle-earth need to know that there are warriors out there capable of incredible martial prowess, risking their lives to fight the enemy.

'For your second task, I want you to travel to Thorin's Hall. Ascend the steps toward Dwalin's throne and proclaim your prowess as a champion to all gathered in the halls of the dwarves!'That's all well and good, ${PLAYER}; but you have much to learn about the telling of a tale.  

Your deeds are impressive, but impress me with your words, if you can.'Well said, ${RACE}. Your proud words show you to be a great warrior in my eyes.

'Return to Valthor in Khazad-dûm and tell him what you have said here today. It will impress even him.''Well done, well done!

'Now, ${PLAYER}, for your next task.'The tale recorded in the Book of Mazarbul has filled Bósi with dread, and he knows that the dwarves in the Great Delving of Moria must prepare for war.The dwarves Slóthi, Sigdan, and Thálfi are in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

Bósi fears that war may be coming, and he wants the defences of the Great Delving made ready.Aid Slóthi with his preparationsAid Sigdan with his preparationsAid Thálfi with his preparationsBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

