'You must be ${PLAYER}. I've been expecting you.

'Come, let us speak more. I am sure there is much I know that you can learn from.'Slóthi is worried that when the Orcs attack, the dwarves might be cut off from the outside world and will not survive a long siege.Thórgnyr is outside Moria by the Doors of Durin before the still pool.

Slóthi wants to ensure that the supply route outside Moria remains open and that there is enough food within the mines for the dwarves to survive a long siege.Slóthi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

Thórgnyr has given you the first of several food deliveries for Slóthi, who can be found in the Chamber of the Cross-roads.'Bósi has tried to keep it quiet, but rumour travels quickly in the passages of Moria. Most of us are now aware of Balin's end. They were surrounded: Orcs from the east and below, and the terrible creature in the pool by the Hollin Gate.

'We cannot afford for that to happen again, ${PLAYER}, but if it does, it is my responsibility to make sure that we have enough supplies to withstand a long siege.

'I want you to leave Moria and speak to Thórgnyr just outside the Doors of Durin; tell him to send us as much food as he has to spare and to arrange for more on a regular schedule. We will not be put in the same dire place as Balin's company. I would see us avenge them so they may then rest in long peace beneath the stones.''Thórgnyr and Tulk are outside Moria by the Doors of Durin. Speak with Thórgnyr about establishing more frequent deliveries of food and supplies, because we may have need of them sooner than we expected.''Many pardons, ${PLAYER}, but I am not the Thorgnyr you seek! You are looking for my brother, also called Thorgnyr, currently on guard outside the Doors of Durin at the Hollin Gate of Khazad-dûm.''So the troubles within Moria have begun already? I am not surprised that they have come, but I did not expect that they would be upon us so soon. I would have urged more caution, but I held my tongue. Bósi and Brogur are capable dwarves, and I did not wish to heed the warnings of my heart.

'I approve of this decision to order an increased frequency of deliveries into Moria. I have long said that food has been too slowly sent into the mines, for any number of obstacles could besiege our supplies, within or outside of the mines.

'I will give you the first of these deliveries; bring it to Slóthi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads and tell him that more will follow.''You were supposed to bring those supplies to Slóthi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads and tell him that more will follow. Do not forget!''Ah, the first of several deliveries from Thórgnyr, I hope? Good, good! We won't be shut off from the outside world and caught unawares this time. We will be ready for anything!'Sigdan has asked you to help his cousin Sporr scout some of the approaches to the Chamber of the Cross-roads for any Orc activity.Sporr is waiting outside the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Sigdan's cousin Sporr is to scout the approaches to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, looking for any Orcs that might be preparing to attack.Talk to SporrSigdan is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

You have accompanied Sporr on his patrol, scouting for Orcs on the approaches to the Chamber of the Cross-roads, and should report now to Sigdan.'Do you think we will be ready by the time the Orcs attack us? I do not know if we will... if the Orcs knew how vulnerable we are now, they would not delay. They would attack us within the very hour!

'My cousin Sporr has taken it upon himself to scout the approaches to the Chamber of the Cross-roads; if the Orcs have any plans to attack soon, he will see the signs and can warn us in time.

'Please go help him with his patrol. I am anxious for Sporr to have some assistance, should any unsavoury foe meander across his path.''My cousin Sporr has taken it upon himself to scout the approaches to this chamber for Orcs. Help him with his patrol, ${PLAYER}, and I will be in your debt.''If you are keen of eye and strong of arm, I would welcome your company on my patrol, ${PLAYER}. Let us scout for any sneaking Orcs that might think to gain some advantage by spying on the approaches to the Chamber of the Cross-roads.''You did well, and I am pleased that you were there with Sporr when he ran into trouble! My cousin is valiant and brave, but some challenges are simply too much for a single dwarf.

'Thank you, my friend. Perhaps we will be ready in time after all.'Thálfi doesn't like the well in the centre of the Chamber of the Cross-roads, and is worried that the Orcs might climb through it if the sentries are not alert.The bottom of the well is likely somewhere in the Water-works, in the depths of Moria, south-west of the mighty aqueduct. The dwarf Melmar may be somewhere near the bottom.

Thálfi is worried that the Orcs might climb up from the bottom of the well, and wants you to investigate to make sure that's not possible.Find the bottom of the wellThálfi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

You found the bottom of the well but discovered it to be well-protected, and should return now to Thálfi.'I do not like that well. I looked down it and couldn't see the bottom, but I'm pretty sure there's water down there. It makes me nervous.

'What if the Orcs find the bottom of the well and try climbing up? They could use it to get into this room without the sentries noticing! I don't need to tell you what a disaster that would be.

'I'd feel better if you could find the bottom of the well and make sure there's no way for the Orcs to climb up into this chamber. Melmar went looking for it, but I never heard back from him. I don't know how you'll get to the bottom safely, but you should find a way down to the Water-works and then look for Narag-kheleb, the bottom of the well. I expect you will find it south-west of the mighty aqueduct in the depths. Don't jump down the well itself, though, unless you think you could fall for uncounted fathoms and land alive on your feet.''Anything that might allow the Orcs to sneak into this chamber makes me nervous. Find the bottom of this well, somewhere in the Water-works south-west of the great aqueduct, and ensure that the Orcs won't be able to climb up from the bottom.

'Melmar went looking for the bottom. You might find him somewhere down there.''This is it! Do you see that hole in the cave ceiling above us? That's the bottom of the well in the Chamber of the Cross-roads. I don't think we need to worry about Orcs climbing up, though.

'Oi! Draw your weapon!''You say that Melmar found the bottom of the well, and that he is confident that the Orcs cannot climb it? That is good news! I am less worried now about its presence.

'We may do all right after all, my friend. Thank you for investigating this for me.'Bósi is pleased that you have aided his dwarves with the preparations, and wants you to do the same for the dwarves in the Heart of Fire.Stóthkell is the dwarf in charge of the Heart of Fire located off the Way of Smiths, among the Silvertine Lodes.

Bósi wants you to lend your aid to the dwarves manning the Heart of Fire so they will be prepared if the Orcs attack the Way of Smiths.'My heart dares to hope that we will be prepared for when the Orcs mount their attack.

'There is still time in which to prepare; we must make the most of it. Travel to the Way of Smiths among the Silvertine Lodes and lend your aid to the dwarves working in the Heart of Fire.

'The hammer-blow may fall hardest there, if Mazog were to learn the importance of those forges to our continued resistance. Stóthkell is in charge of the effort there; go to him with my commendation of your merits.''It is true, then, this rumour that the Orcs are planning some great assault on us? I was afraid it was so.

'I do not need Bósi's recommendation to know that you are an asset to our efforts here; were it not for you, the Heart of Fire would still be sealed to us!''The dwarf in charge of the Heart of Fire is Stóthkell; he will listen to our plight and arrange the best means of preparing to defend the forges that are so valuable to our continued survival.'Stóthkell is glad to have your help preparing the Heart of Fire for the coming storm.Rink Stronghammer is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths, among the Silvertine Lodes.

Stóthkell has asked you to aid his lieutenant with preparations for the defence of the Heart of Fire.Aid Rink Stronghammer with his preparationsStóthkell is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths, among the Silvertine Lodes.

You have aided Rink Stronghammer with his preparations and should now report of your successes to Stóthkell.Talk to Stóthkell in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths'My lieutenant will tell you how best to help us with the preparations, ${PLAYER}. I would trust Rink Stronghammer with my life. Ask him what should be done, and make it so.

'We here in the Heart of Fire will stand against the Orcs until the very end. And then, if all else seems lost, we will shut the door.

'We will only do so at the greatest need, though. Help Rink with the preparation for our defence, and the time until we must shut the door may be long put off.''I have already heard what you have done, here -- excellent work in assisting with the preparations for our defence!

'You have my thanks, even though I start to wonder if the Orcs will even dare to attack us.''Speak to Rink Stronghammer here in the Heart of Fire about preparing for our defence.'Rink Stronghammer is concerned that the goblins have established a network of runners throughout the Water-works and wants you to disrupt it.Goblin-runners bring word of the enemy's plans throughout the Water-works.

Rink Stronghammer wants you to defeat goblin runners, thus disrupting goblin communications in the Water-works.Defeat goblin-runners in the Water-works (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rink Stronghammer is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths among the Silvertine Lodes.

You have disrupted goblin communications in the Water-works and should now return to Rink Stronghammer.'Goblins can move quickly when they want to. The filthy creatures are not very intelligent, but they can still do a lot of damage if they coordinate their attacks. If we disrupt their ability to communicate, they may be less effective at organizing a serious attack on the Heart of Fire.

'Scouts have reported that goblin runners are moving through the Water-works, running and swimming and creeping and crawling. If you defeat many of these runners, they will be less able to signal the timing of their attack.

'The more time we have to construct barricades and other defences, the better off we will be. Disrupting goblin communication in the Water-works will buy us this time.''Good work. The goblins are surely in disarray, and will find it difficult to mount an effective attack for some time.''Travel to the Water-works and defeat goblin-runners there. We will disrupt their communications and leave their plans in disarray. But be alert! The creatures can run and swim with great speed.'Wafi wants you to search through debris piles throughout Moria for useable weapons that can be salvaged for use by the craftsmen in the Heart of Fire.Wafi gave you a list of places to search for debris piles that might contain useable weapons that can be melted down by the craftsmen at the Heart of Fire.

Wafi needs raw materials with which to craft equipment for the defence of the Heart of Fire and has asked you to search debris piles throughout Moria for useable weapons.Search piles of old weapons for useable materials (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wafi is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths among the Silvertine Lodes.

You have collected many suitable weapons that can be melted down for use in the forges of the Heart of Fire.'There is nothing more frustrating for a skilled dwarf-craftsman than having the use of a great forge such as this without enough raw materials with which it can be utilized! And if there is anything more irksome than that, it is the knowledge that when the Orcs attack, we might not have been able to equip our people with sufficient weapons and armour.

'It is my understanding that you aided Lord Bósi's son in taking weapons, armour, and helms from the Orcs so that his assault on the White Hand in Moria would be victorious. You are just the right ${RACE} for the job, then.

'We have sent scouts throughout Moria, and they have catalogued a list of likely places to find such weapons. I will give you this catalogue so you may keep track of the places you have searched for useable weapons.''The catalogue I gave you should tell you the places to search for debris piles. Our scouts believe these places might contain weapons suitable for use in the crafting of equipment here in the Heart of Fire.''These weapons will do nicely -- not for fighting, of course, as they are very old and not in fighting condition, but for melting down over the forges of the Heart of Fire!

'We will get to making higher quality weapons and armour at once! You have been a great help, ${PLAYER}.'Stóthkell is satisfied with the work you have done to help prepare the Heart of Fire for war, and wants you to do the same for the dwarves at the Twenty-first Hall.Brogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.

You have helped the dwarves in the Heart of Fire to prepare the defence, and Stóthkell wants you to do the same for the dwarves of the Twenty-first Hall.'The Heart of Fire is now ready for war, ${PLAYER}. We have begun making high-quality equipment for the defenders and strong barricades to help our position, and we owe much to your great assistance.

'But we absolutely cannot lose the Twenty-first Hall. You must return to Brogur in the Chamber of Leadership and render him equal assistance.

'The Orcs will surely be caught off guard by our excellent defences! I'd wager they are confident that we will be caught unawares.''You return to us in time to help us prepare the defences; and not just the defences, for I will not sit here in idleness while the Orcs make their own preparations. We will harry them even as we make ready to defend Zelem-melek!''Report to Brogur in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. If you can render even half of the assistance you did us, the dwarves there have little to fear from Orcs.'Brogur wants you to harry Orcs in the Flaming Deeps even as you gather materials with which to construct barricades for the defence of the Twenty-first Hall.Iron bars and wooden slats can be found throughout the Flaming Deeps of Moria, where Orcs of the Ghâsh-hai make ready for war.

Brogur wants you to collect materials that can be used for making barricades to defend the Twenty-first Hall.Collect iron bars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect wooden slats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Harass the Orcs of the Ghâsh-hai within the Flaming Deeps, south of Anazârmekhem.

Brogur wants you to harrass the Orcs after collecting the materials that can be used for making barricades to defend the Twenty-first Hall.Defeat Ghâsh-hai Orcs within the Flaming Deeps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Brogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.

You have gathered materials for the construction of effective barricades and have also thinned the ranks of the Ghâsh-hai.'Our defences will be ready by the time the Orcs attack, but I would feel far more secure if we had more barricades. It is clear that Stóthkell and the craftsmen in the Heart of Fire have their hands full making enough for their own defence; we cannot burden them further.

'Nay, we will need to gather iron bars and wooden slats for the construction of our own barricades. Look for these items in the Flaming Deeps, and harass the Orcs of the Ghâsh-hai while you do!''Orcs of the Ghâsh-hai prepare for war within the Flaming Deeps of Moria. Defeat the vile creatures and gather iron bars and wooden slats from their camps that we can use to construct effective barricades.''These materials are just what we need, ${PLAYER}, but I am even more heartened by the damage you have done to the ranks of the Ghâsh-hai.'Caras Galadhon is the mighty city of the Lord and Lady of the Galadhrim, nestled amid the tall mallorn trees.NOT USEDThe House of Celeborn is the home of the Lord and Lady of Lothlórien.This pleasant garden is where Galadriel keeps her most unusual and mysterious possession: the Mirror of Galadriel.This beautiful and ornate fountain is a testament to the artistry of the Elves.This pavilion is where the Company of the Ring resides during its stay in Lothlórien.This series of flets is the centre of learning in Caras Galadhon.Telain Bangad and their sister flets, Telain Melthin, are the centre of trade in Lothlórien.Telain Melthin and their sister flets, Telain Bangad, are the centre of trade in Lothlórien.This series of flets is a popular gathering place among the Galadhrim.Telain Neduil has a far view of the eastern landscapes of Lothlórien.Fungus-infested Orcs, called the Globsnaga by the Orcs of Moria, dwell throughout the Foundations of Stone.Globsnaga Orcs infest the Foundations of Stone.

Valthor has asked you to defeat Globsnaga Orcs to prove your might.Defeat Globsnaga Orcs in the Foundations of Stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Valthor is at the Shadowed Refuge in the northern region of the Foundations of Stone.

You should return to Valthor and tell him of your deeds.Talk to Valthor at the Shadowed Refuge'Few warriors such as ourselves live long enough to recall their deeds in battle. Fewer still live up to their own tales.

'If you wish to further your skills, I'll need to see just how much truth there is to what I've heard of you.

'To begin, prove yourself by defeating some of the Globsnaga Orcs that infest the Foundations of Stone. We'll speak again if you've lived to tell the tale.''If you wish to show me you're a true champion, head out into the Foundations of Stone and defeat a few of those Globsnaga Orcs for me.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. Your skill in battle has lived up to your reputation.

'I have use for one with your skill in arms. Khazad-dûm has been fraught with peril since Durin's Bane slew Durin VI, and we need all the help we can get.

'Speak with me again later, and we will continue your training.'Svanr wishes to travel eastward through Nud-melek once more.The summoning horn can be found near the Bridge of Khazad-dûm, behind Svanr in Nud-melek.

You should summon Svanr to your side when you are ready to leave.Summon Svanr using the summoning horn when you are ready to leaveA good place to rest can likely be found near Sudulthurkh, the northern cross-roads of Nud-melek. Svanr can be summoned using the horn he gave you.

You should make your way east across Nud-melek by heading north of the great chasm.Svanr is at the cross-roads of Sudulthurkh in north-eastern Nud-melek.

You should speak with Svanr.'I am ready to leave and head eastward, ${PLAYER}. Will you escort me on my journey? With the bridge gone, I fear the way might be dangerous.''This is a good place to rest, ${PLAYER}. Let us pause here.''How my feet ache! We have come a long way from Durin's Threshold, my friend. I am glad to make this last leg of my journey with so stalwart a companion!'Svanr was nearly killed by a spear flung at him as he climbed down Khadar-zarâm, the great stair of Nud-melek. That can only mean one thing: goblins up above!Enemies can be found on the highest levels of Khadar-zarâm in Nud-melek.

You should defeat enemies that wait upon the stair to waylay innocent travellers.Defeat enemies atop Khadar-zarâm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Svanr can be found at the foot of the great stair in western Nud-melek.

You should return to Svanr and tell him that you have cleared out many enemies within Khadar-zarâm.Return to Svanr'Did you encounter any danger upon the stair? I ask because I was nearly killed by a spear flung at me from above. I suspect goblins are the culprit, but they were too cowardly to show themselves.

'If you climb up again, I have no doubt that you will find scheming, mischievous goblins waiting with pointy sticks at the ready. I, for one, will not miss them if you wish to cleave a few of their skulls.''Well done! Now I need not fear that my toes get impaled by hurling spears when I begin my ascent!'The Galadhrim are preparing for war against the Orcs of Moria. They have sent a call out to all who will aid them.Complete Lórien Quest Tier 1Complete quests in Lothlórien.Complete quests in LothlórienPada has asked you to find a special sheet of music to accompany the instrument you recovered.The deep-claw Snapjaw can be found in the Redhorn Lodes south-west of the bridge that crosses the crevace south of the Broken Stair.

Snapjaw has been rumoured to hoard a great deal of paper-scraps and texts, undoubtedly some of great historic value, to build nests for its brood. Pada wishes you to recover a sheet of music that can likely be taken from Snapjaw upon its defeat.Defeat Snapjaw in the Redhorn LodesAcquire musical text from Snapjaw's corpsePada is in the Foundations of Stone, east from the Redhorn Lodes and then south to the Shadowed Refuge.

You should return to Pada with the musical text you have found, and hopefully it will be the one that he is seeking.'The instrument you've found will undoubtedly serve you well on your ventures, for you are a great minstrel, and such a tool well befits you. There is nothing better than a tune played from the heart on a piece such as this, but we are still missing a key thing: written music!

'There is a deep-claw in the Redhorn Lodes, Snapjaw, that is known to hoard papers and scraps of text to make nests for its foul broods. I believe that if you go there and slay that beast, you will find the very sheet we seek.

'Snapjaw was last seen just south and west of the bridge that crosses the crevace south of the Broken Stair.  Go there slay this deep-claw, ${PLAYER}. Search its hoard for any musical knowledge that may prove useful and bring it back to me, and I will see if you have found the missing ticket.''You were very brave to face that beastly deep-claw, ${PLAYER}! This looks to be precisely what we needed.

'Now, let me see what is scribed on this sheet....'

Pada begins to pore over paper you've brought him.You and Svanr saw a great number of Orcs pushing mine-carts at Sudulthurkh, clearly bearing war-supplies eastward.Orcs can be found pushing mine-carts at the cross-roads of Sudulthurkh in Nud-melek, north of the great chasm.

You should defeat the war-mongering Orcs of Moria before they can wreak havoc upon the Dale.Defeat Orcs at Sudulthurkh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Svanr can be found in a corner of the path just east of Sudulthurkh.

You should speak with Svanr.Return to Svanr at Sudulthurkh'Did you see those Orcs at the cross-roads of Sudulthurkh, ${PLAYER}? They were pushing mine-carts along the road. I think they are carrying war-supplies eastward!

'I cannot guess why... why would the Orcs of Moria wish to face the sun? I may never know the answer, but we should stop them, if we can.''The Orcs can be found just south of here, on the cross-roads of Sudulthurkh.''I am glad you thinned their ranks, ${PLAYER}! The Dale will be safer, as will the road eastward.'Many enemies prowl the Second Hall of Nud-melek.Enemies and vile creatures can be found in the Second Hall of Nud-melek.

You should defeat enemies in the Second Hall.Defeat enemies and monsters in the Second Hall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of enemies in the Second Hall of Nud-melek.CompletedMany enemies prowl the Second Hall of Nud-melek.

You should defeat the forces of evil that roam this hall.You have defeated a number of enemies in the Second Hall of Nud-melek.A number of flet-runners throughout Caras Galadhon have challenged you to join their ranks by demonstrating your awareness of the city's layout and the quickness of your feet.Complete 'At Home Among the Trees'Complete 'Flet-runner Challenge: Leginiel'Complete 'Flet-runner Challenge: Lagordal'Complete 'Flet-runner Challenge: Bregradel'Complete 'Flet-runner Challenge: Lintwen'Sadreda has more for you to do, but requires one last task of endurance before he begins.Mosco Mudbottom can be found at Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands, far to the north and west of Moria.

Sadreda has instructed you to speak with a warden by the name of Mosco Mudbottom.Talk to Mosco Mudbottom at Ost Guruth'There are things you need to learn before I continue your instruction, and not all of them can be learned here.

'Before we continue, ${PLAYER}, I want you to speak with another member of our order, Mosco Mudbottom. You will find him at Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands, far to the north and west of Moria.

'Mosco, I am sure, will have a task for you. Think of this as part of your training...a test of endurance and patience.''Mosco Mudbottom may be found at Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands.''Well met, ${PLAYER}. You have the look of one of our order about you.

'Sadreda sent you, you say? Well, I can see why. You have the look of an experienced adventurer that yearns for more knowledge.

'I think I know just the thing.'How they found their way into Moria is unclear, but the forces of the White Hand are now entrenched in the Orc communities of Khazad-dûm. However, it appears to Thithrand that they wish to claim leadership over Moria for themselves.White Hand Orcs can be found in the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.

Thithrand mentioned that the White Hand Orcs found in the Grand Stair are lesser images of their leaders, and that there is a good number of the foe within. You should use caution when you face them.Defeat White Hand Pummellers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat White Hand Shields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat White Hand Arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Thithrand with news of your successes.Talk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch'Reports from all throughout Khazad-dûm say that the Orcs of the White Hand have no intention to kneel to Mazog, but still they come to the Grand Stair, offering their tribute to Igash. Still they stand among the Orcs within Khazad-dûm.

'When you breach the Grand Stair, north-east from the Orc-watch, seek to defeat the White Hand Orcs where they stand. There are many of these foes to be found within. The lesser, simpler beings are akin to their masters in many ways.

'Be cautious and decisive in your assault, ${PLAYER}.''It is good to know that the White Hand Orcs meant to betray the other Orcs, and better still that you were able to cull so many.

'The Grand Stair may yet be returned to its former glory, thanks to your efforts.''The White Hand's host can be found in the Grand Stair, mingling with the hosts of Moria. I doubt not that they seek to overturn their leadership.'The Galadhrim are wary of strangers. It takes much to earn their trust.Become 'Known to the Galadhrim'Complete 'The Paths of Caras Galadhon'The outpost of Mekhem-bizru awaits your aid.Mekhem-bizru can be found just outside of the East Gate of Moria, in the Dimrill Dale.

You should speak to someone at Mekhem-bizru.Talk to someone at Mekhem-bizru'You look as though you are ready to move on at last, my friend.

'Why do you not head over to Mekhem-bizru? It will be an adequate resting point before you head into the deadly trees of Lothlórien.''Welcome, welcome! As you can see, all are welcome at Mekhem-bizru, where Elves and dwarves come together to face the enemies of Moria and Lórien.

'What can we do for you here? Your travels in Khazad-dûm must have wearied you.'Valthor considers pride in one's own abilities paramount to a champion.Dwalin's throne is in Thorin's Hall, far to the west of Moria.

Valthor has instructed you to go forth and boast of your great deeds before the throne of Dwalin.Thrymur is near Dwalin's throne in Thorin's Hall.

Speak with him now that you have proclaimed your deeds to all assembled in Thorin's Hall.Talk to Thrymur at Thorin's HallValthor is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone in Moria, far to the east of Thorin's Hall.

Now that you have boasted to the dwarves, return to Valthor.Talk  to Valthor at the Shadowed Refuge'Your skill in battle cannot be denied, ${PLAYER}.

'The difference between a good champion and a great one, however, is their renown. The peoples of Middle-earth need to know that there are warriors in the world capable of incredible martial prowess, risking their lives to fight the Enemy.

'For your second task, I want you to travel to Thorin's Hall. Ascend the steps toward Dwalin's throne and blow this horn, then proclaim your prowess as a champion to all gathered in the halls of the dwarves!''As a champion, demonstrating pride in your abilities speaks well of you. Go to Lord Dwalin's throne in Thorin's Hall and tell of your great deeds!''Ho there, ${PLAYER}. Show those hole-hiders at Thorin's Hall how much greater your deeds have been!''Well said, ${RACE}. Your proud words show you to be a great warrior in my eyes.

'Return to Valthor in Khazad-dûm and tell him what you have said here today. It will impress even him.''Let Valthor know that the Longbeards of Thorin's Hall have heard your tales and now sing songs of your valour.''Well done, well done!

'Now, ${PLAYER}, for your next task.'Orcs are not the only evil creature to inhabit the Foundations of Stone. There are also vile spiders.Luillë can be found in the Redhorn Lodes, north of the Claw Hollow and just west of the Foundations of Stone.

Valthor has asked you to defeat the spider Luillë and bring him her scent-glands.Collect scent-glands from the spider LuillëValthor is at the Shadowed Refuge, east from the Redhorn Lodes.

You should return to Valthor with Luillë's glands.'We are coming to the end of this adventure, ${PLAYER}. My next task for you is more practical in nature. In order to face your greatest challenge, you will have need of the scent-glands of a spider.

'Now for mighty warriors such as ourselves, simply slaying a common spider won't do. No, you will have face the great spider, Luillë. She can be found in the Redhorn Lodes, lurking in the shadows.

'Come back to me with the glands, and we will see this adventure completed.''Luillë is a terrible creature...I want her scent-gland as proof of her demise!''Well done, ${PLAYER}. I have no doubt that your deeds will live on long after your spirit has departed from Middle-earth.

'Now, let us see to your final task.'Nameless hordes plague the deep places of Moria.Nameless can be found in the south-west reaches of the Foundations of Stone.

Sadreda has asked you to prove your worth by defeating the Nameless.Defeat Nameless in the Foundations of Stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sadreda is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, north-west from the lairs of the Nameless there.

You should return to Sadreda with news of your victory.Talk to Sadreda at the Shadowed Refuge'You have the look of an experienced Warden, ${PLAYER}. As you well know, ours is the job of protecting homelands, no matter how odd "home" might seem.

'In this case, the dwarves seek to reclaim their ancient home of Moria, likely the largest city ever known to the peoples of Middle-earth.

'If you would lend your aid, the dwarves of the Iron Garrison would be most grateful, as would I. There are many Nameless that infest the south-east reaches of the Foundations of Stone. Hunt them down, then return to me when you are finished.''Well done, ${PLAYER}.  Let us speak of your next task.'There are many opportunities to perform great deeds for the Galadhrim of Lothlórien.Complete all deeds within LothlórienComplete Wanderer of the Golden WoodComplete Lórien Look-outComplete City of the Lord and LadyComplete Beast-slayer (Advanced)Complete Orc-slayer (Advanced)Svanr would like you to accompany him when he leaves the east gate of Moria.Svanr is in the First Hall of Moria, in Nud-melek.

You should speak with Svanr to travel into the Dale.Journey with Svanr to the Dimrill DaleSvanr is at the First Hall of Moria.

You should speak with Svanr.Talk to Svanr'It is time for us to set foot in the open air once more. I do not know about you, but I never thought Khazad-dûm would be so deadly.

'I am glad I will have completed my venture across all of it, but gladder still to have made it out alive. Come, ${PLAYER}! Let us go smell the fresher air.''To the Dale! Let's go, ${PLAYER}.''I feel better already! A bit of fresh air does one good, even a dwarf. Now I cannot wait to delve back into the great mine! I have not yet decided where to settle... perhaps the Deep Descent, or the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

'Sunlight is a lovely break from the dark, but I am a dwarf, after all.'You have been instructed to find Dithrik in the Foundations of Stone in Moria in order to further your prowess as a Guardian.Dithrik can be found in the Foundations of Stone in Moria. 

You should seek Dithrik if you wish to further your skills as a Guardian, for the trainers of Eriador have little less to show you in this stage of your learning.Speak with Dithrik in the Foundations of StoneDithrik can be found in the Foundations of Stone in Moria. 

You should seek Dithrik if you wish to further your skills as a Guardian, for the trainers of Eriador have little less to show you in this stage of your learning.Speak with Dithrik in the Foundations of StoneYou should find Dithrik in the Foundations of Stone in Moria in order to further your prowess as a Guardian.'Well met, ${PLAYER}. I am at your service, and your family's. I have heard much praise of your deeds in Moria, and I will gladly share anything I have to teach with such a noble Guardian as yourself. The time is nigh for the dwarves to reclaim their ancient home of Moria, and your aid has been invaluable.

'I see that you are here because your strength as a Guardian has outgrown your skills somewhat.  I believe I can teach you a skill that will serve you well into the future.

'Let us speak further of how you can contribute to our cause here in Moria, for there is much to do.'The gredbyg of Skûmfil are a vile breed of scavengers, and among them are terrible warrior-class insects.Longpincer is in Skûmfil, east of the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.

Valthor has asked you to complete the Path of the Martial Champion by slaying the grodbog Longpincer.Defeat LongpincerValthor is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, west from Skûmfil.

You should return to Valthor with news of your victory.'You have done very well to have come this far, ${PLAYER}. One task remains between you and eternal glory.

'Take these scent-glands you collected from Luillë and head into Skûmfil, the vile corpse-pile used by the Orcs. While there, use the scent-glands upon the ancient altar within to summon the grodbog Longpincer. The creature will not be able to resist the scent produced by the glands.

'Be sure to bring your friends, for this is no small feat. Slay the grodbog, then return to me.''Longpincer is yet another verminous threat in the Foundations that needs to be dealt with. You can find the creature in Skûmfil.''Most impressive, ${PLAYER}.  

'This day you have truly earned the title of Champion. May your name ever after serve as a source of terror for the Enemy.

'Rest well, you have earned it.'In order to further your skills as a hunter, you have been instructed to seek out Armbeald in the Redhorn Lodes of Moria.Armbeald is at the Orc-Watch in the north-west region of the Redhorn Lodes of Moria.

You should find Armbeald, a renowned hunter who should be able to assist you with further advancement at a high level of skill.Talk to Armbeald in the Redhorn LodesArmbeald is at the Orc-Watch in the north-west region of the Redhorn Lodes of Moria.

You should find Armbeald, a renowned hunter who should be able to assist you with further advancement at a high level of skill.Talk to Armbeald in the Redhorn LodesIn order to further your skills as a hunter, you should seek out Armbeald in the Redhorn Lodes of Moria.'Well met, friend Hunter. You have sought me and here I am, so what would you ask of me after coming all this way? I see that you wish to find more than a mere shooting-trick today.

'There comes a time in all our lives when standard skills of the trade simply won't suffice, and we must go deeper. Is this why you have sought me, greatest hunter and trapper in the lands from whence I hail?

'Perhaps I can help you. If you pass the test, I will teach you everything I can, for you will indeed be worthy of learning if you can overcome the challenges you have in store. Come, let us speak further.'The call of Nanulg's battle-horn would be such an insult to the Orcs of Fil-gashan that they would not dare to ignore its call.Fil-gashan lies in the south-western reaches of the Flaming Deeps.

Garnyd has instructed you to use Nanlug's battle-horn to challenge the Orcs in Fil-gashan.Challenge Orcs inside Fil-gashan near their battle standardGarnyd is at Anazârmekhem, north from Fil-gashan.

You should return to Garnyd with news of your victory.'For your final task, ${PLAYER}, you will take this battle-horn into Fil-gashan and look for the battle standard of the Orcs therein. When you find the standard, make use of it and defeat the Orcs that come to your call...and come they will. There is no way they can ignore the insult of their former leader's battle-horn being used to challenge them.

'Begin your search in a place where many Orcs gather.  It is likely that their battle standard is there; and more likely still that the Orcs will answer the call of their fallen leader's battle-horn.

'Remember that your task in this fight as a captain is to inspire your fellow warriors to continue the fight.

'When you have won the battle, return to me.'Garnyd salutes you.

'You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Your deeds have inspired warriors on the field of battle and will inspire man, woman, and child for years to come.

'You have shown your worth, and I daresay its worth is greater than the mithril that was once the fame of Moria.'It is time to leave Moria at last, and soak up the fresh air again.Svanr is in the First Hall of Nud-melek.Talk to SvanrSvanr can be found outside of Moria, in the Dimrill Dale.

You should speak with Svanr.Follow Svanr to the Dimrill DaleMekhem-bizru can be found down the path from the East Gate of Moria.Talk to someone at Mekhem-bizruKheled-zâram is the great lake that lies on the Dimrill Dale.

You should speak to a dwarf looking out upon Kheled-zâram.Talk to a dwarf at the Mirrormere's edgeThe Mirrormere, also called Kheled-zâram, is the lake that lies against Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.

You should <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out upon the Mirrormere from Mekhem-bizru.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest requires emotes.</rgb>Svanr is in the Dimrill Dale.

You should speak with Svanr.Return to Svanr'I feel refreshed, and ready to return to the depths of Khazad-dûm to continue helping the expedition establish a foothold.

'What do you plan to do?''I cannot wait to see the sun, moon, clouds, and stars once more! This trek has been a long one, and sad. We have suffered many losses.

'I cannot be more thankful to lay eyes upon the fair sun once more, ${PLAYER}.''Here we are. If you don't mind, ${PLAYER}, I would like a moment to myself.''Welcome to Mekhem-bizru! I am pleased to see that you made it out of Moria with your skin still intact. You must be a bold warrior.

'You may rest here, and look out upon fair Kheled-zâram.''Beautiful, is it not? It is true that the stars of the Mirrormere shimmer always upon the surface of the water, be it day or night. Look for yourself!''How fair and fresh the Dale! I am glad I lived to see it.'You have finally made your way into the mysterious chamber to which the convoluted instructions in a map you found have led you.Search for the innermost chamber of the secret hall -- following the clues may help find it faster.Search for the innermost chamberInvestigate the weapon on the dais within the innermost chamber.Examine the weapon closelyByrski Hardprow has offered to seek out Durin's Crown in the Mirrormere, hoping it might herald an auspicious end to the Iron Garrison's reclamation of Khazad-dûm.Byrski Hardprow has sailed the Saervig onto the Mirrormere.Talk to Byrski HardprowLarboard can be found on the left side of a ship, when facing toward the bow.

