You have been engulfed in a curious light, but Byrski appears concerned. You should talk to Byrski Hardprow.Talk to Byrski Hardprow'I think it is time we sailed back to Mekhem-bizru, ${PLAYER}.''Ah, the Saervig is a fine ship, my friend. And look, Durin himself greets us!'

Byrski takes a moment to look around on the decks of the Saervig.

'Very good! Let us begin our search for Durin's Crown, ${PLAYER}. And remember, you're looking for seven stars in the shape of a crown. I'll start over here, so why don't you have a look from larboard?''Nothing? No luck at all?'

Byrski sighs.

'I had hoped it would be easier than this, my friend. I'll take one last look, and then we can sail back to Mekhem-bizru. I just don't want to let the Iron Garrison down!''${PLAYER}! Are you all right?

'You were looking into the Mirrormere and then it seemed to me that you became lost in some deep reverie. Is this a common occurrence, my friend? I do not mean to alarm you, but it has been nearly ten minutes! What happened? Did you see Durin's Crown?'

You tell Byrski that you were engulfed in a brilliant light, and that its warmth lifted your spirits and granted you a renewed sense of purpose as a Mariner. You suggest that it could have been the fabled Star of Eärendil, but you remain uncertain.

'The Star of Eärendil?! I thought that was just an old Mariner's tale—a guiding star to find shelter upon the Sea. And besides, I didn't see any light! I may be one eye short, but I would think I'd have noticed something like that! Perhaps your adventures have been too taxing of late, my friend.

'Ah, but I am... fairly certain that I spotted Durin's Crown! It had the proper number of stars, and it did appear to be in the shape of a crown, so I think our expedition was a success!'You cannot seem to get the Bridge of Khazad-dûm out of your mind....The bridge of Khazad-dûm lies in the east of Nud-melek.

