'I understand that you have come to a point in your studies that will require more aggressive research in order to better your skills. I believe I know just the thing to help you on your way.

'Come, let us speak further on how we can help each other.'Many flets, where the guards of the Galadhrim keep watch, dot the Golden Wood, ensuring that no enemy can approach unnoticed.NOT USEDTalan Fanuidhol is where the Galadhrim stage their defence against the Orcs of Moria mustering within Fanuidhol.This is one of many flets guarding the borders of LothlórienThis is one of many flets guarding the borders of Lothlórien.This is one of many flets guarding the borders of Lothlórien.This is one of many flets guarding the borders of Lothlórien.This is one of many flets guarding the borders of Lothlórien.This is one of many flets guarding the borders of Lothlórien.This flet overlooks a grove of Melbrethil.This flet overlooks the nests of many hawks.Haldir, Marchwarden of Lothlórien, and his brothers Rúmil and Orophin make their camp here.This is the place where Amroth once had his home, and later, where Aragorn and Arwen first met and fell in love.Deep within the halls of Moria, flames lick out of oily pools. It is here that the Ghâsh-hai make their home. A faction of these is aligned with the master of Moria, Mazog, and has come to the Grand Stair to pay tribute to their leader.Gothghaash can be found within the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.

Ossur told you of Gothghaash, the leader of the Fire-orcs, and directed you to find and defeat him.Defeat Gothghaash the FirecallerOssur is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Ossur at the Orc-watch and tell him of your victory over Gothghaash.Talk to Ossur at the Orc-watch'While the Ghâsh-hai prove to be a potent foe, they too have leaders, and theirs made his way into the Grand Stair some time ago.

'The Ghâsh-hai tend to gather near flame. When you make your way to the Grand Stair, search for a source of flame, and there you will find their leader, Gothghaash.

'Find him and destroy him, so that we might more easily remove the foe from the Grand Stair. Travel north-east from the Orc-watch to find the entrance to the Grand Stair.''With the head of the tribe removed, we should be able to keep the power of the Ghâsh-hai at bay. This news is very good, ${PLAYER}.

'We shall reclaim the Grand Stair in no time.''Be prepared to face a foe at home in the flame. Seek Gothghaash within the confines of the Grand Stair to the north-east of the Orc-watch.'The Grand Stair once stood at the foot of a great cross-roads within Moria. At the height of the great city, it led to all areas of the halls and was a majestic wonder to behold. Now it has fallen to the care of Igash, a lieutenant of the Moria Orc-leader Mazog. Igash assembled the forces of Orcs and trolls within Moria in one place and has collected tribute from each to one day bring to the leader of the Orcs. For now, each tribe vies for favour from the lieutenant, a fanatical follower of Mazog.Avar is at the Orc-watch.

Avar has asked you to assist him with two tasks to earn his faith and satisfy him that the Orcs of the Grand Stair are no longer a serious threat.Help Avar defeat the leaders of the Orcs within the Grand StairHelp Avar weaken the forces of the Moria Orcs in the Grand StairAvar is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

Now that Avar's tasks are complete, you should return to him with your report.Talk to Avar at the Orc-watch'I have watched the comings and goings of the Orcs here and come to know that there are two of great note. The first is Igash, a fanatical leader who is pledged to serving Mazog. He rules the Grand Stair and uses his Devoted, the second of these Orcs of note, to keep his troops cowed.

'Igash collects great tributes from the other Orc-tribes and stores them in his throne room. He coerces them into delivering more of this tribute to him in an effort to play them against one another and gain wealth for his master.

'I have paid closer attention on this foe so that we might ruin his power and drive him from the Grand Stair. There are two tasks I would have you complete to satisfy my call for assistance. Will you aid me?''The leaders of the Moria Orcs must be slain and their number must be thinned. If you complete the two tasks I lay before you, you will earn my favour.''Aye, the tasks are done. The Moria Orcs are weaker, and your efforts will grant us the ability to keep a closer watch on these forces. Once you have completed the tasks for Thithrand and Ossur, I will send word on to Narfi that the Orcs of the Grand Stair are no longer a threat.'You have been instructed to find Pada in the Foundations of Stone in Moria in order to further your prowess as a Minstrel.Pada has travelled to Moria to lend his aid to the dwarf-expedition that has gone to excavate the mines.

Pada is a very advanced Minstrel of great renown, and you should call on him to learn what he has to teach as you bring your skills to a peak.Talk to PadaPada has travelled to Moria to lend his aid to the dwarf-expedition that has gone to excavate the mines.

Pada is a very advanced Minstrel of great renown, and you should call on him to learn what he has to teach as you bring your skills to a peak.Talk to PadaYou have been summoned by Pada in the Foundations of Stone in Moria in order to further your prowess as a Minstrel.'Why hullo there! If you are looking for Pada, you have found him! So stand up straight and let me have a look at you, ${RACE}.

'What have we here? You certainly have a sincere look to you, and a sort of kindness in your expression. Yet you are worn with travel and toil, and sadness too. I think I know why you are here.

'Come, let us talk for a while. I can see that you are also a Minstrel of great skill, nay, not by your instrument, but by the very look of you! Did you not know that Minstrels shine with a subtle radiance? Yet we bow under the heavy burden we carry, for we give our hearts that others may endure.'The Nameless seem to be corrupted creatures of an earlier age, though from what source their corruption comes or what they once were, none can say. They are deadly foes and attack without discrimination, hungry for the blood of any that wander too near their grasp.Defeat Nameless in MoriaYou have defeated many Nameless foes, but their threat in Moria is hardly lessened. Any who combat these terrible beings are worthy of the strength they will gain from such an effort.Defeat Nameless in MoriaRumour of the dark things that dwell in the depths of Moria have reached even the ears of Mosco Mudbottom in the Lone-lands.The Dark Warden, if it exists, dwells somewhere within the Foundations of Stone in Moria, far to the east and south of the Lone-lands.

Mosco Mudbottom has tasked you with discovering the lair of the Dark Warden and bringing the creature's head to Sadreda.'Rumour has reached me here of many dark things that dwell in Moria. The place has an ill reputation, but there is supposedly a creature the dwarves dredged up there that is particularly vile. I'm quite surprised Sadreda did not send you after it himself.

'You should travel back to the Foundations of Stone and seek out the creature known as The Dark Warden. I can't promise it actually exists -- rumours are rumours, after all -- but if it does, it should be defeated.

'If it does indeed exist, bring its head to Sadreda as evidence of your victory.''The Dark Warden may be found in the Foundations of Stone in Moria.''I see your journey was well worth the effort, ${PLAYER}. And what is this you have?

'I see...Mosco Mudbottom was right. I do know how you must proceed from here.

'This next step will be most perilous...are you ready?'It is time to make for the East Gate of Moria, at long last.The Summoning Horn can be found near Svanr at his small camp in northern Nud-melek.

You should use the Summoning Horn to call Svanr when you are ready to depart.Use the Summoning Horn to call Svanr to your sideThe First Hall can be found at the eastern-most gate of Nud-melek. Svanr can be summoned using the horn he gave you.

You should head east with Svanr to finish your pilgrimage through Moria.The First Hall can be found at the eastern-most gate of Nud-melek.

You should head east with Svanr to finish your pilgrimage through Moria.'I am rested, and I see that you are eager to get moving. Shall we make our final journey together, ${PLAYER}?

'I was told by many that the dwarves hold the First Hall. I hope this means that the remainder of our trip will not be too difficult.''From Durin's Threshold to the First Hall, and Great Delving to Nud-melek. Think of all the halls we wandered to make it so far. Well, here we are! Let us put up our feet.''We made it! At last, we will smell the clean air again, and feel the sun upon our faces.

'I am mighty glad we defeated the Orc-parties making their way eastward. I thought this camp would be better defended, but I do not think these dwarves could withstand a push from Mazog's Orcs.'Orc-barriers can be found at the Crack's Edge in central Nud-melek.Orc-barriers can be found throughout the Crack's Edge in the centre of Nud-melek.

You should destroy Orc-barriers.Destroy Orc-barriers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have destroyed several Orc-barriers at the Crack's Edge camp.CompletedThe Orcs at the Crack's Edge have set up barriers to protect themselves. Tearing them down will show them that there is no protection from the Iron Garrison and its allies.You have destroyed several Orc-barriers at the Crack's Edge camp.The Orcs of Moria have poured out of the Misty Mountains into the Dimrill Dale and Fanuidhol. It will take a brave heart to drive them back.Defeat Orcs in the Dimrill Dale and FanuidholThe Orcs of Moria have poured out of the Misty Mountains into the Dimrill Dale and Fanuidhol. It will take a brave heart to drive them back.Defeat Orcs in the Dimrill Dale and FanuidholArmbeald has tasked you with finding the four missing teeth from the skull you brought him. He suggested you go to the White Hand Orcs in the Redhorn Lodes and search among the higher-ranking soldiers there.The Orcs suspected of taking the teeth are in the White Hand Orc-fortress in the Redhorn Lodes.   

Look for high-ranking Orcs in your search for the missing teeth. They should be defeated and their remains searched, and if any teeth are found, Armbeald in the Redhorn Lodes will wish to see them.Armbeald turns the skull over in his hand and frowns.

'Four teeth are indeed missing, but not through any act of violence. It looks like they were extracted, rather than knocked off by some careless gesture. I can venture a guess at what happened here.

'The Orcs of the White Hand favour bones as cosmetic trophies and trinkets. After the dwarf was murdered, his teeth were taken and his flesh devoured. Orcs are terrible creatures, and sport with their prey. They have no dignity, no respect for the dead as we do. They would just as soon despoil their own kind in this hideous manner.

'It is likely that the missing teeth can be found on the White Hand Orcs. Large teeth such as these would be considered valuable and are likely in the posession of the more senior amongst our nearby foes.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. We have begun to avenge our unfortunate friend.'The Orcs of Moria have looted many of the great treasures remaining in Moria after the fall of the dwarf-realm.Folok has been seen in the south-west portion of the Redhorn Lodes, near Malmezel, at the western edge of the Redhorn Lodes.

Márus has asked you to defeat the Orc Folok and recover the mithril chisel.'Well met, ${PLAYER}. There is an air about you that hints at your experience. From your attire, I must assume that you are a Rune-keeper much like myself. If greater knowledge is what you seek, then I can help. First, however, I have a task for you.

'Ancient Rune-keepers used fine chisels to carve out their speech-craft in stone. The finest of these tools were made of mithril and were said to have power in their own right.

'One such chisel has been seen recently, and I think it appropriate that we reclaim this instrument to further your own abilities. There is an Orc, Folok, in the south-west portion of the Redhorn Lodes near Malmezel. Seek out this Orc and slay him; our scouts believe they have seen the chisel in his possession.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}.  

'This is indeed a fine tool of dwarf-craft. Let us hope that it has not been fouled by its recent owner.'You found a journal left behind by a stonecarver from a past age. It relates how he repaid a service from his friend Falgeirr by creating many stone plaques, inscribed with various simple images, and decided to keep some for himself, that he might leave clues for his own descendants as to where his family's treasure was hidden.The plaques are located in Balin's Camp in Nud-melek.

The journal that Melkólf Stonecarver left behind contained the following puzzles:

The journal reads: 
 
"Dwarf who makes me has no need for me.
Dwarf who buys me has no use for me.
Dwarf who uses me would not want me."

"I have a hundred legs and cannot stand.
I have no head and a long neck.
I cannot see, but I am neat as can be."

"A hundred arms, a thousand fingers,
And no eyes to see where it is I linger."

"With a knife, cut open my head,
Then weep beside me when I am dead."

"I have no eyes, yet once did I see.
I once had thoughts, now I'm empty."

And then comes this strange little verse:

"Hundred-arms comes before headless long-neck.
Head-cut-open is alone at the end.
Headless long-neck comes after dwarf-and-me and hundred-arms.
No-eyes comes after headless long-neck.
Dwarf-and-me comes after hundred-arms"

