The plaques associated with this puzzle are here in Balin's Camp!You have solved the puzzle of the carvings!Many of the Longbeards struggling to reclaim Moria have been daunted by the seemingly impossible task set before them.Eldur can be found at the Rotting Cellar, just west of the Flaming Deeps. Lythur can be found at Durin's Threshold at the western edge of the Great Delving, north of the Silvertine Lodes. Skafti can be found at Jazârgund in the middle of Durin's Way in the northern reaches of Moria.

Garnyd has asked you to raise the spirits of three dwarf-soldiers found throughout Moria: Eldur, Lythur, and Skafti.Raise Eldur's spiritsRaise Lythur's spiritsRaise Skafti's spiritsGarnyd is at Anazârmekhem in the Flaming Deeps.

Now that you have raised the dwarves' spirits, it is time to return to Garnyd.Talk to Garnyd at Anazârmekhem'We have seen that your actions will no doubt inspire those around you, but all too often it is a captain's words that embolden the hearts of people around them. It is said that the words of great captains throughout the ages have turned the tides of battles that would have otherwise been lost. Without the power of speech, a captain is little more than a common warrior.

'For your second task, I would have you speak with three dwarves. The first, Eldur, can be found at the Rotting Cellar, which lies west from here. The second, Lythur, is encamped at Durin's Threshold at the western edge of the Great Delving to the north-west. The third, Skafti, is at Jazârgund in the middle of Durin's Way to the north.

'Use your words to lift the hearts of these dwarves, for they have seen all too much despair and are now filled with sorrow.'Eldur's eyes light up ever so faintly as you approach him. You hear the tale of his recent defeat and remind him that death is but another step in one's journey through the ages.

Hearing this, his mood brightens and he nods slowly.

'Thank you, Captain. You have given my heart the strength that had been stolen from it naught but a few days ago.'Lythur stands to attention at your approach. You hear the tale of his recent encounters in Moria and offer him words of encouragment.

Hearing your words seems to put his mind at ease, and he relaxes visibly.Skafti meets your eyes and a look of recognition crosses his face.

'I've heard of you, ${PLAYER}. Your deeds have reached even the ears of the dwarves under the mountains. You need not speak another word. I know why you have come; and I say that a true captain's measure is in their mere presence, as you have shown me just now.

'If you will excuse me, Khazad-dûm is not yet under the rule of its rightful masters. There is much work I must do, and no rest to be had until this great Durin's Folk is completed.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. You are an inspiration to the people of Middle-earth.

'Let us see now to your next task.'The dwarf-mirrors of Khazad-dûm once illuminated the underground halls, but many of them have since fallen into disrepair or have been knocked out of alignment.Dwarves hold the East Gate of Moria in Nud-melek.

You should tell a guard of your continuing efforts towards lighting Khazad-dûm once more.Speak to a Guard at the East Gate of Moria in Nud-melekSwivelling this mirror back into place should restore some light to the halls of Khazad-dûm. Once you have finished, you should seek out someone at the East Gate of Moria in Nud-melek.'You found and corrected that mirror's position? Excellent! Did you run into any trouble?'You have solved a long series of riddles set by Falgeirr Twisttongue, and your journey has taken you through Khazad-dûm and out the East-gate, into the Dimrill Dale.Solve the last of Twisttongue's riddles to find the treasure:

A room in shadows with no door
No wood or tile make up my floor
Nature's art my columns carved
In my belly bears have starved

Step far down and water face
Right foot follow and road trace
Sunsetward and great rocks paired:
Twisttongue for his family cared.Find the answer to Twisttongue's last riddleYour reward lies within the chest in Falgeirr's cave.Collect your reward from the chestThe last of Falgeirr's riddles is affixed to the outside wall of Moria, under the sun. It reads:

A room in shadows with no door
No wood or tile make up my floor
Nature's art my columns carved
In my belly bears have starved

Step far down and water face
Right foot follow and road trace
Sunsetward and great rocks paired:
Twisttongue for his family cared.This chest is ancient but sturdy, and is not locked.Márus received a summons from Dwalin at Thorin's Hall, requesting your presence.Dwalin can be found in Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin, far to the west of Moria.

Márus has instructed you to go to Thorin's Hall and speak with Dwalin.Talk to Dwalin at Thorin's Hall'${PLAYER}, while you were away, I received a message from Thorin's Hall... asking for you. Dwalin would like to speak with you regarding your recent efforts here in Khazad-dûm. He is quite knowledgeable of old dwarf-runes and will likely be a source of great help to you.

'Thorin's Hall lies far to the west in Ered Luin. You should travel there as soon as possible, for Dwalin is a very important dwarf.''You should speak with Dwalin in Thorin's Hall.''Well met, ${PLAYER}. Aye, I've heard tell of you many a time.

'I myself have some skill in runes. When Thorin's Company had reclaimed the Lonely Mountain, we hid the treasure and safe-guarded it using our own rune-craft.'

Dwalin looks far off, as though recalling some memory long forgotten, then smiles.

'But enough about me; I've asked you here to help out with a matter of some great importance to our efforts to retake Khazad-dûm.'The Orcs at Hurmulkezer are led by a great War-leader named Nanulg. Without him, they might fall into disarray.Nanulg is at Hurmulkezer, south of Durin's Court along the southern edge of the Flaming Deeps.

Garnyd has instructed you to defeat Nanulg and take his horn.Collect Nanulg's hornGarnyd is at Anazârmekhem, in the northern reaches of the Flaming Deeps.

You should return to Garnyd with Nanulg's horn.'${PLAYER}, you have no doubt begun to understand the important role you play on the field of battle. But do you understand the importance of your counterparts among the enemy?

'There is an Orc at Hurmulkezer to the south-east named Nanulg. He commands the respect of many Orcs around him and represents a great obstacle in the dwarves' campaign to retake the Mines of Moria.

'I task you now with striking a strategic blow against the Orcs of this region. Find Nanulg and slay him. When you do, be sure to take his battle-horn. The horn alone will lower the morale of the Orcs that knew him in life.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. Now for your final task.'Márus has summoned you into his presence.Márus can be found somewhere within the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

You have been instructed to seek guidance from the Rune-keeper Márus.Talk to Márus at the Foundations of StoneMárus can be found somewhere within the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

You have been instructed to seek guidance from the Rune-keeper Márus.Talk to Márus at the Foundations of StoneMárus has summoned you into his presence to further your training as a Rune-keeper.'Well met, ${PLAYER}.

'I've heard that you are looking for further knowledge considering the crafting of runes. Well, you've come to the right place.

'Let us speak further about how we can help one another.'Sadreda has determined that the Dark Warden which you slew was but a servant of a more vile creature known as the Mad Captain.The Mad Captain dwells within the Dark Delvings, south-east from the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.

Sadreda instructed you to use the crude charm he gave you to summon and defeat the Mad Captain.Summon and defeat the Mad CaptainSadreda is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, north-west from the Dark Delvings.

You should return to Sadreda with news of your victory.'The final step of your quest will take you into great peril. I believe this Dark Warden you slew was but a servant of another creature we call the Mad Captain.

'Gather your friends, ${PLAYER}, and head into the Dark Delvings, south-east from here. Once inside, you will need to use this charm to summon the Mad Captain. Look for a foul altar, and place it there.  The Mad Captain will be sure to come out then.

'Rid Moria of the Mad Captain's foul evil, then return to me.''The Mad Captain may be found within the Dark Delvings in the Foundations of Stone.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}! Your efforts will be remembered for ages to come.'Dithrik has asked you to gather the glands of crawlers found throughout the Water Works.The Water Works are far to the south-west of the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

You should slay many crawlers in the Water Works and collect their pungent glands. When you have acquired enough, you should return to Dithrik at the Foundations of Stone.'You have done well to have come this far, ${PLAYER}, and have humbled me in the meantime. Now, let us see to our final preparations before we send you off to face one of Moria's oldest nightmares.

'The glands of crawlers that slither throughout the Water Works give off a strange scent that has been known to draw attention from the enemy, as one poor dwarf of the expedition was unlucky as to discover. If you wish to ensnare the ancient creature, the heads you acquired for me earlier will need the addition of the glands from these glowing crawlers.

'Go now to the Water Works and slay the glowing crawlers that infest that place. When you have acquired enough, return to me quickly and we will see to your final preparations.''Disgusting, you say? I never said that handling anything from the old roots of the earth would smell of daisies. If you wish to work with more pleasant odours, go deal with the Elves! Maybe an Elf-maid will need assistance in finding a favourite flower.

'Nay, such work is not for you or me. We are Guardians, hearty and true. We fear no darkness and turn our noses from no sickly smells, not when there are walls that stand or good folk in peril. Let us hurry now, before these lose their potency....'The Galadhrim seek to reclaim the balance of nature from those that threaten them in Moria. Do all that the Galadhrim ask and you shall be named the Saviour of LothlórienComplete Liberator of the Halls of CraftingComplete Reaver of Dâr NarbugudComplete Light of Lumul-narComplete Scourge of Nalâ-dûmMárus determined that the rune-stone you found has been corrupted by a fell spirit within the depths of Moria.Helegfan can be found within the Sixteenth Hall, north from the Shadowed Refuge, at the southern edge of Nud-melek.

Márus has asked you to enter the Sixteenth Hall and defeat the shadow-grim Helegfan, cleansing the rune-stone of the spirit's corruption.Use the rune-stone to summon HelegfanDefeat HelegfanMárus is at the Shadowed Refuge, south from the Sixteenth Hall.

You should return to Márus with news of your victory.'We must restore this rune-stone to its former power, ${PLAYER}. There is no doubt that a fell power has corrupted this stone. There is a shadow-grim, Helegfan, that is known to take pleasure in the perversion of good, and this stone reeks of his foul corruption.

'Helegfan was last known to make his home within the Sixteenth Hall, north from here. Use the rune-stone to summon it forth and slay it.

'Return to me when the deed is done, and we will see if the corruption can be undone.''Use the rune to summon Helegfan, ${PLAYER}.''Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'With the fell spirit defeated, the rune-stone will no longer be subject to his corruption. You have done a great thing in restoring this dwarf-stone to its former glory.

'You have the gratitude of all the Longbeards, ${PLAYER}. Take a well-deserved rest and reward. You've earned both.'The White Hand Orc-leader, Drâgh, can be found in the Grand Stair of Moria, bringing terror wherever he roams. A dwarf of the expedition was killed, and you have been asked by Armbeald to avenge the innocent by felling this evil foe.Drâgh can be found at the Grand Stair, east from the Redhorn Lodes and north-west from the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.

You should defeat Drâgh at the Grand Stair to prevent his further interference with the dwarf expedition in Moria.Defeat DrâghArmbeald can be found at the Orc-Watch in north-west of the Redhorn Lodes.

You should return to Armbeald and tell him that Drâgh has been defeated through the efforts of you and your friends.'Your final task will be to defeat Drâgh. Gather your friends, ${PLAYER}, for this will not be an easy feat.

'Take this effigy into the Grand Stair and summon forth the cruel Orc that poses so great a threat to the folk who wish to reclaim their rightful home. I do not wish him to harry the free peoples of Moria any longer.

'Return to me when you have succeeded in banishing this creature, ${PLAYER}. I hope that your arrows will fly true and bring him down once and for all, so that he troubles us no more.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. You are indeed worthy of this reward!'Winiel was unable to translate the texts you brought to her.Mirwen is in Elrond's Library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell, far to the north of Moria.

Winiel has asked you to take the fragments to an Elf named Mirwen.'Strange... the dwarves use our certh, though I understand they use some letters to represent different sounds, but these fragments you brought me are all but unintelligible to my eyes.

'If anyone could decipher these it would be Mirwen. Her knowledge of ancient writings is unparalleled.

'Take these to Rivendell and look for her there. She is an ever-vigilant student and so spends most of her time in the library. Start your search there.''What is that you have there? Let me see....

'Ah yes, very nice indeed. But there is something missing. I can help you; but these writings will not be enough.'Now that you have recovered the instrument, Pada has asked you to head to Bree and use it to brighten the spirits of some of the townsfolk there.Erling Goodbody can be found in the thoroughfare in front of the Prancing Pony.

Pada, a widely-respected Minstrel, has asked you to cheer a friend of his from Bree using the great instrument you recently recovered.Speak with Erling and let him know that Pada sends his best.Speak with Erling GoodbodyPada is in the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

You should return to Pada and tell him that his friend Erling Goodbody was very pleased with the song you played.Return to Pada'It would be a shame if this beautiful instrument were never to leave these halls, for there are many in Middle-earth who would be heartened by its gift of song. Dark places are everywhere, ${PLAYER}, including the hearts of Men, Elves, dwarves, and hobbits alike.

'Darkness prevails especially in times such as these, where doom seems inevitable. You have seen the Orcs prowling as sure as Men walk, and wights leaving their barrows to trouble the fields upon which they fell, and Warg-voices rending the stillness of a quiet night. 

'My thoughts often turn to a dear old friend in Bree-town who goes by the name of Erling Goodbody. He has suffered much hardship of late, and my songs used to cheer him. I have such a song here; but I'm afraid I don't have time to make the journey.  Do you think you could go and play this song for him in my stead, ${PLAYER}?  

'Erling usually spends his days in the thoroughfare in front of the Prancing Pony.  Find him and play him a song to raise his spirits.  When you have done this, please return to me, for I wish to hear tidings of my friend.''Hallo there. What can I do for you?''Oh...forgive me, friend! I did not realize the music had stopped. Pardon me for one more moment...'

Erling Goodbody closes his eyes and smiles, and then opens them again to look at you with a warm expression.

'That may have been the most beautiful song I have ever heard. Since my friend Pada went away, I admit I had fallen into a sort of gloom, for life has grown hard for many of the good folk of Bree, and it is difficult for me not to fret and worrit on all the woes of the world.

'But...when you began to play on that instrument -- I say, I was quite taken away! Why, I fancy I heard singing birds, flowing water, the sound of the sun, whatever that may be, and of things growing in the earth. You played admirably, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for this diversion.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! I knew this would be just the ticket to bring smiles to more than one face today. Now Erling is happy, and I am happy for him! And I can see that even your own spirits have been raised by your selflessness. That is the best thing about being a Minstrel, is it not?

'But do not be content just yet. From here, the quest turns a bit more perilous. Do you think you are ready?'Warg-riders make their way through the mountain-crags and slip into and out of the shadows of Moria with ease. At the Grand Stair, a leader and his aged mount have come to bend knee to Igash the Fanatic and Mazog.The Warg-rider scouts and trainers can be found within the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.

Thithrand fears that the forces of the Warg-riders will grow into a fearsome unit if they are are not stopped from completing their goals.Defeat Highpeak-trainers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Highpeak-stalkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Thithrand at the Orc-watch and tell him that you have defeated the goblins.Talk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch'Among the Warg-riders I watched enter the Grand Stair, I saw many scouts who made certain that the host was neither followed nor traps laid before them. Among the full entourage also walked trainers, whipping and cursing at the youngest Wargs who walked without riders.

'These forces must not be allowed to finish their goals.

'You must enter the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch, and defeat these enemies before they can complete their devious objectives.''Aye, I will sleep better knowing that this foe will not grow in power. I confess that I was shaken some when I saw that foe ride up through the dark tunnels and into the Grand Stair. Now, I need worry no more, thanks to your efforts, ${PLAYER}.''I fear that the Warg-trainers and the stalkers defending the Warg-rider host will prove too difficult to uproot if we do not destroy them quickly. Make your way to the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch, and defeat the foes within.'The Grand Stair once stood at the foot of a great cross-roads within Moria. At the height of the great city, it led to all areas of the halls and was a majestic wonder to behold. Now it has fallen to the care of Igash, a lieutenant of the Moria Orc-leader Mazog. Igash assembled the forces of Orcs and trolls within Moria in one place and has collected tribute from each to one day bring to the leader of the Orcs. For now, each tribe vies for favour from the lieutenant, a fanatical follower of Mazog.Avar, Ossur, and Thithrand are at the Orc-watch.

Avar has asked you to complete the several tasks needed to reclaim the Grand Stair before he sends you back to Narfi at the Twenty-first Hall.Assist Ossur with the trolls in the Grand StairAssist Ossur with the Fire-orcs in the Grand StairAssist Avar with the Moria Orcs in the Grand StairAssist Thithrand with the Warg-riders in the Grand StairAssist Thithrand with the White Hand Orcs in the Grand StairAvar is at the Orc-watch.

The dwarves of the Orc-watch are satisfied that the forces of the Orcs within the Grand Stair no longer pose a threat to Lothlórien.Talk to Avar at the Orc-watch'Narfi was wise to send us help. We have been watching the Grand Stair for some time, and I fear that we are woefully outnumbered. I have split our number: myself, Ossur, and Thithrand have placed our focus on different forces arrayed within the Grand Stair. When all our tasks are complete, I will vouch for you with Narfi, and we will lay claim to this area once again. Until that time, however, there is much to explain.

'Within the Grand Stair are five tribes of Orcs and trolls. There are those from beyond Khazad-dûm: the White Hand and the Warg-riders. I have set Thithrand to the task of tracking their movements. The second are the deep-dwelling forces of trolls and Orcs of fire. Ossur watches over this host. Lastly, there are the Moria Orcs, flocking to Igash the Fanatic, a lieutenant to Mazog. Igash has collected wealth untold at his throne at the crest of the Grand Stair. I know not what he will do with this treasure, but I know there must be a way to lay claim to it all.

'When we are satisfied that the tasks set before you here at the Grand Stair are complete, I will send you back to Narfi at the Twenty-first Hall.''Once this place was a wonder to behold leading to all places within the realm of Khazad-dûm. Now it has fallen to such disrepair. This must be rectified, and your aid will be needed here.

'Assist Thithrand with the White Hand Orcs and the Warg-riders. Assist Ossur with the trolls and Fire-orcs of the deep. Assist me with forces loyal to Igash and Mazog.

'When you have completed these tasks, I will inform Narfi that the Grand Stair is no longer able to support the efforts of the Orcs against Lothlórien.''Though the Grand Stair still remains a pale reflection of its former glory, the threat posed by the Enemy here is diminished greatly. I do not think that they can effectively mount an offensive from this location.

'I will send word to Narfi that you have assisted us most well, ${PLAYER}. This duty will not go unrecognized.'Having discovered the signs of foul play among the nearby Orc-horde, Armbeald has asked you to seek out Frosti Groundshaker, a wise dwarf who is learned in many lores, to discover more about White Hand Orcs and their behaviour.Frosti Groundshaker is in Thorin's Hall, by the auctioneers south of the throne.

You should take the pieces to Frosti Groundshaker in Thorin's Hall so that he may shed some light upon what may be going on.Armbeald is at the Orc-Watch in the Redhorn Lodes of Moria.

Frosti Groundshaker has made you an effigy with some runes that may help to draw the attention of the Orc-wraith. You should return to Armbeald in Moria and he will instruct you on what to do next.'At least our dwarf-friend is no longer scattered in pieces among the wretched Orc-hordes. We have restored a little of his stolen honour. Alas for this poor fellow and the wretched errand that brought him to his doom. 

'I wonder if there was anything behind this attack. Orc-savagery is not surprising in any circumstance, but the taking of trophies is not something that average Orcs do. I wonder what force drives this particular horde, and who commands them?

'We shall find out, ${PLAYER}. Take these pieces to my friend, Frosti Groundshaker, in Thorin's Hall by the auctioneers south of the throne. He is very scholarly, and enjoys solving puzzles such as this.''You should show your grisly trophies to Frosti Groundshaker...he may know more than I about them.''What's that you have there? Ah, that poor dwarf! He went out to do some scouting and exploring. What a terrible end to meet. Terrible! Well, Armbeald was right to have you come to me with evidence of the murder. I have a knack for solving this sort of thing.

'So these teeth were extracted and found as trophies on Orc-leaders bearing the symbol of the White Hand? I bet I know who is behind this. I have heard rumour of a brutal Orc-master near the Redhorn Lodes, and his arm is long. He commands many of the White Hand Orcs in the vicinity.

'I will make you a little idol, an effigy of sorts, with some runes carved upon it, and I wager it will summon the Orc if you brandish it with that intent. You should return now to Armbeald.''You should let Armbeald know what we learned.''Ill tidings! I have heard of this beastly White Hand Master, and the rumours say that he is very strong, and his command expansive. He will be a difficult foe for a bow and arrow alone.

'But Frosti Groundshaker is a useful fellow, is he not? This effigy will be valuable in what is to come next.'The Forges of Khazad-dûm were once the heart of smithing within Moria. Here, the mighty dwarf-smiths would work the mithril and forge their greastest wonders. In the time since its fall, the Forges of Khazad-dûm have been flooded with massive lava-floes and populated by the Orcs of Moria and their troll and goblin-labourers. Here the Orc war-host hammers away incessantly, as they built their weapons and siege-engines in preparation for their war against Lothlórien.Raf is at Anazârmekhem.

Pálmar seemed a bit worried about the leader of the Orcs within the Forges and advised that you speak with Raf before you enter the Forges.Talk to Raf at Anazârmekhem'I do not speak much of this, but the Uruk-leader of this place has something of a darkness dwelling behind his eyes.

'Raf knows more of this than I, as he has spent much time deciphering and looking at old tomes and studying runes. Speak with him about the blackness in the Uruk-leader of the Forges.

'You can find him here in Anazârmekhem.''Aye, Pálmar and I both saw the black fire in the Uruk's eyes. There is something within it that is not normal. I have seen such things before, I fear, but only the most fiendish of creatures. There are tales that tell of spirits giving Wargs the power of speech, and the black powers of the world that make the dead rise.

'I surmise that this is the same power that flows through the Uruk master of the forges, but there is naught that proves this as the case and so we can only surmise.

'Nevertheless, I would suggest that you shield yourself well against the forces of fire and shadow before you face this terror.'The Grand Stair once stood at the foot of a great cross-roads within Moria. At the height of the great city, it led to all areas of the halls and was a majestic wonder to behold. Now it has fallen to the care of Igash, a lieutenant of the Moria Orc-leader Mazog. Igash assembled the forces of Orcs and trolls within Moria in one place and has collected tribute from each to one day bring to the leader of the Orcs. For now, each tribe vies for favour from the lieutenant, a fanatical follower of Mazog.Ossur is at the Orc-watch.

Ossur has asked you to help him against the Orcs and trolls of the Grand Stair. Once satisfied, you will earn a portion of the respect needed to earn favour from Ossur to satisfy Avar and his task at watching the Grand Stair.Defeat the Orcs and trolls in the Grand StairComplete the task involving the troll-handlers within the Grand StairOssur is at the Orc-watch.

You should return to Ossur and tell him that you completed the tasks focusing on the trolls of Moria.Talk to Ossur at the Orc-watch'My charges include the trolls and the Orcs of fire. Watching over them as I do, I must ask that you complete the tasks I lay before you with regard to each.

'The trolls of the deep are unique in that they are as savage and brutal as any other troll, but they require handlers to keep them in line, preventing them from entering such a terrible frenzy that they kill without thought and merit.

'Therein lies the strength of our assaults. Of course, there is also the matter of the great foe among these trolls....''The trolls of the deep are the ones who play the drums all night and all day... or so it is thought. Whatever the case, there is only one good troll in this world, and that is a dead one. Enter the Grand Stair and complete the tasks that I have set for you.''I am pleased to know that the trolls are weakened. This news will please all who hear it. You have done very well, friend.'The Orcs of Moria have come down from the mountains and begun their assault upon Lothlórien.Successfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaThe Orcs of Moria have come down from the mountains and begun their assault upon Lothlórien.Successfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaSuccessfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaThe Orcs of Moria have come down from the mountains and begun their assault upon Lothlórien.Successfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaSuccessfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaThe Orcs of Moria have come down from the mountains and begun their assault upon Lothlórien.Successfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaSuccessfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaThe Orcs of Moria have come down from the mountains and begun their assault upon Lothlórien.Successfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaSuccessfully defend Lothlórien from the Orcs of MoriaMany Guardians wish to be Defenders of the Free, but not all can accomplish their goals alone.The Dark Delvings lie in the south-eastern reaches of the Foundations of Stone.

Ingthor has instructed you to help a fellow Guardian complete his or her final task at the Dark Delvings.Defeat NightshineIngthor is just outside the Dark Delvings.

With Nightshine slain, you should return to Ingthor with news of your success.Return to Ingthor'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. There are many Guardians who wish to be Defenders of the Free, but not all can accomplish their task alone. You should seek to aid your fellow Guardians along their path.

'The greatest danger your fellow will face is at the Dark Delvings.

'Go now and prove your honour.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. You are truly a worthy Guardian-friend.'The Moria Orcs hold control over the Grand Stair, and leading them are Igash the Fanatic and his Devoted minion. Alongside them are a host of fearsome Orcs from the very heart of Moria.Igash and his Devoted are high up in the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.

Avar has asked you to go forth and defeat Igash and his Devoted.Defeat the DevotedDefeat IgashAvar is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Avar and inform him that you have slain Igash and his Devoted.Talk to Avar at the Orc-watch'I know little of Igash... only that he is followed without question, and that his Devoted seems to be nothing more than an ordinary weak-willed Orc. The two of them clutch the many tribes with an iron fist, commanding and taking at will, always unchallenged.

'Igash commands his forces from on high, and the path to him should be clear. Climb the old bridges, up to the highest platform. There, I suspect, he will sit vainly upon his crude throne. But beware... his Devoted will be keeping watch along the way.

'Make your way north-east, ${PLAYER}. There, you should enter the Grand Stair and defeat Igash and his Devoted. But be wary, for the Stairs climb high; a false step will be your doom. Only sure-footed folk should risk this excursion. May the paths of the dwarves guide your feet well.''There may be other ways to defeat Igash and his Devoted. I know that Thithrand has stated he believes that the White Hand may be planning an assault against the Moria Orcs. Still, it would be best to weaken the foe now, for Igash draws power from the forces offering tribute to him.

'It all seems very strange to me, ${PLAYER}.''I hope that this challenge did not prove too difficult for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Igash indeed does draw strength from those within the Grand Stair, assuming their skills while they still live. This would make him a terrible foe to face, I am certain, but how else can we obtain the tribute he maintains if not by defeating him whilst all the others still live?

'For now, I am grateful that you have defeated this terrible enemy.'The Grand Stair once stood at the foot of a great cross-roads within Moria. At the height of the great city, it led to all areas of the halls and was a majestic wonder to behold. Now it has fallen to the care of Igash, a lieutenant of the Moria Orc-leader Mazog. Igash assembled the forces of Orcs and trolls within Moria in one place and has collected tribute from each to one day bring to the leader of the Orcs. For now, each tribe vies for favour from the lieutenant, a fanatical follower of Mazog.Ossur is at the Orc-watch.

Ossur has tasked you with aiding him against the trolls and Ghâsh-hai of the Grand Stair.Deal with the leader of the Ghâsh-hai in the Grand StairDeal with the war-host of the Ghâsh-hai within the Grand StairOssur is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Ossur at the Orc-watch and inform him that the tasks set before you regarding the Ghâsh-hai are complete.Talk to Ossur at the Orc-watch'My responsibilities include dealing with the Ghâsh-hai and the trolls of the deep. Watching over them as I do, I must ask that you complete the tasks that lay before you with regard to each.

'The Fire-orcs fuel the forges in the depths near Anazârmekhem, but their appearance here confirms that tribute is being paid to the leader of the Orcs of Moria, Mazog. I have two tasks that must be met to ensure that their war host is crippled and their numbers lowered in this place.

'Complete these tasks within the Grand Stair, and you will earn a measure of my respect.''The Ghâsh-hai made their way from the Flaming Deeps of Khazad-dûm, where fire belches forth and the land smells like embers. They come here now and pay homage to the usurpers of Moria. Complete the tasks I have set before you, and you will earn my favour.''You have earned much respect by fulfilling these requests, ${PLAYER}. I know now that we will see this effort through to fruition, and the Elves will have no need to know of the great threat they faced from the Orcs in Khazad-dûm.'Deep within the halls of Moria, flames lick out of oily pools. It is here that the Ghâsh-hai make their home. A faction of these is aligned with the master of Moria, Mazog, and has come to the Grand Stair to pay tribute to their leader.Ghâsh-hai Orcs can be found within the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.

Ossur sent you to face the Orc-forces of the fiery depths of Moria, who came to the Grand Stair to pay their tribute to Igash, an Orc devoted to Mazog.Defeat Ghâsh-hai Firebrands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ghâsh-hai Wrathcallers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ossur is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Ossur and inform him that you have defeated many of the Ghâsh-hai.Talk to Ossur at the Orc-watch'The Ghâsh-hai are terrible creatures bred to harness and enjoy the touch of flame. At least this is what I can surmise about these Orcs.

'They glow like torches against the silent dark walls of Khazad-dûm, and I have seen many of these terrible foes enter the Grand Stair. We must do what we can to thin their number and destroy their hold in the depths.

'Enter the Grand Stair to the north-east of the Orc-watch and hunt their number down.''Fine news, friend. This is a step towards crushing the host assembled in the Grand Stair.

'I am pleased to learn this.''Be careful, for it appears that the flesh of these Orcs could scorch any who come near them.'Descendants of Beorn have not traditionally left the skin-changer's home-land, but your journey has brought you to Eriador in defence of the Free Peoples. You should now go to meet your cousin Varthmath in Moria, at the Orc-watch in the Redhorn Lodes.Your journey continues in Moria and Rhovanian.Reach Level 58 as a BeorningSvanr has asked you to look out at the majestic stone trees of the Second Hall.Vantage points for looking out at the Second Hall can be found on the stairs of Khadar-zarâm.

You should <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out upon the majestic stone trees of the Second Hall, for this is an opportunity to behold some of the finest craftwork of the dwarves from Durin's time.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest requires emotes.</rgb>Svanr stands upon the stairs of Khadar-zarâm in western Nud-melek.

You should return to Svanr.Return to Svanr'Hello there, fellow traveller! Are you making your way to the eastern gate as well? I long to walk in the sun again, for the dark of Moria has grown polluted with evil over the years of our absence.

'I came here to make a pilgrimage through the halls of my father, and I am about to embark upon the last leg of my journey.

'Join me, friend! But first, you must meditate upon the majesty of the stone trees, for the Second Hall is a legendary landmark.''I am glad you had a chance to meditate upon the beauty of this view before leaving Moria. But you surely noticed some things amiss, ${PLAYER}... as did I.'You have followed your cousin Varthmath into the depths of Moria, where the dwarves of the Iron Garrison seek to drive out the goblins that inhabit their old kingdom.Orcs can be found throughout the Redhorn Lodes, Nud-Melek, and the Foundations of Stone.

Your cousin Varthmath has asked you to defeat Orcs in the depths of Moria to teach them to fear the line of Beorn.Varthmath is at the Orc-watch among the Redhorn Lodes.Talk to Varthmath at Orc-watch, among the Redhorn LodesVarthmath has asked you to find a location atop the slopes of Zirakzigil from where you can roar your claim to the mountains. He wanted you to find a suitably impressive landmark at which to roar.Varthmath is at the Orc-watch in the Redhorn Lodes.

You have done as Varthmath requested, and should now tell him of your success.Talk to Varthmath at Orc-watch, among the Redhorn Lodes'Ah, my cousin, it is good to see a familiar face! I summoned Sterkist here, but it seems he has sent you in his place. I do not blame him for choosing not to come. I would not have entered this darkness unless I believed I had no choice, but that is the precise situation. It is these dwarves! They rile up the goblins unnecessarily, and wake creatures of evil that should remain sleeping!

'You know that Beorn and his line once originated in the mountains. The mountains above these cursed halls are the true homes of our people, by right. These dwarves stir up the goblins and the creatures swarm all over the mountains. How can we hope to one day reclaim our territory if it is constantly under threat by dwarf or by Orc?

'Fight Orcs throughout the furthest reaches of Moria, ${PLAYER}, and teach them to fear the line of Beorn!''Fight Orcs throughout the furthest reaches of Moria, ${PLAYER}, and teach them to fear the line of Beorn!''You did well, my cousin. The Orcs and goblins thought they were safe in the halls of this cursed city, for the line of Beorn was above-ground and far away. Now they know our reach is great, but I want them to know that we are not mere visitors. We have a claim to the slopes of the mountains above these halls, a claim that is stronger than that of the dwarves to these dim passages.

'Climb out of these halls and make your way to the surface. Atop the peak of Zirakzigil, <rgb=#FF0000>roar</rgb> our rightful claim to the skies, ${PLAYER}! Find someplace suitably impressive, a landmark of some majesty, at which to do this deed. I want all to know, dwarf and Orc alike, that the line of Beorn stakes a claim upon the mountain-slopes, and fears nothing!''Climb out of these halls and make your way to the surface. Atop the peak of Zirakzigil, <rgb=#FF0000>roar</rgb> our rightful claim to the skies, ${PLAYER}! Find someplace suitably impressive, a landmark of some majesty, at which to do this deed. I want all to know, dwarf and Orc alike, that the line of Beorn stakes a claim upon the mountain-slopes, and fears nothing!''I know you have done as I asked, ${PLAYER}. The dwarves may claim these ancient halls, and they are welcome to them. I have no love for these dim passages. It is the cold, crisp air of the mountains that I miss. One day, after the Orcs are gone, and after the dwarves are gone, we will return to the home we left so long ago, and run along the slopes of the mountains, and there find joy.

'That day is not yet here, my cousin, but one day it will arrive and we will make our bold ancestor proud.'Many lore-masters seek the Path of the Ancient Master, but not all can accomplish their goals alone.Ruingal can be found in the Forges of Khazad-dûm, south of the Cross-roads of Ash in the Flaming Deeps, east of the Water Works.

Hugi has asked you to aid a fellow lore-master against the fire-grim Ruingal, in order to fulfil the Path of the Ancient Master.Defeat RuingalHugi is at the camp-site outside the Forges of Khazad-dûm.

You should return to Hugi and inform him of your success.Talk to Hugi at outside the Forges of Khazad-dûm'Hail, friend. I speak for my fellow lore-masters when I ask for your aid in no small task.

'Within the Forges of Khazad-dûm is a spectre of fire known as Ruingal. Apparently, he has caused no small amount of strife in the days since Durin's Bane first came to Moria.

'If you would aid one of my fellow lore-masters in felling this foul creature you would have our eternal gratitude and a small token of our appreciation.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}! Now for your reward.

'There are certainly more lore-masters who will be in need of your aid, ${PLAYER}. Be sure to return to me before entering the Forges of Khazad-dûm should you ever find yourself in the company of an aspiring lore-master again.'Many captains seek the Path of the Healing Hands, but not all can accomplish their goals alone.Fil-gashan lies in the south-western reaches of the Flaming Deeps.

