'Go now and prove your honour.''If you should come across a hunter in need of your aid, you should grant it.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. You are truly a worthy Hunter-friend.'Svanr has asked you to approach the Orc-camp at the Crack's Edge to see if there is any evidence of why the bridge of Khazad-dûm is sundered.Orcs can be found surrounding the Crack's Edge in Nud-melek, near the sundered Bridge of Khazad-dûm.

You should interrogate Orcs to find out what happened at the Bridge of Khazad-dûm to cause such restlessness.Search an Orc from the Crack's Edge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Svanr can be found at the shattered Bridge of Khazad-dûm on the west edge of the chasm in Nud-melek.

You should speak with Svanr.'I wish to know more about what happened here, ${PLAYER}. Why is the bridge broken? And... do you not sense an air of restlessness about the Orcs nearby?

'If you could interrogate one of their leaders, you might be able to find out something about what happened.''Please find out whatever you can, ${PLAYER}. I would like to rest here, and look out upon the chasm.'Svanr reads the charred papers you hand him.

'Interesting... I see the word "Ghâsh" -- that is fire. And fear, terror, written in common-speech. This particular cluster of Orcs seems to be on the move, fast, towards the Dimrill Dale, for they are not from here, nor do they wish to stay here. I believe they are seeking a brief respite before moving out.

'Something has certainly made them uneasy, but I wonder what could have made them overcome their fear of fire and sun to pursue this path? Why do they head towards the Dale?'Warg-riders make their way through the mountain-crags and slip into and out of the shadows of Moria with ease. At the Grand Stair, a leader and his aged mount have come to bend knee to Igash the Fanatic and Mazog.Glothrok the Vile is within the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.

Thithrand seemed unnerved at the sight of a powerful goblin riding an even more powerful-looking Warg. The pair entered the Grand Stair at the head of the Warg-riders and have not been seen since.Defeat Glothrok the VileDefeat ForzunkThithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Thithrand with news of your victory.Talk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch'One by one, the Orcs travelled up the hallways towards the entrance to the Grand Stair. At their head, riding a Warg scarred by many battles, rode a banner-bearing goblin. I heard his name echoed from the forces as they cheered, seeing the entrance to their new home.

'Their tribute rested on litters dragged by other Warg-riders. Glothrok the Vile, a scourge of the Misty Mountains and leader of the Warg-riders, entered at their head. 

'Never have I seen such a terrifying beast ridden by so confident a goblin. They must be destroyed, and to accomplish this, you must enter the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.''You have done well to defeat this foe. I am certain that this goblin was one of the strongest I have ever seen.

'To think that all these foes were preparing to assault Lothlórien. Your efforts will prove to be of great worth, I think, ${PLAYER}.''Enter the Grand Stair to the north-east of the Orc-watch and find the goblin Warg-rider Glothrol the Vile. Slay him and the beast he rides before returning to me.'From your description of the map the torch projected onto the wall, Geirfast thinks the secret chamber must lie somewhere within Nud-melek, perhaps in the southern part of the Second Hall.The entrance lies somewhere in Nud-melek, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall, perhaps the Second Hall.

Geirfast has asked you to find the entrance to the secret chamber depicted in the shadow-map.Discover the entrance to the secret chamberGeirfast is at the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of the Second Hall.

You should return to Geirfast to tell him where the chamber is.Talk to GeirfastGeirfast is at the Twenty-first Hall.

You should speak with Geirfast when you are ready to travel.Geirfast is at the Twenty-first Hall.

You should return at once to Geirfast.Lenglammel is encamped at the Shadowed Refuge.

Geirfast suggested you speak with the Elf Lenglammel.Talk to Lenglammel at the Shadowed Refuge'I cannot wait to discover this new map's secret! It looks as though it may show a destination to the south-east of here. Were I you, I would search within Nud-melek -- let's see, you said it curved downwards... perhaps the southern section of the Second Hall?''The entrance to the chamber lies somewhere in the Second Hall, I think.''Amazing, you found it! Now that we know where it is, getting there again will be much quicker.

'You may wish to bring a friend or two if you are going to plumb the secrets of this chamber. Who knows what dangers may lie within?

'I suspect the strange riddles on the back of this map will help you in this last exploration. I will make you a fair copy of them, so you can bring them into the chamber with you.''Are you prepared?

'What an exciting time to be in Khazad-dûm... so many mysteries being exposed to the light, for the first time in so very long!''Bless my sturdy boots, what a tale! Clues and maps and shadows and riddles and monsters -- this will make quite the story to tell in my old age!

'So you found the innermost chamber of this strange place.... What did you find there? An axe? An axe marked "Dragonslayer"? Durin's beard!

'${PLAYER}, I think there is more to this than meets the eye. I am loth to give this advice, but I think you ought to speak to one of the Elves here in Moria -- I think Lenglammel might be the one to ask, but you'll have to go down to the Shadowed Refuge to find her. Describe your travails, and what you found at your destination, and see what she has to say.''You should speak with the Elf Lenglammel at the Shadowed Refuge. She may know something of what you found.''Can it be? You are the one? The axe you describe is known to me, but only in legend. It was prophesied that one not of our number -- the nearly forgotten secret council of Elves and dwarves -- would find it once more, within our ancient headquarters in the deepest recesses of the dwarf-mine.

'That map you found was a last desperate attempt to leave a record, should Dragonslayer's hiding place be forgotten -- a situation thought impossible then, but we did not forsee the rise of Durin's Bane, the abandonment of Khazad-dûm, and its degeneration into feared Moria. When Smaug was terrorizing the Lonely Mountain, some of us were instructed to search for records of where Dragonslayer might be hid and found nothing.

'You, brave ${RACE}, have discovered a treasure beyond compare. Lord Elrond shall be alerted, as well as Lady Galadriel... your name will be sung by council-members for Ages to come.'Byrski Hardprow has offered to seek out Durin's Crown in the Mirrormere, hoping it might herald an auspicious end to the Iron Garrison's reclamation of Khazad-dûm.Orcs and planks of ilex wood can be found at Uruk-gashan in the Dimrill Dale.

Byrski Hardprow has asked you to fend off the Orcs lurking in the Dimrill Dale, and he has also asked you to collect planks of ilex wood.Defeat Orcs at Uruk-gashan in the Dimrill Dale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect planks of ilex wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Byrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.

You have collected a number of planks of ilex wood and driven off many of the Orcs at Uruk-gashan. You should return to Byrski Hardprow.You should help Byrski Hardprow to build a ship for his expedition.Help Byrski Hardprow build a shipByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.Talk to Byrski HardprowYou should help Byrski Hardprow to build a ship for his expedition, but maybe try a bit harder this time.Help Byrski to build a ship worthy of witnessing Durin's CrownByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.

You have successfully built a suitable ship for your expedition onto the Mirrormere. You should talk to Byrski Hardprow.Talk to Byrski HardprowByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.Talk to Byrski HardprowByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.

You have helped Byrski Hardprow to witness Durin's Crown in the Mirrormere. You should talk to Byrski Hardprow.Talk to Byrski Hardprow'There is one small problem, though, my friend. After all, I could not sail a ship through Moria!

'I have prepared a few designs by which to build a ship, but I am short a few materials I need. Unfortunately, those Orcs over by Durin's Stone—the disrespectful lot they are—are currently in possession of my planks of ilex wood. Why don't you drive them off and collect some of that wood? Once that is done, I think we'll have all the tools we need to build a ship, and quite a bit less to worry about once we're out on the Mirrormere! After all, we don't want an errant Orc-arrow piercing our sails!

'Go on, my friend. There is no time to waste!''I think that will do nicely! Now then, why don't you do the honours? No, no, I insist.

'You are a skilled Mariner, after all! I am certain you can build a suitable ship for our expedition.

'Well then, I'll stand back and let you get to it!''Bah! You have to think a little bigger than that, my friend. We are going on an expedition, not out for a day of fishing!

'Try again, ${PLAYER}. I must have a ship worthy of bearing witness to Durin's Crown!''Ha-ha! Now that is more like it!

'Now then, let us set out onto the Mirrormere. If you need to make any preparations, take whatever time you need, but do not keep me waiting!''Come along, my friend. Durin's Crown awaits us!''Well, I think I saw Durin's Crown at least, so Brogur will be glad to hear it! Maybe you ought to ask one of the Elves about what you saw, though.

'Nevertheless, I thank you for your help, my friend. You have done the Iron Garrison a great service, and I will make certain that Brogur—and Bósi, of course—know of the Mariner who allowed us to find Durin's Crown. Let us hope it means that the reclamation of Khazad-dûm will soon be finished!'The Grand Stair once stood at the foot of a great cross-roads within Moria. At the height of the great city, it led to all areas of the halls and was a majestic wonder to behold. Now it has fallen to the care of Igash, a lieutenant of the Moria Orc-leader Mazog. Igash assembled the forces of Orcs and trolls within Moria in one place and has collected tribute from each to one day bring to the leader of the Orcs. For now, each tribe vies for favour from the lieutenant, a fanatical follower of Mazog.Thithrand is at the Orc-watch.

Thithrand is responsible for guarding against the threat posed by the Warg-riders within the Grand Stair. You should assist him by completing his tasks.Help Thithrand defeat the Leader of the Warg-ridersHelp Thithrand thin the number of Warg-riders within the Grand StairThithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Thithrand and tell him that each of his tasks involving the Warg-riders are complete.Talk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch'Warg-riders make their way through the mountainous passes and crags of the Misty Mountains. It is no surprise that they have thrown their lot in with the Moria Orcs, but this is an alliance that cannot be allowed to remain.

'I have two tasks for you regarding the Warg-riders of Moria. Will you hear me out?''I will speak well of you when you have done all that I ask of you, ${PLAYER}. We must stop the Orcs' war before it begins.''The defeat of these foes will prove a great boon to us. No longer will the Warg-riders think so highly of the protection offered by the so-called king of the Moria Orcs.

