You should return to Svanr.Return to Svanr'You seem ill at ease, ${PLAYER}. What is it?'

After a moment's consideration, you tell Svanr that you are still curious about the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.

'That is an odd thing to say, but you might as well take another look at it, if it will ease your mind. I do not know what came to pass there, or why it was shattered so.

'Do not get your hopes up that there will be further evidence, but look on it once more if you must!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Did you see anything of interest, ${PLAYER}? Any evidence of what happened?'

You feel shaken by what you saw, and uncertain of the truth in it. You choose to say nothing at this time.

'Ah, well. I did not think there would be much worth in scouting it out. Perhaps someday we will solve the riddle!''By all means, go have another look, ${PLAYER}.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>You should collect flowers from the Dimrill Dale and plant them upon the eastern stair to commemorate the dwarves who never made it through Moria.Flowers can be found growing in the sun in the Dimrill Dale, near the East Gate of Moria.

You should pick fair flowers for your tribute to your fallen fellow travellers.Pick flowers to commemorate the fallen dwarvesFlowers can be found growing in the sun in the Dimrill Dale, near the East Gate of Moria.

You should pick fair flowers for your tribute to you fallen fellow travellers.Pick fair flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Old, unused vases can be found lining the east stairs outside of Moria, in the Dimrill Dale.

You should plant the flowers you collected in the vases to commemorate the dwarves who lost their lives, never passing the east door.Plant flowers to remember the fallen dwarves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have commemorated the fallen dwarves of the expedition appropriately.Completed'You would like to pay a tribute to the fallen dwarves of Moria, would you? Well, I noticed some fair flowers and empty vases out on the Dimrill Dale.

'Perhaps you can show your respects to those who never made it out alive by planting some white flowers in their memory.'You have commemorated the fallen dwarves of the expedition appropriately.

The bright flowers will grow here like the hope and boldness kindled in the heart of every dwarf. They may have lost their lives, but their legacy shall live on.Dithrik has tasked you with acquiring materials that will aid in challenging an old horror from ages long passed.The Nameless beings and the ancient creature prowl the vicinity of the Foundations of Stone, especially to the south-east of this region.

Dithrik has asked you to collect twelve unspoiled heads from the Nameless of the Foundations of Stone.'Well met, ${PLAYER}. You sought Dithrik, and Dithrik you have found. I am a defender of my fellow dwarves, and of all the good peoples of this Middle-earth; in that we are akin.

'I can see that your shield arm is as strong as the very stone that holds mountains, and in your eyes I recognize the light of keen hope that defies the darkness of despair. You are a true Guardian, and I have just the task for one such as you.

'There is an ancient horror from days even before Durin's Bane plagued our home of Moria. Dwarves have seen him near here, in the Foundations of Stone, and rumours of his terror spread far.  Find and slay the Nameless, for they walk unchallenged. Bring me the unspoiled heads of these creatures so that we might prepare a suitable bait for the elder terror.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. Now, for your next task....'The Grand Stair once stood at the foot of a great cross-roads within Moria. At the height of the great city, it led to all areas of the halls and was a majestic wonder to behold. Now it has fallen to the care of Igash, a lieutenant of the Moria Orc-leader Mazog. Igash assembled the forces of Orcs and trolls within Moria in one place and has collected tribute from each to one day bring to the leader of the Orcs. For now, each tribe vies for favour from the lieutenant, a fanatical follower of Mazog.Thithrand is at the Orc-watch.

Thithrand believes that the White Hand will openly rebel against the Moria Orcs, but fears they could amass enough strength to wrest control for themselves. To avert this, he would like you to complete a variety of tasks.Help Thithrand defeat the leaders of the White Hand Orcs within the Grand StairHelp Thithrand cripple the White Hand's power in the Grand StairThithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Thithrand with news of your successes in the Grand Stair.Talk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch'I have watched the Orcs arriving from the south, and I tell you that they have no plans to remain loyal to the forces of Moria. They have intentions all their own, and if given leave may yet unseat the current leader here and take command of his forces for their own purposes.

'We cannot let this happen, so I must charge you with the task of thwarting them. Two tasks do I have, so listen well!''We need to thin the number of White Hand Orcs here at the Grand Stair and also remove their leadership. Only then can we hope to unseat their power and stop their attempt to wrest control within Khazad-dûm.''Your efforts against the White Hand are complete, and I am grateful for it.'Celofa has sent you out to the Western Deeps in search of ancient dwarf-style riddles. Apparently clues can be found on the book-shelves there, but Celofa warns that making too much noise may attract the nearby Orcs.The Western Deeps are north-west from the Redhorn Lodes. Celofa suggested that you start your search between Gabil-mamach and the Hall of Flowing Water.

Celofa has asked you to search through any stacks of scrolls you may find in the Western Deeps between Gabil-mamach and the Hall of Flowing Water, but she warned that your search may alert the Orcs of that area to your presence if you are not careful.Find a scroll of riddlesCelofa is at the Foundations of Stone, south-east of the Western Deeps and the Redhorn Lodes.

You should return to Celofa with the scroll you found.'All right, ${PLAYER}. To begin, let's have you go out and dig up some old dwarf-style riddles... or at least riddles that dwarves wrote down. They needn't be dwarvish in origin, of course, but since Moria has such a great store of everything imaginable, just waiting to be uncovered, one would think that some excellent riddles can be unearthed here.

'Now where was I... Ah, yes. Riddles! There are some old shelves in the Western Deeps, but you will find nasty Orcs too, I'm afraid. Try searching the shelves for any good riddles and bring one back to me.

'And about those Orcs: they might hear you if you make too much noise rustling and rummaging about those shelves. I'd keep my eyes open, if I were you, and make quick work of it.''So, ${PLAYER}, have you discovered any of the dwarf-make riddles I requested of you?''Well done! This is a treasure, and no mistake!'

Celofa purses her lips and avidly peruses the faded text, eyes alight with hopeful mischief.

'Now hold on; this text is incomplete! This won't do... won't do at all.

'We'll have to find the missing text to go along with this scroll you found, ${PLAYER}.'How they found their way into Moria is unclear, but the forces of the White Hand are now entrenched in the Orc communities of Khazad-dûm. However, it appears to Thithrand that they wish to claim leadership over Moria for themselves.Ilzkâl and Nardur can be found in the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.

Thithrand believes that the Uruk-hai Nardur and Ilzkâl may be planning to revolt against Igash and steal the tribute kept within his throne for themselves.Defeat IlzkâlDefeat NardurThithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Thithrand with news of your victory.Talk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch'The leaders of the White Hand are a pair of powerful Uruk-hai, a breed of Orc I have never seen before. They wield the power of shadow and strength enough to knock even the sturdiest dwarf off of his feet.

'Nardur and Ilzkâl: those are the names I heard as I watched them argue all the way to the mouth of the Grand Stair. Each of them spoke in hushed whispers growing loud enough at times to make out the words "betrayal" and "assault". Whether they mean to make war on Igash is unclear, but it should be noted that it would be less difficult to dispose of Igash if they were not present.

'You will find Nardur and Ilzkâl in the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.''The betrayal of Nardur and Ilzkâl remains unknown to the Moria Orcs, but we have bested a terrible foe within Khazad-dûm. This will provide us with a strong position should the White Hand return here in the future.''Should the Uruk-hai make battle on Igash, we may lose our chance to defeat Mazog's lieutenant before he runs to a safe refuge.

'Find them and defeat them before this is possible.'Pada has tasked you with recovering an ancient instrument from an Orc within the Foundations of Stone. He wishes to see your skill so that he can assess how best to teach you what is left to be taught.The Orc Shîk can be found in the Foundations of Stone. Pada mentioned looking for Shîk in the pools of water with waterfalls along the northern edges of the Foundations of Stone.

Pada has requested that you venture forth to recover an excellent and famous instrument from the unworthy Orcs to help further your final education as a Minstrel.'Well met, ${PLAYER}, and welcome to the Foundations of Stone. Your renown as a Minstrel precedes you, and I'm honoured to meet you at last. Together I hope we can bring light to this place.

'I see great strength in you, but doubt also. And where there is doubt, there is dread, and morale can wither and break under such strain. But fear not -- you need naught but inspiration, which may then be used to infuse your heart with newfound power and will. 

'I can help you in this regard. To begin this last leg of your journey, I would have you acquire an instrument that once belonged to a great Minstrel. Legend has it that this piece could be well heard singing high above the clamour of battle, drowning out fear, anguish, and even death with its clear music. I have learned that an Orc, Shîk, has been seen with this instrument here in the Foundations of Stone.

'They say that Shîk likes to play in the foetid pools along the northern edges of the Foundations of Stone and is especially fond of the waterfalls that feed them. Go and recover the instrument, and then return to me.''Splendid work, ${PLAYER}. This is indeed the instrument I have sought. Now, let us see to your next task.'Trolls are a formidable opponent and in Moria, the trolls have had much time to develop thicker hides and worse tempers. It falls to Ossur to watch the comings and goings of the trolls and their handlers at the Grand Stair. In the time since he began watching, he has seen one troll that seemed more frightening and deadly than the others and a throng of handlers who kept the savage trolls at bay.The Grand Stair is north-east of the Orc-watch.

The Uruk troll-handlers should be slain for the safety of the dwarves who have come to reclaim Khazad-dûm.Defeat Gazathrûg Handlers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ossur the dwarf can be found at the Orc-watch.

You defeated a good number of the Uruk troll-handlers, but the trolls were unmoved and did not begin attacking other tribes of Orcs within the Grand Stair.Talk to Ossur at the Orc-watch'Watching the Grand Stair as I have, I can tell you that the troll-handlers keep the trolls from entering terrible frenzies. At least, this is the case with the Beast, but there is no reason to think that any other troll is not capable of the same terror.

'The handlers are Uruks and they strengthen the trolls which they watch over. I think that thinning their number may turn the trolls into something of a weapon against the other war-hosts assembled within the Grand Stair; if not, then we have still rid the world of a few Uruks.

'The Grand Stair lies to the north-east of here. Be careful, ${PLAYER}!''A pity that the trolls did not become so irate that they made battle against the other tribes in the Grand Stair...but still, there are fewer Uruks there now and perhaps the trolls, now leaderless, will be easier to remove. 

'You have done well, friend.''You will find the trolls and their Uruk-masters within the Grand Stair to the north-east of the Orc-watch. I do not know, beyond the entrance of the Grand Stair, where you will need to go.'You have discovered treasure that was once guarded by a troll of Khadar-zarâm.Svanr stands upon the stair of Khadar-zarâm in western Nud-melek.

You should bring the contents of the coffer you examined to Svanr.Bring the treasure you found to SvanrThis coffer, once guarded by a great troll of Khadar-zarâm, now stands alone. You should examine it to see what lies within, and bring the contents to Svanr.'That is quite the haul, ${PLAYER}! I am impressed with the goblins' hoard, but they cannot hide valuables from experienced treasure-seekers such as yourself, eh?'The ways of Lothlórien are beautiful and restful. It is easy to lose oneself in the peaceful wood.NOT USEDTraders from Dale travelling south became trapped at the foot of the Misty Mountains as the Orcs of Moria poured forth, forcing the Elves of Lórien to grant them aid.This spot is a favourite resting place of Galadriel, Lady of the Golden Wood.Cerin Nauth is a peaceful hill overlooking the Golden Wood.The Vineyards of Lórien produce sweet grapes and fine wine for the festivals of the Elves.Imlald Lalaith, the Valley of Laughter, is where most of Lothlórien's feasts take place.This garden recalls the past, when Lothlórien was Laurelindórenan.Bain Gwaloth is a private garden, beautiful and secluded.This peaceful glade is a perfect spot to view the stars of Elbereth.This grove of Melbrethil is revered by the Galadhrim.The Quiet Garden is a peaceful place to contemplate the troubles of the world.The Moria Orcs hold control over the Grand Stair, and at their head are Igash the Fanatic and his Devoted. Alongside them is a host of fearsome Orcs from the heart of Moria.The Orcs can be found at the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.

Avar has tasked you with defeating the Orcs who guard the throne of Igash.Defeat Gazathrug Enforcers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Gazathrug Lurkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Avar is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair.

You should return to Avar with news of your success.Talk to Avar at the Orc-watch'Igash's throne dais is patrolled by his master guard. These Orcs seem to be of the same breed found throughout Khazad-dûm, but are stronger and more deadly. 

'We must be diligent in dealing with these Orcs, lest they bring their war-plans to fruition.

'You will find the Orcs beyond the bridges of the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch.''With their numbers dwindling, it will not be long before the Moria Orcs are naught more than a memory in this area. Your efforts are exemplary, ${PLAYER}, and you will be known throughout these halls as a hero to all.

'I thank you for your efforts thus far.''Be cautious as you travel through the Grand Stair and defeat as many of these foes as you can.'Sadreda has summoned you into his presence.Sadreda is at the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

You have been directed to speak with the great warden Sadreda.Talk to Sadreda at the Foundations of StoneSadreda is at the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

You have been directed to speak with the great warden Sadreda.Talk to Sadreda at the Foundations of StoneSadreda has summoned you into his presence to further your training as a Warden.'Well met, Warden ${PLAYER}. No doubt you have come here to learn from my own experiences defending home and country from the forces of the Enemy.

'I will be glad to show you what I know; but first we must act together to quell the forces of the Enemy here in Moria.

'Let us speak further and see how we can help one another.'The Galadhrim are preparing for war against the Orcs of Moria. They have sent a call out to all who will aid them.Complete Lórien Quest Tier 2Complete quests in Lothlórien.Complete quests in LothlórienTyki suspects that the fungus is spreading amongst the Orcs through the stagnant, contaminated water they all drink. He thinks that adding clean, fresh water to their supply may help to cure them.Fresh water may be obtained in the small cave within the Shadowed Refuge. The Globsnaga Orcs' stagnant spring may be found at Dalgum-ru, south of the Shadowed Refuge.

Tyki wants you to add clean water to the Globsnaga Orcs' foetid water in an effort to cure them of their fungal infection.The Globsnaga Orcs' stagnant spring is at Dalgum-ru, south of the Shadowed Refuge.

Bring the water-skin of fresh water to the Orcs' water supply.Tyki is at the Shadowed Refuge, north of Dalgum-ru.

You should return to Tyki and report back with the results of his freshwater cure.Speak to Tyki at the Shadowed Refuge'I rather wonder if the foul, rank, stagnant water that those Orcs drink might have something to do with their horrid condition. Perhaps introducing some fresh water into their supply will help to keep the fungal infection from spreading any further.

'Take this water-skin and fill it with fresh water. Add that to the Orcs' stagnant spring, and I feel confident we could see some significant results!

'The only place you will find fresh water around here is within the small cave nearby. Once you've filled your water-skin, take it and empty it into the Orcs' spring at Dalgum-ru to the south.''Fresh water can be found within the small cave nearby. The Orcs live around Dalgum-ru.''You've filled the water-skin with clear water? Good.

'Now you should bring it to the Globsnaga Orcs' encampment and empty it into their water-supply. You will find it at Dalgum-ru, south of here.''You are back! Well? Is the news good? Did you see any Orcs drinking? Did they get better?'The mirror set within the Foundations of Stone is the sole source of pure light in these stygian depths. The evil things that creep about often ruin its alignment to restore the darkness.Drafli is in the Shadowed Refuge in the western reaches of the Foundations of Stone.

You should tell Drafli that you have re-aligned the mirror.Speak with DrafliThis mirror stands alone in a terrible corrupted mire of passages, with the fungus creeping around it. You should tell someone at the Shadowed Refuge of the mirror you found in the deeps.'My thanks, ${PLAYER}. It won't be long before something or other decides to fiddle with it again, I'm sure, but for the time being it's just a bit brighter down here, don't you think?'Jari is planning to attempt to find the source of the madness affecting the spiders he has been studying.Jari is just west of the entrance of Tunzelgund, east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Klintur has asked you to accompany Jari in his search for answers regarding the madness of the spiders.Find and speak to JariKlintur is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You should return to Klintur and tell him of the terrifying creature you encountered with Jari.Talk to Klintur at the Shadowed Refuge'I think we need to find the reason for this strange madness being displayed by these spiders.

'I think that your answers may lie a little deeper into the dark. I have a friend, Jari, east of here, who is about to embark on a little voyage of discovery around Tunzelgund. Look for Jari and accompany him, if you would, and you may find the answers for which we're all searching.''By Durin's beard! I have no idea what that creature you described to me was, ${PLAYER}, and that's the truth, or may I never hoist another tankard!

'This nameless horror must be involved at the root of the problem...but how can we fight it?

'Don't look so surprised. There is a time for study and thought and lessons and speech, and a time for the axe of a dwarf to do the speaking!''Are you going or not? Jari will need your aid.''Ah! Greetings, ${PLAYER}...come to help, have you?

'Let's start this way. If we are lucky, we won't need to journey very far....'Nökkvi was horrified to discover that the Nameless have been feeding on dwarf-corpses and feels an end must be put to their desecration.You found dwarf-corpses in the place called Mazam-dûm, on the eastern side of the lake in the Foundations of Stone.

Nökkvi has asked you to bury the dwarf-corpses you found.Bury the fallen dwarves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nökkvi is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.

You should return to Nökkvi to tell him of the burials you performed.Talk to Nökkvi at the Shadowed Refuge'Bellows and anvil, this is unacceptable! 

'The bodies of our brethren cannot continue to feed these creatures. We will put a stop to it, or may my beard wither!

'The first step is to ensure the respectful treatment of those bodies. We must allow them to return to the stone of our beloved Khazad-dûm. Please, go inter them, then return to me.''Go to Mazam-dûm, on the eastern side of the lake and lay the fallen into graves, such that these nameless beasts can no longer feed upon them.''Ah, it is a sad day indeed, ${PLAYER}, when a dwarf must worry that his remains will be eaten, instead of interred with the proper respect and memorial speeches.

'Let us hoist a tankard to the fallen... they will be avenged!'You have travelled to the Twenty-first Hall to aid in its defence. Follow Wíli's direction and help the Dwarves of Moria make their stand!Wait for Wíli to finish relaying his orders to his men.Wait for Wíli to finish relaying his orders to his men.Speak with Wíli to see what aid you might lend in his defence.Talk to Wíli in the Twenty-first HallThe first assault on the Twenty-first Hall has begun. Defend the eastern bulwark!Push back the first assaultWíli is at the centre of the Twenty-first Hall.

You should return to Wíli for further instruction.Talk to Wíli in the Twenty-first HallThe second assault on the Twenty-first Hall has begun. Defend the southern bulwark!Push back the second assaultWíli is at the centre of the Twenty-first Hall.

You should return to Wíli for further instructions.Talk to Wíli in the Twenty-first HallThe third assault on the Twenty-first Hall has begun. Defend the western bulwark!Push back the third assaultWíli is at the centre of the Twenty-first Hall.

You should return to Wíli for further instruction.Talk to Wíli in the Twenty-first HallWíli is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, east off the Northern Hallway.

You should speak with Wíli and prepare for the final assaults.Talk to Wíli in the Chamber of MazarbulThe fourth assault on the Twenty-first Hall has begun. Defend the Northern Hallway!Push back the fourth assaultWíli is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, east of the Northern Hallway.

The dwarves were forced to retreat back to the Chamber of Mazarbul. You should join Wíli and prepare for the final assault.Talk to Wíli in the Chamber of MazarbulThe final assault on the Twenty-first Hall has begun. Defend the Chamber of Mazarbul!Push back the final assault and defeat the commander of the OrcsWíli is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, east of the Northern Hallway.

You should return to Wíli to discuss your success against the Orcs of Mazog.Talk to Wíli in the Chamber of Mazarbul'Let us return to the Twenty-first Hall and begin repairs.''Our defences are in order. Now I must tell you the role you are to play in the upcoming battle.''Well done, ${PLAYER}, but the battle has only just begun! See there? Another of the advance guards returns!''Again, well done, ${PLAYER}. I fear, however, that the Orcs will not so easily give up their assault! Look, there is another of the guards!''${PLAYER}! Word comes from the Northern Hallway that the Enemy is preparing for an assault there!

'We must go at once... what remains of the advance guard must deal with any further assaults against the Twenty-first Hall proper.''I will complete preparations here, ${PLAYER}. If the hallway falls, this chamber will be our final hope for waiting out this siege.

'Hark! Do you hear the horns? They come even now... prepare yourself!''The outlook is foul, ${PLAYER}. This horde seems endless, and we are all that remains here. Prepare yourself, for this may well be our final stand.

'To arms!''Well done, ${PLAYER}! I fear, however, that our victory here is short-lived. The Orcs seem nearly endless in number. This expedition is doomed to failure, I believe. It will be years before we are strong enough to cleanse these halls.

'Ah well, this is not the time for fear or grief. You have defended this hall for today.'Bróin is worried that recovering Zigilburk might not be the boon it seems, and that it will cause the dwarves to become overconfident.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek.

Bróin has asked you to warn Bori against the overconfidence he fears the recovery of Zigilburk has awoken in the dwarves.Glúmur is in Nud-melek, overlooking Mazog's fortress.

Bori has asked that you speak to his scout near Zabadgathol, and assist him in scouting out the area.Locate and talk to Glúmur in Nud-melekZabadgathol, Mazog's fortress, is in Nud-melek.

Bori has asked you to locate Zabadgathol and defeat some of Mazog's most loyal bodyguards, members of the Pûlpum.Glúmur is located at the top of the stairs above the chamber in Nud-melek.

You have defeated many of Mazog's loyal servants, the Pûlpum, and should return now to Glúmur.Speak to Glúmur'You have rescued me from the Drowned Treasury, but still I am afraid. I fear that the recovery of Zigilburk will prove ill for the dwarves -- there is something about the axe that fills me with dread, and I worry it will awaken unwholesome greed in my people. Already Bori has risked much in his desire for this weapon.

'Please return to the Chamber of Leadership and tell Bori of my concerns. His words as we left the flooded chambers where I had been trapped by the Watcher filled me with worry.''See? Just as Bori said, nothing bad has happened, ${PLAYER}! Not to us, anyway; Mazog cannot say the same!

'Bróin's worries are needless.''It's good to see you. I am glad that Bori was kind enough to send me a bit of help here. 

'Down below, Mazog's men have been hard at work. Can you defeat Mazog's closest servants, ${PLAYER}? 

'They are called the Pûlpum, and they seem to serve as his most loyal and formidable bodyguards and can be found in the area below.''What tidings do you bring from my friend? Bróin is worried? He has been through much hardship, but he must realize the glory that awaits us! We are so near to casting the Orcs out of Moria that I can taste it! We cannot stop now, now that we have the means for victory. Do you not know the story of Azog? I will not recount it for you now, for it is grim, but know that Mazog, spawn of his spawn, is surely hewn from the same block as he: terrible and merciless.

'More of our scouts have returned, and they believe they have found the location of Mazog's fortress; it is a place called Zabadgathol, in Nud-melek.

'One such scout, Glúmur, is located near Zabadgathol, travel to Nud-melek and speak to him.''The Pûlpum are apparently Mazog's most loyal servants. Look for them outside his fortress, Zabadgathol, in Nud-melek.''Once I longed for adventure, but no more. Tell Bori in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall to beware Zigilburk. I fear its strength will not avail us.''The Pûlpum are apparently Mazog's most loyal servants. Look for them outside his fortress, Zabadgathol, in Nud-melek.'Glúmur is curious about the last utterances of Mazog's servants, the loyal Pûlpum, and wants you to learn if there is some truth in their dying words.Zabadgathol is in Nud-melek.

Glúmur has asked you to return to Zabadgathol, Mazog's fortress within Nud-melek, and to search the area for treasure coffers that might point to the identity of his mysterious ally.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.

You have recovered some treasure coffers from Zabadgathol and should bring them to Bori for his examination.'But enough about Bróin. With all that he has been through, he deserves his rest and I do not want to disturb his peace of mind by telling him all the details of our efforts in Zabadgathol.

'I am curious about the last words of those servants of Mazog, the Pûlpum guards that you defeated. Someone seems to be in league with Mazog, but to what end?

'Return to Zabadgathol, and search that place for treasure coffers. I want to learn more about Mazog's mysterious ally.''You remember where Zabadgathol is, ${PLAYER}, I am sure: in Nud-melek! Search the place for treasure coffers that may tell us about Mazog's mysterious ally.''You remember where Zabadgathol is, ${PLAYER}, I am sure: in Nud-melek! Search the place for treasure coffers that may tell us about Mazog's mysterious ally.''You have returned with the treasure coffers? Good, good. Let us have a look inside.'

Bori opens a coffer and appears very surprised by what he sees inside.

'These are no mere trinkets, but powerful and valuable relics. Look at this, and at this! Evil-looking, to be sure, and wreathed with cruel sigils. And two runes: D.G.

'Oh no... it is worse than I thought! Mazog's mysterious benefactor hails from Dol Guldur, in the depths of Mirkwood! This bodes ill, very ill indeed!'Having learned that some force out of Dol Guldur has allied with Mazog's Orcs, Bori is now doubly determined to assault Zabadgathol.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek.

Bori has decided upon a new plan: to attack Mazog's fortress, wielding Zigilburk, and to slay the evil Orc before the force out of Dol Guldur can take advantage of the situation between the Orcs and the dwarves.Talk to Bori and assault ZabadgatholBrogur is in the Deep-way.

After Bori's failed assault on Zabadgathol, Brogur has moved to the Deep-way where he mourns the loss of both his nephew and Zigilburk.'If Dol Guldur has truly allied with Mazog, there is no time to waste, ${PLAYER}! We will assault Zabadgathol before their plans can come to fruition. With one stroke, we will slay Mazog and end this war between Orcs and dwarves before any force from Dol Guldur can use our conflict to its advantage.

'It will be just like our raid on Stazgnâkh, only this time I will wield Zigilburk, and we will march openly to victory! Our foes shall perish beneath the bite of the mithril axe; this is what it is for, my friend! This is why it comes again out of the darkness!

'Tell me when you are ready, and we will assault Zabadgathol and slay Mazog. I will hand-pick a few others to accompany us.''Tragedy befalls us at all turns! Was my nephew foolish to challenge Mazog so? Perhaps, but he is a dwarf! How could he not challenge the spawn of Azog, thrice-cursed by dwarves?

'To lose both Bori and the axe Zigilburk is a grievous blow, and I fear to think of what this sorceror, this Gorothúl, may have in store for us. It seems clear that though the armies are Mazog's, Gorothúl is making the plans.''We shall assault Zabadgathol and defeat Mazog, ${PLAYER}, and be heroes! He cannot stand against the might of Zigilburk... what Orc could?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>Brogur is uncertain of what to do following the loss of Bori and Zigilburk, and fears the time of the dwarves in Moria may be nearly at an end.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern end of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

Brogur has asked you to consult Bósi for some idea of what to do next, now that the dwarves have lost much of their hope of victory in Moria.'I... do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}. For all of our preparations and the strength of our arms, Mazog and his ally Gorothúl have struck our hearts directly.

'Perhaps Bósi will know what to do, but I fear he will be as lost as I am. Bróin came back to us from out of the darkness, but I am not as confident that Bori will do the same.''You must ask my cousin what to do, for I am completely out of ideas. I do not know how we can stand against Mazog and Gorothúl without the power of Zigilburk.'Bósi stares at you for a moment and then closes his eyes.

'Are we finished, ${PLAYER}? All of the dwarves of this expedition rejoiced when Zigilburk was borne from the depths, but moreso at the safe return of my nephew Bróin. All things seemed possible! But now...'

He sighs heavily.

'My son is gone. How can I hope to lead my people to victory now? I cannot. I have not the will.'The time has come for the dwarves to stand against the Orcs of Moria, but Bósi and Brogur have lost hope that they can achieve victory beneath the mountains.Brogur is in the Deep-way.

The survival of the dwarves in Moria now depends on the ability of you and your allies to defend these locations from attack. You were asked to speak with Brogur first.Talk to Brogur and defend the Deep-wayStóthkell is in the Way of Smiths.

Now that the Deep-way has been secured, you should lend your aid to Stóthkell.Talk to Stóthkell and defend the Way of SmithsWíli is in the Twenty-first Hall.

With both the Deep-way and the Way of Smiths secured, you should head at once to the Twenty-first Hall and aid Wíli in its defence.Talk to Wíli and defend the Twenty-first HallBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern end of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving.

You have helped to fight off the initial assaults of the Orcs on the barricades of the dwarves, and should report of your success to Bósi.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads'It is up to you and your friends now. You must rally my people and coordinate the defence of Moria. We have prepared for war at three key locations: the Deep-way, the Way of Smiths, and the Twenty-first Hall; if these locations fall, we are lost.

'Brogur must fight for the protection of the Deep-way. Tell him I am counting on his strength, and he will stand as long as it takes to fight back the Orc-hordes. Speak with him first.

'The defence of the Way of Smiths is in the hands of Stóthkell. He speaks highly of you and will do as you command. You should speak with him once the Deep-way is secured.

'Wíli will oversee the barricades at the Twenty-first Hall; he fought bravely as part of the diversionary force during my son's assault on Stazgnâkh, and... I am sorry. Wíli will do fine. This will be the last and most vital bastion you must defend. Our survival is in your hands.''You must speak to the following dwarves once you have gathered your allies.

'The defence of the Way of Smiths is in the hands of Stóthkell. He speaks highly of you, and will do as you command.

'Brogur must fight for the protection of the Deep-way. Tell him I am counting on his strength, and he will stand as long as it takes to fight back the Orc-hordes.

'Wíli will oversee the barricades at the Twenty-first Hall; he fought bravely as part of the diversionary force during my son's assault on Stazgnâkh.''You have left me speechless, ${PLAYER}! With your help, we live to fight another day!

'But what if the Orcs return, as they surely will? We cannot stand against them forever; they are simply too numerous!'The Deep-way, a passage connecting the Great Delving to the Water-works, must be defended against the Orc onslaught.Brogur is in the Deep-way.

Once you have assembled your allies, you should speak with Brogur. It will not be long before the Orcs arrive.Complete Skirmish: Battle of the Deep-wayBrogur is in the Deep-way.

You have repulsed the attack on the Deep-way by the Orc hordes, and should speak now to Brogur about the victory.'I am sorry for my despairing words when I spoke to you before. I will rally my spirits, for the sake of Bósi and all of our people.

'We will hold the Deep-way against all our foes, ${PLAYER}. Bring what allies you can assemble, and we will stand against the Orcs as long as we must!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Small Fellowship, or Fellowship group sizes by using the Instance Finder Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 55.

If this is your first Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>'We have done it, ${PLAYER}! I did not think we would come through it alive, but we did, against all the odds!

'The dwarves in Moria stand hardy though all their enemies of the deeps be upon them!''Let us prepare our defences!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Small Fellowship, or Fellowship group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 55.

If this is your first Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>The Twenty-first Hall is a major centre for the dwarf-presence in Moria, and must be held at any cost.Wíli is in the Twenty-first Hall.

The time has come to defend the Twenty-first Hall from attack by the Orc onslaught. Speak with Wíli to arrange the defence.Complete Skirmish: Battle of the Twenty-first HallWíli is in the Twenty-first Hall.

You have successfully defended the Twenty-first Hall from the Orc attack, and should speak now with Wíli.'It comes down to this, ${PLAYER}: if we lose the Twenty-first Hall, we lose Moria. The Orcs will strike soon, and the stroke will be hard and fast. We cannot fall here, or we shall not find our footing again!

'If we must, we will retreat from the forward barricades. Better to lose some ground than to lose good dwarves!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Small Fellowship, or Fellowship group sizes by using the Instance Finder Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 55.

If this is your first Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>'The Twenty-first Hall must not fall to Mazog!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Small Fellowship, or Fellowship group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 55.

If this is your first Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>'We owe you more gratitude than can be expressed in words or salutations. The Twenty-first Hall still stands, and my folk remain upright to cleanse the filth that infested these slumbering halls!

'What a day this has been! From retreat and dishonour springs glory and triumph! Let Mazog cower before the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm!'The Way of Smiths, in which lies the secret entrance to the Heart of Fire, must be defended from the Orcs.Stóthkell is in the Heart of Fire.

You should speak to Stóthkell when you have gathered your allies and are ready to man the defences of the Way of Smiths.Complete Skirmish: Battle of the Way of SmithsStóthkell is in the Heart of Fire.

You have defended the Heart of Fire from attack by the Orc-hordes, and should speak now to Stóthkell.'We are with you, ${PLAYER}. We will stand against the Orcs to the end, whether into ruin or triumph, though the Orcs thirst and slaver for our very blood....

'...And then we will close the door if we must. If it comes to that, your presence will strengthen our resolve regardless.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Small Fellowship, or Fellowship group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 55.

If this is your first Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>'We must protect the Heart of Fire!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Small Fellowship, or Fellowship group sizes by using the Instance Finder Pane. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 55.

If this is your first Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>'I must confess to you that I did not think the Orcs would be able to counter our plan. It is good that you were with us when things went sour, or this would be a grim day for the dwarves indeed!

'Instead, victory! The Heart of Fire remains in our power, and we live still to use it!'Bori suspects that he has stumbled upon something that will enable the dwarves to turn the tables on the threatening Orcs of Moria.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek.

Brogur has told you that his nephew Bori wants to speak with you about something.Room plaques can be found throughout the Water-works, as well as dangerous aquatic creatures.

Bori has asked you to memorize the locations of plaques in several different rooms throughout the Water-works.Memorize room plaques (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dangerous aquatic creatues can be found throughout the Water-works.

Bori has asked you to defeat creatures located amongst the ruins of the Water-works.Defeat creatures in the Water-works (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek.

You have scouted the Water-works for sign of the armouries the dwarf Óin sought, as recorded in the Book of Mazarbul, and should return now to Bori.'In my delight at the blow you have struck the Ghâsh-hai, I nearly forgot: my nephew Bori wants to speak to you about something. He would not tell me what has him so excited, but I am glad to see that he is keeping his spirits up; I have not seen him so cheery since before my son was slain by the Watcher in the Water.

'It is a valuable lesson to turn our grief into strength. Just ask Ashpar about the strength of the dwarves!'Bori greets you warmly and then looks around conspiratorially.

'I think I might be onto something, ${PLAYER}. While visiting my father yesterday, I snuck a peek at the Book of Mazarbul, and I saw something interesting: a line near the end saying that the dwarf Óin sought to find "the upper armouries of Third Deep," and some mention of a mighty axe. Do you think that Óin might have gone looking for Zigilburk?

'If we were to find the mithril axe Zigilburk, I think it could turn the tide of the coming storm! Óin must not have found it, but if he had, do you think Balin's expedition might have survived? We shall never know.

'Journey into the Water-works and look for room plaques; memorize them and return to me with their locations, and we might be able to find the armoury for which Óin searched! Slay any of the deadly creatures there, as well; if I am correct, there may be another journey there in our future!''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}! Tell me about the chambers you discovered. From the room plaques you saw, I may be able to discern which one is mentioned in the Book of Mazarbul, the armoury Óin sought.

'The Hall of Mithril, yes... I think that must be it, ${PLAYER}! Well done!''Bori wants to speak with you about something; I know not what.''The Water-works are likely crawling with dangerous creatures. Defeat them and memorise the locations of the rooms there, and I may be able to discern the location of the armouries for which Óin was seeking.'Bori believes you have discovered the location of the armouries sought by the doomed dwarf Óin many years ago, and which might contain the mithril axe Zigilburk.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek.

Bori is waiting to speak with you to travel to the Hall of Mithril, where he believes you will find the mithril axe Zigilburk. He asked you to bring allies.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: It is suggested that you complete this quest while in a fellowship. Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge alone or with a smaller group.</rgb>Talk to Bori and travel to the Hall of MithrilBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek.

You and Bori discovered Bróin, still alive despite great hardship, and brought him safely from the drowned treasury where he found the mithril axe Zigilburk.Talk to Bori'Imagine how unstoppable we would be if we could retrieve Zigilburk from the darkness of the past. I would fear no attack of the Orcs, that much is certain!

'I have a good feeling about this: The Hall of Mithril must certainly be the armouries for which Óin sought. If only he had found them in time, the dwarves of Balin's expedition might have survived!

'It is too late for them, friend, but not for us. We will travel to the Hall of Mithril in search of these armouries. Speak to me when you are ready.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: It is suggested that you complete this quest while in a fellowship. Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge alone or with a smaller group.</rgb>'This adventure might not be easy, but if we can find Zigilburk within the depths of Ghân-gharâf, it will all be worth it!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: It is suggested that you complete this quest while in a fellowship. Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge alone or with a smaller group.</rgb>''${PLAYER}, we are heroes! Bróin lives still, and the mithril axe Zigilburk has come out of the darkness just at our time of greatest need!

'Can you believe our good fortune? Why, at this rate in a week's time we will surely drive the last Orc howling like a cur from Moria!'Bróin is alive, and is resting from his ordeal now in the Peaceful Path.Bróin is resting in the Peaceful Path, a camp established on Durin's Way, north-east of the gardens there.

Bori is sure that Bróin would like to speak with you about his adventures.'You should go now to see Bróin. I know that he will want to speak with you about his grand adventure.

'He's resting in the Peaceful Path, a camp that my father has made for those recovering from wounds received while reclaiming the mines from the Orcs and other unwelcome creatures that dwell in this place.

'The entrance to the Peaceful Path is along Durin's Way, north-east of the gardens there. There you will find Bróin recovering from his ordeal.''The Peaceful Path is along Durin's Way, north-east of its gardens. I know that Bróin would want to speak with you about his adventures.''Friend ${PLAYER}, I... I thank you for rescuing me. This is not the adventure I had in mind when we arrived in Hollin.

'When the creature of the pool took me from before the Doors of Durin, I thought I was doomed. But the creature must have had a mind to save some of its prey for later, and so I was left within the watery treasury in the depths of Moria, as was Óin so many years ago.

'He found Zigilburk, ${PLAYER}. Who knows how long he wielded it to fend off the monstrous creature in the depths? And yet, in the end, even with the mithril axe itself, he could not escape. That would have been my fate as well, if you had not found your way into the watery depths and driven away the beast.

'I desire adventures no more. No songs or tales for me; I have had enough.'The Forges of Khazad-dûm were once the heart of smithing within Moria. Here, the mighty dwarf-smiths would work the mithril and forge their greatest wonders. In the time since its fall, the Forges of Khazad-dûm have been flooded with massive lava-floes and populated by the Orcs of Moria and their troll and goblin-labourers. Here the Orc war-host hammers away incessantly, as they built their weapons and siege-engines in preparation for their war against Lothlórien.Raf and Sigir are at Anazârmekhem.

Pálmar asked you to speak with Raf and Sigir and to assist them in clearing the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Help Raf drive the Uruks out of the ForgesAssist Sigir in his reclamation effortsAssist Sigir in his effort to recover stolen toolsPálmar is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of the Forges of Khazad-dûm.

You assisted both Raf and Sigir with their tasks and should now speak to Pálmar to obtain his favour with Narfi.Talk to Pálmar at Anazârmekhem'The Forges are lost to us now... but we will reclaim them one day, and there is no time like the present to begin.

'Raf and Sigir, my two aides, need help in clearing out the Forges. They can be found here within Anazârmekhem. Speak with them, learn of the duties they are beholden to, and when you have finished assisting them, I will send word on to Narfi that you have successfully aided us in staving off the invasion of Lothlórien.

'While I have little love for the Elves, it will do us little good if their greatest stronghold falls.''Speak with Raf and Sigir. They can tell you what is expected of them and what must be done to ensure that the forges are maintained while the Orcs are driven out of that place.''Aye, Raf and Sigir both said that you proved a most willing and capable ally. We are fortunate to have folk like you aiding us here.

'Were it not for you, the Orcs may have turned out more arms than we could have handled and a fully armed and armoured force would have swept clear through the Dimrill Dale.

'Fortune shines on us that this will not be the case. You have my thanks, and word has been sent to Narfi that you are true, honest, and decisive. You have our thanks, ${PLAYER}.'The Orcs of Moria are attempting to dig through the avalanche blocking the Redhorn Gate and gain access to Eregion.The Orcs are digging at the Fallen Ice, north-west of Mekhem-bizru.

Raskwith asked you to stop the Orcs who are attempting to dig through the avalanche at the Fallen Ice.Defeat Orcs at the Fallen Ice (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Raskwith is at Mekhem-bizru, south-east of the Fallen Ice.

Raskwith will be pleased to hear the Orcs' efforts have been disrupted.Talk to Raskwith at Mekhem-bizru'Orcs are a trickier lot than you might give them credit for. Travelling from Eregion to here in the Dale through the underground of Khazad-dûm can take days, even when you know where you are going. Heading through the Redhorn Gate is much faster, especially when you are bringing large and heavy loads.

'Mazog has dispatched a company of Orcs to the Fallen Ice, north-west of here. They are attempting to dig through the wrath of Caradhras.

'They cannot be allowed a second path through the mountain. Head up there and interrupt their efforts.''Mazog will have to resort to the depths for his travels now. While he has always had them, it is easier for us to stop him when he only has one route.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for your aid.''The longer you stand here, the more the Orcs dig! Get a move on!'Klintur has been studying the spiders of the area in search of a cause for their queer behaviour.Klintur's spider is north-west of the Shadowed Refuge.

Klintur's spider keeps escaping from its cage. He asked you to find it and 'encourage' it to return, lest it bring an entire clutch back to free the others.Encourage the escaped spider to return to its cageKlintur is at the Shadowed Refuge, east of the spider-cages.

Klintur will be pleased to hear that you 'encouraged' the spider to return to its cage.Talk to Klintur at the Shadowed Refuge'What? Speak up, ${PLAYER}, if you need something. I am Klintur. Are you also here to study the spiders? No? Whyever not?

'Well, look at them! Disgusting things. They have been infected by something, is what I think, but I have no idea what. I have been keeping some of them in cages below this cliff and go down to study them when I get the chance, but I have a small problem. One of them keeps managing to get free. There are many more out there, but the last thing we need is for her to get to the others and bring an entire clutch down upon us.

'Head down the cliff here and then look along the path to the north. She normally does not go far, I think she views this as some sort of wicked game. If you prod her enough, she should come running back to the safety of the cage.''The spider is back? Good, ${PLAYER}, good. That brings me some relief. I know she is a relatively little thing, but I've no doubt she could bring back a horde if she escaped.''The spider that escaped is the first I ever captured.'The Orcs at Drû-garmadh have been gathering up supplies of wood with which to build massive siege-weapons.Wood piles can be found in Drû-garmadh, south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Dagfari, hoping to delay the construction of any siege-weapons, wants you to head to Drû-garmadh and burn the wood-piles in the Orc-camp.Burn wood-piles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagfari is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh.

Dagfari will be pleased to know you burned the Orcs' supply of wood.Talk to Dagfari at Mekhem-bizru'The Orcs have been cutting down trees in the Dimrill Dale, but it does not appear to be just for camp-fires. No, they have cut far too many trees for that. I fear they may be up to something more devious.

'While they are not needed within the depths of Khazad-dûm, Orcs are able to construct great weapons of war, weapons capable of laying siege to village, town, or city. I fear that is where all those trees are going.

'Head to Drû-garmadh, south-east of here, and set flame to the wood-piles you see. Hopefully that will delay them long enough for us to devise a plan to end their destruction once and for all.''Hurry up and get down there. You will not want to have to deal with that wood once it has been turned into a catapult.''I saw the smoke from here. That should set them back at least a few days, and hopefully they will venture into the outskirts of Lothlórien to fell trees... the Elves there will quickly dispatch them.'Káti is disgruntled that his theory seems to be wrong. He thinks you may garner more information from Tyki, a dwarf at the Shadowed Refuge.Tyki is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, far to the south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.

Káti believes his friend Tyki at the Shadowed Refuge may know more about the fungus.Talk to Tyki at the Shadowed Refuge'All right, it appears I may -- may! -- have been wrong. Perhaps.

'I've been sending such glowing reports to my friend Tyki, too...well, theories, anyway. Ideas. About the source of the fungus. He has some ideas too, in fact. Why don't you go talk to him? 

'Tyki is at the Shadowed Refuge, far to the south of here. Head east into Nud-melek but turn south just before you reach the Bridge of Khazad-dûm. Continue south past Mazog's forces and into the Foundations of Stone.''Hello there! Tyki, at your service and your family's.

'Ah, good old Káti sent you? Gracious me. Did he bend your ears about his strange pet theory? The invisible stone-lines? It seems I receive another long letter from him every other week about it. Ha! Yes, that sounds like him. Had you go investigate them? And what did you find?

'I suspected as much. Well, no matter. His ideas may have been...off the trodden path, but he is right in one respect: it is vital to discover why Khazad-dûm is being plagued with this unnatural infestation!''Tyki knows a great deal about mushrooms and infestations and things of that sort. You should consult with him on the possible source of this fungus.'The Orcs have flooded out of Moria and are quickly taking over the Dimrill Dale.Orcs can be found at Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul, all south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Raskwith asked you to head into the Dimrill Dale and thin the ranks of the Orcs there.Defeat Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Raskwith is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of the Orc-camps.

Raskwith will be pleased to hear that the ranks of the Orcs have been thinned.Talk to Raskwith at Mekhem-bizru'Ever since we left Moria the goblins and Orcs have been pouring out into the Dimrill Dale. It has become increasingly difficult to maintain our positions here.

'The Orcs have established three primary camps, all south-east of here: Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul. I care not which camps the Orcs come from, as long as you thin out a good number of them.

'When you have reduced their numbers sufficiently, return here to me.''The rabble has been thinned. This is good, for now we can strike against their leaders.''The Orcs are not going to defeat themselves, ${PLAYER}. Their camps lie to the south-east.'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, has invited you to recollect your experience defending the Deep-way from attack by Mazog's Orcs.The Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'The Battle of the Deep-way.'

A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit the Battle of the Deep-way.Peer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Battle of the Deep-way'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria.

A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting the Battle of the Deep-way.'The tale of your deeds grows ever longer and more full of glory, ${PLAYER}, and your assistance during the great battles of Moria must surely be one of the most notable!

'Your aid proved invaluable during the Battle of the Deep-way, friend ${CLASS}, when hope seemed to be lost. But it was not so, and you helped the defenders to carry the day!

'If ever you wish to revisit the desperation and horror of that battle, you should peer into the Reflecting Pool. War with the Orcs is dangerous and difficult, but there is honour and glory to be had there too.''I am happy that you have revisited your defence of the Deep-way, ${PLAYER}. Only by studying our past can we gain knowledge to aid our future.''Look into the Reflecting Pool and meditate upon your past deeds....'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, has invited you to recollect your experience defending the Twenty-first Hall from attack by Mazog's Orcs.The Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'The Battle of the Twenty-first Hall.'

A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit your defence of the Twenty-first Hall.Peer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Battle of the Twenty-first Hall'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria.

A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting your defence of the Twenty-first Hall.'We would have lost this place and our lives, ${PLAYER}, had you not provided such valuable assistance during the attack. The Iron Garrison owes you a great deal for your aid in defence of the Twenty-first Hall.

'If you wish to relive the experience of that desperate defence, you should peer into the Reflecting Pool to recollect your memories of that dreadful battle. You might learn something of yourself to bring you strength in battles still to come.''I am happy that you have revisited your defence of the Twenty-first Hall, ${PLAYER}. Only by studying our past can we gain knowledge to aid our future.'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, has invited you to recollect your experience defending the Way of Smiths from attack by Mazog's Orcs.The Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'The Battle of the Way of Smiths.'

A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit the Battle of the Way of Smiths.Peer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'The Battle of the Way of Smiths'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria.

A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting your part of the Battle of the Way of Smiths.'The Heart of Fire on the Way of Smiths is still under control of the Iron Garrison, ${PLAYER}, but that is in large part due to your efforts.

'If ever you wish to revisit the great deeds that were done during that battle, you should peer into the Reflecting Pool. It may be that you could learn something that would be of value were you to recollect your part during the defence of the Way of Smiths.''I am happy that you have revisited your defence of the Way of Smiths, ${PLAYER}. Only by studying our past can we gain knowledge to aid our future.''Look into the Reflecting Pool and meditate upon your past deeds, ${PLAYER}....'Tyki wants you to kill some of the fungus-infested Orcs he has seen in the area.Globsnaga Orcs can be found at Dalgum-ru, south of the Shadowed Refuge.

Tyki wants you to slay the Globsnaga Orcs in the area.Defeat Globsnaga Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tyki is at the Shadowed Refuge, north of Dalgum-ru.

You should return to Tyki and report that Dalgum-ru is indeed heavily infested with Orcs, and you have slain many.Speak to Tyki at the Shadowed Refuge'Have you seen the Orcs around these parts, friend ${CLASS}? Disgusting, aren't they?

'I doubt such horrors would have peopled Durin's worst nightmares. In his name, rid us of some of this infestation!

'You will find many of these infested Orcs to the south, around the encampment they call Dalgum-ru.''This situation is revolting! It is a good thing you've gotten rid of some of those Orcs, ${PLAYER}, but our work is far from done!''They are everywhere! If you are having trouble finding some -- and I'm not sure how you could be -- you can look south, around Dalgum-ru.'Bori is certain that with the power of the mithril axe Zigilburk, along with your help, he can defeat Mazog and end the threat of war.Bori is by one approach to Zabadgathol.

Bori is waiting for you to accompany him to Zabadgathol.Talk to BoriThe door to the fortress of Zabadgathol is ahead.

Bori wants you to knock on the fortress door to summon Mazog.Knock on the fortress doorBori awaits an answer to his challenge.

You should speak with Bori and defend him if the need arises.Talk to BoriBori has been frozen by some foul craft, and you are released to bring the grim tidings to the dwarves.Survive your encounter with Gorothúl and do as he saysSweina has arrived on the outskirts.

You should talk to Sweina about the grim turn of events.Talk to Sweina'As much as it pains me to say this, we should go. If this sorceror wields such foul craft as you say, we cannot hope to survive long enough to free Bori or to wrest Zigilburk from his enchanted hand.

'Quickly, ${CLASS}. Before the Orcs decide that our heads would send message enough!''Do you remember our victory at Stazgnâkh? This will be even more glorious, for now I wield the power of Zigilburk!

'With one blow we will slay Mazog and leave the Orcs leaderless and confused.

'Onward, my friends! There are many Orc-necks ahead, and Zigilburk thirsts for battle!''Knock on the door, ${PLAYER}, and tell Mazog that we have come to end his pitiful life and reign!''Why does he not answer? For all the whispering of his warriors, I had not thought Mazog to be as cowardly as he now appears!

'Perhaps the sight of Zigilburk shining in the harsh light of this place has turned his legs to jelly and his courage to water!''${PLAYER}, what has happened? Where is Bori?'

Sweina listens in shocked silence to your account, his fists clenching in wrath.

'Cursed Orcs! Always they seek some strong ally, some powerful force to tell them what to do, a lesser master under their greater one, perhaps, but still terrible!

'We have to get out of here, ${PLAYER}. There is nothing we can do for Bori now.'You have travelled to the Deep-way to aid in its defence. Follow Brogur's direction and help the Dwarves of Moria make their stand.You should speak to Brogur to see of what aid you might be in the coming battle.Speak to BrogurHelp hold the Deep-way against the Mazog's assault.Defend the Deep-wayPrevent a barricade from being overrunPrevent Brogur from being defeatedThe warleader of the assault against the Deep-way has entered the battle. You must strike this Orc down and claim victory.Defeat Horngoth and his minionsPrevent a barricade from being overrunPrevent Brogur from being defeatedWith Horngoth defeated, the battle of the Deep-way has been won. Speak to Brogur to see what else he would have you do.Speak to Brogur'The barricades are set and my dwarves stand ready. All that must be done now is wait for the Orcs to come.

'I would ask that you follow the ebb and flow of the battle and aid where you are needed most. Also, do not forget to unfurl the banners of Khazad-dûm. They can help stir the hearts of all Free Peoples to great deeds and may even help turn the tide of battle. However, do not use them lightly, as once unfurled, a banner's strength is spent.

'Prepare yourself, as I fear it won't be long now...''It was a glorious battle, ${PLAYER}. One that shall be long remembered! The Orcs thought they could use trickery to gain the upper hand, but they could not stand in the face of our combined might.

'Now, let us finish our business here and see what else we can do to push back these foul Orcs!''There is naught else to do here, so we should be off. Are you prepared to leave?'You have travelled to the Twenty-first Hall to aid in its defence. Follow Wíli's direction and help the Dwarves of Moria make their stand!Speak to Wíli to see what aid you might lend in his defence.Speak to WíliHelp hold the Twenty-first Hall against Mazog's assault.Defend the Twenty-first HallPrevent a barricade from being overrunGoblin-sappers have destroyed the barriers at the Twenty-first Hall's barricades. Wíli has sounded a retreat to the hall outside the Chamber of Mazarbul.Fall back and defend the hall barricadesPrevent a barricade from being overrunDefend WíliOnce more, goblin-sappers have destroyed the barriers at the barricades. Wíli has called a retreat to the Chamber of Mazarbul.Fall back and defend the Chamber of MazarbulDefend WíliWith the Orcs driven off, you should speak to Wíli to see if there is anything else he would have you do.Speak to Wíli'I do not believe there is anything else for us here, ${PLAYER}. Shall we go?''Our defences are in order. Now I must tell you the role you are to play in the upcoming battle.

'I would ask that you aid the barricades as they come under assault and ensure they stand. If even one barricade is overrun, all shall be lost. Fortunately, there are many dwarf banners for us. These banners can draw up the courage and strength that is found in the hearts of all and inspire them. Unfurl these banners, ${PLAYER}, when things seem most desperate. They might just turn the tide of battle.

'Those are my orders, friend. Now we must wait and hope we shall draw breath another day.''Mazog's Orcs nearly had us there, ${PLAYER}! His vile tricks were nearly our downfall. Fortunately, with your strength, we were able to make our stand here, in the Chamber of Mazarbul.

'Perhaps after our victory Mazarbul will now be known for something more than being the place where Ori and many other brave dwarves met their end. Perhaps it will be known as the place where the reclamation of Moria truly began.'You have travelled to the Way of Smiths to aid in its defence. Follow Stóthkell's direction and help the Dwarves of Moria make their stand!Speak to Stóthkell to see what aid you might lend in the defence.Speak to StóthkellFollow Stóthkell to learn the source of what is shaking the Way of the Smiths.Follow StóthkellHelp hold the Way of Smiths against Mazog's assault.Defend the SmithwayPrevent dwarves from being defeated (${VALUE}/8)Prevent a forge from being overrunDefend StóthkellWith the Orcs driven off, you should speak to Stóthkell to see if there is anything else he would have you do.Speak to Stóthkell'There is little else for you to do here now, ${PLAYER}. Do you wish to leave with me?''Ah, I fear you have wasted your time coming here, ${PLAYER}. With the way shut, we shall have no problems with the Orcs. Those witless fools have no chance of forcing this door open.

'I wish I could see the look on Amukh's face. Amukh is a goblin who has crafted many foul blades for his Orc masters, but has boasted that his work is as good as dwarf-make! The fool goblin even thought to claim these dwarf works for his own foul purposes! As long as I draw breath, that shall never happen!''I am mortified, ${PLAYER}. My pride nearly lead to Zigilburk being lost to us! If it were not for you and your companions, we would not have withstood this day.

'You have my sincerest thanks. You are a true dwarf-friend.'You have come with Bori to the flooded passages beneath the Water-works, where he believes Zigilburk might yet be found.Bori is just inside the door to Gundlajân.

Bori is waiting to speak with you about his plan.Talk to BoriThe flooded tunnels between Gundlajân and Ghân-gharâf are blocked by ancient dwarf-mechanisms and filled with all manners of dangerous beasts. Both challenges will need to be overcome.Clear a path through the flooded tunnels to Ghân-gharâfBori has helped clear a passage into Ghân-gharâf, and you should now make your way through it.Enter Ghân-gharâf through the unblocked passageYou have discovered Bróin in the flooded ruin of Ghân-gharâf, still alive despite his struggle with the Watcher in the Water before the Doors of Durin.Talk to BróinThrough secret, water-filled passages, the Watcher has returned to Ghân-gharâf to find something unexpected: adventurers who wish to challenge it.Do battle with the Watcher in the WaterBróin is weak, but you may be able to rescue him from the flooded depths before the Watcher returns in anger.Talk to Bróin'Let us... get out of here, ${PLAYER}. I am glad... this place will not... be my grave.''If you and your allies can clear the flooded passages that lie between Gundlajân and Ghân-gharâf, we might yet find the armouries written about in the Book of Mazarbul.

'Could it be that we might find Zigilburk there? I hope so, ${PLAYER}!

'If the records I have studied are to be believed, dwarves erected great mechanisms here to seal off several of the passages when the gredbyg grew too numerous. You will need to deal with the creatures and learn the means of operating the mechanisms to clear the way. I will follow you once I have finished examining the map of these places, for it is very confusing and we will need to keep our bearings.''I... cannot believe....'

Bróin shudders with the very effort of speech.

'The beast... in the water! Beware, friends....''Are you really... here... my friends? Is this some... apparition?'

Bróin coughs, and you see for the first time the axe shining by his side: an axe so fair, bright, and cold that it can only be made of mithril.

Bróin catches your glance and smiles weakly.

'The beast brought me to this place... thinking to save me for later... I expect; one of its victims bore this. He is all bones, now, but I owe him my life, whoever he was. I could keep the beast at bay... with the axe made of mithril... but did not have the strength to escape. I would... surely have starved.

'You say Bori is with you? What... a wonder. I shall give him a surprise, I expect! Good old Bori!'Tyki has been watching the Globsnaga Orcs closely for any signs that his attempted freshwater cure worked. He has determined that it has not, and the Orkish menace must be purged from Khazad-dûm...with fire.The fungal structures can be found in and near Dalgum-ru, south of the Shadowed Refuge.

Tyki wants you to burn some of the strange fungal structures close to the Orcs' camp.Burn the fungal structures (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tyki is at the Shadowed Refuge, north of Dalgum-ru.

You should return to Tyki to tell him how flammable those fungal structures turned out to be.Speak to Tyki at the Shadowed Refuge'It's no use, ${PLAYER}. I was hoping to go back to a nice, quiet, clean lifestyle of killing normal, straightforward Orcs, but it seems that such is not to be. These fungal monstrosities cannot be permitted to continue to sully the beloved stones of our ancient home!

'I have noticed the fungus infesting various structures around the Orcs' camp, as have you, I am sure. I don't know what they are, and I am not sure I care -- but I suspect they are contributing to the problem.

'If purifying water did not work, then perhaps purging flame will! Burn the fungus-covered structures throughout and around Dalgum-ru, then return to me.''Ah, well met, ${PLAYER}! So, did those structures burn? Or were they too wet?''Look to the south for Dalgum-ru, the Orcs' camp, in and around which are the strange fungal structures I mentioned to you. Burn them to ashes!'Nökkvi fears the strange, nameless horrors he has seen in the Foundations of Stone.Nameless can be found throughout the Foundations of Stone, especially along the lake's eastern edge.

Nökkvi wishes you to dispose of the nameless horrors that have been terrifying himDefeat Nameless in the Foundations of Stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nökkvi is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.

You should return to Nökkvi and assure him that you have slain the nameless beasts.Talk to Nökkvi at the Shadowed Refuge'Ah! Perhaps you can be of aid!

'Have you seen these horrific nameless creatures? They have especially infested an area on the lake's eastern edge. I beseech you, ${CLASS}, go there and rid us of some of these revolting things! 

'Have you realized that some of them don't even have heads? Vile, to be sure!''You have greatly lightened my mind, ${PLAYER}. Now perhaps I can just put the whole business out....

'What! You saw dwarf-corpses there? And they were gnawed upon? Ai-oi!''Oh, please don't talk to me until you can assure me those revolting things are no longer here to torment my imagination!'Orcs have left the depths of Moria to establish a camp in the Dimrill Dale. The dwarves worry as to what the purpose of the camp is.Orcs can be found at Drû-garmadh, south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Alrekur is concerned about the number of Orcs setting up camps in the Dimrill Dale and wants you to thin their number.Defeat Orcs in Drû-garmadh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Alrekur is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh.

Alrekur will want to know the Orcs at Drû-garmadh have been thinned.Talk to Alrekur at Mekhem-bizru'All of these Orcs around the Dale concern me. Were they all still in Khazad-dûm, I would feel better, but out here, they can inflict great damage. They have dug countless new tunnels into the depths from which they can launch attacks nearly anywhere at anytime. We can cripple their ability to do that if we control this place.

'I have seen the stockade of a great camp to the south-west. I do not know what is going on in there, but smoke rises from it almost constantly. It is clear that they are up to something which will cause us great trouble if we allow it to continue unchecked.

'Head south-west, to Drû-garmadh and investigate the camp. Thin out some of the Orcs there as well... that will make a second strike go more smoothly.''The Orcs are building too many camps above ground... something has them stirred to action.''So, you have reduced their number, but they have begun making the machines of war. This will require an immediate strike. It will be better for us to catch them unaware than to face the grim alternative.'Klintur is appalled by the sheer number of spiders and believes that killing off their queen may help reduce the damage they inflict upon the halls of Khazad-dûm.The spider-lair is due east of the Shadowed Refuge, which is on the western edge of the Foundations of Stone.

Klintur has asked you to defeat the spider-queen who prowls the nearby spider lair.Defeat UanuilothKlintur is at the Shadowed Refuge, above the spider-lair.

You should return to Klintur and reassure him that Uanuiloth has been defeated.Speak to Klintur at the Shadowed Refuge'You may have seen the spider-queen who calls the nearby lair home. You can find her east of here -- don't hurt your legs jumping off!

'Defeat her, and my breath will come a little easier.''Your efforts are much appreciated, ${PLAYER}. I don't care how many spider-queens rise, I am determined to see them all destroyed!''Has your courage failed you?'The Forges of Khazad-dûm were once the heart of smithing within Moria. Here, the mighty dwarf-smiths would work the mithril and forge their greastest wonders. In the time since its fall, the Forges of Khazad-dûm have been flooded with massive lava-floes and populated by the Orcs of Moria and their troll and goblin-labourers. Here the Orc war-host hammers away incessantly, as they built their weapons and siege-engines in preparation for their war against Lothlórien.The Forges of Khazad-dûm lie to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.

Sigir asked you to collect bits of mithril from the forces of the Enemy now inhabiting the Forges of Khazad-dûm.'It is a terrible shame, what happened here. When I think of all the wonders that were forged within the true fires of this place, and then I think of this....

'Well, there's no time to dwell on that. There is work to be done, and that means I must tell you a bit about this place. Within the walls of the Forges of Khazad-dûm you will find Orcs, Uruks, goblins, and mindless trolls. The goblins mine, the trolls carry foul-smelling powder to and fro, and the Uruks fire the forges so they can craft their arms, all the while carrying bits of precious mithril everywhere they go. Mind you, the mithril is no bigger a sliver the width of your fingernail, but with enough...oh the wonder of it!

'Regardless, the mithril is rightfully ours. I ask you to go there and collect it from the Orcs within. You will find the Forges of Khazad-dûm to the south-west of Anazârmekhem. Make your way there and return to me with the bits.''Mithril! It is not much, but enough to put a smile on the face of this old smith.

'I will keep this well and safe and offer you such great thanks that you might never know how pleased I truly am!'Nökkvi demands vengeance in the name of the fallen dwarves upon which the Nameless have been feeding.Mazam-dûm lies upon the eastern shore of the lake in the Foundations of Stone.

Nökkvi has asked you to return to the lair of the nameless creatures and defeat the greatest of their kind. Its death should serve as a decisive statement to the others.Defeat Blind-striderNökkvi is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.

You should return to Nökkvi and tell him of your victory against Blind-strider.Talk to Nökkvi at the Shadowed Refuge'We will have vengeance, ${PLAYER}. There is no other option. Our blades will sing as they are drawn from their scabbards! Our axes shall make the air shriek with the wind of their passing!

'Return to Mazam-dûm and defeat the largest, fiercest-looking beast that you can find. Let them realize that, whether they have faces or heads or not, we do not fear even the greatest of their defenders!

'Mazam-dûm lies upon the eastern shore of the lake.''Hah! Excellent! No more shall those creatures be able to think -- if they do, in fact, even think -- that their mere size and strangeness will keep our weapons from drawing their blood!''Well, what are you waiting for? Return to that horrid, foggy nesting-place of monsters and rid us of the biggest creature you can find!'The dwarves fear the Orcs are preparing to destroy Durin's Stone, which marks the revered place where Durin I first looked into the Mirrormere.Orc-sappers can be found at Uruk-gashan, south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Haflith asked you to go to Uruk-gashan and defeat the Orc-sappers threatening to destroy Durin's Stone.Defeat Orc-sappers at Uruk-gashan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Haflith is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Uruk-gashan.

Haflith will want to know that the Orc-sappers have been defeated, keeping Durin's Stone safe... for now, at least.Talk to Haflith at Mekhem-bizru'Durin's Stone is a treasure of the dwarves. It is in that spot, staring into the Mirrormere, that Durin decided to settle here and build Khazad-dûm. The stone serves as an eternal reminder to all dwarves of what is rightfully ours.

'I fear for the safety of Durin's Stone. The Orcs spewing forth from Moria have set up a camp around it, and daily I see several of them working on reducing it to dust. This cannot be allowed to happen.

'Head to Uruk-gashan, south-east of here, and defeat the Orc-sappers around the camp. They are the ones with the knowledge to reduce the stone to dust and are the greatest threat to our ancient monument.''Make haste, you fool! If that stone is destroyed, Durin's Folk might as well be destroyed as well.''The Orc-sappers have been stopped and the stone is safe for now. This lightens my heart, but there is more to do. We have not yet ensured Durin's Stone will remain for the generations yet to come.'The Warg-riders of the Dimrill Dale have been harassing the dwarf-encampment at Mekhem-bizru since it was first established.Wargs can be found at Athmadhul, south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Ótam wants you to thin the numbers of the Wargs so there will be fewer Warg-riders to trouble the dwarves.Defeat Wargs at Athmadhul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ótam is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Athmadhul.

Ótam will be pleased to hear that the Wargs around Athmadhul have been thinned.Talk to Ótam at Mekhem-bizru'The Orcs flowing from Khazad-dûm have found a powerful ally in the Wargs here in the Dale. This is a very bad thing for us here, as we cannot match Warg-riders in combat. They are too fast and too strong.

'If we want to fight this new menace, we will first have to strike at the Wargs. Head south-east, to Athmadhul, and thin the numbers of the Wargs there. Once we have done that, we can begin to think about the riders.

'Be careful, ${PLAYER}, for the beasts are dangerous, even singly. Return to me when you are through.''The Wargs have been silenced, but there is much yet to do. The Orcs yet remain, and they are a dangerous foe.''If there are no Wargs to ride, there will be no Warg-riders to raid.'The Deep-way, a passage connecting the Great Delving to the Water-works, must be defended against the Orc onslaught.Brogur is leading the defence of the Deep-way against the forces of Mazog. You should report to him to receive your assignment.Talk to Brogur in the Deep-wayThe first assault on the Deep-way has begun. Protect the barricades!Push back the first assaultThe second assault on the Deep-way has begun. Protect the barricades!Push back the second assaultThe third assault on the Deep-way has begun. Defend the barricades!Push back the third assaultThe fourth assault on the Deep-way has begun. Defend the barricades!Push back the fourth assaultThe final assault has begun. The enemy's numbers are waning, but their ferocity increases. Withstand this assault, defeat their leader, and maintain control of the Deep-way.Push back the final assault'The barricades are set and my dwarves stand ready. All that must be done now is to wait for the Orcs to come.

'I would ask that you follow the ebb and flow of the battle and aid where you are needed most. Also, do not forget to unfurl the banners of Khazad-dûm. They can help stir the hearts of all Free Peoples to great deeds and may even help turn the tide of battle. However, do not use them lightly, as once unfurled, a banner's strength is spent.

'Prepare yourself, as I fear it won't be long now....''It was a glorious battle, ${PLAYER}. One that shall be long remembered! The Orcs thought they could use trickery to gain the upper hand, but they could not stand in the face of our combined might.

'Now, let us finish our business here and see what else we can do to push back these foul Orcs!'The Way of Smiths, in which lies the secret entrance to the Heart of Fire, must be defended from the Ghâsh-hai loyal to Mazog.Stóthkell is leading the defence of the Way of Smiths against the forces of Mazog. You should report to him to receive your assignment.Talk to Stóthkell in the Way of SmithsThe first assault on the Way of Smiths has begun. Protect the forges!Push back the first assaultThe second assault on the Way of Smiths has begun. Protect the forges!Push back the second assaultThe final assault has begun. The enemy's numbers are waning, but their ferocity increases. Withstand this assault, defeat their leader, and maintain control of the Deep-way.Push back the final assaultThere is a pause in the battle. You should talk to Stóthkell on the Supervisor's Platform.Talk to Stóthkell atop the Supervisor's PlatformHarna the troll and his keepers are attacking the entrance hall!Defeat Harna and his keepers'There is little else for you to do here now, ${PLAYER}. Do you wish to leave with me?''Ah, I fear you have wasted your time coming here, ${PLAYER}. With the way shut, we shall have no problems with the Orcs. Those witless fools have no chance of forcing this door open.

'The Heart of Fire is... wait, what is that sound? It cannot be! They have found us!''I do not like this, ${PLAYER}. Can you hear the rumbling beyond the entrance hall? Come! Follow me!'In the deepest regions of Moria, there are strange and frightening creatures. Veúlfur dispatched a host of his finest agents to the Shadowed Refuge to meet up with Elves there to investigate rumours of the deep dark.Orc fungus-collectors can be found at the Foundations of Stone, south-east of the twenty-first Hall. Veúlfur is at the Twenty-first Hall.

Veúlfur wants you to be prepared for the undertaking he intends for you and asked you to retrieve a barrel from the Orc fungus-collectors as the first step in your preparations.'I have known for some time that there was something truly vile happening at the Foundations of Stone. Before I sent my agents to the Shadowed Refuge, I saw Orcs -- or things that looked like they were once Orcs -- picking through the fungus there. They had these great barrels on their side that they stuffed the fungus into and then mashed to a fine pulp.

'Before I send you off to the Shadowed Refuge, I want you to understand what this means and how vile this truly is. On the outskirts of the shadowy dark, you will find these collectors. Hunt one down and bring its barrel back to me.

'Begin your search south-east of here. When the ground grows moist and the area dark with traces of red emanating from the fungus, you will know you are in the right place.''Aye, this is the same mush that I recall seeing before. Did you get a good look at the beast that carried this? Good... good.

'You see, I believe that the Orcs there are changing themselves to become more like that thing, and that is what my agents are looking into at the Shadowed Refuge.'It is a constant struggle to keep the overwhelming numbers of the spiders to a minimum.Spiders may be found around Tunzelgund, east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Klintur has asked you to defeat many spiders in the Foundations of Stone.Defeat spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Klintur can be found at the Shadowed Refuge, west from Tunzelgund.

You should return to Klintur with news of your success.Talk to Klintur at the Shadowed Refuge'Everyday, I find myself astounded by the sheer numbers of the huge, fungus-infected spiders we see near the Shadowed Refuge. If you wish to be of aid to us all, you would help us destroy them!

'They are found everywhere, but most especially around Tunzelgund, east of here. With your aid, their numbers should gradually dwindle.''Ha! That's good news all around! That's one hundred and twelve legs that won't be twitching through MY nightmares anymore! 

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. My most sincere thanks!''The spiders are in the tunnels east of here at Tunzelgund.

'I cannot abide those awful things. Anything with more than four limbs and a tail just horrifies me, deep down.'The Forges of Khazad-dûm were once the heart of smithing within Moria. Here, the mighty dwarf-smiths would work the mithril and forge their greastest wonders. In the time since its fall, the Forges of Khazad-dûm have been flooded with massive lava-floes and populated by the Orcs of Moria and their troll and goblin-labourers. Here the Orc war-host hammers away incessantly, as they built their weapons and siege-engines in preparation for their war against Lothlórien.Kranklûk is in the Forges of Khazad-dûm, south-west of Anazârmekhem.

Raf has asked you to find and defeat the Black Uruk Kranklûk. He told you to shield yourself from fire and shadow when facing this terrible foe as he fears that it may be something more than a common Uruk.Defeat KranklûkRaf is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of the Forges of Khazad-dûm.

Kranklûk proved to be a powerful Uruk and perhaps something more. Still, after scaling down the terrible pit that the Forges of Khazad-dûm has become, you found and defeated the foe.Talk to Raf at Anazârmekhem'If what I surmise is true, this Uruk is no common foe. It is a Black Uruk of Mordor, a blackened spirit riding the Uruk's own strength.

'It is possible that this fiend is even unknown to the army it leads, but who can say for certain? It may all be a trick of light in this place and the dark shadows that lurk in every hall of this once prestigious home.

'Use caution and shield yourself from flame and shadow when you face this foe. Enter the Forges of Khazad-dûm, south-west of Anazârmekhem, and defeat Kranklûk, the leader of the Orcs in the Forges.''This is a great victory, ${PLAYER}. This foe was something more terrible than I feared and still you walked out of the flaming depths victorious.

'I will tell Pálmar of all you have done.''The Forges lie to the south-west. You will need to travel some to find them. They lay beside the barracks of Fil Gashan.'Though fire seemed to destroy the fungal structures, Tyki thinks that an end should be put to the leader of the Globsnaga Orcs.The Globsnaga leader can be found at Dalgum-ru, south of the Shadowed Refuge.

Tyki wants you to find the Orc-leader at Dalgum-ru and put an end to his offending existence.Defeat ZarzaTyki is at the Shadowed Refuge, north of Dalgum-ru.

You should return to Tyki to tell him of the death of Zarza, the Orc-leader.Speak to Tyki at the Shadowed Refuge'Burning fungus-infested structures may be a slow help, but it is not enough, I fear. To end the infestation, I believe we will have to cut the head from the serpent, so to speak.

'The leader of the Globsnaga Orcs can be found to the south at Dalgum-ru. I think his existence has been tolerated quite long enough.

'When the deed is done, return to me.''Zarza is no more? Wonderful news.

'Truly, ${PLAYER}, you have proven yourself to be a stalwart and courageous defender of Khazad-dûm and all of her legitimate inhabitants.''Have you forgotten where you are going? Dalgum-ru is where you will find the leader of those Globsnaga Orcs.'The Forges of Khazad-dûm were once the heart of smithing within Moria. Here, the mighty dwarf-smiths would work the mithril and forge their greastest wonders. In the time since its fall, the Forges of Khazad-dûm have been flooded with massive lava-floes and populated by the Orcs of Moria and their troll and goblin-labourers. Here the Orc war-host hammers away incessantly, as they built their weapons and siege-engines in preparation for their war against Lothlórien.The Forges of Khazad-dûm lie to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.

Sigir is disgusted that dwarf-tools are being used to forge the Orcs' weapons of war. He tasked you with rescuing the tools from their ignoble fate within the confines of the Forges of Khazad-dûm.'I will tell you this, ${PLAYER}: there are some fates worse than death. For tools of the dwarves, one such fate is to be held in the hands of an Orc, and that is precisely what transpires within the Forges of Khazad-dûm. If I had not seen the tools myself, I would not believe it...but I saw them leaning against the anvil as that Uruk forged away!

'Such a thing is incomprehensible to my poor eyes. I will not abide this. I need you to collect the dwarf-tools from within the Forges of Khazad-dûm. You will know them, as they rest against Orc-anvils throughout the forge itself. Collect them and return them to me.

'You can find the Forges of Khazad-dûm to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.''There now, little hammer and vise. We have seen you safely home. Well, ${PLAYER} has at any rate.

'You have my blessing, my friend, and I will be sure to inform Pálmar. Thank you for all you have done.'Wéorn thinks that the rune-rocks can be used to ward off an ancient evil, or at least mitigate its powers.The rune-rock lies near Mazam-dûm, on the eastern shore of the lake in the Foundations of Stone.

Wéorn would like you to press upon certain runes on a rune-rock in order and see what happens.Wéorn is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone.

You should return to Wéorn and relate how the rune-rock irritated a Nameless creature enough to draw it out of hiding.Talk to Wéorn at Shadowed Refuge'I have further examined some relevant records, ${PLAYER}, and I think I may have some new information... these rune-rocks were used to ward off evil creatures in the deepest delvings during Durin's day. But I wager they had never seen the nameless horrors we have uncovered!

'And yet... I have a feeling that the rune-rocks may prove crucial, somehow. You may laugh, but when I follow my feelings, good things tend to happen. Let us follow this one, shall we?

'I think that if you press the runes on one of these rocks in the right order -- don't worry, I will teach it to you -- they make a strange sort of writing. More of an idea, really; an idea of light, and civilization, and truth, and honour, and courage. Will you try it?''Bless me, did I forget to tell you where that rock was? Look for it at Mazam-dûm, on the eastern shore of the lake in the Foundations of Stone.''What did you see?

'And you say it was discomfited by the rune-rock's glow? Interesting. I wonder....

'It's not that simple, is it? Can these nameless things be fought through words, language, speech... names?'Wéorn has discovered records of a mysterious item called a 'rune-rock,' an item that intrigues him.Wéorn wants you to find and examine a rune-rock, whatever that is, though he does not know where to find one.Wéorn is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You should return to Wéorn and tell him of your discovery.Talk to Wéorn at the Shadowed Refuge'Wéorn, at your service. I am an historian. Khazad-dûm's greatest treasures, I believe, are in the records she has managed to keep safe for us, awaiting our return, protected from the ravages of time and Orc alike.

'Some of these records mention strange things only called rune-rocks...and the context seems to indicate it does not mean merely a stone inscribed with written runes, as one could find anywhere in Moria. The text speaks of them in terms of weapons or defences -- the dialect is a bit obscure here and there....

'Will you help me look for them? I have a feeling we will be glad of the knowledge.''You found one? Truly? What a wonderful bit of luck!''Now, I'm not sure where I would start looking...except that if these rocks are actually defences or even weapons, I would search in places where battle would be likely to occur.'Skûmfil is nothing more than a dumping ground, a place where the fallen Orcs of Moria are discarded when they begin to reek. It is here that two foes have gathered, each intent on using the corpses found therein for their own purposes. The kergrim and other scavengers as a source of food, and the insects as a place to lay their eggs to spawn future generations.Skûmfil lies to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Lar wants to see the gredbyg within the depths of Skûmfil defeated. The insects are trying to breed in the bodies dumped by the Orcs within Skûmfil, and if left unchecked, they could breed too quickly to control. Lar also wonders if they might be the source of the plague affecting the Orcs.Defeat grodbog-warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat grodbog hive-defenders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat blind drones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lar is at the Shadowed Refuge, north-west of Skûmfil.

You fought against numerous and varied gredbyg within Skûmfil and now must return to the Shadowed Refuge to inform Lar of your success.Talk to Lar at the Shadowed Refuge'These gredbyg are an annoyance, plain and simple. There is naught in particular I find acceptable with these insects. The best way to deal with them is to rid Khazad-dûm of them completely, I say.

'So that is what I want done. Go to Skûmfil and kill the gredbyg there. There are many of the things, and each and every one of them needs to be destroyed.

'It may seem a bit brash, perhaps, but insects should never grow this large. Skûmfil can be found south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.''Glad to know that you met with good success. This proves that you are a decent warrior indeed.

'I will pass along word of your success to Mallas. I thank you, friend.''If there are too many of those gredbyg, everything in Moria will be overrun. We cannot risk the gredbyg carrying disease or becoming such a numerous menace that they replace the Orcs once we drive them out of Khazad-dûm. We must kill as many as we can now.

'Go to Skûmfil south-east of the Shadowed Refuge and deafeat the gredbyg there.'You and Bingo have successfully passed through Moria, and now your adventurous friend prepares for the next leg of the journey.Durin's Stone can be found to the south-east of the exit of Moria, in Nanduhirion.

Bingo wishes to see the monument Spalvi mentioned, and has asked you to defeat any of the dangers in the Dimrill Dale that threaten the peace of that place.Find Durin's Stone by the edge of the Mirrormere, in NanduhirionDefeat Orcs in Nanduhirion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo wants to speak with you south-east of Durin's Stone, not far from where the Mirrormere drains into a lower pool.Talk to Bingo south-east of Durin's Stone, just beyond the fallsBingo is by the falls south-east of Durin's Stone, in Nanduhirion.

Bingo is waiting for you to speak with him before you continue the journey.Talk to Bingo south-east of Durin's Stone and travel with him throughout NanduhirionBingo is outside the entrance to Caras Galadhon, in Lothlórien.

Bingo has been given permission to stay in Lothlórien for the time being, and he wishes to make the most of the opportunity.Talk to Bingo outside the entrance to Caras Galadhon, in LothlórienPennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, can usually be found at Cerin Nauth, on the western side of the clearing at Cerin Amroth.

Bingo would like for you to find Pennasseth and borrow a book about the Elves of Lothlórien from her, so he can develop a better understanding of them.Find Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth, in LothlórienPennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, can usually be found at Cerin Nauth, on the western side of the clearing at Cerin Amroth.

You obtained a book of history from Pennasseth, but she has indicated that you should not bring it back to Bingo just yet.Talk to Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth once againPennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, can usually be found at Cerin Nauth, on the western side of the clearing at Cerin Amroth.

You obtained a book of history and a book of maps from Pennasseth, but she has indicated that you should not bring it back to Bingo just yet.Talk to Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth once againPennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, can usually be found at Cerin Nauth, on the western side of the clearing at Cerin Amroth.

You obtained books of history, maps, and art from Pennasseth, but she has indicated that you should not bring it back to Bingo just yet.Talk to Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth once againBingo is outside the entrance to Caras Galadhon, in Lothlórien.

Pennasseth, the Keeper of Stories, has given you a stack of books to give to Bingo in order to assist him with writing about the Elves.'I understand that dwarves and Elves do not get along very well, ${PLAYER}, but all of the Elves I have met seem to be fine sorts! I will not forget Spalvi's warning about the Elves that live on this side of the mountains, but I do not think we should be too worried about it.

'He did not speak only of Elves! It seems there is a great stone not far from here that is of some significance to his people: Durin's Stone. We should take a look at this monument, and perhaps I can sketch an illustration of it for my book.

'If we run into any dangers near the stone, you will take care of them, yes? My skill is with the quill, you know. Ha! You see?''We should take a look at Durin's Stone, and perhaps I can sketch an illustration of it for my book. If we run into any dangers near the stone, you will take care of them, yes? My skill is with the quill, you know. Ha! You see?''I will meet you south-east of Durin's Stone, my friend! There is a waterfall near there that I simply must see!''I am glad we were able to see Durin's Stone, ${PLAYER}, and I am gladder still that you managed to defeat some of the vile foes that stalk through this land! This would be a lovely place if it were not for their foul presence.

'Look at this view! Have you ever seen such a vibrant shade to the leaves of trees before, and in this season? Unbelievable! Speak to me when you are rested from your recent exertions, and we can go down to the stand of trees together. We must keep our eyes open for more Orcs, of course!''Are you ready? Let us go down to that stand of trees, but keep your eyes open for more Orcs! The foul creatures seem to be everywhere in this land, despite its natural beauty, or perhaps that is what draws them here... so they can despoil it!''I am not sure what to make of our mysterious hosts, ${PLAYER}! They certainly seemed welcoming, but they are simply so... so...

'I do not know what word I can use to describe them! They seemed somehow other-worldly, but at the same time very much a part of this land. It strikes me as very odd that they can be both, but that is the impression they gave to me!'

Bingo suddenly slaps his forehead.

'I forgot to ask them my questions! If I am going to describe our stay in the Golden Wood for my book, I need to have a better understanding of the Elves and their Lord and Lady. If you can meet the Keeper of Stories that was mentioned by Lady Galadriel, perhaps I can borrow a book that will help me learn about Lothlórien and its people? Find Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth, and see if she will lend me such a book!''If I am going to describe our stay in the Golden Wood, I need to have a better understanding of the Elves and their Lord and Lady. If you can meet the Keeper of Stories that was mentioned by Lady Galadriel, perhaps I can borrow a book that will help me learn about Lothlórien and its people? Find Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth, and see if she will lend me such a book!''Welcome to Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}. I have already heard tell of your deeds, and any aid I can provide to you will be gladly given.'

You explain that Bingo wishes to write a chapter in his book about the Elves of the Golden Wood, and he was hoping that Pennasseth might be able to lend him a book he could study for that purpose.

'It is a noble thing, ${PLAYER}, to seek knowledge of a subject about which you know little. I will happily give to Bingo a book that contains some accounts of the history of the Elves. Beware! The book is many pages, but even so it will not cover the entirety of its subject! What book could hope to do so?''If I am going to describe our stay in the Golden Wood, I need to have a better understanding of the Elves and their Lord and Lady. If you can meet the Keeper of Stories that was mentioned by Lady Galadriel, perhaps I can borrow a book that will help me learn about Lothlórien and its people? Find Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth, and see if she will lend me such a book!''No, do not go just yet! I have given to you a book of history, for if Bingo is to understand my people, he will need to know from where they came, and the trials they faced in their journeys to this point. But that is not all! There are so many names and places described in that book that I fear your friend will be quite overwhelmed and confused.

'To that end, take too this book of maps. With it he will obtain a full understanding of the many places in which Elves have lived, and perhaps he will also attain an appreciation for the great scope and vastness of this Middle-earth, and the lands beyond!''If I am going to describe our stay in the Golden Wood, I need to have a better understanding of the Elves and their Lord and Lady. If you can meet the Keeper of Stories that was mentioned by Lady Galadriel, perhaps I can borrow a book that will help me learn about Lothlórien and its people? Find Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth, and see if she will lend me such a book!''If your friend Bingo examines those books, he will have a basic understanding of the history of the Elves and the lands that shaped their journeys, but it is still not enough. Such a study would leave out one of the most important aspects of my people's experience: the works of Art they fashion, and the Art that fashions them!

'This book contains descriptions of many such works, and in some sad cases that is all that remains, for many have been lost to the ravages of Time and the plots of the Enemy. From these pages, Bingo will learn much about the Elves that he can learn nowhere else!''If I am going to describe our stay in the Golden Wood, I need to have a better understanding of the Elves and their Lord and Lady. If you can meet the Keeper of Stories that was mentioned by Lady Galadriel, perhaps I can borrow a book that will help me learn about Lothlórien and its people? Find Pennasseth at Cerin Nauth, and see if she will lend me such a book!''I have had another thought, ${PLAYER}. If your friend Bingo wishes to write a complete study of the Elves, I would be doing him and his future readers a tremendous disservice if I did not supply him with one more book.

'This is the tome, my studious friend! It contains many of the songs of my people, and within their lines Bingo will find much to feed both his mind and his heart. Sad songs there are, but also songs of triumph and of glad delight.

'The other books I have provided will tell him of Beren and Lúthien, or of Gil-galad, but a true understanding of what they mean to my people can only be found in song.''Your friend Bingo will be fully prepared to write of the Elves once you return to him with those books!''You have returned, and with a book about the Elves? Lovely! I will take that from you, and get to work reading... at... once...'

Bingo trails off as he sees the stack of books you have for him.

'I asked for a single book, ${PLAYER}, and if I am being honest I was rather hoping for a slim volume. But you have returned with three others, and not a one of them of trifling size! If I were to set about reading these, my journey would be halted for a month or more! I wanted to write a chapter about Elves, not a dozen!

'Well, I thank you for the material, and I will read for a time. But it seems to me that a full understanding of the Elves would take a lifetime... or two! Is this why they live such a long time, the better to understand their own complexity? My goodness!'

<rgb=#00FF00>Bert Bartleby has arrived outside the gate to Caras Galadhon.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'A Taste of War' (Recommended Level: 63, and it is further recommended that you have gained access to Mirkwood by obtaining Book 9, Foreword: 'The Dark Shore' from Calengoth at the docks, and completing his quest chain through 'Hilltop Assault.')</rgb>As the Gurvand fell, you saw a swollen sore covered in what appeared to be fungus ooze to the surface of its flesh.Veúlfur is at the Twenty-first Hall.

After discovering a diseased gland on the Gurvand, you plucked the item clear and must now deliver it to someone who might better understand its meaning.You discovered this gland as the Gurvand was slain. Perhaps Veúlfur at the Twenty-first Hall would be interested in this find.'This appears to be the same infection that spreads through the Orcs, but not the source. It appears that this creature was also infected.

'Was there nothing beyond this creature in that place? No?

'I think, ${PLAYER}, that the secrets of the deep dark of Khazad-dûm are not all yet learned. But for now, we know that a great evil is vanquished and that we have you to thank for these efforts.'In the deepest dark of Moria there is a place where the only light that shone emanated from dwarf-lamps and luminescant fungus. Now, these delvings are dim and darker than ever and home to creatures that exist in nightmares. Yet here they are, and Veúlfur's agents sent to the Shadowed Refuge draw little comfort in knowing that there is something within the Dark Delvings that commands the Orcs to poison themselves in a manner that gives them over to some greater will.The Dark Delvings lie far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Ymar's nightmares continue, and he needs you to help him rid them from his mind. He asked you to breach the Dark Delvings and kill the glow-worms there to set his mind at ease.Defeat glow-worms in the Dark Delving (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ymar is at the Shadowed Refuge, far to the north-west of the Dark Delvings.

You found the glow-worms within the Dark Delvings and defeated them as Ymar had asked.Return to Ymar at the Shadowed Refuge'More dreamscapes from my nightmares. I have seen the glow of the worms, the tendrils looking like gleaming diamonds dropping from the heavens.

'They are never diamonds, only worms, descending now to swallow my head choking my breath and ending my life. I awake from these nightmares without breath and sweating.

'Will you help me end these nightmares, end the terror? Kill the glow-worms in the Dark Delvings. You will find the Dark Delvings far to the south-east from our location here at the Shadowed Refuge. Kill them and return to me.''Sleep. I hope to sleep, but the gloom in this place darkens my dreams still. I hope that there will come a time when light returns here, and radiance once again holds sway.

'For now, I take solace in what you have done for me and will see that Gelirwen is informed that you served me well. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''If I knew the worms were dead, I might better rest even in the belly of Khazad-dûm, so dark and deep. Please breach the Dark Delvings to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge and kill the glow-worms there.'The Water-works is a site of importance to the dwarves who wish to remain in Moria. One such dwarf, Foreman Indrith, has made it a mission to repair the channel there. His tasks for you led to the discovery of the Watcher in the Water.The Watcher in the Water lairs within the Vile Maw.

Kaldi warned you that the foe within the Vile Maw was one that would drag the very hearts of those near it towards oblivion without the great power of light on their side. Be cautious and take two fellowships of your staunchest allies.Defeat the Watcher in the WaterKaldi is at the encampment outside of the Vile Maw.

Your victory over the Watcher in the Water will be held as a great triumph amongst the dwarves.Talk to Kaldi outside of the Vile Maw'We have found the location of the Watcher in the Water, the beast we faced outside of Moria... and a terrible foe indeed.

'The dread it causes shakes the foundation of the strongest willed warriors and only through the great power of the light shall it be overcome completely, it appears. Beyond those doors, it is clear that there is a great foe of Durin's Folk, and only those with the stoutest hearts and strongest resolve should enter.

'You will not face this foe with only a few allies. You must go in force, and you must all be prepared for the worst. Enter the Vile Maw, and if you survive, return to me.''I wish you well in your foray against the Watcher in the Water.''Defeated? Defeated! Ha! All hail you, Hero of Khazad-dûm! All hail the heroes who defeated the fiend.

'The Watcher is defeated and shall stir no more! There are cheers to be cheered and songs to be sung bearing your name, ${PLAYER}.

'A happier day in this dwarf's life has not yet been seen!'Nimrodel was the love of Amroth, lost Lord of Lothlórien.A statue of Nimrodel can be found north of Pennasdir along the path, beyond the ladders to Telain Galadhrim.

Pennasdir has asked you to place a flower on the silver plate at the feet of a statue of Nimrodel.Pennasdir is on Telain Glorelloth, in Caras Galadhon.

You have left the flower for Nimrodel by her statue and should return now to Pennasdir.Talk to Pennasdir upon Telain Glorelloth'While you were gone, I travelled to the river Nimrodel, ${PLAYER}. The stream was named for the Elf-maiden that lived upon its banks, and still it sings with her voice. She had the love of Amroth, long ago, and it was despairing of her that Amroth was forced to set sail with the tide that bore him away.

'Golden flowers float gently in the stream. I plucked one from the water and have brought it back with me for you.

'There is a statue of Nimrodel here in Caras Galadhon, north of here along the path, beyond the ladders to Telain Galadhrim. Leave this flower on the silver plate at its base and take a moment to remember the maiden Nimrodel.''Very good, ${PLAYER}, I am pleased that you have done this. May the flower from her stream bring Nimrodel some measure of comfort.

'Take this for your efforts.''A statue of Nimrodel can be found north of here along the path, beyond the ladders that lead to Telain Galadhrim. Leave the flower I took from the stream on the silver plate at the feet of the statue and spare a moment for Nimrodel.'Even the sorcerer Gorothúl must bow to the power of the Lieutenant of Dol Guldur and his wraith-minions.Defeat DúrchestDefeat CargarafDefeat MorgarafDefeat the Lieutenant of Dol GuldurYou have heard it whispered that the libraries of Moria yet contain many tomes, while many other volumes were brought by the dwarves seeking to reclaim their kingdom of old. One such tome in the libraries of the Iron Garrison is said to be the legendary "A Guide to the Quiet Knife." If you can gain enough favour with the Iron Garrison Guards, they may let you have their copy of this book.Achieve level 58Read the book, "A Guide to the Quiet Knife"You have heard it whispered that the libraries of Moria yet contain many tomes, while many other volumes were brought by the dwarves seeking to reclaim their ancient realm. One such tome in the libraries of the Iron Garrison is said to be the legendary "A Keen Blade." If you can gain enough favour with the Iron Garrison Guards, they may let you have their copy of this book.Achieve level 58Read the book, "A Keen Blade"You have found a finely-wrought necklace under the waters of a spring in Egladil.There are Elves throughout Egladil.

You should speak with the Elves in Egladil and learn to whom the finely-wrought necklace belongs.Talk to Hadhelen in EgladilTalk to Aesbrennil in EgladilTalk to Farasdúr in EgladilTalk to Glasnír in EgladilMaliriel is in Imlad Lalaith in Egladil.

You should bring the necklace to Maliriel to see if she knows to whom it belongs.Beneath the waters of this spring you have found a valuable-looking necklace -- perhaps someone dropped it here when they came to draw water from the spring.

One of the Elves in the Vineyards of Lórien may know to whom the necklace belongs.'This is too noble a thing for one such as I!

'Furthermore, it is certainly a woman's necklace, but I cannot say to whom it belongs for I have not seen its like before.''It is beautiful -- and you offer this to me as a gesture of your affections?

'Do not look at me so, my dear ${RACE}. I tease you!

'Truthfully, I have not seen its like before. Such a fine piece would likely belong to someone with considerable responsibility and a more honoured position than mine.''What a fine trinket you have there!

'You found it by the spring? That is odd, for it has the look of a noble lady's jewel. I wonder how it came to rest there.

'The Elves who possess trinkets like this would be found in Caras Galadhon, but those ladies rarely venture into secluded corners of the forest.''Do you think this necklace would go well with my attire? I am rather afraid it would set the colour of my eyes in a poor light.

'On our Mistress of the Feast I think it would look quite radiant, however, though I have never seen her wear such jewels as this.''Where did you get this necklace, ${PLAYER}?

'To whom does it belong, you ask? Why, to me of course. In the rush of preparations, I must have let it fall when visiting the spring. I had not even realized it was lost!

'You cannot know what this means to me, ${PLAYER} -- to live a thousand years with only his memory. Had I lost this forever... nay, such a loss would have been beyond my strength to bear. I am in your debt, kind randir.'

Maliriel quickly replaces the necklace around her neck, turning away momentarily to hide her tears.Istarien has lost to a mischievous breeze the pages of a letter she was writing.The five pages of Istarien's letter to Rilhathel can be found on nearby flets and in the area around Istarien.

The pages of an embarrassingly private letter Istarien was writing have been scattered onto nearby flets by a mischievous breeze, and she wants you to retrieve them.Collect wind-blown pages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Istarien is on one of the upper flets of Telain Galadhrim.

You have recovered the pages of Istarien's letter and should now return them to her.'Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. How are you enjoying your stay in Caras Galadhon?'

Istarien appears distracted and distant as you give your response. After a moment, she apologizes.

'I am sorry, my friend. I was writing a letter to Bruicheron's brother Rilhathel, but a sudden gust of wind grabbed the pages and has carried them from this flet out across the city!

'There were five pages, and some of what I was writing could be considered very private... a matter not for the accidental viewing of others! If you can recover the pages of my letter from the surrounding area, I would be most grateful!''The wind-blown pages of my letter might be anywhere in the nearby area, ${PLAYER}. If you can retrieve all of them and return them to me, I would greatly appreciate it!''Thank you so much, ${PLAYER}! I will keep a tighter grip upon the remaining pages as I continue to write my letter!

'You did not read it, did you? It is nothing embarrassing. Truly, it is not!

'Take this with my thanks, ${PLAYER}! I will be more careful in the future!'Amroth was an Elf-lord who once ruled in Lothlórien, but was lost at Sea, never to be seen again.The circular docks that extend into the Celebrant can be found south-east of Caras Galadhon, south of Imlad Lalaith.

Pennasdir has asked you to stand on one of the circular docks that extend into Celebrant and to <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> into the distance for Amroth.Pennasdir is on Telain Glorelloth, in Caras Galadhon, north-west of the docks.

You have participated in Pennasdir's tradition of looking for Amroth down the Celebrant and should return now to the Elf.Talk to Pennasdir upon Telain Glorelloth'Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel have ruled in Lothlórien for countless years, but they were not the first masters of the Golden Wood. You can hear the tale of Amroth and Nimrodel from others, but know that it is a sad song and does not end as you might wish.

'Amroth sailed into the Sea without his beloved and never returned, but every year my family travels to the circular docks that extend into the Celebrant so we can <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> into the distance for Amroth...though his ship sailed from Edhellond in the far south.

'This tradition allows us to feel closer to our forebears, and I would like for you to experience that connexion as well. Take a moment to remember Amroth of Lórien, ${PLAYER}, for those who have gone before should not be forgotten.''Very good, ${PLAYER}! I am glad you have taken a moment to remember Amroth's last voyage out to the sea, where he was lost and came not again to the land that he loved.''Travel to the circular docks that extend into the Celebrant, south of Imlad Lalaith, and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> into the distance for Amroth. It is a tradition that brings us closer to our shared history.'The banquets of Imlad Lalaith are known throughout Lothlórien for their festive nature -- but even among the Elves, overindulgance can become a problem.

Maliriel has asked you to help keep an eye on the guests, during the <rgb=#FF0000>evening revels</rgb> to ensure that matters do not get out of hand, as they are occasionally known to do.During the <rgb=#FF0000>evening hours</rgb>, find revellers in Imlad Lalaith who have indulged overmuch in wine and have become too loud or boisterous and remind them of their manners.Drunken revellers admonished (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF0000>Sober revellers admonished (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})</rgb>You should speak with Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith.Speak with Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith'My dear ${PLAYER}, I thank you for your help with the preparations for the <rgb=#FF0000>evening revels</rgb>, but there is one last matter. Even among our people, there is the occasional tendency to over-sample the fine products of our local vineyard, and the revellers can become a bit more loose with their tongues than I prefer.

'I must see to my duties as hostess and greeter to guests as they arrive... and so I was wondering if you could help me keep some of our more inebriated guests in line?

'I find it is easiest to determine who has overindulged by listening to their manner of speech. It is the way of the Elves of Lothlórien to remain quiet and well-mannered even during our revels -- so should you hear someone raising their voice over-loud or becoming unseemingly boisterous, it might be best to remind them of their manners.''Please send home any revellers who have had too much wine.''The revels continue undisturbed? My thanks to you, ${PLAYER}.'While the sappers at Durin's Stone may have been stopped, they were still able to inflict severe damage upon the hallowed rock.Fragments of Durin's Stone can be found at Uruk-gashan, south of Mekhem-bizru.

Haflith asked you to venture to Durin's Stone and collect the pieces the Orc-sappers had broken off.Collect pieces of Durin's Stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Haflith is in Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Uruk-gashan.

Haflith will want to see the pieces of Durin's Stone which you collected.'You stopped the Orc-sappers, ${PLAYER}, but I fear you were too late. It is not your fault. I should have gone myself as soon as I saw them. Although Durin's Stone has been saved, severe damage has been done.

'While they were preparing to destroy the stone, they chipped off many pieces. It has been defaced and made the fool of. There is but one course of action for us to take: we must reclaim what is left.

'Head south again, back to Uruk-gashan and search for the broken off bits and pieces of Durin's Stone. Gather up what you find and bring the pieces back here. At the very least we can salvage those, and perhaps one day, make the stone whole again.''You are only beginning to grasp what this stone means to us here. Hurry up and collect the pieces that were broken off.''It is as I feared. The damage was done already. Still, the rest of the stone stands, overlooking the calm depths of Kheled-zâram.

'One day, perhaps, these fragments will rejoin the rest. For now, I will keep them here, safe, in the event the unthinkable happens and Durin's Stone is laid ruin.'Upon defeating Talug, you discovered a note scrawled hastily and in nearly illegible handwriting. After some time you were able to make out what it said.There might be a dwarf who can help with the note in the Twenty-first Hall.

The note seems to indicate that General Talug has some measure of both fear and apprehension of what lay in the deep dark places of Moria.The note reads:

'Mazog, something's off with that Uruk Kranklûk. The boys see it, too. I think we'd best start paying close attention to those troops disappearing in the deep dark of that shadowy place. There might be something more than mushrooms there.'

Perhaps there is someone in the Twenty-first Hall who can help you with this.'Orcs afraid of something other than us dwarves? Ha! It seems that this has something to do with the rumours I have heard from our Elves and the company I sent to the Shadowed Refuge.'Pleased with your efforts on behalf of the Elves of Lórien, Hadroneth has asked you to continue your campaign against the Orcs that have invaded Nanduhirion.Orcs can be found north-west of Talan Haldir, along the road that runs through Nanduhirion to Moria. They have erected barricades outside their camps along the road: Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul.

Hadroneth has asked you to defeat Orcs in Nanduhirion and to set fire to the barricades they erect outside their camps along the road.Defeat Orcs in Nanduhirion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Set fire to Orc barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hadroneth is on Talan Haldir, located on the banks of Nimrodel, south-east of Nanduhirion.

You have continued your efforts against the Orc invaders of Nanduhirion, slaying many of their number and setting fire to the barricades they have erected along the road.'The Orcs have not yet left Nanduhirion, ${PLAYER}; it seems they still have designs on Lórien.

'You have helped us before, and if you continue to do so we will not forget it. Neither will the Orcs, if you continue to harry their fell endeavours in this way.

'Travel north-west to the Orc camps along the road that runs through Nanduhirion. Slay the Orcs there and set fire to any of the barricades they have built anew. We will never cease our efforts to push the Orcs back beneath the mountains, and protect the borders of our fair land.''Once again you have proven yourself a worthy enemy to the Orcs, ${PLAYER}. I will let you know when next we have need of your strength and skill.''The Orcs are still a threat to travellers on the road that runs from here to Moria. Defeat the Orcs and set fire to the barricades they have erected outside their camps in Nanduhirion, to the north-west.'Satisfied with your efforts on behalf of the Elves of Lórien, Maethoron has asked you to continue your campaign against the Orcs that have invaded Nanduhirion.Orc camps can be found all along the road that runs through Nanduhirion, north-west of Talan Haldir. Orc waylayers prowl along the road as well, and can be found on the outskirts of the camps there.

Maethoron has asked you to continue your efforts against the Orcs of Moria that have invaded Nanduhirion: defeating their waylayers along the road and stealing weapons from their camps.Collect Orc weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orc waylayers in Nanduhirion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maethoron is on Talan Haldir, located near the banks of Nimrodel, south-east of Nanduhirion.

You have stolen weapons from the Orc camps of Nanduhirion and defeated more Orc Waylayers along the road, and should return now to Maethoron with news of your success.'The Orcs still endanger travellers on the road through Nanduhirion, ${PLAYER}. The work of their foes is never done, it seems!

'You are familiar with their camps now: Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul; return to these foul encampments north-west of here, along the road that runs through Nanduhirion, and steal more of their weapons from the racks within. An Orc without a blade is an Orc from which we have little to fear.

'Slay too the Orc waylayers that prowl along the road that runs between here and Moria. They cannot be allowed to menace even the few travellers that come this way.''Return to Nanduhirion, to the north-west, and defeat Orc waylayers along the road. Look too for the Orc camps on the road between here and Moria, and steal the weapons you find. The Elves of Lórien will not forget your efforts.''Again you have proven an able ally, ${PLAYER}. I will let you know when we have need again of your help; with so many Orcs this near to Lórien, I fear it will not be long.'Encouraged by your efforts on behalf of the Elves, Celegúien wishes you to continue the work you began against the Orcs.The corpses of Orcs slain by the hidden Galadhrim along the border of Lothlórien, east of Echad Andestel, can be the source of more arrows desired by Celegúien. She warned you against going too near the border, for the Galadhrim will shoot if they do not know you.

Celegúien is waiting for you to recover arrows from the corpses of Orcs slain along the border of Lórien.Recover arrows from Orc corpses near the border of Lórien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Celegúien is in Echad Andestel, the camp along the banks of Nimrodel, west of the border of Lórien.

You have recovered arrows from the corpses of Orcs along the border of the Golden Wood, and should return now to Celegúien.Meredhrandir is at Mekhem-bizru, the camp just outside the eastern entrance to Moria, far to the north-west of Echad Andestel. Celegúien told you to follow the road west and north until you reach Mekhem-bizru, and to avoid the Orcs that prowl within Nanduhirion as you carry the arrows to Meredhrandir.

You have been told to bring a bundle of arrows to Meredhrandir at Mekhem-bizru.Pick up a bundle of arrows next to CelegúienMeredhrandir is at Mekhem-bizru, the camp just outside the eastern gate of Moria.

You have brought the arrows to Meredhrandir and should now speak with him about the journey.'The Orcs remain in Nanduhirion, ${PLAYER}, and as long as they do, the Galadhrim will have need of arrows to oppose them.

'Return to the border of the Golden Wood, east of here, and look for more Orcs slain by the arrows of the Elf-archers. Recover the arrows from their corpses, as you have done before, and return them to me.

'Do not stray too near the border, however! If the hidden Galadhrim do not recognize you as a friend, they may waste some of their arrows on you, and I will need to send other adventurers to recover them from your unfortunate body! That is not how your story should end.''East of here, along the north and south border of Lórien, you will find Orcs slain by the Galadhrim. Recover arrows from their bodies, as you have done before, and bring them to me.''You have returned with more arrows, ${PLAYER}? Very good! I have prepared a bundle of arrows for you to bring to Meredhrandir at Mekhem-bizru, as before.

'Pick them up from the crates right next to me, and carry them west and north along the road through Nanduhirion, to Meredhrandir at the camp just outside the eastern gate of Moria.

'Stay out of deep water, or you will be unable to hold onto the arrows for long!''Pick up a bundle of arrows from the crate next to me, and carry them to Meredhrandir at Mekhem-bizru, the camp just outside the eastern gate of Moria. Follow the road north-west through Nanduhirion, and avoid the Orcs that prowl nearby as you carry the arrows to Meredhrandir.''Another delivery of arrows, ${PLAYER}? Perfect! You have sealed the fate of more Orcs of Moria by bringing these to me.

'The Elves of Lórien will not forget your continuing efforts on our behalf.'Pleased with your efforts against the Orcs, Dindirith wishes you to continue providing aid to the Elves of Lórien.Orc filth can be found north and south along the banks of the river Nimrodel, west of the border of Lórien.

Dindirith has asked you to once again cleanse the banks of the Nimrodel of the Orc filth that sullies them.Collect Orc filth from the banks of the Nimrodel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dindirith is at Echad Andestel, north of the road that runs to Lórien and west of the border.

You have collected Orc filth from the banks of the Nimrodel and should bring it now to Dindirith.There are Orc camps all along the road that runs through Nanduhirion, west and north of Echad Andestel.

Dindirith has asked you to burn the Orc filth you collected in a fire located within one of the Orc camps along the road through Nanduhirion.Dindirith is in Echad Andestel, outside the border of Lórien and east of Nanduhirion.

You have once again disposed of the Orc filth and should report now to Dindirith.'More Orcs have crossed Nimrodel, ${PLAYER}, leaving filth in their wake.

'If you are still willing to help, I would ask you to once again walk north and south along the banks, picking up the filth of the Orcs so Nimrodel can once again run clean.

'Return to me when you have done so, and we will give the Orcs back their foul reek, as we did before.''Walk north and south along the banks of Nimrodel, as you did before, and clean them of Orc filth, ${PLAYER}.''You have my thanks again for keeping Nimrodel free of the filth of the Orcs. Bring it now to the fires within one of the Orc camps along the road through Nanduhirion, to the west and north of here, and dispose of it in an Orc fire, as you did before.''There are Orc camps all along the road that runs through Nanduhirion, to the west. Burn the Orc filth at a fire within one of those camps, ${PLAYER}, and show the Orcs once again that no stain on the land will go unpunished by the Elves of Lórien!''Well done, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs will learn that no stain on our land will go unpunished. I will let you know when I have need again of your help.'Someone has posted a task to deliver broken metal clubs to them. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire broken metal clubs.Wanted: Broken metal clubs taken from the defeated enemies of the Men of Enedwaith.Wanted: Broken metal clubs taken from the defeated enemies of the Men of Enedwaith.You have turned in a laudable number of broken metal clubs.Someone has posted a task to collect the gorgeous ears of the local wildlife. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous ears.Wanted: Gorgeous ears from various beasts that can be found in Enedwaith.Wanted: Gorgeous ears from various beasts that can be found in Enedwaith.You have turned in a worthy collection of gorgeous ears.Someone has posted a task to collect gorgeous furs from the local wildlife. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous furs.Wanted: Gorgeous fur from various beasts that can be found in Enedwaith.Wanted: Gorgeous fur from various beasts that can be found in Enedwaith.You have turned in a worthy collection of gorgeous furs.Someone has posted a task to deliver gorgeous sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous sword sheaths.Wanted: Gorgeous sword sheaths taken from the defeated enemies of the Men of Enedwaith.Wanted: Gorgeous sword sheaths taken from the defeated enemies of the Men of Enedwaith.You have turned in a respectable number of gorgeous sword sheaths.Someone has posted a task to collect nasty skin from the local wildlife. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire nasty skins.Wanted: Nasty skin from various beasts that can be found in Enedwaith. It is for the best that you do not ask questions.Wanted: Nasty skin from various beasts that can be found in Enedwaith. Questions will go unanswered.You have turned in a pile of nasty skins.Limhendeth has beseeched you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you and to instead report his activities to Glordirith in Lórien.Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin.

Limhendeth has asked you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you, and instead to report of his activities to Glordirith in Lothlórien.Talk to Glordirith at Imlad Lalaith'I do not know what you two spoke about, but my heart tells me that my people are right not to allow Asmund beyond the borders of Lórien.

'I beseech you, ${PLAYER} -- do not betray the trust of my people. Whatever Asmund asked of you, I say to you this: ignore it! Go instead to Glordirith, a friend of mine and protector of all things that move within the Golden Wood. He is entrusted to this duty by Celeborn himself, and if you tell him whatever it is Asmund asked you to do, I know you will be rewarded for it.

'Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin.''I thank you for your news of Asmund, ${PLAYER}. You have done well to bring his doings to my attention.

'We will keep a close watch on any who have dealings with Asmund the Poacher from this day forth. You are to be commended for your service in defence of the woods of Lórien.''Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}, at Imlad Lalith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin. Tell him of Asmund's activities and ignore whatever request that dwarf made of you!'Limhendeth has beseeched you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you and to instead report his activities to Glordirith in Lórien.Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil on the banks of Anduin.

Limhendeth has asked you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you, and instead to report of his activities to Glordirith in Lothlórien.Talk to Glordirith at Imlad Lalaith'What did you speak about with Asmund, ${PLAYER}? I am concerned about your dealings with him; he has an unsavoury reputation.

'I beseech you, ${PLAYER}: ignore whatever request he has made of you and instead report of his activities to Glordirith, a friend of mine and protector of all things that move within the Golden Wood. He is entrusted that duty by Celeborn himself, and if you tell him whatever it is Asmund asked you to do, I know you will be rewarded for it.

'Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin.''I thank you for your news of Asmund, ${PLAYER}. You have done well to bring his doings to my attention, though I suspect not as quickly as you might have.

'We will keep a close watch on any who have dealings with Asmund the Poacher from this day forth. You are to be commended for your service in defence of the woods of Lórien, and I have a small reward for you.''Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin. Tell him of Asmund's activities and ignore whatever request that dwarf made of you!'Limhendeth has beseeched you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you and to instead report his activities to Glordirith in Lórien.Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin.

Limhendeth has beseeched you to ignore whatever request Asmund made of you, and to instead speak of his dealings with Glordirith.'${PLAYER}, I beseech you: do not do whatever Asmund has asked you to do! He has an ill reputation, and no good will come of whatever task with which he has charged you!

'Speak instead with Glordirith, a friend of mine and protector of all things that move within the Golden Wood. He is entrusted that duty by Celeborn himself, and if you tell him whatever it is Asmund asked you to do, I know you will be rewarded for it.

'Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin.''Better late than not at all, ${PLAYER}. Asmund the Poacher and his agents will no longer harm the protected animals of Lórien; we will closely monitor his associates.

'You will still be rewarded, though I am loath to forgive the lateness of your message.''Tell Glordirith of your dealings with Asmund, ${PLAYER}. Asmund has an unsavoury reputation, but there is still time for you to avoid receiving the same as he.

'Glordirith is in south-eastern Lothlórien, at Imlad Lalaith in Egladil, on the banks of Anduin. It is not too late, ${PLAYER}.'Vile Wargs and fearsome merrevail darken Lumul-nar, the Hall of Mirrors. The light will not return here until the leaders of these evil creatures are dispatched.

<rgb=#FF0000>This deed can only be completed in the group version of the instance.</rgb>Defeat Frost-tailDefeat ErgothThe river Anduin flows north of Egladil, deep and wide, providing protection against assaults from the East.The river Anduin runs northwards from the Vineyards of Lórien.

Farasdúr has asked you to patrol the banks of the Anduin and ensure that no enemy forces have gained a purchase on the west side of the river.Patrol the banks of the Anduin (0/4)The river Anduin runs northwards from the Vineyards of Lórien.

Farasdúr has asked you to patrol the banks of the Anduin and ensure that no enemy forces have gained a purchase on the west side of the river.Patrol the banks of the Anduin (1/4)The river Anduin runs northwards from the Vineyards of Lórien.

