hest has challenged you to prove your familiarity with Caras Galadhon in a race through the trees.The flet-runner can be found on a flet with a mailbox high above Telain Galadhrim, near the entrance to the Crafting Hall.

Celechest has challenged you to quickly make your way to a certain flet-runner.Find the flet-runner by the entrance to the Crafting HallThe flet-runner by the entrance to the Crafting Hall on Telain Galadhrim is waiting to speak with you.Talk to the flet-runner by the Crafting Hall'Have you yet learned your way through our fair city, ${PLAYER}? Caras Galadhon is both beautiful and complex and to find your way around can be daunting for the newcomer...what few newcomers there are.

'Those who become especially skilled at finding their way among the telain throughout Caras Galadhon are known as "flet-runners."

'Do you have the necessary skills? I challenge you to find the flet-runner atop the high flet of Telain Galadhrim, by the mailbox and the entrance to the Crafting Hall, with utmost haste!''You have surprised me, ${PLAYER}, and I know Celechest will be surprised as well! You have demonstrated both a cursory knowledge of our city and a quickness that has let you reach me in time, but there is much more for you to prove if you wish to be known as a flet-runner.

'Look for certain of my friends throughout the city if you wish to engage in similar tests of your awareness and fleetness: Leginiel, Lagordal, Bregradel, and Lintwen. They will measure your skill.

'Nevertheless, you have earned this gold leaf, ${PLAYER}.''You are wasting time, ${PLAYER}! The flet-runner I want you to seek is on a flet high atop Telain Galadhrim, near the mailbox and the entrance to the Crafting Hall.'Hasta is asking that anyone willing to help him should gather the various ingredients necessary to draw forth the menace from beneath the Water-works.Three-spined Sticklebacks can be fished from the Water-works.

Hasta would like you to bring him five Three-spined Sticklebacks.'I am very glad to have your assistance in this matter, ${PLAYER}. In order to give our lure the proper texture, we will need food similar to what our prey eats normally.

'The creatures we investigated earlier seem to eat a peculiar fish only found down here in the Water-works -- Three-spined Stickleback.  

'If you are an accomplished fisherman, you may use your skills in angling to catch these rare fish. Bring me a fair number of these, and I'll add it to our collection.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! Your contribution is greatly appreciated.

'Be sure to speak with me again if you have more ingredients to add to the pile.'Hasta is asking that anyone willing to help him should gather the various ingredients necessary to draw forth the menace from beneath the Water-works.Hasta can be found in the Rotting Cellar in the Water-works of Moria.

Hasta would like you to bring him ten phials of mint sauce, and ten batches of mashed royal taters.'I am very glad you have decided to help me with this task, ${PLAYER}. These ingredients would be difficult for one person alone to gather.

'While the other materials being gathered will create the visual representation necessary to fool our quarry, the flavoring of our lure will require a special blend of herbs and spices.

'Bring me the following and I'll put them aside with the rest of the materials:

'Ten phials of mint sauce.
'Ten batches of mashed royal taters.''Well done indeed, ${PLAYER}! your contribution is greatly appreciated. Be sure to speak with me again if you have more ingredients to add to the mixture.'Hasta is asking that anyone willing to help him should gather the various ingredients necessary to draw forth the menace from beneath the Water-works.Boiled extraordinary leathers can be processed by the foresters of Middle-earth.

Hasta would like you to bring him twenty boiled extraordinary leathers.'I am very glad to have your assistance in this matter, ${PLAYER}.

'Part of our bait will require a fair number of hides to act as the skin of our fake "fish."  Bring me twenty boiled extraordinary leathers and I'll add them to our collection.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! Your contribution is greatly appreciated.

'Be sure to speak with me again if you have more ingredients to add to the pile.'Hasta is asking that anyone willing to help him should gather the various ingredients necessary to draw forth the menace from beneath the Water-works.Khazâd-steel ingots can be crafted by Prospectors throughout Middle-earth.

Hasta would like you to bring him five Khazâd-steel ingots.'I am very glad to have your assistance in this matter, ${PLAYER}.

'Part of our bait will require a strong metal that can be fashioned into hooks and cable.  Bring me ten Khazâd-steel ingots, and I'll add them to our collection.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! Your contribution is greatly appreciated.

'Be sure to speak with me again if you have more ingredients to add to the pile.'Hasta is asking that anyone willing to help him should gather the various ingredients necessary to draw forth the menace from beneath the Water-works.Pure fire oil can be mixed by Scholars throughout Middle-earth.

Hasta would like you to bring him twenty containers of fire oil.'I am very glad to have your assistance in this matter, ${PLAYER}.

'While luring our prey into the open is one of my goals, the other is naturally to subdue the beast. The purpose of a lure such as this is to be devoured, so I would like to add a poison to our bait.

'Scholars are able to produce a volotile mixture that hunters favour -- pure fire oil. Bring me twenty containers of the flammable oil, and I'll add the materials to our collection.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! Your contribution is greatly appreciated.

'Be sure to speak with me again if you have more ingredients to add to the pile.'Drive evil from Fil GashanComplete Heart of the EnemyComplete Strength of the EnemyComplete Eyes of the EnemyComplete Arms of the EnemyDrive evil from the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Complete Overseers of the ForgeComplete Implements of the ForgeComplete Orcs of the ForgeComplete Slaves to the ForgeComplete Blinded by FireThe Orcs at Drû-garmadh have begun building siege-engines and catapults with which to wage war upon the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm and the Elves of the Golden Wood.Moria siege-engines and Moria catapults can be found in Drû-garmadh, south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Alrekur fears the siege-weaponry being built in Drû-garmadh and wants you to destroy several siege-engines and catapults.Destroy Moria siege-engines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Moria catapults (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Alrekur is in Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh.

Alrekur will be pleased to hear the Moria siege-engines and Moria catapults being built in Drû-garmadh have been destroyed.Talk to Alrekur in Mekhem-bizru'The siege-weaponry you saw in Drû-garmadh disturbs me greatly. I do not believe the Orcs could effectively use it in Khazad-dûm, but with it, they could dominate the Dimrill Dale and possibly threaten the outskirts of Lothlórien, although there seems to be some power within the Wood which defies them.

'Venture back to Drû-garmadh, south-east of here, and destroy the Moria siege-engines and Moria catapults. It is vital to our ability to hold the Dimrill Dale as a strategic location.''So, the large weapons of war have been smashed into tiny pieces. This is good news, ${PLAYER}, but until the builder responsible for them is defeated, there will only be more to destroy tomorrow.''Those siege-engines must be destroyed, for the safety of all!'The Elf-lady Maliriel has long organized the great banquets of Lothlórien, held for honoured guests and special occasions. The strains of unrest and war have distracted many from the preparations needed, and she has asked you to aid the Elves responsible for completing the preparations for an upcoming banquet.Galhíril can be found near the gate to Imlad Lalaith. Aesbrennil and Hadhelen can be found within the Vineyards of Lórien, south of Imlad Lalaith. Glasnír can be found at the entrance to the vineyards, south of Imlad Lalaith.

Maliriel has asked you to help her and her companions to complete all the preparations for the upcoming feast.Maliriel is at Imlad Lalaith.

You should report to Maliriel that all the banquet preparations she asked you to finish are complete.Talk to Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. You come at an auspicious time -- but one that finds me ill prepared for my duties. You see, I am the Mistress of the Feast for Lothlórien, and it falls to me to prepare a great banquet.

'Yet I find myself with few hands to prepare such an event, for many have been called away to guard the borders of our forest or to sojourn further afield against the foes of the Elves.

'So I ask you, if you will, to seek out my companions who labour here and to the south towards the vineyards, and offer them whatever aid you may in these preparations, for time grows short!''We have many preparations for the feast... speak with my assistants and aid them as you may.''${PLAYER}, I am delighted! You have made all the preparations seem so much less arduous and allowed me to more fully devote my time and attention to the complicated ones. 

'Please accept this reward, and know that it comes with Maliriel's warmest regards.'Defeat Wargs in the Grand Stair.Defeat Wargs in the Grand StairDefeat Wargs in the Grand Stair.Defeat Wargs in the Grand StairYou sang to Malbrethil-saplings in an effort to improve their health. Now Sendiel wishes to increase their numbers.Shrews can be found in Taur Hith, particularly in the area around Cerin Brethil, north and slightly east from the Peaceful Glade.

Sendiel has asked you to recover seeds from the shrews.Recover Malbrethil-seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sendiel is in the Peaceful Glade, south and slightly west of Cerin Brethil.

You should return to Sendiel with the seeds.Talk to Sendiel at the Peaceful Glade'You have been of great aid, ${PLAYER}. Thanks to you, not only do we know what was weakening our beloved Melbrethil, but I can send word to Mallendathor to recruit other visitors to help repair the damage that their presence in Lothlórien is causing.

'It is clear that we have been remiss in our vigilant care of the Melbrethil. I have one more task for you: Head into Taur Hith, in particular the area around Cerin Brethil.

'I suspect that the reason we have seen fewer Melbrethil is that the shrews in the area have been dining on their seeds. Please recover some of the seeds and return them here... the animals collect them in considerable numbers to store away for the colder seasons.''You have returned! Let us see...yes, wonderful. These seeds should have survived their little detour through the shrews. I do not forsee any difficulty planting them.

'Hopefully, we shall soon see more Malbrethil-saplings, if all goes well.''Have you found the seeds I asked for? Please bring them as quickly as you may!'Defeat trolls within the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Defeat trolls within the Forges of Khazad-dûmDefeat trolls within the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Defeat trolls within the Forges of Khazad-dûmYou have helped the dwarves to stave off the first attacks of the Orcs, but Bósi does not think his people can stand against these foes forever without the friendship of the Elves of Lothlórien.There are wardens on the bounds of Lothlórien, east of Moria. Such Elves may be found on great platforms, or flets, among the trees to the south-east of the river Nimrodel.

Bósi believes the dwarves cannot turn Mazog's Orcs aside for long if they are truly supported by some force out of Dol Guldur, and wants you to seek an audience with Galadriel of Lórien. The dwarves need allies if they are to stand in Khazad-dûm.Talk to Haldir upon a flet south-east of the river Nimrodel'We have withstood the initial attacks of the Orcs, but for how long will our good luck last? Not long enough, I fear; the Orcs are simply too numerous, and with the support of Dol Guldur, Mazog can surely wage his war long enough to overturn our defences.

'We must seek help of our own. Though the friendship of the dwarves with the Elves of the Golden Wood has suffered strain over the long years, it has never, I hope, been truly abandoned. We need their assistance now more than ever, or we are lost.

'You must seek the aid of the Lady Galadriel. We dwarves know little of her, but it is said she wields some great power. Some say she is fell and perilous, others that she is kind. In this dire time I would risk an audience with her, though I am afraid. Speak with one of the wardens at the bounds of Lothlórien and ask to speak with the Lady of the Wood, ${PLAYER}. Who better than you? You are an Elf-friend and a dwarf-friend both. I understand that there may be great platforms among the trees across the river called Nimrodel, south-east of the Dimrill Dale. You may find wardens of Lothlórien upon them.''We defeated the Orcs this time, but they are too numerous. Without the aid of the Elves of Lórien, we will be overrun.

'I hope that the Lady Galadriel will help us. Look for wardens of Lothlórien upon the platforms in the trees south-east of the river Nimrodel.''A singular request! You are bold, stranger, to seek an audience with the Lady Galadriel. I, Haldir of Lórien, cannot permit you to enter this land.'You have been acknowledged a friend of Lothlórien through your efforts on behalf of the Elves, and should travel to the Hill of Cerin Amroth to affirm that friendship.Milwen is by the archway west of the hill of Cerin Amroth, located in the centre of Lothlórien, far to the north-east of Talan Haldir and east of Echad Andestel.

You have been told to speak with Milwen on the hill of Cerin Amroth, within the woods of Lórien.Talk to Milwen'Have you yet visited the hill of Cerin Amroth, ${PLAYER}? You should do so, for it is lovely at all times of the year.

'Look for it in the centre of Lothlórien; it is both beautiful and peaceful, and Milwen will be pleased to tell you some of its history. Look for her by the archway west of the hill of Cerin Amroth.'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you have not already completed Volume II, Book 6, it is encouraged, though not required, that you do so before beginning this quest.</rgb>'You are welcome within Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}, for the friendship you have demonstrated and your efforts against the Orcs and other dangers within Moria.

'Pass beneath the eaves of the forest, to the east, and travel to the hill of Cerin Amroth in the centre of Lothlórien; it is both beautiful and peaceful, and Milwen will be pleased to tell you some of its history. Look for her by the archway west of the hill of Cerin Amroth.'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you have not already completed Volume II, Book 6, it is encouraged, though not required, that you do so before beginning this quest.</rgb>'You are welcome within Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}, for the friendship you have demonstrated and your efforts against the Orcs and other dangers within Moria.

'Pass beneath the eaves of the forest, to the north-east, and travel to the hill of Cerin Amroth in the centre of Lothlórien; it is both beautiful and peaceful, and Milwen will be pleased to tell you some of its history. Look for her by the archway west of the hill of Cerin Amroth, far to the northeast of here inside the forest.'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you have not already completed Volume II, Book 6, it is encouraged, though not required, that you do so before beginning this quest.</rgb>'As a friend to the Elves of Lórien, you should visit the hill of Cerin Amroth at least once. It is a place of such beauty that rest and contemplation come easily.

'Speak to Milwen by the archway west of the hill and she will tell you some of its history. Cerin Amroth is in the centre of Lórien, and north of Caras Galadhon.''As a friend to the Elves of Lórien, you should visit the hill of Cerin Amroth at least once. It is a place of such beauty that rest and contemplation come easily.

'Speak to Milwen by the archway west of the hill and she will tell you some of its history. Cerin Amroth is in the centre of Lórien, far to the east of here, but north of Caras Galadhon.''As a friend to the Elves of Lórien, you should visit the hill of Cerin Amroth at least once. It is a place of such beauty that rest and contemplation come easily.

'Speak to Milwen by the archway west of the hill and she will tell you some of its history. Cerin Amroth is in the centre of Lórien, far to the north-east of this talan.''Welcome to Cerin Amroth, ${PLAYER}! Few only have had the joy of seeing it in these fading times, its beauty a remnant only of the majesty it once held. For on this mound Amroth Lord of Lórien built his house, in the days before his love was lost and he himself vanished from Middle-earth.

'It is said that when the South Wind blows upon the hill, if you listen for the sound of the gulls, you might hear still Amroth calling, calling for his lost love Nimrodel. But she never came back.'

Milwen pauses a moment, but with a light laugh she recovers herself.

'Do not look sad, ${PLAYER}! Cerin Amroth should be a reminder of happier days. Walk upon the grass and be joyful! Your sorrows will not follow you here.'While Celeborn prepares the Golden Host to move on Mirkwood in a desperate gambit to forestall an attack from Dol Guldur, there are still some matters to be resolved.Issuriel of Lothlórien can be found on the high flet atop Cerin Amroth.

Haldir has told you of the preparations being made for the departure of the Golden Host into Mirkwood and desired that you speak with Issuriel, an Elf being considered to lead the Malledhrim. She had questions to ask of you concerning the capture of Mazog.Talk to Issuriel at Cerin AmrothIssuriel is on the high flet atop Cerin Amroth, in Lothlórien.

Issuriel wishes to hear the account of your escape from Rushdurinul with the captive Mazog, as the other Elves present were reluctant to tell her the rest of the story.Talk to Issuriel and recount the story of your escape from RushdurinulIssuriel is on the high flet atop Cerin Amroth, in Lothlórien.

You have recounted the rest of the tale concerning your escape from Rushdurinul with Mazog, and Issuriel has heard something to cause her concern.Talk to Issuriel at Cerin Amroth'Lord Celeborn is making preparations for a great incursion into Mirkwood, not for conquest, but to forestall the attack from Dol Guldur that must surely come. We are gathering supplies and making all things ready for the passage of the Malledhrim, the Golden Host, and the Lord and Lady are carefully selecting those who will lead it.

'One of those I think likely to travel with the Golden Host is named Issuriel; she is a student of history and of the mysteries of the natural world and spoke often with Mithrandir on the rare occasion his business brought him to the Golden Wood. She seeks to know the true nature of things and loves the unravelling of puzzles and secrets above all else.

'Issuriel has been asking for you, ${PLAYER}. She wished to hear the tale of Mazog's capture in the depths of Moria from your lips and had questions to ask of you. Look for her on the high flet atop Cerin Amroth.''It is a pleasure to meet you at last, ${PLAYER}, and I hope you will assist the Golden Host when the time comes to push forward into Mirkwood. Lord Celeborn has asked me to be involved in planning for the offensive, so in order to fully understand the mind of the captive Mazog, I listened to Corunothiel's account of his capture.

'With interest, I learned of your infiltration through the secret way into the throne-room of Mazog, but Corunothiel ceased her tale at the point where the Orc-leader was captured. I pressed her for more information, but she said the memory was grim, and she did not desire to relive it so soon.

'Tell me what happened following the capture of Mazog, ${PLAYER}. How were you able to escape from the very heart of Mazog's throne room...and with the king of the Orcs still in tow?''The tale of your escape from Rushdurinul with Mazog still a captive was more harrowing than I expected, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for recounting it to me! If we are to work with the dwarves to bring Mazog to Dol Guldur, as Bróin intends, we must learn from the lesson of your tale: the Orc-king is not to be underestimated!

'I trust that Bróin's people are crafting new shackles for Mazog, to begin with the most obvious lesson of your escape.

'But there is more, friend ${RACE}! The words of Mazog make me wonder. Look first to your own doorstep before taking the fight to that of your enemy, it is said by the Wise!''I am ready to hear the rest of the story, ${PLAYER}. I want to know how you were able to escape from Rushdurinul, the very seat of Mazog's power, with the Orc-king still a captive. It could not have been easy!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Issuriel wishes to speak with you concerning the capture of Mazog, ${PLAYER}. Look for her on the high flet atop Cerin Amroth.'The Necromancer's Gate guards the inner courtyards of the fortress of Dol Guldur.The Necromancer's Gate guards the inner courtyards of the fortress of Dol Guldur.Defeat LavalúgDefeat GortagDefeat FiringúlDefeat MurúkDefeat AnnonielDefeat ThrângundDefeat MorgúrDefeat AgardúrDefeat GrishglokDefeat Trolls in the Grand Stair.Defeat Trolls in the Grand StairDefeat Trolls in the Grand Stair.Defeat Trolls in the Grand StairThe Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Bolg Maufulug lies west and a little north from Talan Fanuidhol.

Maenhador has asked you to burn the Orc-banner at Bolg Maufulug and defeat the camp's champion.Burn the banner at Bolg Maufulug and defeat StargûshMaenhador is at Talan Fanuidhol, east and a little south of Bolg Maufulug.

You should return to Maenhador with the tidings of your victory at Bolg Maufulug.Talk to Maenhador at Talan Fanuidhol'Ho there, ${PLAYER}. I have a challenge for you. You have journeyed into Fanuidhol and know what dangers we face in the Orcs of Moria. If we strike fear into their hearts, that threat may be lessened.

'What I would have you do is enter the camp of Bolg Maufulug and burn the standard of the Orcs there. With their banner in ashes, they will know that we are strong enough to defy them.

'Bolg Maufulug lies to the west and a little north of here. Be wary, though, for I do not doubt the camp is championed by a powerful Orc or other creature...if the champion arrives, defeat him as well. When you have done this deed, return to me.''You have burned the banner at Bolg Maufulug and defeated their champion? Well done, ${PLAYER}!''Head a little north and some distance west to Bolg Maufulug and deal with the enemy there.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Drûmaudhul lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith.

Raingon has asked you to burn the Orc-banner at Drûmaudhul and defeat the camp's champion.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>Burn banner at Drûmaudhul and defeat RukalaiRaingon is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Drûmaudhul.

You should return to Raingon with the tidings of your victory at Drûmaudhul.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>Talk to Raingon at Talan Gwilith'${PLAYER}, it is grim to see the banners of the Orcs flying in Fanuidhol. They have come too close to our borders and must be taught that these lands belong to the Galadhrim.

'Enter the lumber-camp at Drûmaudhul and burn the Orc-banner which flies there. That should show them that we do not fear them. And should the champion of Drûmaudhul arrive, deal with him as well.

'Drûmaudhul lies to the north-west of here. When you have done this deed, return to me.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>'You have burned the Orc-banner at Drûmaudhul and defeated their champion? You have done well, indeed, ${PLAYER}!''Head to the north-west of here to Drûmaudhul and deal with the enemy there.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Mokûrz Gundul lies to the north from Talan Fanuidhol.

Maenhador has asked you to burn the Orc-banner at Mokûrz Gundul and defeat the camp's champion.Burn banner at Mokûrz Gundul and defeat NákurzMaenhador is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Mokûrz Gundul.

You should return to Maenhador with the tidings of your victory at Mokûrz Gundul.Talk to Maenhador at Talan Fanuidhol'The Orcs at Mokûrz Gundul must be shown that we are stronger than they. To accomplish this, I would have you enter the encampment and burn their banner down before them.

'This act will no doubt attract the attention of the champion of Mokûrz Gundul...if so, you should dispose of the creature with due haste.

'Mokûrz Gundul lies to the north of here. When you have done this deed, return to me.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. To bring down such a terrible foe is worthy of great praise.''Head north to Mokûrz Gundul and deal with the enemy there.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Nardur-stazg lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith.

Raingon has asked you to burn the Orc-banner at Nardur-stazg and defeat the camp's champion.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>Burn banner at Nardur-stazg and defeat NarashRaingon is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Nardur-stazg.

You should return to Raingon with the tidings of your victory at Nardur-stazg.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>Talk to Raingon at Talan Gwilith'There are many foul Orcs at Nardur-stazg, and many of their most powerful champions. This encampment serves as the chief stronghold of Mazog's Orcs in Fanuidhol, and it would strike a blow to their collective spirit if it were put to shame.

'I would have you enter Nardur-stazg and burn their banner. To have their standard put to the torch will enrage them, but it will also cause them some pause. You may perhaps encounter the champion of Nardur-stazg...if so, defeat him as well.

'Nardur-stazg lies well to the north-west of here. Return to me when the deed is done.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>'You have laid low the champion of Nardur-stazg and brought shame to the Orcs of Moria? I am well-pleased, ${PLAYER}.''Head north-west to Nardur-stazg and deal with the enemy there.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>Maliriel has asked you to help her companions complete preparations for the upcoming banquet.Mushrooms can be found along the bank of the stream that borders Imlad Lalaith. Berries can be found in the forest north of Imlad Lalaith.

Aesbrennil would like you to gather berries and button-like mushrooms for the meal she is preparing for the evening festivities.Collect berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect button mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aesbrennil is at the Vineyards of Lórien, south of Imlad Lalaith.

You should bring the mushrooms and berries back to Aesbrennil.'I see that our fair Mistress of the Feast has recruited you to aid us in our preparations. I truly appreciate your willingness to help, ${PLAYER}.

'Let us see what is on my list... pie fillings! I will need mushrooms for the savoury pies and berries for the sweet ones. The mushrooms I need can be found along the banks of the stream that runs by Imlad Lalaith; it is a variety of mushroom we call "button", because of their round caps.

'The berries I need commonly grow in the forest a short way north of Imlad Lalaith. They should be simple enough to find.''I simply must have more mushrooms and berries for the feast!''You have returned with the ingredients I need... and with little time to spare. I have much to do before the feast.'Defeat insects in the Sixteenth HallDefeat insects in the Sixteenth HallDefeat insects in the Sixteenth HallDefeat insects in the Sixteenth HallIn the Water-works, ancient Caeryg rumble through the halls. Their presence is causing the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm great concern. They often fight in packs and are quite dangerous to those who attempt to disturb them.Deep in the Water-works, there are great Caeryg lurking. You should find them in the hidden rooms of the Water-works and banish them from Moria.Defeat the Caeryg in the southern roomDefeat the Caeryg in the western roomIn the farthest depths of the Water-works, there is the greatest of Caeryg, Caerlug. Defeat him to claim your reward.Defeat CaerlûgHigh up in Zirakzigil, there lies a cave. This cave was a means to harness the light of the sun and bring it down to the depths of Moria. Years of neglect have brought this system to its knees, and now the cave is home to merrevail, Wargs, and other dark creatures.You should defeat the morroval-queen, Ergoth while she is at her strongest. If you weaken her first, you will not be able to claim the greatest of rewards.Defeat ErgothFil Gashan is the barracks and training grounds of the Orcs in Moria. Within those walls, a fearsome general has been readying his troops for an assault upon the Elves of Lothlórien to the east of Khazad-dûm. Brogur and Bósi's dwarves, wishing to reclaim Moria, intend to prevent this at any cost, for they would see the Elves and dwarves reinstate old alliances for the good of both.Fil Gashan is far to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall, and General Talug can be found in the depths of that place.

Sigurd has challenged you to use stealth and wit to conquer General Talug, the leader of a great Orc-host, without defeating too many of his sentries.Defeat General TalugIn the Dark Delvings, the most forsaken depths of Khazad-dûm, the Nameless hold sway over the bitter shadows. Like other creatures that hide in the Black Pit that is Moria, the Nameless dread light, but they will not turn aside from any opportunity to spread corruption and dismay.The region of the Dark Delvings is far to the south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.

The dwarf Sigurd has challenged you to make your way into the Dark Delvings and defeat the Gurvand without the help of runes, wishing you to prove your worth as the great warrior you are rumoured to be.Defeat the GurvandDo not use any of the rune-stonesNo living Man, Elf, hobbit, or dwarf will want to set foot in Skûmfil, grave of the Orcs, feeding and breeding ground of vile kergrim and slavering gredbyg. There, the Orcs pile their dead, and there, disgusting creatures feast on rotten waste.Hwandrin and her brood ever belch unwholesome filth upon the corpse-ridden halls of Skûmfil, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.

Sigurd has challenged you to defeat Hwandrin in Skûmfil as proof of your worth as a warrior. Her threat is great, yet few are wilful enough to withstand the menace of such an old and malevolent being.Defeat HwandrinOnce a great and beautiful cross-roads of Moria, the Grand Stair is a vile haven of many of the gathered tribes of Orcs. Igash, regarded as a leader by all of the varied groups, gathers tribute from every tribe to give to Mazog, the mightiest and greatest of Orcs in Khazad-dûm. The dwarves wish to unseat Igash's Orcs from this Grand Stair and stop Mazog from receiving valuable and unsavoury gifts.Many tribes of Orcs prowl the Grand Stair, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.

Geirr has asked you to defeat Igash in the Grand Stair without defeating any other members of the Moria Orc-tribes. In doing so, you will assist in efforts to reclaim that cross-roads for the dwarves and prove your great worth to Sigurd.Defeat IgashThe Forges of Khazad-dûm, once a glorious smith-hall for the Dwarves of Moria, have fallen into evil hands. The Forges now serve the Orc-masters of Moria and are used to build all manner of weapons and war-machines for an assault against fair Lothlórien. Brogur and Bósi's dwarves, wishing to reclaim Moria, intend to prevent this at any cost, for they would see the Elves and dwarves reinstate old alliances for the good of both peoples.The Forges of Khazad-dûm are to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall.

The dwarf Sigurd has challenged you to fight your way to the Orc Kranklûk. Narkû, who stands between you and your intended quarry, will undoubtedly alert Kranklûk that you are coming. You will have a limited amount of time in which to accomplish your task after the warning goes out.Defeat Narkû to alert Kranklûk of your presenceKranklûk is in the heart of the Forges of Khazad-Dûm.

Narkû has been defeated, and Kranklûk is alerted to your presence. Sigurd believes that Kranklûk is the driving force in the Forges of Khazad-dûm; he wants you to defeat your foe to hinder the efforts of the Orcs.Defeat Kranklûk before the time runs outOnce filled with the thunder of dwarf-hammers and smiths, the Halls of Crafting are now dominated by foul Orcs. Led by the evil Black Uruk, Thaguzg, they are building weapons for a massive assault upon Lothlórien itself.You should defeat Thaguzg without his minions' assistance. They must not reach him, or great woe will befall your fellowship.Defeat ThaguzgIn the Sixteenth Hall, defilers and other Orcs, sworn to some dark power, poison their brethren with a fungal disease. The source of this evil lies far beneath the surface of this stronghold, once inhabited by the dwarves. The Dwarves in Moria wish only to drive the Orcs and the evil of the Sixteenth Hall away from their former realm.The Lost One is below the Sixteenth Hall, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.

You have been challenged to prove your great worth by defeating the Lost One without making the battle easier by killing his summoned gredbyg.Defeat the Lost OneHaldir of Lórien has refused to grant you an audience with Galadriel unless you can provide proofs that you are an enemy of the Orcs of Moria.Haldir is at his camp on the boundary of Lothlórien.

Haldir has asked you to provide proofs that you are a foe of the Orcs and goblins of Moria by completing two deeds: slaying many Orcs and goblins in Moria.Complete the 'Goblin-slayer' deed in MoriaComplete the 'Orc-slayer' deed in MoriaHaldir is at his camp on the boundary of Lothlórien.

You have completed two great deeds within Moria, and it could be that the tally of your victories over the Orcs and goblins of Moria will be enough to satisfy Haldir of your intentions.'The Orcs of Moria are awake. Once they were content to burrow in the deep roots of Fanuidhol the Grey, Celebdil the White, and Caradhras the Cruel; now they pour from the doors of the Black Pit to threaten these woods.

'You say you have fought the Orcs and goblins of Moria -- if you are truly their foe, then show me! How many have you slain in the dark tunnels of Moria? Will I be satisfied that you are the friend you say, and not a spy in league with those forces who wish us ill?

'I will judge your tally, but I promise you nothing.''If you are truly the enemy of my enemies, you can prove your vow by slaying Orcs and goblins within Moria. Complete these two deeds and perhaps the tally of your foes will be sufficient to satisfy my skepticism.''The record of your victories affirms your claim, ${PLAYER}. I am sorry I doubted you, but these are dangerous times. We have had many strange visitors at the boundaries of Lothlórien before you.'Milwen has told you of a number of visitors to Lórien who will be interested in speaking with you.Frodo Baggins is on the crest of the hill of Cerin Amroth with some of the members of his company.

Milwen has asked you to speak with Frodo Baggins, one of the eight visitors that has come to Lórien in recent days. The Elf-maiden is certain that news of Eriador will be of interest to him.Samwise Gamgee is standing on the crest of the hill of Cerin Amroth next to Frodo.

Frodo has asked that you fill him and Sam in on news of Eriador.Meriadoc Brandybuck is taking a walk somewhere in the vicinity of the hill of Cerin Amroth, and he may now be resting in a private garden nearby.

Frodo and Sam were delighted to see you in Lothlórien and know that Merry will be as well.Boromir is wandering somewhere on the north-west outskirts of the clearing from which Cerin Amroth rises, in the centre of Lórien.

Merry has wondered if a conversation with you might cheer up Boromir, who does not seem content with the company's presence in Lothlórien.Gimli is on the flet atop the crest of Cerin Amroth, in the centre of Lothlórien.

Boromir, a little annoyed at Gimli's growing trust of the Elves, has asked you to speak with the dwarf.'Before you go, ${PLAYER}, you should know that you are not the only visitor that has come to Lórien in recent days. In fact, I understand that you are known to these guests, and they will be pleased to see you.

'The hobbit Frodo Baggins is resting with some members of his company on the crest of the hill. I do not know what errand has brought them to the Golden Wood, or if you have been entrusted with knowledge of it, but I am sure he will be pleased to see you.''The hobbit Frodo Baggins rests with some of the members of his company at the top of Cerin Amroth. I know he will be pleased to speak with you, and to hear news of Eriador.''${PLAYER}! When Milwen told me another traveller from over the mountains had come to Lothlórien, I had no idea it would be you! We have come such a long way, haven't we? There is still a long way to go, but here in Lothlórien I have found it difficult to worry too much about the road ahead.

'You have to tell Sam and me what has happened since we parted, my friend! It feels like a lifetime has passed since leaving Rivendell, and several at least since last I saw Bag End!

'But Sam does not seem as surprised to see you as I am, ${PLAYER}. You haven't become the chief conspirator of another conspiracy, have you, Sam?''I can still hardly believe you're really here, ${PLAYER}! Unless I'm far off, it seems to me that Sam does not seem nearly as surprised. You haven't become the chief conspirator of another conspiracy, have you, Sam?''Hullo there, ${PLAYER}! Me, a conspirator? It's not like that at all, Mr. Frodo, and you know I'm not cut out for the keeping of secrets, despite your teasing.

'It's just that so many queer things have happened to us already, and this place being so Elvish and all, I'd just about given up being surprised when something out of the ordinary happens. And here comes ${PLAYER} out of the woods, right enough!

'You should find Mr. Merry somewhere around this hill, ${PLAYER}; I know he'll be pleased as anything to see you! He's taking one of his walks, and might be resting in a private garden nearby.''Mr. Merry is taking a walk somewhere around Cerin Amroth. I know he will be happy to see you, and to hear your news. He was planning to rest in one of the private gardens nearby.''Well hello there, ${PLAYER}! I have to admit I did not think to run into you here in Lórien! You're on the wrong side of the mountains, aren't you? Aren't we all!'

Merry's face lights up as he laughs long and loudly.

'Pippin is around here somewhere, taking a nap, I believe. No, I wouldn't wake him -- we'll all have plenty of time to catch up, I imagine. Lothlórien is so peaceful, it's hard to remember how hard our road will be, and has been!

'I wonder if you might track down Boromir; he doesn't seem to be having as good a time here as the rest of us. I think he's impatient to get going again, but maybe seeing you again will cheer him up. I last saw him on the north-west outskirts of the great clearing from which Cerin Amroth rises.''Boromir does not seem content with our stay in Lothlórien. I wonder if he will be cheered by seeing you, ${PLAYER}?

'I saw him last on the north-western edge of the clearing from which rises Cerin Amroth. Find him and see if you can lighten his mood!''${PLAYER}? It is most strange to see you here, as the last time I saw you was the night Elrond of Rivendell entrusted you with the continued defences of Eriador. Is that land so safe already?'

Boromir sighs and squares his shoulders again.

'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}; my words were borne of frustration, not of dislike. Every hour we spend in idleness here is an hour during which the shadow draws closer to my city.

'I have seen little of Aragorn, and even less of Gimli -- the dwarf seems to have gotten over his distrust of Elves easily enough! Even now he is off with Legolas, atop one of the trees at the crest of the hill of Cerin Amroth. Speak to him and see for yourself.''Gimli is in the trees above the crest of the hill of Cerin Amroth. Speak to him, and see if he is ready yet to leave these woods. I would not have expected a dwarf to trust these Elves so readily, but he has done so.''By Durin's beard! I did not expect to see you again so soon, ${PLAYER}. I am glad to be surprised!

'Legolas has been showing me the woods of Lothlórien, and the majesty of these trees, so like to stone-carved pillars beneath the mountains, fills this dwarf with amazement. But even in a land of marvels, its Lady is the greatest one of all!

'Still, I am ready to return now to the ground. If you ask me, the trees are best admired from below, rather than up among their branches!'Issuriel worries that the words of Mazog may reveal a hidden threat to the Elves of Lothlórien and the Dwarves of Moria.Lenglammel and Forglinn can be found in Gwathrendath, the Elf-outpost in the depths of the Foundations of Stone, in Moria.

Issuriel believes that Gorothúl may have set into motion some evil that might ravage Moria in such a way that even Mazog is seeking another kingdom to rule.Talk to Lenglammel at GwathrendathTalk to Forglinn at GwathrendathBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located off Durin's Way.

The Elves in Gwathrendath agree with Issuriel's assessment that Gorothúl set some evil into motion before leaving for Dol Guldur. Bróin should be notified of this, for it concerns the Iron Garrison and may affect his plans for the rescue of Bori.Talk to Bróin in the Peaceful Path'Much of Mazog's ramblings in the depths of Rushdurinul could have been empty bluster, the boasting and threats of a caged animal. But one thing he said troubles me more than any other: the revelation that the reward he seeks is the rule of another kingdom. Long have the Orcs and the dwarves battled in the caverns beneath the Misty Mountains, and the lineage of Mazog has been at the forefront of that conflict.

'If Mazog, descendent of Azog's line through his son Bolg, has decided to abandon rule of Moria, it can only be because he feels Moria will no longer be fit to rule. What great evil must his ally Gorothúl have set into motion in the depths that could so devastate that vast kingdom and make it unfit even for the rule of Orcs?

'Return to Gwathrendath in the Foundations of Stone and speak with Lenglammel and Forglinn there. They have spent a great deal of time in the depths and may know something about what we might be facing.''The Elf-outpost in the depths of the Foundations of Stone in Moria may hold some answers concerning the danger I fear Gorothúl has raised. Speak with Lenglammel and Forglinn there and hear what they have learned.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}, for I share the concerns of Issuriel: there is more to Gorothúl's interest in Moria than we have so far uncovered.

'Great terrors dwell in the deep places, this we know, for you have faced several of them: nameless beasts that fear the light of the sun, but also the servants of the great spirit that reigned in Moria and ended the dwarf-kingdom. The Balrog of Moria now is defeated, but at the cost of Mithrandir's life and the vast extent of his power.

'But the servants of the Shadow and the Flame were defeated not by the power of Mithrandir, but by your courage and that of your allies. Take no offence at this, ${PLAYER}, but your abilities do not begin to approach that of the Wizard. I fear that your defeat of the servants of Durin's Bane may not have the permanence afforded that of their master's defeat.''Your words confirm what I have been hearing from Lenglammel and Magor, ${PLAYER}: Gorothúl set something in motion before he left for Dol Guldur with the captive dwarves and the mithril axe of the Iron Garrison.

'Did he work some evil to allow the servants of Shadow and Flame to recover their strength and return to places once thought free of their danger?''You go to speak with Bróin about this new danger? I am glad; he must deal with the possibility that all is not well within Moria before setting forth to rescue his cousin Bori.

'Bróin is in the Peaceful Path, located along Durin's Way.''Bróin remains still in the Peaceful Path, the place of rest established by the Iron Garrison off Durin's Way. You should speak to him about this new danger we suspect is growing, for it will affect his planned rescue of Bori.''I had hoped to see you again on the shores of Anduin, ${PLAYER}, well on our way to exchanging the Orc-king for my cousin Bori's freedom, but it was not yet to be. The Elves of Gwathrendath are right: Gorothúl seems to have set some plan into motion here in Khazad-dûm.

'After you returned to Lothlórien to speak with Celeborn, Orvar went back into the depths of Buzun-ghâr. He said he had a "feeling," some idea that things were not quite right. The wilting rot was already beginning to retreat, but he felt still some vile presence, and below the ledge where you handily defeated Grawulun the Caerog, Orvar discovered a dreadful ward covered in unspeakable runes. He sensed it calling, calling into the depths, and smote it with his axe until it was destroyed.

'I believe Gorothúl left this relic in Buzun-ghâr in order to draw Grawulun the Caerog to it, ${PLAYER}. Grawulun did not find that place accidentally, friend ${CLASS}. He was drawn there.'Bróin believes that Gorothúl gave a relic of evil to the merrevail that infest the Mirrors of Lumul-nar.The entrance to the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar is outside, on Zirakzigil, near the ruined crater where the Balrog lies smouldering.

Bróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.Destroy the Gift of Gorothúl in Lumul-narBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located between Zirakzigil and Durin's Way.

You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.Talk to Bróin in the Peaceful Path'Now that Orvar has destroyed the hidden relic Gorothúl left in Buzun-ghâr, that cave should be free of danger. We need not fear that Grawulun or others of his kind will return to that place.

'But Gorothúl may have left other relics of evil throughout Moria; indeed, I think it likely, and recent reports from our scouts indicate one such location: the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar. Merrevail have corrupted the mirrors of Lumul-nar that once fed light from the outside into the deep reaches of Khazad-dûm; the light no longer shines. A number of explorers ventured to Lumul-nar to investigate. Few returned, reporting that the merrevail of that place have been given great courage; their defiance is strong. What else have they been given, I wonder? A relic of Gorothúl's?

'The entrance to Lumul-nar is on the side of Zirakzigil, amid the snow. Find the relic inside, if it exists, and destroy it. Bring one or two allies with you, ${PLAYER}! A small fellowship of the brave-hearted will be required to find the evil relic there.''I knew it, ${PLAYER}! I knew you would find Gorothúl's relic in Lumul-nar. It is good you destroyed it. The merrevail we should be able to keep in check; if the relic had drawn Grawulun or another Caerog to Lumul-nar, our success might not be as sure.''The entrance to the Mirror Halls of Lumul-nar is outside, on the side of Zirakzigil near the smoking crater. Bring a small fellowship of allies with you, for the merrevail at Lumul-nar are dangerous foes.'Bróin believes that Gorothúl gave a relic of evil to the merrevail that infest the Mirrors of Lumul-nar.The entrance to the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar is outside, on Zirakzigil, near the ruined crater where the Balrog lies smouldering.

Bróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.Talk to Bróin and travel to Mirror Halls of Lumul-narBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located between Zirakzigil and Durin's Way.

You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.Talk to Bróin in the Peaceful Path'Now that Orvar has destroyed the hidden relic Gorothúl left in Buzun-ghâr, that cave should be free of danger. We need not fear that Grawulun or others of his kind will return to that place.

'But Gorothúl may have left other relics of evil throughout Moria; indeed, I think it likely, and recent reports from our scouts indicate one such location: the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar. Merrevail have corrupted the mirrors of Lumul-nar that once fed light from the outside into the deep reaches of Khazad-dûm; the light no longer shines. A number of explorers ventured to Lumul-nar to investigate. Few returned, reporting that the merrevail of that place have been given great courage; their defiance is strong. What else have they been given, I wonder? A relic of Gorothúl's?

'The entrance to Lumul-nar is on the side of Zirakzigil, amid the snow. Find the relic inside, if it exists, and destroy it. Bring one or two allies with you, ${PLAYER}!''I knew it, ${PLAYER}! I knew you would find Gorothúl's relic in Lumul-nar. It is good you destroyed it. The merrevail we should be able to keep in check; if the relic had drawn Grawulun or another Caerog to Lumul-nar, our success might not be as sure.''I shall have a scout lead you to the  Mirror Halls of Lumul-nar.'Haldir believes you are an enemy of the Orcs and goblins, and wants you to help defend the bounds of the Golden Wood while Galadriel is sent word of your need.Rúmil and Orophin are stationed along the boundaries of Lothlórien. Haldir told you to walk along the north bank of the river Nimrodel to find his brothers.

Haldir has asked you to lend your aid to Rúmil and Orophin. They do not speak much of the Common Tongue, so if you cannot speak to them in Elvish, your mutual hatred of the Orcs must transcend the need for words.Talk to OrophinTalk to RúmilHaldir is at his camp on the boundary of Lothlórien.

You have spoken with his brothers and repelled an attack by the Orcs, and should return now to Haldir.'I have sent word to Lady Galadriel, ${PLAYER}. She will weigh your need and determine what role the Elves will play in these new deeds in Moria.

'In the meantime, I would appreciate your help in patrolling the boundaries of the wood. Speak to my brothers Rúmil and Orophin and offer them your aid; they speak little of the Common Tongue, but hatred of the Orcs will be understood by all enemies of the one Enemy.

'You will find them on the far shores of Nimrodel, to the north. If you walk along the northern banks of the river, you will find my brothers.''Speak to Rúmil and Orophin, along the northern bank of the river Nimrodel, and offer them your aid. Perhaps when you return I will have received word from Lady Galadriel.'Orophin is about to speak when something distracts him suddenly.

'Yrch!' he hisses.Rúmil bows his head to you and points into the distance, away from the eaves of Lórien. He then shrugs, and puts a hand on his bow.

He may not speak the Common Tongue, but his message is clear: for the moment, his post is quiet. The Orc threat is gone, for the time being.'I thank you for helping my brothers, ${PLAYER}, and for safe-guarding the eaves of Lórien.

'The Lady Galadriel has sent word to me concerning your petition and the fate of the dwarves. I will relay to you her message.'Legolas and Gimli have been walking through the woods of Lothlórien, keeping watch for the Orcs that attempt to infiltrate the bounds.Legolas is standing next to Gimli atop the flet above the hill of Cerin Amroth.

You have been invited by Gimli to patrol the woods of Lothlórien with Legolas and himself, and should speak now with the Elf about the excursion.Legolas is standing next to Gimli atop the flet above the hill of Cerin Amroth.

You have been invited by Gimli to patrol the woods of Lothlórien with him and Legolas, and should speak to Legolas when you are ready to go.Talk to Legolas and travel with him through the Golden WoodGimli is on a flet among the trees above the hill of Cerin Amroth, in the centre of Lórien.

Celeborn has agreed to help the Iron Garrison overcome its problems within Moria, and you should speak to Gimli about what has happened.'Legolas and I were just about to take another walk among the trees of Lothlórien in search of patrolling Orcs, ${PLAYER}. Why don't you come with us?

'What do you think, Legolas? Is there room in our party for a third? Surely ${PLAYER} will enjoy seeing the beauty of the wood, and the possibility of hewing an Orc or three will only sweeten the appeal of such a tour!''I wish I could help the Iron Garrison with their efforts in Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. The Mines have brought me great sadness, but I would have them restored, and the Iron Garrison will need able-bodied dwarves if that is to happen.

'But I cannot. My road lies with Frodo, and I will see this errand through before I return to the Mines. The need of the Iron Garrison is great, but Glóin's son does not turn aside from one charge to begin another!'

Gimli's brow furrows, and then his eyes light with wonderment.

'I am struck by the thought, ${PLAYER}, that Bósi's tidings may not have been unknown to the Lady Galadriel. At my first meeting with her, it seemed to me that she offered a choice; a choice between continuing the Quest and leaving it to others. And here arrives just such a point of decision!''I would be delighted if you would join us, ${PLAYER}. The beauty of Lothlórien is best when shared, though we must all remain alert -- even when walking among the trees of Lórien -- for the Orcs of Moria have come down into Nanduhirion and are able to sneak past the borders on occasion.

'Let me know when you are ready to go.''What do you say, Legolas? I am sure ${PLAYER} would like to join us on a tour of the woods.''I will not blame Gimli if he decides to help the Iron Garrison with their difficulties. Lord Elrond laid no bond upon us to accompany Frodo any farther than we would.

'It is Gimli's decision.''Are you ready to go, ${PLAYER}? It will be my pleasure to walk the woods with both you and Gimli, and we will search too for Orcs that may have slipped past the bounds.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>Bósi believes another of Gorothúl's relics may be found at the bottom of Nalâ-dûm, where the great wheels of Khazad-dûm lie dormant.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way.

Bróin has told you to speak with his uncle about the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roadsThe entrance to Nalâ-dûm can be found in the Water-works of Moria.

Bósi reports that a relic of Gorothúl's lies among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm and will require careful usage of the mechanisms to reach and destroy. He also recommends you bring an ally or two.Destroy the relic of Gorothúl in Nalâ-dûmBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way.

You have destroyed the relic left in Nalâ-dûm by Gorothúl and should report your success to Bósi.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads'My uncle Bósi sent word while you were out. He thinks he knows where another of Gorothúl's relics may be found, and the location is just as dangerous as Lumul-nar, if not more so: the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.

'Travel to the Chamber of the Cross-roads with your allies and speak with my uncle to learn more about Nalâ-dûm.''My uncle Bósi thinks he knows where another of Gorothúl's relics may be found: among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.

'Go speak to him in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, off Durin's Way, and he will tell you more about Nalâ-dûm.''Greetings again to you, ${PLAYER}! I did not have the opportunity to properly thank you for helping to broker this alliance between the Iron Garrison and the Elves of Lothlórien. So I thank you! In Mazog, we have a prisoner worthy of exchanging for those Gorothúl brought to Dol Guldur: my son chief among them. O Bori! Be strong and courageous during your torment!

'Scouts report seeing a relic of unquestionable evil among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm, but were unable to route the flow of the canals in such a way as to reach it. You must determine the proper workings of the system if you are to find and destroy this relic of Gorothúl's.

'Bring several allies to the entrance of Nalâ-dûm in the Water-works. Delving into the flooded deeps will be dangerous, for the mechanisms are very old and have not been used for many years.''The entrance to Nalâ-dûm lies in the Water-works. Bring a small fellowship of allies with you in search of Gorothúl's relic.''Very well-done, ${PLAYER}. The destruction of that relic should keep further evils from being drawn to the Water-wheels.

'Now we must look to the future.'Bósi believes another of Gorothúl's relics may be found at the bottom of Nalâ-dûm, where the great wheels of Khazad-dûm lie dormant.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way.

Bróin has told you to speak with his uncle about the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roadsThe entrance to Nalâ-dûm can be found in the Water-works of Moria.

Bósi reports that a relic of Gorothúl's lies among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm and will require careful usage of the mechanisms to reach and destroy.Talk to Bósi and travel to Water-works of Nalâ-dûmBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way.

You have destroyed the relic left in Nalâ-dûm by Gorothúl and should report your success to Bósi.

You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads'My uncle Bósi sent word while you were out. He thinks he knows where another of Gorothúl's relics may be found, and the location is just as dangerous as Lumul-nar, if not more so: the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.

'Travel to the Chamber of the Cross-roads with your allies and speak with my uncle to learn more about Nalâ-dûm.''My uncle Bósi thinks he knows where another of Gorothúl's relics may be found: among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.

'Go speak to him in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, off Durin's Way, and he will tell you more about Nalâ-dûm.''Greetings again to you, ${PLAYER}! I did not have the opportunity to properly thank you for helping to broker this alliance between the Iron Garrison and the Elves of Lothlórien. So I thank you! In Mazog, we have a prisoner worthy of exchanging for those Gorothúl brought to Dol Guldur: my son chief among them. O Bori! Be strong and courageous during your torment!

'Scouts report seeing a relic of unquestionable evil among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm, but were unable to route the flow of the canals in such a way as to reach it. You must determine the proper workings of the system if you are to find and destroy this relic of Gorothúl's.

'I shall have a scout lead you to the entrance of Nalâ-dûm in the Water-works. Delving into the flooded deeps will be dangerous, for the mechanisms are very old and have not been used for many years.''The entrance to Nalâ-dûm lies in the Water-works. I shall send a guide to lead you to the entrance.

'Are you ready to journey forth?''Very well-done, ${PLAYER}. The destruction of that relic should keep further evils from being drawn to the Water-wheels.

'Now we must look to the future.'Celeborn has sent a number of Elves to assist the dwarves in Moria, and you have promised Gimli that you will continue to lend your aid in the Mines as well.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads near Durin's Way, in Moria.

Gimli has asked you to travel back to Moria to speak with Bósi and to tell him that you will help the Iron Garrison with their distressing problems.Orvar Bellhammer is in Buzun-ghâr, the newly-excavated passage off Durin's Way, located in the southern wall of Tharâkh Bazân's south-eastern corner. Tharâkh Bazân is to the north-east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Bósi has asked you to help Orvar, the dwarf working most closely with the Elves sent by Celeborn to Moria.Corunothiel is at the camp inside Buzun-ghâr, located off Durin's Way in the south-eastern corner of Tharâkh Bazân.

Orvar has expressed his frustration with the Elves that have been sent by Celeborn, and wants you to speak with one of them about his irritation.'That is my decision. I will not abandon the Quest with which I have been charged.

'I hope you will give to Bósi and the rest of the Iron Garrison the aid that I would have provided if I were there, ${PLAYER}. When the errand of this company is finished, I hope to return to a reclaimed Moria, and your efforts will help make that possible.

'Bósi said he would return to the Chamber of the Cross-roads near Durin's Way, in Moria. Go now to him, and give him both my regret that I cannot now return and my fervent good wishes for his success.''I wish I could return and help the Iron Garrison with their efforts to reclaim Moria, but I will not abandon Frodo. My road lies with him.

'I will greatly appreciate it if you can lend your aid to the Iron Garrison. Travel to the Chamber of the Cross-roads near Durin's Way, in Moria, and speak to Bósi. Tell him I cannot return, but that you will continue to help with their efforts.''Welcome back to Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. I am disappointed that Gimli did not return with you, but I am sure he had his own reasons. His father Glóin has long been a close friend of my father and Brogur's father, and Gimli surely retains the honour of his forebears.

'This is my first dealing with Celeborn of Lothlórien, and I must confess I am not sure what to make of him. He has sent a number of Elves to help us, and while I appreciate the assistance, they seem perhaps too eager to blame the dwarves for all troubles, both present and past.

'They have established a camp with one of my dwarves, Orvar Bellhammer, in a newly-excavated passage off Durin's Way: Buzun-ghâr. It is located in the very south-eastern corner of Tharâkh Bazân, in the southern wall, right near the exit from those gardens. You will find Tharâkh Bazân to the north-east of this chamber; yes, the tree-filled area on your map there. Journey there and lend Orvar your aid -- he is having... difficulties... getting along with these Elves.''You will find Orvar Bellhammer in Buzun-ghâr, a newly-excavated passage located off Durin's Way, in the very south-eastern corner of Tharâkh Bazân, right near the exit from those gardens. You will find Tharâkh Bazân to the north-east of this chamber. Find Orvar and help him to work with the Elves sent by Celeborn of Lórien.''I am sorry, but I am not the Orvar you seek! You must be looking for Orvar Bellhammer, currently exploring the depths of Buzun-ghâr, the newly-excavated passage off Durin's Way, located in the southern wall of Tharâkh Bazân's south-eastern corner. Tharâkh Bazân is to the north-east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. I am sorry you have come out of your way, ${PLAYER}!''I am glad you're here, ${PLAYER}. These Elves have been sent by Celeborn for the purpose of helping us drive the evil out of Khazad-dûm, so they say, but they seem much more interested in casting blame about than in doing anything helpful!

'This cavern, Buzun-ghâr, was found shortly after you departed, and many of my folk were impressed by the state of it. The gardens still thrive! At least, up here they do; something rots and corrupts the plant-life as you descend.

'But while we could use some real help in clearing the cave of danger, instead these Elves speak often of "digging too deeply" and "disturbing things best left undisturbed." If this is the best Celeborn has to offer, I'd rather he kept them in the woods!

'You talk to Corunothiel, ${PLAYER}, and see if I'm wrong. You'll see I am not!''You speak to Corunothiel and see if I am wrong, ${PLAYER}. You will see that I am not!''Listen to me, ${PLAYER}, for this Orvar will not listen to reason. Some evil lives at the bottom of this cavern, and if this place is not sealed away the evil may spread.

'This is always the way of dwarves! Why must they always dig into places they were not meant to go? Will they not be satisfied until no evil remains beneath the stone, and all have come to the surface to lay waste to the homes of the Elves and other good people?'Galadriel has told you that by helping the Elves in the Shadowed Refuge, you will be helping the dwarves of Moria as well.The Shadowed Refuge is among the Foundations of Stone beneath Nud-melek.

Galadriel sent word to Haldir that if you would save the dwarves in Moria, you must work together with the Elves she sent to the Foundations of Stone to face some great evil.Talk to Lenglammel at the Shadowed Refuge'A short time before you arrived, an even stranger company came to Lórien. Blindfolded, they were brought to Cerin Amroth, for in no way would we endanger the safety of our land. Sad tidings they brought with them, and grief...'

Haldir pauses, and then goes on.

'The Lady Galadriel sent a small party of Elves into Moria following the tidings this company brought with them. She says if you wish to save the dwarves, you will render your aid unto those Elves, for their task in Moria is very important. They have made a small camp in Gwathrendath, the Shadowed Refuge, among the Foundations of Stone.

'The Lady says that an evil greater by far than the Orc presence lies beneath the Foundations of Stone, and must be faced if your dwarves are to be saved.''I would welcome you to the Shadowed Refuge, ${PLAYER}, but it is not a cheerful welcome; none should wish to come to this place. We are here at the behest of the Lady Galadriel.

'Some terror has made its home in these caverns, and it is loathsome and evil.''The Lady Galadriel did not tell me the nature of the evil beneath Nud-melek, just that you must help the Elves at the Shadowed Refuge to defeat it, or the dwarves will be lost.'Dithaliwenn wants to learn for what purpose Mazog has sent his Orcs into the caverns among the Foundations of Stone.Pûlpum ensnared by the corruption of the Globsnaga can be found throughout the Foundations of Stone, but especially on and around the underground lake in its depths.

Dithaliwenn wants to learn to what purpose Mazog has sent so many of his Orcs to the Foundations of Stone, for it seems to be an uncharacteristic move. She wants you to defeat Globsnaga Pûlpum and wrest away any orders they may still carry.Collect Pûlpum Orders from Globsnaga Pûlpum (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dithaliwenn is in the camp of Gwathrendath, the Shadowed Refuge among the Foundations of Stone.

You have collected orders from the corrupted Globsnaga Pûlpum and should bring them to Dithaliwenn in Gwathrendath.'The dwarves that seek to reclaim Moria, as foolish as they are, do not deserve the fate that Mazog's armies have chosen for them. But why has Mazog sent so many of his Orcs here to the Foundations of Stone, when they might otherwise be used to attack the defences of the dwarves?

'There is some foul purpose in it, ${PLAYER}, and I believe Gorothúl, the sorceror from Dol Guldur, will be at the root of it all. Mazog would not do this by himself; what possible reason could he have for splitting his forces?

'Seek out the members of the Pûlpum that Mazog sent to the Foundations of Stone. They may now be Globsnaga, corrupted by the evil of this place, but it could be they still hold the orders that sent them here. Bring these to me if they exist! You will find the Pûlpum especially among the tunnels near the great underground lake, and on the few outcroppings that break its surface.''The Globsnaga Pûlpum may still carry their orders, ${PLAYER}. Wrest them away and bring them to me, if you can. We must learn why Mazog has made this move.

'You will find the Pûlpum especially on and around the great underground lake.''It is difficult to learn much from these orders, but this I can discern: Mazog is seeking to enslave some of the nameless horrors beneath Moria. But why he wishes to do this remains unknown to me, for he does not need nameless allies to crush the dwarves; they are near enough to destruction as it is.

'No, he must have some other target. I fear it may be the Golden Wood, home to my Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel. Mazog does not have the foresight for such a plan. This must come from Gorothúl of Dol Guldur.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We have learned much from your efforts that will be of use to us, and to the dwarves as well.'Bósi has sent you to retrieve the mithril shackles being crafted in the Heart of Fire to contain Mazog.Stóthkell is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths, among the Silvertine Lodes.

Bósi has asked you to journey to the Heart of Fire to see if the shackles for Mazog have been made.Talk to Stóthkell in the Heart of FireBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located off Durin's Way.

You have collected the shackles to be used to secure Mazog for the journey into Mirkwood and should bring them now to Bróin.Lenglammel is in Gwathrendath, the camp of Elves in the depths of the Foundations of Stone.

Bróin has sent you to tell Lenglammel that the dwarves will not bring Mazog through Lothlórien on their way to Mirkwood, skirting the wood instead. He also wants you to express his displeasure with the requirement.Talk to Lenglammel in Gwathrendath'Bróin told me about your capture of Mazog in Rushdurinul, and it was clear to me that if Mazog is to be brought to Dol Guldur in exchange for my son's freedom, we would need more powerful shackles to hold him. You were able to subdue the Orc-king when he broke free once; we cannot risk the necessity again.

'Therefore I commanded the smiths at the Heart of Fire to craft new shackles for Mazog. We have little mithril as it is, but they should have been able to make very strong bands indeed by mixing small quantities of it with other metals.

'Speak to Stóthkell in the Heart of Fire and see if the shackles are ready.''You remember where the Heart of Fire is, ${PLAYER}, surely? It is off the Way of Smiths among the Silvertine Lodes. Speak to Stóthkell and ask him if the shackles for Mazog have yet been made.''Yes, ${PLAYER}, yes. We combined a small quantity of mithril with other metals to make these shackles. In fact, some of the weapons and armour you previously collected for my smiths were melted down and used in their making.

'These bands will secure Mazog for the journey into Mirkwood. He will not break free of these, or I would be ashamed to call myself Stóthkell of the Iron Garrison!

'Bring these to Bróin for his approval. He is resting in the Peaceful Path, preparing for the journey.''I have given you the shackles, ${PLAYER}. I did not know there was time to be wasted; why have you not brought them to Bróin in the Peaceful Path?''Ah, the shackles! Yes, these look very sturdy indeed. Mazog will not be able to break from these as he did in Rushdurinul, ${PLAYER}.

'We have run into a... disagreement... with the Elves of Lothlórien concerning the plan to bring Mazog to Dol Guldur in exchange for my cousin's freedom. Celeborn has refused to allow us to bring the Orc into the Golden Wood, though it is clearly the most direct route. He wants us instead to skirt the woods, a journey that would take much longer!

'Lenglammel in Gwathrendath awaits my response. Give it to her, grudgingly: we will take the long way with Mazog, though it displeases me tremendously! Tell her, too, that I trust the Elves will shoulder some of the burden of this inconvenience! The delay this will cause is intolerable, and we are asked to bear it! I will do so, for Bori's sake.''Tell Lenglammel in Gwathrendath that I am not pleased with the requirement that we not bring Mazog into Lothlórien on the way to Mirkwood. Instead, we will take the long way around, losing precious days in the process, solely to please the ridiculous requirements of the Elves of Lothlórien. Tell her that and leave out none of my words!''I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. Bróin's concerns are real and understood, but bringing Mazog into Lothlórien is simply unacceptable. Even shackled, Mazog cannot be allowed within the Golden Wood.

'We spoke earlier about the marks Gorothúl left at certain locations in Moria, ${PLAYER}, and you have done well to eliminate some of them. Magor reported to me while you were gone that one at least remains....'Nimpheleg believes it may be possible to end the corruption of the wilting rot within Buzun-ghâr.A stone on which to place Nimpheleg's beryl can be found in the deepest area of Buzun-ghâr.

Nimpheleg believes that you can draw out and defeat the source of the rot in Buzun-ghâr by placing a beryl on a stone in the depths of the cave. He warned you to stay near the beryl once you placed it, for only the stone will diminish the ferocity of the master of the rot.Nimpheleg is at Lossathrod, the encampment in the upper reaches of Buzun-ghâr.

You have drawn forth and defeated the source of the rot within Buzun-ghâr, a diminished spirit: Grawulun the Caerog.'The rot that pervades the lower reaches of Buzun-ghâr is not of the natural world, ${PLAYER}, and that gives us the duty of removing it. If Orvar will not listen to our advice and seal the passage, we must destroy the source of the wilting rot before it escapes into wider Moria and becomes a much greater threat.

'I believe I have the means to do this, ${PLAYER}. This beryl will catch pure light, even at its most dim, and reflect it upon the corrupted walls of the passage. If you place it on a stone in the deepest area of Buzun-ghâr, it will be like a beacon to the evil of the rot -- drawing forth whatever lies behind the wilting rot, in agony.

'At that time you must destroy the source of the rot, but use caution! You must remain close to the beryl or its effects will not serve to weaken the master of the rot, whatever it may be!''You should place the beryl I gave you on a stone in the very deepest reaches of Buzun-ghâr, for that may draw forth the master of the rot, that it may be defeated. Stray not from the beryl once you have placed it, for the stone will diminish whatever creature it is that corrupts this place!''We are fortunate, ${PLAYER}, that Grawulun the Caerog, diminished as already he was, could be weakened further by the light of the beryl you used to draw him forth. No longer will his presence scar the gardens of Buzun-ghâr, or spread out into wider Moria.

'I worry that more and stronger of his kind may lurk in the deep places, but there is little enough we can do if that is true.

'I am delighted to have helped you fight the source of this rot, ${PLAYER}. May the dwarves have learned a lesson in this!'Some madness of mind and body has seized the Orcs of Mazog's command that have come to the Foundations of Stone.Orcs of Mazog's command, corrupted by the sickening evil, can be found throughout the Foundations of Stone.

Forglinn has asked you to defeat as many of Mazog's corrupted Orcs, the Globsnaga, as you can. The creatures seem to be mindless, but are still dangerous.Defeat Globsnaga Orcs throughout the Foundations of Stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Forglinn is in Gwathrendath, the Elf-camp among the Foundations of Stone.

You have defeated many of the Globsnaga Orcs, and should return now to Forglinn.'Mazog has sent many of his kind down here to the Foundations of Stone for some purpose. They seem to be seeking something, but we have not yet determined what that might be.

'It is clear at least that they are having very little success. Nay, these Orcs are being seized by some madness of mind and body that rages within them like a fire, erupting soon onto the surface as a sickening corruption of the flesh.

'This illness makes them even more dangerous, ${PLAYER}, though they seem to lose all reason. They are the Globsnaga now. Defeat them wherever you find them throughout the Foundations of Stone, for their mindlessness makes them more cruel and merciless than before.''We still do not know what causes the corruption that has taken hold of Mazog's Orcs and made them the fierce and mindless Globsnaga, but it is enough for the moment to know that their numbers are fewer.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''Look for Mazog's Orcs throughout the Foundations of Stone, corrupted by the mysterious evil that has taken these caves. They are the Globsnaga now, and though mindless, they must be defeated.'In order to save the dwarves in Moria, you have come to aid the Elves of Gwathrendath, sent into Moria at the behest of Lady Galadriel.Forglinn and Dithaliwenn are in the camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone beneath Nud-melek.

Lenglammel wonders if your fates may be revealed if you help the Elves of her company stand against the darkness.Help Forglinn with his taskHelp Dithaliwenn with her taskLenglammel is in the camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone beneath Nud-melek.

You have aided the Elves of Lenglammel's camp and should speak to her again.'This is a grim and unwholesome place. The air is heavy and stagnant and reeks of the unseen terrors that slither about in the darkness.

'But for the Lady Galadriel we brave the Black Pit, and we will do as we are bid until we can be of no more use here.

'She has sent you to us for a reason, ${CLASS}. The Lady sees many things in her Mirror; perhaps she has seen what fate awaits us in the abyss. Help the Elves of my company, and we will see all that may come to pass in this place.''Mazog must not be aware of the great evil that lurks beneath Moria, or he would not play such dangerous games. His Orcs are no match for what lies in the roots of these mountains.

'Or perhaps Gorothúl, this sorceror from Dol Guldur, has whispered honeyed lies in the ear of Azog's spawn. He may believe his Orcs have the upper hand, but they do not.''Help Forglinn and Dithaliwenn to combat the evils that crawl among the Foundations of Stone, and we may learn what our destinies hold.'Corunothiel and the other Elves of Lórien sent to assist the Iron Garrison are concerned by the corrupting rot that spreads within one of the newly-excavated passages.Nimpheleg is at Lossathrod, the camp-site within Buzun-ghâr, located off Durin's Way. Globsnaga Orcs can be found throughout Buzun-ghâr.

Since Orvar has refused to seal the newly-excavated passage, Corunothiel has asked you to work with her friend Nimpheleg to locate and destroy the source of the wilting rot within Buzun-ghâr, and to defeat the Globsnaga that have been affected by or drawn to the corruption.Defeat Globsnaga warriors within Buzun-ghâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Execute Nimpheleg's plan to destroy the source of the wilting rotDefeat Globsnaga skirmishers within Buzun-ghâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Corunothiel is at Lossathrod, the encampment of Elves and dwarves at the top of Buzun-ghâr.

You have dealt with the wilting rot within Buzun-ghâr and should speak now to Corunothiel of your successes.Orvar Bellhammer is at Lossathrod, the encampment within the passage of Buzun-ghâr, located off of Durin's Way.

Corunothiel said that a message for you was delivered to Orvar while you were in the depths of Buzun-ghâr, and you should speak to the dwarf to learn its content.'If Orvar will not listen to reason and collapse the only entrance to this passage, sealing the corruption within, we must find its source and destroy it. Speak to Nimpheleg about finding this source and dealing with it.

'We have seen Globsnaga Orcs deeper within Buzun-ghâr, and fear that they will soon climb up to this place. Have they been corrupted by the wilting rot, or is there some other cause of their affliction?

'These questions are secondary to the most important matter, ${PLAYER}: that they be defeated before they can do us any harm. Destroy them as you undertake Nimpheleg's scheme for cleansing the source of the wilting rot.''I do not know whether the Globsnaga have been affected by the wilting rot or whether it has merely drawn them near, but they must be destroyed. Seek them out within Buzun-ghâr and slay the creatures before they climb too near this encampment, or worse yet -- find their way too near the other homes of the Iron Garrison.

'Be sure to speak also to Nimpheleg; I know he has some ideas about drawing out the source of the rot and destroying it.''It will be some time before the plants and gardens within Buzun-ghâr can be restored, but your defeat of Grawulun the Caerog will make that possible where it was not before.

'You have done well, ${PLAYER}, and I am pleased that you have helped save the dwarves from their own hard-headed determination to delve where they should not!

'A dwarf of the Iron Garrison came to speak with Orvar while you were in the depths. I believe he had a message for you.''A message for you was delivered to Orvar while you were in the depths, ${PLAYER}. You should speak with him to learn its contents.''Well, ${PLAYER}, that was no great task, was it? Why should Corunothiel and Nimpheleg worry so greatly about sealing away Buzun-ghâr, when you so ably defeated Grawulun the Caerog? And now this passage can be of great benefit to the dwarves!'Lenglammel is worried that the nameless creatures sought by Mazog have been approaching her camp too closely.Cracks in the abyss can be found throughout the Foundations of Stone, not far from Gwathrendath. 

Lenglammel has asked you to place Elf-stones in front of abyss-cracks near the camp to dissuade nameless creatures from approaching.Lenglammel is in the camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone.

You have done what you can to counter the threat of the nameless creatures that lurk among the Foundations of Stone.'The nameless creatures in the depths of the earth are not to be trifled with, but still Mazog insists on attempting to enslave them. There can be no doubt that the hand of Dol Guldur is causing him to try this foolish course, but I have no pity for him. These creatures are deadly, and they approach Gwathrendath more closely with each passing hour.

'And still Magor does not return! This is not like him to be so tardy! Were he not so strong, I would be worried, but Magor trained with Celeborn in the Elder Days and can take care of himself.

'There are cracks in the walls not far from Gwathrendath. Place these beryls in front of the cracks to dissuade the nameless from approaching  the cracks.''You have done what you could, ${PLAYER}, but where the nameless are concerned I hope only that it will be enough.''Nameless creatures sometimes crawl through cracks in the walls of the abyss; place these Elf-stones near them to dissuade them from doing so. You should also defeat the nameless beasts wherever you see them, for they are most dangerous, and are becoming more fell and numerous by the hour.'Bróin is unsure of what he should be doing and wants you to help him try and find some way of helping Bori, captured by the forces of Mazog.Bróin is resting on the Peaceful Path, located in the Mustering Hall, east of Sulnul-dûm and west of the Stone Hall, along Durin's Way. The entrance to the Peaceful Path is north-east of Buzun-ghâr.

Bróin has sent word that he wishes to speak with you again. Orvar told you to treat Bróin kindly, believing that his trials in the watery den of the Watcher and losing his cousin to the forces of Mazog may have affected him deeply.The Chambers of Wisdom, Knowledge, and Deep Thought can be found throughout the Great Delving, as can Katûb-zahar. Any of these places may have the mining records Bróin was tasked with finding.

Bróin is dissatisfied with the mindless tasks his father Brogur has assigned him, and he is extremely frustrated that the dwarves are doing such work as this while Bori remains prisoner to the forces of Mazog.Bróin is on the Peaceful Path, located in the Mustering Hall, east of Sulnul-dûm and west of the Stone Hall, along Durin's Way. The entrance to the Peaceful Path is north-east of Buzun-ghâr.

You have recovered some of the mining records that Bróin's father wanted him to find, but they include some curious details in which Bróin will be most interested.'The messenger sent by Bróin was very clear that we should deal first with the corruption within Buzun-ghâr. Yet once that was done, his master desired greatly that you visit him again on the Peaceful Path, located in the Mustering Hall, east of Sulnul-dûm and west of the Stone Hall, here along Durin's Way. The entrance to the Peaceful Path is north-east of Buzun-ghâr.

'If you will allow me this, ${PLAYER}, I must tell you that Bróin has not been the same since you returned him to us; it is no fault of his own, for he endured much in the watery den of the Watcher, curse its name, but the son of Brogur may be now a little touched in the head. And then to lose his cousin Bori to the forces of Mazog! It cannot have helped.

'Treat him kindly and with patience, ${PLAYER}, but if the requests he makes of you seem a little peculiar, you will at least know the cause.''The messenger sent by Bróin was very clear that we should deal first with the corruption within Buzun-ghâr. Once that was done, his master desired that you come visit him again on the Peaceful Path, located in the Mustering Hall, east of Sulnul-dûm and west of the Stone Hall, here along Durin's Way. The entrance to the Peaceful Path is north-east of Buzun-ghâr.''Hello again, ${PLAYER}. My messenger returned from Buzun-ghâr with the news that you were in the depths trying to end the corruption that was found in that passage; I see that you were successful.'

Bróin seems about to say something else, but decides against it. After an uncomfortable pause, he begins again, and this time the words come in a torrent.

'I cannot understand why we waste so much effort on such insignificant tasks while my cousin Bori languishes in the dungeons of Mazog! Why still do my father's dwarves mine while Bori is held? He may not still live, but if he does, just as I endured in the watery den of the Watcher, could it not be that every hour we waste brings him closer to death at the hands of the Orcs? And still no one does anything!'

Bróin takes a long breath, making an effort to calm himself.

'My father has asked me to search for records of mined nodes in Khazad-dûm, but I cannot bring myself to do such useless work. If you will do it in my place, I can continue trying to think of some way to help Bori. Look for these records in any of the old archives in the Great Delving: the Chambers of Wisdom, Knowledge, or Deep Thought, or in Katûb-zahar.''What use are mining records when cousin Bori remains a prisoner of the Orcs? This is maddening, ${PLAYER}!

'My father wanted me to search for records of nodes mined in Khazad-dûm, but I refuse to do this while Bori remains captive. If you will do this for me, I will stay behind and try to come up with some means of rescuing Bori from the dungeons of Mazog!

'Mining records may be found in the various archives in the Great Delving: the Chambers of Wisdom, Knowledge, or Deep Thought, and in Katûb-zahar. One set of mining records should be enough for my father. Bring them here when you find some. A waste of time!''You have returned with the mining records? My father will be pleased, even if I am not. Why must we waste so much time on meaningless tasks such as this when my cousin remains a prisoner of Mazog?'

Bróin takes the mining records from you with a sigh, but as he reads, his eyes widen and his face brightens.

'Do you... do you understand what you have found, ${PLAYER}? Ha ha! These are not simple mining records at all! These pages may hold the key to rescuing my cousin Bori! Listen to this:

'"Melkólf Stonecarver commissioned for detail work on rear wall of Rushdurinul during night-time for completion of Zurr-thurkh; special instructions withheld by order of Durin."

'The word Rushdurinul drew my attention, ${PLAYER}, for that is the name of the throne of Durin, the very throne that Mazog has claimed for himself. To then see the name Zurr-thurkh, or "secret road..." could it be that this dwarf, this Melkólf Stonecarver, was tasked with creating a secret passage out of Durin's throne room for the king to use in the event of danger? If this passage was completed, it might be used to gain access to Mazog! It might be used to rescue my cousin Bori!'Lenglammel told you that another of Gorothúl's relics has been found in the depths of Azanarukâr and must be destroyed.Lenglammel is in Gwathrendath, the Elf-camp among the Foundations of Stone.

Lenglammel is waiting to speak to you in order to bring you to Magor for an assault on Azanarukâr.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge. This instance can only be completed by a solo or two person group.</rgb>Talk to Lenglammel to travel to AzanarukârLenglammel is in Gwathrendath, the Elf-camp among the Foundations of Stone.

You have destroyed the relic of Gorothúl and sent both Gwathnor and Grawulun formless into the depths, for a time. You should report now to Lenglammel.Talk to Lenglammel in GwathrendathHaldir is on Talan Haldir, just outside the border of the Golden Wood.

Lenglammel has sent you to Haldir to relay a message of importance: the expedition of the Golden Host must happen as soon as it is possible.Talk to Haldir at Talan Haldir'Magor has been venturing into the depths ever since you rescued him, ${PLAYER}, saying only that he considers it his personal duty to prevent the nameless dangers in Azanarukâr from ever leaving there.

'On his most recent journey into the fires of those caverns, he beheld a number of Regmyl carrying what appeared to be an idol of some evil significance. He followed them for a time, but at one point they seemed to become aware of his presence, and he found it necessary to retreat.

'Gather your strength and speak to me, ${PLAYER}. I will bring you to Magor. Together, you must return to Azanarukâr, learn if the Regmyl's idol is a relic of Gorothúl's, and destroy it.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge. This instance can only be completed by a solo or two player group.</rgb>'We are readying to leave as quickly as we are able, ${PLAYER}, but the preparations of the Golden Host cannot be hurried overmuch, lest we doom its mission to failure. It will take some time for the dwarves to bring Mazog to the edge of Mirkwood, and that will allow all the necessary preparations to be made.

'I hope you are ready when that time comes, ${PLAYER}. Both the dwarves of the Iron Garrison and the Elves of Lothlórien will rely on your courage and ability. I hope too that this expedition is not a mistake. It has been a long time since the forest bore the name Greenwood the Great.

'I will see you again, ${PLAYER}, when the time has come.''You have sent Gwathnor and Grawulun formless into the depths, ${PLAYER}, and not a moment too soon! I cannot say if this is the last of the relics left by Gorothúl in Moria, but we have bought some time at least.

'As long as Gorothúl remains alive, so too does the danger that he may create more such beacons, once again drawing forth Gwathnor or Grawulun...and next time we may not find them before they achieve their full level of power.

'You must go now to Haldir on the flet just outside the Golden Wood. Tell him that the dwarves of the Iron Garrison have agreed to bring Mazog to Mirkwood on an indirect route that will not pass through Lothlórien, as requested. Tell him, too, that the expedition of the Golden Host must occur with as much haste as can be arranged. Too great a delay, and we may find ourselves hemmed between Dol Guldur on one side and Gwathnor and Grawulun reborn on the other!''Hurry to Talan Haldir, ${PLAYER}, with the message that the Golden Host must leave as soon as can be arranged.''Are you ready to go? Magor has travelled ahead and will meet you in Azanarukâr.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge. This instance can only be completed by a solo or two person group.</rgb>Lenglammel has so far been unsuccessful at her primary mission in Moria: locating and rescuing Mithrandir, if one can indeed rescue a Wizard.The Black Lake and the bottom of the Endless Stair are both among the Foundations of Stone.

Lenglammel has asked you to search several locations for sign of either Mithrandir or the Elf Magor.Search the Black LakeSearch the top of the bottom portion of the Endless StairLenglammel is in her camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone.

You have searched both locations, and found the burned hat of Gandalf in the middle of the Black Lake. The Endless Stair has been choked by burned and blackened rubble. It seems that Gandalf survived long enough to do battle with the Balrog, but what happened then is unknown to you. You should speak now to Lenglammel.'When first we arrived here at the Foundations of Stone, we did so at the request of Lady Galadriel, and had one primary objective: to learn what fate befell Mithrandir, the Grey Pilgrim, in these very depths.

'Yes, I speak of Gandalf. He passed into the shadow of the abyss, and it was the hope of the Lady that he might be found, and found safe. The Elf Magor sought him for many days, but found no sign. 

'Magor still has not returned, ${PLAYER}, and I am beginning to worry. There are two places I would have you search for sign of either Mithrandir or Magor: the top of the bottom portion of the Endless Stair and the Black Lake. When you have searched both places, I hope you will have some sign of either the Wizard or Magor.''Several places remain to be searched, ${PLAYER}: the top of the bottom section of the Endless Stair and the Black Lake. Perhaps you will find some sign of Mithrandir or the Elf Magor at these places. I pray that you do.'You describe your discovery of Gandalf's burned hat in the middle of the Black Lake and of the rubble that chokes the endless stair. Lenglammel sighs.

'Your news of Mithrandir and the lack of news concerning my friend Magor both fill me with anxiety, for we still do not know their fates. I thank you for it, but it could be that Magor at least may soon return to us.

'Dithaliwenn found something while you were away.'Bróin believes you have discovered mention of a secret passage into Rushdurinul, where Mazog has established his throne, and might use it to rescue his cousin Bori.The passage to Melkólf Stonecarver's workshop can be found in the side of Zirakzigil; take the western exit from the Peaceful Path, and then turn west and climb a short slope to the entrance.

Bróin has asked you to find Melkólf Stonecarver's workshop and search it for any mention of Zurr-thurkh, the secret road into Durin's throne room that might have been built long ago. He has decided not to accompany you to the workshop.Find the workshop of Melkólf Stonecarver and search it for mention of Zurr-thurkhBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located in the Mustering Hall, east of Sulnul-dûm and west of the Stone Hall, along Durin's Way.

You have recovered a set of plans from Melkólf Stonecarver's workshop that reveal a secret way into Rushdurinul, the throne room of Durin, that is now occupied by Mazog and his Orcs.'Melkólf Stonecarver was renowned for much of his work, though I have never heard of this "secret road." Its inclusion in these records may very well have been an oversight by a scribe of Durin's day, but he may have given us what we need to wrest my cousin from the grasp of Mazog's forces!

'Mazog has entrenched himself in the great fortress of Zabadgathol, surrounding himself with Orc warriors. But if a secret escape passage was constructed in the rear wall of Rushdurinul, we might be able to sneak into the fortress unobserved!

'Melkólf Stonecarver's workshop was recently uncovered, but no dwarves were left to guard it; who could have suspected how important it might become? Take the western exit from the Peaceful Path, and once you come out onto the mountainside, turn west and climb the short slope to the cave-mouth. Enter the passage and search for word of the secret way into Rushdurinul!'

Bróin blanches at your request that he accompany you there.

'Oh, no -- I need to stay here. There's so much to be done here. I will come with you on the next adventure, I promise! You should travel to the workshop alone, in order to maintain secrecy.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'The passage to Melkólf Stonecarver's workshop can be found in the side of Zirakzigil. Take the western exit from the Peaceful Path. Once you are outside, turn west and climb a short slope to the cave entrance. You must enter and search for any mention of Zurr-thurkh.

'I will stay behind on this one. I will accompany you on the next adventure, I promise! There's just a great deal to do here, as I am sure you understand.''You've done it, ${PLAYER}! Look at these drawings: this is clearly Zabadgathol, which means these hallways here connect to Rushdurinul, and...'

Bróin laughs with delight.

'See this tunnel here? I would wager all the treasures of Khazad-dûm that this passage appears on no maps save this one!

'Now where can we gain access to this passage, Zurr-thurkh, the "secret road?" If we follow it along this way... we...'

Bróin's smile becomes a mask of confusion.

'Unless I read this wrongly, ${PLAYER}, it seems that Zurr-thurkh connects to... Buzun-ghâr? Can this really be?'Dithaliwenn has found a clue to the lost Elf Magor's whereabouts near Azanarukâr, and Lenglammel wants you to find him.Lenglammel is in her camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone.

Lenglammel is waiting for you to speak to her about travelling to Azanarukâr in search of Magor and the mysterious evil that dwells there.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge. This instance can only be completed by a solo or two person group.</rgb>Talk to Lenglammel and travel to AzanarukârLenglammel is in her camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone.

You have won a great victory in the depths beneath Moria, and should speak now to Lenglammel.'Dithaliwenn found an Elf-stone, much like the ones I gave you earlier, by the cave-mouth to Azanarukâr, from which emanated a vile stench. You did not place this stone, ${PLAYER}. It must have been Magor! But why would he have left the stone rather than return to the camp himself?

'I think the cave Magor found must be the source of the great evil Lady Galadriel sensed beneath Moria, ${PLAYER}. If you can rescue Magor from its clutches, he may be able to tell us something of its power.

'Gather your courage, friend. Whatever this new fell-craft be, if it could best a great Elf like Magor in combat, it must be dangerous indeed!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge. This instance can only be completed by a solo or two person group.</rgb>'Magor told us everything, ${PLAYER}, and he has set off on a journey back to Lothlórien to inform the Lady Galadriel of what has transpired.

'Your feats are truly incredible, my friend! Not only have you rescued Magor, but you have thwarted the plans of not only the Orcs, but, more importantly, of Gorothúl of Dol Guldur as well!

'You are wholly remarkable. You have Magor's highest praise, and my own.''Go with courage, ${PLAYER}, into the depths in search of Magor. He may be able to tell us something about the great evil that Lady Galadriel has sensed in the depths.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge. This instance can only be completed by a solo or two person group.</rgb>You have located the plans for a secret escape tunnel out of Durin's throne room. If it was ever constructed, it might be used to enter Zabadgathol in secret to rescue Bori.Orvar Bellhammer is in Buzun-ghâr, located south-west of the Peaceful Path, in the very south-eastern corner of Tharâkh Bazân, along Durin's Way.

Bróin has asked you to speak with the dwarf Orvar about accompanying you on the secret road into Rushdurinul.The entrance to Zurr-thurkh, the secret road, can be found in the depths of Buzun-ghâr, where you fought Grawulun the Caerog.

Orvar has agreed to meet you inside Zurr-thurkh, if you can find the entrance, in order to mount a rescue of Bori from the clutches of Mazog.Find the entrance to Zurr-thurkh and use it to get behind the walls of ZabadgatholCorunothiel is at Lossathrod, the encampment in Buzun-ghâr.

You have emerged from Rushdurinul victorious over Mazog, but have learned the unfortunate news that Bori and the other captives have been sent to Dol Guldur with Gorothúl. Corunothiel is waiting to speak with you.'How many fates must have entwined for the Iron Garrison to break open the entrance to Buzun-ghâr just when we need it, ${PLAYER}? If the "secret road" was built, you will find the entrance to it deep within Buzun-ghâr! It must be a portent to have happened this day, of all days!'

Bróin suddenly finds himself unable to meet your eyes.

'I wish I could come with you to walk the "secret road" and rescue Bori, ${PLAYER}, but there is still so much to do, and... well, I am needed here. We will fight together on the next adventure -- I swear it.

'Return to Buzun-ghâr, located south-west of here, in the south-eastern corner of Tharâkh Bazân, and speak with Orvar Bellhammer. He will accompany you along Zurr-thurkh, if it exists, though he should be your only companion, in the interest of secrecy.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'I am needed here, ${PLAYER}... there is so much to be done. I swear I will accompany you on the next adventure.

'Return to Orvar in Buzun-ghâr, in the south-eastern corner of Tharâkh Bazân, south-west of here along Durin's Way, and ask him to accompany you on the "secret road." You may yet rescue my cousin Bori from the clutches of Mazog!''You say there is a way behind the walls of Zabadgathol, into Rushdurinul, where Mazog has set his throne? I don't know, ${PLAYER} -- it seems unlikely to me.'

With an eyebrow raised, Orvar listens to your explanation of Bróin's idea that it might be possible to rescue Bori.

'This is all well and good, but why isn't Bróin coming with you on this errand, ${PLAYER}? If you ask me, he's still not over his experience in the watery den of the Watcher. It seems to me that Lord Brogur has been trying to give his son trivial tasks to coax him from this brooding, but it has yet to work. Bróin will not be himself until he is able to conquer whatever fear clutches him.

'No matter. If you descend once again into the depths of Buzun-ghâr, where you stood against Grawulun the Caerog, and can find the entrance to this Zurr-thurkh. I will join you on the other side.''If you can find the entrance to Zurr-thurkh in the depths of Buzun-ghâr, near where you fought Grawulun the Caerog, I will meet you on the other side. Then we will see if we can rescue Bori from the clutches of Mazog!''You see the good that can be done when Elves and dwarves work together, ${PLAYER}; Mazog was right to fear the alliance and hope that it should never come to pass!

'The dwarf Bróin came to Lossathrod, winded from a long run, and asked that we accompany him in his pursuit of you. He claimed to have made an error by leaving you to attempt the rescue of his kinsman with Orvar alone, and his regret of that decision spurred him onward. You are fortunate that he regained his courage when he did, ${PLAYER}, you and Orvar both!'You have overthrown a terrible power deep beneath Moria and have been summoned by the Lady Galadriel of Lórien.Haldir is atop a flet outside Lothlórien, south of the river Nimrodel.

Lenglammel has told you to speak with Haldir about arranging an audience with the Lady Galadriel.Talk to Haldir and arrange an audience with the Lady GaladrielHaldir is at his camp outside Lothlórien.

Galadriel has seen many things about your future in her Mirror, but you cannot make sense of the confused images.'You must return to Lothlórien at once, ${PLAYER}. The Lady Galadriel will want to speak with you about what has happened here, and what it will mean for the future.

'Speak with Haldir atop the flet south of the river Nimrodel and he will arrange a meeting with the Lady.''The Lady Galadriel can see much in her Mirror, but it is not known to her or any Power whether what she has shown you will come to pass.

'One day, perhaps, you will look back on your long road and make sense of what you saw today. Only time can tell such things.

'I thank you for the service you have provided my people, and may the light of the Elves shine upon your path and guide your steps aright.

'For those unfamiliar to Galadhrim, we shall name you Friend, and allow you to enter our fair home.''The Lady Galadriel has called you to her garden, for she wishes to speak with you. I will take you to her.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'You must go at once, to speak with Haldir atop the flet south of the river Nimrodel about arranging an audience with the Lady Galadriel.'Celeborn of Lórien wishes to speak with you about your recent accomplishments in Moria and about what lies ahead.Haldir is in a flet in a great tree on the banks of the Nimrodel, outside Lórien.

You have been told that Celeborn desires to speak with you about recent events in Moria, and should speak to Haldir about arranging a meeting with the Lord of Lórien.Haldir is on Talan Haldir, a flet in a great tree along the banks of the Nimrodel, just outside Lórien.

Haldir is waiting to hear when you are ready to speak with Celeborn.Talk to Haldir and travel to your audience with CelebornHaldir is on Talan Haldir, a flet in a great tree along the banks of the Nimrodel, just outside Lórien.

Haldir is waiting to speak with you now that you have had your audience with Celeborn.'Lord Celeborn wishes to speak with you about what has happened, ${PLAYER}. Return to Talan Haldir and speak with Haldir about arranging an audience with the Lord of Lórien.

'You will find Talan Haldir in a great tree on the banks of the Nimrodel, outside Lórien.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. Is it true that you have defeated Mazog in his own lair?'

Haldir smiles as you briefly tell your tale.

'You are truly an astonishment to me, my friend; I did not really expect the rumour to be true.

'Let me know when you are ready to see Lord Celeborn, and I will bring you to him as he requested.''The winds of change are blowing, ${PLAYER}, and I fear they carry with them the onset of war. Lothlórien cannot remain isolated and in safety forever.

'Lord Celeborn's gaze must turn toward Mirkwood and the great shadow that lies over Dol Guldur. When the time comes to cross the river and fight, as it seems we must, I will call for you.

'Had I once thought it might not be necessary, I do not any longer. Too many signs seem to point in that direction. Stay well, ${PLAYER}. We will have need of you yet.''You should travel to the banks of the Nimrodel to speak to Haldir about arranging a meeting with Lord Celeborn.''I will take you to see Lord Celeborn, if you are ready to speak with him about your great doings in the dark depths of Moria.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>The Halls of Crafting, once inhabited by the Dwarves of Khazad-dûm in ages past, now boast the finest of Orc-smiths, who serve Mazog. Their work can only be hindered by the defeat of those who command them.Defeat Âmbal in the Halls of CraftingDefeat Bashkuga in the Halls of CraftingDefeat Thaguzg in Halls of CraftingThere is an ancient tradition in Lothlórien, wherin one travels throughout the forest, visiting a series of stone glades and meditating within each.The Peaceful Glade lies north of Egladil.

Galhíril suggested you <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> in the Peaceful Glade.The Peaceful Glade lies north of Egladil.

Galhíril suggested you <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> in the Peaceful Glade.The Ring of Melbrethil lies to the north of the Peaceful Glade.

Galhíril suggested that you <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> within the Ring of Melbrethil.The Ring of Melbrethil lies to the north of the Peaceful Glade.

Galhíril suggested that you <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> within the Ring of Melbrethil.The Stone-grove lies well to the south-west of the Ring of Melbrethil.

Galhíril suggested that you <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> within the Stone-grove.The Stone-grove lies far to the south-west of the Ring of Melbrethil.

Galhíril suggested that you <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> within the Stone-grove.The Elder Circle lies to the south-east of the Stone-grove.

Glahíril suggested that you <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> within the Elder Circle.The Elder Circle lies to the south-east of the Stone-grove.

Glahíril suggested that you <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> within the Elder Circle.Galhíril is in Egladil.

You should return to Galhiril and tell her of your meditations within the circles of Lothlórien.Talk to Galhíril in Egladil'By the way, ${PLAYER}, have you yet come upon the ancient circles of Lothlórien? They were raised so long ago that few of our tales even speak of their origins.

'Those among us who feel the need to remind ourselves of our origins often go to these ancient glades and <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> within them, recounting years long past.

'Perhaps you should attempt this pilgrimage? I would be most interested to hear your thoughts upon it should you complete it.''So tell me, what did you experience as you meditated upon the ancient glories of Lothlórien...?

'My, that seems a bit odd. I recall my experience rather differently.''The Peaceful Glade is your first destination through the Circles of Silence.''The Peaceful Glade is your first destination through the Circles of Silence.''The Ring of Melbrethil is your second destination through the Circles of Silence.''The Ring of Melbrethil is your second destination through the Circles of Silence.''The Stone-grove is your third destination through the Circles of Silence.''The Stone-grove is your third destination through the Circles of Silence.''The Elder Circle is your fourth destination through the Circles of Silence.''The Elder Circle is your fourth destination through the Circles of Silence.'Trevadiel has welcomed you to Caras Galadhon and wants you to become familiar with the city.Randiron is in Telain Galadhrim, beneath the flet on which the trainers reside, down the western path and along the first right turn.

Trevadiel told you to seek Randiron to learn more of the ways of Caras Galadhon.Talk to Randiron near Telain GaladhrimRainen is at Telain Galadhrim, the flet upon which the trainers reside, up the winding steps from Randiron.

Randiron has told you to speak with his friend Rainen.Talk to Rainen at Telain GaladhrimPadril can be found at Telain Galadhrim, on the level above Rainen, reached by climbing the ladder.

Rainen has asked you to speak with her friend Padril.Talk to Padril at Telain Galadhrim'Welcome, ${PLAYER}, to Caras Galadhon, beloved city of Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel of Lothlórien! Count yourself among the fortunate few, friend ${CLASS}, for not many outsiders have seen the beauty of this place and could report of it. What make you of Caras Galadhon thus far?

'You wonder how you will find your way among the tall mallorn-trees? It is not as confusing as it may seem at first, my friend, and I will help you to learn your way around.

'To reach Telain Galadhrim, the flets upon which the trainers reside, follow this path to the west and take the first right turning. Follow that path to my friend Randiron, who will guide you further.''When Trevadiel heard there would be another visitor to Caras Galadhon, she hurried to the entrance with all haste; she delights in greeting those unfamiliar to the city, and there are so very few of those that she rarely has the opportunity.

'Look above us, and you will see Telain Galadhrim, a series of flets upon which Elves of the many professions can be consulted for guidance and services. Climb the steps that wind up the bole of the tree here to reach the talan upon which the class trainers reside.

'You will find Rainen on the flet above, and she will continue your tour of the city.''On this high flet of Telain Galadhrim you will find those of my kin entrusted with the rewarding of valuable items to those who have proven themselves true friends of the Elves of Lórien.

'Bring any Lothlórien gold leaves or Lothlórien silver branches to the Elves on this flet for your rewards.

'I hope you will enjoy your stay in Caras Galadhon, ${PLAYER}, and that you will be a valuable contributor to the good welfare of Lothlórien! Namárië!''Many of the services you might need in Caras Galadhon can be found here at Telain Galadhrim.

'On this level you will find the class trainers, a vault-keeper and our hall of trade. If you cross the flet to the ladder on the far side and climb the ladder there, you will find a mailbox for your use. On that level you will find vendors for the scholarly and jewelsmithy pursuits, as well as a healer and provisioner.

'But for now, climb this ladder here to reach the next level and speak with Padril on the level above.''We are beneath Telain Galadhrim, the flets upon which the class trainers reside. Climb these winding steps up to the flets and speak with Rainen, who will continue your tour of the city.''Climb this ladder to reach the higher level and speak with my friend Padril, for she will conclude your tour of Telain Galadhrim.''To reach Telain Galadhrim, follow this path to the west and take the first right turning. Follow that path to my friend Randiron, who will guide you further.'Bahanneth was so pleased with the success of your mission to destroy the Orcs' weapons that he would like you to continue your efforts.Fanuidhol lies to the north-west of Talan Fanuidhol.

Bahanneth wants you to go into Fanuidhol and defeat some of the smiths there, as well as to destroy the stores of weapons they have forged.Defeat Orc-smiths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy weapon-stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol, south-east of Fanuidhol.

You should return to Bahanneth with tidings of your success.Talk to Bahanneth at Talan Fanuidhol'My good ${CLASS}, your efforts were quite successful but the Orcs do not lack for numbers, and they continue to move supplies out from the depths of Moria.

'I think you should pay them another visit. We would not wish them to become complacent, after all, would we?

'Defeat the smiths that have come to replace those slain and destroy their new weapon-stores, then return here to me.''Excellent, excellent. You do us proud, ${PLAYER}. Confusion to our enemies!''The Orcs of Moria are many, but they will break upon Lothlórien like a light tide.'Defeat the sources of the blight within the Sixteenth Hall.Defeat TramugDefeat DhûrzDefeat the Lost OneMaethoron knows that the Orcs of Moria are more limitless than the weapons they wield, and wants you to steal some of these weapons from the Orc camps in Nanduhirion.The Orcs have established three camps along the road that runs through Nanduhirion, north-west of Talan Haldir. Racks of weapons can be found throughout these camps.

Maethoron has asked you to steal Orc-weapons from the camps of the Orcs in Nanduhirion.'The Orcs of Moria seem to be of a limitless supply, ${PLAYER}, but the weapons they wield seem to be much less available; every sword or axe we take from them is an Orc we render defenceless, if only for a short time.

'The Orcs have established camps to the north-west, along the road that runs through Nanduhirion: Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul. Journey to these three camps and steal any of the weapons you find within.

'I will not forget any of your deeds against the Orcs that have invaded Nanduhirion, so perilously close to Lothlórien.''Very good, ${PLAYER}. Each of these weapons will be greatly missed by the Orcs, and will make our task of defending Lothlórien easier!'The trolls of Angmar have a singular vision, one that involves destroying the enemies of Angmar.Taskmaster Sharkûlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors.

The trolls from Angmar, in an effort to speed the victory of Angmar's army, are willing to return Angmar to fight the Free Peoples in exchange for your services in the North. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkûlob.Talk to Taskmaster Sharkûlob at GramsfootTaskmaster Sharkûlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors.

You took the place of a troll while it wrought destruction against the forces of the Free Peoples in Angmar. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkûlob.Talk to Taskmaster Sharkûlob at Gramsfoot'Trolls fight. You die too fast. We strong, where you weak.

'War-tyrant angry you lose Lumber-camp.

'You go to troll-home now. Troll come here and fight. We win war. Take all. I send troll home when done.''Trolls do good. You do good too. We smash and crash and bash! Târks die!''You go now. Troll come here.'The trolls of Angmar have a singular vision, one that involves destroying the enemies of Angmar.Taskmaster Sharkûlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors.

The trolls from Angmar, in an effort to speed the victory of Angmar's army, are willing to go to Eregion to fight the Free Peoples in exchange for your services in the North. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkûlob.Talk to Taskmaster Sharkûlob at GramsfootTaskmaster Sharkûlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors.

You took the place of a troll in Angmar while it wrought destruction against the forces of the Free Peoples in Eregion. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkûlob.Talk to Taskmaster Sharkûlob at Gramsfoot'Trolls fight. You die too fast. We strong, where you weak.

'War-tyrant angry you lose Lumber-camp.

'You go to troll-home now. Troll come here and fight. We win war. Take all. I send troll home when done.''Trolls do good. You do good too. We smash and crash and bash! Târks die!''You go now. Troll come here.'The trolls of Angmar have a singular vision, one that involves destroying the enemies of Angmar.Taskmaster Sharkûlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors.

The trolls from Angmar, in an effort to speed the victory of Angmar's army, are willing to go to Forochel to fight the Free Peoples in exchange for your services in the North. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkûlob.Talk to Taskmaster Sharkûlob at GramsfootTaskmaster Sharkûlob is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors.

You took the place of a troll in Angmar while it wrought destruction against the forces of the Free Peoples in Forochel. You should speak with Taskmaster Sharkûlob.Talk to Taskmaster Sharkûlob at Gramsfoot'Trolls fight. You die too fast. We strong, where you weak.

'War-tyrant angry you lose Lumber-camp.

'You go to troll-home now. Troll come here and fight. We win war. Take all. I send troll home when done.''Trolls do good. You do good too. We smash and crash and bash! Târks die!''You go now. Troll come here.'Complete all deeds within the Forgotten TreasuryComplete all deeds within the Forgotten TreasuryComplete Intruders in the Vault (Advanced)Complete Defilers of the Forgotten Treasury (Advanced)Complete Treasures of the Silvertine LodesDindirith has asked you to remove the Orc filth from the Nimrodel, the fast-flowing stream outside the border of Lórien.The soiled banks of the Nimrodel can be found north and south from Echad Andestel, along the banks of the stream.

Dindirith has asked you to clean up the banks of the Nimrodel, sullied by the passage of the Orcs.Collect Orc filth from the banks of the Nimrodel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dindirith is in Echad Andestel, west of the banks of Nimrodel and the border of Lórien.

You have collected Orc filth from the banks of Nimrodel and should return now to Dindirith, as he asked.'Orcs have been trying to enter the Golden Wood for the past several days, ${PLAYER}, and though they are killed by the arrows of the Galadhrim before they get very far, still there is grievous damage done.

'Curse the foul feet of the Orcs! Their passage across the swift-flowing Nimrodel has dirtied its clean waters. The encrusted filth of their boots collects on the banks of the stream, and the song of Nimrodel is made the more sorrowful for it.

'Travel north and south along the stream and collect the filth left behind by the Orcs' passage. Bring it to me and we will dispose of it, and Nimrodel will run clean once more.''Follow the banks of the Nimrodel north and south from here and clean up the Orc filth left in their passage toward Lothlórien. Return to me when you have collected some of the Orc filth.''Curse the foul feet of the Orcs! You have done well to cleanse the banks of Nimrodel, though as long as the Orcs march toward the Golden Wood, that beautiful stream will be endangered by their filthy careless footsteps.

'I have an idea, ${PLAYER}. Let us return this filth to the Orcs.'The depths of Dâr Narbugud hold both new and long forgotten vestiges of life.Collect smelly, red mushroomCollect strange, blue mushroomCollect colourful mushroomCollect divergent mushroomCollect inconsistent mushroomThe Nameless are fearsome creatures, awakened from the deepest crevices of Moria, where only Durin the Deathless has ever walked.Defeat Nameless in Dâr NarbugudThe Nameless are fearsome creatures, awakened from the deepest crevices of Moria, where only Durin the Deathless has ever walked.Defeat Nameless in Dâr NarbugudThe Globsnaga Orcs dwell deep in the heart of Dâr Narbugud, where they serve the Mistress of Pestilence.Defeat Orcs in Dâr NarbugudThe Globsnaga Orcs dwell deep in the heart of Dâr Narbugud, where they serve the Mistress of Pestilence.Defeat Orcs in Dâr NarbugudOrcs are not the only fungus-infested creatures in service to the Mistress of Pestilence: there are trolls among the Globsnaga, as well.Defeat trolls in Dâr NarbugudOrcs are not the only fungus-infested creatures in service to the Mistress of Pestilence: there are trolls among the Globsnaga, as well.Defeat trolls in Dâr NarbugudIn order to keep the pestilence from creeping to the fair lands beyond the walls of Moria, the Elves of Lothlórien believe the fungus-infested Orcs must be stopped ere they emerge from Moria.The new Globsnaga Orcs can be found throughout Dâr Narbugud, in the southern-most reaches of the Foundations of Stone in Moria.

Donfuin has asked you to slaughter the weaker, newly-altered Orcs to prevent their use as carriers of the fungus they are now infested with.Defeat weak Globsnaga Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Donfuin stands outside of Dâr Narbugud in Moria.

You should speak with Donfuin and inform him of your success against the weak Glabsnaga Orcs in Dâr Narbugud.Talk to Donfuin'There will be lesser creatures in Dâr Narbugud, mere pawns who are but carriers of the sickness their masters wish to spread.

'I believe that the weak, virulent pawns of plague must be wholly destroyed, ere they can emerge from Moria and spread the fungus throughout these lands. I know of no cure for the disease they bear, nor is an Orc deserving of our pity, no matter how much they suffer. They relish torture, and the despair of all creatures but themselves.

'Be wary, for Dâr Narbugud is a terrible place. You should go in strength.''Destroy as many Globsnaga Orcs as you can, ${PLAYER}, though this may seem an unpleasant thought. It is imperative that they do not leave Dâr Narbugud and spread their sickness beyond the Forgotten Treasury, or worse yet -- beyond the walls of Moria.''You have done well this day, ${PLAYER}. I know that the slaughter of the weak, no matter how vile, cannot ever be a pleasant task. But take heart: if you are gripped by black thoughts, you have done a great service to the world beyond this deep pit.'The Elves believe that trolls give a great advantage to the enemy in battle, due to their massive strength and hardiness. The troll-leaders in Dâr Narbugud must be eliminated in order to weaken the enemy's forces.The trolls you seek can be found in Dâr Narbugud, near the Dark Delvings at the southernmost tip of the Foundations of Stone.

Donfuin has asked you to defeat the trolls' leaders, which should disorganize the trolls and deflate their usefulness in battle.Defeat RungDefeat BlaghDonfuin stands just outside of Dâr Narbugud.

You should speak with Donfuin and inform him of your victory over the troll-leaders.Talk to Donfuin'The dwarves' establishment of a foothold in Durin's halls could not have come at a more fortuitous time, for I find that the presence of a certain guest in our lands has drawn the eyes of many foes, near and far.

'There is a great presence of trolls in Dâr Narbugud, and they are deadly foes even when running carelessly about. Imagine the damage that could be done to the dwarves when the trolls are guided by leaders.

'The dwarves are doughty fighters, but I do not believe they will withstand the might of well-led trolls, least of all trolls corrupted by the sickness and plague brewing in Dâr Narbugud. You should destroy the leaders outright, and the lesser trolls will surely be weakened without proper guidance from their superiors. This task will require a great force, to be sure.''The trolls you seek can be found in Dâr Narbugud. You should gather your allies and make haste, ${PLAYER}. The Lord and Lady fear that the dwarves' foothold is not yet strong.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}! I rejoice that you have returned in triumph. It is no small feat to have bested such brutal creatures as the wicked trolls you have faced. You must have the favour of Lady Galadriel to have survived a battle of this magnitude without falling.'The great leaders of the Globsnaga in Dâr Narbugud are essential to the strength and strategy of the enemy. They must be destroyed before they can lead their Globsnaga-hosts to war against the dwarves and Elves of the neighbouring lands.The leaders of the Globsnaga can be found in Dâr Narbugud, in the southern-most reaches of the Foundations of Stone.

You should defeat each leader of the Globsnaga to sever the head of the force that rallies in in Dâr Narbugud.Defeat ZholugaDefeat ÎstumDefeat FlâgîtDonfuin is outside of Dâr Narbugud in Moria.

You should speak with Donfuin and tell him of your success against the leaders of the plague-bearing Orcs.Talk to Donfuin'The bravery and cunning of your allies have bested the mighty trolls of Dâr Narbugud, ${PLAYER}. I was not certain that you would be up to the task I placed upon you, but you are a worthy warrior. I know now that you can accomplish great deeds.

'Now that the first step has been taken, I believe that we can behead the force that threatens to rise against ourselves and the dwarves. Without its head, a serpent will not survive. I believe the same will apply to the armies being rallied in Dâr Narbugud.

'Take your allies and go back, ${PLAYER}, and defeat the leaders of the Orcs who writhe with the fungal plague. With these masters gone, the servants will not be half so deadly as they are now.''You have done very well, ${PLAYER}, but there is more that must be done. Lord Celeborn wishes to speak with you.''Dâr Narbugud, as you know, lies just south of here. You should go there and defeat the pestilent leaders of the Globsnaga forces.'The great fumaroles of Dâr Narbugud fill the chambers of corruption with a noxious gas, creating the perfect atmosphere for the breeding of noxious spores.The greater fumaroles can be found in Dâr Narbugud, at the southern tip of the Foundations of Stone.

Donfuin has asked you to destroy the fumaroles that belch their noxious fumes into the poisoned chambers of Dâr Narbugud.Destroy fumaroles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy greater fumaroles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Donfuin can be found outside of Dâr Narbugud in Moria.

You should go to Donfuin and inform him of your success in destroying the belching fumaroles of Dâr Narbugud.Talk to Donfuin'When you travel to Dâr Narbugud, I believe you will find it filled with an unwholesome air. It is my expectation that the very air provides a lush breeding ground for the corruption that takes place in that sickly place.

'You should seek out the vents from whence the noxious air passes. If you destroy the belching mouths, perhaps the things that grow so freely amongst the gases will not find the environment so hospitable.

'I imagine that you will find great fumaroles in Dâr Narbugud, ${PLAYER}. I have studied things of this kind, and wherever there is bad air in an enclosed space such as this, a gasping vent is usually the source of the trouble.''The greater fumaroles can most likely be found throughout Dâr Narbugud, ${PLAYER}.''I take it the air of Dâr Narbugud was not to your liking, ${PLAYER}? I am not at all surprised.

'You did well to destroy the living vents that gasped the foul fumes into that sickly space. There will now be less fodder for the vile things that grow there.'Celeborn has devised a means to ensure the Globsnaga fungus never survives once the legions of the infested are destroyed.The chambers of rancour can be found in Dâr Narbugud, in the southern-most reaches of Moria's Foundations of Stone.

You should use the contents of the phial to cleanse the rancourous chambers of transformation within Dâr Narbugud.Donfuin is outside of Dâr Narbugud in Moria.

You should return to Donfuin and inform him of your success in purifying the most corrupted places in Moria.'Kind ${CLASS}, you have done much for us in these ventures to Dâr Narbugud. I see that our wishes are the same: we both desire to see the balance of Moria restored and for all the unnatural blights to be swept away.

'Please take this ere you depart. It is a phial of pure water from Galadriel's garden, clear and clean as spring rain, and blessed by my Lady ere it was passed to my hands. You may use it to purify the deadly liquid in the chambers where the Orcs undergo their transformation. 

'The roots of evil will wither and die with this draught flowing as blood in their veins. A little purity may go far in that forsaken place, ${PLAYER}. This draught of Lórien will bring an end to the fell winter of sickness and plague in Dâr Narbugud.''Please take the phial of pure water and use it to cleanse the Globsnaga fungus in the chambers of rancour in Dâr Narbugud.

The chambers can be found in the southernmost reaches of Moria's Foundations of Stone.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}! You have played a great role in our time, for Moria and for fair Lothlórien as well.

'The sickness bred by the contamination of the waters in Dâr Narbugud will not trouble us further, thanks to you and your noble companions.'One of the Nameless creatures that prowled the twisted passages of Dâr Narbugud was found carrying a strange sword-hilt, bearing an inscription in unmistakeable Sindarin letters. While this haft is now fell and cold to the touch, its history might be of interest to one who remembers its making.Celeborn can be found in Lothlórien's main city, Caras Galadhon.

You should show the corrupted hilt you have found to Celeborn, whose wisdom and long memory may dispel the mystery surrounding this artifact.Bring the hilt to Celeborn at Caras GaladhonCeleborn believes that the sword hilt will be recognizeable to someone who lives in Lothlórien. He surmises, based on the words on the handle, that the warrior of old was a loyal protector of the Golden Wood.

You should seek someone who may recognize the befouled relic.The hilt is ice-cold and gives off a fell glow, and it is blackened with the remnants of its Nameless bearer. You would cast it aside without further thought, for it is a sickening relic, but something catches your eye: Elven-script. The letters inscribed upon the hilt are clear, unfaded Sindarin. 

This artifact may have a colourful history. How did it come to live in the hands of this hideous creature? You should bring the hilt to one who may recognize it.'What treasure have you unearthed in Dâr Narbugud, ${PLAYER}? It was a keen observation that let you perceive the writing beneath the grime, for the words have lost their power and their light.

'This is a Silvan blade from the Second Age, and its script tells of sun on golden boughs and likens them to the mighty arm of a marchwarden. I would not be at all surprised if an inhabitant of Lórien knew the one who bore this sword.

'This is the blade of a guard or a warrior who drew upon the beauty and majesty of the mallorns to lend him power when he bore this blade into battle. A warrior of the woods may know this haft.''Bright were the eyes of he who bore this blade to battle long ago. Yes, I remember the sword and the bearer! He was my friend, and we went forth together into many perils.

'Seasons uncounted have turned since he departed Middle-earth to go to the Undying Lands, as is the fate of all my kin. I have remained and will watch over this land until the time of the Elves has passed.

'I have often wondered what became of him, for my heart whispered that he never came to the Sea. Did he meet his doom in Moria where the Nameless walk on black roads? Alas!'Celeborn of Lothlórien believes that the restoration of the natural world is key in the battle against the powers of evil in Middle-earth.The source of the pestilence in Moria is near the Dark Delvings at the southernmost tip of the Foundations of Stone, in a foul place called Dâr Narbugud.

Donfuin wishes you and your allies to defeat the Nameless sources of the sickness spewing from Dâr Narbugud, thus removing the threat of the fungal plague's spread.Defeat the Mistress of PestilenceDefeat the Blind OneDonfuin is outside of Dâr Narbugud in Moria.

You should tell Celeborn of your very great deed in defeating the Mistress of Pestilence in Moria.Talk to Donfuin'You have felt the malice in Dâr Narbugud during your long toils there, have you not? I suspect that you will find a great force at the heart of the evil will. Such is always the case in the black places of the world, as I am sure you have found in your many ventures.

'If you intend to complete the greater task I have given you of banishing the darkness, you must first uproot the evil that is the source of the pestilence.

'May you and your allies go well, ${PLAYER}, and do not allow your valour to waver. Those with pure hearts beating in their breasts will not be swallowed by the sickness of Moria. Defeat the menace and come back hale to allay my fears for the safety of Free Peoples.''I bid you take care, ${PLAYER}, when you face the source of the sickness in Moria. It will not be an easy task. Go to Dâr Narbugud; do your best to stand against the blight that corrupts the fiends who wish to bring harm to all that is good.''Glad am I to see you well, ${RACE}. I am heartened indeed by all that passed in Dâr Narbugud, the beating heart of corruption in Moria.

'The dwarves of the expedition will feel the good of your deed at once, for the bane of their purpose there has been felled by the might of your valiant host. You shall be honoured by the Elves also for quenching the flames of a threat that may have spread far and ruined many fair things.'Celeborn, Lord of Lothlórien, is gravely concerned by the final and most perilous threat in Moria: the plague of fungus threatening to spread with the infected Orcs as they rally to defend their caverns against the dwarves and Elves.Celeborn is in Caras Galadhon, at the heart of Lothlórien.

You should speak with Celeborn at the behest of Baranglim to gain his counsel about the final and most important task to be achieved in Moria.Talk to Celeborn at Caras GaladhonDâr Narbugud is in the Foundations of Stone in Moria, to the south-east near the Dark Delvings.

Celeborn has given you a phial of Elven light to bring to the heart of plague, sickness, and corruption within Moria.Celeborn stands at the heart of Lothlórien, in the hidden city of Caras Galadhon.

You should speak with Celeborn and share the tale of your great success in Dâr Narbugud, dealing a heavy blow to the creatures who would cover the world in sickness.Talk to Celeborn at Caras Galadhon'I find that there is always more to do if we are to keep evil at bay. Lord Celeborn wishes now to speak with you. When you are able, you should go to Caras Galadhon, the city at the heart of our realm.

'I will return to my duties of guarding our borders and watching... watching for the tides of change. You see, change comes with every passing moment, but once in an age, the flowing rivers of time will swell and flood, and things will never be as they were ere the waters came.

'This is no time for the rambling of a wary Elf, though. Lord Celeborn is afraid of what brews within Moria. Lady Galadriel fears it too. There are rumours that our stainless lands will not withstand this threat. I think you know of what I speak, but I will not darken the day further by speaking of it here.''Speak with Lord Celeborn as soon as you are able, friend. We must do our best to rid Moria of its ills. Go to Caras Galadhon, if you can.''Welcome to Caras Galadhon. A friend of Mithrandir and his Company is a friend to the Elves of Lothlórien also. My Lady spoke well of you when first she heard of your coming, but I wished to see for myself how well you served Haldir and Baranglim before employing your skills myself.

'As you have surely seen, Moria is beset with perils, but none so virulent as the disease borne hither and thither wherever the Nameless and sickly creatures prowl. My Lady and I fear that with the brewing of war, the fungus-carriers will be unleashed as the final weapon, and I do not deny that this would be a deadly blow to our stainless land.

'Please go to the cavern where the infected army amasses and bring this phial with you when you go. Use it in the darkest place, and the darkness will shrink and wither as if the full sun and fresh air were beating upon it from the above world. You must gather a full host of allies for this venture, for it will not be easy.''Gather what strength and nourishment you can while you are here, ${PLAYER}. You should prepare yourself for the death and corruption you will meet in Dâr Narbugud in Moria's Foundations of Stone.''Ah! ${PLAYER}, you return hale! You have done what few could in this day and age. Your great deeds are indeed as worthy as the rumours boldly declared. You shall have the blessing of the Elves wherever you go from this day forward. You have saved Moria, Lórien, and undoubtedly the larger world from a terrible fate.

'Alas that we cannot celebrate... not yet. My heart quails again when I look to the East. Perhaps your path will lead you thither someday....'In the Dark Delvings, the most forsaken depths of Khazad-Dûm, the Nameless hold sway over the bitter shadows. Like other creatures that hide in the Black Pit that is Moria, the Nameless dread light, but they will not turn aside from any opportunity to spread corruption and dismay. These terrible foes must be purged from the Dark Delvings before they are able to wend their way into other parts of the mines.The region of the Dark Delvings is far to the south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.

The dwarf Sigurd has challenged you to make your way into the Dark Delvings and defeat the Gurvand without the help of runes, wishing you to prove your worth as the great warrior you are rumoured to be.Defeat the Gurvand without using the rune-stonesSigurd is in the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of the Great Delvings where the Nameless roam.

Sigurd will wish to hear if you have risen to meet the challenge he gave you of slaying the Gurvand without using the runes for help.Return to Sigurd at the Twenty-first Hall'Rumours abound that you are of a tougher mould than most, ${CLASS}. I will admit that you look doughty enough, and your eyes are fiercer than many I see. Perhaps you would hold up against a most difficult foe that threatens our cause.

'There are whispers of a Nameless being in the depths of the Dark Delvings. None will travel there, for all are afraid, but here you stand, unconquered and proud. I would offer you the greatest of all the challenges I could give: will you face the Gurvand?

'And yet, merely to confront the Gurvand will be but a pittance to so mighty a ${CLASS} as yourself. If you can defeat this Nameless foe without the aid of the runes in his room, I will accept that you are as great a warrior as everyone says. You will indeed win my favour if you can manage this task, and I will give you a worthwhile reward upon your triumphant return. You should bring stout companions with you on this venture.''I am tremendously impressed! You have done credit to your fame, great credit indeed. Something troubles me still, though. I have heard your description of this foe; the Gurvand sounds like a twisted being, beyond the understanding of you or me.

'Do you think the Gurvand is gone forever? You saw him bested, I know, but my heart tells me that he will be back before long. A creature so ancient and corrupted does not often fall after one defeat. Mark my words -- he will trouble us again.''Have you defeated the Gurvand? No? Then I suggest you and your friends get to it!'In the Dark Delvings, the most forsaken depths of Khazad-dûm, the Nameless hold sway over the bitter shadows. Like other creatures that hide in the Black Pit that is Moria, the Nameless dread light, but they will not turn aside from any opportunity to spread corruption and dismay. These terrible foes must be purged from the Dark Delvings before they are able to wend their way into other parts of the mines.Gurvand is in the Dark Delvings, far to the south-east of Eilíefr's post at the Twenty-first Hall.

The dwarf Eilíefr has challenged you to make your way into the Dark Delvings and defeat the ancient Nameless creature known as the Gurvand, bringing its tongue back as a trophy when you are finished.'So you are the mighty ${CLASS} of whom everyone has spoken so well! Word of your valour and courage has reached my ears, but seeing as I am a disbelieving sort, I would like to see if you are made for the sort of challenge I have to offer you. 

'Many of us avoid the Dark Delvings where the Nameless walk. If you are truly all that they say you are, you will go there and face the creature that stands at the heart of the Delvings: the Gurvand. I want you to defeat this thing and bring me its tongue as proof that it is dead.

'This will not be an easy task, nor is it impossible. Help can be given to those who seek it. Prove yourself in this challenge of mine, and you will receive a rich reward. Oh, and...there is no shame in bringing friends with you on this venture.''A fine trophy! This beast was a wretched creature, and I am glad to hear that it is gone once and for all.'

Suddenly Eilíefr jumps and lets out an alarmed yelp.

'The tongue! It moved! The vile thing squirms even now! I do not think the Gurvand is truly dead....'In the Dark Delvings, the most forsaken depths of Khazad-dûm, the Nameless hold sway over the bitter shadows. Like other creatures that hide in the Black Pit that is Moria, the Nameless dread light, but they will not turn aside from any opportunity to spread corruption and dismay. These terrible foes must be purged from the Dark Delvings before they are able to wend their way into other parts of the mines.The Dark Delvings are far to the south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.

The dwarf Geirr has challenged you to make your way into the Dark Delvings and defeat many Nameless foes therein.Defeat enemies in the Dark Delvings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The dwarf Geirr is in the Twenty-first hall, north-west of the Great Delvings where the Nameless roam.

Geirr will wish to hear if you have been brave enough to enter the Dark Delvings and face the Nameless ones in battle.Return to Geirr at the Twenty-first Hall'Word of your renown has spread far and wide throughout these long tunnels, ${CLASS}. Aye, don't be modest -- I can see in your eyes the bright look of a valiant adventurer. I would know your ilk even without reinforcement from the rumours.

'Are you up for a small challenge? South-east of this hall lies the Dark Delvings, a terrifying place that none dare approach. A nameless malice is there, brooding in the dark, corrupt, evil, and wretched. Many footsteps and strange sounds echo from the Delvings. I think you know of what I speak. You have seen the Nameless foes, have you not?

'An adventurer such as yourself would look forward to a little dare such as the one I am about to propose: go into the Dark Delvings and slay many enemies there. Fear will not keep you from a place that all others shun. I would have the Nameless destroyed, for it would be a terrible thing if they were to spread into the mines.''I must be honest: I was not sure that you would be up for this challenge today. But I am glad to have been wrong on this occasion! Forgive me for not thinking better of you, ${PLAYER}, for the rumours of your courage were more than true. 

'Here is a token of my appreciation. I hope to see more of you in the following days, for you are quite the asset to our endeavours here.''I do not know what the creatures are that infest the Dark Delvings, but they are a threat to us all.'The forces of the Iron Crown are invading the lands of the Free Peoples.You have been instructed to defeat Black-arrows in Eregion.Defeat Black-arrows in Eregion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The forces of Angmar have marched forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. Among their most fearsome minions are the dreaded Black-arrows.

