'You should keep a wary eye open and defeat any Weavers that you see.'With their communications severed, the Orcs in the Dimrill Dale are now vulnerable. The dwarves wish to demonstrate to them how helpless they truly are.The Orc-camps Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul are to the south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Raskwith asked you to go to the three Orc-camps in the Dimrill Dale and plant dwarf-flags in each, to show the Orcs that the Dale will never be theirs.Raskwith is in Mekhem-bizru, north-west of the Orc-camps.

Raskwith will be pleased to hear that the banners have been placed in the Orc-camps.Talk to Raskwith at Mekhem-bizru'The Orcs in the Dimrill Dale are in disarray. They know not whom to listen to nor whom to trust and have even fallen to fighting each other. It is now time to show them to whom the Dale truly belongs.

'Return south-east to Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul. Find a suitable place in each and plant one of these dwarf-banners. Let them know the Dale will always belong to Khazad-dûm, and Khazad-dûm will always belong to Durin's Folk.

'When you have accomplished this, return to me. If you succeed at this, you will have certainly earned a reward.''Plant the dwarf-banners of Moria in their camps. That will show them to whom the Dale belongs.''I see the banners flying high over the camps of the Orcs. It is a fitting sign.

'You have done good work here, and I am proud to call you friend.'The forces of the Iron Crown are invading the lands of the Free Peoples.You have been instructed to defeat War-leaders in Eregion.Defeat War-leaders in Eregion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The forces of Angmar have marched forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. Among their most fearsome minions are the dreaded War-leaders.

'You should keep a wary eye open and defeat any War-leaders that you see.'Fil Gashan is the barracks and mustering point for the Orcs' invasion of Lothlórien. Hidden deep within the fiery landscape and sharing an adjacent entrance to the Forges of Khazad-dûm, Orcs train here under the watchful eye of General Talug.Fil Gashan is south-west of Anazârmekhem.

Vagun believes that the Orcs of Fil Gashan must be driven out, and that by defeating the lieutenants and taking their gear, you might be able to deceive the other Orcs.Defeat lieutenants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat chief guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Vagun is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of Fil Gashan.

You fought your way through Fil Gashan and defeated the lieutenants as you were asked. Now you should return to Vagun with your report.Talk to Vagun at Anazârmekhem'Throughout Fil Gashan, you will find the lieutenants of Talug. These Orcs are lower in the chain of Fil Gashan's leadership, but the other Orcs still look to them for guidance.

'Our goal in defeating them is two-fold. First, they are Orcs, and we must drive the usurpers out of Moria. Second, if these Orcs are respected or feared by the other Orcs, you might be able to use what you find in their keeping to fool the Orcs within Fil Gashan.

'So, if you see these lieutenants, defeat them and take what you can from them. You might find it easier. Fil Gashan can be found to the south-west of Anazârmekhem. Good luck.''Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'I will inform Teitur that this is done, and I can tell you that he will be pleased, as well. Your efforts here are doing much to stop the assault on the Elves' forest.''Fil Gashan is south-west of Anazârmekhem. Do not forget to search the bodies of the fallen lieutenants. Anything that might save your life is a good thing, I always say.'Defeat the leaders of the invasion of the Forgotten Treasury.Defeat NardurgûlDefeat FrûzgûlDefeat DarûkûrzDefeat NarghugDefeat MokzaDefeat LorzgûlDefeat the leaders of the invasion of the Forgotten Treasury.Defeat MorhûnDefeat SkûmDefeat UrauthHethuwen lacks the components she needs for a thorough study of the contents of a strange delivery from Hasta.The infected Orcs can be found south of the Shadowed Refuge. Crystal fragments can be found in the Fanged Pit, in Durin's Way, to the north-east. Venomous gredbyg can be found in the Redhorn Lodes, west of the Shadowed Refuge.

Hethuwen has asked you bring her a fungal sample from the Orcs in the Foundations of Stone, a crystal from the Fanged Pit, and a venom sac from one of the vicious gredbyg in the Redhorn Lodes.Collect a fungal sampleCollect a crystal sampleCollect a grodbog venom sacThe Shadowed Refuge can be found in the Foundations of Stone, in the south-east reaches of Moria.

You should return with the gathered samples to Hethuwen at the Shadowed Refuge.'Well, let us examine these strange specimens. In order to fully study these samples you brought, I will need some components for my experiment.

'The Orcs here in the Foundations of Stone are infected with a terrible disease; bring me a suitable sample of the fungus that consumes them. The Fanged Pit, north of here in Durin's Way, is home to a luminescent form of crystal that can often be found chipped off of greater pieces of jutting stone. Bring me one of these samples -- but beware the beast Riptalon when you are there! Lastly, the most vicious grodbog species found in the Redhorn Lodes have a rare strain of venom. You must bring me one of their venom sacs.

'Return to me once you've acquired these key materials and I will see if I can get to the bottom of Hasta's mystery.''I need Orc-fungus from the Foundations of Stone, a glowing crystal from the Fanged Pit, and grodbog-venom from the Redhorn Lodes...a sample of each, if you please.''Well done, ${PLAYER}, these should do perfectly for my study. Now then, let me get to work....'The Orcs of Moria have poured out into Fanuidhol, mustering for an assault upon the Golden Wood.Maenhador is at Talan Fanuidhol. Raingon is at Talan Gwilith, north-east of Talan Fanuidhol.

Bahanneth has asked you to aid Maenhador and Raingon with their scouting duties.Aid MaenhadorAid RaingonBahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol, south-west of Talan Gwilith.

You should return to Bahanneth and report your findings.Talk to Bahanneth at Talan Fanuidhol'${PLAYER}, I have an urgent request of you. As you undoubtedly know already, the Orcs of Moria have been roused and have poured forth into the hills of Fanuidhol. There, they are mustering for an assault upon Lothlórien.

'In order to properly prepare for such an assault, we need to know the strength of the Enemy. There are countless Orcs dwelling in the bowels of Moria, and we must know how many have been sent against us.

'Will you speak with my companion Maenhador and with Raingon, who is preparing a defence at Talan Gwilith, north-east of here? They are each concerned with specific encampments. When you have finished with their tasks, return here to me.''So you have completed your patrol, ${PLAYER}? Out of all the Orc-camps in Talan Fanuidhol, only four seem to pose any significant threat: Bolg Maufulug, Mokûrz Gundul, Drûmaudhul, and Nardur-stazg.

'You should speak again with the marchwardens here at Talan Fanuidhol and at Talan Gwilith. They will undoubtedly have tasks for you.''Speak with Maenhador here at Talan Fanuidhol and Raingon at Talan Gwilith, north-east of here. They will need aid scouting Fanuidhol.'The Orcs of Moria have poured out into Fanuidhol, mustering for an assault upon the Golden Wood.Drûmaudhul, Prakûth-fulug, Bidroi Maudhul, and Nardur-stazg all lie to the north-west of Talan Gwilith.

Raingon has asked you to scout four Orc-encampments in Fanuidhol to determine their strength: Drûmaudhul. Prakûth-fulug, Bidroi Maudhul, and Nardur-stazg.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>Scout DrûmaudhulScout Bidroi MaudhulScout Prakûth-fulugScout Nardur-stazgRaingon is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Fanuidhol.

You should return to Raingon with your report.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>Talk to Raingon at Talan Gwilith'Bahanneth sent you, ${PLAYER}? He is correct...if we are to fully prepare for the war ahead, we must know what numbers are arrayed against us. I have a task for you, if you wish to aid us.

'Journey north and west into Fanuidhol and scout the four northernmost encampments. There is a lumber camp called Drûmaudhul which lies west and a little to the north of here. Bidroi Maudhul can be found to the north of Drûmaudhul, as can Prakûth-fulug. Nardur-stazg lies to the north-west of Bidroi Maudhul and is one of the strongest encampments in Fanuidhol.

'Scout each of the encampments, then return to me. I will reward you as I may, but expect a greater reward from Bahanneth.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>'You have completed your patrol? Ah! Drûmaudhul is a strong encampment and supplies the Orcs with wood for their siege-engines, and Nardur-stazg is their chief encampment.

'You should return to Bahanneth at once with this news.''What have you found thus far? That is not much...I need you to scout all four encampments: Drûmaudhul, Bidroi Maudhul, Prakûth-fulug, and Nardur-stazg.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: While Fanuidhol Defence is active, Raingon will not be available for quest completion or comments. You will have to wait for Fanuidhol Defence to end to complete this quest.</rgb>The Orcs of Moria have poured out into Fanuidhol, mustering for an assault upon the Golden Wood.All of the Orc-encampments lie to the north of Talan Fanuidhol. Bolg Maufulug lies the furthest to the west. Golugrak is north-west of Talan Fanuidhol. Gazpush is north of Golugrak. Mokûrz Gundul is east of Gazpush.

Maenhador has asked you to scout four Orc-encampments in Fanuidhol to determine their strength: Bolg Maufulug, Golugrak, Gazpush, and Mokûrz Gundul.Scout Bolg MaufulugScout GolugrakScout GazpushScout Mokûrz GundulMaenhador is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Fanuidhol.

You should return to Maenhador with your report.Talk to Maenhador at Talan Fanuidhol'Bahanneth is correct, ${PLAYER}. If we are to fully prepare for the war ahead, we must know what numbers are arrayed against us. I have a task for you, if you wish to aid us.

'Journey north and west into Fanuidhol and scout the four southernmost encampments. The camp furthest west is called Bolg Maufulug. Almost due north-west is a smaller camp called Golugrak. North of Golugrak, you will come upon Gazpush. Finally, east of Gazpush, you will find Mokûrz Gundul.

'Scout each of the encampments, then return to me. I will reward you as I may, but expect a greater reward from Bahanneth.''You have finished your patrol? That is well.

'Of the southern camps, only Bolg Maudhul and Mokûrz Gundul pose any significant threat. You should speak with Bahanneth regarding your findings.''What have you found thus far? That is not much...I need you to scout all four encampments: Bolg Maufulug, Golugrak, Gazpush, and Mokûrz Gundul.'Fil Gashan is the barracks and mustering point for the Orcs' invasion of Lothlórien. Hidden deep within the fiery landscape and sharing an adjacent entrance to the Forges of Khazad-dûm, Orcs train here under the watchful eye of General Talug.Fil Gashan lies to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.

Vagun directed you to attempt to disable the massive alarm bells that the Orcs have placed throughout Fil Gashan. He mentioned that the sentries are good at spotting any who are not their own kind.Disable the alarms of Fil Gashan (${VALUE}/8)Vagun is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of Fil Gashan.

You attempted to disable several of the alarms. While not always successful, as Vagun had warned, the attempt is more important than the success.Talk to Vagun at Anazârmekhem'Help finally arrives and not a bit too soon. The Orcs are mustering and will soon be ready to pour forth from this place! We went within Fil Gashan only once and hid in the back, covered in armour that could have passed for Orc-make. We heard them talking and saw the giant bells they use for alarms.

'They keep sentries near the bells... good sense of smell those Orcs have, too. They also see pretty well. The alarms have a flaw, though: you can pull pins from the centre pieces and send them to ground with nary a sound.

'So it is that I set you to that task. Enter Fil Gashan, found to the south-west of Anazârmekhem, and attempt to disable the alarms there. Mind you, you may not always succeed, but the attempt must be made.''Disabling those alarms will help to reduce the response of the other Orcs within Fil Gashan and hopefully thwart any chance that they have of setting up some sort of message route for their war-host.

'Go into Fil Gashan and attempt to destroy those alarms. You can find it to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.''Excellent. Without those alarms, I am certain that you had an easier time within Fil Gashan than we did.

'Good work.'Bahanneth is concerned about the siege-parts you stole from the Orcs. Even without them, they will be able to construct primitive weapons to conduct a siege.Fanuidhol lies to the north-west of Talan Fanuidhol.

Bahanneth wants you to enter Fanuidhol and kill several of the smiths there, as well as to destroy some of the stores of weapons they have forged. The weapons can be found stored towards the back of the camp, further to the north-west.Defeat Orc-smiths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy weapon-stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol, south-east of Fanuidhol.

You should return to Bahanneth with news of your victory.Talk to Bahanneth at Talan Fanuidhol'The Orcs may not be the most powerful of foes, but they are numerous, determined, and some among their number are dangerously clever in the ways of siege-craft -- particularly when they are crafting designs supplied by the Enemy himself.

'You have stolen away many of the parts they had hoped to use in the construction of cunning engines of war, but some remain, and even without them their smiths will strive to build more primitive -- but still quite lethal -- weapons.

'I would like to see most of those Orcs defeated, for without them, their soldiers have no real hope of infiltrating the defences of our forest.''Excellent work, my friend! As long as we can continue to disrupt their preparations, the Orcs shall find their efforts to assault Lórien fruitless and most costly indeed.''The Orcs will have no hope of completing their siege-engines if their smiths have been put to the sword.'Hadroneth is worried about the mass of Orcs that have poured from the gates of Moria into the Dimrill Dale, and wants you to thin their numbers.Orcs can be found all along the road that leads through Nanduhirion, the Dimrill Dale, north-west of Talan Haldir.

Hadroneth has asked you to thin the numbers of the Orcs that have come forth from within the mountains.Defeat Orcs in Nanduhirion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hadroneth is on Talan Haldir, along the banks of Nimrodel.

The Elf Hadroneth is waiting for you to report of your success slaying the Orcs that have poured from the Gates of Moria into Nanduhirion.'I have never seen the Orcs like this, ${PLAYER}; they pour from the gates of Moria as they have not done in years, and establish camps and outposts all along the road between here and there.

'If you would be a friend of Lórien, you must help us discourage the Orcs from this endeavour. Seek out these enemies to the north-west, and defeat them wherever you find them in Nanduhirion.

'The more Orcs you slay, the safer will be the road between Lothlórien and Moria. Their boldness worries me greatly.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. We will not forget your help to us, though there be always more to do.''The Orcs have come forth from inside the mountains -- into Nanduhirion, the Dimrill Dale, to the north-west. You must slay these foes wherever you see them if you would be friend to the Elves of Lórien.'Skûmfil is nothing more than a dumping ground, a place where the fallen Orcs of Moria are discarded when they begin to reek. It is here that two foes have gathered, each intent on using the corpses found therein for their own purposes. The kergrim and other scavengers as a source of food, and the insects as a place to lay their eggs to spawn future generations.Ymar, Odmar, and Glorelloth are at the Shadowed Refuge.

Throstur informed you that the kergrim within Skûmfil are eaters of the dead. As such, they are also rife with disease and filth, and he has set his agents to the task of deciphering what ills the kergrim carry through Skûmfil.Help Ymar to control disease in SkûmfilHelp Odmar defeat the kergrim-leaders of SkûmfilHelp Glorelloth collect samples in SkûmfilThrostur is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You completed each task assigned by Ymar, Odmar and Glorelloth within Skûmfil and should now return to Throstur.Talk to Throstur at the Shadowed Refuge'The kergrim are foul creatures, consuming the dead for sustenance. How and why they found their way into Khazad-dûm, I do not know, but they are here, and something must be done about them.

'Odmar, Ymar, and Glorelloth each have tasks associated with the kergrim in Skûmfil that they may be willing to share with you. If you complete these, I will inform Veúlfur that you have done all I asked at Skûmfil.

'You can find the three of them within the bounds of the Shadowed Refuge here.''Your work here is complete in my eyes, ${PLAYER}. I will send word on to Veúlfur and inform him that you have satisfied my needs here at the Shadowed Refuge.

'You have my thanks.''Help my agents with the kergrim problem, and I will do my part and tell Veúlfur that all I needed within Skûmfil is complete.'Tuilinn is surprised that you did not know the full story of how a Man, even one as respected as Aragorn, was able to successfully court a high-born Elf-lady like Arwen.Tuilinn has sent you to three Elves who each know an aspect of the tale of the romance of Elessar and Undómiel.

From Cerin Amroth, Pennasseth can be found to the south-west at Cerin Nauth. Naeris is in the Peaceful Glade, due east. Meluibrennil is in Bain Gwaloth a short ways to the south-east.Talk to PennassethTalk to MeluibrennilTalk to NaerisTuilinn awaits you atop the flet at Cerin Amroth.

You should return to Tuilinn now that you have heard the tale of Elessar and Undómiel.Talk to Tuilinn'My name is Tuilinn. What are you called? ${PLAYER}? The name is familiar...are you a friend to Aragorn son of Arathorn? Ah yes, you helped reforge Narsil from its shards! It is a pleasure and an honour to make your acquaintance.

'I remember when all of us here at Cerin Amroth once greatly doubted his fitness to court our sweet Undómiel...but I am sure you know the tale of their romance. What? You do not? I suppose, with Elessar being as close as he is, it is not all that surprising. Nevertheless, if you are interested, you should certainly learn the tale, as it is sweet indeed.

'Oh, not from me. I have only pieces of it myself; I shall, however, send you to those from whom I learned the rest. Pennasseth, known as the Keeper of Stories, has befriended one of the visiting hobbits, along the path towards the city. Naeris, called the Guardian of Lore, can usually be found in a clearing east of here in Gelirdor, with his friend Sendiel. Meluibrennil, currently visiting the lovely garden of Santhirwen, south of here, helped care for Arwen Undómiel when she was young.''You have learned the tale? It is sad, but beautiful, is it not? I hear that Arwen now resides again with her father in Imladris, awaiting the day when Aragorn claims his rightful inheritance.''Gladly will I share what I know of the tale of Aragorn and my dear little Arwen. Aragorn, called Elessar after the green Elf-stone given him by the Lady Galadriel herself, was just shy of his fiftieth year; still a brash youngling. He was weary, having been long fighting and travelling throughout many kingdoms, and had stopped in Lórien on his way back to Rivendell from the borders of the Black Land of Mordor. The Lady of the Golden Wood insisted that he cast off his ragged travelling apparel and dressed him in silver, white, and Elven grey, such that he appeared almost more than a Man -- nearer to an Elf-lord from the Isles of the West, tall and stern.

'At that moment, Arwen Undómiel, the Lady of Imladris, saw him again for the first time in nearly thirty years. At that moment, indeed, was her choice made: to follow, await, love, protect, and honour Elessar, and share with him the Doom of Men.

'They had but a brief season to wander together through the woods and glades of Lothlórien. The hill of Cerin Amroth was their most particularly beloved place: that is where they wandered barefoot through the blossoms of niphredil and elanor, and it was there that they finally plighted their troth and sealed their fate.''Mae govannen. I am Naeris, the keeper of the histories of the Galadhrim. I have memorized the lays and poems, the lineages, the heraldry, and the great martial and political deeds of our people. How may I be of service? Ah, I see; a tale of recent days, then.

'I have read a tale recorded by Elrond Halfelven of the solemn discourse he held with the son of Arathorn, fifteenth Chieftain of the Dúnedain. The Lord of Imladris had read the heart of Aragorn and seen the new-born love there for Arwen Undómiel. He told Aragorn of the great doom that awaited him: either he would rise above all his lineage since the days of Elendil the Tall, father of Isildur, or he would plunge into darkness with all the remnants of his kin; also, that in the many years of trial that lay before him, he would neither take a wife nor bind a woman's troth to himself, until he should be found worthy of doing so. Elrond further warned Aragorn that the Evenstar of her people was too far above him, and he too young for her. He explained how the long life and youth of the Eldar were hers while her father stayed here, and that she would be able to follow him into the West when he should go. Were she to choose to bind herself to a mortal, her doom would be bleak; her life, shortened. She would never marry a mortal, unless he was king of both Arnor and Gondor.

'The next day, Aragorn son of Arathorn took his leave of his mother, Gilraen, and left the Last Homely House to go forth into the wilds; he was soon, however, seen once more, here in Lothlórien. It is an abiding sorrow and grief to many of us that young Arwen Undómiel will not come with us when we go. Now, I tire...hold this tale close to your heart; consider it, learn from it. Farewell, patient ${RACE}.''Mae govannen, my good ${CLASS}. I am Pennasseth, though I am sometimes called the Keeper of Stories. Have you a tale to share? Ah, a tale to request! And none less than that of Aragorn and Arwen -- wonderful.

'I first met Aragorn when he was a very small child under the care of Elrond Halfelven, with whom I too was staying. His mother, Gilraen the Fair, brought him thither to live when he was but two years of age, his father Arathorn having been recently killed on campaign when an Orc-arrow pierced his eye. Estel, as Aragorn was then known, was a sweet child, serious and intelligent, with no awareness of his kingly lineage -- he would not be given that until his twentieth year -- and we all doted upon him.

'Since its occurrence during the Elder Days, we have sung of the great romance of the Man Beren One-hand and the Elf-princess Lúthien, also called Tinúviel or Nightingale. I tell you this because I know of the first time Elessar set eyes upon the beautiful Undómiel: he was singing of Beren's first view of dancing Lúthien, clad in silver and blue, dark-haired and gem-crowned. Just then, Arwen Undómiel, clad and bejewelled in nearly the same manner, walked before him; believing himself the recipient of a vision, Aragorn called out -- just as Beren had -- "Tinúviel! Tinúviel!" Is that not a sweet tale?

'No, he hadn't ever met her before, despite the fact that she is Elrond's child. Why? It is simple: she had been living here in Lothlórien, for this is the land of her mother's kin.''You should speak with the Elves I told you of, for they can provide you many pieces of the tale of Arwen and Elessar.''I have told you what I may of Elessar and Undómiel...You should return to Tuillin upon Cerin Amroth.''I have told you what I may of Elessar and Undómiel...You should return to Tuillin upon Cerin Amroth.''I have told you what I may of Elessar and Undómiel...You should return to Tuillin upon Cerin Amroth.'You have been charged with the friendly challenge of convincing Aragorn to return to Cerin Amroth.Milwen can be found on the western side of the hill of Cerin Amroth, by the arches. Cerin Amroth is north of Caras Galadhon.

Miluiel has sent you to retrieve a bloom of elanor from Milwen at Cerin Amroth, in order to convince Aragorn to return to the hill despite his mysterious refusal to do so.Talk to Milwen in Cerin AmrothAragorn is at the Company's Pavilion inside Caras Galadhon, south of Cerin Amroth.

You have been given a bloom of elanor to give to Aragorn, and Milwen is certain that it will convince him to return to the hill.Miluiel is outside the Company's Pavilion, in Caras Galadhon.

Aragorn has given his reasons for not returning to Cerin Amroth, and you should tell them now to Miluiel.Talk to Miluiel'Something strikes me as odd about Aragorn Elessar, ${PLAYER}. I received a message from Milwen at Cerin Amroth requesting his presence, and he declined. He was very polite, but I do not understand why he would not wish to return there. The rest of his Company has spent some time at Cerin Amroth in leisure, but he has not done so.

'Perhaps he needs a reminder of the beauty of the hill. Travel to Cerin Amroth and retrieve a bloom of elanor from Milwen. Bring it back here and give it to Aragorn in the Company's Pavilion. He will surely agree that the beauty of Cerin Amroth is such that he must return there.

'You will find Milwen by the arches on the western side of the hill of Cerin Amroth, north of Caras Galadhon.''Well, this is certainly a friendly challenge, ${PLAYER}. I will give you a bloom of elanor possessing such beauty that Aragorn Elessar will be captivated at once and will have no choice but to return.

'I must confess I can think of no reason for him to decline my invitation here. He seemed to be quite happy during his prior visits. It is a mystery I cannot unravel.'

With a smile, Milwen hands you a bloom of the elanor that grows upon the hill.

'Bring that to Aragorn in the Company's Pavilion in Caras Galadhon, ${PLAYER}, and he will hasten to gaze upon the hill of Cerin Amroth again!''Well? Did you succeed in my friendly challenge?'

Miluiel listens to your description of your encounter with Aragorn, and his face falls.

'I had no idea, ${PLAYER}. I did not suspect that Aragorn would have such a reason for not returning to Cerin Amroth. I... I am filled with regret for the asking!

'And yet my heart tells me that Aragorn Elessar will one day walk again among the trees, and climb the hill of Cerin Amroth, and stand there again in happiness. Will it be before his long road is ended? I cannot say.

'I thank you for this, ${PLAYER}.''I will be surprised if Aragorn does not return to Cerin Amroth before night falls again, ${PLAYER}, once you give him that bloom of elanor. Look for him in the Company's Pavilion, inside Caras Galadhon.''Cerin Amroth is north of Caras Galadhon. Speak with Milwen on the western side of the hill, by the arches, and she will give you a bloom of elanor. Its beauty will be such that Aragorn cannot possibly refuse to return to Cerin Amroth!''That bloom of elanor is just the thing to make Aragorn reconsider his refusal to return to Cerin Amroth, ${PLAYER}. Now bring it to him, and you will see that I am right!''Thank you for bringing me this bloom of elanor, ${PLAYER}. It will be a reminder to me of the happier days for which I walk this long road.''Welcome, ${PLAYER}, to Caras Galadhon! My company has been given this pavilion for our use, but I have not seen many of them today. Just young Peregrin, and he seems comfortable enough.'

You hand him the bloom of elanor, and a cloud passes in front of his face; for a moment Aragorn seems to see only the golden flower. Then the cloud passes, and Aragorn once again meets your gaze.

'My heart will dwell always on Cerin Amroth, ${PLAYER}, and the memory of those fair days is pleasant; thought of them keeps my feet walking the long road. I will not return to Cerin Amroth until the long road is ended, whether it be at the end of this journey or the longest. Tell Miluiel it is not despite the beauty of Cerin Amroth that I stay away, but because of it. But my heart sang when I was there, as it always did, and always will.'

Aragorn looks again at the bloom of elanor, and is transported to some distant memory; he knows you not, and you feel you have an answer for Miluiel.Vile foes, both beast and spirit, haunt the flooded depths of the Water-wheels.Defeat CaerlûgSlay Spit-tailOrcs gather beneath several banners, but flock towards a single cause. This is disconcerting for the dwarves, and the intent of the war-host of Moria spurs the staunchest of Durin's Folk to action against the Orcs in the halls they have claimed for many years.Narfi's brethren can be found at the Orc-Watch and Anazârmekhem, south-west of the Twenty-first Hall where Narfi holds his post.

Narfi has asked you to visit his brothers, Avar, Pálmar, and Teitur at the Orc-watch and Anazârmekhem and learn what assistance they need.Complete Avar's tasks in the Grand StairComplete Pálmar's tasks in the Forges of Khazad-dûmComplete Teitur's tasks within Fil GashanNarfi is at the Twenty-first Hall, north-east of the Orc-watch and Anazârmekhem.

After many difficult forays into the very heart of the Orc-strongholds of Moria, you have had decisive victories and thwarted the creatures' attempts to make a devastating blow upon the Elves of Lothlórien.Talk to Narfi at the Twenty-first Hall'My scouts have sent me rumours of a foe named Mazog giving orders to the forces of evil in Moria. I would hazard a guess that they mean to make war to the east, burning through the forest as they go. This must not be allowed to take place... not while I draw breath, nor any of the dwarves here in Moria.

'Too long have we been exiled from this place, and too long will we suffer if the Elves are harmed because we were away. I have sent my brothers below to scout two locations in which we have seen greater numbers of Orcs.

'The first of them is at the Orc-watch, south-west from here. You will want to go there and speak with Avar, the eldest. My second brother is at Anazârmekhem and goes by the name of Pálmar. The youngest, Teitur, is also somewhere in Anazârmekhem. When you have done all that they ask, return to me.''You will find Avar first at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Twenty-first Hall. He watches over the gathered troops within the Grand Stair. Next, seek out Pálmar at Anazârmekhem; he watches the Orcs work tirelessly in the Forges of Khazad-dûm. Last, speak with Teitur at Anazârmekhem and ask him to inform you of Fil Gashan, where an Orc-general gathers an army and prepares his host for battle.

'Make haste, ${PLAYER}. There is no time to lose.''There are few words more important to the dwarves than respect and honour. You have honour in abundance, ${PLAYER}, and have thus earned our utmost respect. Your tales will be sung in our annals, lest we forget the great service done for the dwarves and Elves in this difficult time.

'With this great duty fulfilled, I tell you that I am indebted to you greatly, as are all the free folk who dwell in these great halls.'Angmar's forces cover the Ettenmoors, and you are here to assist the Free Peoples in gaining a foothold on this battlefield. Find and defeat the Enemy where they travel throughout the Ettenmoors.Defeat the forces of AngmarAngmar's forces cover the Ettenmoors, and you are here to assist the Free Peoples in gaining a foothold on this battlefield. Find and defeat the Enemy where they travel throughout the Ettenmoors.Complete the previous deed.Defeat the enemies of the Free Peoples.Defeat the forces of AngmarAngmar's forces cover the Ettenmoors, and you are here to assist the Free Peoples in gaining a foothold on this battlefield. Find and defeat the Enemy where they travel throughout the Ettenmoors.Complete the previous deedDefeat the enemies of the Free PeoplesDefeat the forces of AngmarAngmar's forces cover the Ettenmoors, and you are here to assist the Free Peoples in gaining a foothold on this battlefield. Find and defeat the Enemy where they travel throughout the Ettenmoors.Complete the previous deedDefeat the enemies of the Free PeoplesDefeat the forces of AngmarThe Sword-hall of Dol Guldur is presided over by many champions, who train the soldiers of the Enemy.Defeat UrcheronDefeat CarchrienDefeat DurkârSammath Gûl is a place of terror, inhabited by the sorcerer Gorothúl and the dread spirits which serve him.Defeat UrchírDefeat AlagossírDefeat GorothúlThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Defeat Black-arrows in EregionDefeat Black-arrows in EregionThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Black-arrows in EregionDefeat Black-arrows in EregionThe armies of Angmar march forth from the 