You should speak with Raingon to prepare the defences for battle.Raingon has asked you to defeat the attackers out of Fanuidhol at both Talan Gwilith and Talan Fanuidhol, while protecting the Elven soldiers.Fanuidhol attackers defeated (${VALUE}/30)Raingon is at Talan Gwilith.

With the assault turned aside, you should speak with Raingon.'You have come none too soon, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs have been launching small assaults against us of late, and our scouts have seen another raiding party heading this way.

'I need you at the base of these telain to help our soldiers on the ground drive off the Orcs with minimal casualties. We cannot afford to lose any more of our people, or we will be left shorthanded when their true assaults begin.''The Orcs come even now! Prepare our defences and reinforce our guards where you may! The Orcs will attack both here and at Talan Fanuidhol!''The marchwardens tell me that you have acquitted yourself well during the recent skirmish. Allow me to offer you a token of our appreciation.''Fil Gashan is the barracks and training grounds of the Orcs in Moria. Within those walls, a fearsome general has been readying his troops for an assault upon the Elves of Lothlórien to the east of Khazad-dûm. Brogur and Bósi's dwarves, wishing to reclaim Moria, aim to prevent this at any cost, for they would see the Elves and dwarves reinstate old alliances for the good of both.General Talug can be found in Fil Gashan, far to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall.

The dwarf Eilíefr has asked you to defeat General Talug to demonstrate your excellence, and return with his ring when you are done.'So you are the mighty ${CLASS} of whom everyone has spoken so well! Word of your valour and courage has reached my ears, but seeing as I am a disbelieving sort, I would like to see if you are made for the sort of challenge I have to offer you. 

'Many of us are hoping to thwart the Orcs from their evil intentions to attack the Golden Wood of the Elves. If you are truly all that they say you are, you will go and face the leader that stands at the heart of Fil Gashan; his name is General Talug. I want you to defeat this Orc and bring me his ring as proof that he is dead.

'This will not be an easy task, nor is it impossible. Prove yourself in this challenge of mine, and you will receive a rich reward. Oh, and...there is no shame in bringing friends with you on this venture.''A fine trophy! This Orc was too dangerous to be allowed to live, and I am glad to hear that he is gone once and for all.'

Eilíefr looks long at the ring you have brought him, his brow creased with concern.

'General Talug's ring feels strangely warm, ${PLAYER}, even though the air is chill. It remembers its master. I wonder if Talug is truly dead....'Fil Gashan is the barracks and training grounds of the Orcs in Moria. Within those walls, a fearsome general has been readying his troops for an assault upon the Elves of Lothlórien to the east of Khazad-dûm. Brogur and Bósi's dwarves, wishing to reclaim Moria, aim to prevent this at any cost, for they would see the Elves and dwarves reinstate old alliances for the good of both.Fil Gashan is south-west of the Twenty-first Hall. 

The dwarf Geirr has challenged you to make your way into Fil Gashan and defeat many Orcs therein.Kill enemies in Fil Gashan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The dwarf Geirr is in the Twenty-first hall, north-east of Fil Gashan

Geirr will wish to hear if you have been brave enough to enter Fil Gashan and face the Orcs in battle.Return to Geirr at the Twenty-first Hall'Word of your renown has spread far and wide throughout these long tunnels, ${CLASS}. Aye, don't be modest -- I can see in your eyes the bright look of a valiant adventurer. I would know your ilk even without reinforcement from the rumours.

'Are you up for a small challenge? South-west of the Twenty-first Hall, the forces of Fil Gashan are plotting an assault against our Elf-neighbours in Lothlórien, and this must not be allowed to come about. We are doing all that we can to stop them, but I bet you would like to be involved, outsider though you are.

'An adventurer such as yourself would look forward to a little dare such as the one I am about to propose: go into Fil Gashan and slay as many Orcs as you can. They are many; ever do their numbers swell, and ever does their threat increase.''I must be honest: I was not sure that you would be up for this challenge today. But I am glad to have been wrong on this occasion! Forgive me for not thinking better of you, ${PLAYER}, for the rumours of your courage were more than true. 

'Here is a token of my appreciation. I hope to see more of you in the following days, for you are quite the asset to our endeavours here.''What are you still doing here? There are enemies to be dealt with in Fil Gashan.'Fil Gashan is the barracks and training grounds of the Orcs in Moria. Within those walls, a fearsome general has been readying his troops for an assault upon the Elves of Lothlórien to the east of Khazad-dûm. Brogur and Bósi's dwarves, wishing to reclaim Moria, aim to prevent this at any cost, for they would see the Elves and dwarves reinstate old alliances for the good of both.Fil Gashan is far to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall, and General Talug can be found in the depths of that place.

Sigurd has challenged you to use stealth and wit to conquer General Talug, the leader of a great Orc-host, without defeating too many of his sentries.Defeat General TalugSigurd awaits news of your foray in the Twenty-first Hall, north-east of Fil Gashan.

General Talug has fallen by your hand and you have successfully moved through the uruk sentries without being much detected. Sigurd will wish to hear if you have met all the terms of his difficult challenge.Return to Sigurd at the Twenty-first Hall'Rumours abound that you are of a tougher mould than most, ${CLASS}. I will admit that you look doughty enough, and your eyes are fiercer than many I see. Perhaps you would hold up against a most difficult foe that threatens our cause.

'I have heard that there is a deadly foe who leads the rabble in Fil Gashan, an Orc named General Talug. I would offer you the greatest of all the challenges I could give: will you face this enemy?

'And yet, merely to confront General Talug will be but a pittance to so mighty a ${CLASS} as yourself. If you seek a true challenge, you will be careful not to kill too many of Talug's sentries. There are tools in Fil Gashan to help you with this task, but if you can pull this off, I will be very impressed. You should be sure to bring stout companions on this venture.''I am tremendously impressed! You have done credit to your fame, great credit indeed. Something troubles me still, though. By your description of this foe, it sounds to me like evil will not be held at bay for long in Fil Gashan.

'Do you think Talug is gone forever? You saw him bested, I know, but my heart tells me that he will be back before long. A creature so hard and wicked does not often fall after one defeat. Mark my words -- there will be trouble again soon....''General Talug still lives? Unforgivable! Get back out there and defeat him!'Bregradel has challenged you to prove your familiarity with Caras Galadhon in a race through the trees.You are seeking the flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth.Find the flet-runner on Telain GlorellothComplete the challenge in timeThe flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth is waiting to speak with you.Talk to the flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth'Celechest gave you too easy a challenge, ${PLAYER}. You will not find mine so simple!

'Find the flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth with all speed. Do you know the city well enough to find the quickest path? We will see!''Can it be? You have managed to make it here in time? Astounding!''Is the way of the ${CLASS} to waste time in this way? You will not reach the flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth in time if you do not hurry.'Lagordal has challenged you to prove your familiarity with Caras Galadhon in a race through the trees.You are seeking the flet-runner on a large, high flet of Telain Neduil.Find the flet-runner on the large high flet belonging to Telain NeduilThe flet-runner on Telain Neduil is waiting to speak with you.Talk to the flet-runner on Telain Neduil'You think you have what it takes to be a flet-runner, ${PLAYER}? I do not know that you are familiar enough with Caras Galadhon or have the fleetness that it requires!

'Prove to me that you do by making your way to the flet-runner on the larger of the high flets of Telain Neduil and with time to spare!''You made it here in time, ${PLAYER}! I did not think it would be so!''Why do you delay? Think you that the time is more than sufficient? If you are not correct, you will never make it in time to the flet-runner on the large high flet belonging to Telain Neduil.'Leginiel has challenged you to prove your familiarity with Caras Galadhon in a race through the trees.The flet-runner you are seeking is by the Caras Galadhon Stable-master.Find the flet-runner by the Stable-masterThe flet-runner by the Stable-master is waiting to speak with you.Talk to the flet-runner by the Stable-master'You believe you have the awareness of Caras Galadhon and the quickness to be named a flet-runner? I and my friends will be the judge of that. Can you complete my challenge?

'Reach the flet-runner by the Caras Galadhon Stable-master with utmost haste, and we will see!''Very good, ${PLAYER}. You have impressed me with your quickness and knowledge of the city.''Time is wasting, ${PLAYER}! You are seeking the flet-runner by the Caras Galadhon Stable-master!'Lintwen has challenged you to prove your familiarity with Caras Galadhon in a race through the trees.You are seeking the flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn.Find the flet-runner outside the House of CelebornThe flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn is waiting to speak with you.Talk to the flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn'If you are truly worthy of being named a flet-runner, you will be able to make your way to the flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn in any time I name, will you not, ${PLAYER}?

'For what are you waiting? Begin!''I am beside myself with surprise, ${PLAYER}, that you have made it here in time...but you have done so!''Why do you delay? I will give you no additional time to find the flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn!'Defeat Orcs in the Grand Stair.Defeat Orcs in the Grand StairDefeat Orcs in the Grand Stair.Defeat Orcs in the Grand StairThe Forges of Khazad-dûm, once a glorious smith-hall for the dwarves of Moria, have fallen into evil hands. The Forges now serve the Orc masters of Moria and are used to build all manner of weapons and war-machines for an assault against fair Lothlórien. Brogur and Bósi's dwarves, wishing to reclaim Moria, aim to prevent this at any cost, for they would see the Elves and dwarves reinstate old alliances for the good of both.The Forges of Khazad-dûm are to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall.

The dwarf Sigurd has challenged you to fight your way to the Orc Kranklûk. Narkû, who stands between you and your intended quarry, will undoubtedly alert Kranklûk that you are coming. You will have a limited amount of time in which to accomplish your task after the warning goes out.Defeat Narkû to alert Kranklûk of your presenceKranklûk is in the heart of the Forges of Khazad-Dûm.

Narkû has been defeated and Kranklûk is alerted of your presence. Sigurd believes that Kranklûk is the driving force in the Forges of Khazad-dûm; he wants you to defeat your foe to hinder the efforts of the Orcs.Defeat Kranklûk before the time runs outSigurd is in the Twenty-first Hall, north-east of the Forges of Khazad-dûm where the Orcs hold their camp.

Sigurd will wish to hear if you have risen to meet the challenge he gave you of slaying Kranklûk in the allotted time.Return to Sigurd at the Twenty-first Hall'Rumours abound that you are of a tougher mould than most, ${CLASS}. I will admit that you look doughty enough, and your eyes are fiercer than many I see. Perhaps you would hold up against a most difficult foe that threatens our cause.

