vance.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat War-leaders in ForochelDefeat War-leaders in ForochelThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat War-leaders in ForochelDefeat War-leaders in ForochelThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat War-leaders in ForochelDefeat War-leaders in ForochelThe Free Peoples of Middle-earth must be made to suffer. Force them to bend to the will of the Great Eye and the Iron Crown.Defeat Wardens in ForochelDefeat Wardens in ForochelWardens in Forochel must die!Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Wardens in ForochelDefeat Wardens in ForochelWardens in Forochel must die!Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Wardens in ForochelDefeat Wardens in ForochelWardens in Forochel must die!Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Wardens in ForochelDefeat Wardens in ForochelThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Defeat Weavers in ForochelDefeat Weavers in ForochelThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Weavers in ForochelDefeat Weavers in ForochelThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Weavers in ForochelDefeat Weavers in ForochelThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Weavers in ForochelDefeat Weavers in ForochelThe armies of Angmar march forth from the gates of Carn Dûm. It is up to the heroes of the Free Peoples to halt their advance.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Weavers in ForochelDefeat Weavers in ForochelIn the deepest dark of Moria there is a place where the only light that shone emanated from dwarf-lamps and luminescent fungus. Now, these delvings are dim and darker than ever and home to creatures that exist in nightmares. Yet here they are, and Veúlfur's agents sent to the Shadowed Refuge draw little comfort in knowing that there is something within the Dark Delvings that commands the Orcs to poison themselves in a manner that gives them over to some greater will.The Dark Delvings lie far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Pentlenn asked you to enter the Dark Delvings and collect the fractured and shattered runes there in an effort to restore their light.'In the darkness, nameless things watch us. I have seen them, but with light we can defend ourselves. I have seen savagery in my time, but these Nameless do not turn back from the light. I think this is because the lamps once filled with the power of light are diminished.

'I wish for you to enter the Dark Delvings and collect up the shattered and fractured runes found within, return them to me, and I will see if I can repair them.

'You will find the Dark Delvings far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.''I will begin my efforts to restore these runes immediately. I thank you for all that you have done, ${PLAYER}.'Someone has posted a task to deliver broken metal clubs to them. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire broken metal clubs.Wanted: Broken metal clubs taken from the defeated enemies of the Galadhrim.Wanted: Broken metal clubs taken from the defeated enemies of the Galadhrim.You have turned in a laudable number of broken metal clubs.Someone has posted a task to deliver gorgeous ears to them. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous ears.Wanted: Gorgeous ears from enemy beasts found in Lothlórien and the Dimrill Dale.Wanted: Gorgeous ears from enemy beasts found in Lothlórien and the Dimrill Dale.You have turned in a worthy collection of gorgeous ears.Someone has posted a task to deliver gorgeous fur to them. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous furs.Wanted: Gorgeous fur from enemy beasts found in Lothlórien and the Dimrill Dale.Wanted: Gorgeous fur from enemy beasts found in Lothlórien and the Dimrill Dale.You have turned in a worthy collection of gorgeous furs.Someone has posted a task to deliver gorgeous sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous sword sheaths.Wanted: Gorgeous sword sheaths taken from the defeated enemies of the Galadhrim.Wanted: Gorgeous sword sheaths taken from the defeated enemies of the Galadhrim.You have turned in a respectable number of gorgeous sword sheaths.Someone has posted a task to deliver nasty skin to them. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire nasty skins.Wanted: Nasty skin from enemy beasts found in Lothlórien and the Dimrill Dale.Wanted: Nasty skin from enemy beasts found in Lothlórien and the Dimrill Dale.You have turned in a pile of nasty skins.Fil Gashan is the barracks and mustering point for the Orcs' invasion of Lothlórien. Hidden deep within the fiery landscape and sharing an adjacent entrance to the Forges of Khazad-dûm, Orcs train here under the watchful eye of General Talug.Fil Gashan lies to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.

Úlfur told you that he is trying to devise a counter to the offensive the Orcs have planned against Lothlórien, but he needs more information to create an effective one. He asked you to search through Fil Gashan for any signs of the Orcs' plans.'I have been trying to piece together the Orcs' attack-plans from small scraps and naught more. Now I hear that you may be making a foray into Fil Gashan, and I ask you sincerely to help me with this task.

'The Orcs' orders are scattered throughout Fil Gashan, each telling one group or another what it is to do when they leave Khazad-dûm to the east. If we can gather enough of these plans, then I can devise a strong counter to theirs.

'If you happen upon any of their plans while making your way through Fil Gashan, pick them up and bring them to me. You can find their encampment to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.''Yes, yes, these papers will do nicely.

'Ha! They seem to think that they can use some of the old channels to move their larger companies and arms through.

'Already my plans seem more clear. I am in your debt, ${RACE}. I will see that Teitur is told of all your help.'Defeat Glow-worms in the Dark Delvings.Defeat Glow-worms in the Dark DelvingsDefeat Glow-worms in the Dark Delvings.Defeat Glow-worms in the Dark DelvingsHaldir of Lórien has sent you to the aid of Hrólfur in Moria, a deed that may in turn provide some security for the Elves. Hrólfur and Haldir hope to see the legendary mirrors of Lumul-nar functioning as they did long ago, in Durin's day.Lumul-nar is in Zirakzigil, north and slightly east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Hrólfur, at the bidding of the Elves, has asked you to investigate Lumul-nar to discover why the light-sources no longer throw their beams through the dark halls of Khazad-dûm.Search Lumul-nar for informationHrólfur stands at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, south and slightly west of Lumul-nar in Moria.

You should bring the ancient records of the mirrors to Hrólfur, along with the news that you have been able to restore them to their former state.'The folly of the Elves has made me forget that they have walked this Middle-earth for years uncounted, and that those from the holly-lands were counted friends in friendlier times. Lumul-nar! My eyes water to think of Moria aglow, as the Elves apparently saw it when they came. Forgive my ungenerous words towards the folk of Lórien.

'Do you wish to help us in our need? My dwarves are occupied with solving an alarming summons that may mean our very survival -- I have not a dwarf to spare. Would you go to Lumul-nar and see for yourself why the lights do not shine? You should bring a small company of stout fellows with you.''Did you find anything of value in Lumul-nar, the Hall of Mirrors? Lumul-nar is in Zirakzigil to the north and east of here.''What is this book? Bless my beard! I cannot believe our luck. This book... this book will help us to understand so much of the lore that was lost when Durin's folk were driven from these halls.

'I am deeply indebted to you, ${PLAYER}, and to Lord Celeborn for instigating this fruitful investigation. I hope that we may all benefit from this discovery, as was Celeborn's wish.'The Halls of Crafting supply Mazog's forces with weapons. Any information regarding how they are creating weapons so quickly would be vital in bringing about the Orc-lord's downfall.Collect overflowing supply-boxCollect odd-shaped supply-boxCollect leaky supply-boxCollect cracked supply-boxCollect covered supply-boxMany Orc-warriors guard the Halls of Crafting against reclamation by the dwarves of the Iron Garrison.Defeat melee Orcs in the Halls of CraftingMany Orc-warriors guard the Halls of Crafting against reclamation by the dwarves of the Iron Garrison.Defeat melee Orcs in the Halls of CraftingNot every Orc in the Halls of Crafting is foolish enough to engage a stronger foe in melee combat.Defeat ranged Orcs in the Halls of CraftingNot every Orc in the Halls of Crafting is foolish enough to engage a stronger foe in melee combat.Defeat ranged Orcs in the Halls of CraftingThe wisdom of Baranglim, a watchful scout of the Galadhrim, warns that the movements of the Orcs indicate organized leadership of the war-force that brews in the Halls of Crafting in Moria.Thaguzg can be found deep within the Halls of Crafting, in the southern reaches of Moria's Flaming Deeps.

Baranglim has asked you to defeat Thaguzg when you venture into the Halls of Crafting. Without his leadership, the Orcs will surely despair of their plot.Defeat ThaguzgBaranglim can be found outside the Halls of Crafting in the Flaming Deeps.

You should hasten to Baranglim to inform him of Thaguzg's defeat.Talk to Baranglim'I am glad Haldir sent you my way, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for offering to share the burdens that have weighed upon me since first we learned of what stirred in the Halls of the Dwarves. I have observed a rousing of Orcs from Moria as has not been seen in many a long day.

'In the Halls of Crafting, a great leader of the Enemy's forces is overseeing the war and the gathering of foes. They would be naught but a mindless rabble if there were no greater leaders among them, so I must assume that there is one around whom the stormcloud rallies.

'The Orcs speak his name with fear when they do not perceive our watchfulness. He is Thaguzg. It is a name I do not like to speak. You should defeat this foe ere you partake in the cleansing of the Halls of Crafting. I know it will not be easy, for his minions are strong; therefore he will be mighty. You should bring many friends with you on this venture, and may you return in good health to look upon our fair lands again.''Cruel Thaguzg will surely be found in the Halls of Crafting in Moria. You should travel there when you have gathered strong allies to your side.''You have done well indeed, ${PLAYER}! It is more than I dared to hope. Glad I am to see you well upon your return, with no grievous wounds. You have the thanks of the Galadhrim.'Baranglim of Lórien, a perceptive scout, has theories about the movements and activities of the Orcs in the Halls of Crafting. He believes that war is brewing and that the Orcs are producing a great store of armour, weapons, and vile draughts within Moria.Baranglim can be found in the Flaming Deeps of Moria, near the Halls of Crafting.

You should go to Baranglim and speak with him about what must be done to weaken the Orc-forces rallying to assault Lothlórien.Talk to BaranglimThe Halls of Crafting is in the southern reaches of the Flaming Deeps of Moria, near Fil Gashan.

Baranglim has given you an Elf-stone to place in the Halls of Crafting. If you drive out the enemies and place the stone there, the Orcs will fear to return again.Place the Elf-stone in the Halls of CraftingHaldir is upon his talan on the banks of the Nimrodel, in Lothlórien.

You should speak with Haldir and tell him all that you saw and achieved in the Halls of Crafting.'My friend Baranglim has watchful eyes and a wise heart. He has seen much, and I know that Celeborn has taken counsel with him recently regarding the Enemy's activity on the borders of Lórien.  Baranglim has gone to Moria to see what can be seen.

'Rumour has reached us of a great rousing of a war-force out of Moria. The Orcs have taken the Halls of Crafting, and use the forges of the dwarves to brew war. You should seek Baranglim in Moria, and aid him. I know he made for the Flaming Deeps.''Baranglim is in the Flaming Deeps of Moria, near the Halls of Crafting. You should go to him and hear what he has to say, for he has quick eyes and a perceptive mind.''Well met, ${PLAYER}. I have been expecting you since my counsel with Lord Celeborn. Haldir has told you a little of our plight, has he not? I will continue the story.

'Not long ago, a strange company came under our protection. They passed through Moria and brought behind them a trail of bold and angry Orcs. Our foes rally at many outposts on our borders. They have great strength and are driven by bitter malice. Their armour is thick, such as we have not seen since the dwarves wore the armour of Durin's time, and their weapons are hard and cruel.

'I believe they are using the Halls of Crafting in Moria to produce great stores of tools to assist them in the war. Lord Celeborn agrees, and we fear for ourselves and for the dwarves. Will you go to the source and banish the evil from that place? You will need stout allies to aid you on this venture. Take this Elf-stone; if you defeat our enemies and place the Elf-stone there, they will fear to return.''Do not tarry overlong, ${PLAYER}, for haste is needed if we are to defeat the enemies who are fueling the war. Enter the Halls of Crafting through the door to my left.''I thought that it would be so! I am glad your venture was not in vain, and that you escaped from the peril unharmed. Lady Galadriel made a subtle remark about your coming to our lands, and I discerned from her words that you were a doer of great deeds. I see that you will have much influence over this harrowing time, and that gives me hope.

'I was sure you would rise to this challenge admirably, and you did so. You have my thanks. A burden has been lifted from my mind.'The wisdom of Baranglim, a watchful scout of the Galadhrim, warns that the movements of the Orcs indicates organized leadership of the war-force that brews in the Halls of Crafting in Moria.Âmbal and Bashkuga can surely be found in the Halls of Crafting in Moria, found in the southern reaches of the Flaming Deeps near Fil Gashan.

Baranglim has asked you to defeat Âmbal and Bashkuga, the expert Orc-artisans in the Halls of Crafting, for they cannot be allowed to produce more weapons of war to be used against dwarves and Elves alike.Defeat BashkugaDefeat ÂmbalBaranglim stands outside the entrance to the Halls of Crafting, in the Flaming Deeps.

You should speak with Baranglim and inform him of your success against the masterminds of the Halls of Crafting.Talk to Baranglim'Many have made the mistake of believing Orcs to be mindless, useless war-mongers, but it is Elves they take after, shaped in a darker likeness of ourselves. It is true that many lack true cunning or skill, but some Orcs are foes to be reckoned with. These are keen of mind and can be brilliant in their efforts to cover the world in darkness.

'I believe that the Orcs in the Halls of Crafting are of this nature. That place is rife with an abundance of tools, and it is just the sort of place a fertile Orc-mind could use to devise weapons meant to inflict great wounds upon his enemies.

'When you go to the Halls of Crafting, look out for the Orcs who stand proudly among the rest -- Âmbal and Bashkuga they are called; they will be the masters of the craft. Their minds cannot be left to inhabit a place where so many fell devices will be produced.''The Halls of Crafting are in Moria's Flaming Deeps, friend. You should hurry and defeat Âmbal and Bashkuga, for their continued foothold there will come at the cost of many dear lives.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! You cannot know what a great deed you have done this day. All Orcs are deadly, but brilliant and crafty ones are all the more so. You may have saved many, many lives by felling Âmbal and Bashkuga, experts of the crafts of war.'Gornellon of Lothlórien is concerned that the Orcs, ever in their foul mimicry of the Elves, have devised mixtures meant to lend them unnatural strength, not unlike the mirúvor draught of the Elves.The Halls of Crafting are in the southern reaches of the Flaming Deeps in Moria, near Fil Gashan.

Gornellon, a wary Galadhrim scout, wishes you to destroy the draught being made to lend strength to the Orc forces planning an assault against Lórien.Destroy the foul draught of the EnemyGornellon is outside the Halls of Crafting, in the Flaming Deeps.

You should speak with Gornellon and inform him of your success against the Orc-draughts being brewed in the Halls of Crafting.Talk to Gornellon'Let me share a disturbing story with you before you hasten into Moria's Halls of Crafting. Three nights ago, I trailed a small band of rough-looking Orcs as they sped to rejoin their host in the Halls of Crafting. They were weary, and they complained bitterly to their leader.

'The leader then passed a flask among his companions, and as they drank I caught the scent of a strong, bitter liquor; it seemed to burn their very tongues. But when they stood again, they appeared more grim, for their eyes blazed with a newfound fervour. We Elves have drinks which lend us strength on long journeys, but I had not fathomed that the Orcs could ever craft such a draught.

'When you go to the Halls of Crafting with your companions, you should all seek to destroy as much of their supply as possible. I will not deny that my heart quailed at seeing the Orcs so roused, ${PLAYER}. If this mixture is indeed being produced to strengthen an army, we have great reason to be concerned.''I fear of what the Orcs may be capable of with that terrible draught lending them strength and stamina. You should hasten to the Halls of Crafting and destroy as much of the draught as you can.''You did a brave and dangerous deed to go to the place where this wicked drink was being produced. I hope that the Enemy was caught unawares by the arrival of your small but valiant host and did not have time to harden themselves against your coming.'The Galadhrim wish to collect any salvageable weapons and armour from the Halls of Crafting in Moria, which will hopefully help to better arm the dwarves in their defence of Khazad-dûm.The Halls of Crafting are in the southern reaches of Moria's Flaming Deeps, near Fil Gashan.

Gornellon has asked you to salvage weapons and armour that have not been spoiled by the Orcs and goblins, for they will be better used by the people that made them.Collect unspoiled armour (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect unspoiled weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gornellon is outside the Halls of Crafting, in the Flaming Deeps.

You should bring all that you collected to Gornellon, and he will see that the good dwarves of Khazad-dûm will receive this boon.'Baranglim tells me that you are in Moria to fight the Orcs who have been troubling the borders of our land. I am glad of it, ${PLAYER}, for our guards are hard-pressed to keep the Enemy's advances at bay in Lórien. I have seen many things in my long days of watching over the woods, and I have great concern for the force of arms being mustered here.

'I worry about what will become of us if the Orcs hold the Halls of Crafting in Moria, for there is dwarf-made armour there and great weapons of old that would be fell in the hands of evil. The dwarves deserve to reclaim the weapons and armour that remains unspoiled, if any indeed remain.

'With armour shielding the dwarves and not our foes and weapons of old clenched in their worthy hands, I foresee that the tide of this war could change ere it breaks upon the eaves of our fair realm.''Go forth and collect the unspoiled armour and weapons from the Halls of Crafting in the southern reaches of Moria's Flaming Deeps, near Fil Gashan.''You have done remarkably well, friend. Your eye for quality is excellent; these pieces will indeed be more than acceptable to our new neighbours in this dangerous chasm that is Moria.'Defeat the leaders of the invasion within Fil GashanDefeat Vrarz the CookDefeat Commander GrebDefeat General TalugThe dwarves believe if they defeat the leader of Drû-garmadh, the threat will be defeated as well.Nûst is at Drû-garmadh to the south-east.

Alrekur believes if Nûst, Drû-garmadh's leader, is defeated, the camp will no longer provide a threat.Defeat NûstAlrekur is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh.

Alrekur will be pleased to hear Nûst has been defeated.Talk to Alrekur at Mekhem-bizru'The Orcs' ability to wage a large-scale war has been hindered, but only temporarily. More must be done to cripple their offensive capabilities.

'We must strike against the leadership. If there are none to command the siege-weapons, they are nothing but a pile of timber awaiting a flame. If the commander is defeated, the camp is no threat.

'Nûst commands Drû-garmadh. Head back south-east and defeat him and end this threat.''The head has been chopped off, and the snake lies limp. With Nûst defeated the camp is in disarray. I do not feel they will be making a coordinated attack at any time in the future. Thank you for your help.''Defeat Nûst, and the siege-weapons are but piles of wood.'When the Balrog of Moria was defeated, a gap was left in the leadership of the ancient caverns. The Mistress of Pestilence and her Nameless hordes have pressed to fill that gap.Defeat the Blind OneDefeat the Mistress of PestilenceDefeat ZholugaDefeat ÎstumDefeat FlâgîtDefeat RungDefeat BlaghMaethoron is worried about the growing number of Orc-waylayers on the road that runs through Nanduhirion toward Lothlórien.Orc waylayers can be found all along the road that runs through Nanduhirion, north-west of Talan Haldir.

Maethoron has asked you to waylay the waylayers in Nanduhirion so that the road may be made safe.Defeat Orc waylayers in Nanduhirion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maethoron is on Talan Haldir, near the banks of Nimrodel, south-east of Nanduhirion.

You have defeated many of the Orc Waylayers that make travel on the road through Nanduhirion difficult, and should report of your success to Maethoron.Talk to Maethoron'The Orcs are becoming more bold, ${PLAYER}, and their waylayers have made travel along the road through Nanduhirion very dangerous for the unwary traveller.

'If you are a friend to the Elves of Lórien and share our concerns, you will do something about these Orcs in particular. Travel north-west into Nanduhirion and defeat the Orc waylayers where you find them: along the road and near the outskirts of their camps in the area. The road into the Golden Wood must be made safe.''Excellent, ${PLAYER} -- you have waylaid the waylayers most admirably.

'As long as the Orcs of Moria threaten the road through Nanduhirion, the Dimrill Dale, the Elves of Lothlórien will not be able to rest. We will strike at the Orcs wherever we may, and if hardy warriors such as yourself will help us, we will have victory against them.''Orc Waylayers have become more bold in recent days, and have taken up positions along the road that runs through Nanduhirion to the north-west. You should teach them to fear the good-hearted peoples once more.'Skûmfil is nothing more than a dumping ground, a place where the fallen Orcs of Moria are discarded when they begin to reek. It is here that two foes have gathered, each intent on using the corpses found therein for their own purposes. The kergrim and other scavengers as a source of food, and the insects as a place to lay their eggs to spawn future generations.Skûmfil lies to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Moggi sent you to Skûmfil to destroy the warrior-gredbyg there who have some manner of independence from the queen Brúmbereth. The chief of these is Uammaethor.Defeat UammaethorDefeat NestaduanDefeat GrogDefeat GrothulunDefeat UlugonMoggi is at the Shadowed Refuge, north-west of Skûmfil.

You found and kill the grodbog-warrior Uammaethor and its defenders within the corpse-ridden place called Skûmfil.Talk to Moggi at the Shadowed Refuge'These gredbyg have no thought of their own, that is what I think. I know that there is a big insect in Skûmfil, and wherever you find that, you are sure to find what is in control.

'There are other gredbyg though, smaller ones that have a bit of independence; those are the nasty ones that I think we need to eliminate. So that is the task I will give to you.

'If you are willing to help me, you should make your way toward Skûmfil located to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge. You will find the warrior-caste gredbyg there. Kill Ummaethor, a larger warrior, and its guards, then return to me here at the Shadowed Refuge.''Excellent work, I shall inform my superior that you performed your task admirably and completely.

'You have my thanks.''The gredbyg within Skûmfil mean to breed in the corpses of the fallen. We must stop this, but more, we must stop their warriors. Find the warrior called Uammaethor and slay it within Skûmfil. You can find it south-east from the Shadowed Refuge where we now speak.'With the ranks of the invading Orcs thinned, it is now time to strike against their leadership, hobbling their communication and throwing their forces into chaos.Moria Orc-emissaries can be found at Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul.

Raskwith asked to go to the three Orc-camps in the Dimrill Dale and defeat the three Moria Orc-emissaries.Defeat the Orc-emissary at Uruk-gashanDefeat the Orc-emissary at Drû-garmadhDefeat the Orc-emissary at AthmadhulRaskwith is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of the Orc-camps.

Raskwith will be pleased to hear the Moria Orc-emissaries have been defeated.Talk to Raskwith at Mekhem-bizru'You did well by culling the Orcs. Now it is time to strike a lethal blow against all three camps. Each has a powerful leader, but more important than that, each has an envoy from Mazog, responsible for carrying messages back and forth from the commander of Moria's Orcs.

'Return to the camps south-east of here -- Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul -- and defeat the Moria Orc-emissaries. Breaking their communication lines with Mazog will surely turn them against each other for control of the Dale.

'May you find good fortune awaiting you upon this quest, ${PLAYER}, and may you return with due swiftness.''With their link to Mazog severed, the Orcs have begun fighting among themselves. Soon, the Dale will once again belong to us!

'You have done well, ${PLAYER}.''We will throw them into far more chaos by breaking their communication lines to Mazog, than by simply defeating their leaders.'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, has invited you to recollect your experience exploring the shadowy abyss of Azanarukâr.The Reflecting Pool in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria will allow you to revisit 'New Devilry.'

A Sage of Moria has challenged you to revisit the shadowy abyss of Azanarukâr.

<rgb=#FF0000>You can form a Fellowship to complete this quest with players currently on the original instance or on this Sage of Moria quest. All players will receive credit for completing the instance for their respective quests.</rgb>Peer into the Reflecting Pool and revisit 'New Devilry'Rúnar, a Sage of Moria, can be found in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria.

A Sage of Moria is waiting to speak with you about what you have learned by revisiting your adventures in Azanarukâr.'I do not fully know what horrors you faced in the shadowy abyss of Azanarukâr, ${PLAYER}, but rumour of them is enough to turn my beard white!

'You can revisit your adventures in the depths by peering into the Reflecting Pool, and perhaps you will learn something of value.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You can form a Fellowship to complete this quest with players currently on the original instance or on this Sage of Moria quest. All players will receive credit for completing the instance for their respective quests.</rgb>'I am pleased that you have revisited your adventures in the shadowy abyss, ${PLAYER}. Only by studying our past can we gain knowledge to aid our future.'Find the tools used by the Orcs within the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Find the tools used by the Orcs within the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Find the tools used by the Orcs within the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Find a Khazâd-steel ChainFind a Khazâd-iron HammerFind a Charred Wheel-barrowFind an Ill-treated Pick-axeTuilinn has invited you to solemnly meditate upon Cerin Amroth.The place Tuilinn spoke of is upon the southern side of Cerin Amroth.

Tuilinn wants you to go to the spot on the hill of Cerin Amroth at which Aragorn and Arwen pledged their troth to each other and <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> in honour of their love, as she does.Tuilinn is atop the flet on Cerin Amroth.

You should let Tuilinn know that you have done as she instructed.Talk to Tuilinn at Cerin Amroth'Now that you know the sweet history of Elessar and his lady-love Undómiel, perhaps you understand the solemnity of their joining and their parting. 

'The happiest time they had together was the season they spent in Lórien, especially here upon Cerin Amroth. It is the habit of many of us who have known either of them to spend time upon the hill in the sunshine, reflecting upon the sacrifices they have made for each other. It is a good way to put one's problems into perspective, among other things.

'Would you like to do so as well? It must be during the day: as Aragorn said when they spoke their promises, neither the Shadow, which he always repudiates, nor the Twilight is for him, being mortal. Go to the southern side of the hill and <rgb=#FF0000>meditate</rgb> upon these matters for a time.''You have the peaceful look of one who has meditated, ${PLAYER}: solemn and peaceful.''You should sit upon the southern face of Cerin Amroth and meditate upon the tale of Arwen and Elessar.'Cúbenn has crafted an arrow in memory of Núrelleth's husband Faengris, slain by Orcs.Núrelleth can be found on Telain Glorelloth, where the flets extend over the hedge that encircles Caras Galadhon.

Cúbenn has given you the arrow he crafted in memory of Núrelleth's slain husband Faengris.'Do you have a moment, ${PLAYER}? I am a fletcher, and it is my duty to fashion arrows for the quivers of the Galadhrim. I have done this for many a year, and my shafts have been the doom of many an Orc. But I recently finished an arrow different from all the rest.

'My friend Faengris, with whom I learned the craft of bow-making and arrow-fletching, was recently slain by a company of Orcs that came down from the Misty Mountains. When the sharp pains of grief lessened somewhat, I set to making an arrow of such bite that it could kill a marching line of Orcs with one shot when fired from a quality bow.

'This arrow in memory of Faengris may be some small comfort to his widow, Núrelleth. Bring it to her that she may see that the Orcs will pay for his death. She can often be found on Telain Glorelloth, where the flets extend over the encircling hedge.''There is little I can do to relieve Núrelleth's sorrow, or my own, but I hope the knowledge that this arrow I have fashioned will slay many Orcs will be of some comfort to her. Look for her on Telain Glorelloth, where the flets extend over the encircling hedge.'Núrelleth looks at you silently for a moment before taking the arrow from you and examining it sadly.

'It is most kind of Cúbenn to have worked so long on this arrow in memory of my husband, ${PLAYER}. Their friendship was very important to Faengris, and he spoke often of Cúbenn's skill at bow-making and arrow-fletching. Faengris....'

Her fingers trace the pattern on the fletching, and she no longer seems aware of your presence. After a moment, Núrelleth looks up again.

'This is a fine arrow indeed, ${PLAYER}, but Faengris would not want it wasted on the Orcs.'Skûmfil is nothing more than a dumping ground, a place where the fallen Orcs of Moria are discarded when they begin to reek. It is here that two foes have gathered, each intent on using the corpses found therein for their own purposes. The kergrim and other scavengers as a source of food, and the insects as a place to lay their eggs to spawn future generations.Skûmfil lies to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Glorelloth wants to ensure that the kergrim are not responsible for the disease affecting the Orcs of the shadowy dark and so has sent you to collect samples of the kergrims' skin.'The kergrim are rife with disease, this much is true, but I am not certain that they are behind the plague affecting the Orcs. However, it is possible that they are, and so I ask that you collect samples from the kergrim and their ilk within Skûmfil.

'You will find the place south-east from the Shadowed Refuge. Take small strips of their hide and return it to me so that I might better determine if the kergrim are infested with the same kind of illness that plagues the Orcs.''It will take some time to examine these samples and determine whether the plague is the same or different than that borne by the kergrim. I will also inform Throstur that you have done as I asked. 

'Thank you, friend.'The Sixteenth Hall is an area overrun with Orcs, many of whom suffer from a terrible illness that causes fungus-like growths on their bodies.

Mallas, an Elf ally to the dwarves, believes that there is something secret beneath the Sixteenth Hall and wishes to learn the true purpose and source of the plague.The Sixteenth Hall can be found north-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

You should collect samples from defeated Orcs in the Sixteenth Hall to allow Pentlenn to observe the behaviour of this disease. He advised that you do your best to avoid becoming infected yourself.'I am hoping to assess the disease spreading throughout the Orcs within the Sixteenth Hall, but I dare not enter the Hall by myself, for I am no warrior.

'If you are willing, I would seek your aid. Acquire many samples of tissue from the Orcs to see how potent is their disease, and if it may be passed on to others.

'This will not be an easy task; you should do your best not to allow the infected Orcs to come into close contact with you, for they may be contagious. You will find the Sixteenth Hall to the north-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Collect the samples and return them to me when you are finished.''I will need time to study these samples, but you have served me well thus far. I will be sure to tell Mallas what you have done for me.

'I thank you, ${RACE}, and I am glad to find you hale after so risky a venture.'You collected this piece of chitin from Brumbereth, the queen of the gredbyg of Skûmfil.Mallas is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You should bring the chitin to Mallas. Perhaps he can provide insight as to why there would be insects near the infected Orcs.You discovered this chitin and much more from insects dwelling within the Skûmfil. You should bring this to someone who may know more about the insects.'These insects are like those the dwarves tell me they discovered elsewhere. It is unlikely that the insects are the carriers of this disease, but they would certainly use the corpses of the dead as nourishment for their young.'Bróin believes that Gorothúl gave a relic of evil to the merrevail that infest the Mirrors of Lumul-nar.Bróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.Destroy the Gift of Gorothúl in Lumul-narDefeat Ergoth, the dark Morraval that was drawn to Gift of Gorothúl.Defeat ErgothBósi reports that a relic of Gorothúl's lies among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm and will require careful usage of the mechanisms to reach and destroy.Bróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.Destroy the relic of Gorothúl in Nalâ-dûmDefeat Caerlûg, the foul creature that has taken residence in the depths of the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.Defeat CaerlûgYou, Bingo, and Willem Whisker have emerged from the dark expanse of Moria and now approach the Golden Wood.You have come with Bingo a good distance into the Dimrill Dale, and a path leads to the east in the direction of the Golden Wood.Talk to Bingo on the roadYou defended Bingo from attack by an Orc raiding party, and now the hobbit is ready to continue his relaxing stroll through the Dimrill Dale.Talk to Bingo on the road through the Dimrill DaleHaldir and a number of Elves have arrived at a fortuitous moment, and seem to have been expecting you.Talk to Haldir on the roadYou have come with Bingo through the Dimrill Dale and encountered a small party of Elves sent from Lothlórien to meet you.Talk to Bingo on the roadHaldir has asked for you and Bingo to accompany him into Lothlórien.Travel into Lothlórien with Haldir and BingoYou and Bingo have been escorted into Lothlórien, and now the hobbit is very excited to learn as much about the Elves as he can.Talk to Bingo inside Caras GaladhonYou and Bingo have encountered Celeborn and Galadriel, and they are most interested to hear of your journeys.Listen to the words of Celeborn and GaladrielThe Lord and Lady of Lórien wait to speak with you in Caras Galadhon.Talk to CelebornTalk to GaladrielBingo is within Caras Galadhon, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Bingo in Caras Galadhon'Well, they have given me much to think about, that is for certain!''It is a good day for walking! The cool, crisp air puts me almost in mind of a leisurely stroll along the lanes of the Shire! And yet we are so far from the Westfarthing... indeed, we are so far to the east of the Eastfarthing that I have quite lost track of the miles!

'I can see the golden hue of the woods down this slope, ${PLAYER}. Let us walk and see what awaits us beneath the canopy!''Those Orcs wanted to spoil our relaxing stroll, but I'd say you countered their designs most effectively!

'Let us not dwell upon the shadows that darkened our path, but focus instead on the bright future that awaits us beneath the golden-hued sun and the trees ahead! Let us continue, and perhaps at a quicker pace!''${PLAYER}, we have been expecting you and your friends. The Lady of Lórien gave me particular instruction to set forth from the Golden Wood in search of you and your companions. I am pleased to see you have not come to harm.

'If your friend is willing, I would be happy to bring you beyond the bounds and before the Lord and Lady.''Ah, we have encountered a welcoming party, ${PLAYER}, and we seem to be expected! What a lovely turn of events!

'I will be delighted to accompany these fellows. Onward to the Golden Wood!''I can hardly believe that we have been invited into the Golden Wood, ${PLAYER}, and that we are being given a personal tour of Caras Galadhon!

'I have so many questions to ask the Elves of this place. What brought them to settle here, and for how long have they lived in Lothlórien? Do they live lives of solitude, or do they travel? The sight of an Elf is a very rare thing in the Shire!

'I hope they do not think my questions rude, but I have to know as much about their people as I can, or my book will suffer for such a lack of knowledge!''I hope your friend is not offended! Our welcome to this wood is sincere, and it is my hope he will find it a place of peace and rest before continuing his journey.

'I will speak to the sentries at the gate of Caras Galadhon. The three of you will be welcome within the city from this point.''My mirror shows me many things, and not all of them will come to pass. I know of your own journey, and I know of young Bingo's as well. Is he truly surprised that his feline companion is on a journey of his own? It may be a useful reminder to him that all of us have our own paths to tread in this world, and while they may intertwine for a time, they will not forever.

'My own time in this land that I love will soon be ended, and my journey will take me elsewhere. For now, it is my pleasure to welcome all of you to Caras Galadhon. If you desire to learn more, seek out Pennasseth, our Keeper of Stories, at Cerin Nauth.''I am ashamed to admit that I never gave a thought to Willem Whisker's own journey, and now my face is as red as can be! What do you suppose he's seeking? If it is in my power to help him find it, I will do everything I can!

'You should have told me earlier, Willem!'At the request of Issuriel, you relate the story of your escape from Rushdurinul with Mazog in tow.Bróin is waiting to speak with you in the depths of Rushdurinul.Talk to BróinThe Elves and dwarves are discussing the fate of Mazog.Listen to the discussion of Mazog's fateBróin is in the depths of Rushdurinul, waiting to hear what you have to say concerning the fate of Mazog.Give Bróin your opinion of his decision concerning Mazog's fateThe Elves and dwarves within Rushdurinul are considering the various implications of what must be done with Mazog.Listen to the discussion concerning Mazog's fateBróin is waiting to speak with you in Rushdurinul.Talk to BróinMazog is in Rushdurinul. You must bind him with the shackles Bróin has given you.Shackle MazogBróin is in Rushdurinul, waiting to speak with you now that Mazog is shackled.Talk to BróinBróin has told you how to modify the support role of your allies, by using the banner he has set up, and is waiting for you to do so.Use the banner to change your allies' support roleThe escape from Rushdurinul has begun -- you must defend Bróin from the attack of the Orcs!Protect Bróin from the attacking OrcsYou have come to the entrance to Zurr-thurkh and should now ensure that Mazog's words are merely empty bluster before leaving.Talk to MazogDespite his attempt to escape, you have forced Mazog to submit. You should speak now with Bróin.Talk to Bróin'It is too soon to celebrate over-much, ${PLAYER}, I know; but to have come even this far is something extraordinary!

'And yet, I wonder: Mazog is of great value to the forces of the Enemy. Can it be that they will consider a trade? If we were to bring Mazog before the gates of Dol Guldur, would Gorothúl accept Mazog's life in trade for that of my cousin Bori?

'I have sworn a vow that my axe shall end Mazog's life, but if greater good could be accomplished by his survival, well...it becomes a more difficult question, ${PLAYER}. We cannot abandon Bori now!''That was close, ${PLAYER}, but we have managed to bring Mazog once more under control. I should have known he would have some fight left!

'One thing is certain, friend ${RACE}: we will need to make some stronger shackles to hold our prisoner in the future!''Take these shackles, ${PLAYER}, and use them to bind Mazog's wrists. They are made of iron and should be strong enough to keep him secure as we fight our way from this place.''Now we need to make our way from Rushdurinul, ${PLAYER}, but I fear we have taken too long already: this place will soon be swarming with Orcs. If we hope to escape from here with our lives and that of our captive, we need someone to manage the flow of battle.

'I suggest that you accept that role. You will need to tell us what our support role should be as the battle ebbs and flows. Should we focus on improving your morale, your power, the strength of your attacks, or the fortitude of your defence?''You think these bracelets can bind Mazog in his own domain? You are a fool if you think I cannot sunder these with even the smallest effort!

'But I will wait until you are most vulnerable, ${RACE}, and then you will feel my hands around your neck!''Quickly now, before more Orcs attack, let us take Mazog with us and leave this place behind!''Rule here? You think I want to rule here? I have no desire to rule this miserable kingdom! You have no idea what is happening, do you?

'Gorothúl's master is generous to his friends. He looks out for them. He tells them things. Mine will be the greatest of his armies!

'"What reward do you desire?" Gorothúl asked of me. "Only the kingdom that should be mine," I told him. "That place will not do," he said. "My master has commanded me to draw forth the great terrors of the abyss. That kingdom will never be free of them," he said, and only fools would disbelieve his words!'Unbeknownst to the Dunlendings in Eregion, their largest camp has been built upon an ancient Elf-forge where some of the finest weapons of the early Third Age were once wrought. In order to gain access to this forge, Perimbant has devised a daring plan to raid the camp via the river by moonlight, sneaking in to overcome the guards and set fire to much of the camp, scattering the unsuspecting defenders in the chaos of battle and flame.You must weaken the camp's response to your attack by ambushing and eliminating a number of their veteran guardsman before the main phase of the assault begins.Defeat veteran guardsmen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grab torches from the bonfire in the centre of the Dunlanding camp and set fire to as many tents as possible in order to create panic and disorder.Take a brand from the bonfireBurned tents (${VALUE}/40)You must find and defeat the Dunlending captain before he can rally his troops to fight off your assault.Defeat the Dunlending captainUse the ancient forge to empower your infused adamant.Speak with Perimbant to return to Echad Dúnann.Speak to Perimbant'Quite the display you showed here, my friends. The Dunlendings will not soon forgive you for your deeds here tonight.''Are you ready to return to Echad Dúnann then?'The Elves of Lothlórien have sent you deep into Azanarukâr to find out what has happened to Magor and discover what is really going on in the unmapped depths.Upon entering Azanarukâr, you are confronted with the battallions of Mazog's elite troops.  The Elves have asked you to remove the threat of Mazog in Azanarukâr by defeating their leaders.Defeat Moria Orc-berserkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated the leaders of the Moria Orcs that Mazog sent to Azanarukâr and found Magor, the lost Elf. Now, Magor wants you to help him defeat the Nameless creatures that dwell deep in Azanarukâr. He will need assistance in putting an end to the scourge.Talk to Magor, the Elven prisonerMagor has helped you clear the way to a darker deeper lair. Sensing great danger, he has gone for help, leaving you to seek out the new threat. Seek out the evil ahead and defeat it.You have killed two great Regmyl that have claimed to guard Azanarukâr for a long time. You hear horrible bellowing roars ahead and can only guess at what danger lurks behind the next turn.'Let us leave this place, ${PLAYER}. We have been too long in the presence of this evil, and my heart longs for relief from the dread of it.''Back! You will never defile me with your poison! Good, they are gone; I am relieved. I thought for certain I would become like them: a monstrosity. They came upon me unaware, surrounding me and taking me captive. One hears rumours of such twisted fates, but now I have seen the wicked pool of filth that corrupts the very depths of this place -- I saw it with my own eyes.

'I will give you a moment to collect your thoughts, and then you must follow me. We will crush these monsters before they can corrupt aught else beyond this wicked place. This will be a great task. I can only imagine what horrors we will face as we penetrate the area.

'Hurry; gather your wits and make ready!'You have come to Azanarukâr with Magor in search of an artifact left by Gorothúl in the depths.In the depths of Azanarukâr, Magor wishes to fight alongside you in search of the artifact he believes Gorothúl left there.Talk to MagorYou have found the relic within Azanarukâr, and should destroy it to prevent further of Gorothúl's schemes from hatching.Destroy Gorothúl's beaconGwathnor has awakened, and he must be defeated in order to prevent the growth of his power. 

<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow Gwathnor or any of his minions to approach the door.</rgb>Defeat Gwathnor<rgb=#FF0000> Do not allow Gwathnor or his allies to approach the exit </rgb>Magor is waiting to speak with you in the depths of Azanarukâr after your defeat of Gwathnor and the forms of Grawulun.Talk to Magor'We have ended Gwathnor's growing strength and dispersed the forms of Grawulun that were drawn to Azanarukâr, ${PLAYER}. We have won a short victory, a small respite -- without the beacon of Gorothúl, it will be some time before Gwathnor and his servants can again find the world above.

'But it will not last forever. We do not possess the means of destroying these creatures, lesser spirits though they be -- they are beyond our ability. We can hinder them for a time, and hope the peace we buy is worth the dangers.

'I feel it is.''Are you ready to leave? There is nothing to hold us here; we should return to the upper levels, where the air is clean.''Here we are, ${PLAYER}, where once we came before: the deepest reaches of Azanarukâr. I have come here often since we first met, though better equipped than on that adventure. The Lady of the Wood has given me a great Elf-stone and many things have fled before its light.

'We should be cautious, as there were Regmyl here before, and I saw them carrying an artifact of great evil. I do not see them now, but they are surely not far.

'Let us proceed, friends, and see what lies before us in Azanarukâr.'You have decided to walk through the woods of Lothlórien with Legolas and Gimli in search of Orc patrols.Legolas and Gimli are standing on one of the paths that runs through the woods of Lothlórien.

Legolas is waiting to travel with you through the woods of Lothlórien.Talk to LegolasYou have come with Legolas and Gimli near to the border of the wood, and have been hailed by one of the Galadhrim.Talk to Galadhrim ArcherYou have been told to follow Legolas and Gimli to the eaves of the wood to meet with a dwarf that has asked for you.Follow Legolas and Gimli to the eaves of the woodBósi is at the border of Lothlórien, attempting to get an audience with Celeborn.Talk to BósiThe Galadhrim are waiting to hear what you have to say about Bósi's request.Talk to Galadhrim WardenWhile blindfolded, Bósi has been led to Caras Galadhon within Lothlórien for his audience with Celeborn.Talk to BósiBósi is having an audience with Celeborn of Lórien about sending Elves to assist the dwarves in Khazad-dûm.Watch over Bósi's audience with CelebornGaladriel is waiting to speak with you following the audience with Bósi.'It is time for you to leave, young one. There is much to be done.''Are you ready, ${PLAYER}? It is possible that no further Orcs have crept beyond the borders, but if any have, we must be prepared to do battle.

'Come, then! I will show you the way!''Out of respect for you, ${PLAYER}, and as a courtesy for the good you have done us, I have been told to find you and send you to the eaves of the wood.

'A stranger has arrived on the borders. In these unusual times, such a visitor to Lothlórien has been seen only once.

'This stranger is a dwarf, and he is asking for you, ${PLAYER}.''Things are not going well for the Iron Garrison in Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Mazog still rules much of the deeps and many of the levels from his stronghold of Zabadgathol, and many good dwarves have fallen to his forces. Some, like my own son Bori, are still captives, or worse! I cannot bear to think what torments they may have suffered behind the walls of Zabadgathol.

'Still the dwarves of the Iron Garrison struggle to reclaim the hidden caverns, but for every beauty that is unearthed, two evils seem to spring forth from the depths!

'I have come to enlist the help of the ruler of these Elf-woods. If Celeborn of Lothlórien wishes to reap the benefits of friendship with the dwarves, he must reciprocate in kind. You are trusted by these Elves, ${PLAYER}. Tell this warden, this sentry, of our plight. Perhaps they will listen to you.''Talk to these Elves, ${PLAYER}. They seem to trust you, and perhaps your word will get me the audience with Celeborn I have requested.''We will bring this dwarf to speak with Celeborn, ${PLAYER}, but you will be held responsible for him. You will be accountable for any and all of his actions while he remains within the Golden Wood.

'Come with us.''For the sake of the Iron Garrison I have put up with the indignity of being blindfolded during the passage here, ${PLAYER}, but my people could teach the Elves of this place something of courtesy were they to visit Khazad-dûm.

'Let us see now if the ill manners of the Elves spring from their Lord.''The Lord of the Galadhrim has much wisdom, and it is his wish that the dwarves not face the darkness of Khazad-dûm unaided.

'So it will be, and you too shall stand against whatever evils lie now beneath the mountains, ${PLAYER}, if this is your wish.'Agorin asked you to launch an assault upon the summit of Minas Gîl, where some powerful sorcery appears to be underway. Upon your arrival, you have discovered a band of sorcerers led by the Black Númenórean Gúlbenn in the midst of an evil ritual of shadows.Defeat the sorcerer Gúlbenn and his servants atop Minas Gîl.Defeat Gúlbenn, the sorcerer of Minas GîlDefeat Twilight atop Minas GîlThe Orcs of Moria have begun their assault on Lothlórien, and it is up to you, your allies, and a small number of Elves to repel them.Belvagor is at the base of the slope that climbs up into Fanuidhol.

The Elf Belvagor is waiting to speak with you about his plan for repelling the Orc-attack.Talk to BelvagorBelvagor and his two friends wait for orders on the slope that climbs up into Fanuidhol.

Belvagor and his two friends wait for you to tell them which passes to defend. To do this, you should first travel to the Northern Pass, Western Pass, and Eastern Pass and note the composition of the defenders at each; then you can make an informed decision.The Orc-attack is underway! You must work together with your allies to carry a Banner of Lórien to the four Orc-encampments so the Idol of the Enemy at each can be destroyed, and you must do it before any of the three passes can be overrun.Destroy Idols of the Enemy (${VALUE}/4)Defend BelvagorDefend all passes from the OrcsTime is of the essenceYou have destroyed four Idols of the Enemy and should return now to speak with Belvagor at the pass you told him to defend.Talk to Belvagor'Are you ready to leave this site of battle, ${PLAYER}?''We have arrived, ${PLAYER}, and it seems the Orcs have not yet begun their attack. Good! Then we have a moment to make our plans. Further up the hill are the three passes that gate entry to the Golden Wood: the Northern Pass, the Western Pass, and the Eastern Pass; a number of my people have already gone to each of the passes to defend them.

'Travel up to each of the passes and make note of the skills of the Elves at each location: melee combat, ranged combat, or the healing arts. Then return here and tell myself and my two friends where you would like us.

'Once all three of us have our orders, you and your allies can begin carrying the Banners of Lórien to the four Orc-encampments. Only when a Banner is near an Orc-encampment will you be able to destroy the idol of the Enemy there.''The Orcs are retreating! The Golden Wood is safe, for now. We cannot rest long, but for today you have helped us achieve victory!'The year is 1980 of the Third Age. You are Nafni, a trusted servant of Durin VI, the Lord of Khazad-dûm, and have no idea what will befall your fellow dwarves on this fateful night.Sverri is standing at the doors before the great throne of Durin.

The doorkeeper of Durin's throne room is waiting to speak with you about some matter.Talk to SverriDurin VI, Lord of Moria, is waiting at the dais on the north side of the great throne room.

Durin is waiting to speak with you about some matter before the Elves from Lórien arrive.Talk to Durin VIMelkólf Stonecarver is on the west side of Durin's throne room.

Durin has asked you to commission a statue of his son Náin from Melkólf Stonecarver.Talk to Melkólf StonecarverDurin VI is by the dais in the great throne room.

You should return to Durin and tell him that Melkólf Stonecarver has agreed to make a great statue for Durin's son Náin.Talk to Durin VISverri is at the front entrance to the throne room, south of Durin's great dais.

Durin has asked you to speak with Sverri and await the party of Elves from Lórien.Talk to SverriNáin is at the doors that enter Durin's throne-room, with the party of Elves from Lórien.

Náin is waiting to speak with you.Talk to NáinDurin VI is at the dais at the north end of the throne-room.

Náin has asked you to tell Durin, his father, that the host of Elves from Lothlórien has arrived.Talk to Durin VIDurin VI is addressing the Elves from Lothlórien.Wait for Durin VI to finish addressing the ElvesDurin VI is at his dais on the north side of the throne-room.

Durin is eager to impress the Elves from Lothlórien with the glory of the mithril mines.Talk to Durin VIDurin VI is standing with the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm.

Durin is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Durin VIDurin VI is standing with the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm.

Durin is waiting for you to clear the cavern of cave-claws and deep-claws.Defeat cave-claws and deep-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Durin VI is standing with the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm.

Durin is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Durin VIDurin VI and his party is walking to the mithril deposits in the caverns deep beneath Khazad-dûm.Follow Durin VI and his companyDurin VI is standing with the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm.

Durin is waiting for you to help break through the cracked wall beneath Khazad-dûm.Help break through the cracked wallSome great terror has slumbered beneath Khazad-dûm for a long age.Survive!The dwarves are fleeing from the great terror that has been awakened beneath Khazad-dûm!Escape!Náin is standing with what remains of the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm.

Durin has been slain by the terrible creature that slept beneath Khazad-dûm, and now Náin is the ruler of the dwarf-kingdom.Talk to Náin, Lord of Moria'There thou art, Nafni! Where hast thou been? Lord Durin has been asking for thee; the Elf delegates from Lothlórien are soon due, and he has some business to which he wants thee to attend before they arrive.

'He sits on his throne, Nafni. Go to Durin and lend him thine assistance, as is thy wont and thy duty.''Thou must not keep our lord waiting! Speak with Durin by the dais at the north end of this great hall!''Thank thee for coming, Nafni. The delegation of Elves will be here very soon, and I had hoped to ask thee something.

'We have not had as many dealings with the Elves as once we did, and it is my hope that this meeting will rekindle the old friendships. The glory and wealth of Khazad-dûm is limitless, even if mithril is becoming more scarce by the year, but with the aid of the Elves we might delve even farther afield.

'We must look to the future. It is to that end that I wish to make a gift to my son Náin, for he will be king when I am gone, though it not be for many years.

'Speak to Melkólf Stonecarver on the western side of the hall about making a statue for my son. It will stand in this throne room when the time of his kingship is nigh.''Melkólf Stonecarver is my court sculptor, and does very fine work. He will make a statue worthy of my son Náin, who will reign in Khazad-dûm when I am gone, years hence, if fortune is kind.

'Speak to him on the west side of this hall, where he is wont to stay when he is not working.''Nafni, hello, hello! It is an honour to speak with one held so highly in my lord's esteem!'

You describe the statue Durin wishes Melkólf to make for Náin.

'It will be done, friend Nafni, with all haste; but not so quickly that the product suffers! It will capture young Náin's lordly countenance, and were he to stand very still, no dwarf in Khazad-dûm could tell the difference!

'Please tell my lord Durin that I will begin right away!''Thank thee, Nafni. Melkólf is an unparalleled artist whose works will always have renown for their place within Khazad-dûm.

'Go to Sverri at the front gate of the throne room and await the delegates from Lórien. My son will be escorting them hither.''The Elves are nearly here, Nafni, escorted by Náin, the son of Durin. They will surely be impressed by the majesty of Durin's halls, but let us not reveal our pride. The way of the dwarf is to be humble before his guests, Nafni, as thou dost know well.

'They shall not but help to marvel at the halls of Durin. Do they not live among the trees? The great pillars of Durin's city are like to trees, but shaped from the very roots of the stone Earth in stunning artistry!''They are impressed, are they not, Nafni? But do not keep Náin waiting! He has asked to speak with thee!''Nafni, these are the Elves of Lórien, come to speak with my father about our continued friendly relations and trade. Wouldst thou announce to my father that we have arrived?''Tell my father that the party from Lothlórien has arrived, Nafni. He will be at the dais on the north end of the throne-room, as usual.''I thank thee, Nafni. I see that they have come, and I am ready to speak with them about the continued friendship of the dwarves.''We will go at once, and impress upon our visitors the glory and bounty of the dwarves!''This cavern is deep and untamed, Nafni, and something seems to have stirred up the cave-claws and deep-claws that burrow here in the depths.

'Be so good as to clear this cave of the beasts so we may proceed to the mithril deposits in safety.''Clear this cavern of cave-claws and deep-claws, Nafni! We must be able to proceed to the mithril deposits in safety.''Very good, my friend. Now we will show the Elves the great bounty of mithril that still lies beneath Khazad-dûm!''I need thee to break through the wall, Nafni. There is sure to be mithril on the other side!''We must retreat, Nafni! We have no other option!

'But I swear on my father's name that I shall slay this Balrog, this ancient evil, this horror from a distant age!

'Khazad-dûm will not fall!'The Library of Steel is under attack by a band of Fire-orcs from the depths of Moria. They are attempting to summon enough fire-spirits to break the wards protecting the library and turn it into an inferno. You must protect the library and defeat the Orcs if you wish to make use of the ancient forge within to complete your quality.You must defeat the Fire-orc summoners in order to prevent them from summoning enough spirits to destroy the library. If too many spirits are gathered within the library, it will be consumed in an inferno and lost. Once the summoners have been dealth with, you must then face the leader of the Orcs....Defeat Fire-orc summoners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat OshadhúrUse the ancient forge to emopwer your infused adamant.You have entered a passage leading to the one-time workshop of Melkólf Stonecarver to search for any mention of Zurr-thurkh, the 'secret road' he may have built as an escape tunnel from the throne room of Durin.Pages from the workshop of Melkólf Stonecarver have been scattered all throughout the passage, and you should search them for any mention of Zurr-thurkh, the 'secret road' that might lead into the throne room of Durin.Search the scattered papers for mention of Zurr-thurkhPages from the workshop of Melkólf Stonecarver have been scattered all throughout the passage, and you should search them for any mention of Zurr-thurkh, the 'secret road' that might lead into the throne room of Durin.Search the scattered papers for mention of Zurr-thurkhThe Lady Galadriel wishes to speak with you in her garden in Lothlórien.Galadriel is waiting for you in the centre of the garden.

You have been summoned to Galadriel's garden in Lothlórien, for she hopes to speak with you.Talk to GaladrielThe Mirror of Galadriel is in the centre of her garden.

Galadriel has invited you to gaze into her Mirror to see what you will.Look into the Mirror of GaladrielGaladriel is waiting for you in the centre of the garden.

You have seen strange sights within the Mirror of Galadriel, including confusing images of Gandalf and a terrible creature: a Balrog, Durin's Bane.Talk to GaladrielGaladriel is waiting for you in the centre of the garden.

The Lady Galadriel has seen more than the fate of Mithrandir in her Mirror; she has seen some hints of your fate as well.Listen to Galadriel's words concerning your fateGwaihir the Windlord has come to rest in Galadriel's garden.

Galadriel has asked you to speak with Gwaihir concerning the fate of Gandalf the Grey.Talk to Gwaihir'I am aware of your kindness to Magor beneath the mountains, ${PLAYER}. You are now held high in his esteem, and he accords you great fondness for your part in his rescue.

'Strange deeds unravel on the many paths of your journey, for as your footsteps lead you to and fro, I perceive that many fates are entwined with your own. Some of your tales seem ended, but locked doors may yet be pried open.

'My Mirror can show many things, and you may ask it what you will. But heed this before you peer into the water: many valuable answers may come unbidden. Look now, and see what may be seen.''Some light is now shed on the riddles, do you not agree? The clues left behind among the Foundations of Stone begin to form a clear picture at last. Gandalf the Grey strove in Moria with Shadow and flame, and they fell, and perhaps rose again. Who had the mastery?

'It has been said that my eyes see farther than many who are deemed wise, yet keener eyes we need to pierce the darkness that shrouds Mithrandir from my sight. Who can spy upon Moria from all sides and gain rumour of the fate of Gandalf? Only Gwaihir the Windlord can do this.''I have carried Gandalf before now, and if he yet lives, I will carry him again. I will send out the sharpest-sighted eagles to seek him from every corner of this land, and I will fly until we have learned what befell him.

'If he is to be found, I and my kind will find him.

'Return to the Lady and tell her I will do this.''Gwaihir is resting in the rear of my garden. Speak to him, and we shall ask him to spy from the heights for rumour of Gandalf. He may yet live. I do not think that his purpose upon Middle-earth would be so soon spent, for his tasks will be great ere the end.''I know that Gwaihir will find Mithrandir, if he is to be found.

'Haldir will show you from this place, ${PLAYER}. I will call for him.'The Elf-scout Ianudirel has been trapped across the river from Krul Lugu. She must return to the near side, but expects to be ambushed when she attempts to cross the bridge.Speak with Ianudirel and fight your way across the bridge to Krul Lugu.Talk to IanudirelTalk to Ianudirel to return to Iavassúl.'It was a pleasure fighting by your side, ${PLAYER}. I will be able to make it back to my brother's camp easily enough from here.

'You should report to him as well. I am sure there is more to be done here.''It was a pleasure fighting by your side, ${PLAYER}. I will be able to make it back to my brother's camp easily enough from here.

'You should report to him as well. I am sure there is more to be done here.''Let us be off before the fell spirits find us!

'Are you ready to go?'You have come with Orvar Bellhammer to Zurr-thurkh, the 'secret road' that was built as an escape passage from the throne room of Durin, and will use it to gain access to Mazog's fortress.No one has walked the 'secret road' since before the Fall of Moria, but now you and Orvar Bellhammer will use it to get behind the walls of Mazog's fortress, Zabadgathol.Talk to Orvar in Zurr-thurkhYou should clear the way for Orvar to follow when he is ready.Clear the way ahead for OrvarOrvar is waiting outside the secret road, in Rushdurinul.Talk to Orvar in RushdurinulOrvar has told you to search the large Orc encampment in the throne room for the captive Bori.Search the Orc encampment for BoriWith no sign of Bori in the Orc encampment within Rushdurinul, Orvar has decided to confront Mazog directly.Talk to OrvarYou have come with Orvar to Rushdurinul, the throne room in which Mazog makes his lair, and will now confront the Orc leader.Protect Orvar as he confronts MazogWith the sudden appearance of Bróin and the Elves from Buzun-ghâr, Mazog has been defeated.Talk to BróinTalk to Corunothiel'Let us leave this place, ${PLAYER}, and arrange for the prisoner to be kept somewhere safe. Mazog will not trouble us on the journey or he will lose his life, and painfully!''This is incredible, ${PLAYER}. Can we really use this passage to get behind the walls of Zabadgathol? For how long has this tunnel remained undiscovered by dwarf or Orc?

'Let us find out!''You were right, ${PLAYER}! This was once Rushdurinul, the great throne room of Durin! The Orcs have surely given it a crude new name, but it will always be Rushdurinul to the dwarves!

'Fight on into the Orc encampment, and search for Bori, Bósi's son! I will watch the rear to ensure that no creatures from Zurr-thurkh surprise us while we are doing battle with the Orcs!''Search the Orc encampment for Bori, ${PLAYER}. I will wait here and guard the rear from attacks launched from Zurr-thurkh.''We will confront Mazog directly, ${PLAYER}, and force him to tell us where Bori has been imprisoned!''I got to thinking, ${PLAYER}, after you left, about all the things that you and others have been through, and I realized something: I can no longer stand by while others fight my fight.

'Once I resolved to leave my self-pity behind, I hurried to Buzun-ghâr and convinced the Elves there to come with me in pursuit of you. Our fortunes held, and we arrived just when most needed!

'I must hope that Bori is still alive, and that he is one of the two dwarves sent to Dol Guldur. It is only this hope that can keep me fighting.''The dwarf Bróin came to Buzun-ghâr not long after you left, and gave such a rousing speech that we could do nothing but follow him here. Who knew dwarves could speak with such vigour?

'And now he has a prisoner, and has spoken an oath beside. I hope it will not end poorly for Bróin or his friends, for there is a curious power to vows taken lightly.'You have been asked to rescue the dwarf-expedition that has been captured within the old armoury before they are devoured by the foul spiders who have woven a great nest within. Should you succeed, you have the blessing of Durin's Folk to make use of the anvil there to empower the infused adamant you bear.You must rescue the dwarves cocooned within the ancient armoury before they are devoured by the ravenous hatchlings from the nest.Rescue cocooned dwarves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the crystal brood-motherUse the ancient forge to empower your infused adamant.You have been called to speak with Celeborn of Lórien following the defeat of Mazog.You have been summoned to an audience with Lord Celeborn of Lórien, and should speak now to Haldir.Talk to HaldirCeleborn has called you to an audience in Caras Galadhon.Listen to what Celeborn has to say to youHaldir is waiting to speak with you about the worries of Lord Celeborn.Talk to Haldir'Lord Celeborn is waiting, ${PLAYER}. Come with me, for he greatly desires to speak with you.''Are you ready to leave, ${PLAYER}? I share Lord Celeborn's concerns; let us discuss them as we walk.'In the deepest dark of Moria there is a place where the only light that shone emanated from dwarf-lamps and luminescant fungus. Now, these delvings are dim and darker than ever and home to creatures that exist in nightmares. Yet here they are, and Veúlfur's agents sent to the Shadowed Refuge draw little comfort in knowing that there is something within the Dark Delvings that commands the Orcs to poison themselves in a manner that gives them over to some greater will.Complete the task set before you by Ymar, Moggi, Pentlenn and Glorelloth surrounding the Dark Delvings and then return to Gelirwen.

Gelirwen wishes to know what secrets the darkest halls of Moria can offer the expedition to the Shadowed Refuge.Help Ymar rid the Dark Delvings of the glowing wormsHelp Moggi rid the Dark Delvings of the terrible things in the darkRecover the runes from the Dark Delvings for PentlennDiscover the secret of the Dark Delvings for GlorellothGelirwen is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You completed all tasks set before you by Moggi, Ymar, Glorelloth, and Pentlenn and should return to Gelirwen with this news.Talk to Gelirwen at the Shadowed Refuge'Greetings, I have expected your arrival since first I saw the others in the Shadowed Refuge speaking with you. You show little fear of this place, but the right amount of respect to know that nothing here is safe. I also see that you do not let the gloom affect your heart, and this brings a smile to my face.

'I am here at the behest of Veúlfur, who is posted at the Twenty-first Hall, and I have been watching as you seek to discover the secret of the plague carried by the Orcs. I too am after this secret.

'There are four others here whom I have asked to assist me. I would ask that you entreat with them, here in the Shadowed Refuge before making your way into the Dark Delvings to discover what secrets they may hold. Ymar, Moggi, Pentlenn, and Glorelloth will all require your aid. Please, speak with them.''I will send word to Veúlfur and share with you great knowledge, given me by those you aided.

'The Gurvand you faced in the Dark Delvings was not the architect of this plague. Nay, it was the work of another, and we still do not know the identity of this creature. Its malevolence knows no bounds, and we shall need to remain vigilant here for signs that it might be rising ever closer to the surface.

'You have our thanks for aiding in this discovery.''Speak with Ymar, Moggi, Pentlenn, and Glorelloth ask them what must be done within the Dark Delvings. Once you have finished their tasks, I will send word to Veúlfur of all the aid you have rendered to us here in the Shadowed Refuge.'Defeat intruders within the Forgotten Treasury.Defeat enemies within the Forgotten TreasuryDefeat intruders within the Forgotten Treasury.Defeat enemies within the Forgotten TreasuryYour efforts within Tham Mírdain have not gone unnoticed by the Elves of Rivendell. Because of your unceasing aid in the defence of Mirobel, they have bestown upon you the title of Protector.Defeat the leaders of the invasion of the Library at Tham Mírdain.Defeat Chieftain GûrshDefeat Commander UnudhuDefeat Commander PiztorDefeat the leaders of the invasion at Tham Mírdain.Defeat StrokDefeat Priestess GráinneDefeat the leaders of the invasion of the School at Tham Mírdain.Defeat Llygad the BladeDefeat Commander TârshDefeat Chief Warrior ThurgtârkStrange lizards have recently come to infest the forests bordering the Anduin, killing off many of the native animals.Anduin lizards can mostly be found in Egladil in the south-east reaches of Lothlórien.

Farasdúr has asked you to defeat several of the Anduin lizards that have encroached upon the hunting grounds of the Galadhrim.Defeat Anduin lizards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Farasdúr is near the Vinyards of Lórien in Egladil.

You should speak with Farasdúr near the Vinyards of Lórien.Talk to Farasdúr near the Vinyards of Lórien'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. I am the master huntsman of Egladil and the lands surrounding it. I and my hunters provide much of the meat we partake of during feasts and banquets in Lothlórien, though we are careful never to take too much from the forest's bounty.

'Unfortunately, I have recently seen a new sort of creature about which threatens to throw matters awry -- a variety of large lizard that breeds along the banks of the Anduin. They used to be quite rare here, but of late their numbers have grown rapidly. Perhaps something evil has driven them from their territory upstream? I know not, but they are voracious hunters, and if we are to keep sufficient game within the bounds of Lórien's forests, then we must trim their numbers quickly. Will you lend us your aid?

'It is unfortunate that Aesbrennil has not yet found a proper recipe for their tough meat, or we would be well-lardered indeed upon these beasts.''Commendable work, ${PLAYER}. I have no ill-will towards those creatures, but their presence here threatens the bounty of Lothlórien. 

'Perhaps when this dark time has passed, they shall return to their rightful grounds and prosper there again.''The Anduin lizards are a vicious breed and must be driven from Lothlórien.'Collect samples of the blight that is corrupting the Sixteenth HallCollect samples of the blight that is corrupting the Sixteenth Hall.Collect samples of the blight that is corrupting the Sixteenth Hall.Find a sample of Virulent SporesFind a sample of Noxious SporesFind a sample of Infectious SporesFind a sample of Pestilent SporesSkûmfil is nothing more than a dumping ground, a place where the fallen Orcs of Moria are discarded when they begin to reek. It is here that two foes have gathered, each intent on using the corpses found therein for their own purposes. The kergrim and other scavengers as a source of food, and the insects as a place to lay their eggs to spawn future generations.Bonetooth and Old Gnawer are within Skûmfil, south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Odmar wants you to put an end to the kergrim-leaders who brought the corpse-eating creatures through the tunnels of Moria to Skûmfil.Defeat BonetoothDefeat Old GnawerOdmar is at the Shadowed Refuge, north-west of Skûmfil.

You found the two kergrim, one ancient and the other a summoner, and destroyed them both. Odmar, at the Shadowed Refuge will be pleased to know that this is done.Talk to Odmar at the Shadowed Refuge'Kergrim are disgusting creatures, feeding off the rotting flesh of the dead. I think it should be one's duty to destroy them. Nothing good can come of such behaviour.

'Look for Bonetooth and Old Gnawer, both kergrim. Find them and slay them so they can no longer perform their vile acts upon the dead.

'You will find them in Skûmfil to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.''It is good to know that we will no longer need to fear the likes of such creatures. Would that we should never need to do battle against such terrible foes again.

'Alas, that is not our lot. Still, you have done good work this day, ${PLAYER}. I thank you and will inform Throstur of your efforts.''I do not know how these beasts found their way within Skûmfil, but I think that we should be pleased to know that it will be our task to remove them. Head to the south-east and enter Skûmfil. Find the two kergrim, Bonetooth and Old Gnawer. Defeat them, then return to me.'Explore the Grand Stair.NOT USEDDire symbols warn against passage into this cave where a beastly menace bides its time, waiting to be wakened to unleash its terror upon he who disturbs its slumber.Filth and refuse bespeckle this wasted height upon which a misstep is ever threatened by a slip off a high, sheer drop.Feet that go thither blister and burn, for molten fluid bathes the ring where cruel Gothghaash kneels.Nardur of the White Hand guards this platform at this junction of passes within the Grand Stair, shielding each gateway from unwelcome visitors.After much wearying climbing, your tired feet have brought you to the Throne of Igash, the very centre of corruption in the Grand Stair.Maliriel has asked you to help her companions finish the prepartions for the upcoming banquet.There are lanterns along the path between Imlad Lalaith and Caras Galadhon. Wait for night fall, and then light them to help lead revellers to the feast.

As part of the preparations for the evening feast, Galhíril would like you to light the lanterns that will lead the evening revellers to the banquet.Light lanterns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Galhíril is at Imlad Lalaith.

You should return to Galhíril with your report.Talk to Galhíril at Imlad Lalaith'You are here to help with the preparations for tonight's feast? Ah! We shall make the night glow with lantern-light.

'The lanterns line the path on the other side of this gate. When night falls, I would like you to light them for me.''The lanterns are lit? Very good, ${PLAYER}.''Have you finished lighting the lanterns along the path yet?'Defeat the leaders of gredbyg in SkûmfilDefeat UammaethorDefeat UlugonDefeat NestaduanDefeat GrogDefeat GrothulunDefeat BrúmberethThe Sixteenth Hall is an area overrun with Orcs, many of whom suffer from a terrible illness that causes fungus-like growths on their bodies.

Mallas, an Elf ally to the dwarves, believes that there is something secret beneath the Sixteenth Hall and wishes to learn the true purpose and source of the plague.Guardians, curse-shouters, and fungal Orc bombs can be found in the Sixteenth Hall, north-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Odmar sent you to find and destroy the Orcs that he believes are leading this diseased incursion into the Sixteenth Hall.Odmar is in the Shadowed Refuge, south-west of the Sixteenth Hall.

You fought valiantly against the infected Orcs of the Sixteenth Hall and defeated many guardians, curse-shouters and the Orcs bearing terrible fungus. You should now tell Odmar that you did as he bade.Return to Odmar at the Shadowed Refuge'It falls to me to oversee the slaughter of the leaders of this disgusting encampment. The Sixteenth Hall was once used as housing and storage for the Dwarves of Moria, but now it is an infestation of Orcs!

'Well, I aim to put a stop to this problem. Enter the Sixteenth Hall, north-east of here, and remove the taint of the guardians, curse-shouters, and those especially dreadful Orcs that explode into spores when they draw near.

'Do these things, and then return to me when you are done, for I should like to count the notches on your weapon. This gloom on me will ease when I see evidence of the Orcs' downfall.''The filthy creatures deserve the disease that plagues them, but I will not sit by and abide their presence in our mines any longer. Get into the Sixteenth Hall and see that the clean-up effort is begun.''Your weapon is handsomer after this deed, is it not? See how it glows with pride! I will inform Mallas that you have done as I asked. You have the thanks and goodwill of the dwarves, my friend.'Defeat the leaders of the Nameless horrors within the Dark Delvings.Defeat the Void-eaterDefeat the Doom-speakerDefeat the Gurvand<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Acquire the Legend of Moria Title<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Complete Legendary Moria: Dark DelvingsComplete Legendary Moria: Fil GashanComplete Legendary Moria: SkûmfilComplete Legendary Moria: The Forges of Khazad-dûmComplete Legendary Moria: The Forgotten TreasuryComplete Legendary Moria: The Grand StairComplete Legendary Moria: The Sixteenth HallComplete Legendary Moria: FilikulComplete Legendary Moria: The Vile Maw<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Defeat The Mistress of Pestilence.<rgb=#00e4ff>Defeat The Mistress of Pestilence</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Defeat Gurvand.<rgb=#00e4ff>Defeat Gurvand</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Complete the Eregion - Library at Tham Mírdain instance.<rgb=#00e4ff>Complete the Eregion - Library at Tham Mírdain instance</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Complete the Eregion - School at Tham Mírdain instance.<rgb=#00e4ff>Complete the Eregion - School at Tham Mírdain instance</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for 