Completing this quest will unlock Legendary Moria: Vanquishing the Deep (Advanced), and can be replayed weekly. This quest will be removed on the weekly reset time, and so must be completed weekly by that time.</rgb>Complete FilikulComplete The Vile MawComplete Dâr NarbugudComplete Dark DelvingsComplete Fil GashanComplete SkûmfilComplete The Forges of Khazad-dûmComplete The Forgotten TreasuryComplete The Grand StairComplete The Sixteenth HallComplete Halls of CraftingComplete The Mirror-halls of Lumul-narComplete The Water Wheels: Nalâ-dûmComplete Library at Tham MírdainComplete School at Tham MírdainComplete The Battle of the Deep-wayComplete Battle of the Way of SmithsComplete Battle of the Twenty-first HallComplete Bult-kârComplete Fulz-zaharComplete Mekeb-fahamComplete Sejer-tharâkhComplete Tumun-ghârComplete The Battle of Lórien'There is much to be done, if we are ever to reclaim Moria.'

<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#FF00FF>Complete twelve quests and instances to aid those in Moria.</rgb>Complete FilikulComplete The Vile MawComplete Dâr NarbugudComplete Dark DelvingsComplete Fil GashanComplete SkûmfilComplete The Forges of Khazad-dûmComplete The Forgotten TreasuryComplete The Grand StairComplete The Sixteenth HallComplete Halls of CraftingComplete The Mirror-halls of Lumul-narComplete The Water Wheels: Nalâ-dûmComplete Library at Tham MírdainComplete School at Tham MírdainComplete The Battle of the Deep-wayComplete Battle of the Way of SmithsComplete Battle of the Twenty-first HallComplete Bult-kârComplete Fulz-zaharComplete Mekeb-fahamComplete Sejer-tharâkhComplete Tumun-ghârComplete The Battle of LórienThis quest is for Legendary Servers.Rilhathel is determined to sing songs of your efforts in defence of Lórien, and has issued you a truly legendary challenge in addition to simply repelling the Orcs.Rilhathel has asked you to not only successfully win the battle for Lórien, but to also defeat both Narshpug and Grakâmâb before they leave the field of battle, to prevent Belvagor from sustaining any serious wounds, and to do it all within thirty minutes.You must complete Rilhathel's most legendary challenge during the Battle of LórienRilhathel has asked you to not only successfully win the battle for Lórien, but to also defeat both Narshpug and Grakâmâb before they leave the field of battle, to prevent Belvagor from sustaining any wounds, and to do it all within thirty minutes.Successfully complete the Battle of LórienDefeat NarshpugDefeat GrakâmâbPrevent Belvagor from sustaining any serious woundsWin the battle within thirty minutesRilhathel is at Caras Galadhon, waiting to hear if you successfully completed his legendary challenge.Talk to Rilhathel at Caras Galadhon'I have devised numerous challenges for you to undertake, ${PLAYER}, but this one will surely be the most difficult -- and most rewarding -- of them all.

'During the next battle, you must defeat both Narshpug and Grakâmâb before they leave the field of battle, you must prevent Belvagor from taking any wounds, and you must successfully win the battle...all within half an hour.

'Lesser heroes might individually complete certain portions of this challenge, but only the greatest of heroes will be able to do them all at once. I look forward to hearing of your ability to do this, ${PLAYER}!''This will not be an easy challenge, ${PLAYER}. Only a truly legendary hero will be able to do defeat both Narshpug and Grakâmâb, prevent Belvagor from sustaining any serious wounds, and win the battle, all within less than thirty minutes.''I can hardly believe it, ${PLAYER}, but you have successfully completed my legendary challenge! Now this was a deed truly worthy of the songs of the minstrels!

'Take this reward and be content with the knowledge that you earned it with a truly spectacular display of prowess!'Lembas is the fabled waybread of Lórien, and a staple for those who stand long guard-shifts.Losdirith is at the entrance to the garden of Lady Galadriel. Minathlang is at the entrance to the city.

Basdan has given you packets of lembas to bring to the guards at various gates within the city.Basdan is on Telain Bangad in Caras Galadhon.

You have delivered packets of lembas to the guards and should return now to Basdan.Talk to Basdan upon Telain Bangad'Watching the gates of Caras Galadhon is hungry work, ${PLAYER}, and too often a thankless task.

'I have prepared packets of lembas for you to bring to guards at the various gates within the city: to Losdirith at the gate of the garden of Lady Galadriel and to Minathlang at the entrance of the city.

'I hope the lembas will restore the strength of the guards and tell them their service is appreciated by all of us.''You have delivered the lembas to the guards, ${PLAYER}? Very good! Take this for your trouble and know that you have made them feel that their service is appreciated, as surely it is by every member of the city!''Bring those packets of lembas to Losdirith at the gate of Lady Galadriel's garden and to Minathlang at the entrance of the city.''Thank you for this, ${PLAYER}! I will enjoy this lembas tremendously as the hours pass.''Thank you very much for this lembas, ${PLAYER}. Sometimes the hours pass in tedium, and it will give me the strength to maintain my vigil without complaint.'Find various texts in the Grand StairFind pieces of treasure within the Forgotten Treasury.Find various texts in the Grand Stair.Find Drums and the BeastFind the Highpeak Kennel ReportFind  Pleas of the LoyalFind the Tome of IgashThe Orcs of Moria forge weapons of war with which to assault Lothlórien, while the Iron Garrison and the Galadhrim seek to reclaim the Halls of Crafting and hinder their production.Complete Chieftains of the Halls of CraftingComplete Halls of Crafting Crate InvestigationComplete Halls of Crafting Melee Orc-slayerComplete Halls of Crafting Ranged Orc-slayerSkûmfil is nothing more than a dumping ground, a place where the fallen Orcs of Moria are discarded when they begin to reek. It is here that two foes have gathered, each intent on using the corpses found therein for their own purposes. The kergrim and other scavengers as a source of food, and the insects as a place to lay their eggs to spawn future generations.Lar, Moggi, and Pentlenn are at the Shadowed Refuge.

Mallas has told you that he will speak well for you to Veúlfur at the Twenty-first Hall after you have assisted his agents in the Shadowed Refuge.Assist Lar in ridding Skûmfil of gredbygAssist Moggi in ridding Skûmfil of gredbygCollect samples from the gredbyg of Skûmfil for PentlennMallas is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You have completed all the tasks set before you by Lar, Moggi, and Pentlenn. You should now return to Mallas and inform him that your efforts are complete.Talk to Mallas at the Shadowed Refuge'In nature, as it is here -- though more perverse and thoroughly corrupted -- the insects dwelling within Skûmfil will use the corpses of the Orcs there to feed their young. It is possible that these gredbyg are bringing disease to the unsuspecting Orcs who deliver the bodies to Skûmfil.

'I have set Lar, Moggi, and Pentlenn upon tasks needed to ensure that the insects within Skûmfil are not responsible for the plague spreading among the Orcs. Assist them as you can, and I will see that word reaches Veúlfur of your support against the dangers of Skûmfil.

'You can find my three agents here in the Shadowed Refuge.''It is clear that something within Moria has tainted these gredbyg. Now, their numbers are fewer.

'You will be spoken well of to Veúlfur, and you have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.''Speak with Lar, Moggi, and Pentlenn within the Shadowed Refuge. Return to me when you have completed their tasks, and I will inform Veúlfur of your assistance.'If the Hall of Mirrors can be liberated from Ergoth and Frost-tail, light may return to the Mines of Moria.Complete The Crystal Mirror-shardsComplete An Evil ReflectionComplete Lumul-Nar Morroval-slayerThe Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Bolg Maufulug lies to the west and a little north from Talan Fanuidhol.

Faelleron has asked you to enter Bolg Maufulug and collect any stolen belongings you find there.Collect crates of stolen belongings at Bolg Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Faelleron is at Talan Fanuidhol, east and a little south of Bolg Maufulug.

You should return to Faelleron with the stolen belongings you recovered.'${PLAYER}, many Galadhrim have fallen in battle here at the eaves of Lothlórien. The accursed Orcs of Moria have taken trophies of their victims...items belonging to the Elves who fell.

'Would you journey to Bolg Maufulug, one of the Orc-camps in Fanuidhol, and see if you can recover any of these items? It would be a pity if the Orcs defiled them -- though it is likely they have already done so.

'Bolg Maufulug lies to the west and a little north of here. Anything you bring back will be greatly appreciated.''The Galadhrim will be grateful for any stolen belongings you can return to us.''You have found more than I thought you would, and many of these items are yet unspoiled!

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}...I will return these to the families of the departed.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Drûmaudhul lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith.

Maeriel has asked you to enter Drûmaudhul and collect any stolen belongings you find there.Collect crates of stolen belongings at Drûmaudhul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maeriel is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Drûmaudhul.

You should return to Maeriel with the stolen belongings you recovered.'Many Galadhrim have fallen to the blades of Mazog's Orcs, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs have spirited away many items belonging to those Elves as trophies, and we wish them returned to us.

'Will you travel to the lumber-camp of Drûmaudhul and search for any of these stolen belongings? The encampment is large and surely well-guarded, but I am confident in your abilities.

'Drûmaudhul lies to the north-west of here. Recover what you can and bring it to me, and you will be rewarded.''The Galadhrim will be grateful for any stolen belongings you can return to us.''You have recovered more than I could have dreamed possible, ${PLAYER}! Thank you for your earnest efforts.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Mokûrz Gundul lies to the north-west from Talan Fanuidhol.

Faelleron has asked you to enter Mokûrz Gundul and collect any stolen belongings you find there.Collect crates of stolen belongings at Mokûrz Gundul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Faelleron is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Mokûrz Gundul.

You should return to Faelleron with the stolen belongings you recovered.'This is not acceptable, ${PLAYER}...the Orcs of Moria have defiled the bodies of our gallant defenders who have fallen and taken away trophies. Those stolen belongings must be recovered!

'Go to Mokûrz Gundul, one of the Orc-camps in Fanuidhol, and recover any of the stolen items that you can find. They belong to the families left behind.

'Mokûrz Gundul lies to the north of here. Anything you bring back will be appreciated.''The Galadhrim will be grateful for any stolen belongings you can return to us.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Most of these items remain unspoiled and may be returned to the families of their rightful owners.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Nardur-stazg lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith.

Maeriel has asked you to enter Nardur-stazg and collect any stolen belongings you find there.Collect crates of stolen belongings at Nardur-stazg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maeriel is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Nardur-stazg.

You should return to Maeriel with the stolen belongings you recovered.'The Orcs of Moria have stolen many beloved items from the bodies of those who have fallen defending Lothlórien from their assaults. I doubt not that many have been defiled or destroyed, but there must be some which can be recovered and brought to the families of the lost.

'Nardur-stazg is the chief encampment of the Orcs in Fanuidhol and the most dangerous to attack, but would you go there and recover what you may? I am sure some of the finest trophies have been sent there.

'Nardur-stazg lies to the north-west of here. Bring back any stolen belongings that you find, and you will be rewarded.''The Galadhrim will be grateful for any stolen belongings you can return to us.''Your bravery is undeniable, ${PLAYER}. Not many would enter Nardur-stazg to recover trophies for sentimental Elves.'Forbad thinks you should meet with Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel outside their majestic house.Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel can be found outside their house, high atop the greatest mallorn in Lothlórien. The carpeted path near Forbad winds up to the flet beneath the House of Celeborn.

Forbad has recommended that you speak with Celeborn and Galadriel and to take advantage of the opportunity to see the view from the top.Talk to Lady Galadriel in the House of CelebornTalk to Lord Celeborn in the House of CelebornForbad is at the base of the carpeted path that climbs the mallorn to the House of Celeborn.

You have spoken with Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel and should now return to Forbad.Talk to Forbad at the base of the carpeted path beneath the House of Celeborn'Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. This carpeted path winds its way up this tree, the mightiest mallorn in all of Lothlórien, until it arrives finally just beneath the House of Celeborn.

'You should climb your way up and speak with Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel outside their house and tell them what you think of your stay here in Caras Galadhon so far.

'Additionally, it will be a good excuse to see the view from high atop the mallorn!''You have come to Caras Galadhon, ${PLAYER}, and it is to be hoped that you will do what you can to ensure its safety and the well-being of its people.''I am pleased that you visited the Lord and Lady, ${PLAYER}, and trust you were welcomed by them to Caras Galadhon? Good. They are always gracious to their guests.

'Take this golden leaf as a keepsake of your visit.''Welcome to Caras Galadhon, ${PLAYER}. I hope you have had a comfortable stay in our city and that you will carry the memory of it with you when again you depart.''Make the most of your time here in Caras Galadhon, ${PLAYER}, and do what you can to remedy the worries of its people.''This carpeted path will take you to the flet just below the House of Celeborn. You should climb up the mallorn and speak to Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel...and admire the view from the top as well!''You are welcome in Caras Galadhon, ${PLAYER}. Remember your time here always and do so fondly.'Find the forgotten volumes of lore within the Library at Tham Mírdain.Find the forgotten volumes of lore within the Library at Tham Mírdain.Find the forgotten volumes of lore within the Library at Tham Mírdain.Find the Yellowed VolumeFind the Frayed VolumeFind the Ancient VolumeFind the Frail VolumeFind missing dwarves within the Vile Maw.Find missing dwarves within the Vile MawFind missing dwarves within the Vile MawFind the missing dwarf-merchantFind the missing dwarf-minerFind the missing dwarf-adventurerFind the missing dwarf-warriorSileffind believes that the Orcs of Moria are planning an attack on Lothlórien and wants you to search for their battle plans.Sileffind is in Caras Galadhon. Orcs and goblins on the outskirts of Lothlórien and throughout Moria may hold battle plans that will help the Elves prepare for the attack.

Sileffind has asked you to defeat Orcs and goblins and gather battle plans from them.'It seems clear to us now that the Orcs of Moria are planning an attack upon the Golden Wood, ${PLAYER}, and the more prepared we are for it, the better our defence will be.

'Search out Orcs and goblins wherever you find them on the outskirts of Lothlórien and throughout Moria and collect anything that might give us some insight to their battle plan.

'We will spread the word to other adventurers like yourself -- the more we can learn of the Orc plans, the better prepared we will be when the attack comes.''I thank you, ${PLAYER}, for these numerous plans. The schemes of the Orcs will be studied so that we may be prepared for the attack that is surely coming.'Donndageth has asked you to defeat Orcs within the many dungeons of Moria in order to lessen the forces available for their upcoming attack on Lothlórien.Strong Orcs and goblins can be found within the many dangerous dungeons within Moria: the Forges of Khazad-Dûm, the Forgotten Treasury, the Grand Stair, and the Sixteenth Hall.

Donndageth has asked you to defeat Orcs and goblins within the dangerous dungeons of Moria to limit the forces that might attack Lothlórien.Defeat Orcs and goblins within the dungeons of Moria (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Donndageth is at Caras Galadhon.

You have defeated many Orcs and goblins within the dangerous dungeons of Moria and should return to Donndageth with news of your triumphs.Talk to Donndageth at Caras Galadhon'The Orcs are going to attack Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}; that much is clear. It is still unknown when they will do so, but this foreknowledge will give us the strength to oppose them whenever it comes.

'Many of their strongest fighters dwell within the deepest and darkest dungeons of Moria: the Forges of Khazad-Dûm, the Forgotten Treasury, the Grand Stair, and the Sixteenth Hall.

'Defeat Orcs and goblins in these dungeons and return to me confident in the knowledge that we have weakened their attack force somewhat.''The strongest Orcs and goblins will be found within the dungeons of Moria, ${PLAYER}: the Forges of Khazad-Dûm, the Forgotten Treasury, the Grand Stair, and the Sixteenth Hall. Defeat many of them so they will not be able to attack the Golden Wood with all their force.''Very good, ${PLAYER}! Those foes will not join in the attack on Lothlórien, thanks to you.

'The battle steadily approaches, I am sure of it, but they will miss it. We, however, will not!'An attack on Lothlórien by the Orcs of Moria is surely coming, and Mithenn wants to ensure that the outposts on the border of exposed Fanuidhol are supplied.Mithenn inside Caras Galadhon wishes you to carry supplies he left outside the gates of that city to the base of Talan Fanuidhol.

Mithenn wants to ensure that the flets on the outskirts of exposed Fanuidhol are well-supplied for the Orc-attack.Pick up supplies outside the entrance to Caras GaladhonFaelleron is at the base of Talan Fanuidhol.

You have delivered a crate of supplies to Talan Fanuidhol and should now speak with Faelleron.Talk to Faelleron at Talan Fanuidhol'I do not know when the attack of the Orcs will come, ${PLAYER}, but it is surely coming soon. I worry for my brothers at the outposts on the border of Fanuidhol, for that land is exposed to the west, and from there the attack is likely to be launched.

'I have been bringing supplies just outside the entrance to Caras Galadhon. If you will carry some of these supplies to the base of Talan Fanuidhol, I will appreciate it and so will my brethren.''I left some crates of supplies just outside the entrance to Caras Galadhon, ${PLAYER}. Pick one of them up and carry it to the base of Talan Fanuidhol so my brothers there will be well-supplied for when the Orc-attack comes.''Thank you for bringing these supplies from my brother Mithenn, ${PLAYER}. It seems increasingly likely that the Orcs will soon begin their attack, and we will be glad to have these supplies.'Aesgyl has prepared some supplies to aid with the defence of Lothlórien from the Orcs of Moria.A stack of crates is next to Aesgyl on Telain Galadhrim. Sileffind is at the entrance to Caras Galadhon.

You have been asked to carry a crate to Sileffind at the entrance of Caras Galadhon.Pick up a crate from the stack near AesgylSileffind is at the entrance to Caras Galadhon.

You have delivered a crate to Sileffind and should now speak with him.Talk to Sileffind at the entrance to Caras Galadhon'The Orcs of Moria are a matter of great concern, ${PLAYER}, and we need to be prepared for the attack that is surely coming.

'Pick up a crate from the stack and carry it to Sileffind at the entrance to the city. But be careful, for you will not be able to climb any ladders while you are carrying the crate!''You can pick up a crate from the stack here and carry it to Sileffind, ${PLAYER}. He is helping prepare for the defence at the entrance to Caras Galadhon.''You need to speak to Sileffind now that you have delivered the supplies, ${PLAYER}.''Thank you for bringing these supplies here, ${PLAYER}! We will now be better prepared to stand against the Orcs.'Celegúien has asked you to recover arrows of the Galadhrim archers that have already been used to slay Orcs on the outskirts of the Golden Wood.Orc corpses are strewn along the north and south borders of Lórien, east of Echad Andestel.

Celegúien has asked you to find the bodies of Orcs slain by arrows along the outskirts of Lórien, and warned you against getting too close to the border. She wants you to recover the arrows so that they may be used again against the Orcs.Recover arrows from Orc corpses near the border of Lórien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Celegúien is in Echad Andestel, the camp along the banks of Nimrodel, west of the border of Lórien.

You have recovered arrows from the slain Orcs along the border of Lórien, and should bring them now to Celegúien.'The Orcs of Moria are numerous, ${PLAYER}, and have become bolder than ever in recent days. Some of them have even managed to pass the border of the Wood, though none of them will ever come again out of Lothlórien.

'The sharp eyes of the Galadhrim are quick to discern passage of the Orc-hosts, and any Orc so found cannot expect to live for long. But there are so many of the vile creatures that the arrows of the Galadhrim will be in short supply before much longer.

'Look for Orc corpses along the border of the Golden Wood, east of here, and recover arrows from their bodies. Do not get too near the border, for the Galadhrim may shoot you from hiding if they do not know you! Stray not too near to the border if you value your life.''Orcs that stray too near the borders of Lórien are slain by arrows from hidden Elves who guard this land. Travel east to the border of the Golden Wood and recover arrows from the Orc corpses so they may be used again. Be wary of getting too near the border, or you may be shot by the hidden Galadhrim!''Very good, ${PLAYER}. The Elf-arrow that kills more than one Orc is a lucky arrow indeed.'The merrevail of Ergoth strive to keep the mirrors of Lumul-nar darkened.Defeat merrevail in Lumul-narThe merrevail of Ergoth strive to keep the mirrors of Lumul-nar darkened.Defeat merrevail in Lumul-narBased on the sounds and odours wafting from near the entrance to Lumul-nar, Frár believes that the Hall of Mirrors is infested with bats... or worse. He does not think that the mirrors can be restored when their home is teeming with so many vile winged creatures.Lumul-nar, the Hall of Mirrors, can be found in Zirakzigil, to the north of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Frár has asked you to clear the Lumul-nar of bats and merrevail to make the place more suitable for the dwarves to take over.Defeat merrevail in Lumul-nar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat bats in Lumul-nar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Frár is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, to the south of Lumul-nar.

You should speak with Frár of your defeat of the many bat-creatures in the Hall of Mirrors.Talk to Frár'I believe Hrólfur wanted me to arrange this meeting with you because I am the only dwarf thus far to venture so near the entrance to Lumul-nar before my courage failed. I heard many chilling shrieks that made me tremble, and the smell was terrible.

'All I could imagine was fluttering bat-wings blocking out the sun, and where there are bats, there are surely fearsome merrevail to be found as well. These hideous creatures cannot be allowed to continue their inhabitance of this promising hall if the rumours of the mirrors are true.

'Go to Zirakzigil, north of here, and you will find the entrance to Lumul-nar as I did. If I were you, ${PLAYER}, I would bring a stout companion or two with you when you go.''The bats and winged creatures you seek will be in Lumul-nar, the Hall of Mirrors, to the north of here in Zirakzigil.''To defeat so many of the vile beasts was quite a feat, ${PLAYER}! You have done very well indeed against our foes in the Hall of Mirrors. We will surely be able to make progress there after your deeds today.'Frár of the Chamber of the Cross-roads explored near the entrance to Lumul-nar, the Hall of Mirrors, and recalls that a great feeling of menace turned him from his path.The Hall of Mirrors can be found in Zirakzigil, to the north of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.

Frár has asked you to defeat the menace that holds the Hall of Mirrors in its clutches. You should bring a friend or two on this dangerous venture.Defeat the evil presence in the Hall of MirrorsFrár is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, to the south of Lumul-nar.

You should speak with Frár and inform him of your success against Ergoth in the Hall of Mirrors.Talk to Frár'Hello, ${PLAYER}. Hrólfur tells me you are here to give us a leg up on our enemies. I will not turn my nose up at the help! The illumination of our halls will wreak havoc on the ill-accustomed eyes of Moria's foes.

'When I was exploring Durin's Way, I very nearly found myself in Lumul-nar, where you plan to go. But some great evil there sapped my will, and I decided I valued my life more than my curiosity at that particular moment.

'I saw and heard many clues of what terror may lurk within, but I do not wish to speak of it. All I ask is that you defeat whatever holds Lumul-nar, the Hall of Mirrors, in its evil clutches. But I beg you to bring a friend or two with you, for I had not the heart to make this venture alone.''The menace of Lumul-nar awaits you in the Hall of Mirrors, ${PLAYER}. You should strike north from here, towards Zirakzigil. The entrance to Lumul-nar is beyond there.''The creature is defeated? Then you have done what I could not! I applaud you, ${PLAYER}. Your services to the Iron Garrison will never be forgotten.'Frár believes that the greedy creatures of Lumul-nar may have some relics of interest in their possession, and wishes to know all that he can of any ancient tokens found in the Hall of Mirrors.Lumul-nar, the Hall of Mirrors, can be found north of the Chamber of the Cross-roads, in Zirakzigil in Durin's Way.

You should venture to Zirakzigil and search among the creatures there for any relics of Durin's time.Collect relics of interest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Frár awaits your return in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, south of Lumul-nar.

You should give Frár the many rings you collected from the foul creatures of the Hall of Mirrors.'The merrevail that I believe to reside in Lumul-nar are greedy creatures by nature, so I can only assume that they possess hoards of dwarf-relics. How my beard quivers to think of those distasteful wretches handling our precious goods!

'When you go to Lumul-nar, I bid you to reclaim as many such relics as you can from the creatures that dwell there. Curse their vile filth! I wonder what you will find when you go?

'You should bring a friend or two with you, ${PLAYER}. I do not think it will be easy to wrest the precious goods from the grasp of such horrid beasts as the ones you will face on this venture. I do not want to see you wheeled back to me in pieces, torn limb-from-limb by the greedy wretches of Lumul-nar.''Lumul-nar is north of here, in Zirakzigil. Be careful when you go! The creatures will not be glad to part with their treasures.''Rings! Of all the things I imagined, this was not one of them. These rings are lesser rings -- the seven Great Rings given to the dwarves were lost, yes, but lesser rings were handed out to those blessed by the favour of Durin. You have found them! We did not even know where to begin looking. Now the ancient heroes of Moria can be remembered as they deserved, for these rings are inscribed with their names and those of their families. I wonder if any of these families have survived to our generation....

'What a delightful project this will be, to reunite my folk with such an important piece of history! Thank you, ${PLAYER}!'The health of a certain type of birch, called Malbrethil by the Elves, seems to strongly affect the overall health of the forest. Mallendathor is worried about their declining numbers and health and wants you to investigate.Malbrethil-saplings can be found in Taur Hith, north-east of Cerin Amroth.

Mallendathor would like you to find and examine some Malbrethil-saplings.Examine Malbrethil-saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mallendathor is near Cerin Amroth, south-west of Taur Hith.

You should tell Mallendathor about the Malbrethil-saplings you found.Talk to Mallendathor at Cerin Amroth'Mae govannen, ${CLASS}. I am Mallendathor, one of the wardens of the revered woodlands of Cerin Amroth. I and my fellows have accepted the solemn charge of custodianship; we ensure that the forests are not thrown out of balance.

'A problem has come to my attention within the last few decades: a particular birch, the Malbrethil, has not been seen as often as in days past, and when it is sighted, the saplings seem spindly and overly delicate. I want you to find and examine some of these saplings, if you would, that we might determine the cause of their malady.

'I would suggest heading east, then north-east once you are past the low white cliff.''What ails the saplings of Taur Hith? Will you learn for me?''Brittle bark? Drooping boughs? These are not signs of any particular ailment with which I am familiar. I think we shall need to seek advice about this.'Your efforts within Tham Mírdain have not gone unnoticed by the Elves of Rivendell. Because of your unceasing aid in the defence of Tham Mírdain, they have bestown upon you the title of Marshal.Drive evil from Fil Gashan and the Forges of Khazad-dûmComplete Bane of IndustryComplete Bane of Fil GashanIn the deepest dark of Moria there is a place where the only light that shone emanated from dwarf-lamps and luminescant fungus. Now, these delvings are dim and darker than ever and home to creatures that exist in nightmares. Yet here they are, and Veúlfur's agents sent to the Shadowed Refuge draw little comfort in knowing that there is something within the Dark Delvings that commands the Orcs to poison themselves in a manner that gives them over to some greater will.The Dark Delvings lie far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Glorelloth warned that there is an evil present within the Dark Delvings that fears not the light. She cautioned you to tread carefully within the Dark Delvings located far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.Defeat the Evil within the Dark DelvingsGlorelloth is at the Shadowed Refuge, north-west of the Dark Delvings.

After making your way through the Dark Delvings you found the source of the evil there, an ancient creautre called the Gurvand. After a difficult battle, you destroyed the creature and now must return to Glorelloth at the Shadowed Refuge.Talk to Glorelloth at the Shadowed Refuge'Gelirwen asked me to discern what manner of fiend dwells deep within the Dark Delvings, but I have yet to understand the true horror within that hold. I know that there is great evil there, a nameless thing unaffected by the power of light. Radiance is rebuffed by the strength of its corruption. I know only that something there is evil beyond my understanding.

'So I caution you, ${RACE}, that when you enter the Dark Delvings you must be prepared for something as ancient as the Elves, savage and terrible.

'Discover what evil dwells there and return to me here at the Shadowed Refuge.''Such an evil can not be loosed upon the world. You have done well to drive it back into the darkness, though I do not think that an evil so great is so easily disposed. 

'I have hope within my heart that it is gone and know that you speak no lies to me now. The Gurvand is defeated -- at least for now -- and I will inform Gelirwen of your efforts.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''The nameless things within that place will not shy from the radiance in your hearts. In fact, I think that the dark shall strengthen them. While this is true, they may lose their strength in the light so be wise in your approach.

'Seek the source of evil within the Dark Delvings and return to me once you have dealt with it.'With the materials for building gone, the dwarves want to next eliminate the operators of the siege-weaponry.Moria siege-masters can be found at Drû-garmadh, south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Dagfari wants to next eliminate the Moria siege-masters who operate the great siege-weapons.Defeat Moria siege-masters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagfari is in Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh.

Dagfari will want to hear of the defeat of the siege-masters.Talk to Dagfari at Mekhem-bizru'The Orcs no longer have the materials to build more siege-weapons, which is a strong blow against their continuing ability to wage war; however, we have yet to reduce their existing ability.

'Our next strike needs to focus on making sure the weapons they have are useless. Return to the south-east, back to Drû-garmadh, and defeat the Moria siege-masters. Without them, the siege-weapons are nothing but piles of wood.''The siege-masters have fallen, and thus their weapons stand idle. We have little to fear from Drû-garmadh, yet there is one final strike yet to be made.''If the siege-weapons do not have masters, they are no threat.'Drive evil from the horrible deeps in the Foundations of StoneComplete Purifier of SkûmfilComplete Triumph within the Forsaken DeepsMaliriel has asked you to help her companions complete the preparations for the upcoming banquet.Boars can often be found roaming the forest north of the banquet grounds along the eastern border of Gelirdor.

Hadhelen has requested that you fetch boar-meat for the main course of the feast.Collect cuts of boar-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hadhelen is at the Vineyards of Lórien, far to the south of Gelirdor.

You should return to Hadhelen with the meat he requested.'What am I missing? Ah, of course -- meat for the spit. I have neglected my duties for the banquet and must quickly rectify the situation.

'There is a herd of boars that can be found along the eastern edge of Gelirdor a fair way north of here, though any boars of Lothlórien will do. Bring me back some nice, large cuts of boar-meat.

'Did I say something amusing? Do they not hunt boars in your lands?''I have not enough meat for the feast... hurry along and hunt some boars for me.''Ah, boar! There is nothing like it, is there? I do not think anyone could ever get tired of juicy....

'What is the matter with you, ${PLAYER}? Why do you roll your eyes every time I speak of boars?'Defeat Dunlendings in Tham Mírdain.Defeat Dunlendings in Tham MírdainDefeat many Dunlendings in Tham Mírdain.Defeat many Dunlendings in Tham MírdainUnbeknownst to the Dunlendings in Eregion, their largest camp has been built upon an ancient Elf-forge where some of the finest weapons of the early Third Age were once wrought. If use is to be made of this forge, the Dunlendings must be forced to retreat.Perimbant has asked you to bring him an infused adamant to imbue the quality you desire upon your weapon. He does not, however, know where you might find such a stone.Perimbant can be found at Echad Dúnann, west of the gates of Moria.

Perimbant has bidden you to speak with him when you are ready to depart for the Dunlending-camp, where you will conduct a midnight raid against the soldiers encamped there.Talk to Perimbant to travel to the Dunlending-campPerimbant can be found Echad Eregion, west of the gates of Moria.

You should return to Perimbant to complete the enhancement of your weapon.'There is but one forge remaining in Eregion where the quality you wish to obtain may be acquired. After the early years of the Third Age, the old smithy fell to ruin, and in this day the Dunlendings have built a large fortified camp upon them. Thankfully, they remain unaware of the significance of the ruins, but their presence complicates matters.

'I think it is time we did something about that camp, and though we have not the forces for a direct assault upon it, I have a more cunning, though un-subtle plan in mind.

'You must gather a small group of companions and prepare a midnight raid upon the camp! If you are successful, then making use of the forge should be within your grasp.''Ah! You were able to acquire an infused adamant. Now you will need to bring it to the Dunlending-camp.

'Let me know when you and your companions are ready to depart, and I will impart to you the plan I have devised.''If you and your companions are prepared, then you can set off. I have prepared a small boat for you to take up river to the eastern side of the camp, where my scouts say the defenders are the least watchful. Once you land you must quickly dispose of as many of the veteran guardsmen as possible, as they pose the greatest threat of spoiling the plan by raising an alarm.

'Once the threat of the guardsmen is removed, make your way to the centre of the camp where you will find a great bonfire that the Dunlendings keep well lit day and night. Once you reach it, you should put someone to the task of setting fire to as many of the tents surrounding it as possible, sowing chaos throughout the camp.

'If you can set enough of the camp alight, the remaining soldiers should quit the camp in fear, leaving you the space you need to do your work at the forge.''Ah, I rather wish I could have been there to see it. As much as fire is a clumsy weapon, it does make for a merrily lit evening by sword and bow, does it not?

'With the Dunlendings routed and their camp in ruins, we should have little to worry about from that quarter for a time.

'Now, let us see about imbuing the qualities you seek, shall we?'Aid the Malledhrim in securing their military objectives during the landing of their forces in Mirkwood.Complete any Mirkwood questComplete the final assault on the Orc fortress that controls the Mirk-eavesThere are two major, surviving towers in the ruins of Ost Galadh: Minas Celebolf and Minas Glórelloth. From these pinnacles, much of the expanse of Mirkwood may be seen.Climb Minas CelebolfClimb Minas GlórellothAn arrogant Orc named Târgrat holds great sway over many of his followers, and it would be best if he were removed from his post. Unfortunately, he commands a powerful troll bodyguard. Maenhador believes that the Orc's pride may be his weak point, if you can find some way to exploit it.Târgrat is at Nardur-stazg in Fanuidhol, north-west of Talan Fanuidhol.

In order to defeat Târgrat, despite the protection of his troll bodyguard, Maenhador has suggested that you try <rgb=#FF0000>mock</rgb>ing him before his underlings.Târgrat is at Nardur-stazg in Fanuidhol, north-west of Talan Fanuidhol.

In his rage over your insults, Târgrat the Proud has forsaken the protection of his bodyguard to pursue you personally. You must defeat him in battle.Defeat Târgrat the ProudMaenhador is at Talan Fanuidhol, south-east of Nardur-stazg.

You should return to Maenhador with tidings of your victory against Târgrat.Talk to Maenhador at Talan Fanuidhol'Our scouts report a particularly large and loud Orc by the name of Târgrat who commands many of the Orcs in Fanuidhol. He is a preening fool by all accounts, but dangerous nonetheless, particularly due to the huge troll who acts as his bodyguard.

'Nevertheless, pride goes before a fall, as they say, and I suspect that his pride is indeed his greatest weakness. If you were to <rgb=#FF0000>mock</rgb> him before his followers, he may well lose his composure and make a deadly mistake.

'This Orc can be found in the north-west reaches of Fanuidhol, in the encampment of Nardur-stazg.''Welcome back! How went your battle against Târgrat? Pride and vanity are ever the weakness of fools.''Târgrat is a proud and arrogant creature...he will not abide your mockery.''Târgrat is a proud and arrogant creature...he will not abide your mockery.'Gandalf the Grey fell in Moria, and his loss has been felt by many of the Elves he once knew.Losdirith watches the gate to the garden of Lady Galadriel, south along the path from the pavilion where Demlindeth sings songs of mourning.

Demlindeth has asked you to speak words of comfort to Losdirith, who has been acting strangely in the wake of Mithrandir's passing.Talk to Losdirith at the gate of Galadriel's GardenTelain Neduil consists of a series of flets north-west of Galadriel's Garden in Caras Galadhon, and the leaves grow over the edge of one of its flets.

Losdirith wants you to stand at the place he saw in his dream, within the canopy of leaves that cover part of a flet in Telain Neduil, and to <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for Gandalf.Losdirith is outside the entrance to Galadriel's Garden.

Losdirith will want to hear what you saw when you looked through the canopy of leaves at Telain Neduil, even if it is not what he hoped.Talk to Losdirith at the gate to Galadriel's Garden'You knew the Grey Pilgrim, ${PLAYER}, did you not? He was known by many names, travelling to and fro as he did, but to us in Lórien he was called Mithrandir. News came lately that he had fallen in the shadows of Moria; his travels now are ended.

'These three behind me sing now a lament for him, but the words cannot fully express the sorrow that descends even into Lórien at his passing. We will need time to mourn, but there is little time left to us in this Middle-earth. We will take our grief across the Sea.

'If you have words of comfort, save them for Losdirith, who watches the gate to the garden of Lady Galadriel. He has taken the fall of Mithrandir very much to heart, and I have heard that his grief has made him act strangely. Follow the path south to speak with Losdirith.''Mithrandir meant so much to all of us, ${PLAYER}, and his passing brings with it a measure of grief I did not ever think to feel. But it is not sorrow that fills me with these confusing thoughts. Nay, it is something else: a dream I have dreamed these past three nights, and I have no reason to believe I will not have it again this night.

'I dreamed I stood within golden leaves, high atop a flet, and as I stared through a break in the trees, I saw a great eagle in the north-east sky. And I heard the voice of Mithrandir, but I could not make out the words.

'There is such a place here in Caras Galadhon, ${PLAYER}! The leaves grow close over the edge of one of the flets of Telain Neduil, north-west of here. Stand there and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb>, and perhaps you will see something of Mithrandir!''You did not see anything, ${PLAYER}? I am saddened to hear it, but will not give up hope that my dream will one day come true. I will go myself to Telain Neduil every day, and perhaps one day I will see the sight of a Great Eagle bearing forth Mithrandir.

'I thank you for supporting me in this, even if it may seem futile to you. Mithrandir has fallen, but the lesson he taught to me is that even in dark times, we must hope for bright days to come.

'Take this as a token of my friendship, ${PLAYER}.''Telain Neduil is a series of flets north-west of here, ${PLAYER}, and the canopy of leaves intrudes upon one of the flets there. That is the place I saw in my dream, and perhaps if you stand there and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> into the distance, you will see something of Mithrandir!

'It may be a foolish hope, but the loss of Mithrandir is too much to bear.''Follow the path south until you reach the gate of Lady Galadriel's garden, for there you will find Losdirith. He has been acting strangely since we received news of Mithrandir's passing, and I would have you speak to him words of comfort.'Since the fall of Khazad-dûm, the ancient Water-wheels of Moria have become choked with lizards of varying sizes.Defeat lizards in Nalâ-dûmSince the fall of Khazad-dûm, the ancient Water-wheels of Moria have become choked with lizards of varying sizes.Defeat lizards in the Water-wheelsDór of the Chamber of the Cross-roads explored near the entrance to Nalâ-dûm near where the Water-wheels once turned, and he is concerned by the abundance of noisome croaking that emerged from within that grimy place. He is certain the the lizards' filth is at least partially responsible for the clogging of the Water-wheels.Nalâ-dûm, where the Water-wheels lie still, is below the Chamber of the Cross-roads in the Water-works.

Dór wishes for you to defeat lizards around the Water-wheels because of the damage they must wreak upon Nalâ-dûm. He warned that you should take a friend or two with you.Defeat lizards in Nalâ-dûm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dór is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, awaiting news of your venture into Nalâ-dûm.

You should return to Dór and tell him of your success against the lizards around the Water-wheels.Talk to Dór'I only ever walked by Nalâ-dûm briefly before I was turned away. I did not know that there were Water-wheels there, nor what they were for! I am glad you will be taking over my investigation.

'I have never seen these wheels, and I do not know what made them stop, but my memory now serves to give me a clue. I heard croaking as I drew near, the bellowing of lizard-throats. They are filthy beasts; I wonder if their muck is clogging the works.

'While you are there, you should defeat many lizards. As long as they are living there, the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm will never be clean as they should be. Return to me when you are done, and tell me if I guessed right. There are great dangers there, so I would take a friend or two.''You can find the Water-wheels by striking south from here, to the Water-works. Kill as many of those vile lizards as you can!''I am glad to hear you were so successful in dispelling the lizard presence. Excellent work!'Dór of the Chamber of the Cross-roads believes that worms will be among the creeping, slimy beasts in Nalâ-dûm where the Water-wheels sleep. The scales of rock-worms can be used to lend extra strength to armour.The scales can be found on the skins of worms in Nalâ-dûm, below the Chamber of the Cross-roads in the Water-works.

You should collect scales while in Nalâ-dûm for the dwarves to tailor into their armour. This will strengthen their defences significantly.Collect rock-worm scales in Nalâ-dûm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dór is north of Nalâ-dûm, in the Chamber of the Cross-roads in Durin's Way.

You should bring the scales to Dór so that he may begin to craft better armour for the dwarves of the expedition.'You will have your hands full when you go to investigate the Water-wheels, but I have a feeling you will also find yourself beset by worms when you are there. I find that worms infest every place where creeping things reside.

'The scales of rock-worms are hard as bone and can strengthen our armour with very little smithing effort. I'll not lecture you on our process of tailoring these scales to fit our hauberks, for I fear there isn't time for proper instruction.

'If you could collect some rock-worm scales while you are there, I would be very grateful. The scales may turn many an Orc-sword, and the warriors shall be in your debt.''Have you been yet to Nalâ-dûm in the Water-works? You may find the scales I seek upon the worms there.''So many scales! I am at your service, ${PLAYER}. I hope that you did not meet too much hardship in Nalâ-dûm.'Dór of the Chamber of the Cross-roads explored near the entrance to Nalâ-dûm where the Water-wheels once turned, and he recalls that a great feeling of menace turned him from his path.Nalâ-dûm, where the Water-wheels lie still, is far below of the Chamber of the Cross-roads in the Water-works of Moria.

Dór has asked you to travel to Nalâ-dûm and defeat the menace that lurks deep inside that forsaken hall. He warned you to take a friend or two with you.Defeat the menace in Nalâ-dûmDór is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads in Moria, above Nalâ-dûm in Durin's Way.

You should return to Dór and tell him of the Caerog you bested, thus removing the menace of the Water-wheels.Talk to Dór at the Chamber of the Cross-roads'Are you the ${CLASS} that bore the message from Lothlórien? Ah, so that means that you are the one who will be venturing into Nalâ-dûm to investigate the ancient Water-wheels. If you are, you should heed my warning: beware the menace that lurks in the deeps.

'I know that there is something there, but I do not know what. I was not foolhardy enough to go looking for the creature whose will made me shudder as I came near. Even if you can make the wheels turn again, it will all be for naught if the dwarves cannot maintain them for fear of being eaten alive.

'I would ask you to destroy the beast while you are there. Take care, ${PLAYER}! I do not think it will be easy. Perhaps you should take a friend or two.''If you want to best the menace of the Water-wheels, you should go to Nalâ-dûm, south of here, and far down into the deeps of Moria.''A Caerog! That is news indeed. I had no idea that a beast so foul had made its abode in Moria's great water-works of old. You deserve an ample reward for your deeds today, ${PLAYER}.'Defeat Nameless in the Dark Delvings.Defeat Nameless in the Dark DelvingsDefeat Nameless in the Dark Delvings.Defeat Nameless in the Dark DelvingsA particularly brutal and cunning troll named Dhît has been waylaying travellers in the Trollshaws as they attempt to reach Rivendell.Níels has asked you to seek out the troll Dhît in the western Trollshaws in the vicinity of the Stone-trolls' Glade and claim his club as proof of his death.Collect Dhît's clubNíels is at Esteldín in the North Downs.

You should bring Dhît's club to Níels.'Hey there, ${PLAYER}. If you've got a few stalwart friends who are willing to stand by your side, I've got a task for you.

'Dhît is the name...a troll, a big, nasty one by all accounts that has been waylaying travellers on the road towards Rivendell in the Trollshaws. Both the Elves and the Rangers would like nothing more than to hear that Dhît has come to an unfortunate end!

'The only news I have is that he usually lurks in the forests of the Trollshaws, somewhere north of the road, near some statues or the like? I heard that third-hand, and it didn't make much sense to me, but I hope it helps.''Have you dealt with Dhît? I can tell you that the bounty is worth the effort.

'Head to the Trollshaws and see if you can bring down the lumbering oaf.''My, my...now that's a club all right. I wonder where he found that? It's sure as silver that he didn't forge it himself, and no Man nor Orc could ever wield it.

'I'm thinking now that our little Dhît was likely a War-troll, lost or escaped from Angmar. That must have been a fight!'One of Níels' clients seeks a rare and unusual scale from the far north...a scale from Farathlúg the Ice-worm.Níels has asked you to seek out Farathlúg's cave along the northern edge of the Great Glacier in Forochel and collect his scales.Collect Farathlúg's scalesNíels is at Estldín in the North Downs.

You should bring Farathlúg's scales to Níels.'This is an unusual request, I'd say. One of my clients has a desire for rare and unusual things, you see, and now he wants the scale of an old northern ice-worm of all things.

'I asked my kindred prospecting up in Forochel to send word if they have seen such a creature, though I never expected to hear back from them. As it turns out, Lossoth lore speaks of such a beast that lairs along the northern slopes of some glacier.

'That is quite a trek and no mistake, but I can offer a substantial sum for your trouble if you succeed.''I suppose my client likes shiny worm-scales...though I can't for the life of me understand why.

'If you want this bounty, you'll have to journey to Forochel.''I can hardly believe it! You actually made the journey all they way to Forochel and fought that beast?

'Well, my client will be pleased, however you managed it, so let me see to your bounty.'Níels has offered a bounty for whoever can bring him the fur of Mangemaw, a deadly wolf of unusual cunning that has been devouring helpless hobbits in the Shire.Níels has asked you to seek out Mangemaw in Rushock Bog in the Shire and claim his pelt as proof of his death.Collect Mangemaw's peltNíels is at Esteldín in the North Downs.

You should bring Mangemaw's Pelt to Níels as proof of his death.'It looks like those hobbits have run into a problem quite a bit larger than themselves this time. An enormous wolf has sneaked into the Shire past the Rangers -- likely down from the forests of Evendim -- and has begun preying upon the locals. To hear the tale, you would think it was gobbling them up by the baker's dozen!

'You had best put a stop to it, and I am willing to pay a fair penny for whoever does. The Rangers haven't the spare men to hunt him down, or they would have pulled his tail already, but they say they are sure he's hiding out somewhere within the Rushock Bog.

'Do you care to take up the hunt?''The Shire has always had problems with wolves, but Mangepaw is something else altogether. The hobbits are afraid to go marshflower-picking!

'Mangepaw can be found in Rushock Bog.''Ah, I see you've found yourself a rather ratty pelt there...Mangemaw's is it?

'Well then, good hunt and done with, I say. Here's your bounty as we agreed.'The Rangers of Esteldín tell of a limrafn spirit named Morrafn which has lured many of their kindred to their deaths in the Fields of Fornost.Níels has asked you to seek out Morrafn among the ruins in the western Fields of Fornost and banish the spirit beyond the Void.Collect Morrafn's crystalNíels is at Esteldín in the North Downs.

You should bring Morrafn's crystal to Níels as proof of its defeat.'Good day, ${PLAYER}. Are you looking for some work? Well, here's a nasty bit of business that needs tending to....

'Something strange lurks in those barrows to the west, out in the Fields of Fornost. The Rangers say it is a spirit of some sort that has lured more than one of their scouts to an untimely end. It is like some wandering light bereft of its proper lantern, and they have named it Morrafn.

'The few Rangers available here are too young and inexperienced to face such a thing...do you think that you might be up to it yourself? There's a sizable sum involved if you can rid the Fields of the spirit.''I will not even pretend to know how to deal with a spirit...I only know that my client wants it gone.

'You can find Morrafn in the Fields of Fornost, west past Amon Raith.''What is this? A crystal?

'It is a strange and baleful glow that shines forth from it, and I'm betting this is what remains of Morrafn....

'Well then, I must see to your bounty!'The Elves of Rivendell have discovered a deadly drake living among the peaks of the Misty Mountains that threatens to consume any who attempt the crossing. They have offered a bounty to any who would take up arms against Rothlúg, the drake of Storms.Níels has asked you to seek out Rothlúg atop the ridges of the southern Misty Mountains and claim his scales as proof of his defeat.Collect Rothlúg's scalesNíels is at Esteldín in the North Downs.

You should bring Rothlúg's scales to Níels as proof of his death.'Listen closely, ${PLAYER}. It seems those oh-so-wise Elves in Rivendell have managed to get their trousers in a bunch over some great squalling lizard that has made a nest in the mountains above the House of Elrond.

'More to the point, they are offering a nice sum for anyone brave enough to rid them of it! Rothlúg is its name, and they say it only attacks in the midst of a great storm, so keep your eyes open.

'Oh, and you had best bring friends if you want to survive...otherwise I'll just save you the trouble and send your portion of the bounty straight off to the casket-maker in Trestlebridge....''The drake Rothlúg makes his lair in the Misty Mountains. I would be wary if you seek this bounty...but it is certainly worth your while.''It is a strange scale indeed...I've not seen its like before.

'Proof enough, methinks, that Rothlúg no longer flies over the peaks of the Misties, so I shall see to your bounty.'In the deepest sections of Moria, there are strange and frightening creatures. Veúlfur dispatched a host of his finest agents to the Shadowed Refuge to meet up with a company of Elves there to investigate rumours of the deep dark.Mallas, Throstur, and Gelirwen are at the Shadowed Refuge, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.

Veúlfur wants to better understand the enemy appearing from the edges of the shadowy dark. He sent you to the Shadowed Refuge to assist his agents and allies there with various tasks meant to divine the dangers and meanings of the nefarious creature found therein.Assist Mallas with his efforts at the Sixteenth HallAssist Mallas with his efforts at SkûmfilAssist Throstur with his efforts at SkûmfilAssist Gelirwen with her efforts at the Dark DelvingsVeúlfur is at the Twenty-first hall, north-west of the Shadowed Refuge.

You successfully assisted all of Veúlfur's agents at the Shadowed Refuge, earning from them honour and respect.Return to Veúlfur at the Twenty-first Hall'I have dispatched my agents to meet with the Elves who came to the Shadowed Refuge. They are at the Foundations of Stone now, and they all have tasks that I have set them to. We are too few in number to undertake them on our own.

'I would ask that you complete all the tasks set forth by Mallas, Throstur, and Gelirwen then return to me. We must understand better the foes that we face out of that dark place.

'You can find my agents and our Elf-allies within the Shadowed Refuge, located to the south-east of the Twenty-first Hall.''Orcs fear the place, but far be it from a dwarf to not enter a cave that needs exploring. My agents at the Shadowed Refuge south-east of the Twenty-first Hall can all use your help.

'Our allies there are also aiding us in better understanding just what kind of threat grows from that place. Will you go there and help Mallas, Throstur, and Gelirwen?''A terrible discovery is this Gurvand, creatures without heads, and Orcs being claimed by the fungus. What terror is this that dwells within the darkest depths of Khazad-dûm?

'Your efforts have done much to prove that there is indeed a great evil yet lurking within these halls. We are in your debt for assisting us in our investigations. Further, we are indebted to you for ridding us of such a terrible creature.

'We shall ever more call you a hero of our folk. You have our deepest thanks and will be written of in the annals of Durin's Folk, I promise you that, ${PLAYER}.'Concerned by all the recent upheaval disturbing Lothlórien, Tuilinn has had an idea for bolstering the morale of the Elves throughout the forest.Elanor and niphredil can be found upon and around the hill of Cerin Amroth.

Tuilinn has asked you to pick elanor and niphredil.Collect elanor-blossoms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect niphredil-blossoms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol, west of Cerin Amroth. Ambendel is in Echad Andestel, south-west of Cerin Amroth. Maliriel is at the Hythe, east and south of Cerin Amroth, by the river.

Tuilinn has asked you to bring elanor and niphredil-blossoms each to Bahanneth, Ambendel, and Maliriel the Feast-mistress.Tuilinn is atop the flet at Cerin Amroth.

You should return to Tuilinn and relate to her how her gift lifted the spirits of her friends.Talk to Tuilinn at Cerin Amroth'Turmoil threatens our Golden Wood for the first time in many a year, ${PLAYER}; the ravages of Orc-kind to the north-west, the unusually aggressive river creatures to the south-east... I worry that fear may be taking more of a toll upon us than we might admit.

'I have an idea, and if you will help me see it to completion, it may aid in staving off the insidious dread that is the Enemy's weapon. Now, the golden flower we call elanor and its pale counterpart, niphredil, are nearly as much in the heart of every Elf as is Cerin Amroth itself, the hill upon which they grow. Their smell revives us; their gentle colours rest our eyes. Please, pick some and bring them to my friends elsewhere in Lothlórien.

'Maliriel is the Feast-mistress at Imlad Lalaith: follow the road east and south until you reach the Hythe, by the river. Ambendel is at Echad Andestel -- you may already have met him. Retrace your steps back to northern Nimrodel, south-west of here. Talan Fanuidhol is west of Cerin Amroth; there you will find Bahanneth, the quartermaster.''White niphredil and yellow elanor... the beautiful flowers of Lórien. Pick some and bring them to my friends.''White niphredil and yellow elanor... the beautiful flowers of Lórien. Pick some and bring them to my friends.''Your pardon, friend, but I have no time to speak with you just now; there is too much to do to prepare for tonight. Whatever message Tuilinn has can wait... what have you for me?

'Elanor! And sweet niphredil. These shall have pride of place at my table tonight. Their smell will enhance every dish!

'My sincere thanks. Please, tell Tuilinn that she knows well how to lift a busy Elf's spirits.''Whence come you, friend, bearing pale niphredil and golden elanor?

'From Tuilinn at Cerin Amroth! My heart is gladdened by her gesture and by yours in bearing these blossoms here.

'Ah, these flowers never seem as bright when plucked from other hills! My sincere thanks to you, friend ${CLASS}; know that Ambendel is at your service.''I have no time just now for any... what is that aroma? By sea and stars! Whence came these blooms?

'Tuilinn has, as always, cut to the heart of the matter in her own quiet way. My steps are now lightened.

'I shall display these, that all the warriors here might also benefit from their sweet smell.''Niphredil and elanor... beautiful flowers to brighten these dark days.''Thank you for the lovely flowers, ${PLAYER}... they will find a place of honour at the feast.''Standing watch upon the borders of Lothlórien can oft lead to a dreary spirit... thank you for lifting mine once more!''Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. The hearts of Elves throughout the Golden Wood beat a little more lightly thanks to your errand.'You have brought some arrows to Celegúien, and now she wants them delivered to Meredhrandir at Mekhem-bizru.Celegúien has a bundle of arrows for you to deliver on the crates by her in Echad Andestel. She wants you to carry them to Meredhrandir at the camp of Mekhem-bizru, very near to the entrance to Moria. She advised you to follow the road west and north as it passes through Nanduhirion, and to beware of Orcs on the road.

You have been asked to deliver arrows from Echad Andestel to Mekhem-bizru.Pick up a bundle of arrows next to CelegúienMeredhrandir is at Mekhem-bizru, right by the eastern entrance to Moria.

You have brought a bundle of arrows to Meredhrandir and should speak to him about the journey.'The arrows you have brought to me will have a second chance at slaying Orcs, ${PLAYER}, but their chance will come nearer to the entrance to Moria, from which the Orcs pour into Nanduhirion.

'My friend Meredhrandir journeyed to Mekhem-bizru, the outpost far to the north-west, very near to the entrance to Moria. He will be able to make use of these arrows if you bring them to him with all speed.

'Pick up a bundle of arrows on the crate to my right and carry them to Mekhem-bizru. You will need to follow the road to the west all the way through Nanduhirion; beware of Orcs on the road, and do not let the arrows get wet! You will be unable to hold onto them if you enter deep water.''Carry a bundle of arrows to my friend Meredhrandir at Mekhem-bizru, the camp at the end of the road that runs through Nanduhirion, right by the entrance to Moria. Pick up a bundle of arrows from the crate right next to me, and follow the road to the west all the way back to the camp outside Moria!''I can tell these arrows have already slain an Orc or two. How many more of the creatures will fall to each of these, I wonder?

'You have done most well, ${PLAYER}. Your efforts will not be forgotten by the Elves of Lórien.'The Warg-pits of Dol Guldur are overseen by the goblin Athgrat and the Warg Kranklob, vile servants of the Enemy.Defeat AthgratDefeat KranklobFil Gashan is the barracks and mustering point for the Orcs' invasion of Lothlórien. Hidden deep within the fiery landscape and sharing an adjacent entrance to the Forges of Khazad-dûm, Orcs train here under the watchful eye of General Talug.Fil Gashan lies to the south-west of Anazârmekhem.

Yngvi has asked you to enter Fil Gashan and defeat General Talug. He suggested that heating the General's armour may make him more vulnerable to attack.Defeat General TalugYngvi is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of Fil Gashan.

You found a way to defeat General Talug and turned his forces against him. With the general defeated, it is possible that Mazog and his army will be slowed to a crawl. You should return to Yngvi and tell him this news.Talk to Yngvi at Anazârmekhem'It is my charge to tell you about General Talug, and that is not an easy thing to do. We only saw him once, speaking to the Orcs within Fil Gashan. He was attended by goblin-aides. I remember that one used fire and another oil. Talug himself is clad in thick armour, against which even dwarf-made weapons are almost futile. But it makes him slow, and metal gets hot when heat is applied.

'Aside from this, we only know that he is Mazog's chosen general and thus his right-hand. Defeat Talug and cripple Mazog? It is a difficult question to answer, but we can hope this is the case.

'You will need to scour Fil Gashan, south-west of Anazârmekhem, to find the General.''With the General removed, the forces of the Orcs are diminished and ripe for the picking. This is a happy day, my friend.

'We owe you much. I will tell Teitur that you have performed beyond the scope of my expectations. You will forever have my thanks.''Use your wits! I have a feeling they will help you more than anything else while battling Talug. Find him in Fil Gashan, south-west of Anazârmekhem. Return to me when the deeds is done.'You have heard it whispered that the libraries of Moria yet contain many tomes, while many other volumes were brought by the dwarves seeking to reclaim their ancient realm. One such tome in the libraries of the Iron Garrison is said to be the legendary "On the Patterns of Wind and Rain." If you can gain enough favour with the Iron Garrison Guards, they may let you have their copy of this book.Achieve level 58Read the book, "On the Patterns of Wind and Rain"Defeat Orcs within the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Defeat Orcs within the Forges of Khazad-dûmDefeat Orcs within the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Defeat Orcs within the Forges of Khazad-dûmDefeat Orcs in the Sixteenth HallDefeat Orcs in the Sixteenth HallDefeat Orcs in the Sixteenth HallDefeat Orcs in the Sixteenth HallDefeat the leaders of the invasion within the Forges of Khazad-dûm.Defeat NarkûDefeat DhaubDefeat ThrugDefeat KranklûkDrive evil from the Sixteenth HallComplete Corruption in CommandComplete Investigating the BlightComplete Orcs of the Sixteenth HallComplete Fallen to BlightComplete Carriers of the BlightThe Sixteenth Hall is an area overrun with Orcs, many of whom suffer from a terrible illness that causes fungus-like growths on their bodies.The Watchers of the Sixteenth Hall are in the Shadowed Refuge in Moria. The Elves and dwarves you seek are named Lar, Ymar, Odmar, Pentlenn, and Glorelloth.

Mallas has asked you to help his fellows at the Shadowed Refuge do various tasks in the Sixteenth Hall.Aid Glorelloth: collect fungus from the Sixteenth HallAid Pentlenn: collect samples from the Sixteenth HallComplete Odmar's task in the Sixteenth HallComplete Ymar's task within the Sixteenth HallComplete Lar's task in the Sixteenth HallThe Elf Mallas is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You have completed the tasks set before you by the dwarves Ymar, Lar, and Odmar and the Elves Glorelloth and Pentlenn, and should now bring tidings to Mallas of all that has transpired.Return to Mallas at the Shadowed Refuge'I am glad that Veúlfur was able to earn the favour of so stout a warrior as yourself. We are in need of such spirit in this darkened place. The gloom here clouds our sight and disheartens even the hardiest among us.

'Veúlfur likely told you that I am charged with watching the Sixteenth Hall, and with the aid of dwarf and Elf alike, I am cataloguing my findings to report to Veúlfur of any significant movement in this area. If you are willing to aid in our vigil, I will be certain to mention your assistance in my report.

'There is much to be done. I suggest speaking to the others who aid me already. Each can be found here within the Shadowed Refuge. Lar, Ymar, and Odmar are the dwarves who mind the Sixteenth Hall, and the Elves are named Pentlenn and Glorelloth. When you have spoken to them and given them what they need, return to me with tidings.''Would that we had greater numbers and were not daunted thus by the Sixteenth Hall. As such, however, we must rely on the assistance of others to learn what threat looms in the darkness.

'Speak with Odmar, Lar, Ymar, Pentlenn and Glorelloth in the Shadowed Refuge for instruction.''This is ill news. The appearance of a nameless evil such as this beneath the Peasant Halls belies an even greater corruption of the Orcs than I foresaw.

'Your information gives us but a piece of the puzzle that is unfolding in depths. It is clear, though, that the curse-shouters here are working to infect other Orcs for some fell purpose. What it is, I cannot guess.

'Yet it is good to know that the disease is not something that can be passed easily among enemies of evil such as ourselves.'The Water-works house many creatures and types of life. The dwarves have yet to delve and catalogue even a fraction of the changes in this mysterious environment.Collect unusual plantCollect strange plantCollect abnormal plantCollect large plantCollect colourful plantAsmund has one final request of you: to hunt the Hornéd Wood-lord, mightiest of the animals protected by the Elves of Lothlórien.The Hornéd Wood-lord roams the Golden Wood in an area called Egladil, in south-east Lothlórien.

Asmund has asked you to undertake one last hunt: to claim the antlers of the Hornéd Wood-lord.Hunt the Hornéd Wood-lord for his antlersAsmund is in Echad Andestel, west of the border of Lothlórien.

You have hunted the Hornéd Wood-lord for his antlers and should bring them now to Asmund.'This will be my final request of you, ${PLAYER}, for it is my greatest hunt, and will be the last I ask you to undertake beyond the border of Lothlórien!

'Deep within the woods, protected by the Elves, lives the Hornéd Wood-lord, a creature of such impressive size and stature that its horns far surpass those of any creature that walks in Middle-earth!

'It is said that the Hornéd Wood-lord walks in the Golden Wood in an area called Egladil. Bring me his antlers, and I will reward you greatly!''It is said that the Hornéd Wood-lord's antlers are unsurpassed by any other creature that walks in Middle-earth! I must have them, ${PLAYER}, even though the Hornéd Wood-lord is protected by the Elves. Look for him in a place called Egladil, in south-east Lothlórien.''You have hunted the Hornéd Wood-lord, ${PLAYER}? Let me see those antlers!'

Asmund's face falls as he examines them.

'These are not as impressive as I was expecting, ${PLAYER}. I had thought, after all the stories, that these would be bigger. If I had known...

'What's done is done, I suppose. I promised you a reward, and you shall have it, though I am filled with a regret I had not expected.'Pleased with your previous hunt, Asmund has another request of you.Protected boars can be found within Lothlórien, in places called Eryn Laer and on the banks of the Anduin in Gelirdor.

Asmund has asked you to hunt protected boars within Lothlórien.Hunt protected boars in Lórien for boar meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Asmund is in Echad Andestel, west of the border of Lothlórien.

You have hunted the protected boars of Lothlórien and should return now with the meat to Asmund.'I like you, ${PLAYER}. You wouldn't believe how difficult it is to find a kindred spirit on this side of the mountains, and a ${CLASS} to boot!

'If you're willing, I have another hunt for you to undertake: boars within the Golden Wood are said to have the most tender meat you ever tasted, and I know I could get a good price for a haunch or two. The Elves protect many of the boars, of course, but I know you won't shy away from helping me out!

'It's said that there are protected boars inside the woods, in places called Eryn Laer and on the banks of the Anduin in Gelirdor. I've never been, of course, but that's what they say.''Hunt the protected boars of Lothlórien for me, ${PLAYER}. It's said they can be found in places called Eryn Laer and in Gelirdor, though I've never seen them. The Elves do not allow me inside.''Splendid, ${PLAYER}, splendid! This meat will surely fetch a high price! I can see why the Elves valued those boars so highly!

'I have one last hunt for you, my friend. The most valuable yet!'Asmund has asked you to poach protected deer within Lórien, and has promised to reward you for doing so.Protected deer can be found in Lórien, wandering in Nan Celebrant and Gelirdor.

Asmund has asked you to hunt the protected deer of Lórien, promising to reward you well for it.Hunt protected deer in Lórien for deer meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Asmund is in Echad Andestel, west of the border of Lórien.

You have hunted some of the protected deer of Lórien for Asmund and should return now to him.'Hello there, my friend! I understand that you are permitted beyond the borders of the wood? I have a proposal for you, and I hope you will give it some thought. You will be well-rewarded for it!'

Asmund flashes a toothy smile and goes on.

'The Elves that live in the wood have some very strict rules concerning what animals they hunt; certain animals fall within their protection, and are off-limits for hunting.

'The meat and hides of these animals are said to be of extremely high quality. If you don't mind, since you have access to the woods and I do not, could you hunt a few of these protected deer? The Elves surely won't miss the few you hunt for me! I have heard they can be found in places called Nan Celebrant and Gelirdor, though I have not seen these places for myself. I thank you for the consideration, my friend. If you do as I ask, you'll find yourself well rewarded!''Since you have access to the woods and I do not, I will reward you very well for hunting the protected deer of Lórien. I understand you can find them in areas known as Nan Celebrant and Gelirdor, though I have not seen these places for myself.''Excellent, ${PLAYER}! I am glad that your hunt went so well, and as promised I have a reward for you.

'And not just that, but more work as well, if you'd like it!'Bahanneth's scouts report that the Orcs of Fanuidhol may be preparing to attempt some sort of incursion or even a siege of Lothlórien. He has asked you to take some pre-emptive measures to disrupt their plans before they pose any real threat.The lumber and crates are at the Orc-encampment of Drûmaudhul, north-west of Talan Fanuidhol.

Bahanneth has asked you to sabotage the lumber the Orcs have cut for their war-machines. He also wants you to steal the contents of the storage crates from their surrounding encampments.Soak lumber-pile with liquid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect contents from crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol, south-east of Drûmaudhul.

You should return to Bahanneth with the metal parts and let him know of your success.'I am Bahanneth, the Quartermaster of this force. Are you here to help in our struggle against the Orcs? Our scouts have noticed that they are cutting a great deal of lumber -- likely for use in constructing fortifications and siege-engines. We must not stand by while such a threat develops!

'Were matters more urgent, I would ask you to burn those supplies, but as things are not yet that pressing, I would have you take these phials of liquid and apply it to their wood piles before they are finished curing. This will weaken the wood, rendering it useless for their purposes -- but without their knowledge.

'The Orcs have also recently brought a number of crates out from their stores deep in Moria -- I would like you to steal the contents of a number of these crates so that we can perhaps guess at what evils they are preparing.''Without strong wood and other materials, the Orcs will not be able to bring their siege engines against us.''Excellent! These parts were for the construction and repair of siege-weapons. The Orcs shall have to make do without them, thanks to your efforts.

'You also dealt with their supplies of lumber? That is well.'Thangúlhad is being assaulted by the forces of Dol Guldur. They wish to reclaim it and eliminate the foothold the Golden Host has secured.Rodelleth is the commanding officer at Thangúlhad. She is waiting for you to report in.Talk to RodellethThe forces of Dol Guldur are marching against the defences of Thangúlhad. You must protect the fort and keep it secure.Defeat the first assaultThe first assault has been defeated, but the battle is far from over.Defeat the second assaultThe second assault has been defeated, but the battle is far from over.Defeat the third assaultThe third assault has been defeated, their numbers are beginning to thin.Defeat the fourth assaultThe fourth assault has been defeated. The Enemy is launching one final desperate assault against the walls of Thangúlhad.Defeat the fifth assaultThe enemy leader is approaching: a fearsome Olog-hai. Rodelleth wishes to discuss the final battle-plan with you.Talk to RodellethThe enemy leader has challenged you to come and fight him outside the protection of your fortifications. Fortunately, Rodelleth is manning the catapults.Defeat Mazaukal and claim the Enemy's banner'It is good you are here. The others stationed here are all out on patrol, and I fear the Enemy is stirring.''Prepare yourself, this battle is not yet over.''You have aided me greatly. They picked an excellent time to strike, while our patrols were out. Were it not for you, this forward position would have been lost.'Thangúlhad is an advance position of which the Golden Host has managed to wrest control from the forces of Dol Guldur.Complete everything in the Protectors of Thangúlhad SkirmishDefeat BorndolDefeat RuithrovalDefeat AzríDefeat HokarulDefeat GrudomDefeat FrúzglobDefeat GolugthrugDefeat LapusDefeat TorúglupDrive evil from SkûmfilComplete The Fallen HeroesComplete The Corpse-eatersComplete Leaders of the HiveComplete The Hounds of SkûmfilComplete The Horrors with Many LegsComplete The Corpse-beasts of SkûmfilComplete The Blighted  OnesThe Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Bolg Maufulug lies west and a little north from Talan Fanuidhol.

Caredwen has asked you to attack Bolg Maufulug and defeat any enemies you find there.Defeat enemies at Bolg Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Caredwen is at Talan Fanuidhol, east and a little south of Bolg Maufulug.

You should return to Caredwen with the tidings of your victory at Bolg Maufulug.Talk to Caredwen at Talan Fanuidhol'${PLAYER}, I fear that Mazog's forces are growing too strong. While they may not be able to pierce the defences the Lady Galadriel has placed upon the Golden Wood, they may keep us at bay, unable to march against the Shadow.

'It is up to us, then, to make certain they remain weakened. Every day, more Orcs pour forth from Moria to reinforce their assault force. I need you to enter the encampment of Bolg Maufulug and defeat any enemies you find there.

'Bolg Maufulug lies to the west and a little north of here. When you have done this deed, return to me.''The enemy presence at Bolg Maufulug has been weakened? This is good news for us, ${PLAYER}! Your aid is much appreciated.''Head a little north and some distance west to Bolg Maufulug and deal with the enemy there.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Drûmaudhul lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith.

Belegoth has asked you to attack Drûmaudhul and defeat any enemies you find there.Defeat enemies at Drûmaudhul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Belegoth is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Drûmaudhul.

You should return to Belegoth with the tidings of your victory at Drûmaudhul.Talk to Belegoth at Talan Gwilith'${PLAYER}, I have a vital task for you. Drûmaudhul is a lumber-camp used by the Orcs of Moria to prepare their siege-engines. We need to remove this threat from the borders of Lothlórien.

'Go to Drûmaudhul and defeat any enemies you find there. This encampment is one of the largest in Fanuidhol and should not be approached lightly.

'The encampment lies to the north-west, beyond Golugrak and Gazpush. Return to me if you should succeed.''Ha! That should hinder Mazog's efforts for a while.

'It is a victory, ${PLAYER}, but I fear a temporary one.''Drûmaudhul supplies the Orcs of Moria with the wood they need to build their siege-engines...the encampment must be razed, ${PLAYER}.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Mokûrz Gundul lies to the north from Talan Fanuidhol.

Caredwen has asked you to attack Mokûrz Gundul and defeat any enemies you find there.Defeat enemies at Mokûrz Gundul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Caredwen is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Mokûrz Gundul.

You should return to Caredwen with the tidings of your victory at Mokûrz Gundul.Talk to Caredwen at Talan Fanuidhol'Mokûrz Gundul is the largest of the Orc-encampments in the southern reaches of Fanuidhol. It is vital that we eliminate the threat this camp imposes upon Lothlórien.

'Travel there, ${PLAYER}, and deal with any foes you find. Do not expect this encampment to be as easy to defeat as their smaller encampments, such as Gazpush.

'Mokûrz Gundul lies to the north of here. Return to me when you have completed this task.''You have made your presence felt at Mokûrz Gundul, and that is all we can ask. Your aid will greatly reduce the Enemy's ability to assault the Golden Wood.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}!''Mokûrz Gundul lies to the north, ${PLAYER}. This is the largest of the encampments in the southern reaches of Fanuidhol...it is vital that this threat is eliminated.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Nardur-stazg lies to the north-west from Talan Gwilith.

Belegoth has asked you to attack Nardur-stazg and defeat any enemies you find there.Defeat enemies at Nardur-stazg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Belegoth is at Talan Gwilith, south-east of Nardur-stazg.

You should return to Belegoth with the tidings of your victory at Nardur-stazg.Talk to Belegoth at Talan Gwilith'Nardur-stazg is the chief encampment of the Orcs of Moria in the northern reaches of Fanuidhol. It is a dangerous task, but I must ask you to enter Nardur-stazg and defeat any enemies you find there.

'This encampment is a danger to all who dwell upon the eastern side of the Misty Mountains. The threat must be put to rest.

'Nardur-stazg lies far to the north-west of here. When you have defeated the enemy there, return to me.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! Laying low the enemy at Nardur-stazg is quite an accomplishment!

'Accept this reward as a token of my gratitude.''Nardur-stazg is the chief encampment of the Orcs in Fanuidhol. The threat of it must be removed, else the Orcs will only grow stronger.'The dark hole known as Dâr Narbugud was only briefly glimpsed by Durin the Deathless...and even he wanted nothing to do with the place.Complete the Hierarchy of the NamelessComplete Dâr Narbugud Nameless-slayerComplete Dâr Narbugud Orc-slayerComplete Dâr Narbugud Troll-slayerComplete Dâr Narbugud Fungus-investigationThe legacy of Durin's Stone is now threatened by one final force: Istash, a powerful Orc from the depths of Moria.Istash is at Uruk-gashan, south of Mekhem-bizru.

Haflith believes Durin's Stone will never be safe until Istash, an Orc-leader, is defeated.Defeat IstashHaflith is at Mekhem-bizru, north of Uruk-gashan.

Haflith will be pleased to hear Istash has been defeated, and Durin's Stone remains safe.Talk to Haflith at Mekhem-bizru'You have done everything I have asked, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for that, but we are not yet done. The audacity of these fiends amazes me. It is not enough that we have cast down their sappers, nor gathered up what they attempted to destroy. They persist!

'One Orc in particular is leading the entire throng. I will die before I see him succeed in tearing down what remains. This must end here and now.

'Return south, to Uruk-gashan and defeat Istash. Durin's stone will never be safe so long as that foul Orc still walks among the living.''I will die before I see him tear down Durin's Stone.''You have done it! Istash has fallen, Durin's Stone still stands, and my heart weeps with joy. We dwarves are not an emotional people, as I am sure you have found in your ventures, but the destruction of Durin's Stone would have made any dwarf sob.

'You have the thanks of all dwarves, and I am proud to call you my friend. Durin's Stone will continue to stand for many generations to come, and serve as a place where all dwarves can come and remember who we are... and why we are here.

'All dwarves have you to thank for that. We are at your service.'Recover Lugazag from the forces of Angmar and fulfil your duty here in the Ettenmoors.Recover Lugazag from the forces of AngmarRecover the Grimwood Lumber-camp from the forces of Angmar and fulfil your duty here in the Ettenmoors.Recover the Grimwood Lumber-camp from the forces of AngmarRecover the Isendeep Mine from the forces of Angmar and fulfil your duty here in the Ettenmoors.Recover the Isendeep from the forces of AngmarRecover Tírith Rhaw from the forces of Angmar and fulfil your duty here in the Ettenmoors.Recover Tírith Rhaw from the forces of AngmarRecover Tol Ascarnen from the forces of Angmar and fulfil your duty here in the Ettenmoors.Recover Tol Ascarnen from the forces of AngmarMeredhrandir at Mekhem-bizru is concerned for your well-being with all the Orcs of Moria so stirred in the Dimrill Dale. He has recommended that you seek refuge in Lórien and appeal to the good will of Haldir at his talan, which is hidden.The talan of Haldir is at the banks of the Nimrodel, south of the road that leads to the broken bridge.

Meredhrandir at Mekhem-bizru has urged you to seek the protection of Haldir before you come to harm so near the stirring mouth of Moria.Speak with Haldir at his talan'So you have come through the dark halls of Moria to sunny Nanduhirion, have you? Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. The eaves of Lórien are near, and if you gain the trust of my people you shall find refuge beyond the Nimrodel. These are very dangerous times in which we live.

'Word of your ventures has reached my ears. I bid you what welcome I can as you emerge from the darkness, and I say this to you also: take care! Many evil things have stirred from the dark, and this dale is not safe.

'Upon the Nimrodel is a talan belonging to Haldir, a protector of the eaves of Laurelindórenan. He will offer you refuge. The way is hidden! Seek him beyond Echad Andestel, and wet your feet in the Nimrodel, near the bridge that is broken. South of that bridge and upon the shore is a great mallorn-tree. Upon that tree you shall find Haldir. He will trust you if he knows you have come with my leave.''Haldir and his brothers are the Marchwardens of Lothlórien. They make their post at a flet to the south-east.''Welcome to Lothlórien, ${CLASS}. We have had many strange visitors of late. You shall find refuge here, if refuge you seek. I am very pleased to make your acquaintance, for even in this remote place we have heard rumour of your valour.'Bróin believes that Gorothúl gave a relic of evil to the merrevail that infest the Mirrors of Lumul-nar.The entrance to the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar is outside, on Zirakzigil, near the ruined crater where the Balrog lies smouldering.

Bróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.Talk to Bróin and travel to Mirror Halls of Lumul-narBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located between Zirakzigil and Durin's Way.

You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.Talk to Bróin in the Peaceful Path'Now that Orvar has destroyed the hidden relic Gorothúl left in Buzun-ghâr, that cave should be free of danger. We need not fear that Grawulun or others of his kind will return to that place.

'But Gorothúl may have left other relics of evil throughout Moria; indeed, I think it likely, and recent reports from our scouts indicate one such location: the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar. Merrevail have corrupted the mirrors of Lumul-nar that once fed light from the outside into the deep reaches of Khazad-dûm; the light no longer shines. A number of explorers ventured to Lumul-nar to investigate. Few returned, reporting that the merrevail of that place have been given great courage; their defiance is strong. What else have they been given, I wonder? A relic of Gorothúl's?

'The entrance to Lumul-nar is on the side of Zirakzigil, amid the snow. Find the relic inside, if it exists, and destroy it.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest is a Solo version of the dungeon.</rgb>''I knew it, ${PLAYER}! I knew you would find Gorothúl's relic in Lumul-nar. It is good you destroyed it. The merrevail we should be able to keep in check; if the relic had drawn Grawulun or another Caerog to Lumul-nar, our success might not be as sure.''I shall have a friend lead you to the  Mirror Halls of Lumul-nar.'Bósi believes another of Gorothúl's relics may be found at the bottom of Nalâ-dûm, where the great wheels of Khazad-dûm lie dormant.Bósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way.

Bróin has told you to speak with his uncle about the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roadsThe entrance to Nalâ-dûm can be found in the Water-works of Moria.

Bósi reports that a relic of Gorothúl's lies among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm and will require careful usage of the mechanisms to reach and destroy.Talk to Bósi and travel to Water-works of Nalâ-dûmBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located off Durin's Way.

You have destroyed the relic left in Nalâ-dûm by Gorothúl and should report your success to Bósi.

You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.Talk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads'My uncle Bósi sent word while you were out. He thinks he knows where another of Gorothúl's relics may be found, and the location is just as dangerous as Lumul-nar, if not more so: the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.

'Travel to the Chamber of the Cross-roads with your allies and speak with my uncle to learn more about Nalâ-dûm.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest is a Solo version of the dungeon that can be attempted if you have completed a version of Chapter 4: A Relic in Nalâ-dûm.</rgb>''My uncle Bósi thinks he knows where another of Gorothúl's relics may be found: among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm.

'Go speak to him in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, off Durin's Way, and he will tell you more about Nalâ-dûm.''Greetings again to you, ${PLAYER}! I did not have the opportunity to properly thank you for helping to broker this alliance between the Iron Garrison and the Elves of Lothlórien. So I thank you! In Mazog, we have a prisoner worthy of exchanging for those Gorothúl brought to Dol Guldur: my son chief among them. O Bori! Be strong and courageous during your torment!

'Scouts report seeing a relic of unquestionable evil among the Water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm, but were unable to route the flow of the canals in such a way as to reach it. You must determine the proper workings of the system if you are to find and destroy this relic of Gorothúl's.

'I shall have a scout lead you to the entrance of Nalâ-dûm in the Water-works. Delving into the flooded deeps will be dangerous, for the mechanisms are very old and have not been used for many years.''The entrance to Nalâ-dûm lies in the Water-works. I shall send a guide to lead you to the entrance.

'Are you ready to journey forth?''Very well-done, ${PLAYER}. The destruction of that relic should keep further evils from being drawn to the Water-wheels.

'Now we must look to the future.'Dindirith wants you to return the filth you cleaned from the banks of the Nimrodel to the Orcs.The Orc camps of Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul can be found all along the road that runs through Nanduhirion, west and north of Echad Andestel.

Dindirith has asked you to burn the Orc filth you collected in one of the fires the Orcs have set in their camps in Nanduhirion.Dindirith is in Echad Andestel, the camp north of the road outside Lórien, and east of Nanduhirion.

You have disposed of the Orc filth and should return now to Dindirith.'We will show the Orcs that the Elves of Lórien will not tolerate their presence here, ${PLAYER}. Bring the Orc filth you scoured from the banks of Nimrodel to one of the fires in the Orc camps of Nanduhirion, to the north-west, and set it aflame.

'The reek of the burning will send a message to the Orcs of Moria: no stain on these lands will be permitted from this day forth.

'Follow the road west and north into Nanduhirion and look for the Orc camps along the road: Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, or Athmadhul. Burn the Orc filth in one of their fires, and return to me when you have disposed of it all.''I know you have done what I asked, ${PLAYER}, for I could smell the reek from here. The Orcs should know now that no offence against the land will go unanswered.

'Thank you for your aid, ${PLAYER}.''There are Orc camps all along the road that runs through Nanduhirion to the west of here. Burn the Orc filth you collected from the banks of Nimrodel in one of the fires inside the camps, and then return to me.'Skûmfil is nothing more than a dumping ground, a place where the fallen Orcs of Moria are discarded when they begin to reek. It is here that two foes have gathered, each intent on using the corpses found therein for their own purposes. The kergrim and other scavengers as a source of food, and the insects as a place to lay their eggs to spawn future generations.Skûmfil lies to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Ymar told you that he was set to the task of ridding Skûmfil of the disease-carrying cave-claws within.Defeat cave-claws in Skûmfil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the kergrim-summonerYmar is at the Shadowed Refuge, north-west of Skûmfil.

You found your way to Skûmfil and destroyed the cave-claws there, halting the spread of the disease that they carry.Talk to Ymar at the Shadowed Refuge'This task does not come from my dreams, but from the words of Throstur who told me that these creatures bring disease.

'The kergrim and their ilk, the cave-claws digging beneath the stone tunneling towards their quarry -- tunneling towards the corpses they eat in Skûmfil -- bring terrible disease. 

'We must rid the place of these carriers, in order to help purge the disease. You must go to Skûmfil, south-east of the Shadowed Refuge, and rid the place of these disease carriers.''Ridding the place of disease is a task worthy of a ${CLASS}, is it not? Destroy the bearers of the disease so that it cannot spread.''I will tell Throstur of your efforts. He will be pleased that this is done.

'I thank you, friend. I thank you.'The Warg-riders in the Dimrill Dale have been terrorizing the dwarf-encampment at Mekhem-bizru. With the Wargs thinned, it is now time to strike at the riders.Moria riders can be found at Athmadhul, south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Ótam wants you to defeat the goblins training to become new Warg-riders.Defeat Moria riders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ótam is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Athmadhul.

Ótam will be pleased to hear the goblin Warg-riders have been defeated.Talk to Ótam at Mekhem-bizru'The Wargs have been severely reduced, and that is good, but I have no doubt their numbers will soon be restored. Their weakened state right now, however, gives us our opportunity to strike at their heart.

'There are many goblins at Athmadhul who now lack Wargs to ride. If you were to attack them, they would not have their mounts to aid them, and they should fall easily in combat.

'Return to Athmadhul to the south-east and defeat the Warg-riders.''The goblins were defeated before new mounts could arrive. Very good tactical strike. Now there is but one more thing to do.''If we attack the goblins before they can ride, then they are not Warg-riders. They are only goblins, and goblins we can defeat handily.'Find the forgotten manuals of Ring-lore within Tham Mírdain.Find the forgotten manuals of Ring-lore within Tham Mírdain.Find the forgotten manuals of Ring-lore within Tham Mírdain.Find the Torn Manual of Ring-loreFind the Aged Manual of Ring-loreFind the Dusty Manual of Ring-loreFind the Rotten Manual of Ring-loreFind hidden rune-stones in the Dark DelvingsFind hidden rune-stones in the Dark Delvings.Find hidden rune-stones in the Dark Delvings.Find a Sparkling Rune-stoneFind a Chiselled Rune-stoneFind an Ancient Rune-stoneFind a Dim RunestoneMaenhador seeks to disrupt the lines of communication among the Orcs attempting to assault Lothlórien.The Orc-scouts can be found running to and fro throughout eastern Fanuidhol, to the north of Talan Fanuidhol.

The scouts that have accompanied the expeditionary force of Moria Orcs into Fanuidhol are quick and clever. They ensure that the Orc-leaders are well-informed, enabling them to make deadly decisions. Maenhador has asked you to put an end to them.Defeat Orc-scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maenhador is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Fanuidhol.

You should return to Maenhador with news of your success.Talk to Maenhador at Talan Fanuidhol'Greetings to you, friend. Are you here to help in our martial endeavours against the invading Orcs? If so, I have a small assignment for you. The Orcs frequently employ runners and scouts to deliver messages between their camps, and we will hamper their efforts to coordinate their warriors if these scouts are defeated.

'If you would be so kind as to defeat a few of these message-runners, I would be much obliged.

'They have been spotted patrolling throughout the eastern half of Fanuidhol, north of here.''Ah, you have returned. Tell me -- are the scouts' numbers reduced?''The eyes of Moria must be put out...have you dealt with their scouts yet?'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Bolg Maufulug lies to the west and a little north from Talan Fanuidhol.

Bahanneth has asked you to enter Bolg Maufulug and defeat the Orcs there. He has also asked you to collect any stolen belongings you find as well.Collect crates of stolen belongings at Bolg Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat enemies in Bolg Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol, east and a little south of Bolg Maufulug.

You should return to Bahanneth with the stolen belongings you recovered and news of your victory against the Orcs.'Your efforts on behalf of my fellow marchwardens are commendable, ${PLAYER}, but alas, the Orcs of Moria continue to pour out of the Black Hole and my kinsmen continue to perish from Middle-earth.

'I must ask you to sally forth once more into Bolg Maufulug and defeat the foe there. If you should find any more belongings stolen from the fallen Elves, please bring those to me as well, so that they can be returned to the families of the lost.

'Bolg Maufulug lies to the west and a little north of here. Anything you bring back will be greatly appreciated.''The Galadhrim will be grateful for any assistance to us that you can grant against the Orcs of Moria. Any stolen belongings you can recover for us would be much appreciated as well.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs have suffered another defeat at your hands, and the Galadhrim will benefit from the recovery of their kinsmen's belongings.'The Orcs of Moria have begun mustering in Fanuidhol in preparation to assault Lothlórien.Drûmaudhul lies to the north-west from Talan Fanuidhol.

