Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.Sendiel is in Gelirdor, south-west of the Malbrethil-trees, east of Cerin Amroth.

Orthir instructed you to tell Sendiel of your success.Talk to Sendiel in Gelirdor'If you are willing to be of further aid, ${PLAYER}, I would ask that you seek out the counsel of Orthir, a Scholar of the Trees who has made the woods of Lothlórien, and especially the majestic trees in and around Cerin Amroth, his particular study. Describe to him the symptoms you found on the Malbrethil saplings and follow his advice. You will find him not far west of here, near the path.''Speak with Orthir...who should know what to do about the ailing Melbrethil.''Mae govannen. You were sent from Mallendathor? Very well, what assistance do you need?

'Ah! The Melbrethil! The first Malbrethil-tree was a gift from those who dwell beyond the Sea. We prize them so because they listen to the harmonies of Middle-earth itself and breathe them out to their surroundings. But you say they are suffering? This is no small matter....

'I fear that since our lands have been...visited...by so very many of the friends and allies of Gandalf the Grey and Elrond Halfelven, the forest and its beasts have been quieter--frightened, perhaps. I think that you might remedy this were you to <rgb=#FF0000>sing</rgb> to the saplings. Any song will do. Perhaps hearing of your homeland will strengthen them. When you have sung to them, seek out Sendiel, another warden of the woods, whom I last saw in a clearing in Gelirdor, south-west of the hill of the First Malbrethil.''Have you spoken yet with Orthir? If so, I would do as he instructed you.''Raise your voice in song, ${PLAYER}...only then will the Melbrethil heal.''Sendiel will wish to know of the marvelous cure of the Melbrethil!''You should let Sendiel know that your song was strong enough to bring life to the Melbrethil.''Whence do you come, ${CLASS}? From Orthir? That is strange; he usually has little patience for visitors. Perhaps you should start from the beginning....

'Singing to the saplings! What a lovely cure--marvellous in its simplicity! If we are to take what the Scholar of the Trees says to heart, more music will have to be made throughout these woods, to replace the natural tunes of beasts and birds that have been silenced by the trampling of so many feet.

'The mention that you say Orthir made of the first Malbrethil-tree has given me an idea....'Hasta has asked you to deliver the specimens you gathered to his friend Hethuwen in the Shadowed Refuge.Hethuwen can be found in the Shadowed Refuge, in the south-eastern reaches of Moria.

Hasta has asked you to take the package to his friend Hethuwen in the Shadowed Refuge.'All right, ${PLAYER}. Now that we've gathered evidence that there are some unusually strange creatures in the Water-works, we ought to have someone more knowledgeable than I take a look at what you've collected. Such a person should be able to shed some light on the matter.

'My old friend Hethuwen conducts studies of this sort in Shadowed Refuge, for she has a curious nature. Seek her there, and tell her I sent you to speak with her. She should be able to offer insight that will be helpful to us.''Take that package at once to Hethuwen at the Shadowed Refuge!''Well met, ${PLAYER}. How can I be of service to you? I hope nothing dire has brought you here this day.'

Hethuwen takes the package you brought and reads the note attentively.

'I see...Hasta, my zealous friend, is pursuing another wild rumour.'

Hethuwen shakes her head and a slight sigh can be heard passing her lips. She does not trouble to hide her amused smile.

'All right, all right, ${PLAYER}. Very well. I will help Hasta once more, but this is the last time! Just give me a few moments to look over these specimens, and I shall see whatever there is to see.'Tuilinn, delighted by the success of her plan to bolster the morale of her friends, wants you to visit them regularly bearing blossoms from Cerin Amroth.Elanor and niphredil can be found upon and around Cerin Amroth.

Tuilinn has asked you to pick more elanor and niphredil.Collect elanor-blossoms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect niphredil-blossoms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol, west of Cerin Amroth. Ambendel is at Echad Andestel, south-west of Cerin Amroth. Maliriel is at the Hythe, east and south of Cerin Amroth, near the river.

Tuilinn has asked you to bring elanor and niphredil-blossoms to Bahanneth, Ambendel, and Maliriel the Feast-mistress.Tuilinn is atop the flet at Cerin Amroth.

You should return to Tuilinn and relate to her how her gift lifted the spirits of her friends.Talk to Tuilinn at Cerin Amroth'The blossoms of niphredil and elanor that you brought to my friends were so well-received, ${PLAYER}, that I think a delivery of peace and cheer should become a regular occurrence! Will you retrace your steps? Pick six of each flower and deliver them to the same three Elves you did before.

'Do you remember the way? Maliriel is the Feast-mistress at Imlad Lalaith: follow the road east and south until you reach Hythe, by the river. Ambendel, if you recall, is at Echad Andestel. Retrace your steps back to northern Nimrodel, south-west of here. Talan Fanuidhol is west of Cerin Amroth; there you will find Bahanneth, the quartermaster.''Niphredil and elanor, ${PLAYER}, are found in few other places than Cerin Amroth.''Take the flowers you collected to my friends, ${PLAYER}... they will receive them gratefully, I am certain.''${PLAYER}, the sight of you gladdens my eyes as the scent of the blossoms you bear gladden my heart.

'Blessings upon you and upon Tuilinn.''I maintain that these flowers are not as bright nor as aromatic if they are plucked from other hills!

'My thanks once more, friend ${CLASS}; Ambendel remains at your service.''Mae govannen, friend! Bring you more flowers from Tuilinn?

'Ah, elanor, and sweet niphredil... you quicken the bow-arm and lighten the gait of every warrior under my command with this errand.''The flowers are beautiful, ${PLAYER}... thank you much for bringing this bit of light into the dark world.''Thank your for the flowers, ${PLAYER}... they will join their sisters in honour at the feast.''Perhaps I shall send my warriors into battle with niphredil and elanor in their hair... perhaps the Orcs will be driven into a careless frenzy by their beauty!''Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. The hearts of Elves throughout the Golden Wood beat a little more lightly thanks to your errand.'Menassiel is an artist tasked with supplying pigments to other artists in Caras Galadhon. She has asked for your help in gathering the base ingredients for some of the more dramatic colours she will be making.Menassiel in Cerin Amroth wishes you to collect chalk and red berries, to create the stark colours that help make Elven art so striking.

Chalk can be chipped from white rocks to the north. Gather red berries from the bushes that can be found in the forests to the west.Collect chalk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect red berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Having collected the raw materials for red and white pigments, you should bring them back to Menassiel at Cerin Amroth.'Mae govannen, friend. I am Menassiel. How fare you and whither go you?

'I? I am here to gather some of the elanor that grows so brightly upon this hill; an extract of the juice from its stem and heart make a marvellous golden-yellow colour. The creation of pigments and paints is an art unto itself, nearly as engaging as the uses to which I and my fellow-artists put them. Unfortunately, it is time-consuming... unless -- if you had some time to aid me, it would be most appreciated.

'You have not the knowledge of refining the raw ingredients, but you could help gather them. Stark white chalk can be pried out of the soft white rocks all along the rock-face north of here. Berries from some of the local plant life provide the base for a vibrant red dye. These bushes grow in relative abundance in the forests west of Cerin Amroth.''Have you yet found the materials I need to make the pigments for the artists?''You have returned! Please, let me see what you have gathered....

'Wonderful, ${PLAYER}, wonderful. These supplies are of excellent quality -- perhaps you, too, have a little of the artist about you?

'It would be most welcome were you to return and help me gather these ingredients while you are here; perhaps I can stockpile enough to remove the need for another such trip for a good long time!'Menassiel is an artist tasked with supplying pigments to other artists in Caras Galadhon. She has asked for your help in gathering the base ingredients for some of the more dramatic colours she will be making.Menassiel in Cerin Amroth wishes you to collect chalk and red berries, to create the stark colours that help make Elven art so striking.

Chalk can be chipped from white rocks to the north. Gather red berries from the bushes that can be found in the forests to the west.Collect chalk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect red berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Having collected the raw materials for red and white pigments, you should bring them back to Menassiel at Cerin Amroth.'You are willing to help me again? Blessings upon you!

'Artists throughout the Golden Wood produce a near-insatiable demand for the basic colours. Do you recall where to find the raw ingredients required?

'Chalk can be pried out of the soft white stone along the rock-face to the north, and you should also seek berry bushes in the woods to the west, from which you can gather red berries.''Have you yet found the materials I need to make the pigments for the artists?''Again, you have a good eye for raw materials. Any time you wish to help me with this, you will be welcome to do so!'Skûmfil is nothing more than a dumping ground, a place where the fallen Orcs of Moria are discarded when they begin to reek. It is here that two foes have gathered, each intent on using the corpses found therein for their own purposes. The kergrim and other scavengers as a source of food, and the insects as a place to lay their eggs to spawn future generations.Skûmfil is south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Pentlenn would like to study the innards of the gredbyg at Skûmfil to see if there is any disease within them that could be affecting the Orcs.'The malevolence of the gredbyg of the deep dark of Khazad-dûm is clear. What is unclear, however, is whether or not these insects bear disease or are otherwise responsible for the plague affecting the Orcs.

'I would ask that you collect the innards of these insects from within the area called Skûmfil. I can better appraise whether there is disease within the gredbyg, and thus better inform Mallas if the insects pose a greater threat to us than what we expected.

'You can find Skûmfil by heading to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.''I will take time to study these and determine if there is a threat to be found here. I will tell Mallas of your efforts.

'I thank you for all you have done, ${PLAYER}.'Hasta has asked you to investigate reports of strange creatures lurking in the Water-works.The creatures under suspicion are rumoured to be found to the south and west of the Rotting Cellar.

Hasta has asked you to confirm the reports of strange creatures in the Water-works by bringing back sufficient evidence of their existence.'Well met, ${CLASS}. I'm here on account of reports concerning strange creatures roaming about these parts. Presumably the creatures are off to the south and west throughout the watery regions of this area. I would like you to confirm the rumours and bring back sufficient evidence of their existence.

'If you find anything to verify my concerns, be sure to look for a suitable sample of their flesh. I have a friend who can discern the nature of these beasts by looking at their hides.

'Return to me here when you've done what I ask, and we shall proceed from there.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. May I have a look before you bring them to my friend?'Hethuwen has examined the contents of the package you brought her and discovered a disturbing substance. Hethuwen has asked that you bring the sample, along with her extensive notes, back to Hasta in the Water-works.Hasta is at the Rotting Cellar in the Water-works, far to the west from the Shadowed Refuge.

Hethuwen has given you a phial of the substance she uncovered during her experiment, along with copious notes. She has asked you to bring these to Hasta in the Water-works.'I've examined the samples you brought me and discovered a strange substance that I have not seen before.'

Hethuwen hands you a phial filled with a dull, green slimy substance and a note full of hastily written information.

'If you would be so kind, ${PLAYER}, please take this sample and my notes back to Hasta. In this letter I ask him to send you to look formore of this substance. You should try to find the source in order to find a pure, original sample for a more thorough observation. Perhaps then we can get to the bottom of this.

'I am sure Hasta is anxious for news in the Water-works. Make what haste you can, ${PLAYER}. I fear this is not the laughing matter I suspected it would be.''You must hurry and bring the sample and letter to Hasta in the Water-works at once!'Hasta takes the phial and reads the note with rapt attention.

'This is strange indeed! Hethuwen is a very knowledgeable master of lore and learning. If this substance is new to her, as seems to be the case, I am troubled.'Defeat Orc-fighters within Fil GashanDefeat Orc-fighters within Fil GashanDefeat Orc-fighters within Fil GashanDefeat Orc-fighters within Fil GashanThe ancient Elf-ruins of Dannenglor howl during the dark Mirkwood nights.Complete everything in the Strike Against Dannenglor SkirmishDefeat HelchfaerDefeat GhostfangDefeat RuingaladDefeat SwartclawDefeat RimdelothDefeat GorogmúlDefeat GothlingDefeat FiklúkDefeat SeregruinMaliriel has asked you to help her companions finish preparations for the upcoming banquet.The spring lies directly west of the Vineyards of Lórien.

The Elves of Lothlórien draw water for their feasts from the clearest and sweetest spring in the forest. Glasnír has asked you to draw some water and return it to the cistern in front of the Vineyards.Bring the water back to the Vineyards' cisternGlasnír is at the Vineyards of Lórien, east of the spring.

You should speak with Glasnír regarding your task.Talk to Glasnír at the Vineyards of Lórien'If it is not too onerous a task, my good ${CLASS}, may I ask you fetch water for me? We will need much for the banquet.

'The water of the Anduin is fine for most uses, but for our festivities, we prefer to use water drawn from the clearest spring in the forest of Lothlórien. It is not too far at all, simply proceed west from here, and you will find the spring tucked away along the side of the southern ridge.

'Be careful not to spill too much on the way back... I expect a thirsty crowd this evening!''Only the sweet waters of the clearest spring are worthy for our cistern.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Thirsty guests will toast your name tonight!'Cúvroval wants you to help her defend flet against an incursion of angry crows.Cúvroval is at Talan Revail.

A flock of crebain is descending upon Talan Revail from the West. Cúvroval has asked you to help defend the talan and drive the crows off!Prepare to defend Talan RevailCúvroval is at Talan Revail.

You should speak with Cúvroval regarding the craban-attack on Talan Revail.Talk to Cúvroval at Talan Revail'Alas, it has been long since I laid eyes upon the Great Eagles of the Misty Mountains, whose ancestors served the Elder King in ages past.

Lo, what is that? Do you see that black cloud approaching? Ai-oi! It is a flock of crebain from the west descending upon us.

'Please lend me your aid in driving them off!''Excellent work, my friend! You are welcome to stand at my shoulder any day.''The crebain are descending even now! Stand by my side, and we shall drive them off!'Defeat Goblins in the Grand Stair.Defeat Goblins in the Grand StairDefeat Goblins in the Grand Stair.Defeat Goblins in the Grand StairFind the forgotten instructional ledgers within the School at Tham Mírdain.Find the forgotten instructional ledgers within the School at Tham Mírdain.Find the forgotten instructional ledgers within the School at Tham Mírdain.Find the Charred LedgerFind the Tattered LedgerFind the Ruined LedgerFind the Mouldy LedgerCleave the arms of the Watcher in the Vile Maw.Cleave the arms of the Watcher in the Vile MawCleave the arms of the Watcher in the Vile Maw.Cleave the arms of the Watcher in the Vile MawThe Enemy is entrenched within the Tower of Dol Guldur. It is time to strike them at their heart.In order to secure the Tower, the Entrance Hall must first be claimed.Claim the Entrance HallThe Entrance Hall is secure, and Sigileth will ensure nothing enters from behind you. The next target is the Audience Chamber across the hall.Claim the Audience ChamberWith the Entrance Hall and Audience Chamber claimed, you may begin to climb the Tower and seek to claim the Lower Mustering Hall.Claim the Lower Mustering HallThe Upper Mustering Hall is directly above the Lower...with it claimed, the Enemy will be confused and any reinforcements poorly armed.Claim the Upper Mustering HallWith the Mustering Halls claimed, it is time to take the Armoury and reclaim Zigilburk.Claim the ArmouryWith the Mustering Halls claimed, it is time to take the Armoury and reclaim Zigilburk.Claim the ArmouryBróin must survive the battle'Mazog has fallen and Zigilburk is returned, it is a good day to be a dwarf. Let us head back and celebrate with some ale.'Belvagor believes the Orc-attack on Lórien is imminent and hopes your preparations -- and the strength of your will -- will be enough to keep the enemy from victory.Belvagor is in Caras Galadhon, waiting for you to gather allies and speak to him to begin the defence of Lothlórien.Talk to Belvagor and begin the defence of LothlórienBelvagor is waiting to speak with you in Caras Galadhon about your defence of Lothlórien from the Orcs.Talk to Belvagor at Caras Galadhon'It is time, ${PLAYER}. We must hope our preparations are sufficient, for I fear the attack of the Orcs will be upon us at any moment. We must discuss our plan to repel them.

'There are three passes into Fanuidhol: the Western Pass, the Northern Pass, and the Eastern Pass. We will have defenders at each of these passes, for if any of them fall, Lothlórien will be imperilled. But it is not enough to stand against the Orcs; we must turn back their assault and remove their foothold within Fanuidhol. Scouts tell me they have four encampments among the hills and have erected an idol to the Enemy at each. By carrying a Banner of Lórien to each encampment, your allies will be able to destroy the idol. You will not have much time to destroy all four idols, ${PLAYER}, and will need to move with all haste. But beware! The Banner-carrier will be a very ready target of the Orcs.

'Speak to me when you are ready and have gathered allies, and we will travel to the passes into Fanuidhol.''Have you gathered your allies, ${PLAYER}? We will need their help as well as yours if we are to repel the attack of the Orcs that is almost upon us!''Lothlórien is safe for now, but the Orcs may attack again. You and your allies have my heart-felt thanks.

'In the event the Orcs launch another assault, we will be ready, and I ask you to stand with us again if the need comes.'The Elves of Lothlórien subsist mostly upon the flowering bounty of Lothlórien, but there are those among them that enjoy the chase of the hunt and a finely cooked roast upon special occasions as well.Bears can be found in the dens of Brochos, which is a ways to the west of the Vineyards of Lórien.

Farasdúr has asked you to hunt the bears of Brochos and return with rich meat.Collect bear-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Farasdúr is near the Vineyards of Lórien in Egladil, east of Brochos.

You should bring the bear-meat you have collected to Farasdúr.'We have had much reason to gather and share meals of late, both for honouring the visitors who seek respite in our land, and for the tragic news that reached us in the wake of their arrival.

'For the most part, our people are more than content to subsist upon the bounty of our breads and the greenery cultivated by our gardeners, but we also enjoy the hunt and a fine roast now and again. After all, it does not hurt to bolster the morale of our folk with a little indulgence in such dark times, when battle seems always close at hand.

'To this end, I would have you hunt a few of the wild bears to the west, in the rocky dens of Brochos. Their meat is rich and well worth savouring when properly prepared.''The bears of Brochos produce a very hearty meat.''Ah! A choice set of cuts, ${PLAYER}. The upcoming feast shall be fine indeed!

'I only hope it bolsters the strength of our guests, for it seems that they will have a long and perilous journey ahead of them.'Defeat Spiders in Skûmfil.Defeat Spiders in SkûmfilDefeat Spiders in Skûmfil.Defeat Spiders in SkûmfilYou have heard it whispered that the libraries of Moria yet contain many tomes, while many other volumes were brought by the dwarves seeking to reclaim Moria. One such tome in the libraries of the Iron Garrison is said to be the legendary "The Boiling Rage." If you can gain enough favour with the Iron Garrison Guards, they may let you have their copy of this book.Achieve level 58Read the book, "The Boiling Rage"You have heard it whispered that the libraries of Moria yet contain many tomes, while many other volumes were brought by the dwarves seeking to reclaim their ancient realm. One such tome in the libraries of the Iron Garrison is said to be the legendary "The Book of Nature." If you can gain enough favour with the Iron Garrison Guards, they may let you have their copy of this book.Achieve level 58Read the book, "The Book of Nature"Defeat Kergrim in Skûmfil.Defeat Kergrim in SkûmfilDefeat Kergrim in Skûmfil.Defeat Kergrim in SkûmfilDefeat the leaders of the Kergrim within SkûmfilDefeat BonetoothDefeat Old GnawerDefeat RockjawDefeat ShalebiterDefeat GrimreaverThe Hall of Mirrors was once a conerstone to light in Moria. Now the pieces of that once majestic system litter the floor.Collect the Large Mirror-shardCollect the Cracked Mirror-shardCollect the Minor Mirror-shardCollect the Broken Mirror-shardCollect the Shattered Mirror-shardYou have been acknowledged as a friend of Lothlórien through your efforts on behalf of the Elves.Bahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol to the north.

