Nembes has asked you to deliver pitchers of cool water to parched Elves.Pick up a pitcher for the House of CelebornNembes is at Celúrlin, Galadriel's fountain in the centre of Caras Galadhon.

You have delivered pitchers of cool water to parched Elves throughout the city and should return now to Nembes.Talk to Nembes at Celúrlin'Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. If you are willing to help me with a simple task, I would be most grateful.

'This fountain is Celúrlin, and its water is both refreshing and invigorating. I have filled pitchers with its cool water and would appreciate your help delivering the pitchers to parched Elves throughout Caras Galadhon. Just pick one up from the terrace here and bring it to a parched Elf. Then return here for another pitcher.

'There are three locations to which I would have you bring pitchers of water: parched Elves beneath Telain Neduil, at the base of the ladder that climbs up to the House of Celeborn, and at a gathering of musicians north of here.''Very good, ${PLAYER}! The cool water of the fountain will refresh the parched throats of my kinsmen.

'Take this with my thanks.''Pick up a pitcher from the terrace here and bring it to a parched Elf, then return here for another pitcher.

'There are three locations to which I would have you bring pitchers of water: parched Elves beneath Telain Neduil, at the base of the ladder that climbs up to the House of Celeborn, and at a gathering of musicians north of here.'The Sixteenth Hall is an area overrun with Orcs, many of whom suffer from a terrible illness that causes fungus-like growths on their bodies.

Mallas, an Elf ally to the dwarves, believes that there is something secret beneath the Sixteenth Hall and wishes to learn the true purpose and source of the plague.The fungus of which Glorelloth spoke is to the north-east of the Sixteenth Hall.

Glorelloth wishes you to collect fungus so that she may get a closer look at it and determine its nature.'In the Sixteenth Hall lie many evils; we thought that Orcs were the greatest. Yet recently I saw from my watch some growths of fungus spattered throughout the hall.

'I hail from the woods, and lichens do not generally make me afraid, but these fungi did so. Indeed, my skin crawls when I remember them. There was something terrible about those growths.

'I yearned to go back and study these things, but there is so much else to do ere I will have time, and I do not wish to put this off. I ask you to enter the Sixteenth Hall in my stead. Go to the north-east of the Shadowed Refuge and collect samples of this fungus for me. When you bring them back, I should be able to discern what ills can be derived from this new silent foe.''I am not familiar with this species. It bears no semblance to any fungus I have seen in all my long years.

'I will need to take more time to study this, but I consider your service complete, for you have done exactly as I bid. You have my thanks.'You have been acknowledged a friend of Lothlórien through your efforts on behalf of the Elves.

You should visit the glades of Hythe, well to the south and east, along the banks of the river Anduin.Maliriel can be found in the field of Imlad Lalaith in the eastern reaches of Egladil, along the banks of the river Anduin.

You have been asked to introduce yourself to Maliriel, the Mistress of the Feast for Lothlórien.Talk to Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith'Welcome to Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}, your efforts on our behalf have proven you a friend to the Elves.

'You may wish to visit the glades of Egladil during your stay. Maliriel, the Mistress of the Feast, is known throughout Lothlórien for the grand banquets she prepares in honour of special occasions and important guests.''Welcome to Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}, your efforts on our behalf have proven you a friend to the Elves.

