hispered that the libraries of Moria yet contain many tomes, while many other volumes were brought by the dwarves seeking to reclaim their ancient realm. One such tome in the libraries of the Iron Garrison is said to be the legendary "The Path Less Trod." If you can gain enough favour with the Iron Garrison Guards, they may let you have their copy of this book.Achieve level 58Read the book, "The Path Less Trod"You have begun to follow the path of the Freedom's Defender. If you follow this path to its end, you will find that your already considerable ability to survive attacks in a fight is much improved.Complete the quest 'Thrill of Danger'Complete the quest 'Litany of Defiance'Complete the quest 'Salt the Wound'You have begun to follow the Path of the Ancient Master. If you follow this path to its end, you will gain insight into the events surrounding you and see how they will end.Complete the quest 'Beacon of Hope'Complete the quest 'Share the Power'Complete the quest 'Knowledge of the Lore-master'You have begun to follow the Path of the Foe-trapper. In time you will learn that a trapped enemy makes a much easier target.Complete the quest 'Blindside'Complete the quest 'Passage of Foes'Complete the quest 'Strength of the Earth'You have begun to follow the Path of the Healing Hands. If you follow this path to its end, you may learn how to better restore the morale and vigour of your companions in combat.Complete the quest 'A Cry of Vengeance'Complete the quest 'Rallying Cry'Complete the quest 'Routing Cry'You have begun to follow the Path of the Martial Champion. Mastery of the arts found along this path will allow you to suffer the most cruel attacks and remain in the fight.Complete the quest 'Controlled Burn'Complete the quest 'Getting Strong Now'Complete the quest 'Glory'You have begun to follow the Path of the Masterful Fist. If you follow this path to its end, you will learn how to draw the ire of your enemies, keeping your companions safe.Complete the quest 'Goad'Complete the quest 'Forced March'Complete the quest 'Offensive Strike'You have begun to follow the Path of the Mischief-maker. If you follow this path to its end, you may learn how to become a master of mischief, increasing your abilities to distract foes in combat.Complete the quest 'Bag of Tricks'Complete the quest 'Tracking Treasure'Complete the quest 'A Startling Twist'You have begun to follow the Path of the Resolve-watcher. If you follow this path to its end, you will be better able to aid your companions in a prolonged fight, giving them the resolve necessary to meet the challenge they are facing.Complete the quest 'Triumphant Spirit'Complete the quest 'Song of the Hopeful Heart'Complete the quest 'Echoes of Battle'You have begun to follow the Path of the Restoring Rune. If you follow this path to its end, you will gain greater insight into various runes, allowing you to be more of a strengthening aid to your companions in difficult fights.Complete the quest 'Prelude to Hope'Complete the quest 'Rousing Words'Complete the quest 'A Rune of Restoration'You have earned the trust of the Elves of Lothlórien, and the Galadhrim Guards outside of Caras Galadhon will allow you to enter.The Galadhrim Guard outside Caras Galadhon is waiting to speak to you.Talk to a Galadhrim Guard outside Caras Galadhon'You have earned the trust of my people, ${PLAYER}. Let me know if you have a desire to see the beauty of Caras Galadhon.''Very well, ${PLAYER}. You may now pass into Caras Galadhon if you so desire.'Hasta has let you know of his plans to deal with mysterious creature who lurks behind some unpleasant rumours in the Water-works.Hasta is in the Rotting Cellar in the Water-works of Moria.

You should speak with Hasta to find out what he will need to prepare a lure for the creature behind the disturbing rumours.Speak with Hasta'Hethuwen took a closer look at that sample you gathered earlier and found some troubling results. Evidently, the source of the substance is a living creature!

'If this creature is allowed to persist, it will surely endanger the efforts of the hardy dwarves here in the Water-works, and perhaps in all of Moria. I have a plan, ${PLAYER}, that is sure to help us, but it will take some time to set it in motion.

'We shall bait the creature from out of its hiding place, and I have reason to believe it will be very large. A large stock of ingredients will be needed to prepare a lure that will be sufficiently appetizing. Speak with me again, and I'll let you know what I need. Oh, and...spread the word around to any friends who are fit to assist you. We will be needing rather a lot of ingredients.''Excellent; now, let's get started.  There is much to do and many items we need to prepare.'The Sixteenth Hall is an area overrun with Orcs, many of whom suffer from a terrible illness that causes fungus-like growths on their bodies.

Mallas, an Elf ally to the dwarves, believes that there is something secret beneath the Sixteenth Hall and wishes to learn the true purpose and source of the plague.The Sixteenth Hall lies to the north-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Lar has asked you to delve deep into the Sixteenth Hall and see if you can locate the source of his unease.Find and eliminate the source of Lar's worryLar can be found in the Shadowed Refuge, south-west of the Sixteenth Hall.

You should return to Lar and tell him what you discovered and slew: a terrible headless creature in the depths of the hall, lurking in a room full of spores and slime.Retrurn to Lar at the Shadowed Refuge'The Sixteenth Hall is a vile place, ${CLASS}. The Orcs there bear a terrible disease, but there is something more that troubles me.

'My intuition is excellent, mind you, or else I would not be troubling you with my guesswork. I have been watching the enemy closely from my watch; based on their behaviour, I would venture that something lies hidden away yonder.

'Delve as deeply as you dare into the Sixteenth Hall and discover their secret! Worry not; I do not think this will be a fool's errand. You can find the hall by making your way north-east from the Shadowed Refuge.''Though I send you into grave danger, I cannot tell you much more of this errand, for I do not know myself. I hope you will trust me in this: all the signs indicate that there is something of significance to be discovered in the Sixteenth Hall.'There is no name for a horror such as that, but my feeling of foreboding has passed now that you say it is gone. I can breathe a little easier now.

'I will tell Mallas of your great deed, ${PLAYER}.'Hasta has asked you to find a pure sample of the substance discovered by Hethuwen, who researched the strange creatures rumoured to be found in the Water-works.The highest concentration of the creatures can be found near Gabil-Munz, the great structure to the south-west.

Hasta has asked you to find the source of the strange substance and bring back a pure sample of the stuff for further study.Find the source of the strange gooHasta is at the Rotting Cellar in the Water-works, north-east from Gabil-munz.

Now that you have found the source of the strange substance and extracted another sample, you should bring it to Hasta for more extensive study.'Hethuwen has requested that a pure sample of the strange substance be extracted from the very source of our inquiries. I am afraid you must venture forth once again and accomplish this task, if you are able.

'The highest concentration of the creatures you encountered is centred around Gabil-Munz. You should begin your search for the source of this substance there.

'Find a way to extract a pure sample of the foul stuff, and bring it back to me when you are finished. Hethuwen has sent along a mixture of sorts along with some instructions, and this will test the purity of what you bring back. Good luck, ${PLAYER}!''Head to Gabil-Munz and bring back as pure a sample as you possibly can.'Hasta takes the sample that you have brought him and pours a solution into the jar with it, watching the reaction closely.

'Good work, ${PLAYER}, I think you've unearthed the very source of everything! Now where exactly did you find it?'

Hasta listens intently as you recount your exploits, nodding his head.

'I believe we will to need to do some preparations before we can explore this matter further. Come back to me later, for I need to consult with Hethuwen to discuss how we are to proceed from here. I may need your help again in the coming days. Thank you for your steadfast efforts, ${PLAYER}!'A long-disused armoury belonging to Fastarr's forebears contains an anvil that would be suitable to bestow the quality you seek for your weapon, and a dwarf-expedition has already been sent to secure it.Fastarr has asked you to bring him an infused adamant which he can prepare for use in bestowing a quality upon your weapon. Unfortunately, he does not know where such a stone may be found.Fastarr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria.

Fastarr has bidden you to travel to the armoury of his forebears and rescue his kinsmen trapped within from the ravenous spiders who have captured them.Talk to Fastarr to travel to the spider-nestFastarr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria.

You should return to Fastarr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.'Aye my friend, I know of a place where the quality you seek can be obtained. It is an ancient armoury belonging to the line of my own kin. Upon the anvil within were crafted many fine weapons.

'Indeed, I only yesterday sent an expedition of my fellows to reclaim this hallowed chamber, so there should be no problem with your use of it -- save, of course, for the matter of fees and recompense.

'However, before you even consider going to the armoury, you need to bring me an infused adamant, which I can prepare to receive the quality. Alas, I cannot tell you where to find one.''Ah! Terrible news, ${PLAYER}! A runner has just returned from the armoury -- my kinsmen have been captured! He claims that the expedition stumbled upon some horrid nest of evil spiders within the armoury. They will be devoured for certain, if they cannot be rescued!

'Please, ${PLAYER}, I beg you: go as quickly as you may and rescue my kinsmen from the spiders, and you may make any use you wish of my forebears' forge and tools within...just hurry before it is too late!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Ah, you were able to find an infused adamant! I will get that back to you before you head to the armoury.

'Speak with me again when you are ready to leave.''Still all in one piece? Excellent -- and what is more, you've empowered the stone! Well done, indeed.

'Let us have that adamant, and we will see if we can't bestow the quality you desire.'A reeking ward found, sundered, upon the corpse of the leader of Skûmfil could be a means to enter the depths of the area plagued by kergrim and insects.Gelirwen is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You discovered an item on the master of Skûmfil. It is possible that another half of the item rests on the other combatant at the location.This fragment, found upon the kergrim-king, appears to have been sundered in twain. It is possible that this item can be fused with another like item.

You should find the second half of the object and show them to Gelirwen at the Shadowed Refuge.'It is as I thought, a ward used to seal a doorway. If there are doorways within Skûmfil, it is possible that this item was used to allow passage, much like a key.'A stinking ward found, sundered, upon the corpse of the leader of Skûmfil could be a means to enter the depths of the area plagued by kergrim and insects.Gelirwen is at the Shadowed Refuge.

You discovered an item on the grodbog-queen in Skûmfil. It is possible that another half of the item rests on the other combatant at the location.This fragment, found upon the grodbog-queen, appears to have been sundered in twain. It is possible that this item can be fused with another like item.

You should find the second half of the object and show them to Gelirwen at the Shadowed Refuge.'It is as I thought, this is a ward used to seal a doorway. If there are such doorways within Skûmfil, it is possible that this item was used to allow passage.'A thieving shrew has made off with Pippin's pipe-weed pouch.The shrew ran off to the north of the Company's Pavilion.

A shrew has run off with Pippin's pipe-weed pouch, and you should find it before the hobbit awakes.Find the stolen pipe-weed pouchGladmeldis is at the Company's Pavilion in Caras Galadhon.

You have recovered Pippin's pipe-weed pouch and should bring it to Gladmeldis at once.'Did you see it, ${PLAYER}? A shrew just came running by, dragging a small pouch behind it! I believe that shrew has stolen Master Peregrin's pipe-weed pouch, and all the galenas contained therein!

'If you can find that shrew before Peregrin awakes, I can set the pouch back, and he will never know anything was amiss. I want his visit to Caras Galadhon to be a pleasant one, unmarred by any theft!

'The shrew ran to the north, in the direction of those descending steps! Follow him, and keep watch for any Elves that may have seen which direction he ran!''The shrew ran north, in the direction of those descending steps! Follow it, ${PLAYER}!''You are looking for that shrew? It ran down the steps right past me! I saw it head south-east and up the winding steps that climb up to Telain Neduil.

'If you hurry you might still catch it!''A shrew ran up to me, ${PLAYER}, but he did not keep climbing up the steps! Instead, he jumped down from this great height and ran up the winding path that climbs the slope to the south-east!''I did see that shrew you mention! He ran to the south-west, across that covered bridge!''A shrew did run by here, soaking wet, but he did not seem to be carrying anything. I am sorry to not be of any more help than that.''You found it, ${PLAYER}, and I am glad too that you did not disturb the nest the shrew was building. I am sure Peregrin would be pleased to know that he helped in some small part to provide a home for the shrew and his family. What other galenas can claim so much?

'Still, I am glad you recovered it before he awoke. I will replace it at once, and he need not be the wiser!

'Thank you for your quick action, ${PLAYER}!'In the deepest dark of Moria there is a place where the only light that shone emanated from dwarf-lamps and luminescant fungus. Now, these delvings are dim and darker than ever and home to creatures that exist in nightmares. Yet here they are, and Veúlfur's agents sent to the Shadowed Refuge draw little comfort in knowing that there is something within the Dark Delvings that commands the Orcs to poison themselves in a manner that gives them over to some greater will.The Dark Delvings lie far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Moggi made mention of lamps placed in the Dark Delvings by the dwarves and how they may drive back some of the Nameless, but he thinks that there are others who are unafraid of such Light. Use caution as you fulfill this task.Defeat howling overseers in the Dark Delvings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat snarling overseers in the Dark Delvings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Dark-maw masters in the Dark Delving (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated dark world-eaters in the Dark Delving (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Moggi is at the Shadowed Refuge, far to the north-west of the Dark Delving.

You fought your way into the Dark Delving and there defeated many of the nameless horrors. You should now return to the Shadowed Refuge and inform Moggi of your success.Talk to Moggi at the Shadowed Refuge'The nameless creatures of the dark are a blight on Khazad-dûm and must be destroyed. I ask you to go to the Dark delvings far to the south-east of our location here at the Shadowed Refuge and destroy the evil creatures that dwell there.

'We cannot suffer their existence when it is within our means to rid them from the world. The dwarves built lamps in the Dark Delvings long ago to keep the nameless horrors at bay...they may still exist, but some of these Nameless seem to have overcome the wards.

'Please, go there and clear away the evil things.''Aye, there is something of honour in this place yet. You have proven it thus.

'I will tell Gelirwen that you have done what I asked, and you will be well-respected always by myself and my brethren.''Use the lamps as you can, but I do not think that all the Nameless there will be driven away. Do not fight them in the dark as that is their home and their strength will grow.

'Defeat these nameless horrors in the Dark Delvings, far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge, then return to me.'You have earned the trust of the Elves of Lothlórien, and the Galadhrim Archers at the border must be told you are not an enemy.The Galadhrim Look-outs along the border are waiting to speak with you.Talk to a Galadhrim Look-out'You have earned the trust of my people, ${PLAYER}, but it will do you no good to pass beneath the eaves of the forest unless someone alerts the archers hidden along the border of your nature.

'I will do this. Speak to me again when you wish to enter Lothlórien.''I will spread the word to my people that you are not an enemy, ${PLAYER}. You can now pass beyond the borders of Lothlórien without incident.'You have heard it whispered that the libraries of Moria yet contain many tomes, while many other volumes were brought by the dwarves seeking to reclaim their ancient realm. One such tome in the libraries of the Iron Garrison is said to be the legendary "The Verses of the North." If you can gain enough favour with the Iron Garrison Guards, they may let you have their copy of this book.Achieve level 58Read the book, "The Verses of the North"The Sixteenth Hall is an area overrun with Orcs, many of whom suffer from a terrible illness that causes fungus-like growths on their bodies.

Mallas, an Elf ally to the dwarves, believes that there is something secret beneath the Sixteenth Hall and wishes to learn the true purpose and source of the plague.Crawlers can be found in the Sixteenth Hall, north-east of the Shadowed Refuge.

Ymar seems to be affected differently than all the others who keep watch at the Shadowed Refuge. He is haunted by visions of crawlers, and wishes you kill them while you are in the Sixteenth Hall.Defeat crawlers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ymar is at the Shadowed Refuge, south-west of the Sixteenth Hall.

You have slain many, many vile crawlers and should inform Ymar that the nightmarish threat has passed.Return to Ymar at the Shadowed Refuge'Bless my beard! I am glad you are here. I made the mistake of seeing them, and now I can't get them out of my head! They are there when I close my eyes, infesting my nightmares, and every thing I see, I mistake for one of them! How my skin itches and crawls! They grow in the very bellies of their victims and spew forth to plague my sanity.

'I cannot go back into the Sixteenth Hall, for I do not wish to see the creeping crawlers again -- once was enough to do lasting damage! Call me a coward if you must. I will not go near that place as long as the crawlers are there.

'If Mallas sent you here to do my bidding, you will slay the crawlers to the slithering last. How I hate them! How the sight of them weakens my knees....''The Sixteenth Hall is to the north-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Do not tarry!''They are gone, all gone... good. I believe you, but I see them still. I wonder if this nightmare will ever cease.

'Why am I the only one to have these dreams and visions? I do not like it. Nonetheless, you have done me a great kindness, and I will tell Mallas of your worth.'Defeat the Watcher in the Water.Drive back the Watcher at the Black PoolDrive back the Watcher in the Flooded TreasuryDefeat the Watcher in the WaterBruicheron is hopeful that her beloved friend Belvagor will leave the Orc-fighting to others and instead share a relaxing visit with her.The vintner Glasnír is outside the Vineyards of Lórien, south-east of Caras Galadhon.

Bruicheron has asked you to retrieve a special vintage of wine from the vintner and to bring it to her beloved Belvagor, with the request that he join her for a relaxing day.Talk to Glasnír at the Vineyards of LórienBelvagor is guarding the gates of Caras Galadhon.

Glasnír has given you the special vintage of wine requested by Bruicheron, and now you should deliver it to Belvagor.Bruicheron is on Telain Glorelloth, in Caras Galadhon.

Belvagor has decided his duty requires him to remain on guard against the Orcs for the moment, and he regretfully cannot yet join Bruicheron for a day of relaxation. You should return to Bruicheron with the tidings.'It is good to see you here, ${CLASS} ${PLAYER}. Adventurers are not often permitted within the boundaries of Lothlórien, but that you are here tells me that the Lord and Lady truly intend to defend us from the Orcs at any cost.

'Have you met my beloved? He often stands guard at the entrance to Caras Galadhon with my brother Rilhathel; Belvagor is his name. Now that you are here, perhaps Belvagor can take a rest from his station and share a bottle of wine with me in peace. It will do him good to have a break from the worries of facing the Orcs.

'Travel to the Vineyards of Lórien, south-east of Caras Galadhon, in Egladil, and speak to the vintner Glasnír. He will give you the bottle of wine which I have requested... a special vintage that has great meaning for Belvagor and me. Bring the bottle to Belvagor and tell him that I request he share a relaxing day with me.''The vintner Glasnír is just outside the Vineyards of Lórien, south-east of Caras Galadhon. Retrieve the special vintage of wine I have requested from him and bring it to my beloved Belvagor, currently guarding the entrance to Caras Galadhon. I would share it with him on a relaxing day, a break from his troubles.''You have been sent by Bruicheron for the special vintage she requested? I will retrieve it for you.

'I remember when this vintage was laid down; it was many years ago now, and I was gratified to see we still had some bottles of it remaining, for Bruicheron noticed that it had been laid down on the very day she met Belvagor. She requested that I set some of that vintage aside, saying that it had special meaning for her: it was exactly as old as her love for Belvagor.

'She asked you to bring this to him? You will likely find him guarding the gates of Caras Galadhon.''You have retrieved the special vintage! Bring it now to my beloved Belvagor, currently guarding the gates of Caras Galadhon, and tell him I would share it with him on a relaxing day, that he may forget his troubles.''Bruicheron wanted you to bring this special vintage of wine to Belvagor, did she not? Look for him at the gates of Caras Galadhon, to the north-west.''What is this that you have brought to me, ${PLAYER}?'

'This vintage has special meaning for me and Bruicheron, ${PLAYER}, and it would delight me to no end to share it with her among the golden leaves atop a great mallorn. But my duty is here, and it is for her sake that I must maintain my vigil. The Orcs cannot be permitted to threaten beautiful Lórien or any of its people, especially not she who is dearest to me.

'Bring this vintage to her now and tell her I will join her as soon as I am able. But I must be certain the Orcs are not near enough to launching an assault.''Return to Telain Glorelloth, ${PLAYER}, and tell my beloved Bruicheron that I cannot yet join her for a day of peace.''I understand, ${PLAYER}. Belvagor has his duty, and he would not be my beloved if he did not treat it seriously. But woe betide any Orc that threatens even a single hair of his!

'I will keep this bottle, unopened, until such day that Belvagor is free to take the peace he deserves. He will set aside the vintage of war, and we will once again enjoy the comfort we have earned.'The Warden of the Dungeons of Dol Guldur is a terrible Cargûl, rumoured to be one of the knights of Eärnur, last King of Gondor, lost at Minas Morgul.Defeat the WardenDefend Moria from the evil of the Watcher in the WaterComplete Lost to the DeepsComplete The Vile MawComplete The Arms of the WatcherHaldir of Lórien has sent you to the aid of Hrólfur in Moria, a deed that may in turn provide some security for the Elves. Hrólfur and Haldir hope to see the legendary water-wheels of Nalâ-dûm functioning as they did long ago, in Durin's Day.Nalâ-dûm is south of the Chamber of the Cross-roads, in the Water-works.

Hrólfur wishes for you to investigate the ancient waterway of Nalâ-dûm and recover any lost information about the water-wheels that once fuelled Moria of old.Investigate Nalâ-dûm for informationHrólfur is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, in Durin's Way.

You should bring the ancient records you found to Hrólfur, who will be excited to find a ledger of records of the lore that was lost when Moria fell.'The impertinence of the Elves is forgivable because of the hope Celeborn has kindled with the intent of his well-meaning message. I wish that I could invest every pair of hands in the expedition to re-igniting the lost lore of Durin's Day as our Elf-neighbour describes.

'Alas that I cannot spare them, for I know that fell rumours hiss from the deep wells of Nalâ-dûm where the water-wheels once spun; long ago did Khazad-dûm hum with the murmur of great power surges leaping across the caves. Celeborn's message has put a warmth in my heart... there must be a way to solve this problem.

'${PLAYER}, will you come to our aid again? I would ask you to travel to Nalâ-dûm with a small company and defeat whatever menace lurks there, for something has destroyed the works that once pumped life into these silent halls. If you find anything of value while you are there, I would give you a sturdy reward for such priceless knowledge.''Have you gone yet to the great Nalâ-dûm? Have you seen the water-wheels or the menace that stops them from spinning?''I do not think I can bow low enough to show you the honour I feel, ${PLAYER}. Truly, I cannot believe the extent of your success. The Dwarves of Khazad-dûm owe you much for what you have accomplished today!

'Haldir may bear the message to Celeborn his lord that their Enemy is ours also. We have never varied in our defence of Lorien, but for their part in our recovery of the deeds of Durin's day, we shall be ever thankful.

'Return to Haldir with that message and this also: war is coming. My kinsmen have unearthed much information as to the workings of our enemies; our forges and craft-halls are being used against us in preparation for a blow against Lothlórien. Something has stirred them, and now they seek revenge.'The Dungeons of Dol Guldur are presided over by a Cargûl known only as the Warden. This creature makes entry into and escape from the Dungeons nearly impossible.Complete The Warden of the DungeonsComplete Liberation from the Merciless DungeonsComplete Leave No One Behind<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Adventure to Level 60Fil Gashan is the barracks and mustering point for the Orcs' invasion of Lothlórien. Hidden deep within the fiery landscape and sharing an adjacent entrance to the Forges of Khazad-dûm, Orcs train here under the watchful eye of General Talug.Úlfur, Vagun, and Yngvi can be found in Anazârmekhem.

Teitur directed you to speak with his aides and complete their tasks before he tells Narfi that Fil Gashan is no longer a threat.Help Vagun disable alarms in Fil GashanHelp Vagun with lieutenants in Fil GashanHelp Úlfur gather plans from Fil GashanHelp Yngvi defeat General Talug in Fil GashanTeitur can be found in Anazârmekhem.

You successfully completed each of the tasks  Úlfur, Vagun, and Yngvi gave you. Now you should return to Teitur with your report.Talk to Teitur in Anazârmekhem'My assistants and I have been watching this place for some time now, and we have learned much of what is going on within the walls of Fil Gashan.

'My aides can explain in greater detail, but let me tell you what I know. Orcs are not the most clever creatures, though not stupid by far. We learned a good deal while sneaking within Fil Gashan ourselves. We hid beneath their noses simply by wearing rough-shod armour. Of course, we stayed away from the ones that seemed a bit more clever, but you might find the same success.

'If you are willing to help, I will surely tell Narfi that you assisted me, once Úlfur, Vagun, and Yngvi are all pleased with your efforts, that is. You can find them here in Anazârmekhem.''You will find Úlfur, Vagun, and Yngvi within the bounds of our encampment here in Anazârmekhem. Speak with them and complete the tasks they have, and I will speak very well of you to Narfi.''A worthy accomplishment, ${PLAYER}, very worthy indeed. While there is much work still to be done to reclaim Moria, I think that we have staved off this foray against the Elves. No need to anger others, I say.

'All that you have done will be remembered here, ${PLAYER}. I will speak very well of you to Narfi.'Hadroneth is concerned about the Orc camps that have been established in Nanduhirion, and wants you to tear down the barricades that have sprung up outside them.You will find barricades to the north-west of Talan Haldir, outside the Orc camps of Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul, along the road that runs through Nanduhirion.

Hadroneth has asked you to damage the permanence of the Orc camps in Nanduhirion by burning down the barricades they erect outside them.Set fire to Orc barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hadroneth is on Talan Haldir, located on the banks of the Nimrodel, south-east of Nanduhirion.

You have set fire to many of the Orc barricades in Nanduhirion and should report now to Hadroneth.Talk to Hadroneth'You have slain many Orcs, but their camps in Nanduhirion are still a danger to those forced to travel the road between here and Moria. The Orcs have erected barricades outside their outposts along the road.

'Set these barricades afire, ${PLAYER}, and perhaps we can convince the Orcs to return to their vile warrens beneath the mountains.

'You will find barricades to the north-west, outside the camps of Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul, along the road that runs through Nanduhirion.''The Orcs build barricades outside the camps they have established in Nanduhirion to the north-west. Set these barricades alight! You will find them along the road that runs from here to Moria.''Very good, ${PLAYER}! Setting fire to their barricades will tell even the most dull-witted Orc that he is not welcome in Nanduhirion, so close to Lórien. You have done well.'Find pieces of treasure within the Forgotten Treasury.Find pieces of treasure within the Forgotten Treasury.Find pieces of treasure within the Forgotten Treasury.Find a large gemFind a pile of gold coinsFind a small treasure chestFind an ancient vaseDrive evil from the Dark DelvingsComplete Runes of the Dark DelvingsComplete Leaders of the NamelessComplete Glow-worm SlayerComplete Nameless-slayerHunt the Free People throughout the region of Eregion. You may hunt for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Hunt in Eregion.Hunt in EregionHunt the Free People in Forochel. You may hunt for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Hunt in Forochel.Hunt in ForochelNúrelleth wants the memory of Faengris to live on in Lórien and to do more than simply slay some Orcs in his name.The lonely tree where Núrelleth wants the vengeance arrow placed is on the bank of Anduin, east of Imlad Lalaith.

Núrelleth wants the Elves of Lothlórien to remember her husband Faengris, and to that end, she would rather the vengeance arrow stand in his memory rather than be used to slay more Orcs.Núrelleth is on Telain Glorelloth, on one of the flets that extends over the hedge that encircles Caras Galadhon.

You have left the vengeance arrow at the lonely tree as Núrelleth requested of you and should now return to her.Talk to Núrelleth at Telain GlorellothNúrelleth is silent for a moment.

'Do not misunderstand me, ${PLAYER}. I am grateful for Cúbenn's thoughtful gift of this arrow, and I am pleased that the Orcs could be made to pay for the death of my husband...but it is not enough. I cannot put into words how important Faengris was to me, but vengeance upon the Orcs would in no way repay them for what they have taken from me.

'No, instead I want the memory of my husband to live on in Lothlórien. I want to tell my people what he was, and why it is such a sorrow that he is gone.

'There is a lonely tree on the bank of Anduin, just east of Imlad Lalaith. Bring this arrow to that tree and set it at its base. Faengris and I would watch the sun rise in the east sitting by that tree, and I would like this arrow to remain there in remembrance of him.'Núrelleth is silent for a moment, and then gives you a brief smile.

'You have been a great comfort to me in my sorrow, ${PLAYER}. I wish only you had been able to meet Faengris, for he would have delighted to hear tales of your adventure.

'Thank you for listening to my grief, friend ${CLASS}. You will be a friend to me always for this.'Núrelleth sighs, her face a sorrowful mask.

'The lonely tree where I would like you to place the arrow is east of Imlad Lalaith, on the banks of Anduin.''Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. This is a beautiful place to watch the sun rise in the mornings. Anduin sparkles like gold in the light of the sun and like silver by the light of the moon.

'The tree there sees them all.'Defeat the villains of the Grand Stair.Defeat Ilzkâl the PummelerDefeat Glothrok the VileDefeat ForzunkDefeat Gothghaash the FirecallerDefeat the villains of the Grand Stair.Defeat Dorozg the Beast TamerDefeat The BeastDefeat Nardur the ShieldDefeat Igash the FanaticDefeat Uruks in Tham Mírdain.Defeat Uruks in Tham MírdainDefeat many Uruks in Tham Mírdain.Defeat many Uruks in Tham MírdainMaliriel has asked you to help her companions complete the preparations for the upcoming banquet.Grapes can be found growing upon trellises in the Vineyards of Lórien.

Glasnír has asked you to collect some grapes for the new wine. No banquet would be complete without fine wine with which to toast, but making a fine wine takes time. Fortunately, the Elves make particularly fine vintners, for there is no lack of time in the long lives of these fair folk.Gather grapes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The tub is in the Vineyards of Lórien.

You should take the grapes to tub to be crushed.Glasnír is in the Vineyards of Lórien.

You should let Glasnír know that you have collected grapes and crushed the berries as he wished.Talk to Glasnír in the Vineyards of Lórien'There is a traditional toast at the beginning of every feast, for which we will provide the wine.

'The wine for this feast is, of course, already aged to perfection, but it is our custom to lay down the makings of a future vintage just before each gathering.

'We need to gather a few last clusters of grapes before this evening's festivities. If you would be so kind as to find some ripe bunches in or around the Vineyards and bring them to one of the tubs, you would have my gratitude.''Have you harvested the grapes for the wine?''Whole grapes do not wine make... you must crush them first.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Today we laid down a vintage that will be consumed by revellers many years from now -- perhaps even on distant shores, as a fond memory of Middle-earth for those who pass beyond the Sea.'The dwarves do not believe the threat of the siege-camp will be silenced until the Orc-wright making the weapons is defeated.Lûrkh is at Drû-garmadh to the south-east of Mekhem-bizru.

Dagfari does not believe the siege-weapons will stop until their mastermind, Lûrkh, has been defeated.Defeat LûrkhDagfari is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh.

Dagfari will want to hear of the defeat of Lûrkh and the end of the siege-camp.Talk to Dagfari at Mekhem-bizru'The Orcs will not be able to make war upon us today, which is good. It allows us a moment of respite, though only a brief moment. They will have more catapults and siege-weapons built within days, and more siege-masters will pour out from the deeps.

'There is only one way to put an end to this camp. There is an Orc, Lûrkh, who is a master weapon-wright. It is his guiding hand that has made or directed all of the siege-weapons you have seen.

'Return to Drû-garmadh, to the south-east, and defeat Lûrkh. It is the only way the Dale will be safe.''This is a joyous day, indeed! With Lûrkh defeated, the making of siege-weapons has come to a halt. Now our foothold here and the outskirts of Lothlórien are both safe from serious threat--though I daresay the Elves would not tolerate Orcs on their borders.''I feel we have only delayed the Orcs. In order to truly put an end to this operation, we will need to destroy the mastermind behind the weapons.'The Elves at the way-post atop Amon Angened provide supplies and provisions for the main force of the Malledhrim in the east.Blacktusk and the Mirkwood boars may be found around the ruins of Fállug, west of Amon Angened.

Gaerfalas has asked you to hunt Blacktusk and the Mirkwood boars for their meat.Collect boar-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Blacktusk at FállugGaerfalas is at the way-post atop Amon Angened, east of Fállug.

You should bring the boar-meat you collected to Gaerfalas and tell him of Blacktusk's defeat.'Besides medicine, the Malledhrim need food. We have seen few creatures fit to consume in this forest, but we must certainly continue to try.

'You can help with this. There are many boars now dwelling in the ruins of Fállug. As they live near the river-banks, perhaps they have not suffered the corruption of Dol Guldur.

'Would you hunt these boars and bring their meat to me? You will be compensated. Be wary, though... Blacktusk, an immense boar of vicious temperament rules over the boars. You will need to slay him as well.''It is to be hoped that the boars of Fállug are not wholly corrupted, for our forces need meat.''You have slain the great boar Blacktusk, ${PLAYER}? Well done!

'Unfortunately, this meat is no good for provisions. Alas, the shadow of Dol Guldur reaches too far, too far!'Beside the Orc-camp at Ashúrz Maufulug, the Elf-scouts discovered a smaller kennel of Wargs and their goblin-keepers not far to the east of the stronghold of the Orcs.Wargs can be found at Maudhul-ulur, south from Echad Glamodúd.

Goldínwen has asked you to defeat many Wargs at the kennel nearby.Defeat Taughâsh Wargs in Maudhul-ulur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Goldínwen is at Echad Glamodúd, north from Maudhul-ulur.

You should return to Goldínwen with the news that you have defeated many Wargs at Maudhul-ulur.Talk to Goldínwen at Echad Glamodúd'${PLAYER}, I am sure you learned that there is a kennel of Wargs, kept by several goblins, not far to the east of Ashúrz Maufulug. Maudhul-ulur is what the Enemy calls it.

'This camp is surely where the Wargs roaming the shores of the Mirk-eaves are coming from, and it is a threat we must deal with at once. I need you to enter Maudhul-ulur and defeat as many Wargs as you can.

'When you have completed your task, return to me.''There were too many Wargs for you to destroy utterly? That is a pity, for we cannot hope to attack Ashúrz Maufulug while the beasts still wander.''You have not slain the Wargs of Maudhul-ulur? That is fell news. Perhaps you should return there to complete your task.'The Dunlending deserters at Lhe Lhechu are led by a ruffian by the name of Lhew, whom Dagoras came to know during his imprisonment at the Dunlending camp.Lhew is at Lhe Lhechu, south-west of Echad Dagoras.

Dagoras has asked you to defeat Lhew, commander of the band of Dunlending deserters in Fordirith.Defeat LhewDagoras is at Echad Dagoras, north-east of Lhe Lhechu.

You should speak with Dagoras and let him know that Lhew has been defeated.Talk to Dagoras at Echad Dagoras'During my brief stay with the deserters at Lhe Lhechu, I learned more than perhaps they hoped. While they are in hiding from the minions of Saruman the traitor, they are still dangerous to the Grey Company: their leader wished to use me to regain Saruman's favour.

'Lhew, the leader of the deserters, can be found towards the rear of their encampment. He is a brash fellow, but a coward at heart. He has led his men to an end that may not bode well for them...perhaps if Lhew were to be defeated, the rest will disband and return to their homes.

'If nothing else, Lhew's defeat may draw their attention away from the passing of the Grey Company.''A blow well struck, ${PLAYER}. With the loss of their leader, the remaining deserters are quite unlikely to interfere with the Grey Company again.''Lhew is a base coward, but he is also intimidating. His men will follow his lead as long as he remains at Lhe Lhechu.'The Elves of the Golden Host seek a way to cripple the Orcs of Durbúrz-stazg.Durbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion.

Aemeldir has asked you to defeat the Black Uruk Ulkúrzlam at Durbúrz-stazg. You will need to enter the encampment through the eastern gate.Defeat Ulkúrzlam at Durbúrz-stazgEchad Sirion lies to the south of Durbúrz-stazg.

You should return to Aemeldir with news of your victory against Ulkúrzlam and his soldiers.Talk to Aemeldir at Echad Sirion'We have learned much from your foray into Durbúrz-stazg, ${PLAYER}. First, we have learned that a troll of a strange kind ranges among the forces of the Enemy at Durbúrz-stazg. Secondly, we learned that the Orcs are led by a Black Uruk named Ulkúrzlam.

'Tethafnel here at Echad Sirion will speak with you more about the troll. She has had more experience in dealing with such creatures and may have some insights for you.

'I want you to enter Durbúrz-stazg through the eastern gate once more and confront Ulkúrzlam. With his defeat, the forces at Durbúrz-stazg shall fall apart.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! This victory is a terrible blow against the Enemy.

'You have earned this reward.''Without the leadership of Ulkúrzlam, the Orcs of Durbúrz-stazg shall be disrupted.'Amarion left camp to search the Black Dens where he believed he might find some way to destroy the Shadow-wolves -- but he has been gone too long.Amarion is in the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras.

Braigiar has asked you to find Amarion and rescue him from the Shadow-wolves.Find Amarion the Ranger near the Black DensAmarion is at the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras.

Amarion has asked for your help to escape from the Black Dens.Help Amarion escape from the Black DensAmarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens.

You should speak with Amarion about your escape from the Shadow-wolves.Talk to Amarion at Echad Dagoras'Who is that down there? ${PLAYER}? It is long since you aided me at Amon Raith. I do not suppose you could lend me a hand once more?''Amarion's absence troubles me greatly, ${PLAYER}. He said he would return within a few hours, and he is not one to lose track of time in the field.

'That he has not returned yet bodes ill. He said that he wished to examine the Black Dens for himself, hoping to find some way to stop the scourge of the Shadow-wolves, but that was the last I saw of him.

'The Black Dens lies to the south-east of here. I ask that you search for him there...I fear for his life if they have caught him unaware.''My thanks for your aid, ${PLAYER}! 

'For a little while, I was not sure I was going to make it back alive....''I am afraid that the Shadow-wolves caught my scent and chased me up here some hours ago...I have been biding my time in the hopes that perhaps they would leave, but I have had no such fortune.

'Now that you have found me here though, I think it would be best if we left swiftly before they find you as well.''Let us be off then, shall we?''Amarion went to the Black Dens alone...I hope he is well.''Help Amarion if you can...he went to the Black Dens alone.''What of Amarion, ${PLAYER}? Did you find him?'The Elves at the way-post atop Amon Angened provide supplies and provisions for the main force of the Malledhrim in the east.Spent Malledhrim arrows may be found around the ruins of Fállug, west of Amon Angened.

Thindiel has asked you to recover spent Malledhrim arrows from the ruins of Fállug.Collect spent arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thindiel is at the way-post atop Amon Angened, east of Fállug.

You should bring the arrows you collected to Thindiel.'${PLAYER}, I have a task for you. When our forces ravaged the Enemy in the Mirk-eaves, they left behind many spent arrows in their rush to press deeper into Southern Mirkwood. Now we have received word that the Malledhrim are suffering a shortage of arrows.

'Would you go to the ruined Orc-camp of Fállug to the west and see if you can find any of these spent arrows? It matters not whether they are broken or whole... we can make use of any.

'When you have collected a number of these arrows, bring them to me, and I will reward you.''Bring me any arrows you can find at Fállug, ${PLAYER}. Our forces are running short.''These arrows will be of great use to the Malledhrim, but they will not be enough.

'You have done as you were asked, and so you deserve this reward.'Braigiar's companion Dagoras has been captured by the Dunlending deserters after going to negotiate an agreement with them.Dagoras is being held in Lhe Lhechu, south-west of Echad Dagoras.

You must free Dagoras and escort him from the Dunlending camp.Rescue Dagoras from Lhe LhechuDagoras ia at Echad Dagoras, north-east of Lhe Lhechu.

You should speak with Dagoras at his encampment.Talk to Dagoras at Echad Dagoras'My captain, Dagoras, went to visit a small encampment to the south-west of here that the Dunlendings call Lhe Lhechu. It seems that a number of the Dunlendings who were sent to fight in Eregion have since deserted and retreated back here. It was Dagoras' hope that we might be able to strike some kind of bargain with the deserters, given their obviously questionable loyalty to Isengard, but he has been gone for nearly a day now with no word.

'Dagoras is a cautious man, but his strength lies in wit and cunning, more than might. If the deserters have indeed captured him he may need a hand.

'Try and find some sign of him down there and free him if he is captured. We will need a man of his experience and skills once we reach Rohan!''${PLAYER}! Never did I think to find you here! It has been long since Esteldín, but we will have to reminisce later.

'I came here to try and negotiate with these deserters, thinking they might not have much in common with the forces from Isengard after being abandoned to their fate in Eregion, but they had other ideas.

'In any case, it seems these folk are not open to parley. They have been betrayed with too many false promises. Release me, and let us return to my camp.''If you find Dagoras, bring him back here, ${PLAYER}.''Braigiar will have some choice words for me, I am certain, for he advised me against parleying with the Dunlendings. First, however, we must escape this place, which means we will need a key....''Were you able to find Dagoras, my friend?''Ah, you have my thanks, friend ${PLAYER}. I was not looking forward to ending my days in some Dunlending cell. Soon, we will forge on to join with the rest of our kinsmen.'The Shadow-wolves of the Black Dens are clearly no ordinary wolves. Some spirit of evil empowers them and guides them.The Black Dens lie to the south-east of Echad Dagoras.

Amarion has asked you to enter the Black Dens and find the source of the Shadow-wolves' power.Find the source of the Shadow-wolves' powerShadow-torches can be found throughout the caverns of the Black Dens.

You should douse the torches within the Black Dens to break the strange enchantment that summons forth the Shadow-wolves.Douse torches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Amarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens.

You should return to Amarion with tidings of what you found in the Black Dens.Talk to Amarion at Echad Dagoras'Our attempts to stop these Shadow-wolves have borne no fruit thus far.

'The source of their evil must lie within the caverns in the Black Dens. If you can find your way into them and destroy it, we may gain some respite from their relentless hunt.

'Go now, and may the Valar watch over you.''You found and extinguished a number of strange black torches?

'I think you have likely found the power behind the Shadow-wolves. I cannot say whether your efforts will destroy them for good or not, but I will be most surprised if they are able to take up the hunt for us again so soon with their dark power so diminished.

'You have my gratitude, ${PLAYER}.''Seek the source of the Shadow-wolves' power in the Black Dens to the south-east.''Have you found the source of the Shadow-wolves' power yet?'The time has come for the Malledhrim, the Golden Host, to cross the river Anduin and assail the forces of the Enemy in Dol Guldur.Braiglinn is at Imlad Lalaith, on the shores of the Anduin, in Lothlórien.

You have been told to speak with Braiglinn about the crossing of the Golden Host into Mirkwood.Talk to Braiglinn at Imlad LalaithCalengoth is at the docks near Imlad Lalaith, on the shores of Anduin, in Lothlórien. Once you have made the crossing, you will find Fuirgam working to secure a foothold in Mirkwood.

Calengoth, the launch officer, is waiting to see you to one of the boats that will carry you across Anduin with the first crossing. Once you have done so, seek out Fuirgam, the Elf in charge of securing a foothold for the Elves.Board Calengoth's boat and assist Fuirgam with his tasks among the Mirk-eavesAlfirimbes is waiting to speak with you in Echad Sirion.

The Elves have established their foothold on the dark shores of Mirkwood and are ready to begin their push into the forest.Talk to Alfirimbes at Echad Sirion'At last, the preparations are complete. The Malledhrim, the Golden Host of Lothlórien, are now ready to cross the river Anduin and assail the forces of Dol Guldur.

'The Golden Host is to have two objectives: to bring battle to the Enemy in Dol Guldur at a time of our choosing, before he can attack the woods of Lothlórien in force, and to exchange Mazog, the prisoner of the Iron Garrison, for the captives in the dungeons of Dol Guldur.

'Your aid has been requested for both of these aims. Speak with Braiglinn, by the hythe up the slope from the docks of Lothlórien. He will recount to you details of each plan.''It has taken a great while, ${PLAYER}, but at last the preparations are complete. The Malledhrim, the Golden Host of Lothlórien, are now ready to cross the river Anduin and assail the forces of Dol Guldur.

'I do not yet know the specifics of the plan, friend ${CLASS}, but it seems the Golden Host is to have two objectives: to bring battle to the Enemy in Dol Guldur at a time of our choosing, before he can attack the woods of Lothlórien in force, and to exchange Mazog, the prisoner of the Iron Garrison, for the captives in the dungeons of Dol Guldur.

'Your aid has been requested for both of these aims. Go now to Imlad Lalaith on the shores of the Anduin and speak to Braiglinn there. He will recount to you details of each plan.''It was not easy, ${PLAYER}, but we have made the crossing and expelled the Orcs from their fort atop Amon Angened. The Golden Host is now ready to begin the passage into Mirkwood.

'I hope we are not wrong in this. A great deal is at stake.''You have come at last, ${PLAYER}; I had begun to wonder if you would not wish to be part of the first crossing! But I am pleased to see this is not so.

'See you the river Anduin? Its currents are strong, though this be a calm enough place to cross, and once we land on the far shore we will need to be ready for anything. The landing may be uneventful, but then it may be tumultuous indeed. It will be up to Fuirgam, on the other side of Anduin, to ensure that all goes as smoothly as it may.

'Once we are secure on the beaches, I will arrange for a second crossing to bring the company that will escort our prisoner to Dol Guldur. Are you ready to travel upon the first boats across? Speak with Calengoth down at the docks if you are ready.''Climb the slope from these docks and talk to Braiglinn. He will tell you the details of the aims of the Golden Host in Mirkwood.''Speak with Calengoth down at the docks; he will have a boat you can use to make the crossing. Once on the other side, you should assist Fuirgam with the many tasks necessary to secure a foothold in Mirkwood.''I am filled with anticipation, ${PLAYER}, and my fingers seek the strings of my bow eagerly! The Golden Host is now ready to depart, to cross the river and bring the fight to the Enemy. It has been long since we have done more than watch our borders; too long.

'Go now to Imlad Lalaith on the shores of Anduin, in Lórien, and speak with Braiglinn. He will recount to you the details of the Golden Host's aims.''If you are ready to cross the Anduin with the first company, board the boat. I know that Fuirgam, in charge of the landing, will be grateful for your assistance on the other side.'Nordan has a different approach to dealing with the Wargs and their handlers than Goldínwen's.Barrels of Warg-food can be found at Maudhul-ulur, south from Echad Glamodúd.

Nordan has asked you to enter Maudhul-ulur and burn any casks of Warg-food you may find.Burn barrels of Warg-food (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nordan is at Echad Glamodúd, north from Maudhul-ulur.

You should return to Nordan with tidings of your success.Talk to Nordan at Echad Glamodúd'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. Might I have a word with you?

'Goldínwen believes that we can only reduce the threat of the Wargs by destroying both the beasts and their handlers. I, however, believe there is a much more efficient way to handle them: destroy their sustenance.

'When next you enter Maudhul-ulur, look for barrels of food for the Wargs...if you destroy these, the Wargs and their handlers will be forced to retreat or at least refrain from foraying against us. This flint, steel, and kindling should be of help.''Their food burns? That is well. It will, however, take some time before we notice any results.''Have you burned the Wargs' food yet? No? Then you must return to Maudhul-ulur.'Braigiar has assigned you the task of finding a number of hidden caches of supplies scattered throughout northern Enedwaith. If you can uncover these supplies, the Grey Company will be able to pass through swiftly without having to resort to bartering with hostile locals or stopping to hunt.Braigiar has pointed you to a cache of foodstuffs he says is hidden in the north-western area of Fordirith. He believes it should be buried about twenty paces west from a tree marked with the Ranger's rune.Braigiar said the cache of foodstuffs would be buried about twenty paces west of the rune-marked tree.Braigiar is at Echad Dagoras in Fordirith.

You discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the foodstuffs hidden there. Now you should return with them to Braigiar.'We need additional supplies if we are going to make it through all of Dunland without slowing to hunt or barter -- assuming the locals will deal with us at all, which seems doubtful in these dark times.

'Fortunately there are those among our number that have long made the trek to Gondor and back to bring news and lore between the North and the South. These wayfarers laid in caches of supplies -- food, medicine, bandages, weapons, even some scrolls of lore we stowed away.

'The caches are well hidden, but can be spotted if you know what to look for. There should be a few such here in Fordirith.''My kinsmen have oft hidden caches of supplies along the path south... I only hope they are intact and will be enough to supply us all the way to Rohan.''The cache should be hidden twenty paces west of the rune-marked tree... bring it to me as soon as you can, for we need to move on.''Excellent. This food will last us a while -- hopefully through to the borders of Rohan where we should be able to trade for additional supplies with the Rohirrim, though it is a long journey.'Amarion has told you of a particularly valuable hidden cache secreted within the Black Dens -- unfortunately this was before it was overrun by the deadly Shadow Wolves. If you can recover the Weapon-lore scrolls hidden away within, it would be a considerable boon to the Grey Company.Amarion has pointed you to a cache of weapon-lore scrolls he says is hidden within the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras. He believes it should be buried about fifty paces west of the cavern floor marked with the Rangers' rune.Amarion said the cache of weapon-lore scrolls would be buried about fifty paces west of the rune-marked cavern.Amarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens.

You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the scrolls of lore hidden there. Now you should return with them to Amarion.'The provisions will come in handy, but there are other caches as well.

'I know of another further to the south-east. It contain scrolls of weapon-lore recorded by the Elves of Rivendell long years ago.

'The virtues such lore might bestow upon our weapons would be invaluable to us in the South.''The lore I have sent you to find will be invaluable to us in the days to come.''The cache should lie fifty paces to the west of the rune-marked cavern in the Black Den.''Excellent. These scrolls were scribed by the most skilled scholar among the Elves of Rivendell and will serve us well in our journey south.'Braigiar has assigned you the task of finding a number of hidden caches of supplies scattered throughout northern Enedwaith. If you can uncover these supplies, the Grey Company will be able to pass through swiftly without having to resort to bartering with hostile locals or stopping to hunt.Braigiar has pointed you to a cache of herbs and poultices he says is hidden in the north-eastern area of Fordirith. He believes it should be buried among a stand of pine trees eighty paces north of a boulder marked with the Rangers' rune.Braigiar said the cache of medicines would be buried among a grove of pine trees roughly eighty paces north of a large rune-marked boulder.Braigiar is at Echad Dagoras, south-west of the medicine-cache.

You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the medicines hidden there. Now you should return with them to Braigiar.'There is another cache to the east of here, that one should contain a number of poultices and reagents useful in the arts of healing.

'I suspect we will be in great need of such things before long, and many of the familiar herbs we might find in the north are not to be found here.

'The cache lies more to the north-east, about eighty paces north of a boulder marked with the Rangers' rune.''Medicine will be in short supply upon our journey... we need that hidden cache!''The medicine-cache lies about eighty paces north of the rune-marked boulder.''Excellent. These medicines were crafted by our most skilled healers and will serve us well in our journey south.'Some among the northern Rangers have often made the trek through Dunland to Gondor, far to the South. During these prior journeys, they left cleverly hidden caches in case one of their number should be injured or in desperate need of supplies during their journeys. Now with the Grey Company travelling into the south they have decided to collect these caches to ensure they are ready to deal with the dangers ahead.Braigiar has pointed you to a cache he believes is hidden in the Southern area of Fordirith. First, you should find a marker rune atop a small rounded hill with several trees upon it.Braigiar said the cache of weapons would be buried about sixty paces east of the rune marker, amid a jumble of large boulders.Braigiar is at Echad Dagoras, north of the weapon-cache.

You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the weapons hidden there. You should return with them to Braigiar.'The spare food will come in handy, but there are other caches as well.

'I know of another a distance to the south...that one should contain a bundle of spare blades.

'We shall face many dangers on our way through Dunland, and a spare weapon can mark the difference between life and death in battle. The cache itself should be hidden about sixty paces from a rune-marked hill.''We will need the weapons my kinsmen have hidden in these lands.''The weapon-cache should lie about sixty paces west of the rune-marked hill.''You found the weapons-cache? That is good. We are well-armed, but the journey ahead is long, and battles will take their toll on our blades.

'Dunlending weapons will not be in short supply, but their lore of steel is poor at best. I am glad that we will have our own spares for this journey.'The first crossing of the Anduin by the Malledhrim has been successful, and now it is time for the company charged with transporting Mazog to cross as well.Braiglinn is at Imlad Lalaith on the Lothlórien side of the river Anduin.

Alfirimbes is pleased that the first crossing has been successful and has sent you to Braiglinn to notify the party responsible for bringing Mazog to Dol Guldur the time has come for their own crossing.Talk to Braiglinn at Imlad LalaithBraiglinn is at Imlad Lalaith on the Lothlórien side of the river Anduin.

The time has come to meet the members of the company bringing Mazog to Dol Guldur. You should speak with Braiglinn when you are ready.Talk to Braiglinn and travel to meet the members of the companyAlfirimbes is waiting to speak with you at Echad Sirion, the camp on the shores of Anduin, on the border of Mirkwood.

You have met the company responsible for bringing Mazog in secret to Dol Guldur, and they have crossed into Mirkwood. You should speak now to Alfirimbes.Talk to Alfirimbes at Echad Sirion'Now you must return to Imlad Lalaith and tell Braiglinn that we have seized our first foothold across the river. It is time for the second party to cross, for it is they who hold the stealthy undertaking of bringing Mazog to Dol Guldur in trade for the dwarf-prisoners. The launch-officer, Calengoth, near the boats, will ferry you back to Lothlórien.

'I will see to the rest of the preparations necessary for Echad Sirion to serve as the camp for our first excursions into Mirkwood.''It has now begun, ${PLAYER}. For good or ill, we now have no choice but to embark upon this journey. May both aims of the Malledhrim see victory in the end: the rescue of the prisoners held by the Enemy in Dol Guldur and the delay of an attack out of Mirkwood upon Lothlórien.

'We will do all that we can to see both of these done.''The first crossing was a success, ${PLAYER}? That means it is time for the second, smaller company to cross Anduin.

'I will bring you to meet them; after all, you will be assisting these Elves with the transport of Mazog to Dol Guldur, and the way will be fraught with danger.

'Let me know when you are ready, and I will introduce you to them.''Return to the launch-officer, Calengoth, near the boats, and he will ferry you back to Lothlórien so you can speak with Braiglinn. Tell him it is time for the second crossing.''Alfirimbes has begun making preparations to bring Mazog out of the Mirk-eaves and closer to the fortress of Dol Guldur. Speak with her at the camp of Echad Sirion, across the river.''Are you ready to meet the company responsible for the dangerous undertaking of bringing Mazog to Dol Guldur in exchange for the prisoners? I will bring you to them and make the introductions.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>Alfirimbes believes the success of the Hidden Guard's errand depends on keeping the presence of Mazog a secret from the Orcs of Mirkwood.Taughâsh Orcs and vile goblins can be found throughout the Mirk-eaves. Coffers that may contain Orc-communications can be found inside the camps of Maudhûl-ulur and Ashúrz Maufulug, south-east of Echad Sirion.

Alfirimbes has asked you to search the Orc-fortifications in the Mirk-eaves to learn if the Orcs of Mirkwood have learned of Mazog's presence.Find a coffer in Maudhûl-ulur or Ashúrz Maufulug containing information about MazogDefeat Taughâsh Orcs or goblins in the Mirk-eaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Alfirimbes is at Echad Sirion, the camp of the Golden Host in the Mirk-eaves, north of Maudhûl-ulur and Ashúrz-maufulug.

You have found a report addressed to Mazog in the coffer of an Orc-leader and should bring it now to Alfirimbes.Lúth Greyhammer is making his ill feelings known as he wanders about Echad Sirion.

Alfirimbes wants you to reassure Lúth Greyhammer that the necessary steps are being taken to ensure the errand of the Hidden Guard is being conducted safely and that Mazog's captivity is not threatened.Talk to Lúth Greyhammer at Echad SirionAlfirimbes is at Echad Sirion, cautiously overseeing the defence of the camp.

Lúth Greyhammer has demanded that one member of his family be posted as sentry watching the captive Orc-leader.Talk to Alfirimbes at Echad Sirion'The success of the Hidden Guard's errand will depend, I think, upon secrecy. We must ensure that the Orcs of Mirkwood do not learn of Mazog's presence beneath the eaves, or they will surely launch an attack upon us in such number we cannot repel them.

'To the south-east are two forts from which the Orcs of Mirkwood maintain a watch over this part of the forest. Search any coffers you find at Maudhûl-ulur and Ashúrz Maufulug for Orc-communications and defeat any of the Taughâsh you find in the Mirk-eaves as you do.

'If you can return to me with any plans or messages that mention Mazog, we can determine how to proceed. If they are aware that we have brought him out of Moria, we may need to act quickly to survive.''The Taughâsh have a firm hold upon this area, ${PLAYER}, leading raids from their camps to the south-east. Defeat these Orcs and their goblin-cousins wherever you see them and search Maudhûl-ulur and Ashúrz Maufulug for coffers containing information about Mazog.

'If you find any communications from which we can learn if they know we have captured Mazog, bring them back to me so we may prepare.''You found a report addressed to Mazog in the coffer of the Orc-leader at Ashúrz Maufulug? Let me see what it says, ${PLAYER}....

'Fortune is with us, my adventurous ${CLASS}: these Orcs do not yet know we have captured Mazog and brought him into Mirkwood. They think he resides still in Moria; the errand of the Hidden Guard remains secret.

'A problem arose while you were away. Lúth Greyhammer, a dwarf of Bróin's company, has become increasingly agitated about the plans of the Golden Host. Speak with him here at Echad Sirion, if you would, and assure him that we are doing all that we may to make this journey a safe one. His family has many grievances with the Orcs, but I fear the Greyhammers may do us ill if they do not keep their heads about them.''Lúth Greyhammer walks throughout the camp of Echad Sirion, making known his feelings about this endeavour. Speak with him and keep him calm, ${PLAYER}. He may unknowingly do us harm if he persists in his unrest.''At last, someone who will listen to me! I might have known it would be you, ${PLAYER}. You are held in great esteem by my lords Bósi and Brogur and have proven yourself a friend of the Iron Garrison. You will be a friend, too, of the Greyhammers!

'These Elves do not have the experience with Orcs that we Greyhammers do! Oh, they seem understanding enough when I recount the many grievances my family has suffered at the hands of Mazog and his forebears, but I can tell they think I exaggerate. Do I exaggerate the wounding of my grandfather Thormar at Azanulbizar, who walked with a limp ever after? Or the curse levied against my father Tandri by Bolg himself, that he never again find valuable ore in the deeps?

'I just want these Elves to acknowledge how dangerous Mazog is, even in captivity, and to post a Greyhammer sentry wherever he is being kept. You go back and tell Alfirimbes that. My family deserves this honour after all the hurts Mazog and his kin have wrought on mine.''The fate of the Greyhammers is tied up with the Orcs of Mazog's line and have been for long years. We deserve to be his jailors now! You go and tell Alfirimbes this. We won't be left out of this duty, to stand by and let Mazog escape the judgement coming to him!''I see. I admire the determination of the Greyhammers and am sure that Lúth and the rest of his family will be a great help to the Golden Host, but I hope he will spend more time with his duties and less time explaining the various grievances he bears against the Orcs.

'We have all suffered at their hands, and Lúth no more than the rest of us. Achardor might say he has suffered less than some.

'Mazog will account for all slights in time, both real and imagined. Raddir spoke with me while you sought the dwarf. It is time to bring Mazog deeper into Mirkwood.'The mission of the Hidden Guard begins as they take Mazog on the first leg of the journey through Mirkwood mapped by Raddir.Alfirimbes is at the Elf-camp of Echad Sirion in the Mirk-eaves.

The Hidden Guard is ready to begin the first leg of the journey to bring Mazog to Dol Guldur, by way of the Drownholt. Alfirimbes will bring you to them.Talk to Alfirimbes and travel with the Hidden GuardCúcheron is on the front porch of the Haunted Inn, mourning the loss of Raddir.

Raddir may be gone, but the mission of the Hidden Guard must continue. Cúcheron will tell you what should be done as the Elves try to regroup from the loss of one of their own.Talk to Cúcheron on the front porch of the Haunted Inn'Raddir has plotted a course through Mirkwood that avoids some of its more overt dangers, but this first leg may be treacherous. The path he has chosen winds through the foetid marshlands of the Drownholt. He names it Râd Cened and tells me it should be free of Orcs.

'But Raddir spoke of other hazards, the like of which we may not expect: spongy earth that clings to the foot, thickets of briars that will catch clothing and armour and break your concentration, great pools of stagnant water that can slow your progress to a crawl. You and the other members of the Hidden Guard will need to be cautious of these and other dangers. Few travel through the Drownholt, unless they have very good reason to do so. Keeping beneath the Enemy's notice until Mazog is at his doorstep is one such reason.

'Speak with me again, and I will show you to the rest of the company for this leg of the journey.''The Hidden Guard departs for Raddir's course through the Drownholt at midnight, ${PLAYER}. I hope you are prepared to join them.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>'I cannot believe that Raddir is dead! How can this have come to pass? And what now becomes of the mission of the Hidden Guard?''I do not know what we can do, ${PLAYER}. Only Raddir knows upon what paths he planned to bring us to Dol Guldur with our captive, and without him, the secret ways are veiled to us. I fear our errand stands on the very brink of failure before it has begun.'Defeat Cuthraul and Elhudan in Enedwaith.Defeat cuthraul and elhudan in EnedwaithDefeat many cuthraul and elhudan in Enedwaith.Defeat cuthraul and elhudan in EnedwaithYou eliminated much of the threat of traps and archers that made attacking Ashúrz Maufulug a particularly hazardous proposition, but there is more yet to do.Weapon-racks and crates of supplies can be found in Ashúrz Maufulug, to the south and a little west of Echad Glamodúd.

Glamodúd has asked you to further weaken the Orcs of Ashúrz Maufulug by destroying their weapons and supplies.Destroy crates of supplies at Ashúrz Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy weapons in Ashûrz Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, south and a little west from Ashúrz Maufulug.

You should return to Ashúrz Maufulug with news of your success.Talk to Glamodúd at Echad Glamodúd'You have removed many of the defences protecting Ashúrz Maufulug by disarming the traps of the Orcs, but there is more yet to do. Our forces in the Mirk-eaves are but a small portion of the company that ventured from Lothlórien. We must weaken the enemy, if we are to defeat them.

'I bid you foray against the camp and destroy any weapon-racks and crates of supplies you may find there. Without these, the Orcs will be hard-pressed to defend themselves.

'If you have lost your bearings, Ashúrz Maufulug lies to the south and a little west of here.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! The Orcs will not be able to maintain their presence here much longer without those weapons and supplies.

'I have one task left for you, if you would hear me out....''Do not return, ${PLAYER}, until you have destroyed the weapons and supplies of the Orcs. They are a threat to our very survival.'You found a set of orders in the quarters of a deserter in Enedwaith that partially detailed Isengard's plans for the region. Such information would doubtless be of interest to the Grey Rangers, and you believe you may be able to find the rest of these papers among the officers in Lhe Lhechu.Dunlending officers can be found in Lhe Lhechu, south-west of Echad Dagoras.

You should collect papers from the Dunlending officers in Fordirith and learn more of the reason for their presence on the borders of the old North Kingdom.Collect deserters' orders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagoras is at Echad Dagoras, north-east of Lhe Lhechu.

You should return the orders you have found to Dagoras.The papers you have found speak of the purpose behind Dunland's intrusion into the North, but they are partial and damaged by careless handling.

If you can find more parts of this document upon former officers among the Dunlending deserters, you may be able to piece together Saruman's intentions for the region.'What are these you have found...orders from Isengard? It seems the Dunlendings from the south were sent to capture the old Elf-ruins in Eregion. It seems Saruman was seeking something there, though I cannot begin to guess what that traitorous wizard would want from such a place.

'More importantly now, it seems that Saruman is bent on consolidating his power in Dunland. His thralls and allies are on the move, subduing any clans that have refused to join him up till now.

'We must make haste, for soon all of Dunland will be mobilized for war under the banner of Isengard!'Defeat Dunlendings in Enedwaith.Defeat Dunlendings in EnedwaithDefeat many Dunlendings in Enedwaith.Defeat Dunlendings in EnedwaithThe presence of goblin-spies in the Mirk-eaves also infers the presence of an enemy encampment somewhere in the vicinity.Glamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, south-east from Echad Sirion, at the southern foot of Amon Angened. Aemeldir is at Echad Sirion.

Farasgon has asked you to speak with Glamodúd regarding the Orc-camp to the south and Aemeldir regarding Dúrburz-stazg, the encampment to the north.Talk to Glamodúd at Echad GlamodúdTalk to Aemeldir at Echad Sirion'${PLAYER}, while you were gone, one of our scouts discovered the location of an Orc-encampment to the south and another to the north. However, these tokens you brought me belong to four different tribes or companies. I fear there are other camps we may not have found yet.

'While I send more patrols out to find the other encampments, you should travel to Echad Glamodúd, near the Orc-camp, and speak with Glamodúd, the chief scout there. He will give you further instruction.

'You should also speak with Aemeldir here at Echad Sirion... he was involved on the initial attack against Durbúrz-stazg and may know more about the remnant of the Orcs there. We must not be caught unaware between enemy forces!''You should meet with Glamodúd at Echad Glamodúd, south-east from here, at the southern foot of Amon Angened, where the main way-post of the Malledhrim has been established. He will tell you what aid he may need.

'Aemeldir here at Echad Sirion will know more about Dúrburz-stazg.''You have come from Echad Sirion? That is well, for we are in dire need of your assistance.''Greetings, ${PLAYER}. Yes, Falasgon is correct. I could most certainly use your assistance....'The Elves of the Golden Host seek a way to cripple the Orcs of Durbúrz-stazg.Durbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion.

Aemeldir has asked you to defeat servants of the Enemy at Durbúrz-stazg. You will need to enter the encampment through the eastern gate.Defeat servants of the Enemy at Durbúrz-stazg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Echad Sirion lies to the south of Durbúrz-stazg.

You should return to Aemeldir with news of your success.Talk to Aemeldir at Echad Sirion'It appears we may take advantage of the weaker defences at the eastern gate at Durbúrz-stazg, ${PLAYER}. It is time to test their strength.

'Enter Durbúrz-stazg by the eastern gate and engage the Enemy there. Test their mettle, then return to me. We may learn something about the encampment which may aid us.

'Durbúrz-stazg lies to the north, and the gate you seek opens through the eastern bulwark.''You have returned! What did you learn, ${PLAYER}?''Return to Durbúrz-stazg and defeat many of the Enemy there. You may learn something of value to us.'The Elves of the the Golden Host landed on the shores of the Mirk-eaves and drove the Orcs of the river-banks into the forest. Once they secured the shores, they established a camp there.Fállug lies to the south of Echad Sirion, overlooking the Anduin.

Tethafnel has asked you to plant the banner of the Malledhrim at Fállug so their kindred in Lothlórien will know of their victory.Tethafnel is at Echad Sirion, north from Fállug.

You should return to Tethafnel and let her know that you have planted the banner as she requested.Talk to Tethafnel at Echad Sirion'${PLAYER}, it is good that you have come. Our forces swept through this area like a storm, but we were unable to signal our kindred in Lothlórien that all went well.

'If you would, I have a task for you. Take this banner to Fállug, the ruins of an Orc-tower overlooking the Anduin to the south of here, and brace it with stones. Surely you will find a suitable pile of stones there.

'When our banner flies for our kindred to see, return to me.''Does our banner fly yet upon Fállug? The ruins lie to the south, overlooking the Anduin.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. You have planted the banner? Then all is well.

'Once the threat of siege is lessened, Lord Celeborn will muster a greater force to join us.'A few Elves who were among the first to cross the Anduin to make way for the main landing were captured by Orcs. If they are not rescued before the Malledhrim make their final assault upon Amon Angened, the prisoners will likely be killed.Elvish prisoners are being held in the Orc-fortress upon Amon Angened, south-east of Echad Sirion.

Agorin has asked you to mount the rescue of Elvish prisoners from their Orc-captors.Rescue a captured soldierAgorin is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern bank of the Anduin.

You should return to Agorin with news of your success.Talk to Agorin at Echad Sirion'I fear that a few of our number have been captured by the Orcs, pathfinders who came across the river in silence before our attack to mark the landing spots and eliminate the Enemy's sentries.

'Most of them have returned since we began our assault in earnest, but a few have not, nor have we seen any sign of their bodies, which the Orcs would have left to rot had they been slain. Thus I must believe that they yet live and are held captive nearby...most likely in the central fortification upon Amon Angened, as they have not had time to move prisoners to Dol Guldur.

'However, once we assault that fortress in earnest, they would most certainly kill any prisoners held there. If you could manage to get them out before then, the Malledhrim would be in your debt.''So the rescue attempt was a success? My thanks to you, ${PLAYER}! Now Fuirgam can launch his assault upon that fortress without fear for our brethren.''Hurry, ${PLAYER}! Fuirgam's assault upon the fortress will begin as soon as his forces are in position! If you cannot rescue our scouts from Amon Angened before he begins his attack, their fates are sealed.''Agorin sent you? Here?

'Well, I will not debate your bravery, friend ${RACE}, but let us fly swiftly!'Two bridges ford the stream south of Echad Sirion. By means of these bridges, Orc-reinforcements may flank the Malledhrim.The two bridges lie to the south of Echad Sirion, along a small tributary to the Anduin.

Ivorel has asked you to take the two bridges allowing access to the Mirk-eaves from the south.Capture the western bridgeCapture the eastern bridgeIvorel is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

You should inform Ivorel that both bridges were already destroyed.Talk to Ivorel at Echad Sirion'A fine day for battle, do you not agree, ${PLAYER}?

'In any case, Fuirgam has tasked me with ensuring that we are not taken unaware from the south. There is a small river there, with a few bridges leading to Orc-encampments on the far side. We cannot spare the forces to assault those fortifications, so we are going to take the bridges instead and prevent them from crossing over.

'I am certain that you can handle a straightforward task such as that, can you not?''The bridges were already down by the time you arrived?

'Typical Orc-cowardice. They cut them at the first sign of danger and saved us the trouble of even worrying about them for the moment.''Celeborn has bidden us make haste in our assault, and so we have come lightly prepared. We have no tools of siege with which to reduce Dol Guldur, and Amrúnwen has prepared supplies for little more than two weeks' effort.

'It seems that our assault is not meant to destroy Dol Guldur at all...so why assault the fortress at all?'Communication between the Orc-fortifications scattered across the Mirk-eaves are handled by goblin-runners who rush messages from one to another. The defeat of these runners not only would cut the encampments off from each other, but may result in the interception of important information about the Enemy's movements.Goblin-runners can be found throughout the Mirk-eaves.

Ivorel has asked you to intercept and defeat the goblin-runners that carry messages from camp to camp in the Mirk-eaves.Defeat goblin-runners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ivorel is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

You should return to Ivorel with news of your success.Talk to Ivorel at Echad Sirion'I have a little challenge for you, ${PLAYER}! Do you see all of those Orc-fortifications out there? They communicate with each other through trained runners -- goblins, usually -- who carry messages from one to another. Defeat those messengers, and their communication will be disrupted.

'If you are fortunate, you might even capture a message or two from them, though they usually memorize the information they are supposed to deliver to avoid such issues.

'When you have done as I have asked, return to me here.''So, were you able to learn anything from the goblin-runners? No?

'Do not fret. They are rarely entrusted with anything of import, and this stage of the battle should not last long enough for anything we learned from them to matter much.

'Our main goal is to cut them off from each other and leave them disorganized, and in that, you have performed admirably.''In recent years, my scouts have kept a watchful eye upon Dol Guldur, and in the past, the Lord and Lady have forbidden any assault upon it, believing the risk of defeat too great should our forces prove unable to tumble its obsidian walls.

'What counsel has changed their minds, I wonder? It must have something to do with our recent visitors from afar.'A handful of Elves have become separated from the main host during the battle to take the Mirk-Eaves.The Elf-soldiers may be found among the trees of the Mirk-eaves.

Agorin has asked you to aid the missing Elves should you find them amongst the forests of the Mirk-eaves.Rescue desperate soldierRescue exhausted soldierRescue wounded soldierAgorin is at Echad Sirion on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

You should return to Agorin and let her know that you have found and aided the missing soldiers.Talk to Agorin at Echad Sirion'A handful of our soldiers have gone missing and I fear they may have been cut off from our forces during the initial rush of the assault. Keep a watchful eye out for any of them while you are out in the Mirk-eaves and lend them whatever aid you can if you do come across them.

'They are skilled warriors in their own right, but there are a great many Orcs still roaming the area....''It seems that you have managed to recover our missing soldiers, ${PLAYER}. Excellent.

'We cannot afford to lose too many soldiers this early in the campaign...we have a hard road ahead of us still.''So many of our kindred will die this day, and I do not understand the meaning of it.

'Our strength is far greater in Lothlórien where the Lady's powers confound our enemies...why has Lord Celeborn ordered us against the walls of Dol Guldur?'In battles of such a scale as the Mirkwood landing, severe wounds and even death are an inevitable consequence, even among such fine warriors as the Mallhedrim.The supplies are at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

Agorin has tasked you with finding clean bandages that have been misplaced among the rest of the military supplies that were hastily brought across the Anduin.Collect bandages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The wounded Elves are at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

Now that you have collected enough bandages, you should see to the treatment of the Elf-soldiers who were seriously wounded during the first wave of the assault upon Mirkwood.Agorin is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the AnduinTalk to Agorin at Echad Sirion'We have little time here before more wounded arrive or those who have been most sorely injured pass into the West, but we have not even had a chance to unpack our supplies as yet, and in the rush of the landing, these fools have mixed the bandages and other healer's goods in with the rest of the crates!

'I need you to find the bandages in among the other supplies, then see to as many of the wounded as you can... and quickly!

'Return to me when you have completed this task.''Do not mourn for us, ${PLAYER}, for our fallen await us in the Halls of the West.

'We regret only the pain that such darkness inflicts and the vast gulf of time during which we must be parted from those we dearly love, and so we fight to live as fiercely as any mortal must.''Do not mourn for us, ${PLAYER}, for our fallen await us in the Halls of the West.

'We regret only the pain that such darkness inflicts and the vast gulf of time during which we must be parted from those we dearly love, and so we fight to live as fiercely as any mortal must.''My thanks to you, stranger. That seems to have stopped the bleeding.''Thank you! I could not have done as well myself... even were my arm not broken!'The Elf grimaces silently as you try to staunch the bleeding of a severe stomach wound.

After you do the best you can, you move on, unsure whether he will live through the night.'You... you have my thanks... good ${RACE}.'This soldier is having serious trouble breathing and cannot speak. You realize that the left side of his chest has been nearly crushed by some massive blow.

You bandage some of his lesser wounds in an effort to comfort him, but he is clearly dying and beyond aid.'Your care for our soldiers is timely and much appreciated, ${PLAYER}.

'With some rest and healing, most of them should be able to return to Lothlórien to recover in a few days.

'Those who cannot, we shall be reunited with in ages to come in the Furthest West....'The Elves of the Golden Host have established an encampment on the shores of the Mirk-eaves and seek to protect it against the spies of the Enemy.Crebain and Wargs can be found throughout the Mirk-eaves.

Faroniel has asked you to blind the eyes of Dol Guldur by defeating many of the crebain and Wargs which roam the Mirk-eaves.Defeat Darkwing spies in the Mirk-eaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Warg-scouts in the Mirk-eaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Faroniel is at Echad Sirion in the Mirk-eaves.

You should return to Faroniel with tidings of your success.Talk to Faroniel at Echad Sirion'If you have a moment, ${PLAYER}, I would speak with you. Our forces landed recently upon this shore and drove off the Orcs after a mighty battle; however, many dark creatures have been seen lurking upon these shores still.

'Many Wargs and crebain roam the Mirk-eaves, undoubtedly spying for the Enemy at Dol Guldur. The eyes of Dol Guldur must be blinded to our movements. If you would purge the crebain and Wargs from these shores, I would be most grateful.

'Be wary upon your task, for goblin-scouts also roam the beaches, and they may ambush you.''Very good, ${PLAYER}! It will be long ere the eyes of Dol Guldur will be fixed upon us. Perhaps by then, the rest of our forces will have joined us.''Have you defeated the spies of Dol Guldur? Their masters must not learn how small our camp is.'Among the fell spirits which have taken form as Shadow-wolves, there is one that is more dangerous than all the rest.The Fang of Shadows stalks the area outside the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras.

Amarion has asked you to hunt the Fang of Shadows, leader of the Shadow-wolves in the Black Dens.Defeat the Fang of ShadowsAmarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens.

You should speak with Amarion and let him know that you have defeated the Fang of Shadows, but that the power of the Black Dens seems unbroken.Talk to Amarion at Echad Dagoras'Something particularly evil stalks this corner of Enedwaith. We have no idea how they came here, but the wolves of the Black Dens are altogether unnatural. They look like wolves and seem to behave as such, but they are not mortal creatures. They are fell spirits that stalk and hunt Men.

'Nor are they aimless -- they are seeking something. The locals say that some were seen in Eregion weeks ago, ranging far and wide in search of their prey, but then they left and returned here to their dens. Only when we of the Dúnedain came did they emerge and resume their hunt...for us it now seems. They can be slain as any wolf might be, but with death they melt away like a shadow in the light of the noon sun.

'When you rescued me I was hunting one of their kind that seemed unique -- a great feral shadow that dominated the others. It was my hope that should this one be slain, then whatever power binds them here would be broken -- but as you know, I became the hunted instead and am still too injured to try my hand at it again. Would you take up my hunt? I cannot say what will come of it, but the passage of our brethren through Enedwaith would be considerably simpler without packs of Shadow-wolves nipping at our flanks the whole way.''So, even with the defeat of the Fang of Shadows, we still seem no closer to breaking the spell that binds these terrible spirits.

'Well, at least that one shall not hunt today, though I suspect we shall see it again before long. My thanks for your efforts...and hopefully a short respite.''The Fang of Shadows is a leader among the Shadow-wolves...hunt him and defeat him, ${PLAYER}.'While most of the Stoors of Maur Tulhau are master farmers and expert hunters, a few choose to make their living fishing.Discover the Fishing Hole.Discover the Fishing HoleThere are two Orc-fortifications along the Anduin which are a cause of concern for Fuirgam.Durbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion. Fállug lies to the south of Echad Sirion.

Fuirgam has ordered you to take the gate of one of the Orc-fortifications along the banks of the Anduin river.Take the gate of one of the Orc-fortificationsDurbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion. Fállug lies to the south of Echad Sirion.

Now that you have taken the gate of one of the Orc-fortifications, you must hold it against the Enemy.Hold the gate against the Enemy<rgb=#FF0000>Do not surrender the gate</rgb>Fuirgam's Aide is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern bank of the Anduin.

You should return to him with tidings of your victory.Talk to Fuirgam's Aide at Echad Sirion'${PLAYER}, there are a pair of Orc-fortifications defending the banks of the Anduin: one which they call Durbúrz-stazg lies immediately to our north; the other -- Fállug -- a bit further to the south. One of our first objectives here is to eliminate these two fortifications so that our landing can continue unimpeded.

'We need you to bolster our forces attacking the encampments, particularly the assaults upon their gates. You must choose one of them to assault -- you cannot be in two places at once -- take its gate, and hold it for as long as you can. We will send reinforcements there as soon as possible.''Well fought, ${PLAYER}. Now that the Enemy is pinned within those fortifications, we can work on destroying them altogether.''The camps to the north and south are heavily defended, but Malledhrim forces are already assaulting them.

'With your aid, we should be able to take them swiftly, and time is of the essence as we open our assault.'The Gostannon guards the way between the Mirk-eaves and the Dourstocks in the east. It allows the Enemy passage to reinforce their armies in the Mirk-eaves.The Gostannon lies in the north-west corner of the Mirk-eaves, some distance to the east of Echad Sirion.

Fuirgam has asked you to jam the mechanism of the Gostannon to delay enemy reinforcements from coming out of the east.Jam the gate mechanismFuirgam's Aide is at Echad Sirion, west of the Gostannon.

You should return to him with your report.Talk to Fuirgam's Aide at Echad Sirion'We must ensure that the commanders in Dol Guldur cannot get reinforcements into the Mirk-Eaves during our assault upon the fortress.

'Any large number of troops would have to come through the Gostannon, the gate upon the road that leads to the east. The Orcs still control it for now, but I am certain that we will soon capture it as well.

'For the moment, I need you to see that the gate is made useless to them. Try to jam the mechanism by which it is raised and lowered on this side. It will not slow them down for long, but by then our assault will be complete and the Mirk-eaves will be ours.''The Gostannon has been jammed?

'That will not slow the Orcs down for long, but it does not have to. Within hours, the Enemy's fortification up there will have fallen, and I will welcome any assault they care to waste against us there.''Our scouts tell us that the roads that lay between here and Dol Guldur are poorly defended. If we can take the fortress and that gate before the day is out, the Enemy will not be able to field forces quickly enough to prevent us from advancing at least as far as the ruins of Ost Galadh.'The approach to the Orc-fortress atop Amon Angened is watched by many siege-engines based at the Gostannon. If those engines cannot be destroyed before the Malledhrim's attack, the Golden Host will suffer grievious casualties beneath the hail of bolts and stones.Siege-engines can be found at the Gostannon Orc-camp, north-east of Echad Sirion.

Fuirgam has asked you to destroy the Orkish siege-engines in the Mirk-eaves.Destroy Orc-catapults (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Orc-ballistae (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fuirgam's Aide is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin, south-west of the Gostannon.

You should return to him with news of your success.Talk to Fuirgam's Aide at Echad Sirion'We are nearly ready for a decisive assault upon Amon Angened, but my men have warned me that a set of siege-engines lies in wait, looking upon the steep paths that we must scale to take the fortress.

'To muster an assault under the rain of such dark engines would result in needless death and might even cause our assault to falter.

'If you can destroy those engines before we begin the assault, the Orcs will have no choice but to face us in battle, where our valour shall prove unmatched!''It has been many long years since the Malledhrim have gone to war afield, ${PLAYER}. Such engines as the Enemy fields against us now seemed a distant, unpleasant memory... but too well do we recall their power.

'We will face many such as we approach Dol Guldur, so be on your guard.''You need say nothing, ${PLAYER}. I witnessed the smoke rising from the burning engines of the Orcs with my own eyes.

'We shall begin the assault shortly. Before night falls, the Mirk-eaves shall be in our hands, and we shall continue our march upon Dol Guldur.'The Taughâsh tribe which guards the Mirk-eaves against invasion use Wargs and Warg-riders to patrol the beachhead.Taughâsh Riders can be found throughout the Mirk-eaves.

Fuirgam has asked you to defeat the Taughâsh Riders that have been harassing the flanks of the Malledhrim soldiers invading the Mirk-eaves.Defeat Taughâsh Riders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fuirgam's Aide is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

You should bring your report back to him.Talk to Fuirgam's Aide at Echad Sirion'A problem has arisen for the Malledhrim, my friend. Our forces are being harried by groups of Warg-riders who are ranging throughout the Mirk-eaves. Normally, we rely upon speed and our superior skill in battle to ensure victory even when outnumbered, but the Warg-riders' great speed allows them to harry and assault my soldiers at will.

'We need you to help thin out their numbers and keep them at bay...at least until we have secured the Mirk-eaves from the Enemy. When you have done this, return to me for further instructions.''While there are doubtless more of these beasts and their goblin-masters in Dol Guldur, you have done well to thin their packs for the present.

'With our soldiers free to manoeuvre in small bands again, the Orcs will be pinned down and unable to leave their camps for fear of assault.''The keen senses and swift gait of the Wargs have ever been a danger to our scouts and skirmishers. Here, for once, we move in force with the strength to drive them back, but your help in winnowing their numbers would be much appreciated.'Fuirgam is prepared to launch his assault upon the Orc-fortification overlooking the Mirk-eaves, which, if successful, should break the back of the Orc-forces defending the forest, allowing the Malledhrim to advance to the tower of Dol Guldur.

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will end the assault upon the Mirk-eaves.

Any quests you have not yet completed in this area will be cancelled and will no longer be accessible afterwards.</rgb>Fuirgam's Aide is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

You should speak with him when you are ready to venture forth to conquer the fort atop Amon Angened, overlooking the Mirk-eaves.Talk to Fuirgam's Aide at Echad Sirion when you are ready to begin the assault on Amon AngenedAlfirimbes is at Echad Sirion on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

Fuirgam has asked you to return to speak with Alfirimbes, who is re-organizing the Malledhrim forces in the Mirk-eaves after the success of the landing.Talk to Alfirimbes at Echad Sirion'Many preparations have been made ready... in no small part due to your efforts upon our behalf, ${PLAYER}. Fuirgam is prepared to strike against the fortress that overlooks the Mirk-eaves, and with this thrust, we shall claim the banks of the Anduin as our own and drive the Orcs forth!

'Will you aid us in this endeavour? If so, speak with me again when you are ready to depart.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will end the assault upon the Mirk-eaves.

Any quests you have not yet completed in this area will be cancelled and will no longer be accessible afterwards.</rgb>'Fuirgam's force is ready to march...will you join them, ${PLAYER}? Battle awaits!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will end the assault upon the Mirk-eaves.

Any quests you have not yet completed in this area will be cancelled and will no longer be accessible afterwards.

This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'I am glad to see that you survived the opening stage of our assault, ${PLAYER}!

'It is thanks in no small part to your efforts that our advance upon Dol Guldur has been only lightly impeded by the servants of the Enemy. Our forces now advance through the forest of Mirkwood to claim Emyn Lûm, well to the east, but there is much to be done before we reach it.

'Gird yourself well, for the blackest of terrors yet stand before us.'The Enemy forces in the Mirk-eaves are commanded by uruks, grim and terrible.Taughâsh War-leaders can be found throughout the Mirk-eaves.

Fuirgam has asked you to defeat Taughâsh War-leaders which command the Enemy forces in the Mirk-eaves.Defeat Taughâsh War-leaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fuirgam's Aide is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

You should return to him with news of your success.Talk to Fuirgam's Aide at Echad Sirion'The battle is well underway now, ${PLAYER}, but time is not on our side, and we must hasten the defeat of our foe by any means.

'The Orcs and goblins here in the Mirk-eaves are driven by uruk-warleaders who drive them into battle. Without these strong leaders to threaten and lead them into battle, the rest will fall aside in disarray and fear of our strength!

'Take the battle to any of the uruks whom you should encounter... each one you defeat shall mean a swifter victory for us all.''The order for an assault upon Dol Guldur was sudden and unexpected, but we of the Malledhrim stand eternally vigilant and ready to heed Celeborn's call.

'Fortunately, our Enemy is overconfident and seems to have ignored the possibility that we might strike first, and so we hold the advantage for now.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! Your skills in battle match even those of the Malledhrim!

'With most of their uruk-leaders fallen, the remaining forces of the Enemy shall soon be driven back to Dol Guldur.'The Taughâsh tribe defending the Mirk-eaves against the Malledhrim rely heavily upon stores brought to their encampments before the invasion began.Supplies can be found at Durbúrz-stazg to the north of Echad Sirion and Fállug to the south.

Fuirgam has asked you to find and destroy the supply-crates in the Orc-fortifications of the Mirk-eaves.Destroy supply-crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fuirgam's Aide is at Echad Sirion, on the eastern banks of the Anduin.

You should return to him with news of your success.Talk to Fuirgam's Aide at Echad Sirion'The battle goes well thus far, ${PLAYER}, but the Orcs in the nearby fortresses are proving tenacious. It seems they have also laid in supplies for a prolonged siege, should it come to that... but we cannot afford to be tied down here for so long, or the might of Dol Guldur shall push us back into the Anduin!

'We bid you fight your way into those camps and destroy their supplies. This will both weaken their defence and ensure that none of them are able to retreat with valuable stores back to their dark tower.

'When you have completed this task, return here to me for further instructions.''The supplies have been destroyed? Well done, ${PLAYER}. Without those supplies of arrows and provisions, the Orcs will not be able to hold out much longer...and the rest of our forces are coming ashore and moving further into the forest as we speak.''While we seek to destroy the Enemy's supplies, our own stocks are in complete disarray.

'Poor Amrúnwen was caught totally unaware by Celeborn's sudden order for an attack and has been struggling mightily to put all in order, but the scale of our assault is of too great a scope, and she cannot possibly maintain the line.

'At least this battle shall not last overly long, and so if we must go hungry, it will only be for days, not weeks. I am more worried about our medicines and poultices, which we have great need of.'Defeat half-orcs in Enedwaith.Defeat half-orcs in EnedwaithDefeat many half-orcs in Enedwaith.Defeat half-orcs in EnedwaithYou were unable to defeat all of the Wargs, but Goldínwen has another plan.Goblin Warg-keepers can be found at Maudhul-ulur, south from Echad Glamodúd.

Goldínwen has asked you to defeat the goblin Warg-keepers in order to throw the kennel into disarray.Defeat Taughâsh Warg-keepers in Maudhul-ulur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Goldínwen is at Echad Glamodúd, north from Maudhul-ulur.

You should return to Goldínwen and report your success.Talk to Goldínwen at Echad Glamodúd'Besides slaying the Wargs, perhaps there is another way to make their Warg-breeding ineffective. Every camp has a leader, and these Wargs have many handlers.

'If you would, go to Maudhul-ulur and defeat any goblin-keepers you find. Perhaps by defeating the handlers, the Wargs will be thrown into disarray.

'When you have slain the goblin-keepers, return to me.''You have done well to defeat so many of the goblins, but I fear it is still not enough. This beast has many hands, but only one head....''Please...you must defeat the Warg-handlers of Maudhul-ulur, or they will continue to threaten Echad Sirion.'The Malledhrim seek to drive back the forces of Dol Guldur from the eaves of Southern Mirkwood.YOU SHOULDNT SEE THISDefeat enemies in the Mirk-eavesThe Elves of the Golden Host are concerned with the continued presence of Orcs in the Mirk-eaves and in procuring supplies for the Malledhrim in the east.The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angened, leading eastwards. The first patrol point lies to the north-west of Amon Angened, upon the road.

Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.Patrol the road to the GostannonThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.

Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.Patrol the road to the GostannonThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.

Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.Patrol the road to the GostannonThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.

Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.Patrol the road to the GostannonThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.

Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.Patrol the road to the GostannonDannaswen is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon.

You should report back to Dannaswen at once.Talk to Dannaswen atop Amon Angened'As you know, Falasgon sent word of another Orc-encampment near the Gostannon to the north. From what the scouts reported, the presence of the Enemy has been nearly wiped out at that camp, but we must be certain before devoting resources to destroy it.

'I would ask you a favour, ${PLAYER}: patrol the lands to the north, especially along the road leading to the Gostannon, to determine the strength of the foe.

'When you have completed your patrol, return here.''Then the scouts reports were accurate? This will make our task much easier.''The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}...when you have finished your patrol, return to me.''The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}...when you have finished your patrol, return to me.''The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}...when you have finished your patrol, return to me.''The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}...when you have finished your patrol, return to me.''The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}...when you have finished your patrol, return to me.'Amarion left camp to search the Black Dens, where he believed he might find some way to destroy the Shadow-wolves -- but he has been gone too long. Braigiar has asked you to search for him among the Dens in the hope that he might be found unharmed.Help Amarion escape from the Black Dens.Talk to AmarionSpeak with Amarion and return to Echad Dagoras in Fordirith.'Let us be off then!''Enough! You have fought well, ${PLAYER}, and at last we have a moment's respite.

'I have found something of import here, but this is neither the place nor time to speak of it, as we should leave this place swiftly.''I would say that we should move quickly before the wolves notice us....

'Wait, no, it is too late...they come!'Braigiar believes that his captain, Dagoras, has been captured by the Dunlending deserters after going to negotiate an agreement with them. He has asked you to try to find and rescue Dagoras from Lhe Lhechu.Speak with Dagoras and find a way to release him from his cell.Talk to DagorasFind the key to Dagoras' cell in the jailor's quarters.Find the key to Dagoras' cellFind the key to Dagoras' cell in the jailor's quarters.Release Dagoras from his cell.Release Dagoras from his cellEscape from Lhe Lhechu with Dagoras.Talk to DagorasEscape from Lhe Lhechu with Dagoras.Help Dagoras escapeSpeak with Dagoras again.Talk to Dagoras'Let us return to Echad Dagoras. I would not want to deny Braigiar his chance to ridicule me for allowing myself to be captured.''Listen carefully now: the guard who carries the key to this cell usually sleeps in the next room.

'You should be able to sneak in there and find the key -- or if necessary just relieve him of it personally.

'Try not to make too much noise though: this cell is small, and I do not have room for a lot of company here.''There is no time to waste! Let us depart.''Ah! It is good to be out in the open air again, but let us not tarry. The others will soon realize that something is wrong.''Good, they seem to have given up their pursuit. I think we are finally safe...for now.'Fuirgam is prepared to launch his assault upon the Orc fortress overlooking the Mirk-eaves. He has asked you to join his forces for the attack, which, if successful, should break the back of the Orkish forces defending the forest, allowing the Malledhrim to advance to the tower of Dol Guldur.

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will end the assault upon the Mirk-eaves. 

Any quests you have not yet completed in this area will be cancelled and will no longer be accessible afterwards.</rgb>Speak with Fuirgam and begin the assault upon the Orc fortress!Talk to FuirgamTalk to Fuirgam to end the battle and claim the fortress for the Malledhrim!'Your valiant strength has bought us this day, ${PLAYER}!

'With the fall of this cur, the Orcs are broken and no strength of theirs can stay our advance until we stand athwart the gates of Dol Guldur itself!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will end the assault upon the Mirk-eaves. 

Any quests you have not yet completed in this area will be cancelled and will no longer be accessible afterwards.</rgb>'This fort is ours now and the Orcs have been sent reeling back to cower at the heels of their masters in Dol Guldur!

'Now we must make haste to claim the roads that lie between the Mirk-eaves and the Necromancer's dark abode! I plan to make base amongst the ancient ruins of Emyn Lum, ${PLAYER} - may fate bring us together again there, for the days ahead shall be consumed with tumult and pain, ere we reach our final goal.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You have completed the invasion of Mirkwood Landing. You are now free to explore further into Mirkwood.</rgb>'Now is the time for us to strike! The uruk commander atop the fortress within is our target, should he fall, so falls the fortress to our claim!

'If you are prepared in body and mind, then I shall begin the assault!'The Hidden Guard begins the perilous crossing of the Drownholt with Mazog.Issuriel is waiting to speak with you upon the path of Râd Cened.

You have come part of the way along Raddir's chosen route through the Drownholt and must now walk the path of Râd Cened with Mazog.Talk to IssurielIssuriel has asked you to use her banner of the Golden Host to issue commands that she may support you in battle with whatever approaches.Use the banner of the Golden Host to issue support commands to IssurielRâd Cened Creepers have gathered to attack intruders within the Drownholt! You must defend Mazog from this threat!Defend MazogIssuriel is waiting to speak with you along the path of Râd Cened.Talk to IssurielIssuriel asked you to secure Mazog's shackles and to escort him forwards through the fens of the Drownholt to Cúcheron, waiting further ahead.Secure Mazog's shacklesCúcheron has scouted the next leg of your journey through the Drownholt with Mazog.Talk to CúcheronCúcheron has asked you to use his banner of the Golden Host to issue commands that he may support you in battle.Use the banner of the Golden Host to issue support commands to CúcheronCúcheron's position along the Hidden Guard's road through the Drownholt has come under attack. You must defend Mazog from these foes.Defend MazogCúcheron is waiting to ask you something, now that the attacks have ceased for the moment.Talk to CúcheronCúcheron has asked you to clear the tunnel north-east of his position of danger while he guards Mazog and to then return to him.Clear the tunnel of danger so Mazog can be safely escorted through itCúcheron is outside the tunnel, guarding Mazog and waiting for your return.Return to CúcheronIt is time to bring Mazog further along Râd Cened, the route Raddir has selected to bring the Hidden Guard through the perilous Drownholt.Secure Mazog's shacklesSigileth has scouted the next leg of your journey through the Drownholt with Mazog.Talk to SigilethSigileth has asked you to use her banner of the Golden Host to issue commands that she may support you in battle.Use the banner of the Golden Host to issue support commands to SigilethSigileth's position along the Hidden Guard's road through the Drownholt has come under attack. You must defend Mazog from these foes.Defend MazogSigileth is waiting to speak with you, now that the attacks have ceased for the moment.Talk to SigilethSigileth asked you to secure Mazog's shackles and to escort him forward through the fens of the Drownholt to Raddir, waiting further ahead.Secure Mazog's shacklesThe unthinkable has happened: Raddir has been slain within the Drownholt.Examine the bodyMazog has a sinister look in his eye. Ensure that his shackles remain secure.Secure Mazog's shacklesMazog is trying to escape! You must reach Achardor, further along the path chosen by Raddir through the Drownholt, before Mazog does!Reach Achardor before Mazog doesYou have warned Achardor of Mazog's attempt to escape, and now the Orc can be recaptured.Talk to AchardorFollowing the death of Raddir, the Hidden Guard has made its limping way to the cellar of an inn among the Dourstocks, there to decide what can be done.Talk to Achardor in the cellar of the Haunted InnBróin is in the Bleak Cellar, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Bróin'I need some fresh air, ${PLAYER}. Let us go out onto the porch of the Inn. The sight of our prisoner makes me feel ill.''We have come part of the way, ${PLAYER}, but there is a long way to go yet; the Drownholt is perilous, and while Raddir has chosen our road with care, we must still use caution. The rest of the Hidden Guard have gone on ahead, for we cannot move as a group if we are to maintain our secrecy. You will bring Mazog to the members of our company, further ahead in the fen.

'Did you hear that? Something approaches! I will leave the coordination of our attack in your hands; shout your commands of me by this banner, and we will repel whatever evil approaches! My talents are for the restoration of morale and power, though they will be of no use for our prisoner. Do not let Mazog sustain injury!''Use this banner of the Golden Host to issue commands to me, ${PLAYER}. I will do my best to support you during battle with the restoration of morale and power.''We have done well to repel the creepers of the Drownholt, ${PLAYER}, but there will be more, I am sure of it. We must protect Mazog from their barbs and grasping tendrils, though our hearts be not fully in it!

'Make certain his shackles are secure, and travel forward with him through the swamp. Cúcheron should be just ahead.'You ensure that Mazog's shackles are secure. The Orc sneers at you, and his eyes glow yellow with hate.'The passage so far has gone smoothly, but our fortunes in this miserable swamp can change in a moment, if we let down our guard; so we must not!

'If you stand by this banner and shout your commands for me, I can provide support in battle. Arrows I let fly from Cúmaeth can slow the attack speed of our foes or make difficult their movement; additionally, I can pepper our enemies with such a flight of shafts that their general defences are broken.

'Use this banner of the Malledhrim during battle to tell me which of these tactics you desire!''I can target specific limbs of our foes to either slow their attack speed or movement speed, or rain such fury upon them with my bow Cúmaeth that their defences be broken. Tell me which of these tactics you wish me to use by using this banner of the Malledhrim.''I have not seen creatures of that sort within a league of Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}. They fill me with disgust. Still, we triumphed over them, and Cúmaeth has many arrows left in reserve.

'There is a tunnel just ahead; it lies upon the route Raddir selected for us. I do not wish to bring Mazog through there until we know it be clear.

'I will stay here and guard Mazog. Enter the tunnel and clear it of any dangers and then return here to me. Then you can bring the Orc safely through the tunnel.''The tunnel is just to the north-east, ${PLAYER}. Clear it of dangers and then return to me. I will remain here and guard Mazog until your return.'You explain Cúcheron's desire that you clear the tunnel of dangers before bringing Mazog through it, and Raddir nods.

'That is a good idea; the creepers here remained asleep for Sigileth and I to pass through, but of course Mazog would have sought to awaken them at the worst possible moment! Cúcheron is perhaps more canny than I gave him credit for being!'

Raddir seems to think for a moment, and then haltingly begins.

'I came back here because I thought I saw... I thought I saw someone I knew, ${PLAYER}... a friend. But it could not be, for this friend... this friend has not walked this way for many a year and has since gone where none may follow.

'If I did not know better, I would have sworn it was he. But here there is nothing but creepers. It was a trick of the light, my error in the dim.''The tunnel is clear? Good. I fought off some more fen-lizards, but it was nothing I could not handle with Cúmaeth.

'Ensure that Mazog's shackles are secure and bring him through the tunnel. You should have no more problems.'You check Mazog's shackles, and they remain secure. He stares assessingly at you, which is somehow more disconcerting than his usual sneer.'According to Raddir, this is the mid-point of Râd Cened, the road he has chosen for us to take through the Drownholt. You are lucky, Mazog, that we have need of you alive! Were it my decision to make, or Achardor's, you would be slain already and left to rot within one of the foetid pools of this swamp!'

Mazog says nothing, and Sigileth continues.

'This banner of the Golden Host will allow you to select a support role for me to use during battle, ${PLAYER}. I can draw the life-blood of our foes with Lanchigil and Egnassigil or provide you with morale or power support. It is up to you.''Shout your commands for my support role by this banner of the Malledhrim, ${PLAYER}. I am expert at drawing the life-blood of my foes with my twin knives, Lanchigil and Egnassigil, but I am also adept at restoring depleted morale and power.''We have done well to repel these attacks, ${PLAYER}. Ensure that Mazog's shackles remain secure and bring him further into the Drownholt.

'You will encounter Raddir next along Râd Cened. Give him my thanks for planning this route. We have done well to weather its dangers, and Mazog's presence is still a secret to the Orcs of Mirkwood.'You ensure that Mazog's shackles remain secure. Once again, the Orc rewards you only with an appraising stare.You call his name and try to get a response from the Elf, but it is already too late: Raddir is dead.

There are no signs of a struggle or any mark of injury that you can see, but despite that puzzle, one thing is clear: the Hidden Guard has lost one of its own.'What a delight! Look how fall the Elves that seek to imprison me, one by one. Perhaps you will be next, ${PLAYER}, ${RACE} that deserves it so!

'So end all enemies of Mazog, Lord of Caves! No shackles can bind me forever, and if my hands be bound let my legs carry me to the allies that must have done this, the allies that even now seek to free me from bondage!

'Ho, Orcs of my distant kin! You seek to free Mazog, and he will be free with the rewards of generosity!''We cannot talk here, ${PLAYER}. We have blocked the Orc's escape, but now we must gather the rest of the Hidden Guard and devise a new plan. Without Raddir....'

Achardor's face is a storm-cloud of emotions. He brings himself under control, but it is clearly an effort.

'We must rejoin the Malledhrim. There is a village called Audaghaim among the Dourstocks. The plan was for the main body of the Malledhrim to use it as a supply point before advancing further into Mirkwood. We must go there and discuss what is to be done.''The memory of our desperate journey overland out of the Drownholt is a hazy one, ${PLAYER}, but we have arrived at Audaghaim. It is a place for us to lick our wounds, though not all our wounds can be healed, here or anywhere.

'I cannot believe Raddir is gone! Can our mission have failed even as it begins?

'I will sharpen my blade. It may drink the blood of our prisoner soon, once we see wisdom and abandon this foolhardy errand.''This journey has already cost us a great deal, ${PLAYER}, and with every loss, it becomes more difficult to keep this wretch alive!

'I cannot stand to look at him. To tally up the pain he has already cost us would take a long while already, and I worry he is not done adding to it!

'Let us leave this cellar for now. Achardor will watch him... and Sigileth and the others will watch Achardor.'The Hidden Guard, the company of Elves charged with delivering Mazog in secret to Dol Guldur, is preparing to make the crossing of Anduin, after which they will meet the dwarves transporting the Orc-leader.Braiglinn is waiting to speak with you at Imlad Lalaith.Talk to BraiglinnBraiglinn has brought you to meet some of the Elves you will be fighting alongside during the Golden Host's journey through Mirkwood: Raddir, Sigileth, and Achardor.Talk to RaddirTalk to SigilethTalk to AchardorBraiglinn is waiting to bring you to more of the Elves that make up the Hidden Guard.Talk to BraiglinnBraiglinn has brought you to meet two more of the Elves you will be fighting alongside during the journey to Dol Guldur: Cúcheron and Issuriel.Talk to CúcheronTalk to IssurielCairches is waiting to transport you across Anduin with the company of Elves charged with delivering Mazog to Dol Guldur.Talk to CairchesYou have crossed the river with the company of Elves charged with delivering Mazog to Dol Guldur, and Raddir is now waiting to speak with you.Talk to RaddirThe Elves and dwarves are discussing the plans concerning Mazog.Listen to the discussion of the plan concerning MazogBróin has asked to speak with you.Talk to Bróin'It will be my pleasure to guide the Hidden Guard across the river on this, the first step of their journey.

'May it end in victory.''Welcome, ${PLAYER}! We are the Hidden Guard, formed by order of the Lord and Lady, and it is our mission to bring Mazog to the gates of Dol Guldur, there to trade his life for those of the prisoners held in that fortress. Secrecy is our watchword, and surprise our ally!

'Issuriel has told me already of your great deeds. I know you will be a vital member of the Hidden Guard on this journey!''At last we are underway, ${PLAYER}! If you have faith in these Elves, this "Hidden Guard," then I will as well.

'May our journey through Mirkwood be swift, and our return trip be the swifter, with Bori and the other captives hale and hearty!''Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel have determined that the Elves of Lothlórien must stand allied with the dwarves of Moria, as long ago they once did. They have selected a number of Elves to oversee the passage of Mazog through Mirkwood to Dol Guldur, where the Orc will be exchanged for the prisoners held by the Enemy in that fortress.

'I will bring you to these Elves, this Hidden Guard, as they make their preparations.''The Elves of the Hidden Guard were chosen for their varied expertise in a number of areas: Sigileth for her skill in melee combat and Raddir for his expert tracking ability.

'Were it my decision, I might have let Achardor join the main force of the Malledhrim rather than the Hidden Guard, given the recent tragedy of his brother's death. But I am sure Lady Galadriel had her own reasons for speaking on his behalf and believes he will be an important part of the Hidden Guard.

'I will bring you to the rest of the company, ${PLAYER}.''I am Sigileth, ${PLAYER}, and I know already of your deeds. You are welcome to accompany us upon this errand, though I have my doubts as to its wisdom. It is a sorrow that the dwarves have lost their own to the cages of the Enemy, but that is the way of war. Returning Mazog to his allies seems indefensible to me.

'If Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel see value in it, it is not the place of Sigileth to question.''Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}! It is good to see you again, and I welcome you to the ranks of the Hidden Guard. The knives of Sigileth, the bow of Cúcheron, the path-knowledge of Raddir, and the strong will of Achardor will see this mission through, and the friendship between Moria and Lothlórien will be stronger for it.

'Let the Enemy quake when he learns of the approach of the Golden Host, and he will think nothing of the Hidden Guard until we be at the gates of Dol Guldur and demand the prisoners kept there in exchange for the life of Mazog.''My brother Faengris was slain by Orcs that came down from the mountains following the company that sought refuge in the Golden Wood recently, and I desire to end Mazog's life myself! It pains me to know we must turn him over to his allies, and I have argued long against it already.

'I petitioned Lord Celeborn to let me accompany the group transporting the prisoner, but he denied my request. Only once the Lady Galadriel spoke to him did he change his mind; I do not know what she said, but I am grateful to her for it! Now I will keep a close eye upon Mazog for the duration of the journey, and if he gives me the slightest reason, I will take my vengeance upon him.''It is a pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}. I know that you will be a great asset to us upon this errand. If we are to bring the Orc-leader to Dol Guldur with the hope that we can exchange his freedom for that of the dwarf prisoners, we must do so in secret. Our numbers are not so great that we can resist a determined effort to take him from us before reaching the fortress.''We have made the crossing, ${PLAYER}. The dwarves should be just ahead with their captive; let us greet them and discuss the plans for our journey.''Let us see the camp these Elves have made. There will be little in the way of dwarf-comforts here in these dark woods, but I will do the best I may not to complain. A great journey awaits us!''Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. I did not expect to see you here, but I am glad that you have come.

'The Golden Host departs for Mirkwood to bring war upon the Enemy beyond the borders of Lothlórien, and I sat by Faengris' tree and watched them depart. Faengris' brother Achardor goes with them, seeking vengeance for my lost husband. I told him what I told you, that I want to cherish Faengris' memory instead of seeking revenge, but he did not listen.

'Please keep him from harm, ${PLAYER}. Too much death has come to my family already.''Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. I did not expect to see you here, but I am glad that you have come.

'The Golden Host departs for Mirkwood, to bring war upon the Enemy beyond the borders of Lothlórien, and I sat by Faengris' tree and watched them depart. Faengris' brother Achardor goes with them, seeking vengeance for my lost husband. I told him what I told you, that I want to cherish Faengris' memory instead of seeking revenge, but he did not listen.

