'Please keep him from harm, ${PLAYER}. Too much death has come to my family already.'The organized Wargs of Maudhul-ulur remain a great threat to the Elves of the Malledhrim.Âthruk can be found at Maudhul-ulur, south from Echad Glamodúd.

Goldínwen has asked you to defeat Âthruk, the overseer of Maudhul-ulur.Defeat Âthruk at Maudhul-ulurGoldínwen is at Echad Glamodúd, north from Maudhul-ulur.

You should return to Goldínwen with news of your victory.Talk to Goldínwen at Echad Glamodúd'In the end, I believe the only way to truly reduce the threat of the Wargs is to defeat their leader. Cut off the head, and the serpent will die.

'Amid the Wargs of Maudhul-ulur, there is a Warg-rider who leads them all. Defeat Âthruk and his beast, and the Wargs will surely be thrown into disarray.

'Return to me when your task is done, and I will reward you as best I can.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}! The Wargs of Maudhul-ulur will surely fear us now.

'You have earned this reward and the gratitude of the Malledhrim.''Âthruk still lives? That is ill news. He must be slain, or the Wargs remain a threat.'The Elves of the Golden Host seek a way to cripple the Orcs of Durbúrz-stazg.Durbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion.

Aemeldir has asked you to scout the gates of Durbúrz-stazg to determine which is the least guarded.Scout the southern gate of Durbúrz-stazgScout the eastern gate of Durbúrz-stazgAemeldir is at Echad Sirion, south of Durbúrz-stazg.

You should return to Aemeldir with the results of your patrol.Talk to Aemeldir at Echad Sirion'Hail, ${PLAYER}! Falasgon was right to send you to me. The Orcs of Dol Guldur mustering in the Mirk-eaves were well nigh destroyed, but a few survived and have holed up in the ruins of their encampments, attempting to regroup against us.

'One such encampment is Durbúrz-stazg, which lies just to the north of Echad Sirion. While the encampment was severely damaged in our first assault, it may still only be entered through two gateways.

'Go north and find the gateways into Durbúrz-stazg and determine which one is the least heavily guarded; it is upon that gate that we shall lean our assault.''You met resistance at both gates? Tell me more.''Scout the gates of Durbúrz-stazg; we must determine the best way into the camp.'The Elves at the way-post atop Amon Angened provide supplies and provisions for the main force of the Malledhrim in the east.Ninglyr may be found around the ruins of Fállug, west of Amon Angened.

Gaerfalas has asked you to gather ninglor flowers for use in preparing medicines.Collect ninglyr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gaerfalas is at the way-post atop Amon Angened, east of Fállug.

You should bring the flowers you collected to Gaerfalas.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! Do you wish to be of assistance? Good! This waypost is the beginning of the supply line to our main force fighting its way to Dol Guldur. There are some supplies that we are short of, however. One of those is medicine.

'Fortunately, I think this shortage may be resolved quickly. It is said that life oft springs up where death has passed. Flowers sometimes grow where battle has occurred.

'If you could go to the ruins of the Orc-camp Fállug to the west, you may find ninglyr growing there. These flowers may be used in preparing medicines. Bring some to me, and you will be rewarded.''The beautiful ninglor is also a marvelous curative. Please bring me some from the ruins of Fállug.''Yes, these flowers will be of much value to us. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'While patrolling the Gloomglens, you were amazed to find items clearly belonging to hobbit-folk, however rustic.Find evidence of the Stoors who settled in Enedwaith.Find a hobbit-arrow in the GloomglensFind hobbit-boots in the GloomglensFind a hobbit-bucket in the GloomglensFind a hobbit-skeleton in the GloomglensFind a hobbit-pick in the GloomglensFind a hobbit-bow in the GloomglensThe Elves at the way-post atop Amon Angeled provide supplies and provisions for the main force of the Malledhrim in the east.Agonglok may be found around the ruins of Fállug, west of Amon Angeled.

Thindiel has asked you to defeat the Warg Agonglok.Defeat Agonglok at FállugThindiel is at the way-post atop Amon Angeled, east of Fállug.

You should bring news of your victory against Agonglok to Thindiel.Talk to Thindiel atop Amon Angened'At Fállug, our scouts have encountered a vicious Warg, who stalked them all the way back to our encampments. This creature is a threat to those of us who continue to patrol the wilds of Southern Mirkwood.

'Travel to Fállug, if you would, ${PLAYER}, and put an end to this beast. For such a deed, you will receive what reward I may offer.

'Hurry, ${PLAYER}! We cannot allow this Warg to continue harrying our scouts.''You may find Agonglok in the ruins of Fállug to the west.''Agonglok has been defeated? That is a relief, ${PLAYER}. You have well-earned this reward.'Shadow-wolves stalk the lands of Fordirith, hunting the members of the Grey Company with deadly intent.At night, Shadow-wolves can be found throughout the region, but during the light of day they seem to lair in and around the Black Dens only.

Amarion has asked you to defeat several of the Shadow-wolves that stalk Fordirith.Defeat Shadow-wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Amarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens.

You should bring news of your success to Amarion.Talk to Amarion at Echad Dagoras'These strange black wolves stalk Fordirith, particularly at night as the shadows grow long and the sun is hidden from view.

'These fell spirits hunt us with dark purpose, ${PLAYER}, and if our company is to pass safely, we must slay as many as we can and drive them back to their lairs.

'Go forth, my friend, and aid us with your prowess. Drive back this shadow, so that we may fulfill our purpose in the South.''These fell spirits are relentless, ${PLAYER}. Despite your efforts, these creatures reappear in full number.

'Ah well, I must thank you for your efforts nonetheless.''Deal with the Shadow-wolves, ${PLAYER}...they are a great threat to our quest.'The Grey Company rides to the aid of their chieftain Aragorn in Rohan. While travelling through the sparsely inhabited region of Enedwaith, they uncover many strange mysteries.Complete quests within Enedwaith.Complete quests within EnedwaithThe Grey Company rides to the aid of their chieftain Aragorn in Rohan. While travelling through the sparsely inhabited region of Enedwaith, they uncover many strange mysteries.Complete quests within Enedwaith.Complete quests within EnedwaithThe Grey Company rides to the aid of their chieftain Aragorn in Rohan. While travelling through the sparsely inhabited region of Enedwaith, they uncover many strange mysteries.Complete quests within Enedwaith.Complete quests within EnedwaithThe Grey Company rides to the aid of their chieftain Aragorn in Rohan. While travelling through the sparsely inhabited region of Enedwaith, they uncover many strange mysteries.Complete quests within Enedwaith.Complete quests within EnedwaithRangers of the North, kinsmen of Aragorn son of Arathorn, have ridden forth to their chieftain's aid. As they pass south to Rohan, scout the way ahead for the best roads.Discover the camps of the Grey Company.Discover Echad DagorasDiscover Echad SaeradanDiscover Echad IdhrenfairDiscover Echad DaervunnDiscover HarndirionThe Elves of the Golden Host landed on the eastern shore of the Anduin and drove a wedge through the heart of the Orcs, but there is still danger within the Mirk-eaves.Goblin-scouts can be found sneaking throughout the Mirk-eaves.

Falasgon has asked you to find and defeat some of the goblin-scouts that have been spotted near Echad Sirion. Perhaps they might carry something that will suggest the location of their camp.Collect tokens of Dol Guldur from goblin-scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Falasgon is at Echad Sirion in the Mirk-eaves.

You should bring the tokens you found to Falasgon for his examination.'We took the Orcs by surprise when we landed, and quickly routed them into the forest; however, we believe they may either have another camp nearby or are preparing a retaliatory assault, for we have recently seen goblin-scouts on occasion.

'We have dispatched our own patrols to find their camp, but have thus far been unsuccessful. If you would, scour the Mirk-eaves for these elusive scouts. Perhaps they may carry some clue as to their camp's whereabouts. They have a mastery of stealth, so it may be difficult to find them.

'Also, you should speak with Tethafnel and Faroniel here at Echad Sirion. They may have other tasks for you.''Have you learned anything yet? We have seen goblin-scouts throughout the mirk-eaves, but they are masters of stealth.''These tokens bespeak of several encampments, ${PLAYER}. I will send scouts out immediately to find them.

'Remain here, though...I may yet have a task for you....'The Orcs of Ashúrz Maufulug have placed many traps around their encampment, but those were only one of many defences.Orc-archers can be found patrolling the outskirts of Ashúrz Maufulug, south and a little west from Echad Glamodúd.

Glamodúd has asked you to defeat the Orc-archers who defend Ashúrz Maufulug.Defeat Taughâsh archers at Ashúrz Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, north and a little east from Ashúrz Maufulug.

You should return to Glamodúd with news of your victory.Talk to Glamodúd at Echad Glamodúd'The traps were only one of many defences Ashúrz Maufulug maintains, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs are also defended by several skilled archers.

'These archers patrol the outskirts of Ashúrz Maufulug for signs of approaching enemies. Defeat these archers, or we will be unable to attack the camp.

'When you have completed this task, return to me.''Very well done yet again, ${PLAYER}! However, there is still a great threat within Ashúrz Maufulug.''The archers of the Taughâsh are highly skilled. They are a threat that must be removed.'The Elves of the Golden Host are concerned with the continuing presence of Orcs in the Mirk-eaves and in procuring supplies for the Malledhrim in the east.The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.

Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.Find signs of the Malledhrim's passing at the Gostannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dannaswen is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon.

You should bring the Malledhrim weapons you found back to Dannaswen and explain where you discovered them.'It is clear that a great battle was fought at the Gostannon and that the Malledhrim were the clear victors, for the Orc-camp lies in ruin. However, we must learn whether this is the route the Host took eastwards, for if it is, then it would likely be the safest route for any reinforcements that may follow.

'Travel to the Gostannon and seek any signs you may find of the Malledhrim's passing, then return to me with your report. I do not imagine you will encounter much resistance from the Orcs there...they appear to be in disarray after their loss.''The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}; when you have finished your patrol, return to me.''You found these weapons throughout the area and even on the eastern side of the Gostannon? Then the Malledhrim did indeed take that route. This, then, shall be our road for reinforcements and supplies.'You have weakened the Orcs of Ashúrz Maufulug by disarming their traps, leaving them vulnerable to attack.Morsharpat is at Ashúrz Maufulug, south and a little west from Echad Glamodúd.

Glamodúd has asked you to defeat Morsharpat, the captain of the Orcs at Ashúrz Maufulug.Defeat Morsharpat at Ashúrz MaufulugGlamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, north and a little east from Ashúrz Maufulug.

You should return to Glamodúd with news of your victory against Morsharpat.Talk to Glamodúd at Echad Glamodúd'You have done well to weaken the Orcs so. There is but one vital task left for you to do, ${PLAYER}: sever their sword-arm.

'Deep within Ashúrz Maufulug, you will find their captain, whom we have learned is called Morsharpat. He is a vicious creature of great skill in arms. Slay him, and the Orcs will be easy prey.

'When you have accomplished this task, return to me, and I will reward you as best I may.''You have defeated Morsharpat? Then victory is nearly ours! You have earned this reward, ${PLAYER}.''Morsharpat still lives? Until he is defeated, the Orcs of Ashúrz Maufulug will remain a threat to us.'The Elves of the Golden Host have discovered that the Orcs of Dol Guldur have established an encampment at Ashúrz Maufulug, within striking distance of Echad Sirion.Orc-traps might be found anywhere between Echad Glamodúd and Ashúrz Maufulug, to the south and a little west.

Glamodúd has asked you to find and disarm any traps the Orcs may have placed in the Mirk-eaves.Find an Orc-trapOrc-traps might be found anywhere between Echad Glamodúd and Ashúrz Maufulug, to the south-west.

Glamodúd has asked you to find and disarm any traps the Orcs may have placed in the Mirk-eaves. Now that you have seen one of the Orc-traps, the rest should be much easier to find.Disarm Orc-traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, north-east of Ashúrz Maufulug.

You have disarmed many of the Orcs' traps and should now return to Glamodúd with your report.Talk to Glamodúd at Echad  Glamodúd'The Orcs of Dol Guldur have established a camp at Ashúrz Maufulug, not far to the south-west from here. Unfortunately, we learned that there is also a kennel of Wargs located to the south of here. Goldínwen will have more knowledge of that camp, as she is the one who discovered it.

'When I tried to get closer to Ashúrz Maufulug, I nearly set off a trap set by the Orcs. I found no others, which I thought strange, until I realized that they were perhaps spread out to discourage larger forces from moving against them.

'If you would, search the fields between here and Ashúrz Maufulug and see if you can find any more traps. Disarm any that you find -- eventually we will want to attack the camp directly -- then return to me.''The traps are disarmed? Very well done, ${PLAYER}!

'Do not go far...I have another task for you.''You must disarm those traps...we cannot defeat the Orcs of Ashúrz Maufulug while they remain.'The clansmen of the Uch-lûth have many outlying farmsteads, though they have come under attack by invaders from the South.Discover the Cartrevs of Enedwaith.Discover Cartrev DuvedDiscover Cartrev EmlunDiscover Cartrev RurithDiscover Cartrev MathoDiscover Cartrev HamonThe Malledhrim of Echad Sirion have discovered the location of yet another enemy encampment.Mothelen is at Echad Mothelen, far to the north-east from Amon Angened.

Dannaswen has suggested you speak with Mothelen regarding the recently discovered enemy encampment in the western Dourstocks.Talk to Mothelen at Echad Mothelen'${PLAYER}, I have received word from Falasgon at Echad Sirion: the second enemy encampment has been discovered. It appears, though, that this encampment is not nearly the threat that Ashúrz Maufulug had been.

'You should travel to Echad Mothelen, far to the north-east from here, in the western part of the Dourstocks, and speak with the patrol captain, Mothelen. He will be able to tell you more.''Welcome, ${PLAYER}, though I wish it were less disturbing circumstances. Something queer is afoot in this place, and we need your help learning exactly what that is.''Hurry to Echad Mothelen, ${PLAYER}. Mothelen has need of your assistance.'The presence of goblin-spies in the Mirk-eaves also infers the presence of multiple enemy encampments somewhere in the vicinity of the Mirk-eaves.Dannaswen is at Amon Angened, atop Amon Angened to the north, above Echad Mothelen.

Glamodúd has asked you to speak with Dannaswen regarding the Orc-camp near the Gostannon in the north.Talk to Dannaswen atop Amon Angened'${PLAYER}, while you were out about your tasks, Falasgon sent word that another enemy encampment has been discovered near the Gostannon. You should speak at once with Dannaswen in our way-post atop Amon Angened above us to the north.''Speak with Dannaswen at once, ${PLAYER}! She is at our way-post atop Amon Angened above us.''Yes, ${PLAYER}, it is true... another Orc-camp has been discovered. I fear we have our work cut out for us.'The Elves of the Golden Host are concerned with the continuing presence of Orcs in the Mirk-eaves and in procuring supplies for the Malledhrim in the east.The pile of stones is atop a small rise in the Orc-camp at the Gostannon, north-east of Amon Angeled.

Dannaswen has asked you to plant the banner of the Malledhrim at the Orc-camp near the Gostannon and defend it against the Orcs.The Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angened.

Dannaswen asked you to defend the banner you planted in the enemy encampment at the Gostannon.Defend the banner of the Malledhrim<rgb=#FF0000>Do not fall before the Enemy</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the banner undefended</rgb>Dannaswen is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon.

You should return to Dasswen with news of your victory.Talk to Dannaswen atop Amon Angened'${PLAYER}, it would behoove us to be certain that the Orcs at the Gostannon do not regain their courage and inconvenience our forces moving through the area. To that end, I have a task for you.

'Take this banner and plant it upon a prominent place within the ruins of the Orcs' encampment. This will likely enrage the Enemy into attacking you, but should you defend the banner for long enough, they will become disheartened, for you will have proven the glory of the Malledhrim.

'Return to me with the tale of your battle. I will be very pleased to know whether you have succeeded or not. Do not leave the banner unattended, or I will consider your task a failure. Defend it!''You have earned great honour in the eyes of the Malledhrim and of all the Galadhrim.

'I fear, however, that this may not be the last time we will need to make such a show of strength.''Remember: once you have planted our banner, do not leave it undefended until the required time has passed, or I will consider your task a failure!''Remember: once you have planted our banner, do not leave it undefended until the required time has passed, or I will consider your task a failure!'The Elves of the Golden Host are concerned with the continuing presence of Orcs in the Mirk-eaves and in procuring supplies for the Malledhrim in the east.The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.

Rongal has asked you to utterly destroy the Enemy at the Gostannon.Defeat enemies at the Gostannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rongal is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon.

While the Enemy encamped at the Gostannon is greatly weakened, they are still stronger than Rongal surmised. You should return to Rongal with the tidings.Talk to Rongal atop Amon Angened'${PLAYER}, if you are journeying again to the Gostannon, you may be able to effect a greater victory against the Enemy than merely frightening them as Dannaswen would have you do.

'I suggest you enter the camp and wipe the last vestiges of the Enemy from the Gostannon. Our passage would then be assured for the duration of this expedition.

'Return to me when you have completed your task.''It seems that I was hasty in my judgement, ${PLAYER}. It will take more than a single assault to drive the Orcs out for good.''The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}. The Enemy encamped there is not strong...I believe you could destroy them all in one assault.'The Stoors of Maur Tulhau pride themselves as farmers, using only the finest boar-droppings as fertilizer and marigolds around their gardens to ward off pesky animals.Complete Miraculous Growth -- RepeatableComplete Miraculous Growth -- RepeatableBraigiar has asked you to forge ahead to find Saeradan's encampment in the Windfells to the south. The southern Dunlendings are reported to have a large watchtower and encampment in this region, watching the Great North Road for unwanted intrusion from the direction of Bree or the Shire.Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells, south of Echad Dagoras.

Braigiar instructed you to find Saeradan and lend him your aid.Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan'We have sent many scouts ahead to determine the safest and most secret path through Enedwaith. There is rumour of a large ruined watchtower where Saruman's Dunlending minions have established a vigil.

'One band of scouts is led by Saeradan, who went south to determine the strength of the enemy there. By now they should be in the midst of the Windfells. When you are done here, seek him out and offer him what aid you can, for we must ensure that as many of the Grey Company arrive safely in Rohan as possible if we are to be of aid to Aragorn when the time for battle comes.''By now, Saeradan has likely made camp in the Windfells to the south.''Braigiar sent you, has he? I hope Dagoras and his party are finally on the move, for we have much ground to cover and little time before us.'The Elves of the Golden Host seek a way to cripple the Orcs of Durbúrz-stazg.The eastern gate of Durbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion.

Tethafnel has asked you to defeat the Olog-hai warrior Skûm at Durbúrz-stazg. You will need to enter the encampment through the eastern gate.Defeat Skûm at Durbúrz-stazgEchad Sirion lies to the south of Durbúrz-stazg.

You should return to Tethafnel with news of your victory against the olog-hai Skûm.Talk to Tethafnel at Echad Sirion'Greetings again, ${PLAYER}. So the Orcs of Durbúrz-stazg have one of the strange trolls that have been seen by our forces in the east? Olog-hai, I believe they are called.

'These creatures are of a fearsome sort, invulnerable to the effects of sunlight. I need you to find this creature they name Skûm and defeat him. Alas, I have no words of advice for you...I have never faced a creature such as this, for it is no ordinary troll.

'Skûm, from what you tell me, still roams among the Orcs of Durbúrz-stazg to the north. Be careful to enter the encampment through the eastern gate.''The death of this creature will be a mighty blow to the heart of the Enemy. You have our gratitude, ${PLAYER}, Skûm-slayer.''Skûm is a troll of a different kind...olog-hai, I believe they are called. He must not be allowed to remain in Durbúrz-stazg.'Unlike the local clansmen, the Dunlendings sent north by Saruman seem to wear a form of livery, denoting their service to Isengard.Dunlending deserters can be found throughout Fordirith, but especially at Lhe Lhechu, south-west of Echad Dagoras.

Gather uniforms from the band of Dunlending deserters in Fordirith.Collect deserters' helms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect deserters' baldrics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect deserters' leggings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect deserters' boots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagoras is at Echad Dagoras, north-east of Lhe Lhechu.

You should bring the uniforms you collected to Dagoras.'Many Dunlendings were sent up from the southern regions to fight in Eregion and claim the Ring-forges. It seems that Saruman is seeking something there, though I know not what. Their battle against the Elves has not gone to their liking, however, and some of them have fled here to hide as deserters. These southern Dunlendings are not loved by the people of Nan Laeglin, and they survive here now as little more than brigands in the wild.

'The livery that some still wear may be of some use to us, however. It is difficult for Men of the North to pass as Dunlendings -- doubly so for we of Dúnadan descent -- but were we to don the livery of Saruman's army and skirt away from habitation, few would look closely enough to discern us, and we might pass through the South unmolested.

'If you can manage to scrounge some uniforms for us -- preferably not torn to shreds or bathed in blood, mind you -- it may help us slip a few of our number through into southern Dunland to scout ahead for the rest.''Bring me the livery of the Dunlending deserters, ${PLAYER}...it may be of some use to us.''Yes, a few bloodstains here and there, but nothing too apparent.

'These should do nicely in the event we are forced to mingle closely with the Dunlendings or pass close to any encampments.'Defeat wolves and Shadow-wolves in Enedwaith.Defeat wolves and Shadow-wolves in EnedwaithDefeat many wolves and Shadow-wolves in Enedwaith.Defeat wolves and Shadow-wolves in EnedwaithMany dark and vile creatures dwell beneath the eaves of southern Mirkwood. Among these are terrible bats...some of which are creatures of an ancient age.Bats may be found throughout the Dourstocks. Carcharan may be found in a cave at Gorotham, north-east from Echad Mothelen, beyond Burgûl-stazg.

Lavanferon has asked you to recover his lost satchel and to defeat the bats of Mirkwood, including the vampire, Carcharan.Defeat Carcharan at GorothamDefeat bats in the Dourstocks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect the stolen satchelLavanferon is at Echad Mothelen, south-west from Gorotham, beyond Burgûl-stazg.

You should return the satchel to Lavanferon with news of your victory against Carcharan.'Alas, ${PLAYER}, I have proven a coward when I should show no fear. When I was scouting for the location of Burgûl-stazg, I was swarmed by bats. These vile creatures were not the cause of my fear, however; among them was a great creature that emanated terror. I have no doubt that it was a vampire, such as those which once dwelt in the lands ages past.

'In my terror, I dropped my satchel. It contains many items which may be of use to the Enemy and must be retrieved, but I cannot face that creature again. I ask you to face Carcharan and recover my satchel.

'Carcharan inhabits a cave in Gorotham to the north-east of here, beyond Burgûl-stazg. While you are about this task, please slay as many of those vile bats as you can.''I am sure the creature that I confronted was no mere mortal...I am sure it was a vampire of Morgoth.''Ah! You have destroyed Carcharan and recovered my satchel? That is well.

'You greatly deserve this reward!'Fernachar noted the movements of a truly terrifying spider seen roaming in the Dourstocks, bearing a great Orc unconscious to her den.The Dourstocks Lair-spinner can be found in the Dreadweaver's Lair.

You should go to the spider-lair and face the Lair-spinner.Summon and defeat the Dourstocks Lair-spinnerFernachar is in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should return to Fernachar with word of your triumph against the Dourstocks Lair-spinner.Talk to Fernachar at the Haunted Inn'You have done well indeed, but you will not believe what report I have heard. One of our scouts returned and said he saw a deadly-looking spider bearing a great burden -- an Orc that was unconscious from poison.

'This spider carried her prey in the direction of the Dreadweaver's Lair, south-west from here. Will you pursue her there? I fear for our safety with such a monster roaming about, though I'll not hold her choice of food against her.

'If you can rid the Dreadweaver's Lair of this menace, I do believe we will have secured the Dourstocks against the greater threat of spiders, ${PLAYER}.''Very good! The spider threat is greatly lessened now, thanks to you, ${PLAYER}. The Malledhrim owe you much.''The Dreadweaver's Lair is to the south-west of here. That is the direction in which I saw this great predator dragging away her enormous prey. Such a foe cannot be allowed to endure.Violed Isbrun is a good friend of Maur Tulhau's most respected farmer, Iago Glennudh. She is well-known for her knowledge of ways to protect gardens from pests.Marigolds can be found throughout the Gloomglens.

Violed Isbrun has asked you to gather marigolds for her. She uses the flowers to defend her garden against small pests.Collect marigolds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Violed Isbrun's garden is in Maur Tulhau.

You should bring the marigolds you collected back to Violed's garden and plant them.Violed Isbrun is in Maur Tulhau.

You should speak with Violed Isbrun again and let her know that you have done as she asked.Talk to Violed Isbrun at Maur Tulhau'So, Duvodiad, ye are the giant which Rhus has befriended? I'm not so sure I trust ye. Do ye honour the art of gardening? If ye do, then we may be friends ourselves.

'My mothers from many generations have passed down a secret for protecting gardens from the small pests who like to defile them: marigolds. Aye, ye heard aright. Marigolds. Pests can't stand the smell of them.

'Go out and gather me some marigolds, if you would...I need some to plant around my garden. For that matter, ye could do with some honest labour: you can plant them here, as well.''I'm not sure what causes the vermin to avoid marigolds, but I am supposing it's the smell.''I'm not sure what causes the vermin to avoid marigolds, but I am supposing it's the smell.''Mercy me! It looks like ye knows something about gardening yourself! Well, I should say I'm impressed!'Rhus Cornchúthur believes you to be a giant come down from the Misty Mountains, though he is far from impressed by your stature.Gavar-diavol can be found at night in a gully south of Rhus Cornchúthur.

Rhus Cornchúthur suggested you rid the Gloomglens of the Druggavar called Gavar-diavol. Doing so may go a long way to building a friendship with the hobbits of Enedwaith.Defeat Gavar-diavol at nightRhus Cornchúthur awaits your return to the west of Gavar-diavol's haunting grounds.

You should return to Rhus Cornchúthur with news of your victory.Talk to Rhus Cornchúthur in the Gloomglens'A giant! Fearsome tales have we of your kind! What do ye want of me? Are ye going to eat me? Though to be truthful, I would have expected a beast of greater stature....

'Now what is that ye say? No giant are you, but a Man? Some of our elders swear they've met Man-creatures before, but I can't say that I have. Why should we deal with the likes of ye?

'Well, if ye want to speak with Maer Brochtû, you'll need to do something for us. To the east of here is a small gully where our hunters found a strange shrine...perhaps made by one of ye big Men. At night, the hunters claim to have seen a terrible goat-demon, which we call Gavar-diavol...defeat the creature, and we may have more to say to ye.''Defeat Gavar-diavol, and I must consider trusting you....''Most amazing, tall one! Maer Brochtû will surely wish to speak with you now!

'As well, accept this gift of gratitude...you may find it useful in the future.'You found a crushed boulder amid the bluffs of the Gloomglens. It looks to have been thrown to the ground and broken.There are Rangers at Echad Idhrenfair to the east of the boulder.

You should bring news of the crushed boulder and skeleton to the Rangers of the Grey Company, for it may portend a greater foe than you have previously encountered.Talk to a Ranger at Echad IdhrenfairThis boulder seems strangely out of place here. It appears to have been thrown down and broken...and judging from the skeleton beneath it, it was not an accident.

You should bring this discovery to the attention of the Rangers of the Grey Company.'The boulder was thrown down you say? But from where? The place you describe is far from any height from which such a stone could be thrown down and broken.

'I fear you may be right. It appears there may be a greater threat in these hills.'The Hobbits of Maur Tulhau believe there is a nearby village of hobbits turned wild from years of separation from their kin. Iolo Brochtû is interested in making peace with them.The neighbouring village lies to the south of Maur Tulhau.

Iolo Brochtû has asked you to deliver the peace offering to the hobbits of the neighbouring village.Deliver the peace offering to the hobbits of the neighbouring villageThe 'hobbit'-village south of Maur Tulhau is inhabited by a strange variety of wild goblin.

You should do your best to remove the threat of the goblins.Defeat goblins at Khoblún Utot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iolo Brochtû is at Maur Tulhau, north of Khoblún Utot.

You should return to Iolo Brochtû with news of your discovery at Khoblún Utot.Talk to Iolo Brochtû at Maur Tulhau'So, you've been a great help to my folk, so perhaps you will aid with another task. A while back, our hunters discovered a village of hobbits to the south-east of here. They've gone wild -- I suppose from too many years apart from us civilized folk.

'We thought to send a peace offering to them, as they've been none too friendly to us when we've come across them in the forest, but Gwin Cuthonon went missing. Perhaps you would take this peace offering to the village?

'Perhaps they've gone too wild, but we should try nonetheless, as we're neighbours.''What say ye? Those are no hobbits at all? What ye describe sounds like bugan to me! We've had trouble with them in the past, or so our old tales say....''Have you delivered that offering yet, Duvodiad?''Have you delivered that offering yet, Duvodiad?'The Rangers of the Grey Company seek to acquire the good will of the Uch-lûth, the Dunlending clan inhabiting Enedwaith.Beehives, goat's rue, klamath weed, mistletoe, and sweet myrtle can be found throughout the Windfells. Look on trees for mistletoe and bee-hives. 

Saeradan has asked you to collect several herbs and bring them to him to be prepared for delivery to the Uch-lûth.Collect goat's rue flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect klamath weed flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect mistletoe (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect royal jelly (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect sweet myrtle roots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should bring the herbs you foraged to Saeradan.'As I mentioned before, ${PLAYER}, our stores run low, and we must seek the good will of the Algraig to replenish them.

'Herbs for medicines will benefit both us and the Algraig...will you forage some up for me? Search on trees for beehives...within, you may find the royal jelly the bees produce. This can be used to treat many illnesses. You should also seek out goat's rue...it can be used to treat ailments of the liver and to combat fever. Klamath weed fights many diseases. Mistletoe, which grows on tree-branches, may be used to treat cancers and strengthen the heart. Sweet myrtle has a property to relax the ill.

'When you have found everything we need, bring them to me.''You may find the herbs we require throughout the Windfells...beehives will be found near trees, though, to be certain.''Ah! The herbs I asked you to forage. These will aid us upon our journey and perhaps help to earn the good will of the Algraig.'Andreg regrets his decision to have you hunt the dun oxen of the Windfells from which the Uch-lûth draw their herds.The oxherds of the Uch-lûth are encamped at Uch Cadlus, south-east of Echad Saeradan.

Andreg has asked you to deliver the ox-meat you collected to the oxherds of the Uch-lûth.'${PLAYER}, I must confess that my heart is heavy. Our actions may hurt the herdsmen of the Uch-lûth, for the oxen we have slain are the same from which they draw their own herds.

'I must ask you then to take this meat you collected to the Uch-lûth oxherds who have encamped far to the south-east near the northern end of the bridge which leads into Nan Laeglin. Present them this gift with our apologies and promise them that we will hunt no more.

'Perhaps they will agree to trade with us, if you can make them understand that our apology is sincere.'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you accept this quest, you will not be able to accept the quest Feeding the Company -- Repeatable.</rgb>'Have you brought our gift to the Uch-lûth yet, ${PLAYER}?''What is this? So you are responsible for this slaughter? Why should we accept the apology of your wandering friends after this?'Pleased with your assistance protecting their herds, the oxherds of the Uch-lûth have agreed to trade provisions to the Grey Company.Andreg is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith, north-west of Uch Cadlus.

Wunne has asked you to deliver a package of meat to the Grey Company.Wunne is at Uch Cadlus in the Windfells, south-east of Echad Saeradan.

Andreg instructed you to return to Wunne and offer her your services should she need them again.Talk to Wunne at Uch Cadlus'We cannot deny that your help has secured the health and safety of our people. We will then grant you your wish: we will trade meat to the other duvodiad.

'Take this first package to your friends with our gratitude.''Your friends offer your arm quite freely, do they not? Perhaps they are not so much your friends as you think.

'Nevertheless, I will not refuse a strong arm to protect our herds.''Return to Wunne and offer her your services.''You will take that meat to your wandering friends, yes?''You turned the hearts of the oxherds? Then I am in your debt, ${PLAYER}. These provisions will be a boon to us.

'Return to Mistress Wunne and offer her your services should she need them again...we have little else to trade.'Saeradan fears that the road south into Dunland may be watched too closely, forcing the Rangers of the Grey Company to seek a safer route to Rohan.Idhrenfair is at Echad Idhrenfair in the Gloomglens, north and west of Echad Saeradan.

Saeradan has suggested you might help Idhrenfair seek a more secret path southwards.Talk to Idhrenfair at Echad Idhrenfair'${PLAYER}, I fear the road below may be watched too closely for our company to move as secretly as our purpose requires. To this end, I have sent some of my kindred west into the Gloomglens to seek a less travelled path into the south.

'We need your aid here, but when all is ready, you should head to Echad Idhrenfair in the Gloomglens and speak with Idhrenfair himself. I am certain he could use your help scouting the way.''Welcome, ${PLAYER}. Saeradan sent you to aid us? That is well, for these myriad gorges are a mystery to be unravelled. Your aid will be greatly appreciated.''Echad Idhrenfair lies to the west in the Gloomglens.'You wandered across a strange and suspicious hobbit in the wilds of the Gloomglens... a long-lost Stoorish brother, no doubt.Expert pipe-weed seeds can be purchased in the Shire.

Rhus Cornchúthur has suggested that bringing him something of importance related to pipe-weed might earn you the trust of the Stoors of Enedwaith. Perhaps a supply of pipe-weed seeds from the Shire will appease him.Collect expert pipe-weed seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhus Cornchúthur is outside Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith.

You should bring the Longbottom Leaf seeds to Rhus Cornchúthur.'Well now, you're dressed mighty queer for one of our folk, and I've never seen you before. Your speech is strange too.

'Where did you say you were from? The Shire? Never heard of it! Well now, you won't get far with my folk unless you can prove yourself trustworthy... we're not keen on duvodiad -- strangers -- around here.

'Perhaps if you bring something of importance from your kindred in that Shire-place, our mayor might give you a fair hearing.''Ye will need to prove yourself worthy of our trust... our folk have been too long estranged.''What is this? You call it pipe-weed? What do you do with it? Smoke it? This is something I must see!

'For this gift, receive this in return... you may find it useful one day soon.'Idhrenfair, a Ranger who travels with the Malledhrim, shows more curiosity than the Elves for what has come to pass in the abandoned town. The shades that stir here are strange, and Idhrenfair would like to know the history of Audaghaim.The graveyard of Audaghaim can be found south of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

Idhrenfair has asked you to search for any clues as to the history of Audaghaim in the town's graveyard.Read the first grave-stoneThe graveyard of Audaghaim can be found south of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

Idhrenfair has asked you to search for any clues as to the history of Audaghaim in the town's graveyard.Read the second grave-stoneThe graveyard of Audaghaim can be found south of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

Idhrenfair has asked you to search for any clues as to the history of Audaghaim in the town's graveyard.Read the third grave-stoneThe graveyard of Audaghaim can be found south of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

Idhrenfair has asked you to search for any clues as to the history of Audaghaim in the town's graveyard.Read the fourth grave-stoneThe graveyard of Audaghaim can be found south of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

Idhrenfair has asked you to search for any clues as to the history of Audaghaim in the town's graveyard.Read the fifth grave-stoneThe Haunted Inn can be found north of the graveyard of Audaghaim in the Dourstocks.

You should return to Idhrenfair with your discoveries.Talk to Idhrenfair at the Haunted Inn'Hail, ${PLAYER}. I have heard much of your deeds from my people and from the good Elves with whom I travel. I bid you welcome to our encampment. You may rest here from the darkness, for the Galadhrim keep it at bay.

'This is a strange place we have landed in; the shades here are troubled. If the Necromancer had ruined this place, I do not think it would feel so disturbing. Nay, some other factor played a role in the collapse of this village. The curiosity of the Elves, however, is not raised by mortal affairs, and I am here to aid them. I cannot peer into the matter as I would wish, however.

'You are not bound to the Golden Host, ${CLASS}. Will you find out what has come to pass in this strange and troubled town? The shades stir as if roused, but they do not behave as most Oathbreakers do. I believe there is some grim history here that has been overlooked by every tale. There is a graveyard yonder -- perhaps you should begin your search there.''Here lieth Fritigern, age 31, who perished from Natural Causes on July 2, TA 2461.''Here lieth Hachulf, age 19, who perished from illness on June 30, TA 2461.''Here lieth Beremud, age 41, who took his own life on July 4, TA 2461.''Here lieth Vatigas, age 27, who fell to his death on July 1, TA 2461.''Peculiar. It sounds as though all those who were buried around the same time died of different causes. Why would this place be haunted by Oathbreakers if the deaths were things like sickness and natural causes? And the blank gravestone does not make sense at all.

'The ages, too, give me doubt. These were young folk. The deaths were so close to one another. Something is amiss. I wonder if there are more clues about the town....''There is a graveyard to the south of here; perhaps you should begin your search there.'The goblin-deserters roaming the Dourstocks indicated that something their leaders were up to in Burgûl-stazg was the cause of their desertion.Burgûl-stazg lies to the north-west of Echad Mothelen.

Mothelen has asked you gather information from nervous goblins at Burgûl-stazg; however, he also warned you to avoid being seen by the guards of the goblin-camp.Uncover the mystery at Burgûl-stazgMothelen is at Echad Mothelen, south-east from Burgûl-stazg.

You should bring the deserter's note to Mothelen with what you have learned.Talk to Mothelen at Echad Mothelen'${PLAYER}, we must learn the root cause of the goblins' fear. Something is taking place at Burgûl-stazg, and it must be stopped, but first we must learn exactly what it is.

'You should go to Burgûl-stazg and see if you can find anything out, but be careful not to be seen by the guards. Detection of your presence may make your quest more difficult. Look for goblins that are especially nervous.

'Return to me when you have learned more.''This note is written in their foul Black Speech, but I know somewhat of it.

'Interesting! The goblins have stolen an idol from the haunted ruins. It is no wonder that they are terrified. I dare not consider the horrors they have unleashed!''${PLAYER}, enter Burgûl-stazg and gather the knowledge we require.'The hobbit Rhus Cornchúthur was surprised by your appearance, believing you to be a legendary creature called a Stone-eater.Enaid-helgi appears at night upon a plateau to the north-east of Rhus Cornchúthur.

Rhus Cornchúthur suggested that the mayor of his people might speak with you if you were to prove yourself to him. Slaying the demon-dog Enaid-helgi would go a long way towards that goal.Defeat Enaid-helgi at nightRhus Cornchúthur awaits your return south-west of Enaid-helgi's hunting ground.

You should return to Rhus Cornchúthur with news of your victory.Talk to Rhus Cornchúthur in the Gloomglens'A Stone-eater! Our Lûth-fathers told how they had seen your kind long ago in the mountains, but I never would have believed it if I didn't see ye now! Stone-eaters have always been a thing of legend to us.

'What? Ye say ye are not a Stone-eater? Ye call yourself a dwarf? I have not heard of the like. No matter... we've naught to do with the likes of ye.

'Well, I won't say we won't have naught to do with ye... if ye can prove your faith with us. Some of our hunters say that have seen an evil Cun Annun howling atop a plateau to the north-east of here at night. Enaid-helgi, we call it. If ye will slay the beast, Maer Brochtû might give ye a fair hearing.''Enaid-helgi is a thing of terror... you should be careful!''You have slain Enaid-helgi? A deed most wondrous! I am sure Maer Brochtû will wish to speak with you now!

'As well, take this gift... you may find it useful when dealing with the dangers in these woods.'The spiders that roam the Dourstocks spill out from the Dreadweaver's Lair, making the forest all the more perilous for the Malledhrim.Spiders can be found throughout the Dourstocks.

You should defeat many spiders to make the Dourstocks safer for the Malledhrim who wish to travel unhindered.Defeat spiders in the Dourstocks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fernachar can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should return to Fernachar with word of your success against the spiders.Talk to Fernachar at the Haunted Inn'You have been sent to aid us and aid us you may, mellon. There are many tasks ahead of us, and our numbers are fewer than we would wish, especially with our scouts missing in the north.

'This forest is rife with poison-fanged spiders, seemingly everywhere one looks. They spout from the Dreadweaver's Lair, south-west from here.

'You should defeat as many Mirkwood spiders as you can, mellon. They are ever a threat to the Elves, and are our enemies of old.''Suillaid, mellon. You have our thanks for your efforts to pave the way for our offensive against Dol Guldur. This forest is still evil, but it is a little less so with every malicious spider that is brought to death.''Spiders can be found everywhere you look, ${PLAYER}. If you have trouble finding them in the woods, you could investigate around the Dreadweaver's Lair, south-west from here.'The hobbit Rhus Cornchúthur was frightened by your appearance, believing you to be one of the evil spirits rumoured to haunt the Gloomglens.Tulwulh-gwirod can be found at night in a ravine amid many high bluffs to the south-east of Rhus Cornchúthur.

Rhus Cornchúthur suggested that you banish the Cuthraul Tulwulh-gwirod to prove that you are not yourself an evil spirit.Defeat Tulwulh-gwirod at nightRhus Cornchúthur awaits your return to the north-west of Tulwulh-gwirod's haunting grounds.

You should return to Rhus Cornchúthur with news of your victory.Talk to Rhus Cornchúthur in the Gloomglens'An evil spirit! I knew it! Please don't hurt me! My own spirit isn't worth eating!

'What? Ye say you're not an evil spirit? What then are ye? An Elf? Goodness! Do legends spring to life?

'If ye want to prove you're not an evil spirit, you're going to have to banish one yourself! In a deep ravine to the south-east, our hunters have seen a Cuthraul which we call Tulwulh-gwirod...banish the fiend, and we might have more to do with ye....''Are you sure you're not an evil spirit?''Well now, if you've done away with Tulwulh-gwirod, I guess ye can't be half bad yourself! Maer Brochtû'll wish to see you I'm sure.

'Here...take this as a gift of gratitude. Ye may find it useful in the future.'Saeradan and several other Rangers have ventured into the Windfells as advance scouts for the Grey Company to help ensure that their purpose remains secret, but also to help provision the Company.Saeradan, Andreg, and Amlan are at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

Saeradan has asked you to aid the Grey Company in their many tasks. He told you that he had a task for you, and that Amlan and Andreg might as well.Complete A Healing HandComplete Warmth for the WinterComplete Feathers for FriendshipSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should speak with Saeradan regarding his plans for the items you collected.Talk to Saeradan at Echad SaeradanThe Algraig goatherds are at Gavar Cadlus, north-east of Echad Saeradan, along the foothills of the Misty Mountains.

Saeradan asked you to deliver the herbs, pelts, and feathers you collected to the Algraig goatherds as a peace offering.'Hail, ${PLAYER}. It has been long since you and I worked together to hinder the efforts of the traitor Saruman in Bree. Chief Watcher Grimbriar still does not comprehend the significance of what we have done.

'But never mind that now... we have other matters to discuss. You know already that we go to the aid of our chieftain Aragorn in the South, but we travel through hostile lands and must secure our route. Besides that, we will need provisions. This will require the good will of the Algraig, the Dunlending clans which have migrated into this region.

'Will you help us? I have a task in mind for you, and I believe Amlan and Andreg may as well.''Complete the tasks you have been set, ${PLAYER}, and I will have more for you to do.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. The Algraig will hopefully find our offering of peace acceptable and grant trade with us through you as our agent.

'Some distance to the north-east, along the foothills of the mountains, we noticed a camp of Algraig goatherds. Take these goods to their leader and present them to him with our request for trade.''Deliver the goods to the Algraig goatherds, ${PLAYER}... I believe they are our best hope for obtaining provisions.''What is this? Who are you? We do not know your kind... you are duvodiad to us! You speak on behalf of some wanderers of the wild? Algraig! That is an insult! Do you speak on behalf of our brothers of old? The clans of Dunland say we are Algraig... Outliers.

'We are no lesser Men than they! You do not speak for the Others? Then perhaps I will forgive the insult, for your wanderers may not know our ways. Tell me what it is you wish of us.'Grufudh of the Uch-lûth has agreed to trade with the Grey Company in exchange for medicines and goods.Grufudh is at Gavar Cadlus, north-east of Echad Saeradan.

Saeradan has asked you to deliver more pelts, feathers, and herbs to Grufudh the goatherd.Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith, south-west of Gavar Cadlus.

Grufudh told you to return to Saeradan with the thanks of his people and assurance that supplies will be sent.Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan'${PLAYER}, I must thank you for your efforts on our behalf. With the agreement of Grufudh, we shall continue to supply his people with pelts, feathers, and herbs in exchange for provisions.

'Will you take this new delivery to Grufudh at Gavar Cadlus? When you have delivered the goods, return to me, and I will reward you as I may.''Take the goods to Grufudh... hopefully, he will prepare more supplies for our Company.''These goods are much welcomed, Duvodiad, though I am still not sure I trust these wild-wanderers.

'Return now to your friend with our thanks. Assure him that we will make good on our promises.''Take our thanks to your wild friends.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Your services have been invaluable.'Many dark and evil things dwell in the southern reaches of Mirkwood, spiders not the least.Spiders may be found throughout the Dourstocks. Laehendiel may be found at the Dreadweaver's Lair, south-east from Echad Mothelen.

Lavanferon has asked you to defeat many spiders and their mistress, Laehendiel.Defeat Laehendiel at the Dreadweaver's LairDefeat spiders in the Dourstocks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lavanferon is at Echad Mothelen, north-west from the Dreadweaver's Lair.

You should return to Lavanferon with tidings of your success.Talk to Lavanferon at Echad Mothelen'If you are willing to aid me, ${PLAYER}, I could use your help. When I was scouting for the location of Burgûl-stazg, I came across a great spider.

'I cannot walk these woods of our kindred of old and not purge it of these creatures. Defeat as many spiders as you may, and their vile mistress Laehendiel. Her lair, I believe is at the Dreadweaver's Lair, south-east from here.

'When you have completed this task, return to me, and I will reward you for your efforts.''I am pleased that you were able to slay that vile spider-queen. You have earned this reward.''Defeat Laehendiel and her brood, ${PLAYER}...they are a threat to the Malledhrim.'Bats lend added protection to the stronghold of the morroval-inhabitants of Dannenglor.Ruins-bats can be found in the ruined Elf-stronghold of Dannenglor, north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

Mírdiniel has asked you to defeat several bats in Dannenglor when you venture next into the wilds of the Dourstocks.Defeat ruins-bats in Dannenglor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mírdiniel is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood, south of Dannenglor.

You should speak with Mírdiniel and tell her of your efforts in dealing with the problem of bat-swarms in the woods.Talk to Mírdiniel at the Haunted Inn'I am glad that you have come to our aid, my good ${RACE}. As our path leads us through Mirkwood, we see many evil things which we wish to make right. Alas that we have not the resources for such a great undertaking. Even the smallest good deeds must often go undone, for our eyes are fixed upon one target only.

'Dannenglor was once an Elven-home and is overrun now by shrieking beasts of all kinds. The merrevail and mervyl are violations of nature, and even the bats of this forest are unwholesome and evil.

'If you wish to make Mirkwood a little better on behalf of the Galadhrim who must pass through it, you should cleanse those ruins of the vile swarms of bats that give strength to the presence of the merrevail. Will you do this for us? Dannenglor will never be fair again, but you can perhaps begin to cast the evil from within its walls.''I am glad to see you well after your venture into Dannenglor...and not a scratch upon you! You have done a considerable kindness to all the Elves of Middle-earth, ${PLAYER}; you have my thanks!''Dannenglor is north of here. I believe you will find many ruins-bats there.'Idhrenfair, unconvinced by the contrary words of the condemned shade, believes that the stones of Audaghaim should not remain unturned any longer and that the town's secret should be revealed if at all possible.Audaghaim lies to the east of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should search Audaghaim carefully for any telling scenes that may have lain hidden during your previous hasty observations of the town.Search for evidence of violenceSearch for old weaponsSearch for a sign of the Necromancer's influenceThe Ranger Idhrenfair is in the Haunted Inn, west of Audaghaim.

You should return to Idhrenfair and tell him of all you have seen.Talk to Idhrenfair at the Haunted Inn'So, we are armed at least with the knowledge that there is a mystery. The shade's words were very contrary to the stark reality to which we bear witness today.

'There is much evidence that these accursed folk became tied to the Dark Lord in the second year of his sojourn at Dol Guldur, but we must now look deeper. We have given the shades a chance to tell their own story, but it seems that they wish the truth hidden from us.

'You should search everything but the shades themselves when you go to Audaghaim this time. Seek some evidence of the Necromancer's influence and search for any signs of violence...or perhaps a stockpile of weapons. If you can find these things, we will gain more understanding of the events that occurred here.''Are you still prying, young ${CLASS}? Get away from here! I warn you -- do not disturb the peace of our fair village.''Continue your search in Audaghaim, ${PLAYER}. I feel certain that we will learn something, even if it takes some prying.

'I would like you to seek evidence of the Necromancer's influence, evidence of violence, or evidence of violent intent.''Ah...I think I see. How sad! But I suspected it would be something of this nature. There was murder in this town...of that you have seen strong evidence.

'Here is what I think the condemned shade meant when he said that many of his folk were set in their ways, and that change was coming: The change was the Dark Lord, and some Men resisted.

'I believe the shades trapped here have done their best to pretend the evil events never happened, though it means their redemption will never be achieved. Even the gravestones lie. These shades believe that all is as it was just before the Necromancer corrupted them. The murders are buried, collectively hidden. All were guilty, and all are determined to deny the truth.'The appearance of the shades at Burgûl-stazg disturbed the Elf Mothelen, foreshadowing a more dire evil.Prestadír is at the Haunted Inn, east from Echad Mothelen.

Mothelen suggested you speak with Prestadír to learn more about the shades of the Dourstocks.Talk to Prestadír at the Haunted Inn'${PLAYER}, I fear something dire is about to occur. The shadow of the Necromancer lies still upon Mirkwood. I know little more of these forsaken shades, but perhaps you may learn more if you speak with Prestadír at the Haunted Inn.

'The Haunted Inn lies to the east of here, deeper into the Dourstocks.''${PLAYER}, you have come to me at a fortuitous time. Something is amiss here. The shades of dead Men roam these lands. Of what broken oaths could have cursed them here, I am not yet sure....''${PLAYER}, you must journey to the Haunted Inn and speak with the Ranger Prestadír. I am certain he could use your assistance.'The Hidden Guard is in disarray following the death of Raddir, and Cúcheron has decided that you should aid the Golden Host while they decide what to do next.Dúndurion is at Audaghaim, outside the Haunted Inn, overlooking the view from the cliffs.

Cúcheron has decided to send you to Dúndurion to aid the Golden Host with their military matters while the Hidden Guard decides on a course of action.Talk to Dúndurion at AudaghaimThe ruins of Dannenglor are the location for a planned strike by Dúndurion.

Dúndurion has asked you to participate in the strike against the merrevail-occupied ruins of Dannenglor.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, Fellowship, or Raid group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 60.</rgb>Complete Skirmish: Strike Against DannenglorDúndurion is at Audaghaim, outside the Haunted Inn, overlooking the view from the cliffs.

You have participated in the successful strike against Dannenglor and should return now to Dúndurion.Talk to Dúndurion at AudaghaimCúcheron is on the front porch of the Haunted Inn, at Audaghaim.

Dúndurion has sent you back to Cúcheron. Perhaps the Hidden Guard have decided what course to take on the next leg of their journey.Talk to Cúcheron outside the Haunted Inn'We must persevere, ${PLAYER}, though we grieve for Raddir. The road he planned to take is unknown to us, but his mind is not: I know he would be wroth if we were to abandon hope.

'But we need time to decide what to do. Instead of dwelling upon our losses, I want you to offer your strength to Dúndurion here in Audaghaim. He has planned a number of strikes against important locations in Mirkwood, and the Golden Host could use your honed skills as a ${CLASS}.

'Aid Dúndurion with whatever skirmish he has planned, then return to me. By the Lord and Lady, I hope we will have decided what next to do with Mazog. We cannot stay here long without the Enemy learning of the Orc-leader's presence.''The Hidden Guard needs to decide upon a course of action. While we try and recover from the loss of Raddir, I believe the Golden Host will best be served by your abilities.

'Speak with Dúndurion here in Audaghaim. He is planning a strike against some location here in Mirkwood, and you will be of the greatest value fighting alongside the Golden Host instead of waiting here while the Hidden Guard decides what to do.''Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. I have been charged by the Lord and Lady with maintaining control over locations in the western areas of this region. We have had nothing but success thus far...By Elbereth, may it continue!

'My Elves prepare for another skirmish: a strike against the ruins of Dannenglor, populated by filthy merrevail. If you are as skilled a ${CLASS} as Cúcheron has led me to believe, you will be most welcome to join us in this skirmish. Doubly so if you command the loyalty of a skilled soldier!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, Fellowship, or Raid group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 60.

Before launching the Skirmish, you should visit one of the Skirmish Camps found throughout Middle-earth and speak with a Skirmish Captain to properly train. Skirmish Camps can be found in the following regions: Ered Luin, Bree-land, the Shire, the Lone-lands, the North Downs, the Trollshaws, Evendim, Forochel, Angmar, Eregion, Moria, and Lothlórien.</rgb>'My Elves prepare for another skirmish: a strike against the ruins of Dannenglor, populated by filthy merrevail. If you are as skilled a ${CLASS} as Cúcheron has led me to believe, you will be most welcome to join us in this skirmish. Doubly so if you command the loyalty of a skilled soldier!

'Return to me in victory, ${PLAYER}, after participating in the strike against Dannenglor.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, Fellowship, or Raid group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 60.</rgb>'Well done, ${PLAYER}. Dannenglor is ours, and it is to be hoped the merrevail will not return.

'Go now to Cúcheron on the porch of the Haunted Inn here at Audaghaim and give him my thanks. I am pleased that he sent such a skilled ${CLASS} to us, and Dannenglor is proof of your worth to the Golden Host.''Go now to Cúcheron on the porch of the Haunted Inn here at Audaghaim and give him my thanks. I am pleased he sent such a skilled ${CLASS} to us, and Dannenglor is proof of your worth to the Golden Host.''I have heard already of your victory at Dannenglor, ${PLAYER}. Would that I could give you such pleasing news of the Hidden Guard, but our situation is little changed. Issuriel has spent the hours poring over what few maps we possess of this region of Mirkwood, but still she has not decided on a safe and secret route to Dol Guldur.

'We have another concern now, as well. A Greyhammer concern.'Cúcheron has given you the unfortunate news that the Hidden Guard's mission remains stalled and that the Greyhammer dwarves have caused another delay.Otri Greyhammer is inside the Haunted Inn.

Cúcheron told you to speak with Otri Greyhammer about some problem that has plagued the dwarves.Talk to Otri Greyhammer in the Haunted InnRósar and Stígur Greyhammer are lost somewhere within the fens of the Drownholt, south of the Dourstocks.

Otri Greyhammer is desperate for you to find his brothers, lost within the marshes of the Drownholt.Find Rósar Greyhammer and ensure his safetyFind Stígur Greyhammer and ensure his safetyOtri Greyhammer is by the fireplace in the Haunted Inn, among the Dourstocks.

You have broken the Greyhammer brothers from their reveries and should return now to Otri.Talk to Otri Greyhammer in the Haunted InnBróin is in the cellar of the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks.

Otri has asked you to tell Bróin that his brothers are safe and to see if the Hidden Guard has yet decided on a route.Talk to Bróin in the cellar of the Haunted Inn'I worried that the Greyhammers would become a problem, ${PLAYER}, but what could I say about it? Nothing, and now they have gotten themselves -- and us as well -- into trouble!

'Otri Greyhammer can tell you more. I saw him last inside the Haunted Inn, raging at the hearth there to anyone who would listen.''Otri Greyhammer is inside the Haunted Inn, ${PLAYER}. See to his problem before it grows worse, as I fear it surely will. Have we not already suffered enough setbacks without the troubles of these brash dwarves?''${PLAYER}, will you help me? You had better, for that is why you're a part of this foolish endeavour, is it not? I would not speak ill of the plans of Bósi and Brogur, but Bróin has not had the experience of his uncle or his father, has he? Nor that of the Greyhammers, truth be told!

'Now two of my brothers have gone missing in the swamp, and if the Elves know the difference between treacherous ground and solid footing, they have taken care not to tell us which is which!

'Find Rósar and Stígur Greyhammer, somewhere among the fens of the Drownholt, ${PLAYER}, and find them quickly. There are watery terrors in that place, and no self-respecting dwarf would be pleased to be stuck in such a vile marsh with the only help to be had these Lórien Elves!''My brothers went into the fens of the Drownholt, south of the Dourstocks, and never returned. It is said there are watery terrors within the marshes of the Drownholt, and I believe it! Rumour has it an Elf was lost to one of these!

'If some evil has seized hold of my brothers, I must know about it so I can add its name to the list of Greyhammer foes!'As you stare into the glassy eyes of the dwarf, you come to know that this is not Rósar Greyhammer at all, but an image conjured out of the evils of the marsh. Do not let it lead you astray!As you stare into the glassy eyes of the dwarf, you come to know that this is not Stígur Greyhammer at all, but an image conjured out of the evils of the marsh. Do not let it lead you astray!'Rósar and Stígur were just here, ${PLAYER}, and they had the strangest stories to tell. Each of them reported seeing familiar faces among the tangled bushes and briars and hearing voices on the wind, but when they approached, filled with amazement to see lost friends in such a place, there was no sign of anyone. But lo, further ahead...an encouraging wave and a smile!

'This place fills me with unease, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for rescuing my brothers. Without your aid, I fear there would have been two fewer Greyhammers in this world come sundown, if sundown ever truly leaves this grim wood.

'Bróin is in the cellar. Tell him my brothers are safe and ask him, too, if the Elves have come to an agreement on how to proceed. The sooner we move on from this place, the happier this Greyhammer will be!''Bróin is in the cellar of this inn, ${PLAYER}. Tell him my brothers are safe and ask him, too, if we are ready yet to move on. I hope we are, for this wood is no place for dwarves!''Hello again, ${PLAYER}. This waiting has already begun to wear thin, and my patience was stretched to begin with! The Elves have not yet decided which way to go. Perhaps you can help them decide, if anyone can.'You found a black collar marked with evil-looking runes upon the corpse of one of the Druggavar you slew.Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan, south-west of Gavar Cadlus.

You should bring the collar you found to Saeradan for his examination.This collar is cold to the touch and sends a chill down your spine. You cannot read the evil runes upon it, but perhaps Saeradan can.'I know these runes well enough to know that the tongue written hereupon is the Black Speech. I will investigate this further.'You found the corpse of one of the mysterious white stags of Enedwaith and harvested its strange antlers.There are Rangers at Echad Idhrenfair to the north-east of the stag-corpse.

You should bring the rack of antlers you harvested to one of the Rangers of the Grey Company.You carefully harvest the antlers from this corpse. The extraordinarily large rack of antlers is without blemish and perfectly symmetrical.

Such a specimen might be of interest to the Rangers of the Grey Company.'Greetings once more, ${PLAYER}.  What have you found there? Indeed, this is a strange specimen. I have never seen such a large and perfect rack of antlers. And the polished sheen of the ivory? This was borne by no natural creature.

'We have seen many strange things since coming to this place, but always at the edge of our vision. We thought the mysteries but spectres of the imagination. Now I must wonder....'While searching for information about the evil which drove many goblins to desert Burgûl-stazg, you learned that the enemy forces there are commanded by an Uruk called Talûntûm.Talûntûm may be found within the bulwark at the rear of Burgûl-stazg, north-west from Echad Mothelen.

Dagorchiel has asked you to defeat Talûntûm, the captain of Burgûl-stazg.Defeat Talûntûm at Burgûl-stazgDagorchiel is at Echad Mothelen, south-east from Burgûl-stazg.

You should return to Dagorchiel with tidings of your victory.Talk to Dagorchiel at Echad Mothelen'${PLAYER}, a moment please.

'I understand that Mothelen wishes you to enter Burgûl-stazg...perhaps while you are there, you will attempt to defeat Talûntûm, the captain of the camp? With many goblins deserting their posts, the enemy there is already in a weakened state...slaying Talûntûm may just be the key to breaking their spirits once and for all.

'Talûntûm will likely be found in the bulwark at the rear of the camp. Return to me when the deed is done.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! The goblins of Burgûl-stazg will not likely recover from that blow, unless a new leader rises among them.''Talûntûm is a fierce foe...be careful, ${PLAYER}.'The Ranger Himeinior was disturbed by the crushed boulder and skeleton you discovered while patrolling the Gloomglens.The footprint you found lies to the west of Echad Idhrenfair.

Himeinior has asked you to return to the site of the footprint you found and track the beast to its lair.Return to the site of the first footprintThe second footprint lies to the south of the first, which was to the west of Echad Idhrenfair.

You should continue to track the beast to its lair.Find the second footprintThe third footprint lies to the west of the second, south and west of Echad Idhrenfair.

You should continue tracking the beast to its lair.Find the third footprintThe fourth footprint lies to the west of the third, south and west of Echad Idhrenfair.

You should continue tracking the beast to its lair.Find the fourth footprintThe fifth footprint lies to the south-west of the fourth.

You should continue tracking the beast to its lair.Find the fifth footprintThe creature's lair lies to the north-west of the fifth footprint, south-west of Echad Idhrenfair.

Himeinior bade you defeat the unknown creature.Enter the Grey King's lair and defeat the creatureHimeinior is at Echad Idhrenfair, north-east of the Grey King's lair.

You have defeated the creature known as the Grey King and should return to Himeinior with news of your victory.Talk to Himeinior at Echad Idhrenfair'I am concerned, ${PLAYER}, by the evidence you discovered while patrolling the Gloomglens. The crushed boulder and skeleton would be enough to cause concern, but I find the footprint particularly worrisome. The might and stature of the creature suggests a giant or some kind of troll, but the footprint you describe seems more bestial.

'There are many creatures in this world of which we have little or no knowledge, and such a creature would pose a genuine threat to the Grey Company. Therefore, I ask that you track the monster to its lair and dispose of it.

'Be wary upon your hunt, ${PLAYER}. I fear this beast is more cunning and subtle than its stature suggests.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! I have never heard of such a creature as you describe, but I do not doubt the danger it represented.''I know not what this portends, but I fear a terrible beast lurks in the hills....''I know not what this portends, but I fear a terrible beast lurks in the hills....''I know not what this portends, but I fear a terrible beast lurks in the hills....''I know not what this portends, but I fear a terrible beast lurks in the hills....''I know not what this portends, but I fear a terrible beast lurks in the hills....''I know not what this portends, but I fear a terrible beast lurks in the hills....'You found this dark crystal at the place where you had banished a Cuthraul.Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan, south-west of Gavar Cadlus.

You should bring the crystal to Saeradan for identification.This dark crystal is cold to the touch and sends chills down your spine. It may have something to do with how the Cuthraul were summoned to Gwyllion's Gate to begin with.

Saeradan will likely wish to see this crystal.Saeradan shudders as he touches the crystal.

'Alas! This foul crystal bears the taint of morgul! Someone of great power in service of the Enemy was responsible for summoning these spirits!'The Uch-lûth received the gift of the Grey Company, but still do not trust you fully.Gwyllion's Gate lies to the south of Gavar Cadlus.

Rhiain has asked you to seek evidence of the Cuthraul's presence and to banish the spirit if you may.Cuthraul have appeared at Gwyllion's Gate, to the south of Gavar Cadlus.

Rhiain sked you to banish the Cuthraul if you can.Defeat Cuthraul in the Windfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhiain is at Gavar Cadlus, north from Gwyllion's Gate.

You should return to Rhiain with tidings of your success.Talk to Rhiain at Gavar Cadlus'Grufudh says that your friends sent medicine and furs for trade... it is a good demonstration of trust, but our trust is not so easily earned. Too much dwells in this land that we do not understand... many evil spirits.

'Just last night, I was seeking a lost goat and saw what I believe was a Cuthraul, an evil spirit, floating in the air near Gwyllion's Gate. The Old Woman of the Mountain who lives beyond that pass is a strange creature, so the sight of such a spirit was not surprising, but I fear its presence.

'Will you seek evidence that what I saw was not just my imagination? If the Cuthraul appears, will you be able to banish it? Gwyllion's Gate lies south from here. I have only seen the spirit at night.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Some creatures may only be found at night; however, the first stage of this quest may be advanced during the day.</rgb>'The Cuthraul are fearsome spirits of folktales... now they are come to life!''The Cuthraul are fearsome spirits of folktales... now they are come to life!''You are glûs -- holy -- Duvodiad! None of our folk have ever been able to banish the Cuthraul... we praise you, Glûs Duvodiad!'The Uch-lûth were impressed by your victory against the Cuthraul at Gwyllion's Gate and seek your aid once more.Cuthraul haunt the lands around Gavar Cadlus.

Iuan has asked you to banish the Cuthraul from the land.Defeat Cuthraul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iuan is at Gavar Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should return to Iuan with tidings of your victory against the Cuthraul.Talk to Iuan at Gavar Cadlus'${PLAYER}, Glûs Duvodiad! We beseech you to aid us once more. Your power against the Cuthraul is great, but more have been seen haunting the lands!

'Will you seek out these fell spirits and banish them as well? I fear they will possess our goats and call forth Druggavar!''You are the bane of the Cuthraul, Glûs Duvodiad.''I do not know how you are able to banish these spirits, Glûs Duvodiad, but for it, we praise you in song!'The Elves of the Golden Host discovered a second enemy encampment on the western edge of the Dourstocks, but something seems to be wrong.Goblin-deserters can be found in the Dourstocks, between Echad Mothelen and Burgûl-stazg, to the north-west.

Mothelen has asked you to hunt down some of the goblin-deserters and discover what has terrified them.Defeat goblin-deserters in the Dourstocks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mothelen is at Echad Mothelen in the western Dourstocks, south-east of Burgûl-stazg.

You should return to Mothelen with the information you have gathered.Talk to Mothelen at Echad Mothelen'${PLAYER}, as we expected, we found another enemy encampment here in the Dourstocks; however, something seems to be terribly wrong. There are not enough goblins and Orcs in Burgûl-stazg to mount any kind of counterattack against Echad Sirion, and more goblins are deserting everyday.

'Perhaps you could go out into the Dourstocks between here and Burgûl-stazg and see if you can find any of the deserters. You might be able to learn what has them so terrified.

'When you learn something, return to me.''This becomes more mysterious. From what you say, it appears the leaders of the encampment are up to something that has even the goblins unnerved. We shall need to learn exactly what that is....''Something queer is occuring here, ${PLAYER}. Keep your eyes sharp and your wits about you.'With one last effort and dwindling hope, Fernachar urgently wishes to locate the whereabouts of his missing friends and see them safely returned.The missing Malledhrim scouts can surely be found in Dannenglor, north of the Haunted Inn.

You should search Dannenglor for the missing Elves, though whether they are alive or dead is yet to be seen.Search for the first scout in DannenglorSearch for the second scout in DannenglorSearch for the third scout in DannenglorFernachar is in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, south of Dannenglor.

You should speak with Fernachar and tell him that the three scouts met their doom in Dannenglor.Talk to Fernachar at the Haunted Inn'You must make one final venture into Dannenglor, ${PLAYER}, and this is the most important one. Pray do not return until this last hope is either verified or put to rest forever, for my heart cannot bear the suspense much longer.

'I need you to go back to the morroval-roost and search high and low for my friends, the missing scouts. You have proven yourself more than capable of battling the vile foe that wanders that place, and so I put my last hope in you.

'Three went forth, and three you must account for, be they alive or dead. Go north one last time, Randir, and do not leave until you find them.''Alas, alas! It is just as I feared! Let this be a lesson to us all that no matter what distractions may tempt us while on this dark and seldom-travelled road, we must not stray from our course. Vainly did they pass into the West, never to return.

'Truly does my heart despair at this terrible news, though I long expected it.

'You have my most heartfelt thanks for your part in this, my dear friend. I would still be driven mad with worry, but for your efforts. You are most deserving of the trust of the Malledhrim.''Pray make haste! There cannot be much time, if they are indeed alive at all. Go to Dannenglor and do not return until you have learned aught of their fate.'The Rangers of the Grey Company seek to acquire the good will of the Uch-lûth, the Dunlending clan inhabiting Enedwaith.Pristine feathers might be found in the nests of the crebain at Pluvun Gwern, north-east of Echad Saeradan.

Amlan has asked you to collect pristine feathers to trade to the Algraig of Enedwaith.Collect pristine feathers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith, south-west of Pluvun Gwern.

Amlan told you to take the craban-feathers to Saeradan to be prepared for delivery to the Algraig.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! It has been long since you rid the Hobbits of Buckland of the threat of the giant. Thanks to you, they may wander the Brandy Hills with little fear.

'Now, I am in need of your aid once more. The Algraig use feathers for bedding and decoration, ${PLAYER}. It may be to our benefit to collect many pristine feathers to bring to them as an offering of peace. Perhaps such an offering will entice them to trade with us.

'Crebain nest at Pluvun Gwern to the north-east of here. Perhaps you may find pristine feathers within their nests. Bring them to Saeradan...the feathers must be of the highest quality.''Search the nests of the crebain at Pluvun Gwern, north-east of here, for the feathers we require.''Aye, ${PLAYER}, I believe these will do well. Bring them to Saeradan...he will know what to do with them.''These are the feathers that Amlan requested of you? Good! Then all is nearly in readiness.'The Rangers of the Grey Company are running short of provisions and seek ways to supplement their remaining supplies.Dun oxen can be found throughout the Windfells.

Andreg has asked you to hunt the dun oxen of the Windfells for meat. He warned you not to harm the domesticated oxen of the Uch-lûth.Collect ox-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Andreg is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should bring the meat you collected to Andreg.'${PLAYER}, I know that Saeradan seeks to befriend the Uch-lûth in the hopes of opening trade with them, but we have a more immediate need for provisions. To this end, I would ask a favour of you.

'As we entered the Windfells, we have seen many herds of oxen roaming the wilds. Would you hunt some of these oxen and bring me the meat?

'Be wary, however... the Uch-lûth also maintain herds in this region. You should not harm any domesticated oxen that you find.''We will need plenty of meat, if we are to continue our journey.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! This will help us greatly, though I fear it will not be quite enough. Nevertheless, you have our thanks.'The Rangers of the Grey Company are running short of provisions and seek ways to supplement their remaining supplies.Dun oxen can be found throughout the Windfells.

Andreg has asked you to once more hunt the dun oxen of the Windfells, but warned you not to harm the herds of the Uch-lûth.Collect ox-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Andreg is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should bring the ox-meat you collected to Andreg.'While I feel some remorse for hunting the beasts from which the Uch-lûth draw their herds, our quest is urgent, and we must have provisions to complete it. Therefore, I must ask you to go forth once more and hunt the dun oxen of the Windfells.

'Again, do not harm the domesticated herds of the Uch-lûth. I should hope to avoid angering the Uch-lûth as much as possible.'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you accept this quest, you will not be able to take the quest A Matter of Doubt.</rgb>'There are plenty of oxen in the Windfells, ${PLAYER}... the few we hunt should not harm the livelihood of the Uch-lûth.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. This meat will go far in provisioning the Grey Company.'Mírdiniel of the Malledhrim is interested in the Elf-ruins to the north, especially because of their close proximity to Lothlórien. She wishes to recover relics of the Elves who lived there to learn more of them.The ruins of Dannenglor are north of the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks.

You should search the Elf-ruins of Dannenglor for any treasures that might recall the Elves of old.Search treasure-piles for relics of worth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mírdiniel awaits you in the Haunted Inn, south of Dannenglor.

You should speak with Mírdiniel and inform her that there was nothing to be found among the morroval-hoards in Dannenglor.Talk to Mírdiniel at the Haunted Inn'Mae govannen, Elf-friend, and welcome to our meagre refuge. You may tarry here, if you wish, but I think you may be of some use to me ere we depart this place.

'Have you ventured north and beheld the ruined walls of the Elves who lived here long ago? We ourselves have only espied them from a safe distance, but some of our scouts did go that way and have not returned. There are merrevail who live there now; all the signs are there -- the filth, the intense evil in the very air....

'I suspect that there are great hoards of relics beyond those sinister walls. The filth of the merrevail dulls all things fair, but they care for treasures with a fierce jealousy. I believe there will be memories of the Elves among the foul refuse. Will you search the ruins for treasures of worth? These relics belong in the possession of the Elves, where they can be properly attended.''The ruins you seek are to the north of here -- Dannenglor, I believe they are called. The name is known to me, but the history is not.''How odd! Was there really nothing of worth -- nothing at all? I was sure that the merrevail there were guarding something. I am still not convinced that there is nothing of worth there.'You encountered a strange breed of goblin in the wilds of the Gloomglens, taking its spear as evidence of your victory.There are Rangers at Echad Idhrenfair in the Gloomglens.

You should bring the spear you collected to the Rangers of the Grey Company. They may know more about the strange goblins.This spear is evidence of your encounter with a strange breed of goblins in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith. While no less aggressive than the goblins of the Misty Mountains, these creatures appeared to be closer akin to Men than to their mountain-bred brethren.

Perhaps the Rangers of the Grey Company will know more about these creatures.'You were right to bring this to me, ${PLAYER}. That the spear is of goblin-make is not in doubt, but the craft has its differences. As well there are no markings which indicate which tribe the creatures belong to.

'From your description of them, I ween that these goblins are outcasts, distanced from their brethren from the Mountains for many generations. We should learn more about them.'Your discovery of a strange breed of goblin in the Gloomglens is a source of concern to the Ranger Idhrenfair.The gate to the goblin-village lies to the south-east of Echad Idhrenfair.

Idhrenfair has asked you to scout the goblin-village you discovered while patrolling the Gloomglens to determine its strength and to whom its inhabitants owe allegiance.Return to the gate of the goblin-villageThe goblin-village lies to the south-east of Echad Idhrenfair.

You should continue deeper into the goblin-village.Go to the second patrol pointThe goblin-village lies to the south-east of Echad Idhrenfair.

You should continue deeper into the goblin-village.Go to the third patrol pointThe goblin-village lies to the south-east of Echad Idhrenfair.

You should continue deeper into the goblin-village.Go to the fourth patrol pointIdhrenfair is at Echad Idhrenfair, north-west of the goblin-village.

You should return to Idhrenfair with tidings of what you have learned.Talk to Idhrenfair at Echad Idhrenfair'The goblin-village you discovered is very much a source of concern for me, ${PLAYER}. Goblins of any breed are servants of the Enemy and pose a threat to the secrecy of our quest. However, if these creatures are outcasts, it may be that they will pay us no mind, beyond seeking our lives.

'I would like you to return to the village and learn what you can of the goblins. I would like to know what their strength is and to whom they owe allegiance.

'Be careful, friend, for you may have to travel to the deepest reaches of their village.''You say these goblins appear to be wild? That may explain why they have become as they are, seeming more like to men than to Orc-kind.

'They have some small strength, you say? But you survived their village alone, so I am sure they will pose no significant threat to the Grey Company.''I have not seen the like of these goblins before...these must be the bugan that the Algraig have spoken of in the past.''I have not seen the like of these goblins before...these must be the bugan that the Algraig have spoken of in the past.''I have not seen the like of these goblins before...these must be the bugan that the Algraig have spoken of in the past.''I have not seen the like of these goblins before...these must be the bugan that the Algraig have spoken of in the past.'Gwin Curhonon had come to the goblin-village of Khoblún Utot under the mistaken impression they were hobbits of another family lost during the ancient exodus from the east.Gwin Curhonon is at Khoblún Utot in the Gloomglens.

Gwin Curhonon has asked you to help him escape the bugan of the Gloomglens.Talk to Gwin Curhonon to escape Khoblún UtotGwin Curhonon is hiding outside Khoblún Utot in the Gloomglens.

You should speak with Gwin Curhonon about your successful escape from the bugan of Enedwaith.Talk to Gwin Curhonon'Hullo there! As you can see, I've gotten myself into a spot of trouble. You see, we thought these critters were fellow hobbits, but these bugan share no blood with us!

'Could you let me out of this cage? Perhaps together we can get away from here!''Thank you, whoever you are... ${PLAYER} you say? Could I ask one more favour of you?''Thank you, friend...if you are ready, let's go!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>The object you found while patrolling the Gloomglens intrigued the Ranger Idhrenfair.Hobbits apparently dwell somewhere in the Gloomglens.

Idhrenfair suggested you seek the hobbits in the west, as that is the likely direction the first hobbits would have taken on their journey into Eriador.Find the Hobbits of Enedwaith'Halflings! Halflings in these hills! It is said that long ago when the hobbits first crossed the Misty Mountains in the east that some of the Stoors settled here in Enedwaith, but it has also long been believed that they were wiped out during the time of the Plague.

'This proves otherwise to me. Will you seek out these hobbits, ${PLAYER}? It may be that in these dark times, they should be encouraged to continue their journey and rejoin their kindred in the Shire. Darkness is quickly falling across this land.

'You might try searching in the west, ${PLAYER}, for that is the direction the first hobbits likely would have taken.''What! Who are ye? What do ye want?''I have oft wondered if any of the old halfling tribes still existed....'Fernachar has asked you to defeat many merrevail in pursuit of the Malledhrim scouts who have been waylaid at Dannenglor.Merrevail can be found in the Elf-ruins of Dannenglor, north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should fight the merrevail in pursuit of the Malledhrim Elves who were most likely waylaid at the gates of Dannenglor.Defeat merrevail at Dannenglor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fernachar awaits you anxiously at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, south of Dannenglor.

