'You should go back to Dannenglor, this time armed with the knowledge you have gained from your first exploration. Cut down as many merrevail as you can, and then report back to me when the way is clearer.

'If you can do this, we will surely be able to find my lost friends! I dearly hope that they live yet, but I am deeply troubled, deeply troubled....''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. I believe we are coming closer to uncovering what happened to my lost brethren.''How have you fared thus far, ${PLAYER}? The merrevail are in Dannenglor, to the north.'The persistence of the Darkrage wolves, despite your efforts to thin their pack, leads Prestadír to believe that the wolf-pack is being used for evil, tamed by the forces of Dol Guldur to combat intruders in the wild.Pack-howler's Hill is to the south of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should go to Pack-howler's Hill and attempt to draw out the wolf-tamer who has trained the Darkrage wolves against the Malledhrim.Use the wolf-whistle to summon the Wolf-keeper and defeat himPrestadír is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should return to Prestadír with news of your success.Speak with Prestadír at the Haunted Inn'You have done well to thin the pack, ${PLAYER}, but still the creatures persist, and with more fervour than ever. They press closer and closer with every passing night.

'It becomes clear to me that these are no reckless wild beasts. Nay, I believe they are driven by some fell hand. Their efforts against us are not those of animals, but of a host of enemies rallying their defences against an invasion.

'Surely someone from Dol Guldur has tamed this pack for their own evil purposes. You should try to draw him out, whomever he is! Go to the Pack-howler's Hill, my friend, and see if anyone answers your summons.''Good! I am glad we are rid of the Orc who twists the animals here for his evil purposes. You have done well indeed, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for your efforts on behalf of the Golden Host.''The Packhowler's Hill lies to the south of here, ${PLAYER}.'Gwin Curhonon asked you to help him escape from Khoblún Utot.Escort Gwin Curhonon out of Khoblún Utot.Escort Gwin Curhonon to safety'Lets get out of here!''Thank you! Now let us hurry before more bugan arrive!'The Grey King of the Gloomglens is a menace which must be dealt with.Find and defeat the Grey King in its lair.Defeat the Grey KingSaeradan has charged you with confronting Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, and driving her forth from the Windfells of Enedwaith.Speak with Saeradan at Gwyllion's Gate.Accompany Saeradan to confront GwyllionSeek out Gwyllion at her hut beyond Gwyllion's Gate.Defeat Gwyllion and her lieutenantsSpeak with Saeradan to return to Echad Saeradan.Talk to Saeradan'Gwyllion has escaped, ${PLAYER}. While she may no longer bring terror to the Uch-lûth, I fear we have not yet seen the last of her.

