'The mystery, I'm afraid, has deepened.'Rhosun Turio is an artist in Maur Tulhau who works with stag-ivory scrimshaw.White stags can be found throughout the Gloomglens in Enedwaith.

Rhosun Turio has asked you to collect stag-antlers for her to continue her scrimshaw.Collect stag-antlers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhosun Turio can be found in Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith.

You should bring the stag-antlers you collected back to Rhosun Turio.'Ho there... are ye that giant Rhus Cornchúthur befriended? I can't say I approve... what should we have to do with duvodiad? Well, while you're here, I suppose I could make use of ye.

'I'm an artist, you see, and need materials for my work. I make art from the antlers of the white stags. Unfortunately, I usually have to settle with ivory that our hunters collect from stags which the Rhi Helvarch has slain... they are too afraid to hunt the stags themselves.

'If ye could hunt some of the white stags and bring me their antlers... well, ye might make more of an impression on me.''Have ye found such antlers as I need, giant?''Oh my! These antlers are most beautiful... they will become more beautiful yet at my hand!

'Thank ye, Duvodiad! You've proven your worthiness to me.'Rhus Cornchúthur, impressed by your performance of the task he set before you, has recommended you to Iolo Brochtû, the mayor of Maur Tulhau.Iolo Brochtû resides at a large house at the end of the road leading into Maur Tulhau, north-west from Rhus Cornchúthur.

Rhus Cornchúthur told you to speak with the mayor, Iolo Brochtû.Talk to Iolo Brochtû at Maur Tulhau'We've been afeared of Gavar-diavol for a long time, ${PLAYER}... now that he's gone, we'll all sleep better at night, for sure!

'I've sent word to Iolo Brochtû, our Maer, and he wishes to meet the giant what saved us. Perhaps ye can be of further aid to my folk! Maer Brochtû resides in our village, down the path to the north-west.''I'm not sure but what the maer might be frightened by ye yet, Duvodiad.''Rhus seems quite taken with ye, Duvodiad, but we've not dealt with many folk other than our own. You'll have to do more to prove yourself to me.'Iago Glennudh is one of the most respected farmers of Maur Tulhau.Boar-droppings can be found throughout the Gloomglens.

Iago Glennudh has asked you to gather boar-droppings for use as fertilizer.Collect boar-droppings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iago Glennudh is at Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith.

You should bring the boar-droppings you collected to Iago Glennudh.'Ha! A giant, indeed...I've seen the Rhi Helvarch at night hunting the white elk, and you've naught on him for height.

'Well, if ye want to be put to use, ye could gather fertilizer for me. I'm considered the most respected farmer in Maur Tulhau, and that's because I know what it takes to grow vegetables.

'Aye, ye know what I mean, I see...or ye think you do. Boar-droppings, Duvodiad, that's what I need. Ye can find them everywhere...ye just have to look.''Boar-droppings...that's the secret!''Well now, you're not too proud to do the dirty work, Duvodiad...I must say that I'm impressed!'Master Farmer Iago Glennudh, impressed with the tasks you completed for him and Violed Isbrun, desires your help once again.Boar-droppings and marigolds can be found throughout the Gloomglens.

Iago Glennudh has asked you to go out and find more boar-droppings and marigolds.Collect boar-droppings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect marigolds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iago Glennudh is at Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith.

You should bring the droppings and flowers you collected back to Iago Glennudh.Talk to Iago Glennudh at Maur Tulhau'Stay and speak with me a bit, ${PLAYER}. You've a good eye for farming, and I was wondering if ye would help me again.

