You should return to Lavanferon with news of your success.Talk to Lavanferon at Echad Mothelen'Hail, ${PLAYER}! Please stay and speak with me. While my companions fret over the strange happenings in Burgûl-stazg, my forays into the western Dourstocks have discovered more threats, and no less dangerous in my opinion.

'One of these threats is the black wolves. These beasts are vicious and unpredictable. I have also seen a great wolf, which I have named Blackmaw. His lair lies some distance to the south-east of here at the Packhowler's Hill.

'I bid you go forth and defeat as many of the wolves as you can and lay low Blackmaw.''It is well, ${PLAYER}, that you have returned victorious. Such evil cannot be allowed to persist in this place which was once the fair Greenwood.''Blackmaw and his pack have been terrorizing the flanks of our host. They must be defeated!'After you rescued Gwin Curhonon from the bugan-village, he told you to visit his home.The hobbit-village of Maur Tulhau lies to the north-west of Gwin Curhonon's hiding place.

Gwin Curhonon asked you to bring word of his rescue to his kinsfolk in Maur Tulhau.Talk to a hobbit at Maur Tulhau'It is good to be free of those vile creatures. That any of us ever thought they were brother hobbits is beyond me!

'Would you go to Maur Tulhau and speak with my kinsfolk there? They should know that I am safe, thanks to you.

'The village lies to the north-west of here, off a hidden path.''Ye say Gwin is safe? Well then, that's a good thing....''I wish I could be there when my folk meet ye!'Pleased with your dispatch of the legendary Black Sow, the oxherds of the Uch-lûth seek your aid in protecting their herds.The herds of the Uch-lûth range to the north-east of Uch Cadlus.

Wunne has asked you to go among the herds of the Uch-lûth and protect them from wolves and other predators.Defeat creatures hunting the oxen of the Uch-lûth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wunne is at Uch-lûth in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should return to Wunne with news of your success.Talk to Wunne at Uch Cadlus'So, Duvodiad, you slew the legendary Black Sow? Then perhaps your skills will aid us further. Despite the death of the Black Sow, our herd is still being attacked. I have seen wolves prowling about during the day, but at night I have heard howls that chill my bones to the very marrow... I fear something prowls the night more fearsome than wolves.

'Will you go among our herds and guard them from the beasts which prey upon them? I cannot promise great reward, but you will have our gratitude.

'Our herds range to the north-east of Uch Cadlus.''Please, if you do not protect our herds, they will be destroyed, and our people will not survive the winter!''You have our thanks, Duvodiad. Your arm is quite skilled!'The oxherds of the Uch-lûth were pleased with your efforts upon their behalf.The Uch-lûth's herds graze to the north-east of Uch Cadlus.

Davudh has asked you to continue protecting their herds against the wolves and other fell things which hunt them in return for a continuing supply of meat for the Grey Company.Defeat creatures hunting the ox-herds of the Uch-lûth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Davudh is at Uch Cadlus, south-west of the ox-herds.

You should return to Davudh with news of your success.Talk to Davudh at Uch CadlusAmlan is at Echad Saeradan, far to the north-west of Uch Cadlus.

