'Return to Davudh with our thanks.''Give our thanks to the Uch-lûth, ${PLAYER}.''Your friends have honour, Duvodiad.'You learned from your investigation of Burgûl-stazg that the goblins, under orders from their captain, stole an idol of the Necromancer from the haunted ruins.The idol of the Necromancer can be found in Burgûl-stazg, north-west from Echad Mothelen.

Mothelen has instructed you to find and destroy the idol of the Necromancer.Destroy the idol of the NecromancerMothelen is at Echad Mothelen, south-east from Burgûl-stazg.

You should return to Mothelen with news of your success.Talk to Mothelen at Echad Mothelen'An idol of the Necromancer, which the White Council had discovered was in fact the Dark Lord himself...though Sauron may have been driven forth, his minions still serve him at Dol Guldur. It is said that the Lieutenant of Dol Guldur commands there once again.

'There is no telling what grief will come of these goblins' foolishness. That idol must be destroyed!

'Go at once, ${PLAYER}. Enter Burgûl-stazg and find that statue. Let nothing stand in your way. An icon of such dark power cannot be permitted to remain!''You were attacked by the shades of Men? It was rumoured that the Woodmen who had lived in the Dourstocks had fallen into evil over two-hundred years ago and had worshipped the Necromancer. It appears those rumours are true.

'It is well that you destroyed the idol, but I fear a terror has been unleashed unlike any this land has seen.''You must stop these Orcs' vile plans, ${PLAYER}. They know not what powers they are toying with.'After learning that the 'hobbits' of the neighbouring village were actually a breed of wild goblin called the bugan, Mayor Brochtû declared a blood feud against them.Khoblún Utot lies to the south of Maur Tulhau.

Iolo Brochtû has asked you to return to Khoblún Utot and drive out the bugan.Defeat bugan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iolo Brochtû is at Maur Tulhau, north of Khoblún Utot.

You should return to Iolo Brochtû with news of your success.Talk to Iolo Brochtû at Maur Tulhau'Why if I'd known that village was full of bugan, I would never have thought to make a peace offering! We've had such troubles with them that I find it an affront that they should dwell so near!

