'What is more, you tell me that this shrine appears to be in pristine condition, as though it has been visited and cared for recently...perhaps a hermit lives nearby?'You slew a wolf in the Gloomglens and harvested its fine pelt.There are Rangers at Echad Idhrenfair in the Gloomglens.

You should bring the wolf-pelt you harvested as evidence of the threats the Grey Company might face in the Gloomglens.This sleek and smooth wolf-pelt shimmers somewhat in your hands, making you wonder if it, like everything else in this wood, is somehow enchanted.

Regardless, the Rangers of the Grey Company will wish to know that wolves are a threat to them in the Gloomglens.'Wolves. Minor servants of the Enemy they are, corrupted hounds of ages past now turned to evil.

'Nevertheless, we have dealt with our fair share of the brutes, and a few more will not be an impediment to our quest.'The Rangers of the Grey Company seek to ensure the secrecy of their purpose and their passage through Enedwaith.The first patrol point is north-east of Echad Idhrenfair.

Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.Scout the first patrol pointThe second patrol point is north-west of the first.

Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.Scout the second patrol pointThe third patrol point is south-west of the second.

Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.Scout the third patrol pointThe fourth patrol point is south of the third.

Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.Scout the fourth patrol pointThe fifth patrol point is east of the fourth.

Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.Scout the fifth patrol pointIdhrenfair is at Echad Idhrenfair in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith, north-west of the fifth patrol point.

You should return to Idhrenfair with news of your discoveries.Talk to Idhrenfair at Echad Idhrenfair'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. It has been long since we spoke with each other at the Haunted Inn of Audaghaim. I must confess that I am relieved to be gone from that place.

'I understand that you are aware of our purpose and would ask for your assistance. It is of utmost importance that our passage remains hidden from the eyes of the Enemy, and for that purpose are we here in the Gloomglens.

'Will you scout the paths of the Gloomglens and learn whether any enemies patrol these lands? Return here when you have completed your patrol and let me know what you have found.''What is this you say? You found a village of strange, halfling-like creatures? But they are not of the halfling people? I must think on this.''Have you finished your patrol already?''Have you finished your patrol already?''Have you finished your patrol already?''Have you finished your patrol already?''Have you finished your patrol already?'The Uch-lûth goatherd Grufudh accepted the gift of the Rangers, but he still does not trust you.The goat-herds graze the land to the west of Gavar Cadlus.

Grufudh asked you to investigate the evil shadows he and his fellow goatherds saw among their herds. They only seem to come at night, but may be found elsewhere during the day.Druggavar have appeared among the herds of the Uch-lûth, west of Gavar Cadlus.

Grufudh asked you to find a way to banish the Druggavar from their lands.Defeat Druggavar in the Windfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grufudh is at Gavar Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith, east of the goat-herd.Talk to Grufudh at Gavar Cadlus'The gift of your duvodiad friends is welcome, but we are not prone to blindly accept the friendship of strangers. If you wish to earn our trust, you must lend us your aid.

'I and my people have seen evil shadows moving among our herd at night... shadows of goat-shape, but blacker than night and with red eyes like fire. They remind us of the Druggavar, demon-goats of our legends. I had never seen such things in my childhood, and so I never believed... now it seems many things of old tales haunt us.

'Perhaps you may find the truth of the matter among our goats. Our herd is there, to the west of our camp.''I never believed the old tales, but now I must wonder....''I never believed the old tales, but now I must wonder....''You indeed saw Druggavar? This is a fell sign....

'You were able to banish the spirits from our goats? You have our praise, Duvodiad... you are glûs -- holy -- among us.'Impressed by your apparent power over the evil Druggavar of Enedwaith, the Uch-lûth seek your aid once more.Druggavar haunt the lands to the west of Gavar Cadlus.

Iuan has asked you to hunt down and banish the Druggavar of Enedwaith.Defeat Druggavar or wolves in the Windfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iuan is at Gavar Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith, east of the goat-herd.

You should return to Iuan with news of your victory.Talk to Iuan at Gavar Cadlus'Ah! You are the Glûs Duvodiad! You have proven your power, but the banishment you performed seems only to have been temporary... the Druggavar have returned and threaten our herds!

'Will you go out once more and fend off these evil demons? If you will, I will reward you. Our herds graze there, to the west.''O Glûs Duvodiad, you come to our aid once more....''Once again, you have saved our goats, Glûs Duvodiad... we shall praise you always!'You found a medallion inscribed in a language with which you are not familiar.There are Rangers at Echad Idhrenfair to the south of where you found the medallion.

You should bring the medallion you found to one of the Rangers of the Grey Company.This strange medallion depicts an antlered helm, encircled by writing in a language with which you are not familiar. The only words you can make out are "Rhi Helvarch."

Perhaps one of the Rangers of the Grey Company will be able to decipher it.'What is this you have found, ${PLAYER}? I know a little of this language, yes. It is the native Dunlending tongue.

'These words here -- "Rhi Helvarch" -- mean the Hunter King. I must confess that I have never heard of such a person before. Perhaps it is the title of a local chieftain?

'And this here -- "Galar-gwig" -- could be translated as the Mournshaws. I wonder....'Near the place called Gwyllion's Gate, you found a banner bearing the symbol of the White Hand.Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan, west from Gwyllion's Gate.

You should tell Saeradan of the banner you discovered.Talk to Saeradan at Echad SaeradanThis banner bears the symbol of the White Hand, the charge of the traitor Saruman. Saeradan will certainly wish to know of this.'You found a banner bearing the sign of the White Hand. It is no secret that Saruman the White has a strong influence over the Men of Dunland, but we did not know that he troubled Enedwaith...there are few inhabitants, and they keep to themselves.

'If Saruman's influence has indeed reached into Enedwaith, many of these strange happenings are easily explained.'Caradog Henbuch is the village butcher of Maur Tulhau. As winter approaches, he finds himself in greater need of meat for the village's stores.White stags can be found wandering throughout the Gloomglens in Enedwaith.

Caradog Henbuch has asked you to hunt white stags and bring him the meat.Collect stag-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Caradog Henbuch is at Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith.

You should bring the meat you collected back to Caradog Henbuch.'Ye are the giant duvodiad Rhus has taken a fancy to? Well, ye don't look too impressive to me. Nevertheless, I'll give ye a chance to prove me wrong.

'Winter is coming on, and it looks to be bad this year. We're running short of meat, and our hunters are too afraid to go for more. Go hunt the white stags of the Gloomglens and bring the meat to me... then we'll talk more.''The white stags of the Gloomglens have a strange taste to them, but we prize their meat nonetheless when winter comes.''Well now... perhaps ye aren't so bad after all! Not many would dare to hunt the white stags... they say the stags are the prey of the Rhi Helvarch, and he wouldn't like his sport interrupted.'Impressed by your abilities and grateful for the meat you provided him, Caradog Henbuch has become a trusted friend.White stags can be found throughout the Gloomglens.

Caradog Henbuch has asked you to collect more stag-meat for himself and antlers for Rhosun Turio.Collect stag-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect stag-antlers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Caradog Henbuch is in Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens fo Enedwaith.

You should bring the meat and antlers you collected to Caradog Henbuch.'So, Duvodiad -- my apologies, ${PLAYER}...I should no longer call ye stranger. Anyways, Would ye be willing to bring me more stag-meat? Also, Rhosun could use more antlers for her scrimshaw.''You've been such a great help!''Thank ye, ${PLAYER}. We will make good use of these!'Prestadír now understands that the condemned villager to whom you spoke earlier orchestrated the murders of any and all who resisted the "progress" of the Necromancer's influence. He wishes for the shade's denial to be confronted with the long-buried truth at last.The condemned villager is in the accursed village of Audaghaim, in the Dourstocks, east of the Haunted Inn.

You should confront the condemned villager once more, this time armed with full knowledge of the truth he strove to conceal.Confront the condemned villager once morePrestadír awaits you at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, west of Audaghaim.

You should speak with Prestadír and tell him that the evil past of Audaghaim has been confronted at last.Talk to Prestadír at the Haunted Inn'We have the truth now, but it should not stop here. The murderers should not be allowed to dwell under their curse in this way, their guilt smothered and pacified by denial and lies!

'You must confront the shade again, but armed with the truth this time. I wish to see if he will admit his wrongdoing like an honourable man, but somehow I doubt he will.

'The mystery is solved, but what good is it if the murderers are allowed to endure? You will do much for the memory of those worthy Men who perished in this horrible time for Audaghaim.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}! You have done a very, very good deed in the name of those who fell while resisting the Dark Lord's evil influences. It is a tragic tale, but it is for the best that you did not allow its denial to be endured.

'You should be proud of what you accomplished today, even if it is too late to benefit the poor woodsmen who fell so many years ago. Their story should not be buried under the corruptions of Mirkwood, for they were heroes, and the truth deserves to be woven into song -- not forgotten, as the murderers would wish.

'Guilt and denial are the cruelest of enemies, my friend. You did well to fight them with such vigilance.''We are close to avenging the brave Men who fell while standing against the evil that took hold here. You should confront that condemned shade to whom you first spoke once more.''No! It is impossible! That...that story is no longer true. We destroyed that past and moved on with our lives. Why do you disturb our long peace with evils better left buried? That tale cannot be allowed to endure! You shall pay dearly for your meddling, Outsider!'The Uch-lûth were greatly displeased by the gift of meat presented to them, for they suspect the Grey Company of slaughtering their herds.There may be dead oxen among the herds of the Uch-lûth at Uch Cadlus in the Windfells.

Alun has asked you to examine the dead oxen among the herds of the Uch-lûth to determine what may have slain them.The Black Sow wanders the wilds of the Windfells.

Having determined that a great boar did indeed slay the oxen of the Uch-lûth, you should hunt down the Black Sow of the Windfells.Defeat the Black Sow of the WindfellsAlun is at Uch Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should return to Alun with news of your success.Talk to Alun at Uch Cadlus'Perhaps I was hasty in my judgement. These cuts were carefully taken from the carcass of a dead animal...our oxen which were slaughtered were gored, their meat ruined.

'Perhaps if you could help us discover what creature has been hunting our herds, we will consider trading with your friends. There is a legend which tells of a great black boar the likes of which has not been seen west of the Mountains in many long ages. It is said it may be the mate or descendant of the Boar of Everholt. Perhaps the Black Sow is responsible for this slaughter.

'Will you accept my offer? If so, look to our herd there to the north-east beneath the foothills. Almost nightly a beast or two has been slain.''So the Black Sow was indeed more than just a legend? Your deed then was heroic and worthy of song...even for a duvodiad, a stranger.''Have you determined what creature it is that hunts our herds?''You believe it is indeed the Black Sow that hunts our herds? The beast must then be slain, for it is too dangerous to be permitted to wander these lands.'Iolo Brochtû has told you of a legendary creature they call the Grey King who haunts the bluffs of the Gloomglens, crushing passers-by with great stones.The entrance to the Grey King's lair lies in a gully to the south-west of Maur Tulhau.

Iolo Brochtû has asked you to rid his village of the threat of the Grey King.Find and defeat the Grey KingIolo Brochtû is at Maur Tulhau, north-east of the Grey King's lair.

You should return to Iolo Brochtû with news of the Grey King's defeat.Talk to Iolo Brochtû at Maur Tulhau'So, ${PLAYER}, now that you've done so much for us, perhaps there is one more thing ye could help us with. I daresay it will be dangerous, though!

'There is a great beast -- some kind of troll or ogre, I don't know -- that haunts the bluffs and passes hereabouts, crushing folk with great boulders as they pass near. Occasionally it comes down out of the hills and roams the forest, they say, though I've never seen it.

'The Grey King we call it, for it's king of this wood, to be sure. Perhaps ye could rid us of this fearsome beast? You've proven a great friend so far, so how about it? Our hunters say the entrance to the Grey King's lair lies in a gully to the south-west. By the way, ye might want to look to that gift Rhus Cornchúthur gave you a while back....''Hooray! The Grey King has been defeated! No duvodiad are ye to us for certain, ${PLAYER}. Ye are a friend and kinsman to us all!

'Take this reward with our gratitude.''We would be most grateful if ye could do something about the Grey King!'According to Prestadir, the medallion you found says something about a Hunter King and the Mournshaws.Daervunn is at Echad Daervunn in the Mournshaws, far to the south of Echad Idhrenfair.

Prestadir suggested you take the sigil you found to Daervunn in the Mournshaws.'Some of our kinsmen have gone on to the Mournshaws to scout the way. Perhaps you should bring this sigil to Daervunn at Echad Daervunn...perhaps he has come upon some knowledge of this Hunter King.

'Echad Daervunn lies far to the south of here in the northern reaches of the Mournshaws.''You should speak with Daervunn in the Mournshaws, ${PLAYER}. He may have learned something of this Hunter King.''What is this? The Hunter King? It is a name we have heard rumoured, but there is not much more I can tell you. Perhaps you can help us find the truth.'A small party of explorers set off for Dannenglor and have not yet returned, and Fernachar is anxious for word of their fate.Dannenglor is to the north of the Haunted Inn.

Fernachar has asked you to search the ruins of Dannenglor for signs of the Elf-scouts who went that way. You should approach Dannenglor cautiously, following the road where the Elf explorers went.Search near Dannenglor for the Malledhrim scoutsFernachar awaits you in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, south of Dannenglor.

You should speak with Fernachar and tell him of the worrying scene you beheld when you approached Dannenglor.Talk to Fernachar at the Haunted Inn'Hail, ${CLASS}; welcome to our meagre establishment. It is not much, but it is safer than the wild woods beyond that door. I hope you will be careful when you venture out again -- a small party of our own went out to explore, and they have not returned.

'I will not deny that I am very worried for them. They espied the Elf-ruins to the north of here, which, if memory serves, was once the fair Elven-realm of Dannenglor. They left some days ago, and I fear the worst....

'Will you search for them, and scout the ruins so that we know what we are up against? Be very careful -- I do not wish you to meet the same fate that they met.''Alas! This does not bode well. My fears are all but confirmed. Oh, ${PLAYER}...do you think there is any hope?''Dannenglor is to the north. You should follow the road there, for that is the path our friends took when they ventured thither.'The mervyl-slaves are led by one of their own in subjugation to the merrevail.The master of the morvul-slaves can be summoned in Dannenglor, north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should use the merrevail's horn to summon the morvul-guard.Summon and defeat the morvul-guardPuiguil can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, south of Dannenglor.

You should return with news of your success to Puiguil.Talk to Puiguil in the Haunted Inn'Now that we have learned a bit of the nest of merrevail in Dannenglor, I think we can take some action against them. Those tokens you collected were made by one of their own.

'I am guessing this particular morvul is a strong brute, and you would do well to remove him if we are to secure Dannenglor against these beasts.

'I am sure he keeps well hidden. Hopefully when you return to Dannenglor, you will find some way to summon him to a confrontation. I do not think he will be able to resist a direct challenge. Be careful, ${PLAYER}; this is sure to be a dreadful challenge.''Wonderfully done, ${PLAYER}! You have given us much aid in this dark and dreary place. Everything we do to combat the countless evils here plants a seed of hope.''The morvul-guard can surely be called by some means within Dannenglor. You should search for a way to summon him.'Using the items and information you brought to him, Saeradan believes that it is a certainty that Saruman the White has a hand in the strange happenings in the Windfells.Grufudh is at Gavar Cadlus, north-east of Echad Saeradan.

Saeradan instructed you to speak with Grufudh about the banner of the White Hand that you found near Gwyllion's Gate.Talk to Grufudh at Gavar CadlusGwyllion's Gate, the entrance to the path which leads to Gwyllion's hut, lies to the south of Gavar Cadlus.

Grufudh told you to speak with Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, if you wished to know the source of the White Hand banner.Talk to Gwyllion at her hutSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan, west of Gwyllion's Gate.

You should return to Saeradan with news of your discovery of the Uruk-hai Filskûm at Gwyllion's hut.Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan'${PLAYER}, the banner you found is itself enough evidence that Saruman the White stirs trouble in this land, but the evils which you have encountered speak to a much more sinister plan.

'You should go to Grufudh and learn if he has encountered any emissaries of the White Hand, and if so, what the emissary desired of his people.

'Grufudh and his goatherds are at Gavar Cadlus to the east.''I have never seen such a banner, nor spoken with anyone who bore such a sign. If you found the banner near to Gwyllion's Gate, then there is one person and one person alone who may be able to help you.

'You must speak with Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain. Her hut sits upon the side of the mountain beyond Gwyllion's Gate. All you have to do is follow the path.

'Be wary though...the Old Woman of the Mountain is a Gurach, a witch from a lûth in the south. If you do not come in respect, she may take it ill.''You were waylaid by an Uruk-hai at the home of this Gwyllion, and he seemed to be guarding the old woman's hut? I fear this Gurach, as the Uch-lûth call her, is a sorceress in league with Saruman.'You learned that Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, is in league with the traitor Saruman. It is likely that she is responsible, as well, for the appearances of evil creatures in the Windfells.Talk to Saeradan to journey to Gwyllion's hutSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should return to Saeradan with news of your victory against Gwyllion.Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan'So, ${PLAYER}...from what you have told me, it appears that Gwyllion is indeed in league with the traitor Saruman. I expect she is also responsible for the apparitions which have been troubling the Uch-lûth.

'Return tonight, ${PLAYER}, and confront this sorceress. Perhaps with her gone, the Uch-lûth may be able to live without fear.

'Speak with me again when you are ready to leave.''I fear the door opened by the Old Woman of the Mountain will be a hard one to close; fortunately, Gwyllion herself shall no longer trouble the Uch-lûth.''Good, you have returned. May the Valar guide you, ${PLAYER}.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest, and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>You harvested the enormous tusks of the Black Sow, which remain in pristine condition.Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

You should bring the tusks of the Black Sow to Saeradan for his examination.These enormous tusks are evidence of the existence of a boar of legendary size.

Saeradan may be interested in seeing them.'You took these from a great boar, you say? Indeed, this beast must have rivalled the Boar of Everholt, slain in ages past by Folca, king of Rohan.

'That great beast terrorized the road through the Firienfeld for a long time, until at last King Folca, famed hunter that he was, took it upon himself to rid Rohan of the Boar. Alas, his victory was also his death, for the tusk-wounds he received were mortal.

'It would not surprise me to learn that this sow was in fact a distant descendant of that monster... what power created such a creature, I cannot say.'You have found a book of records buried in the ruins of Audaghaim, but many pages are missing from the period when Sauron returned to Mirkwood.The blank gravestone is in the graveyard to the south of Audaghaim and the Haunted Inn.

You should search the area of the uninformative gravestone again for anything you may have missed.Examine the blank gravestone more closely this timePrestadír is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, north of the graveyard.

You should tell Prestadír of your encounter with the condemned Record-keeper who appeared when you searched his grave.'So, it appears that someone kept a faithful record, but this record was not to the liking of those who carried out the murders. 

'If you are still invested in the story of this town, you should look into finding the missing pages. Perhaps they have been destroyed, and perhaps not.

'But where to start? In the case of hidden relics, sometimes it is best to start where you began. That blank gravestone was the first thing to rouse my interest in this mystery, and perhaps it can tell us more now.''I should have stood with the four who resisted, but I did not. I watched it all happen. Only when they had perished did I feel the effects of the true evil that was at work in Audaghaim. Too late did I record the truth.

'When they found what I had written, they came after me as well. I anticipated them. Here is a copy of the truth that was destroyed. Let this be my last effort on behalf of the true heroes of Audaghaim who resisted the evil corruptions of the Necromancer. Our blindness was our undoing!

'Yes -- the Necromancer came and promised much, and we saw the opportunity for progress and prosperity. The four that stood against him attacked the altar, and we cut them down in the name of Dol Guldur. They cursed us as they fell.

'Ah! My oath is fulfilled, my redemption nigh....''Have you found anything yet? Sometimes it is best to trace our steps from the beginning.''Ah! You have found the lost pages! I am astounded. May I take a look?

'At last, the truth -- and so it all comes together. Some of the townsmen resisted, and they were executed by their own folk. That settles the mystery. The guilty shade you spoke to before was the one who led the movement to accept the Necromancer's advances here. He was also the one who led in the murders.

'Everything is documented in this account, until the Record-keeper writes of his own guilt for not standing up for his fallen townsfolk. Here he writes that he knows his enemy will destroy the truth and execute him as well. This is the last entry by his hand.'Dangerous morvul-slaves stalk the city of Dannenglor, protecting their kind from intruders.Morvul-slaves can be found in Dannenglor, to the north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

Puiguil has asked you to defeat many morvul-slaves in Dannenglor and collect the tokens of bondage that can be found on them.Collect tokens of bondage from morvul-slaves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Puiguil is at the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood, south of Dannenglor.

You should speak with Puiguil and bring him the tokens of the mervyl's allegiance to their family.'How have you found Mirkwood thus far, randir? It is not to my liking at all. Several of our number have gone missing on a mission to Dannenglor. We know now that the place is rife with merrevail.

'If you find yourself there, you should defeat many of the morvul-slaves and see if you can learn of this morroval-nest. Any interesting relics you come across while in Dannenglor would be of use to me in discerning the nature of these beasts.

'Just be cautious when you go, ${PLAYER}. It bodes ill that our scouts are still missing. I worry very much that this particular mission will be perilous for you.''The morvul-slaves can be found defending the keep their kind has pillaged -- the Elf-ruins of Dannenglor, to the north of here.''Thank you, randir, for bringing me these. These tokens look to have been crafted by the beasts themselves, for they are very crude. This means that there is a leader among them, binding them to a life of allegiance towards defending their roost.'Darkrage wolves wander the Dourstocks, harassing the Malledhrim and their efforts. These bold creatures attack at every opportunity, then swiftly vanish into the black trees beyond the sight of the sharp-eyed Elves.Darkrage wolves can be found throughout the Dourstocks and in Audaghaim.

The Ranger Prestadír has asked you to collect the pelts of several of the evil wolves that harass the Malledhrim-guards.Collect wolf-pelts from the Darkrage wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Prestadír can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, near the abandoned village of Audaghaim.

You should bring the wolf-pelts you have collected to Prestadír, for he wishes to examine them.'Do you hear the howling from the trees, ${PLAYER}? We hear them, but we cannot see them when they wish to be scarce -- nay, not even my long-sighted Elf-friends. The Darkrage wolves of Mirkwood are vicious beasts, and their attacks upon the Malledhrim are ceaseless.

'While they are no match for the Elves of Lórien, I believe they are acting on more than instinct. They harry us day and night and seem more bent on distracting our guards and archers than coming in for an actual kill. Such prey as we are not appealing to these beasts.

'I am not sure what motivates them, but I would see them hindered. You should venture into the Dourstocks and remove the harrying threat of these sly beasts. Please bring me as many hides as you can collect, and I will examine them for anything strange. At the very least, the furs will make hardy provisions for my kindred when I return to them.''The wolves can be found all throughout the Dourstocks. If you do not find them, it is likely that they will come to find you. Keep your wits about you, ${PLAYER}! This is a deadly wood.''Ah! The skins of the Darkrage wolves! I thank you, friend. I am glad you were able to hunt so many without being hunted yourself. Now, let us see....'

Prestadír takes a hide and examines it long. It seems to be of interest to him, though you cannot perceive that it is anything extraordinary.

'Did you observe the strange pattern of the skin? There are subtle striations all over it, as if branded. I believe these beasts are in the service of the Necromancer.'Mírdiniel of the Malledhrim wishes you to search Dannenglor one last time -- this time for the most priceless remnants of the days when Elves lived there, before the merrevail took hold.The primary thief among the merrevail can be found in Dannenglor, north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should confront the morroval who hoards the priceless Elf-treasure and attempt to reclaim it for the Elves.Defeat the greedy morroval-thiefCollect the priceless Elf-treasureMírdiniel awaits you at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, south of Dannenglor.

You should bring the priceless Elf-treasure to Mírdiniel so that she may send it to be kept by the Galadhrim in Lothlórien, where it will remain safe as long as the Elves exist to watch over it.'These small treasures almost certainly came from a priceless Elven creation, a treasure beyond treasures, and a gift to the memory of the Elves who walked here once. Such a prize should not be left to be swallowed by filth and corruption.

'Once more, ${PLAYER}, I must encourage you to go on a quest for a relic of my ancient kindred. I do not think the acorn will have fallen far from the oak. I believe this greater treasure is still somewhere in Dannenglor, waiting to be reclaimed by those who will return it to its proper glory.

'Go to Dannenglor once again, if you dare. This treasure will surely not be unguarded, so go with care. You will have done a great deed for my kindred if you manage to return to me in triumph. Good fortune to you, mellon!''Dannenglor is north of here. You should search for the greedy morroval-thief there. She will surely be deep within its walls.''You have done it! This is wonderful, ${PLAYER}. I cannot believe that such a treasure has been restored to us. I will keep this safe for now and send it to Lothlórien at the next opportunity. I cannot thank you enough, mellon.'The Ranger Prestadír is very perturbed by the atmosphere around Audaghaim and is curious about the history of the town.Shades can be found in Audaghaim in the Dourstocks, just east of the Haunted Inn.

You should confront shades and see if you can find anything out about why this ruined town feels so fell.Confront shades in Audaghaim and search them for clues (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Prestadír can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, west of Audaghaim.

You should return to Prestadír with the strange tokens you collected from the shades of Audaghaim.'I, too, am interested in what you had to tell of the graveyard. I find I am ill at ease in this place, and my curiosity has been raised by your tale of the stones in the plot below. The Elves care not for the troubles of Men long departed from this world, but they hold a great interest for me.

'East of here, across the bridge, you will find a town that fell long ago. I believe it was called Audaghaim, and there are many shades there. Fell spirits of the Enemy do not trouble me, but I believe there is something more to this place, and I wish to know what it is.

'Will you confront the shades? I do not think they are wholly evil. Perhaps they bear some knowledge that will reveal what befell this place.''I do not like this feeling of unease that has settled upon my shoulders. Have you spoken to any shades?''Now, this is a bewildering find. Let me see those.'

'These coins, as you have surely noticed, are tokens of fealty to the Necromancer in Dol Guldur. They are from nearly six hundred years ago, when this simple town of woodsmen was filled with warm-blooded folk, and not the cold spirits that linger in cursed rage.

'These were gifts, and some pact was exchanged with Dol Guldur. What happened here? What cruel fate has made these people linger to fill the very air with such wicked dread?'Idhrenfair's curiosity has been roused by the grave-stones. He believes that something went amiss in this town if it is filled with such restless shades.Shades can be found in Audaghaim, east of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

Idhrenfair would like you to glean information from any shade in Audaghaim who is not hostile.Find a shade in Audaghaim who will speak with youThe Ranger Idhrenfair awaits you in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, west of Audaghaim.

You should return to Idhrenfair and convey the words of the shade to whom you spoke.Return to Idhrenfair with the evidence'It is a riddle indeed, and my curiosity is far from satisfied. While many of the shades seem hostile, surely some will not be so, if you approach them in peace. What I am proposing, ${PLAYER}, is that I hope you will make another try at uncovering the full tale behind this town.

'Cross the bridge into Audaghaim and learn if any of the spirits will have words with you. I am sure there is a story here to be unearthed. I am most interested in the blank grave-stone, but I would not be surprised if all were tied together to some strange event.

'With Dol Guldur so near, this town cannot have met a happy end.''Who are you, and why do you disturb our peaceful town? Why do you pry? We have nothing to hide. Our forest is fair, and its resources plentiful. Our folk want for naught. Leave us be!

'We are but simple woodsmen and have been so for many centuries. Many of our folk are set in their ways, but a little change has never hurt anyone. There is always room for a people to grow. And what better time could there be for us to grow and change for the better?

'The graveyard, you ask? What of it? Every mortal creature must die, and so we bury them, as is our tradition. There is nothing unusual about Audaghaim. Now move along, or you shall be sorry.''Now that is a curious tale! Some points caught my interest as you conveyed the shade's message. He spoke of fair trees, as if he still sees Mirkwood as it was before the Watchful Peace ended.

'He also mentioned that his folk were simple, but that change seemed to be imminent. Based on the years on those tombstones, it is safe to assume that the dark Lord's reclamation of his seat at Dol Guldur was the change of which he spoke.

'So the Dark Lord came, naturally. How did the Woodmen receive him? We are getting closer to an answer, but it is a shame that the shade did not offer the whole story.''There is nothing to see in Audaghaim, for we are but a simple folk. Move along, or you will be sorry indeed!''See what you can learn in Audaghaim. I am certain a brief search will be fruitful.'Mírdiniel, unconvinced by the absence of Elf-relics among the refuse in Dannenglor, desires to wrest the stolen plunder from the vile grasp of the merrevail.Merrevail can be found in large numbers at Dannenglor, the ruins north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should collect treasure from the greedy morroval beasts that hoard it.Collect relics of interest from merrevail (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mírdiniel waits in the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood, south of Dannenglor.

You should bring Mírdiniel the plunder you wrested from the merrevail of Dannenglor so that she can examine it.'This will not do. I believe that the most important treasures left behind by our brethren will be found on the merrevail themselves. You should return at once to Dannenglor and wrest what you can from the hideous beasts!

'Be very careful, for the mervyl and merrevail are deadly foes. The ruins, as you know, are fraught with peril. You should defeat enough merrevail to get a sense of what sort of treasures they bear.

'When you have collected a fair number of relics, you should bring them to me. I will be able to tell more about the Elves who were here before and perhaps discern some of the history of this place.''Have you found anything of value on the merrevail? You will find them in Dannenglor, to the north of here.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! I see that you had more success this time. I should have guessed that the filthy beasts would have kept the dearest treasures for themselves, for they have no wish to share among one another. Such is not the nature of these wicked foes.

'Why, these are interesting -- mere crumbs from the treasure that precedes them! I should dearly like to find the source; such an object would be sacred in Lórien and would be properly tended and honoured by the Elves, as it was meant to be.'The Rangers of the Grey Company seek to acquire the good will of the Uch-lûth, the Dunlending clan inhabiting Enedwaith.Wolves may be found throughout the Windfells of Enedwaith.

Andreg has asked you to hunt the wolves of the Windfells for their warm pelts, which may be used as a defence against the cold of winter.Collect wolf-pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.

Andreg told you to bring the wolf-pelts to Saeradan to be prepared for delivery to the Algraig.'${PLAYER}, welcome and well met! Because of your aid, we were able to drive back the Tarkrîp Orcs of Angmar before they could fall upon Bree!

'Now we journey south to the aid of our chieftain, Aragorn. I am certain Saeradan has told you of our needs. Will you aid us?

'Throughout the Windfells, you will find terrible wolves. Hunt the beasts and gather their pelts... these will prove beneficial against the cold of the growing winter. Bring them to me for examination, then take them to Saeradan... he will prepare them for delivery to the Algraig once he has replenished our own stores.''Wolves may be found throughout the Windfells... hunt them and bring me their pelts.''Aye, these will do perfectly, ${PLAYER}. Bring them at once to Saeradan, so he can prepare them for delivery to the Algraig.''Ah! These must be the pelts that Andreg requested of you. These will do well. Perhaps the Algraig will be persuaded to trade with us after all.'Prestadír hopes to learn more of the history of Audaghaim and determine why the former inhabitants of this town are doomed to remain.Records might be found in the town of Audaghaim, east of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks.

You should comb through the ruins of Audaghaim and try to uncover any records that may have been kept around the time of the Necromancer's influence.Search Audaghaim for town recordsPrestadír is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, west of Audaghaim.

You should show Prestadír the book you unearthed in Audaghaim.'The Dark Lord has a remarkable talent for corrupting nearly all that is good, but even he cannot doom mortal Men to remain cursed after death by association alone. Such a curse would only take hold for the deepest of betrayals, when the hearts of Men are willingly inclined to evil...only by the greatest of Powers can the spirits of Men be held to this world.

'These tokens of fealty are surely only the beginning of the story. The Necromancer persuaded his woods-dwelling neighbours to swear allegiance to him, but what after that? I have my suspicions. One hears oft of such tales.

'You should search the rubble of the town and see if any history can be found. Perhaps there are records kept by these Woodmen in the months preceding or following the intrusion of Dol Guldur.''Surely these Woodmen kept some written history of their town and its events. I wonder if we will find a record of what transpired to doom them to remain after death. You should search the ruins of Audaghaim, ${PLAYER}.''Ah! This is just what I was hoping for. I am not surprised that someone took the time to bury it. Many pages are missing, as you can see, as is the case with many aged books, but these were deliberately ripped out.

'Is it not a fine coincidence that the pages that were removed are from TA 2461, and the same week that marks the "accidental" deaths of many folks who rest in the graveyard yonder?

'I would dearly like to find those missing pages, or at least hear the account that is missing from this book.'The Elf Nífdir is moved by the unhappy state of the Mirk-huorns and the tale of their slow loss of hope. He wishes to do something to alleviate their sadness and despair.Menassiel can be found at Cerin Amroth in Lothlórien.

You should speak with Menassiel and see if she will gift the Huorns of Mirkwood with a young mallorn, a light to dispel the shadows upon their wretched existence.Talk to Menassiel at Cerin AmrothNífdir is at his camp in the Drownholt, west of the Malledhrim outpost of Estolad Mernael.

You should return to Nífdir to show him the seedling donated by Menassiel.'I can think of one small gesture that might do some good. The mallorn trees of Lothlórien, thriving under the power of Galadriel and the care of the Galadhrim, inspire all who harbour love for the wilderness. The mallorns will resist stain as long as the Elves are here to tend them.

'I want you to go to my friend Menassiel in Lothlórien, at Cerin Amroth. Surely her heart will be moved by your tale, as mine is. I would like to plant a mallorn sapling here, in this glade. It will give hope to the Huorns. I do not think it will fully quell their wrath, but it has been long since they have seen any light. They deserve a glimmer of hope, for someday the shadows of Dol Guldur will trouble this place no more.

'Go to Menassiel now, ${PLAYER}, and see if she will help you.''You indeed tell a sad story, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for offering to return to that dangerous place for so generous a deed. Not many outsiders love the trees as much as we Galadhrim do.

'I only hope that I do not send this child to its death in that forsaken swamp. Please see that it is cared for, if you pass it by. It has some power to spread its light and dispel the cruel corruptions of Mirkwood, but...nay, I will trust to hope. The power of Galadriel is in the very sap of this young one.

'Return to the glade if you dare, ${PLAYER}, and plant this seed. See that none disturb it.''Bring this little seedling to Nífdir, mellon. It is my gift to the aged trees who live in despair. I hope it brings them light, as the mallorns have done for us also.''Menassiel stands near Cerin Amroth, in Lothlórien. You should go to her and see if she will help us.''You have returned! I am glad. Let me see what Menassiel has given us.'Most of the kindling immediately surrounding Estolad Mernael is very damp and causes the camp-fires to smoke and burn badly. Dry wood must be sought in other parts of the Drownholt's swampy terrain.Dry branches for kindling can be found throughout the Drownholt where the ground is a little higher, due west of Estolad Mernael.

You should collect dry branches for the Elves at Estolad Mernael.Collect dry branches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rocheledh is in Estolad Mernael in the Drownholt, tending his sick horse.

You should bring the dry branches for kindling to Rocheledh, who will be grateful for the cleaner camp-fires.'How these fires smoke! How can this poor steed recover when the air is filled with putrid fumes from this polluted kindling? This will not do....

'The firewood we have collected around this camp has been completely soaked through with vile swamp-water and dries poorly in this climate. It burns through far too quickly, and we must tend it constantly. The smoke is terrible, as you see!

'I saw a rise to the west of here where some thick trees seemed to grow in a great cluster. Would you be so good as to search there for dry kindling? You may be able to find some on that higher ground. It would be a great help to us.''Search on higher ground to the west of our camp. Hopefully some better firewood can be collected there.''Thank you, randir! These branches will burn much better than the soggy, rotting logs we picked up around here. This place will be a little more hospitable to us now.'Despite its reputation, Bingo wants to see within Mirkwood forest, but the Elves of Lothlórien are beginning an assault on Dol Guldur and do not wish to endanger the hobbit.Faelleron is beneath a flet on the north-western edge of the Golden Wood, near the border with Fanuidhol.

Bingo wants to prove that he is not afraid of Orcs, and wants you to volunteer the two of you to fight the foes of Lórien in Fanuidhol.Talk to Faelleron in north-west LothlórienYou have agreed to fight the Orcs in Fanuidhol, north-west of Lothlórien, for Faelleron.Defeat Orcs or goblins in Fanuidhol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Faelleron is south-east of Fanuidhol, on the border of Lothlórien.

You have defeated some of the Orcs that threaten the Golden Wood, and should now return to Faelleron.Talk to Faelleron on the north-west border of the Golden WoodBingo is south-east of Fanuidhol, on the border of Lothlórien, with Faelleron.

You have defeated some of the Orcs that threaten the Golden Wood, and should now return to Bingo.Talk to Bingo on the north-west border of the Golden Wood, near FaelleronCalengoth is at the docks of Lothlórien, west of Imlad Lalaith.

You have attained the permission to fight the enemies of Lothlórien for which Bingo hoped, and now he wants you to show it to Calengoth at the docks.Bingo has obtained permission to follow the Golden Host into Mirkwood. Now you should gain access to Mirkwood by completing 'Book 9, Foreword: The Dark Shore' by speaking to Calengoth at the docks in Lothlórien and completing his quest chain through 'Hilltop Assault.'Gain access to Mirkwood by completing 'Book 9, Foreword: The Dark Shore' by speaking to Calengoth and completing his quest chain through 'Hilltop Assault.'Bingo has arrived in Mirkwood, and he has naturally gone to the first tavern he could find: the Haunted Inn of the Dourstocks, west of Audaghaim.Find Bingo Boffin within the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks.Bingo has asked you to find a number of locations near the Haunted Inn and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> at them closely to help him learn about the area.Bingo is by the fire inside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks.Talk to Bingo inside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks'I have been reading some of those books you brought me, ${PLAYER}, but I have to confess that this bench is not the most secluded of spots, and I have overheard a number of interesting conversations from this perch! It appears that the Elves have begun to mount an offensive on an evil stronghold in Mirkwood, and even now they begin to seize footholds on the other side of the river.

'Now, I am not keen on participating in any battles, but I do believe that it is my authorial responsibility to see the inside of Mirkwood if my book is to be complete. I spoke with an Elf named Calengoth at the docks, but he refused my request that I be allowed across the river! He said he would not be responsible for my safety. Can you believe that?

'Well, I have had a capital idea! If we can prove that I am not afraid of Orcs, Calengoth will have no choice but to recognize that I deserve to cross the river! I have heard that Orcs have invaded an area in the north-western reaches of the Golden Wood, and that an Elf named Faelleron needs help to combat them. Let us find him and volunteer to help!''I am not keen on participating in any battles, but I do believe that it is my authorial responsibility to see the inside of Mirkwood if my book is to be complete. I spoke with an Elf named Calengoth at the docks, but he refused my request that I be allowed across the river! He said he would not be responsible for my safety. Can you believe that?

'Well, I have had a capital idea! If we can prove that I am not afraid of Orcs, Calengoth will have no choice but to recognize that I deserve to cross the river! I have heard that Orcs have invaded an area in the north-western reaches of the Golden Wood, and that an Elf named Faelleron needs help to combat them. Let us find him and volunteer to help!''This is Faelleron. Tell him that I am not afraid of Orcs, and I would love to prove it to him!''You are the companion of Bingo Boffin? He is an amusing fellow, and insists that he is not afraid of Orcs. He asked me to write this note granting him permission to fight our foes, and I have complied, though on some level I must doubt whether this is wise!

'Here is the parchment. May it put his mind at rest, and if you will fight the Orcs in Fanuidhol, to the north, this simple act of script may prove worth the time and the ink!''I gave you a note granting permission to Bingo Boffin to fight the Orcs. Now go north-west to Fanuidhol and do so!''We showed those Orcs a thing or two, that's for sure!''Well done, my friends! I am pleased that you have returned from your campaign against the Orcs in good health and with victory. It seems you did not really need my permission at all, but I am glad to have granted it all the same.''I am pleased that you have returned from your campaign against the Orcs in good health and with victory. It seems you did not really need my permission at all, but I am glad to have granted it all the same.''We did it, ${PLAYER}, we did it, and we also made certain the Orcs that threaten the Golden Wood know it to be well-defended by adventuring types such as ourselves!'

Bingo lowers his voice conspiratorially.

'And did you notice? The note that Faelleron wrote for us says that we have permission to engage with the enemies of Lothlórien, but it does not specify WHERE those enemies are to be found! Bring that parchment to Calengoth at the docks, and he will have no choice but to bring me across the river into Mirkwood!''The note that Faelleron wrote for us says that we have permission to engage with the enemies of Lothlórien, but it does not specify WHERE those enemies are to be found! Bring that parchment to Calengoth at the docks, and he will have no choice but to bring me across the river into Mirkwood!''I am sorry, but I told your friend that the Golden Host is beginning a dangerous assault, and I will not be responsible for his well-being. He would be better served remaining behind and writing in relative safety. What is this?'

You hand Calengoth the note from Faelleron, and he looks at it with surprise.

'Well, I cannot say I agree with Faelleron's assessment, but this parchment does relieve me of any responsibility should anything happen to Bingo within the forest. I will no longer prevent him from crossing into Mirkwood, but know that you will need to survive the landing and do as the Golden Host commands before Bingo will be free to explore.''I cannot say I agree with Faelleron's assessment, but this parchment does relieve me of any responsibility should anything happen to Bingo within the forest. I will no longer prevent him from crossing into Mirkwood, but know that you will need to survive the landing and do as the Golden Host commands before Bingo will be free to explore.''I am ready to begin the journey into Mirkwood, ${PLAYER}!''What excitement, ${PLAYER}! The Golden Host and the Rangers have crossed into Mirkwood and they are making their way toward a frightful-sounding stronghold in the south-east. I am glad to have seen within the woods, but I think I will leave a survey of this Dol Guldur to the experts!

'Instead, I think I will stay here by the fire and work on my book. This is not the most welcoming of taverns, but at least it is warm! I do wonder about the history of this place, though. This is one of the few buildings that seems to still be intact. Why not go explore the rest of the town, and report back to me when you have seen the sights? I will be here!'

<rgb=#00FF00>Bert Bartleby has arrived outside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood.</rgb>'I think I will stay here by the fire and work on my book. This is not the most welcoming of taverns, but at least it is warm! I do wonder about the history of this place, though. This is one of the few buildings that seems to still be intact. Why not go explore the rest of the town, and report back to me when you have seen the sights? I will be here!''Hmm, your description of the areas nearby make them sound much as I expected, ${PLAYER}: tumbled down and in disrepair. Folk have not lived in this town for a very long time, and it feels to me that unhappiness lies upon it like a shroud.

'While you were gone I spoke with one of the Rangers, Aduiallin, and she gave me a lovely book of recipes. Perhaps I will work to bring some measure of cheer and comfort to this tavern by preparing one of the recipes from this book. Yes, that will be just the thing! But I will need to choose one to make, and that will not be an easy task!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'First, Breakfast!' (Recommended Level: 66)</rgb>Lomdognir has asked you to take a vital message to one of his compatriots in the Dourstocks.The first milestone is along the road west of Emyn Lûm.

Lomdognir laid out a specific route he needs you to take with the message you are carrying.Head for the first milestoneThe second milestone lies further along the road west of Emyn Lûm.

Lomdognir laid out a specific route he needs you to take with the message you are carrying.Head for the second milestoneThe third milestone lies along the road where it turns north towards the abandoned village in Dourstocks.

Lomdognir laid out a specific route he needs you to take with the message you are carrying.Head for the third milestoneLaeginn is stationed in the inn at Audaghaim in the Dourstocks.

Lomdognir has instructed you to hand the message over to the Elf Laeginn.'Something important has transpired, and I need a message taken to our outpost in the Dourstocks as quickly as possible, ${PLAYER}.

'Are you willing to act as our courier in this matter? I will warn you that I need it run by a very specific route -- one that may be watched by the Enemy, who may attempt to intercept you. It is very important that you fight your way through any obstacles they offer, and get there in time.

There are a series of milestones along the road between here and the ruined village in the Dourstocks, pass each of these as you travel there.

'When you arrive, turn the message over to Laeginn -- he will know what to do with it.''Do not misundertand me, ${PLAYER}, I expect you to face dangers along the way -- you may even find yourself walking into a trap -- but you must win through regardless. Your role to play in this battle is no less than mine or any other's as we face this darkness.

'Now be off, quickly!''Do not misundertand me, ${PLAYER}, I expect you to face dangers along the way -- you may even find yourself walking into a trap -- but you must win through regardless. Your role to play in this battle is no less than mine or any other's as we face this darkness.

'Now be off, quickly!''Do not misundertand me, ${PLAYER}, I expect you to face dangers along the way -- you may even find yourself walking into a trap -- but you must win through regardless. Your role to play in this battle is no less than mine or any other's as we face this darkness.

'Now be off, quickly!''Do not misundertand me, ${PLAYER}, I expect you to face dangers along the way -- you may even find yourself walking into a trap -- but you must win through regardless. Your role to play in this battle is no less than mine or any other's as we face this darkness.

'Now be off, quickly!''What is this? A message from Ost Galadh? I shall see to it right away.

'I am glad to see that you made it here swiftly and unharmed. Give Lomdognir my regards and tell him I have matters well in hand here.'Penlhun Brehur, one of the leaders of Nan Laeglin, has asked you if you know of any way to repair the dwarf-axe handed down to him from his father. The axe was forged in Thrór's Coomb, and it is rumoured that at least one dwarf remains among the ruins. Alternatively, if you are a weaponsmith of considerable skill you might try a hand at repairing it yourself.Aedh may be found in the crafting hall.

You should speak with Aedh to learn if there is any way to reforge Penlhun's axe.Talk to Aedh at the Lhanuch crafting hallThe mad dwarf dwells somewhere in the mountains surrounding Thrór's Coomb, far to the east of Lhanuch.

Aedh told you to seek out a mad dwarf in the valley of Thrór's Coomb and see if he can repair Penlhun's axe. Alternatively, if you are a master weaponsmith, you might attempt to repair the axe yourself at the forge in Lhanuch.Penlhun Brehur is at the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch, far to the west of Thrór's Coomb.

You should return to Penlhun with his father's axe.'Tell me, Duvodiad, is it true that the powers of Angmar stir anew? Have the Elves truly allied with the Witch-king in the North as the tales say? Some weeks ago, warriors from the South under the direction of Isengard passed by to do battle in Eregion, but we have heard little but dark rumour since.

'No matter the details, war shall be upon us soon... you mark my words. Would that my father's axe was yet true, I would be unafraid of battle! It was made by the dwarves back when Thrór's folk lived in the mountains, but time takes its toll on all things, and it broke some years ago. None here have the skill to reforge such a weapon, but it is said that the dwarves yet remain in the far north and have shared some secrets of craft with the Men there as well.

'I was thinking that if this is true, then I might have the axe re-made. What of it, Duvodiad? Do you know the secrets of the craft or perhaps know a dwarf who might reforge my father's blade? Take it, if so. It is of no use to me now, and my brethren would have me melt it down to make a less worthy blade. I would not see it end so if it might be made whole again. If it can be done, then I shall be in your debt and shall speak in your favour at the Council of Brehur.''Would that my father's axe were whole once more....''Penlhun gave you this? I will tell you what I told him. I cannot repair it.

'I do not know how Thrór's smiths forged it to such a temper, but anything I could do to it would make the steel so brittle that it would shatter at the first blow.

'You want this weapon repaired? Go to Thrór's Coomb. There is rumour that a mad dwarf lives there still among the ruins. Perhaps he can repair it.'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you have Master proficiency in the Weaponsmith profession, you may repair the axe yourself using the anvil in the Lhanuch crafting hall.</rgb>'Talk to the mad dwarf if you want that axe repaired!''This is a dwarf-axe! Whence did you steal it? From a Man?

'Where did the Man get it? From his father? This man's father was a dwarf? Well, you should have said so to begin with! I will gladly repair this for my half-brother!

'This shouldn't take long... here you go!''Tell Penlhun's father Nár sends his greetings... a good dwarf, he is. Or was? He is a dwarf, yes?''My father's axe! It is nearly as sound as the day he brought it from the dwarves!

'You have my thanks, Duvodiad. I shall do what I can to dissuade Glynn Brenin from aiding Isengard.

'We of the Uch-lûth should be our own people, not servants of some power-hungry wizard....'Agorin, the record-keeper of the Malledhrim, has asked you to foray into the Wild Ruins and collect notes on the ancient Sylvan records scattered among the ruins there.The Wild Ruins lie to the south of Ost Galadh.

Agorin has asked you to examine and record the records of the Silvan Elves of Ost Galadh in the Wild Ruins.Examine Silvan records (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Agorin is at Ost Galadh, north of the Wild Ruins.

You should return to Agorin at and tell her what you discovered about the records of the Silvan Elves that once inhabited this place.Talk to Agorin at Ost Galadh'${PLAYER}, when you next wander the ruins about Ost Galadh, please keep an eye for any old plaques or engravings that might remain? There must be some left, and my hope is to record their lore as we knew it in the days before we left this place to the wilds.

'This may mark my last chance to do so before we withdraw back to Lothlórien -- and likely before I myself head into the far West -- but my duties compel me to remain within this encampment, and I dare not venture forth against Fuirgam's command!

'I beseech you...would you venture forth into the ruins and make record of any engravings you find within? They would be of great interest to me and my fellow scholars, and who knows when or if we might ever look upon them again?''Ah, so I was right, there were some remaining records of the old settlement. I have no time to pore over these now, or Fuirgam will be cross with me, but I thank you for your efforts.

'Fuirgam himself once lived here in Ost Galadh, before it was left to the forest. Alas, the memories of those who left this place seem dark and difficult, and I have yet to find one who will speak at any length of it, and so these words of stone provide my only window to the past of this place.

'One day I will catch Fuirgam in a more talkative mood and obtain the whole story, but he is oft reticent, and it might be another Age before I pull it out of him. That is assuming of course that any of us do not find ourselves in Valinor prematurely....''Would that I could have shown you this place when it was still called Greenwood the Great by Men and dwarves! It was as wonderous and beautiful as any city my brethren among the Silvan Elves had built, a fair reflection for grand Lórien in those days.

'Now it is....

'I would be alone now, please.'Culang has assigned you the task of finding a number of hidden supply caches scattered throughout Nan Laeglin. If you can uncover these caches, the Grey Company will be able to pass through the land swiftly without having to risk bartering with potentially hostile locals.The cache is somewhere a short distance north-west of Lhanuch where you can see a small set of curious ruins. You should be able to find the Rangers' rune on an overlook above them.

Culang has sent you to find a cache of arrows, which can be found sixty paces south of a Rangers' rune.The cache of arrows is buried about sixty paces directly south of the Rangers' rune, along the base of a small cliff there.

Culang asked you to find a hidden cache of arrows.Culang is at his camp in Nan Laeglin, south-east of the cache.

You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the arrows hidden there. Now you should return with them to Culang.'In these days, previously tranquil lands are now fraught with danger and enemies at every turn. Already, we have expended most of the arrows we brought with us.

'I need you to find a hunter's cache that was put aside some years ago, should we find ourselves in need. Within it, you will find a considerable supply of arrows and spare bow-strings, both of which we are now in sore need of.

'The cache is a short distance north-west of Lhanuch, within sight of a small set of curious ruins. A rune can be found on an overlook above the ruins. Once you have found it, make your way sixty paces south and search near the base of a small cliff there.''We need that cache of arrows, ${PLAYER}.''We need that cache of arrows, ${PLAYER}.''Good, ${PLAYER}. That is a fair bundle of arrows and strings. It ought to last us until we reach the southern border of Dunland...it will have to.'Culang has assigned you the task of finding a number of hidden caches of supplies scattered throughout Nan Laeglin. If you can uncover these supplies, the Grey Company will be able to pass through swiftly without as having to resort to bartering with possibly hostile locals or stopping to hunt.The cache of bandages he says is hidden east of Lhanuch. The rune-marker should be carved on a solitary tree somewhere directly east of the Lhanuch.

Culang has sent you to retrieve a hidden cache of bandages.The cache of bandages is buried in a small copse of trees directly north-east of the rune.

Culang asked you to retrieve a hidden cache of bandages.Culang is at his camp in Nan Laeglin, to the south of the cache.

You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the bandages hidden there. Now you should return with them to Culang.'We need to be ready for anything, and there are some supplies we were unable to gather before our hasty departure. Among them is a decent supply of bandages for the wounded.

'However, there is a traveller's cache laid in not far from here, if you are willing to try and retrieve it. I believe the rune-marker can be found carved on a solitary tree directly east of Lhanuch.

'Once you have found the marker, the cache itself should be buried in a small copse of trees directly to the north-east.''We need those bandages, ${PLAYER}.''We need those bandages, ${PLAYER}.''In endeavours such as these, it is inevitable that some among us will be wounded. These bandages have been steeped in potent herbs that help ward off infection and speed the healing of such wounds.'The road east of Ost Galadh is the most direct route to the fortress of Dol Guldur.Upright stones can be found along the sloping road to Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh.

Enedhel has asked you to hide behind upright stones on the road to Minas Gîl in order to learn how closely the eastern way to Dol Guldur is being watched by the Orcs.Hide behind upright stones on the road to Minas Gîl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enedhel is within Ost Galadh, in Emyn Lûm.

You have hidden behind the upright stones on the road to Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh, and should return now to Enedhel with what you have learned.Talk to Enedhel at Ost Galadh'You have come to Ost Galadh, ${PLAYER}, where the Golden Host prepares for the next leg of its journey. Is the road of the Malledhrim also the road of the Hidden Guard? I do not know if it should be, but if it must we shall learn at least what dangers lie along it!

'Travel east of Ost Galadh and keep your eyes open for enemies on the road. As the road climbs towards Minas Gîl, there are upright stones on one side of the path. Perhaps you can hide behind these stones and learn what the Orc-presence may be in Emyn Lûm.''The eastern way to Dol Guldur may be watched by the Orcs, ${PLAYER}. Travel east of Ost Galadh and hide behind the upright stones that line the way to Minas Gîl. You may learn something of the Orc-presence in Emyn Lûm.''I see, ${PLAYER}. It would appear that the Orcs are indeed watching the road through Emyn Lûm very closely. What is safe for the Golden Host then is not safe for the errand of the Hidden Guard.

'I cannot recommend this way to Cúcheron. The Hidden Guard must find another way to Dol Guldur... a secret way. Passage through Emyn Lûm is too closely watched.'The Orcs have a strong presence in Taur Morvith.Krul Lugu is the Orkish name for a pair of Orc-fortifications in the centre of Taur Morvith, south of the Verdant Shrine.

Erymbes has asked you to investigate the Orc presence at Krul Lugu and to then find her friend Malendol.Assess the Orc-presence at Krul LuguMalendol may be somewhere in or around the Orc-fortifications of Krul Lugu, in Taur Morvith.

You have assessed the Orc-presence at Krul Lugu and should now search for Malendol, who may be in trouble.Find Malendol in or around Krul LuguErymbes is at the Verdant Shrine, north of the Orc-camps of Krul Lugu, in Taur Morvith.

You have scouted the Orc-camps of Krul Lugu and defended Malendol and should return now to Erymbes with what you have learned.Talk to Erymbes at the Verdant Shrine'There are a number of Orc-camps in Taur Morvith, ${PLAYER}. I do not know if the southern way is the ideal road for the Hidden Guard to take to Dol Guldur. My friend Malendol headed south to investigate, but he has not returned.

'If you will travel south and scout the pair of Orc-forts there, you may find some sign of my friend. If the Orc-presence is so great as to cause him trouble, it is certainly too dangerous for the Hidden Guard to bring Mazog this way.

'It is to be hoped that Malendol is not in Krul Lugu itself, but you should start your search there, in case the worst has happened.''Thank you for scouting the Orc-camps of Krul Lugu and for coming to the aid of Malendol, ${PLAYER}.

'With what you have to say about the Orc-presence in Taur Morvith, it must be my recommendation to the Hidden Guard that the southern route to Dol Guldur is not safe. Bringing the Orc Mazog this way would be ill-advised indeed.

'They must find some other way to the fortress, a way that preserves the secrecy of their errand.''I want you to assess the Orc-presence at Krul Lugu, the Orc-fortifications located to the south, in the very centre of Taur Morvith, and to then search for my friend Malendol.''You must search for my friend Malendol in or around the Orc-fortifications of Krul Lugu, to the south, in the very centre of Taur Morvith. He may be in trouble!''${PLAYER}, have you come from Krul Lugu? I went to scout those Orc-camps, but more Orcs came marching out of the east, from Dol Guldur, and I could not rejoin Erymbes in the north. I have been resting to regain my power before attempting to make my way there.

'I am not yet at my full strength, and more Orcs are coming up from the south. You must help me!'The spiders of the Scuttledells pose a danger to all who pass through, but it remains to be determined how great a threat they are to the Hidden Guard.Spiders can be found throughout the Scuttledells.

Gladiel has asked you to gather venom from the spiders of the Scuttledells by using the cloth she gave you.Collect venom samples from spiders in the Scuttledells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gladiel is by the Shrine of the Ancient One, in the Scuttledells.

You have collected a number of venom samples from the spiders of the Scuttledells and should return them to Gladiel so she can examine them.'Hail, ${CLASS}, and well-met indeed, for I have seen naught but spiders and black dogs for three days now, and it is good to speak with an ally at last. A great gloom hangs over this corner of the wood, likely emanating from the barrows just to the north of here; no one has tended those barrows for an age, and they are home now to evils only... and the spiders are everywhere!

'I cannot recommend that the Hidden Guard come this way until we know for sure how deadly the venom of these spiders may be. It seems that the eyes of Dol Guldur are not watching the Scuttledells, but that will be no relief to any of our company who fall to the spiders in the name of secrecy!

'Take this cloth, and use it to gather the venom from slain spiders here in the Scuttledells; I will see how perilous it may be.''Use the cloth I gave you to collect samples of venom from the spiders of the Scuttledells, and I will determine how dangerous this road may be for the Hidden Guard.''Let me see the samples of venom you have collected using the cloth I gave to you, ${PLAYER}.

'In such small quantities as you would encounter with a single spider, this venom will make you ill, but should have no lasting effects. Large doses of the venom would be more serious, of course, but I can recommend passage through the Scuttledells to the Elves of the Hidden Guard, as long as they can limit exposure to large numbers of these spiders as they pass.'The Elves of the Hidden Guard have run into a difficulty: with the death of Raddir, none of them know for sure what route he had planned by which to bring them to Dol Guldur in secret.The Elves of the Hidden Guard can be found within the cellar of the Haunted Inn.

Bróin has asked you to speak with the Elves of the Hidden Guard about what must be done next.Cúcheron is outside the Haunted Inn, located among the Dourstocks.

You have obtained the opinions of the Elves of the Hidden Guard concerning what route to take to Dol Guldur and have received three different proposals.Talk to Cúcheron at the Haunted InnThree scouts have been sent into the Scuttledells, Emyn Lûm, and Taur Morvith.

Cúcheron has asked you to speak with the Elves he sent to investigate the areas along the proposed routes of the Hidden Guard. Gladiel is in the Scuttledells, west of the Shrine of the Ancient One, near the border of Gathbúrz. Erymbes is in Taur Morvith, by the Verdant Shrine, south of the Wild Ruin. Enedhel is in Ost Galadh.Aid Enedhel in Ost Galadh, in Emyn LûmAid Erymbes in Taur MorvithAid Gladiel in the ScuttledellsCúcheron is outside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks.

You have done as Cúcheron asked by gathering information on the possible routes toward Dol Guldur and should now return to him.Talk to Cúcheron at the Haunted InnIssuriel is within the cellar of the Haunted Inn, located among the Dourstocks.

Based on the information you have provided, Cúcheron has decided that Issuriel's proposed route to Dol Guldur has the greatest chance of success. He wants you to inform her that this is the way the Hidden Guard will take.Talk to Issuriel in the Haunted Inn'The death of the Elf Raddir has made uncertain the fate of this journey, ${PLAYER}, for none of the Elves know by which way he planned to bring us in secret to Dol Guldur.

'Speak with the Elves here in the cellar and try to decide on the proper course. Someone must step forward and take charge, or it will be next winter before we advance even a single step...and who knows what will befall Bori in the meantime?''This is as I expected, ${PLAYER}: ask three Elves which way is best to take, and you will receive three answers, each different.

'We have little time left to waste. I want you to scout these proposed roads, my accommodating ${CLASS}, and assess the dangers along each.

'Perhaps that will aid with our decision. Seek the scouts we sent to the Scuttledells, Emyn Lûm, and Taur Morvith and question them about the dangers they have encountered.''I have decided what we must do, ${PLAYER}. The path through Taur Morvith would bring us too near the Orc-camps in that valley, and we are certain the direct way through Emyn Lûm, along which the Golden Host will march, is already being watched. No, our path lies through the Scuttledells. It will be dangerous, but that will itself serve as a cloak for spying eyes.

'Speak with Issuriel in the cellar of this inn and tell her I have chosen her suggested path.''Raddir brought us into the Drownholt despite the danger for a reason, ${PLAYER}. He must have planned for us to take the southernmost way towards Dol Guldur and to bring us in secret up to the southern base of the rocky spire upon which the fortress stands.

'We should therefore head south through the stony reaches of Taur Morvith. That is the way Raddir wanted us to go, I am sure of it.

'The other members of the company may disagree, but we must at least set out, or his death will have been for naught!''I do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}. I believe Raddir thought to approach Dol Guldur by the ways least likely to be watched by the forces of the Enemy, but our excursion into the Drownholt....

'I have to believe that Raddir knew what he was doing, ${PLAYER}, and that he knew the risks. But still he took us into the Drownholt; he must have had a good reason.

'The Enemy would never expect us to take the road through the Scuttledells, for that place has a dangerous reputation. That is the path of greatest secrecy, and only through the Scuttledells will we come to Dol Guldur with our prisoner and our presence unannounced.''I see, ${PLAYER}. I do not know if I should be pleased that our path will bring us into the Scuttledells, but my heart tells me this is the way we must go.

'There is one more thing, ${PLAYER}. I hesitate to mention it, but something has been bothering me for a while now....''We cannot wait here for a revelation that may not come, ${PLAYER}: we will never know what road Raddir intended for us to take.

'No, we must decide and decide quickly. The quick road will be the safest road. Let us move directly eastward to Dol Guldur by the straightest way; Raddir believed our greatest strength was in secrecy, but the dangerous path through the Drownholt cost him his life.

'Let us be done with secret ways. The straightest course, like a swift arrow, is the one we should now take if we wish to avoid a similar fate.''We sent scouts ahead of us, ${PLAYER}, as we are wont to do; seek them in the wild places and ask them what dangers they have discovered. Find them in the Scuttledells, Emyn Lûm, and Taur Morvith.''Issuriel is in the cellar of this inn. Tell her I have decided that the path of the Hidden Guard must lead through the Scuttledells, dangerous though it will be.''These Elves have to come to an agreement on what next to do, ${PLAYER}, or we will waste even more time in idleness!''As I expected, the Elves cannot agree on this, and no one member of this company has the power to simply say what route they will take!

'Leave the Haunted Inn and tell Cúcheron the opinions of the Elves...and tell him, too, that we cannot waste any more time in idleness!''We should head south through the stony reaches of Taur Morvith. That is the way Raddir wanted us to go, I am sure of it.''The Enemy would never expect us to take the road through the Scuttledells, for that place has a dangerous reputation. That is the path of greatest secrecy, and only through the Scuttledells will we come to Dol Guldur with our prisoner and our presence unannounced.''Let us be done with secret ways. The straightest course, like a swift arrow, is the one we should now take if we wish to avoid a similar fate.'Issuriel is concerned by the great feeling of dread that hangs over the abandoned village of Audaghaim and by the strange things the Elves have seen there.Nervous Malledhrim can be found throughout Audaghaim.

Issuriel has asked you to reassure nervous Malledhrim throughout Audaghaim that all will be well, despite the disturbing things they have seen at this abandoned village.Issuriel is in the cellar of the Haunted Inn, in Audaghaim.

You have reassured a number of nervous Malledhrim and should return to Issuriel.Talk to Issuriel at the Haunted Inn'Surely you have noticed the feeling of dread that hangs over portions of Audaghaim, ${PLAYER}. I did not think much of it when we arrived, but my unease has grown, and now others are reporting seeing strange spectres throughout the town.

'Can you put my mind at ease, friend? I would ask you to speak with some of the Elves throughout Audaghaim about the disturbing things they have seen and to reassure them that all will be well. We cannot tarry here much longer, but I want the nervous Malledhrim among us to know that we are safe while we must stay.''This abandoned village has me on edge as well, ${PLAYER}, so I can understand why our friends are nervous. There is something about Audaghaim that makes me uneasy.''I am ready to leave this place, ${PLAYER}. I have seen ghostly shapes in the half-light, vague images around corners and among the trees here in Audaghaim.'

You offer comforting words to the nervous Elf, and he thanks you for taking the time. Suddenly, his eyes widen in alarm.'Do you sense it, ${PLAYER}? I cannot shake the feeling that there is something very wrong happening in the ruins of this village. I was looking out over the waterfall, and a great wave of dread washed over me. I do not know what it was, but I did not linger.'

You reassure him with comforting words, and he appears to feel better.'All of my friends are on edge, reporting strange visions just on the edge of sight. We cannot move on from Audaghaim quickly enough for me!'

You reassure her with kind words, and she thanks you for taking the time to comfort her.'Speak with some of the Elves throughout Audaghaim about the disturbing things that they have seen and reassure them that all will be well. We cannot tarry here much longer, but I want the nervous Malledhrim among us to know we are safe while we must stay.'Issuriel and the Elves of the Hidden Guard are now ready to bring Mazog on the next stage of the journey to Dol Guldur: a perilous route through the Scuttledells.Issuriel is inside the cellar of the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks.

The time has come for the Hidden Guard to journey into the Scuttledells with Mazog. Issuriel is awaiting your word that you are ready to begin.Talk to Issuriel and travel along Râd Iorist with the Hidden GuardAchardor is in Gadorgar, a storage room within the ruins of Ost Galadh.

The journey through the Scuttledells proved disastrous: both Mazog and Issuriel have been poisoned by the lethal venom gwigael. Achardor is raging and must be calmed.Talk to Achardor in Ost GaladhBróin is in Gadorgar, a storage room within the ruins of Ost Galadh.

Achardor is at the end of his temper, and it will require a great deal to keep him from slaying Mazog in his frustration. Bróin wishes to reason with him.Talk to Bróin in Ost GaladhIssuriel is in Gadorgar, a storage room within the ruins of Ost Galadh.

Weakened by the effects of the gwigael, Issuriel has something to say about the mission of the Hidden Guard.Talk to Issuriel in Ost Galadh'Now that the decision has been made, my mind is more at ease, ${PLAYER}: our path to Dol Guldur will run through the Scuttledells, dangerous though it be, for only by that way can our errand remain a secret; and secrecy is our greatest weapon.

'Let me know when you are ready to make the journey, and we will leave for Râd Iorist, the route we have chosen.''It does not matter, ${PLAYER}. The errand has failed. Even were we now to come to the gates of Dol Guldur, we would possess only a body to exchange. Mazog will not be alive at the end of the journey.

'Our chance of saving Bori dies with Mazog. The Hidden Guard? They cannot guard even themselves!'Issuriel coughs weakly and struggles to speak.

'I...do not...want the Hidden Guard...to fail. Mazog...Mazog cannot die.''This cannot have gone worse, ${PLAYER}! This terrible misadventure will have claimed another life by sunrise, and we are no closer to accomplishing it and being done with this foolish errand!

'I care not for Mazog -- let the gwigael wrack his body until its ending, and we shall all be better off -- but the wounding of Issuriel I cannot tolerate and will not!

'I would slay a thousand spiders were it to mean saving poor Issuriel, but I shall slay a single Orc should she die on this ill-omened journey!''Had I the chance to live this mission again, I would not attempt it, ${PLAYER}. Too many have died, Elf and dwarf alike, and that knowledge lies heavily upon my shoulders.''Are you ready to leave? The Scuttledells are full of danger, and it will be no small thing to come through them to the other side in safety.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>'Your words are no balm for my anger! You can say nothing that will change my mind!''How many of my friends must die before we abandon this ridiculous journey? A plague on the Iron Garrison and their stiff necks!'Issuriel knows of someone who can brew an antidote for the gwigael poison, but the components are so rare that it is only realistic to expect a single dose.The Sereglos flower grows for a short span of time on untended barrows in Mirkwood. Unmarked venom sacs from Saewathel or Blackvenom spiders, of the breeds related to the spider that poisoned Mazog and Issuriel may be found throughout the Scuttledells, north of Ost Galadh.

Time is short: if the errand of the Hidden Guard is to succeed, Issuriel demands that you gather the components of an antidote to cure Mazog of the gwigael poison.Collect a rare Sereglos flowerCollect unmarked Saewathel venom-sacIssuriel is within the makeshift camp in the storage room Gadorgar, inside Ost Galadh, south of the Scuttledells.

You have found the rare ingredients for the antidote Issuriel mentioned and should return to her with them at once.Barvessain is somewhere in Ost Galadh, in Emyn Lûm, south of the Scuttledells.

Issuriel has weakly asked you to find Barvessain, somewhere in Ost Galadh, and to get her to brew the antidote for the gwigael poison from the components you collected.Mazog and Issuriel are both within Gadorgar, the makeshift storage room in Ost Galadh.

You now have a single dose of Laidhris antidote and must give it to one of the victims of the Gwigael poison.Achardor is in Gadorgar, the makeshift storage room in Ost Galadh.

You have given the antidote to Mazog, and Achardor is not pleased.Talk to Achardor at Ost GaladhGruingalas is outside the door to Gadorgar, in Ost Galadh.

Archardor wants no one coming into Gadorgar anymore, in order for Issuriel to rest. He also wants the scouts recalled in preparation for the exchange of Mazog and has asked you to tell Gruingalas of these requests.Talk to Gruingalas at Ost Galadh'I know of... an antidote. The ingredients are very rare... but....'

Issuriel winces, clearly in a great deal of pain. When she has recovered enough to speak, she weakly continues.

'I need an unmarked venom sac from... the same brood of spider, Saewathel, or Blackvenom... and a flower. The flower Sereglos grows upon untended barrows... in Mirkwood. It blooms only for a few days... in the year... and dies. There may not... be any remaining... this season....'

She gasps for air and is silent.'A Sereglos flower... I have heard tales of them, but they are so rare and bloom so infrequently that I cannot say I have ever seen one.

'There are barrows just to the north of here, and they cannot have been tended for an age. Is it beyond hope to think a Sereglos flower might grow upon one of them?''The Sereglos flower... grows only on untended barrows... in Mirkwood... for... a few days out of the year. I do not know... where any may be. It may be already too late.

'We also need... an unmarked venom sac... of the same brood... as Saebereth....

'Look in the Scuttle... the Scuttledells.''You found... found the components. Good, ${PLAYER}....'

Issuriel closes her eyes briefly, then opens them again sharply.

'Find Barvessain! She... she can make... the antidote....'

She struggles visibly, then manages to gasp out, 'She is somewhere in Ost Galadh!' before sleep takes her.Issuriel is asleep. She told you to find Barvessain, somewhere in Ost Galadh, and to have her brew the antidote to the gwigael poison.'What is this? A Sereglos flower? How did you find this? These bloom so rarely and under such specific conditions....'

Barvessain trails off as you explain the need for an antidote to the gwigael poison.

'Laidhris, it is called, and I can brew it from these ingredients immediately. But there will be enough for only a single dose. I hope this will not be a problem.''I have given you the single dose of the Laidhris that I was able to brew. I hope you can use it to cure whomever is afflicted with gwigael. It is a terrible poison.'Mazog is visibly ill, his body weakened from the effects of the gwigael poison. Still, he manages to sneer as you give him the Laidhris antidote.

'Kolfrangíz....' he manages to mutter and gives a short barking laugh before lapsing into sleep.Issuriel is barely conscious, but her mouth forms a thin line when she realizes what you are trying to give her.

'No... ${PLAYER}... I will not... take the antidote....

'You must give it to Mazog... or the Hidden Guard... has failed....''Thank you... ${PLAYER}....

'It is important... that the Hidden....'

Issuriel is unable to finish the thought before she lapses again into unconsciousness.Mazog has fallen asleep, but already his strength is beginning to return.'I have nothing to say to you, ${PLAYER}. I cannot understand how we have come to this point, saving the life of a filthy Orc and allowing a friend to... to....'

Achardor visibly brings himself under control.

'Tell Gruingalas outside the door that no one is to come into Gadorgar. I want no one disturbing Issuriel. She needs... rest.

'The scouts should also be recalled in preparation for the exchange of Mazog.''Tell Gruingalas, right outside, what I have told you! Now leave us!''I understand, ${PLAYER}. I will allow no one to enter Gadorgar. We are all doing everything we can.'Agorin revealed that the relics of Minas Gîl have been irreversibly corrupted by the sorcerers of Dol Guldur.The corrupted relics lie within Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh.

Agorin has asked you to destroy the corrupted Silvan relics within Minas Gîl.Destroy corrupted relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Agorin is at Ost Galadh, west of Minas Gîl.

You should report your success to Agorin.Talk to Agorin at Ost Galadh'There is no other way, ${PLAYER}: while it pains me more than anything to order it so, any Elven relics remaining within Minas Gîl must be destroyed...and quickly! Their purpose has been corrupted beyond recovery, and the powers they now shape at the hands of the Enemy are too dangerous to be left unchecked.

'Return to Minas Gîl and destroy these artifacts wherever you find them within, so that they are of no further use to our enemies.

'In the meantime, I shall attempt to divine who or what has brought about this evil deed, so that we may have our vengeance upon them for this grievous loss.''All the relics are destroyed then. I...very well. You have done as I asked, though I had long dreamed to return to the West holding such treasures of my youth aloft. I must harbour no such hopes in this dark place.

'I shall focus instead on the task at hand, and nothing more. All that matters now is the defeat of the sorcerer responsible for this evil!''Please...I would rather not speak of the task I have set before you.

'It was hard enough to ask it of you once; I could not do it again....'One of Fuirgam's trackers has been ambushed and slain by wolves in the forests of Emyn Lûm.Sharpfang may be found at Hrigg Vidukuni, west of the Wild Ruins, south-west of Ost Galadh.

Fuirgam has asked you to travel to Hrigg Vidukuni and search the area for the Emyn Lûm pack-leader, Sharpfang, and defeat him.Defeat SharpfangFuirgam at Ost Galadh is at Ost Galadh, north of the Wild Ruins, north-east of Hrigg Vidukuni.

You should return to Fuirgam with news of your success.Talk to Fuirgam at Ost Galadh'Sorry news, I am afraid. One of my kin was slain in the forests just west of here, by wolves no less. Though we have encountered many Wargs trained as curs of the Enemy since we entered Mirkwood, we had thought the common wolves would stay at bay from our forces. It seems we were wrong, and there are those among them that would stalk our scouts should they travel alone.

'Those of us who have learned the guttural speech of their kind have made out the name 'Sharpfang' among their wild howls -- it seems this leader claimed the kill, and I would see the beast put down as a lesson to the others that they dare not obstruct the Malledhrim.

'They have been seen to gather some evenings by a stone circle to the west of the Wild Ruins called Hrigg Vidukuni by the Woodmen who dwell in Mirkwood. You may be able to find their leader there and deal with him.''Excellent. With the crebain kept at bay and the wolves leaderless, I think we have dealt with the feral threats of Emyn Lûm for the time being. 

'Long enough to do what we must, for we shall not tarry long beneath these dark boughs.''I fear that Ivorel will have naught but unkind words for me when we return to Lothlórien.

'I have pushed her and her scouts to the point of recklessness -- and spent several of their lives in so doing -- but we have no time for delicacy, and we need their eyes on every road and ravine.

'If you should encounter her in the Scuttledells, please aid her in any way you may. I would very much like to see her return home unharmed.'Fuirgam has asked you to undertake a patrol of the forests surrounding Ost Galadh and to keep an eye out for Orcs attempting to waylay scouts and messengers.The Elf waypoint can be found marked by a stone to the north of Emyn Lûm.

You should scout the first waypoint of the patrol that Fuirgam has asked you to undertake and defeat any Orcs you might find there.Patrol the forest north of Emyn Lûm and ensure waypoints are clear of enemies (0/4)The Elf waypoint can be found marked by a stone to the north-east of Emyn Lûm.

You should scout the second waypoint of the patrol that Fuirgam has asked you to undertake and defeat any Orcs you might find there.Patrol the forest north-east of Emyn Lûm and ensure waypoints are clear of enemies (1/4)The Elf waypoint can be found marked by a stone to the east of Emyn Lûm.

You should scout the third waypoint of the patrol that Fuirgam has asked you to undertake and defeat any Orcs you might find there.Patrol the forest east of Emyn Lûm and ensure waypoints are clear of enemies (2/4)The Elf waypoint can be found marked by a stone to the south-east of Emyn Lûm.

You should scout the fourth waypoint of the patrol that Fuirgam has asked you to undertake and defeat any Orcs you might find there.Patrol the forest south-east of Emyn Lûm and ensure waypoints are clear of enemies (3/4)Fuirgam is at Ost Galadh.

You should return to Fuirgam and report in.Talk to Fuirgam at Ost Galadh'Good, you have returned. The Orcs have found some way to slip behind our post upon Gathbúrz above and are sending down small groups to try to waylay our scouts and messengers. I need you to patrol the surrounding forest and rout any of them you should happen to find along the way.

'We must not let them hamper our preparations for our assault upon Dol Guldur!''I trust the Orcs out there were not too much trouble? They do not seem to have found a way through in any significant numbers yet, or we would be suffering a terrible setback -- but for the time being, they seem content to dig in around the tower and in their fortresses in Gathbúrz.

'That would be just as well for us, if it were not for the Nazgûl....''Does it seem to you as if the Enemy's numbers are growing rather than waning as we battle them? It is because they are.

'When we launched our strike across the river, Dol Guldur was manned only by its garrison and the watch they had placed upon the river -- now we have received news of a great army approaching through the forest from the East.

'Already forward elements of this army have arrived to bolster Dol Guldur's strength, and when the main body arrives, we shall surely be driven back across the river. We have little time left to us, but we have nearly achieved our objectives, so take heart, my friend.''Does it seem to you as if the Enemy's numbers are growing rather than waning as we battle them? It is because they are.

'When we launched our strike across the river, Dol Guldur was manned only by its garrison and the watch they had placed upon the river -- now we have received news of a great army approaching through the forest from the East.

'Already forward elements of this army have arrived to bolster Dol Guldur's strength, and when the main body arrives, we shall surely be driven back across the river. We have little time left to us, but we have nearly achieved our objectives, so take heart, my friend.''Does it seem to you as if the Enemy's numbers are growing rather than waning as we battle them? It is because they are.

'When we launched our strike across the river, Dol Guldur was manned only by its garrison and the watch they had placed upon the river -- now we have received news of a great army approaching through the forest from the East.

'Already forward elements of this army have arrived to bolster Dol Guldur's strength, and when the main body arrives, we shall surely be driven back across the river. We have little time left to us, but we have nearly achieved our objectives, so take heart, my friend.''Does it seem to you as if the Enemy's numbers are growing rather than waning as we battle them? It is because they are.

'When we launched our strike across the river, Dol Guldur was manned only by its garrison and the watch they had placed upon the river -- now we have received news of a great army approaching through the forest from the East.

'Already forward elements of this army have arrived to bolster Dol Guldur's strength, and when the main body arrives, we shall surely be driven back across the river. We have little time left to us, but we have nearly achieved our objectives, so take heart, my friend.'Lomdognir believes goblin-spies are coming down from the heights of Gathbúrz and skulking in the forest outside of Ost Galadh.Goblin-spies can be found in the forests east and north of Ost Galadh.

Lomdognir has sent you to hunt down the goblin-spies.Defeat goblin-spies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lomdognir is at Ost Galadh.

You should return to Lomgodnir with news of your success.Talk to Lomdognir at Ost Galadh'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. I fear that the next several days' duties are likely to be dangerous indeed. The might of the Enemy is gathering on the heights above us around Dol Guldur, and if we are unable to break their forces swiftly, all of Lothlórien may be in danger.

'I am in charge of the defence of the main encampment here at Ost Galadh, a challenge made doubly difficult by the accursed fog that seems to shroud most of this forest -- even Elven eyes cannot see far through these cloaking mists, which are likely some contrivance of the Enemy against us.

'My guards have caught some hint of goblin-activity in the forests east and north of here, however. No great force, but furtive spies most likely attempting to gauge our strength. I do not think it will be easy, but if you could hunt down a few of their number then perhaps the remainder will fly back to Gathbúrz from whence they descended.''So, you caught a few of the vile creatures at their work, did you? That should teach them not to dare our territory lightly.

'There is much more to be done, however, if this camp is to be made secure for our advance upon Dol Guldur.''The goblins will not learn our plans, I think, because Fuirgam declines to tell even those of us here! It is clear that Celeborn's decision to attack Dol Guldur has some secret meaning behind it, but we have not the forces to take it. We are destroying everything around the tower and creating a spectacle before its gates, but I still have not fully fathomed why it is we do so.

'It must be that Celeborn wishes to keep the Enemy's attention here -- some kind of grand feint -- but from what, I cannot guess....'The Hidden Guard has begun the dangerous journey through the Scuttledells along Râd Iorist.Sigileth is waiting to speak with you along Râd Iorist, in the Scuttledells.Talk to SigilethSigileth's position within Râd Iorist is under attack by the spiders of the Scuttledells. You must defend Sigileth and Mazog.Defend MazogYou have weathered a first attack by the spiders along Râd Iorist and should speak now to Sigileth.Talk to SigilethThe time has come to bring Mazog further along Râd Iorist, though the woods be haunted by spiders.Secure Mazog's shacklesAchardor is holding vigil along Râd Iorist, the dangerous road to Dol Guldur that has been chosen by the Hidden Guard.Talk to AchardorAchardor is waiting for you to provide a support command for him by using his Malledhrim banner.Use the Malledhrim banner to issue support commands to AchardorAchardor's position along Râd Iorist has come under attack by the spiders of the Scuttledells. You must defend Mazog from their attack!Defend MazogYou have weathered another attack by the spiders of the Scuttledells and should speak now to Achardor.Talk to AchardorThe way Cúcheron scouted is not safe, and now the Elf must be defended from the spiders that chase him. Ensure that Mazog is not slain.Defend MazogCúcheron has been saved, thanks to yours and Achardor's efforts, and Mazog remains a prisoner of the Hidden Guard.Talk to CúcheronIssuriel is somewhere along Râd Iorist, to the north-east of Achardor and Cúcheron. The spiders of the Scuttledells have woven webs behind her, and they must be cut away if the Elves are to join her with the prisoner.Talk to Issuriel beyond the webs to the north-eastIssuriel's position within Râd Iorist has come under attack by the spiders of the Scuttledells. She must be defended.Defend IssurielAchardor has arrived at Issuriel's position along Râd Iorist, with Mazog in tow.Talk to AchardorIssuriel has a bad feeling about something and wants to speak to you even as her nervousness grows.Talk to IssurielAchardor needs your help to break free of the webs and to follow Issuriel and Mazog deep into the forest of the Scuttledells.Help Achardor break free of the binding websIssuriel has been grievously injured by the spiders of the Scuttledells and lies swooning beneath the light of the full moon. Mazog too has suffered an injury and seems to be in the same state.Check on the wounded IssurielThe Hidden Guard fights for its survival against the spiders of the Scuttledells, even while one of its number and its charge succumb to the poison of the spiders' master.Defend Achardor and the Hidden GuardThe path of the Hidden Guard along Râd Iorist has ended in disaster: Issuriel and Mazog have both been poisoned, and now the very success of the mission is endangered.Talk to Sigileth'Let us go, ${PLAYER}. We will limp now in defeat to Ost Galadh, where the Golden Host have established an outpost. I cannot believe we have come to this disastrous end!''For good or ill, we must walk this dangerous road, ${PLAYER}; our path lies through the Scuttledells.

'The rest of our company have gone on ahead and will hold the way for you to bring the prisoner to each of them. Spiders and black dogs are everywhere, so remain alert!

'You are familiar already with the support I can provide: I can make our foes bleed out their life-blood, or I can support you with power or morale. Let me know which you desire by shouting your commands for me by this banner.''We may not have much time. Ensure that Mazog's shackles are secure and bring him ahead to where Achardor and Cúcheron await. The sooner we emerge from this web-infested warren, the better for all of us!'You pull sticky, clinging webs from the loops of Mazog's shackles, and the Orc stares at you impassively.'I do not like this place, ${PLAYER}; better to have taken the straight road east to Dol Guldur than to stumble about in these spider-haunted woods! Already I have slain many of the creatures, and I heard Cúcheron's bow singing to the north-west after he went that way.

'That argument is ended, though, and now that we are forced to walk this road, I will do my duty to the Lord and Lady of Lórien and to this Hidden Guard.

'We will fight together! Make use of this Malledhrim banner to provide commands to me: either to support you entirely with offence or defensively, or with a pleasing blend of the two!''You fought well, and the creatures have been repelled. Perhaps this road will not be as perilous as I feared after all.

'Cúcheron and Issuriel went ahead, each in a different direction, to scout which way we should proceed.

'They have not returned.''Quick thought and quicker action, ${PLAYER}! I have come to expect both from you, and it is fortunate for my continued good health that this is so!

'We cannot take Mazog that way. The spiders become increasingly dense in that direction, and I saw some great bulk moving behind the spiders. There is terrible menace that way.

'Achardor and I will remain on guard here with Mazog; the spiders have woven great webs behind Issuriel as she passed to the north-east. Clear the way of webs and find Issuriel, and we will follow afterwards.''Issuriel went to scout the other path, to the north-east. I hope she did not encounter as much danger as did I, for both her sake and ours! You will need to break the webs along the way, for spiders have woven them behind her, and we will need a clear path if we are to bring Mazog that way.''Issuriel and Cúcheron went ahead to scout which way we can bring the prisoner. You see the result of Cúcheron's errand; we must hope that Issuriel fared better on hers.

'Travel to the north-east, breaking the webs along the way, until you reach Issuriel. We will need the way to be clear if we are to bring Mazog there.''I am so glad to see you, ${PLAYER}! I thought being here on a mission of such importance would give to me bravery enough... but here among the webs my courage fades, and I just wish to be home.

'It was wisdom to come this way, for we needed secrecy, but here in the dark it is difficult for me to truly know it. I will rely upon you to provide me commands by using this Malledhrim banner. I will support you as I did in the Drownholt: with power, with morale, or with a bit of both. Together, my courage will be the greater against the spiders of this place.

'We are not alone! They return!''Cúcheron and Sigileth have remained behind, for the moment. They will ensure that no spiders can surprise us from the rear.

'The rest of us will move forwards as a group. This way is full of danger, and now we are too far in to turn back! We must continue forwards!''Something is wrong. Can you feel it? This place is not safe!''You have done it, ${PLAYER}! We are free of the webs and can now follow Issuriel and Mazog before they come to harm!'Issuriel has been grievously injured and is swooning just on the edge of consciousness. Her eye-lids flutter weakly, but she does not seem to recognize you.'This is not how this was supposed to end, ${PLAYER}. Not only has our charge been poisoned by the venom of Saebereth, but so too has Issuriel. There may not be hope of survival for either of them.

'We cannot proceed any further like this. We must go to the nearest outpost of the Malledhrim, to recover from this sad development.

'If we can recover, ${PLAYER}. If we can.'The Brehur of Lhanuch have gathered in Glynn Brenin's hall to discuss whether they shall swear their allegiance to Isengard alongside their brethren in Dunland.Speak with Dufrig before the Council of Brehur begins.Talk to DufrigObserve the deliberations of the Council.Observe the deliberations of the CouncilBring forward the items you found upon the half-orc raiders as evidence of Isengard's involvement in the attacks.Place the sword before the breninPlace the helm before the breninObserve the deliberations of the Council.Observe the deliberations of the CouncilDefeat the Champion of Isengard.Defeat the Champion of IsengardSpeak with Glynn Brenin regarding the emissary from Isengard.Talk to Glynn Brenin'Enough! Begone from my hall, ${PLAYER}.

'We have other matters to discuss that are not for the ears of duvodiad.''The council is prepared to gather now, ${PLAYER}. I do not know what will transpire, but rumours continue to be bandied about.

'I know you have spoken with many of the Brehur of late -- please remain in the hall during the deliberations, should one of them wish to call upon you for your testimony.''You have little time, Duvodiad.

'Should the Horse-lords fall to the forces of the White Hand, Saruman will have armies to spare to deal with our refusal of his demands... and I shall have little choice but to swear our fealty to Isengard, if he allows me to live at all.

'Tell your duvodiad friends that they may pass through our lands, but we shall offer them no aid upon their way.'It is time at last to make the exchange of Mazog for the dwarf-prisoners. Many fates may be decided by the outcome of this negotiation....The Elves of the Hidden Guard have a decision to make: to wait for Bróin to return or to bring Mazog to the gates of Dol Guldur without him.Talk to AchardorThe Elves of the Hidden Guard deal with frustration and the wicked words of Mazog as they decide what is to be done.Wait for the Hidden Guard to decide what can be doneBróin has returned, but for what purpose did he leave Gadorgar without warning?Talk to BróinAchardor is waiting to speak with you about the upcoming exchange of Mazog for the dwarf-prisoners.Talk to AchardorThe Hidden Guard has come to the gates of Dol Guldur with the prisoner Mazog in tow.Travel with the Hidden Guard to the gates of Dol GuldurBróin is leaning on a walking-stick, waiting to speak with you.Talk to BróinAchardor has asked to speak with you before you proceed to the gate.Talk to AchardorBróin is down the hill from Achardor and the rest of the Hidden Guard.Talk to BróinAchardor is up the hill from Bróin.Talk to AchardorThe gate-keeper of the gates of Dol Guldur is considering the offer.Stand by the Hidden Guard as the Gate-keeper considers the offerThe Hidden Guard stands ready at the gates of Dol Guldur, waiting for the return of the Gate-keeper.Talk to CúcheronThe Gate-keeper has called you past the gate of Dol Guldur to discuss the exchange of Mazog for the dwarf-prisoners.Follow the Hidden Guard beyond the gateGorothúl has emerged from the fortress to negotiate the exchange of Mazog for the dwarf-prisoners.Talk to GorothúlAchardor is concerned about the terms of the deal as presented by Gorothúl.Talk to AchardorAchardor is trying to decide what can be done.Talk to AchardorGorothúl has used his powers to freeze you in place, as he did before Zabadgathol.Continue the negotiationsThe exchange has been a failure, and you must escape...if you can!Survive and escape, if you canThe Hidden Guard has fled from the gates of Dol Guldur to regroup at Ost Galadh, its errand a failure.Talk to BróinTalk to CúcheronTalk to Sigileth'There is little time to explain, ${PLAYER}, so I must be quick! After you gave the Laidhris to Mazog and the more I dwelled upon it, the more I came to regret that necessity. If only another dose could be made!

'I spoke with the Elf Barvessain atop the great tower here in Ost Galadh, and she said that more unmarked venom sacs of the Saewethil might be found, with time, but that the Sereglos flower is so rare that finding another one would be impossible. The conditions for such a flower to grow are so specific that only if the growing season could be slowed might such a flower still be found.

'I walked through the forest for many hours, heading north, and passed into lands beyond the reach of the Golden Host. I walked, and walked, and walked, and just as I was about to turn back in defeat, I beheld a grave mound among the tangled undergrowth. A stream flowed by its side, and now and then droplets of the water splashed atop the mound, where, bursting forth, grew a single flower, still in season.

'With this second Sereglos flower, and another unmarked venom sac, another dose of the Laidhris might be made!''It is over, ${PLAYER}. So many have died, and still Bori languishes within the dungeons of Dol Guldur. How can we hope to fight such evil?''Lord Celeborn believed some of the Nazgûl had come to Dol Guldur, but did not know for certain which of the Nine had done so. Now we do, though it is of little comfort to us.

'The Lieutenant of Dol Guldur commands the others; he is second only to the Witch-king, he who hailed from Angmar in the north. The Lieutenant of the Tower rules the fortress; it is he who struck down Achardor.

'The Gloom of Nurn was a wild-man of that land; it is peopled now only by slaves of Mordor. He wields a war-hammer in battle.

'I know nothing of the Black Blade save that he hailed once from Lebennin. He is fully a thrall now, as are all the Nazgûl, though it was not always so.'Sigileth ignores you, her face a mask of anger and grief. You decide to leave her be.'I was most wrong about the dwarf Bróin, ${PLAYER}. I have come to regret my words about him, and perhaps about all dwarves. To make such a seemingly futile journey in search of the one thing that might save someone he barely knows, someone not even of his own race...he showed a fortitude I had thought only Elves could possess. And he did it with much less complaining than I have done!

'But look at him. His journey north into the far reaches of Mirkwood has taken a toll even on his stout form; he needs to rest. The guards at the gate ahead will see his exhaustion as weakness, and we cannot afford that.

'Will you tell him to remain here in such a way as to spare his feelings? He has proven himself to me and to the others for the rest of time; he has no need to accompany us the rest of the way. He helped Issuriel, and now I wish to help him save his cousin and the rest of the dwarves.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. It feels good to have a reason beyond revenge for this errand of ours. I still burn with hatred for the Orcs, but now too I desire to rescue the dwarves, whereas before it was only a vague purpose. 

'We will do this now for Bróin.''None of those dwarves is Bori, ${PLAYER}? I thought not. They have been cruelly mistreated and seem close to death. Where is Bori?''I do not like this, ${PLAYER}. We must make Gorothúl turn Bori over to us, in addition to these three dwarves, or we will have failed. What can we do?''I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. Give me just a moment....'

Bróin leans on his walking-stick and tries to catch his breath.

'I walked many miles to the north in search of the Sereglos flower, and though I have my father's hardiness...it was still a most taxing journey. That it ended in success, and that Issuriel will recover from the Gwigael poison, was enough to give me further strength, but....

'One more moment, friend. I will have my breath back in a moment....''I do not want the guards at the gate to think we are weak, ${PLAYER}. They would not think so if they knew the distance I travelled, and in so short a time!'

Bróin laughs.

'I wonder if that will be the main verse of "The Glorious Tale of Bróin the Mighty," after all? It did not seem so glorious when I was hurrying through the dark, tripping over stones and treacherous roots, searching for a flower that might not even exist in the world any longer.

'Maybe my part in all this is over, ${PLAYER}. I do not want to hurt the negotiations for Bori. I will remain here and guard the rear. I trust that Achardor and the others will be able to fulfill this mission.''Well, here we are, ${PLAYER}. Now we will see if this errand was not as foolhardy as first it seemed.

'I will have Cúmaeth at the ready, in case we find our first belief justified!''Your offer does not interest me, ${PLAYER}. What use do I, Gorothúl, have for a useless Orc such as Mazog? Lord of Caves? He is lord of nothing! The dwarves crawl all over his caves like worms on mouldy bread! Bolg would be ashamed of his son, and Azog would slay him for dishonouring his family line!

'But it would humour me to hold Mazog in the dungeons of this fortress until the world's ending, so he may have time to think about how he failed his Master.

'I will accept your offer.''What is the meaning of this, ${PLAYER}? While you were recalling the scouts on the perimeter of Dol Guldur, the dwarf Bróin vanished from Ost Galadh. He told no one where he was going...and right on the eve of the exchange of Mazog for his kin!

'You had spoken for him, ${PLAYER}. You failed to speak of his cowardice! Do all dwarves abandon their companions when the road turns treacherous?''Look! Already Issuriel's strength returns! The Laidhris is working to fight the Gwigael poison!

'I...I do not know what to say. While I railed at unjust fate, the dwarf combed the forest for many miles to find a way to save Issuriel! It should have been me, ${PLAYER}....

'I cannot believe I was beginning to listen to the words of Mazog! Now there are no delays. We will go to the gates and exchange Mazog for the prisoners and be done with him at last!''It is no use, ${PLAYER}. We have failed. Let us go now inside Ost Galadh, though there be little we can do now.'Rocheledh is concerned that many sources of poison are potential threats to those who assist the Golden Host on their venture through Mirkwood. He wishes to craft an antidote to have on hand against the firefly poison.Fireflies can be found throughout the Drownholt in Mirkwood.

Rocheledh has asked you to collect the venomous stingers of fireflies so that he may craft an antidote against the poison. He fears for safety of the Elf-friends who travel with the Malledhrim.Collect luminous stingers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rocheledh is at Estolad Mernael in the Drownholt.

You should bring the stingers you collected to Rocheledh so that he may craft a useful antidote from their luminous venom.'Welcome to our small stronghold, good ${CLASS}. We are beset by dangers all around, both in the swamp-lands and beyond. There are many poisonous things, and while they do not threaten us, a great risk is posed to our horse-friends, and those of other races who travel with us as well.

'I saw the fell glow of fireflies as we travelled here, and such a sickly light can only be poison from such a creature. Could you collect the stingers of these flies? I could use the venom stored within to craft an antidote, as a precaution.

'Please collect for me as many stingers as you can, but be careful -- I do not wish to see you come to harm. These insects are strong and swift and will have no mercy upon any who draw too near.''You may find the stinging flies throughout the Drownholt, glowing among the darkness of these dense trees. Be wary of their poison, mellon!''Thank you, ${PLAYER}; you have done well to bring me these. Now I can set to work at making a draught that will act against this venom.

'What a sickly glow emanates from it still!'Someone has posted a task to deliver plies of gorgeous dust. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous dust.Wanted: Gorgeous dust taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.Wanted: Gorgeous dust taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.You have turned in a respectable quantity of gorgeous dust.Someone has posted a task to deliver tapered carapaces. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire tapered carapaces.Wanted: Tapered carapaces taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.Wanted: Tapered carapaces taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.You have turned in a respectable quantity of tapered carapaces.Someone has posted a task to deliver vile essences. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire vile essences.Wanted: Vile essences taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.Wanted: Vile essences taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.You have turned in a respectable quantity of vile essences.Someone has posted a task to deliver vile filth. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire vile filth.Wanted: Vile filth taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.Wanted: Vile filth taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.You have turned in a respectable quantity of vile filth.Someone has posted a task to deliver vile finger bones. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire vile finger bones.Wanted: Vile finger bones taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.Wanted: Vile finger bones taken from the defeated enemies of the Malledhrim.You have turned in a respectable number of vile finger bones.Half-orcs and Wargs out of Isengard raid the lands around Nan Laeglin to force the people to bow to Saruman's demands.Wargs and half-orcs from Isengard can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

Siorus Brehur has asked you to defend his people against the marauding Wargs and half-orcs in the region of Nan Laeglin.Defeat Wargs in Nan Laeglin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat half-orcs in Nan Laeglin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Siorus Brehur is at the Brenin's Hall in the village of Lhanuch.

You should return to Siorus Brehur with news of your victory.Talk to Siorus Brehur at the Brenin's Hall'Wargs have on occasion threatened our lands, but never have they come down from the hills in such numbers. It almost seems as if they are working alongside the raiders.

'Glynn Brenin has forbidden us to foray from the village for so long as Isengard's threat persists, but if we do nothing, our livestock will be slaughtered. Please, if you have the strength will you drive off these beasts?

'Whether it be to save us from savage raiders or starvation in the next winter's snow, we may indeed have to bend to Isengard's will....''Another day, another battle. If Saruman thinks we will join him with a boot upon our necks, he should best think again!''Drive back the foul marauders, ${PLAYER}, and you will earn my respect.'Fuirgam believes that the Enemy will use the crebain of Mirkwood as spies against the Malledhrim.The Wild Ruins lie to the south of Ost Galadh.

Fuirgam has asked you to thin the flocks of crebain that inhabit the Wild Ruins.Defeat crebain within the Wild Ruins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fuirgam is at Ost Galadh, north of the Wild Ruins.

You should tell Fuirgam that the crebain in the Wild Ruins have been dealt with.Talk to Fuirgam in Ost Galadh'While there do not appear to be Orcs in the ruins surrounding us, the presence of so many crebain disturbs me.

'The Enemy has been known in the past to use them as spies, and while my sentinels will shoot any from the sky that dare come too close, it will be difficult to hide any of our movements from them.

'Perhaps you might enjoy a relaxing hunt? I need their numbers thinned considerably to teach them to fear for their lives should they continue to haunt those ruins.''Good work, ${PLAYER}. There is no way we will dispatch all of them, but if enough fall to our arrows then the rest will be forced to keep their distance, and their value as spies to the Enemy will be greatly reduced.''Rodelleth might well have enjoyed such a hunt, but even now she leads the vanguard of our forces up upon the flanks of Dol Guldur.

'She is one of the most aggressive and violent warriors I know, and normally I am loath to leave tasks of any delicacy to her whims, but in this case we need some fire and spectacle before the gates of Dol Guldur, and she is well-suited to that role.'Lomdognir wonders if the glowing glands of the local fireflies can be used as a more reliable source of light in the unnatural mists surrounding Mirkwood.Fireflies can be found throughout Emyn Lûm.

Lomdognir has asked you to hunt down the fireflies in Emyn Lûm and attempt to collect a handful of the glands that produce a glow, which can cast a light even through the mists enshrouding Mirkwood.Collect glowing glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lomdognir is at Ost Galadh.

You should return to Lomdognir with the firefly-glands which you have collected.'By now I am sure you have noticed how difficult it can be to see through the fog that lies constantly upon Mirkwood. I have little doubt that this is some contrivance of the Enemy, for even torches and bonfires seem to flicker weakly through these accursed mists.

'We have an idea, however -- one of my guards noticed last evening that the flickering lights of those overgrown fireflies can be seen from some considerable distance even through the fog. Some quality of their light cuts through the mists and makes them visible.

'So, for the purposes of having some reliable light with which to observe our perimeter and to signal with, I would ask you to go collect some of the glands from the fireflies. Do be careful, though: if they are damaged at all, the light fades quite rapidly and is of little use.''Agorin assures me that these dark mists have not always lain upon Mirkwood. She claims that the forest here was once as fair as that which girdles Lothlórien!

'Ah, would that I had seen it then rather than now, but I am too young, and this place is as distant history to me as it would be to any Man or dwarf.''Ah, you managed to collect a handful of the glands intact. Good!

'I am not certain how long their light will last, but in the meantime my guards can make use of them to provide a bit of light to cut through this strangling mist.'You have put forth your best efforts to protect the peoples of Enedwaith against the evils which arose in their land.Agorin believes that relics of the Silvan Elves might remain within Minas Gîl, from the time when it served as an observatory studying the heavens above Ost Galadh.Relics might be found within Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh.

Agorin has asked you to recapture Silvan relics from the sorcerers in Minas Gîl.Find Silvan relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Agorin is at Ost Galadh, west of Minas Gîl.

You should bring the relics you found to Agorin.Talk to Agorin at Ost Galadh'So, ${PLAYER}, the tower of Minas Gîl now lays open to us -- I should tell you something of its nature before you enter therein.

'Minas Gîl was once an observatory built by the Elves of Ost Galadh, my kin of old. We used it to study the stars in their myriad dance across the sky. We gathered much knowledge of the heavens there long ago, and some relics may remain from among the mechanisms and arts that we employed in those studies.

'Once you gain access to the tower's interior, see if you can gather any such relics. It is likely that the Enemy has turned them to their own uses or destroyed them altogether, but if you can recover any, I would be very interested to see them.''What is this!? These devices...they have been touched by sorcery most foul, turned from their simple purposes to ends most evil....

'The firmament of stars above us, which we Elves have always revered most among all creation -- for they were made by Elbereth -- light a great Void of which we know little. But it seems that our Enemy knows something of its true nature, for our instruments which once turned to the study of the stars of Elbereth now look deep into that endless Void and draw upon it to sustain the shadows which they now bring into our world!

'There is nothing I can do to unravel the corruption of our relics, ${PLAYER}, had I the time to even attempt it. They must be destroyed and quickly if we are to prevent more of these unnatural spirits from being drawn into the light of our world!''Agorin tells me that you are helping her untangle the mysteries of Minas Gîl, ${PLAYER}. That is well, but take care, do not let yourselves be drawn into the mists of what once was. We have a mission here that must not fail if Lothlórien...no, if all of Middle-earth is to survive.

'If there be some evil in Minas Gîl then deal with it and be done, but do not let Agorin become distracted by it. We need her aid against the greater evil of Dol Guldur.''Would that my duties would allow me to visit my beloved Minas Gîl again. Just to see it there through the mists, standing almost within reach is almost more than I can bear.

'But while my heart beckons me to it, I know that it cannot be the tower I remember, for surely the Enemy has twisted it beyond recognition.

'I know my place is here alongside Fuirgam and the others, for the sake of our future rather than our past...and yet....'You now carry a gift of light and hope for the corrupted Mirk-huorns of Sâd Meryrn. However evil they now seem, these old creatures of Mirkwood stir pity, for their long memory has not let them forget the taste of clean air and sunlight, when life was greener.Sâd Meryrn can be found due south of Nífdir's camp, but you should strike north and west to reach the glade.

Nífdir has asked you to plant the mallorn seedling in Sâd Meryrn.Nenedhel awaits news of Nífdir's endeavour at Estolad Mernael, east of Nífdir's encampment.

You should speak with Nenedhel and inform him that Nífdir's task is complete.Talk to Nenedhel at Estolad Mernael'Here, mellon; take the seedling back and keep it safe. Do not let any harm it!

'Menassiel chose a promising young mallorn, and I am very pleased to offer this to the Mirk-huorns. Good fortune upon this venture, ${PLAYER}. I hope all goes well this time.''You have not been gone very long, ${PLAYER}, but it sounds as though much has been accomplished! You have my thanks. I am glad Nífdir will have fulfilled his wish to be of aid to the pained creatures here.''I hope that you can find a way to help the trees, ${PLAYER}. No creature deserves such suffering.''You have done very well, my good friend! You should speak with Nenedhel now and tell him that I will be along shortly. Thank you for all you have done.'Half-orc raiders from the mountains have attacked a number of small farmholds around Nan Laeglin. Guladus Brehures suspects that forces from Isengard may be behind the attacks, but she needs evidence before she dares speak openly of it in council.Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

There must be some bosses driving the half-orc raiders into Nan Laeglin. It is possible that among them one may be carrying equipment with the sigils of Isengard upon it.Find equipment on Half-orc Bosses (0/2)Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

There must be some bosses driving the half-orc raiders into Nan Laeglin. It is possible that among them one may be carrying equipment with the sigils of Isengard upon it.Find equipment on Half-orc Bosses (0/2)Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

There must be some bosses driving the half-orc raiders into Nan Laeglin. It is possible that among them one may be carrying equipment with the sigils of Isengard upon it.Find equipment on Half-orc Bosses (1/2)Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

There must be some leaders driving the half-orc raiders into Nan Laeglin. It is possible that among them one may be carrying equipment with the sigils of Isengard upon it.Find equipment on Half-orc Bosses (1/2)Guladus Brehures is at the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch.

Having found gear bearing the sign of the White Hand upon the half-orcs raiding Nan Laeglin, you may return to Guladus Brehures with the evidence she needs to speak out against Isengard in the Council of Brehur.'If I am to speak openly against Isengard, I need evidence that the half-orcs serve Saruman. We do not wish to kneel to Orthanc, but there is much fear of what will happen if we do not.

'With true evidence of Isengard's involvement in these attacks, I and many of my people will be free to speak our anger and deny Saruman the easy submission he expects of us.

'If you can find some sign of Isengard's involvement with the raiders in Nan Laeglin, that will give me all that I need.''Find evidence of Isengard's involvement in the half-orc raids, and I shall speak out against Saruman the White.''Find evidence of Isengard's involvement in the half-orc raids, and I shall speak out against Saruman the White.''Find evidence of Isengard's involvement in the half-orc raids, and I shall speak out against Saruman the White.''Find evidence of Isengard's involvement in the half-orc raids, and I shall speak out against Saruman the White.''This is it then. Now we know for certain that Isengard has set these devils upon us to force us to heel.

'Neither I, nor any among my fellows who dare count themselves Men shall speak in favour of this emissary from Orthanc.

'I do not know what the future holds for us, Duvodiad -- it may be that in a season's time all of Enedwaith shall be burned and barren -- but at least we shall die as stalwarts and not as cowards.'Half-orc raiders from the mountains have attacked a number of small farmholds around Nan Laeglin. Guladus Brehures desires to display trophies of their defeat upon the walls of her home.Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

There must be some bosses driving the half-orc raiders into Nan Laeglin. It is possible that among them one may be carrying equipment with the sigils of Isengard upon it.Find equipment on Half-orc Bosses (0/2)Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

There must be some bosses driving the half-orc raiders into Nan Laeglin. It is possible that among them one may be carrying equipment with the sigils of Isengard upon it.Find equipment on Half-orc Bosses (0/2)Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

There must be some bosses driving the half-orc raiders into Nan Laeglin. It is possible that among them one may be carrying equipment with the sigils of Isengard upon it.Find equipment on Half-orc Bosses (1/2)Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads.

There must be some leaders driving the half-orc raiders into Nan Laeglin. It is possible that among them one may be carrying equipment with the sigils of Isengard upon it.Find equipment on Half-orc Bosses (1/2)Guladus Brehures is at the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch.

Having found gear bearing the sign of the White Hand upon the half-orcs raiding Nan Laeglin, you may return to Guladus Brehures and present her with your trophies.'My hatred of the White Hand and his half-orc minions knows no bounds, ${PLAYER}. You brought to me the evidence I needed to openly speak against Saruman, but there is more you can do for me.

'Go forth once more and defeat Saruman's lieutenants and bring me trophies of your victory...I will display them upon my cartrev for all to see!''Bring me the trophies I desire, ${PLAYER}, and I will grant you a reward.''Bring me the trophies I desire, ${PLAYER}, and I will grant you a reward.''Bring me the trophies I desire, ${PLAYER}, and I will grant you a reward.''Bring me the trophies I desire, ${PLAYER}, and I will grant you a reward.''Fine trophies, ${PLAYER}. I will display these with pride!'The swamp-cats of the Drownholt prowl hungrily about, stalking any that move about unawares. They are causing the Elves of Estolad Mernael great unease.Swamp-cats can be found in the drowned lands of the Drownholt, all around Estolad Mernael.

Laidhriel has asked you to defeat many of the hunting swamp-cats that stalk the camp.Defeat swamp-cats in the Drownholt (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Laidhriel can be found at Estolad Mernael, the Malledhrim camp in the Drownholt.

You should speak with Laidhriel and tell her of your success against the evil swamp-cats of the drowned lands.Talk to Laidhriel at Estolad Mernael'How eerie! I can see them from this very spot, when they dare to come into view. Surely you have been hunted by them on your way here, have you not, ${PLAYER}? I am speaking of the dire cats of this vile black swamp.

'I daresay those beasts have never had a wholesome meal in their lives, for generations uncounted. They seem to be driven mad by our presence, for apparently we and our horses seem like the best food that has ever presented itself before them.

'I do not like how they prowl and stalk. Please go and thin their numbers so that the good folk who may have need to travel can do so without being eaten.''Well done, my good ${RACE}. I am sure the tentative paths of this swamp will be safer now for those who have need to travel. We can rest easier now.''If you can thin the numbers of swamp-cats about Estolad Mernael, we will all be much safer.'Agorin has asked you to gather a group of companions in order to launch an assault upon the summit of Minas Gîl, where some powerful sorcery is underway.The sorcerer responsible for the corruption of Minas Gîl may be found atop the pinnacle of that tower.

Agorin has instructed you to gather allies and defeat the sorcerer responsible for the corruption of Minas Gîl and put an end to his sorcery.Talk to Agorin to travel to Minas GîlAgorin is at Ost Galadh.

You should return to Ost Galadh with news of your victory.Talk to Agorin at Ost Galadh'Something stirs atop the tower of Minas Gîl, ${PLAYER}, I can feel it from here. Powerful sorcery is being wrought and will soon come to its culmination -- we must put an end to it before it is completed!

'The power I feel gathering is too great for you to face alone, and it is likely wielded by the sorcerer responsible for the desecration of Minas Gîl, against whom I would seek swift vengeance!

'You should prepare for an assault upon the tower's summit -- little time remains!''So, it was Gúlbenn who wielded the sorceries atop Minas Gîl? I have heard his name before -- he was said to be a powerful sorcerer, descended from the bloodlines of the Black Númenóreans. It is good that his evil has come to a final end, and the spirit he sought to summon has been cast back into the Void.

'Minas Gîl shall never serve the Elves again, but now perhaps it may be left to fall into timeless ruin among the silence of the forest.''Are you and your companions prepared to make your assault upon the summit of Minas Gîl? It will be a dangerous endeavour, and there is little time remaining....'A large and wary panther called Mirefang stalks near the Pool of Creeping Death, feeding upon the corpses of those who have died there.The vicious cat Mirefang can be found to the west of Estolad Mernael, near the Pool of Creeping Death.

You should summon and defeat this vicious hunter before he decides to hunt you, for his attack is sure to be deadly.Summon Mirefang and defeat himLaidhriel awaits you at the entrance to Estolad Mernael in the Drownholt, east of Mirefang's lair.

You should return to Laidhriel and inform her of your defeat of Mirefang.Talk to Laidhriel at Estolad Mernael'There is one more task I would have you do for us if you can, randir. While you were away, I felt a great malicious gaze bent upon me from this very spot. My eyes were barely able to pierce this gloom, but I beheld at some distance a terrifying cat. He does not seem pleased with our presence in his swamp.

'I saw him pace off to the west, surely towards his lair, wherever that may be. This cat is as death itself, and surely you will find a trail of death around the home of this terrible beast.

'Go west if you dare, ${PLAYER}, and attempt to remove this great threat. He will strike soon if we do not, and I fear to match wills with such a fiend.''You have slain this menace, then? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I cannot tell you how relieved I am. I have not felt at rest since I first beheld the brutal beast.''You should hunt for this cat I saw, ${PLAYER}. This swamp is perilous enough without menaces of his ilk stalking about in the gloom.'The chieftains of Nan Laeglin will soon hold a council under Glynn Brenin to decide how to treat with the emissaries of Isengard and the passage of the Grey Company through Enedwaith.The brehur of Lhanuch are in the brenin's hall in Lhanuch.

Dufrig has told you to earn the favour of the brehur of Lhanuch before Glynn Brenin's council comes to a decision on whether to bow to the demands of Isengard.Complete 'A Weapon of Old'Complete 'The Half-orcs'Complete 'Signs Among the Ashes'Complete 'Where There is Smoke....'Dufrig is in the brenin's hall in Lhanuch.

You should speak with Dufrig to enter the brenin's hall and observe the deliberations of the Council of Brehur.Convince Glynn Brenin to reject the emissary's demands'Your presence here is no mystery to me, Duvodiad. Our village is caught between powers. On one hand, we have the emissaries of Saruman the White, who demand our fealty in battles to come, while the Duvodiad of the North once again tresspass unwanted upon our lands.

'Glynn Brenin will soon hold council to decide our course. We have no love for the Men of the North, but we are not blind...we see what is happening to our brethren in Dunland. They will serve Isengard as pawns in the war to come, and many will never see their homes again. Yet if we refuse, we may come to blows with our own kinsmen, or the savage half-orcs who serve under the banner of the White Hand. I cannot say which would be worse.

'Know that Glynn Brenin's mind is not yet resolved in this matter, Duvodiad. Prove your worth to the brehur, and he may yet find the will to reject the entreaties of Isengard. Otherwise, I suspect that your wandering friends will soon be hunted down by Saruman's armies, and our Men-folk shall march to war in the South, to what fate, I know not.''You must earn the trust of the brehur, if you wish to secure the safety of your friends.''The Council of Brehur has begun its deliberations...do you wish to watch them?'Athradnir, a Galadhrim stationed at the Haunted Inn, wishes to convey a message to Laidhriel at Estolad Mernael.The second part of the Golden Host set off south, to the drowned part of the wood known as the Drownholt.

You should seek Estolad Mernael, the camping place of the Elves in the Drownholt, so that the Elves stationed in the Dourstocks can maintain communication with their brethren nearby.Talk to Laidhriel in the Drownholt'Welcome to our temporary establishment, ${PLAYER}. You may rest here a short while, but pray do not get too comfortable. There is a task I would have you do.

'Several days ago, our host split in two, and half our numbers travelled south to explore the swamplands in the Drownholt. We have not heard from them since, but it is important that we establish some lines of communication with them.

'I do not think the distance is very far, but it will be a treacherous journey. There is no friendly creature in Mirkwood, randir -- not one. Laidhriel will receive you, when you find her. She travels among the southern host at Estolad Mernael.''Mae govannen. I am glad Athradnir sent you to us, mellon! There is much to be done in this drowned land, for we are beset by many troubles.''The host you seek travelled south, into the part of the forest known as the Drownholt. You should speak with Laidhriel, who goes with them. It is best if we maintain communication with those stationed near us.'Himeinior told you that the Dúnedain are not welcome in the halls of Lhanuch, for the Uch-lûth are wary of strangers.Lhanuch lies to the south-east of Echad Idhrenfair, in Nan Laeglin.

Himeinior has asked you to seek entry into the Uch-lûth village of Lhanuch.Approach the gates of LhanuchThe guard is at the entrance to the Brenin's Hall of Lhanuch.

The guard at the village gate instructed you to speak with the guard before the Brenin's Hall of Lhanuch.Speak with the guard before the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch'To the south-east of here is the village of Lhanuch. It is the only significant settlement of Men in Enedwaith -- though we have seen evidence of a lost clan called the Turch-lûth -- and we shall have to pass near it on our path to Rohan.

'Once it was a place we often stopped to rest on our journeys through Dunland, but no more. Some years ago there was an incident in Nan Laeglin, and Glynn Brenin, the chieftain of the Algraig clan known as the Uch-lûth, declared all outsiders -- or duvodiad, as they say -- unwelcome in his halls, especially those of us known as Rangers.

'I would ask you to enter the village in our stead. Isengard is in motion, and we must learn anything we can before we pass Dunland. Glynn Brenin and his people should be able to tell us what we need to know. The people of Enedwaith are wary of strangers, but their laws of hospitality are ancient and deeply held. They will not turn you away without reason should you come to them in friendship.''Who goes there? You have the look of a northerner about you. We have seen more of your kind of late, but I cannot say you are welcome here.

'If you seek the hospitality of the Hall of Lhanuch, then I will not stop you...but the days grow dark, Duvodiad, and you may not find the mood of the brenin's hall to your liking.

'Speak with the guard outside the brenin's hall. Perhaps he will let you in, perhaps not. Be the cause of trouble in our village, and you will be spitted to warn off the rest of your ilk....''Halt! Declare yourself before the hall of Glynn Brenin, brenin of the Uch-lûth!

'${PLAYER}? You must be one of the duvodiad that have been sneaking about of late. What ill-wind brings you before our gates like some beggar from out of the wild? If you wish to invoke the hospitality of our hall then so be it, but it shall be allowed at Glynn Brenin's discretion, not mine.

'One word to the wise, Duvodiad. There has been rumour that Rangers from the wild have been skulking about of late. By the law of this house, they are not welcome, nor those who would spy for them in our midst. So watch your tongue and your idle hands, lest they earn you trouble.''We need the good will of the Uch-lûth at Lhanuch, ${PLAYER}.'The Elves of the Drownholt are missing one of their own -- a curious Elf who fancied he heard the sorrow of the trees as they made their way through the swamplands. He has not returned, and his companions yearn for news of him.Nenedhel parted ways with Nífdir to the west of Estolad Mernael.

Nenedhel, leader of the Malledhrim in the Drownholt, has asked you to seek Nífdir in the swamp-lands.Seek Nífdir in the DrownholtNenedhel is at Estolad Mernael, east of Nífdir's small camp.

You should speak with Nenedhel and assure him that Nífdir is safe, but not yet ready to rejoin his companions.Talk to Nenedhel at Estolad Mernael'Hail, ${CLASS}, and welcome. I am the leader of this company, though I fear I do poorly with the safekeeping of our goals. Perhaps I am rather too lenient with the whims of my good people, for I gave Nífdir leave to investigate the whisperings, and now it has been many days since his return.

'The whisperings, yes. Have you not heard them? We all perceived the shudderings and discontent amongst the trees as we travelled through the drowned lands. Good Nífdir wished to remain and hear them, for he is more concerned with the trees than with the Orcs and wraiths. He loves all forests, however bleak and black they seem. I had not the heart to forbid him.

'Did I do wrong to leave him behind? It has been many days since we parted ways to the west of here, in the heart of the swamp. I yearn to know if he has come to harm, but I do not wish to send others into danger for my foolishness, for we are precious few, and our mission is clear. I have already compromised our plans. Will you seek Nífdir?''Nífdir lives! You lift a great burden from my shoulders with this news, ${PLAYER}; I thank you. You have been very helpful.

'I do wish he would hasten with his work, however. Perhaps you can help him to speed this along, for I fear that further delay will compromise our aims.''Mae govannen, mellon. Nenedhel sent you to find me, did he? I am sorry to have given him anxiety on my behalf, and I hope that he will forgive me. I fear I am not ready to leave just yet. Can you perceive the wrath and fury of the trees all around us? I must know what angers them so.

'Please return to Nenedhel with my apologies and word that I am whole and well. Tell him that I will return when I can, but not before I attempt to discern what ails the trees of this swamp. I do not think they are evil! Alas, my heart is saddened by their pain.''Nífdir was last seen to the west of here, deep within the swamp, but that was many days ago. I hope that he is safe....''You are very good to have sought me for Nenedhel's peace of mind! Please assure him that I am well enough.'Bands of savage half-orcs have set upon the folk living on the outskirts of Lhanuch. Siorus Brehur of the Council of Thanes has asked if you have the strength to aid the people of Lhanuch and defeat these raiders before they destroy more homesteads. If you can do so, he will argue in council against the demands of Isengard.Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farms.

Siorus Brehur has asked you to repel the half-orc raiders and their leader Bûzog from Nan Laeglin.Defeat half-orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat BûzogSiorus Brehur is at the Brenin's Hall in the village of Nan Laeglin.

You should return at once to Siorus Brehur with news of your success.Talk to Siorus Brehur in the Brenin's Hall'Columns of smoke rise through the air south of here. The homes of my people are burning, and we have not the strength to defend them while raiders threaten the walls of this village.

'If you can aid us by doing battle with the half-orcs -- at least keep them at bay for a time -- then I will support you in the Council of Brehur.

'Otherwise, it seems that we must take up the banner of Isengard along with our kinsmen in the South, lest we be swept away upon the tides of war with no allies to call upon in time of need.''You have fought bravely on our behalf, Duvodiad. 

'I have little doubt that these raiders owe their allegiance to Isengard, but that matters little if they force us to concede to Saruman's demands.

'You have bought us some time and shown us the strength of the North-men. I shall try to convince Glynn Brenin to remain neutral for as long as we may.''If you can defend us against the half-orcs, I will speak in support of your duvodiad friends.'Bands of savage half-orcs have set upon the folk living on the outskirts of Lhanuch. Siorus Brehur has asked if you have the strength to aid the people of Lhanuch and defeat these raiders before they destroy more homesteads.Half-orcs can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farms.

Siorus Brehur has asked you to repel the half-orc raiders from the farms of his people.Defeat half-orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Siorus Brehur is at the Brenin's Hall in the village of Nan Laeglin.

You should return at once to Siorus Brehur with news of your success.Talk to Siorus Brehur in the Brenin's Hall'Your aid against the half-orcs of Saruman meant much to my people, ${PLAYER}. Unfortunately, the vile creatures have renewed their attacks upon the cartrevs.

'Will you aid us once again by hunting the foul vermin?''You have fought bravely on our behalf, ${PLAYER}. Saruman's lackeys will think twice about attacking us again...I hope.''Any aid you can provide us will be much appreciated.'You have encountered an unusual pair of Men, sent it seems from Isengard to offer a treaty of fealty between the Uch-lûth and Saruman.The emissary's champion is in the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch.

You should speak with the emissary's champion.Talk to the emissary's champion in the Brenin's Hall'And what do we have here? A bit far afield aren't you, Duvodiad? You are not welcome here. The affairs of Dunland do not involve you, and your presence does naught but threaten the tentative peace of these lands.

'With the pact I offer, these lands shall be forever safe from the looming threat of the North-men under the protection of Isengard.

'Now begone, before I am tempted to rash and unsightly action to remove you.''And here I was just looking for a bit of sport among this backwater collection of hovels. I had not dared hope for any fool Duvodiad to offer themselves up to my blades.

'Alas, it shall have to wait. My lord has business to attend to with the brenin.

'But do not wander too far, little vagabond. Once our treaty is in hand, I shall have the time to deal with the likes of you.''You are not welcome here, Duvodiad!'Fuirgam believes that Gollum has fled into the twisted paths of the Scuttledells to avoid capture and wishes you to aid his scouts in attempting to track down the skulking creature before he escapes or falls into the hands of the Enemy in Dol Guldur.Miluimil is at Ivorel's camp in the Scuttledells, north of Ost Galadh.

Fuirgam has asked you to inform the scout Miluimil that Gollum may have come north into the Scuttledells and to offer what aid you can in finding and capturing him.Talk to Miluimil in the Scuttledells'Gollum has slipped through our fingers yet again! I have good reason to believe that he has fled to the north, into the Scuttledells -- a warren of ravines and gullies infested with spiders and other foul beasts.

'I have sent instruction to my scouts there to be on the look-out for him, but I have received no word from them since and fear that something may be amiss.

'Would you be willing to journey into the Scuttledells and lend my scouts aid in capturing Gollum? He is more elusive than any creature I have encountered before, and they may need your help. Speak with Miluimil.''See to it that you find Gollum and ensure that he does not fall into the Enemy's clutches! Everything we have gained here -- and everything we have lost here -- will be for naught if he is captured. Find Miluimil, find Gollum and do so as swiftly as you may!''I have known Fuirgam for a long time, ${PLAYER}, and I have rarely seen him this upset over anything. Since that Gollum creature escaped into the Scuttledells he has seemed preoccupied with the matter.

'Whatever it is that Gollum knows, it must be of dreadful importance. We must capture him quickly.''Fuirgam believes Gollum is now here in the Scuttledells? I would feel better about our chances of finding him if most of my scouts were not already missing themselves.

'These ravines are treacherous to any who dare them, and I fear we will be lucky to emerge from them unscathed, much less to capture one such as this Gollum within them.

'Nevertheless, Fuirgam's order is clear, and he would not have made it if the need were not dire. Let us see what we can find of this lurking creature, shall we?'Nestawen has turned the herbs you brought her into a tincture that will dispel the evil poisons of the forbidding pool. It is time for the source of the sickness to be driven away so that it can do no more harm to unwitting passersby.Nestawen gave you a draught for your inventory that will protect you against the fell lights that gently sap life from all around.

Nestawen wants you to sip from the tincture she made so that you will be strengthened against the bog-lights.Use the draught to strengthen your resolve before entering the poolThe sickly pool is just to the south of Estolad Mernael.

Nestawen wants you to drive away the bog-lights that reside in the Drownholt and has provided you with a draught that will protect you against the dire effects of the water.Defeat bog-lights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nestawen is at Estolad Mernael, north of the sickly pool.

You should return to Nestawen at once and inform her of your success against the fell lights in the pool.Talk to Nestawen at Estolad Mernael'These plants you collected have already proven their use, mellon. You have an excellent eye for spotting healing herbs; I am very impressed.

'If you have any wish to cleanse that area of the horror that inhabits it, you should take the remainder of this draught. It has already proven its effects on dear Alagos, for I can feel his presence returning. Soon he will be awake. Drink it, and it will dispel the effects of that evil water.

'You may use the time it buys you to drive off whatever menace lurks there. Something saps that water, turning it into poison. Perhaps you can drive fear into whatever creature would have such a terrible effect on a place.''You have done a great service to us! The lights that inhabited that pool were sapping the strength from all around them, growing more and more fell.

'I am very grateful for what you have done, ${PLAYER}. It was a brave deed.'Drink of the tincture I gave you, ${CLASS}. It will protect you against the bog-lights, and the water that drains life from those who pass through it.''Good -- now that you have drunk of the warding mixture, you should hasten to quell the lights in that bog before its effects wear off.'One of the horses travelling with the Malledhrim has fallen ill, and the Elves begin to lose hope that he can be healed. His illness began as they passed through the Drownholt and has grown steadily more grave over time.Nestawen rode upon Alagos on her route to Estolad Mernael.

You should explore possible routes Nestawen may have travelled and look for anything out of the ordinary that could have induced the steed's strange illness.Explore the Drownholt for the source of illnessNestawen can be found at Estolad Mernael, the Malledhrim camp in the Drownholt.

You should speak with Nestawen immediately and tell her of the particularly fell pool in the Drownholt.Talk to Nestawen at Estolad Mernael'We are terribly distraught, randir. This dear one fell ill as we passed through the swamp-lands. It was day when we crossed the Drownholt, and Alagos bore me hither. But after a time his step became slower, and the moment we had successfully defeated the Orcs in a great skirmish, he collapsed where he stood.

'He seemed to sleep, but alas, he recedes further from my calls every moment! I fear there is not much time to cure whatever malice ails him, ${PLAYER}. What wretchedness could affect him thus? The Drownholt is an evil place.

'Until we know exactly where this began, I do not think we can help him. I fear to leave his side, though -- I am doing everything I can to hold him here. Could you go into the swamp and seek the source of this malady?''How awful! I could not perceive the difference when I walked through that pool upon Alagos, for the evil of this swamp is overwhelming wherever I go. I wonder what troubles the waters there....''Please hurry, ${PLAYER}. I do not think I can keep Alagos with us much longer if I do not know more about what befell him in the swamp!'Athradnir is anxious to hear what has become of the Malledhrim host who marched east to Emyn Lûm, for the closer the Elves draw to Dol Guldur, the more perilous the journey becomes.Fuirgam should be among the Malledhrim at their stronghold in Emyn Lûm.

You should seek Fuirgam and establish a line of communication between the Elves of Emyn Lûm and the Dourstocks.Talk to Fuirgam in Emyn Lum'We have split into many factions in order to organize our assault on Dol Guldur. While we feel that this is the best way to plan our offence, we worry very much during those periods in which we hear nothing from our kindred while they establish their footing.

'It is not safe to send scouts out until we hear from the advancing party, so we wait. If you are going to Emyn Lûm, will you keep an eye out for the host that marched thence? They will welcome your presence gladly, for we are stretched in every direction.

'Emyn Lûm is a dangerous wilderness to the east of here, closer to Dol Guldur. You should seek Fuirgam, for he is a commander of that faction. Be wary, ${PLAYER}; keep your wits about you! We do not know what evils lie yonder.''Mae govannen! How fare my kin in the Dourstocks? I am glad you have come -- I was anxious for word from Athradnir. Now that we have established a line of communication, there will be but one more small burden lifted from my shoulders.

'There is much to be done between marches, as I am sure you can understand. Will you be staying with us for a while?''Fuirgam is a commander among the host that marched east to Emyn Lûm -- you should speak with him first.'Antidotes often grow from the same soil as poisons; herbs from near the sickly pool should be collected so that the Elves can examine them for medicinal properties.Plants can be found growing near the dreadful pool in the Drownholt, south from Estolad Mernael.

You should hasten to the pool and collect many herbs there, for these may possess some property that could heal the steed Alagos.Collect unfamiliar plants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect unfamiliar herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nestawen can be found at Estolad Mernael, tending her sick steed Alagos.

You should bring the plants and flowers you collected to Nestawen to see if they can be of any use to her.'There is a phenomenon that often happens in nature in which remedies grow hand-in-hand with poisons. Weeds that harm can often be found nestled amongst leaves that cure. Now that we know just where the source of this strange illness lies, we should search the area for any plants which may have grown to resist the harmful environment.

'If you see any plants that seem to stand out, can you collect them for me? I believe we can devise a remedy if healing herbs can be unearthed from this polluted swamp.

'Return to that sickly place, ${PLAYER}, and make haste. Collect as many plants as you can. Please hurry! Alagos is fading....''Please hurry, ${PLAYER}. Alagos will not wait much longer.''Ah, mellon! I am glad you have returned so soon. These are strange plants, are they not? I have never seen the like. I will bruise their leaves and see if I can infuse a worthy draught from their essences.

'Thank you most kindly, ${PLAYER}! You are indeed a great friend to the Malledhrim. I see why Galadriel and Celeborn hold you in such high esteem, outsider though you are.'Nífdir wishes to learn what ails the violent trees of the Drownholt, and help them if it is possible to do so.Nífdir can be found at a small camp to the west of Estolad Mernael.

Nenedhel has asked you once again to seek out Nífdir in the heart of the Drownholt.Talk to Nífdir at his campHuorns can be found in Sâd Meryrn, due south of Nífdir's small camp. You should travel north and west to reach their glade.

You should approach Huorns and attempt to speak with them, but Nífdir has advised you to be prepared for much open hostility.Approach Mirk-huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Wrathful Huorn stands in Sâd Meryrn.

One Mirk-huorn does not seem as malicious as the rest; you should approach it and learn what you can from it.Approach the largest Mirk-huorn and attempt to speak with itNífdir is at the camp overlooking Sâd Meryrn from the north.

You should speak with Nífdir and tell him of the strange conversation of sorts that passed between yourself and the Mirk-huorn.Talk to Nífdir at his camp'My host of the Malledhrim will not be marching without Nífdir among them; I will wait for him, but he must not tarry long. Please make sure he knows this. If you can find a way to assist him so that his work does not delay him overlong, you will be helping me also.

'Go back to Nífdir, ${PLAYER}, and lend what aid you can. I do not know if there is much that can be done for the poor inhabitants of this foreboding swamp. Many of my folk feel that there is no hope or heart left in the swamp-lands...but you should not despair.

'The fear from Dol Guldur has thrown a long shadow across these once-fair woods, yet the power of the Elves is strong also. Do not give up hope.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! I am surprised to see you and very pleased that Nenedhel sent you back to me. When we passed through the swamp-lands, we all heard it -- the wrath and pain from deep within the hearts of the trees. The others took a wide detour to avoid the glade that seemed to be the very heart of malice.

'I have a way with trees, but I fear these Huorns. I am no warrior, you see, so I have been watching their movements from this outlook. But perhaps you, a worthy ${CLASS}, will have better luck if you approach them.

'Try to speak with them, but do not let yourself come to harm! You might be met with much hostility if you dare this task. Be wary, friend.''That is a sad tale, ${PLAYER}! Most of the creatures you will find as you wander this dour forest are evil and have always been evil. But trees have long, long memories, unlike the other children of this Middle-earth -- that is why they are so familiar to me, I think.

'It is long since these trees have had any hope, but they have not forgotten the brighter days. Poor creatures! Perhaps I can devise a way to help them, if you could give me a moment to think....'This Huorn's twigs shiver menacingly as you draw near, but it does not attack. It is a very old tree, and its will is strong. Surely this is the tree that the Elves perceived as they passed Sâd Meryrn.

As you stand at its roots, your mind is impressed with recollections of a fair green forest full of new life, and of a shadow of fear, ever-growing. The green life withers, blackens, and dies. Evil poisons consume the very water and air.'Please hasten to Nífdir's aid, mellon. The Malledhrim will not march while one of their host remains behind. He can be found to the west of here.''Go, ${PLAYER}, and speak with the trees of Sâd Meryrn if you can! But you must defend yourself if they attempt to attack you, for I would not have you come to harm on my behalf.'Agorin, the lore-mistress of the Malledhrim, has asked you to do battle with the spirits of shadow that surround Minas Gîl and return with some essence of their being that she might use to divine the nature of the ward that seals the tower itself.Shards of Twilight can be found around Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh.

Agorin has asked you to gather some aspect of the Shards of Twilight outside Minas Gîl.Collect obsidian gems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Agorin is at Ost Galadh, west of Minas Gîl.

You should bring the obsidian gems back to Agorin for her study.Talk to Agorin at Ost Galadh'${PLAYER}, a serious matter has come to my attention. Our scouts have examined the tower of Minas Gîl -- you can just make it out on the slopes to our east through the mist -- and they have returned to me with tales of deadly spirits of shadow surrounding it, and a shadowy ward upon the door that prevented them from gaining access to the tower's interior.

'I do not yet know what transpires within that tower, but it reeks of the Enemy's sorcery, and we dare not ignore such a threat so close to the path of our advance. Fuirgam has tasked me with ensuring that the threat is dealt with, and so I turn to you for aid.

'To begin with, can you do battle with the spirits surrounding the tower and bring me some aspect of their being? They are almost certainly bound up with the ward upon the tower itself, and if I can divine its nature, then we may be able to break it.''Such odd gems! They seem almost unreal and weightless, as if they were formed of smoke or mist made solid....

'This is enough, though. The nature of these gems tell me that the ward upon the door is no physical thing at all or even true magic -- it is a glamour woven of shadows, no more.

'Now that you know its nature, you will find that it has no power over you, and it will unravel at your approach, as do so many of the Enemy's lies once they are laid bare to the light.''Fuirgam has shadows enough to concern him within the heart of Dol Guldur. Let us deal with this other threat so that he may proceed unchecked, though I must admit that I do not fully understand his purpose...or Celeborn's.'Laidhriel is interested in collecting samples of water to keep for study upon her return to Lothlórien so that she can better understand the environs of Mirkwood's swamp-lands.Samples of water can be collected throughout the many shallow pools of the Drownholt in Mirkwood.

Laidhriel has asked you to wander among the pools of the Drownholt and collect several phials of water for her collection.Collect water-samples in the Drownholt (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Laidhriel stands at the entrance to Estolad Mernael in the Drownholt.

You should return to Laidhriel with the water-samples she requested of you.'We are very busy here with planning our offensive, as you see. Unfortunately, this does not leave me with much opportunity to pursue my usual studies. I am a scholar of nature, you see, as are many of my kindred.

'I have great interest in the natural world, even one as corrupted as this black forest. At home in Lórien I have a great collection of water-samples; it has taken me many long years to build. It would be a shame to leave the Drownholt without expanding my library.

'You would be doing a great favour to me if you would take samples from pools in the Drownholt as you go thither. Such items would be worth more to me than gold, ${PLAYER}.''I am so glad that you are willing to gather phials of water for my collection! I very much look forward to studying the samples you bring me, for there is much to be learned of a place from its still waters.''How wonderful, ${PLAYER}! I think these will do very well for the purpose of my studies. I hope to learn much of Mirkwood from these drops, for they can tell me many long tales of the rain and the plants and the earth of these parts. I suspect these will be sad tales, but perhaps some helpful knowledge can be gleaned from them in time.'Neirin Brehur has asked that you ride out to the cartrevs south of Nan Laeglin and see if any of them have escaped destruction at the hands of the marauders that beset Nan Laeglin.The cartrevs of the Uch-lûth lie to the south of Lhanuch.

Neirin Brehur has asked you to seek out the cartrevs of his people and learn if any survived the attacks of the half-orcs.Patrol Cartrev HamonPatrol Cartrev EmlunPatrol Cartrev RurithPatrol Cartrev MathoNeirin Brehur is at Lhanuch, north of the cartrevs.

You should return to Neirin Brehur with news of your discoveries.'Marauders have come to our lands, killing our livestock and threatening our people. Smoke rises from the south, and I fear that it comes from our cartrevs, burned in the night by the half-orc invaders.

'Glynn Brenin has forbidden our warriors from taking the field, fearing that the village itself might be burned, so I would ask you to seek out the cartrevs and see if anything remains.''Seek the cartrevs to the south and learn if any still remain there.''It is good that Hamon's home remains whole, as does Emlun... I only hope Emlun escaped the wrath of the half-orcs. Alas for Rurith, Matho, and their families.

'I thank you for your assistance, Duvodiad.'The Wild Ruins mark the remains of an ancient Silvan settlement, founded not long after Lothlórien itself. While the Malledhrim have retaken the large structure at the centre of the ruins, they have had neither the time nor the resources to spare to explore the remaining ruins on its outskirts.The Wild Ruins lie to the south of Ost Galadh.

Fuirgam has asked you to keep an eye out for enemies out of Dol Guldur or anything else out of the ordinary in the Wild Ruins.Scout the south-east ruinsScout the southern ruinsFuirgam is at Ost Galadh, north of the Wild Ruins.

You should report back to Fuirgam with the results of your exploration. In particular, he may be interested in the odd footprints you discovered during your trek.Talk to Fuirgam at Ost Galadh'Welcome to Ost Galadh, ${PLAYER}. Once long ago it was an outpost of our kind, when this forest was still called Greenwood the Great -- but that time is long past, and the power of Dol Guldur is great here now.

'While our forces have taken and secured this courtyard as a base to strike at Dol Guldur, we have neither the time nor forces to explore and secure the surrounding tangle of ruins and forest. In this, I am hoping that you can aid us.

'If you can take the time to quickly scout the more extensive ruins immediately to our south and report back on what you find there, it would be most helpful. What we can see from here suggests that it is mostly inhabited by wild beasts -- but even they must be assumed to be servants of the Enemy in a place like this, so foray with care.''So, the ruins are overrun with cruel and evil beasts, but little sign of goblins or Orcs? Good.

'These solitary footprints you mention, though...those are of considerable interest to me. When Lord Celeborn dispatched me across the Anduin, he bade me keep watch for a strange creature he named 'Gollum'. More than once he was nearly captured on the outskirts of Lothlórien, but he slipped away each time. Celeborn suspected he may have crossed the river to avoid capture, and it appears he was right.

'My sentinels claimed to have spotted a strange creature in the wild a few days ago -- they thought it a goblin, but were unable to capture it before it fled into the twisting ways of the Scuttledells. Your discovery tells me that our mysterious interloper was likely this Gollum creature. Would that we had laid hands upon him then!''There are a few among the Malledhrim -- Agorin among them, I believe -- who once called Ost Galadh home. How it must confound them now to return at last and stand within these ancient walls, remembering times of song and laughter long ago swallowed by darkness.

'I do not envy them this bittersweet return.'The Elf Iavassúl and his companions are tasked with preventing the Orcs of Taur Morvith from closing in behind the main force of the Malledhrim.Orkish war-banners can be found in Krul Lugu below Iavassúl's Watch.

Iavassúl has asked you to destroy several of the Orcs' war-banners to demoralize the Enemy.Destroy Orc-banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch, above Krul Lugu.

You should return to Iavassúl and inform him that the Orkish banners have been destroyed.Talk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch'Welcome to Taur Morvith, ${PLAYER}. We have few warriors to spare with the strength of our forces heading towards Gathbúrz and Dol Guldur...your aid is most appreciated.

'Can you make out those Orkish fortresses down below? They call them Krul Lugu in their Black Speech. Krul Lugu marks the southern flank of our advance, and I am tasked with ensuring that they are unable to mount a strike against us at Ost Galadh. The Orcs are cut off from the bulk of their forces in Dol Guldur, so their numbers are not great...but ours are spread even more thinly here, so we are trying to keep their attention occupied rather than risk a large-scale battle. To that end, we strive to demoralize and blind them, keeping them in place and paralyzed with uncertainty.

'I have a simple task for you: Destroy their war-banners. It is naught but a symbolic effort, but as they appear to be bereft of strong leadership, it should be sufficient to set them back before they can rebuild their courage.''Yes, I can see it from here even through the mist. You have made them quite angry by the looks of it -- angry, but uncertain, and that is a fine line we must walk.

'We need to keep them off balance, but not enrage them into risking a headlong assault that might threaten our flank.''Throw down the banners of Krul Lugu, ${PLAYER}, and show to the Orcs to whom this land truly belongs!'A band of Orcs dispatched from the tower of Dol Guldur is hunting through the Scuttledells for the furtive Gollum.Miluimil is at Ivorel's camp in the Scuttledells.

Miluimil has asked you to travel with him into the caves in the northern Scuttledells and prevent the servants of Dol Guldur from capturing Gollum.Talk to Miluimil to travel to the cavesMiluimil is at Ivorel's camp in the Scuttledells.

You should speak with Miluimil about Gollum's escape.Talk to Miluimil at Ivorel's camp'It seems that Celeborn himself has said that we must not permit Gollum to fall into the hands of the Enemy, for the creature holds some knowledge that would upset the entire campaign of the Malledhrim against Dol Guldur.

'I know not what morsel of knowledge this Gollum creature possesses to so trouble the brow of mighty Celeborn, but we must move quickly if we are to prevent his capture!

'The goblin you interrogated claimed that the Orcs had pursued Gollum into the caves to the north, did he not? Swiftly then! Let us rush into peril, all wiser thoughts of caution unheeded, for now is the time!'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready? There is no time like the present, so let us tarry no longer!'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Aye, it appears that Gollum has slipped our noose once again. It is a bit embarrassing, I will admit. There are few who can so readily outwit me in the brush.

'Our most important task has been achieved, however: the servants of Dol Guldur have been slain or chased off empty-handed, and Gollum's trail grows cold behind him.

'So long as he does not choose to consciously betray it to the Enemy, I think Celeborn's secret is safe for the moment. I doubt they will get another chance at him here in Mirkwood now that he is on his guard against them... but then, we may not either.'The Orcs of Taur Morvith have been partially cut off from their leadership in Gathbúrz, but are held together by a handful of brutal lieutenants.Dushmau lieutenants can be found in the encampments of Taur Morvith.

Iavassúl asked you to find and defeat Dushmau lieutenants in Taur Morvith.Defeat Dushmau lieutenants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith.

You should let Iavassúl know of your success.Talk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch'While we have not the forces to encircle the Orcs of Taur Morvith, we have cut off their main lines of communication to Gathbúrz, depriving them in part of guidance and leadership.

'There are a handful of Orc-lieutenants remaining in the camps below, however, and they may manage to keep their fractious troops in line. If you can eliminate this nuisance, it will keep the Orcs off balance and delay them from mustering any real force to assault Ost Galadh.''The loss of several of their officers will no doubt disrupt the Orcs' attempts to strike back at us.

'Now that they are held at bay, we can focus on trying to destroy these encampments altogether, but I fear that Fuirgam will allow no diversion of forces from the planned assault on Dol Guldur, so we remain on our own where that is concerned.''The Orcs of Taur Morvith rely upon the guidance of their lieutenants. The Dushmau will be thrown into disarray if enough of their leaders are defeated.'The Orc-scouts ranging out from Taur Morvith act as the eyes for their gathering forces.Orc-scouts can be found throughout Taur Morvith.

Iavassúl asked you to defeat the Orc-scouts ranging outside of the forts in Taur Morvith and to intercept any messages they might be trying to carry through to Gathbúrz.Defeat Orc-scouts in Taur Morvith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Gathbúrz messageIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith.

You should bring the message you intercepted to Iavassúl.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. Do you see those camps down there? You can faintly make them out through the shrouding mists, but they are there, and they are looking for us as well.

'Orc-scouts range throughout Taur Morvith, trying to find us and entrap us so that their larger forces at those encampments can come down upon us with superior numbers. That, we cannot allow!

'I need you to hunt down the scouts...and while you are doing so, attempt to intercept any of the messages they have been trying to get through to Gathbúrz.''If the Enemy's eyes are removed, he will not see that we do not have quite the strength we claim...our tactics will prove successful.''So, you managed to lay your hands upon one of the Orcs' messages. They have been trying desperately to get one through to Gathbúrz since we blockaded the forest...and we have been trying just as hard to obtain one.

'This is a terrible mess...it is barely legible at all! The masters of Dol Guldur should really teach better Black Speech to their warriors if they expect them to be reading orders and the like. 

'Anyway, once I decipher this pathetic scribbling, we should have a better idea of what they are up to down in Krul Lugu.'This ancient piece of an amulet seems strangely out of place among the other belongings of the wight.Mincham is camped east of the road along the northern border of the Lich Bluffs.

You should bring this amulet-fragment to the Ranger Mincham.This fragment of an amulet appears to be worn with age and is scrawled with an ancient text. It may lead to something which will shed more light upon the mystery of the Oathbreaker shades in the Lich Bluffs.

Perhaps you should take this fragment to the Ranger Mincham, whom you know to be versed in ancient languages.'${PLAYER}, we seem doomed to meet ever and anon among the Dead. What is this you have?

'Ah, thank you for bringing this amulet to me. The markings seem to match some of the symbols on a few of the local barrows.

'When I first arrived, a hermit named Lhudd approached me and asked me to keep an eye out for objects bearing these markings. For what cause, I know not.'Several older cairn stones are scattered among the barrows in the Lich Bluffs. Perhaps the ancient writing may provide a clue to the past of the amulet that you recovered.The ancient cairn-stones are located south of the Hall of Sanctuary, among the rolling hills and barrows.

Lhudd has asked you to seek out ancient cairn-stones and place the amulet upon them. He believes that this may somehow help to mend the amulet.Find cairn-stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lhudd is at the Hall of Sanctuary in the Lich Bluffs.

You should return to Lhudd with news of your discoveries.'I wish to thank you for recovering both halves of this amulet, Duvodiad. My hope has been that when this item is mended, that it might weaken the shades that stalk this troubled land. I fear a great evil has bound them here, and they have become dangerous.

'Take both pieces of the amulet and seek out several of the unusual cairn stones that dot the landscape. These ancient cairn stones are covered with inscriptions that are much older than those that surround them. The inscriptions on these stones match that of the amulet and can hopefully be used to help mend it to its original shape.

'Travel to the south-east and locate several of these cairn stones. Place the amulet upon them, then bring me word of the effects, if any, you witness.''I believe that the amulet may be mended by placing it upon the correct cairn stone. Perhaps you will discover if my belief is true....''This amulet may very well be the symbol of an ancient settlement here. The cairn-stones that you visited are said to date back to that time, and now the amulet appears to be mending itself. 

'I believe those cairn-stones were left by a branch of an ancient lûth -- clan -- that fell to conflict within itself. This may be what caused the shades to be bound here.

'My hope is that somehow this amulet will allow us to put these poor spirits to rest.'One of Ivorel's scouts has returned to tell of a deadly black dog named Trapjaw who was seen following Hal Tiller's trail two days ago. Ivorel believes that Trapjaw is likely responsible for his death.Trapjaw's lair lies a distance to the north-east of Ivorel's camp in the Scuttledells.

Ivorel has tasked you with avenging Hal Tiller by hunting down the deadly black dog, Trapjaw, within the Scuttledells.Find TrapjawIvorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells, a distance south of Trapjaw's lair.

You should speak with Ivorel and tell her that Trapjaw has been slain and that Hal Tiller is alive.Talk to Ivorel at her camp'One of my scouts managed to return on his own, ${PLAYER}, and he brings important tidings. The evening before last he found himself tracking an unusually large and cunning barghest -- he believes the creature may have been stalking  little Hal Tiller at the time -- but he lost the trail when he was himself ambushed and injured.

'This creature -- named Trapjaw by the local folk -- evidently cornered and killed Hal a short while after. Now all that is left to us is to avenge the hobbit and destroy this monster before any more fall to it!

'My scout tells me that Trapjaw has a lair out among the Scuttledells, a distance north of here. Find him and slay him, ${PLAYER}, in the name of Hal Tiller.''The lives of the hobbits are short enough and far too innocent for such matters. It grieves me deeply to realize that I am responsible for the death of one such....'Trapjaw looks up from his grisly meal angrily, then leaps to his feet to attack!'Hey there, my good ${RACE}! Glad to see a friendly face out here. That overgrown dog and I have been hunting each other in circles for two days straight! Luckily, I was just ready to spring my trap when you showed up, or it might have gone badly for you.

'Well, I'm off to continue the hunt! Good luck to you!''Trapjaw is dead... and... what? You claim that Hal Tiller yet lives?

'We shall see about that! The little trickster has caused me more worry and care over the last week than I have known in two-hundred years! Here I thought him tormented or dead, and he has been off shirking duty to play hide and seek in the ravines!

'When he returns, I will make him wish that he was safely tucked in Trapjaw's belly!'Miluimil's scouts have reported on the existence of a deadly spider-queen named Delúris that lurks in the northern depths of the Scuttledells. Her poison is so deadly that none who have dared face her have survived.Blackvenom Spiders can be found in the caves at the northern end of the Scuttledells.

Miluimil has asked you to gather venom glands from the Blackvenom brood of the Scuttledells, so that he can make an antidote to Delúris' poison.Collect black poison-glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Miluimil is at Ivorel's camp in the Scuttledells.

You should return to Miluimil with the poison-glands you have collected.'I have received dark news indeed, ${PLAYER}. One of my scouts has told me of a deadly queen to the Blackvenom spiders - a brood that infests the caves in the northern Scuttledells. One of his companions fell to her, succumbing to a poison so quick and deadly that he was compelled to flee from her as swiftly as he could.

'We have little chance of destroying the brood so long as this creature lives, but I do not think you should dare to face her without some counter to her poison!

'If you can gather samples of the Blackvenom spiders' poison, I may be able to help you concoct such an antidote. Gather a few venom glands from Delúris' brood, then we shall make our preparations.''Keep an eye open for an Elf named Gladiel. She passed through here a while ago seeking some passage and muttering about another brood of spiders she called the Saewathel.

'As if one brood of these creatures was not enough...I know nothing of the Saewathel, but she seemed concerned about their presence and seemed to be seeking some way through the Scuttledells towards Dol Guldur. I could not help her, I am afraid.''Be careful with those, ${PLAYER} -- the venom of the brood is not so deadly as that of Delúris herself, but it is not to be taken lightly.

'It is similar enough that I should be able to concoct an antidote from it, then perhaps you will be able to defeat Delúris without fear of her deadly sting!'Having helped Miluimil craft an antidote from the poison of her own brood, you are now prepared to sojourn against Delúris the brood-queen of the Scuttledells.Delúris' nest is in the northern Scuttledells, north of Ivorel's camp.

Miluimil has asked you to confront and defeat the spider-queen Delúris and has supplied you with the antidote to her venom.Defeat DelúrisMiluimil is at Ivorel's camp in the Scuttledells, south of Delúris' nest.

You should return to Miluimil to tell the tale of Delúris' defeat.Speak with Miluimil  in the Scuttledells'Are you ready to face Delúris, ${PLAYER}? I have completed the antidote. Be sure to use it swiftly should you feel the sting of her poison upon you -- you will not have much time.

'The antidote's effects are short-lived, should the battle draw on, you may have to use more, but a few drops should suffice to counter her sting.

'She lairs in the caves up at the northern end of the Scuttledells, and many of her brood are gathered there, so take great care lest you be overwhelmed by their numbers before you even reach her.''And so the evil brood-queen has fallen. Well struck, ${PLAYER}...without their progenitor, the vile brood will wane as they are hunted to extinction. But much of that task will have to wait until after the fall of Dol Guldur.

'For now, it is enough to know that Delúris is gone and my scouts no longer need fear her black venom.''Where have all of these horrid spiders come from, I wonder? Agorin did not speak of such beasts when recounting the time when she lived within Greenwood the Great.

'Yet Celeborn once spoke of a black and evil creature that passed this way in the intervening years as the forests darkened, crawling out of the Misty Mountains and passing through the forests into the south, whereupon it again disappeared.

'Could it be that these creatures are the spawn of that evil?'If Ivorel's scouts are to have any hope of moving without the Enemy knowing their every step, the crows of the Enemy will need to be kept at bay.Scuttledells crows can be found throughout the Scuttledells.

Ivorel has asked you to hunt down Scuttledells crows to prevent them from finding her scouts or reporting back to Dol Guldur.Defeat Scuttledells crows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ivorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells.

You should speak with Ivorel and tell her that many of the Enemy's flying scouts have been slain.Talk to Ivorel at her camp'Keep one eye to the skies, ${PLAYER}. There are a number of the Enemy's black-feathered servants about. My scouts will be hard pressed to move unseen with such keen eyes above us.

'Defeat them quickly if you should come upon them in the ravines and gullies below... the fewer that make it back to Dol Guldur alive, the better.''Agorin tells me that even when our Silvan kin still inhabited Ost Galadh, they warned their children to stay away from these dangerous ravines and dells, but that later they would challenge each other to dare the maze despite their elders' warnings.

'Now only a hardened warrior has any chance of surviving in this place. It is hard to imagine her holding fond memories of this death-trap.''So, there are fewer of the Enemy's crow-spies about? Excellent.

'If we can move about unseen, we have a better chance of rescuing a few of our people from these cursed ravines.'Throughout the Lich Bluffs, the despondant shades of ancient Algraig clansmen watch over ancient barrows. Perhaps the amulet that you recovered may begin to unravel the mystery of the Oathbreakers that plague the land.The sorrowful and mournful shades can be found to the north-west of the Hall of Sanctuary, near the entrances of several barrows on the ridge above.

Lhudd has asked you to present the shades with the broken amulet that you recovered and observe what unfolds.Present the amulet to the mournful shadePresent the amulet to the sorrowful shadeLhudd is at the Hall of Sanctuary, south-east of the barrows.

You should return to Lhudd and explain the happenings outside of the barrows.'I thank you again for recovering both pieces of this amulet. I have a feeling that, once repaired, this may weaken the shades that patrol the barrows in the Lich Bluffs. 

'To the north-west, there are many shades that stand vigil over several barrows. For some reason, these creatures are not aggressive, unless provoked. 

'Seek out a couple of these shades and present them with the amulet. If you should learn anything, return to me with your knowledge.''Have you presented the amulet to the shades yet, Duvodiad?''It is interesting that these spirits spoke to you upon presenting them with the amulet, but it does lend credence to a belief that I have held. These shades are held here due to an ancient rheg -- curse -- upon their people. 

'Perhaps we might free these poor spirits from their sorrowful state?'Culang has assigned you the task of finding a number of hidden caches of supplies scattered throughout Nan Laeglin. If you can uncover these supplies, the Grey Company will be able to pass through swiftly without as having to resort to bartering with possibly hostile locals or stopping to hunt.The cache of healing draughts is hidden well to the south of Lhanuch, on the border of the Lich Bluffs. The Rangers' rune may be found atop a green hill with many trees upon it.

Culang has sent you to retrieve a hidden cache of healing draughts.The cache of potions would be buried around the base of a boulder some forty paces west into a stand of evergreens.

Culang asked you to retrieve a hidden cache of healing draughts.Culang is at his camp in Nan Laeglin, north-east of the cache.

You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the healing draughts hidden there. Now you should return with them to Culang.'We need to be ready for anything, and there are some supplies we were unable to gather before our hasty departure. Among them is a decent supply of healing draughts to alleviate the effects of dangerous poisons, wounds, and the like.

'However, there is a traveller's cache laid in not far from here if you are willing to try and retrieve it. It lies somewhere well to the south of Lhanuch, near the edge of the Lich Bluffs.

'You should be able to find the rune atop a green hill with many trees upon it. Once you have found the rune, turn west and search around the base of a boulder some forty paces on into a stand of evergreens.''We need those draughts, ${PLAYER}.''We need those draughts, ${PLAYER}.''The draughts you have brought us will be invaluable in battle. The Enemy is well-known for his use of deadly poisons and cruel weapons that cause wicked wounds, and these will help prevent the worst effects of such devices.'The mission of the Hidden Guard goes on: it is time to call back the scouts of the Golden Host and to bring Mazog to the gates of Dol Guldur in exchange for the prisoners.Laeglang, Lamwen, and Súlthel are somewhere in Gathbúrz, east of Ost Galadh and outside the walls of Dol Guldur.

Gruingalas has told you to recall the scouts that are keeping watch on the fortress of Dol Guldur in Gathbúrz.Talk to Laeglang in GathbúrzTalk to Lamwen in GathbúrzTalk to Súlthel in GathbúrzGruingalas is outside the entrance to Gadorgar, in Ost Galadh.

You have recalled the scouts from Gathbúrz and should return to Gruingalas with the news they gathered in the wild.Talk to Gruingalas at Ost GaladhGruingalas is in Ost Galadh, waiting to speak with you.

The mission of the Hidden Guard is at its end: the time has come to exchange Mazog for the dwarf prisoners.Talk to Gruingalas and meet with the Hidden GuardGruingalas is outside the entrance to Gadorgar, in Ost Galadh.

The exchange did not go according to plan, and the mission of the Hidden Guard has ended in failure: Achardor is dead, Mazog is taken, and Bori remains in captivity.Talk to Gruingalas at Ost Galadh'The Malledhrim sent a number of scouts ahead to spy the lay of the land in front of the fortress of Dol Guldur; we will want to know what they have learned and have them return here before we bring Mazog the rest of the way to the gates of the fortress.

'Seek out the scouts Lamwen, Súlthel, and Laeglang in the wild lands of Gathbúrz, east of here and before the walls of Dol Guldur. Tell them to return and that the final leg of the Hidden Guard's mission will be undertaken.

'With the information of these scouts, we will be best prepared to effect the exchange of Mazog for the dwarf-prisoners.''There has not been a great deal of activity beyond the walls of Dol Guldur, ${PLAYER}. By now they are surely aware of the Golden Host; do they suspect any of its real purposes, I wonder? It is a great offensive, true; but do they suspect that we do not seek victory? That we are drawing their eyes to a point of our choosing, rather than theirs?

'I will return to Ost Galadh at once. It is to be hoped that we have not alarmed the Enemy overmuch, and we will catch them unaware in all respects.''Achardor gave me a message for you, ${PLAYER}. Your friend, the dwarf Bróin...he cannot be found. He has been missing ever since you left to recall the scouts. Achardor does not want to wait for him; he says that he wants to be rid of Mazog at once and have the errand completed.

'Speak with me when you are ready, and I will bring you to the Hidden Guard so you can discuss the matter with them.''The Hidden Guard has failed, ${PLAYER}. Achardor is slain, Mazog is taken, and Bori remains in captivity.

'Sigileth is mourning with Issuriel inside Gadorgar. She has asked not to be disturbed.''From my exploration, it seems likely that Gathbúrz will serve as the staging area for the armies of Dol Guldur when they move to attack Lothlórien. There are a number of camps here, but the Orcs are fortunately not yet massing here in great numbers.

'I will return to Ost Galadh and share what I have learned.''You have met me on my way back from the southern marches among the Ashenslades. The land there is blasted and dead, and the stench of evil is everywhere.

'It appears that Gorothúl has trained evil Men in the arts he learned from his own master; they are seeking to bind fell spirits to their service in the far reaches of the Ashenslades.

'I will return to Ost Galadh with my report of that place.''Tell Gruingalas I will be there soon. He is at Ost Galadh, is he not?''Lamwen, Súlthel, and Laeglang are somewhere in Gathbúrz, east of here and outside the long walls of Dol Guldur. Learn what they have discovered from their time scouting the wild lands between here and Dol Guldur and tell them to return here in preparation for the exchange of Mazog.

'We must know everything there is to know of the dangers in Gathbúrz before the Hidden Guard makes its move.''Will you not speak with Achardor? I know that Bróin will want to be a part of this final stage of the mission, and Achardor must not let his anger blind him to the dangers of haste.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>'Report to Gruingalas with the news I have given you. I will return shortly and give him further detail on the Orc-presence in Gathbúrz.

'He is at Ost Galadh, I believe?''You were going to return to Gruingalas in Ost Galadh and tell him what I have seen in the Ashenslades, were you not? I will be there as soon as I may, but surely you will arrive before I do.

'Please hurry, ${PLAYER}. It might be important.'The mission of the Hidden Guard has failed, and now the remaining hopes of Celeborn and Galadriel rely solely upon the main arm of the Golden Host.Ningloril is in Thangúlhad, east of Ost Galadh, in Gathbúrz.

Gruingalas has sent you to offer your aid to Ningloril, now that the errand of the Hidden Guard has failed.Talk to Ningloril at Thangúlhad'Perhaps it was foolish to think that treating with the Enemy was possible, ${PLAYER}, but there was enough to gain that it seemed worth the attempt. It has now failed, but the forces of Dol Guldur will see the effect of betraying us beneath a flag of peace.

'The main arm of the Golden Host has camped at Thangúlhad, a camp east of here, in Gathbúrz. Present yourself to Ningloril there, for she will have something a ${CLASS} such as you could do for the benefit of the Golden Host in the next stage of this campaign. A word of warning: Ningloril is stern, and not given to idle jest. Do not try her patience, or it will go ill for you.''Are you here to lend your aid, ${PLAYER}? We are met in time of war, though it be a war for which lasting victory may not come. Celeborn has started the Golden Host marching not to win the day, but as a delaying action.

'Even a failure here will be of some value, for the real aim of the Golden Host is to keep the attention of the Enemy, and that we have for certain. I hope we will live long enough for it to be of consequence.''Ningloril is in Thangúlhad, a camp of the Golden Host located in Gathbúrz, east of here. She will have much work for a ${CLASS} such as you.

'Remember my warning: Ningloril is stern, and not given to idle jest. Do not try her patience.'The Orc armies of Dol Guldur are being assembled in large camps in the northern reaches of Gathbúrz.Búrzkala, Kúfuzg, and Hongoi are Orc-camps in the northern reaches of Gathbúrz.

Ningloril has asked you to slay the uruk-commanders of the large camps in the north of Gathbúrz and to search the camps for plans of battle.Defeat an uruk-commander in BúrzkalaDefeat an uruk-commander in KúfuzgDefeat an uruk-commander in HongoiFind plans of battle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ningloril is in Thangúlhad, the closest camp of the Golden Host to Dol Guldur.

You have defeated the uruk-commanders in Búrzkala, Kúfuzg, and Hongoi and recovered some of their battle plans. Ningloril is waiting for your return.'The Orcs of Dol Guldur are being made into a dangerous fighting force, ${PLAYER}, under the leadership of ferocious uruk-commanders. A great force of the creatures are being organized into troops in several great Orc-camps in the northern reaches of Gathbúrz.

'Bring the fight to these camps: Búrzkala, Kúfuzg, and Hongoi, and defeat their uruk-commanders, for without them the Orcs will be less effective and the oncoming assault must be weaker.

'You should also find any battle plans that may be lying about these camps. We may learn when to expect their attack, that we may brace against it.''Go to the northern reaches of Gathbúrz -- to Búrzkala, Kúfuzg, and Hongoi, the great camps where the Orc-armies are organizing -- and slay as many of that troop as you are able. Slay, too, their commanders, in order to make their oncoming assault less effective, and search the camps for plans of battle so we may know when the attack is coming.

'An attack is inevitable, ${PLAYER}. We can best help ourselves by learning when it will come, rather than deluding ourselves with denial.''I could hear the shouts coming from the Orc-camps even from here, ${PLAYER}; you have done well to sow disarray in the camps of the Orcs!

'Much of these plans are indecipherable to me, but I do recognize the word "dush," meaning sorcery, and this circled area can mean only one thing: peril for the Elves lies there!'Ningloril has studied the plans that you recovered and learned that sorcerers under the tutelage of Gorothúl are raising fell spirits in the Ashenslades.Fell spirits and the sorcerers that draw them forth can be found at Sâd Doldúr and throughout the Ashenslades.

Ningloril has asked you to defeat the fell spirits being bound to the service of the students of Gorothúl in the Ashenslades and to deprive the sorcerers of their spell tomes.Collect spell-tomes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat fell spirits in the Ashenslades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ningloril is at Thangúlhad, in Gathbúrz.

You have defeated fell spirits in the Ashenslades and seized the spell-tomes used by the students of Gorothúl to bind them to their service.'According to these plans of battle, sorcerers under the tutelage of Gorothúl are seeking to draw fell spirits to the service of the armies of Dol Guldur. This is not the first we have heard of this, but it supports the words of Súlthel, a Malledhrim scout who passed this way when returning to Ost Galadh.

'This foul craft of the Enemy cannot be permitted. Travel south and east into the Ashenslades and seek out Sâd Doldúr. Defeat any of the fell spirits the sorcerers there have already bound to their service. Defeat too the students of Gorothúl and seize the spell tomes with which they work their evil.

'None of these sorcerers will have Gorothúl's skill, but they will still be dangerous foes. Underestimate none of the Enemy's forces.''Fell spirits and the sorcerers who draw them forth can be found at Sâd Doldúr and throughout the Ashenslades. Defeat these students of Gorothúl and deprive them of the spell tomes with which they work their evil!''You have done well to bring me these tomes and to defeat the fell spirits you found at Sâd Doldúr before they could be used against us. I will see the tomes destroyed.

'There is little time to be wasted, ${PLAYER}. Scouts report the armies of Gathbúrz may be on the march.'The Golden Host is in peril, for the armies of Gathbúrz are about to be unleashed upon Thangúlhad.Ellunen is in Thangúlhad, preparing for its defence.

Ningloril has asked you to come to the defence of Thangúlhad and directed you to speak with Ellunen.Talk to Ellunen at ThangúlhadEllunen is waiting for you to participate in the defence of Thangúlhad.

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, Fellowship, or Raid group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 60.</rgb>Complete Skirmish: Protectors of ThangúlhadEllunen is at Thangúlhad, the camp of the Golden Host in Gathbúrz.

You have helped defend Thangúlhad and should report now to Ellunen.Talk to Ellunen at Thangúlhad'The scout Lamwen reports that the Orcs of northern Gathbúrz have begun to move, and a great troop of the creatures march towards our encampment.

'Thangúlhad must be defended, or the sorrows we have endured reaching this point will have been for naught. This cannot be, ${PLAYER}, and will not!

'Ellunen prepares the defences. Speak with him and ready yourself for battle! Thangúlhad must not fall!''This site will soon be the location of a skirmish with the forces of the enemy. Your skills as a ${CLASS} will be of great use here, if you offer them willingly.

'The Orcs hope to drive us from this place in defeat, but I swear by the power given to me as a leader of the Golden Host, by Lord Celeborn of Lórien himself, that we will not fall this day! Stand with us, ${PLAYER}, and together we will protect Thangúlhad from the forces of the enemy!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, Fellowship, or Raid group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 60.</rgb>'Thangúlhad stands still in the control of the Golden Host, a symbol of Lord Celeborn and Lady Galadriel's intent to oppose the forces of the enemy. I am glad, ${PLAYER}.

'We have weathered their attack. Let them now fear ours!''We must stand against the Orc-armies of Gathbúrz, ${PLAYER}! You must aid us in the skirmish with their advance parties! We must protect Thangúlhad!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest involves a Skirmish that can be completed at Solo, Duo, Small Fellowship, Fellowship, or Raid group sizes by using the Skirmish Join Panel. This Skirmish has a minimum level of 60.</rgb>'Ellunen is here in Thangúlhad. Speak with him and prepare for battle. The armies are marching as we speak, you and I, and every moment you stand here is a moment wasted!'The ancient homes of the interred dead have been violated. Cairn-stones that once stood as markers for the honoured dead are now being corrupted towards a dark purpose.The corrupted cairn-stones lie to the north of Trac-plas, south-west of Mincham's camp.
  
Mincham asked you to seek out corrupted cairn-stones, examine them, and report back with your findings.Investigate cairn-stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mincham's camp is north-east of Trac-plas.

You should return to Mincham and report that you discovered a strange liquid had been poured on the cairn-stones, and that several dark markings were engraved upon them as well.Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs'According to Algraig legends, the barrows of the interred dead are marked with cairn-stones.  These cairn-stones are rememberances of past glories and the stories of the dead. Recently, however, several of the cairn-stones located north of Trac-plas have been cruelly corrupted, violating the resting places of the dead.

'Will you look for these markers and examine them, so that we might see what has happened to them and what the cause of the corruption might be?

'Travel south along the road, until you reach a broken bridge. Then head westwards to the entrance to Trac-plas. You will find the corrupted stones to the north.''The symbols and the liquid that you discovered are strong evidence of the evil that has befallen the Lich Bluffs.

'I fear an ancient enemy has emerged, and the unrest in the tombs may be its work.''The corrupted cairn-stones lie among the barrows to the north of Trac-plas.'Among the newly-risen wights, several older, more powerful creatures have been sighted. Perhaps defeating these creatures may shed light upon the emerging threat.Trac-plas lies south and west of Mincham's camp.

There are older, more powerful wights haunting the barrows of Trac-plas among their younger brethren. Mincham has asked you to seek out these creatures and defeat them.Defeat grim Ashenwight-captains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mincham's is located north and west of Trac-plas.

You should return to Mincham and let him know that you have dispatched several of the grim Ashenwight-captains.Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs'At Trac-plas, several elder wights have been sighted among the newly-risen. These creatures appear to be gathering the risen wights and are trying to control them. Perhaps the elder wights may reveal what purpose, beyond the spread of terror, these raisings serve.

'Will you seek out these wight-captains and defeat as many as you can find?

'They can be found in the upper portions of Trac-plas, on the southern border of the Lich Bluffs, west of the main road.''The description of these captains match the descriptions of several creatures we have faced before. I fear these wights may have a powerful master.

'I must thank you for seeking them out and putting them to rest.''The captains of the Ashenwights are foul indeed and must be defeated.'Ianudirel has discovered the location of a number of evil relics being wielded by the sorcerers in Taur Morvith to summon fell spirits.The dagger and cup are held in the ruins of Sâd Morangol. The staff may be carried by one of the sorcerers of Sâd Morangol.

Ianudirel has asked you to collect three relics -- a dagger, a cup, and a staff -- from the sorcerers of Sâd Mornagol.Find the accursed daggerFind the accursed cupFind the accursed staffIanudirel can be found just south of the bridge at Krul Lugu.

You should return the accursed relics you have gathered to Ianudirel.'When I was spying on those ruins to the south-east, I saw a number of sorcerers wielding accursed relics in rituals meant to draw these fell spirits to Taur Morvith.

'I have seen three such accursed relics. A dagger, a cup, and a staff. The dagger and cup are held in the ruins themselves, but I was unable to find where the staff is kept. I believe that one of the sorcerers must carry it upon his person?

'If you could sneak in and lay your hands upon these accursed items, it might prevent them from summoning more fell spirits, which would be a great relief to us.''Recover the implements of the sorcerers' foul rituals, ${PLAYER}. A stop must be put to their evil.''You found all of the relics? Well done!

'I will return these to Ost Galadh as soon as I am able. Agorin will properly dispose of them.'Below Drug Haniad, within an abandoned crypt, resides the source of the darkness creeping into the Lich Bluffs.Mincham is at his camp in the Lich Bluffs.

You should speak with Mincham when you are prepared, and he will lead you to the entrance of Lhe Colvern.Talk to Mincham in the Lich BluffsMincham's camp lies in a small grove of trees, north of Drug Haniad.

You should return to Mincham and inform him that the ritual has been stopped and that a greater force is behind the raising of the wights in the Lich Bluffs.Talk to Mincham  in the Lich Bluffs'Beneath Drug Haniad lies an ancient crypt that appears to be the cause of the darkness that is growing in the southern Lich Bluffs. One of our scouts recently reported seeing a crude entrance dug into the ground there, and from within he heard dark chanting.

'Could you seek out the entrance to this barrow and disrupt whatever foul ritual is taking place down below? If so, speak with me again.''I am glad to see that you were able to disrupt that grisly ritual. From what I understand, the body that was on the table was a new vessel for Ferndúr the Virulent. 

'I fear that, unknown to us, one of the Lords of the Gauntmen settled here some time ago and has been using the barrows of the Lich Bluffs to raise wights for an army of his own.

'Thank you for disrupting the ritual, as it may have well saved the lives of the entire Grey Company and many of the men and women that call this land home.''My scout entered the cave and reported foul chanting deep within. When he ventured further into the cavern, he saw several dark figures overseeing a grisly ritual behind a locked gate.

'You should try to unlock the gate and disrupt the ritual.'The Orcs of Taur Morvith have unleashed packs of Wargs to harry intruders who would dare approach through the forests to the north.Wargs can be found roaming throughout Taur Morvith.

Iavassúl has asked you to hunt down the Wargs roaming Taur Morvith and collect their war-collars as trophies.Collect war-collars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith.

You should return the war-collars to Iavassúl.'You may have noticed a number of Wargs roaming about this diseased forest. The Orcs unleashed a large pack of them shortly after our arrival -- presumably to keep our forces at bay while they strengthened their defences.

'Should you wish to hunt them, you will find that the Wargs are fitted with war-collars that make fine trophies; otherwise, we risk having them find us here and bring the Orcs down upon us with their accursed howls.''The hounds of Sauron must be routed, ${PLAYER}. Our forces are slowed by their harassment.''It appears that you have dealt with the Wargs admirably! The Orcs will no doubt miss their loathsome companions, but for the time being, this will allow the Malledhrim a free hand as we try to dislodge the Orcs from their outposts in Taur Morvith.'A number of Ivorel's scouts have not returned from their mission in the Scuttledells. Miluimil saw some of them entrapped by the spiders to the north.The ensnared Elves may be found in the nests of the spiders to the north of Ivorel's camp.

Miluimil has asked you to set forth to free his ensnared companions.Free Elves from the cocoons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Miluimil is at Ivorel's camp, south of the spider-nests.

You should speak with Miluimil and tell him that the scouts have been freed.Talk to Miluimil at Ivorel's camp'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. You have not come at a particularly auspicious time. Most of our number is already lost to us out in the lands that we call the Scuttledells.

'We were sent out to scout the terrain but a few days ago, but only a few of our small company have yet returned, and they tell of twisted ravines crawling with evil things. To the north, in particular, are the spiders that give this place its name, and it is there that I believe several of our comrades have been ensnared by the spiders.

'There may yet be time to free them before they are slain, if we are fortunate. Can you assist with this deed?''Fuirgam has forbidden his troops from entering the Scuttledells. He gauges the odds of a band of regular soldiers facing ambush and entrapment too great to risk so many Elves.

'I cannot say that our scouts have fared much better though, and it leaves us to dig our way out of our own mess without the help of soldiers from Ost Galadh.''It appears that some of the scouts did not survive...I had feared as much, but at least you were able to rescue most of them.

'Unfortunately, even among those who returned, most were too ill from the spiders' venom and their entrapment to continue, and I had to send them back to Ost Galadh to recover.

'Could I have you stay here for a while longer to aid us? The Scuttledells are too dangerous for us to leave unattended while facing the forces in Dol Guldur.'Deep within the forgotten barrows of the Lich Bluffs lies Crug Fernvael, the tomb of Cadelhin's father. His defeat might lead to his people's freedom from an ancient curse.Cadelhin is at Crug Cadelhin in the Lich Bluffs.

You should talk to Cadelhin when you are ready to travel into Crug Fernvael to confront Cadelhin's father.Lhudd is at the Hall of Sanctuary in the Lich Bluffs.

Following Fernvael's defeat, many shades have been released from their ancient curse. You should return to Lhudd with the news.Talk to Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary'Following your departure, I was visited by a powerful emissary of the Rhi Helvarch. As he was the spirit that blessed my union, I asked if there was a way for my people to be freed from this ancient curse. He asked that I choose a champion to go forth and confront my father with what he has done.

'I sent my men to seek out a safe path to Crug Fernvael. I will need to enlist your aid to defeat my father, so our people might be released.

'I will return the amulet that you have mended, as it may aid you when fighting him. Will you travel to Crug Fernvael and defeat him?''My men have returned and have found an entrance to the place where my father was put to rest.

'Please be careful... the shades of his men have been seen there and will attack anyone who might enter therein.''I am eternally grateful to you, ${PLAYER}.''With the death of Fernvael, many of the shades in this land are free to move on. The shades that remain have been weakened.

'Your actions bring honour to yourself and your bloodline.'Fell spirits drawn into the world by powerful sorcery now haunt the hills of Taur Morvith.Fell spirits gather in the hills south of the river in Taur Morvith.

Ianudirel asked you to banish the fell spirits that are gathering in Taur Morvith.Defeat fell spirits in Taur Morvith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ianudirel is hiding in the hills just south of the bridge in Taur Morvith.

You should let Ianudirel know that you have done what she asked.Talk to Ianudirel in Taur Morvith'I have seen many fell spirits wandering these hills, but I do not yet know from whence they came.

'If they are gathering there in numbers, then something is drawing them hence...we will need to deal with that soon but until we discover the source, I need you to banish as many of those spirits as you can lest their power grow too great.''Well fought, but it bodes ill for us that there are so many spirits here.

'We must find whatever power is drawing these spirits to Taur Morvith and dispatch it swiftly.''Fell spirits of Morgoth have begun to appear in Taur Morvith, and their terror spreads through every living thing. We must hinder these creatures as we may, ${PLAYER}.'Within Lhe Colvarn, the ancient crypt below Drug Haniad, several wights are gathering components to fuel rituals across the Lich Bluffs.Lhe Colvarn, an ancient crypt below Drug Haniad, may be found due east of the main road, in the southern portion of the Lich Bluffs. A small crypt opening that has been dug into the ground.

Mincham asked you to locate the entrance to Lhe Colvarn and enter therein.Find Lhe ColvarnThe wights and their ritual components may be found in Lhe Colvarn, beneath Drug Haniad, south of Mincham's camp.

Mincham asked you to enter Lhe Colvarn and destroy the wights' ritual components.Retrieve and destroy components (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mincham's camp is located north of Drug Haniad, along the road.

You should return to Mincham and let him know that you retrieved and destroyed the ritual components of the wights at Lhe Colvarn.Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs'From within Lhe Colvarn, the ancient crypt below Drug Haniad, wights are gathering materials for the foul rituals taking place in and among the barrows of the Lich Bluffs.

'I must ask you to enter Lhe Colvarn and seek out the wights there. Their ritual components must be retrieved before they can attain their goal.

'Travel south along the road until you locate a small crypt opening that has been dug into the ground at Drug Haniad.''The destruction of those ritual components is but a step in stemming the tide of darkness throughout the Lich Bluffs. I thank you for all of your hard work.''The entrance to Lhe Colvarn lies to the south in Drug Haniad.''The ritual components of the wights must be retrieved and destroyed, ${PLAYER}.'Defeat giants in Enedwaith.Defeat giants in EnedwaithDefeat many giants in Enedwaith.Defeat giants in EnedwaithIvorel feels personally responsible for poor Hal Tiller, a young hobbit that accompanied her scout expedition.Black dogs can be found throughout the Scuttledells.

Ivorel has asked you to hunt down black dogs in the hopes of finding some clue -- or perhaps the remains -- of Hal Tiller.Collect clues to Hal's fate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ivorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells.

You should return to Ivorel and show her the remains that you have collected.'I must not give up all hope for poor Hal, though in a place as cruel as this I dare not hold too much....

'We must hunt down the black dogs that cornered him and see if we can find any clues to confirm his downfall... or perhaps a body so that we might at least put him to rest, though the Black Dogs are rarely so considerate as to leave much behind.''What possessed an innocent such as Hal to join us out here? These halflings are not known for such spirit so far as I have heard, though tales do speak of a few. Nevertheless, even the boldest halfling should not come to such a place as this!''What are these...? No!

'Are these all that remains of Hal Tiller? I was a fool to ever let him come here!

'I will see his bravery avenged! The creature who did this deed must pay thrice-fold!'Defeat gwiber in Enedwaith.Defeat gwiber in EnedwaithDefeat many gwiber in Enedwaith.Defeat gwiber in EnedwaithIvorel, the leader of a scout expedition into the Scuttledells, is concerned about the fate of Hal Tiller, an adventuresome young hobbit who asked to be allowed to aid the Elves on their expedition into Mirkwood. Ivorel fears that the inexperienced hobbit may have been slain by the horrors lurking in the clefts of the Scuttledells.Search the southern Scuttledells for signs of Hal Tiller.

Ivorel suggested a few places where he might most likely be found as part of the mission he was assigned, but she believes that he is most likely dead.Search east of the Pool of TranquilitySearch the paths north of the Pool of TranquilityIvorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells.

You should return to Ivorel and show her the pack you found.'Greetings, traveller. My name is Ivorel, and I serve at Celeborn's request as the scout-leader for the Malledhrim expedition into Mirkwood. Alas! His trust in me was misplaced, for we have come to ruin here in this twisted place! Few of my scouts have returned at all, but worst of all is the loss of poor Hal Tiller!

'Hal was a young hobbit of an unusually adventurous strain who begged to join us in this expedition. He was also a burglar with an unusually light step -- even for his kind -- and of such earnest heart that I accepted... and in so doing I surely signed the warrant for his death. My fellow scouts were all of fine mettle and experience, and the risks they knew well, but poor Hal was but a child compared to them, and I should never have allowed it.

'I cannot abandon my watch for my duty to the Malledhrim is clear and should any of my scouts yet live they shall come here. Yet you are clearly an adventurer of great mettle to have come this far yourself -- would you help me discover the fate of poor Hal? There must be some trace of him in the Scuttledells....''I saw several halflings accompanying the band of strangers who came into Lórien these past weeks, and they were taken into the Lady's presence and set, or so I am told, to tasks most dire.

'I had thought that perhaps they held some hidden strength, not apparent to the eye, and so I allowed young Hal to join us when he offered his services.

'Now though I feel sick, as if I had sent a child into battle ahead of me. He must be alive, or I shall never forgive myself.''What a cruel fate for such a young innocent! These look to be the claw-marks of a Black Dog on the pack -- there is only a spark of hope left, for we have not yet found his body.

'Most likely because he was torn to pieces by the Black Dogs....'Within the depths of the barrows, foul creatures are performing a dark ritual of death.Levers that control the locking mechanism to the gate of the summoning chamber can be found in several large antechambers scattered within the barrow.Locate and use first leverLocate and use second leverLocate and use third leverIn the furthest chamber of the ancient barrow, behind the now-open steel gate, resides the ritual chamber. Enter the chamber and disrupt the dark ritual that is taking place.Enter the chamber to disrupt the ritualDefeat the ritualist performing the ceremony on the fallen corpse.Defeat IargandirWithin the depths of Crug Fernvael lies the restless spirit of Fernvael father of Cadelhin, who brought the curse of the Wild Huntsman down upon them.Find Fernvael's resting place and present the shade with the amulet you remade.Find and confront Fernvael'${PLAYER}, thank you for your assistance, please allow me to lead you from this place. Your service will not be forgotten.'Lhudd has asked you to explore the ancient barrow in an attempt to discover more about the shades that dwell still in the Lich Bluffs. He believes that the shade of Cadelhin may know how to break the curse that binds them.Seek out the tomb of Cadelhin within the barrow and place the amulet thereon.Place the amulet on Cadelhin's tombListen to Cadelhin's tale.Listen to Cadelhin's taleProtect Cadelhin from the shades that seek to do him harm.Talk to Cadelhin'I am grateful to you for your assistance. Weakened am I and weary of this curse. My people suffer from this curse because of my father, but I am not wholly without blame.

'I was a very capable hunter, and sought out the Rhi Helvarch, a powerful spirit near here, to bless my betrothal. Upon completing an arduous challenge, the Rhi Helvarch blessed the amulet that you recently recovered. The marriage was not to last, however, for my father murdered my wife and sundered the amulet. My belief is that when my father slew my wife and broke the amulet that I had given to her, the curse unfolded upon us. Such an act of betrayal is what brought this down upon us.

'Please go, so that I might regain my strength and summon those that would aid me. I will send word to the man that led you to this place when it is time to return.''Following my father's betrayal, I led a group of friends away from my home, as none of my followers could believe what my father and his men had done.

'We saw no other way to avenge this foul deed but to stand against them. Unfortunately, after some time we were defeated, and I was laid in this barrow and held here, never to be free. I will need to gather strength before I can assist you further.

'What? Wait... to arms! The shades of my father's men seek to destroy me and recover the amulet. Please, defend me as I muster my strength.'The Elf-scout Miluimil has been charged with capturing the creature named Gollum to prevent him from falling into the hands of the Orcs.Speak with Miluimil and proceed into the caverns to stop the Orcs pursuing Gollum from capturing him.Defeat the Orcs pursuing GollumTalk to Miluimil to depart from the dark caverns.'Quickly! We must be away from this place!''Quickly! We must be away from this place!'The Orcs of Taur Morvith are in disarray. Iavassúl now has a plan to keep them that way.The guard-towers are in Krul Lugu below Iavassúl's Watch.Place the Malledhrim war-bannerThe guard-towers are in Krul Lugu below Iavassúl's Watch.

Iavassúl has asked you to claim one of the two guard-towers in Taur Morvith with a banner of the Malledhrim, then hold it against the Orcs for a time.Defend the banner of the MalledhrimIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch, above Krul Lugu.

You should speak with Iavassúl regarding your efforts in the Orc-camps.Talk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch'I hope you have prepared yourself for the battle ahead, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs of Taur Morvith may be in disarray, and now is the time to strike against them and shatter their will to fight altogether!

'In each of their fortresses, there is a guard-tower that overlooks the approaches...I want you to either fight or sneak into those encampments and claim the top of one of those towers with a banner of the Malledhrim, then hold it against any Orcs who attempt to reclaim it from you!''Ha! Well fought, ${PLAYER}! Well fought, indeed!

'Surely the Orcs' will to fight will be broken by such valour as you have shown today. With your aid, we shall hold this front, and our forces at Ost Galadh shall be free to lay low the tower of Dol Guldur!''Bring our war-banner to Krul Lugu and defend it against the Orcs...they will learn that it is futile to defy the Malledhrim!'The road leading to Nar's Peak is a long and arduous one.Climb the stairs to Nár's Peak.Ascend the stair to Nár's PeakReach the top of the stairs to Nár's PeakThree gaunt-men called Gaunt-masters have been building a wight-army to use against the Malledhrim.The Gaunt-masters can be found in the eastern reaches of the Scuttledells.

Ivorel has tasked you with destroying the three Gaunt-masters who are raising the Dead from their barrows.Defeat BrungúrDefeat ThorúnDefeat MordelothIvorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells.

You should inform Ivorel of the destruction of the Gaunt-masters.Talk to Ivorel at her camp'The Men of the East who were brought to construct Dol Guldur were driven hard by their masters, yet unbeknownst to them their final resting places were being prepared by evil beings who would become their masters in death as well, once the life was driven from them by their brutal labours.

'In these runes I see the inscriptions of three fell hands...gaunt-masters in the service of the Nine, who even now summon fell spirits to draw the Dead from their graves to move against us.

'These three sorcerers must be destroyed before they complete their rituals, or the numbers of the Dead will multiply greatly, and we may find ourselves hard pressed to hold Ost Galadh from them.''Excellent! With those fiends no longer a threat, the spells they have laid upon the barrows will begin to unravel.

'If the barrows themselves are sealed, then the greater part of the danger shall be contained.''The foul art of raising wights is a sorcery of unequalled evil. That creatures such as the gaunt-men may summon their spirit-brethren from beyond the Void to defile the corpses of Men is unimaginable!'You have taken a sample of a strange foetid liquid from outside one of the barrows in the Lich Bluffs.Mincham's camp is located north and west of the main road, in the north-west portion of the Lich Bluffs.

You should return to Mincham and provide him with a sample of the foul liquid that you have recovered.This strange puddle of foetid liquid may hold some clue as to the corruption occurring in the Lich Bluffs.

The Ranger Mincham might have further insight on the origins of this strange, foul liquid.'The place where you found this horrific liquid bodes ill for all. I fear that this might be one of the instruments that some darker force is employing to raise the wights in the area.

'My hope is that we can locate an intact phial of this liquid so we may discern its origins.'The sorcerers of Taur Morvith have lit a series of pyres across the nearby hills that spew clouds of acrid smoke into the sky and cover the land in a choking haze.The dread pyres have been lit throughout Taur Morvith, south of the river.

Ianudirel has asked you to extinguish the dread pyres of the sorcerers.Extinguish dread pyres (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ianudirel is hidden just south of the bridge in the midst of Taur Morvith.

You should speak with Ianudirel.Talk to Ianudirel'Have you seen the awful fog that often lies upon Taur Morvith? I have found its source, at least in part. There are large pyres built throughout the area south of the river. These pyres are fed by fell spirits, and the smoke they belch out clings to the land, covering it in this suffocating haze.

'I need you to extinguish several of these fires, or soon we will not be able to see anything here -- we may not even be able to breathe....''The sorcerers of Taur Morvith use dread pyres to perform their foul rituals...do what you must, but extinguish those pyres!''You have managed to extinguish some of those pyres? Good! That should secure us some time to deal with whomever -- or whatever -- kindled them.'The Lich Bluffs are the final resting place of many of the fallen from the Algraig clans. However, a dark force has emerged from the shadows, bringing forth wights to attack the living.These creatures move among many of the barrows in the southern reaches of the Lich Bluffs. 
  
Mincham has asked you to seek out and defeat any wights that you might encounter.Defeat wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mincham is located south and slightly east of the large Gondorian ruins in the Lich Bluffs.

You should return to Mincham and let him know that you have defeated many wights.Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs'In the past few months, there have been sightings among the Uch-lûth of foul wights rising from their barrows. These creatures are defiling the ancient dead in a most horrific manner and threatening to spill out into inhabited lands.

'Can you seek out the foul monsters and defeat them?

'The wights can be found throughout the southern and western barrows of the Lich Bluffs.''Thank you...this is a good start to returning the bodies of these poor men and women to rest.

'This may also allow my brethren to pass through these places unmolested.''What evil stirs the dead, I wonder? The raising of wights is the art of but a few -- the Witch-king for one, but others more dire as well.'The location of the final resting place of Cadelhin's father Fernvael has been lost over the years. There are a series of inscriptions which denote his tomb that, once deciphered, will reveal his location.The first cairn-marker may be found outside a barrow to the north of the Hall of Sanctuary.

Lhudd instructed you to find the cairn-markers which denote the house of Fernvael, bearing the mark of a crowned boar. This symbol may also be found among the barrows of Fernvael's followers.Locate the correct inscriptionThe first cairn-marker may be found outside a barrow to the north of the Hall of Sanctuary.

Lhudd instructed you to find the cairn-markers which denote the house of Fernvael, bearing the mark of a crowned boar. This symbol may also be found among the barrows of Fernvael's followers.The second cairn-marker may be found outside a barrow to the south of the Hall of Sanctuary.

Lhudd instructed you to find the cairn-markers which denote the house of Fernvael, bearing the mark of a crowned boar. This symbol may also be found among the barrows of Fernvael's followers.Locate the second inscriptionThe second cairn-marker may be found outside a barrow to the south of the Hall of Sanctuary.

Lhudd instructed you to find the cairn-markers which denote the house of Fernvael, bearing the mark of a crowned boar. This symbol may also be found among the barrows of Fernvael's followers.The third cairn-marker may be found outside a barrow further to the south of the Hall of Sanctuary.

Lhudd instructed you to find the cairn-markers which denote the house of Fernvael, bearing the mark of a crowned boar. This symbol may also be found among the barrows of Fernvael's followers.Locate the last inscriptionThe third cairn-marker may be found outside a barrow further to the south of the Hall of Sanctuary.

Lhudd instructed you to find the cairn-markers which denote the house of Fernvael, bearing the mark of a crowned boar. This symbol may also be found among the barrows of Fernvael's followers.Cadelhin is at Crug Cadelhin in the Lich Bluffs.

Lhudd told you to bring news of Crug Fernvael's location to the shade Cadelhin.Talk to Cadelhin at Crug Cadelhin'With Cadelhin's awakening, it has become of greatest import for us to find the ancient resting place of his father Fernvael. 

'Among the barrows, there may be markings near the entryways that denote who was interred at each place. They may provide clues to the identities of those who are buried within. Seek out these markers in front of the cairns. One of them will be Crug Fernvael, I am certain. Look for the symbol of a crowned boar.

'The first cairn-marker lies to the north of here, the second to the south, and the last even further south, deeper into the barrows. If you find Crug Fernvael, you should bring news of its location to Cadelhin.''The first marker lies to the north of here.''The first marker lies to the north of here.''The second marker lies to the south of here.''The second marker lies to the south of here.''The third marker lies further to the south of here.''The third marker lies further to the south of here.''Bring news of Crug Fernvael to Cadelhin at once!''Your assistance is greatly appreciated, Duvodiad. Our knowledge of my father's final resting place shall lead to my people's freedom. 

'Fernvael will be put to rest.'After sucessfully repairing the amulet, an ancient barrow may reveal evidence of how to put the restless shades in the area at peace.Lhudd is at the Hall of Sanctuary in the Lich Bluffs.

You should travel with Lhudd to discover what lies within the ancient barrow of Cadelhin.Talk to Lhudd at the Hall of SanctuaryLhudd is at the Hall of Sanctuary in the Lich Bluffs.

You should speak with Lhudd again.'The origins of this amulet are very old, and now that it has been repaired, it does indeed appear to be what I have been searching for. 

'The amulet itself is not an extraordinary thing; however, it may be the key to ridding this area of the shades that roam the land. This amulet belonged to Cadelhin, the son of a chieftain, who perished ages ago. I believe that this amulet may be able to be used to awaken him, and that he may be a powerful ally in attempting to cleanse these lands. 

'If you wish, I can lead you to Cadelhin's barrow, so that you might use the amulet to summon him.''Please follow me, Duvodiad, but be on your guard, for there are those that would stand against us in lifting this curse.

'I will escort you to the entrance, but once there you must go alone. Return to me with news of your discoveries.''What Cadelhin speaks of is a tale that has been passed along for generations. 

'His people have fallen to an ancient curse for breaking an oath. They are bound to roam the land without rest, shackled for their atrocities.

'My hope is that by learning what exactly happened we might be able to release them from their curse.'Ivorel is concerned that the damage caused by the Gaunt-masters may not be reversible, but the barrows must be sealed to prevent more of the dead from emerging to threaten the Malledhrim.The barrows lie to the north-east of Ivorel's camp.

Ivorel asked you to shut the barrows of the Scuttledells and place seals of Elven-make upon them so that the fell spirits of Morgoth cannot rise up as wights.Ivorel is at her camp, south-west of the barrows.

You should return to Ivorel with news of your success.'The inscriptions you described to me speak of the great labour that went into the building of Dol Guldur as the abode of the Necromancer. Many men were brought here from the far east, and they worked upon its stones, and their labour was cruel beyond endurance. As they died of weariness, they were interred in the barrows here to continue their servitude eternally as guardians of last resort.

'They remain his servants still, and now are called forth to stay our advance against the tower, animated by fell spirits of Morgoth -- but many remain that have not yet awakened, and we must ensure that they do not come forth in greater numbers. We must seal these barrows so that their inhabitants remain therein forevermore.

'Shut the barrows and place these seals upon them -- these seals were given to me by Agorin before I left Ost Galadh, for she suspected that these barrows would be disturbed. I give them now to you.''It is an evil fate that the shells of simple folk like the Woodmen should be made to serve the Enemy....''You have sealed the doors of the barrows, ${PLAYER}? Well done. We have only to banish the fell wights that roam still in the Scuttledells... then perhaps peace will find this part of the forest.'The foetid liquid you discovered in the barrows of the Lich Bluffs may yet provide a clue to the mystery of the Dead in that place.Wights can be found in great numbers among the southernmost barrows of the Lich Bluffs.

Mincham has asked you to try and recover an intact phial of the foetid liquid from the wights of the Lich Bluffs.Collect an intact corrupted phial from the wights of the Lich BluffsWights can be found in great numbers among the southernmost barrows of the Lich Bluffs.

Mincham has asked you to try and recover an intact phial of the foetid liquid from the wights of the Lich Bluffs.Collect an intact corrupted phial from the wights of the Lich BluffsMincham is at his camp north of the barrows.

You should return to Mincham and deliver the intact corrupted phial you collected.'This liquid you recovered may yet provide us a clue as to the forces behind the raising of the wights in the Lich Bluffs. I have heard of only a few creatures with such power, one of whom is the Witch-king of Angmar, but he is accounted for.

'Perhaps if you can secure an intact phial of this liquid from one of the wights, I may be able to determine something of its origin.

'I have seen many wights wandering among the barrows in the southern hills of the Lich Bluffs.''Perhaps if you can find an intact phial of this liquid, I may be able to determine its source.''Perhaps if you can find an intact phial of this liquid, I may be able to determine its source.''The delivery of this phial is a grim but important discovery. It appears that these phials are being used to corrupt the bodies of the fallen in the Lich Bluffs. It may also partially be the cause of the corrupted cairn-stones.

'We must work quickly to unravel who is behind this plot.'A large pack of Cun Annun haunt the barrows of the Lich Bluffs, presenting a danger to those that would call Enedwaith home.Cun Annun can be found in the southern reaches of the Lichbluffs. 

Mincham has asked you to find and defeat as many Cun Annun as you are able.Defeat Cun Annun (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mincham's camp is south and slightly east of the large Gondorian ruins in the Lich Bluffs.

You should return to Mincham and let him know that you have located and dispatched a pack of Cun Annun.Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs'A large pack of fell spirits the Algraig clans call Cun Annun have settled among the hills and valleys of the Lich Bluffs recently. These creatures are fearsome and are an indication of a darker power at work.  

'Can you seek out Cun Annun in this area and defeat any that you might find? They can be found roaming to the south and east of my camp.

'Be wary, ${PLAYER}, for they are no ordinary hounds. The Cun Annun are demons of the ancient world.''Thank you for dispatching these insidious creatures. I fear that their arrival may give credence to tales of a darker force at work in the Lich Bluffs.''What evil summons forth wights and fell hounds must have great power indeed. We shall have to be cautious.'One of the Malledhrim scouts reported a goblin-like creature out in the ravines, not unlike the creature Gollum.Gollum might be found at one of several locations suggested by Miluimil.

Miluimil has asked you to search for any signs of Gollum in the Scuttledells. You should start with the Pool of Tranquility.Search for signs of Gollum at the Pool of TranquilityGollum might be found at one of several locations suggested by Miluimil.

Miluimil has asked you to search for any signs of Gollum in the Scuttledells. Perhaps you should try the Low Pond.Search for signs of Gollum at the Low PondGollum might be found at one of several locations suggested by Miluimil.

Miluimil has asked you to search for any signs of Gollum in the Scuttledells. Perhaps you should try the Crawling Waters.Search for signs of Gollum at the Crawling WatersMiluimil is at Ivorel's camp in the Scuttledells.

You should return to Miluimil and tell him what you have learned of Gollum's whereabouts.Talk to Miluimil at Ivorel's camp'Fuirgam sent word to look for that Gollum creature? Well, the Scuttledells is an ideal haven for the likes of him, I am afraid. I was part of the effort to capture him on the fringes of Lórien a few weeks ago, but we had little success. One would think he could vanish into thin air, the way he evaded us.

'Very well. I doubt we will find him out here, but at least if we do catch sight of him, these ravines may act to trap him where we can lay hands on him. One of my scouts reported seeing a small, goblin-like creature scuttling furtively about in the Scuttledells. I thought little of it at the time, but if Fuirgam's suspicions are correct, it may have been Gollum.

'Here are a few places where he might be lurking, so keep a sharp eye out.''So, it seems very likely that Gollum is indeed in the Scuttledells, but this news you bring of Orcs and goblins also hunting the Scuttledells is ill indeed.

'It is one thing if we are unable to lay hands upon this Gollum, but quite another if the forces of Dol Guldur were to do so. Fuirgam seemed most concerned that this might occur.

'Whatever happens, ${PLAYER}, we must not allow Gollum to be captured by the Orcs!''I do not know how Fuirgam expects us to catch one such as Gollum in a place like this. I would be tested to lay hands upon one as slippery as him if I were to find him in an open field! But here?

'Yet the tone of his message seemed almost desperate -- as if all might be undone were Gollum taken by the Enemy -- and so we must bend all our will to his capture if it be possible at all.''I do not know how Fuirgam expects us to catch one such as Gollum in a place like this. I would be tested to lay hands upon one as slippery as him if I were to find him in an open field! But here?

'Yet the tone of his message seemed almost desperate -- as if all might be undone were Gollum taken by the Enemy -- and so we must bend all our will to his capture if it be possible at all.''I do not know how Fuirgam expects us to catch one such as Gollum in a place like this. I would be tested to lay hands upon one as slippery as him if I were to find him in an open field! But here?

'Yet the tone of his message seemed almost desperate -- as if all might be undone were Gollum taken by the Enemy -- and so we must bend all our will to his capture if it be possible at all.'Recently, several barrows in the Lich Bluffs have been disturbed. The bodies of the dead have been removed from their crypts and desecrated.The barrows Mincham wants you to investigate are located to the east of the road, along the southern border of the Lich Bluffs.

Mincham has asked you seek out the entrances to some of the barrows and investigate the corpses of the recently disturbed dead.Find the first skeleton pileFind the second skeleton pileFind the third skeleton pileMincham is at his camp, north of the barrows.
 
You should return to Mincham and report what you found at the ancient barrows.Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs'These barrows have long been home to the dead of the Algraig clans of the Dunlendings -- and many other older peoples -- the bodies lain to rest after the customs of these people. Recently, however, several of the barrows have been desecrated for some nefarious purpose. I have heard that some of the corpses have recently been dragged out of their resting places and left for scavengers.

'Perhaps you would be willing to travel into the barrows where these bodies have been seen and investigate for me? It is a gruesome task, but I fear a great evil is growing within this place.

'The barrows I speak of are located east of the main road, upon the southern border of the Lich Bluffs.''My fears are true, it seems: a dark force is at work, raising wights across the Lich Bluffs. It is a tragedy that the bodies of these good people are being used for such nefarious purposes. 

'We will yet discover what evil force is at work here.''I fear that a great evil is behind the desecration of the dead.'A powerful Orc named Durshâtaz keeps his underlings in Taur Morvith in line with strength and a cruel lash, but without his domineering will to force them to battle, the Orcs there will likely fall to chaos, giving the Elves a free hand to act in the area.Durshâtaz can be found at Krul Lugu, below Iavassúl's Watch.

Iavssúl has asked you to find and defeat the Orc-leader Durshâtaz. He suggests trying to attract his attention as he roams between the two fortresses.Defeat DurshâtazIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch, above Krul Lugu.

You should return to Iavassúl with news of your victory.Talk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch'It seems that there is one thing left to hold the Orcs in check from a complete rout -- one powerful Orc-leader with a cruel whip and the strength to bend the others to his will.

'If you can find and defeat this Durshâtaz, as he is called, the final pin holding the forts of Krul Lugu together will be removed, and we shall be free to move as we wish against them.

'One of my scouts tells me that Durshâtaz travels frequently between the two encampments, trying to keep his underlings in line. If you can catch him in the open, you might be able to defeat him before help arrives.''Durshâtaz is dead? Elbereth be praised! Without his strength to hold them together, the Orcs are now bereft of leadership and at our mercy. You have opened the way for us, ${PLAYER}...now we shall discover whatever strength they may have been hiding on the other side of that river.

'What is that? Of course there is something over there! Who would build a pair of fortresses to defend a bridge if there was not something of value on the other side?

'I have already had my scouts slip across during the distraction afforded by your previous forays. They should be back shortly.''The Orcs of Krul Lugu are disheartened, and they will collapse completely, I believe, if their chieftain is slain.'Fuirgam has asked you to lend your aid to Rodelleth as she launches her assault upon Gathbúrz on the slopes before Dol Guldur.Rodelleth is encamped at the captured tower of Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz, east of Ost Galadh.

Fuirgam has asked you to join Rodelleth's forces in battle against the Orcs of Gathbúrz before the gates of the tower of Dol Guldur.Report to Rodelleth in Gathbúrz'The battle has been joined upon the slopes above us ${PLAYER}. Fierce Rodelleth leads the Malledhrim in battle against the Orcs encamped in Gathbúrz, and strives to lay siege to the tower itself.

'Ultimately, she has not the Elves to defeat the walls of Dol Guldur, but with the aid of valiant warriors such as yourself, she may inflict grievious harm upon their forces.

'Once you have completed your tasks here, you should join her forces above.''Fuirgam has sent more reinforcements? What does he take me for, some delicate maiden in need of heroic rescue?

'Very well then. There are more than enough Orcs to go around, so take your pick - but unless the Lady herself strides forth or Fuirgam provides enough Elves that we can stride over its walls upon our own fallen, we're not likely to breach that tower by force.

'Still, we'll make a merry game of it, and any enemy who does dare emerge will pay swiftly for their folly.''Once you have completed your tasks here in Emyn Lûm, Rodelleth needs all the soldiers we can muster in Gathbúrz.'The Cargûl, Mâb Rhûnadan, dwells among the ruins of Sâd Morangol, using a corrupt altar to summon fell spirits to Taur Morvith.Mâb Rhûnadan and his altar may be found at Sâd Morangol.

Ianudirel has asked you to destroy the altar of Mâb Rhûnadan or defeat the Cargûl himself.Defeat Mâb RhûnadanDestroy the corrupted altarIanudirel is just south of the bridge at Krul Lugu.

You should return to Ianudirel with news of your success.Talk to Ianudirel'I have found where the Enemy conducts the rituals to summon fell spirits to Taur Morvith. There is an altar in the crumbling cellar of one of the ruins to the south-east...but I also found out what power is behind it. There is a Cargûl -- one of the cursed knights of Eärnur -- hiding somewhere in those ruins! I have heard his name whispered by his servants. He is known as Mâb Rhûnadan. 

'I consulted Agorin on the matter. It seems that this creature is a favoured apprentice to one of the Nine, and a powerful sorcerer in his own right. Be very careful should you encounter him!

'If you can make your way to the altar and destroy it, that should put an end to their power here for the time being -- barring that, you may have to destroy the Cargûl himself. I also doubt he will allow you to interfere with his place of power unmolested.''Very good, ${PLAYER}! The Nine will surely be angered that one of their favoured slaves has been destroyed, but this should break the spells gathering power against us here.

'Now Fuirgam should be able to focus his attention towards Gathbúrz and Dol Guldur and not have to worry about a strike at his flank from Taur Morvith.''Destroy the altar, ${PLAYER}, or if you cannot, defeat the Cargûl himself. To be forced to such corruption must be a terrible thing for a knight such as he once was...free him!'This letter reveals that a group of the Draig-lûth are in the process of making plans to send men to kill anyone hiding in an old dwarf home.The dwarf-hall can be found high within a mountain pass, north of the river on the north-west face of Thrór's Coomb.

As the note reveals a threat upon those that make their home in the heights of the mountains, you may wish to warn them.Travel to the dwarf-hall in Thrór's CoombYou have recovered a note that reads as follows:

'In the western reaches, there is said to be a small dwarf-home located in the mountains. It is believed that several duvodiad have gained entrance and are encamped there. We must enter this lair and kill everyone within. The consequences will be severe if you fail. 

'Use care as you approach the cave, for very powerful draig-math -- gwiber and others -- dwell in that vale, do not send scouts as lone scouts would likely become draig-fodder.'

Perhaps you should traverse the pass and speak with these hold refugees and warn them of the coming attack.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest opens up a number of fellowship quests and is not intended for solo play.</rgb>'You are quite bold to enter this hall unannounced. However, thank you for bringing this note to our attention.  We shall prepare the hall for unwelcome visitors. 

'Be wary as you journey in Thrór's Coomb, for there are quite a few dangerous creatures in these lands.'Mincham is interested in finding the remaining fragments of the amulet you brought him, in hopes that a local hermit might be able to decipher the mystery it represents.The second half of the broken amulet may be found on shades throughout the Lich Bluffs.

When you locate the other half of the broken amulet, seek out and locate the hermit Lhudd in a small grove of trees to the west of the road called the Hall of Sanctuary.The second half of the broken amulet may be found on shades throughout the Lich Bluffs.

When you locate the other half of the broken amulet, seek out and locate the hermit Lhudd in a small grove of trees to the west of the road called the Hall of Sanctuary.Collect the second half of the broken amuletLhudd the hermit dwells at the Hall of Sanctuary, west of the main road and south-west of Mincham's camp.

Mincham told you to bring both halves of the amulet to Lhudd the hermit.'The hermit who inhabits a small grove near here has been searching for relics from older days, and this fragment you brought me appears to resemble some of those things he seeks.

'You should seek out the shades that have been haunting this place. My hope is that you might be able to find the missing half of the amulet among them.

'Please take this fragment and seek the other half. If you can complete the amulet, bring it to the hermit Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary, south-west of here. He may be able to unravel this mystery.''Seek the second fragment of the amulet, ${PLAYER}. I am confident that you are correct...it should shed some light upon the mystery of the Oathbreakers.''Seek the second fragment of the amulet, ${PLAYER}. I am confident that you are correct...it should shed some light upon the mystery of the Oathbreakers.''If you have found the remaining fragment of the amulet, bring it to Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary.''Ah, I see your Ranger friend has sent you.

'I hope that the two pieces of this amulet when mended become the object that I have long sought. My belief is that this amulet may be the key to an ancient rheg -- a curse -- that has held the land and causes Men to wander as shades across the Lich Bluffs. 

'Thank you for delivering these to me, as I truly hope it may allow these spirits to be released from their suffering.'The Elven scout Ianudirel was sent ahead to explore the far side of the river from Krul Lugu, but she has not yet returned.Ianudirel may be found on the far side of the river from Krul Lugu.

Iavassúl has asked you to find Ianudirel, his sister, and help her to return safely, if she still lives.Talk to Ianudirel to assist in her escapeIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith.

You should report to Iavassúl regarding his sister's rescue.Talk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch'It seems I may have been overhasty in sending my scouts out across the bridge. One of them who goes by the name Ianudirel has not yet reported back, and I grow worried.

'See if you can find her upon the far embankment. If she is not too sorely wounded or dead, then she should be trying to win her way across...but her path may be barred.

'Also, while I know it is improper to say it under these circumstances...she is my sister, and I would be personally grateful if you are able to ensure her safe return.''My sister is safe for the time being, ${PLAYER}, and the information she brought us was of great importance.

'Something far more dangerous than Orcs lurks in the ruins upon the far side of that bridge -- a servant of the Nine, if Ianudirel has marked her guess correctly!

'We need to deal with this quickly! My sister saw many fell spirits gathering to the call of this servant, and their power could prove a greater threat to us if it is allowed to build.''Greetings, my good ${RACE}. You are a welcome sight indeed in this dark place. I have been awaiting my chance to cross the bridge for nearly a day, but there are too many eyes searching for me -- and not all of them belong to Orcs....

'Something terrible lurks on this side of the river, and I need to inform my brother of it!

'What say we take our chances now? With the two of us, I think we will have a good chance of fighting our way across, even if we are discovered.''Find my sister, ${PLAYER}. I have not heard from her since she went out to scout the land.'A shadow has fallen upon the Lich Bluffs, the ancient burial grounds of the Algraig clans of Dunland and Enedwaith. The Rangers of the Grey Company have sent one of their number to investigate.The ranger camp is located south and slightly west of Harndirion in the Lich Bluffs.

Find Mincham and speak to him of the curse upon the lichbluffs.Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs'You have aided us, ${PLAYER}, but it also appears that you have brought great strife to our lands - you may wish to move on before too many of our people blame their woes upon your name.

'The southern road through Enedwaith passes through the area known as the Lich Bluffs. This grim land is the ancient burial ground of the Algraig clans of Dunland and Enedwaith. Those lands have long been accursed, but rumour holds that the outsiders have foolishly built a camp near its bounds.

'You should go and warn them of their danger - and tell them to leave our lands if they wish to maintain any peace between our peoples.

'The outsider's camp is located south-west of Harndirion, on the west side of the road. Watch yourself. You have likely made powerful enemies this day.''The southern road through Enedwaith traverses the area known as the Lich Bluffs. This grim land is the ancient burial ground of the Algraig clans of Dunland and Enedwaith. We have heard rumour that a shadow and a curse has fallen upon the land, so we have sent Mincham to investigate.

'Will you seek our companion out and see if he requires any assistance? If indeed the shadow has grown in that grim place, we may have to find a different path southwards.

'Mincham's camp is located south-west of Harndirion, on the west side of the road. Be well and be wary, my friend.''Take care ${PLAYER}, your aid is appreciated, but we must deal with these problems ourselves now.''There are few among us who are so willing to dwell among the Dead...Mincham is a strange one....''${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. This place is grim and dark and foul in such a way that even the Fields of Fornost are not.

'There appears to be a large number of wights that have been raised recently and Oathbreaker shades that haunt the land. I may need your help.'In the depths of Trac-Plas, several wights are enacting a grisly ritual to bring more of their kind to life.Trac-Plas lies to the south and west of Mincham's camp.

Mincham asked you to defeat the wights performing the foul rituals at Trac-Plas.Defeat grim Ashenwight ritualists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mincham's camp is located south and slightly west of the large Gondorian ruins in the Lich Bluffs.

You should return to Mincham and let him know that you have defeated the ritualists and disrupted their ritual.Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs'There have been reports of dark rituals being enacted upon barrows near Trac-plas. These creatures are said to be creating the vile liquid that you have discovered. 

'Will you seek out these creatures and defeat the wights performing the ritual? 

'Travel south along the road, until you reach the broken bridge. From there, head westwards into Trac-plas.''With the disruption of the dark rituals, the wights will be unable to quickly raise more of their foul brethren. You have done a great deed for the peoples of Enedwaith and the Grey Company.''The wights of the Lich Bluffs must be hindered in their vile plans.'Ivorel wishes to learn the origins of the Dead that stalk the eastern reaches of the Scuttledells.The barrows are in the eastern reaches of the Scuttledells, north-east of Ivorel's camp.

Ivorel has asked you to study the stones in the barrows, looking for any engravings that might describe their history and give some clue as to the nature of the threat they contain.Examine engraved stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ivorel's camp is south-west of the barrows.

You should return to Ivorel with the engraved stones you found.'A word of caution, ${PLAYER}...if you head into the Scuttledells towards the east, you will soon find yourself among a number of barrows from which the Dead have risen to serve our Enemy. It was for good reason that he once hid beneath the name of the Necromancer after all.

'These are not ancient barrows, however. None such were here in the time when my people lived in Emyn Lûm.

'Thus I do not know who -- or what -- rises up against us now. Seek out the barrow-stones if you can and take note of their engravings. Perhaps we can learn more about the nature of this place and how best to subdue it.''I see. The runes you have discovered tell a painful tale indeed. One of the Men brought by Sauron from the East was literally worked to death in the construction of his fortress here upon Amon Lanc many years ago.

'Even in death these Men are yet forced to serve, their barrows serving as a line of defence should Dol Guldur be pressed. Or their bodies at least, for the Dark Lord cannot bind their spirits.''The Fate of Men is puzzling indeed to we of the Firstborn. To die and leave the world itself? To go where? It is said that even the Lords of the Uttermost West do not know the full answer.

'But no matter their fate, it is a dishonour to allow creatures such as the gaunt-men to make use of their empty husks.'One would think that Wargs on a full belly would be sluggish....Defeat Kranklob after allowing Wargs to eat all the meat slabs throughout the Warg-pits of Dol GuldurThis piece of boar-meat, while slightly discoloured, seems to be a wonderful cut of meat. Perhaps someone in Ost Forod might be really looking for something to hit the spot.Parr Chopley is in Ost Forod in Evendim, far to the north of the Shire.

You should bring the boar-meat to Parr Chopley.Deliver the boar-meat to Parr Chopley in Ost ForodYou have gathered a perfect cut of boar-meat, which brings to mind a tale of woe you overheard from a bard:

'Poor Parr Chopley has left all he has known and struck forth into the world, finding himself in Evendim, in Ost Forod.

'The sad little hobbit has been searching high and low for a little piece of boar to remind him of home.'

Perhaps you should travel north to Ost Forod and seek out this hobbit. He may appreciate this prize piece of boar-meat.'Oh me, oh my, what do you have there?

'Could that possibly be a little cut of boar-meat found within the confines of Evendim. 

'Thank you so much, I will go and cook it at once.'The Orcs of the Ashenslades have stockpiled ore at the camp of Gâthlata, awaiting shipment up to Dol Guldur.Gâthlata lies to the south-east of Mithecad.

Scattered throughout the small camp of Gâthlata, several piles of ore can be found. Eirien has asked you to collect a few samples of the ore and bring it back to her.Collect blighted ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eirien is at Mithechad, north-west of Gâthlata.

You should return the samples of ore to Eirien.'Several of our scouts have reported that many shipments of ore have been moved through Gâthlata on its way to Dol Guldur and that there are still many stockpiles awaiting shipment from the camp.

'We must determine the quality of this ore. If it is as blighted as the trees of the forest, I do not much fear its strength; however, if it remains untouched by the blight, it may be used to forge powerful weapons for the Enemy's use.

'If you would, go to Gâthlata and collect a few samples of the ore for me. The encampment can be found by travelling along the road to the south-east.''Travel south-east to Gâthlata, collect a few samples of ore, and bring them to me.''This ore appears to be imbued with a strange quality that was not found in the discarded ore in Garmadh-maudhûl.

'Fortunately, despite its strange appearance, it does appear as if the blight affects the ore; however, it appears to merely change the colour of this ore.'Unravel the Epic Story for Allies of the King.Complete 'Prologue: Messages from Lórien'Complete 'Book 1 Chapter 9: The Gathering of the Grey Company'Complete 'Book 2 Chapter 15: An Echo of Days Past'Complete 'Book 3 Chapter 11: Grief and Insight'Complete 'Book 4, Chapter 30: The Rescue'Complete 'Book 5, Chapter 4: The Prince of Rohan'Complete 'Book 6, Chapter 12: Mists of Anduin'Complete 'Volume III Book 7: A Fellowship Endangered'Complete 'Volume III Book 8: Into the Riddermark'Complete 'Volume III Book 9: The Third Marshal'Complete 'Volume III Book 10: Snows of Wildermore'Complete 'Volume III Book 11: The Golden Hall'Complete 'Volume III Book 12: War in the Westemnet'Complete 'Volume III Book 13: Helm's Deep'Complete 'Volume III Book 14: The Waters of Isengard'One of the Malledhrim has been wounded, and fallen behind enemy lines. While the valiant warrior can still move, he can fight only weakly and requires your aid to escape from enemy territory.Aid the fallen Malledhrim warrior in his escape from the war-torn fortifications of Gathbúrz, back towards Thangúlhad.Escort the wounded Elf to safetyHandelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

