'I fear that while this creature was powerful and deadly, it may not be the same beast that has pushed the brood of gwiber out from their mountain home, however....'The Wargs of Gathbúrz are led by Athdurub, a Warg-rider with a reputation for cunning and viciousness.Athdurub patrols the woods of Gathbúrz.

Rodelleth has asked you to hunt down and defeat the Warg-rider Athdurub, commander of the Wargs of Gathbúrz.Defeat Commander AthdurubRodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Rodelleth with tidings of Athdurub's defeat.Talk to Rodelleth at Thangúlhad'The Wargs of Gathbúrz are led by a particularly cunning goblin named Athdurub. His cunning and viciousness is matched by the size and power of the Warg he rides. Together they have already claimed the lives of several of the Malledhrim, striking without warning, then fleeing into the shadows of the forest as we advanced.

'For now, he has withdrawn into Gathbúrz to help organize the Wargs against us, and I would have you strike against him while he can be more easily found and cornered -- even if it means dealing with several of his minions as you hunt.

'He was seen patrolling the woods of Gathbúrz, so keep a wary eye out for him, lest he take you by surprise.''I hear from the others that Athdurub the rider is no more, and that he fell at your hands.

'And so the Malledhrim are avenged for their fallen! Well done.''The vile Wargs of Dol Guldur harass our flanks...defeat Athdurub, and they will know fear....'The Orc-garrison at Bûrzkala is commanded by a fearsome creature known as Fikthrug.Fikthrug is at Bûrzkala, directly north of Thangúlhad.

Rodelleth has asked you to find and defeat the Orc-commander Fikthrug.Defeat Commander FikthrugRodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz, south of Búrzkala.

You should return to Rodelleth with news of your victory.Talk to Rodelleth in Thangúlhad'We have learned that the Orcs of Gathbúrz are led on the ground by a commander named Fikthrug, somewhere in Búrzkala.

'Alas, he himself is no more than a pawn of their masters in the tower, so it will not leave them leaderless, but if you can find and defeat this Orc it will be a significant blow to the Orcs' morale.

'Bûrzkala lies to the north of here. When you have completed this deed, return to me.''As long as Fikthrug remains, the forces of the Enemy here will be strong...he must be defeated!''Fikthrug has fallen then? Good!

'He may be easily replaceable, but every time a powerful Orc-leader falls, it sets off a merry row of infighting and assassination among the officers beneath him while they sort out who will take his place.

'It is better that they spend their time fighting each other rather than us, I would say.'The entrance to the court of the Wild Hunstman has been opened and is waiting for you to explore within.The Huntsman's Hall is in the south of the Mournshaws. It can be entered through Tûm's portal or by crossing the river to the south.

