You should return to Rodelleth with news of your victory.Speak with Rodelleth in Thangúlhad'While the forces of the Orcs in Gathbúrz lay disorganized and open to attack, the Enemy is not without resources to counter our advance. My scouts tell me that no less than three Olog-Hai champions have been released from Dol Guldur into Gathbúrz to rampage against our forces.

'Olog-hai are trolls of enormous size and devestating strength, and these have been well-armed against us.

'Gather your companions and stop them if you can, lest their rampage buy enough time for the Orcs to rally their forces against our attack.''With their Olog-hai fallen, it remains to be seen what the masters of the tower will do next. I suspect they will now hold against us, risking no more of their strength until the eastern army arives.

'We shall see about that!''The Olog-hai are a force to be reckoned with, ${PLAYER}...be wary on your journey to defeat them.'The Orc-encampment of Garmadh-maudhûl boasts a mine which produces ore for the use of the armies of Dol Guldur.Garmadh-maudhûl can be found to the north-east of Mithechad by following a trail that traverses up the mountain.

Eirien has asked you to destroy the ore-carts which the Orcs at Garmadh-maudhûl are using to resupply Dol Guldur.Destroy ore carts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eirien is at Mithechad, south-west of Garmadh-maudhûl.

