You should bring the relic that you recovered to Frithgeir.'The ruins where the giants have settled were once part of the home Thrór established during his exile from the Lonely Mountain. These foul creatures have destroyed our halls, crushed our statues, and raided ancient tombs for relics of our past.

'The relics I spoke of hold many secrets that our kindred collected over many years, from our first fathers. They must be recovered, ${PLAYER}.

'If you would, go to the giant encampments and bring back any relics you find there.''The relics of our people must not be lost to the giants.''The relics of our people must not be lost to the giants.''This relic will be well-protected, as it is a symbol of our fathers. Each of the recovered relics is a small piece of our history reclaimed from Gunnberg and his giant rabble.'With the defeat of Darúk, the forces of Ânghum-maudhûl have fallen into disarray, providing the perfect opportunity for the Malledhrim to strike.Ânghum-maudhûl lies to the south-east of Mithechad.

Harchador has asked you to journey to Ânhum-maudhûl to defeat the Orcs and collect the grim tokens they bear.Defeat Orcs at Ânghum-maudhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect grim tokens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Harchador is at Mithechad, north-west of Ânghum-maudhûl.

You should return to Harchador with news of your success.'The forces of Ânghum-maudhûl have been scattered with the defeat of Darúk, which grants us the perfect opportunity to strike. However, we have received reports that Dol Guldur has sent reinforcements to bolster the forces in the Ashenslades. These reinforcements are said to carry a grim token to drive the Orcs against us. 

'Would you travel to Ânghum-maudhûl and collect some of the tokens these Orcs carry? It may be that we can learn what foul craft was used to make them.

'Ânghum-maudhûl can be found by travelling south-east on the road across the central Ashenslades.''Travel south-east to Ânghum-maudhûl, defeat the Orcs, and collect the grim tokens they bear.''The weakening of Ânghum-maudhûl is paramount to our mission in the Ashenslades. Each time we push back the Orkish forces in the Ashenslades, the southern flank of the Malledhrim becomes more secure.'Golodir has ventured deep within Nûrz Gâshu, and his close friend Corunir is desperate to save him.Corunir is waiting to speak with you outside Norbar within the depths of Nûrz Ghâshu.Talk to CorunirGolodir is within Norbar. You must reach him as quickly as possible.Make your way to NorbarAn ancient fumerole, Torech Lach, has erupted and is blocking your path forward. It must be dealt with so you can proceed.Destroy Torech LachGolodir is within Norbar. You must reach him with haste.Make your way to NorbarAn ancient fumerole, Torech Naur, has erupted and is blocking your path forward. It must be dealt with so you can proceed.Destroy Torech NaurGolodir is within Norbar. You must reach him with haste.Make your way to NorbarAn ancient fumerole, Torech Ruin, has erupted and is blocking your path forward. It must be dealt with so you can proceed.Destroy Torech RuinCorunir has ventured into Norbar. Follow him and speak with him about rescuing Golodir.Talk to Corunir in NorbarGolodir has been driven mad by some force within Nûrz Ghâshu and must be subdued.Pacify GolodirGolodir must surviveCorunir is troubled by his friend's actions. Speak with him within NorbarTalk to CorunirErebún, an ancient Rogmul, has imposed its will upon Golodir's mind. If he is defeated, perhaps Golodir's grief-borne madness will dissipate.Defeat ErebúnGolodir must surviveCorunir must surviveErebún has been defeated, and Golodir's mind is clear once more. You should speak now with him.'We have done well to make it this far, ${PLAYER}, but it seems that many of the evils that once dwelt here have retreated into the deepest depths of Nûrz Ghâshu. It may be too much to hope for our passage to remain unnoticed.

'What can have driven Golodir to make this dangerous journey? Has he lost all hope for the future? He has suffered so much, more than any one Man should, and yet he persevered. Has he at last given in to despair?

'We must keep moving. Norbar is ahead. I fear what we may find there.''He speaks of his daughter as if she still lived, ${PLAYER}...there is some great evil at work here.

'What has raised this madness in the mind of my mentor, to cruelly seize upon the grief within his heart? And what can be done about it?''Look there, beyond the great pit of fire: it is Golodir! We have found him!

'Let us make our way to the far side of Norbar, ${PLAYER}. There we will speak with Golodir and bring him from these perilous depths!''What has happened? Where...where am I? Who...who are all of you?'

Golodir looks around in amazement and confusion.

'There was a ringing in my ears, as if I swam in deep water...but it is gone now. There was something else....''What has happened? Where...where am I?'

Golodir looks around in amazement and confusion.

'There was a ringing in my ears, as if I swam in deep water...but it is gone now. There was something else...''I shudder to think of what awaited Golodir beyond that door, ${PLAYER}. Erebún's dominance on the mind of my mentor was strong; what would Golodir have seen there had he remained under the Rogmul's power?

'I care not to guess. I know only that it would not have been Lorniel, and perhaps that would have been enough to destroy Golodir forever.

'Let us escape to the surface! Nûrz Ghâshu is no place for us, or for our loved ones!'The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu is a place where a man goes alone only if he has no wish of returning....Defeat NarubrasDefeat GormalithDefeat GháshglobDefeat MorfuinDefeat SnagtalúnDefeat LúgrynDefeat NurnorDefeat CefrogEnit believes she can summon one of the spirits of the forest and speak with it -- though it seems that she may have her own reasons for doing so.Most of the items Enit requires can be gathered throughout the northern Mournshaws, but the living bark may only be collected from the wild Wood-trolls that lurk west of Galar Culch.

Enits has asked you to gather many natural materials for her ritual.Complete Oaken LimbsComplete MistletoeComplete Creeping MossComplete Skin of WoodEnit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws.

She is prepared to begin the ritual to commune with one of the great spirits of the forest.Observe Enit's RitualEnit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws.

You should speak with Enit after she has communed with the spirits of the Mournshaws.Talk to Enit at Galar Culch'The forest has been disturbed and the spirits silent of late. I will summon one and speak with it, if you can bring me what I need for this ritual.

'There are several plants that are sacred to the spirits, but the forest has grown wild and terrible of late, and it is dangerous to travel within it. If you will gather the things I need and bring them to me, I will perform this ritual. Then we shall learn the truth of both your purpose and the forest's anger.

'Nearly everything I need can be foraged from the forest, but the living bark must be collected from the wild Wood-trolls which dwell to the west of here.''You have returned with what I require? In truth, I did not think you would emerge from the forest again, Duvodiad.

'That only means it is all the more important that I speak with the spirits of the Mournshaws.

'I shall begin....'Enit looks pale and shaken.

'The spirits have forsaken me! Who are you, Duvodiad? What does it mean that you have come among us even as the forest turns upon its faithful servants?

'The Rhi Helvarch himself has never called upon the folk of Nan Laeglin. I do not know what this means, but I can neither help nor hinder you now....

'Go then and curse you! Speak with our Elder upon Gwaed Brun at the heart of the forest. Perhaps he knows the way to the Huntsman's hall. I know it not. May you meet your doom there, Duvodiad. May the great spirits of the forest consume you!''I need many things before I can perform the ritual to summon the forest spirit.'Enit has asked you to retrieve several pieces of club moss as part of a ritual to summon one of the spirits of the forest.The moss Enit has requested can be gathered along the edge of the river in the north-west region of the Mournshaws.Collect club moss (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws.

You should bring the club moss you have collected to Enit.'The third ingredient I need are some clumps of club moss. You can find it growing among the rocks at the edge of the river to the north-west.''I trust this task was not overly difficult? The forest can be frightening to those who do not understand its ways.'Enit has asked you to retrieve several sprigs of mistletoe as part of a ritual to summon one of the spirits of the forest.The mistletoe Enit has requested can be gathered in the forest across the river to the north-west.Collect mistletoe (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws.

You should bring the mistletoe you have collected to Enit.'The second ingredient I need are a number of sprigs of recently cut mistletoe. You can likely find it hanging in the forest to the north of here.''This mistletoe is fresh enough, place it here. Do you have the rest?'Enit has asked you to retrieve several strong oaken branches as part of a ritual to summon one of the spirits of the forest.The oak branches Enit has requested can be gathered in the northern stretches of the Mournshaws.Collect oak-branches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws.

You should bring the oak branches you have collected to Enit.'The first ingredient I need is several sturdy oak branches recently fallen. You can likely find several in the forest to the west of here.''You have the oak branches? Very well, leave them with me and find the rest of the things I have asked of you.'Enit has asked you to retrieve several pieces of living bark as part of a ritual to summon one of the spirits of the forest.The living bark Enit has requested can be gathered from any of the wood-trolls that stalk the forests of the Mournshaws.Collect living bark (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws.

You should bring the living bark you have collected to Enit.'The final ingredient I need is the living bark taken from the wood-trolls that wander the Mournshaws. They can be found throughout the forest, but needless to say they shall not part with their bark quietly, for they hate all who intrude upon their domain.''You have the living bark? It should suffice, though I would rather you had not returned...'Gâthlata stands at the cross-roads of the Ashenslades. This camp is led by the nefarious Nulfríb, a vile creature who organizes the flow of information, goods, and troops to other parts of the Ashenslades.Nulfríb is at Gâthlata, south-east of Mithechad, along the central Ashenslades road.

Eirien has asked you to defeat Nulfríb and destroy his standard.Defeat NulfríbDestroy Nulfríb's standardEirien is at Mithechad, north-west of Gâthlata.

You should inform Eirien that Nulfríb has been slain and his standard lies in tatters.Talk to Eirien at Mithechad'Gâthlata stands at the cross-roads of the Ashenslades. It dispatches information, supplies, and troops throughout the region, preparing the armies of Dol Guldur for invasion.

'The creature known as Nulfríb reportedly leads the camp and is said to marshal forces and carry information to Dol Guldur. Will you seek out this creature, defeat him, and destroy his banner? By this, the Orcs will know they have no hope of success against us.

'Gâthlata is located east off of the main road that runs through the Ashenslades, south-east of here.''Please go to Gâthlata, defeat Nulfríb, and destroy his standard.''With the defeat of Nulfríb, the organization of Gâthlata has been thrown into disarray.

'By disrupting the central hub of the Ashenslades, other camps in the area will be slower to resupply, which will make reinforcing those areas more difficult.'The Enemy's forces of Ânghum-maudhûl have been felling wood in the Ashenslades area in an attempt to procure the blighted wood for spears and other wooden implements.Blighted wood stockpiles may be found at Ânghum-maudhûl, south-east of Mithechad along the central road.

Harchador has asked you to find and destroy the Orcs' blighted wood stockpiles.Destroy blighted wood pile (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Harchador is at Mithechad, north-west of Ânghum-maudhûl.

You should speak with Harchador and let him know that the Orcs' blighted wood stockpiles have been destroyed.Talk to Harchador at Mithechad'Desperate for wood to use for spears and other implements, the forces of Dol Guldur have begun to fell trees and gather wood in the Ashenslades. The Orcs believe the wood, when used for weapons, may spread the blight that has affected the trees in the region.

'Will you travel to Ânghum-maudhûl and destroy the Orcs' wood stockpiles? While there is no way to tell whether their hopes may prove true or not, there is no doubt such weapons would bring illness with them.

'Ânghum-maudhûl is located on the southernmost border of the Ashenslades. Follow the central road south-east across the Ashendslades.''With the destruction of the Orcs' stockpiles of blighted wood, the forces of Dol Guldur have lost a potentially terrible tool in the fight against the Malledhrim.

'You have saved many lives this day, and I appreciate your courage in the face of such danger.''Travel south-east to Ânghum-maudhûl and destroy the Orcs' wood stockpiles that can be found scattered throughout the camp.'The Gaunt-lord Ivar, aided by a band of sellswords, swept through the village of Stoneheight in his search for his helm. When his goals were reached, he abandoned the village to the mercy of the sellswords.Complete the Oppressors of Stoneheight DeedComplete the Challenger of Stoneheight DeedComplete the Stoneheight DeedThe Orc-camp at Ânug-stazg is the primary sentry-post for the Enemy's forces in the Ashenslades.Ânug-stazg can be found east and slightly north of Mithechad.

Perindúr has asked you to scout out the path leading into Ânug-stazg and the camp-fires at the edges of the camp.Scout the western camp-fireScout the path to Ânug-stazgScout the eastern camp-firePerindúr is at Mithechad, west and slightly south of Ânug-stazg.

You should return to Perindúr with your report of the Enemy's forces at Ânug-stazg.Talk to Perindúr at Mithechad'A smaller Orc-camp, known as Ânug-stazg, lies to the east of here. It is the primary sentry-post for the forces of Dol Guldur in the Ashenslades. What other forces are stationed there is currently unknown.

'There are three points at Ânug-stazg we would like you to scout: the western camp-fire, the southern path that leads into the camp, and the eastern camp-fire. All of these are found along the edge of Ânug-stazg. Perhaps from those vantage points, you may be able to learn something of the camp's strength.

'When you have completed your patrol, return to me with your report.''Have you travelled east to Ânug-stazg and scouted the outskirts of the camp?''It appears as if the camp is weaker than we expected. Our hope now is that reinforcements do not arrive soon, or this position may be lost.

'The time may be near to strike out against Ânug-stazg.'The Draig-lûth have created a village on the northern shore of the river, presenting a danger to travellers in the area.Gwâl Draig lies on the southern shore of the river, north-east of Gronu's camp.

Gronu has asked you to scout out the entrances to the camp and dispatch any guards you might encounter.Scout the western entrance of Gwâl DraigScout the southern entrance of Gwâl DraigScout the eastern entrance of Gwâl DraigDefeat Draig-lûth guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gronu is at his camp south-east of Gwâl Draig.

You should seek out Gronu and let him know what lies within the village of Gwâl Draig.Talk to Gronu at his camp'I suppose I should be grateful for the kindness of any willing to aid a wounded man, even if it is from a duvodiad. I received my wounds when a small raiding-party from Gwâl Draig attacked and slew my fellows.

'On the southern shore of the river stands an encampment that these duhirun -- these blackguards -- call home. My party was sent to scout this camp to see if we could rout them from the area. The Draig-lûth butchered the entirety of our sister clan, the Turch-lûth, and now seek our demise as well. Our former brethren from Dunland call us Algraig -- Outliers -- and have ever been our enemies.

'Perhaps you will scout this camp for me? Seek out the entrances and dispatch any guards that you encounter. The camp can be found by following the southern shore of the river to the north and heading due east.''It is good to hear that Gwâl Draig is indeed the main encampment for the most vile Draig-lûth. Perhaps when more hunters emerge from my clan, the Uch-lûth, we can mount an attack upon these duhirun.

'Thank you for your assistance, Duvodiad.''The Draig-lûth are a vile and merciless people, and these seem more so than their brethren in Dunland.'In the southern reaches of the Ashenslades, Ânghum-maudhûl stands as the central rallying point for Orcs in the area.Ânghum-maudhûl lies to the south-east of Mithechad.

Harchador has asked you to explore the western and eastern approaches to the camp and a small camp directly across from the main rallying point at Ânghum-maudhûl.Scout the eastern approachScout the northern campScout the western approachHarchador is at Mithechad, north-west of Ânghum-maudhûl.

You should return to Harchador and give your report on Ânghum-maudhûl.Talk to Harchador at Mithechad'In the southern reaches of the Ashenslades, the Orcs have built a large defensible position surrounding a set of ancient ruins. These ruins are called Ânghum-maudhûl by the Enemy.

'Would you travel to Ânghum-maudhûl and scout the area? There are three specific areas that I wish you to patrol for me: the western and eastern approaches to the camp and a small camp directly across from the main rallying point.

'Ânghum-maudhûl lies south-east of here, along the southern border of the Ashenslades.''Thank you for scouting this dangerous place...perhaps it would be a good target for a distraction, so that our incursions to the north might go well.''Please travel to Ânghum-maudhûl, south-east of here, and scout out the forces arrayed against us.'Handelen fears that the Orcs are mustering their forces in the northern reaches of Gathbúrz.The first point is north-east of Thangúlhad. The second point is to the north-west of the first, direcdly north of Kúfuzg. The third point is directly north of Thangúlhad, a little south of Búrzkala. The fourth point is just north-west of Thangúlhad.

You should scout the waypoints of the patrol that Handelen has asked you to undertake and defeat any enemies you might find there.Patrol the first point in northern GathbúrzPatrol the second point in northern GathbúrzPatrol the third point in northern GathbúrzPatrol the fourth point in northern GathbúrzHandelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Handelen with the report of your patrol.Talk to Handelen at Thangúlhad'The Orcs of Gathbúrz are a shattered force, but we must continue our forays against them to keep them from regrouping. I am asking the Malledhrim and our allies to mount frequent patrols through the area north of here, skirting their fortifications and engaging any enemies attempting to reinforce those positions.

'Are you up for the task, ${PLAYER}? If so, I bid you good fortune. Return to me when your patrol is complete.''Our survival here depends upon performing routine patrols to sight the approach of the Enemy.''There are still a lot of Orcs down there? I expect there are still hundreds of stragglers wandering back into the encampments after fleeing from the force of our initial assault.

'The real problems will start when the first elements of that eastern army begin to arrive... we must be ready for them.'Scouts of the Malledhrim witnessed the Orcs of Garmadh-maudhûl discarding piles of ore.Garmadh-maudhûl lies to the north-east of Mithechad.

Eirien has asked you to collect some of the ore discarded by the Orcs of Garmadh-maudhûl.Collect sack of discarded ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eirien is at Mithechad, south-west of Garmadh-maudhûl.

You should bring the discarded ore to Eirien. Perhaps she will be able to see if this ore has been affected by the blight.Talk to Eirien at Mithechad'In the north-eastern reaches of the Ashenslades, a small Orc-encampment known as Garmadh-maudhûl can be found overlooking the valley below. This encampment is believed to be a staging point for supplies into Dol Guldur.

'There have been rumours that some of the raw materials in this area have been affected by the blight that has swept across the region. Please go to the outskirts of Garmadh-maudhûl and retrieve several satchels of discarded ore and bring them to me, so that we can determine if the ore is blighted in some way.

'Garmadh-maudhûl lies to the north-east of here. The ore has been placed in sacks and can be found in the surrounding area.''Travel to Garmadh-maudhûl to the north-east of here. Please retrieve ore that has been placed in sacks and scattered in the area surrounding the camp.''Thank you for recovering these pieces of ore. Interestingly, it appears as if this ore has not been affected by the blight in the region, which makes me wonder why the Orcs discarded it in the first place.

'This does, however, mean that the stores of Garmadh-maudhûl are of high enough quality to be used in making armour and weapons.'You discovered a blighted branch in the Ashenslades, corrupted by an unknown disease.Himeinior is at Barad Angol, a small camp at a tower overlooking Sâd Doldúr.

You should seek out Himeinior and give him the branch you found. Perhaps he can discern more about what is happening to the trees in the Ashenslades.As you look down, you find a remnant of a fallen branch. The bark appears to be ashen-coloured and smells of decay, though something still speaks of an ancient beauty it may once have possessed.

Perhaps you should bring this to Himeinior at Barad Angol to see if he can tell you anything about the branch.'Thank you kindly for gathering such an exquisite specimen, ${PLAYER}. I have gathered several such branches myself, and this is the best of them thus far. 

'Sadly, it appears as if this poor branch has been blighted by some form of foul sorcery. It seems as if this sorcery has consumed its life and has left it naught but a husk, bereft of its former glory.'In the deepest reaches of Garmadh-maudhûl, the Orc-leader Ukhurk rallies his troops.Ukhurk and his standard can be found in Garmadh-maudhûl to the north-east of Mithechad.

Eirien has asked you to defeat Ukhurk, leader of the Orcs at Garmadh-maudhûl and cast down his standard.Defeat UkhurkDestroy Ukhurk's battle-standardEirien is at Mithechad, south-west of Garmadh-maudhûl.

You should return to Eirien and let her know that Ukhurk has been defeated and his standard destroyed.Talk to Eirien at Mithechad'At the heart of Garmadh-maudhûl, the leader of the Orcs there, a creature named Ukhurk, rallies his troops beneath his horrible standard.

'Perhaps if you were to journey to Garmadh-maudhûl and dispatch with Ukhurk? Cast down his standard and drive fear into the hearts of his followers.

'Garmadh-maudhûl lies to the north-east of here... be wary on your journey.''Seek out Ukhurk in Garmadh-maudhûl and defeat him. Destroy his standard and strike fear into the hearts of his minions.''Through your dedicated efforts, the leadership of Garmadh-maudhûl has been defeated and his forces have been thrown into disarray for the time being.

'Hopefully, our efforts will assist those who seek to disrupt the forces of Dol Guldur.'There are many watching stones placed in and around Dol Guldur, guarded by Cargûl sentries. Anyone who foolishly approaches too close to one of these stones is struck with a black curse that sunders the will.Watching stones and their Cargûl sentries can be found throughout Gathbúrz.

Handelen has asked you to defeat a number of the Cargûl sentries found near the watching stones in Gathbúrz to learn if a way might be found to protect the Malledhrim from the effects of the stones.Search Cargûl sentries for cluesWatching stones and their Cargûl sentries can be found throughout Gathbúrz.

Handelen has asked you to defeat a number of the Cargûl sentries found near the watching stones in Gathbúrz to learn if a way might be found to protect the Malledhrim from the effects of the stones.Search Cargûl sentries for cluesHandelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should bring the engraved dagger you found to Handelen.Talk to Handelen in ThangúlhadAgorin is at Ost Galadh in Emyn Lûm, west of Thangúlhad.

Handelen instructed you to bring the engraved dagger you found to Agorin, the Malledhrim Lore-master in Emyn Lûm.Handelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Handelen and tell him what you have learned from Agorin about the Watchers of Dol Guldur.Talk to Handelen at Thangúlhad'Have you seen the sentries, ${PLAYER}? I do not refer to the Orcs, of course -- there is little challenge in avoiding the eyes of Orcs. I refer to the ones carved of stone, with unblinking eyes that strike your will with a crushing darkness if you should stray too close.

'We have quickly learned to stay away from them as much as we may, but they make manoeuvering through Gathbúrz difficult, and I imagine the inner walls of Dol Guldur are likewise defended. We must find a way to defeat their power if we are to achieve our goals here.

'The robed Cargûl have been seen tending to these stone sentries on occasion... if you could approach close enough to defeat one, then perhaps you might be able to find something to aid us against the stones.''It is said that the satching stones of the Enemy are possessed of fell spirits and that the Cargûl which guard them were once knights of Eärnur of Gondor... you would do well to be wary.''It is said that the watching stones of the Enemy are possessed of fell spirits and that the Cargûl which guard them were once knights of Eärnur of Gondor... you would do well to be wary.''So you found these knives upon the Cargûl? I am not certain if they can help us or not. They look similar in make to the dread morgul-blades carried by the Nazgûl....

'I think you had best bring this to Agorin in Emyn Lûm. She might have some insight as to what might be done with them.''Agorin may know something of what you found... speak with her at Ost Galadh at once!''These knives were carried by the Cargûl who guard the Watchers of Dol Guldur? They are not morgul-blades, though they are indeed of a similar make. Unfortunately, I do not think they can be used to negate the power of the watchers... however, there may be another way.

'I can bind these blades as tokens that you may keep upon you. They are still evil things, I fear, but so long as you carry them, the watchers will not be able to distinguish you from their own dark servants, thus you should be able to pass them unmolested.

'That is the best I can do for you, I am afraid. Lady Galadriel cannot cross the river without leaving Lothlórien defenceless, and Mithrandir is lost to us. I do not know of any other who might be strong enough to break the power of the watchers.''Return to Handelen, ${PLAYER}... he will wish to know what we have learned.''In truth, I had not imagined that the watchers would be so powerful that even Agorin cannot answer them. This will be a serious thorn in our sides as we do battle for control of Gathbúrz.

'Still, at least she found a way for you to avoid their power. I shall have to see if we can get our hands on a few more of those blades....'Tûm, the Derudh elder, believes that the essence of the wild spirits which roam the southern reaches of the Mournshaws may be they key to a ritual that will open the way to the Huntsman's Hall.The wild spirits known as elhudan can be found throughout the Mournshaws.

Tûm has asked you to gather the essence of the elhudan that haunt the Mournshaws.Gather wild essences (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tûm is at Gwaed Brun at the heart of the Mournshaws.

You should return to Tûm with the essence you have procured.Bring the wild essence to Tûm at Gwaed Brun'The last Elder among us spoke of a ritual that might be performed here atop this hill. It was taught to us by one of the Forest Lords and is said to open the door to the Huntsman's Hall.

'He was quite old, and I was still a young man when he performed this ritual himself. I never saw him again. Nevertheless, if you wish to speak with the Forest Lords, it is perhaps the only way.

'Gather the essence of the elhudan that roam this forest and bring them here. Their anger is such that they will likely attempt to destroy you, so take care. When you have done so, I shall open the door for you. But you shall go in alone... I do not wish to share my master's fate, whatever it may have been.''The essence of the elhudan may open the way to the Huntsman's Hall.''You have gathered the wild essence I require? Very well then. I shall begin the ritual.

'The ritual should allow you to pass through the door into the Huntsman's Hall.

'Whether you will ever emerge again, I do not know. Good luck to you, Duvodiad... I do hope that you can find some way to soothe the forest's anger.'Vatnar the dwarf has seen the Orcs of northern Gathbúrz moving catapults into position to attack Thangúlhad.Orkish catapults can be found throughout northern Gathbúrz.

Vatnar has asked you to destroy several Orkish catapults.Destroy catapults (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Vatnar is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Vatnar with tidings of your success.Talk to Vatnar in Thangúlhad'So, we've managed to capture this tower, and it grants us a fine look at the surrounding land, but one thing I have seen that doesn't sit well with me is the Orcs moving a number of catapults nearby.

'The weather here in Mirkwood is not the finest at the best of times, but in a few hours it's going to include a fair hail of falling rocks, if you catch my meaning.

'Be a good sort and see if you can set a few of those on fire, would you? It is one thing being rained on day and night, but I'm not wanting a sharp crack on my head to go with it.''So you managed to wreck a few of the Orc's toys? Well that's done then, on to the next order of business shall we?

'Time is of the essence, if we're to bring that great pile of rock down around the ears of those cloaked fiends!''The catapults of the Enemy will be a bane upon the Golden Host if they are not dealt with, and quickly!'There are many positions throughout Gathbúrz that remain contested by both sides of the conflict in Southern Mirkwood.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail on logout, make sure to turn in before you leave the game.</rgb>Contested camps can be found in Gathbúrz.

Rodelleth has asked you to place a Malledhrim war-banner at a contested camp.Place a Malledhrim war-banner in a contested campDefend the Malledhrim war-banner at the contested camp in Gathburz.Defend the Malledhrim war-bannerRodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Rodelleth with news of your success.Talk to Rodelleth at Thangúlhad'I have a challenge for you, ${PLAYER}: take this banner and plant it among the rabble down below and ensure that it stands proudly as a sign of our victory in Gathbúrz!

'Let us see how many of those cowards will dare to take up the challenge, shall we?''Proudly done, ${PLAYER}! We long ago taught the servants of the Enemy to fear the sign of the Malledhrim upon the field of battle, but I find that they need an occasional reminder of this.''Show the Orcs of Dol Guldur that we do not fear them...plant our banner and defend it against all foes, ${PLAYER}!''Show the Orcs of Dol Guldur that we do not fear them...plant our banner and defend it against all foes, ${PLAYER}!''Well done, ${PLAYER}...speak with Rodelleth, and she will reward you.'There are two small encampments that the Draig-lûth established. These men are dangerous and prey upon the Uch-lûth.The Draig-lûth camps are east and north-east of Harndirion.

Gronu has asked you to seek out Pruv Cadlus and Sarf Cadlus on the eastern slope below Harndirion and defeat sentries at each of the camps.Discover Pruv CadlusDefeat sentries near Pruv Cadlus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Discover Sarf CadlusDefeat sentries near Sarf Cadlus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gronu's camp lies almost due north of Harndirion.

You should return to Gronu and let him know that you have defeated many of the sentries near Pruv Cadlus and Sarf Cadlus.Talk to Gronu at his camp'It is well, I suppose, that you have found me. The Draig-lûth who came from the South are a vile and cruel people. It is said that they take captive those that would enter this land and offer them to the gwiber and giants that dwell within.

'On the other side of this hill, there are two small encampments: Pruv Cadlus and Sarf Cadlus. These encampments are used as forward outposts for the Draig-lûth in this area. If you could go to these camps and dispatch their sentries, I would be very appreciative.

'The camps can be found to the east and north-east of Harndirion. Please be careful, Duvodiad, for it is said that those ruins are cursed place and that foul spirits call it home.''The defeat of the sentries marks the beginning of the end for these foul duhirun. I appreciate your assistance, for it shows that there are duvodiad who will fight for my people.''The Draig-lûth do not belong in this land...it belongs to the Uch-lûth.'There are two small encampments that the Draig-lûth established. These men are dangerous and prey upon the Uch-lûth.The Draig-lûth camps are east and north-east of Harndirion.

Gronu has asked you to seek out Pruv Cadlus and Sarf Cadlus on the eastern slope below Harndirion and defeat sentries at each of the camps.Discover Pruv CadlusDefeat sentries near Pruv Cadlus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Discover Sarf CadlusDefeat sentries near Sarf Cadlus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gronu's camp lies almost due north of Harndirion.

You should return to Gronu and let him know that you have defeated many of the sentries near Pruv Cadlus and Sarf Cadlus.Talk to Gronu at his camp'Duvodiad, your aid is welcome. Continue, if you would, to harry the sentries of the Draig-lûth at Pruv Cadlus and Sarf Cadlus. If you do this, my people will keep you in esteem.''The defeat of the sentries marks the beginning of the end for these foul duhirun. I appreciate your assistance, for it shows that there are duvodiad who will fight for my people.''The Draig-lûth do not belong in this land...it belongs to the Uch-lûth.'The silk of the spiders in the Scuttledells is very strong and useful for a variety of purposes.Spiders can be found throughout the Scuttledells in Mirkwood.

Legindir has asked you to collect pristine webbing from the spiders and environs of the Scuttledells.Collect pristine webbing (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Good day to you, though the circumstances are dark ones. I have heard tell that you are a worthy and brave adventurer who has aided the Malledhrim in this deadly venture into Mirkwood. Though my cause is less worthy -- but no less deadly -- I have need of your aid if you will help me.

'The silk of the giant spiders of Mirkwood is of surpassing quality and has myriad uses if it can be collected pristine and fresh. I have need of quite a bit of this silk -- not the least to produce bandages for those wounded in these battles.

'I myself am well-studied in the lore of runecraft, and I may have some writings here that are of interest to you to trade for your efforts.''Have you brought me the spider-silk I requested?''You have brought the webbing I requested?

'Ah! My sincerest thanks to you! Such creatures do not stalk the realm of Lothlórien, so it is rare for me to have the opportunity to collect so much of their silk.

'What can I offer you in trade for your efforts?'There are many villainous monsters roaming Mirkwood, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many Angmarim in MirkwoodSlay many beasts in MirkwoodSlay many dead in MirkwoodSlay many Orcs in MirkwoodSlay many spiders in MirkwoodSlay many Wargs in MirkwoodThe servants of the Enemy are a formidable presence in Mirkwood as the Malledhrim press forward.The Golden Host is ever-threatened by the presence of Black Númenórean sorcerers in and around Dol Guldur, lending their aid and fealty to the strength of the Enemy.Defeat sorcerers in Southern MirkwoodThe servants of the Enemy are a formidable presence in Mirkwood as the Malledhrim press forward.The Golden Host is ever-threatened by the presence of Black Númenórean sorcerers in and around Dol Guldur, lending their aid and fealty to the strength of the Enemy.Defeat sorcerers in Southern MirkwoodDefeat many spiders in Southern Mirkwood.Defeat spiders in Southern MirkwoodDefeat many spiders in Southern Mirkwood.Defeat spiders in Southern MirkwoodThe camp at Sâd Doldúr proved to be a terrible place, full of sorcerers and fell spirits. Worse yet, it appears to be the source of the blight in the Ashenslades.Faerchiril is at Barad Angol.

Himeirion has asked you to tell the Elf-scholar Faerchiril about your findings in Sâd Doldúr.Talk to Faerchiril at Barad Angol'Your discoveries at Sâd Doldúr will be of interest to Faerchiril at Barad Angol. You should go to her at once with your report...the darkness stirring there cannot be permitted to continue.''I have long feared that the blight which has befallen the Ashenslades and the rise of the fell spirits are due to the foul sorcerers dwelling in the ruins below.

'Our worst fear is that the blight is spreading westward across Mirkwood, and sadly, this appears to be the case. It is good to hear that the blight has not corrupted the ancient stones below; however, I still fear for the trees.

'We must put a stop to this evil before it is too late.''Speak with Faerchiril, ${PLAYER}, and offer any help you may'On the topmost reaches of the ruins of Sâd Doldúr stands Orthadban, the foul sorcerer that the Malledhrim believe to be responsible for the summoning of fell spirits to the Ashenslades.Orthadban can be found upon the topmost tier of Sâd Doldúr, south of Barad Angol.

Faerchiril has asked you to defeat the foul sorcerer Orthadban.Defeat OrthadbanFaerchiril is at Barad Angol, north of Sâd Doldúr.

You should speak with Faerchiril and regale her with stories of your victory.Talk to Faerchiril at Barad Angol'Reports from our scouts indicate that Orthadban, a most foul sorcerer, has made his home among the ruins of Sâd Doldúr. We believe this man to be responsible for summoning the fell spirits of Morgoth to the Ashenslades.

'Will you brave the perils of Sâd Doldúr, seek out this vile sorcerer, and put an end to his fiendish plan?

'Orthadban makes his camp upon the topmost tier of Sâd Doldúr, south of here.''Find Orthadban and put a stop to his fiendish plans. He makes his camp upon the topmost tier of Sâd Doldúr, south of here.''The Golden Host thanks you for your dedicated service.

'Our hope is that, with the defeat of Orthadban, the Black Númenóreans will be unable to summon fell spirits to the ruins of Sâd Doldúr.

'This is a major victory for the Golden Host before we must withdraw from Mirkwood.'The Black Númenórean sorcerers in Dol Guldur use a strange ash in their foul rituals.Sâd-en-Dagor is in Dol Guldur, north-east of Helethir.

Stirnir has asked you to enter Sâd-en-Dagor and recover the strange ash from the Black Númenórean sorcerers there.Collect strange ash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Wargs of Draugdegil are fed foul meats to make them stronger and more vicious.Draugdegil lies to the north of Helethir, just inside the gate of Fennas Guldur.Collect meat-scraps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Orcs of Gathbúrz are rasing banners of Dol Guldur in an attempt to rally against the Malledhrim onslaught.Banners of Dol Guldur can be found throughout Gathbúrz.Burn banners of Dol Guldur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Rodelleth with tidings of your success.Talk to Rodelleth at Thangúlhad'The Orcs are trying to rally against us, raising the banners of Dol Guldur wherever they believe that they can bring forces together.

'Destroy those banners before they can gather to them. We must keep the forces in Gathbúrz scattered and leaderless while we attempt the gates of  Dol Guldur.

'When you have done as I have asked, return here to me.''Well struck, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs may rally to ashes and fear for today. Thanks to you, their banners stand no more!''We will not tolerate the presence of our enemies in this, our home of old! Burn their banners, ${PLAYER}!'Draugdegil, the Warg-stables of Dol Guldur, is commanded by the goblin Athgrat and the Warg Kranklob.

The Orcs and goblins of Dol Guldur are not alone in their efforts. The Enemy breeds foul Wargs there, as well. These foul beasts have proven a difficult challenge to the Malledhrim, for they are skilled in the hunt and hunger for living flesh.Draugdegil lies north and east of Helethir.Defeat AthgratDefeat KranklobWithin the abandoned Northcotton Farm, Thadúr has created a powerful poison known as Darkthorn. Thadúr plans to unleash his poison on the unsuspecting hobbit-folk. You must foil his plans and defeat him before the poison can be unleashed.To earn this deed, you must defeat Legbarthil the Spider, Úmheryn the vile cauldron, and Thadúr the Ravager.You have defeated Thadúr, his lieutenants, and foiled his plans.To earn this deed, you must defeat Legbarthil the Spider, Úmheryn the vile cauldron, and Thadúr the Ravager.Defeat LegbarthilDestroy ÚmherynDefeat ThadúrThe tower is the pinnacle of the fortress of Dol Guldur. Its terrible shadow casts darkness and dread over the forests of Mirkwood.Complete everything in the Battle in the Tower SkirmishDefeat ThangaranDefeat IaerienDefeat HogawardDefeat MúdkuDefeat BlordDefeat GundnákhDefeat GadhumúrzDefeat UrborDol Guldur claims many champions, not the least of which are those who preside over the Sword-hall.Defeat all of the champions of the Sword-hall of Dol Guldur after challenging them all at once.Among the broken rocks of Thrór's Coomb, the feared gwiber Tantafod and Harcennun make their nests. These matrons are fiercely protective of their nests.Tantafod's clutch can be found on the western border of Thrór's Coomb, almost due south of Nár's Peak.

Frithgeir has asked you to seek out Tantafod's clutch and destroy it. Tantafod herself may need to be dispatched as well.Find Tantafod's clutch and defeat TantafodHarcennun's clutch can be found west of Tantafod's clutch, near a large rock outcropping.

Frithgeir asked you to seek out Harcennun's clutch and destroy it. You may have to dispatch Harcennun herself as well.Find Harcennun's clutch and defeat HarcennunFrithgeir is at Zudrugund within Nár's Peak, north of the gwibers' clutches.

You should return to Frithgeir and tell him of your heroic deeds.Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund'There are two larger female gwiber that have made their home among the hills below. These dreaded beasts are two of the more powerful gwiber and a great threat to not only us, but the Men who dwell to the west. They are wily and will lurk in hiding, only to emerge when their eggs are disturbed.

'I would have you seek out the clutches of Tantafod and Harcennun and destroy them, lest the gwiber continue to replenish.

'These two clutches can be found in the far western reaches of Thrór's Coomb. Tantafod's clutch can be found on the western border, while Harcennun's clutch might be found near a large standing stone to the west of Tantafod's.''Tantafod and Harcennun have long been the scourge of Thrór's Coomb. The defeat of these creatures marks a step forwards for our safety and the restoration of our home.''I have seen Tantafod, and she is terrible....''Harcennun is no less terrible than her sister....'The Black Uruks are the masters of Gathbúrz, driving the Orcs and goblins into battle beneath their lashes. As long as they remain in command, it will be difficult to fully break the forces defending Dol Guldur. More importantly, if the uruk-leaders can be defeated, then the masters of the tower will find it considerably more difficult to prepare the upcoming army for their inevitable assault upon Lothlórien.Black Uruks can be found in Gathbúrz.

Rodelleth has asked you to defeat the uruk-leaders in Gathbúrz to deplete the reserve of officers available to the Orc-forces in the battle for Mirkwood.Defeat Black Uruks in Gathbúrz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Rodelleth with tidings of your victory over the Black Uruks of Mirkwood.Talk to Rodelleth in Thangúlhad'While it is the Nazgûl in that black tower who command all of the forces here in Mirkwood, it is the uruk-lieutenants and generals who actually give the orders and organize the troops.

'There is a large encampment of these brutal Orcs deep within Gathbúrz, and if they can be rooted out, then the rest of the rabble will fall apart, leaving them as useless fodder upon the battlefield.

'I would bid you seek out the Black Uruks of Mirkwood and slay them. When you have succeeded, return to me.''I am impressed by your skill, ${PLAYER}, but I will be more impressed when you have returned with news of the defeat of the Black Uruks of Mordor.''Ha! With the number of the uruks in Mirkwood depleted, there will be few left to help drive the Dark Lord's armies when they come to cross the Anduin!

'With any fortune, our archers will have naught but practice at targets as they attempt the crossing: a display I find myself looking forward to.'Naerdolen has asked you to go into Sammath Gûl and destroy the protective Black Uruks that attempt to stop all intruders.Sammath Gûl, a tower deep within Dol Guldur, is in the Eastern reaches of southern Mirkwood.

Naerdolen has asked you to enter Sammath Gûl and defeat many Guldur Brutes.Defeat Guldur Brutes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Among the ruins in the southern reaches of Thrór's Coomb, several pillars with rune-carvings still stand. The messages on the pillars may speak of lost knowledge and should be recovered.The ruins on the southern hills lie to the south of Nár's Peak, through the mountain pass.

Frithgeir has asked you to seek out the ruined pillars among the ancient dwarf-ruins and take rubbings of the runes found upon them.Take rubbings of the ancient pillars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Frithgeir is at Zudrugund within Nár's Peak, north of the ruins, through the mountain pass.

You should return to Frithgeir and present him with the rubbings of these pillars.Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund'Among the old ruins of our home, there are a series of pillars near the entrances to the halls. These pillars are etched with ancient runes. These runes are fine examples of our craftsmanship in this area, and the knowledge contained on these pillars cannot be replaced.

'Will you find these pillars and take rubbings of the runes, so that this knowledge may be passed down to our future generations?

'The rune-pillars are located among the ruins in the southern hills of Thrór's Coomb.''These rubbings will be added to our fine library. The knowledge discovered will no longer be in danger of being lost like many precious things that once resided within our ancient halls.''There is much knowledge in these ruins which must not be lost.'Darkthorn is a horrible poison brewed by Thadúr the Ravager within the Northcotton Farm. By allowing Úmheryn, the vile cauldron, to boil over while destroying it, you will destroy any trace of this horrific poison.

<rgb=#FF0000>This deed can only be completed on Tier 2 difficulty.</rgb>Avoid quenching the fire beneath Úmheryn while destroying the cauldronIn the valley below, in the eastern reaches of Thrór's Coomb, gwiber have begun building nests to swell their numbers.Gwiber-nests may be found to the south of Zudrugund.

Frithgeir has asked you to hunt down nests of gwiber-eggs and destroy them.Destroy gwiber egg-clutches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Frithgeir is at Zudrugund, north of the gwiber-nests. 

You should return to Frithgeir and inform him that you have destroyed many gwiber-eggs.Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund'In the valley below, gwiber have begun to emerge from their caves in the mountains and build new nests. With each new gwiber, the creatures will grow in power and will eventually overrun the whole of Thrór's Coomb.  

'Not only do the gwiber themselves need to be destroyed, but their eggs as well, so as to stem their growth. Would you do that for us?

'Travel south across the river and seek nests full of eggs. Destroy these, then return to me here.''The gwiber spread like a plague across Thrór's Coomb, but your efforts will at least slow their growth.''Gwiber are foul beasts and dangerous, and they are fast becoming a threat to all the peoples of Enedwaith.'Tûm, a mystic of the Algraig clans known as a Derudh, told you of an old woman who plies the waters of the river. He believes this crone may know more about the spirits they call the Forest Lords than any other.The old woman Tûm spoke of can occasionally be found along the banks of the river that passes through the Mournshaws.

Tûm suggested you find the old woman who plies the river of the Mournshaws. It is possible that she knows something of the Forest Lords.Talk to the old woman of the river in the MournshawsCun Annun can be found throughout the Mournshaws.

The River-woman has offered you passage along the river's length if you can bring her the teeth of the Cun Annun that haunt the forest in the Mournshaws.Collect Cun Annun teeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The River-woman may be found along the banks of the river in the Mournshaws.

You should return to the River-woman with the Cun Annun teeth that you have collected.'The Forest Lords may not heed our calls, Duvodiad, but there may be other ways to find their ancient halls. One such path may be through the old woman who has long plied the river that passes through Galar-gwig -- this place you call the Mournshaws.

'No one has ever seen her beyond the boundaries of the forest, nor do the wild spirits of the wood seem to trouble her. We do not know who she is, save that she will occasionally allow others to ride the river's length with her in silence.

'I have long suspected that she may be a servant of the Forest Lords, but she has never admitted this to me or any other. Seek her out along the banks of the river. Perhaps she will help you... or perhaps not.''Perhaps the old woman of the river may help you.''So, you seek the Forest Lords? They are here, but no mortal may approach their halls uninvited. It is said that the Rhi Helvarch resents such intrusions upon his court. Mayhap one of his servants might call you forth, yet the Master of the Hall may still find you unworthy and your life forfeit. Who can say?

'I can take you hither and yon upon the waters of this river, but the banks of it have become dangerous in these days, and I demand a toll for your passage first. The Cun Annun who stalk this forest are not of this place. They come upon evil winds, blowing out of the graves of Men to the East.

'Slay these beasts and bring me a string of their teeth. Then shall I ferry you upon the river's length as you please, though it does not lead to the Huntsman's hall.''I will not take you upon the river until you bring me the toll I require.''Give the teeth here. Yes... yes....

'Very well, this will have to do. I shall grant you passage upon the river, Duvodiad.

'But be warned that the Derudh here do not care for duvodiad -- outsiders -- and the Huntsman has no love for mortals of any nature, so you must be wary!'Umfrë told you of a small community of Dunlendings who are chosen by their clans to enter the Mournshaws and commune with the spirits who live there. He believes that they might know of a way through the deep woods into the south.Berries may be found along the forest paths in the Mournshaws.

Umfrë suggests that you gather berries as a tithe to the Derudh of the Mournshaws before you approach them.Collect wild berries in the Mournshaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Derudh of the Mournshaws may be found at a stone circle called Galar Culch to the south of Echad Daervunn.

Umfrë told you to approach the Derudh with an offering of berries.Enit is at Galar Culch, south of Echad Daervunn.

Enit the Derudh may know a way through the Mournshaws into Dunland.Talk to Enit at Galar Culch'If you must find your way through this accursed forest, then I cannot show it to you, for I never go so deep... but the Derudh may know a way.

'A few among our people are chosen to learn the forest's secrets. Those that return claim to have communed with the spirits of the forest, but speak little of it. These are the Derudh of the Mournshaws.

'There is an ancient circle of stone in the northern reaches of the forest called Galar Culch where you might find them. Bring them some tithe of berries or the like, and they may grant you some piece of wisdom. Do not expect much from them, however, for they care little for duvodiad like you.''The Derudh must be appeased before they will speak with you.''Who are you, Duvodiad? How is it that you dare these woods and carry an offering in the way of our people?

'I do not care for your presence, nor your presumption, but our ways are old, and I would not break them in times such as these.

'Speak then... what is it that you seek?''A path to the south? Once perhaps, but not in these days. The spirits of the forest have grown wild and more dangerous than they once were... certainly they would devour one such as you!

'I might commune with the spirits and speak with them myself, but there is a ritual that must be performed, and the things I need are dangerous to gather now.'Enit was greatly angered and shamed by the spirit's rejection of her demands.

In her anger she has told you to speak with her elders upon a great hill in the centre of the forest.Tûm, the elder of the Derudh, is at Gwaed Brun, south of Galar Culch.

Enit has instructed you to speak with Tûm, the Derudh elder.Talk to Tûm at Gwaed Brun'Go then and curse you! Speak with our Elder upon Gwaed Brun at the heart of the forest. Perhaps he knows the way to the Huntsman's hall. I know it not.

'May you meet your doom there, Duvodiad. May the great spirits of the forest consume you!''So you have come, Duvodiad. The Forest Lords have spoken to us and said you would come. It seems they would speak with you, if you are able to prove your worth to them. Most odd.

'Oh, do forgive young Enit. She knows little yet of the Forest Lords. They have ever been of fickle whim, and she takes such things rather personally, I am afraid.''I have no more to say to you!'The Derudh Tûm claims that the spirits of the forest have been angered and have driven away the rest of the Derudh. He hopes to reclaim their grove and perhaps help you find the way into the Huntsman's hall.A maddened elhudan spirit has claimed Oirnad Culch, south of Gwaed Brun.

Tûm has asked you to defeat the wild spirits that have overrun the grove the Derudh once called their own.Defeat the maddened elhudan at Oirnad CulchTûm is at the grove atop Gwaed Brun in the Mournshaws, north of Oirnad Culch.

You should return to Tûm with news of your success.Talk to Tûm at Gwaed Brun'Our tales say that the Rhi Helvarch came to these lands long ago, and that his power gradually claimed the forest, making it strange and dangerous to the unwary.

'But he has never pursued or hounded us, and the spirits that are drawn to him have rarely disturbed us... but now they have become filled with anger and lash out at any who enter the forest.

'These wild spirits have overrun the circle which lies nearest the Huntsman's hall. If they can be driven away, then perhaps we can beseech the Forest Lords to open the way within.''Confront the wild spirits, if you dare, Duvodiad... though I doubt you will succeed.''You have fought valiantly, but it does not seem that the spirits can be driven away by brute force. I feared as much.

'We must open the way nevertheless for so we have been bidden.'The time is nigh for the annual Feast of the Running Stag. You have been asked to be present for the rites as an honoured guest of Lhan Tarren.You should speak with Elder Riagán in Lhan Tarren.

The Elder of the Stag-clan has looked forward to inviting you to the festival.Talk to Riagán to attend the Feast of the Running StagElder Riagán is in Lhan Tarren.

You should speak with Elder Riagán.Talk to Elder Riagán'You have done enough for the day, my friend. More than enough! Now it is time to take up your seat as an honoured guest of the Caru-lûth.

'Our annual festival is almost upon us. I hope it will not be so bad as the impetuous young fawns have led you to believe... ha!

'Speak with me again when you are ready.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready for the festival? Come, ${PLAYER} -- to me, you are an honoured friend and guest.''I fear for what may have taken place in the herd-lands after that crow returned last night. A farmer lives there with his son, and a farmhand as well. I must ponder what to do....'You have learned that an unknown Ranger of the Grey Company has entered the Mournshaws in search of a hidden path to the south. 

The Algraig firmly believe this forest is haunted by powerful and fey spirits. Only the Derudh of Nan Laeglin and a few brave hunters dare enter the place.

Even fewer return....Find Daervunn the Ranger who has wandered into the northern reaches of the Mournshaws.

It is uncertain whether he still lives, but if so it is possible he has found a path into Dunland that is unwatched by enemy eyes.Find Daervunn in the Mournshaws'Several days ago, Daervunn entered the Mournshaws -- a great forest to the west of here.

'He was hoping to find a way through that forest to the south that would be hidden from the prying eyes of our enemies, but I have heard nothing from him since.

'The locals call the forest Galar-gwig, and believe it to be inhabited by powerful spirits that do not care for the company of Men.

'There is one group among the Dunlendings, called the Derudh that dare frequent the forest - and even among their ranks it said that one will occasionally vanish into the forest... never again to be seen beneath mortal sun.

'I'd watch your step there.''${PLAYER}! You are the last person I expected to meet here. I have not had much success here. The forest is treacherous and wild, and I do not know its paths. I have made the acquaintance of one hunter who will dare the place -- indeed, he rescued me from a pack of strange hounds just last morning.

'What little I know concerns tales of a gathering of 'lords' in the forest...wild spirits or some such according to the tales, but each story I have heard is different, save they all refer to a great Huntsman who leads them.

'My hope is that they might be a hidden company of Elves, hiding themselves from the people of Nan Laeglin behind veils of myth and folk tales -- that might be a real stroke of fortune if we could find them.''Seek out Daervunn in the northern reaches of the Mournshaws.''I have heard that a duvodiad wandered into the haunted wood....'The Wargs of the Enemy will present the greatest threat to the Malledhrim when it comes time for the Golden Host to withdraw from Mirkwood, for they would be able to overtake the Elves swiftly.Wargs can be found in Gathbúrz.

Rodelleth has asked you to defeat several of the Wargs prowling through Gathbúrz to help ensure a safe retreat for the Malledhrim.Defeat Wargs in Gathbúrz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Rodelleth and let her know that many Wargs fell beneath your assaults.Talk to Rodelleth at Thangúlhad'We know we do not have the power to pull down Dol Guldur now, ${PLAYER}, and with an enemy army approaching, it is only a matter of time before we must retreat. My people are swifter than any enemy bound by foot, but we cannot run faster than Wargs.

'There is a force of these beasts housed in Gathbúrz, and if they are free to pursue us when we begin our retreat, they will pull down many a valiant Elf, ere we can reach the boats.

'Those Wargs must be slain ere the time for our withdrawal comes, and I believe that you have the strength to accomplish this task.''Your hunt has gone well, and the Wargs of Gathbúrz have suffered badly this day. That is one less threat to worry about when it comes time for us to withdraw back beneath the boughs of Lothlórien.''Curses upon the Wargs of Dol Guldur...if you will hunt them, I will be most appreciative.'The Wargs of Naur-hoit are led by a great pack-leader called Morglok. The Elves of the Golden Host believe that his defeat may be the key to driving forth the Wargs from the ruins.Morglok is at Naur-hoit, south of Mithechad.

Perindúr has asked you to seek out and defeat the Warg-packleader Morglok.Defeat Morglok the Warg-packleaderPerindúr is at Mithechad, north of Naur-hoit.

You should return at once to Perindúr and let him know that Morglok has been defeated.Talk to Perindúr at Mithechad'The Wargs of the Ashenslades follow a pack-leader by the name of Morglok, who drives them to harry our forces. If Morglok were to be defeated, the Ashenslades may become safe enough for our scouts to explore further.

'I charge you with hunting down this Morglok and bringing his reign of the pack to an end. He will likely be found among the pack at Naur-hoit, to the south of here.

'When you have defeated Morglok, return to me with your tale.''By defeating Morglok, you have made our mission in the Ashenslades easier.

'While there may be call to thin the numbers of the Wargs patrolling the area, you have struck a great blow to the forces of Dol Guldur here in the Ashenslades.''Seek out Morglok and bring his reign as leader of the pack to an end. He will likely be found among the Wargs at Naur-hoit, to the south of here.'The Library at Tham Mírdain was once one of the greatest repositories of the Elves' knowledge in Middle-earth. After Sauron's forces razed Eregion, much of that knowledge was lost.Forces for Good and Evil race to recover scraps of lost knowledge from the Library at Tham MírdainComplete Purging the OvermastersComplete Matters of KnowledgeComplete Pillagers of KnowledgeComplete Chieftain GûrshComplete Challenge: Chieftain GûrshComplete Lore of the Forgotten LibraryComplete Invaders of Tham Mirdain (Library)Daervunn has befriended a Dunlending hunter by the name of Umfrë on the fringes of the Mournshaws after the hunter rescued him from a pack of vicious hounds. However, Umfrë has recently disappeared into the Mournshaws after giving chase to one of the hounds, and Daervunn is concerned that he may be in some danger...or even dead.Umfrë is lost somewhere in the Mournshaws.

Daervunn asked you to find Umfrë the hunter, who disappeared into the forest, hunting for a Cun Annun that had been terrorizing his village.Find Umfrë in the MournshawsUmfrë is at Echad Daervunn in the Mournshaws.

You should return to Daervunn's camp and speak with Umfrë.Talk to Umfrë at Echad Daervunn'Umfrë the hunter it was, who rescued me from a ravening pack of strange white hounds shortly after I entered the forest -- Cun Annun, he called them.

'He seems a good Man, though when he realized I was a northerner he seemed dismayed. Nevertheless, he helped me tend my wound, and I had hoped to ask for his services as a guide through these woods. He left, though, in search of one of these hounds that he said had been terrorizing the people of his village of late. Yet a full day has since passed, and I have seen no sign of him. I fear he too may have been injured or killed beneath the forest's eaves.

'My leg is still not fit to walk -- if you could find Umfrë and help him return here, I would be obliged, as I owe him a debt, and he may be the only one who can help us through this forest.''My thanks to you, Duvodiad.

'These woods have grown more dangerous than ever in recent days. These Cun Annun that hunt and kill Men and beast alike are a terror from our old wives' tales.

'I do not know in truth what brings your people here, but I also in truth do not care to. Whatever your purpose, unless it is to bring harm to my people, I will help you if I may.''Please stranger, help me!''I would be grateful if you could find Umfrë and assure his safety.'The School at Tham Mírdain once trained the mightiest Elf-smiths in Middle-earth. Much to their dismay, their learning was used against them when the Great Rings were created.Forces for both Good and Evil race to uncover lingering secrets from the ruins of the School at Tham Mírdain.Complete Musings and TeachingsComplete Blade of the DunlendingComplete Biting the White HandComplete Chieftain TarshComplete Flames of KnowledgeComplete Texts of the Crumbling SchoolComplete Invaders of Tham Mírdain (School)The Black Númenórean sorcerers use skulls as harbingers of the Dead. The foul relics bode ill for the Malledhrim.The Relics of Necromancy can be retrieved from Sammath Gûl and should be returned to Laegalar in Helethir.

