You should return to Torist for your reward.Talk to Torist at Helethir'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. We have much to discuss. Our forces have encountered three champions of Dol Guldur: a sorcerer named Urcheron, the morroval-queen Carchrien, and the Gorthorog war-leader Durkâr. Dread follows in their wake...they must be dealt with, lest our hearts quail and our strength wavers.

'Deep within the fortress of Dol Guldur is a sword-hall, which our scouts believe to be the training-grounds for the warriors of Dol Guldur. If this is so, Urcheron, Carchrien, and Durkâr will surely be near at hand.

'Enter Sâd-en-Dagor and slay these three champions.''You have done it! Fine work, ${PLAYER}! These warriors posed a great threat to us, but no more.''These are mighty warriors you will be facing...do not underestimate their strength!'Having finally found an entrance to the court of the Wild Huntsman, you have come upon a number of powerful spirits -- some of whom look upon you with disdain. Now you must prove yourself before them if you are to find a way through the haunted forests of the Mournshaws for the Grey Company.The Wild Huntsman resides in the Huntsman's Hall.

You have been instructed to approach the Huntsman and ask that the Grey Company be allowed to pass through the southern Mournshaws into Dunland.Talk to the Wild Huntsman in the Huntsman's HallThe servants of the Wild Huntsman are in the Huntsman's Hall.

The Huntsman has bidden you complete the tasks that the his hand-maidens set before you.Hunt Munfaeril's spiritHunt Gwenaewen's spiritHunt Lavaneth's spiritArassiel is at the Huntsman's Hall.

