Having completed the Wild Hunt, you should return and speak with the Huntsman on behalf of the Dúnedain.Talk to the Wild Huntsman in the Huntsman's Hall'Welcome to the Huntsman's Hall, mortal. There are few who dare this place in these latter days, and fewer still who stand here worthy of the fate that brought them hence. What brings you here, I wonder?

'So you come in the name of the Dúnedain? Such glory as they held was forfeit in long ages past, and now they come to slink through our lord's realm as thieves might?

'Yet it is not for me to judge, for the Huntsman has forbidden us to decide the fate of mortals here. Speak with him if you would buy passage for the lost lordlings of Númenór, if this is indeed their final call to battle.''Ye are not welcome here, ${PLAYER}. The peoples of Middle-earth have proven their weakness as many times as needed to convince me of their folly.

'Yet ever and again my lord in the Uttermost West has bidden me be patient. He tells me that it may yet come to pass that my bow need not be nocked ere the Darkness ends -- and yet I remain against that eventuality.

'And so I challenge thee, remind me again of the myriad faults of Men, the hubris of the Elves, the greed of the dwarves, and the timid cowardice of halflings. Or prove to me that there is some mettle left in the folk of Middle-earth to take their fate into their own hands. Join my hunt and see it through, that I may judge you worthy or not.''So you have completed the Wild hunt. It seems there is some spark of valour left within your kind, ${RACE}. Very well then. The Dúnedain lordlings may pass through my forests unmolested. The spies of the Enemy will not see them here beneath these boughs.

'But be wary nonetheless: evil things creep here now, though they be blind before my power, nor can I see what fate awaits the Men of the West as they march to meet their doom. But I do know this: few days remain before the decisive battles are joined. The eyes of the Uttermost West watch keenly the struggle here, for its outcome will soon be decided.

'Take care, little one, and may your hunt be fruitful.''Do the bidding of my servants, and I may grant your Dúnedain friends safe passage through my lands.''One last hunt remains...speak with Arassiel.''Speak not with me, but the Wild Huntsman instead.''You have done your part...return to the Huntsman.'Arassiel has sent you forth to challenge the last of the spirits of the Wild Hunt in a test of wisdom.The stag-spirit of Arassiel dwells in the southern reaches of the Mournshaws.

