You have cleansed the Hall of Lights of the dangerous glow-worm infestation and should return to Alfirimbes with the news.Talk to Alfirimbes at Echad Sirion'We have victory for a short time, ${PLAYER}, and until the army from the East arrives, we must make the most of it.

'A company of Orcs fled from the assault upon Dol Guldur, and scouts tracked them from a distance until they entered a cavern here in the Mirk-eaves. I fear what evils they may be up to inside the tunnels there.

'Enter this cavern and find out what the Orcs are up to, ${PLAYER}. Defeat them once you do...and any other dangers that lurk within!''Thank you for cleansing the Hall of Lights of the glow-worm infestation, ${PLAYER}. That they disposed of the fleeing Orcs for us is a boon, but they still posed a threat to Echad Sirion. Our safety here was in jeopardy, and that must be our primary concern.''The Orcs entered a cave here in the Mirk-eaves and surely seek to effect some evil. Follow them and put an end to their schemes!''It is good to know that the Orcs have run afoul of danger, but the glow-worms are a threat to us as well! Return to the Hall of Lights and cleanse the cavern of them, ${PLAYER}!'Barvessain has requested you to aid her with collecting components for her alchemical investigations.Gath Ulunn is located behind the walls of the Orc-camp in Gathbúrz. The Hall of Lights, a cavern among the Mirk-eaves, is home to pestilent glow-worms and their queens. The ruins of Agistath, located among the Dourstocks, appear to be the final resting place of aged Audaghaim wine.

Barvessain has asked you to bring her egg-shells from the worms of Gath Ulunn, slime from the glow-worms of the Hall of Lights, and aged Audaghaim wine from Agistath.Collect egg-shells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect glow-worm slime (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect aged wine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Barvessain is high atop one of the towers in Ost Galadh.

You have collected many components for Barvessain and should bring them to her at Ost Galadh.'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! I am spending my time while we remain in Mirkwood refining the process of brewing balms and salves to heal the hurts of those wounded during the assault on Dol Guldur. It is slow work, but that is the price of truly useful business.

'A number of my company have reported to me the location of places that may contain useful alchemical ingredients. From Gath Ulunn, behind the walls of the Orc-camp in Gathbúrz, you might recover egg-shells from the worms being bred in that place. I hear too that the Hall of Lights, a cavern among the Mirk-eaves, is home to pestilent glow-worms and their queens; you might bring me slime from them that I could turn to useful purposes.

'My friend Cairches informs me too that the ruins of Agistath, located among the Dourstocks, appear to be the final resting place of aged Audaghaim wine. If you can bring me all of these useful ingredients, my work will be accelerated.''A number of my company have reported to me the location of places that may contain useful alchemical ingredients. From Gath Ulunn, behind the walls of the Orc-camp in Gathbúrz, you might recover egg-shells from the worms being bred in that place. I hear too that the Hall of Lights, a cavern among the Mirk-eaves, is home to pestilent glow-worms and their queens; you might bring me slime from them that I could turn to useful purposes.

'My friend Cairches informs me too that the ruins of Agistath, located among the Dourstocks, appear to be the final resting place of aged Audaghaim wine. If you can bring me all of these useful ingredients, my work will be accelerated.''You have returned with the ingredients I seek, and so quickly! I did not expect you to return with such haste, but you have my thanks for doing so.

'When crumbled into a fine powder, the egg-shells will be used as part of an unguent that can shield the bearer from the effects of fire. The slime provides the base for a soothing salve that can mitigate the effects of poison.

'The wine? It is thirsty work, the brewing of potions and the crafting of salves! You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, and those of the Elves who will be burned or poisoned as the campaign in Mirkwood continues!'Braiglinn is eager to keep the campaign against Dol Guldur in motion before the reinforcements from the East arrive.Entrances to the Warg-pens, the Sword-hall, and the Dungeons of Dol Guldur can be found along the rocky spire on which the fortress stands.

Braiglinn has asked you to gather a small fellowship of allies and to seize a strategic location in Dol Guldur.Seize the Warg-pens of Dol GuldurSeize the Sword-hall of Dol GuldurSeize the Dungeons of Dol GuldurBraiglinn is in Imlad Lalaith on the shore of Anduin, in Lothlórien.

You have seized a strategic objective in Dol Guldur and should report now to Braiglinn.Talk to Braiglinn at Imlad Lalaith'We have won as great a victory as we might have hoped, ${PLAYER}; the assault on Dol Guldur has surely set the plans of the Enemy back a step. An army marches from the East to reinforce the fortress, and we do not have the numbers to oppose it in strength.

'And yet until it arrives, there are still strategic objectives that can be won to strike further still against the forces that hold the fortress.

'Gather a small fellowship of allies and take one of these strategic locations, ${PLAYER}: the Warg-pens, the Sword-hall, or the Dungeons of Dol Guldur. We will sting the Enemy while we may!''You will need a small fellowship of allies to seize one of these strategic locations: the Warg-pens, the Sword-hall, or the Dungeons of Dol Guldur.''We may not hold it long, but let this be a reminder that the Golden Host still must be feared! We do not possess the numbers of the Enemy, but we make up for that lack with skill and with strength!

'The fortress of Dol Guldur is not unassailable, and we will continue to strike beyond its walls until such time as Lord Celeborn deems we must retreat. I remain here in the Golden Wood, to my dismay, but at his command; and from here I form the plans by which we can best leverage our abilities.

'The Enemy is surely learning that our abilities are not what he believed them to be. The Elves are not weak. The Elves, and their allies, are strong.'Cúcheron wishes for you to solve the mystery of the connexion between Audaghaim and the ruins of Agistath.The ruins of Agistath are located beyond a cave-mouth in the Dourstocks.

Cúcheron has asked you to investigate the ruins of Agistath.Defeat gaunt-men in Agistath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find some connexion between Agistath and AudaghaimCúcheron is outside the Haunted Inn, in Audaghaim.

You have investigated the ruins of Agistath for Cúcheron and should tell him what you found.Gravestones can be found throughout Audaghaim.

Cúcheron has asked you to leave the broken wooden toy at one of the gravestones located in Audaghaim.Cúcheron is outside the Haunted Inn, in Audaghaim.

You have done as Cúcheron asked and left the broken wooden toy at one of the gravestones in Audaghaim.Talk to Cúcheron at the Haunted Inn'When this campaign ends, I will lay down my bow and depart the shores of Middle-earth. I have had my fill of fighting. But still I am intrigued by the mystery of Audaghaim. What happened to this town, and to its people? Scouts recently discovered some ruins amid the Dourstocks, where gaunt-men roam and shades flit among the trees.

'I cannot leave this place until I know what connexion there is between Audaghaim and the ruins of Agistath. I cannot bear to leave this mystery unsolved, to rest heavily upon my mind during the uncounted years!

'Travel to Agistath for me and investigate the ruins, ${PLAYER}. This is the only tie to these lands I have left. I have spoken with Issuriel about this, but she does not agree with me. She has returned already to Cerin Amroth, and there will stay in contemplation for a little while yet.''There is a sad story behind Audaghaim's abandonment, I am certain; but it is to be hoped we have given whatever spirits still linger here some measure of peace.

'My time in Middle-earth is nearing its end, ${PLAYER}. I have no more need for my bow, Cúmaeth. If you desire to have it, it is now yours.''The ruins of Agistath are located beyond a cave-mouth here in the Dourstocks, ${PLAYER}. I must know what connexion there is between the ruins of Agistath and Audaghaim.''There are gravestones located throughout Audaghaim. Leave the broken wooden toy you found at one of them, and its former owner may find some measure of peace.''Tell me what you discovered among the ruins of Agistath.'

Cúcheron listens intently as you describe your adventure among the ruins, and the broken wooden toy you found.

'I think the townsfolk of Audaghaim fled this place, ${PLAYER}, with what possessions they could carry. Why they fled with such haste, or where they were heading, I cannot say, but it seems certain that few made it out of Agistath with their lives.

'There are graves among the weeds here in Audaghaim. Is it possible some of the townsfolk were left behind? It is clear to me that the wooden toy you found should be returned to its home. Leave it at one of the graves here in Audaghaim, and perhaps the shades that linger here and at Agistath will have some measure of peace.'The sorcerer Gorothúl still reigns from Sammath Gûl, his chambers in the depths of Dol Guldur.Gorothúl can be found in Sammath Gûl, his chambers within the fortress of Dol Guldur.

Bori has asked you to gather a fellowship of allies and to defeat the sorcerer Gorothúl in his chambers in Dol Guldur.Defeat Gorothúl in Sammath GûlBori is in the Chamber of Leadership, located off the Twenty-first Hall, in Moria.

You have defeated Gorothúl and should report the happy fact to Bori in Moria.Talk to Bori in the Chamber of Leadership'Zigilburk now rests in the depths with Óin its keeper, but the cause of our hurt remains. Gorothúl, sorcerer of Dol Guldur, still lives, and so long as he does he endangers the peace of Moria and Lothlórien.

'Gather a fellowship of allies and set forth for Sammath Gûl, his chambers in the fortress of Dol Guldur. Slay Gorothúl and end his menace, ${PLAYER}! We will not be free of this threat until the sorcerer is defeated.''You have triumphed over the sorceries of Gorothúl? A fine victory indeed, and hard-fought to be sure! A strong pupil and ally of the Enemy lies dead this day, ${PLAYER}. He is certain to feel this loss, knowing that his power to attack Khazad-dûm of the dwarves and Lórien of the Elves is lessened by this defeat!

'Again I thank you, my friend. You have done us all a great service this day!''Gather a fellowship of allies and set forth for Sammath Gûl, his chambers in the fortress of Dol Guldur. Slay Gorothúl and end his menace, ${PLAYER}! We will not be free of this threat until the sorcerer is defeated.'Lúth Greyhammer has envisioned the most grand statement of his hatred for the Orcs that have wronged his family and wants you to effect it!You are looking for Orcs, goblins, and uruks in Mirkwood, Lothlórien, and Moria.

Lúth Greyhammer wants you to find and defeat a single Orc, goblin, or uruk in all the regions in which a Greyhammer has been wronged.Defeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in MirkwoodDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in LothlórienDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in MoriaYou are looking for Orcs, goblins, and uruks in Eregion, the Trollshaws, and the Misty Mountains.

Lúth Greyhammer wants you to find and defeat a single Orc, goblin, or uruk in all the regions in which a Greyhammer has been wronged.Defeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in EregionDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in the TrollshawsDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in the Misty MountainsYou are looking for Orcs, goblins, and uruks in the Lone-lands, Bree-land, and the North Downs.

Lúth Greyhammer wants you to find and defeat a single Orc, goblin, or uruk in all the regions in which a Greyhammer has been wronged.Defeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in the Lone-landsDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in Bree-landDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in the North DownsYou are looking for Orcs, goblins, and uruks in Evendim, Forochel, and Angmar.

Lúth Greyhammer wants you to find and defeat a single Orc, goblin, or uruk in all the regions in which a Greyhammer has been wronged.Defeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in EvendimDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in ForochelDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in AngmarYou are looking for Orcs, goblins, and uruks in the Shire and Ered Luin.

Lúth Greyhammer wants you to find and defeat a single Orc, goblin, or uruk in all the regions in which a Greyhammer has been wronged.Defeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in the ShireDefeat an Orc, goblin, or uruk in Ered LuinTandri Greyhammer is in Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin.

Now that you have completed Lúth Greyhammer's glorious deed of sending a statement to the Orcs in every region where a Greyhammer was wronged, it is time to tell his father Tandri of your exploits.Talk to Tandri Greyhammer at Thorin's Hall'I have told you of my hatred for the Orcs, ${PLAYER}, and you know that no bounds can hold it! My passion for slaying Orcs cannot be contained by the borders of this forest, nor by those of any region in this Middle-earth!

'I have envisioned the grandest statement possible of my hatred for the Orcs. Let them rue the many times they have crossed the Greyhammer family and gnash their teeth in anguish that they ever did so!

'You will travel to every region in which an Orc, goblin, or uruk has caused harm to a Greyhammer and slay one of their kind, and you will shout "For the Greyhammers!" as you do so. Then perhaps the Orcs will know and fear my family, as they should! Do this first in Mirkwood, Lothlórien, and Moria, and work your way westward in sequence. Then speak to my father Tandri in Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin, and tell him of this glorious deed!''What in the names of all the dwarves has my son had you do? Travelling to all the regions in which a Greyhammer has been wronged and slaying a single Orc in each? I cannot believe you humoured him thus, ${PLAYER}! Does a ${CLASS} such as you have nothing more pressing to do than this?

'If my son Lúth and his brothers spent less time dreaming up ways to tell folk of their grievances with the Orcs and more time mining and working, perhaps we would have found some precious gemstones by now!

'Take this for your effort, ${PLAYER}. I will speak to Lúth myself. It is high time he began doing something productive with the time he currently spends complaining to strangers about his lot in life!''You are seeking Orcs or goblins here in Forochel to slay? I thoroughly approve of this aim, ${PLAYER}!

'There are few in this frigid land, however. Do not despair! I have seen a party of shivering goblins just to the west of this settlement, this Kauppa-kohta outpost!

'Look for shivering goblins on the far shore of the lake just to the west of here. Slay one for me, even though I am not a Greyhammer; but I like what I have heard of them!''You will travel to every region in which an Orc, goblin, or uruk has caused harm to a Greyhammer, you will slay one of their kind, and you will shout "For the Greyhammers!" as you do so. Then perhaps the Orcs will know and fear my family, as they should! Do this first in Mirkwood, Lothlórien, and Moria, and work your way westward in sequence. Then speak to my father Tandri in Thorin's Hall, in Ered Luin, and tell him of this glorious deed!''You're looking for goblins or Orcs in the Trollshaws? Well, I'll tell you this: you'd be out of luck if it were a week or so ago. Most of their kind is holed up in the mountains, or down deep in forgotten caves!

'A small party of goblins crossed the Last Bridge out of the Lone-lands a few days ago, and caused some trouble for one of me waggons! You might still find 'em, if you go now!

'These goblins were in the South Trollshaws, just south-west of the cave-claw infested ruins of Ost Dúrgonn. Defeat one for me, if your travels take you there!'Given time to reflect on her adventure with the Hidden Guard, Issuriel has come to a decision concerning her future.Bróin is in the Peaceful Path, located off Durin's Way, in Moria.

Issuriel has given you a beautiful flower to give to Bróin as a token of her friendship and thankfulness.'Thank you for coming to see me, ${PLAYER}. I have spent many days in restful peace here in Cerin Amroth, and it has done me a great deal of good; the effects of the Gwigael poison are now just a memory, and the spells of weakness have passed.'

Issuriel pauses for a moment, and seems unable to meet your gaze.

'I do not regret my decision to do without the Laidhris antidote, ${PLAYER}. Events unfolded differently than we thought they would, but I could not let the mission end in failure because of my own selfishness. Raddir did not have the choice I did, nor did Sigileth. Only Achardor seems to have understood what I came to know: that I would have closed my eyes forever if it meant the death and loss that happened to that point would have had a reason; that it would have mattered.

'Still, I am grateful for the actions of Bróin. I have picked a beautiful flower from the slopes of Cerin Amroth. Will you bring it to him in Moria, with my good wishes and my thankfulness? I understand he is recovering in the Peaceful Path, along Durin's Way.''I owe my life to Bróin. I did not think to count a dwarf among my closest friends, but now I cannot help but do so.'You give Bróin the flower and tell him of Issuriel's words.

'Well, uh, I don't know what to say! I... well... it is an honour, of course, and....'

Bróin turns a bright shade of pink and manages to stammer out an apology before starting again.

'It was nothing, of course, just the decent thing to do, and she such a noble Elf and all, and being so courageous on my people's account. It would be a dwarf of little honour who would abandon Issuriel to that vile poison. A Dourhand might, but no son of Brogur nor of Bósi, for that matter!

'She has the heart of a dwarf, I will tell you that! I mean... by that I mean that she is as brave as a dwarf, you understand, and not that she has my own heart, though of course she does, for how could she not? But what I mean is....'

Exhausted from the effort, Bróin lapses into confused silence and stares at you, red-faced.

'I should stick with the Orc-slaying, ${PLAYER}. I find it to be much easier!'Laeglang knows the counterattack from Dol Guldur is coming and wants you to do everything in your power to hinder it.Orcs can be found throughout Dol Guldur, as can the entrances to the Warg-pens, Sword-hall, and Dungeons of Dol Guldur.

Laeglang has asked you to defeat Orcs throughout Dol Guldur and to scout the locations of various points of interest throughout the fortress.Defeat Orcs throughout Dol Guldur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the entrance to the Warg-pensFind the entrance to the Sword-hallFind the entrance to the DungeonsLaeglang is outside the fortress of Dol Guldur.

You have done as Laeglang asked and should return to the scout now in victory.Talk to Laeglang outside Dol Guldur'Despite the losses, our assault upon Dol Guldur must be judged a success, ${PLAYER}, if not a lasting one. An army marches from the East to reinforce the fortress, and the Golden Host cannot hope to stand against the combined might of this new army and the Orcs already within Mirkwood.

'But we can sting this latter force, sting them with our arrows and the bite of our blades, and make them count the days until their reinforcements arrive. This we must do, ${CLASS}.

'Make the climb once again to Dol Guldur and slay Orcs within its bounds. Find too the locations where great concentrations of the Enemy reside, the entrances to the Warg-pens, the Sword-hall, and the Dungeons of Dol Guldur.''The Orcs must be counting the days until their reinforcements from the East arrive, ${PLAYER}! This is no lasting victory, to be certain, but it tastes sweet all the same!''Orcs can be found throughout Dol Guldur, ${PLAYER}; they must be defeated. Find too the entrances to the Warg-pens, the Sword-hall, and the Dungeons.'Ningloril has learned that the Orcs are attempting to breed worms in the hatchery of Gath Ulunn, following the assault on Dol Guldur.Worms and Orcs can be found within Gath Ulunn, a cavern located among the Orc camps in the northern reaches of Gathbúrz.

Ningloril has asked you to gather some allies and to defeat worms and Orcs within Gath Ulunn and to tip over any of the odorous barrels being used in the breeding of the worms.Defeat worms within Gath Ulunn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orcs within Gath Ulunn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tip over odorous barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ningloril is in Thangúlhad, the camp of the Golden Host in Gathbúrz.

You have hindered the worm breeding program in Gath Ulunn and should tell Ningloril about your success.Talk to Ningloril at Thangúlhad'The Golden Host has assaulted the fortress of Dol Guldur, but now we wait for the hammer-blow to fall. We do not have the numbers to stand long against the armies that approach from the East, so we must do what we can before the Enemy's counterattack.

'Scouts report that among the Orc-camps in Gathbúrz, numerous enemy forces have been seen entering a cavern in the hills. Many of the Orcs carry barrels full of some odorous substance with them into this cave. They call this place Gath Ulunn, and our scouts fear the Orcs are using this cavern as a hatchery for breeding worms.

'Find Gath Ulunn and defeat Orcs and worms alike within its passages. Tip over any of the barrels you see within the cave, ${PLAYER}. We must hinder these breeding efforts soon, lest we face an army of worms as well as an army of Orcs! You may wish to have a few allies with you, for Gath Ulunn is sure to be crawling with both Orcs and worms!''It pleases me to know that you have dealt with the threat of Gath Ulunn. The Orcs will be unable to raise enough worms now to threaten the Golden Host while still we remain within sight of Dol Guldur.

'You have given us a great gift with this deed, ${PLAYER}: the gift of time. I thank you for it.''A cave entrance to Gath Ulunn can be found among the Orc-camps in northern Gathbúrz. Enter the cavern and defeat the Orcs and worms you find. Tip over the odorous barrels within, as well, to hinder the breeding program of the vile creatures!

'An army of Orcs is bad enough. An army of Orcs and worms is even worse! You may wish to have one or two allies with you on this adventure.'Sigileth fell during the assault on Dol Guldur, and it is now your duty to present her knives to Lord Celeborn, as she wished.Lord Celeborn is in the city of Caras Galadhon, in Lothlórien.

Ellunen has asked you to deliver Sigileth's knives to Lord Celeborn, as that was her wish in life and is certain to be the same in death.Talk to a Galadhrim Guard outside the gates of Caras Galadhon and complete 'The Paths of Caras Galadhon'Lord Celeborn is at his house in Caras Galadhon, the Elf-city of Lothlórien.

Ellunen has asked you to deliver Sigileth's knives to Lord Celeborn.'It grieves me to tell you this, ${PLAYER}, but Sigileth of the Hidden Guard fell during the assault on Dol Guldur. She fought bravely, and slew countless Orcs, but in the end, Lanchigil and Egnassigil availed her not. I retrieved them from the body of a slain Olog-hai.

'Sigileth was given to carving a notch in the hilts of her knives when one of them delivered a killing stroke -- there would not be sufficient space on the hilts left following her final stand in the fortress of Dol Guldur.

'She desired to make a gift of the knives to Lord Celeborn when the hilts were full of such marks. Will you deliver Lanchigil and Egnassigil to him? It is what Sigileth would want.''Sigileth fell during the assault on Dol Guldur, but she slew many foes. Bring her knives, Lanchigil and Egnassigil, to Lord Celeborn in Caras Galadhon. She wished to gift them to the Lord and Lady when she had filled their hilts with death-marks, and she has more than done so. It is time to fulfill her wishes.''Sigileth fell during the assault on Dol Guldur, but she slew many foes. Bring her knives, Lanchigil and Egnassigil, to Lord Celeborn in Caras Galadhon. She wished to gift them to the Lord and Lady when she had filled their hilts with death-marks, and she has more than done so. It is time to fulfill her wishes.''It saddens me to know that Sigileth of the Hidden Guard will not return to this land she loved. She knew the dangers she faced and wrote the tale of her victories on the hides of Orcs with her beloved knives.'

Celeborn sighs and carefully studies Lanchigil and Egnassigil.

'It was the desire of Sigileth to gift me these knives, and I do not wish to gainsay that desire; but so too does it grieve me that they will no longer strike fear into the hearts of her foes, remaining as they would within Caras Galadhon.

'I propose then a compromise. I will retain one of the knives, and its brother I give to you to do with as you will.'Many dwarves of the Iron Garrison have returned to Moria with Bori and Bróin, and the fate of Zigilburk must be decided.Bori is in the Chamber of Leadership, a small room located in the southern wall of the Twenty-first Hall, in Moria.

Goldagnir has told you that Bori has returned to Moria and desires to speak with you when next you pass through the dwarf-kingdom.Talk to Bori in the Chamber of Leadership, in MoriaBori is in the Chamber of Leadership, located in the southern wall of the Twenty-first Hall, in Moria.

Bori and Bróin have determined that the dwarves must not retain possession of Zigilburk and have decided to return the mithril axe to where it was found.Talk to Bori and aid him with the return of ZigilburkBori is in the Chamber of Leadership, located in the southern wall of the Twenty-first Hall, in Moria.

Zigilburk has been returned to the watery chamber where it once lay hidden. You should speak now to Bori about the decision to abandon possession of the mithril axe.Talk to Bori in the Chamber of Leadership'The Golden Host has accomplished what it set out to do, ${PLAYER}: we have delayed an attack by the forces of Dol Guldur, kept their attention focused upon the doorstep of the fortress, and proven strong our friendship with the dwarves of the Iron Garrison. We wait now for the next stroke to come, and must stand against it as best we may.

'The dwarves Bróin and Bori have returned to Moria bearing the mithril axe, Zigilburk. When next you return to the Twenty-first Hall, Bori desired that you visit him in the Chamber of Leadership. He wishes to discuss the final fate of the mithril axe.''Thank you for coming back here to Khazad-dûm, my friend! It was a long journey for Bróin and me, and we spoke at length concerning the mithril axe. It has brought us little but misery, and my cousin convinced me that it could still do great harm in the future, if wielded.

'Truth be told, I did not need much convincing! I have seen first-hand the recklessness the axe stirs in the hearts of those who wield it; my stay in the dungeons of Dol Guldur speaks loudly of this point!

'Our fathers initially resisted, but have now grudgingly assented to our plan: the dwarves cannot retain possession of Zigilburk. Speak to me again, and we will make this a reality.''I must thank you again, ${PLAYER}: abandoning such a precious and valuable weapon is not an easy thing, even for dwarves for whom it has brought such grief. But it is for the best. Desire to possess items of such beauty and value has often led my people down the path to misfortune. With your help, Bróin and I have had the chance to turn aside from that path before it was too late.''Bori and Bróin have returned to Moria with the mithril axe, Zigilburk. Bori wished to see you when next your travels bring you by the Chamber of Leadership, located off the Twenty-first Hall in Moria.''Are you ready to witness the sealing of Zigilburk, ${PLAYER}? The sooner it is done the better it will be for the Iron Garrison, I believe, as does Bróin.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>Pethelen the Elf has been entrusted with bringing word to you of an urgent matter that is a great concern of Master Elrond of Rivendell.Pethelen is at the front porch of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.

The Elf Pethelen is eager to speak with you and travel together to see Master Elrond about some urgent matter.Talk to Pethelen and meet with Master ElrondPethelen is at the front porch of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell.

You have met with Master Elrond of Rivendell, and have been charged with an important task: the gathering of Aragorn's kin from all throughout Eriador, that they may come to his aid in the south.Talk to Pethelen at the Last Homely House'${PLAYER}, we are met in time of need, and it is a joy to see you! You must have received my message, for little else could have brought you hither with such haste!

'I did not dare to speak openly of the reason for Master Elrond's request in my letter, for fear that the message might be intercepted. I apologize for drawing you here with so little information, but Master Elrond will explain in detail what I could not.

'Speak, if you are ready! We will go to him together, and he will tell you what has prompted his call.''Master Elrond was right to impress upon me the need for haste, ${PLAYER}! If Aragorn has need of the Dúnedain, they will need to be gathered with as much speed as can be managed. It will not be an easy task, for the Dúnedain are given to wandering the wild. They may be scattered across all of Eriador!''Master Elrond awaits. Quickly, ${PLAYER}! It is my understanding that any delay will serve to do us great harm, so let us act with haste!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>The battle upon the slopes below Dol Guldur rages fiercely. As the Malledhrim attempt to lay siege to its walls, the Orcs of Gathbúrz launch one counterattack after another in an attempt to drive them back.Orcs can be found throughout Gathbúrz.

Rodelleth has bidden you lay waste to the Orc-soldiers garrisoning Gathbúrz, to hinder their own imminent assault upon Lothlórien.Defeat Orcs in Gathbúrz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.

You should return to Rodelleth with news of your success.Talk to Rodelleth in Thangúlhad'Listen to me carefully ${PLAYER}, the tower of Dol Guldur is our ultimate objective, but it is not fated to fall to us this day. We have not the power to bring down those walls -- not as long as the Eye of Sauron is turned towards Lothlórien -- and soon Mirkwood will be overrun with Enemy reinforcements.

'We are here to draw the enemy's ire and to inflict as grievous a wound as we may before we are driven back across the Anduin. The Orcs of Dol Guldur will eventually fall upon the Golden Wood, but we can and will delay that day.

'Thus our true goal here is to destroy as much of the garrison of Gathbúrz as possible before then: soldiers, supplies, leadership...whatever we can lay to ruin before we are forced to retreat. Every Orc you slay here is one less to ford the Anduin when they come against Lothlórien in the coming days.''The foul Orcs of Dol Guldur dare tread upon this ground, once the home of Elves...for that, they must perish.''Well fought, ${PLAYER}. The garrison of Gathbúrz is disorganized and vulnerable. You can inflict many casualties there while the Orcs vainly attempt to drive us off of this hill.

'Look to your own survival, though: we cannot afford to lose many, or we will find ourselves overwhelmed ere our task is complete.'Defeat many Wargs in Southern Mirkwood.Defeat Wargs in Southern MirkwoodDefeat many Wargs in Southern Mirkwood.Defeat Wargs in Southern MirkwoodThe Wargs of Draugdegil are among the most powerful that Haukur has ever seen.Kill Wargs in Draugdegil.Defeat Wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Wood-trolls in Enedwaith.Defeat Wood-trolls in EnedwaithDefeat many Wood-trolls in Enedwaith.Defeat Wood-trolls in EnedwaithBledhun's party was attacked and scattered by the Dievlig, wicked Dunlending outcasts dwelling in the Bonevales.Evil Dunlendings may be found along the path and up the hill south of Bledhun.

