You hastily introduce Blodwen to the Elder as being the new relation of the dead folk at the Herd-lands.

'Ah! Poor child! You risked much to bring us this news... ${PLAYER} was good to help you find us. Find some place to rest, and the people of Lhan Tarren will tend your hurts.''You have saved my life by bringing me here. I thank you, ${PLAYER}. I hope I may make a home here.'The wights of the Bonevales and the Dievlig pose a great threat to all the clans of Dunland.Echad Naeglanc lies to the south and east of Bledhun's camp.

Bledhun has asked you to warn his allies regarding the evil ones who dwell in the Bonevales.Talk to Haul at Echad Naeglanc'The wights and the movements of the Dievlig pose a growing threat to the clans of Dunland. Several of our allies are located at Echad Naeglanc, the camp of a northern Duvodiad like yourself, on the southern border of the Bonevales...will you bring word to them and warn them of the danger that the evil ones pose?

'Travel south along the road, then turn due east and travel up the path to Echad Naeglanc.''Only a few hours ago, Echad Naeglanc was attacked by the Dievlig. These foul vermin took my friends captive, but I was able to fight them off in the end.''Seek out the Ranger-encampment of Echad Naeglanc.'The looters you harassed all spoke of the likelihood of an invasion upon all of Trum Dreng. Such an invasion would end with the Stag-clan being driven out of Dunland once and for all.The chieftain of the Dragon-clan invaders can surely be found at the main house in the Herd-lands, looking down upon the farm from on high.

You should kill the chieftain and steal the plans for the invasion of Trum Dreng by the Dragon-clan.Collect plans for the invasion of Trum DrengBlodwen awaits you in her hiding place near the river in the Herd-lands.

You should return to Blodwen with the map you found and with the dire news that Murig has escaped you.'${PLAYER}, I owe you an apology. I asked you to leave me to die, but I see now that I must endeavour to help my late husband's clan. Lhan Tarren must be warned!

'The chief of this invasion party has taken the farmhouse near here; I have seen the comings and goings of the Draig-lûth. Our best hope is to kill him, and learn what we can of the Dragon-clan's plan to invade.

'I will wait for you here, ${PLAYER}. Be careful... the chief will be a strong man.''Please hurry, ${PLAYER}. You must search for some hint of their mission, or else Trum Dreng will surely be lost. The Dragon-clan is cruel -- they attack by night, when all good folk sleep.''Murig escaped? That is ill news, but no matter -- we cannot waste any more time here. We must bring this information to Lhan Tarren.

'I have not yet met the Stag-clan of that town. They were my husband's people, not my own. We must rely upon your favour there to make sure this warning reaches them in time!'

Blodwen hesitates.

'They are the closest family I have now, yet I do not even know them. Will they turn me away, ${PLAYER}?'After their rescue, Naeglanc and his allies returned to their encampment.The Dievlig patrol can be found upon the hill north of Echad Naeglanc.

Naeglanc has asked you to defeat the remnant of the patrol which attacked him and his allies and bring him their sigils.Defeat Dievlig in the Bonevales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect sigils (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Naeglanc is at Echad Naeglanc, south of the hill where you fought the Dievlig patrol.

You should bring the sigils you collected to Naeglanc with news of your victory.Talk to Naeglanc at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales'Thank you for coming to our rescue, ${PLAYER}. Several of the local Dunlendings have played an important role in bringing members of the Grey Company through the Bonevales. These fine people have risked their lives to help us, and we must do the same in kind.

'I would have you seek out the Dievlig and lay them low, both to avenge the folk who have fought at our side and to secure our passage through the Bonevales.

'Travel north and up the hill... there you will find the remnant of the patrol that attacked us. Bring me their sigils as evidence that the deed is done.''Have you dealt with the Dievlig patrols yet?''With the patrol scattered, we should be able to learn what is happening here in the Bonevales.'The wolves of Trum Dreng press ever closer to the village, and Guto cares more for the safety of the Stag-clan than preparations for a superfluous festival.Wolves roam the rocky plains south of Lhan Tarren.

You should slay wolves for the protection and well-being of the Stag-clan.Defeat wolves in Trum Dreng (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Guto holds his post at Lhan Tarren, the village of the Stag-clan in Trum Dreng.

You should speak with Guto and tell him that you slew many wolves while roaming the wilds beyond the village.Talk to Guto at Lhan Tarren'My grandfather talks of the importance of remembrance, family, and clan pride, but what of the real dangers pressing against us? Every year, more people of Trum Dreng fall to the evils of the wild.

'My people dwindle, and they are weak and afraid. The old blood of the Stag will likely not survive another generation.

'If you want to truly help my folk, worry less about the Feast of the Running Stag and more about the wolves that loom nearer and nearer.''I am sorry if I put you to any trouble, ${PLAYER} -- though I am not sorry that we have fewer wolves to harry us.

'My grandfather and I see things very differently, and I was only complaining, but it was wrong of me to tease you about doing the work of my own people.

'I find that I often despair of our future, when we are so hopeless and useless a people. I am glad you are among us now, even if only for a short time.''Do not waste my time with silly thoughts of feasts and festivals, not while we are troubled by wolves and worse!'You have decided to travel with the group heading south into Dunland by way of Trum Dreng, the Land of the Stag.Braigiar will speak with you again just across the border of Enedwaith and Dunland, at Dúvispont, in Trum Dreng.Talk to Braigiar once you arrive at Dúvispont, in DunlandThe plains of Trum Dreng lie to the south.

Braigiar has asked you to scout Trum Dreng, keeping an eye out for its residents.Scout ahead and help an inhabitant of Trum DrengBraigiar is waiting to speak with you just outside Lhan Tarren, the village of the Stag-clan.

You should speak with Braigiar before proceeding.Talk to Braigiar in Lhan Tarren, the village of the Stag-clan'Very good, ${PLAYER}. I welcome you into the group that will travel into Trum Dreng, the Land of the Stag! We will do our best to come that way into Dunland free of danger.

'We will move swiftly and silently, and our company will be in number small enough as to escape prying eyes. Saruman knows that we must pass into Dunland, but the time and manner of our coming is still ours to control.

'Let us be off at once! We can stop and see how things fare once we have crossed into Trum Dreng.''Here we are. We have crossed into Dunland, and now find ourselves in the Land of the Stag. Be on your guard. We need to know what the situation here is, and we can only know that by observing its people.

'Scout the area to the south and determine what we will be dealing with as we pass through this land.''We have already learned much about Dunland from your brief encounter, ${PLAYER}. There is much we can do here in Trum Dreng to help its people and also to smooth the passage of the Grey Company through this land.''Scout the area to our south, and remain on your guard. We must know what the situation here in Trum Dreng may be before we travel south in greater number.''We should leave at once, ${PLAYER}, and pass south into Dunland. We can speak again just inside Trum Dreng.'You have decided to travel with the group heading south into Dunland by way of the Bonevales.Prestadír will speak with you again just across the border of Enedwaith and Dunland, in the Bonevales, west of the road.Talk to Prestadír just inside the entrance of the Bonevales, west of the road from EnedwaithPrestadír has asked you to scout the Bonevales and learn what threats may lie in wait here and to help Bledhun and his friends.Help Bledhun and his friends, then meet Prestadír at the hidden valleyPrestadír is waiting to speak with you at the camp he established in a hidden valley in the Bonevales.Talk to Prestadír at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales'I am glad that you have chosen to accompany my group into the Bonevales, ${PLAYER}. The road will be dangerous, and I could use your abilities. We will be mostly in the open and exposed unless we are very careful to stay in the shadow of the cliffs.

'We will not travel by the road! I will meet up with you just west of the road as it enters Dunland.

'Let us be off at once! We can assess what awaits us once we cross into the Bonevales.''We are here, ${PLAYER}. We have crossed over into the Bonevales. We need to know what the situation in this valley may be, and what threats could endanger this leg of our quest.

'Bledhun here tells a tale of mysterious happenings. You should hear him out and do as he says. We will need allies in this land.

'Once you have aided Bledhun and his friends, we can meet up again in a hidden valley to the south. It will be the perfect location from which to scout the twisting ways of the Bonevales. Travel ahead and meet me at the camp there.''This will be a good place from which to launch our exploration of the Bonevales, ${PLAYER}. We should help the people of the Bonevales as much as we can, for they could be valuable allies against the dangers that await us further south.''There is a hidden valley to the south which will serve us well for a camp. Go there, and we will speak again if it be so, but first you should help Bledhun and his friends.''Let us now travel south into Dunland by way of the Bonevales, ${PLAYER}. We will speak again once we cross over, west of the road that enters Dunland.'Among the buildings in Lhan Gogledh, Trehéarn Brenin has begun to accept offers from unnatural forces in the area.You should seek out and destroy any banners that you find in the area.Destroy banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Among the buildings in Lhan Gogledh, patrolling sentries watch for enemies attempting to enter the encampment.Lhan Gogledh lies along the path north of Lhucu's hut.

