Ilar told you to bring word of your discoveries to Naeglanc.Talk to Naeglanc at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales'With the recovery of the chain-links, I have no doubt that the Dievlig are indeed complicit in the raising of the wights here in the Bonevales. This must not be allowed to continue.

'Return to Naeglanc at Echad Naeglanc, south and west of here. He will wish to know what we have learned.''While the attack by the Dievlig was unexpected, I fear that I must agree with Ilar: these chains confirm that Trehéarn Brenin is complicit in these actions.

'One of our allies, Lhucu, is actually his daughter, and I now fear for her safety.''Bring word at once to Naeglanc!'The Feast of the Running Stag is in need of a significant bonfire, so you have been asked to collect a fuel mixture of kindling and scented herbs.Kindling and scented herbs can be collected on the stark and rough plains around Lhan Tarren.

You should collect herbs and kindling for a magnificent bonfire to be lit at the festival.Collect kindling for the bonfire (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Pick scented herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ivor awaits you in Lhan Tarren, the Stag-clan's village of Dunland.

You should bring the kindling and scented herbs you gathered to Ivor, who wishes to use them to fuel an especially magnificent bonfire.'Honoured traveller! I am so glad that you brought Elain back to us in time for the feast. Many feared that she was dead. If only she would take a husband, she would not get into so much trouble! But she is a headstrong girl.

'I wish to build this bonfire to represent the depths of my gratitude that she has come back to us safe and whole. It should be towering, burn hot as the summer, and smell of fair flowers.

'I will need more kindling and scented herbs to fuel it as it burns, if it is to be so great. Will you help me collect these things?''The fuels I need are simple. They can be found in the plains around our village. You could collect them in half a day if you wished.

'The fire must burn as bright as the spirit of Elain and as that of her saviour!''Ah, these will do just fine. Take heed tonight of the bonfire...it will fill the air with lovely scents and will burn as hot and bright as the stars in summer.'The Dievlig have attacked travellers and even the village of Lhan Bach and stolen food and supplies, leaving the villagers with little to sustain themselves.The stolen food can be found at Lhan Gogledh, north of Lhucu's hut.

Lhucu has asked you to recover the stolen food for the people of Lhan Bach.Collect food-stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lhucu is at her hut, south of Lhan Gogledh.

You should bring the food-stores to Lhucu so that she may redistribute them to the people of Lhan Bach.Talk to Lhucu at her hut'Among the scattered homes below, my father's men have stolen supplies and food. The food was taken for his soldiers, leaving the people of Lhan Bach with little to sustain themselves.

'Undoubtedly, my father had the food taken to Lhan Gogledh, which lies on the road to the north. Will you go there and recover it?

'Returning the provender to its rightful owners may go a long way towards convincing the folk of Lhan Bach to take up arms against my father.''This food will be distributed among our people, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for recovering it from my father's men.''Have you captured the food-stores?'The Elder has asked you to remind the gentle folk of Lhan Tarren that the festival is to begin at sundown.The people of Lhan Tarren can be found throughout the village.

You should speak with the members of the Stag-clan to remind them to be present at the Feast of the Running Stag. Their presence will ease the Elder's worry that his clan has grown soft and weak.The Elder awaits you in the village of Lhan Tarren.

You should return to the Elder and tell him that you spoke gentle reminders to many of the villagers.Return to the Elder of Lhan Tarren'Have you been enjoying your stay thus far, dear ${PLAYER}? There are not many hours left until the Feast of the Running Stag, and I want to make certain that everyone is ready precisely at sundown. The ritual is an important part of our heritage.

'My good clansmen are not always the most observant when it comes to these things. Indeed, the blood of the Stag-clan grows thin, and only Elain and Guto show promise of growing into true Stags.

'My feet are sore and my words are tired, but I do what I can to nurture my folk, so that they will be able to carry on when I am gone. I wish that they could be more like you! Please, will you go and remind them all to be present at sundown?''You will find the clansmen about Lhan Tarren. You will not have to search far.''Aye, I know. The Elder sent someone to remind us all yesterday, and the day before that as well. We will all attend, as we do every year, but I do not see the point in continuing on with this ritual.

'We go to humour the Elder; that is all.''Is it really that time again? It is a tedious way to spend a night, but at least we can enjoy a feast.

'I do not see the point of carrying on this old tradition. No one cares but the Elder.''Bah! The Elder's eyes are not good, nor is his memory. He will surely not notice if I am not present at the Feast of the Running Stag. It is an old tedious rite, anyhow.

'But I see that you are here to nag me in his place, which means that you will tell him. Very well, I will go! But there is no sense in it.

'I will surely sleep while the rites are performed; wake me when it is time to eat!''Do not worry, ${PLAYER}, I will attend! I intend to learn more of the rites of the Stag-clan. I fear that the Elder shall soon need assistance when he performs the Feast of the Running Stag. Someone will need to be his eyes when he is blind.

'Will you be there, my friend? I have been hoping to share the meal with you, after what you did for me.''I will promise no such thing, Duvodiad. My grandfather believes in the preservation of our culture, but I believe in the preservation of our lives.

'If you failed to notice, one of our clanswomen was attacked not many days ago. Someone must remember these things, rather than remember a history lived long, long ago.

'I am grateful to you, but I make no promises. Now, stop troubling me and go humour my grandfather somewhere else.'The Elder listens with a sad smile as you recount your conversations to him.

'Aye, they are generally a soft lot. But that is no matter... I am glad they are coming. Most of them, at least. Thank the Gwirod for Elain; she is a jewel among coals!

'My grandson is a good boy, but like a bull in both body and mind. I pray he will learn to think of living as oft as he thinks of war. When I die, he will lead this clan in my stead....

'Yes... I hope there is still time for him to learn.'This note details the order to attack Echad Naeglanc.Haul is at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales.

You should bring the note to Haul at once.Bring the note to Haul at Echad Naeglanc in the BonevalesThis note reads:

'Seek out any duvodiad and drive them from this place. There are two encampments... capture as many of them as possible, kill the rest.

Trehéarn'

Haul at Echad Naeglanc will be interested in this note.'I should have known. Trehéarn of the Dievlig is a vicious monster.'Makeshift barricades have been built by the Dragon-clan raiders who took this important Trum Dreng landmark, and while the Stags stand on the other side, they have no hope of winning back the watch-tower.Barricades can be found surrounding the watch-tower in Trum Dreng.

You should destroy the barricades and defeat the vigilant raiders who guard them.Destroy barricades around the watch-tower (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elain guards the path leading up to the watch-tower.

You should speak with Elain and tell her that the barricades have been destroyed, and the path to the tower is now clear.Return to Elain at the watch-tower'Do you see the barricades around the tower? They were hastily built, but seem to be well-guarded by the Dragon-clan.

'You should destroy those and defeat the guards as well, or else we can never hope to win back the tower.

'Please hurry, ${PLAYER}! I will hold the path as best I can, but I am not half the warrior that you are.''The barricades must fall before we can hope to get closer. The tower is too well-guarded.''Well done as always, my friend. The way is safer now. We may press nearer and bring down the Draig-lûth.

'They picked an unfortunate time to try to take our lands from us. How fortunate for us, however, that a great hero from faraway lands chose to lend us aid!'It is clear the the Dragon-clan invaders are amassing weapons for a siege against anyone who rails against the tower. Destroying the tar will be crucial to reclaiming the watch-tower.Buckets of tar can be found around the watch-tower in Trum Dreng.

You should destroy buckets of tar so that it cannot be used to make flaming arrows.Destroy buckets of tar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elain can be found on the path by the watch-tower in Trum Dreng.

You should tell Elain that you have destroyed the tar that was meant to be brought to the top of the tower.Return to Elain at the watch-tower'I can see buckets of tar scattered about... surely they mean to light flaming arrows and set people afire should they threaten their conquest.

'If you destroy the tar, approaching the lot within the watch-tower should be safer. It looks like they only just arrived and ran in before their hoard could be delivered up.

'Quickly, ${PLAYER}, before they can bring more supplies into the tower!''If these archers make flaming arrows, there is no telling what could happen....''Well done! We will stand a much better chance now. Are you ready to face the leader of this rabble and drive him off for good?'Murig has settled at the watch-tower of Trum Dreng. If this waypoint is to be secured, he must be called down and defeated so that the Stag-clan can reclaim it.Murig can be found at the watch-tower in Trum Dreng.

You should bang on the door to see if Murig will be foolish enough to come down from his eyrie.Bang on the door to the watch-tower to summon MurigElain can be found on the hill that leads to the watch-tower, defending against approaching Dragon-clansmen in the plains.

You should return to Elain and tell her that the watch-tower has been reclaimed for the Stag-clan.Return to Elain on the path to the watch-tower'The leader of this band has taken up residence within the watch-tower. With them peering out over all the lands from such a high point, we cannot hope to secure Trum Dreng once more without a full army. Alas that my peoples have grown so few and weak.

'But there is still hope, ${PLAYER}. If we can cut our way through to the tower, we can surely call Murig down from high. He will surely think that a commotion at the door will be his own folk making the noise. He will come down, I think, and we can defeat him on the ground.''Try banging on the door and see if Murig comes down. He might think it is his own kin making the commotion.''You have done better than I could have hoped to do myself, ${PLAYER}; the watch-tower is ours again! I wish that you could join our clan for good.

'Trum Dreng would be so much safer if you were here.'The Dragon-clan must be taught a lesson if they are to attack their fellow Men at the bidding of Isengard.Dragon-clansmen in the White Hand encampment show signs of belonging to Isengard instead of acting upon their own motives.

You should collect evidence of the White Hand from the Dragon-clan warriors of the encampment.Collect symbols of the White Hand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Guto can be found at his small camp-site in the southern fields of Trum Dreng.

You should return to Guto with the White Hand symbols you collected.'The Dragon-clan killed my father, and I was more than ready to believe that they have attacked Trum Dreng for no better reason than their own menace.

'It would seem that they are being driven by a force larger than themselves, however. What does the White Hand have to do with it? Does not that emblem belong to Isengard?

'If you would, go collect emblems of the White Hand from the Dragon-clansmen at the encampment. They should be ashamed for attacking their own people at Isengard's bidding!''How do your efforts against the Dragon-clan go thus far, ${PLAYER}? Is this not much better than standing around, thinking and waiting, as my grandfather does?''Well done, ${PLAYER}! This is just what I was looking for.

'It is the queerest thing, is it not? The Dragon-clan has always acted on its own.

'No matter; now that we have proof that Isengard is involved, we shall attack them too!'The peaceful people of Lhan Tarren are rattled by the recent violent aggression of the Dragon-clan in Trum Dreng. It would ease the disturbed fears of the villagers to see their food-stores supplemented.Wild turnips tend to grow in the fields south of Lhan Tarren.

You should collect wild turnips to help bolster the food-stores in Lhan Tarren.Collect wild turnips (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grigor resides in Lhan Tarren, worrying over the food-stores and the distressing thought of a future emergency.

You should bring the turnips you gathered to Grigor.'${PLAYER}, I am pleased that you are here. Ever since Elain was attacked by the Dragon-clan, I have not been able to calm myself. What if we are attacked? We have not the stores to feed our village if some catastrophe were to befall us.

'There should be a few hours yet before the Feast of the Running Stag. I happen to know that wild turnips are in season, and they grow in the fields to the south this time of year. Would you be so good as to collect some so that our stores may be supplemented? It would do much to ease my worries.''I am in constant terror of what state we would be in if you had not brought Elain back to us. But how can we prepare against such a terrible situation? If only we had harvested more crops this year....''These were all the turnips you could find? I suppose it will do, for a short day's work. It is not much, but I thank you.'

Grigor turns back to his troubled thoughts.

'What can we do, what can we do...?'Heartened by the potential allegiance of the elders of Lhan Bach, Lhucu proposes a plan to liberate the village.Trehéarn Brenin's banners fly in Lhan Bach, south of Lhucu's hut.

Lhucu has asked you to tear down her father's standards that now hang throughout the village of Lhan Bach.Tear down Dievlig banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lhucu is at her hut, north of Lhan Bach.

You should return to Lhucu and let her know that the standards have been destroyed.Talk to Lhucu at her hut'From this vantage point, I can see new standards flying in the valley below. These standards seem to indicate that my father may be seeking new allies to renew his fight.

'Will you go down to Lhan Bach and tear down these standards? That, perhaps, will embolden the people against my father's tyranny.''With the banners removed from the village below, we have sent a clear message to my father's forces: their tyranny shall not be tolerated!''Have you torn down my father's banners?'Naeglanc and his allies continue to battle the evil wights and spirits which have arisen within the Bonevales.Wights can be found among the cairns east along the road above the Bone Quarry.

Naeglanc has asked you to banish any wights you might find around the cairns in the eastern valley.Defeat wights in the eastern valley (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mair can be found in the eastern valley above the Bone Quarry.

Naeglanc asked you to speak with Mair.Talk to Mair among the cairns'Along the valley wall above the Bone Quarry, a small set of cairns trail further to the west. A large number of wights have been drawn to this area for some unknown reason.

'Can you seek out the wights in these cairns and banish them from the Bonevales? It is troubling that the foul demons have begun to move more freely.

'Travel eastwards along the ridge above the Bone Quarry and follow the valley to its end. There you will find the cairns in question. When you have done this, seek Mair among the cairns.''Thank you for sending these abominations to oblivion. The evil they represent cannot be tolerated in these sacred lands.''Deal with those wights, then speak with Mair.''Mair is encamped above the Bone Quarry.'Elain, the huntress you rescued not long ago, wishes to finish the hunt she began on the day she was captured.Red-eye was said to be at a den to the south-west.

Elain has asked you to hunt down Red-eye in her stead while she prepares for the evening's rites.Defeat Red-eyeElain awaits you in Lhan Tarren.

You should speak with Elain and inform her that you slew her old enemy.Talk to Elain at Lhan Tarren'${PLAYER}! We seem to have a little time left before the Feast of the Stag begins. I wish to finish the hunt I began the day I was taken, but the Elder has asked me to help him prepare for tonight.

'There is an old fiend who has brazenly walked into town and stolen hens from right under our noses. His howl sends a jolt of fear down the spines of my kin. I was stalking him to his den to the south-west while the Draig-lûth rogues were likewise stalking me.

'His name is Red-eye, an evil old menace of a wolf, and I intend to see him on the end of a spear! If you happen to slay him while you are out in the plains, I will be even more impressed with you!''Old Red-eye's cruel howls will trouble the Stag-clan no more! Perhaps now our roosts will remain at peace.

'Come, ${PLAYER}. It is almost time for feasting and the telling of tales. You have done quite enough for one day!''The wolf I sought was deep in a den, and I stalked him for many long hours before I became aware that the Dragon-clan was trailing me in the same manner. They took me before I could get too close!'Wights have begun to rise up from the cairns of the Bonevales, presenting a threat to all who dwell in Dunland.The Bone Quarry lies to the east of Echad Naeglanc.

Naeglanc has asked you to close several cairn-openings within the Bone Quarry.Seal cairn-openings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ilar is at his camp, north and east of the Bone Quarry.

You should seek out Ilar and let him know that the cairns have been sealed.Talk to Ilar at his camp in the Bonevales'There have been reports of wights rising from the ancient cairns that line the Bone Quarry. These cairns have stood for generations, unsullied until now. We must find a way to close the cairns.

'Will you seek out the cairn-openings and seal the entrances? If so, travel down the path, then east to the Bone Quarry.

'When you have sealed the cairns, find Ilar and tell him of your deed.''With the cairns sealed, fewer of the wights can emerge to stalk the land.  It is a shame that this has come to pass.''Have you sealed the cairn-entrances?''Ilar is encamped north of the Bone Quarry.'Bingo has been given a book of recipes, and he wants to prepare a delicious meal from within its pages.Bingo has tried to translate the locations mentioned in the recipe book where you might find the ingredients for the breakfast:

Marshy taters can be found on the edge of foetid pools in the middle of the Drownholt.
Sage bushes grow at the Wild Ruin, south of Ost Galadh, in Emyn Lûm.
Mirkwood crows can be found around Emyn Lûm, and spiders can be found in the Scuttledells.
Sprigs of mint grow around the tower of Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh.Collect marshy taters in the middle of the Drownholt (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect bushels of sage at the Wild Ruin, south of Ost Galadh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect meat from crows throughout Mirkwood, especially in Emyn Lûm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect sprigs of mint from around the tower of Minas Gîl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect choice cuts of spider from the Scuttledells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo is inside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood.

You have collected the ingredients Bingo will need to prepare the breakfast he wants, and should bring them back to him.Prestadír is inside the Haunted Inn, located within the Dourstocks of Mirkwood.

Bingo has asked you to see if any of the other Rangers know where Aduiallin has gone.Bingo is inside the Haunted Inn, within the Dourstocks of Mirkwood.

Prestadír claims to have never heard of a Ranger named Aduiallin before.Adolinda is in a shadowy corner of the Haunted Inn.Talk to Adolinda in the Haunted InnBingo is in the Haunted Inn, located in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood.

You have learned that Adolinda is not a Ranger at all, but is instead a resident of Audaghaim lingering beneath a curse from long ago.Talk to Bingo in the Haunted Inn'I have been leafing through the recipe book that was given to me by Aduiallin, trying to decide upon what meal to prepare, and I think I have finally settled upon one. A tasty breakfast would be just the thing! I have been quite hungry ever since we came into this wood!

'Now, this recipe does seem to be rather exotic, but I think that will be just perfect for our stay within Mirkwood. It calls for marshy taters, a little sage, some mint for seasoning, the meat of several crows, and... choice cuts of spider? Oh my. I do not know about that, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps if the meat is prepared just right it will not be unsuitable? I am dubious, but let us see how it goes. I will try to keep an open mind. After all, if I did not wish to have new experiences, I could have stayed back in the Shire!

'The author of this book must not have liked the name Mirkwood, for the descriptions always refer to 'Greenwood the Great!' That is very quaint. It seems as if some ingredients can be found in the southern swamps, throughout the Scuttledells, by the town south of Ost Galadh, and the tower to the east of it. It is difficult to tell, because the author refers to these places with different names than those we know!''This recipe does seem to be rather exotic, but I think that will be just perfect for our stay within Mirkwood. It calls for marshy taters, a little sage, some mint for seasoning, the meat of several crows, and... choice cuts of spider? Oh my. I do not know about that, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps if the meat is prepared just right it will not be unsuitable? I am dubious, but let us see how it goes. I will try to keep an open mind. After all, if I did not wish to have new experiences, I could have stayed back in the Shire!

'The author of this book must not have liked the name Mirkwood, for the descriptions always refer to 'Greenwood the Great!' That is very quaint. It seems as if some ingredients can be found in the southern swamps, throughout the Scuttledells, by the town south of Ost Galadh, and the tower to the east of it. It is difficult to tell, because the author refers to these places with different names than those we know!''Ah, good, good! Thank you for bringing these ingredients back to me. I am very excited to prepare this breakfast, for my belly feels so empty! I have been so hungry lately!

'While you were gone, I went to look for Aduiallin to consult with her about how best to prepare this spider-meat so it will not taste vile or make us sick, but I could not find her. Could you ask one of the Rangers where I might find her? Prestadír seems to be in charge. He might know where she has gone.''While you were gone, I went to look for Aduiallin to consult with her about how best to prepare this spider-meat so it will not taste vile or make us sick, but I could not find her. Could you ask one of the Rangers where I might find her? Prestadír seems to be in charge. He might know where she has gone.''I am sorry, ${PLAYER}, for whom are you looking? Aduiallin? I do not know anyone by that name.'

You tell Prestadír that Bingo met a Ranger named Aduiallin and she gave him a book of recipes, but now she seems to have disappeared.

'I do not know what to tell you, friend. There is no Ranger by that name here, nor anywhere, unless our ranks are much larger than I realized or my memory is much worse than I believed. Perhaps both are true, but I do not think so.''I do not know what to tell you, friend. There is no Ranger by that name here, nor anywhere, unless our ranks are much larger than I realized or my memory is much worse than I believed. Perhaps both are true, but I do not think so.''Well, this is quite a puzzle! You say that Prestadír does not know of any Rangers by that name? If Aduiallin was not a Ranger, then with whom was I speaking? Who gave me this book of recipes?''Oh my! Do you see that?''I am sorry I deceived the two of you. My name is Adolinda, and I lived in Audaghaim long ago. A great evil was committed here, and I did not speak against it; for that I am cursed, never to find rest or peace.

'I arranged for your friend to find my old book of recipes, for I wanted nothing more than to pass on the activities that gave me such joy in life, when joy was possible. But I know now that it can never be, and it was the sense of family, the sense of belonging that I truly missed.

'Mirkwood was not always called such! Once it was Greenwood the Great, and the Woodmen thrived beneath its canopy. The recipes I wrote for my people made exclusive use of the herbs and creatures that dwelled within, but so many of them will never return, and those meals will never be made again. Such is the nature of my curse: all else will change, but I will not.

'Watching the two of you has been bittersweet, but it dispelled my loneliness for a time, no matter how briefly. I thank you for that kindness.''Perhaps one day the curse will be lifted, but for now each day is the same as every other.''This experience has sent shivers down my spine, ${PLAYER}! I am astounded to learn that Adolinda labours beneath a curse, and has done so for who knows how many years? I mean, this place is called the Haunted Inn, but I did not really think...'

Bingo sputters into silence.

'To be fair, the lighting in here is very dim. I think my mistake is quite understandable, and Adolinda did not go out of her way to correct me, did she? I thought her name was Aduiallin, which seems to me more likely a Ranger's name than Adolinda! I must confess that I am pleased I need not try spider-meat now. But I am still hungry... I will need something! My rumbling belly could wake the dead! Oh. That may have been in poor taste. I am terribly sorry! But it does not change the fact that I have missed a breakfast and cannot continue my adventure until I have something!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Second Breakfast' (Recommended Level: 68)</rgb>Guto has ventured on his own mission to track and hunt the Dragon-clan invaders who seem to be pressing on all sides in Trum Dreng.Guto has made camp south-east of the watch-tower in Trum Dreng.

You should seek out Guto and help him track the Dragon-clan chieftain who has stirred up so much trouble.Find Guto at his encampment'I think that you have secured the watch-tower, so perhaps now would be a good time to help Guto as well. He told me that he would be making camp not far from here -- to the south-east, I believe.

'Guto means to scout a place on the map you brought us. It would seem the Dragon-clan are amassing there, for all of their tactics seem to branch from it.

'If you find Guto, you may be able to help him thwart the violence of the Dragon-clan.''I hope that you can be of help to Guto. He would be wise not to let his rashness guide him at such times as these.''I did not expect to see you here, ${PLAYER}. I thought you only worked for my grandfather. But perhaps we can actually accomplish something now that you have come to assist me!'You brought the remnants of an ancient, rune-engraved vessel to Mair among the cairns.Naeglanc is at Echad Naeglanc, west of the cairns where Mair is posted.

Mair has asked you to speak with Naeglanc regarding the remnants of the vessel you recovered.Talk to Naeglanc at Echad NaeglancLhucu's hut sits upon a ridge west of Echad Naeglanc, between Lhan Gogledh and Lhan Bach.

Naeglanc suggested that you speak with Lhucu, daughter of Trehéarn Brenin, regarding the urn.Talk to Lhucu at her hut'I think the message upon this vessel may explain what has happened here. Perhaps in ancient days, a great evil was captured and bound to this place. Unfortunately, it would appear that the Dievlig have fallen prey to that evil.

'If you would, bring news of the message upon this urn to Naeglanc. Mayhaps, he will know better what it means.

'The Ranger is at his camp, Echad Naeglanc, to the west of here.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! Thank you for rescuing me from the thing that my father has become. I believe the Ranger may be right.

'Several moons ago, in the depths of his anger, my father must have been preyed upon by the foul spirit of this legend. It pains me to know that my father has not learned from what happened in ages past.

'My hope is that I can rally my people from his influence, and that we might depart from this place. Perhaps we may yet reclaim our clan name of old and divest ourselves of the name Dievlig.''This vessel appears to be similar in nature to one in an old story which was told by an ally of ours in the Lich Bluffs.

'It is said that a vessel of this nature was sighted many years ago in the possession of a clan brenin, who planned to betray his hosts in a most foul manner. It is said that it influenced his actions and caused the destruction of his people, for they were branded Oathbreakers. 

'I fear that the Dievlig are the descendants of these Oathbreakers and that their brenin, Trehéarn, has fallen under the same influence as his ancestor. Speak with Lhucu at her camp to the west...she is Trehéarn's daughter and may actually know more.''You should take this vessel to Naeglanc at once.''Perhaps Lhucu will know more about the vessel.'Lhucu confirmed Naeglanc's suspicions regarding the urn-shards you discovered.Nia and Parru are elders of Lhan Bach, found along the path south of Lhucu's hut.

Lhucu asked you to speak with Nia and Parru and convince them to turn away from the service of Trehéarn Brenin.Talk to Nia at Lhan BachTalk to Parru at Lhan BachLhucu is at her hut, north of Lhan Bach.

You should return to Lhucu with the answers from Nia and Parru.Talk to Lhucu at her hut in the Bonevales'In the village below, Lhan Bach, there are two influential elders that guide the people. These folk have been pressed into assisting my father and his men against their will.

'Will you speak with the elders, Nia and Parru, and see if they would be willing to put aside the fouling of our ancestors?

'Travel south along the path and you will eventually come to the gate of Lhan Bach.''I should have known that my father was doing this, but he kept his plans from me. I am glad that the elders from Lhan Bach will stand with me against the monster my father has become.''In the past, we had always served Trehéarn Brenin without fail. His rule was difficult, but just.

'However, he now views our people as cattle and presses us into service with these evil men. We cannot openly fight against his might, but would assist those who would depose him.''In the past, Trehéarn Brenin was able to rally our people to retake what was our birthright, but then the warriors abandoned us. I fear what has happened to our once-great leader.''You should speak with the Elders of Lhan Bach.'Naeglanc has sent you to uncover what is happening in Plas-maru.Defeat the wights that have arisen within the great cairn of Plas-maru.Defeat wights in Plas-maru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the wight-captainYou agreed to find and rescue the prisoners taken by the Dievlig from Echad Naeglanc.Defeat several of the sentries guarding the prisoners.Defeat Dievlig sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rescue Ilar, Mair, and Naeglanc from the Dievlig.Talk to IlarTalk to MairTalk to NaeglancFind and defeat Gerwun.Defeat Gerwun'Thank you for freeing me from those accursed betrayers!''This place was once sacred to our ancestors. These Dievlig have betrayed this place, and their people. Thank you for your assistance.''Thank you for releasing me from the Dievlig. I will speak with you again at Echad Naeglanc.''Thank you for rescuing my companions, ${PLAYER}. We are regrouping at Echad Naeglanc...follow me!'You have agreed to join this Dunlending band for a time.The Dunlending band you have joined is in the fields of Trum Dreng.Talk to the Dunlending look-outThe Dunlending band you have joined is in the fields of Trum Dreng.Follow the look-outThe Dunlending captive wishes to speak with you.Quickly speak with the captiveIt seems best to free the captive and attempt to drive off this hostile band of Dunlending outcasts.Free the captive woman from her bondsYou must defeat the band of brigands in order to save the innocent village from being raided.Defeat the band of outcastsThe woman from the Stag-clan wishes to thank you.Talk to the woman you freed'Let us leave here.''There are not many of us, but we are enough to stir up some trouble when we wish to! You will find that we value those who are strong and war-like, duvodiad or no.

'Come, I will bring you to the others.''You do not look so evil, Duvodiad. Please... if there is any good in you, free me! My village depends upon me; I am their chief huntress and protector.

'My weapons were taken from me, but I will help you fight. I beg you!''Thank you, friend. I am Elain... and you have the gratitude of myself and my village.

'Should you wish it, you may have refuge in Lhan Tarren for as long as you like. We do not normally invite strangers into our midst, but I will tell the Elder what you have done for us.'You and Guto have discovered that the White Hand is behind the recent aggression by the Dragon-clan.Guto is at his encampment.

You should speak with Guto.Hear Guto's propositionGuto is at his encampment.

You should speak with Guto.Follow GutoThe Elder is in Lhan Tarren.

You should notify Elder Riagán that Guto is arriving soon with the half-orc guest from Isengard.Notify Elder Riagán that Guto brings a guestGuto and the servant of Isengard are just behind you.

You should observe the meeting with the Elder and make sure that nothing goes awry.Make sure that the servant of Isengard keeps to his peaceful intentionsThe Elder looks like he wishes to speak with you.

You should talk to Elder Riagán.Talk to Elder Riagán'These are troubling times indeed....''If I am not mistaken, it appears that these White Hand half-orcs are behind all of the Dragon-clan's attacks on Trum Dreng, and the villainous plan to uproot the Stags once and for all.

'My grandfather might stand in the way of an open attack on these fiends, but it must be done. Will you stand with me, ${PLAYER}?''Ah, you have returned! Elain was just telling me of your many victories in our lands.'

The Elder listens with concern as you tell him quickly of what transpired between Guto and the half-orc emissary of Isengard.

'You do not trust this man, ${PLAYER}. You have had dealings with this White Hand before now, have you? And this emissary comes here to treat with me... how interesting.''${PLAYER}, I am troubled. I understand Guto's vision... to see the Stag-clan glorious and strong once again, living in our lands of old, but I will not compromise the integrity of my people for a dream that cannot be.

'That meeting with the servant of Isengard was disconcerting; I did not like the look of that man. I may have been lulled by his words, had you not expressed your immediate distrust of Isengard.

'I thank you for keeping me alert during that strange discourse.'You have accompanied Lhucu to the village of Lhan Gogledh to confront her father, Trehéarn Brenin.Talk to Lhucu.Talk to LhucuClear a path through the wights for Lhucu.Clear the path of wightsLet Lhucu know that the path has been cleared below.Talk to LhucuConfront and defeat Trehéarn Brenin.Defeat Trehéarn BreninBanish the fell spirit Mostun from the mortal world.Defeat MostunSpeak with Lhucu.Talk to LhucuLeave Lhan Gogledh as the Huntsman commanded.Withdraw through the main gate'It appears that my father has fallen completely under the sway of Mostun and has driven all of our people from the village. Look! He is protected by the abominations that walk the cairns!

'Go, ${PLAYER}, and clear a path so that I might confront my father.''It is time, then, that I confront my father and make him atone for his deeds. Thank you for all of your help, ${PLAYER}.''The Wild Huntsman is revered by all of the clans, for he rules over the gwirod. His judgement is final and exacting.

'We should leave this place immediately.'Naeglanc has sent you to uncover what is happening in the depths of Plas-maru.Seek out the main chamber of Plas-maru.Enter Plas-maru and seek out the main chamberTravel deep into Plas-maru and locate the levers that control the gate to the main chamber.Use levers to open the gate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enter the main chamber of Plas-maru and uncover the secret of the cairn.Discover what is causing the wights to stir within the BonevalesDrive back the fell spirit from Lhucu.Defeat MostunSpeak with Lhucu and escape Plas-maru.Talk to Lhucu'Untie me, Duvodiad, and I shall lead you out of this place.'The emissary of Isengard has left you with an uneasy feeling. You should track him and see if the White Hand encampment shows any signs of rallying for retribution at the Stag-clan's refusal to join them.The half-orc emissary retreated southwards towards the White Hand encampment, probably following the road.

You should follow the emissary and make sure that he does not plan to attack Lhan Tarren after being insulted by Riagán.Track the half-orc emissary to make sure he is not causing troubleIt can only be hoped that Guto and Elain are safe at least, since they were not there during the attack.

You should seek them in Lhan Tarren and try to help recover from the attack by the White Hand.Guto is in Lhan Tarren.

You should speak with Guto.Speak with Guto'Elain will find Guto and bring him back in good time, but at the moment I am more worried about that emissary who stormed back to his camp.

'Will you track him, ${PLAYER}, and warn us if you see signs of retribution for our insult? We can escape to the hills if we have warning.

'That man did not speak of war against us, and I cannot see what they could gain from it, but I am worried nonetheless.''I thought I heard the pitter-patter of nosy feet upon the road behind me. What do you want, ${PLAYER}? Are you here to make sure that I am not causing any trouble?

'Your friends in Lhan Tarren are the trouble-makers, not I, and the White Hand is swift and just to slap away its foes.

'Oh, have you not heard? You came the wrong way if you wanted to pick a fight with Isengard. The act of retribution is behind you, not ahead. Hurry home to your friends, ${PLAYER}! Ha!''Thank you for all you have done, ${PLAYER}. I see now how wrong I was to trust the words of strangers over those of my grandfather. I will endeavour to be more like him....''Thank you for all you have done, ${PLAYER}. I see now how wrong I was to trust the words of strangers over those of my grandfather. I will endeavour to be more like him....'Wights have arisen in the Bonevales, presenting a terrible threat to all who dwell in Dunland.Chain-links may be found on wights outside Plas-maru, east of Ilar's camp.

Ilar has asked you to recover chain-links from fallen wights.Collect chain-links (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ilar is at his camp, west of Plas-maru.

You should bring the chain-links that you recovered to Ilar.Talk to Ilar at his camp in the Bonevales'Among the remains of the creatures that we have dispatched, several chain-links have been recovered. These links hold the key to the travesty that has occured here.

'Will you bring me any of these links that you may find while dispatching the wights plaguing Plas-maru?''Sadly, these chains are indeed the ones that were gifted to the Dievlig. I feared that this might be so.

'I am unsure how this has been done, but we must do what we can to prevent our ancestors' bodies from being befouled further.''Bring me any chain links that you find upon the wights.'While the clan's chief huntress was missing, the meat for the Feast of the Running Stag was perilously neglected. A productive hunt would rectify this situation.Boar and oxen roam the rough plains around Trum Dreng.

You have been asked to hunt the beasts of Trum Dreng for the Feast of the Running Stag that takes place tonight.Hunt game beasts of Trum Dreng (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hav can be found in Lhan Tarren, the Stag-clan's village in Trum Dreng.

You should bring the meat you collected to Hav at once so that she can begin roasting it for the feast.'Welcome to Lhan Tarren! The Elder has sent word that you will be joining us for the feast tonight. Many hungry people will be there, along with Stag-clansmen from other parts of Trum Dreng.

'It is my duty to prepare the meat, but since our clan's huntress was taken captive, the men have been hard-pressed to find food. Our tribe is not what it once was....

'But do not worry yourself; you look to be a sturdy ${RACE}. Will you participate in the hunt, ${PLAYER}? We wish to feast on boar and oxen tonight.''If you are to hunt the boar and oxen of the plains, you can find them roaming throughout Trum Dreng, not far from our village.

'Very few people in our village are able to hunt these days....''Oh! So much? This is more than enough, ${PLAYER}. And it did not take you an expedition of many days to bring it back.

'The Elder says that you are to be treated as family while you pass through our village, but we have need of a stout provider like yourself....'Haul informed you that the Ranger Naeglanc and the rest of his companions were either captured or killed when the Dievlig attacked their camp.Haul is at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales.

You should speak with Haul when you are ready to track down the Dievlig who captured his companions.Rescue the prisoners from the DievligSpeak to Haul in Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales.

With several of the prisoners free, you may begin investigating what is happening within the Bonevales.Speak to Haul'Several of my companions were taken from this place following the attack. I was able to fight off the last of the Dievlig, but I need help to rescue my captive friends.

'Will you help me? If so, let me know when you are ready to leave.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'With our allies now freed, we can begin to investigate what is happening here.''I have discovered the Dievlig's trail...they have not gone too far, I think. I believe you will find them on the ridge to the north.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Recently, there have been rumours of strange occurrences in the Bonevales, which have brought Bledhun into the ancient burial grounds.Signs of the strange happenings might be found in the Bonevales, west of Bledhun.

Bledhun has asked you to seek out and discover any signs of the strange happenings in the Bonevales.Examine disturbed piles of earth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Examine remainsCaron awaits you to the north-west of the area you searched.

You should seek out Caron, as Bledhun instructed, and discuss what you have found.Talk to Caron in the Bonevales'You are a duvodiad here... you do not belong here any more than I do. Among the vales and cairns of the Bonevales, a clan has long dwelled. This clan called the Dievlig -- Accursed in the Westron -- are Oathbreakers and were driven into the Bonevales as punishment.

'Recently, strange occurrences and evil rumblings have been heard from the cairns that have long laid dormant. Will you search for signs that might explain what is happening here?

'Journey west from here and see what you can find. When you have found the signs I seek, you should find my friend, Caron, and deliver the evidence to him. I last saw him heading west through the valley.''Look for signs of the mysterious happenings to the west.''You should speak with Caron.''Ah, it appears, ${PLAYER}, that we have another duvodiad in our lands. In these troubled times, sadly, outsiders seem to be the people who are the most willing to give aid.

'If you must know, it appears as if the honoured dead are being twisted and are now stirring from their cairns.'The farm on the herd-lands is useless to the Stag-clan now; its farmers were slaughtered, and the Dragon-clan desires it. If it is destroyed, however, the Dragon-clan will not wish to remain here.The store-houses can be found in the huts and towers throughout the herd-lands, not far from Blodwen's hiding spot. Flaming brands used by the Dragon-clan to conquer the farm are likely near the huts.

You should burn down the seed store-houses so that they cannot continue to supply the Dragon-clan.Blodwen still lingers in her hiding place, waiting for death to reunite her with her new family.

You should tell Blodwen that you have destroyed what was left of the farm.Return to Blodwen in the herd-lands'This farm is nothing to the Stag-clan now -- it only serves to keep the Draig-lûth too close to Lhan Tarren and the wilds of Trum Dreng while they feel the need to occupy it.

'It would be better if the whole place was burned to the ground, and me with it. Without hope, there is no future here. Not for me, and not for them.'

There is some sense to what Blodwen says. It would likely be for the best if the farm was burned to the ground. The Dragon-clan would have no choice but to leave.'If you wish to rid this place of the Dragon-clan invaders, you should destroy the store-houses.''I saw the flames and smoke from here, ${PLAYER}. You did well.

'It grieves me to know that the herd-lands are destroyed beyond repair, but at least the Dragon-clan will want nothing more with this land. They will not settle here. They wanted our food-stores... now they have nothing.'You have passed very recently into the land of Dunland.You should speak with the look-out in the northern pass of Trum Dreng.Talk to the look-out to join the Dunlendings of Trum DrengLhan Tarren, the village of Elain of the Stag-clan, lies to the south of where you found her.

You have been urged to seek the hospitality of the humble Caru-lûth clansmen while you pass through Trum Dreng.Find the village of Lhan TarrenElain made it safely back to her village, Lhan Tarren.

You should speak with Elain briefly before presenting yourself to the Elder of the Stag-clan in Trum Dreng.Find Elain inside the villageThe Elder of Lhan Tarren is inside the bounds of the village.

You should speak with the Elder, for he wishes to thank you for your kindness to Elain.Talk to the Elder of the Stag-clan'Hail, Duvodiad. Will you stay a moment? We have need of a strong warrior like yourself in our little band.

'We can find work for you and reward as well, for there is much to be done, and even more to be gained....'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'You are willing to join us, then? Good, consider it done. You are one of our small clan now. We are not so different; we all want the same things: wealth, power. Run with us, and you shall have both! Of this, we have been assured.''Hold, Duvodiad. Let me have a look at you.

'Ah, you are the kind ${CLASS} of whom Elain spoke! We have been expecting you. You have our gratitude and our hospitality.

'We do not make a habit of welcoming outsiders into our midst, but exceptions are to be made for a hero. Come... there are many who wish to thank you, and most of all the Elder. He can be found within.''I knew you would come, ${PLAYER}! I hope Cadelh did not give you any trouble on the bridge -- my people are suspicious of duvodiad, but I told them about how you rescued me from the outcasts.

'The Elder wishes to speak with you, my friend. He means to give you a proper welcome.''Ah! You must be ${PLAYER}! Come, come. Make yourself at home. I like the look of you, ${PLAYER}! A good, strong, sturdy ${RACE} -- that is what I like in a warrior.

'You have done us a great service by rescuing our headstrong little huntress. Elain is a brash girl... but we would be helpless without her!'You had an idea to collect weapons for the destitute band of outcasts hiding on the far side of the river.Daggers, bows, spears, and shields can be found on the various Dunlending-scouts who roam the northern fields of the Herd-lands in Trum Dreng.

You should defeat the Dragon-clan invaders and collect their weapons to give to the small band of trapped Dunlendings.Collect daggers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect spears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect shields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect bows and arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ceri can be found on the overlook to the north of the Herd-lands.

You should bring the weapons you gathered to the small group of hiding Dunlendings, which will help them be better prepared for the troubles they will face upon their escape.As with most evil Men, the Dunlending raider you killed bore a cruel weapon -- in this case, a dagger.

It would actually benefit the small clan of destitute outcasts to have weapons such as these. You should collect more and give them to the friendlier Dunlendings.'You gathered these weapons for us? That was a generous gesture....

'We have some hope of getting out of here alive now, thanks to this. You are very kind, ${PLAYER}. I did not expect a Duvodiad to help us.'Heartened by the potential allegiance of the elders from Lhan Bach, Lhucu proposes a plan to liberate the village.Dievlig overseers and warriors can be found in Lhan Bach, south of Lhucu's hut.

Lhucu has asked you to return to Lhan Bach and rid the village of her father's men.Defeat Dievlig at Lhan Bach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Dievlig Overseer at Lhan BachLhucu is at her hut, north of Lhan Bach. 

You should return to Lhucu and let her know that the town is free of the tyranny of her father and his men.Talk to Lhucu at her hut'My father has sent many of his brutal men to Lhan Bach to quell any murmurs of rebellion. These men are the worst of our people, and their support of my father's actions must not go unpunished. 

'Will you help to put an end to the tyranny of my father's men in Lhan Bach? If so, return to the village and dispatch the overseers and their warriors.''With the overseers deposed from the village below, we have sent a clear message to my father's forces: their tyranny shall not be tolerated!''Have you dealt with my father's minions?'The resting places of the honoured dead in the Bonevales have been defiled in some manner, causing the Dead to rise.The cairn-entrances lie to the south and west of Bledhun's camp.

Bledhun has asked you to examine the entrances of the cairns to see if you can discern what power is behind the raising of the wights.Examine cairn-entrances (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bledhun awaits your return at his camp to the east and north of the cairn-entrances.

You should return to Bledhun and let him know what you found.Talk to Bledhun at his encampment in the Bonevales'Among the cairns to the south-west, the bodies of those that have long lain in eternal rest have begun to stir and rise up from their graves. I would know what evil causes this to happen.

'Perhaps if you examined the cairn-entrances, you might find some evidence of the power behind this abomination. Will you do this for me?

'Journey south and then west through the valley. There, you should find the cairns.''When the wights first emerged from their graves, I had hoped someone had simply crept into their cairns and removed their bodies.

'However, it appears as if these cairns were disturbed from the inside. I fear what this might mean for the interred.''Have you examined the entrances to the cairns yet?'You have travelled to Lhan Gogledh with Lhucu to confront her father.Defeat the wights that protect Trehéarn Brenin in Lhan Gogledh.Defeat wights in Lhan Gogledh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Guto is eager to drive the half-orc and Dragon-clan trespassers from Trum Dreng once and for all.Guto is at his encampment, south of the watch-tower.

You should talk to Guto again when you are ready to begin your assault.Go with Guto to resolve the dispute in Trum Dreng'You have softened them up, and now they are ready to be defeated. Let us drive these trespassers from Trum Dreng once and for all. This feeble army will think twice before troubling the Stag-clan again!

'What do you say to that?'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'So, you will do it? You are ready to fight off these foes? Our blood may spill, but it will be Dragon-clan that burns and White Hands that are severed!

'Follow me, my friend!'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Lhucu is determined to confront her father and make him atone for the evils that he has committed.Lhucu is at her hut in the Bonevales.

You should speak with Lhucu when you are ready to depart for Lhan Gogledh.Confront Trehéarn BreninLhucu is at her hut, south of Lhan Gogledh.

You should speak with Lhucu regarding the unfortunate encounter with Trehéarn Brenin and the fell spirit Mostun.Talk to Lhucu at her hut'The time has come for me to confront my father and make him atone for the evils that he has committed. Our people have suffered and our lives may well be forfeit because of his actions.

'Will you travel with me to Lhan Gogledh? It shall be dangerous, but it is a danger I am willing to face.... Are you?

'If you wish to accompany me, speak to me when you are ready to leave.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready to confront my father?'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'I wish my father could have understood what was happening to him and what he had become. At least the creature that preyed upon him will never again return to this place.

'I hope there will come a time that I might lead my people away from this place, for we have paid far too great a price.'Corrupted by a fell power, the interred bodies of the Dunlending ancestors have begun to rise from their resting places.Wights can be found in the valley south and west from Bledhun's camp.

Bledhun asked you to enter the Bonevales and defeat the wights that have arisen from the cairns.Defeat wights in the Bonevales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bledhun awaits you at his camp, north and east of the wight-infested valley.

You should return to Bledhun with news of your victory.Speak to Bledhun'Within the past moon, our ancestors have begun to rise from their resting places here in the Bonevales. These once-great heroes' bodies have been twisted and corrupted and attack those who still draw breath.

'If you journey south and west into the valley, you will come across these terrible wights. Defeat them, if you would, for such an abomination should not be permitted to continue.''Unlike the Lich Bluffs to the north, this place has always remained undisturbed, until now. We must discover what has caused the wights to walk among us.'Before his capture, the Ranger Naeglanc received scattered reports about wights rising from the cairns of the Bonevales.Wights may be found in the Bone Quarry, east of Echad Naeglanc.

Naeglanc has asked you to defeat the wights that have risen in the Bone Quarry.Defeat wights in the Bone Quarry (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ilar is at his camp, north of the Bone Quarry and east within the valley.

Naeglanc asked you to speak with Ilar after dealing with the wights in the Bone Quarry.Talk to Ilar at his camp in the Bonevales'Before our encampment was attacked, several of our allies were investigating the rise of the Dead in the Bone Quarry to the east. According to their reports, unlike in the Lich Bluffs, the Dunlending ancestors that were lain to rest here have never stirred until now.

'In respect to my Dunlending friends, will you seek out the wights of the Bonevales and lay them to rest? When you have done this, seek out Ilar at his encampment at the north end of the Bone Quarry.''The plight of the Bonevales saddens my heart. The bodies of those that have passed on should not be fouled in this manner. I weep for those who have fallen.''Have you dealt with the wights yet?''Ilar is encamped north of the Bone Quarry.'When Bledhun's band was attacked, sigils were stripped from the corpses of the fallen and distributed to the Dievligs as a reward.The hill where Bledhun's party was once encamped lies to the south of Bledhun's current camp.

Bledhun asked you to hunt down any Dievlig and recover the sigils stolen from the corpses of his companions.Collect sigils (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bledhun is at his camp, north of the hill where his party once encamped.

You should bring the sigils that you recovered to Bledhun.Talk to Bledhun at his encampment in the Bonevales'${PLAYER}, my companions each carried a sigil to signify our allegiance to our clan. When my companions fell to the attack, many of these sigils were taken.

'Will you attempt to recover the sigils from the dunlendings atop the hill? If so, journey south and up the hill. The scouts will be the ones carrying the sigils.''You have done me a great service, Duvodiad. The cowards will not sully the memory of those who stood beside me in honour.''Have you collected my companions' sigils yet?'Naeglanc and his allies continue to battle the foul wights arising within the Bonevales.Undisturbed cairns lie to the east of Echad Naeglanc, along the southern ridge.

Naeglanc has asked you to scatter ashes before undisturbed cairns in the Bonevales.Scatter ashes before undisturbed cairns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Seek out an ally among the cairns to the far eastern reaches of the Bonevales.

You should speak with MairTalk to Mair among the cairns'I have spoken with my Dunlending allies, and they seem to have a belief that spreading ashes before the cairns of the dead will prevent the wights from escaping their tombs, though I have many doubts of the veracity of this claim.

'Nevertheless, I have promised that this task will be performed before I leave this place. Will you help me?

'Travel due east from camp, along the southern fork. There you will find the cairns before which you should spread these ashes. When you have done this, find Mair among the cairns.''The ashes you spread should prevent more of these abominations emerging from the cairns. Thank you, Duvodiad.''Have you scattered the ashes yet?''You may find an ally among the cairns.'Several Dunlendings have been assisting members of the Grey Company as they search for a safe and secret path through Dunland. Recently, their camp was attacked, and they have hidden themselves in the valley.Caron's companions can be found east of his position, possibly near Bledhun's camp.

Caron has asked you to seek out his companions and help them.Find and talk to EilunedFind and talk to GlundurBledhun is encamped east and slightly north of Caron's companions.

Caron asked you to let Bledhun know that the few survivors of Caron's band are safe.Talk to Bledhun at his encampment in the Bonevales'Recently, a large army was gathered within the Bonevales, poised to attack the Algraig clans of Enedwaith. However, Yorath, a great Brenin among the clans, summoned the warriors south to Wulf's Cleft to ready an attack against the accursed strawheads.

'Following the withdrawal of the forces, Trehéarn, Brenin of the Dievlig, began attacking all those who would assist outsiders like yourself. My band was scattered throughout the valley.

'Will you seek out those who survived the attack and assist them if possible? Travel east and look among the rocks and hills for my companions. When you have found them, return to Bledhun and let him know we are safe.''I am glad to hear that some of our band survived the Dievlig's brutal attack. I swear that the treachery of the Dievlig shall not go unpunished.''Caron sent you? Then we shall speak.

'We had a peaceful arrangement with the Dievlig at one time. We would bring them goods, and they would allow us to pass unimpeded northwards. Ever since the warriors marched to Wulf's Cleft, the Dievlig have become increasingly hostile to those they saw as duvodiad -- outsiders.  

'They attacked our band, and we were taken unaware...only a small number of us survived.''Caron sent you to find me?

'I do not understand what has happened. Will you please let any of my companions you come across know that I escaped the Dievlig's attack unscathed?

'Thank you, Duvodiad.''Please, find my friends, ${PLAYER}.''Since you have found my friends, go speak with Bledhun.'Guto has asked you to spoil the food-stores at the White Hand encampment, hoping that this will serve to weaken the enemy.Food-stores can be found within the White Hand encampment in Trum Dreng.

You should break into the encampment and spoil all the food-stores you find there.Spoil White Hand food-stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Guto is at his small encampment in the southern fields of Trum Dreng.

You should return to Guto with news of your success.Return to Guto at his encampment'We are sorely outnumbered, so we must not attack now. But I have an idea: you should spoil their food-stores, which will make them sick. Sick enemies are not very good at fighting.

'You should hasten to the encampment and find a way to spoil the stores of food within. They will eat, and they will weaken, and we will drive them out of Trum Dreng. It is a perfect plan!''Ha! I relish the thought of humiliating sick half-orcs and the Dragon-clan. Let us prepare to leave soon to fight them. This will be quite the adventure.''Every encampment has some supply of food, my friend. All you need to do is find it, then find a way to spoil it. Perhaps cut it open to let the rats and mice and maggots have at it. Or get it wet.

'It does not matter, at long as they eat foul food by evening.'Many innocent townsfolk have been slain, and they deserve to be properly buried.The villagers can be found around the town of Lhan Tarren.

You did not know many of these people personally, but they should be laid to rest below the earth all the same.Also among the dead in Lhan Tarren are Elder Riagán and Blodwen, two people that you considered friends in Trum Dreng.

You should lay the Elder and Blodwen to rest.Bury Elder Riagán's bodyBury Blodwen's bodyGuto is grieving at the head of Lhan Tarren.

You should speak with Guto and offer him your deepest sympathies.Return to Guto'So many dead, ${PLAYER}, all because we were not here for the one moment when they needed us most. Would that I was one of them! My poor, poor grandfather.

'Please, bury them. Lay them to rest. I do not want their cold, staring eyes to look upon our home in ruin, and their kinsmen dead and dying and missing all around them.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. This... this was a terrible thing that happened. We must move forward... and I hope we can have revenge as we take our next steps!

'A thousand curses on Isengard!'Plas-maru appears to be a focus for the evil spreading across the Bonevales.Naeglanc is at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales.

You should speak with Naeglanc when you are ready to leave for Plas-maru.Investigate Plas-maruSpeak to Naeglanc in Echad Naeglanc.Speak to Naeglanc in Echad Naeglanc'Before our imprisonment, we had heard rumours that the Brenin of the Dievlig, Trehéarn, has begun to fall to dark influences. His daughter, Lhucu, fearing the decisions that he was making, sought assistance from us.

'Recently, she has become missing, and we fear the worst. One of our scouts saw her being brought to Plas-maru... which most certainly bodes ill for her. Will you enter that terrible place and find her?

'Speak with me when you are ready to leave.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Very well, ${PLAYER}. May the Valar light your way in that dark place.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Lhucu has been one of our allies since we made our way into Bonevales. Her release bodes well for our chances of escaping the Bonevales.

'However, her father's fall into darkness and the foul creature whose machinations were the cause of it may lead these poor people to unending torment.'You recovered this sword from the corpse of a wight. It bears the sigil of the Dievlig.Bledhun is at his encampment in the north-east part of the Bonevales.

Bledhun will wish to see this sword.Talk to Bledhun at his camp in the BonevalesThis sword bears a striking similarity to those that the Dievlig wield.

You should bring it at once to Bledhun at his encampment.'I fear this bodes ill for us, Duvodiad. It appears as if there are some among the Dievlig who have been complicit in raising the wights from their graves.

'We should warn our allies among the cairns about this foul betrayal.'Looters have descended upon the Herd-lands to make off with Trev's goods. Since these Men are usually more peaceable than the Dragon-clan raiders, they might be willing to give you information with a little persuasion.Looters can be found stealing stores throughout the Herd-lands.

You should attempt to question looters on the farm, for they are generally more neutral than the Dragon-clan raiders.Question the first looterQuestion the second looterQuestion the third looterQuestion the fourth looterQuestion the fifth looterBlodwen can be found hiding among the rocks at the southern end of the Herd-lands.

You should bring the map you uncovered to Blodwen before you hurry back to Lhan Tarren.Return to Blodwen with the information'Looters came after the warriors to pluck valuables from the carnage left behind by the Dragon-clan. They will do the same wherever the raiders strike next.

'These greedy men are not warriors themselves. They do not have it in them to fight and kill. Do what you will with them; I care not.

'Men such as these might be able to give you information, since you are intent upon saving us all.''Those looters will have more information than I -- they are close to the Dragon-clan, but not of them.''I will not be telling you anything. I am doing just fine with this lot, thank you.''A duvodiad trying to question me? You are a brave one....''Begone with you, duvodiad!''Question me, will you? We will see about that!''You will get no song from this bird, duvodiad!''I cannot believe this! Why would the Dragon-clan invade Trum Dreng? This land is all but barren. It is wild, and the few Stags that remain have no wish to join the wars of other Men.

'Lhan Tarren must be warned of what is coming... but what can they do if they do not know how, when, or where the Dragon-clan will attack them next?'Elain awaits you at the watch-tower in the centre of Trum Dreng, long held by the Stag-clan. The watch-tower has likely been captured by the Dragon-clan invaders.Elain awaits you at the watch-tower in Trum Dreng, on a hill to the east of Lhan Tarren.

You should join Elain at the watch-tower and see what can be done about the Dragon-clan invaders there.Find Elain at the watch-tower'The watch-tower is evidently the first place the next wave of invaders means to take over. Elain will join you there to help secure our lands. If we can frighten away the Draig-lûth, I believe that we will remain safe from them for at least a generation.

'Guto would have us wage a war of revenge that lasts a hundred years. I would give anything to teach him the error of judgement before I die. Wars are crueller than anything in this world.

'Elain has more wisdom than Guto and is a strong warrior, but even strong warriors can be hurt. I beg you to keep her safe, ${PLAYER}... and keep yourself safe as well!''Elain is a good girl, but I worry for her so. She is strong for her size and wise for her age, but even those who are blessed with such gifts can come into harm's way. Please, ${PLAYER}, keep her safe.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! We are like old friends now. I am glad that you have joined me, for it seems the Dragon-clan have arrived before us.

'I fought many Draig-lûth off the path, but I dare not go nearer to the watch-tower. They will surely see us if we venture into the stone circle, and our hides will be sprinkled with a rain of arrows from the sky.'The half-orcs of Isengard now trespass on the land they attempted to conquer. Trum Dreng will not be safe until these violent conquerors are removed once and for all.The half-orc servants of the White Hand can be found in the encampment in southern Trum Dreng.

You should travel to the encampment and defeat the slavers and murderers who have rallied there.Defeat half-orcs at the White Hand encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Guto now stands in his grandfather's place in Lhan Tarren.

You should bring news to Chief Guto that the half-orc trespassers have been driven out of Trum Dreng.Return to Chief Guto at Lhan Tarren'Curse the wicked servants of the White Hand! My poor grandfather... my poor people!

'I must stay here and protect what is left of my people, but ${PLAYER}... the servants of the White Hand cannot be allowed to remain in this land. Will you drive them out of Trum Dreng?''Curse the wicked servants of the White Hand! My poor grandfather... my poor people!

'I must stay here and protect what is left of my people, but ${PLAYER}... the servants of the White Hand cannot be allowed to remain in this land. Will you drive them out of Trum Dreng?''The half-orcs are a menace to Dunland as long as they live, hissing the cruel assurances of Saruman's neighbourly kindness in the ears of the clans.

'You did well to drive them out, ${PLAYER}. The Dragon-clan maimed us, but I believe Isengard is the greatest enemy we have faced yet....'Several of the younger men of Lhan Tarren were taken during the raid on the village. They are surely being kept at the half-orc encampment in Trum Dreng.The White Hand encampment is in the south-eastern part of Trum Dreng, and this is where the half-orc soldiers retreated with the kidnapped men of Lhan Tarren.

