'I watched the Dragon-clan invaders set traps for the poor beasts. If you have any kindness in you, you will disable the traps to ensure that the cattle are not cruelly harmed upon their return.''That was a kindly done deed, ${PLAYER}. But do not waste any further time on me; you should leave before the Dragon-clan finds you and kills you, like they did my husband, his father, and gentle Celun.''The traps are on the west side of the river, where the cattle roamed before the Dragon-clan attacked us.'While you are attempting to set the farm to rights, Blodwen anticipates that you will encounter many Dragon-clan as you roam.Dragon-clan invaders can be found all over the Herd-lands.

You should defeat the Dragon-clan invaders as you wander throughout the farmlands.Defeat Dragon-clan invaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Blodwen can be found hiding among the rocks at the far southern edge of the Herd-lands in Trum Dreng.

You should return to Blodwen and see if she has any more need of your assistance.Return to Blodwen in the Herd-lands'You will encounter many Dragon-clan while you roam the fields here. You would do well to thin their numbers, though I doubt we can be certain of their being truly gone from this area for a number of days yet.

'The Dragon-clansmen are many, but their numbers cannot be endless. You should be merciless when these evil Men attack you, ${PLAYER}.

'They do not know mercy themselves. They showed none to my poor husband and his kin.''I wish you would not venture out again, but if you must, you must.''You slew a good number of them, ${PLAYER}. For that, I am grateful. Your thirst for vengeance against the evils in this world is greater than my own.

'You should return to Lhan Tarren; the fires of a village are warmer than the words of a lone widow in the wilds. Aye, ${CLASS}, you have done enough!'You discovered the remnants of an ancient rune-covered vessel among the cairns.Mair is posted among the cairns in the Bonevales.

