Perhaps you should deliver these remnants to Mair among the cairns.'These pieces appear to be from an ancient urn of my people. These remnants speak of a place to capture a darkness that whispers to others.

'I wonder what that means?'You helped some travellers who witnessed the sacking of the herd-lands, but it is now time to seek the farmer and his family. They have not been seen since the Dragon-clan came.The farmer's family should be somewhere in the herd-lands.

Whether dead or alive, you should find Trev's family before reporting back to Lhan Tarren.Search for the Celun, the farmhandSearch for Trev, the chief herdsmanThe farmer's son should also be somewhere in the herd-lands in Trum Dreng.

There is only one Stag-clansman left to find, and he is not with the others: the herdsman's son Dilwun.Search for the farmer's son Dilwun'I might have heard someone from the herdsman's family the night the Dragon-clan came. I heard a terrible scream, but there was naught that we could do without weapons.

'There was no light at all. No light... only screams. The screaming went on, then was silent. Whatever happened to that poor family, it was nothing good.

'It is good of you to want to look for them, but are you certain it is worth the risk? It is folly to seek the dead while their killers lurk nearby.''I hope you do not meet an untimely end with your good intentions, ${PLAYER}. It would be a tragedy for a good soul like yourself to die needlessly while seeking the dead.'This man probably worked for the farmer, but he lies face-down in the water. It is obvious that he has not drawn breath for too long now....This is undoubtedly Trev, the chief herdsman in these lands.

Trev appears to have been murdered during the invasion. His face and body are contorted as if he died in considerable pain; perhaps his were the screams heard on the night of the raid.You have discovered the last member of Trev's family, and he too is dead... murdered and left at the river-bank to be carried away when the rains come.

The Elder will be sorely grieved by this news. The Stag-clan has now grown smaller and more vulnerable.Since the craban from the farm on the herd-lands returned injured and without the presence of its recipient, the people of Lhan Tarren have been worried about the herdsman Trev and his family.Elder Riagán is in Lhan Tarren.

You should tell the troubled Elder that you volunteer your own strength and skill for the task of finding out what might be wrong in the south.Tell the Elder that you volunteer yourself to investigate his missing clansmenThe herd-lands can be found by following the road south from Lhan Tarren.

You should travel down the road in search of what may have intercepted the crow.Take the road south towards the herd-lands'This is dreadful, ${PLAYER}... you saw the crow with your own eyes. I know something terrible has happened where Trev and his folk live in the herd-lands.

'Trev, his farmhand Celun, and his son Dilwun have been helping to feed our folk from the wealth of the herd-lands for a long time.

'We must investigate. I worry that Elain's safety must be compromised again, or Guto's. I do not like throwing my only warrior into danger, or my only grandson. Alas! What am I to do?''You offer to go in Elain's stead, ${PLAYER}? Is there no end to your bravery and generosity? You, a duvodiad to us, would put yourself in danger to find a missing man you have never met?

'It does not seem possible. I do not know how we can ever repay you, good ${PLAYER}!''I am so worried, ${PLAYER}. I do not know how to protect my people with what little strength we have left.''Are you certain that you want me to remain here? I am accustomed to danger, ${PLAYER}. But... I suppose the Elder wants me near in times such as these.

'I wish more than anything that my people were more like you so that I could fulfill my duties....''Do you mean to hurt us, Duvodiad? You and many others, I am sure. Well, get it over with.

