You should use the weaver's loom to weave the feathers into an iridescent cloak.Rook is at his hut in Pren Gwydh.

You should bring the iridescent, many-hued cloak you crafted to Rook, who wishes to be as great a Wizard as Saruman.'I am well on my way to being as great as Saruman, ${PLAYER}, but there is something more I would ask of you. As I observed my master of old, I saw that his robes appeared white, but shimmered with many subtle hues.

'I am quite certain that the subtle colours help to infuse the power that the lord of Isengard possesses. I need an iridescent cloak! With such a garment, I too shall be powerful beyond belief!

'I do not care how you find it, but I want a many-hued cloak.''Have you brought me a many-coloured cloak yet? My garb will not be complete without it.''Ah! Look how it glistens! Now black... now green... now violet. Incredible, ${PLAYER}. It looks like the plumage on my dear craban-friends.

