You should collect ore deposits for the smithing of the ring Rook desires.Mine for ore at towering rocks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There is a small forge at Rook's Hut in Pren Gwydh.

You should return to the hut with the ore you collected and craft a sufficient ring.Forge a ring that will satisfy RookRook is at his hut in Pren Gwydh, waiting for a Ring of Power to be brought to him.

You should bring Rook the ring you forged from local metal veins and see if it will suffice for his needs.'What qualifies me to be an apprentice Wizard, you ask? I studied long under Saruman the White as his servant and caregiver to his flocks of crebain. I watched him closely, then stole away one night to pursue my own lofty dreams!

'And now here I am, a Wizard in the making. I shall soon be the great Wizard of Dunland! But first, I need a Ring of Power. 

'I learned much in Isengard about the Great Rings, and I must have one of my own if I am to be respectable in this profession.''Have you found a Ring of Power? No? You are not searching hard enough. I would like to have one by nightfall, but it is my understanding that they are very difficult to come by. It may take you all day!''A Great Ring! I can feel the power surging from it. It is a wonder you did not keep it for yourself -- but ah, you are wise. You know that you are too weak-minded to bear such a heavy burden.

'Yes, it is best to leave such things to the great Men, like myself. How did you come by this, ${PLAYER}? Does it not look marvellous upon my finger?'The other labourers of Galtrev seem to have borrowed many nails from Rhianu, and now she does not have enough to complete work on the siege-engine.Nails have been borrowed from Rhianu by the various peoples of Galtrev and can likely be found around the village.

You should collect the missing nails and return them to Rhianu so that her work on the siege-engine can be finished.Collect missing nails (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhianu can be found at the fourth worksite in Galtrev.

You should bring her the nails you collected so that she can finish her day's work.'This is what happens when you are too generous with people. They borrow all of your nails and never bring any back! I am out of nails, and the work on this siege-engine shall never be finished.

'Would you be able to go find my missing nails for me? I need to finish assembling this, or else I will not receive any rations today. I did not receive rations yesterday either, and tomorrow I will likely not be able to get out of bed.''Everyone needs nails, so they come here to "borrow" them frequently. Unfortunately, they never seem to bring any back....''My nails! So many... I did not even know this many had gone missing. This was surely but a small task for an adventurer like yourself, but you have helped me greatly, ${PLAYER}.'An absurd number of spears must be made before the day's end, but Wunne only has two hands. There is no way she can finish the task on her own.Bowstaves are scattered about the worksite.

Wunne has asked you to help craft spears. You should collect many bowstaves. Once you collect them, they can be used from your inventory to craft spears.Craft the staves you collect into spears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wunne can be found at the fourth worksite in Galtrev.

You should bring the spears you made to Wunne so that she can deliver them to Flint Ironheart.'So many staves, so many staves! All of these staves you see must be turned into spears... in fact, they should have been turned into spears hours ago!

'I do not know what to do. Do you know how to craft spears, duvodiad? I would certainly appreciate the help. I worry about what the Overseer will do to me if I fail....''If I do not finish, I shudder to think what they will do to me....''I cannot believe it, ${PLAYER}! You have put me ahead for today's workload. Thank you -- I cannot express the trouble I would have been in had this supply of spears not been delivered to the overseer.'Some goblins of Isengard have been using a remote corner of Pren Gwydh to raise Wargs for steeds and are careless about keeping the dangerous beasts contained to their pens.Warg-pens can be found in the Howling Caverns.

You should burn the pens while fighting your way through the camp to ensure that the goblins leave and do not think to return.Burn Warg-pens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Goronu can be found outside of the Howling Caverns.

You should tell Goronu that you have burned many Warg-pens to dissuade the goblins from rebuilding here.Talk to Goronu'I am not certain what the best course of action is here, ${PLAYER}. I am but a simple scout, not a Warg-slayer or goblin-butcher!

'If I were younger, perhaps I would make some effort to burn the Warg-pens within that horrifying camp. If you burn their pens while you kill Wargs and drive out goblins, perhaps they will not come back.

'It is unfortunate that I am not younger.''May the Gwirod be with you, ${PLAYER}... I fear you will need their guidance.''Ah, you are very brave! I was certain you would die within, and that I would have to find another solution to this problem. I am glad that such a measure was not necessary, ${PLAYER}.'You have helped the driver, but he risks an uncertain future if he returns to Galtrev as late as he is.Galtrev is not far. The wood that you have brought to Fraid at the Galtrev Lumber-camp can surely be carried the rest of the way.

You should carry the wood shipment to Galtrev.Deliver the wood to Urien to complete the shipmentUrien is in Galtrev.

You should speak with Urien now that you have delivered the wood successfully.Talk to Urien in Galtrev'Here is another difficulty. I cannot return to Galtrev now. I believe the White Hand Overseers will beat me for my lateness... or worse. They executed my neighbour for losing an important crate bound for Isengard.

'I wish to escape, ${PLAYER}, but if the wood does not arrive, they will make an example of someone else. Will you deliver it?''He escaped? Good... that is good. They wanted to kill him for his lateness. But it is the Dragon-clan that they should punish! Why do they not defend us when our warriors are gone?'The people of Trum Dreng need your help if they are to stand against the clans siding with Saruman.There are many things you can do in Trum Dreng to aid the Stag-clan and gain their favour. Once you have satisfied their needs, Braigiar would like you to meet up with Halbarad outside the village of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh.Help the people of Trum Dreng as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Halbarad in Pren Gwydh'The Stag-clan is not as powerful as it once was, and now its people are being marginalized. If we can gain their favour, it could be that they will resist the call of Saruman.

'Stay here and help the people of Trum Dreng, ${PLAYER}. Once you are satisfied that you have done all you can to earn their respect and favour, continue south-east into the lands of Pren Gwydh. There you will find a large village called Galtrev. Just outside this village we can meet up with Halbarad and see what must be done next as we pass through Dunland.''The passage through Trum Dreng went smoothly? Good. It is the same for the group that braved the Bonevales. Now we must see what awaits us here in Pren Gwydh.''There are a great many things that you can do in Trum Dreng to earn the favour of its people, ${PLAYER}. You should do everything you can here before travelling to Pren Gwydh and meeting Halbarad outside Galtrev.'The people of the Bonevales need your help if they are to survive in this harsh land, haunted by the wights and warriors loyal to Saruman.There are many things that you can do in the Bonevales to aid its people and gain their favour. Once you have satisfied their needs, Prestadír would like you to travel south into Pren Gwydh to meet up with Halbarad.Help the people of the Bonevales as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Halbarad in Pren Gwydh'The people of the Bonevales are in need of our help, ${PLAYER}. You should continue to give them your support in any way you can, for we will need allies if we are to make it through Dunland.

'There are mysteries a-plenty in the Bonevales. If we can get to the bottom of them, we may have earned allies without which our passage south could be difficult.

'Once you are satisfied that you have done what you can for the people of the Bonevales, travel south-west to the village of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh. There you will find Halbarad, and we can decide what should be done next.''The passage of the Bonevales went smoothly? Good. It is the same for the group that braved Trum Dreng, and they were able to provide some help to the people there. Now we must see what awaits us here in Pren Gwydh.''We need to help the people of the Bonevales, if we can. Once you are satisfied that you have done as much as you can for them, you should travel south-west to the village of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh. Halbarad will be waiting there for you.'The village of Galtrev is a village divided. Does it pose a danger to the Grey Company?Halbarad wants you to talk to the residents of Galtrev in order to learn of the situation in Pren Gwydh.Find someone in Galtrev who will share information with youCatrin is in the village of Galtrev.

You have been told to speak with Catrin.Talk to Catrin in GaltrevCatrin has directed you to speak with Dai, Hulun, or Idwal in Galtrev.Talk to Dai, Hulun, or IdwalCatrin is in Galtrev.

You should speak with Catrin again.Talk to Catrin in Galtrev'We need information, ${PLAYER}. Galtrev is a place of no little significance in Dunland, and I want to know if Saruman's promises have already taken hold here.

'Start in the lower reaches of the village and see if anyone will speak to you of the situation here in Pren Gwydh.''Someone in the village may tell us what to expect in Pren Gwydh. Speak first to people in the lower reaches of the village.''Who are you, Duvodiad? You do not belong in this land. You are not welcome.'

She scowls at you.

'Speak with Catrin and leave me be! She knows what should be done with duvodiad.''Do not waste my time! Speak with Catrin if you must speak with anyone!'She looks you up and down appraisingly.

'You want to know what is happening in these lands? You are far from home... so far from home. In Galtrev you must not offend the wrong people. It is dangerous to make enemies here, yes it is.

'If you seek information, you seek one of these three: Dai, Hulun, or Idwal. They will teach you about these lands.''You should find Dai, Hulun, or Idwal here in Galtrev. They will teach you about Dunland, Duvodiad.''This land belongs to the Ox Clan! You will not leave here alive!''I did not think to see you again, Duvodiad, but I was wrong, yes. I heard the cries of that pathetic Ox from here!

'Folk of many clans live in Galtrev, but those who have grown wealthy from the gifts of Saruman float to the top. We of the lower village work hard just to get by, but the task-masters in the upper village live off of our labours and return the products of them to the Wizard.

'Perhaps you can be of some use to the Hebog-lûth, the Clan of the Falcon. We stand against those who have thrown in with Saruman.'Catrin desires to use you in her efforts to make things difficult for Saruman's servants in Pren Gwydh.The lumber-camp in Pren Gwydh is north-east of Galtrev.

Catrin has asked you to steal axes at the lumber-camp or from other hostile Dunlendings throughout Pren Gwydh, then throw the axes in a pond east of the camp.Collect lumber-axes from the camp north-east of Galtrev (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The pond where Catrin wanted you to throw the lumber-axes is east of the lumber-camp.

Catrin asked you to steal lumber-axes from the camp north-east of Galtrev and throw them into the pond east of the camp.Catrin is in the lower village of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh.

Catrin will be pleased to hear that you have disrupted work at the lumber-camp.Talk to Catrin at GaltrevLumber-piles can be found in the upper village of Galtrev.

Catrin in the lower village of Galtrev has a torch for you to carry to lumber-piles throughout the upper village.Catrin is in the lower village of Galtrev.

You have burned wood-piles throughout the upper village and should return now to Catrin.Talk to Catrin in Galtrev'People of many clans have listened to the promises of Saruman, and where his words are not enough, his gold does the trick. Even the folk of Galtrev are put to work to further the Wizard's aims.

'At the lumber-camp north-east of here, trees are felled and the wood prepared for carting to Isengard. Go there, steal their axes, and throw them in the pond east of the lumber-camp. Even if they fish them out, the rust will make the axes unreliable and difficult to use. Members of the dragon clan may have brought the axes to other settlements in Pren Gwydh. Those will do as well!

'A simple act of rebellion, maybe, but its effect could be sweeping.''You caused some trouble out there, I trust? Ha! Good. There is more for you to do.

'Wood from the lumber-camp has already been collected and is being stored in the upper village until it can be carted south. Take this torch and burn the wood-piles! That will make them scurry!''Wonderful, wonderful! Oh, you are a treat, my new friend.'

Catrin cackles with delight.

'The Hebog-lûth, the Falcon-clan, stands against Saruman and seeks to cause trouble for those who side with him. I think you will be a comfort to us...and perhaps we to you and yours.''The lumber-camp is north-east of here. Go there and steal some of the axes, or take them from hostile Dunlendings throughout Pren Gwydh, then bring them to the pond east of the lumber camp and throw them into the water. Rust will be our ally!''You have only done half of what I asked. The theft is done, but the axes could be taken from you and used again! You must throw them into the pond east of the lumber-camp before I will be satisfied with your efforts.''Use that torch to burn piles of lumber throughout the upper village of Galtrev! That will make them scurry!'Galtrev, the largest village of Dunland, is in Pren Gwydh to the south of the Bonevales.Galtrev, the main village of Pren Gwydh, can be found by taking the road south from the Bonevales.

You should go to Galtrev as you make your way through Dunland.Gain admittance to the village of Galtrev in Pren Gwydh'${PLAYER}, my friend, you have the look of one who is growing ready to leave. I want to thank you for all that you have done.

'Galtrev is the largest village in Dunland, and it is not far to the south of here in Pren Gwydh. Surely you will want to stop there as you make your way through Dunland.

'You are welcome back any time.''What do you want here, stranger? Why should the White Hand grant you admittance?

'I'm not sure I like the way you're looking at me, ${RACE}.''You will find Galtrev if you take the road south. Make sure you come back to visit, if you can! You will be missed by all here, ${PLAYER}.'Galtrev, the largest village of Dunland, is in Pren Gwydh to the south-east of Trum Dreng.Galtrev, the main village of Pren Gwydh, can be found by taking the road south-east from Lhan Tarren in Trum Dreng.

You should go to Galtrev as you make your way through Dunland.Gain admittance to the village of Galtrev in Pren Gwydh'${PLAYER}, my friend, you have the look of one who is growing ready to leave. I want to thank you for all that you have done for us during one of the Stag-clan's most trying times.

'Galtrev is the largest village in Dunland, and it is not far to the south-east of here in Pren Gwydh. I doubt you will encounter any folk of the Caru-lûth if you venture there, but surely you will want to stop there as you make your way through Dunland.

'I will miss you, ${PLAYER}! You are always welcome in Lhan Tarren.''What do you want here, Stranger? Why should the White Hand grant you admittance?

'I'm not sure I like the way you're looking at me, ${RACE}.''You will find Galtrev if you take the road south-east. Make sure you come back to visit, if you can! You will be missed by all here, ${PLAYER}.'Upon learning of Galtrev's current weakness, the Dragon-clan has settled nearby to prey on the people of Pren Gwydh.Dragon-clan invaders roam the western reaches of Pren Gwydh freely after having settled there.

You should protect the weakened peoples of Pren Gwydh by defeating the cruel folk of the Dragon-clan.Defeat the Dragon-clan in their new settlement (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tomos is near the Dragon-clan's new settlement in the western reaches of Pren Gwydh.

You should return to Tomos and tell him of your success against the Dragon-clan.Talk to Tomos'The Draig-lûth has learned of our weakness and decided that now would be a fine time to settle so near. Now they steal from us and threaten us day and night.

'The Dragon-clan is the bitter enemy of all the other clans of Dunland, ${PLAYER}. They are behind the crimes and the mischief done in these parts, more often than not. The White Hand will not deal with them, so we must take it upon ourselves.''There are many of these foes, ${PLAYER}. Please be careful!''You are a fine warrior. I could see you from here... brave and fearless and strong. I was like you once, but now I must watch from my hiding place. These foes would have overwhelmed me.'You have ventured into Galtrev, the capital settlement of Dunland in Pren Gwydh. It would appear that the White Hand currently governs this expansive village.The White Hand Overseers can be found in the lower areas of Galtrev, guarding their four respective posts.

You should speak with White Hand Overseer at the west gate to see if he needs your help.Speak with the first White Hand OverseerSpeak to the second OverseerSpeak with the third OverseerFlint Ironheart, the Overseer at the fourth workstation, seems to be at the root of the delay in the day's productivity.

You should speak with Flint Ironheart and find out if there is anything you can do to help.Find out why Flint Ironheart is blocking the entire day's work'A traveller wishes to gain access to Galtrev? Tell me, why should the White Hand wave you into Saruman's most productive new village?

'Galtrev is home to many wonders and conveniences that cannot be found anywhere else in Dunland, but only labourers and workers and close allies of Saruman may come here now!

'If you enter, you are to find work immediately. Travellers will find no easy accommodations here; report instead to each of the overseers in town. The supply lines are blocked, our shipment is late, and I will not answer for the failures of my inferiors!''If you are as lazy as the rest of this rabble, you will fit right in, stranger. Go find out where the supply lines are blocked, and be quick about it!''A recruit for the labour force? I don't like the looks of you, but we will take what allies we can. The White Hand does not discriminate!

'This is my work area here -- staffed by incompetent mongrels, as you can see.

'If you want to work for me, I'll have you know that I am completely blocked by the second Overseer. His supply line has been held up all day, and I can't make any progress without him! Go find out what's keeping that shipment, and be quick about it!''Who do you think you are, bullying me about my shipment schedule? The insolence of some folk these days... the third station hasn't sent over anything today, and we can't even get started.

'If you want to make yourself useful, go find out what is holding them up.''Are you questioning me? Who are you, anyway? I haven't seen you around these parts, and you don't look like one of the clansmen.

'Whoever you are, you can tell the gate-keepers that we will have their shipment ready, if the fourth station ever comes through with their promises. I don't know what those sluggards are about, making us wait so long!''I know everything is held up; you don't have to remind me, whoever-you-are! These lazy fools who work for me here can't seem to do anything right, and I can't punish them fast enough to fix matters.

'I don't know why our great lord would wish to ally himself with such feeble, incompetent folk. They would be more useful as food for the uruks than as suppliers and warriors.

'It looks like you have just volunteered to flog these useless mules until the supply lines are running smoothly again!'What does Saruman want with all of the goods coming out of Galtrev, anyway? It would be prudent to discover why the inhabitants of this town are forced to work so tirelessly for this effort.Crates that are destined to be shipped to Isengard can be found around Galtrev.

You should peek into the shipments destined for Isengard to see what Saruman might be plotting for these goods.Examine shipments destined for Isengard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gethin is at the fourth worksite in Galtrev.

Now that you have taken a good look at the various weapons and strange goods being shipped from Galtrev to Isengard, you should return to Gethin at the fourth worksite.Talk to Gethin at the fourth worksite'You have done a great service to us by helping with the labour, ${PLAYER}, so I will try to help you as well. Perhaps I can give you news that will be of interest to you.'

You ask Gethin what manner of goods were in those boxes, and where they were headed.

'Ah. Well, I know that Saruman has rallied his White Hand servants to oversee the delivery of the weapons and goods that are manufactured in Dunland. I can only imagine that these items are going to supply a great war. You are free to peek into the boxes if you wish, but do not let the White Hand see you at it....''Did you find what you were looking for, ${PLAYER}? It seems clear to me that our people are fuelling a great army.

'The young men go the same way as those crates you see. Saruman promises that the lands of Rohan will be returned to us, but the Horse-lords are vicious foes....''If you want to peek into the crates going to Isengard, I certainly will not tell anyone. They can be found throughout Galtrev.'The people of Galtrev wish to free themselves from the unfairly one-sided alliance with Isengard's White Hand presence.Tomos stands nearby.

You should speak with Tomos.Talk to TomosTomos is searching for his wife, Mari.

You should follow Tomos through Galtrev.Follow TomosTomos is searching for his wife, Mari.

You should follow Tomos to Mari's side.Follow TomosAn angry White Hand overseer has appeared to make Tomos answer for his crime of missing the day's work.

You should speak with the overseer to try to appease him.Try to appease the White Hand overseerThe half-orc to whom you spoke seems unreasonably angry.

You should defend yourself and the townsfolk from the wrath of the servants of Isengard.Help defend the people of GaltrevDefeat the servants of the White Hand.Help the people of GaltrevMari is in Galtrev.

You should speak with Mari.Talk to Mari'We are safe, even if only for a short time. Rest, friend. Retribution may still come, but I hope it will not be soon.''I believe my people are ready to be free of this burden... but there is only one way to find out. But first, I must find my wife.

'Come, my friend. She will be glad to know that you survived the ordeal as well.''Two little mongrels went rogue today and missed their day's work, ${PLAYER}. How do you propose to make up that labour to Saruman?

'You had best start running, little ${RACE}, you and your friend Tomos. I will not be merciful....'Thank you for helping my husband, ${PLAYER}! You did what many of us could not: stand up to the injustices of Isengard. You were a great boon to the people of Galtrev today.Many folk in Galtrev have sighted a massive, oversized boar roaming in Pren Gwydh, one that they have named "Big Bloodtusk". Big Bloodtusk is likely the patriarch of Pren Gwydh's vicious boars.Big Bloodtusk's den can be found in Bloodtusk's Dwelling.

You should lure Big Bloodtusk, the sire of all boars in Pren Gwydh, and attempt to defeat him.Lure and defeat Big Bloodtusk at his denLouri is in Galtrev.

You should return at once to Louri to let her know that you have accepted her challenge to defeat Big Bloodtusk.Tell Louri of your victory against Big Bloodtusk'Now that you have tried your hand at dealing with the nasty piglets, you should look to the great sire of this family: Big Bloodtusk. He is descended, they say, from an old and grisled boar who wandered into Dunland from the far north and has only been seen by a few people.

'There is a great den near Bloodtusk's Dwelling, and it can only be his, but he is not there often.

'You should lure him there and try to make him attack you. I doubt you will survive, ${PLAYER}, but at least it can be said that you were brave!''Why are you still here, ${PLAYER}? Are you afraid of Big Bloodtusk? I would be too, if I were you. Well, I am pleased to have made your acquaintance. I am sure I will not be seeing you again.''You! Why are you still alive, ${PLAYER}? I heard the distant squeals of wild boars engaged in a great battle and assumed you met an untimely end at the tusks of Big Bloodtusk. You certainly smell like a wild pig at the moment, but here you stand.

'Could this mean that you bested him? I suppose you are not so feeble as I presumed, duvodiad.'Nasty, wild boars, rumoured to be descendants of the Bloodtusk family, roam the wilds of Trum Dreng. They are dangerous, but also very tasty.Common forest-boars of the Bloodtusk family can be found throughout Pren Gwydh.

You should hunt for meat from common boars in Pren Gwydh, as they generally have vicious tempers and pose quite a threat to travellers.Collect meat from common forest-boars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Louri is in Galtrev.

You should bring the boar-meat you collected to Louri.'There is a fabled monstrous boar that wanders these parts, and he is known as Big Bloodtusk. He has been fathering many of the wild boars that roam Pren Gwydh over the years, and now they pose a serious threat to travellers.

'You should venture out into the wilds and try to do some hunting of the Bloodtusk family of boars -- especially the common forest-boars that stalk the wooded areas, ready to waylay anyone who comes too near.

'And while you are out there, you ought not hesitate to bring back some provisions for Galtrev! Those pigs are delicious.''Oh, how terrible, ${PLAYER}...are there wild boars in Galtrev now? I did not see any, but perhaps a great throng of them have recently moved in.

'No, you say? No boars in Galtrev? Then why are you still in Galtrev, when the boars roam elsewhere?''These shanks will make a lovely meal for my folk, ${PLAYER}, and we need all the nourishment we can get in these uncertain times.

'Thank you for your service to Galtrev, but I have more to ask of you.'The hardier, elder generation of the Bloodtusk family can be found in Bloodtusk's Dwelling in Pren Gwydh.The hardy forest-boars of the Bloodtusk family can be found in Bloodtusk's Dwelling, north and west of Galtrev.

You should prove your worth as a master of the hunt by defeating many of the greater boars in Pren Gwydh on their own turf.Defeat hardy forest-boars in Bloodtusk's Dwelling (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Louri is in Galtrev.

You should return to Louri now that you have killed many of the vicious boars on their own turf.Talk to Louri in Galtrev'In the western parts of Pren Gwydh, you will find a huge den of the even meaner, nastier kin of the Bloodtusk lurking in great numbers. These are the elders of the common boars, and they are even worse than their younger cousins.

'If you wish to prove that you are a worthy hunter of game, you should go cull some of those hardy boars next.''You have done well for an outsider. But I am not yet impressed....''You are still here, are you? What sort of hunter do you think you are, standing around in villages while your prey roams free?'After the untimely death of Leolin, a Man of Galtrev, by a vicious Warg, Luned wants to know if the evil beasts have invaded Pren Gwydh.Wargs can be found throughout Pren Gwydh, especially around the easternmost edge of Pren Gwydh.

You should defeat Wargs in Pren Gwydh to protect the folk of Galtrev.Defeat Wargs in Pren Gwydh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Luned sent forth a scout to find out where the Warg may have come from.

You should meet up with Goronu to figure out why the Wargs have gathered in Pren Gwydh.Find Goronu and find out if the source of the Wargs has been discovered'I have sent one of our last remaining scouts out to see if he can discover where that Warg may have come from. If they are indeed gathering in the wilds of Pren Gwydh, we must be prepared and ask the White Hand for their protection from this menace.

'And you, ${PLAYER}... will you help to protect us as well? For Galtrev, you should hunt down any of these monstrous foes that roam in Pren Gwydh.

'When you are finished, you should meet up with my scout.''Have you seen any more Wargs yet, ${PLAYER}? The thought of those monsters roaming outside our walls give me chills....''You must be ${PLAYER}... I am glad that you have come. Luned said she had sent you, but I was worried you would not make it here.

'As you can see, I have found the source of the Wargs in Pren Gwydh. Of what to do about them, however, I am not so certain.'Rook, a former servant of Isengard, now feels that he is a fully equipped Wizard.It would seem that Rook has taken a bit of an evil turn now that he sees himself as a fully accomplished Wizard.

You should defeat Rook before he tries to hold to any of his promises.Defeat the evil Wizard and take back the "magical" items he stoleEnvus is in Galtrev, still without her stolen toy ball.

You should return the toy ball to Envus, who has been without it long enough.'I am now a mighty Wizard, thanks to you! I will take over Dunland first, and Saruman will know that he has a force to contend with as a neighbour. Soon, I will conquer Isengard...and then all of Middle-earth!

'But first, ${PLAYER}, I must defeat you. All of Dunland will fall under my sway, and here it will start!''Ahahaha! You cannot escape, ${PLAYER}! The great Wizard Rook the Many-hued has declared his intent, and now it will all come to pass!''You found my shiny ball! Oh, thank you, ${PLAYER}! I am going to go play. Good-bye!'A shipment of wood from the lumber-camp was meant to arrive at Galtrev quite a while ago, but was stalled somewhere along the the road.The driver of the wood-waggon has become lost somewhere between Galtrev and the nearby Galtrev Lumber-camp to the north.

You should search for the missing driver and help the missing shipment reach Galtrev.Assist Fraid with thieves at the Galtrev Lumber-campAssist Fraid with stolen stacks of lumberFraid lies injured by his broken waggon in Pren Gwydh, near the Galtrev Lumber-camp.

You should speak with Fraid again, now that you have helped to allay the threat of the Dragon-clan at the Galtrev Lumber-camp.Talk to Fraid at his waggon'Pardon, duvodiad, but may I speak with you for a second? Please, this must be quiet. I need your help.

'The daily wood shipment from the Galtrev Lumber-camp is late, and I fear for the... well-being of the driver, Fraid, upon his return. I heard the Overseer of Isengard whispering that he would be sorely punished for this delay.''I do not know what is keeping Fraid, but more fearful than what may have happened to him beyond the gates is that which awaits him here.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You were most kind to come and help me, but should not Isengard protect us? That was their promise....'Many pieces of lumber were stolen when the Dragon-clan thieves attacked the waggon with Galtrev's shipment.Stolen stacks of wood can be found around the Galtrev Lumber-camp, just north of Galtrev.

You should gather wood as you investigate the Dragon-clan thieves in the Galtrev Lumber-camp.Collect stacks of stolen lumber (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fraid can be found at the broken waggon near the Galtrev Lumber-camp in Pren Gwydh.

You should bring the wood you recovered from the Galtrev Lumber-camp to Fraid.'So much lumber was stolen when those horrid thieves attacked! If I do not get it back, I will not be able to deliver the full shipment to Galtrev.

'Please, help me recover the stolen wood-stacks, ${PLAYER}. I am very afraid of the punishment the Overseers have in store for me.''What can we do against those reckless, murderous brigands?''Ah, you have recovered all of the missing lumber! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You are a true friend!'An elderly warrior of Galtrev, infuriated by the unwillingness of Isengard's guards to protect Pren Gwydh from the violence of the Dragon-clan, has decided to take matters into his own hands.Tomos has escaped his forced labour to look into doing something about the Dragon-clan menace in Pren Gwydh.

You should seek out Tomos and help him so that he can return before the White Hand Overseers notice that he is gone.Find Tomos in the wild'${PLAYER}, you must help me! It is my husband Tomos... he is a stubborn old warrior, and he has gone to fight the Dragon-clan alone.

'He says that the White Hand does not do enough to protect Galtrev, and so he must do so himself... but he is missing his work while he is gone. They will surely kill him upon his return!''Please help him and bring him back to me, ${PLAYER}. Tomos was a great warrior when he was a young man, but those years are behind us now. We should do as the White Hand commands, for they hold the power now....''Hail, ${PLAYER}! Look... the Draig-lûth! I knew that they had settled nearby. They can smell the weakness of Galtrev.

'I know I risk all to come here, but someone must deal with this menace. The White Hand does nothing but force us to labour for a war that does not help us.'It appears that the overworked townsfolk who labour to fill the White Hand's shipments are behind in their duties and attracting unwanted attentions from the White Hand Overseers.The workers who have slowed the day's progress can be found at the fourth post in Galtrev.

The Overseer has demanded that you beat the slow labourers, but there is probably a better way to move things along. You should assist the workers who need help meeting the demands of the White Hand.Help Wunne make spears more quicklyHelp Rhianu find missing nails and pins for the siege-enginesHelp Gethin deliver the heavy boxes and crates to the other worksitesThe Half-orc overseer, Flint Ironheart, can be found at the fourth worksite in Galtrev.

You should speak with the Overseer of this work-camp and show him that the supplies are once again moving along adequately.Talk to Flint Ironheart at the fourth worksiteGethin can be found at the fourth worksite.

You should speak with Gethin now that the Overseer is somewhat appeased.Talk to Gethin in Galtrev'If the guards sent you here to join the labour force, then you have come to the right place. We are hopelessly behind, as you see, and blocking the entire day's supply chain.

'Here is your first task: go flog, beat, and torture the workers until they are productive again. I want them working twice as fast! I want them doubling their production! If they still don't work, kill them, and take their place!

'If you can manage to get them working today, you will likely be welcome to come and go from Galtrev as often as you like.''Were my directions unclear, stranger? Make yourself useful and beat those ingrates within an inch of their lives until they work harder!''You're not so bad, ${PLAYER}. Has anyone ever told you that before? When I whip those sluggards, I could swear they are even less productive than before.

'Someday you should show me your flogging techniques. They seem to be most effective!

'Well, get moving! Find more work, so I can finally finish that nap....''What a relief it is to have such a kindly traveller in Galtrev! Flint Ironheart is finally distracted; perhaps now I can rest.'A child's toy ball seems to have gone missing, and a witness is positive it was stolen by a crow.Myve, the child who seemed to covet the shiny toy, is somewhere in Galtrev.

You should speak with Myve to see if she is hiding the shiny ball from its rightful owner.Talk to Myve in Galtrev about the missing toySomeone who may have witnessed the pilfering of Envus's toy would likely be in Galtrev.

You should look around and see if anyone saw someone make off with the shiny ball.Search Galtrev for someone with information about the toy ballThe crow that stole the ball was seen flying to the north-west.

You should head north-west to try and recover Envus' favourite toy.Find the crow that stole the child's toy ball'My shiny ball is gone! It was a gift from my father, before he went away to battle the strawheads. I would give anything to find it, but it does not seem to be anywhere I look.

'Could you ask around, please? Please, please, please! Maybe one of the other children took it. I know Myve was looking at it quite a lot when my father first gave it to me....''So you come seeking to reclaim the palantír? I knew someone would be back for it; yes, it was my craban that brought it to me!

'But hearken: a palantír is no toy for a child. 

'I am Rook, an apprentice Wizard. You should leave this dangerous object in my capable hands for the time being.''Envus is missing that silly shiny ball? Sure I looked at it, but I did not take it. What would I do with a ball like that? I want to play with spears, not useless, shiny toys.''I heard you mention Envus' missing toy -- a shiny ball, you say? I think I saw a crow taking off with just such a ball last night.

'It is strange, I know, but there could be no mistake. It was a black bird flying off with a shiny object clutched in its talons, heading north-west.''The shiny ball is the only toy I really care about. This is terrible!'The elusive Hardfang roams the Fanged Lair, striking terror into the hearts of all who dare face him.The elusive Hardfang can often be found circling the Fanged Lair, north of Galtrev.

You should find and defeat Hardfang as part of the ritual wolf-hunt in Pren Gwydh.Defeat Hardfang, leader of the wolvesHopcun is in Galtrev.

You should tell Hopcun that you have faced and bested Hardfang during your hunt.Talk to Hopcun in Galtrev'If you happen to see Hardfang when you venture out, you must face him. The hunters of Galtrev have all tried and failed, and many who met him were borne home with mortal wounds.

'A hunter of Galtrev must attempt to defeat Hardfang, for every battle weakens him.''You have done better than I expected! You are truly a remarkable warrior and hunter...better than any I have seen in my lifetime here in Galtrev. I am glad that you were not forced to join the war, ${PLAYER}.''Beware of Hardfang! His bite is deep, and he is a cruel foe....'It has become apparent to many that the White Hand alliance with the folk of Galtrev is not a fruitful one for the people of Pren Gwydh.Tomos is at the outskirts of the Dragon-clan's encampment in western Pren Gwydh.

You should speak with Tomos to travel to Galtrev.Accompany Tomos to establish a fair alliance between the people of Galtrev and the White HandMari is in Galtrev, the main village of Pren Gwydh.

You should speak with Mari in Galtrev.Talk to Mari'You have shown me what a true alliance should be, ${PLAYER}... and what Saruman has offered is no alliance. He has stolen our warriors and made us slaves. It is clear that the people of Dunland are nothing to him but thralls.

'Let us return to Galtrev now. Perhaps with your help, I can demand a fair alliance from the White Hand peoples stationed in our village.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready to leave, ${PLAYER}? Come... let us return to Galtrev together.''You fought bravely for our people, ${PLAYER}! You are a true hero... like the folk in the old tales. We owe you much!

'Thanks to you, our people are slaves to the White Hand no longer. But I fear that Saruman will retaliate when he hears of what happened here.'Now that you have used most of his trained flock feathers, Rook wishes to retrain a new flock, and looks for a collection of eggs to hatch.Craban roosting spots can be found in the lands of Pren Gwydh not far from Rook's Hut.

You should search for crow-eggs so that Rook may train another flock of crebain from chicks.Collect eggs from crow-nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rook is at his hut in Pren Gwydh.

You should bring the eggs you collected to Rook in Pren Gwydh.'It is very strange... my flock has significantly dwindled of late. I wonder where they all went off to? Very peculiar.

'I was ready to become a great Wizard, but it seems that I have one more task -- I should look to replenishing my flock. I need eggs from craban-nests, and the sooner the better, but the wild crebain that guard them can be a bit... hostile.

'You should go collect wild craban-eggs for me, ${PLAYER}. Make haste!''You can find craban-nests around this area, if you know where to look. The birds are wild, though! These crebain of Dunland are fierce.''Ha! Perfect, ${PLAYER}, and excellent timing, for I was beginning to grow impatient.

'I am now a great Wizard, you see, and it is all thanks to you!'At the source of the Wargs in Pren Gwydh are goblins training the vicious monsters as steeds, which are then carelessly released into the wild to roam as they wish.The chief of the Warg-riders is somewhere within the Howling Caverns.

You should defeat Mange-rider, the chief of the Warg-riders.Defeat Mange-riderGoronu can be found outside of the Howling Caverns in Pren Gwydh.

You should inform Goronu that you have defeated the chief of the Warg-riders.Talk to GoronuLuned is in Galtrev, waiting anxiously to hear of the vicious Wargs that roam the landscape of late.

You should tell Luned that you have brought down many Wargs and their riders and hopefully rooted out the source of the evil that entered these lands.Talk to Luned in Galtrev'I believe this goblin-band has a chief somewhere within this camp. They are slovenly, but they are organized as well in their efforts. These Wargs are trained, vicious, and unfortunately intelligent.

'You should defeat whoever or whatever is behind these terrible beasts leaking out into our lands.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! Goronu was just here. He spoke highly of your bravery in driving out the Wargs and their riders at the Howling Caverns. You are a great hero, and the folk of Galtrev will sing of your deeds here!''I heard a terrible disturbance within, ${PLAYER}, and feared the worst for you, but you have arrived triumphant! Have you truly defeated the terrifying leader of these creatures?

'I will return to Galtrev at once and tell Luned that we have dealt with the threat of Wargs in Pren Gwydh!''I would help you, ${PLAYER}, but I am only a humble scout, you see. I am sure you will do much better than I.'A shipment of wood from the Galtrev Lumber-camp was meant to arrive at Galtrev quite a while ago, but it was held up when the waggon-driver was attacked by hostile Dunlendings.Dragon-clan brigands and thieves roam the Galtrev Lumber-camp.

You should defeat a number of Dunlending thieves to secure the Galtrev Lumber-camp.Defeat Dragon-clan thieves at the Galtrev Lumber-camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fraid awaits you near his broken waggon in Pren Gwydh, not far from the Galtrev Lumber-camp.

You should speak with Fraid and let him know that the woods are a little safer now.Talk to Fraid at his waggon'Help, Duvodiad! It was the Dragon-clan, those fiends. They have grown bold of late, probably because the young men and warriors went away.

'This is meant to be the daily wood shipment, but as you can see, there has been an attack. Curse the Draig-lûth!''Brave warrior! Stout ${CLASS}! You have done well, indeed! You do more to protect us than those White Hand guards and Overseers in Galtrev....''The Draig-lûth is cruel, ${PLAYER}. Be wary when you fight them!'Trum Dreng is in the north-west of Dunland, below the Mournshaws.Trum Dreng can be found by travelling south through the Mournshaws. It is in the north-west corner of Dunland, directly west of the Bonevales.

You should visit Trum Dreng in your travels through Dunland and help whoever is willing to talk to you there.Find someone in Trum Dreng who will welcome you, and help themTrum Dreng can be found by travelling south through the Mournshaws. It is in the north-west corner of Dunland, directly west of the Bonevales.

You should visit Trum Dreng in your travels through Dunland.Find someone who will talk to you in Trum Dreng'So you leave us to make for Trum Dreng? I know little of that land, but I hear that it is mostly uninhabited. But if you wish to explore it, that is up to you, of course.

'You can find it by travelling south through the Mournshaws of Enedwaith, though there may be other paths with which I am unfamiliar. It is a stark land in the north-west of Dunland.''Thank you for helping our huntress, kind duvodiad!''You can reach Trum Dreng by travelling south through the Mournshaws in Enedwaith, ${PLAYER}.''I am sorry, traveller, but our town is not open to Duvodiads. We do not trust strangers here. You should head north along the road to get back to lands that may welcome you better.'Evan of the Falcon-clan is mistrustful of Elves and wants to be sure you know it.Elladan is south of the Brenin's house, by the ruins of the ancient fort near Tûr Morva. Elrohir is on a small rise overlooking the lake, west of the entrance to Tûr Morva.

Evan wants you to ask Elladan and Elrohir what they know about Dunland. He thinks they, and all Elves, look down on the shorter-lived races.Talk to Elladan in Tûr MorvaTalk to Elrohir in Tûr MorvaEvan is just inside the entrance to Tûr Morva.

You have spoken with Elladan and Elrohir concerning their knowledge of Dunlending history and should now report it to Evan. You may wish to be tactful.Talk to Evan in Tûr MorvaPenrod is among the northern buildings of Tûr Morva.

Evan has decided he is not as angry about Elves as he once was and wants you to tell Penrod.Talk to Penrod in Tûr Morva'Not many Elves pass through Dunland, ${PLAYER}. I will not lead you false; for my part, there are three too many Elves in Tûr Morva right now.'

Evan studies you closely, seeking a reaction of some kind.

'I know what you think of my folk. You call us short-lived, cursed to a hard life in hard lands, while you enjoy many life-times of pleasure. But what do you know of us? What do you know of the history of my people? Ask those other Elves that came with you what they know of Dunland. I want to hear what they say.''Your friends, those other Elves...ask them how much they know about Dunland. Not much, I would wager! You Elves are all the same, always looking down on the shorter-lived peoples!''I will be honest, ${PLAYER}. I do not know a great deal about Dunland or its people. I know they claim right to lands in the kingdom of Rohan and hold the Rohirrim as bitter enemies. They are organized into clans led by charismatic leaders. The Hebog-lûth, the Falcon-clan, does not trust Saruman, but it seems other clans in Dunland have allied themselves with the Wizard.

'Perhaps you should ask this Evan what he knows about the history of our people. I do not think he would do much better than I have done with his!''This Dunlending thinks we do not respect his people or their history? What history? The most note-worthy event I ever heard tell of was the Dunlending invasion of Rohan, which did not last long and eventually ended in defeat.

'You may not want to convey my opinion to this Evan, ${PLAYER}. I am grateful that his clan resists the promises of Saruman, but I am under no bond to admire their histories.''I still think you should ask this Evan what he knows about the history of our people, ${PLAYER}. Not much, I would wager.''I am glad that Evan's clan resists the promises of Saruman, ${PLAYER}, but I will not pretend to care about the history of Dunland. That will have to be enough for him.''Well? Did those other Elves know even the smallest thing about the history of my land and its people?'

Evan listens to your tactful distillation of the Elf-brothers' answers.

'They know broad strokes. That is better than I expected. But they know nothing of the flavour! Spurned marriages, rebel armies, and finally a Dunlending power strong enough to avenge the injustices visited upon it by the King of Rohan! Do they know that mighty Wulf, son of the valiant Freca and greatest of all Dunlending warriors, claimed the Golden Hall and sat upon its throne?

'So much for the Rohirrim! Only through deception and with a small force could they remove Wulf as lord of all the land! The history of Dunland is a full one, and you Elves know little of it.

'But I am pleased to have taught you this much, at least: that there is more to know. Perhaps there can be an understanding between your people and mine after all. Go tell Penrod, to the north, that my previous misgivings have been lessened.''Go tell Penrod that my misgivings are lessened. He is to the north.''You spoke with Evan? Do not take his words much to heart. We do not see many Elves in Dunland, and some are rightly suspicious of such rarities.'Arwel is delighted to meet a dwarf, considering how few he has seen, and tells you about another who visited the Brenin recently.Lheu Brenin is outside his home on the upper-most level of Tûr Morva.

Arwel, delighted at meeting a dwarf, thinks you should speak with Lheu Brenin about another dwarf who passed through Tâl Methedras recently.Talk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr MorvaWeapons are arrayed on a table next to Lheu Brenin.

Lheu Brenin has asked you to examine the weapons on the table next to him and to identify which of them was Lindar's gift to him.Examine the axe on the table near Lheu BreninExamine the sword on the table near Lheu BreninExamine the staff on the table by Lheu BreninLheu Brenin is outside his home on the upper-most level of Tûr Morva.

You have examined the weapons and should now tell Lheu Brenin which weapon was a gift from the dwarf Lindar.Talk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr MorvaPenrod is among the northern buildings in Tûr Morva.

Lheu Brenin has asked you to speak with his Brehur, Penrod.Talk to Penrod in Tûr Morva'Mair told me that there was a dwarf with the company, but I did not believe her. But here you are! We see so few of your people here.

'Is it true what they say about your cities under the mountains, that they stretch for leagues and leagues? How can you build for so long, and so great a distance? Do you not miss the daylight?

'You must excuse my questions. You are only the second dwarf I have seen in many months, and the other did not speak to me, as he met only with the Brenin. You should speak with Lheu Brenin, and he can tell you of your kinsman.''You will find Lheu Brenin outside his house at the top of the village. Speak with him about your kinsman, the other dwarf that passed through Tâl Methedras recently.''What can I do for you, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell him that Arwel wanted you to ask him about his previous dwarf guest. Lheu Brenin laughs heartily.

'Arwel has always been fascinated with your people; I think he wishes he had been born a dwarf! That would be a loss for the Falcon-clan; my daughter Mair has always been fond of him.

'It is true, we played host to one of your people not long ago. His name was Lindar, and he gifted me a weapon when he departed. Dwarves are keen of eye, yes? Examine these weapons and tell me which of them was his gift to me.''The weapons are right there on the table. Which of them was Lindar's gift to me?''Well? Which weapon was a gift from Lindar?'

You tell him your answer, wondering what his reaction will be. His surprise is obvious.

'All three of them? Are you certain? Why do you say that?'

You tell him that it was not your examination of the weapons that led you to the answer. Instead, it was the visible reaction on his face every time you handled one of the weapons that made you realize the question was not a fair one.

'Ha! That will teach me to think I know the ways of dwarves, ${PLAYER}! Well done, indeed! Lindar did gift each of these to me: the axe as a present from his people for past aid, the sword to combat present strife, and the staff to lean on in my old age, if I live to see it.

'You are indeed a rare dwarf! Go speak with my Brehur, Penrod, to the north. He wanted to speak with you.''Penrod is the first of my Brehur and wished to speak with you.''We truly do not see many dwarves in these lands. Lindar was quite close with Lheu Brenin, and the gifts he gave to him were most thoughtful. I wonder if the Brenin will have occasion to use any of them but the sword, given these times.'Catrin of the Falcon-clan wants you to help the oppressed people of Galtrev and those who live throughout Pren Gwydh.Tûr Morva is in Tâl Methedras, to the east of Pren Gwydh.

Catrin has asked you to aid the people of Galtrev and Pren Gwydh as much as you can before moving on to Tâl Methedras.Aid the people of Pren Gwydh as much as you can before moving on to Tâl MethedrasLéolin is suspicious of you, but has agreed to bring you to meet Lheu Brenin.

You have met the guard at the pass into Tâl Methedras, but he is wary of you and the Rangers. He is waiting to travel with you to Tûr Morva.Talk to Léolin, and he will bring you to Tûr MorvaPenrod is waiting to speak with you in Tûr Morva.Talk to Penrod in Tûr Morva'The clans of Dunland have a proud history, ${PLAYER}, and none prouder than the Falcon. Weaker clans have forgotten where they came from, forgotten their honour, but not my people.

'But dangers press on us from all sides. Good people live here in Galtrev and throughout Pren Gwydh, and they must be protected, their ills cured.

'Once you have aided the people of Pren Gwydh to your satisfaction, go to Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras. The people of the Falcon will be glad to have your help! Tûr Morva is to the east of here, beyond the Gravenwood.''For my part, I am glad to have your help, ${PLAYER}, and that of these Rangers. Even the Hebog-lûth cannot stand against Saruman alone.'The guard looks you up and down, suspiciously.

'You say you have helped Catrin in Galtrev? That old woman is always sending us help, but the help is almost never what we need. If you and these Rangers are different, I will bring some of you to see Lheu Brenin. But I hope you do not expect aid from us. The People of the Falcon have their own problems.''Help the people of Pren Gwydh as much as you can before moving on to Tâl Methedras, to the east. There are good people here, despite the presence of some who think Saruman can better their lives.''I will bring you and your people to Tûr Morva to speak with the Brenin, but I promise you nothing else. The Falcon-clan has its own problems to solve.'Penrod has told you there is much work to do before the Falcon-clan can have much hope of standing against Saruman.Each member of the Falcon-clan in Tûr Morva has a task to do to prepare for battle against Saruman. Penrod has asked you to aid them with their tasks.Penrod will be glad to hear that you have aided the people of Tûr Morva with their preparations.Talk to Penrod in Tûr MorvaLheu Brenin is outside his home, up the hill to the south of Penrod, in Tûr Morva.

Penrod has told you that the Brenin wants to see you concerning some trouble with the captive emissary of Isengard.Talk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva'If it took only courage to win battles against Wizards, the Falcon-clan would have marched south, put Saruman in his place, and be on its way home already...but it is not enough.

'Tûr Morva must be made ready. Rhus prepares the leather that Taf will fashion into armour. Our Brenin's daughter, Mair, trains youthful fighters in the combat arts. Idele sees to the gathering of foodstuffs for the journey. All have their work, but still it will be a while before the Falcon can fly to war.

'With your help and the help of the Rangers, it will go more quickly.''The preparations have been coming along very well, ${PLAYER}. These Rangers are hard workers, but none more so than you, good ${RACE}!'

Penrod's approving laughter fades, and he becomes solemn once again.

'Lheu Brenin wishes to see you. The emissary from Isengard that he captured is giving the guards trouble.

'Go see the Brenin outside his home, up the hill to the south.''All of Tûr Morva is alive with the sound of work, ${PLAYER}. It is good. There are many clans siding with the Wizard in this conflict, and I feared the Falcon-clan would not be ready if it came to war with them. With your help and that of these Rangers, the Falcon can show its talons!''Every man and woman of Tûr Morva has a job to do if the Falcon-clan is to stand against Saruman. Help them all with their tasks, and the preparations will go more quickly.''Lheu Brenin wishes to see you. The emissary from Isengard that he captured is giving the guards trouble.

'Go see the Brenin outside his home, up the hill to the south.'Lheu Brenin wants you to speak with the emissary of Isengard he is holding captive in the cave behind Tûr Morva.Nai is guarding the captive emissary of Isengard in the prison-cave, south of Lheu Brenin and in the wall of the cliff to your left.

Lheu Brenin has asked you to press the captive for information. First, you should speak to the guard Nai outside his cell.Talk to Nai at the prison caveNai has given you permission to enter the cell with Dondhreg to see if you can get any information from the captive emissary.Talk to DondhregYou have spoken with Dondhreg, but if there was anything valuable in his words it will be up to Lheu Brenin to discern it.Talk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva'You know of the emissary Saruman sent to us to force our cooperation? He is being kept under watch in the prison-cave. He has not told us anything of use yet, but perhaps you can inspire him to speak.

'Go into the prison-cave and speak to the guard Nai. He will allow you to press the captive for information. Return and tell me if the captive has anything useful to say. If he does not, perhaps his usefulness is at an end, and Nai can be given something else to do.

'The prison-caves are to the south. Follow the path and you will see the entrance among the ruins on your left-hand side, in the cliff.''You have the permission of the Brenin to speak with the prisoner? Very well. You may go in. He should pose you no danger. He knows that if he tries anything, he will do without meals.''What have you learned from our guest, ${PLAYER}?'

Lheu Brenin listens to your report of Dondhreg's words.

'There is truth there, I fear, if only a kernel. We must learn how large the kernel may be.''Have you come to gloat, ${RACE}? You are no Dunlending. Do not mistake these people for friends. It will be you in my place next! Mark what I say!'

Dondhreg glowers at you, his eyes full of hate.

'They cannot defeat Saruman. They are fools to try! The other clans are wiser and know which way the tide is going. Already, most of Dunland pledges their swords to my master. His armies come from Dunbog and Carreglyn and Starkmoor, and these unprepared fools will find themselves on the wrong side of the wave!

'It could have been different. I care not. It is enough to know that my captors will be slain by their own kinsmen soon enough, and you gloaters along with them!''You can go on in. He will not bite, if he knows what is good for him.''He is full of bluster, but I pay it no heed. We are out here, and he is in there.''Enter the prison-caves and speak with Nai. He will allow you to talk to the prisoner, and you may learn something of use to us. If not, well...it is of little account to me whether he lives or dies.

'The prison-caves are to the south. Follow the path and you will see the entrance among the ruins on your left-hand side, in the cliff.''You cannot stand against Saruman. Too many of the clans are already sworn to him. You have lost before you have begun.'Lheu Brenin has given you a task that will help gauge the severity of the threat posed to both the Falcon-clan and the Grey Company.Catrin is in Galtrev, the Dunlending village in Pren Gwydh, west of Tâl Methedras.

Lheu Brenin has asked you to travel through the lands of Dunland, seeing where the loyalties of the Dunlending clans lie and aiding those of like mind.Talk to Catrin in Galtrev'Wadu's Ghost' has a camp to the west of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh.

Catrin told you of a girl that helped her with her resistance against the Ox-clan in Galtrev. This girl called herself 'Wadu's Ghost' and was asking about the Grey Company.Talk to Wadu's Ghost in Pren Gwydh'Our prisoner spoke of the other Dunlending clans as if they were already in Saruman's satchel. That is my fear, but his words may be borne from bluster and desperation. The Falcon-clan is strong, but even our strength may not be enough to face all the clans of a united Dunland.

'I need someone that I can trust to travel throughout Dunland and see the state of things. Is Galtrev still as it was? Do the herds of Starkmoor feed Saruman's lackeys? What is the mood of the people of distant Dunbog? Are the mines of Carreglyn still being worked and for whom?

'I need you to be my eyes in this, ${PLAYER}. Go first to Catrin in Galtrev, she who sent you to us. See what is happening in Dunland and help those who share our goals. Saruman must be opposed, by the Rangers and by the Falcon-clan, if by no others.''You have returned, and on an errand from Lheu Brenin? Old Catrin is still a good judge of character, is she not?'

Catrin cackles and does a shuffling type of dance.

'To answer your questions, Galtrev is home to people of many clans, as it has been for all of my memory. The Ox-clan has been more brazen in recent days, and it seems to me that they must have received encouragement from some source. Some Wizard, if you ask for Catrin's opinion!

'While you were at Tûr Morva, someone has been helping me with my little resistance against the Ox-clan. She did not want to stay within the walls of Galtrev and has a camp to the south-west. She would not tell me her right name, but asked that I call her Wadu's Ghost. You should seek her out; she was asking about your Ranger friends.''We meet again, ${PLAYER}, as I knew we would. I am a free woman of the Uch-lûth, sister to Wadu and with victory notches already upon my sword.

'I am free to go where I please. I need no permission from your northern friends to walk these lands that belong to me and mine.

'Catrin of the Hebog-lûth and I of the Uch-lûth have already made things difficult for those who would sell these lands and its people to Saruman. I am ready to strike against them throughout all of Dunland, in my brother's name, if you are willing!''We must know if our prisoner speaks truth, ${PLAYER}. Have the other clans all sided with Saruman? You must be my eyes throughout Dunland. Start first at the village of Galtrev and speak with Catrin about the situation in Pren Gwydh.''Catrin does not ask questions of allies as useful as Wadu's Ghost. Her reasons for keeping her name a secret are no business of mine.

'She was asking about your friends; perhaps you two can be travelling companions and cause some trouble for the clans that have allied with Saruman. Nothing would please me more!

'Wadu's Ghost has a small camp west of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh.'Cungen has given you a wooden charm he carved of the mighty Rhi Helvarch, the Wild Huntsman, and wants you to go hunting with it.Wild creatures can be found throughout Tâl Methedras.

Cungen has asked you to defeat wild creatures throughout Tâl Methedras while bearing the charm of the Wild Huntsman, believing it will become even stronger with every victory.Defeat creatures in Tâl Methedras while bearing the Charm of the Huntsman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cungen is on the uppermost level of Tûr Morva.

You have defeated many creatures while bearing the Charm of the Huntsman and should return the charm to Cungen.'What do you know of the hunt, ${PLAYER}? I have been the greatest hunter of the Hebog-lûth for many summers, but it was not always so. When I was a boy, I wandered far and wide in search of the greatest prey I could master, but I searched in vain.

'Finally I came to a clearing in the trees, and amid the brilliance of a noon-time sun, I beheld a mighty figure. He was many times the height of a normal man, and it seemed he wore a great antlered helm. I was beneath his notice. He turned to gaze between the trees, and even as I contemplated the great Huntsman he was gone.

'I never found that clearing again, though I sought it. I fashioned this charm in his shape out of wood, and every time I go on the hunt I carry it with me. I give it to you now. Defeat creatures of Tâl Methedras, and each one will add to the legacy of this charm. Its legend will make me stronger when I bear it south against our enemies.''Every victory you attain while bearing the charm I gave you will add to its legend. It is a token of good fortune on the hunt, and I will be pleased to have as much fortune as possible when we go to fight the other clans.''Did you feel the Rhi Helvarch, the Wild Huntsman, with you while you were on the hunt? Sometimes I have felt sure he was helping guide my bow or strengthening my blade. That is why I carry that talisman with me and will bring it with me to battle.'

You return the Charm of the Huntsman to Cungen, and he grins.

'I would not want to lose this, I will tell you that much! But I can feel that touring with you has done it some good, and now it will be of even more use to me.'Maelona had never seen a hobbit before your arrival in Tûr Morva and wants you to share stories of your homeland with members of the Falcon-clan who are concerned by you.Gwynna and Olwen can be found in Tûr Morva.

Maelona told you that some of her fellows are distrustful of hobbits, having never seen one before, and you should tell them stories of your homeland.Talk to Gwynna in Tûr MorvaTalk to Olwen in Tûr MorvaMaelona is in Tûr Morva.

Maelona will want to speak with you once you have regaled Gwynna and Olwen with tales of your homeland.Talk to Maelona in Tûr MorvaPenrod, the first Brehur of Lheu Brenin, is in Tûr Morva. He has been asking for you.

Maelona told you to speak with Penrod now that you have reassured her friends Gwynna and Olwen.Talk to Penrod in Tûr Morva'You are the first halfling I have ever seen, ${PLAYER}. What strange times we live in!'

Maelona laughs nervously.

'I hope you do not think me rude to say so, but your appearance is most curious to my eyes and those of my fellows. We have seen dwarves, of course, but you are different even than that folk!

'Perhaps if you were to share stories of your people and your homeland with the more distrustful members of my clan, they would be put at ease, good halfling. I am speaking of Gwynna and Olwen, who expressed their concerns to me when you arrived. You will find them here in Tûr Morva.''I think you are looking for my sister Olwen. She is here in Tûr Morva.''Gwynna and Olwen are here in Tûr Morva. Do not confuse Olwen with her sister! One of them is training to be a warrior, and one of them is a singer of songs. It is the singer who expressed her concerns to me.'Gwynna looks at you warily, his face a mask of curiosity and fear.

'You are a... halfling? Why are you... why are you so small?'

He turns a bright shade of red, and you decide to defuse his embarrassment with tales of the Shire.Olwen looks at you distrustfully.

'How do we know that you are what you say you are? A hobbit? I have not heard of hobbits before. How do we know that you are not in league with Saruman?'

You decide that Olwen might be more accepting if you tell her tales of the Shire.'Your homeland, this Shire, sounds most comfortable. Would that we were all so fortunate to live in such a place!''What could have driven you to leave the Shire? It sounds like such a peaceful place, and I would have stayed there in comfort if even half of your stories about it are true!''Thank you for speaking with Gwynna and Olwen, ${PLAYER}. I know that your stories have helped show them that halflings are not a people to be feared.

'Penrod, the first Brehur of Lheu Brenin, was looking to speak with you. He is here in Tûr Morva.''Penrod is here in Tûr Morva. He was asking for you.''Ah, ${PLAYER}, the halfling! Very good. I have heard you were telling some of our people stories of your homeland. It sounds like it was a good home.

'My people had a good home once, but it was taken from us, long ago. Perhaps one day, we will have it again, but not as thralls to some Wizard. It is not worth that.'Rhus has been given the task of tanning leather to be used in the preparation of armour for the Falcon-clan and will appreciate your help.Tâl Methedras Oxen can be found on the far side of the lake, across from Tûr Morva.Rhus is on the eastern shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras, by his tanning tools in Tûr Morva.Buckets of sudsy water are set out near Rhus in Tûr Morva.

Rhus has asked you to help clean the leather strips he is soaking in the sudsy buckets.Clean strips of leather in sudsy buckets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhus is by his tanning tools in Tûr Morva.

You have cleaned several of the strips of leather that Rhus has been soaking and should now speak with the tanner about what he needs next.Talk to Rhus in Tûr MorvaThere are hides stretched between poles near Rhus in Tûr Morva.

Rhus wants you to beat the stretched hides in order to smooth them out for use in armour-making.Beat the stretched hides to improve their suitability for armour-making (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhus is by his tools in Tûr Morva.

You have helped Rhus considerably, and he wishes to speak with you.Talk to Rhus in Tûr MorvaTaf is at the leather-working pavillion, north of Rhus's home and on the shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras.

Rhus has given you treated ox-skins to bring to Taf.'I have heard about you, ${PLAYER}. You are here to help me prepare leather to be used in the making of armour for the Falcon-clan?'

Rhus grins at your nod of assent.

'Tanning is a complex and lengthy process, but so is the business of war; I began to prepare much of this leather some days ago. But we will need more.

'On the far side of the lake you will find oxen. I need tough skin from one of them. Make sure it is suitable before you return to me!''The leather strips have been cleaned? Good. I have stretched some of the hides between poles here to make them more pliable.

'Use this club to beat the rough patches of the hides smooth. The fewer uneven patches there are, the more well-fitting any armour made from it will be.''I have several batches of leather in various stages of readiness, ${PLAYER}, and you have helped with many of them.

'Here are some ox-skins that have been treated. Bring them to Taf in the leather-working pavillion on the edge of the lake, north of here. He should be just about ready for them.''The oxen on the far side of the lake should have tough enough skins for my purpose. You just have not found one yet.''Leather must be thoroughly cleaned if it is to be made into strong armour-pieces. Clean the strips which I am soaking in these buckets; it may take a while, but that is true of much that is worthwhile.''The hides are right there, stretched between those poles. Beat them smooth, and the armour we make from them will be better-fitting.''Taf should be ready for those ox-skins now. Bring them to him at his pavillion north of here.''This ox-hide will serve, ${PLAYER}.'

Rhus points to the buckets of sudsy water lying nearby.

'I have cut strips of leather from some of the ox-hides your Ranger friends brought me this morning. The strips are soaking in these buckets for now. Dunk them thoroughly and comb out any of the grime that still remains in the hides.

'It may take a while, but that is the way of things that are worthwhile.''You are the ${RACE} who has been helping Rhus? I see, I see. You have helped him with the various stages of preparing leather for use by the Falcon-clan? It is only right that you now help me, is it not?'The Dragon-clan thieves have become a persistent problem at the Galtrev Lumber-camp, causing some problems with timely deliveries.The Galtrev Lumber-camp is not far to the north of Galtrev.

Wood is needed from the Galtrev Lumber-camp, but the threat of Dragon-clan thieves have made delivery a problem.Collect stolen lumber (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Dunlending thieves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fraid is near the overturned waggon on the outskirts of the Galtrev Lumber-camp.

You should bring the wood you gathered to Fraid.The wood you collected is in a pile near the overturned waggon.

You have recovered some wood and should now carry it to Galtrev.Deliver the wood shipment to Macsen in GaltrevMacsen is in Galtrev.

You should speak with Macsen to complete your daily delivery of the wood shipment from the Galtrev Lumber-camp.Talk to Macsen in Galtrev'The wood must be collected from the Galtrev Lumber-camp once again, but everyone is afraid to go out with the Dragon-clan roaming about unhindered.

'You have proven a worthy opponent to their numbers, duvodiad. Will you go bring today's wood delivery to Galtrev?''Ah, well done. Let us bundle these into one shipment that you can carry to Macsen.''You are a valuable asset to our village, ${PLAYER}! Thank you again... I know this must be a chore for you, but you help us greatly with tasks such as these.'The Grey Company has come to Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras, to meet with Lheu Brenin, the leader of the Falcon-clan.Halbarad is on the path leading up to Tûr Morva.Talk to HalbaradLéolin is on the path leading up to Tûr Morva.Talk to LéolinLéolin is leading you up the hill to meet with Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva.Follow Léolin into Tûr MorvaSaeradan has been hit by a stone thrown by a Dunlending. You should check to make sure that he is all right.Talk to SaeradanMair is not pleased at whoever threw the rock at Saeradan.Talk to MairLéolin is leading you through Tûr Morva to meet with Lheu Brenin, the leader of the Falcon-clan.Follow Léolin through Tûr MorvaLheu Brenin's first Brehur, Penrod, is ready to speak with you.Talk to PenrodYou have come into Tûr Morva to meet with Lheu Brenin, leader of the Falcon-clan.Meet with Lheu Brenin, leader of the Falcon-clanLheu Brenin is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Lheu BreninHalbarad is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Halbarad'This way, please. I have sent word ahead to Lheu Brenin, and he is awaiting your arrival.''I am sorry your welcome to Tûr Morva was marred in this way, ${PLAYER}. Saruman will never command the loyalty of the Falcon-clan, and the more he tries, the stronger my resolve will grow. I had thought my people stood with me in this, but it seems some are unwilling to respect my wishes.

'The Wizard sent an emissary to buy our loyalties with gold and silver. I have him locked in the dungeon. It will not be long before he sends another, but this one may have an army at his back. We can help you against Saruman, but first we need to prepare our own defences.''I will find out who threw that stone, and they will pay for it. You are the guests of my father, and you are under his protection while you are in our village!

'It is an affront to my father, it is an affront to me, and it is an affront to the Hebog-lûth!''Welcome to Tûr Morva, travellers from the north! It is the hope of Lheu Brenin that you share our desire for peace. Can there be friendship between our people?''It is nothing, ${PLAYER}. The stone only grazed me. I am fine.''Remain alert, ${PLAYER}, but try not to offend them. This is their land, and passage south will be easier if we can count the Falcon-clan among our allies. If half the stories they tell in Lhanuch about Lheu Brenin are true, we do not need him as an enemy.''We will help them make their preparations, ${PLAYER}. Our aims do not line up perfectly with those of the people of Dunland, but we do share a common enemy. Let Saruman be distracted by the Falcon-clan while we make our way through the Gap of Rohan unobserved.''Penrod will tell you what still needs to be done. I will show you to him.'Taf is responsible for crafting much of the armour the Falcon-clan will wear into battle and could use your help.Lake-side plants with red flowers can be found growing alongside the shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras, but only where the dirt comes right down to the water.

Taf has asked you to collect lake-side plants with red leaves that he can grind up for dye.Collect lake-side plants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Taf is at the leather-working pavillion in Tûr Morva.

You have collected the lake-side plants Taf asked you to gather and should bring them to him.There is a grinding stone at the leather-working pavillion near Taf, in Tûr Morva.

Taf has asked you to grind up the plants you gathered on his grinding stone, in order to make the colouring for the dye he needs.Taf is at the leather-working pavillion in Tûr Morva.

You have ground up some dye on his grinding stone and should show the product of your labour to Taf.Partially-completed leather armour is on the table near Taf in the leather-working pavillion of Tûr Morva.

Taf has asked you to use the dye you prepared to put the mark of the Falcon on some of the partially-completed leather armour he has set out on a table.Taf is at the leather-working pavillion in Tûr Morva.

You have drawn the mark of the Falcon on some of the partially-completed armour and should return the excess dye to Taf.'I have been working as quickly as I can to fashion armour from the leather that Rhus prepares, but it is time-consuming work. It is important that the armour be strong, but it must also bear the mark of the Falcon; our enemies quail when they know who it is they fight, and Saruman will be no different!

'My stock of the dye used to mark the finished armour with the mark of the Falcon is low. Can you pick the red plants along the lake-side here in Tâl Methedras? Bring me several handfuls of their leaves, and we can grind more of the dye.''Plants with red leaves grow along the lake-side in Tâl Methedras, but only where the dirt comes right down to the water. Bring me their leaves, and I can grind them up to make the dye that I will need to mark this armour.''Use my grinding stone to crush the plants that you collected into colouring for the dye I need. It is right over there.''I have set some armour there on the table. Use the dye you prepared to put the mark of the Falcon on it, ${PLAYER}. You have earned the right!''These are the plants I asked for, ${PLAYER}? Good. Take them to my grinding stone over there and grind the leaves into a fine powder. It will provide the colour my dye requires.''This is just the right shade for our purposes, ${PLAYER}. Use it to mark the leather armour I have nearly finished with the claw of the Falcon.''That is an acceptable Falcon's claw, ${PLAYER}. That will drive fear into any of the clans that try to fight us!

'Thank you for the help you have been today. I will not forget it!'The Dunlending taskmaster wants mucky filth. She can be found at Galtrev in Pren Gwydh.You have accepted a task to acquire mucky filth. You are to deliver it to the Dunlending taskmaster in Galtrev.Wanted: Mucky filth from swamp-dwelling creatures in the Dunbog. Collect them and deliver them to the taskmaster in Galtrev to earn favour with the Men of Dunland.Wanted: Mucky filth from swamp-dwelling creatures in the Dunbog.'I hate those creepy things. Good riddance to them all!'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Iwan believes the clans that have pledged themselves to Saruman deserve no mercy and plans to brew a poison with which to fight them.Toads can be found throughout Tâl Methedras, on the far shore of the lake and the island in the middle of the water.

Iwan has asked you to collect some of the residue from the skins of toads in Tâl Methedras.Defeat toads and scrape residue from their skins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iwan is sitting on the shore of the lake near the orchard of Tûr Morva.

You have collected residue from the toads of Tâl Methedras and should bring it back to Iwan.Maelona is outside her house near the entrance of Tûr Morva.

Iwan has inadvisably tasted the toad-residue that he wants to coat the Falcon-clan's weapons with and is now sick. He has sent you to the healer Maelona to bring him something that will cure him.Talk to Maelona in Tûr MorvaIwan is at the lake's edge near the orchards of Tûr Morva.

Maelona has given you some powder that should cure Iwan of his digestive complaint.'The clans that have agreed to follow Saruman deserve no mercy, ${PLAYER}. Let them fear the talons of the Falcon! My people will show them that Dunland needs no Wizard sovereign. This land is for Dunlendings, not the thralls of Saruman!

'Toads frequent the far shore of the lake and the eyot in the middle of the water. Scrape some of the residue from their skin and bring it to me. Handle it carefully! I may be able to put it to use.''Toads can be found on the far shore of the lake and on the eyot in the middle of the water here in Tâl Methedras. Bring me the residue of their skins, and I can put it to use.''Toad-residue? Ah, there it is. Thank you. Let us see how potent it is.'

Before you can stop him, Iwan sticks out his tongue and licks the residue. Suddenly his eyes cross, and he turns a pale shade of green.

'It... is just what we need... a coating of this... on our weapons... will do great harm to the... disloyal clans....

'Find our healer, Maelona... ask her to make something... that will cure me... she is... in the village....''The healer... Maelona... she may have something that will... cure me.'

Iwan shudders weakly and turns a deeper shade of green.

'But look... at how effective....''Iwan is a fool, and always has been! Never taste the poison you are making!'

Maelona sighs.

'There is a root that grows at the base of trees along the shores of the lake here in Tâl Methedras. I have some of it in my stock. When grinded into a powder, it can cure most digestive ailments.'

Maelona digs around in one of the pouches tied about her waist and produces some of the powder.

'Give this to Iwan. He should start to feel better.''Certain roots can be found in the shadow of the trees that surround the lake. I have made a powder of these roots, and I have observed its ability to ease the stomach. Iwan should consume the powder I gave to you, and he will recover.''I feel... terrible... is that not wonderful?'

Iwan accepts the powder Maelona gave to you, and in a few moments his colour begins to return.

'Ah, thank you, ${PLAYER}. I think... I think that tells us everything we need to know! Coating the weapons of the Falcon-clan with this toad-residue will cause our enemies some real distress!

'I would normally not resort to poison, but the clans that side with Saruman are Dunlendings no longer. They do not deserve mercy, and I feel no regret wielding poisoned weapons against them!'Idele is charged with collecting food and smoking meats for when the Falcon-clan must go to war.The orchards of Tûr Morva are to the north-west.

Idele has asked you to bring a basket of apples to her from the orchards where several of the Rangers are picking fruit.Talk to Golodir in Tûr MorvaA basket of apples near Golodir in the orchard of Tûr Morva is ready for carrying to Idele.

Idele has asked you to bring a basket of apples to her from the orchard of Tûr Morva.Pick up a basket of apples near Golodir in the orchardIdele is in Tûr Morva.

You have brought a basket of apples to Idele in Tûr Morva and should now speak with her.Talk to Idele at Tûr MorvaThere are empty baskets near Idele in Tûr Morva.

Idele has asked you to pick up an empty basket and carry it back to Golodir in the orchard north-west of Tûr Morva.Pick up an empty basket near Idele in Tûr MorvaGolodir is in the orchard of Tûr Morva.

You have brought back an empty basket to the orchard and should now speak with Golodir.Talk to Golodir at Tûr MorvaIdele is in Tûr Morva, south-east of the orchard.

Idele is waiting for some of the apple-wood branches that Golodir collected from the orchard.Pick up an armful of wood from the orchardIdele is in Tûr Morva.

You have brought an armful of apple-wood to Idele, and she wants to speak with you.Talk to Idele in Tûr MorvaThe fire Idele is using to smoke the meat for the journey south is by her in the middle of Tûr Morva.

Idele has given you some wood to throw on the nearby fire.Idele is in Tûr Morva.

You have helped to smoke some of the meats for the journey of the Falcon south and should speak to the fire-tender, Idele.Talk to Idele at Tûr Morva'It is my task to prepare food for the warriors when they must travel south to fight the hostile clans: apples, hazelnuts, elderberries, and smoked meats. Some of your friends are picking apples at the orchards of Tûr Morva. Go there and bring back a basket of apples, and I will wrap them up.

'The orchard is to the north-west.''If you would like to help out, go to the orchards to the north-west and bring me a basket of the apples picked by your Ranger friends.''This is a curious land, ${PLAYER}... very different than I expected. I expected Dunlendings to charge heedlessly to war, but these folk of the Falcon-clan are taking great pains to prepare for battle.

'It worries me that the other clans, the ones sworn to Saruman's service, are likely cut from the same cloth. We must not underestimate his allies if they are as tough as the Men that we have seen in Tûr Morva.

'You are ready to bring a basket of apples back to the woman Idele? Take one of these... they are ready.''Any one of these baskets of apples are ready for you to bring to Idele, ${PLAYER}. She is south-east of here in the village, is she not? By one of the camp-fires?''Thank you for bringing me that basket of apples. I will prepare them for travel. While I do that, will you bring this empty basket back to your Ranger friend in the orchard?

'When you see him, ask if he has collected the fallen apple-wood branches I asked him to gather. I will need them to smoke some of the meats the warriors will bring south.''Pick up one of these empty baskets and carry it to your Ranger friend in the orchard to the north-west. Then bring back some of the apple-wood branches I asked him to gather.''Did you ask your Ranger friend at the orchard to the north-west if he gathered the apple-wood I asked him to collect? I need it to smoke the meats for the journey south.''You have returned already? Oh, I see. Yes, I did gather some apple-wood branches for Idele. You can bring some of them to her now, if you like.''You are to bring an armful of apple-wood to Idele in Tûr Morva? She is to the south-east of here, is she not?''Thank you for bringing me these branches! The smoke from these should do very nicely. You can throw them on the fire, if you like.''Go ahead. You can throw the wood on the fire. The smoke will do the meats a world of good.''Well done! I have many more preparations to make before we will have enough food for the warriors of the Falcon-clan, but it is a start, and I thank you for it!'Penrod wants you to check in on some of the Rangers who are helping the Falcon-clan prepare for war and see how they are doing.Halbarad, Radanir, and Braigiar can be found throughout Tûr Morva.

Penrod wants you to check on with members of the Grey Company helping the Falcon-clan prepare for war with Saruman.Talk to Halbarad in Tûr MorvaTalk to Radanir in Tûr MorvaTalk to Braigiar in Tûr MorvaPenrod is among the northern buildings of Tûr Morva.

You have spoken with a number of Rangers and found how they are helping with the preparations.Talk to Penrod in Tûr Morva'Your Ranger friends have already been very helpful, ${PLAYER}. If the clans loyal to Saruman try to strike us before we are ready to leave, we may yet have a chance.

'Speak with your friends and see how they progress with their tasks.''Your Ranger friends are helping us prepare for war. You should check with them and see how they are doing.''There is a great deal to do before the Falcon-clan is ready, but this work will be worth it in the end. We have few enough allies in this land. If the sweat of our brow can help the Hebog-lûth stand against the clans loyal to Saruman, the work is worth it.

'We have already brought much in the way of food. Once it is dried or preserved, it will be wrapped and ready. My arms ache, but not so badly that I must stop.''I know allies among the Dunlendings are precious few, ${PLAYER}, but I do not see what is so different about the Falcon-clan than others that we have seen.

'They have me mucking out the oxen! I have seen more manure already in Dunland than I have in my entire life back north. I could be doing something useful, but instead they hand me a hay-fork and a broom and tell me to get to work.

'I do not like these men, ${PLAYER}, and it is not because of the manure. There are plenty of reasons, but the smell of manure has made me forget most of them. I say we bid them farewell and leave them to their own devices!''We are doing all we can, ${PLAYER}. I have been assisting Rhus with the tanning; it is dirty, odious work, but the Falcon-clan needs the leather if they are to have fresh armour for its warriors.

'I saw Radanir not long ago. He was not very happy about something, but would not tell me what it was. Right now I am working to clear this brush so we can stretch some more hides as they come in.''Ha! Ha! I am sorry your friend Radanir is unhappy. Mucking out the oxen is not a pleasant task, but if it is not done, all suffer. There are very few desirable tasks when it comes to preparing for war, ${PLAYER}, but all must be done.'

Penrod laughs heartily.

'But I am not ankle-deep in manure, am I? Perhaps I will find someone to take Radanir's place. We are grateful for the help and do not want any of the Rangers to resent volunteering it!

'Thank you for your help and theirs, ${PLAYER}. The clans arrayed against us are fierce and merciless, but they do not have allies from the North, as we do!'Bingo's stomach has made it quite impossible for the hobbit to concentrate on the further writing of his book, and he needs you to do something about the hungry situation.Willem Whisker is somewhere within Mirkwood. If you ask around the Haunted Inn, and elsewhere within the forest, you may be able to learn where the lynx might have gone.

Bingo wants you to find Willem Whisker and send him back to the Haunted Inn, with breakfast if possible!Find Willem Whisker somewhere within MirkwoodWillem Whisker is within the outer wall of Dol Guldur, up a slope to the north of Fennas Guldur.

You have found Willem, and it seems that he has found a dirty satchel of some kind.Collect the satchel Willem has found, and tell him to return to the Haunted InnBingo is in the Haunted Inn, located in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood.

You recovered an Orc-satchel found by Willem Whisker, and should bring it to Bingo.Bingo wants to meet you outside the gate to Caras Galadhon, in Lothlórien.

Bingo has seen enough of Mirkwood, and has decided to travel with you back to Lothlórien.Talk to Bingo outside Caras Galadhon, in LothlórienCalengoth is at the docks of Lothlórien, west of Imlad Lalaith.

Bingo believes that he has fallen prey to a curse causing him unnatural hunger pangs, and he wants you to apologize to Calengoth for the deception that enabled the hobbit to cross the river into Mirkwood.Talk to Calengoth on the docks of LothlórienBingo is outside the gate to Caras Galadhon, in Lothlórien.

Calengoth gave you a small packet of lembas to give to Bingo, and also forgave the hobbit for his deception.'This empty belly of mine has made it quite impossible for me to concentrate on further documenting our stay in Mirkwood, ${PLAYER}! I am glad that we were able to give Adolinda a momentary distraction from her curse, but the fact remains that her recipe for breakfast involved spider-legs, and while I am powerless to do anything about the curse, it is within my power to refuse a breakfast of hairy spider-legs! No spider-legs for me, thank you! Yuck!

'I told Willem about my dissatisfaction and my hunger, and he ran off. Can you ask around the Inn and see if anyone knows what has become of him? I expect he has gone in search of a second breakfast, and I would greatly appreciate your hastening him back here with it!''I told Willem about this problem of ours, and he ran off. Can you ask around the Inn and see if anyone knows what has become of him? I expect he has gone in search of a second breakfast, and I would greatly appreciate your hastening him back here with it!''The lynx that follows your friend Bingo around did not stay in the Inn. I think he was searching for food, and went somewhere to the east.''I saw that lynx run to the east. He was moving with a great deal of haste.''I have not seen any lynxes that match your description anywhere in the Drownholt. Perhaps you should travel to the north-east and ask if anyone at Ost Galadh has seen anything.''I have seen this lynx you seek! He ran right past the three of us, heading east! He disturbed the papers on this table! I think he was looking for food of some sort, but nothing here satisfied him, and he ran through Ost Galadh after a brief search.''Yes, I saw your lynx! He ran right past us, but not before jumping onto this table and scattering papers everywhere!

'He did not stay. He ran east out of Ost Galadh.''Oh, I have seen your lynx. He ran through here, disturbed the papers on this table, and continued on his way to the east. He is no longer in Ost Galadh.''I think I did see your lynx, from a distance. I saw him a good distance to the east, heading in the direction of Dol Guldur. He was making straight for the gate of Fennas Guldur, but I was beset by Orcs and did not see if he reached it.''I saw the lynx you seek. He was running at great speed to the south-east, in the direction of Fennas Guldur. Whether he passed through that gate and is now on the other side of the wall, I do not know.''Willem Whisker? What sort of a name is that?

'Rodelleth told me she saw a lynx running to the south-east, toward Fennas Guldur, but I did not see him myself.''I have just returned from Dol Guldur, ${PLAYER}, and I saw something most peculiar. There was a lynx fighting Orcs just within the gate of Fennas Guldur, to the east. As I crept away, I saw the lynx making his way north up a slope just behind the wall.

'If you are looking for this curious creature, you should go east to Fennas Guldur, and then climb the slope to the north once you are through the gate. If he is an enemy of the Orcs, he must be a friend to the Golden Host!''I do not think your lynx-friend is still within Audaghaim. He has gone elsewhere in the Greenwood.''I have just returned from Dol Guldur, ${PLAYER}, and I saw something most peculiar. There was a lynx fighting Orcs just within the gate of Fennas Guldur, to the south-east. As I crept away, I saw the lynx making his way north up a slope just behind the wall.

'If you are looking for this curious creature, you should go south-east to Fennas Guldur, and then climb the slope to the north once you are through the gate. If he is an enemy of the Orcs, he must be a friend to the Golden Host!''You found Willem? Did you tell him to follow you back here?'Willem Whisker stands by a dirty satchel that appears to have once been the property of an Orc. The lynx beams at you proudly, and you pick up the satchel. 

You take a quick peek inside, and the contents make you laugh in spite of yourself. You resolve to bring it back to Bingo in the Haunted Inn.Willem Whisker beams proudly at you. Perhaps the satchel contains something of use for Bingo after all?Bingo gingerly takes the Orc-satchel.

'What's that? W.W. found this satchel for me? How thoughtful! Does it contain food, do you think? The bag does seem to be rather worse for wear, but let's see... small trinkets... bent bits of metal... this is rather fuzzy...'

Bingo suddenly jumps backwards and drops the satchel onto the table. After a moment he begins to laugh.

'There are spider-legs in here! Willem, did you think I was unhappy about how FEW spider-legs ${PLAYER} brought back? That was not it at all! Why does everyone want me to try these unpleasant things? Do you know something, ${PLAYER}? I think I am ready to return to Lothlórien! I will meet you out in front of Caras Galadhon, and perhaps we can find some real food, for now my belly is quite complaining!''Do you know something, ${PLAYER}? I think I am ready to meet you back in Lothlórien! I will meet you out in front of Caras Galadhon, and perhaps we can find some real food, for now my belly is quite complaining!''We are back in more pleasant lands. It is something of a relief to leave Mirkwood behind us, but... well, I have been worrying about something.'

Bingo's cheerful expression is gone. He seems quite upset.

'It is this appetite of mine! We Boffins like to have as many meals as anyone, and I am no stranger to nipping off to the larder for a snack or two between meals. But this hunger is sharper, in a way, than any hunger I can remember! I got to thinking about what has gotten me this hungry, and I realized that it began around the time we crossed the river into Mirkwood.

'There is something unnatural about this! Is this a curse? You need to have done something bad to be cursed. Didn't Adolinda say something about a great evil in her past? Well, I was thinking about it, and while I wouldn't say I have done anything especially evil, I wasn't honest with Calengoth, was I? We used deception to get him to allow us across the river! Is my increasing hunger a curse for my poor behaviour?

'You have to go to Calengoth at the docks and apologize for my lies, ${PLAYER}! I fear I will waste away from this curse if you do not!''You have to go to Calengoth at the docks and apologize for my lies, ${PLAYER}! I fear I will waste away from this curse if you do not!''You have come back, I see. What did your friend think of the Golden Host's adventures in Mirkwood?'

You explain Bingo's deception, and give Calengoth the hobbit's sincere apologies. The Elf nods solemnly, but there is a smile on his lips.

'Bingo must have a low opinion of the intelligence of Elves if he believed I was truly fooled by his deception. I was not. But it takes a large heart to admit such a thing, and my refusal to bear him across the river was borne not of malice but of concern for his safety. I accept his apology.

'I may also have the solution for his hunger. Give him this small packet of lembas, along with my well-wishes. I think the one will cure his hunger and the other may assuage his guilt, for I imagine the latter is the truest source of his curse, and once forgiven I expect he will be fine. That is my guess!''Bingo must have a low opinion of the intelligence of Elves if he believed I was truly fooled by his deception. I was not. But it takes a large heart to admit such a thing, and my refusal to bear him across the river was borne not of malice but of concern for his safety. I accept his apology.

'I may also have the solution for his hunger. Give him this small packet of lembas, along with my well-wishes. I think the one will cure his hunger and the other may assuage his guilt, for I imagine the latter is the truest source of his curse, and once forgiven I expect he will be fine. That is my guess!''Calengoth accepted my apology? Lovely, lovely! I am glad to hear it! And what is this? Lembas? How interesting. It looks to be a type of cake, if a little plain-looking. It is a gift from Calengoth?'

Bingo takes a small bite and nibbles at it for a moment.

'Ah! I did not expect it to be so delicious! And how filling! My, this lembas has quite cured my curse, if such it was! It is good to have a full belly, for now I am ready to travel down the Great River in search of further adventures!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'The Banks of the Great River' (Recommended Level: 70)</rgb>Wynfor has fashioned three traps from the avanc-jaws that you brought him and wants you to set them out for the mysterious intruder.You found footprints on the far shore of the lake, north-west of the eyot and beneath the cliffs west of the shore, and now Wynfor wants you to set three traps he made at those locations.

Wynfor has given you three traps he has made, and he wants you to set them in the vicinity of the footprints you found earlier.You have placed the snap-jaw traps in Tâl Methedras, as Wynfor wanted.Wynfor is in Tûr Morva.

You have set the traps for Wynfor and should now return to him.Talk to Wynfor at Tûr Morva'I will take this string and stretch it here... and here....'

Wynfor works for a few moments, then is satisfied.

'Aye, this will do. See! I have made of this avanc-jaw a trap! It will snap shut on the leg of its unsuspecting prey, and this intruder will find it much more difficult to evade capture!

'Let me make a few more, and... all right. I will give you these three traps. Set them in the vicinity of those footprints you found, and we will see if this unwelcome intruder strays into our trap! Use up the bundle of traps and return to me.''Set those three traps near where you found those footprints, ${PLAYER}. We will catch this intruder with one of them, then we will see what she has to say for herself! Use up the bundle of traps and come back here.''You set the traps? Good. We do not want anyone sneaking around who should not be here.

'I wonder if that was enough traps? I may see if your Ranger friends will help me collect more avanc-jaws.'Mair has asked you to challenge some of the Falcon-clan's best fighters for the purpose of training.Mostun and Gaenor are somewhere in the village of Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras.

Mair wants you to challenge two masters of the fighting arts in Tûr Morva, so that they may learn from your fighting skills.Find Mostun and challenge him to combatFind Gaenor and challenge her to combatMair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras.

You have defeated both Mostun and Gaenor, and the pair have learned some of your fighting skills.Talk to Mair in Tûr Morva'There may be value in the martial training that you can provide us, ${PLAYER}. I want you to challenge some of our most experienced fighters, masters in the martial arts, so that they may learn from you the skills of the North.

'Look for Mostun, Gaenor, and Kenned in Tûr Morva and fight with each of them. They will learn your skills.'

Mair looks thoughtful for a moment.

'Actually, fight only Mostun and Gaenor. Kenned has not been seen for some days. I think he may be out on a hunt.''Thank you for sparring with Mostun and Gaenor, ${PLAYER}. I have heard that they are both a-chatter with excitement about your northern fighting skills. They will refine those arts and perhaps become even more deadly than before.

'You have already become a great help to the Falcon-clan! Let Saruman tremble!''Look for Mostun and Gaenor in Tûr Morva and challenge both of them to combat so they may learn some of your fighting skills. I would have you fight Kenned as well, but he has not returned from his hunt yet, so those other two will have to be enough.''Let us see what you can teach me about combat, ${PLAYER}. I doubt there is anything in the North that we have not seen in Dunland.''What is there that you can show me that I have not already seen? Well, let us find out. Prepare yourself!'Mair has asked you to teach the warriors of the Falcon-clan fighting skills from the North.Yevan, Olwen, and Wundod can be found in Tûr Morva.

Mair has challenged you to defeat one of the youthful fighters of the Falcon-clan in combat.Find and challenge Yevan, Olwen, or WundodMair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva in Tâl Methedras.

You have easily defeated a youthful fighter of the Falcon-clan and should return to Mair.Talk to Mair in Tûr MorvaSors, Eiviona, and Owein can be found somewhere in Tûr Morva.

Mair has challenged you to defeat one of the more accomplished fighters of the Falcon-clan in Tûr Morva.Find and challenge Sors,  Eiviona, or OweinMair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva in Tâl Methedras.

You have defeated an experienced fighter of the Falcon-clan and should return to Mair.Talk to Mair in Tûr Morva'Many clans have joined with Saruman, ${PLAYER}, and the Hebog-lûth may need to face them before it is all over. We need every advantage we can get, and my father the Brenin thinks that you and your Ranger friends are just such an advantage.'

Mair assesses you shrewdly.

'I am not so certain. Are there any fighting skills in the North worth knowing? Find some of our most youthful fighters and challenge them to combat. That will tell me if my father is right to think so highly of your skills. I speak of Yevan, Olwen, or Wundod. If you cannot defeat any of those youths in combat, you have nothing to teach us.''Your defeat of the youth proves little, ${PLAYER}, but it does prove this: you have some small skill in combat. More than one of our unskilled youths, at the least.'

Mair studies you appraisingly.

'How will you handle one of our more experienced fighters, I wonder? Seek out and challenge Sors, Eiviona, or Owein here in Tûr Morva. They will be more of a challenge, I trust.''Well now, perhaps you do have things to teach us in the ways of combat. I am listening.''Defeating Yevan, Olwen, or Wundod will tell me if my father is right to believe that you have anything to teach us in the ways of warfare. They are youthful and inexperienced.''Can you defeat one of our more experienced fighters? Seek out and challenge Sors, Eiviona, or Owein, here in Tûr Morva. They will be more of a challenge, I trust.''I am no fighter, I am a singer of songs! I am not the Olwen you want! You are looking for my sister, I think. She is outside our home, to the north, near Penrod.

'Do not worry, it happens a lot. I do not know what Mother was thinking.''Mair expects us to fight? I am not afraid of you! I will show you the strength of the Hebog-lûth, though I be but a fledgling in the art of combat!''Do you think that you can defeat me? I have seen service in war, Duvodiad. I am not a fresh-faced youngling untested by combat. Prepare yourself!'Dúrchest commands the Guard of Barad Guldur, defending his master from the assaults of his enemies.Defeat Dúrchest after defeating several of his personal guardsWynfor has seen someone sneaking around the far shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras and wants you to investigate.There may be footprints on the far side of the lake, and there certainly are avanc.

Wynfor wants you to look for footprints on the far side of the lake in Tâl Methedras. He also wants you to slay avanc and bring him their jaws.Find a set of footprints on the western shore of the lake, north-west of the eyotFind a set of footprints beneath the rocky cliffs west of the western shoreCollect avanc-jaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wynfor is at Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras.

You have scouted the far shore of the lake for footprints and have also collected the jaws of the avanc that live there. You should bring them to Wynfor as he requested.'I do not like it, ${PLAYER}. Someone has been sneaking around the far shore of the lake under cover of night. It is not one of my people, and I do not think it is one of yours, either.

'I am not as spry as I was when I was young. I cannot track this unwelcome guest, but perhaps you can. Go to the far shore of the lake and look for the footprints of this intruder. That may tell me something I can use.

'Kill the avanc while you are there and bring me their jaws. I have an idea.''Someone has been creeping around on the far side of the lake under cover of night. I do not like it. Search for this intruder's footprints while you are out there. They may tell me something useful.

'Slay avanc on the lakeside and bring me their jaws, too. I have a notion that I will be wanting them.''That was fast. Did you really find any sign of the intruder I saw?'

Wynfor listens as you describe the footprints you found on the far shore of the lake. He nods.

'Those sound like women's feet, ${PLAYER}. Some woman is creeping around in the dark, and she does not want to be found. If she is not one of ours, and she is not one of yours, then she is an enemy.

'Hand me those avanc-jaws.'Seren is the mother of Anirin, the messenger you met in Enedwaith and rescued from Lhaid Ogo. She wants news of her son brought to those who love him.Wenda's home is down the hill to the south of Seren, in Tûr Morva.

Seren wants you to bring news of her son Anirin to his beloved Wenda.Talk to Wenda in Tûr MorvaSeren is in Tûr Morva.

You have given tidings of Anirin to his beloved, and Wenda now wants you to return to Seren with her thanks.Talk to Seren in Tûr MorvaPenrod is among the northern buildings in Tûr Morva.

Penrod wishes to speak with you.Talk to Penrod in Tûr Morva'A moment, if you would, Duvodiad. You have come from the lands of the Algraig, from Lhanuch? Did you see a young man there named Anirin?'

You tell her that you did encounter such a man, rescuing him from peril in the depths of the cave called Lhaid Ogo.

'My son! My Anirin! Thank the spirits! Oh, ${PLAYER}, you must give me any word of him you have.'

You tell her that he seemed to be doing fine and planned to return to Tûr Morva once he recovered from the experience.

'Thank you for these tidings! You must bring them to his beloved, to whom he is promised. Her name is Wenda, and her home is down the hill to the south.''My son is promised to Wenda, who lives down the hill to the south. She will want to hear any news of him you can give her!''You have news of Anirin?'

You tell her about your encounter with Anirin in the depths of Lhaid Ogo, in Enedwaith, and she seems relieved to hear he plans to return soon.

'I told him not to go, but he could not be persuaded. Anirin is stubborn! He gets that from his mother.

'Thank you for saving my beloved, ${PLAYER}. I am indebted to you, and when Anirin and I have married, our family will be indebted to you as well. It is our way.

'Return to Seren and thank her for sending you to me.''Return to Seren and thank her for thinking of me. I will be glad when Anirin is safely returned, but any news of him makes my day brighter.''Wenda is such a nice girl. She did not want Anirin to bring Lheu Brenin's message to the Algraig, but he saw the need and could not be dissuaded.

'Have you met Penrod, the Brenin's first Brehur? He is among the northern buildings of Tûr Morva. He was looking for you.''Penrod wanted to speak with you. Look for him among the buildings to the north.''I saw you speaking with Anirin's family. It was a difficult decision for him to make, to be the bearer of Lheu Brenin's message north to the Algraig, but he knew its importance. He is swift; it is one of the reasons the Brenin tasked him with that journey. He will be back with his mother and with Wenda soon enough.'Among Barad Guldur's most powerful captains are the wraiths Morgaraf and Cargaraf.Defeat Morgaraf and Cargaraf at Barad Guldur within 10 seconds of each otherThe cart's wheel is damaged and broken. For Andras to continue on, a new one will need to be found.The camp of the Dragon-clan raiders to the east may be a place to find new wheel.

A new wheel for the cart must be found before it can continue on.Find a new wheel for the cartThe broken wheel is at Andras' cart on the road in northern Starkmoor.

Now that you have found a new wheel you should replace the old broken one.The wheel is damaged and broken. It does not look like it is possible to repair it here on the road. If Andras is to continue on, a new wheel must be found. 

The Dragon-clan camp to the east would be a good place to start looking for a new wheel.The more you look at this wheel, the more convinced you become that its only future use will be as fire-wood.With a tug and a jolt, the old wheel comes off. The new one slides on with ease. It is not the sturdiest wheel you have handled, but it should last the short trip to the next town.The bag was filled with bandages soaked in healing salves, items that would fetch decent coin at auction.The bandages were taken by raiders from the Dragon-clan who have a camp in the ruins to the east of the cart.

You should recover the stolen bandages.Collect bandages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The shredded bag the bandages belong in is at Andras' cart in the north of Starkmoor.

The bandages should be placed back inside the bag they originally came from.The bag is mostly empty, but a few of the bandages it once held remain. They are soft and damp to the touch. Your skin feels soothed when your fingers glide over them. No doubt these bandages are very valuable, and the Dragon-clan raiders would have taken them.There is no doubt that these bandages would catch a hefty price at auction.You place the bandages back into the bag from which they originally came. While the bag is not quite full, the majority of them have been returned.The crate is filled with shattered pieces of pottery. The pieces indicate that several pots are missing.The pottery missing from the crate must have been taken into the hills to the east by the Dragon-clan raiders.

You should recover the missing pottery.Collect pots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The crate to safely transport the remaining pots is at Andras' cart on the northern road of Starkmoor.

The pots should be returned to the crate from which they were stolen.The crate is filled with shattered pieces of pottery. The pieces indicate that several pots are missing. The quality of the smashed ones is very high, and the pattern is foreign to Dunland. If any remain they would bring a good price at auction.The paint and patterns on the pottery are striking in their beauty; however, they are clearly not Dunlending in design.After removing the smashed pieces, the pots easily fit within the crate. They may bounce a little during the ride, but they should make it intact.The ledger's pages detailed the items at Andras' estate that are ready for auction: a very important list for a man in desperate need of money.The missing pages of the ledger have been taken by the Dragon-clan raiders in the hills to the east of the broken caravan.

You should recover the missing pages of Andras' ledger.Collect ledger-pages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The ledger is with Andras' belongings in his caravan on the northern road in Starkmoor.

The pages should be placed back within the ledger.Most of the pages of this ledger have been ripped out and taken. The few remaining pages appear to detail crop amounts and various household items. This is most likely an accounting of all goods Andras has at his homestead.

The missing pages are vital if he is to put together a respectable auction. The Dragon-clan raiders must have taken the pages with them.It would take much more time than Andras has to reassemble this ledger from scratch. The pages must be found and returned.The pages fit back within the ledger, and it closes smoothly. Care will need to be taken to make sure they do not fly out, but at least they have all been returned.Nona has agreed to accompany you on your information-gathering journey through Dunland for Lheu Brenin.Nona is by the farmhouse in the north-western reaches of Starkmoor.

Nona has agreed to meet you in the Starkmoor to scout for the information Lheu Brenin needs.Talk to Nona in the StarkmoorThere is a farmhouse in the north-western corner of the Starkmoor.

Nona wants you to scout the farmhouse atop the slope to the west to see if it is held by those loyal to Saruman.Scout the farmhouse atop the north-western hillScout the sheep-enclosureScout the planted fieldNona is by the farmland in the north-western reaches of the Starkmoor.

You scouted the farmland in the north-western Starkmoor and should speak with Nona.Talk to Nona in the Starkmoor'Danger seems to follow you wherever you go, ${PLAYER}. I like that. I will be Wadu's Ghost and defeat the true enemies of Dunland: faithless clans who swear loyalty to Saruman.

'The land to the west is called the Starkmoor. You say that Lheu Brenin wished to know the state of its herds? There are many herd-animals in the Starkmoor, and he who controls them will have much food production close at hand. Enough for an army? Aye.

'There is a farmhouse in the north-west corner of the Starkmoor, among the hills. I have seen it from afar. I will meet you there, and we can scout for the information Lheu Brenin desires to know.''I will meet you in the Starkmoor, ${PLAYER}, by the large farm in the north-western reaches. Then we will scout the state of the herds for Lheu Brenin.''The herds of the Starkmoor feed many of the clans of Dunland. If this farmland is held by those loyal to Saruman, he will have a source of food for his armies, but can also starve those who oppose him.

'Go up to the farmhouse at the top of the slope to the west and see how things stand, ${PLAYER}. You should also scout some of the fields and enclosures nearby, to the west.''The farmhouse to the west may be held by those loyal to Saruman. You should investigate and see if it be so.''I think this is what Lheu Brenin feared, ${PLAYER}. The farms of the Starkmoor are not held by friendly clansmen any longer.

'The main trading settlement to the south may be similar, but we will not know it without going there.'The great Dunlending camp of Wulf's Cleft lies to the south of Avardin and the Starkmoor.Bedwur is in Avardin in the central Starkmoor.

Bedwur has asked you to travel to an overlook of Wulf's Cleft and destroy whoever comes to find you.Talk to Bedwur to raid the outpost outside the Wulf's Cleft encampmentBedwur is in Avardin in the central Starkmoor.

Bedwur will be pleased to hear you have secured a large profit for him from the forces at Wulf's Cleft.Talk to Bedwur in AvardinEva is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor.

Eva may have knowledge of where the boy has gone.Talk to Eva in Avardin'There is one last thing you must do for me, then I will consider Mabon's debt paid, and he will be free. If you fail me now, I will sell the boy off to the mines.

'To the south of Starkmoor is Wulf's Cleft. The armies of Dunland have been gathering and training there. I often sell them weapons, armour, and slaves for training practice. Lately, the sales have been slowing. You are going to fix that for me.

'There is a cliff to the south that overlooks Wulf's Cleft. Once there, I want you to do as much injury as possible. The more weapons and armour you destroy, the more I can sell the warriors tomorrow. Speak with me when you are ready to go, and I will show you the path.''You are looking for Mabon? I do not know where he went, but I have my suspicions.''Make sure you do as much damage as possible. I have a fresh set of conscripts and weapons ready to sell.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>The stables of Avardin have been in turmoil as of late. Lack of money, supplies, and storms have all contributed to the stables being shuttered.Hay can be found to the east of Avardin.

Levelha has asked you to collect hay for the horses.Collect stalks of hay (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Levelha is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor.

Levelha will be pleased to see you have brought the hay back.'The stable-boy is returning, which pleases me. It means that we have a chance to renew the stable's business. The next step is obtain supplies for the horses.

'The boy will take care of getting everything straightened back up. I dare not send him into the fields to gather more supplies, though, and we are in desperate need of hay. Yes, there are no horses to feed, but without food you cannot have any horses.

'The fields of the moors to the east have some hay-stalks in them that were not gathered for harvest. If you can bring several of them back, then the only thing left to do will be to get the actual horses.''You can find the hay to the east of here.''This will do perfectly. Now, to find ourselves some horses!'Andras is not the only one who wishes to obtain valuables from his homestead.Mabon is just east of the homestead in the northern Starkmoor.

Mabon needs your help to drive the raiders out of his father's homestead and protect the valuables within.Aid Mabon in searching the homesteadMabon is just east of the Homestead in the northern Starkmoor.

Mabon will want to speak with you about the raid.Talk to Mabon at Andras' homestead'If we are to recover anything from the homestead, we must move quickly. A group of Dragon-clan raiders just passed by here. They must have copied down some of the items from the ledger before you recovered all of the pages.

'This homestead is all my family has. I beg you to help me save it.''If I could, I would do this myself. Please, help me save our land!''I thank you for all of your help. I do not know who those men were, but it is clear that they knew my father and were friends. I am very glad for that.'The great Dunlending camp of Wulf's Cleft lies to the south of Avardin and the Starkmoor.Bedwur instructed you to inflict as much damage as possible upon the army at Wulf's Cleft.Defeat Dunlendings at Wulf's CleftAndras is not the only one who wishes to obtain valuables from his homestead.Speak with Mabon at Andras' homestead.Talk to Mabon at Andras' homesteadDefeat the Dragon-clan raiders at Andras' homestead.Defeat the Dragon-clan raiders at Andras' homesteadSpeak with Mabon at Andras' homestead.Talk to Mabon at Andras' homesteadDefend Mabon from the Dragon-clan raiders.Defend Mabon at Andras' homesteadSpeak with Mabon at Andras' homestead.Talk to Mabon at Andras' homesteadDefend Andras' homestead from the Dragon-clan raiders.Defend Andras' homesteadSpeak with the Dunlendings at Andras' homestead.Talk to the Dunlendings at Andras' farmstead'Thank you for helping me to defend our home.''My father gave you the ledger? Let us head up the hill then and see what we can find.''Where did they come from? I hope we do not meet any more. The homestead is just up the hill.''You are very powerful. I am glad that my dad sent you here. It is just a little further up the hill.'The strange warrior says to Mabon:

'The Boar-clan remembers those who aid us, and we honour our friendships. Not long ago, your father helped us in a time of need. When you are in trouble Mabon, we will always be there for you.'

To you, he says:

'You are kind to aid this boy, duvodiad... kindness is a dying virtue in these lands.'Merchants of the Ox-clan gather frequently for auctions, where large amounts of goods -- and money -- trade hands.Many merchants have gathered here tonight.Talk to BedwurMany merchants have gathered here tonight.Observe the auctionMany merchants have gathered here tonight.Talk to Bedwur'The boy will pay his father's debt. Whether through the war-camps or the mines, I will get what is owed to me.''I see that you are all here... and, I assume, ready to begin. Andras even brought his boy with him. I hope his wares fetch a price that is not embarrassing.

'Shall we begin then?''It is commendable that you wish to aid the boy, but I must finish the other lots before we can discuss an arrangement.'Of the Nazgûl, the Lieutenant of Dol Guldur is second in power only to the Witch-king himself. After escaping the wrath of the Bruinen and the arrows of the Elf-prince Legolas, he has returned to the fortress of Dol Guldur....Defeat the Lieutenant of Dol Guldur before defeating his fell-beast mountBedwur is feeling cheated by Saruman the White and wishes some retribution.The caravan to Wulf's Cleft is travelling the southern road out of Avardin.

Bedwur asked you to raid the caravan heading to Wulf's Cleft and return to him the goods he sold to Saruman.Collect goods (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bedwur is in Avardin in the central Starkmoor.

Bedwur will want to receive the goods so he can ready them for the next auction.'Saruman cheated me out of much money with this last auction. You cannot go against the Wizard... once he names his price, the purchase is finished, whether it is fair or not. At the end of the day, however, I will always get paid.

'The goods he purchased are travelling by caravan south to Wulf's Cleft. I do not know whether they plan to stay there or head further to Isengard, but I do know they will not make it. You will intercept them before they reach the camp.

'Head south and follow the road. When you find them, be quick about it. They are evil men and do not deserve any quarter. Bring back the goods you find there. Once this is done, there is only one more task I will require of you before the boy will be considered free of his debt.''Saruman will not suspect anything other than Dragon or Boar-clan raiders, and I will be able to turn a better profit.''Very good! It appears that my goods survived both the trip and the battle in good condition. With these returned, I can now obtain the profit that Saruman denied me.'Warg-teeth necklaces are highly valued as a symbol of strength in battle and power among the Dunlending clans.Hormgrat can be found at the Hound's Rest to the east of Avardin.

Cadvan asked you to get him a tooth from the most powerful Warg on the rock to the east.Collect Hormgrat's toothCadvan is in Avardin in the central Starkmoor.

Cadvan will be eager to place the Warg's tooth into the necklace.'You are looking for more sellers for the auction? I have a necklace which I am nearly done with and almost ready to sell. It is crafted of Warg-teeth. Dunlendings who wear them are powerful and demand respect from all around them, whether they retrieved the teeth themselves or not.

'There is one last tooth which I need to finish this necklace, then it will be ready for sale. On the rock to the east is a powerful Warg, larger than the rest, called Hormgrat. His tooth shall be the centrepiece of this necklace. Bring it to me, and I shall sell in your auction.''No other tooth shall do. It must be that of the most powerful Warg on the rock. With that, I can command any price I wish.''With this, my necklace will be noticed by everyone. You will command respect and power when you wear it. I will come to your auction.'Keeping your cattle alive long enough to be worth slaughtering is a struggle with hungry Wargs roaming the plains.Stones can be found around the Warg-rock to the east of Avardin.

Eva asked you to collect rocks from around the Warg-rock so she can build an enclosure for cattle.Collect stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eva is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor.

Eva will be eager to use the stones you found to begin building an enclosure.'An auction, you say? I wish to trade cattle. I have saved enough to buy many tags, and my uncle is willing to give me several head from his herd. I have the land for them to graze on, but not the means to keep them safe.

'If you are venturing to the great rock to the east, you will find several smaller stones around it. With enough of them, I could build an enclosure around my land to keep my cattle safe. If you bring me the stones, I will attend the auction.''A dead, young cow is worth nothing, a dead cow in his prime, however, is worth a great deal. The trick is keeping them alive long enough to make them worth killing.''With these, I can make an enclosure that will keep my livestock safe. I will attend your auction.'The Wargs to the east have devastated the local cattle population, and Folant seeks to rectify the Warg-problem before he will attend the auction.Wargs can be found to the east of Avardin in the Starkmoor.

You should go to Hound's Rest and defeat Wargs.Defeat Wargs at the Hound's Rest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Folant is in Avardin in the central Starkmoor.

Folant will be pleased to hear that the Warg-population has been thinned.Talk to Folant in Avardin'You are preparing an auction? Yes, I am interested. I am in need of cattle, for I sold my last ones to the war-effort. I made a decent profit, but I fear I sold too many. The Warg-packs to the east devoured the few I had left.

'I am willing to buy more, but not until I know my investment is safe and secure. If you were to head into the hills east of here, to the rock the Wargs call home, and thin their numbers, I will consider coming to the auction to buy cattle.''I can tell from the stench upon you that you have been fighting Wargs, and given that you are standing here, I assume you were victorious. I will attend the auction.''The Wargs are not good for business. I will not attend while there are so many wandering the hills.'Due to limited grazing grounds, cattle are a controlled and regulated resource.Tags can be found on dead cattle around the rock to the east of Avardin.

Hevina asked you to collect tags off the dead cattle around the Warg-rock.Collect cattle-tags (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hevina is in Avardin in the central Starkmoor.

Hevina will be pleased to get her cattle tags back.'Herding is the fastest way to make money here in Avardin, presuming you have the right connexions and enough money to start with. The clan tightly controls who can have cattle and how many. There are tags that are sold and attached to the animals. If any animal is found without a tag, it is brought to auction, and Bedwur keeps whatever the profit is. He is also the one who sells the tags.

'I had a herd of cattle that strayed too far to the east, and many were devoured by the Wargs. I have sold the herdsmen to the mines to regain some of my losses, but now I need enough to get started again. If you can get me the tags from my dead cattle, I will sell them at auction. They can be found around the rock to the east.''Those tags are often worth more than the cattle that they are placed upon.''Yes, these were indeed mine. They should bring a good price. I will attend your auction.'Auctions are held frequently in Avardin, but only when enough merchants commit to attending.Merchants can be found around Avardin, in the central Starkmoor.

There are several merchants within Avardin that may be willing to attend the auction.Convince Folant to join the auctionConvince Cadvan to join the auctionConvince Hevina to join the auctionConvince Eva to join the auctionBedwur is in Avardin in the central area of the Starkmoor.

Bedwur will be pleased to hear that you found several merchants committed to participating in the auction.Talk to Bedwur in Avardin'I am more than willing to help out; however, auctions are very time-consuming, and I have a reputation to maintain. I need assurances that there will be enough merchants in attendance to make it worth my time.

'If you can convince several of the other merchants around Avardin to participate, then I will consider putting together an auction for you. But I caution you: do not waste my time. There is very little I tolerate less than someone wasting my money.''So, the merchants are all willing to come to the auction? It appears this may be my most profitable auction yet, then.''I will not waste my time unless I know that there will be enough people involved to turn a tidy profit.'The stables of Avardin have been in turmoil as of late. Lack of money, supplies, and storms have all contributed to the stables being shuttered.Horses can be found in the fields surrounding Avardin.

Levelha asked you to find and ride back several horses.Ride horses back to Avardin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Levelha is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor.

Levelha will be pleased to hear that you have brought him several horses.Talk to Levelha in Avardin'Not long after the boy left, we had a terrible storm. The lightning frightened the horses, and they bolted, knocking the gates down and fleeing into the plains.

'Now is the time to gather the horses back up. They are prone to flight, and you will need to ride them back in if you want them to get here in time.

'You can find them all over the moors, grazing. We should not need more than a few to get back up and running.''This is wonderful. Now that we have horses, I can renew the stable's business. Is there anywhere you would like to go?''We only need a few horses to renew the stable. Bring them back in quick, though.'Andras' caravan has been attacked by Dragon-clan raiders. All of his valuables have been taken. They must be reclaimed if he is to make it to auction successfully.The scattered pieces of Andras' caravan are on the northern road in Starkmoor.

Andras asked you to judge the state of the caravan and retrieve whatever goods you can from the Dragon-clan raiders encamped to the east.Aid Andras with The Broken WheelAid Andras with The Shredded BagAid Andras with The Smashed CrateAid Andras with The Torn LedgerAndras is on the northern road leading out of Starkmoor.

Andras will be pleased to hear that his cart has been repaired and most of his goods returned.Talk to Andras in the Starkmoor'I do not have anything left, I swear! The raiders before you took it all, please do not hurt me! Wait... you do not have the look of rival clansmen.

'My name is Andras. I was taking this caravan to Avardin for the upcoming auction when I was beset by the Dragon-clan. They are an evil lot, and I suspect they answer to Isengard. Saruman is not the friend that he claims to be. There are few who can see through his tangled web of lies, and my clan, the People of the Ox, least of all, it seems. I seek to change that, but to do so, I must be in a position of power. Among the Ox-clan merchants that means money, which I had hoped to raise at the coming auction.

'Please, I ask your help. I have not yet had time to assess the damage to my caravan. If you could check my cart and goods, then venture out against the raiders, I would be grateful. They came from the hill to the east.''If we cannot get this caravan moving again with most of my goods, then I stand no chance to save my clan.''It is a strange day when a duvodiad has more kindness than clansmen you have known your entire life. A very strange day, indeed.'Andras has told you about his homestead in the north-west of the Starkmoor.Andras' homestead is in the north-west of the Starkmoor.

Andras asked you go to his homestead and give the ledger to his son.Talk to Andras' son at his farmstead'The things you helped recover will bring good coin at auction, but the raiders ensured that it will not be enough. I will need more if I am to make the kind of money needed to pay off my debts and ascend within the clan. Only then can I hope to sway them away from the Wizard's murmurings.

'I have a homestead, just west of here over the ridge. We farm and raise livestock. Take the ledger to my son. He should be able to show you where everything is and help you pack it all up.

'I am moving on to Avardin to the south. Come and find me there once everything is in order.''You say my father sent you? I hope you are skilled with a weapon. The Dragon-clan must have heard that he was gone, for they have begun to raid the farm. It was all that I could do to sneak down here unseen.'Merchants of the Ox-clan gather frequently for auctions, where large amounts of goods -- and money -- trade hands.Bedwur is at Avardin, central to the Starkmoor.

Bedwur is waiting for you to begin the auction.Attend the AuctionBedwur is at Avardin, central to the Starkmoor.

Bedwur will want to discuss the events of the Auction.Talk to Bedwur at Avardin'Everything is prepared, ${PLAYER}. You have secured enough merchants to attend the auction that I feel comfortable with how much this night will yield for me. I have gone through Andras' goods and believe that if he gets a fair value, he should be able to honour his debts, even after my share is paid.

'Speak with me when you are ready to attend the auction.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'It is always a pleasure to do business with Saruman of Many Colours, and always a mistake to challenge a Wizard.

'The debt is now the son's to bear and pay. He will work it off, beginning today.''Are you ready to begin?'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Avardin is run by Bedwur, a leader among the Ox-clan who runs the auctions and controls the local economy.Bedwur is in the centre of Avardin at the auction-platform.

Andras asked you to speak with Bedwur regarding the auction.Talk to Bedwur in Avardin'You have done much good work to help me, and I am very grateful for that, but I fear the most difficult parts are still ahead of us. Bedwur is the auctioneer here... he is the local leader of the Ox-clan, and a very powerful man. He is also as corrupt as they come, having long ago given his will to Saruman.

'Unfortunately, he is an evil I must deal with if I am to pay off my debts. Any transaction of noticeable size must go through his auction, and he happily takes a price from each lot.

'I need some time to take inventory and get everything cleaned and ready for sale. While I do that, you go talk with Bedwur and secure a position in the upcoming auction. You can find him near the centre of town by the auction-platform.''Bedwur will likely ask you to do some small tasks. I would be grateful if you could, while I prepare things here.''So, you represent Andras, do you, duvodiad? I hope he has brought something worth selling this time. I do not tolerate my time being spent and my money wasted.'Dunbog is an untamed swamp to the south-west of Avardin. Few live there by choice.Dunbog lies to the south-west of Starkmoor.

Eva told you of a terror in the swamps of Dunland who comes in the night and steals away orphans and lost children.Talk to someone in the Dunbog'Mabon is not the first child to disappear from these lands. For the past several months, nearly one vanishes per week from Avardin, mostly orphans. They disappear in the night...naught but a few tracks heading to the south-west are ever seen.

'Those who have caught a glimpse tell of a horrible creature, an abomination of nature, striding across the plains with a bag over his shoulder, filled with lost children.

'If you wish to find this boy you must venture to the swamps. Head south-west along the roads until you find Dunbog. They may know more of this abomination there.''What do you want here?''If that creature did take him, I would not hold much hope.'Mabon has marked up the ledger that you brought with notes about what is important and may still be found around the homestead.The items on the ledger may be found throughout Andras' homestead.

