The final page of the ledger speaks of the chicken coops and the amount of eggs the homestead produces daily.Collect chicken eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The final page of the ledger details the schedule of the chicken coop and the laying of their eggs. If they have not been destroyed, at least a good handful should be ready for the taking.The stables of Avardin have been in turmoil as of late. A lack of money, supplies, and storms have all contributed to the stables being shuttered.Ianto is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor.

Levelha asked you to speak to Ianto and convince him to return to work.Talk to Ianto in AvardinLevelha is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor.

Levelha will be pleased to hear Ianto is returning to work.Talk to Levelha in Avardin'A week ago, I had a fully running stable here. You may have noticed that we do not have any horses here anymore. I suppose that is well because I do not have anything to feed them. I also do not have anyone to take care of them.

'My stable-boy left, because his father was taken to Wulf's Cleft to serve the army. The boy ran off to work the fields and scavenge the Moor to provide for his mother and siblings. Had he stopped and talked to me, I would have helped however I could.

'I believe the boy is here in Avardin. Please find him and let him know that I will provide for his family. Once he returns, we can work on the rest of the stable.''Levelha says he will pay me enough to take care of mam and my brothers and sisters? Of course, I will go back then. I should have asked him to begin with.''With the boy returning, I can now turn my attention to the stable.''Over the years, I have had many stable-boys. Ianto is the best I have had. I cannot keep this stable running without him.'The Pit in the Starkmoor serves as a proving ground for conscripts. Those strong enough to withstand it join the army in Wulf's Cleft; those too weak are sent to dig in the mines.The banner is on the arena floor at Avardin in the Starkmoor.

