You should sneak to the camp, crouch in some undergrowth nearby, and perform tricks to try to frighten away the men.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest uses emotes. You must target the intended recipient of the emote in order for quest emotes to work.</rgb>Noriel has retreated to the Elf-ruins of Haldirith in Thinglad, at the centre of the forest, upon a hill.

You should speak with Noriel.Find the Elf-outpost of Haldirith'The Rohirrim have always believed our kind are evil, and that Lothlórien is a haunted place. We feel that this is not entirely a bad belief for them to hold, as it will frighten them away from our borders.

'I had the idea that you could crouch hidden near their camp and make strange noises to frighten the fishermen away. Hopefully, we will not need to resort to more force than simple manipulation.''I think it is much better if the Rohirrim find these lands haunted; do you not agree? They will not disturb us again for two, maybe three generations. Then perhaps we will have to frighten them away once more.'Renfaer has asked you to deliver Noriel's gift for the departing Rohirrim of Stangard.Wynmar and his men are at their new temporary camp on the southern river-bank of Thinglad.

You should bring the hides to Wynmar as a final parting gift, a token of good will from the Elves.'Here are the hides that you gathered -- and now they should go to their proper home: the Rohirrim from Stangard. They have made camp at the bottom of the wood along the river before they make the remainder of their journey home.

'You should bring them this gift from the Elves before they depart for good, for this will be our last chance to make contact with the trespassers.''Hail, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for this gift... but tell me: is this from Noriel? How does she fare? What can you tell me about her? Do you think she would agree to see me again?'Wynmar was killed in the clash with the Orcs, and now, too late, Noriel feels for the Man who loved her.Wynmar's resting place lies a short distance south of the hunters' camp-site.

You should find Wynmar's gravesite to pay your last respects to a bold and kind man.Find the site of Wynmar's grave to pay your respectsNoriel is at Wynmar's grave.

You should find out why Noriel lingers here.Ask Noriel why she lingersWynmar's grave is upon the hilltop in the south of Thinglad.

You should pay your respects at Wynmar's grave.Pay your respects to Wynmar with a moment of silenceNoriel lingers at Wynmar's grave.

You should speak with Noriel, now that you have paid your respects.Talk to Noriel'Alas for Wynmar. The Elves bore his body away after the fight and made him a grave between here and Stangard, his true home. He will rest in both lands: land of his home and land of his heart.

'If you wish to pay your respects, you can find him a short distance south of here.

'Your help will not be forgotten, nor will we forget our good leader on this fruitless expedition. Go well, ${PLAYER}.''${PLAYER}, I have lived many years, but in all my years I have failed to acquire wisdom. I thought it would be best to push this foolish mortal away, but... in truth, I felt it too.

'Their lives are but a heart beat of my own, even if they survive all the battles in the world; I wasted that heart beat.

'How keenly I feel it.''I should have been more welcoming to these Men and not so cold to this one in particular. Hopefully, I will not be so unyielding in the future.

'The Rohirrim will never welcome the Elves of Lórien, but I would like to help them from afar nonetheless. Will you go to them, ${PLAYER}, and see what need drove the folk so near the place they feared?

'I wish to find ways to help these folk whilst they linger at our borders. They are perhaps not so bad as we once thought....'Noriel wants to help you search for the missing Rohirrim hunter to speed along the intruding party's departure from Thinglad.

<rgb=#FF0000>Use the whistle to summon Noriel to your side if you become separated.</rgb>Signs of the missing hunter can likely be found north-east of the hunters' camp in Thinglad.

You should search the woods around the camp for signs of the missing hunter's passage or indications of where he might have gone.Search the forest floor for signs of the missing hunterNoriel is nearby and can be summoned by whistle if you have become separated.

You should speak with Noriel, your companion on this mission.Talk to NorielAnother sign of the missing hunter looks to be not far from the first in Thinglad, just south of that spot.

You should search the woods around the camp for signs of the missing hunter's passage or indications of where he might have gone.Search for another sign of the missing hunterNoriel is nearby and can be summoned by whistle if you have become separated.

You should speak with Noriel, your companion on this mission.Talk to NorielSigns of the missing hunter can be found near the hunters' camp in Thinglad.

You should search the woods around the camp for signs of the missing hunter's passage, or indications of where he might have gone.Search for signs of the missing hunterNoriel is nearby and can be summoned by whistle if you have become separated.

You should speak with Noriel, your companion on this mission.Talk to NorielThe missing hunter is surely nearby, south and east of the hunter's camp in Thinglad.

You should search for the missing hunter.Search for the missing hunterNoriel can be summoned by using the Elf-whistle you were given.

You should speak with Noriel.'I cannot banish those men from Thinglad without their missing friend. You should search the wood for him and return him to his companions. Here is a whistle -- use this when you find his tracks, and I will join you.

'Hopefully we can finish this task soon, then Thinglad can have some peace again from these unwelcome intruders.''Dunstan went north-east as he went off to hunt. I would begin my search in that direction, if I were you.

'If you find him, we will leave as the Elves wish it. My men do not like this forest anyway... we can sense the nearness of the evil Golden Wood. We are eager to leave this land.''Good hunting, ${PLAYER}. I hope you find Dunstan whole and hale.''Perhaps the hunter shot at some game and gave chase... or something startled or frightened him, and he loosed arrows. The tracks seem to go south... so let us follow them and see.''More arrows... and blood! The arrows hit their mark this time. And look: the hoof-prints of the horse go in one direction and the footprints another. A strange gait to the footprints, heading south-east -- let us follow them further!''The hunter's own bow! ${PLAYER}... I think the hunter was the hunted. Someone was shooting at him, and I think he was struck by many arrows as he chased his ambushers. I do not like this one bit. Ready yourself, my friend....'This brave hunter has been pierced by many unfriendly arrows and perished upon this hilltop in pursuit of his attackers.'I do not like the looks of this. Investigate him further, if you would; I must go scout this area.'Renfaer has asked you to collect hides as a parting gift of good will towards the Men of Stangard, on behalf of Noriel.Hides can be found on the bears and deer of Thinglad.

You should collect hides from beasts you encounter to use as a gift for the Rohirrim.Collect hides from beasts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Renfaer is near the centre of Thinglad.

You should bring the hides you gathered to Renfaer.'Though the Men of Stangard are not allowed in these woods, their trespass has caused no lasting harm. I wish to make them a gift of neighbourly good will.

'Please gather hides from the beasts of the forests, so that the Rohirrim may craft clothes and blankets to ward against the cold.''Ah, thank you, ${PLAYER} -- you have done well, once again.

'These should make a suitable parting gift to the Rohirrim before they fulfill their banishment from Thinglad.'Wynmar wishes to make a gift of the flowers to fair Noriel, risking the displeasure of the Elves for overstaying his very temporary welcome in Thinglad territory.Wynmar is at the hunters' camp in Thinglad.

You should speak with Wynmar once more to help him with what seems to be a harmless wish: to look upon the object of his love one last time.Help Wynmar see Noriel one last time before his departureNinil is at Haldirith in Thinglad.

You should speak with Ninil.Talk to Ninil'I am stricken, ${PLAYER}. I have never seen a woman so fair or brave as Noriel, nor so cold. I know she wants me gone from these lands for good, but I do not think I shall ever smile again if I am not to see her one last time.

'Please, ${PLAYER} -- take me to their keep. The Elves' secret is already out, is it not? We know they are here, and we know not to disturb them.

'What harm could there be in saying farewell? We are close neighbours, after all. I merely wish to offer the good will of Stangard.''That Man was most smitten with Noriel, poor fellow. It is unfortunate that she has no interest in such attentions, especially from one who is not Elf-kind.

'I know his intentions were good, but I think you should not have brought him here. Noriel did not appear to like his romantic inclinations one bit.

'Poor man! I hope he recovers soon....''Will you really lead me there, my friend? This is wonderful! Do not let me keep you! Come, let us go!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is intended to be a single-player encounter, but up to two players may enter at a time. It is recommended that guests do not join if they have not reached this part of the story.</rgb>While fighting in the Dunbog, you came across a mud-covered object. It seems like a child's toy.Lhan Rhos is at the centre of the Dunbog.

You should return the toy to its owner.Find the owner of the toy in Lhan RhosWhile fighting in the Dunbog, you came across this mud-covered object. It seems like a child's toy... perhaps someone in Lhan Rhos will want it back.

You should return to the village and find the owner of the toy.'Who are you? Wait, you have found my toy! Thank you, thank you. May I have it please?

'I did not think I would ever find it. Did nasty beetles take it? They always steal our things. I hate them!'Maugan is preparing to defend the Pristine Glade against the onslaught of Saruman's forces.There are three guardposts throughout the Pristine Glade.

Maugan has asked you to go and check at each guardpost for any signs of Saruman's forces.Talk to Guard Ambras at the western guardpostTalk to Guard Cai at the eastern guardpostTalk to Guard Edrud at the southern guardpostMaugan awaits you at the Tree.

You should return immediately to Maugan and let him know that Saruman is attacking the Glade.Talk to Maugan at the Tree'The Elders wish to call Assembly? I cannot leave until I know that the Glade is safe. First, we need to make sure the borders are secure. 

'Saruman is constantly trying to discover what we have hidden here. We watch the edges of the Glade very carefully for any of his spies because if he finds out the true magic of this place, we fear that he will destroy the Tree. We found this craban and killed it but, I worry that it is one of the Wizard's.

'Go to each guardpost and check with the guards there, then report back to me with your findings.''What? Saruman has attacked? The Elders must be told! This is ill news. Go back to the Elders. Tell them that I, myself, will attend the Assembly.

'The Tree cannot be allowed to perish. I must reinforce the guards, then I will meet you in Lhan Rhos.

'Go. Hurry!''Secure the guardposts, ${PLAYER}, then return to me.'The Abominations have become a problem for the inhabitants of the Dunbog, and Blaire is concerned that Saruman will use them against the forces of good.The Abomination trolls can be found at Lhan Colvarn, north of the Boar-clan encampment.

Blaire has asked you to thin the ranks of the Abominations by defeating some of the trolls.Defeat Abomination trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Blaire is at the Boar-clan encampment, south of Lhan Colvarn.

You should return to Blaire with news of your success.Talk to Blaire at the Boar-clan encampment'Duvodiad, we need to strike at Lhan Colvarn and defeat as many of the Abominations as possible...can you do this? The time for war is on the horizon.

'If you are willing, go north into Lhan Colvarn and defeat as many of the trolls as you can, then return to me when you are done.''Impressive. The Elders were right to send you to me. I have spent a long time trying to convince them that we need to take action now, but they are stuck in their ways. They love this pile of mud too much for their own good.

'Perhaps we can convince them that change has to happen now if they are to survive this war.''Hurry to Lhan Colvarn and defeat the Abominations. We have no time to lose.'Since your prankish tactics worked so well to persuade the fishermen to leave, you have been asked to try the same ploy on the huntsmen from Stangard.The hunters' camp is a little to the north of Haldirith.

You should try to frighten Wynmar, the leader of the hunters' camp.Wait a few moments before trying again.Wait a few momentsThe hunters' camp is a little to the north of Haldirith.

You should try to frighten Wynmar, the leader of the hunters' camp.The Rohirrim leader of the hunters' camp is in the north-western woods of Thinglad.

Since your tactics are not working against this stubborn Rohirrim, you should try speaking with him instead of trying to frighten him away.Talk to the leader of the men at the hunters' campNoriel is at the Elf-outpost of Haldirith.

You should bring news of this twist in the plan to Noriel.Consult with Noriel at HaldirithWynmar is at his camp in Thinglad.

You should tell Wynmar to stay put while you and Noriel search for his missing friend.Tell Wynmar and his men to stay put'The ploy to frighten the fishermen worked rather well. I think we should use it again on the huntsmen and see if they scare as easily as their kinsmen.

'Try once more to make these woods look haunted, so that the rumours will follow these Men back to Stangard and weaken their desire to come here for another generation. Good luck -- and try not to be spotted by the hunters.''A ${RACE} and not a spirit? You wanted to frighten us off, and I see the edge of the Dwimordene's haunted wood nearby. Perhaps you see us as trespassers.

'We shall go, but only if you return our missing hunter to us. He has not been seen since daybreak, but would not have wandered far. Have you seen him?''You seem somewhat disconcerted, ${PLAYER}. Did your plan not go well? Was there trouble?'

Noriel listens gravely as you tell her of the stubborn hunter Wynmar, and his fearlessness in the face of concern for his missing companion.

'I see. Let me think a moment, my friend. They must leave, but I would not have them abandon their lost fellow.''You again? Why do you return, ${RACE}?'

Wynmar listens as you explain that he and his folk trespass in Thinglad, but the Elves wish to help them find their missing companion... on the condition that they do not wander from their camp.Elder Déin has agreed to call an Assembly of the Avanc-lûth.The hunters are encamped to the south-east of Lhan Rhos. The scouts are encamped to the north-east of Lhan Rhos. The Protectors of the Pristine Glade are encamped to the west of Lhan Rhos. Speak to Maugan under the tree.  He may need you to do additional work for him.

Elder Déin has asked you to gather the people of the Dunbog for Assembly.Call the scouts to AssemblyCall the hunters to AssemblyCall Maugan and the protectors to AssemblyThe Elders await your return at Lhan Rhos in the centre of the Dunbog.

Having called the people of Dunbog to Assembly, you should return to the village and speak with Elder Déin.Talk to Elder Déin in Lhan RhosTalk to Elder Dein'It is time to call the people together for Assembly. We must explain to them that the situation is dire, and the time for action is now.

'I want you to return to the hunters and the scouts and bring them back to Lhan Rhos. You also need to seek out the Protectors of the Pristine Glade to the west of the river. Speak to Maugan underneath the Great Tree. He may need to put his affairs in order before he will help you.

'We must go to war, but we will go to war as a united people!''It is time, ${PLAYER}...call the people of Lhan Rhos to the Assembly.''I understand that the Elders seek our presence.  But you must first help us here in the Glade before I can help the Elders.''Elder Déin sent you? I am glad that they have finally seen fit to do something. All of this endless waiting and time away from my family has been maddening.

'Tell Elder Déin that I will come, and if you see my wife, tell her as well.''The Elders sent you? Then this must be of grave importance. We will return to Lhan Rhos. 

'Thank you, fearsome hunter, for summoning us.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. You will be remembered always for everything you have done for the Dunbog, though I suspect your chapters are not yet fully written.

'The Assembly will take place tonight. Prepare yourself well.''You have represented yourself well.  Thank you.  We will talk more shortly.  For now, have this.'The avanc, to many beyond Dunland a mythical beast, serve as a staple for the people of the Dunbog.Avanc can be found throughout the Dunbog.

Harri has asked you to help him fight the mighty avanc.'One of your first tasks of the hunt will be to survive. I cannot teach you that, it is something you must learn on your own.

'Once you have mastered survival, we will hunt some avanc. A mighty beast, the avanc.

'We will need to collect as much of their meat, tails, and hide as possible, so try to be precise with your attacks! We go at once!''You did well, friend. I am impressed. Do all duvodiad fight as well as you? Actually, nevermind, I know the answer. They do not.

'We must find more suitable tasks for you then, since even the mighty avanc seems easy prey for you.'The hunters are very impressed with your work. You have earned the respect of the Avanc-lûth Elders, and they wish to speak with you about the plight of the Dunbog.Lhan Rhos is to the north-west of the hunters' camp.

Harri has asked you to return to the village of Lhan Rhos and speak with the Elders there.Talk to Elder Déin at Lhan Rhos'You have done much already for the People of the Avanc, and you have survived all of the challenges my men and I presented you. I am impressed.

'You may go and speak with the Elders. Tell them that you have my respect and gratitude. They will be able to help you more with the duvodiad you seek.''It is time that we spoke, ${PLAYER}. We have been keeping watch on you, and you have proven good to the Avanc-lûth. It is time that we spoke of some of the secrets of Dunbog.''You should speak with the Elders at Lhan Rhos.'The scouts of the Dunbog have tasked you with several gathering exercises. Nye specifically does not like you and has instructed you to do his task for him.Bog-reeds be found the north-east area of the Dunbog. Nye is also encamped in the north-east Dunbog.

Nye has intimidated you into fetching him more bog-reeds for bow-strings.'Well, well. Another duvodiad trying to please us. I am tired of your kind coming into our bog, thinking you can change the world with your mere presence. Well, it will not happen, but you can make my life easier, and I will let you live.

'Fetch me bog-reeds so I can string these bows. The reeds around here grow strong, like us. They are better than any other material out here.

'You doubt me? One more word and I will... never mind. Go gather reeds!''Well, you are not completely useless like the others I have seen come through here. Still, my life is no better, and the Elders will just send me out for more bow-strings tomorrow. Thank you for nothing, ${RACE}.

'Now get out of here before I decide to stop being nice.'You should help the people of the Starkmoor before moving south to meet Nona in the Dunbog.Nona is along the road that runs south out of the Starkmoor into the Dunbog, near a natural arch of stone.

Nona has asked you to help the people of the Starkmoor with their problems, especially at Avardin to the south, and to meet her by the road into the Dunbog when you are satisfied.Help the people of the Starkmoor as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Nona by the road into Dunbog'The people of the Starkmoor are on the tipping point, ${PLAYER}. If we can help its people, we may be able to deprive Saruman of the food he needs to feed his armies.

'Travel south to Avardin and help the people there and all throughout the Starkmoor. It may prove the difference in this region.

'Once you are satisfied that you have done all you can to help the people of the Starkmoor, I will meet you where the road passes from the Starkmoor to the Dunbog in the south by a great stone arch, and we will continue our journey together.''I am glad you are here. The Dunbog is just ahead.''Help the people of the Starkmoor as much as you can, ${PLAYER}, especially south of here, at Avardin. We must keep them from allying with Saruman if we can.

'Once you have helped them to your satisfaction, meet me by the road south into the Dunbog from the Starkmoor. There is a great stone arch over the road. That is where I will meet you.'You have come to the outskirts of the Dunbog on Lheu Brenin's information-gathering errand.A Dunlending-scout is by the large rocky outcropping that stands by the entrance to the Dunbog, and to the south-west of her is a small camp belonging to her people.Determine whether the scout by the rocky outcropping is friendlyScout the small camp of Dunlendings south-west of the rocky outcroppingNona is to the north of the rocky outcropping that marks the boundary between the Starkmoor and the Dunbog.

You have scouted the border of the Dunbog and should return to Nona.Talk to Nona in the Dunbog'Do you see the scout up ahead, by the large rocky outcropping? I do not know to what clan she belongs. Go see if she is friendly, ${PLAYER}. The people of the Dunbog keep to themselves, and I know little of them, but if Saruman has paid for their loyalty, they are already our enemies.''Scout ahead and see if that look-out is friendly to us. I know little of the Dunbog and do not know what we should expect.''These people are like my own, ${PLAYER}: they are outliers, on the edge of great danger but not given in to it. May they resist as well as my people have done!

'We must help the Avanc-lûth to stand against Saruman.'The Orc-attack upon the Rohirrim-camp is now imminent, but preparations will hopefully help this small group of hunters and fishermen survive the assault.Swords, spears, and barricades can be found around Wynmar's southern camp.

You should help the men of Stangard prepare for the imminent attack.Sharpen swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sharpen spears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Reinforce the camp's fortifications (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rothulf is at Wynmar's camp in the south of Thinglad.

You should tell Rothulf that you have assisted with preparations for the imminent Orc-attack.Return to Rothulf'Wynmar does not even stir! We must prepare now, with or without his say. He will stir enough when Orc-swords run him through.

'There is much to do...barricades to reinforce, and swords and spears to sharpen. We will be lucky to survive the night, even if we can manage to prepare....''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. With you here, I have hope...even with Wynmar in his bewitched state. And now we wait.''The Orc-attack is imminent. We must do what we can!'Noriel does not permit trapping in the forest of Thinglad and wants the Rohirrim traps removed.Traps can be found on the north-western edge of Thinglad's trees, set by the huntsmen of Stangard.

You should destroy the traps, for they are not permitted in the Elf-lands.Destroy forbidden traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Noriel is awaiting you in Thinglad's Elf-keep of Haldirith.

You should return to Noriel, now that you have destroyed the unlawfully-placed traps.Return to Noriel in Haldirith'The hunters must be dealt with now. Their traps cannot be permitted in this wood, for it is against our law.

'Please, go and destroy all the traps you find, good ${PLAYER}, as you did with the fishermen's nets. All creatures must die, but none should die locked in a cage or choked in a snare.

'I must warn you again, though... do not be seen.''The traps can be found in the northern parts of these woods. You should avoid being spotted by the hunters while you roam.''That was a good deed, ${PLAYER}. You have been helpful to our little watch-post here, though I am sure Thinglad is drear compared to the fair mallorns of Lórien.

'Nevertheless, I will defend this wood, though it lacks the beauty of the greater forest.'You have arrived at the eastern guardpost in time to defend it from attack.Boulders can be found near the roots of the Tree.

Guard Cai has asked you to move the boulders near the crebain so the Tree can help you defeat them.Defeat the craban-spies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Move the rocks to enlist the aid of the Old TreeGuard Cai is at the eastern guardpost of the Pristine Glade.

The craban-spies are redoubling their efforts. You should speak with Guard Cai again and find out what can be done to stop them.Talk to Guard Cai at the eastern guardpost'The crebain are everywhere. Saruman's spies! We need to rid the Glade of them; however, they fly too quickly and too high for us to kill them.

'The Tree will help defend itself. You must move the boulders blocking the Tree's roots. Move three rocks near one of the crebain, and the Tree should help you pull down one of the spies.  

'Hurry. Kill as many spies as you can find and return to me when the deed is done.''Move the rocks and boulders to elicit the aid of the Tree!''Well done, but the crebain will be back! Hurry quickly and make sure all of the guardposts are safe, then report back to Maugan!

'Saruman is here.'You have arrived at the southern guardpost in time to defend it from attack.Half-orcs are attacking the southern guardpost from the west.

Guard Edrud has asked you to defend the southern guardpost with his guards.Defend the southern guardpost from half-orcsGuard Edrud is at the southern guardpost of the Pristine Glade.

The half-orcs are redoubling their efforts. You should speak with Guard Edrud again and find out what can be done to stop them.Talk to Guard Edrud at the southern guardpost'Half-orcs are attacking from the south! Hurry! Help us defend the Tree!''Well done, but the half-orcs will be back! Hurry quickly and make sure all of the guardposts are safe, then report back to Maugan!

'Saruman is here.'You arrived at the western guardpost in time to defend it from attack.Guard Ambras is at the western guardpost of the Pristine Glade.

Guard Ambras has asked you to stop all the torch-bearers from reaching the Tree.Defend the western guardpost from the Uruk-haiGuard Ambras is at the western guardpost of the Pristine Glade.

The Uruk-hai are re-doubling their efforts. You should speak with Guard Ambras again and find out what can be done to stop them.Talk to Guard Ambras at the western guardpost'The Uruk-hai are attacking from the cave across the river. They carry torches and are attempting to light the Tree on fire. We must stop the torch-bearers from reaching the Tree.

'Protect the Tree at all cost! Get ready!''Well done, ${PLAYER}, but the Uruk-hai will be back! Hurry quickly and make sure all of the guardposts are safe, then report back to Maugan!

'Saruman is here.'Noriel is a sentinel of Thinglad, the southernmost reach of Lothlórien. She believes that trespassers have appeared on their lands of late and wishes for you to investigate.Evidence of trespassers can likely be found at the water's edge in the northern part of the road in Thinglad, near where the sentinel Noriel is guarding the road.

You should search for evidence of trespassers while Noriel stands guard.Search the river's edge near Noriel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Noriel, sentinel of Thinglad, stands on the road near the edge of Lothlórien.

You should tell Noriel of the nets you found.Tell Noriel of the nets you foundNoriel has asked you to search the woods nearby for signs of trespassers.

You should search the forest floor for anything out of the ordinary.Search nearby for a sign of trespassersNoriel guards the forest edge along the border of Lothlórien.

You should bring the horseshoe to Noriel.Bring the horseshoe to Noriel'I am glad you were passing through this part of the wood, ${PLAYER}. While the mellyrn fade here, Thinglad is still part of Lothlórien.

'I have heard and seen strange signs of trespassing of late. Will you investigate near here and see what there is to see? Make note of what you find; we can try to solve the riddle of who -- or what -- is invading the land so close to Caras Galadhon.''There have never been fishing-nets along this stretch of the Anduin as far as I can remember. What do we make of this? Who is trespassing on our land?

'If you have any skill in tracking, you should search the woods for signs of these invaders.''A horseshoe! This must belong to one of the horses of Stangard, a Rohirrim settlement south of here. What great need drove these men to hunt and fish in Thinglad? They fear these woods, and anything to do with the Elves.''How strange it is that Thinglad should suddenly be disturbed after so many years of quiet. Only Elves and beasts roam these parts.''Look around for signs and see what there is to see. I would like to know who walks our lands without our leave.'While fighting in the Dunbog, you discovered a man sitting under a tree. smiling and surrounded by Avanc-corpses.Edhow is in Lhan Rhos, at the centre of the Dunbog.

Gwin the Avanc-hunter has asked you to return to Lhan Rhos and fetch him a new sword from Edhow.Talk to Edhow in Lhan RhosGwin can be found under the tree outside Lhan Rhos.

Edhow asked you to tell Gwin that he will not provide him another sword.Talk to Gwin in the Dunbog'Well met, ${RACE}. I was just resting here for a moment after fighting these avanc! The trick to fighting avanc is to turn your ordinary fighting skills into extraordinary fighting skills!

'You could do it as well, if you would put your mind to it. It really is not all that hard! Now, while I take a short nap, I need a favour. Go and tell Edhow that I am well, but I need a new sword. My last one broke in the gullet of that large avanc over there. 

'Do as I ask, and I will be in your debt.''Gwin sent you? Tell him that he has taken quite enough swords from me already. I am usually quite pleasant, but Gwin...he is always out in the bog trying to kill the biggest monster he can find to prove that he is the best hunter. Let us see how he survives without the best swords, perhaps then I will be impressed. 

'Tell him that if he really wants to be the best hunter, he will survive with his own two hands for once. You deliver that message for me, and hopefully I will have one less problem on my hands.''A challenge! I have not been challenged in quite some time. I will do it. Let me go prepare, and when you need me, look for this banner beside me, and I will be at your feet to help you!

'Thank you for breathing life into an otherwise dull day.''Go tell Gwin that I have no help for him.''You should speak with Edhow in Lhan Rhos.'There is great rumour about the Abominations stealing children, and they also have been attacking Lhan Rhos.Blaire is at the Boar-clan encampment, south of Lhan Colvarn.

Blaire has asked you to accompany him to Lhan Colvarn for a night raid.Talk to Blaire when you are ready to leave for Lhan ColvarnBlaire is at the Boar-clan encampment, south of Lhan Colvarn.

You should talk to Blaire now that you have ended the Abomination threat.Talk to Blaire at the Boar-clan encampment'We must put an end to the Abominations, once and for all. They are naught but an evil hindrance. We also need to discover if there is any evidence that these truly are created by Saruman himself. If so, then the situation is much graver than we had feared.

'Come with us. We attack at night and will destroy these Abominations once and for all.

'Speak with me when you are ready to depart.''Are you ready to end the terror of the Abominations and defeat their leader? Knotfist will be in the cellar of the largest hut. He rarely shows his face.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'You did well, ${PLAYER}. The important part is that we found evidence that Saruman is behind the creation of these Abominations. The Elders must call Assembly and unite the Avanc-lûth!

'We will meet you there as soon as we prepare our camp. Thank you for all of your help.'Some Orcs survived the brief skirmish over the slain Rohirrim huntsman, and they should not be permitted to escape.Orcs are likely to still wander the site of the skirmish near the slain hunter.

You should defeat Orcs around the central hill of Thinglad.Defeat Ûngund Orcs near the site of the skirmish (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wynmar awaits you at his camp in the north-west of Thinglad.

You should return to Wynmar with new of the many Orcs you defeated.Return to Wynmar'I know Noriel did not wish us to wander Thinglad any longer...unless we wander back home, of course. But surely you saw the tracks of Orcs that did not die with the others. I believe there are still many out there, waiting to gather their strength for another attack.

'Since you are free to wander whither you will, you should return to the site of the skirmish and defeat any Orcs you find there.''I was correct, then? I suspected more Orcs could be found nearby, trying to rally their strength again.

'I am glad to have done this last service to the fair wood of Thinglad ere my folk depart.'Séarl has been tasked with gathering food for the Avanc-lûth. He personally does not have a taste for toad-legs, but that is what has been demanded by the Elders.Toads are all around the camp-fire where Séarl is encamped in the Dunbog.

Séarl has asked you to fetch toad-legs for him.'Since you seem to be doing Alun's labour, then you can help me, as well. I am not certain what I did to upset the Elders, but they always give me the worst tasks.

'They want me to gather food -- which is what I am accustomed to -- but toad-legs? Toads are disgusting creatures and make even worse food. Nevertheless, it is what they demand.

'If you are to be of help, go hunt toads and take their legs. Bring them back to me, and perhaps I will not think of you as the bog-scum you are.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. You have saved me a tremendous amount of time and effort doing work that I detest.

'Take this and go do your other tasks. These chores will not complete themselves.'Blaire wishes for you to defeat all of the Abominations.Blaire wants you to defeat Knotfist and end the Abominations once and for all.Defeat Knotfist, the leader of the AbominationsHaving defeated the Abomination leader, Knotfist, speak with Blaire outside Lhan Colvarn once you have left the instance.Talk to Blaire'We have delivered a significant blow to the ranks of the Abominations...now it is time to finish their leader. End this once and for all, Duvodiad. Do not listen to Delwin. It is time to kill these creatures and put an end to them.''A great warrior does not hesitate when unpleasant decisions must be made. You have proven yourself one of the greatest warriors I have met.

'Thank you...I am in your debt.'Wynmar has asked you to gather flowers to remind him of the beauty of Noriel, which he does not wish to ever forget.Gold-and-white flowers grow throughout the northern parts of Thinglad.

You should collect flowers for Wynmar to have as a keepsake, to remind him of fair Noriel.Collect flowers for a keepsake (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wynmar is at his camp in Thinglad, soon to depart.

You should bring the lovely flowers you gathered to Wynmar before he leaves Thinglad for good.'I must ask one other favour of you, ${PLAYER}. The lovely lady I saw you with...Noriel was her name, was it not? I find that I cannot seem to stop thinking about her.

'I saw lovely flowers growing throughout this forest, but I dare not wander out to pick them for fear of angering Noriel further with our presence. Perhaps you would be so good as to pick me some flowers...for I wish to have some as a keepsake, to remember her loveliness by.''They are lovely indeed, ${PLAYER}. They are nothing to her beauty, but they will serve as a reminder, at the very least.'

Wynmar gazes at the flowers, then starts, as if struck by a sudden notion.

'I have thought of an even better use for these flowers, ${PLAYER}. I know how they could become much more dear to me. I would make them a gift to Noriel herself.'Iestin has been asked to find more food for the Dunlendings... a challenge in the mires of the Dunbog.Food-stores can be found at Lhan Colvarn, north of the Boar-clan encampment.

Iestin has asked you to gather food-stores for him.'Find more food, find more food... this is all Blaire ever tells me... just shouting orders all the time. Am I just a mule?

'Well, if you want to help me and help the Boar-clan, he is right. We do need more food. So if there is any way you can fetch us more provender, that would be a great help. Perhaps there are stores at Lhan Colvarn... even the abominations must eat!

'I think they store their food in crates. Bring me several of them, and perhaps we will survive long enough to do some good here.''Wonderful, good ${RACE}! Hopefully, this will help allay starvation... and Blaire's nagging!

'Perhaps this duty will be over sooner, and we can head for the real war.'During your travels in Thinglad, you have defeated a monstrous bear at his den. You now carry his hide and should show this to the Elves of Haldirith.Limfind is in Haldirith.

You should bring the hide of Foul-maw to Limfind.Foul-maw viciously attacked you during your adventures in Thinglad, and now you bear his great hide as a trophy of your battle.'Ah, ${PLAYER}! I thought you looked somewhat shaken as you approached; anyone would be after being attacked by that great old bear.

'Foul-maw has fought and won many battles, and many creatures have lost their lives to his cruel temper, but I see he was wrong to pick a fight with you.'You will be travelling by boat downriver. A group of Boar-clan supporters there will need to know the latest information on Saruman's movements.Driftwood can be found along the banks of the river.

Tecwin has asked you to gather up driftwood to use for oars.'We have been here looking for signs of Saruman's plans for quite some time. While we do not know what his end goal is, we now know that the time of his attack seems imminent. He is much more active now and has done worse things than we had ever expected.

'We need to move upriver and warn the rest of the Boar-clan resistance. The easiest way to get there will be by boat down the river past Wulf's Cleft.

'We must prepare for the trip, however. There are rumours that some of the clans are uniting and forming large forces. We cannot travel with a small group of people. There is a large amount of driftwood near the borders of the river along the bog. We can make oars for the trip with it. Hurry. Gather as much as you can carry.''Well done. We will begin carving these immediately in preparation for the voyage. Make sure that you have gathered everything else, then we will talk more.'Turtle-shells are used for many purposes in Lhan Rhos.Turtles can be found throughout the southern Dunbog.

Luarch has asked you to hunt turtles in the area and collect their shells.'There are some people that speak highly of the virtues of the beetle-shell. How can they even begin to talk about the beetle-shell when there is a much better shell for many more purposes? 

'I speak of the turtle-shell, of course. Can you tell me that you can make a shield out of a beetle-shell? Can you make food for a whole village in one single beetle-shell? Nay, you cannot. 

'So we hunt turtles, and we take their shells, and we thank them for the amazing things that we can only do with a turtle-shell. Gather for me many turtle-shells, and we will all be happy as a village.''You now know the power of the turtle-shell firsthand. You have learned why I am so incredibly excited about collecting these great shells.

'Thank you very much. You have proven -- to me at least -- that you are a good hunter and a duvodiad to be trusted. So will I tell Harri.'The avanc of the Dunbog are ruled by a terrible matriarch, Bloodmaw.Bloodmaw may be found at the centre of the Withered Stones in the southern Dunbog.

Harri has asked you to kill Bloodmaw, the Avanc matriarch.Defeat Bloodmaw, the avanc matriarchHarri is at the hunters' camp, near the western edge of the southern Dunbog.

You should return to Harri and tell him that you have accomplished all that he has asked.Talk to Harri at the hunters' camp'You are ready for the ultimate challenge, ${PLAYER}. We must defeat the avanc called Bloodmaw. All of these avanc come from her. She must be dealt with, or Lhan Rhos may one day be overrun. If you can do this, you are truly a friend of the Avanc-lûth.

'Bloodmaw will not be easy prey. I have sent many hunters into the ruins to fight her and none have reported the deed is done. Go... gather any help you wish or prove that you can do it yourself, just come back when she is dead.''Defeat Bloodmaw, ${PLAYER}, and you may receive my respect.''Indeed, you are worthy of the name of hunter. Well done. The Elders will hear of your great deeds when the day is done.

'Thank you for your bravery. You have put my hunters to shame.'The Protectors of the Pristine Glade need your help defending the Glade from invaders.River-turtles and dun-crows roam the lands outside the cave to the Pristine Glade.

Win has asked you to defeat foul monsters outside the cave entrance to the Pristine Glade to earn his trust. The only monsters, however, are river-turtles and dun-crows.Defeat river-turtles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat dun-crows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Win is at the entrance to the Pristine Glade.

You should return to Win at the cave entrance and tell him the deed is done.Talk to Win at the entrance to the Pristine Glade'Stop! No one is allowed through here.

'You want to be allowed entrance here? I do not care if the Elders themselves... 

'They did? 

'Nevertheless, you need to prove yourself to me. I am the Keeper of the Cave. Before you enter, you must clear the land of the foul monsters. Return when you are done, and you may safely pass.''Well done. You have completed the Task of the Keeper. You may pass.''Defeat the turtles and crebain, and I may permit you entrance to the Glade.'Elder Kedivor is worried about the sickness and disease that are spreading from the camp in the north.Rats and clouds of swamp gas can be found to the north of Lhan Rhos.

Elder Kedivor has asked you to reduce the number of diseased rats and clouds of swamp-gas.Defeat diseased rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scatter clouds of swamp-gas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Anurin is at the northern lines of the Avanc-lûth.

You should report to Anurin now that you have disposed of the rats and scattered the swamp-gas.Talk to Anurin in the Dunbog'You have become an asset to the Avanc-lûth and Lhan Rhos, ${RACE}. Thank you for all that you have done. Our work, however, is never done.

'Living in a wet environment allows for many diseases among the people. We do our part to allay such illnesses, but it always seems like there are more and more every day.

'I believe that some of this sickness is coming from Lhan Colvarn, the village of the Abominations, to the north. We have seen a rise in rats and the diseased swamp-gas. Please, do something to dispose of these, then speak with Anurin.''The Avanc-lûth are very grateful and just a bit healthier now. And this is good, for the Abominations are becoming more and more difficult, just as rumours of ill tidings from Isengard are on the rise.

'I do not know if there is any connexion, but Saruman seems to have increased his studies in the Dunbog.''Please, rid us of as many rats as you can and disperse the swamp-gas. We need to cut down on disease as quickly as possible.

'Go north, and you will not be able to miss them.'With the Rangers of the North now journeying in the South, it falls to heroes such as yourself to defend the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.Complete the Mysterious Relics DeedComplete the Champion of the Northcotton Farm DeedComplete Saviour of StoneheightComplete Champion of the Lost TempleComplete the Atop the Glacial Throne DeedComplete Champion of the Fortress of the Western Host DeedWynmar has begged you to let him see Noriel one last time to make a gift of flowers.Wynmar has followed you to Haldirith and stands beside you now.

You should talk to Wynmar.Show Wynmar the ruins of Haldirith on the path aheadWynmar followed you to Haldirith and seeks a final word with Noriel.

You should escort Wynmar to Haldirith.Escort Wynmar to HaldirithNinil is outside of Haldirith, waiting to speak with you.Tell Ninil why Wynmar begged to comeNoriel is at Haldirith.Tell the Elves why you have brought a trespasser to the Elf-keepNoriel is at Haldirith.Talk to NorielNoriel and Wynmar are at Haldirith.Observe the meeting of Wynmar and NorielNoriel is at Haldirith.Talk to NorielYou tell Ninil that Wynmar wishes more than anything to speak with Noriel before leading his people from Thinglad for good.You explain to Noriel that Wynmar has been intent on seeing her again since their first meeting.

'This is folly, ${PLAYER}! I do not think you were right to bring this stranger to our hidden keep, no matter what the reason.''How infuriating, ${PLAYER}! I did not ask for this foolishness. Bah, let him return to his home. I am sure he will forget all of this soon enough, the foolish Man.'Ah! Hidden Dwimordene-ruins! My men and I have surely walked by this spot a score of times and never saw this place.

'What sorcery conceals the lovely Noriel and her folk from our eyes? Thank you for leading me to this place before our banishment from Thinglad, ${PLAYER}.''You do not...think I was too hard on him, do you? But I had to be firm -- under no circumstances would an Elf of this age choose to love a mortal Man...would she? His life will be as fleeting as a single breath.'The Elders of Lhan Rhos have called Assembly with the members of the Avanc-lûth. Now, you must attend the Assembly and hear what the Avanc-lûth have to say.Speak with Elder Déin.Talk to Elder DéinListen to the Assembly. The people of Avanc-lûth have much to say.Listen to the Avanc-lûth'You have done much for our people and opened our eyes to many things. We will hear from all of the Avanc-lûth as is our custom. 

'Sit and listen to our people. They will have much to say about the situation and the knowledge which you have brought before us.''Thank you, friend of the Avanc-lûth. You have brought our people to the war that would have consumed us all had we remained unaware.

'We are saved because of you.'You have accompanied Blaire to Lhan Colvarn to put and end to the Abomination threat and their leader, Knotfist.Speak with Blaire before continuing.Talk to BlaireEnter Knotfist's hut.Enter Knotfist's hutThe time to end the nightmare of the Abominations has come. Finish what has been started.'The deed is done. For better or for worse, we have dealt with these Abominations. Let us leave here and return to camp. We will talk at greater length there.''You have done well to clear out a large portion of this village.

'We must end this menace now. The Abominations must cease to exist.'The Elves of Thinglad are unveiled to their Stangard neighbours at last.You should speak with Noriel at once.Talk to NorielOrcs are attacking Thinglad!

You should defeat many Orcs.Defeat attackersYou should talk to Wynmar.Thank Wynmar for his interventionObserve the dialogue between Noriel and Wynmar.Listen to Noriel and WynmarYou should talk to Noriel.Talk to Noriel'I greet you, ${PLAYER}. I apologize for following you, but we did...and it is a good thing, too. It looks like we were just in time to save you and your fair friend.

'Pray...introduce me to this brave lady. I rarely see a warrior fight so well, man or woman.''Those who did this are surely still nearby. I can smell their foul breath upon the air. Be alert, ${PLAYER}!''${PLAYER}, I look to you to ensure that Wynmar keeps his word. Please help the Rohirrim with anything they need before they depart these woods.

'Will you see our friends back to their camp?''Are you ready to bring Wynmar back to his camp?'The Orcs have begun their attack on the Rohirrim's vulnerable encampment in Thinglad.Wynmar, Rothulf, and the other Rohirrim hunters now brace themselves against an onslaught.Talk to RothulfRothulf and Wynmar are at their camp in Thinglad.Help Rothulf rouse Wynmar from his woeRothulf and Wynmar are at their camp in Thinglad.See if Wynmar is ready to fightOrcs are attacking! You must defeat them.Defeat the attacking OrcsRothulf is at the camp.Talk to RothulfWynmar is at his camp.Talk to WynmarNoriel and Wynmar are speaking quietly between themselves.See if Wynmar and Noriel need your helpNoriel is tending to Wynmar's wounds.Ask Noriel if Wynmar will live'Let us say our good-byes, dear friend....''They are coming any moment, ${PLAYER}. I can sense it... we must wake Wynmar from this foolish stupour, or he will surely die in this battle!''I suppose it is time to let her go. I must. But... this all just seems so wrong now.

'Why did this happen, ${PLAYER}? Have you ever felt this backwards sense that your life was fine until you met someone you could not have, then nothing would ever be as it should again?''Do you think that was all of them, ${PLAYER}? I am weary, but I could stand another attack.

'I wonder who leads this rabble.

'I think I am all right. What of Wynmar? He looks tired to my eyes.''What is going on?''He is poisoned, ${PLAYER}! I was coming to make amends for my coldness from our earlier meeting... if only I had been one moment sooner!

'There is nothing I can do. It will not be long now. Poor Wynmar!'The Boar-clan is assaulting Wulf's Cleft in an effort to hinder the army there.Tecwin kneels before you. Speak with him to discuss his plans.Talk to TecwinSpeak with Elder Déin as he addresses the warriors.Talk to Elder DéinElder Déin has asked you to choose four of his finest soldiers to join you in your attempt to destroy the siege engines of the Dunlending army.Choose 4 soldiers to assist youSpeak with Gwin at the front lines. The Boar-clan will move out and attack the main camp, while you destroy as much of the camp as possible.Talk to GwinDestroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.Destroy the first siege-engineDestroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.Destroy the next siege-engine further in the campDestroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.Destroy the next set of siege-enginesDestroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.Destroy the final siege-enginesSpeak with Elder Déin in the centre of the conflagration.Talk to Elder Déin quicklyDefeat the Dunlending siege-captain quickly.Defeat Dunlending siege-captainSpeak with Elder Déin again.Talk to Elder DéinFlee upon Elder Déin's horse before the chance to survive is no more!Flee on Elder Déin's horse'This horde is greater than we could have possibly imagined. We have defeated the forces holding the beach, but more will arrive soon.

'We are too small a force to do much against such a massive army. Let us talk to the Elder.''We will take the main force up the river-bank and attack the gates. You must fight through the chaos and destroy as much as you can.

'We are few against an entire army, but we must do all we can. Probably most of us will not survive. Do your part for the good of Dunland.

'Take four of my best warriors to help you. Some of them will help in healing, some will help protect you, and some will attack from a distance. Go now!''We have been holding the line for as long as we can. If the Elders want us to attack, then we will! We will head to the right... you must go straight ahead and destroy those siege-engines.

'Wait for our assault; otherwise, there will be too many guards for you to handle.''We have little time. The enemy is too great. We broke into this courtyard, but I fear the nest is truly stirred now.

'We must hold out as long as we can. It has been an honour knowing you, ${PLAYER}. May your name be heard in the songs of legends.

'Brace yourselves for the final attack.''You fought with honour. I do not have much time left. Take my horse and ride away. Tell any who will listen of Saruman's treachery.

'Do not let the end of the Avanc-lûth be for naught. Be well....'Renfaer has noticed the Orcs of Thinglad greedily hoarding locked chests of loot, and he is curious to see what the enemies hold so dear.Orc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad.

You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.Orc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad.

You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.Orc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad.

You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.Orc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad.

You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.Orc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad.

You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.Orc-guarded lockboxes can be found in Hîs-urdan in southern Thinglad.

You should examine the contents of the lockboxes, but first you will likely need to pry keys from the Orcs who hoard them.Renfaer, the scout of southern Thinglad, awaits you at his watch-post.

You should bring the treasure you gathered to Renfaer.'The Orcs that have settled in the south of Thinglad were spotted carrying strange lockboxes with them. We wish to see what they are hiding and why they are here.

'When you kill Orcs in Thinglad, you should search them for keys. I am curious about what may be so precious to Orcs that they store them away in little locked boxes.''I am sure the Orcs guarding the lockboxes will have keys for the treasure, whatever it is. I am very curious about their hoard!''You found Elf-treasure in the lockboxes? How strange that the Orcs would endeavour to keep it and guard it so jealously.

'I wonder if this particular band of Orcs are on the run from their masters, looting as they escape to survive wherever they land.'The missing hunter has been found dead, and his companions should be alerted to this unhappy turn of events.The hunter lies dead on a hilltop in Thinglad, a forest guarded closely by the Elves of Lórien.

You should search the dead hunter once more to make an argument for chasing the true enemy out of Thinglad.Make a case to chase out the true enemy, not the RohirrimWynmar stands at the site of the Orc-siege in Thinglad.

You should speak with Wynmar.Talk to WynmarThe enemies who slew this fellow may yet be near.

You cannot help but wonder what Noriel would wish you to do. Will driving out the unwelcome Rohirrim still be the first priority when a true enemy is surely so near?'Thank you for looking after us, ${PLAYER}. You are a stout warrior, and I was glad to have you at my side in battle.'The arrows that pierced this man's body so many times are crude, likely Orkish in make. The Orcs that loosed these cannot be far.

There is only one choice in this matter: driving out these foes is the more pressing task. Noriel should abandon her wish to send the Rohirrim away.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is intended to be a single-player encounter, but up to two players may enter at a time. It is recommended that guests do not join if they have not reached this part of the story.</rgb>After a brief skirmish with the Orcs, the poorly-equipped hunting party of Thinglad wishes to recover their dropped arms.Spears and arrows loosed in the battle can be found near the Orc battle-site in Thinglad.

You should collect the fallen weapons for Wynmar to expedite the departure of his hunting party from Lórien territory.Collect spent arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect spears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wynmar is at his camp in the north-west of Thinglad.

You should bring the weapons you collected to Wynmar.'We must prepare to leave, I know. Our weapons are now scattered throughout this wood after the skirmish...but did you see her when she fought, ${PLAYER}? Did you see how deft her blade-work, and the way her hair shone like gold? She was lovely....

'Hm? Oh, yes, the weapons! Will you help me gather them? Our supplies are scarce, and we must make ready to depart.''Ah, thank you for returning these, ${PLAYER}. Did you happen to see your fair friend as you wandered the wood?

'No? A shame....'During your travels in Thinglad, you felled a vicious but ancient-looking buck. You should bring his antlers to the Elves of Haldirith.Ninil is in Haldirith.

You should bring the antlers of Oldheart to Ninil.Oldheart, a vicious and ancient-looking buck of Thinglad, attacked you quite violently. You took his antlers as a trophy after winning this clash of horn and sword.'Poor Oldheart met his match at last!

'Oldheart was once a beautiful creature, but he grew cruel and hard with time, heeding the whispers of evil in the earth and not the gentle goodness of Lórien. 

'All creatures must die, and it was his time, but I will endeavour to remember him as the majestic beauty he once was!'As you entered the Dunbog, you stumbled across the Avanc-lûth. You clearly get the sense that these people do not like strangers, nor do they want you anywhere within their bog.Alun is encamped to the south-west, near a large bent tree.

Bethan has asked you to talk to Alun if you wish to learn more about the people of Dunbog.Talk to Alun at the look-out camp'We do not get many travellers down this road. Is there something that I can help you with? What could you possibly want down this way? The Avanc-lûth do not take kindly to duvodiad.

'There is a small band of us here, but we ask for naught, nor do we need anything from you. If you insist, you may speak with Alun. He is leading a scouting party nearby.''You should speak with Alun.''Bethan sent you here, did she? Interesting. I am not certain that she was wise to do so, but we have naught we can hide here. The land is open as far as you can see, and there is not anything to see. Why would you even want to come here?

'Perhaps you can prove that you would be a valuable ally to the Avanc-lûth. Food and supplies are scarce here, as you can see. Maybe you can help us gather some things.'Every hut needs repairs, and the huts of the Dunbog are no different. In fact, they need repair even more than most.Mud-balls can be found where the bog-beetles dwell, east of Lhan Rhos, and sometimes upon the beetles themselves.

Edhow has asked you to gather up as many mud-balls as possible and bring them to him.'Greetings. You are new here, are you not? Well, that is wonderful. I love meeting new people, even if we do not get to meet many very often. Since Bain has you helping us, I have a chore for you.

'As you can see, we are a village of huts... lots and lots of huts. Sadly, these huts do not stand up well to being half-submerged in swamp-water all day. They are in constant need of repair, and what better way to repair them than with mud. It patches holes and makes things new again.

'Can you bring us some mud-balls then? The beetles of the area east of here love to gather up the mud and roll it into neat little balls. I am not sure why, but we use them to patch our huts.''A true gatherer. Impressive. Usually the beetles put up more of a fight for these. I am not sure why they want them, but they guard them jealously.

'Thank you for gathering these. Perhaps, you will stay for a while so we can learn more about the world beyond the Dunbog? We do not often have the opportunity to talk to duvodiad.'As you entered the Dunbog, you stumbled across the Avanc-lûth. You clearly get the sense that these people do not like strangers, nor do they want you anywhere within their bog.Bog-beetles can be found in the Dunbog. Alun is encamped in the north-eastern part of the Dunbog.

Alun has asked you to gather beetle-shells for the Avanc-lûth and bring them to him.'Since you are so persistent, perhaps I can put you to some use. The Elders have asked us to gather supplies while we are out here on watch. I personally would rather be in my hut with my wife keeping warm.

'Do you think you can help me then? We need to collect shells from the beetles in the area. We use their shells for armour and cooking, and their meat is passable. But the shells are what we are looking for... undamaged, of course. Bring them to me when you are done.''Impressive. This will make my time here go much more quickly. Thank you.

'Perhaps there is more to you than there seems, Duvodiad. My wife will be happy when I return home sooner than usual.'The Elders of Lhan Rhos spoke of terrible creatures that they call the Abominations.The Abominations attack Lhan Rhos from the north.

Elder Déin has asked you to stop the Abomination invasions.Defeat Abomination Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Anurin is on the northern lines of the Avanc-lûth.

Elder Déin instructed you to speak with Anurin once you have defeated the waves of Abomination Orcs.Talk to Anurin in the Dunbog'We have much to talk about, Duvodiad. Here in the Dunbog we are able to stay out of the affairs of the rest of Dunland. We know that storms brew on the horizon, but we make certain that we keep out of the rain.

'Part of the reason is that we have a constant reminder to the north of what happens when we do not mind our own affairs. The last time that we interfered, Saruman took many of our people and did foul things to them. I am not sure what he was doing there, but he returned one day with an army of twisted monsters, abominations to nature.

'Now we need to deal with the attacks of the Abominations every day. Go north and help stave off the attacks of these creatures, and when you are done, speak with Anurin.''I should not be impressed since you have done all that we have asked, but I am. You do as we ask without thought or question.

'The Abominations are a sad tale, indeed. They also kill without thought or question but for all the wrong reasons. We watch them, but we are wary of destroying them all because it is not in our nature.

'Now, I may have information regarding the Dunlending strangers you are seeking.''Please, stop the next assault from the Abominations. We can not afford to lose our village.

'The creatures attack from the north.'Delwin wishes for you to save the Abominations.Delwin wants you to speak with Knotfist and stop the violence.Talk to KnotfistHaving heard from the Abomination leader, Knotfist, speak again with Delwin.Talk to DelwinSpeak with Delwin outside Lhan Colvarn.Talk to Delwin'We cannot kill these Abominations. They were once like us, and many still are. Please, ${PLAYER}, do not harm these people anymore. They have already been through so much.  

'Instead, speak to Knotfist. He will let you see the errors of your ways. Save our twisted kin once and for all from the mass slaughter Blaire desires.''I told them all. I knew it. They just want to be left alone. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You can walk with a lighter step today. You have stopped the violence for now.

'Let us leave when you are ready, and we will speak at the camp.''What an incredible act of kindness. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Not many would choose the path you followed. You are a shining example to us all.

'Please, take this small token of my appreciation.''You help us? You stop the death? You save us? Please? We no want to be killed. We want to be left alone.

'That all.'To overthrow Gorothúl, it becomes necessary to overthrow the Lieutenant of Dol Guldur as well...a task not to be taken lightly.Defeat the Captains of Barad GuldurComplete The Ten GuardsComplete Two with One BlowComplete King of the EastBlaire is greatly worried about the presence of Saruman in the Dunbog and fears that the Avanc-lûth will be attacked shortly.Elder Déin is at Lhan Rhos, south of the Boar-clan encampment.

Blaire has asked you to talk to Elder Déin and call an assembly of the Avanc-lûth.Talk to Elder Déin at Lhan Rhos'The abominations have been dealt with, and that is a very good thing. You are clearly a person to be trusted. We need the Elders to know, however, that the threat of Saruman is real.

'Return to Lhan Rhos and tell the Elders that the time for action is now. Explain to them what the abominations truly are, and maybe they will listen... although, I do not have much faith. Tell them that the time for Assembly is here, and we will stand with them.

'Go. Now!''You should return at once to the Elders at Lhan Rhos.''I see. This is what I had most feared. I am thankful to you for relaying this information to me.

'I am afraid that Blaire is right... we can no longer wait and hope for peace. I have need of you again, ${PLAYER}.'Delwin believes that the abominations are not truly monsters. They were once people. She wants you to speak with them and give them one last chance to escape before the Boar Clan destroys the camp.Abomination Dunlendings can be found at Lhan Colvarn, north of the Boar-clan encampment.

Delwin wants you to save the abomination Dunlendings from the killing ways of her companions by warning them to flee.Warn the Dunlending abomination (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Delwin is at the Boar-clan encampment, south of Lhan Colvarn.

You should return to Delwin and let her know that you have saved many of the Dunlending abominations.Talk to Delwin at the Boar-clan encampment'All of this killing sickens me. Blaire and the others just want to kill anything that moves and has a White Hand emblazoned upon it.

'Well, I will not stand for it. These were once our people. It is not their fault that Saruman wants to make half-orcs and uruks. They did not ask to be made into this.

'Warn our twisted kin and save them. They are not abominations. We need to help them, not destroy them. Go north to Lhan Colvarn and tell them to leave before Blaire and the rest destroy the camp. You may see them as abominations, but I ask you to look more closely.''You must save our twisted kinsmen!'The Dunlending abomination looks at you with a wary eye, cowering slightly. It is not sure if you mean it harm or help.

As you approach, it tenses, looking at you with a blank stare....'Thank you for saving our twisted kin. I know that some may have resisted your help. That is all right. It is a sad but foreseen loss.

'I hope that Blaire and the Boar-clan will understand now that these are not monsters... they are just like us. One day, this will never happen again. Thank you for saving our people.'With Wynmar distracted by his admiration for Noriel, Rothulf is deeply concerned about the movements of Orcs on the fringes of the camp.Rothulf stands near Wynmar at the southern Rohirrim camp.

Wynmar is distracted by his love for Noriel, but Rothulf has asked for a word with you.Talk to Rothulf, who seems to have something important to tell youRothulf suspects that a threatening presence can be found around Wynmar's camp in the south of Thinglad.

You should search for and defeat any threats to the Rohirrim hunters.Defeat any threats to the Rohirrim's camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A hardy leader of the Orc-scouts' initiative is likely somewhere near Wynmar's camp.

You should try to defeat the scouts' leader before he can alert the attackers of the Rohirrim's whereabouts.Stop the scouts' leader from sounding the alertRothulf is in Wynmar's camp in southern Thinglad.

You should return to Rothulf with the dire news of the escaped scout.Return to Rothulf with news of the Orc-threat'Please, ${PLAYER}, you must tell me more of Noriel. I would give anything to see her again. I have never seen a maiden so fair nor so bold.

'Do you think her brethren would let me approach their keep again, so that I could speak with her one last time? I am loath to leave these woods!''Wynmar has been like this ever since his first encounter with that woman. I think she has bewitched him!

'He pays no mind to the strange sightings and sounds; I have a bad feeling, ${PLAYER}. I feel that we are being hunted as we move south....''Orc-scouts surrounded us? That is dire news -- and more dire that one escaped, and our leader is hopelessly bewitched. What are we to do?''Alas, alas! Why cannot our folk be friends?''Trying to stop us from spreading the word of your little camp, are you?

'Cursed ${RACE}, the Orcs will feast upon the flesh of Man tonight!'You have been asked to go back into the woods of Thinglad to investigate more signs of trouble, now that the Rohirrim have departed.Thinglad's scout can be found south-east from Haldirith.

Limfind has asked you to find and help the scout Renfaer.Find Renfaer in Thinglad'Noriel has gone off into the woods once again to investigate more signs of trouble, and she would like you to do the same by helping our scout, Renfaer, to the south. He saw animals and birds fleeing, and we want to know why.

'What do you say, ${PLAYER}? You seem a helpful sort of ${RACE}, and a stout fighter from what I have heard. He went south-east only a little while ago.''Greetings to you, ${PLAYER}. Now that the Rohirrim are gone, it would seem that we have enemies at our doorstep, and not just mere trespassers.

'I have spotted signs of Orcs and Wargs, newly moved into this part of the woods.''Renfaer headed south-east to follow signs that animals were fleeing that part of the woods.'Bain insists the the meat from baby slugs is a delicacy in Lhan Rhos. The slugs, however, are protective of their young.Slugs reside east of town. Bain is at the centre of Lhan Ros, west of the slug bogs.

Bain wants you to hunt baby slugs for their meat.'All of us need to eat. It is as simple as that. The Dunbog does not offer the most traditional food sources, but we think it is some of the best provender ever eaten.

'I become hungry just thinking about our delicacies. You may not really understand, and that is fine. I am not asking you to eat it, just bring some. What am I talking about? Slug-meat, of course...specifically tender, baby slug-meat. The taste is nothing short of amazing.

'There are slugs to the east of the village. The baby slugs are protected by the adults, so be careful. You do not want to be attacked by a group of angry slug-matrons!''Well done, Duvodiad. Baby slugs are difficult to hunt. The mothers seem to be able to communicate well with their young. Thank you. We will enjoy this during our next feast.

'You are well on your way to proving that you are not just another intrusive duvodiad.'Dol Guldur is among the mightiest strongholds of evil in Middle-earth. While it cannot be hoped that it will be overthrown while Sauron's Eye is turned northwards, a mote may be temporarily cast in the Eye....Complete There is a New Warden in the DungeonsComplete Leader of the PackComplete Throwing Down Sammath GûlComplete Regent of the TowerYou have found Anurin tending to the wounded guards north of the village.Wounded guards can be found along the northern lines of the Avanc-lûth.

Anurin has asked you to patch up some guards and heal them quickly.Heal the wounded guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Anurin is at the northern lines of the Avanc-lûth.

You should return to Anurin and tell him that you have healed the guards.Talk to Anurin in the Dunbog'I do not have time to talk, ${RACE}! There are wounded and sick guards everywhere. Lend me your aid and tend to a couple of them, then return to me when you are done.

'Are you waiting for a sealed letter in the mail? Go!''Well done, Duvodiad. You have actually proven useful.'There is no time to waste. Heal the injured guards with the supplies I gave you, then return when you are done.'Bingo now has a full belly and is excited to continue his journey into the lands south of Lothlórien, along the banks of the Great River.Bingo has decided to travel along the banks of the Great River, south of Lothlórien, and wants to meet you at the Elf outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad.Talk to Bingo at Haldirith, in Thinglad along the Great RiverBingo has asked you to speak to the Elves at Haldirith, in Thinglad along the Great River, about the possibility of borrowing an inkpot.Find an Elf at Haldirith willing to help you with Bingo's ink shortageRiver-side reeds and dark mud can be found to the north-east of Haldirith, along the banks of the Great River.Collect river-side reeds north-east of Haldirith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect dark mud north-east of Haldirith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Maervadhor has told you to collect a number of ingredients which you can use to make a high-quality ink. The next step involves grinding them into pigment at a stone in Haldirith.Maervadhor explained the ink-making process to you, and the next step is to add the pigment you created to the nearby bucket of water.Bingo is at the Elf-outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad on the banks of the Great River.

You have replenished Bingo's supply of ink, and should learn what the hobbit wishes to do next.Maervadhor is at the Elf-outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad, along the banks of the Great River.

Bingo has asked for Maervadhor's recommendation of exciting places to visit along the Great River.Talk to Maervadhor at HaldirithMaervadhor recommended that Bingo explore the Old Burrows, to the south of Haldirith, and Foul-maw's Den, to the south-east of Haldirith, if he seeks adventures worth writing.Find Foul-maw's Den, south-east of HaldirithFind the Old Burrows, south of HaldirithBingo is at the Elf outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad along the banks of the Great River.Talk to Bingo in Haldirith'My belly is delightfully full, and I am ready to continue our journey! I have spoken with a few of the Elves here, and they have told me about a small outpost to the south of Lothlórien. The outpost is called Haldirith, and the folk there can guide us as we move south along the banks of the Great River.

'Are you ready to go, ${PLAYER}? I am very curious to see the scenery, and am hoping for a little more sunshine than the grim canopy of Mirkwood provided us!''I am ready to continue our journey! I have spoken with a few of the Elves here, and they have told me about a small outpost to the south of Lothlórien. The outpost is called Haldirith, and the folk there can guide us as we move south along the banks of the Great River.

'Are you ready to go, ${PLAYER}? I am very curious to see the scenery, and am hoping for a little more sunshine than the grim canopy of Mirkwood provided us!''That was a brisk, enjoyable walk, and I have already noticed a change in the scenery as we leave the Golden Wood behind us. The trees here are still lovely, but they are smaller and their beauty is of a different sort than those in Lothlórien proper. I should write down my impressions before I forget to do so!'

Bingo takes out his jar of ink, removes the stopper, and stares inside with dismay.

'My inkpot has quite run dry, ${PLAYER}! There is only enough ink remaining for the very briefest of descriptions, and that simply will not do!

'Do you remember the books you brought to me from Pennasseth? One of them spoke at great length about the art of the Elves. They must know a thing or two about the importance of ink in creative endeavours, and perhaps can lend us an inkpot's-worth? Ask some of the folk here at Haldirith and see if any of them have an artistic bent and can help us, ${PLAYER}!'

<rgb=#00FF00>Bert Bartleby has arrived at the outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad along the Great River.</rgb>'The Elves here must know a thing or two about the importance of ink in creative endeavours, and perhaps can lend us an inkpot's-worth? Ask some of the folk here at Haldirith and see if any of them have an artistic bent and can help us, ${PLAYER}!''It is a pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}, and I sympathize with the plight of your friend Bingo. For the ink to run dry when the ideas still flow is truly a sad occurrence, one with which I am all too familiar!

'I must confess that I do not have an inkpot for your friend, for this outpost is a place of watchfulness, not of creation, but I may still be able to help. You see, I know of a way to make a high-quality ink from ingredients found along the banks of the Anduin.

'If you grind up a certain type of dark mud with special river-side reeds, you can obtain a thick pigment. Adding water to this pigment will produce a high-quality ink that should serve your friend well. If you do as I instruct, he will be writing again with little delay.''I do not have an inkpot for your friend, for this outpost is a place of watchfulness, not of creation, but I may still be able to help. You see, I know of a way to make a high-quality ink from ingredients found along the banks of the Anduin.

'If you grind up a certain type of dark mud with special river-side reeds, you can obtain a thick pigment. Adding water to this pigment will produce a high-quality ink that should serve your friend well. If you do as I instruct, he will be writing again with little delay.''It would have been more convenient to borrow an inkpot, but this will work just as well. And perhaps it will be fun, too!''You found the ingredients? I am pleased to see that did not take too much time. Grind the reeds and the mud into a paste to form a dark pigment.''How goes the ink-making, ${PLAYER}?''Now that you have made a dark pigment, you should add it to the bucket of water to form the ink Bingo has requested. You are nearly there!''Is the ink nearly ready?''Yes, that does seem to have turned out quite well. You have a talent for the production of ink, my friend!''What high-quality ink! I cannot believe you were able to make such a fine ink so quickly, and with such common ingredients! This must be the ingenuity of the Elves, truly!

'I will get to work writing once again. Could you ask Maervadhor if there are any points of interest nearby that would suit my book? Be sure to tell him that I am writing an account that should be both exciting and true, ${PLAYER}, so I hope any place he suggests will be ripe for adventure!''I will get to work writing once again. Could you ask Maervadhor if there are any points of interest nearby that would suit my book? Be sure to tell him that I am writing an account that should be both exciting and true, ${PLAYER}, so I hope any place he suggests will be ripe for adventure!''Bingo wants to know of interesting places to explore along the Great River? Well, there are a few locations he might find exciting, but I cannot guarantee his safety. I suppose if he has come this far from his home, he must be a formidable adventurer... or be in the company of one, ${PLAYER}!

'To the south you can find the Old Burrows, which were once the home to peaceful creatures of nature. They have recently been claimed by ferocious Wargs, so if Bingo wishes to see them he would be wise to do so with caution!

'To the south-east you will find Foul-maw's Den, where lives a mighty bear grey of coat but black-hearted. You would be wise to stay away from Foul-maw, but he is of tremendous size and an encounter with him might make for a thrilling chapter in Bingo's book.''To the south you can find the Old Burrows, which were once the home to peaceful creatures of nature. They have recently been claimed by ferocious Wargs, so if Bingo wishes to see them he would be wise to do so with caution!

'To the south-east you will find Foul-maw's Den, where lives a mighty bear grey of coat but black-hearted. You would be wise to stay away from Foul-maw, but he is of tremendous size and an encounter with him might make for a thrilling chapter in Bingo's book.''This place smells awful, ${PLAYER}! I will certainly have my work cut out for me when coming up with synonyms for 'foul-smelling!'''What a thrill, ${PLAYER}! I have never been this close to a Warg before. It would be difficult to be any closer than this, without being in the very belly of the creature!''This place smells awful, ${PLAYER}! I will certainly have my work cut out for me when coming up with synonyms for 'foul-smelling!'

'I will meet you back at Haldirith!''What a thrill, ${PLAYER}! I have never been this close to a Warg before. It would be difficult to be any closer than this, without being in the very belly of the creature!

'I will meet you back at Haldirith!''Something occurred to me while we were exploring the Old Burrows and Foul-maw's Den, ${PLAYER}. There is an outpost of Rohan not far from here, but Maervadhor did not suggest that we pay a visit to the folk there. They are neighbours, but I wonder if there is some bad blood between them?

'It would have been rude to ask him, so I do not regret failing to investigate further. But I think I would like to pay a call on these neighbours when we set forth again. It would be nice to get a full picture of the situation here along the Great River for my book!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Unusual Friends' (Recommended Level: 72)</rgb>There is nothing left to do but to brace for the impending Orc-onslaught and hope that you and the Rohirrim make it through the battle....The Orc-attack will be soon now.

You should speak with Rothulf once more to begin the defence of Wynmar's small camp.Defend the Rohirrim-encampmentRothulf is at the hunter's camp in the south of Thinglad, making ready to leave for Stangard.

You should speak with Rothulf.Talk to Rothulf'I sense that this attack will come soon now, ${PLAYER}. Are you ready to stand with us and fight? It will be an honour to draw my sword with you.

'We must rouse Wynmar at once from his daze.''Are you ready to begin the defence? I do not think we can make it without your aid, with Wynmar in this state....'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is intended to be a single-player encounter, but up to two players may enter at a time. It is recommended that guests do not join if they have not reached this part of the story.</rgb>'Wynmar...will be missed. The Elves bore his body away, and the woman Noriel stayed with him to the last. When they carried him off to his burial site -- well, I do not know how to describe it.'Rhodri is worried about the endless slaughtering of turtles and feels that eventually there will be no more turtles in all of the Dunbog.Turtle-eggs can be found throughout the southern Dunbog.

Rhodri has asked you gather turtle-eggs from all over the southern bog so that the turtles can be saved.'Do you know what the hunter's favoured game is in the Dunbog? Turtles. They present a challenge because they protect themselves so very well. We love hunting them... too much, perhaps.

'The turtles are in danger of vanishing from the Dunbog. We cannot let this happen. We must protect the turtles.

'Go forth and gather turtle-eggs from around the edges of the great southern bog. We need to save the eggs so that we can make sure there are always turtles to hunt!''You have done a great thing, stranger. Saving the turtles is very important to the hunters of the Avanc-lûth.

'Please, take this as a token of my appreciation.'The Boar-clan is holed up in the fishing-village of Durgors.The leaders of the Boar-clan can be found at Durgors, south-west of Lhan Rhos.

Elder Déin has asked you to report to the leaders of the Boar-clan movement.Talk to Tecwin at Durgors'The Assembly has made their decision. We have pushed back and stopped Saruman for now, but perhaps at too great a cost. I require one last favour of you. 

'You must report to the fishing-village of Durgors in the south-west corner of the Dunbog. There, you will find some of the leaders of the Boar-clan movement. They must be told what has happened. Saruman is becoming a greater threat than we had ever believed.

'Hurry!''Thank you for coming. This is terrible news. With the reported kidnappings, the Abominations, and now the attack on the Pristine Glade, Saruman is clearly planning something terrible. We need to prepare to meet with the leaders of the Boar-clan.

'Speak with me again after you have caught your breath. We need to gather supplies for a long journey.''Report to the leaders of the Boar-clan in Durgors.'The Abominations dwell at a village called Lhan Colvarn, the Village of the Condemned.The strangers Anurin spoke of are encamped just south of Lhan Colvarn, north of Lhan Rhos.

Anurin told you to speak with the strangers who passed through Lhan Rhos not long ago.Talk to one of the strangers Anurin spoke of'I am very thankful for all that you have done, ${PLAYER}. You have given the Avanc-lûth much to think about. It seems that the outside world will invade into our own no matter what we do. It would be best that we prepare for that time, rather than hide from it.

'I hope that the duvodiad you seek can be of help to you. They are part of a group who seek to protect Dunland from the upcoming storm and call themselves the Boar-clan, in honour of the clan who resisted the White Hand to their very end. We may have to join them in their fight sooner than we had anticipated.

'You will find them to the north, just south of Lhan Colvarn, the Village of the Condemned. It was once Lhan Rhos before Saruman forced us to move here.''Anurin sent you, did he? Well, it is about time the Avanc-lûth came to their senses. We need fighters, not speakers.

'Come! If you are ready, we need to destroy these Abominations before any more of them escape Lhan Colvarn.

'I do not have time to mince words with you, Duvodiad. Either you are ready to fight, or you can go back and join the Elders. The time for words is well past.''There are Dunlendings of another clan encamped to the north.'Alun has become impressed with you and your performance and recommends you to the Elders of Lhan Rhos.Bain is at Lhan Rhos, south-west of the scouts' camp.

Alun has asked you to talk to Bain, but warned you that most of the inhabitants of his village will not trust you or speak with you.Talk to Bain in Lhan Rhos'You have done all that we have asked of you and even dealt with Nye's rudeness without complaint. I am impressed. Perhaps you can do the Dunbog some good, unlike the other duvodiad that have passed through here... and I am now one step closer to returning to my wife.

'There will be few who will venture out of doors with you around. Speak with Bain, and perhaps he can help you gain some trust among the People of the Avanc.

'Lhan Rhos lies to the south-west of here. You cannot miss it, for there is not much else to see in that direction.''You should speak with the Elders at Lhan Rhos.''What are you doing here? Alun sent you? He is too trusting these days. Strangers dance their way through our lands with no regard to the plights of my people. Nevertheless, I will trust him this once.

'If you wish to help us, you must help our village. War has not touched these lands, but that does not mean the weather and hardships of life avoid us. Why do we live here, you ask? That answer is not yours to have quite yet.

'For now, help us further, and we will make sure your questions are answered in time.'You have helped in Thinglad as much as was needed, and now it is time to offer your aid to the folk of Stangard.Stangard is the city to the south of Thinglad, in Eorlsmead.

You should attempt to gain entry to the city of Stangard.Call at the northern gate of Stangard'I cannot help Wynmar now, but I wish to send help to his people. Please go to Stangard and do all that you can for them, my friend.

'The Elves will hold this border for them and ensure that they receive gifts from the forest when they find themselves hungry or ill-equipped.

'As for me, I will remain here and contemplate this unlooked-for loss. Perhaps in the future, I would not act as I did to someone like Wynmar on principle only and instead listen to my heart before precious time is wasted....''What have we here? A ${RACE} calling at our gates during these strange times?''I will remain here and think for a while on what has passed. My heart is heavy.'Saruman is attempting to attack the sacred ground of the Dunbog, and the Avanc-lûth need your help.The Pristine Glade lies to the west of Lhan Rhos, beyond a cave.

Elder Déin has asked you to quickly go and help protect the last remaining secret of the Dunbog: the Pristine Glade.Talk to Maugan at the Pristine Glade'Quickly! There is no time to lose. The Pristine Glade is being threatened. We protect one of the last of the sacred Old Trees. It helps us survive in this otherwise impossible land. As protectors of the Tree, we can not allow anything to happen to the Glade. 

'Go quickly. Do not waste time. Protect the Glade to the west from Saruman's prying eyes and soldiers.''You have made it in time, I hope. The Elders sent word that you were coming to defend the Glade. We have been protecting this Sacred Tree for generations. There is no duty with higher honour. 

'We must protect the Glade from Saruman's destructive ways. This is one of the last remaining Old Trees. We have heard that he has destroyed all others in Dunland. We cannot allow this to happen here.'You continue to earn the trust of the people of the Dunbog. The Avanc-lûth must constantly hunt and scavenge, or they will go hungry quickly.The hunters' camp lies to the south-east of Lhan Rhos.

Bain has asked you to talk to the hunters and aid them, with the hope that your success will convince the Elders of Lhan Rhos to speak with you.Talk to Harri at the hunters' camp'You have helped us greatly already, but any one person can perform a handful of tasks. Perhaps you can assist our hunters if you truly wish to prove your courage and strength. They oft gather to the south-east. 

'The hunters will have much for you to do, I am certain. Hurry there, and if you return successful, then I am certain that the Elders will speak with you.''So you believe you can hunt, Duvodiad? We shall see. The beasts of the Dunbog are stronger, faster -- and probably stranger -- than anything you have seen before. 

'We do not lay traps. We hunt...with our bare hands, if necessary. Come fight with us. We shall see if you live to tell the tale.''You should find the hunters at their camp to the south-east.'Fishermen from Stangard seem to have moved too far upriver to spread their nets. They should be encouraged to return to their own lands, if possible.The fishing-nets can be found along the river-banks of northern Thinglad.

You should destroy the fishing-nets without letting the fishermen from Stangard see what you are doing.Destroy fishing-nets without being seen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Noriel has returned to Haldirith and awaits you there.

You should return to Noriel and inform her that you have destroyed the forbidden fishing-nets laid out by the trespassers from Stangard.Talk to Noriel, who has joined her folk at Haldirith'The Men of Stangard once stayed clear of these lands. They must be truly desperate if they have come so far north into woods haunted by the Elves of Lórien -- Dwimordene, as the Men of Rohan name our lands. Such insults shall not be borne by trespassers.

'We would rather remain hidden so that they do not see how few we are in number, so this must be done carefully. Let us begin by destroying those fishing-nets, for trapping is not permitted in Thinglad.

'Avoid being seen, if you may. I will return to my people at Haldirith... meet me there when you have completed this task.''Return here when you have destroyed the fishing-nets, ${PLAYER}. Do try not to be seen!''Ah, you have returned without alerting the Rohirrim of our presence? That is good. I think we will be convincing them to leave by reinforcing their own superstitions of these lands.

'Well done, ${PLAYER}.'Renfaer has asked you to destroy the amassed weapons that Orcs use to harm forests.Orc-weapons have been amassed in their large camp to the south of Thinglad.

You should destroy the weapon-stores of the Orcs before these tools can be used to harm the trees or creatures of the forest.Destroy Orc weapon-stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Renfaer is at his scouting location near the centre of Thinglad.

You should return to Renfaer.Return to Renfaer'If the Orcs mean to settle here, they will have spears and axes with them for the hewing of Thinglad's old trees, and the slaughter of all its inhabitants.

'You should destroy the weapons of the Orcs before they can be put to such cruel use. Be careful, ${PLAYER}...be sure that they do not cleave you first!''I am glad you made the effort to destroy the Orcs' means of harming Thinglad! They will not last here long...the power of Lórien will prevail.''Be careful when you face the Orcs in the south. They have gathered their strength quickly.'Tecwin has told you that the time is now for the voyage downriver. The boats and supplies are ready. The people are ready. Now you need to find the rest of the Boar-clan and report what is happening in the Dunbog and western Dunland.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Tecwin is waiting for you in Durgors.

Tecwin will accompany you to the east to inform the rest of the Boar-clan resistance what has happened.Talk to Tecwin to begin the journey past Wulf's CleftGwin awaits you above Wulf's Cleft.

Having narrowly escaped Wulf's Cleft with your life, you find yourself on the cliffs of Carreglyn with members of the Boar-clan by your side.Talk to Gwin above Wulf's Cleft'It is time. You have prepared us well, and with your strength, we will voyage onward to spread word of Saruman's evil ways. This will be a hard trip, but we must do it for the safety of Dunland and the Avanc-lûth.

'When you are ready, speak with me again, and we will travel together.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Well done, friend. I knew you would see us through.''Are you ready to travel downriver, friend?'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Tecwin has told you that the time is now for the voyage downriver. The boats and supplies are ready. The people are ready. Now you need to find the rest of the Boar-clan and report what is happening in the Dunbog and western Dunland.Gwin awaits you above Wulf's Cleft.

