You should plant the mint in soil at the Old Burrows.Plant mint to ward off the Wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Renfaer is at his new watchpost in the centre of Thinglad.

You should return to Renfaer.'I have spent a good part of the morning picking fresh shoots of mint for you, ${PLAYER}. The flower has many beneficial properties, including its scent's ability to repel many beasts.

'I believe if we plant high concentrations of mint in the Old Burrows, the Wargs will not dream of returning.''The Old Burrows are the dens to the west of here. I am sure you will find plenty of soil there that will be fine for the planting of these flowers.''Greetings again, ${PLAYER}! I hope you did not encounter any trouble when planting the flowers, aside from the Wargs themselves, of course.

'Hopefully your efforts will not have been in vain, and the Wargs will stay away.'Renfaer has made a discovery of Wargs in a once-abandoned part of Thinglad.Wargs are along the south-western edge of Thinglad in the Old Burrows.

You should slay many Wargs in the Old Burrows.Defeat Wargs at the Old Burrow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Renfaer can be found near the centre of the woods of Thinglad.

You should speak with Renfaer.Talk to Renfaer'I have made an unsettling discovery: Wargs in Thinglad! This has not happened for many a long year. The Old Burrows are now overrun with them.

'Evil is certainly spreading over the lands in these dark days, but I believe we can prevail, my friend. Will you go slay as many of the dire beasts as you can?''So you have defeated a number of those awful beasts? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I speak for the sentinels of Thinglad when I say that your deeds are greatly appreciated here.''I spotted the Wargs in the Old Burrow, settling into the long-abandoned animal dens there.'Noriel has an idea for making the woods near the river less attractive for the Rohirrim trespassers from Stangard.Reek-weeds grow along the river-banks of the Anduin to the north of Thinglad.

You should crush reek-weed leaves along the river-banks to help dissuade the fishermen from setting up camp there.Crush reek-weeds to unleash foul odours (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Noriel can be found in the watch-post Haldirith in northern Thinglad.

You should return to Noriel and tell her that many horrid smells have been unleashed upon the forest.Find Noriel at Haldirith'If you are looking to discourage our southern neighbours from wandering so far north, ${PLAYER}, I have an idea for you.

'There is a weed that grows along the river-banks of the Anduin, and its leaves smell quite terrible when crushed. We Elves do not disturb these plants. If you find any, however, it might benefit our cause to befoul the air with their odour. Do you not agree?''I think you will recognize the plant if you try breaking a leaf. The effects should be immediate! I only hope they do not dissuade you from remaining in Thinglad as well.''You need not tell me that your mission was a success, ${PLAYER}. I could tell the deed was done before you even came through the brush.

'Fear not! The odour will fade soon. This is a clean place, and the airs here will soon wash you of that putrid scent.'The Rohirrim guarding the Cuthstan have divided opinions of what should be done next.The Rohirrim are stationed at Lanbert's camp near the base of the Cuthstan.

Lanbert has asked you to speak with the other soldiers in his company and convince them that the Orc-threat has been dealt with.Talk to Ithamar about the OrcsTalk to Nothelm about the OrcsTalk to Hygerad about the OrcsLanbert is at the Rohirrim-camp at the base of the Cuthstan.

Lanbert is awaiting your return with the suitable weapons taken from Orcs.Talk to Lanbert at the Cuthstan-campOdda can be found to the south of the Cuthstan, hidden to the south of the road.

Lanbert sent you to speak with Odda.Talk to Odda south of the Cuthstan'Good are the deeds that you have done for us, ${PLAYER}. The Orcs responsible for the desecration of our monument must regret their actions on this day. Surely, that worthless lot will soon retreat back into the mountains from whence they came.

'Our camp will remain vigilant here until we receive new orders from Stangard, but I believe your work here is done. Before departing, please speak with the other men and assure them that their concerns about the Orcs have been dealt with.''Hail, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for assisting us, as you have.

'The weapons which the Orcs carry... are they not suspicious? Many are the Orcs I have encountered, yet only as of late have I seen blades of such craft. Sharper and sturdier are these blades... from whence could such steel have come?

'I must admit that my worries have only grown stronger with this new discovery.''So Lanbert believes the threat has passed?

'I do not wish to speak ill of my Sergeant, but he seems to be ignorant of the potential dangers. Guards and scouts have gone missing during patrols, and not once has Lanbert sent out a search party. He believes them to be deserters, or he devises other excuses in the hopes that they will eventually return on their own. Never is it considered to be the work of the Orcs.

'Perhaps there are Men still out there, waiting for a rescue party that will never arrive. What if the next to be taken is me? I find it difficult to be at ease.''You plan on leaving so soon? It feels as if you have only just arrived. Your strength will be sorely missed, but we have managed to carry on when others have left before.

'That reminds me, has Lanbert mentioned my old friend Odda? He was a member of our company, until he and Lanbert had some sort of disagreement. Soon after, Odda departed on his own. We always laughed at him when he said that Lanbert was underestimating the Orcs... but perhaps he was right, after all.''My men seem more tense now than ever. They are acting as nervous and queer as that old fool, Odda.

'You have heard of Odda, yes? He packed his gear and left us, a few days ago. He mentioned going to observe the road to the south, claiming that someone needed to keep closer watch over the Orcs.

'It is all rubbish if you ask me, but why don't you speak with him yourself. You should be able to find him to the south. The man is a stubborn ox, but I  hope you find him still in one piece.''A pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}. I take it that you have already heard about me? I truly am sorry about leaving Lanbert's camp, but I refused to let these Orcs carry on their plans unwatched.

'I observed some of your bold deeds earlier, and I think you may be able to help me. There is much about these Orcs that you do not yet know.'Green grass covers the rolling hills of Eorlsmead, but the horses within Stangard have little to eat.Green grass grows all over the rocky plains of Eorlsmead.

You should collect bundles of grass to feed to the horses of Stangard.Collect bundles of grass (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The horses of Stangard are in the stables of the city.

You should bring the grass you collected to Tatwine.Tatwine is in Stangard.

You should speak with Tatwine now that you have provided the horses with a better meal.'As you have seen, my horses are hungry, ${PLAYER}. I am the keeper of the stables, but... I do not have leave to take them out to graze. It would be too dangerous.

'Would you be willing to bring back some heaps of grass for them? Your help would be much appreciated. I will not tell Sithric -- it can be our secret.''These horses deserve to be better fed.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. That was a very good deed! I do not like to see these great creatures go hungry.'Vicious hounds roam the fields of Eorlsmead and have gathered in a dangerous den not far from the city.Evil, slavering hounds can be found in the Foetid Caves in Eorlmead, south-east of Stangard along the river Limlight.

You should slay many of the evil hounds.Defeat vile hounds at the Foetid Caves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sabert can be found in Stangard, guarding the main gate.

You should speak with Sabert about the help you lent the city.Talk to Sabert'You have been given some leave to help me ease my troubles, have you? I have just the thing for you.

'I cannot leave my post as the gate-watcher, but I long to be cleaning the fields of the fanged menace that roams ever nearer to our doors. Those evil hounds grow bold -- they do not fear us as they should. It would be a good task for you, ${PLAYER}.''You can find the vicious hounds in the Foetid Caves, I believe.''Wonderfully done, my friend! That was a kind deed you did for us. I hope they do not interfere with you as they do with the rest of us....'Landroval has been following the trail of a small shadowy creature and is uncertain if his mark has been ensnared by the spiders native to the region.Cocoons of spider-webbing may be found to the west of the hidden clearing, among the northern hills.

Landroval has asked you to search among the spider-cocoons for any sign of the creature he was tasked with following.Search the spider-cocoons in search of the strange creature (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Landroval can be found at the clearing of trees in the north-east section of Wailing Hills.

Landroval must be informed of the results of your search for the sneaking creature.Talk to Landroval about what you have found'I have found no trace of the creature we were tracking. Our eyes could still follow him through the shadows, but we cannot see into the depths of every crag and cave in these hills, and we may have lost his trail.

'If the creature came this way, it is possible he may have succumbed to the large spiders that dwell in these parts. Would you search some of the spider-cocoons for the creature? If you find him, do not harm him... simply return to me with news.''Have you discovered something? The spiders have spun several webbed cocoons to the west. I fear that one of them contains the small creature we have been tracking.''It is as I feared, we have lost the trail. I shall take this news to Gwaihir, perhaps we will be able to track our target again with his help.

'Nevertheless, it is worth knowing that his path did not end at the fangs of a spider. Your help has been most appreciated.'The problems of Stangard are clear, and it is time to try to change the way the settlement is run.Gadda is outside of the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should speak to Gadda to gain audience with the leaders of Stangard.Address your observations of Stangard's hardships to its leadersGadda is outside the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should speak with Gadda regarding the council with Stanric.Talk to Gadda'I think it is time we brought these issues to Stanric himself. Come, let us seek an audience with him. Perhaps we will catch him away from Sithric for once.''Perhaps we can make some headway at last. The situation in Stangard is growing too dire.''How frustrating! If Sithric represents the king's wishes, I have no desire to be a subject of Théoden any longer. Our king was once a great man, but now....'

Gadda gives a quick glance around him, then lowers his voice.

'I must be careful what I say from now on, I think. Sithric's men are everywhere.'An important message has been left for you near Landroval at the hidden clearing.The message has been left for you near Landroval at his clearing in the north.

Someone has left you a letter, which you may open and read.Read the message that was left for youLandroval and Meneldor can be found at the clearing of trees in the north-east section of Wailing Hills.

Landroval and Meneldor wish to speak with you once more, before you depart for Stangard.Talk to LandrovalTalk to MeneldorSabert guards the north-eastern entrance to Stangard, in Eorlsmead.

Sabert wishes to speak with you about the events that have transpired in Stangard during your absence.Talk to Sabert at the north-eastern gate of Stangard'A message was left for you, while you were away. It was brought by one of the Men of Stangard. I take it that there is some urgent matter which is worthy of your attention.''It would be an honour to consider you a friend to the Eagles. Farewell, ${PLAYER}.''It appears that we must part ways now. May we meet again in better days, brave ${RACE}.

'I shall never forget what you did for me. Farewell.''${PLAYER}, you have returned! We have greater need of you than ever.'

Sabert peers around suspiciously to make sure no one is listening.

'Something terrible has occurred. Things have grown even worse here, though I can hardly believe this to be a possibility!'Dargum has been defeated, and he should now be taken before the leaders of Stangard to determine his fate.The Uruk-hai Dargum may be bound using the coil of strong rope near his tent along the river in the southern Wailing Hills.

Odda has asked you to take the Uruk before Stanric if you could manage to capture him alive.Use the rope to bring Dargum before the leaders of StangardByrnstan can be found on duty in Stangard, outside the Mead Hall.

Gadda is displeased with the command to release Dargum and has asked Byrnstan to express his concerns to you.Talk to Byrnstan in StangardThe strong ropes on the ground here would work well to bind the Uruk's hands. You may constrain him and take him safely before the leaders of Stangard for them to evaluate the situation.'While Sithric places no value in your deeds, your efforts have not gone unappreciated. Although this is not the result Gadda had sought, for your part, there was nothing more that we could have asked of you. 

'Gadda has been asked to remain silent on the matter, so I will thank you on his behalf.'Using the coil of strong rope, you are able to safely secure Dargum. The beaten Uruk may be brought before the leaders of Stangard, Sithric and Stanric, for them to determine what should be done next.

You will travel with all haste to Stangard with Dargum as your captive.Worms haunt the northern reaches of Eorlsmead near Thinglad's edge.Worms can be found at Teeming Nests to the north of Eorlsmead.

You should go defeat many worms in Teeming Nests to lessen the threat of attacks by the evil creatures.Defeat worms from the Teeming Nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sabert stands at the gate of Stangard.

You should return to Sabert with news of your victory over the worms of the Teeming Nests.Return to Sabert'If you find yourself near the Teeming Nests where the worms roam freely, you should hew down as many of the menaces as you see.

'No good can come of those vile things being allowed to endure, and that is certain.''Well done, noble ${CLASS}! I envy your ability to freely go and fight who or what you will. Here we can only watch as the forces of evil creep ever closer to our walls....''Anything you can do to reduce the number of those slimy worms in Eorlsmead will be a boon to us.'After escaping the perils of Wulf's Cleft, you have arrived at the village of Barnavon in Carreglyn. There is little sense of safety in this place, though no one has yet made an overt gesture of hostility.The first patrol point lies to the south of Barnavon at Lhun Avanc.

Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.Search the first patrol pointThe second patrol point is at the Barnavon mine, far to the east of Barnavon-town.

Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.Search the second patrol pointThe third patrol point is at Hen Turrau, an old watchtower upon the hill west of the Barnavon Mine.

Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.Search the third patrol pointThe fourth patrol point is at Munfaeril's Shrine, upon the lake far to the north-west of Hen Turrau.

Gwilum has asked you to patrol Carreglyn and discover whence came the Warg-riders plaguing his clan's land.Search the fourth patrol pointGwilum is at the gate of Barnavon.

You should return to Gwilum with news of your discoveries.Talk to Gwilum at Barnavon'So, Duvodiad, you have passed through many dangers to come here. I do not believe in chance, so it must be by someone's -- or something's -- design that you are here.

'Believe it or not, word came hither of your journey -- nay, fear not... your secret remains secret. You have assuredly met some of my brethren in arms in the Dunbog... I have learned of your coming through them, and through northern duvodiad who passed through Carreglyn not long ago.

'If you will aid me with a few tasks, I may be able to lend assistance to your cause, as well. First, I would like you to patrol our territory... Warg-riding goblins plague our lands, and I wish to learn whence they came, so that we may drive them back. Seek for signs of the Warg-riders on the banks of Lhun Avanc, at the Barnavon Mine, upon Hen Turrau, and at the shrine of the Uch-gwirod, whom you might call Munfaeril. What say you?''The first place to look lies at Lhun Avanc. Be wary, for legend tells that the Great Avanc lairs there, waiting for the foolish to fall into its trap!''The second place to look will bring you near to the Barnavon Mine. The workers there may need your assistance.''The third place to look is found at Hen Turrau on the hill above the Barnavon Mine. It has long been a watch-tower of my people, but I fear it is now being used for evil purposes.''The final place to look is at the shrine of the Uch-gwirod. Long ago, the Ox-spirit dwelt there and spoke oft with my forefathers. Perhaps she may be persuaded to intercede on our behalf once more.''Your patrol was not fruitless, though the discoveries are not what I had expected. I am grateful for your efforts. I will review the evidence you have brought to me, and perhaps we will still learn where these Warg-riders come from and what their purpose here is.

'In the meantime -- and if you are willing -- I have more yet for you to do.'The Ox-clan of Barnavon, allied with Saruman the White, holds the remnant of the Boar-clan in thralldom and oppression.Rhuwalhan Brehur is at his home in Upper Barnavon.

Eres has asked you to speak with Rhuwalhan Brehur and convince him to release the hostages he took to force the men of the Boar-clan to work the mine.Talk to Rhuwalhan at his home in BarnavonEres is in Lower Barnavon.

You should return to Eres with news of Rhuwalhan's refusal and defeat.Talk to Eres in Barnavon'Please, duvodiad, if Gwilum thinks you may be able to help us, hear me out! Many of our folk have been taken by Rhuwalhan Brehur and held captive to force our men to labour in the mine... my own daughter among them!

'If you would, go to Rhuwalhan Brehur's home in Upper Barnavon and parley with him. Perhaps if you tell him that the men are still working the mine, he will let the captives go.

'Will you do this?''What? You want me to release the thralls? Do you think me a fool?

'Duvodiad, you make me laugh. These dung-hill swine are less than the rats which feast upon the refuse.

'If you will not go your way, you will never leave here!''Rhuwalhan refused to release the captives? Curse his bones and may his spirit rot in whatever place of punishment he now dwells!'A captured member of the Rohirrim is in need of rescue from the Orcs.Magla remains captured in the southern Wailing Hills.

Magla has asked you to release him from his bonds, so that he may escape the Orcs.Release Magla from his bondsMagla has fled back to the Rohirrim-camp at the base of the Cuthstan.

Magla is awaiting your return at camp. He has something to discuss with you.Talk to Magla at the Cuthstan-camp'Oh, how good it is to see you, stranger! Was it my Sergeant, Lanbert, who sent you?

'For now, it matters not. You must free me! Hurry, before more of them return.''I cannot break free from these bonds without help. Please, untie the rope from around this pole, before more of them return!''Good fortune has graced me this day. I expected never to be free of those so-called Nink-hai! However, there is a thought that gnaws at me deeply.

'The others have told me that Lanbert had not sent you to search me out, nor had any other. Did he not become alarmed when I failed to return from scouting duty? Bolder do the Orcs become with each passing day, and still he considers them not a threat! Perhaps Odda was right... nay, forget my words. It is not our concern.

'I am truly grateful for being rescued. My thanks to you, ${PLAYER}.'The miners Yago and Matho were found dead in the Barnavon Mine, slain by the bugan which attacked.Gwilum stands outside the gate to Barnavon-town, far to the west of the Barnavon Mine.

Cada asked you to bring word of Yago's and Matho's deaths to Gwilum.Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon'I must ask a grave favour of you, ${PLAYER}. News of the deaths of Yago and Matho must be taken to their families in the village. Go at once to old Gwilum and tell him the tidings...he will direct you from there.''Alas that lives were lost in that accursed mine. The families of Yago and Matho will need to be told of their deaths.'The watch-duties have not been performed in many long months in Stangard, and Sabert is unable to leave his post at the gate.Watch-towers have been built around the perimeter of Stangard.

You should climb the perimeter watch-towers and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out at the Wailing Hills and Eorlsmead.Gadda can be found near the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should report what you saw to Gadda.Talk to Gadda about the dangers you saw'It has been months since anyone has been posted on any of the watch-towers, ${PLAYER}. Men go out to hunt or gather to bolster our stores, and too many die on the way because they do not know what faces them.

'It would be a great help to us if you could just climb the watch-towers and look at what roams Eorlsmead and the Wailing Hills.''You can enter the watch-towers through the doors and look out once you reach the top. Only the perimeter towers will have good vantage points.''You must be jesting, ${PLAYER}. You did watch-duty? No one has done watch-duty since Sithric came here. Please, tell me what you saw from the towers.'

Gadda listens gravely as you tell him what you saw from your high vantage point.

'Orcs to our west, worms and wicked beasts to our east, and a haunted wood to the north. Things have worsened for us since the patrols lessened. Now there is no hope of us getting food from Eorlsmead without losing many men to the predators that roam the river-lands.'Evidence supports Gwilum's beliefs that the Warg-riders plaguing Carreglyn are in fact servants of Saruman the White... and that his own rulers are in league with them.Gwilum is at the gate to Barnavon.

Gwilum has asked you to help him against the Warg-riders in the north.Complete Hounds of the White HandComplete Servants of the White HandComplete Summons of the White HandComplete Guidance of the White HandAmlan is encamped beneath the eaves of the Gravenwood.

Gwilum asked you to bring word of your successes to the Ranger Amlan.Talk to Amlan at his camp in the Gravenwood'While you were lending aid to the Turch-lûth, I looked over the items you brought me from your hunt. I fear the news is grim. It is clear to me now that the Warg-riders are in fact servants of Saruman of Many Colours. It also appears that the Brenin and his brehur are in league with them!

'I believe I now know the origin of the Wargs... one of the items you brought to me was a piece of rune-marked tree-bark. It is in the tongue of my own people and can be found upon ritual trees in the Gravenwood. I believe that the Warg-riders must be encamped somewhere near the Gravenwood, along the road to the north.

'You should know as well that other duvodiad from the north passed that way, Men allied with the Boar-clan resistance. One of them -- Amlan, I believe his name is -- is encamped just within the eaves of the Gravenwood. If you would help me against the riders, I am certain Amlan will have a reward for you.''Well met again, ${PLAYER}. So you were able to bring aid to old Gwilum and the Boar-clan? That is well.

'Now, however, I have a vital task for you....'You must help the people of the Dunbog as much as you can, then meet with Nona in Carreglyn.You should help the people of the Dunbog with their worries, then meet up with Nona in the town of Barnavon, in Carreglyn, when you are satisfied.Help the people of Dunbog as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Nona in Carreglyn'The people of the Dunbog have been on the edge of the coming conflict for some time, forgotten by all but their nearest neighbours. Did Saruman factor them into his calculations?

'We must help them resist him, ${PLAYER}! They remind me of my own people, estranged from the other clans, and I do not want them to labour alone. Help them resist the Wizard.

'When you are satisfied that you have done all you can for the people of the Dunbog, travel to Carreglyn. I will meet you in Barnavon, for it seems to be a village of some importance, and Lheu Brenin wanted to learn the status of the mines of iron.''I am glad to see you, ${PLAYER}! From the swamps of the Dunbog to the rocky crags of Carreglyn, we have endured much already. Each step brings us closer to depriving Saruman of his allies.''Help the people of the Dunbog stand against Saruman, ${PLAYER}. If he has forgotten them, they could be the surprise allies we need to make him pay for his crimes against my kin.'Nona wants you to recover some of the gold that has been paid to Dunlendings by Saruman's agents.Hostile Dunlendings in Barnavon carry the gold with which they were bribed.

Nona wants you to defeat hostile Dunlendings throughout Carreglyn, but especially in the upper village of Barnavon, and take the bribing gold from them.Collect bribing gold from hostile Dunlendings in Carreglyn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nona is in the village of Barnavon, in Carreglyn.

You have retrieved the bribing gold and should bring it to Nona.'I have spent some time watching the people of Barnavon, ${PLAYER}. Saruman has paid no small sum of gold to the leaders of Barnavon for their loyalty, and I fear what that might buy him.

'The iron mines of Carreglyn are at stake. The men of the upper village will attack you on sight. Defeat them and take the gold with which they have been bribed. Teach them the true cost of forgetting their honour as Men of Dunland.''What is the price of a Dunlending's honour? It is the amount of gold Saruman gave these fools in return for their loyalty. Defeat them and take back this bribing gold.''It took so small a sum to buy the loyalty of these men? A dozen curses upon the Wizard for his crimes, but a thousand upon the Dunlendings for forgetting their honour!'Word has come to Barnavon of troubles at the mine.The Barnavon Mine lies far to the east of Barnavon-town, beyond the tower of Hen Turrau.

Gwilum has asked you to lend aid to the miners at the Barnavon Mine so that Madin Brenin will not punish the Boar-clan for the disruption of ore production.Assist Melvun at the Barnavon MineAssist Argel at the Barnavon MineAssist Bervun at the Barnavon MineAssist Cada at the Barnavon MineMelvun is at the Barnavon Mine, east of Barnavon. Gwilum is at Barnavon, west of the Barnavon Mine.

You should speak with either Melvun or Gwilum regarding your successes at the Barnavon Mine.'You know by now that Saruman of Many Colours seeks to sway the clans of Dunland to wage war against the Horse-lords of Rohan. Here in Barnavon, my people -- the People of the Ox -- have pressed the last remnant of the Boar-clan into service in the mine, extracting ore to make weapons and gear for Saruman's allies.

'It is an abuse that Madin Brenin will come to rue, I believe, for it goes against what his grandfather stood for when he granted refuge to the Boar-clan. However, should the mines cease to be worked, it will go poorly for the Turch-lûth -- the Boar-clan. We have received word of troubles there, and the miners are frightened. If something is not done soon, I fear the backs of the Boar-clan will feel the Brenin's wrath.

'The Barnavon Mine is the second place where I asked you to seek for signs of Warg-riders... will you help with this?''You have proven yourself a friend to the unfortunate, and thus I will consider you a friend as well. Will you continue to aid us?

'Fear not concerning the weapons the ore from the mine will bring into being... the resistance will see to it that not all is as it seems. Concern yourself only with the well-being and good will of the Turch-lûth of Barnavon... they may find they have a stronger will than Madin Brenin believes.''You have completed many tasks on behalf of the Turch-lûth, the People of the Boar. There are not many of us alive today, but those of us who are will continue to grow and thrive.

'I know that you fear that the iron we mine will continue to be made into weapons of war for Saruman -- and that is true -- but Gwilum has friends among us who will see that such weapons do not prove their worth.

'Thank you.'Byrnstan, a guard of the Mead Hall, noted that his rations went missing recently and wants you to search for them during your stay in Stangard.The stolen rations can likely be found hidden somewhere in Stangard.

You should try to recover the stolen rations for Byrnstan, so that he does not go hungry.Search for Byrnstan's stolen rationsThe stolen rations are in the kennels of Stangard.

Someone in Stangard stole rations from the lock-house; this food should be recovered, and the thief identified.Recover the stolen rations (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Confront Athulf, the owner of the dogs, for his crimeByrnstan can be found guarding the door to the Mead Hall.

You should plead Athulf's cause to Byrnstan.Gadda can be found near the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should speak with Gadda about the food being so scarce that it drives men to steal.Talk to Gadda about what transpired'I have an issue for you to look into, ${PLAYER}. Someone took my rations while I was catching a little rest... and it is not the first time, either.

'If you can find out who stole from the stores, I will be in your debt. A thief must be brought to justice!''I would start looking in the houses if I were you.'Athulf looks shocked as you show him the rations you recovered from his home.

'I am discovered! Are you going to turn me in, ${PLAYER}? That is just, but I wish to tell you why I did it and ask for your help if I am thrown in the lockhouse.

'If I do not steal, the dogs will starve. As their keeper, I cannot let that happen. I give them my own food, but it is not enough. I try to make sure I do not take too much from the other men when I steal... but I fear we all go so hungry.

'Tell Byrnstan I am sorry, will you?''It was Athulf? He shall....'

You explain that Athulf was using the food to feed the dogs of Stangard, who would starve without his help.

'I have noticed that he does show particular kindness to those dogs. There was once a time when we had food enough for all, sparse though it was, but nobody thinks of the dogs anymore.

'I will keep this incident a secret, and even share some of my food with the beasts, provided Athulf does not steal anymore!''It is not good that there is stealing in Stangard. This was rarely a problem before. If Byrnstan does not wish to take further action against Athulf, I will gladly let this matter drop.

'The food issue is reaching the point of crisis. Something must be done, and soon.'The Ox-clan of Barnavon, allied with Saruman the White, holds the remnant of the Boar-clan in thralldom and oppression.Crates of supplies can be found in Upper Barnavon.

Lhur has asked you to enter Upper Barnavon and burn the supplies Madin Brenin's men have gathered for Saruman's war efforts.Burn crates of supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lhur is in Lower Barnavon.

You should return to Lhur with news of your success.Talk to Lhur in Barnavon'So, Old Gwilum wishes to help us against our oppressors? His goals may be served by serving ours.

'Much of our oppression comes from the labour we must endure to provision and supply Saruman's war efforts. If you were to burn some of the supplies that the Brenin's men have collected thus far, it may go far towards hindering the Wizard.

'Will you do this? The Brenin must be taught that Dunlendings should stand for Dunland, not a Wizard from afar.''Indeed, you are resourceful, Duvodiad. The Boar-clan and its allies thank you for your aid.

'This will perhaps hinder the efforts of Saruman in Barnavon, but perhaps it will also teach the Ox-clan what it is like to go hungry.'The incident with the bugan at the Barnavon Mine has left the mine with a shortage of healthy workers.Gwilum is at Barnavon-town, far to the west of the Barnavon Mine.

Melvun asked you to go to Gwilum and ask for replacement workers.Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon'${PLAYER}, your efforts have gone a long way towards securing the mine, but so many of the workers have been left wounded or dead that we will not be able to continue our work. If we do not work, it will go poorly for our families.

'Our Ox-clan overseers have no pity upon the People of the Boar... they care only that we collect iron for Saruman of Many Colours. Will you go to Gwilum at Barnavon and ask for more workers? He is one of the few of the Uch-lûth who has compassion upon my people.''The mine was overrun by bugan, and many workers were hurt or killed? I did not at all expect this.

'Melvun is right... if Prudwen Brehur learns that the miners are falling behind, things will indeed go ill for the Turch-lûth.

'We will have to mend the situation, you and I.'Gadda wishes to bolster the food-stores by asking that you hunt the wild goats in Eorlsmead, as well as deal with other issues troubling the men of Stangard.Goats can be found roaming wild throughout Eorlsmead. 

You should hunt goats for meat to help stock the ration supply for Stangard.Collect goat meat to bolster the rations (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Help Sabert deal with the threat of wormsHelp Sabert prevent worms from spreading their numberHelp Tatwine with a farming taskGadda awaits you outside of the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should bring the meat you gathered to Gadda.'A shortage of meat is a problem of late, as you have surely noticed. Our rations are small and sparse, and Sithric insists that no men can be spared save the ones that went north to Thinglad.

'Wild goats roam the plains of Eorlsmead in plenty, and I do not see why none of us are given leave to hunt them. Perhaps you could do this deed while you venture out to do other tasks for my folk, could you not?''You can find wild goats roaming the plains of Eorlsmead.''Ah! I am hungry just looking at your burden. Well done, my friend! This meat will save us many empty stomachs.'Several hound-corpses litter the dens. It appears that an especially vicious pair of pack-leaders has turned to eating their own kind.Gripjaw and Dreadgaze are in the foetid caves.

You should defeat the two vilest hounds of all.Slay GripjawSlay Dread-gazeSabert is at the gate of Stangard.

You should speak with Sabert of the two vile hounds you encountered in the foetid caves.Talk to SabertThis hound appears to have been attacked by its own kind, a particularly vicious pair of hounds that has taken up residence nearby.

Any creature that could menace its own kind so brutally must be a great threat to the Men of Stangard.'I knew those hounds were vile creatures! I cannot believe that any animal would resort to devouring its own kind. It is a disgusting thought... I am glad you slew them, ${PLAYER}. I shudder to think of such beasts so near our walls.'Meneldor has failed to return to the agreed-upon meeting location. Landroval grows concerned for his friend's safety, as the spider-hole to the west remains the most likely unsearched location.Venom-bite spider-cave lies west of Landroval's hidden clearing.

Landroval has requested that you discover the entrance to the spider-lair he viewed to the west.Locate the entrance of the spider-caveVenom-bite spider-cave lies west of Landroval's hidden clearing.

Landroval has asked you to search inside the spider-lair for his missing friend, Meneldor.Enter the cave and search for MeneldorLandroval can be found at the clearing of trees in the north-east section of the Wailing Hills.

Landroval awaits your return and will be eager to see his friend Meneldor as well.Talk to Landroval'I believe that Meneldor may be in great danger. He should have returned by now. It is not in his nature to ignore a meeting, yet there is no trace of him in these hills.

'Only one location remains unsearched. I do not wish to place you in such danger, but I dare not go there myself. There is a cavern to the west of here that appears inhabited by spiders. Such a place is treacherous for an Eagle! Explore the cave and attempt to locate Meneldor within.''Be on guard, for there are foul things which may lurk in the dark. Gather your courage and seek out the cave in the hills to the west.''I am relieved to see you again... and still whole and hale. You have done us a great service, and we shall not soon forget the aid that you have lent us, ${PLAYER}.'A handful of miners remain unaccounted for after the retreat from the Barnavon Mine.Yago, Wilim, Siam, Matho, and Inir are lost in the Barnavon Mine.

Cada asked you to enter the Barnavon Mine and find the missing miners.Find YagoFind WilimFind MathoFind SiamFind InirCada is at the camp outside the Barnavon Mine.

You should return to Cada with news of your success.Talk to Cada at the mine'So, old Gwilum sent you to help us? There are few among the Uch-lûth of Carreglyn upon whom I do not wish death and torment, but he is one of them.

'Very well. I will tell you my trouble, and you will tell me if you will help, duvodiad. When the bugan attacked, we fought our way to freedom; however some few of us did not come out of the mine: Yago, Wilim, Siam, Matho, and Inir.

'What say you? Will you enter the mine and find them?''You have earned my trust and friendship, ${PLAYER}. I wish only that you had been able to bring all of the miners out safely.

'Yago and Matho both had families who will suffer for their loss. The Ox-clan cares not for the well-being of my people.'Tatwine, once a farmer, believes that crops should be planted throughout Eorlsmead to ensure the survival of his people over the coming years.An old, abandoned farmstead lies south along the River Limlight in Eorlsmead.

You should plant the seeds Tatwine gave you at whatever fertile-seeming land you find in Eorlsmead.Plant seeds in fertile patches of land (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tatwine is at the stables in Stangard.

You should return to Tatwine and tell him that you planted seeds and hope for a healthy harvest in the future.'I will tell you the real problem with Stangard, ${PLAYER}. There are no crops, and no crops means no harvest, and no harvest means no food... now, or ever.

'I was a farmer once, but I have been told to stay here and tend to these horses, day in and day out. If I was permitted to leave this post, I would plant until my back gave out.

'Here -- if you have time, here are some seeds. There are fertile enough spots in the plains of Eorlsmead.''If you see any fertile land, do not hesitate to stop and plant the seeds. Folk around here do not value planting as I do.''You planted the seeds at the old abandoned farmstead along the south river-bank, did you? That is wonderful news! Now, if only the fools here would have the wisdom to harvest it when it is time.

'No matter. I will find a way to gather that crop. I swear it, your efforts will not be wasted!'The Ox-clan of Barnavon, allied with Saruman the White, holds the remnant of the Boar-clan in thralldom and oppression.Food stores can be found throughout Upper Barnavon.

Kai has asked you to collect food stores from the Ox-clan and distribute it among the Boar-clan.Collect food stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Starving families can be found throughout Lower Barnavon.

Kai asked you to distribute the food stores among the families of Lower Barnavon.Kai is in Lower Barnavon.

You should return to Kai and let him know that you have distributed the food as he had asked.Talk to Kai in Barnavon'Gwilum sent you, duvodiad? The old man is good to our people, and if he trusts you, then I will lend you a measure of trust as well.

'Indeed, my people are oppressed, treated as less than the earth we walk upon. We are given no ground to till and what animals we raise are often taken by the Brenin to fill his larders. The Uch-lûth are slowly starving us to death.

'Rumour tells that there are excess stores gathered throughout Upper Barnavon, perhaps to provision this mad war of the Wizard's. Will you seek these stores and apportion it among my people? Perhaps if you do this deed, suspicion will not fall upon the Boar-clan.''Thank you, duvodiad! With Yago gone, food will be even scarcer... now my children will not have to go hungry.''With Matho gone, I did not know how I would feed my children. You must have been sent by the Turch-gwirod to free us from the oppression of the Ox-clan!''Is this the new generosity of the Uch-lûth? Ha! I did not think so!

'You are a boon to the People of the Boar, duvodiad... may the Turch-gwirod bless you.''Blessings upon you, duvodiad! This provender will go far to feed my family!''On behalf my husband, Inir, and our children, I thank you for this food and ask the Turch-gwirod's blessing upon you.''This act of kindness shall not be forgotten, duvodiad. I will sing your praises before the Turch-gwirod!''Thanks to you for this food, for I shall not be so aggrieved when I leave to work in the mine.''This food will leave my family able to care for itself while I am at the mine. My thanks to you.''You have risked much to bring this food to my family. Perhaps I should rethink my decision not to help in the mine....''What is this? Even though I refused to work in the mine, you bring me this food?

'I must gather my tools at once. I cannot permit this charity, without showing some myself.''My thanks to you, ${PLAYER}. This was an act of great charity to the People of the Boar and will not be forgotten.'You found the key to the cages where the Uch-lûth's hostages are being held.The hostage-cages are in Upper Barnavon.

You should unlock the cages where the hostages of the Uch-lûth are being held.Open the cages and free the captives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gwilum is at the gate to Barnavon.

You should bring the cage keys to Gwilum and let him know that the hostages have been freed.These keys should unlock the cages where the Uch-lûth's hostages are being held.'You have done a good thing, ${PLAYER}. I will see to it that the Turch-lûth resistance finds a place to keep and protect the hostages.'Spiders and Orcs are on the verge of discovering the hidden vale which is to be the mustering location for the Eagles, Landroval and Meneldor.Spiders and Orcs wander among the trees just west of the hidden clearing where Landroval waits.

Landroval has asked you to defeat the nearby Orcs and Spiders to allow his meeting location to remain hidden from enemy eyes.Defeat Orcs and spiders in the northern Wailing Hills (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Landroval can be found at the clearing of trees in the north-east section of the Wailing Hills.

Landroval awaits your return at the hidden clearing.Return to the eagle Landroval in his clearing'This location must remain secure. I travelled into these lands with my companion, Meneldor, and we had agreed to meet here. We have been tracking a shadowy, slinking creature out of Moria, at the behest of Gwaihir, but we had lost him among the mountain-caves. We agreed to search independently for a time, but to reunite at this location.

'As we speak, spiders and Orcs creep ever closer to discovering this clearing and placing us in great danger. Please defeat any nearby enemies which may threaten this hidden vale.''Do you need further guidance? I have noticed several Orcs to the west, scavenging among the spiders.

'We must not let the spiders nor the Orcs penetrate the hidden safety of this clearing.''I see that you have dealt with the threats. You have my thanks.

'It is important that my presence here remain a secret, so as not to draw the unwanted attention of our enemies.Evidence supports Gwilum's beliefs that the Warg-riders plaguing Carreglyn are in fact servants of Saruman the White... and that his own rulers are in league with them.White Hand orders might be carried by goblins and Warg-riders at Naur-maudhûl, north of Barnavon.

Gwilum told you to search for orders on the corpses of the goblins you defeat at Naur-maudhûl.Collect orders of the White Hand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Amlan is at his camp beneath the eaves of the Gravenwood.

Gwilum told you to take the White Hand orders to Amlan.'Besides small raids on our herds, the Warg-riders do not seem to care much about Carreglyn. Perhaps they are here only as a stopping point on their march northward, or perhaps they are hunting for someone specific... like your Ranger friends.

'It may be that the goblins at Naur-maudhûl carry orders which might enlighten your friends. While you are at the Warg-camp, be sure to search any goblins you defeat there and take any orders you find to the duvodiad encamped beneath the eaves of the Gravenwood.''What are these? Ah, orders carried by the goblins at the camp nearby. Indeed, it is good that you have brought these to me... it appears that our passing has not been as secret as we had hoped.'The Barnavon Mine has been infested by bugan who are terrorizing the miners. Many of the workers have been injured or slain, while the rest have been driven out of the mine.Red clover can be found in the hills near the mine, particularly at Hen Turrau.

Melvun has asked you to collect red clover which he can use to make medicines for the injured miners.Collect red clover at Hen Turrau (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Melvun is at the Barnavon Mine.

You should bring the red clover you collected to Melvun.Melvun is at the Barnavon Mine.

You should speak with Melvun again to see if he has finished the salve.Talk to Melvun at the mineThe wounded miners can be found in the camp outside the Barnavon Mine.

Melvun asked you to take the salve and bandages to the wounded miners and bind their wounds.Melvun is at the Barnavon Mine.

You should speak with Melvun and let him know that you have completed his task.'Talk to Melvun at the mine'What? Who are you? You have come to help? That is well, for we are in great need of aid, and the accursed Ox-dung will not see fit to lend it!

'The mine has been overrun by bugan. They came out of nowhere and fell upon us as we laboured. We were able to fight our way out, but not without loss. Many are wounded, many dead.

'We are in need of medicine, duvodiad. Red clover grows in the hills near the mine, especially around Hen Turrau. Would you collect some and bring it here to me?''Ah! Yes, these will do nicely. It will take but a moment to finish the salve, then I will have more for you to do.''It is done!

'Take this meillionen salve and these bandages to the wounded miners and bind their wounds, then return to me.''You have my gratitude, duvodiad.''I am feeling better already. Thank you.''I am not sure Melvun's medicine will work... my wounds are terrible. Nevertheless, you have my thanks, duvodiad.''I do not think I would have survived if you had not come....''The gratitude of the Turch-lûth goes with you.''What wonder is this? Thank Melvun for me.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I will call you duvodiad no more.'Stangard is the chief settlement of Rohan in the Great River area. It is an expansive city with many homes, stables, guard-houses, and watch-towers.Cynred, the keeper of the food and keys, is near the lock-houses of Stangard in Eorlsmead.

You should speak with Cynred at Sabert's recommendation that laws of hospitality be honoured.Ask Cynred if he will give you rations for your stay in StangardThe Mead Hall is the large structure at the top of Stangard's hill.

You should seek entrance to the Mead Hall by speaking with Gadda, the guard.Talk to Gadda, Lieutenant of Stangard, to gain entrance to the Mead HallStanric, the leader of Stangard, can be found in the Mead Hall.

You should seek hospitality in Stangard from Stanric.Talk to Stanric, the captain at StangardSithric stands at the head of the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should speak with Sithric.See what Sithric has to say'A traveller in these parts? Very strange... but you do not look evil. Where do you hail from? What news of the lands to the west?

'In Rohan, guests to our homes must share our bread with us, but I am afraid I have no bread to share. Cynred is the keeper of the food-stores these days, and the food is well-guarded in the lock-house.

'You should speak to Cynred, and he will honour the Rohirrim laws of hospitality.''You are looking for rations, traveller? Who sent you? Stanric or Sithric? It was Sabert, you say?

'My apologies, but I cannot give out rations without the permission of the council -- the laws here are higher now than the old laws of hospitality.

'You should speak with our leader... leaders, I should say. They are in the Mead Hall, and Gadda will let you in.''You may enter, traveller. My captain, Stanric, can be found within. If it is hospitality you seek, Stanric will provide it. He is a good man.''Hail, friend. I am the captain of this outpost here in Stangard... rather, I was the captain. It is complicated now....

'Nevertheless, you are welcome to break bread with us as our guest.''Stanric makes me laugh. He knows full well we have barely enough bread to share among his own men. You will need to earn your own bread, traveller.

'Stanric, this is exactly the sort of behaviour that got you into this trouble to begin with.'Evidence supports Gwilum's beliefs that the Warg-riders plaguing Carreglyn are in fact servants of Saruman the White... and that his own rulers are in league with them.Wargs and Warg-riders may be found at their camp, Naur-maudhûl, to the north of Barnavon.

Gwilum asked you to defeat many Wargs and Warg-riders.Defeat Wargs and Warg-riders at Naur-maudhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Wargs are foul creatures... more than half demon, they say. Combine them with goblin-riders and they become a terror.

'Will you go to their camp to the north and defeat the monsters? Any number you kill will reduce the threat to the people of Carreglyn and hinder the efforts of the Wizard in Barnavon.

'When you have laid the beasts to rest, speak with the duvodiad Amlan at his camp beneath the eaves of the Gravenwood.'The Men of Stangard are evidently going very hungry of late, despite the small number of mouths to feed.Cynred can be found at the lockhouse in Stangard.

You should appeal to Cynred for entry to the lock-house to collect the food stores.Talk to Cynred to gain entry to the lock-houseFood-stores can be found in the Stangard lock-house.

You should collect food-stores from the sacks in the lock-house.Search food-store sacks for rations to give out (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Horses can be found in the stables of Stangard.

You should bring feed-pouches to the horses so that they will be fed.The Men of Stangard can be found throughout the city.

You should bring the men their rations for the day.Bring rations to TatwineBring rations to ByrnstanBring rations to WadaBring rations to AthulfGadda can be found near the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should speak with Gadda.Talk to Gadda near the Mead Hall'I suppose it would be helpful if you brought the men their daily rations, traveller. You can see for yourself how the Men at Stangard fare when they receive their food.''You have been sent to give out the daily rations, have you? Help yourself and mind you do not take too much! That store is meant to last us a month.''Food can be found below. Do not take too much.''Oh... thank you, stranger. I was hoping that since a new person was delivering these, perhaps there would be a bit more. But... I am grateful, nonetheless.''Is this all? Curse Stanric for dooming us to starvation!''Does Stanric really think his men will follow him if this is all he feeds us? I grow hungrier every day, ${PLAYER}. We will not take it much longer....''Thank you for -- oh. There is not much there, is there? Well, thank you just the same.

'It is just that... I think this is less than what we got before Sithric came to make things better for us here.''You brought the men their rations, did you? And the horses as well, I see. It is terrible that there is not enough food to go around.

'We have always had to tighten our belts at Stangard, but things have only become worse since Sithric came and involved himself in every aspect of rule here.'Now that you have assessed the hardships of Stangard, it is time to make an appeal to the leaders for change.Gadda stands with you in the Mead Hall of Stangard.

You should speak with Gadda.See what Gadda plans to doStanric is in the Mead Hall.

You should speak with Stanric about what you saw in Stangard.Address your observations to Stanric when he is ready to hear youStanric is in the Mead Hall.

You should speak with Stanric about what you saw in Stangard.Address your observations to Stanric when he is ready to hear youYou should observe the discussion between the leaders of Stangard.Observe the leaders' discussionSithric is in the Mead Hall of Stangard.Talk to SithricWatch the discussion in the Mead Hall.Watch the discussionSithric is in the Mead Hall at Stangard.Talk to SithricStanric is in the Mead Hall at Stangard.Wait until Sithric is gone, then speak with StanricStanric is in the Mead Hall at Stangard.Talk to Stanric'That is all I can say for now. I thank you for your interest in our hardships, ${PLAYER}. Your concern is deeply felt.''Come, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps hearing of our unnecessary hardships from a stranger will make them realize that something must be done.'Stanric listens calmly as you share your impressions of the stagnant, malnourished state of things in Stangard.

'Yes, ${PLAYER}... everything you say is true. Perhaps there is something that can be done. Let us all speak our minds!''Nay, do not interrupt, ${PLAYER}. I am waiting for Gadda to finish his thought.

'You were saying, Gadda? Things are worse now -- since what? What has changed, in your view of things?''It is well that Stanric sent that fool back to his post. Any more insolence, and I would have seen to it that he was imprisoned for his treasonous words.

'Keep out of this, ${CLASS}. You are not of the Rohirrim, and Stangard's affairs are no concern of yours.''Our hands are tied here, ${PLAYER}. The king... is not the man he once was. To defy him, even for good reason, would not end well for me or my men.

'But I have an idea. You are not truly bound by our laws. If you can think of anything you could do that would help us, you have my blessing.

'That... that is all I will say on this matter. Sithric cannot imprison you, a guest, for any of your deeds in Eorlsmead, as long as no crime is committed.'Dargum has been bound and brought before the leaders of Stangard. They will decide his fate and what should be done about this new-found threat.Odda is waiting to speak with you inside the Stangard Mead Hall.Talk to OddaStanric stands at the head of the Stangard mead hall.

Stanric wishes to discuss the capture of Dargum, and decide an appropriate course of action.Talk to Stanric about the Uruk's fateSithric stands beside Stanric in the Stangard Mead Hall.

Sithric wishes to discuss the capture of the Uruk and respond to Stanric's judgement.Talk to Sithric about the Uruk's fateGadda stands before Stanric and Sithric in the Mead Hall.

Gadda wishes to discuss the result of Stanric and Sithric's council.Talk to Gadda about the Uruk's fate'This is madness! Where is the justice in letting our enemies just walk away freely?

'This Uruk-hai has seen the layout of our city, our lack of supplies, and the conflicts in our leadership! We only show further weakness by letting him go.''You have done well to capture the Uruk and to expose the betrayal that besets us. I wish to stay and hear Stanric's judgement, but I must depart with haste.

'I have been granted leave of my company and will join another band of men in the Wailing Hills. Perhaps my eagerness for action will not be considered such a burden, as it was at the Cuthstan.''What foolishness is this? You would have me believe that the White Wizard himself is now our enemy...?''It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. I must commend you for subduing the one responsible for damage to the Cuthstan and for bringing him before us.''I will deal with escorting this Uruk out of Stangard. You should leave this hall before irritating Sithric further.'Landroval has directed you to the entrance of a large hill-cave, which is home to a dangerous breed of spiders. If Meneldor has entered this cave, he may be in great peril.Landroval has asked you to search for signs of Meneldor in the cave and to lend him aid if you happen upon him.Talk to the Great Eagle, MeneldorMeneldor has warned you of the presence of a dangerous creature in the cave. This threat must be dealt with quickly before attempting to free the Great Eagle.Defeat the spider, MeneghenMeneldor remains entagled in the spider's webbing. He may safely break free now that the spider-queen has been defeatedTalk to Meneldor and release him from the webbingMeneldor has escaped the webbing and wishes to depart from the cave at once.Talk to Meneldor to leave the spider-cave'Let us leave this dreadful place at once. I was foolish to have come here at all.

'Enough of my strength remains to bear us both safely back to Landroval. You may climb upon my back, but hold on tightly!''Be careful, friend! We are not alone here....

'Hurry, she moves ever closer to me!''With the swiftness of the northern winds, I will break free from this cursed webbing. Just a moment.''I cannot thank you enough for freeing me. I am most fortunate that Landroval sent such a hardy liberator. You fared well against that dreadful spider!'Munfaeril has asked you to take a warning to Madin, Brenin of Barnavon.Deliver Munfaeril's warning to Madin Brenin in Barnavon.Deliver Munfaeril's warning to Madin BreninDefeat Madin Brenin and his guards.Defeat Madin Brenin and his guards'Murderer! Begone from this place and never return, else you will be killed.''Ha! You dare threaten the Brenin of Barnavon? I have the protection of Saruman the Wise... you have no authority here.

'Oh-ho! You present me with the Sigil of the Uch-gwirod and expect me to believe the spirit herself sent you? How do I know you did not steal it from the shrine? For that alone you should die.

'Indeed, your interference and blasphemy will not be brooked, duvodiad. Prepare to join the spirits. Guards!'Sithric has at last caught wind of your deeds on behalf of Stangard, and for some reason he is displeased....Gadda is outside of the Mead Hall at Stangard.Talk to GaddaStanric is inside of his house in Stangard, near the Mead Hall.Talk to Stanric inside his houseStanric is in his household near the Mead Hall.Tell Stanric of your methods and hear his thoughtsTalk to Stanric.Talk to StanricStanric has gone outside.

You should follow him.Follow Stanric outsideGadda is outside of Stanric's house.Talk to GaddaGadda, Stanric, and Sithric are outside of the Mead Hall.Observe the confrontation between Sithric and StanricTalk to Stanric.Talk to Stanric'Stanric wishes to speak with you in private, ${PLAYER}. He is inside of his house now.

'Go on, there is little time. Unfriendly eyes are all around us.''Sithric has his eye on us already. He grows suspicious whenever anyone he deems dangerous to his cause leaves his sight for long.''Sithric does not seem happy with my newfound zeal, eh? No matter; I endeavour to do all that you did and more to get Stangard back on its feet, ${PLAYER}.

'Sithric can go rot for all I care. You are welcome in Stangard any time, but I will venture to say that your work here is done!''My men have been coming to thank me for various good deeds you have done for them, traveller.

'Please, tell me how you were able to do so much for us, for I wish to continue this trend after you leave.''Come with me, ${PLAYER}. It is high time for change.''Come, let us retire for now. Talking and thinking are more exhausting than a day's labour, when such heavy topics are underway.'The Barnavon Mine has been infested by bugan, who have driven forth the Boar-clan miners.Bugan can be found within the Barnavon Mine.

Argel has asked you to enter the Barnavon Mine and defeat many of the bugan which drove them out.Defeat bugan in the mine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat bugan chieftainArgel is at the camp outside the Barnavon Mine.

You should return to Argel with news of your deeds.Talk to Argel at the mine'So Gwilum sent you to help? That is good, for we need many strong arms.

'Bugan have infested our mine, and we were fortunate to escape with as few casualties as we did. If you wish to help, duvodiad, enter the mine and kill the bugan.

'Will you do this? Destroy the bugan and their chieftain! If we cannot work the mine, I fear the Brenin will punish our families.''I am impressed, duvodiad. It takes great courage to face those vile creatures.

'Soon, we will be able to return to the mine, and our families will remain safe. My thanks to you.'Odda has observed the movements of the Nink-hai Orc-tribe. The tribe has a number of dangerous chieftains that are at the head of the chain of command.The Nink-hai Orc-tribe can be found south-west of Odda's tent.

Odda has asked you to remove the chieftains who are atop the tribe's chain of command.Defeat Nink-hai chieftains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Odda can be found near the road south of the Cuthstan.

You have disrupted the Nink-hai chain of command, and Odda is awaiting your return.Talk to Odda at his tent near the road'I have been watching the comings and goings of these Orcs for some time now. They broke off from a larger group dwelling in the Misty Mountains, and they now call themselves the Nink-hai.

'The Nink-hai have a few chieftains which seem to give orders to the rest of the tribe. I must remain here to watch the path east to Stangard, but if you were able to deal with some of these chieftains, it should utterly disrupt the plans of the Nink-hai.''Good. Your actions have surely sown confusion among the Nink-hai. The Orc-warriors will be lost without the orders handed down from their chieftains.''The Nink-hai chieftains will rarely stray too far north. I would look about their tents to south, nearer to the river.

'I will be watching you from here and await your safe return.'The miner Inir was wounded during the attempt to flee the Barnavon Mine, but managed to hide from the bugan.Inir awaits rescue in the Barnavon Mine.

You should escort Inir to the mine entrance.Talk to InirCada is outside the Barnavon Mine.

You should return to Cada with news of Inir's rescue.Talk to Cada at the mine'Ah! I never thought to see the face of ${RACE} in this mine, for there are so many of the filthy bugan! Will you help me to escape?

'I can offer no reward, but perhaps Cada will part with something?''I am ready to go... lead on, friend!''Aye, Inir has returned already, and his wounds are being tended.

'You have our gratitude, ${PLAYER}.'The miner Siam was wounded during the attempt to flee the Barnavon Mine, but managed to hide from the bugan.Siam is awaiting rescue in the Barnavon Mine.

You should escort Siam to the mine entrance.Talk to SiamCada is outside the Barnavon Mine.

You should return to Cada and let him know that Siam is safe.Talk to Cada at the mine'Ah! Help has come at last! I have been trapped here for days... will you help me to escape?

'I have little to offer, but perhaps Cada can part with some gold?''I am ready to go, friend. Thank you for your help!''Aye, Siam just returned, and his wounds are now being tended.

'Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}.'The miner Wilim was wounded during the attempt to flee the mine, but managed to hide from the bugan.Wilim awaits rescue in the Barnavon Mine.

You should escort Wilim to the mine entrance.Talk to WilimCada is outside the Barnavon Mine.

You should return to Cada and let him know that you escorted Wilim to freedom.Talk to Cada at the mine'Ah! You have come to find me? I have been trapped here since the bugan attacked and could not escape on my own because of my wounds.

'Will you help me escape? The Turch-lûth are a poor people, and I cannot offer much, but perhaps Cada will have something with which to rewards you?''I am ready to go... lead on, friend!''Aye, Wilim has returned already, and his wounds are being tended to.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for your aid.'The miner Wilim has been rescued from the clutches of the bugan in the Barnavon Mine.Gwilum is outside the gate to Barnavon-town, far to the west of the Barnavon Mine.

Cada asked you to bring the good news of Wilim's survival to Gwilum.Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon'${PLAYER}, you have done well by rescuing Wilim from the mine and have proven yourself a friend. Will you, then, as a friend grant me a favour?

'Go to Barnavon-town and tell Gwilum that he still lives and is being cared for here. He will return when he is well enough to travel or when we can spare someone to escort him.''There were rumours of troubles at the mine, and I feared for the workers. Thank you for bringing this joyous news!'The miner Siam has been rescued from the clutches of the bugan in the Barnavon Mine.Gwilum is outside the gate to Barnavon-town, far to the west of the Barnavon Mine.

Cada has asked you to bring the good tidings of Siam's survival to Gwilum.Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon'${PLAYER}, you have done well by rescuing Siam from the mine and have proven yourself a friend. Will you, then, as a friend grant me a favour?

'Go to Barnavon-town and tell Gwilum that he still lives and is being cared for here. He will return when he is well enough to travel or when we can spare someone to escort him.''Siam lives? So joyous a day! Would that we could feast, but we will thank the spirits for Siam's life, nevertheless.'The miner Inir has been rescued from the clutches of the bugan in the Barnavon Mine.Gwilum is outside the gate to Barnavon-town, far to the west of the Barnavon Mine.

Cada asked you to take the good tidings of Inir's survival to Gwilum.Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon'${PLAYER}, you have done well by rescuing Inir from the mine and have proven yourself a friend. Will you, then, as a friend grant me a favour?

'Go to Barnavon-town and tell Gwilum that he still lives and is being cared for here. He will return when he is well enough to travel or when we can spare someone to escort him.''Inir is safe and will return soon? My thanks to you for bringing this news! We shall speak a prayer of gratitude for you to the spirits.'You brought news of the fates of the missing miners at the Barnavon Mine to Gwilum, as Cada had requested.Usbail, Vevinn, Tafin, Rhonwen, and Nesta may be found at their homes within Lower Barnavon, far to the west of the Barnavon Mine.

Gwilum has asked you to take news of the once-missing miners to their families.Talk to Rhonwen in BarnavonTalk to Nesta in BarnavonTalk to Usbail in BarnavonTalk to Vevinn in BarnavonTalk to Tafin in BarnavonGwilum is outside the gate to Barnavon-town.

You should return to Gwilum and let him know that you have done as he requested.Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon'${PLAYER}, you did a great service for the Turch-lûth, the Boar-clan, by finding the missing miners. Will you now go to the families of the miners and relay to them the news of their husbands' and fathers' fates?

'We will help the families of those who perished as best we can, but perhaps Gwilum will be better able to help them.

'Return to Barnavon and speak with Usbail, Vevinn, Tafin, Rhonwen, and Nesta.''Yago is dead? N-no... this cannot be true! How dare you say such things, Duvodiad?

'Ah, but nay, I see in your eyes that it is true... thank Gwilum for his concern and thoughtfulness.''This cannot be! Matho has perished in that accursed mine? What shall we do now? The Ox-clan pigs will starve my children to death!

'Perhaps Gwilum will know what to do?''Wilim lives! What joyous news! May the blessings of the Turch-gwirod be ever with you!''Siam was hurt, but lives still? Then we shall be thankful that worse did not come upon him. We shall prepare for his joyous return!''Inir will be a welcome sight... praise be to the Turch-gwirod for his safe return!''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You have proven a true friend to the Boar-clan once again.

'There is little that I can do personally for the families of Yago and Matho, for if the Brenin learns of it, my life would be at greater risk than it is... but perhaps together we may find a way to aid them.'You have found a placard upon Munfaeril's shrine that describes the ritual of the Dunlending Derudh to call upon the ox-spirit Munfaeril for aid.Warg-riders and Ox-clan warriors wander the landscape of Carreglyn.

Perhaps one of the Warg-riders or Ox-clan warriors came upon the shrine and stole Munfaeril's sigil.Collect Munfaeril's sigilMunfaeril's shrine lies to the north of Barnavon.

You should place Munfaeril's sigil upon her shrine and perform the ritual to call upon her aid.Place Munfaeril's sigil on the shrineMunfaeril is at her shrine, north of Barnavon.

You should speak with Munfaeril through the shrine regarding the evils committed by the brenin of Barnavon.Talk to Munfaeril at her shrineMunfaeril is at her shrine, north of Barnavon.

You should speak with Munfaeril when you are ready to depart for Barnavon.

<rgb=#FF0000>This instance is intended to be run solo, but can be run duo as well.</rgb>Let Munfaeril know when you are ready to depart for Barnavon. <rgb=#FF0000>You may summon her through the shrine if necessary</rgb>Munfaeril is at her shrine, north of Barnavon.

You should return to Munfaeril and tell her of the events at Barnavon.Talk to Munfaeril at her shrineThis placard describes the ritual used by the Derudh of Dunland to call upon the ox-spirit Munfaeril, which they call the Uch-gwirod, for aid. The troubles in Barnavon may be cause enough to attempt such a feat.

The placard demands the use of a sigil, which you do not possess. Perhaps one of the foes wandering Carreglyn may have one in its possession....'I am pleased that you have heard my summons, good ${RACE}. Does it surprise you that your coming is of my design? I care very much for the People of the Ox, but Madin Brenin has fallen to corruption. He and his people oppress the remnant of the Turch-lûth, the People of the Boar, and plot war with the Horse-lords who are in the favour of the Valar. This cannot be tolerated.

'I ask that you go to Barnavon and bring this message to Madin Brenin: if he does not turn from his evil ways, he and his people will feel the wrath of the Uch-gwirod and the Huntsman.

'Take my sigil as proof of my words and speak with me when you are ready to depart.''Alas, Madin Brenin was a fool, and his son no less. Yet, the true blame for these evils falls to one of my own kindred, and I fear they will all suffer in the end.

'I thank you for bringing my warning to Barnavon and grant you what grace I may.''Very well, ${PLAYER}. May your quest be fruitful.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This instance is intended to be run solo, but can be run duo as well.</rgb>You found the carcass of a wild ox slain by some predator and left to rot; however, you were able to procure a small portion of edible meat from the corpse.Dun Oxen can be found throughout Carreglyn.

You should hunt the wild oxen for meat to bring to the oppressed inhabitants of Barnavon.Collect ox-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gwilum is at the gate to Lower Barnavon.

You should bring the meat you collected to Gwilum for distribution.This ox was slain by some predator and left to rot, but there is some meat on the carcass that has not yet spoiled. Perhaps it would be a great kindness to collect more meat from the wild oxen to help feed the oppressed inhabitants of Barnavon....'I am moved, ${PLAYER}, that you would think of the People of the Boar when my own people consider them naught more than thralls.

'I will see this meat delivered to the poor families.'The Ox-clan of Barnavon, allied with Saruman the White, holds the remnant of the Boar-clan in thralldom and oppression.Prudwen Brehur may be found at his home in Upper Barnavon.Defeat Prudwen's guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find Prudwen Brehur at his home and confront himLunwen is at the centre of Lower Barnavon.

You should return to Lunwen with news of Prudwen's defeat.Talk to Lunwen in Barnavon'You there, young duvodiad. Gwilum sent you to help us? He is a kind child... a true child of the Ox.

'If you wish to help, then I have a task for you. Prudwen, the chief of Madin Brenin's brehur, is also the overseer of the Barnavon Mine. So many of our men have perished or become infirm from working that terrible place.

'I ask that you go to the home of Prudwen Brehur and teach him the meaning of kindness and compassion in a way that only one such as yourself might accomplish. Will you do this?''I confess that I knew the Brehur would not heed kindly words. I also confess that this is exactly the outcome I had intended.

'I hope you will forgive an old woman for using you thus. You may tell Gwilum that I appreciate his offering of peace.'The Nighthowlers' den is filled with the discarded remains of many victims of the vile dogs.Remain-piles can be found throughout the Nighthowlers' Den in Eorlsmead, east along the river from Stangard.

You should examine remains in the den for signs whether innocent passers-by have fallen victim to the wild dogs.Examine remains for signs of innocent victims (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Examine remains for signs of animal victims (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sabert is at the north gate of Stangard.

You should return to Stangard with news of the human remains in the lairs of the wild dogs.Return to SabertThis pile of gnawed, discarded remains could have been anything...possibly even a person at one point. You should examine the food-remains of the vicious hounds to see if any Men of Stangard or innocent passers-by fell victim to the evil dogs.'It is shocking that things have gotten so bad as this! Rohirrim men -- warriors -- outnumbered by wild slavering dogs and falling prey to naught but filthy beasts in the plains.

'At least you have thinned the pack somewhat, friend. Your work is deeply appreciated.'During the flight from the Barnavon Mine, many of the miners' tools were broken and lost.Iron ore and broken tools can be found within the Barnavon Mine.

Bervun asked you to enter the Barnavon Mine and collect iron ore and broken tools.Collect broken tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect iron ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The forge is outside the Barnavon Mine.

Bervun asked you to bring the iron ore and broken tools to the forge and repair the tools.Bervun is near the forge outside the Barnavon Mine.

You should bring the restored tools to Bervun.'You have come to help? At the old Ox-warden's behest? The Uch-lûth are a greedy and oppressive lot, but old Gwilum is a good sort. There is rumour that he is part of a rebellion against the brenins of all the clans who have pledged allegiance to the Wizard.

'Well, if you are here to help, duvodiad, then I have a task for you. When we fought our way free of the mine, many of our tools were lost and broken. Even if we were to drive out the bugan, we could hardly continue our work without tools.

'I need you to enter the mine and recover as many of the broken tools as you can. While you are in there, you should also try and mine some of the ore. Bring both the ore and the tools here to the forge and repair the tools. Will you do this?''Ah! You have done well, duvodiad, and have earned my respect. I shall call you ${PLAYER} from here on.

'With these tools, we will be able to continue our work, and the Brenin will not turn his anger upon our families.'Odda has observed a White Hand Uruk-hai among the Nink-hai. He believes there may be evidence as to the Uruk's location among the Orc-tribe tents.The Nink-hai Orc-tribe can be found south-west of Odda's tent.

Odda has asked you to search among the Nink-hai tents for evidence leading to the location of the Uruk-hai.Search around the Nink-hai camp for evidence of the Uruk-hai's locationThe Uruk-hai, Dargum, may be found along the Limlight River to the south-east.

You have discovered a note which reveals the name and location of the Uruk-hai emissary who has swayed the Nink-hai to ally with Isengard.Defeat Dargum, the White Hand emissaryThe Uruk-hai may be bound with the rope on the ground near his tent.

With Dargum defeated, he must be bound and escorted in custody to Stangard.Search Dargum's camp for something with which to bind him'I have discovered something most disturbing. The source of the Nink-hai's supplies... it may be none other than Saruman the White!

'I caught sight of an emissary of Isengard, an Uruk, conversing with the Nink-hai. No small coincidence is it that we discover the presence of this White Hand Uruk-hai when a hand from the Cuthstan has gone missing. There is no doubt that he is influencing the actions of the Orcs.

'This must come to an end now, before further plots are set against us! Search the Nink-hai encampment for evidence as to the location of the Uruk-hai. Find him and take him alive. We must bring him before Stanric for questioning.''The Uruk has left messages at the Nink-hai encampment... perhaps one of his notes will reveal his location.

'If you manage to best the Uruk, capture him alive and make haste to Stangard. I will do my best to meet you there!''Found me, have you? Well aren't you clever. Too bad all your effort will get you nothing. This ends now!'This coil of rope seems strong enough to safely bind the hands of the routed Dargum.You found a sheet of tree-bark etched with ancient Dunlending writing.Gwilum is at the gate to Lower Barnavon.

You should bring the rune-marked tree-bark to Gwilum.This piece of tree-bark is etched with ancient Dunlending writing. It may be a clue as to the origins of the Warg-riders in Carreglyn and should be brought to Gwilum.'Alas, this is the most disturbing piece of evidence regarding the origin of the Warg-riders you have brought to me yet. I will study this and learn what it may portend.'Evidence supports Gwilum's beliefs that the Warg-riders plaguing Carreglyn are in fact servants of Saruman the White... and that his own rulers are in league with them.Amlan is at his camp beneath the eaves of the Gravenwood.

Gwilum asked you to speak with Amlan regarding your successes at Naur-maudhûl.Defeat goblins at Naur-maudhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The Wizard uses goblins to maintain control over his Wargs, and they are a particularly cunning breed. If you would, strike at the heart of Naur-maudhûl and defeat the goblin-keepers there.

'Without the goblins to keep the beasts under control, they might become dangerous enough that the Brenin will have to send out patrols to destroy them.

'When you have done this, speak with the duvodiad Amlan at his camp beneath the eaves of the Gravenwood.'Gwilum is a member of the Dunlending resistance against the influence of Saruman the White upon the clans of Dunland and seeks to undermine that influence within Barnavon.Kai, Lhunwen, Lhur, and Eres can be found within Lower Barnavon.

Gwilum has asked you to lend aid to some of the inhabitants of Barnavon.Assist Kai in BarnavonAssist Lunwen in BarnavonAssist Lhur in BarnavonAssist Eres in BarnavonKai, Lunwen, Lhur, and Eres may be found within Lower Barnavon.

Gwilum has asked you to lend aid to the Boar-clan dwelling in Lower Barnavon.Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon'As I have tried to make you understand, I am a member of that resistance you first came upon in Lhan Rhos. This resistance has taken the guise and mantle of the Boar-clan, the Turch-lûth, as a symbol of defiance. Why, you may ask?

'The Turch-lûth were a clan of the Algraig in the land to the north you call Enedwaith. When the Turch-lûth refused to bow to Saruman, the Draig-lûth destroyed them almost utterly.

'The people here in the lower village are all that remain of the true Turch-lûth. Madin Brenin's grandfather gave them refuge out of kindness, but Madin himself has placed them under thralldom. They are now little more than slaves of the White Hand. I ask that you go now into the village and speak with the People of the Boar and learn what you can do to help them.''My thanks to you, ${PLAYER}. The Brenin and his brehur shall incur the wrath of Saruman for their inability to supply iron for the Wizard's war, but they may now be too frightened to retaliate against the Turch-lûth.'Worms have completely taken over a northern stretch of Eorlsmead, and they have been spawning without any intervention at all.Worm-eggs can be found throughout the Teeming Nest.

You should destroy worm-eggs in the Teeming Nest to slow the rate of spawn of the vile worms in Eorlsmead.Destroy worm-eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sabert awaits you at the front gate of Stangard.

You should return to Sabert.Return to Sabert'The worms of northern Eorlsmead have been spawning unchecked for months uncounted, and without intervention, they will only continue to grow in number.

'Their eggs must be destroyed if we have any hope in checking the size of future populations of these vile creatures.''You are indeed a great boon to Stangard, ${PLAYER}. I cannot thank you enough!''I worry that without anyone to check the rate of their spawn, the worms will consume Eorlsmead in no time.'Gadda wishes to thank you for your hard work on behalf of Stangard.Gadda is outside of the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should speak with Gadda.Help Stanric and Gadda to take a standGadda is outside of the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should speak with Gadda.Talk to Gadda'${PLAYER}, I suppose you have accomplished more by yourself in just a short time than all the Men of Stangard could do in a month.

'I cannot thank you enough. Let us talk further, for I believe Stanric has a desire to meet with you.''You have certainly caught Stanric's attention with all the good you have done...but unfortunately you have caught Sithric's as well.

'I believe Stanric wants to thank you personally, away from the eyes and ears of Théoden King's envoy.''You inspired Stanric beyond anything I could have done, my friend! I think things will be different around here now.

'Sithric will no longer share in the leadership of Stangard, and we will be able to fend for ourselves without interference again.'You found a medallion bearing the emblem of the Boar-clan. It undoubtedly belongs to one of the inhabitants of Lower Barnavon.The remnant of the Boar-clan dwells in Lower Barnavon.

You should find the owner of the medallion you found.This medallion bears the emblem of the Boar-clan. It undoubtedly belongs to one of the inhabitants of Lower Barnavon. You should see if you can find its owner.'Where did you find this? The thieving ruffians!

'Alas, it belonged to my wife, who was taken by the Ox-clan. I have not seen her since. I fear she was set to work in those accursed mines or worse.

'I thank you for bringing this to me... it is all I have left of her.'Evidence supports Gwilum's beliefs that the Warg-riders plaguing Carreglyn are in fact servants of Saruman the White... and that his own rulers are in league with them.Nagrut may be summoned by blowing the horn of challenge in Naur-maudhûl, north of Barnavon.

Gwilum asked you to go to Naur-maudhûl and defeat the leader of the Warg-riders, Nagrut.Use the horn at Naur-maudhûl to summon NagrutNagrut is at Naur-maudhûl, north of Barnavon.

Gwilum asked you to defeat Nagrut, the Warg-riders' leader.Defeat Nagrut at Naur-maudhûl'There have been sightings of a great Warg, ridden by a goblin who goes by the name of Nagrut. I believe this may in fact be the leader of the Warg-riders in Carreglyn. Perhaps if he can be challenged and slain, the rest of Saruman's hounds will be routed.

'Go to Naur-maudhûl and find the horn of challenge... blow it to summon forth this Nagrut, then slay him and his Warg. When you have done this, go to Amlan at his camp beneath the eaves of the Gravenwood.'The men at the Cuthstan-camp are short on supplies, and the camp's leader has turned to scavenging weapons from fallen Orcs.The tribe of Orc vandals is south-west of the Cuthstan.

Lanbert has asked you to search defeated Orcs for suitable weapons and to return them to him at his camp.Collect weapons from defeated Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lanbert is at the Rohirrim-camp at the base of the Cuthstan.

Lanbert is awaiting your return with suitable weapons taken from the Orcs.Talk to Lanbert at the Cuthstan-camp'How does one lead a company of soldiers when he cannot keep them armed? We have not enough arms to go around, yet still my requests to Stangard for new supplies are denied! I fear we must take this matter upon ourselves.

'My scouts report that many of the Orcs in this region are carrying blades which would be suitable for our use. I would ask you to collect swords from fallen Orcs and return them to me here. Ensuring we are well-equipped is of the utmost importance.''Ah yes, these are suitable blades. Strong and well-made are the weapons you have brought before me. Are you certain these came from those miserable savages?

'Well, no matter. You have both weakened the Orcs and strengthened our camp, in a single bold act. I am in your debt.''Now is not the time to be particular! Gather any working swords you can from the Orcs and bring them back to me.'You have slain a formidable giant worm and now bear his fang as a trophy of your battle.Sabert stands at the gate of Stangard.

You should bring the fang you collected from the corpse of the Ancient Rock-worm to Sabert.You found this broken-off giant fang as a reminder of the great battle you did with the Ancient Rock-worm. You should bring this trophy to Sabert to show him how large the worms were beginning to grow in the Teeming Nests.Sabert gives a long whistle as you hand him the fang of the Ancient Rock-worm.

'That is a fine trophy, ${PLAYER}! You must have had quite a fight on your hands as you wrestled with this one. It is lucky this tooth did not pierce your armour before you broke it loose from its owner!'Lhun Avanc is said to be the lair of the Great Avanc, a creature of legend to the Dunlendings of Carreglyn. The beast is said to use deception to draw its victims near to the water, then it grabs them and drags them under to their deaths.The Great Avanc is at its lair in Lhun Avanc.

You should defeat the Great Avanc, terror of Carreglyn.Defeat the Great AvancGwilum is at Barnavon, north of Lhun Avanc.

You should tell Gwilum of the death of the Great Avanc.Talk to Gwilum in BarnavonTugging on this chain does not seem to accomplish anything. You tug on it again....'So! It was not an old wives' tale after all? The Great Avanc was indeed responsible for the disappearances of many of the folk of Barnavon.

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, for disposing of this problem.'Ithamar has lost a small trinket while on patrol and wishes to have his personal keepsake returned to him.Ithamar believes that he lost his trinket in a skirmish that took place south-west of the road that leads east to Stangard.

Ithamar would like for you to find his missing trinket and return it to him at the Cuthstan-camp.Collect Ithamar's missing trinketIthamar can be found at the Cuthstan-camp in Wailing Hills.

Ithamar waits for the return of his treasured trinket.Return the trinket to Ithamar at the Cuthstan-camp'Welcome to our camp. I understand that Lanbert has explained our situation to you? Dealing with these encroaching Orcs is frightening. Many years has it been since they have wandered openly outside of their caves.

'During our last patrol, we encountered a small party of Orcs waiting in ambush, just south-west of the road. We managed to wound a few of them and escape, but in the skirmish, I dropped a small trinket. It may not be worth much silver, but it has personal value, and I miss it dearly.

'I have orders not to leave camp...would you be willing to search for it on my behalf? It would mean a great deal to me.''Oh, you have found it! Aye, this is it. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.

'As soldiers, we are allowed very few personal comforts while on duty, making the loss of my keepsake even more difficult to endure. Having it in my possession once again has already raised my spirits.''Have you found my trinket, ${PLAYER}?

'Search among the items left in the wake of the clash, a few paces south-west of camp. It may still be there if the Orcs have not discovered it.'Gadda is looking for someone to help a camp of men sent to protect the Cuthstan, the Stone of Friendship, in Wailing Hills, from vandals.Lanbert is in charge of the Rohirrim camp at the Cuthstan in Wailing Hills.

Gadda has asked you to seek out Lanbert at the Cuthstan.Talk to Lanbert at the base of the Cuthstan in the Wailing Hills'There is another matter, outside of Stangard, which could use your attention, ${PLAYER}. 

'Are you familiar with the Stone of Friendship, the Cuthstan? It is a large stone monument in the Wailing Hills to the west, dedicated to the alliance of the Men of Gondor and the Eorlingas and to the victory at the Battle of the Field of Celebrant. This memorial has fallen under some ruin, with unseen culprits removing a section of the statue. 

'Men have been dispatched and have set up camp to keep watch for vandals, in the event they should return. Go there now and speak with Lanbert, Sergeant of the outpost. See what can be done to aid him in his task.''Welcome to the Cuthstan, friend. I am Lanbert, the Sergeant of this camp.

'My men have been guarding the statue from further harm, after we discovered that a band of Mountain-orcs appears to be responsible for the damage. You are welcome to stay and help us, so long as you do not put anyone in needless danger.''Was there some trouble in finding Lanbert? 

'Travel west out of Stangard and follow the road south as it forks. Stay to the path as it steers up the ridge for quite some distance, where it eventually leads into the camp.'Hen Turrau is ancient Gondorian tower that was later occupied and built onto by the Dunlending clans inhabiting Carreglyn.Crates can be found around Hen Turrau, east of Barnavon.

