You should speak with Gadda about what to do to assist the Men of Stangard.Help Gadda give food rations out to the menHelp Sabert by performing a long-overdue watch-tower dutyHelp Byrnstan find what was stolen from himGadda is outside the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should tell Gadda of the many problems and hardships you observed in life at Stangard.Tell Gadda of the hardships you observed'Sithric has been sent by Théoden King and is an advisor of Edoras. I... have no power over him, and he asserts his will in all that goes on here.

'I am sorry that we cannot welcome you here more warmly, according to our traditions, ${PLAYER}. But if you wish to do my men a kindness, you may help them with their duties.

'Gadda is a good man and will know where you can begin.''Ah, Stanric sent you to see me? I understand -- I will not say a word to Sithric on this matter.

'I have plenty of ideas as to how you can help in Stangard, ${PLAYER}. Let us begin with delivering rations, performing the watch, and dealing with some of the petty crime we have been experiencing of late.

'Please go and help the men with their duties. You will be of great help!''Yes, the Men of Stangard carry many burdens. There was hope that Sithric would make things better here, but life is harder now.

'Men are hungrier, and many leave and do not return. Those who stay carry more weight than ever.'You found an ornate spear upon the corpse of a goblin Warg-rider. The quality and make of the spear seemed unusual for a goblin.Gwilum is at the gate to Lower Barnavon.

You should bring the spear you found to Gwilum.This ornate spear is of a much higher quality than is usual for goblins. Perhaps it may hold a clue as to the origins of these Warg-riders. You should bring it to Gwilum at Barnavon.'Indeed, this spear seems to be of particular quality... not at all like that of a coblun -- goblins as you call them. However, I'm not familiar with these decorations.

'I will need to study this further.'The Rohirrim taskmaster wants blotchy skins. He can be found in the Rohirrim encampment of Forthbrond in the Isendale.You have accepted a task to acquire blotchy skins. You are to deliver them to the Rohirrim taskmaster at Forthbrond.Wanted: Blotchy skins from the beasts in eastern Dunland. Collect them and deliver them to the taskmaster at Forthbrond to earn favour with Théodred's Riders.Wanted: Blotchy skins from the beasts in eastern Dunland.'Well, that is a few less beasts stalking after our horses. My thanks to you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Rohirrim taskmaster wants decorative sword sheaths. He can be found in the Rohirrim encampment of Forthbrond in the Isendale.You have accepted a task to acquire decorative sword sheaths. You are to deliver them to the Rohirrim taskmaster at Forthbrond.Wanted: Decorative sword sheaths from enemies in eastern Dunland. Collect them and deliver them to the taskmaster at Forthbrond to earn favour with Théodred's Riders.Wanted: Decorative sword sheaths from enemies in eastern Dunland.'Well, that is a few less threats that we will need to fight in the days ahead. My thanks to you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Rohirrim taskmaster wants marked furs. He can be found in the Rohirrim encampment of Forthbrond in the Isendale.You have accepted a task to acquire marked furs. You are to deliver them to the Rohirrim taskmaster at Forthbrond.Wanted: Marked furs from the beasts in eastern Dunland. Collect them and deliver them to the taskmaster at Forthbrond to earn favour with Théodred's Riders.Wanted: Marked furs from the beasts in eastern Dunland.'Well, that is a few less beasts stalking after our horses. My thanks to you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Rohirrim taskmaster wants punctured shields. He can be found in the Rohirrim encampment of Forthbrond in the Isendale.You have accepted a task to acquire punctured shields. You are to deliver them to the Rohirrim taskmaster at Forthbrond.Wanted: Punctured shields from enemies in eastern Dunland. Collect them and deliver them to the taskmaster at Forthbrond to earn favour with Théodred's Riders.Wanted: Punctured shields from enemies in eastern Dunland.'Well, that is a few less threats that we will need to fight in the days ahead. My thanks to you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Rohirrim taskmaster wants speckled ears. He can be found in the Rohirrim encampment of Forthbrond in the Isendale.You have accepted a task to acquire speckled ears. You are to deliver them to the Rohirrim taskmaster at Forthbrond.Wanted: Speckled ears from the beasts in eastern Dunland. Collect them and deliver them to the taskmaster at Forthbrond to earn favour with Théodred's Riders.Wanted: Speckled ears from the beasts in eastern Dunland.'Well, that is a few less beasts stalking after our horses. My thanks to you.'You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.A band of disorganized Orcs has roamed into the areas south of the Cuthstan and has vandalized the monument. The leader of the Rohirrim there hopes that thinning the tribe's numbers may scare the rest of the Orcs into retreating from the area.The tribe of Orc-vandals is south-west of the Cuthstan.

Lanbert has asked you to thin out the numbers of the Orc-tribe, in the hopes of scaring them from the area.Defeat Nink-hai sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Nink-hai skirmishers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Nink-hai ravagers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lanbert is at the Rohirrim-camp at the base of the Cuthstan.

You have thinned the numbers of the Orc-tribe, and Lanbert awaits your return.Talk to Lanbert at the Cuthstan-camp'I assure you that the wretched Orcs responsible for damaging the Cuthstan pose no further threat. They seem wholly disorganized. We are simply here to protect the statue, and that is what we will do.

'Their intrusion onto our lands from their caves in the mountains, however, has become quite bothersome. I wager that if you were to thin their numbers a bit, they would feel threatened enough to retreat back into their holes.''The Orcs have built some small huts and tents to the south, and there have been several roaming just south of the roads. Remember to return here when your work is done.''Well done. The blow you have dealt these Orcs is sure to have left them reeling. Without a doubt, they will be fleeing from this region in no time.'Many workers at the Barnavon Mine were wounded or slain when the mine was overrun by bugan. More miners are needed to restore operations.Daf, Edar, Galvin, Hadun, and Idwal all live within Barnavon.

Gwilum has instructed you to summon the workers Daf, Edar, Galvin, Hadun, and Idwal to the Barnavon Mine.Gwilum is at the gate to Barnavon.

You should return to Gwilum with the workers' answers.Talk to Gwilum in Barnavon'Melvun is right. We must make sure the mine is being worked and quickly enough that Prudwen Brehur does not notice the disruption.

'There are a few of the Boar-clan miners left in the village who might be convinced to help in the mines for the sake of their people. Daf, Edar, Galvin, Hadun, and Idwal all dwell within Barnavon. Go to them and tell them of their clan's need.''What do you want, Duvodiad?

'What is this you say? The mine was attacked by bugan? Of course I will go and at once!

'Thank you, but I need no escort.''The Barnavon Mine was overrun by bugan? How many were hurt?

'Alas, many good men were lost there. Of course, I will come to the aid of my people!

'Nay, I need no escort... I am man enough to take care of myself.''My brother worked in the mine! Is he well? Bervun... ah, he is well, you say?

'I do not wish to bring trouble upon my people, but I have a wife and children... I do not know if I would risk my life in those mines.''Bugan? In the mine? I will get my pick at once...!''I would not work in those mines if Prudwen Brehur himself put a knife to my throat or my children's.

'There are few enough of the Boar-clan left... I would rather die by my own hand, than be devoured by bugan.''It should have been expected that not all would risk themselves, even for the good of their people.

'Nevertheless, three is better than none. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'You found a strange token bearing a foreign symbol upon a Dunlending warrior.Gwilum is at the gate to Lower Barnavon.

You should bring the token you found to Gwilum.The symbol on this token does not appear to be of Dunlending origin. Gwilum at Barnavon may be interested in studying it.'This token disturbs me, ${PLAYER}. I have seen this symbol upon the trappings of the Warg-riders. It is not a symbol of my people, and I know not why the warriors of the Uch-lûth would carry such a thing.

'It troubles me to think that my people might consider allying themselves with goblins and Wargs.'Penda has spotted an unusual visitor to the Wailing Hills, north of Aster Hill.The clearing can be found in the north-east section of the Wailing Hills, north of Aster Hill.

Penda has mentioned meeting unexpected visitors in a clearing far to the north.Talk to the visitor in the clearing, far to the north-east'You have proven yourself to be a true friend to the Rohirrim, and I believe you are worthy of receiving some interesting information.

'As you know, I was away from camp, scouting among the hills to the north, when the trouble began. It was there that I encountered, concealed among a clearing of trees, allies unexpected.
 
'I think it would be best if you visited them for yourself. Go north-east, beyond Aster Hill, and seek out the clearing. Their presence in these lands leads me to believe that they may be in need of assistance, perhaps your abilities would be of use to them.''A pleasure to make your acquaintance. My name is Landroval, and I am brother to the Windlord, Gwaihir. 

'I have observed some of your deeds in these lands, and I believe that you may be capable of helping me with my task.''Do you need a bit of guidance? Travel north of here, beyond Aster Hill, and you will come to a small clearing of trees. Introduce yourself to the company there and lend them aid if you can.

'May fortune go with you, friend.'Odda is concerned about the number of supplies being moved into the Nink-hai camp and from whence the supplies might be coming.The Nink-hai Orc-tribe can be found south-west of Odda's tent.

Odda has given you a torch which can be used to set fire to the supply-stores of the Orcs.Odda can be found near the road south of the Cuthstan.

The Orcs' supply-stores have been destroyed by your actions, and Odda is awaiting news of your success.'These Orcs, the Nink-hai...there is more to them than meets the eye. You saw their swords yourself. Tell me, were they typical Orc-swords? Nay, I believe that weapons and supplies are being transported here from afar, through hidden passages under the Misty Mountains.

'They have gathered great caches of tools and food in order to fortify themselves away from their caves. Their resources must be destroyed if we ever hope to drive them back.

'Take this torch and set fire to their supply-store, then return to me once the deed is done.''Without their supplies, we may yet be able to drive the Nink-hai back to the mountain holes from whence they came!

'Thank you again, ${PLAYER}.'Stanric has given you leave to do as you will in Stangard.Sabert guards the north gate of Stangard, and Tatwine tends the stable near the Mead Hall, in Eorlsmead.

You should assist Sabert and Tatwine with anything they might need that can be done without interference from Sithric.Help Tatwine to better tend the horsesHelp Sabert deal with the threat of vicious dogs in the plainsGadda is near the Mead Hall in Stangard.Tell Gadda of your successes in Stangard'It is good that Stanric has given you leave to do as you will. If only I had that liberty....

'Ah well. Sabert and Tatwine are good men... and better yet, are not loyal to Sithric. They will accept your help more readily than the others if you wish to lend aid.''Sabert guards the north gate, and you will find Tatwine at the stable.''You are an admirable ${RACE}, ${PLAYER}! I wish Sithric had the wisdom to see what good could be done here if only he stepped out of our way!'Gadda and Tatwine have set up their new free settlement on the farmstead where you planted seeds not long ago.Tatwine, happy with his new position as a free man maintaining the farming work you started, has invited you to join him in his maintenance of the farm.

You should help Tatwine with the farm chores.Harvest the crops from the seeds you planted (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Pull weeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tatwine is tending the fields at the abandoned farm.

You should return to Tatwine with the goods you gathered.'Do you see, ${PLAYER}? I have freed myself from Stangard, and now your efforts will not have been in vain.

'I am a farmer in my heart, and this is where I belong. I do not know if I will ever return to Stangard, but men in Eorlsmead who want for food need only ask. It has been far too long since crops were grown in these stark lands.

'Would you care to tend the farm for a while? I find it very tranquil work.''I cannot thank you enough for inspiring me to do this, ${PLAYER}. No matter what the consequences for my leaving Stangard, I believe that this is right. What you did for us... was right.'Frithstan's soldiers have been captured and taken into a mountain-cave by the Mor-hai Orcs.The entrance to the Orc-caves may be found along the western rock wall in the Wailing Hills, behind the Orc-camp that held Frithstan.

Frithstan believes that his men have been taken alive and are being held within the nearby Orc-caves.Enter into the Orc-caveThe entrance to the Orc-caves may be found along the western rock wall in the Wailing Hills, behind the Orc-camp that held Frithstan.

The Rohirrim-captives are being held within caves by the Mor-hai Orcs.Talk to the first captive and release himThe entrance to the Orc-caves may be found along the western rock wall in the Wailing Hills, behind the Orc-camp that held Frithstan.

The Rohirrim-captives are being held within caves by the Mor-hai Orcs.Talk to the second captive and release himThe entrance to the Orc-caves may be found along the western rock wall in the Wailing Hills, behind the Orc-camp that held Frithstan.

The Rohirrim-captives are being held within caves by the Mor-hai Orcs.Rescue the third captive from his cellFrithstan can be found at his camp to along the road north of the Cuthstan.

He awaits your return from the Orc-caves.Return to Frithstan's camp and talk to Frithstan'The Orcs managed to overwhelm us with their numbers. They drove away our steeds and took my men into their cave. I heard one of the defilers speaking about brewing some sort of poison, and I fear for the lives of my warriors.

'Enter into their dwelling and release as many of the captives as possible. Radmund, Gyrth, Lytman, and Odda were all with me during the assault. Find them quickly!''I am not too badly injured, thank you, friend.

'The Orcs... they brew some vile poison using spider's venom and corrupted plant-roots. I fear that they plan to test this poison on the other captives. Hurry, you must hurry save the others!''Thank you... for saving me. Another dose of this poison... and I would surely have perished!

'My pain will subside, but you must press on. Some of the others have been given larger doses of the poison.'You recognize this soldier as your ally Odda. He does not appear to be breathing, and despite your best efforts, you cannot revive him. Odda has already succumbed to the effects of the poison.'You have returned and have freed some of my men! Well done... but where is our companion Odda?'

He looks at you for a moment, then tilts his head down.

'I see. We are fools to have acted so aggressively against the Orcs, and dear Odda has paid the ultimate price for it. We owe you gratitude, for we would have met the same fate as he, were it not for you.'Stanric is alive, defying the lies of Sithric. It is clear that Stanric must be freed at once, so that justice may be done for this betrayal.Stanric is in the lock-house.

You should free Stanric from his bonds.Help Stanric take back StangardStanric is now in the Mead Hall, alone, in his proper place.

You should speak with Stanric once more.Talk to Stanric'Sithric is a lying, greedy, power-hungry traitor. I must have justice for what was done here! He and I may disagree, but imprisonment and death have never been warranted.

'But perhaps it is time I stand up for what is really right for Stangard and risk breaking the law at last. Free me from these bonds, ${PLAYER}!''Come, my friend. Let us go and end this now. Sithric must pay for what he has done to me... and to Stangard!''You have my gratitude and the lasting friendship of Stangard for what you have done, ${PLAYER}. You will always be welcome among the Men of Stangard.

'Please... take this as a token of my appreciation! I hope to see more of you here at Stangard, ${PLAYER}, for things will be improving again for my men, no matter what the consequences with the king.'The Rangers Saeradan, Amlan, and Andreg have tracked Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, from the Windfells in Enedwaith to the Gravenwood of Dunland.Amlan told you to summon Andreg and accompany him to the Rohirrim scout-camp to meet with Saeradan.

If you become separated from Andreg, you may summon him using the bird-whistle Amlan gave you.Aid Andreg with Eyes in the ForestAndreg has accompanied you for some distance. Now the time has come to part ways.

You should speak with Andreg.

<rgb=#FF0000>Advancing this quest will no longer allow you to summon Andreg and will cancel any quests bestowed by him that are currently underway.</rgb>Saeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Andreg told you to continue on to the Rohirrim scout-camp and let Saeradan know that he is scouting the wood to the south and east.Talk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp'When we first came to this place, we stumbled upon a party of Rohirrim scouts, led by Théodred, the king's son. They were attempting to creep behind the Dunlending lines, but unfortunately for them, the Horse-lords are not the most cautious warriors.

'We helped them to sneak past their enemies and establish a camp here in the Gravenwood. Saeradan remained with them, believing it to our mutual benefit to aid them. Their mission here might help us to regain Gwyllion's trail.

'You should head east at once to the Rohirrim's scout-camp and join with Saeradan. Take this whistle...it is made to sound like the call of a bird not found here. If you sound it, Andreg will come to take you to Saeradan.''${PLAYER}! It is good that you have come, though I must say I did not doubt much that our paths would cross once more.

'There is great evil afoot, and we could use your aid!''You have been of great aid to me upon this road, ${PLAYER}. I must turn aside now and scout the woods to the south and east.

'If you turn north, you will eventually come upon the Rohirrim scout-camp, where Saeradan awaits you.

'Farewell, ${PLAYER}. May we meet again!'

