'Farewell, ${PLAYER}. May we meet again!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Advancing this quest will no longer allow you to summon Andreg.</rgb>'${PLAYER}! It is good that you have come, though I must say I did not doubt much that our paths would cross once more.

'There is great evil afoot, and we could use your aid!'Andreg is taking you to meet with Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp; however, he needs help with his own mission first.Andreg has asked you to collect leaves and bark covered in the strange corruption so that Saeradan might be able to examine it.Collect piles of oozing corruption in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the corrupted materials you collected to Andreg.'While returning here from the Rohirrim scout-camp, I thought I saw some strange form of corruption in the wood... like none I have ever seen. Unnatural, it seemed to me.

'Saeradan knows more of this sort of corruption than I. Perhaps we should collect some as we journey back to the scout-camp and bring it to him.

'Will you help?''Aye, this should be enough. We should bring this to Saeradan as soon as possible.'Saeradan and his companions sensed a queer stillness about the Gravenwood when they arrived and are seeking answers as to why the forest would feel so empty.The Mustering Tree lies to the north-west of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Saeradan asked you to scout to locations for clues regarding the evil in the Gravenwood.Scout the Mustering TreeThe Tree of Tribute lies almost due south of the Mustering Tree, south-west of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Saeradan wants you to scout two locations for clues regarding the evil in the Gravenwood.Scout the Tree of Tribute'${PLAYER}, when I and my companions first came here, we noticed almost at once a queer stillness about the forest. There is undoubtedly a foul presence at work here, and I would wager that Gwyllion has something to do with it, but thus far we have been unable to find the source.

'Perhaps you will aid us in this task? There are two trees -- one to the north-west and one to the south-west -- which were clearly once used in some Dunlending ritual. One is called the Mustering Tree, for it is where the forces of Dunland gathered to go to war against Gondor and Rohan long ago. The other is called the Tree of Tribute, for a brave Dunlending warrior stood alone there against a strong force of their enemies and sacrificed himself to allow his clan to escape.

'Search these places for any clues, then follow the signs wherever they may lead. When you have discovered the source of the evil here, return to me. I have provided you tools to dig with, should the need arise.''Scout the Mustering Tree and the Tree of Tribute, and tell me if you find anything.'A company of Ox-clan warriors are encamped on the western edge of the Gravenwood, arrayed for war.The Ox-clan captain's tent may be found within Rhuvel-cadlus, in the valley below Cuthric's post.

Cuthric wants you to place a desecrated ox-skull before the tent of the Ox-clan's captain in an effort to goad him into single combat.Place the desecrated ox-skull before the tent of the Ox-clan's captainCuthric is hiding on the ridge above Rhuvel-cadlus.

You should return to Cuthric and tell him that you have done as he asked.Talk to Cuthric'I wonder if you have the temerity to provoke the captain of these wild men? Perhaps, perhaps not.

'Prove it to me. Take this ox-skull, upon which I have engraved insulting signs, and place it before the tent of the Uch-lûth's captain. If he has any sense of honour, he will come forth and do battle with you.

'If you defeat him, perhaps the Ox-clan will return to their homes peaceably.''Ha! I wish I could have seen the wild man's face!

'At least it shows that some Dunlendings do have a sense of honour which can be insulted.'When Saeradan asked you to search near the Mustering Tree and the Tree of Tribute for signs of other evil tokens, he gave you a pick-axe with which to dig them up... which you promptly lost.Saeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in the Gravenwood of Dunland.

Saeradan has spoken with the Rohirrim and is waiting upon you.Talk to Saeradan to receive the pick-axeThe Tree of Tribute lies to the west of the Rohirrim Scout-camp.

You should return to the Tree of Tribute and complete the task Saeradan set before you.Use the pick-axe in your inventory to accept the quest Seeking a Solution, then complete it'${PLAYER}! I am disappointed. If we are to unravel the mystery of this wood, we must find more tokens... yet you managed to lose the pick-axe I gave you? Very well, let me see if one of these Rohirrim brought a pick with him into these wilds.''We are fortunate. These good people did indeed have a pick-axe among their goods. Go now and complete your task!'The work is difficult and the conditions poor beneath Isengard, and even those who serve Saruman remain prisoners.The ill-tempered Uruk gave you a small food portion to deliver to an unruly prisoner in the left-hand cell in the dungeons.The prisoner seems somehow familiar to you.Wait... can it be?Egfrith has been imprisoned beneath Isengard, despite her betrayal of Rohan.Talk to Egfrith beneath Isengard'Yar! You there! I've got better to do than bring food to haughty prisoners in the dungeons. You take this small portion to the unruly prisoner in the left-hand cell in the dungeons. Maybe the scarcity of the food will teach her she's no better than the rest of us!''You take that small portion of food to the unruly prisoner in the left-hand cell in the dungeons. Maybe the scarcity of the food will teach her she's no better than the rest of us!'The woman does not look you in the eye when you hand the small food portion through the bars.'It is you, ${PLAYER}? I did not know if I could trust my eyes... I have seen others during my captivity, others I have betrayed, and they were not truly here. No, you have been brought here for another unknowable purpose of Saruman.'

Egfrith stares at you sadly, her face drawn and her armour hanging on her now-gaunt frame.

'When I returned to Isengard with what I had learned of Boromir's journey, Saruman was wroth. The dream that sent Boromir in search of Imladris had the feel of prophecy to the son of Gondor, but to Saruman it signaled even more. In it he saw the unravelling of countless plans, schemes he hid from even his closest advisors, and it filled him with a great and terrible rage, frightening to behold. That I had not slain Boromir, as he commanded, was beyond his understanding, and from that failure he wove a tapestry of cruel words that ensnared Rohan in a spiral unto doom.

'But that was not the worst, ${PLAYER}. The worst were the last words he spoke to me, before the Uruks carried me to this cell. "You are a blind fool, Egfrith, to believe that Rohan would fall without help. How oft did I tell you Théoden grew ill, and his strength waned, and he would never recover? That was my doing," Saruman gloated, "a gift carefully-administered by others of my servants. But you despaired at the first opportunity! Let that knowledge eat you alive, broken hound of Rohan! You abandoned your king and your kingdom, for yours was no strength at all, and now you will waste away in the dark, and your only companions will be men of Dunland and Rohan who will know you for a traitor."

'I failed my king, ${PLAYER}, and I failed Rohan. How could I have been so blind, so easily used?'

Egfrith smiles, the dry lines of her face cracking with the unfamiliar effort.

'It is best that you are not really here, ${PLAYER}, for I do not think I could stand to see you or our companions in this place: weary Meneldir, a Ranger who insists he is no Dúnadan, or noble Boromir, so far from home. Better to believe they came to the end of their respective journeys with the successes they deserved, and earned the happiness due them, unlike Egfrith, great fool of Rohan, prisoner of her own deception.

'But that deception... it was for Rohan.

'Always.'The circumstances of Stanric's death are certainly suspicious, so you decide to investigate further.Stanric's house is near the Mead Hall in Stangard.

You should investigate Stanric's house, and do your best to keep beneath the notice of the residents of Stangard using what sneaking skill you can muster.Investigate Stanric's houseSomething glints on the floor of Stanric's house in Stangard.

You should investigate the glinting object more closely.Investigate the glinting itemCynred is at the lock-house in Stangard.

You should find Cynred and ask him why his jail keys are in Stanric's home.Ask Cynred why his jail-keys were on the floor of Stanric's homeAccording to Cynred, Stanric is down below in the lock-house.

You should find Stanric at once.Find Stanric in the lock-house'The circumstances surrounding Stanric's death are most suspicious; do you not agree? You should investigate his house, near the Mead Hall.

'If you see anything suspicious, you should by all means investigate further. Just...be careful not to be seen, ${PLAYER}. I worry that all of Stangard will be seeking your capture. You should move with as much stealth as you can muster.'Cynred glances from side to side with a look of panic on his face.

'Sithric tells me I will be committing treason if I tell of what passed. You found the hint I left behind though: Stanric is not dead. Sithric is ordering him kept below.

'The guards and I were ordered to lock him away, so we did. Sithric said he would have Stanric killed if I did not help, so I complied.

'I will not stop you from righting this wrong. I cannot believe I ever trusted such a man as Sithric!''${PLAYER}! I cannot believe you found me!'The Slade of Shadows appears to be a focal point for the evil that is growing within the Gravenwood.Druggavar can be found within the Slade of Shadows, south of Andreg's position.

Andreg has asked you to defeat the Druggavar summoned by the Old Woman of the Mountain.Defeat Druggavar at the Slade of Shadows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Among the creatures inhabiting the Slade of Shadows are the Druggavar. The presence of these fell spirits is a clear sign that the Old Woman of the Mountain is near at hand, for it was she who summoned them at first to Enedwaith.

'As you investigate the Slade of Shadows, banish as many of the Druggavar as you are able... such fell creatures cannot be allowed to enter our world, for their combined power may prove the undoing of the Free Peoples.'You must help the people of Carreglyn stand against Saruman, if you can, and when you are satisfied, Nona thinks you should meet up with the Rangers in Gravenwood.The Ranger Amlan is east of Carreglyn, just over the border with Gravenwood.

Nona wants you to help the friendly people of Carreglyn as much as you can and to then meet up with the Rangers in Gravenwood when you are satisfied.Help the people of Carreglyn as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Amlan on the western border of GravenwoodSaeradan is at the Rohirrim Scout-camp, east of Amlan's camp in Gravenwood.

Amlan told you that a small party of Rohirrim have come to Gravenwood and are meeting with Saeradan.Talk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-campThéodred is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in Gravenwood.

You have encountered Saeradan again and he has introduced you to Théodred, the son of the king of Rohan.Talk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp'I do not think Carreglyn is lost, ${PLAYER}. There are still good people in this land, strong warriors who did not accept gold from Saruman to fight his battles. Help them as much as you can! If we can aid them, they may stay resolute against the Wizard.

'Just inside the boundary of the Gravenwood, to the east, one of your Ranger friends has established a small camp. Once you have helped the people of Carreglyn to your satisfaction, travel east into Gravenwood and meet up with this Ranger.''We are well met, ${PLAYER}! It is good to see a friendly face.

'You should speak with Saeradan. A small band of Rohirrim have come to the Gravenwood, and he is meeting with their leader. Their camp is to the east.''Your journey through Dunland for Lheu Brenin is almost at its end, ${PLAYER}? What have you learned of the Dunlending clans?'

Saeradan listens to your report.

'I see. Saruman's influence is greater than we thought. It is good that you sought to help the people resist him, even if it bears little fruit.

'This man here is Théodred, the son of the king of Rohan. He has crossed into Dunland with a small party on a similar mission: to see what is happening in the heart of Dunland.''We are met in dangerous times, ${PLAYER}. You run errands for folk long sworn to be the enemies of my people.'

Théodred sighs heavily.

'It has been a long time since the Dunlendings crossed into my father's kingdom with design of conquest. Without the urging I fear Saruman is giving to them, they would not have the courage to do so again. The Wizard has done my people a great wrong with this, and he must pay for it.

'My men and I forded the Isen and came by animal paths into this wood. That is where we encountered Saeradan and learned of his mission. We could use your help, if you can spare it.''You should go speak with Saeradan. He has been meeting with the party of Rohirrim that have come to Gravenwood. Their camp is east of here.''This man is Théodred, son of the king of Rohan. He has come into Dunland with a small party of men to gather information.''Help the people of Carreglyn to stand against their enemies. We must keep them from falling further under the sway of Saruman.

'Once you have aided them as much as you can, travel east across the border with Gravenwood and meet with the Ranger at his camp.'The stillness of Gravenwood has Théodred and his men on edge, and they have asked for your help to set their minds at ease.Théodred's men have felt the watchful presence at an old tree to the north-west of his camp, and in the back of Uvel-cadlus, the Dragon-clan camp to the north.

Théodred wants you to see if you can sense a watchful presence at the places his men experienced such feelings.Check near the mustering tree for signs of a watchful presenceCheck in the back of Uvel-cadlus for signs of a watchful presenceThéodred is at his camp in the eastern reaches of Gravenwood.

You have sought out the watchful presence in Gravenwood, but did not experience anything unusual.Talk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp'We are all ill at ease in this forest, ${PLAYER}, and your Ranger friend here is not the reassuring sort. My men have reported feeling a watchful presence as they walk beneath the trees. I do not like it.

'I have heard that Saruman can move about, unseen by mortal eyes. Could it be his presence my men have felt?

'If you oppose the Wizard, go to these places and see if you feel a presence at them, as my men do. One of these places is a gnarled tree to the north-west, and the other is a camp of Dunlendings far to the north, Uvel-cadlus, between the arms of the mountains.''You felt nothing at those locations? Perhaps my men have been too long in this wood. It is taking a toll on even their stout hearts.''Go to those places and see if you feel the watchful presence my men experienced. These are the locations: a gnarled tree to the north-west, and the back of Uvel-cadlus, a camp of Dunlendings far to the north.'You have travelled through the regions mentioned by Lheu Brenin's prisoner, and have learned much about the state of things in Dunland.You should help Théodred's men deal with the mysteries of the Gravenwood before returning to Lheu Brenin with what you have learned in Dunland.Help the people of the Gravenwood as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, report to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva'It is time you returned to Lheu Brenin with what you have learned of Dunland, ${PLAYER}. But I ask you to keep this in mind: there are Dunlendings and there are Dunlendings. This Falcon-clan may oppose Saruman, and for that I am thankful, but they still bear no love for my people.

'Do not mistake them for friends in anything but necessity.''It is good to see you again, friend from afar. You have been long away. What is the situation with the other clans? How many have thrown their lot in with Saruman?'

Lheu Brenin listens with interest to your news from other regions of Dunland: of the herds of the Starkmoor, of the distant folk of the Dunbog, of the iron mines of Carreglyn, of armies marshalling and of frightened townsfolk.

'Saruman's grasp on our land and its people is tighter than I thought! Still, we have closer matters to attend to for now.''Dunlendings bear no love for my people, or for yours. The Falcon-clan is no different, but if they help us against Saruman, perhaps we can set aside our differences for the moment.

'If you will help my men delve into the mysteries of the Gravenwood, I would greatly appreciate it. Once you have done so, you can return to the leader of the Falcon-clan with what you have learned.'The emissary from Isengard that Lheu Brenin has imprisoned is not doing well, and the leader of the Falcon-clan wants you to try and learn something of Saruman's plans before the captive dies.Lheu Brenin is outside his home in Tûr Morva.

Lheu Brenin has asked you to come with him to speak with his captive.Talk to Lheu Brenin and travel with him to speak with the captive<rgb=#FF0000>If you left the Isengard Depths without the Reminder of Captivity in your inventory, go to the cart just to the right of the gate of Isengard and use it to return to the Depths.</rgb>

You have been taken prisoner and brought to Isengard. The Falcon-clan has betrayed you, and you are now the prisoner of Saruman.'I thought that the captive might tell us more about Saruman's plans if he was hungrier. I told Nai to stop feeding him, but now he has taken ill and will not last much longer.

'Come with me to speak with him before he dies. There will be no more chances to learn what the Wizard is up to behind his walls before it comes to open war.

'We will give him a meal if he cooperates. That may be the encouragement he needs.''We will go to speak with the captive and learn what we can of Saruman's plans. He does not have long to live, and we must go now or lose the opportunity.''Make yourself at home, little ${RACE}! You now belong to me and will do as I say!'

Fâsh laughs heartily.

'We will find tasks enough to keep you busy, and once you die, someone else will take your place. Sharkû doesn't lack for thralls, little ${RACE}, and there is plenty of work to be done in the pits!'You have been imprisoned beneath Isengard and must now report to Fâsh, an Uruk-hai charged with maintaining the work of the Saruman's thralls.

<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon your Uruk Overseer, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>Fâsh has assigned an Uruk-hai to keep an eye on you in the caverns beneath Isengard and to give you work. If your overseer wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.Fâsh has assigned an Uruk-hai to keep an eye on you in the caverns beneath Isengard and to give you work. If your overseer wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.Fâsh has assigned an Uruk-hai to keep an eye on you in the caverns beneath Isengard and to give you work. If your overseer wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.Fâsh is in the centre of the caverns beneath Isengard.

You have finished a series of tasks for your Uruk-hai overseer and should return to Fâsh.'I've assigned someone to keep an eye on you and give you work. If he's not happy with your work, I will hear about it.

'You don't want that, little ${RACE}.

'If your overseer wanders off for a spot of grub or a swig of brew, rattle your shackles, and he'd better come running. Don't let me see you without him.'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon your Uruk Overseer, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>'Talk to your overseer and do the work he asks of you! Rattle your shackles if he has wandered off, and that'll draw him near. If it doesn't, he'll have to answer to me!'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon your Uruk Overseer, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>'Talk to your overseer and do the work he asks of you! Rattle your shackles if he has wandered off, and that'll draw him near. If it doesn't, he'll have to answer to me!''Talk to your overseer and do the work he asks of you! Rattle your shackles if he has wandered off, and that'll draw him near. If it doesn't, he'll have to answer to me!''I did not expect much from you, but you did all right... for a ${RACE}. You must know it is pointless to resist! That's a shame. There's usually some sport in getting the Old Man's thralls to behave.

'Disappointing. But enough of that: time is wasting. You need to come with me. The Old Man wants you.'You have been summoned before Saruman, but for what fell purpose you cannot guess.In the caverns below Isengard, Fâsh is ready to bring you to Saruman.Talk to Fâsh and go with him to see SarumanAs it appears that you are still of some use to Saruman, you have survived your encounter with the Wizard. You have been deposited before Morflak, your new handler while within the ring of Isengard.Talk to Morflak in the Ring of Isengard'You had better come with me. The Old Man does not like to be kept waiting. If you displease him, perhaps he will no longer need you alive! Ah, wouldn't that be nice?''Come with me! The old man does not like to be kept waiting!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>'It looks like this is your lucky day, vermin! You now have the privilege of working for me. You had better prove yourself useful, or it's back to the pits with you.

'Sharkû may want you alive, but my friends are quite skilled at inflicting enough pain to hurt, but not enough to kill.

'Unless I give them the word, that is. Then it's all killing.'Morflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the Ring of Isengard.

<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon Morflak's Lackey, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>Morflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the ring of Isengard and to give you work. If this Uruk-hai wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.Complete 'Their Best Interests' for Morflak's lackeyMorflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the ring of Isengard and to give you work. If this Uruk-hai wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.Complete 'Raiding the Larder' for Morflak's lackeyMorflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the ring of Isengard and to give you work. If this Uruk-hai wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.Complete 'Trivial Business' for Morflak's lackeyMorflak is waiting to speak with you within the ring of Isengard.'We are all servants of Sharkû here, but some of us are given more freedom than others. I am one of these, little ${RACE}, and in return I help my friends.

'I have assigned one of my trusted lackeys to watch you while you do my work. If he lets you out of his sight, rattle your shackles to draw him near. If he does this too often he may find himself out of my favour, then out of a head...in that order!'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon Morflak's Lackey, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>'Talk to my lackey and do the work that he gives you. If he's wandered away, rattle your shackles, and he'd better appear. If he doesn't, he'll answer to me!'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon your Uruk Overseer, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>'Talk to my lackey and do the work he gives you. If he's wandered away, rattle your shackles, and he'd better appear. If he doesn't, he'll answer to me!''Talk to my lackey and do the work that he gives you. If he's wandered away, rattle your shackles, and he'd better appear. If he doesn't, he'll answer to me!''I may have been wrong about you after all. These others complain about the work they do for me, and it is only fear of my retribution that keeps them in line. But you have served me well, and without complaint.

'I do not think you need a shadow any longer. You will stay in line or you will answer to Morflak; that will be guard enough!'Morflak wants you to report to Fâsh with the message that you no longer need a guard to watch your comings and goings. Fâsh is to keep you busy until Morflak has need of you.Fâsh is in the caverns beneath Isengard, accessible by a door directly north of the tower. Once in the depths, you should take the sloping paths downward to Fâsh's command.

Morflak has sent you to deliver a message to Fâsh and to do more work for him.Talk to Fâsh in the Isengard DepthsBarkh is in the kitchens beneath Isengard, south-west of the main cavern.

Fâsh has sent you to help out in the kitchens once again.Talk to Barkh in the kitchensThe floor of the kitchen is covered in slop.

Barkh has given you a dirty rag and wants you to clean the slop up off the floor.Clean up piles of slop in the kitchens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dulan in the kitchens has tried to catch your eye.

You should talk to Dulan and see what he wants.Uruk-hai meals can be found on the tables in the kitchens below Isengard.

Dulan has secretly given you a small quantity of poison and wants you to add it to one of the Uruk-hai meals.Slop covers the floor of the kitchens below Isengard.

Barkh wants you to clean up the slop.Clean up piles of slop in the kitchens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})It is time for you to squeeze out the dirty rag into the slop bucket in the kitchens.Barkh is in the kitchens below Isengard, south-west of the main cavern.Barkh wants you to fill a pan from the slop bucket in the kitchens and carry it to the bucket in the dungeons from where the prisoners are fed, as you did before.Fill up a bucket of slop from the slop bucket in the kitchensBaldgar wants to speak with you. He is in the dungeons below Isengard.Talk to Baldgar in the dungeon'Go to the caverns and tell Fâsh that he is to keep you busy until I call for you. If he gives you any trouble, you come and let me know.

'You get to the depths by way of a door north of the tower. Once you're down there, keep taking the sloping paths down into the centre of the cavern, where Fâsh has his command.''Fâsh will give you no trouble, if he knows what's good for him. If he does, you send him to me. He will not defy the will of Morflak.

'Fâsh is in the caverns below. You get to the depths by way of a door north of the tower. Once you're down there, keep taking the sloping paths down into the centre of the cavern, where Fâsh has his command.''Morflak says that you can walk about unguarded? Well, it won't be my hide if you cause trouble.'

Fâsh snorts loudly.

'Go help Barkh in the kitchens. You know where they are. And be quick about it! You might be Morflak's latest pet, but I won't have you getting underfoot and slowing things down!''What are you still doing here? You might be under Morflak's protection, for now, but if you cross me, I may forget that for a moment...and a moment is all it would take to ensure you'd never cross me again!

'Go help Barkh in the kitchens!''Back for more? I'm surprised you're still alive!'

Barkh sneers at you, his fangs bared, and hands you a dirty rag.

'Clean the slop up off the floor. You know how it's done.''Clean up that slop! You know what to do!''What are you doing? There's slop to clean up!''Hey...you there...no, don't look at me. I don't want to attract attention.'

Dulan keeps wiping down the table and talks to you out of the side of his mouth.

'I've gotten my hands on a pinch of poison, just a thimble-full. If I give it to you, can you add it to one of the meals for the Uruk-hai? Don't let anyone see you!'

Dulan silently hands you a small half-shell containing a few drops of clear liquid.'Back to work, vermin! Slop still covers this floor!''Be careful...do not let them see you adding the poison...and do not stand so near to me. You will make them suspicious!''What is taking you so long? Back to work, vermin! Clean up that slop!''Don't give me that dirty rag! Squeeze it out in the slop bucket first!''You do everything slowly and poorly! Is every ${RACE} as useless as you?

'Go fill up a pan from the slop bucket and carry it to the bucket in the dungeons. It's time for the prisoners to be fed again!''Have you lost your way? The slop bucket is right there! Fill up a pan and bring it to the bucket in the dungeons so the prisoners can be fed! Move, or I'll tan your hide!''Get to the dungeons! The prisoners need to be fed! If you stay here, I'll make you the main course!''You have managed to slip away from your guard? That is good! That is very good, indeed!'

Baldgar peers from side to side, making sure the guards are out of earshot.

'I am working on a plan to escape, ${PLAYER}, but I could use your help.'Baldgar is forming an escape plan, and he says a fellow prisoner is the key to its success.Acca is in the dungeons below Isengard, located in the north-west corner of the main cavern.Talk to Acca in the dungeonsAcca is imprisoned in the dungeons below Isengard.

Acca, once the steward of Isengard, has agreed to tell you the story of his fall.Talk to Acca and experience 'Session: The Wizard's Vale' or read the shortened account insteadAcca has told you the story of his fall and has warmed up to you. He is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Acca in the dungeonBaldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard.

Acca has agreed to help you escape and wants you to tell Baldgar.Talk to Baldgar in the dungeon'One of the other prisoners was once the steward of this place. His name is Acca, and he ran the day-to-day affairs of Saruman's household while the Wizard concentrated on other matters. But Acca fell out of favour with Saruman and is now a prisoner like the rest of us.

'There is little to do in these dungeons but talk, and Acca has boasted that he knows secrets about Isengard that none save Saruman possess.

'Talk to Acca about these secrets. He may reveal something that we can use to escape.''Acca was once the steward of Isengard and ran Saruman's household. He may know something of use to us in planning our escape.''I was the steward of Isengard, and this is how I am repaid for my long service! It is all Gríma's doing!

'I will tell you of my fall, if you wish to hear the sad tale. I know secrets, secrets of this place... secrets you might use!''I will tell you the tale of my fall, and you shall judge whether I was treated harshly. Perhaps then, I will share with you my secrets!'The plans of a Wizard cannot remain entirely secret to the steward who runs his household. When Acca learns that Saruman has captured his former ally Gandalf the Grey, the steward finds himself conflicted. It takes little time for such worries to be noticed by one who is only too eager to speak of these doubts to his master...'Do you see how it was now, friend? I served Saruman well and faithfully for many years, and but for the lies of Gríma, I would still!

'I like you. I will help you escape. There is a way out of the Ring that only I know about; you will not find it without my help! Tell your friend if he can get us to the surface and create some kind of distraction, I can get us beyond the Ring.''Tell your friend that I can help us escape. You will not find the secret way without my help!''The steward will help us? Good. I do not like being so dependent upon him, but it seems that we have no choice.'Baldgar has come up with an escape plan, and he wants you to use your relative freedom of movement within Isengard to help him carry it out.Sagrúrz is by the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard.

Baldgar wants you to do the work Sagrúrz asks of you, but while you are doing that, he also wants you to collect some black powder.Talk to Sagrúrz at the forgeWeapons are scattered around the floor near the forges. Sagrúrz wants you to pick them up and put them back in an empty barrel. Meanwhile, Baldgar wants you to collect some of the black powder that spews from the works and collects on the floor.Collect scattered weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect piles of black powder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The empty barrel is near the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard.

Sagrúrz wants you to put the scattered weapons you collected in an empty barrel.Sagrúrz is waiting to speak with you by the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard.Talk to Sagrúrz at the forgeBaldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard.

You have stolen some black powder and should bring it to Baldgar.'Acca will tell us the location of the secret way out of the Ring, but we will need two things: a way out of these cells and a large enough distraction to keep the Uruk-hai occupied once we reach the surface.

'When Fâsh took me from my cell to work, I saw some of Saruman's experiments. One of these involved a black powder that, when set aflame, caused a tremendous roar and smoke. Some of the machinery seems to spew this powder. If you can collect enough of it, we could use it for our distraction.

'Your relative freedom of movement can help us here, ${PLAYER}, but you must still keep up appearances. Do not let the Uruk-hai know what you are up to! Report to Sagrúrz by the forges and do his work in addition to collecting the powder for me.''Do the work that Sagrúrz will ask of you, but as you perform his tasks, you should also collect any black powder that you can. Do not let him catch you at this work! It would go badly for us.''Back for more work? There's plenty to do, so don't let me catch you dozing!'

Sagrúrz motions at the scattered weapons near the forges.

'One of the Old Man's thralls dropped a barrel of weapons and tried to run for it. He was... dealt with... but now there are weapons scattered all over the place! Pick them up and put them back in that empty barrel there!''The weapons are right there, scattered all over the floor! Pick them up and put them in that empty barrel there.''Well? Put the weapons you gathered up in that empty barrel there! What are you waiting for?''Good, I'm glad you've cleaned up those scattered weapons. That servant who ran for it made it further than they usually do... he made it to that ramp over there. I just wish he hadn't spilled that barrel and caused me this extra work.'

You breathe a sigh of relief. Sagrúrz does not seem to have noticed your theft of the black powder.'Why are you standing around? Isn't there somewhere that you should be? Stop bothering me!''You managed to get some of the powder! Perfect. This is going to be the key to the distraction that we will need once we make it to the surface.'Baldgar has given you your final instructions for the escape plan: to leave the black powder near one of the great war-machines on the surface, for later ignition.The largest of the war-machines is being constructed on the surface, within the Ring of Isengard. The door to the surface is in the north wall of the caverns. The war-machines are south-east of the steps of Orthanc.

Baldgar has asked you to leave the black powder that you collected near the largest of the war-machines under construction. You have enough black powder for four small piles.You have sprinkled the black powder near the largest of the war-machines under construction.Leave the black powder near the largest of the war-machines under constructionThak is near the war-machines on the surface, within the Ring of Isengard.

Thak noticed you lingering near the war-machines and has called you to speak with him.Talk to ThakThak gave you some trouble when you went to leave the black powder at the war-machine. Now you can either speak to Morflak about Thak, as you threatened, or you can go directly back to Baldgar in the dungeons below Isengard. The door to the depths is north of Orthanc, and Morflak is south-west of the tower.Talk to MorflakTalk to BaldgarBaldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard. The entrance to the depths is north of the tower of Orthanc.

You have left the black powder near the largest of the war-machines within the Ring and should speak now with Baldgar in the dungeons.Talk to Baldgar in the dungeon'The guards do not bring us to work on the surface very often, but the last time that they did, I saw some of the great war-machines being constructed within the Ring. I do not know how close they are to being completed, but if we can do anything to prevent them from leaving Isengard, we surely must.

'What is it they say about birds and stones? I think the black powder you collected might serve as the perfect distraction and also deprive our enemies of one of these war-machines.

'Go to the surface and leave the black powder near the largest of the war-machines, south-east of the steps of Orthanc. The amount you have should suffice for four small piles. We will set the war machines aflame when it is time for us to make our escape. The door to the surface is on the north side of the caverns.''Leave the black powder that you collected near the largest of the war-machines being constructed on the surface. You have enough black powder for four small piles. I think the war machines are south-east of the steps of Orthanc. We will set the war machines aflame when the time comes for us to make our escape, then we must trust that Acca's secret way is as secret as he suggests.''What were you doing lingering around there? Explain yourself! I don't like the look of you, ${RACE}. Start talking!'

Thak eyes you hungrily, confident that he has caught you doing something suspicious, so you appease him: you start talking.

You tell him angrily that it is Morflak's will that you walk around Isengard unguarded, and if Thak wishes to question the will of Morflak, you can bring the two together. All of Thak's bluster vanishes in an instant.

'Don't tell him about this! I'm sorry, I didn't mean anything by it. Really! You don't need to trouble Morflak about this!''Don't tell Morflak about this little discussion of ours! I didn't mean anything by it!'Morflak stares at you for a long moment before speaking.

'Thak gave you some trouble? Doesn't he know you're one of mine? I will have one of my boys take care of him. No one disrespects Morflak!''Ah, you have returned! Were you able to leave the black powder at the place that we spoke about?'Morflak stares at you for a long moment.

'It is done. No more words are necessary.''You have done as I asked! Good, good! I hope setting that black powder aflame will be the distraction that we need to make good our escape.'The time has come to carry out Baldgar's escape plan. If all goes well, you will soon be free of Isengard.Baldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard.Talk to Baldgar and carry out the escape planWhen you awaken, you find that you have been carried to the Gravenwood, but Baldgar is near death.'There is no sense in delaying this, ${PLAYER}. It is time that we were free of this place. Speak with me when you are ready.''Are you ready? We will only get one chance at this. We must make it count!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>'I carried you... this far... but this is... the end... for Baldgar son of Beldgar.'You have escaped from Isengard with the help of Baldgar, but he did not survive. You should rejoin Théodred at his camp in the Gravenwood to decide what to do next.Théodred should be at his camp in the Gravenwood.Find Théodred at his camp in the Gravenwood and talk to him'Do not weep for me... my friend... it is enough to be... free....'

Baldgar's eyes flutter closed for the last time, and he dies a free man. You decide to return to Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood and see what has become of the Grey Company during your captivity.Baldgar is dead. You should return to Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood to learn what has become of the Grey Company during your captivity.'${PLAYER}, you are alive! We feared the worst. Few of your friends made it out of Tâl Methedras, and the tales of those who did are not encouraging.

'I do not think that the Falcon-clan was with Saruman in the beginning; rather, it seems the tide turned while you were travelling through Dunland. The news you brought Lheu Brenin, that Saruman's influence could be felt everywhere, may have been the information for which he was waiting. A pox on these Dunlendings! They cannot be trusted!

'Very few folk made it out of Tâl Methedras, but some did: the rare few Dunlendings who spoke against the Brenin's decision, and a handful of Rangers. If we work together, we can repay Lheu Brenin for his treachery.'Théodred wants you to speak to some of the survivors of the Falcon-clan's betrayal of the Grey Company.Saeradan, Seren, and Hogawise are at Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood.

Théodred wants you to speak to survivors of the Falcon-clan's betrayal in order to learn what happened while you were imprisoned in Isengard.Talk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-campTalk to Seren at the Rohirrim scout-campTalk to Hogawise at the Rohirrim scout-campThéodred is at his camp in the Gravenwood.Talk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp'Not every member of the Falcon-clan agreed with Lheu Brenin's decision; those that did not were slain or forced to flee. One of those who escaped is the woman Seren, and it is from her that I have learned much of what befell within Tâl Methedras.

'I had been working closely with your friend Saeradan before you were captured, and he now burns with the desire to free what Rangers still live, if any do. He is very wise, and it seems if there is any hope of rescue he may be able to devise it. Speak with him on this account.

'You might also seek the advice of my trusted friend Hogawise. He excels in battle and has been a boon companion on this excursion into Gravenwood.''You must tell me of your time in Isengard, ${PLAYER}. It cannot have been pleasant, and you were often in my thoughts.

'I heard what happened within Tâl Methedras from Radanir. Some time after you were secreted away to Isengard, he managed to escape the prison-cave with poor Braigiar. The two of them fought their way into the centre of Tûr Morva, but then....'

Saeradan sighs heavily, and he seems in that moment much older than his years.

'Braigiar did not make it. They cut him down in the road, and only Radanir escaped. He has gone back with some of Théodred's men to try and recover Braigiar's body, but they have not returned.

'Many of our friends have fallen, and the rest are still captives of Lheu Brenin. According to Radanir, Halbarad and the sons of Elrond are still alive, but who can say for how long?''I cannot believe this! How can this have happened?'

The old woman is quivering with anger and grief.

'The Brenin called the heads of households to him, and declared that we were at last ready to reap our reward; we had only to bend the knee to Saruman. But Lheu Brenin himself had said to us the Hebog-lûth would not be the tool of some Wizard! He said it often, and loudly, and we came to believe it!

'I have no love for these Horse-lords, and this strutting princeling least of all, but what can be said? The honour of the Falcon-clan...sold to Saruman? Wulf sought his enemies in open battle! He was no Wizard's hireling!'

Seren chokes back angry tears.

'My boy Anirin has not returned yet from the lands of the Algraig, but his beloved spoke out against this treachery and is still a prisoner! What will I say to him if she dies?''There is no sense in delaying this any further. Your friends are held captive by our shared enemy. This enemy has a strong defensive position, but we have this advantage: we know where he is. Once the Falcon-clan leaves Tâl Methedras, that advantage dissipates. We must deal with them here, before they leave that valley.

'Once the Falcon-clan leaves the valley, my men and I must retreat to hold the Ford. The defence of Rohan is my main object. Until that time, I will help you free your friends.''We crossed the Ford of Isen in secret to learn what the Men of Dunland were up to, but it is worse than we suspected. I think it surprised the leader of the Falcon-clan, as well. It seems to me that he was biding his time until the victory of one side seemed assured. Then he needed to simply throw his lot in with the side likely to come out the victor.

'Let us hope that he is mistaken, ${PLAYER}. I think that he is undervaluing the prowess of the Men of Rohan. I would take ten Rohirrim on horseback over a thousand Dunlending wild men. I have spoken with your friend Saeradan, and it sounds like these Rangers are the same. The more of them we free now, the fewer thousands of Dunlendings I need concern myself with! Ha!''Seren feels the sting of this betrayal most keenly, ${PLAYER}. Her family is still in peril within Tûr Morva, subject to the whims of Lheu Brenin. She will help us.

'Your friend Saeradan is even now attempting to devise a plan with which we can rescue the Rangers, and I know Hogawise's sword is pledged to the cause as well. Speak with them at once, and we will act.'Théodred has established a small camp within Tâl Methedras from which he and his men will help to save the captured members of the Grey Company.Théodred's men have formed a camp in sight of the lake in Tâl Methedras. You should go there to begin planning the rescue of the Grey Company.Travel into Tâl Methedras and find Théodred's forward encampmentThéodred is waiting to speak with you at his forward encampment, in Tâl Methedras.Talk to Théodred at the forward encampment in Tâl MethedrasFrom his forward encampment in Tâl Methedras, Théodred makes preparations to launch an attack on Tûr Morva.Théodred is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.

You have completed the necessary preparations and are now ready to attempt the rescue of the Grey Company from the prison-caves of Tûr Morva.Talk to Théodred at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras'I sent some of my men into Tâl Methedras to establish a camp, ${PLAYER}. We should go to join them. Pass into Tâl Methedras and follow the road as it approaches the lake.

'From this camp, we can scout the area and make a plan for rescuing the Rangers. Some of your people should already be at this camp, such is the fire in their hearts. Let all who wish to join them do so!''From this forward encampment, we will mount our attack on the city of traitors! But not yet. We must first take action to scout the area and learn the extent of the Falcon-clan's defences.

'Speak with our allies at this encampment and help them with their aims. It will all be of use when we make our attack.''It is time. The preparations are made. Now we must strike.''Soon, we will mount our attack on the city of traitors, but first we must make ready. We must be not hasty, lest it prove our undoing!

'Help the people at this encampment with their aims. They all desire justice. They will have it! But we must remain cautious, and strike the Falcon-clan only when we are most ready.''We must go to the camp that my men have established inside Tâl Methedras. It is to the north and east, in view of the lake. Once we are in Tâl Methedras, simply follow the road to the camp.''We must go to the camp that my men have established inside Tâl Methedras. It is to the north and east, in view of the lake. Once we are in Tâl Methedras, simply follow the road to the camp.'Théodred is satisfied with the steps you have taken to prepare and is now ready to move on the prison-caves to rescue the Grey Company.Théodred is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.

Théodred is waiting to speak with you about beginning the attack on the prison-caves where the Grey Company is being held.Talk to Théodred and begin the attack on the prison-cavesHalbarad is at Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood.

You have come alive out of the prison-caves, along with Halbarad and some other surviving members of the Grey Company.Talk to Halbarad at the Rohirrim scout-camp'The time is now. We are as ready as we will ever be. Let us move on the prison-caves to rescue as many of your friends as live still to be rescued.

'Speak with me when you are ready.''You and the prince of Rohan have my thanks, ${PLAYER}. These have been dark days, both for my people and for Middle-earth. I am grateful for the lives that you have saved and mourn the friends we have lost.

'Today, we rest. Tomorrow, we will go to the Fords with Théodred. He has aided us; we will then aid him and pass into Rohan to search for Aragorn my chieftain.

'It is a thing of wonder to me that you have seen within the Ring of Isengard and escaped to speak of it. You bring word of the rise of Isengard, but do those tidings hold anything we can use to stop it? Is this notice enough for us to stop the designs of Saruman?

'I hope it is, ${PLAYER}. I fear that it is not. We will speak again soon.''I am ready to begin if you are. Let us rescue your friends from the traitorous Falcon-clan.'A company of Dragon-clan warriors is encamped at the northern end of the Gravenwood, marching down from Enedwaith.Crates of black fire can be found within Uvel-cadlus.

Thurbald has asked you to enter Uvel-cadlus and destroy the Draig-lûth's supply of black fire.Destroy crates of black fire (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thurbald is hiding to the south of Uvel-cadlus.

You should return to Thurbald with news of your success.Talk to Thurbald'I have seen wagons bearing crates coming from the south to Uvel-cadlus. I wondered at first why the Dunlendings would be bringing provisions and supplies northward to a company that is moving southward towards their muster, but later I saw something that terrified me.

'The Draig-lûth took from the crates a black powder which they were able to ignite into a terrible fire which scorched tree and earth and shattered stone. I fear the Dragon-clan will use this black fire against our people, should all-out war ensue.

'Will you enter Uvel-cadlus and destroy this black fire? The Rohirrim would be greatly indebted to you if you should succeed.''It is good news that you bring. I do not fear so much now for the safety of my people.'After confronting and defending against the Dunlendings at the Mustering Tree, your duties in the Gravenwood have come to an end.Léofward is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in the Gravenwood.

Saeradan instructed you to speak with Léofward before continuing your journey southward.Talk to Léofward at the Rohirrim scout-campArdwyn is at Forthbrond in the Isendale, south of the Gravenwood.

Léofward asked you to take a report to Ardwyn regarding the strength of the Dunlending forces.Talk to Ardwyn in the Isendale'Though Gwyllion is not dead and will likely return again, I believe your duties here are ended, ${PLAYER}. Halbarad and the Grey Company will have need of you in the South.

'Speak with Léofward before you go, but I doubt not that the Horse-lords will also retreat from this place soon.

'Amlan and I will remain here. If Gwyllion returns, she must be dealt with, for she is a powerful adversary who might bring trouble to our chieftain from afar. Fare thee well, ${PLAYER}.''Speak with Léofward, ${PLAYER}. I must return to my duties.''Saeradan is correct, ${PLAYER}. Our mission here was both a success and a failure. We can no longer tarry here, for both the Ox and Dragon-clans are aware of our presence.

'We will come along as we can, but in the meantime, journey south to Forthbrond in the Isendale and report to Ardwyn. Let him know that the Dunlendings are coming... and in greater force than we could imagine.''Hurry to Forthbrond, ${PLAYER}... our people must be warned of the Dunlending force at Wulf's Cleft.''You have come from Léofward? This is grim news you bring, but not unexpected. The Enemy is already upon us.'The champions of the Falcon-clan must be faced in Tûr Morva and defeated before you can undertake the rescue of the Grey Company.Horns outside several dwellings in Tûr Morva will allow you to challenge the inhabitants to combat.Challenge Mostun to combat and defeat himChallenge Gaenor to combat and defeat herChallenge Wundod to combat and defeat himThéodred is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.

You have challenged and defeated three champions of the Falcon-clan and should now return to Théodred.Talk to Théodred at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras'Some members of the Falcon-clan are masters of combat, fearless and quick to engage their enemies. I want them defeated before we enter the prison-caves.

'Let us use their courage against them! They will not refuse a fight. Blow into the horns outside some of the dwellings in Tûr Morva to call them forth to battle. Not every dwelling will house a champion, but some will, and he will answer the call.

'Defeat three of their deadliest warriors and return to me when it is finished.''It is good that you bested the champions, ${PLAYER}. Venturing into the prison-caves will be dangerous enough without the threat of highly-skilled Falcon-clan champions in our path.''Issue challenges to the inhabitants of dwellings within Tûr Morva by blowing the horns outside their houses. Not every dwelling will house a champion, but if one does, he will not decline the challenge.'You have returned to Stangard to hear some dire news from your friend Sabert at the gate.Gadda and a small handful of men loyal to Stanric have escaped Stangard and set up camp at the little farmstead where you planted some hopeful seeds.

You should find Gadda at the abandoned farm in the east of Eorlsmead.Find Gadda at the abandoned farm'It is terrible, just terrible! Stanric has died! He was healthy as could be, and on a mission to improve things, and for a time things were getting better.

'The men who had supported Sithric slowly began to change their favour...until suddenly, in the dead of night last night, Stanric -- he is gone!

'Gadda has committed treason and abandoned his post here, and Sithric vows to arrest him and those who went with him on sight. They have set up an outpost at the abandoned farm. Gadda wishes very much to speak with you!''${PLAYER}! You received my message; that is the only good that has come of this mess! You are truly welcome here, my friend.

'Stanric is dead, and I cannot believe it was an accident. He was as healthy a man that ever walked, and Sithric will not give particulars on how he died.

'I suspect treachery, so I escaped while I could. Tatwine and one other came with me....'A company of Ox-clan warriors are encamped on the western edge of the Gravenwood, arrayed for war.There might be some indication of who is pressing the Ox-clan into service within Rhuvel-cadlus, in the valley below Cuthric's post.

Cuthric asked you to search for some sign of who is behind the muster of the Ox-clan.Scout Rhuvel-cadlusCuthric is hiding on the ridge above Rhuvel-cadlus.

You should return to Cuthric with news of your discovery.Talk to Cuthric'The Ox-clan -- the Uch-lûth -- are known as traders and merchants, not warriors. I wonder what power motivates them to go to war?

'If you would enter their encampment below us, Rhuvel-cadlus, and seek some sign that might indicate who is pressing them into service, it would be of great aid to my prince.

'What say you, ${PLAYER}? Will you enter Rhuvel-cadlus?''You say this White Hand is a symbol used by Saruman the White? Then you speak truly that Saruman is a traitor?'You have chosen to read from the Chronicle of Events concerning the story of the Wizard's Vale.You have chosen to read from the Chronicle of Events concerning the Wizard's Vale of Isengard.Read from the Chronicle of Events and complete The Wizard's ValeYou have read from the Chronicle of Events of some of the history of the Wizard's Vale.Close the Chronicle of EventsYou turn the pages and come to an account of Isengard, the Wizard's Vale.You turn the pages and become immersed in the chronicle of 'The Wizard's Vale.'You think about what you have read and ponder the history of the Wizard's Vale.Orcs serving the White Hand are clear-cutting the forest and shipping the wood off to an unknown location.Orcs can be found at Ak-ghru.

Elfrith has asked you to defeat many of the clear-cutting Orcs.Defeat Orcs at Ak-ghru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elfrith is hiding beyond the bounds of Ak-ghru.

You should return to Elfrith with news of your success.Talk to Elfrith'The Orcs of Ak-ghru may be preparing to wage war on the Dunlendings -- though I doubt it, for they seem not to care about the Dunlendings moving through the Gravenwood -- but they might just as well be preparing to pour out of the Misty Mountains against Rohan.

'I would have you clear-cut these Orcs just as they lay waste to the forest around them... perhaps then they will understand that Rohan is still strong.''Well done, ${PLAYER}... the Orcs of Ak-ghru will know now that the Rohirrim are not to be trifled with.'Following the Battle of the Mustering Tree, a scout from the Dunlending Boar-clan resistance sent word to Léofward that she had news regarding the Old Woman of the Mountain.Huwela awaits you near the road to Tâl Methedras, north of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Léofward told you to meet with the Dunlending scout, Huwela, regarding the Old Woman of the Mountain.Talk to Huwela near the road to Tâl MethedrasSaeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp, south of the road to Tâl Methedras.

Huwela told you of a path she found leading up Methedras and instructed you to bring the information to Saeradan.Talk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp'${PLAYER}, word has come via craban from one of the Boar-clan scouts who are aiding us in this accursed place. Huwela reports that she may have found the witch your Ranger-friends seek...this Old Woman of the Mountain.

'Huwela awaits you near the road to Tâl Methedras to the north. I thank you for your aid here, but soon I fear we must escape back to our own lands. We have taken too many losses here.

'May fortune go with you, my friend.''It is well that you have come, Duvodiad. It is known among my people that the Old Woman of the Mountain is called such because she dwells upon the heights of the mountain you call Methedras, but we have never known the way to her abode...she always came down among us.

'I have discovered a path leading from the road to Tâl Methedras up the mountainside. There is an evil air about the path, so I will not go there, but I believe this may well be the path your friend Saeradan seeks.

'Return to Saeradan and thank him for the kindness he has shown the People of the Boar and tell him of the path. Tell him also that none have travelled it recently.''Huwela found the path, but none have travelled it recently? I wonder, then, what has become of Gwyllion since her defeat at the Slade of Shadows.

'I think she must do one of two things: seek refuge with Saruman or find her way back to her own abode to recoup her strength.

'I think if she appears at Orthanc in defeat, she will not find herself welcomed.''You should speak with Huwela on the road to Tâl Methedras.'Concerned by the words of Saruman while you were imprisoned within Isengard, you wanted to check on the well-being of Nár and Frithgeir.Nár is in the library at Zudrugund.

You have spoken with Frithgeir and confirmed to yourself that Saruman was lying when he spoke of killing these dwarves.Frithgeir is in Zudrugund.

You have spoken with Nár, who seems to be fine, as normal as he ever is. You should return to Frithgeir.'Well, this is a surprise! ${PLAYER}! I did not think to see you again. I thought you would be well on your way through Dunland by now!'

Frithgeir listens with mounting surprise as you tell him that Saruman spoke as if he had killed Nár.

'What lies this Wizard spins! He is like a great, fat spider, weaving webs of treachery and deceit! We have seen no sign of him or of his uruks since you departed. Something must have been keeping him busy. You can speak to Nár yourself, if you like. He is here in the library, as he generally is.''Thank you for returning to Zudrugund to check on our safety, ${PLAYER}. It means a great deal to me to know that you were concerned for our well-being.

'Perhaps you can ease my mind in something, as well. One of the Rangers stayed here for awhile, a young man named Corunir. Does he still fare well?'

You tell Frithgeir that Corunir was fine the last time you saw him, but you have not seen him since you left the Gravenwood.

'I see. I hope he is fine. I am sure he will be. I know he was frustrated by Nár, perhaps with reason, but he was generally kind to us in a difficult situation. When the uruks attacked, he would have died for us. I have not forgotten.

'Thank you for coming to see us, ${PLAYER}! Take care of yourself, wherever you tread.''Hervin! What a long time it has been! I was just thinking about you. Did you ever find that bauble you wanted?'

Nár laughs and strokes his beard.

'Ah, too bad. I did miss you. I am glad you came back! That Ranger doesn't visit as much anymore. You know the one. His name was Túgonn. Never ate with us, which I thought was odd. Wasn't that his name? Túgonn? Or did it begin with a C?'

Nár's brow creases with worry, but then just as suddenly the cloud passes.

'Bring the beer over here, Hervin! We will drink to that Ranger, wherever he has gone, and wish him well!''You will find Nár here in the library. He is fine, but keep in mind that he is still Nár. His mind wanders.'Nár looks at you happily, but says nothing. It is a great relief to know that Saruman's words to you in Orthanc concerning this ancient dwarf were untrue.Frithstan is concerned with the growing lack of provisions and supplies at Stangard.Wild goats can be found throughout the Wailing Hills.

Frithstan has asked you to hunt the wild goats of the Wailing Hills for their hides.Collect goat-hides in the Wailing Hills (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Frithstan is at his camp near the Cuthstan.

You should return to Frithstan with news of your success.Return the hides to Frithstan'Resourceful are the soldiers of Stangard. Supplies are few, yet the need for armour, weapons, and provisions is great. We must gather resources whenever there is opportunity to do so, and there is an asset in the Wailing Hills which should not be overlooked.

'The wild goats in these hills are exceptionally lean and are often poor sources of meat, but their rough hides can still prove to be quite useful. Goat-hides may be tanned into leather, then used to produce a wide assortment of important equipment, which Stangard desperately needs.

'Would you gather these hides, so that we may improve our stores of materials?''Flawless are the hides which you have brought with you. These will make fine armour and tools once they have been tanned. My thanks.'Andreg is taking you to meet with Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp; however, he needs help with his own mission first.Andreg has asked you to help him find and disable Orc-traps throughout the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>.Destroy Orc-traps in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should speak with Andreg regarding the traps you disabled.Talk to Andreg'Orcs are cruel beings. They have left many traps throughout the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>, designed to injure and maim, more than to capture.

'Will you help me find and disable them?''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Now the beasts of the wood and the Men who journey here will be able to pass without fear of maiming.'The Slade of Shadows appears to be a focal point for the evil that is growing within the Gravenwood.Elhudan may be found within the Slade of Shadows, south of Andreg's position.

Andreg has instructed you to defeat elhudan at the Slade of Shadows.Defeat elhudan at the Slade of Shadows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Among the fell spirits I noticed amid the trees of the Slade of Shadows, I saw many of the wisps the Dunlendings call elhudan. These spirits are perhaps the least of the Dark Lord's minions, but in large numbers, they may prove dangerous still.

'As you investigate the Slade of Shadows, take some time to banish the elhudan... they must lead no one else to their doom.'You discovered several important pieces of evidence of the treachery occuring in Stangard.Gadda is at the abandoned farm near the Eorlsmead Tower.

You should bring the evidence you found to Gadda.Talk to Gadda'Gadda was right to trust you. I will remain here and keep an eye on this place. Take what you have found back down to the farm and show Gadda, for he will be very interested.''Ah! How interesting. This does not bode well at all, for you have found a great deal more dire evidence than I expected.''I do not like any of this. You should take those items to Gadda at once!'Upon his banishment, the Cuthraul Nulchulth dropped a fell token similar to those you had dug up from beneath the Tree of Tribute.Saeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp, north-east of the Tree of Tribute.

You should bring the tokens you found to Saeradan.Upon his banishment, the Cuthraul Nulchuth dropped a token similar to those you dug up from beneath the Tree of Tribute. You should bring all three tokens to Saeradan at once.'Indeed, these medallions confirm what I suspected all along. I thought that Gwyllion might have allies in Dunland, and it seems I was right.

'One of these tokens bears the mark of the goat... the Druggavar summoned by the Old Woman of the Mountain. This one bears the mark of the Stag, and the third is the Ox, clans we encountered here in Dunland.'You found an object carved with a strange and evil-looking icon.Saeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp.

You should bring the evil object to Saeradan for his examination.The icon upon this object looks like some kind of animal with horns, but it has an evil-looking air about it. Perhaps Saeradan will be able to make some sense of it.'What is this that you have for me? Aye, I have seen this symbol before. I am not sure what it is supposed to represent, but it reminds me of some of the demons that Gwyllion summoned against us in the Windfells.'The Rangers Saeradan, Amlan, and Andreg have tracked Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, from the Windfells in Enedwaith to the Gravenwood of Dunland.

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will make it impossible to acquire new discoverables from Andreg and will fail the Tracking an Old Goat deed and any unresolved discoverables.</rgb>Andreg has asked you to help him scout the Gravenwood -- specifically the path to the Rohirrim scout-camp -- for signs of Gwyllion's passage.Scout the path to the Rohirrim scout-campAndreg is preparing to part company with you. You should speak with him to find out where to go from here.

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will make it impossible to acquire new discoverables from Andreg and will fail the Tracking an Old Goat deed and any unresolved discoverables.</rgb>Talk to Andreg'Indeed, I will set you on the path to Saeradan and the Horse-lords, but first I need your assistance. My mission in this wood is to scout for signs of Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain. My efforts have proven unfruitful as of yet, but perhaps with your aid, that will change.

'As we journey towards the scout-camp, perhaps you may help scout the forest between here and there? If we find signs of Gwyllion's passage, you can then deliver word of it to Saeradan.

'What say you? We will need to stay along the north face of the southern hills, for that is the section I am assigned to scout, and I can only take you as far as the pass to the Isendale, for I must part ways with you there.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will make it impossible to acquire new discoverables from Andreg and will fail the Tracking an Old Goat deed and any unresolved discoverables.</rgb>'We have seen strange things on this path, ${PLAYER}, and strange things are a good sign that Gwyllion has come this way.

'Thank you for your help.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will make it impossible to acquire new discoverables from Andreg and will fail the Tracking an Old Goat deed and any unresolved discoverables.</rgb>The Rangers Saeradan, Amlan, and Andreg have tracked Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, from the Windfells in Enedwaith to the Gravenwood of Dunland.Andreg has asked you to help him scout the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> -- specifically the path to the Rohirrim scout-camp -- for signs of Gwyllion's passage.Andreg is preparing to part company with you. You should speak with him to find out where to go from here.Talk to Andreg'Indeed, I will set you on the path to Saeradan and the Horse-lords, but first I need your assistance. My mission in this wood is to scout for signs of Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain. My efforts have proven unfruitful as of yet, but perhaps with your aid, that will change.

'As we journey towards the scout-camp, perhaps you may help scout the forest between here and there? If we find signs of Gwyllion's passage, you can then deliver word of it to Saeradan.

'What say you? We will need to stay along the north face of the southern hills in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>, for that is the section I am assigned to scout, and I can only take you as far as the pass to the Isendale, for I must part ways with you there.''We have seen strange things on this path, ${PLAYER}, and strange things are a good sign that Gwyllion has come this way.

'Thank you for your help.'Théodred's scouts have come to the Gravenwood seeking tidings of the Dunlendings' movements.Léofward is at the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Saeradan asked you to speak with Léofward and offer him your services.Talk to Léofward at the Rohirrim scout-camp'I am more determined than ever to find Gwyllion's hiding hole, but she is a wily one and more familiar with this land than the Dúnedain. I have sent for Amlan and a few of the Boar-clan resistance are helping us scour the Gravenwood for further signs of Gwyllion, but in the meantime, I want you to speak with Léofward, the chief of Théodred's scouts.

'Perhaps by aiding the Rohirrim, we will aid our own cause, as well.''I am grateful for the Rangers' help sneaking us into the Gravenwood past the Dunlendings, but I am not certain what aid one such as yourself could offer us.

Léofward sighs.

'I must beg your pardon, ${CLASS}. We have never come this far into enemy lands. I do indeed have a use for you, if you are willing.''Speak with Léofward, ${PLAYER}.'Braigiar was slain when he and Radanir tried to escape from Tûr Morva. Radanir was wounded and wants you to retrieve the body of his friend.Braigiar's body is in the centre of the village of Tûr Morva, where he fell during his escape with Radanir.

Radanir has asked you to recover Braigiar's body from the centre of Tûr Morva.Find Braigiar's body, and Théodred will carry it back to the encampmentRadanir is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.

Radanir will be pleased to know that you have recovered Braigiar's body.Talk to Radanir at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras'The guards were careless, and Braigiar and I took advantage of their lapse to escape. We planned to run to the prince of Rohan's camp in the Gravenwood, but...'

Radanir winces and clutches his leg.

'They cut us off from the straight path out of the village, and we had to take the long way. At every turning, it seemed that there were more and more of the Falcon-clan. Braigiar fought bravely, but there were simply too many foe-men. He fell in the centre of the village, and I ran. I twisted my leg jumping from a rock as their arrows rained around me, but somehow I made it to safety.

'We cannot leave Braigiar to them, ${PLAYER}. Théodred has agreed to help carry his body back here. Go to Tûr Morva and find where Braigiar fell. He deserves better than to be left in that town of jackals.''You have to recover Braigiar's body, ${PLAYER}. I would do it myself, in a heart beat, if it was not for this leg. I would stand no chance against the Falcon-clan.

'Braigiar fell in the centre of the village. Théodred has agreed to help carry him from the village; you must just show him where our friend lies.'You stare at Braigiar's fallen form and wonder how many other friends must die within the walls of Tûr Morva.'Thank you for recovering the body of our friend, ${PLAYER}. He is now at peace.'You found a range-finding flag on the top of the tower. The placement of the others would provide useful information as to the vulnerability of the tower.The top of the Eorlsmead Tower will likely be a good vantage point.

From the top of the tower, you should <rgb=#FFFF00>look</rgb> at the land around the tower for range-finding flags.This flag is used by archers to determine range and wind conditions of their target so that they can adjust their aim. Such flags are likely placed in the fields around the tower; you should look for them from the parapets.A set of orders has been posted, instructing the Mor-hai to carry pouches of remedy in order to safe-guard against their own poisons.Mor-hai Orcs can be found within their cave in the western section of the Wailing Hills.

Securing remedy from defeated Orcs will likely prove to be a worthwhile endeavour for the Men of Stangard.Collect pouches of the Orcs' poison remedy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Penda may be found back at the camp, along the road north of the Cuthstan.

Frithstan and his men should be able to make good use of the remedy you have collected from the Mor-hai.Return to Penda with the pouches of remedyThis scribbled note contains a set of orders to the Mor-hai Orcs, signed by one named Dushatár. It seems that the Mor-hai have often been careless when creating and handling their poisons. The orders demand that pouches of herbal remedy be carried in order to help cure their mistakes.

It would certainly be helpful to collect some of these remedy pouches and to bring them to Frithstan's camp.'You have done well to secure this poison remedy. This will help us deal with our injured, and the rest shall be stockpiled to combat further attempts of poisoning by the Mor-hai. Frithstan will be pleased to know of your efforts.'Frithstan and his men have a need for more of the remedy that is carried by the Mor-hai Orcs within their hillside cave.Mor-hai Orcs can be found within their cave in the western section of the Wailing Hills.

Securing remedy from defeated Orcs will help Frithstan be prepared for further encounters with the Mor-hai.Collect pouches of the Orcs' poison remedy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Penda may be found back at the camp, along the road north of the Cuthstan.

Frithstan and his men should be able to make good use of the remedy you have collected from the Mor-hai.Return to Penda with the pouches of remedy'We have need for more of the remedy you procured from the Mor-hai. If you are able to acquire any additional pouches, bring them to me, and we will make good use of them.''You have done well to secure this poison remedy for us. This will help in dealing with the sick. The remainder will be stockpiled to combat further attempts of poisoning by the Mor-hai.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''The Mor-hai that carry remedy seem to dwell within the Orc-cave to the west, just beyond their war camp.

'I will remain here at my post, watching toward the west for your return.'The map on the first floor was incomplete and missing several pieces. It seems likely that these pieces have been distributed to the guards.The guards' chests are on the second floor of the tower.

You should search chests for fragments of the map.Find the map-fragments (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})This map of the Great River region is covered with markings and symbols indicating plans for the future, though several key pieces have been ripped off and are currently missing. It is likely that these pieces have been distributed among the guards of the tower.A company of Ox-clan warriors are encamped on the western edge of the Gravenwood, arrayed for war.Uch-lûth can be found at Rhuvel-cadlus, in the valley below Cuthric's post.

Cuthric asked you to defeat Ox-clan warriors to dissuade them from warring upon Rohan.Defeat Uch-lûth at Rhuvel-cadlus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cuthric is hiding on the ridge above Rhuvel-cadlus.

You should return to Cuthric with news of your victory.Talk to Cuthric'There can be only one reason for the muster of the Ox-clan... they plan to wage war upon Rohan, or to at least show their support for their countrymen's war. I would have you show them that such a demonstration of solidarity is futile.

'Enter Rhuvel-cadlus below us and confront the Uch-lûth... teach them -- with sword, if need be -- that to attack the Riddermark would be insanity at best.

'What say you, ${PLAYER}?''That should teach the wild men a lesson they won't soon forget! Ha!'Your Uruk-hai overseer has more work for you to do in the caverns beneath Isengard.Sagrúrz is in the centre of the main cavern beneath Isengard.

Your Uruk-hai overseer has another task for you, this one near the great forges in the centre of the caverns.Talk to Sagrúrz in IsengardSagrúrz wants you to carry heavy barrels of armour and weapons up the slope to the north and to leave them on the wooden platform directly above Fâsh with the others.Pick up a barrel of weaponsSagrúrz wants you to carry heavy barrels of armour and weapons up the slope to the north and to leave them on the wooden platform directly above Fâsh with the others.Pick up a barrel of armourSagrúrz is waiting in the centre of the main cavern beneath Isengard.Talk to Sagrúrz in IsengardThe prisoner Kenned is exhausted and cannot carry the barrel Sagrúrz wants him to.Talk to Kenned in IsengardKenned's barrel of weapons is right next to him.

Kenned cannot carry the barrel of weapons Sagrúrz has charged him to carry, so you are going to carry it for him.Pick up Kenned's barrel of weaponsSagrúrz is in the centre of the main cavern beneath Isengard.Talk to Sagrúrz in Isengard'I have more work for you, and this will be tough, back-breaking labour! I could have given this to one of the other prisoners, but I saved it up special for you. It's just my way of saying how pleased I am to waste my time making sure you don't fall into one of the pits.

'Sagrúrz is in the centre of the main cavern, ${RACE}. What do you say to us paying him a little visit? It doesn't matter! We're going anyway!''What is this? You're much too scrawny for this work! I need a good strong Uruk-hai to carry these barrels, not some pitiful little ${RACE}.'

Sagrúrz sniffs the air and glowers at you in disapproval.

'You'll have to do. It's no care of mine if you kill yourself lugging them around. Just another body for the pile! Haul a couple of these barrels up the path to the north, and leave them on the wooden platform with the others. You see it there, directly above Fâsh? Now get moving!''You left the barrels where I said? You'd better have. This worthless prisoner says he's too tired to carry his load. He'll get the lash again if he doesn't shift that barrel in a hurry!''You won't be able to do his work forever, worm. This weakling won't last, and I'll be ready with my lash when he stumbles.

'Find more work from your overseer. I'll summon you when I have more for you.''So...so tired...cannot....'

Kenned cannot go on. You are certain that Sagrúrz will kill him if his work is not completed. You decide to carry the barrel of weapons in Kenned's stead.'What are you still doing here? Carry those barrels of armour and weapons up the path to the north and leave them on the wooden platform directly above Fâsh with the others!''If this captive cannot do his work, he is of no use to me! I will have him put to death!''I don't care who moves that barrel of weapons, as long as it is moved! It's all the same to me which of you worthless slimes does it!''Can't...go on...so tired....'

You resolve to help him, that he might not suffer more injuries at the hand of Sagrúrz.Andreg is taking you to meet with Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp; however, he needs help with his own mission first.Andreg has asked you to help him slay a few dusk-hounds in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>.Defeat dusk-hounds in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should speak with Andreg about your successes against the dusk-hounds of the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>.Talk to Andreg'The Dunlendings use the dusk-hounds of the Gravenwood as hunting dogs. They are a vicious breed with a keen sense of smell. A couple of the Horse-lord's mounts were badly mauled by the dogs...we would do well, I think, to slay a few dusk-hounds and lessen the threat they pose.

'What say you? Shall we hunt the pack?''Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. There will be fewer dusk-hounds now to harry us and our allies.'The Rangers Saeradan, Amlan, and Andreg have tracked Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, from the Windfells in Enedwaith to the Gravenwood of Dunland.Andreg is near the Slade of Shadows, south of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Andreg has asked you to help him face the evils at the Slade of Shadows.Complete Mystery of the TreesComplete Baa, Baa, Black SheepComplete Dimming the LightsComplete Spirits of DunlandAndreg is near the Slade of Shadows, south of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

You should return to Andreg with news of your successes.Talk to Andreg near the Slade of Shadows'I thank you again for coming, ${PLAYER}. When I found the Slade of Shadows, I did not expect it to be so utterly inhabited by evils from the ancient world. I avoided detection for a short time, but I did not wish to risk betraying our presence here to the Enemy.

'It may be, though, that one such as yourself, with no true tie to the Dúnedain, might be able to confront the foe without breaking the secrecy of the Grey Company.

'Will you lend me your aid?''With what you discovered in the Slade of Shadows, I think I know how to ensnare Gwyllion. We shall be revealed, but I think the risk is worth the gain.'A camp of Rohirrim located north of the Cuthstan has missed delivering a report to the soldiers of Stangard. Byrnstan wishes to check on the camp's leader and ensure that all is well.The Rohirrim-camp may be found along the road north of the Cuthstan, to the west of Stangard.

Byrnstan has asked you to visit Frithstan and ask about the delay in his report to Stangard.Visit the Rohirrim-camp along the northern base of the CuthstanPenda may be found in the Rohirrim-camp along the road north of the Cuthstan, to the west of Stangard.

Penda seems to be the only man left at Frithstan's camp.Talk to Penda about Frithstan's location'Early is the hour in which you return to Stangard. I welcome your presence here, as does Gadda, but there are further matters which need attention in the Wailing Hills. North of the Cuthstan, along the road to the west, lies a small camp of riders led by a man named Frithstan. Their position in the shadow of the Stone allows them to keep watch over the western roads out of Stangard, while remaining secluded from the eyes of Hill-orcs.

'On occasion, Frithstan sends a patrol to Stangard with reports of any enemy activity in the west. A message was expected days ago, yet still we have received no word. After your most recent discovery, I take this as a cause for concern.

'Head west out of Stangard and take the road north as it forks. Seek out Frithstan at his camp and discover the cause for the absence of tidings.''Frithstan's camp is west of Stangard. When you see the fork, bear north and keep the Cuthstan to your left.

'Frithstan and his men should be stationed on guard along the road.''Greetings. You are looking for Frithstan, friend? Then you are not alone.

'Penda is my name, and Frithstan is my sergeant. This is where last I saw him, at his camp in the shadows of the Cuthstan.'Stanric is alive, defying the lies of Sithric. It is clear that Stanric must be freed at once, so that justice may be done for this betrayal.Stanric is in the lock-house.Free Stanric from his bondsStanric is in the prison of Stangard.Talk to StanricStanric is in the prison of Stangard.Help Stanric out of his cellStanric is in the lock-house of Stangard.Listen to Stanric's planThe inn in Stangard is full of suspicious Rohirrim.Rally the men in the innAthulf is in the tavern of Stangard with some equally suspicious men.Tell Athulf of Sithric's deceptionStanric is now in the Mead Hall of Stangard.Talk to StanricDefend Stanric and defeat Sithric.Help Stanric take down Sithric once and for allStanric is in the Mead Hall.Talk to Stanric'There is nothing left for you to help with! You have freed us from Sithric's mad corruption at last.''Free at last! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I cannot believe the gall of Sithric, nor how deep corruption runs in his veins.

'It is time to take back my city!''Go rally the men, and I will make my way to the Mead Hall to confront Sithric. The men are often in the inn at this time of night.

'Meet me at the Mead Hall when you can -- I don't have the strength to fight Sithric alone now. I have not eaten or slept since I was locked up down here.''But -- ${PLAYER}! What are you doing here? Sithric has men looking for you at this very moment! You should run.

'Why have you returned, friend? It must be urgent, if you are risking so much.''${PLAYER}, I must ask to borrow your strength this night. It looks to me like Sithric does not intend to go down without a fight.''You did it, ${PLAYER}! Sithric will be locked up, for his proper place is in a prison. Stangard will be made right at last... and it is all thanks to you!'It is time to carry out Baldgar's plan to escape from Isengard.Baldgar is in his cell. He wants to speak with you one last time before you begin.Talk to BaldgarThe key-master is somewhere in the dungeons. Baldgar wants you to take him by surprise, and told you to climb the slope, turning right into the other wing of the dungeons when you have the opportunity.Find the Uruk-hai key-masterOne of the Dunlending prisoners has tried to attract your attention.Talk to the Dunlending prisonerYou have recovered the keys from the Uruk-hai key-master.Return to BaldgarYou have freed Baldgar and Acca from their cells, and now Baldgar wants to speak with you.Talk to BaldgarAcca is ready to speak with you.Talk to AccaYou, Baldgar, and Acca will go before the rest of the prisoners, running up the slope to the entrance to the dungeons.Run up the slope to the entrance to the dungeons with Acca and BaldgarBaldgar wants to speak with you before you leave the dungeons.Talk to Baldgar just inside the entrance to the dungeonsYou need to walk slowly through the large, open room with Baldgar and Acca so as not to attract undue attention.Walk slowly through the large room with Baldgar and Acca so as not to attract attentionYou have made it to the surface of Isengard. You are almost there!Talk to BaldgarAcca has volunteered to light the black powder to provide you with the distraction which you need to escape.Talk to AccaAcca has gone to light the black powder, and you should hide with Baldgar until you see the signal: a giant plume of smoke and flame!Wait with Baldgar for Acca's signal: an enormous blast of flame and smokeYou are hiding with Baldgar, still awaiting Acca's signal.Talk to BaldgarMorflak has killed Acca, and now Baldgar wants you to keep Morflak busy so that he can light the black powder.Talk to Morflak and keep him busy'What... what is that noise?''Here is what we need to do, ${PLAYER}. The key-master is an Uruk-hai who carries a ring of keys that can open these cell doors. He tends to come down into the dungeons several times a day... or what passes for a day here in the lightless reaches.

'Look for him somewhere in the dungeon and see if you can catch him unaware. He is likely to be down the other wing of the dungeons. Climb the slope and turn right when you can. Once you have the keys, come back here and release me! We can then open the door for Acca, and we will make our way to the surface.

'The Uruk-hai must have seen you walking about Isengard. They may believe that you are bringing us to see Saruman, by order of the Wizard. They may let us pass.''What are you doing down here? Fâsh didn't tell me you had any business here today.

'I don't like the smell of you. Get out of here!''You have got the keys there, do you not? You must let us out! You cannot leave us to die here, friend! We can help you!''This is not what I meant, ${PLAYER}.''There is a gap in the wall between the buildings on the western side. Once the black powder does its work, you should be able to make it there in the confusion.

'But first we need to get to the surface. It will not be easy with so many of us.''We do not want to attract attention, ${PLAYER}. We should walk slowly from here, so as not to attract undue attention.

'Let us go!''We are almost out! Now we just need to light the black powder ${PLAYER} set up ahead of time, and we will have all the chaos we need to make it to the other side of the Ring... and freedom!''I am ready for what comes, ${PLAYER}. I will set the black powder aflame, and it will draw all of Isengard to this side of the Ring.

'When that happens, the western side should be empty, and you will be able to slip through the gap in the Ring-wall.

'Farewell, ${PLAYER}. May you live past tonight and help put an end to my master's evil.''You have my word: I will help you to save your Ranger friends from their captivity at the hands of the Falcon-clan. I am sorry that we can do nothing for the Ranger that was sent here with you. Lothrandir, he was called?

'If Lothrandir lives still, Saruman has kept him very close. We cannot hope to gain entrance to Orthanc.

'What is taking Acca so long?''You would be nothing without me, ${PLAYER}. I gave you the run of Isengard. It was the fear of me that kept you from being thrown in the cells alongside these vermin.

'But now we will see. Oh, yes, we will see whose time it is to die. See how I repay treachery!'You have been called to Orthanc to appear before the Wizard Saruman.Fâsh has brought you inside Orthanc and is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Fâsh inside OrthancYou have been summoned inside Orthanc to present yourself to Saruman and have been ordered not to stray from the path.Saruman has brought you to a library within his tower of Orthanc.Talk to Saruman in the tower of OrthancThe power of Saruman's voice is seductive, his words convincing. You find yourself nodding in agreement.

