You must <rgb=#FF0000>resist</rgb>. You must not succumb.Listen to Saruman within OrthancYou have not seen the Angmarim once known as Avair since you were in Forochel. Her name was taken from her, and now she serves Saruman as Gun Ain, 'Without Name.'Talk to Gun AinYou have not seen the Angmarim once known as Avair since you were in Forochel. Her name was taken from her, and now she serves Saruman as Gun Ain, 'Without Name.'Listen to Saruman within OrthancYou have not seen this Angmarim woman since you left the north-lands. When last you saw her, she had been cast out by her clan for dishonouring them. Her name was taken from her, and she became known as Gun Ain: without name.

She survived in the wastes of Forochel by stealing food from the Lossoth hunters once their prey was felled. Lothrandir gave her a bag of food to last until she could rebuild the wreckage of her life.

What is she doing here?'Well, you're here. This is as far as I go. Follow the stairs straight up and don't wander. The Old Man will know if you do!''We have much to discuss, ${PLAYER}. I am Saruman the Wise, and I know much that might surprise you, but still there are mysteries. I need your help.

'Together, we can learn much that would otherwise remain hidden. There is much we could accomplish.''Why do you reject this course? Can you not see that it is futile to continue this fools' charade?''I will bring you to Morflak. But soon I will kill you, and I will kill your friend Lothrandir, and I will earn my new name. My master has promised.'You have travelled with Léofward to the Mustering Tree, where Thurbald, Elfrith, and Cuthric have joined you to defend against the combined forces of the Dragon and Ox-clans.Léofward is at the Mustering Tree.

You should speak with Léofward to learn his plan before the battle begins.Talk to Léofward to learn his planDefend the Mustering Tree from the Dunlending forces.Defend the Mustering Tree from the Dunlending forces'Plan, ${PLAYER}? We are few against two companies of Dunlending warriors. I plan only to take as many of them as I can with me to the grave and hope that my sacrifice is not in vain.

'I cannot fault you for preserving your own life, so if the battle goes ill, you may take Longstride and escape the battle.

'To arms, brothers! For Eorl! For Helm! To arms!'You have come with Lheu Brenin to speak with the captive emissary from Isengard one more time before he dies and hopefully learn something of use to the Falcon-clan and the Grey Company.Lheu Brenin has come with you into the prison-caves behind Tûr Morva to speak with the captive emissary.Talk to Lheu Brenin in the prison-cavesLéolin is waiting to speak with you in the prison-caves.Talk to Léolin in the prison-cavesYou have met Lothrandir in the prison-caves, coming back from an errand in the depths.Talk to Lothrandir in the prison-cavesNai is guarding the cell where Dondhreg is being held captive in the prison-caves.Talk to Nai in the prison-cavesBetrayal... you were attacked by two members of the Falcon-clan, but Lothrandir was able to turn the tables on them. You should speak with him now.Talk to Lothrandir in the prison-cavesLheu Brenin has blocked your passage with a group of armed warriors. He wishes to speak with you.Talk to Lheu Brenin in the prison-cavesYou have been brought to Isengard by waggon along a bumpy road.Survive the waggon ride along a bumpy roadIwan is ready to bring you into Isengard.Talk to Iwan at the gate into IsengardLothrandir has been badly beaten by your captors and is finding it difficult to go on.Talk to Lothrandir at the gates of IsengardLothrandir is running into the heart of Isengard by his own power. It is a small gesture, but it is something, and gives you a glimmer of hope.Follow Lothrandir into IsengardAn Uruk-hai named Morflak has made you pull up short before the tower of Orthanc.Talk to Morflak in Isengard'You are Fâsh's problem now. He will find work for you! Ha!''We will make the captive sing for us, ${PLAYER}. He will sing of Saruman's plans, or I will end his captivity with steel.''The cells further in are damper and less pleasant, filled with refuse and home to rats. The captive will have much to say of Saruman's plans for the Falcon-clan, I am certain of it.''Calenglad and some other Rangers are below, bringing up some of the supplies the Falcon-clan stored in the depths. The caves go quite some way into the mountain. Halbarad sent me to bring you down to help, but if you are busy with something else....''See how weak our captive is! He will not live through the night if he does not have a meal and an escape from the damp.''This is bad, ${PLAYER}, very bad! The Falcon-clan has turned on us! I do not know why, but we are betrayed, and many of our friends are still below!

'We will cut our way out!''I am sorry that it turned out like this, ${PLAYER}. I mean that. These Rangers are good folk, strong folk, and I see in them an echo of my own people. But you told me yourself of the great armies Saruman has already amassed. He is prepared to give us back the lands that belong to us. It is so close now!

'I am no Wizard's servant. Saruman prizes knowledge above all else, and now the Falcon-clan can give him that.''Let us go. I do not want to stay here any longer than I need to. I will leave you captives with someone and be back on the waggon headed for Tûr Morva before the next bell.''I cannot... go on like this... ${PLAYER}. What... can we...?'

Lothrandir's pains are evident; both of you were cruelly-treated by the long waggon journey to Isengard and the whips of your captors, but Lothrandir bore the brunt of the ill treatment.'We will keep you busy, little ${RACE}, and your friend too. I think the Old Man will want to speak with him directly.

'There's a place for you in the caves below, if Fâsh doesn't kill you first. If you have any fortune at all, you won't see me again, little ${RACE}.

'You're ours now. Let's see how long you last.'Théodred and some of his loyal men have come with you to the prison-caves behind Tûr Morva to try and rescue the Grey Company.Théodred is a short way ahead in the prison-caves.Talk to Théodred within the prison-cavesHerestan and Hogawise are ready to fight the defenders at two rooms of cells within the prison-caves.Find Herestan within the prison-cavesFind Hogawise within the prison-cavesThéodred is in one of the tunnels of the prison-caves you passed through to reach the prisoners.Return to Théodred in the prison-cavesThéodred is within one of the rooms of cells within the prison-caves.Talk to Théodred in the prison-cavesHalbarad and the sons of Elrond are further within the prison-caves.Find Halbarad and the sons of Elrond, deeper within the prison-cavesLheu Brenin guards a bridge that leads deeper into the caves, but you cannot pass. Archers of the Falcon-clan make crossing impossible.Talk to Lheu BreninHalbarad needs to speak with you.Talk to Halbarad'Penrod thought to bring us before Lheu Brenin. He did not choose men strong enough for the task.

'I am glad to see you, ${PLAYER}! Let us go to see Lheu Brenin now, and on our own terms!''He is right, ${PLAYER}. We cannot raise a hand against him in this position. They are too many, and we are too few.

'There may be another time, but this is not it.''You are full of surprises, ${PLAYER}. I did not think that you would cross my path again in this life. How is it that you came to escape the clutches of Saruman?'

Lheu Brenin smiles mockingly at your silence.

'You were a fool to return here. You may have freed some members of your company, but I have exacted my price from the Grey Company.''None of your friends have been imprisoned in this room of cells. Lheu Brenin must be keeping them further ahead, away from the entrance.

'My men have gone on ahead. Join them at each room of cells and fight for the freedom of your friends! I will scout around for sign of our enemies.''Another room of Rangers to free! Let us give them their freedom, ${PLAYER}.''We can do nothing more from here. We must lick our wounds, bury our dead, and wait for another time.

'But I swear it: before this war is over, the Falcon-clan will taste our vengeance!''You will pay for your treachery, honourless ones! To battle, ${PLAYER}!''Release your prisoners or die, low ones! To battle!''That was good work, ${PLAYER}, but I fear it was only a start. More of your friends are being held below.'Acca is telling you the story of his downfall as the steward of Saruman's household.You are Gríma Wormtongue, advisor and servant to Saruman the White. He has been visited by Radagast the Brown, and you and Acca are waiting to hear if your master has any commands for you.Talk to Acca in the gardens of IsengardYou have overheard Saruman speaking of some troubling things, but Acca can make no sense of them.Talk to Acca in the gardens of IsengardSaruman is in the gardens of Isengard and wants to speak with you.Talk to Saruman in the gardens of IsengardAcca's story continues.Listen to Acca continue his taleAcca is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Acca near the gates of IsengardYou are to take care of Gandalf's horse while Acca brings the Wizard to speak with Saruman.See to Gandalf's horse while Acca escorts the Wizard to SarumanListen to Acca's story continue.Listen to Acca's story continueAcca is near the steps of Orthanc, listening to the conversation of Gandalf and Saruman. You should speak with him.Talk to Acca outside OrthancSaruman is on the steps of Orthanc.Talk to Saruman on the steps of OrthancListen to Acca continue his story.Listen to Acca's story continueAcca has come to the pinnacle of Orthanc with a basket of bread for Gandalf. You should talk to him.Talk to Acca on the pinnacle of OrthancAcca wants to speak with you on the pinnacle of Orthanc.Talk to Acca on the pinnacle of OrthancAcca's story continues.Listen to Acca's story continueYou must find Saruman within Orthanc and tell him of Acca's sympathies.Find Saruman within Orthanc and tell him of Acca's sympathies'They have been long in conversation, Gríma. What do you think they are speaking about?''Could you make any sense of that, Gríma? Our master holds you in closer confidence than he does me. Have you heard nothing of these matters?

'I need not be counted among the Wise to know that they have Radagast worried, and that gives me reason to worry as well!

'I am sure our master will know what must be done. That is why he is the Wizard, and we are the servants! We know our place, do we not? We do!''It is done. Radagast will find Gandalf, if he is to be found, and I doubt not he will speed with all haste here to Isengard.

'There are some other small matters I need you to attend to before my guest arrives....''Our master was right, Gríma! The guards report that Gandalf was seen riding hard alongside the river, and now he is here! Radagast has done as he was asked!

'Let us go meet Gandalf and bring him to Orthanc!'Gandalf's horse is tired from its long journey and will benefit from a stay in the stables with food and water.'Gandalf seems much older than I remember from his last visit, older and weaker. Look at him there, then look at our master. See how Saruman's raiment glows! Gandalf's cloak seems so tattered.

'It is charitable of our master to offer his wisdom to the Grey Wizard. Perhaps he could offer some finer clothing, as well!''Stay out from underfoot. I do not want to be disturbed until I send for you.''No, I will not be dissuaded, Gríma. He is an old man and does not deserve this treatment at the hands of our master. If Saruman fears Gandalf plans to hatch an evil plot, keep him imprisoned, yes, but in comfortable quarters. The pinnacle is exposed to the elements. It is cruel treatment, not befitting Saruman the Wise.

'It is not our place to challenge Saruman's decisions, but I will do what I can to ease Gandalf's stay with us. An extra ration of bread will do no harm.

'There is no need to tell Saruman of this, of course.''Promise me that you will not tell our master about this. We have done nothing wrong, of course, but there is no sense in disturbing him. What is one more loaf of bread? No one will miss it.'Saruman listens as you breathlessly recount Acca's recent delivery of a loaf of bread to Gandalf, and their ensuing conversation. His face is a thundercloud.

'Why did you allow Acca to do this? Dog! What would you have done if he allowed Gandalf to come down? What would have been your answer if my worthless steward had freed him?'

Saruman masters his anger, but his tone is no less stern.

'From this point onward, none will climb the steps to the pinnacle save myself. I will have Acca thrown in the dungeons, where he will have time enough to consider this betrayal. He will have not even a crust to chew upon; let him eat slop instead.

'You will perform Acca's duties in his stead, until I have others for you. And I will, Gríma. Soon you will return to your homeland. But not yet.'Andreg has a plan to draw forth and ensnare Gwyllion and her allies at the Slade of Shadows.You should speak with Andreg to learn his plan.Talk to AndregFollow Andreg to the Slade of Shadows.Follow Andreg to the Slade of Shadows.Speak with Andreg at the Slade of Shadows.Talk to AndregThe three altars can be found between the trees at the heart of the Slade of Shadows.

Andreg instructed you to place the tokens of the gurach on the altars within the Slade of Shadows.Andreg is hiding near the Slade of Shadows.

You should return to Andreg at once.Talk to AndregWait with Andreg to see what happens.Wait with Andreg to see what happensDefeat the Tribunal of Shadows.Stop the elhudan and defeat the Tribunal of ShadowsAndreg is lying among the shards of the Dutegelh.

You should see if there is anything you can do to help Andreg.Talk to AndregThe tokens of the gurach are upon the altars at the heart of the Slade of Shadows.

Andreg instructed you to collect the tokens of the gurach and return to him.Collect the Token of the Goat from the first altarCollect the Token of the Ox from the second altarCollect the Token of the Stag from the third altarAndreg is lying mortally wounded among the shards of the Dutegelh at the heart of the Slade of Shadows.

You should bring the tokens of the gurach to Andreg at once.Talk to Andreg'I shall not...be returning with you...${PLAYER}. The cost of defeating...death...is the life...of the living.

'Return to...Saeradan and tell him...of our victory. Fare...well....''${PLAYER}, you told me that the altars bore the same marks as the tokens you brought from Saeradan. If this is indeed the case, the tokens may perhaps be used to call Gwyllion and her allies to the Slade.

'Come with me to the Slade of Shadows. There, we will see how the tokens may be of use to us.''Enter the Slade and place the tokens upon the altars, then return here to me. If I am correct, we may soon see the end of the Old Woman of the Mountain.''Let us see if my plan will bear fruit....''Unnh...${PLAYER}...when Gwyllion...said what she did...about the living...it...it reminded me of the...rest of the legend.

'The Dutegelh's weakness is the...living spirit...the gift of life. It has...ended the darkness.

'Collect the tokens of the gurach...from the altars, then...return to me...while I still have...breath....''The Old Woman of...the Mountain...lingers still, but not...unharmed. Now is the time to...strike. Now is the time to...move....'A company of Dragon-clan warriors is encamped at the northern end of the Gravenwood, marching down from Enedwaith.One of the Dunlending captains might carry the orders Thurbald seeks.

Thurbald has asked you to find a copy of the Draig-lûth's orders.Collect ordersThurbald is hiding to the south of Uvel-cadlus.

You should bring the orders you found to Thurbald at once.'Though the Dragon-clan has long been known to war with even their own countrymen, I fear this company is not here to stir trouble in Dunland. There have been Dunlending travellers going to and fro between Pren Gwydh and Tâl Methedras, and the Draig-lûth have ignored them.

'Perhaps one of them carries orders from their chieftain, or a general of their forces -- if there are such ranks among these wild men. Would you enter their camp, Uvel-cadlus, and seek such orders among their captains?

'It will be dangerous, but such information can only benefit our cause.''Indeed, this is as I feared. These orders are directing the Dragon-clan to join with a company from the Ox-clan at the Mustering Tree, from where they will march south to Wulf's Cleft.

'This is troubling, but useful information.'The Rangers Saeradan, Amlan, and Andreg have tracked Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, from the Windfells in Enedwaith to the Gravenwood of Dunland.Andreg is near the Slade of Shadows, some distance to the south of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Saeradan asked you to meet with Andreg and offer him your assistance.Talk to Andreg near the Slade of Shadows'While you were away, Andreg sent a message to me. He came upon a grove where creatures of darkness haunt the Gravenwood.

'With your tale of the Cuthraul at the Tree of Tribute and your discovery of these tokens, it is clear that Gwyllion is near at hand. Go meet with Andreg and see what assistance he requires of you.

'You may find Andreg near a place called the Slade of Shadows some distance to the south.''Meet Andreg near the Slade of Shadows... he will have work for you, I am sure.''It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. If you peer around the rock to the south, you will see that trouble is brewing in this place... I have need of your aid.'The barracks beneath Isengard are full of rats, and your Uruk-hai overseer thinks you should take care of the problem.The entrance to the barracks is located in the south-east wall of the main cavern beneath Isengard.

Your Uruk-hai overseer wants you to kill the rats that have taken over the barracks.Defeat rats in the barracks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should talk to your Uruk-hai overseer now that you have defeated many rats in the barracks.Talk to your Uruk-hai overseer'My brothers sleep in the barracks when they are not working, but there are not enough beds. We sleep in shifts: when one Uruk wakes, another takes his place. There is no room for laziness! Any Uruk who tries to stay in bed is likely to sleep forever... with a knife in his belly!

'It is one thing to share quarters with my fellow warriors... but the rats have become a real nuisance, gnawing and biting. Thin them out some, little ${RACE}, and be quiet about it! There will be warriors sleeping!

'The entrance to the barracks is in the south-east wall of the main cavern beneath Isengard.''You took care of the rats? It's about time! Maybe tonight I won't be gnawed half to pieces by the rotten things!

'You won't be my problem for much longer. Fâsh wants to see you again.'Andreg is taking you to meet with Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp; however, he needs help with his own mission first.Crebain can be found throughout the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>.

Andreg wants your help hunting crebain to rid the world of some of Saruman's spies.Defeat crebain in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should speak with Andreg about your successes against the crebain of the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>.Talk to Andreg'Look, ${PLAYER}, can you see them? At the very least, you can hear them...crebain. Crows are vile creatures to begin with, but the crebain of Dunland have been corrupted by Saruman and act as his spies.

'We should hunt a few of the wretched birds while we are here in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> and rid the world of a few more of the Wizard's spies.''Perhaps we should not have deviated from our mission, but I did not feel that we could afford not to take the opportunity to slay the crebain while we were here.

'Thank you.'The Slade of Shadows appears to be a focal point for the evil that is growing within the Gravenwood.The cauldron and altars which Andreg mentioned can be found between the great trees at the heart of the Slade of Shadows.

Andreg has instructed you to try and examine the altars and cauldron within the Slade of Shadows to learn what purpose they serve.Examine the cauldronExamine the first altarExamine the second altarExamine the third altar'Before I retreated to this rock, I was able to glimpse what appeared to be some small altars and a cauldron set between the large trees at the heart of the Slade. While you hunt the creatures within the Slade, try to get a glimpse at the structures... perhaps we can learn what purpose they serve.'Hogawise is worried about two of his kinsmen, who have not reported back to the camp since they went scouting the lake's edge.Two of Théodred's men went to scout the lake's edge: Déormund to the north-west and Herestan to the north. They have not returned, and Hogawise wants you to find them.Find DéormundFind HerestanHogawise is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.Talk to Hogawise at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras'Two of my kinsmen went to scout the lake's edge, and they have not returned. Déormund planned to scout the shore of the lake to the north-west, and Herestan followed the shore to the north.

'They are stout men and have seen service in war. Herestan has ridden to battle with Théodred's father, the King. I am sure they are fine, but still they should have returned by now.

'Scout for the scouts, ${PLAYER}, and help them if they are in need.''Déormund and Herestan should have returned by now. I am certain they are fine, but... still you should find them and ensure it.

'Déormund went to scout the north-west shore, and Herestan planned to follow the lake's edge to the north.''It is good... good to see you... friend. My leg... has been savaged by a trap of some sort. I was able to break the trap with a heavy stone, but I cannot yet walk on my leg.''I am...glad to see you... friend. I was scouting the edges of the village, near an orchard, when I was beset by three Dunlendings. I proved their better, but I think one of them had a poisoned blade. I suffered a cut during the fighting, and now I am very weak.

'I managed to make it away from the site of the battle, but my strength is gone and I can go no further.''You found Déormund and Herestan? I am relieved that they still live, but their encounters are a reminder that Tâl Methedras is full of danger. The Falcon-clan is not unprepared, and they have a strong defensive position.'Andreg is taking you to meet with Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp; however, he needs help with his own mission first.Andreg asked you to help him hunt Orcs in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>.Defeat Orcs in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should speak with Andreg regarding your successes against the Orcs of the White Hand in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>.Talk to Andreg'Orcs! These creatures bear the markings of the White Hand. What are Saruman's cronies doing here in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb>?

'I believe it is time to do some Orc-hunting, as well. Are you with me?''There is little worse than Orcs in this world. They may not be the most powerful creatures of evil, but they are among the most proliferate.'Penda fears for the fate of his missing allies. He now believes that they have battled into the territory of the Orcs who dwell in the mountain-caves.The Orcs dwell near the mountains to the north-west of Penda's camp.

Penda has requested a search for evidence of his campmate's presence among the tents and crates of the Orc-tribe.Frithstan is bound to a pole among the Orc-tribe in the western Wailing Hills.

Speaking with Frithstan may reveal the fate of the missing Rohirrim.Talk to the bound RohirrimThere is a crate near Frithstan in the western Orc-encampment.

Frithstan would you like to search the nearby crate for a set of keys.Search the crate near FrithstanFrithstan remains bound in the western Orc-encampment in the Wailing Hills.

You have found the keys that he has asked you to look for.Talk to Frithstan and release him from his shackles'Brave and skilled are the men under Frithstan, but they are no match for the sheer numbers of the Orc-horde. I fear that it may already be too late to aid them, but I must know for certain.

'If you have the courage, I would ask you to press onward into the territory of the Mountain-orcs to search for signs of my companions. Look among the Orc-tents and supply-crates for their belongings or for other evidence of their presence.''An Orc you are not, and you are no Rohirrim...so who are you and what are you doing here? You say Penda sent you?

'Oh, thank you! I am Frithstan. My men and I were captured by the Orcs when we launched an assault against them. 

'Look in the crate to my left and search for the Orc's key-ring.''The keys! You have found them! If I don such shackles never again, it will be too soon.

'Thankful am I for the pride of these Orcs. They were quite ill-prepared for your attempted rescue. It is shameful to have been captured by such beasts, but I am truly grateful for my release.''Search the Mor-hai camp thoroughly, there must be something there worth finding.'In order to prove that evil deeds are afoot in Eorlsmead Tower, evidence must be gathered.There is likely evidence of betrayal somewhere in the tower.

You should collect any evidence you find in the tower.Swithulf is at the Eorlsmead Tower.

You should speak with Swithulf and confirm the evidence you have collected.Talk to SwithulfThis blue scrap of cloth strikes you as odd. It does not seem to belong to a Rohirrim, by the look of it. Perhaps there is more to find that would indicate its source.'Gadda's concerns are well-founded. There is much going on here that Stanric could not have known about when he was alive, for I am sure he would not have approved. I can let you explore the tower, but I fear to rouse the suspicion of my peers.

'There is much evidence here of Sithric's dire corruption. Find any such evidence you can and bring it back to Gadda; hopefully, it will aid his cause.''Aye, this is everything I had noticed as well. I do not think anything has been missed.

'I was starting to worry that I was losing my wits, but I am relieved that you have reacted as I did!''Gadda will want to know as much as you can find out, so search well.'The Orcs in the Wailing Hills have begun leaving their caves and have compromised the safety of travellers along the road.The Orcs have been wandering north of the road that leads west from Stangard, in the north-west regions of the Wailing Hills.

Penda has made it clear that the Orcs pose a threat to the safety of travel along the road and that they must be dealt with carefully.Defeat Mor-hai defilers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Mor-hai scavengers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Penda can be found at the Rohirrim-camp along the road north of the Cuthstan and west of Stangard.

Penda awaits your return from protecting the road from the Orcs.Return to Penda at Frithstan's Camp'Our primary task is still to keep safe the road and protect the travel routes from Stangard to the west. This was an effortless chore in the past, but the Orcs have grown more agitated and daring, making things quite dangerous. They have crawled forth from their cave-dwellings and now venture into the light of day to cause us harm.

'We must still maintain the safety of the road, despite any other circumstances. Travel west again and put an end to any Orc-forces who may be openly walking in our lands. I will stand guard at this post and will await your return.''Keeping the road safe is a more important task than you might know. If it were to be cut off, the Orcs might be able to divide our forces.

'Return to me when the nearby Mor-hai have been defeated.''Rewarded shall you be for your service to Stangard and its people. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Seren wants you to steal back some of the provisions the Falcon-clan has stored in Tûr Morva.Provisions for war can be found throughout the village of Tûr Morva.

Seren has asked you to steal provisions back from the Falcon-clan.Collect provisions within Tûr Morva (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Seren is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.'My people have stored many provisions for war, ${PLAYER}. Ha! Listen to me: my people. They are no longer my people! I have not been a Falcon from the very moment Lheu Brenin sold us to the Wizard.

'Your friends helped the Hebog-lûth store many provisions. Take away these goods, and they will be less prepared to fight on behalf of Saruman. Go into the village and steal back some of these provisions!''Do not allow the Falcon-clan to keep the provisions your friends helped collect! Travel into Tûr Morva and steal back these goods!''Let us see how well the Falcon-clan wages its war without these goods!'A company of Dragon-clan warriors is encamped at the northern end of the Gravenwood, marching down from Enedwaith.Draig-lûth can be found in Uvel-cadlus.

Thurbald has asked you to defeat several Dragon-clan warriors.Defeat Draig-lûth at Uvel-cadlus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thurbald is hiding to the south of Uvel-cadlus.

You should return to Thurbald with news of your victory.Talk to Thurbald'Yonder company of Draig-lûth warriors present a threat, not just to my prince's scouting party, but to Rohan as a whole, I believe. Perhaps if we were to weaken their force, the threat would be lessened enough to make it impotent.

'Enter Uvel-cadlus, if you will, and defeat as many of the Dragon-clan's warriors as you can. When you have done so, return to me.''Well done, ${PLAYER}. That should give the Dragon-clan pause. Léofward will be pleased to hear of your courage!'Morflak's lackey has told you that the best food is saved for the guards at the gate, but Morflak wants some of it.The largest larder is within the guard-house, atop a short stair within the southernmost point of the ring-wall, right by the entrance to Isengard.

Morflak's lackey wants you to get some of the good food from the guard-house and to bring it to Morflak, north-west of the southern entrance and south-west of Orthanc.Find the guard-house by the southern gate and pick up some good foodYou have delivered the food to Morflak and should speak with him.Talk to MorflakMorflak's lackey is very pleased about your delivery of the food to Morflak.Talk to Morflak's lackey'There are larders in the buildings that line the Ring, and that's where the good food is kept. The largest one is within the guard-house, right by the entrance at the southern-most point of the ring. A set of steps lead to the door. You've seen the slop they feed us here. The good stuff is saved for the guards at the gate!

'Well, Morflak wants some of the good stuff, and if you get it for him, he's bound to share some of it with the ones he can trust. That's me, and if you do this well, maybe it's you too.

'So go to the larder and grab some of the good food -- don't let the gate-keepers see you with it -- and bring it back to Morflak!''This is much better than the slop we usually get! Those who serve Morflak well are always rewarded! You did very well, little ${RACE}.''Ah, the good stuff! This is much better than the usual slop we Uruk-hai get here.''Morflak is good to his friends. Just don't cross him, and you'll be fine. Keep it up, ${RACE}!'You discovered that the earth has been disturbed at the roots of the second tree Saeradan sent you to scout.The earth is disturbed at the foot of the Tree of Tribute, south-west of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Saeradan told you to follow the clues to the source of the evil in the Gravenwood. You should dig in the disturbed earth.Dig in the disturbed earth at the foot of the Tree of TributeYou should use the pick Saeradan gave you to dig at the disturbed roots of the tree.Théodred, son of King Théoden of Rohan, has led a small party of scouts into the Gravenwood to determine the movements and motives of the Dunlendings.The Rohirrim scouts Thurbald and Cuthric are somewhere in the northern reaches of the Gravenwood, while Elfrith returned south to watch the road into Wulf's Cleft.

Léofward has asked you to find the scouts he sent out into the Gravenwood and make sure they are well.Talk to ThurbaldThurbald is hiding outside a Dragon-clan encampment, north of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Thurbald needs your help with several tasks.Assist Thurbald with Breath of the DragonAssist Thurbald with Into the Dragon's MawAssist Thurbald with Pulling the Dragon's TeethThe Rohirrim scouts Thurbald and Cuthric are somewhere in the northern reaches of the Gravenwood, while Elfrith returned south to watch the road into the Isendale.

Léofward has asked you to find the scouts he sent out into the Gravenwood and make sure they are well.Talk to CuthricCuthric is hiding outside an Ox-clan encampment, west of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Cuthric needs your assistance with some tasks.Assist Cuthric with Charge of the OxAssist Cuthric with Heading off the StampedeAssist Cuthric with Prime CutThe Rohirrim scouts Thurbald and Cuthric are somewhere in the northern reaches of the Gravenwood, while Elfrith returned south to watch the road into the Isendale.

Léofward has asked you to find the scouts he sent out into the Gravenwood and make sure they are well.Talk to ElfrithElfrith is hiding outside and Orc-camp, south-west of the Rohirrim scout-camp.

Elfrith needs your assistance with some tasks.Assist Elfrith with Clear-cutting OrcsAssist Elfrith with Trophies of the EnemyAssist Elfrith with Wanton DestructionLéofward is at the Rohirrim scout-camp.

You should return to Léofward with the information provided to you by the Rohirrim scouts.Talk to Léofward at the Rohirrim scout-camp'${PLAYER}, if you wish to be of aid to me, I have a task of great import -- though it may not seem so at the first. I sent several scouts out into the Gravenwood to discover any movement of Dunlending forces, but I have not yet heard from any of them.

'Would you seek out the scouts and learn if any ill has befallen them? It has been too long, and I fear for my companions. Their names are Thurbald, Elfrith, and Cuthric. Thurbald and Cuthric have gone north and east into the Gravenwood, while Elfrith has returned south to watch the road to Wulf's Cleft.

'I will reward you for your efforts.''Seek out Thurbald, Cuthric, and Elfrith and find out what they have discovered.''Léofward sent you? That is well, for I have discovered an encampment of Draig-lûth -- Dragon-clan warriors -- moving down from Enedwaith. News of their movement should be taken to Léofward at once... I will remain and keep an eye on the encampment.

'If you wish to be of further aid, I may have other tasks for you before you leave, though.''Indeed, I am well, ${CLASS}. I have discovered an encampment of warriors of the Uch-lûth, the Ox-clan, marching eastward out of Carreglyn. I daresay they are up to no good. Take this news at once to Léofward.

'If you wish to be of further aid, I may have other tasks for you before you leave.''You there, Léofward sent you? I have news for you to take to him: a band of Orcs bearing the mark of the White Hand has entered the Gravenwood and has been clear-cutting the forest here. I know not for what purpose, but they have been shipping the wood eastward.

'If you wish to be of further assistance, I may have other tasks for you before you go.''This news is distressing. The Orcs are of little concern to me -- let them consume the Dunlendings' wood -- but the companies of Dunlending warriors troubles me. From what you tell me, they will be converging upon the Mustering Tree, and that is an ill omen.

'Despite the enmity the Draig-lûth have shown to their own countrymen, I think it more likely that both companies are meeting as allies to join the host gathering in Wulf's Cleft.

'I must think upon this problem.'You found a dead rat in the cellar of the tower. Some foam around the mouth indicates that it may have died of unnatural causes. You should search for whatever may have caused dead rats to appear in a tower occupied by healthy men.Whatever caused the rat to die can be found somewhere in the tower.

You should search for whatever the rat ingested that would have caused it to die.Search for possible ingredients of the ingested substanceSearch for whatever contained the ingested substanceThe rat's body is contorted as if it died in pain, but there are no obvious signs of external damage. A green foam around its mouth seems suspicious. You should search for signs of what the rat may have ingested to cause its death.You found a mysterious scrap of blue cloth near the armour on the second floor. It does not match anything you have ever seen a Rohirrim wear.Scraps of blue fabric can likely be found in the Eorlsmead Tower.

You should search the tower for more scraps of this strange-hued cloth.Find more of the blue fabricThis blue scrap of cloth strikes you as odd. It does not fit or belong with anything else you have seen the Rohirrim wear. Perhaps there is more to be found that would indicate a possible source of this strange fabric.The Slade of Shadows appears to be a focal point for the evil that is growing within the Gravenwood.Cuthraul can be found in the Slade of Shadows, south of Andreg's position.

Andreg has instructed you to defeat the Cuthraul in the Slade of Shadows.Defeat Cuthraul at the Slade of Shadows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Cuthraul are among the deadliest of the fell spirits haunting the Slade of Shadows. As you investigate the Slade, try to banish as many of the spirits as you can, for I fear they will become an army against whom there can be no reckoning if they are not curbed.'You found all of Léofward's scouts and reported back to him. Now Léofward prepares to act upon your discoveries.

<rgb=#FF0000>This instance can only be run solo.</rgb>Léofward is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in the Gravenwood.

You should let Léofward know when you are ready to depart for the Mustering Tree.Accompany Léofward to the Mustering TreeLéofward is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in the Gravenwood.

You should return to Léofward to discuss the battle at the Mustering Tree.Talk to Léofward at the Rohirrim scout-camp'I am distressed, ${PLAYER}. I fear that Cuthric's insolent goading of the Ox-clan captain has compromised our mission. More than that, both companies now converge upon the Mustering Tree, and I fear that once they have combined their strength, they will overrun our camp, and Théodred will have to fall back.

'I will join Thurbald, Elfrith, and Cuthric and make a stand against the foe...will you join me, ${PLAYER}? At the least, we will have an end worthy of rememberance.

'Let me know what you decide, my friend, but I must know soon.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This instance can only be run solo.</rgb>'Ah, ${PLAYER}. I was rendered unconscious during the battle, but apparently the Dunlendings thought me dead. When they had removed themselves from the Mustering Tree, your Ranger friend found me and brought me back here.

I will live, but others are lost forever but in song. Our lost companions will be missed, but I believe our actions will hinder the war-efforts of the Dunlendings...though to what degree, I cannot yet say.''It is decided then! Let us be off and let the Dunlendings beware!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This instance can only be run solo.</rgb>Warriors of the Falcon-clan can be found throughout Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras.Warriors of the Falcon-clan can be found throughout Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras.Defeat Falcon-clan warriors in Tâl Methedras (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Théodred is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.

You have defeated many Falcon-clan warriors and should return to Théodred at the forward encampment.Talk to Théodred at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras'The warriors of the Falcon-clan that have fortified the village are deadlier than most, ${PLAYER}. Their leather armour is strong and tough, their weapons are coated in some poison, and they have learned fighting skills from the Rangers. These are not the rabble with which we have grown accustomed.

'Go to the village and face their warriors. The talons of the Falcon must be dulled or broken before we can hope to rescue your friends from the prison-cave.''You have done well to defeat warriors of the Falcon-clan, ${PLAYER}. Their champions, however, remain.''We must dull the talons of the Falcon. Face the warriors in Tûr Morva, but do not underestimate them! Their armour is sturdy and tough, their weapons are coated in some poison, and they have training in the melee arts of the North.'Penda is disturbed by the loss of his companions at his Rohirrim-camp and is trying to discover what has happened.Penda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge.

Penda believes that there may be clues around the Rohirrim-camp that could reveal what may have happened to cause his companions to leave so suddenly.You have collected sufficient evidence and should now return to Penda.Return to Penda to discuss your findingsPenda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge.

You have discovered a few clues around the abandoned camp and should report your findings to Penda.Return to Penda to discuss your findingsPenda has asked you to search for clues to the west of the Rohirrim-camp.You have collected sufficient evidence and should now return to Penda.Return to Penda with the results of your searchPenda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge.

You have discovered a few clues while investigating outside of the Rohirrim-camp. You should return to Penda and report your findings to him.Return to Penda with the results of your search'Several nights have I spent to the north, scouting in the hills for Frithstan. I have returned too late, only to discover these empty tents and dying fires. Our orders were to watch the road and to send word to Stangard on occasion...as to what would cause my companions to simply depart so suddenly, I cannot imagine.

'Would you look around the camp for clues as to why they might have left or to where they might have gone? Return to me if you find anything of note.''Empty tents and missing horses...were you able to find anything else?'

Penda listens as you detail the discoveries you have made.

'My companions had been drinking more than usual it seems, and when they left, they took along weapons but not their personal belongings. I am beginning to envision what may have happened here.

'It is a start, but we need more evidence. Head to the west of here and look for more clues. Be careful of ambushes by the Orcs, as they have become more bold and fierce of late.''This evidence all suggests that Frithstan and my fellows have assaulted the Mountain-orcs head on.

'Oh, the impetuous fools! What have they rushed into? The men in camp were always anxious for action and silently cursed the orders from Stangard to sit and guard. I fear that their desire to charge valiantly to battle may have now wrought their doom.''It seems there are still more things in camp which should be inspected. I am interested to know what you might find.''I believe there is some clue still waiting to be found. Keep searching to the north-west...I am interested to know what you might find.The Mor-hai defiler, Dushatár, is brewing poison made from spider's venom to be used against the Men of Stangard.Dushatár dwells in the depths of the Mor-hai cave to the north-west.

Frithstan has asked you to gather allies in order to put an end to Dushatár and his schemes of brewing deadly poisons.Defeat Dushatár the DefilerFrithstan is waiting at his camp along the road west of Stangard.

Frithstan awaits news of your attack against the Defiler, Dushatár.Return to Frithstan at his camp'I have been told of the Orc in charge of the Mor-hai, the one guiding the production of the poisons to be used against us. His name is Dushatár the Defiler.

'Action must be swift, but we are still feeling the effects of the venom. We must rely on you to put a stop to this! Gather your allies and seek out the defiler in the Mor-hai cave.''It is comforting to know that you have put a stop to Dushatár. Without their leader and his terrible poisons, the Mor-hai will think again before confronting us.'Gadda has a longstanding friendship with a guard at the tower near the abandoned farm.Swithulf is at the tower near the farmstead.

Gadda wants you to speak with his friend Swithulf and learn what transpires at the tower.Talk to Swithulf'The tower near here has long been under the control of men I do not consider trustworthy. I have seen many carts of goods enter full and leave empty...things I believe intended for Stangard.

'A few weeks ago, a longstanding friend of mine was enlisted to join them. Would you be so good as to find out what he knows? I fear to approach the tower, for I am wanted for treason at Stangard.

'My friend's name is Swithulf.''You are a friend of Gadda? That is well. I do not feel any kindness towards the happenings surrounding this place, nor towards the men who serve here.''The men at the tower have long made me suspicious.'Herestan has suffered a poisoned wound from a Dunlending blade and needs your help to brew an antidote.Digestive roots can be found throughout Tâl Methedras, around the shores of the lake and on the eyot in the middle of the water, at the base of trees.Collect digestive roots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The grinding stone is at the armour-making pavillion north of Herestan.

You now have some digestive roots and need to grind them into powder.Herestan is to the south of the grinding stone, by the lake's edge, where you left him.'I do not feel well...so weak....'

You think back to your time in Tûr Morva and remember Iwan of the Falcon-clan experimenting with poisons. You remember too the words of Maelona, who spoke of collecting certain roots throughout Tâl Methedras and grinding them up to form a digestive powder. The roots could be found at the base of certain trees around the lake in Tâl Methedras.

You tell Herestan that you may be able to help him.'You think...you can help me? I am...so weak from...the poison....'

You remember the powder Maelona made that cured Iwan of his self-inflicted poisoning and think you might be able to help Herestan. You need to find digestive roots from the base of certain trees located around the lake in Tâl Methedras.'I am sorry that I cannot...be of more help...to you...so weak....'

You remember the grinding stone at the pavillion to the north. You can use that to grind up the digestive roots.'You have...returned...my friend....'

You gently give Herestan the root powder, and he swallows it with some difficulty. After a moment, he takes a deep breath and much of the colour returns to his face.

'I feel much better already, my friend. Thank you for taking the time to find this antidote! But...how did you know how to make this curative? I am fortunate you did!'There is work to be done in the kitchens beneath Isengard.Barkh manages the kitchens in the south-west wall of the cavern beneath Isengard.

Your overseer wants you to report to the kitchens beneath Isengard for work.Talk to BarkhPiles of slop litter the floor of the kitchens beneath Isengard.

Barkh has given you a rag and the unenviable task of cleaning up after the Uruk-hai.Clean up piles of slop in the kitchens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The slop bucket is in the kitchens.

Barkh wants you to squeeze out the rag you used to clean up the slop into the slop bucket in the kitchens.Barkh is waiting to speak to you in the kitchens beneath Isengard.Return the dirty rag to BarkhThere is still slop to be cleaned up in the kitchens beneath Isengard.Clean up piles of slop in the kitchens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The slop bucket is in the kitchens.

Barkh wants you to squeeze out the rag you used to clean up the slop into the slop bucket in the kitchens.Barkh is in the kitchens beneath Isengard, waiting to speak to you.Barkh wants you to get some slop from the slop bucket in the kitchens and bring it to the bucket in the dungeons. The entrance to the dungeons is in the north-west wall of the main cavern.Get some slop from the slop bucket in the kitchensOne of the prisoners has tried to get your attention. You should talk to him.Talk to Baldgar in the dungeonYour Uruk-hai overseer wants to talk to you.Talk to your Uruk-hai overseer'There's work that needs doing in the kitchens! You think this army feeds itself? There's meat roasting, gruel boiling, and bread baking day and night!'

The Uruk-hai grins, baring his fangs.

'Not that you'll get any of that. Prisoners have their own ration. Barkh'll have something else for you to do, I'd wager. To the kitchens with you! They're in the south-west wall of the cavern, and if you don't make good time, I'll tan your hide!''Another worm from the surface! I'm of a mind to chop you up for stew... give the boys something they can sink their fangs into!'

Your Uruk-hai overseer grunts sadly, shaking his head with disappointment.

'It's like that, is it?' responds Barkh. 'Too bad. It's not worth my head to cross the Old Man, and once he's done with you, you won't be fit for stew anyway. Take this rag and clean some of the slop off the floors. You might as well be good for something! Once you're done, squeeze that rag out into the slop bucket there.''Well, get to it! That slop's not going to clean up itself! Use that rag I gave you; you won't be getting another! Once you're done, squeeze out the rag over the slop bucket over there.''Can you do anything right? The slop bucket is right over there! Squeeze out that rag I gave you into the bucket!''You think you're done? You're not done until I say you're done! Clean up more of the slop, then dump it into the slop bucket again!

'You work for Barkh, and Barkh says there's more to be done!''Get to it, slime! You clean up that slop with the rag I gave you, or I'll send you back to Fâsh in pieces and let him figure out what to tell the Old Man!

'When you're done, squeeze out that rag into the slop bucket, like before! And you'll do it as many times as I say you'll do it!''Don't give me that dirty rag! Squeeze it out in the slop bucket! If Sharkû didn't want you, I'd have your head for that!''You could not have done that more slowly if you tried, worm. Still, the slop had to be cleaned, and you cleaned it. There will be more later. There's always more!'

Barkh bares his teeth at you.

'It's time to feed the prisoners. Scoop out some feed from the slop bucket and carry it to the dungeons in the north-west wall of the main cavern. Empty the slop into the bucket by the cells. And be quick about it. The thralls have got to eat! Ha! Ha!''Why are you just standing there? Get some slop from that bucket and bring it to the slop bucket in the dungeons! The prisoners have to eat, after all!

'The entrance to the dungeons is in the north-west wall of the main cavern. Get moving!''Hey! ${RACE}! Do you know anything about what is going on outside? I am a man of Rohan, Baldgar by name, and I was separated from my men not far from the river. Can you tell me if Rohan is still safe?'

But there are too many guards around, and it is not safe to talk.'We will talk later, if we get the opportunity!''No talking to the prisoners! You are no less a captive than they, and if you weren't in my company, you'd be thrown in a cell to rot. Remember that. One word to Fâsh, and you won't even have the benefit of stretching your legs.

'A different word, and you might call those locked in the cells the lucky ones!'Gadda wishes for you to ask around Stangard about the death of Stanric, hoping that someone will know if Sithric was involved.Sabert, your friend at Stangard, still guards the gate.

You should speak with Sabert upon your return to Stangard.Talk to Sabert, your one remaining friend at StangardMen of Stangard can be found throughout the town.

You should question many men about the death of Stanric, for Gadda suspects treachery on Sithric's part.Ask Byrnstan about the death of StanricAsk Uthrad about the death of StanricAsk Wada about the death of StanricAsk Athulf about the death of StanricAsk Adalbert about the death of StanricSabert guards the front gate of Stangard.

You should speak with Sabert at once about all that transpired during your questioning.Return to Sabert at the front gate'Now that you have seen our new mission here in carrying on what you began, I hope that you will help me one last time. If I return to Stangard, it will be my death... but I could not serve under such a man as Sithric. Stanric was my commander.

'I fear that there was treachery involved in Stanric's death, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot go back to investigate. No one will talk to me -- they will only arrest me or kill me on sight. I hope that you can discover what really happened.''I am glad to see you again, my friend. Things are not well here since our good leader passed. How fares Gadda? I wish he would return to set things right....

'Gadda told me he suspected treachery in Stanric's death, but I have not the courage to ask anyone. Too many here have grown loyal to Sithric.''You again? I would be careful if I were you... I hear Sithric has the guards on order to take you in for treason and trespassing.

'But you asked about Stanric... and indeed it is curious that he died so suddenly, not ill, not frail, strong and hale as an ox. I did not see it, myself, so I cannot say more.''You! Sithric is wanting to have words with you. Come along nice and quietly to the lock-house....''I... do not wish to speak too loudly on this issue, but I agree with Gadda. I was half tempted to leave with him, but I fear the repercussions.

'Things are worse than ever now, and I think Stanric was trying to stand up to Sithric... that is, right before he died. It is strange, is it not?''Nobody saw what happened, but Stanric seemed healthy and inspired just before his death! In fact, he kept talking about you. He was trying to motivate people to do what was right and not what was ruled.

'He felt that the council was too slow to make decisions, and Stangard had suffered too long. And... it seemed that the men responded very well to his guidance. Then... he was dead!''You! Sithric is wanting to have words with you. Come along nice and quietly to the lockhouse....''Sithric ordered guards to arrest you? Why, I heard nothing of that! And how suspicious that nobody saw Stanric die or even saw him sick. He was in perfect health just the day before.

'I am beginning to grow roused, ${PLAYER}. The investigation should not stop now!'Morflak's lackey has given you the names of some Uruk-hai his boss does not trust and that he wants you to punish.The Uruk-hai named Gluthrak, Hoital, and Farmak can be found somewhere within the Ring of Isengard.

Morflak's lackey wants you to fight one of the Uruk-hai named by his boss in order to quell any challenges to his power.Find and challenge Gluthrak, Hoital, or FarmakMorflak's lackey has some more names for you.Talk to Morflak's lackeyThe Uruk-hai named Matum, Urbhár, and Golb can be found somewhere within the Ring of Isengard.Find and challenge Matum, Urbhár, or GolbMorflak's lackey is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Morflak's lackey'You heard the boss. As long as we stay in line, he treats us well and everybody wins. But if you cross him, that's another story.

'Sometimes, an Uruk-hai gets it into his head to try and displace Morflak. He thinks maybe if he's in charge, he'll get noticed by the Old Man and be given some treat. He sees what Morflak has, and he wants it. It's in his best interest not to cross the boss, but he forgets it.

'The boss gave me the names of some of the boys who might be planning on acting up. The names are Gluthrak, Hoital, and Farmak. Let's pay one of them a visit. That might put the fear of Morflak back in the others, where it should be. I could use a fight.''Ah, that was just the thing. Nothing like a good fight to make you feel alive!

'I have some more names for you: Matum, Urbhár, and Golb. Choose one of them to punish and remind the other two why it is wisest not to cross the boss. You'll find any of them within the Ring.''That was well done! Morflak will be pleased, and when Morflak is pleased, it is good for all of us.''You're one of Morflak's new pets, are you? Well, the way I see it, you'll end up the same way as all the others. And maybe I'll be the one to help you on your way!''Do you think you can defeat me? You have no chance! Morflak should have come himself and done his own dirty work!'Gadda hopes to hold this farm long against such hunger and short supply as befell Stangard.Wood and ore can be found in the plains surrounding the abandoned farm.

You should collect wood and ore for the farm's supply.Collect wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gadda can be found at the abandoned farm.

You should bring the materials you gathered to Gadda for his supply.'I hope to hold this farm long against the ills that befell Stangard when Sithric arrived. This place can be a haven to all who come here, and I will defend it with my own life.

'I wish to see us well-supplied for the coming months, and I have been gathering ore and wood whenever I get a chance. Would you be willing to add some to our stores?''Hail, friend! Ah, this is a very good supply. I appreciate your great efforts on our behalf, as always.'Déormund's leg was caught in a snap-jaw trap and the Rohirrim has been injured. He needs time to recover, and he wants you to destroy the other traps.Snap-jaw traps have been placed in the undergrowth on the western shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras.

Déormund has given you a heavy stone with which to smash the snap-jaw traps you find.Break snap-jaw traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Déormund is waiting to speak with you on the western shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras.'There are certain to be more traps like this one on this side of the lake, ${PLAYER}. I have seen strange creatures in this land, creatures with powerful jaws full of sharp teeth. I do not know what they are called. I have not seen such creatures in Rohan.

'The Falcon-clan has taken the jaws of these creatures to make traps and have hidden them in the undergrowth. Take this heavy stone and use it to break some of these traps. You will need to get close to the traps, but try not to get too close, or you will set them off!''Use the stone that I gave you to destroy the snap-jaw traps hidden on this side of the lake. You will need to get close to each trap... but do not get too close.''You have destroyed the traps? Good! I would not want any of my kinsmen to suffer the same injury as I have done. It was very painful... and not just physically. I am shamed to have stumbled into such a trap.

'Such traps are the province of lesser men. A man of Rohan would not resort to such measures.

'Thank you for your help, ${PLAYER}. I believe that I will soon be able to walk on my injured leg.'The Slade of Shadows is the site of a nefarious ritual conducted by the Old Woman of the Mountain to summon fell spirits out of the world of shadow.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Andreg awaits you near the Slade of Shadows.

You should speak with Andreg when you are ready to put his plan in motion.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Accompany Andreg to the Slade of ShadowsSaeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp, north of the Slade of Shadows.

You should return to Saeradan with the news of Andreg's sacrifice at the Slade of Shadows.Bring the tokens of the gurach to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp'Matters here are more dire than I had first believed, ${PLAYER}. From your description, I believe the cauldron that rests within the Slade of Shadows is the fabled Dutegelh.

'Legend tells that it is a relic once kept by the Necromancer at Dol Guldur, lost when he was driven forth by the White Council. It is rumoured to have the power to create an army of wights... if I am correct, Gwyllion may be trying to use it on behalf of Saruman. She must be stopped.

'For this, I have a plan... speak with me when you are ready.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Good! Let's us move closer to the Slade of Shadows... I have a plan to ensnare Gwyllion and her allies.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Alas, Andreg was a good friend and a stout companion. He will be remembered for his sacrifice.

'Gwyllion has much to answer for... it is a pity that she escaped. At least her allies from the Ox and Stag clans will be of no further trouble. Nevertheless, we will renew our efforts to find the Old Woman of the Mountain and bring her to justice.

'Thank you for returning these tokens... I may yet have a use for them.'Penda has invited you to participate in a traditional memorial service to the departed soldiers who had once fought alongside you.Red aster may be collected north of Frithstan's camp, scattered around Aster Hill.

Penda has asked you to collect red aster, a bright flower that blooms in the Wailing Hills.Collect red aster for the tribute (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The memorial location is at the base of the Cuthstan, atop the large hill where Lanbert's camp may be found.

The flowers may be placed at the memorial site in order to pay respect to all those honourable warriors who have passed on.Place the flowers at the base of the Cuthstan'When the spirits of those who have fought alongside us pass on from this land, it is traditional to pay them tribute for their service. Sadly, the men of this land know this practice all too well, and a common memorial area has been placed at the Cuthstan monument.

'You are welcome to join in our tradition. I ask that you collect the red flowers scattered across Aster Hill. Bring them south and place them on the stones around the Cuthstan in memory of Odda and the other fallen Rohirrim.''The flowers that you will need are called red aster and can be found growing among the other flowers on Aster Hill to the north.

'Take them to the Cuthstan when you are ready to pay your respects.'Morflak's lackey wants you to see if there is anything Urdan, the builder of war-machines for Saruman, needs you to do.Urdan is by the large war-machines on the eastern side of the Ring of Isengard.

Morflak's lackey wants you to see if Urdan has anything that needs doing.Talk to UrdanUrdan wants you to fetch him a crate of tools from the anvil field north of Orthanc. He told you to follow the Ring-wall north to reach it.Pick up a crate of toolsMorflak's lackey wants to speak with you.Talk to Morflak's lackey'You aren't like others of your kind, are you? You know when to do as you're told!

'Urdan has built many of the siege-engines the Old Man plans to use for the war, and many are still under construction. Go see if he has any work for you to do.''I am going to speak with Morflak about this. Urdan should know better than to give you such trivial business. Hauling crates around? Doesn't he know you belong to Morflak now?''You're one of Morflak's underlings? I'd rather he left me alone! I've got work to do, real work, and don't have time for his bluster.

'Most of these engines are nearly finished, ${RACE}. I could use another crate of tools if you need something to keep you busy. Follow the Ring-wall to the north; you'll find the crates near the anvil field by the great bellows, north of the tower.''Stop standing around and fetch me a crate of tools from the anvil field north of here! Just follow the Ring-wall north until you see the anvil field and the great bellows! Morflak will hear about this if you don't do this at once!'Orcs serving the White Hand are clear-cutting the forest and shipping the wood off to an unknown location.Orcs can be found at Ak-ghru.

Elfrith asked you to collect Orc-heads as trophies to display as a warning to the Enemy in the Gravenwood.Collect Orc-heads at Ak-ghru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elfrith is hiding beyond the bounds of Ak-ghru.

You should bring the heads you collected to Elfrith.'If you enter Ak-ghru to hunt Orcs, bring back trophies of your victories. I would build a wall of Orc-heads to stand as a warning to these vile creatures... what say you?''Victory, ${PLAYER}! I will use these as a warning to the Orcs that their presence will not be tolerated! My thanks to you.'Bingo wants to meet the folk who live at the outpost of Stangard and learn of the situation along the banks of the Great River.The gate-keeper Sabert guards the eastern gate of Stangard, south of Haldirith.

Bingo wants to do what he can to help relations between the Elves and the Rohirrim, and wants to travel south to Stangard.Talk to Sabert at the east-gate of StangardBingo is outside the east-gate of Stangard, in Eorlsmead along the Great River.

Sabert has rudely refused Bingo entrance to the outpost of Stangard.Talk to Bingo outside the east-gate of StangardSabert turned a woman away from the gate of Stangard and now Bingo wants to search north-west of the outpost to find her and ensure her safety. Sabert thought she was headed in the direction of Frithstan's Camp.Search for the missing woman north-west of Stangard, near Frithstan's Camp in the Wailing HillsLanghár is outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills.Talk to Langhár outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing HillsOrcs can be found throughout the Wailing Hills.

Langhár has asked you to help her defeat Orcs throughout the Wailing Hills, not really to aid the men of Stangard so much as to protect her home in the Vales of Anduin.Defeat Orcs throughout the Wailing Hills (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo is outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills.

You have defeated Orcs in the Wailing Hills, and should now return to Bingo and Langhár outside Frithstan's Camp.Talk to Bingo outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing HillsLanghár is outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills.

You have defeated many Orcs in the Wailing Hills, and should now return to Langhár.Talk to Langhár outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing HillsLanghár saw an Eagle descend into a stand of trees in the north-east corner of the Wailing Hills, on the edge of Thinglad, and thinks you should find him.Talk to Landroval in the secluded clearingBingo Boffin is in a secluded clearing in the north-eastern corner of the Wailing Hills.

You have found Landroval the Eagle, and Bingo seems to be quite overwhelmed by the great creature.Langhár is in the secluded clearing in the north-east corner of the Wailing Hills.Langhár thinks you should collect venom-sacs from spiders throughout the Wailing Hills, both in order to provide a helpful service and to give Bingo time to speak to Landroval.Collect venom-sacs from spiders throughout the Wailing Hills (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected venom-sacs from the spiders of the Wailing Hills, and should return to the Secluded Clearing.Bingo is in the secluded clearing in the north-eastern corner of the Wailing Hills.Sabert guards the east-gate of Stangard, and Bingo wants to warn him of the enemy presence Landroval saw gathering.Bring Landroval's warning to Sabert at the east-gate of StangardBingo is outside the east-gate of Stangard.

Sabert did not heed your warning of an army in the Brown Lands.Talk to Bingo outside the east-gate of Stangard'The outpost of Stangard is a short distance to the south, but none of the Elves here will speak of it to me. That is not very neighbourly! Do you think there may be some unfortunate slight behind these poor feelings? It may have taken me some time to return Poppy's ball of twine or Merrimac's teapot, but I did eventually. Do you think something similar happened between the Elves and the Rohirrim?

'Let us go south to Stangard and ask someone about it at the front gate of the outpost. Perhaps we can ease these poor feelings in some way, ${PLAYER}, and if we cannot at least I will obtain some more material for my book. But I hope we can help!''Let us go south to Stangard and ask someone about it at the front gate of the outpost. Perhaps we can ease these poor feelings in some way, ${PLAYER}, and if we cannot at least I will obtain some more material for my book. But I hope we can help!''Well, this is Stangard. Now let us see what is going on here!''This halfling may have come to Stangard with a desire to see our lands, but this is not a holiday retreat. There is nothing here for your diminutive friend. He is not the first peculiar visitor I have turned away from this outpost. With my ill fortune, he will not be the last.

'What is it that draws such unwelcome guests hither? Tell your friend to find the woman I turned away to the north-west, and perhaps the three of you can journey with haste away from Rohan. When last I saw her, she was headed in the direction of Frithstan's Camp. May the three of you find your way to some other land.''This very morning, a rough and uncouth woman sought to gain entrance to Stangard, but I turned her away as is my duty. If you find her somewhere to the north-west, perhaps the three of you can journey with haste away from Rohan. May the three of you find your way to some other land.''Well! That was quite a rude greeting! Perhaps the animosity between the Elves and the Rohirrim is not the result of a borrowed item unreturned after all.

'If this fellow does not want me to come inside, I will respect his wishes. Perhaps we should find this woman of whom he spoke, and see if she needs our help? Sabert may not care if she runs afoul of some beast, but he should feel some responsibility if it were to happen!

'He said she went to the north-west?''If this fellow does not want me to come inside, I will respect his wishes. Perhaps we should find this woman of whom he spoke, and see if she needs our help? Sabert may not care if she runs afoul of some beast, but he should feel some responsibility if it were to happen!

'He said she went to the north-west? What did he call her? Rough and uncouth? It seems to me that is a fitting description of Sabert himself!''I wish you luck, for so long as your feet take you away from Stangard.''Hail, travellers!''This must be the woman. She looks very fierce!''Is she... of Beorn's line? I have heard tales of the Beornings! She looks very strong, and a little frightening! Why would the Rohirrim turn her away?''I bid you welcome, travellers, and would advise you to avoid Stangard, if you have not come from there already. The men of that place do not recognize their own friends or allies, even as they have need of them.

'I am Langhár, of the line of Beorn, and I have set forth from the Vales of Anduin at the command of Grimbeorn. Orcs threaten the shores of the Great River, and someone must beat them back. The men of Rohan cower behind their walls, and they refused my offer of help. They are fools.

'If I returned to Grimbeorn with this tale, I am certain he would send me elsewhere, and leave the Rohirrim to fend for themselves. But the Vales of Anduin are not far from here, and any victory by the Orcs here might endanger my own home, so I will help the fools of Stangard, whether they accept it or not. If you would help me in this, defeat Orcs throughout the Wailing Hills! I am a skin-changer, and more than capable of felling these foes, but it seems the supply of them is never-ending.''The Vales of Anduin are not far from here, and any victory by the Orcs here might endanger my own home, so I will help the fools of Stangard, whether they accept it or not. If you would help me in this, defeat Orcs throughout the Wailing Hills! I am a skin-changer, and more than capable of felling these foes, but it seems the supply of them is never-ending.''We should help her with her task, ${PLAYER}! I have heard some frightening things about the Beornings, but she seems to have the right idea as far as the Orcs are concerned!''Let the Orcs tremble in their caves! Perhaps now they will remain within, and trouble these lands no more. If the Rohirrim will not drive them out, it is up to us to take care of this blight.''I have seen more than my share of Orcs by now, ${PLAYER}, but we are truly making these lands more safe with each meeting, aren't we? It is good we encountered Langhár here, instead of continuing elsewhere.

'She is the first Beorning I have ever met, and she is not what I expected. There have been stories about her people even in the Shire, and many of them portray the line of Beorn as being bloodthirsty and angry, more beast than man. It is true that Langhár has no mercy for her enemies, and does not speak well of the men of Stangard, but I am moved by the realization that she carries out her duty despite the outright rejection of those it serves.

'She helps those who refuse her help. I wonder how many of us would do the same?''Beornings are an interesting people, are they not?''Very good, my new friends. You have done well to fight the Orcs, and certainly better than the cowardly men of Stangard could have done!

'I too fought the Orcs among the Wailing Hills, and as I searched for foes to defeat I saw an Eagle in the skies to the north and watched it descend into a stand of trees. The Eagles have been on good terms with my people for many years.

'We should go to him and learn what he has seen from the heights. Such knowledge might be of use to me as I seek to accomplish my task.''As I searched for foes to defeat I saw an Eagle in the skies to the north and watched it descend into a stand of trees. The Eagles have been on good terms with my people for many years.

'We should go to him and learn what he has seen from the heights. Such knowledge might be of use to me as I seek to accomplish my task.''Langhár saw an Eagle somewhere to the north? We should go find it!''Greetings, little ${RACE}. You would be wise to use caution in these lands, for you are bound to the earth and many dangerous beings crawl there, eager to do you harm. Indeed, some of these foes aim their weapons skyward, intending to do harm to my kind as well.''Will you look at that, ${PLAYER}? I have never seen one of the Great Eagles before, and I never expected to do so. What an honour! Have you ever seen such majesty before? And he can speak!'

Bingo stammers with excitement.

'Do... do you think he will give me an interview for my book? I would not even know what to ask him, but I have to think of something. Oh, I am so nervous... I hope I do not embarrass myself. He seems so wise and well-spoken, and I am just a small hobbit from the Shire, and feeling smaller than usual!''Will you look at that, ${PLAYER}? I have never seen one of the Great Eagles before, let alone two of them! What an honour! Have you ever seen such majesty before? And they can speak!'

Bingo stammers with excitement.

'Do... do you think they will give me interviews for my book? I would not even know what to ask them, but I have to think of something. Oh, I am so nervous... I hope I do not embarrass myself. They seem so wise and well-spoken, and I am just a small hobbit from the Shire, and feeling smaller than usual!''I take it Bingo has never seen one of the Great Eagles before! I remember when Grimbeorn first took me to see them. I was just a cub, and was quite overwhelmed by the experience! Meneldor was the name of the Eagle I met, and he towered above me. I cannot begin to guess at his true size, but in my memory he seemed as big as a house. I wonder what became of him?

'We should give Bingo some time to speak with Landroval. After all, if we were to take him away now he would be able to think of nothing else!

'Let us defeat some of the venomous spiders that stalk among the Wailing Hills, and collect their venom-sacs. That way we will be giving Bingo time to speak with the Eagle and we will be combating a threat at the same time.''I take it Bingo has never seen one of the Great Eagles before! I remember when Grimbeorn first took me to see them. I was just a cub, and was quite overwhelmed by the experience! It is good to see Meneldor again! He does not seem quite as large as I remember, but I was smaller then.

'We should give Bingo some time to speak with the Eagles. After all, if we were to take him away now he would be able to think of nothing else!

'Let us defeat some of the venomous spiders that stalk among the Wailing Hills, and collect their venom-sacs. That way we will be giving Bingo time to speak with the Eagles and we will be combating a threat at the same time.''That was good work against the spiders, ${PLAYER}. Do you think Bingo is done speaking with Landroval yet?''That was good work against the spiders, ${PLAYER}. Do you think Bingo is done speaking with the Eagles yet?''${PLAYER}! I have had a lovely conversation with Landroval, but I have learned something most troubling, and it has brought our chat to an end!

'He is quite a delightful fellow, if you ask this hobbit, and his patience with my questions was really quite extraordinary. I asked him some details concerning what it must be like to fly, and he was very good-natured with his responses. In fact, he launched directly into the air and flew a brief circuit over the hills to demonstrate his form to me, and it was really something!

'But when he returned to earth, he told me he saw something troubling: a cluster of brightly-coloured tents and canopies clustered in the Brown Lands. Enemies are massing along the river, and they will surely attack the men of Stangard! We have to warn them.''${PLAYER}! I have had a lovely conversation with Landroval and Meneldor, but I have learned something most troubling, and it has brought our chat to an end!

'They are quite delightful fellows, if you ask this hobbit, and their patience with my questions was really quite extraordinary. I asked them some details concerning what it must be like to fly, and they were very good-natured with their responses. In fact, Landroval launched directly into the air and flew a brief circuit over the hills to demonstrate his form to me, and it was really something!

'But when he returned to earth, he told me he saw something troubling: a cluster of brightly-coloured tents and canopies clustered in the Brown Lands. Enemies are massing along the river, and they will surely attack the men of Stangard! We have to warn them.''A great army is encamped in the Brown Lands!''You again? Was I not clear enough the first time?'

Sabert listens impatiently as you tell him what Landroval saw from high above: an army of foes gathering in the Brown Lands.

'Eagles? Skin-changing bear-folk? Nosey halflings, far from home? You keep odd company, ${PLAYER}, and there is no need for you to bring them here. The men of Stangard will face whatever foe tomorrow brings. Good day to you, and may it bring you and your peculiar friends elsewhere!''The men of Stangard do not fear anything or anyone.''This is terrible, ${PLAYER}! He doesn't believe us! Beornings and Eagles give the warning, and Rohirrim ignore it!

'The enemies are massing on their doorstep, ${PLAYER}. We will have to do something about this... ourselves!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Enter the Easterlings' (Recommended Level: 75)</rgb>Orcs serving the White Hand are clear-cutting the forest and shipping the wood off to an unknown location.The clear-cut forest can be found at Ak-ghru.

Elfrith asked you to investigate the clear-cut part of the forest to determine how much wood the Orcs have gathered.Scout Ak-ghruElfrith is hiding beyond the bounds of Ak-ghru.

You should report to Elfrith that the Orcs have cut a large amount of wood, probably for use in building siege-engines.Talk to Elfrith'${PLAYER}, while I have no care for the Dunlendings and their forest, I do wonder how much wood these Orcs have already cut... this may help decipher for what the wood will be used. A relatively small amount may indicate something as simple as fire-wood or spears. A large amount, on the other hand may indicate the construction of siege-weapons.

'If you wish to help me, go to their encampment, Ak-ghru, and investigate the clear-cut wood. Perhaps you will be able to determine exactly how much wood the Orcs have taken and how much more it appears they are determined to take.''I think you are right, ${PLAYER}. I wager that the Orcs are indeed preparing for war... this is more dire than I thought.'While venturing through Ost Celebrant, Doron has noticed grim standards flying among the ruins. Doron wishes for you to recover symbols of the brigands' allegiance so that he and your Rohirrim allies may better understand the foe that faces them.Brigands are camped throughout Ost Celebrant.Collect sigils from brigands in Ost Celebrant (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Doron is within Ost Celebrant. If he has left your side, he can be summoned with your horn.Talk to Doron'${PLAYER}, halt! Do you see the banners that adorn these ruins? These men...they have been turned from tomb-robbers into an army. Could the Easterling be behind this?

'We must bring the fight to these brigands before they are too many to stop! See if they carry any symbol of their true allegiance; I am certain your allies will want to know of this!''These men are vicious -- I saw the fury in their gaze as we battled. The symbols they hold are worn and hastily made, but inspire dread nonetheless. Keep those symbols among your belongings for now...you shall deliver them to your allies once we finish here.'Idmar wants you to track down and confront the leader of the shades. He has given you a token of his people, the descendants of Eorl, in hopes that the shade will recognize it. He has surmised that the leader must be stationed among the vast number of spirits at the camp to the west.The Oathbreaker captain lurks among his men atop the hill to the west.

Idmar has asked you to find the captain of the shades.Find a clue to the shade-captain's whereaboutsThe Oathbreaker captain's men have sprung forth to guard him. They must be defeated if you are to continue your charge.Defeat the shade-captain's defenders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A peculiar skull is impaled on a nearby tree...perhaps this is the key to drawing the Oathbreaker captain forth.Examine the skullThe Oathbreaker captain is atop the hill to the west of Idmar's camp. You should attempt to speak to him now that he has revealed himself.Talk to the shade-captain'I think I have a plan, ${PLAYER}. You have been of great aid thus far, and you should be the one to take up this charge.

'They must have a leader, nestled deep within their forces. Judging by the size of the force, I would guess that he lurks among the spirits of his men to the west. 

'Here, take this, a symbol of my people. Hopefully, he can recall the battle and remember that the horsemen of the North once saved his people from certain defeat. Find out what he knows of the curse and why his men have returned if you can. I can only hope he has more to say than the others.''Deal with the Oathbreakers' captain, ${PLAYER}.''Deal with the Oathbreakers' captain, ${PLAYER}.''Deal with the Oathbreakers' captain, ${PLAYER}.''Deal with the Oathbreakers' captain, ${PLAYER}.''Why have you come, outsider? Do you too seek to pilfer the lost riches of the field or are you just here to revel in my anguish?

'No matter, any conflict between you and me is without cause. If you strike me down, I shall always return until I atone for my actions. If I strike you down, your journey ends. Nothing is accomplished for either of us should this turn to violence.

'Know this...I seek redemption, for it was my actions that brought this terrible curse upon us...and my actions that betrayed my lord, Cirion, in his time of need.

'I see that sigil you hold, and I know the men who have sent you. You may learn of my curse in time, but first, there are enemies among us that need to be dealt with.'Doron has relayed the tale of how he and his men came to be cursed. He now wishes for you to meet with one of his men, who has become aware of more sinister dealings in Parth Celebrant.Cabed is near Ost Celebrant, on a small hill off the side of the road south.

Doron has sent you to find the lost messenger, Cabed.Talk to Cabed'One of those that fell to the curse was not of my company...he merely sought shelter with us after faltering in his task. Cabed is his name, a messenger of Cirion sent to find aid from the North-men. However, seeing his fellows fall and sensing the futility of his charge, he fled instead to the south...to Ost Celebrant.

'The curse compounded with his guilt has driven him away from us. I do not know whether he truly seeks redemption or merely escape.

'Seek him out near Ost Celebrant. I fear that there are things occurring in that ruin that have fallen beneath notice. Perhaps he can be of help to us...I only hope he has not fallen to madness like the others.''Why would you seek an audience with me? I am a failure, a traitor to the great kingdom of Gondor.

'Doron sent you? Curse that man. He deserves only the worst of fates for what he did to so many of us. 

'The shadow that has fallen on Ost Celebrant has fallen beneath the notice of the Horse-lords and Doron alike. I have seen what lurks within these walls, and Doron has been given a chance to redeem us all...and it must be Doron, for I have no desire to atone for the folly of another.

'Listen to me, and I will guide you to the answer.''Seek the messenger Cabed...he may be able to reveal more to you.'Brifard has finished his task to gather reeds with your help. The arrogance of the man is nearly overwhelming, and it would be a relief to be gone from him.Idmar and his scouts are along the road to the south-east.

Brifard requests that you head south-east to meet his captain, Idmar, who has travelled with his men to deal with a mysterious task.Find Idmar and his menYou have come across a fallen Rohirrim. You should examine him and determine what fate befell him.Examine the fallen soldierUncertain what remains of the scouting party Brifard mentioned, you should continue south-east along the road and search for Idmar or any other Rohirrim.Search the road for Idmar and his men'Now that you have the reeds, my work here is done. My captain, Idmar, and his men were patrolling along this road. They told me they were keeping watch on the brigands to the south-east, but would not tell me more of their charge. I wonder if there is more afoot than they were willing to speak?

'As for myself, I must attend to other matters. I should be with Idmar, bringing the fight to those brigands, but once again, I am left with the most uninteresting tasks.

'Bring these reeds south-east to Idmar... I am certain someone will return them to Stangard. For now, farewell.''Go find Idmar and his men.''Greetings, stranger. I am Idmar, captain of the watchers of Parth Celebrant. What brings you here?'

Idmar accepts the reeds and puts them aside, then looks suddenly stone-faced as you relay your tale.

'Dead? At the hands of a spirit? This bodes poorly for us. You see, my men and I have been investigating a matter which we wish to keep as much a secret as possible.

'Here, take your wage for providing us these reeds. Brifard will be disciplined for shirking his duties... again. Allow me a moment, and I shall tell you more.'Ardwyn has learned that the Rohirrim patrol which encountered the Dunlendings had ranged further north than usual, perhaps inciting the Dunlendings to attack.The patrol path runs through the valley west of Forthbrond.

Ardwyn has asked you to patrol several points for signs of the Dunlendings.Patrol the first rally pointPatrol the second rally pointPatrol the third rally pointArdwyn is at Forthbrond, east of the valley.

You should report what you have seen to Ardwyn.Talk to Ardwyn at Forthbrond'After speaking with the leader of our patrol, I learned that they ranged further south than usual... it is possible that the Dunlendings attacked because we had encroached openly upon their land, though I have my doubts.

'Perhaps you would patrol the valley to the west for me. I have the feeling that there is more to this attack than we understand.''The reports have been unclear regarding what has been happening in Brôntrig. It seems that the Dunlendings are intentionally striking at our patrols, then fading into the wilderness.

'Alas, you have not shed much more light upon the situation than my patrols.'The Rohirrim forces prepare to launch a pre-emptive strike against the village of Brôntrig in hopes of confounding the Dunlendings' own attack plans.Answith is encamped near the tower west of Brôntrig.

You should speak with Answith when you are ready to depart for Brôntrig.Talk to AnswithArdwyn is at Forthbrond, north of Brôntrig.

You should return to Ardwyn and speak with him regarding the defeat of the Rohirrim at Brôntrig.Talk to Ardwyn at Forthbrond'It is time, ${PLAYER}. We know that the Dunlendings at Brôntrig intend to attack us here at Forthbrond. Instead, we will take the battle to their own doorstep.

'Your task will be to create a diversion while our forces position themselves to take the Dunlendings by surprise.

'Speak with me when you are ready to depart.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'${PLAYER}, the routing of the Rohirrim forces at Brôntrig is a grim reminder of the resourcefulness of our enemies. I fear that this may shake the morale of our warriors.''We will enter the village in the dead of night and create several distractions, which will allow our men to push along the southern road into Brôntrig and take the Dunlendings by surprise.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Going through Lanferth's personal effects, you have discovered a grim trinket depicting an eye wreathed in flame.Idmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant.

You should bring the symbol you found to Idmar.Talk to IdmarDoron is among his men on the crest of the hill in western Parth Celebrant.

Idmar suggests that Doron might know something about the symbol you found.Talk to DoronIn your hand, you hold a scratched symbol of the Eye, wreathed in blue and red flames. As you look over the trinket, you note that it appears much less worn than the other treasures the brigands have amassed.

Perhaps it would be best to return this to Idmar.'What is this that you bring me?

'I do not know where Lanferth would have come across such an object. It fills me with dread. It seems far too recently made, even with its wear.

'I have a thought, ${PLAYER}. Take this to Doron and see if he knows what it is or where it could have come from. I fear that some greater forces are at play on the field....''So you return...what is this you have brought me? This symbol...I have seen its make before. The Eye I do not recognize, but these markings along the edge remind me of trinkets once carried by those that brought war to our land.

'Aye, it must be them. Why would such a symbol be in the hands of these men? And why would it look so far beyond my time?

'${PLAYER}, you were wise to have brought this to me. You have proven your worth and your trust. It is time that honour was returned unto you.'Cabed has sent you to investigate the outskirts of Ost Celebrant near the Rushgore where he believes that an unknown force passed through before entering the ruin.Cabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.Find the wanderer's trail outside Ost CelebrantCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.Examine the boot-printCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.Follow the trail of boot-printsCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.Follow the trail of boot-printsCabed has sent you to track down a mysterious invader's trail. The trail ends at the bridge to Ost Celebrant, but Cabed is unsure where it begins.Follow the trail of boot-printsYou should examine the glint you saw in the distance.Examine the glint in the distanceCabed is atop a small hill along the southern road in Parth Celebrant.

You should bring the twisted blade to Cabed.Talk to Cabed'In my time, I have seen many arrive and depart the Field of Celebrant, but there is one who has not yet left.

'He crept into the Field among the fog of the Rushgore and hid within the ruins of Ost Celebrant. I know not who this man is, nor what his purpose in Ost Celebrant can be. However, I fear that no good can come of his presence here.

'Search the outside of Ost Celebrant near the Rushgore, perhaps this wanderer left some clue to his origin.''What is this?

'I know this blade...and others like it. This is the blade of an Easterling. I had my suspicions of who the stranger could be, but I wished to believe it untrue.

'These men do not belong on the field and such audacity cannot go unanswered, you must show this to your allies and Doron when the time comes.''Did you find something?''You should follow the tracks of the Easterling....''You should follow the tracks of the Easterling....''You should follow the tracks of the Easterling....''You should follow the tracks of the Easterling....''You should follow the tracks of the Easterling....'Stanric is troubled by a late delivery from one of his men, Brifard, in Parth Celebrant. He wishes for you to seek out Brifard and discover why he is running so late.Brifard is stationed at a camp in northern Parth Celebrant near south-east Thinglad.

Stanric has asked you to attend to one of his men, Brifard.Talk to Brifard'Do you have a moment, ${PLAYER}? In all of our recent turmoil, there is something that completely escaped my memory. To the east lies Parth Celebrant, and more importantly, one of my men, Brifard.

'I sent him out with a peasant to gather reeds for Stangard, but he has yet to return. Brifard means well, but sometimes he fails to see the importance of small tasks.

'It would mean a great deal to me if you would track him down. He should be at a small camp in northern Parth Celebrant, just outside Thinglad. You have my thanks.''Of course, Stanric would send someone. Come then, let us speak.'Garrun told you of a pack of Wargs holed up in some warrens east of his encampment.The Warg-warren lies to the east from Garrun's camp.

Garrun asked you to drive the Wargs from their warren in the Isendale.Defeat Wargs at their warren (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Garrun's camp is west of the Warg-warren.

You should return to Garrun with news of your success.Talk to Garrun in the Isendale'Among the crags to the east, a pack of Wargs have holed up in some warrens. From there, they hunt our patrols and harry our forces.

'I believe we should root out the Wargs and drive them from this place. It would make our movements easier and less noticed by the enemy, I think.

'The warren lies to the east, not far from the northern pass into the Gravenwood.''With the Warg-threat reduced, our patrols can scout more effectively and secretly.''Have you hunted down the Wargs yet?'A Rohirrim messenger disappeared when travelling to bring word to Forthbrond.The missing messenger might be found somewhere to the north and west of Forthbrond.

Ardwyn has asked you to find Cadforn, a messenger who is late returning to Forthbrond.Find CadthornArdwyn is at Forthbrond, to the south and east of Cadthorn's position.

You should return to Ardwyn with Cadthorn's message.Deliver Cadthorn's message to Ardwyn at Forthbrond'Recently, Cadthorn, one of our messengers,  failed to report back. He is a capable courier that had gone to receive word from Edoras regarding our strategic goals for Forthbrond.  

'Will you set forth and discover Cadthorn's location?

'Begin your search to the north and slightly west from here along the cliff walls. Surely, he has set forth from Edoras already.''The messages that Cadthorn bore were of import, but this edict from Edoras was the word that we sought. It shall be known among the captains.

'Thank you for bringing us this news.''I was unexpectedly attacked by Orcs and their ilk. They ambushed my party and stole a satchel that bore important messages for Forthbrond. Many of my companions fell, and I barely escaped with my life.

'I was given word to bring to Grimbold and his captains: Théoden King has commanded that Isengard is to be called friend, and any reports to the contrary should come only from his son, Théodred.''Look for Cadthorn, ${PLAYER}, north and west of Forthbrond.''You should return to Ardwyn, ${PLAYER}.'After searching the ruins of Ost Celebrant for signs of the Easterling invader, you have discovered a passageway under the fortress. Doron believes that this is where the Easterling has sought shelter.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>Doron has brought you to the ruins of Ost Celebrant in search of the Easterling invader.

Doron believes that the Easterling lurks somewhere in the tunnels below Ost Celebrant.Talk to DoronDoron can be summoned to your side by using your horn.Talk to Doron'This does not bode well, ${PLAYER}. We have scoured this fortress and the Easterling's whereabouts are still a mystery.

'I know of a passage that leads down into the heart of Ost Celebrant, but I thought it crumbled with the passing of the years. If the tunnels still remain, the Easterling must surely be lurking under these ruins.

'I can show you the way, but you must be ready for the danger we face. Gather your wits and make strong your resolve, we must depart now or risk losing all.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>'The day is ours, ${PLAYER}.

'I was not certain what we would face in those ruins, but it eases me to know that Ost Celebrant is once again in the hands of my people and our allies.

'Your journey is far from over, but delight in this moment of peace.''We must end this threat before it spreads further out of the East. Are you ready to depart?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>Brifard is worried that the wolves have acquired a taste for Man-flesh.Brifard has advised you to hunt down wolves in the nearby wolf-den to the north-east. This particular wolf-den has been nicknamed 'The Murderous Pit' by the Rohirrim of Stangard.

Brifard wants you to cull the wolf-pack in response to their violence.Defeat wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Brifard is located at the camp-site to the south-east of Thinglad.

You should return to Brifard with news of your success.Talk to Brifard'I know not why these wolves have taken to preying on our men, but it must be stopped. Everyone must be kept safe, and more importantly, I cannot return to Stangard with more blood on my hands.

'Their den is to the east along the shore of the Great River. May fortune be with you... I desire not to explain another loss.''Good, you made it back alive. Not that I doubted your resolve, but the Pit has claimed many a creature.

'Now that the way is cleared, I have another task for you.'Brifard told you how Stangard is in dire need of repair and that the reeds along the river are quite helpful for patching.Reeds can be found along the shore of the Great River to the north-east of Brifard's camp.

Brifard wants you to gather the reeds that his peasant failed to deliver. He wishes you to return to the wolf-den one last time.Gather reeds from the river's edge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Brifard can be found at the camp on the path out of southeastern Thinglad.

You should bring the reeds you gathered to Brifard at once.Talk to Brifard'The tidings you bring me are gravely concerning. We must send word of these discoveries to Idmar and the watchers along the road to the south, but first, would you be willing to finish the task my unfortunate servant and I started? 

'Stangard needs repairs constantly, and the reeds from the river's edge are very helpful to us. Please gather some, then return to me.''I need you to bring me those reeds, ${PLAYER}.''Good, good. I am glad that you again made it past the wolves with little difficulty. If we had more servants like you, ${CLASS}, I would not find myself in such situations....

'Perhaps such a sentiment is callous, but I do not seek your approval. Come, let me bundle those reeds. It is time you brought these to Idmar. 

'Are you ready to depart?'Cabed wants you to help him not only deliver a message, but also discover the identity of the threat that has taken hold in Ost Celebrant.Cabed has sent you to complete two tasks before he reveals what he knows about a hidden threat in Parth Celebrant. Cabed is located along the southern road of Parth Celebrant.Complete 'The Lost Message'Complete 'A Threat Unseen'Cabed is located along the southern road of Parth Celebrant.

You should return to Cabed with news of your success.Talk to Cabed'I know what Doron told you, ${PLAYER}. However, there is much that you still do not know.

'Something terrible has come to Ost Celebrant, and while I am not sure exactly what it is, I know it can only bring more destruction to this field.

'There are two tasks I have for you. If you will honour me with your service, I will guide you to the knowledge you seek.''Very good then...it is done. You honour me with your aid, and for that, I will serve you in turn.''Complete my tasks, I shall speak more with you.'Medwine wants you to deal a final blow against the brigands of Parth Celebrant.The brigand-camp is to the south of Idmar's camp along the banks of the Limlight River.

Medwine has asked you to burn down the brigand-camp.Burn the guard-tentBurn the pile of firewoodBurn food-storesBurn Lanferth's tentMedwine is at Idmar's camp in central Parth Celebrant.

You should return to Medwine wih news of your success.Talk to Medwine'I have one last task for you, ${PLAYER}.

'Even with the assault we have levied against these Men, they remain entrenched, and we cannot drive them out completely.

'Perhaps if their torches were used against them, we would be able to run them off our land for good. Travel south to their camp and burn them out.''It is done? Excellent. With so much of their camp burned to the ground, it should be very difficult for them to recover. You have done my people a great service this day.''If you burn the brigands' camp to the ground, they will have no recourse but to find new shelter.'The cave-openings scattered throughout the southern section of the Isendale provide the Orcs passage onto the landscape.The cave-openings can be found along the hills east of Innoth's encampment.

Innoth has asked you to collapse the cave-openings from whence the Orcs have been issuing.Collapse cave-openings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Innoth is at his camp near the Isen, west of the caves.

You should return to Innoth with news of your success.Talk to Innoth near the Isen'Orcs have begun to emerge from several cave-openings that lie at the base of hills along the southern ridgeline of the Isendale. This is surely how they are bringing aid to the Dunlendings.

'If you would, travel back up the switchback and find these caves. Collapse the entrances and deny the Orcs passage onto the landscape.''Ah, I am relieved by your tidings, ${PLAYER}. With the caves sealed, the Orcs should pose little threat to us.''You need to collapse those tunnel entrances, ${PLAYER}!'Answith reports that many prisoners were taken by the Dunlendings and are being held in Brôntrig.Prison-cages may be found within Brôntrig, east of the tower where Answith is hiding.

Answith has asked you to enter Brôntrig and free any prisoners you find there.Open cages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Answith is encamped at the tower, west of Brôntrig.

You should return to Answith with news of your success.Talk to Answith in the Isendale'While I was scouting Brôntrig, I noticed that many captives were dragged into the village and put in cages. Unfortunately, there was naught that I could do for them.

'Will you enter Brôntrig and try to free the captives? This would be a terrible blow to the Dunlendings and a victory for Rohan.

'Brôntrig lies just to the east of here.''Those who were captured fled northward towards Forthbrond. On behalf of my people, I thank you.'You found a crude and unusually crafted spearhead among the belongings of the fallen Dunlendings.Garrun is at his camp, west of Cuvnerth.

You should bring the cruel barb to Garrun.Bring the cruel barb to Garrun in the IsendaleAmong the fallen Dunlendings, you found this spearhead. The similarity to this and those found in Brôntrig is disconcerting.

The origin of these cruel barbs may lead to the identity of those who are supplying the Dunlendings. You should bring the spearhead to Garrun.'In my many years of fighting, I have seen things such as these. This kind of weapon is far too cruel for any of the Dunlending peoples to forge. It resembles much more those wielded by Orcs and their kind.

'How the Dunlendings obtained these weapons is mystery... one which we must uncover.'An advance force from the Wulf's Cleft army has occupied the village of Cuvnerth.Cuvnerth lies to the south-east of Garrun's camp.

Garrun has asked you to enter Cuvnerth and drive the Dunlendings from the village.Defeat Dunlendings at Cuvnerth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Garrun is at his camp, north-west of Cuvnerth.

You should bring word to Garrun that the Dunlendings have been driven out of the village.Talk to Garrun in the Isendale'The town of Cuvnerth has become of strategic importance in our on-going attempt to hold back the impending invasion from Wulf's Cleft, ${PLAYER}. An advance force from the Cleft has occupied the village, but if we can drive them out, it might be that our own men can use it as a stronghold against the Cleft.

'Will you attempt this? Cuvnerth lies to the south-east of here and is well-garrisoned.''Alas, though you have driven a number of the enemy from Cuvnerth, they will soon regarrison the village. However, though it may seem like we are simply forestalling the inevitable, your actions will delay the Dunlending army from marching forth.''I need you to break the defences of the Dunlendings, ${PLAYER}!'The Rohirrim messenger Cadthorn and his companions were set upon by goblins as they were returning to Forthbrond with important messages from Edoras.The cave mouth where the goblins may be found lies to the north of Cadthorn's position, along the ridge.

Cadthorn has asked you to hunt down the goblins that attacked his party, drive them off, and recover his companions' stolen belongings.Defeat goblins in the Isendale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Rohirrim belongings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ardwyn is at Forthbrond, south and east of the goblin-cave.

Cadthorn asked you to bring the effects of the fallen Rohirrim to Ardwyn.'The goblins responsible for the attack on my party were a vicious lot, butchering my slain companions beyond recognition. Besides stealing the pouch we carried our messages in, the foul creatures scavenged goods from my companions' corpses, as well.

'Will you seek out the goblins and drive them from this place... and recover my companions' belongings?

'They have encamped at the mouth of a cave to the north, along the ridge. When you have recovered my companions' belongings, you should bring them to Ardwyn at Forthbrond.''Thank you for returning the belongings of our fallen kinsmen. We are in your debt for your help.

'It is strange that the goblins are so bold as to attack our patrols and scouts. They shall pay for it with their blood... I promise that.'Brifard is concerned that the servant he was escorting has not returned yet.Brifard mentioned that the servant was gathering reeds along the shore of the Great River to the north-east.

Brifard wants you to investigate the river's edge and find out what is taking the servant so long.Search for the missing Rohirrim servantBrifard is at his camp to the north-east.

Having found the remains of the servant, you should return to Brifard.Talk to Brifard'Ho, there! Have we met before? Your face is familiar... perhaps I have seen you in Stangard. No matter. Am I to assume you have been sent to find out what is taking us so long?

'You see, several of our servants have gone missing over the past few weeks while gathering reeds for Stangard. None have returned. I was sent myself to watch over a peasant today... to make sure we do not have any more problems.

'The man I escorted is taking longer than expected... I had to return here to attend to some personal matters after bringing him to the river's shore. Go search for him. He had better have a good reason for working so slowly.''Have you found my servant yet?''Dead at the maws of wolves? They have never been this hostile towards our men. You have my thanks for finding him, despite the circumstances. I will send word to Stangard explaining the situation.

'I suppose I will need to keep a closer watch on these peasants from now on....'Word has arrived from Garrun that Rohirrim scouts have discovered that the caverns beneath the Isendale are much more extensive than previously thought.Ardwyn is at Forthbrond, far to the north of Innoth's camp.

Innoth instructed you to bring news of the Orc-caverns to Ardwyn.Talk to Ardwyn at Forthbrond'Word has recently arrived from Garrun that our scouts have discovered that the caverns beneath the Isendale are much more extensive than previously thought. They run west beneath Dol Baran and north to Nan Curunír. Hopefully, Saruman will deal with the beasts, but in the event they prove too overwhelming, our people must be warned.

'Bring word to Ardwyn at Forthbrond, ${PLAYER}. He will know what to do.''These words are among the most terrifying you could bring to me, ${PLAYER}. We must warn Grimbold at the Ford of Isen and send word to Théodred at once!''Speak with Ardwyn at once, ${PLAYER}!'Doron has commanded you to cast the treasures which once cursed his men into the Limlight River, directly to the south of Ost Celebrant. These treasures are strewn about the southern part of Ost Celebrant.The treasures are strewn about the southern side of Ost Celebrant on the shore near the Limlight River.Throw cursed treasures into the Limlight (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Doron is at your side in Ost Celebrant. If he has wandered from your sight, he can be summoned with your horn.Talk to Doron'These ruins hold many memories for me, ${PLAYER}. As you have been shown, the bribe my men and I accepted in return for standing down in the face of the Easterlings was once held in these ruins.

'I see treasures of significant age strewn about the ruins here. Much of it seems familiar to me...I think it is the very same!

'Please, cast the treasures into the Limlight just south of Ost Celebrant. Let us be rid of them forever. Please do this for me, as my arms no longer grant me strength in this world.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I know that this alone is not enough to release us from our curse, but destroying the bribe that brought us to ruin is a relief.'Several Warg pack-leaders and goblin Warg-riders patrol beyond the Warg-warrens.Warg pack-leaders and goblin Warg-riders can be found near the Warg-warrens, east of Garrun's camp.

Garrun asked you to defeat the pack-leaders and Warg-riders among the Warg-warrens.Defeat Warg-riders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat pack-leaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Garrun is at his camp, west of the Warg-warrens.

You should return to Garrun with tidings of your success.Talk to Garrun in the Isendale'Several Warg pack-leaders and goblin Warg-riders have been sighted among the Warg-warrens east of here. These creatures clearly guide the actions of the Wargs and must be dealt with... I find it strange that the Dunlendings tolerate the vile creatures.

'The Warg-warrens lie to the east of here, and the pack-leaders and Warg-riders can be found near there. Go forth and slay the vile beasts... for Théodred and Théoden King!''Wargs are a fearsome foe!''With their leadership dispatched, perhaps the rest of the pack will disperse and return from whence they came.'Medwine has been tasked with trapping the brigands on the Field of Celebrant, so that the Rohirrim can mount an attack.The brigands' horses are located inside of Hordfierd, the large camp in south-west Parth Celebrant.

Medwine has asked you to frighten the horses of the brigands.Frighten brigand horses at Hordfierd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Medwine is at Idmar's camp in central Parth Celebrant.

You should return to Medwine with news of your success.Talk to Medwine'If you have a moment, I would like a word with you, ${PLAYER}. For my part, I have seen several brigands travelling by horse between the Rushgore and Parth Celebrant.

'We cannot allow them to rally with any other forces they have outside of the Field. Return to their camp to the south-west and frighten their horses. With enough luck, we will trap them on the field and have little trouble rounding up the stragglers.''The horses are driven off? Good. I will send word to Stangard to see if we cannot track a few down...our stables have been very busy lately.

'I am certain the brigands are realizing their folly by now.''If you frighten away the brigands' horses, they will be put at a disadvantage.'Orcs have begun to appear along the southern ridge overlooking the Isendale.Orcs can be found near the bases of many of the hills east of Innoth's camp.
  
Innoth has asked you to find the Orcs in the Isendale and drive them back into their caves.Defeat Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Innoth is at his camp near the Isen.

You should inform Innoth that the Orcs have been driven back into their caves.Talk to Innoth near the Isen'${PLAYER}, Orcs have begun to venture forth from several caverns within the valleys of the Isendale. They present a great threat to my people and must be driven back into their holes.

'They have been seen near rocky outcroppings around the bases of several of the hills to the east. You can reach the hills by travelling up the switchback to the north.

'Will you deal with these Orcs for me?''I fear that the Orcs might be traversing beneath the Isendale a long way to aid the Dunlendings. These are dark tidings, indeed, for it means that the Dunlendings have an ally who is determined to see them victorious.''${PLAYER}, there are still many Orcs threatening my position!'Several weapon caches have been identified throughout the Isendale.The crates of supplies can be found on the hill east of Innoth's camp.

Innoth asked you to collect several of the Orkish weapon-caches.Collect supply-crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Innoth is at his camp, west of the weapons-caches.

You should bring the supplies you recovered to Innoth.Talk to Innoth near the Isen'The Orcs have been leaving caches of weapons for the Dunlendings within the Isendale. I am not sure the Dunlendings actually know who is supplying them, since the Orcs deposit the supplies, then leave before the Dunlendings arrive.

'It is safe to assume, I think, that the Orcs want us fighting each other. In order to disrupt their plans, we need to recover the supplies the Orcs leave for the Dunlendings.

'With the supplies lost, the Dunlending force will be greatly weakened. The supplies can be found atop the hill to the east.''I will see that these weapons are disposed of, ${PLAYER}. No civilized man would dare to use such cruel weapons.''Have you collected the Orcs' weapon caches?'The supplies that were being ferried beneath the Isendale to Cuvnerth are now being brought to several outposts, including Brôntrig. Stop any Dunlendings from ferrying supplies.The Dunlending transporting the supplies can be found along the hill east of Innoth's camp, reached by travelling the switchback to the north.

Innoth has asked you to stop the Dunlendings from delivering their Orc-provided supplies to their various outposts.Collect supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Innoth is at his camp, to the west and south of the Dunlending supply-line.

You should return to Innoth with the supplies that you recovered from the Dunlendings.Talk to Innoth near the Isen'${PLAYER}, the supplies once being ferried beneath the Isendale to Wulf's Cleft are now being delivered to many Dunlending outposts, including Brôntrig.

'The Dunlendings hauling these supplies have been spotted along the hill to the east of here. If you would, follow the switchback to the north and look for the Dunlendings... they must be stopped!''Bring me those ill-gotten good, ${PLAYER}!''These supplies will be sent to Forthbrond, where they will benefit our men.'With Doron's guidance, you have discovered a passageway under Ost Celebrant. Doron bids you to enter and confront the Easterling invader.Doron hopes to find the Easterling invader among the crumbling tunnels of Ost Celebrant. Explore the ruins and try to uncover his whereabouts.Explore the ruins under Ost CelebrantYou have uncovered a room decorated with strange banners and trinkets that fill you with dread. While you do not see the Easterling, you believe him to be nearby.Search the ruins for the EasterlingThe Easterling, Maraz, has revealed that he drove the brigands into serving his brotherhood, and that he and his people seek to crush Rohan beginning with Parth Celebrant. He must be defeated before his plans can come to fruition.Defeat MarazDoron can be called to your side with the horn you carry.Talk to Doron'The Easterling is vanquished and our search is at an end, but this man brings grim tidings for the days to come. If his people are truly as strong as he claims, the Horse-lords have much to fear. 

'Come, let us depart. You must bring word to your allies immediately.''The day is ours. Let us leave this foul place.'You have entered the caverns beneath Cuvnerth in an effort to discover the benefactor of the Dunlendings at Cuvnerth.Discover the source of the Dunlending supplies.Discover the source of the Dunlending suppliesSeek out the first store of supplies.Find the first store of suppliesDestroy the first store of suppliesSeek out the second store of supplies.Search across the bridge for suppliesDestroy the second store of suppliesSeek out the third store of supplies.Find the third store of suppliesDestroy the third store of suppliesHead to the cave entrance to make your escape.Return to the entrance of the cavernUpon entering the caverns beneath Cuvnerth, you discovered Orcs infesting the cave.Discover the source of the Dunlending supplies.Discover the source of the Dunlending suppliesDefeat the Orcs that inhabit the cavern beneath Cuvnerth.Defeat Orcs in the cavern (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Upon entering the caverns beneath Cuvnerth, you discovered Orcs infesting the cave.Discover the source of the Dunlending supplies.Discover the source of the Dunlending suppliesDefeat the three captains that watch over the supply stores.Defeat supply-captains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have journeyed with Answith to Brôntrig to distract the Dunlendings from the southern road and the advancing Rohirrim force.Seek out and destroy supply stores in Brôntrig to distract the Dunlendings from noticing the Rohirrim advance.Destroy supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn huts to further distract the Dunlendings.Burn Dunlending huts in Brôntrig (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})All is lost. It is time to flee Brôntrig.Flee Brôntrig'This day is lost, ${PLAYER}! It is time to leave.'Doron, leader of the Oathbreakers in Parth Celebrant, has decided to tell you how he and his men came to be cursed. As he speaks, you find yourself drawn into a daydream, experiencing the tale alongside Doron and his men.Doron is stationed outside of Ost Celebrant, after having patrolled the road down to the Limlight with his men.Talk to DoronDoron is stationed outside of Ost Celebrant. You should follow him as he tells his tale.Having survived an Easterling assault, Doron is entering Ost Celebrant, where he hopes to reunite with the rest of his men.Follow Doron into Ost CelebrantDoron is inside Ost Celebrant with his men. You should listen as he continues his tale.Follow Doron into Ost CelebrantHaving heard the roar of an approaching force, Doron and his men have decided to cross the bridge of Ost Celebrant and confront the invaders.Follow Doron outside Ost CelebrantDoron is standing on the edge of the bridge into Ost Celebrant.Talk to Doron'In times long past, my men and I were stationed in Ost Celebrant, a gorgeous Gondorian fortress that overlooked the Limlight river. 

'We were under siege by a terrible force of Easterlings for some time before this, and eventually they claimed Calenardhon -- the land which became Rohan. They drove us north, into these fields, and it was here that we prepared to make our final stand.

'My men and I guarded the Limlight, hoping to keep their forces from the south at bay, while our leader, Cirion and his force secured the rest of the field.

'The night we were cursed began as I was patrolling back from the Limlight with my men....''The wrong choice was made, but how could I have known? Some of my men were overjoyed by our tainted riches, while others condemned my actions.

'Cirion never forgave us...the oath we made to protect Gondor was broken by my actions, and all suffered for it.''Let us leave this memory, there is more to be said.'Doron and his men have discovered brigands to the south that have pillaged the nearby ruins at Ost Celebrant.Idmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant.

Doron bade you return to Idmar.Talk to Idmar'The fate that befell me and my men is more frightful than any the living can imagine. The decision I made that day long past will haunt me for however long I remain in this realm.

'I can no longer control my men...that much is clear to me. Our once strong force is broken, most of them driven mad by the passing of the years, while others still foolishly revel in the riches that cursed us.

'To the south, brutish men have gathered and seek to pilfer the relics of this land. It disgusts me that they have remained mostly beneath the notice of your allies. Return to whoever sent you here and alert them of their foolishness.'Idmar listens as you tell the tale of Doron and his cursed forces.

'So, he is aware of the brigands to the south? Interesting. We know of them, but our attempts to root them out have been fruitless as of yet. Perhaps it is time for us to take action against them.

'Thank you for bringing this to my attention. I am sure that this is not the last of our dealings with Doron and his men.'The brigands are led by a man named Lanferth, and Idmar believes eliminating him may put an end to their invasion.Lanferth's tent is located deep within Hordfierd.

Idmar has asked you to defeat Lanferth, leader of the brigands.Find and defeat LanferthIdmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant.

You should return to Idmar at once with news of your victory.Talk to Idmar'${PLAYER}, you have aided us well. Only one task remains...we must break their leadership. My men have heard talk of a brutal man named Lanferth, who dwells deep within Hordfierd. He leads the brigands on raids into Ost Celebrant and is notorious for making certain that he gets his cut of the loot by any means necessary.

'We have heard whispers from his men recently that he has become very queer and often will no longer personally venture into Ost Celebrant. We have no idea why.

'Journey to Hordfierd and defeat him. Without his leadership, the brigands will not find riches in Parth Celebrant. Go, and if he has anything of value, return it to us.''Lanferth is no more? Good. These brigands should be thrust into chaos without his leadership, as vicious as it was.

'Did you find anything of value among his keepings?''Defeat Lanferth, ${PLAYER}, then perhaps the rest of his men will depart this land.'You have retrieved a set of orders detailing an impending attack on Forthdbrond from Brôntrig.Ardwyn is at Forthbrond, north of Brôntrig.

You should bring the orders you found to Ardwyn without delay.Bring the orders to Ardwyn at ForthbrondThis set of orders details an impending attack on Forthbrond being launched from Brôntrig.

'Brothers, we shall push forth the forgoil from our lands, once and for all. We will rally our forces with those of our kindred throughout Dunland, so that we might crush the Horse-lords.'

You should bring these orders to Ardwyn without delay.'This note speaks of an impending attack... we will need you to strike at the Dunlendings before they can gather their strength.'Despite your efforts to disrupt the stockpiles at Cuvnerth, a new store of supplies has appeared at the village.Garrun is at his camp, west of Cuvnerth.

You should speak with Garrun when you are ready to enter Cuvnerth.Talk to Garrun to journey into the cavern below CuvnerthGarrun is at his encampment, west of Cuvnerth.

You should speak with Garrun regarding your discoveries in the cavern.Talk to Garrun in the Isendale'${PLAYER}, it does not seem possible, but I am not blind and have seen it with my own eyes: already a new store of supplies has been deposited at Cuvnerth.

'The Dunlendings have not had time to secure more supplies... they must have a benefactor with great resources, and we must discover who that benefactor is.

'Let me know when you are ready to travel once more to Cuvnerth. There are caverns below the village through which the supplies were probably brought.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready to enter the caverns below Cuvnerth? We must discover the source of the Dunlendings' supplies.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'These tidings trouble me, ${PLAYER}. I do not understand why the Orcs are supplying the Dunlendings... they are as much enemies as the Rohirrim and the Orcs.

'Even if these Orcs are rogues serving no one, this is a troubling alliance.'You found a hastily scribbled note, ordering the goblins to watch for a Rohirrim messenger.Ardwyn is at Forthbrond, south and east of Cadthorn's position.

You should bring the note you recovered to Ardwyn.Bring the note to Ardwyn at ForthbrondThis hastily scribbled note details instructions for the goblins. 

