You should return to Edhere and let him know that you have found fresh water.Talk to Edhere in the Orc-mines'The water that the Orcs bring us comes from the dank pools that gather in the low areas of the mine. It is contaminated and poisonous, and those who drink it eventually fall ill, so we are left either to die slowly from the poison or more swiftly from thirst... an unpleasant choice of evils. Eventually, we just collapse from exhaustion or sickness, and the Orcs toss us into some pit to die.

'If you could find some source of fresh water in these caverns and get it to the exhausted miners, it would help restore their strength and purchase us some time to plan our escape.''What is this? Water? You have my thanks, stranger. My strength was at an end.''So, there is a fresh spring among the rocks at the northern end of the mine?

'We would have to find some way past those vile worms to get there, but at least now we know where it is.

'I can try and have one of my men sneak away now and again to get us some fresh water. It is a great risk, but worth the danger if we can keep ourselves alive in this terrible pit.'You have discovered the pick-axe of Ondor the dwarf, whom you aided earlier in his attempt to gain revenge on the Orcs who slew his father.Ondor the Dwarf might be within the Orc-cavern in the northern Heathfells.

You should find Ondor the Dwarf and return his pick-axe to him.Talk to Ondor in the Pit of IronA dwarf-made pick-axe lies here on the ground, dropped amid the signs of a struggle. At a second glance, you realize that this is the same pick wielded by Ondor the Dwarf while he strove to collapse a cave entrance with your aid.

Ondor must be somewhere nearby -- and the yawning cave entrance before you suggests darkly where the valiant but foolish dwarf is likely to be found....'Ah, ${PLAYER}! It is good to see you again. We seem to have found the main nest of these villains, we have. I've been scouting it out a bit.

'The Orcs here, they're mining... well, being Orcs, they're too lazy to mine, so they use slaves to do it for them. It seems they've been gathering slaves from among the Dunlendings for a long while, and more recently, they've captured some Rohirrim during their nightly raids.

'I guess they think they're pretty safe down here with all the fighting going on up above. That's where we will get them!'Intrigued by the mortal qualities of the avanc, Amal has gained a curiosity as to the value of avanc-hides.Avanc can be found throughout the Rushgore.

