You should return to Edhere and let him know that Golvorn's captives have been freed.Talk to Edhere in the Orc-mines'There is something strange here, ${PLAYER}. While you were gone, one of my men and a few of the Dunlendings were taken away... not by the Orcs, but by a Man.

'He wore strange raiments, marking him as a person of some station, but I do not know whom he served. He was looking for the strongest and healthiest of the men among us. For what purpose, I do not know.

'They were taken away to the north, and the Orcs laughed cruelly as they left. You must find out where they were taken... and what fate could possibly be worse than to die in this dark pit.''Interesting. It seems that my servants have not been thorough enough in securing the slaves of late.

'No matter, you have already saved me the trouble of sending them to hunt you down. But wait, you do not have the bearing of one who seeks escape. You have come to fight... me?

'Truly? Well then, I imagine you will make a fine specimen for Saruman's experiments. I shall have to take care not to injure you too severely!'The prisoner seems to slip in and out of a daze as you cut him free, but he quickly recovers his senses once the bonds are removed.'Good. I do not know whether they have escaped the cave or gone into hiding awaiting our own attempt, but either way we are now ready to make our escape.

