You should return to Captain Féarn with tidings of your victory.Talk to Captain Féarn atop Dol Baran'The Dunlendings have been attacking our positions for nearly three days... not in any great numbers, but in small bands, attacking and withdrawing, then sending fresh men into the fray.

'My own men are exhausted, and some have been caught away from our fortifications, suffering serious injuries. The Dunlendings have let them lie where they fell, hoping to draw us out.

'If you could find some way to rescue my fallen men, I would be indebted to you, for we are sorely put upon.''You came! I thought I would die out here.''You came! I thought I would die out here.''You came! I thought I would die out here.''You came! I thought I would die out here.''I saw you return with a number of our injured warriors to our lines. Your valour speaks well of you!'The Dunlendings assaulting Dol Baran have set the makeshift fortifications alight.Dunlendings are assaulting the barricades atop Dol Baran.

Captain Féarn has asked you to defeat the Dunlending warriors by the barricades atop Dol Baran.Douse burning fortifications (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Captain Féarn is atop Dol Baran.

You should inform Captain Féarn of your victory.Talk to Captain Féarn atop Dol Baran'The Dunlendings are testing our resolve to hold Dol Baran, but they underestimate us.

'We must hold this position, or we will be blind to the approach of their main force when it marches out of Wulf's Cleft. If that happens, Grimbold will have to pull us back across the ford without a fight.

'Aid my men by the fortifications and hold off the Dunlendings. If we can force them to give up on Dol Baran and march their army past us, we will have a critical advantage in the battle to come.''Well fought out there, but I fear these attacks are just a prelude to a larger assault.

'If they were going to give up so easily, they would have done so by now. Be on your guard, ${PLAYER}.'The Dunlendings are mounting a series of attacks upon the hill-top of Dol Baran in an attempt to test the resolve of the Rohirrim defenders.Dunlending warriors can be found near the barricades atop Dol Baran.

Grimbold has asked you to defeat Dunlending warriors by the barricades atop Dol Baran.Defeat Dunlending warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Captain Féarn awaits your return atop Dol Baran.

You should bring Captain Féarn news of your success.Talk to Captain Féarn'The Dunlendings are testing our resolve to hold Dol Baran, the great hill to the west, but they underestimate us.

'We must hold that position, or we will be blind to the approach of their main force when it marches out of Wulf's Cleft. If that happens, we may have to pull back across the Ford without a fight.

'Aid my men by the fortifications and hold off the Dunlendings. If we can force them to give up on Dol Baran and march their army past it, we will have a critical advantage in the battle to come.''Well fought out there, but I fear these attacks are just a prelude to a larger assault.

'If they were going to give up so easily, they would have done so by now. Be on your guard, ${PLAYER}.'Wynstan witnessed the shades of Oathbreakers assisting the brigand treasure-seekers as they brought relics out of Parth Celebrant and was disheartened that the Oathbreakers remained honourless.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you take this quest, you will begin Wynstan's Call of Honour line and will be unable to accept Bagmund's Dishonoured Dead line.</rgb>The captain of the shades is somewhere at Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore.

Wynstan has asked you to convince the captain of the shades to rejoin the fight against the Enemy and fulfill his oath.Talk to the captain of the shades at Atburg in the RushgoreRelics can be found at Atburg and upon the brigands therein.

Brúngwath has asked you to complete Aculf's request and collect the stolen relics to show your honour.Complete Stolen Pride and obtain the good will of the shadesEowils is outside Atburg in the Rushgore, south-east of Aculf's camp.

Wynstan told you to report your successes to the scout Eowils.Talk to Eowils outside Atburg in the Rushgore'Alas, the sorrow...there was once a company of Men from Gondor who had betrayed their lord in Parth Celebrant, allowing their great fortress to fall. They were cursed for breaking their oath and continue to wander these lands to this day. Such spirits should not remain, but may only find peace upon fulfillment of their oath.

'I have seen these shades at Atburg, lending aid to the treasure-seekers there. Perhaps you might find their captain and convince him to rejoin the fight against the Enemy...perhaps then, they may find both peace and honour.

'I cannot do this myself, for I am in terror of the shades. We have sent young Eowils to watch Atburg...when you have completed your task, find him and report to him.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you take this quest, you will begin Wynstan's Call of Honour line and will be unable to accept Bagmund's Dishonoured Dead line.</rgb>'You are not of Ulferth's band, yet I will not slay thee needlessly. What have thou to say to such as I?

'Thou sayest that the Great Eye has arisen once more and urge me to fulfill my oath? Ulferth and his men have shown us that honour is dead and hope is gone.

'But nay, I weary of this honourless existence. My oath was sworn in these lands, and here it must be fulfilled. Prove your honour by fulfilling the task appointed to you by your friend Aculf. Recover the relics of his people, but do not turn your eye upon my brethren.

'If thou take up arms against them, I will be your enemy until the end of your days. If thou provest your honour, we shall in turn prove ours in the day of need.''So, for better or for worse, the deed is done. We can only wait now and see what happens.'Grimbold has come up with a plan to deal with two problems at once: a treacherous warrior and an imprisoned Ranger. The man he believes to be a lackey of Isengard volunteered to guard the Ranger and might have his fondness for strong drink exploited.Daervunn the Ranger is detained at the Ford of Isen.

When the current guard leaves, put the ale someplace where Arbald is likely to stumble upon it.Daervunn the Ranger is detained at the Ford of Isen.

You should wait until Arbald drinks himself into a stupour, then cut the imprisoned Ranger loose, but be careful not to let the guard spot you.'You say that you need some ale for a friend of yours? Ha! But you did us a great favour, so I am more than happy to indulge you.

'Here you go. You and your 'friend' can drink to your health.''I see now. A clever plan, indeed! This way, Grimbold frees me and gains the excuse he needs to deal with a likely traitor in their midst.

'Well, as much as I would like to hear news from my kinsmen, I think I had best be going now.'After every attempt to intimidate the treasure-hunters into retreating from the Rushgore failed, Aculf has decided to take more drastic measures.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest can only be completed by a Solo player. It cannot be completed as part of a Fellowship.</rgb>Aculf is at his camp in the Rushgore, north-west of Atburg.

Aculf has asked you to join him and his companions as they assault Atburg.Talk to Aculf to join the assault on AtburgAculf is at his camp in the Rushgore, north-west of Atburg.

You should speak with Aculf regarding your victory at Atburg.Talk to Aculf at his camp in the Rushgore'We have given the brigands every opportunity to cease their thievery and leave our lands, but Eowils reports that they have refused at every turn. The time has come to take more drastic measures.

'We must assault Atburg and drive them forth at swordpoint! Are you with us, ${PLAYER}? It will be no mean feat, but we are of the sons of Éorl! We will not relent!

'If you intend to join us, speak with me again.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest can only be completed by a Solo player. It cannot be completed as part of a Fellowship.</rgb>'The brigands are resilient, ${PLAYER}. They have been routed for a time, but they will soon return...and we will rout them once again!

'Thank you for your aid.''Let us go, ${PLAYER}...the element of surprise is upon our side.'

