<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest can only be completed by a Solo player. It cannot be completed as part of a Fellowship.</rgb>Vicious Orc-slavers torment the Dunlending and Rohirrim captives in their mines.Orc Slavers can be found throughout the Orc-mines.

Ondor asked you to claim the whips from the Orc Slavers.Collect Orc-whips (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ondor the Dwarf is in the Orc-mines.

You should bring the whips you collected to Ondor the Dwarf.'Look at those poor beggars down there. Those Orcs employ the lash without mercy.

'I cannot stand the sight of it! If you wish to be of help, you bring me those whips, and I'll see to some compensation for your efforts.''Ah, I see you brought me those whips. It is good to know that these will not be seeing any more use.'The goblins in the Orc-mines seem to have gotten their hands on a new weapon that is even more dangerous than the fire-pots they had previously devised... most likely some new wizardry produced by Saruman.Goblins can be found throughout the Orc-mines.

Ondor asked you to defeat goblins in the Orc-mines, but warned you to beware their deadly new weapons.Defeat goblins in the Orc-mines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ondor the Dwarf is in the Orc-mines.

You should return to Ondor with news of your success.Talk to Ondor the Dwarf in the Orc-mines'There... did you hear that, ${PLAYER}? Those blasts you're hearing in the distance... it sounds like thunder down here, but it's actually one of those fool goblins playing with something new and dangerous.

'It sounds like something that mad, old Wizard up in the Shire might have cooked up, but I don't think he would be sharing it with the goblins. No, I'd wager Saruman is behind this devilry somehow. Anyway, goblins are nasty enough with their usual toys... I don't relish fighting them armed with whatever that is.

'Let us see if we can dissuade them from using it any more....''There is something dreadfully unsettling about a creature too stupid to know that the weapon it's holding is as likely to kill it as the person it's fighting. I just wish it made them easier to fight, but that kind of madness is hard to counter.

'Well, we'll just have to do our best. Good work down there, ${PLAYER}.'The avanc-nests along the Limlight have become a danger to those travelling south from Mirkwood.Avanc-nests can be found at their breeding grounds, north-west of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore.

Amal has asked you to destroy the avanc-nests in hopes of driving the creatures from the shores of the Limlight.Destroy avanc-nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Amal is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, south-east of the avanc breeding grounds.

You should return to Amal with news of your success.Talk to Amal at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore'While I find the hides of these avanc to be fascinating, the construction of their nests upon the shores of the Limlight will make travel between my village in Mirkwood and the south very dangerous.

'Would you go to their breeding grounds and destroy their nests? Perhaps that will drive them from the shore.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. As long as the avanc remain inland, my people should remain safe.'The Woodmen's boats were attacked and damaged by creatures that Amal described as demons and monsters.The demons Amal spoke of, which sound suspiciously like avanc, wander the Rushgore.

Amal asked you to banish the demons of the Rushgore to secure the safety of his party.Defeat avanc in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Amal is at the Woodman camp at the heart of the Rushgore.

You should return to Amal and let him know that you have culled the number of avanc in the area.Talk to Amal at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore'Ah, ${PLAYER}, it is terrible! I told you that we were attacked by monsters, but I must say that I believe they are instead demons!

'These beasts have the form and scales of a worm, but are also furred like the beavers of our land. I have never seen their like -- and must confess that I never wish to again -- but I have seen them wandering throughout the marsh.

'Have you skill in banishing demons? Will you put your talents to use against these monsters for us, so that we might survive to see our homes again?''Ah! They are mortal beasts, you say? And you have culled their number?

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for your mercy upon us.'Bagmund is appalled by the presence of the Oathbreakers at Atburg. Despite their noble heritage as Men of Gondor, he despises them for the betrayal they performed in ages past and for the dishonourable deeds they commit on behalf of the brigands.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you take this quest, you will begin Bagmund's Dishonoured Dead line and will be unable to accept Wynstan's Call of Honour line.</rgb>Shades can be found at Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore.

Bagmund has asked you to banish the shades from Atburg and the Rushgore.Defeat shades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eowils is outside Atburg in the Rushgore, south-east of Aculf's camp.

Bagmund asked you to report your successes to the scout Eowils.Talk to Eowils outside Atburg in the Rushgore'Is it not revolting? The Dead have no honour...cursed they were for betraying their lord, yet still they have no honour and fight for none. Instead they barter with brigands and thieves.

'How I wish we could banish them from this place so I would not have to endure their accursed presence. But wait! Perhaps we can! Perhaps you would be willing to do so?

'Drive them out, every one...that is all I ask. Let Stangard deal with these rebel spirits! When you have done this deed, speak with young Eowils, who watches Atburg for us...he will relay your news.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you take this quest, you will begin Bagmund's Dishonoured Dead line and will be unable to accept Wynstan's Call of Honour line.</rgb>'Ha! So much for those honourless devils! Well done, ${PLAYER}!'Dunlending patrols roam the road running south-west along the banks of the Isen.Dunlending outriders are patrolling the road along the Isen, south-west of the Rohirrim encampment.

Grimbold has asked you to eliminate some of the Dunlending patrols in order to give the Rohirrim room to manoeuvre unseen.Defeat Dunlending patrols (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grimbold is at the Ford of Isen.

You should inform Grimbold that the Dunlending patrols have been eliminated.Talk to Grimbold at the Ford of Isen'There are patrols running up and down the road along the Isen to the south-west of here.

'As long as they can keep an eye on that road, it will be difficult for us to make a move in that direction without them knowing about it.

'We are outnumbered badly enough as it is...we need the element of surprise where we can get it. If you could eliminate some of the outrider patrols on the road, I would greatly appreciate it.''The patrols have been dealt with? Good. That will buy us some space to manoeuvre in if we are forced to defend Dol Baran in the coming days.''Drive the Dunlending out of these lands!'Daervunn the Ranger was detained by the Rohirrim at the Ford of Isen when he attempted to warn them of Saruman's treachery. It appears that some faction within the Golden Halls of Edoras has a grudge against the Dúnedain and has ensured that their passage through the region will not be easy.Grimbold is at the Ford of Isen.

Daervunn has asked you to speak with Grimbold on his behalf.Talk to Grimbold at the Ford of IsenGrimbold has outlined his suspicions about Isengard's involvement in the orders he has received. You must find some way to free the Ranger without Grimbold's direct involvement.Talk to Grimbold at the Ford of Isen'${PLAYER}! Well met... or so I would say were I not bound to a post. I came here to warn Théodred of Saruman's schemes, but I am afraid the Wizard remains a step ahead of us.

'One of Grimbold's men produced a message from Edoras ordering the detainment of any Men of Dúnadan descent. It seems that Isengard may have wormed its tendrils into the nobility, if I do not miss my guess.

'Now, as much as I enjoy the comforts of a cheery camp-fire and the good company of my guards, I do not suppose you could see fit to speak on my behalf with the camp commander? I suppose I might be able to free myself, but I would likely injure or kill some of Grimbold's men in the process, and I would rather not give credence to Saruman's claims against us.''The Ranger? Aye, we detained him yesterday when he entered our camp unheralded.

'We are under new orders as regarding the Dúnedain. It seems that they have managed to cross the lords of Edoras in some manner.

'Come, let us speak more of this... in private.''My hands are bound with ties that no knife can cut. Only a sharp wit will suffice to break them....'Aculf wants to make it clear that the brigands are not welcome in the territory of the Riddermark, although he is willing to entertain a peaceful resolution.Ulferth can be found at the edge of Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore.

Aculf asked you to deliver his ultimatum to Ulferth, captain of the treasure-seekers in the Rushgore.Talk to Ulferth at Atburg in the RushgoreEowils is outside Atburg in the Rushgore, south-east of Aculf's camp.

Aculf instructed you to bring Ulferth's answer to the scout Eowils.Talk to Eowils outside Atburg in the Rushgore'Among the tasks that I have set you to, I want you to speak with Ulferth, the captain of these brigand treasure-seekers. Tell him that we will allow his band to leave peacefully, but they must leave behind all the relics that they stole from the Field of Celebrant.

'Ulferth is oft seen at the edge of their encampment at Atburg. This offer will only be open for a short time. If he refuses, then we shall take more drastic measures.

'Return to Eowils, our scout outside Atburg, with Ulferth's answer.''Are you serious? The horse-boy wants us to leave? The Field of Celebrant is rife with relics and trinkets from which my men and I can make a fortune...tell your friend that if he wants us gone, he will have to move us himself.''This is it, then. Ulferth has refused my demands. He shall rue the day he ever came to the Rushgore....'Grimbold has suggested that one of his less-well-loved guards is a minor noble and political schemer who happens to be overly fond of drink. This guard may be the weak link to allowing Daervunn to escape.The quartermaster can be found in the Rohirrim camp at the Ford of Isen.

Grimbold subtly inferred a plan to allow Daervunn to escape, but you will have to obtain some of the strong ale favoured by the Men of Rohan.Talk to the Rohirrim quartermasterThe Dunlendings have a camp not too far from the Ford of Isen, where the stolen ale is being kept.

You will need to fight your way into the Dunlending camp and retrieve the stolen casks if you want to enact Grimbold's plan to secretly release Daervunn.Recover ale-casks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Rohirrim quartermaster is at the Ford of Isen.

You should return the ale-casks that you recovered to the quartermaster at Grimbold's encampment.'The man responsible for your friend's imprisonment is a soldier under my command... an over-privileged fool from a minor noble house of Edoras. It would not surprise me in the least if his family had unsavoury dealings with Isengard... and it happens that this man has volunteered to guard the prisoner today.

'I happen to know that this fellow is more fond of strong drink than is good for him. If he were to be swayed by such temptations during his watch, there is a danger that the Ranger would slip away.

'That would be most unfortunate, as dereliction of duty is a severe offence that carries a stiff punishment. In any case, I have little more to say on the matter. Good day, ${PLAYER}.''What is that? Ale? Bah, you will have no such luck, I am afraid. The Dunlendings raided our camp two nights ago and made a fierce fight of it. Only a few of our men were hurt, so it could have been worse, but the distraction of the attack bought their kin a few minutes to inflict some real hurt on us... they stole our entire supply of ale!

'I can tell you what that will do to morale around here unless we can get that ale back, but Grimbold will not let us send out men on a dangerous mission just to retrieve some casks. He says it is 'frivolous.'

'Bah! You would think he would know better after leading men of war for so many years.''What is this? Our dear lost casks... you are a fine ${RACE}, indeed!

'I have no means to thank you enough, but should you need a drink, I will make certain that you get your fill before the rest of these louts drain the ale dry.'A young nobleman, one of Théodred's distant but well-loved kin, has crossed into Dunland in hopes of proving himself in battle, but the danger here is far greater than he imagined, and it is no place for an inexperienced young warrior.Dunstan and his company is abroad in the Heathfells.

Grimbold asked you to find Dunstan and his company so that you can deliver the Rohirrim lord's orders requesting the young warrior's return to the Ford of Isen.Find Dunstan and his company'Ah, my friends. I have a personal favour to ask. Two nights ago, a small band of riders joined us from the fields of Rohan, and glad I was of the additional men and horses...but alas, just this morning, I learned that one of the riders was a passing acquaintance of mine, and a much-beloved kinsman to Théodred, my prince.

'Dunstan is his name, and it seems he came here hoping to prove himself in battle...yet he wears too few years upon him and does not understand the peril of our position here.

'I need someone to retrieve him from the front where he and his men rode, and quickly, for I think there is little time left before the Dunlendings make a move against us...then it will be too late.'While fighting Orcs in the Heathfells, you found a sword one of them dropped. While it bore the usual crude hallmarks of Orc-crafting, it was very nearly brand new, suggesting that Orcs must have a lair nearby where they are forging these weapons.Orcs can be found in the northern Heathfells.

Cadfrith has asked you to defeat bands of Orcs that have crept into the northern Heathfells in hope that you can discover from whence they came.Find the Orc-cave in the north-east HeathfellsOndor the Dwarf is at the Orc-cave in the north-east Heathfells.

You should speak with the dwarf Ondor.Talk to Ondor the Dwarf at the Orc-caveThis blade was taken from a fallen Orc in the Heathfells. While forged in the usual crude and utilitarian manner of the Orcs, it appears to be almost brand new.

Somewhere nearby must be a cave or encampment where these particular Orcs are forging weapons. If you can find it, you should be able to tell the Rohirrim of its presence so that they can take action against them.'As if you aren't a sight for sore eyes. I have seen naught but Orcs for days now. A band of them struck my father's caravan a few days north of here. We were minding our own business, and this rabble fell upon us without warning.

'Well, we fought them off, of course, but my father died in the battle. The rest of our caravan returned south to Zigil-jâbal, but I swore an oath of vengeance against them.

'I don't suppose you could lend me some aid here?'You found a message upon the Dunlending Hound-master regarding a Rohirrim herald who has been sent to speak with a clan-leader among the Dunlendings. The herald is to be ambushed and slain before he reaches his destination.The herald is supposed to be travelling towards Dol Baran from an encampment at the Ford of Isen.

You should find and defend the herald of the Rohirrim.Defend the herald of the RohirrimThe body of the fallen Rohirrim herald lies before you.

You should collect the fallen herald's horn and return it to Grimbold.Check on the Rohirrim heraldThe Ford of Isen demarks the eastern boundary of Dunland. The Rohirrim have established an encampment on the western side of the ford, where Grimbold of the Grimslade can be found commanding their local forces.

Bring the horn to Grimbold and tell him of the herald's fate.Talk to Grimbold at the Ford of IsenThe message you found upon the Hound-master speaks of a Rohirrim herald who is travelling to parley with a Dunlending brenin. The Hound-master has been instructed to waylay and kill the herald before he arrives at the meeting.

While the Hound-master has been defeated, it appears that his allies have already departed to hunt down the herald. You should find the meeting place and rescue the herald before the trap is sprung.'What is this? You are no wild man... what are you doing out here?'

...

'I... I see. Well, we knew this was a danger when I agreed to parley with their chieftain.

'It was supposed to be a secret, but it seems there is little hope of that now.

'Wait - do you hear that? The baying of those accursed hounds of theirs. They have found us already!'The herald lies dead at last from a mortal arrow-wound, and you rise from your death vigil.

Gripping his horn you determine to deliver it to Grimbold at the Ford of Isen and tell him of the herald's fate.'Welcome to the Ford of Isen, ${PLAYER}. Some word of your exploits has preceded you here, thanks to the work of my outriders.'

Grimbold stands silently in thought for several long seconds as you hand him the herald's horn and tell him of the battle in which he fell.

'Fastgyl was a good and brave man. He knew it likely that any offer of the Dunlendings would be rife with treachery, but he took it upon himself to speak with them in hopes that this war could be averted.

'I thank you for abiding with him in his last hours.'You collected many relics of the Dunlendings for Bagmund, but his purpose for them is at yet unclear.The Dunlending Bagmund spoke of can be found at the Easterling camp, south of the Woodmen's camp in the Rushgore.

Bagmund asked you to take the Dunlending relics you found to a Dunlending his party has seen in the Rushgore.Find the Dunlending representativeThe Dunlending Bagmund spoke of can be found at the Easterling camp, east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore.

Bagmund asked you to take the Dunlending relics you found to a Dunlending his party has seen in the Rushgore.Bagmund is at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore, west of the Easterling camp.

You should return to Bagmund and revile him for sending you on such a dishonourable errand.Talk to Bagmund at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore'I am nearly done with these...ha! This is perfect!

'A Dunlending has been seen among the Easterlings at their scout-camp to the east. Take these to him and tell him that they are returned courtesy of the Riddermark!

'I am sure he will reciprocate in kind....''You dare speak to me of honour? By your own admission you consorted with the Dunlending dogs while journeying through their land!

'Begone with you...I have no more words to waste on you!''Dunlending? Nay, the man you seek is among those who call themselves the Khundolar to the south.

'I have much to say on the Khundolar, if you will stay and speak with me.''What is this? This is an outrage! These tokens once bore the visages of our people's greatest heroes, but they have been defaced!

'You tell the forgoil that if they want war, it will come to them soon enough! Now, begone before I have you slain!'You have come upon a cave entrance in the northern Heathfells, on the border of Isengard, where you have encountered a rather unusual dwarf. Seemingly without heed to his own safety, he seems to have set about collapsing the cave entrance, which he claims leads to a warren of Orcs below.Help Ondor the Dwarf collapse the entrance to the Orc-cave.Help Ondor collapse the caveWith the cave entrance collapsed, you might have a few spare moments to speak with Ondor.Talk to Ondor'Hey there, my good ${RACE}, I don't suppose you would be up for a quick bit of sport?

'This cave is packed full of Orcs, and I see no reason to leave it as is... it is better to seal the lot of them in the dark below!

'I have found a weak point in the rock here that should bring it down, but it will take a few minutes and make a whole lot of noise, so I could use a hand holding the Orcs off until I can bring it down.''These rocks are not going to knock themselves over. Let's get on with it!''When I start swinging this pick, the Orcs are likely to come running, so let me know when you are ready....''There we go, and a job well done, if I do say so myself. Ondor is my name, by the way. I followed a raiding party for three days until they disappeared in here... after they smashed my family's caravan and killed my father, of course.

'The rest of the family is headed back south to find refuge in Zigil-jâbal -- but I swore to hunt down the ones that did for my father. Of course, I cannot tell one Orc from another, so now I am left trying to deal with the whole lot of them.

'It looks like it could take a while... well, no sense staying here. There is too much to do. Perhaps I will see you about, if we are both lucky!'You have accompanied Aculf and his companions to Atburg to try and rout the brigands there.You should speak with Aculf.Talk to AculfYou must drive all of the brigands from Atburg.Defeat all treasure-huntersSpeak with Aculf about your victory.Talk to Aculf'This is it, ${PLAYER}...there is no turning back. We must clear these brigands out, or die trying! Forth the Éorlingas!''Well done, ${PLAYER}! We have driven off the brigands...for now at least. They are resilient and will likely return, but they will be weaker for it.''Let us leave before the brigands return.'You have come upon a cave-entrance in the northern Heathfells, on the border of Nan Curunir, where you have encountered a rather unusual dwarf. Without heed to his own safety, he has set about collapsing the cave-entrance, which he claims leads to a warren of Orcs below.Defend Ondor as he works to collapse the cave-entrance.Talk to OndorOndor is at the Orc-cave.

You should speak with Ondor the Dwarf once more.'It has been a pleasure working with you, ${PLAYER}.''All right, here we go. Keep an eye on that cave, and if any Orcs come running... well, you know what to do.''Well, I suppose that's the last of the Orcs. It will take them weeks to dig out that mess... lazy curs.

'If it were dwarves trapped in there, they would be out in a day!'The Khundolar prepare to lay siege to Etheburg, and you have chosen to defend the way-post.Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

You should speak at once with Céola to learn his plan.Talk to CéolaDefeat all of the attacking Khundolar.Defeat all of the attacking KhundolarCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

You should speak with Céola regarding the battle at Etheburg.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'We shall speak again later, ${PLAYER}.''${PLAYER}, I am glad that you have chosen to stand with us! Twiga will lead the forces in the upper tier of Etheburg, while you, our men, and I defend the lower tiers.

'If you so desire, you may enter the watch-towers and speak with the archers on duty. If you do, they will rain arrows down upon our foes.

'Now, to arms!''I will rain arrows upon our enemies!''I will rain arrows upon our enemies!''I will rain arrows upon our enemies!''I will rain arrows upon our enemies!''You have acquitted yourself well, ${PLAYER}, and have most definitely earned this reward. May our arms remain strong!'You have disturbed the insect-nest, producing unexpected results.Defeat all insects at the nest to draw forth the queen.Defeat the Queen of Queens and her broodYou prod at the nest, but nothing happens.Having made what preparations you could, you must help the Orcs' slaves reach the exit of the mines as you fight your way past the brutal Orc-overseers.Speak with Edhere and tell him to lead his men out of the mine.Talk to EdhereSpeak with Ondor and release him from his cell.Talk to OndorSpeak with Meriun and tell him to lead his men out of the mine.Talk to MeriunFight your way towards the forges and free any slaves you come across.Talk to OndorFight your way up onto the platforms to reach the bridge spanning the cavern.Talk to OndorThe shortest way out of the Orc-mines lies across a long trestlebridge that spans the cavern. It is likely to be the most perilous step of your escape.Talk to OndorYou must make your way up the slopes, then fight your way past any remaining Orcs to the exit of the caverns.Talk to Ondor'We made it! Let's be out of this cavern and let our allies know what is going on down here!''My men are ready to leave, ${PLAYER}. We will make for the bridge across the centre of the mine and free as many of the slaves as we can along the way.''Aye, well, your timing's good. Those accursed Orcs snuck up on me and all went black! I woke up in here just a short while ago.

'It looks like my stay is to be a short one, though, so let's be about it!''We will fight alongside the Horse-lords, for even they know far greater honour than these foul Orcs.''Well, there goes the alarm. The Orcs will be after us now. Let's cut a way through and quick!

'There's a number of slaves near the forges, so we had best head that way and see how many we can free as we go.'You unshackle the slave and tell him to make for the exit while your band draws the attention of the Orcs.'The bridge is up at the top of this platform... it's the quickest way out, so that's the way we are going before a hundred more of these brutes come up from the deep caverns.'You unshackle the slave and tell him to make for the exit while your band draws the attention of the Orcs.'Well, if they don't have some trouble waiting for us on this bridge, then I will shave my beard, so gird your loins... it gets rough from here.'You unshackle the slave and tell him to make for the exit while your band draws the attention of the Orcs.'We are almost there. If we can make it to the cavern entrance before anymore Orcs show up, we will be free.'Having quickly moved to rescue a herald of the Rohirrim from a Dunlending ambush, you have arrived only in time to desperately fend off the attackers.Defend the herald of the Rohirrim from his ambushers.Talk to the Rohirrim heraldOverwhelming numbers of wild men are approaching. Summon the Rohirrim to your aid.Blow the Horn of the RohirrimHold out until reinforcements arrive.Defeat the Dunlending attackersWith the battle over, the herald you strove to protect lies dying. You speak to him, hoping to bring his final words to his allies at the Ford of Isen.The herald has fallen silent, his breath coming in a few last ragged gasps as his life fades.'You are correct... I hear the baying of the Dunlending hounds approaching even now.

'It seems we were fools to trust these wild men to parley fairly, but so be it... let us show them the quality of our valour!''You are a fine ${RACE} to stand by me in my final hour.

'Take my horn to the Ford and let Grimbold know that I have fallen. Tell him I am sorry....'

The herald's voice trails off into laboured breathing as he closes his eyes in pain and exhaustion.

He does not speak again.You have travelled to the Easterling camp in the Rushgore to carry out a pre-emptive assault in defence of Amal and his companions.Defeat all Khundolar Easterlings at the camp.Defeat all Khundolar Easterlings at the campThe Dunlendings are assaulting the Rohirrim encampment atop Dol Baran.Defend against the Dunlendings atop Dol Baran.Talk to GrimboldDestroy Dunlending banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the Dunlending chieftain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grimbold awaits you atop Dol Baran.

You should speak with Grimbold regarding your victory.Talk to Grimbold atop Dol BaranSee to the dead atop Dol Baran.See to the dead atop Dol Baran'This battle is over, for the time being.

'I do not expect the Dunlendings will be ready to muster another assault upon Dol Baran until their main force moves out of Wulf's Cleft... and for that, we shall have sufficient warning to gauge their thrust.

'Let us hope that is enough.''Here they come, ${PLAYER}! We must hold this position against the Dunlendings!''Well done, ${PLAYER}! Our losses were great, but we held out against the foe... it will take them time to recover, and by that time, we should have reinforcements.'Enraged by your attack upon Lashkarg and the death of their chieftain, the Khundolar stage an assault upon Etheburg.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo, but can be run with a Duo as well.</rgb>Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to help the Rohirrim border-guard defend against the Khundolar's retaliation.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo, but can be run with a Duo as well.</rgb>Talk to Céola when you are ready to defend EtheburgCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

You should speak with Céola regarding the victory at Etheburg.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'There are lights in the land, ${PLAYER}. The fires of Lashkarg burn brightly, for the Khundolar prepare to lay siege to Etheburg. You had a mighty victory at Lashkarg, but now I fear we must pay the price for it.

'Will you stand with us and defend Etheburg? If we can rout the enemy here, then we may actually survive this war!

'If you do wish to help us defend Etheburg, speak with me again, and we will go to prepare ourselves.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo, but can be run with a Duo as well.</rgb>'Ah, ${PLAYER}, we were fortunate to survive that attack; however, I think the Khundolar will be unable to attack again for some time.

'Thank you for your courage and your weapon!''Good! Let us prepare ourselves for battle!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo, but can be run with a Duo as well.</rgb>Ondor wants to know what the Orcs are mining in this cave. Saruman must have some use for the strange minerals they are digging up.Ore can be found throughout the Orc-mines.

Ondor the Dwarf asked you to bring him some of the mysterious ore the Orcs are mining.Collect strange ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ondor the Dwarf is in the Orc-mines.

You should bring the ore you collected to Ondor.'Saruman isn't just mining iron ore down here, ${PLAYER}... there are other things as well, but I can't quite figure out what it is that he is after.

'If you could get me a few samples of that ore, I will take a closer look at it and see if I can determine what it is.''Well done. I will need as much of this ore as you can bring me, so if you happen to come across more, bring it here.'Amal is concerned by the ever-increasing attention the Easterling scouts in the Rushgore have begun paying the beleaguered Woodmen.The Easterling camp lies to the south of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore.

Amal asked you to speak with the leader of the Easterlings in the Rushgore and convince him that they are not a threat.Talk to the leader of the Easterlings at their camp in the RushgoreAmal is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, north of the Easterling camp.

You should return to Amal with Nafrati's warning.Talk to Amal at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore'Not only are we surrounded by demons, but we have seen Men from the East scouting these lands. At first, they paid us little heed, but of late, they have begun watching us more closely. I fear that they may consider us a threat or easy prey.

'Will you go to their camp and speak with their leader? Perhaps you might convince them that we are of no threat and likely have nothing of worth to a warband.

'If you would indeed go, their camp lies to the south of here.''So, you come on behalf of the Woodmen? They wish us to leave them in peace? They are no threat?

'That they are no threat to us is clear, but they are the friends of our enemies. We have come to wage war upon the Horse-lords of Rohan, for it is demanded by the Great Eye.

'For that, the Woodmen must perish. We will give them time to prepare themselves, but their end is nigh. Go now and warn them: leave this place or become a sacrifice to the Dark Lord.''This is what I feared most, ${PLAYER}! We have not the means to defend ourselves against Nafrati's men, nor can we escape. We will perish!''The Woodmen of the North are the friends of our enemies...we will have no mercy.''Please...convince the Khundolar to leave us be!'Small bands of Orcs have been spotted wandering in the foothills in the northern Heathfells. The Rohirrim are not sure where they hail from, but they are a threat that must be dealt with.Orcs can be found throughout the northern part of the Heathfells.

Captain Cadfrith has asked you to defeat the bands of Orcs that have crept into the northern Heathfells and discover where they are coming from.Defeat Orc grunts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orc guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Captain Cadfrith is at the Rohirrim encampment in the north-west Heathfells.

You should return to Captain Cadfrith with your report.Talk to Cadfrith at the Rohirrim encampment'It seems this barren land is twice accursed. Not only have we the Dunlending barbarians ready to fall upon us, but the most recent messenger from the Ford claims that he was ambushed and pursued by Orcs as he travelled through the vale east of here.

'I do not know where they come from, but we have problems enough without those foul curs pouring down from the mountains upon us. See if you can hunt a few of them and discover where they are coming from.''Hunt the Orcs in the Heathfells, ${PLAYER}.''So, the Orcs are indeed coming down out of the mountains... and in significant numbers.

'These had best be wandering bands of raiders and nothing more... if they are allied with the Dunlendings, our hold on Dol Baran is as good as lost.'Many of the Woodmen's crates and containers were damaged during the avanc-attack. They managed to salvage many of the contents, but the containers need to be patched.The burrow Gisalic mentioned lies to the north-east of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore.

Gisalic asked you to collect reeds and clay from the burrow he saw nearby.Collect Rushgore clay (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Rushgore reeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gisalic is at the Woodman camp at the heart of the Rushgore.

You should return the materials you gathered to Gisalic and tell him of the insect infestation.'${PLAYER}, will you hear me out? When the demons of the Rushgore attacked our boats, many of our crates and containers were damaged. We salvaged most of the contents, but the containers need to be patched to transport them safely when we arrive in the land of the Horse-lords.

'Will you go forth into the marsh and collect reeds strong enough to bind the containers and mud to patch them? While we scouted for an ideal camp-site, I saw a great burrow of mud and clay to the north-east of here. Perhaps you may find the materials I require there?

'Thank you for any assistance that you will provide.''You say that you were attacked by great, envenomed insects at the burrow? That could bode ill for us, but it could also prove useful... let me think upon it.

'As for the reeds and clay, aye... these will do well. Thank you!'Your discovery of great insects among the burrows has both caused Gisalic concern and inspired brilliance.Insects may be found at the Creeping Mud to the north-east of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore.

Gisalic has asked you to collect venom sacs from the insects of the Rushgore.Collect venom-sacs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gisalic is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, south-west of the Creeping Mud.

You should bring the venom-sacs you collected to Gisalic at once.Talk to Gisalic at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore'These insects you discovered at the burrows are a source of both great concern and great inspiration. To have such venomous creatures nearby is a cause of fear, but it may prove a boon as well.

'As you may be aware, we have been attacked by the creatures you call avanc, but we have also been threatened by the Men from the East who have encroached upon these lands. Perhaps I could use the venom of these insects to make a poison to defend ourselves with.

'Would you return to the burrows and gather the venom sacs from these insects? Only the venom of the insects at the Creeping Mud will suffice. I know it seems a harsh method of defence, but we are truly vulnerable in this place.''Aye, these will do nicely. I think I might indeed be able to make a poison to use as a defence against those that threaten us.

'Thank you.'One of the nests among the insect burrows seems to bear signs of much activity. Perhaps this is the nest of the brood's queen?

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>The queen's nest is at the insect-nest, north-east of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore.

Perhaps disturbing the nest will produce the brood's queen.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>Disturb the nest to draw forth the Queen of QueensGisalic is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, south-west of the insect nest.

