<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>You study the maps placed on the table and consider Théodred's plan.

This is indeed a daring move, and the Prince expects it to renew Saruman's caution. By nightfall, who knows what the situation may be? It could be that night will bring with it renewed hope for Rohan. There are other possibilities as well, but they are darker and more grim.

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>Edbrit saw something fall from the sky, but before he goes with you to investigate it he needs your help in the Rushgore.Edbrit has asked you to defeat gredbyg, turtles, and avanc that have been stirred up in the Rushgore.

Something has caused the creatures of the Rushgore to become more hostile than usual, and Edbrit wants you to help him deal with them before the two of you go in search of the falling shadow.Defeat gredbyg in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat avanc in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat turtles in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Edbrit is at Aculf's Camp in the Rushgore.

You have helped deal with some of the newly-aggressive creatures in the Rushgore, and should return now to Edbrit.Edbrit saw a mysterious shadow fall from the sky far to the south-east, in the Brown Lands.

You have decided to travel to the Brown Lands in search of the mysterious shadow Edbrit saw.Find the location in the Brown Lands where the falling shadow came to earthEdbrit is standing by the corpse of a mighty beast in the Brown Lands.

You have found the body of a massive beast, and should speak to Edbrit about it.Nona is standing by the corpse of the fallen beast in the Brown Lands.

Nona is waiting to speak with you.'I saw a great shadowy shape fall from the sky not long ago. You can come with me to investigate it, if you wish, but first I need to ensure the safety of the Rushgore. Something has stirred up the creatures of this swampy land, and it is my duty to keep them from becoming a serious threat.

'I am not as young as I once was, but my arms are still strong and can still swing a sword. I may not sit the saddle as I used to, but my legs are stronger than many a young man's. Together we will travel in search of the falling shadow, and see what there is to see.

'But first we must thin back the newly-aggressive creatures of the Rushgore. If you help me in this, we will be sooner underway. Defeat gredbyg, turtles, and avanc throughout the Rushgore, and then return to me. Then we will search for the place where this falling shadow came to ground.''See what I have found, ${PLAYER}! Something is wrong in this land. I can feel it. This must be why we are here. This is the reason for your dream! Remember the words of Suvulch my father: dreams have power. We ignore their warnings at our peril.

'This beast is dead, but something rode it, and that creature is not here. Your dream brought us here to keep that creature from doing great evil, ${PLAYER}. I feel it in my very bones.''This must be the shape my men and I beheld as it plummeted from the sky. What a terrible creature!'

Edbrit shivers, and his eyes go wide as he turns away from the dead beast.

'Is that... riding gear? Did someone ride astride this terrible creature? And if so... where is the rider?''Good, I thank you for your hard work against the unusually aggressive creatures of the Rushgore. I would not have wanted to leave my post with those threats unmet, but now I feel we have earned a time of peace. Enough time for us to seek the falling shadow, at any rate. I will need to return before long.

'While we walk, perhaps you can tell me of your adventures? Why do you smile? I can tell by your face that you have seen more adventure in recent days than even Edbrit, in all his years, can claim to have experienced. I would be pleased to hear anything you would tell me about yourself.

'I will go with you into the Brown Lands to search for the falling shadow. Let us look for it far to the south-east. I believe that is where it came to ground.''${PLAYER}! What a terrible marvel this is!''The reek of this creature overpowers the senses!''Look at this! What is this beast?''We are fortunate this terrible creature is dead. But where is its rider?''Something has stirred up the creatures of the Rushgore. Deal with the gredbyg, turtles, and avanc that have become aggressive, and return to me. We will then go in search of the falling shadow I beheld.

'When I was young, I rode far afield among the waving grasses of Rohan. Few could match me for wanderlust, and I saw many wondrous sights. Few men could claim to see as many.

'Now that I am grown old, I find I am more interested in the people that walk these lands than in the places I meet them. Each of their stories is singular and unique, and it is for these people I accepted this work. We must keep the Rushgore safe for their benefit.''We will search the Brown Lands for the falling shadow. I think it fell across the river, far to the south-east.

'I do not know what it could have been, ${PLAYER}. I have seen many strange things in my time, but... something about this shadow filled me with dread.'

Edbrit falls silent, his face suddenly pensive.

'I do not know what we will find, ${PLAYER}, but I fear it will prove a danger to my people and these lands.'Someone rode astride the beast that now lies dead in the Brown Lands. But where is this vanished rider?The great beast that crashed in the Brown Lands is missing its rider, but people throughout the lands bordering the Great River may have seen signs of it. You should seek them out and learn where the rider has gone.Complete the deed 'The Vanished Rider' to learn the location of the missing NazgûlYou have scoured the lands near the Great River for some sign of the missing Nazgûl, but have always been half a step behind. You should meet with Nona back by the corpse of the crashed beast as you agreed.'This is the reason for your dream! This is why we are here! I have never seen a creature as terrible as this, lest it be the mighty worm my brother slew beneath Zudrugund.'

As you stare at the corpse of the massive beast and contemplate the mangled harness and its missing rider, a single word echoes in your mind: Nazgûl. Nona watches you closely.

'Do you know something about the rider of this beast, ${PLAYER}? Your face tells me it must be a creature of terrible power. We must find it! We must search for it throughout this land! Look for signs of its passage among the lands of the Great River! After we have scoured these lands, we will meet back here at this creature, ${PLAYER}. Let this purpose guide our steps!''We have learned much of this creature, but not what we need to know. Where has its rider gone, and what cruel fate has kept us a step behind it at every turn?''The creature that rode upon this beast is missing. We must find it. Seek through the lands next to the Great River to find people who may have seen sign of its passage!'You have followed signs left by the rider of the terrible beast that met its end in the Brown Lands, but have not been able to find the rider itself.Nona is standing by the carcass of the beast in the Brown Lands.

Your search for the missing Nazgûl has proven fruitless, and Nona wants to walk with you back to Stangard where you can find more information.Talk to Nona by the Carcass of the Beast and walk with her back to StangardGaladriel is atop the flet on which is built the House of Celeborn, in Lothlórien.

The night was long, but Galadriel has once again summoned you to speak with her.Talk to Galadriel outside the House of Celeborn'This rider... what was the word you used? Nazgûl? The creature was looking for something. We need to think. It brought us on a chase through these lands, but I cannot tell what it sought, or if it found what it desired.

'We have no choice but to return to the village of the horse-lords. I will wait outside while you speak with that man Horn. We are strangers in this land. He is not. He may know of a place we have not yet searched.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'You have journeyed far, and have come very close to death and sadness. And yet, still you skirt the gravest danger and come safely through the other side. I hope that our mutual friends fare as well.

'I told you earlier I had nothing to do with your dream, and this was true. But when you described your visions to me, I did not tell you everything I suspected. It seemed clear to me that your paths must cross one of the Nine. I believed the girl would die.

'And yet, unbelieveably, she did not. Either through your own actions, or hers, you both escaped the clutches of the Nazgûl. And either through curious good fortune or powers unknown to me, our mutual friends seem to have outdistanced its pursuit.

'But there is no rest for we who worry for their safety. The Nazgûl is not the last danger they will face. They, and you, are not free of evil's clutch just yet. Rest for a time, but not for long.

'There are plans to be made, ${PLAYER}. We will speak again, and soon.''Let us talk on the way back to the village of the horse-lords.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>Your body is exhausted and your mind is ill at ease following the Battle of the Ford.A bedroll you can use is located south of Grimbold's position in his camp, by the milestone.

Grimbold wants you to get some rest while you can.Find a bedroll in Grimbold's camp and get some restGrimbold is in his camp, north of your bedroll.

You have had a most peculiar dream, if dream it was, and you should tell Grimbold of it.Talk to Grimbold in his camp and tell him about the strange dream'It has been a long day, ${PLAYER}, and we all could use a rest. We have held the Ford, but have lost Prince Théodred, and that weighs heavily upon my mind. I fear the doom of Rohan is near. My men are tired, weary in body and mind, and we cannot stop it.

'Go south of here, to the milestone located in this camp. You will find a bedroll you can use there. Take your rest while you can. You may not have another opportunity for a while, and we will need you to be ready.''We should all get some rest, ${PLAYER}. We will be the better for it.

'Find a bedroll south of here in the camp, by the milestone, and get what rest you can. I think you have need of it, as do we all.'The bedroll is uncomfortable, and you can feel every jutting stone of the hard ground through it. Even so, you are so exhausted by the events of the day that you fall into a troubled sleep.

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'What? You had a bad dream? Such things are to be expected after a battle.'

Grimbold's expression becomes darker and more concerned as you tell him what you remember of the troubling dream.

'Ah, this is not merely a bad dream, ${PLAYER}. This is Elf-magic of the worst sort. You have dallied with strange peoples and mysterious forces, and are now caught in their net! If you were not so valuable in a fight, I would command you to leave and never return! You could not leave my sight quickly enough!'If the dream that troubled your sleep is as it seems, Grimbold is right: you need to take it seriously and act upon its mysterious message.Wilfrith is in Forthbrond, to the west of Grimbold's Camp.

Grimbold thinks you should travel to Forthbrond and speak with Wilfrith for information about tracking down Wadu's Ghost in the Gap of Rohan.Wilfrith heard the sound of swords clashing from the direction of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr, west of Forthbrond. He wants you to defeat Wargs there while you search for Nona.

Wilfrith thinks you might be able to learn news of Nona by travelling to the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr.Defeat Wargs at Âthdâr (${NUMBER}/4)Wilfrith heard the sound of swords clashing from the direction of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr, west of Forthbrond. He wants you to defeat Wargs there while you search for Nona.

Wilfrith thinks you might be able to learn news of Nona by travelling to the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr.Defeat Wargs at Âthdâr (3/4)You caught a glimpse of gold from the western side of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr.

You should investigate the golden glimpse you saw at Âthdâr.Investigate the flash of gold on the western side of ÂthdârYou have spied another glint of gold to the west of Âthdâr, where two trails meet.

