'But now you should return to the House of Celeborn and speak with your Dunlending friend. Tell her we are almost ready to leave.'The first stage of your journey south with Corudan and Nona involves a brief stop in Thinglad to collect Corudan's bow.Corudan is in Thinglad, in the Great River.

You have come to Thinglad with Nona and Corudan, and should speak to Corudan, who wanted to recover the bow he lent to Fimloth.Orcs can be found throughout Thinglad, alongside the Great River. Defeat them while Corudan and Nona do the same, and perhaps you will find Corudan's lost bow.Defeat Orcs in Thinglad while Nona and Corudan hunt for the bow as well (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Corudan is at Haldirith, in Thinglad.

You have searched for the Orc that took Corudan's bow, but did not find it.Talk to Corudan in HaldirithNona is in Haldirith, in Thinglad.

You should speak to Nona about her experience hunting with Corudan.Talk to Nona in Haldirith'I am grateful for the healing arts of Galadriel and her people, and for the lady's willingness for me to see her city. But there is something strange about this place, and I must tell you the truth: it is no place for me. I want my feet upon the ground and my foes in front of me. This land of Elves is a long way from Enedwaith, a long way from my people.

'I am ready to depart, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps things will feel more familiar to me as we journey south along the river.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Haldirith in the Great River when you accept this quest.</rgb>Nona looks around Haldirith with interest, but says nothing.'This is a setback. This Elf gave his bow to someone, and that Elf lost it. This is why none but me wield Wadu's sword.''I am not pleased about this, ${PLAYER}. I lent Fimloth my favourite bow to use while I remained in Lothlórien, and now she has lost it!'

Corudan lowers his voice and turns to his apologetic friend.

'No, Fimloth, I am not upset. If those Orcs were as numerous as you report, you were right to flee. A bow is a bow, and the lives of my friends come first! I will search the woods of Thinglad for the Orc that picked it up as you escaped.

'Are you of a mind to join the hunt, ${PLAYER}? Your Dunlending friend has already agreed to fight the Orcs with me as well. Perhaps we can make a game of it! The first of us to find my lost bow will be the victor, but I shall be the happiest of all to have the bow back in my hands!''Search Thinglad for Orcs! The Dunlending girl and I will do the same. Whoever first finds my bow will be the victor in our little game.'Nona looks at you with disappointment on her face, and you can tell that she has not found Corudan's bow either.'You did not find the bow? Nona and I did not either. The Orc that seized it must have already left this area. Pity. This spare bow does not fire as accurately as my other did. I am still a deadly shot, ${PLAYER}. Do not worry on that score!

'Did you know how dangerous Nona is in combat? I did not think the Dunlendings were more than barbaric hill-dwelling Men, but she is a deadly warrior indeed! I underestimated her, and will not do so again. If we are surprised by Orcs as we journey further along the Anduin, I will be glad to have her along!''Nona is quite a warrior. I did not expect it!''You did not find Corudan's bow? We did not either. He seemed surprised, but I was not. Whatever Orc took the bow must have known an Elf would come looking for it, and fled the area.

'This Orc is lucky it did! For its hunters numbered three: ${RACE}, Uch-lûth, and Elf! Flight alone could have saved it. I am sorry Corudan does not have his favourite bow, but I still enjoyed the hunt.

'Do you think you can humour me on one count, ${PLAYER}? I understand we must hurry, but this should not take long.'Nona has requested that you stop by the Rohirrim outpost of Stangard so she can thank Horn for speaking on her behalf.You should speak with Afic, the guard at the gate of Stangard, about meeting with Horn.Talk to Afic at the gate of Stangard to learn of Horn's whereaboutsHorn is atop the hill of Stangard.

You have spoken with Afic, the guard at the gate of Stangard, and he had some inexplicably harsh words concerning Horn.Talk to Horn in StangardHorn is no longer welcome in Stangard, and has asked you to collect his harp from the Stangard Tavern, and his writing supplies from Wada's house.Collect Horn's harp from the Stangard tavernCollect Horn's writing supplies from Wada's houseHorn is in Stangard, waiting for you to bring him the items for which he asked.Nona is in Haldirith, in Thinglad.

Horn has decided to travel with you, and now you should go back to Nona so she can be told.Talk to Nona at HaldirithCorudan is at Haldirith, in Thinglad.Talk to Corudan at Haldirith'When we were last in this region, I was wounded in the swamp, and you brought me to the nearby outpost of the horse-lords. I was a wounded enemy to everyone there save one: the Rohirrim man called Horn. He spoke on my behalf, and when you suggested that I be taken to the Elf-woods for healing...'

You interrupt Nona at this point and tell her that it was actually Horn's idea. A confused look crosses her face.

'Really? Well, that is one more thing for which I should thank him. And that is what I want, ${PLAYER}: a brief detour to the outpost of Stangard so I can give him my thanks. Perhaps you can have him meet me here. I do not think I would be welcome once again within their walls.''I want to thank the Rohirrim man Horn for speaking on my behalf, ${PLAYER}. Go to Stangard and tell him to meet me here. I cannot think I am welcome within the walls of that outpost.''Oh. It's you. Still travelling with unsavoury types, are you?'

Afic looks you up and down, and the disgust on his face is clear.

'You are looking for Horn? Good! Take him with you! Take him and begone! You will find him up the hill.''You will find Horn atop the hill. Take him with you and begone! This is no place for him, or for you!''I did not think to see you again, ${PLAYER}. How is the Dunlending girl? Did she survive?'

You tell Horn that the healing arts of Galadriel were sufficient, and that Nona has come to Thinglad and wishes to thank him in person for his kind words and actions.

'Oh, I see... I am glad.'

Horn seems conflicted about something, and when you ask him if everything is all right he sighs heavily.

'It seems there is no place for me anymore, ${PLAYER}. I am no longer welcome in Stangard. My fellows feel that I have been somehow tainted by stepping foot within the Elf-woods, and by speaking on behalf of a Dunlending... well, they no longer trust me. They want me to leave by sunrise tomorrow.'

You ask if there is anything you can do to help.

'Well, I do not have many possessions. If you bring me my harp and my writing supplies, I will be ready to go. My harp is in the tavern, and my writing supplies are in Wada's house, where I have been staying.''I do not have many possessions, but if you bring me my harp and writing supplies, I can leave Stangard. My harp is in the tavern, and the writing supplies are in Wada's house, where I have been staying.

'I must leave Stangard by sunrise.''Thank you for bringing me these. I am not welcome in Stangard, but where can I go? By order of Théoden King I am not to return to Rohan until my term of service in Stangard is finished.'

Horn looks uncomfortable.

'Where are you travelling, ${PLAYER}? Could you use another companion on the road? I do not wish to intrude, but I believe my place is with you and with the Dunlending girl for whom I gave up... well. It was no life I gave up. I only did what was right, though my fellows fail to see it.'

You tell Horn that he is welcome to travel with you as far as he will.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I owe you a great deal for this. An aimless life would ill suit me. Your goals are now mine, and the dangers you face I will face as well.''I am in your debt, my friend. Let us go to see the other members of your party!'Corudan looks at you silently, brooding about his lost bow.You tell Nona that Horn has been cast out of Stangard and is no longer welcome there.

'This confirms all I ever suspected about the horse-lords, ${PLAYER}! They are cruel even to their own, and are not deserving of our sympathies! I will speak with Horn, thank him for his words on my behalf, and give him my sorrow that he has suffered for me. But I will also tell him that he is now better off, and need shed no tears for his lost fellows!

'We will be ready to leave when Corudan says we should leave. Speak with him when you are ready to go.''I am very sorry that Horn gave up his life at that outpost on my behalf, but he will be better off with us. The horse-lords do not deserve him.

'Speak to Corudan when you are ready to go.''Our band of companions grows: a Dunlending girl, a Rohirrim man, an Elf, and you. It sounds like a joke, does it not?'Your group of companions is ready to continue your journey down the Anduin.Corudan is at Haldirith, in Thinglad, waiting to continue your journey down the Anduin.Talk to Corudan at Haldirith and continue your journey down the AnduinYou have travelled with Corudan, Nona, and Horn to the Argonath, the Pillars of the Kings. Horn would like to speak with you.Talk to Horn near the shadow of the Argonath'We will still fit in the one boat... but it will not be comfortable. I do not think we should recruit any more companions, ${PLAYER}, unless you fancy swimming alongside the boat!

'Are you ready to continue our journey?''They are not my kings, but there is still something majestic about the twin statues of the Argonath. Many songs have been sung about the men in whose likenesses they are carved, and I know most of them by heart. I will not sing them now. There is too much we must do here.''How many lives of Men did it take to fashion those great statues? I have never seen anything like it before!''The Argonath, the Pillars of the Kings. I have seen them often, but even so they still capture the breath as they emerge from the mist, do they not?''Let us go to the boat together. I want to have a good seat and a comfortable place to rest my arm as we paddle.'Defeat Brigands in the Great River.Defeat Brigands in the Great RiverDefeat many Brigands in the Great River.Defeat Brigands in the Great RiverYou found Mabon, son of the merchant Andras whom you aided in the Starkmoor, with Gwin the hunter in Galtrev.The escaped prisoner is at the Ox-clan merchant camp in Nan Curunír.

Mabon has asked you to take him to meet the prisoner who escaped from Orthanc to learn if he knows whether his father, Andras, yet lives.Talk to AndrasMabon is at the Ox-clan camp outside of Isengard in Nan Curunír.

You should speak with Mabon at once.Talk to Mabon'${PLAYER}! Have you heard yet? Some of the prisoners you helped to escape from Orthanc survived... my father might be among them!

'The Boar-clan resistance says that one of the prisoners has taken refuge among a party of my people, the Ox-clan, outside of Isengard in Nan Curunír. Will you take me there? I must know if my father is alive, and the man they found might know.

'Please... Gwin has been good to me, but I must know if my father lives.'

<rgb=#FF0000>If you accept this quest, you will be teleported to the Ox-clan merchant-camp outside Isengard in Nan Curunír. You may wish to take the quest Slipping Through the Fingers of the White Hand from Gwin before accepting this quest.</rgb>'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you have returned my son to me! He was foolish to strike out on his own, but this place is as safe as any in these days.

'You have brought me hope when I had none. Thank you!

'Now I think that Mabon has something to say to you.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for bringing me to my father... I did not hope that it was he who had escaped! Will you make the Wizard pay for betraying us?

'Oh, it matters not! I am with my father!'Rohirrim scouts have discovered other medallions upon the Khundolar sorcerers that are similar to that which you found.Khundolar sorcerers can be found throughout the Brown Lands and at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to find some of the other medallions his scouts reported seeing.Collect light blue medallions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg.

You should bring the medallions you found to Céola.'So, ${PLAYER}, that medallion you found turns out to be an insignia for their order, which they call the Blue Caste. However, our scouts have reported seeing other medallions that are similar, but not exactly the same.

'Would you go forth and find some of these medallions? Undoubtedly, you will find them upon the persons of the Khundolar sorcerers.''Gather for me medallions belonging to the Blue Caste....''These medallions name the sorcerers you defeated as members of the Brotherhood of the Mind. I daresay this Blue Caste must be fractured in their disciplines...perhaps if there are other factions, we may put them at odds one with the other.'Rohirrim scouts have discovered other medallions upon the Khundolar sorcerers that are similar to that which you found.Khundolar sorcerers can be found throughout the Brown Lands and at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to find some of the other medallions his scouts reported seeing.Collect dark blue medallions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg.

You should bring the medallions you found to Céola.'So, ${PLAYER}, that medallion you found turns out to be an insignia for their order, which they call the Blue Caste. However, our scouts have reported seeing other medallions that are similar, but not exactly the same.

'Would you go forth and find some of these medallions? Undoubtedly, you will find them upon the persons of the Khundolar sorcerers.''Gather for me medallions belonging to the Blue Caste....''These medallions name the sorcerers you defeated as members of the Brotherhood of the Spirit. I daresay this Blue Caste must be fractured in their disciplines...perhaps if there are other factions, we may put them at odds one with the other.'The Brown Lands were once a green land, lush with vegetation, until war and corruption turned them into a desolate waste-land.Discover the camps and sites of the Brown Lands.Discover EtheburgDiscover HelstorDiscover LashkargDiscover the Desolation of the GardensDiscover the Stone-holeThe Khundolar fly the banner of the Great Eye in open demonstration of their service to the Dark Lord...in apparent disregard to the mandates of their mysterious master, Yirokhsar.Banners of the Great Eye can be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

Dagbert asked you to enter Lashkarg and burn the banners of the Great Eye.Burn banners of the Great Eye at Lashkarg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagbert is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg.

You should return to Dagbert with news of your success.Talk to Dagbert at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'The Khundolar have the gall to fly the banners of the Dark Lord at Lashkarg. I have heard that they serve Mordor in direct disregard for the mandates of their master, a man who calls himself Yirokhsar the Blue, a sorcerer of no small power, they say.

'We should show this Easterling rabble that the Riddermark does not fear the Dark Lord...would you enter Lashkarg and burn the banners of the Great Eye? That should dishearten them, at the very least.

'If you would do this, you should leave at once.''Dagbert said what? Of course, we fear the Dark Lord...we do not serve him and will fight him -- or would, if Gríma Wormtongue did not hold the king's ear -- but fear him, we do.

'Alas, I fear nothing good will come of this.''Y-you live? You are a wonder to behold, and that is for sure!

'Good work, ${PLAYER}!'The Khundolar fly the banner of the Great Eye in open demonstration of their service to the Dark Lord...in apparent disregard to the mandates of their mysterious master, Yirokhsar.Banners of the Great Eye can be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

Céola asked you to enter Lashkarg and burn the banners of the Great Eye.Burn banners of the Great Eye at Lashkarg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg.

You should return to Céola with news of your success.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'In view of Dagbert's treason, we are forced to deal with the Khundolar at once. We must find a way to discourage them...and I may have it.

'The Khundolar fly the banners of the Dark Lord at Lashkarg. I have heard that they serve Mordor in direct disregard for the mandates of their master, a man who calls himself Yirokhsar the Blue, a sorcerer of no small power, they say.

'Perhaps if we burn these banners, we can convince them that the Eye is not greater than the Mark, and they will depart. I hold no great hope of this, but should you accomplish this deed return to me with the results.''Alas, it is as I expected. They were not deterred.

'Thank you, nonetheless, for your valiant efforts.'Ondor spoke of a goblin-captain which they refer to as the Captain of Fangs... perhaps a Warg-rider or commander of the Warg-forces in Nan Curunír.The Captain of Fangs is in the stockade, north of Ondor. It can best be reached through the caves behind the stockade.

Ondor has asked you to defeat the Captain of Fangs, a goblin Warg-rider of fierce renown and the leader of these goblins.Defeat the Captain of FangsOndor is encamped south of the stockade.

You should return to Ondor and tell him that the Captain of Fangs is no more.Talk to Ondor in Nan Curunír'I finally found the goblin in command. He is up in that stockade to the north. It's a bit tricky to get in there without being spotted by the guards though... your best chance may be to sneak in through the caves behind the stockade.

