'Well, in any case, keep dismantling any of these devices that you come across. Nothing good could be coming out of Orthanc.'Dagoras saw a strange figure creeping about in southern Nan Curunír, but soon lost its trail.Dagoras is at his camp in Nan Curunír.

You should speak with Dagoras to discover what clues he can offer to help find the strange figure's trail.Talk to Dagoras at his campDagoras is at his camp in Nan Curunír.

You should speak with Dagoras about the mysterious executioner who attacked him.Talk to Dagoras at his camp'Be wary, ${PLAYER}. A short while ago, I saw a strange figure moving south towards the pass, but it disappeared before I could determine who or what it might be.

'Stranger still, it left no trail that I could follow. I do not know what became of it.''There are not many who can so easily evade my eye. I fear that this individual may have some sinister purpose in mind... we should redouble our efforts to discover what that is.''Well, ${PLAYER}, you have my gratitude and then some. It has been a while since I have allowed myself to be caught unaware, and I feel more the fool for it... but I am still alive and that is something, at least.'Dunland is a large and wild land, inhabited by good and wicked folk alike. You should explore the many landmarks of Dunland.Explore the BonevalesExplore CarreglynExplore the DunbogExplore the GravenwoodExplore the HeathfellsExplore the IsendaleExplore Nan CurunírExplore Pren GwydhExplore the StarkmoorExplore Trum DrengYou have explored the length and breadth of the Great River lands on your trek into the south, towards the open plains of Rohan.Carreglyn has many places to explore.Find Lower BarnavonFind Upper BarnavonFind Naur-maudhûlFind the Barnavon MineFind Hen TurrauFind Lhun AvancFind Munfaeril's ShrineNan Curunír has many places to explore.Find the Gates of IsengardFind the Pillar of the White HandFind the Fang-rider's WarrenFind the Blackmarch FortFind Quickbeam's GroveFind Dagoras' CampPren Gwydh, home of the city of Galtrev, has many places to explore.Find the Fanged LairFind Bloodtusk's DenFind the Galtrev Lumber-campFind the Dragon-clan SettlementFind the Howling CavernsFind Rook's HutStarkmoor has many places to explore.Find AvardinFind Flam-cadlusFind Cartrev AndrasFind the Hound's RestFind the Culling PitFind the Overlook of Wulf's CleftThe Bonevales has many places to explore.Find the Bone QuarryFind Plas-maruFind Echad NaeglancFind Lhan BachFind Lhan GogledhDunbog has many places to explore. As you tread through the swamps, be careful to stop and smell the sulfur.Find Lhan ColvarnFind Lhan RhosFind The Withered StonesFind DurgorsFind The Pristine GladeThe Gravenwood has many places to explore.Find the Tree of TributeFind the Mustering TreeFind the Rohirrim Scout-campFind the Slade of ShadowsFind Uvel-cadlusFind Rhuvel-cadlusFind Ak-ghruThe Heathfells have many places to explore.Find Grimbold's CampFind Dol BaranFind River-watchFind the Pit of IronFind the Slave StockadesFind the SmeltersFind the UnderworkingsIsendale has long been on the edge of border skirmishes between the Rohirrim and Dunlendings, and has many places to explore.Find ForthbrondFind CuvnerthFind ÂthdârFind BrôntrigTrum Dreng, home of the Stag-clan, has many places to explore.Find Dire HollowFind the Herd-landsFind Lhan TarrenFind the North PassFind the Watch-towerFind the White Hand OutpostYou have found the body of a fallen Rohirrim scout in the southern part of the Vale of Nan Curunír.The personal effects of the Rohirrim scout are scattered about the area in Nan Curunír.

You should collect the personal effects of the fallen Rohirrim scout.Collect Rohirrim helmCollect Rohirrim spearCollect Rohirrim shieldDagoras is at his camp in Nan Curunír.

You should bring the fallen rider's personal effects to Dagoras.Bring the rider's effects to Dagoras at his camp in Nan CurunírThe body of a fallen Rohirrim soldier lies here, recently slain in battle. Grimbold had ordered that none of his warriors should enter Nan Curunír, so it is something of a mystery how this poor fellow came to his fate here.

There is no way you can return the fallen warrior's body to Grimbold's encampment, but if you could gather his effects, you have no doubt that they would be much appreciated. Unfortunately, they seem to have been scattered about in the chaos of whatever pursuit claimed his life.'What is this? The belongings of a fallen Rohirrim warrior... I see. I will see to it that Grimbold or one of his men receives these.

'I do not know what brought that warrior up here, though I suspect he was trying to find out where some of the horses stolen from the Rohirrim were taken.'You discovered a number of unimagineably old ruins within the Limlight Gorge. They appear to be Elvish, but it is impossible to say what age they may have hailed from.Erymeldir claims to know little of the ancient Elvish ruins within the Limlight Gorge, saying that they were abandoned even before he was born

He suggested that you may want to ask Ordhrien about them as she is a good bit older than he.Talk to Ordhrien'Oh, you noticed those old ruins out there in the Gorge did you? I must admit, they are from before even my time, so I know little about them.

'You could ask Ordhrien about them, she is a fair bit older than myself and may know more.''Erymeldir said that you should ask me about those ruins?

'His ignorance has less to do with his tender age than it does with his flighty nature and lack of interest in anything that does not catch his fancy at the moment.

'Any child of Lórien could have told you what they were, for once they were part of Lórien itself, long ago.

'If you wish to know more about them, you should speak with the Gorge itself, for fragments of the spirits that once dwelt there with us yet remain, for those who know what to look for. Return to the Gorge by starlight and look more closely at those faded lights you have seen in your wanderings, and you may learn of its past.'Fangorn itself is being destroyed by Saruman and his war-efforts. You have been sent to destroy his lumber-camp and the forces there.Defend Fangorn from the press of Saruman's foul 'industry' and destroy the Wizard's forces there.Save Fangorn from Saruman's forcesSaruman has reinforced the edge of Fangorn with some of his toughest forces. You and your fellows must stop the lumber-camp from destroying Fangorn and the Ents that protect it.Work your way up the side of the hill and to the edge of the Fangorn. Defeat all the enemy forces that stand in your way. Protect the Ents!Save Fangorn by destroying Saruman's forcesUnnerved by the knowledge that the wild cats were trained to attack the Rohirrim, Twiga seeks to remove or lessen that threat.Wild cats can be found throughout the Brown Lands and at the Khundolar encampment of Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg.

Twiga has asked you to hunt the wild cats of the Brown Lands and bring him their fangs as a testament of your valour.Collect wild cat fangs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Twiga is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg.

You should bring the fangs you collected to Twiga as a token of your valour.'I must confess, the knowledge that these cats are trained to attack us is quite unnerving. The Khundolar did not come unprepared, that is for certain.

'For this reason, we must seek to remove -- or at the very least lessen -- the threat the wild cats pose to us. Will you go forth and hunt the beasts? Bring me their fangs that I may know the number you have slain.''Bring me the fangs of the wild cats, ${PLAYER}.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}, but I fear not well enough. However, I have a plan which may prove a greater boon to us.'Finnvarth, companion of Armund, is lost somewhere near the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge. Armund claimed that he was searching for likely stands of lumber that could be cut once the dwarves get the mill working again, but he has not turned up for several hours.You should find Finnvarth the dwarf and help him get back to the mill.

Armund suggested that he should have been exploring somewhere not far to the east of the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge.You should speak with Finnvarth at the Limlight Gorge sawmill.Talk to Finnvarth'Our youngest companion, Finnvarth, wandered off hours ago.  He said he was going to check out some stands of lumber nearby.

'I have not heard back from him since, and I expect the young fool has gotten himself lost. If you want to make yourself useful, you can go find him and show him the way back to the mill.''My thanks to you again, but Armund did not believe a word of my tale. He says that I have been sneaking from the kegs before heading out and tripped on some bramble.

'Bramble! The nerve! If he were not my second cousin, I would knock him upside the head with a keg....''Have you found Finnvarth yet?''Finnvarth is a fool.'The Pits of Isengard is a dangerous place filled with all kinds of Orc-kind. Defeat the Fire-orcs...as many as you can!To earn this deed, you must defeat as many Fire-orcs as possible inside the Pits of Isengard.To earn this deed, you must defeat as many Fire-Orcs as possible inside the Pits of Isengard.Defeat Fire-orcs in the Pits of Isengard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Captain Agelbrit claims that a pair of Elves from Lothlórien passed by his guard-post in the dark of night, heading down towards the far end of the Limlight Gorge. What business would the servants of the Sorceress of the Golden Wood have in the Limlight Gorge?You should speak with Galadriel's envoys in the Limlight Gorge.

Captain Agelbrit says the Elves were last seen headed down towards the far end of the Gorge.Talk to OrdhrienYou should ask the Ents of Fangorn what troubles have beset them recently.Talk to ThickbarkGreylimb waits with Thickbark beside the river.

You should speak with Greylimb about his illness.Talk to GreylimbErymeldir waits beside the river.

You should speak with Erymeldir and learn if he knows a remedy for the Ents and their trees.Talk to Erymeldir'Greetings. You must be ${PLAYER}. The Lady Galadriel suggested that we might encounter you and your friends here.''A few days ago, we saw a pair of Elves headed down into the Gorge under cover of darkness. They did not seem to be trying to hide, but by the time we noticed them they were already well past us...we did not dare go after them.

'The way they were dressed, I would say they must have been servants of the Sorceress of the Golden Woods to the north. I have no idea why they would come down here, though, and as long as they stay away from Stangard, I am not of much mind to interfere with them.

'Still, it is my duty to keep an eye on what is going on down there, so if you should happen upon them -- and survive -- I would be interested to know what those two are up to.''You may want to find the Elves who passed into the Gorge.''The Rohirrim asked you to learn our purpose here? I do not suppose that it occurred to them to just ask us themselves? It is for the best, I suppose. The Men of Stangard have long held a great fear of our people in their hearts...and in truth, we do not discourage this. It helps dissuade them from intruding upon our forests without the need for cumbersome treaties or shows of force.

'We have come to speak with the ancient Onodrim of Fangorn...the Ents. Have you met one in your travels before? We hope to convince them of the need to rouse themselves from their long peace, lest the course of the world pass them by still asleep here in their deep forest.

'Alas, it seems that they already face their own concerns, and I cannot convince them to aid us. I think you should speak with them yourself...perhaps you and your allies may be able to help us resolve this situation?''Greetings, little ${RACE}. Hoom, you have come at a strange time, hoom-hom, strange indeed. Why, we have not had so many guests beneath our boughs in many years. Ta-rum! Perhaps since I was an Enting even. Perhaps never before? It is hard to say.

'It is sad, then, that you come to us with such troubling tales. Of war, of sorrow, of the ancient Enemy returned. I would tell you to go, that my people have already had their fill, hoom! All the memories of war that we could ever desire and many that we would forget. We would remain here in our forests while such sorrows exhaust themselves in the outside world, and we endure.

'But they have already come, ta-rum, or so it seems. My companion Greylimb has fallen ill, and that is a rare thing indeed for my folk, unless the winter should bite so deep that our bark cracks in the cold. Hoom-hom! Something has sickened him in a way we do not understand, and some of the trees have likewise grown ill here on the edge of the Forest.

'I can feel it now too, it is as if some poison has seeped into the very ground beneath our roots...but from where? We do not know. Hoom, Greylimb may be able to tell you more, if he feels up to speaking.''What is this? Hoom-hom, more of the little folk among us? How queer, how queer indeed. Would that I felt fit for company, but I fear I am not. Not at all fit, I am afraid. Ta-rum! I feel as weak as an ancient fir facing his last storm.

'Nay, I am not that old. Why? Do I look it? If you had asked me a little while ago, I would have said that I felt up to another Age at the least! But not anymore. Now, I feel mighty old indeed. Hoom! I just hope the beetles do not notice. Detestable things, beetles.

'It is something in the roots I would say. That is where it started, sort of a strange tingling in the water. An odd taste, but I did not think much of it. I like to take my drink down by the river you see, each morning. But I noticed that the trees...they were not looking so well. Hoom-hom, it was not long before I felt ill myself.''I have considerable learning as a healer, and I examined Greylimb. I must admit my knowledge fails me when dealing with these creatures. 

'Anyhow, I expected to find that he had been poisoned -- likely by some vile effluent dumped into the river by Orcs in the Misty Mountains or the sort -- but now I believe it to be venom from a creature.

'I do not know how such a venom might have found its way into the Limlight, yet its source cannot be far off, for such venom does not keep its nature long.

'The only hint I have seen of such would be the spiders that hunt the northern edge of the Gorge. But what spider would prey upon trees...or would dare to prey upon the Ents?'Defeat the Wraiths of Fornost and free Deadmen's Dike from Angmar's influence.Complete Fornost -- Wraith of WaterComplete Fornost -- Wraith of EarthComplete Fornost -- Wraith of FireComplete Fornost -- Wraith of ShadowDefeat Megoriath, the Wraith of Water, to unlock the Gate of Earth.Complete Megoriath, the Wraith of WaterDefeat Rhavameldir, the Wraith of Earth, to unlock the Gate of Fire.Defeat Rhavameldir, the Wraith of Earth, to unlock the Gate of Fire.Complete Rhavameldir, the Wraith of EarthDefeat Brogadan, Wraith of Fire, to unlock the Gate of Shadow.Defeat Brogadan, Wraith of Fire, to unlock the Gate of Shadow.Complete Brogadan, Wraith of FireDefeat Rhavameldir, the Wraith of Earth, and his minions.Defeat Rhavameldir, the Wraith of Earth, and his minions.Complete Rhavameldir, the Wraith of EarthComplete Challenge: Pillars of EarthComplete The Jern-elygComplete Weapons of WarDefeat Brogadan, Wraith of Fire, and his minions.Defeat Brogadan, Wraith of Fire, and his minions.Complete Brogadan, Wraith of FireComplete Challenge: Into the FireComplete Leaders of OrcsComplete Idols of SauronDefeat Remmenaeg, Wraith of Shadow, and his minions.Defeat Remmenaeg, Wraith of Shadow, and his minions.Complete Remmenaeg, Wraith of ShadowComplete Challenge: Light in the DarkComplete Ambassadors from AngmarComplete Free the FallenDefeat Megoriath, the Wraith of Water, and his minions.Defeat Megoriath, the Wraith of Water, and his minions.Complete Megoriath, the Wraith of WaterComplete Challenge: The Deep EndComplete The Forgotten CompanyComplete The BrackGerfinn, another companion of Armund, has gone somewhere to the north of the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge. Armund needs him back at the mill to help finish the repairs.You should find Gerfinn the dwarf and help him get back to the mill.

Armund believes he headed roughly north of the sawmill to look for materials of some sort.You should speak with Gerfinn at the Limlight Gorge sawmill.Talk to Gerfinn'Now Gerfinn is gone as well! Can you believe it? These dwarves would lose track of their own heads if they were not stuck in place! I expect some Orc or goblin would solve that problem for them in no time if they did not have me to help guide them....

'Gerfinn was heading to the north to look for some materials, but I need him back here to help get this place fixed up, or we will never get it running.''Have you found Gerfinn yet?''Gerfinn is a fool.''${PLAYER}! You believe me, do you not? Armund will not listen to reason!

'You saw it, did you not? Staring at me like that, hungry-like... its eyes like knotholes, its sap dripping like the saliva of a wild beast, its foetid breath like a musty summer breeze... I cannot stand to recall it.

'You have got to help us! Armund does not know what they are like! He has not seen their dark hearts. They are likely to devour us all the moment we drop our guard!

'Shhh... they are right outside, listening... waiting....'Many valuable relics of old were lost in a battle that took place long ago in the Dunbog. It is often said that night-time fishing excursions will produce ancient and wonderful gems that enhance powerful items.Bron is in Galtrev.

You should speak with Bron to begin your fishing expedition in the Dunbog.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must have the fishing hobby trained in order to complete this quest.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>Talk to Bron to travel to the DunbogBron is in Galtrev at the milestone marker in the centre of town.

You should speak with Bron to collect your reward.Talk to Bron in Galtrev'Battles were once fought in these lands among great Men, ${PLAYER}, and relics from the swords of the dead fell to the earth. In most places, the gems have long since been picked up by greedy fingers, but the pools of the Dunbog have been known to be rich with glinting treasures, lost in the deep mud.

'If you go to the Dunbog at night and try your hand at fishing there, you may pull up many great treasures that will improve your gear.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must have the fishing hobby trained in order to complete this quest.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready to travel to the Dunbog, ${PLAYER}?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must have the fishing hobby trained in order to complete this quest.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'You were a great help to the peoples of Dunland, ${PLAYER}! Please, choose a reward as a token of Galtrev's gratitude.'Wargs allied with the goblins haunt the western reaches of Nan Curunír, much to Ondor's chagrin.Wargs roam the western reaches of Nan Curunír.

Ondor is concerned that, left unchecked, the Wargs will eventually converge on his location.Defeat Isen Wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ondor is encamped near the caves in western Nan Curunír.

You should tell Ondor that you have managed to defeat a fair number of the Isen Wargs.Talk to Ondor in Nan Curunír'Where there are goblins, there are almost certainly Wargs. And this place is no exception.

'Those accursed Wargs are everywhere around here. We must thin out their numbers before they smell us out and hunt us down.''That is one more pack of the flea-bitten beasts that we will not have to worry about. Good work, ${PLAYER}.''Have you dealt with the Wargs yet?'Wherever war and violence lash out, goblins are there to cackle while they reap the plunder from the chaos.Defeat goblins in DunlandWherever war and violence lash out, goblins are there to cackle while they reap the plunder from the chaos.Defeat goblins in DunlandAn enormous breed of evil spider has taken up residence in the Limlight Gorge. These gorge-crawlers hunt along the northern ridge of the Limlight Gorge, searching for unwary prey. Those willing to hunt such monstrosities must be stalwart, well-armed, and travel in bands if they hope to survive many encounters with these horrors.

The soldiers of Stangard have taken to using the spider's silk as a replacement for bandages for those who are injured, but it has become too dangerous to gather.You should gather webs from the gorge-crawlers and gorge-lurkers that hunt the northern ridge of the Limlight Gorge.Collect gorge-webs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the webs you collected to Captain Agelbrit at the Limlight Gorge guard-post.'I suppose that you have had some fortune fighting those spiders down there.

'We once gathered the silk of the Gorge-spiders for a number of things -- bandages in particular -- when we were short of cloth. It works remarkably well.

'Since those huge ones showed up, though... well, we have not been able to go down there safely since. If you can gather some of that silk for us, it would be a great help. I do not think we are going to be getting any supplies from Edoras any time soon, from the sound of it.''Have you collected any spider-webs yet?''You managed to gather some of those webs? Thank you. These can stop bleeding faster than any normal bandage in a pinch, you know.'The half-orcs in Dunland all hail from Isengard, where they strive to carry out Saruman's plan to oppress his neighbours.Defeat half-orcs in DunlandThe half-orcs in Dunland all hail from Isengard, where they strive to carry out Saruman's plan to oppress his neighbours.Defeat half-orcs in DunlandSomeone has posted a task to collect knotted heartwood from Huorns. They can be turned in at any task-board in Great River.You have accepted a task to acquire knotted heartwood.Wanted: Knotted Heartwood from the Huorns in the Great River region. Collect them and deliver them to a task-board in Great River to earn favour with the Heroes of Limlight Gorge.Wanted: Knotted Heartwood from the Huorns in the Great River region.You have turned in the knotted heartwood for a modest reward at the local task-board.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect thick branches from Huorns. They can be turned in at any task-board in Great River.You have accepted a task to acquire thick branches.Wanted: Thick Branches from the Huorns in the Great River region. Collect them and deliver them to a task-board in Great River to earn favour with the Heroes of Limlight Gorge.Wanted: Thick Branches from the Huorns in the Great River region.You have turned in the thick branches for a modest reward at the local task-board.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Céola is concerned that the brigand threat in the Brown Lands will make it impossible to even attempt to hinder the Khundolar.The brigand hideaway is located somewhere in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to scout the first patrol point for the location of the brigand hideaway.Scout the first patrol pointThe brigand hideaway is located somewhere in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to scout the second patrol point for the location of the brigand hideaway.Scout the second patrol pointThe brigand hideaway is located somewhere in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to scout the third patrol point for the location of the brigand hideaway.Scout the third patrol pointThe brigand hideaway is located somewhere in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to scout the fourth patrol point for the location of the brigand hideaway.Scout the fourth patrol pointCéola is at Etheburg, south of Helstor, in the Brown Lands.

You should return to Céola with news of your success.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'Our scouts have been too frightened by the creatures of the Brown Lands that I think they have not been thorough in their patrols. We have yet to learn the location of the brigand hideaway here.

'However, I deem we must find it soon, for if the brigands are not dealt with, I fear it will be impossible for us to even attempt to hinder the advance of the Khundolar.

'Would you make a patrol of the Brown Lands and see if you can learn the location of the brigands' encampment? You need not engage the enemy...only learn their location.''Very good, ${PLAYER}! This Helstor must be where the brigands are delivering the relics they have stolen from Parth Celebrant. Though I must admit, the size of the encampment is frightening.

'What is this? You have seen Lashkarg, the war-camp of the Khundolar? Your description is fearsome...even with the brigands disposed of, I am concerned. I think it best if we leave the Easterlings alone for the present.''Have you found the brigand camp yet?''Have you found the brigand camp yet?''Have you found the brigand camp yet?''Have you found the brigand camp yet?'Dagoras saw a group of figures passing in the night, leading Rohirrim horses up into the hills of western Nan Curunír.The horses were taken into the hills of western Nan Curunír.

Dagoras asked you to find out where the stolen horses had been taken.Find the missing horsesOndor is encamped near the caves of western Nan Curunír.

You should tell Ondor that the goblins have been stealing horses and other livestock to feed the Wargs.Talk to Ondor in Nan Curunír'Last evening, I spotted a number of horses being led past... by goblins, I think, though it was a dark night, and I could not make out the figures clearly. The horses seemed wild and upset, and there were lower, stockier creatures around them -- Wargs, most likely.

'If I had to venture a guess I would say it was a party of Warg-riders back from a raid on the Rohirrim encampments near the Ford, returning with stolen horses.

'I am curious where they were taking the poor beasts, for horses have no love of goblins and will not permit them to ride.''Have you found the missing horses yet?''So that is where the poor beasts were being taken? A goblin slaughter-house.

'Dwarves have little love of full-grown horses, but I would not wish that fate on any creature, hooves or no.'The Ents of Fangorn have asked you to gather seeds from the wild and dangerous Huorns of the Limlight Gorge.Thickbark has asked you to gather seeds from the hostile Huorns growing on the Gorge side of the Limlight River and to drive the dangerous creatures back into slumber if you can.Collect Huorn-seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the Huorn-seeds you have collected to Thickbark at the Limlight Glade in the Limlight Gorge.'Hoom. Your tales of wild trees on the far side of the river are troubling. It has been some time, ta-rum, since a shepherd of the forest has been over there... the Huorns there must have long ago grown wild and dangerous.

'Yet I recall them from when I was an Enting, and would have them rest, if they can, and see their seedlings grow in a more peaceful place where we can watch over them. Hoom-hom, if you could bring me a few of their seeds, I would be much obliged... though it is likely that they will not let you gather them peacefully.

'Simply fend them off and wear them down if you can... often when a Huorn becomes exhausted in battle, it may fall asleep, becoming much like any other tree for a time.''Hoom, have you gathered the seeds?''Ah... seeds from old friends, long missed. You have my thanks.

'Some day, when things are more peaceful once more, we must find the time to try and tame them again... or help them sleep peacefully.'You have travelled by boat down the Anduin in the company of Nona, Horn, and Corudan, but must camp for the night before you proceed further.Corudan is waiting to speak with you beside the river where you have stopped for the night.Talk to CorudanHorn and Nona are sitting on opposite sides of the camp-fire by the Anduin.Talk to Horn by the camp-fireTalk to Nona by the camp-fireCorudan is sitting by the camp-fire.Talk to Corudan by the camp-fireCorudan is sitting by the camp-fire.Talk to Corudan and decide upon a tale to shareHorn is sitting by the fire.Talk to Horn by the camp-fireListen to Horn tell his story of King Fengel.Listen to Horn's storyHorn is waiting to finish the story of King Fengel and Wyrgende the crone.Talk to Horn by the camp-fireNona is sitting by the camp-fire, waiting to tell her story.Talk to Nona by the camp-fireNona is telling a story by the camp-fire.Listen to Nona's storyCorudan is by the camp-fire, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Corudan by the camp-fire'We will leave at first light. For now you should get some rest.

'In the morning we will continue our journey down the Anduin.''That is far enough for today, ${PLAYER}. Horn has already seen to the fire, so now we may sup and take some rest before the night-watches begin.

'We will leave in the morning, at first light. It is not good to travel further south on Anduin at night, unless the need is considerable. The waters become treacherous the nearer you get to Sarn Gebir.''You are fortunate to have friends among the Elves, ${PLAYER}. I would not want to make this journey without a guide, and Corudan appears to know what he is doing.

'But it is not seemly for a Man of Rohan to mingle with Elves, as you saw in Stangard. Of his kind my people have little to say but this: "long-lived and dangerous."

'They have more to say of the folk of Dunland, but none of it is kind and I will not disturb the girl's ears with any of it. I regret Nona's ill welcome at Stangard when she had need of aid, though I understand its root. Her people and mine have a long and unhappy history. I have no quarrel with her personally, but our shared friends and duties make us allies, nothing more than that.''The Elf-queen was right to send this guide with us, ${PLAYER}. He knows the waters and how to keep a boat afloat, which is more than the daughter of Suvulch knows. Were it up to me, I would lead us south on dry land, with springy turf underfoot and no fear of foundering.'

Nona lowers her voice, a rare event for the Dunlending woman.

'The boat is not large enough to keep us from speaking, ${PLAYER}, but as you saw, this horse-lord managed to avoid addressing me in any way once we were on the river. If he has a grievance with me, tell him to air it so I may respond appropriately: with words or with Wadu's sword! I have become tired of his ability to look all around him but not in my direction, whatever direction that happens to be!''We have some time before we should begin the night-watches, ${PLAYER}. Would you find some tale-telling agreeable? I find that the weaving of a good story among companions around a fire can be a pleasant way to pass the time.

'Have a seat and listen, ${PLAYER}. I will begin, and perhaps our companions will have a tale to share as well.''Do you have a story to share?''I shall go next. My tale concerns King Fengel of Rohan, the grandfather of Théoden King. It is a sad tale, given the happenings of late, but you may find it interesting.''This is what she carved into the stone:

'Feckless Fengel, fool I name thee,
Grief shall be the get of thy greed.
No lord of your line shall long live,
Upon thy seat no son shall settle.
Kin and kingdom your craving hath killed,
Until the might of the Mark is mended.
Wyrgende.'

Horn sighs heavily and continues.

'King Fengel was furious, and he ordered Wyrgende's body burned and the stone destroyed, but no man of his company could move her, and every hammer and mattock they set to the stone shattered on contact.''I do not have the flowery words or turns of phrase that Corudan and this man Horn have, ${PLAYER}. I write my tale in the hide of my enemies, with Wadu's sword as my quill!''I think that is enough tale-spinning for one night, ${PLAYER}. I will take the first watch, and I will wake you when it is your turn.

'We will set out again at first light.'You prepare to assault the Khundolar war-camp of Lashkarg in hopes of driving them back from Rohirrim territory.Fight your way through the first ward of Lashkarg and defeat its captain.Fight through the second ward of Lashkarg and defeat its captain.Fight through the third ward of Lashkarg and defeat its captain.Fight through the fourth ward of Lashkarg and defeat the commander of the Khundolar.For centuries the Mearas have freely roamed the plains of Rohan, bowing only before the kings and princes of the Rohirrim.Shadowfax is waiting for you here in the fields of Rohan. Shadowfax has led his companion here to wait for you, though the companion is not yet aware of why he came to this place.Approach and listen to Shadowfax and his companionShadowfax awaits you on the border of the eastern fields of Rohan.Approach and listen to Shadowfax and his companion'Welcome back, my brother. He who rides me, Gandalf, is right to say that you are a descendant of the Mearas. I summoned you here to remind you of your true home.

'A darkness spreads over the lands. Soon, a time shall come when the herd will need to ride again. Return to us, when you are ready.'You and Bingo have uncovered an Easterling plan to attack the outpost of Stangard.Sabert is at the entrance of Stangard, ready to prepare for the Easterling attack.Talk to Sabert within the entrance of StangardBingo is just inside the entrance to the outpost of Stangard.Talk to Bingo and learn what tasks he will handleLanghár is just inside the entrance to Stangard.Talk to Langhár and learn what tasks she will handleThere has been a loud commotion to the south-west. Is the Easterling attack underway?Investigate the commotion to the south-westSabert has been stunned into silence by the appearance of Landroval, but you need him ready for battle: the Easterlings have begun their attack on Stangard!Talk to Sabert in StangardBingo has returned from his errands, and is ready to participate in the battle... which is now concluded!Talk to Bingo in Stangard'If the battle has already happened, I suppose we accomplished what we set out to do, ${PLAYER}!''I cannot stop thinking about that Beorning woman! She cut a most impressive swath through the Easterling invaders, did she not? Such strength and ferocity!''We may not have much time before the Easterling raiding party attacks Stangard. We must make the most of the time we have available if we are to be prepared!''Finally, a task for which I am well-suited, ${PLAYER}! I will take care of the dirty dishes, and you can handle some of the tasks that require heavy lifting!

'I will find you when I have finished!''I am not doing any of those things, ${PLAYER}.''What a creature, ${PLAYER}! I have never seen anything that might hope to compare! To think that such a majestic creature could come to the aid of my people... it defies expectation!

'And this woman, this Beorning. She too fights for Rohan? We will stand together, ${PLAYER}, and cast back our foes! From this point forward, we stand as friends and allies!''That Beorning woman really is something, isn't she? Did you see the way she fought? Such strength and ferocity! I must admit that she put even my own skills to shame!''What's that? The battle has already happened? I thought I heard something over the splashing of the suds, but I told myself it was simply my imagination!

'At least the dishes are clean. Still, it would have been exciting to see Landroval and Langhár in action! I do not mean to discount your own contribution, ${PLAYER}... I know you are quite impressive in battle yourself!'The town of Floodwend has been besieged. You must do everything in your power to drive back the evil forces of Isengard and Mordor and save the town from imminent doom!Speak with Elfhelm before you. He will lead the way to the gates of Floodwend!Objective 1: Speak to ElfhelmElfhelm has asked you to ride and push back the enemy forces.  The horses are dead, reinforcements are ariving late, and only you can stop the threat.Objective 2: Ride out and trample the unmounted forces.Continue through the valley. You must chase down the Nazgul rider.Objective 3: Defeat the enemies on the roadContinue through the valley. You must chase down the Nazgul rider.Objective 4: Defeat the remaining enemies on the roadAt the end of the valley, waits the Nazgul rider.  Defeat him and reclaim Floodwend for Rohan!Objective 5: Defeat the NazgûlSpeak with Elfhelm again.Objective 6: Speak with Elfhelm'Grimbold told us he would send help.  You are it?  Where are the Riders of Rohan? Is there no one else who will come to our aid?  

'You must succeed where othere could not, then.  You must drive back the evil of Mordor itself.  These forces are driven by a dark rider.  Come with me to the gates.  Then we ride from there!''You were a blur of blade and hoof.  Your prowess will be recorded this day!  Floodwend is in your debt. You have the gratitude of all of Middle-earth!'Many valuable relics of old were lost in a battle that took place long ago in the Dunbog. It is often said that night-time fishing excursions will produce ancient and wonderful gems that enhance powerful items.Franis is waiting for you in the Dunbog.

You should speak with Franis.Talk to Franis to continue through the bogAvanc circle the pools in which a soggy Relic of Strength might be found.

You should defeat the avanc so that you can fish in peace in the pools.Defeat the avanc at the first poolA soggy Relic of Strength can likely be found in the nearby pools.

You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.Fish up a soggy Relic of StrengthFranis is waiting for you to speak with him again.

You should talk to Franis; his knowledge of the Dunbog will steer you to the most promising pools.Follow Franis to the turtle-guarded poolsThe turtles roam the pool that Franis led you to.

You should defeat the turtles that romp in this area so that you may fish in peace when all is done.Defeat each of the turtlesA muddy Seal of Patience can likely be found in the nearby pools.

You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.Fish up a muddy Seal of PatienceFranis is waiting for you to speak with him again.

You should talk to Franis; his knowledge of the Dunbog will steer you to the most promising pools.Talk to FranisElhudan circle the pools in this area of the Dunbog, casting their fell light upon your wary faces.

You should defeat all of the elhudan in this area.Defeat all of the elhudan around this poolA glinting Relic of Inner Fire can likely be found in the nearby pools.

You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.Fish up a glinting Relic of Inner FireFranis is waiting for you to speak with him again.

You should talk to Franis; his knowledge of the Dunbog will steer you to the most promising pools.Talk to FranisSlugs slither around the pools to which Franis has led you.

You should defeat all of the slugs of this area before you attempt to fish here.Defeat all of the slugsA worn Relic of Time can likely be found in the nearby pools.

You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.Fish up a worn Relic of TimeFranis is waiting for you to speak with him again.

You should talk to Franis; his knowledge of the Dunbog will steer you to the most promising pools.Talk to FranisFranis has led you to a pool that is surrounded by menacing bog-lurkers.

You should defeat all of the bog-lurkers so that you may fish in peace.Defeat all of the bog-lurkers in this areaA dripping Relic of Cunning can likely be found in the nearby pools.

You should use your fishing skill to try to snag a relic.Fish up a dripping Relic of CunningFranis is waiting for you to speak with him again.

You should talk to Franis; his knowledge of the Dunbog has steered you successfully to the most promising pools.Talk to Franis'Are you ready to travel back to Galtrev? I will have you there before you can snap your fingers. Come, follow me.''I can help you pick a path to the best fishing pools, ${PLAYER}. Just stay close and do not stray. I might not be able to help you fight, but I do have a knack for finding relics.''Come along, ${PLAYER} -- there is no time to waste! The next pool is this way. Oftentimes, there are rather menacing turtles in that area, but hopefully they will not be there.''Let us keep moving, my friend. The night is not growing any younger, and I would like to dry my feet before the sun comes up.''I hope you are not tired! There are still more pools to fish from tonight. Follow me, and keep up!'Are you ready to move to the next pool? Follow me closely, and I will lead you there now.''You are quite the fisher-${RACE}, ${PLAYER}! And a warrior also -- I would be happy to scout these parts with you any time you want it. You have quite a talent for hooking the lost valuables. I hope your catch will be of great use to you.'You are returning with Nona to Stangard, in order to regroup and plan your next move.You are walking through the Rushgore with Nona when she stops and wants to talk to you about something.Talk to Nona in the RushgoreYou are making your way through the Rushgore with Nona.Walk with Nona through the RushgoreNona is standing on a small rise amidst rocks in the Rushgore.

Some terrible presence has come near to you in the Rushgore.Talk to Nona atop the rocky rise in the RushgoreAn evil presence has come to the Rushgore, and you are in great danger!Survive your encounter with great evil in the RushgoreThere are Easterlings in the mists of the Rushgore, and something worse beside!Survive the Easterling ambush and prevent any of them from alerting their fellowsAn Easterling has attempted to escape, and you need to defeat him before he alerts his fellows.Talk to the Khundolar CaptainNona is somewhere in the Rushgore, and it sounds like she's in trouble!The Nazgûl stands atop the hill. You need to find a means of driving it off!Nona is somewhere in the Rushgore, and it sounds like she's in trouble!Find Nona! She is in grave danger!You have brought Nona to Stangard, but do not know if the Rohirrim will be able to save her life.Bring Nona to Stangard for the healing she needsYou have brought Nona to Stangard, but do not know if the Rohirrim will be able to save her life.Talk to Nona where she lies in StangardHorn is waiting to speak to you about the price for healing Nona.Talk to Horn in StangardNona is struggling to speak.Talk to Nona where she lies in StangardHorn is waiting for your answer in Stangard.Talk to Horn in StangardYou have come to seek the aid of Galadriel. Will she give it?Travel to Lothlórien to seek the aid of GaladrielHorn is standing uncomfortably in Lothlórien, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Horn in LothlórienGaladriel has come to speak with you about Nona.Talk to Galadriel in Lothlórien'There is clearly some glamour on this land. I feel as if I could take on any foe and achieve victory, or cross any landscape, no matter the obstacles!

'Your Elf-witch works wonders! Only song could do justice to her powers of healing! The relief I feel is... it is overwhelming, ${PLAYER}. The girl will live!

'Unless it is rude to ask it, I would like to return to the forest floor now. I will return to Stangard by myself, but I would like to see you again! Once the girl is recovered, bring her as well. If I am to compose a song of your adventure, I will need both of your accounts, after all.''We have a long way to go, ${PLAYER}. As much as I wish we did not need to refuge at the town of the horse-lords, it seems we must. We have lost the trail of this creature, this wraith of which you speak, and until we can learn where it has gone we are only wasting time.

'It is frustrating to know our purpose and be unable to accomplish it!''Something is near, ${PLAYER}! It must be the wraith we have sought... it makes my blood run cold!'

Nona looks at you with wide eyes, and you are suddenly reminded that she has not had much experience with creatures of such evil. She puts her hand on the hilt of Wadu's sword, her sword, and her former fright is replaced with grim determination.

'We found it. Now what do we do with it?''I will not run from you. I am your better. My people have powerful friends. I will show them how strong a man of the Khundolar can be!'Nona lies crumpled on the ground before you, soaking in the blood from a sword-wound in her side. She struggles weakly to speak.

'${PLAYER}... are you...?'

The effort is too great for her; she needs the aid of a healer if she is to survive this wound. In the back of your mind, one worrying question refuses to go away. From what blade did she take this wound? Did an Easterling blade cause this injury, or was it the blade of the Nazgûl?

You prepare yourself for the long journey back to Stangard with Nona.'${PLAYER}... is everything... all right?'

Nona's breathing is ragged and shallow, and the gash in her side still bleeds around the cloths with which you tried to staunch it.

When you brought her to Stangard she was barely conscious. You found Horn near the entrance and begged for his people to tend to Nona's hurts. He sought out the leader of Stangard to see what could be done, and has not yet returned.'I did my best for you, ${PLAYER}, but you are not going to be pleased. He did not understand why we should heal the hurts of this Dunlending girl.

'Eventually he relented somewhat, and he has agreed that our healers will do what they can for the girl.''Do not... let them...'

Nona struggles to speak, but the effort is too great for her to make out the words. She beseeches you with wide eyes, but you cannot meet her stare. Your gaze keeps returning to the blood soaking the floor beneath her.

She tries again.

'Wadu's... it was...'

You cannot give the Rohirrim what they demand. There has to be another way to save her life.'There has to be some other way, ${PLAYER}. You spoke of the Elf-witch in the woods to the north along Anduin. My people shun that place as a den of evil glamour, but... if there was a power that could heal this girl...'

Horn glowers at you, his eyebrows knitted together angrily.

'A pox on her! I will not have her blood on my hands, or on her own. Lead us to this Elf-witch, ${PLAYER}! I have heard the tales. Perhaps she will be unable to bewitch me if I am expecting it! Why did you ever bring this girl to Stangard, ${PLAYER}? This is not her place.'

Horn gazes into the middle distance, and in a quiet voice he continues.

'In Stangard, is a sword valued more highly than the life of a girl? What sort of man would willingly serve in such a place?'

He shakes his head, and the urgency returns to his voice.

'Well? For what are you waiting? Let us go at once!''I will never call my people distrustful again, ${PLAYER}. The blindfold felt somewhat unnecessary to me. Only the most urgent of need has driven me here, and I would not want to return!'

Horn's face softens, and his brow creases with worry.

'Do you think the girl will recover? I saw the way those Elves looked at her wound. Whatever they saw there, they did not like it. If it was not an Easterling blade... what does that mean for her? What is wrong? ${PLAYER}?''The danger has passed, ${PLAYER}. The wound was deep, but it did not fester. And yet, I did not wish to leave this girl to the care of my healers. The risk that her wound was caused by a morgul blade, and that she could become a wraith like the creature you encountered that night, compelled me to heal her hurts personally. If that had proven the case, I would have ended her suffering. It would have been a mercy, and necessary to safe-guard Lothlórien and indeed all lands.

'Do you think me cruel? I am glad it did not come to that. I do not believe her wound was caused by a morgul blade, and it is my hope and belief she will live. I am... surprised. We will speak more of it later, away from watchful ears.

'The girl Nona is sleeping. When she is awake you will be brought to her. For now you should rest, ${PLAYER}. Dream no troubling dreams! In Lothlórien your rest will be peaceful. I am certain of it.'The Shakh-hai of Isengard have come to claim the last wood standing in Nan Curunir -- Quickbeam's grove.

You must aid in its defence, and ensure that none escape to warn Saruman of the presence of an Ent so close to Isengard.Speak with Quickbeam.Talk to QuickbeamSpeak with QuickbeamTalk to QuickbeamHIYAY WE WONTIME TO LEAVEYou have come to Lothlórien with Nona to learn the meaning behind your curious dreams.Haldir is in the woods of Lothlórien.Talk to Haldir within LothlórienHaldir is in the woods of Lothlórien, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Haldir within LothlórienNona is in the gardens of Galadriel, and wants to speak with you.Talk to Nona in Galadriel's gardenGaladriel is waiting to speak with you in her gardens.Talk to Galadriel and describe to her your dreamAgainst all your hopes, Gandalf has returned!Gandalf is in Galadriel's garden, waiting to speak with you.Talk once more to GandalfGaladriel is in her garden, waiting to speak with you.'I did not expect you in Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}. What need has driven you hither, when so many need your help elsewhere?'

You relate to Galadriel the troubling images you beheld while dreaming in Grimbold's camp, but your spirits fall when she betrays no sign of understanding.

'Your dreams are your own, ${PLAYER}. I had nothing to do with these images you saw.''I will send for Alfrohir to bring you down the river to Thinglad, ${PLAYER}. Gandalf believes a great evil harries our absent friends. Perhaps your presence on the banks of the Anduin can prevent it from discovering or endangering them.''We have both been through a great deal since last we met, ${PLAYER}, and neither of us is the same person we then were. I do not have the time to tell you what befell me since we parted, but know this: the Quest remains. Your dream tells Galadriel more than she lets on, and it tells me more yet. Our friends face a grave danger along the Anduin. I hope it is not too late for them to avoid it.'

Gandalf's eyes seem to pierce you, and you shiver uncomfortably; there is something unfamiliar in the Wizard's bearing. He reminds you of Saruman.'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. It is good to see you. There is just so much that needs to be done! The Eagles have proven able companions to me in these dark days. Gwaihir has agreed to bear me where next I need go, and his brother Landroval has been keeping his sharp eyes on the Anduin. Would that I could be everywhere!

'I fought against fire and shadow in the depths of Moria and on the peak, and when returned to this world I faced another foe from afar. These deeds have left me tired, and I will not speak of them now.

'We will speak again, ${PLAYER}, if our deeds prove fruitful. If they do not, well...'

Gandalf trails away. Suddenly, with a blaze in his eye and a tone of mirthful anger, he continues.

'Perhaps they would have proven enough had we not stood around talking about them for so long, my sentimental ${RACE}! We have our own tasks now... let us get to them!''Guide your friend well, for I will not be responsible for any injuries she suffers while blindfolded. This is the law of the Golden Wood. No outsiders must see the secret trails of Lothlórien. It is out of respect for you, ${PLAYER}, that I permit even this.

'Follow me with care.''All right, I think this is far enough. You may remove the blindfold now, and I will bring you to the Lady Galadriel.''This land is a pretty one, as these Elves seem fond of saying, but this is what the daughter of Suvulch has to say: the hills of Nan Laeglin at sunset are more beautiful by far.

'I submitted to the binding of my eyes for your sake, ${PLAYER}, and to learn the secret behind your dream, but do not expect it again. I will leave this land with my sight unhindered, or these Elves will learn a sharp lesson at the point of Wadu's blade.

'Where is this Elf-queen?''I do not know what to think of this Galadriel, ${PLAYER}. Her words are fair, but beneath the surface she wields strength to match even the fiercest warrior of my people. I am... surprised.

'Let us do as she says, and perhaps the answer to the riddle of your dream will be revealed along the Great River.'Théodred's host has been driven back from the gates of Isengard in disarray, and pockets of Rohirrim are fighting for their lives as they retreat.You have come down the road in retreat with Grimbold, and he has put up his hand to stop you.Talk to GrimboldYou have retreated further down the road and are once more embroiled in the fighting. You must buy Théodred as much time as you can!Fight off the attacking forces in order to buy Théodred precious time to retreatGrimbold has fought off his opponent and wants to speak with you while he catches his breath.Talk to GrimboldThe men are disorganized and in chaos, and Grimbold wants to gather them together for one last stand.Talk to GrimboldA rider has brought disturbing news: a second force of uruks has left Isengard in secret and has driven the defending force at the Ford of Isen back into Rohan.Talk to Grimbold'We are doing well, ${PLAYER}! Every second we give to Prince Théodred is a second unwasted! So long as we stand, Rohan stands with us!''They will be on us in moments, ${PLAYER}. Let me gather the men about us and ready them for this last assault.''A thousand curses upon Saruman! He sent a second force of uruks to the Ford on the other side of the river! We have to get back to the Prince at once! Without Cadda at the Ford, Prince Théodred cannot drive them off with the few men he has in his party!''We cannot die here! We have to get back to the Ford at once to save Prince Théodred! He will be caught between the hammer and the anvil of Saruman!''This is far enough, ${PLAYER}! Let us turn and face our pursuers! We must give Prince Théodred some time to move further south!'You have returned with as much haste as you can to the Ford of Isen and must now try to save Prince Théodred from the forces of Saruman.Grimbold needs you to fight alongside him to where Théodred is suffering the fierce attacks of Saruman's forces.Talk to GrimboldPrince Théodred is in trouble on the eyot in the middle of the Isen! You need to fight alongside Grimbold to come to the aid of the Prince!Talk to Grimbold on the bank of the IsenYou have come to the eyot in the middle of the river Isen and have found the uruk Morflak gloating over Théodred's fallen form.Confront MorflakYou have come to the eyot in the middle of the river Isen and have found the uruk Morflak gloating over Théodred's fallen form.Talk to MorflakMorflak's attention is drawn to the eastern bank of the Ford, but before you can take advantage of his inattention, you are yourself rooted to the spot with wonder.

A line of riders has come from Rohan, and the courage of the uruks melts away as the Rohirrim prepare to charge.'${PLAYER}! I thought we would not meet again. The old man was not pleased to lose you as his guest, and he was very cross with Morflak. But in his wisdom he sent me forth to gain his forgiveness, and with a simple mission!''Death to the forces of Saruman! Death to them all! Quickly, ${PLAYER}, we must get to the water's edge and see what has happened to the Prince!''There is no time, ${PLAYER}! Prince Théodred is beset on all sides! We have to cross the river and break through the ring that surrounds him!'The sun rose on the Twenty-fifth of February, and Théodred and Grimbold made final preparations for a daring strike on the forces of Isengard.Théodred is waiting to speak with you on the eyot in the middle of the Isen.

It is dawn and nearly time to begin the daring strike on Isengard. Théodred is waiting to speak with you before his host rides north.Talk to Théodred on the eyot in the IsenThéodred has given Cynstan a message to deliver and is waiting to speak with you again.Talk to Théodred on the eyot in the IsenCynstan is on the eyot in the middle of the river Isen.Talk to Cynstan on the eyot in the IsenCynstan is in the middle of the Ford. He is concerned about something and wants to speak with you.Talk to Cynstan in the middle of the FordCadda is on the east bank of the Ford, and he wants to speak with you.Talk to Cadda on the east bank of the river IsenCynstan is on the east bank of the river Isen and wants to talk to you.Talk to Cynstan on the east bank of the IsenThéodred is on the eyot in the middle of the river Isen. Cynstan has asked you to tell him that the Ford will be in Cadda's capable hands while the Prince rides to Isengard.Cross the Ford of Isen once more and speak with Théodred on the eyotThéodred has asked you to mount your steed and talk to Grimbold when you are ready to ride to Isengard.Mount your steed and talk to Grimbold when you are ready to rideYou have travelled up the road towards Isengard with the host.Travel up the road to IsengardYou have travelled up the road towards Isengard with the host, and Grimbold wants to speak with you.Talk to Grimbold on the road to IsengardYou have come part of the way up the road to Isengard, and now Théodred is waiting for the return of his scout. You should speak with the Prince.Talk to Théodred on the road to IsengardThe scout has returned from Isengard and brings word to Théodred that the number of Orcs and half-orcs outside the walls is not to be feared.

Théodred wants to discuss this report with you.Talk to Théodred on the road to Isengard'I should not be left behind! My place is at the front of the column with my Prince!'

Cadda's eyes flash angrily at you from beneath the rim of his helmet.

'I will do as I am commanded, but I wish it were not necessary. My men will hold the Ford against whatever comes, as my Prince desires. But I think we wait here uselessly, while our brothers and our friends ride into battle against the armies of Saruman.

'I understand the need for it. But I chafe at that need and do not want to sit here in idleness while Prince Théodred rides into danger!''I hope you don't mind getting your feet wet again, ${PLAYER}. Cadda is on the east bank of the river, and the stones can be treacherous.''You have come a long way from your homeland, ${PLAYER}, and you have seen a great deal of danger. These battles in which you have fought...when you were embroiled in the thick of them, were you frightened? I cannot ask this of the men, they would think me a coward.

'But I am already frightened, and we have not yet begun to march!''I did tell the Prince that Cadda would not be happy about staying here. You heard me tell him that.

'I am going to stay here for a few minutes and see if I can find my missing bracer. You should cross the Ford again and tell the Prince that the Ford will be defended while we are away.''Let us ride together, ${PLAYER}! Let us bring news of our defiance to Saruman himself!''It is a pleasant morning for riding, ${PLAYER}. If it stays thus, we will be at Isengard by mid-day and have brought Saruman to heel not long after!

'Let us catch up to the Prince and get a good view of the road ahead.''I hope you have awakened refreshed, ${PLAYER}. I doubt not this will be a long day. I have a few matters left undone, which must be resolved, then we will ride.''All is ready, then? Cadda will hold the east bank of the Ford with the men at his command, and the rest of us will ride north to Isengard. The Éored will follow my lead, and Grimbold will dismount and command the foot as a separate unit if the terrain off the road warrants it. Athelard will call the mark for his archers.

'It will be some hours before we are in sight of Isengard. It is best we get started.''Cadda is a man of Rohan and will understand what is needed of him. I will not advance through the front gate to victory while leaving the postern gate open to the enemy; someone must stay to hold the Ford in the event I have misjudged Saruman's mind.'

Théodred lowers his voice and addresses you quietly.

'You should go with Cynstan to deliver my words, ${PLAYER}. He is untested by battle, and the men see him still as a green boy. Cadda may be less bristly towards my esquire if you are there as well. I need a word with Athelard before we go. He is not pleased at the quality of the spears we have, but it is too late to make more. They will have to suffice.''We are nearly there, ${PLAYER}. I can smell the stench of Isengard even from here.''This news lightens my heart, but we must not forget that Saruman is devious. This strike will remind him we are not to be lightly set aside and that he is not immune to attack. Any more than that is more than I expect.

'The dawn has passed. It will be mid-day when we move to the next stage of my plan. Ready yourself for what comes next, ${PLAYER}.''We have several hours' ride ahead of us, ${PLAYER}, then we will see if Saruman is prepared to face me in battle, or if he will cower behind his walls in perpetual caution.'Prince Théodred and his host have come to the gates of Isengard, and it is now time for his daring strike to begin.Théodred is waiting to address his assembled men, and you should speak with him.Talk to ThéodredPrince Théodred has asked you and Grimbold to cut through the brush on the eastern side of the road to attack the half-orc flank.Talk to Grimbold at the head of the hostRungar has arrived on the flank of the main host, and you should speak with him.Talk to RungarBefore the gates of Isengard, the Rohirrim led by Théodred have come under attack by an overwhelming force of Saruman's uruks.

