'Our riders have managed to net some of our foes! Attack the netted uruks and keep them from breaking through!

'I will try to drive some of the others away!''Prince Théodred has routed the enemy! Victory is ours! ${PLAYER}, Grimbold, come with me, and we will send them howling back into the Ring of Isengard! We will send them back to Saruman!''Hildred spoke true. There are Orcs outside the walls, but their numbers should not be a problem for us, ${PLAYER}.

'Let us see what they think of my riders!''Are you ${PLAYER}? You are! We have to get out of here!'

Shouts of despair and cries of terror rise from the pockets of Rohirrim still fighting for their lives. The archer looks at you with fear in his eyes and throws his bow down in the dust.

'The day is lost! There are too many uruks!'

The men begin to break for the road back to the ford, and all sense of order is lost as the uruks gather on all sides.'We will cut through the brush on this side of the road, ${PLAYER}, and attack our enemies' flank!'The servants of Isengard want revenge for the uprising of the people of Galtrev.You should talk to Bron.Talk to BronDefend Galtrev from the White Hand forces.Defeat the Uruk-hai master and his forcesBron is in Galtrev.Talk to Bron'We will await your return and welcome you as a friend.''Saruman's Orcs have come to burn out the village. There are many people inside... we must defend them!''Thank you, Duvodiad, for your aid... the people of Galtrev are in your debt.'Saruman is attempting to forge legendary weapons of his own to get the upper hand in his war against the Horse-lords of Rohan.Enemies in the employ of Saruman can be found throughout the Forges of Isengard.Defeat the Orc-smiths of Saruman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the Uruk-hai Slave-masters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the Master of the ForgeYou have come to the very gates of Isengard in the company of one of Théodred's emissaries, hoping to discover at last Saruman's purpose for meddling in the conflict between the Dunlendings and Rohirrim.Escort Ordwaer to the gates of Isengard.Talk to OrdwaerSpeak with Ordwaer before the gates of Isengard.Talk to OrdwaerObserve the confrontation between Ordwaer and Saruman.Observe Ordwaer's challengeOrdwaer's nerve appears near to broken beneath the power of Saruman's voice. Speak with him and try to bolster his resolve.Convince Ordwear to persistObserve Ordwaer's confrontation with Saruman.Observe Ordwaer's challengeSpeak with Ordwaer about his conversation with Saruman.Talk to Ordwaer'I must return to the Ford now, ${PLAYER}.

'I wish you would not remain here in this forsaken place, but you have your own business to be about.

'May fortune ride with you!''Grimbold told me that you were last seen heading into Nan Curunír, ${PLAYER}, but I confess I did not expect to encounter you here.

'While I was sent alone to avoid raising the ire of Isengard, I have had a distinctly unwelcome feeling since I entered Nan Curunír, and I think I should welcome some company before I reach the gates of Isengard.''What is Saruman thinking? To yoke trolls -- ever the servants of the Dark Land -- to his cause?

'I had feared that he had some ambition to bring Dunland under his sway, but this....''Saruman is right... if the power of Mordor is rising, we should not be here. It would be best to leave the Ford to the wild men and reinforce Meduseld....'

...

'You do not believe him? Surely, Saruman means to aid Rohan in this dark hour... and we see here that his strength is considerable.'

...

'It may be as you say, and the darkness of this place brings doubt to my heart. Do we dare trust our borders to this Wizard, who so hides his purpose behind strange and perilous guardians?''I will convey Saruman's message to Théodred, and I hope that he will follow Saruman's advice, but I do not think he will.

'I fear we are destined for war, no matter which way we turn.'The Fellowship of the Ring has come at last to the ultimate decision: the East road or the West?Aragorn and the rest of the Fellowship are camped on Parth Galen, in the East Wall.

