'Your valour continues to amaze me, ${PLAYER}. You have my gratitude and that of the Men of Stangard.'Gnarlstump is angered by the presence of trolls in the Brown Lands, especially the desolation of the Entwives' gardens, and wishes them removed.Gozug can be found deep within the troll-infested Stone-hole, north of Gnarlstump's camp.

Gnarlstump has asked you to defeat Gozug, chieftain of the wild trolls of the Brown Lands.Defeat GozugGnarlstump is at his camp, south of the Stone-hole.

You should return to Gnarlstump with news of your victory.Talk to Gnarlstump in the Brown Lands'Ta-room, ta-rum, little ${RACE}! If we cannot move the trolls out by force, perhaps they will depart if their chieftain is slain.

'There have been whispers on the winds of a great wild troll named Gozug, who dwells in the Stone-hole. Would you enter that foul cave and defeat him? Perhaps then the trolls shall depart this place.''Ah, this was a good deed, little ${RACE}. Trolls are a bad lot, to be certain. Ta-rum!''Defeat Gozug, and it may be that the trolls will leave this place.'When the odds are against you and the battle seems lost, can you rally and find a way to win?  Defeat the final bosses of the instance with just one Ent standing. Be a true hero!To earn this deed, you must defeat the three trolls with only one Ent left alive.To earn this deed, you must defeat the three trolls with only one Ent left alive.Defeat the three trolls with only one Ent alive<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Complete Limlight Gorge Explorer DeedComplete The Spirits of the Limlight DeedComplete Ancient Ruins of the Limlight DeedComplete Quests of the Limlight Gorge DeedEarn Kindred standing with the Heroes of Limlight Gorge<rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Defeat Dargnákh.<rgb=#00e4ff>Defeat Dargnákh</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Defeat Draigoch.<rgb=#00e4ff>Defeat Draigoch</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Save Fangorn.<rgb=#00e4ff>Save Fangorn</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Defeat Ironarm.<rgb=#00e4ff>Defeat Ironarm</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#FF00FF>Complete five quests and instances to aid those in Isengard.</rgb>Complete five quests and instances to aid those in Isengard<rgb=#FF00FF>Complete five quests and instances to aid those in Isengard.</rgb>Complete Pits of IsengardComplete Fangorn's EdgeComplete Dargnákh UnleashedComplete The FoundryComplete The Tower of OrthancComplete Draigoch's LairComplete Storm on Methedras at the level capComplete Roots of FangornComplete five quests and instances to aid those in Isengard.

<rgb=#FF00FF>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Defeat Gurthúl.<rgb=#00e4ff>Defeat Gurthúl</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Complete the Skirmish - Storm on Methedras.<rgb=#00e4ff>Complete the Skirmish - Storm on Methedras</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Thwart Saruman's plans within the Foundry.<rgb=#00e4ff>Thwart Saruman's plans within the Foundry</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This quest is for Legendary Servers.</rgb>Fight Saruman.<rgb=#00e4ff>Fight Saruman</rgb>Enraged by your attack upon Lashkarg and the death of their chieftain, the Khundolar stage an assault upon Etheburg.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo, but can be run with a Duo as well.</rgb>Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to help the Rohirrim border-guard defend against the Khundolar's retaliation.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo, but can be run with a Duo as well.</rgb>Talk to Céola when you are ready to defend EtheburgCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

You should speak with Céola regarding the victory at Etheburg.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'There are lights in the land, ${PLAYER}. The fires of Lashkarg burn brightly, for the Khundolar prepare to lay siege to Etheburg. You had a mighty victory at Lashkarg, but now I fear we must pay the price for it.

'Will you stand with us and defend Etheburg? If we can rout the enemy here, then we may actually survive this war!

'If you do wish to help us defend Etheburg, speak with me again, and we will go to prepare ourselves.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo, but can be run with a Duo as well.</rgb>'Ah, ${PLAYER}, we were fortunate to survive that attack; however, I think the Khundolar will be unable to attack again for some time.

'Thank you for your courage and your weapon!''Good! Then let us prepare ourselves for battle!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo, but can be run with a Duo as well.</rgb>The Limlight Gorge has always been a wild and sparsely inhabited area, but since a band of trolls came down from the Misty Mountains, what few inhabitants there were have fled its rocky slopes. Massive creatures now inhabit the Gorge, making travel through the area perilous, and it is said that even the trees themselves sometimes move about, perhaps thanks to some strange magic from the neighbouring forest of Fangorn....Explore the Limlight Gorge in Great River.Discover the Limlight Gate-houseDiscover Limlight FallsDiscover the Ent-groveDiscover the Fallen Watch-towerDiscover the PotholeDiscover the Prospector's ShackDiscover the Old SawmillEver since the Brown Lands became the barren waste-land they now are, brigands have used them for a hideaway from those who would seek to bring them to justice.Brigands can be found at Helstor, north of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

Céola has asked you to defeat brigands at their encampment in the Brown Lands.Defeat brigands at Helstor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, south of Helstor.

You should return to Céola with news of your success.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'You have found the brigands' hideaway, and that is a small victory for us. We must move quickly to render them useless to the Khundolar. They fancy themselves the lords of the Brown Lands... but whether this land holds any value or not, it belongs to the Lord of the Mark.

'Let us deliver this message to the brigands at Helstor. Enter therein and defeat many of their fellows. That will be a harsh lesson to them, but an effective one, I think.''Have you dealt with the brigands yet?''You have delivered a mighty blow against the brigands, but not one strong enough to remove their threat, I wager.

'Nevertheless, I thank you.'The Draig-lûth have been hauling treasure into hills of Thrór's Coomb.The Draig-lûth can be found in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith.

Frithgeir asked you to search the Draig-lûth in Thrór's Coomb to see if you can find a map indicating where they are taking their treasure.Collect a map from the Draig-lûthFrithgeir is at Zudrugund in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith.

The map is full of scribbles and nonsense. Perhaps Frithgeir will be able to help you decipher it.Show the map to FrithgeirNár is in the library at Zudrugund in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith.

Frithgeir examined the map and found nothing he could decipher. He suggested you bring it down to Nár in the library and see if he could make anything of it.Show Nár the map you foundFrithgeir is at Zudrugund in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith.

Nár mumbled what seemed to be a bunch of nonsense while scribbling on the map. Hopefully, Frithgeir can help to translate the mad dwarf's ramblings.'The past few months, during the night, the Draig-lûth have been hauling bags and crates through the forests of Thrór's Coomb. The weapon you told me about must have fallen out of them.

'I have not yet been able to determine where they are taking their goods, though. I have watched them wander the hills, criss-crossing back and forth, looking or searching for something as they go. I wonder if they do not know where they are going either.

'Head down into the hills and forest below and see if you can find the Draig-lûth. Perhaps one of them may have a map that shows where they're going or will give us a sign to pursue.''If we don't know where they're going with those bags and chests, we can't do anything.''I do not know what this means. It's indecipherable to me. Nothing more than scribbles and nonsense. These symbols here -- a fish and a volcano -- seem to refer to things that aren't even in Enedwaith let alone Thrór's Coomb. 

'Perhaps Nár will be able to tell us more, presuming he is lucid. I suppose there's nothing to lose. Bring it down and show it to him, and let's see what he says.''I cannot make heads nor tails of this map. We have no choice but to see if Nár can be helpful.''Fire burns over a sea of gold beneath the rising sun. Teeth, scales, claws... ripping... rending... tearing....''Teeth, tails, claws, scales... and fire... terrible, roaring fire.''If this is what he said and wrote, Nár must not have been having one of his lucid moments. This makes almost less sense to me than what we started with. Allow me to think for a moment.'Dagoras told you that an oddly intense dwarf passed by his camp a short while ago, leaving a message for you. He asked you to meet him by a set of caves to the north-west to 'Have some fun.'The dwarf Dagoras spoke of can be found near some caves some distance to the north-west of Dagoras' camp.

The dwarf that Dagoras described is reminiscent of Ondor, whom you met in the Heathfells.Talk to the dwarf Dagoras spoke of'${PLAYER}, what know you of dwarves in this place? I must say I was taken aback by a fellow who came by here unexpectedly. He claimed to know you and said that you should meet him near some caves some distance north-west of here to... how did he say it? "Have some fun?"

'I will warn you, there is a den of goblins up that way.''Have you found the dwarf yet?''Ah, ${PLAYER}, fancy us meeting in a place like this! But then, where else would we find enough goblins to make sport of?'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Complete Volume III, Book 6: Mists of AnduinBy completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Creatures of Angmar.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me in peace!'By completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Free Peoples.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me in peace!'By completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Creatures of Angmar.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me in peace!'By completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Free Peoples.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me in peace!'By completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Creatures of Angmar.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me in peace!'By completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Free Peoples.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me in peace!'By completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Creatures of Angmar.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me in peace!'By completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Free Peoples.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me in peace!'By completing this quest, you will gain rank amongst the Creatures of Angmar.'So maggot, you want to be ranked up a bit? Well I'll allow it, but just this one time. Don't get used to it!''Alright, here you go. Now leave me alone!'This will grant you what is needed to participate in mounted combat across Rohan.Speak to Shempf.Speak to Shempf'Hello, little one. Have you come to learn the ways of mounted combat? Speak to old Shempfy again and you will be ready to go!''Oh, you're still here? I was distracted by the sound of the wind.  Here we are, you'll be ready for mounted-combat in no time!'You have been sent for training in the handling of a Rohirrim warhorse by the riding instructor Seoca upon the Tourney Field south of Harwick.Speak with Seoca at the tourney field directly south of Harwick.Complete the riding course upon the tourney fieldSpeak with Seoca to complete your war-steed training.Speak to Seoca at the Tourney Field'You'd like to try the training course again? Of course, let us get right to it.''You are ready now ${PLAYER}. Your skills in battle are already formidible. With one of our finest steeds beneath you, you shall be undefeatable!

'Trust in your mount and in your valour, and your banner shall wave above these fields as a beacon of hope for all the Free Peoples of Middle-earth!

'Now I believe you should speak with the Thane of Harwick before you proceed further. Much is a afoot in our lands, and it would be best if you made your presence known to our local lord.''Come with me, we've little time to waste, so lets be about our business.'Gnarlstump is angered by the presence of trolls in the desolation of the Entwives' gardens and the Brown Lands.Trolls can be found throughout the Brown Lands, in the desolation of the Entwives' gardens, and the Stone-hole, north of Gnarlstump's camp.

Gnarlstump has asked you to defeat trolls in the Brown Lands.Defeat wild trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gnarlstump can be found near the desolation of the Entwives' gardens in the Brown Lands.

You should return to Gnarlstump with news of your victory against the wild trolls of the Brown Lands.Talk to Gnarlstump in the Brown Lands'Hoom! Hom! It is an outrage, little ${RACE}! Trolls -- such abominations -- have made a home in the gardens of the Entwives and freely roam the Brown Lands.

'Ah, ta-rum, I must calm myself. It would not do to be too hasty, but it is hard not to be roused. Trolls were made in mockery of Ents by Morgoth himself, if you did not know.

'Would you go forth and defeat a few of the terrible beasts? They should know, at least, that the Ents have not forgotten this land.''Hoom, now, that is a fine tale you tell. I would be pleased if all the stone-mockeries were felled, but I do not see that happening any time soon....'Ondor has warned you against underestimating the Warg-matron. She has a hungry brood of pups every bit as vicious and hateful as she is.The Warg-matron can be found in the caves of western Nan Curunír.

Ondor suggested a way to defeat the Warg-matron, using the deadly spice to subdue her pups by tainting the horse-meat they feed upon.Poison the horse meat and defeat the Black MatronOndor is encamped near the caves of western Nan Curunír.

You should tell Ondor that the Warg-matron has been defeated.Talk to Ondor in Nan Curunír'The evil matron of this particular Warg-pack has unleashed yet another litter of the filthy beasts upon the world. She may not look like much, but when I was sneaking about earlier, I saw her pups strip the flesh off of an entire ox in a just a few minutes... which gives me an idea.

'That evil spice you made... there is a bit left, yes? A light sprinkle of that into the pups' next meal ought to keep them subdued while you deal with their mother!''Well, that should take care of the matron then. I am afraid her pups are probably too tough to expire to a single dose of that spice, but I don't think I could bring myself to kill off a bunch a pups anyway, even if they are Wargs.

'I will regret that in a few months when they are gnawing on my entrails, mind you.'Quickbeam is concerned about the large engines of war that the uruks possess. The enormous bolts they throw could seriously injure even an Ent.The ballistae can be found in the uruk-encampment of eastern Nan Curunír.

Quickbeam asked you to plant seeds beneath the ballistae protecting the uruk-encampment.Plant seeds beneath ballistae (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Quickbeam is at his home upon the north-eastern slopes of Nan Curunír.

You should let Quickbeam know that the seeds have overgrown the uruks' siege-engines.Talk to Quickbeam in Nan Curunír'Though I dare not reveal myself yet, these little uruks are not much of a threat to me, even if their axes do sting a bit... but they have constructed engines that can hurl great bolts, often set aflame. These things could seriously harm even an Ent.

'There are ways to deal with such things, however. Take these seeds -- they have been bathed in one of my Ent-draughts -- and bury them beneath each of their engines. They will not threaten us much longer.''As you can see, trees are strong... stronger than any troll or artifice of the Enemy. Our hands can crush iron and rock when we are roused to anger.

'Soon, the forest will be roused. The trees of Fangorn to the east grow restless as they look down over the ruin of this vale. They will not remain quiet and still forever.'The Shakh-hai of Isengard have come to claim the last wood standing in Nan Curunir -- Quickbeam's grove.

You must aid in its defence, and ensure that none escape to warn Saruman of the presence of an Ent so close to Isengard.Dagoras is at his camp near Isengard.

Dagoras asked you to accompany the Grimbold's emissary to the gates of Isengard. You should speak with Dagoras when you are ready to meet the emissary.Travel with Dagoras to defend Quickbeam's groveDagoras is at his camp near Isengard.

You should tell Dagoras what transpired at the meeting between Ordwaer and Saruman before the gates of Isengard.Speak with Quickbeam'I bear terrible news ${PLAYER} - even now a force of Uruks is approaching Quickbeam's grove.

'I do not think that Saruman yet knows that Quickbeam is there - more likely he thinks it a staging point for our efforts against him - but it is vital that he not learn of the Ent's presence so close to Isengard!

'We must go now to Quickbeam's aid. Your friend Ondor is already there, but there are many of the enemy, and if we do not move swiftly, it shall be too late!'THANKS'Time is of the essence! Let us make haste!'At Ondor's behest, you wrought havoc among the Warg-riders of the White Hand, putting an end to one threat in Nan Curunír.Dagoras mentioned that he was heading north towards the gates of Isengard.

Ondor suggested you rejoin Dagoras.Talk to Dagoras at his camp near Isengard'Well, ${PLAYER}, since we have done what damage we can here, it's about time you meet back up with your friend Dagoras.

'He said he would be headed towards the gates of Isengard and could probably use a hand there.''You should go find your friend Dagoras.''${PLAYER}... so you have made it this far? It is good to see you well, for this vale is treacherous, indeed.

'I have yet to find a way into Isengard unseen, but I have spotted someone unusual headed towards Isengard by the road.

'We will want to watch carefully to see what transpires.'Defeat Orcs in the Great River.Defeat Orcs in the Great RiverDefeat many Orcs in the Great River.Defeat Orcs in the Great RiverOrcs are always evil, no matter whom they serve. The Orcs of Isengard are no better than those who come from Mordor.Defeat many Orcs in DunlandDefeat Orcs in DunlandOrcs are always evil, no matter whom they serve. The Orcs of Isengard are no better than those who come from Mordor.Defeat Orcs in DunlandBrutal Orc-overseers ensure that the Orcs working the engines of Isengard continue their labours without respite or complaint.Orc-overseers can be found throughout Isengard.

Dagoras asked you to defeat the Orc-overseers keeping the labourers of Isengard in line.Defeat Orc-overseers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagoras is within the Ring of Isengard.

You should return to Dagoras with news of your success.Talk to Dagoras within the Ring of Isengard'Do you see those brutes up on the platforms there? Those are the overseers that keep the rest of the Orcs in line.

'Orcs like each other only slightly more than the rest of us, so if there is no one watching over them, they are about as argumentative and lazy as a sack of rats.

'If you can slay those overseers as you make your way through Isengard, it may buy some time for the Rohirrim to gather their strength and their wits.''I am not sure what to make of these Uruks of Saruman's. They may be a greater threat than even the Orcs and goblins.''That should hamper Saruman's plans, for a short time at least.'Parth Celebrant is an old cross-roads and battlefield that holds a long significance to the Rohirrim as the birthplace of their kingdom.Discover the camp-sites of the hobbit pioneers.Discover Idmar's CampDiscover the Field of CelebrantDiscover HordfierdDiscover Ost CelebrantDiscover the Murderous PitThe threat of Saruman's expriments within the Pits of Isengard must be ended once and for all.End Saruman's experiments by defeating both the leader of the Abominations and the leader of the Fire-orcs.Defeat FúshbrafDefeat IronarmAs you progress deeper into the Pits of Isengard, you find yourself faced with a large cave covered in poisonous sludge and the Abominations of Saruman's army.The source of Saruman's Abominations must be destroyed at last.Defeat IronarmAs you progress further into the Pits of Isengard, you find yourself exploring a fiery cave, filled with Saruman's latest creation -- Fire-orcs.Destroy Saruman's Fire-orcs before he can breed more.Defeat FúshbrafBrid has asked you to complete his map by collecting samples from across the Gorge.Brid wants you to finish the mission of his prospectors. You should search for a deep copper vein in the Limlight Gorge to help complete Brid's map. 

Beware of bands of marauding trolls that might be attracted by the sound of your mining.Search for a deep vein of copper oreBrid wants you to finish the mission of his prospectors. You should search for a deep copper vein in the Limlight Gorge to help complete Brid's map. 

Beware of bands of marauding trolls that might be attracted by the sound of your mining.Search for a deep vein of copper oreYou should seek out a deep vein of iron ore to help complete Brid's map.

The trolls seem to have been angered by your activities, so be on guard.Search for a deep vein of iron oreYou should seek out a deep vein of iron ore to help complete Brid's map.

The trolls seem to have been angered by your activities, so be on guard.Search for a deep vein of iron oreYou should seek out a deep vein of silver ore to help complete Brid's map.

The trolls are infuriated and likely to attack in great force should you continue.Search for a deep vein of silver oreYou should seek out a deep vein of silver ore to help complete Brid's map.

The trolls are infuriated and likely to attack in great force should you continue.Search for a deep vein of silver oreYou should let Brid know that you have discovered all three veins of ore, completed the prospector's map, and driven off many of the trolls in the area.Talk to Brid'The map is not complete, alas. We were unable to finish taking our samples from the various areas of the Gorge to judge their value. If you can finish that last part of the task, then the map will be complete...and quite valuable to the right sort of folk!

'The problem is, it was the sound of our picks that brought the trolls down upon us. We had expected some trouble when we started to dig, but there were several of us, and we had no idea that so many might come.

'What say you? You have done so much already...do you think you can finish the task? The risks are great, I am afraid.''You really succeeded? You were able to drive off those marauding trolls and complete the entire map?

'And the veins? Were they as rich and deep as we hoped? This is great news! It will take some time and considerable effort to gather enough men to drive out the remaining trolls and spiders, but with any luck we should be able to open the first mines here within a few years!

'You have my deepest gratitude ${PLAYER}! You and your friends have been a great help to me.''Have you found a deep vein of copper ore yet?''Have you found a deep vein of copper ore yet?''Have you found a deep vein of iron ore yet?''Have you found a deep vein of iron ore yet?''Have you found a deep vein of silver ore yet?''Have you found a deep vein of silver ore yet?'Brid believes that his friends were dragged off into the lairs of a pair of enormously powerful trolls. The last pieces of the map were likely in their possession, meaning you will have to defeat those trolls and search their lairs for the remaining pieces.You must defeat the giant troll Ghâmp in his lair east of the prospector's shack and search for Witmund's remains.Defeat GhâmpYou should search Ghâmp's lair for Witmund's remains.Search for Witmund's remainsHaving defeated Ghâmp, you must now defeat Gank in his lair, west of the prospector's shack and search for Gyrth's remains.Defeat GankYou should search Gank's lair for Gyrth's remains.Search for Gyrth's remainsHaving defeated the two great trolls and recovered the final segments of the map, you should return to the prospector's shack and speak with Brid.'It is too late to save my friends...they were devoured long ago, I am sure, unless they escaped by some miracle, but that is too much to hope.

'As we explored the Gorge we spotted a pair of larger caves...probably the lairs of the larger trolls. I warrant that is where they were dragged off to. If we have any hope of finding the remaining pieces of the map we were making, it would be there.

'Do you...do you really think that you have a chance against those monstrosities?''Have you defeated Ghâmp yet?''Have you found Witmund yet?''Have you defeated Gank yet?''Have you found Gyrth yet?''That is it, then, the last parts of the map. It is not truly complete, of course...we had only finished our initial survey of the area and just begun taking samples of the local ore when we were attacked by that band of trolls.'You have found a lone, surviving prospector from the expedition that came into the Limlight Gorge a month ago. The prospectors made a map of the area, but it was lost along with most of the prospectors when they were attacked by a band of trolls.Brid wants you to take vengeance upon the marauding trolls in the Limlight Gorge and recover the prospector's map.Defeat Marauding Stone-trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect prospector's map-fragments (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Having defeated a number of trolls and gathered several pieces of the map, you should return them to Brid at the prospector's shack.'Thank goodness you have come. It was only a matter of time before those trolls came for me too. They tore all the others apart and took everything. It was a disaster.

'You look to be heroic warriors...please help me avenge my friends and finish the expedition we started. If I can just complete the map we were making, then I could at least sell that to the dwarves or a rich Rohirrim lord and return home.''Have you defeated the trolls yet?''My thanks! You seem to have found some parts of the map, but two pieces are still missing...probably the ones that my friends were working on at the time.

'Two of my companions, Witmund and Gyrth, were helping me lead the expedition and were working on separate sections of the prospecting map. It is probably still with them.

'Sadly, I saw the two of them being carried off to their fates by a few of the trolls leading the attack on our expedition. I suspect they were taken to some dank cave and devoured.

'It seems hopeless now.'Andras, believing he was visited by the Ox-spirit, Munfaeril, in a dream, has asked you to defeat the forces of Saruman, who are clear-cutting the edges of Fangorn.Drive Saruman's forces from the eaves of Fangorn.Defeat Saruman's forces in Fangorn'Hoom-hom, little ${RACE}. We did not expect to meet your kind here. Your help was kind, though hardly necessary. Burárum snap as easily as dry twigs.

