You have seen to the comfort of several injured Rohirrim, and should return to Céolbald.'I am Framric, a man of Rohan proud and true, and I need your help. Orcs have crossed the river, and now they swarm throughout this land, all along the East Wall of my homeland.

'I came south from the Wold with a party of some thirty riders to investigate what could have drawn the Orcs across the Great River. When we arrived, the force was even larger than we expected, and they set upon us. We drove them away, but suffered many losses and our camp is in disarray.

'My people could use your help to restore the camp and make safe the border of Rohan. Go to the south-west, near the passage into the Norcrofts. Make your presence known to my brothers, if you wish to aid us.''My name is Léomund, and I need your help. Orcs have crossed the river! Now they swarm throughout this land, and all along the East Wall of my homeland.

'Thirty of my people rode south from the Wold to investigate what could have drawn the Orcs across the Great River. When we arrived, the force was even larger than we expected, and they set upon us. We drove them away, but suffered many losses and our camp is in disarray.

'My people could use your help to restore the camp and make safe the border of Rohan. Go to the south-west, near the passage into the Norcrofts, and make your presence known to my brothers, if you wish to aid us.''Welcome to Mansig's encampment, friend. We came south from the Wold with a party of some thirty riders to investigate what could have drawn the Orcs across the Great River. When we arrived, the force was even larger than we expected, and they set upon us. We drove them away, but suffered many losses and our camp is in disarray.

