'Just head south along the road. You will not miss Langhold, where Utred is Thane.'Entering the eeries natural caverns that extend beneath the fringe of the Forest of Fangorn, you discovered and defeated the terrible Gurthúl and her brood, thus foiling their attempt to poison the ancient roots of the forest above.To earn this deed, you must defeat Gurthúl.Defeat GurthúlAn ancient evil has burrowed its way beneath the roots of the forest of Fangorn, using labour provided by a band of enslaved Orcs. The leader of these Orcs is Frûshkul, and he must be defeated if you are to reach the spider queen and prevent the roots of the forest above from being poisoned and corrupted.To earn this deed, you must defeat Frûshkul.Defeat FrûshkulThe marshes of the Rushgore have long been uninhabited... or so the border-guard of Rohan believed. Besides wild beasts, villains of a two-legged variety have recently come....Discover the camps and sites of the Rushgore.Discover Aculf's CampDiscover AtburgDiscover WyrmdennDiscover the Creeping MudDiscover Tik BotokhDiscover the Clutch-groundThe Huorns of Fangorn are special creatures. They hold no hate in their heart and must be saved. Save them from the Orcs and their axes!To earn this deed, you must save all eight Huorns in the Fangorn's Edge instance without letting any die.To earn this deed, you must save all eight Huorns in the Fangorn's Edge instance without letting any die.Save all eight Huorns in one runThose who would call themselves the Saviour of the Roots of Fangorn must overcome all of the challenges they face within.Complete all the Deeds within the Lost Temple.Complete 'Slaves of the Spider Queen'Complete 'Roots of Fangorn: Defeat Gurthul'Complete 'Challenge: Roots of Fangorn -- Green Thumb'While accompanying the Ranger Andreg through the Gravenwood, you have completed many tasks.Assist Andreg with Eyes in the ForestAssist Andreg with Grave CorruptionAssist Andreg with Cruel TrapsAssist Andreg with Hunting the PackAssist Andreg with Lost CawsAssist Andreg with Orc-mischiefThe Vale of Nan Curunír lies before you. Tales described it as a lush and green valley, but the devastation stretched out before you tells a dark tale. You must learn more of the land before you proceed further.Nan Curunír lies to the north of the Ford of Isen.

