You should tell Dagoras that many of the White Hand sentries have been driven off.Talk to Dagoras at his camp in Nan Curunír'We stand here on the edge of the Vale of Nan Curunír, at the north end of which lies the stronghold of Isengard. Saruman's schemes hatch from here, and he guards it jealously.

'Nearby, you will find the Pillar of the Hand. Around it are arrayed a number of sentries -- strange and unpleasant, I think they may be more of these queer half-orcs we have been seeing of late.

'They stand watch over the road leading into the Vale, and if we are to untangle Saruman's plots unhindered, we will need to weaken their guard.''Have you dealt with the sentries?''Saruman's remaining sentries will spend more time looking out for themselves than looking for intruders... for a while, at least.'Isengard is littered with strange devices which have some role in Saruman's preparations for war. These machines are frequently maintained by goblins or by human apprentices who have been trained in their operation by Saruman.Saruman's apprentices can be found in Isengard.

Dagoras has asked to you to hunt down any of Saruman's apprentices that you come across in Isengard.Defeat Apprentices of Saruman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dagoras is within the Ring of Isengard.

