'They are some sort of apprentices in Saruman's service. Without them, he will have more trouble running Isengard. Will you see if you cannot deal with a few of them quietly?''It seems like there is no end to those foolish enough to throw in their lot with the forces of darkness.''You managed to deal with a few more of those apprentices? Good.

'I do not know where he procured all of these servants, but Saruman is going to need a fair number of replacements by the time you are through with them.'Defeat Shades in the Great River.Defeat Shades in the Great RiverDefeat many Shades in the Great River.Defeat Shades in the Great RiverNafrati, the leader of the Khundolar Easterlings in the Rushgore, is a merciless and cruel barbarian.To secure the safety of the Woodmen, you should defeat Nafrati.Defeat NafratiThe Ox-clan merchants offered you a gift to aid you in your efforts against Saruman...and the knowledge to use it.The ancient forge of the Númenóreans is at the Ox-clan encampment in Nan Curunír.

Andras gave you a worn Sigil of Orthanc and told you to deconstruct it at the ancient forge of the Númenóreans.Use the Sigil of Orthanc in your inventory'My kindred wish to offer you this Sigil of Orthanc, imbued with ancient power. You may use the forge over there to deconstruct this Sigil, which may grant you a Sigil-fragment that the merchants may take in trade for a powerful necklace.

'Take this Sigil and deconstruct it at the ancient forge of the Númenóreans.'There are many villainous monsters roaming Dunland, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many beasts in DunlandSlay many crebain in DunlandDefeat many hostile Dunlendings in DunlandDefeat many goblins in DunlandDefeat many half-orcs in DunlandDefeat many Orcs in DunlandDefeat many of the Dead in DunlandDefeat many Wargs in DunlandDefeat many Uruk-hai in DunlandIt is an evil sign when the Dead wake from their long slumber to walk the earth again.Defeat the Dead in DunlandIt is an evil sign when the Dead wake from their long slumber to walk the earth again.Defeat the dead in DunlandThere are many villainous monsters roaming the Great River, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many beasts in the Great RiverSlay many brigands in the Great RiverSlay many easterlings in the Great RiverSlay many Orcs in the Great RiverSlay many shades in the Great RiverSlay many spiders in the Great RiverSlay many huge enemies in the Limlight GorgeThe hunter of the Avanc-lûth named Gwin, who brought you safely to Carreglyn through Wulf's Cleft, met you in Galtrev and asked you to seek out a Dunlending who escaped captivity from the dungeons of Orthanc.The escaped Dunlending prisoner is at a camp of Ox-clan merchants outside of Isengard in Nan Curunír.

Gwin asked you to speak with a Dunlending who escaped from the dungeons of Orthanc during your own flight from there with Baldgar, after the Falcon-clan's betrayal.Talk to the escaped Dunlending prisoner in Nan Curunír'Greetings, ${PLAYER}, we meet again. I cannot help but believe the Avanc-gwirod, the great spirit of the Avanc, guided us here for a purpose. Indeed, I have learned through my countrymen and members of the Boar-clan resistance that you have actually been imprisoned within and escaped from the bowels of Orthanc!

'What you may not know is that some of those Dunlending prisoners you aided also survived, and one has taken refuge with some Ox-clan merchants in Nan Curunír. He sends word through the Boar-clan that Isengard has emptied and may be ripe for attack.

'Perhaps you and your friends from the north might be willing to meet with this man and learn his intentions? If so, you may wish to take this boy with you... I found him starving in the wilds of Carreglyn and brought him here, but he claims his father was taken by Saruman and is determined to find his way to Isengard. He will not listen to my reason.''The escaped prisoner has taken refuge among a party of Ox-clan merchants outside of Isengard in Nan Curunír.''Ah, ${PLAYER}... I had hoped you would be among those who might answer my call to arms. When we escaped, I found refuge here among my kinsmen of the Ox-clan. I thank the Uch-gwirod that some of my people still prize loyalty.

'I have seen a great force -- nearly the whole of Isengard's great legions -- march forth from the gates of Isengard. They are marching to the Ford of Isen, where I hope they and the accursed Horse-lords will destroy each other.

'What this means, though, is that Isengard is weak and perhaps ripe for an assault of our own. There is still a strong enough force here that it will take a great many warriors to accomplish the deed, but thanks to you and the Forgoil Baldgar, I have learned the ways into Isengard... and even Orthanc itself!'Defeat spiders in the Great River.Defeat spiders in the Great RiverDefeat many spiders in the Great River.Defeat many spiders in the Great RiverDiscover all of Stangard's interiors.Discover the buildings of Stangard.Discover the Mead HallDiscover the LockhouseDiscover the Skirmish HallDiscover the Auction HallDiscover the Stangard VaultDiscover the Stangard TavernDiscover Stanric's HouseDiscover the Stangard KennelDiscover the Stangard StableDiscover Wada's HouseDiscover the Legendary Item StoreDiscover the Supplier's HouseDiscover the Provisioner's HouseDiscover Byrnstan's HouseDiscover Dunstan's HouseDiscover Uthrad's HouseDiscover Tatwine's HouseDiscover the Abandoned HouseDiscover Adalbert's HouseDiscover Sabert's HouseIfing, one of the guards outside Stangard, had a curious experience and doesn't understand it.Ifing saw a curious figure to the north-west, atop the rising slope in that direction, before he collapsed.

Ifing has asked you to search to the north-west for the hissing figure he saw, if you are not too frightened to do so.Search for the hissing figure north-west of Ifing's locationA booted footprint north-west of Ifing's location, atop the rising slope, bears further investigation.

Ifing was accosted by a hissing figure, and this booted footprint north-west of his location may help you find it.Examine the booted footprintIfing is waiting south-east of the booted footprint for you to report what you found.'Oh... I am sorry... I cannot seem to clear my head...'

Ifing shakes his head as if to try and clear it of cobwebs. He squints at you blearily.

'Where... am I? I saw... something. And then...?'

Ifing tries to focus on your face. He finally manages it, and takes a deep breath.

'It was dark, and I could not see far into the night. But I saw... I saw a figure in the darkness. I thought it was one of my men, returned from a patrol in Eorlsmead, but then it... well, it rather hissed at me. I approached, and demanded that the stranger identify himself, but then everything went black. I fell down, and only now have I come back to my senses.

'The shape came from the north-west, I think, atop that rising slope. You can look for it there, if you like. I will... I will stay here. I am still not right, I fear.''You found a booted footprint? I wonder what it means? Can you tell who it was that attacked me?'

You try to console Ifing and assure him that he is in no more danger, but you have few words of comfort; you know what it is that befell him. Ifing ran afoul of the Nazgûl, succumbing to the Black Breath, the stench of death and foul instrument of the Nine.

He is fortunate the creature must have been hurried for some unknown reason, or he would certainly have been killed. He was lucky, but your fortune seems poor: the whereabouts of the Nazgûl remain unknown to you.'The shape I saw... came from that direction... to the north-west... atop that rising slope.''Did you... find anything? I saw it... to the north-west, atop that rising slope.'This token you found seems to signify some sort of order among the sorcerers of the Khundolar.Rohirrim may be found at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

You should bring the strange medallion to one of the Rohirrim border-guard.This blue token that you found upon a Khundolar sorcerer bears writing that you cannot comprehend. Perhaps someone at Etheburg, the way-post of the Rohirrim border-guard in the Brown Lands, may know something of it.'Hail, ${CLASS}! What have you there? This medallion is of Easterling make, to be sure, but I am not sure what it portends.

'You say that you found this upon one of their sorcerers? Most likely, then, it is a sign of their order....'Scouts report that forces of the White Hand have been seen marching on Galtrev, surely as an act of revenge for what was done to the Overseers of Galtrev.Bron is at Galtrev.

Talk to Bron to defend Galtrev.Talk to Bron to defend GaltrevBron is in Galtrev at the milestone marker in the centre of town.

You should speak with Bron to collect your reward for assisting in the defence of Galtrev.Talk to Bron in Galtrev'Scouts report that strong forces from Isengard are marching upon Galtrev... surely to take retribution for our defiance of the White Hand Overseers.

'Will you help us to defend the village?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Let us prepare for the attack, Duvodiad!''You were a great help against the marauding villains of Isengard, ${PLAYER}! Please, choose a reward as a token of Galtrev's gratitude.'Saruman is devising his own legendary items to supply his war-efforts. His forges must be shut down.Bron is in Galtrev.

You should speak with Bron to travel to the Forges of Isengard.Investigate the Forges of IsengardBron is in Galtrev.

You should speak with Bron to tell her of your success against Saruman's attempts to forge legendary weapons.Return to Bron in Galtrev'Word has come to us that Saruman has taken an interest in legendary weapons for his own armies and has built a great forge full of Orc-slaves for the creation of this dangerous supply.

'He must be stopped! Will you sneak into the forges and defeat his smiths and slave-drivers?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Are you ready to travel to the forges of Saruman? It will be dangerous, but I know that you are a great warrior.''Ah! I am glad to see you whole, ${PLAYER}. Saruman is dangerous enough by himself... but I shudder to think what he would be like towering above a great army of strong Orcs and uruks, each wielding a weapon of superior make.'The Foundry of Isengard houses  the mighty Ring-forge where Saruman plies the knowledge of Ring-smithy he has acquired down through the ages.Thwart Saruman's plans within the Foundry by destroying his Ring-forge and defeating his lieutenants.Thwart Saruman's plans within the FoundryDefeat Dhâr in the Smelting RoomDefeat Gurbák in the Bellows RoomThe Foundry of Isengard houses the great Ring-forge where Saruman plies the knowledge of Ring-smithy that he has acquired down through the ages.Thwart Saruman's plans within the Foundry by destroying his Ring-forge and defeating his lieutenants.Thwart Saruman's plans within the FoundryDefeat Dhâr in the Smelting RoomDefeat Gurbák in the Bellows RoomSaruman has placed two of his most powerful servants to watch the gates of Isengard and destroy any who approach unannounced.Defeat Ufdrágh, Gatekeeper of IsengardDefeat Barashal, Gatekeeper of IsengardGrimbold's emissary has come north to speak with Saruman and demand to know why Orcs and goblins have been seen gathering in numbers near Isengard, and why the Wizard is meddling in the affairs of the Dunlendings and Rohirrim.Dagoras is at his camp near Isengard.

Dagoras asked you to accompany the Grimbold's emissary to the gates of Isengard. You should speak with Dagoras when you are ready to meet the emissary.Talk to Dagoras to accompany Grimbold's emissaryDagoras is at his camp near Isengard.

You should tell Dagoras what transpired at the meeting between Ordwaer and Saruman before the gates of Isengard.Talk to Dagoras at his camp near Isengard'Grimbold's emissary will arrive shortly. You must escort him to the gates of Isengard and ensure that no ill befalls him there. Perhaps we shall have some answers as to the full extent of Saruman's treachery at last.

'Speak with me when you are ready to meet the emissary.''You should head off quickly... Grimbold's man will be here at any moment.''Such is the influence of Saruman's voice upon the unwary. Even now, I find myself wishing to believe the truth of what he said, though I need but look around myself to see his dark intent.

'I do not know what words Ordwaer will return with, but I fear it will only serve to confuse matters further for Théodred and Grimbold as they weigh their next choice.'Quickbeam says that there is little more he can do until his kindred decide upon some course of action... but he believes that he has found a way for you to enter the fortress of Isengard undetected.Quickbeam is at the river's edge, down in the Vale below his home.

Quickbeam has asked you to meet him down by the river's edge, where he believes he has found a way to sneak you into Isengard.Talk to Quickbeam by the IsenYou should sneak into Isengard through the tunnel Quickbeam has opened for you.Speak with Dagoras within Isengard'You want to find a way into Isengard? Hoom. Well. There is no way one such as I could enter unseen, but you are so small, little ${RACE}, it seems that you could slip in through the cracks in the stone!

'Perhaps I can help you there. I saw a small stream made by the hands of Men coming from within Isengard. It carries the stench of fire and iron, so I suspect that you can find your way inside along it.

'Meet me down by the edge of the river below, and I will show you the way.''Hoom now, meet me by the river, little ${RACE}.''There you are, little ${RACE}. Do you see this grate? Perhaps you can enter Isengard through there.''You must not delay overlong, little ${RACE}. Ta-rum, it is dangerous here.''Ah, there you are, ${PLAYER} -- I thought Quickbeam would find you a way in here eventually, but keep your head down lest the Orcs discover us.'The Woodmen believe that the Easterlings in the Rushgore are descended from the tribe which Eorl the Young had aided Gondor against at the Field of Celebrant and are the precursor of another major invasion.Céola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, south-east of Aculf's camp.

Aculf asked you to warn Céola, the commander of the border-guard in the Brown Lands, of the Khundolar's impending invasion.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'${PLAYER}, if these Khundolar are indeed descended from our foes of old and that they are but the precursor of an invasion, their main force will likely come down through the Brown Lands from the passes in the east. We have a watchpost there which may be threatened.

'Would you go to Etheburg in the Brown Lands and warn Céola? Our men there must not be taken unawares.''Aculf's intentions were noble, but this news comes late to us, ${PLAYER}. The Khundolar have already come. As well, brigands have taken up a hideaway to the north. We are surrounded at every turn, it seems....''Bring tidings of the Khundolar at once to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands!'Captain Agelbrit stands guard at a lonely gate-house on the upper edge of the Limlight Gorge. His duty is as much to keep unwary travellers out of the Gorge as it is to keep the beasts within from climbing out to threaten the folk of Stangard.Speak with Captain Agelbrit at the Limlight Gorge Guard-house.Talk to Captain AgelbritSigelm is near the Limlight Gorge Guardhouse.

Captain Agelbrit has asked you to listen to Sigelm's tales of the Limlight Gorge before you explore the dangerous valley.Talk to SigelmTalk to Captain Agelbrit'Hold on a moment, stranger! I am sorry to take you to task, but I must ask what brings you this way?''You are headed west of Stangard? Well, let me give you a piece of advice, friend.... Stay clear of the Limlight Gorge if you know what is good for you.

'I have heard tell of Orcs and the like raising trouble in the Wailing Hills... but I assure you they are not half as dangerous as the monstrosities wandering down in the Gorge these days.

'If you do head out that way, just make sure to check in with Captain Agelbrit. You should at least know what you are getting into.''What is that? You want to explore the Gorge? That is folly and then some, unless you plan to lead a whole company of stalwarts with you.

'But I see in your eyes that you are not the sort to be so easily dissuaded. Well, do not blame me when some troll uses you for a football, or a spider the size of a horse has you dangling as a snack in its larder.

'Tell me, did the Men of Stangard put you up to this? Because if they did it is not funny any more. Three lads this week alone have gone down there, trying to prove their worth, and that will be the last we see of them. Enough is enough!

'I will tell you what: you go talk with Sigelm over there... he has a tale or two to tell about the Gorge back before we stopped patrols down into it.''The Gorge? Oh aye, I have been down there many times. Not so much in the last couple of years, but we used to patrol it regularly.

'Pretty place, really, but it has always been a bit queer. Strange things there. I would swear that the trees had moved from one patrol to the next, or that some boulder had shifted to face north, or all of the birds would suddenly get all quiet on a midsummer's day.

'That was before those great cursed trolls arrived of course. They crawled up out of the rocks, or down from the mountains... I could not say which, but they are a handful for even a band of men.

'Fortunately, they do not much like the sun... it has been overcast down in the Gorge a lot lately, but they are still too scared of it to wander as far from their caves as Stangard, so that is a blessing.

'It was after the trolls arrived that we saw something that REALLY gave the men a nasty turn... we were watching from a safe distance as one of those great brutes was lumbering along, when it took a swing at some old fir-tree, and the accursed thing came alive! Vines and branches wrapped up round the troll, and there was such a to-do as we have never seen.

'We had not been imagining that the trees down there wander about... they DO walk, you see, and they had been watching us all those years! That was the last patrol we did down there, and you could not pay any man of us to go back down there again.''So, do you still want to head down there? It is your life to lose, I suppose.'The dwarves sent a small expedition to try and rebuild the old sawmill in Limlight Gorge.You should find the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge and learn if Armund and his companions are still alive.Talk to Armund in the old sawmill'Who is there?

'We have not seen many travellers since we started work on the sawmill...are you looking for work?''Something you could look into while you are in the Gorge is a band of dwarves that headed down there about a week ago. You see, there is an old sawmill in the Gorge, along the river. It has been abandoned for a few years now because of the troubles in the Gorge.

'These dwarves heard about the sawmill, and their eyes lit up...with greed, no doubt. They believed they were just the sort to get it working again and do business up in Stangard from it. A fine enough endeavour, if the Gorge were not crawling with all manner of dwarf-devouring beasts.

'I do not guess that the trees themselves will be too kindly to folk trying to run a sawmill, either, now that I think of it. Anyway, if you should run into the dwarves -- and they are still alive -- see if you can convince them to come up out of there. It is not worth their lives to get a simple mill up and running. If they are dead...well, I would be obliged if you would let us know. There is not much we can do, but I like to keep track of such things.''You should seek the dwarves who passed into the Gorge.''Well, I do not know as I have any proper work for you.

'The old mill is in rough shape, but nothing me and my folk cannot put to right with a bit of dwarf-ingenuity!

'The only problem now is that all of the others seem to have wandered off and lost track of the time or some-such. None of them have come back from their jobs out in the Gorge....'It is clear that the wild cats of the Brown Lands are anything but wild, and Twiga has a plan to do away with them.The trainer of the Khundolar battle-cats may be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

Twiga asked you to hunt down the trainer of the Khundolar battle-cats and defeat him.Defeat SherkózTwiga is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg.

You should return to Twiga with tidings of your victory.Talk to Twiga at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'We could probably slay these vile cats from dawn 'til dusk and not see the end of them. We need to strike them where it will do the most harm.

'Surely among the Khundolar at Lashkarg is one who trains these creatures. Hunt him out and defeat him. With their trainer gone, the cats may even turn upon their own.

'Will you do this?''You slew this Sherkóz? Did the cats turn upon the Khundolar?

'Ah, I suppose it was too much to hope for. You have my thanks for your efforts, ${PLAYER}.''Have you dealt with the Khundolar's cat-trainer yet?'The goblin known as the Master of Beasts trains the Isen Wargs so that the goblins may ride them into battle. His defeat would mean a considerable setback to the riders as they struggle to tame their vicious mounts.The Master of Beasts resides in the caves of western Nan Curunír.

Ondor instructed you to defeat the Master of Beasts.Defeat the Master of BeastsOndor is encamped near the caves of western Nan Curunír.

You should tell Ondor that you have defeated the Master of Beasts.Talk to Ondor in Nan Curunír'So, you may have noticed that Wargs do not exactly make the best behaved mounts. Well, it takes a powerful goblin to keep them cowed enough to train and ride them.

'That is where the Master of Beasts comes in. If you kill him, the rest of the goblins will have a difficult time keeping their mounts in line.''Warg-riders may be the strongest among goblins, but their mounts are hard to control. With the Master of Beasts gone, this band will have a difficult time mounting up for a while.''Have you dealt with the Master of Beasts yet?'Prospectors have dared the dangers of the Limlight Gorge, determined to reap the mineral bounty of the Gorge.You should find the prospector's shack down in the Limlight Gorge.Find the prospector's shackYou should speak with the remaining prospector from the expedition.Talk to Brid'We had a small band of prospectors and fortune-hunters pass through Stangard a month or so ago. They had bought some old dwarf-made prospector's map of the Gorge...it must have been twenty-years-old or more, if it was not fraudulent.

'They wanted to head down into the Gorge and investigate the old prospecting sites. We told them not to waste their time, but I guess they had already spent much coin on that fool's map, so they insisted on heading down all the same.

'For the first week or so, they got on all right -- set up some sort of camp, made a few runs into town for supplies -- but we have heard nothing recently. It has been a while, and I do not have high hope that you will find them alive, but if you can find out what happened to them, it would take some weight off my mind.''Ho there friend! Please, you must help me!''Forgive me for my desperate plea, stranger, but my expedition has fallen to ruin, and most of my companions have been set upon by trolls.

'I pray that you can aid me, for my livelihood, too, is in ruin, unless I can salvage something from this disaster.

'Everything was going well, too...until the trolls caught us.'Andras is afraid that Saruman is forging weapons of great power in his personal Foundry beneath Isengard... though he knows not what form those weapons are taking.Andras asked you to enter Saruman's Foundry and defeat his acolyte, Penrith, a Dunlending who has forsaken the ways of the clans and has embraced the world of the foul magic called 'industry' which Saruman espouses.Defeat PenrithYour discovery in the Foundry caused Andras great alarm. Even the wild men of Dunland have tales of the Walking Shadows -- the Nazgûl, Ringwraiths under the domination of Sauron -- and he does not wish for such evil to come upon his people.Andras has asked you to enter the tower of Orthanc and wrest Saruman's rings from him and dispose of them before the curse of the Nazgûl can fall upon any of his people.Take Saruman's rings and destroy themQuickbeam feels that to get at the root of the Orc-problem, he will need to learn more about the Uruks' purposes... and those of Saruman.The tent of the Uruk-commander lies somewhere in the Vale below Quickbeam's home.

You should search for orders in the tent of the Uruk-commander.Examine the Uruks' orders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Uruk-commander is at his tent.

You have been discovered by the Uruk-commander.Defeat the Uruk-commander (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Quickbeam is at his home upon the north-eastern slopes above Nan Curunír.

You should bring the Uruks' orders to Quickbeam.'Ta-room. Yes, well, there are rather a lot of Orcs, are there not? I suppose you cannot drive them all away.

'Well then, we shall have to learn more about them and get to the root of why they are here... and what purpose Saruman has for them.

'They must have a leader... if you can find his dwelling, perhaps you might learn more.''Have you found the burárum's orders yet, little ${RACE}?''Hoom, does the foul leader of the burárum yet live?''Hoom-hom. Saruman intends to march south, and soon I think. My fellows are unlikely to decide on their purpose before then, for they are not so quick to judge as I.

'That is unfortunate, I think, for so many Orcs can cause a great deal of trouble, yet at least they will be out of our forests for a time.

'It also means that fewer will be here, near Isengard. Hoom, ta-rum, now that presents possibilities!'Thickbark believes that something may be awry within the caves that cut beneath the Limlight Falls, where the roots of Fangorn gather to drink from the pure waters of the river.Thickbark has asked you to gather your fellowship and explore the interior of the caves that stretch beneath the Limlight Falls.

These caves can be found a short way from the Limlight Glade, on the western side of the river.Discover the roots of FangornYou have discovered a band of Orcs in the lower stretches of the cavern.

You must locate their leader and defeat him in battle in order to drive the rest from the caverns.Protect the roots of Fangorn'It seems that the Elf Erymeldir agrees...the source of the venom is likely within the nearby caves.

'If we could enter ourselves, it would be a simple enough matter to clear out any vermin within...but alas, a full-grown Ent is much too large for such a place.

'If you could see fit to gather your friends and take a look around inside, it might be a great relief to us. I suppose we could even consider helping the Elves with their little problem....'Magla heard something sniffing around the goats in the Wailing Hills, and he cannot explain what about the experience filled him with such terror.Goats mill about the Wailing Hills in their enclosures to the north and to the south-west of Magla.

Magla had a frightening experience near the goats of the Wailing Hills and wants you to see if there is any sign of what so frightened him.Visit the goats south-west of Magla and search for what frightened himVisit the goats north of Magla and search for what frightened himMagla is near the two goat enclosures in the Wailing Hills.

You visited the goats milling about the Wailing Hills but found no sign of the creature that so frightened Magla.'I should not be out here. I wanted to be a farmer! But my father said I should follow my older brothers, and... well, here I am. And last night... well, I cannot explain it. Something spooked the goats, and I climbed up the ridge to investigate... and that's when I heard it.

'Something was... how can I describe it? It was a sniffling sound, like someone with a cold. But there was something about that snuffling sound that made my blood run cold, and as I approached the milling goats, I saw that I was not the only one disturbed by the sound. The eyes of the goats were wild, and they stamped the ground, desperate to get away from... something.

'Something moved among them, low to the ground. It made no sound but that snuffling, as if it was smelling for something. I ran. I ran and ran, and I feel as if my heart has only now calmed itself. If you decide to visit the goats at the enclosures to the north and to the south-west, use caution! That thing might come back!''Something was sniffing around those goats, and it filled me with terror. If you want to investigate, go to the enclosures to the north and to the south-west. But be careful! That thing might come back!

'Oh, what am I doing here, ${PLAYER}? My hands are better-suited for a hay-fork than for a sword and shield!''I suppose I may have imagined it? You didn't see anything there? Just goats?'

You know what Magla saw, but the man is frightened enough without knowing the identity of the creature that sniffed so near to him that night: Nazgûl.

He is slowly becoming more calm, but is still shaken by the experience.

'I am not cut out for this sort of thing, ${PLAYER}. My brothers are bold and courageous, and would certainly not have been as frightened. And my sister! She is a handmaiden at the Golden Hall, in Edoras, and she would have marched right up to that... whatever it was... and given it a tongue-lashing it would not soon forget! Not like me.

'Ah, well. I am the one who is here. I am doing my best. I hope my father and brothers and sister are proud, or will be. Thank you again, friend.'Ordhrien has suggested that you attempt to speak with the spirits of the Limlight Gorge. The Elves of Lothlórien once communed with these spirits and claim that they can only be seen by the light of the stars.Complete Ancient Ruins of the LimlightOrdhrien has suggested that you attempt to speak with the spirits of the Limlight Gorge.

The Elves of Lothlórien once communed with these spirits, and claim that they can only be seen by the light of the stars.Speak with the Spirit of ReverenceSpeak with the Spirit of RemembranceSpeak with the Spirit of AmitySpeak with the Spirit of MelodySpeak with the Spirit of EnlightenmentSpeak with the Spirit of Destiny'Greetings wanderer... your bravery does you credit, but this is no place for mortal spirits. Even the Elves come here no longer.

'Long ago this place lay under the protection of my lady's power, and it was here that the trees were taught to speak.''What is it you seek here? The lady long ago withdrew her power from this place, leaving us to act as its custodians.

'I long to return to the West, but so too does the memory of this land hold me here, till at last all that stood here is no more, and those memories are no longer needed.''Once, two ancient forests came together here, and so the Firstborn and the Shepherds of the Forest communed over the nature of the world under the tutelage of our mistress.

'But the Elves left long ago, and the trees speak rarely now, and it has become a lonely, wild place.''I often find myself dancing to the music of the birds and the river -- but I do miss the songs of the Firstborn.

'Perhaps I wish that they would return some day? Alas, I do not think that likely.''It was long ago that we aided the Elves, helped teach them the secrets of the trees, that they might speak with them, and so teach them to speak in turn.

'But even the trees have now grown old, and most are wild, and few remember any of the words that they learned so long ago.''Here we remain after the forest itself has retreated, with little to remind us of the past save these tumbled remains.

'Even those shall soon be gone -- and then what shall we remember? I suppose then at last we shall return into the West.'You have been sent for training in the handling of a Rohirrim warhorse by the riding instructor Seoca upon the Tourney Field south of Harwick.You may not obtain a war-steed until you finish assisting the town of Langhold.

To begin the lesson, you must first obtain a war-steed.Obtain a war-steed by helping LangholdSpeak with Seoca at the tourney field directly south of Harwick.Complete the riding course upon the tourney fieldSpeak with Seoca to complete your war-steed training.Speak to Seoca at the Tourney FieldSpeak with Anmar, guard at the Mead-hall of Harwick in the Wold.Speak with Anmar at the Harwick Mead-hall'Ha! What a nice little steed you ride! Nothing like our own horses, but a nice little steed just the same. Though, if you are to ride alongside our warriors upon the plains of Rohan, you must learn how to fight from horseback as well.

'Our steeds are not so gentle-bred as those of the north. They are stronger, yes - but also more wilful and difficult to handle.

'I have asked one of our finest riding instructors to teach you in the ways of handling a steed of the Rohirrim. You will find Seoca at the Tourney Field north of Harwick. First, though, you should look into getting a steed.

'Go and learn all you can from him - and good luck to you ${PLAYER}.''So, you wish to be trained in the ways of riding a horse to war, eh?

'Well, you've come to the right place. I've trained hundreds of riders over the years - though few as experienced in battle as yourself, I must admit.

'Come then, let us begin!''You are ready now ${PLAYER}. Your skills in battle are already formidable. With one of our finest steeds beneath you, you shall be undefeatable!

'Trust in your mount and in your valour, and your banner shall wave above these fields as a beacon of hope for all the Free Peoples of Middle-earth!

'Now I believe you should speak with the Thane of Harwick before you proceed further. Much is afoot in our lands, and it would be best if you made your presence known to our local lord.''You seek audience with the Thane? Well, I'll see what I can do for you, but he has not been in a sociable mood of late....'You have begun a short training tutorial at the Harwick Stables to teach you how to control your war-steed.Begin your instruction in how to ride a war-steed by speaking with Seoca.Speak with SeocaMount your war-steed near the outer track starting line.Mount your war-steed near the outer starting lineFollow the direction of Seoca as you circle the tourney field and learn to control your steed.

You must make two full circuits of the outer track in order to proceed.Laps completed (${VALUE}/2)Speak with Seoca.Speak with SeocaRun the flags course as directed by Seoca.

On the first round, you must pass through the blue flags.

On the second round, you must pass through the red flags.

On the third round, you must pass through both sets of flags at once.

