'Would you go to Helstor and see if you can find the treasure stores of the brigands? It will likely be in a cave at the back of the camp.''Surely, you have not found all the relics stolen from Path Celebrant...?''These are a wonderful find, ${PLAYER}. I see here relics both of my ancestors, but also of the Men of Gondor, the Easterlings, and some Dunlendings.

'You have earned this reward.'Rohirrim scouts from Etheburg have claimed to have seen trolls in the distance and are now afraid to venture forth into the Brown Lands.Scouts claimed seeing trolls in the distance throughout the Brown Lands.

Céola wants you to seek out evidence -- or the lack thereof -- of trolls in the Brown Lands.Seek out evidence of trolls in the Brown LandsCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

You should return to Céola and warn him that there are indeed trolls in the Brown Lands.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'Among the other threats we face, there is one that I find difficult to believe and feel is more rumour than reality. A few of our less favourable scouts have claimed seeing trolls in the distance, and now many of the scouts fear to go out into the Brown Lands.

'While you are out on patrol would you keep a sharp eye out for any sign of trolls? If we can find no evidence of trolls, they might feel more secure, and I will have the evidence I need to discipline the rabblerousers.''Have you found any signs of trolls in the Brown Lands?''Alas, I wish you had not told me this! I fear these tidings more than I do the entire Khundolar host at Lashkarg.

