Céola asked you to aid him and his lieutenants, Twiga and Dagbert, with several tasks to help reduce the threats in the Brown Lands.Assist Céola with Hide and SeekAssist Twiga with Wild Cats of the Brown LandsAssist Céola with Trolls in the Brown LandsCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands.

You should return to Céola and let him know that you have completed the tasks requested of you.Talk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands'We had trouble enough already without the Khundolar crossing into the Brown Lands, ${PLAYER}, but it is our duty to Théoden King to defend Rohan, and to that end, we will need your aid, stranger though you be.

'Would you grant us some small service before you continue to Edoras? I have a few tasks for you myself, but speak also with my lieutenants, for they have their own concerns which need to be addressed.

'You can find Twiga in the western part of the camp and Dagbert in the south-west corner. Time is running short, ${PLAYER}...I fear too short.''I thank you for your efforts, ${PLAYER}, but it appears that our trials are more difficult than we previously guessed. There is much more yet to do....'The mighty Uruk-hai are loyal only to Saruman. They are more clever and cruel than even the vile Orcs.Defeat Uruk-hai in DunlandThe mighty Uruk-hai are loyal only to Saruman. They are more clever and cruel than even the vile Orcs.Defeat Uruk-hai in DunlandThe Wailing Hills, north-west of Stangard, are so named due to a great battle and the slaughtering of Orcs that occured there many years ago, around the time of Rohan's founding.Explore the Wailing Hills in the Great River.Discover the CuthstanDiscover Frithstan's CampDiscover the Nink-hai CampDiscover the Mor-hai SettlementDiscover the Secluded ClearingDiscover Venom-Bite CaveDiscover Aster HillIsengard operates under the rule of Saruman the White.

In his efforts to maintain control of his growing army and industry, he has assigned powerful Men to see to the working of each of the wards of the fortress.

If you can defeat the ward masters, you will significantly disrupt the efficiency of Isengard's industry of war.The Masters can be found at each of the spokes of the roads that dissect the Ring of Isengard.

Dagoras has instructed you to defeat the Master of each of the wards of Isengard.Defeat the Master of the East WardDefeat the Master of the North WardDefeat the Master of the West WardDagoras is hiding within the Ring of Isengard.

You should return to Dagoras with news of your success.Talk to Dagoras within the Ring of Isengard'It would not do to be seen in here, ${PLAYER}. The servants of Saruman are everywhere!

'Saruman has made certain there are no shortcomings in his defences. He has placed each of the wards of the Ring of Isengard under a master to ensure that all matters follow his schedule and purpose.

'Orcs are not independently responsible, so that is understandable, but it also means that if you can dispatch the master of each of these wards, his finely-oiled engine of war should shudder to a halt until he can replace them.''Have you dealt with the Masters of the Wards yet?''That did not take you very long.

'I wonder that you are able to move about Isengard without drawing greater alarm... something must be afoot to distract the master of the house from dealing with such an incursion.

