'This statue was made by the smiths of Gondor and given to Eorl the Young in honour of the aid he gave at the Field of Celebrant. It has long been an heirloom of the Eorlingas!

'How did this come to be in the hands of the brigands? Ah, that I think I can answer well enough: Gríma Wormtongue, no doubt. He probably gave it to Hafoc as a reward for betraying us all....'Dagoras has told you of a Dunlending messenger who is relaying information from Isengard to the clans in Dunland. The messenger is expected to pass by the Pillar of the Hand shortly.The Pillar of the Hand lies to the east of Dagoras' camp.

Dagoras has asked you to intercept a Dunlending messenger as he passes by the Pillar of the Hand. You should first eliminate the sentries by the Pillar.Dagoras is encamped near the entrance to Nan Curunír, west of the Pillar of the Hand.

