'Speak up! What dire news have you?''I'll take you to Feldburg right away.'Frodo has asked for an hour in which to decide the course of the Fellowship, but you are worried he will not choose to bring the Ring to Minas Tirith.Aragorn is by the camp-fire on Parth Galen.Talk to Aragorn by the camp-fireThe Elf, Legolas, is by the camp-fire.Talk to the Elf, Legolas, by the camp-fireYour companions do not understand. You have to find Frodo and make him understand that the Ring must go to Minas Tirith.Find Frodo and convince him to bring the Ring to Minas Tirith. He wandered somewhere to the north-west.Frodo has wandered partially up Amon Hen. He needs to be told of your city's great need for the Ring.Talk to Frodo and see if he has yet decided what to doFrodo has wandered partially up Amon Hen. He needs to be told of your city's great need for the Ring.Talk to Frodo and tell him of Minas Tirith's great needFrodo has wandered partially up Amon Hen. He needs to be told of your city's great need for the Ring. Perhaps he will lend it to you? You can use the Ring to save Minas Tirith, and all of Gondor!Talk to Frodo and ask to borrow the Ring so you can save GondorFrodo will doom us all! You have to take the Ring from him before he ransoms Middle-earth to Sauron!Seize the Ring from Frodo!The sneak must be hiding somewhere around here! Search the places he might be hiding, and seize the Ring!Search the hollow log for the sneaking hobbit!Search the leaf pile for the sneaking hobbit!Search through the bush for the sneaking hobbit!Frodo is gone, and the anger has lifted from your senses much as a cloud moves on from covering the sun. You should return now to Aragorn and the rest of your party. Perhaps Frodo has returned to them and will forgive you your outburst.Frodo is gone. You should return to the camp-site and see if he will forgive your outburstAragorn wants to know where you have been.Talk to Aragorn'I understand, Boromir, but you know the words of Gandalf. Though there be strength in Minas Tirith, it is not a strength that will avail us in the matter of Frodo's burden. If this were a contest that could be won by strength of arms, I would readily agree to go at once to your city. But I fear it is not.

'When Frodo returns he will give us his decision, and we will do what we can to support him, will we not?''I believe we should go to Minas Tirith, Boromir. If it came to a vote, that would be my decision. You have told us of the Enemy's desire to destroy Minas Tirith, and I think that is where we are most needed.

'But I will stand with Frodo, whatever his decision.''You are very kind, Boromir, but I have seen no danger. If there are Orcs about, they must remain on the other side of the river. I have simply been walking and thinking about what I must do. But it is not an easy decision to make. I know what I must do, but... I am afraid.''I know Minas Tirith is endangered, Boromir, but I cannot bring the Ring there. You heard what Gandalf said at the Council, and Elrond... my road lies to the east, and to the Fire. The Ring cannot save Gondor. Its only power is the power to destroy.''Boromir, it is my burden, and I will not give it to you! You are not yourself! The Ring has influenced your words, do not let it influence your actions as well! I have nothing more to say to you!''Boromir, no! The Ring cannot save Gondor! It must be destroyed!''Boromir, what have you done?'Aragorn has given you an important charge, perhaps the most important charge you have been given on this entire journey: keep the hobbits safe!The hobbits Meriadoc and Peregrin are in danger! You have to come to their aid!Come to the aid of the hobbits!An Uruk threatens the hobbits!Defeat the Uruk that threatens the hobbits!Meriadoc and Peregrin need your help. They are not safe of the Uruks yet!Talk to MeriadocThe number of the Uruks is overwhelming! You need aid! Blow the Horn of Gondor!Blow the Horn of Gondor to summon aid!Meriadoc and Peregrin need your help. They are not safe of the Uruks yet!Talk to PeregrinThe number of the Uruks is overwhelming! You need aid! Blow the Horn of Gondor!Blow the Horn of Gondor to summon aid!You have to protect the hobbits, at any cost!Examine the dying Uruk in the middle of the gladeThe Uruks are closing in...Defend the hobbitsYou have done what you could, Boromir.Defend the hobbitsThis fallen Uruk is barely alive, but the mark of the White Hand on his armour is unmistakeable.

