You should bring everything you collected to Cíllan.'As you saw, my friend, we left in a great hurry when Langhold fell. Thanks to you, we had enough time to save so many lives, but our belongings were left behind.

'If you could find any gold that was left behind, perhaps we can afford that great manor. Looters may have taken all we held dear, but if someone could search for anything that could be salvaged, it would be incredibly helpful to us.

'Frithbéorth asks a heavy price for the housing we hope to acquire. If my husband were alive...but no matter.''You found so much, ${PLAYER}! I cannot believe all of this was left intact after the fire.

'I was near sick with worry once I knew we needed to send you back to Langhold for something that was unlikely to be there. Your courage and goodness never ceases to impress me, my friend.

'I believe we may have enough to purchase the house from Frithbéorth! I will begin to look closely into the particulars of this arrangement.'An unpleasant buzzing noise has been disturbing the rest of the pampered war-steeds of Harwick.The source of the buzzing noise is coming from somewhere in the bog west of Harwick.Find the source of the buzzing noiseThe guard of the stables waits by Harwick's horses for you to return.

