'No, but his horse arrived shortly before you did... and without him! Something must have happened to him. You have to retrace your steps, and look for him! He must be somewhere between Elthengels and Floodwend. Look among the trees to the south of the road between here and Floodwend. You could have passed him without seeing him!''I am sorry if I came across as a bit of a fool, ${PLAYER}. I did not think you would be much of a rider, but not only are you a skilled rider, you are a good person as well. I thank you for coming to find me. I have already given your Elf his bow, and I renounce any claim to it I may have had. It is done.''I was trying to take a short-cut to Elthengels when Hreohmanu was surprised by a patrol of Orcs! He reared, and I fell... did he make it to Elthengels? I can... I can probably walk now. I could not put weight on it, but now it is feeling better. I will meet you ahead in Elthengels, and we can discuss... the wager. I will be there soon. Thank you for coming back to find me.''Why are you still here? Do you not want to win your wager with Elfsige? Elthengels is south-west of here! Ride with utmost haste!''You need to go to Elthengels. Did Elfsige get there before you?''You have to retrace your steps, and look for Elfsige! He must be somewhere between Elthengels and Floodwend. Look among the trees to the south of the road between here and Floodwend. You could have passed him without seeing him!'Hreohmanu gazes at you balefully. This is Elfsige's horse, but you see no sign of the brash young Rohirrim.Horn looks at you silently, his expression unreadable.'My leg is feeling better. Thank you. I will meet you back in Elthengels.'The Easterlings have employed a number of workers to construct deadly siege-weapons, a task which they perform with fierce pleasure and pride, for they loathe the Rohirrim.The Woodyard is on the eastern side of Jóshkhin Orda in the Wold, to the north of North-torr.

