Cúfaron has asked you to hunt some of the swert-hounds that haunt the East Wall.Defeat swert-hounds throughout the East Wall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cúfaron is at Hestil's camp on Parth Galen.

You have defeated many swert-hounds and should now return to Cúfaron as he asked.Talk to Cúfaron'Greetings to you, ${CLASS}. My name is Cúfaron, and I am a hunter of great skill. Ask anyone! I will not regale you with tales of my many accomplishments, but if you are not careful I fear my companions might!

'Isteron was always very impressed with my stories of the lands to the distant east. Great beasts and dangerous birds can be found there, and I have hunted them all! Rodwen might speak of my prowess in the south-lands. Do you know those mighty four-legged monstrosities, the great mûmakil?'

Cúfaron quickly shakes his head as you ask if he hunted one of those.

'Nay, not as such...but I saw one. In the distance, but still, you have not seen one, have you?'

The hunter regains his composure.

'There are a lot of vile dogs around the East Wall, and I do not think they are creatures of nature. The Rohirrim call them swert-hounds, and they seem to me to be quite evil. You should hunt them, as I plan to do. I think they could cause trouble for us if they get too near to our camp.''You have returned to compare notes with the master hunter? Sounds good to me, ${PLAYER}! I strode about the East Wall and defeated... how many swert-hounds did you defeat?'

Cúfaron listens as you answer, then nods.

'Six? I see, I see. Well, I defeated seven. It is true that you almost bested me. I know it is not a competition, but it is still nice to know the score.

'These creatures are not natural, that much seems certain. Their evil is evident. They were drawn here by something, but I know not what. We should not stay here. The sooner my friends and I can be gone from this place, the better! But I will, of course, continue to hunt the deadliest of creatures for as long as we remain in the East Wall, and you should strive to match me in this, if you can.''You should hunt the swert-hounds that haunt the East Wall, and I shall as well. Let us meet back here, and we can compare tallies?'Deadly Easterling Horsemen patrol the plains outside of their large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda, north of North-torr.Mounted Easterlings train on their newly acquired horses outside their large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr.

You should defeat the Easterling Horsemen, for they are powerful and dangerous foes.Defeat Easterling Horsemen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sergeant Guthferth rallies the defences of North-torr just north of Floodwend, attempting to hold back the flood of Easterlings threatening to drown the Wold in chaos.

You should speak with Sergeant Guthferth.Return to Guthferth, Sergeant of North-torrDeadly Easterling Horsemen patrol the plains outside of their large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda, north of North-torr.'I find it cruel that the Easterlings train to use our own good horses against us! Are they trying to even the odds in open field warfare against the Rohirrim?

