'See how they stare! I cannot help but feel that I am being spied upon. I would appreciate if you could climb Cracabor and find out what you can about those vile birds.''You found an evil object upon the crest of Cracabor? Perhaps it is the work of that Nazgûl you spied earlier; he may have summoned the crebain. The black birds are surely spies for some evil plot....'Crebain gather upon Cracabor, the highest hill near Twickenburg. These fell birds give unease to the warriors stationed nearby.The hill of Cracabor is the highest point in the Wold and is located just north of Twickenburg.Defeat crebain near Cracabor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sergeant Tidlac is keeping watch on the road from the fort of Twickenburg, between Harwick and Floodwend.Return to Tidlac, Sergeant of TwickenburgCrebain gather upon Cracabor, the highest hill near Twickenburg. These fell birds give unease to the warriors stationed nearby.'Hopefully reducing the number of crebain spies will remind the Nazgûl that we are not going to roll over. If they want the Wold to fall, they will have to do better!'Floodwend's peril has come to a boil. The Orcs and Easterlings have advanced on Floodwend, lead by the Nazgûl: the Grim Southron.The town of Floodwend is besieged by the forces of Jóshkhin Orda, led by the Grim Southron who re-grouped the routed army. You must protect the Mead Hall, and the young Thane of Floodwend!Help Radwig defend the Mead HallThe Mead Hall was saved in the assault on Floodwend, but the town has taken its losses.

