You must protect the Mead Hall, and the young Thane of Floodwend!Speak with the young ThaneRadwig is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend, awaiting the approach of the forces of Mordor, let by the Grim Southron.Listen to RadwigRadwig is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.Protect the Mead Hall from the forces of MordorThe Mead Hall of Floodwend has been defended, and Radwig is excited to congratulate you, and thank you for your help.Speak with Radwig'We could not have managed this without you, ${PLAYER}. I owe you so much. I do not think I would have embraced my responsibilities with such confidence if you had not been here to show me the way a true leader, a true warrior, must be.''It is time to brace for battle, ${PLAYER}. I can already hear the sounds of war outside. We must take a stand here, in this very Mead Hall, and ensure that it does not fall as Langhold did, not many days ago.''Look, ${PLAYER}! Floodwend still stands!

'The Easterlings are truly driven off. I cannot thank you enough for helping us here, my friend. Look at my people, whole and hale.'It is time for Hestil's group of adventurers-for-hire to rescue their guardian from his captivity, and you have agreed to help with the task.Hestil is outside the Uruk encampment on Amon Hen, waiting to speak with you before setting the plan into motion.Talk to Hestil outside the Uruk campMaedal is outside the Uruk camp on Amon Hen, waiting to speak with you for your part of the plan to rescue Drafli Broadshield from captivity.Talk to Maedal outside the Uruk campYou need to observe what's going on inside the Uruk camp on Amon Hen. Be careful not to be seen!Listen to the situation within the Uruk campAvoid being seen!The Uruk camp has mostly emptied in pursuit of Isteron! You need to go and rescue Drafli Broadshield while the others see to Isteron's well-being.Enter the camp and defeat the Uruk guarding Drafli's cageDrafli Broadshield is inside his cage in the Uruk camp on Amon Hen. You need to speak to him to get him out of his depression.Talk to Drafli BroadshieldDrafli Broadshield has recovered his confidence and needs to speak to you.Talk to Drafli BroadshieldIsteron is in trouble near the top of Amon Hen.Talk to Isteron atop Amon HenHestil's group of adventurers-for-hire is in danger near the summit of Amon Hen.Survive your encounter with the Grim SouthronRamdir is near the summit of Amon Hen, and you should speak to him.Talk to Ramdir atop Amon Hen'The glowers worked tremendously, ${PLAYER}! I cannot believe I took glistershade so much for granted! All they do is glow? Sometimes that is enough!

'But they can't help us now, can they? Look at that thing!''Our part of the plan to free Drafli should be easy, ${PLAYER}. We are to sneak up to the gate and listen to the conversation of the Uruks. Listen for anything that would make us need to change our plans.

'I may not be much of a Captain, but I will be the best Burglar I can for my friends. Follow me, and do not let yourself be seen!''There is the encampment, ${PLAYER}. Do you remember the plan? You and Maedal will creep up to the entrance so you can spy on the activities of the Uruks within the walls. Once you have determined that things are as we expect them to be, Rodwen and I will drop into the camp from above while Cúfaron sows confusion among the Uruks with his arrows.

'I have tasked Ramdir with keeping an eye on Isteron. Our lore-master has decided that he wants to study the effect of some plant he found on the Uruks, and I... well, I am sure Ramdir can keep him from interfering with the plan.

'It is time, ${PLAYER}. May good fortune shine on all of us, and we will have Drafli Broadshield back with us before the moon is any higher in the night sky!''It is no use, ${PLAYER}. My friends are better off without me. I am no use as a guardian. Look at me! Stuck in this cage, depending on someone else to free me. That is not the way of a dwarf!'

You tell Drafli that his friends are endangered and need his help.

'But what can I do? I am stuck here in this cage!''That was a fortunate gambit, ${PLAYER}! We survived, but I do not dare to call that a triumph. We must leave the East Wall as soon as we can, for the wraith may return when it recovers from the disappointment of which it spoke.

'We cannot stay here.''Let us hurry back to Parth Galen, ${PLAYER}. We do not want to be here when our foe returns.''Ha ha! I am ready to fight once more, ${PLAYER}! I am a dwarf, I am a guardian, and I am free! Now let us go save my friends!'You met a curious man beneath the East Wall, and he told you of his friends, a party of adventurers camped on Parth Galen.Isteron's friends are camped on Parth Galen, a grassy lawn to the south-east of the Under-wall tunnels, by a stream that runs from the lake of Nen Hithoel.Find the camp of Isteron's friends on Parth Galen'You have been a good help to me, it is true. What do you think, Mossy? Would Hestil welcome the aid of this ${RACE}? She would?

'Then it's decided! You should go to Hestil's camp and see if you can help my friends with their problems. They do have a lot of problems.

'They're camped on Parth Galen, a grassy lawn to the south-east of here, by a small stream that runs from the large lake in the East Wall.'Isteron stares at you, but refuses to speak further. You recall his words that his friends are camped on Parth Galen, a grassy lawn to the south-east of here, by a small stream that runs from the large lake in the East Wall.Isteron wants you to defeat one of the leaders from Moria that leads the Orcs in the Under-wall.Leaders of the Moria Orcs can be found in the northernmost and southernmost side passages in the Under-wall.

Isteron wants you to send a message to the Moria Orcs by challenging one of their leaders in battle.Find and defeat an Under-wall Captain in the Under-wallIsteron is by the northernmost exit from the Under-wall.

You have defeated a Moria Orc-leader and should return to tell Isteron of your success.Talk to Isteron'While you were away, I did some research, and I have determined from where these Orcs came. They are from Moria, deep beneath the Misty Mountains. According to conversations I overheard while examining the moss that grows down here in the Under-walls, they came to this place by following a trail of some kind.

'I do not know what they were following, but it sounds like they skirted some "Elf-woods." That has to be the Golden Wood I have heard so much about! It is no wonder that they avoided it, but I am surprised that they have come this far from Moria in pursuit of their prey.

'It is only right that these Orcs be sent back to Moria! If you find one of their leaders, challenge him to combat and defeat him to send a message to his underlings!''You did it! That is a job well done, ${PLAYER}.'

You tell Isteron what the Orc said before the battle, and the lore-master shrugs.

'I do not know what he was talking about, ${PLAYER}. Maybe he thought you were someone else? It does not matter now, I suppose.

'Thank you for all your help! I do not need anything else right now, so you can just let yourself out. The southernmost exit from the Under-wall should leave you right near the camp my companions established, if you would like to help them as you have helped me.''Look for the leaders of the Moria Orcs in some of the side passages you explored here in the Under-wall, ${PLAYER}.''You led us on a pretty chase, ${RACE}! But now it's the end of the road for you, and me and my boys will bring you back to Moria in pieces!

'You were right to abandon your Wizard on that bridge! You would have died with him if you had stayed and fought instead of running away and hiding in the Elf-woods. But now we've found you, and it's the end for you!'Nîn-stazg's war-leader poses a dire threat to the city of Floodwend and its young Thane.The Warleader of Nîn-stazg can be found deep within the Orc encampment of Nîn-stazg, south-east of Floodwend.

You should defeat the Warleader of Nîn-stazg.Defeat Nîn-stazg's Warleader from MordorThane Radwig is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.

You should tell Thane Radwig that the Warleader has been slain, which should bring some peace of mind to the young Thane.Return to Radwig in FloodwendEtta, mother of Thane Radwig, is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.

You should speak with Etta.Speak with Etta'The overseers of Nîn-stazg were an Orkish version of our Sergeants, but they must have a true leader -- a Thane, but in the dark fashion of Mordor.

'He will be the most dangerous one of all. It is imperative that we remove their leader to slow their advance on the town of Floodwend!''Now my son is angry at me, and talking nonsense about battle and freedom. I do not appreciate this meddling, ${PLAYER}. I wish you would stay out of the affairs of Floodwend.

'Aldor Harding sent you, and for that reason I do not set my guards to knock you out of town, but I must insist that you cease this meddling with my son.

'He is only a boy!''I am sorry I was not allowed to fight by your side, ${PLAYER}. Someday, the men loyal to my mother will show their loyalty to me, and I will be able to act the part of a true Thane, not some cowed boy-child.

'I was inspired by your feats at Nîn-stazg. It was a pleasure to watch a free warrior do what was right.''We are here only to protect Thane Radwig, at the bidding of Lady Etta.''You fight like none I have ever seen, ${PLAYER}. I wish to fight like you, someday, when I have put a few notches on my blade.'Ramdir has one request before he prevails upon Hestil to get her band of adventurers moving: he wishes to see the Argonath.Ramdir wants to speak with you in the shadow of the Argonath, north along the Anduin.

Ramdir has wanted to gaze upon the Pillars of the Kings for many years, and he has asked to meet you at a place where he has a good vantage point of them.Talk to Ramdir beneath the shadow of the Argonath'Before I prevail upon Hestil to get her band of adventurers moving, I have a request, ${PLAYER}. I wish to see the Argonath. The Pillars of the Kings stand in the cliffs north of here.

'It would mean a great deal to me to see them. I will meet you in their shadow, ${PLAYER}, and we will speak again.''I will meet you north of here, in the shadow of the Argonath. I wish to gaze upon the Pillars of the Kings.''Behold the Pillars of the Kings, ${PLAYER}. I wish I had the words to explain to you what I am feeling, but I simply do not. Isildur. Anárion. It is... overwhelming.

'The Wardens of Minas Ithil have long fought on in the memory of the Tower of the Moon, though it has been lost to the Enemy for so many years. It is called Minas Morgul now, and those of us who remember what it once stood for are few. Many of my fellows abandoned the cause, because it seemed impossible to go on. They said we toiled for naught.

'Would they think so if they could stand where I stand now and gaze upon these likenesses of Isildur and Anárion? They are a reminder, ${PLAYER}, that the works of Men will last, that the spirit of Man cannot be crushed, despite adversity and the passage of time. Even the Orcs cannot tear them down, and if they sought to, my heart sings that Men would take the pieces and build them anew.'Easterling Overlords in the Woodyard near Jóshkhin Orda oversee the construction of fearsome siege-weapons.The Woodyard is on the eastern side of Jóshkhin Orda in the Wold, to the north of North-torr.

