'Ah... my mother wishes to say something. Well, please do not take too long. I will meet you out on the field of battle, my friend -- at Nîn-stazg!''Do not encourage him, ${PLAYER}! Radwig is no warrior yet, and he endangers his life with such mad ideas.

'No, Radwig, you must not go to this Orc encampment.''Nonsense. My father would never have stood by while the forces of Mordor captured our defences. I will go and fight these Orcs. How else will I command the respect of my people?

'My mother cannot change my mind.

'I will see you at Nîn-stazg, ${PLAYER}! I look forward to drawing my sword with yours.''My lady Etta has sent us to protect the Thane. He should not go into battle, but he may observe the battle from here, should he wish it.''My... my mother sent these guards to keep me out of harm's way, and now they will not let me anywhere nearer Nîn-stazg than this. So many Orcs! Yet I yearn to prove myself in battle....'

Your heart goes out to this bold young man, but it is clear that this is not the time for him to be fighting.

He was brave for venturing out, but he is not ready, and he is of more use to his folk alive than dead. You tell him what you think.'My lady Etta has sent us to protect the Thane. He should not go into battle, but he may observe the battle from here, should he wish it.''I long for the day when I can fight my own battles without adults interfering....''My lady Etta has sent us to protect the Thane. He should not go into battle, but he may observe the battle from here, should he wish it.''It was a pleasure to watch you fight, ${PLAYER}! I have never seen such bravery on the training ground. When I saw you fight, I imagined my father in battle, and it gave me heart.

'You were good to destroy those siege-machines. They would have done Floodwend much harm. The next time Orcs attack our lands, it will be me hewing at their limbs!'A great matron to the Wargs of the Howling Wood has settled near the abandoned worksite.A great matron to the Wargs of the Howling Wood has settled near the abandoned worksite.Defeat the Warg-matronWargs have recently moved into the work site to the east of Floodwend.Defeat the Warg-matronYou have defeated the Warg-matron of the Howling Wood.CompletedDefeat the Matron of the Warg pack at The Howling Wood.You have defeated the Warg-matron of the Howling Wood, responsible for spawning and protecting the pack that settled so near Floodwend. With the matron defeated, the good Rohirrim of Floodwend are safer, and can hope to reclaim this abandoned worksite.The Easterlings have been snatching wild horses from the herds to train them for evil purposes.A pen of stolen horses can be found in the south-east of the enormous Easterling encampment on the banks of the Anduin.

