'Will you search the encampment below for anything that might tell us what the Orcs had in mind for Floodwend?''How fascinating, ${PLAYER}! Each of these three parchments crudely describes a different assault-plan upon Floodwend.

'I believe this indicates a collaboration between the Orcs and Easterlings. This must be the work of the Nazgûl, to rally Men and Orcs -- even if they do squabble over the particulars. This does not bode well for Floodwend.'The wounded Uruk is almost ready to tell you what happened at the Dead Orc Glade, but he still wants you to do something for him first.The distinctive scavenging Orc is probably lurking south-east of the Dead Orc Glade, in the East Wall. The wounded Uruk believes the scavenging Orc would seek higher ground.

The wounded Uruk in the Dead Orc Glade has promised to tell you what happened there... once you recover the purse of gold that was stolen by an Orc.Collect the purse of gold from the Orc that stole itThe wounded Uruk in the Dead Orc Glade is waiting for you to return his stolen purse of gold.'You want to know... what happened in this place? I was lying here, cut down in battle... and left for dead... and an Orc came running by... and he just reached down and stole my purse of gold! I was too hurt to keep him from taking it! A pox on the maggot-faced slime!

'You track him down, ${RACE}... he ran off to the south-east... he would want to find high ground... you'll know him by the scavenged and mismatched armour he wears. Get my gold back!'

He laughs weakly.

'Only then... will I tell you what else happened here... ha! Ha!''Track down the Orc that stole my gold, ${RACE}... he ran off to the south-east and would seek higher ground... you'll know him by the mismatched armour he wears. Get my gold back!''You found it! Well... done. That Orc now knows that Zerlúk can reach... even from the grave for his vengeance! Ha!'

Zerlúk's laughter is interrupted by a fit of coughing, but he does not seem to mind.

'Ah, it feels good to have my gold again. No one steals from me... and lives, even if I must get... vermin like you to carry out my will.

'But you wanted to hear the tale of what happened at this place... and now I will tell it to you.'Before you left Floodwend, Etta mentioned a report of Easterlings invading the Wold just north of the city. North-torr is all that stands in the way of this Easterling invasion reaching Floodwend and laying it to ruin.North-torr is a fort north of Floodwend, and is the last defence standing in the way of the Easterlings assaulting Floodwend directly.

You should find North-torr and speak with Guthferth, the sergeant of that outpost.Report to Guthferth, Sergeant at North-torr'That is enough of that talk, Radwig! You mustn't wish for such things. The Mead Hall is safe for you, and here you may protect your people. You should not be anxious to throw your life away.

'The road has been eerily empty for some time, ${PLAYER}. Will you not go to North-torr, our nearest outpost, and see how they fare? It will be easier for my son to accept his role when you are not standing before him, perhaps.''I asked for reinforcements! Are you really all they sent? Please, let this be a jest. Alas for my luck!

'Well, you look capable, so you'll have to do. The Easterlings are camped north of here, and the size of their camp grows every time I turn around.

'I cannot believe they send me one warrior when the Easterlings grow by the hour, and you are not even Rohirrim.'Sergeant Tidlac is stationed at Twickenburg, an outpost on main road running through the Wold. The watch-tower of Twickenburg has a good vantage point of the Wold cross-roads.The fort of Twickenburg is north of Floodwend along the main road between Harwick and Floodwend.

You should seek the sergeant in charge of Twickenburg to see how they fare.Find Sergeant Tidlac at Twickenburg'Thank you for your efforts in assisting Harwick, ${PLAYER}. I am in your debt.

