<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>'There were some close moments, ${PLAYER}, but Maedal's plan worked flawlessly. Well, perhaps not flawlessly, but it did what it was supposed to. Drafli is rescued, and now we can resume our journey.

'Thank you very much for your help, ${PLAYER}! Now we can....'

Hestil looks around.

'Where did Drafli go? He was here a moment ago, and... Isteron? Isteron, where have you wandered off to now?'

Hestil sighs.

'And they are off again! It is not easy leading this company, that is for certain! I wonder if Cuilinn needs any help running his farm? Oh no! What am I saying?

'Thank you once again, ${PLAYER}. They are my friends, but sometimes I think they have more to fear from themselves than they do from Orcs! Good fortune upon your journey!'Isteron wants you to map out the cave-network beneath the East Wall so he can efficiently advance his studies.Isteron wants you to thoroughly map the three side passages that branch off the main tunnel that runs beneath the East Wall.Explore the northernmost chamber off the tunnelExplore the middle chamber off the tunnelExplore the southernmost chamber off the tunnelIsteron is by the northernmost exit from the caves that run beneath the East Wall.

You have explored the side passages beneath the East Wall's main passage and should return to Isteron with the information you have collected.Talk to Isteron'Orcs and insects, insects and Orcs. If I were studying either of these things, this cave-network would be a dream come true! But, sadly, I am not. My studies are more esoteric than those trivialities. But they are endangered by the dangers in this place!

'My friends have a camp near the grassy lawn of Parth Galen, if you know where that is, and they have decided the Orcs in the East Wall are too dense for us to proceed northwards. I left them to discuss what to do next and found my way to these caves. Why not explore while they determine the next course of action? I learned quickly that the water is very treacherous. Try not to fall in, because you will not come back out.

'I entered this cave-network from what must have been the southernmost entrance, and from my exploration it appears that there are three entrances to this network, as well as three side tunnels. Explore those three side tunnels and tell me what you find, and I will reward you with the twin gifts of knowledge and of gratitude...and perhaps a more monetary gift as well.'Isteron listens as you describe your painstaking exploration of the tunnel beneath the East Wall and its many side passages. After you are done speaking, the lore-master's eyes light up.

'I have decided, ${PLAYER}! I shall name this tunnel system "the Under-wall." Do you see why? It runs beneath the East Wall. Very clever, is it not?''This tunnel runs primarily north and south, but there are three passages that branch off of it. I want you to explore these side passages in the interest of preparing a comprehensive map of this cavern's layout.'Ramdir is concerned about the massive presence of Orcs on Amon Hen and wants you to scout the hilltop to see how many Orcs gather on Amon Lhaw.The Seat of Seeing is located atop Amon Hen, east of Parth Galen.

Ramdir has asked you to climb Amon Hen, defeating Orcs as you go, and to stand at the Seat of Seeing and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> across the river.Ramdir is at Hestil's camp near Parth Galen.

You have seen evidence of a large massing of Orcs on Amon Lhaw and should report it to Ramdir.Talk to Ramdir'How much do you know of this area, ${PLAYER}? Two hills rise on either side of the river and between them the torrent descends at Rauros. You can hear the falls from quite far away, such is the power of his voice as it echoes between the slopes of the hills. The names of these hills are Amon Hen, on this side of the river, and Amon Lhaw, on the far side.

'There are great stone seats on the crest of each hill, the Seat of Seeing on Amon Hen and the Seat of Hearing on Amon Lhaw. In days of old, great kings came to sit in those high places and much was revealed to them.

'There is a massive Orc-presence upon Amon Hen, just to the east of here. Climb the hill, defeating as many of the Orcs as you can, and stand at the summit. If you <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> across the river, you may be able to see if Amon Lhaw is host to a similar Orc-presence. That will tell me with what we may deal.''It is as I feared, then: there are more Orcs on Amon Lhaw to reinforce the creatures that have already crossed the river. We cannot stay here. I need to convince Hestil that she and her friends need to move again.''I do not know what the great kings saw atop Amon Hen, at the Seat of Seeing, but I know what you may be able to see: if there is a gathering of Orcs across the river on Amon Lhaw. If there is such a gathering, we will know that the Orcs here are only an initial force, and they could be reinforced.

'Stand at the Seat of Seeing and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> across the river.'The cave of Wódscrafen has been quiet for ages, but recently there has been a sense of disturbance about that ancient place.North of Twickenburg is the highest point in the Wold, Cracabor, and over that hill is the ancient cave of Wódscrafen.

You should head to Wódscrafen and search for the soldier who went that way.Find the missing soldier near WódscrafenNorth of Twickenburg is the highest point in the Wold, Cracabor, and over that hill is the ancient cave of Wódscrafen.

You should explore the cave north of Twickenburg.Investigate the old caveThe cave of Wódscrafen can be found north of Twickenburg in the Wold.

You should explore the cave of Wódscrafen to find out what disturbed the dead there.Find the root of the disturbance in WódscrafenThe frightened soldier is outside of Wódscrafen in the Wold.

You should return to the frightened soldier and tell him of the Ringwraith you saw in Wódscrafen.Return to the frightened soldier'Just over the ridge north of this fort is a bog where the creatures seem different than they were a month or two ago. Something is affecting this swamp, and I suspect it has to do with an old cave around there -- the Wódscrafen.

'This cave has always been empty and quiet, but felt like a hallowed ground from before my time. I worry something wicked is happening in there, so I sent one of my men out to investigate, but he has not returned.

'Will you look for him, ${PLAYER}?''I could not do my duty! I have been standing here, trying to rally my courage, ever since the sergeant first sent me out. I cannot seem to go in....

'Do you feel that terrible shadow upon the very air?''A... a Nazgûl of Mordor was behind it all? I had heard of the Nazgûl's involvement in the sacking of Langhold.

'I suspect from your findings that the servants of Mordor are rallying allies. That is a disturbing thought, indeed....'Orcs have been hard at work chopping down trees and harvesting wood for their siege-weapons in Nîn-stazg.Orcs build siege-weapons in the forest south-east of Floodwend.

You should gather wood from the encampment where the Orcs have been chopping down trees.Collect wood in Nîn-stazg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The supplies you captured from the Orcs will be put to far better use in the hands of Floodwend's people. You did well to retrieve the wood stockpiles from the grip of Mordor.Orcs have been hard at work chopping down trees and harvesting wood for their siege-weapons in Nîn-stazg.'My lady Etta has sent us to protect the Thane. He should not go into battle, but he may observe the battle from here, should he wish it.''Look at them, tearing down our forest. We cannot let them go on!'The supplies you captured from the Orcs will be put to far better use in the hands of Floodwend's people. You did well to retrieve the wood stockpiles from the grip of Mordor.Thane Radwig of Floodwend and his mother Etta are not in agreement about the best approach for handling the enemies surrounding their town.Etta is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.

You should speak with Etta and hear her opinion.Speak with Etta and hear her counselSoldiers of Floodwend can be found guarding the three gates of the town.There is a tower behind the Floodwend Mead Hall that offers a view of the forest.

You should climb the tower and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for something unusual.

<rgb=#FF0000>You must perform an emote to advance this quest.</rgb>Radwig, Thane of Floodwend, awaits you in the Mead Hall.

You should speak with Radwig and tell him of the information you gathered.Return to Thane RadwigEtta is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.

You should speak with Etta.Speak with Etta'My mother and I are having a bit of a disagreement. I realize I am a newly-made Thane, but my father was a great man, and I aspire to do as he would have done. I believe we should ride out and meet our enemies on the field, and drive them from our lands.

'Mother, on the other hand, wishes to shelter and hide here in Floodwend. I do not think my father would have wished this, but I do not reject my mother's counsel lightly. Will you ask my people what they think?''I am Etta, the principal counsellor and advisor in all matters of Floodwend. My son is young yet to bear all of the responsibilities of a Thane, and so I help where I must.

'Radwig is not ready to ride into war, and war it is upon our fair fields and forests. We must invest all of our strength in defences, and dissuade the enemy from venturing near our city.

'I think you will find that many agree with me, if you ask around.''I can hear the howl of Wargs coming from the forest to the north-west. There are some odd sounds coming from the forest to our south, as well, but for the most part things have been quiet at this gate.

'I do not think the beasts will attack our city. I loathe sitting here idly and listening while they take over our forest. Why do we not ride out to rid our lands of the vile beasts?''Things have been very quiet... almost too quiet, if you ask me. I have not seen much of anything lately, neither enemy nor ally.

'Would you like to hear what I really think? The lack of Rohirrim coming to and from is more concerning than the lack of enemies.

'We should bolster our defences, and quickly, if you ask me. I do not know what enemies move about our lands, but I am worried.''The road to the south has been ominous for a while. I have been told the road towards the East Wall is crawling with Orcs and Uruks.

'A number of Orcs seem to have moved into the forest right outside Floodwend of late, and I would guess that they came from the East Wall. We have defences already set up in the forest to deal with any foes, so I believe we should be on our guard here in Floodwend.''I suppose that is fair, then. If nearly everyone agrees that we should bolster our defences, then bolster them we must.

'My mother was likely right in her counsel. I will follow her direction, but... perhaps you might be able to help me, since you are free to do as you will here.''I am glad my son came around. Seeing to our defences is the only wisdom at such a time.

'He wishes to be like his father, but his father died from his rash bravery.'The Easterlings have established a dangerous organization under the watch of the Sorcerer, making them a more deadly foe than ever. The council of the Sorcerer should be destroyed.The Sorcerer's Council resides in five towers throughout the large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr.

You should defeat each of the members of the Sorcerer's Council.Enter the Easterling encampment of Jóshkhin OrdaThe Sorcerer's Council resides in five towers throughout the large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr.

You should defeat each of the members of the Sorcerer's Council.Defeat a member of the Sorcerer's Council (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sergeant Guthferth stands guard at North-torr, just north of the city of Floodwend in the Wold.

You should speak with Guthferth.Return to Guthferth at North-torrThe Easterlings have established a dangerous organization under the watch of the Sorcerer, making them a more deadly foe than ever. The council of the Sorcerer should be destroyed.'I am grateful to you, ${PLAYER}. That council oversaw the Easterling battle strategy and were at the head of all enemy movements in the Wold.

'There are likely many more to come from the Undeep, but this will surely slow them down. This was no small victory! My own soldiers would be hard-pressed to execute such a bold plan.'Hestil asked Cúfaron to find another route through the East Wall that will improve their chances of survival.The pass to the Sutcrofts is located south-west of Parth Galen and has been barricaded by the Orcs.

You need to defeat the Orcs to allow Hestil's company to pass.Defeat Orcs at the Sutcrofts barricade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat an Orc-leader at the Sutcrofts barricade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cúfaron is waiting to speak with you.

You have defeated Orcs at the barricade into the Sutcrofts and should return to tell Cúfaron.'Now that these lands are full of Orcs and other dangers, Hestil has asked me to find another route through the East Wall. We had planned to keep going north, but that does not seem as safe as it would have been if this land were empty. Instead, it is crawling with Orcs, and those unnatural swert-hounds are not to be trifled with either. Of course, you know that: you fought some of them too.

'There may be another way through this land, ${PLAYER}. There is a canyon to the west that leads into an area of the Kingdom of Rohan known as the Sutcrofts. From a distance I saw the Orcs working to barricade that pass. I will go there with you, taking you by secret paths that I alone, as a hunter, can find!

'Then you will defeat some of the Orcs at the barricade. That way, if we remain unable to progress north, at least we will have another option available to us. Hestil is sure to be pleased with that possibility, even if it means going into Rohan. Better the horsemen than more Orcs!'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to the Sutcrofts Barricade in the East Wall when you accept this quest.</rgb>'Go to the pass into the Sutcrofts and defeat the Orcs at the barricade there. We need to keep that pass open to us in case we are not able to proceed north as Hestil had planned.''See? I have brought you here by hidden paths! I am a hunter of great skill and know how to move quickly through the wilderness.

'The barricade is just over there, ${PLAYER}. Defeat the Orcs that guard it, then return here to me when you are done.''You have returned from the pass into the Sutcrofts? I am glad you ran into little trouble there...only a few Orcs is all, correct?'

Cúfaron looks uncomfortable.

'While you were gone, I spoke with Hestil, and it appears that she does not want to explore the west option at all. It seems that she is willing to risk the northward journey and does not want to go into Rohan at all. She says the horsemen do not treat outsiders very kindly.

'I am sorry you went to the barricade for naught. I am all ready to rescue Drafli, if everybody else is ready.''Well done, ${PLAYER}! Now, if we must, my band can travel west into the Sutcrofts. I know Hestil does not wish to, but there may be no other way. The huge gathering of Orcs in the East Wall may require us to deal with the horsemen of Rohan instead.

'I will bring us back to Hestil's camp with my secret hunter knowledge of the best paths and trails to take throughout this land. I think I may remember the way... if you keep your eyes open and help me look for our footprints....'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Parth Galen in the East Wall when you complete this quest.</rgb>A party of Rohirrim headed south from the Wold to investigate the Orc presence in East Wall.Léomund is just south of the southern border of the Wold, in East Wall.

You have been told to assist Léomund in the East Wall against the Orcs.Find and speak to Léomund in East Wall'You fought back the Easterling assault, and devastated the Orcs encamped in the forest nearby who came from East Wall. A party left for East Wall to investigate the Orc presence there, and you should find them to continue what you started here. Should you find yourself in the area, you are always more than welcome here.

'Look for Léomund just over the border with the East Wall. He travelled with Mansig, and may be able to tell you where they are encamped.''You are here to help? Very good! Mansig and the rest of my people could use your help here in the East Wall!'The presence of traders from the town of Elthengels to Harwick has been all but extinguished. Etta worries that the tragedies befalling Thane Mildrith of Elthengels have thrown the farmers of the Norcrofts into a state of peril.Thane Mildrith resides in the town of Elthengels, in the Norcrofts, south-west along the road from Floodwend.

Etta has suggested that you lend aid to Thane Mildrith of Elthengels.Speak with Thane Mildrith of Elthengels, in the Norcrofts'Traders from the western towns were once a common sight along the road to Harwick. Of late, the troubles befalling Thane Mildrith and the people of Elthengels seems to have stalled all travel from that once calm land.

'The loss of supplies from the Norcrofts will have a terrible impact on us all. If you desire to offer your skills to Mildrith and her people, travel with haste, due west along the road.''Welcome to Elthengels, traveller. I must ask your pardon for the sorrowful state of matters. We mourn for the former Thane, my husband Pendrad, and our son Pendulf. Do not feel obligated to grieve on our behalf; it will help matters not for you to dwell in sadness.'The Easterlings have built a massive encampment on the bank of the Anduin river. This camp is growing at an alarming rate as more enemies flow down the river from the ford.The fallen Rohirrim watch-tower is in the north-east corner of their large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr.

You should search for a torch near the watch-tower and burn it to drive out the evil that dwells there.Use a torch to burn the Watch-tower Súth-torrSergeant Guthferth is rallying the defences of North-torr just north of Floodwend, attempting to hold back the flood of Easterlings threatening to drown the Wold in chaos.

