You should return to Adalmód now that you have done as he asked.Talk to Adalmód at the Mead Hall of Eaworth'You come from Faldham, seeking an audience with Reeve Ingbert? You have come at an inopportune time, ${CLASS}. Dark days are upon us, and the Reeve is wary of strangers.

'As well, he is closeted in discussion with his son, Lord Ingmar. We expect to fall under siege by Orcs at any time, and they debate the best strategy to deal with them.

'If you desire to help -- and perhaps to prove your friendship to Eaworth -- you may put your talents to use aiding with our siege-preparations. Many of our guards are overtasked and in need of assistance.''You have shown courage and kindness in your efforts, ${PLAYER}, but I still cannot allow you to pass.'Lady Tóla summoned you to her house so that she could express her gratitude for your kindness and make a request of you.Adalmód stands guard outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.

You should speak with Adalmód to gain access to the Mead Hall of Eaworth.Talk to Adalmód outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth'Alas, ${PLAYER}, you have no doubt learned that we are facing a siege by Orcs from the Misty Mountains. Théoden King has decreed a ban on the hunting of Orcs in Rohan, which my husband's father is rightly hesitant to break.

'Nevertheless, Ingmar, my husband, desires to earn glory in battle and counsels his father to defend our lands by allowing him to lead an assault on the Orcs. I fear that if he does this thing, he will not return, and I will be left a widow, only newly married.

'Ingmar's grandmother is Reeve Ingbert's chief counselor and speaks wisdom on behalf of Théoden King's decree. Perhaps if you speak with her, she can help to convince the Reeve of the wisdom of preparing our defences here at Eaworth, rather than send my husband to meet the enemy on the open field. Will you do this?''Hold, ${CLASS}. Did I not say the Reeve was not to be disturbed?'Free-roaming aurochs-bulls could provide meat and hides for the entire town of Eaworth.Hunt aurochs-bulls in the Entwash ValeAurochs-bulls can be found throughout the Entwash Vale, but especially in the herds to the south and the east of Eaworth.

