Elfmar and the Elfward must be notified that you have defeated the commanders of the attacking army.Speak to Thane Elfmar at the mead hall gates'I will gather up the others when the last enemy has been driven back, and we can discuss matters when all is quiet again.''The enemy forces have reached the threshold of Faldham. The Elfward have  taken up positions around the perimeter to defend our borders, but they will need your assistance.

'I expect the first waves to come from the north. Ride with me as we watch the northern borders. Take courage, and fight well.''The initial surge of riders has been dealt with, and I will be able to hold the North-east edge on my own.

'Nothwulf was protecting the perimeter of the farms a short distance to the south, I would ask that you see to his success there.''Elfmar holds the east? Then we must defend the other borders! Will you ride out to meet the enemy at my side?''I am pleased to have you along with me, ${PLAYER}. Let us show these invaders the merit of the Elfward!''We still hold the southern edge intact, the enemy shall not penetrate from this side while I remain vigilant.

'The enemy will try to find another way around our defences. Osin will need your aid to the west, while I remain behind to watch the flank.''To the west, I spotted several bands of Orcs headed towards Faldham. They seem to be pressing from every flank.

'I came at once. I require your aid if we are to dispose of the attacking foes.''Make haste, friend! Langfrith awaits at the mead hall entrance, to the north.''Exceptional work at the borders, ${PLAYER}. Few Orcs have made it this far into the village.

'I noticed a few of the invaders shouting about their war-chieftains, commanding from just north of the mead hall. Defeat this Urbhár and this Botglim, and throw the attacking force into chaos.''The invading forces are in utter disarray. The loss of their leaders has caused great chaos, resulting in many of their riders and infantry retreating back north, towards Elthengels.

'The Elfward continue to drive back those intent on pursuing the assault, but I believe we have saved the village and its people.'You have accompanied Getfleda, a girl of Eaworth, to help break up a fight between two of her friends, Brunstan and Sperling.Talk to Getfleda.Talk to GetfledaTalk to Brunstan and Sperling.Hear Brunstan's side of the storyHear Sperling's side of the storyTalk to Getfleda and let her know what her friends had to say.Talk to GetfledaTalk to the children observing the fight between Brunstan and Sperling and learn if any of them saw what happened.Talk to the children observing the fight between Brunstan and SperlingTalk to Getfleda.Talk to Getfleda'Let us talk somewhere else....''Oh, you must hurry, kind ${CLASS}! Brunstan and Sperling will surely harm each other if they continue fighting!''Sperling has accused me of stealing the toy sword his father gave him, but I tell you I did not! I am no dishonourable dog that would steal from his friends!

'Sperling lent me the sword, and I returned it... I swear it! He only blames me because he does not want to blame himself for the loss of it.''Brunstan is a liar and a thief! My father gave me a wooden practice sword before he went away to fight, and I let Brunstan play with it... now it is gone.

'He swears that he returned it to me, but I swear he did not! He is a liar without honour!''Oh my! I do not know who to believe! I cannot believe that Brunstan would be so dishonourable, but I also do not believe that Sperling would accuse him without cause!

'Perhaps one of the other children saw something... would you ask them?''N-nay, I saw nothing! I-I....'

The child sighs and looks distraught.

'I cannot tell a lie. I borrowed the sword from Brunstan and was playing in the burned yards to the south. When my mother called me to dinner, I forgot the toy and left it behind. When I went back, I could not find it again.

'Please, do not tell Sperling and Brunstan! They are both bigger than me!''I heard and saw nothing... I swear it!''I never liked either one of them to begin with... I am only here to watch the fight.''I am pretty sure I saw someone playing with Sperling's sword down in the southern part of the city, but it was not Brunstan.''If Brunstan stole Sperling's sword, he should be fed to the Orcs. Sperling's da gave him the sword before he went away....''Oh dear, you say that another of my friends was actually to blame for the loss of Sperling's sword? Oh my....'You have led the good master and his protector into the mountains, as you were asked. The Straight Stair and the Winding Stair are behind, and the Tunnel lies ahead.The nice master is near the top of the Winding Stair, looking out upon the dead city below.Talk to nice MasterThere is one more stair to climb before the hobbitses can put the Winding Stair behind them.

And then?Climb the final stair with the hobbitsesThe nice Master and the other hobbit need to rest.Talk to nice MasterThe nice master has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>lie down</rgb>, at least for a little while.<rgb=#00FF00>Lie down</rgb> and get some sleep, as the nice Master requestedWait for the hobbitses to become absorbed in their conversation.Wait until the hobbitses are deep in conversationYou have business ahead. Leave the hobbitses behind and go to the east, beneath the tower.Sneak to the east, towards the tower, preciousSméagol is here. What does he want? Why is he in my way, gollum, gollum?Talk to Sméagol, preciousThe tunnel lies ahead. You need to go there, precious, and make certain all is ready!Sneak to the east, towards the tunnel, gollumSméagol is back. He doesn't have the nerve to get the Precious!Talk to Sméagol and tell him this will retrieve the PreciousShe will help us get the Precious, yes she will, gollum, gollum!Sneak east to the tunnel, preciousSméagol is back, and he wants to keep us from the Precious! Only we know what we must do, gollum!Talk to Sméagol outside the tunnelWe have to tell Her what we have brought. She will be so pleased, gollum, gollum!Enter the tunnel, gollum, gollum!We have to find Her, and tell her what we have brought with us!Find Her, precious, and tell Her what we have brought!'Sam and I need to rest from the climb before we move on to this tunnel you mentioned, Sméagol. I am exhausted, and I do not want us to pass beneath that tower without recovering whatever strength we may.

'You should <rgb=#00FF00>lie down</rgb> and get some sleep as well, Sméagol. We will all need our rest for what lies ahead, I imagine.''No, precious, don't go this way! We mustn't hurt the nice Master!

'We swore, precious! We swore to serve the nice Master! Do not try to hurt him! Must not, gollum! Gollum!''Please don't go inside the tunnel, gollum, gollum! We can't bring the hobbitses to Her! She'll eat them, yes, not just the fat one but the Master too, and Sméagol can't do that to them! No, precious, no! Don't go to Her!''Thank you for bringing us this far, Sméagol. I know it cannot have been easy for you to come this way again, or to creep so near to the city below, but you have done right by your promise.

