'I need you to go out into the Vale and collect some materials for me. We will need arms and armour to spare, but for that we will need materials to forge with.

'You can mine ore in the cliffs of the Vale. Wood can be found in the marshes to the north. When you have gathered the materials, return here to me.''Ah, you have returned! The materials you have brought will go far to aid my people.

'If you still desire to aid us, I have more tasks for you.'Langfrith, of the Elfward, has scouted a tribe of Orcs rallying within the mountain passes to the east and worries that Faldham will be surrounded when the anticipated siege begins.The Orc tribe has been scouted along the south-east pass leading into the mountains.

Langfrith has asked you to drive back the Orcs encroaching on the lands south-east of Faldham.Defeat Orc scouts at the camp to the east (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orc ravagers at the camp to the east (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orc defilers at the camp to the east (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Langfrith prepares outside the mead hall of Faldham, west of the mountain pass.

Langfrith is expecting news of your infiltration of the Orc camp.Speak to Langfrith about the Nink-hai Orcs'The Elfward alone must defend the people of Faldham. Reeve Athelward sits fortified to the north, unwilling to send aid to us, and the people under Thane Mildrith's watch have been trampled in the wake of the Orcs heading west. When their wicked blades turn towards Faldham, it will come from the north and from the west. My thoughts dwell ever in a different direction, I look towards a danger from the east.

'We have seen much activity of Orcs in the mountain passes leading towards the East Wall. I fear these Orcs plan to ambush our flanks when the force from the north approaches. We cannot allow ourselves to become surrounded. Strike against the Orcs that dwell along the pass to the east, and we shall observe how they respond.''The Nink-hai seem shaken by our unexpected interference. I expected the Orcs to retaliate, but they seem satisfied to have shrunk back into the mountains beyond our watch. Perhaps they had not expected such strong resistance from the residents of Faldham.

'Fine work, ${PLAYER}. This will be one less opponent to concern ourselves with in the coming hours.'Finish the quests of Langhold.Finish the quests of Langhold.Finish the quests of Langhold.Complete all of Langhold's questsFinish the quests of the East Wall.Finish the quests of the East Wall.Finish the quests of the East Wall.Complete all of the East Wall's questsThere is much to do while travelling through the lands of the Eastemnet.Complete Quests of the East Wall deedComplete Quests of the Entwash Vale deedComplete Quests of the Eaves of Fangorn deedComplete Quests of Langhold deedComplete Quests of the Norcrofts deedComplete Quests of the Sutcrofts deedComplete Quests of the Wold deedComplete quests in the Eaves of Fangorn.Complete quests in the Eaves of Fangorn.Complete quests in the Eaves of FangornComplete quests in the Entwash Vale.Complete quests in the Entwash Vale.Complete quests in the Entwash ValeComplete quests in the Norcrofts.Complete quests in the Norcrofts.Complete quests in the NorcroftsComplete quests in the Sutcrofts.Complete quests in the Sutcrofts.Complete quests in the SutcroftsComplete quests in the Wold.Complete quests in the Wold.Complete quests in the WoldAdalmód asked you to aid the guards of Eaworth as they prepare for the coming Orc-siege.Botulf has asked you to go throughout the city, reassuring the people of Eaworth that the city shall stand and all will be well.Botulf stands near the road leading from the Mead Hall of Eaworth to the northern part of the city.

You should let Botulf know that you have brought reassuring words to the people of Eaworth.Talk to Botulf at Eaworth'This is madness! Orcs ravage our walls, burn our homes, and prepare to lay siege to the city, and our Reeve does nothing!

'Ah, I must beg your pardon, stranger. I am frustrated by the apparent inaction of Reeve Ingbert, but forsooth, Théoden King is to blame. The king has declared that we are not to hunt Orcs within our own borders, and so the Orcs hunt us.

'Many here have lost their homes and all they own, and others fear the same will happen to them. Perhaps you could go to the people of Eaworth and reassure them that our city will stand strong?''You speak truly. My house yet stands, burned though it be. We shall persevere!''Gone, it is all gone... yet my family is safe. There is some consolation in that.''I have friends who have lost everything. The south walls lie in ruins, yet you say we are not to be afraid?

'I am Rohirrim, so I will fight for my home, but will Reeve Ingbert do nothing to avert the attacks of the Orcs?''You come to give me comfort? My home stands but barely, and all I own is lost. Your comfort is too little too late.''I am sure that you are right. Ingbert and Ingmar shall come to a decision, and I am certain that it will save us all!''We are Rohirrim. We will not cower in the face of defeat. We will continue!''My wife, my children, they are safe... that is all I desire. Ingbert shall see that Eaworth stands.''I have seen much death and injury since the Orcs came. I am called to comfort the wounded and the families of the slain. It is small comfort you bring to me, but I thank you for it anyway.''Your kindness is appreciated, ${PLAYER}. While I do not believe myself that we can stand while Ingbert and Ingmar are at odds one with another, the people must feel secure.'The Orcs have a collection of dangerous powder kegs within their camp. To overcome the threat of the Nink-hai's black powder kegs, it is possible to ignite their fuses while they remain within the enemy's grasp.The Nink-hai powder kegs can be found within their camp, east of Faldham.Ignite powder kegs at the Nink-hai campThe Nink-hai powder kegs can be found within the Orc camp east of Faldham.

You plan to disrupt the Nink-hai plans by detonating their stores of dangerous powder kegs.Ignite powder kegs at the Nink-hai camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Langfrith can be found outside the meadhall of Faldham.

Langfrith awaits the results of your actions with the Nink-hai powder kegs.Speak to Langfrith about the ignited powder kegsThe Nink-hai have stockpiled barrels of explosive black powder and threaten to use them against the walls of Faldham. Having infiltrated the Orc encampment, you have gained an opportunity to ignite the powder kegs while they still remain within enemy territory.'You return unscathed, remarkable! When I heard the sound of each blast resounding across the plains, I feared for your safety. I can see now that you had matters under your control.

