'Be careful of your actions, ${CLASS}, for they may put you in a position you do not want to be in....'Hwitmon awaits news of your venture with Inhild to Randgar's farm.Hwitmon can be found at his home within Cliving.

Hwitmon awaits news of your venture to Randgar's farm with his daughter, Inhild. You have decided to reveal the truth to him.Speak to Hwitmon and reveal the truth'What makes you hesitate, ${PLAYER}? Is there something you have not told me?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Accepting and completing this quest will reveal the truth of Inhild's actions to her father. You will not be allowed to complete the quest 'Inhild's Wish' to deceive Hwitmon.</rgb>You explain to Hwitmon that Randgar feigned his death as part of a scheme to run off with Inhild, because the two were in love.

'This is intolerable, ${PLAYER}! How dare they? That miserable crofter Randgar puts my dear Inhild's life in danger! He always seemed a rough character, but I never imagined he would take my daughter from me.

'Thank you for revealing the truth to me. I vow to find my daughter again some day, and we will have all of this foolishness sorted out. I owe you much for your honesty, ${PLAYER}.'Spiders are naught but the spawn of utter evil, covering all they conquer in sticky, smothering webs.Defeat spiders in the EastemnetSpiders are naught but the spawn of utter evil, covering all they conquer in sticky, smothering webs.Defeat spiders in the EastemnetReeve Ingbert, still undecided about what course of action he should take regarding the Orcs in the Entwash Vale, has put his faith in your advice.

<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. The other will fail. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>Lady Góda stands near Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.

Ingbert has asked you to speak with his mother, Lady Góda, and learn the heart of her arguments.Talk to Góda in the Mead Hall of EaworthReeve Ingbert stands near Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.

You should consider Góda's argument. If her reasoning seems preferable to Ingmar's, you should speak with Reeve Ingbert on her behalf.Talk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth'My mother, ${PLAYER}, is a strong woman and wise. She has long been my chief counsellor and has never led me astray. In the matter of the Orcs, she counsels that we refrain from attacking them directly, for Théoden King has forbidden it.

'My loyalty and duty to the King dictates that I comply, yet I am uneasy. Eaworth itself has been raided on numerous occasions, and large numbers of Orcs amass not far from here in clear preparation to lay siege upon us. Why, then, should we refrain from attacking them first, as Ingmar would do?

'Alas, I know not the answer. Speak with my mother and learn the heart of her arguments. Let me know if you decide that hers is the wisest course.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. The other will fail. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>'I understand that Tóla sent you to speak with me, to help you convince my son to refuse Ingmar's plan. Indeed, as you have heard, I have been doing just that.

'The argument is moot, for Théoden King's law must rule our decisions. This land is ours only by his command, and we owe our allegiance to him through unbreakable oaths.

'Understand, I do not debate Ingmar's position. If we were permitted, I would be the first to say "Strike at the heart of the Enemy!" But we ARE restricted. That is why I propose that we strengthen our defences here in Eaworth. Defending a bastion such as this would reduce our losses well beyond what we would see assaulting the Orcs.

'My grandson questions my reasoning, citing the safety of the outlier farms, but many of those farms have already been abandoned, and many more refugees arrive in Eaworth every day. I believe his lust for glory has blinded his sensibilities.

'The greater wisdom says that we should defend Eaworth with all our might. Word has already been sent to Thornhope, our city in the north...I expect further aid from Thane Wulfrad at any moment. Will you defend my position with Ingbert? Consider it well.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>You take a moment to convey your support of Góda's position to Reeve Ingbert.

'I understand my son's desire to ride into battle...in my youth, I was much the same. Few beyond Rohan comprehend what it is to earn glory in the heat of battle.

'However, my mother's advice, as you say, seems the greater. My mind is decided: we shall follow Lady Góda's advice.'Reeve Ingbert, still undecided about what course of action he should take regarding the Orcs in the Entwash Vale, has put his faith in your advice.

<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. The other will fail. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>Lord Ingmar stands near Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.

Ingbert has bidden you speak with Ingmar regarding his plan, to learn whether the greater wisdom is to follow his son into battle.Talk to Ingmar in the Mead Hall of EaworthIngbert stands near Ingmar in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.

If you believe that Ingmar's reasoning is greater than Góda's, you should bring your support of his plan to Ingbert.Talk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth'How I yearn to ride forth with my son against these Orcs who dare intrude upon the lands of the House of Léotharn! Yet I know in my age that my desire, like Ingmar's, is driven more by a lust for glory than for the care of my people.

'I am torn, for I do see reason behind Ingmar's arguments, but is it greater than my mother's? The lives that would be saved by following my mother's advice would be great, but would it resolve the issue of Orcs marauding in the Entwash Vale?

'Speak with Ingmar and learn the full reason behind his plan, then return to me, and I will make my decision.''Bah! We stand here and debate the wisdom of attacking the Orcs as if driving away invaders in the Entwash Vale could possibly be the motive behind Théoden King's edict.

'There is rumour that Saruman the White, ever the friend and ally of the Rohirrim, has subjected a tribe of Orcs beneath his hand... surely, these are the Orcs which the King protects, yet the invaders are from the Misty Mountains!

'What glory is there in holing up behind these walls, waiting for the Orcs to burn them down around us and kill every man, woman, and child within? It is cowardice!

'Understand, my grandmother is indeed a wise woman, but she is also stubborn. She does not comprehend the opportunity that we have! The Orcs have not yet mustered enough strength to lay siege to Eaworth... if we strike now, we can cripple their efforts and drive the mongrels forth from the Entwash Vale.

'There is no safety within these walls of wood. Fire burns wood, and the Orcs are master wielders of fire. Will you support my position with my father? Perhaps you may bring him courage and wisdom.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. The other will fail. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>You take a moment to convey your support of Ingmar's plan, igniting the passion for glory within Ingbert's heart.

'Aye! I will not remain holed up within these walls like a coward!'

His manner calms a little.

'It is true that we have the opportunity to scatter these Orcs like chaff on the wind... but only if we attack first. I have made my decision.'Impressed by your courage and willingness to assist the people of Eaworth, Goldwine has decided to offer you another task.The blacksmith's forge is in Eaworth, near the Mead Hall.

Goldwine asked you to forge spears for the guards of Eaworth.The guards of Eaworth can be found throughout the city.

Goldwine asked you to bring the spears you crafted to the guards of Eaworth.Goldwine stands guard near the blacksmith's forge in Eaworth.

You should let Goldwine know that you have delivered the spears to the guards of Eaworth.Talk to Goldwine'I am impressed by your courage, ${PLAYER}. The Vale has become a dangerous place, and you braved it to bring us the materials we need to arm ourselves for the siege.

'If you are willing, I have one more task for you. Use the ore and branches you gathered to craft spears at the blacksmith's forge.

'When this is done, deliver the spears to the guards throughout the city, then return to me.''Thank you for this spear, ${PLAYER}. The shaft of my old one had been cracked for some time.''This, at least, is a sign that we will defend ourselves if attacked. I only hope that Lord Ingmar convinces his father to take swifter action.''Be of good cheer, ${PLAYER}! This spear shall skewer Orcs before long!''A fresh spear... that is well. We shall soon be overrun by Orcs.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I was in need of a fresh spear!''Thank you for your services, ${PLAYER}. We shall be prepared for whatever course of action Reeve Ingbert decides upon.'After hearing from both Lord Ingmar and Lady Góda, you brought your support of Góda's plan to Reeve Ingbert.Lady Góda stands near Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.

