Norbald needs to know that you have repelled several of the mounted Orcs approaching Faldham.Speak to Norbald at Enswith's farm'The hour has come, ${PLAYER}. We have received no answer from Théoden King to our request for reinforcements, and Reeve Athelward has made it known that our fate is now our own. Retreat is not an option, we must stand against the first waves of the coming storm.

'I think now upon my father's training and his wisdom. I must rally my people, and trust in the great skill of the Elfward. I ask that you ride north and assist Norbald with the defences. You have done much to help the people of Faldham, we must not let it fall in its most crucial moment!''You are not a moment too soon! The first waves of the Uruk force have begun to arrive in earnest. We must hold off the enemy's riders, and grant Thane Elfmar and the others a moment to rally.''Fine work, that ought to slow the enemy's advance. We have stopped their first efforts but we must not lower our guard, there will surely be more on the way.'Thane Elfmar and his Elfward have prepared for the defence of Faldham. Outnumbered, the skill, determination, and focus of each man will surely be tested.Thane Elfmar awaits at the mead hall of Faldham.

The Elfward of Faldham will have all of their abilities tested in defending their home.Defend Faldham with the help of the ElfwardElfmar can be found at the mead hall of Faldham.

Thane Elfmar wishes to discuss the outcome of the battle, and the future of Faldham.Speak to Thane Elfmar'The task set before us may be the most important challenge that the Elfward will ever encounter. We ride now to meet our destiny, perhaps for the final time. We must not let the defences of Faldham fall, or all will be lost to us.''Prepare yourself, ${PLAYER}. United, we shall face our enemies.''Victory for the Elfward! The people of Faldham will continue to live and prosper free from the tyranny of the White Hand Uruks and their cruel master. 

