'If you wish to be of aid to the Eastemnet, journey west to Eaworth and offer your services to Reeve Ingbert. I am sure that he will be grateful for the assistance. The people of Faldham must carry on under their own defences, but we will not forget your aid.''Hold there, stranger! You come at a dire time and the doors of the Mead Hall are closed.'You helped break up a fight between Getfleda's friends Brunstan and Sperling, but the troubles have not yet passed. Both boys are convinced that the other is to blame for the loss of Sperling's toy sword.Sperling's toy sword is likely somewhere in the southern part of Eaworth.

