'I-I will do so... I-I will live, if only to have my revenge upon the beasts.''I should thank you, stranger, for by living I may be avenged for the deaths of my family.'You rescued Éorpwald, a wounded Rohirrim warrior, from Thornhope and helped him reach the relative safety of Béortnoth's camp.Bidroi, Grish, and Rûkaz can all be found within the walls of Thornhope.

Éorpwald asked you to take revenge upon Bidroi, Grish, and Rûkaz, three lieutenants of the invading forces, on behalf of Thane Wulfrad's family.Defeat GrishDefeat BidroiDefeat RûkazÉorpwald is encamped outside the walls of Thornhope.

You should return to Éorpwald with news of your victory.Talk to Éorpwald outside of Thornhope'Ah, ${PLAYER}! I did not... have the time to properly thank you... for your assistance.

'The affront against my Thane and my people is unforgiveable. Many died -- men, women, children, young and old alike -- butchered... by the Orcs. There were three of the creatures in particular that I would see slaughtered where they stand. They deserve no less.

'These three -- Bidroi, Grish, and Rûkaz -- murdered Thane Wulfrad's family... and would have slain Béortnoth as well, had the giant not come and saved him. Aye, Béortnoth is not as mad as he seems.

'Would you enter Thornhope and bring these three devils to justice?''Ah... I am satisfied then. You have my gratitude, ${PLAYER}.'Goldwine informed you that Lady Góda wished to speak with you regarding her betrayal.Lady Góda is in her cell within the prison of Eaworth.

You should learn what Lady Góda wishes to say.Talk to Lady Góda'Ah, ${PLAYER}, it saddens all of us to learn that Lady Góda was party to the betrayal of the Entwash Vale. Vale-minded it is.

'Be that as it may, Lady Góda wishes to speak with you... perhaps to state her case, though I fear Reeve Ingbert is stung to the heart and will not relent.

'You will find Góda in her cell in the prison.''Ah, you have come. Nay, I do not wish to atone for my so-called crimes, for I do not believe I have committed one.

'You, however, have committed a great atrocity against my people. You have caused my son and grandson to defy the laws of Théoden King, making them traitors to Rohan... and you have removed the favour of Gríma, who holds counsel with greater powers than our king.

'You know not what you have done, for great wrath shall now be poured out against us... now leave me to await our doom.'You rescued Frána, a minor nobleman of the House of Thornhope, who had hidden himself away during the Orcs' attack on the city.Some of Frána's comforts may yet be found near the Mead Hall of Thornhope.

Frána has rudely commanded you to find any of his comforts which may have survived the Orcs' attack and bring them back to him.Collect Frána's pillowCollect Frána's cloakCollect Frána's robeFrána is encamped outside the walls of Thornhope.

You should bring the items you found to Frána.'This is insufferable. My dear cousin, Béortnoth, is hardly in a position to lead our people... what remains of them. He persists in the belief that we should stay and fight for this ruin. Well, I will not suffer this discomfort any longer.

'Surely, some few comforts of mine survived the destruction of the city. Go into Thornhope and bring me whatever comforts you can scavenge. I simply refuse to sleep upon this hard ground for one more night.''I suppose I must be grateful. You have performed your duty well.

'These trifles must do, I suppose.'You arrived at Thornhope to find it in ruins, and its only known survivor -- Béortnoth, son of Wulfrad -- more than half mad.Fangorn lies to the west of Thornhope.

You should go near Fangorn and <rgb=#FF00FF>look</rgb> for signs of the eyes that Béortnoth claims he saw.Find a place to <rgb=#FF00FF>look</rgb> for the eyes Béortnoth sawYou should now <rgb=#FF00FF>look</rgb> for the eyes that Béortnoth claims he saw.<rgb=#FF00FF>Look</rgb> for the eyes Béortnoth claims he sawThane Béortnoth is camped near the ruins of Thornhope to the east.

You should return to Béortnoth and assure him that the trees do not have eyes and that they are not watching.Talk to Thane Béortnoth near ThornhopeThere is a wild look in Thane Béortnoth's eyes as he speaks.

'Shhh! Be silent! They will hear!'

He glances west towards Fangorn.

'The forest... it is watching! The trees have eyes... deep, deep eyes, full of sorrow. If we are not careful, it will come! Do you not see the eyes?''I tell you I SAW the eyes... while the tree was carrying me!'

He pauses, a look of confusion on his face.

'Trees cannot walk, can they? So no tree could have been carrying me. Was it a dream? I was sure it said its name was Blackthorn....'While searching the ruins of Thornhope for survivors, you find a clever servant who managed to avoid the Orcs.Talk to MáthildMáthild is hiding near the Mead Hall of Thornhope.

