You should speak with Wisewood.Talk to Wisewood'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. How goes your quest in Fangorn? You are a long way from home, my old friend.

'Tell me: why do you waste your time on mindless Orcs in some ragged old forest when there are more pressing issues at hand?''Your heroic efforts are needed elsewhere in Rohan. Do you not agree, my old friend? Think of the elderly Théoden King, surrounded by disloyal men.

'Surely you must wish to help the King of Rohan....''Yes, ${PLAYER}. These Orcs are not the real threat to Rohan. The King's nephew, Éomer, wishes to harm the King.

'You and I are old friends, are we not? You should trust me, ${PLAYER}, and go help the King free himself from his nephew's influence.

'Leave this forest at once. There is nothing for you here.'The old man's voice has grown cold and hard.

'You defy me! You are a fool. You could have left this forest alive, ${PLAYER}, but now you will die. Of this, you may be assured.''Hrumm....'

The Ent spoke! At least, you think it spoke. Regardless, a sound was made, possibly one to indicate approval of your actions on his behalf.

This is a good sign, but also a frustrating one; the Ents are slow to wake. It seems that it will take a lifetime of a mortal Man to rouse them as Gandalf wished....The Ent you encountered has a memory he wishes to impart upon you, for he is too sleepy to pursue his own interests.The Ent Baillas can be found towards the central southern edge of Fangorn Forest.

