You should speak with Gandalf.Talk to Gandalf upon Treebeard's Hill'I wish to speak with you about Fangorn, ${PLAYER}. I have great faith in your good sense, and I am relying heavily upon it now. I believe your deeds can do much to affect change here in these troubled times.''We do not have much time, but I think you will want to hear my tale. Will you not stay for a spell, ${PLAYER}?''Does that satisfy your curiosity about the fate of the young hobbits? They are in good hands now, safe as can be. I am deeply relieved that they came to no harm.

'As for you... will you stay here and do what deeds you can? The forest may never be the same, but I believe your actions will change it for the better.'Now that his mind is beginning to clear, Thane Béortnoth recalls seeing smoke and ashes in the air near the eaves of Fangorn when he was wandering back to Thornhope from the forest.The place where Béortnoth recalled seeing the ashes and smoke lies to the west of Thornhope.

Thane Béortnoth has asked you to investigate the cause of the smoke he saw.Investigate the smoke and ashes near the eaves of Fangorn'${PLAYER}, it occurs to me now that I recall seeing smoke and ashes in the air near the eaves of Fangorn while I was wandering back from Blackthorn's grove. Now that I consider it, it seems strange, for the forest there was not burned, and my folk seldom go so close to Fangorn.

'Will you journey to that place -- it is west of here -- and learn if my memories are true and not simply imaginings of my maddened mind?''Ah, ${PLAYER}, I have been waiting for you. Yes, I know you... and you know me, though you may not realize it yet.

'I have heard from Blackthorn, an Ent of Fangorn, that you have been aiding young Béortnoth of Thornhope. His hopes of restoring his home, alas, are in vain... at least until this War is ended and the Orcs are driven forth.

'Nevertheless, there are a few things you may yet do to hasten the victory of the Free Peoples in Rohan.'Tiny spiderlings crawl all over the Silkenhold of Fangorn, threatening to grow into larger, crueler, hungrier foes.Stairs lead up to a forebidding area near the Huorn you rescued in northern Fangorn.

