You should speak with Léofmar and hear his tale.Listen to Léofmar's taleLéofmar is in Fangorn.

You should speak with Léofmar.Reassure Léofmar that you do not think his crime so terribleYou should <rgb=#FF0000>whistle</rgb> for Léofmar's horse.

You must be standing near Léofmar in order to do this.

<rgb=#FF0000>You must perform an emote to advance this quest.</rgb>Léofmar is in Fangorn.

You should talk to Léofmar once more.Talk to Léofmar againYou should search for other sleeping Ents in the forest, heading north-east from Léofmar's location.Find a new sleeping Ent in the north'I will tell you my tale of woe, ${PLAYER}, but I promise that you will wish to undo all of the kindness that you have done for me when you hear of my cowardice.

'Let me tell you first that I am no soldier. I have never been a brave man. My duties in my home called me to take the city-watch for a night, and I did that duty at least, but I am ashamed to speak of what came after....'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'I will tell you all, ${PLAYER}. You will regret ever helping me; I know it.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'I rode my horse to the edge of the wood, but I would not let him follow me inside. I came here to hide... and to die. My poor steed should not meet the fate of a coward.'Léofmar's horse has responded at once to your summons, ready and willing to bear his master to safety.'My steed! I cannot believe it, ${PLAYER}. I cannot believe that you found him. I had not even hope that he was near, the foolish beast.'

You tell Léofmar of the small boating camp on the edge of Fangorn, where he will likely be welcomed with his bow and arrows.

'I will go there now, ${PLAYER}; thank you. I am blessed, not cursed, to have so many good folk and creatures looking after me. I will not be afraid anymore.'Another Ent sleeps here, surrounded by smoke, fires, and grief. What harries this poor creature's home?Léofmar will not survive for much longer without an antidote to the poison he ingested when eating the inedible berries.Plants that have mild anti-poison properties can be found throughout the forest near Léofmar.

You should pick medicinal plants in the hope that they will cure Léofmar.Collect potential medicinal plants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Léofmar is where you left him, sick and dying in the centre of Fangorn's eaves.

You should rush the medicine to Léofmar at once.Léofmar will not survive for much longer without an antidote to the poison he ingested when eating the inedible berries.'It was good of you to help, ${PLAYER}, but they will be back. A curse does not throw up its hands and abandon its purpose because of a minor setback.

'Death will take me, and I will be a tortured shade, haunted by my crimes. It is hopeless.'You gently feed the herbs to Léofmar, but you do not see any positive effect. His condition is unchanged.

'You see? It is the curse. Thank you for your goodness, ${PLAYER}, but you cannot stop my fate.'Bingo has grown very fond of Tanglemane already, and is ready to begin his ride across the vast fields of Rohan.Bingo wants to travel to the town of Cliving, in the Norcrofts of East Rohan, and has asked you to defeat the enemies of Rohan in the Wold and the Norcrofts as you journey.Defeat enemies of Rohan in the Wold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat enemies of Rohan in the Norcrofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo is outside the entrance to the town of Cliving in the Norcrofts, in East Rohan.Talk to Bingo outside the entrance to Cliving, in the NorcroftsWillem Whisker is outside the entrance to the town of Cliving in the Norcrofts, in East Rohan.Learn what is wrong with Willem WhiskerBingo is outside the entrance to the town of Cliving in the Norcrofts, in East Rohan.Talk to Bingo outside the entrance to Cliving, in the NorcroftsThe Mead Hall of Cliving is in the north-east corner of the town.

Bingo wants to walk to the Mead Hall of Cliving and learn the situation for adventurers in the Norcrofts.Walk to the entrance of the Mead Hall in ClivingEgwylf is outside the Mead Hall of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.Talk to Egwylf outside the Mead Hall of ClivingBingo is outside the Mead Hall of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.Talk to Bingo outside the Mead Hall of ClivingAgents of the Cult of the Blood Eye may have come to the town of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.

Egwylf asked you to search the town of Cliving for any sign of the agents of the Blood Eye.Find some sign that the agents of the Blood Eye are in ClivingYou found a brooch with a red gem on a log behind some tents in the eastern reaches of Cliving, and should pick it up.Pick up the Blood Eye brooch from behind the tentsEgwylf is outside the Mead Hall of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.

You found a brooch with a red gem abandoned in a corner of Cliving, behind some tents.Bingo is outside the Mead Hall of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.Talk to Bingo outside the Mead Hall of Cliving'It did not take long, but I have already become quite fond of Tanglemane! He is a gentle fellow, and very friendly. The ground does not seem to be very far down from here, and while I do not wish to take a tumble, if I did happen to bounce from the saddle I believe I would be quite all right. And he seems to have no interest in nipping at my hat or my person, which I very much appreciate.

'What a good boy you are, Tanglemane! Cuthbald shared something of the geography of Rohan with me, and I think our next destination should be the town of Cliving, in the Norcrofts to the south-west. I will concentrate on staying a-saddle, if you can fight any foes that cross our path, ${PLAYER}! Let us defeat enemies in the Wold and in the Norcrofts as we journey, and in that way our presence will be a boon for the good folk of Rohan!''I think our next destination should be the town of Cliving, in the Norcrofts to the south-west. I will concentrate on staying a-saddle, if you can fight any foes that cross our path, ${PLAYER}! Let us defeat enemies in the Wold and in the Norcrofts as we journey, and in that way our presence will be a boon for the good folk of Rohan!''I think our next destination should be the town of Cliving, in the Norcrofts to the south-west. I will meet you outside the entrance, if Tanglemane is amenable to the journey!''What a lovely ride! Nice work, Tanglemane! I think there is little question that you are truly the finest steed in all of Rohan! What do you say, ${PLAYER}? Do you think Tanglemane and I look quite at home galloping on the fields of Rohan?

'But what is wrong with Willem? He does not seem to be his usual self. Is everything all right, W.W.?''What is wrong with Willem? He does not seem to be his usual self. Is everything all right, W.W.?'You do not speak the language of lynxes, but even without that skill it is easy to understand what is wrong with Willem Whisker: he is jealous of Bingo's new friend, Tanglemane!Willem is jealous of all the attention Bingo is giving to Tanglemane. Anyone could see that.'Jealous? Willem, there is no reason for that! I have never had such a wonderful lynx-friend before, and ever since you joined our little band of companions I have never forgotten how lucky I am to have you by my side on this adventure!'

Bingo grimaces.

'Well, I might have forgotten it once, but in my defence I forgot a lot of things when I fell into the caverns beneath the Misty Mountains. But it won't happen again, Willem! Tanglemane is a new friend, it's true, but you're the only W.W. in this group! I think you two should get along, or it will just break my heart in two. Say something, ${PLAYER}!

'Well, for now we should go up to the Mead Hall in Cliving and see what there is to learn about this town. But I want you two to get along! This adventure will not be as fun if everyone has hurt feelings!''Hello again, adventurers.''Look who it is, ${PLAYER}!''I did not expect to see Egwylf again so soon! Her errand must have brought her back to Rohan with haste!''I did not expect to see the two of you again so soon, but the trail I followed has returned to Cliving. My errand in Stangard was brief; the men there will remain alert for my prey, but there are so few good men in Stangard I do not know if I should trust any net they might weave.

'There are forces at work in Rohan that seek to bring the kingdom low. It is with greatest shame that I tell you that not all of these evils come from without the borders. Some of the greatest evil is worked by men and women of Rohan! A cult calling itself the Blood Eye has allied itself with Orcs of the Black Land. I believe there are three agents of the Blood Eye active in Rohan; I have tracked two of them here to Cliving.

'Will you help me find them? You will know them by the brooches or necklaces they wear: each one bears a red gem, prominently displayed. They are certain to be hidden in out-of-the-way corners of the city, away from prying eyes. If this is too dangerous for your friend Bingo, I will understand. But I would welcome your aid.''A cult calling itself the Blood Eye has allied itself with Orcs of the Black Land. I believe there are three agents of the Blood Eye active in Rohan; I have tracked two of them here to Cliving.

'Will you help me find them? You will know them by the brooches or necklaces they wear: each one bears a red gem, prominently displayed. They are certain to be hidden in out-of-the-way corners of the city, away from prying eyes. If this is too dangerous for your friend Bingo, I will understand. But I would welcome your aid.''The Blood Eye? It sounds dangerous!'

Bingo shivers, and then clenches his fists together.

'I am not afraid, ${PLAYER}! If we can help Egwylf apprehend these villains, we should do what we can! I will keep an eye out for them here in Cliving, and you should do the same!''The two men I tracked to Cliving will look for hidden, out-of-the-way places somewhere in the city. Look for some sign of their presence!''We should search the city for some sign of these men! It sounds to me as if these agents of the Blood Eye intend no good for Rohan!''I think I saw something suspicious on the south-eastern side of the Mead Hall, behind some of the tents. Something red and bright caught the light and flashed in my eyes. I wonder what it was? I do not see it now, but perhaps if the light returned the red glinting object would reveal itself?''Did you find something?''Any luck yet? I have found nothing of interest, but it will not stop me from looking!''Oh, you should give that to Egwylf! I do not want it! I don't like the look of it one bit, not one little bit!''Did you and Bingo find any sign of the agents of the Blood Eye, ${PLAYER}?'

You hand Egwylf the brooch you discovered and tell her that it reminds you of the Rothstone, a similar piece of jewellery you encountered in your travels. She nods.

'I do not know where the Cult of the Blood Eye finds these treasures, but they prize red gems above all others and look for them exclusively. Still, I have found that the men who bear these brooches are not unwilling to leave them behind when they near capture. Without these identifiers, they become nearly invisible to my pursuit, but it is not a complete loss, friend. They use these gems as proof of their allegiance, and without such proof as this, what Orc will be willing to trust they are who they claim to be?

'So one of the men I followed has been effectively declawed. As for the other, his trail has gone cold. I would ask for your help and for Bingo's, if you continue to offer it!''The trail has gone cold. I would welcome your help to follow it!''I do not like the sound of this Blood Eye group, especially if its members are in league with Orcs! Who would wish to ally themselves with such terrible creatures? I know that I would not, not for anything!

'I do not know if I can be much help to Egwylf in this. After all, she is a skilled tracker and has followed these agents of the Blood Eye for what sounds like a long time. But we are adventurers, and if we can help her with her task, we definitely should do so! It is a pity that the trail has gone cold. Do you think she will be able to pick it up again? If so, it may make for an exciting chapter in my account of our journey!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'A Cold Trail' (Recommended Level: 85)</rgb>Having returned from Thrug-unur victorious, the mysterious old man reveals another task that is more vital to the Rohirrim than the death of any Orc or goblin.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance is meant to be run with Mounted Combat. It may be run on foot, but will be considerably harder.</rgb>The mysterious old man is at Éomer's Vengeance, near the eaves of Fangorn, in the Entwash Vale.

You should speak again with the mysterious old man if you are willing to defend the herd of wild horses.Let the mysterious old man know that you will defend the herdThe mysterious old man is at Éomer's Vengeance, on the eaves of Fangorn, in the Entwash Vale.

You should return to the mysterious old man with news of your success.Talk to the mysterious old man at Éomer's VengeanceThane Béortnoth is encamped beyond the walls of Thornhope, east of Éomer's Vengeance.

You should return to Thane Béortnoth and tell him of the mysterious old man.Talk to Thane Béortnoth outside of Thornhope'The true treasure of the Riddermark lies in one of its most royal bloodlines... the Mearas, lords of horses. While most of the wild horses of Rohan are not of pure Mearas stock, they all share in the bloodline, making them highly desirable to all.

'Long has Mordor raided the herds of Rohan, taking the black horses and slaughtering the rest. I have learned that Orcs from Mordor are preparing to attack a herd not far from here... to the south-east.

'You must not allow these noble beasts to be taken or slaughtered! Speak with me again if you are willing to go to their defence.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance is meant to be run with Mounted Combat. It may be run on foot, but will be considerably harder.</rgb>'You must hurry if you are to save the horses!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance is meant to be run with Mounted Combat. It may be run on foot, but will be considerably harder.</rgb>'You discovered the source of the smoke and ashes? You say that a battle was fought there and that the bodies of the Orcs were burned? That would mean the Rohirrim were victorious.

'This old man you speak of sounds much like Saruman... it is said he goes to and fro in such disguise; however, why would he send you to kill the captain of the goblins if he is behind the invasion as you say?

