'I know not when it will fall, but Snowbourn will be prepared!'The Orcs have erected sizeable camps near Walstow, and Winsig fears the fate that will befall her town if they are left unchecked.Tents can be found inside the Orc camps to the north and south of Walstow.Burn Orc-tents (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thanks to your efforts, the Orc camps burn brightly. This is surely a sign of better days to come for Walstow.CompletedYou have discovered numerous tents about the Orc camps. They appear shoddily made, and would likely burn with little effort. You should light them ablaze for the good of Walstow.Thanks to your efforts, the Orc camps burn brightly. This is surely a sign of better days to come for Walstow.Winsig wants you to aid her in creating grim standards for Walstow. At Fastred's command, Orc heads shall only occupy one location in the Sutcrofts - the tip of a pike.Orcs and their heads can be found in the camps of Ufum-mau and Ash Durub, located to the south-west and west of Walstow, respectively.Behead Orcs in the south camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect spears from Orcs in Ash Durub or Ufum-mau (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Winsig can be found in the Mead Hall of Walstow.Talk to Winsig'These Orcs know nothing of retreat - they will throw themselves at our feet until finally we wither and fall.

'To the west, Fastred employs a far more terrifying tactic - he makes of our enemies' heads grim standards that litter the ground as reminders to his foes that he is not to be crossed.

'Whether the Orcs pay this any heed, I know not. However, I know that Snowbourn stands still, and Walstow enters its fleeting throes. I would have us employ this strategy in Walstow... as gruesome as it is.

'Travel to the Orc camps of Ash Durub and Ufum-mau to the west and south-west of Walstow - take a trophy of each Orc's head, and steal their spears. Upon your return, we will mount them about town.''While such a vicious show of force is not normally my favoured choice, if we are to survive, I feel nothing can be lost by imitating Fastred.

'His thirst for destruction has made an impression on the Orcs and if they could feel such a thing as fear when approaching Snowbourn, I am certain they would.

