Fastred wishes to hear Gísling's thoughts on the note you discovered.Talk to Gísling in SnowbournFastred can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

Gísling bade you return to Fastred with his response.'${PLAYER}, if you have a moment, I must speak to you.

'We have aided Reeve Fastred in every manner I can think of, but perhaps there is more yet to be done here. I cannot help but feel that my presence here has been less than welcome - perhaps Fastred thinks ill of my father and me for further burdening this settlement.

'Speak to Fastred, and see if we can aid him in any other task. I would not wish my years of service to be tainted by a decision that had to be made.''Ah, ${PLAYER}. It is good that you have returned.

'While you were aiding the people of Snowbourn, a man came to me and spoke of a deeply troubling matter. He claimed that an agent of the Enemy had taken root among my people - a most serious accusation to be certain. I shall not allow my people to be brought to ruin by anything, especially not a foolish defector.

'He claimed to have seen this spy poisoning food-stores about town, and lurking about the oven to the east of the Mead Hall. Start your search there, and report your findings to me.''What is this you have brought me?'

Fastred's face sinks and then tightens in distress as he reads the note.

'This... this doesn't make any sense. Gísling is the son of my most trusted Thane. Could he really be behind such a plot?

'Go to Gísling at once. I wish to know what he would say to such accusations.''How can you believe this, ${PLAYER}? My father and I have fought tirelessly for the safety of the Sutcrofts and for the good of Rohan. Why would I throw such labours away so brashly?

'Someone is trying to pit Fastred against us, I am certain of it. I know not who, but the Reeve has not been himself since the death of his father, Dagred. I think him vulnerable to such deceptions, though he will protest.

'We need to be very cautious in our approach to this, ${PLAYER}. Return to Fastred and tell him what I have said. I can only hope that my years of service loyal to Dagred and the King can speak for me.''Aye, I am well aware of Gísling's efforts in the past. Such a note troubles me greatly, though, and in these dark times, I cannot be too careful about those I allow within Snowbourn. 

'I fear that inaction is the greater of two evils in this situation, but I have many things to consider. Gísling may speak true or he may not - I will take action as I see fit to protect my people.'You have come across a most peculiar sight - a strange man appears to be riding an avanc eastward.A strange man sits atop an avanc in the distance - you should speak to him, for surely he is an interesting fellow.Talk to the strangerThe stranger is located in western Sutcrofts along the shore by the Entwade.Talk to the strangerYou have discovered a peculiar man who appears to be riding an avanc. You should speak with him.'Greetings! I am Rook, a Wizard of Dunland.

'While I would not normally stoop to asking for aid, it seems my avanc has grown tired on our journey eastward to learn of more magics from the Easterlings.

'If you would help me, I would be happy to reward you with the finest of treasures. By the way, stranger, you look familiar... have we met?'Winsig has lamented the lack of supplies since the Orc-invasion of the Sutcrofts and believes that the Orc-fortifications might prove useful to the people of Walstow once they are dismantled.Orc-barricades can be found in the Orc-camps to the north and south-west of Walstow.

Winsig wants you to destroy the Orc-barricades and collect wood-scraps from the wreckage.Destroy Orc-barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect wood-scraps from dismantled Orc-fortifications (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Winsig can be found in the Mead Hall of Walstow.

You should return to Winsig with news of your success.Talk to Winsig'The Orcs have made a great effort to reinforce their new-found holdings in the Sutcrofts. They brought a significant amount of supplies in through the East Wall before we were able to contain them.

'Following the sacking of Hytbold to the north, they had even more materials with which to work. I want you to raze their structures and return with some of their stolen wood. We can use it to bolster our own defences and keep Walstow standing.

'Carry as much as you can and return to me!''Such foolish creatures... we shall benefit greatly from these resources. I will have my men begin work on erecting even more defences along our borders.'In Fastred's absence, Snowbourn must be provisioned and supplied for the coming war.Piles of logs can be found near felled trees outside the walls, while spears and leather can be gathered within the city.

Léofhelm has asked you to gather the materials needed to supply Snowbourn.Collect piles of logs outside Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect leather-scraps in Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect spears in Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Léofhelm can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

You should return to Léofhelm and let him know that you have done as he asked.'If you wish to aid us while you wait for Fastred's return, I have a task for you.

'The Riders have been facing more opposition in the fields as of late, and we constantly need more materials for repairs to the farmsteads, as well as new arms and armour for the Riders themselves.

'If you would, gather wood, spears, and leather scraps for me, and I will send them along to the appropriate craftsfolk.''You have my thanks.

'Through your efforts, we did not have to spread ourselves as thin upon the fields.'Winsig has expressed concern that the Orc camps near Walstow will soon pose too great a threat along with the Orcs entering through the East Wall. She wishes you to completely dismantle their fortifications so that Walstow can redouble its efforts on a single force.Winsig has directed you to assault the Orc camps to the south-west and west of Walstow.Complete 'Circling The Kill'Complete 'Borrowing Barricades'Complete 'A Cut Above'Complete 'A Controlled Pyre'Complete 'Crippling The Front'As you've completely destroyed the Orc fortifications, you should now return to Winsig with news of your victory.

Winsig can be found in the mead-hall of Walstow.Talk to Winsig'${PLAYER}, the time has come to make a decisive strike against our enemies.

'To the west and south, Orcs have set up their camps and intend to starve us out as more forces of Mordor pour in from the East. We cannot allow this to happen.

'I want you to travel to these camps and raze them. If we can eliminate the Orcs that already seek shelter in our lands, we will be much less ill-prepared to deal with the arrival of new foes.

'Make haste... every passing minute brings more Orcs in the Sutcrofts. Their camps must burn or all will be lost.''You have done what I thought impossible, ${PLAYER}.

'The Orcs may still pose a threat to us, but they will no longer lurk just outside our homes.

'We will strengthen our defences at the East Wall and block as many of their number as we can from invading our lands.'While sieging the Orc camps near Walstow, you have heard a name snarled by the Orcs. If there is a leader of this force, it must be defeated.You have overheard Orcs of Mordor uttering a particular name - a name that can only belong to their leader. Thauk can be found deep in the Orc camp to the south of Walstow.Defeat ThaukThauk can be found deep in the Orc camp to the south of Walstow.Defeat ThaukYou have defeated Thauk and shattered the leadership of the invading Mordor Orcs.CompletedYou have overheard Orcs of the camps near Walstow snarling something that can only be the name of one Orc. You should defeat the leader of this force and plunge the remaining Orcs into disarray.You have defeated Thauk. The Orcs will surely prove far less of a challenge with their leadership broken. Winsig will be very pleased to hear of this.Fastred wants you to distribute rations to the people of Snowbourn along with his guards.The food-cart is near the kitchen of Snowbourn.

As food is scarce, Fastred wants you to make sure that people wait and do not swarm the food-stores. Perhaps a stern <rgb=#FF00FF>ahem</rgb> will do.Prepared rations can be found inside the kitchen of Snowbourn.

You should collect rations for the people of Snowbourn.Collect prepared rations for the people of Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dudweld, Ganburh, and Elfswith can be found throughout Snowbourn.

You should distribute the food to Dudweld, Ganburh, and Elfswith.Talk to DudweldTalk to GanburhTalk to ElfswithGísling can be found in central Snowbourn.

You should speak with Gísling and let him know you distributed the food as Fastred ordered.'You have been a great help thus far, ${PLAYER}. If you would, I require your aid in handing out rations to the people of Snowbourn. Food has become scarce since you left for Walstow, and the people are getting restless.

'There is a cart of food in Snowbourn...keep an eye on it, then distribute food to people once you have established some sort of order.

'Thank you for your assistance. I will continue to make ready our battle plan.''Oh, thank you so much!

'Reeve Fastred has been a more stern leader than Reeve Dagred, but I fear that this change has not been for the good of the people.

'My family and I have fallen on hard times, especially now that Snowbourn grows more crowded with people fleeing the Eastemnet.

'Thank you again, ${PLAYER}.''You did not have to be so abrupt before, but you have my thanks.

'I know not why Fastred has moved to establish such a strict order within Snowbourn. People continue to pour in, but he allows none of us to travel to the West where resources might be more abundant.

'Fastred has proven himself a worthy leader, but I am uncertain what the future holds for the Sutcrofts.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}...

'The crowds grow day after day... The Sutcrofts still provide a wealth of food to our people, but with more people coming here each day, I worry that we cannot sustain this.

'Fastred is a bold leader, but he must allow the people to journey west. We cannot support ourselves as the last sanctuary of the Eastemnet, not for long, anyway.''You did well in maintaining order. I am sure Fastred's guards were pleased that they could keep at watch instead of performing such a task.

'The concerns of those people are real, though. I worry that Snowbourn will not be able to support such a wealth of people for much longer.'

'Nevertheless, well done.'Rook is getting extremely frustrated that his avanc will not rise and continue on their journey.As Rook's avanc is his steed of sorts, whistling might be a good way to call him.

The avanc can be found under Rook to the west of Snowbourn.Whistle and try to grab the avanc's attentionWhistling didn't prove helpful, so perhaps a more direct approach would work.

The avanc can be found under Rook to the west of Snowbourn.Poke at the avancThe avanc can be found under Rook to the west of Snowbourn.Attempt to speak to the avancRook can be found to the west of Snowbourn.Talk to Rook'Puzzling... very puzzling, indeed. You should give him a good talking to, perhaps I was too gruff with him earlier.

'Yes, that will surely work. Just make sure you get his attention first, he can be very easily distracted.''...'

This avanc has clearly reached the end of its days. It is a wonder that Rook has not realized this yet. Perhaps the best thing would be to tell Rook the truth.'Dead? I don't believe you. He was fine just a moment ago!

'You just don't know how to talk to him, here let me try again!'Adalgifu of Walstow is concerned that time is running short to finish this season's harvest and wants you to collect as much wheat as you can, as untrained as you are.Wheat can be found in the fields just outside Walstow.Gather bundles of wheat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Having collected the wheat, you should return it to Winsig.

Winsig can be found inside the mead-hall of Walstow.Talk to Winsig'The Orcs have laid waste to our crofts, and barely any of our crops still stand. 

'We will soon find ourselves starving if we do not harvest anything and leave it to the Orcs to finish what they have begun.

'Go to the crofts to the west of here. When I fled, I saw some of the wheat still standing amid the destruction. Harvest as much as you can - it will be our last chance to do so.''This was a risky move, but if we were to claim any of our remaining crops, we had to harvest them now or risk losing everything to Orcs.

'Thank you for your aid.'Sigeric, the man you rescued from the sacked farmstead, has asked that you look for three Men that left the morning of the attack to go fishing. They have not returned and Sigeric fears the worst.Sigeric wants you to look for three men dispatched to deal with the Orc situation outside the fishing village to the south-east.

He also wants you to slay the Orcs that have sacked the town.Defeat Mordor Spear-fishers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the first Rohirrim scoutFind the second Rohirrim scoutFind the third Rohirrim scoutSigeric, the survivor of Garsfeld, can be found in northern Snowbourn.Talk to Sigeric'The morning my croft was attacked was a very strange one indeed.

'We had heard the troubles surrounding Garsfeld, but for our own part, we faced very little danger from our enemies in the Sutcrofts. They seemed to have little interest in attacking us... though I do not know why.

'Also, while it was not completely unheard of, three of our best riders, and also three of my closest friends, left the croft that morning to go fishing at what they thought to be a lucky fishing hole south-east of Snowbourn.

'While they were gone, the attack fell, and all were slain, save for me. Even as I stood bound to that pole, they did not return. I know not where they are now, and if you would find them for me, I would be very grateful.

'I would begin your search at the fishing docks to the south-east... if they are not there, I know not where else they could be...''I - I should have expected this, ${PLAYER}... but it does not dull my pain.

'Those men were great warriors, and it is a shame that such ill fortune found them when they could have aided us so greatly at the croft.

'I need some time to consider these losses, friend. Thank you for aiding me, but please leave me to my thoughts for now.'Sigeric was revealed to be the traitor in the midst of the Men of Snowbourn.Sigeric is in the prison of Snowbourn.

Gísling wants you to interrogate Sigeric and see if he is willing to part with any information about who sent him to undermine Snowbourn.Talk to SigericSigeric is in the prison of Snowbourn.

Perhaps if you <rgb=#FF00FF>stare</rgb> Sigeric down, he will break.<rgb=#FF00FF>Stare</rgb> Sigeric down and see if he talksSigeric can be found inside the prison of Snowbourn.

Sigeric refuses to cooperate with the people of Snowbourn and has now mocked your attempts to break his will. Perhaps you should take a more threatening approach.<rgb=#FF00FF>Shake your fist</rgb> at SigericSigeric can be found inside the prison of Snowbourn.

You should talk to Sigeric.Talk to SigericGísling can be found in central Snowbourn.

You should report Sigeric's refusal to cooperate to Gísling.Talk to GíslingFastred can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

Sigeric has proven to be a brutal traitor of Rohan, and Gísling wishes for you to tell Fastred of Sigeric's threats against the Sutcrofts.Talk to Fastred'I thank you again for my freedom. I respect Fastred still, even after this wronging....

'${PLAYER}, head back to the prison of Snowbourn.

'Let not Sigeric rest from his ordeal; the time to question him is now. He might resist, but the time to hesistate is over... do whatever is necessary to make him talk. Rohan will not fall because we were too frightened to take the proper action.''...''Do you honestly believe that I have anything to fear? It is not as if I shall be sent to Stangard. All I have to do is wait.

'Snowbourn will lie in ashes, the fool Reeve and his filthy kin will be no more, and the rest of the Eastemnet will fall with them.

'So I urge you, tell them. Tell that man I shared this prison with, tell the Reeve; it will not matter.''That arrogant fool. He would see all of the Riddermark burn for his own ends?

'Fastred must be told of this immediately.''So that wretch had more to say, eh?

'He was wise to silence himself in my presence.... Such a traitor to my people will never taste freedom again.

'Come then, what had he to say?'Egelferth is concerned that some crofters and his men have gone missing along the road to Snowbourn.Egelferth suspects that Orc-killers have taken up holdings near the road west and can be flushed out into the open if provoked.Investigate along the road west for signs of Orc-killersEgelferth suspects that Orc-killers have taken up holdings near the road west and can be flushed out into the open if provoked.Investigate further west along the roadEgelferth suspects that Orc-killers have taken up holdings near the road west and can be flushed out into the open if provoked.Investigate the sacked cart along the road to SnowbournEgelferth can be found in northern Walstow.

You should return to Egelferth with news of your success.Talk to Egelferth'Ho, there! If you are travelling near the East Wall, have a care! A few of my men and some crofters we sent west to Snowbourn have gone missing, and I fear that some terrible fate befell them.

'In my travels on the road, I have heard many a suspicious sound, but I know not if my mind is playing tricks on me. If I had to guess, though, I would suspect that Orc-killers were lurking just beneath my notice.

'You are a hardy one, are you not? Perhaps you can lure those cowards out of hiding and discover the fate that befell my fellows on the road west. Return to me with what you learn.''Ah then, it is as I assumed. Such a loss...great folk were they.

'At least those shameless Orcs met a fate so deserved. You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'Winsig is concerned that Walstow is about to become the victim of a vicious Orc-assault and wants you to assess the nearby forces to the north and south.The first Orc-camp can be found to the south of Walstow.

Winsig has suggested that you investigate the path near the East Wall as well as the camp across the stream to the south.Scout the Orc-camp to the south-west of WalstowThe second Orc-camp can be found to the north-west of Walstow.

Winsig has suggested that you investigate the path near the East Wall as well as the camp across the stream to the south.Scout the Orc-camp along the path to the East WallThe Rohirrim helm lays on the ground near the pathway to the East Wall.

You should examine the Rohirrim helm.Investigate the Rohirrim helm and attempt to find its ownerWinsig is in the Mead Hall of Walstow.

You should return to Winsig with news of your discoveries.Talk to Winsig'As I have said, the Orcs have been mustering to camps to the north and south of Walstow. I fear what they have planned for us, but I know it cannot be anything good.

'I want you to scout these camps -- I am uncertain how many foes we face.

'Also some of our Riders have not yet returned...I am worried about them. If you see them in your travels, please bring it to my attention.''The camps have grown then...this does not bode well for Walstow. We cannot delay any longer: the fight must be brought to the Orcs before they grow even further out of our control.

'I will have need of you again very soon.'Sigeric believes he has discovered a spy near Snowbourn. He has found a crude trail along the road south of Snowbourn and wishes you to follow it.Sigeric has told you that the trail of the man he spotted begins outside the south gate of Snowbourn.Follow the road south of SnowbournThe trail can be found along the road south and east of Snowbourn.

The trail has been cold so far, but in the interest of Snowbourn, you should keep searching.Continue along the road to the south of SnowbournThe crofts can be found just off the road far to the south-east of Snowbourn.

Having found a banner of the White Hand, you should investigate the nearby crofts and homes for any sign of a spy.Search the nearby crofts for the spyThe barn can be found among the croftlands to the south-east of Snowbourn.

Following the trail from Snowbourn, you have found yourself outside a barn.Investigate the barnYou have found Sigeric outside the barn, and he looks quite pleased to see you.

You should speak to him and discover why he sent you on this hunt.Talk to SigericFastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

You have bested Sigeric, the man you rescued from Orcs near Garsfeld, and now the Rohirrim have him in their control. Fastred must be told of Sigeric's treachery.Talk to Fastred'Ah, ${PLAYER}.... It is good to see you again! As I was just telling the Reeve, I believe I have uncovered another spy near Snowbourn.

'I was walking near the south gate when I spotted a figure in the distance wearing a bold white hand on his garb. When I caught his eye, he fled with haste along the road.

'If you would, see if you can discover his trail along the road south... I know one such as yourself would be much better equipped to handle such a fellow were you to find him!''It is truly a pleasure to see you, ${PLAYER}....

'You see, the White Hand has a great interest in seeing the Eastemnet weakened. For your part, you have made my task quite difficult, but no matter, that shall be resolved soon enough.

'With you out of the way, that fool Reeve will do my work for me. He serves up the defenceless like sheep to the slaughter and imprisons an innocent, loyal fellow for little more reason than the vaguest of suggestions... my note.

'Now, for the matter at hand....''That wretched man, Sigeric... I cannot believe that he blinded me so. Gísling has always been a faithful subject... I know not why I would have doubted him.

'You dealt with Sigeric in a most merciful manner, ${PLAYER}. He is fortunate that it was you and not I who discovered his deception.

'Now then, let us see what he has to say for himself.'The crofters and guards of Walstow are beginning to lose hope in the face of the dangers which plague them.The crofters and guard-captain are in Walstow centre.

Winsig is worried that her crofters are losing hope and wants you to speak with them about their concerns. After that, she would like to hear a report.Talk to HubyrtHubyrt is standing in Walstow.

You should try to comfort him with a <rgb=#FF00FF>hug</rgb>, some <rgb=#FF00FF>calm</rgb>ing words, a mighty <rgb=#FF00FF>flex</rgb>, or an enthralling <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb>.Comfort Hubyrt with a <rgb=#FF00FF>hug</rgb>, <rgb=#FF00FF>calm</rgb>ing words, a mighty <rgb=#FF00FF>flex</rgb>, or a <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb>Adalgifu is standing in central Walstow.

Winsig is worried that her crofters are losing hope and wants you to speak with them about their concerns. After that, she would like to hear a report.Talk to AdalgifuAdalgifu is in Walstow.

You should try to comfort her with a <rgb=#FF00FF>hug</rgb>, some <rgb=#FF00FF>calm</rgb>ing words, a mighty <rgb=#FF00FF>flex</rgb>, or an enthralling <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb>.Comfort Adalgifu with a <rgb=#FF00FF>hug</rgb>, <rgb=#FF00FF>calm</rgb>ing words, a mighty <rgb=#FF00FF>flex</rgb>, or a <rgb=#FF00FF>story</rgb>The Rohirrim guard-captain, Egelferth, is stationed at the north end of Walstow.

Winsig is worried that her crofters are losing hope and wants you to speak with them about their concerns. After that, she would like to hear a report.Talk to EgelferthThe guard-captain is in Walstow.

You should give the guard-captain a <rgb=#FF00FF>salute</rgb>.<rgb=#FF00FF>Salute</rgb> Egelferth before returning to WinsigWinsig can be found in the Mead Hall of Walstow.Talk to Winsig'You have seen the state of Walstow...I am certain that you can tell that things look grim for us.

'The crofters cannot even approach their fields, and the Orcs have set up camps to the north and south, effectively blocking us from any dealings with Snowbourn.

'The crofters are losing hope, and I blame them not. If you would, please speak with them. You have given so many in the Sutcrofts hope already...to see that in my own people again would be so inspiring, even if only for today.''So, you are the one Snowbourn sent to save us?

'I have heard of your exploits, and I can only hope that you will be the one to save us from the Orcs. We have lost so much and so many...I know not how much more we can endure.''What does it matter now? Even if we are saved, the entire harvest is lost. My croft was burned to the ground by the Orcs, and now look at our town...we have but moments left.

'Winsig is a great leader, but she cannot face a force of this strength. None among us can, and I cannot believe that any brighter days lie ahead.''Welcome, stranger. So you come from Winsig? She is a bold leader, to be certain. My men and I have fought hard to keep Walstow from those fiends, and so far, we have survived. 

'Confuse not our town's disrepair with weakness. We have fought the Orcs from the wall constantly, and we have lost only a few crofts. The Orcs rally to the north and south, but my men and I still hold strong.

'They will not breach our defences, and when the time comes, we shall deliver such a blow that they shall never dare return to Rohan. Your prowess precedes you, but know this: you will have to earn my respect. Now then, I am sure Winsig has many a task for you...as she does for us all.''Thank you for speaking with each of my people -- morale has been very low as of late, and I need the trust of my people as we move forwards.

'I have many thoughts on what we can do to secure Walstow from the Orcs, but their risk is great.'You have accompanied the Riders Four to the camp of Reeve Fastred in the Sutcrofts in the hope of discussing the Khundolar invasion with him.Talk to Burnoth.Talk to BurnothListen to the discussion between the Riders Four and Reeve Fastred.Listen to the discussion between the Riders Four and Reeve FastredDefeat the Orcs attacking Fastred's camp.Defeat the Orcs attacking Fastred's campDefeat Zakrif, the troll-commander of the Orc-company.Talk to Fastred.Talk to Reeve Fastred'Ah, my friends, you have arrived. I have told Reeve Fastred of the Easterlings coming from the north, but he will not relent....''Well-fought, ${CLASS}! That was a dire fight, but we proved victorious.

'I do not doubt the accuracy of Burnoth's report, but this battle only proves my will. The people of the Sutcrofts shall stand and defend their lands.''Alas, we have failed here. Let us return to Snowbourn.'The Rohirrim of Snowbourn have captured Sigeric from the croft where you defeated him.Fastred is in the prison of Snowbourn, located near the Mead Hall.

Fastred wants you to meet with him so that he can right his recent wrongs.Meet Fastred in the prison of SnowbournFastred has told you to meet him in the prison of Snowbourn, located near the Mead Hall.

You should speak with Fastred, as he instructed.Talk to Fastred in the prison of SnowbournGísling's cell is inside the prison of Snowbourn.

You should open Gísling's cell and return to him his freedom now that Sigeric has been exposed as a traitor.Release Gísling from his cellGísling can be found in eastern Snowbourn to the north of the east gate.

You should speak with Gísling now that he has been freed from his imprisonment.Talk to Gísling in Snowbourn'Sigeric will pay for his actions against Rohan, ${PLAYER}. Of this, you can be certain.

'Let us travel to the prison and speak with him. I will meet you there.''Before all else, I will right the wrong that was done here.

'Gísling, you are free. For your imprisonment, I am deeply sorry. You will always find Snowbourn a home, and anything you desire will be yours.

'${PLAYER} will let you out of your cell, then we will deal with this wretch.''Thank you for everything, ${PLAYER}.

'Fastred's wrath is a very dangerous thing, but his heart is in the right place. I say this, even with all that I have been through these past few days.

'Let us now deal with Sigeric. Such a fool cannot be allowed to go without punishment.'Orcs have been poaching the fish from near the docks and are likely carrying them, if they have not already eaten them.The docks can be found to the south-east of Snowbourn.

Sigeric is concerned for the health of the city and wishes for you to recover fish from the Orcs that have been spotted by the docks near Snowbourn.Recover fish from Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gísling can be found in northern Snowbourn.

Sigeric told you to bring the fish you collected to Gísling.Talk to Gísling'I have unfortunately heard that Orcs may have been... lurking near the fishing docks. If my friends encountered them, I am certain they would have defeated them. Nevertheless, if the Orcs remain, they may have fish on them... if they have not already devoured them.

'While you are investigating the docks, would you also be so kind as to gather fish for Snowbourn? I am so grateful to have any home at all, I would be rude to not give something back to this city.

'Once you have gathered many fish, bring them to Gísling. He is a resourceful man... I am sure he will know what to do next.''Where did you get these? Orcs?

'I am shocked that any creature escaped their wrath, even if it was just until their next meal.

'Very well, I will have the fish cleaned and given to the people. In the meantime, there are other matters to discuss.'Fastred's hatred for the Orcs has shaped Snowbourn as of late. He has asked that you collect Orc heads to decorate the pikes outside the city as he returns to the mead-hall.Fastred wants you to gather Orc heads to add to the grim display outside Snowbourn. 

Orcs can be found throughout the Sutcrofts.Behead Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fastred will be pleased to hear that you have added to the collection of Orc heads outside Snowbourn. 

Fastred can be found inside the mead-hall in Snowbourn.Talk to Fastred in Snowbourn's mead-hall'I am not certain that you saw it before you travelled out this way, but I have amassed a rather sizeable collection of Orc heads outside Snowbourn.

'If you would be so kind as to provide more for my collection, I am certain I can find space enough for them. Now then, I will take my leave.''Ah, beautiful work... your name?

'${PLAYER}? Very well.

'${PLAYER}, I am well aware of the problems facing this city as well as the rest of the Sutcrofts. 

'Our enemies have grown in number and I have heard grim news from the Wold. Nevertheless, Snowbourn remains strong and should it fall to me, I will ensure the survival of the Eastemnet myself!'Fastred is hesistant to believe Gísling's warning that Snowbourn is being sized up by the forces of the Enemy.Gísling mentioned that he saw trees being marked with weaponry, especially around Snowbourn's weakest walls.

Fastred wants you to investigate his claim that Snowbourn is being marked by the forces of the Enemy marshalling in the Sutcrofts.Fastred can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

You should return to Fastred with news of your discoveries.Talk to Fastred'How do I know that Gísling is not just sending us on a wild hunt for naught?

'I care for Snowbourn, and that is the sole reason I will even acknowledge his request. Search outside Snowbourn... if the Enemy has been marking the trees near our weakest walls as he claims, we will be able to prepare for whatever may come.

'In the meantime, I will speak with the traitor and see if he might grace us with more information.''So, his claim rings true?

'I will admit that he has done us a favour... perhaps there is more to this than I supposed.

'Let us talk of other things.'Rook is frustrated that his steed will not budge from this spot. He believes the avanc to be thirsty, so he wishes for you to fetch some water from the nearby Entwash.Rook wants you to attempt to wake his avanc so he can continue his journey to the East. 

He mentioned seeing a bucket along the edge of the Entwash.Find a bucket and attempt to wake Rook's avancRook can be found to the west of Snowbourn.Talk to Rook'I don't understand. He was so spry this morning, but now he will not budge. Perhaps he is thirsty... he did slow down this afternoon... before he stopped, of course.

'I spotted a bucket as he and I passed across the Entwash, would you go fetch him some water?''What a splash that was! Hopefully, my journey will begin anew in just a moment!'The Orcs of the Sutcrofts have too long been encroaching ever-closer to Snowbourn. Fastred's fervour is not misplaced, though a bit extreme - the less Orcs the Rohirrim have to contend with, the better.Fastred has decreed that no Orc is to find shelter in the Sutcrofts and all must be slain.

Orcs can be found throughout the Sutcrofts, especially near Snowbourn.Defeat Orcs in the Sutcrofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cynelac is outside the mead-hall of Snowbourn.Talk to CynelacYou have encountered an Orc of the Sutcrofts. Fastred would be greatly pleased if more of their kind were purged from the Sutcrofts.'Fastred is more than willing to part with a bounty for your services on the field.

'Your efforts against the Orcs will not be forgotten.'Alwyn of Snowbourn wishes to aid in boosting the morale of the Rohirrim defending the city.Alwyn can be found inside the kitchen of Snowbourn.

Fastred has praised the mead of Alwyn, a local crofter. He hopes to have mead delivered to his guards stationed at the edges of town in hopes that their spirits will be renewed.Talk to Alwyn in the Snowbourn KitchenHops can be found in the crofts just south of Snowbourn.Gather hops from nearby crofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Alwyn can be found inside the kitchen of Snowbourn.You have been given a powerful mead to bring to the Rohirrim that guard the gates of Snowbourn. Gates can be found at the north, east, and south sides of Snowbourn.You have refreshed the soldiers and should now return to the crofter in Snowbourn.Fastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

Having delivered the mead to the gate guards of Snowbourn, Fastred will be pleased to know that morale has been restored to his people.Talk to Fastred'${PLAYER}, you have tasted our mead.

'Spectacular is it not? Now, I have heard talks from around Snowbourn that our gate guards have been worn thin with fighting against our foes...

'This will not do! Travel to the kitchen of Snowbourn, and speak to Alwyn. We must keep my brethren at their best!''Hail, it seems more and more travellers are visiting our fine city even in these trying times.

'The Orcs throw themselves at us constantly, and our soldiers never stand down. I know not how they do it... they must have such great strength. I know they struggle, though, and we have lost some great warriors in the past weeks. Perhaps if I were to brew them some delicious mead, it would lift their spirits.

'Please, go to the crofts outside town and gather hops for me, and I shall craft a truly refreshing brew.''It is done, then?

'Excellent, it is always remarkable how such a simple pleasure can remedy such problems.''Excellent, here, I have crafted a brew from what was left of my stores. Take this to the soldiers - may they enjoy a brief moment of rest.''I hope they enjoyed the refreshments, I would be happy to make more when I have time, especially with the hops you have brought for me.'

'I know how difficult times have been for them as of late, so anything I can do to help brings me great joy.

'Thank you for aiding me in keeping our soldiers at their best.'Winsig is heartened that Walstow will now be able to stand against the Orc-invasion.Fastred can be found inside the mead-hall of Snowbourn.Talk to Fastred in Snowbourn'You have aided us beyond what I could have ever imagined, ${PLAYER}. Walstow will still have many fights ahead of it, but the Orcs no longer lurk just outside our borders.

'The time has come for you to return to Fastred. I am sure that Snowbourn faces new threats in your absence, and there will be much for you to do upon your return. My men and I can hold here for now, thanks to you.

'It was an honour, ${PLAYER}. Go with our respect.''Ah, you have returned. Am I to assume Walstow stands strong?

'Many peculiar things have occurred since you left us to aid my Thane. The traitor has been left to rot in our prison, but yet more threats face us every day.

'You have returned at a most opportune time... I think.'Fastred wants you to travel to the town of Walstow to the east and meet with Winsig, the Thane. He is concerned about the number of Orcs that have been pouring into the Sutcrofts and hopes that the town has held.Fastred wants you to defeat riders on your journey to Walstow.

Goblin and Orc riders can be found just off the road to the east.Defeat goblin harriers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Mordor siege-breakers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Winsig is in the mead-hall in Walstow.Talk to Winsig'${PLAYER}, you have done me a great many services in your short time here.

'I have one more task to ask of you for now. To the east is the town of Walstow and more importantly, the path to the East Wall from which countless Orcs are spilling into our lands.

'I want you to fight your way to Walstow and ensure that the town still stands. Riders of the enemy patrol the roads and will make every attempt to cut you down on your way. Once you make it to Walstow, speak to the Thane, Winsig. She is young, but she has strength far beyond her years.

'May fortune find you well on your journey. For Rohan!''I am Winsig, Thane of Walstow. What business have you here? You bring word from Snowbourn? Well then, what is it?

'So Fastred is concerned by the outpouring of Orcs into our lands? As am I, since they pour onto my doorstep.

'Fastred may be brash, but I respect his leadership. If he has sent you to us, he must trust in your skill as well. Now then, if you wish to see Walstow survive another week, we must move at once.'The town of Walstow is falling into ruin, and the townsfolk need aid with repairs.Reeds can be found along the stream to the south-west of Walstow.

Winsig wants you to aid the crofters of Walstow in repairing their rapidly deteriorating town. The reeds along the nearby stream should be suitable for repairing rooves.Collect reeds near Walstow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Winsig can be found inside the Mead Hall of Walstow.

You should return to Winsig with news of your success.Talk to Winsig'We have neither the time, nor the means to restore all of Walstow, but I believe you can aid us with some small repairs.

'Along the stream to the west, there are a great number of reeds. These reeds can be used to repair the rooves for the townsfolk here in Walstow.

'However, these reeds are very close to the Orc-camps nearby. It is more than likely that you may quickly find yourself surrounded by Orcs while there. That said, be swift about your business. I will await your return.''Wonderful work, ${PLAYER}. I hope the Orcs did not cause you too much trouble. 

'I will alert my men and have them begin repairs while you and I continue to work on reinforcing Walstow.'Orcs have been spilling through the barricade at the East Wall, threatening the folk of Walstow and beyond. Their assault must be quelled.Winsig and her men have been facing great difficulty in containing the Orc invasion of the Sutcrofts from the East Wall.

Orcs can be found near the pathway to the East Wall to the north of Walstow.Defeat Orcs near the East Wall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Winsig can be found inside the mead-hall of Walstow in south-eastern Sutcrofts.Talk to WinsigYou have discovered an outpouring of Orcs near the East Wall. You should defeat them for the good of Walstow.'Any Orc that will no longer threaten my people brings me great joy.

'You have done well in defeating our foes.'Pressured by foes from all sides, Gísil has prepared the crofters of Garsfeld to journey to the south and seek shelter within Snowbourn.Gísil can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld.

Gísil has ordered you and Gísling to escort the people of Garsfeld to safety in the south. He is waiting for you to make any final preparations.Talk to GísilGísling can be found in northern Snowbourn.

You have successfully brought the crofters of Garsfeld to safety inside the walls of Snowbourn and should now speak to Gísling.Talk to Gísling'The preparations have been made, ${PLAYER}. My people make ready as we speak.

'They must reach the safety of Snowbourn, for no other place in the Sutcrofts will keep them from harm. The Reeve of the Sutcrofts, Fastred, is a brash young man, but a caring leader... he will not suffer the deaths of his people if they could easily be saved by our actions.

'I cannot thank you enough for the aid you have provided me and my people. It is unfortunate that our paths must split, but it is my duty to hold Garsfeld to my last. When you are ready to depart, speak with me. Time grows short.''Gísling has gathered the crofters. Are you ready to depart?''We have made it, ${PLAYER}. Thanks in no small part to you.

'I can only hope that my father and his men will hold Garsfeld in the days to come....'Fastred wants you to speak to a recently apprehended prisoner in Snowbourn. The prisoner has been without food for some time now, so Fastred wants you to bring food to the cell as well.Fastred wants you to bring a plate of food to a prisoner of Snowbourn.  The food can be found in the prison, near the prisoner's cell.Collect food for the prisoner in the Snowbourn prisonThe prisoner can be found in the prison-house just outside the mead-hall in Snowbourn.Deliver the food to the prisonerFastred can be found in the mead-hall of Snowbourn.Talk to Fastred'As I said, the traitor has been sent to the prison. He will be hungry by now, so you should feed him rations through the wall of his cell. Perhaps by the time he has eaten, I will be willing to look him in the face again.

'Go, before starvation grants him the freedom he so little deserves.''Of course, he would claim loyalty... what traitor would not?

'We shall see if his claim holds up in time - I have heard rumblings of a coming conflict outside Snowbourn, but I am unsure when the hammer will fall.

'I must make ready my own men before dealing with one so far removed from the favour of Rohan.''By the King, I never thought I would see you again, ${PLAYER}...

'After you departed for Walstow, Fastred's men dragged me here. I know he worries for the safety of his people and family, but surely, he cannot believe that I would work against him!

'Fastred will not hear my words, of this I am certain. You must warn him! Before I was sent here, I noticed trees outside Snowbourn being marked by the Enemy. I fear they intend to attack Snowbourn directly, and soon! Go now!'Adalgifu wants you to attempt to recover a keepsake that was lost when she fled to Walstow from her old home to the north.The keepsake can be found near the ruins of Hytbold to the north-west of Walstow.Find the lost keepsake near the ruins of HytboldAdalgifu can be found in central Walstow.Talk to Adalgifu'${PLAYER}, I know you are quite busy helping others about town, but if you have a moment, I would ask one last favour of you.

'To the north lies the ruins of my home, Hytbold. It was a beautiful town that was sacked and destroyed utterly by the Orcs of Mordor. I, like so many others, fled in terror as our home burned.

'As I ran, I dropped a precious pendant, an heirloom of my line that had persisted from the days of Eorl. Knowing the nature of those detestable creatures, I would assume they shattered it along with everything else. Yet, I have hope that it remains.

'If you would, travel to the north, near the remains of Hytbold and see if my pendant still remains. I will reward you with everything I can spare should you find it intact.''I am amazed that you found it... I know not what to say.

'When I fled Hytbold, I was sure that nothing would be left by the horrid Orcs.

'Alas, I fear that Walstow will come to a similar end, but that is a conversation for another time...'You have happened upon more of the missing Rohirrim's belongings. If he can be found, Winsig would surely like to know of his findings at the East Wall.The Rohirrim must surely be nearby. You should try to find this Man, and see if he has strength enough to return to Walstow.Talk to AldstanWinsig will be most interested to learn of this man's assault against you. 

Winsig can be found in the mead-hall of Walstow.Talk to WinsigYou have found more of the Rohirrim's trappings. You should seek out the Rohirrim nearby, and see if he has survived the Orc attacks.'I know not what horror seized control of his mind like that. Once he wakes, I will speak with him.

'Thank you for bringing him back to Walstow - I only hope that he shall recover from such a thing.''No! Stay away from me!

'My head... you meant to hurt me, he said! You are no saviour of Rohan!

'Mordor will bring us glory, and you stand in the way!'You have encountered the Riders Four once more in Snowbourn, capital of the Sutcrofts.The doorwarden stands before the doors to the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

You should seek entrance to the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.Talk to the doorwarden at the Mead Hall of SnowbournBurnoth stands outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

You should speak with Burnoth and discover what to do next.Talk to Burnoth outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn'${PLAYER}! I am pleased to see you, though I will not say that I am surprised... our paths seem destined to cross at the most opportune times.

'We have only just arrived ourselves. Indeed, it seems that we are both here to see the Reeve, Fastred. Would you join me?''You have come too late. Reeve Fastred is abroad, hunting Orcs. If you wish to speak with him, I can show on your map where his camp lies.

'Here... though I doubt you will find a warm welcome. His mood has been harsh of late, and a thirst for blood has been upon him.''Well, we have come a long way, only to find the master of the house absent.'Fastred has appreciated your labour thus far and wishes for you to meet his family before speaking further with him.Fastred's home can be found slightly south and east of the Mead Hall.Enter Fastred's homeThéodhild can be found inside Fastred's home in central Snowbourn.Talk to ThéodhildElflád can be found on the second floor of Fastred's home in central Snowbourn.Talk to ElfládFolcred can be found on the second floor of Fastred's house near Elflád.Talk to FolcredFastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

Cynelac has informed you that Fastred wants to speak with you after you have finished meeting with his family.Talk to Fastred in the Mead Hall of SnowbournFastred has set out a drink on the table in front of him inside of the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

Reeve Fastred bids you drink with him.Share a drink with FastredFastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

Reeve Fastred desires to speak with you.Talk to Fastred'${PLAYER}, Reeve Fastred has expressed a desire for you to meet with his family. Once you have met with them, you should return to him as soon as you are able.''Ah, so my son has sent you to me?

'I overheard him speaking to Elflád of a mighty visitor in these lands.... You are welcome here, traveller. Fastred would not send you to us unless you earned his trust.

'Sadly, my son has lost sight of my husband's ideals. He would be wise to heed Éomer's call to abandon these lands, if only to spare the defenceless. Such stubbornness is difficult to influence, though....''Hello, traveller. Fastred has told me much of your journey through the Eastemnet and the aid you provided for Garsfeld.

'I thank you for bringing renewed hope to the people of the Sutcrofts. While many of the soldiers stand by my husband, some of the crofters fear for their safety. Our son would perhaps be safer elsewhere, but Fastred has decreed that none shall leave. As always, I must stand with him.

'You are always welcome here, ${PLAYER}. I must tend to Folcred, so you may return to Fastred when you see fit.'Beneath the veil of this Rohirric bassinet, you see a small boy. He coos inquisitively at your presence, but then appears to lull himself back to sleep.'Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. I have considered the note you brought me, considered your efforts thus far, and I have decided what needs to be done.

'If you would, have a drink, and we shall speak further.''I trust you enjoyed the drink? Aye, our mead is among the finest in Rohan, as you will come to learn. On the matter at hand, though... that note has raised my ire.

'I have enough trouble dealing with the Orcs and ignoring the King's call to retreat from the Eastemnet. I will not uproot my people, under any circumstance. If the Sutcrofts are to fall, I will fall with them and not before I slay every Orc that dares stand against me.

'Snowbourn must ready itself for battle; meanwhile, I will instruct my guards to attempt to expose the traitor, whomever he may be.'After arriving in Snowbourn, Gísling is unsure where the refugees are to find shelter.Baldnoth can be found outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

Gísling believes the guards of the city can aid you in assisting the new inhabitants.Talk to BaldnothEmpty homes can be found throughout Snowbourn and are near the city's major services.

Baldnoth mentioned that he would have the guards free space for the crofters of Garsfeld during these dangerous times.Search for a home just to the east of the KitchenSearch for a home east of the BarracksSearch for a home to the west of the Auction HallSearch for a home near the TavernSearch for a home to the south of the Mead HallVarious homes about Snowbourn have been condensed by the guards. Now that you have found their locations, you should send the refugees to their new shelters.

The refugees can be found in northern Snowbourn.Gísling can be found north-east of the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

You should return to Gísling and let him know that you have done as he asked.Talk to Gísling'We have made it, ${PLAYER}. The crofters are now safe in Snowbourn, but I know not where they are to stay. 

'I do not think Fastred would be so cold as to see them live in the streets of his fine city, so I am certain there is something we can do.

'Seek out a guard and see if they are aware of any open homes in Snowbourn.''My father knew what he was bringing upon himself by doing this, and I am certain that he does not fear any reprisal from Fastred.

'You have done well, and I would wager that the crofters of Garsfeld will not forget you for all you have done for them.

'Now then, there is more business to attend to here in Snowbourn....''Your actions were bold, traveller. Gísil will hear much for such a blatant disregard for Fastred's rule. 

'Nevertheless, we cannot keep them in the streets. I will have my men clear room in some of the nearby homes.

'Most of the homes near our tradesfolk are not filled, so you will likely find room there. Be quick about this, though!'Gísling is concerned that the people of Snowbourn may soon be the victim of a disease spreading through the nearby crofts. The crofters informed him that there may be tainted food supplies about town, but Fastred will not acknowledge the truth of the situation.Crates of food can be found scattered about Snowbourn.

Gísling wants you to investigate crates of food in Snowbourn for any sign of a rampant crop-disease.Destroy tainted food-crates within Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gísling can be found in northern Snowbourn.

You should return to Gísling and let him know that you have done as he asked.Talk to Gísling'While you were dealing with Sigeric, I took the opportunity to speak to some of the crofters. They alerted me to some rather grim news. Apparently, there is a vicious disease running rampant through the crops on some of the nearby crofts.

'They cannot be certain what crops have been affected, but many may already be inside the city waiting to be consumed. To make matters worse, Fastred will not believe these claims and denies that there is any cause for alarm.

'This is foolish, ${PLAYER}. I want you to inspect the stockpiles of crops throughout Snowbourn. The crofters said a darkened dust will be present on the tainted crops. If you find any of these crops, destroy them: we cannot risk another problem plaguing the Sutcrofts... not now.''It worries me greatly that so much was affected by the disease. I hope the people of this city do not soon find themselves in the same position as we did in Garsfeld. I am glad that you were able to yet again protect the people of the Sutcrofts.

'Fastred must come to his senses... his people are in danger from a great many sources.'Orcs trouble the outskirts of Snowbourn, wielding terrible weapons against the people of the Sutcrofts.Orcs can be found north of Snowbourn.

Gísling wants you to thin out the Orcs surrounding Snowbourn and recover their vile weapons so that no other Orc may wield them again.Defeat Orcs at Wyrthing (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Orc-weapons from fallen Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gísling is in central Snowbourn.

You should return to Gísling with news of your success.Talk to Gísling'This great attack could come at any time, ${PLAYER}. Yet, even now, the Orcs lurk outside the walls.

'If we can thin their numbers before the attack, we may stand yet a better chance of defeating this force.

'Hunt the Orcs outside Snowbourn and take their weapons. We cannot allow any other Orc to take up the arms of the fallen. We will starve them of resources, one-by-one.''Well done. I know not how many more Orcs will fall upon Snowbourn, but you have slain a great many, and for that, I thank you.'The Rohirrim of Walstow have attemped to hold back the forces of Mordor pouring through the barricaded East Wall, but they have seen several Orc riders slip through their defences.Orc Warg-riders can be found near the stream to the north-west of Walstow and along the sides of the road west to Snowbourn.Defeat mounted Orcs from the East Wall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated the mounted riders and beaten back the renewed assault from the East Wall.CompletedYou have encountered mounted riders out of the East Wall while aiding Walstow in rebuilding their defences. You should defeat as many mounted riders as you can to prevent any enemy force from regaining a foothold in the Sutcrofts.You have defeated more mounted forces out of the East Wall, and stopped any Orcs from rebuilding their camps within the Sutcrofts.Winsig wants to ensure that the East Wall remains barricaded to the best of Walstow's ability. She can spare a few riders, and wishes for you to signal some to take up a position near the Wall.The barricades can be found along the road near the East Wall to the north and north-west of Walstow.Signal riders to the barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The guard-captain of Walstow can be found at the north end of Walstow.Talk to the guard-captain'The Orcs will be reeling from your assault for a great long time, ${PLAYER}. I am certain of that.

'Now, we must work to ensure that no more of their ilk slip past our defences and into the Sutcrofts.

'Travel out to the pathway that leads into the East Wall. You will find barricades there, but unfortunately, none of my men. Due to your efforts, I can now afford to have my riders defend those positions. Signal them from the barricades and they will hold the position.

'Return to me when this is done.''Excellent, those Orcs should find much more trouble waiting for them when they pass out of the East Wall. Now then, more must be done.'An undeniable way to confuse and thwart the efforts of the White Hand is to defeat their leader, Nágri, at Fushaum-dorám.Nágri, the leader of the White Hand Orcs in the Writhendowns, can be found at Fushaum-dorám.

