Mossbeard has asked that you break the cruel axes of the Orcs in the Balewood to prevent further harm from coming to the trees and his kind.Destroy Orc-axes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mossbeard can be found following you, or if you have become separated, he can be called with your whistle.

You have defeated many Orcs and destroyed their vile tools. You should now speak to Mossbeard and see if he has more tasks for you.Talk to Mossbeard'Can you hear that, ${PLAYER}?

'The trees cry out in the distance, fearful of the Orkish blades that have already felled others. So many have been hewn... to what end?

'These tools of destruction have no place in our forest... hom. You are an able ${CLASS}... perhaps you can take their axes from them. If you were to break their tools, they could not bring such harm to Fangorn.

'Let us confront them and shatter their axes!''These Orcs have chopped away at far too much of the forest... felling many of my friends.

'Hom... the least we can do is strip them of their weapons so that no others suffer that fate.

'Thank you, little one.'The people of Rohan are being starved out by the destruction of their farms and crops. A large quantity of fish would help ease the shortage.Fish can be caught in the lake and river just east of Snowbourn.

Héalac asked you to go fishing and bring him several dozen cuts of fish.Collect cuts of fish (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Héalac is at Snowbourn.

Héalac will be pleased to get all of the cuts of fish you were able to catch.Bring the cuts of fish to Héalac'The Enemy has been rampaging through our fields and destroying our crops. Food-supplies are low and will not last much longer. We need to supplement the farms with what the lakes and rivers can provide.

'The best place for catching that many fish is the lake just outside of town to the east. The fish swim into it and get caught between the water-wheel to the south and waterfall to the north and cannot get out. Stuck inside, they just feed and grow.

'Several dozen cuts of fish should help to fill the stores and get us through a few more days. Slice up the fish you catch in order to get cuts... the larger the fish the more the cuts.'

<rgb=#FF0000>The Fishing Hobby is required to complete this quest</rgb>'This is more than I expected. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We will be able to feed many mouths.'The Ent, Barallas, wishes to share his memories of the Balewood before Núrzum's assault shattered the forest.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>Barallas is at Stonecliff with Tithenolf in northern Balewood.

Barallas wishes to tell you more of the Ents of the Balewood. You should speak with him to learn more of his tale.Talk to Barallas to hear more of his taleBarallas is at Stonecliff with Tithenolf in northern Balewood.

Barallas has finished his tale. You should now speak with him and discover if more can be done to aid the Ents.Talk to Barallas'Hoom. Little one... I find that the Men outside the forest either say too much or far too little. So, which is it for you? Too little then, I suppose. We shall see if that does not change... for a great many things have changed here.

'The forest has not been chilled such before. Yes, we have had winters, and the cold does yet come, but this... this goes far beyond a simple changing of the seasons. When Tithenolf and I awoke, nothing was as I remembered it. There were times when I and the other Ents conversed at length, for there was much still to say, and even more time to say it. But now... the Enting Hollow has frozen solid, our enemies set siege to the forest, and Leaflock slumbers, unable to tend the Huorns.

'Ah, to be free of such problems... and to think of better times....'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>'Come, we must travel to the Enting Hollow. Are you ready to follow, little one?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>'Duskleaf was right, ${PLAYER}. I knew my mistake well once Núrzum carved his path under the canopy. I still hold out hope that the forest may be reclaimed, dim as it may be. The Men and their horn have paled in comparison to such wanton destruction.

'Aside from Tithenolf, I have not seen the others since awakening. I cannot help but wonder what has become of them. I worry greatly for Duskleaf... he is quick to action, and if he dared stand against Núrzum, I fear what horrors might have befallen him.

'If you would, let us talk of finding the others. It may be that you find such eagerness to aid us misplaced... or perhaps not. We shall see, little one....'There is much to do while travelling through the lands of the Westemnet.Complete Explorer of the Westemnet deedComplete Quests of the Westemnet deedComplete Slayer of the Westemnet deedComplete Survivor of the Long Night deedThere is much to do while travelling through the lands of Wildermore.Complete Explorer of Wildermore deedComplete Quests of Wildermore deedComplete Slayer of Wildermore deedDefeat the leader of the Morgul Army.Defeat The Witch-king, leader of the Morgul ArmyDefeat the leader of the Morgul Army.Defeat The Witch-king, leader of the Morgul ArmyDefeat the leader of the Morgul Army.Defeat The Witch-king, leader of the Morgul ArmyThe archers of Harwick can focus their fire if you present them with a target.Direct archers with your flag while defending Harwick.

Wulfin has given you a flag you can use to direct the archers defending Harwick.Wulfin is in Harwick.Talk to Wulfin'We are low on supplies and weapons, but that does not mean we cannot fight back. Even without swords, a soldier can still strike at the enemy from afar with a good bow and a stack of arrows. That is presuming he has a target to focus on. That is where you come in, ${PLAYER}.

'When you are near the Easterlings, raise this flag and the archers from Harwick will fire over the wall and strike any enemies around you. Direct them, and we shall win this battle.''Are you prepared to join the battle and defend this town?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'The Easterlings are skilled in combat, but nothing bests a Rohirrim.'Easterlings have come across the river and are marching on Harwick.The Easterlings are attacking Harwick.

Wulfin has alerted you to the fact that Easterlings are about to descend upon Harwick.Defeat Easterlings in the defence of Harwick (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wulfin can be found in Harwick.

Wulfin will be pleased to hear Harwick is secure.Talk to Wulfin'There is no time to talk. Easterlings are cresting the hill and about to crash into the walls of this town.

'Are you ready to join the defence?''Are you ready to make a stand with us and defend Harwick?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'I do not know how they got up from the river so quickly, but I am glad you were here to aid us.'Thrymm has returned, and the time of the attack is nigh. Scylfig must brace itself for an assault by the White Hand Orcs.Thane Cynegar is in the Mead Hall of Scylfig.

You should go to the Thane and tell him that the time for battle draws near.Speak with Thane CynegarCyneberg is in the icy ruins of Scylfig.

You should comfort Cyneberg after her great loss.Try to comfort Cyneberg'What was that?! I thought I heard an Orkish-sounding horn blow in the distance. I believe the time for battle is nigh.

'Will you go to my father and tell him? I must get the villagers inside and the soldiers ready, and look for Thrymm and his riders at the gate.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'My daughter has sharp ears! If she says the Orcs draw near, then they draw near, and we must arm ourselves.

'Thrymm will be here; do not worry. Will you fight alongside us, ${PLAYER}?'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'I... I have lost everything! My father... my future husband, gone.

'Please leave me be!! I cannot think straight right now. What nightmare is this?'Walstow has been surrounded on all sides by an army of Orcs and trolls.Orcs and trolls are attacking Walstow.

Waldeg asked you to join in the defence of Walstow, protecting it from an army of Orcs and trolls.Defeat Orcs and trolls in the defence of Walstow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Waldeg is at Snowbourn.

Waldeg will be pleased to hear that Walstow has been defended.Talk to Waldeg'The Enemy is once again on the march, this time to the south. A concerted force approaches Walstow from the north, south, and east. The town has already suffered great losses. Without reinforcement it may not last this battle. If Walstow falls, the southern gate into Rohan belongs to the Enemy.

'You must aid Walstow and stand with its defenders. It cannot fall.''Are you prepared to withstand the Enemy's assault at Walstow?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'They will come again, they always come again, but for tonight the people of Walstow can sleep secure.'Many Rohirrim have been injured defending Walstow from the Enemy.Injured Rohirrim can be found in Walstow.

Waldeg asked you to triage and treat the Rohirrim who have been injured defending Walstow.Treat injured Rohirrim soldiers during the defence of Walstow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Waldeg is at Snowbourn.

Waldeg will be pleased to hear that you were able to treat the wounds of several injured Rohirrim.Talk to Waldeg'Walstow has been under almost constant siege. The warriors there have fought their hearts out, but their numbers dwindle. Small wounds have begun catching up with the men. If they can be treated, the wounds will heal, and they can rejoin the battle.

'Take this kit and head to Walstow. Use it to treat the injured and heal their wounds.''Walstow has suffered heavy losses... be prepared for a fight.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'Every warrior treated enough to rejoin the battle could be the warrior that tips the scales to our favour.'Easterlings prepare to lay siege to Dale and the Lonely Mountain. The bells of Dale must be rung to signal the inhabitants to retreat into Erebor.Complete the deed The Bells of Dale -- Tier 1Complete the deed The Bells of Dale -- Tier 2Complete the deed Challenge: The Bells of DaleComplete Tormentors of Dale questThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...The people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...Complete 'Challenge - An Army from the East'Complete 'Flight to the Lonely Mountain  - Tier 1'Complete 'Flight to the Lonely Mountain - Tier 2'Dígelir, queen of the Great Spiders of Mirkwood, has established a nest in the heart of the Scuttledells, where she is breeding an army to answer the call of Sauron.You must defeat the draug-lord Beremud and the Great Spider Dígelir in the heart of the Scuttledells.Complete the deed Webs of the Scuttledells -- Tier 1Complete the deed Webs of the Scuttledells -- Tier 2Complete the deed Challenge: Webs of the ScuttledellsComplete the quest Spiders and FliesDrugoth has gathered his lieutenants and generals to the fortress on Sâri-surma. You must kill his generals so that they may not send evil spreading across the south.

