You have discovered the second general, Osan. The giant and his minions will attempt to block your path, preventing you from confronting Drugoth.Defeat the second general, OsanDrugoth the Death-monger has relocated from the Misty Mountains and made his new home in the largest glacier in the Icebay of Forochel.  Now, his mad, rambling mind is planning an attack on Annúminas to the south.

Drugoth has fled to the summit of Sâri-surma. Confront him, and put an end to his malicious plans.Defeat Drugoth the Death-mongerStem the tide of Orc-defilers in the War.Defeat Orc-defilers in the WarStem the tide of Orc-defilers in the War.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Orc-defilers in the WarStem the tide of Orc-defilers in the War.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Orc-defilers in the WarStem the tide of Orc-defilers in the War.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Orc-defilers in the WarStem the tide of Orc-defilers in the War.Complete the previous deed tier.Defeat Orc-defilers in the WarSearch for the Rohirrim outpost outside southern BalewoodHaving found the camp, you should now speak to the captain of the Rohirrim stationed here and discover if he knows anything of the whereabouts of the refugees of Byre Tor.'It is time we attend to another pressing matter, ${PLAYER}. Before you arrived, several of my people fled Byre Tor into the dark eaves of Fangorn. I would have pursued them but the wood is deep and dangerous, and I know not the way through those twisted branches. That weald has come to be known as Balewood and is a haven for none, especially those left defenceless after Núrzum ravaged our lands. I only hope they travelled elsewhere as they fled, for settling in such a place would not bode well.
'To the south-west of here, near the southern border of Balewood in Whitshaws, there may still remain a small camp of Rohirrim who kept watch on the Orcs passing into our lands. Should you find them, search for my people among their number - I can only hope that not all were lost in the dark.''You heard my men and I? We must be more cautious then, it seems...

'So you come from High Knolls in search of survivors... I am saddened to say, I have heard naught of the people of Byre Tor since the settlement fell to the monster. If they truly fled into the forest, then perhaps they remain there still, but I hold not much hope for them. The forest crawls with Orcs and countless other foul things - if you count yourself bold enough to venture into the dark, my men and I shall aid you in your preparations here.'The mushrooms that grow within the Dígelon are highly regarded by the Rohirrim.Glowing mushrooms can be found in Dígelon.

Wulfin asked you to venture within Dígelon and gather several glowing mushrooms.Collect glowing mushrooms from Dígelon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wulfin is at Harwick.

Wulfin will be happy to see the glowing mushrooms you were able to gather from Dígelon.Talk to Wulfin'During war it is difficult to keep the morale high. Warriors are used to the battle and the constant loss, but the farmsfolk, women, and children...their spirits cannot handle such violence and turmoil. They need reminders that there is still good and virtue within the world.

'Such a reminder grows in the Dígelon. By the shores of the great underwater river there are glowing mushrooms unlike any ever seen. They remind people that light can overcome darkness. Only a few of them are needed to rekindle the fire within the people.''Are you prepared to visit Dígelon and see the fury of the underground river?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'These will do nicely. While war is fought with weapons, and stomachs are filled with food, hope is inspired from things like this.'The salamanders and lizards within Dígelon feast upon the mushrooms.The salamanders and lizards can be found in Dígelon.

Wulfin asked you to drive out the lizards and salamanders found within Dígelon.Defeat salamanders and lizards in Dígelon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wulfin can be found in Harwick.

Wulfin will be pleased to hear you have driven out many of the lizards and salamanders that were within Dígelon.Talk to Wulfin'The mushrooms that grow within Dígelon are unique and a great source of inspiration and hope to my people. Unfortunately, the lizards and salamanders that frequent the underground river feast upon them.

'Go to Dígelon and drive out the lizards. The mushrooms' inspirational powers are too important to let them be used as a meal for a salamander.''Are you ready to brave the currents of the Dígelon?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'They will return at some point, the mushrooms are too delicious for them not to, but for now they -- and our hopes -- are safe.'Céolflad, a healer, has vowed to ensure that Ránmald can deliver her child amongst friends and helpers. She has asked that plenty of firewood be collected to get the women ready for digging into their new temporary home.Firewood can be found around clusters of trees in the northern High Knolls.

You should collect firewood so that the women can comfortably settle into their new temporary home.Collect firewood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Céolflad is in the refugees' cave in northern Byre Tor.

You should bring the firewood to Céolflad.'Don't ye worry no more, ${PLAYER}. We were petty before, but there's a child coming, and we're women of Byre Tor. I've delivered plenty of babies; Ránmald is in good hands.

'Well, since we'll be settlin' in for a while until mother and child are fit to walk far, I'll be needing some firewood to get us started.

'See if the other ladies need anything for our stay, and then ye must go and continue yer heroism in the rest of Wildermore, so we can get home again.''This'll do nice, ${PLAYER}. We'll keep Ránmald warm until she's out of danger.

'Now go help the other refugees! If they ran into the Balewood, they'll need it....'Orcs have planted their flags before the doors of Byre Tor homes as a trophy of their thorough efforts at pillaging.Enemy flags can be found outside of the homes in Byre Tor.

You should destroy enemy flags and search the homes for survivors of the White Hand assault.Tear down enemy flags and investigate homesEnemy flags can be found outside of the homes in Byre Tor.

