Gladsnel will be surprised to hear that you passed the dressage practice.Talk to Gladsnel'Dressage has been around almost as long as we have ridden horses. Any warrior can mount a horse and charge headlong into battle, but only someone truly joined with his steed can carefully balance a series of moves as if they were dancing.

'One of our greatest riders is in a field here in Cliving practising his basic manoeuvres. He is preparing for any order or combination the judges may throw at him.

'The basic moves include calling for a charge, cheering, drinking, flexing, and laughing. When he begins his course, watch for the move he does and perform it with him. Be quick about it too... lagging behind is not tolerated.''Not bad, but these were only the basic moves. Any Rohirrim child could have performed them.'Defeat Dunlendings in Western Rohan.Defeat Dunlendings in the WestemnetDefeat Dunlendings in Western Rohan.Defeat Dunlendings in the WestemnetDefeat dwarf-players battling in the War.Defeat dwarf-playersDefeat dwarf-players battling in the War.Defeat dwarf-playersDefeat dwarf-players battling in the War.Defeat dwarf-playersDefeated dwarf-players battling in the War.Defeated dwarf-playersDefeat dwarf-players battling in the War.Defeat dwarf-playersIf the mechanisms within the Dwergfant do not work, the Limlight will be ruined.The impaired mechanisms can be found within the Dwergfant.

