de of town were not exempt from the Orc-raiders...they burned everything. All of the Eastemnet is suffering from the attacks, and food is short everywhere. If we are to survive, we must be able to provide for ourselves, and that means the farms must be rebuilt.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'A farm can only grow food as good as the land it is upon. We should take three of our fields and cover them with premium peat and fertilizer, one for pipe-weed, one for grains, and one for vegetables, then allow the best of our farmers to grow their crops there.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'There are many ways to prepare food, and many different tools and ingredients used in doing so, but none are as important as the oven. If you want to make the finest of baked goods and cooked dishes, you need a superior oven with which to practice your craft. I think we should add one down near the farms.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'You are upgrading the farms of the town.Complete Farmhouse of the Entwash ValeComplete Farmhouse of the SutcroftsThe farms in the Fallows were abandoned when Núrzum attacked Forlaw, and it was deemed unsafe to be outside the city walls. Thrymm's Farm is the meeting place for anyone in the outlying farms who are escaping to the safety of Forlaw.Thrymm's Farm is south-east of Forlaw. The road outside the east gate has a fork, and the southern path runs straight through this farm.Find Thrymm's Farm near ForlawThere are a few survivors calling for help around Thrymm's Farm. These calls seem to be coming from around the outer edges of the farm.The rescued farmers ran off toward the barn in the centre of the farm. Find and talk to Oter, who seems to be the senior among these farmers.Find Oter in the centre of Thrymm's Farm'The farmlands were recently abandoned when Núrzum and the Orcs attacked Forlaw. Not everyone from the farms has made it back, and they could be in trouble. Forlaw is losing contact with so much of Wildermore these days.

