<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time-limit. The timer will begin upon accepting this quest.</rgb>Ethelbryt has asked you investigate the village and find a way to discourage the invaders from remaining there.Defeat the leader of the enemies within Impingyou should return to Ethelbryt and apprise him of your efforts.Talk to Ethelbryt'You look the sort who is up for some danger. To the south, our milling-camp fell under attack. Most of my men were able to escape but we were forced to abandon Imping. Imping is one of our most important mills and one of the last timber caches on the Entwash. Should we lose it for good, we will also lose the resources it provides us.

'With our forces busied elsewhere, we are hard pressed to muster a response to these invaders, but perhaps a smaller effort will do. Travel to Imping and see about the demise of whatever creature leads our enemies there.

'Gangfinda knows the way and will lead you to the shores directly across from Imping. From there, you will need to take a boat across to the docks, I am certain there remains one of ours upon that shore.'

