You have discovered much of Núrzum's destruction and should now return to Strongroot to discuss what you have found.Talk to Strongroot'Barallas is a wise Ent, and he is my elder. However, many are elders to us, for us young Ents are all that remain here. My bark looks old and weathered, you say? Old, my small friend... may still be young to us.

'The monster, Núrzum, has been a cause of great destruction to my friends in this forest. The cries of the trees as he pulled them from the earth is not something I long to hear again. His assault on this forest was swift and brutal, and many of his damages remain still.

'Along the side of that twisted path through the forest that the Orcs defile with their crude machinery, you will find his handiwork smashed into the earth.

'If you search for signs of his destruction, I would ask that you examine them... for strange things have been cropping up in this forest as of late, and none of them good.''Hoom. Perhaps there is more to this monster than we thought....

'Such strength is uncommon, even for a giant of stone. And that foul roots sprang from the earth amid his havoc... this is odd, indeed. Hom. Odd and gravely unsettling....

'${PLAYER}, we must speak of what is to be done to learn more of this monster lest any hasty action be taken....'Cyneberg has moved mountains in Grimnesberg as her grief caught up with her at last.Cyneberg did a great deal of work in Grimnesberg as her grief overwhelmed her.

You should have a look around and see where Cyneberg's mind was while she captured this town.Cyneberg can be found in the centre of Grimnesberg.

You should speak with Cyneberg.Tell Cyneberg what you saw'I should have done Gárwig's bidding and helped at Byre Tor, but I was blinded by my desire to find Thrymm alive.

'I came here and found... horrible things, and that's when I understood. I understood that Núrzum has won. My family is dead, all of them. Thrymm is dead. The enemy has taken Wildermore, and there is nothing left.

'When I came here, my eyes were opened at last.'You gently tell Cyneberg that you saw the brave, heroic work she did when she came to this town, and the view of her fallen home. She looks at you with tear-filled eyes.

'I did what I could for them, but I was too late. Luckily the Orcs were not many, and they were scattered. But my heart broke when I saw Scylfig down below....'A disturbance at the west gate has come to the attention of the Reeve.Gárwig is in the Mead Hall of Forlaw.

You should speak with Gárwig.Speak with GárwigAssist Gárwig in Forlaw.Follow Gárwig and speak with himAssist Gárwig in Forlaw.Assist Gárwig in ForlawSpeak with Gárwig at the gate.Help Gárwig'I... I cannot believe this. What do we do?'

Cyneberg recovers a little when she sees her Reeve lying still in the snow.

'We must get the Reeve indoors at once. He is too frail to be out in the snow!''We have always had to defend our lands from the creatures of the wild, and from bands of roaming Orcs. But things have never been this bad in Wildermore.''Well, at least we have defeated them, from the looks of it. You there -- tell me what happened here.'Gárwig is pale and breathless, his eyes wide in his shock at the cruel death of his remaining sons.

'Why did it not take me instead? What does the creature want with us?

'How can it be stopped?'You appear to have come upon a trail of vengeance, left by a mysterious warrior whose deeds strongly resemble Thrymm's....Cyneberg is in the northern High Knolls.

You should follow Cyneberg.Talk to CynebergCyneberg is in the northern High Knolls.

You should follow Cyneberg.Follow CynebergThrymm is in the northern High Knolls.

You should speak with Thrymm.Reassure Thrymm that Cyneberg is all rightThrymm and Cyneberg are in Thrymm's cave in the northern High Knolls.See if Cyneberg is feeling betterYou should listen to Thrymm and Cyneberg.Listen to Thrymm and CynebergYou should listen to Thrymm and Cyneberg.Talk to CynebergYou should listen to Thrymm and Cyneberg.Listen to Cyneberg'I cannot wait to see Gárwig's face when he sees that Thrymm is alive!

'Let us leave at once. We must prepare for battle.''Do we continue to follow this trail, or do we admit our defeat and return to Forlaw?'

You tell Cyneberg that you have a strange feeling about the trail of felled Orcs. Cyneberg shrugs in reply.

'If you wish to live in denial of our doom a little longer, I am not one to criticize.''Is she ill? I cannot bear to lose her now that I have found her again. I thought everyone dead!'

You assure Thrymm that Cyneberg is as healthy as can be.

The shock of seeing Thrymm alive when she had given up hope seems to have overwhelmed her.'I am well now, ${PLAYER}. The joy overwhelmed me, for I thought all hope was lost.

'Thrymm, why did you not return to us? I knew you were alive, but no one believed me!

'I searched everywhere for you.''Now... now we can defeat Núrzum, or die trying. We have Thrymm, and we have so much more knowledge of our foe.'Théoden has emerged from the Golden Hall to look out over his kingdom, and to issue the commands necessary for its survival.Gléowine is outside Meduseld, worrying.Talk to Gléowine outside MeduseldHorn is outside Meduseld, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Horn outside MeduseldAragorn is outside Meduseld, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Aragorn outside MeduseldGandalf is outside Meduseld, speaking words of wisdom to Théoden.Talk to Gandalf outside MeduseldThéoden stands atop the steps outside Meduseld, gazing out upon his lands.Stand with Théoden and hear the commands of the kingGríma has been brought out of Meduseld and awaits the King's judgement.Talk to Gríma outside MeduseldThéoden stands atop the steps outside Meduseld, gazing out upon his lands.Stand with Théoden and hear the commands of the kingGríma has asked to be named steward of Meduseld in Théoden's absence.Talk to Gríma outside MeduseldTalk to Éomer outside MeduseldGríma has asked to be named steward of Meduseld in Théoden's absence.Talk to Gandalf outside MeduseldThéoden stands atop the steps outside Meduseld, gazing out upon his lands.Stand with Théoden and hear the commands of the king'I have long known there was strength still in this land, and in its king. Théoden's decisions on this day are not a surprise to me, and they should not have been surprising to you either, ${PLAYER}.''Théoden King has gone ahead with Gandalf, ${PLAYER}. Do you think he has forgiven us? I know in my heart we returned for the good of the kingdom, but it is a serious crime to disobey the word of a king!

'My heart is a-flutter, friend.''Gléowine still believes we will be punished, but my mind is not troubled. We returned to Théoden at the right moment for forgiveness. Was Gandalf not sent away with equal force? And yet now he has the ear of the king, and speaks wisdom to him.

'We return without the insight of the Wizard, but we bring something valuable all the same: warning of Saruman's reach and power. That warning too has value to the king, and when he chooses his course he will weigh what we have to say alongside the words of his advisors.''Now we will hear the commands of Théoden, and learn if we have truly come to him in time. Rohan stands at a crossroad, and it is up to her King to choose the correct course. We will help him choose aright, to the sorrow of Saruman!

'It is not magic that Gandalf uses to cure Théoden of the hurts that Saruman and his agent Gríma have wrought. No, our wise friend seeks to cure Théoden with words: words of friendship and hope. Already I see it working.''The air is fresh and clean, ${PLAYER}, and the tall grasses sway in the breeze. From here we can look out over the fields of Rohan. See how the sunlight dances upon that distant river?

'It has been some days since Théoden beheld his own lands, I warrant. Gríma gave him report of them, but always in such a way as to advance his own ends, and those of Saruman his master.'Gríma's eyes dart back and forth from face to face, sizing up the assemblage.

'My lord, can you not see what this Wizard and his ragged band seek to achieve? They do not care for your health or for your safety, and seek to lead you into danger. Your death would grieve them little, but there are those close to you who would mourn even the smallest hurt to your person.

'Listen to Gríma, and come back inside. Abandon the madness these cruel ones have instilled in your mind. Let me send them away. Speak not of war! That is a young man's endeavor, and you have ruled the Mark for many seasons. Will you not listen to your faithful Gríma? Send me not away!'Gríma hisses at you, his eyes narrowed unpleasantly.

'Do not disturb my lord more than you have already! He is weary, and needs his rest. Only when you and your irksome friends leave his lands will he be once again at peace.''Do you hear how desperately he wishes to be relieved of this charge? If that plea does not excuse Gríma from war, I can think of no other that will. I would not trust him to carry a sack of grain into the mountains, for fear he would steal either the sack or its contents, whichever he thought we would desire more!

'My uncle is no fool. He will not humour this request.''Enough! Gríma succeeds again, if not at his truest goal then still at one of value to his master. For Saruman is his master, and every hour we delay plays into his hands. We can spare no more time on him.'Barallas wishes to tell you of times before the siege of Fangorn Forest and the scattering of the Ents.Barallas is standing at the Enting Hollow in eastern Balewood.

Barallas has chosen to tell you of times long past in Fangorn Forest, when the Ents still stood united.Talk to BarallasBarallas is recounting his tale of the Ents at the Enting Hollow in the Balewood.

Barallas and the other Ents of the Balewood once stood united at the Enting Hollow before Núrzum came to Fangorn.Listen to Barallas' tale at Enting HollowBarallas is standing at the Enting Hollow in the Balewood.

Barallas has finished his tale of the Ents. You should speak with him before setting off.Talk to Barallas'Hoom. And so, little one, my tale ends. 

'Let us speak of other things...''We have made it, ${PLAYER}. Hoom... this forest has become so unfamiliar to me since Núrzum returned.

'Ah yes, he was here once before, little one, but then... he was different. What he gained in might, he lost in compassion for the creatures of this realm.

'Let us walk, and I shall tell you more of Núrzum and the Men of these lands.''And so, little ${CLASS}, you have heard all I wish to say on these matters.

'Let us return to Stonecliff... such an open space is a perilous place to remain....'The attack the people of Scylfig feared is now upon the town. Villagers throughout Scylfig need protection from the White Hand, but ultimately, the Mead Hall must not be breached. Therein are the women and children of the town.The White Hand have already penetrated the perimeter of Scylfig and are attacking. Speak with Thrymm to find out the plan to defend Scylfig.Speak with ThrymmFollow Thrymm to the northern stables to fend off the White Hand attackers.Follow Thrymm to the northern stablesFend off the White Hand attackers near the northern stables.Fend off the White Hand attackers at the northern stables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The northern stables have been secured. Speak with Thrymm to find out where to head next.Speak with Thrymm at the northern stablesFollow Thrymm to the centre of Scylfig to defend against the White Hand attackers.Follow Thrymm to the centre of townGárwig's grandson, Grimgar, has been holding his own along with his brother, Humbald in the centre of town. Speak with him.Speak with Grimgar in the centre of ScylfigA giant has breached the gate to Scylfig and is charging forth into the centre of town.Assist Thrymm in defeating any remaining Orcs in the centre of ScylfigThe southern stables have been secured, but the giant Núrzum has breached the gate. Speak with Thrymm to find out what to do next.Speak with Thrymm in the centre of ScylfigFollow Thrymm up towards the Mead Hall to make sure nothing gets past.Follow Thrymm to the Mead HallHelp Thrymm fend off the White Hand attackers along the path leading to the Mead Hall.Fend off the White Hand attackers along the path up to the Mead Hall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grimgar and Humbald met an unfortunate fate while dealing with Núrzum. Speak with Thrymm to find out the next course of action.Speak with Thrymm on the road leading up to the Mead HallGarsig and Cynegar are now trying to head Núrzum off at the road before he gets to the Mead Hall.Stand beside Thrymm and guard the Mead HallThe giant, Núrzum has breached the gate and is now heading towards the Mead Hall. It needs to be defended at all costs.Go to the Mead Hall and stand guardCynegar and Garsig were the latest to perish at the hands of Núrzum.Speak with Thrymm in front of the Mead HallThe giant, Núrzum charges forth towards the Mead Hall and is met there by Thrymm Red-beard. Observe the battle between the two warriors and ensure that no one gets into the Mead Hall.Stand with Cyneberg and observe the battle between Thrymm and NúrzumAfter defeating Thrymm, Núrzum turns and departs Scylfig. The women and children inside the Mead Hall appear to be safe.Speak with Cyneberg'We've experienced much grief today, ${PLAYER}.''${PLAYER}, we must hurry! The Orcs have penetrated the wall and are now attacking villagers. Follow me up to the northern stables!''My brother and I have this area well defended. We will not allow anything to get past us. Wait... do you hear that sound? What is that? The gate, the sound is coming from the front gate!''I don't know what I'll do without them...''Good work so far, ${PLAYER}. Our work is far from done though. Let's head to the centre of town to cut off the Orcs before they head towards the Mead Hall.''This is not good. Grimgar and Humbald were defeated rather soundly by the giant. We must not let their defeat be in vain. You and I need to go protect the Mead Hall at once!''${PLAYER}, we must protect the Mead Hall at all costs! Come with me!''${PLAYER}, whatever happens, you and Cyneberg must protect the Mead Hall. 

'Your assistance has proven valuable. Myself and all of Scylfig are thankful for your efforts.

'I must do this myself. You and Cyneberg must not intervene.'Núrzum is making his way towards Forlaw. He must be stopped before he is able to complete his path of destruction.Thrymm, Cyneberg, and Gárwig are prepared to defeat Núrzum. Speak with Thrymm along the ice bridge.Speak with ThrymmThe giant Núrzum is heading to Forlaw in an attempt to extinguish the last bastion of hope for the people of Wildermore. Run towards Núrzum until you're close enough for him to hear the sound of the Winter's Horn.Get close enough for Núrzum to hear the Winter's HornYou are close enough to Núrzum for him to hear the sound of the Winter's Horn. Blow the horn to get the giant's attention.Blow the Winter's Horn to get Núrzum's attentionClear the area of all threats before using the Winter's Horn again.Defeat frost grimsSound the Winter's Horn to damage Núrzum.Sound the Winter's HornClear the area of all threats before using the Winter's Horn again.Defeat frost grimsSound the Winter's Horn to further damage Núrzum.Sound the Winter's HornClear the area of all threats before using the Winter's Horn again.Defeat frost grimsNúrzum has been weakened. It should take one more sounding of the horn to finish him off.Sound the Winter's Horn to defeat NúrzumThe Winter's Horn caused massive damage to Núrzum, but he struggles through the pain. Make sure that Gárwig remains protected.Protect GárwigNúrzum has been defeated. The people of Wildermore will be terrorized no longer. Speak with Thrymm.Speak with Thrymm'We should leave this place now and  head back to Forlaw.''This is it, ${PLAYER}. We must make a final stand here and stop Núrzum. We mustn't fail, or we risk losing Forlaw.

'Once we get within range of the giant, you must blow the Winter's Horn. Once we have his attention, I will hold him off.

'Here, take the Winter's Horn. It will take some time to recharge its power, but you may need to blow it several times until Núrzum falls.''This nightmare is now over, ${PLAYER}. Our losses were great, but this giant will terrorize us no longer.'Barallas and the Ents have decided to assault Drû Vádokan and put an end to the White Hand presence in Fangorn Forest.Barallas is standing outside Drû Vádokan.

Barallas and the others have travelled to Drû Vádokan and now stand ready to raze what remains of the Orc forces in Balewood. You should speak to him while you wait for the others to arrive.Talk to BarallasBarallas is outside Drû Vádokan.

You should wait for the other Ents to arrive before beginning the assault.Wait for the Ents to arrive outside Drû VádokanBarallas and the other Ents are outside Drû Vádokan.

The Ents are ready to assault Drû Vádokan. You should speak to Barallas and begin the assault.Talk to BarallasBarallas and the Ents are marching to assault Drû Vádokan.

You should follow Barallas and the other Ents as they march to the gate of Drû Vádokan.Follow Barallas and the Ents to the gateBarallas and the Ents are attacking Drû Vádokan.

You should follow them into battle to ensure their success.Fight your way through Drû VádokanVoskor is standing in the middle of Drû Vádokan.

You should approach Voskor and confront him with the Ents of Balewood.Approach VoskorVoskor can be found inside Drû Vádokan.

Barallas and the Ents have discovered a vile Uruk leading the Orc forces in Balewood, but he appears to be wounded.Defeat Voskor'The Orcs will trouble us no longer, my bold friend. Hoom. Let us return to Stonecliff and enjoy this peace.''Hooom. We have travelled far, little one... and the time has come for us to reclaim our forest.

'The others have journeyed here, and should be arriving soon...

'Of course, if Tithenolf has fallen asleep again.... Hum, I could not speak to where he might be.'

Barallas appears to become lost in thought for a moment before remembering he is speaking to you.

'Hoom, I think I hear their approach.... Let us hope it is them, ${PLAYER}.''Hoom, I see the first of their kind just outside their camp up the road.

'Let us bring our branches crashing down upon them....'Following the tragic deaths of his wife and people, Thane Edric journeys to Edoras to confront Éowyn.Thane Edric can be found on the stairs to Meduseld in Edoras.

You have arrived in Edoras and should now follow Edric as he seeks Éowyn.Talk to Thane EdricThane Edric can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.

You have ridden to Edoras with Thane Edric in search of Éowyn. You should follow Edric.Follow Thane Edric to MeduseldThane Edric is standing outside the doors to Meduseld.

Thane Edric is clearly overcome by his recent loss. You should speak to him.Talk to Thane EdricThane Edric is outside Meduseld in Edoras.

Edric seeks an audience with Éowyn. You should wait at his side.Wait with Thane EdricThane Edric is outside Meduseld.

Éowyn has arrived in response to Edric's shouts. You should wait until Edric demands your account of the events on the road to Aldburg.Listen to Edric and Éowyn's conversationThane Edric can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.

Thane Edric has argued with Éowyn and has now drawn his blade against her. You must defeat him.Defeat Thane EdricÉowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.

You have defeated Edric, subduing him before his madness could inflict any harm on Éowyn. You should now speak to Éowyn.Talk to Éowyn outside Meduseld''Come, we have more to speak of.''It was a long ride, ${PLAYER}. I hope your wits are still about you. Now, let us seek Éowyn...''Where is she? Where?!'

Edric seems oblivious to your attempts to speak to him.'If he spoke true, I grieve for his wife and people...

'These are dark times in Rohan, and it pains me to see our people faced with such brutality. I know not when his madness will leave him, but I shall speak of the good he and Léoflad have done for our people and she shall live on in our songs.

'I know not why he forced you to follow him here, but I am thankful that you fought alongside me.'Ránmald feels isolated from the other women, and you do not wish to leave her alone with them in her vulnerable condition.You should speak with Ránmald.Talk to RánmaldYou should speak with Céolflad.Ask Céolflad why she is cold to RánmaldYou should speak with Edhild.Ask Edhild why the women do not like RánmaldYou should speak with Frithwyn.Ask Frithwyn why she does not like RánmaldYou should express your frustration and <rgb=#FF0000>roar</rgb> at the women.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This objective requires an emote.</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Roar</rgb> at the unkind womenYou should speak with Ránmald.Ask Ránmald if she will excuse you while you talk to the othersThe women of Byre Tor can be found at Aldstan's grave.

You should speak with the women.Meet the women of Byre Tor at Aldstan's graveYou should speak with Edhild at Aldstan's grave.Speak with EdhildListen to Céolflad's speech.Listen to Céolflad's speechTalk to Céolflad.Talk to CéolfladTalk to Frithwyn at Céolstan's grave.Talk to Frithwyn at Céolstan's graveListen to Frithwyn.Listen to FrithwynTalk to Edhild at Céolstan's grave.Talk to Edhild at Céolstan's graveTalk to Edhild again.See if Edhild needs comfort'I've seen enough, ye troublesome meddler. Let us return to the Steaping Cave.

'I'll not give Ránmald any more trouble.''They do not accept me. Do you see how they will not stand near me? Without Céolstan or the Thane nearby, they will be openly unfriendly.

'I have always been kind to them, ${PLAYER}! I must get used to being alone, until the child comes.''Leave us be, meddler! Ye'd rather talk to the nobility than to us, anyhow, eh?''Don't ye involve me in it, stranger. I've no love for the girl either, even if the Thane wished things different.''She thinks she's better than us, that's why! Has ever since she came to our little town from the south, from some fancy city.''You see? There is no hope to reconcile us.'

You ask Ránmald for a few moments to speak alone with the women outside.

'Yes, I will be fine by myself. Take as much time as you need.''What now, hm? Are ye telling us how we should grieve for our own Thane? Aldstan is our loss, not yours.'You ask Céolflad of what squabbles she speaks. What is the women's problem with Ránmald?

'It is no longer my concern. Now leave me be, meddler. Ye have struck me hard with grief, bringing me here to see my dear Thane in the ground.

'I'll be kind to the girl from now on. For him.''Why did ye have to bring me here, ${PLAYER}? I did not want to see him like this, buried, surrounded by wicked Orcs!

'This was a cruel trick. Ah! It is a stab of pain to see Céolstan this way!''Ye heard right, ${PLAYER}. I thought Céolstan would be mine forever, and he let me think so, until he brought Ránmald here.

'I'll never like her, no matter how hard ye try to stir pity in my heart. When I look at her...

'...I see that I was not good enough for him.''I shall miss ye, Céolstan.'

Edhild bows her head, and when she looks up again, her eyes are sharp and clear.

'I'll help Ránmald and see that the son of Céolstan, my future Thane, will survive this fell winter. I swear it on this grave.'Mossbeard wishes to tell you more of Núrzum's origins and the strange man who returned to the forest with him.Mossbeard is standing outside of Drû Vádokan.

Mossbeard is ready to tell you more of Núrzum's origins. You should speak with him and listen to his tale.Talk to MossbeardYou feel as if you can see Mossbeard's memories all around you.

As Mossbeard speaks, he describes a meeting between Núrzum and Saruman inside Drû Vádokan. Núrzum's past and his purpose in Wildermore are becoming more clear with each passing moment.Observe Núrzum's meeting with his ally'Now you understand, ${PLAYER}.... Let us leave this memory.''The rest of my tale begins where Brúndoron fell... though since that tragic day, much time had passed and many more trees had fallen to shape the walls of their disgraceful camp.

'Hoom. It is clear now that Núrzum's ally was no better than those he harboured within these walls, though far more mighty.

'When you are ready, little one, I will tell you what I know of Núrzum and how he came to possess such a stone.'You have come to Byre Tor with your companions to see what you can learn of Núrzum's seeming interest in the city.You have come with Horn, Corudan, and Nona to the city of Byre Tor.Talk to Horn in Byre TorYou have come with Horn to the eastern gate of Byre Tor, and the cold winds begin to rise.Talk to Horn in Byre TorNúrzum has returned to Byre Tor! Stay close to Horn, and out of the sight of the giant!Stay close to Horn and survive your encounter with NúrzumHorn is hiding behind a barricade in Byre Tor, as Núrzum encroaches upon his position.Talk to Horn in Byre TorStay close to Horn! Núrzum is moving through the streets of Byre Tor and you must not lose track of your companion!Stay close to Horn and survive your encounter with NúrzumHorn has retreated to the stables of Byre Tor, while Núrzum continues his destructive march through the city.Talk to Horn in Byre TorYou and Horn have found Corudan in Byre Tor, but the Elf and the Dunlending were separated by attacking Orcs and now Nona is missing.Talk to Corudan in Byre TorCorudan became separated from Nona when Orcs attacked, and now she is by herself somewhere in Byre Tor, with Núrzum stalking through the streets.Stay close to Horn and survive your encounter with NúrzumHorn is by the side of a building in Byre Tor. He is desperate to think of some way to keep Núrzum from finding Nona.Talk to Horn in Byre TorHorn is by the stables in Byre Tor, trying to come up with a way to keep Núrzum from finding Nona.Talk to Horn in Byre TorNona is in danger, but you can do nothing without putting the rest of you at risk! You must stay close to Horn and Corudan!Stay close to Horn and survive your encounter with NúrzumYou have escaped the centre of Byre Tor, but Nona is still in danger! Horn is at a loss, and does not know what he can do to help her.Reassure Horn that all will be wellNona has given Núrzum the slip, much to your relief and that of your companions... especially Horn.Talk to Nona in Byre Tor'We made it! Now we need to come up with some way to attract Núrzum's attention before he sees Nona...''I do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}! We cannot leave her! I refuse to leave Byre Tor without Nona!''The wind is picking up, ${PLAYER}. Do you feel it?'

Horn looks about with concern.

'I think we may have found what we sought, my friend! Stay by me, and get ready to run if we must!''It is one thing to hear of Núrzum's great size and strength, but it is entirely different to see it for yourself! How can we hope to fight such a creature?

'Woe be to Aldstan, if Núrzum finds him!''We cannot keep like this for long, ${PLAYER}. Núrzum may not be looking for us, but if he happens upon the two of us while searching for Aldstan, he will not show mercy. That much I know for certain!

'And what if he happens upon Nona and Corudan? We cannot stay here. We have to find them and leave the city!''We cannot do anything from here, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps if we could get to the other side of the courtyard...'

Horn's eyes are alight with the desperation of fear.

'We might be able to run behind Núrzum while his back is turned! From the far side of the courtyard we can get his attention, and draw him away from Nona!''It was not difficult to escape the giant, ${PLAYER}. He is big and I am small. He is slow and I am fast. He is an unnatural thing, given to evil, and I am the sister of Wadu, the daughter of Suvulch. He is alone and I have friends who care for me.

'This Núrzum was o'ermatched before he even came to Byre Tor today. I was never frightened of him.

'Still, I am glad we are safe. We should leave this place before he realizes we have gone. And ${PLAYER}, thank you for watching out for Horn, today and for the last several days. It eased the worry of my heart to know you were by his side.''What a relief it is to see Nona safe again! Núrzum will answer to me for threatening her!

'Another day, perhaps. Now we should return to Nona's cave and puzzle over the meaning of why Núrzum seeks this man Aldstan.''Byre Tor looks much as it did when last we were here. We have been fortunate to run into fewer Orcs than before, but remain alert, for they still hold this city.

'I have seen nothing yet that might reveal Núrzum's interest in Byre Tor.''Nona and I were driven apart by attacking Orcs, and I have not seen her since. She must still be in the city. We will find her again!

'That great shaking can only be Núrzum! We must not let him see us. If we do not dispose of these Orcs quickly he is sure to find us!'The Ents of the Balewood wish to impart their knowledge of Núrzum's assault into Wildermore upon you.The forest's edge can be found outside the eastern gate of Drû Vádokan in north-western Balewood.

You are standing inside Drû Vádokan, the White Hand's base in the Balewood. You must travel to the forest's edge and wreak havoc upon the Men of Wildermore.Leave Drû Vádokan and travel to the forest's edgeThe forest's edge lies to the south-east in Whitshaws.

You have found yourself beset on all sides by denizens of the forest. You should continue travelling to the east, but be sure to defeat any that stand in your way.Journey into Wildermore and defeat any that stand in your wayThe forest's edge lies to the south-east in Whitshaws.

The trees of the Balewood are enraged at your presence in the woods. You must defeat them if you are to seek your revenge on the Men of Wildermore.Journey into Wildermore and defeat any that stand in your wayDuskleaf is standing in northern Balewood.

You have found your path blocked by a strange tree that is looking at you with a mix of anger and confusion. You should speak with this tree before continuing eastward.Talk to the strange tree, DuskleafThe lands of Men lay to the east beyond the forest's edge.

You have defeated the Ent, Duskleaf. You should now continue eastward and fulfil the bargain that you made with Saruman.Journey deeper into the forest'What purpose could you have for such destruction, giant? Hoom. Do you even understand what agony you have brought upon the creatures here? You tear the trees from the ground, you freeze the Huorns where they take root, and even the foul wood-trolls are not spared your ire.

'My friends either lay sleeping in this winter you have buried us in, or they lack the courage to stand against you.

'Hooom... but I do not. I shall not allow you any further in these woods, monster!'Winsig seeks your aid in fighting to repel the vicious assault of Crúmgam on Snowbourn.Winsig is standing outside the east gate of Snowbourn.

Winsig has ridden with you to Snowbourn in hopes of fending off an Orc assault on the town. It seems you are already too late!Talk to WinsigWinsig has gone to find Fastred. You should aid the people of Snowbourn in repelling the Orc assault.Defend Winsig as she enters SnowbournGísling can be found in south-eastern Snowbourn.

Winsig asks that you find and aid Gísling and the people of Snowbourn while she seeks out Fastred.Find and talk to GíslingGísling can be found in eastern Snowbourn. He is overwhelmed defending the city from the siege and requires your aid.Defend GíslingGísil is said to be near the north gate of Snowbourn.

Gísling has moved to aid the people of Snowbourn and asks that you seek the aid of his father and Fastred.Fight your way to the north gate of SnowbournGísil is standing at the north gate of Snowbourn.

Gísil and his men were struck by a vicious assult of Orcs. Gísil is wounded, but seeks to locate Fastred.Talk to GísilGísil is in northern Snowbourn, and has asked you to follow him to the Mead Hall in hopes of meeting with Fastred.Fight your way to the Mead Hall of SnowbournFastred is standing outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

Fastred has emerged from the Mead Hall. You should speak to him at once.Talk to FastredAs the sky darkens, a familiar figure appears in Snowbourn. You should confront this man, and put and end to his villainy.Confront CrúmgamFastred now seeks to exact his revenge on his son's abductor.Defeat Crúmgam's forcesCrúmgam stands outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. Fastred's vigour is renewed after the safety of his son was assured. Crúmgam must be defeated to return peace to Snowbourn.Defeat CrúmgamFastred is standing in central Snowbourn.

Crúmgam has been defeated and the Orc force is broken. Fastred, his Thanes, and his people are safe for the moment.Talk to Fastred'Come, let us rest from such an ordeal. Once you are ready, I believe Gísil wishes to speak with you, but for now, we shall take our leave.''We have made it, ${PLAYER}, but I fear we have come too late....

'I must find Fastred at once... would you be willing to fend off the Orcs as I push through the front line?

'I'll meet up with you deeper in Snowbourn once I find him.

'On your mark, I will start my charge!''What luck! I expected not to see you again, ${PLAYER}....

'The Orcs are relentless, and I fear they shall soon overwhelm us.

'When you departed for Walstow, I sent word to my father in Garsfeld. I can only hope my message was received.

'If he has made it here, he would be near the north gate. I must hold this location, but please, seek out my father!''Ah, it is good to see you....

'My men and I were ambushed as we approached Snowbourn, and I fear I am the last standing among us.

'I'd come to aid when Gísling warned me of the impending attack on Walstow. I hope that girl brought the might of my people down on those monsters.

'Fastred is somewhere among all of this chaos, but I have seen him not.

'He must be found - the man may be brash, but I fear for his family, and more importantly, the Sutcrofts. Let us search near the Mead Hall, perhaps he has set up his defences there.''What madness is this?!

'These fiends think us so weak that they strike at us in Snowbourn? I have slain many Orcs this day, and many more will fall before it ends.

'My own home was invaded by that scum, and I sent Elflád to safety in the barracks once I slew the Orcs to their last.

'I will slay as many as I must to see my son returned to my care. If I should find his abductor, I will split them from head to toe.''That wretch will not threaten the lives of those for whom I care most dearly ever again.

'His foul sorcery was no match for the might of Rohan and the valour of my people. The Sutcrofts will stand strong, as we always have.

'I wish to spend time with my son, now that I know he is safe. Such fear can never consume me again - he will be kept safe from harm.'Cyneberg tells you of the first attack on Forlaw by the White Hand. Not long ago, while Cyneberg was in Scylfig and before Thrymm left to join her, Thrymm and the twin sons of Gárwig courageously defended Forlaw from a large Orc attack.Edsig and Gárferth are prepared to defend the city of Forlaw, or die trying. They are encouraged by Thrymm's arrival, knowing that he could probably single-handedly defeat the attacking Orcs.Speak with EdsigThe Orcs have arrived with a rather large raiding party. This attacking force is quite possibly the largest to ever march on the city of Forlaw.Defeat the Orcs assaulting Forlaw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Orcs marching on Forlaw are almost defeated, but the worst is yet to come. They are spurred on by two lumbering and brutal war-trolls.Push back the final assaultThe enemy attack has been broken, and Forlaw remains unscathed. However, that this many Orcs are marching on the roads of Wildermore is troubling.Return to Edsig'We will go to our father right away to let him know what happened here.''Thrymm! We are glad you could make it. We sent word through town calling for those who could aid in our defence, but it is early and not many heard it. 

'A scout came to Lornsettle, frantic to report to Gárwig and the rest of us of a good sized formation of Orcs that were marching down the road toward Forlaw. They should be here any moment now!

'Gárferth and I will stay here to guard the gate. We will make sure none pass.''That appears to be all of them! Well done, Thrymm and Gárferth. You both fought well.

'Thrymm, this many Orcs marching down the roads is alarming. I can see it on your face. You look worried. 

'I share your concern for Cyneberg in Scylfig, and whether Scylfig is prepared. You should send word as soon as you can. Gárferth and I will see to the defence of Forlaw while you are away.'In the dark of Balewood, you have discovered a snow-covered pack, a sign that the refugees of Byre Tor may yet live.The Orc roadway stretches through much of Balewood.

Sensing that the refugees may be nearby, you decide to search the barren roadway for any sign of Byre Tor refugees before more Orcs return.Search the roadway for sign of Byre Tor refugeesThe man's attackers can be found on the roadway.

You have discovered a man of Byre Tor fleeing from vicious wood-trolls of Balewood.Defeat the refugee's attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Húna can be found along the Orc roadway in Balewood.

Having saved the man from certain doom, you should now speak to him to learn of his plight and the fates of the other refugees.Talk to HúnaHúna is travelling along the Orc roadway in Balewood.

You should aid Húna in seeking out his fellows in Balewood.Follow Húna deeper into BalewoodHúna is on the roadway in Balewood.

The snarls of Orcs in the distance have cut short Húna's heroics, and you should speak to him to discern what action is to be taken.Talk to HúnaHúna is running north-east of the roadway in Balewood.

Húna believes that his fellows might be found off the side of the road in Balewood. You should continue to follow and protect him.Follow Húna deeper into BalewoodThe Orc roadway can be found to the west of the cave Húna discovered.

Húna has reunited with Bebbe, but during their conversation the frantic screams of one of their fellows nearby has filled them with grave concern.Follow Húna and Bebbe to the Orc roadwayThe Uruk captain can be found along the roadway in Balewood.

Húna's fellow, Leodwald, has been wounded and captured by a vile Uruk captain of Isengard. You should confront the Uruk before any more harm can come to the Rohirrim.Approach the Uruk captain, VoskorThe Orc attackers can be found on the roadway in Balewood.

In response to your defiance, the Uruk captain has set his Orcs upon you. They must be defeated if the refugees are to escape the forest alive.Defeat the attacking Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Leodwald can be found laying on the roadway in Balewood.

You should speak to Leodwald about his condition before confronting the Uruk captain a second time.Talk to Leodwald and confront VoskorYou are frozen in fear as the ground trembles - you must wait to see what unfolds.Attempt to stand against Voskor and his forceThe cave can be found to the east of the Orc roadway.

The Uruk captain has been brutally defeated by a raging Huorn. You should flee for safety while the Huorn pursues the wounded Uruk into the woods.Flee to the cave with the Byre Tor refugeesHúna can be found outside the cave to the east of the roadway in Balewood.

You have escaped certain defeat from a powerful Uruk captain and a vicious Huorn, and should now seek shelter with the other refugees in the nearby cave.Talk to Húna and flee into the cave'Come, let us flee into the cave and leave such violence to the likes of them! Are you ready to follow us?''Thank you for your aid, friend....'

Húna struggles to catch his breath.

'My fellows and I became separated when the wood-trolls attacked us... I feel a coward for abandoning them so, but we are defenceless... I know not what fates have befallen them by now.

'You look like a hearty ${CLASS}. Will you aid me in my search for them?''Let us away, ${PLAYER}... I fear no good will come of us staying on this road. We should take refuge among the trees here, and perhaps then we shall find my fellows....''If these are truly the forces we are to contend with in this forest, I hold not much hope for our escape....

'Nevertheless... thank you for your aid, friend. We would have succumbed to the cold, even if those monsters had not found us.

'I mean you no ill-will, but such terrors are likely even beyond your skill, friend. You are welcome to stay with us until it is again safe to leave the cave.

'Come, let us warm ourselves and rest inside.''I... I think there's no rescue for me, stranger....

'The Uruk... he is too strong. Leave me....'Mossbeard has chosen to tell you of Brúndoron, an elder Huorn of the Balewood slain before Núrzum came into power.Mossbeard is standing outside the future location of the White Hand encampment in the Balewood.

Mossbeard is prepared to tell you a portion of what the trees have told him of Núrzum's origins before returning to Barallas and the others.Talk to MossbeardMossbeard's story is still unfolding.

Mossbeard is sharing his memories as learned from the trees of the Balewood. You should listen as he tells you more of this story.Listen as Mossbeard tells the tale of Brúndoron's fallMossbeard is standing in the future location of the White Hand encampment in the Balewood.

Mossbeard's story has come to a close. You should speak to him before continuing your journey to Barallas and the others.Talk to Mossbeard'Come, let us leave this memory and return to the others. Are you ready, little one?''Viler truths I have seldom known, ${PLAYER}. The others must know of these happenings soon, but you must understand as well if you are to continue to aid us.

'Hoom, where the Orc-camp now lies once stood a bold Huorn... one of the very greatest in this forest.  My memories of those days are as clear as ever they have been... but they are tainted by the knowledge I have gained from the trees.

'Come, let me tell you of the Huorn's fate....''Hoom. I have told you but half of what there is to tell... for far grimmer tales remain.

'Let us leave this place and return to Barallas and the others.'Hoping to cut down the White Hand invaders once and for all, Éowyn rides to Entwade with vengeance in her heart.Éowyn is standing outside the Mead Hall of Entwade.

You should speak to Lady Éowyn and drive the White Hand from Entwade.Talk to ÉowynÉowyn can be found near the Mead Hall of Entwade.

You should follow Éowyn.Follow ÉowynThane Edric's men can be found to the east of the Mead Hall of Entwade.

You should aid Agelman and Éowyn in combat.Aid Agelman and Éowyn in defending EntwadeAnrad can be found at the gate of Entwade near the Sutcrofts.

You have defended the southern flank of Entwade and should now secure the gate.Talk to AnradMordor Orcs can be found outside the gates of Entwade, hacking at the nearby fences.

Anrad has asked that you slip past the Orcs at the gate and engage Orcs attacking the walls of Entwade.Defeat Orcs attacking the palisades of EntwadeSíric can be found in northern Entwade with Womar and Gifel.

You should seek out Síric and aid him.Find SíricSíric is in northern Entwade.

You have discovered Síric and his men amidst slain White Hand forces. You should speak to Síric.Talk to SíricÉowyn and the others can be found to the west.

Éowyn is running toward the western flank of Entwade. You should follow her.Follow Éowyn to the western flankNâdar can be found at the western edge of Entwade.

You have encountered the leader of the White Hand forces in Entwade. You should defeat him.Defeat NâdarÉowyn can be found inside Entwade in eastern Kingstead.

You have repelled the White Hand and brought some measure of peace to the Wade. You should now speak to Éowyn.Talk to Éowyn'Come, let us return to Edoras.''The White Hand shall not trouble the Wade again, ${PLAYER}.

'While Edric may never have those he lost back, I know he felt what he did was right and I trust his dedication to his duty. I hope this can bring some sense of closure to him.''It is as I feared! The White Hand have already begun their strike against Entwade.

'We must move swiftly to aid Thane Edric's men in holding against the Enemy's forces.

'Follow me, ${PLAYER}!''You have come just in time, ${PLAYER}!

'The Orcs are upon us, and we cannot allow them to raze the palisades!

'We will slay any that make for the gate, but you must defeat those that attack the fence! Swiftly now!''${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again!'

'These wretched Orcs will trouble us no longer, but what of the others?'

You speak of the forces you encountered in the south and east of Entwade.

'Aye, that is heartening! We have slain all they mustered here, but we must secure the western flank.

'Let us move swiftly, lest the White Hand gain the advantage!'You have earned a moment's rest with your friends while you wait to see if Leaflock will come through with the aid Corudan thinks you have earned.Your companions are sitting around the fire in Nona's cave, and you should do the same. Simply <rgb=#FF0000>sit</rgb> by the fire and relax while you can.<rgb=#FF0000>Sit</rgb> by the fire with your companionsYour companions are relaxing around the fire in Nona's cave, having earned a small, and overdue, respite.Relax around the fire with your companionsNona has leapt to her feet, and wants to see what you think of the rumbling sound.Talk to Nona inside the caveYou have come outside with your companions to see what has happened.Join Nona outside the caveA mighty force of Huorns are leaving the Balewood. They can have only one destination: Núrzum!Watch the mighty force leaving BalewoodYour companions are transfixed by the sight. Only Corudan can manage the words to describe it.Talk to Corudan on the slope outside the cave'We should go back inside and bring what people we can out here to see this sight, ${PLAYER}. Who can say when such a marvel will be seen again?''${PLAYER}, what do you think makes that sound? Is it Núrzum? Has he found this cave at last? We must see what has happened outside!''Leaflock has done as we hoped he would, ${PLAYER}. He has sent Huorns to seek Núrzum. Will they prevail against him? I cannot say, but I know this: my heart is stirred by their march!

'They seem so different from you or I, and from Horn or Nona, so far removed from the daily worries of Men or Elves. But still they march for us against the evil of Núrzum, against the evil of Saruman.

'Even now Leaflock and his herd have not retreated so far from Middle-earth as to abandon its people. It is worth remembering.

'It seems our friends have remembered something as well, ${PLAYER}. I told you it would happen, did I not? I am certain I did.'At the order of Gísil, you are to aid to the crofters of Garsfeld as they travel south to seek safer shelter within the walls of Snowbourn.Gísling is standing with the crofters at The Raided Crofts.

Having made it this far, Gísling has asked for your aid in escorting the crofters of Garsfeld to Snowbourn.Talk to GíslingGísling is walking with the crofters along the road south to Snowbourn.

Gísling hopes you can aid him in escorting the crofters of Garsfeld to Snowbourn. However, he fears that Orcs lurk just beyond his sight and threaten to harm his people.Escort the crofters of Garsfeld to safetyGísling can be found along the road to Snowbourn.Talk to Gísling'Our journey has only just begun, ${PLAYER}... are you prepared to continue aiding the people of the Sutcrofts?''We have made it this far, ${PLAYER}, but I fear the road south will be fraught with danger.

'You have done well to deal so severe a blow to our foes near Garsfeld, but the fields to the south may be rife with Orcs.

'Let me gather the crofters, we must set out as soon as we are able!''We have made it, ${PLAYER}.

'Perhaps you and I are worse for the wear, but thankfully, the crofters have made it here unscathed.

'We have much to do in Snowbourn... let us get to it!'You have come outside of your home in town to find the snow worse than any weather you have seen in this part of Rohan.You have come outside of your home in town to find the snow worse than any weather you have seen in this part of Rohan.Ask Ludeca about the snowYou have come outside of your home in town to find the snow worse than any weather you have seen in this part of Rohan.Listen to your neighboursYou have come outside of your home in town to find the snow worse than any weather you have seen in this part of Rohan.Talk to LudecaThe rumbling came from north-west of town.

You should search for the source of the rumbling.Search near the windmill for the source of the rumblingLudeca is in Dunfast.

You should speak with Ludeca.Tell Ludeca of the terrible force north-west of DunfastSomething evil bears down on Dunfast.

You should ensure that everyone has evacuated their homes.Forthere's house is on the outskirts of Dunfast.

You should break into Forthere's house.Break the lock to Forthere's homeForthere is in his home in Dunfast.

You should convince Forthere to evacuate immediately.Convince Forthere to evacuate'The weather brought you out of your warm home as well, did it?

'A little snow never bothered anyone, but this is indeed strange.''What in the world was that??

'Gifemund, will you go look? You have experience in arms....''You are pale as a ghost, Gifemund! Whatever is it?'

You explain to your worried neighbours about the terrible force of menace and the blinding cold you felt north-west of the village.

'We should evacuate! Whatever terror approaches, I do not like it!''What is it, Gifemund?? Why does the earth shake?'

You hastily tell Léofburg to gather warm cloaks, food, and water, and meet at Herethryth's farm.

'I will do as you say, but...if we leave town, we shall all die of cold!''O what will become of us? I am slow, but I will try to keep up.

'Thank you, dear Gifemund, for coming to warn me! I am so afraid!''I will be out to meet you shortly, Gifemund! I will not be much longer.

'Between you and me, old friend, I have never been so afraid in my life! This unnatural winter has had me on edge, but...but this is worse....''Only cowards flee their homes. Fight alongside me, Gifemund, and drive the enemy back!'

Gifemund now recalls that he was still chilled by the icy power just outside of Dunfast. A heated argument between the two neighbours ensued, and Forthere became obstinate.Fastred wants to speak to you of his father, Dagred, the past Reeve of the Sutcrofts.Fastred is standing just outside his father's gravesite with Framferth.

Fastred wishes to speak to you about his people and his father's legacy.Talk to FastredFastred is walking through his father's gravesite.Walk with FastredCrúmgam stands at the eastern side of Dagred's Grave.

The darkening of the sky has heralded the arrival of a fierce Man of Mordor, Crúmgam. You and Fastred should confront this Man.Confront CrúmgamFastred is standing outside Dagred's Grave.

Having defeated the Orcs brought to his father's grave by Crúmgam, you should return to Snowbourn with Fastred.Talk to Fastred'Come, let us allow my father his rest. Are you ready to depart this place?''I come here often for peace, ${PLAYER}... though I seldom find it.

'The Orcs of these lands are relentless, yet... they find a far more dangerous foe in me than I them.

'You have much still to learn of my people and the troubles that come to the Sutcrofts. Come, walk with me.''I know not what dark machinations that man has laid for my people, but his presence here fills me with dread.

'I am certain this is not the last we shall see of him, but Snowbourn shall stand prepared against any terrors that come for us. In this, I shall not falter.'Walstow is under siege by Orcs of the East Wall who have finally brought their plans to fruition. Winsig and her folk require aid or another settlement of the Sutcrofts will fall to the same grim fate as Hytbold.Winsig stands just outside Walstow.

The town is under siege by the Orcs of the East Wall. You should speak to Winsig and begin your assault.Talk to WinsigWinsig is in Walstow.

Nearby homes have been set ablaze by Orcs, and Winsig hopes to keep her town from ruin.Follow Winsig into WalstowThe first stable lies just to the west of the Mead Hall of Walstow.

