Barallas and the other Ents wish to tell you of the day Núrzum came to the Balewood.Talk to Barallas and witness Núrzum's wrathBarallas can be found at Stonecliff in northern Balewood.

Barallas' tale of Núrzum's arrival in the Balewood has ended. You should now speak with the Ent and discover what is to be done.Talk to Barallas'Mossbeard has spoken true of many things over ages past, and as wild as his claims may be, I believe his tale. Hom. He has spoken to us further of the things the trees came to know of Núrzum's arrival in the forest and what destruction he visited upon the creatures of this wood... and my friend, Duskleaf.

'Núrzum's assault began to the west, upon the hill where Brúndoron fell. Hoom. Even the Orcs were terrified of his presence, and not one sought to follow him too closely in his trek through the woods to forest's edge. Already, he had drowned the surrounding lands in snow by bringing the stone into the forest, and the creatures of this wood knew well that something horrible had come with the winter's chill.

'Listen well, little one, and I shall tell you of how the forest rose and fell to Núrzum's might.''Are you ready to learn of Núrzum's destruction?''Learning of such things has brought a great sadness to me, ${PLAYER}. Núrzum's destruction did not end there, as you have long known. He rampaged throughout the forest floor, cutting a frozen scar through those helpless trees. Yet, even when he left the forest, the wounds he dealt to our lands would not be quick to mend.

'Hoom. Duskleaf was always quick to act, but in the face of such an evil, he also proved himself the bravest of us Ents.

'We cannot allow his sacrifice to wither upon the frozen earth here. To not involve ourselves in such a dire matter... hum, would be a disgrace to Duskleaf's memory and the good of this forest. If the Orcs yet linger in these woods, we must drive them out.'Mossbeard is greatly concerned for an elder Huorn of the Balewood. He wishes to seek it out and discover where the White Hand is making camp.The ice-floe can be found at the western end of Finglas' mead.

Mossbeard has asked you to examine the unnatural ice-floe in Finglas' Mead.Examine the strange ice-floe into Finglas' meadThe branches are above on a raised section of the hill. Perhaps you can look from atop the hill on the left side of the ice-floe.

Mossbeard wants you to look at the branches atop the hill to the right of the ice-floe in Finglas' Mead. He fears they may belong to the elder Huorn of which he spoke.The younger Huorn can be found on the hillside in north-west Balewood.

Mossbeard wants you to search on the hillside for a sign of the Huorn. He hopes that the elder Huorn has escaped a foul fate.Search for some sign of the elder HuornMossbeard is at your side.

Your search has come to an end. Mossbeard is deeply saddened by the loss of life in the forest. You should speak to him.Talk to Mossbeard'As we have journeyed, little one, the trees have spoken to me of many things.  Hoom. They are not as they once were, ${PLAYER}. I feel their fear, and as we draw closer to the hill above, I sense that the White Hand's encampment cannot be far. However, should that be true, I am filled with dread.

'An elder Huorn, one of the mightiest of his kind, once lived atop that hill. Either he has gone from this wood, or some terrible fate may have befallen him. The trees do not know of his fate, at least not those we have travelled among, so we must seek to learn what has become of this Huorn.

'Hum. Let us search these woods for any sign of him, and if he cannot be found for better or worse, we must discover where the Orcs are camped.''A Huorn frozen to the earth?

'What other horrors have the Orcs and Núrzum visited upon this forest?

'Wait, little one. With what little life remains, the Huorn is trying to speak to me.

Mossbeard creaks with fear as he listens to the Huorn.

'Brúndoron is slain, ${PLAYER}. We must return to the others at once.... Hum.

'As we travel, I will tell you more of what this Huorn has seen, my friend, but we must make haste to Stonecliff!'White Hand Orc-riders roam too near Alferth's memorial, and must be driven off.White Hand Orc-riders roam too near Alferth's memorial, and must be driven off.

