Cendal will be pleased to hear the south-west tower has been resupplied with arrows.Talk to Cendal'The assaults on this town have been unending. Every day, the enemy marches out with a new force. Catapults and siege weaponry have shattered many of our defences. The towers in the south have been devastated. Many have been destroyed, while the standing ones are no longer accessible from the ground.

'Our archers still stand at the tops of those towers and loose down upon our enemies. They are valiant warriors, but they are running out of arrows. We have strung up ropes from one of the standing towers to the tops of the others, but they are thin, and crebain are assaulting any who attempt to cross.

'Get to the top of the western tower, grab a stack of arrows and make your way across the ropes, avoiding the crebain and resupplying the archers in the south-west tower.''They will need more arrows soon, but I believe they are well stocked to fend off the next assault.'The Warg-riders use poison on their arrows that is designed to slow their targets when used in small amounts, but a lot can be deadly. A versatile weapon of this potency should not be left in the hands of the enemy...Barrels of poison, a favoured weapon of the Warg-riders, are stored around Edsig's Farm.Steal the poison from barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})New pups are being raised as Warg-mounts for riders in the back of Edsig's Farm. The Warg pups have supplies of meat and water that the Orcs placed for them. These would be effective places to put the poison you gathered.Poison raw meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Poison water bowls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The poison has been placed, and the Orcs in Edsig's Farm will hopefully not realize the source of the problem for some time.CompletedThese barrels are filled with deadly poison used for the Warg-riders' arrows. Taking the poison will make their weapons less effective, and it could be used for another purpose...The Warg-riders' poison has been put to good use. The Warg-trainers hopefully won't find the poison you placed until it's too late!Harding has not heard from the people of Wildermore in some time, and he grows worried that something has gone amiss in those feral lands.A camp of Wildermore's folk can likely be found near the northern border of the Wold and the Writhendowns.

