'My men and I will hold their attention here along the road. You must go now!'You have stumbled upon a snow-covered rucksack in the Balewood. If you move quickly, it is possible you may find some of the refugees of Byre Tor nearby.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>'I cannot thank you enough for your aid, ${PLAYER}. We have wandered in the cold and dark for some time now, and many of our number splintered when the Orcs and trees fell upon us.

'Your bravery in aiding us, especially Léodwald, was remarkable. I know not what horrible fates would have visited us had you not intervened. The creatures that roam this forest are those of the most dangerous breeds -- you too should remain here at least for a short time lest they find you again.

