Destroy targets to gain points towards the success of the celebration event.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest auto-completes upon beating the course.</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow time to expire</rgb>Points: ${NUMBER}'The people of Wildermore have much to be thankful for, ${PLAYER}, despite the destruction wrought by the giant Núrzum. The folk of Scylfig celebrate by holding a small festival outside their town.

'You should go there at once and join the festivities. I hear that they are holding a demonstration of mounted archery in the form of a race. Whether you are skilled or not, you should try your hand at it.

'A friend of mine, Wulfherr, is overseeing the festivities. He will be able to provide you with everything you need. Let me know when you are ready to go to Scylfig, and I will arrange your travel.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest requires Mounted Combat</rgb>

<rgb=#00FF00>Note: This quest auto-completes upon beating the course.</rgb>'You should speak with Wulfherr when you arrive in Scylfig.''So, Gyric sent you? Indeed, we do have much to be thankful for. While the giant wrought terrible damage upon our village, he is dead and we are alive. That is all the motivation we need for celebrating.

'We are hosting a demonstration of mounted archery in the form of a race. Take this bow and mount your war-steed. Follow the targets around and up the mountain and back down to the road, shooting targets as you go. I will score your performance. Green targets will yield one point, while blue targets will earn you five. Keep an eye out for the rare red targets -- often on high ledges -- for they will yield ten points.

'If you reach one hundred points, you will earn a reward! The race is timed, so you must hurry!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This quest requires Mounted Combat</rgb>

<rgb=#00FF00>Note: This quest auto-completes upon beating the course.</rgb>'You should speak with Wulfherr when you arrive in Scylfig.'You have realized with some alarm that you have not seen or heard from Cyneberg since venturing north, and decide it is time to search for her in the High Knolls.Cyneberg is somewhere in the High Knolls.

You should search a peak in the eastern part of the High Knolls to see if signs of Cyneberg can be detected.Search for signs of Cyneberg from the eastern peaks of the High Knolls'You have my thanks for your help, ${PLAYER}. I think we can make it from here.'

You are now able to search for Cyneberg, at last. Perhaps she will have given up on her search for Thrymm.

You should find her and return to Gárwig. There is not much hope for Wildermore, but perhaps its surviving people can still be saved.'You found me, ${PLAYER}? I did not expect to be found by a friend.

'I have been looking and looking... everywhere. There are no signs of Thrymm, from the High Knolls to the Writhendowns.

