 Tier 1'Complete 'The Fires of Smaug - Tier 2'There are many villainous monsters roaming the Westemnet, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many boars and bears in the WestemnetSlay many crebain in the WestemnetSlay many dunlending in the WestemnetSlay many goblins in the WestemnetSlay many Half-orcs in the WestemnetSlay many Herd-creatures in the WestemnetSlay many Orcs in the WestemnetSlay many trolls in the WestemnetSlay many Uruks in the WestemnetSlay many Wargs in the WestemnetSlay many wolves in the WestemnetThere are many villainous monsters roaming Wildermore, and the Free Peoples must do their part to slay them.Slay many mounted enemies in WildermoreSlay many Orcs in WildermoreSlay many snow-cats in WildermoreSlay many Uruks in WildermoreSlay many wolves and Wargs in WildermoreSlay many Wood-trolls in WildermoreDefeat many wolves and Wargs in Wildermore.Defeat many wolves and Wargs in Wildermore.Defeat many wolves and Wargs in WildermoreDefeat many wolves and Wargs in Wildermore.Defeat many wolves and Wargs in Wildermore.Defeat many wolves and Wargs in WildermoreDefeat many snow-cats in Wildmore.Defeat many snow-cats in Wildermore.Defeat Snow-cats in WildermoreDefeat many snow-cats in Wildmore.Defeat many snow-cats in Wildermore.Defeat Snow-cats in WildermoreThe refugees from Byre Tor holed up in the Balewood are fearful of the Orcs invading the forest, but also of the threat of freezing.Húna has asked that you scout the eastern edge of the Orc roadway through the Balewood and steal torches from their keeping.Search the roadway for signs of the Orcs' plansSearch the roadway for any foes the Orcs faceScout the roadway for sign of an Orc-leaderDestroy torches at the roadway's edge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Húna can be found in the hidden cave in southern Balewood.

You have scouted the path along the eastern border of the Orc roadway and destroyed a substantial number of torches. You should return to Húna and inform him of what you have seen.'I know not what to do... we have been away from our kinsmen for too long now, and the chill of this place has overcome us all. With the Orcs patrolling constantly, there remains little hope of our escape unless something can distract them, but I would not ask you to stand against them, ${PLAYER}... not yet.

'Before the others and I lost our way, we saw the glow of many torches in the distance. I knew well of the presence of the Enemy in this wood, and so we strayed far from their warmth. The Orcs must feel this chill, too....

'If you were to scout along the eastern edge of their roadway, perhaps we could learn more of their purpose here. Were I you, I would avoid travelling their path... their numbers overwhelm even the heartiest of our warriors.''You bring good tidings, ${PLAYER}... any ill-fortune that visits those creatures is all the better for us! Let us see how the Orcs handle themselves now! I wager they shall find their troubles insurmountable without the warmth of their torches in this harsh clime.

'You may yet be able to stand against them, friend. If their carts are halted and they are beset by the Wood-trolls, there can be no greater time to bring their schemes to ruin.

