Since Fastred will not hear you, you should speak with Gísling.Talk to Gísling'The tidings you bring are most... ill-timed. ${PLAYER}, Fastred's son has been taken.

'We know not by whom, as Sigeric still sits in the prison, but Fastred is consumed with rage like I have never seen him.

'To come between a father and son...that is truly unwise. I would not try to speak with him, but if you insist, I will not stop you.''My son...my only son, taken from me under my nose! Elflád claims she had left for but a moment and upon her return Folcred was gone...

'Fool guards! CAN I TRUST NO ONE?

'He will not be hidden from me, and when I discover who has taken him, I will make them regret the moment they stepped into Rohan.

'I have no desire to speak with you...get out of my sight!''This bodes ill for us, ${PLAYER}. Fastred is not himself, and our enemies beat at our door. We must aid Walstow before it is too late!'The wailing Daegul is bound to this location and cannot leave until it is freed by defeating its captor located within an island crypt.Head to the island in the middle of Lake Isingmere and find the crypt located there.Locate the crypt in the middle of Lake IsingmereEnter the crypt and look for the the wailing Daegul's casket located deep within.Open the wailing Daegul's casket deep within the cryptThe captor Daegul is not pleased that it has been disturbed.Defeat the captor Daegul located deep within the cryptNow that the captor Daegul has been defeated, the wailing Daegul will no longer be bound to the lighthouse.Speak with the wailing Daegul'I do not wish to be here. I am bound by my captor and cannot leave until freed.

