You should talk to the cow.Herethryth is at the Dunfast refugees' hideout in the Whitshaws.Talk to Herethryth'The cows were left behind when we left! I wish to go and lead them back here, but no one will let me leave.

'Do you think you could check on them? Their milk would help us survive....'

'There are four cows. Please bring back as many as you can!''It is good that we have stopped to help these folk, but we must find Thrymm. Let us hurry!'You have found the fourth cow, alive and well!

She was clever enough to evacuate Dunfast when the farmers were no longer there to protect the small herd.The cow looks pleased to be amongst farmers again, instead of braving the cold, harsh wild alone. She will provide milk for these hungry people, and will help them endure this strange winter.'Did you have any success?''I am so glad that you were able to find the one survivor! I wish I could return the favour for you, but sadly I have no information -- only gratitude. I hope you will accept it.'Fastred wishes to speak to you in private at the site of his father's grave. He has expressed a desire to explain his father's legacy and his hopes for the future of his people.Fastred can be found in the mead hall of Snowbourn.

Fastred has asked you to accompany him to the site of his father's grave, where he wishes to speak to you in private.Talk to FastredFastred can be found inside the mead hall of Snowbourn.

Having spoken to Fastred at his father's grave, and fended off a strange, powerful foe, you should speak to Fastred in Snowbourn.Talk to Fastred'${PLAYER}, you have done many a service for me and my people. While there is still more to be done, I wish to speak with you about a most personal matter.

'My father, Dagred, was the Reeve until quite recently. He died at the hands of those wretched Orcs on the field, and I will not rest until every last one of their ilk are slain and adorn the walls of Snowbourn.

'I wish you to travel with me to my father's grave - he was a great, great man, and many lessons can be learned from him even with his passing.

'When you are prepared, we shall depart.''${PLAYER}, something terrible our way comes. I fear it not, though.

'The Sutcrofts have stood strong through all trials that have faced us, and one man's arrival in our midst will not change that.

'I thank you for hearing my words in the field, and for your action when the time came. You will be of great aid to my people, of this I am sure.''Let us depart... there is much to speak of.'The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.Approach the Grim and begin the battle.The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.Defeat the Grim fueling the Easterlings furnace before it explodesDo not allow too much smoke to fill the cavesThe Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.Approach the Grim and begin the battle.Defeat the Grim fueling the Easterlings furnace before it explodesDo not allow too much smoke to fill the cavesThe Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.Complete 'The Fires of Smaug - Challenge'The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.Complete 'The Fires of Smaug' on Tier 1The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.The Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.Complete 'The Fires of Smaug' on Tier 2Gísling has decided that Snowbourn must be protected from the looming threat of Crúmgam, regardless of Fastred's orders.Gísling can be found in northern Snowbourn.

Gísling is frustrated by Fastred's distraction from the danger at hand, even with the disappearance of his son. He wants you to travel to Walstow with haste to aid Winsig and her people.Talk to GíslingWinsig can be found inside the Mead Hall of Walstow.

The Orc-force has been repelled, and Walstow is safe for the moment. You should speak with Winsig in the aftermath of the battle.Talk to Winsig'Fastred's grief has consumed him, yet a rider of Walstow lays dead off the road near Snowbourn from what you have said.

'I feel for him, I truly do, but he risks the lives of all of his people by forgetting what foes come for us. Walstow is in grave danger -- the fallen rider tells me that much.

'We cannot wait for Fastred to act: you must ride to Walstow and aid Winsig and her folk.''Walstow is in great peril... have you made ready to ride?''You fought well, ${PLAYER}.

'The Orcs fell upon us with such fervour, but their retreat fills me with grave concern. One of their strongest was slain, aye, but the advantage was still theirs.

'I must ponder this for a moment.'You have found some fresh fish on a rack outside of a locked-up home in the northern Whitshaws. You should find the owner of this home, likely a fisherman.The fisherman can likely be found at the lake's edge.

You should search for the fisherman and encourage him to seek refuge in Forlaw.Speak with the fishermenThe two fishermen are at their camp on the edge of the Isingmere, in the northern Whitshaws.

You should speak with the fishermen, now that they are done attacking you on sight.Speak with the fishermanYou have found some fresh fish on a rack outside of a locked-up home in the northern Whitshaws. You should find the owner of this home, likely a fisherman.

A fisherman would likely be at the lake's edge, hopefully not far from his home.'Enemy! We'll not suffer ye in the Whitshaws.

'Run, or I'll have yer head.'The fisherman no longer looks as if he will attack you (which is a good sign).

'You mean us no harm, then? I am sorry we came at you like that. The wilds have been dangerous of late.

'What is an outsider like you doing wandering the Whitshaws while our enemies roam unhindered?'Smala has asked you to bury supplies in the hope that they may return when the plains are safe from Núrzum's threat.The fishermen's supplies can be gathered around their camp in the north-eastern Whitshaws.

You should gather the supplies.The fishermen's home can be found south-west of their encampment on the lake.

You should bring the supplies to the homestead and bury them, in hopes that they will be useful in the future.Bury supplies in adequate locations (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Smala can be found at the fishermen's encampment in the north-eastern Whitshaws.

You should tell Smala that you have buried his supplies where he wished.'I'll pack up what I can, but most of this gear'll not travel well to Forlaw. I should hate to see it get into them hands of them Orcs.

'Will ye bury some of our goods for us, friend? I'd like to think that we'll be back before long. Back at the house, if you would. We'll find 'em again.''A very good deed ye did, ${RACE}! We'll be off at once.'Today's fishing catch should be drawn in and packed so that the fishermen may swiftly evacuate to Forlaw.The fish of today's catch can be found in nets along the northern edge of the Isingmere in the Whitshaws, near the fishermen's encampment.

You should draw in the nets to gather fish for the two men's journey to Forlaw, for they will need fuel for their trek.Collect fish from nets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The fishermen can be found at the north-eastern edge of the Whitshaws on the edge of the Isingmere.

You should bring the fish to the fishermen so that they will have food for their journey to Forlaw.'Morcar is a stubborn one, but perhaps we should leave. The Whitshaws has never been so cold, nor so deadly.

'I do not fancy the thought of wasting our catch, though. 'Twould be a favour if ye check the nets we have along the bank.'The man nods his gratitude and takes the fish you pulled in from the shore.

'Aye, this will do. Now we shall have food for our packs, if we can get Morcar to heed yer advice.'The fishermen complain of Warg-riding Orcs harrying them more and more frequently, making them uneasy.Harrying Orcs riding on Wargs can be found in the northern Whitshaws.

You should defeat several Orkish Warg-riders near the fishermen's haunt.Defeat harrying Warg-riders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat brutal Warg-riders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The fishermen are at their small encampment on the banks of the Isingmere in the northern Whitshaws.

You should speak with the fishermen.Return to Morcar'You urge us to leave, stranger? We are safer here than we would be on the frozen fields, where we have seen Orcs riding on Wargs. Some have even dared approach us, but our arrows sent them off again.

'No, we could not hope to leave while such deadly foes roam unchallenged through the lands.''I am glad you spilled the blood of the Warg-riders, friend. I am not sure that we will leave, but I am glad we will be safer whether we stay or go.'The fishermen have offered to carry meat to Forlaw to help bolster the food stores for refugees and townsfolk.Moose can be found in the Whitshaws, especially towards the north.

You should hunt moose and bring cuts of meat to the fishermen, so that they may bring it to Forlaw to help feed the people there.Collect large cuts of moose-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Morcar can be found at the fishermen's camp in the northern Whitshaws, on the edge of the Isingmere.

You should bring the cuts of meat to Morcar.'All right, all right! We'll go, then! We shall even try to carry as much as we can, since them gentle-folk at Forlaw shiver and go hungry.

'Food will be short. You kill the moose, we carry the meat, hm? Fair?''That's the stuff. Give it here, eh, and I'll see it gets safe into hungry bellies.'Gifemund spoke of two fishermen who often sold goods to the people of Dunfast who are not yet aware of the threat of Núrzum.Gifemund spoke of two fishermen who live in a house in the Northern Whitshaws, near the edge of the lake and the woods.

You should search for the fishermen's home.Find the fishermen's homeA fishing rack stands in front of the house in the northern Whitshaws.

You should examine the fishing rack.Examine the fishing rack'Come to think of it, there are other residents of the Whitshaws who have not been warned of Núrzum's presence. If Gárwig wishes everyone to evacuate to Forlaw, it would be good of you to let them know.

'The fishermen live in a lonely house in the northern plains, at the edge of lake and wood. They are not friendly, but they trade us fish and game every so often. While I do not like them, I do not wish them to be eaten by a giant!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest must be completed before the refugees leave the Whitshaws.</rgb>The fish on this rack are fresh-caught. Perhaps the fishermen are nearby, catching more fish....The Easterlings have set up a massive encampment along the eastern shore of the Anduin.The Easterlings can be found at the Ford.

Wulfin has asked you to venture to the Ford and defeat the Easterlings encamped there.Defeat Easterlings at the Ford (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wulfin can be found in Harwick.

Wulfin will be pleased to hear you disrupted the Easterling-camp at the Ford.Talk to Wulfin'The Easterlings trouble me, ${PLAYER}. They have set up a large encampment along the eastern shores of the Anduin, to the north near our guard-towers. I fear a large incursion is coming soon, and we may be ill-prepared to handle it.

'I wish you to strike first. Enter this camp and bring the battle to the Easterlings. Let us not give them the opportunity to fight upon our shore.''Are you ready to cross the Anduin and enter the Ford?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'They will regroup, but a few days' respite is all we need to recover and heal our wounds.'The runes that the Cargûl drop seep into the land and defile it.Runes can be found on the paths the Cargûl of the Ford walk.

Wulfin asked you to destroy the runes the Cargûl drop before they defile the land.Destroy Cargûl-runes at the Ford (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wulfin is in Harwick.

Wulfin will be pleased to hear that you destroyed several runes before they were able to defile the land.Talk to Wulfin'The land of the Ford was once green and lush, but it has been perverted and destroyed. Not by the Easterlings, but their foul masters, the Cargûl. As they wander the camp, they drop runes which burn their way into the spirit, filling it with malice and hate.

'If the rune is destroyed, its power fades and the land can be preserved. Do not get too close to the Cargûl, for they can destroy any ${RACE} with a single attack, but follow them closely. When you see a rune, destroy it.''Are you prepared to face the Cargûl of the Ford?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'One day, either the Cargûl will leave, or we will force them out. For now, I feel content that the land itself is safe.'Many were lost in the recent battles at Scylfig and Forlaw. Gárwig has lost many of his sons, but none were more important to the people of Wildermore than their hero Thrymm Red-beard. A funeral is being planned by Gárwig and Cyneberg so that the people of Forlaw can pay their respects and say good-bye to those who lost their lives.Cyneberg is keeping close to Gárwig in Lornsettle, the mead hall of Forlaw.

Funeral preparations are being made and the townspeople are getting ready to gather at the graveyard.Go to the funeral with CynebergCyneberg is back in Thrymm's home near the southern gate of Forlaw.

Thrymm and the others are now buried, and the time has come for the people of Forlaw to try to move on from their passing.Speak with Cyneberg'This is a day I hoped I would never see. I am burying so many of my kin today; Edsig, Gárferth, Thrymm and Gársig. Thrymm wasn't of my blood, but he was closer to me than any of my kin. He was my foster-son, and more importantly, was beloved by the people of Wildermore. Today we bury the men we lost in Scylfig and at the gate here in Forlaw.

'I need a moment to myself after everything that has happened, and will come to the graveyard when the gathering begins. Cyneberg is gracious enough to handle organizing the funeral for me. I believe it is about to begin. She is being strong for me, but please give her company today.''I had to lend a hand and organize this funeral for Gárwig. He has lost so many of his sons and grandsons. It is as if the enemy hunts his family as a cruel act of torture. I lost both my father and my love in Scylfig, but that is nothing compared to what he has lost. It is only right that I help with the arrangements.

'I am not sure if I am ready to say good-bye to both my father, Cynegar, and the man I love... loved, Thyrmm. But, whether I am ready or not, this is an important day. We can head down to the graveyard whenever you are ready.''I'd rather fight a thousand Orcs at once than do something like that again. I still cannot believe he is gone. Is this not just a bad dream?'The stream just north of Garsfeld is the breeding ground for a type of guppy unique to Rohan. The rib-bones of this fish are strong yet pliable, making for perfect needles for stitching wounds.Garsfeld guppies can be found in the river just north of Garsfeld. The fish is elusive though and rarely stays in the same location for very long.

Héalac asked you to catch several Garsfeld guppies.Catch Garsfeld guppies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Héalac is at Snowbourn.

Héalac will be eager to begin de-boning the Garsfeld guppies you caught.Bring the Garsfeld guppies to Héalac'While the Entwash has many fish, so do the streams that pour into it. Just north of Garsfeld is a small stream that comes up from undergound. In between the mouth and the first waterfall, a kind of guppy can be found.

'The Garsfeld guppy is unique because its bones are tough but pliable. There are no better needles for stitching and closing wounds. The fish is elusive though and rarely stays in the same location for very long.

'Head to the waters north of Garsfeld and catch several Garsfeld guppies, then bring them back here.'

<rgb=#FF0000>The Fishing Hobby is required to complete this quest</rgb>'These look like nice fat fish...I might be able to get a bit of meat out of them in addition to the rib-bones.'You are upgrading the gates of the townComplete The East GateComplete The West GateYou are adding a library to the town.Complete The Library: RebuildComplete The Library: Enhancements IComplete The Library: Enhancements IIComplete The Library: InhabitantsComplete The Library: Superior StudyThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The structure is rebuilt and ready to be turned into a library. There are many books and scrolls we can gather from across the cities and towns of the Eastemnet. The more we add to our library, the more our warriors can learn, and the better prepared we will be for whatever battles we find in our futures.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The structure is rebuilt and ready to be turned into a library. There are many books and scrolls we can gather from across the cities and towns of the Eastemnet. The more we add to our library, the more our warriors can learn, and the better prepared we will be for whatever battles we find in our futures.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Library is fully stocked with all the books and scrolls we could find. It is ready for someone to come in and manage the building, keeping track of the books and helping those who are seeking knowledge to find it.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'Knowledge is power, and the warrior that studies the battles of the past and the tendencies of his enemy greatly increases his chances of winning the battle. There is a small building in the back of town that, if rebuilt, we can outfit as a library and fill with books and scrolls that will allow our Rohirrim to gain the edge in battle.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'Books and scrolls are important, but without the right environment and tools to use to study them, you cannot get the full value out of them. We can add a superior study to our library that will allow those who are trained to utilize the building to its fullest extents.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'The goblins in the Living Deep use barrels of black powder to destroy the forest from below.Powder-kegs can be found within the Living Deep.

Dernstan asked you to venture within the Living Deep and safely destroy the enemy's black powder.Bring powder-kegs to the central pit of the Living Deep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dernstan is at Eaworth.

Dernstan will be pleased to hear you have safely destroyed several barrels of black powder.Talk to Dernstan'Goblins are clever creatures, dastardly in their approaches to war and the battlefield. Unlike the Orcs who walk about within the forest itself, the goblins have taken to the caves and are destroying the forest from below with their sorcerous black powder.

'The goblins plant the barrels, then the soil explodes out and the trees fall into the tunnels below. They are then dragged to feed the Enemy's war-machine. The forest cannot defend itself from this destruction.

'Head into The Living Deep, find the black powder, drag it to a safe place and destroy it.''Let me know when you are ready to venture beneath the forest and enter the Living Deep.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'More black powder will come, but any effort to slow the Enemy's advance is a victory for us.'The goblins within the Living Deep are attempting to destroy the forest from below.Goblins can be found in the Living Deep.Defeat goblins in the Living Deep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dernstan is at Eaworth.

Dernstan will be pleased to hear you defeated several goblins within the Living Deep.Talk to Dernstan'The Living Deep has been invaded by the sappers of the Enemy, foul goblins skittering about through the caves, assaulting the forest from below. The more of the forest that they claim, the greater their war-machine becomes.

'To defend ourselves, we must strike at our enemy. Head into the Living Deep and defeat the goblins within.''When you are ready to brave the tunnels of the Living Deep, we can depart.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>'They will return, I have no doubt, but for tonight we can sleep without the ground rumbling.'Refugees from Byre Tor have taken shelter in a cave within the Balewood, but not all came there safely.Léodwald has asked you to seek out other refugees that fled into the Balewood and help them find the cave.The cave can be found to the east of the Orc roadway through the Balewood.

You have found the six refugees of which Léodwald spoke. You should return to the cave and inform him of those that fell in the wilds.Talk to Léodwald'I am certain that you have heard, but we were not the only ones who fled into the Balewood. Our kinsmen are lost in the forest, and I fear we may never see them again. They are ill-equipped to survive in such conditions, and the Orcs hounded us at every turn.

'From what I have seen of you, you can handle such troubles, my friend.

'If you could, please search for them. When we separated, we were not far from here, but I know not how far they may have wandered in the dark.''A cave? Oh, thank you... thank you, stranger!''How lucky I am to have been found! Thank you for your aid, friend.''The cold bites at me, stranger. I must reach shelter!

'Thank you for finding me in these bleak woods.''It is sorrowful to hear of the fates that befell some of my kin, ${PLAYER}. This forest is a sorry place to meet one's end... and to such creatures....

'Although I am glad to see these three among our number again, I fear that we, too, are simply awaiting a similar fate here. If you would remain here with us, I am certain there are more ways you can aid us still.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Lumber-mill has been rebuilt, but there is much to do to get it fully functional and have it look like it belongs within our town. Bunks for the residents, crates and barrels for storage, and tools for the workers are all things that need to be added for the mill to begin full production.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Lumber-mill has been rebuilt, but there is much to do to get it fully functional and have it look like it belongs within our town. Bunks for the residents, crates and barrels for storage, and tools for the workers are all things that need to be added for the mill to begin full production.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Lumber-mill has been rebuilt, but there is much to do to get it fully functional and have it look like it belongs within our town. Bunks for the residents, crates and barrels for storage, and tools for the workers are all things that need to be added for the mill to begin full production.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Lumber-mill has been rebuilt, but there is much to do to get it fully functional and have it look like it belongs within our town. Bunks for the residents, crates and barrels for storage, and tools for the workers are all things that need to be added for the mill to begin full production.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Lumber-mill has been rebuilt, but there is much to do to get it fully functional and have it look like it belongs within our town. Bunks for the residents, crates and barrels for storage, and tools for the workers are all things that need to be added for the mill to begin full production.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Lumber-mill is ready for the woodcutters and workers to move in and begin cutting the lumber into boards that we can use to repair and rebuild the palisades and buildings of Hytbold. None of that can happen without the workers, though. It is time we send out a call across the Eastemnet and get this mill fully up and running.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Lumber-mill is ready for the woodcutters and workers to move in and begin cutting the lumber into boards that we can use to repair and rebuild the palisades and buildings of Hytbold. None of that can happen without the workers, though. It is time we send out a call across the Eastemnet and get this mill fully up and running.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'Most of a town is made of wood...it is a quick material to build with and makes strong structures. We have to be watchful for fire, but if we built with stone, it would be ten years before we finished. In order to get the wood we need cut into boards, we need to repair the Lumber-mill.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Lumber-mill allows for woodworkers to ply their craft and create anything from boards, to bows, to exquisite instruments. The better the quality and tools available on the workbench, the greater quality of item can be produced upon it. We can update and upgrade our Lumber-mill with a superior workbench that will allow us to craft the finest of goods.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'You are adding a lumber-mill to the town.Complete The Lumber-mill: RebuildComplete The Lumber-mill: Enhancements IComplete The Lumber-mill: Enhancements IIComplete The Lumber-mill: Enhancements IIIComplete The Lumber-mill: Enhancements IVComplete The Lumber-mill: Enhancements VComplete The Lumber-mill: Superior WorkbenchComplete The Lumber-mill: Inhabitants IComplete The Lumber-mill: Inhabitants IIYou are upgrading the Mead Hall.Complete The Mead Hall: RebuildComplete The Mead Hall: Outdoor EnhancementsThe Mead Hall: Interior EnhancementsThe Mead Hall: InhabitantsThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'A Mead Hall is nothing but a stacked pile of wood unless there are people living near and able to use it. With all the upgrades that have been made, we have a Mead Hall that the Rohirrim would be proud to call their own. If we send out a call, many will answer.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'A Mead Hall is nothing but a stacked pile of wood unless there are people living near and able to use it. With all the upgrades that have been made, we have a Mead Hall that the Rohirrim would be proud to call their own. If we send out a call, many will answer.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'A Mead Hall is nothing but a stacked pile of wood unless there are people living near and able to use it. With all the upgrades that have been made, we have a Mead Hall that the Rohirrim would be proud to call their own. If we send out a call, many will answer.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'A Mead Hall is nothing but a stacked pile of wood unless there are people living near and able to use it. With all the upgrades that have been made, we have a Mead Hall that the Rohirrim would be proud to call their own. If we send out a call, many will answer.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'A Mead Hall is nothing but a stacked pile of wood unless there are people living near and able to use it. With all the upgrades that have been made, we have a Mead Hall that the Rohirrim would be proud to call their own. If we send out a call, many will answer.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'A Mead Hall is nothing but a stacked pile of wood unless there are people living near and able to use it. With all the upgrades that have been made, we have a Mead Hall that the Rohirrim would be proud to call their own. If we send out a call, many will answer.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is the central meeting place of the town, where all come together for feasts and parties in the good times, and where they gather and lock the doors to defend themselves in times of battle. There is much to add to bring life, warmth, and the history of Rohan to the interior of ours.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is the central meeting place of the town, where all come together for feasts and parties in the good times, and where they gather and lock the doors to defend themselves in times of battle. There is much to add to bring life, warmth, and the history of Rohan to the interior of ours.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is the central meeting place of the town, where all come together for feasts and parties in the good times, and where they gather and lock the doors to defend themselves in times of battle. There is much to add to bring life, warmth, and the history of Rohan to the interior of ours.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is the central meeting place of the town, where all come together for feasts and parties in the good times, and where they gather and lock the doors to defend themselves in times of battle. There is much to add to bring life, warmth, and the history of Rohan to the interior of ours.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is the central meeting place of the town, where all come together for feasts and parties in the good times, and where they gather and lock the doors to defend themselves in times of battle. There is much t