ebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is rebuilt, but there is much to do in order to bring it to its full glory. There are many upgrades and enhancements we can make to the exterior appearance and landscaping surrounding the Hall. These small but important touches help to make a town feel unique and make it a home for its inhabitants.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is rebuilt, but there is much to do in order to bring it to its full glory. There are many upgrades and enhancements we can make to the exterior appearance and landscaping surrounding the Hall. These small but important touches help to make a town feel unique and make it a home for its inhabitants.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is rebuilt, but there is much to do in order to bring it to its full glory. There are many upgrades and enhancements we can make to the exterior appearance and landscaping surrounding the Hall. These small but important touches help to make a town feel unique and make it a home for its inhabitants.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The Mead Hall is the heart of any Rohirrim town. It represents strength, hope, and tradition. Once it is rebuilt, it will signal to the people of the Eastemnet that we are serious in restoring Hytbold to its former glory.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'Cyneberg decided she could no longer spend all day and night in Thrymm's home, if she wanted any hope of moving on. Before returning to Lornsettle to be with Gárwig, her rage boiling from those who defiled and destroyed the Wildermore she loved, she set out in search of Orcs and found them to the south....Gárnoth's Farm is south of Forlaw. When taking the road south out of Forlaw, the first road to the right goes to Gárnoth's Farm.Find Gárnoth's FarmSomewhere on Gárnoth's Farm there could be signs of Núrzum having been there.

Gárnoth's Farm is south of Forlaw. When taking the road south out of Forlaw, the first road to the right goes to Gárnoth's Farm.Search Gárnoth's Farm for signs of NúrzumNúrzum recently made a trail through Gárnoth's Farm. The path of footprints starts near the road toward Gárnoth's Farm.Follow Núrzum's trailThe Lieutenant of Núrzum is leading the forces occupying Gárnoth's Farm, and was found at the end of the trail made by Núrzum.Defeat Núrzum's LieutenantCyneberg is keeping Gárwig company in Lornsettle, the mead hall of Forlaw.Return to Cyneberg in Lornsettle'I miss Thrymm, and will probably always mourn his loss. If he were here, we could re-take the Fallows from the occupying force of White Hand. I cannot stand by while Orcs take over the Fallows, and all of Wildermore. I wish nothing more than to send Núrzum back whence he came.

'My hatred for these Orcs grows stronger by the day. I set out to scout their movements and found them at the farm directly south of Forlaw. Perhaps you can find signs that Núrzum was there, or what the Orcs may be doing?

'Please go to Gárnoth's Farm and find out what those Orcs are doing.''You found the farmers, and signs of the giant, but he wasn't there? Núrzum hasn't returned since his attack on the western gate, but he could come at any time to wipe Forlaw off the map for good. Núrzum must have given this Uruk-hai control of the assaulting forces in the Fallows until he returned.

'By killing his Lieutenant, the Orcs here in the Fallows should be disorganized and disconnected from the other White Hand forces throughout Wildermore. They won't be able to organize another raid on Forlaw for some time.'A number of nobles from the Reeve's family have taken up arms for the coming attack on Scylfig.The kin of the Reeve of Wildermore can be found in Scylfig.

You should see if the Reeve's son or grandsons need any assistance.Speak with Humbald, grandson of Reeve GárwigSpeak with Grimgar, grandson of Reeve GárwigSpeak with Gársig, son of Reeve GárwigCyneberg can be found sharpening her sword in Scylfig.

You should speak with Cyneberg.Speak with Cyneberg'The battle looms near, and we are as prepared as we will ever be! We have Thrymm on our side, my brave daughter, and the brave kindred of our Reeve, Gárwig.

'Will you speak with Gársig, the son of the Reeve, and make sure he has everything he needs? The Reeve's grandsons are here also, and ready to fight -- Humbald and Grimgar. Please help them however you can.''Another strong soldier to brave the Orcs' assault? Excellent!

'As grandson of the Reeve, my duty is similar to that of a wandering hero such as yourself -- to assist where I am needed!

'I relish a good fight. Let the Orcs come!''Ah, welcome to the battle-ground! I do not need any help, but thank you for asking.

'With the greatest strength of Wildermore's people gathered here, it would take a great army of Orcs to conquer Scylfig.''I am Gársig, son of Gárwig. Thrymm sent us warning not long ago of an unusual number of Orcs in the Writhendowns, and we have come to lend our arms to the defence of Scylfig.

'The Reeve's kin are responsible for the protection of these lands. We suffer no enemy to pass our borders!

'Thrymm is like a brother to me. I look forward to drawing swords with him once more.''Yes, I believe we are quite ready to fight whatever dares to come our way.

'I cannot wait to test my skill in battle alongside such great warriors of our realm!'You are upgrading the palisade.Complete The Palisade: Rebuild IComplete The Palisade: Rebuild IIComplete The Palisade: Rebuild IIIComplete The Palisade: Rebuild IVComplete The Palisade: Rebuild VComplete The Palisade: Rebuild VIComplete The Palisade: Rebuild VIIComplete The Palisade: Rebuild VIIIThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The palisade may stand, but the timbers are burnt and ready to fall at the slightest touch. It would be better if they were not there at all, for they provide naught but false security. We need to replace the wall, section-by-section, piece-by-piece.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The palisade may stand, but the timbers are burnt and ready to fall at the slightest touch. It would be better if they were not there at all, for they provide naught but false security. We need to replace the wall, section-by-section, piece-by-piece.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The palisade may stand, but the timbers are burnt and ready to fall at the slightest touch. It would be better if they were not there at all, for they provide naught but false security. We need to replace the wall, section-by-section, piece-by-piece.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The palisade may stand, but the timbers are burnt and ready to fall at the slightest touch. It would be better if they were not there at all, for they provide naught but false security. We need to replace the wall,