Gladsnel will be pleased to hear you finished the course in time.Talk to Gladsnel'Every Rohirrim must be able to ride as if he were riding the wind, he and his horse moving together as if they were one. The best way to test this is to race.

'We have set up a course that travels from Cliving up into the southern Wold, around the edge of the cliffs, then down and back west along the road until you return to the city.

'There are thirty points to hit among numerous twists and turns and curves. You are welcome to try if you think you are up to the challenge.''You handle your steed well. That course is not for beginners. I am impressed you were able to navigate it.'Fastred wishes to speak with you about your victories in the Sutcrofts, and the great work you have done for the safety of his people.The pendant can be found on a table next to Fastred inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.Pick up Fastred's pendantFastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.

You should speak again with Fastred.'You have done a great many things for the people of the Sutcrofts, ${PLAYER}. I wish to reward your tenacity with a symbol of our appreciation.

'On the table there is a pendant, a pendant of the Sutcrofts. Take it, for you have earned it most thoroughly.''Treasure that as a reminder of all you have done for the people of the Sutcrofts.

'We must rebuild in wake of this attack, but rest assured, our strength will never waver, and no Orc will ever claim these lands again!

'Glory for Rohan... may your courage never falter!'Cuthbald's Farm is the closest of the outlying farms to Thrymm's Farm, where those working the farms were supposed to meet should the outlying farms be attacked. Oter made it there and is worried because his brother Ragnold has not yet arrived.Oter asked you to call him over to you on your way to Cuthbald's Farm. On the road south of Thrymm's Farm is likely a good spot to summon him.Now that he is with you, speak to Oter before heading to Cuthbald's Farm.Talk to OterCuthbald's Farm is south-east of Thrymm's Farm.Find Cuthbald's FarmOter's brother must be on or around Cuthbald's Farm somewhere. With Wargs and Warg-riders around he likely didn't make it far.Find and help Oter's brotherOter's brother was trapped under debris, but appears to be all right. He looks eager to leave Cuthbald's Farm quickly, but would like to speak to you first.Speak with RagnoldOter's brother, Ragnold, has gone back to Thrymm's Farm. You should speak to Oter about saving his brother.Since his brother has been saved and has safely returned to Thrymm's Farm, Oter will be eager to speak with you there.Speak with Oter at Thrymm's Farm'With the farms being attacked by Warg-riders, I expected my brother to be here by now. He works on Cuthbald's Farm, which is just to the south-east of here. I think I see black smoke rising in the distance from that direction!

'I want to go look for him, but if Warg-riders are there I will be in as much trouble as he is. Can you help me find out what happened to him?

'I need just a moment to collect myself before we go. Here, take this horn and summon me when you are ready to go, and I should be ready by then. Use the horn down the road south of here, and I will catch up with you.''Help!''Help!''Help!''I sincerely cannot thank you enough. I'm getting out of here as soon as I can, and you should do the same!''Any ${RACE} that would risk their life to save my brother is a friend of mine. Thank you, friend. I should probably follow him back to Thrymm's Farm, to make sure he makes it back all right.''Not many of those that have been missing are found, and even fewer are found alive. I am one of the lucky ones, since you helped me find my brother! I am forever in your debt.''Help!''I am ready to come with you to find my brother. It isn't a good sign that he hasn't shown up yet, and that smoke rises from there. He is in trouble, so let us please hurry to Cuthbald's farm!'Gandalf the Grey is troubled by recent stirrings in the East. He wonders what has become of his allies and enemies of the past.Gandalf the Grey is troubled by recent stirrings in the East. He wonders what has become of his allies and enemies of the past.Complete 'Usurper of the Great Goblin's Throne'Complete 'Defender of Thranduil's Hall'Complete 'Champion of Iorbar's Peak'Complete 'Defender of the Road'Complete 'Defender of the Dale-lands'Complete 'Slayer of the Golden Dragon'Complete 'Warden of the Lonely Mountain'Mounted uruks are marauding across the north of the Entwash Vale, closing off the road to Thornhope and threatening any effort to reclaim the town.Mounted uruks can be found on the Road to Thornhope.

Holenmal has asked that you clear mounted uruks from the Road to Thornhope.Defeat mounted uruks on the road to Thornhope (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Holenmal is at Eaworth.

Holenmal is waiting to speak with you about your victories along the road to Thornhope.Talk to Holenmal at Eaworth'If we have any hope of reclaiming Thornhope for the people of Rohan, the road to the north must be kept clear and open. If we cannot travel along those paths, then there is no chance Thornhope will be ours ever again.

'The road is currently being patrolled by groups of mounted uruks. Roving bands move through the hills to the east and west of the road itself. While the enemy holds this ground, Thornhope will never return to our control.

'Speak with me when you are ready to ride north.''The road to Thornhope is not yet cleared, and more battles are yet to be fought, but you have won some great victories today.''Let me know when you are ready to depart for the road to Thornhope.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>An inhabitant of Dunfast has left and abandoned his home, and you cannot help but hope that he may have information for you.Cyneberg is at the refugees' hideout in the Whitshaws.

You should speak with Cyneberg.Talk to CynebergBased on the memories of the townsfolk, Iothete likely headed north into the woods from Dunfast.

You should search for Iothete, the man with the empty home.Find Iothete, the owner of the empty homeYou ask Gifemund about Iothete, the man who no longer lived at Dunfast. The draughty home piques your interest once again.

'Oh, Iothete? A senile old fool. He kept insisting that he was given a cursed relic, and then he left town when no one believed him.

'He holes himself up in the northern woods, now.''Another stranger come to lay a curse on me? Or...do you seek refuge from the cold?

'Which is it? Speak up at once!''That was an interesting tale! It would seem that this missing fellow might have information for you, ${PLAYER}.

'I will remain here and help these people get back on their feet. Do come back when you find that man! I must continue my search....Cyneberg has recovered enough to ask that Thrymm's body be recovered for a proper burial.Thrymm was hurled north-west by Núrzum.

You should <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> north-west of Scylfig for signs of Thrymm.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest requires emotes.</rgb>The item that caught your eye (a horn, perhaps) is just to the west of your last vantage point.

You should examine the item you spotted in the snow.Pick up the object that caught your eyeA body lies below the horn in the north-western Writhendowns, upon the road.

You should investigate the body, for it is likely Thrymm's.See if the body on the road below is ThrymmCyneberg is in Scylfig.

You should return to Cyneberg and show her the horn.Bring the horn to CynebergGárwig, the Reeve of Wildermore, can be found in Forlaw.

Cyneberg has asked you to deliver Thrymm's horn to Gárwig.'I know what I need to bear this grief. I need to see Thrymm's body properly buried.

'You saw yourself which way the giant threw him. Will you look for him, and bring him home to us? We should bear him to Forlaw then, for he is like a son to Reeve Gárwig.''Thrymm's horn! But no sign of Thrymm himself? Do not tell me this! My heart still thinks he is alive, but no one could have survived such a fall.

'Gárwig must be told. I was hoping we could bear Thrymm's body to Forlaw to be buried there, but... we must deliver the horn instead.

'I will meet you there, ${PLAYER}. I must attend to my people, and then I will leave.''I bid you welcome! Cyneberg told us of your valour at Scylfig.''Cyneberg told us that you defended Scylfig like it was your own home. I thank you for that, ${PLAYER}.''More dead... and you witnessed it all, stranger. News of your deeds has reached me, and I honour you for fighting alongside my son Gársig.

'More and more die, ever since this cold has set in. And now Gársig... Thrymm, Grimgar, Humbald... and Cynegar, a Thane!

'Thrymm was like a son to me, and I will keep his horn to honour him until the end of my line. I name it Winter's Horn, until a hero of Thrymm's ilk can claim it again.'Gárferth's Farm is one of the three smaller farms, and was abandoned recently when the others were attacked by the White Hand. Torwulf managed to escape, but his father never made it to Thrymm's Farm.Torwulf asked you to call him to you on your way to Gárferth's Farm. On the road south of Thrymm's Farm is likely a good spot to summon him.Now that he is with you, speak to Torwulf before heading to Gárferth's Farm.Speak to TorwulfGárferth's Farm is down the road south of Thrymm's Farm.Find Gárferth's FarmTorwulf's father must be on or around Gárferth's Farm somewhere. With many Warg-riders roaming the area, he probably didn't make it far.Winerad was barely hanging on, but didn't make it. Torwulf is likely in shock from what has happened, but he wants to have a word with you at the location of his father's death.Torwulf has gone back to Thrymm's Farm, and will want to have a word with you.Speak with Torwulf back at Thrymm's Farm'My father is missing! I can't believe he didn't make it here by now. I do not want to leave these men behind, but I cannot live without knowing what happened to my father. I need to go look for him. 

'Can you please help me find him? Here take this horn and summon me when you are heading that way, and I'll catch up to you.'You hear the old farmer's last breath rattle from his lungs as you kneel down to check on him. A peaceful look creeps across his face, in that final moment. He must have been on the verge of death for some time. He may have found peace knowing he was found, or from catching a glimpse of his last living son.'My father... he's gone? But he was just here. We saved him! I... don't know what to say.

'At least we found him, and he can be given a proper burial now. It is the least I can do for him. I can only hope he didn't suffer too much before we arrived.''It was not the outcome I was hoping for, but I appreciate your help. There is some comfort in knowing his fate instead of a gnawing unknown. Thank you ${PLAYER}.''Thank you for helping me find him. Let us make our way to Gárferth's Farm.'Gársig's Farm is in a remote location of the Fallows, and was recently abandoned. Siric made his way to Thrymm's Farm, where those escaping the outlying farms were supposed to escape to. But his friend Manléof, a fellow farmer, has not yet arrived.Gársig's Farm is on the far eastern side of the Fallows, near the Wold.Find Manléof at Gársig's FarmManléof, who was left behind at Gársig's Farm, is in very poor condition. He isn't likely to live much longer.Check on Manléof's injuries and defeat any nearby foesManléof didn't survive the encounter with Warg-riders at Gársig's Farm. You should let Siric know what has happened, and he is awaiting your return at Thrymm's Farm.Return to Siric at Thrymm's Farm'I barely made it here from Gársig's Farm! Warg-riders came out of nowhere... Manléof and I split up trying to escape. He should have made it here by now. 

'Those Warg-riders got my leg while I was escaping, and had to limp my way here. I can't make it back there with my leg like this. I beg you, mighty ${CLASS}, please look for him?''Thank you for trying, ${PLAYER}. The enemy came fast, and we had little chance to survive. I was lucky to make it. I will let Manléof's family know what has happened to him.

