The stone Saruman gave Iothete is the key. It is a fragment chipped from the very stone that Núrzum carries with him upon his back.

It is the source of the cold spreading throughout Wildermore, for it goes where Núrzum goes. Gárwig must hear of this discovery at once!The survivors of Wildermore still need a great deal of aid if they are to endure the long winter.The survivors of Wildermore still need a great deal of aid if they are to endure the long winter.Complete Deed - Wildermore's BountiesComplete Deed - Battles and EventsComplete Deed - Protecting the Lands of WildermoreComplete Deed - Riding in WildermoreComplete Deed - Warbands II: Wildermore's Roaming EnemiesGoblin-town's rich history can be found around every corner as the goblins have adorned their home with murals of ages past.Discover the first goblin-muralDiscover the second goblin-muralDiscover the third goblin-muralDiscover the fourth goblin-muralDiscover the fifth goblin-muralThe Gaunt-lord Ivar, aided by a band of sellswords, swept through the village of Stoneheight, in search of his missing helm. When his goals were reached, he abandoned the village to the care of the merciless sellswords.Search through the town for the leaders of the mercenary minions who still remain in Stoneheight.Search for Ivar's minions in StoneheightGundúl is one of the minions of the Gaunt-lord Ivar who remain behind in the village of Stoneheight. Defeat him and put an end to the evil caused by the goblin mercenaries.Defeat GundúlSearch through the remnants of the town for the commanders of the sellsword rebels.Search for more of Ivar's minionsBúbhosh-grat is yet another of the minions of Ivar at Stoneheight. This uruk-hai must be defeated in order to drive the bandits from the village.Defeat Búbhosh-gratThe leader of Ivar's sellswords has yet to be seen. This man must be overcome to end the occupation of Stoneheight.Discover the location of the sellsword leaderDale Truitt is the last of the sellswords in the service of Ivar. You must remove the mercenary leader to free Stoneheight from the grip of the vandals.Tithenolf wants you to discover what is causing the Wood-trolls and Huorns of the Balewood to become so aggressive.Wood-trolls and Huorns can be found to the south, east, and west of Stonecliff.

Tithenolf wants you to defeat corrupted Wood-trolls and Huorns of the Balewood and examine their remains in hopes of understanding what has driven them to such aggression.Examine remains of Baleful Wood-trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tithenolf can be found in northern Balewood at Stonecliff near the path to the Limlight Gorge.

You should return to Tithenolf with news of the unnatural chill surrounding the Wood-trolls and Huorns of the Balewood.Talk to Tithenolf'The forest... is not itself, friend. When Barallas and I awoke from our sleep, we did so in darkness. And... we awoke into violence. Hoom. Such happenings are troubling, and I fear that Finglas cannot wake to aid us, for he had been becoming more and more tree-ish, so to speak, before our sleeping.

'The Wood-trolls harry us wherever our limbs carry us in this gloom and the Huorns... they are unruly without Finglas's tending. They may be beyond saving, though I do not wish to believe it so....

'Hoom. The Wood-trolls must have been affected by Núrzum's passing. I can only wonder what wounds he inflicted upon them to make them far more hostile than they already had been to my kind.' 

Tithenolf heaves a heavy sigh.

'Seek out the Wood-trolls, and for the good of this forest, please return them to the earth. However, I would ask that you examine their remains and perhaps then we can discover what has driven them to madness.''You ask if this is the work of the cold? Hom. I have seen many a winter, little one, and this is not the craft of merely a chill in the forest.'You are upgrading the West Gate of the townComplete The West Gate: RebuildComplete The West Gate: Enhancements IComplete The West Gate: Enhancements IIComplete The West Gate: DefendersThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The West Gate is fully rebuilt and ready to be manned. It is a dangerous post, looking out into the hills of the East Wall, and one we will want well-guarded, for it is surely where the Enemy will march from. Brave warriors will be needed to stand guard.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The West Gate has been rebuilt and now stands firmly, but there is much to do to finish it. Banners, flags, shields, and places for the warriors who will man it and stand to defend us against assault must all be set up and built.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'The West Gate has been rebuilt and now stands firmly, but there is much to do to finish it. Banners, flags, shields, and places for the warriors who will man it and stand to defend us against assault must all be set up and built.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.'Hytbold only has two gates: one in the east and one in the west. Both of the gates still stand, but the timbers are burnt out and would not hold against any concerted assault. The West Gate must be replaced and rebuilt if we are to have any security.''Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'One of the three widows is Hereswith. She cannot fathom life without her husband, Edsig, who fell in the Battle at Forlaw's Gate. However, she must find a way to go on as she is now raising their two daughters, Luba and Sigburga, alone.Hereswith is inside Edsig's house, near the stables and centre of Forlaw. Hereswith is trying to stay busy with household tasks, and not focus on the events of the day.Speak to HereswithGárferth's shield is kept in the bedroom of Edsig's home.Pick up Gárferth's shieldThe path to the graveyard of Forlaw is just outside Forlaw's southern gate.Place Gárferth's shield at Edsig's graveRespects have been paid to Edsig.Completed'Hereswith was devastated at the funeral earlier, and I imagine she is having a hard time today. Please check on Hereswith, who is now the widow of Edsig.'You paid your respects to Edsig, Gárferth, and both of their families. Hereswith will appreciate your help.'Forlaw has lost too many good men of late. My husband was one of those men. Edsig, and his twin brother Gárferth, were beloved by this town. They protected Forlaw in the Battle at the Gate, but fell to that seemingly indestructible giant. 

'Please pay respect to my husband. Edsig loved his brother, and would do anything for him. It is a fitting tribute since Gárferth was always Edsig's protector. Please take Gárferth's shield and place it on Edsig's grave.'One of the three widows is Ebba. She is reeling from the death of her husband, Gárferth, who fell in the Battle at Forlaw's Gate. Her kindness is unwavering as she cares for the orphans, Ansith and Cuthmar, as if they were her own children.Ebba is inside Gárferth's house, near the centre of Forlaw. Ebba and Ansith are preparing dinner after the long day.Speak to EbbaEdsig's helmet is kept on a shelf in the main room of Gárferth's home.Take Edsig's helmetThe path to the graveyard of Forlaw is just outside Forlaw's southern gate.Place Edsig's helmet at Gárferth's graveRespects have been paid to Gárferth.Completed'Ebba cares for the orphans, but has no children of her own. Now, with Gárferth's death, she will find it hard to not feel alone. Please check on Ebba.'You paid your respects to Gárferth, Edsig, and both of their families. Ebba will appreciate your help.'My husband, Gárferth, was a pillar of strength for Forlaw. Much like Thrymm, he was a great warrior, but nobody could match Thrymm. Gárferth's twin Edsig was wise beyond his years, and kept him focused on his goals and helping people. There was no one Gárferth cared for more than his twin brother.

'Could you help me honour Gárferth? He and I would be honoured if you placed Edsig's helmet at Gárferth's grave.'One of the three widows is Burghild. She and her youngest son Gárwald were devastated by losing three of their family in the Battle at Scylfig.Burghild is inside Gársig's house on the western side of Forlaw. Burghild is doing anything she can to keep herself from falling apart entirely, as she must keep it together for her only remaining son.Speak to BurghildGársig's sword is kept on the dresser in the sleeping quarters of Gársig's Home.Take Gársig's swordThe path to the graveyard of Forlaw is just outside Forlaw's southern gate.Place Gársig's sword at his graveRespects have been paid to Gársig.Completed'Burghild was especially hard hit by recent events. She lost her husband and two sons in a matter of days! There is not much one can do for someone in her state, but nevertheless, please see if she needs anything.'You paid your respects to Gársig for his family. Burghild will appreciate your help.'Are we doomed to wait for our death, as Gárwig is resigned to do? I don't fault him. He has lost everything he held dear. But today, we put what was left of our hope in the ground. Is there anyone left who could possibly save us from Núrzum? 

'I lost almost everything in the battle at Scylfig. My husband, Gársig, and our two sons; Humbald and Grimgar.

'I cannot go back to the graveyard today. Could you pay respect to Gársig and place his sword at his grave?'Explore the wilds of Wildermore.Explore the wilds of Wildermore.Discover The ElderwoodDiscover SteapingDiscover Enting HollowDiscover StonecliffDiscover Leaflock's MeadThe Lords of the Eastemnet have decided to hold a Witan in the newly rebuilt Hytbold.The Witan is being held at the Mead Hall of Hytbold.

