Hytbold has come under assault from an unknown enemy.Complete The Witan: The Battle for HytboldEdgal is at the Mead Hall of Hytbold.

Edgal will want to speak to you about what has just happened.Talk to Edgal'I never thought it would come to this, but perhaps we are more lost than I could have imagined. The Lords have agreed on a location for the Witan, and they are to have it here.

'The Witan is an ancient rite, a meeting among the leadership of the plains. Calling it is a privilege granted only to the King. If they are actually having one on their own, they must have lost faith and trust in his leadership.

'The Lords will be here soon, and we will be prepared for them. Today will be an important day in the history of Rohan, though I do not know if it will be remembered for good...or for evil.''We have suffered great losses...far beyond what I could have ever imagined from a single battle. However, Athelward and his betrayal was routed out.

'Perhaps now we will have a chance to unite the Eastemnet.''Are you prepared to attend the Witan?''Hytbold is under assault! Are you prepared to stand and defend it?'The Lords of the Eastemnet are holding a Witan to decide the fate of their lands.The Witan is being held in Hytbold.Talk to Harding to signal the beginning of the WitanThe Witan has begun and the Lords are discussing the future of the Eastemnet.Attend and observe the Witan'It is time to stand and defend all you have built here.''As Hytbold is your town, upon your permission I will open the Witan, and we shall decide if we will stand up for our people and defend the Eastemnet.'Hytbold -- and the Witan -- have fallen under siege by a great army of the Enemy.Defend Hytbold at all costs.Talk to HardingDefend Hytbold at all costs.Join Harding on the north flankDefend Hytbold at all costs.Defend the north flankDefend Hytbold at all costs.Join Ingbert on the south flankDefend Hytbold at all costs.Defend the south flankDefend Hytbold at all costs.Join Ides in the centreDefend Hytbold at all costs.Defend the centreDefend Hytbold at all costs.Defeat the trollDefend Hytbold at all costs.Regroup with the Lords of the EastemnetHarding waits to speak with you.Talk to Harding'Are you prepared to vacate the field of battle?''Are you prepared to join us on the field of battle this day?''The battle is over, our enemy is routed, and Hytbold is secured. Can we really declare that we won this battle, though? Béortnoth, Radwig, Gísil, Athelward... we have paid a high price for this victory. Perhaps too high.'Thrymm is concerned about the the damage the prolonged cold and snow has had on the Writhendowns, and would like to see how severe its impact upon the region has been.Ponds can be found near Thrymm's Camp in the north-eastern Writhendowns.

You should investigate the effects of the cold and snow around the frozen ponds of the Writhendowns.This situation appears more dire than originally thought. Thrymm Red-beard will be waiting back at his camp.Speak with Thrymm Red-beard'Wildermore has always been a green land with mild winters. We have never encountered snows such as these, as long as I can remember.

'I must prepare these men for battle against Orcs, for they have crept in with the cold, but if you are offering your aid, you may investigate the effects of the weather on our land.

'It cannot be coincidence that the Orcs and cold have arrived together.'Thrymm's face is lined with worry as you relay your findings to him.

'I do not like this at all. I am a warrior, and I will drive the Orcs off. But we are a simple farming folk here in Wildermore. We live off of this land. Even if we are safe from Orcs, we cannot escape this strange weather.'Discover where the foes of the Rohirrim dwell in Wildermore.Discover where the foes of the Rohirrim dwell in Wildermore.Discover FiskworthDiscover Fushaum-dorámDiscover Kadar-golnaukDiscover The Hungry PathsDiscover Drû VádokanThe farmers of the Fallows were captured by the Lieutenant of Núrzum at Thrymm's Farm. If they still live, they are probably being held captive somewhere in Gárnoth's Farm.The farmers survived their capture at Thrymm's Farm. They appear to be relatively healthy, all things considered. After all they have been through, they should at least have their freedom.Free the farmers (0/4)The farmers survived their capture at Thrymm's Farm. They appear to be relatively healthy, all things considered. After all they have been through, they should at least have their freedom.After being freed, the farmers have likely made their way back to the safety of Forlaw. You should head to the tavern since after surviving such an ordeal, some ale would look promising to anyone.Gárwig is in Lornsettle, the mead hall of Forlaw. He will be happy to know the farmers have safely returned.Speak with Gárwig in LornsettleThe farmers have been through enough and should be freed from captivity. Their captor, Laudh, must be close by. Perhaps the farmers can sneak out unnoticed once freed.'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for everything you've done for us. We will find a way to make a living here inside the city.

'My heart lives out on the land, on the plains... I was stubborn to give up that freedom before, when it was probably more wise to run to Forlaw. Trying to salvage that farm almost got us all killed. I would rather live, even if it's within these walls.''Things didn't quite go as planned, but we appreciate your help through it all.''Thank you, ${CLASS}. We would not have made it without you.''I think you have saved me three times over by now, or have I lost count? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We all owe you our lives.''Those good men did everything they could to maintain those farms, and tried to help Forlaw the only way they knew how. But, the enemy has made sure our farms remain smouldering, and those brave men were lucky to live through their ordeal. I will try to help them find work here inside the city.

'Your efforts to help them were courageous, and they owe their lives to you. The people of Forlaw appreciate when we can see good men return alive, when so many do not.'The farmers are desperate to get Thrymm's Farm growing crops again for Forlaw.  The supplies in Forlaw may not last much longer with this unnaturally long winter.Work has begun to repair Thrymm's Farm and it is almost time to begin working the fields.Help Oter prepare Thrymm's FarmThrymm's Farm was burned to the ground, and the farmers were captured by the Lieutenant of Núrzum, Laudh. Gárwig should be informed of what has happened.Speak with Gárwig'The next step is to get a field prepared so we can start planting. The sooner the better! Let me know when you are ready to get started.''We should get started on the field over there first!''The enemy mentioned an artifact or weapon that Núrzum is using? That is interesting news, but may not make much difference. Núrzum will be the end of us all, no matter what kind of artifact he is or isn't using.

'It is unfortunate that we lost the farm and those poor farmers, but there is not much we can do for them. Their efforts will not be forgotten, but they are likely lost to us like many of our good men have been lately.'Uruk-hai riders have been seen at Thrymm's Farm in the Fallows, leaderless without Núrzum, but nonetheless bent on wreaking destruction upon the lands of Wildermore.Thrymm's Farm can be reached by speaking with Dudoc to travel there.

You should travel to Thrymm's Farm and clean up the mess left by the roaming Uruk-hai.Cleanse Thrymm's Farm of messes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dudoc is in Forlaw.

