You should bring pelts to these people, so that they can survive here.'Did ye not hear me, ${RACE}? I said we don't need yer help! The women of Byre Tor are --'

Edhild pauses to eye the pile of warm pelts.

'I suppose... there is no use letting these fine furs go to waste. Thank ye, I suppose.'Cyneberg wants you to ask the people who escaped Dunfast what they saw.The refugees are huddled in their tiny camp south-west of Dunfast.

You should ask the refugees if they observed any relic to cause the ice-spire to appear where Núrzum sat.Cyneberg is at the refugee's hideout south-west of Dunfast.

You should speak with Cyneberg.Tell Cyneberg of the survivors' plight'I think we should ask these people what they saw that made them leave. Perhaps one of them knows aught of the artifact you seek.

'I do not suppose they will have any news of Thrymm, but no matter. We must see to the artifact first.''If I were to guess, these people need our help...but so does Thrymm! What should we do, ${PLAYER}?

'Please hurry and find out everything you can about the artifact....''Artifact? I have seen no artifact, and I did not see the giant who drove us off! Only a violent blizzard, and a terrible ruckus.

'Now we are here, freezing every night with no roof above our heads! My fool neighbours will not let me be warm! We will all die of cold, mark my words.''Do not bother to stop and help this lot of cowards! Anyone who abandons their home without fighting deserves just this: to be stranded, cold and homeless.

'These silly wretches fled, and dragged me with them, for they did not want me angering the enemy. They broke my door, knocked me down when I put up a fight, and then I woke up here.'

As one who barely survived a harrowing encounter with Núrzum, you can only shake your head at this man's foolishness.'I think we are doomed to starve here, stranger. It is very unfortunate that you did not come with provisions for my folk.

