'If only we had thought to bring them when we ran, but it was all such a terrible blur!''You ask strange questions of such desperate people, stranger. We saw nothing but our own shame as we fled our homes. Never have I been so afraid.

'No, I saw nothing, and I can barely remember anything of that day, for I have never been so hungry or cold in my life!''They cannot help us in this state, but we can certainly help them. I suppose I must put aside my search for Thrymm for the moment....

