'We must move swiftly if we are to escape with our lives!'Thane Edric and his men have turned their attention to protecting Entwade now that the people have fled to safety in Aldburg.Planks can be found outside several homes in Entwade.

Gifel has asked that you take some of the pressure off of Edric's men by boarding up some of the houses.Board up homes in Entwade with wood planks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gifel can be found inside the Mead Hall of Entwade at one of the tables.

You have finished boarding up the homes of Entwade, and should now return to Gifel.Talk to Gifel'Traveller, would you do me a favour?

'Thane Edric has asked that the homes of those who departed today be boarded up to protect them from any assaults that our foes might launch. I would complete this task myself, but I -- and I am certain many others -- would like to prepare the defences for the coming siege.

'If you would aid us, I have already set out the planks near the homes that need to be boarded up, so all you have to do is hammer them into place. This would save us a great deal of time, friend.''Thank you for taking the time to do this, ${PLAYER}. You bought our men more time to prepare for the coming siege in doing so.

'When this war has finally ended and our people can return, they can rest easy knowing that our foes did not invade their homes to any vile end.'In the wake of a sudden and brutal assault, Thane Mágla's trusted warrior lies slain by Uruks of the White Hand.Egbalth's horn can be found outside one of the burned homes at Bosa's Farm.

The leader of the White Hand forces at Bosa's Farm has not made himself known. You should sound Egbalth's horn to lure the Uruk leader to your position.Lure and defeat CurrThane Mágla can be found inside the Mead Hall of Middlemead.

You have dispatched the Uruk leader, Curr, who spoke of something deeply unsettling before being defeated. You should return to Thane Mágla with this information.Talk to Thane MáglaAs you look over Egbalth, you notice his horn lying amidst the nearby wreckage. While he likely sounded it to call for aid, only Uruks stood ready to answer. 

You have not been able to identify the leader of these Uruk forces thus far, but you suspect that sounding the horn once again might draw what remains of their force.

You decide to learn what you can of the White Hand's purpose at Bosa's Farm before returning to Thane Mágla.'Back so soon? What word does Egbalth send?

Mágla shrinks into a depressed slump as you inform him of Egbalth's demise and the fate of Bosa's Farm.

'I... he was the last of my council. What sense have I to continue this fight?'Thane Mágla fears for the safety of his people as supplies continue to leave Kingstead for other lands in Rohan.The traders' pavillion can be found to the south of the Mead Hall of Middlemead.

Mágla has asked you to take inventory of currently stocked goods in Middlemead. You can find these goods amongst the traders in Middlemead.Hildulf can be found on the raised platform at the traders' pavillion. 

You have noted the stock of Middlemead and should now speak to Hildulf.Talk to HildulfThe manifest can be found near Hildulf in the traders' pavillion of Middlemead.

You have spoken to Hildulf and should now take the manifest and return to Mágla.Collect Hildulf's manifestMágla can be found inside the Mead Hall of Middlemead.

You have obtained Hildulf's manifest and should now present it to Thane Mágla.Talk to Thane Mágla'${PLAYER}, there is a matter I have been helpless to affect in Middlemead.

'As a trading town, we gather many goods of Rohan here, but as of late, it appears more have been snatched up by our kinsmen in other lands, leaving little for the people of Kingstead and Middlemead. I would ask that you travel to the traders' pavilion and take inventory of the goods we currently store.

'Hildulf may know more of these troubles as well, as I have known him to keep a current manifest. When you have done this, return to me.''Ah, so you return!

'I have seen you peeking and poking about at the traders' posts. I trust you have found something of interest? Hm, your face says otherwise. A shame... 

'Mágla wants to see the manifest, you say? He may have it, and you should know that it is quite current.

'Before you go... I know his concerns, my friend, but tell him the trade still thrives! Goods leave just as quickly as they might return, such is the market in times of war.''Well, what have you to report?

'Crops remain the only plentiful thing in Kingstead, thanks to Bosa and the others on the plains. Our lack of arms and horses is greatly troubling though, despite Hildulf's feelings on the matter.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Sit a moment, I must review the manifest.'Agelman desires to earn Thane Edric's approval to take up arms against the White Hand and defend the Wade.Thane Edric can be found inside the Mead Hall of Entwade in eastern Kingstead.

Agelman has asked that you speak to Edric on his behalf about remaining in Entwade to combat the White Hand forces.Talk to Thane EdricAgelman can be found at your side or can be rallied to you by using your horn.

Thane Edric has denied Agelman in his request to remain in Entwade and battle alongside the other warriors. You should now speak to Agelman about what is to be done next.Talk to AgelmanA sword and shield can be found scattered about Entwade.

Agelman has asked that you arm him. He believes a sword can be found near the training dummies, and a shield can be found near the stable-master.Find a sword in EntwadeFind a shield in EntwadeAgelman can be found at your side or can be rallied with your horn.

You have recovered a sword and shield for Agelman at his request, and should now return them to his keeping.Talk to Agelman'Surely the Thane cannot be serious!

'The White Hand will return with their forces bolstered soon enough, and when the time comes, we must be prepared to defend Entwade! I was trained in the art of sword-play by my father before his passing, as were my brothers before they travelled to aid the King... certainly I can be of more use to the Thane here than I would be inside the walls of Aldburg. One man cannot tend the farms in the absence of our people, so what other purpose have I if not to defend the lands of the King.

'I beg you, ${PLAYER}, speak to the Thane on my behalf. Edric needs every able man he can spare, and I stand ready to fight for the Wade.''What madness is this? I have little time to ready our forces and he seeks to delay us even further with such bold declarations?

'I knew well his father and his skill with a blade, but this man has always been a crofter and though his hands be worn from his labours in the Wade, he is ill-equipped to battle against the Uruks and their ilk. I doubt not that he means well, but we do not have time to prepare him....'

Edric sits up in his chair and looks over your shoulder.

'Do you hear me, Agelman? I shall not hear such a plea, and though I apologize, you will find safety in Aldburg. ${PLAYER} will bring you to reunite with Léoflad and the others and that will be the end of it.''Thane Edric is a brave man, but he can fly into a rage like no other I have known.

'We will travel south then, but I shall not merely watch these conflicts unfold in my lands. Before we depart, I wish to arm myself. If I cannot protect the Thane and Entwade, his people shall be safe behind my shield.

'Let us look about town for a sword and shield, and then we shall be on our way.''Ah, these will do nicely.

'They have seen many a battle, ${PLAYER}, but such arms will aid me well enough. If Edric truly wishes me gone, we shall go, but I will take up arms for the people of Kingstead.'Thane Edric grows increasingly concerned by the presence of queer Orcs that have fled into the Westemnet from the Sutcrofts.Orcs can be found to the south of Entwade near the shores of the river Entwash.

Thane Edric's guard, Magenred, has asked you to slay Orcs that have fled into Kingstead from the Sutcrofts.Defeat fleeing Orcs near the Entwash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thane Edric can be found in the Mead Hall of Entwade in eastern Kingstead.

You have defeated the remainder of Orc forces that fled into the Westemnet. You should inform Thane Edric of your success.Talk to Thane Edric'As you have no doubt heard from Thane Edric, Orcs have crossed the Wade into our lands from the Sutcrofts. We know not what has driven them here, but they cannot remain for their numbers will bolster the already sizeable forces of the White Hand.

'They bear queerly adorned armour, but beneath it, they appear frailer than most we have seen thus far. It is my thought that Reeve Fastred and his men drove them off, though I would imagine Edric would take him to task for not slaying all of their number.

'We cannot abide them near our border. Ride south of Entwade along the edge of the river, and slay them. For how gaunt they appear, it may well be a mercy.''I know not if Reeve Fastred drove them from his lands, but the Orcs will find no safety here.

'You have removed another threat facing me and my men, and for that I am grateful. Though I have no love for Théoden, the Orcs of the White Mountains have long lain dead, and I shall not tolerate another Orc on the plains of Kingstead.'Thane Edric and his men have grown concerned about the Enemy's forces amassing outside Entwade and wish for you to investigate.The road to Middlemead runs along the northern fork of the road west out of Entwade.

Kenbert has asked that you patrol the road to Middlemead for the traders that often visited Entwade have not been seen in some time.Patrol the road to MiddlemeadThe road to Middlemead runs along the northern fork of the road west out of Entwade.

You have found naught but a barren road. You should continue your patrol along the road to Middlemead.Patrol further along the road to MiddlemeadThe road to Middlemead runs along the northern fork of the road west out of Entwade.

You have discovered the remains of the traders' carts, but no sign of the traders. You should continue your patrol.Patrol further along the road to MiddlemeadKenbert can be found near the fork in the road outside the western end of Entwade. 

You have discovered the remains of traders as well as their destroyed carts and goods. You should return to Kenbert and inform him of this dire news.Talk to Kenbert'Hail!

'I heard word of a hardy ${CLASS} that had come to Entwade, and surely that must be you. I have little time for introductions, but I am Kenbert. Thane Edric sent me to patrol the road to Middlemead, but I've met some resistance. The Uruks lurk all around us here, but I doubt myself seen. Middlemead is a valuable trading post of Kingstead, and Entwade was oft host to scores of traders. As of late, none have made it to Entwade, and Edric is convinced the King's departure marked an uprising of Uruks in our lands. If the trade routes are truly overrun, our situation will be dire.

'Patrol along the road to Middlemead, and I will hold my position here. If you can find any sign of traders or their goods, we will need to act swiftly or the Uruks will claim all!''Alas, I had worried this would be the case.  I mourn for the people of Middlemead, and I hope that such loss will not continue to visit our lands.

'Now then, we must form a plan...for the Uruks must be dealt with and our goods salvaged.'Thane Edric has turned his attention to the defence of Entwade as he and his men rally against the threats that surround the town.The privies can be found throughout Entwade.

Womar has asked that you investigate queer noises coming from the privies in Entwade.Womar can be found atop the raised landing inside the Mead Hall of Entwade.

You have searched the privies and found peculiar things, including an Orc and a man who hid away to avoid travelling to Aldburg. You should return to Womar.Talk to Womar'${PLAYER}, I have something to ask of you.

'As Síric said, I have heard noises coming from the privies about town in the night, but I have not been able to track their source. Síric and the others think me mad, but I know that something has taken up hiding in Entwade. If we are to secure the town as Edric demands, would it not be reasonable to investigate such a thing?

'If you would humour me, I would be grateful for your kindness. Go into town and search the privies. I am certain the noise must be coming from one of them, but the sounds have come from a different direction each night, so you shall need to check them all.''Ha! I knew my ears had not deceived me, but this begets yet more troubles for Entwade.

'Orcs hiding in the town? Unthinkable....and as for this man you found, Thane Edric will not be pleased that one of his people was left behind, especially if they intended to stay against his orders.

'We must speak more of this once the other threats outside Entwade have been quelled.'Thane Edric grows concerned for his men and steeds alike at Entwade as they make ready to repel a mighty assault by the White Hand.The stolen horses can be found among the Orcs near the river Entwash to the south of Entwade.

You have discovered slain horses of the Rohirrim of Entwade. In keeping with the Rohirric culture, you should bury them on the fields of Kingstead.Bury fallen horses on the fields of Kingstead (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have buried the stolen horses, bringing some honour to their grim end.CompletedAmidst the starved Orcs of the Sutcrofts, you have found a grim source of food sustaining them - the horses of the riders of Entwade. 

The fallen horses must have been stolen away as they wandered the fields. These mighty steeds of the Rohirrim ill-deserved such a fate, and should be buried on the plains of Kingstead.Although you could not save them from their grim fate, you have returned honour to the horses of the Rohirrim of Entwade and buried them upon the wide, beautiful plains of Kingstead.Aided by your efforts, Thane Edric's people begin their journey to safety, and now the threats that dwell nearby must be handled.Síric can be found inside the Mead Hall of Entwade, atop the raised landing.

Thane Edric has sent you to speak with his guard-captain, Síric. He wishes for you to brief the captain on the threats you recently learned of and aid him in any way you are able.Talk to SíricThe maps and papers can be found on a table near Síric.

Síric has asked for you to review maps and notes from other settlements in Kingstead to better understand the situation before speaking with one of his men.Examine the notes and map of the Westemnet nearbyWomar can be found near Síric on a raised landing inside the Mead Hall of Entwade.

Having reviewed the notes and map on the table, you should now speak with Womar before returning to Síric.Talk to WomarSíric can be found on the raised landing inside the Mead Hall of Entwade.

You have reviewed the notes and map in the Mead Hall and spoken with Womar. You should now return to Síric to learn more of what is to be done.Talk to SíricThane Edric can be found inside the Mead Hall of Entwade in eastern Kingstead.

You have spoken with the guard-captain and one of his men and have been briefed on the happenings in the Westemnet. You should now speak with Thane Edric in the Mead Hall.Talk to Thane Edric'My people stand ready, ${PLAYER}. I do not wish for them to delay any longer, for the sooner they depart, the sooner I can turn my efforts to defending Entwade once again. If you will allow me a few moments to say my farewells to my people, and to my beloved Léoflad, I shall find you after they begin their journey. Léoflad is a strong woman, of this I am sure, and she will know how to handle things should any trouble arise on their journey.

'${PLAYER}, these new troubles my men spoke of... they are greatly concerning. I worry that the White Hand rallies for a great assault. Our foes shall not break Entwade, not while I draw breath, but I fear for the folk upon the plains.

'The captain of my guard may not know of such threats, as he, too, has been distracted by the bustle of my people, but he must be told, for the time to act draws near. If you would, speak with him in the Mead Hall.''You bring ill tidings, traveller. ${PLAYER}, was it?

'I knew of a great many threats in Kingstead, including the Uruks to the north and west, but these Orcs that have crossed the shores... they complicate the already wide front of Entwade. We will need to deal with such things soon.

'I will speak with my men of what is to be done to defend our settlement, and you should acquaint yourself with the map and notes over on the table, while we wait for Edric's return. He will have much to say to Léoflad before he bids her farewell, so take as much time as you need. When you are able, speak with Womar, for he will be happy to talk to one as seasoned as yourself.'Notes and a map of the Westemnet lay strewn about the table before you.

The notes are primarily comprised of terse, unsent missives to Thane Mágla of Middlemead and Reeve Fastred of Snowbourn, but one in particular calls for able-bodied men to ride to Théoden King's side in the Westfold.

The map is heavily marked with numerous forces being noted in central and eastern Kingstead, and it also depicts the path of Edric's people through south-eastern Kingstead into the Eastfold. The largest threats are marked to the west and north of Entwade and the road to the north-west has been marked as overrun.'You know much of the threats facing us for having arrived so recently, ${PLAYER}. I mean no offence, but I wish that the others had spoken with us sooner of such concerns so that plans might have already been formed. Our men in the field likely know well of such problems, so perhaps they have already begun to work against our foes.

'For my part, I have heard noises about town at night, though I know not whence they come. I shall soon have to investigate those, but the others refuse to aid me.

'No matter, I have dealt with worse on my own. Síric has more to say to you, so I shall not keep you from your charge.''Womar is young and untested, ${PLAYER}. The last mysterious noise he heard was a chicken making a ruckus in a shed, so such an assertion is not new to me.

'His spirit is strong, though, and I know that in time, he shall become a fine warrior.

'Ho, did you hear that? I believe Edric has returned and the people have set off. You should speak with him below when you are able.''Aye, ${PLAYER}. Léoflad and the others have begun their journey. I pray that their travel is swift and unhindered, and I shall send word to them in Aldburg when such time is afforded me.

'Now then, let us speak of other matters.'Thane Mágla of Middlemead has readied his people but is hesitant to ride to Edoras until a troubling matter is resolved.The people of Middlemead can be found throughout the settlement in north-western Kingstead.

Mágla of Middlemead has asked that you acquaint yourself with the people of Middlemead. You should speak to any villagers or traders you encounter.Hildulf can be found near the traders' pavilion in southern Middlemead.

You have spoken to the people of Middlemead, and should now speak to the trade-master, Hildulf.Talk to the trade-master, HildulfThane Mágla can be found in the Mead Hall of Middlemead.

You have spoken to several inhabitants of Middlemead, and should now return to Mágla.Talk to Thane Mágla'Yes, yes... I know well of Théoden's charge and what my people are to do. They have made ready, and wait on my command to take their leave to Edoras and then further to Dunharrow.

'I am truly sorry for delaying Éowyn, but I refuse to send my people away until certain matters have been attended to.'

Mágla's voice drops to a whisper.

'I have reason to believe the Worm has eyes in Middlemead, and I shall not risk sending someone so treacherous to Edoras with my people.

'As a trading post, there are as many different goods as there are minds gathered here. For now, you would do well to acquaint yourself with the people and trade-master of Middlemead, traveller. I will tell you more of my troubles on your return.''Hail, traveller.

'I know not why we dally in our journey to Edoras, and I fear for my family. Mágla is a bright Thane, but I fear his injury has left him in a bad way.

'I wonder if he even intends to leave Middlemead....''If you'll excuse me, I have little time to talk.

'I must make it to the auction today for my family is in need of goods, and they have become scarce in these dire times.''The trades have become far too costly for my family - I have to work constantly to afford new goods. I see so little coming into town these days, and so much leaving it....

'We should journey to Edoras, for the King shall provide for us once more!''Ah, welcome to Middlemead, ${PLAYER}.

'Have you come to trade from faraway lands? Here, we trade the finest wares of Rohan... fine weaponry of the Stonedeans, the strongest steeds of the Broadacres, and the lushest crops of our Kingstead!

'Our traders are often travellers like yourself, you see. Perhaps you can join us for an auction if your time here can afford it.''I take it you have met with my people, ${PLAYER}. Now then, let us speak of more pressing matters.'Léoflad, wife of Thane Edric, seeks to lead her people south to Eastfold where they will seek safety in the settlement of Aldburg.The people of Entwade can be found throughout the settlement.

