You have spoken to numerous groups of people in Entwade and have sent them to gather at Léoflad's side. You should now speak to Léoflad and inform her that her people are ready.Talk to Léoflad'Ho, traveller. Edric has sent you to me? Good, perhaps now we shall be able to depart in some timely manner.

'It has been a great undertaking to uproot the people of Entwade, ${PLAYER}. At my husband's request, I shall aid in escorting them to safety in Aldburg to the south. Many have packed for weeks now, but we cannot afford to wait any longer. I protested when Edric bade me stay in Aldburg as well, but if I cannot return to Kingstead, then I shall aid the people of the Eastfold during my stay. Truly, they face great troubles as well.

'As for you, my people are as ready as they likely ever will be. Would you do me a great favour and bid them all join me here?''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You allowed me a chance to finish with other preparations, and now, it appears that everyone is here!

'Keeping them at my side will likely prove more challenging, but worry not, ${PLAYER}, for I have handled far worse!'As Théoden King rides to war with Saruman, Éowyn commences her efforts to gather the people of Kingstead to Edoras.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest will fail if you complete 'In the King's Wake' before speaking to Thane Edric.</rgb>Thane Edric can be found outside the Mead Hall of Entwade in eastern Kingstead.

Éowyn has asked you to travel to Entwade to assist Thane Edric in securing the Wade as his people evacuate to a more defensible shelter.Talk to Thane Edric'With my uncle Théoden bringing the war to Saruman, there remain a great many things to do in the Westemnet.

'To the east, the river-fort of Entwade lies along the Entwash's shores, and has held the Wade for years innumerable. Thane Edric commands the post and holds but a few men in his service. The White Hand has pressed into the King's lands as of late, and the cost of losing the Wade would be unknowable.

'I have many matters to attend to in my uncle's stead, but I know this is a task for which your skills are suited. If you would aid me, I will have your steed readied for the journey at once.'


<rgb=#FF0000>Note: When you accept this quest, you will immediately travel to Entwade in Kingstead.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest will fail if you complete 'In the King's Wake' before speaking to Thane Edric.</rgb>'At long last, Edoras sees fit to send anyone at all to the Wade. Perhaps Éowyn is a bolder leader than her uncle...'Hoping to cut down the White Hand invaders once and for all, Éowyn rides to Entwade with vengeance in her heart.Éowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.

