'The Uruks cannot be allowed to lay claim to our trade routes and goods. There must be some reason for their wanton violence, and I fear that they will use the resources of our rich lands against us.

'Ride along the road and slay the Uruks you encounter. Those near the carts have likely pillaged our goods, and they must be returned to Entwade if we hope to win this war.''You have lessened the blow to our lands, ${PLAYER}, if only to a small degree. With only my men and I stationed here, we will use these supplies to arm and defend Entwade.

'You have my thanks for bearing such a burden.'With dwindling supplies, the men of Kingstead cling to whatever rations and weapons they can muster.Fish-filled nets can be found along the river Entwash to the south-east of Entwade in eastern Kingstead. 

