You have built several warriors out of the materials Ellen suggested, and should now return to her.Talk to Ellen Fremedon'Look around you, ${PLAYER}. Do you see how many people take shelter under these trees?

'We are neither Edoras nor even Middlemead, and to host this many people stretches us far beyond our breaking. Yet, even now, evils lurk in the mountains above and what defences have we? None. 

'The men have gone to the side of the King, and left us naught but the shoddy remains of our barricades. What fear has an Orc of a pointed stick?

'Gather sacks and the armour from about town for they will remain unused otherwise, and assemble the crudest warriors you can along the edge of town. If even one Orc is fooled, we may consider our situation better.''Well done, ${PLAYER}, well done...

'These new defences are truly a boon to my people, or they would be... if they were not made of sacks! 

