Éothain recommended that you seek out the Thane, Arcil, who has been regent of Aldburg in Éomer's absence.Talk to Arcil'Hello there, ${PLAYER}. It is good to speak with you again; however, the circumstances could be better. Though Éomer has been freed already, word has not made its way to the Eastfold, where he is Reeve. The people, I am sure, would be pleased to hear it, and the news could bolster their spirits.

'Ride to the former capital of Rohan, Aldburg, and give the people there the news. While you are there, be sure to lend a hand...I fear that the Eastfold will be vulnerable with most of their men heading west. Be wary, though...the road to Aldburg may be dangerous in these days.''Éomer has been freed? He never should have been held captive in the first place, but I will not speak ill of Théoden King. 

'You say that you were attacked by Orcs unknown to you upon your journey here? I was recently following a party of White Hand Orcs, but you are certain these were not the same? My cousin Éomer and I have had many encounters with Saruman's Orcs, and I fear that they may attack us here in Aldburg.

'We will be watchful, but you should go speak with Arcil. He is a stout warrior, but as a Reeve...well, my cousin he surely is not.''You say that Éomer has been freed? This is surely wonderful news. However, while I am thankful to hear of this, we have pressing matters to attend here in Aldburg. 

'These Orc-attacks should not be taken lightly, but with our depleted numbers, we must bolster our defences.'Through your efforts in the Harrowdale, Ellen Fremedon and the people of Kingstead stand ready to travel to Dunharrow.Éowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.

Ellen Fremedon has asked you to speak to Éowyn.Talk to Éowyn in Edoras'We are as ready as we shall ever be, ${PLAYER}. 

'If Éowyn and the rest of Kingstead stand ready, we can begin moving to Dunharrow at her command. I know not if more matters demand her attention first, but Underharrow is prepared.

'I must tend to the people here, but ${PLAYER}, I would ask you to return to Edoras. Inform Éowyn that her people stand ready and waiting for the journey ahead.''Ah, so Ellen has made ready the preparations?

'I am glad to hear such tidings. She and I have not seen eye to eye on many matters, but surely, we both see the importance of sheltering the people of Rohan from harm.

'When we have made ready here in Edoras, we can begin our journey to Dunharrow!'After you saved Meregyth from the Boar-tribe Orcs, she went to Beaconwatch and waits for you there.Beaconwatch is south along the road.

