You have found safety within the fortified walls of Beaconwatch and should now seek out Meregyth to ensure that she arrived safely.Talk to Meregyth'Now that you have cleared a path through the camp, I think it will be safe for me to leave. 

'I will travel to Beaconwatch, as it is nearer and more heavily fortified than Fenmarch. There is a spot near the Mead Hall that overlooks Firienwood. I like to go there when I need to be alone.

'Beaconwatch is just down the road to the south. Meet me there when you are finished here.''I still cannot help but be sad; however, I realize that I am fortunate to have my life after being taken by those dreadful Orcs. I know in time that the pain will subside, but for now I cannot help but grieve for my misfortune.

'I should not burden you so with my troubles. I cannot thank you enough for your bravery and honour. There is no telling what those Orcs would have done had you not arrived.'Meregyth wants to make one last plea for help to Cútha.Thane Cútha is in the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch.

Armed with more information about the Boar-tribe Orcs, provided by Cútha's own son, you should speak with the Thane of Beaconwatch once more.Talk to Thane CúthaMeregyth stands near the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch.

Cútha was firm in his position and would not falter. He did, however, give permission to Cúthing to assist in whatever capacity he was able. You should inform Meregyth of the unfortunate news.Talk to Meregyth'We have more information now than the last time we spoke with Thane Cútha. Perhaps he will reconsider his position.

'Go to the Mead Hall and speak with him once more to see if he will provide assistance.''It is unfortunate to hear what happened to my son and his hunting party, but it does not change my position.

'As I have already said, as Thane of Beaconwatch, my sole duty is to stand watch over Halifirien and ride west when the beacon is lit.

'I will make one small compromise: I will allow Cúthing to assist in whatever capacity he is able. Now leave me, I must return to my watch.''I know that the Thane is duty-bound, but I did not realize that he was also heartless. It appears that we must do without assistance.

'Cúthing anticipated this and has been working on a plan to strike at the Boar-tribe.'The Boar-tribe camp is littered with bones. Examining them may yield more information.Bones litter the camp of the Boar-tribe Orcs.

