Éowyn has asked you to speak to Céolflad and obtain a description of the suspicious figure that interfered with her duty to empty the city.Talk to Céolflad in Edoras, north-east of the Meduseld stepsCéolflad saw a suspicious figure in Edoras, and now you should ask her questions to learn what you can of his appearance.Ask Céolflad questions about the suspicious man she saw in EdorasÉowyn has hurried up to you near Céolflad with news.Talk to Éowyn outside Céolflad's houseElfburg is in Edoras, north of Céolflad's home. She too has seen a suspicious figure in Edoras, and Éowyn would like you to ask her questions as well.Find Elfburg and question her about the suspicious man she saw in EdorasHorn has come to your position near Elfburg, and you should tell him what you have learned.Talk to Horn in Edoras'Let us go to Éowyn together, and tell her what we have learned of this man.''This way, ${PLAYER}. We will find the Lady Éowyn and see how her efforts have progressed while we saw to the will of her brother in Aldburg.'Nona's hands are clenched, and her eyes are ablaze.

'Step aside, ${PLAYER}. I will not listen to these children speak ill of my people.''Ha! I did not expect this turn, ${PLAYER}! It seems our Nona has an effect even on the children of Rohan! If Horn is not cautious, he may find she has little time for him, so busy will she be instructing these children in sword-play!

'You should go on ahead, my friend, and find Éowyn outside Meduseld. It may take us some time to get there.'Éowyn listens to your report of your visits to Underharrow and Aldburg, but you can tell from her guarded expression that something troubles her.

'I fear we did not root out all of Gríma's allies when last you were in Edoras, ${PLAYER}. I believe someone interferes with my efforts to empty the city. Someone cut holes in the sacks of grain we set by, and damaged the wheels of one waggon I did not think needed guarding. Céolflad saw a suspicious figure flee the city to the north.

'Speak to her and see if she can provide you with a description of this man. If we do not know his appearance, we will not be able to prevent him from doing more damage, should he return. Find her outside her home, to the north-east.''I will help you with anything I can, ${PLAYER}, if it will help the Lady Éowyn catch this man. Ask me what you will, and I will tell you what I remember of the man I saw.'Éowyn listens to the description you obtained from Céolflad and nods excitedly.

'Very good, ${PLAYER}, but we need confirmation and may now be able to obtain it. Another citizen of Edoras is claiming to have seen this man. Follow the road to the north and speak to Elfburg. If her description matches that of Céolflad, we should be able to trust their memory of this man.'Horn listens to your account, and nods.

'There are many men with blond hair and beards in Rohan, ${PLAYER}, but this brooch sounds distinctive. A red gemstone in the shape of an eye is not a common adornment among my people. This is how we will find this treacherous snake, and keep him from doing further hurt to Éowyn or her people.'Meregyth begins to regale you with the tale of King Folca the Hunter and the Boar of Everholt.The Boar of Everholt is nearby.

