The overseer asked that you gather ore for him.Collect ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The mine overseer is at Wid Isernore.

The ore you gathered should be returned to the mine overseer.Talk to the mine overseer'I have seen what you are doing for Gifemund, and I may have been wrong about you. I have been harsh towards you on a number of occasions, but you may yet prove useful. I still have my eye on you, though.

'I need you to deliver a letter for me. It has come time for me to step down as an advisor and better fulfil my role here.

'I now work with Gifemund, but I will not betray Herubrand's secrets. They are safe with me.''At least Elda had the courtesy of resigning, but if he returns he will have much to answer for. I am concerned that he could unravel everything that we have done, but I must trust that he told you the truth and will keep my secrets safe.

'His service to Gifemund is also concerning, for they make a powerful alliance that could unite Woodhurst behind them. For now, I need you to work for Gifemund and learn what he is up to....''You accept my offer? Then I welcome you, ${CLASS}. I will not deceive you: I have had my eye upon the seat of power here in Woodhurst for some time. I think you can help me acquire it.

'First, anyone who serves me must dedicate some time in my mine. Anything good in this life comes from hard work and dedication. Even Elda spent time there when he first came to me. Speak with the overseer there when you are ready.''Gifemund sent you? That is all I need to know. We are happy to have you. However, I tolerate no slacking on my work-site, so you had best be ready to work.

'I could always use more ore. Take this pick-axe and find a good vein to mine.''All right, not a bad find, but you should not be too proud of yourself, as I am not done with you yet. Gifemund did not specify how long I could have you for. Hold a moment and let me see if there is more that I can have you do for me....'Warg-riders from Isengard ride to and fro throughout the Broadacres, burning the fields as they go.Warg-riders from Isengard ride to and fro throughout the Broadacres, burning the fields as they go.

