You should return to Reeve Fríthild and let her know of her son's request.Talk to Reeve FríthildSuitable trophies might be found upon fallen enemies.

Fríthbert asked that you bring trophies from your forays to him and Edhild, and Reeve Fríthild has approved.Fríthbert and Edhild are at Fríthild's house, east of the Mead Hall of Stoke.

You should bring the trophies you collected to Fríthbert and Edhild.'I thank you for your kind words, ${PLAYER}. It means much, and I believe that Edhild is less afraid now.

'I wonder, though, if you would do us another kindness? As you battle alongside our mother, would you collect for us trophies from your fallen enemies? We are the children of a shield-maiden and should have tokens to display in honour of her victories.''Trophies of battle for the children? Indeed, Fríthbert is my son and his father's...I do not doubt that he will be a great warrior when he comes into his own.

'Indeed, let us watch for suitable trophies that they may display with pride.''These are wonderful trophies! I know what I shall do with this breastplate...it shall be well-displayed! And I shall learn to wield this sword with honour.''With these I shall follow in my mother's footsteps as a shield-maiden of Rohan! Thank you, thank you, good ${CLASS}!'You have accompanied Reeve Fríthild, Thane Ordlac, and Dudsig to the enemy encampment of Bardh-dorám.You should speak with Reeve Fríthild before starting your attack.Talk to Reeve FríthildDefeat the gate-guard and its minions.Defeat the gate-guard and its minionsDefeat Mabaj and his minions.Defeat Mabaj and his minionsDefeat Ushatar and his minions.Defeat Ushatar and his minionsDefeat Illska and his minions.Defeat Illska and his minionsEscape from Bardh-dorám through the postern gate.Escape from Bardh-dorám through the postern gate'So we have come to it, ${PLAYER}. The enemy is great, but they shall soon know the courage and strength of the Riddermark!

'Yon gate is guarded by a great troll. We will need to slay the beast ere we can enter the encampment.'You have joined Reeve Fríthild and her guests in the Mead Hall of Stoke for a feast celebrating the victory at Bardh-dorám.You should speak with Reeve Fríthild.Talk to Reeve FríthildObserve the feast in the Mead Hall of Stoke.Observe the festivities in the Mead Hall of StokeYou should speak with Thane Ordlac.Talk to Thane OrdlacA mug of water sits on one of the tables below the dais.

