'My leg is hurt badly, and I think I could use a splint and some bandages. Could you please see if the healer in the shop nearby has any supplies to spare?''Oh, how awful...that poor man! Aye, I have some supplies in a spare pack, which I save for emergencies. I have extra, so I can part with it without much concern. Please take it and use whatever you need to help him.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I must be more aware. The ruffians seemed to come out of nowhere! Will their friends come to finish what they began? 

'You will not always be around to protect me, and it seems that I cannot rely upon the guards. Some of the others have been leaving town, and I may have to follow if I wish to stay alive.'Madh-fushaum is home to an army of the White Hand's minions, and any army needs a network of sentries to alert the others of incoming threats.There are many Warg-rider sentries riding around Madh-fushaum alert for threats or victims. You should defeat as many of them as possible.Defeat Warg-rider sentries (0/8)There are many Warg-rider sentries riding around Madh-fushaum alert for threats or victims. You should defeat as many of them as possible.Defeat Warg-rider sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You managed to defeat the Warg-rider sentries without the force within Madh-fushaum being alerted to your presence.CompletedWhite Hand sentries are circling the perimeter of Madh-fushaum. They must be defeated before they sound an alarm, or if you need to escape quickly without risk of being pursued.The Warg-rider sentries are defeated, and the larger army is not yet alerted to your presence. You should be more easily able to slip into the camp undetected.The stalemate in Brockbridge was only temporary, as the enemy is marching to assault the city, and war drums can be heard in the distance to announce their approach.Talk to Herefara to aid the defence of Brockbridge.Talk to HerefaraHerefara is in Brockbridge.

Herefara would like to thank you for your aid in the battle.Talk to Herefara'We have stood toe-to-toe with the enemy for some time and have managed to force this stalemate. They are receiving supplies and reinforcements, and it seems they are setting the stage for an assault. I fear that when the hammer comes down, we will not have the men or supplies to withstand it.

'War drums can be heard in the distance. My worst fears are coming true, and they march on us in force. Please aid our defence!''The sound of the drums has grown louder, and the enemy cannot be far from us now. We must be ready!''${PLAYER}, you have my thanks. We could not have survived the attack, nor suffered so few losses without your help. You are an accomplished ${CLASS}, and you have proved your mettle. I would have you fight by my side any day.'The trolls from Isengard would put fear in any Man, and their brute strength would make them a force to be reckoned with on any battlefield.The pungent and unmistakable odour of troll fills your nostrils, and a small shiver of fear creeps up your spine. There must be one or more close by. You should deal with them before they become too great a threat.Defeat White Hand trolls (0/3)The pungent and unmistakable odour of troll fills your nostrils, and a small shiver of fear creeps up your spine. There must be one or more close by. You should deal with them before they become too great a threat.Defeat White Hand trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Trolls are among the more feared weapons of the Enemy. They were bred for war and can devastate a front line, break through barricades or defences, and can bring down structures as well as any ballistae.CompleteYou detect the unmistakable smell of troll coming from somewhere nearby. The trolls from Isengard are walking siege-breakers and are more versatile than the crude ballistae machinery.The defeat of the trolls will weaken the White Hand forces immensely, and may also hinder the use of their ballistae.Herefara has found that the map contains markings for an old fortification called Flodgeheld. It seems likely to have been attacked by the White Hand as was Brockbridge.Flodgeheld lies along the Swiftwater River to the south-west of Brockbridge.

