You should speak with the injured Rohirrim and learn what happened at this place.Talk to the injured RohirrimOne of the two slain Rohirrim you found earlier should have supplies that would aid Wilberth, the injured man you found.Search slain Rohirrim for healing suppliesThe healing supplies you found will stop Wilberth's health from declining due to the injuries, but it will take some time for him to fully recover.Wilberth would like to thank you for your aid, as he would probably have died not too long from now without help.Talk to Wilberth'I have been able to further study the map you found. I determined that one of these markings represents an old fortification called Flodgeheld, which lies to the south-west of here along the Swiftwater River. We have not heard from the men who guard it for some time, and they are likely in trouble, have abandoned it, or are dead.

'Please follow the river south-west and find out what state Flodgeheld is in, and if there are any survivors.''You have my thanks, kind ${CLASS}. My strength was fading quickly, and I am not sure how much longer I would have remained conscious. Once I am well enough, I will attempt to make my way to Woodhurst, but it will take time for these wounds to heal.

'In the meantime, I could use your aid in other matters, if you wish to give it.''You are not an Orc or Dunlending! I have need of your aid. I was convinced that I would die here. My wounds have grown worse, and I am weak.

'Are you truly there or do my eyes play tricks upon me?'Thane Léoferth oversaw the defence of Brockbridge when the White Hand first arrived, until his body gave out. He cannot fight and is barely able to speak, but his fighting spirit is an inspiration to Brockbridge in such dark times.Thane Léoferth is inside the mead hall which is near the centre of Brockbridge.Talk to Thane LéoferthDunith has long been Thane Léoferth's hand-maiden, and stays near his side to aid him in his regressing health.

