'It is time my advisors and I discuss our plan. We must discover who was behind the attack and reclaim my seat in the mead hall. If I returned now, I feel it might become my tomb, as it almost did before.''The advisors are on their way here, and the council meeting should begin in a few moments.''I believe I may trust the council, as they were always loyal to my father, Heremond. However, I have doubts regarding some of their motivations.

'Arnwi's observation about the missing guards is very troubling. Had they been there to help, my family might still live.

'Nevertheless, I believe that speaking with the guards who remain at their posts will yield our best chance of discovering the source of the attack.'Everyone in Brockbridge has prepared for a long siege. Despite any amount of preparation, however, there is always a need for more weapons.There are many Dunlending warriors along the perimeter around Brockbridge.

