You should bring the weapons you collected to the weapons cache in Brockbridge.Put weapons in the weapon cacheWeakening the perimeter gives the town a fighting chance to survive the siege, or at least maintain the stale-mate.CompleteEveryone in Brockbridge has prepared for a long siege. Despite any amount of preparation, however, there is always a need for more weapons. You should defeat Dunlending warriors in the perimeter around Brockbridge and collect their weapons.The enemies patrolling or holding the line were thinned out, and you helped re-stock Brockbridge's weapon supply by salvaging their weapons. This should help sway the battle in the defenders' favour.It appears that Gríma Wormtongue does indeed have business in Madh-fushaum, and his journey this far north was no coincidence. He may yet have a role to play in the struggle in the Stonedeans.You once again encounter Gríma Wormtongue, this time reprimanding the leaders of Madh-fushaum for what appear to be failures on their part. He clearly had business to attend to here before departing for Isengard.Observe Gríma reprimanding the White Hand leadersYou should observe Gríma reprimanding the leaders of Madh-fushaum for what appears to be failures on their part. You may be able to learn what involvement he has in the situation in the Stonedeans.Observe Gríma reprimanding the White Hand leadersGríma has finished his business in Madh-fushaum and now departs for Isengard.Observe Gríma reprimanding the White Hand leadersWhat you observed of Gríma Wormtongue's business with the leaders of Madh-fushaum and the role he has played in the Stonedean's turmoil would be wise to share with Herubrand.Talk with HerubrandYou find Gríma Wormtongue in a heated discussion with the leaders of Madh-fushaum. It is pretty clear he is unhappy about something, and you should see what he has to say....'You found Gríma Wormtongue among the White Hand in Madh-fushaum? He is a very powerful man, even after being removed from Edoras. It appears he still has quite a bit of influence here in Woodhurst.

