You should return to Herubrand to inform him of your success in bringing aid from Gapholt and defeating the White Hand forces in Mate Isernore.Talk to Herubrand'I have gathered the men, and they await my order to depart. I must speak with those who are coordinating the defence while I am gone.

'You seem eager to return to Woodhurst... feel free to depart when you are ready, and we will meet you there. I am a man of honour and will keep my word.''On our way here from Woodhurst, we saw that the White Hand had taken Mate Isernore!

'What can be done about them? They shot arrows at our caravan on the way by, and it seems like they could threaten Gapholt if left unchecked. The road to Woodhurst goes right by there!''Ah, ${PLAYER}, you have returned. It is good to see you again.

'Gifemund will be happy to know his mine will be less difficult to reclaim. The White Hand encamped there would only have added to our difficulties here eventually.

'Thane Nothmar arrived with his men shortly before you did, and we need to gather Gifemund and his men. The time has come for us to act.'The army gathered within Madh-fushaum is mostly comprised of ragtag Dunlendings, but they are mingled with Orcs and Uruk-hai. You should defeat as many as possible.The army gathered within Madh-fushaum is mostly comprised of ragtag Dunlendings, but they are mingled with Orcs and Uruk-hai. You should defeat as many as possible.Defeat enemies in Madh-fushaum (0/24)The army gathered within Madh-fushaum is mostly comprised of ragtag Dunlendings, but they are mingled with Orcs and Uruk-hai. You should defeat as many as possible.Defeat enemies in Madh-fushaum (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There are far too many of the enemy gathered in Madh-fushaum for one to handle alone. However, those that remain will never forget the day the you stepped foot in Madh-fushaum.CompleteThe army that built and now resides within Madh-fushaum has destroyed Flodgeheld and is responsible for the attacks and siege on Brockbridge. The time has come to go on the offensive.You have left a mark upon those that remain in Madh-fushaum, having seen their fellows soundly defeated. You took them by surprise, and they will not soon forget this day.The guards of Gapholt are not allowing entry without papers being checked and signed. This process is causing too much delay for the long line of refugees.There is a Gapholt guard behind a mountain of papers.

You should speak with a guard to see if there is an exception that can be made to help the refugees settle into Gapholt sooner.Talk to the guardThane Nothmar is near the bridge of Gapholt.

The guard told you to take your concerns to Thane Nothmar.Talk to Thane NothmarHrothwaru is near the bridge of Gapholt.

Thane Nothmar would not recant his position regarding entry into Gapholt.Talk to Hrothwaru'My children are crying and hungry, and I am at my wits' end. These guards refuse to let us enter until we present papers and have them approved and signed. Can anything be done to expedite this process?

'I have said everything I can, and they will not relent. Will you speak with them and see if you can sway them?''I do not have the authority to grant their entry without papers. They have all tried, and I will tell you what I told them: their papers must be checked and signed before I can allow entry, without exception.

'If you have concerns, then feel free to bring them up with Thane Nothmar. I am only doing my duty.''The process to enter Gapholt is the same as it always has been. It will stay that way. My priority is making certain that Gapholt remains secure. Making a few refugees wait is unfortunate, but necessary.''Do we look like Dunlending riffraff? It is absurd that we must wait to enter the safety of Gapholt...what if the Dunlendings fall upon us?'A scout has just come from the Stonedeans, and it would seem that the people of that land are in need of aid.Oter can be found on the road in the Stonedeans, near Woodhurst.

You should hasten to the Stonedeans and find out more from Oter.Find Oter in the Stonedeans'I have just come from the Stonedeans. A fellow I met on the road there, Oter, told me of the many problems afflicting those folk.

'It would seem that people are beginning to flee the land. Who will help them, when everyone is looking west to the Fords and to Helm's Deep?''Beware, traveller! We are trying to flee this land, and I hate to see unwary folk risk their lives by going in.

'You are here to help, are you? Well! That is a surprise unlooked-for!'The White Hand built a large and impressive fortification in the southern Stonedeans called Madh-fushaum. This is a staging area for attacks and it supports their efforts to conquer all of the Stonedeans.Madh-fushaum lies just to the south-east of Flodgeheld.

Wilberth has asked you to scout around the perimeter of the fortress of Madh-fushaum.Wilberth asked that you create a distraction while he is able to heal, and one way to do that would be to create turmoil in the fortress of Madh-fushaum.Wilberth is at Flodgeheld.

The White Hand in Madh-fushaum have been distracted by your efforts for some time, and you should now return to Wilberth.Talk to Wilberth'The White Hand has constructed a large fortification nearby from which they launch their attacks. We discovered it just before they razed Flodgeheld.

'I am unable to defend myself. If you come through here again, I will likely be dead...unless you could keep them distracted for a time.

'I would begin by scouting around the perimeter. From there, opportunities to cause turmoil should present themselves.''I could hear the explosions from here! That was masterfully done, my good ${RACE}. You really went above and beyond, and for that I thank you. My wounds have mended, and I will be making my way to Woodhurst soon.

'However, I did notice something concerning while you were gone.'Herubrand and his family valiantly fought to defend the mead hall. When they were almost overwhelmed, the advisors organized a hasty escape for Herubrand, but were not able to save most of his family.The mead hall of Woodhurst has become a scene of battle, like much of Rohan. Calin mentioned that there were members of Herubrand's family who did not return after the battle and are presumed dead.

