'The townsfolk must not know that the mead hall was attacked, or that Herubrand has remained hidden for his safety. Disorder might ensue if they knew that the mead hall -- the symbol of authority here -- has fallen.

'You should let Herubrand know what you have found.''Ah, so you are the ${CLASS} that I have heard about? What news might you have for me?

'Ah, I did not expect less, alas.

'You are kind, stranger. This was a grisly task, but I am glad that you performed it... and for that I thank you.'There are a few ballistae along the perimeter outside of Brockbridge. The enemy wheeled them outside of town and already they have caused much devastation.There are ballistae shooting at the towers and Brockbridge defenders. They must be destroyed.Destroy siege machines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your actions gave the defenders a brief rest from the threat of the siege machines.CompleteThere are ballistae shooting at the towers and Brockbridge defenders. They must be destroyed.Destroying the war-machines allows the towers to be manned without as much risk. The defenders of Brockbridge now have a better chance to hold back the siege.Geralht is a fierce warrior charged with training of new Dunlending recruits. He prepares them for the rigours of being a member of the White Hand army within Madh-fushaum.Geralht is taking his fresh Dunlending recruits on their first scouting mission along the eastern plains of the Stonedeans.Find GeralhtGeralht is taking his fresh Dunlending recruits on their first scouting mission along the eastern plains of the Stonedeans.Defeat GeralhtGeralht and his ragtag band of Dunlending recruits have been defeated.CompleteGeralht leads a ragtag group of Dunlendings from Madh-fushaum on their first scouting mission. They can normally be seen watching the road south-east of Brockbridge and roaming around the south-eastern plains.Defeating Geralht will impact the training of any new Dunlending recruits within Madh-fushaum, as he was an astute instructor in matters of war.A large wolf has become the biggest predator in the southern plains of the Stonedeans. Inras and his pack of wolves are almost rabid with hunger.The hungry wolf pack led by Inras is hunting in the southern plains of the Stonedeans.Find InrasThe hungry wolf pack led by Inras is hunting in the southern plains of the Stonedeans.Defeat InrasInras and his pack of wolves are defeated, and no longer hunt the southern plains of the Stonedeans.CompleteThe plains north-west of Edoras were rich with wildlife, but the arrival of the White Hand reduced the amount of food for the local predators. One such predator is now almost rabid with hunger. Inras and his pack of wolves hunt the plains and attack anything that moves.Inras, the biggest predator has been defeated and is likely to be replaced by another predator eventually. For now there is some semblance of peace in the land.Macsen leads an elite band of riders out of Madh-fushaum, and was trained in combat on a horse by the Uruk-hai of the White Hand.Macsen and his band of riders have set ablaze the farms in the southern Stonedeans, and keep watch on the road south-east of Brockbridge for trade or reinforcements.Find MacsenMacsen and his band of riders have set ablaze the farms in the southern Stonedeans, and keep watch the road south-east of Brockbridge for trade or reinforcements.Defeat MacsenMacsen and his elite band of riders are now defeated, and can no longer ravage the plains in the eastern Stonedeans.CompleteMacsen is the leader of an elite band of Dunlending riders that are quite formidable despite the Dunlendings not having much history as riders of horses. They would give all but the most skilled Rohirrim trouble in battle.With the mighty Macsen and his riders now defeated, it has left Madh-fushaum more susceptible to mounted attacks; though with the siege on Brockbridge, one may not come from the Rohirrim for some time.Neivion leads a strong band of Dunlending warriors that managed to cross a ford of the Swiftwater River to the north-east of Brockbridge.Neivion and his band are scouting the northern bank of the Swiftwater River after crossing a ford to the north-east of Brockbridge.Find NeivionNeivion and his band are scouting the northern bank of the Swiftwater River after crossing a ford to the north-east of Brockbridge.Defeat NeivionNeivion and his band are defeated and no longer a threat to either Brockbridge or Woodhurst.CompleteNeivion leads a raid party of elite Dunlending warriors who crossed the Swiftwater River into the northern Stonedeans. They crossed the shallows to the north and east of Brockbridge, and are now a threat to both Brockbridge and Woodhurst.You defeated the mighty Neivion and his band who will no longer threaten to surround Brockbridge, or to attack Woodhurst.Ognir, a troll who seems as old as the mountains nearby, has long hunted the beasts along the northern banks of the Swiftwater River.Ognir hunts the lands along the northern banks of the Swiftwater River to the north-east of Brockbridge.Find OgnirOgnir hunts the lands along the northern banks of the swiftwater river to the north-east of Brockbridge.Defeat OgnirOgnir has finally met his match and was hunted down and defeated by a mighty ${CLASS}.CompleteStories of Ognir have long been told to the children in the Stonedeans, of an ancient troll who lurks near the northern banks of the Swiftwater River. Those who hunt the lands of the Stonedeans have learned to avoid the area, or risk finding themselves hunted.The ancient troll Ognir has been defeated, and will now only lurk in the nightmares of the people of the Stonedeans.Rog-votak and his band are well-trained riders, and will soon aid the siege on Brockbridge. If they do, it would end the stalemate and be the doom of Brockbridge.Rog-votak leads a strong band of riders that are a part of the White Hand army within Madh-fushaum in the southern Stonedeans.Find Rog-votakRog-votak leads a strong band of riders that are a part of the White Hand army within Madh-fushaum in the southern Stonedeans.Defeat Rog-votakRog-votak and his band are no longer another threat posed by the army within Madh-fushaum.CompleteRog-votak and his band of Uruk-hai riders are within sight of Edoras and wait for the day they can burn it down. They ravage the land around Madh-fushaum and ensure no Rohirrim riders reach its gates.The mighty Rog-votak and his band are defeated, and they can no longer be a threat to end the siege in Brockbridge.The Mine Overseer appears to be taking advantage of your presence by having you perform additional tasks for him.The new shipment of pickaxes is near the Mine Overseer, near the bottom of Wid Isernore.

