The Mine Overseer instructed you to return to Gifemund.Talk to Gifemund'I have put together a list of tasks which I believe you can accomplish. Once they are completed, I will consider your obligation to me fulfilled and you will be free to return to Gifemund.

'The first task is simple. I received a shipment of new pickaxes, and the workers near the top of the mine are in need of replacements. Take these up to them and hurry back...we have much to get done.''That was an easy one, and you still managed to take too long. There is too much work to do!

'This next task will be a little more difficult. The workers have gathered a fair amount of ore down here, but it needs to be loaded into the carts. Three carts need to be loaded, so you will need to be quick about it!''You took long enough! I am glad that you are only temporary help, because you would not last in this mine a day more.

'This last task will be the most difficult, but perhaps you are up to the challenge...though I doubt it. Those scoundrels from lower Woodhurst keep damaging my track at night, and I think that they may have the stolen stakes that keep it in place. I need you to repair the track.''Very well, that is all I require of you. You are free to return to Gifemund. Good day to you, ${CLASS}.''You have proven your loyalty. The Overseer can be a true task-master, but you look none the worse for wear. 

'I am on the cusp of making my first step towards the seat of Woodhurst. Before I do, however, I think the time has come to obtain a different perspective...one might say a unique perspective. I believe she can help me ensure that my affairs are in order....'Isengard has moved some advanced siege-craft south to attack Helm's Deep. You should count the different types of siege-craft to learn more of the enemy.Siege-craft and war machines can be found in Shatorthum.

