Hopefully you can help the defenders of Helm's Deep with your knowledge of the enemy.Agelwyn has found herself in an uncomfortable position as acting Thane of Marton during a very troubled time, and she does not feel up to the responsibility.Agelwyn needs confidence to lead her people.

You should speak with Agelwyn and encourage her to be strong.Try to help Agelwyn be confident while her husband is awayAgelwyn is in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton.

You should speak with Agelwyn.Speak with Agelwyn'No, I have heard nothing of Erkenbrand, or Grimbold, or any of them! I care only for news of my husband Gladsúnu. We had a rider telling us the Fords of Isen had fallen, but no news of my husband and Thane.

'And not long after, the Orcs came, and we fled. Did I do right? Perhaps we should have fought! I am no leader. Please, do not ask me anything else! I do not know; I am distraught!''We are all going to rot here, without food or shelter! I have lost my husband's city.''You are right, ${PLAYER}. I am convinced that I must act a leader now, however uncomfortable the role may be.'

You assure Agelwyn that she will learn as she goes, and that she will have help as long as you can spare it.Bingo has not taken the departure of Willem Whisker very well, but he is trying to continue his journey.Bingo wants to travel to Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh. He will meet you inside the city, east of the centre of town.Talk to Bingo east of the town-centre of Galtrev, in Pren GwydhHumfrey Rumming is to the east of the town-centre of Galtrev, in Dunland.Talk to Humfrey Rumming in Galtrev, in DunlandHumfrey Rumming gave you a riddle to solve. It should point to the destination for which Haley Meadowsweet and Theodore Gorse were making.Haley Meadowsweet is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.Talk to Haley Meadowsweet in AvardinTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.Talk to Theodore Gorse in AvardinTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.Talk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin... againTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.Talk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin... againTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.Talk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin... againTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.Talk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin... againHaley Meadowsweet is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.Talk to Haley Meadowsweet in AvardinBingo is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.Talk to Bingo in Avardin, in Dunland'I suppose it is time to continue our journey. I have written some more pages about our time in Rohan, but I am finding it hard to write about Dunland. Do you think Willem Whisker is doing all right?

'Bah! I know I should not dwell on it, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot help it! There is a large settlement to the north-east. It is called Galtrev. Let us go there and see what there is to learn about Dunland. Perhaps if we learn more about it I will not miss Willem Whisker so keenly!''We should travel north-east to the settlement of Galtrev. It could be I will find something interesting there to write about.''Hello there, ${CLASS}! I was just talking about you.''Look who I have run into, ${PLAYER}... it's Humfrey Rumming!''This Humfrey does seem to be a curious fellow, doesn't he?''This is lucky fortune indeed, ${CLASS}! A short time ago, I encountered a pair of Treasure Seekers, a man and a woman, and the conversation was quite pleasant. Well, it turns out that these two knew about you, ${PLAYER}. I decided right then and there to give them quite a good deal on a number of treasure maps that had come into my possession.

'You would like to find this pair? Well, you are in luck, because I know where they were going! While we were conversing, they told me that you have quite a head for riddles. I find that hard to believe. A master lore-master such as myself cannot be bested at the riddle-game!

'I will write down their destination in riddle-form, and if you can solve it, you will find them there! Good luck, ${CLASS}. Confine your search to Dunland, and let us see if your good fortune holds!''Solve my riddle, and you will find your friends! They are somewhere in Dunland, but that is the only hint you will get from me!''Hello there, ${PLAYER}! It has been a long time, hasn't it?''Well hello, ${PLAYER}! I did not expect to see you in this place!''I suppose we solved the riddle, ${PLAYER}. But we were just here!''You have seen Haley and Theodore since we parted in the Lone-lands? Oh, that must have been while I was lost in Moria. That was such a long time ago, I had quite forgotten!''It has been a long time, ${PLAYER}! I am glad to see that you found Bingo! I knew he would turn up again.

'Our own journey has been fairly uneventful. I think Theodore may be less of a Treasure Seeker than when I took him on as a pupil, if you can believe it!

'He will want to tell you about our journey.''Theodore will go on for awhile, if you let him.''I have a complaint to lodge with you, ${PLAYER}! Do you remember that shiny necklace you tried to give me back in Eregion? Well, that was not a fake at all, as I thought it might have been at the time. No! It was a real artifact of the dwarves, and Haley has held onto it ever since we took your leave in Eregion.

'And ever since, ${PLAYER}, we have been beset with ill fortune! This southward journey has been a constant cavalcade of catastrophe! And it is all your fault! That shiny necklace, that Rothstone... it bears a curse of ill fortune!''Now you have done it, ${PLAYER}.''How do I know? I will tell you how I know. The weather has been terrible! As we made our way south through Eregion, the skies opened up and the downpour was torrential! You have never seen rain like this, ${PLAYER}. It was cold as ice, and each droplet hit the skin like hail!

'Thunder rolled across the sky, booming and crashing, and the wind threatened to pick you up and toss you against trees or stones! We were in that land for several days before you gave Haley the Rothstone, and I did not see any weather like that before. But afterwards? It was nearly constant, except for a few days when it was sunny and nice. But those days were the exception!

'Further proof: we had to pick our way across a stream when we entered Enedwaith, and I hurt my ankle sliding down the river-bed. It has only recently started feeling better.''I should have warned you about this.''And furthermore, you know I am a Treasure Seeker of some renown. Well, ever since you gave Haley the Rothstone, I have found nothing in the way of treasure at all! It is as if some secret force has cast a shroud over my sight, preventing me from finding even the least valuable trinket or bauble.

'Every ruin is picked clean. Every chest or strongbox is empty. There is no gold, there is no silver, there are no gems. The curse of the Rothstone has so damaged my fortunes that I cannot even hope to amass a fortune of any type!''I feel badly about this, ${PLAYER}.''You said you met Humfrey Rumming, and he sent you to find me and Haley? Did he tell you that he sold us a number of treasure maps? They cost me a pretty penny, I don't mind telling you, and so far every single one has come up empty! All my hopes rest on the only treasure map I have not yet tried, but those hopes have become as faint as a guttering candle in a drafty room!

'Bingo said that you were in Avardin earlier today, and yet Humfrey's riddle sent you right back here? That sounds like very bad luck as well, ${PLAYER}. I think you too may have become ensnared in the curse of the Rothstone!''He is nearly finished. I have grown able to tell.''We need to do something about the Rothstone, ${PLAYER}. This string of bad luck has become unbearable. We have had such a grievous journey south that I am ready to turn around and head back north! That is how terrible this adventure has become!

'Ask Haley! She will confirm everything I have said to you!''Our luck has turned sour! And it is all because of the Rothstone!''It rained once or twice. I haven't noticed that our luck has been any poorer than it ever was, ${PLAYER}.

'But if Theodore wants to turn around and head back north, I would not be opposed to travelling with you and Bingo for a spell, if you would have us as companions on your way.''Beware, my friends! The curse of the Rothstone will ensnare your fortunes as well!''We would be glad to journey with you and Bingo for a time.''The more the merrier, that's what I always say! Theodore and Haley will be more than welcome to journey with us as we head northward. It is about time we started that way, I would say. The Shire is still a long ways off, and it will be nice to have some company on the road.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Treasure Lost, Treasure Found' (Recommended Level: 93)</rgb>Agelwyn has decided upon her next course of action, and has asked for help in determining the best path for the refugees' escape towards Helm's Deep.The east road should be scouted by heading east and then south from the refugees' camp. The west road should be scouted by heading west through the woods. The river should be scouted by heading directly south-east.

Agelwyn has asked you to scout possible routes towards Helm's Deep: the road to the west, the road to the east, and the along the river banks.Scout towards the road to the westScout the road to the eastScout the river to the south-eastAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton.

You should return to Agelwyn.Return to Agelwyn with your report'Now that I know we are going to Helm's Deep, I would have your counsel, ${PLAYER}. Which way should we go? Is it safe to pass Marton? There are two roads coming from the north on either side of the town, but I would not usher my people down them if they are not safe. Maybe investigate the river, as well.

'Will you scout some possible routes for us to take? Please hurry -- I wish to begin our journey as soon as possible.''To the river, then! I mourn for our lands, and for the people who met their doom upon roads that should be safe for travel.

'I only pray that we do not share their fate....'The trolls here are resting before a final march to haul the siege-weapons to Helm's Gate and beyond. You should do your best to stall them by thinning their numbers.Trolls can be found in Shatorthum to the north-west of Marton.

You should defeat the trolls of Shatorthum.Defeat Shatorthum Pullers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of troll-pullers in Shatorthum, hopefully stalling the march of the siege-weapons towards Helm's Deep.CompletedThe trolls here are resting before a final march to haul the siege-weapons to Helm's Gate and beyond. You should do your best to stall them by thinning their numbers.You have defeated a number of troll-pullers in Shatorthum, hopefully stalling the march of the siege-weapons towards Helm's Deep.Bingo has almost reached the end of his journey.Bingo's hobbit-hole is in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.Travel to Bingo's hobbit-hole in Michel DelvingMyrtle Boggs stands outside Bingo's home, her arms crossed disapprovingly.Talk to Myrtle Boggs outside Bingo's home in Michel DelvingBingo is outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.Talk to Bingo outside his home in Michel DelvingThere is a notice pinned to the door of Bingo's hobbit-hole.Examine the notice pinned to Bingo's doorBingo is outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.Talk to Bingo outside his home in Michel DelvingDonnamira Took is the librarian in the library of Great Smials, located atop the hill in Tuckborough.

Bingo has amassed many overdue fees on the cookbook that began his journey, and he has asked you to settle his debt.Bingo is inside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.Talk to Bingo inside his hobbit-hole in Michel DelvingBoffin Manor has become filled with cobwebs during Bingo's long absence, and he asked you to help him tidy up.Bingo is inside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.Talk to Bingo inside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving'My journey is nearly over! It will not be long before we have arrived back at my doorstep in Michel Delving.

'I must confess to a certain reluctance on this last stage of our adventure, ${PLAYER}. Think of all those hills we did not climb, all those cross-roads where we took the left path and not the right! I will be glad to see my home again, do not doubt it! But as we get closer to the journey's end, I find myself already thinking about the next! It is a curious thing, truly!

'Let us continue to Michel Delving, my friend! I am ready to see the old place again!''Let us continue to Michel Delving, my friend! I am ready to see the old place again!''Hello there, Myrtle! How have the weeks treated you?''Myrtle does not seem happy about this. Poor thing!''Bingo Boffin! How many weeks has it been since any upstanding hobbit has seen you within the hedges or upon the lanes of the Shire? More than is proper, I'll warrant!

'You have no respect for your neighbours, Bingo! Did you give any thought to what WE might be going through during your ill-advised and improper jaunt to foreign lands? A neighbourhood needs neighbours, and you have been quite absent for many seasons! And the talk! The whispered rumours! It has cast this lane and its residents in a poor light, and all of our reputations have been sullied by our mere association with you!

'We expect this behaviour from one such as ${PLAYER}, but not from you, Bingo! You are no adventurer! Are you?''We expect this behaviour from one such as ${PLAYER}, but not from you, Bingo! You are no adventurer! Are you?''I am sorry that Myrtle was so upset by my absence from the neighbourhood... I did not know she cared so much for me! That is a surprise, to be honest. I will do my best to make up for it!

'But what is that pinned to my door, ${PLAYER}? It seems to be a notice of some kind. Can you see what it might be?''But what is that pinned to my door, ${PLAYER}? It seems to be a notice of some kind. Can you see what it might be?''Bingo's long absence from the Shire has put all of us in a disreputable light!''An overdue notice from the library of Tuckborough? My face is red, ${PLAYER}. I feel certain you told me to return that cookbook before my journey began, but I confess I never got around to it.

'Would you mind terribly taking that cookbook back to the librarian in the Great Smials for me? Here, bring the brigand treasure with you as well. That should serve to pay the overdue fee, several times over!

'In fact, I think we should donate that treasure for the upkeep and maintenance of the library. Some good should come of it! My only condition for that donation is that the library keep a copy of my book when it is finished!''Please settle my debt with the library, ${PLAYER}! That treasure should be more than enough, and I would be happy to donate the remainder for the continued maintenance of the library... if they will stock my book and lend it out to readers when it is finished!''You have returned, and with the missing cookbook! How unexpected and delightful! I had quite given up on seeing this book ever again, but I have always been so dedicated to the operation of this library that I was thinking of trying to recreate some of the recipes myself, from memory!

'It is a relief to learn that will not be necessary. There is still the matter of the fee, however. Has Bingo given you the money with which to settle his debt? I am glad to have the book returned, but overdue fees exist for a reason.'

You show her the brigand treasure and explain that Bingo would like to pay the fine with it, and to donate the remainder directly to the library.

'That will keep the library open for many years! Bingo is a charitable sort indeed! The two of you have my thanks, for with this money we will be able to continue the education of young hobbits in the Shire. A love of books will spread throughout the neighbourhood, and I hope it will do so throughout your own as well!''A love of books will spread throughout the neighbourhood, and I hope it will do so throughout your own as well!''Look at this place, ${PLAYER}! Hobbits like things tidy, and seeing my home in this state is quite troubling!

'Would you mind helping me clear away some of these cobwebs? Now that I am home, I must return to my normal routine of dusting the mantelpiece and sweeping in the corners every three days! And if I drag my feet at the chore, I will simply remind myself of how messy my home became while I was away on my journey, and the memory will speed my feather-duster and hasten my broom!''Look at this place! Hobbits like things tidy, and seeing my home in this state is quite troubling!'Ah, that is quite a lot better. Thank you!'

Bingo looks around at his home, and sighs.

'Does it feel larger to you than when we left? It feels that way to me: larger and more empty. It was loneliness that propelled me on my journey, and here I am at the end of it and I am still lonely! I know what I need, ${PLAYER}! I miss my new friends, and my old ones. I shall throw a dinner party! Allow me to write up some invitations, and you can deliver them for me!'

