You should speak with Gandalf.Speak with Gandalf'Erkenbrand, lead on! We will go to your encampment, for we must plan our next move at once.''Leave me be and let the enemy come. Just let them come! I will fall here with Prince Théodred.

'I should have been the one to die, not him, for I had nothing to live for.''If my aging king can bring himself from a warm hearth and soft chair, then I will not yet condemn Rohan as lost. I will fight for Théoden, as I have always done!

'Erkenbrand, Erkenbrand. We must find him, for he had good soldiers with him before we were split asunder. Erkenbrand! He cannot be far.'Grimbold has stopped short, his voice dropped to a whisper.

'Look out ahead. Do you see the size of that troll?

'We must try to take him down. I do not think we will die today, ${PLAYER}, however the odds may be against us. For Rohan!''You have found Grimbold, and Erkenbrand has found us! This is an unexpected turn of fortune indeed. 

'I am sorry that your reunion must be swift, but we cannot tarry here, my friends. It is to the Hornburg that we must look.'The day for Bingo's party has arrived... will any of the invited guests show up?Myrtle Boggs leads a small group of Bingo's neighbours on the path outside his hobbit-hole.Greet Bingo's neighbours outside his hobbit-holeMyrtle Boggs is outside Bingo's hobbit-hole. Is she coming to the party?Talk to Myrtle on the path outside Bingo's hobbit-holeMore guests are arriving for Bingo's party, and you should greet them and make them feel welcome.Greet the guests for Bingo's party as they arriveMore guests are arriving to Bingo's party every moment, but there is no guarantee they will all get along!More guests are arriving for Bingo's party!Greet the new arrivalsBert Bartleby has arrived outside Bingo's hobbit-hole, and he is ready to commence with the feasting!Talk to Bert Bartleby outside Bingo's hobbit-holeThe party is in full swing!Enter Bingo's home for the partyBingo's home is packed with many of the friends he made on his journey, and you should mingle with the guests before the bell is rung for dinner.Bingo is near the kitchen of his hobbit-hole. Now that you have done some mingling, you should see how your host is enjoying his party.Talk to Bingo in his home'I am ready for dinner, my friend! Let us join the guests and eat our fill!''Well, I suppose it would be rude not to attend Bingo's party, so here we are, ${PLAYER}. Do you think he has forgotten that business about the petition I began before he left on his adventure? I would appreciate it if you did not remind him about it.''Greetings to you, ${PLAYER}. I know I did not receive an invitation to Bingo's party... no, do not worry! I do not begrudge him that, nor did I expect one! I spoke with him only briefly, a long time ago, and was compelled by other duties at the time.

'I was recently in Rivendell at the behest of the Lady Galadriel, and while there I spoke with quite a fellow. Bilbo is his name, and it seems he is quite eager to read Bingo's book. He told me about this party and that he sadly would not be able to attend, and I told him I would go on his behalf and report back concerning Bingo's progress on the book.

'To that end I have prepared a large quantity of ink and have brought it with me as a gift for Bingo. May his quill never run dry!''${PLAYER}... I did not know where to go. I wandered for a long time, never knowing why the Rangers spared me, or why Bingo showed me kindness. My unguided steps took me north, not with any plan or design, but simply because that was where they carried me. Would they bring me to the Angmar where Avair dwelled, or to the Forochel that made Gun Ain? Where could I begin again, as Mercy?

'In Galtrev I found a parchment on the wind. It was an invitation to a dinner party, addressed to a man I never met, a man named Humfrey. He must have set it down, or lost it, and so it came to me. I did not know where else to go... but I had not forgotten Bingo's kindness, and will not. I wanted to tell him I was grateful for it, and my northward passage gained its destination.

'On the road I passed a number of men, former brigands all, who also spoke loudly of Bingo's deeds. It seems they will be farmers. I do not know if that will be my course, but perhaps I can find a path of my own once I have thanked Bingo for the good of his.''I am sad to report that none of my brothers will be able to make it to the party today, ${PLAYER}. They all have obligations in other lands, but I promised that Old Rattlepacks and I would represent the Bartleby family to the very best of our abilities!

'Now, where is our host? I am ready to have a plate or two of tasty victuals! Let us go inside!''Ah, I can remember such fine parties as this! It has been so long, and even longer than death, for things were not well enough for parties in Audaghaim. But when I was a mere lass, not more than eight or nine, I remember the excitement of a gathering of friends!

'How did I come to be here? Why, I found a curious attachment to that horseshoe you have been carrying around! Perhaps some small portion of its metal came once from Audaghaim, long ago, and it was combined with other metals during the years since? I cannot say... but as I am bound to the place of my curse, that is as good a reason as any I can fathom.

'I am delighted to see such a merry gathering once again, though I deserve it not. Still, I thank you for bringing me here, however unknowingly!''This girl has not stopped dancing since she arrived. She seems to delight in it, but I admit I do not understand why!''I did not expect so many people to come to my party! Surely I did not send out this many invitations!

'Willem even made the journey, and he brought his mate and his many cubs! Prisca's children seem quite taken with them... I must remind W.W. to count his cubs carefully when it is time for my lynx friends to return home!''Haley is incredible and remarkable, especially for one of the Big Folk! She is telling me all about her adventures. Did she really descend into the lair of a DRAGON... and emerge once again, AFTER waking it up?

'You were there too, ${PLAYER}? That certainly is something. I need to find a dragon of my own to best!''We certainly had quite an adventure, didn't we, ${PLAYER}? I do hope you will remind Bingo of our part in it, so he does not leave our contribution out of his account. He spent much of my portion water-logged and not knowing who he was, so he might not have as much to say about it.

'It has occurred to me that perhaps you should not remind him of my contribution, ${PLAYER}. I think that perhaps not all dwarves are meant to be written about!''There are many ferocious creatures in the woods of the Gloomglens, but as distant cousins ye must possess the same skills as we! Ye will be able to avoid their notice, Merrimac, and visit us straight away!

'Hello, ${PLAYER}! I have been telling these good folk that they should come visit us in Maur Tulhau and enjoy a traditional Welcoming Feast, as Bingo did!

'If they eat as much as Bingo, they may need to also enjoy the traditional week of recovery following such a Feast, but we would find a place for them! I hope they will come visit!''My sister is quite taken with this Merrimac fellow. I do not think he seems as happy about this fact as she!''I have not been able to get a word in edge-wise! I do not remember agreeing to leave the Shire, but Violed seems to think I did!

'What has this party gotten me into, ${PLAYER}?''When you and Bingo came to Newbury to visit, you beheld me at my lowest point, ${PLAYER}! But after a year of courting, Celandine Brandybuck finally agreed to attend a social gathering with me! All I needed was a party to attend with her!

'And so when my mother said that Bingo, my first cousin, once removed, was hosting a dinner party... well, it seemed like providence most fortuitous!

'But alas! She is spending the whole time fawning over these lynx cubs, and sparing not a moment for me! Cruel fortune!''Ooooh, look how cute they are! And their fur seems so soft! I love them all!''I thought this was a dinner party? Why is it taking so long to get dinner on the table?

'The rumbling in my belly will drown out all the conversation if we don't eat soon!''This is a nice table. I don't see any scuff-marks upon it at all. And yet, judging from Bingo's dancing upon the tables of the Prancing Pony, he must have gotten some practice in the art from somewhere!''This has been quite an adventure, ${PLAYER}. I do not know what Haley and I will do from here on out, but I do not doubt that it will be an experience full of danger and excitement!

'Do not tell her I said this, but I do think that without her by my side, I might have gotten in over my head a time or two on this adventure. Nothing I wouldn't be able to solve by myself, of course! You were a help too, from time to time, once or twice. What I am trying to say is that even an experienced adventurer like Theodore Gorse needs friends from time to time!'

Theodore coughs with embarrassment, and his usual bluster returns.

'Now then! Enough of the sugary platitudes! My past is magnificent! My present is satisfactory! I defy you to disappoint me, future!''I must ask Theodore where he got his hat. I would like to add it to my collection!''Is this map accurate? There certainly are a lot of villages in the Shire. I respect their burrows, and a hobbit-hole seems to be a very tidy place to live, but I could do with a little more in the way of large, echoing chambers. And not a great hall in sight!'

Ketill sighs.

'How do hobbits live like this, ${PLAYER}?''I like this hobbit lass! She is most attentive, and reminds me somewhat of myself when I was that age.'

Haley suddenly turns bright red.

'Oh, I am so sorry. Hobbits age differently than my folk, don't they? Marigold is indeed a child? Still, I am sorry to have spoken so thoughtlessly. Spending so much time around Theodore may have brought me down to his careless level! What a frightening thought!''It is good to sit down for a moment. All of my children are occupied for now, and I can have a moment to myself!

'I should tell cousin Bingo to host these parties more often!''Bingo's manuscript is very good so far, ${PLAYER}, but I do wish he showed a little more proficiency with spelling and grammar. This book will need some refinement before I am comfortable placing it on a library shelf!''Bingo has amassed quite a collection of books! I am impressed with his scholarly dedication, and I wonder what the great collections of my people are missing for their lack of hobbit literature?

'It was very nice of Bilbo Baggins to give me his invitation when I visited Imladris!''It is nearly time for dinner, ${PLAYER}, but there is still a small matter to which I'd like to attend. It will not take long.

'Do you have a moment?'Herubrand has brought you to Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.Herubrand is inside Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.Talk to Herubrand inside Orlag DenHildegard is inside the cave of Orlag Den, where she makes her home.Talk to Hildegard in Orlag DenHildegard has asked you what adventuring discipline you follow.Answer Hildegard's questions, and hear what she has to sayHorn has made his disbelief of Hildegard most plain.Answer Hildegard's questions, and hear what she has to sayHildegard has asked to speak with Nona.Listen to the words of HildegardHorn is in Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.Talk to Horn in Orlag DenListen to Horn's confrontation with Hildegard in Orlag Den.Listen to Horn and Hildegard's confrontationNona is in Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.Talk to Nona in Orlag DenHildegard stares sightlessly forward.Hildegard stands, unblinking, but does not appear to see you any longerHildegard stands, unblinking, but does not appear to see you or Nona any longer.Talk to Hildegard in Orlag Den'${PLAYER}, what can we do? If Hildegard speaks the truth, it means Horn will fall in battle. A good death for any warrior, but he is not just any warrior, ${PLAYER}. He is mine, and it is not glory he seeks. I know this to be true!

'I will keep Horn from meeting this end. Others have fought their fates. Why not Nona, daughter of Suvulch, sister of Wadu? You will help me in this, ${PLAYER}. You will say none of this to Horn. Do you understand?''We have arrived, ${PLAYER}. Hildegard has sight of many things still to come, and the source of her power is unknown to me. Many of my kinsmen call it witchcraft, sorcery such as that practiced by the Elves, but I say Hildegard was a woman of Rohan, and remains so.

'Speak to her with courtesy.'You give Hildegard your name and she nods.

'It is a pleasure to meet you, friend of Herubrand. Many are the roads you have walked to get here, and many more you will walk before you are at last given rest.'Hildegard looks at you curiously. Her face is a quiet mask, and you cannot tell what hides behind her calm expression.Hildegard looks at you curiously. Her face is a quiet mask, and you cannot tell what hides behind her calm expression.'This woman speaks in riddles and rubbish, ${PLAYER}. If she has knowledge of days to come, why does she not spell it for us plain? Were she to do that perhaps I would give her my belief, but until then I remain unconvinced.''I cannot believe Horn would act this way, ${PLAYER}! Has he closed his eyes to everything we have experienced on this journey? He shares the maddening outlook of his people! Suvulch will not understand him.'

Nona clenches her fists and tosses her hair in frustration.

'We cannot choose to whom we give our hearts, ${PLAYER}. That is our lot, but I might have chosen one less stubborn, from out of all the kingdoms of Men!'The soothsayer Hildegard stands upright, staring forward sightlessly. She still breathes, but she no longer appears to see either you or Nona.The long road north has been blockaded by unsavoury sorts, but Bingo will need to pass them by if he is to reach the end of his journey.Haley is on the road north through Enedwaith, and she has some words for you before you continue.Talk to Haley on the road through EnedwaithBingo is on the road through Enedwaith, preparing to deal with the Orc blockade.Talk to Bingo on the road through Enedwaith<rgb=#FF0000>Bingo must not be defeated!</rgb>The brigand leader has motioned for you to speak to him.Talk to Bloody Graham, the brigand leaderThe brigands will not let you pass, and must be slain.Kill all the brigandsBingo has something to say to the brigands.Let Bingo have his say, but remain alertOne of the former brigands has motioned for you to speak with him.Talk to William at the blockadeWilliam told you that some of the plunder was left behind by the Orcs, and he wants Bingo to have it.Examine the treasure coffer William wants to give BingoBingo is at the blockade in northern Enedwaith.Talk to Bingo at the blockade'This road leads north for many miles. Haley tells me that it will bring us to the Bree-land!''I do not like the sound of this Orc blockade, ${PLAYER}. It is one thing to squish bugs in a dragon's lair, but quite another to fight creatures such as Orcs! I do not think I am prepared for this.

'I will do as Haley suggests, and let you do all the fighting!''I suppose you fancy yourselves adventurers? Well, you'll have to give us what we want or you'll find yourselves on the wrong side of our blades!'

You silently appraise the band of brigands, taking in their mismatched clothes and the poor quality of their weapons. These men are very inexperienced, more likely to wield shovels and ploughs than knives and swords. They are new to banditry, and if it does come to combat, you know something else: all of these men will be dead before Bingo has uncovered his eyes.'William wants me to have the treasure? Well, I suppose we can bring it with us. I did not do anything to deserve it, but its rightful owners are probably not going to come looking for it. The Orcs that collected it in the first place likely saw to that.

'I am glad it did not come to bloodshed today, ${PLAYER}. I took one look at the brigands and knew they were no match for any of us. They needed words more than they needed to suffer for their poor decision to accost us.

'I am ready to continue our homeward journey!''When Theodore and I passed this way on our southward journey, there was a great massing of Orcs and half-orcs in the ruins just ahead. We were able to slip by unnoticed, but I do not think we will be as fortunate this time.

'If it does come to fighting, you should try and protect Bingo from the swords and arrows of the Orcs. I will have my hands full trying to keep them from felling Theodore with a lucky stroke!

'Perhaps we can skirt the ruins if their numbers have increased. We will not know until we get closer.''I want to thank you for letting your friend talk some sense into Graham. I wasn't certain this endeavour was going to work, and when we saw your group approaching on the road, I became convinced that we were all about to die. Our career as brigands was short-lived, but better that than our own lives be short.

'The Orcs had abandoned this blockade by the time we arrived. Graham thinks something must have drawn them away, and in a hurry too. Whatever the reason, they left some plunder behind. I want you to give it to Bingo, as a gift from those whose lives he saved today!

'Farewell! It will be farming for the rest of us from now on, as it should always have been.'Bingo has entered the lair of the mighty Draigoch in order to rescue Theodore Gorse... if it is not already too late!Bingo is inside the entrance to Draigoch's Lair, hoping to rescue Theodore Gorse before it is too late!Talk to Bingo in Draigoch's lairHaley has followed you to a ledge overlooking the sleeping dragon.Talk to Haley in Draigoch's lairTheodore is on the floor of Draigoch's lair, and you need to climb down to reach him.Climb down the rope to reach the floor of Draigoch's lairBingo is on the floor of Draigoch's lair, and he wants to talk to you about something urgent.Talk to Bingo on the floor of Draigoch's lairYou have found Theodore in Draigoch's lair!Sneak by the sleeping dragon with BingoYou have found Theodore in the depths of Draigoch's lair.Talk to Theodore in Draigoch's lairThe dragon stirs awake!Leave the lair with Theodore, Haley, and BingoThe dragon is awake! You must make it to the rope before the lair fills with fire!Run to the rope and escape from Draigoch's lair<rgb=#FF0000>Escape before the lair fills with fire</rgb>You have escaped from the dragon's lair... but just in time!Talk to Theodore outside Draigoch's Lair'Is that a village down there, across the plain? Let us head for it at once, and leave this dragon behind us!''Oh dear... look at this poor fellow! This is not a safe place at all, ${PLAYER}. It seems burglars have come in here from time to time, and any that did not fall prey to the dragon's fire may have met their ends at the hands of those they brought with them! When treasure is involved, good friends can become enemies over the distribution of even a single coin.

'But it is the dragon we should worry about for now!''I could not wait any longer, ${PLAYER}, and it is a good thing I followed when I did, for you seem to have no way of descending from this ledge to the floor of the lair. How can you rescue Theodore if you cannot get down to him?

'Well, I have a coil of rope. I will tie it to a rock up here, and we can descend to the floor of the lair to save Theodore! We will have to be very, very quiet, so use caution!

'Now let me tie this rope!'Bingo's voice is little more than a whisper.

'Walk with care, ${PLAYER}. We do not want to wake this dragon.'Theodore does his best to whisper.

'The Rothstone will be safe here, ${PLAYER}. May it give this dragon all the misfortune it can produce, and leave me and Haley alone!

'It is a funny thing, but I look around at all this treasure and I find that I don't desire even the smallest portion of it. Perhaps I am done being a Treasure Seeker after all. You did not need to come in after me, but I am touched all the same. I surrendered one treasure, but I found another treasure all the same: what good friends I have!

'We should make for the exit before this creature wakes, though. I know when I wake in the morning the first thing I want to have is a snack!''Well, that was close! Still, everything turned out all right, did it not? And I am glad to be rid of the Rothstone!

'So what shall we do next, my adventurous friends? Theodore Gorse is ready for anything!'The White Hand have conquered Woodhurst and are now openly marching in the streets. You must aid Herubrand, Gifemund, and Nothmar in reclaiming the city.Speak with Gifemund ahead of you.

The time has come to re-capture the fountain area, but you will need Gifemund's aid.Speak with GifemundDefeat the enemy who hold the fountain area in Woodhurst.Capture the fountain area<rgb=#FF0000>Manna must survive</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Scurfa must survive</rgb>Herubrand has arrived at the fountain.

Herubrand wishes to speak with you about the plan to retake the mead hall.Speak with HerubrandThe enemy has heavily guarded the pathway up to the mead hall, and appear to be guarding the front door.Defeat the enemy outside the mead hallHerubrand is standing outside the mead hall door.

Herubrand wishes to speak with you after defeating Arnwi.Speak with HerubrandEnter the mead hall with the others.

The battle for Woodhurst has progressed into the mead hall.Follow the others into the mead hallHerubrand is within the door of the mead hall.

Herubrand wishes to give directions on how the group will approach the coming battle.Speak with HerubrandDefeat the enemy throughout the mead hall and make your way to the throne.Make your way to the throneHerubrand waits to speak with you before approaching those waiting for you at the throne of the mead hall.Speak with HerubrandThurferth, a White Hand Emissary and a Dunlending named Cadwalader are standing in front of the throne.

Those who organized the fall of Woodhurst now boldly claim ownership of the city.Defeat Thurferth and the enemy at the throneHerubrand is near the throne in the mead hall.

Herubrand would like to thank you for your part in aiding their victory.Speak with Herubrand'If any enemy still remain in the city they will be routed out. With their leaders defeated there will no longer be organized resistance. The city is finally ours again.''We have a fight ahead of us. Herubrand and Nothmar said they would meet us at the fountain. We should capture and hold the fountain area while they make their way to us.''This is only the beginning. We need to make our way to the mead hall door. Nothmar's men will stay with Manna and Scurfa, and will hold the fountain area behind us.''Arnwi's fate was sealed when he killed Calin, and turned on all of us with the White Hand.

'They are likely prepared for us inside. We need to be careful. The time to end this is now.''You and I will take the right side. Gifemund and Nothmar should be able to handle the left. Keep your eye on them and help if they need it, but you should stick with me.

'We will make quick work of the defilers of our great hall.''We are victorious! ${PLAYER}, I cannot thank you enough for your aid in reclaiming Woodhurst from the cruel grip of the White Hand. We could not have claimed victory today without you.

'Gifemund and I have much to discuss about the future of Woodhurst. There is time for that. Today, we celebrate our victory.''Thurferth, that vile traitor! He helped them take the city...

'Weapons ready! For glory!'Calin is nervous about an unusual invitation for a drink with Arnwi, who has been out of touch for some time. Calin may be overly cautious, but a lot has happened lately to put him on edge.Accompany Calin to the nearby tavern, where he has arranged to have a drink and catch up with Arnwi.Speak with CalinHerubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse.

He needs to know what has occurred in the tavern.Speak with Herubrand'Calin proved his loyalty, and has not left my side. At first, I thought he stayed close to keep his eye on me, but I have found he is simply dedicated to me. He is a good man, and I see why my father liked him.

'Calin came to me a few minutes ago looking nervous. Arnwi invited Calin for a drink at the nearby tavern, which seems harmless, but Calin wouldn't be worried for nothing. Please accompany Calin to help calm his nerves.''Thank you for agreeing to come with me. I believe Arnwi simply wants to catch up after being out of touch for some time, but something just did not seem right. I feel more comfortable having you come with me.

'We will leave as soon as you are ready to depart.''That rotten traitor! Why would Arnwi do such a thing? I wonder if he has been working against me this entire time. He coordinated that attack, and showed that he is working with the Dunlending ruffians.

'I am a fool for not seeing it earlier. The Dunlendings have been the source of trouble brewing here. Was I blinded by my mixed heritage, and my view of them being brothers?'The farmlands of Marton burn, torched by the marauding Orcs that conquered the town.The well stands in the farmlands, and the fires burn rampant in the fields at the farms surrounding Marton (to the east, south-west, and north-west).

