This is more than can be said of other towns you've encountered.CompletedIt is possible that some people did not escape Marton after the recent Orc assault, and might need rescue.

You should search for hidden places where townsfolk might be trapped.'Thane Gladsúnu, you have come for me at last!

'You -- you are not Gladsúnu! Did he send you? Where are the others? Are they safe?'

You have not the time or the knowledge to satisfy all of this farmer's questions, but you urge her to run quickly to a safe place, away from this dangerous town.

'Right you are, stranger! Thank you for helping me.''You are not an Orc! Nor are you my Thane, who fought at the Fords and has not been heard from. Does this mean that Gladsúnu is dead, and cannot take back our town? I was waiting for him.'

You tell the farmer that it would be wise to flee, for the town is certainly far from secure.

'Thank you -- I will do so. There is a cave of sorts to the north where we go in case of danger.''Thank you for coming! I could not get out. I had hoped our Thane would set these Orcs straight, but the enemy is many, and our warriors are still at the Fords of Isen.

'It grieves me that Gladsúnu will come back to this! Would that we could have saved Marton.''I was asleep when the attack happened, and now I am trapped! That is, until you came to rescue me. Are we taking back the town now?'

You inform the man that the town is not safe, and that there are no Rohirrim soldiers in sight. He looks crestfallen.

