<rgb=#FF0000>Thank you for playing through The Ballad of Bingo Boffin!</rgb>Apparently much hope lies heavily on Erkenbrand and the lords of the Westfold -- Grimbold, Elfhelm, and Dúnhere. The Hornburg needs strong arms to defend it, but Gandalf may need help finding Erkenbrand.Éomer is at Helm's Gate.

You should speak with Éomer.Ask Éomer how you can help the WestfoldAragorn is at Helm's Gate.

You should speak with Aragorn.Ask Aragorn how you can help the WestfoldThéoden is at Helm's Gate.

You should speak with Théoden.Take leave of King Théoden'If you wish to know about the state of things in Westfold, I am glad to tell you all that I know.

'Erkenbrand, the lord of Helm's Deep, took command of the ford after Prince Théodred fell. Elfhelm was with him, and Grimbold too -- Grimbold is the Thane of Grimslade, a town to the east.

'I do not know what happened at the Fords of Isen, but I do know that all of Westfold braces for war and awaits news of the scattered lords, for enemies of Isengard now roam free. They march here even now as we speak.

'If Erkenbrand and the others can get here, we have a chance to survive. If they do not....' Gamling trails off.'It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''If you wish to help the Westfold and Rohan, think to helping yourself. Seek shelter in the Hornburg, and defend it with us! Help us ready for battle.

'If reports hold true, it is folly to roam the plains right now. Yes, we need Erkenbrand...but can he get here in time, if he even lives?'

You thank Éomer for his advice, but you wonder what Gandalf would have you do.'It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''I cannot advise you easily, ${PLAYER}. I truly worry that those of us who ride on to the Hornburg will not live to see the morning -- but I believe that crossing the plains of the Westfold before Saruman's army will mean certain death.

'Yet the hope lies in Gandalf. For myself, I will stay and defend Théoden and Rohan with my life, for Rohan has ever been an ally to my people.

'I hope that Gandalf can find Erkenbrand in time.''It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''It is nearly time for us to retreat within....''So you have decided to part ways here, ${PLAYER}? I pray for your safe return, and I hope that there is still time to draw swords with you at the Hornburg.

'Good luck with your search for Erkenbrand. Be careful -- the Westfold is not what it once was. The enemy has claimed this land.

'The battle at the Hornburg will decide the fate of Rohan....'King Théoden indicated upon leaving Edoras that he would ride to the Fords of Isen. You should ride to the road in the Westfold and meet the king's company and search for Gandalf.King Théoden, along with Éomer, Aragorn, Legolas, and Gimli, have begun a journey towards the Fords of Isen.

You should meet the king and his company upon the east-to-west road in the Westfold to lend them aid at the brink of war.Search the road in the Westfold for signs of Théoden's companyYou have spotted a gathering of people on the road in the centre of the Westfold.

You should speak with someone in this company to get word of Gandalf or King Théoden.Speak with someone in the small company on the roadYou have spotted a gathering of people on the road in the centre of the Westfold.

You should ask the refugees if they need assistance.Ask the refugees if they need any assistanceHelm's Deep is in the valley in the south-western corner of the Westfold.

You should ride with all speed to the gate of the stronghold of Helm's Deep.Search for Théoden at Helm's Dike'King Théoden has ridden to Helm's Deep in a great change of plan -- but I have not time to explain.

'I must search for Erkenbrand, Grimbold, Elfhelm, and their company, for they are missing since the Fords fell to the enemy. Ride along the road and find the king, ${PLAYER}. Help him if he needs help, and then help me find the lords of the Westfold.''A stranger on the road at such a time? How can this be? You had best go back to where you came from. This is no place to be wandering.

'We make for Helm's Deep, the last great stronghold in the Westfold; the Fords of Isen are lost. Have you not heard? Erkenbrand is gone, as are Grimbold and Elfhelm! Our last hope is at the mighty Hornburg.'

If the people of the Westfold make for Helm's Deep, then perhaps Théoden's company did as well...for you do not see any sign of them upon the road.'Hello there, fellow traveller! You look to be in quite a rush, and I do not blame you.''Hail, friend.''Hail, friend.''Hail, friend.''Hail, friend.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! I did not expect to see you here on the eve of the greatest assault Rohan has ever endured. I am glad you are here to aid us, and not trapped beyond the gate when it locks behind us.

'I trust the rest of my realm does not fare so badly as the Westfold, with doughty warriors such as yourself to defend it. Tell me: what news of the Westemnet?'You ask the man if he or his fellows need any assistance.

'I thank you, stranger, but no. We hope to reach the Hornburg by nightfall. The enemy will not dare to strike us there!

