You should discover the source of the felled trees.Discover the source of the felled treesYou have discovered a large encampment of trolls, too close to Marton for your comfort. This path is certainly not safe for the refugees.CompletedSomething on the western side of Marton has been felling trees north-west of town. This does not bode well for the western route to Helm's Deep.You have discovered a large encampment of trolls, too close to Marton for your comfort. This path is certainly not safe for the refugees.You reunited with Bingo and Tanglemane, but the frightening experience has left the hobbit with a pang in his stomach and a desire for the foods of his home.Egwylf has decided that the time has come to report the result of her errand seeking the Blood Eye cultists to Erkenbrand.Talk to Egwylf before the wall of Helm's DeepBingo is outside the great wall of the fortress at Helm's Deep.Talk to Bingo before the wall of Helm's DeepBingo wants to journey to the village of Marton, north-east of Helm's Deep in the Westfold, in order to look for some food to quiet his grumbling stomach.Talk to Bingo at the town of Marton, in the WestfoldBingo has been devastated by the evidence of the destruction of Marton, and wants you to search the ruined town for any survivors that might be trapped within the rubble. He also wants you to defeat any enemies that threaten the Westfold.Defeat any enemies that threaten the Westfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search burned debris in Marton (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bingo is on the road that runs through the ruined town of Marton, in the Westfold.Talk to Bingo outside Marton, in the WestfoldBingo found a woman wandering among the ruins of Marton, in the Westfold. He asked you to tell her that you would bring her to safety in the town of Grimslade.Bingo is in the centre of the town of Grimslade, in the Westfold.Bingo wants to meet you inside the Grimslade Mead Hall, located atop the hill in the centre of Grimslade.Talk to Bingo inside the Grimslade Mead Hall'I am mostly recovered from that frightening experience, ${PLAYER}, but if I am being honest with you I must confess something: I am very hungry! I am craving food... any food at all! Pies, cheeses, breads, delicious beer, roasted meats... anything will do! Tanglemane had his fill of these apples, but that does not do me any good!

'I have spoken with Egwylf, and it seems that she wishes to take her leave of us. We will accompany her to her destination and be on our way!'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Egwylf's destination when you accept this quest.</rgb>'Egwylf has decided that she must leave us. It is a pity, but she does have a duty to her kingdom. I do not blame her for it!''That is quite a fortress! Do you see it, ${PLAYER}?''It was a pleasant ride from Gapholt, ${PLAYER}, and I was pleased to have your company. I know that Bingo will be quite safe with you to watch over him, and the lynx and the pony seem to be quite effective guardians as well!

'But I cannot travel with you forever. My duty is to Rohan, and I must tell Erkenbrand what I learned about the Blood Eye cultists on my journey. This is his fortress, and if any place must be made ready in time of war, the Deep is best suited for it.

'Go with my good wishes, my friends! Beware of Orcs in the Westfold!''That is the great fortress where Erkenbrand dwells. I will report to him what I have learned of the Blood Eye cultists.''It is always sad to bid farewell to companions on the road, but Egwylf has her duty and I would not keep her from it! She will be fine. Look at that impressive wall!

'We should do something about my grumbling stomach, ${PLAYER}! I would not ask any of these men for a meal, because men stocking a fortress must carefully ration their food in time of war, or so I have read in books. But let us follow the road to the north-east and see about getting some supper at the first village we come across. I overheard some men speaking of a town called Marton. Let us look there for some means of curbing our appetites!''Let us follow the road to the north-east and see about getting some supper at the first village we come across. I overheard some men speaking of a town called Marton. Let us look there for some means of curbing our appetites!''Oh no...'

Bingo looks on the ruin of Marton in despair, and all the good cheer drains from his face.

'I am not hungry any more, ${PLAYER}. War has already come to the Westfold, and the good people who dwelt in this town have suffered so much!

'We must do something! There could be survivors trapped among the rubble! There could be Orcs and Wargs still hunting down the people that remain behind! We have to help anyone that remains in Marton! This is no pleasant stroll, ${PLAYER}... this is serious!''We must do something! There could be survivors trapped among the rubble! There could be Orcs and Wargs still hunting down the people that remain behind! We have to help anyone that remains in Marton! This is no pleasant stroll, ${PLAYER}... this is serious!''I found this woman among the ruins! She seems to be in shock, and I have been trying to cheer her up as much as I can. I think she lived in this town before it was attacked, but now she will need a new place to stay. I think we should bring her to the town of Grimslade, to the south-east. If there is still safety to be found in the Westfold, it will be there... at least according to the men with whom I spoke at Helm's Deep!

'Please tell her that we will bring her safely to Grimslade. I know that she has gone through a lot, but we cannot leave her here among these dangers, and she in such a state!''Please tell her that we will bring her safely to Grimslade. I know that she has gone through a lot, but we cannot leave her here among these dangers, and she in such a state!'The woman looks up at you with tear-stained eyes, and in a single look you know that she has never lived anywhere but Marton. With soft words, you tell her that she will not be safe here, and ask that she come with you and Bingo to Grimslade, to the south-east.

'My home...' she says sadly.Bingo has never met this woman before, but your path has crossed with hers more than once. Her expression is dazed, and Mercy looks now at the destruction Saruman's armies caused in Marton with pain etched across her face.

'I did not know where to go,' she says to you, and nothing more. You tell her that she may be able to find safety and a home of her own in the town of Grimslade, if she is willing to go.'Please tell her that we will bring her safely to Grimslade. I know that she has gone through a lot, but we cannot leave her here among these dangers, and she in such a state!

'The men at Helm's Deep told me that Grimslade is still peaceful enough, for now. It is to the south-east, in the Westfold. Let us go there, and quickly! This woman should not stay too near this unhappy scene.''We have made it safely to Grimslade. I do hope that our friend will be able to make a new life for herself here.'

The woman smiles at you and Bingo sadly. The scars of lost Marton will always remain, but her expression shows a resolve to rebuild and recover from the experience.

'This was quite enough for one day,' Bingo continues. 'We have been invited to take our supper in the Grimslade Mead Hall, atop the hill. I will meet you inside, ${PLAYER}!''I do not know when it happened, ${PLAYER}, but somewhere between Marton and here, Mercy gave us the slip!

'I don't understand why she would not want to make a home for herself among the people here in Grimslade. She could have been perfectly happy here in Rohan, couldn't she? We did what we could, I suppose. I hope she will be all right out there in the wild.

'At any rate, we have been invited to rest our feet and take some supper at the Grimslade Mead Hall, atop the hill. I will meet you inside!''I will meet you inside the Mead Hall.''I do not know why Mercy did not want to try and make a new home in Grimslade. I cannot understand it!

'No sense puzzling over it, I suppose. I will meet you inside the Mead Hall, ${PLAYER}!''This has been a long day, ${PLAYER}. So much of my journey has been pleasant, full of sunny days and good company, but the sight of Marton burning has... well, it has left me quite upset, and I am not sure what to do next. It is not just me, either. Even Willem seems to be rather down in the dumps.

'I am worried about the Shire. Is it time to return home? Oh, I do not know what to do!  Thoughts of home can be comforting, but these thoughts of the Shire have me turned around and upside-down, and now I say to you quite honestly that I do not know which way is up!'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Willem Whisker and the Wide World' (Recommended Level: 93)</rgb>Bingo is ready to leave Maur Tulhau and continue his journey northward.Bingo is saying his farewells to the hobbits of Maur Tulhau, and said he would meet you at the southern exit of the village.Talk to Rhus Cornchúthur at the entrance to Maur TulhauTalk to Iola Isbrun at the entrance to Maur TulhauBingo is at the entrance to Maur Tulhau, in the Gloomglens.

Bingo has said his good-byes and is now ready to continue his northern journey.Talk to Bingo at the entrance to Maur TulhauBingo is at the entrance to Maur Tulhau, in the Gloomglens.

Bingo has said his good-byes and is now ready to continue his northern journey.Talk to Bingo at the entrance to Maur Tulhau and continue the journey northBingo has passed through the blockade and is now in the Andrath, in the southern reaches of Bree-land.Talk to Bingo in the AndrathHaley Meadowsweet and Theodore Gorse are now in the Andrath, in the southern reaches of Bree-land.Talk to Theodore Gorse in the AndrathTalk to Haley Meadowsweet in the AndrathBingo is now in the Andrath, in the southern reaches of Bree-land.Talk to Bingo in the Andrath'Are you ready to leave Maur Tulhau? I will say my good-byes to the good folk of this village and meet you at the southern path out of the village, ${PLAYER}.''I will say my good-byes to the good folk of this village and meet you at the southern path out of the village, ${PLAYER}.''I am very pleased to have met you both, and to have seen your lovely village! Hobbits far from the Shire, and far from Bree? What a wonder!''I suppose ye are no duvodiad after all. Travel with care on the roads that lead from the Gloomglens. Return with Bingo someday and ye will have a friendly greeting from Rhus, to be sure!''We do not roam far afield from Maur Tulhau, but from time to time one of our folk will get an unusual yearning for travel and bring us news from distant lands. That is why I want to warn ye about the road north.

'Orcs, half-orcs and other fouler sorts have made camp that way, and they allow none to pass. There may be fighting if ye try to follow the road. Take care of Bingo! Ye do not need me to say that, I know it. But do it just the same, ${PLAYER}!''Orcs, half-orcs, and other fouler sorts have made camp on the northern road, and they allow none to pass. There may be fighting if ye try to follow the road. Take care of Bingo! Ye do not need me to say that, I know it. But do it just the same, ${PLAYER}!''Orcs on the northern road? It is good of Iola to warn us about such things, but we cannot let the fear of them keep us from continuing our journey!

'Let me know when you are ready to leave, and we will set our feet once more upon the road.''I am ready to go if you are, ${PLAYER}.''We are nearly home again!''We really should be getting back.''We have come a long way, ${PLAYER}, and the tree-lined paths of Bree-land seem quite welcoming in comparison to some of the lands through which we have travelled! Do you remember when we began? Bree seemed so distant and exotic, but now it appears friendly and quaint to my eyes!

'This is a joyful return, but my heart is not gladdened by everything today, for Haley and Theodore have decided to take their leave of us now that we have come back to the north-lands!''I will miss these two, ${PLAYER}!''It has been quite an enjoyable journey, my friends, but there are even greater adventures that demand my attention! I may be retired from the Treasure Seeking game, and I think I have had my fill of dragons, but there are surely other adventures out there, just waiting to be had!

'I bid you and Bingo a fond farewell! If you ever have need of a journeying companion in the future, look to the most dangerous spot... for that is where you will find me!''Good-bye, friends. I will see you again, if Theodore doesn't get me eaten by a dragon first. Now that I think about it, too much more of Theodore's stupidity may make that seem a mercy.

'Let me know if you find any hungry dragons in your future travels, ${PLAYER}. Just in case.''I am sad to see them go, ${PLAYER}, but I suppose every journey has to come to an end sometime. The end of my own journey approaches!'

<rgb=#00FF00>Bert Bartleby has come to the Andrath, in Bree-land.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Bingo Returns Home' (Recommended Level: 93)</rgb>You should seek Gandalf in the Westfold.You believe that Gandalf can be found in the centre of the Westfold, perhaps on the road.

You should seek Gandalf.Find Gandalf in the Westfold'You have helped a great deal, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you for it! I believe all will be well now. Surely there are others you might help!'

Your thoughts travel to Gandalf, and your heart pulls you towards the Westfold -- the westernmost area of the Westemnet, the gate that holds the enemy at bay. You should hasten to that land at once.'How did you know I would be here, ${PLAYER}? It is no matter -- there is no time! I will thank providence for this happy coincidence, and leave it at that.

'Come, we have much to discuss, and quickly!'A scout has encountered Gandalf while riding in the Westemnet, and the wizard mentioned that he wishes to speak with you.Gandalf can be found upon the road in the centre of the Westfold.

You should make haste and ride to Gandalf.Speak with Gandalf in the Westfold'I passed the wizard Gandalf upon the road not long ago, and he mentioned that he wishes to speak with you. The king is in the Westfold, at Helm's Deep -- he braces for war!

'Will you ride to him? Gandalf is apparently searching high and low for Erkenbrand, Elfhelm, Grimbold, and all their company. He needs your help.''We meet again! Good, I am glad. I have great need of you. The more eyes I have out upon the plains, the better.'Bingo is ready to travel north through Dunland, now with Haley Meadowsweet and Theodore Gorse as travelling companions.Theodore Gorse is in the small settlement of Avardin, on the western side of Dunland.

Bingo has asked you to see what Theodore thinks about beginning the journey north in the settlement of Galtrev.Talk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin, in DunlandBingo is down the hill west of the eastern entrance to Galtrev.

Bingo has agreed to meet you and his other companions in Galtrev, the large settlement in the middle of Dunland.Talk to Bingo in Galtrev, in DunlandHaley Meadowsweet is down the hill west of the eastern entrance to Galtrev.

Theodore seems to be missing, and Bingo wants to know if Haley knows where he has gone.Talk to Haley Meadowsweet in GaltrevTheodore Gorse is missing, and Haley Meadowsweet wants you to search various locations in Galtrev for her absent student.Search the upper eastern plateau in GaltrevSearch the skirmish camp in GaltrevSearch the farmland outside of GaltrevSearch the south-west entrance of GaltrevHaley Meadowsweet is down the hill to the west of the eastern entrance to Galtrev.

You were unable to find Theodore in Galtrev, and should return to Haley to see if she found him.Talk to Haley Meadowsweet in GaltrevHumfrey Rumming is on the hill west of the eastern gate of Galtrev.

Theodore is missing, and so is the Rothstone. Does Humfrey Rumming know something about these disappearances?Talk to Humfrey Rumming in GaltrevBingo is down the hill west of the eastern entrance to Galtrev.

Theodore has apparently gone to a place of great danger with the Rothstone, and Bingo wants to speak with you before it is too late to rescue the foolish Treasure Seeker.Talk to Bingo in GaltrevBingo is on the hill west of the eastern gate of Galtrev.

Bingo has resolved to follow Theodore to the lair of the dragon in Thrór's Coomb, and is waiting for you to speak with him.Talk to Bingo in Galtrev and travel with him to Draigoch's LairTheodore Gorse is outside the settlement of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.Talk to Theodore Gorse outside LhanuchHaley Meadowsweet is outside the settlement of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.Talk to Haley Meadowsweet outside LhanuchBingo Boffin is outside the settlement of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.Talk to Bingo outside Lhanuch'I have learned a little more about the settlement of Galtrev since we spoke with Humfrey Rumming there on our last visit. It is home to folk from many different Dunlending tribes, and they do not always see eye-to-eye. Perhaps we can better teach them to get along, ${PLAYER}!

'Do you mind asking Theodore if he thinks this is a good route for us to take? He and Haley passed through there on their way south. I would ask him myself, but he seems to be quite occupied with his own thoughts at the moment!''Do you mind asking Theodore if he thinks this is a good route for us to take? He and Haley passed through there on their way south. I would ask him myself, but he seems to be quite occupied with his own thoughts at the moment!'Theodore jumps when you speak to him, as if he were startled out of some reverie by your words.

'Yes? What is it, ${PLAYER}? I am sorry, I was not listening!'

You ask Theodore what he thinks of Bingo's plan to begin the northward journey in Galtrev, and he shrugs.

'Yes, yes, it seems fine to me. It makes no difference to me where we begin... ill fortune will follow us wherever we go unless we do something about it! Lead the way and I will meet you in Galtrev.''It makes no difference to me where we begin... ill fortune will follow us wherever we go unless we do something about it!''I wonder where Theodore has gone. Have you seen him?''So you found the Treasure Seekers? Well done, well done. Next time I shall make certain the riddle is more difficult to untangle!''Here we are, here we are. I am pleased to see that Humfrey is still here, and even more pleased to see that he has not fashioned another riddle for us. If he sent us back to Avardin one more time...

'Thankfully he is riddle-free for the moment. But have you seen Theodore lately? I must say that I haven't seen him since we arrived in Galtrev, but I am not sure exactly when I saw him last.

'Perhaps Haley knows where he has gone?''Have you seen Theodore lately? I must say that I haven't seen him since we arrived in Galtrev, but I am not sure exactly when I saw him last.

'Perhaps Haley knows where he has gone?''I hope you are having a fine adventure. I know that I am, but I am a master of lore, after all. Adventure finds me wherever I go!''Now that you mention it, I have not seen Theodore for a while now. I know he was with us when we arrived at Galtrev, but now he seems to have gotten himself lost. That is so typical, ${PLAYER}!

'Perhaps we should look for him. If you search a few of the likely spots around Galtrev, we may find some clue to his whereabouts. Knowing Theodore, he has probably gone off in whatever direction will cause us the most trouble!''If you search a few of the likely spots around Galtrev, we may find some clue to Theodore's whereabouts. Knowing him, he has probably gone off in whatever direction will cause us the most trouble!''Where can he have gone?''Your adventure continues, I expect?''I have had no luck finding Theodore either!''How goes the adventure?''${PLAYER}! Something had been troubling me, but I had not been able to put the worry into words. While you were looking for Theodore, I finally realized what it was. I looked through my possessions for the Rothstone, the golden necklace you put into my keeping in Eregion, but I cannot find it anywhere!

'Theodore has taken it! I do not know for what purpose he has stolen the Rothstone, but I do know that he blames it for the misfortune he thinks has befallen us. Where has he gone with it?''I do not know why he has taken the Rothstone, but I do know that he blames it for the misfortune he thinks has befallen us. Where has he gone with it?''This is unfortunate! Where can he have gone?''This is a little embarrassing, ${PLAYER}. I would have said something before, but I was very busy with my own affairs and you did not ask, so I figured all was done with your knowledge and approval. I am sorry to learn that was not the case.

'You see, your friend Theodore purchased a number of treasure maps from me some days ago, and I understand that he made use of all but one of them to no avail: there was no treasure at any location he searched... quite a pity for a Treasure Seeker! Mere hours ago he asked me about the last of the maps, and I assured him that there should be quite a collection of treasure there, given the nature of that spot. Well, he got a funny sort of look in his eye and said, "What's one more treasure added to the pile?" I see now that he had designs on returning a treasure rather than obtaining one.

'You want to know to where the last treasure map points? Did I not say? It guides adventurers to the lair of a dragon in Thrór's Coomb.''Your friend Theodore purchased a number of treasure maps from me some days ago, and I understand that he made use of every one to no avail: there was no treasure at any location he searched... quite a pity for a Treasure Seeker! Mere hours ago he asked me about the last of the maps, and I assured him that there should be quite a collection of treasure there, given the nature of that spot. Well, he got a funny sort of look in his eye and said, "What's one more treasure added to the pile?" I see now that he had designs on returning a treasure rather than obtaining one.

'You want to know to where the last treasure map points? Did I not say? It guides adventurers to the lair of a dragon in Thrór's Coomb.''Oh, Theodore! You foolish fool of a man!''This is terrible, ${PLAYER}! Theodore thinks this treasure has caused him ill fortune, and he has gone to the lair of a dragon in order to be rid of it? He is going to find no end of ill fortune there, and he will be the cause of it!'

Bingo shakes with nervousness, and you are reminded of how he quaked with fear on the slopes above Helegrod, when Spalvi said that a dragon had once lived there. Now, many months later and many hundreds of miles further on, Bingo closes his eyes and clenches his fists. When he opens his eyes again a moment later, his jaw is set and his shaking has stopped.

'We have to stop him, ${PLAYER}. I am not going to let some dragon put an end to Theodore's story, no matter how much he might deserve it for walking right into its waiting jaws! I will talk some hobbit-sense into him! Let me know when you are ready, and we will go to the dragon's lair together!''Let us go find our friend! No dragon will stand in our way!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Oh, that foolish man. What will we do with you, Theodore? This worrying will send me into an early grave!''All is well after all! What a relief that is, ${PLAYER}!''I am sorry to have caused you such trouble, ${PLAYER}, but I am glad to be rid of the Rothstone all the same!

'In fact, it seems to me that our fortunes are already beginning to turn around. After all, I could have been devoured by that dragon, or roasted to a crisp... and neither of those things happened! Perhaps I should not be a Treasure Seeker after all. I think I might be more of a Daring Dragon Dancer, what do you think?

'Ha! I am only teasing, ${PLAYER}. Tell Haley not to look so cross with me!''What an adventure! I have no regrets, ${PLAYER}, and although Haley is grumbling I am quite certain she has none either!''I am very pleased that Theodore was not eaten by that dragon!''Thank you for rescuing Theodore from himself, ${PLAYER}. I am very grateful to have met you and Bingo, and Theodore should be grateful for it as well; I do not think I would have had the patience to drag this purple-garbed fool from too many more dangers of his own making.

'Let us hope the rest of our northward journey is quieter and less eventful!''What am I going to do with you, Theodore?''Another successful adventure!''What a day this has been! I will need to spend some time coming up with the perfect way to describe that dragon. He was very impressive. I am glad I was able to see him, but I am even more glad that I was able to leave his lair without singeing the hair on my toes!

'I much preferred my encounter with the Green Dragon of Bywater to the Black Dragon of Thrór's Coomb, ${PLAYER}. Let us have no more dragons on this journey!'

<rgb=#00FF00>After you complete this quest, Bert Bartleby will arrive in the centre of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Full Course, Of Course!' (Recommended Level: 93)</rgb>Bingo is concerned that something seems to be troubling Willem Whisker, and he wants to learn what it may be.Willem Whisker is inside the Grimslade Mead Hall, in the Westfold.Talk to Willem Whisker inside the Grimslade Mead HallBingo is inside the Grimslade Mead Hall, in the Westfold.

To Bingo's surprise, Willem has suddenly run outside!Talk to Bingo inside the Grimslade Mead HallYou have followed Willem through the Gap of Rohan and to the entrance of the Dunbog. Now the lynx has stopped, and he seems to be waiting for you.Follow Willem WhiskerYou have followed Willem Whisker to the entrance to the Dunbog, where he has stopped and waited for you to catch up.Talk to Willem Whisker outside the DunbogWillem ran to the west, into the Dunbog.Follow Willem Whisker to the west, into the DunbogWillem Whisker has found a group of lynx in the north-east corner of the Dunbog, and many of them share his pattern and colour. Is this his family?Talk to Willem Whisker by the lonely tree in the DunbogBingo is by the lonely tree in the north-east corner of the Dunbog, with Willem's family.Talk to Bingo by the lonely tree in the DunbogBingo wants you to help make the Dunbog the perfect home for Willem and his family. You should defeat Orc abominations in the north-west of the Dunbog, collect meat from toads throughout the swamp, and collect suitable stones with which to build a sheltering wall.Defeat Orc abominations in the Dunbog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect toad-meat from adult bog-toads in the Dunbog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect suitable stones in the north-east corner of the Dunbog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have gathered some things to make Willem's home a little nicer, and should go now to the north-east area of the Dunbog to set Bingo's plan in motion.Build a nice sheltering wall for Willem's familyWillem Whisker is at his nest in the north-east corner of the Dunbog with his family.Bingo is at Willem Whisker's nest in the north-east corner of the Dunbog.Talk to Bingo at Willem's home in the north-east corner of the DunbogBingo has said farewell to Willem Whisker and wants to meet you at the nearest town in the Starkmoor.Talk to Bingo in the town of Avardin, in the Starkmoor'Do you think I should turn around and head for home? I am worried about the Shire, and this has been quite a long journey already... I do not know what to do!

'And furthermore, I have noticed that Willem has not been his usual self for a short time now. Do you think he is angry with me for even considering bringing this adventure to an end? Oh, I hope not! Perhaps you can learn if this is the root of his dissatisfaction, ${PLAYER}. Please find out if Willem is disappointed with me for thinking of returning to the Shire, will you?''I have noticed that Willem has not been his usual self for a short time now. Do you think he is angry with me for even considering bringing this adventure to an end? Oh, I hope not! Perhaps you can learn if this is the root of his dissatisfaction, ${PLAYER}. Please find out if Willem is disappointed with me for thinking of returning to the Shire, will you?'Willem looks at you closely. Curiously, the impression you get is that he is trying to make up his mind about something.'What did you say to him, ${PLAYER}? Where is he going? We have to follow him!'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel in pursuit of Willem when you continue this quest.</rgb>'We have to follow him! Where did he go? The Dunbog? Why would he go there?'Willem looks at you expectantly.'We have to follow him! Where did he go? The Dunbog? Why would he go there?'Willem looks at you expectantly, and then bounds away to the west. He seemingly wants you to follow him into the Dunbog.'Where is Willem going? We have to follow him!'Willem seems happy.'Look at these lynx! Is this Willem's family?'You look at Willem nuzzling with the she-lynx and understand that this is his mate, and the smaller lynx curled up nearby are their cubs.'This must be Willem's family, ${PLAYER}! I think I understand what Lady Galadriel meant when she spoke of his journey! I think he was looking for a better home for his mate and his cubs. Did you find one, W.W.?'

Even Bingo can read the disappointment in Willem's face.

'I am sorry, Willem! We found him caught in a trap in the Trollshaws, ${PLAYER}, do you remember? That is no place to raise a family! Rohan is embroiled in war, Moria is too dark, the mountains are too cold....'

Bingo trails away, and looks around at the marshes of the Dunbog.

'Do you know something, Willem? Your cubs look satisfied to live here, and it seems that they've already developed a taste for toad-meat. The temperature suits them and they know the nearby landmarks, and now that you're back, your family seems to want for very little. What if ${PLAYER} and I built a bit of a shelter for you, and gathered some food for your family? We could also defeat some of the more unpleasant foes that stalk the marsh!

'This might not have seemed the perfect home before, but compared to the other lands we've seen, I think we might be able to turn it into the perfect place for your family! What do you say to that?''We should build a shelter for Willem, and gather some food for his family! We could also defeat some of the more unpleasant foes that stalk the marsh!''I hope this wall does the trick!''I suppose this is good-bye, then. You take care of yourself and your family, W.W.!'You set the toad-meat down within the wall, and some of the young cubs sniff it with interest. Willem blinks at you slowly, and you know that this is good-bye. He looks from you to Bingo, and you assure him that you will continue watching out for the hobbit adventurer.Willem purrs loudly, and the rumbling fills the air.'I suppose this is the end of our journey together, Willem. I am sad to see you go, but I know that your family needs you and I don't want to keep you from them any longer than I already have! I have really enjoyed our travels together, and I wouldn't trade them for anything! I... I'll miss you, W.W.. You take care of yourself and your family too, you hear me?'

A loud rumbling sound fills the air.

'Are you purring, Willem? No, couldn't be. You are a rough and tough adventurer, a veteran of many campaigns! It must just be my stomach rumbling. I never did get enough meals to suit me on this journey, and today is no different! Well... well... so long, Willem. I will take my rumbling belly away now, so as not to wake the little ones. You are welcome in the Shire any time. Any time, Willem, I mean it!

'It is difficult to say good-bye, ${PLAYER}, but we had better leave now or we won't! Let us go north-east to the nearest village in the Starkmoor. I think it is called something like Avardin, but I do not know for certain.''Good-bye, Willem! We will miss you! Come visit anytime!'Willem looks at you gratefully and purrs loudly.'I am glad we were able to help Willem and his family, ${PLAYER}. I will miss that fuzzy fellow, though. I think I will try to do some writing in my book in order to keep myself busy for now, if that is all right with you.'

<rgb=#00FF00>After you complete this quest, Bert Bartleby will arrive in the centre of Avardin in the Starkmoor, in Dunland.</rgb>

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'A String of Ill Fortune' (Recommended Level: 93)</rgb>Those allied against the new claim for the throne have gathered and are ready to confront those who now hold the mead hall.Gifemund is in the ore refinery building near the centre of Woodhurst.

The time has come to reclaim the throne of Woodhurst.Speak with GifemundHerubrand is in his hideout in the cellar of the farmhouse in Woodhurst.

Herubrand wishes to speak with you after the battle in the mead hall.Speak with Herubrand'The city has fallen as the soothsayer predicted. I was a fool to think Guard Captain Thurferth was the rising darkness, but he was a part of the problem. I should have known the Dunlending were involved, and though it was his duty, Thurferth was doing nothing about them.

'The time has come to confront our true foe. Woodhurst will be changed forever after this, either for better or worse.

'Speak to me again when you are ready.''The enemy no longer hides in the shadows, and has taken the mead hall by force. There are so many. This will surely be a battle.

'When you are ready we will fight our way to the mead hall.''That was a great battle - one we will not soon forget. I have reclaimed the seat that was my father's, but I am leaving Gifemund in charge. He has proven his loyalty, and will make a dependable steward until I return.

'I have heard rumour of aid needed in Westfold. I will soon pack my belongings and join those following Erkenbrand at the ford of Isen. May we meet again some day.'Dunward fears that Hildith's mission for the scouts may prove too dangerous when they are all split up.The four scouts rode out west, north-west, north-east, and south-east from Grimslade.

You should search for and assist the four scouts sent out by Hildith to search for Grimbold.Find Húnbrit, who rode east and southFind Winmar, who rode northFind Ordgar, who rode north-westFind Cúthsig, who rode west(Assist Húnbrit)(Assist Gandalf)Hildith can be found in the Mead Hall of Grimslade in the Westfold.

You should return to Hildith.Return to Hildith'I cannot bear to see us lose more of Grimslade's finest men. I want Grimbold found, and Erkenbrand and the rest, but I believe he would have come directly to Grimslade if he headed this way.

'We should not be wasting good men on wild goose chases. Will you help them in their missions and speed their return?''Half-orcs! The woods here are utterly crawling with them. There must be a large encampment nearby, for there to be so many. I must return to warn Lady Hildith!''I have noticed rather a lot of Wargs roaming the fields, where a year past there were none. They are fell, nightmarish creatures. What is to be done?'The poor man has been killed, not unlike the many who rode out into the Westfold before him in recent times.

It was perilous to venture out alone.'It is Elfhelm! I cannot believe my eyes. Elfhelm was one of the last men to see Grimbold and Erkenbrand.

'And....and I believe the old man is Gandalf Greyhame, if stories be true. But he is all white now. You seem to know the wizard, ${PLAYER}. You must be quite the adventurer....''So Elfhelm rides to protect Edoras while my husband and Erkenbrand are nowhere to be found? Elfhelm is a coward. It is the Westfold that needs aid -- if it falls, there will be no Edoras.

'No matter. We have a prisoner to deal with. Perhaps he can tell us about Isengard's movements.'Rohirric banners planted upon the bodies of the Uruk-hai you've slain should send a strong message to the foes coming down from Isengard.Uruks can be found at the Fords of Isen in the western Westfold.

You should plant banners in the bodies of Uruks you've killed.Plant Rohirric banners over slain UruksUruks can be found at the Fords of Isen in the western Westfold.

You should plant banners in the bodies of Uruks you've killed.Plant Rohirric banners over slain Uruks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of Uruks at the Fords of Isen, and claimed their deaths with proud banners of the Rohirrim.

The Fords will not be safe for foes while Rohan endures.CompletedRohirric banners planted upon the bodies of the Uruk-hai you've slain should send a strong message to the foes coming down from Isengard.

You should defeat several Uruks and plant banners upon them where they fall.You have defeated a number of Uruks at the Fords of Isen, and claimed their deaths with proud banners of the Rohirrim.

The Fords will not be safe for foes while Rohan endures.The unfriendly acting Thane, Hildith, grows concerned with the state of the Westfold, and summons a council to her, and does not wish to be disturbed while she calls the meeting.Townsfolk of Grimslade can be found in the town.

You should speak to townsfolk of Grimslade.Hildith is in the Mead Hall of Grimslade.

You should return to Hildith.Return to Hildith'I will summon a small council to discuss the tidings you bring, stranger. You may leave my presence. I have no further need of you until I have gathered the council here.

'If you wish to occupy yourself, you may speak to the townsfolk.''I am Grimwald, son of Grimbold! My father is away at the fords, and now my mother is Thane in his place.

'Where are you from? You have very strange clothing.''Are you here to ask after my son Grimbold? Alas, he is away at the Fords. He is a great Thane, and I watch for his return every day. I know Erkenbrand will take good care of him.''It is wartime, and our food-stores are alarmingly low now that our supply-lines are cut off. Lady Éowyn has left Meduseld empty, Marton is silent, and the people of Rohan fear to use the roads. We must bolster our supplies.''I cannot talk now, stranger. If you wish to make yourself useful, you will help us make more arrows for defending our walls.''Let us discuss the matters at hand.'Half-orcs are growing in number in the woods near Grimslade, and Húnbrit has found the source: a large encampment.Half-orcs can be found in their encampment south-east from the gates of Grimslade.

You should defeat Half-orcs at Fushum Raus.Defeat Half-orcs at Fushum Raus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of Half-orcs near Grimslade, but there are too many to uproot the entire encampment. You have done all that you could here.Completed'All who have ventured into the woods of late have quickly returned home because of the half-orc scouts, but I have found the source of them!

'Look at this great encampment, ${PLAYER}. What should we do about this?'You have defeated a number of Half-orcs near Grimslade, but there are too many to uproot the entire encampment. You have done all that you could here.The Wargs have had a detrimental effect on the lands of the Westfold, destroying herds of wild horses and cows.Remains of herd-animals can be found throughout the plains of the eastern Westfold.

You should examine the remains of herd-animals to see how much the Wargs have affected the landscape.Examine remains of herd-animals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Winmar is near the road leading north from Grimslade.

You should speak with Winmar.Return to Winmar'I worry that the Wargs from Isengard have destroyed the herd-creatures that roam wild in the Westfold. They are our horses, our beasts of burden, our cows, our goats, and we cannot manage without them.

'Will you look to see if they are affected by the deadly hunters?''You found many remains of our wild herds, did you? I feared as much. Even if we survive the war, times will be hard for us all.'You have arrived at Helm's Deep as the King's men prepare to defend the Hornburg.A road runs from Helm's Dike through the valley and to the Hornburg.Follow the road that runs from Helm's Dike to the HornburgTalk to Gimli at Helm's DikeTalk to Thurketel along the road from the DikeThe guard-house provides a sturdy defence for the Hornburg.Find the guard-house of the HornburgTalk to Háma at the guard-house of the HornburgTalk to Déorwine at the guard-house of the HornburgThe Deeping Wall provides a sturdy defence for the Hornburg, and allows its defenders a commanding view of the gorge.Find Legolas atop the Deeping WallTalk to Legolas atop the wallTalk to Sigferth atop the wallThéoden and Éomer are overseeing the preparations outside the Hornburg.Find Théoden and Éomer outside the keep of the HornburgTalk to Théoden outside the keep of the HornburgTalk to Éomer outside the keep of the HornburgAragorn is outside the keep of the Hornburg, alongside Éomer and not far from Théoden.Talk to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg'The armies of Saruman assaulted the men at the Fords of Isen, and the survivors of the rout are scattered now across the Westfold. No one seems to know where Erkenbrand might be found. He is the lord of the Hornburg, during time of peace, and would make his way here if he could.

'Théoden King turned aside from his course and made for the Deep when the size of Saruman's force became clear. His army is already on the march, and will soon be here. I welcome all able folk willing to offer assistance, but I know you by reputation and count your aid double!

'Friends of yours already lend us what help they can. You will find them in the Dike, throughout the Deep, and at the Hornburg.''Your friends can be found along the road from the Dike, and near the Hornburg. Speak to them and assess their moods.''Hail, friend! I knew you would not miss this chance! This dwarf has had enough of running, and riding, and talking! Now is the time for fighting, and quite a battle it is shaping up to be, too!

'The walls of the fortress seem very sturdy, and the men say that the Deep has never been taken by an enemy. Aye, and may it not be taken this time, either, but I tell you true that I will be a mite disappointed if my axe sees little use. There are Orc necks to hew, and I am just the dwarf to do it!

'I expect you will find Legolas atop the fortress wall. He would prefer a nice long view of the approaching Orcs, whereas I want to see their ugly faces up close!''This is the home of Erkenbrand, but none know what has become of him. Now the King will rely on the walls of the Hornburg, and on the strong arms of his people. Will you help us defend the Deep?'

Thurketel smiles when you say that you will.

'The Hornburg has never fallen, and if fortune be with us I will one day tell my children and theirs that it still has not, even many years hence. This night may be its gravest test, and ours. May we be found sufficient!''Travel up the road and see the fortress, my friend. It is quite well-built, by the standards of men. Dwarves could do better, but is this not always true?''The Hornburg has never fallen to any enemies of the Mark. I pray we may still say this on the morrow!''The tides of war bring you once again to the King's shore, ${PLAYER}! No, this time I will not take your weapons, or keep you from seeing Théoden. Now I am pleased you are here, and hope that your skill in battle is as great as I am told!'

'Déorwine and I seek to reinforce the doors of this guard-house, but it is to be hoped that the forces of Saruman do not get this far into the Deep. Still, it is good to be prepared.'

You tell Háma of your meeting with Léoferth, in Brockbridge, and the doorward sighs heavily.

'Thank you for the news of my father. He has been in poor health for many years, but I am glad to know that he thinks of his son from time to time. He is often in my thoughts. If there is some measure of glory to be had in the hours ahead, I hope it is my lot to make Léoferth proud.''We are trying to reinforce the doors, but there is not enough sturdy wood in the Deep! Everything is either rotted or dry and old. Brittle wood will do us no good. We must hope that Gamling and the other soldiers are able to keep the armies of Saruman from breaching the Dike, for these doors will not keep them long.

'Háma says I am wrong. I hope he is right.''You should climb to the top of the wall, and see the strength of our defence. The view will be a good one, as well. You should see it before the view is marred by the sight of ugly Orcs!''You should climb the wall and see how fare its defenders.''We meet once more, my friend! If you seek battle, you have come to the right place, but if you seek a good rest or peaceful quiet you should leave this ravine at once! If the numbers reported by Théoden's scouts can be trusted, this entire gorge will be filled with Orcs before the moon is down.

'From here I will have a clear shot upon any foe that seeks to cross the flat plain before the Deeping Wall. Every arrow I loose will spell death for one of our enemies, but which will I first exhaust: my arrows or our foes?

'All of us will have our part to play during the coming night.''We are well-met, my new friend! These are the times that prove the strength of our hearts, are they not? We are lucky to live in such times, for the opportunity to prove ourselves up to the task!

'Saruman's Orcs will arrive at the Dike, and if they are not defeated outright, they will push into the space before our walls. We will whittle down their numbers with arrows and with thrown spears, and they will shake their blades and gnash their teeth and will have no choice but to turn away.

'The Hornburg has never been breached. It will not be breached tonight, either!''Aragorn and the King are outside the keep of the Hornburg, seeing to the preparations. You should ask them if there is aught you can do to help. There is sure to be something you can do.''Welcome to the Hornburg, ${PLAYER}. This is where I will make my stand. Let Saruman's armies come! They will break upon our walls and we will scatter them across the fields. There is no shortage of tasks to be done. The only thing we lack is time: the scouts tell me Saruman's forces will be here before the moon is high.''You ride a fast steed, my friend! Were you able to be a help to my sister Éowyn? And how did you find my own home of Aldburg? Has Arcil maintained the village as well as his father once did?'

You give Éomer what tidings you can in the little time you both have to spare.

'I see. My uncle believes this battle will be over quickly, but I am not so certain. I hope he is right. There will be much work to do to restore the Mark, even once the fighting is done. But first we must survive the coming battle.''Aragorn tells me the defences of the Hornburg are not strong enough. Speak to him and learn what he means by this.''If Aragorn says our defences are not sufficient, I believe him. He is a strong man, and wiser than you might think to look at him.''I am glad to see you, my well-travelled friend! My heart tells me we are in for a long night. The Men of Rohan have sheltered in the Hornburg before, and its walls have never failed them. I have seen many points of weakness already, and we have only been here a short while. We must ensure this fortress does not fall. If Rohan falls, I fear the rest of Middle-earth will not stand long.'Aragorn is desperate to ensure that the Hornburg is well-defended before Saruman's forces arrive.Barrels of iron goods from the farmers of Westfold can be found outside the keep of the Hornburg, near Aragorn.

Aragorn has asked you to sort through an iron goods barrel using one of the nearby sorting mats.Retrieve iron goods from a barrel near Aragorn, outside the keep of the HornburgYou can use one of the mats near Aragorn to sort the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold.Use the mat near Aragorn to sort through the iron goodsYou can use one of the mats near Aragorn to sort the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold.Use the mat near Aragorn to sort through the iron goodsYou can use one of the mats near Aragorn to sort the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold.Éomer is outside the keep of the Hornburg.Talk to Éomer outside the keep of the HornburgÉomer has asked you to carry one of the nearby training dummies up to the wall by Legolas, the better to draw fire away from the defenders.Pick up one of the training dummies near ÉomerLegolas is atop the wall.

You have carried a training dummy to the top of the wall and Legolas has caught your eye.Talk to Legolas atop the wallCorudan has gone down to the Dike, beyond the walls of the Hornburg.

Legolas told you that Corudan planned to scout the armies of Saruman, and you should speak to him before he leaves.Talk to Corudan by his horse at Helm's DikeGamling is at Helm's Dike.

There is always work to be done to get ready for battle, and Gamling will tell you what he needs.Talk to Gamling at Helm's DikeGamling has asked you to carry a barrel of iron goods from Helm's Dike to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg.Pick up the barrel of iron goods near Gamling, in Helm's DikeAragorn is outside the keep of the Hornburg, and wishes to speak with you.Talk to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg'Weapons are in short supply here. Erkenbrand had a small amount for the garrison, but his men took most of the weapons and armour with them when they rode to the Fords, and most of them have not returned. Théoden has called for the people of the Westfold to send as many iron goods as they can spare to the Deep. It is not much, but we may be able to fashion weapons and crude armour from these iron goods in the hours we have before the battle is joined.

'Search through one of the barrels of iron goods, and sort its contents on the nearby mat. Any strong iron could be useful, but we need to know what we have available.''The farmers of Westfold have contributed barrels of iron goods. Sort through the iron goods on the nearby mats, for there may be some use we can make of their contents.''Use the mat right over there to sort through the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold. There may be something we can use in the defence, and if there is I want to be certain we find it.''Use the mat right over there to sort through the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold. There may be something we can use in the defence, and if there is I want to be certain we find it.''Use the mat right over there to sort through the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold. There may be something we can use in the defence, and if there is I want to be certain we find it.''Éomer has had a very cunning idea. I think you should speak with him and help carry it out. It is very clever and may save some lives before the Orcs realize what we have done.''I have had an idea, friend. While watching the men training, I realized something interesting: from a great distance, I could not tell if a man was training with a straw dummy or if his opponent was merely parrying his blows without a great deal of motion. If I, with the keen eyes of my people, could not tell the difference, what would one of Saruman's ill-bred minions make of it?

'I think we should carry some training dummies to the top of the wall, ${PLAYER}. It will make our numbers seem the greater, and any arrow wasted upon a dummy is one which could have struck a fighting man. That is a trade worth any amount of heavy lifting!''I think we should carry some training dummies to the top of the wall, ${PLAYER}. It will make our numbers seem the greater, and any arrow wasted upon a dummy is one which could have struck a fighting man. That is a trade worth any amount of heavy lifting! Pick up one of the dummies and carry it to the top of the wall by your friend Legolas.''You should check on your Elf friend atop the wall, where you brought the training dummy.''That is a clever idea, if it proves successful. Unless Saruman's armies turn aside for some reason I cannot tell, they will arrive at the Deep during the hours of darkness. They will not be able to tell the difference between these dummies and the defenders atop the wall until they get very near to the wall. And by then I will have claimed many lives of Orcs.

'I spoke for a time with your friend Corudan. I met his sister when we stayed in Lothlórien. If Sigileth were here, with her deadly knives, the Orcs would have a great deal to fear! While I am wishing for unlikely happenstance, why not hope for the arrival of an army of my own kin? That would be a sight indeed! But they are far from here, and have their own concerns and their own lands to defend. The Rohirrim are on their own. They will have to make do with two Elves, one dwarf, and two Men.

'Speaking of Corudan, he wanted me to send you to him. He rode down to the Dike, and said he wished to see the approaching armies with his own eyes.''Corudan wished to speak with you before he left to scout the forces of Saruman. He said he would wait for you at Helm's Dike.''There you are, my friend! I am glad to see you before I leave. I am going to ride from the Dike and see what I can tell of Saruman's forces. There may be some weakness in their ranks we will be able to exploit, but until I see his armies on the march all we have is rumour and fear. I will return before long, and tell you what I have seen.

'Do not fear! I will return before the battle is joined, and perhaps with news that can help us. Stand strong and inspire the Men of Rohan, ${PLAYER}! I know you will not let them down.''I will see you again. I will only be gone for a short time, and will return before the battle is joined.''We have been fortunate so far, ${PLAYER}. Farmers of Westfold have brought more iron goods for us to use. Carry one of these barrels of iron goods to your friend Aragorn, outside the walls of the Hornburg. He has been sorting through the barrels for anything of use in preparing the defences.''Aragorn will be pleased to receive another barrel of iron goods. Bring it to him outside the keep of the Hornburg.''You should return to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg and see what else needs to be done.''I am glad more barrels of iron are coming into the Deep, but there is no certainty that we will be able to make use of their contents. It is worth the wager. Thank you for bringing this all the way here.'As the night deepens, battle approaches the defenders of the Hornburg.Gléowine is on the lowest level of the fortress, by a pile of straw near the west wall.

Aragorn wants to determine the mood of Théoden, but has sent you not to the King but to Gléowine to learn it.Talk to Gléowine near the map table by the western wallGléowine wants you to show him on the nearby map table what the night may hold for the defenders of Helm's Deep.

<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the map table near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume after midnight, when the battle is joined.</rgb>Study the map table near the western wall, by Gléowine, and time will passIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep.

Gléowine is by the map table, near the pile of straw by the western wall.Talk to Gléowine, by the map table near the western wall, after midnightIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep.

Gamling is by the map table with Gléowine, on the lowest level of the fortress, by the western wall.Talk to Gamling by the pile of straw near the western wallAragorn speaks to you in hushed tones.

'The next few hours will sorely test us all, my friend, but none more than the King of Rohan. It will be Théoden's resolve, as much as the strength of his fighting men, that will govern our chances of survival. He will not speak plainly to me, or to any of us, on this matter. It is not his way, nor the way of most who rule.

'Find Gléowine and ask him what he makes of the King's mood and temperament. I cannot tell if the King is putting on a brave face, but Gléowine has served him for many years and will know better than I the truth of this. I last saw the minstrel below us, by a pile of straw near the western wall.''You will find Gléowine below us, by the western wall. Ask him what he makes of Théoden's mood and temperament. We will need the King to be strong of will if we are to survive what this night promises.''I saw the King not long ago, and he seems to be in fine spirits, ${PLAYER}. He is not blind to the danger, but he does not ignore it, either. His is not bravery without cause, but courage based on confidence in his men and his own strength. He sheltered too long in his own hall, and now that he emerges and sees battle he is ready for it.

'I do not think Aragorn should worry about my King. Théoden will surprise him, when the battle is upon us. Ah, I speak of battle, but I am a minstrel and know little of strategy or tactics. You have seen more of war than I have, and this old man counts himself fortunate! There is a map on the table over there. Will you show to me how the attack will progress, while we wait?'

<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the map table near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume after midnight, when the battle is joined.</rgb>'You have seen more of war than I have, and this old man counts himself fortunate! There is a map on the table over there. Will you show to me how the attack will progress, while we wait?'

<rgb=#FF0000>Interacting with the map table near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume after midnight, when the battle is joined.</rgb>'Gamling has come from the Dike, and he seeks our aid! Speak to him and find out what we can do! There is little hope we can hold that pass for long, but standing for even a short while may save some lives.'

<rgb=#FFFF00><b>Interact with Gamling to experience 'Epic Battles: Basic Training,' the tutorial for the Epic Battles system, if you are interested in the Epic Battles system. The tutorial is optional, and can be skipped if you intend to play the Storied Tales in Helm's Deep.</b></rgb>'I think battle is almost upon us. If you are willing to stand with my men, come with me to hold Helm's Dike for as long as we are able!''Thank you for the lesson in strategy and tactics, my friend. I cannot say the lesson will remain long in this old head of mine, but for now I feel glad having learned something of what awaits us here.

'But look! It is Gamling, from the Dike. He seeks our help!'

