Quickbeam is at Derndingle.Speak to Quickbeam'I left Lassemista's Seed at Isengard. It will grow and watch the tower, ensuring no evil will come to it again. Lassemista loved to walk the forest though, and I wish to honour his memory.''I need time to remember what the next step is.''On many occasions, Lassemista enjoyed long conversations with Treebeard. To next honour him, I think we should say good-bye to Wellinghall.''I need time to remember what the next step is.''I spent many hours with Lassemista watching the river that feeds the forest. There is a small island; having a good look around there feels right.''I need time to remember what the next step is.''There is one more thing I can think of. Lassemista trusted Saruman, and I know he was deeply wounded by the betrayal. I have planted a seed for Lassemista at Orthanc. To show my sadness, please visit it and let Lassemista know I remember him with a tear.''Lassemista was my closest friend. He loved the forest more than most others. I will miss him for a very long time.'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Complete Volume III, Book 14: The Waters of IsengardEarn Friend standing with the Ents of FangornLéofdag perished at the Battle of the Hornburg, vindicating himself from the accusations against his honour.Léofdag's wife, Fleda, is in Aldburg.

