'Help me untie our proud beasts and set them free! At least that way they may be able to fight back against those who come to destroy us!''It was a good thought to untie the horses, for now they will not be left defenceless in the face of our enemies. Even a cornered animal might slay an Orc or two.'

Thenca looks at you sternly.

'This seems to me clear, ${PLAYER}. We cannot hold the Dike any longer, and the men at Helm's Deep are truly cornered themselves, and we with them. The Orcs will see how ferocious we can be! To the fortress, my friends!'Saruman's assault upon the defenders of Helm's Deep has begun, his forces scaling the Deeping Wall seeking to put an end to the people of Rohan.Legolas stands atop the Deeping Wall, ready for battle.Talk to Legolas atop the Deeping WallOrcs climb up the ladders leaning against the Deeping Wall and must be defeated. Legolas also asked you to push down as many of the ladders as you can.Patrol the wall and defeat Orcs as they climb up and attackPush ladders away from the wallEgláf has loaded the western rock trap on the Deeping Wall and waits for you to set it off.Drop the readied stones from the west trapOrcs continue to climb up the ladders leaning against the Deeping Wall and must be defeated. You should continue to knock down their ladders, slowing their progress.Patrol the wall and defeat Orcs as they climb up and attackPush ladders away from the wallTwo more rock traps have been loaded atop the Deeping Wall, and Egláf waits for you to release their deadly contents onto the Orcs below.Drop the readied stones from the remaining trapsEgláf has called for you to come to his aid.Talk to Egláf by the rock trap on the Deeping WallOrcs have gained access to one of the towers and dealt Egláf a grievous blow. Protect him from their weapons!Defend Egláf from the OrcsThe surprise Orc attack knocked Egláf down, but he has recovered from the surprise and wishes to speak to you.Orcs have climbed onto the top of the tower, and Egláf has sent you to clear them away.Defeat the Orcs on top of the tower above the Deeping WallThenca has followed you onto the top of the tower above the Deeping Wall.Talk to Thenca atop the tower above the Deeping WallThere seems to be no end to Saruman's Orcs, but Thenca has sworn to defend the Deeping Wall and will do so with his life, if that proves necessary.Defend Thenca and keep him alive'The battle is joined, ${PLAYER}! Saruman's Orcs felled many trees on the outskirts of Fangorn, and from those trunks they assembled great wooden ladders. They use these to scale the Deeping Wall! Even now the Orcs use these constructions to come within reach of axe and sword!

'My arrows will teach them this is folly, for I can slay many of them before they reach the top; but I cannot bring them all down. You and the other defenders must fight those Orcs who reach the top of the wall. Take the time to push down as many ladders as you can and you will slow their progress, my friend. Now we fight for Rohan.''Our supply of stones runs low; even were it otherwise, the Orcs would learn to avoid the outlets from which fall the rocks. The cost of that knowledge was high, but the effectiveness of our traps is at an end. For every Orc we slay, five take his place! At this rate we will be overrun.

'Come with me, ${PLAYER}. We are needed elsewhere on the wall!''I will be all right, my friend. The wind was knocked from my lungs and I received a few scrapes, but nothing serious. The Orcs are beginning to overrun our position; I hear them atop the tower!''${PLAYER}, are you all right? My sword has ended the life of many an Orc this night, but even so there seems to be no end to the creatures! Let there be no end to our courage either!'Saruman's foul craft has claimed the lives of both his own Orc-warriors and Rohirrim defenders on the Deeping Wall. Now his forces seek to gain access to the valley through the wreckage that remains.Aragorn has returned from his sortie with Éomer, and now he has an urgent task for you.Talk to Aragorn in the Deeping-coombAragorn has asked you to defeat the Orcs and Dunlendings that have passed through the hole in the Deeping Wall and threaten the Rohirrim within the Deeping-coomb. He also wants you to extinguish the lit fuses on any black powder devices you find.Defeat forces of Saruman inside the Deeping-coomb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Extinguish lit fuses in the Deeping-coomb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Orcs have set more devices containing black powder near the hole in the Deeping Wall, and the fuses have nearly reached the end of their short, dangerous lives!Extinguish more black powder devices near the hole in the Deeping Wall (${NUMBER}/4)Egláf needs your help to retreat further into the Deeping-coomb.Help Egláf to his feetLéofdag and the rest of the Riders Four delight to stand alongside you in defence of their land, and together they hope to push back Saruman's forces.Talk to Léofdag in the Deeping-coombYou have fought bravely against the forces of Saruman with the Riders Four in the Deeping-coomb, and now their captain Burnoth wishes to speak with you.Talk to Burnoth in the Deeping-coomb'Saruman has used some foul craft to destroy part of the Deeping Wall, and the coomb lies undefended before his forces! Orcs and Dunlendings alike pour through the hole, wielding sword and axe, but I count other of their weapons more deadly: some of our foes carry devices bedecked with lit fuses. The black powder contained within is harmless on its own, but causes a tremendous explosion when set aflame. Did one of these destroy the wall?

'Slay our foes on this side of the wall, ${PLAYER}, and extinguish the fuses of any lit devices you encounter!''I should have known to see you here, ${PLAYER}, for heroes such as you are oft encountered where the fighting is thickest and the need most pressing! So it is with the Riders Four!

'Who is this injured man? Egláf, you say? Come with us, my friend, if your leg allows you to stand. You may find a moment's respite within the mill, and take the chance to bind your wounds.

'${PLAYER}! I will bring you to my captain, and to the others. There will be deeds of valour to perform on this night, enough for the Riders Four and more beside, I do not doubt!''The victory is ours, and the night is not yet ended; there will be plenty of time for more deeds of valour, my friend. Ah, do not worry yourself on our account! The Riders Four have seen worse scrapes than this, and I deem you have as well.

'Take care of yourself, ${PLAYER}, and of Théoden King! We will defend Rohan to the very last!'Some of Saruman's allies have discovered tunnels behind Helm's Deep, and threaten the sheltering Rohirrim in the haven they believed safe. Éomer and Gimli need your help to close off these tunnels and prevent such craven attacks.Éomer has come to the Glittering Caves and his anger at Lheu Brenin's attempted attack on his people knows no bounds.Talk to Éomer in the Glittering CavesÉomer has asked you to reassure the folk sheltering within the Glittering Caves that Théoden's warriors will keep them safe.Éomer has asked you to reassure the folk sheltering within the Glittering Caves that Théoden's warriors will keep them safe.Reassure sheltering folk that they will be safe (3/4)A woman in the Glittering Caves has heard your reassurances but still has questions for you.Talk to Ardith in the Glittering CavesLéofa, a child of the Westfold who helped you defeat Lheu Brenin in the Glittering Caves, wishes to speak with you.Talk to Léofa in the Glittering CavesGimli is in the Glittering Caves, attempting to balance his awe at its beauty with the dangers contained within.Talk to Gimli in the Glittering CavesYou and Gimli have fought a number of enterprising Orcs and found Éomer deep within the Glittering Caves, at the passage where his scouts disappeared.Talk to Éomer in the Glittering CavesSpiders have trapped some of Éomer's scouts and must be slain if the men are to be freed.Defeat spiders in the Glittering Caves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Free Éomer's scouts from cocooned imprisonment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Éomer is waiting to hear of your success in the Glittering Caves.Talk to Éomer in the Glittering Caves'I spit on the memory of this Dunlending chief, ${PLAYER}. He sought to surprise my people from the rear, breaking into their haven of safety and putting them to the sword under the cover of darkness? He deserves a coward's death, and I am pleased he received it!

'I have sent some scouts to the furthest reaches of the caves in order to find the place where this craven Dunlending entered, that they may collapse it and any others they find. We cannot allow any more enemies to get behind the folk who shelter here.

'While my scouts undertake that mission, I ask you to reassure those who hide here that Théoden's warriors will keep them safe. Will you do that for me, my friend?''I thank you for the kindness of your words, even if they are lies. Yes, I know of the Dunlendings that attempted to sneak into the caves.
 
'This is my daughter Léofa. It was she who stood with you and the dwarf against the Dunlending chief, and she has told me all. Do not think to hide such dangers from women of Rohan! We will fight and die for this land, if we must, no less eagerly than any of our men. If you think otherwise, you shame yourself.

'If the enemy finds us here, we will fight to protect the honour of Théoden King and of Rohan. So it has always been, and so it will be.''Hello again, ${PLAYER}! It is nice to meet in less-dangerous circumstances, even if the reprieve won't last for long! I will fight a hundred Dunlending chiefs, and as many Orcs, if that is what it takes to protect my mother, or my father!

'You came to the caves only recently. Did you hear any news of my father while you were fighting outside? His name is Cenric and he has a distinctive wooden shield, given to him by a great hero before I was born: its edges are trimmed with gold, and it bears an embossed horse's head in the centre. He is very brave.'

You tell Léofa that you fought alongside Cenric at Helm's Dike earlier in the evening, but have not seen him since then.

'Ah, well, I am sure he is still fighting. He is very brave, you know.''I hope you are ready for some more fighting, ${PLAYER}. One of Éomer's scouting parties did not come back when he expected, and he went in search of it. It seems to me they may have found the foes for which they searched, and now those enemies might think to ensnare Éomer. Let us go after him!''I have located my missing scouts, ${PLAYER}, but I was not the first to find them... the spiders found them first! Free my men and let these creatures know that the caves here belong to Rohan and its people!''The folk sheltering in the caves should now be safe from attackers thinking to surprise them from tunnels in the mountains, but there are still foes in the Deep! We are needed outside, my friends!'In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman show no sign of relenting. The defenders have retreated into the Hornburg, uncertain of their ability to long survive against the forces of Isengard.Háma, the door-ward of Théoden, stands before the Hornburg. He braces himself for news of the battle.Talk to HámaThéoden stands atop the fortress, surveying his seemingly insurmountable foes.Talk to ThéodenAragorn refuses to give in to despair. He intends to defend the Hornburg even as the Orcs threaten to overrun the fortress.Talk to AragornKing Théoden has slain a mighty war-troll, but the beast carried a black powder bomb with a lit fuse!Quench the fuse on the black powder bombThe fuse on the black powder bomb has been quenched, and the immediate danger has been avoided. Aragorn wishes to speak with you.Talk to AragornThe defenders have thrown back another of Saruman's assaults, but ten thousand Orcs remain outside the walls. Aragorn and Théoden must decide if anything can be done.Listen to Aragorn and Théoden and decide what can be doneThéoden has asked you to join his riders on their assault from the Hornburg.

<rgb=#00FF00>Mount your travelling steed and speak to Théoden.</rgb>Mount your travelling steed and talk to ThéodenThéoden leads a charge of his riders down the causeway into the waiting Orcs, and he has requested that you ride with him.Ride with Théoden down the causeway into the waiting Orcs'How fares the battle down below, ${PLAYER}? There has been hard fighting up here, and Théoden King has bloodied his sword already. So far we have turned aside all our foes, but I fear they will storm the lower levels and we will be surrounded. 

'Do you have any good tidings for the king, or has all been lost? This night seems never-ending, and that is a trait it shares with the forces of Isengard!''My sword rests no longer in idleness! I am prepared to fight and die for my land and my people! It should have been so earlier, but for the honeyed words of Saruman, poured into my ear by his servant Gríma.

'But no longer! My place is here, in defence of my people until the very end. It will not be much longer.''If the Hornburg falls, there will be none left to safe-guard the kingdom of Rohan. We must defend the fortress for as long as we can!

'There is no other choice left to us, ${PLAYER}. It falls to us to save Rohan!''That was quickly-done, ${PLAYER}. You may have purchased us a reprieve, and saved the fortress from another of Saruman's sorcerous devices!

'We are safe, for now.''We will ride from the Hornburg and bring death to the Orcs! Riders, to me! Let none fear to ride with us, for the bards will sing of our deeds long after we are gone!

'This is the hour of Rohan!'Cenric will not forget the ordeal of night at Helm's Deep.Cenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.Talk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: Helm's Dike'Cenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.Talk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Deeping Wall'Cenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.Talk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Deeping-coomb'Cenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.Talk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Glittering Caves'Cenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.Talk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Hornburg'Cenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.Talk to Cenric on the field of victory after the battle of Helm's Deep'I will not forget the long night, ${PLAYER}. Many are the tales we will tell of the great battle at Helm's Deep!'

<rgb=#00FF00>If you did not complete the Storied Tales while playing through Volume III Book 13, this quest will give you the opportunity to play them. Successfully completing a Storied Tale will add it to the West Rohan Reflecting Pool at Dunharrow.</rgb>'I remember the defence of Helm's Dike. This is how it was...''I remember the defence of the Deeping Wall. This is how it was...''I remember the defence of the Deeping-coomb. This is how it was...''I remember the defence of the Glittering Caves. This is how it was...''I remember the defence of the Hornburg. This is how it was...''My family and I will never forget how you helped us during the long night of Isengard's attack, ${PLAYER}! We are forever grateful to you, as is all of Rohan!

