You have placed bait on all of Dírion's traps and should now return to him.Talk to Dírion'So am I to feign terror simply because you bring Malthellam's word to us?

'There is no need for us to travel north, much less remain confined to Alagrant. We are hardy folk, and familiar with the dangers of these lands. I wish to continue my daily hunting, but if that is not to be the case, I expect something from you in return.

'Could one as mighty as you stoop to baiting my traps outside town? Given how dangerous the vale is said to be now, surely you must be the only one among us up to the task.''Ah, you are back so soon.

'It was that trying a task? You must tell me more of your adventures in placing bait on traps. Actually, no... I would rather you did not. 

'Here, take these. Assuming the bait works, I can spare these coins.'After travelling through the Paths of the Dead, you have arrived in Gondor at long last. With war looming on the horizon, your skill shall once again be tested.Morlad can be found to the south and slightly west of the Paths of the Dead in Blackroot Vale.

Ludhír has asked you to travel to Morlad, the chief settlement in the Blackroot Vale, and speak with the steward.Follow the river Blackroot south to MorladMalthellam can be found in Morlad, to the south-west of the Paths of the Dead.

Ludhír has asked that you meet with Malthellam, the steward of the Vale. Gondor's armies have ridden east and many troubles face the people that remain.Talk to Malthellam in Morlad'How did you come to be here? I must be mistaken, but I am certain I saw you come from those haunted paths under the mountain.

'If that is true and you are as mighty as you appear, the steward will want to speak with you. We are in need of hardy folk, especially now that Lord Duinhir has ridden east.

'Follow the river Blackroot to the south, and you shall find a settlement called Morlad upon a hill to the west. There you shall find Malthellam, our steward.''I thought naught but death itself would ever wander forth from those wretched paths... I now see my folly.

'Tell me, stranger, what has brought you to Gondor?'Reduced to a small group of guards as the war intensifies, the archers of Morlad work to combat the forces encroaching on the vale.Arrows can be found littering the ground and the corpses of slain Orcs outside Morlad.

Uidor has asked you to retrieve arrows so that the guards of Morlad might conserve their dwindling resources.Collect arrows from the fields outside Morlad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Uidor can be found near the entrance to Morlad in north-west Blackroot Vale.

You have recovered many arrows from the fields of Blackroot Vale and should now return them to Uidor.'Hail! ${PLAYER}, is it?

'I and the archers of Morlad have been spending more and more time holding the Blackroot from the Orcs. They stage raids from Tingobel and have grown so bold as to approach Morlad. I assure you, none of them shall get past us. You see, the archers of the vale are known throughout Gondor for their skill with the bow.

'However, we have fewer and fewer arrows each day, so I would ask that you travel into the field and return some to us. I promise that if the Orcs should return while you are away, we shall not pierce you with our arrows.''Ah, these shall do nicely. You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.

'I told you we wouldn't hit you!'Heartened by your arrival in Gondor, Belegant suggests that you speak to the people of Morlad in hopes of raising their spirits.Rodaglar can be found to the north of the entrance to Morlad.

