You should question Fuirion about his wounds.Question Fuirion about his attack'I will hasten to Gladion's home at once, dear. Follow me, please! I might need your aid when I arrive, depending on his condition.'Limril, white as a ghost, does not speak. Her eyes are fixed on her brother-in-law, alarmed and concerned.'This is a peaceful town. How could he have gotten so injured?''Come, come! Let us make haste!''A nasty wound, this. He won't seem to say a word. You should ask his family if he's said anything to them, and I will have a look at Fuirion's wound.''He has not spoken a word, save what he said to you. It is unlike him. What could have happened? Why will he not speak?''My brother! How could he have sustained such a wound, ${PLAYER}? We are but peaceful farmers here....''My uncle Fuirion has been strange lately. I do not understand. Why is he bleeding?

'Is this because of his adventure? I saw him leaving town this morning, and he said he was going on an adventure, but would be back for dinner. He wasn't supposed to get hurt!

'He told me not to tell anyone about that....''My uncle is hurt badly, isn't he? I don't like it.

'He has been very sad lately. I don't think anyone notices, but I do, because he never wants to play or read with me anymore. He does not eat as much as a farmer should. But nobody notices but me.

'Do you think he will be all right?''Well, that doesn't give us any answers. But I have gained a little knowledge: this is a knife wound. A clean cut, easy to stitch up. It will take a little time.

'While I take care of Fuirion, would you be so good as to mind my chores at the shop? I was about to pull down the linens for bandages. Also, we are always needing more Kingsfoil. It grows wild in these parts... a lovely plant, with great healing qualities.''You may leave those with me, dear. Fuirion is resting now, and should remain so for a fortnight at least. I stitched him up while you were out collecting goods for me.

'He did not speak a word the entire time I was there. I suppose he is just in shock from the attack. It will pass.

'Thank you for the supplies! I am tired after the excitement of this day. You saved me a good deal of work.'Limril stares intently at Fuirion, brows knit in concern.Fuirion, pale from blood loss, his face drawn with pain, does not speak when you approach him.Míreth hopes to share her most treasured belongings with Fuirion in order to cheer him up.Míreth's doll and book can be found in her bedroom. The flowers can be collected outside the house.

