'My doll cheers me up, so I think Fuirion must borrow her while he is in bed. And maybe you could pick some nice flowers for him, because everyone likes flowers when they're sick. And our favourite book, the one he used to read to me so often... it is open where he left off. Perhaps I could read to him this time!''Oh, yes! This will do nicely for my uncle. I am not allowed inside, says Mama. Will you bring these to Fuirion for me, and tell him I want him to get well soon?''That sweet girl. No, no more. I can see them no more. No more reading books, no more flowers. No dolls! Take them away. I cannot bear to look upon them. I will be gone soon, and they must learn to never think of me.'

