You have defeated Corsair raiders throughout Edhellond and collected a number of forgotten relics, and should bring them now to Lathlorn.'These Corsair raiders likely landed at the shore west of here, in Belfalas. I expect they have established a foothold in the old ruins on the coast. People say Elves once lived there, but that must have been a thousand years or more ago. No Elves have come near Calembel for as long as I have run my shop, at any rate.

'If you are of a mind to deal with these Corsairs, that would be the place to do it! And while you're at those ruins, if you happen to see any old remnants of the Elves, bring them back to me and I will pay you good coin for them. The Elves won't be needing them, after all.

'I have not travelled that way since I was a young man, but I remember an overlook with a good view of the ruins. That would be a good place to survey the situation, and you should go there first.''I have not travelled that way since I was a young man, but I remember an overlook with a good view of the ruins. That would be a good place to survey the situation, and you should go there first. Find it to the west, in Belfalas.''I have not travelled that way since I was a young man, but I remember an overlook with a good view of the ruins. That would be a good place to survey the situation, and you should go there first.''If you are a friend, you are welcome to share my watch. I would be pleased to have your company, for Men of Umbar have brought their ships to shore, and threaten Edhellond. My people have not inhabited the refuge for a thousand years, but we bear enough affection for places once dear that we cannot allow the raiders to remain.

'If their goal is plunder, they will be disappointed. The only relics that remain will be of historical value only. Any valuable artifacts or jewels were taken long ago.

'There are others of my people nearby. If you can defeat some of the raiders throughout Edhellond, I will bring you to them. Return hither with any relics you find, and I will be doubly-pleased, for I do have an interest in curiosities from my people's history.''If you are a friend, you are welcome to share my watch. You are doubly-welcome if you defeat Corsair raiders throughout Edhellond, and return to me with any relics you find!''It always warms the heart to meet a new friend in these dangerous days, ${PLAYER}. We do not have enough warriors to cast the Corsairs into the sea, but your efforts in the refuge have told them that even an abandoned refuge is never truly forgotten by the Elves.''Ah, you brought me some relics from that abandoned Elf refuge? Well, why delay? Let me see them!'

You remove the dusty shards from your pack, and Galengam looks puzzled.

'This is it? These dirty old fragments? I expected jewels, or gems, or fine weaponry! I suppose all of those have already been taken. Thank you for trying, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot pay for any of these pieces. No one would have any interest in purchasing them!'Lathlorn has told you how to find the location from which the Avorrim keep watch over Edhellond.The Cave of the Avorrim is located in a cliff-wall overlooking the sea, on the road to Dol Amroth. Lathlorn described it in this way:  'If you follow the road south-west on the way to Dol Amroth, you will come to a rocky cleft in the ground to your right. Follow it down to a cliff-side path over the water, and you will come to the entrance.'Find the entrance to the Cave of the Avorrim, overlooking the seaDorthaneth is within the Cave of the Avorrim, in Belfalas.Find Dorthaneth within the Cave of the AvorrimDorthaneth is within the Cave of the Avorrim, in Belfalas.

