You were unable to capture the stag due to its agility, but should report back to Dírion in Alagrant.Talk to DírionThe posted note advertises a bounty on a particularly elusive white stag, described as 'a powerful and brilliantly white stag whose speed is unmatched by any in the vale,' and invites all interested hunters to seek out Dírion in Alagrant for more information on the stag's last known whereabouts.'So, you seek to capture the white stag? A noble goal to be certain, but one that countless others have failed to achieve.

'You see, nature has not brought forth such a wondrous symbol of Gondor since the White Tree, and I can think of no better symbol to hearten the people of the vale. I would never ask you to harm such a beautiful beast, but perhaps you can capture it for the people of Morlad.

'I have heard such varying accounts of its whereabouts, but it was last seen far to the east and beyond the Stone. Good fortune and swift strides, ${PLAYER}... you shall need both!''It got away, didn't it?

'I assumed as much, ${PLAYER}, for none have been able to keep pace with it yet. Still, the fact that you have seen one in the vale heartens me.

'Do not fret, I shall track it myself now that I know its whereabouts.'Fearful of the grim alliance between the Dead and the invader from Tarlang's Crown, Gúrion asks you to seek Malthellam's counsel in confronting them.Malthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad.

Gúrion asks that you return to Malthellam in Morlad to warn him of the impending union between the Dead and the invader from Tarlang's Crown.Talk to Malthellam in MorladArchers can be found along the borders of Morlad in Blackroot Vale.

