You should return to Rhovendol.Bring your notes to Rhovendol'Hm? I am sorry, I was lost in thought. I am a poet, you see, and my mind often wanders amongst my yet unwritten verses.

'Today I think of Barían, the lady I love. She is oft in the Mason's Quarter, and fair as any maiden I've seen.

'They say that meditation upon certain lovely objects will help the words flow, and come to think of it, I do wish to write a poem for fair Barían. Here, have a spare journal. Go take notes for me, if you would, on lovely things in the Court of the Fount. The clear water so like her voice, or the blue canopies so like her eyes. Your notes will help me profess my admiration.''Let us see what you wrote there.'

You hand Rhovendol your thoughts on Barían.

