Boradan has asked you to look from the beacon to Edhellond.Boradan can be found on the beacon, Amon Lontir, just outside Ost Lontir.

You have looked upon Edhellond and should now speak to Boradan.Talk to Boradan'Thank you for allowing me another moment to speak with you, ${PLAYER}.

'There are things you must be made aware of if you seek to aid our people. To the west, Dol Amroth overlooks the bay... and a glorious city it is. Yet, we stand at the edge of ruin as Corsairs run rampant throughout our lands. I do not ask anything of you but to understand what is at stake.

'Look to Dol Amroth, and understand what could be lost if we fail to defend ourselves.''It is beautiful, is it not? Should the war turn against us, you can consider yourself fortunate to have looked upon it.

'Alas, it is not the only thing I wish you to see. To the north lies the ancient Elf-haven of Edhellond... and more importantly, those who would seek to claim our lands. It is one thing to tell you of this, but another to look upon it with your own eyes.

'Look to Edhellond, and see the ships that have claimed the harbour!''So now you see what troubles us so, ${PLAYER}....

'You see, this is no small raid by the Corsairs. The people of Belfalas face an invasion on our shores, and unless we can discover a means to defend ourselves with so many of our warriors gone to the east, I fear that our lands shall soon fall to the Enemy.'Captain Abedec is on a mission to have the heads of Jajax and yourself for your offences to the Corsairs.Jajax is in Abedec's Watch, the Corsair encampment in the ruins south of Dol Amroth.

