<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail on defeat.</rgb>Try to free Jajax from his bonds<rgb=#FF0000>Do not let Abedec defeat you</rgb>Jajax is in the large tent at Abedec's Watch in southern Belfalas.

You should speak with Jajax.Speak with JajaxLothíriel is in the Great Hall of the Prince in Dol Amroth.

You should speak with Lothíriel.Tell Lothíriel of all that transpired'He is coming, ${PLAYER}, he is coming! Do not tarry here any longer. He is coming for my head, and he will take yours too!'

Jajax seems afraid for the first time since you've known the bold and unusual Corsair. You should free him from his bonds at once, and make your escape.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail on defeat.</rgb>'We've done it, ${PLAYER}! The last captain has been defeated, and we are free to do as we will without being hunted.

'I suppose you'll go back to your silly heroic ways, and I'll go back to my mischief, but I will never forget the ${CLASS} who bested my men at drinking and avenged them in death.

'Go well, ${PLAYER}. May the seas take you gently to the shore on which you find your rest.'You tell Lothíriel of Jajax and your journey amongst the Corsairs, ending in the defeat of the cruelest captain of all.

'An incredible tale, ${PLAYER}! It sounds as if you have done much to aid us against the Corsairs of Umbar, though I do not think much of your choice of friends.

'I only hope that your efforts may keep us safe.'Gilanor of Ost Lontir seeks to assault the Corsair forces stationed at Edhellond, and has sent his scout, Dolvir, to learn more of their plots.Dolvir can be found on a hilltop to the east of Edhellond.

Gilanor has asked you to seek Dolvir outside Edhellond in hopes you can weaken the Corsairs' hold on the coast.Talk to Dolvir'We have weakened their forces near the beacon, we know their movements, and we know of their leadership... now is the time to strike at the heart of their force in Edhellond!

'While you aided me, I sent a scout named Dolvir to observe the Corsairs moored at the Elf-haven. Seek him out, and aid him in ridding the coast of Corsairs. I will not allow that Umbarian filth to lay any further claim to our lands.

'Go, ${PLAYER}! May we fight alongside one another before this war comes to an end!''Ah, you must be ${PLAYER}... Gilanor told me you would arrive soon.

'It will not take you long to see what peril faces Gondor down in the Elf-haven. The Corsairs have moored three ships full of men, and have pillaged Edhellond to nearly nothing.

'We must move quickly to save the history here, and even more quickly should we hope to quell the Corsair threat.'Lothíriel has heard reports of Corsair scouts who may have infiltrated the great city of Dol Amroth.The Corsairs have landed on a beach south-west of Dol Amroth.

Jajax has asked you to search for Abedec at the beach-side landing spot, while he searches some ruins to the south.Find the beach upon which the Corsairs have landedGood vantage points for searching for signs of Abedec can be found atop the watch-towers in Hashadîr, south-west of Dol Amroth.

You should climb the watch-towers on the beach and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for signs of Abedec.Jajax's meeting place is where the roads meet between the two Corsair encampments -- one leads from the south-west, from Hashadîr, and the other leads from the ruins to the south.

You should meet Jajax at the cross-roads.Meet Jajax at the cross-roadsJajax is likely somewhere in the ruins to the south of Dol Amroth.

You should search for Jajax, for he is probably in need of rescue.Search for Jajax in the ruins to the south'If we do not take out Abedec, he will not rest until we are both hunted down and beheaded, for that is his style. I always admired him for it, but not when it's my head on the line.

