You should speak with Laegened.Speak with LaegenedBarían can be found in the Mason's Quarter in Dol Amroth.

You should tell Barían the good news.Speak with BaríanRhovendol is in the Scholar's Quarter of Dol Amroth.

You should tell Rhovendol that Barían is not interested in him.Tell Rhovendol that Barían has no interest in him'Here, I did away with your odd notes and composed a poem of better taste, more suited to woo a lovely young lady such as Barían.

'Bring this to her, if you please. I know she will not be able to resist my sweet words. Do tell her where to find me when you're done, please.''I am sorry, but I'm busy. I am trying to get Master Laegened's attention.'

You apologetically hand Barían the poem written for her, and she reads it with a scowl.

'I don't have time for this nonsense. I'm trying to get an apprenticeship, but Master Laegened won't even see me. He says he has too many worthless apprentices already. I want to show him my work, but I cannot haul it up the stairs!

'My work is down in the Scholar's Quarter. If only I could lift it!''What is this you have brought me? Ah, that girl Barían who comes to me every day, did her father do this? He was a great stone-mason.'

You explain that this is Barían's own work, and Laegened stares at you incredulously.

'I confess that I had no idea she was so advanced in her artistry. I have never had a young lady as an apprentice before, but I can see that she has what it takes. She may even become a master someday.''He has accepted me as an apprentice!? This is wonderful, ${PLAYER}, truly wonderful. I cannot wait to start!

'Thank you so much for your help. I did not know if he would even like the stone, but getting it to him has been such a great hassle.''What do you mean, not interested? You mean she would rather dirty herself with rocks and dust than accept my courtship? I do not understand.'

