Polla has asked you to introduce yourself to the band before taking over Góthrik's duties.Talk to Gord DunleyTalk to Robbo GristbackTalk to DaenarTalk to FrókiTalk to HollurPolla Stoutley can be found just outside the Stone Theatre in Minas Tirith.

You have introduced yourself to the Cloudyheads and should now return to Polla.Talk to Polla Stoutley'Hallo, traveller!

'Are you an admirer of music? My band, the Cloudyheads, has travelled about from the Shire to Bree to the Trollshaws to Rohan and now to Gondor! We've come to Minas Tirith to perform in its grand theatres and we're almost ready!

'Yet... in a manner of speaking, we are a bit stuck at the moment.

'The Stone Theatre is a lovely place and one I'd much like to show my family back home, but the workers within are far too noisy! We tried to practice earlier and they made such a ruckus that we had to leave!

'They seem like fine, diligent Men, but what good is a theatre if it cannot be used by musicians?

'If you would convince them to shirk their duties, even for an hour or two, I would be most grateful!''Oh, thank you! Those workers were being much too noisy when we tried practicing in the theatre earlier.

'If we are to perform in the Stone Theatre soon, everything must be in order. Sweeping and hammering have no place in a hall of music!

'I know it was a simple task to ask of one as travelled as you, but we are in quite the pickle, you see. Our stagehand, Góthrik, has been... lacking in his duties as of late. He has spent more of each recent day huddled in local taverns than he has with the band.

'If you would search the taverns for him, starting in the Wheel and Cask nearby, please tell him his help is sorely needed!''What - what do you want?'

Góthrik is clearly enjoying his time at the Wheel and Cask, but you inform him of Polla's request to return.

'Ho ho! I do not think so, ${RACE}... I have had enough of their demands, and not nearly my fill of these fine draughts. This is war-time - there are barely enough people to mount even a meagre showing! I don't know what Polla is on about!

'If these are to be my final days, am I to spend them lugging around instruments and picking up after Gord and the others? Nay, I am finished with them. Tell her that I quit!

'You are welcome to take my place, but do not say I didn't warn you.''He quits?! He can't quit!

'This will not do at all, ${PLAYER}. We cannot manage our performances without a stagehand - it is simply not possible!

'What do you think of Góthrik's offer to join us? He seems to have painted us in a rather grim light, but I assure you, we are good folk!

'If you are uncertain, why don't you speak to the others first and introduce yourself?''Polla sent you to talk to me?

'I am glad to meet you, but as you can see, I am busy at the moment.'

Gord nods downward at the crowd of women gathered before him.

'Góthrik has quit, eh? It's just as well. You'll do fine in his stead. Now then, shouldn't you be off meeting the others? 

'Sorry for the interruption, ladies.''Hallo there! I am Robbo Gristback, but you may call me Robbo.

'I'm a practised lutenist and one of the two founders of the Cloudyheads along with my dear friend, Polla.

'Am I to understand that Góthrik has abandoned his position in the band? A shame... I'd rather grown to like having so many dwarves around. They remind me of home, as strange as that might sound.

'In the meantime, I hope you consider Polla's offer. I'd be glad to have you around as we ready ourselves for our biggest show yet!'Daenar watches as you approach, but gives no reply as you introduce yourself. She merely smiles, and returns to walking about the garden.'Ah, hello, ${PLAYER}! Polla has been talking to me about you since you first arrived, and I haven't seen her this excited in some time. For my part, I am glad to finally have a word with you!

'Truth be told, we are all a tad anxious to perform. We came to the city just before the battle intensified, and now it seems we are trapped in here with the folk of Gondor. We only came to perform a show, and if it could be our last, I would prefer it to be our finest.

'Góthrik is a fine dwarf, and I am disappointed that our paths are no longer aligned. Perhaps the fate of Gondor weighs too heavily on him...

'We could all use a bit more joy in such times. If you would join us, perhaps it might lift the gloom hanging over the City.'Hollur is playing a drum as you approach, but does not stop as you begin to introduce yourself. Instead, he simply talks over it as he introduces himself in turn.

'Ho there, ${PLAYER}! I did hear your name correctly, didn't I? It is nice to meet you, and even nicer for you to take up Góthrik's duties in his absence.

'Oh, you haven't accepted yet? Hah! I must be getting ahead of myself!

'Robbo and I are busy practicing a little tune of ours, so I'll get back to it now if you don't mind. If you haven't met Robbo, make certain you introduce yourself to him. He's a fine hobbit, he is.''I hope the others gave you a warm welcome, ${PLAYER}! Don't mind Daenar - she's a bit of an odd one, if I might say so.

'You seem like a fine ${RACE}. Robbo and I have come a long way from the Shire and met many friends along the way - I would be glad to count you among them.

'If you'd like to join the Cloudyheads, you need only say the word and we can get to work!'Angmar claims the central keep of the Ettenmoors, but the main army has yet to receive the news. The War-tyrant has ordered his soldiers to collect the materials needed to set a beacon fire.Head south from Tol Ascarnen into Hithlad to seek out the wood needed to build the signal fires to the south.

Though your forces took Tol Ascarnen, the keep is woefully undefended, and Kaasak has ordered you to build a pyre to call in reinforcements from the south. You should make your way into the Ettenmoors and search for kindling, timber, and larger logs to build a beacon fire large enough to call in reinforcements to Tol Ascarnen.'There is no rest for the wicked, ${PLAYER}. There is much yet to do...mainly getting forces here to stand against the enemy.

'Our troops are scattered throughout the wilds of the Ettenmoors, and we must make them aware of our victory. We can do this by setting a large beacon fire.

'Make your way through the Ettenmoors and gather the wood need to make this pyre, then return to me so we can light the fires to call our war-host home.''Yes, this will do nicely. If only there were more like you within our ranks, ${PLAYER}. The speed at which these slugs move is abominable.'Angmar claims the central keep of the Ettenmoors, but the main army has yet to receive the news. The War-tyrant has ordered his soldiers to collect the materials needed to set a large beacon fire.Head south of Tol Ascarnen into Hithlad and the Grimwood forest to collect the wood needed to build the blaze.

Though your forces took Tol Ascarnen, the keep is woefully undefended, and Kaasak has ordered you to build a pyre to call in reinforcements from the west. You should make your way into the Ettenmoors and search for kindling, timber, and larger logs to build a beacon fire large enough to call in reinforcements to Tol Ascarnen.'There is no rest for the wicked, ${PLAYER}. There is much yet to do.....mainly getting forces here to stand against the enemy.

'We need a fire so big that Lugbúrz will take notice! Ha! On the western parapet, we will build a massive beacon and call our reinforcements!

'Get your brethren together and bring us the wood we need to build that pyre. Go now, maggot!''We will build a fire and they will come. The western bridge will be safe! Best you think on this in the future, whelp. We might often have need of this type of defensive service.

'Best to be prepared, no?'Paashum is trying to make his superiors in Angmar's army notice him. To that end he has asked you to undertake a mission involving great risk but a potential for great success.Make your way to the copse of trees in the woods on the western side of Tol Ascarnen. Make your presence know there.

Paashum asked you to make your way into the small section of woods on the western shore of Hoardale near Tol Ascarnen. He hopes to send a force into the keep after setting the woods ablaze. You will need to be obvious enough to attract the enemy's attention.Stand in the open among the trees near Tol Ascarnen's western wall'${PLAYER}, I have worked with you before, and though I must continue to berate you in front of others, I believe you have earned my favour.

'I wish to assist Uzulthrang in his quest to recover Tol Ascarnen, and to that end, I would ask that you undertake a very dangerous mission for me. I have an archer who will fire a blazing arrow into the trees when you arrive within them. When this is done, a force will cross the bridge to battle into the keep.

'My only fear is that the foe is strong in those woods. This could mean your defeat.'Now that Erchar and his men are properly armed, he sends you to find Herion and aid him so that they may both return to Linhir together.Herion's encampment is located somewhere south of Erchar's encampment, along the River Ernilos.

