'Until next time, ${PLAYER}. May your adventures be profitable my friend!'Captain-General Makan wishes to strengthen the defences of Tol Ascarnen by building a terrible weapon to wield against those attacking the fortress.Iron ore can be found in the Isendeep Mine to the north, in Arador's End, or from the goblins of Grothum to the north-east of Tol Ascarnen.

Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr at Tol Ascarnen is working to forge an iron cauldron to fill with oil to be used against the forces of Angmar as they try to retake the keep from the Free Peoples. He has asked you to help collect the iron ore needed to forge the cauldron.'This is war, friend, and in war you make choices that you might regret when all is done. Yet, if we do not make these difficult decisions, then there may be no tomorrow for regret. It is a terrible and confusing situation sometimes, but I follow my orders, and they are clear.

'I am to charge you with collecting iron ore from the Isendeep or those wretched goblins which make Grothum their home. Either way, the iron is to be used to craft a giant cauldron. We will fill the cauldron with oil and boil it to douse Angmar's forces when they assail the fortress.

'A terrible fate for certain, but no different than they shall do to us. The ore can be found in the Isendeep Mine to the north or from the goblins of Grothum in the north-east. Go quickly, friend, for we must prepare our defence.''This ore will do nicely, ${PLAYER}. With enough of this, I will forge a sturdy iron cauldron, which we can use to douse our enemies.'Easterling riders lurking close to the Rammas in Talath Anor worry Ingold, for their purpose is unknown.Easterling riders can be found in southern Talath Anor.

You should defeat Easterling riders.Defeat Sûhalar riders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ingold can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas.

You should speak with Ingold.Speak with Ingold'Could the Sûhalar axe-men know about the Rohirrim? If this is true, what accursed magic gives them this tactical advantage?

'Perhaps I am thinking too much, but I cannot devise another reason as to why the Sûhalar would be patrolling the fields north of here.

'We must do something about this!''I suppose I can worry less thanks to your efforts. Still, the tide of enemies advances. We must remain strong and protect the White City at all costs.'Borhador hears a loud noise outside and wants you to investigate as he fears a cave troll has come for him.Borhador can be found in his hall above Ethring village.

Borhador asks you to investigate a sound he heard.Speak to BorhadorBorhador can be found in his hall above Ethring village.

You should speak with Borhador.Speak with BorhadorLaerind can be found in Ethring village.

You should speak with Laerind.Speak with Laerind'You there, did you hear the noise? It was a thunderous pounding coming from outside!''Protect me!''I have seen something that made me remember how I felt in my younger years. It took my people risking their lives for me to realize this. Yes, I miss my wife Halwen and my son Dervorin greatly. I must lead this Vale again so that my son will have a place to come home to. What is the difference between losing your home and death, I ask you that?

'Please take my word to Laerind and let her know that I am deeply sorry for my reclusiveness and I cherish all that she and Arvaethor have done of late for the Vale. I bestow Laerind and Arvaethor with command over the Vale until Dervorin returns to take over my reign. Now I must rest to regain my strength for the coming days.''I know that deep down the Lord of the Vale's sadness stems from how much he cares for his land and misses his wife Halwen. It is a burden. Arvaethor and I shall continue leading while Borhador regains his strength.

'I thank you, ${PLAYER}, for all that you've done. I hope that you will stay in the Vale longer and continue assisting our efforts.'Talfadan refuses to leave his farm until after his grazing sheep are brought back so that he may lead them to safety.Sheep can be found grazing in the south-western corner of Pelennor Fields.

You should find and return the sheep to Talfadan.Find the area where the sheep are grazing in PelennorSheep and Morgul Scouts can be found grazing in the south-western corner of Pelennor Fields.

You should find and return the sheep to Talfadan as well as defeat the Morgul Scouts.Herd grazing sheep back to the farm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Morgul scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talfadan is at Pel Dúven.

You should speak with Talfadan.Speak with TalfadanTurgon can be found at the South-gate of the Rammas.

You should speak with Turgon.Speak with Turgon'All right, I hate to say this but you've convinced me that I should head over to the White City. There's one last thing that needs to be done though.

'My sheep are out grazing and I can't leave them here. I would never forgive myself if some ruffians got to them!

'Will you go get my sheep and bring them back to the farm so that I may herd them to City?''It's about time! I might have been able to do that faster myself and on these old legs!

'Eh, you've got spirit though, that's for sure. Heh heh! I'll be on my way to the White City then, young one.''${PLAYER}, that sounds like quite the endeavour to get that one man to safety. I'm sorry to put you through that trial.

'Well, now that Pelennor is clear of men, we can turn our attention to the offensive.'Drawn to Tarlang's Crown by Azruthor, the Ruthless Dead continue to strike fear into the enemies of the Heirs of Castamir.The Dead can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown.

You have encountered the Dead and should defeat them to free the Crown of their terror.Defeat the Dead in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many Dead in Tarlang's Crown.CompletedWhile battling against the forces in Tarlang's Crown, you have encountered the Ruthless Dead. Rallied to the side of the Dark Lord by Azruthor, an Heir of Castamir, these cursed Men strike fear into the hearts of any that look upon them.

Although they may never be brought to rest, they must be banished from the Crown back into their darkened paths under the mountain.You have defeated many of the Dead in Tarlang's Crown. They may never truly find rest under the Heirs of Castamir, but you have done well to purge the Crown of their frightful forms.Taskmaster Gukthor admits hating the taste of gruel, but has found that the seeds the rat-folk use to grow their leaf adds a nice bite to the mash he uses in his gruel. He has asked that you collect ten seeds for the evening meal.The rat-folk living south of Dâr-gazag along the river grow a plant that can be crushed to make a tasty spice.

Taskmaster Gukthor waits for you to return with the brittle-leaf seeds.'Ar, ${RACE}. You can find a way to carry something back to me, I'm certain. It's a little task, hardly worth mention, I will admit, but then again so is feeding a bunch of thankless maggots like you!

'The rat-folk in the south grow a strange leaf. The leaf tastes terrible and more often than not the rat-folk burn it after drying it out, strange little blighters. But the seeds can be ground up and used as a fairly tasty addition to gruel.

'If you can gather up a bundle of the seeds, I would be very grateful.''These will do nicely and make the gruel taste more bland and less terrible!'The Corsairs of Tarlang's Crown wield many weapons against the people of Gondor, but without them, their forces would be greatly weakened.Corsairs can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown.Collect weapons from corsairsCorsair raiders' swords, corsair look-outs' bows, and corsair hound-masters' clubs can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown.

You have encountered well-armed corsairs in Tarlang's Crown and should claim their weaponry lest another corsair raise arms against Gondor.Collect swords from corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect bows from corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect clubs from corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Harnion can be found alongside the road in Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond.

