Talk to Bereneth and see what she wishes to do next.Talk to BerenethThe Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.

Meet Bereneth back at the Old Guest-house.Meet Bereneth back at the Old Guest-house'If you please, ${CLASS}... I heard tell of what you did for Bergil and you see, the thing is... well, my father went out to fight when they rode to get Lord Faramir.

'And, well, he took a wound out there and is in the Houses of Healing now and I haven't been to see him and I should like ever so much to do that but I dare not go in all alone and it is just that I was hoping - I was hoping you might go in with me, if you would.''Oh good, ${PLAYER}, you are here. My heart felt like butterflies. My stomach felt like butterflies. My head felt like butterflies!

'You see, I was only told that Father was hurt, but I do not know how bad and I am afraid to see. And also the Healer, Delion is his name, is tall and grave and I am afraid of him as well.

'Still, now that you are here, I shall try to be brave. Father is brave and so are you, and I shall try to be as well.''I will try to be brave, if that is what I must do to see Father.''Bereneth, is it you? You have come. Or do I dream once more?'

A nearly silent choking fit overtakes the wounded soldier.

'No, I dream not. Bereneth, it is you. And this good ${RACE} has brought you to me? No thanks...'

Another coughing fit overtakes him.

'...no thanks can suffice.''What is wrong with him? Is he dying? Oh, ${PLAYER}, what should we do?''Is he dying, ${PLAYER}? What should we do?''I am right here, daughter, and I have not gone deaf. I need only a little water. Will you bring me that cup there, ${PLAYER}, if that is your name? I fear it is beyond my grasp.''I tremble just thinking of that man. How could I ever go up to him and say - no, you will have to do it, ${PLAYER}!''Find Delion, if you can, and tell him I need attending some time before the next meal.''Have you brought the salve? You have not. You are empty-handed and I do not know who you are. Why is this little girl in my ward? There are wounded men lying about.'

You explain that Araslant needs the healer's help.

'His poultices might be nine days old and still there would be others in greater need of my aid here. I am but one man, though a healer trained and called, and these men, their wounds, I...'

The healer stares wide-eyed at his own hands.

'If you want my help, then help me. Go about and see what aid you can lend. I am healer, hosteller, and hand-holder all in one, and it is too much.''Do not worry for me, ${PLAYER}. A man's wound does not frighten me half as much as that Delion.''I don't see what was so hard or lengthy about that!''What? You're still here? You mean you actually attended to the men? I hardly expected - please tell me you did not have that girl at your elbow the whole time.

'Well, perhaps I shall have time to attend to Araslant. I would have got to him sooner or later, anyway. I am up to my elbows, not my eyebrows!

'Now leave me to my work, or you'll use up the time you have saved me. Shoo!''Yes, let's leave him and go back to Father. We have good news and how I would like to make him smile!''Let us go back to Father, ${PLAYER}.''Oh, but I do not want to go away and leave him now! What if I have to come back alone? What if he, if he...

'Can we stay a little longer, ${PLAYER}? Please? I know, why don't we stroll about the tier, like you did with Bergil? Only it's so much prettier up here. Then we'll come back, and Father will be awake, and I will speak to him again before I go.

'First, let us visit the Greensward. It is just outside!''We will just walk about a bit, and when we return, Father will have woken. First, I think, the Greensward.''I know, let's pick some flowers. Surely, nobody will mind!''We'll have a bouquet of them, and we'll bring them to Father!''There, I made a bouquet of them. Isn't it pretty? Say, do you think it's true what they say about Mithrandir's steed, that he can talk and play the harp, and that his mane is true silver threads?

'Well, he is here in the High Stables, or so I have heard. Let us go and see for ourselves, if we can!''Let us see if Mithrandir's steed truly is in the High Stables.''Do you think… do you think we might feed him an apple?''Do you think… do you think we might feed him an apple?''Oh, you feed it to him. I wouldn't dare!'Shadowfax accepts the apple with gentle dignity.'Oh, how regal he is!

'His mane is more like silk than silver, and he has not spoken, at least to us. But see his eyes, ${PLAYER}, see how wise they look. Do you think he understands? I think he does.'

Bereneth takes a deep breath.

'I think we should go back to Father now.''Yes, I think it is time to see if Father is awake.''There you are, Bereneth. How good to see your face. And what do you have there? Flowers? Let me smell them. Mmm... ah.

'Delion has just come and gone, and I am much refreshed, though he interrupted my slumber and I think soon I will need to sleep again.

'Listen, there is one more thing I want you to do for me today. There are other men who are wounded worse than me, and who do not have brave daughters with big hearts to bring them flowers. Will you go about the ward and bring each of them some of the flowers you picked? That's my girl.''Try to understand what I ask, Bereneth. I prize these flowers you picked more than gold and that is the very reason why I would give it to my brothers in arms.''If it is Father's wish, let us give out these flowers to the other wounded men.''I saw to Araslant. Now there are others who need me more. Off with you and out of my ward.''A little maid, handing me a flower? Surely I am dreaming, but at least I dream no more of Orcs and mud and slashing swords.''Is this for me? And here I thought I was all but forgotten.''I thank you, little one. My own daughters are far away, in Tumladen. You make my heart sore for the sight of them.'The man takes the flower with a grave and sorrowful face, holds it to his nose, and nods.'Oh, thank you. Thank you.''Why, what a lovely flower. When I wake to its fragrance, I shall think I am in Lossarnach and these are not times of war.''We've given out the flowers. Now we should return to father.''You have given the flowers out? This kindness is a finer gift than any flowers.

'Bereneth, I would hold your hand until the end of days, but I must sleep and Delion might cuff you on the ears if he finds you here again. Will you visit me tomorrow? Are you brave enough to come on your own? Good.'Bereneth wipes her face, concealing a tear.

'I will come tomorrow, and the next day, and the next day, and the next day, until he is all well again.

'Are those footsteps? Do you think the healer's coming? We'd better go!''There you are, ${PLAYER}. You may be very brave, but I can run back to the Old Guest-house faster than you! Do you think Father will be well enough to walk tomorrow? What do you think I should bring him? Not another flower. I wonder if Mithrandir's steed will be there when I return? Maybe I can pet his neck, if he'll let me.''Ah...'

Araslant takes a long, unsteady draught.

'That is better. Bereneth, do not tremble for I am not so poorly as I appear. The healer who attends to us here, Delion, is as severe as he is thoughtless.

'He starves me and then brings me two meals at once. I ask for water and he leaves it out of my grasp. If I did not know better, I might say the sight of true war-wounds has unnerved the man.

'If you would do one thing more for me, daughter and friend, go and find him now. The poultice on my wounds is long past changing, and I require some other respites from my discomfiture, but I fear there is not a bell in all Gondor I could ring loud enough to catch that man's ear.'Lord Angbor of Lamedon makes ready to travel through Upper Lebennin as he leads his host to Minas Tirith.Angbor's men can be found throughout the eastern half of Pelargir.

Angbor has asked you to rally his men in Pelargir before he sets out into Upper Lebennin.Angbor can be found by the eastern gate of Pelargir.

You have rallied many of Angbor's men and should now return to Angbor.'We can tarry no longer, my friend.

'Aragorn has bid us travel to Minas Tirith across the plains of Upper Lebennin and Lossarnach, and I shall not abandon him in this crucial hour. However, my men have grown weary and many have not found rest since our defeat of the Corsairs.

'I know well the pain they feel, but they must press on through it, as have all of Gondor's great warriors. Go to them, and sound this horn that they might find themselves renewed.

'When you have done so, return to me, for our journey is just beginning!''Thank you, ${PLAYER}.

'I know many of my men desire rest after our siege of Pelargir, but that time cannot come until this war is at an end.'Authest, the caretaker of Eilendoth, has asked you to investigate the source of the spider infestation and halt the inpouring of these creatures.Spiders infest the woods in the western part of Ringló Vale.

Stem the spider infestation in Ringló Vale.Defeat spiders in Ringló Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy spider webs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Investigate the source of the spider infestationThe Weft-mother can be found inside the spider infested cave.

You should defeat the Weft-mother.Defeat the Weft-motherThe beacon of Eilendoth is located south-west of Ethring in Ringló Vale.

You should speak with Authest.Speak with AuthestBorhador can be found in The Crossing-hall.

You should speak with Borhador.Speak with Borhador'Borhador tasked me with maintaining the beacon. It was peaceful work until the skies grew dark. Laerind sent a look-out up here to keep an eye on Ethring. The spiders got to him first. I would have been next had you not come when you did.

'These creatures came out of the woods to the west. I've not laid eyes upon such sizeable creatures before, and I've lived in Ringló all my days. Perhaps an adventurer such as yourself would be willing to search out the source of this insurgence. If I had to guess, I would say the darkened skies have something to do with it.''You say there was a strange dark stone inside a spider nest? Perhaps the stone is what drove the brood's mother to send her children out of the mountain's crevasses. Now that she is no longer a threat, I shall be safe up here as will the beacon. Return to Borhador and let him know that the beacon is safe, but do not mention the strange stone. His mind is plagued with worry. Another mysterious threat may sink him even lower.''Does the beacon glow brighter? This is the first good news I have been given in quite some time. I only ask, will this one light be enough to ward off the growing darkness?'Elaglar of Dol Amroth fears that the Corsair forces under Azruthor's rule in Tarlang's Crown will soon grow beyond control.Harnion can be found off the side of the road leading through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond.

Elaglar has asked you to seek Harnion in Tarlang's Crown and investigate the Corsair forces massing there.Talk to Harnion in Tarlang's Crown'A great threat rises to the north, ${PLAYER}....

'What I have heard of the forces in Tarlang's Crown has grown more and more unbelievable with each account. This much remains clear... we cannot allow the Corsairs or their leader in the Crown, Azruthor, to gain any more of a foothold in our lands.

'Once you have readied yourself and your allies, travel to Tarlang's Crown and find Harnion. He is a scout of mine and can guide you and your allies through our plans. I would prefer you keep this a quiet matter, for I do not wish to frighten the people.''Keep your voice down, traveller....

'The Corsairs have seized the road through Tarlang's Crown and foul things are afoot. We shall need more than you or I alone if we are to drive them out.'The leaders of the Haradrim forces in Upper Lebennin bear vile missives from the Enemy detailing their plans for Gondor.Haradrim war-leaders can be found along the banks of the Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.

Irodon has asked you to seek out any orders the Haradrim war-leaders might bear.Retrieve a missive from a Haradrim war-leader near the EruiThe letter can be found in your inventory.

You have discovered orders carried by one of the Haradrim war-leaders and should now read it.Read the missive to the HaradrimIrodon can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have uncovered the plans of the Haradrim in Upper Lebennin as well as Enemy's plans for Osgiliath. You should now return to Irodon in Halach.'Even after so many attacks, we still know little of the plans of the Haradrim aside from their slow advance across the Erui to the East.

'I have seen their captains, or however they are named among their people, bearing small missives during their assaults on Halach. I do not know if these are letters they have seized from settlements they have already razed or their orders from some unseen master, but I wish to know... for the good of all in Lebennin and beyond.

'You are a hale ${CLASS}, and can stand against the Haradrim! If you seek out their leaders near the banks of the Erui, you might be able to relieve them of these missives... and shed some light on their designs for Gondor.''These are grim tidings, ${PLAYER}...

'This missive fills me with dread, and I ask that you take it away from me. Do with it what you will, but remove it from my sight!

'The Lady must be told of this... I only hope she can send word to the Steward in time!'The Haradrim and Corsair forces have advanced northward in Dor-en-Ernil and now pose a great threat to the people of Gondor.Lang Boha can be found far to the west of Linhir in Dor-en-Ernil.

Herion has asked you to weaken the forces at Lang Boha to keep them from advancing to the north.Defeat Corsairs and Haradrim at Lang Boha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Half-trolls at Lang Boha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Herion can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have defeated many of the Corsairs and Haradrim in Lang Boha and should report your success to Herion.Talk to Herion in Linhir'Far to the west, the Enemy holds a camp on our beaches. We cannot allow this intrusion to stand!

'Each day, they work to gain more ground in Dor-en-Ernil and surely, it shall not be long until they breach the vale to the north.

'I would ask that you travel to their camp and weaken their forces as best you can. I do not expect one to stand against so many, but it is my hope that your assault will delay their advance another day.''You have done well to weaken them so, ${PLAYER}. Our work is not done, but your efforts shall delay them long enough for us to plan our next assault.'The Ettenmoors has several locations which allow for an advantage over the foe.The Grimwood Lumber-camp is west of Glân Vraig. Lugazag is west of Glân Vraig, on the west side of the Hoarwell. The Isendeep Mine is far to the north-west of Glân Vraig. Tol Ascarnen is south of the Isendeep Mine, north-west of Glân Vraig. Tírith Rhaw is east of Tol Ascarnen and north-west of Glân Vraig. Observe your map to see who currently controls the location. Red locations are held by the Enemy, and blue by the Free Peoples.

Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn explained that the contested locales throughout the Ettenmoors hold some manner of importance to the Free Peoples and the forces of Angmar and suggested that you visit each.Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn is at Glân Vraig within the Coldfells.

You have found your way through the Ettenmoors and located the Grimwood Lumber-camp, Lugazag Tower, Isendeep Mine, Tol Ascarnen and Tírith Rhaw. Now you should return to Glân Vraig and speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn.Talk to Ascwyn'You will face a great many foes here in the Ettenmoors: cunning sorceresses, dangerous Orcs and Uruks, blood-thirsty Wargs, and deadly spiders.

'They bear the brunt of their commanders' derision and still attack without care for their lives, continuously crashing against the walls of the strongholds throughout the Ettenmoors. You must use caution once you leave the safety of this fortress... and yet, you must learn the paths available to you in this wild place.

'You should strike out into the Ettenmoors and visit the locations which enhance our ability to fight on this front. In the south, deep in the Grimwood Forest, is the Grimwood Lumber-camp; once used by the hobbits in Hoarhallow, it is now a contested location with rich wood for constructing palisades. North of the lumber-camp, on the west side of the Hoarwell River, is Lugazag, a tower oft in the control of the Enemy. Deep in the hills at the base of the Misty Mountains in the lands called Arador's End, you will find the Isendeep Mine, where rich minerals and ore can be found. South from there, on an island in the centre of the Hoarwell, is Tol Ascarnen. The last location east from Tol Ascarnen and not far to the north and west of Glân Vraig is Tírith Rhaw. Make your way to these locations, and when you have visited them all, return to me. I will see that you are well rewarded.''Be cautious as you make your way through these lands. You will find support in smaller numbers as you venture further from our holdings here. Remember, the bears and eagles are our allies. They will assist you should you come under attack.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. Scouts reported that you visited each location. It is good to know that you were so diligent in accomplishing this task.

'We have need of people like you. As promised, I have a gift for you. You will find that many here are willing to part with these tokens in exchange for assistance. Quartermaster Ash, in the stonework gazebo to the east of my location will exchange these tokens for keys to the chests we have at Glân Vraig.

'These chests contain the odds and ends we find during the battles which occur throughout the Ettenmoors and are only a small piece of what we can offer you in exchange for your assistance. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. If you have a chance, speak with Captain-General Tordúr before heading back into the wild.'Herion decides to return to Linhir with Erchar who has waited for him.Herion can be found in his encampment in western Dor-en-Ernil.

Herion asks you to travel with him back to Linhir.Speak to HerionErchar can be found in the town of Linhir.

You have finished your journey from western Dor-en-Ernil to Linhir, and should now speak with Erchar.Speak with Erchar'The time has come to return to Linhir for Erchar and I. Come with us, ${PLAYER} and we shall all return victorious thanks to your deeds. Garvir will welcome us back with open arms. Together we can repair Linhir and defend it from the Corsairs.

'First, we must pay our respects to those who have fallen in battle during this noble protection of Dor-en-Ernil. Let me know when you are ready and we shall begin our journey.''Let us pay our respects before returning to Garvir in Linhir.''Though we do not always agree, my brothers and I must stick together. We are stronger as one than when we are apart.

'I thank you again for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. We could not have reunited without your help. If only my father Comeldir were alive. I could use his guidance in these dark times.'A letter that Landath was supposed to deliver got lost and turned up, worse for wear, in the Finding Place.Landath was supposed to deliver the letter three days ago. He is so upset he has asked you to examine the letter.Inspect the letterLandath stands in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.

Tell Landath that the letter isn't in terrible shape.Talk to LandathThe Clothiers' Fellow-hall is in the Third Circle, just south of the Pier.

Landath feels the letter can still be delivered if the seal is re-made. This can be done with Master Habdir's seal, found in the Clothiers' Fellow-hall.Find Habdir's wax and sealLandath stands in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.

Show Landath that the letter has been re-sealed.Return to LandathMaster Aglarang should be at the Smiths' Fellow-hall, in the northern part of the Third Circle. If you should get separated from Landath, use Bergil's whistle to call him back.

The letter should be delivered to a smith named Rhofin. Find Master Aglarang and ask him where Rhofin can be found.Talk to Master AglarangThe Smiths' Market lies just north of the Pier, the Court of Eärnil lies south of the Pier, and the Merry Swan lies on the far south of the Third Circle. If you should get separated from Landath, use Bergil's whistle to call him back.

Ask around the Third Circle for the whereabouts of Rhofin the Smith.Inquire at the Merry SwanInquire at the Smiths' MarketInquire at the Court of EärnilLandath has come along with you on the errand. If you should get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call him back.

You have asked after Rhofin in the three locations. See what Landath has to say about it.Talk to LandathThe Forges of Cirion are in the northern stretch of the Third Circle. If you should get separated from Landath, use Bergil's whistle to call him back.

Based on the people who had seen Rhofin today, Landath believes he will be working in the Forges of Cirion.Landath has come along with you on the errand. If you should get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call him back.

