Talk to Landath now that the buckle has been safely delivered.The Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.

Meet Landath back at the Old Guest-house.Meet Landath back at the Old Guest-house'What am I to do? I should have delivered that letter three days past! I couldn't say if your finding it was a blessing or a curse! Either way, I fear my goose is cooked.

'Oh, I cannot bear to even look at it. Will you?'

Landath holds out the crumpled letter.'Just look and tell me if the letter is entirely ruined.''Is it not ruined beyond reading? Let me look.'

Landath apprehensively peers at the letter.

'Oh, by the White Tree, there is hope. But we can't deliver it with a broken seal. Would you - could you?'

Landath hesitates.

'If it is not too much to ask, do you think you might go into the Clothiers' Fellow-hall, find Master Hadbir's things, and reseal the letter with them?''You'll need Master Habdir's wax and seal. I'm sure they're in the Clothiers' Fellow-hall... somewhere!''It will take forever to search the whole Third Circle for Rhofin. We should find Master Aglarang, and see if he knows where he is.''A message for Rhofin, you say? I saw him this morning, but that won't do you much good. Given the hour, he might be at the Smiths' Market, or maybe the Merry Swan, or even out upon the Court of Eärnil, despite these darkling skies.

'Ask about those places and you'll find him, like as not.''Well, we've got a start, haven't we? Ask about in the Merry Swan, Smiths' Market, and… what was it, Court of Eärnil?''Rhofin? Aye, he was in here. Said he was going to do some work after his meal.''Oh yes, Rhofin. He stopped to wish me health, as he often does, and showed the hammer he'd just bought. Broke his old one on the anvil, it seems.''I did see Rhofin, though it was earlier. Let me see... I do recall he mentioned he would neither be taking commissions nor selling his goods today.''Why - why you've done it! But I'm not out of this scrape quite yet, ${PLAYER}. The letter's still got to be delivered. Will you come with me? I'm feeling, well, faint of heart.

'It's supposed to go to a smith named Rhofin, but I've no notion where to find him. We should probably start by asking old Aglarang, the Master Smith. That's up in the Third Circle of course.''We haven't found Rhofin, but we have learned a thing or two. Let's see, now. He's gone to work, but he's not taking any commissions nor delivering them. And he's bought a hammer.

'Why that's it! He must be in the Forges of Cirion. Let's go see if I'm right.''Never mind that we seem to have found him. I won't breathe my sigh of relief until this errand's seen to the very end.''Well, hello there, ${RACE} and young master! What is this here?'

He takes the letter and furrows his brow as he reads it.

'A buckle for Lord Forlong's armour? Broke it putting it on, did he? Ah ha ha ha! And as he's a lord, it must be a fine-filigreed buckle, musn't it? Rhofin's the man for such a job. Now you'll have to give me a moment, but I promise, it won't take long.''It makes me anxious, watching him work. What if something goes wrong? Let us walk around the forge and see some of the other smithing. It's a marvel to see, is it not?''Look at how their hammers fall!''It won't be long. Just you wait.''It won't be long. Just you wait.''Do you think he's done? Yes, I think maybe he is. Let's go over and see.''He might be done with the buckle. Let us go and see.''There you are, then. If it is not boasting to say so, I think this will please old Lord Forlong quite well. Now run along and bring that to Master Habdir. He's still got to work that into the strap!''Here comes the last trial, ${PLAYER}. We have done it, but we are over three days late! What do you think Habdir will say when we deliver the clasp?''Go on. Take that buckle to Master Habdir.''What's this? Ah, the buckle. That took Rhofin a rather long time. Well, I imagine quite a few lords are dusting off their arms and armour and finding bits that need to be mended or replaced. Maybe even a few that were smaller round the waist, last time they garbed for war!''It is done! Let us get home, to the Old Guest-house. I dare say I'll feel safer then.''I have made many a delivery up and down the City, ${PLAYER}, and none has had me quaking in my boots as this one has. You are a good ${RACE}. Thank you for saving my hide.'Baranor thanked you for your help in Arnach and asked you to bear an important letter to Lady Vanyalos, in Imloth Melui.Lady Vanyalos can be found in her hall, located on a rise to the north-east of the entrance to Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach.

Baranor asked you to deliver a letter describing the attack on Arnach to Lady Vanyalos, who rules Imloth Melui while her husband Forlong is at war.'We must remember the dead, but not at the expense of the living. Arnach will not forget your name, ${PLAYER}, and neither will I!

'I have one last favour to ask of you, and it requires less in the way of valour but more in the way of haste. It is a service to both of us, for this letter to Lady Vanyalos speaks of all that has passed in Arnach, and therein your name is greatly praised. Will you bring it to her, and earn the privilege of her company? Her hall is on a rise in the north-east of Imloth Melui.

'Lady Vanyalos is the sister of Steward Denethor, and the rule of Imloth Melui has fallen to her while her husband Forlong is gone to war. She is a wise woman, and the knowledge of what befell in Arnach may help her prevent it in Imloth Melui.''Lady Vanyalos is the sister of Steward Denethor, and the rule of Imloth Melui has fallen to her while her husband Forlong is gone to war. She is a wise woman, and the knowledge of what befell in Arnach may help her prevent it in Imloth Melui.''Welcome to Imloth Melui, the Vale of Sweet Flowers. Breathe deeply of its fragrances, ${CLASS}, and be renewed. Sadly, I have grown too accustomed to the aroma for it to lift my spirits in these dark days, when I have need of it!'

Lady Vanyalos takes the letter from you and reads it carefully.

'I am pleased that you helped to repel the attack upon Arnach, and my heart goes out to the poor boys who fell in Gondor's name. The kingdom is more full of mourners than I have ever known it, ${PLAYER}.'Arodor has asked that you help the Council of Gondor inventory the supplies in the city in order to prepare for a long siege.Merethien, the Master Foodmonger of the Council, is in the Dome of the Sun.

Arodor told you that Merethien could use your assistance.Talk to Merethien, Master Foodmonger, in the Dome of the SunMirudal, the Warden of the Stores, is in the Dome of the Sun.

