You should defeat Orcs within the Harlond.Defeat Orcs within the Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Many Orcs await orders in the Harlond. You should defeat any Orcs in the port if Aragorn and his men are to make landfall with haste.'Aragorn will need the port of the Harlond cleared if he and his men are to make landfall with haste.Orkish siege engines can be found in the Harlond.

You should destroy these siege engines before the Rammas is toppled by the Orkish forces gathered in the Harlond.Destroy siege engines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The Morgul troops in the Harlond have constructed metal siege weapons. We must destroy these abominations before they tear down the Rammas!'Aragorn will need the port of Harlond cleared if he and his men are to make landfall with haste.Orc tents can be found around the port of Harlond.

You should destroy Orc tents in Harlond.Destroy Orc tents (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Orc encampments clutter Harlond. If we are to clear the port, we must destroy their camps. Burning their tents should send the Orcs a message to leave Harlond for good!'Aragorn will need the port of the Harlond cleared if he and his men are to make landfall with haste.Trolls can be found in the port of the Harlond.

You should defeat trolls within the port of the Harlond.Defeat trolls in the Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Many trolls await orders in the Harlond. You should defeat any trolls in the port if Aragorn and his men are to make landfall with haste.'Erchar informs you of a hamlet to the north that may be under siege. He has asked you to rescue any survivors.The hamlet of Tungobel can be found north-east of Erchar's encampment.

Rescue the townsfolk from the Corsair and Haradrim forces.Erchar can be found at his encampment in the western end of Dor-en-Ernil, south-west of Tungobel.

You should speak with Erchar.Speak with Erchar and inform him of your success'Not an hour ago, a band of Corsairs travelled past this camp-site. As luck would have it, we remained undetected.

'The enemy band was heading north-east towards Tungobel, a small hamlet. If it is not too late for the village, perhaps you would be able to rescue any townsfolk from a certain death. These people are wood cutters and fishermen, they are not warriors.''You sent the survivors to Ethring? Good work. I'm sure they will find temporary shelter there from the Corsair threat.'Hoping to find any means to slow the advance of the Ruthless Dead, Tancestel begs you to call upon the fabled Sister of the Gilrain.The mere can be found far to the north and slightly east of Linhir in Dor-en-Ernil.

Tancestel has asked you to bring his river-stone to the great mere along the Gilrain.Search for the mere on the GilrainThe pile of river-stones can be found at the edge of the mere along the Gilrain.

You have arrived at the mere on the Gilrain and should now place Tancestel's river-stone.Place Tancestel's river-stone on a pile of stonesThe mysterious woman can be found on the banks of the mere.

You have placed the stone, and now a mysterious woman has appeared. If what Tancestel said is true, you should honour her by kneeling before her.<rgb=#FF0000>Kneel</rgb> before the mysterious womanThe mysterious woman can be found on the banks of the mere.

You have honoured the mysterious woman and should now attempt to speak with her.Talk to the mysterious womanThe centre of the mere can be found in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

The mysterious woman has begun to walk into the centre of the mere. You should follow her.Follow the woman into the mereRoamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have been ferried to a beautiful glade by the mysterious woman, and should now speak to her.'Long ago, the people of Gondor spoke of five sisters... one that held sway over each of the rivers of Lebennin. Now, most people think them little more than a tale passed down from their forebears, but I assure you... they are as real as I am.

'Before you ask... no, they have not revealed themselves to us, but it has been said that they return to watch over us in times of strife. With war at our gates and the sky smothered in fumes and smoke, I can think of no more likely time for them to return.

'The faithful of my people pay tribute to the Sister of the Gilrain and we hold river-stones in her honour. Take my stone and travel to the mere along the Gilrain. Once you are there, lay it at the water's edge and let us hope our faith has not been misplaced... or the Dead will consume us all.'As you attempt to introduce yourself to the woman, she stands silent with the water lapping at her feet.

Her visage is that of an amused smile as she turns and beckons you into the mere.'You are a most interesting one, ${RACE}....

'I know why you have sought me, but the time has not yet come for that. This is no dream of yours, ${PLAYER}... I have ferried you here to speak far away from those that might wish to do you harm.

'You are not of this land and much still remains beyond your grasp....'A force out of Angmar threatens to press south into Eriador. A lone Elf has organized a band of defenders to stand against the army out of the north and dispatched emissaries to the Free Peoples in search of heroes willing to make a stand against Angmar's army.Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors.

Captain-General Lainedhel's emissaries are asking any would-be heroes to make their way into the Ettenmoors to bolster their small numbers. Many stable-masters have trained horses who can take you to the Ettenmoors. You should speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn upon your arrival there.'I speak for the Free Peoples of Eriador, friend. The Ettenmoors, a land corrupt and lost to evil for many years, is the staging ground for an invasion from the north. Angmar's forces muster beneath the shadow of Mount Gram and plan to launch an assault into the south.

'Captain-General Lainedhel headed north against his Lord's wishes and called a host to stand with him. Now a small, but able band of us stands against the onslaught, but we are outnumbered, and if not bolstered, we will succumb to the tide.

'If you are willing, I would ask you to make your way to Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors. Many of the stable-masters have assisted us and trained horses to find their way to the Ettenmoors. When you arrive, speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn.''I ask a request for the Free People of Eriador, friend. The Ettenmoors, a land corrupt and lost to evil for many years, is the staging ground for an invasion from the north. Angmar's forces muster beneath the shadow of Mount Gram and plan to launch an assault into the south.

'Captain-General Lainedhel headed north against his Lord's wishes and called a host to stand with him. Now a small but able band of us stands against the onslaught, but we are outnumbered and if not bolstered we will succumb to the tide. 

'If you are willing, I would ask you to make your way to the Ettenmoors. Many of the stable masters have assisted us and trained horses to find their way to the Ettenmoors. When you arrive, speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn; she is acclimating all new recruits to the defence.''I ask a request for the Free People of Eriador, friend. The Ettenmoors, a land corrupt and lost to evil for many years, is the staging ground for an invasion from the north. Angmar's forces muster beneath the shadow of Mount Gram and plan to launch an assault into the south.

'Captain-General Lainedhel headed north against his Lord's wishes and called a host to stand with him. Now a small but able band of us stands against the onslaught, but we are outnumbered and if not bolstered we will succumb to the tide. 

'If you are willing, I would ask you to make your way to the Ettenmoors. Many of the stable masters have assisted us and trained horses to find their way to the Ettenmoors. When you arrive, speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn; she is acclimating all new recruits to the defence.''I ask a request for the Free People of Eriador, friend. The Ettenmoors, a land corrupt and lost to evil for many years, is the staging ground for an invasion from the north. Angmar's forces muster beneath the shadow of Mount Gram and plan to launch an assault into the south.

'Captain-General Lainedhel headed north against his Lord's wishes and called a host to stand with him. Now a small but able band of us stands against the onslaught, but we are outnumbered and if not bolstered we will succumb to the tide. 

'If you are willing, I would ask you to make your way to the Ettenmoors. Many of the stable masters have assisted us and trained horses to find their way to the Ettenmoors. When you arrive, speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn; she is acclimating all new recruits to the defence.''Our emissaries have succeeded beyond our expectations. I am Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn and this is Glân Vraig, our foothold in the Ettenmoors. We are led here by Captain-General Thurimbent... Lainedhel is to the north at the ruined keep, Ost Ringdyr.

'I am sorry. I am getting ahead of myself. There are several enemies in the Ettenmoors and few allies. The eagles led by Golloval support us here in the Coldfells, as do the golden bears led by Goldhead. Far to the west, a small town of hobbits rests on the Hoarwell. None knew they were here.

'It is good to see more arrivals. I have much to teach you, if you are willing to assist us.'Brunil believes someone is poisoning her medicines, and she wants you to search for the culprit.Possible hiding-places can be found both within and without the Hall of the Gentle Hand.

Brunil believes someone has poisoned her medicines and she wants you to check likely hiding-places.Search hiding-places inside the Hall of the Gentle Hand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search hiding-places outside the Hall of the Gentle Hand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Brunil can be found within the Hall of the Gentle Hand, in Imloth Melui.

Your search of possible hiding-places turned up nothing suspicious. You should return to Brunil and see if she is satisfied.Talk to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand'There are so many demands upon my time, ${PLAYER}, and I cannot be everywhere that needs me! I have spoken with the Captain of the Guard, but Merenir thinks I am jumping at shadows and will not look into this matter for me. Perhaps you can be my agent in this?

'It is my duty to heal the sick, but six of those in my care have taken turns for the worse beyond all reason. It is no chance, if you want one healer's opinion: they drank of the same mixture, but where it should have helped it has only hindered!

'I think some sneak has poisoned my medicine! Some lurking foe wishes to bring down the Hall of the Gentle Hand, and cast doubt upon my own abilities! Someone is lurking within or without the Hall, and I need you to search any possible hiding-places for this villain!''You found nothing unusual? Well, you have my thanks for conducting the search anyway, ${PLAYER}. Merenir did not even do that!'A scouting party was dispatched to investigate Egind's story of Orcs in Lossarnach, and none of the scouts have returned.The scouting party was sent south-east of Imloth Melui, and intended to investigate the old ruin of Ost Norhír.

Merenir has asked you to look for the scouting party he sent in search of Orcs, and to bring his men back if that proves possible.Search for the scouting party at Ost Norhír, south-east of Imloth MeluiThe scouting party was sent south-east of Imloth Melui, and intended to investigate the old ruin of Ost Norhír.

Merenir has asked you to look for the scouting party he sent in search of Orcs, and to bring his men back if that proves possible.Free the scout captain from Ost NorhírMerenir is in Imloth Melui, and will want to hear about your encounter with the Orcs in Ost Norhír.Talk to Merenir in Imloth Melui'Egind claimed that he ran afoul of Orcs in Lossarnach, so I sent some of my best lads to see if he spoke the truth. They have not returned, which speaks to me as loudly as if they had. They were going to begin their search at the old ruins of Ost Norhír, south-east of town.

'Can you go in search of my boys, and return with word of them or the foes they sought? If there are Orcs already in Lossarnach, I want to know about it!''Egind claimed that he ran afoul of Orcs in Lossarnach, so I sent some of my best lads to see if he spoke the truth. They have not returned, which speaks to me as loudly as if they had. They were going to begin their search at the old ruins of Ost Norhír, south-east of town.

'Can you go in search of my boys, and return with word of them or the foes they sought? If there are Orcs already in Lossarnach, I want to know about it!''My men and I were scouting for Orcs in Lossarnach, and as you can see we found some! The others suffered grievously at the hands of our captors, and I am the only man that remains. If you had come any later than this, I fear you would find no survivors!

'Quickly, untie me from this post and we can escape!''${PLAYER}! Thank you for freeing Filegnas from his captivity at the hands of the Orcs! I will mourn for the lost members of his party, Rothel and Sardir, when there is time for such remembrances. That time is not now, for something happened while you were away and I do not know what to do!'Arvaethor asks for you to follow him to the very heart of the caverns, deep inside the mountain.Arvaethor can be found within the caverns of Nimrond.

Arvaethor asks for you to follow him to the very heart of the caverns, deep inside the mountain.Speak with ArvaethorArvaethor can be found in the village of Ethring.

You should speak with Arvaethor.Speak with Arvaethor'I thought they would have killed me, instead they were waiting for instructions on what to do with me. Instructions from who, is what I would like to know! Whoever is behind this growing army of Dead and Orcs, we must work together to stop them from amassing their forces and marching on Gondor!''For the Vale!''We have defeated Drugât! He will plague this land no more, thanks to your heroics. Nerzus escaped but I believe we will not see him again.'Lieutenant Unferth wishes you to find books from the libraries of Rhudaur to support his fears. The more he learns from recovered notes and tomes, the more he believes that there is something within the Ettenmoors that the army of Angmar seeks.The books and tomes Unferth desires may be carried by Orcs, Uruks, and possibly even goblins or trolls, which can be found throughout the Ettenmoors.

Lieutenant Unferth has asked you to collect any books or tomes which might uncover what Angmar seeks in the Ettenmoors.'My concern over the true desire of Angmar's forces within the Ettenmoors grows with each passing moment, ${PLAYER}. I have acquired and translated only a few documents, but I have learned that the Witch-king very likely visited these lands as he fled after his defeat.

'The dealings of the Hillmen of Rhudaur with Angmar confounds me, and I must learn more before I deliver my findings to Captain-General Lainedhel. Please, if you recover any tomes from the Enemy deliver them to me so that I might learn more of the history of this place.''I will begin my translation of this work immediately. You have helped us greatly, friend.

'For your efforts, I give you this token. I will have need of your service in the future, ${PLAYER}, so remember me.'Lieutenant Unferth is concerned over items which he found on the corpses of many of the Orcs and Uruks he killed when first arriving in the Ettenmoors: scraps of text cataloguing the history of Rhudaur.Goblins, Orcs, and Uruks may be found throughout the Ettenmoors. Lieutenant Unferth is located within the relative safety of Ost Ringdyr.

Lieutenant Unferth is concerned that Angmar's army may be searching for something terrible in the Ettenmoors, but little of the history of the region survived Rhudaur's destruction. He is looking for any shred of information that he may find.'Greetings, ${CLASS}. I am Lieutenant Unferth. Before my arrival here in the Coldfells, I was a student of ancient lore.

'I know much about Rhudaur, the kingdom which once stood here in the Ettenmoors, but my knowledge of this specific place is limited. Most documents surrounding the kingdom's decline were lost to the ages and in the great war that saw their ruin. When I arrived here in the Ettenmoors, we fought many skirmishes against the host out of Angmar, and I discovered that many of the Orcs and Uruks carried parchment from the ancient libraries of Rhudaur.

'I fear that they seek something here in the Ettenmoors, and these texts may reveal what that is. Would you return any that you find to me? You would receive a reward, of course.''These will take me time to translate, but they will help me to know what evil was done in these lands. If there is something foul here, we will learn what it is, and we will root it out.

'For your efforts, I give you this token. I will have need of your service in the future, ${PLAYER}, so remember me.'Bergil has invited you on a stroll around the First Circle of Minas Tirith.Bergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back.

