Stroll with Bergil up upon the outer walls of Minas Tirith. If you should get separated, the whistle Bergil gave you will call him back.Tour the southern wallLook out from over the City GatesTour the northern wallTour the far northern wallWhile touring the city walls with Bergil, you have crossed paths with Oryat, the soldier who berated Bergil earlier. You should intervene before he lays his hands on the boy.Talk to OryatYou intervened to keep Oryat from striking Bergil, and Oryat challenged you to what is surely an ill-advised duel.

See where Bergil wishes to go now. If you should get separated, the whistle Bergil gave you will call him back.Talk to BergilAmonel is in the Wrights' Fellow-hall, in the southern stretch of the First Circle.

Return to the tinker Amonel, to see if Himnir's whisk has been mended. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.Return to Amonel the tinkerBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back.

See where Bergil wishes to go next.Oryat will be waiting in the Second Circle, between the Feasting Hall and the tavern.

Bergil has implored you to go and fight Oryat, to teach him a lesson. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.Meet OryatOryat stands in the Second Circle, between the Feasting Hall and the tavern.

Bergil has implored you to go and fight Oryat, to teach him a lesson. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.Defeat OryatRossaran stands in the Second Circle, across from the Feasting Hall.

After facing down the bully Oryat, you noticed the Swan-knight Rossaran standing nearby. See what he has to say. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.Talk to RossaranBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back.

See what Bergil has to say.The Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.

You have beaten Oryat and scared him from troubling the children in the First Circle... but he has threatened harm to any who trespass in the Second Circle. Meet Bergil back at the Old Guest-house, where he stays.Meet Bergil back at the Old Guest-house'Greetings! I am friend to the prince of the halflings. Have you ever seen a halfling? I'll wager you haven't.'

When you tell him that you in fact have, he seems crestfallen. A moment later, his face lights up again.

'All the same, you are a stranger in the city. Will you walk with me? I'll show you things to see. And we can go places I would be shooed away from, were I alone!

'Here, take this whistle. If we somehow get separated, you sound it and I'll come running.''Come! Come! You must see the ranks of soldiers. They are a sight to see!''There they are! If only the sun were shining, how fine their gleaming arms and armour would be.

'Look, there are others, over there. Let us get a look at those ones, too!''There are others over there!''Why, were I the Enemy I would throw down my weapons and despair!

'What are those soldiers, over there? We should see.''Those soldiers, there. Let us get closer to them.''That man would not truly do harm to me, would he?'The Knight gives the slightest of nods to you, and then addresses Bergil.

'It pains me that even in this dark hour, we cannot count on each other for common kindness. Yet it is ever so.

'Young man, know that had he raised his arm to you, I would have intervened. I saw clearly that this ${RACE}, your companion, was one breath from doing the same.

'But someone elder and stronger than you cannot be always by your side. I therefore council you to look before you step, and to learn to judge the character of men before they are within striking range. Look into their eyes. You will learn to know. See that one there, who so discourteously spoke to you? An unhappy storm is writ upon his face.

'You may grow to be strong and maybe even take the trappings of a knight in your time. But a cautious step and keen judgement will guard you from blows that no armour ever can.''A cautious step and keen judgement. Remember that!''A cautious step and what was it, clear judgement? I must commit those words, for they seem good ones to live by.

'Fa! I am shaking a bit from that mean fellow, though I do not like to admit it. Let us look elsewhere, on something more pleasant.

'See the horses over there? Shall we feed them some apples?''They brought out new apple crates just this morning. Let us feed the horses!''First, let us go and look upon the ranks of soldiers by the gate. There have never been so many out and at the ready, as far as I can recall. And I am no small boy.

'I am ten years old, and soon shall be five feet tall!''Isn't it funny how their lips brush against your hand?''It's not only horses who enjoy a treat now and then. With you along, I might be allowed in the Foodmongers' Market. There is a 'monger there, Himnir he is called, who likes me well enough and might give me something to eat.'

Bergil's face grows serious and seems to think a moment.

'What that knight said about kindness was also very fine. Perhaps if I ask the right way, Himnir will send food to all the children.

'Yes, let us go find him!''No doubt you saw, when we met, that I am not the only youth in Minas Tirith. Mind you, most left with the wains some days past. But a dozen of us remained for this reason and that.

'It is for them, as well as I myself, I wish to ask Himnir for some treats.'Himnir smiles indulgently at Bergil.

'Sweets not just for you, but also for the other children? Well, that is a bold thing to ask! Others would pay good coin for such a parcel of my goods. Ah, but who am I fooling? Like as not, I would have given it to you freely.

'Today, however, I have an errand you may run to earn your treat. This whisk I use to whip up cream for my pastries has come apart, and it is my favourite whisk!

'I ask you to bring it to Amonel, a tinker in the Wrights' Market, and beg her to set it right. In return, I'll have a bounty of sweets sent over for the whole lot of you.''The Wrights' Market! I wouldn't mind poking my nose in there, anyway. This Amonel, she must be awfully clever with her hands. Tinkers are, you know!''Bring that broken whisk to Amonel, around or about the Wrights' Market, and I'll send treats for all your friends.''Well, this is an odd pairing!'

The tinker eyes you and Bergil.

'So, old Himnir's favourite whisk finally failed him. Go lightly with it, I told him! Ah, well. Let me have a look and see what I can do.

'You come back in a while and with any luck, I'll have it fixed.''Run along. This will take a moment... or two. I haven't decided yet how the whisk could be fixed.'A thought seems to suddenly strike Bergil.

'Say, when did you get here, ${PLAYER}? Were you upon the Pelennor when Lord Faramir came back to us? How I should like to have seen that! I went to the gates with Pippin - that's the prince of the halflings I spoke of - when all the men arrived from Belfalas and Lossarnach and elsewhere. That was a sight to see. But they only rode in on their horses. That is fine, but it is nothing to a fight!

'How would you like to go up upon the walls and see what we can? I hear the Enemy is within the Rammas Echor now and would like dreadfully to see how that is. I can hardly imagine it!''A tour of the city walls is just the thing. I wish to see everything I can up there!''Run along. This will take a moment... or two. I haven't decided yet how the whisk could be fixed.''You - you talk to him, ${PLAYER}.''And just what are you then, the champion of orphans and wretches? What gives you the right to stand between me, a soldier of Gondor, and that impudent, sniveling, little...'

He makes as if to go past you, then sees the dangerous look in your eye.

'Oho, is that how it is? You'd strike at me, would you, just to spare this urchin a bit of a thrashing? Just you try it. I'm a soldier trained and hardened, and I'll strike back. I'll strike whatever cheeky boy or foreigner I choose, to let them know their place.

'Now skulk away - or if you've any spine, meet me up in the Second Circle later, between the Feasting Hall and the tavern, and we'll see who strikes who, when it comes to it.''Second Circle between the tavern and the Feasting Hall, O Champion of Brats. We can settle this there.''Let us go, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps Amonel has finished mending that whisk.''Yes, let us go. Amonel will have mended the whisk, and Himnir will give all the children treats!''Second Circle between the tavern and the Feasting Hall, O Champion of Brats. We can settle this there.'Amonel greets you and Bergil with a low sigh.

'The whisk is not mended. Nor shall it be, for it is beyond repair. Himnir should not go so hard on so delicate a tool and I have told him so...

'Nor will I send you to bear this ill tiding for me. Some things must be faced bravely. A knight cannot send someone in his stead to face the foe, nor can he shirk his duty and let innocents come to harm.

'Go now. Somehow I think Himnir will send some sweets to your friends all the same.''Please, ${PLAYER}. Oryat will never leave us children be, if you do not face him. And how I long to see that sneer wiped from his face!''Got a spine then after all, have we? I reckoned there was a chance you might - so I made sure I had some friends at hand.

'Ha ha! Why should I chance a wound for the sorry likes of you!''By the kings of old! You showed Oryat a thing or two!''You showed bravery just now, both of you. Sometimes we rush into a fight that might be averted. Other times we do what must be done, even though the consequences of our acts bring us no good fortune. You must ask yourself which you have chosen. But regardless of what lesson you draw, you will live with the result.

'You have won yourself freedom in the First Circle, but neither you nor any of the other children should venture up here anymore. Oryat will surely do you harm. I read that plainly in his eyes.''I bid you heed Oryat's words. If this boy or any other children venture into the Second Circle, he will do them harm.''Not venture into the Second Circle? I suppose we dare not, lest Oryat find us. Oh, ${PLAYER}! What have we done? Somehow I felt for sure that if only you bested Oryat, he would never trouble us anymore.

'We had better not stay. I shall go back to the Old Guest-house now. I must think and talk with the other children.

'Will you meet me there?''I bid you heed Oryat's words. If this boy or any other children venture into the Second Circle, he will do them harm.''What fun we've had, strolling about, ${PLAYER}! I will not let that last grim turn spoil my enjoyment of the day, and I hope you won't either.

'Still, it will be hard not going to any Upper Circles. I owe it to the others to find some way out of this - or around it - if I can.''Run along, you two. I will go see Himnir myself, shortly, and tell him the ill news of his broken whisk.''She speaks nearly as well as the swan-knight, ${PLAYER}. Some things must be faced bravely...

'Do you know what I think? I think that you must face that swaggering soldier, Oryat! Surely you are a match for him. Surely you can cow him and make him relent.

'Please, ${PLAYER}. He will not leave us children alone until someone stops him. Oh, and how I would love to see you stand him on his head!'It seems that your appearance and the timing of your arrival in Imloth Melui bears a striking resemblance to a dream Lady Vanyalos had the night before.Lady Vanyalos can be found in the great hall on the north-east rise of Imloth Melui.

Merenir has asked you to pay a visit to Lady Vanyalos, insisting that somehow she dreamed of you.Talk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall on the north-east rise of Imloth Melui'Forgive me, ${CLASS}. This is exactly Lady Vanyalos's dream, as she told it to me: a ${RACE}, looking as you, coming up this road under a strangely darkened sky. The description fits exactly!

'Lady Vanyalos will want to speak with you, and at once! You can find her within her hall on the north-east rise. I do not pretend to understand how this can be, but she will certainly be filled with wonder at seeing her dream made flesh. What can this mean?''Welcome to Imloth Melui, good traveller. Captain Merenir believes it was you I saw in my dream? Are you the only traveller of your kind who will visit us during this strange darkness, I wonder? Will Merenir send me every one who does? He is a good captain but perhaps not the best interpreter of dreams.

'Still, it is true and well known that I and those of my blood have had dreams of great portent. Are you a bearer of good tidings, ${PLAYER}, or ill? And if you were, would you know the difference?'You have been asked to help two soldiers settle a wager regarding the Ship's Prow and updrafts.The soldiers Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.

Talk to Tawaris to hear his side of the argument.Talk to TawarisThe soldiers Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.

Talk to Gradir to hear his side of the argument.Talk to GradirGradir said chickens could be found in the Court of Eärnil. The Ship's Prow lies at the very top of Minas Tirith, jutting out of the Citadel.

Find a chicken and drop it off of the Ship's Prow to determine whether Gradir or Tawaris is right.Carry the chicken to the Ship's ProwYou should check the First Circle below the Ship's Prow to see what became of the chicken.Find out what happened to the chickenThe soldiers can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.

You should return to Gradir and Tawaris and tell them what happened with the chicken.Return to Gradir and Tawaris'Ah, what have we here? A ${CLASS}, is it? Perhaps you can help us settle this matter!

'You see, my friend and I cannot come to an agreement. We have argued back and forth and then forth and back, and I will confess that in a heated moment, Tawaris here has even wagered good Gondorian gold if he should be proven wrong.

'Come now, you'll hear us out, won't you?''Do you see the pier up there, or the Ship's Prow, as some call it? Well, a man told me that the winds race up its face so fiercely, you couldn't walk off of it if you tried. You'd be shoved back!

'It stands to reason, does it not?''What a load of fish-guts! First off, the winds clearly run along the pier down from the tower and fall to the land below. Winds going up. Ha! Doesn't rain fall? Has anyone ever seen rain fly up the pier?

'No, my friends. The winds go down, not up. So say I - and you say otherwise. How shall we settle this? There's gold in your pockets, Tawaris, that should really be in mine.

'What do you say to this? Our ${CLASS} friend here carries a chicken up to the pier's end and tosses it off. If it comes back, you've won. Down it goes? I've won!'

Tawaris nods in agreement and the two look at you expectantly.

'I'll save you the chore of carrying a hen straight from the First Circle. There are some hens in the Court of Eärnil, up in the Third Circle. Go for one of those.'The two soldiers listen to your account.

'Clearly, I have won. We said that if it fell, the wager was mine, did we not?'

Gradir pauses, shakes his head, and sighs.

'Bah! The gulls can take the rules. You swore there was an updraft, old friend, and it is plain to see that there was. Here, the wager is yours.

'Well, ${PLAYER}, it's a good thing you did not jump off yourself... though that would likely have won me the bet! Still, I thank you all the same.'Gradir wants to share a drink of his rotgut with you. Unfortunately, he's all out.The soldiers Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.

Hear what Tawaris has to say.Talk to TawarisThe soldiers Gradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.

Hear what Gradir has to say.Talk to GradirYou should bring Gradir the items he needs to make rotgut: ale dregs from the Splintered Shield, hot brazier ash, and Healer's Caustic.

All three ingredients can be found on the Second Circle: the dregs in the southern section, the brazier ash in the northern section, and Healer's Caustic at any healer's stall.Collect dregs from ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect brazier ash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Healer's CausticGradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.

You should return to Gradir with the rotgut ingredients.You should drink the rotgut that Gradir prepared for you.Drink the rotgutGradir and Tawaris can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.

Hear what Tawaris has to say.Talk to TawarisStanding after a drink of rotgut is not enough for Tawaris. He wants to see you tap the left-hand archer on the shoulder to compliment his aim, walk between the last two ranks of soldiers to his right, and then stand on the barrels and give a wave.Tap the left archer on the shoulderWalk between the last two ranks of menThe soldiers can be found on the northern side of the Second Circle.

You should return to Gradir and Tawaris so they can settle their bet.Return to Gradir'Well, ${PLAYER}, you are a good sort! I would share a drink with you, if I had aught worth drinking. 

'But alas! Tawaris here drank the last of our rotgut.''Do not listen to this scoundrel. First of all, it was he who drank the last of it. 

'But never mind that. Rotgut is not for the likes of you. Why, I have never met anyone but us fisherfolk of Ethir who could stomach it!''Tawaris, you do grievous wrong to our ${CLASS} friend, a seasoned adventurer who could clearly stomach rotgut, even if most could not.

'Why, I dare say we are in disagreement once again. Let us wager on it, and perhaps I can win my gold back. 

'${PLAYER}, find me what I need and I will make you some rotgut. If luck would have it, you can find all the ingredients on this very tier so I expect your trip to be swift. 

'First, I'll need dregs from ale, which you might find at the Splintered Shield. Then I need hot ash from a brazier and some Healer's Caustic, which is a powerful and pungent tincture used for closing wounds.''This will do the trick, ${PLAYER}! Now mind you, the ashes here are not quite what they are in Ethir, never mind the difference in the ale dregs, but it will have to do. Yes, it will have to do!

'There, now it's made. Go on, have a taste!''Ha ha! The ${CLASS} has done it, Tawaris, and this time the wager is mine. I'll have my gold back, thank you.

'You are welcome back for a drink with us any time, ${PLAYER}. And do not worry, the rotgut will wear off soon and the headache that follows will be fleeting, though quite strong!''Well! The ${CLASS} can drink some rotgut and stay standing, perhaps. But one step and down you'll go.

'Let us put you to the test. Walk over to that left archer, tap him on the shoulder, and tell him he's aiming well. Then, over on my right, walk between the last two ranks of men there. And last... last... why, climb up upon that barrel there and give us a wave!

'Do all that, and I'll confess you can hold your rotgut after all.'Help the old poet Dúrbethir compose a war-poem for the coming days.Talk to Dúrbethir in the Fourth Circle and ask how you can help him compose a war poem.Talk to DúrbethirSoldiers can be found training and making ready in the Second Circle.

Dúrbethir asked that you go among the soldiers and listen to them train, as well as retrieve a cold knife and a sweaty rag.Listen to the soldiers trainingFind a cold knifeFind a sweaty ragPillaged farmsteads and the enemy army can be found across the Pelennor, outside Minas Tirith.

Dúrbethir asked that you find ruined farmsteads and gather charred wood and trampled wheat. He also asked that you hear for him the death-rattle of enemy soldiers and see the gleam in an enemy captain's eye in combat and defeat.Find pieces of charred wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find trampled wheat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hear the death-rattle of enemy soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Observe the gleam in the eyes of a captainReturn to Dúrbethir in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.'Never have I been a poet of war. If we found glory in naught more than gleaming armour and feats of battle, then the Enemy has won his first victory against us.

'And so I wrought poetry of the grandeur of works or stone, of the beauty of blossom and branch, of the love of young men and maidens, fair and proud. When I put history to verse, it was of our works and journeys and failings.

'But today - today is a day of war! It is close upon us as the breath in our lungs, and I would write a song of it. As you came upon me here, I was brooding on how to begin. I think I must fill my senses with things dark, dread, and bloody. Will you help me in this?'Dúrbethir takes the items you have brought him and listens with a grave expression to the impressions you gathered. 

'Perhaps I asked too much of you - but yet, it is no more than we ask of every soldier here. Nevertheless, you have brought me ample inspiration. Let me ponder a moment....

'Dark the day and bright the fire 
The fires in the trenches' veins
Veins go cold and life expires
Expiring joy and dread and pain
Dark the day and blood shall flow
Dark the day and still we go

'Blood shall flow and fear shall clamour
Clamour like the soldiers' cries
Cries of fury, hope, and valour
Valour chance and death defies
Dark the day and still we go
Dark the day and blood shall flow

'There, it is done. I have wrought a song for war. Perhaps we will take these words to our graves. If that is so, take my thanks as well.''If you would, go down among our soldiers in the Second Circle. Listen there to the sound of their training. Find for me a cold knife and a sweaty rag. 

'Then go out into the fields - as you are fit for such deeds - and explore our ruined farmsteads. Find for me some charred wood and trampled wheat. Then go in among our foes and hear the death-rattles of their dying soldiers. Observe for me the fell gleam in the eyes of one of their captains as he fights and falls. 

'Hm... yes. When you have done what I ask, return to me and I shall make a poem fit for war.'In order to save his family, Faltharan asks you to organize an incursion onto the Corsair blockade.Thandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Thandor.Speak with ThandorThe Corsair ships can be reached using the boat to the south of the Gondorian Captain.

You should board the Corsair ships and rescue the captured nobles.Locate the rescue boat near the docksRescue SirielRescue LorvegilRescue CelebrosThandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Thandor.Talk to Thandor'Your arrival in the city is well-timed, ${PLAYER}.

'When the city fell, my kin were presumed captured or dead. Fortunately, we have located them as hostages aboard the remaining hostile Corsair ships. My advisors say that a direct assault would be too risky, and since your reputation precedes you, I would ask you to sneak aboard their ships, and rescue my family.

'Captain Thandor is in charge of city defence, and will be able to provide you with more information.''Remarkable work, ${PLAYER}. You were able to climb aboard without even our notice!

'Now that you've found the missing nobles, we will be able to deal with matters elsewhere. The war continues to rage beyond the city, and we will need to be ready for what is next.

'For now we will remember this as the day where the bloodline of Pelargir was saved.''Faltharan may trust you with this task, but that does not make it any easier.

'In order for this rescue to work, we will need a way to sneak on and off the ships. Fortunately, we have no shortage of small landing craft.

'If you head to the docks behind me, you should be able to find something suitable you can use to sneak aboard. Tread lightly, ${PLAYER}'Merenir wishes to speak with you before you depart from Imloth Melui.Merenir stands by the entrance to Imloth Melui.

Lady Vanyalos has asked you to talk to Merenir, who has one last favour to ask you before you depart Imloth Melui.Talk to MerenirDindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.

Merenir has asked you to visit his scout, Dindal, at the look-out and assist in any way that you can.Find Dindal at the look-outDindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.

Dindal has asked you to stand by his side and look out to the north-east.Dindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.

Now that you have looked out to the north-east, you should talk to Dindal again.Talk to Dindal'I have one last favour to ask of you, ${PLAYER}. Or rather, Captain Merenir does. Believe me, he asks only out of our great need. We will hold you in great regard no matter your choice.''Well met, ${CLASS}. Did I, by any chance, see you sparring with the guards back in Imloth Melui? No matter. If the ${RACE} I saw was you, you are no common hand in combat.

'Are you as keen in sight as in combat? Look down there and tell me what you see.'You tell Dindal what you saw.

'Your eyes are not poor. I have watched them for some time, and they are beyond count. All I can do is watch, but you are mighty and capable of much.

'If you were to help us against these Orcs, what could you do? Hm....''How relieved I am that all under my charge are safe within these walls, ${PLAYER}! Still, I must not take the arrival of these Orcs lightly. I have sent one of my best scouts, Dindal by name, up to a secluded look-out. It lies north off the road east of here. The unknowing eye would miss its rise up into the hillside of the mountain's feet.

'There he will have a perfect view of the Harlond and the walls of Rammas Echor, on our northern border... for it is there, I fear, where the Orcs have crossed and entered Lossarnach. I would ask you to find him there and assist in whatever way you can.'Lord Angbor has heard tales of a great beast flying in the darkened sky above Gondor and seeks to learn more of what his men have seen.Angbor's men can be found in the eastern half of Pelargir.

Angbor has asked you to question his men about strange things they claim to have seen in the hours preceding the battle in Pelargir.Talk to DaelarthTalk to LaervenTalk to ThamdirAngbor can be found inside the eastern gate in Pelargir.

You have questioned his men and should now report what you have learned to Angbor.Talk to Angbor in Pelargir'As my men and I journeyed to Pelargir from Linhir, we felt a great weight upon us.

'Days without rest and the fatigue of battle had worn on us all, but this filled me with dread in a way that I had never known. And just as it took hold, it faded away, and those of my men that had cowered found their way to their feet once more.

'I have heard many rumours of what happened that day, but I do not know if there is any truth in them. I have not had much time to think on this matter until now, yet it still troubles me.

'Speak to my men of this, and see if there is any truth to these tales.''As with Lord Angbor, I wish I knew what happened in that moment.

'My armour grew heavy and I fell to the ground before I could realize what happened. I regret that I cannot be of more help to you, ${CLASS}.''Why do you ask me to recall such things?

'Before terror pulled me to the ground, I saw the form of a great beast above the ashen clouds. It let out a shrill cry as it flew overhead and then it was gone. I swear to you, I speak true!''Since the sun was blotted out days ago, we have seen little without the use of torches, but what I saw I shall never forget.

'A flying beast bore a rider in darkened robes and the blade he held reflected what little light passed through the murky sky. As I looked upon him, a great pain overtook me and I turned away.

'When I turned to look again to the sky, he had gone.''I do not doubt their words, my friend. Could this be one of the nine wraiths of which Aragorn spoke?

'Let us hope it has flown back to its master and shall not harry our journey to Minas Tirith. I will not allow its dread to burden my mind any longer.

'My men and I must press on into Upper Lebennin!'A scarce few Rangers from Esteldín came east to the Ettenmoors to support Lainedhel's efforts against Angmar's army.Uirnen is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors.

The Rangers are attempting to augment the forces fighting in the Ettenmoors, but fear that committing too much to the battle will result in Angmar succeeding elsewhere. The Ranger Uirnen has asked you to speak with him if you wish to assist the Rangers with their duties.Speak with Uirnen and complete your patrol of the Ettenmoors as a Ranger (Cost: 500 Commendations)Uirnen is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors.

You should return to Uirnen and inform him that you have fulfilled your duty.Talk to Uirnen at Glân Vraig'Greetings, ${RACE}, you fight against the foes of Eriador in these lands, and this is good. There is no doubt within me that your resolve to win this battle is strong.

'Please, hear me out. We are assisting in this battle where we can, and we will continue to do so. I would ask, though, that you support us in our endeavours elsewhere to safe-guard Eriador from the machinations of the North.

'Should you wish to assist us, return to me, and I will arrange for you to take the place of one of my brethren while he patrols the wilds of the Ettenmoors.''I expected that you would return, ${PLAYER}. If you are prepared, I will set you to your task and call one of our number to patrol the Ettenmoors in your stead.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This quest begins a special session quest. You will be logged out of your normal character and take on the guise of a player-friendly npc. You will not be able to leave the Ettenmoors as this character and will attain a set of skills unique to this special player character.</rgb>'Your efforts allowed one of our number to assist the Free Peoples greatly, ${PLAYER}. You are to be thanked for the efforts that you put forth.

'The Rangers of Esteldín are indebted to you. You are truly a hero in the war against the Iron Crown.'Turthoren the locksmith held spare keys to all the houses in Tungobel, until a half-troll stole them.Turthoren's keys are on a half-troll in Tungobel.

Retrieve the keys for Turthoren.Retrieve Turthoren's keysEach home in Tungobel has an unlocked door.

Lock each door in Tungobel.Lock doors in Tungobel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Turthoren is near the village of Tungobel.

Return the keys to Turthoren.Return the keys to TurthorenTurthoren the locksmith speaks to you in a hushed tone.

'Ah you are not a Corsair. Good! I am afraid for my life but even more afraid for the future of my profession. You see, I make keys and locks for the whole village to protect the townspeople's homes from bandits. Some of the villagers lose their keys from time to time so I keep a spare for each home. That is, I had a spare key for each home until one of those monstrous beasts stole the keys from my shop! You've got to get those keys back for me and lock the doors so when the townsfolk return they know I looked after their homes. Please, ${RACE}, will you help me?''Oh, you are indeed a hero. I thought that I'd never be able to return to Tungobel. Now that I have my keys back, I can leave for safety, then return to my work once this corsair threat is taken care of.

'No, I'm not worried about the Corsairs. They try this every once in a while. These large half-trolls in their ranks frighten me though. They wield a sword as well as any man.'After her husband left Minas Tirith to aid in the war, Mílien has grown increasingly concerned by her son's behaviour.The Baths of Belecthor can be found to the north in the Fourth Circle.

Mílien has asked you to seek out her son, Círgon, at the Baths of Belecthor near their home or below in Egalmoth's Green.Search for Círgon near the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth CircleEgalmoth's Green can be found to the north in the Third Circle.

You were unable to find Círgon at the Baths and should now search Egalmoth's Green.'Do you have a moment, ${PLAYER}? 

'Forgive me if I am too direct, but I have heard your name spoken among the people since your arrival in Minas Tirith and I hoped you might aid me with a personal matter.

'My son, Círgon, has not been himself. My husband has gone to war and Círgon will not say it, but I know it tears at him. He has spent much time alone over the past few weeks, and does not even speak to his friends. He spends every morning down at the Baths sailing the ships he and Círhir built together. That, or he wanders Egalmoth's Green and sits alone in the dark of the trees.

'Is this how a child should cope? It does not seem so to me, and I worry for him. We all feel the loss of our loved ones and he must understand that we are together in our sorrows.

'Please, go find him, and tell him to return to me. I have prepared supper and I cannot allow Círgon to sacrifice another meal to his sadness.''Mother sent you, didn't she?

'She doesn't need to worry about me, you know. I just come down here to think about father and my family... and how things used to be. I don't want to talk about that right now.

'Oh, I was just about to leave to sail my ships! Would you like to come along?'Edenos has tasked you with destroying the enemies supplies in order to weaken their efforts to take the city.Enemy supplies can be found on the Eastern side of Osgiliath.

You should destroy enemy supplies.Destroy enemy supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Edenos is at the Palace of Eldacar.

You should speak to Edenos.Speak with Edenos'The time has come for a covert mission. I'm sending you behind enemy lines, soldier. The Orcs have supplies to help repair some of their damaged siege equipment. I'm sure you understand we can't let that happen.

'Use some stealth when you're out there. Destroying those supply crates will weaken their efforts to take the city from us.''You have done much for the Gondorian army. We will take back this city!'A band of thieves has taken over one of the districts of Pelargir, and Thandor is requesting assistance in their removal.The ruffians can be found in the abandoned district to the north-east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should defeat the ruffians who are harbouring Lorvegil.Defeat city toughs and scoundrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Thandor.Talk to Thandor'Not every person who held out against the Corsair siege was an upstanding person. Many were in fact thieves and brigands who banded together in the face of a larger threat.

'Ever since the city was retaken, they've done nothing but harass, threaten, and harm anyone that crosses their path.

'Because they've been encroaching so deeply into the city, I'm wondering if you might be able to send them a message that we will not be pushed around.''I must say that you handled yourself well against a pretty dirty sort of outlaws. Most of my men wouldn't dare to cross their path.

'Although they will likely regroup once our host has departed, this should keep the streets a little safer in the short-term.'After hearing of many strange occurrences within Ost Anglebed from her guards, Nimithil has need of a discerning eye.Ost Anglebed can be found in north-central Lebennin.

Nimithil has asked you to search Ost Anglebed for signs of treachery from within the guard.Nimithil can be found in the lowest section of Ost Anglebed with her guards.

You have found a few pieces of concerning evidence in Ost Anglebed, and should return to Nimithil.Talk to Nimithil'Milonnen and my guards have spoken of strange happenings in Ost Anglebed, but I have yet to see any of them with my own eyes.

'Still, I do not doubt the truth to their words, and I would ask that you investigate this further, ${PLAYER}. They have spoken of ill-crafted weaponry and fragile defences about town, but I am certain more troubles have visited Ost Anglebed since this morn.

'Search thoroughly, and tell me of what you find.''This is most disturbing, ${PLAYER}...

'Someone in Ost Anglebed must be behind this, but who... I cannot be certain. We must soon speak to the Steward of this matter.'Herion sends you to the Haradrim camp, Lang Boha, to hinder the destructive powers of the Corsair forces.Aras can be found just north of the Haradrim camp, Lang Boha.

You should speak with Aras.Speak with Aras at Lang BohaLang Boha can be found on the eastern shores of Dor-en-Ernil.

Enter Lang Boha and hinder the Corsair forces.Collect weapons of the enemy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn the provision tents (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Captain of the Haradrim camp can be found in Lang Boha.

Find and confront the Haradrim Captain.Summon and confront the Haradrim Captain of Lang BohaAras can be found just north of the Haradrim camp, Lang Boha.

You should speak with Aras.Speak with Aras at Lang Boha'Erchar can return to Linhir now or wait for me. I always respect his decision. At this time, I choose my own path.

'We must remove the power behind the Corsair threat in Dor-en-Ernil before returning to Linhir. Aras has gone to scout the land east of our camp. Meet him on the northern border of Lang Boha. There you should find the leader of the one who killed many of my men. These were good people, ${PLAYER}. Avenge them as you would avenge your own kin.

'May those who oppose you be blinded by your strength.''${PLAYER}, I am glad to see you unharmed. There are enemies on patrol everywhere. I have scouted Lang Boha. I shall recount what I have seen....

'There are four tents in the camp that are used for food storage. Burning them will indeed set them back on provisions.

'The enemy has many weapons. Take the weapons from those you defeat and return to me with them. I shall dispose of them in the waters. The rusted weapons will be of no use to the Corsair forces. Take care to avoid the Half-trolls though, they will not part with their swords so easily.

'Lastly, the one who led the ambush against Erchar and Herion is indeed the captain of this camp. I warn you though. He is a powerful man. Do not fall for his tricks!''You dare try to destroy these forces? The flames only make me stronger.

'All of Gondor will burn before we are victorious. Best that you run away before you meet a fate worse than death.

'For I am the Eye of Dolgimil. Blinding me is but a scratch on his face!''He called himself the Eye of Dolgimil? I fear then this Dolgimil is the true threat we seek. Perhaps we can look elsewhere for clues to Dolgimil's whereabouts.'The Free Peoples will return to take Tol Ascarnen, and Angmar's defenders wish to strengthen the walls with deterrents that will drive the foe away.Iron ore can be found on the dwarves who fight for the Free Peoples or from the Isendeep Mine to the north.

Angmar's army is shoring up the defences at Tol Ascarnen. Glat intends to build a massive iron pot to heat oil with which to douse the Free Peoples who attempt to assail the keep.'Well, the War-tyrant isn't satisfied with just oil. He wants iron, he says, for the oil.

'My head swims a moment, and I realize what he's saying. We need ore, iron ore to build a great iron belly to house the oil. Then we'll heat the oil and douse those wretches. Cooked meat for all!

'We know that the Isendeep Mine houses a great deal of ore. Go there, or if you think it too far a trek, find the dwarves. Those bearded slugs carry the ore sometimes.''This will do nicely, get others to the task so we can build the iron belly and cook us some meals.'Cangoras has noticed increasing numbers of spying crebain on the Western side of Osgiliath that need to be dealt with.Crebain can be found on the Western side of Osgiliath.

You should defeat crebain.Defeat crebain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many spying crebain.Completed'Have you noticed, among the crows there are spying birds of the enemy? These crebain watch us with their beady little eyes. I know not who their master is but it surely is the enemy trying to get the upper hand.

'You should defeat the crebain quickly before these birds report back to their master with information that could turn the tide of the battle.'You have defeated many spying crebain and thwarted the enemies' plans of learning your battle strategies.The people of Glaniath have remained relatively sheltered from the horrors of war, but it is unclear how long this peace will last.Arvellon's folk can be found throughout Glaniath in Upper Lebennin.

Arvellon has asked you to convince his people to seek refuge in Tumladen.Arvellon can be found at the southern entrance to Glaniath in Upper Lebennin.

You have urged the folk to seek shelter in Tumladen and should now return to Arvellon.Talk to Arvellon'I have been trying for days now to convince the people to leave... to seek shelter in Tumladen.

'It is a great and fortified shelter for our people, one of a few in Gondor, and the brother to one that lies within the lands of Rohan. It is more than able to house all of the people of Lebennin and beyond, and its walls would keep us from the growing war in Gondor.

'My folk are headstrong, traveller. They think that since Pelargir has been reclaimed and no foes have come to our doors that we are safe. I do not think it so!

'Would you speak to them for me? Urge them to reconsider before it is too late!''I cannot say I'm surprised that many of them ignored your advice to seek shelter... they have paid me no mind either since the skies went dark.

'Still... I thank you for trying on my behalf. I only wish to see my people safely through this war, but it remains their choice to make.'First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr is collecting seals found on the Chieftains of Angmar's army in the Ettenmoors.The Chieftains of Angmar may be found among the Enemy in the Ettenmoors.

Chieftains amongst Angmar's army bear seals that denote their station. Slay them and take their seals to earn recognition amongst the Free Peoples. First Marshal Sathryth has promised a reward for the seals you bring her.'You there, ${RACE}, I have task for you.

'Chieftains command great numbers of the Enemy's forces, second only to the tyrants that lead the war-host.

'Should you run afoul of these terrors, slay them and bring me their seals so that I might see you rewarded for their defeat.''Each Chieftain that falls strengthens our position, ${PLAYER}. You are a hero to all the Free Peoples. Seek Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig to earn greater recognition of your efforts in the Ettenmoors.'First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr is collecting badges taken from Angmar's weakest forces.Trackers can be found among the Enemy in the Ettenmoors.

Forces in the service to Angmar may each carry a seal of their station. Search among the enemy for these badges. First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr has promised a reward for the badges you bring her.'Ho there, ${RACE}, lend me your ear!

'There are many servants of Angmar scattered throughout the Ettenmoors. Search amongst their army for the tracker's badges. These can be found on the lowliest of their forces.

'If you collect some of these badges and return them to me, you will be honoured with a commendation of valour.''Your efforts are welcomed, ${PLAYER}. Please take this with my thanks. Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig will recognize you for your efforts in the Ettenmoors should you visit him.'First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr is collecting badges taken from Angmar's soldiers.Soldiers in the service to Angmar may each carry a seal of their station. Search among the enemy for these badges. First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr has promised to reward you for the patches you bring her.'Have you been ignoring me, ${RACE}? I have need of your services.

'Above the rank and file, the soldiers of Angmar act as lesser leaders of the Ongbúrz forces. These beasts are savage and cruel and capable of leading only small numbers before their tempers lead to bloodshed amongst their own kind.

'Find these vile forces and bring me the patches that adorn their armour. I will reward you for ten such patches.''Your efforts are heralded, ${PLAYER}. Take this with my thanks. Remember that Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig will recognize you for your efforts in the Ettenmoors should you visit him.'First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr is collecting badges taken from Angmar's taskmasters.The taskmasters of Angmar can be found among the Enemy in the Ettenmoors.

The taskmasters who drive the Angmarim war-host into a frenzy bear honourifics of their station. Collect these to earn commendation from the Army of the Free Peoples. First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr has promised to reward you for the taskmaster's honourifics you bring her.'You there, ${RACE}, what are you doing? I need your assistance.

'Beneath the chieftains of the Ongbúrz are the taskmasters who drive the host into a frenzy and force them to set upon our forces with sadistic glee.

'Seek them out and take their honourifics. Return some of these honourifics to me, and I will see that you are justly rewarded.''Your continued efforts fuel the strength that fills the arms and hearts of the Free Peoples. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Visit Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig to earn greater recognition of your efforts in the Ettenmoors.'First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr seeks the honourifics of the true leaders of Angmar's army, the tyrant's lashes.Tyrants can be found among the Enemy in the Ettenmoors.

Known by many names, the true leaders of Angmar's army are nothing more than tyrants, and the symbol of their station will earn you favour with the Free Peoples. First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr has promised to reward you for the tyrant's lashes you bring her.'Pay attention, ${RACE}... I need your services.

'At the head of the war-host of Angmar are the tyrants who drive all others ahead of them. They are without fear and know only how to bring destruction to the world.

'Should you defeat one of these terrors, return to me with the lash which is the symbol of his command, and you shall be rewarded.''With every victory we achieve against the Ongbúrz leaders, we not only claim the land where they stand, but also weaken the war-host of Angmar. Your involvement is a blessing, ${PLAYER}. Deliver this to Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig to earn greater recognition of your efforts in the Ettenmoors.'Thisarti, a Haradrim master-archer, has snuck up from behind and fires on us with deadly aim. Deal with him quickly so he cannot fire on Aragorn and his troops.

