* Defeat Thisarti
* Defeat Thisarti quicklyDefeat the archer Thisarti swiftly, for his arrows and his aim are deadly.Defeat the archer Thisarti quickly<rgb=#FF0000>Defeat Thisarti before he falls back into the Corsair ranks</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Defeat Thisarti before he falls back into the Corsair ranks</rgb>Quartermaster Apsduf believes that the lesser creatures in Angmar's army -- spiders and Wargs -- need armour and thinks that he can assist them by crafting armour from the chitin of the Neekerbreekers nearby.Nerbyg, also called Neekerbreekers, dwell near the river-banks.

Quartermaster Apsduf directed you to collect chitin to craft the armour he intends for the Wargs and spiders.'Listen well, maggot. I'm working on getting protection on the vermin around us. Many think my idea foolish, but you've no opinion worth hearing... so you'll do as I say.

'Get the chitin from the little bugs hereabouts and return it to me so I can make it into suitable armour for Wargs and spiders.''We shall soon know if the chitin is worth crafting into armour for the vermin. Should this work, perhaps I can convince the War-tyrant to use them in our battle. You have earned a good word from me, ${PLAYER}.'The empty armours of Men who long ago fought in the Kin-strife now stalk the Erui. While their purpose remains unknown, their presence deeply unsettles friend and foe alike.Risen armours of fallen Kin-strife warriors can be found in the river Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have encountered armours given form by the waters of the Erui and should reclaim the armour pieces for the people of Gondor.Recover the armour of Kin-strife warriorsRisen armours of fallen Kin-strife warriors can be found in the river Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have encountered armours given form by the waters of the Erui and should reclaim the armour pieces for the people of Gondor.Recover the armour of Kin-strife warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glassiel can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have defeated many of the risen armours in the Erui, and should return the armour pieces you recovered to Glassiel.In the aftermath of your encounter with the Lone Lady, you have been assaulted by the Erui itself in the form of armours once worn by the Men who fought in the Kin-strife.

While you cannot tell if these armours belonged to Gondorians who fought for King Eldacar or Castamir the Usurper, you decide to bear them away to the people of Lebennin if only to deprive the Lone Lady this unsettling power.

Once you have recovered enough armours, perhaps Glassiel of Halach will know what should be done with them.'I am saddened to know that the Lone Lady has grown so cruel in her rage, but these armours are of great import to the history of our people.

'It is true that many of the Usurper's followers were left to rot in the waters of Erui alongside their master, but I never expected to see their armour pulled from the river-bed after so many centuries.

'I shall see that these are given to Lord Sirgon of Pelargir when this conflict has ended. As ruler of the home of the Ship-kings, he may decide their final place of rest.'The chests in the armoury are not locked, allowing the corsairs full access to the weaponry within.The chests must be locked to protect the weapons within.Lock chests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Reinforcing Tol Ascarnen requires tactics that are not often used in battle among the Free Peoples, but the forces from Angmar are nothing like the civilized peoples of Eriador, and so they must be stopped quickly. Captain-General Makan has ordered that archers be stationed behind the safety of the walls at the tunnel entrance of Tol Ascarnen, where they will unleash arrows at all who attempt to assault the keep.Kindling can be found among the fallen logs, and other pieces of wood found throughout the Ettenmoors. You will find a greater concentration near the Grimwood lumber-yard within Hithlad.

Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr sent you into the Ettenmoors in search of wooden shafts or kindling. He is making arrows to supply the Elves who will guard the front channel of Tol Ascarnen.'Yes, we still need shafts for our arrows, and the best way to collect those is to find fallen branches and logs from the Grimwood. I know that another here wishes you to collect them for him as well. Aiding either of us is aiding the Free Peoples, but aiding me will enable us to strengthen our position here.

'We need straight bits of wood to craft into arrow-shafts. Elves will be making their way here once we have enough arrows to support them. We need to hasten this task along, friend: Angmar will not rest. They will press us.

'Get the kindling we need from the wood you find laying about the Ettenmoors, I will wager there is more of it near the woods of Hithlad and the Grimwood lumber-camp. Be quick so that we can supply our forces.''Excellent work. I will set about crafting these arrows. Soon enough we will have the support of the Elves and be better able to fight off Angmar's assaults!'Reinforcing Tol Ascarnen requires tactics that are not often used in battle among the Free Peoples, but the forces from Angmar are nothing like the civilized peoples of Eriador and so they must be stopped quickly. Captain-General Makan has ordered that archers be stationed behind the safety of the walls at the tunnel entrance of Tol Ascarnen, where they will unleash arrows at all who attempt to assault the keep.Orcs and Uruks throughout the Ettenmoors carry the shattered blades taken from the Free Peoples that they defeat.

Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr sent you into the Ettenmoors in search of shattered blades. He is making arrows to supply the Elves who will guard the front channel of Tol Ascarnen.'The Elves will fire their bows but take no part in making the arrows. They need them, but they turn to the dwarves to collect them. Very well, say I.

'The Orcs and Uruks scattered throughout the Ettenmoors fight our forces, often breaking the blades of the fallen. These snapped blades can be melted down and made into arrowheads to use against the Orcs.

'It's a fitting honour to use the blades of the fallen to slay our enemies, and so we will do so. Go into the Ettenmoors and collect these broken blades. Return them to me so I can begin outfitting our troops.''Aye, these will do nicely. I will set about crafting these sundered weapons into something more fitting to strike down the Enemy. You have well earned your thanks for this, ${PLAYER}.'Arvaethor asks for assistance as he patrols the Vale and secures its safety.Arvaethor is near the pillaged lumber camp in Ringló Vale.

You should speak with Arvaethor.Speak with ArvaethorThis noble Arvaethor wishes to help you deal with the invasive White Mountain Orcs that descended upon Ringló Vale.

You should complete a number of tasks in Ringló Vale, using the whistle to call your friend for help if you become separated.Complete Vale of ShadowComplete In Ethring's DefenceComplete The Orkish PathComplete White Mountain PlagueComplete Under the White MountainUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated'Let us take back the Vale and push these Orcs into the mountains from whence they came! No longer will they pillage our trees and defile our waters.''Call me to your side when you wish to depart.''I thank you for your aid in protecting the people of Ethring. Still, there is much to do.'Forced into the tunnels under Osgiliath after a daring ploy by Faramir, the Rangers of Ithilien, led by Mablung, now hope to reunite with their lost captain.Damrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

Mablung has asked you to speak to Damrod about Faramir's daring attack that allowed many of their number to escape the city.Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have spoken to Damrod about Faramir's gambit, and should now speak to Mablung about searching for Faramir in the tunnels under Osgiliath.Talk to Mablung'Our captain, Faramir, is lost. All of our number became separated after he dealt a great blow to the Enemy's forces, and we only realized our loss after we regrouped here in the culverts.

'To my dismay, I was unaware of Faramir's ploy. It must have been a plan he put into action swiftly, but such haste did not lessen its impact. I heard a great shriek in the distance, like the deafening sounding of a Mûmak's trunk, but shrill as the pitch of a bat's cry. No sooner had the forces of the Enemy rallied to its source, and we were overwhelmed. We scattered, leading the foes with us, but we all made for the western gates... for our escape.

'I did not make it so far - great trolls blocked my advance, and I was forced to abandon my escape. I fled into the culverts and there I found the others. So it has been...

'If Faramir made it beyond the western gates, he may yet live, but that is unknown to us all. Damrod, one of my most trusted men, saw first-hand the fury Faramir loosed upon the Enemy. While he knows little else of Faramir's fate, all must be told of our captain's valour... especially if it may be his last.''You should speak to Damrod at once, my friend.  With his own eyes, he saw the mighty blow Faramir dealt to the host of Minas Morgul and knows well of the chaos that followed.''Mablung wishes for me to tell you of Faramir's daring assault? I shall tell it then, but until he is found, it shall have no ending.

'We had crossed to the eastern side of the city to disrupt the Enemy's forces before they could rally again. We were outnumbered, but we held the eastern end of the north-bridge for a time... until the most vile of the Enemy's forces took notice of us.

'A great, winged beast swooped down and swept a crowd of men aside, friend and foe alike, as if they were leaves amid the winds of a storm. Its wings blotted out the sun, and many of our number fled at once, but my captain and I held strong.

'Faramir took a spear from one of the fallen and called the beast as it clawed at the dead. Before I could stop him, he charged at the beast and thrust the spear into its dark heart. What happened then is a blur to me, for it let loose a great cry and thrashed in a fury as my captain and I fled to the west.

'We became separated on the bridge-rafts, and soon, forces of the Haradrim had cut me off from him completely. I was forced to retreat into the culverts, and that is where my story ends for now. Mablung seems to have a plan for you, and I would not deny him his chance to speak.

'Let us see what our next move shall be!''${PLAYER}, now you know of our plight. Will you stay and aid us here? Or do you heed the call of another? If you stay, our search shall begin at once, else I shall have to proceed with caution... for too few men still stand among us, and to weaken our guard is to invite defeat.

'If Faramir yet lives, I shall find my captain and have him lead his men to freedom beyond the Rammas Echor!'Desperate to learn of their lost captain's fate, Mablung and Damrod begin their search for Faramir in the winding tunnels beneath Osgiliath.Faramir might be found somewhere within the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath.

Mablung has asked you to search the depths of Osgiliath for Faramir, who may have fled into the tunnels in the wake of his attack on the fell-beast.

<rgb=#FF0000>You must complete the "Sunken Labyrinth" instance to complete this quest.</rgb>Search for Faramir in the depths of OsgiliathThe letter can be found at the make-shift camp-site in the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath.

You have discovered a small, empty camp-site in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath. You should take the note and examine it before pressing onward.Examine the note at the abandoned camp-siteFaramir might be found somewhere within the sunken labyrinth beneath Osgiliath.

You have not yet found Faramir in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath, but you should continue your search deeper in the labyrinth.Search further in the depths of OsgiliathThe Ranger is standing near the gate to Muzgásh's chamber in the sunken labyrinth.

You have defeated Muzgásh, but now a strange Ranger stands near the gate to his chambers. You should approach the Ranger and attempt to speak to him.Approach the mysterious RangerMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have recovered a troubling letter and encountered a strange hooded Ranger in the sunken tunnels of Osgiliath. You should now return to Mablung.'We must begin our search, ${PLAYER}, and I would have us begin here in the culverts where we can move beneath the notice of the Morgul-host above. It is possible that Faramir also fled into the tunnels as we did when the fighting erupted after he speared the fell-beast, but there are many places he may have sought refuge - and too few of us to spare from our posts.

'Search the depths, but do not search alone. These tunnels wind far underneath the city as a vast, sunken labyrinth, and it is likely that some of the Enemy's forces have travelled down into the dark - unwittingly or not.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: You must complete the "Sunken Labyrinth" instance to complete this quest.</rgb>'What news have you of your search, ${PLAYER}? There are many places where Faramir may have sought refuge in this sunken labyrinth, and I fear we shall not have time to search them all.''The tidings you bear disturb me, ${PLAYER}. The letter you bear mentions that terrible wraith thrust a blade into his chest, but that he did not die - only his body began to wither. It then reads only of a man succumbing to madness, and I fear his mind can only have grown more twisted since its writing.

'For Faramir to come to such an end would be devastating, and I fear that we must uncover this man's identity before our search can continue elsewhere. There are many ways out of these tunnels, but his flight cannot have taken him far from the culverts.'Disturbed by the note you recovered and your sighting of a mysterious Ranger in the depths of Osgiliath, Mablung sends you to the streets above to track this elusive stranger.Signs of the Ranger's passing can likely be found in southern Osgiliath, especially around the wharfs and nearby ruins.

Mablung has asked you to pursue the mysterious Ranger you encountered in the sunken tunnels of Osgiliath. By the way he took to escape, Mablung suggest searching the wharfs and the nearby ruins.Mablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have lost the trail of the mysterious Ranger, and should now report his elusiveness to Mablung.Return to Mablung and tell him of the Ranger's elusiveness'You have told me much of this strange man, ${PLAYER}, but most troubling is your description of his clothing.

'By your account, he bears a cloak that belonged to none but our captain, Faramir. If this man is Faramir, our cause is lost, and we should forge a new strategy to escape the city before dawn. However, if he is not - who would be so bold as to take up a mantle beyond his standing and elude the aid of his brethren?

'Search the southern ways of the city, on both shores of the Anduin, for his path would lead him either to the camps of the Haradrim or the ruins of the armoury across the Orkish bridge-rafts. Track him, and capture him if you must - for we must learn of his identity!''This man bears a grave wound, and yet eludes us at every turn... what force could empower a man so?

'We must hasten our search, and work to corner this man - be he friend or turned foe.'After losing the trail of the mysterious Ranger, Mablung asks you and your fellows to search the ruined city and uncover his identity at any cost.The mysterious Ranger can be found somewhere within the ruined city of Osgiliath.

Mablung has asked you to search the ruined city for any sign of the mysterious Ranger you encountered in the sunken tunnels.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: You must complete "The Ruined City" instance to complete this quest.</rgb>Pursue and confront the mysterious RangerThe fallen Ranger can be found inside the Palace of Eldacar.

You have defeated the corrupted Ranger bearing the cloak of Faramir and should now reclaim it for the Rangers of Ithilien.Reclaim Faramir's cloak from the fallen RangerMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have defeated the corrupted Ranger that bore Faramir's cloak. You should now return the cloak to Mablung.'I do not know what compels this man to flee at our approach, but it is clear that we must capture him before his madness can overtake him. His wound needs the care of a practiced healer, and yet he can still run as fast as any of our number. I fear that this bodes ill for us, ${PLAYER}, but I do not wish to abandon hope.

'Whether he is friend or foe, I would have you subdue him for his mind is not his own. You must not lose his trail this time, or I fear we will never have another opportunity to learn of his identity.

'Throughout your pursuit, he remained in the southern streets of the ruined city, so I would have you begin your search there once again. However, I suggest you bring your allies, for with them it may be easier to subdue this strange man and return to us in the culverts.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: You must complete "The Ruined City" instance to complete this quest.</rgb>'Lúmithil was a bold Ranger, and I am saddened that the Enemy twisted him into something so vile. His death shall be mourned, and, if I were to have my way, avenged! Sadly, a foe who bears no form does not make vengeance an easy task...

'While I am glad that Faramir did not meet with such a fate, we are no closer to finding him, and I fear our trail has gone cold.

'Allow me a moment to ponder our course of action, and I shall speak to you once more.'After pursuing and defeating the Ranger corrupted by a Morgul-blade, Faramir's trail is all but lost. As his hope begins to wane, Mablung sends you to the location where Faramir struck down a mighty fell-beast of Mordor.The site where Faramir speared the great fell-beast can be found to the north-east of the Dome of Stars.

In desperation, Mablung has asked you to search the site where Faramir speared a fell-beast in hopes of uncovering where he may have gone.Search the site where Faramir slew the fell-beastThe broken spear can be found near the ruined bridge to the north-east of the Dome of Stars.

You have found the site as well as the broken spear that Faramir once wielded. You should examine the spear.Examine Faramir's broken spearMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have encountered one of the Nazgûl, the Black Blade of Lebennin, who claims to hold Faramir captive atop the Dome of Stars. You should tell Mablung of this at once.Talk to Mablung of the Nazgûl's captive'We are without direction, my friend. The trail is cold, and none that live know of Faramir's fate. Alas for poor Lúmithil... may he be at peace.

'I have thought much on where our search might continue, and one thought has lingered in my mind. You have done much for us, but this may be too perilous a task to put upon you. Since our flight into the culverts, none of us have dared to return to the site where Faramir speared the great fell-beast. 

'I thought our course wise, and it may still be, but I must ask you to travel there, my friend. What became of the beast? Did it fall as we thought? Has some hidden insight to our captain's flight gone unnoticed? These thoughts trouble my mind, ${PLAYER}, and I cannot rest.

'If you dare, travel far to the north-east, beyond the Dome of Stars... and search by the broken north-bridge. When you find Faramir's spear, you shall know you have found the site.''It cannot be! Hope is lost, ${PLAYER}. None can stand against the servants of the Dark Lord... their might is limitless!

'Even if this Nazgûl - this "Black Blade" speaks true, how can we be assured that Faramir's fate will be any different than that of Lúmithil? Our captain may already serve the Dark Lord, if still he lives.'One of the Nazgûl, the Black Blade of Lebennin, has revealed himself as Faramir's captor and now holds the captain of the South-rangers atop the Dome of Stars.The Black Blade of Lebennin and his captive can be found atop the Dome of Stars.

Mablung has asked you to free Fararmir from the Black Blade of Lebennin and attempt to banish his spirit before the coming battle.

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: You must complete "The Dome of Stars" instance to complete this quest.</rgb>Confront and defeat the Black Blade of LebenninFree Faramir from the Dome of StarsMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have triumphed over the Black Blade of Lebennin if only for a moment, and learned of Faramir's fate. You should return to Mablung with this news.Talk to Mablung and tell him of Faramir's fate'I know not if Faramir lives or if this is merely one of the Nazgûl's vile designs to draw the last of us from hiding. I cannot know, and it pains me to face such uncertainty without the guidance of our captain.

'The Dome of Stars lies in the heart of the Enemy's forces and until they wrested control of the western city, it was there that the leaders of the host oversaw their cruel servants. It is still a place of great evil, and dread grips the entire isle on which it stands.

'The Enemy has thrown down the western bridge to the Dome, so the only way into the structure is across the eastern bridge by Rómendacil's Square. The Enemy has heightened their guard near the culverts, so I can guide you to the western side of the Great Bridge safely, but no further.

'Do not dare face the Black Blade alone, for you will need all the allies you can muster to stand against such evil. Faramir's fate may well rest in your hands, my friend. May your fellowship be the light to pierce these ashen skies...'

<rgb=#FF0000>Note: You must complete "The Dome of Stars" instance to complete this quest.</rgb>'My captain is held prisoner by one of the Nazgûl... never has there been a darker day in my life.

'I know the strength of Faramir's resolve well, but so too do I know the might of the Enemy. If he yet lives and the wraith speaks true, we must act swiftly!''You have come... seeking Faramir?

Struggling to speak, Norhún's coughs are wet with blood.

'He... is gone - gone from Osgiliath. We had made it to the western gates when the shadow... fell upon us. I threw myself in its path, and soon I was carried above by a terrible, winged beast. From the sky, I saw my captain escape... he passed along the Causeway and through the Rammas Echor before I lost sight of him.

'Tell the others of his fate, for they must know that he still lives!

'The wraith... he...'

Norhún's breath slows, and is still.'I cannot believe it! I felt a cold rush pass over the city as I looked to the Dome outside the culverts... could that have been his foul spirit sent away to the Land of Shadow?

'You have done a truly great thing, my friend, but Faramir is not among your number.... Tell me, ${PLAYER}, what has become of my captain?'Through Norhún's steadfast loyalty and sacrifice, Faramir was able to escape the western gates of Osgiliath. Their hope restored, Mablung and his men make ready for the journey ahead.Damrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

Mablung has asked you to tell Damrod of Faramir's escape from Osgiliath.Talk to DamrodMablung can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have told Damrod of your successes in Osgiliath and should now speak to Mablung once more.Talk to Mablung'What has become of Faramir, ${PLAYER}? Were you too late to save him?'

You tell Mablung of Norhún's sacrifice and his bravery in allowing Faramir to escape from the western gates of Osgiliath.

'My captain lives yet! I shall rest easier knowing Faramir made it past the Gates of the Sun, even though his fate beyond remains unclear. Such a sacrifice... Norhún shall be hailed as a hero among my people, I swear it.'

Mablung turns to Damrod and gestures for him to listen.

'Damrod, have you heard this joyous news?''You slew the wraith? Is such a feat possible? The servants of the Dark Lord do not suffer defeat easily, my friend... but let us hope that we shall be free of his evil for a time.

'Faramir has escaped beyond the Causeway Forts into the Pelennor Fields? This is a joyous turn, indeed, but I fear we must not forget the horrors looming above.

'I sense the war shall soon reach a turning point, and I hope you will be among us at that critical hour.''As merry a day as this may be, Damrod speaks true.

'The might of the Morgul-host stands poised to spill forth into the Pelennor Fields and to the very walls of Minas Tirith. Through your efforts, we have slowed their advance, but the thousands that rally above cannot be stopped... not by us alone.

'Take your leave, ${PLAYER}, and rest well after this victory... but be ready. For on the morrow, the war for Gondor shall truly begin!'The corsairs are burning the books from the great library of Dol Amroth.The books must be saved and preserved.Recover books (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The host of Angmar swept into the central keep of the Ettenmoors and drove Captain-General Makan from Tol Ascarnen. This affront is more than an honourable dwarf can stand, and First Marshal Án will stop at nothing to take it back, though he wants assurances that the force he leads will stand beside him.Tokens of valour are bestowed at Glân Vraig. First Marshal Án is at the camp south of Tol Ascarnen.

