'I think you are right, ${PLAYER}. He is the key to ending the threat of Umbar. We have to find him and put an end to his leadership of the Corsairs.'Aragorn agrees that the threat of Umbar will not be ended until you face Balakhôr the Scourge on his flagship.Aragorn is at his camp in Lebennin, outside the city of Pelargir.

Aragorn is ready to put an end to Balakhôr the Scourge, and the threat of Umbar, once and for all.Talk to Aragorn and storm Balakhôr's flagship, the Night-jewelAragorn is outside the city of Pelargir.

You have driven Balakhôr away in shame, and the threat of Umbar is ended for now.Talk to Aragorn at his camp outside Pelargir'I knew the flagship Night-jewel at once, for it dominates the harbour. That is where we will find Balakhôr the Scourge, and put an end to the threat of Umbar. Speak to me when you are ready to do this.''Most of the Corsairs have fled in terror, but Balakhôr will not be without his defences. Remain on your guard, and I will remain on mine!''We have ended the threat of Umbar for now, and Balakhôr will rally no more Corsairs to his banner. The memory of the Dead will keep others from taking up arms against Gondor. Now my attention must turn to the foe in the East.

'The shadow of unending night will lend speed and surety to the armies of the Enemy. They will march upon Minas Tirith. Indeed, they must have already begun! I must get to the city with utmost haste, but the Gondorian fleet is burned. What can be done?'

Aragorn thinks for a moment, and then a strange light flickers within his eyes.

'Black sails, ${PLAYER}. I will sail the ships of Umbar to Minas Tirith. Let us rest for a brief while, and then we will make ready the ships. I thank you again for your part in this most recent victory, my friend! Rest now, and then we will return to the tasks ahead of us.'The threat of the Corsairs is over, but Aragorn does not have any time to rest. He has another charge for you, one that must be completed with haste and with utmost secrecy.Haradrim fleeing in the direction of the town of Erynos, east and north of Aragorn's camp, must be defeated before they can bring word of his victory at Pelargir.

Aragorn has asked you to find tracks left by terrified Haradrim near the town of Erynos.Haradrim fleeing in the direction of the town of Erynos, east and north of Aragorn's camp, must be defeated before they can bring word of his victory at Pelargir.

Aragorn has asked you to find tracks left by terrified Haradrim near the town of Erynos.Thurineth has some news for you at the gate of Erynos.

You defeated several of the Haradrim that fled from Pelargir, and a woman has hailed you from the gate of Erynos.Talk to Thurineth at the gate of ErynosThurineth saw a Haradrim sorcerer creeping around the outer wall of the town of Erynos, and wanted you to defeat him before you leave.Talk to the Haradrim Sorcerer near ErynosAragorn is at the Camp of the Grey Host, to the north-west of Pelargir.

You have tracked down and defeated the Haradrim warriors that fled from Pelargir.Talk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Grey Host'The threat of the Corsairs is over, but many of their allies still live and could endanger my next course, ${PLAYER}!

'Several of the Haradrim fled from the city when the Men of the Mountain fulfilled their oath, and I fear they might bring word of the Corsair defeat to the armies of Mordor. I would rather this did not happen, but I cannot spare the time to track all who fled from Pelargir. Will you do this for me, my friend?

'Travel east in pursuit of these terrified Haradrim! I believe they will come to the walls of Erynos before they can break free of their fright. Defeat them and keep word of our victory at Pelargir from reaching unfriendly ears!''Travel east in pursuit of terrified Haradrim! I believe they will come to the walls of Erynos before they can break free of their fright. Defeat them and keep word of our victory at Pelargir from reaching unfriendly ears!''Travel east in pursuit of terrified Haradrim! I believe they will come to the walls of Erynos before they can break free of their fright. Defeat them and keep word of our victory at Pelargir from reaching unfriendly ears!''I watched you fight those evil warriors, hero, and I wanted to thank you for making safe our lands! But that is not all, for if you leave now you leave us still in peril!

'I saw another one of these invaders nearby. I think he fancies himself a sorcerer of some sort, for he carried many unsavoury trinkets and muttered strange incantations under his breath.

'He crept that way, around the outer wall of Erynos!''I saw another one of these invaders nearby. I think he fancies himself a sorcerer of some sort, for he carried many unsavoury trinkets and muttered strange incantations under his breath.

'He crept that way, around the outer wall of Erynos!''You may slay my men, hated ${RACE}, and you may end my own life, but you will have no lasting victory. The Great Master we follow is a giver of gifts, and he gives life unending to those who faithfully serve! You could slay all the Corsairs to a man, and all of my own people, but the commanders of the Master's army will always return, even in death!''Did you put an end to that sorcerer? I did not like the look of his trinkets or the sound of his mutterings!''You found the Haradrim that fled from Pelargir? Very good, ${PLAYER}! I hope this will keep word of our victory here a secret from the enemy. But something troubles you. Share it with me, and we will bear the burden of it together, my friend!'

You tell Aragorn of the sorcerer's words: that the commanders of Sauron's armies cannot be stopped, even by death.

'I confess to you that I have heard these whispers as well, my friend, so I cannot banish the fear of them from your mind. But it does not change my resolve, and I believe it will not change yours, either. We place a greater value on life than does our Enemy, so every loss pains us all the more. But that is our strength as well for we will fight even harder to protect it, even beyond our limits.'

Aragorn smiles.

'Ours is not the real quest, ${PLAYER}, for even if we have all the success we desire, the Enemy will remain. The real quest is elsewhere, my friend, and only its successful completion can end Sauron's evil forever.''Travel east in pursuit of terrified Haradrim! I believe they will come to the walls of Erynos before they can break free of their fright. Defeat them and keep word of our victory at Pelargir from reaching unfriendly ears!'Aragorn has a plan: he wishes to sail up the river on the deck of the Corsair ships, coming to the aid of Minas Tirith to the surprise of its enemies.Aragorn has asked you to help the members of the Grey Company prepare to depart on the Corsair ships bound for Minas Tirith.

<rgb=#00FF00>Rangers at the Camp of the Grey Host have begun to perform Aragorn's tasks. Help them with their 'Black Sails' quests to fulfill his wishes.</rgb>Aragorn is at the Camp of the Grey Host, waiting for your report on the preparations of the Corsair ships.Talk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Grey HostAngbor the Fearless is at the Camp of the Grey Host, waiting to speak with you.

Aragorn is ready to depart for Minas Tirith on the Corsair ships, and has asked you to travel overland with Angbor and his men to learn the state of the war.Talk to Angbor at the Camp of the Grey Host'We still have our own parts to play, and I deem it important that we play them well! I wish to sail up the river on the deck of the Corsair ships, and come by that route to the aid of Minas Tirith. It is my hope that we will arrive in time and with such surprise that we can strike a blow to the fighting will of those who threaten the city.

'We do not have much time to prepare, but there are a number of tasks I have given my friends to perform that will help us set forth as quickly as possible. Help them with these tasks, if you would, for every moment we hesitate is a moment the Enemy would relish!''We do not have much time to prepare, but there are a number of tasks I have given my friends to perform that will help us set forth as quickly as possible. Help them with these tasks, if you would, for every moment we hesitate is a moment the Enemy would relish!''I asked that you help prepare the ships with haste, but I did not expect such speed even from you, ${PLAYER}! I thank you for your efforts and know that we are put in the best position we could be as a result.

'I have given some thought to this next request, my friend, and I hope you agree with me on this. I do not ask you to accompany me on the ships. Instead, I ask you to travel by land through Upper Lebennin and Lossarnach. We must learn the state of the war to the east. The vale of Tumladen and the town of Imloth Melui had strong walls of old, and were used as places of safety for the people in times of war. The people there will tell you much of what has transpired elsewhere in Gondor. Angbor will go that way as well, with his men, and will be a boon companion as you go.

'I have another purpose for you, my trusted friend. I want you to find Gandalf or true-hearted Faramir in Minas Tirith and tell them about our victory here. Tell no others! In Faramir I place the trust I would not give to the father. There is too much I do not know about the situation in the White City.''I have heard a great deal about you, ${PLAYER}, and I welcome you as a travelling companion into the lands to the east. If you are half as brave and skilled as Aragorn tells me, we shall have no trouble at all!'Aragorn has given you an important mission: to travel by land the route he takes by ship, and come in that way to Minas Tirith to find Gandalf or Faramir.The road into Upper Lebennin passes through the port-city of Pelargir.

Angbor has asked you to travel east into Upper Lebennin and to defeat many of the Haradrim there.Defeat Haradrim in Upper Lebennin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The vale of Tumladen is in the northern reaches of Upper Lebennin.

You have defeated many Haradrim in Upper Lebennin and should now find the vale of Tumladen.Find the entrance to the vale of Tumladen, in Upper LebenninMany refugees from elsewhere in Gondor can be found throughout the vale of Tumladen.Angbor has come to the entrance to the vale of Tumladen.

You have learned that folk have been evacuated from Minas Tirith, and the war is about to be joined. You should find Angbor and tell him what you have learned.Talk to Angbor outside the entrance to the vale of TumladenAngbor wants you to travel east of Tumladen to the Crossings of Erui, and to defeat the Haradrim camped there.Find the Crossings of Erui, east of TumladenDefeat Haradrim that threaten the Crossings of Erui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Angbor keeps watch on a hill just to the west of the Crossings of Erui.Talk to Angbor on the small hill west of the Crossings of Erui'Before he departed for Minas Tirith, Prince Imrahil charged me with the defence of the fiefs he left behind. I accepted this duty, knowing it might end in death, and left my son to protect my own lands. I engaged the Corsairs and Southrons at the city of Linhir, but we were heavily outnumbered and our defeat seemed certain.

'And then a new force joined the fray: a vast army of shadows from the forbidden paths under the mountains! They were Dead Men, and they brought death with them, silent and sure. My men cast aside their weapons and fled, but I stood my ground, and when I saw the banner of he who led them I was glad, for it was Aragorn, and he rode 'neath the standard of the King. 'Fearless' he called me, but what man can be afraid when a King has returned to a kingdom that needs him?

'I have four thousand men with me, and they will travel behind us. It will be slow going for them, so we will ride ahead and see what awaits them. Let us fight the Southrons in Upper Lebennin and clear the way for their swords! Then we will come to the vale of Tumladen and see the state of the war.''I have four thousand men with me, and they will travel behind us. It will be slow going for them, so we will ride ahead and see what awaits them. Let us fight the Southrons in Upper Lebennin and clear the way for their swords! Then we will come to Tumladen and see the state of the war.''Find the vale of Tumladen in Upper Lebennin, and see how the war has treated the rest of the kingdom. I will follow behind with four thousand swords and strong men to wield them!''Find the vale of Tumladen in Upper Lebennin, and see how the war has treated the rest of the kingdom. I will follow behind with four thousand swords and strong men to wield them!''Do you plan to travel to Minas Tirith? I would advise you to rethink your course! If the city is not already besieged, it soon will be! Much of my family has been evacuated, but my sons remained behind at the request of their commander. They will defend the city, and are glad for the chance, but I am afraid for them.

'As we left Minas Tirith, I saw smoke rising from Osgiliath. I hope Faramir holds it still, but I do not know how long even he can last. He is the son of the Steward and very brave, but I have heard that the armies arrayed against us are vast and uncaring. I have heard also that Boromir left on an errand to the north, and has not yet returned. I would feel better for my sons if Boromir returned and stood on the front lines... may it be soon!

'Right now we await word that it is safe to return to the city. Tumladen has enough supplies for its garrison, now absent, so we should be able to stay as long as necessary. But I hope this is resolved quickly.''Hullo there! You look like a real adventurer! Are you really a hero?'

The boy looks at you with wide eyes and an admiring expression.

'You must be journeying to Minas Tirith! They are going to need you there, I am certain of it! There is going to be a war... it may have already started! Are you going to be in the thick of the fighting? I would be, if they'd let me!

'I heard there was a Halfling in the White City! I did not see him, but he could not have been much taller than I am, and I wager he will be allowed to fight! Why not me? I heard tell he was a friend of Mithrandir, the Grey Pilgrim. Perhaps that is the reason.

'Some folk have all the good fortune, and leave none for the rest of us! It is not fair!''They say I am too old to fight, even if the desire to protect my home and my family burns as brightly within my bosom as it does within those of younger men. I am not afraid to die, if that death were to be in service of Steward Denethor or his brave sons!

'Still I have been carted here to wait for the end with the children and the women. What justice is there in that? They say the son of the Steward holds Osgiliath, but how long can he hope to stand against all the armies that pour out of the East? That city has changed hands before, but it seems to this old man that the next time it falls may be the last.

'When that happens, I think they will rue sending us away. The White City will have need of folk to wield swords, no matter their ages. Mark my words, and mark them well!''As we left Minas Tirith, I saw smoke rising from Osgiliath. I hope Faramir holds it still, but I do not know how long even he can last. He is the son of the Steward and very brave, but I have heard that the armies arrayed against us are vast and uncaring. I have heard also that Boromir left on an errand to the north, and has not yet returned. I would feel better for my sons if Boromir returned and stood on the front lines... may it be soon!

'Right now we await word that it is safe to return to the city. Tumladen has enough supplies for its garrison, now absent, so we should be able to stay as long as necessary. But I hope this is resolved quickly.''I heard there was a Halfling in the White City! I did not see him, but he could not have been much taller than I am, and I wager he will be allowed to fight! Why not me? I heard tell he was a friend of Mithrandir, the Grey Pilgrim. Perhaps that is the reason.

'Some folk have all the good fortune, and leave none for the rest of us! It is not fair!''They say the son of the Steward holds Osgiliath, but how long can he hope to stand against all the armies that pour out of the East? That city has changed hands before, but it seems to this old man that the next time it falls may be the last.

'When that happens, I think they will rue sending us away. The White City will have need of folk to wield swords, no matter their ages. Mark my words, and mark them well!''You have done good work here. I suspected that we would find these havens full of refugees from the White City, which means that the war will soon be joined if it has not already begun.

'Four thousand swords travel slowly, but when they arrive they will make all their points, with sharp arguments! We must make sure their path is free of obstruction. There is a good place to cross the River Erui, to the south, but it is held by the Haradrim. Let us go to the Crossings and defeat these Southrons so my army can pass.

'Any Haradrim in Upper Lebennin pose a threat to the Crossings, and they must be stopped!''The Haradrim hold the Crossings. They must be defeated.''Four thousand swords travel slowly, but when they arrive they will make all their points, with sharp arguments! We must make sure their path is free of obstruction. There is a good place to cross the River Erui, to the east, but it is held by the Haradrim. Let us go to the Crossings and defeat these Southrons so my army can pass.''Very good, my friend. You have disrupted the preparations of the Haradrim, and my men will be able to cross the Erui without fear of Southron fortifications. Even a force of four thousand can suffer many losses when attacking a much smaller force, provided the smaller force has time to prepare.'Angbor is ready to cross into Lossarnach, continuing the journey toward Minas Tirith and the onset of war with the forces of evil.Angbor has asked you to travel to the meeting of the roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach, to learn the state of the war in that land.Find the meeting of the roads just south of Imloth Melui, in LossarnachBandron and Nethadan have stopped their waggon south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach, and you should find out what has brought them here and why they have stopped.Talk to Bandron on the road south of Imloth MeluiBandron has asked you to go to Harlond and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> at certain locations to determine whether it is safe for him to go that way: the entrance of the city, the docks, and the gate in the Rammas Echor, the Pelennor's encircling wall.Bandron is by his waggon in Lossarnach, south of Imloth Melui.

You have investigated the port of the Harlond and found that it is occupied by the enemy. Bandron will not be able to go that way.Talk to Bandron on the road south of Imloth MeluiNethadan is somewhere within Imloth Melui, looking for a purchaser for the Cemenduril liquor.Talk to Nethadan in Imloth MeluiBandron is on the road south of Imloth Melui, waiting for his son Nethadan to return.Talk to Bandron on the road south of Imloth MeluiAngbor is standing by Bandron's waggon on the road south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach.Talk to Angbor on the road south of Imloth Melui'Lossarnach is a land of beauty, but we must not slow our steps to admire its sweet-smelling flowers! There will be time enough for that when this war is won! We must go to Minas Tirith. The fields of the Pelennor outside the White City are encircled by a great wall, the Rammas Echor, through which we must pass.

'The south-gate in the Rammas is located in the haven of the Harlond. That is where we must go. First we will do as Aragorn requested, and see how fares the settlement of Imloth Melui, to the north along the road. There is a meeting of roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach. Let us go there and assess the situation.''We must go to Minas Tirith. The fields of the Pelennor outside the White City are encircled by a great wall, the Rammas Echor, through which we must pass.

'The south-gate in the Rammas is located in the haven of the Harlond. That is where we must go. First we will do as Aragorn requested, and see how fares the settlement of Imloth Melui, to the north along the road. There is a meeting of roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach. Let us go there and assess the situation.''I did not expect to see you again, ${PLAYER}.''Oh, hello there, ${PLAYER}. How have you been keeping? I have been doing well.

'My father was not pleased with me when I returned to him in Tarlang's Neck, but he is always looking for a reason to be unhappy. I told him to look on the bright side, as I do. After all, we will never want for nails! I have never known him to have enough of something before, and now he does. How many can say that? Very few folk!''We must go to Minas Tirith. The fields of the Pelennor outside the White City are encircled by a great wall, the Rammas Echor, through which we must pass.

'The south-gate in the Rammas is located in the haven of the Harlond. That is where we must go. First we will do as Aragorn requested, and see how fares the settlement of Imloth Melui, to the north along the road. There is a meeting of roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach. Let us go there and assess the situation.''Oh, hello there, ${PLAYER}. How have you been keeping? I have been doing well.

'My father was not pleased with me when I returned to him in Tarlang's Neck, but he is always looking for a reason to be unhappy. I told him to look on the bright side, as I do. After all, we will never want for nails! I have never known him to have enough of something before, and now he does. How many can say that? Very few folk!''I did not expect to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I am not too proud to tell you that when Nethadan returned to my waggon with that second barrel of nails, I considered giving up on my profession and becoming a recluse then and there! I weighed that course very seriously, but in the end I decided it would be shameful to surrender to such a trial and I remain a waggon-driver.

'My son has done nothing but make me regret that choice ever since! "Father, I ate too many apples." "Father, I think I have a splinter." "Father, I miss the sun." When I was a boy, I would have taken this eternal night with more grace than he does, truly.

'We are bound for Minas Tirith and its Houses of Healing with a supply of Cemenduril liquor from Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, but I do not know if we will have safe passage. We encountered a traveller on the road who says the Harlond is full of Orcs! Can you investigate if this is so? There are three places I would know about, in particular: the entrance to Harlond, the docks, and the gate-house in the Rammas Echor, the wall that encircles the Pelennor.''We are bound for Minas Tirith and its Houses of Healing with a supply of Cemenduril liquor from Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, but I do not know if we will have safe passage. We encountered a traveller on the road who says the Harlond is full of Orcs! Can you investigate if this is so?''The Harlond is overrun? If we cannot get to the south-gate in the Rammas, we will not be able to bring our wares to Minas Tirith! What is it like to have good fortune? I would truly like to know, for I have never had it!

'If there is a bright side to this news, it is that I suspected it was so. No ill news is truly surprising to me anymore, ${PLAYER}! We cannot return to Galengam without selling his goods, so I sent Nethadan to Imloth Melui to find a purchaser for our Cemenduril liquor. Go north to the town and find my son, for he has not yet returned.''We cannot return to Galengam without selling his goods, so I sent Nethadan to Imloth Melui to find a purchaser for our Cemenduril liquor. Go north to the town and find my son, for he has not yet returned.''Hello there, ${PLAYER}! What good timing! I was just telling these ladies about some of our adventures. Do you remember when we fought off those Corsair raiders together? That was really something, was it not?'

Nethadan already looks happier than you have ever seen him, and his mood only improves when you tell him that the road through the Harlond is closed.

'How unfortunate! How ill-fated! Even so, I think this will be a fine place to stay until the road is clear. This is the perfect place to bring our waggon of valuable healing liquors. Did you know that this town has produced some of the finest healers in all the kingdom?

'Now where was I? Oh yes! I have always sought to provide for my family and my dear old dad. He will never want for nails, for example....''I think this will be a fine place to stay until the road is clear. This is the perfect place to bring our waggon of valuable healing liquors. Did you know that this town has produced some of the finest healers in all the kingdom?

'Now where was I? Oh yes! I have always sought to provide for my family and my dear old dad. He will never want for nails, for example....''This waggon-driver serves Galengam, a merchant from my own town of Calembel. I have found Galengam's prices to be rather higher than is fair, and have spoken to the merchant about it before.''I did not know you travelled with Lord Angbor of Lamedon, ${PLAYER}! It is my honour to serve him in any way I can, and I truly hope you have no tidings of Nethadan that might embarrass me in the presence of my liege!'

Bandron is shaking with obvious terror of what you might say, and he exhales with obvious relief when you tell him that Nethadan believes Imloth Melui will be a good place to stay until the road through the Harlond is open.

'That is my responsible boy! I have often prided myself on the example he sets for others, my Lord Angbor! Why, I think he seeks to model his behaviour after your own son, Drambor. That is my Nethadan, all right!'

Privately, you think to yourself that perhaps both father and son have more in common than either would admit.'That is my responsible boy! I have often prided myself on the example he sets for others, my Lord Angbor! Why, I think he seeks to model his behaviour after your own son, Drambor. That is my Nethadan, all right!''The waggon-driver's son speaks wisdom. I have heard that Imloth Melui is known for the quality of its healers, and the folk here will know the value of the goods on this waggon.'Angbor and his four thousand men must get to Minas Tirith, but the only acceptable road for such a force leads through the south-gate of the Rammas, which is held by a large enemy force.A friend of Gondor operates a secret ferry across the river among the reeds that border the Anduin, on the eastern side of Lossarnach.

Angbor has asked you to enter Ithilien by yourself while he seeks to assail the Harlond with his army.Find the secret ferry among the reeds in the eastern reaches of LossarnachA friend of Gondor operates a secret ferry across the river among the reeds that border the Anduin, on the eastern side of Lossarnach.

Angbor has asked you to enter Ithilien by yourself while he seeks to assail the Harlond with his army.Talk to the secret ferrywomanYou have been given permission to cross into Ithilien and seek Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin, as long as you defeat Haradrim in those woods as you go.Defeat Haradrim in South Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have crossed into Ithilien and seek Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin.Find the camp of Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin, in South IthilienDuilin is at the camp of Faramir's Rangers, at Bâr Húrin in South Ithilien.

Duilin of the Blackroot Vale has called your name and beckoned you to speak to him.Talk to Duilin at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien'Enemy forces must have crossed the Anduin and taken the port of the Harlond by surprise. They have had time enough to fortify the south-gate of the Rammas against us. That makes things more difficult to be sure. Only that road can support the movement of my four thousand men. We simply do not have the time or the resources to ferry that many warriors across the Anduin, and moving them through the forests of Ithilien in a wide sweep would be far too slow and take too much time. If we take such a course, the war will be ended before my men get there! No, they must retake the Harlond, and they will need me to lead them in this effort.

'You, however, have another errand. Aragorn wanted you to reach either Gandalf or Faramir? You can take a single craft across the Anduin and move more swiftly than four thousand. You must pass into Ithilien and come by that way to Osgiliath. Meanwhile, my men will assail the Harlond.

'My scouts learned that a friend to Gondor operates a secret ferry to the east, among the high reeds that border the river. Find her and see if she will bring you across the river into Ithilien, ${PLAYER}.''My scouts learned that a friend to Gondor operates a secret ferry to the east, among the high reeds that border the river. Find her and see if she will bring you across the river into Ithilien, ${PLAYER}.''My scouts learned that a friend to Gondor operates a secret ferry to the east, among the high reeds that border the river. Find her and see if she will bring you across the river into Ithilien, ${PLAYER}.''You approach from the west? I have seen precious few foe-men come from that way. Most enemies to Gondor have come from the east. Why do you seek to cross the river?'

You tell the woman that you have important tidings of the war, but have sworn to give them only to Gandalf the Wizard or to Faramir of Minas Tirith.

'I suspected as much, and will not ask for you to break your vow. I have not seen any Wizards in these parts, and the name Gandalf is unknown to me, but Faramir has spent more time of late ranging in the woods of Ithilien than he has in the White City. You are welcome to use my boat, and to have this advice: seek for Faramir and his Rangers at Bâr Húrin, to the east. I ask only this: defeat any Haradrim you encounter in Ithilien. They are a danger to my friends and my kingdom.''Faramir has spent more time of late ranging in the woods of Ithilien than he has in the White City. You are welcome to use my boat, and to have this advice: seek for Faramir and his Rangers at Bâr Húrin, to the east. I ask only this: defeat any Haradrim you encounter in Ithilien. They are a danger to my friends and my kingdom.''Faramir has spent more time of late ranging in the woods of Ithilien than he has in the White City. You are welcome to use my boat, and to have this advice: seek for Faramir and his Rangers at Bâr Húrin, to the east. I ask only this: defeat any Haradrim you encounter in Ithilien. They are a danger to my friends and my kingdom.''Faramir has spent more time of late ranging in the woods of Ithilien than he has in the White City. You are welcome to use my boat, and to have this advice: seek for Faramir and his rangers at Bâr Húrin, to the east. I ask only this: defeat any Haradrim you encounter in Ithilien. They are a danger to my friends and my kingdom.''I knew it was you the moment you came to this place! The Rangers of Ithilien have been watching your progress through the woods, speaking of your deeds, and my brother and I have been looking forward to meeting you!

'I am Duilin, and this is my brother Derufin. We are no Rangers! We are from the Blackroot Vale, far west of here, and we marched to Minas Tirith with our father when the beacons were lit. And then... nothing. Sitting in idleness while excitement happens elsewhere has never been to either of our tastes, so we escaped from the White City and crossed the river in secret.

'Now we seek adventure!'You have encountered Duilin and Derufin of the Blackroot Vale, becoming entangled in their quest to hunt the giant Mûmakil the Haradrim have brought to Gondor.Duilin is at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien.

You have grudgingly agreed to help Duilin and Derufin hunt the mighty Mûmakil, in return for their help finding Faramir.Talk to Duilin and hunt the mighty MûmakilDuilin is at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien.

The Mûmak hunt did not go as planned, but Duilin and Derufin do not seem to mind.Talk to Duilin at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien'The people of the Blackroot Vale know of our grand adventures throughout the wild, and certainly speak of the ferocious creatures we have hunted. They will be as nothing compared to the prey we now seek: the mighty Mûmakil!

'The Rangers have seen these great beasts in the service of the Haradrim of the south, but so far none have felled even a single Mûmak. My brother and I will be the first to do so, and we would be honoured for you to accompany us on this hunt!'

You tell Duilin that you are looking for Faramir, and cannot delay from that errand.

'He is not here, but if you help us hunt the mighty Mûmakil, you have my word that the sons of Blackroot will help you find him! Speak to me when you are ready to depart, ${PLAYER}!''I can hardly contain my excitement! It is time to hunt the mighty Mûmakil the Haradrim have brought to Gondor!''What a delight! Did you see the size of those Mûmakil? They were even larger than I expected, and twice as ferocious! I am still winded from their pursuit, and I could not be happier about it!'

Duilin's eyes are bright and words tumble from him in an excited torrent.

'Next time we will have one for sure! Their hides are thick, but seeing them up close has shown me where to aim: their eyes! That is the only unprotected spot... I see that now! Oh, what a prize this will be! And certainly it will be pleasant to deprive the Haradrim of such a mighty beast of war. But think of the tales they will sing of my brother and me! And you too, ${PLAYER}!

'But for now we are to help you with an errand of your own, I suppose.'Duilin and Derufin have agreed to travel with you to Osgiliath. There you hope to learn the state of the defences and what has become of Faramir.Faramir and his men may be found within the Osgiliath Culverts beneath the city, if they still stand against the armies of the enemy.Find Faramir or his men within the Osgiliath CulvertsDamrod and the few Gondorian soldiers that still defend Osgiliath can be found among the culverts beneath the city.Talk to Damrod among the Osgiliath CulvertsOrcs can be found throughout Osgiliath, and Damrod hopes that you might find Faramir or soldiers with news of him in the south-western area of the city.Defeat Orcs throughout Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search the south-western area of Osgiliath for one of Damrod's menInthol told you that he last saw Faramir and Gelnor racing to the north-west area of Osgiliath, pursued by a frightful commander of the enemy forces named Gothmog.Defeat Orcs throughout Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search the north-western area of Osgiliath for another of Damrod's menGelnor saw an Orc runner crushed beneath falling stones near a fountain to the east, and he wants you to dig through the rubble in search of the message it carried.Gelnor saw an Orc runner crushed beneath falling stones near a fountain to the east, and he wants you to dig through the rubble in search of the message it carried.Maybe you missed something. Keep digging! (${NUMBER}/3)You have recovered one of the messages sent by Gothmog to his forces in Osgiliath, and should bring it to Damrod among the culverts beneath the city.'The men here think Faramir can be found to the north, somewhere in the city of Osgiliath astride the Anduin. The Steward of Gondor charged his son with the defence of Osgiliath, but none here know if he has repelled the enemy. Some speak of a hidden encampment within the culverts beneath the city. If Faramir or his men still defend the city, that is where they will be.

'My brother and I will go with you to Osgiliath. There are certain to be more than enough Orcs for the both of us to hone our skills in battle!''The men speak of a hidden encampment within the culverts beneath Osgiliath. If Faramir or his men still defend the city, that is where they will be.

'My brother and I will go with you to Osgiliath. There are certain to be more than enough Orcs for the both of us to hone our skills in battle!''The men here think Faramir can be found to the north, somewhere in the city of Osgiliath astride the Anduin. The Steward of Gondor charged his son with the defence of Osgiliath, but none here know if he has repelled the enemy. Some speak of a hidden encampment within the culverts beneath the city. If Faramir or his men still defend the city, that is where they will be.

'My brother and I will go with you to Osgiliath. There are certain to be more than enough Orcs for the both of us to hone our skills in battle!''These are the men who remain in defence of the city? That means more glory for the rest of us, ${PLAYER}!''I gladly welcome your help, even as I fear it comes too late, ${PLAYER}. The city is lost. There are too many Orcs, and every passing hour brings more of their kind, as well as ferocious warriors from the South. I do not hope to save the city, ${CLASS}. Now my hope is to purchase as much time for the defenders of Minas Tirith as I am able. Osgiliath will not be retaken, but until we are slain we might slow the forward march of these foes with our efforts.

'Faramir is in charge of the defence, but we were separated during the fighting and no man has seen him. When last I saw my captain, he was fighting by the south-west wall of Osgiliath in the company of doughty warriors Inthol and Gelnor. If you can find one of them, they may have tidings. Do what you can to slow the Enemy's march and to find Faramir!''Faramir is in charge of the defence, but we were separated during the fighting and no man has seen him. When last I saw my captain, he was fighting by the south-west wall of Osgiliath in the company of doughty warriors Inthol and Gelnor. If you can find one of them, they may have tidings. Do what you can to slow the Enemy's march and to find Faramir!''You are a friend? I am Inthol, soldier of Gondor. The pain is still overwhelming, but I feel it less keenly to know there are still good folk fighting to defend the city!

'Captain Faramir is not here, friend. He went north with Gelnor, but they were pursued by a terrible apparition and I do not know what became of them. It was a man, I think, but tall, and clad all in armour. My blood ran cold at the sight of him. The Orcs followed his commands, and they named him Gothmog.

'I would never question Faramir's courage or his resolve, but I hope for his sake, and for Gondor's, that he remained two steps ahead of this terrible commander!''Captain Faramir is not here, friend. He went north with Gelnor, but they were pursued by a terrible apparition and I do not know what became of them. It was a man, I think, but tall, and clad all in armour. My blood ran cold at the sight of him. The Orcs followed his commands, and they named him Gothmog.

'I would never question Faramir's courage or his resolve, but I hope for his sake, and for Gondor's, that he remained two steps ahead of this terrible commander!''You there! You are a friend, I can tell from your dress and bearing. You have to help me! I was separated from Faramir and sustained this injury, and it keeps me from doing something that I must!

'Many of the Orkish forces are led by a terrible man clad all in armour. He is Gothmog, and they cower at his approach, but they follow his commands. Runners bring messages from him throughout the city, and I saw one of these runners perish beneath many falling stones near a fountain to the east. I was injured before I could dig through the rubble to find the orders.

'I have overheard the Orcs speaking of a mighty weapon they plan to use against the White City! Go to the fountain and search through the stones for the dead message-bearer. The message he carries might give us knowledge of this weapon!''You have to help me! I was separated from Faramir and sustained this injury, and it keeps me from doing something that I must!

'Many of the Orkish forces are led by a terrible man clad all in armour. He is Gothmog, and they cower at his approach, but they follow his commands. Runners bring messages from him throughout the city, and I saw one of these runners perish beneath many falling stones near a fountain to the east. I was injured before I could dig through the rubble to find the orders.

