You have shaken away the remnants of the terrible prophecy Denethor spoke to you, but you cannot forget the images his words raised in your mind. To convince yourself that it was simply a tale, you should find Peregrin and ensure he is well.Talk to Peregrin Took at his post in the Seventh Circle'We have to get down to the gate! Talk to me when you are ready, and we will go with haste!''To the gate! We must get to the gate!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Hullo there, ${PLAYER}. How was your audience with the Steward?'

At the sound of the young hobbit's voice, a tremendous smile brightens your face and you fight the urge to clasp Pippin in a tight embrace.

'What is the joke, ${PLAYER}? I've never seen you this happy! It's a little peculiar, if you ask me, this being war-time and all, but I suppose that's no reason not to look on the bright side, is it?

'You do seem a little flustered, now that I think about it: both happy and sad at the same time, if that makes any sense. I saw you not ten minutes ago, when the Steward summoned you before him. What could you have talked about in so short a time that would work such a change in you?'You have heard Denethor's tale of what he expects from the siege of Minas Tirith, and should convey the Steward's words to Mithrandir before the hour grows too late.Mithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith.

Peregrin Took has suggested that you tell Mithrandir about your audience with Denethor, the Steward of Gondor.Talk to Mithrandir in the Court of the Fountain'Well, it does not matter. Whatever you and the Steward spoke about, it is not my business to hear! I will do as I am told, and though that may not amount to a great service in the tales of heroes, may it prove as useful and as important as any hobbit deserves!

'But you should find Gandalf! I know that he is very worried about the city, and about Gondor, and any information you might have about the Steward's state of mind could be useful to him. Did I say Gandalf? I mean you should find Mithrandir. I will never get used to calling him that, ${PLAYER}. Why does he need two names, anyway? It's not proper!'

You point out that the young Took himself has two names, going sometimes by Peregrin and sometimes by Pippin.

'Well, that's different. That's different! Ah, you got me. Well-played, ${PLAYER}. Well-played indeed.''You should find Mithrandir! I know that he is very worried about the city, and about Gondor, and any information you might have about the Steward's state of mind could be useful to him.''I understand you had an audience with Denethor, ${PLAYER}. I might have given you some wisdom concerning how to handle the Steward, but I was not consulted. I trust you did not spoil any of our plans, or cause any harm that cannot be undone?'

You tell Mithrandir that Denethor spoke to you of many things that he saw within the depths of a palantír. At that, Mithrandir looks up sharply.

'So the Anor-stone did remain within the tower. I wondered if it was so. Denethor has had a stubborn and strong will for all the years of his life, but if he seeks to gain some advantage over the enemy by using the palantír...'

You interrupt the Wizard, and his initial offence is quickly assuaged as you recount the worrying tale of Denethor's prophetic words concerning the siege to come. Mithrandir is silent for a long while. Finally he speaks.

'I do not think he has seen the siege itself in the Anor-stone, ${PLAYER}, and that is very important to us. A palantír cannot be made to lie, though its images might deceive if the user interprets them incorrectly. But I fear that the future in which Denethor believes, while not certain, could still come to pass. There is a question that his tale raises in my mind, a question I had not fully considered before now.

'Where was Rohan? If the events of the coming siege will indeed transpire as Denethor foretells, and Théoden does not come to the aid of Gondor, I fear that the Steward of Gondor may be right. Minas Tirith will fall.

'It is absolutely imperative that you learn what has happened to the Riders of Rohan. They must come to Minas Tirith in time, or all is lost. The siege is still ahead. Time yet remains.'

<rgb=#00FF00>To be continued in Volume IV, Book 5, 'The Ride of the Rohirrim.'</rgb>Osgiliath has been lost, and the defenders who still remain in the city must escape to the Pelennor.Duilin is outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern side of the Pelennor Fields.

Osgiliath has fallen to the enemy, and the men there can no longer mount an effective resistance.Talk to Duilin outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor FieldsThe safety of Minas Tirith is threatened by the foes that have come to the Pelennor Fields. Men fled from the occupation of the Causeway Forts and fell not far from Osgiliath.

Duilin and Derufin have asked you to search for survivors injured while fleeing from the Causeway Forts, and to defeat foes on the Pelennor.Defeat foes on the Pelennor Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Check fallen soldierCheck fallen soldierCheck fallen soldierDuilin and Derufin are outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern side of the Pelennor Fields.Talk to Duilin outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor FieldsDuilin and Derufin are outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern side of the Pelennor Fields.Talk to Derufin outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields'The city has been lost, ${PLAYER}. Faramir is missing, and his men are dead or captured. We have slowed the enemy's march as much as we could, but now we must see to our own safety. I will bring us by secret passages beyond the enemy camp, and from there we will make our way to the causeway.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel outside the Causeway Forts on the Pelennor Fields when you accept this quest.</rgb>'How fares Osgiliath and the Causeway Forts? I have seen few survivors! There may still be men out there!'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel outside the Causeway Forts on the Pelennor Fields when you accept this quest.</rgb>'We have slowed the enemy's march as much as we could, but now we must see to our own safety. Go now to the Pelennor Fields! We must see if the Causeway Forts have been taken by the enemy. I believe they surely have. Duilin and Derufin will help you in this.''Osgiliath has fallen, and its defenders fled in a great rout. They may have purchased some few hours for the people of Minas Tirith, but they paid dearly for it.''My brother and I left Minas Tirith to seek adventure and hunt the mighty Mûmakil, and at that time it felt a prison. Now I see the White City on the horizon and it seems a refuge instead! Can its walls stand against the evils we have beheld?

'I cannot stop thinking about that frightful apparition: Gothmog. Is it true he has the power to escape death? What will happen when the great ram Grond is repaired and he brings it across the Pelennor?

'We will do what we must, as always, and not shrink in fear! Truly, we will let it drive us to greater heights of courage! It seems that some of the defenders of the Causeway Forts fled before the encroaching army, and were slain before they reached safety. See if any men survived, and defeat their pursuers. It could be their injuries were grave, but not yet mortal.''Some of the defenders of the Causeway Forts fled before the encroaching army, and were slain before they reached safety. See if any men survived, and defeat their pursuers. It could be their injuries were grave, but not yet mortal.''Osgiliath has fallen, and its defenders fled in a great rout. They may have purchased some few hours for the people of Minas Tirith, but they paid dearly for it.''There were no survivors? I am sorry to hear it, but I am not surprised it is so.''You found no survivors? I am not surprised, but I am disappointed to hear that good men of Gondor were bludgeoned or hewn even after death. We needed no further reason to hate the Orcs, but still they provide it for us! We will not forget, and every insult will be repaid ten-fold!''I hate the Orcs for what they have done, and will not rest until they have paid in full for every life they have extinguished! I know that my brother feels the same!''This place will be crawling with enemies before long, ${PLAYER}. It is time for us to leave.'The forces of the Enemy have taken the Causeway Forts, and now the expanse of the Pelennor lies between you and the walls of the White City.Derufin is outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields.

Duilin and Derufin are ready to climb aboard their steeds and ride to Minas Tirith. They wait only for your word that you are ready to do the same.Mount your steed and talk to Derufin outside the Causeway Forts to begin the ride to Minas TirithPrince Imrahil has dismounted from his steed just inside the gates of Minas Tirith, on the western end of the Pelennor Fields.

You helped save Faramir from death at the hands of the Orcs, but he is grievously wounded. Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth has borne him back to the city, and wishes to speak with you.Talk to Prince Imrahil just inside the entrance to Minas TirithGandalf can be found just within the gates to Minas Tirith.

Faramir has suffered an unnatural wound during the retreat from the Causeway Forts, and Gandalf bears a concerned expression.Talk to Gandalf just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith'The Pelennor is wide, and it will not be long before it fills with the forces of the Enemy. Climb aboard your steed, ${PLAYER}, and tell me when you are ready to ride to Minas Tirith!''Quickly, now! Let us ride to the White City! Follow me!''Tell my brother when you are ready to ride to Minas Tirith!''Faramir lives, but that is no natural wound. I hope there is little foundation for my fears, but I will tell you that I have seen one in his condition before.''I wish we had met under different circumstances, ${PLAYER}, but I am glad you came to Faramir's defence when you did. His wound is not deep, but I fear that some fell sorcery remains within it. He swoons, and does not respond to our voices.

'I will bring him to his father in the White Tower. Steward Denethor will want to see what has become of his son. I hope that son and father both will have the strength to come through this. The line is strong; I am sure they will.

'Still, for Faramir to be wounded thus, and so soon after word reached us of his brother's demise... it seems that there will be no end to the challenges set before us in these dark days! I wish we could sit and speak in peace of Dol Amroth my home, but that is a wish that must wait. I go now to the Steward!''I do not want to worry you, ${PLAYER}, but there is something unnatural about the wound suffered by Faramir during his retreat from the Causeway Forts. I have seen a wound of its type before, but this seems to have a greatly-accelerated pace and the healing hands of Elrond are many mountains away.'

Gandalf sighs wearily.

'There were many servants of the Enemy near to Faramir on that field, ${PLAYER}. We must hope that his wound was not caused by a weapon of morgul-make, for there will be no hope of a cure if that be so. I told Imrahil the same as I am telling you: do not speak of this worry to Denethor. It may prove unnecessary, but we must not give him reason to despair for the life of Faramir. The young captain is his only remaining heir, and we need the Steward to focus on the battle that is sure to come if Minas Tirith is to stand.'

Gandalf suddenly stares at you piercingly.

'Of course I am glad to see you, ${PLAYER}! But there is now work to be done, and little time in which to do it! The pleasantries can wait until after the war is done, if that is a boon we are to be given!'Gandalf has arranged for you to be given the pass-words to the gates of the city, so you may travel freely among the various tiers of Minas Tirith.Thalgam guards the Sword-gate to the Second Circle of Minas Tirith.

Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.Talk to Thalgam at the Sword-gate to the Second CircleSoromar guards the Silver Gate to the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.

Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.Talk to Soromar at the Silver Gate to the Third CircleIdhir guards the Lords' Gate to the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.Talk to Idhir at the Lords' Gate to the Fourth CircleDoronir guards the Gate of Stars to the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.Talk to Doronir at the Gate of Stars to the Fifth CircleGarthor guards the Gate of Stones to the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.Talk to Garthor at the Gate of Stones to the Sixth CircleLinharn guards the Gate of the Citadel of Minas Tirith.

Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.Talk to Linharn at the Gate of the Citadel to the Seventh CircleMithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the uppermost level of the city.

You have obtained pass-words for the seven levels of Minas Tirith, and should now talk to Mithrandir in the Seventh Circle.'You travel as I do, ${PLAYER}, on the wings of the storm. Men may call you a harbinger of dark times, but in truth we go where we are most needed. Today that is Minas Tirith, the Tower of Guard. You will need to freely travel throughout the city if you are to best serve the people of Minas Tirith. Any obstruction to your free passage will hinder your efforts, and that is a help to the Enemy!

'The city climbs this easternmost spur of the White Mountains, ascending in seven levels, each separated by a gate. Men of Gondor safe-guard greater and lesser pass-words for each gate; the lesser pass-words change frequently, and the greater pass-words remain in use for much longer.

'I will give you my pledge of your trustworthiness. Show it to the guards at each gate and they will teach you the pass-words for each gate. And one more thing, ${PLAYER}. The men of Gondor do not know me by the name Gandalf. They call me Mithrandir, and I invite you to do the same!''I have given you my pledge of your trustworthiness. Show it to the guards at each gate and they will teach you the pass-words.''Mithrandir's word is enough for me, ${PLAYER}, and I will teach you the greater pass-word for the Sword-gate. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>Beacons of Gondor</rgb>. Share it with no one!

'Beyond this gate lies the Second Circle of the city, known to the people of Gondor as the Soldiers' Tier. This tier of the city is home to several ale-halls and barracks catering to soldiers and the town-guard, as well as a number of armouries and the Wielding-yard.

'Go in peace, and cause no trouble within the city. We have enough of that to spare, if the scouts can be trusted!''I will teach you the greater pass-word for the Silver Gate. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>Anárion</rgb>. You will find it easy to remember, for he was the son of Elendil who ordered the construction of this city. At that time it was called Minas Anor, the Tower of the Sun, though it has since been renamed Minas Tirith, the Tower of Guard.

'Beyond this gate lies the Third Circle of the city, the Craftsmen's Tier. This tier of the city houses shops and smithies, as well as the Clothiers' Market and Fellow-hall. Builders and merchants will find much to attend their needs on this tier of the city, as will any who seek the auctioneers at the House of Clamor.''Mithrandir says you are trustworthy? There are some for whom that would not be enough, ${PLAYER}, but it is not my place to deny you. I will teach you the greater pass-word for the Lords' Gate. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>House of Stewards</rgb>. There has been no King for nearly a thousand years, and Gondor is now ruled by a line of Stewards.

'Mere minutes ago, I allowed the Prince of Dol Amroth passage through this gate, and it seemed to me that he bore the body of Faramir, the son of Steward Denethor. I could not tell if there was life in him, but I fear for the line of the Stewards if he should die, or has done so already. It is whispered that Boromir has already fallen.'

Idhir shakes his head with a frown.

'Forgive my gossiping tongue! Beyond this gate is the Fourth Circle, known to folk of the city as the Players' Tier. Minstrels and actors frequent the Court of Voronwë and the Blue Theatre, and their wealthy patrons gather at the baths and guest-houses between performances. The entrance to the great cistern that feeds most of the city is also on this level, but you would be wise to leave it be. The footing can be treacherous, and the Waterstead has claimed more than a few careless lives.''I see that Mithrandir has vouchsafed for you, ${PLAYER}, but it is not enough for me to teach you the greater pass-word for this gate. I will teach you the lesser pass-word, as I have been instructed to do for friends of the Wizard that are not known to me. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>Poetry</rgb>. Understand that the lesser pass-words change frequently, so conclude your business here with haste.

'The Fifth Circle of the city is known as the Sages' Tier, and it is a place of learning. Scholars study the stars from its orrery and tower, and natural philosophers make learned arguments within its quiet courtyards. Several archives can be found in the Fifth Circle, as can the Houses of Lore and the scriptorium where copies are made of valued documents and records.''This is the Gate of Stones to the Sixth Circle of the city, and it is my duty to tell you that Mithrandir's word of your worthiness earns you the lesser pass-word only. Conduct your business with speed and depart. The pass-word for now is <rgb=#00FF00>Vigilance</rgb>.

'The Sixth Circle is known to folk of the city as the Masters' Tier, but few of them ever climb to this gate. The Houses of Healing can be found on this tier, along with the Cold Hall where the dead are brought to be washed, clothed, and prepared for internment in the tombs or, in the case of the common folk, the ossuaries within the Hill of Guard.

'The Dome of the Sun can also be found on this level. That is where the Council of Gondor meets to decide matters of state, and errand-riders bring their resolutions throughout the city and to the other reaches of Gondor. They have had much to discuss of late, and I urge you not to bother them.''Mithrandir's pledge is of value, ${PLAYER}, but I must follow the commands of the Steward. It is his wish that friends of the Wizard learn the lesser pass-word for the Citadel and no other. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>Justice</rgb>.

'The Seventh Circle of the city is called the Citadel, but it is also known as the Stewards' Tier. Some of the common folk refer to it as the Kings' Tier, but that seems distasteful to me. There has been no King in Gondor for many hundreds of years, and the wise rule of the Stewards has served us well, if you ask me.

'The Tower of Ecthelion stands proudly atop the city, a sign of Gondor's might. Steward Denethor rules within the Hall of Kings, but you will only see within at his direct invitation. The path atop the city's pier is patrolled by guards of the Citadel and kept clear of obstructions, if you wish to walk the Ship's Prow and behold the view. Do so in safety, while that is still possible!''You were denied the greater pass-words for some of the levels? What rubbish, ${PLAYER}! Denethor seeks to demonstrate his authority. He should be preparing for war with his enemies instead of hindering his allies! It does not matter. For now you have free passage through the city.

'Minas Tirith is strong, and it was built in seven levels with strategic purpose. Did you notice how the gates alternate sides, first on the south, then the north, and then on the south again? Such a design causes the ascending road to pass through the Neaths in the pier at regular intervals, and carving so many arched tunnels in the stone cannot have been easy. It was done at Anárion's command so the city could be easily fortified, and an opposing force would have a long road to march before reaching the heights of the city.

'The walls of the city have never been breached. No enemy has broken the gates. Denethor knows this. He believes that Minas Tirith cannot fall, and that knowledge gives him strength, but it is also a weakness. He refuses the help I might give him, and the help you could provide. I think that is an error.'With battle on the horizon, Mithrandir wants you to help the people of Minas Tirith ready themselves for the coming storm.The Council of Gondor meets in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Peregrin Took can be found somewhere in the Citadel. Duilin and Derufin can be found within one of the taverns in the lower circles of the city.

Mithrandir has asked you to provide help to a number of people within the city before the city is besieged.Talk to Othnar and complete 'The Council of Gondor'Talk to Peregrin Took and complete 'Guard of the Citadel'Talk to Duilin and complete 'In Need of Discipline'Mithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith.

You have aided the Council of Gondor, Peregrin Took, and the sons of Lord Duinhir of Blackroot Vale, and should now return to Mithrandir.Talk to Mithrandir in the Court of the FountainPrince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate of the city, looking for someone to undertake a dangerous mission.Talk to Imrahil in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate to the city'We must not rely solely on the strength of the walls, ${PLAYER}. We must ensure that the people are strong as well. It will not be long before the Enemy is arrayed before the walls, and in that moment the city's defenders will need courage with deep foundations. There are some folk with whom you should speak, my friend; unresolved matters may linger, and cast hearts into confusion when the end approaches.

'Day to day affairs in the city are managed by a group of officials that comprise the Council of Gondor. They meet in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle. Introduce yourself to the doorward and do what you can to aid the Council.

'I came here in the company of Peregrin Took, hobbit of the Shire. He is now a Guard of the Citadel -- the less said of that, the better -- and I expect he could use a friendly word from you, ${PLAYER}.

'I spoke with Lord Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale a short time ago, and it seems that his sons left the city without his permission, and indeed against his direct command. I understand you met Duilin and Derufin during their ill-advised adventure. Find them within one of the taverns in the lower circles of the city, and perhaps something can be done to soothe their father's temper.''There are some folk with whom you should speak. The Council of Gondor meets in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle. Introduce yourself to the doorward and do what you can to aid the Council.

'I came here in the company of Peregrin Took, hobbit of the Shire. He is now a Guard of the Citadel -- the less said of that, the better -- and I expect he could use a friendly word from you, ${PLAYER}.

'I spoke with Lord Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale a short time ago, and it seems that his sons left the city without his permission, and indeed against his direct command. I understand you met Duilin and Derufin during their ill-advised adventure. Find them within one of the taverns in the lower circles of the city, and perhaps something can be done to soothe their father's temper.''There you are, ${PLAYER}. I have been looking for you!

'The Prince of Dol Amroth was looking for someone to undertake a mission of some danger, and I suggested that you would make the ideal candidate. Hurry down to the First Circle and learn if Imrahil has already sent someone else.''The Prince of Dol Amroth was looking for someone to undertake a mission of some danger, and I suggested that you would make the ideal candidate. Hurry down to the First Circle and learn if Imrahil has already sent someone else.''Mithrandir said you would be happy to undertake this errand, ${PLAYER}. I am pleased to see he was right.'Prince Imrahil needs someone to learn what the situation may be north of the city, in Talath Anor.Ingold is the Captain of the Out-wall, and can be found at the North-gate in the Rammas Echor.

Prince Imrahil has asked you to learn why Ingold has not yet returned to Minas Tirith, and to learn the situation in Talath Anor.Talk to Ingold at the North-gate in the Rammas EchorSûhalar Easterlings can be found throughout the plains of Talath Anor, in Old Anórien.

Ingold, Captain of the Out-wall, has asked you to defeat Sûhalar Easterlings throughout Talath Anor.Defeat Sûhalar Easterlings in Talath Anor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})If he still lives, Barathant should be somewhere within the town of Crithost, in Talath Anor.

Ingold asked you to find Barathant after you defeated some of the Sûhalar Easterlings.Talk to Barathant in CrithostWarg-riders can be found throughout Talath Anor.

Barathant has asked you to defeat the Warg-riders that have overrun the lands north of the Rammas Echor.Defeat Wargs or Warg-riders in Talath Anor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Barathant is in the town of Crithost, in Talath Anor.

You defeated many foes and should now return to Crithost.Talk to Barathant in Crithost'When Mithrandir came to the city, he told me that he passed through the North-gate in the Rammas Echor and spoke with its captain. He found Ingold supervising the repair of the wall, and advised him that it came too late; swords would be of more use than trowels in this late hour.

'Ingold has not yet returned to the city, but I need to know the situation north of the Rammas. Go to the North-gate of the Rammas Echor, and learn why Ingold has not yet come back. I applaud him for bracing the wall and the gate in it, but he will be of more use to Gondor alive in Minas Tirith than dead at the North-gate.''I need to know the situation north of the Rammas Echor. Go to the North-gate of the Rammas, and learn why Ingold has not yet come back. I applaud him for bracing the wall and the gate in it, but he will be of more use to Gondor alive in Minas Tirith than dead at the North-gate!''We are still working to repair the wall. I cannot return to the city just yet! I have disturbing news, and it enforces my desire not to leave my post until the last possible moment.

'There is a second army, ${PLAYER}. I think this second Mordor-host crossed the river at Cair Andros, though I cannot be certain; none of my scouts have made it near enough to the island to see in whose hands it lies. I await word from my man in Crithost, Barathant, but he has not returned yet; I do not know if he still lives.

'I do know that Orcs, Wargs, and a strange group of Easterlings have overrun the plain of Talath Anor. It is this last that gives me the most concern. They are called Sûhalar, and little is known of them. If you can defeat these new foes in Talath Anor, we may learn how best to face them, and I ask that you then look for Barathant in the town of Crithost. Once he returns, all of us can then return to Minas Tirith.''Orcs, Wargs, and a strange group of Easterlings have overrun the plain of Talath Anor. It is this last that gives me the most concern. They are called Sûhalar, and little is known of them. If you can defeat these new foes in Talath Anor, we may learn how best to face them, and I ask that you then look for Barathant in the town of Crithost. Once he returns, all of us can then return to Minas Tirith.''After you have defeated the Sûhalar Easterlings, look for Barathant in the town of Crithost. He is a passionate man and will not retreat until the very last moment, but I feel that moment is fast approaching.''I am alive, ${PLAYER}, and I still possess the fighting spirit! I will not retreat to Minas Tirith until the very last moment, and you will not be able to convince me. It is futile!

'Much of my family evacuated Minas Tirith and went to the vale of Tumladen among the last few waggons, but my brothers remain in the White City. I can still slay Wargs and their riders in Talath Anor, and every foe I dispatch means one fewer to menace my brothers.

'Aid me in this! You are an adventurer and can do a great deal of good in this land beyond the Rammas! Once we have faced these threats, I give you my word that we can return to the North-gate.''You are an adventurer and can do a great deal of good in this land beyond the Rammas! Help me defeat Warg-riders, and once we have faced these threats, I give you my word that we can return to the North-gate.''You have done well, my friend. I too have slain many of our enemies, but it seems that two more cross the river from Cair Andros for each one that I defeat. This does not seem to be a battle we can win.'Barathant is almost ready to return to the city, but first he wants you to recall the scouts he sent out from Crithost.Cangrail and Brúnion can be found to the north-west and north-east of Crithost, in Talath Anor.

Barathant asked you to find and recall the scout he sent out from Crithost, and to defeat any enemies you come across in Talath Anor.Find Cangrail and tell her to returnFind Brúnion and tell him to returnDefeat foes throughout Talath Anor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Barathant is in the town of Crithost, waiting to hear that his scouts have agreed to return to the North-gate of the Rammas Echor.Talk to Barathant in CrithostIngold, the Captain of the Out-wall, is at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor.

The scouts in Talath Anor are retreating to the North-gate, and you should do the same. Ingold is waiting for your return.Talk to Ingold at the North-gate of the Rammas EchorBarathant never returned to the North-gate, but Ingold cannot wait long for him.Wait for Barathant at the North-gate of the Rammas EchorIngold, the Captain of the Out-wall, is at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor.Talk to Ingold at the North-gate of the Rammas EchorPrince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, waiting for you to return with news of the situation in Talath Anor.Retreat to Minas Tirith and talk to Imrahil in the First Circle of the city'We are nearing the end now. The Mordor-host that pours into Talath Anor shows no sign of slowing. I am almost ready to return to Minas Tirith.

'But first we need to recall two of the scouts I sent forth from Crithost. Go to the north-west and north-east and tell Cangrail and Brúnion that it is time for them to return to the North-gate. They have done well, but now they must think of their safety! Find them quickly, ${PLAYER}! They are sure to be in danger as the situation north of the Rammas worsens!

'Defeat any enemies you come across, as well. We may be readying for our retreat, but that is no reason not to strike at our enemies while we do!''We need to recall two of the scouts I sent forth from Crithost. Go to the north-west and the north-east and tell Cangrail and Brúnion that it is time for them to return to the North-gate. They have done well, but now they must think of their safety! Find them quickly, ${PLAYER}! They are sure to be in danger as the situation north of the Rammas worsens!

'Defeat any enemies you come across, as well. We may be readying for our retreat, but that is no reason not to strike at our enemies while we do!''You found them both? I am glad to hear it!

'Now, ${PLAYER}, lead the way to the North-gate in the Rammas Echor! I will be right behind you!''Lead the way to the North-gate in the Rammas Echor! I will be right behind you! Quickly, now!''Some of the scouts have returned, and I am grateful, for I have need of their weapons, as you can see!

'Barathant? No, I have not yet seen him! Did he say he was coming?

'We cannot wait long, ${PLAYER}! If he is coming, he has to get here soon!''We cannot wait any longer, ${PLAYER}! We must fall back to Minas Tirith! Ride, ride to the city!''We cannot wait any longer! We must fall back to Minas Tirith! Ride, ride to the city!''You have already returned? I did not expect to see you so soon after your departure, ${PLAYER}. What can you tell me of the situation in Talath Anor?'

You tell Imrahil about your encounter with the Orcs, Wargs, and Sûhalar Easterlings that occupied Cair Andros and have poured into Talath Anor.

'A second force? It must be a pincer attack! Our Enemy has been planning this for some time, and soon each host will close upon the city.  It will make the triumph of Gondor all the sweeter when those plans are destroyed.'The enemies of Gondor approach Minas Tirith from the north and from the east, and many folk in the city desire your help before the city is completely surrounded.The Council of Gondor meets in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir can be found at the Court of the Fountain, in the Citadel atop the city. Echadon can be found at the south end of the Second Circle.

Imrahil has asked you to provide help to a number of people within the city before the city is encircled by a ring of foes.Talk to Mithrandir and complete 'A Matter of Lineage'Talk to Arodor and complete 'A Long Siege'Talk to Echadon and complete 'Reserves of Courage'Prince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate of the city, preparing for battle.Talk to Imrahil in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate to the cityOrmatar is in the Citadel, the highest level of Minas Tirith.

You learned that Ormatar has been seeking you, and you should find out what he wants.Talk to Ormatar in the Citadel atop Minas Tirith'Minas Tirith will soon be encircled by our enemies, ${PLAYER}. Time is getting short, but we must fill the hours or minutes that remain to us with preparations that will help us survive the approaching onslaught!

'While you were surveying the situation in Talath Anor, I learned of a handful of folk who desire your assistance with matters both large and small. Go to them and see what they need, if you can.

'Mithrandir wished to speak with you at greater length about your encounter with the enemy commander in Osgiliath. Find him in the Citadel, atop the city.

'Arodor, the chief scribe of the Council, was impressed with your work on his behalf and asked for you to speak with him in the Dome of the Sun, in the Sixth Circle. The Council was waiting for Ingold to return to the city; perhaps your experience beyond the Rammas Echor will be of interest to them.

'In other Council matters, the Captain of the Garrison has been trying to improve the morale of folk remaining in the city. Find Echadon and see what you can do to help.''While you were surveying the situation in Talath Anor, I learned of a handful of folk who desire your assistance with matters both large and small. Go to them and see what they need, if you can.

'Mithrandir wished to speak with you at greater length about your encounter with the enemy commander in Osgiliath. Find him in the Citadel, atop the city.

'Arodor, the chief scribe of the Council, was impressed with your work on his behalf and asked for you to speak with him in the Dome of the Sun, in the Sixth Circle. The Council was waiting for Ingold to return to the city; perhaps your experience beyond the Rammas Echor will be of interest to them.

'In other Council matters, the Captain of the Garrison has been trying to improve the morale of folk remaining in the city. Find Echadon and see what you can do to help.''It will not be long before the city is surrounded. I hope we are ready.'

Imrahil stares at you appraisingly.

'I have a message for you, ${PLAYER}. I received word that Ormatar, the Captain of the Citadel, has been looking for you. You should speak to him in the Citadel, without delay, for that can mean only one thing. Go to Ormatar with haste.''I received word that Ormatar, the Captain of the Citadel, has been looking for you. You should speak to him in the Citadel, without delay, for that can mean only one thing. Go to Ormatar with haste.''You are ${PLAYER}, the ${CLASS}? You must be. Who else might carry themselves as you do?

'I have been looking for you. The Steward has summoned you.'As the armies of Mordor begin to encircle the city, the Steward of Gondor summons you before him.Peregrin Took is in the Seventh Circle of the city.

You have been summoned before Denethor, the Steward of Gondor. Peregrin Took has been charged with bringing you into Denethor's presence.Talk to Peregrin Took and travel with him to your audience with DenethorMithrandir is in besieged Minas Tirith, in the south-eastern area of the Second Circle.

<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Talk to Mithrandir in besieged Minas Tirith, in the south-eastern area of the Second Circle'Am I right to believe that you have met Peregrin the Halfling? Lord Denethor has named him a Guard of the Citadel, despite his stature. He will bring you before the Steward. Tarry not!''All right, ${PLAYER}, I will bring you before the Steward! You may wish to keep your wits about you, for he has a somewhat frightening countenance. He is a great man of importance, I don't doubt it, but he is very stern and does not go out of his way to cushion the effect of his words!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Are you looking for Mithrandir? Go to the Dome of the Sun and use the model of the city. That will bring you to the city besieged, where Mithrandir mounts the defence!'

<rgb=#00FF00>If you wish to return to Minas Tirith during the siege, you may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun.</rgb>'The armies of Mordor have encircled the city, ${PLAYER}. The siege has begun.'

You tell Mithrandir that you spoke with the Steward, and that Denethor spoke to you of many things that he saw within the depths of a palantír. At that, Mithrandir looks up sharply.

'So the Anor-stone did remain within the tower. I wondered if it was so. Denethor has had a stubborn and strong will for all the years of his life, but if he seeks to gain some advantage over the enemy by using the palantír...'

The Wizard scowls, and shakes his head.

'Denethor is too occupied with his grief for Faramir to work any evil on that score, but he will also be of no use in the defence of the city. Imrahil and I will mount the defence, and we will need your help!'With Steward Denethor shut in the tower, mourning the final hours of his son Faramir, it is up to Mithrandir and Imrahil to mount the defence of the besieged city.Lamlor can be found in the Dome of the Sun in besieged Minas Tirith. Ingold can be found atop the wall on the north end of the Third Circle in besieged Minas Tirith. Rathon can be found in the Sixth Circle near the street to the Citadel in besieged Minas Tirith.

<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Talk to Lamlor in the besieged Dome of the Sun and complete 'The Withered Tree'Talk to Ingold in the besieged city and complete 'Mad With Terror'Talk to Rathon in the besieged city and complete 'Fires in the City'Prince Imrahil is in besieged Minas Tirith, atop the wall on the south-east end of the Second Circle.

<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Talk to Prince Imrahil in besieged Minas Tirith, atop the wall on the south-east end of the Second Circle'There is no more leaving the city, ${PLAYER}. The Morgul-host has surrounded Minas Tirith, and the Pelennor is filled with their weapons of war. They have not yet broken the gate, but there is still much harm they can cause even from their position beyond the walls. You must do what you can to help the city's defenders!

'The Council of Gondor is in disarray. Go to the Dome of the Sun and learn what you can do to help them communicate their resolutions. Lamlor, the Captain of Tidings, will need help to send messages throughout Minas Tirith.

'Ingold is atop the wall on the north end of the Third Circle, and will need your help to manage his fear and the fears of the men behind the walls. Terror will be the greatest foe of our guardsmen, and they will need to master it if they are to mount an effective defence!

'The armies of Mordor have been using catapults and other siege weapons to launch burning stones over the walls and into the city. Find Rathon, the Warden of the Wells, in the Sixth Circle near the street that leads up to the Citadel, and help him extinguish some of the fires before they can spread!''You must do what you can to help the city's defenders, ${PLAYER}!

'The Council of Gondor is in disarray. Go to the Dome of the Sun and learn what you can do to help them communicate their resolutions. Lamlor, the Captain of Tidings, will need help to send messages throughout Minas Tirith.

'Ingold is atop the wall on the north end of the Third Circle, and will need your help to manage his fear and the fears of the men behind the walls. Terror will be the greatest foe of our guardsmen, and they will need to master it if they are to mount an effective defence!

'The armies of Mordor have been using catapults and other siege weapons to launch burning stones over the walls and into the city. Find Rathon, the Warden of the Wells, in the Sixth Circle near the street that leads up to the Citadel, and help him extinguish some of the fires before they can spread!''Ready yourself! The enemy is preparing another assault, ${PLAYER}!'Jajax knows of a group of corsairs under the command of Hebil that have overtaken the beacon at the edge of Lamedon and Ringló Vale. He asks you to rough them up for him.The Fallen Beacon can be found on the border of Lamedon and Ringló Vale.

You should defeat corsairs at the Fallen Beacon.Roughed up corsairs at the Fallen Beacon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Jajax is located inside the Ethring tavern.

You should speak with Jajax.Speak with Jajax'My good adventuring friend, I am much too busy enjoying this tavern right now to adventure with you but might you have some time to listen to my request? Some men that were under Hebil's command have captured the beacon between Lamedon and this fine wooded Vale. I am sure they are up there right now thinking they are the best corsairs in all of Gondor but you and I know that they are just idiots. Look my friend, go up there and rough them up for me, will you? Wipe the smiles off their faces. Take back the beacon if you want as well. I do not understand Gondorians, but you seem to like them. Well, back to my pint! I'll see you again when you're done?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This bounty can only be completed a maximum of three times.</rgb>'Huzzah! I bet they ran down the hill crying like dogs! Haha, I wish I was there to see the looks on their faces. Har! You are a good friend. I am feeling much better!'Erchar's warriors hope to stem the tide of Haradrim troops by decimating the numbers of powerful half-trolls in their ranks.Half-trolls can be found throughout Dor-en-Ernil.

