You should try and talk some sense into members of the Withered Tree.'Perhaps the followers of the Withered Tree can be redeemed. Though they are wrong in their ways, they are still just men of Gondor. Try to talk to some of them if they are willing. The men of Gondor must band together if we are to win this war.''No, it is you who spouts lies and deceit!''You have no business down here, ${RACE}.''I was just minding my own business, until you came along and told me what I should be doing!''Hey, you're not one of us!''I can see that those up above have poisoned your mind. There is no stopping the Enemy.''Are you done preaching to me? Good, now die!''You do not understand, do you? This is the end of Gondor!''You best get out of here quickly before you get hurt!''I see what you mean. I shall leave these misguided men and continue fighting to keep Gondor alive.''Your words have convinced me to depart from these fools down here. I honestly was not sure these people were ever my friends.'The Withered Tree has taken hold of the Cisterns and it is up to you to destroy their lies.The Withered Tree can be found in the Cisterns.

You should find and destroy documents belonging to the Withered Tree.Destroy papers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'I noticed posters blowing through the Cisterns filled with lies from the Withered Tree. You must find their camps in the Cisterns and destroy their fear-mongering papers.'As the forces of the Morgul-host ready for war, the Black Blade of Lebennin holds close his valued prisoner and awaits the arrival of the Corsairs forces led by the Scourge.Complete the deed The Dome of Stars -- Tier 1Complete the deed The Dome of Stars -- Tier 2Complete the deed Challenge: Painful MemoriesComplete the deed The Lord of PinionsNow that Faltharan's family is safe from the Corsairs, you have been asked personally to deliver the good news.Faltharan is located at the steps to Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Faltharan.Talk to Faltharan'You have done Gondor a great service today, ${PLAYER}. The lordship of Pelargir has survived its greatest challenge, and we are now ready for what is next.

'Please inform the Lord-Regent that we located his family, and that we have people tending to their injuries. I am sure that Faltharan would appreciate the news coming from you.'Faltharan looks to you, and lets loose a relieved sigh.

'Very good. It pains me to know that my father is still missing, but I will try to carry on his legacy as best I can. The bloodline of Sirgon shall endure.

'We have tough days ahead of us, but no matter what, Pelargir will stand as a testament to Gondor's defiance in the face of war.'Angmar once again holds the Isendeep Mine and Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn believes that the time has come to purge them from the depths to take the mine back for the Free People. He suggests a drastic measure to do so in an effort to defeat the foe.Search the areas south of Tol Ascarnen or west along the plains, south of Dâr-gazag for the Thistledown Grazers. Collect some of their haunches and bring them to the slab within the depths of the Isendeep.

Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn believes that the drakes can be used against the Orcs of Angmar and wishes to use them as a diversion while you attack the Tyrant.'The mines are fallen to Angmar again and I will not stand for it, ${PLAYER}. We must get the mine back.

'I suggest that we use the drakes stalking the depths as cover for our attack. Search the lands south of Tol Ascarnen or west and south on the plains of the Steps of Gram for the Thistledown grazers. Collect haunches from those beasts and deliver them to a flat stone near where the Tyrant holding the mine keeps his company.

'The blood from the haunches should draw the drakes within range of the foe and bring about the battle needed to bring these foes down!'Terror weighs heavily on the Men of Gondor, and some have thrown down their arms in fear. Worse yet, others move to open the Great Gate in desperation and madness.

