You should speak to with Ormatar.Speak to Ormatar and cover for the brothers‘${PLAYER}, I must confess, there is a shortage of staffing in all the buildings of the Citadel. Only the guard posts are fully stationed on the eve of war. Still we have nobles staying at the Southern Great Guest-house and eating at the feast-hall, Merethrond. I need some of my guards to leave their post and take on additional duties up here. Would you mind delivering these orders in my stead?

'Speak with Iorlas and send him to the Southern Great Guest-house to tidy up the baths. Also, speak with Beregond and send him to Merethrond to tidy up the tables. We must all do our part to keep this city running.''Thank you for your help. I just received word that there is some sort of disturbance on the Prow. Perhaps a scuffle. Would you mind looking into that for me?''I do not understand your jovial attitude, brother. How can you be happy in time of war!? Is it that hobbit friend? You spend so much time with that Halfling, it's like your own brother does not even exist! Bergil, your son, needs your guidance on the eve of battle. You may not see him tomorrow!'Beregond looks calm, yet troubled. A moment passes before he speaks.

'It is true, my brother. Spending time with Peregrin has indeed allowed me not to dwell on the bloodshed to come. Before I met the Halfling, I was worried for you, for Bergil, and for Gondor. This worrying only left my spirits in decay. With my spirits fading, I pushed those I cared about away. I am ashamed to have been so distant, Iorlas.''Beregond, I did not realize the weight you have been carrying. You know that you can always share that burden with your brother. I would treat Bergil as a son if the worst came to pass. Do not worry for your son; be with him instead. On the battlefield, I shall protect the both of you until the bitter end.

'I do not want to stop your friendship with the Halfling. He brings you joy and hope. That is something we all need.''Thank you, Iorlas. It is good to hear these words coming from you. I will spend more time with my family. Hopefully, Peregrin will be able to join us. I am sure we will all enjoy the hobbit's company.

'Now, ${PLAYER}, there is something that I must ask of you. I believe you came here to investigate our argument, most likely on Ormatar's orders. If you would be kindly to us, keep our quarrel a secret whilst we return to our posts. We would rather not get in trouble for this little family dispute.'You explain to Ormatar that the noise was just some nobles who were staying at the Southern Great Guest-house. They were having a heated discussion but you calmed them down.

'Good, I am glad it was not any of my men. Those nobles spend so much time bickering and not enough time getting actual work done. Well, enough talk from me. I'll let you get back to more important matters.

'You are quite efficient. Perhaps you would be willing to join the Citadel Guard one day?'Desperate to weaken the Great Bridge before the forces of Minas Morgul can ferry siege equipment across it, Damrod hopes the weight of trolls might break the span once more.The crude span can be found at the centre of the Great Bridge in central Osgiliath.

Damrod has asked you to defeat trolls atop the crude span constructed by the Morgul-host in the hope that it will weaken the bridge.Damrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have defeated several trolls atop the Great Bridge, but it is unclear if your efforts bore fruit. You should now return to Damrod.Talk to Damrod'Time grows short, ${PLAYER}.

'The host of Minas Morgul has readied their siege equipment, and now it is only a matter of time before they send it across the Anduin and begin their great assault. We must try to slow their advance... at any cost! The span they constructed is of Orkish make, and I do not think it as stable as they believe! They have many trolls among their forces... perhaps if the heaviest among them were slain on the span, their weight might cause it to cave in before their equipment crosses.

'Go to the Great Bridge and slay trolls upon their span. Let us see if my thinking is correct!''I heard the thundering of their falls even down here, ${PLAYER}, but the bridge did not break?

'Unfortunate, but we cannot let that halt our efforts!'The Cloudyheads have negotiated a performance in the legendary Blue Theatre of Minas Tirith, but now they must think on how best to utilise the theatre's grand scale.The Blue Theatre can be found to the south in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Polla has asked you to meet her and the rest of the Cloudyheads in the Blue Theatre as they work to prepare their performance.Travel to the Blue Theatre in the Fourth CircleMembers of the Cloudyheads can be found inside the Blue Theatre in the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You have arrived at the Blue Theatre and should now speak to someone from the Cloudyheads about what is to be done next.Talk to someone from the Cloudyheads inside the Blue TheatreFróki can be found inside the Blue Theatre at the southern end of the Fourth Circle.

Fróki has asked you to help The Cloudyheads prepare for their performance in the Blue Theatre.Talk to Fróki in the Blue TheatrePolla Stoutley and the Cloudyheads can be found inside the Blue Theatre to the far right of the entrance in an alcove with a fire-place.

You have helped the Cloudyheads perform inside the Blue Theatre, and should now speak to Polla Stoutley.Talk to Polla Stoutley in the Blue Theatre'Do you want to know, ${PLAYER}?

'Perhaps you should take a seat first - poor Robbo almost fainted when I told him! Very well, very well... we are going to be performing at the Blue Theatre! It is a theatre of remarkable size and wreathed in every shade of the most beautiful blue you can imagine. I have only visited it once, and never dreamed to perform there! 

'Our performance is soon... possibly a bit too soon, but I cannot deny the band such an opportunity. I only hope we are prepared!

'The Blue Theatre is to the south in the Fourth Circle - I can never remember their proper names! Will you aid us one last time, my friend?''All right, let us go!''By Durin's beard, you are just in time, ${PLAYER}!

'Polla told me to keep watch for your arrival, and now that you have come, I feel as if a great weight has been lifted from our backs. The others are scrambling to prepare and we are in great need of aid if we are to perform today!

'Tell me when you are ready, and we can join the others behind the stage!''We cannot thank you enough for what you have done, ${PLAYER}.

'It was an honour to perform in this theatre, and better yet to bring a small measure of joy to those who have so much to fear in the coming days.

'You may be a ${CLASS}, a warrior, an adventurer - but among us, you shall always be a friend in our hearts.'

The other members of the Cloudyheads salute and bow in your honour.

'May your days ahead grow brighter, my friend... even if the skies do not. Remember, no matter what evil may come - our music shall never die!'The combined forces of the Morgul-host pose a serious threat to Minas Tirith and the fate of Middle-earth.Haradrim and Easterling forces can be found in eastern Osgiliath.

Damrod has asked you to seek out and defeat Haradrim and Easterling forces in Osgiliath.Defeat Haradrim and Easterling forces within Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Damrod can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have defeated many of the Haradrim and Easterling forces and should now return to Damrod.Talk to Damrod in the culverts of Osgiliath'The host of Minas Morgul has grown beyond my imagining, my friend.

'Orcs, Trolls, Uruk-hai, Haradrim, Half-trolls, and now Easterlings... it has not done much for the spirits of my men, as you might suppose. It is a truly daunting force, but we cannot lose hope... not yet.

'The Easterlings and Haradrim have made camp in the eastern streets of the city, but I know from my many years that they scare far more easily than Orcs. Travel to the eastern streets and slay many of their numbers. If their morale might yet be broken, I can think of none other than Faramir or such a fine ${CLASS} who might drive them from our lands.

'Tread carefully, ${PLAYER}.''They number in the thousands, my friend, but each one that we defeat bolsters my hope for the future of the White City.

'You have done well.'Drakes stalk the mines and are a foe that often destroys the Orcs and trolls within the mines. It is time to turn that power against the Free People.Search the areas south of Tol Ascarnen or west along the plains south and west of Dâr-gazag for the thistledown grazers. Collect some of their haunches and bring them to the slab within the depths of the Isendeep.

Soldier Golb directed you to turn the force of drakes often found stalking the Isendeep Mines against the Free People. He wants you to draw the drakes in with the promise of aurochs meat.'Being sent here to Grothum was bad enough, now I have to deal with these fool târks and dwarfs stalking the mines. I'll not have this, maggot!

'We know them drakes stalk the mines, and it is time that we use their strength against our foes! We need to call them to action and get them to fight their leaders!

'Very near where their leader stands is a nice, flat rock just waiting for slabs of meat to be tossed atop it to get those drakes running. Get some haunches from those aurochs and toss them on the slab. That ought to get the drake's attention. Then we'll see how strong these wretches truly are!'At the head of the enemy forces stand the Captain-Generals. Their symbols garner great favour amongst Angmar's army, and presenting these to Mordirith will undoubtedly earn you favour with Lugbúrz.Captain-Generals can only be found at locations where the enemy army holds power.

Chieftain Durulkum directed you to collect Captain-General symbols from enemy leaders and then return to him.'Weakling! I charge you with a task that will see your body bloodied, broken, and left for the crebain. You will do this task because I say you will do this task.

'Fail me and live, and I will cover your flesh in the sweet drippings from the roasting rat-folk and drop you near the trolls. Your end will be painful and merciless, and I shall revel in it. Do well, and I will forgo the threat and let you live out your miserable life.

'Captain-Generals are present wherever the enemy controls. Slaughter them, skin them if you like, snap their bones and consume them... I don't care. Save the symbols they wear and return them to me!''A pitiful display of battle! Took you longer than a slug to crawl out of the dead târk's belly.

