You should tell Laerind of what you have seen.Speak with Laerind'Greetings traveller. I have need of your assistance if you can spare the time. We have not received many travellers these last few days since the army marched through. They took many of our best men. Those that remain hide in fear from the darkened skies and ghost stories of blue lights in the woods at night. With this, I am doing what I can to provide Ethring with the defence and supplies it needs but remain short-handed.

'If you are able, I could use assistance in catching fish from the nets down by the river.''A body has washed up on the river-bank! This is disturbing news as Ethring has not seen an unnatural death in many years.'

You explain that you are not sure how the man died or if it was a murder.

'I see. Perhaps one of the few villagers who have been walking about these last few days knows something about this man's death.'Scout enemy camps scattered throughout Central Gondor.Scout enemy camps scattered throughout Central Gondor.Discover GríshruDiscover Dâr MatumDiscover Lang BohaDiscover Barad RillDiscover Hata KhezratDiscover Hata KebirDiscover Thama AklamScout Gondorian settlements in Central Gondor that are in ruins or under siege.Scout Gondorian settlements in Central Gondor, that are in ruins or under siege.Discover TungobelDiscover GaerlondDiscover LornostDiscover the Ruins of EthillornYou have pursued a mysterious figure dressed in Faramir's cloak ever since you saw it exiting the tunnels under Osgiliath.Complete 'The Ruined City' without defeating any harrowing fell spirits.Complete 'The Ruined City' without defeating any harrowing fell spirits.No harrowing fell spirits defeatedThe Black Blade of Lebennin can manifest painful memories that will bring even the most hardy warrior to ruin.Complete the quest Challenge: Painful MemoriesThe tunnels beneath Osgiliath have many challengers - all of whom must be defeated with haste if Faramir is to be found.Defeat Culvert Slugs rapidly.Defeat Culvert Slugs rapidly.Defeat Culvert Slugs rapidlyCorsairs may be hiding in the various buildings within Dol Amroth.The houses must be searched.Search houses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Haldil, a local at the Cape Docks, enjoys working on the shore and on the water.Fish traps can be found around the shores of either of the Cape islands.

You should check the traps for fish.Collect Saithe from fishing traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Haldil is down by the Cape Docks.

You should speak to Haldil when you have a moment.Talk to Haldil'Have you set foot upon those lovely islands out there? No sense just going out there to look around though. You must have a reason, I tell you. I have some traps out there. If you go out there to look around, check the traps for me. Then you will be living like me. One with the sea. Aye, that is the only life I want.''Well will you look at that? Quite the haul, I do say. I must bring you out on a boat with me some time. You, my friend, are good luck!'Erianir of Sarnhad has begged you to travel north to Malbarth before journeying east to Ost Anglebed for fear of the growing Corsair and Haradrim force on the coast.Malbarth can be found to the north of Sarnhad in western Lebennin.

Erianir has asked you to travel north to Malbarth before journeying east in Lebennin as the Corsair and Haradrim forces have seized much of the eastern lands.Speak to someone in Malbarth about travelling east'You have been of great help to us, my friend, but one of your skill would do well to join our forces to the east.

'However, the Corsairs and Haradrim have seized much of the land to the east and the road is unsafe for travel. I would beg that you travel north through Malbarth before journeying east to the beacon-settlement of Ost Anglebed. The hearty folk that dwell there can provide you safe passage to the east.

'Our guards in Ost Anglebed and Pelargir are all that remain, so your aid could be vital. Go swiftly, my friend, and let us hope we see you again in brighter times.''You say you have come from Sarnhad?

'I am glad it has not yet met with a grim fate as so many others have... I saw the smoke rising this morn, but could not tell which of our settlements had fallen to the Corsairs.'In the wake of a mysteriously stifled Corsair attack, the people of Erynos have been granted an unexpected peace.Tucharn can be found in Erynos in eastern Lebennin.

Glathril is unclear how the Corsairs met with such a fate and asks you to speak to Tucharn.Talk to TucharnCorsairs can be found along the road outside Erynos.

Tucharn has asked you to look over the fallen Corsairs on the road out of Erynos.Glathril can be found in Erynos in eastern Lebennin.

You have examined the fallen Corsairs and should now return to Glathril.Talk to GlathrilNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.

You have found the people of Erynos safe from harm, and should now tell Nimithil of what happened.Talk to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed'When I awoke this morn, I found these men lying in the road. I dared not get too close to them for I have known the Corsairs to be deceitful folk... but strange things are afoot, traveller.

'They have not moved for hours, so I think them dead, but you must forgive my caution. They look as if a great wave had crushed them where they stood, but no one seems to know what actually happened.

'Tucharn is often one of our earliest risers in the morning, so perhaps he saw something while we all slept.''I awoke to the sound of water rushing away, but by the time I could clothe myself, all I found was the company of men on the road.

'I do not know what to make of it, traveller. We are not like the folk of Malbarth in our devotion to old fables, but... perhaps we should be.

'I looked them all over, but I could not understand what I found. I would urge you to search them yourself before you return whence you came.''All of them drowned... but we are so far from the water's edge, and so much higher! This makes little sense, ${PLAYER}.

'As for Tucharn, he moved here from Malbarth when he married, but I think he has always carried his beliefs with him. I do not know if this truly could mean that the Sisters have returned to aid us... but I struggle to find any other meaning from this.

'Thank you for coming to our aid, but we are safe... and I wonder what this could mean for my people. I am sure we shall all soon speak of what has happened here today.''The tale you have told me is a strange one, ${PLAYER}...

'I, too, am not sure what to make of it. However, it is heartening to know that some of our folk remain safe from the Enemy.

'Thank you for travelling so far on my behalf - these tidings have eased some of my worries.'Captain-General Tordúr explained that scouts near Tol Ascarnen have seen a number of Angmar's servants dumping the contents of barrels into the river. Drawing water from the river shows that the river is slowly being poisoned. If this is allowed to continue, then the hobbits at Hoarhallow will certainly perish.The poison was introduced to the Hoarwell at the waterfall overlooking Tol Ascarnen, in the central area of the Ettenmoors, north-west of Glán Vraig.

Captain-General Tordúr asked you to make your way to the top of the waterfall overlooking Tol Ascarnen to assist in cleansing the poison that the goblins of Angmar introduced into the Hoarwell River.Captain-General Tordúr is at Glân Vraig.

You should return to Captain-General Tordúr with news of your success.'${PLAYER}, you are known to many of the Elves of Rivendell... nay, do not be surprised. I have a delicate matter that needs attention, and I believe you may be the ${RACE} for the matter.

'The waterfall above Tol Ascarnen has seen Angmar's forces visiting near its banks. Scouts report that they dump barrels of viscous material into the Hoarwell and further investigation has yielded evidence that the river is being poisoned. I have created a draught that will counteract this poison, but it must be delivered to the Hoarwell quickly.

'I ask that you take this draught and make your way to the waterfall overlooking Tol Ascarnen and deposit it into the river to cleanse the poison. Do this, and I shall see that you are rewarded.''Is it yet done, ${PLAYER}? We must be swift, else the Little Folk at Hoarhallow will suffer a terrible fate at the hands of Angmar.''This is a great success. You are most welcome here at Glân Vraig, and I hope that you are able to assist the other Free Peoples throughout the Ettenmoors.

'Remember, this war will not be decided easily. We are too few in number to score a decisive blow to the encampment at Gramsfoot. Ofttimes we will lose our holdings, but while we retain them there is much to do.

'Be well, friend.'The corsairs have spread traps out within the city to slow any assault.The traps must be removed for the people to safely return.Disable traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The corsairs used grappling hooks to help climb the cliffs.The grappling hooks should be removed so no more corsairs may climb them.Destroy grappling hooks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The corsairs are reinforcing their positions by moving between the city and port.The gate to the port should be closed to seal the corsairs off from their ships.Close the gate to the portCranniel, a passing merchant, is interested in sampling the wild berries dotting the shoreline.Berries can be found along the coastline of the Cape of Belfalas.

