'Hope you didn't bring down the bridge! We'll need that bridge if we're to take and hold the Palace of Eldacar!'Growing concerned in the wake of Lornost's fall, Steward Malthellim hopes to defeat the Haradrim forces camped nearby before their numbers become too great.Thama Aklam can be found to the south-east of Ost Anglebed.

Steward Malthellim has asked you to defeat the Haradrim camped nearby before they grow beyond control.Defeat Haradrim in Thama Aklam (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Half-trolls in Thama Aklam (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search Haradrim sorcerers for orders from the Scourge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Steward Malthellim can be found in the Lord's Hall in Ost Anglebed.

You have defeated many Haradrim in Thama Aklam, but were unable to find any orders. You should return to Steward Malthellim.Talk to Steward Malthellim'While you seek out their leader, I would ask that you take the fight to the Haradrim across the river.

'Their men and their... trollish men are of great concern to my warriors, ${PLAYER}, and we know little of their plans. They laid siege to Lornost and soon I fear their attention shall turn to my people in Ost Anglebed. These half-trolls are beyond our understanding... it is said that their skin protects them from flames! I would advise you to be cautious around them, for despite their size, they are strikingly precise with blades.

'Seek out orders held by their sorcerers, but leave none behind to strike against us. I await your return, ${CLASS}.''I am glad you have thinned their numbers, even if you were unable to provide us with their plans. We shall have to keep a closer eye on them, it seems...

'And those half-trolls... by the way you describe it, they seem to honour the Haradrim sorcerers above all. We may never know if it is loyalty or fear that motivates them.

'I am thankful my men can keep their posts here while we have one as skilled as you patrolling the fields.'The Free Peoples will return to take Tol Ascarnen, and Angmar's defenders wish to strengthen the walls with deterrents that will drive the foe away.Oil can be found on the Free Peoples fighting throughout the Ettenmoors. The closest camp is over the southern bridge, though a larger group can be found at Ost Ringdyr, far to the east.

Angmar's Army is shoring up the defences at Tol Ascarnen. Glat needs oil with which to douse the Free Peoples who attempt to assail the keep.'When the War-tyrant told me that he didn't like the bare walls we had here, I was at first confused. Don't smirk... you would be too, whelp, thinking that the War-tyrant wants to decorate the walls with something other than the mark of the Iron Crown or Lugbúrz. But then he tells me... oil, great gobs of boiling oil.

'We're going to need this oil, and we can only get it from the Free Peoples... the very ones we're trying to boil! We know there is a camp of them over the bridge to the south, so that is a good place to start.

'Scouts tell us that they can be found all throughout the Ettenmoors as well, though the best location is at Ost Ringdyr to the east. Get the oil and bring it back here. We'll cook up a nice surprise for the wretches.''This will do nicely. Get others to the task so we can build the iron belly and cook us some meals.'Defeat many Corsairs in Central Gondor.Defeat many Corsair in Central Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in Central GondorDefeat many Corsairs in Central Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in Central Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in Central GondorDefeat many Corsairs in West Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in West Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in West GondorDefeat many Corsairs in West Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in West Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in West GondorAn overeager dwarf-warrior made his way to the camp east of Tol Ascarnen when Angmar captured the keep. This dwarf would call the Free Peoples to his banner and make an assault against the fortress on his own, if given leave to do so.The Free Peoples' encampment is somewhere to the east of Tol Ascarnen.

Paashum sent you to the enemy encampment of Tol Ascarnen to find and defeat First Marshal Án. You should not attempt this alone as Án is a powerful combatant.The Angmar-encampment is somewhere to the west of Tol Ascarnen.

A successful assault against the Free Peoples' encampment resulted in the slaughter of the First Marshal and many of the forces located in the encampment east of Tol Ascarnen.Return to Soldier Paashum at the encampment north-east of Tol Ascarnen'We won the day, no thanks to sluggards and dullards like you. Now we must continue to press our enemy, lest they regain a foothold and strike against us.

'We've received reports that there is a dwarf who arrived at the enemy encampment somewhere on the east side of the Hoarwell River. We must get to him before the enemy can call him to action.

'Gather some other maggots and make your way across the river to assail that Marshal Án at the camp. Stop him before he arrives to assail Tol Ascarnen. Do not fail us!''Quickly! We cannot risk this dwarf facing our champions in battle.''You fight well, at least within the company of a great many. You think that makes you something more than a maggot? Think again, slug. You are not worthy of Angmar's honour, no matter how much you think you have earned.

'Soon, when the true war begins and this battle is behind us, you will see. You will march in front of our war-host and fall first to the blades of our enemies.

'I hope to become a Taskmaster someday... do you think this speech was chiding enough?'Lintanar, a city guard, is being handed tasks from many important people around the city. He fears that there just isn't enough time in the day to complete them all, and seeks your assistance.The Middle Stores are in the southern part of the Third Circle.

