You should tally sacks of grain in the Middle Stores and keep an eye out for any rats.Tally sacks of grain in the Middle Stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat any rats you encounter (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Middle Stores are in the southern part of the Third Circle.

You should speak with Rastion, and let him know that you are finished in the Middle Stores.Speak with RastionLintanar can be found in the northern part of the Third Circle.

You should speak with Lintanar.Speak with Lintanar'Might I have a word with you? Mirudil, the Warden of the Stores, has taken it upon himself to give tasks to some of the guards. While I do not agree with this shift in power, I can see we are all being asked to pull the weight of two men, and for good reason.

'While I am not readily scolded for neglecting some of my duties every now and again, I must try to do what is asked of me. I simply do not have the time to finish this task of Mirudil's though! Perhaps you would be able to lend me a hand? I have been spending much of the day tallying various supplies in the Stores of the city and there are but a couple left. Perhaps you would take count of sacks of grain in the Middle Stores? Speak with Rastion before you begin your task.''You are more than welcome to tally the sacks of grain scattered throughout the Middle Stores. Before you set about on your errand, however, I must tell you that I think I've been hearing rats scuttling around. I have not seen any signs of them yet, though. If you find any while you are back there, please dispose of them. There are many foodstuffs laying about and a rat infestation would surely ruin us.''Oh my, you did find some rats. I am glad they had not yet devoured these precious rations. Now that I know of their presence, I shall make sure no more get into the Stores.''You have counted the grain in the Middle Stores? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I was able to count the shields in the armour Stores. That now accounts for everything Mirudil wanted tallied. Hopefully, for my sake, he will not require anything else. I could use a rest!'In the wake of the Grey Host's arrival in Linhir, the Corsairs that fled the settlement stole valuable goods from the people of Dor-en-Ernil.Corsairs can be found at Hata Khezrat in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

Corsairs have stolen valuable goods from Linhir, leaving those Gondorians that remain in even more dire circumstances.Recover goods stolen from LinhirCorsairs can be found at Hata Khezrat in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

Corsairs have stolen many goods from Linhir and hoarded them in Hata Khezrat. You should defeat the Corsairs and reclaim these goods.Recover goods stolen from Linhir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have recovered many goods from the Corsairs.While scouting Hata Khezrat, you notice the Corsairs have stolen away many of Linhir's goods in their sashes.  The Corsairs took these goods out of spite as they fled Aragorn and the Grey Host, sensing an unavoidable defeat.

If the people of Dor-en-Ernil are to survive the coming days, they will need all of the supplies and rations they can muster. You would do well to return their goods to Linhir.Although the Corsairs did not easily part with them, the goods you recovered will be of great aid to the people of Dor-en-Ernil in the coming days of war.The corsairs have their own craftsmen already working within the mason.The corsair craftsmen must be prevented from producing anything.Defeat craftsmen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Efficient hunters within the crags of the Steps of Gram, the Cragstone-spiders allied themselves with the Enemy, stalk the hobbits at Hoarhallow, and drive out the Free Peoples from the west.The Cragstone-spiders can be found in the crags west of Tol Ascarnen, beyond the tower Lugazag in the shadow of Dâr-gazag.

Quartermaster Cynwiss asked you to defeat the Cragstone-spiders in the moors of the Steps of Gram.Defeat Cragstone-spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Quartermast Cynwiss awaits your return at Tol Ascarnen.

You made your way into the moors in the Steps of Gram and slaughtered a host of the Cragstone-spiders.Return to Quartermaster Cynwiss at Tol Ascarnen'Long have the Elves of Mirkwood spoken of spiders with great intelligence, but until I came here, I did not believe such tales.

