'A bundle of sticks is strong, whilst any one twig may be broken. We must seek out the Harad swordsmen in their camps and hideaways, and strike them before they strike at us in force! 

'Duty binds me to my post, here. But you, ${CLASS}, could help to strike this blow and win the glory in so doing!''Ha ha! My plan goes well apace. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We will soon send these Southrons back with their tails between their legs!'You have learned that the Orcs were sent into the Dead Marshes for some purpose. Did Frodo come this way, and does the Dark Master of the Orcs know of his passage?Artamir has asked you to investigate a number of different locations in the Dead Marshes, seeking some clue to the Orkish presence here. He asked you to seek out notable spots to the north, north-west, and west, and said he would do the same.Explore to the west of Artamir's campExplore to the north-west of Artamir's campExplore to the north of Artamir's campFind the entrance to the Orc campYou have found some interesting spots within the Dead Marshes, but few clues to the Orkish presence here. You should return now to Artamir's camp. Perhaps he found something of note.Talk to Artamir at his camp in the Dead Marshes'I am troubled by the presence of the Orcs, ${PLAYER}, and I can tell by your expression that you are as well. Have they come here for the same reason that I have? I daresay they have some fell purpose, quite unlike that of the Ruling Steward, but still I must ask: how many reasons can there be to come to such a miserable land?

'Perhaps you can find some hint to their objectives by exploring this foul swamp, my friend. There are notable places to be found, of a certainty, but you must step carefully! Try searching to the north, north-west, and west of my camp, and you may find some clues to the Orc interest here. While you are at it, you might also find the entrance to the Orc camp, for I think it likely they have established one. Do not go inside just yet! But we should know where it might be found, wouldn't you say?

'I will search as well, and meet you back at this place. Walk with caution! I have found the footing to be treacherous.''Perhaps you can find some hint to their objectives by exploring this foul swamp, my friend. There are notable places to be found, of a certainty, but you must step carefully! Try searching to the north, north-west, and west of my camp, and you may find some clues to the Orc interest here. While you are at it, you might also find the entrance to the Orc camp, for I think it likely they have established one. Do not go inside just yet! But we should know where it might be found, wouldn't you say?

'I will search as well, and meet you back at this place. Walk with caution! I have found the footing to be treacherous.''Ah, hello... hello, my friend. You... you have come back?'

Artamir blinks at you groggily. He seems to be having some difficulty focusing on your face, and often shakes his head, as if trying to clear it of a foggy sensation.

'I am fine, ${PLAYER}. I just... you know, I saw the oddest thing: a treasure, just below the water. I could nearly reach it, but then it seemed to be gone. I remembered that you were expecting to see me again, and I came back to meet you.

'This place does play tricks upon the mind, does it not?'Candúr, the town guard, asks you speak with Borhador of the situation in the Vale.Borhador can be found in The Crossing-hall.

You should speak with Borhador.Speak with Borhador'If you have a moment to spare, I must ask for your help in these dark times. Three days ago a man from the north came through this town with an army of warriors and ghosts. If you do not believe me, I understand, but I assure you I speak the truth.'

You say you know of this man and that his name is Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

'Yes, I think I recall someone saying that name. I did not know this man but many in town did or were persuaded by his words and joined him on his eastern march. He took many and the rest stayed in their homes out of fear. After this frightful army of Men and Dead left the vale, the sky grew dark and rumours spread of Trolls lurking in the woods. Three days have passed and many still say they've seen The Dead wandering through the trees.

'Borhador, the lord of the Vale, rests in his hall. Much has left his realm in these recent days, including his hope. Perhaps an outsider such as yourself, spending some time in the Vale, will give Borhador strength to lead his people again.''I have nothing to say to you, stranger. Leave me be for my days are numbered.'Darkwater drawn from the river Blackroot by Azruthor threatens people throughout the vale and could soon wash over all of Gondor.Darkwater can be found in and along the river Blackroot in Tarlang's Crown

