You stood against the foe within the walls of Lugazag. Your efforts were not in vain, and you are owed a well-earned reward.'Our fortunes will not hold forever, ${PLAYER}. Soon the dark charges of Angmar will muster and crash, wave after wave upon the walls of this forsaken tower. If we stand fast, we may yet survive the assault. If you are willing, stand with us, and we shall give them all we have and more. They will fall by the score to our host, and we shall hold them at bay until we drive them from this place.

'Stand with us, defeat the foe as they crash against the walls of Lugazag, and when this is done, I shall see you rewarded. If I fall in battle, scouts will inform Captain-General Tordúr of your bravery, and you may claim your reward from him.

