You should talk to Thurindol.Return to Thurindol'I have heard that Anborn was not displeased with the help you have given us. I believe you are trustworthy. Now let us send you out on Ranger's work so you may prove your skill and discretion.

'Not far from here lies Harlanc. It is the ruins of a small town overlooking the southern cliffs of Emyn Arnen. The ruins have recently been taken over by Haradrim who make camp there. The walls of the ruins remain mostly intact, making it a viable fortress. I want you to infiltrate the ruins and disrupt the camp however you see fit. I do, however, recommend destroying their supplies before they fortify their encampment. I wish you luck, ${PLAYER}.''Your mission went well. Truly, I am impressed! With your help we will now be able to keep the Haradrim at bay on the western side of the Gaelos. Are you sure you do not wish to stay here and join our cause?'Anborn sends you on a mission to disrupt the forces gathered at Lân Mefam. There, you will see what you can do to efficiently cripple the encampment.Lân Mefam is located east of Bâr Húrin.

You should enter the Haradrim camp, Lân Mefam.Disrupt the forces gathered at Lân MefamLân Mefam is located east of Bâr Húrin.

You should defeat Haradrim Sorcerers and search for other ways to disrupt their operations there.Complete Quest, Lân Mefam: MarksmenComplete Quest, Lân Mefam: Mûmakil FeedComplete Quest, Lân Mefam: Haradrim TentsComplete Quest, Lân Mefam: Half-troll AxesDefeat Haradrim Sorcerers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Anborn can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin.

You should return to Anborn and tell him how you disrupted the Haradrim camp.Talk to Anborn'I must say that I am surprised at your accomplishments. You've helped us at Bâr Húrin a great deal. Be not mistaken! You are still a stranger and an outsider in my eyes. I know you search for our leader, Faramir. Perhaps we can strike a deal. I will tell you of Faramir's whereabouts in Ithilien if you return alive from the mission that I myself was about to embark upon.

'Go to Lân Mefam, a Haradrim camp bordering the road to Harad. The encampment is heavily manned, but it must be brought down. If this southern camp falls, Haradrim will be less inclined to complete the journey north to the Cross-roads. Do this in whatever way you can, and I will grant you what you seek.''In truth, I doubted that you would return, but you consistently prove me wrong. Do not wax angry with me. You went full willingly, nor would I risk Lord Faramir's whereabouts with someone I did not fully trust. I trust you now. You have earned it.

'Still, I apologize for delaying you in your mission, if it be as important as you say. I deemed it a necessary precaution. Let me make amends by telling you what I know of Faramir.'Jajax is desperate to find his brother in Hata Kebir and hopes to free him from the misguided rule of the Heirs of Castamir.Jajax's brother can be found somewhere in Hata Kebir.

Jajax has begged your aid in finding his brother who he believes is among the forces at Hata Kebir.Search for Jajax's brother'There is another matter I have been hesitant to share, ${PLAYER}. I believe my brother is here among these men, and be it selfishness or sentiment, I want to help him be free from these men before he meets with some grim fate.

'We were separated when our fleet split, you see, for he has long been a favoured deckhand of the Scourge. I did not seek to deny him the honour of serving on such a ship, but now... I wish him to be as far away from the Scourge and his brothers as he can.

'Let us search for him, and then leave this place.''Jajax, can it be you? And what are you doing with this ${RACE}? Have you lost your edge, brother?'

Jajax and Daxamat laugh and the two men share a brief embrace. Jajax explains your unconventional friendship to Daxamat before asking why he's tending the stables in Hata Kebir.

'As you can see, I am no longer so favoured amongst the Heirs, but I think the horses have grown to appreciate me. Still... why have you come here?'The Corsairs are attempting to collapse the bridge leading to the Swan-knight Barracks.The sappers must be defeated.Defeat sappers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Become Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - ArmouryBecome Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - BankAchieve Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - ArmouryComplete Tol Fennas - Hunting the HuntersComplete Tol Fennas - The Corsair CroupComplete Tol Fennas - Corsair CrafstmenComplete Tol Fennas - Floating KindlingComplete Dol Amroth - Armoury - Weapons of the GuardComplete Dol Amroth - Armoury - Guarding the OceanComplete Dol Amroth - Armoury - Tending the WoundedComplete Dol Amroth - Armoury - Checking for IntrudersComplete Dol Amroth - Armoury - Arms and ArmoursComplete Dol Amroth - Armoury - Punishing the PurloinersAttain Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - BankComplete Dol Amroth - Bank - Looking for InterlopersComplete Dol Amroth - Bank - Securing the SavingsComplete Dol Amroth - Bank - Closing the PortComplete Dol Amroth - Bank - Clearing the PathComplete Dol Amroth - Bank - Pilfer and PlunderComplete Dol Amroth - Bank - Up in SmokeComplete Tarlang's Crown - Servants of the HeirsComplete Tarlang's Crown - Waters of the BlackrootComplete Tarlang's Crown - A Dangerous ThirstComplete Tarlang's Crown - Carried DownriverAchieve Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - DocksComplete Turtles in the DepthsComplete The Salmon RunComplete Baiting the HookComplete The Bait BallComplete Dol Amroth - Docks - Shelter in PlaceComplete Dol Amroth - Docks - Supplies from the SeaComplete Dol Amroth - Docks - Sinking the FleetComplete Dol Amroth - Docks - Sealing the CityComplete Dol Amroth - Docks - Down with his ShipComplete Dol Amroth - Docks - The Fleet of GondorAchieve Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - Great HallComplete Tol Fennas - Planting AnewComplete Tol Fennas - SnaresComplete Tol Fennas - Ravens' RookeryComplete Tol Fennas - Caught and CagedComplete Dol Amroth - Great Hall - There's Always One...Complete Dol Amroth - Great Hall - Climbing a CliffComplete Dol Amroth - Great Hall - Garden of LumberComplete Dol Amroth - Great Hall - The Heart of Dol AmrothComplete Dol Amroth - Great Hall - Foul WatersComplete Dol Amroth - Great Hall - Stripping it BareAchieve Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - LibraryComplete Hashadîr - Captains of the CrewComplete Hashadîr - A Place to Lie at NightComplete Hashadîr - Slavers of MenComplete Hashadîr - Trapping the BeachComplete Dol Amroth - Library - Ashes of KnowledgeComplete Dol Amroth - Library - Guardians of Dol AmrothComplete Dol Amroth - Library - Shattered GlassComplete Dol Amroth - Library - Securing the PastComplete Dol Amroth - Library - Freedom's ThiefComplete Dol Amroth - Library - Saving the ScholarsAttain Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - MasonComplete Dol Amroth - Mason - Tools of the TradeComplete Dol Amroth - Mason - Stealing a SoulComplete Dol Amroth - Mason - Flooded with ArrowsComplete Dol Amroth - Mason - The Materials of WarComplete Dol Amroth - Mason - Locked UpComplete Dol Amroth - Mason - Crafting CommandeeredComplete Emyn Ernil Tunnels - Forgotten OreComplete Emyn Ernil Tunnels - Corsair SurveyorsComplete Emyn Ernil Tunnels - Claws of the DeepComplete Emyn Ernil Tunnels - Twists and TurnsComplete Emyn Ernil Cave - Shattered CrystalsComplete Emyn Ernil Cave - Mining with OarsComplete Emyn Ernil Cave - Shaky ScaffoldsComplete Emyn Ernil Cave - Captain Without a ShipAchieve Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - Swan-knightsComplete Kêr Izel - Lenn DûskudComplete Kêr Izel - The Shadow-watchComplete Kêr Izel - Fallen but not ForgottenComplete Kêr Izel - The Ruthless DeadComplete Kêr Bras - A Message of CourageComplete Kêr Bras - The Ruthless DeadComplete Kêr Bras - The FallenComplete Kêr Bras - Bloom of DecayComplete Dol Amroth - Swan-knights - Dividing the BridgeComplete Dol Amroth - Swan-knights - Death From AboveComplete Dol Amroth - Swan-knights - Sweeping for StragglersComplete Dol Amroth - Swan-knights - Wounded in ActionComplete Dol Amroth - Swan-knights - Looting the SwanComplete Dol Amroth - Swan-knights - Rescuing the KnightAchieve Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - WarehouseComplete Tol Aduial - A Feast of DrakesComplete Tol Aduial - CorsairsComplete Tol Aduial - Smoke SignalsComplete Tol Aduial - A Hunter's ProwessComplete Dol Amroth - Warehouse - Stores for WinterComplete Dol Amroth - Warehouse - Slave to the SeaComplete Dol Amroth - Warehouse - Fire and WaterComplete Dol Amroth - Warehouse - Securing the WayComplete Dol Amroth - Warehouse - Fanning the FlamesComplete Dol Amroth - Warehouse - Very Hungry RatsBecome Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - DocksBecome Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - Great HallThe guard has long been responsible for watching over Dol Amroth and ensuring the safety of its townsfolk.Beriaudur has much to tell you about the city guard of Dol Amroth.Speak to Beriaudur to learn more about the city guardTo prove yourself able to watch over the library, you must first accomplish a series of tasks.

Tolrían will be able to inform you of the necessary tasks.Complete Hashadîr - Captains of the CrewComplete Hashadîr - A Place to Lie at NightComplete Hashadîr - Slavers of MenComplete Hashadîr - Trapping the BeachYou must be acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - Library to be allowed to guard over it as part of the Dol Amroth town watch.Use the Library Tokens to earn Acquaintance with the LibraryBeriaudur is in Dol Amroth.

Beriaudur will be pleased to hear you are now acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - Library.Speak to Beriaudur'Welcome to Dol Amroth, ${PLAYER}. I have seen you about the city as of late, and you appear to have done much to aid Belfalas and our peoples here. But the threat against us looms ever present, and one must be vigilant in their watch for the shadows.

'If you are interested, we could find a place for you within the city guard. You would need to prove yourself, many times over. Should you rise to the mark though, Dol Amroth would consider you one of her own.

'Speak to me again if you wish to know more.''Dol Amroth is not a small city. We have stretched and sprawled over the years to cover many an acre, and that's without considering the docks and port. It is a large area for us to patrol and cover. Each section of the city has its own personality and people who call it home. Each has its own needs and dangers.

'Our guards are not all allowed to patrol and keep watch over every section of the city. You must learn that section to earn the right and privilege of serving it.

'You shall start where all young recruits do, with the library. Do a series of tasks for Tolrían and you shall receive some recompense. Return when you have it.''Good, now that you have attained their respect, you will be able to watch over the library district and quell any problems that arise there.

'Each of the districts has its own tokens their people consider valuable. Gather them up and earn their respect and then you will be able to serve them as well.'Become Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - LibraryBecome Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - MasonBecome Acquaintance with the Dol Amroth - Swan-knightsYou are retaking the armoury of Dol Amroth!Retake the armoury.Defeat JabburDefeat bands of corsairs (${VALUE}/5)You are retaking the bank of Dol Amroth!Retake the bank.Defeat KhabecDefeat bands of corsairs (${VALUE}/8)You are retaking the docks of Dol Amroth!Retake the docks.Defeat DarîjanDefeat bands of corsairs (${VALUE}/9)You are retaking the Great Hall of Dol Amroth!Retake the Great Hall.Defeat MîkhinDefeat bands of corsairs (${VALUE}/8)You are retaking the library of Dol Amroth!Retake the library.Defeat UrbinYou are retaking the mason of Dol Amroth!Retake the mason.Defeat BarkyatDefeat bands of corsairs (${VALUE}/7)You are retaking the barracks of the Swan-knights of Dol Amroth!Retake the barracks of the Swan-knights.Defeat KesekhosDefeat bands of Corsairs (${VALUE}/8)You are retaking the warehouse of Dol Amroth!Retake the warehouse.Defeat DabardonDefeat bands of corsairs (${VALUE}/5)The city guard has asked you to join it on a patrol of the immediate area.The city watch of Dol Amroth is performing a training exercise in which they wish you to participate.

<rgb=#FF0000>Once accepted, this quest cannot be cancelled. You must complete the training exercise to finish the quest.</rgb>Speak to Beriaudur and start the training exercise'Join us on a patrol of the area surrounding the city. This will be a full march, all of the city guard participating in an exercise and show of force. We shall meet outside the gate, ride to Amon Lontir and then loop our way back.

'Along the way we will stop to practice certain maneouvres and do a mock assault on Amon Lontir. We shall be gone for several hours and return to the city around nightfall.

'Speak to me when you are ready to depart.'

