You have listened to Faltharan's troubles, and should now assure him of your intent to help him.Talk to Faltharan'${PLAYER}, have you noticed the lord regent up above? His eyes have not left my men and me for some time now.

'I believe he means to join our charge, but the boy is... not suited for battle. He bears ill-fitting armour and is not skilled with a blade, despite what he may think after his recent heroics in the city. I see a darkness in his demeanour, and I believe he intends to rush into the war without care for himself or his family.

'Convince him of his folly, my friend. See that he remains here with his people, for there is much rebuilding to be done here - for the city and its folk.'Faltharan appears lost in thought as you approach, and his gaze is fixed on the eastern gate of Pelargir.

'I know you have come to dissuade me, friend, but I cannot be turned from my task.

'So much has happened in so swift a time... it has been but a few days since Pelargir was reclaimed, but still many more troubles weigh on me...''Will you aid me in this, ${PLAYER}?

'I know your journey shall soon take you far from Lebennin, but I can think of no other that might spare the time for such a task.'Aragorn will need the port of the Harlond cleared if he and his men are to make landfall with haste.Turgon can be found at the southern gate of the Rammas.

