The goblins believe that the beards are a matter of pride amongst the dwarves and want you to help them humiliate their hated foes. Fim the Worm bade you strip the beards of the dwarves in return for favour from the Snowreap.'Long have we fought in the mountain-hearts, through caverns and ice floes, over the halls of dead dwarves across our bridges and theirs. It is a battle that scars my folk, stays with us always. We hate the dwarves!

'Slaughter them all, we say. Take their beards and destroy them. They take pride in beards, or so it says. So we strip them of their pride, make them suffer as they make the goblins suffer.

'Bring us their beards, and we speak well of you. Bring the beards of the dwarves to me.''Look at these, so thick and full! We burn them on the fires and praise the Great Eye! We cull the dwarves! We meet them in battle and face them with our brothers from Angmar!

'Dead dwarves! Dead dwarves! We cheer your name by the light of fire, ${PLAYER}! We cheer and praise you to the Eye!'Goblins complain that the mine is overrun by dwarves, and they are not pleased by the intrusion. They bid you to enter the Isendeep to slaughter the dwarf-miners.The Isendeep mine lay to the west of Grothum. If there are no dwarves within the mine, make your way to the western entrance and search for them there.

Gasham asked you to enter the mine and slaughter the dwarves so the goblins can return to work.Gasham awaits news of the mines at Grothum, the goblin-village in the north-east Ettenmoors.

You entered the mine and slaughtered all the dwarves you found. You should return to Gasham with the news.'People come and take the mine, and the Snowreap retreat to the village. You come now to take back the mine so we work and give you ore again?

'Too many dwarves. Too many dwarves poking about in the stone, digging the ore for themselves. Kill them, says I. Kill them all.

'You kill them, and we work extra hard and speak good of what you done. Kill them, aye?''You go to the mine and kill dwarves. Come back when done.''You done? Killed them good. Good. No more dwarves means goblins can mine and then give ore to Angmar!

'Kill them all, says I. For the glory of the Great Eye!'Defeat many Easterlings in Eastern Gondor.Defeat many Easterlings in Eastern Gondor.Defeat many Easterlings in Eastern GondorDefeat many Easterlings in Eastern Gondor.Defeat many Easterlings in Eastern Gondor.Defeat many Easterlings in Eastern GondorDefeat many Easterlings in Old Anórien.Defeat many Easterlings in Old Anórien.Defeat many Easterlings in Old AnórienDefeat many Easterlings in Old Anórien.Defeat many Easterlings in Old Anórien.Defeat many Easterlings in Old AnórienTaskmaster Ghamp offered you a reward to find sticks not as big as logs. This likely means smaller-sized wood, like the kindling found throughout the Grimwood.Grimwood-kindling can be found throughout the Grimwood area, from fallen timber. You might also find it on the Leafcull-trees in the wood.

Taskmaster Ghamp, in his own way, directed you to get Grimwood-kindling for repairs at the lumber-yard.'Not log.

'Big sticks.

'You get!''Sticks used to fix things.'The Maresfoot that tainted Brunil's draught is delivered daily by a man named Egind.Egind should be at the front gate of Imloth Melui with the day's delivery of Maresfoot.

Brunil has asked you to confront Egind with the knowledge of his treachery.Confront Egind at the front gate of Imloth MeluiBrunil can be found in the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of Imloth Melui.

Egind has confessed that he did not mean to ruin the healing draughts. He substituted a similar-looking plant when he could not collect the proper Maresfoot that Brunil expected.Talk to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand'The Maresfoot that goes into the healing draughts is gathered by a man named Egind, and delivered to me daily. I have never had any problems with him before now, but it seems he has shown his true colours at last, the treacherous knave! 

'Egind will likely be somewhere near the front gate of the city, hoping to hand us another bushel of poisoned greens! Confront him with our discovery and see what he has to say for himself!''Please don't hurt me! I'm sorry, so sorry! I beg of you, mercy!

'I could not get the proper Maresfoot by the banks of the river, on account of all those Orcs haunting the place. So I picked some ones that looked just like 'em, up in the hillside scrub. I didn't mean for any harm to come of it!

'Please tell Brunil to spare my hide, ${PLAYER}! I feel terrible about this, but we cannot all be warriors! I am an old man, and my fingers are for picking herbs and flowers, not for swinging swords in anger!''Well, ${PLAYER}? What did Egind have to say for himself?'

You explain what the old man said about his ill-advised substitution of another herb for the Maresfoot, and Brunil scowls.

'I should have known! He must have given me Beruthiel's Rue instead of Maresfoot! They bear similar appearances, it is true, but they could not be more different in effect! It seems there was never a rat in Imloth Melui after all... merely a frightened old man making things worse instead of better! I cannot blame him for his fear, ${PLAYER}. I am not a warrior either, and these Southrons are fearsome indeed. What did you say? Orcs? No, I am certain Egind was frightened of the Southron warriors I have heard rumour of in these lands. There are no Orcs in Lossarnach.'Lieutenant Solvi asked that you assist him in collecting emergency rations for the fortress.There are nerbyg all around Tol Ascarnen. Lieutenant Solvi is at Tol Ascarnen.

Lieutenant Solvi awaits your return with the meat and gizzards from the nerbyg.'Listen well, ${CLASS}. We're in a battle that will rage for a good long time, and we're in need of supplies. Though the land will give up some edible meats, much of what is here is useless.

'Now, food stores are raided often, and we've lost a good portion of our supplies. We need to be mindful of the future and think about ways that we can increase our existing food sources. This might turn your stomach some -- it does mine -- but there are nerbyg surrounding this fortress, and though they might seem a might unsavoury, we've found that cooked long enough and with enough spice, they can make a good source of food... in a pinch.

'Round up a bundle of their gizzards and meat, and I'll reward you for what you bring.''Terrible sort of thing to do, but we're not here to be making a comely home. We are in a war, ${CLASS}. War makes you do things you would ought not normally do.

'You've earned this, ${PLAYER}. Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig is collecting these for greater rewards.'Corsair foremen are directing the digging within the large cave under Emyn Ernil.The Corsair foremen are patrolling the large cave beneath Emyn Ernil.

Lhossil asked you to defeat the Corsair foremen directing the miners beneath Emyn Ernil.Defeat Corsair foremen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lhossil can be found in Dol Amroth.

Lhossil will be very pleased to hear the Corsair foremen have been eliminated.Speak to Lhossil'Several Corsair captains have been spotted within the large cave beneath Emyn Ernil. I suppose without a ship they cannot be regarded as captains anymore, since they are directing the digging and mining efforts. Let's call them foremen instead.

'Head into the cave and eliminate them. Without leadership the miners will cease digging and we can slow down their operation.''Without direction their mining efforts will slow for the foreseeable future.'Corsair miners are digging for ore and crystals within the large cave under Emyn Ernil.Corsair miners are digging in the large cave beneath Emyn Ernil.

Lhossil asked you to defeat the Corsair miners digging beneath Emyn Ernil.Defeat Corsair miners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lhossil can be found in Dol Amroth.

Lhossil will be very pleased to hear the Corsair miners have been defeated.Speak to Lhossil'The Corsairs are digging within the large cave beneath Emyn Ernil. I am not sure if they are searching for ore or more of the crystals found within the cave. Either way, any raw materials they can use to make further weapons and armour is only a bad thing for us.

'Defeat the miners within the cave to put a hold on their operations.''The miners have been eliminated, putting any digging operations on hold.'The scaffolding holding up the ceiling of the large cave in Emyn Ernil is old and rotting.Rotting scaffolding may be found in the large cave beneath Emyn Ernil.

Lhossil asked you to venture beneath Emyn Ernil and repair some of the scaffold within that is rotting away.Repair rotting scaffold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lhossil can be found in Dol Amroth.

Lhossil will be pleased to hear the scaffold has been shored up.Speak to Lhossil'The caves within Emyn Ernil don't simply support themselves, they are held up by networks of scaffolding. This scaffolding is decades old and surely has started to rot and fail. If it does, the entire cave will come collapsing down and anything of value within will be lost.

'While we cannot replace all of the scaffolding, we can do some spot repairs on some of the worst areas. Look around in the cave for scaffolding that appears particularly bad and shore it up.''Once we are rid of these Corsairs we'll need to go in and do a proper job of replacing them fully. For now, spot fixes like this will have to do.'The large cave within Emyn Ernil hosts some very mysterious crystals in which the Corsairs hold great interest.Crystal shards may be found in the large cave beneath Emyn Ernil.

Lhossil asked you to venture beneath Emyn Ernil and recover some crystal shards from the large cave.Acquire crystal shards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lhossil can be found in Dol Amroth.

Lhossil will be pleased to begin examining the crystal shards you found.Speak to Lhossil'There is a large cave within Emyn Ernil to which the Corsairs have taken a particular focus. Within it, there appear to be several crystal formations. While that's not altogether unique, what is peculiar about these crystals is they glow, even in pure darkness.

'The Corsairs have taken a particular interest in these crystals. I do not know why, whether for a military purpose or some ancient ritual. Either way, if they want them, we must know why. Gather some samples and bring them back to me.''They look ordinary to me. I will need to do some further testing to determine if there is anything peculiar or unique about them.'The Corsair intrusion has awoken the deep-claws beneath Emyn Ernil, threatening the stability of the tunnels.Deep-claws are digging in the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil.

Gelloth asked you to defeat the deep-claws that are threatening to collapse the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil.Defeat deep-claw diggers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gelloth can be found in Dol Amroth.

Gelloth will be very pleased to hear the tunnels are safe from collapse.Speak to Gelloth'The Corsairs know not what trouble they awaken, nor do I think they care. Their explorations of the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil have awoken several beasts from the depths, deep-claws. Large lumbering creatures that, when awake, serve only to dig.

'We cannot allow the tunnels to collapse from their work. The deep-claws must be stopped so we can continue to search and recover whatever of value is beneath. Head into the tunnels and defeat the creatures.''I am sure there are more down there sleeping, waiting to be awoken. But for now, the tunnels should be safe.'Corsairs have been exploring and scouting the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil.The Corsair surveyors are exploring the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil.

Gelloth asked you to prevent the Corsair surveyors from exploring and mapping the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil.Defeat Corsair surveyors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gelloth can be found in Dol Amroth.

Gelloth will be very pleased to hear the surveyors have been eliminated.Speak to Gelloth'We've seen Corsair flags on the top of Emyn Ernil. I believe they have scaled the sides of the mountain and somehow found a way in through some cracks and open air caves.

'If they are down there they are surely exploring and mapping the tunnels. Search the tunnels and find any Corsair surveyors. Make sure their information doesn't get back to their ships.''We don't know the full extent of the tunnels yet ourselves. Until we do, the Corsairs cannot have that information.'Emyn Ernil was home to a thriving mining operation in past generations. Remnants and leftovers may still be found within the twisting tunnels.Ore may be found in the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil.

Gelloth asked you to venture beneath Emyn Ernil and try to find ore within the tunnels.Acquire ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gelloth can be found in Dol Amroth.

Gelloth will be pleased to process the ore you found beneath Emyn Ernil.Speak to Gelloth'In my grandfather's time they used to mine in the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil. But then a great rock slide happened. Many perished and the entrance was sealed up. Only recently have we found ourselves with a pressing need to open them again.

'There should still be ore to be found within the tunnels. With some of it we can make some more weapons and armour to defend ourselves. Head to the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil and try to find some leftover ore.''We likely won't be able to get more than a sword out of this amount, but that is one more weapon than we have now.'The tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil are a maze of twists and turns.Posts can be found in the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil.

Gelloth asked you to venture beneath Emyn Ernil and mark the posts throughout the tunnels to aid in navigation.Mark posts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gelloth can be found in Dol Amroth.

Gelloth will be pleased to hear the posts have been marked.Speak to Gelloth'Any map of the tunnels beneath Emyn Ernil has long since been lost. That makes exploration a dangerous endeavour. The tunnels are a maze of twists and turns, intersections and dead-ends. It is easy to find yourself suddenly turned around and lost.

'There are beams to be found amongst the scaffolding holding most of the tunnels up. As you descend, mark the beams you come across. This will help others who follow in your stead to map their route and find their way back out.''Hopefully that will lead to fewer lost explorers over the next several days.'A scouting force of Corsairs has been lurking nearby the small settlement of Malbarth and seeks to pillage and overpower the few people that dwell there.Corsair scouts can be found on the outskirts of Malbarth in north-western Lebennin.

Melawen has asked you to search for and defeat any Corsair scouts encroaching on Malbarth.Defeat Corsair scouts near Malbarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Melawen can be found in Malbarth in north-western Lebennin.

You have defeated many Corsair scouts and should now return to Melawen.Talk to Melawen'It is good that you have come to us, ${PLAYER}.

'The war has brought few ills to the people of Malbarth, but with each passing day, we seem drawn closer to the invasion on the coast. Men lurk in the trees... just beyond our sight. In the dark of this morn, I slew one attempting to pillage my home and where there is one Corsair, there shall always be more.

'We are not weak folk, traveller, but we are few. If you would aid us in driving them back for even one day more, we would all be thankful.''I am grateful you have driven them back once more, ${PLAYER}.

'We enjoy a peace here that few others in Lebennin can claim in these dark times, and through your aid, we shall be free of those raiders for another day.'Edenos has tasked you with defeating encroaching spiders from the Morgul Vale that have recently crossed the river.Spiders can be found on the Western side of Osgiliath.

You should defeat the encroaching Spiders.Defeat Spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many Spiders in Western Osgiliath.Completed'Spiders from the East have marched into the city, most likely under command of the Morgul army. It seems they found a way to cross the river.

'I'm sending you out there to kill any of those creatures you can find. I don't need those beasts ambushing my soldiers.'You have defeated many Spiders thus making the Western side of the city a safer place to defend against the enemy.Far to the north, where the Isendeep Mine runs beneath the shadow of the Mountains of Angmar, a brood of drakes threatens the workers within the mine.Wintersebb-drakes can be found north in the area of Arador's End.

Lieutenant Swithulf directed you to make your way north with others in search of a way to destroy the Wintersebb-drakes.Lieutenant Swithulf awaits your return at the Grimwood Lumber-yard.

Climbing high into the foothills of the Mountains of Angmar in Arador's end, you faced down many foes from the Wintersebb-brood and emerged to collect your reward.Return to Lieutenant Swithulf at the Grimwood Lumber Camp'In the north, at the edge of the Mountains of Angmar, there are drakes the Hobbits of Hoarhallow call Wintersebb. So named for their trek down the mountain when the winter breaks and the Hoardale flows strong again.

'These drakes have become active since the arrival of the Free Peoples, and often they hamper our efforts to mine the Isendeep. We are in need of help culling their number to ensure that our efforts there go smoothly.

'If you are willing, gather allies and make your way north to confront the Wintersebb brood.''You will find the Wintersebb-drakes north of here in the land called Arador's end. Seek out and destroy the drakes and drakelings you find there. A word of caution, friend: you will not want to venture there alone.''A great victory is earned this day, and it is by your hand that it has been gained. You have proven your worth to the Free Peoples and deserve this reward for your efforts.

'Should you wish to claim your ultimate prize, seek out Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig.

'You have earned your honour well, ${PLAYER}.'Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn has an idea that could give the Free Peoples the ability to drive the forces of Angmar from the Isendeep, but the plan is not without grave danger.Thistledown grazers are found on the southern side of the Hoarwell River or on the plains of the Steps of Gram. The grazing land near the Hoarwell is south and west from the dwarf camp and the grazing land in the Steps of Gram is to the south and east.

Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn believes that with some clever tactics, the Free Peoples may use the drakes against Angmar's host and sweep through the mines behind them to recover the position.The flat stone is very near where the War-tyrant commands his forces within the Isendeep Mine.

Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn wants to drive the forces of Angmar from the Isendeep. He believes with some clever placement, the Free Peoples may use the drakes against Angmar's host and sweep through the mines behind them to recover the position.'Angmar has got hold of the mine, and we need to get back in there. There are not enough forces to call from the south to storm such a large place, but all may not be lost yet.

'Our enemy here has enemies, and if we are smart about how we handle this, we might yet turn the enemy of our enemy into an ally, at least for a moment.

'I'm talking about the drakes that make the mine and the surrounding areas their home. We might get them to fight against the Orcs if we can draw their attention to them. To do that we need to get some meat...Thistledown haunches ought to do, ${CLASS}. Collect some and bring them back to me.''These will do very nicely. Now you must make your way into the mine and find the flat stone near the War-tyrant watching over the mine. Place the haunches on this stone, and I'll bet the smell draws the drakes to the location.'Grazadhal commands you should fight and slaughter foes around the Armoury for the glory of Mordor.The Armoury is located on the Western side of Osgiliath.

You should fight and slaughter foes around the Armoury.Slaughter members of the Gondorian Army at the Armoury (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grazadhal is at Dâr Dugoth.

You should listen to Grazadhal yell at you.Listen to Grazadhal yell at you'Turns out those measly Gondorians have set up a base at the Armoury across the river. I don't like the sound of that!

'Go over there and slaughter any foe! If they're alive, you didn't do a good enough job!''For your sake, I hope they're all dead. I just want to see dead bodies when I go over myself to take the Armoury!'Melethon has ordered you to fight and slaughter foes around the Eastern Wharf in the goal to retake Osgiliath.The Eastern Wharf is located on the Eastern side of Osgiliath.

You should fight and slaughter foes around the Eastern Wharf.Defeat minions of Mordor at the Eastern Wharf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Melethon is at the Causeway Forts.

You should speak to Melethon.Speak with Melethon'The time has come to retake the Eastern Wharf! I need every soldier to stand with me as we march upon the enemy.

'Go and defeat as many foes as you can at the Eastern Wharf. We shall take back this city!''You have done much for the Gondorian army. Victory will surely be ours!'The Host of the West has many fine wares for those who would aid them.The Host of the West Quartermaster asked you to bring them fifty Host of the West Silver Pieces.'I have some special inventory on offer. If you bring me 50 Host of the West Silver pieces, I will give you Enhancement Runes. I can offer you this deal once a day at most.''Excellent. Our business is concluded for now.'The Host of the West has many fine wares for those who would aid them.The Host of the West Quartermaster asked you to bring them one-hundred Host of the West Silver Pieces.'I have some special inventory on offer. If you bring me 100 Host of the West Silver pieces, I will give you Enhancement Runes. I can offer you this deal once a week at most.''Excellent. Our business is concluded for now.'Seeking vengeance against the Men of Gondor, the Hand of the First Blade has come to Minas Tirith to cut down the innocents that still dwell within the besieged city.

