Dorthaneth wants to fulfill the wishes of Lady Galadriel, and has asked you to borrow a fast horse from the Master of Horses and carry out an important errand in the Dead Marshes.Borrow the swift horse from the Master of Horses and ride to the Dead MarshesArtamir, son of Ilcamir, has come to the Dead Marshes on an errand, but Galadriel of Lórien fears his presence there may draw unwanted attention to those lands.Talk to Artamir at his camp in the Dead Marshes'I am glad you have come to the Cave of the Avorrim, ${PLAYER}, for with the dawn came messages from afar, and one of these concerns you directly. The Lady of Lórien speaks in cryptic words, but I can discern enough to know that you will be able to interpret her wishes.

'Lady Galadriel speaks of a Gondorian man on an errand he believes important. It has drawn him into the Dead Marshes by the Battle Plain of old, and his feet are dogged by servants of the Enemy. The Lady of Lórien does not need to express her desire in words for me to know what drives this message: she does not want this Gondorian man to draw the attention of the Orcs to this place.

'The Avorrim keep several fast horses for their personal use, but none so swift as that cared for by our Master of Horses. Speak to him and ride to the Dead Marshes with all the speed you can muster, and hasten this Gondorian back to his home-lands before he causes great harm by his presence there.''The Avorrim keep several fast horses for their personal use, but none so swift as that cared for by our Master of Horses. Speak to him and ride to the Dead Marshes with all the speed you can muster, and hasten this Gondorian back to his home-lands before he causes great harm by his presence there.''If it be Dorthaneth's wish for you to depart in such haste, I will not stand in your way. The steeds of the Avorrim may give even the fabled Mearas a close race, if you want to know my opinion!

'Ride swiftly, and at once, if it is the wish of Dorthaneth!''If it be Dorthaneth's wish for you to depart in such haste, I will not stand in your way. The steeds of the Avorrim may give even the fabled Mearas a close race, if you want to know my opinion!

'Ride swiftly, and at once, if it is the wish of Dorthaneth!''The Avorrim keep several fast horses for their personal use, but none so swift as that cared for by our Master of Horses. Speak to him and ride to the Dead Marshes with all the speed you can muster, and hasten this Gondorian back to his home-lands before he causes great harm by his presence there.''If it be Dorthaneth's wish for you to depart in such haste, I will not stand in your way. The steeds of the Avorrim may give even the fabled Mearas a close race, if you want to know my opinion!

'Ride swiftly, and at once, if it is the wish of Dorthaneth!''The Avorrim keep several fast horses for their personal use, but none so swift as that cared for by our Master of Horses. Speak to him and ride to the Dead Marshes with all the speed you can muster, and hasten this Gondorian back to his home-lands before he causes great harm by his presence there.''Hail, stranger! It is good to see a friendly face in this inhospitable land! I caution you to watch your step, for I would not want to lose you so quickly beneath the mire... we have only just met!

'I am Artamir son of Ilcamir, and I call the White City my home. From where do you come, my friend? No matter your answer you are far from home in this place, I warrant!'Sheltered from the conflict growing on the coastline, the people of Malbarth look to their ancient beliefs for answers in these dark times.Melawen can be found in Malbarth in western Lebennin.

Barchir has asked you to speak with the people of Malbarth before you depart for the east.Talk to MelawenLendithil can be found in Malbarth in western Lebennin.

Barchir has asked you to speak with the people of Malbarth before you depart for the east.Talk to LendithilArvaeth can be found to the north-west of Malbarth in western Lebennin.

Barchir has asked you to speak with the people of Malbarth before you depart for the east.Talk to Arvaeth'I am not certain what to make of your presence here, traveller.

'Am I to be concerned that the war marches closer to our doors this day? Or... am I simply fortunate to have one as well-equipped as yourself visit our village?'

You tell Barchir of Erianir's suggestion to travel north and then east to meet the other warriors near the Enemy's holdings outside Pelargir.

'Ah, so that is it then. I am afraid I cannot offer you much in the way of aid in your journey beyond a cooked meal and firm bed, but my friends in Malbarth may have yet more to ask of you.''I bid you welcome to Malbarth, traveller.

'If you have made it this far north, the Corsairs must be wary of you. For my part, I miss the bright, peaceful days that were once common in Lebennin... with the darkening of the sky, I do not see how any can be happy.

'Strange things have been afoot near our homes, and I fear we will soon be forced into this war. I would ask you remain here a moment if you would seek to aid me.''I have heard word from Ost Anglebed that Lornost fell to the Corsairs...

'Their stone walls did nothing to repel the Corsairs and Haradrim, much less those horrible half-trolls... what hope do we have?

'I am sorry, traveller, I do not wish to speak more of this.''I refuse to believe our end comes soon.

'Have even the most devout people of these lands dismissed the tales of old? I will not abandon hope while the Sisters still watch over Lebennin.'Faltharan has asked you to accompany him as his family departs for more safe lands.Faltharan can be found at the steps to Tol Ciryarani.

Speak with Faltharan to head to the shipyard.Join Faltharan as he says his good-byesFaltharan can be found at the steps to Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Faltharan.Talk to Faltharan'All the plans are set, and we are finally ready to set our matters into motion.

'Pelargir is a city that deserves to be restored to its former glory. With that, we will need to preserve its people, as well as its bloodline. We cannot protect everyone from the storm that has arrived, but we can try to steer them away from it.

'I understand that my family wishes to speak before their departure. Will you accompany, ${PLAYER}?''Come, let us make our way to the docks. I don't intend to stay for longer than is necessary, but I wish to make sure everything is in order for their departure.''And so, the ship has left our gates to make way towards the western coast. It had to be done, ${PLAYER}, for I cannot guarantee their safety here, nor my own.

'Hopefully it will reach Dol Amroth without incident. I would only expect to set my mind at rest once I've heard word from them, but until that day comes, I must carry out my duties.'Corsairs have fled into the hills of Dor-en-Ernil, hinting that their forces may be beginning to regroup further from Linhir.The Corsairs' hideout can be found somewhere to the north-west of Hata Khezrat along the mountainside.

