You have found naught but slain Corsairs in the cave and should examine their bodies to determine what has occurred.Examine a fallen Corsair'It would be a far easier task to stop these Corsairs if they had not fled throughout our lands. Those to the north concern me greatly, but not nearly as much as those that fled into the hills.

'The mountainside is rife with small passages and it is likely they hide their numbers within. If we do not rout them now, I can think of few better places to hold for a prolonged conflict.

'Search the mountainside to the north and west of here, ${PLAYER}. Since we have learned much from these Corsairs, I shall return to Linhir and speak with Garvir. When you have learned of their hideout, I trust I shall see you in Linhir once more!'This fallen Corsair curiously bears no wounds. Stranger still, a mixture of surprise and fear are readily apparent in his face, hinting that he and his men were taken unawares by some unknown foe.Not all who rise to military prominence are capable of complete conversations. Trolls, known for their strength, sometimes manage small words. For instance, Taskmaster Núrsufum. Apparently, Taskmaster Núrsufum likes to place feathers in his helmet and wants you to go about getting the feathers he desires.Sun-touched eagles are found throughout the Coldfells and sections of Arador's End.

Taskmaster Núrsufum wants you to get him tailfeathers for his helm.'Feathers... good... crown.

