Smith, is in need dire need of additional metal for barricades, armour, and weapons for those in Minas Tirith.Metal scrap can be found in Orkish encampments near the Causeway Forts in Pelennor.

You should collect metal scrap for Aglarang.Collect metal scrap on Pelennor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aglarang can be found outside the Smiths' Fellow-hall on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should bring the metal scrap to Aglarang.Speak with AglarangThe Forges of Cirion can be found near the Smiths' Fellow-hall on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should bring the metal scrap to to the Forges of Cirion for smelting.Bring the metal scrap to the forges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aglarang can be found outside the Smiths' Fellow-hall on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak to Aglarang.Speak with Aglarang'I have been working in the forges every day since I was a young apprentice. I could not imagine a better life than shaping metal into useful objects. Yet, in all my days have I not run into a shortage of metal!

'I've seen the siege towers looming in the distance. There must be plenty of metal in the camps on the other side of Pelennor. If only I knew someone brave enough to venture out there. You're not volunteering, are you?''Look at all this metal! I'm amazed you made it back unscathed! Now, you should bring the scrap metal to our forges. You'll find them in the Forges of Cirion.''Thanks again for replenishing the forge. We will be able to make some more barricades for the wall now. With the height of those siege towers, I suspect we'll need them!'Tolwin has asked you to mitigate the damage done to crops north of Cirthost by putting out fires in the fields, then collect any supplies that haven't been burned by the enemy.Fires can be found in the fields near Parth Lisc.

You should put out fires in the fields.Put out fires in the fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Supplies can be found around the farm houses in Parth Lisc.

Now that the fires are dealt with, you should recover any supplies from the farm.Recover supplies from Parth Lisc (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.

You should speak with Tolwin.Bring the supplies for Tolwin'The look-out in Crithost's tower has seen fires in the farmlands north of here. I suspect there is no saving Parth Lisc's crops, but many are concerned that the fires will spread if left unchecked. Ceveneth says that a small shift in the wind is all it would take.

'If you are heading to Parth Lisc, please douse the flames. I do not want all of this peaceful land to burn. If you happen to spy any supplies on the farm, salvage them as this village desperately needs additional supplies.''I am glad to hear that fires will not spread. It is a shame that the farm is lost. I know that we can not save all of Talath Anor. Let us hope that Crithost will stay strong though.'Lieutenant Ingi explained that the Snowreap goblins are the same who inhabit Goblin-town and the bulk of the Misty Mountains. He knows that they are an ally to Angmar and wants to see their numbers culled.There are Snowreap-guards and sappers at Grothum, north of Ost Ringdyr.

Lieutenant Ingi wishes to cull the Snowreap goblins from the Ettenmoors and weaken the forces which Angmar can bring to bear against the Free Peoples.Ingi is at Ost Ringdyr, south of Grothum.

With the goblins dispatched, the time has come to return to Ingi.'In an age long past, the Misty Mountains were home to many of my kin. Now they crawl with goblins in all places save Moria where Durin's folk still hold the darkness at bay.

'The goblins in the north, at Grothum their accursed village, are the same that dwell in the place called Goblin-town. These savage little beasts are vile and cruel fiends, desiring only to serve the Dark Lord and the will of all evil manner. We can do our part, however, and crush them. Drive them back into their mountain halls and pursue them until there is nowhere else for them to flee.

'Go north, friend. North to where the hills take on the dark colour of mountain slate. You will find their accursed village. Find the guards and sappers there and put an end to their fiendish ways.''See this done, friend. Goblins are among the cruelest creatures in these hills. We'll be better served with them driven far from these lands.''A glorious victory for the Free Peoples! Those little beasts deserve no better.

'Your work is far from done, but this is a victory well-earned. Take this with my thanks. Remember that Quartermaster Ash will furnish you a key in exchange for a fair number of these.'Baranor's two captains are busy guarding the town and keeping watch on the Haradrim who have snuck into Lossarnach.Dagor and Indir can be found at the keep in Arnach.

Baranor has asked you to help his two captains, Dagor and Indir, protect the town from the Haradrim.Baranor can be found at the keep in Arnach.

You have helped Dagor and Indir work against the invading Haradrim, as Baranor asked. Now you should return to Baranor in Arnach.Talk to Baranor'Ah, yes! Where was I? Welcome to Arnach! I can't give you half the welcome old Lord Forlong would do. But he's gone off to Minas Tirith - off to war - and here I am! Baranor, Captain of the Guard, is who I am, and I must do my best to fill his shoes. Only he left me with such a great lot of green lads, all restless and rousting about. It's like herding mice!

'So I've made captains of Dagor and Indir. There's Dagor over there. Destined for greatness, if you ask me. At any rate, between guarding Arnach and keeping watch on these damned Haradrim, we three have had our hands full, and then some!

'Now you look a well-travelled and sensible ${RACE}. Could you lend my captains a hand? I assure you, Arnachrim lives depend on it!''The truth is, Lord Forlong left me with too many men. We sent as many as we could up to Imloth Melui, but the lads with war in their eyes couldn't bear to be cooped up behind those walls. I couldn't handle them all myself, so I made Dagor and Indir my captains.

'Like the sun and moon, those two are! Dagor's the more soldierly and fit for the role. Whereas Indir is clever and steady enough, but he worries and broods. We have enough darkness from the skies above! A captain should keep his head high.''Do not let my furrowed brows weigh on your heart, ${CLASS}. 

'Dagor plays at war and good-hearted Baranor keeps watch over the township as if these were times of peace. While I would curb the one and rouse the other, to do so would be out of my place. So I, who harbour no dreams of war and glory, take the burden willingly. I will plan and brood so that their dreams are not darkened... and so Arnach remains safe.''Ah, would that I were off, marching with Forlong to war! Still, I will not let ill chance rob me of any glory. There are enemies in Lossarnach, now, and I may prove my mettle as a captain and warrior here, as well.

'Baranor sees. He smiles on me, and when Forlong returns victorious, Baranor will tell him of my deeds.''${PLAYER}! There's no time now. The Haradrim - they're planning an attack. Ah, what shall we do? We mustn't stand around. We must act!'The Withered Tree has taken hold of the Cisterns and let a raiding party of Orcs into the city. It is up to you to regain control of the Cisterns.Rathon can be found at the northern end of the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Rathon and assist him with protecting the Cisterns.Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The Back DoorComplete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The InvadersComplete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: KamabhoshComplete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: TreacheryComplete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The Withered FoeRathon can be found at the northern end of the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Rathon.Speak with Rathon'The Withered Tree somehow found a way into the Cisterns and set up encampments there. You would think it a small nuisance but they've been talking with the enemy! There's a raiding party of Orcs in the Cisterns right now and the Withered Tree let them into the city! To think the Withered Tree are Gondorians! We must band together, not fight one another. Please stop them, ${PLAYER}.''Quickly, into the Cisterns!''I thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. With time, I hope to drive our enemies back whence they came and restore the Cisterns to their former state.'Rathon has been tasked with maintaining many of the cisterns in Minas Tirith by himself and could use some assistance in tracking down those who sabotaged the main cistern valve.Saboteurs are hiding in the cisterns.

You should defeat the saboteurs.Find and defeat saboteurs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Rathon.Speak with Rathon'Could those who sabotaged the valve actually be from outside the city? Most think there is no way into and out of the city right now with the front gate being heavily guarded, but I know this is false. There are a few cisterns that can take one out of the city. Guards are posted on the lower cisterns at the base of the city but none are posted at the entrances from the mountain. Could Orcs have scaled Mount Mindolluin and snuck in the northern cistern entrance? I shudder at the thought!

'Either way, if the saboteurs are still hiding nearby in the cisterns, they must be apprehended or dealt with in some manner. I leave that to you, my good ${CLASS}.''Orcs were trying to sabotage the lesser drainage gates in the cisterns? I assume you dealt with them reasonably then?

'Not only do I not have enough men to maintain the cisterns but now a small band of invaders bide their time under the city. This is a most unfortunate day!'Corsair ships are docked in the harbour.Sinking a corsair ship will cripple their occupation.Set fuses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rathon, the Warden of the Wells, has his hands full trying to keep the fires in Minas Tirith from spreading out of control.A burning stone landed in the Sixth Circle. Rathon wanted you to pick up a water bucket and use that to extinguish the stone.

