<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Pick up a water bucket in the besieged cityDuinhir and his sons are in the Second Circle of the besieged city, and have sought to get your attention.

<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Talk to Duinhir in the Second Circle of the besieged city'The armies of Mordor have catapulted flaming stones onto the city, and the fires threaten to spread! My men have set water buckets on each level, but there are simply not enough to go around.

'If you can help put out the blazes before they spread, you would be doing the city a great service. Quickly, ${PLAYER}! Start here in the Sixth Circle and use one of the water buckets to put out the flaming stones, and then work your way down the city, level by level. There will be water buckets near the ramps down from each Circle, but they may not be near enough to the fires... unless you hurry!

'Go with my blessing, friend! We cannot fight both the fires and our foes at the same time. We must control the blazes before the enemy gets into the city!''Put out the blazes before they spread, ${PLAYER}! Start here in the Sixth Circle and use a water bucket to put out the flaming stones, and then work your way down the city, level by level. There will be water buckets near the ramp down from each Circle, but they may not be near enough to the fires... unless you hurry!

'Go with my blessing, friend! We cannot fight both the fires and our foes at the same time. We must control the blazes before the enemy gets into the city!''Put out the blazes before they spread, ${PLAYER}! Start here in the Sixth Circle and use one of the water buckets to put out the flaming stones, and then work your way down the city, level by level. There will be water buckets in each Circle, but they may not be near enough to the fires... unless you hurry!

'Go with my blessing, friend! We cannot fight both the fires and our foes at the same time. We must control the blazes before the enemy gets into the city!''Put out the blazes before they spread, ${PLAYER}! Start here in the Sixth Circle and use one of the water buckets to put out the flaming stones, and then work your way down the city, level by level. There will be water buckets in each Circle, but they may not be near enough to the fires... unless you hurry!

'Go with my blessing, friend! We cannot fight both the fires and our foes at the same time. We must control the blazes before the enemy gets into the city!''You found Forlong and Golasgil in the Fourth Circle? Return to them and see how they fare before continuing with your task.''Ha! ${PLAYER}, how do you fare? This gets the blood flowing, does it not? It puts me in mind of any number of great adventures, and I look forward to adding to my list of great deeds!

'Golasgil here does not share my enthusiasm, so I have resolved to have enough for the both of us! Let the enemy gain the wall and we'll see how many of them it will take to wipe the smile off my face and the laughter from my lips... more than they've brought, I wager!''An air of doom hangs over the city, but my companion here does not seem to care! Does he not realize that this night could spell the end for Minas Tirith, and for Gondor? We are surrounded! The gate has never fallen, but there has never been an army on the Pelennor like the one that fills it now!

'I cannot explain Forlong's disposition. I cannot even understand it!''Ha ha ha! I am ready for anything the hosts of Mordor wish to throw at us!''I cannot bear to look. What awaits us in the hours to come?''Fear not, Golasgil! I will protect you from the darts of the enemy! Stand behind me and they will not even see you!''Oh, what now? What new horrors await us?''I will fight until the end! Fear not, Golasgil!''What new horrors await us?''It is good to see you are making yourself useful, friend. My sons wanted to charge out of the city and take on the enemy by themselves. Their hearts burn for battle, but I have set them to more reasonable tasks.

'When that great ball came down, trailing fire behind it, it took a large bite from the wall. For now my sons work to shore up the defences, and repair what they can. They grumble about it, but I know there will be fighting before the night is over. They will have their chance.

'I hope you will be ready as well, when that time comes. It will not be long now, ${CLASS}!'First Marshals stand only behind the Captain-General in rank among the enemy army. Chieftain Durulkum wants their marks of rank to further the favour this war-host gains with Angmar, Mordirith, and Lugbúrz.First Marshals can only be found in towers and keeps claimed by the enemy.

Chieftain Durulkum at Dâr-gazag informed you that the marks borne by the First Marshals of the enemy army gain great favour with Mordirith in Angmar.'Your weak frame and tender flesh will bruise too easily if you attempt this, sluggard! But if you desire great favour and glory in the name of the Great Eye, then perhaps you will throw your life away on this endeavour.

'Within the towers and keeps of these lands, our enemy takes root from time to time. When they do, First Marshals of their army stalk the halls as attendants and support for their masters.

'Storm their holdings and collect their marks. Bring me one, and I will be well-favoured indeed. Accept this task and fail, and I will feed your gizzard to the trolls!''Scraps! You bring me scraps! What am I to do with these, you pathetic ${RACE}? I should gut you where you stand and use your entrails to season the gruel.

'Such failures cannot be tolerated... but they must, only because you are the troops we have for our menial tasks. Begone from my sight.

Chieftain Durulkum mutters. 'Yes, this suits my purpose well.'After weakening the forces in Tarlang's Crown, the time has come to confront Azruthor and put an end to the Scourge's plans for the Anfalas.You should continue to weaken the forces of Tarlang's Crown.

Harnion has asked you to weaken the forces of Tarlang's Crown before confronting Azruthor. 

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing the deed Quests of Tarlang's Crown will advance this quest.</rgb>Aid Harnion in weakening the forces in Tarlang's CrownHarnion can be found along the road into Tarlang's Crown from Belfalas.

Harnion has asked you to weaken the forces of Tarlang's Crown before confronting Azruthor. You should now speak to Harnion.Talk to HarnionElaglar can be found in the Court of the Fount in Dol Amroth.

You should speak to Elaglar about your first victory against the Heirs of Castamir.Talk to Elaglar in Dol Amroth'Until Azruthor himself lies broken in the crown, we shall not see a victory against the Heirs of Castamir.

'If what you told me of Blackroot Vale is true, Azruthor is a not a man to be trifled with - fell allies or not. I would ask that you continue to weaken his forces until he stands alone... only then can we hope to defeat him.

'Continue your assault on Tarlang's Crown, my friend, for the time shall soon come!''Are you and your fellows ready to confront Azruthor, ${PLAYER}?''It is good to see you among our folk again, ${PLAYER}. From the looks of you, you have seen a great battle indeed. Although Azruthor's warning of the Scourge, Balakhôr, troubles me greatly, you have returned peace to Western Gondor.

'The people of Dol Amroth wish to thank you for defending our lands so honourably, so we have crafted the finest of wares for you.

'May our city ever be a home to you and your fellows!'Haldil, a local at the Cape Docks, enjoys each day by fishing.Fish can be caught down at the Cape Docks.

You should catch some fish at your leisure.Catch silvery pout (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Haldil is down by the Cape Docks.

You should speak to Haldil when you have a moment.Talk to Haldil'Aye, do you fish? I come to these docks every day. I fish all along the coast. You want to know the secret to a relaxing life? Well, I will tell you. You sit on the dock over there and you catch some silvery pout. Aye, reeling in a pout is not too hard, but just enough challenge to matter. It is a fine feeling.''Well, will you look at that? Caught a bunch of pout, did you? Quite the fisher you turned out to be. Aye, you caught more than I have ever caught in a day, I will tell you that!'Flying the flags of the Free Peoples at Tol Ascarnen gives hope to those entrenched in the battle. Each time the fortress is taken, the flags are destroyed by the Enemy and they must be remade.Thistledown-aurochs can be found throughout the Ettenmoors.

Quartermaster Cynwiss asked you to assist her in collecting hides to craft the flags of the Free Peoples in the Ettenmoors.'Greetings, ${CLASS}. No doubt you are here to assist us in seeing that the flags over our positions here in the Ettenmoors continue to fly. There are a few ways that you can contribute to that cause.

'First, continue your battle against the forces of the Enemy... this will ensure that we continue to drive the front forward. Second, assist me in acquiring the materials to make new flags. As each of our strongholds is overrun -- and it does happen, despite our best efforts -- we lose munitions and our flags. The material cost and shipment of new ones would take too long, so artisans amongst us are handling the craftwork, but we still need to gather the materials.

'We are only using the hide of the Thistledown-aurochs as they are the creatures least corrupted in these lands. If you are willing, help us collect their hides and return them to me.''You return with all that I asked for, ${PLAYER}. This may not seem as important as defeating the Enemy on a field of battle, yet knowing that your standard still waves above a fortress can instill fear into the hearts of the foe and inspire those under your command.

'Take this... Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig will reward you well.'As the darkness in the sky intensifies, keeping the fires lit and the Enemy at bay has become an even greater challenge.Haradrim and chopped wood can be found among the trees to the south of Glaniath in Upper Lebennin.

Arvellon has asked you to recover wood and defeat any Haradrim scouts that have passed into Upper Lebennin.Defeat Haradrim scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect piles of chopped wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arvellon can be found in Glaniath to the north-east of Pelargir.

You have defeated many scouts and recovered a substantial amount of wood. You should now return to Arvellon.'If we are to remain here, as I fear many will, we must better prepare ourselves.

'When the Corsairs came to Pelargir, we fled the plains back into our homes, and in doing so, we left a great deal of wood behind.

'I have seen shadows moving among the trees to the south, and I fear it can only be the Haradrim come from across the river. We can lift wood as well as any might, but we cannot fend off swordsmen of their skill.

'If you would seek them out and recover our wood, we could keep the fires lit and rest a mite easier.''If my people will not be moved, I am thankful that you have kept us from harm.

'This wood will keep our fires lit for some time... I just hope to see the sun again one day.'Concerned that the war will soon consume all of Lebennin, Barchir bids you seek out the Steward of Ost Anglebed and aid in repelling the invaders near Pelargir.The Steward can likely be found in his hall in Ost Anglebed.

Barchir has asked you to travel east to Ost Anglebed and aid the men there in holding against the Enemy's forces.Talk to the Steward in Ost Anglebed'You have brought much hope to my people, ${PLAYER}. Although we wish to distance ourselves from the troubles in Lebennin, we cannot deny that soon the war shall come to us.

'In the hills to the east lies the settlement of Ost Anglebed, and it is there you must go. The Lord has gone, but the Steward and his men hold against all of the forces outside Pelargir. They would be aided greatly by one such as you, and should they fail to hold the beacon, the rest of Lebennin would soon fall.

'Go swiftly to Ost Anglebed in the east and follow the hills, for the roads are unsafe as of late... even for a ${CLASS}.''Why have you come here, traveller?

'War is at our doorstep and soon the threshold shall be crossed. I will not beg your aid, ${CLASS}, but if you wish to stand against the darkness alongside my men, I will see you rewarded.'Soldier Fandmau fears reprisal for the assault of Tírith Rhaw and wants you to attack the Free Peoples quickly before they retaliate.Defenders of the Free Peoples can be found throughout the Ettenmoors.

Soldier Fandmau directed you to slaughter the defenders loyal to the Free Peoples.Slaughter members of the Coldfells Army (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Soldier Fandmau is at Tírith Rhaw.

You found and slaughtered a good number of the enemy.Return to Soldier Fandmau at Tírith Rhaw'Taking this tower puts us in harm's way, and the Free Peoples will not sit idly by while we are so close to their keep. We must slaughter them now and slaughter them quickly, lest they enter the tower and do us all in.

'Go quickly! Kill them!''I don't smell the blood of innocents on you. Get out there and kill the enemy! Only then will I respect you enough to not see you as a worthless wretch!''Dead? Yes, dead. You did well. Perhaps we will survive a bit longer.

'Leave now. Please, keep watching the area.'Corsair snipers have gathered on the high ground, taking out the attackers in the docks.The snipers must be defeated so the assault on the docks can be victorious.Defeat the snipers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A tender patch of flowers proves there is hope even in the depths of this marsh.Standing in the small patch of sweet-smelling flowers, you feel refreshed and, for a moment, at peace. Could there be other such blossoms here in the Marsh?

Search for other patches of the flowers in the Dead Marshes.You have discovered all the flower blossoms in the Dead Marshes.CompletedStanding in the small patch of sweet-smelling flowers, you feel refreshed and, for a moment, at peace. Could there be other such blossoms here in the Marsh?

Search for other patches of the flowers in the Dead Marshes.You have discovered all the flower blossoms in the Dead Marshes.Angmar's command of the Ettenmoors is unquestioned, but as the battle rages and the strongholds which the enemy and your army clash over change hands, the flags that show your dominance are taken and destroyed. You must assist the war-host by supplying your quartermasters with the necessary materials.Thistledown aurochs can be found throughout the Ettenmoors.

Quartermaster Apsduf sent you into the wild to collect the hides of the mighty Thistledown aurochs. Their hides will be made into flags for Angmar's army.'${RACE}, listen here. As the battle rages about us, we must remember that we serve the glory of the Great Eye and his servant Mordirith in the Army of Angmar. There is no better way to show our prowess in battle than to fly our standards when we take these fortresses!

'Our enemy tears down our flags and destroys them. Materials are hard to find in this desolate land, so we must hunt for the materials we need. Scattered throughout the land here, there are massive aurochs. Their hides are sizeable and can easily be used to make the flags we need.

'Hunt them in packs and skin them for their hides.''These hides will suffice. With them we shall rebuild the flags torn and burned by the enemy. These fields will run red with their blood, and soon the air will burn, and these flags shall fly throughout all lands!

'For the glory of Angmar, Mordirith, and Lugbúrz!'Edenos has tasked you with searching for Orkish blades on the battlefield that can be melted down and reforged into Gondorian blades.Orkish blades can be found on the Eastern side of Osgiliath.

You should collect Orkish blades.Collect Orkish blades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Edenos is at the Palace of Eldacar.

You should bring the Orkish swords to Edenos.Bring the Orkish swords to Edenos'We've slain many enemy upon the battlefield of Osgiliath. I'm sending you on a mission to retrieve some of the Orkish weapons strewn about the battlefield.

'We could use these by melting them down to reforge new weapons for my soldiers. What I wouldn't give to stab an Orc with his own blade. Also, it would mean that less weapons are in the hands of the enemy.''Good work. I'll bring these blades to my smith. He'll make some new weapons for the next wave soldiers coming to help us battle.'As everyone waits for Faltharan's decision, Siriel has asked for your help with passing around food to refugees.The cooking pot can be found next to Siriel.

You should use the cooking pot to fill the bowls with food.Use the cooking pot to fill the bowlsHungry refugees can be found to the east of Siriel, near the shipyard.

You should feed the nearby hungry refugees.Siriel is located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Siriel.Talk to Siriel'Oh, ${PLAYER}, look at all these poor people! Many are not even from here. They were abducted as the Corsairs sacked the countryside and taken to slave aboard the galleys.

'I've been told that we do not have enough food for all of them, so I prepared some warm meals for our stranded friends. Could you help me pass them around to any hungry refugees that you might find?''Goodness, I was not expecting you to feed so many people!

'That's so wonderful to hear. I feel better knowing that someone besides myself is looking out for these people. The tough times aren't over, but I feel like we've crested "over the hill" with today.

'Thank you for making a difference, ${PLAYER}.'Footmen, wardens, and scouts patrolling the wild of the Ettenmoors adorn their uniforms with badges denoting their rank. You have been tasked with recovering these badges and delivering them to Chieftain Durulkum at Gramsfoot.Seek footmen, wardens, or scouts throughout the Ettenmoors and slay them.

Chieftain Durulkum directed you to seek out the weakest of the enemy soldiers and claim their badges as proof of your duty.'Listen well, ${RACE}. I'm not here to wipe your nose and look after you. I'm here to see that the war-host out of Angmar clears the way of the enemy. To do that, I need to prove that we're doing well against these curs.

'I need your help for that. These duties are beneath an Orc of the Krahjarn, and I'll not dirty my hands with such worthless creatures. You, on the other hand, seek the approval which I've already earned.

'So here's what we're going to do. You'll kill the footmen you find out there and bring me their badges.''These badges are barely worth my time, worm, but they'll have to do. Now, get out of here before I gut you!'Galathir, the Master Herbalist, seeks various plants from nearby lands to make potent healing salves. These will be important for healing soldiers after the coming battle.Tunglewort can be found in Osgiliath near the Anduin. Maiden's Helm can be found in the northern woods of Lossarnach. Wanderbeard can be found at the base of the mountains in Pelennor. Settlegang can be found in the woods of Talath Anor.

You should seek out these particular plants for Galathir.Collect Tunglewort (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Maiden's Helm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Wanderbeard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Settlegang (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Galathir can be found in the Houses of Healing on the southern end of the Sixth Circle.

You should speak with Galathir.Speak with GalathirThe mortar and pestle can be found near Galathir in the Houses of Healing.

You should grind the herbs with the mortar and pestle.Grind up the herbs with the mortar and pestleThe mortar and pestle can be found near Galathir in the Houses of Healing.

You should grind the herbs with the mortar and pestle.Grind up the herbs a little moreGalathir can be found in the Houses of Healing on the southern end of the Sixth Circle.

You should speak with Galathir.Speak with Galathir'As you are aware, battle is surely upon us. There will be casualties and there will be injuries. The casualties will be unavoidable. If we are to act fast and have the proper healing salves, we should be able to abate the injuries. I have been insisting that we stock up on herbs with healing properties but I do not know anyone who is willing to leave the safety of this city on the eve of battle. If you collect these plants, then I and many soldiers to come will be in your debt.'

Galathir shows you a book containing labeled drawing of several plants of the region with healing properties:

Tunglewort, a weed that grows in Osgiliath near the Anduin.
Maiden's Helm, a flower only found in the northern woods of Lossarnach.
Wanderbeard, a type of moss-flower growing at the base of the mountains in Pelennor.
Settlegang, a green flower-less plant found in Talath Anor.'I am forever grateful for your efforts, as will any warriors injured in battle. I must say, you have a keen eye for finding outstanding herbal specimens. If you would, bring the herbs to the mortar and pestle and grind them up for me.''Nicely done, ${PLAYER}.''You have done well. The other herbalists will take over from here and make potent salves. Thank you again for aiding the Houses of Healing.'Seeking vengeance against three captains of Harad for twisting the Way of the Corsairs, Jajax hopes to confront them in Hata Kebir.The three captains can be found throughout Hata Kebir.

Jajax has asked you to aid him in seeking vengeance against the captains in Hata Kebir.Defeat AkimunDefeat RalthatDefeat KuriJajax can be found at your side or called with your horn.

You have defeated the three captains of Harad and should now speak to Jajax.Talk to Jajax'When our fleet split between the bay and sailing to Pelargir, I found myself sharing a ship with Hebil and that pompous man, Azruthor.

'Hebil got what he deserved for slaying my men in Lamedon, and I heard rumour that Azruthor's flowery words weren't able to save him... pity that. Yet, before we set out, Hebil honed his harshness from three captains of Harad and I saw him throw the weak from the ship as we sailed.

'We may not have honour as you or the Swan-men see it, but to slay our own for the smallest of trespasses is not our Way. I believe these captains are here, and I will see them pay for what they have done to my people.''Whether you believe in my cause or not, I think you have done something heroic here today.

'I have my vengeance, and you can rest knowing the people of Gondor will not meet with the same brutality that befell my men.

'More still weighs on my mind, my friend, but let this victory be remembered by us both.'Horrified by the Lone Lady's rage, Glassiel sends you deep into Lebennin to commune with the Lady of the Erui's four Sisters.The rivers of Sirith can be found throughout Upper and Lower Lebennin. The Sirith flows out of Tumladen, the Celos joins Sirith to the north of Erynos, and the Serni flows to the east and south of Ost Anglebed.

Glassiel has asked you to seek an audience with the other Sisters of Lebennin in the hopes that they might calm the rage of the Lone Lady.Seek the Maiden of SirithSeek the Maiden of CelosSeek the Maiden of SerniRoamingstar, the Maiden of Gilrain can be found in her glade to the north-east of Linhir in Dor-en-Ernil.

You have found and spoken to three of the Five Sisters. You should now seek the Maiden of Gilrain.Seek the Maiden of Gilrain'What can be done, ${PLAYER}? Even if we succeed in pushing the Enemy from Lebennin, the Lone Lady's fervour will deliver ruin unto our lands and waters for years untold.

'It is clear that our words no longer bear any importance to her... her mind has been twisted by the return of great evils and she will not rest until all have been punished for the deeds of the past. I fear that only her Sisters might calm her now, but I have never looked upon them... and I know not where they might hide away in such dark times.

'Seek them at the rivers Sirith, Serni, Celos, and Gilrain. I cannot promise you shall ever find them, but if you do, they must be told of the Lone Lady's madness.

'Even if you do not succeed, I shall know you did all you could for my people.''My waters have whispered of a ${RACE} such as you. You have come bearing ill tidings, have you not?'

You tell Truetongue of her Sister's rage.

'She has not spoken to me and my Sisters in many long years, but she knows well that we do not involve ourselves in the troubles of mortal Men unless it is for the good of all.

'I must free her from her blindness before it consumes her.''The waters have told me much of you, ${PLAYER}. You need not speak, for I already know all you have to say.

'It is clear that my Sister has grown mad... for who among us would garb her own waters in the weak armours of Man? Are not our currents unbreakable?

'Perhaps she should try dancing instead...'

Silverfroth lets out a laugh.

'I do not know if she shall listen to my words, but I shall try when the time comes.''And who are you to step so boldly into my waters?

'I could drown you with a thought, and yet I do not, for I know well of your purpose here.

'My Sister's rage overflows from the Erui and I feel her anger even now. She pulls more armour of the dead from her waters with each passing moment, and soon not even the banks of her river shall contain her.

'I know the truth of what must be done, even if the others do not see it.''It is good to look upon you, ${PLAYER}.

'My Sisters have told me of what troubles you and how the evils of Men have once again tainted the Erui. My Sister has grown wild, and she must be calmed before this corruption can overtake her completely.

'I fear that Grey-eye may speak true, for time grows short indeed. We must soothe her wounds of old before it is too late!'Ceveneth, one of Crithost's head farmers, has been put in charge of fortifying the town and could use some assistance in her task.Broken barricades and spots for bear traps can be found around Crithost.

You should repair barricades and set bear traps.Repair barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Place bear trap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ceveneth can be found in the hall of Crithost.

You should speak with Ceveneth.Speak with Ceveneth'Greetings, my name is Ceveneth. I am the head farmer of Crithost. It has been a difficult past few days here with the refugees coming from all over Talath Anor.

'I've been put in charge of strengthening the defences of the village but honestly I do not know much about building things. I'm as good as they come for tilling the land though!

'I could use a little help if you have a moment. Some of the barricades we made are in dire need of repair. Also, I was given these bear traps by one of the Cair Andros guards to place around the village. Perhaps those will be useful in protecting us as well?''This should keep us safe for a time. You sure are a handy ${RACE}. Hopefully those who captured Cair Andros don't all come this way at once!'The corsairs have filled the ponds of the Great Hall with poison.If the poison is removed quickly enough the waters may be saved.Remove poison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Corsair slavers are entrapping those holding out within the library.The slavers must be defeated.Defeat slavers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Faltharan has grown curious of what the refugees of Minas Tirith have learned about the war in the East.Refugees of Minas Tirith can be found throughout Tumladen.

Faltharan has asked you to speak to many of the refugees in Tumladen so he might learn more of the growing conflict in the east.Faltharan can be found in Tumladen in northern Upper Lebennin.

You have spoken to many of the refugees camped in Tumladen and should now return to Faltharan.Talk to Faltharan in Tumladen'When my father and I arrived here, the gate-warden told us of the many folk of Minas Tirith seeking shelter within these walls.

'Many, indeed. From what I can tell, they seem to delight in rumour-mongering, and I do not blame them, for thinking of unbelievable tales and happenings may be the only respite from this encroaching darkness.

'For my part, I have heard little of Minas Tirith in recent days, and I suspect that the folk here might know more. Speak to them while I tend to my father, and tell me of what you learn.''I did not believe I would ever think such things, but I am glad to be so far from my home.

'I have heard tales of a great army mustering in the ruins of Osgiliath, and though the Steward has sent his son, I fear for us all in the coming days.''I have heard tales of many strange things at the battle of Pelargir, but I do not know what truth there is to any of them.

'You travelled with Lord Sirgon and his son... what have you seen?'

The man's face sinks as you remain silent.

'Forgive me, traveller, I only wished to keep my hopes up...''A ${CLASS} or not, you would be wise to seek shelter here, traveller. The Steward showed great wisdom in sending us to safety.

'Minas Tirith's defences are great, but even greater are the forces of the Enemy who would see it torn down stone by stone!''Do you know what happened in Pelargir? The people of Glaniath that have come to Tumladen have told of hearing a great chorus of screams, even from so far away.

'What happened to the Corsairs and why do their ships still sail on the Anduin? Lord Angbor has come, and he does not speak to us as openly as he once did.'

You tell the woman only that you cannot speak on the matter.

'Why do you keep secrets from us? Does the war go so poorly?''Do you think we'll be safe here? My mother says we will be, but she hasn't spoken much since we arrived here.

'Father stayed in Minas Tirith to guard the gates, but I wish he had come along with us.

'If you travel that way, you'll look after him, won't you?''I share their concerns, my friend. These are uncertain times, and the fates of many may be decided by the actions of a few.

'It saddens me that their curiosity about the battle at Pelargir must go unanswered for the moment, but the Rangers have bidden me to keep my silence.

'Let us hope that Lord Angbor and Aragorn can reach Minas Tirith in time to repel the Enemy.'Artamir has told you the reason for his errand, and the sooner it is accomplished, the sooner he will leave the Dead Marshes. For Frodo's sake, if the hobbit did come this way, you should do what you can to hasten Artamir's departure.The Orc camp is to the west of Artamir's encampment, in the Dead Marshes.

Artamir has asked you to search storage caches in the Orc camp, to see if they have recovered the Banner of King Ondoher from the mud and the marsh-waters.You have found no sign that the Orcs have recovered the Banner of King Ondoher, and should return to Artamir at his camp.Talk to Artamir at his camp in the Dead Marshes'I trust you, ${PLAYER}. I will tell you the nature of my errand in this miserable land, and perhaps you can better help me accomplish it and then return to my home in triumph. I would give anything for this victory, my friend! The gratitude of the Steward would do much for my family's position.

'Long ago, the peace of Gondor was threatened by Wainriders from the East, cruel men who rode down their enemies in great wheeled chariots. It is said that Ondoher, one of the last of the true line of Kings, faced the Wainriders in battle on the great plain but was defeated. No sign was ever found of the King or his force, and Steward Denethor believes that the Wainriders might have driven him into the Dead Marshes before he perished.

'You think it unlikely? I would say so too, but for this. Denethor had of late a dream, in which he beheld the banner of the King flying proudly against the night sky. Could it be the banner of Ondoher, last of the line of Kings descended from Meneldil, Anárion's son? The strange waters of the swamp must have preserved it, after all this time, and I must find it and return with it to Minas Tirith!

'If these Orcs have found the King's Banner, they might be keeping it in a storage cache in their camp. Return to their camp and search these caches to ensure they have not!'The corsairs are cutting down the trees around the Great Hall to create ships.The gardens are one of Dol Amroth's most prized locations.Defeat Wood-cutters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Habdir, a Master Clothier, is in need of assistance with gathering donated clothing from nobles on the Fourth Circle.Noble chests can be found on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should collect donated clothing from noble chests on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.Collect clothing from noble chests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Habdir can be found within the Clothiers' Fellow-hall on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Habdir.Speak with Habdir'Many of the good noble families living on the Fourth Circle left extra clothing for those in the city when they departed for Imloth Melui. There is much bedding and clothing that will need tending to over the days ahead and the extra cloth will be vitally useful. I've collected much of the clothing donated by those who left the city but there is still more to be collected. Do you have a moment to assist me in collecting the last of the clothing on the Fourth Circle?''This will do nicely. I believe I have enough now, so long as the war does not last too long. We will all face hardship in the days to come but perhaps a soft place to lay one's head will make all the difference!'Efforts to liberate Lugazag succeeded, but now the tower is largely undefended. Word must reach the War-tyrant at Gramsfoot that we need troops to defend the walls.Cross the Ettenmoors and deliver the message to War-tyrant Akúlhun that Lugazag is in need of reinforcement.

Soldier Dumûl ordered you to seek reinforcements for Lugazag. The tower fell to the forces of Angmar, but must be reinforced or it will be summarily lost to the Free People.Inform War-tyrant Akúlhun that more forces are needed at Lugazag'Glory for Angmar! We control Lugazag, but our forces are week and will remain that way until the War-tyrant is informed of our victory.

'Go now and tell the tyrant of the victory here! Tell him that we require troops and do so quickly without incident.''More forces for the front, eh? You maggots might yet make me proud! For Angmar! For Lugbûrz!'Grimwood is fallen to the hands of Angmar, and the forces have returned to the fortified section of the area. The forces here are meagre and if left unsupported the Free People will surely recover the location. You must get word to Gramsfoot.Cross the Ettenmoors and deliver the message to War-tyrant Akúlhun that the Grimwood Lumber Camp is in need of reinforcement.

Soldier Kraibag ordered you to seek reinforcements for the Grimwood. Though the lumber camp is controlled by Angmar, it must be reinforced or it will be summarily lost to the Free People.Inform War-tyrant Akúlhun that more forces are needed at the Grimwood Lumber Camp'Listen well, cur. This place is terribly undefended. We're a crew of too few against a host of many.

'Get word to the north, to the War-tyrant and tell him that we have liberated this fortress for Angmar. Tell him that we need support and that we need it now.

'Go swiftly and make sure that the message is delivered without incident.''Get that message to the War-tyrant, worm!''More forces for the front, eh? You maggots might yet make me proud! For Angmar! For Lugbûrz!'The Isendeep Mine is fallen to the hands of Angmar, and the forces have returned to the fortified section of the area. The forces here are meagre and if left unsupported the Free Peoples will surely recover the location. You must get word to Gramsfoot.Cross the Ettenmoors and deliver the message to War-tyrant Akúlhun that the Isendeep Mine is in need of reinforcement.

Soldier Baush ordered you to seek reinforcements for the Isendeep. Though the mine is controlled by Angmar, it must be reinforced or it will be summarily lost to the Free Peoples.Inform War-tyrant Akúlhun that more forces are needed at the Isendeep Mine'I've little time for words if I am to organize a defence with such a withered force. 

'Return to Gramsfoot and deliver the War-tyrant the message that we have recovered the mine. He will send troops if he hopes to see us defend this massive space.

'Go now and do not fail me!''More forces for the front, eh? You maggots might yet make me proud! For Angmar! For Lugbûrz!'Efforts to drive the Free Peoples from Tírith Rhaw succeeded, but now the tower is largely undefended. Word must reach the War-tyrant at Gramsfoot that we need troops to defend the walls.Cross the Ettenmoors and deliver the message to War-tyrant Akúlhun, at Gramsfoot, that Tírith Rhaw is in need of reinforcements.

Soldier Gaath ordered you to seek reinforcements for Tírith Rhaw. The tower fell to the forces of Angmar, but must be reinforced or it will be summarily lost to the Free People.Inform War-tyrant Akúlhun that Tírith Rhaw requires forces'Our forces proved worthy, wretch, but this tower is too close to the Free Peoples for us to rest easy.

'I need you to deliver a message to the War-tyrant at Gramsfoot. Tell him that we need reinforcements, and be swift!''More forces for the front, eh? You maggots might yet make me proud! For Angmar! For Lugbûrz!'The children have decided to hold a 'Gathering' and everyone needs to bring some things to the table.The Old Guest-house is in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.

Ask Húndil in the Old Guest-house for some small ale.Ask Húndil for small aleThe Wheel and Cask is at the northern end of the First Circle.

The Old Guest-house has run out of small ale, but Húndil thinks the Wheel and Cask might have some.Ask at the Wheel and Cask for small aleThe Wheel and Cask is at the northern end of the First Circle.

Meldis has invited you to collect all the small ale you want yourself, from her stores.Gather small ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bergil stands before the Old Guest-house, south of the City Gates.

You should return to Bergil with the small ale you have gathered.The Lower Stores are just south of the City Gates in the First Circle.

Bergil has asked you to procure some victual packages from the butteries of the Lower Stores, which contain some dried meat.Go to the Lower StoresThe Lower Stores are just south of the City Gates in the First Circle.

Gather parcels of soldiers' victuals from the buttery in the Lower Stores.Gather victuals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bergil stands before the Old Guest-house, south of the City Gates.

You should return to Bergil with the soldiers' victuals.The Wrights' Market is in the southern reach of the First Circle.

Check in the Wrights' Market to see what's become of Landath, who was supposed to be procuring candles there.Find LandathChandler's Lane is on the southern reach of the First Circle.

Find out why the chandler is berating Landath out in the street.Talk to the chandlerLandath stands accused in Chandler's Lane, which is on the southern reach of the First Circle.

Talk to Landath to hear his side of the story.Talk to LandathChandler's Lane is on the southern reach of the First Circle.

Vouch for Landath to the chandler.Talk to the chandlerThe Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.

Go back to Bergil at the Old Guest-house to see how the Gathering preparations are faring.Return to Bergil'${PLAYER}, there you are! The sweets have come from Himnir and we've decided to hold a Finder's Gathering. Of course you will join us, won't you? Oh, but you must. You're to be the guest of honour!

'We can't have a gathering with just sweets, of course, and besides, everyone's got to bring a thing or two. That's what makes it a Gathering!

'Now what should YOU bring, I wonder? Hm... Well, we'll need some small ale. And you need only ask Húndil here in the Old Guest-house for some. Why don't you start there?''The Old Guest-house has plenty of small ale. Just ask Húndil, inside. He might give it to you, or maybe you'll have to pay him.''Small ale, is it? Don't you want something stronger? Eh heh heh heh! But of course I know this is for the boys and girls, isn't it? Well, I'm afraid you'll be the bearer of ill tidings, for I haven't any. Gave those urchins the last of it three days back.

'Say, you might ask at the Wheel and Cask though. Yes, they might have some there.''Ask Meldis at the Wheel and Cask. With any luck, she'll have some small ale for you.''Húndil hadn't any? These are dark times, ${PLAYER}. Let us hope the Wheel and Cask does!''Small ale? I have some and you're welcome to it. We may die tomorrow and those urchins may drink fine wine, for all that I care. You can go back there in my stores and take it yourself.''The small ale is back in my stores. Help yourself to it.''Small ale! Good. Now let's see, we've got the sweets, Mídion's brought bread, Landath's gone for candles and Gelwen and Glatham have gone for some jars of jam... ah, but what else could you bring, ${PLAYER}?

'I know! In the butteries of the Lower Stores, there are parcels of soldiers' victuals. They've got tack and some herbs, but most of all, dried meats. It should be awfully nice to have some meat, and I think the dried kind is the best that we shall get. Perhaps for you, they would be willing to part with some.''Soldiers' victuals from the butteries in the Lower Stores. That's the second thing you can bring, ${PLAYER}.''Why, aren't you the ${RACE} who gave Oryat a proper thrashing? Oh, word's gone round among the soldiers, right enough. And all agree - all but Oryat's cronies, leastwise - that it was a fine thing to do.

'Now you go on and take anything you like from the buttery. I'll look the other way, eh?''I'll just be studying the wall over here. I won't see anything you walk off with.''And the victuals! You are tried and true, ${PLAYER}, that's what you are. I wish I could say as much for Landath. He went off for candles quite some time ago and still has not come back. ${PLAYER}, will you go look for him in the Wrights' Market, and see if he hasn't got himself in some scrape or another?''Landath went to the Wrights' Market for some candles. I would start searching for him there.''Oh, why do these things always happen to me? Please, talk to her, ${PLAYER}!''Look at this ragged urchin, will you, and tell me how he could have come by coin in this amount. By picking pockets, that's how!''He thinks to buy my candles with purloined coin. Hmph!''Truly, ${PLAYER}, I would never steal a single coin, let alone this many! Didn't I set things right with Master Habdir in the end? By the kings of old, I swear, I found these coins in the Finding Place. But just you try and explain the Finding Place to HER!

'Please, speak to her. I only want to buy some candles!''Please, tell her I haven't stolen a thing and only wish to buy some candles!''You vouch for this child? Well, he is dressed rather wretchedly and has a hangdog look, you must admit. But some other chandler will take his coin, if I don't. And if it is ill-got, let it be your conscience that wakes you at night!''You have saved my hide again, ${PLAYER}! You go ahead and tell Bergil I'm coming. I'll gather up these candles and be on my way in a moment.''The boy will have his candles, don't you worry. But I'll be rid of these coins as soon as business allows, in case they bear ill fortune!''You and Landath are back. Gelwen and Glatham aren't, but I'm sure they will be, any moment now. They're coming all the way from the Upper Stores, after all.

'Yes, I think it's best if we began without them. Everyone else is here and the hour grows late.'Pip Diggins meant to deliver a large amount of Hoarhallow ale to the Big Folk at Ost Ringdyr. As he was making his way towards the camp, he was forced to run from a pack of savage goblins and left the ale behind. He would truly appreciate any adventurer willing to collect the prize for him from the goblin-village at Grothum.Grothum lies north of Ost Ringdyr. Pip Diggins is located within the safety of Ost Ringdyr near the cooking oven.

Pip Diggins would like you to recover some of the ale the goblins stole in exchange for a small reward.'I've something rather difficult to ask you. On my way to Ost Ringdyr, I was to bring two things with me. The first was much too large and the charge was given to your people to handle, that being a large shipment of food and brittleleaf.

'The second was in my charge, and my pony -- loaned me by Captain-General Lainedhel himself -- was doing well until we were beset by the Snowreap goblins out of Grothum. Terrible creatures, those. Never had I seen one up close until that moment, and I admit that I was more than startled! I fought for a short time before they ran me off from the cart and pony. I know something terrible became of the pony, but the cargo I was hauling is most likely intact as many enjoy the spirits that we folk of Hoarhallow brew.

'If you could, make your way north from here to Grothum and recover the ale for me. I would be very appreciative.''The ale! You brought the ale back. I am indebted to you!

'This was meant to be a gift to the Captain-General for his assistance against the foe from Angmar. We were grateful for his offer and assistance.

'You have helped to preserve my honour and the honour of the people of Hoarhallow. Please take this with my thanks.'Gasham conveyed a tale of goblin-miners and goblins out and about from the village attacked by drakes stalking down from the mountain. He asked for your assistance in ridding the peaks of the beasts.Wintersebb drakes and drakelings can be found throughout Arador's End.

Gasham begged for your help against the Wintersebb drakes.Gasham is in the goblin-village of Grothum.

You hunted the drakes in the mountainous area of Arador's End and culled their number. You should return to Gasham with the news.Return to Gasham at Grothum'Swoop down, they do. You'll see when they come, flying on armoured wings, swooping into the tunnels, eating up a goblin in one gulp!

'Now you here to help. Snowreap help Angmar, Angmar help the Snowreap. Into the mine, out of the mine, flying, walking, stalking, they seek us in the hills and snow. They are the ebb of winter and have fangs as tall as me!

'Kill the drakes, yes? Kill them to help the Snowreap.''Seek them in the hills here and there to the west. They like the winter land and snow.''We thanks you! We thanks you great for the help you give.

'No more gobbled up goblins. We fight, but they strong. We give them meat, but they eat us. Too strong the drakes be, but not for Angmar!

'Glory to Angmar!'Defeat many Goblins in Eastern Gondor.Defeat many Goblins in Eastern Gondor.Defeat many Goblins in Eastern GondorDefeat many Goblin in Eastern Gondor.Defeat many Goblins in Eastern Gondor.Defeat many Goblins in Eastern GondorTrolls do not communicate well, as is proving true time and again. You think you were able to piece together a terrible truth from what Taskmaster Núrsufum tried to say. A bear named Goldhead may be aligned with the enemy, and if they act quickly enough, may assist the enemy against the tower.Old Goldhead may be within a bear-den near Tírith Rhaw.

Taskmaster Núrsufum seems to have communicated that a great bear nearby named Goldhead may be allied with the enemy.Taskmaster Núrsufum is at Tírith Rhaw.

You found and destroyed Old Goldhead. Now you should return to Taskmaster Núrsufum.Return to Taskmaster Núrsufum'Big bear... head of gold... come... fight.

'You go stop.

'Now!''Smash bear!

'Now!''Good.

'Me no kill you.'Golloval of the Golden Eagles will come to the aid of the Free Peoples provided that the Free Peoples are willing to prove their intention and valour.Golloval is hidden to the west amongst the hills near the central entrance to the Isendeep Mine. He hides in the hills protected by other golden eagles.

Golloval pledged to assist you in retaking the Isendeep mine if you return to him with proof of your valour within the Ettenmoors.'I have come to this field of battle to support the Free Peoples and my brethren among the Eagles. Long have we battled the spiders of Gorgoris's brood, and we are pleased to help the Free Peoples against the foes out of Angmar.

'I see that the Isendeep has fallen to the Enemy. I pledge to join you in an assault against the enemy within the mine if you bring me the tokens proving your valour in these lands.''You have proven your valour, ${RACE}. Now I shall show you the valour of the Eagles!

'I will make my way into the mine through the hole in the wall. Meet me within, and we shall begin our assault on the tyrant who claims control within.'Find West Gondor's treasure that has been lost over the years.Find West Gondor's treasure that has been lost over the years.Find West Gondor's lost treasureGorgoris, the ancient brood-mother of the Grimfang, will assist you in claiming the Grimwood Lumber-yard, if you help her defend her brood.Eagles can be found throughout the Ettenmoors.

Gorgoris wishes to know that the threat against her brood is diminished before she enters the fight against the enemy. She asked you to slay the eagles and bring her their feathers as proof of the deed.'Your presence in my wood disturbs me, but not so much as the bearers of light, ${RACE}.

'My brood grows weak and is culled further by the enemy, and I seek my revenge. My first thought must be for my children, and so I task you with this:

'Eagles from the north join with your enemy and their lords have long sought to end my reign. Bring me proof of their destruction by way of their feathers, and I shall lend you my strength against the enemy.''Yes. This will do. The talons of the enemy will no longer harm my children. Let us march forwards and give them a lesson they will not soon forget!'The Grimwood Lumber-yard once again falls to the control of the Free Peoples.Travel east and south from the Grimwood Lumber Camp to inform Captain-General Tordúr that the Grimwood Lumber Camp belongs to the Free People.

You have been tasked with informing the Captain-General that the battle at the Grimwood is won.Talk to Tordúr at Glân Vraig'${PLAYER}, I have need of your assistance. We have won the day here but our numbers are thin, and if we are not reinforced quickly, the forces of Angmar will strike back and take this place.

'Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig must be told that we are in need of reinforcements. Make your way to him and apprise him of the situation.

'Be swift!''There is no time for discussion. Quickly, make your way to Glân Vraig and tell the Captain-General that we need reinforcements.''Your arrival is a boon, ${PLAYER}. I will dispatch forces to the Grimwood Lumber-yard at once!'Chieftain Torbok prepares the defence of the Grimwood Lumber-yard against the Free Peoples.Fight Angmar's foes within the bounds of the Grimwood Lumber-camp.

You were instructed to stand this ground and fight for the glory of Angmar in defence of the Grimwood Lumber-camp.Defeat Free Peoples at the Grimwood Lumber-camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})If Torbok is defeated or the lumber camp has fallen to the Free Peoples, return to Gramsfoot and face the wrath of War-tyrant Akúlhun.

You should return to Chieftain Torbok at the Grimwood Lumber Camp to gloat of your victories against the Free Peoples.'Listen well, you pathetic excuse for a warrior. Battle will soon come to this lumber-camp, and we'd best prepare for the onslaught.

'You'll defend the camp, staying within the bounds of the lumber-yard itself, and stand against the enemy as they come. You'll do this because I say you will.

'If we lose the camp or I should fall, report to the War-tyrant at Gramsfoot. Face him and tell him that you fought against the foe... he will choose your fate. If I stand, I will see that you are rewarded for your efforts.''Prepare yourself, the Free Peoples will not let us stay here long without coming to liberate the camp. We are too close to their precious rat-folk.''Our victory is complete, and you have been a necessary member of the defence. You are to be commended for your assistance here, maggot.

'Do not let this meagre success boost your thoughts of rising through the ranks of Angmar, though. You are nothing more than a maggot meant to be slaughtered by our enemies, until you prove otherwise.

'For now, I recognize your contributions. You will need to perform as well in the future to earn my respect.''You did well against our enemy at the Grimwood camp....

'Yet you return to me for your reward, which means my kin is lost. I will check my ire and curb my disappointment, for I know that many of the Free Peoples suffered by your hand. This success is fleeting, maggot. See that you do better in the future.'Choice food, meat from Men and the rat-folk, goes to the Krahjarn. Quartermaster Apsduf realizes that you need to eat as well, and since the mash cooked at Dâr-gazag doesn't always reach Tol Ascarnen, he needs help getting dinner for your rumbling bellies.Nerbyg can be found along the banks of the Hoardale River surrounding Tol Ascarnen.

Collect the gizzards and meat from the nerbyg to give to Apsduf for your nightly gruel.'${RACE}, you want to eat, and though it pains me to waste even the lowliest gruel on a pathetic thing like yourself, I've orders to keep you well fed. You'll not taste the tribute collected for the tyrant, nor the foods we eat.

'Your meal comes from the bugs outside these walls. If you don't like it, you can take the chance that a wandering giant or drake doesn't gobble up the goblins or couriers from Dâr-gazag. Oh, we've got food from the rat-folk too... but that is for the Krahjarn, you lowly little beast.

'You'll eat what you get and nothing more. Be thankful I'll prepare it for you! Catch your meal and bring it back here!''Mash this together, boil it well, and your dinner will be ready.

'Now is not time for eating, worm.'Peregrin Took may be a Guard of the Citadel, but he is still a hobbit and enjoys good food and good company above all else.The Thirsty Seer is in the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith. The picnic lunch that Pippin ordered should be ready for you to pick up and carry to the Watch-point at the end of the pier on the top of the city.Pick up the picnic lunch from The Thirsty Seer in the south-west section of the Fifth CirclePippin is waiting for you at the Watch-point on the end of the pier at the top of Minas Tirith.Talk to Peregrin Took at the Watch-point at the end of the pierYou are sharing a delicious picnic with Pippin at the Watch-point atop the city.You are sharing a delicious picnic with Pippin at the Watch-point atop the city.Talk to Peregrin Took at the Watch-point at the end of the pierYou are sharing a delicious picnic with Pippin at the Watch-point atop the city. The hobbit became very evasive when recounting the reason for his journey to Minas Tirith with Gandalf.You are sharing a delicious picnic with Pippin at the Watch-point atop the city. The hobbit became very evasive when recounting the reason for his journey to Minas Tirith with Gandalf.Talk to Peregrin Took at the Watch-point at the end of the pierYou are sharing a delicious picnic with Pippin at the Watch-point atop the city. He has reluctantly begun to tell you what brought him to Minas Tirith with Gandalf, but he could use some coaxing.Talk to Peregrin Took once more, despite his reluctanceYour picnic at the Watch-point is done, and now it is time to clean it up.Clean up the picnic at the Watch-pointPippin has returned to his post in the Citadel, the Seventh Circle of the city.Talk to Peregrin Took at his post in the Citadel'Well hello, ${PLAYER}! Gandalf hinted that I might be seeing you shortly, but I wasn't sure I believed him! It is good to see a familiar face in this grand city of strangers! I have met a few friends already, but this city is not built to hobbit-scale, is it? I find it quite overwhelming!

'On the off chance that you really would be turning up, I arranged with one of the taverns for a picnic lunch, and I expect it is nearly ready! There should be enough good food and drink for the two of us, and we can share stories and catch up on our adventures! I say 'our' adventures, but really mine has not been very eventful since last we met. I hope it stays that way, and I am not ashamed to admit it! It doesn't seem likely, though, does it?

'The proprietor of The Thirsty Seer in the Fifth Circle of the city should have the picnic basket set out by now. If you go down there, pick it up, and carry it out to the edge of the pier, we can have a lovely lunch at the Watch-point. I will meet you out there, but be sure to bring the picnic basket!''The proprietor of The Thirsty Seer in the Fifth Circle of the city should have the picnic basket set out by now. If you go down there, pick it up, and carry it out to the edge of the pier, we can have a lovely lunch at the Watch-point. I will meet you out there, but be sure to bring the picnic basket!''Ah, look at this delicious spread, ${PLAYER}! I see why Gandalf spoke so highly of The Thirsty Seer. It's his favourite tavern in Minas Tirith, apparently, and I can see why!

'Well, do not be shy, my friend! Let us dig in, and we can talk after we have taken the edges from our appetites!''Well, do not be shy! Let us dig in, and we can talk after we have taken the edges from our appetites!''That is a good start, but by no means an end! I will nibble a bit while we speak, if that is all right with you.'

You ask Pippin how he came to the White City.

'Oh, Gandalf brought me here. I slept much of the way, but Shadowfax is the swiftest of his kind and he was at a gallop for most of the journey. Why did we leave our friends behind? Well... Gandalf thought... he just thought I should see Minas Tirith, is all. The others had their own plans, and... you know. He's a Wizard.'

Pippin awkwardly stops speaking and picks at the food in silence. You wonder at his sudden evasiveness, and decide to have a little more of the lunch.Pippin is focused on his food, and does not seem eager to talk.'I... wasn't entirely honest with you, ${PLAYER}, and I am sorry for it. Gandalf did not bring me to Minas Tirith without cause, or as a simple sight-seeing trip. I know you were not deceived, but... it is difficult to speak of, and I am still ashamed that I might have worked some harm. Not on purpose! Gandalf called me a fool once, or twice, and he was right to do so! But I would never endanger my friends on purpose.

'There was an artifact at Isengard. Wormtongue threw it down from the tower, intending to do some harm to either Saruman or Gandalf, and I saved it from rolling away into a pool. Gandalf claimed it soon afterward, but not soon enough... I found I could not stop thinking about the dark globe.

'I... I stole it away from the Wizard when he slept, and looked into it, ${PLAYER}. I saw... I saw...'

Pippin trails away into silence, shame and fear written upon his face.'I saw... a tall tower and a black sky, and wheeling shapes... like bats, but much larger, and more frightening. And then... I saw... I saw him, ${PLAYER}. He looked at me, and his voice came not to my ears but to my mind, if that makes any sense. He asked me questions, and when I did not answer, I felt searing pain. I told him I was a hobbit, and his laughter was cruel. He said I would see him soon, and then Gandalf broke the spell and took away the stone.

'The artifact was a seeing-stone, a palantír, and Saruman had used it to communicate with... with his dark master. Gandalf would not tell me very much about the stone, but he seemed to think we escaped a much worse fate through a lucky chance of good fortune. I... I think he was right. I could not turn my eyes from the stone, and if that horrible figure had continued his questions, I know I would have answered him. What else might he have showed me in the palantír? I cannot guess, and do not wish to!

'This is not the sort of conversation that suits a picnic, ${PLAYER}! Let us clean up our food, and we can speak again back at my post!''Let us clean up our food, and we can speak again back at my post!''I would like to apologize for spoiling our picnic with such frightening conversation, ${PLAYER}. The food was delicious, and the company was excellent, of course, but I should not have spoken so much about the seeing-stone and what I saw within it.'

You assure Pippin that it did not ruin the picnic, and that you are simply glad he is all right now.

'Well, I thank you for saying so, my friend! I will give such artifacts a wide berth from now on, I can assure you of that! There may have once been good reasons for using them, as Gandalf says, but now that there's so much trouble in... well, you know what land I mean... now that there's so much trouble away to the East I daresay no one should peek into one of those stones... ever!

'I will get back to my duties now, ${PLAYER}. It was nice to see you again!'The fountains at the base of the stairs leading to the Great Hall serve to honour the memory of ancient defenders.The fountains must be preserved.Fountain defended (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Concerned that the Corsairs will continue to assault Linhir, Erchar has asked you to patrol the crossing.Linhir's gates to Dor-en-Ernil can be found in the north-western part of the city and Linhir's gates to Lebennin can be found to the south-west.

Erchar has asked you to patrol the gates of Linhir for any sign of the Enemy.Patrol Linhir's gates to Dor-en-ErnilPatrol Linhir's gates to LebenninThe overlook can be found in the southernmost part of Linhir.

You should patrol the overlook and ensure that the Corsairs at Ethillorn are not rallying a new assault.Patrol the overlook in southern LinhirCorsairs and their grappling hooks can be found atop the overlook in Linhir.

You have discovered Corsairs that scaled the walls of Linhir and should defeat them before throwing down their hooks.Defeat Corsairs that climbed into Linhir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy grappling hooks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Erchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have completed your patrol and routed a small band of Corsairs that attempted to infiltrate the city. You should now return to Erchar.Talk to Erchar in Linhir'Since Azgarzôr's assault on Linhir, all has been quiet. Neither Corsair nor Haradrim have dared to attack our walls, but still... I cannot find comfort in this.

'Many of their forces still patrol the lands outside Linhir, and I am certain they will renew their assault soon. If any Corsairs would strike against us, I believe it would be those that sacked Ethillorn.

'I would ask that you patrol Linhir's gates and then look to Ethillorn from the overlook in the south of our city. Tell me what you discover, ${PLAYER}... I hope we shall be granted peace for even one day more.''I knew we could not hope for such luck, ${PLAYER}. We will have to keep a watchful eye on the forces of the Enemy outside Linhir, and I would ask you to aid us again on the morrow.

'Thank you for keeping them from our folk this day.'The corsairs have disabled the ballistae Dol Amroth uses to defend against ships.The ballistae need to be repaired.Repair ballistae (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lugazag, the western tower in the Ettenmoors, is defended by a host of Orcs, Uruks, and trolls.Lugazag lies far to the west of Tírith Rhaw.

Sergeant-at-Arms Milbrethil instructed you to find and slay guards in the area of Lugazag.Defeat Orc, Uruk, and troll-guards at Lugazag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tírith Rhaw is far to the east of Lugazag.

Making your way across the Ettenmoors, you found and faced a host of the Ongbúrz defending the tower, Lugazag. You should return to Tírith Rhaw and inform Sergeant-at-Arms Milbrethil of your success against the guards near Lugazag.'Greetings, friend ${RACE}. I urge you to listen and consider my words, for this battle is one that shall assist in deciding the fate of all who are threatened by the shadow growing over Middle-earth. To the west of this tower there is a place of evil. Within the walls once held by the Men of Rhudaur, corruption seethes and grows.

'A host of the Enemy awaits an assault from the Free Peoples that must be levied with swiftness, strength, and courage. The tower is called Lugazag, and I ask you to assist us in defeating the Enemy that guards the tower.

'You will likely need the assistance of others as they will fight to the death if need be. Find them and meet them, return to me when you have done as charged.''I only wish to know that the guards near and within Lugazag are slain. Though the battle is fought on many fronts, I wish to liberate and seize this tower above all else. Return to me when the guards are defeated.''You have proven to be a ${RACE} of honour. You shall be rewarded and your tale shall be told amongst the forces here in the Ettenmoors.

'For all you have done to aid us, I salute you, ${PLAYER}.'Tírith Rhaw stands in the east, near the camp of the Free Peoples at Ost Ringdyr. The tower is under the control of the Free Peoples, and you are tasked with killing the guards in the area.Tírith Rhaw is a tower in the eastern area of the Ettenmoors. It lay between the central keep of Tol Ascarnen and Ost Ringdyr.

Soldier Gazlup ordered you to slaughter the guards keeping watch over Tírith Rhaw.Defeat guards at Tírith Rhaw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Soldier Gazlup is at Lugazag.

You were tasked to kill the guards at Tírith Rhaw by Soldier Gazlup of Lugazag. You should return to Gazlup with news of your victory.Speak with Soldier Gazlup at Lugazag'Maggot! You've been conscripted, like it or not, to assail our enemy at the walls of their tower in the east.

'Travel across the Ettenmoors, always east, beyond the Hoardale River and Tol Ascarnen, to the shadow of Ost Ringdyr where you will see the tower Tírith Rhaw rising upon a great hill.

'Kill the guards about this tower to weaken our enemy, and you shall see respect. Fail, and you will face your doom.''Go to Tírith Rhaw, maggot! Kill the guards and give our army the chance that it needs to slaughter these fools!''A victory today, maggot! A victory!

