Tolrían asked you to eliminate the slavers working out of the camp to the south.Defeat corsair slavers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tolrían can be found in Dol Amroth.

Tolrían will be very pleased to hear the slavers have been eliminated.Speak to Tolrían'There are few things in this world that make me truly angry. Make my spine shudder and fingers clench with rage. Seeing a man enslaved by another, reduced to nothing but property, makes my teeth gnash.

'The corsairs are men who do not share this belief. Instead, they would enslave all of their enemy. Put them into camps making ships and weapons, and whip and beat them until they died, then simply replace them with the next.

'Several slavers are working out of the camp to the south. Ensure they never get the chance to take another as property again.''Such vile men deserve a punishment far worse than what you were able to deliver, but for now it will have to satisfy.'The Corsair camp at Hashadîr is home to several slavers. These foul men are preying on unaware travellers on the roads of Belfalas.The Corsair slavers are at Hashadîr, to the south of Dol Amroth.

Tolrían asked you to eliminate the slavers working out of the camp to the south.Defeat Corsair slavers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tolrían can be found in Dol Amroth.

Tolrían will be very pleased to hear the slavers have been eliminated.Speak to Tolrían'These Corsairs are not like us... they are Men of the worst sort. Wherever their ships make landfall, they pillage... they ruin... and they enslave all in their path.

'Many are put to death before the Men of Umbar even set sail, but the strongest are put to work in camps. If they dare to tire, the slavers whip and beat them mercilessly... and that is if they are lucky.

'Alas, now the slavers of Umbar have come to our shores! I have seen them patrolling the camp to the south, and it will not be long before they set their eyes upon the people of Dol Amroth.

'Drive them back into the bay, ${PLAYER}, and show them that the Men of Gondor will never again be enslaved!''Such vile men deserve a punishment far worse than what you were able to deliver, but for now it will have to suffice.'Traps need to be placed along the beach near Hashadîr. These will damage any small boats they bring ashore.The beach is at Hashadîr, to the south of Dol Amroth.

Tolían asked you to place several traps along the beach to damage the corsair boats.Trap the beach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tolrían can be found in Dol Amroth.

Tolrían will be pleased to the beach has been trapped.Speak to Tolrían'There is a small beach alongside the camp to the south the corsairs have been using. They pull up their boats on it and bring supplies ashore, then row back out to the larger ships. This is an opportunity for us.

'Plant some traps along the beach. These will damage the bottoms of the boats and make them take on water when they are put back to the waves. They will either sink on the way, or take several precious days and supplies to be repaired.''Corsairs live and die by the sea and by their boats. Now that they are trapped on the shore, they shall be easy pickings for us.'Traps need to be placed along the beach near Hashadîr. These will damage any small boats they bring ashore.The beach is at Hashadîr, to the south of Dol Amroth.

