Golthor has asked you to recover hidden stores of food and athelas that were stowed away by the Rangers for times of war.Recover hidden food-stores from the Houses of Healing (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Recover stores of athelas from the Houses of Healing (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golthor can be found outside the Houses of Healing in eastern Osgiliath.

You have recovered many food-stores and bundles of athelas and should now deliver them to Golthor.'I will soon make for the tunnels below, but first, I would ask your aid in recovering more of our hidden-stores from the old Houses of Healing just over there.

'A few of the Easterlings began to search it after they lost my trail, and I had not yet finished my task. If you have made it this deep into the city, you must either be a deft traveller or a practiced warrior - either of which I would welcome to my side.

'Within the ruined Houses, you will find stores of simple rations and athelas. Both of these are of great value to us, and I will see you rewarded if you return them to me.''It is fortunate that the Easterlings had not yet picked the old Houses clean for we shall have much need of these goods.

'I shall see them returned the rest of my men in the tunnels. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Weapons are difficult to come by in war-time as many are shattered as the sides of battle clash.Ore can be found on the Snowreap-goblins or in the depths of the Isendeep. Logs can be found on Leafcull-trees or scattered on the ground within the Grimwood.

Lieutenant Swithulf directed you to collect the ore and wood he needs and return to him at the Grimwood Lumber-yard.'The battle goes poorly, if you ask me, ${CLASS}. We drive the Enemy back, and then they return to run us out. All the while, our resources dwindle, while the Enemy continues to garner strength.

'We are in dire need of replenishing our supplies for the effort, and that is why I need your help. To the north there is a mine where our dwarf-allies delve when the Snowreap-goblins are not within the caverns. There are stores there of unrefined ore. We can refine the ore and build axes, swords, and hammers... but first we need the ore.

'Ore alone, however, will not solidify the war effort. There are thicker logs, some already hewn to the ground, scattered throughout the Grimwood and others still may be obtained from the deadly, walking Leafcull-trees. If you mean to aid us, gather logs and ore for me and bring them back so I may continue to fuel our efforts.''You are to be commended for your efforts, ${PLAYER}. This was a difficult undertaking, and you have performed it well. Take this with my thanks and the thanks of the Free Peoples.

'Should you desire to exchange the token, seek Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig.'Plump Hens the enemy is keeping escaped their cages and should be stolen before the enemy find out they're missing.Escaped Chickens can be found roaming around Western Osgiliath.

You should steal the escaped chickens.Steal escaped chickens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dulglok is at Shrak Mauruk.

You should bring the chickens to Dulglok.Bring the chickens to Dulglok'Drop what you're doing and listen to me you filthy minion. The Men across the water have some plump and delicious chickens that just escaped their cages.

'Go over there and steal them before those Gondorian pukes find out!''Oh you've done well. Real well! I'd promote you but then who would be my favourite ${RACE} to yell at?!'Hens providing eggs and meat for the troops in Osgiliath have escaped their confines and should be found and returned before the enemy finds out.Escaped Chickens can be found roaming around Western Osgiliath.

You should find the escaped chickens.Collect Escaped Chickens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Chicken coop is located outside the Palace of Eldacar.

You should bring the Chickens to the Chicken coop.Bring the Chickens to the Chicken coopCangoras is at the Palace of Eldacar.

You should speak to Cangoras.Speak to Cangoras'The hens have escaped! We've been keeping hens near the Western wall to provide eggs and meat for our soldiers. Someone didn't latch the cage door properly last night and now all the hens are missing!

'You must find them quickly before those nasty Orcs find out and pluck them up for themselevs!''Ah good work, the hens are all safe within their cage. And you made sure to lock it properly?'Lenglír, a Master Artist, is concerned for the safety of her art if the enemy somehow manages to infiltrate the city and is looking for the perfect hiding place for her greatest works of art.Potential hiding spaces for Lenglír's artwork can be found on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should scout out hiding spaces for Lenglír's artwork.Lenglír can be found outside the Artists' Fellow-hall on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Lenglír.Speak with Lenglír'I am upset. Why, you ask?! Nasty Orcs are going to get into this city and the first thing they will do is destroy my artwork! I and my assistants have been creating beautiful paintings, documenting this great city. If they are ruined so dies the history of Minas Tirith!

'Now, perhaps you could help me out. I need to find the perfect hiding place for my greatest works of art. There are a few locations that I hear might be ideal but I need someone to scout them out for me. What do you say, will you help protect this city's rich history?''Alas, only one location not already occupied! I suppose it will have to do.'

You ask Lenglír if she would like you to move the painting to the hiding place.

'I could not put that burden on you. No, no, it is something I must carry myself. Also, if you dropped one, I would never be able to forgive you!'Emissary Pip Diggins of Hoarhallow told you a tale of woe concerning the destruction wrought on his village by the Snowreap-goblins far to the north-east of Hoarhallow.The goblin-village of Grothum lies far to the north-east of Hoarhallow.

Emissary Pip Diggins asked you to recover food stolen from Hoarhallow. He directed you to search among the goblin village at Grothum or on the persons of the enemy.'A moment of your time ${RACE}, if you would. I am Pip Diggins, from Hoarhallow. We have a small village on the eastern side of the Hoardale River and have lived here in the place you call the Ettenmoors for as long as my grandfather's grandfather's....

'I think you know what I am getting at. The arrival of these tall folk was providence, ${RACE}, simply providence. We had been set upon by all manner of foul creatures and were not well-prepared to defend ourselves.

'We had seen trolls before, but the Wargs, Orcs, and goblins were another story. Since their arrival, and yours, our little village has seen a number of raids where they have stolen villagers, pipe-weed, and food! If you are willing to visit the goblin-village of Grothum to recover some of our food, I would be very grateful. Grothum is a good distance north of here near the place your folk named Arador's End.''You found it! This is a fine day indeed! A fine day, and I have you to thank for it, ${PLAYER}. There are many here who have learned your name!

'Thank you, thank you for all you have done!'Taskmaster Bárzqhosh is preparing the defence of the Isendeep Mine against the Free Peoples.Fight off invaders who meant to take the Isendeep mine.

You must fight the foe within the Isendeep mine and drive them out for the glory of Angmar.Defeat Free Peoples in the Isendeep Mine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})If the mine is fallen or Taskmaster Bárzqhosh is fallen in the battle, make your way to Gramsfoot and speak with War-tyrant Akúlhun.

Your success is complete. Return to Taskmaster Bárzqhosh and tell him of your victory.'You pathetic worm. You look as though you've soured yourself in my presence and that gives me the urge to scourge the flesh from your back.

'You'll be useful to our army if you sacrifice yourself against the enemy. Stand within the Isendeep and repel the invaders as they cross into these halls. Survive and you might just earn a little favour.

'If you succeed return to me. If you fail, and I feel the sting of arrows...know that I will find you one day and scourge your body to the bone.''Leave my sight, cur! Do what I ask, or I'll lose my temper!''Well done! I may have misjudged your resolve.

'I'll try to remember to look favourably upon you in the future. Don't expect that I shall!''Your efforts are noted, and the failures of others to hold their position is well-known to me. I recognize what you have done, ${PLAYER}.

'Know this...letting superiors die will be punishable by whipping and reassignment to the brimstone-pits of Angmar. Remember well that you're nothing more than a maggot, and you'll live. Try to reach beyond those bounds, and I'll see you spend your life in the brimstone-pits.

'For now, I recognize your efforts and will honour you with thanks.'With the parts of Belfalas under threat, many nobles have left their homes for the safety of the city, leaving much of the coastal areas quiet and vacant. A broker has suggested you might take the opportunity to purchase your own home in Gondor.You can take the horse by the housing broker in either Dol Amroth, Pelargir, or Minas Tirith.

You should visit and take a tour of the Cape of Belfalas housing and environs.Visit the Cape of BelfalasFalastír is located at the lighthouse on the Cape of Belfalas.

The housing broker has recommended that you speak with Falastír, the old lighthouse keeper.Talk to Falastír'Good ${RACE}, you seem a well-travelled one, I dare say! Surely you are aware of what has passed in these troubling times - and that from trouble may come opportunity? Many wealthy Gondorians have well and fully abandoned their homes upon the coast of Belfalas, fearing Corsairs and other unpleasantnesses.

'Many of these are for sale, and if you wished to, you could own one. But why should my blustery words persuade you? You should see the Cape of Belfalas for yourself! Make a holiday of it - or merely take a moment of respite from your travels. If you do so, I would recommend you start up a conversation with Falastír, the old lighthouse keeper.''Well met, traveller! What brings you to this sleepy little coastal community? If you have come seeking rest and sea air, I can say for certain, you have come to the right place! I would love to show you around!'Fearing his people will become slaves to Mordor at the war's end, Jajax weighs his decision to strike against the Heirs of Castamir.Hata Kebir can be found due east of Aerthir in south-eastern Lebennin.

Jajax has asked you to aid him in fighting against the Heirs of Castamir at Hata Kebir.Meet Jajax at Hata KebirHata Kebir can be found in south-eastern Lebennin.

Jajax has asked your aid in weakening the forces of the Heirs of Castamir in Hata Kebir.Aid Jajax in weakening the leaders of Hata KebirAid Jajax in stealing his fellow Corsairs' pillageAid Jajax in crippling the forces of Hata KebirJajax can be found at your side or called with your horn.

You should aid Jajax in his search of Hata Kebir.Aid Jajax in searching Hata KebirDaxamat can be found in the northernmost area of Hata Kebir in south-eastern Lebennin.

You should listen to Daxamat as he recounts the story of his journey to Lebennin alongside the Scourge.Listen to the tale of Daxamat's journey with Balakhôr the ScourgeJajax can be found at your side or can be called with your horn.

You have listened to Daxamat's retelling and should now speak to Jajax.Talk to JajaxErchar can be found in Linhir along the Gilrain in western Lebennin.

Jajax has decided to remain with his brother until you are able to rally the forces of Erchar and Herion against the Heirs of Castamir. You should return to Linhir.Talk to Erchar in Linhir'I suppose it is a bit harder to blend in here in a town so small, but I had hoped our paths would cross once more, ${PLAYER}!

'You are an honourable ${RACE}, and a great burden weighs on me since coming to Lebennin. I believe that our leaders have sought to deceive us, or are so blinded themselves, as to think that our victory will be a prosperous one and bring about a new age for Umbar.

'I have heard many rumblings amongst the men I camped with on my way here that the Scourge merely speaks for one of the Black Riders. If that is so, I fear our people will become naught but slaves to Mordor at the end of this war.

'It is a decision I have not made lightly, but my brethren camped outside Pelargir must be stopped before the Heirs overtake these lands. Meet me at their camp to the east, my friend, if you wish to fight at my side once more.''I will remain here with my brother, but I trust you and your allies shall soon return!

'I never thought I would aid a man of Gondor, but for once our aims have aligned. Let us hope this is the last time, eh! 

'Return to their city, and tell them of the man who rules Hata Kebir. Let them avenge their brother, my friend, for they shall also be saving my people from a terrible fate.

'Until I see you next, ${PLAYER}...''You say a Corsair has led you to the whereabouts of the man who killed Garvir?

'I question your choice of allies, ${PLAYER}, but I will not deny his aid. Let us hear more of this man, and ready our weapons!'The folk of Malbarth pay tribute to the river Gilrain for the bounty it has granted the people of Lebennin and to honour the fabled Sisters of their land.Baskets and cloth can be found in Malbarth, and reeds can be found along the banks of the Gilrain.

Arvaeth has asked for your help in crafting the traditional tribute baskets woven by the people of Lebennin.Collect hand-woven baskets in Malbarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect fine cloth in Malbarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect reeds from the banks of the Gilrain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arvaeth can be found on the banks of the Gilrain, to the north-west of Malbarth.

You have gathered all of the materials Arvaeth asked for and should now return to him with them.'I would like to share something with you, my friend.

'There is a practice among my people to honour the Sisters of Lebennin with tribute baskets given to the river's current.

'Many of our people observe the tradition, yet most do not believe as we do. The Sister of the Gilrain has long brought peace to these lands... a certain harmony even amidst trouble. I can think of no better time to pay her tribute than for keeping us from harm on this darkest day.

'If you would help me craft a few of our traditional baskets from materials in Malbarth, my folk would certainly hold you in high regard.''You have done us a great service by honouring our traditions, ${PLAYER}.

'Let us hope that our tribute and need for hope shall urge the Sister of Gilrain forth from wherever she and her Sisters have gone.'You have pursued a mysterious figured dressed in Faramir's cloak ever since you saw it exiting the tunnels under Osgiliath.Complete the deeds in Osgiliath.Complete the deeds in Osgiliath.Complete the deed The Ruined City -- Tier 1Complete the deed The Ruined City -- Tier 2Complete the deed Challenge: Harrowing OrdealTol Ascarnen has fallen to the combined might of Angmar's army, but their forces are meagre, and they must fortify quickly, else the Free Peoples will regain a foothold here.Rockwithers can be found among the Thistledown Grazers, south across the Hoarwell River.

Angmar's forces at Tol Ascarnen are building a horn with which to call reinforcements to the fight when the Free Peoples return to assault the area. Kaasak has tasked you with retrieving the horn of the great aurochs, Rockwithers.'We've won the keep for a moment only, cur. You've a new task handed down from the War-tyrant himself, and you'll see it done or feel my boot!

'Across the river to the south, in the woods of Hithlad, stalks a great beast with shaggy fur. This beast has two great horns, though only one is needed for our purpose. The horn belongs to the mighty Rockwithers. We think it is the eldest of the Thistledown herd. Slaughter the beast and get its horn. Together with the sinew of drakes and the heartwood of a great Leafcull Huorn, we will build a horn to call our brethren to battle.

'To the south with you and don't return without the prize, maggot!''It's about time, you useless bag of flesh. I've a mind to flay your hide just for you taking so long.

'No matter...you did what was needed, and though I've a mind to see you suffer for your sluggard's way, I'd rather see the horn built so that there is a better chance we hold this tomb of stone.

'I'll pay you attention as you deserve. Take no solace though, you weak-livered wretch: it's a fleeting bit of accomplishment for you in a lifetime of worthless and wasted effort.'Grazadhal commands you to kill enemy Captains to show those foolish men that their hope is lost.Gondorian Captains can be found in enemy strongholds in Osgiliath.

You should kill Gondorian Captains.Kill Gondorian Captains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grazadhal is at Dâr Dugoth.

You should listen to Grazadhal yell at you.Listen to Grazadhal yell at you'Those men have Captains! Pah! Their leaders are weak! Go kill their Captains and drive the hope right out of that weakling army.

'Are you even listening to me?! Get out of my sight and don't come back until all those Captains are dead, you filthy peon!''By the Morgul Blade, you're alive? Guess you want a congratulations. How bout I give you some more orders, you wretch! Har, har!'To retake the Grimwood the forces of Angmar will need to be vigilant and  assisted, so thinks Taskmaster Gazgortag. He thinks that the living trees near the lumber camp will come and fight for the forces of Angmar and sets you to the task of calling them to the fight.Seek a Leafcull Huorn within the southern stretches of the Grimwood. Cut out its heart and place it on the stump near the Grimwood Lumber Camp.

Taskmaster Gazgortag believes that you can draw the Huorns into conflict with the Free People currently occupying the Grimwood Lumber Camp. He directed you to cut out the heart of the leafcull Huorn in attempt to draw out the enemy.'Listen.

'We lose Grimwood.

'Take it back. Get help. Trees have hearts. Get hearts. Put hearts on stump near Grimwood. Call Trees.

'Trees stomp târks good.

'Go now and get hearts to make trees angry!'Soldier Fandmau believes that he can aid in ending the threat posed by the eagles from the north by feeding them troll-stone. How an Orc like this one became a leader is beyond you.Troll-stone shards will likely be found from smaller or larger pieces of the trolls caught in the sunlight. Food can be found on the enemy or the rat-folk in Hoarhallow.

Soldier Fandmau needs some help proving out a theory he has.'I've been thinking of ways to keep the eagles away from this place. Their claws make me wince, and I'm not one to like blood.

'You're the perfect fool to test this theory with, or at least to be an accomplice to me. So you'll do as I say, or I'll call for the trolls.

'Shards of troll-stone, wrapped in foodstuff might fill the birds' bellies with so much weight that they can't fly anymore! I need you to get me little shards of troll-stone and some food to test the theory.''Ha! When next the eagles come to prey on us, we will feed them the stones and they will fall to the ground and die!

'If this fails... you will serve as a suitable reason for the failure!'Harnion fears for the life of his friend, Gondren, who disguised himself in an attempt to discover more of the Heirs of Castamir and their vile plans.Gondren can be found in central Tarlang's Crown.

Harnion has asked you to rescue Gondren from the forces in Tarlang's Crown.Talk to Gondren in Tarlang's Crown'${PLAYER}, there is another matter that has me worried.

'You see, my friend Gondren devised a plan to discover more of our enemies' plans. He thought to disguise himself as a Corsair to sneak behind their lines... and the man cannot even grow a beard! It was a truly foolish plan, but I believe he went ahead with it anyway.

'Gather your allies and search for him near their camps. If he spoke true, he will be dressed like one of them, so take care not to rough him up too badly!''Come back to taunt me, have you? I'm already a dead man, I hardly see the point....

'You... you're not a Corsair! If Harnion sent you, I'm afraid you are too late to save me... but I learned many things of their plans here before I was captured. They seem to take a great deal of joy in bleeding me out, so much so that they have even kept the hounds from me.

'Come close, my friend, I must speak while I still can....'Alf Earthenway was out for a leisurely stroll when goblins found him and dragged him to the north. He has spent the time since his capture cooking for the goblins as they think he makes the tastiest food. It was the only thing that he could do to prevent the goblins from eating him.Alf Earthenway is at Grothum.

Alf Earthenway asked you to help him escape from the goblins.Talk to AlfMarigold Winterdown is at the hobbit-village of Hoarhallow, found on the western edge of the Grimwood Forest in Hithlad. The village is found on the shores of the Hoarwell River.

Alf is free, but before he left you, he asked that you inform Marigold Winterdown that he would be returning to work at the bakery in Hoarhallow shortly.'Please, no more beatings.

'Y-you're no goblin. Merry me! I have never been so pleased to see someone in all my days.

'As you see, I am in a spot of trouble and need a fair bit of rescuing, if you wouldn't mind. Can you help me get clear of these accursed goblins?''Alf was captured by the goblins! We had all thought him lost for good.

'You saved him, ${PLAYER}! We should have a party in your honour. Mayhaps we will, once we get to see the sun shining in these parts again.

'One day it will happen, I know this in earnest. For the moment, I feel it fitting to part with a couple of these tokens the Big Folk from Glân Vraig gave us. Thank you for saving my baker!'Lord Forlong sits in the Merry Swan Tavern, drinking with his old friends Lord Hirluin and one Neldir of Minas Tirith, making the most of the calm before the storm.The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Lord Forlong has recalled an old wine they used to drink, named Beren's Blood, and has asked you to bring him some.Ask Imadan for Beren's Blood wineThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Imadan has some of the Beren's Blood wine Forlong wants. You should gather some yourself from the storage area.Take some Beren's Blood wine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Bring the wine back over to Forlong's table.The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Hear to what Neldir has to say.Talk to NeldirThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Find some of the Old Calembel cheese that Forlong and his friends used to eat with their favourite wine. Start by asking Imadan, the barkeep of the Merry Swan.Ask Imadan for Old CalembelThe Middle Stores are in south part of the Third Circle.

Imadan has no Old Calembel cheese, but thinks the back reaches of the Middle Stores might have some.Ask for Old Calembel in the Middle StoresThe Middle Stores are in south part of the Third Circle.

They have some Old Calembel deep at the back of the Middle Stores. You should gather some for Forlong's table.Take some Old Calembel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Bring the cheese back to the Merry Swan.The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Forlong, Hirluin, and Neldir have tasted the Old Calembel. See how they liked it.Talk to ForlongTalk to NeldirTalk to HirluinThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Hear what Forlong has to say.Listen to ForlongThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Hear what Hirluin has to say.Listen to HirluinThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Listen to Forlong's reply.Listen to ForlongThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Hear what Hirluin has to say.Listen to HirluinForlong claims the mark can be found in the Third Circle, just north of the Pier.

Look for a mark on the column where the old Master of the Burg swung at Forlong's head. Forlong claims it can still be seen but Hirluin disbelieves him.Look for the mark on the columnThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Return to the Merry Swan and tell Hirluin the mark can, in fact, be seen.Return to HirluinThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Listen to Forlong continue his tale.Listen to ForlongThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Listen to Neldir's interjection.Listen to NeldirSearch for these things in the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.

Look for a hat, some bread, some flowers, and a small rug to help prove Neldir's point.Find a hatFind some breadFind some flowersFind a small rugThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Bring the things you have gathered back to Neldir, in the Merry Swan.The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Try to carry the pile of things across the room.Carry the pile of thingsThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Hear what Neldir has to say.Listen to NeldirThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Listen to Forlong's reply.Listen to ForlongThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Hear what Hirluin has to say.Listen to HirluinThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Hear what Forlong has to say.Listen to ForlongGo up to the Fourth Circle and see if anyone knows what became of the minstrel Authlin.The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

You have learned what became of Authlin, Master Minstrel. Now you should return to Forlong and company in the Merry Swan.Return to ForlongForlong and his friends are in the Merry Swan, in the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.

Drink with Forlong and company.Raise a glassThe Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Hear what Forlong has to say.Listen to ForlongAuthlin's favourite spot was across from the Artists' Fellow-hall in the Fourth Circle.

Place the empty bottle of Beren's Blood at Authlin's favourite spot, to commemorate the old minstrel.The Merry Swan Tavern is on the southern end of the Third Circle.

Return to the Merry Swan and tell Forlong the bottle has been placed at Authlin's favourite stone.Return to Forlong'And there we were, stumbling down the darkened street, all that wine and what-have-you stuffed under our coats! Now what was it called, that wine? The name escapes me! And to think I drank so very much of it in those years!

'Ah, hold your tongue, Hirluin! I hear the dart of wit upon it before you ever moved your lips. Forgetting comes of drinking, you will say, and so that wine was its own undoing. I guess correctly, do I not? Ha ha! But let me think one moment... was it? ... yes! Beren's Blood, it was named. How I should like a taste of that wine now!

'You there, my good ${RACE}. Since you are standing right at hand, be so good as to go ask old Imadan if he has got any.''Be a good ${RACE} and ask old Imadan if he's got any Beren's Blood wine, would you?''Beren's Blood?'

Imadan lets out a low whistle.

'You might say that old stuff's a bit beneath lords such as they. But I know what they're at. It's what they drank when they were young men and went free about the City. I suppose recollecting old times can recollect old thirsts, eh?

'There's some over there, among my stores. You may help yourself.''That old Beren's Blood wine is over yonder, among the storage. Take what you please.'Hirluin catches your arm as you come up.

'Give that wine here, friend. Should you place it before Forlong, we others might never have a taste.'

This is met with hearty laughter, not least by Forlong himself.

'Here friends - a glass for you Neldir, a glass for me, yes, and one for you, Forlong, old friend. To our days of youth!''And with one sip, a flood of memories! How we sat at this very table, night upon night. Our glasses full of Beren's Blood and Old Calembel cheese upon our plates.

'${CLASS}, you have kindly furnished us with the wine. Can you find us the cheese, as well? Do some old men a kindness!''Do us a kindness and see if Imadan's got some Old Calembel cheese lying around.''Old Calembel? Ah, well. I don't know what to say, but that some things linger and some things fade away. I haven't had any of that cheese for a good many years. Though now that I think of it, you might try the back of the Middle Stores, just up the way. You'll find all kinds of things back there, you will.''I haven't had any Old Calembel in years. But you might find some in the Middle Stores.''What? Old Calembel? Aye, I think we might well have some, farther in. I'm not going back there. If you want some, you'll need to go yourself.''If we've got any Old Calembel, it's far at the back. Take any you find in there. Nobody else seems to want it.''Why, what have we here? It is a memory in the round, my friends! I thank you, good ${CLASS}. Hirluin, hand me that bread. Forlong, the knife. Let us put fond memory to our lips.''I will confess, this is not how I remembered it. Ha ha! No, it is quite... different.''Is this truly the companion to our youthful wine? My eyes tell me so, but my tongue calls them liars!''It is tart - or perhaps merely bitter - and yet mellow. Or perhaps not so mellow as bland.''Well, my dear friends. If we've learned something tonight, it is that in drink old friends stay true. In taste, they may differ. Ha ha! Ha ha ha!

'Let us wash away that unfortunate taste with another drink of Beren's Blood!''But now we have our wine and our regrettable cheese. Finish your tale, Forlong. You had so many bottles of Beren's Blood under your coats... and what then?''Why, old Minastúr, the last Master of the Burg stumbled across us! It was blind luck, and very bad at that. He knew at once we were the ones who'd done it, and he set to chasing us, waving that iron cane he went about with at us most menacingly!

'In fact, he swung at my head and nearly took it off. To this day, there is a mark against the stone that he hit instead!''Ah, now you go too far! I will not allow such a wanton claim to stand. Someone must be sent. You, ${RACE}, will you go out on the street and show this for a braggart's lie? It was just north of the Pier, Forlong, was it not? Against an alley-column? Yes. Will you go and see?''If you could settle this question of whether the old Master's cane-mark has lasted to this day, or not, we should be ever so grateful.''Well, what did you see? I was right, wasn't I?''The mark can be seen? And you swear to it? Well! I cannot shout at the sun that it is night, can I? Ha ha!

'But we interrupted ourselves mid-tale. Please, carry on!''Well! As I was saying, there we were with some bottles of wine tucked in our arms, but I, for one, had also a hat, bread, some flowers, and a small rolled up rug.''Hold! Hold! This is too much. Confess, Forlong, for NOW you have embellished! Ah, I know that set of the jaw. You stand by your story, do you? So be it.

'Friend ${CLASS}, as you have not wandered off, I wonder if you will settle another quibble. Can you find such things as these and bring them here? Surely they can all be found somewhere in this Circle. What did you say, Forlong? It was a hat, some bread, some flowers, and a small rug?''Lord Forlong here must not be indulged or allowed such extravagant tales. Do see if you can find those things somewhere nearby.''You will see, Neldir. It can be done and I did it!''Hm... Is this claim to be the wine... or the cheese?''How marvelous! You have brought the things. Now we will put it to the test. Can you walk from here to there and carry these? I do not even ask you to run.''That wasn't how it went at all. You haven't the grasp, and besides, your heart wasn't in it!''Well done. That was quite amusing.''Ho ho! This is a mess! I am sorry, friend. Forlong, we see through your plans now. You fed us one truth in hopes we would swallow a lie!

'But tell me, even if you could bear all that in your arms, why in Isildur's name WOULD you?''Why, to woo the heart of my Vanyalos! Oh, do not give such frowns, you goats. None of us have forgotten the procession of maids swooning over you, Hirluin. Nor that tale of climbing the circle-wall, with... what was her name, that one maid with the dark hair?''That was an invention of the minstrel Authlin, and what is more, I think you know it. Though I hold that she spread the tale with as much relish as the minstrel ever did.''I doubt it not, Hirluin. The maids ever fell under your cold spell.

'Old Authlin, though. Now there was a minstrel of uncommon gifts! And a bit of a mischief-maker, too, wasn't he? But who would not forgive words so sweetly sung, or deftly penned! Of war he sang and kings of old, of flowery vales and shepherd's pipes, and of fair-eyed maids.

'You, Neldir, you have lived in Minas Tirith all this time. Does he live and play still? You know not? I must learn his fate. My good ${RACE}, may we lean upon your goodness once again? Will you go up into the Fourth Circle and learn what became of Authlin, Master Minstrel?''If you are looking for Authlin, you have missed him by ten years. Though, for what it's worth, I have heard he died with a glass of wine in his hand and a song on his lips.''How many times have I heard Authlin the Minstrel's name spoken? There are many tales told of that man. Why that patch of green, across the way over there, was his favourite place to perform. They say the night air filled with his harp as he stood there and played sweet melodies to the stars.''Authlin? Why I knew him well, perhaps better than most, though I have not seen him in many a year. I will tell you something I remember of him. Sometimes, after a night of drink and merriment and song, he would confess to me that though his heart burned bright, there was a well of sorrow in it, too, and they ever wrestled. Sorrow for what, he would never tell. And then, sometimes, he would tell me he meant to fight the sorrow and love all the world until he knew his time had come, and then how sweet his rest would be. That is what he told me.''So Authlin lived a good life and died a willing death? Truly, that is the wisdom of old Westernesse!

'Let us honour him and raise a glass. You, too, friend ${CLASS}! You have earned your place, I think!''And look, we have drained this bottle of Beren's Blood. Why, friend, I know what you should do. You should run and place it on that stone he loved, as a tribute to his memory. Yes, that is just the thing!''The bottle is placed? That is good. We did well to honour old Authlin.'

Forlong closes his eyes and for a moment, the garrulous conversation comes to a rest.Arvaethor has asked you to accompany him back to Ethring and help strengthen their defences.Laerind can be found in the village of Ethring.

You should speak with Laerind.Speak with LaerindCandúr can be found patrolling the village of Ethring.

You should speak with Candúr.Speak with CandúrDefend the four entrances of Ethring.Defend the north-east entrance near the lumber millDefend the west entrance leading to EilendothDefend the south entrance leading to Dor-en-ErnilDefend the north-west entrance leading to CalembelSpeak with Arvaethor.Speak with Arvaethor'I wonder how long these Orcs have been waiting in the mountains so that they may once again prey upon the hard-working folk of the Vale.

'Come, let us return to Ethring. This news of the Orc camp is worrying. We must help strengthen Ethring's defences before returning to the Orkish threat in the woods.''Quickly, Orcs have been spotted around Ethring! We must protect the village. To arms!''I am Laerind, wife of Arvaethor. My husband has returned and I am glad that he is safe. I thank you for aiding him.

'Arvaethor should not worry of Ethring. In Borhador's reclusiveness, I have taken it upon myself to organize the village defences with what little resources we have. I have men upon the beacon of Eilendoth, on look-out for attacking Orcs. Our woodworkers have been tasked with making barricades and placing them at the town's four entrances.''Not just Orcs in these mountains but cave trolls as well! I fear the worst is yet to come. Let us bring the fight to the Orcs instead of waiting here for them to attack Ethring.'Duilin and Derufin left Minas Tirith without their father's permission, and now that they have returned they want to make amends.Duilin and Derufin have been firing arrows at the makeshift Mûmak in the Mûmak and Keep Tavern, in the Second Circle of the city.

Duilin has asked you to recover the arrows he has already fired at the Mûmak, and give them to Derufin for his turn.Retrieve arrows from the makeshift MûmakDerufin is inside the Mûmak and Keep Tavern in the Second Circle of the city.Duinhir is somewhere within the city of Minas Tirith.

Derufin asked you to find his father Duinhir and put in a good word for he and his brother's forbidden adventure in Ithilien.Talk to Duinhir atop the wall in the Second CircleLord Duinhir asked you to help his men gather up the equipment he had been inspecting.Collect Blackroot bows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Blackroot swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Blackroot shields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lord Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale went to the Mûmak and Keep Tavern in the Second Circle of Minas Tirith to reprimand his sons.Lord Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale went to the Mûmak and Keep Tavern in the Second Circle of Minas Tirith to reprimand his sons.Talk to Lord Duinhir once again, in the Mûmak and Keep TavernDuilin is in the Mûmak and Keep Tavern in the Second Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Duilin in the Mûmak and Keep Tavern'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! My brother and I have been teaching the folk here where to shoot at a Mûmak in order to bring it down. This crafted fellow is not as large as one of the actual beasts, but it still serves as good practice for letting fly our arrows.

'If you retrieve the arrows I have already fired and give them to my brother, he will be able to practice. He has been asking for his turn for awhile now.''Give those arrows to my brother and he will be able to practice these shots. He has been asking for his turn for awhile now.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Have you seen our father around the city anywhere? I ask only because we have not yet seen him since we returned, and I am afraid he might be rather cross with us.

'You see, he commanded us not to leave the city... but we left anyway. You understand, I am sure. There were Mûmakil to hunt! And furthermore, we learned how best to bring down the mighty beasts. That must be worth something, even to our stern and disapproving father!

'Find him in the city for us, ${PLAYER}. He will be atop the wall somewhere in the Second Circle, probably with a view of the gate to the city. And perhaps you could plead on our behalf for leniency? He will be stern, I do not doubt it, but perhaps you can convince him that we need not be reprimanded for this adventure of ours? It ended happily, did it not?''Find our father in the city for us, ${PLAYER}. And perhaps you could plead on our behalf for leniency? He will be stern, I do not doubt it, but perhaps you can convince him that we need not be reprimanded for this adventure of ours? It ended happily, did it not?''I know you, ${PLAYER}. You are the ${RACE} that brought my boys back to the city. You have my thanks for that. I will have some words for them when I catch them, I don't mind telling you! I am the Lord of the Blackroot Vale, and within those boundaries my command is the law. Outside of them, I am given authority over others by the grant of the Council and the Steward. But in affairs of my own house, and over the actions of my sons, I have complete authority no matter where I am!'

Duinhir thunders his displeasure, and some of the men nearby shrink away involuntarily.

'I commanded them to stay within the city for their own safety. What would I tell their mother if they ran afoul of some evil in Ithilien? Rosfin would never let me hear the end of it! Tell me where they are, ${PLAYER}, and I will teach them obedience!'

You tell him that they learned something valuable about fighting Mûmakil, and that he can find them in the tavern in Minas Tirith named for the beasts.

'I know the place. If you help my men finish gathering up these bows, swords, and shields, I will meet you there. My sons must learn to obey my words, or they will be no sons of mine!'You have arrived to find Lord Duinhir mid-shout.

'...and as my sons, you are responsible for upholding my good name! If you do not do as I command, folk will look at your example and say, "Duinhir cannot even control his own sons! What sort of a man is that?" And furthermore... furthermore!'

Duinhir splutters into silence.'Give him a moment, ${PLAYER}. I have a feeling about this, and I am rarely wrong about such things!'Lord Duinhir stares at the sight of the arrows flying toward the makeshift Mûmak, and is silent for a moment. Suddenly he erupts once again, but with quite a different exclamation.

'Ha! A palpable hit, Derufin! That is the way!

'Why did you not tell me about this, ${PLAYER}? This exercise seems to me quite a useful one. Can I have a try, my son? I will show you how this is done, I warrant! You will see your sire get it on his first try, Duilin!

'I cannot stay mad at my boys. They get their skill at archery from me, you know!''Oh! I will get it next time! Watch this, my boys!''Do you see, ${PLAYER}? There is nothing to worry about after all! He has never been able to stay mad at Derufin or me for very long. Our mother thinks we remind him of himself when he was young. Or perhaps old! He insists he has not changed, after all.

'Thank you once again, my friend! We will be here, practicing our technique! If the battle comes, we will be ready!'After reuniting with Faltharan, the time has come to seek Lord Sirgon in Upper Lebennin.Faltharan can be found just inside the western entrance to Glaniath in Upper Lebennin.

Arvellon has heard of Faltharan's arrival in Glaniath. You should now reunite with him and aid in his search.Talk to Faltharan in GlaniathSirthanc can be found to the north-west of Glaniath in Upper Lebennin.

Faltharan has asked you to accompany him to the beacon Sirthanc where he believes his father may have been taken.Follow the road north towards the beacon SirthancHaradrim guards can be found along the pathway leading to the beacon Sirthanc in north-western Upper Lebennin.

You have discovered Haradrim near the base of the beacon-hill, and should defeat them.Defeat Haradrim guarding the beacon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A watch-horn can be found somewhere near the beacon Sirthanc.

You have defeated many of the Haradrim and should now confront their leader.Call forth and defeat the leader of the HaradrimSirthanc can be found in north-western Upper Lebennin.

You have defeated the leader of the Haradrim and should now search the beacon for Lord Sirgon.Search Sirthanc for the source of the moansThe binding pole can be found on Sirthanc in north-western Upper Lebennin.

You have discovered Lord Sirgon bound to a pole on Sirthanc, and should now free him.Free Lord Sirgon from his bondsFaltharan can be found at your side or can be called with your horn while you are in Upper Lebennin.

