Faltharan has asked you to speak to his father while he examines the Lord's injuries.Talk to Lord SirgonFaltharan can be found at Sirthanc in north-western Upper Lebennin.

You have spoken to Lord Sirgon and should now speak to Faltharan.Talk to Faltharan at Sirthanc'Ah! My friend, the lord regent has arrived in Glaniath. I heard a great commotion by the western road as he rode in, and he has made it known that he seeks his father who was lost in the conflict at Pelargir.

'Our folk have heard many strange things of late, but I am not certain of his whereabouts. Perhaps he has already spoken to the others of such matters...

'You have been a great help to me and my folk, ${PLAYER}. I hope your charge bears fruit, for the sake of all in Lebennin.''Ah, there you are, ${PLAYER}!

'I was beginning to worry that you had set off without me. The folk of Glaniath have told me the Haradrim passed by along the roads to the west and south, and did not halt their advance to attack. These folk have also spoken of hearing weakened cries of a man among their ranks... I hope my father yet lives, but I fear the tortures the Haradrim might inflict upon him if he is indeed their prisoner.

'The roadway to the west passes to the north and leads up a great hill to one of the south-beacons of Lebennin. Let us follow it and see if we can discover where the Haradrim have gone!''I had begun to lose hope, my friend, but I fear our journey is not yet over. My father's condition is greatly concerning... he looks starved to the bone and his wounds risk infection!

'I wish to look over his wounds, but I do not wish him to see the worry in my eyes. Speak to him, and draw his attention for a moment.'Sirgon gazes into the distance at the ruin of Pelargir, his eyes heavy and laden with tears. He musters a weak smile as you approach him.

'I believed none yet lived to search for me... but you have proven me wrong, ${CLASS}. You have renewed the hope that the Men of Harad stole from me as they forced me to watch my city burn.

'I may be but a lord of ruins, but my family lives yet and there is still a dawn waiting to pierce these skies.''My father needs the care of a healer, and Pelargir is no place for the wounded.

'There is a fortified haven nestled in the mountains to the east known as Tumladen. It is a shelter to my people during times of war, and indeed, many of the folk of Lebennin and Lossarnach have already sought refuge within its walls.

'It is there I must bring my father, and with haste.'Suspicious of recent events, Thandor has asked you to inspect the eastern river-gate for any clues about what caused Pelargir to fall.Thandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Thandor.Speak with ThandorThe eastern river-gate can be found on the east side of the city.

You should investigate the river-gate.Investigate the area near the river-gateThe stray note can be found near the eastern river-gate of Pelargir.

You should bring the note to Thandor.Take the noteThandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Thandor.Talk to Thandor'I've heard rumours which are unsettling. It is believed that the Corsairs were let into the city by someone from within. I do not know who would have done this, though I've heard the name of every captain and noble thrown around, including myself.

'I want this dealt with, ${PLAYER}. You and Thandor are the only two I can trust with this matter, so I would ask that you seek counsel with him.''It is most perplexing, ${PLAYER}. Despite the havoc they wrought, the Corsairs seemed able to take the city without much resistance.

'My men were not able to find anything of note at the eastern river-gate, but I suspect that we may find something at one of the other gates. Certainly if the gates were opened, then it probably would have happened with more than just the one.

'I would ask that you start with the eastern river-gate, and make sure to not overlook anything too small.'Thandor carefully reads the note.

'These orders bear the seal of Sirgon? This cannot be. It would mean that the lordship itself is responsible for the fall of the city! I know Faltharan too well to think that he would have a hand in this, but I'm almost too afraid to ask.

'Those men who tried to attack you are part of a larger group. They've made the east-garth their own personal haven. Why they would want these orders has me concerned.'Inhabited by foul fell spirits, hulking fell trolls now lurk Tarlang's Crown and are among Azruthor's most powerful allies.Fell trolls can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown, especially along the main pathway.

Gondren has asked you to defeat fell trolls and quell the fell spirits he believes is inhabiting their bodies.Defeat a fell troll in Tarlang's CrownFell spirit tormentors can be found inhabiting fell-trolls in Tarlang's Crown.

You have discovered foul fell spirits inhabiting trolls in Tarlang's Crown and should defeat them before they can be used against Gondor.Defeat fell spirits inhabiting trolls in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gondren can be found near the main encampment in Tarlang's Crown.

You have quelled several fell spirits and trolls, severely weakening Azruthor's forces in Tarlang's Crown.Talk to Gondren'The things I have seen here, ${PLAYER}....

'When first the Corsairs began to set up their tents, they killed the trolls that came down from Tarlang's Peaks. All of them were to rot where they fell... when suddenly this wave of terror came over me. When I awoke, the trolls walked the Crown once more... but they were dead, I tell you! I know what I saw!

'What manner of foul power could bring forth such a thing, ${PLAYER}? You must see them slain, I beg you!''You... you slew them, ${PLAYER}?

'Let us hope they remain dead this time, my... friend... at least for Gondor's sake... for I fear I do not have long.'Much of Lossarnach's farmland is burned and the first planting has been missed. Indir fears that if the Haradrim discover Arnach's grain supplies, no victory will forestall thin crops and starvation in seasons to come.Lossarnach's seed stores can be found in the farms north-east of Arnach.

You should travel to the remaining farms to the north-east and do what you can to hide and protect the seed stores there.Defeat Haradrim Raiders near the farms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hide the seed stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Indir can be found in Arnach, near the keep.

You should return to Indir and tell him that the remaining seed stores have been safely hidden from the foe.Talk to Indir'These times of war have thwarted spring planting, ${CLASS}. The Haradrim have put some of our farmland to the torch, and in the rest our seed stores lie exposed and vulnerable.

'Even if Dagor's grand war-plans defend us from the Haradrim here, we may yet starve in the coming winter. Already we have missed first planting. We face hard times at our most fortunate!

'Good ${CLASS}, will you visit the farms to Arnach's north-east and defend its stores of seed?''Though Dagor might care little, I for one will sleep easier knowing we might eat in nine months' time, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for helping us in these dire times. I know we are one among many needing help from heroes like you.'Indir seeks to further disorganize the Haradrim by sabotaging their war-horns.War-horns can be found in the Haradrim camps south and east of Arnach.

Indir's men have seen great warhorns in the Haradrim camps. He believes that if you sabotaged the horns, any assault on Arnach would be disorganized.War-horns sabotaged (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Indir can be found in Arnach, near the keep.

Indir believes that if you sabotaged the Haradrim's war-horns, any assault on Arnach would be disorganized. You should return to him and tell him this has been done.Talk to Indir'There is no doubt in my heart: the Haradrim will launch an assault on Arnach. I lay awake at night, imagining how it will go, and last night I dreamt they came with a great blowing of horns. Imagine my surprise when one of my most keen-eyed men told me he had seen great war-horns among the Southron camps!

'Would you humour my whim, ${RACE}? You seem intrepid enough to do the deed. I believe they intend to use these war-horns to call the attack. If the horns were sabotaged, they may be unable to assail us in one overwhelming force. And perhaps, just perhaps, we might withstand them!''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You have brought peace to my troubled heart by shattering those war-horns. Let us hope my dream of them saw true.'Knowing Baranor's men are not prepared, Indir seeks to slow down the Haradrim by disabling their communications.The message ribbons can be found east and south of Arnach.

Haradrim scouts seem to be tying ribbons to trees to send each other messages. You should tear down as many of these ribbons as you can.Tear down Haradrim message ribbons  (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Indir can be found in Arnach, near the keep.

Haradrim scouts were tying ribbons to trees as a means of communicating. You have torn many of them down and should return to Indir to tell him.Talk to Indir'Whilst Dagor dreams of playing at war, he ignores the plain facts before him. Though we are many, we are ill-trained and poorly organized. If the Haradrim who have crept into Lossarnach were to attack now, we would be done for!
 
 'I fear we must take desperate measures to delay this possibility. In a foray yesterday morn, I found strange ribbons tied to a tree. I did not know what it meant at first, but later I returned to the tree and found the fashion of the ribbon's knotting changed.
 
 'Clearly the Haradrim scouts are using these ribbons to speak with each other in simple signs. Would you, good ${RACE}, find what ribbons you can and tear them down? I feel sure it will buy us greatly needed time.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}, and I thank you. With any luck, you have bought us time to prepare ourselves for the inevitable blow that shall fall on Arnach.'Borhador hears a loud noise outside and want you to investigate as he fears the a cave troll has come for him.Borhador heard sounds coming from outside the hall.

You should speak with Borhador.Speak with BorhadorLeave Borhador and face whatever is pounding upon the walls of the Crossing-hall.Leave Borhador and face whatever is pounding upon the walls of the Crossing-hallLet the events transpire.Let the events transpireBorhador stands outside the Crossing-hall.

You should speak with Borhador.Speak with Borhador'This day has given me strength.''You hear it, too. The sounds grow with each passing minute. I fear the town is under siege! My time has come. This is surely the end of days!' 

Borhador begins to weep.

'Leave my hall. It is to be my tomb!''I saw strength in my people today and the strength of this Vale. How did I not see it before?'Erchar and Herion return to the site of the battle that drove them apart and pay their respects before the returning journey to Linhir.Erchar and Herion meet at the battleground.

You should speak to Erchar.Speak with ErcharErchar and Herion meet at the battleground.

You should listen to the conversation between Erchar and Herion.Listen to the conversation between Erchar and Herion.The bodies of Gondorian warriors slain by the Corsair forces can be found at the battleground.

You should cover the bodies with soil and pay your respects.Covered fallen warriors in soil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Herion is at the battleground.

You should speak with Herion.Speak with HerionErchar is at the battleground.

You should speak with Erchar.Speak with Erchar'We have returned but not without great loss.''Erchar does not see the greatness that we have accomplished, only the loss. Do not mistake my words, for I too am saddened by the difficulty of our enemy and the lives they have taken. What I ask for is hope from my brothers to get through this dawn-less day.''Herion is stubborn and cannot see that I have made a mistake in riding west into the enemy. This is not a decision I wish to make again be it rash or wise.

'Come. Let us return to Linhir where I shall apologize to Garvir for my absence and for Herion's.''You have made your way to this place of grief with Herion and I thank you for reuniting us for the return to Linhir.'You have come with Mithrandir to the Old Archives of Minas Tirith, in order to help the Wizard piece together something that has troubled him.Mithrandir is in the Old Archives of Minas Tirith.Talk to Mithrandir in the Old ArchivesMithrandir is inside the Old Archives.Talk to Mithrandir in the Old ArchivesMithrandir has asked you to search one of the chambers in the Old Archives for mention of Eärnur, the last King of Gondor.You have found a scroll bearing Eärnur's name in many locations, and should show it to Mithrandir.Show the Eärnur scroll to Mithrandir in the Old ArchivesMithrandir is in the Old Archives.Talk to Mithrandir in the Old ArchivesMithrandir has asked you to search another of the chambers in the Old Archives for mention of Eärnur, the last King of Gondor.You have found a book detailing the lineage of the Kings and the Stewards of Gondor, and should show it to Mithrandir.Mithrandir is in the Old Archives, and he bears a worried expression.Listen to Mithrandir in the Old ArchivesMithrandir is in the Old Archives.Talk to Mithrandir in the Old Archives'We should leave this place. It is no longer as comfortable or as familiar as it once was.''Welcome to the Old Archives, ${PLAYER}. They were carved into the pier-rock in the centre of the Sages' Neath when the city was still called the Tower of the Sun. This was the original library and store-house of the city, and it remains a trove of ancient knowledge and secrets.

'There is much to discover in the scrolls and books that are here kept, but few in these days give much thought to these dusty shelves. There is no semblance of order to be found. It was in these dark chambers that I found the Scroll of Isildur, and learned much that I needed to know.''You had better fortune than I did, ${PLAYER}, for I have yet to find anything. Let me see this scroll.'

Mithrandir takes it from you and quickly reads the yellowed parchment. After a moment he looks up at you again.

'There are matters of interest in this scroll. It speaks of not one challenge but two, a detail of which I was not aware. It appears that the Witch-king challenged Eärnur to ride forth, and the King was dissuaded from that foolishness by his Steward, a wise man named Mardil. That name I do know, for he would become the first of the Ruling Stewards when Eärnur disappeared into Minas Morgul. It is from his line that Denethor draws his authority.''You found something else? Ah, yes, this book contains diagrams describing the passage of succession through the line of Kings, and then through the line of the Ruling Stewards.

'Do you see? Here is Mardil, the first of the Stewards, who ruled Gondor after Eärnur was taken into the darkness of Minas Morgul. Mardil swore an oath to rule only until the King returned, and each Ruling Steward has made the same vow.'

Mithrandir looks around, furtively, ensuring that you are alone. When he is satisfied that you are alone in the Archives, he continues.

'Perhaps at one time the Stewards believed the line of Kings would return, but that possibility must now seem quite unlikely. We should not speak of it, even here, but there is one on his way to Minas Tirith who will remind Denethor of his vow. The King may very well return to Gondor, and the rule of the Stewards will no longer be necessary.''It may come to nothing, ${PLAYER}. There are few in the city who would believe that a man might return from the darkest depths of evil. Though he was once Eärnur, he has worn many guises since he was King of Gondor. He cannot be the man he was, and despite the rules of succession he has been corrupted by Angmar, and by Mordor.

'But we must remain alert. If Gothmog does seek to seize the throne of Gondor, we must oppose him... no matter the cost.''Eärnur was mighty, and he did not lack for courage, but he possessed none of the caution that could have saved him from doom. He had great victory at Fornost, when he defeated the Witch-king of Angmar, but that victory stirred his pride to great heights. The Witch-king fled; Prince Eärnur believed he had nearly rid Middle-earth of that terrible foe, and cursed his failure to end it there.

'Years later, the Witch-king issued a challenge to Eärnur, now the King of Gondor, and summoned him to Minas Morgul. Eärnur went to that dark city to face his hated foe, and was lost.

'We know now that his will was mastered, and he became the loyal servant of his former enemy. He took a new name, Mordirith, and was given the rule of Angmar while the Witch-king managed the interests of Mordor elsewhere in Middle-earth. Through your own efforts and those of the Rangers and the Champion of Angmar, he was defeated, but it seems that victory was not to last. He maintains some bond to his former life, and it allowed his dark master to draw him back before he was lost for good.''These names are not familiar to me, but I do have a dim recollection that a man named Orolang may have committed some heroic deed at the Battle of Fornost. It is the barest hint of a memory, but I have not even that for these others. Macilnis is a common name among the women of Gondor; none of the histories I have seen include any women in the retinue of Eärnur's knights, but this scroll appears genuine to me and I have no reason to doubt it.

'Some of Eärnur's knights have returned to trouble Middle-earth as Cargûl, but the power he wielded as Mordirith seems more deadly than theirs. We should expect he will be more powerful still in his guise as Gothmog.

'And yet, somewhere behind these masks, does any of Eärnur remain? He was bold but foolish. Can it be that Gothmog will be the same?'Arvaethor asks for you to follow him to the very heart of the caverns, deep inside the mountain.You should speak with Arvaethor.Speak with Arvaethor.Delve to the deepest chamber of the caverns of Nimrond.Delve to the deepest chamber of the caverns of NimrondDestroy the dark stones to gain entrance to the inner hall of Nimrond.Destroy the dark stones to gain entrance to the inner hall of Nimrond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Drugât and Nerzus can be found in the innermost chamber of Nimrond.

