Now I must address the men.''Oh, Dagor! What good can come of this folly? My heart cries, none, none at all.''What madness is this? Running off into the night! Perhaps I was wrong... perhaps it is better he remained here in Arnach. Had he gone with Lord Forlong and behaved thus on the true field of battle... just think of the disgrace!

'But I am rattled and winded from the combat. Let us retire, set the townsfolk at ease, and tend to the wounded. Then, without delaying overlong, we should set out in search of Dagor.'The fearsome Sûhalar, Korpûrta, must face the consequences of his actions for the slaughter of Gilgír and Tolwin's older brothers.Stay close to Tolwin and Dúneth and defeat enemies at Jal Kepir.Defeat enemies at Jal Kepir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cross the bridge to Cair Andros and find The First Blade.Find The First BladeDefeat The First Blade.Defeat KorpûrtaYou should speak with Dúneth.Speak with Dúneth'We have accomplished what we came here for. Let us retreat to Crithost.''We shall not tarry here much longer. We have finished what we have set out to do. It would be foolish to take on the entire army gathered within these walls.

