You should search for a Ranger base in the tunnels under Osgiliath.Search for Rangers beneath Osgiliath'You and I both seek Faramir, do we not? I seek his guidance and safe return to Ithilien. You seek him out to inform him of some matter in the west. If that is so, then I believe we must get  you into Osgiliath.

'First you'll need to patrol the path taken by the Morgul-host. Once you have finished your patrol, return here and we shall see if the time is right to send you into the city.''It seems that the enemy is no longer on the move, but the entrance to Osgiliath is overrun. I know of another way into the city.

'After the conflict some of the south wall of the city was destroyed. This may be your best point of entry as I doubt it will be guarded. Once inside the city, seek out the tunnels, as they will allow you to move around the city relatively unnoticed. If Faramir and his garrison are still trapped inside the city, he would have established a base in those culverts. Stay safe, ${PLAYER}.''How did you find us stranger? I hope you were not followed!'

You assure Mablung that you were not followed and that with help from the Rangers of Ithilien, you have come seeking Mablung's leader, Faramir.

'You are not the only one who seeks Faramir. I, too, am searching for my Lord and captain.'With the Haradrim assault coming any moment, Indir is worried that some of the townsfolk are still outside the bailey walls.Some people remain outside the keep, in the town of Arnach.

