Avordur asked you to venture to Kêr Bras within the Paths of the Dead and plant several banners of Gondor to show you do not fear the Ruthless Dead.Plant banners at Kêr Bras (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Avordur is in Dol Amroth, far to the south of the Paths of the Dead.

Avordur will be pleased to hear you planted the banners within Kêr Bras.'The Ruthless Dead now rule the Paths of the Dead. They are Oath-breakers who denied their chance at redemption. Even getting near the Paths of the Dead, you can feel their anger emanating from within.

'Head north, to the Paths of the Dead and venture to Kêr Bras, right into the heart of them. Plant these banners of Gondor within. Let them know we do not fear them.''Fear is a powerful force. Letting them know it is no longer on their side provides us an advantage.'Blooms of Decay grow within Kêr Bras.Blooms of Decay can be found at Kêr Bras, inside the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of Dol Amroth.

Avordur asked you to gather several Blooms of Decay from Kêr Bras.Gather Blooms of Decay from Kêr Bras (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Avordur is in Dol Amroth, far to the south of the Paths of the Dead.

Avordur will be pleased to begin working on the Blooms of Decay you recovered.'There is a type of mushroom, the Bloom of Decay, that is very potent and powerful. Its primary use is to make poisons, very virulent concoctions that can kill a man within minutes. However, few know of its other, more valuable use. With the right treatment, patience, and time, it can cure a myriad of poisons and diseases.

'Blooms of Decay grow at Kêr Bras, within the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of here. Bring me back several and I will begin the lengthy process.''It will take many weeks to properly treat these, but once they are, they will be a great boon to us.'When an Oathbreaker is quieted, the ground where it falls is tainted.Kêr Bras is within the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of Dol Amroth.

Avordur asked you to apply a lacquer to the ground beneath any Ruthless Dead you quiet. This should prevent any taint.Lacquer the ground beneath quieted Ruthless Oathbreakers at Kêr Bras (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Avordur is in Dol Amroth, far to the south of the Paths of the Dead.

Avordur will be interested to hear if the lacquer worked.'I have been reading reports from those venturing within the Paths of the Dead. When an Oathbreaker is quieted, something odd seems to happen. The ground turns black and foul, any plants around are killed, and waters are tainted. As we try to quiet the Ruthless Dead, we may end up destroying the Morthond in the process.

'After you have quieted one of the Ruthless Dead within Kêr Bras, apply this lacquer to the area they fell. It should counteract the taint. The Paths of the Dead are far to the north of here.''Sometimes yes, sometimes no, eh? I will continue to work on the formula, but at least we appear to be on the right track.'The Ruthless Dead are concentrating their forces at Kêr Bras within of the Paths of the Dead.Ruthless Dead are at Kêr Bras, within the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of Dol Amroth.

Avordur asked you to quiet as many Ruthless Dead within Kêr Bras as you can manage.Quiet Ruthless Dead at Kêr Bras (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Avordur is in Dol Amroth, far to the south of the Paths of the Dead.

Avordur will be pleased you quieted many Ruthless Dead within Kêr Bras.'The Ruthless Dead are growing in number, I do not know how. I'm not sure if there are some who were hiding in the deeper caves, or some who have abandoned Aragorn's army and returned to the Paths of the Dead.

'They are concentrating in Kêr Bras. Head there and quiet as many as you can. Kêr Bras is within the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of here.''They will arise again, they always do. But we have bought ourselves some more time.'Over the years many have entered the Paths of the Dead. None returned.Fallen adventurers can be found at Kêr Izel, within Paths of the Dead, far to the north of Dol Amroth.

Golusel asked you to return any remains of those you found within the Paths of the Dead.Recover remains from Kêr Izel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golusel is in Dol Amroth.

Golusel will be eager to properly bury the remains you have recovered.'The Paths of the Dead have long been a forbidden place, but that didn't always stop people from venturing within. Whether by choice, force, or mistake, many have gone into those tunnels and never been heard from again.

'Their bodies, or what is left of their bones, are likely still within Kêr Izel and the caves under that wretched mountain. Bring back whatever you can find, I'd like to ensure they get a proper burial. Kêr Izel is in the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of here.''These people deserve a proper burial. I will see to it that they get one. Thank you.'A pool of foetid water is in the ancient city within the Paths of the Dead.Lenn Dûskud, a small pond, is at Kêr Izel, within the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of Dol Amroth.

Golusel asked you to venture to a pond within the Paths of the Dead and clear it of any foul objects.Remove ruthless rune-stones from Lenn Dûskud (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golusel is in Dol Amroth.

Golusel will be pleased to hear the waters have been cleansed.'The Morthond, the great river that flows through these lands, begins from within the Paths of the Dead. Rumour is Lenn Dûskud, a pond within the ancient city, has been corrupted by the dead within. If those waters were to find their way into the Morthrond the entirety of this region would be irrevocably harmed.

'Venture north to the Paths of the Dead, find this city and remove any ruthless rune-stones within this pond that could corrupt the waters.''With the Ruthless Dead angry and stirred up, we will have to watch these waters more closely.'The Ruthless Dead, irredeemable Oathbreakers who did not follow Aragorn, are still within the Paths of the Dead.Ruthless Dead can be found within Kêr Izel, in the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of Dol Amroth.

Golusel asked you to quiet the Ruthless Dead within the lower city of the Paths of the Dead.Defeat Ruthless Dead in Kêr Izel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golusel is in Dol Amroth.

Golusel will be pleased to hear many Ruthless Dead have been quieted.'Many of the Oathbreakers appear to have marched with Aragorn. A group of them however, the Ruthless Dead, refused to accept his offer and now stew within the tunnels and caves of the Paths of the Dead. They are beyond redemption. Though they cannot be killed, they can be quieted for a period.

'Kêr Izel is within the Paths of the Dead, far north of here. Venture within and quiet any Ruthless Dead you encounter within.''I fear we are ultimately fighting a losing battle, but at this point I do not know what else we could do.'There are reports of powerful Ruthless Dead preying on those brave enough to now use the Paths of the Dead.The Shadow-watch is within Kêr Izel, in the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of Dol Amroth.

Golusel asked you to venture to the Paths of the Dead and disperse some Ruthless Dead who are preying on travellers from an overlook.Defeat Ruthless Banner-bearers at the Shadow-watch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golusel is in Dol Amroth.

Golusel will be pleased to hear the Paths of the Dead should be safer for a period of time.'With most of its occupants now gone, a few brave souls are using the Paths of the Dead to traverse between here and Rohan. The majority are now making it through, a welcome departure from even just a week ago. However, some are not so lucky.

'I have heard about a group of Ruthless Dead watching over the path from the Shadow-watch, an overlook within Kêr Izel. Find them and disperse them. Kêr Izel is within the Paths of the Dead, far to the north of here.''They will return, you cannot defeat an Oath-breaker, you can only quiet it for a time. But still, a time is better than not at all.'Half-troll axes should be collected and brought to Anborn as proof that you have completed your mission to disrupt the enemy gathered at Lân Mefam.Lân Mefam is located east of Bâr Húrin.

You should collect Half-troll axes by defeating Half-trolls in Lân Mefam.Collect Half-troll axes at Lân MefamLân Mefam is located east of Bâr Húrin.

You should collect Half-troll axes by defeating Half-trolls in Lân Mefam.Collect Half-troll axes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Anborn can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin.

Show Anborn the Half-troll axes you collected.Bring the Half-troll axes to AnbornYou need some way to show the Rangers that you've completed your mission to disrupt the Haradrim at Lân Mefam. Half-trolls patrol the paths of Lân Mefam. Perhaps returning to Anborn with a few Half-troll axes will convince him of your heroics and earn his trust.'This is proof enough that you have completed your mission. We will be able to rework the metal in these axes into fine arrowheads. Nothing like piercing your enemy with their own weapons. I commend your efforts.

'If you are finished with Thurindol's mission then we should discuss upholding my end of our agreement.'Haradrim tents line the hillside at Lân Mefam and should be destroyed to disrupt the enemy forces gathered there.Lân Mefam is located east of Bâr Húrin.

