You should destroy Mûmak feed bags at Lân Mefam. Destroying them should make the Mûmakil hungry, restless, and difficult to control.Destroy Mûmak feed sacks at Lân MefamLân Mefam is located east of Bâr Húrin.

You should destroy Mûmak feed bags at Lân Mefam. Destroying them should make the Mûmakil hungry, restless, and difficult to control.Destroy Mûmak feed sacks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroyed Mûmak feed bags.CompletedYou notice large sacks scattered about Lân Mefam. These must be Mûmak feed bags. Destroying them should make the Mûmakil hungry, restless, and difficult to control.By destroying the feed sacks you have weakened the usefulness of the Mûmakil to the Haradrim forces.Binding the walls at the lumber-yard requires roots to be used as lashings.Roots can be found upon the downed trees throughout the Grimwood and the saplings that sprout from the ground. You might also find them on the Leafcull-trees.

Chieftain Torbok wants you to get lashings for the walls at the Grimwood Lumber-yard.'Maggot! Your role in this war is clear. You do as the Krahjarn say!

'In the wood are saplings. These saplings and some of the fallen timber might have long roots attached to them. We need roots from the Grimwood to tie the posts together.

'We need this place in perfect repair for when the enemy returns. If you prefer something more martial, you might find the wood crawling with creatures that have roots as well! Get out there!''These will do, but you took longer than I would have liked, worm! Make your way through these woods faster in the future, or I'll do some culling of my own.'When the rat-folk in the south were discovered, they scored a blow against the scouts who found them, slaughtering all but one. The leader of the rat-folk village was responsible for the attack, and Taskmaster Fikdag thinks that you can assist with exacting vengeance.Make your way south along the Hoardale River to the village of Hoarhallow.

Taskmaster Fikdag directed you to find and kill Mayor Wat Mudbottom, the leader of the rat-folk village.Taskmaster Fikdag is at Dâr-gazag.

You stalked through the trails to the centre of Hoarhallow and struck down their leader. You should return to Taskmaster Fikdag with the news.'When we discovered the rat-folk village in the south, our scouts engaged them to force them into the service of Angmar. Their leader rallied them together and organized their number into a fighting force that bested all but one of our scouts.

'I tell you this so you understand the disgrace that awaits failure in this task, ${PLAYER}. Seek out the leader of these rat-folk and carve his heart out of his chest!''Bring no more disgrace to this war-host, ${PLAYER}. We fight for the glory of Angmar and the favour of Lugbúrz! Find and kill the rat-folk's leader!''You think this was a victory? My scouts tell me that Wat Mudbottom still lives.

'You beat him, yes! But he is not dead. There is no end to the incompetence found in the lesser tribes!

'A victory indeed, but a hollow one!'Lieutenant Ingi not only desires the destruction of the goblins, but the dismantling of their leadership as well. He knows that Bok and Gasham are both leaders amongst the Snowreap goblins and wants them removed.Grothum, the goblin-village in Arador's End, lies to the north. One of the leaders there watches the road into the Isendeep, the other hides deep within the crags of the camp.

Lieutenant Ingi's hatred for the goblins knows no bounds. He wishes you to target the leaders of the Snowreap tribe at Grothum and remove them from the area.Lieutenant Ingi is at Ost Ringdyr, south of Grothum.

Fighting through the Snowreap village of Grothum you found and defeated the two goblin leaders, Bok and Gasham. Now you should return to Lieutenant Ingo for your reward.'My hatred for the goblins runs as deep as the veins of mithril in Moria. I'll not mince words.

'There are leaders, Bok and Gasham, at the village at Grothum. They are cunning and cruel. Each capable of leading the goblin-folk and both fiercely set against the Free Peoples. Defeating them is possible, but we must strike swiftly. If you go to Grothum, fight and kill these two creatures, then return to me. I will see that you receive a fitting reward.

'Beware their strength. They are not of normal goblin-stock.''Bok and Gasham can be found north in the goblin-village of Grothum. One watches the road from the mine, the other is cowardly and stays deep within the camp.''You've done well, ${PLAYER}. Bok and Gasham will return, that is assured. Until they do, we shall earn a small reprieve. For that reprieve you are owed a reward.

'Here, take these. Remember, Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig will trade these for a key to the chests she guards.'Concerned by the growing influence of the Heirs of Castamir in Lebennin, Nimithil hopes to warn Steward Malthellim of treachery within Ost Anglebed and prevent her people from splintering.Nimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.

Nimithil has asked you to accompany her in speaking to the Steward of Ost Anglebed of her worries about the Heirs of Castamir and their influence on her people.Talk to NimithilNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.

You have survived Malthellim's betrayal and should now speak to Nimithil about what is to be done next.Talk to Nimithil'I have seen enough, ${PLAYER}.

'We must go to the Steward at once and convince him to do something before our people turn on each other. Each day has brought more and more rumours of the supposed greatness of these Heirs, but it is clear that they mean naught but harm for Gondor. The people are divided, and I see them look with such disdain at their fellows... I fear this conflict shall soon come to blows.

'And this treachery in Ost Anglebed... who could be behind it? We must find out before they can weaken us enough for the Enemy to overcome our defences.

'Let us go, ${PLAYER}!''Let us speak with the Steward at once, ${PLAYER}.''Were it not for you, I fear Malthellim would have slain any who defied him.

'I do not understand how he could align himself with such vile men - a new king is not worth the deaths of your country and kin.

'We can only count ourselves lucky that more of the disillusioned folk in Ost Anglebed did not come to his aid.'Shíktarb commands you to destroy enemy barricades scattered around Western Osgiliath to dismantle the Gondorian defences.Enemy barricades can be found on the Western side of Osgiliath.

Destroy the enemy barricades.Destroy enemy barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Shíktarb is at Shrak Mauruk.

You should listen to Shíktarb yell at you.Speak with Shíktarb'Can you believe those Men put up rickety barricades to keep us out?! Foolish!

'Go destroy them, they look stupid. They don't understand the power of the Morgul army! Show them what we are!''Destruction is what I like to hear! Keep at it you peon. There might be hope for you yet to rise through the ranks!'Lieutenants watch over the sergeants and lesser guards of the enemy as they drive their war-efforts deeper into the Ettenmoors. Plucking the seals worn by each of these warriors will earn you greater favour with your leaders.Positions held by the enemy are often watched over by the lieutenants in their army. You may even find a lieutenant flanked by sergeants in the wild-lands.

Chieftain Durulkum commanded that you retrieve the seals worn by the lieutenants in the enemy army and return them to him at Dâr-gazag.'Across this foetid land you will find many who are clinging to the hope that they can defeat this war-host. I know as well as you their hope is ill-placed. We grow stronger with every passing hour, and there is no stopping the forces Mordirith sends forth from his palace in Carn Dûm.

'Keep your head about you when you face these foes, you pile of dung. I'll not tolerate failing easily. Your failure will cast me in an ill shadow, and I will see your failure purged before my name is tarnished.

'Collect the seals carried by the lieutenants in their army and return them to me. Much favour is earned by their acquisition.''This pleases me. Not enough to pay you a compliment, though, vermin. Yet, I am obligated to reward your efforts with something. This pittance will suffice.

'Whine or prattle on about how little I give, and I will drive my sword through your gullet!

'I serve Mordirith, Angmar, and Lugbúrz without question, so you should follow me as well.'Something stirs in the tunnels and passageways beneath the crumbling ruins of Osgiliath.Complete the deeds beneath Osgiliath.Complete the deeds beneath Osgiliath.Complete the deed Sunken Labyrinth -- Tier 1Complete the deed Sunken Labyrinth -- Tier 2Complete the deed Challenge: Subterranean SlugfestComplete the deed Memories of the Second AgeCaptain-General Mákan does his best to assist the morale of the troops stationed at Tol Ascarnen. The relentless battle takes its toll on a being over time, and ale is the best way to keep the Free Peoples prepared.You may be able to find some in Hoarhallow itself, but it will likely be costly. You may even find the draughts stored at Grothum and Dâr-gazag.

Lieutenant Solvi asked you to find and recover draughts of Hoarhallow-ale.'Listen here. Captain-General Makán looks out for the Free Peoples as best he can, and that's why he has me working on restocking food and ale.

'Hoarhallow, that little village of hobbits to the south-west, makes the finest ale in the region -- well, the only ale in the region. Slightly bitter to appeal to the taste of dwarves and Men, with a sweet finish that the Elves desire.

'Raiders from the forces of Angmar have looted so much of the ale that there is not enough left to go around. Find some Hoarhallow-ale and make your way back to me, and I will see you suitably rewarded.''Ah yes! A great many of the draughts, indeed! This'll warm our bones on long nights looking out over the walls of this fort.

'You've earned this, ${PLAYER}. Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig is collecting these for greater rewards.'Lady Vanyalos wishes to know the current mood and thoughts of the people of Imloth Melui.Hathalon trains new recruits in the northern part of Imloth Melui. Merenir oversees the flow of refugees by the fountain in the middle of town. Master Healer Brunil treats the injured within the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of Imloth Melui.

Lady Vanyalos has asked you to talk to the people she trusts in Imloth Melui and determine their moods.Talk to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of Imloth MeluiTalk to Merenir, Captain of the Guard, in the centre of Imloth MeluiTalk to Hathalon, Master-at-arms, in the north of Imloth MeluiLady Vanyalos is in her hall on the north-eastern rise in Imloth Melui.

You should return to Lady Vanyalos and report what you have heard from her three trusted advisors.Talk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall on the north-east rise of Imloth Melui'It is good to speak with someone new, even if you were driven here by sorrow and war. So many good men have gone away to Minas Tirith, my husband Forlong not least of them. Indeed, he exceeds them all, in girth, at least! My Forlong always had such a sense of humour, and fond of his dinners, too.

'One sound has fled beyond the walls of my city, ${PLAYER}, and I miss it almost as much as Forlong. The sound of laughter has quite vanished from the vale. Has its absence affected my people as grievously as it has me? I ask you to speak with the few trusted folk who remain, and learn if they have given up hope of victory and peace in Imloth Melui.

'Hathalon is my Master-at-arms, and he is responsible for training the few warriors who remain. If he has given in to despair, I fear the sickness will spread to his recruits. Merenir, my Captain of the Guard, oversees the flow of refugees by the fountain in the middle of town. And Master Healer Brunil treats the injured within the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of town. I rely on all three of these good people, and I need to know they are still able to carry out their duties.''I ask you to speak with the few trusted folk who remain, and learn if they have given up hope of victory and peace in Imloth Melui.

'Hathalon is my Master-at-arms, and he is responsible for training the few warriors who remain. If he has given in to despair, I fear the sickness will spread to his recruits. Merenir, my Captain of the Guard, oversees the flow of refugees by the fountain in the middle of town. And Master Healer Brunil treats the injured within the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of town. I rely on all three of these good people, and I need to know they are still able to carry out their duties.''Lady Vanyalos sent you to ask after us?'

Brunil scowls at you.

'The sick are sick and the well are weary. I would not expect the Lady to come to these halls, but I suppose sending you shows that at least she thinks of us on occasion, toiling away for the health of her people. Tell her that we do what we can with less than we need, and if we complain we do it only as a result of much hardship.''Lady Vanyalos wishes to know the mood of the people? That is why Imloth Melui will thrive even in the absence of Lord Forlong, ${PLAYER}. What ruler cares as much about her people as Lady Vanyalos? Very few, I wager!

'When you return to her hall, please bring my assurances that we keep good watch on all who approach the vale. Nothing will threaten Imloth Melui without me hearing of it first!''How am I feeling? I have seen better days and better nights, ${CLASS}! Most of the warriors have already left this city, and now I am forced to remain behind and train youths and old men!

'This is a city of healers and potion-makers, not fighters. Even with the finest training I can give to them, this vale is nearly undefended! Tell Lady Vanyalos we must hope the enemy does not come to Imloth Melui, for that is the only way we might survive!''I thank you for judging the mood of my people, ${PLAYER}. If I were a potion-maker, I would think two parts despair and one part hopefulness a poor mixture indeed, but perhaps I should be grateful it is no worse.'As the battle for the Ettenmoors rages on, the host of the Free Peoples is beginning to realize that they must think about reinforcing their positions throughout the land.Tortmund Cliffside is at the tower on the eastern border of Hoarhallow, just over the bridge.

Sergeant-at-Arms Aeglas has asked you to see the safe arrival of the hobbits from Hoarhallow. The hobbits will be assisting the Free Peoples in acquiring enough materials to create bulwarks throughout the Ettenmoors.Escort Tortmund Cliffside to the Grimwood Lumber camp'We have allies to the west, ${PLAYER}, allies willing to come and assist us in the collection of much needed resources in this battle. The battle is taking longer than we thought, and we must prepare battlements throughout the Ettenmoors. To do this, we must have proper provisions and materials, which means that we need to get this lumber-camp operational.

'Tortmund Cliffside, one of the halflings, has agreed to lead a group of his people to the Lumber Camp. He is located within the tower at the eastern edge of Hoarhallow. Go and speak to him, then bring him safely to the Grimwood Lumber-yard.

'Be swift, but be cautious.''Tortmund can be found at Hoarhallow, my friend. You should find him and speak with him.''Let us move along. If all goes well, we will arrive swiftly.'There are many chests within the mason containing weapons and armour.The chests within the mason should be locked to prevent the corsairs from getting the contents within.Lock chests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Shíktarb commands you to patrol the Eastern side of Osgiliath and make sure those pesky Men haven't crossed the river.Patrol the Eastern side of Osgiliath.Patrol the Southern docksPatrol the central docksPatrol the central lookoutPatrol the bridge to the Dome of StarsPatrol of overlook of the Northern courtyardPatrol the central courtyardShíktarb is at Shrak Mauruk.

You should listen to Shíktarb yell at you.Listen to Shíktarb yell at you'Those crafty Men have been spying on us! You better patrol the Eastern side of Osgiliath. Make sure they don't get the idea to come over here again.

'If I see one, I sure won't be inviting him in for bones and slop! I'll kill him and eat him I will!''Hope you weren't slacking off on your patrol. I don't want to have to execute my favourite minion to make an example out someone who doesn't do their orders right!'Corsairs may be hiding within some of the houses in Dol Amroth.The houses should be searched for corsairs.Search houses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Balangyl will not leave the ruined fishing village of Gaerlond until he finds his dog Pebble.Pebble the dog can be found somewhere within the village of Gaerlond.Find the lost dogYou have come across Pebble the dog and should now aid her in returning to her master.Aid the lost dogBalangyl can be found near the village of Gaerlond.

You should speak with Balangyl.Speak to Balangyl'Good ${RACE}, have you come across my dog Pebble?

'Oh, I lost her, I did. After years of fishing together on my rowing boat, now she is gone! I can't find her anywhere. We were fleeing the village when she saw a cat and ran off chasing it. I had to hide from the Corsairs as they came through the village. I'm afraid Pebble may have got caught in some rubble, or worse! Can you find her and bring her back to me? I'll forever be grateful.'The dog looks happy to see you and you believe she is ready to return to Balangyl.'Oh, this is a day to remember. I thank you ${RACE}, for rescuing my Pebble. She thanks you too! Well we should be off to safer ground. Thank you again, good adventurer!''Woof, woof!'Corsairs are looting the Swan-knight Barracks for the valuable weapons and armour within.The looters must be defeated and the weapons and armour secured.Defeat looters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Celebros, the wife of Lord Sirgon, lost a family heirloom during her capture. She has asked for your help in finding it.The capture site can be found to the north-east of Celebros.

