<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Ingold is in the besieged city, atop the wall at the north end of the Third Circle.

You have convinced some of the fleeing men to return to their posts, despite their terror.

<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Talk to Ingold in the besieged city, atop the wall at the north end of the Third Circle'${PLAYER}! An icy chill grips my heart, and it takes all of my strength to stand here at the wall; my heart quails, and would have me fly from my post in terror!'

Ingold lowers his voice and speaks in hushed tones.

'The Enemy has catapulted vile ammunition onto the city: heads they have taken from soldiers caught outside the walls, in the Pelennor and Talath Anor. The barrage has caused men to cast down their weapons, fleeing from the sight of friends and family returned in this horrible fashion. I am not immune to this weapon of Mordor! I have recognized faces in that terrible rain: it was the fate of Barathant, ${PLAYER}, and I wept to see it.

'Can you gather up the weapons and shields that were dropped by frightened men as they fled their stations? We need that equipment, and those men, if we are to stand against the armies of Mordor!''Gather up the weapons and shields that were dropped by frightened men as they fled their stations, ${PLAYER}. We need that equipment, and those men, if we are to stand against the armies of Mordor!''Thank you for gathering up that equipment, my friend. Now we need men to wield them once again!

'I do not blame them for running. Evil are the sights in war, but this is worse than even a hardened soldier of Gondor could expect. But we must not give up hope! If the men who ran do not return and fight, they will prove great allies to the foes outside the city. Only by returning to their posts and facing their fears can they strike a blow against such evil!

'Find the men who ran, ${PLAYER}. Tell them to return! We need every soldier of Gondor to master his fear and stand against the host of Mordor, or all is already lost.''Find the men who ran, ${PLAYER}. Tell them to return! We need every soldier of Gondor to master his fear and stand against the host of Mordor, or all is already lost.''You did well, my friend. I, too, will fight until the last of my courage is spent, in order to avenge the sad fate of my friends! Barathant will be avenged, and if it is in my power to prevent the destruction of Gondor, I will do it!'While scouting the western side of Osgiliath, Halhir learned of the horrible fate that awaits all who are captured by the Morgul-host.Imprisoned Rangers can be found in and around Meneldil's Square in western Osgiliath.

Halhir has asked you to free imprisoned Rangers of Ithilien before they are executed in Meneldil's Square.Halhir can be found due east of the Palace of Eldacar in western Osgiliath.

You have rescued many imprisoned Rangers and should now return to Halhir.Talk to Halhir'Have you passed through the square, stranger? I doubt you have... for your head still sits upon your neck.

'They gather the imprisoned in the theatre to the south, and then they drag them out into the square to be tortured... and beheaded. They play with the bodies, and they toss around the heads laughing with those horrible Orkish tongues. After a time they burn the corpses, but the heads they keep, and I do not know to what vile end - nor do I wish to.

'This is war, ${PLAYER}... make no mistake of that. If you are to be one of us, you must know the horrors we have endured. Make for the square and free any of our men that yet live, and slay any of those Troll-men that stand in your way!''It pains me to see so few left alive, but any who were spared that fate have truly been granted a new life.

