Defeat a good number of fell spirits in the Dead Marshes.You have defeated a number of spirits in the Dead Marshes.Gruel comes from somewhere, and with an army as large as the forces Angmar has sent to the Ettenmoors, gruel is needed in great abundance. You have been charged with collecting the main ingredient in the mush Taskmaster Gukthor makes.Giant slugs make the Steps of Gram their home.

Taskmaster Gukthor awaits your return with the slug-meat he demanded.Collect chunks of slimy slug-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Giant slugs make the Steps of Gram their home.

Taskmaster Gukthor awaits your return with the slug-meat he demanded.'If you are looking for something more violent than scouting, who isn't, ${RACE}? You could help Taskmaster Gukthor out of Dâr-gazag. 

'He cooks the meals for the forces there and needs help with gathering supplies. He told me to set new recruits out hunting for slug meat.

'You heard me right, maggot. You'll be hunting slugs for their meat. When you've got a large bundle make your way to Dâr-gazag far to the south in the Steps of Gram and give the meat you got to Taskmaster Gukthor, or come back here and I'll see they gets where they needs to be.''Dallying about, shifting your weight to and fro, is not helping the army in any way. Want to make yourself useful then, do you?

'Right then. All over the Steps of Gram are these giant slugs... we seen 'em before in the slave pits of Carn Dûm. They're tough things with a grand bit of meat on 'em.

'You want to eat, and I want to cook! So we got a bit of a good thing happening here. Go out there and kill the slugs and bring me their meat.''Get out there and get our dinner, cur!''Go out there are get some tasty, chewy slug-meat so I can make us some gruel!''These'll do nicely. Firm and fresh. Time'll come soon enough to mash the meat up and make it into something edible.''You sluggard! You should have brought this to the cook, Gukthor! I've a good mind to give your hide to the slave mines in Angmar!'Meet the Masters of Minas Tirith.Meet the Masters of Minas Tirith.Meet Carethon, Master WrightMeet Aglarang, Master SmithMeet Habdir, Master ClothierMeet Bariel, Master HostellerMeet Curugond, Master BuilderMeet Lenglír, Master ArtistMeet Sarnion, Master ArchivistMazauk, a grizzled Warg of unknown years, pledges to join the battle against the enemy should you provide his den with the meat of his hated enemy, the Morningthaw-bears.Morningthaw-bears can be found throughout the Ettenmoors.

Mazauk directed you to get meat from the Morningthaw bears.'You trespass where you are not welcome, ${PLAYER}. I shall allow this, for I know you mean to cull the enemy from our home, and I shall even pledge my bite to your effort for recompense.

'Long has my pack struggled to oust the Morningthaw-bears beyond the borders of the Misty Mountains. Long have we battled them and sometimes won. With the arrival of the Elves, the bears drove us back and flocked to their side. My pack came to your leaders and chose to work with them in service to Lugbúrz. I will order my pack to slaughter in Angmar's name, and now, I ask that you slaughter to sate my hunger.

'I want meat. Meat from the Morningthaw. Deliver me enough to sate the hunger of all my years, and I will drive the enemy from that tower by your side.''My hunger dies a little with every swallow, so sweet is the taste of revenge. They shall pay more than they know for their intrusion into these lands.

'Come ${PLAYER}! Let us tear the throats from the enemy and slake our thirst now with their blood!'Harnion wishes to assess the might of the Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown before engaging in a fully-fledged battle.The road to Tarlang's Crown can be found to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas.

Harnion has asked you to patrol the road into Tarlang's Crown in hopes of discovering more of the Heirs' plans and their numbers.Patrol the roadway into Tarlang's CrownThe road to Tarlang's Crown can be found to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas.

