You have encountered the Dead in Tarlang's Crown. You should continue patrolling the road and learn more of the Heirs' plans and numbers.Patrol deeper into Tarlang's CrownHarnion can be found along the road through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas.

You have explored as far as you dare to for now, and should now return to Harnion.Talk to Harnion'It is good that you have come, ${PLAYER}. I have heard much of your deeds in Gondor thus far, and I hope you are willing to aid us once more.

'One of the Heirs of Castamir has assembled a substantial force in Tarlang's Crown. We do not yet know to what end, but it is clear that it cannot be for the good of Gondor. Based on what we have learned from Steward Malthellam and the others, we know this Man is in league with the Corsairs and the Dead, but we are not sure if his alliances end there.

'If you would gather your allies and make for Tarlang's Crown, any information you can provide us on their numbers and plans would be most helpful! And I urge you, my friend... do not go alone.''The Corsairs, the Dead, and now this strange rumbling... I fear we know even less of the Heirs' plans than we thought.

'We cannot allow them more time to ready their forces, ${PLAYER}. It is time we bring the fight to them!'Fearing there is yet more to lose beyond their homes, Amrúngal begs you to help guard the heirlooms of the people of Ethillorn.Heirlooms can be found throughout the ruins of Ethillorn in western Lower Lebennin.

You have discovered heirlooms uncovered by the Corsairs in Ethillorn. You should gather them and bring them to Sarnhad until Ethillorn is reclaimed.Recover Gondorian heirlooms from Ethillorn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A cache can be found near one of the homes in Sarnhad in western Lower Lebennin.

You have gathered all of the heirlooms you could find and should now store them in Sarnhad until Ethillorn can be reclaimed.Store the heirlooms in a cache at SarnhadErianir can be found in Sarnhad in western Lower Lebennin.

You have stored the heirlooms and should inform Erianir of what you have done for the people of Ethillorn.Talk to Erianir'Much has been lost to the Corsairs, ${PLAYER}. Life, land, and now our memories...

'I care far more for the lives of my folk here in Ethillorn, but I know many who would be grateful if their family heirlooms survived this horror as well. Search the town and the Corsairs' ships... if you can find anything of note, return it to the people of Sarnhad. They are hale, trustworthy folk and could look after them until we can reclaim Ethillorn.

'I am glad you are here to aid us, my friend... I shall try to escape once you have thrown the Corsairs into disarray, a-ha!''You have done a noble thing, ${PLAYER}. We shall ensure that no harm comes to their belongings, even if we are forced from our homes as well.'Lost Gondorian relics from the Second Age lie scattered and forgotten beneath the ruins of Osgiliath.Lost Gondorian relics from the second age lie scattered and forgotten beneath the ruins of Osgiliath.Lost Gondorian relics from the second age lie scattered and forgotten beneath the ruins of Osgiliath.Find Gondorian relics of the Second AgeCorsairs of Umbar have seized the coastline of Lebennin and seek to pillage and destroy each coast-town until they reach Pelargir.Corsairs can be found in the ruins of Ethillorn to the south of Linhir in Lower Lebennin.

