You tell Beregond that you appreciate his words and explain that you are here to give orders from Ormatar.

'All in a day's work, I suppose. Is it true that you are a friend of Peregrin Took? He is a friend of mine as well!

'You must come with me to Merethrond. You should see the grand feast-hall of Minas Tirith as it is truly a sight to behold. Also, I would very much like to hear all about your adventures with Peregrin Took! Meet me in Merethrond when you are ready.''This feast-hall is quite spectacular, is it not?''Please let me hear a story, and then we shall get started with this task.'

You recount a story about your time with Pippin in Rivendell.

'What a fantastic tale! I wish Peregrin were here right now. I bet he'd have some bits to add. I do enjoy the way he tells stories. Well, enough from me, shall we complete this task?''Thank you kindly for the plates. As you can see, there are not many of us down here. We appreciate any help.

'If you have a moment, we were just discussing the best way to defeat those Easterlings we keep hearing about. You look like a skilled warrior. Perhaps you would be able to show us a move or two? We would love to learn how to take them on if they ever got into the kitchen.'

You gladly accept to give them a demonstration of your combat skills.'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You make even a simple chore an adventure. No wonder you are also friends with Peregrin.

'That was nice of you to teach the kitchen staff some basic fighting skills. It brought some joy to their tired faces. It saddens me to think that tomorrow they may have to put that knowledge to practical use on the battlefield.'Discover the Fellow-halls of Minas Tirith.Discover the Fellow-halls of Minas Tirith.Discover the Artists' Fellow-hallDiscover the Builders' Fellow-hallDiscover the Burgsmen's Fellow-hallDiscover the Clothiers' Fellow-hallDiscover the Foodmongers' Fellow-hallDiscover the Hostellers' Fellow-hallDiscover the Smiths' Fellow-hallDiscover The Black HouseDiscover The Fair HallDiscover the Wrights' Fellow-hallSomeone has posted a task to collect clipped ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire clipped ears.Wanted: Clipped Ears from the Old Anórien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Old Anórien.Wanted: Clipped Ears from the Old Anórien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect damaged claws. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire damaged claws.Wanted: Damaged Claws from the Old Anórien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Old Anórien.Wanted: Damaged Claws from the Old Anórien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect pitted sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire pitted sword sheaths.Wanted: Pitted Sword Sheaths from the Old Anórien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Old Anórien.Wanted: Pitted Sword Sheaths from the Old Anórien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect shining carapaces. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire shining carapaces.Wanted: Shining Carapaces from the Old Anórien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Old Anórien.Wanted: Shining Carapaces from the Old Anórien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect thickened goo. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire thickened goo.Wanted: Thickened Goo from the Old Anórien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Old Anórien.Wanted: Thickened Goo from the Old Anórien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect torn skins. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire torn skins.Wanted: Torn Skins from the Old Anórien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Old Anórien.Wanted: Torn Skins from the Old Anórien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The battle raging in the Ettenmoors demands more resources than can easily be acquired, and the dwarves called to the mines in the north are here to do their work.Tyrfing is at the small encampment of the Free Peoples outside the western entrance to the Isendeep.

Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn directed you to safely escort Tyrfing and his miners into the mine so they can return to mining the ore needed for the battle in the Ettenmoors.Escort Tyrfing into the Isendeep'The iron in this place will not mine itself, my friend. We have need of your assistance in getting our workers back into the depths.

'Outside of the western entrance of this mine is a small encampment of Free Peoples. There you will find Tyrfing, the mine's foreman. He needs you to lead him into the mine. Once here, he and his fellows will begin their work again in earnest.

'Be swift, ${PLAYER}. We need the ore.''Move swiftly. If we encounter danger, my men will fight, but we are not true warriors. You've been warned, friend.'Men of Umbar defile the river Gilrain with their filth, leaving only polluted water for those who dwell in Linhir.Corsair-filth can be found along the shores of the Gilrain to the north of Linhir.

Erchar has asked you to clear the Corsairs' filth from the Gilrain before it can pollute more of Linhir's water.Clear Corsair-filth from the river Gilrain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Corsairs polluting the Gilrain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Erchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have cleared the river of filth and should now return to Erchar.Talk to Erchar in Linhir'Have you looked upon the water of the Gilrain as of late, ${PLAYER}?

'It has grown foul and thick with the filth of the Corsairs, and soon it will be nearly impossible to imbibe it. Some of their number must still lurk among the trees to the north and have a mind to poison us!

'Clear their filth from the river and drive them from our lands. For aiding me such a vile task, I shall see you well-rewarded.''Thank you, my friend, for the waters already look clearer.

'I shall ask my men to barrel more of the Gilrain's waters should the Corsairs think to defile them more in the coming days of war.'You returned to Artamir's camp, but the Gondorian man is missing. What happened to him?Artamir never returned to his camp, and you have resolved to fight the Orcs and search for any clue the creatures may have to his location.Defeat Orcs in the Dead Marshes, and remain alert for clues to Artamir's locationArtamir never returned to his camp, and you have resolved to fight the Orcs and search for any clue the creatures may have to his location.You found an Orkish map with one location encircled in blood. You should return to Artamir's camp to see if the Gondorian man has returned, but if he has not, you may have learned the next place to search for the missing man.Return to Artamir's camp to see if the Gondorian man has returnedArtamir has still not returned to his camp, but you found an Orkish map with a location encircled in blood. Perhaps this will give some clue to the Gondorian man's location.

Check Artamir's bedroll to ensure it was not slept in while you were away, and then you can depart for the location on the map.Check Artamir's bedroll to ensure it was not slept in while you were away, and then find the location circled on the mapYou rescued Artamir from a sad end in the Dead Marshes, and should speak to him back at his camp.You examine Artamir's bedroll, but it has not been slept in for some time. It is possible the Gondorian man will return, but as you peer into the distance and see the inhospitable swamp-lands extending to the horizon in all directions, you fear that some trouble has befallen him. There are many threats in this place, from the treacherous terrain to the searching Orcs, and any might have claimed the life of poor Artamir.

If the Gondorian has blundered into a sinkhole, there is little you could do to save him, but if he has run afoul of Orcs there may be some sign to find. You resolve to defeat Orcs in search of such a clue, if clues there are to be found.Artamir's bedroll has not been slept in for some time. It is possible the Gondorian man will return, but as you peer into the distance and see the inhospitable swamp-lands extending to the horizon in all directions, you fear that some trouble has befallen him. There are many threats in this place, from the treacherous terrain to the searching Orcs, and any might have claimed the life of poor Artamir.

If the Gondorian has blundered into a sinkhole, there is little you could do to save him, but if he has run afoul of Orcs there may be some sign to find. You resolve to defeat Orcs in search of such a clue, if clues there are to be found.Artamir's bedroll has not been slept in for some time. It is possible the Gondorian man will return, but as you peer into the distance and see the inhospitable swamp-lands extending to the horizon in all directions, you fear that some trouble has befallen him. There are many threats in this place, from the treacherous terrain to the searching Orcs, and any might have claimed the life of poor Artamir.

If the Gondorian has blundered into a sinkhole, there is little you could do to save him, but if he has run afoul of Orcs there may be some sign to find. You resolve to defeat Orcs in search of such a clue, if clues there are to be found.The bedroll remained undisturbed while you were away. Artamir never returned to his camp.

There is nothing else to be done save to travel to the location circled on the Orkish map you recovered. Perhaps a clue to Artamir's fate can be found at that location.'I cannot thank you enough for the timely rescue, ${PLAYER}! I peered into the water and really thought I saw... well, it does not matter now. If Steward Denethor truly did see the Banner of the King flying high against the night sky, perhaps it does not tell what he supposed. I think King Ondoher's banner perished in the marshes, when the King fell.

'Do you want to know something curious, ${PLAYER}? King Ondoher was not alone when the Wainriders of the East drove him to his death. He was accompanied on his final journey by two of his sons, and they perished with him, perhaps in these very marshes. The names of these sons were Faramir, and, well... Artamir.'

He laughs wryly.

'Were it not for your help, ${PLAYER}, I would have met my end in the same foetid swamp that claimed my namesake! I will find no honour when I return to the White City without the prize I sought, but I will still have my life, and that is more than enough for Artamir son of Ilcamir! You have my thanks and that of my family. I will leave these miserable marshes, and at once!'In the crags to the west of the Isendeep, the Shadowmaw pack bolsters the forces of Angmar.The Shadowmaw stalk the Steps of Gram.

Lieutenant Octa at the Isendeep Mine asked you to reduce the threat posed by the Shadowmaw-wargs.Defeat Shadowmaw-wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lieutenant Octa is at the Isendeep Mine.

Lieutenant Octa will be pleased to learn that you have succeeded at destroying a good number of the Wargs in the Steps of Gram.Return to Lieutenant Octa at the Isendeep Mine'In the west, in the shadow of Mount Gram, a pack of Wargs with a vile and dark bite roams freely and stalks out towards our holdings. These Wargs, the Shadowmaw, are responsible for many attacks on our number.

'We must find a way to cull their number. If you are willing, travel west and cut them down. Strike a telling blow against this foe lest their danger grow over time.''You will find that the Shadowmaw are drawn to the Steps of Gram. Be cautious when travelling through that land. It teems with the forces of Angmar and is perpetually cast in shadow.''While the battle rages there is no rest from the foes that we face, but for the moment we are spared. Take this reward, ${PLAYER}.

'In time, you will learn that these shall earn you great wealth. Seek out Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig to learn more.'Hoping to put an end to the raids into Blackroot Vale, Melril seeks to hunt sneaking Corsairs and recover what they have stolen.Corsair cutthroats can be found lurking in and around the Corsair encampment in Tarlang's Crown.

Melril has asked you to defeat Corsairs before they can sneak into Blackroot Vale and recover more crates stolen from Sardol.Defeat Corsair cutthroats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect supply crates in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Melril can be found at the northern end of Tarlang's Crown in Blackroot Vale.

You defeated many of the Corsair cutthroats and recovered several supply crates. You should deliver this news and the crates to Melril.'The time has come to put an end to these Corsair raids into the vale, ${PLAYER}.

'If they think us so weak or blind to all that has been stolen from us, they are sorely mistaken! Some of the Corsairs lurk in the shadows along the roadway, even past their barricades... their arrogance will be their undoing, I am sure of it!

'I would ask that you hunt them down, and take back what was stolen from us.''Now then, ${PLAYER}, I believe they shall think twice before making another raid into Blackroot Vale.

'We are hardy folk and will not see the fruits of our labours stolen away by some unkempt Men!'Rathon has been tasked with maintaining many of the cisterns in Minas Tirith by himself and has come to find piles of muck spreading through the cisterns.Piles of muck can be found within the cisterns.

You should remove piles of muck from the cisterns.Remove piles of muck from the cisterns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Rathon.Speak with Rathon'Upon my last walk through the cisterns, I noticed some strange piles of muck. Some of the mountainous cave-lizards have ventured into the cisterns recently and I believe they may be causing a mess in there. If you're already going into the cisterns, perhaps you would be inclined to clean up some of this filth? It would put me at ease to not get any of this muck into the city's drinking supply.''Once again, I thank you for your assistance. The cisterns were not always like this, you know. Beasts did not wander freely underneath the city. Hopefully, we can work together to return the tunnels to just the sound of running water.'Lord Forlong sits in the Merry Swan, drinking with his old friends Lord Hirluin and one Neldir of Minas Tirith. The conversation turns to matters close at hand and dear to heart.The Third Circle wall can be accessed via staircase, near to the Merry Swan.

