'Hunt the Orcs and Uruks throughout the Ettenmoors and gather barrels of oil. Bring it to me, so that we can boil it for use in the cauldron. Go quickly.''Excellent work, friend. This will serve us well. We shall get about the forging of the cauldron as soon as we have all the materials we need. Then we shall prepare for the Enemy.'Lugazag is in need of stronger defences. In order to build a significant defence, the Captain-General has ordered that a great cauldron of iron be forged and filled with oil.Enemies throughout the Ettenmoors carry stolen barrels of oil.

Sergeant-at-Arms Kolr received orders to forge a great iron cauldron to fill with oil. This cauldron will be used to defend the walls of Lugazag from the Enemy. He has asked you to recover the stolen barrels of oil which are in the possession of the Enemy.'I've orders from the Captain-General that need following, friend. You look the type of ${RACE} that knows well how to follow them, so I find myself here asking you to undertake a simple, though possibly dangerous task that needs doing and quickly.

