 a reward suitable for a collector in Central Gondor.Wanted: Pitted Sword Sheaths from the Central Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect shattered hatchets. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire shattered hatchets.Wanted: Shattered Hatchets from the Central Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Central Gondor.Wanted: Shattered Hatchets from the Central Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect shining carapaces. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire shining carapaces.Wanted: Shining Carapaces from the Central Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Central Gondor.Wanted: Shining Carapaces from the Central Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect torn skins. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire torn skins.Wanted: Torn Skins from the Central Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Central Gondor.Wanted: Torn Skins from the Central Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The people of Lebennin have learned much about how to gather hearty fish from the rivers that carve through their lands.Pike can be found by fishing off the low docks in Pelargir.

Firiondur has asked you to gather pike from the waters of Pelargir for the people displaced by the war.Catch pike in the waters of Pelargir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Firiondur can be found inside the lighthouse at Aerthir in southern-central Lebennin.

You have caught several pike and should now bring them to Firiondur.Deliver the fish to Firiondur in Aerthir'Refugees of Pelargir, like myself, have placed a great burden on our kinsmen. You see, in wartime we have all struggled to keep ourselves well-fed and... being pushed from Pelargir, we can no longer fish from its rich bounty.

'Pelargir is dangerous even now, my friend, but I bet a ${CLASS} of your skill could reach the lower docks unharmed. If you could bring us even a few fish, it would help my fellows and I make it through another night.

'I cannot offer much in return, but I shall give what I can.''I shall get to work right away to prepare these fish for my folk.

'You have done us a great service, my friend.'Dulglok commands you to kill those pesky hendrevail that keep diving at Orcs.Hendrevail can be found on the eastern side of Osgiliath.

You should defeat the pesky hendrevail.Defeat frenzied hendrevail (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have slaughtered many hendrevail in eastern Osgiliath.Completed'These hendrevail keep diving at my troops! These pesky birds are causing a lot of frustration!

'Take care of them. I don't care how, just get rid of them! Still don't get it? Kill those birds!'You have slaughtered many hendrevail and now the Orcs won't keep thinking they're getting attacked by filthy Men archers.Corsair looters are plundering the bank.The looters must be stopped.Defeat looters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Battle in the Ettenmoors is uncertain, with forces losing footholds as easily as they gain them. The Free Peoples have taken Tol Ascarnen but now must hold the location. To do this, they will need to strengthen their position as best they can.Leafcull Huorns can be found in the Grimwood Forest, south-west of Tol Ascarnen.

Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith has asked you to assist her in crafting a horn to call forces to fight against Angmar's army when they assail Tol Ascarnen. To complete the stand, she needs a heartwood from the Leafcull Huorns. She suggests you take allies, for the Huorns are a dangerous foe.'A moment if you will, ${PLAYER}. Captain-General Makan has bid me craft a horn to call our allies to battle when they are needed. I am in need of able-bodied heroes to assist me in this task.

'To the south-west, in the Grimwood Forest near the edge of the tall hills sheltering these lands from the Trollshaws, are the Leafcull Huorns. These twisted and malevolent creature lost their way long ago and have turned to corruption.

'This does not lessen the strength of their heartwood. I need one such heartwood to craft the Horn of Tol Ascarnen. If you would, head to the south with allies and collect a heartwood for me. This service will be remembered.''Take heart, ${PLAYER}. We will soon raise the horn and be prepared against our enemy. We will call allies to our side with this, the Horn of Tol Ascarnen.'There is much to see within the walls of the White City.There is much to see within the walls of the White City.Complete: Explorer of the White CityComplete: The Statues of Minas TirithUglash provided you with a barrel of poison and a directive. Make your way to the waterfall overlooking the fortress Tol Ascarnen and empty the barrel into the water. With enough poison, you may force the enemy to leave the wood.The source of the Hoardale is at the waterfall overlooking Tol Ascarnen.

Uglash sent you to poison the enemy's water source.Uglash awaits your return at Gramsfoot.

You climbed to the top of the falls and poisoned the waters of the Hoardale. You should return to Uglash with the news.Return to Uglash at Gramsfoot'My time is better spent speaking to something with a spine. You'll likely wilt as a flower in the face of the dangers in this land, whelp! Still... you stand before me. Perhaps I should order you to cower and wait to be given a task.

'Very well. I shall quicken your death or return you to the slave pits in Carn Dûm, ${RACE}. Take this barrel. It is filled with poison from the spider-keepers of Angmar. Mordirith is specific in his orders. All that stand against this army must perish.

'We will poison the Hoardale River and slaughter all who are made weak by the poison. Take the barrel to the waterfall that overlooks Tol Ascarnen at the centre of the Ettenmoors and dump the poison into the river. Fail me, and I will flay your flesh open to let the rats consume your innards... but I will see that you live to feel the pain. Succeed... I will see you are not made to labour in the slave pits of Carn Dûm a while longer.''I am almost impressed with what you have done, ${RACE}. You might one day prove a fine conscript in this army. I shall take great satisfaction when I grind my boots on your corpse as we scale the walls of the târk cities!'Fearing a renewed Haradrim force in Lebennin and Lossarnach, Irodon hopes to put an end to the Haradrim's efforts to expand the Crossings of Erui.Haradrim woodworkers and their bridge-rafts can be found along the banks of the Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.

Irodon has asked you to cripple the efforts of the Haradrim to expand the Crossings of Erui.Defeat Haradrim woodworkers near the Erui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn bridge-rafts near the Erui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Irodon can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have defeated many of the Haradrim woodworkers and burned their bridge-rafts.Talk to Irodon'After the Haradrim left Halach during one of their raids, I followed some of their forces... at quite a distance, mind you.

'I saw them encamped along the banks of the Erui and a few among them had set to work on crafting crude bridge-rafts. The Crossings of Erui are wide indeed, but these men seemed to be preparing the way for an invasion. If their forces could cross the entire southern span of the Erui, the people of Lebennin, Lossarnach, and even the White City would be indefensible.

'I ask that you burn their bridge-rafts and slay the woodworkers who crafted them before they can be used to any vile end.''As much I wish the Haradrim gone from our lands, I would gladly keep them from returning to their cruel masters in the East.

'You have done well to slow their advance even further, my friend. Let us hope that this delay leaves their plans undone!'Melril of Sardol fears for all in the vale who have gone into Tarlang's Crown, and worries that the Corsairs have begun to take prisoners.Prisoners from Blackroot Vale can likely be found near the northern end of Tarlang's Crown.

Melril has asked you to search for prisoners in Tarlang's Crown after finding that more people have gone missing from Blackroot Vale.Search for prisoners in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Melril can be found at the northern end of Tarlang's Crown in Blackroot Vale.

You searched for prisoners in Tarlang's Crown, but only discovered the remains of people of Gondor scattered about their camps. You should speak to Melril.Talk to Melril'I know you are no stranger to the troubles we face in the vale, ${PLAYER}. It is for that reason I come to you with this matter....

'More of our hunters have gone missing and it is clear they were taken by force. I fear they have been taken as prisoners in Tarlang's Crown for being so bold as to draw a bow against those that would lay claim to our lands.

'When the time comes, we shall need all who can fight to stand against these foes. Go into the Crown and seek them out... I only hope they still live.''I feared this would be the case, ${PLAYER}....

'I thank you for finding them, but it shall not lessen the blow to their families. I will send one of our number to inform them all of what has happened.

'Know this... I intend to see the Corsairs pay for what they have done to us!'Discover Gondorian settlements in West Gondor.Discover Gondorian settlements in West Gondor.Discover MorladDiscover LothgobelDiscover DínadabDiscover CalembelDiscover TadrentDiscover Ost LontirDiscover Dol AmrothYou and Tolwin notice that Orcs are starting to cut down Talath Anor's wooded lands. This destruction to beauty must be stopped.Mordor loggers can be found on the edge of Talath Anor's woods.

You should defeat Mordor loggers.Defeat Mordor loggers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Tolwin.Speak with Tolwin'Look over to the edge of the woods. Do you see the Orcs cutting down the beautiful woods of Talath Anor?!

'We must stop them. They have destroyed so much of this land, the farms, the orchard. We can not let them take the forests as well!''We did it! I'm so glad that we were able to save the trees from being turned into machines of war. I hope to take walks here with my children when I am older. That sounds nice.'Cangoras asks for your assistance in gathering materials to help patch worn armour for the Gondorian soldiers within Osgiliath.River Turtles can be found along the Anduin in Osgiliath.

You should collect River Turtle shells.Collect shells from River Turtles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cangoras is at the Palace of Eldacar.

You should bring the Turtle Shells to Cangoras.Bring the Turtle Shells to Cangoras at the Palace of Eldacar'This battle is weakening some of our soldier's armour. With the holes I've seen in some of the armour, a blade in just the right spot could be fatal.

'There are turtles around the Anduin with very tough shells. Collect some of these shells and I'll have my best smith patch up the armour. We cannot afford these soldiers to fall on the battlefield on account of their clothes!''I shall bring these shells to the smith. Great work soldier. You've no doubt saved a life or two with your efforts.'Corsairs are looting the weapons and armour within the armoury.The looters must be defeated.Defeat looters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Umbarrim in Tarlang's Crown enjoy the strength of the Black Númenóreans, a line long-assumed to have vanished from Middle-earth.The Umbarrim can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown, especially in the central camp.

You have encountered the Umbarrim and should defeat them, lest their might be used against Gondor.Defeat Umbarrim in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many Umbarrim in Tarlang's Crown.CompletedWhile battling against the forces in Tarlang's Crown, you have encountered the Umbarrim. These hale Men seemingly possess Black Númenórean-blood, and stand taller than the other Corsairs that serve under Azruthor.

Unless they are defeated, such strength could be devastating to the people of Gondor.You have defeated many of the Umbarrim in Tarlang's Crown. While not all of their number have been slain, you have slowed their advance into the Anfalas and protected the lands surrounding the Crown.Well-aware that the Corsairs that fled from Linhir will surely return once more, Garvir hopes to hunt them down before they can bring their plans to bear.The Corsairs have likely fled into the hills to the north of Linhir.

Garvir has asked you to seek out the Corsairs that fled during the recent attack on Linhir.Search for the Corsairs that fled LinhirGarvir's scout can be found somewhere within Hata Khezrat in Dor-en-Ernil.

You have discovered the Corsair encampment and should now seek out Garvir's scout.Search the camp-site for Garvir's missing scoutGorroch can be found in Hata Khezrat in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have found Garvir's scout and should now free him from his bonds.Gorroch can be found in Hata Khezrat to the north and slightly east of Linhir.

You have freed Gorroch from his bonds and should now speak to him.Talk to Gorroch'The Corsairs that fled from the battle continue to trouble me, ${PLAYER}. We cannot be certain where they have gone and every moment they elude us gives them more time to ready a new assault.

'When we scattered from Linhir, I saw a great number of them run to the north... yet I do not know if that was even a large part of their forces.

'I would ask that you seek the Corsairs to the north. If they have truly rallied there, we will need to act swiftly to keep them from renewing their attack.''I thank you for your aid, my friend, but I do not think I am quite ready to leave just yet....

'I was sent here to discover their plans, but all I have heard thus far are drunken ramblings and tales of the Dead at Linhir.

'If you seek to aid Linhir, I beg your aid once more.'Complete quests in Belfalas.Complete quests in Belfalas.Complete quests in BelfalasComplete quests in Blackroot Vale.Complete quests in Blackroot Vale.Complete quests in Blackroot ValeThere is much to do while travelling through the lands of Central Gondor.There is much to do while travelling through the lands of Central Gondor.Complete Quests of Ringló Vale DeedComplete Quests of Dor-en-Ernil DeedComplete Quests of Lebennin DeedComplete Central Gondor's Roaming Enemies DeedComplete Vanguard of Central Gondor DeedComplete quests in Dor-en-Ernil.Complete quests in Dor-en-Ernil.Complete quests in Dor-en-ErnilThere is much to do while travelling through the lands of Eastern Gondor.There is much to do while travelling through the lands of Eastern Gondor.Complete Quests of Lossarnach DeedComplete Quests of Osgiliath DeedComplete Quests of Southern Ithilien DeedComplete Quests of Upper Lebennin DeedComplete Eastern Gondor's Roaming Enemies DeedComplete quests in Lamedon.Complete quests in Lamedon.Complete quests in LamedonComplete quests in Lebennin.Complete quests in Lebennin.Complete quests in LebenninComplete quests in Lossarnach.Complete quests in Lossarnach.Complete quests in LossarnachComplete quests in Minas Tirith.Complete quests in Minas Tirith.Complete quests in Minas TirithThere is much to do while travelling through the lands of Old Anórien.There is much to do while travelling through the lands of Old Anórien.Complete Quests of Minas Tirith DeedComplete Quests of Pelennor DeedComplete Quests of Talath Anor DeedComplete Old Anórien's Roaming Enemies DeedComplete quests in Osgiliath.Complete quests in Osgiliath.Complete quests in OsgiliathComplete quests in Pelennor.Complete quests in Pelennor.Complete quests in PelennorComplete quests in Ringló Vale.Complete quests in Ringló Vale.Complete quests in Ringló ValeComplete quests in Southern Ithilien.Complete quests in Southern Ithilien.Complete quests in Southern IthilienComplete quests in Talath Anor.Complete quests in Talath Anor.Complete quests in Talath AnorComplete quests in Tarlang's Crown.Complete quests in Tarlang's Crown.Complete quests in Tarlang's CrownComplete quests in Upper Lebennin.Complete quests in Upper Lebennin.Complete quests in Upper LebenninThere is much to do while travelling through the lands of West Gondor.There is much to do while travelling through the lands of West Gondor.Complete Quests of Lamedon DeedComplete Quests of Belfalas DeedComplete Quests of Blackroot Vale DeedComplete Quests of Tarlang's Crown DeedComplete West Gondor's Roaming Enemies DeedThe Sisters of Lebennin seek to calm their Sister's fury before it consumes both the Enemy and the people of Gondor alike.Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

Roamingstar has rallied her Sisters and is now prepared to confront the Lone Lady. You should speak to her when you are ready.Talk to Roamingstar, Maiden of GilrainAngbor can be found on a hill to the west of the Crossings of Erui.

You have aided Roamingstar and her Sisters in calming the Lone Lady's rage, and have also recovered pieces of Castamir's armour. You should bring the armour to Angbor near the Crossings of Erui.Lady Terenis can be found in the Great Hall of Tumladen.

You have delivered Castamir's armour to Angbor, and should now speak to Lady Terenis.Talk to Lady Terenis in Tumladen'The Lone Lady...

'She has always been the most distant of my Sisters, but I never sensed such darkness within her. Only a great sadness... a sadness she has carried with her for many of your years. She never spoke much to us... never even speaking of her true name, but I wish she had come to us with her troubles. We have all seen horrors in the long years we have spent in these lands - she must know that she does not stand alone!

'The Men of Lebennin fought brother against brother and spilled much blood in her waters, but now you say the southern Men that seek to cross her waters are met by rotting suits of armour? I fear she will not be calmed easily, but my Sisters and I must reach her somehow.

'Travel to the Crossings of Erui... for it is there that my Sisters and I shall meet you. We shall put an end to this, no matter what action must be taken!''We will do what we must, ${PLAYER}. Are you prepared?''What is this armour you lay before me? An ornate piece despite such age and wear... it can be none other than the armour worn by the Usurper himself!

'As much as I wish to trust your words, I cannot fathom these tales you tell of the Five Sisters... they are naught but fables told to the young. Yet, the river has held close a relic of our bloody history, and I would not dishonour our people by ignoring such a find!

'I shall send this armour to Lord Sirgon and see it returned to Pelargir until this war comes to an end. Perhaps the Lady would like to hear more of your tale, but I can tarry no longer in Lebennin.''You speak of unbelievable things, ${PLAYER}, but you assure me that my people are safe, so I shall hold your words to be true.

'This Glassiel you spoke of in Halach, she seems to be a most interesting woman and one whom I would like to speak with in time. Ah, but such things are for another day...

'I have one last thing to ask of you, my friend.'The Grimwood forest covering most of Hithlad is home to a lumber-yard established by a race of small, tasty folk. The rat-folk dwell far away from the lumber-yard, but the enemy is there now. What is worse, an Elf stands at the head of the enemy's army.The Grimwood Lumber-yard is at the heart of the Grimwood Forest.

Soldier Bagfra directed you to find your way to the Grimwood Lumber-yard and destroy the Elf-lord in charge of the enemy forces there.Defeat Captain-General Bordagor and claim the Grimwood Lumber-yard. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls'South across the river and east into the dark depths of the Grimwood, you will find a lumber-yard. We happened upon this yard a while ago, and it was devoid of any sign of enemy, but the small houses left behind were made by the rat-folk far to the south.

'The forest is ripe for harvesting, and the lumber-yard still functions. We must take this location back from the enemy, lest they continue to make their bows and arrows to garner strength for their number.

'We will also strike a blow against their leadership as an Elf stands against us at the lumber-yard.''Make your way into the centre of the Grimwood and slaughter the Elf who leads the enemy at the Grimwood lumber-yard.'Captain-General Harvestgain is the leader of the Free Peoples at Lugazag.Captain-General Harvestgain, a târk, leads the forces within Lugazag.

Soldier Súmtharb made it clear that the only objective is to strike down the enemy's leader.Defeat Captain-General Harvestgain and claim Lugazag. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls'${RACE}! Your brethren failed us. Lugazag, our tower here in the west, has fallen to the hands of a târk! We must make our way to the tower and slaughter the forces standing watch.

'Do this, and I might think more of you than a maggot, ripe for smashing. Fail me, and I will see you posted to the slave pits of Carn Dûm!''You best be back to tell me you've followed your orders, sluggard! Else I'll throttle you and put you on a cart bound for the muck beneath Mordirith's throne!

'Get out there and slaughter the Captain-General at Lugazag!'Attempts to weaken the enemy forces are proving fruitful, and the keep east of Tírith Rhaw, where the Elf Captain-General Lainedhel rules, is the target of assault. You are charged with organizing a war-band to assault Ost Ringdyr in an effort to slaughter the lord of the keep.Ost Ringdyr is far to east beyond the Hoardale River and Tírith Rhaw.

Task-master Krul directed you to make your way to Ost Ringdyr to slaughter the lord of the keep.Defeat Captain-General Lainedhel at Ost Ringdyr. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General fallsTask-master Krul is at Gramsfoot.

After storming the walls of Ost Ringdyr, you fought through the enemy and defeated the leader of the keep. You should return to Task-master Krul with news of his defeat.'Ost Ringdyr is a thorn, ${PLAYER}. A place we can penetrate and nearly destroy, but one we cannot hold for any true time. Like us, the enemy is entrenched deeply at their camp of Glân Vraig, and Ost Ringdyr is simply too close to hold the keep.

'We can, however, slaughter their numbers and kill the master of the keep. This is what I ask of you, ${RACE}: go to Ost Ringdyr and kill the lord who commands the enemy there. Do this and you will earn favour with Angmar and Lugbúrz.''Do not test me, ${PLAYER}. Seek the Captain-General of Ost Ringdyr, and do not return to me until he is dead!''A day of victory for Angmar and Lugbúrz! This victory shall echo through the moors and mountains.

'You have earned the favour of the Great Eye, ${PLAYER}.'The ancient keep Tol Ascarnen was once home to the Witch-king of Angmar as he returned to Mordor after facing the armies of Glorfindel in the north. The keep long lay in ruins, but still it holds majesty for the minions of Mordirith. You are tasked with assembling a force to liberate the holding from the dwarf who now calls the place home.Tol Ascarnen sits on an island in the centre of the Hoardale River.

You have been tasked with finding and slaughtering the dwarf-leader who now stands in command of Tol Ascarnen.Defeat Captain-General Mákan and claim Tol Ascarnen. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls'Stand fast, worm. There is a task that needs doing, and your blood will stain the ground as well as any others.

'Where the Hoardale splits the battlefield, there is a keep. It was there that the Witch-king of Angmar stopped to give strength to the betrayers before returning to the Great Eye's service in Mordor!

'The keep is now in control of the enemy, and a dwarf stands as the head of the forces watching over the keep! You are charged with the recovery of the keep and return of it to the rightful holders!''Stop wasting time! Get your feeble innards out on the field of battle and earn your glory or die in the attempt!

'Go now, to Tol Ascarnen and face down the dwarf there!'A dwarf patrols the streets of Hoarhallow, defending the rat-folk. End him.Hoarhallow is south of Gramsfoot.

Soldier Dalgumthak directed you to Hoarhallow to kill the dwarf-lord in power there.Defeat Captain-General Meldún'Look lively, you sack of filth! I've no time for chatter, only time for killing!

'The Snowreap-goblins in Arador's End sent scouts to us with news that Meldún, a dwarf who defended the Isendeep moved to Hoarhallow!

'Get down there and tear the dwarf's beard off his face before you gut him like a Nimwaith!''Get out there and slaughter that dwarf, you piss-ant! I'm not here to see you dally behind the safety of these walls! I will flay your hide and hang it from the walls of this fort if I must!

'To Hoarhallow... slaughter the dwarf Captain-General.'Târks control the tower on the eastern front of the battlefield in the Ettenmoors. The tower, Tírith Rhaw, is held by the Captain-General Verdantine and must be crushed for Angmar's Army to drive the enemy to the precipice of destruction.Captain-General Verdantine is at Tírith Rhaw, far to the east and south, beyond the Hoardale River.

Soldier Dahámab directed you to gather others and lay siege to the tower Tírith Rhaw in an effort to kill the leader of the forces there.Defeat Captain-General Verdantine and claim Tírith Rhaw. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls'You miserable cur! You lack ferocity or strength in your arms to face down a troll and ask me to find something for you to do? Best thing I can find for you involves mixing that pile of dung into that stew for the goblins!

'I've something you might yet prove yourself useful for. Far to the east, beyond the Hoardale River and Tol Ascarnen, there is a tower: Tírith Rhaw. We want to take the tower, but a force lead by the târk, Verdantine, stands in our way.

'If we gain that post, we'll give ourselves a position to launch more direct assaults on their camp and keep. Get some more of these worthless maggots about to help you take down the târk! Win this battle, and we'll feast on man-flesh in your honour! Fail... and we'll still feast on flesh and in your honour.''You maggot! Get to the east and Tírith Rhaw. Slaughter that târk! For the glory of Mordirith, Angmar, and Lugbúrz!'Within the depths of the Grimwood, beneath a great stone shelter west of the Grimwood Lumber-yard is the lair of a terrifying spider, Gorgoris. She is a terrible threat to the Free Peoples.Gorgoris, the brood-queen of the Grimfang, dwells somewhere within the Grimwood forest in Hithlad.

First Marshal Núrdram asked you to find the brood-queen of the Grimfang and destroy her.First Marshal Núrdram awaits your return within the Grimwood Lumber-yard.

You found and destroyed Gorgoris, the Grimfang brood-queen.Speak with First Marshal Núrdram at the Grimwood Lumber-yard'A moment, ${PLAYER}. I am troubled by this wood -- not surprising given the corruption long seeping into the world -- but there is something more. Since our arrival, I have felt a sense of encroaching dread.

'To the west, there are a host of spiders stalking through the woods. I believe that the brood-mother may have returned to their home.

'If this is true, we must move at once to destroy her, lest Angmar's army convinces her to join the battle against us.''Seek out the brood-queen west of our camp and destroy her before Angmar's army draws her into the battle against us.''With Gorgoris defeated, the brood will not be drawn into the battle against us. We may be able to stand against this foe for some time now.

'Take this with my thanks and seek out Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig.'Taskmaster Bárzqhosh wants you to ensure that the threat posed by the eagles and their leader, Golloval, is diminshed. He has ordered you to gather a great number and assail the eagle-lord at his eyrie in Arador's End.Golloval can be found south of the mine in an eagle-eyrie.

Taskmaster Bárzqhosh tasked you with finding and slaughtering the eagle, Golloval.Taskmaster Bárzqhosh awaits your return outside the Isendeep Mine.

Golloval found his end at your will. You should return to Taskmaster Bárzqhosh with the news.Return to Taskmaster Bárzqhosh at the Isendeep Mine'Goblins will aid us in this place, and this is good. Mining is for such lowly races.

'It is the place of warriors, like you, to seize moments and become great! We are vulnerable -- I fear assault at the hands of the eagles who are not far from here.

'The greatest among them, Golloval, is a lord of the sky, and it falls to you and others to bring him at last to the ground!''Do not fail, or this mine will fall into the hands of the enemy, and you will suffer in the slave-pits of Carn Dûm.''A threat such as this will not last. I have word that even as he fell and you left him to rot, that the eagle-lord took to the sky again.

'He will return, but we have earned a reprieve by your will!'The Hardened enemies of Central Gondor have banded together to stand off against those who oppose them.The Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor asks you to band together and vanquish the Roving Threats of Central Gondor.Speak to the Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central GondorThe Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor can be found in Central Gondor.

You should speak with the Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor.Speak to the Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor'This is a dire situation. The Hardened enemies of Central Gondor have banded together to stand off against those who oppose them. Many have fought these Roving Threats alone but together their strength is unequalled. Call upon your allies to vanquish this assemblance of evil before we are all in danger.''Now is the time to fight!''You have done a great deed to all on Central Gondor. You shall be remembered by many Gondorians from this day forward.'The Hardened enemies of Central Gondor have banded together to stand off against those who oppose them.Push the Orkish forces further into the mountain.Defeat AbrakhòrDefeat AnbúrzDefeat Du-kalonDefeat GundashDefeat KeterangDefeat LuruyakDefeat RenderDefeat RipperDefeat Scythe-jawA powerful Orc warrior, the Tyrant Barashish has taken command of Tírith Rhaw. Sergeant-at-Arms Hesten has enlisted your talents in removing the Orc from the tower.The Tyrant Barashish is at Tírith Rhaw, north of Glân Vraig, in the centre of the Coldfells.

Sergeant-at-Arms Hesten at Glân Vraig directed you to seek out and defeat the Orc Tyrant, Barashish who holds command at Tírith Rhaw.Defeat Tyrant Barashish and reclaim Tírith Rhaw. You must not be defeated when the tyrant fallsSergeant-at-Arms Hesten awaits your return at Glân Vraig.

You defeated the Tyrant Barashish to reclaim Tírith Rhaw. You should return to Sergeant-at-Arms Hesten with the news.Speak with Sergeant Hesten'The Orcs proved strong enough to overwhelm our forces in Tírith Rhaw. Now a fell foe has taken control of the tower. We must muster our forces and drive them from that place at once.

'Gather a force together and make your way north into the Coldfells. Tírith Rhaw stands overlooking the valley to the west. You must enter and defeat the master of the Ongbúrz at this location.

'Seek out the Tyrant Barashish at Tírith Rhaw and defeat him. Fight with honour and return the tower to our control.''We must retake Tírith Rhaw. Make your way to the tower, north of this location, in the centre of the Coldfells. Defeat the Tyrant Barashish, then return to me.''You did well, ${PLAYER}. We need to continue our efforts in driving these Orcs from the Ettenmoors. Take this and know that you are well-thanked for your efforts.

'Seek out Quartermaster Ash in Glân Vraig to retrieve your greatest rewards.'A great leader of the Ongbúrz, Tyrant Durgrat, is holed up in Dâr-gazag, far to the west.Dâr-gazag, built on the ruins of a Rhudauran citadel, lay far to the west of Ost Ringdyr, across the Hoardale River. Make your way to the fortress and defeat War-master Durgrat at this location.

Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent directed you to kill the Uruk-warmaster Durgrat at Dâr-gazag.Kill Tyrant Durgrat at Dâr-gazag. You must not be defeated when the tyrant fallsSergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent awaits your return at Glân Vraig.

Facing down the Enemy, you destroyed the War-master at Dâr-gazag. You should return to Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent with the news.Speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent at Glân Vraig'We face an organized tribe of Orcs here, ${CLASS}. We will need the assistance of all capable peoples to defeat these foes.

'Scouts, reporting from the deepest parts of the front, have discovered that the leader of this war-host resides at Dâr-gazag, an encampment built on the ruins of an ancient Rhudauran fortress, far to the west of Ost Ringdyr.

'I am authorized to present you with much acclaim if you assist in defeating this war-master. Be cautious as the enemy is strong at this fortress. You will need a great number to overwhelm their forces and defeat the War-tyrant, Durgrat.''You will find the War-tyrant in the upper reaches of Dâr-gazag. Make your way there and defeat him and his war-host. Return here when the deed is done.''Durgrat's defeat is a great one, but he will return. His forces will not allow his defeat to influence them for long.

'We have earned a brief respite from their assaults thanks to you, ${PLAYER}, but we must not rest on these successes.'Lugazag, a tower far to the west of Glân Vraig, is held by the Ongbúrz Orc-tribe and commanded by the Tyrant Tharbil.Lugazag looks east out over the Hoardale River.

Once Lugazag was a great tower, part of the Rhudauran kingdom. Now, in the corrupt lands of the Steps of Gram, the tower stands as a location controlled by the Ongbúrz tribe and their Tyrant, Tharbil. Sergeant-at-Arms Hesten at Glân Vraig directed you to seek out and defeat the Tyrant Tharbil who holds command at Lugazag.Defeat Tyrant Tharbil and claim Lugazag. You must not be defeated when the tyrant fallsSergeant-at-Arms Hesten awaits your return at Glân Vraig.

You defeated Tyrant Tharbil with the help of others to reclaim Tírith Rhaw. You should return to Sergeant-at-Arms Hesten and tell him of your victory over Tharbil.Speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Hesten at Glân Vraig'Lugazag is a tower claimed wholly by the Enemy. If we are to tame this battlefield and control it for the cause of the Free Peoples, we must overwhelm their position and defeat their leader.

'With the head of the tower removed their forces will sunder, and we shall win the day. Take heart and seek the aid of many.

'Journey to the west beneath the shadow of Mount Gram in the Steps of Gram and siege Lugazag. Drive within its heart and defeat the leader of the Ongbúrz there, the Tyrant Tharbil. Do this, and you will earn great honour.''We must defeat these curs. Make your way to the tower, north and west of Glân Vraig in the Steps of Gram, defeat the Tyrant Tharbil, and return to me.''You did well, ${PLAYER}. Take this with our thanks and seek out Quartermaster Ash here to lay claim to the rewards which await you.'Tol Ascarnen has fallen to the Enemy. You have been tasked by Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent at Glân Vraig to find and defeat Tyrant Trintrû within the walls of Tol Ascarnen.Tol Ascarnen, once the citadel responsible for the manufacture and storage of Rhudauran weapons and armour, lay to the north and west of Glân Vraig.

Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent directed you to kill Tyrant Trintrû at Tol Ascarnen.Defeat Tyrant Trintrû and reclaim Tol Ascarnen. You must not be defeated when the tyrant fallsSergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent awaits your return at Glân Vraig.

Facing down the enemy, you destroyed the Tyrant at Tol Ascarnen. You should return to Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent with the news.Speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent at Glân Vraig'Captain-General Mákan wishes to retake Tol Ascarnen, and we are enlisting all who are able to take the fight to the Hoardale and defeat the Uruk in charge of the Ongbúrz war-host.

'North and west of Glân Vraig lay the Hoardale and on an island in the centre of the river is Tol Ascarnen. Make your way there and defeat the tyrant and his war-host.

'Return to me when you have done this. Do not be fool-headed, this is not a mission for one or a handful. You will need a great many to best this foe.''You will find the tyrant in the upper reaches of Tol Ascarnen. Make your way there and defeat him. Only then can Captain-General Mákan retake Tol Ascarnen and secure this most important location.''You have scored a great victory for the Free Peoples, ${PLAYER}. We honour your accomplishment and duty, but also warn that we cannot relent in our battle against the Enemy.

'If we do not remain resolute, the Enemy will drive south and swallow this land in war.'The severed heads of numerous slain Gondorians have been hurled over the walls of Minas Tirith. The warriors and inhabitants of Gondor alike shall soon fall to despair unless the Enemy's vile design is undone.

