Garvir has asked you to aid in repairing the defences of Linhir before the Corsairs and Haradrim can rally against the settlement once more.Repair damaged barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Warriors of Linhir can be found outside Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

Garvir has asked you to rally warriors that fled when Aragorn and the Grey Host passed through Linhir.Garvir can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have readied the defences of Linhir and rallied the frightened Men who abandoned their posts. You should now speak to Garvir.Talk to Garvir'Allow me a moment to turn my mind from my brothers, ${PLAYER}. The recent battle in Linhir was brought to an abrupt end by the arrival of Aragorn and the Grey Host. Corsairs, Haradrim, and my fellow Gondorians alike threw down their arms and fled at the sight of them. I saw only Angbor standing amidst the tumult, but now he too has gone from these lands....

'It was a battle half-fought, and one that is bound to be finished. Our barricades are in ruin and many of our men are scattered still. If you would aid us in restoring our defences, I would be most grateful.

'Let us hope the Grey Host has left us for good... I doubt any of us could bear such terror a second time.''I thank you for your aid, ${PLAYER}. Fearful as we all were at the sight of the Dead, I do not think it long before the Corsairs and Haradrim return to our gates once more.

'Now that our defences are prepared and the men again hold their posts, I believe us ready for the coming battle.'Patrol the Ettenmoors in search of the Enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the Ettenmoors for 60 minutes'Trolls have been called from the north. We must redouble our efforts, else the Free Peoples here will fall, and Angmar will flood Eriador through the Trollshaws. Steel your nerve, brother, and know that the hero who stands at your post will not fail us.'Patrol the Ettenmoors in search of the Enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the Ettenmoors'Trolls have been called from the north. We must redouble our efforts, else the Free Peoples here will fall, and Angmar will flood Eriador through the Trollshaws. Steel your nerve, brother, and know that the hero who stands at your post will not fail us.'Patrol the Ettenmoors in search of the Enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the Ettenmoors'Trolls have been called from the north. We must redouble our efforts, else the Free Peoples here will fall, and Angmar will flood Eriador through the Trollshaws. Steel your nerve, brother, and know that the hero who stands at your post will not fail us.'Patrol the Ettenmoors in search of the Enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the Ettenmoors'Trolls have been called from the north. We must redouble our efforts else the Free Peoples here will fall and Angmar will flood Eriador through the Trollshaws. Steel your nerve, brother, and know that the hero who stands at your post will not fail us.'Patrol the Ettenmoors in search of the Enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the Ettenmoors'Trolls have been called from the north. We must redouble our efforts, else the Free Peoples here will fall, and Angmar will flood Eriador through the Trollshaws. Steel your nerve, brother, and know that the hero who stands at your post will not fail us.'Patrol the Ettenmoors in search of the enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the Ettenmoors'Trolls have been called from the north. We must redouble our efforts, else the Free Peoples here will fall, and Angmar will flood Eriador through the Trollshaws. Steel your nerve, brother, and know that the hero who stands at your post will not fail us.'Someone has posted a task to collect clipped ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire clipped ears.Wanted: Clipped Ears from the Eastern Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Eastern Gondor.Wanted: Clipped Ears from the Eastern Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect clipped wings. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire clipped wings.Wanted: Clipped Wings from the Eastern Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Eastern Gondor.Wanted: Clipped Wings from the Eastern Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect damaged furs. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire damaged furs.Wanted: Damaged Furs from the Eastern Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Eastern Gondor.Wanted: Damaged Furs from the Eastern Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect pitted sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire pitted sword sheaths.Wanted: Pitted Sword Sheaths from the Eastern Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Eastern Gondor.Wanted: Pitted Sword Sheaths from the Eastern Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect shattered hatchets. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire shattered hatchets.Wanted: Shattered Hatchets from the Eastern Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Eastern Gondor.Wanted: Shattered Hatchets from the Eastern Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect torn skins. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire torn skins.Wanted: Torn Skins from the Eastern Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Eastern Gondor.Wanted: Torn Skins from the Eastern Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect toxic filth. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire toxic filth.Wanted: Toxic Filth from the Eastern Gondor region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Eastern Gondor.Wanted: Toxic Filth from the Eastern Gondor region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.In the wake of the Morgul-host's advance into western Osgiliath, many Gondorian weapons and armour pieces were left behind that might serve the Rangers of Ithilien in their defence.Undamaged blades and armour scraps might be found throughout the western half of Osgiliath.

Meldir has asked you to seek blades and armouring that were left behind when the Morgul-host broke through the western defences of Osgiliath.Collect undamaged blades in Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect armour scraps in Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Meldir can be found in the culverts of Osgiliath.

You have gathered many weapons and armour scraps and should now bring them to Meldir.'For many years, the Men of Gondor held the western half of the city against the ever-amassing forces in the East, but now... we are broken.

'They swept over us like the strongest currents of the Anduin and in the aftermath, the loss of life was immeasurable. Many still lie where they died, unless their heads have been taken by the Uruk-hai, but their armour and weapons still line the streets of Osgiliath.

'I do not wish their blades or armour to fall into the hands of the Enemy, for they would better serve us, even in the absence of the dead. Search the western streets and ways through the city, and return what you find to us here in the tunnels. Go with haste!''It is bittersweet, indeed. These blades were once held by men I considered brothers, but for those of us that yet live, they may still protect us from the Darkness.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Longing to raid once more, Jajax hopes to inspire the Corsairs to shed the rule of the Heirs of Castamir and revel in their mischief.Ale and treasure can be found scattered about Hata Kebir in south-eastern Lebennin.

Jajax has asked you to aid him in stealing ale and stolen treasures from the forces in Hata Kebir.Collect bottles of ale for Jajax (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Reclaim Corsair pillage for Jajax (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Jajax can be found at your side, or called with your horn.

You have gathered many bottles of ale and reclaimed much of the treasure stolen from the people of Lebennin. You should now speak to Jajax.'Look around at these men, ${PLAYER}... There was a time I might have called any of them my brother, but see how the excitement is gone from their eyes.

'These so-called Heirs... they steal the fun out of our mischief and treat their men as dogs. I wish to remind them what it truly means to be a Corsair, my friend, and they have been kind enough to gather so much of value here.

'Let us steal it all and drink to our victory!''Look at this haul, ${PLAYER}. You make a good Corsair, even if you do not think yourself one of us!

'I... suppose your honour might get in the way of me keeping this treasure, but you are a friend of mine, and I shall respect your ways since we fight side by side. I make no promises for the next time, though!

'All I ask is that you finish this ale with me, and you can return the treasure to the people of this land.'The Ettenmoors is home to many terrifying beasts, but the most frightening are the trolls. It is from here that the trolls pushed to infest the Trollshaws, and still many stalk through the wilds of the Ettenmoors.Snowreap-trolls are likely to be found in the northern stretches of Arador's End, near the Isendeep Mine. You may also find Coldeve stone-trolls, but they have been known to wander the entirety of the Ettenmoors.

After speaking to Lieutenant Osur, you were enlisted to assist in destroying the Snowreap and Coldeve-trolls.Defeat Snowreap-trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Coldeve-trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lieutenant Osur awaits news of your success at the Isendeep Mine.

You found and slaughtered the Coldeve and Snowreap-trolls as directed to by Lieutenant Osur. Now you should return to him with the news.Return to Lieutenant Osur at the Isendeep Mine'We know that there are trolls scattered throughout the north and certainly in service to Angmar. What we did not expect was the number of the trolls in service to the Snowreap-goblins, and worse, the Coldeve that roam the Ettenmoors.

'We need to do something about these beasts, lest they become a greater threat to us over time. Gather a fellowship of like-minded people and seek a way to destroy these deadly beasts.''You'll likely find the Snowreap in areas where you would find the goblins. The Coldeve may be a bit harder to locate. They migrate all throughout the Ettenmoors, from what we have seen.''Knowing that their number has been culled gives me reason to pause and reflect on my youth. I was once a brazen youth willing to face down such foes without concern. I envy the wild nature you possess, ${PLAYER}. It suits you well and is needed as this battle begins to progress.

'Here, take this, you should seek out Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig to claim your true prize.'Nimithil of Pelargir grows concerned for the people of Erynos after the sacking of Lornost and bids you travel to their aid in the east.Erynos can be found far to the east of Ost Anglebed near the confluence of the rivers Celos and Sirith.

Nimithil has asked you to travel to Erynos to learn if the people there are still safe from the Corsair occupation of Pelargir.Travel east to ErynosErynos can be found far to the east of Ost Anglebed near the confluence of the rivers Celos and Sirith.

You have discovered Erynos unharmed by the forces of the Enemy and should now speak to one of its inhabitants.Talk to someone in Erynos about the Corsair threat'Since the fall of Lornost, I have been unable to rest, and I fear for the settlement of Erynos.

'It lies far to the east beyond even Lornost, and its walls are not nearly as strong as those here. Few folk dwell there, and those that do are ill-equipped for battle. The settlement is shrouded by trees, so I can only hope the Corsairs have not yet moved against them.

'I would ask that you go to their aid, and help protect them from the Corsairs and Haradrim before it is too late.'It has been a strange day, traveller.

'We are not in need of aid, that much is certain. You must have seen the Corsairs on the road as you arrived, but none of us know what to make of it.'Fearing for his father's safety as well as his own, Faltharan has urged you follow him to the mountain refuge of Tumladen.Tumladen can be found in northern Upper Lebennin.

Faltharan has asked you to meet him in Tumladen in Upper Lebennin.Travel to Tumladen in Upper LebenninThe gate-warden can be found immediately outside Tumladen in northern Upper Lebennin.

You have arrived at Tumladen and have been sighted by one of the gate-wardens. You should speak to him before attempting to enter the refuge.Talk to the gate-ward of TumladenThe gate-warden can be found immediately outside Tumladen in northern Upper Lebennin.

The gate-warden of Tumladen has questioned your intent. You should kneel and declare your loyalty to the people of Gondor.Kneel before the gate-ward and swear your loyalty to GondorFaltharan can be found somewhere within Tumladen.

You have been granted entry to Tumladen and should now seek out Faltharan.Find Faltharan in Tumladen'With Pelargir in such ruin, Tumladen may well be the only shelter that still remains in Lebennin. While I long to look upon my wife and son again in Ost Anglebed, we have come too far to make such a journey.

'My father is in dire need of food and rest, and I too grow weary... for bearing this blade and armour so long has tired me greatly. I know you desire to rejoin Lord Angbor, but if you would meet me and my father in Tumladen, I can aid you in readying yourself for the journey ahead.

'The gate-wardens have been known to refuse outsiders during times of war, but if you mention my name, I am certain they shall let you pass.''What interest have you in Tumladen, traveller?'

You explain your adventures with Faltharan and Lord Sirgon and your desire to reunite with them.

'Ah, so that's it, then? Yes, the Lord and his son arrived quite recently, but how can I be certain of your intent?''Ah, ${PLAYER}, at last you have arrived!

'My father and I were beginning to worry that you were not coming after all.

'In our short time here, I have heard peculiar things, but there are more pressing matters at hand.'Aware of the Corsairs' desire to strike against Linhir once more, Gorroch hopes to discover their plans before they can be put in motion.Orders can be found in Hata Khezrat to the north and slightly east of Linhir.

Gorroch has asked you to recover orders from the Corsairs to aid the warriors of Dor-en-Ernil in preparing for a renewed assault on Linhir.Gorroch can be found in Hata Khezrat to the north and slightly east of Linhir.

You have recovered two pages of the Corsairs' orders and should now return them to Gorroch.The last page of orders can likely be found on a Corsair captain in Hata Khezrat.

Gorroch has asked you to seek one last page of orders from the Corsairs at Hata Khezrat.Search for the last page of the Corsairs' ordersThe orders can be found in your inventory.

You have skilfully taken the orders from a drunk Corsair and should now read them.Read the Corsair ordersGorroch can be found in Hata Khezrat to the north and slightly east of Linhir.

You have found and read the last of the Corsairs' orders, and should now tell Gorroch of what you have learned.'The Corsairs are planning a new attack against Linhir, ${PLAYER}. I suspect they are still sore from their shameful retreat from the Dead!

'That being so, I would ask that you seek their orders in this encampment. When we have learned all we are able to, I shall return to Linhir with our findings. You see, I do not wish to cause too much of a commotion here before the time is right.

'I am thankful that the Corsairs have their orders written down, for I doubt their slurred speech can ever be trusted. I shall keep my bonds loose and wait here, ${PLAYER}. Swiftly now - little time remains!''Bah!

'None of this is useful to us, ${PLAYER}! The battle these orders speak of at Linhir has come and gone, and the shores of Lebennin are already aflame.

'We need more current orders... something in response to their defeat at Linhir. I would wager that one of their captains holds the orders, but I do not know why he would not have shared them already.

'Seek out a captain here, my friend, and see if you cannot relieve him of his orders.''These are ill tidings, ${PLAYER}.

'If this was all that remained of their forces, I would be less concerned, but it is clear they have scattered since their defeat at Linhir. Some have gone further north along the river's edge, and others still have fled to the hills in the west to rally their numbers once more.

'We must work to keep them weakened, my friend.'The Corsairs have taken some of the swan-knights prisoner.The swan-knights must be rescued.Free swan-knights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison, is worried about the effect a group called the Withered Tree might be having on the morale of his soldiers.Parchments posted by the Withered Tree and despairing citizens who read their messages can be found throughout the First and Second Circles of the city.

Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison, has asked you to help raise the morale of the people of Minas Tirith in any way you can.Tear down Withered Tree posters in the lower Circles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Try to inspire despairing citizens in the lower Circles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Echadon is in the Second Circle of the city.

You have sought to raise the spirits of people in the lower Circles of the city.Talk to Echadon at the south end of the Second CircleEchadon is concerned about the morale of a group of his men on the north end of the Second Circle of the city.

A feeling of hopelessness has begun to spread throughout the city, and it has affected not just the common folk, but the men of the garrison as well.Find the group of unhappy guards Echadon mentioned, at the north end of the Second CircleCelonor looks especially worried and downcast.Talk to Celonor at the north end of the Second CircleCelonor and other men of the garrison are at the north end of the Second Circle, and need tales of courage to inspire them.Celonor and other men of the garrison are at the north end of the Second Circle, and need tales of courage to inspire them.Echadon is at the south end of the Second Circle of the city.

You have raised the spirits of Celonor and the other men of the garrison.Talk to Echadon at the south end of the Second Circle'Only a fool would deny that things look bleak for Gondor, ${PLAYER}. A group calling themselves 'The Withered Tree' has begun committing acts of cruelty and dissent within the streets of Minas Tirith, and their actions have lowered the morale of my men and the folk that remain.

'These lower Circles of the city are especially at risk of suffering at the hands of the Withered Tree; perhaps the pass-words for the upper levels remain out of reach, at least for now. If you would help raise the spirits of my guards and of the citizenry, you will tear down any seditious parchments the Withered Tree has posted upon the walls. While you do this task, speak to any despairing folk you find and try to lift their spirits. Hope may be in short supply, but even a little of it may go a long way during the trials we will face in the hours ahead.

'Confine your search to the First and Second Circles of the city, ${PLAYER}.''If you would help raise the spirits of my guards and of the citizenry, tear down any seditious parchments the Withered Tree has posted upon the walls in the First and Second Circles of the city. While you do this task, speak to any despairing folk you find and try to lift their spirits. Hope may be in short supply, but even a little of it may go a long way during the trials we will face in the hours ahead.''You have done well to inspire some of the common folk that listened to the lies of the Withered Tree. It is all too easy to listen to their whispers when there is little certainty that a new day will dawn tomorrow. We cannot listen, or we will give in to despair, and that only ensures that the dawn will be further off.

'Some men in the garrison have also begun to listen to these despairing whispers. Find them on the northern side of the city, in the Second Circle, and speak words of courage to inspire them to go on. Perhaps tales of your adventures will help, ${PLAYER}? Find them and stir their hearts to bravery, or they will be of no use to anyone in the battle to come!''Some men in the garrison have begun to listen to the whispers of the Withered Tree. Find them at the north end of the Second Circle, and speak words of courage to inspire them to go on. Perhaps tales of your adventures will help, ${PLAYER}? Find them and stir their hearts to bravery, or they will be of no use to anyone in the battle to come!''Some men in the garrison have also begun to listen to the whispers of the Withered Tree. Find them at the north end of the Second Circle, and speak words of courage to inspire them to go on. Perhaps tales of your adventures will help, ${PLAYER}? Find them and stir their hearts to bravery, or they will be of no use to anyone in the battle to come!''We heard the news from beyond the North-gate of the second Morgul-host, and I was watching with my own two eyes when the Prince of Dol Amroth came back to the city with Faramir. The young captain's face was as pale as death. His father the Steward lets none in to see him. He may have already died, for all we know!

'You are an adventurer, but I would wager you have never been in this grim a situation before. How can we hope to have victory? Nay, not even that. How can we hope to survive?''You are an adventurer, but I would wager you have never been in this grim a situation before. How can we hope to have victory? Nay, not even that. How can we hope to survive?''Can it be? Can we find such courage as this?

'I do not know, ${PLAYER}... but I know that we will try! We are men of Gondor! We will not give up hope... not now, and not ever! You have reminded us that even when the night is darkest, dawn must come at its ending, and will banish even blackest midnight.

'You have my thanks, adventurer, for the reminder that courage can be found, even when it is thought lost!''You have reminded us that even when the night is darkest, dawn must come at its ending, and will banish even blackest midnight. You have my thanks, adventurer, for the reminder that courage can be found, even when it is thought lost!''I thank you for inspiring my men to go on, at least for a little while. I must confess something to you, however. I myself am worried. This is going to get worse before it gets better.

'We will stand against it for as long as we can, will we not? We will. With adventurers such as you aiding in the defence, we may stand a little longer than we might, ${PLAYER}. I am glad for it.'Dol Amroth has been taken by corsairs. Select the area of the city you wish to retake then speak to the commander to begin.Before the operation can begin, you must select which area of the city you wish to retake.Speak to the soldiers and select your target buildingSpeak to the commander to begin the assault.Speak to the Commander to begin the assault'You know your orders. Let us retake Dol Amroth! To battle!'Easterlings have nearly destroyed Parth Duin, a farm east of Crithost. Tolwin is determined to show the Easterlings that they are not welcome in Talath Anor and asks you to give them this message.Parth Duin is located east of Crithost.

You should defeat Easterlings at this settlement.Defeat Sûhalar at Parth Duin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.

You should speak with Tolwin.Talk to Tolwin'Many Easterlings have started to gather in Parth Duin, east of here. I fear that they are grouping before marching south. Are you willing to confront them and drive them away from Talath Anor and Minas Tirith?''Good work. I look up to your skills in conflict. Perhaps one day I shall be as adept as you in the ways of fighting.'Easterlings have taken the northern Rammas and it is up to you to regain control of the Out-wall.Ingold can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas.

You should speak with Ingold and assist him with protecting the Rammas.Complete Quest: The North Rammas: SûhalarComplete Quest: The North Rammas: CaptainsComplete Quest: The North Rammas: SuppliesComplete Quest: The North Rammas: HooksComplete Quest: The North Rammas: BannersIngold can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas.

You should speak with Ingold.Speak with Ingold'A band of Easterlings have taken the Rammas over the Forant River! They must be defeated if we are to keep hold of the northern gate!

'Will you travel there and see this threat off the Out-wall?''Protect the Out-wall!''This is a mighty blow to these Easterling axe-men. They had better not try anything like that again or they shall surely meet the same fate!'Now that Dolgimil has been located, Aras calls upon you to infiltrate Dolgimil's stronghold at Barad Rill and stop him before he sends forces to Linhir.Barad Rill is located at the southern tip of Dor-en-Ernil.

Enter the stronghold at Barad Rill.Enter the stronghold at Barad RillDolgimil's lieutenants can be found in the stronghold at Barad Rill.

Defeat Dolgimil's lieutenants.Defeat Dolgimil's Corsair lieutenants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Dolgimil's Haradrim lieutenantDolgimil can be found somewhere in Barad Rill.

Summon and confront Dolgimil.Summon and confront Dolgimil at Barad RillAras can be found at encampment in western Dor-en-Ernil.

You should speak with Aras.Speak with Aras at Herion's encampmentHerion can be found at his encampment in western Dor-en-Ernil.

You should speak with Herion.Speak with Herion at his encampment'Dolgimil destroyed Barad Rill and now resides within its ruins. Go quick and silent into the stronghold and put an end to Dolgimil's plans.

'I know not how guarded Barad Rill is, but I trust that you will make it through.

'I shall return to Herion with haste. We will defeat nearby scouts in Dor-en-Ernil to stop any additional enforcements from arriving at Barad Rill. I wish you luck my friend.''It ends here, ${RACE}. I know not why you are in my presence and I do not care for it.

'The blood of Castamir runs through my brothers and I. This land is ours! I have claimed this once great beacon of Gondor as my throne. Look how easy it fell! Azruthor would have claimed Langstrand if it weren't for a band of warriors. I would very much like to kill those who took Azruthor's life.

'Azgarzôr and Balakhôr have their own thrones to claim. May Azgarzôr give me strength and Balakhôr guide me to victory!''Ah, ${PLAYER}, you have returned! You provided Gondor with light in these dark times. I am sure others will look up to you as much as I do now.

'While you were conquering the forces at Barad Rill, Aras and I managed to defeat a half-dozen scouts. A mere grain of sand next to your mountainous deeds. I suppose we all do our part in this conflict.

'We have dwelled here too long, my friend. The time has come to meet with my brother Erchar and return to Linhir.''${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. I am just about to head north to Erchar's encampment. I will give him the meeting place that Herion suggested.'

You ask where the meeting place is.

'I will let Herion tell you for it is not my place. We shall all return to Linhir together. For Gondor!'Many supplies went missing during the Battle at Pelargir, and Thandor has asked you to locate where they went.The stolen army supplies can be found in the abandoned district to the north-east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should reclaim the stolen supplies.Collect stolen supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Thandor.Talk to Thandor'After the battle, we noticed that some of our supply caches began to mysteriously dwindle. We traced this back to a group of ruffians who have taken up shelter in an abandoned part of the east-garth. I cannot tell you how many brave souls gave everything to protect this city, and this criminal element seeks to profit from it!

'We would ask you to bring back any supplies you might find from that place.''Well done ${PLAYER}. It might not seem much, but every bit will aid the war effort. We still need to gather much before we will be ready to march forward.

'Hopefully this sends a message to those thieves, and we can take inventory of what is available without worrying about anything else going missing.'Tolwin is worried about Orkish Warg-riders patrolling the northern fields of Talath Anor and wishes for you to deal with this threat upon Crithost.Warg-riders are located in northern Talath Anor.

You should defeat Warg-riders for the safety of Crithost.Defeat Warg-riders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.

You should speak with Tolwin.Talk to Tolwin'The look-out in Crithost's tower has spotted Warg-riding Orcs north of here. If you're heading towards Parth Lisc, perhaps you could defeat a few of these beasts. I fear for the safety of the town if they were to advance any closer.''Thank you. With your help, Crithost continues to be safe for these good people, myself included.'Battle in the Ettenmoors is uncertain, with forces losing footholds as easily as they gain them. The Free Peoples have taken Tol Ascarnen but now must hold the location. To do this, they will need to strengthen their position as best they can.Rockwithers can be found in Hithlad, south of Tol Ascarnen.

Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith has asked you to assist her in crafting a horn to call forces to fight against Angmar's army when they assail Tol Ascarnen. She needs the horn of the great aurochs Rockwithers to complete it. She suggests you take allies, for Rockwithers will be a formidable adversary.'You there, ${CLASS}. I have orders from the Captain-General that need attention, and I have heard that you are a noble adventurer, willing to do what must be done to ensure our victory. This is good. Listen well, for this is a matter of utmost importance.

'In the plains and wooded lands south across the bridge, you will find Hithlad. There, you will find many aurochs grazing and moving through the fields. You will likely find the great aurochs Rockwithers among their number. You will know him by his shaggy mane and extraordinary size.

'While I do not condone the slaughtering of wild animals without purpose, we have a need for this culling. Rockwithers' horns will serve as the centre of a great battle-horn which we shall use to alert our forces when Angmar's host attacks. Gather allies, for Rockwithers is said to be a tremendous beast, and return to me with his horn.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. I will set about fashioning this into a proper battle-horn. After we have collected the sinew and craft the stand, we will raise the Horn of Tol Ascarnen and prepare for Angmar's assault.

'You have done well.'After the events in the Nimrond caverns, Ringló Vale faces continued threats, including Corsair raiding parties from the south.Corsairs can be found in the southern woods of Ringló Vale.

You should defeat Corsairs.Defeat Corsairs in southern Ringló (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Candúr can be found in the village of Ethring.

You should speak with Candúr.Speak with the town guard'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you have returned to the Vale at a time when we could use someone with your skills. A look-out upon the beacon of Eilendoth has spotted a Corsair raiding party heading north. They recently went into the southern woods where we lost sight. Perhaps you would be able to head them off before they discover Ethring.''Ethring shall remain hidden from the conflict in the south thanks to your efforts in defeating the Corsair raiding party.'Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Defeat many Roving Threats throughout Middle-earth.Chief among the Scourge's warriors, Abrakhôr carries out the Scourge's will on the people of Lebennin who dare to defy his claim to the throne.Abrakhôr can be found somewhere in Lebennin.

Milonnen has asked you to track and defeat the Black Númenórean warrior, Abrakhôr.Find and defeat AbrakhôrMilonnen can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.

You have defeated the Black Númenórean, Abrakhôr, and should now report your success to Milonnen.Talk to Milonnen in Ost Anglebed'There is rumour of an unusually hardy man who aided in the sacking of Lornost.

'It is said that he is second only to the Scourge's brothers in might, and that he has been vital in laying claim to several settlements here and in Dor-en-Ernil.

'He must be stopped before he can rally more forces to his side and bring ruin to Ost Anglebed. We do not know where he is currently making camp, but he must still be within Lebennin.

'Go, ${PLAYER}, and may your pursuit be swift.''You have done us a great service, my friend. Let us hope that none as hardy as him still remain in the Scourge's forces.'Azruthor's forces venture out of Tarlang's Crown including Amorchant, whose lifeless corpse is controlled by The Dead.Amorchant can be found somewhere in Western Gondor.

You should defeat Amorchant.Defeat AmorchantAelnir can be found in the city of Dol Amroth.

You should speak with Aelnir.Speak with Aelnir'The Sorcerers of Umbar have called forth evil spirits to carry out their orders. Fell spirits under the command of Azruthor's forces have possessed the bodies of many slain beasts.

'One such beast was once a Mountain Drake, Amorchant. Now it is a twisted creature, not of the living. I have looked into the eye of this Fell-drake and only saw pain and suffering. Your aid would be appreciated in putting Amorchant to rest and taking it away from Tarlang's numbers.''What a sad, tortured beast. You did what had to be done. I am sure if any bit of Amorchant still lived in that defiled husk it would have thanked you for setting it free.

'I thank you for your efforts, especially these difficult ones.'The Half-troll, Anbúrz, has been sighted throughout Dor-en-Ernil and poses a constant threat to its people.Anbúrz can be found somewhere in Dor-en-Ernil.

Erchar has asked you to track and defeat the brutal Half-troll, Anbúrz.Find and defeat Anbúrz in Dor-en-ErnilErchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have defeated the Half-troll, Anbúrz, and should now return to Erchar.Talk to Erchar'My men have heard terrifying rumours of a great Half-troll known as Anbúrz in Dor-en-Ernil.

'It is said that he is strong enough to swing a man as one would swing a mace. I know not if such boasts can be true, but if they are, we have much to fear.

'We do not know where he has made camp this day, but I would ask that you gather your allies and seek him out. I shall await your safe return, my friend.''You have done a great thing in defeating that vicious Half-troll, ${PLAYER}. His bloodlust struck fear into many of our people, and they shall rest far easier with him gone.

'Thank you, my friend.'Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Ashthrok, who feels no pain from the deep fires.Ashthrok can be found somewhere in Angmar.

You should defeat Ashthrok.Defeat AshthrokCánnakh can be found in Aughaire.

You should speak with Cánnakh.Speak with Cánnakh'Have you been to The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu?

'Did you know that the deep fires imbue the evil creatures with unheard strengths? Ashthrok is one of these abominations. His feet melt sand! I shall continue my research on the why these creatures of The Rift have made their way to the surface. Be careful out there!''You have returned the Fire-troll to The Rift, have you?

'Thank you for your help. I am making progress on my research. It seems that there are many ancient stories about Angmar that have been passed down over the years.'Droghus, a Gauradan spirit-caller has allied with the Angmarim, in order to find a powerful artifact within the hills of Evendim.Droghus can be found somewhere in Evendim.

You should defeat Droghus.Defeat DroghusBrangil can be found in Tinnudir.

You should speak with Brangil.Speak with Brangil'The Gauredain across the lake are not our allies nor our greatest concern. However, the renewed threat in Annúminas has angered these mountain men. Their high chieftain, Droghus, commands their numbers. You must be careful though, he also has command over wolves as though he were a wolf himself.''We Rangers thank you for your efforts. May the mountain slopes once again be quiet and peaceful.'After the events in the Nimrond caverns, Ringló Vale faces continued threats, including Du-kalon, a Ruthless Dead who takes no pity on the living.Du-kalon can be found somewhere in Ringló Vale.

You should defeat Du-kalon.Defeat Du-kalonArvaethor is in the village of Ethring.

You should speak with Arvaethor.Speak with Arvaethor'This is a dire situation. A Ruthless Dead by the name of Du-kalon has ventured into this Vale. No one knows where he came from and I hear his strength is unequalled. He has begun to take notice from those who followed Drugât and Nerzus. I fear he may be able organize the Dead into the army that Drugât only envisioned.

'Call upon your allies to vanquish Du-kalon before we are all in danger.''We shall remember you for many years to come. The defeat of the mysterious Du-kalon is truly a heroic feat. It fears me to think what may have happened had he gained command of the Ruthless Dead lurking in Ringló Vale.'The corruption out of Angmar has angered and misguided many of the creatures in The North Downs, including Dúrlum, a disturbed spirit of Fornost.Dúrlum can be found somewhere in The North Downs.

You should defeat Dúrlum.Defeat DúrlumOthwen can be found in Esteldín.

You should speak with Othwen.Speak with Othwen'The enemy forces occupying Fornost have angered and corrupted even the dead. Recently a powerful shade has begun stalking the Fields. The Orcs must have been searching the deepest of tombs. Now even the Orcs are afraid of the one they call Dúrlum. This spirit must be put to rest.''You bring with you good news and hope that once again The North Downs will be a peaceful place. Thank you, brave ${RACE}.'Elite lieutenants of Dol Guldur have been seen patrolling the hostile region of Southern Mirkwood, including Ghámgur, a brutal warrior with a thirst for death.Ghámgur can be found somewhere in Southern Mirkwood.

You should defeat Ghámgur.Defeat GhámgurGellamiel can be found in Ost Galadh.

You should speak with Gellamiel.Speak with Gellamiel'Ghámgur, a powerful Gorthorog out of Dol Guldur stalks the hills and valleys of Mirkwood. His mission is unknown to us but perhaps he merely patrols to intimidate us. If you encounter this powerful foe, defeat him quickly.''The forces of Dol Guldur may outnumber us but our hope outshines all. You have done a great service for the Malledhrim.'Evil stirs in the Northern realm, including Gronkerna, who has become corrupted by the Guaredain over years of enslavement.Gronkerna can be found somewhere in Forochel.

You should defeat Gronkerna.Defeat GronkernaOstasänt can be found in Sûri-kylä.

You should speak with Ostasänt.Speak with Ostasänt'We Lossoth care for our Mammoths. They are a valuable creature for travel and protection from the Northern storms.

'The Gauredain do not hold the Mammoth in as high regard. They corrupt them, raise them with hatred.

'The largest of their Mammoths is Gronkerna. I warn you, this creature is deadly. Its rider can barely control the beast. Sadly this menace needs to be dealt with.''At last, Gronkerna can rest. That creature has endured a fate worse than death for far too long. No Lossoth would ever treat a Mammoth with such disregard as the Guaredain do. I hope that one day we shall put an end to the Guaredain's treachery in the North.'Beasts of various origins have been causing problems for the dwarves in the Misty Mountains, including Gróthurs, whose endless boulder hurling endangers all mountain explorers.Gróthurs can be found somewhere in The Misty Mountains.

You should defeat Gróthurs.Defeat GróthursAuthi can be found in Glóin's Camp in the Misty Mountains.

You should speak with Authi.Speak with Authi'Stone-giants have no respect for the mountains! They spend all day throwing boulders at each other while trees and animals are flattened and killed without their knowing!

'One particular giant, that we call Gróthurs, has made it impossible to venture through these mountains. Could you talk some sense into that imbecile?!''How does a dwarf relax when a boulder flies over a peak, right at him? Well, he doesn't!

'Finally, the infernal racket of that stone-giant can make way for the sounds of birds and wind. You have done well.'After driving the Orcs back into the Nimrond caverns, Ringló Vale faces continued threat as the Orkish forces once again amass in the foothills with new monstrosities among their ranks, including the giant cave-troll Gundash.Gundash can be found somewhere in Ringló Vale.

You should defeat Gundash.Defeat GundashLaerind is in the village of Ethring.

You should speak with Laerind.Speak with Laerind'When all is quiet you can make out the faint chanting of the Orcs gathering in the foothills. They have brought with them a monstrous beast who shakes the ground when he walks. Gundash the cave-troll is a menace that must be stopped. Will you defeat him for the Vale?''You have defeated the menacing Gundash! This is good news. If he made his way to Ethring, that beast would have surely pummeled our village into ruin.'Azruthor's forces venture out of Tarlang's Crown including Gundlag, whose lifeless corpse is controlled by The Dead.Gundlag can be found somewhere in Western Gondor.

You should defeat Gundlag.Defeat GundlagAelnir can be found in the city of Dol Amroth.

You should speak with Aelnir.Speak with Aelnir'The Sorcerers of Umbar have called forth evil spirits to carry out their orders. Fell spirits under the command of Azruthor's forces have possessed the bodies of many slain beasts.

'One such beast was once a cave-troll, Gundlag. Now it is a colossal creature, not of the living. This beast was a menace even before it was corrupted in death. This fell troll must be dealt with before it ventures out of the woods and into a town.''I am thankful to hear that the thundering footsteps of Gundlag shall not be heard again.

'I am not one to side with the likes of trolls, but no creature should be invaded by a fell spirit. It is an act of defilement. These Umbarrim will pay for their heinous deeds.'Azruthor's forces venture out of Tarlang's Crown including Haldalona, who seeks to corrupt Western Gondor's waters.Haldalona can be found somewhere in Western Gondor.

You should defeat Haldalona.Defeat HaldalonaAelnir can be found in the city of Dol Amroth.

You should speak with Aelnir.Speak with Aelnir'Not only do Azruthor's forces seek to corrupt our lands, but our waters as well!

'I have seen a darkness that stirs in the rivers. It is an ancient fell power, manifesting into a form known by some as Haldalona. This may be difficult for you to believe, but you must take my words as truth.

'The forces of Tarlang's Crown are beginning to spread into the rest of Western Gondor. I do hope that you will be able to stop Haldalona before our waters cease to carry fish or travellers.''You were able to defeat the Darkwater, Haldalona? I commend you for your bravery.

'Perhaps now the waters will flow freely and without the vile corruption caused by these ghastly spirits. I shall reward you well for your efforts.'Elite lieutenants of Dol Guldur have been seen patrolling the hostile region of Southern Mirkwood, including Helchurth, an eternal servant of the Nazgul.Helchurth can be found somewhere in Southern Mirkwood.

You should defeat Helchurth.Defeat HelchurthGellamiel can be found in Ost Galadh.

You should speak with Gellamiel.Speak with Gellamiel'I have seen black robes in the night, wandering with soundless footsteps. The Cargûls of Dol Guldur are equally sad and dangerous wraiths. Any ${RACE} should heed caution when encountering a Cargûl. This warning holds true to Helchurth, a truly terrifying minion of the enemy. Tread carefully or this apparition will trick you.''The forces of Dol Guldur may outnumber us but our hope outshines all. You have done a great service for the Malledhrim.'Beasts of various origins have been causing problems for the dwarves in the Misty Mountains, including Hrimdyr, who ambushes wary explorers on the high mountain pass.Hrimdyr can be found somewhere in The Misty Mountains.

You should defeat Hrimdyr.Defeat HrimdyrAuthi can be found in Glóin's Camp in the Misty Mountains.

You should speak with Authi.Speak with Authi'Some creatures in these mountains are quite dangerous, but none are as deadly as Hrimdyr.

'Hrimdyr may not be as strong as a giant, but it hunts from snowdrifts and in blinding snows. You never see the creature coming until it is too late!

'I could use your skills in dealing with this dangerous creature.''The Snow Beast is no more? Great news, my friend. This will indeed make travel through the mountains much safer. You shall be rewarded for your efforts.'The vile Haradrim sorcerer, Keterang, has been sighted throughout Dor-en-Ernil and poses a constant threat to its people.Keterang can be found somewhere in Dor-en-Ernil.

Erchar has asked you to track and defeat the cruel Haradrim sorcerer, Keterang.Find and defeat KeterangErchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have defeated the Haradrim sorcerer, Keterang, and should now return to Erchar.Talk to Erchar'I have heard tell of a mighty sorcerer named Keterang among the forces of the Haradrim in Dor-en-Ernil. It is said that he can conjure foul spirits from the very air... can such a thing be?

'His whereabout are unknown, but he cannot be allowed to rally more of the Enemy's forces to his side. I would ask that you seek him out and defeat him before he can rally his men against us.''You have dealt a great blow to the Haradrim in Dor-en-Ernil, ${PLAYER}.

'With this threat gone, it is my hope that our people will be safer in the days to come.'The forces of Harad have made their way to South Ithilien and Osgiliath, including Kethat-sai, a massive and deadly Mûmak.Kethat-sai can be found somewhere in South Ithilien or Osgiliath.

You should defeat Kethat-sai.Defeat Kethat-saiNanoth can be found in Bâr Húrin.

You should speak with Nanoth.Speak with Nanoth'The Haradrim are bringing powerful beasts known as Mûmakil up from the south to create the foundation of the Morgul-host. These tusked creatures are nearly impervious to our swords and arrows and Kethat-sai seems to be the largest and strongest of them. If you were able to somehow stop this beast from making it across the Anduin, we would be most indebted to you.''You have brought down Kethat-sai. When I am able I shall bring word to the Rangers in Osgiliath. They may rethink their plans with this threat taken care of. For the Moon-land!'Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Khruthakh, who scouts these lands for a lost power.Khruthakh can be found somewhere in Angmar.

You should defeat Khruthakh.Defeat KhruthakhCánnakh can be found in Aughaire.

You should speak with Cánnakh.Speak with Cánnakh'Khruthakh is most likely a Wight of sorts. This being may be under the control of Ulkharn or some other ancient evil dwelling in the depths of The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.

'This ancient armour, animated by the darkness of Nûrz Ghâshu searches for something. If we are looking for the same object, this creature should be dealt with soon! My research continues.''Another creature of the darkness falls. What I wouldn't give to study some of that ancient armour.

'I know, it is too much of a risk as the armour was most likely forged and corrupted by an ancient darkness. I would not want to corrupt myself in the process of studying those dark metals.'Beasts of various origins have been causing problems for the dwarves in the Misty Mountains, including Krabakam, an expert hunter from the North who seeks only the most difficult game.Krabakam can be found somewhere in The Misty Mountains.

You should defeat Krabakam.Defeat KrabakamAuthi can be found in Glóin's Camp in the Misty Mountains.

You should speak with Authi.Speak with Authi'I am not a hunter. If it weren't for my companions, I'd starve to death on these slopes.

'I saw a strange fellow when last I was out. Either he did not notice me or he was looking for something. He is a Gauradan and a hunter from the North. I am worried that the next time I venture onto the slopes, he may hunt me!

'Will you drive this Gauradan away so that I may continue my exploration of the Misty Mountains?''That Gauradan hunter from the North made me wonder of what else survives in these frozen wastes. As an explorer, I may have another expedition lined up after this one. Thank you for providing a safe route for those who travel through the Misty Mountains.'Evil stirs in the Northern realm, including Krevchal, who leads his Gauradan tribe on violent rampages around the ice bay.Krevchal can be found somewhere in Forochel.

You should defeat Krevchal.Defeat KrevchalOstasänt can be found in Sûri-kylä.

You should speak with Ostasänt.Speak with Ostasänt'The Gauradan Chieftain known as Krevchal, is on the move.

'His tribe has already murdered many Lossoth over the years. Now that he is out in the open, it is our time to strike.

'I wonder if his movements are connected to these foul winds from the East.''You have done a great deed for the Lossoth. Something dark angers the Gauradan spirits. May Sûri-kylä be spared or be able to defend itself. We shall be ever watchful.'After arriving with the forces at Hata Kebir, Luruyak has wandered Lebennin and sows destruction in his wake.Luruyak can be found somewhere in Lebennin.

Nimithil has asked you to track and defeat the Haradrim sorcerer, Luruyak.Find and defeat LuruyakNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.

You have defeated the Haradrim sorcerer, Luruyak, and should now report your success to Nimithil.Talk to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed'I have heard rumblings of a vile sorcerer of Harad who can call forth grim spirits.

'True or not, he might soon rally more to his cause and soon the Haradrim could find their morale bolstered.

'If you and your fellows can discover his whereabouts, I ask that you defeat him swiftly. Let us not allow him time to prove his claims!''I am glad to hear that Luruyak will trouble my people no longer, ${PLAYER}.

'Here, I have had a suitable reward prepared for you.'The forces of Harad have made their way to South Ithilien and Osgiliath, including Morgrish, a Half-troll who thirsts for battle.Morgrish can be found somewhere in South Ithilien or Osgiliath.

You should defeat Morgrish.Defeat MorgrishNanoth can be found in Bâr Húrin.

You should speak with Nanoth.Speak with Nanoth'A Half-troll captain called Morgrish has led a few of us Rangers to an early death. His strength is unmatched and he is skilled with a sword, overcoming any foe with his tactical finesse. I have often seen him travelling between Haradrim camps, most likely to train and muster soldiers. If you and your kinsmen were able to defeat Morgrish it would indeed strike a blow to the Haradrim forces gathered in South Ithilien and Osgiliath.''What news have you? Morgrish has been defeated? This Half-troll captain stood for strength within the Haradrim ranks. Though others will rise to take his place, Morgrish's defeat will set the Haradrim forces back long enough for us to strike. The Rangers are thankful of what you and your kinsmen were able to accomplish.'Azruthor's forces venture out of Tarlang's Crown including Mota, who seeks to destroy Western Gondor in Azruthor's name.Mota can be found somewhere in Western Gondor.

You should defeat Mota.Defeat MotaAelnir can be found in the city of Dol Amroth.

You should speak with Aelnir.Speak with Aelnir'Sorcerers from Umbar hold high rank in Azruthor's forces. It seems that one of their most powerful sorcerers has been sent out to cause destruction in Western Gondor. I fear he may just be a distraction for a much more devious plan. Either way, the Sorcerer Mota should be dealt with.

'I will continue to find out what Azruthor's forces are up to.''You look weary after your recent battle. May you rest well knowing the good you have done. The people of Western Gondor owe you much for your effects to halt the Eastward march of Azruthor's forces.

'I have been told that this Umbarrim man, Mota, leads this movement. This surely is a great blow to Azruthor's forces!'Evil stirs in the Northern realm, including Mustarka, who walks the frozen wastes with a murderous gaze, seeking lost treasures.Mustarka can be found somewhere in Forochel.

You should defeat Mustarka.Defeat MustarkaOstasänt can be found in Sûri-kylä.

You should speak with Ostasänt.Speak with Ostasänt'Something sinister stirs in my land. We Lossoth feel a foul wind blowing from the East.

'The winds brought with them a creature we call Mustarka. This terrifying Wight from Angmar disrupts the balance in my icy land. It searches for something, perhaps a treasure, and kills anything in its path.

'Will you help us to protect this cold North?''You say the Wight wore armour from Angmar? This is unsettling. The Lossoth are not prepared to fight what lies to the East. Even our best warriors are no match for the strange creatures from over the mountains that I have heard about. Perhaps having you around will keep the dark winds from blowing too far West.'The drake, Render, has come down from the White Mountains, striking greater fear into the already terrified people of Lebennin.Render can be found somewhere in Lebennin.

Milonnen has asked you to track and defeat the drake, Render.Find and defeat RenderMilonnen can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.

You have defeated the drake, Render, and should now report your success to Milonnen.Talk to Milonnen in Ost Anglebed'I have received word of a great drake that has come down from the mountains.

'It is said that he has preyed only on our goats so far, but such a beast is beyond our control and may soon bring further ruin to our lands.

'Seek him out and defeat him, ${PLAYER}, before he can set flame to any of our settlements that the Corsairs and Haradrim spared. A drake of his size should not be difficult to track....''You did well to cut down that drake, for his presence filled many of our folk with dread, ${PLAYER}.

'I am certain it was no simple task, so take this as your reward.'The drake, Ripper, has been sighted throughout Dor-en-Ernil and poses a constant threat to its people amidst the War.Ripper can be found somewhere in Dor-en-Ernil.

Herion has asked you to track and defeat the drake, Ripper.Find and defeat RipperHerion can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have defeated the drake, Ripper, and should now return to Herion.Talk to Herion'People have spoken of a great shadow passing overhead - a winged beast beneath the murk of the sky.

'Our scouts tell us it is a drake, and I would ask that you and your fellows hunt it down before it can bring any more ill-fortune to the people of Dor-en-Ernil.

'We have no idea where this... Ripper... has gone, but I would ask that you search swiftly. Go, my friend, for I shall have a great reward waiting for you.''Ripper was of great concern to us and you have my thanks for cutting him down. Our lands were besieged by many forces, and that drake only added to our many troubles.

'I shudder to think what may have happened had he set the vale ablaze. Thank you again, my friend.'The corruption out of Angmar has angered and misguided many of the creatures in The North Downs, including Rotspittle, a diseased mountain Drake.Rotspittle can be found somewhere in The North Downs.

You should defeat Rotspittle.Defeat RotspittleOthwen can be found in Esteldín.

You should speak with Othwen.Speak with Othwen'Have you seen the Drakes up in the mountains? If you leave them alone they usually won't trouble you. Lately things have changed. There are tales of a Drake who comes down from the Mountains, killing large animals and men! Though I wish it were not true, I have seen some of these corpses. The skin and hair has been burnt, not with fire, but with some sort of putrid poison! Is Angmar corrupting and defiling the mountain Drakes as well?! You must take care of this corrupted Drake before more innocent lives are taken.''You bring with you good news and hope that once again The North Downs will be a peaceful place. You have done a great service for the Free Peoples.'After the events in the Nimrond caverns, Ringló Vale faces continued threats, including Scythe-jaw, the Weft-mother's greatest spawn.Scythe-jaw can be found somewhere in Ringló Vale.

You should defeat Scythe-jaw.Defeat Scythe-jawCandúr can be found in the village of Ethring.

You should speak with Candúr.Speak with Candúr'I heard you were the one who defeated The Weft-mother. The people here have been talking about you. They need good stories to get them through these dark times.

'It is unfortunate that there are dreadful stories of a beastly spider of immense size stalking in the Vale. This so called Scythe-jaw fills the folks of Ethring with dread. I know the Vale owes you much thanks for your deeds. I hope that you can once again aid us.''We all owe you thanks for defeating Scythe-jaw before any more fell victim to its deadly bite.'Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Shakatrog, who will destroy anything in his path.Shakatrog can be found somewhere in Angmar.

You should defeat Shakatrog.Defeat ShakatrogCánnakh can be found in Aughaire.

You should speak with Cánnakh.Speak with Cánnakh'Gertheryg are ancient Trolls. I know you've dealt with Trolls before but prepare yourself if you haven't faced a Gorthorog.

'Shakatrog is a brutal creature. If he finds the ancient power before I do, he will certainly wield it for the will of Sauron. I shudder to think of such things. Please stop Shakatrog from his mission and I will continue to study my old maps and manuscripts.''That Gorthorog was a powerful enemy. I hope that your heroics have gone unnoticed by the enemy. They certainly have not gone unnoticed by me.

'I was discussing The Rift with an old friend and he mentioned that the forgotten city once covered much of the land. What ever we're looking for was most likely lost ages ago.'The forces of Morgul Vale have made their way to South Ithilien and Osgiliath, including Shardrágh, a great siege-beast from Minas Morgul.Shardrágh can be found somewhere in South Ithilien or Osgiliath.

You should defeat Shardrágh.Defeat ShardrághNanoth can be found in Bâr Húrin.

You should speak with Nanoth.Speak with Nanoth'Let me share with you information on Shardrágh. He is a massive Morgul-troll, as strong as the great beasts that pull the Morgul seige equipment to war. Shardrágh has been seen wandering South Ithilien then returning to Osgiliath. I am not certain to what this creature's mission is - perhaps he just awaits orders for the Morgul-host to continue its western assault. Something must be done about Shardrágh before he is able use his strength in battle over the days to come.''You have defeated Shardrágh?! You and your kinsmen have done a great service to the Rangers of Ithilien and the people of Gondor. I shall not forget your deeds.'Azruthor's forces venture out of Tarlang's Crown including Skorkaz, a Ruthless Dead with no remorse for the living.Skorkaz can be found somewhere in Western Gondor.

You should defeat Skorkaz.Defeat SkorkazAelnir can be found in the city of Dol Amroth.

You should speak with Aelnir.Speak with Aelnir'The forces in Tarlang's Crown work with the Ruthless Dead to gain control of Western Gondor. This I know.

'One of The Dead, known as Skorkaz, is of a particular concern to me. He wanders far from Erech, much farther than I have ever seen The Dead travel. I've not come across Skorkaz yet. I've only heard tale of his destruction from others. A farmer in Lamedon told me that he saw a dozen men slaughtered by this menace. Skorkaz strikes down his enemies with fear.

'It is hard to say if he is aligned with Tarlang's Crown at all considering his affliction for the living. Either way, Skorkaz is a threat that must be dealt with.''You live to tell the tale. May Skorkaz never trouble these lands again.

'We will never know if Skorkaz took commands from Azruthor or if he had his own agenda. Alas, I hope for one day when The Dead leave the Stone behind and no longer haunt these lands.'The nefarious forces of Angmar travel to Evendim in search of powerful artifacts, including Súnath, who commands forces within Annúminas.Súnath can be found somewhere in Evendim.

You should defeat Súnath.Defeat SúnathBrangil can be found in Tinnudir.

You should speak with Brangil.Speak with Brangil'A powerful Angmarim sorcerer has journeyed to Evendim. Perhaps he has come to lead an attack upon Annúminas? One thing is for certain: Súnath, this powerful man of Angmar, must be dealt with.''We Rangers thank you for your efforts. May we soon chase the last of the Angmarim out of Annúminas and reseal the city's ancient tombs.'Beasts of various origins have been causing problems for the dwarves in the Misty Mountains, including Sútmoth, who brings harsh weather in his wake that endangers any mountain explorer.Sútmoth can be found somewhere in The Misty Mountains.

You should defeat Sútmoth.Defeat SútmothAuthi can be found in Glóin's Camp in the Misty Mountains.

You should speak with Authi.Speak with Authi'The cold does not bother me too much my friend. However, some areas of the Misty Mountains seem colder still.

'At first I thought it was my imagination, but then I saw a creature of frost and cold. It was an ice-giant! If this beast is not dealt with, I will surely freeze to death and you will have to thaw me in the Forges of Khazad-dûm!''The camp-fire only provides so much warmth as I am sure you know.

'You have done a great service in defeating that frigid ice-giant. Now the Misty Mountains can remain cold instead of bitter cold.'The nefarious forces of Angmar travel to Evendim in search of powerful artifacts, including Tárlug, who knows only to serve the Angmarim's will.Tárlug can be found somewhere in Evendim.

You should defeat Tárlug.Defeat TárlugBrangil can be found in Tinnudir.

You should speak with Brangil.Speak with Brangil'The Angmarim have brought a massive Gorthorog to Evendim. Tárlug is completely loyal to the Angmarim. He will carry out any of their orders without hesitation. I believe that this beast is helping the Angmarim discover and plunder tombs. We must stop their efforts before any more powerful artifacts are unearthed.''We Rangers thank you for your efforts. May we soon chase the last of the Angmarim out of Annúminas and reseal the cities ancient tombs.'Elite lieutenants of Dol Guldur have been seen patrolling the hostile region of Southern Mirkwood, including Thorang, a spirit trapped within deadly armour.Thorang can be found somewhere in Southern Mirkwood.

You should defeat Thorang.Defeat ThorangGellamiel can be found in Ost Galadh.

You should speak with Gellamiel.Speak with Gellamiel'I have seen strange lights in the forest, like a storm in the night. There is a servant of Dol Guldur that wields lightning. This is no creature of the living but some sort of sorcery controlled armour. Thorang has no will of its own. It is a shell of evil-imbued metals controlled by ancient, dark magic. You must break the bond the animates this monstrosity.''The forces of Dol Guldur may outnumber us but our hope outshines all. You have done a great service for the Malledhrim.'Evil stirs in the Northern realm, including Ukko Surma, whose resurrected body seems to be controlled by another.Ukko Surma can be found somewhere in Forochel.

You should defeat Ukko Surma.Defeat Ukko SurmaOstasänt can be found in Sûri-kylä.

You should speak with Ostasänt.Speak with Ostasänt'An evil seeps through the ice like water running off a glacier in spring.

'I have seen a Giant wandering the frozen plains. You may not believe me, but it is not a creature of the living. His skin is decayed, frozen, and there is a strange glow around him! Could it be a Wight or perhaps something worse?

'My people need less to fear. Tales of this Giant they call Ukko Surma are already starting to spread.''This foul creature is no more? This is good news for all of Forochel.

'What is this you say? You believe that this Giant may have been controlled by some other mysterious force. The dark winds from the East must have something to do with this.'Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Ulkharn, who commands this evil for an unknown purpose.Ulkharn can be found somewhere in Angmar.

You should defeat Ulkharn.Defeat UlkharnCánnakh can be found in Aughaire.

You should speak with Cánnakh.Speak with Cánnakh'Regmyl are deadly. I am certainly not going near one! I shall leave it up to you if you want to seek out this particular Rogmul.

'Ulkharn seems to be leading the others who left The Rift, but for what purpose? My research continues.''The Rogmul has been defeated?! You are indeed an accomplished warrior!'

'I know not how long and deep the caverns under The Rift stretch. I can only speculate the many nameless foes still lurking down there. I shall continue my research.'The corruption out of Angmar has angered and misguided many of the creatures in The North Downs, including Valikas, whose temptation of Angmarim riches has blackened his heart.Valikas can be found somewhere in The North Downs.

You should defeat Valikas.Defeat ValikasOthwen can be found in Esteldín.

You should speak with Othwen.Speak with Othwen'Since some of the Earth-kin have sided with Angmar, their minds have slowly warped. One Earth-kin, called Valikas, walked an even darker path. He trained with the Angmarim and now seeks to corrupt his fellow Jorkyn to the ways of the Witch-king of Angmar. There is no path back to the light for Valikas. He must be dealt with.''You bring with you good news and hope that once again The North Downs will be a peaceful place. You have done a great service for the Free Peoples.'Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Vélnas, who seeks a lost power buried somewhere in these lands.Vélnas can be found somewhere in Angmar.

You should defeat Vélnas.Defeat VélnasCánnakh can be found in Aughaire.

You should speak with Cánnakh.Speak with Cánnakh'Vélnas is a creature of nameless evil from an age that time forgot. They say that this creature can look right through you and into your deepest, darkest fears.

'This seer of fear must be dealt with if we are to find this ancient power before anyone else. Are you up for the challenge?''A horrid creature such as this nameless abomination has no right to be walking above the ground. You have done much to hinder their efforts in locating this ancient power before I figure out where and what it is.

'I will continue to pour over these old stories and maps.'Powerful creatures have been seen patrolling the hostile region of Southern Mirkwood, including Woe-weaver, a poisonous giant spider.Woe-weaver can be found somewhere in Southern Mirkwood.

You should defeat Woe-weaver.Defeat Woe-weaverGellamiel can be found in Ost Galadh.

You should speak with Gellamiel.Speak with Gellamiel'More spiders have descended upon Mirkwood. They come from the direction of Dol Guldur. Of all we have encountered, Woe-weaver is the deadliest. Be careful, this giant spider can paralyze even the strongest warrior.''The forces of Dol Guldur may outnumber us but our hope outshines all. You have done a great service for the Malledhrim.'Authi requires assistance as The Misty Mountains are once again under threat.Authi can be found in Glóin's Camp.

You should speak with Authi.Speak with AuthiAuthi can be found in Glóin's Camp.

You should speak with Authi.Speak with AuthiIn your absence, new threats have come to The Misty Mountains. Authi, an explorer in Glóin's Camp, seeks assistance if he is ever to finish exploring the peaks and caverns of the Misty Mountains.'Greetings, I am Authi! You have come at a most fortuitous time.

'I am an explorer by trade, always looking for an interesting artifact or lost treasure. Unlike many dwarves I am happy exploring the highest peak as I am happy exploring the deepest depth. You look like you could assist me. My exploration of the Misty Mountains has been hindered by some creatures on the slopes. Will you help me out?'Strong enemies still roam in Angmar.Strong enemies still roam in Angmar.Complete Roving Threat: Khruthakh, the UntiringComplete Roving Threat: Shakatrog, the DreadedComplete Roving Threat: Vélnas, the SeerComplete Roving Threat: Ulkharn, the CommanderComplete Roving Threat: Ashthrok, the Fire SeekerComplete Epilogue: Amardam, the Ancient EvilStrong enemies still roam in Central Gondor.Strong enemies still roam in Central Gondor.Complete Roving Threat: Scythe-jaw, the Dread SpiderComplete Roving Threat: Gundash, the White Mountain MenaceComplete Roving Threat: Du-kalon, the Pitiless DeadComplete Roving Threat: Ripper, Bane of the Prince's LandsComplete Roving Threat: Anbúrz, Wielder of MenComplete Roving Threat: Keterang, Master of SpiritsComplete Roving Threat: Render, Shadow of the White MountainsComplete Roving Threat: Luruyak, Terror of HaradCompleted Roving Threat: Abrakhôr, Chosen of the ScourgeStrong enemies still roam in Eastern Gondor.Strong enemies still roam Eastern Gondor.Complete Roving Threat: Morgrish, the Beast from HaradComplete Roving Threat: Shardrágh, the Morgul Siege-beastComplete Roving Threat: Kethat-sai, the DestroyerStrong enemies still roam in Evendim.Strong enemies still roam in Evendim.Complete Roving Threat: Súnath, the TreacherousComplete Roving Threat: Droghus, the ChieftainComplete Roving Threat: Tárlug, the ServantStrong enemies still roam in Forochel.Strong enemies still roam in Forochel.Complete Roving Threat: Krevchal, the Brutal ChieftainComplete Roving Threat: Ukko Surma, the Undying GiantComplete Roving Threat: Gronkerna, the Juggernaut SlaveComplete Roving Threat: Mustarka, the Treacherous WightStrong enemies still roam in Southern Mirkwood.Strong enemies still roam in Southern Mirkwood.Complete Roving Threat: Thorang, the Spirit ArmourComplete Roving Threat: Helchurth, the Eternal ShadowComplete Roving Threat: Ghámgur, the Giant DreadComplete Roving Threat: Woe-weaver, the Silent FearStrong enemies still roam in The Misty Mountains.Strong enemies still roam in The Misty Mountains.Complete Roving Threat: Krabakam, the Master HunterComplete Roving Threat: Sútmoth, the Ice-giantComplete Roving Threat: Hrimdyr, the Beast KingComplete Roving Threat: Gróthurs, the Stone-giantStrong enemies still roam in The North Downs.Strong enemies still roam in The North Downs.Complete Roving Threat: Rotspittle, the CorruptedComplete Roving Threat: Valikas, the MisguidedComplete Roving Threat: Dúrlum, the DisturbedStrong enemies still roam in Western Gondor.Strong enemies still roam in Western Gondor.Complete Roving Threat: Haldalona, the Vile DarkwaterComplete Roving Threat: Amorchant, the Winged DeathComplete Roving Threat: Skorkaz, the Callous DeadComplete Roving Threat: Mota, the Umbarrim ScourgeComplete Roving Threat: Gundlag, the Death TrollYet unpunished for their treachery, the Corsairs of Umbar have laid waste to the lands of Dor-en-Ernil and stolen away the goods of its people.Corsair vandals and stolen tribute baskets can be found on the outskirts of Roamingstar's glade.

Roamingstar has asked you to punish the Men encroaching on her glade and dishonouring her people.Defeat Corsair vandals near Roamingstar's glade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Recover tribute baskets stolen from the Gilrain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have defeated many of the Corsairs threatening Roamingstar's glade and retrieved the baskets woven for her by the people of Gondor. You should now return to Roamingstar.Talk to Roamingstar'Although there are few that believe my sisters and I still dwell in these lands, they have always strived to care for our lands and our rivers.

'These Men from Umbar... they do not honour these lands as the others do. They defile, they steal, and they dishonour and for no greater purpose than their own gain.

'Soon they shall levy their destruction against my waters as well, but already they have taken from my people. Those that still believe pay tribute to me and my sisters with baskets they float down my waters... but the Men have claimed those too!

'I do not know what drives them - be it greed or spite, but they must be punished for the harm done to those that honour us.''These Men repulse me, ${PLAYER}. They dishonour me and my people and cannot be allowed to hold sway over our waters.

'I hope that soon all of their number are gone from these lands, and that I can return to the Gilrain in peace.'Lieutenant Ingi at Ost Ringdyr may be able to tell you what you can do to support the Free Peoples in the Ettenmoors.Lieutenant Ingi is at Ost Ringdyr, north and east of Glân Vraig.

Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn directed you to report to Ost Ringdyr to learn about the allies of Angmar's Army from Lieutenant Ingi.'Your time in the Ettenmoors will be fraught with danger. Angmar's army is bolstered by their own allies, and they are cruel and vicious.

'If you make your way north of Glân Vraig and follow the valley to the east, you will emerge at the ruins of Ost Ringdyr. Inside, you should seek out Lieutenant Ingi. He is a dwarf of great repute who has come to help us. He is handling the assault on one of Angmar's allies.

'To reach Ost Ringdyr, travel north along the edge of the hills and outcroppings that lead towards the Misty Mountains. You will ride through a valley for a short time and emerge on a path guarded by our people. Be wary, the woods are teeming with the Enemy.''Another fresh recruit? Well you've come to a place in dire need of your aid, ${CLASS}.

'Ever since we arrived, Angmar's forces have made a regular habit of assailing us wherever we travel. There are very few safe places to move. You're here to learn a bit about the Enemy, and I am ready to oblige, but be warned the Enemy travels the Ettenmoors largely unchecked and in great number. You will need to use caution and stealth.

'North of our location, behind the safety of great dark stones, lies the goblin-village of Grothum, a vile place that sits at the east side of the Isendeep Mine, once a dwarf-mine. I need help in defeating those goblins.'Scout the ruins of Southern Ithilien.Scout the ruins of Southern Ithilien.Discover DuindirDiscover Ost SarramDiscover BrangobelDiscover TunthamDiscover RolanthirRathon has been tasked with maintaining many of the cisterns in Minas Tirith by himself and has come to find one of the main drainage valves suspiciously broken.The missing parts of the main cistern valve can be found within the cisterns.

You should find and collect these parts for Rathon.Find the valve chainFind the valve gearFind the valve rodRathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Rathon.Speak with RathonThe main drainage valve can be found outside the cisterns on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should repair the main drainage valve for Rathon.Repair the main drainage valveRathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Rathon.Speak with Rathon'What brings you to the end of Wellman's Way? I myself am here to see to some maintenance of Minas Tirith's under-workings. The cisterns run throughout much of the city, bringing fresh water from Mount Mindolluin to all the buildings, from the Hall of the Kings to the Keep of the Keys. Many of my workers have traded the cisterns for the wall and now work to defend the city. Do you blame them?

'On my weekly inspection of the cisterns I've come to find this main drainage valve here completely broken. It was in perfect order just last week! I highly suspect sabotage, but who in the city would do such a thing?

'I could use your help as various parts of the valve are missing and I think they may be somewhere in the cisterns. It is a vast cavernous series of tunnels, and a good place to hide something. If I don't fix this valve soon, the lower cisterns could flood!''You found the missing parts to the valve? Good, good! And you say some goblins were lurking about in there? This is indeed dreadful news! I shall alert the city guard to this development.

'Right now, we must fix this master valve so the lower circle does not flood.''Great work, ${PLAYER}. One crisis averted but another remains. Continued threats and enemies still lurk in the cisterns. Unless the tunnels are clear of danger, I won't be able to go into the cisterns any time soon.'Círgon spends his days sailing the model ships he built with his father, but has become withdrawn from his family in his father's absence.The Baths of Belecthor can be found in the northern part of the Fourth Circle.

Círgon has asked you to join him at the Baths of Belecthor where he sails his model ships.Meet Círgon at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth CircleCírgon is standing at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle.

You have arrived at the Baths and should now talk to Círgon.Talk to CírgonCírgon's cart can be found near the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle.

Círgon has offered to let you place one of his ships into the Baths.Collect Círgon's model ship of Umbar from his cartThe Baths of Belecthor can be found to the north in the Fourth Circle.

You have picked up one of Círgon's ships and should now place it in the Baths.Place the model ship of Umbar in the Baths' watersCírgon is standing at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle.

You have set down the ship in the Baths and should now talk to Círgon.Mílien can be found outside her home in the Fourth Circle.

Círgon has asked you to tell his mother that he will come home for supper once he finishes packing up his ships.Talk to Mílien'Father and I used to sail our ships every day - they're a little big for the Baths, but it hasn't stopped us yet! 

'If you want to join me this time, I'll meet you up in the Fourth Circle by the Baths of Belecthor. It's the big fountain by the bridge to the cisterns - I'm certain you can figure it out.

'The sooner we set sail, the sooner I'll go home - deal? Come on, it'll be fun!''You made it!

'${PLAYER}, I left one of the ships for you! Would you like to set it in the Baths? You can if you want.

'It'd be great to have someone else here to share in the fun!''Look how they float, ${PLAYER}! Father and I built them together, you know. He did most of the work, but I built a lot of the little details. See the tiny Corsair on that one?

'I wonder what it would be like to sail on a real ship. Father said he'd take me to Pelargir someday soon, but I don't know when he'll be home. My uncle, Ristagír, isn't as fond of rivers and seas as Father and me, but he's a skilled craftsman all the same. Don't you see? It runs in my family, ${PLAYER}. I want to be a wood-worker and warrior just like my father!

'Mother wanted me to come home, yes? I'd be glad if you could join us for supper. Allow me a few minutes to pack up my ships and I'll meet you at our house!''You convinced him to hurry home?

'Oh, thank you - thank you!'A look-out has spotted a band of Orcs headed for Eryn Cordovath, a nearby orchard that is in the process of being evacuated, and Tolwin wishes for you to ride out there and assist the farmers.Travel to Eryn Cordovath and assess the situation.Travel to Eryn Cordovath and assess the situationFarmers can be found around Eryn Cordovath.

