You should speak with Ingold.Speak with Ingold'At any moment the Rohirrim may come to our aid. I will welcome them like my own brother.

'As I await the arrival of the Rohirrim, my men scout the land north of the Out-wall, while we hold the northern gate from the enemy.

'I am afraid to leave the North-gate unattended as many spies of the enemy roam nearby. Would you check in with my men upon the wall in my stead so I may learn what they have seen today?''Nothing stirs upon the mountainside today. See for yourself.

'Just don't tell Ingold that I've nearly fallen asleep up here!''I see. So, ${PLAYER}, it seems there is much to be done if we are to make safe passage for the Rohirrim when they approach this great city.

'I am counting on you for assistance in this matter.''Look closely out there and you will see men on horseback in the fields north of here. It is not the Rohirrim though...

Easterling riders patrol the fields of Talath Anor. Perhaps they know of the Rohirrim and plan to ambush them?''I am concerned with what I have been watching today. Look across the river and you will see men and Orcs preparing for war!''I've been watching Pelennor Fields and the news I have is nothing that Ingold does not already know. The eastern fields are overrun with the enemy.

'However, I have noticed some of the northern forces are starting to converge with the forces already in Pelennor. I fear war is upon us.'The gate that connects the docks to the rest of Dol Amroth must be sealed.To close off the city from more corsair reinforcements, the gate at the top of the stairs must be closed.Close the gateIngold has learned of an injured farmer who has made his way to the North-gate!The injured farmer can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas.

