You have found numerous plans for the Corsairs amidst their camp, and should now search for any missives to Azruthor himself.Search for any further communication between Azruthor and the Scourge'We need to push deeper into their encampment, ${PLAYER}... and that is no simple task.

'Their defences are considerable, and we know little of their plans in the Crown. Dol Amroth cannot field the men to confront such a foe with so many of our number gone to the east, and without knowledge of their intent, it is ill-advised at best to move against them in force.

'I have known the Corsairs to be slovenly men, and should they possess orders from Azruthor, it is likely that they may have left them within reach of you and your allies. Return to me with what you discover, and let us hope they are as careless as they seem!'The missive before you contains detailed information about Azruthor's forces in Tarlang's Crown, including a planned assault into the Anfalas to the west. Finally, it concludes with a vague, ominous mention of the Scourge's plans for Gondor.

You decide to continue looking over these notes for much may be learned from them that could aid the people of Gondor.Sergeants command smaller units of the enemy army. These feeble creatures believe that they can stand up to the might of Angmar's army, but they shall soon learn that they face a relentless foe.Sergeant-at-Arms lead small numbers of Men, Elves and dwarves throughout the Ettenmoors.

Chieftain Durulkum directed you to obtain sergeants' patches before returning to him at Dâr-gazag.'Maggot! You try my patience by the very sight of you. Skulking about with a sluggard's look about you. You make me sick and long for the vile bile spewed from Carn Dûm's underbelly.

'I'd sooner speak with the Pale Folk than you, if I had the choice. As I cannot choose where I am forced into duty, I shall take pleasure in causing you limitless pain.

'Our enemy calls feeble creatures leaders. Simple things who command small units. Sergeants, they call them. Our war-host will thrive only when we show our strength, and what better way than by defeating the lowliest of their leaders. Find them and take their badges off their warm corpses. You will do this for me, or I will see that you are fed the leavings in the bile from the north.''Feeble, yes? Such creatures cannot hope to match the might of Angmar's Army. Mordirith will be pleased with my progress!

'You did well for me, filth. I will see that you are given favour.'In spite of their dwindling numbers, the Haradrim forces in Upper Lebennin are poised to spill forth into Lossarnach through the settlement of Arnach.Othor can be found at Minlos in eastern Upper Lebennin.

Othor has asked for your aid in defending Arnach from the Haradrim. You should speak to him when you are ready.Talk to Othor<rgb=#FF0000>Othor must not be defeated</rgb>Othor can be found at Minlos in eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have successfully defended Arnach from attack and should now speak to Othor.Talk to OthorLady Terenis can be found in her hall in Tumladen.

Othor has asked you to return to Lady Terenis and warn her of the Haradrim forces readying to cross into Lossarnach.Talk to Lady Terenis'It is a grim day, traveller. My men and I have held out here for hours now, and the Haradrim continue to push their advance against Arnach. We have held them back for hours now, but I grow concerned that their numbers shall soon overwhelm us.

'They stalk the road to Tumladen, and we in turn have barricaded the bridge into Arnach. 

'Would you lend us your aid? If even one of my men can rest as you defend the bridge, it would bolster our resolve for the coming assaults.''My men have spotted the Haradrim approaching from the west. We must drive them back!

'Are you ready, ${PLAYER}?''I thank you for your aid, ${CLASS}. That should break their assault for some time!

'This assault troubles me, though... for what reason would the Haradrim throw themselves against the walls of Arnach instead of passing across the Erui? We have not the men to guard the Crossings, and could not repel their advance there.

'Return to the Lady, and tell her of my concerns. I do not believe we should leave this matter to speculation.''You have my thanks for keeping the people of Arnach safe, ${PLAYER}. It is yet another thing my sister could not manage without my help. You see, she and her husband lead Arnach, but that is a story of which I do not wish to speak more.

'It is strange, indeed, that the Haradrim would more readily set siege to Arnach instead of fording the Erui at the Crossings. Why would they march directly into superior numbers instead of hastening to the East?

'I believe this might be a matter for you and Lord Angbor to investigate.'Enemies assail the walls of Lugazag often. Trolls are clumsy and strong and often throw enemy soldiers through walls, shattering the stone therein and making holes in the stonework that must be repaired. Fortunately, trolls are also dumb and turn to stone in the sunlight.Soldier Gazlup is at Lugazag.

Soldier Gazlup directed you to collect troll-stone to repair the damage the trolls delivered to the walls of Lugazag.'Battles ebb and flow, ${RACE}. We fight war as we can and with the weapons at our command. Among those weapons are the trolls. As strong as they are stupid, massive as they are clumsy, and killing machines unmatched! With their benefits come drawbacks.

'The largest is their penchant for smashing walls apart. Holes in the wall mean that an enemy can easily breach our forces, so we must repair those holes. But the trolls pound the stone to dust and we haven't the numbers to dig a quarry here in the Ettenmoors, so we use the trolls.

'How, you wonder? Ever seen them in the sun? Solid as the rock from whence they were first drawn. The Coldeve-trolls wandering throughout the Ettenmoors often get caught in the sun and die. Chip away their stone and return it to me for repairs.''What's this? Ah, troll-stone, just as I asked. This will prove well for you, worm.

'Your efforts will continue to draw attention, and you will continue to earn the favour of the Krahjarn!'Displeased with the theatre in the First Circle, the Cloudyheads have chosen to explore another before putting on their show.Gord Dunley can be found just outside the Stone Theatre in Minas Tirith.

