You should follow Lady Raenemel back to her house.Return to Lady Raenemel's houseBergil stands outside Lady Raenemel's house in the Fourth Circle.

Lady Raenemel and Bergil were speaking as you approached. Now Bergil seems to have something to say to you.Talk to Bergil'You will not believe your ears, ${PLAYER}. She says it was she who placed all the things in the Finding Place. But I think that also - ah, never mind that. You should speak to her yourself.''Speak with her, ${PLAYER}.''I owe you much, ${CLASS}, but first the breach within the cisterns must be mended. You can be trusted with such a task, yes?''Why look there. Good as any mason! You are full of marvels, ${PLAYER}.

'The lady, Lady Raenemel it is, she told me where she lives. We should go there now, and speak with her. She is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place, of course.''Lady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, right by the Finding Place.''How did Lady Raenemel stay in the City, I wonder? I don't think anyone has ever seen her before!''She lives just around the way from the Finding Place! How many times have we gone past her, and never known!''Here is the ${CLASS}. Bergil, would you be good enough to stay here a moment? This ${RACE} and I must speak alone.''Go on, if that's what she wants. I'll be all right.''I have some words that I wish to say to you... over there.''${PLAYER}, there is something I must say. An explanation is in order. But no, not here.

'Walk with me.'

Lady Raenemel nods southward down the street.'Over there, where there is a small garden beside the path.''These children. One can plainly see - even from afar - how they are untouched, untouched by the dark despair that has fallen over this fortress-city. Untouched by even the Enemy's pall that has darkened the skies. And I cannot, will not...

'You see, it was my sons who first discovered the hole in that wall. And you should have seen the light in their eyes when they discovered what I had hidden there. Do you think, had they known it was I, the same light would have shone?

'Come. Up that way.''Up the stairs to the wall-walk, where we may have a view.''Where was I? These children have only the barest of notions what hopelessness there is, and though all should fall tomorrow, I will NOT have unquenched candles dimmed. I will not break that spell. Nor would you! I see it in your eyes. I know of how you stood up to that petty ruffian. Yes, I hear much, though I am not seen.

'I heard of Lord Boromir's end and it pierced my heart, it did. And now - Lord Faramir! Though all others remember them as grown men, noble and brave, in my mind they are but boys. For I was their tutor and governess, and the memory of the light in their eyes when I showed to them knowledge, truth, and wisdom - it fades not.

'But let us not tarry here.''Let us not tarry, but go on along the wall-walk.''Do you doubt that I tutored the Steward's sons? Many years had I laboured in the Houses of Lore, and after my sons perished in Lord Denethor's bid to retake old Osgiliath, he was wise and kind and generous in charging me with his own sons.

'Few have seen my face in the years since they left my tutelage. Indeed, I have rarely left my chambers. But when I discovered the prizes I left in that crevice being taken not by the season or the month, but by the day - or more often - I found ways of watching the takers without being seen.

'Like you, I have watched over these children. Only, in my own way, and you must understand that. This is what I am trying to impart to you. My own way.''I have always loved the fountains outside the Baths. Let us stroll over there.''Had I gone to Tumladen with the wains, as I was meant to... but I am an old thing, withered with grief and more at ease with my books than with living souls. Do you know, I wander the City by night, greeting ancient stones like friends, taking care never to cross the path of a living, breathing soul?

'And so you must understand, ${PLAYER}, you must undertake for me - these children, though I will love them from afar, they cannot, I will not... I am old, you see, and crooked with grief...

'I am like a troubled pool, ${PLAYER}, and nothing is clear to me. Let us return. I must think. Yes, think.''Speak not until we are back at my home. I must think!''Do you know why I took you on this stroll? To explain to you how I would not budge. How I would remain a watchful statue, above and far off, and help only as I may from the shadows.

'But, I know not how, in endeavouring to explain myself, I have budged. Relented! I am a clouded pool, I am a troubled heart, but I cannot help but feel that beyond this pain I feel lies, might I call it... hope?'Lady Raenemel beams.

'Speak with the boy, ${PLAYER}. He will tell you all.''${PLAYER}! ${PLAYER}! I can hardly believe it. It WAS she who left the things for us. And she will come to see us now at the Old Guest-house, and we are all welcome to come here now, at any time. And she will let us see old rooms in the Houses of Lore we would never be allowed into otherwise. And any who wish it shall receive lessons!

'But I am going on, aren't I? Ha ha! This is a good day, ${PLAYER}, even if tomorrow will not be so. And I thank you, for you have brought many things to light, haven't you, in the end?'Arrows are a commodity that will eventually run out and while bone and metal can be used to fashion the arrow-heads, only the straightest of branches can be used for the shaft.Small branches can be found scattered on the ground and on the Leafcull-trees throughout the Grimwood.

First Marshal Núrdram asked you to search along the Grimwood and Hithlad for small branches that might be turned into arrowshafts.'Greetings, ${CLASS}. It is good to see the faces of so many willing to aid in this battle. As you know, we are an island in this dangerous land. We have no true supply lines and must rely on our own number to satisfy the many needs this war-host commands.

'At the moment, we are in need of arrow-shafts. Scattered throughout this wood, and perhaps on the vile and corrupted Leafcull-trees, you will find small branches. Some, though certainly not all, of the branches will suffice, and we will offer you rewards for your assistance.

'Seek the wood throughout the Grimwood and Hithlad.''At a cursory glance it appears that many of these will make fine arrow shafts. You are due a reward, and I am an Elf of my word. Take this with my thanks.

'Should you find yourself with several of these, deliver them to Quartermaster Ash.'Angmar seeks to reinforce Tol Ascarnen, employing the assistance of goblin-archers, who hide behind the walls and launch deadly attacks at the Free Peoples foolish enough to enter the tunnel leading to the inner courtyard.The Free Peoples carry weapons from which the blades can be taken and used to craft crossbow bolts. The Free Peoples can be found at any of the locations they control, including the encampment south of Tol Ascarnen.

In an effort to better fortify Tol Ascarnen, the War-tyrant has called to the goblins at Grothum and told his soldiers to craft bolts for the goblins to shoot into the tunnel at the mouth of the keep. Glat has left the task of obtaining the blades of the Free Peoples to you.'Listen well, maggot. The War-tyrant wants to lay traps for the enemy, and so we shall. We've told the goblins in Grothum that they'll be sending us some fools capable of holding a crossbow and pulling its trigger. First, though, we need to get the goblins bolts they'll use to make the enemy dead.

'The enemy carries blades, and these blades can be shattered. Kill the enemy and shatter their blades. Then return those blades to me. We'll fasten together enough bolts to keep the goblins firing.

'Across the bridge to the south, you will find a small encampment of the enemy. Start there. Just know that you will find the enemy at any of the locations they control and always at Ost Ringdyr in the east.''Good work, maggot. A few more now, and we'll be ready to call in the goblins.'Corsairs are vandalizing Dol Amroth by tossing rocks at the windows of the cities' buildings.The windows should be saved.Defeat corsair looters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Corsairs may be hiding in some of the buildings within the docks.Bandits may be hiding in some of the houses at the docks.Search houses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})After learning the secret truths of Aragorn's siege of Pelargir, Lady Terenis wishes to silence any lingering rumours and ready the defences of Tumladen.Guards can be found throughout Tumladen, especially near the refugees of Minas Tirith.

Her curiosity appeased, Lady Terenis has asked you to scold the guards of Tumladen that are spreading rumours about the battle at Pelargir.Lady Terenis can be found in her hall in Tumladen.

You have scolded several guards and sent them back to their posts. You should now return to Lady Terenis.Talk to Lady Terenis'It is true that none of our foes have yet made an assault against Tumladen, but I believe it to be only a matter of time.

'In the past days, I have seen the guards speaking to the people and abandoning their posts for hours at a time. And for what? To speculate about the fate of Minas Tirith and the truth of the battle of Pelargir!

'Such matters are not of their concern! If only they knew the truth, they would know how important it is that it remains secret! I have a mind to scold them for their foolishness, but instead, I leave this matter to you.''I see how you look at me, ${PLAYER}.

'You know that I would not be so easily dissuaded from my curiosity, and you wonder how I could be so bold to demand that others abandon theirs. You see, these men are not like me... and you would do well to remember that.

'They hold their position here to protect the people, not to spend their days engrossed in speculation.'Siege equipment used to take Osgiliath should be destroyed before it is moved across the river.Siege equipment can be found just outside of Osgiliath in Southern Ithilien.

You should destroy the siege equipment before it can be conveyed across the river.Destroy Ballistae (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Catapults (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Trebuchets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroyed the siege equipment.CompletedThese siege weapons were used in the taking of Osgiliath. They will most likely be deployed across the river as well. Destroying them now seems like a sound idea.You have destroyed many pieces of siege equipment in Southern Ithilien and have weakened the grip of the Morgul-host on these lands.Tol Ascarnen is under the control of the Free Peoples, but their forces are still scattered to the corners of the Ettenmoors.Wolves can be found throughout the forests south and east of Tol Ascarnen. Drakes can be found to the north in Arador's End. Aurochs can be found in the pastures south and east of Tol Ascarnen.

In an effort to call defenders to the central keep of Tol Ascarnen, Sergeant-at-Arms Iafileg has asked you to collect hides to weave into banners that will call the defenders to their posts at the southern bridge.'We must call our forces to service, ${PLAYER}. If we fail at this task, we will suffer an onslaught too quickly, and the keep will fall. We require your aid in calling our forces to the bridge at the south, and so I ask you to assist us.

'We must make flags to fly near the bridge to the south, but they must be made swiftly. We need hides from the beasts found throughout these lands. Wolves and drakes are those you should hunt, for their hides will make the strongest banners. You may also find usable hides on the aurochs.

'You will find wolves in great number throughout the woods, and drakes are found to the north in Arador's End. Move quickly, friend.''You have done well, my friend. These will be woven into the banners we need to call our allies to the bridge. We will stand vigilant and win this day.'Tol Ascarnen is under the control of the Free Peoples, but their forces are still scattered to the corners of the Ettenmoors.Wolves can be found throughout the forests south and east of Tol Ascarnen. Drakes can be found to the north in Arador's End. Aurochs can be found in the pastures south and east of Tol Ascarnen.

In an effort to call defenders to the central keep of Tol Ascarnen, Sergeant-at-Arms Iafileg has asked you to collect hides to weave into banners that will call them to their posts at the western bridge.'We must call our forces to service, ${PLAYER}. If we fail at this task, we will suffer an onslaught too quickly, and the keep will fall. We require your aid in calling our forces to the bridge to the west, and so I ask you to assist us.

'We must make banners to fly near the bridge to the west, but they must be made swiftly. We need hides from the beasts found throughout these lands. Wolves and drakes are those you should hunt, for their hides will make the strongest banners. You can also find suitable hides upon the aurochs.

'You will find wolves in great number throughout the woods and drakes are found to the north in Arador's End. Move quickly, friend.''You have done well, my friend. These will be woven into the banners we need to call our allies to the bridge. We will stand vigilant and win this day.'Borhador has a melancholic disposition and could use a reminder of the beauty that the Vale still holds.Signs of hope may be scattered around Ringló Vale near Ethring.

