You should bring the signs of hope to Borhador.Bring the signs of hope to Borhador'You are still here? I do not seek your counsel, ${RACE}.

'Look upon my weary face. Do you see a leader perched over this Vale or a tired man? They call me Borhador the Old, my own people! My time to step down from Lordship was taken from me when my eldest son Dervorin answered the call of the beacons. Now I dwell in limbo waiting for my son's return or death from the monsters lurking in shadow. Does hope even exist? Now be gone from my sight!'

Perhaps Borhador needs some tangible signs of hope to lift his spirits in these dark times.'What is the meaning of this? These things are meant to cheer me up? This is foolishness. It is not a simple matter of waning prosperity in my Vale.... Hmm, but perhaps you could be useful as I admire your persistence. In some ways you remind me of my wife Halwen, rest her soul. She loved this Vale until her death.'The corsairs used several small boats to help them come ashore.The small boats the corsairs used should be destroyed.Destroy boats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})As thanks for your aid and to protect the lands of Gondor, Roamingstar seeks to prevent the Ruthless Dead from crossing into Lebennin.Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

Roamingstar has agreed to aid you in preventing the Ruthless Dead from crossing into Lebennin. You should speak to her when you are ready.Talk to RoamingstarRoamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have aided Roamingstar in banishing the Ruthless Dead and should now speak to her.Talk to RoamingstarGarvir can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have prevented the Ruthless Dead from crossing into Lebennin and should return to Garvir to tell him of your deeds with Roamingstar.Talk to Garvir in Linhir'Long ago, through my curiosity alone, I caused two lovers' hearts to be broken upon the western shores.

'I have been troubled by this for many ages... and it was not long after that my sadness compelled me to hide myself away from the folk of these lands. Yet, evil has come to these lands in great force, and I hold the power to change the fates of my people. If I fail to act this day, I shall suffer a sadness far beyond my knowing.

'You spoke of the Dead and their plan to reunite with their Master. That shall not be!

'My waters will consume them, but... I shall have need of your aid.''None shall threaten the folk of my lands, ${CLASS}.''It is done, ${CLASS}. It feels to me as if a great weight has been lifted from this land, but I sense that many more troubles await you.

'Return to my people and tell them of what has happened this day. I shall tend these waters as I always have and strike down any Dead who dare to approach my banks again.

'You shall always be welcome at my side, ${PLAYER}.''You tell a most interesting tale, ${PLAYER}, but I do not have the time to hear all of it right now!

'Many things are happening in Linhir, and I must remain vigilant!

'Let us speak of this another time, my friend.'Taskmaster Izubuzri communicated that he wants proof that you killed many eagles. Apparently the eagles are too free with where they perch.Eagles can be found throughout the Coldfells and in a small section of Arador's End to the south of the Isendeep Mine.

Taskmaster Izubuzri wants you to return eagle feathers to him to prove that you have slaughtered a good number of the birds.'Me no likes eagles.

'Eagles go... on dead troll.

'You kill eagles, take feathers.

'Make me like you.''No more fouling dead troll... eagle-bird!'

The troll eats the feathers. Peculiar.Corsair slavers are on the ships in the harbour, taking stock of their catch.The slavers must be defeated to secure the safety of those in Dol Amroth.Defeat slavers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Although the Corsairs have been defeated by Aragorn and the Grey Host, many slaves still await their freedom from the emptied ships in Pelargir.Slaves can be found on the Corsair ships moored by the West Seagate in Pelargir. These ships can be reached by using nearby rowing boats.

Firiondur has asked you to rescue any slaves that still have not been found on the ships in the harbour of Pelargir.Free enslaved Gondorians from ships in Pelargir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Firiondur can be found inside the lighthouse at Aerthir.

You have rescued several enslaved Gondorians and should now report your success to Firiondur.Talk to Firiondur inside the lighthouse at Aerthir'The harbour at Pelargir has gone quiet, ${PLAYER}. Have the Corsairs truly been defeated or do our ears deceive us?

'Many are their ships, and even more still slave on their decks. If their forces are truly broken, we must work to free the poor folk that the Corsairs took as slaves before they starve on those dingy crafts.

'The other refugees here have family that were taken in the first assault, and I know they would give anything to see their families made whole once more. Search the ships in the harbour, and send any folk you find back to us here.''Oh, to see them freed from those vile men... it is wonderful.

'Yet... their ships are many, and I worry that some still remain lost in Pelargir. Let us rest for now and begin our search anew tomorrow.'There are many villainous foes roaming Central Gondor.There are many villainous foes roaming Central Gondor.Slay many Beasts in Central GondorSlay many Corsairs in Central GondorSlay many Half-trolls in Central GondorSlay many Haradrim in Central GondorSlay many Orcs in Central GondorThere are many villainous foes roaming Eastern Gondor.There are many villainous foes roaming Eastern Gondor.Slay many Beasts in Eastern GondorSlay many Easterlings in Eastern GondorSlay many Goblins in Eastern GondorSlay many Half-trolls in Eastern GondorSlay many Haradrim in Eastern GondorSlay many Orcs in Eastern GondorThere are many villainous foes roaming Old Anórien.There are many villainous foes roaming Old Anórien.Slay many Beasts in Old AnórienSlay many Easterlings in Old AnórienSlay many Haradrim in Old AnórienSlay many Orcs in Old AnórienSlay many Trolls Old AnórienThere are many villainous foes roaming West Gondor.There are many villainous foes roaming West Gondor.Slay many bandits in West GondorSlay many beasts in West GondorSlay many Corsairs in West GondorSlay many Oath-breakers in West GondorSlay many Orcs in West GondorConcerned by the Haradrim forces stalking Upper Lebennin, Lady Terenis hopes to ensure the safety of Tumladen and Arnach.Haradrim scouts have been sighted near the beacon Minlos, which overlooks the river Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.

Lady Terenis has asked you to investigate the Haradrim presence near Minlos and defeat them.Defeat Haradrim scouts near Minlos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Guards can be found at the beacon Minlos in eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have defeated many Haradrim scouts and should report to a guard at Minlos.Talk to a guard at Minlos'I have heard reports of the Haradrim scouting their way up the hill toward the beacon Minlos, and I worry for the folk of Arnach. It is home to many warriors, but as with our own, so many have gone to my brother's aid in Minas Tirith.

'The Haradrim have not made a move against Tumladen, but perhaps that is not their purpose in Upper Lebennin. Whatever the truth of the situation, they hasten to the East, across the Erui and if they succeed in their assault, through Arnach.

'I ask this of you: rout the Haradrim, and ensure the safety of the people of Arnach.''The Lady sent you, did she?

'Indeed, you have come at a fortuitous time. You see, the Haradrim have been rallying under the cover of trees nearby and they mean to invade Arnach.

'If you would keep watch with us for a time, we would be most thankful.'After learning of a great battle in Pelargir, Nimithil grows concerned for her husband, Faltharan, who remained behind in the city to challenge the Corsairs.Faltharan can be found somewhere in Pelargir.

Nimithil has grown concerned for her husband after hearing news of a great battle in Pelargir. You should seek out Faltharan.Talk to Faltharan in Pelargir'You have done much for me and the people of Ost Anglebed, but I have heard naught but horrid things of Pelargir. While you and the men of Linhir battled the Heirs on the beach, I heard tell of a great calamity in Pelargir.

'My husband, Faltharan, bid us flee to safety when the Corsairs came to the city, but now I fear for him. Although I know he would never surrender the city willingly, I also do not wish him to lay down his life for a hopeless cause.

'Search for him within Pelargir's walls, ${PLAYER}. If he fights yet, I trust you will join him in reclaiming the city from the Corsairs!''Ah, you say my wife has sent you?

'I am heartened that she and my son are safe, but I cannot say the same for myself or my men. Although the battle has ended, many troubles still plague Pelargir.'Seeking to put an end to the reign of the Heirs of Castamir, Jajax prepares himself for an uneasy and hopefully brief alliance with Garvir's brothers.Erchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

Jajax has asked you to rally Garvir's brothers to Hata Kebir so they may seek vengeance against Azgarzôr.Talk to ErcharNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed.

After dispatching Azgarzôr, Erchar and Herion suggested you return to the people of Lebennin. You should speak to Nimithil.Talk to Nimithil'You say a Corsair by the name of Jajax has sent you here? What sort of a name is that?

'If I did not know you as well as I do, I would think you a most unskilled liar. I question his motivation for acting against his own people, but I shall grant him my trust... at least for the moment. Still, I will seize any chance I can to slay Garvir's murderer, even if it means fighting alongside a Corsair.

'When you are ready, we shall ride. Be ready, ${PLAYER}, for I will not allow anything to hold me back once we reach their camp!''Let us go now, ${PLAYER}. I shall see that worm suffer!''You have done so much for us, ${PLAYER}... I do not even know what we can offer in return.

'The Heirs of Castamir have been critically weakened by your hand, and soon they shall be defeated altogether.

'Celebrate this day, my dearest ally, for you have won a crucial victory for the people of Gondor.'With the Enemy looming close, the soldiers of Minas Tirith are on edge from anticipation.Talk to Harnion in the Training Ground about sparring with his soldiers.Speak to Harnion'Some restless soldiers are in need of a new opponent with whom they can sharpen their skills before the coming battle. I've heard your name whispered between citizens and soldiers alike, boasting of your prowess in battle and helpful demeanour. Will you aid us, ${CLASS}?''Are you ready to aid the soldiers in their training?'Faltharan seeks to learn who leads the people of Tumladen and hopes they can guide you back to Lord Angbor and his host.Guards can be found throughout Tumladen in northern Upper Lebennin.

Faltharan has asked you to seek out a guard of Tumladen and determine who speaks for the people of the settlement.Talk to a guard in TumladenImladir can be found at the barracks near the entrance to Tumladen in northern Upper Lebennin.

A guard of Tumladen has directed you to a man named Imladir. You should find and speak to him.Talk to Imladir in TumladenLady Terenis can be found in the great hall of Tumladen in north-western Upper Lebennin.

Imladir has informed you that Lady Terenis, the sister of Steward Denethor, has placed herself in charge of Tumladen.Talk to Lady Terenis in the great hall of Tumladen'I have never seen Tumladen so filled with the people of Gondor. I suppose it should not surprise me, but it is a marvel nonetheless.

'You have done much for my father and me, ${PLAYER}, and I think it is time at last for you to rejoin Lord Angbor and his host. It has been difficult to discern who truly leads the guards here with so many folk milling about, but perhaps you would do well to speak to whomever does. 

'I have seen many guards patrolling the roads nearby, and I am certain they can guide you to their captain.''You wish to speak with the captain of the guard?

'You should seek out Imladir at the barracks near the entrance to Tumladen. He leads the defence of Tumladen, even in times of peace.''Hah! You think I still speak for anyone here? No, no... that honour was taken from me the moment the Steward's sister arrived.

'She speaks so surely of what she does not know, and those that seek shelter here will lend their ears to any whose voices boom above the rest.

'If talk is what you desire, then seek her out in the great hall. As for me, I shall keep these people safe from the Enemy.''Greetings, ${CLASS}. Am I to presume that you travel with Lord Angbor? If he has arrived, I have much to ask him of the war.'

You inform Lady Terenis that you travelled with the Lord of Pelargir and his son, but intend to rejoin Angbor.

'So, you were at Pelargir then? You have my attention... for the moment.'The Grimwood is secured for Angmar's purposes. To ensure that it remains this way, we must grow our forces and support.

You must draw the web-weavers from the nearby tower to come to Angmar's aid at the Grimwood Lumber Camp.Caragdal can be found in the ruins near the Grimwood Lumber Camp, nesting amongst her broodlings.

Caragdal must be escorted safely to the Grimwood Lumber Camp.Escort Caragdal to the Grimwood Lumber CampSoldier Golb is in the Grimwood Lumber Camp.

You should return to Soldier Golb with the news that Caragdal is on the move.Return to Soldier Golb with news of your success'To the west, in a tower draped in the webs of their mistress, lay a great spider. She will come to us and oversee the collection of wood through her minions if we beseech her aid.

'Go there now, maggot, and speak with her. Bid her draw the spiders from the tower to the woods surrounding this camp.

'Be quick!''Be swift. I will not suffer the slings and stones of those accursed little folk any longer. The time has come to decimate their ilk and wipe the world clean for our conquest.''So Caragdal is on the move? If you weren't such a blubbering weakling, I'd say you were beginning to be of some worth to us here! At least you do not fail in all that you attempt. You have impressed me... for now.

'What are you looking at? Get back to work!'Barad Rill, a crucial tower of the Prince's lands, has fallen into the hands of the Enemy, and Herion hopes to reclaim what was lost.Barad Rill can be found far to the south-west of Linhir in Dor-en-Ernil.

Herion has asked you to recover relics from Barad Rill as well as plant a banner of Belfalas atop its ruins.Recover Gondorian relics from Barad Rill (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Plant a banner of Belfalas atop Barad RillHerion can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have recovered the relics and planted a banner atop the ruins of Barad Rill. You should now return to Herion.'I still cannot believe what was done to Barad Rill, ${PLAYER}.

'It was one of the Prince's most beautiful towers and it shone light for all who would sail the Great River. The Corsairs and Haradrim seek to wrest it from us, but I will not see it done.

'Travel to Barad Rill, plant a banner of Belfalas atop its ruins, and steal away our relics from those vile men. Let them know that Dor-en-Ernil is still ours!''I am gladdened that so many of our relics survived the toppling of Barad Rill, my friend.

'Even if they tear our banner from the ruins, we shall raise it anew until all of their men are pushed from Gondor. You have my thanks.'Turgon is concerned about Haradrim forces that have taken the nearby Hillock and wishes to drive them off the best vantage point on Pelennor Fields.The Hillock can be found in Pelennor Fields, north-east of the South-gate.

You should defeat enemies upon the Hillock.Defeat enemies upon the Hillock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Turgon can be found at the South-gate of the Rammas.

You should speak with Turgon.Speak with Turgon'The enemy has captured the best vantage point on the Pelennor -- the Hillock.

'Haradrim have turned the hill into a mighty encampment. I suspect they will use the vantage point to command troops in battle.

'Please go to the Hillock and defeat enemies there to disrupt their plans.''Your efficiency is exemplary. The Haradrim will remember this day so we must be on guard if they decide to retaliate. I am sure it will take some time for them to recover from the damage you caused, though.'The Corsairs of Umbar keep a well-stocked camp in Tarlang's Crown with resources that could be of great aid to the people of Gondor.Bags of rations can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown, especially near Corsair tents.

You have found bags of rations that might be of aid to the people of Gondor and should take them from the Corsairs.Steal bags of rations from Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have recovered many bags of rations in Tarlang's Crown.The Corsairs have stocked their camp with enough rations to hold for at least several weeks. These rations could be of great help to the people of Dol Amroth and Gondor in the coming days of the War and could also weaken the resolve of the Corsairs if enough are taken.

You should take them from the Corsairs, and see them brought to the people of Gondor.You have recovered many bags of rations from the Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown. With their forces pressing the assault to the south, these rations may be of great use to the soldiers and people of Dol Amroth.Corsair slavers have gathered up the craftsmen and are preparing to move them.The craftsmen must be rescued before the corsairs ship them off.Defeat slavers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A grim leader of the Dead has revealed himself in Tarlang's Crown, pledging those who follow him to service of the Heirs of Castamir.The leader of the Dead can be drawn forth by defeating many of the Dead in the main encampment in Tarlang's Crown.

Gondren has asked you to seek out the leader of the Dead in Tarlang's Crown, hoping that it will weaken the alliance between the Dead and the Heirs of Castamir.Draw forth and defeat the leader of the Dead in Tarlang's CrownHarnion can be found along the road through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas.

You have defeated the oathbreaker, Nerzus, for a third time and weakened Azruthor's hold on Tarlang's Crown. You should now return to Harnion.Talk to Harnion'Throughout my life, little has instilled more fear in me than the Dead Men.

'Even the Corsairs still bristle at their approach, fearful of what these new allies mean to their cause. The Dead are led by a ghastly man, and though I do not know his name, he looks long upon all he sees here with a discerning eye. Could it be that he and his people once again have doubts about throwing their lot in with the Enemy?

'If he reveals himself, confront him and let the others look upon him as you defeat him. Although he shall only be gone from this world a short while, perhaps it will drive the Dead to abandon their oaths once more. Let us hope so, ${PLAYER}... for little else would grant me peace in death.''You say you have seen this oathbreaker before?

'His persistence is... unfortunate. If only the Dead could be made to see the foolishness of this alliance... perhaps then they would abandon the Scourge and the Heirs.

'Regrettably, I fear we will have to contend with them until then.'Angmar's inability to destroy the Free Peoples holed up in the farthest reaches of the Ettenmoors has prompted the army's leaders to summon more trolls from the north.Taskmaster Dromdas is at Gramsfoot.

Angmar's army wishes to dislodge the Free Peoples from the Ettenmoors and has enlisted the assistance of trolls to undertake the endeavour. Of course, the work of Angmar must continue and the troll's work must be completed. If you wish to help the trolls, you should speak with Taskmaster Dromdas again.Talk to Taskmaster Dromdas at Gramsfoot and complete a patrol through the Ettenmoors as a Troll (Cost: 500 Commendations)Taskmaster Dromdas is at Gramsfoot.

You should return to Taskmaster Dromdas and inform him that you did the work he requested done.Talk to Taskmaster Dromdas at Gramsfoot'Trolls will come help, but you must go work. I will send you. I have been told to send you.''You go now. Troll, come here.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: You will be logged out of your current monster play session and logged into a new one. This new avatar is not permanent and cannot trade items or otherwise interact with much of the world.</rgb>'Troll, come back. Now you come back. You do good work? Better have.'Soldier Fandmau needs stone to repair the holes blasted through the walls of Tírith Rhaw and sent you to find the materials from the trolls caught in the sun.Trolls that have been turned to stone by the sun are scattered throughout the Ettenmoors.

Soldier Fandmau tasked you with obtaining a fair number of large to small bits of troll-stone to repair the walls of Tírith Rhaw.'Guarding this post makes me nervous. So close to the enemy and trolls bashing holes through the stone. We need to shore the walls here and fast.

'Get stone from the dead trolls throughout the Ettenmoors and return them to me. No stone is too small!''I'd build a wall if I could to keep the enemy from getting into our halls. We should be more defensible. Higher walls, larger tower... more trolls!!!

'You did well, ${PLAYER}. I will speak well of you for a time.'The corsairs are plundering the supplies from the warehouse.The supplies must be recovered.Recover supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Melethon has ordered you to defeat enemy guards at Shrak Mauruk in hopes of capturing their stronghold.Shrak Mauruk is located on the Eastern side of Osgiliath.

You should defeat enemy guards within Shrak Mauruk.Defeat enemy guards at Shrak Mauruk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Melethon is at the Causeway Forts.

You should speak to Melethon.Speak with Melethon'Orcs and other foul creatures have repurposed one of the old Eastern courtyards into a stronghold they call, Shrak Mauruk. Their numbers are great there. I want to send you in to defeat some of their guards so that we may capture their stronghold.

'I recommend not taking on this mission alone. There are many other able and willing warriors ready to fight. May hope be by your side.''You have done much for the Gondorian army. Victory will surely be ours!'Tyrant Uzulthrang is here for battle and only battle. Stationed outside of Tol Ascarnen, the Tyrant pledges that he will fight against the enemy if you prove that you are worthy of his notice.Tyrant Uzulthrang told you to assemble proof of your deeds, then and only then will he assist you in destroying the fools within Tol Ascarnen. He did not, however, tell you what proof he requires.'I've no time for chatter or chittering. Listen well, as I've a temper built only for battle and I will not tolerate failure.

'I need proof that you are worthy of fighting along my side, ${PLAYER}. You are a lowly worm to me, and without proof, I will not assist you... my strength and standing are not for risking on such pitiful slugs like you.

'Bring me proof that you are a true combatant in the service of Mordirith, Angmar, and Lugbúrz, and I will join your assault against the enemy!''Let nothing ill be spoken of you this day, ${PLAYER}. I shall heed your call and storm the castle with you.

'We shall rise for the glory of Angmar!

'We shall rise for the favour of Lugbúrz!

'We shall die to see that Mordirith's Army does not fail!

'Come on, lads! Let us have fun storming the castle!'Marooned by a foolish captain, Corsairs have stranded themselves and their pillage on a shoal along the Anduin.The marooned ship and its crew can be found to the south-west of Aerthir upon the Anduin. A rowing boat on the shore will allow for swifter passage.

Aerin has asked you to help recover pillage from the Corsairs that have become trapped on shoals in the Anduin.Recover buried pillage near the marooned ship (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aerin can be found in the lighthouse at Aerthir in southern-central Lebennin.

You have recovered a great deal of pillage from the marooned Corsairs and should now bring it to Aerin.'The others and I have seen a great Corsair ship marooned on one of the shoals along the Great River.

'Whether they were drunk or simply foolish, the crew is now stranded there with all of their pillage. I would ask that you recover as much as you are able, but leave the Corsairs and let the river claim them!

'There is a small boat on the shore nearby, and it will allow you passage to the shoals. I do not advise swimming, for the current is strong and swift, ${CLASS}.''They have taken so much from our people...

'I shall keep what you can recover for us here, for I am sure the Corsairs still had more stored away on that ship of theirs. I hope that when this war is over we will see all of these stolen items returned to their owners.'Battle in the Ettenmoors is uncertain, with forces losing footholds as easily as they gain them. The Free Peoples have taken Tol Ascarnen but now must hold the location. To do this, they will need to strengthen their position as best they can.Drakes can be found in Arador's End, north of Tol Ascarnen.

Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith has asked you to assist her in crafting a horn to call forces to fight against Angmar's army when they assail Tol Ascarnen. To do this, she asks that you collect sinews from the drakes of Arador's End with which to bind the Horn of Tol Ascarnen. She suggests you take allies.'${RACE}, we have a mission of great importance for you to undertake. Provisions are low, as you likely are aware, and the Captain-General has ordered that we craft a horn to call resting troops to service. We shall do this, but we need your help, for we must hold these posts at all cost.

'What I must say next troubles me, but these are desperate times, and we must make due with what we can.

'North of here, in the place called Arador's End, you will find drakes. These creatures have very strong sinew that ties their bones and muscles together. I ask that you collect sinew from these beasts so we can make straps to bind the Horn of Tol Ascarnen. Do not travel alone and be careful not to damage the sinew.''You have done well. I will set others to the task of cleaning these straps so that we might yet make the Horn of Tol Ascarnen.'Angmar seeks to reinforce Tol Ascarnen, employing the assistance of goblin-archers, who hide behind the walls and launch deadly attacks at the Free Peoples foolish enough to enter the tunnel leading to the inner courtyard.Search the area of Hithlad for the kindling needed to make the arrow shafts. Hithlad and the Grimwood forest are south of Tol Ascarnen.

In an effort to better fortify Tol Ascarnen, the War-tyrant has called to the goblins at Grothum and told his soldiers to craft bolts for the goblins to shoot into the tunnel at the mouth of the keep. It falls to you to collect the wood for the shafts.'Listen well, maggot. The War-tyrant wants to lay traps for the enemy, and so we shall. We've told the goblins in Grothum that they'll be sending us some fools capable of holding a crossbow and pulling its trigger. First we need to get the goblins bolts they'll use to make the enemy dead.

'There are many trees within this land, and though I'd rather take an axe and cleave them all down, the War-tyrant says that'll take too long and wants us looking for the chaff that has already fallen.

'We need to make many arrows for the goblins, so it is up to us to collect as much of the smaller bits of wood as we can. Search across the Ettenmoors and return the wood to me.''Good work, maggot. A few more now, and we'll be ready to call in the goblins.'Building a horn to summon reinforcements at Tol Ascarnen requires that several pieces are collected and assembled for an Orc to watch over and use when the Free Peoples make their assault against the fort.The Wintersebb-drakes are found north, in sections near the Hoarwell's source and at the foot of the Misty Mountains.

Angmar's forces at Tol Ascarnen are crafting a great horn to call reinforcements to the fight when the Free Peoples return to assault the area. Kaasak has tasked you with collecting sinew from the Wintersebb-drakes to secure the many horns that will adorn the post.'We'll need reinforcements against these maggots. For that we need a way of calling more forces to the keep. The War-tyrant wants us to build a great horn to summon our forces to patrol the keep, and we'll do what he wants or feel the crack of his whip. This means that orders trickle down to you, and that means that you do my bidding, whelp.

'Take others and head north into Arador's End. Find the Wintersebb-drakes there and slaughter them for the pieces of their innards that join their bones. Collect them and return them to me.

'Whatever you do maggot, don't destroy the sinew. Ruined sinew is useless.''This will do well. I'll see that you are rewarded for your effort. Don't let a success like this go to your head though, whelp. You've a long way to go before the War-tyrant sees you as more than gristle on a tasty slab of rat-folk.'Corsair vandals are ransacking the Great Hall.The Great Hall is the crown jewel of Dol Amroth.Defeat Vandals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scout settlements and strongholds in Eastern Gondor.Scout settlements and strongholds in Eastern Gondor.Discover GlaniathDiscover TumladenDiscover ArnachDiscover Imloth MeluiDiscover Bâr HúrinDiscover Faramir's Look-outThandor has asked you to board the Corsair ships, and free the remaining slaves.The Corsair ships can be reached using the boat to the south of Thandor.

You should board the Corsair ships and free the captured slaves.Free slaves aboard the Corsair ships (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Thandor.Talk to Thandor'During their assault, the Corsairs captured citizens from town and ship to serve aboard their galleys as slaves. Although we were able to halt their advance into Gondor, many remain trapped aboard their vessels.

'We no longer have the proper resources to mount a rescue, so I would ask for you to board the remaining Corsair-occupied ships, and free any prisoners of war that you find.''Well done, ${PLAYER}.

'Although this will leave many displaced refugees within our walls, this means fewer innocents being subjugated by the enemies of Gondor.

'Our next move is to make sure they find their way to some place that's safer. We won't be able to keep them here.'The discovery of a northern army and strange axe-wielding Easterlings concerns Ingold and threatens his ability to hold the North-gate.Easterlings can be found across the River Forant in southern Talath Anor.

You should defeat Sûhalar patrols and destroy Easterling barricades.Defeat Sûhalar patrols (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Sûhalar barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ingold can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas.

You should speak with Ingold.Speak with Ingold'This northern army consists of Orcs from Mordor and Sûhalar Easterlings. These strange, axe-wielding Easterlings are a new threat, the likes I have not seen before. If we are to hold the northern gate for the Rohirrim we will need to deal with these northern forces.

'Venture into Talath Anor, the lands north of here and defeat patrols of these Easterling axe-men.

It has also come to my attention that these Easterlings are trying to construct barricades along the Forant River. This should be dealt with as well.''This is a fine start down the path to victory! There is much more to do though if we are to stand a chance in the days to come.'Goblins have been the main foe the Hobbits of Hoarhallow have contended with in all their years. They believe with the aid of the Tall Folk they can score a final victory against the Snowreap-goblins.Snowreap-goblins inhabit Grothum, a village they established east of the Isendeep Mine in Arador's End.

Ned Claybrick asked you to assail the goblins in their home to deter them from future raids on Hoarhallow.Ned Claybrick awaits your return at Hoarhallow, south and west of Grothum.

You found the Snowreap-goblins in Grothum and defeated them at their village. You should return to Ned Claybrick with the news.Return to Ned Claybrick at Hoarhallow'We welcome the arrival of our tall friends to Hoarhallow. With them, we hope to end the plight which has faced our people for a great long time.

'In the north, beyond the place where the Hoardale rises sharply by the Tall Folk fortress and bends to the east, at the crest of the hill, you will find Grothum where the goblins dwell. We wish to show them that we are not afraid of their ilk, and truly we are not. There are some of us willing to fight, but they have gone off to protect the wood and help the Tall Folk.

'If you are willing to help us, make your way north-east and defeat the goblins.''You will find the goblins in their village, Grothum. It is far to the north and east in Arador's End.''Such heroism! We are indebted to you, ${PLAYER}. We will not forget all that you have done for us.

'Please take this. The Tall Folk at Glân Vraig said that Quartermaster Ash there would assist all those that give us aid.'Something stirs in the tunnels and passageways beneath the crumbling ruins of Osgiliath.Explore the tunnels and culverts for signs of Faramir.Defeat the Troll Abomination, DagronDefeat the Half-troll Abomination, MuzgáshSomething stirs in the tunnels and passageways beneath the crumbling ruins of Osgiliath.Complete the quest Sunken Labyrinth -- Tier 1Complete the quest Sunken Labyrinth -- Tier 1Complete the quest Sunken Labyrinth -- Tier 1Something stirs in the tunnels and passageways beneath the crumbling ruins of Osgiliath.Complete the quest Sunken Labyrinth -- Tier 2Complete the quest Sunken Labyrinth -- Tier 2Complete the quest Sunken Labyrinth -- Tier 2Something stirs in the tunnels and passageways beneath the crumbling ruins of Osgiliath.Explore the tunnels and culverts for signs of Faramir.Defeat the Troll Abomination, DagronDefeat the Half-troll Abomination, MuzgáshCorsairs have started moving supplies into the docks.Corsair supplies are spread out throughout the docks.Confiscate supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Trapped within the tunnels below Osgiliath, the Rangers of Ithilien struggle to survive as their supplies dwindle.Supply-stores can be found hidden throughout Osgiliath.

Echil has asked you to seek out hidden supply-stores and return them to the Rangers of Ithilien within Osgiliath.Recover supply-stores in Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Echil can be found in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath.

You have recovered many hidden supply-stores from Osgiliath, and should now deliver them to Echil.'As with weapons and healing herbs, we have hidden numerous supply-stores throughout the city containing rations and fresh water.

'If our stay in this sunken labyrinth is to be a lengthy one, we will have need of those supplies.

'Travel to the surface and search throughout the city for our supply-stores. When you have found as many as you can bear, return them to me!''There are many to look after down here, ${PLAYER}. You have made that task far easier this day.

'You have my thanks.'Corsairs may be hiding in some of the houses of Dol Amroth.The houses must be checked for corsairs.Check houses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})At the request of Aragorn, Lord Angbor has come to Tumladen to privately deliver a message of victory to Lady Terenis.Angbor can be found outside Tumladen in Upper Lebennin.

You have delivered Terenis's warning to Lord Angbor. He bears a missive from Aragorn that must be brought to the Lady at once.Talk to AngborLady Terenis can be found in her hall in the rear of Tumladen in Upper Lebennin.

You have delivered Aragorn's missive to Lady Terenis, and should now aid her as Lord Angbor requested.Talk to Lady Terenis'Aragorn has told me much of Lady Terenis, though she was much younger when last they knew each other. Even then, she had a keen wit about her and when that failed, a decidedly sharp tongue.

'You say she noticed the ships as they sailed, as he expected, and he will see that she learns of the fate of Pelargir before her curiosity drives these people into a misplaced fervour. The true challenge for her, I suspect, will be keeping such knowledge to herself. As it is with you and I, she too shall be bound by an oath to Aragorn... an oath to a King. 

'We shall go to her in her hall, and speak of this when you are ready. Let us be done with this errand, ${PLAYER}, for four thousand men should not wait upon the meddling of nosey folk - even if they are kin of the Steward!''Let us ease the Lady's curiosity, shall we?''I... am sorry for the manner of our meeting, ${PLAYER}.

'Surely, you realize my threats were empty and borne only out of desperation! I welcome any aid that you can offer to my people.'A look-out has spotted a band of Orcs headed for Eryn Cordovath, a nearby orchard that is in the process of being evacuated. Tolwin wishes for you to ride out there and assist the farmers.Eryn Cordovath is located north-west of Crithost.

Travel to Eryn Cordovath and assess the situation.Travel to Eryn Cordovath and assess the situationOrcs can be found with Eryn Cordovath.

You should defeat Orcs in the orchard.Defeat Orcs in Eryn Cordovath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.

You should speak with Tolwin.Talk to Tolwin'The look-out said the band of Orcs were at least a dozen strong. If we do not get to the orchard quickly, I fear our beautiful trees will be destroyed.

'Please go to Eryn Cordovath at once and stop this band of Orcs before the orchard is no more!''It saddens me that much of the orchard burns. I've spent many days playing in Eryn Cordovath. Hopefully, we will be able to rebuild from what is left of the orchard back into something as wonderful as it was before the invasion upon these lands.'Edenos has tasked you with taking back the Ornendil Bridge in Northern Osgiliath by defeating enemy guards.The Ornendil Bridge is located in Northern Osgiliath over the Anduin River.

You should defeat enemy guards on the Ornendil Bridge.Defeat enemy guards on the Ornendil Bridge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Edenos is at the Palace of Eldacar.

You should speak to Edenos.Speak with Edenos'The enemy is on the Ornendil Bridge! I want to send you in to defeat the guards on the bridge so that we can recapture this key defensive point.

'Taking hold of the Ornendil Bridge is important to the safety of our stronghold at the Palace of Eldacar. May hope be by your side.''You have done much for the Gondorian army. We will take back this city!'Complete story quest arcs in Minas Tirith.Complete story quest arcs in Minas Tirith.Complete the Children of Minas Tirith arcComplete the Forlong's Feast arcComplete the Travelling Band arcThe Corsairs of Umbar have stocked Tarlang's Crown with ale that could easily be turned against them.Barrels of ale can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown, especially near Corsair tents.

Elaglar has asked you to destroy barrels of ale in Tarlang's Crown in hopes that it will throw the Corsairs into disarray.Destroy barrels of ale in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elaglar can be found in Dol Amroth.

You have destroyed many barrels of Corsair ale, and should report your success to Elaglar.Talk to Elaglar'We can count ourselves lucky that most of the Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown do not seem to be any different than the others on the coast.

'They still go far out of their way to secure more ale, and they keep much of it nearby even in times of war. If you were to destroy their stores, I am certain they would descend into chaos and begin to fight amongst themselves.

'Be wary of how simple this may sound, ${PLAYER}, for the Corsairs are not ones to leave their barrels unguarded.''I am certain it will be a long time before we can deprive them of all of their ale, but this ought to rile them up for some time.

'I would much rather they fight amongst themselves over what little remains than take the fight to us!'In the wake of numerous thefts in Blackroot Vale, many supplies have been ferried downriver into Tarlang's Crown.Barrels can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown and the river Blackroot.

Elaglar has asked you to recover barrels stolen from Blackroot Vale in Tarlang's Crown.Recover stolen barrels from Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elaglar can be found in Dol Amroth.

You have retrieved many stolen barrels from Tarlang's Crown and should deliver them to Elaglar.'Based on what we have learned of the Corsair presence in Blackroot Vale and Belfalas, they seem to enjoy ferrying their supplies downriver. You mentioned that in Blackroot Vale, they sneakily stole goods away and sent them down the Blackroot.

'The time has come for us to reclaim what was stolen, ${PLAYER}. Travel to Tarlang's Crown and recover the barrels taken from Blackroot Vale by the Enemy.

'Be prepared to move carefully or gather your allies before you depart, ${PLAYER}.''Thank you for bringing these to me, ${PLAYER}. I shall see them returned to Blackroot Vale at once.

'If the Corsairs seek to steal more for their needs, I will know to call on you again.'The Corsairs of Umbar work in service of The Scourge and his ally, Azruthor, in Tarlang's Crown and present a constant threat to the people of Gondor.Corsairs can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown.

Elaglar has asked you to thin the numbers of the Corsair forces in Tarlang's Crown.Defeat Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elaglar can be found in Dol Amroth.

You have slain many Corsairs and should now report to Elaglar.Talk to Elaglar'We have heard that The Scourge has sent Corsair forces into Tarlang's Crown. While we are still unsure of their purpose there, I do not wish to wait to find out.

'Travel to Tarlang's Crown and defeat the Corsairs there. However, I would not go alone if I were you... you would do well to gather your allies before setting off!''Their numbers may recover in time, but you have dealt them a harsh blow this day!'Swelling from the waters of the Blackroot, darkwaters now wander Tarlang's Crown in service of the Heirs of Castamir.Darkwater can be found in and along the river Blackroot throughout Tarlang's Crown.

Elaglar has asked you to venture to Tarlang's Crown and defeat the darkwater under the thrall of the Heirs of Castamir.Defeat darkwater in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elaglar can be found in Dol Amroth.

You have defeated darkwater lurking in Tarlang's Crown and should report to Elaglar.Talk to Elaglar'My scouts have told me that vile things have been seen in Tarlang's Crown. The water of the Blackroot itself has risen against us and serves only to strengthen the already considerable forces there.

'If the water can be returned to the river, perhaps we can then mount a more successful assault on The Scourge's forces.''The Enemy is bold to summon our own rivers into battle against us, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for quieting the waters of the Blackroot once more.'At Tol Ascarnen, Taskmaster Raulik explained in his limited capacity that he desired to feast upon Elf-ears.Elves can be found within the Ettenmoors.

Taskmaster Raulik attempted to communicate that he wishes you to find Elves from which to cultivate their ears... a rare delicacy.'Kill Elves.

'Take ears.

'Food!''Taste good. Me eat now. Leave.'Upon arriving in the Ettenmoors, scouts were sent to the far corners in search of allies and enemies within the land. In the south, just across the Hoardale River, a secluded village of plump rat-folk was found, and the inhabitants there were found to be resistant to the forces of Angmar. It was also discovered that the folk were quite tasty.Rat-folk with fat round bellies are rumoured to live in a village far south beyond the Steps of Gram.

Taskmaster Fikdag wants you to make your way into the southern area of the Ettenmoors in search of rat-folk.Taskmaster Fikdag is at Dâr-gazag.

You slew the rat-folk with ease and now should return to Taskmaster Fikdag.'You little maggots make me want to vomit! Worthless sores on the hide of Mordirith's great army. Never killed before, never seen steel in the hands of a filthy târk, or Elf, or worse... a dwarf. You're nothing more than a heap of dung piled as high as you stand, and none will show you respect until you done proved yourself worthy.

'I don't see that happening, you worthless, good for nothing ${RACE}! You look like a slimy scum that crawled out from the deepest cave near the sludge spilling from the gutters in Carn Dûm! I've got to find something simple for a piss-ant like you to kill with ease... and I know just the things! We found them only recent-like, and they're a tasty bunch of rats. Not much fight in them, being as small as they are... might be a tough wrangle for you, though.

'Rat-folk with big bellies meant for stabbing live near the water in the wood south of here. Kill their farmers and gardeners, and if you don't fall on your face and break my cold black heart, return to me! Get a move on, you dung-hill rat!''Get out there and kill them rat-folk, you worthless gob of flesh! Hoarhallow is found south of here and across the Hoardale River.''Killed them did you? A fine start, ${RACE}. You may find yourself on the front lines someday, doing your service to the Iron Crown by being a body on the heap!

'Keep working like this, and we might find a way to promote you to the top of the filth-pile one day!'Though the rat-folk have proven a thorn in the side of Angmar's Army, they have also proven a viable source of food. Not only do the rat-folk have seemingly endless food-stores, but their flesh is sweeter than Man's.Hoarhallow lay to the south on the eastern side of the Hoardale River.

Taskmaster Fikdag at Dâr-gazag has grown fond of the flesh found on the bones of the rat-folk, and he has asked you to collect some of their legs.'One thing that the rat-folk have proven to be, ${PLAYER}, is a tasty source of food. Their flesh is sweet and soft, tasting better than the flesh of any Man I have ever eaten.

'I will tell you this, while you stalk through their trails and amongst their homes, be wary not to destroy the meat on their legs. If you return them to me, I will be sure to give you a worthy reward.''Ahh, a tasty treat to fill my belly. Their flesh is supple and slides from the bone with ease when boiled in a stew.

'Keep up your efforts here in the Ettenmoors, and one day I might share some of the stew with you, ${PLAYER}.'Bok captured himself one of the rat-folk one day, and he has proven a great asset. His toes tasted good when the goblin ate one, but the little man is a better cook than anything, and so they keep him alive to cook their meals. But this does not deter Bok from wanting to eat more rat-folk toes.Hoarhallow is far to the south-west on the eastern bank of the Hoardale River.

Bok waits for you to return to him with the hobbit-feet you were sent to harvest.'Caught me one of the rat-folk, I did. Tasty little morsel, sweet toes melting in the mouth. Can't have him! He's mine... ours, the Snowreap's! I'll call the trolls if you try to take him! But I tell Angmar's army how nice you be to Snowreap if you help me.

'Rat-folk has such tasty little toes, but this one makes such tasty little dishes with his little hands that we keeps him around to make our gruel better. The trolls like his food and eats less goblins, so we keeps him hidden. But I like their toes, the rat-folk toes.

'Get me their feets, get me the rat-folk feets, and I tells others how good you are to Snowreap!''You brought me feet! I tell everyone you help the Snowreap. Everyone I sees will know you helped us, filled my belly.

'Such a treat, a treat to eat the tasty rat-folk feet!'Dulglok commands you to gather some tasty slug goo to feed the war-leaders within Osgiliath.Slugs can be found in Osgiliath.

