'It is time! Time for the Finder's Gathering!''Come, ${PLAYER}. The Finder's Gathering begins. We wouldn't want to keep them waiting!'Melethon welcomes you to the battle for Osgiliath and orders you to assist him and the other captains in their efforts to retake the city.Gondorian captains can be found in the main strongholds of the Free Peoples.

You should speak with the other captains of the Gondorian army.Speak with CangorasSpeak with EdenosSpeak with Arthon'Osgiliath is under siege! We need all the able bodies we can muster to take back the city. This will not be easy though. You will indeed face hardship in the days to come.

'Though I am glad to fight along your side, you should report in to the other captains in Osgiliath. They will welcome your help in fighting off the foul creatures from the Morgul Vale.''Ah, you must be the new recruit! I am Captain Cangoras.

'When you're settled in, come speak to me and I'll have orders for you. There is much to do around here.''I am Captain Edenos, soldier. This is not a place for small talk. We are here to hold the Palace.

'When you're ready I will send you on missions to take back this city. Prepare yourself.''I am Captain Arthon. The Armoury holds for now but we are close to enemy territory. If the Armoury falls, it could spell disaster for our efforts. Help me to defend this point when you are able.'Explore the battleground of Osgiliath.Explore the battleground of Osgiliath.Discover the ArmouryDiscover the Belegiant BridgeDiscover the Londiant BridgeDiscover the Ornendil BridgeDiscover the Palace of EldacarDiscover the Eastern WharfDiscover Shrak MaurukGrazadhal commands you to defend the Belegiant Bridge from puny men who are trying to take it for themselves.The Belegiant Bridge is located in centre of Osgiliath over the Anduin River.

You should defend the centre of the Belegiant Bridge.Defend the centre of the Belegiant BridgeThe Belegiant Bridge is located in the centre of Osgiliath over the Anduin River.

You should keep your post and defend the centre of the Belegiant Bridge.Keep your post and defend the centre of the bridgeDo not leave the centre of the bridgeGrazadhal is at Dâr Dugoth.

You should listen to Grazadhal yell at you.Listen to Grazadhal yell at you'Can you believe this?! Men are trying to take the big bridge! You know, the one they call Belegiant. That's a foolish thing to do if ever I heard one.

'You go over there right now and stop those puny men. It's my bridge! If we don't get it back the Witch-king will have my head!''You've done good work. I don't have a problems with you right now, but don't push your luck. I still don't like you. Har, har!'Falastír, the friendly lighthouse keeper of the Cape of Belfalas, has agreed to show you around the coast.Falastír wants you to see the sites of the Cape of Belfalas.Visit the Cathlond, the cape docksVisit the Court of AnglindVisit the interior of NarvindonTake a boat to one of the islands off the coastVisit one of the smaller houses on the CapeVisit one of the standard sized houses on the CapeVisit one of the largest houses on the CapeFalastír is located at the lighthouse on the Cape of Belfalas.

You should let Falastír know that you have toured the Cape as he suggested.Talk to Falastír'The Cape of Belfalas is under rule of Dol Amroth and it has been this way since I can remember. Not that I have been to the city in many a long year. Ha, that is how it goes sometimes, I reckon!

'Some prefer the view from this rock or that hill, but in truth there is hardly a spot to stand in the Cape of Belfalas that does not show a lovely sight! You should explore and see it for yourself. I know you will enjoy every moment! Be sure to visit the stage, the docks, and either of the islands!''So, my new friend, what do you think of the Cape of Belfalas? Is it not the most relaxing place in all of Gondor - nay, of Middle-earth?'The Council of Gondor meets within the Dome of the Sun to decide matters of state. Their meetings have been more frequent of late as the situation in Gondor worsens.The Council of Gondor meets inside the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Othnar has invited you to enter the Dome of the Sun and lend your assistance to Arodor, chief scribe of the Council.Enter the Dome of the Sun, where the Council of Gondor holds its meetingsArodor is in the Dome of the Sun, writing resolutions recently decided by the Council of Gondor.Talk to Arodor in the Dome of the SunThe Dome of the Sun is filled with the scattered notes of the recent meeting of the Council.

Arodor asked if you would gather up the scattered papers within the Dome of the Sun.Gather the scattered papers in the Dome of the Sun (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arodor is in the Dome of the Sun.

You have gathered up the scattered papers that remained behind after the meeting of the Council of Gondor, and should bring them to Arodor.Arodor is in the Dome of the Sun, writing out the resolutions of the Council.Wait for Arodor to finish writing the Council ResolutionsArodor is in the Dome of the Sun.Talk to Arodor in the Dome of the SunYou have agreed to deliver resolutions of the Council to several leaders of the city throughout Minas Tirith:

Torchún, the Warden of the Houses of Healing.
Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison.
Celephir, the Warden of the Coffers.
Mirudil, the Warden of the Stores.Parthadan, the Warden of the Green, can be found in the Sixth Circle of the city.

Echadon asked you to find Parthadan once you finished delivering the Council resolutions throughout the city.Talk to Parthadan, Warden of the Green, in the south-east section of the Sixth CircleThalhír, the Warden of Laws, can be found in the Second Circle of the city.

Parthadan gave you a grim report of the situation in the Pelennor to show to Thalhír.Arodor is in the Dome of the Sun, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Thalhír asked you to deliver Parthadan's grim report to Arodor for filing.'Welcome, ${PLAYER}, to the Dome of the Sun. Word of your deeds is moving throughout the city like a fire in the brush. It sounds as if you have had many adventures, and saved many good folk from the swords and axes of evil! May you continue to do so on our behalf, worthy ${CLASS}!

'You have just missed a meeting of the Council, but if you go within you may be able to lend some aid to Arodor, chief scribe of the Council. The meetings have been contentious of late, and the number of raised voices I have heard from my position here has only increased in recent days. It seems no two voices can agree on a single course of action, for each member of the Council has his own interests to look after. Can they not see that we must be united if we are to survive the coming storm?

'Ah, I am just a doorward. It is not my place to speak so. There are some in the city who speak against the Council, but you will not find me speaking such sedition!''You have just missed a meeting of the Council, but if you go within you may be able to lend some aid to Arodor, chief scribe of the Council. The meetings have been contentious of late, and the number of raised voices I have heard from my position here has only increased in recent days.''You have just missed a meeting of the Council, but if you go within you may be able to lend some aid to Arodor. The meetings have been contentious of late, and the number of raised voices I have heard from my position here has only increased in recent days.''Yes? You must be ${PLAYER}, the ${CLASS} of whom Mithrandir speaks so highly. I am sorry to tell you that you have just missed a meeting of the Council. See the state in which they have left this place?

'I wonder if you might do me a favour? I need to finish organizing these papers. Perhaps you might gather up the rest of the notes scattered about the chamber? The members of the Council are masters of their various duties, but they trust that I will note down the matters of decision and do not stay behind to ensure I have recorded everything. I do my own duty as best I may, but I must ensure nothing slips by my notice amid the confusion.''I wonder if you might do me a favour? I need to finish organizing these papers. Perhaps you might gather up the rest of the notes scattered about the chamber? The members of the Council are masters of their various duties, but they trust that I will note down the matters of decision and do not stay behind to ensure I have recorded everything. I do my own duty as best I may, but I must ensure nothing slips by my notice amid the confusion.''Ah, thank you very much. Let me copy down any of the important matters from these papers, and then I will have another request for you. It will not be long.''There we go! I have finished writing out the Council of Gondor's most recent resolutions. Now I need someone to bring these throughout the city so the city leaders can take the appropriate action. Normally I would send an errand-rider, but if you'd like to meet some members of the Council perhaps you would like to perform this duty?

'Very good! Here is the stack of resolutions that will require immediate action. They are labeled with the correct recipient, do you see? Here is the list:

   Torchún, the Warden of the Houses of Healing.
   Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison.
   Celephir, the Warden of the Coffers.
   Mirudil, the Warden of the Stores.

'Thank you for this, ${PLAYER}. You will be doing the city a great service!''Thank you again for agreeing to deliver those resolutions, my friend. Here is the list of recipients:

   Torchún, the Warden of the Houses of Healing.
   Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison.
   Celephir, the Warden of the Coffers.
   Mirudil, the Warden of the Stores.

'You will be doing the city a great service!''That was very fast, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps you should become an errand-rider for the city! I suppose it would be difficult for you to leave the adventuring life behind, but prompt delivery of messages is something to be prized, and you seem quite skilled at it.

'As you know, I am the Warden of the Houses of Healing. At the Council-meeting that just concluded, I requested an increase in supplies and goods for the use of my healers: spare cloths, water for boiling, warm blankets. The Council agreed with the principle of my request, but not to its whole extent. I have been granted an increase, but a small one.

'It is better than no increase at all, I suppose. We will take blankets and cloths from evacuated houses, for their owners have no current need of them, and I will arrange with the Warden of the Wells to provide me with spare buckets.''Thank you for bringing this to me so quickly, ${PLAYER}. I am the Captain of the Garrison, which means the training and command of warriors in the city falls to me. I take this duty very seriously.

'At the latest Council meeting, I spoke on behalf of my men. The garrison lacks the weapons and armour needed to mount a true defence of the city, should our enemies breach the gate. Furthermore, we simply do not have enough men! To that end, I argued that the scouts should be recalled from the Pelennor and Talath Anor and put to work as part of the garrison. Parthadan did not like this suggestion. When you have finished with this duty, perhaps you can see if his temper has cooled?

'The Council did not agree with me, and there was much sympathy for the ideas of Parthadan. Still, the Guild of Smiths has been commanded to double its production of weapons and shields, so the men I do have can hope to be better equipped for the battle ahead. It is not everything for which I hoped, but it is something, at least.''I am grateful that you have brought the Council's resolution to me with such haste, ${PLAYER}. As the Warden of the Coffers, it is my duty to maintain the guard upon the treasury.

'To my relief, the Council agreed with my proposal that the guard upon the treasury doors be increased. If the city is soon besieged, as seems certain, the gravest threat to the coin of the city might not be the enemies outside the walls but the folk within them. Indeed, an unsavoury group has already begun speaking out against the Council and the Steward, and I am sure they would try and pilfer the treasury if given the opportunity.

'I thank you once more for bringing this resolution to me.''Ah, the Council resolutions are already written? That was very fast. It is good to see such haste, for it usually takes much longer for the orders of the Council to be put into action. Everyone is worried about what lies ahead, and it spurs them to move with haste.

'I am the Warden of the Stores, which means that all the food and goods brought into the city fall within the scope of my duty. I find where they can be stored safely and free from theft or spoilage, and ensure that the folk who need access to them have it.

'I must confess some trepidation to you, ${PLAYER}. If the city is besieged, I will surely become the most hated man in Minas Tirith. The man who rations the food is never loved by the hungry.

'This resolution will allow me to conduct a full inventory of the stores, so I will know how much food and other supplies we will have at our disposal. If the gates are sealed by war, that inventory may become very important indeed!''Echadon wanted you to speak with Parthadan? That is a good idea, ${PLAYER}. The two of them became quite heated during the last Council meeting, and those bridges ought to be repaired before the next.''Echadon sent you? I have nothing to say to him. As the Warden of the Green, it is my duty to preserve the townlands and its people. I refuse now as I refused then to call back the few scouts and guards that now defend them! They are the folk who will first face the swords and axes of the Orcs!

'Ah, I have recovered my temper. The Council dismissed his suggestion. That made me feel rather better.

'I have compiled a report of the situation on the Pelennor Fields. Can I trust you to deliver it to Thalhír, the Warden of Laws? Many of the farms there have been evacuated, and this report may help their owners receive recompense if their homes are destroyed by the Orcs. Thalhír can be found in the Second Circle of the city.''Can I trust you to deliver that report to Thalhír, the Warden of Laws? Many of the farms there have been evacuated, and this report may help their owners receive recompense if their homes are destroyed by the Orcs. Thalhír can be found in the Second Circle of the city.''What is this? It is a report concerning the land holdings of folk who had to abandon their homes on the Pelennor? I see. I suppose Parthadan is doing his duty to take care of the townlands by preparing this report, but I think he is dreaming if he thinks the city will repay the owners of these farms for any damage the Orcs inflict upon them.'

Thalhír snorts mirthlessly.

'He may be dreaming if he thinks there will be anyone left to repay them, ${PLAYER}. The word out of Osgiliath is not good, and the army arrayed against us sounds vast.

'Well, I promise nothing, but bring this report back to Arodor for filing. If we do survive the siege that must be coming, we may need paper to burn, and Parthadan's report may be good for that, at least.''Bring that report back to Arodor for filing. If we do survive the siege that must be coming, we may need paper to burn, and Parthadan's report may be good for that, at least.''Thank you very much, ${PLAYER}. Those Council resolutions will help the defenders of Minas Tirith work to safe-guard the city!

'I will take this report from you and make sure it is put in the proper place, but I share Thalhír's belief that we should first survive the battle before thinking about the aftermath!

'I am sure I will see you again, friend. Take care of yourself until then.'Vile sorcerers of Umbar serve Azruthor tirelessly and seek to bring forth more fell spirits in Tarlang's Crown.Umbarrim sorcerers can be found in Corsair encampments in Tarlang's Crown.

Gondren has asked you to defeat Umbarrim sorcerers to prevent them from bringing forth any more fell spirits in Tarlang's Crown.Defeat Umbarrim sorcerers in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Harnion can be found along the road through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas.

You have defeated many Umbarrim sorcerers and stopped them from summoning more vile fell spirits into Gondor. You should now return to Harnion.Talk to Harnion'I do not have much time, ${PLAYER}...

'...so should you wish to honour the last request of a dying man, heed my words! There are Men here that wield foul power - power that no man should ever have. I have seen it with my own eyes, ${PLAYER}... I have seen their sorcerers calling forth vile spirits of the same lot that took hold of the trolls.

'These Men alone could spell doom for Dol Amroth, and they must be defeated before their might grows beyond control. Go now, my friend... let us hope there are brighter days ahead....''Gondren's sacrifice may have saved us from ruin, ${PLAYER}. Without his aid, we would have learned of the Heirs' plans far too late to act against them.

'You have done well to weaken their reinforcements and break their resolve. Soon, my friend, we shall strike at Azruthor himself.

'Let us hope that his forces remain weakened when the time comes....'After shattering the lighthouse at Barad Rill, Balakhôr the Scourge has called Daxamat to the peak to look upon the lands he intends to claim.The Night-jewel deckhand can be found on the shore of Barad Rill.

Daxamat made landfall with his brethren at Barad Rill and then spoke to a deckhand.Talk to the Night-jewel deckhandThe lighthouse of Barad Rill can be found at the centre of the small shoal off the southern coast of Dor-en-Ernil.

The deckhand has directed Daxamat to enter the lighthouse and speak to the Scourge at his request.Enter the lighthouse of Barad RillThe peak of Barad Rill can be found by climbing the stairs in the ruin.

Daxamat searched Barad Rill for Balakhôr and climbed toward the top of the ruin.Meet the Scourge at the peak of Barad RillBalakhôr can be found atop Barad Rill.

Daxamat then went into Barad Rill to seek Balakhôr at the top.Talk to Balakhôr the ScourgeBalakhôr and the Black Blade of Lebennin can be found atop Barad Rill.

Daxamar is describing the meeting between one of the Nine and Balakhôr. You should listen to his tale.Observe the meeting of the Black Blade and BalakhôrBalakhôr seems lost in thought as his gaze falls on Dor-en-Ernil, but he swiftly notices your presence.'That took you a while...

'Currents a little rough for you today, Dax?'After shattering the lighthouse at Barad Rill, Balakhôr the Scourge has called Daxamat to the peak to look upon the lands he intends to claim.Daxamat can be found in the northernmost part of Hata Kebir in eastern Lebennin.

Daxamat has asked to share his account of an upsetting meeting he witnessed in Dor-en-Ernil. You should listen to his tale.Listen to Daxamat's recounting of his journey through Dor-en-ErnilDaxamat can be found in the northernmost part of Hata Kebir in eastern Lebennin.

Daxamat has finished telling the tale of his encounter with the Black Blade of Lebennin. You should speak to him.Talk to Daxamat in Hata Kebir'I ask again, brother, why have you come here?'

Jajax explains his desire to help Daxamat escape from the Heirs of Castamir before they bring themselves to ruin.

'You will have little trouble convincing me, Jajax, for I have seen things you would not believe... but it is one thing to wish to help me, and another entirely to steal me away under Azgarzôr's gaze.

'These grim clouds hide far worse things... terrible things that weigh heavily on me. Let me tell you my tale, and then we can speak of leaving this place.''Let me tell you my tale, ${CLASS}.''Now, do you understand? That terrible wraith, one of the Nine, looked upon Balakhôr as a mere tool... how lowly might the rest of us be in the Master's eye?

'Balakhôr has his mind set only on Pelargir, and I fear that if we fail to reach the Guarded City in time, there will be no place for our people to hide from the Dark Lord's gaze.

'I see no way off this course, brother, other than to flee.'Arvaethor has asked you to destroy any mysterious stones found within Ringló Vale and then meet him near the newly discovered mountain encampment of the Dead.Arvaethor can be found in the village of Ethring in Ringló Vale.

