Garvir has bid you speak to Tancestel, an old and superstitious man of Dor-en-Ernil, in the hope that he may have insight on these dire times.Talk to Tancestel'This bodes ill for us, ${PLAYER}.

'The Dead only serve to add to our troubles, and I now fear that any hope of an advantage has gone. I have thought much about what can be done to stop them, but nothing has proved worthwhile.

'Speak to my men, Glanion and Durnir. They are my only two remaining captains... perhaps they may see something where I have not.''How are we to defeat the Dead? Neither man nor beast can raise arms against them and Garvir knows this well. They simply vanish from sight when we think them wounded and reappear not long after - it is a fruitless endeavour! The only hope we have is that they pass over the Gilrain and leave us be!

'I say we hold as best we can against the Corsairs and Haradrim. At least a blade might wound them!''I do not see what can be done....

'Look to the sky, ${PLAYER}... hope is in short supply here, and most of our men have gone east to face down the growing darkness.

'We have no heroes here, no one left to protect the people... except for us. Who are we to stand against such numbers? The return of the Dead is just one last cruel jest....''I guessed as much, ${PLAYER}. It is hard to keep the men from despair in these dark days. I do not know what can be done... nothing outside of the Sisters in the stories of old could aid us now, but they are just that... stories.

