Explore the cisterns with Bergil, Gelwen, and Glatham, and search for a passage up to the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.Exit into the Fourth CircleIf you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you.

You have come out of the secret passage through the cisterns, to the Fourth Circle of the City. Gelwen again appears to have something she wishes to say.Talk to GelwenThe Finding Place lies near the cisterns' exit in the Fourth Circle.

The children have spotted something they call the "Finding Place." Walk over to it and see what it is. If you get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call the children to you.Investigate the Finding PlaceIf you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you.

Show Bergil the slightly crumpled letter you found in the crevice of the Finding Place.The Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.

Meet Bergil and the other children back at the Old Guest-house.'Now that I think of it, there may be a way around the Second Circle, but... no, we must try, and with your help, ${PLAYER}, maybe, just maybe, it can be done.

'You see, I have heard that within the City Cisterns, you may climb right up to the Fourth Circle - which is just where we wish to go! Only, we'd never be allowed in through the Clean-waters. Not by ourselves. Not whenever we pleased!

'There is a hidden entrance, though, by the Wrights' Fellow-hall, that is seldom used. And as it should happen, one of the keys for it was lost just last week. I know because I heard Master Carethon cursing out the lad who lost it. If it could be found - if you could find it - why then, we'd be one step closer to that secret passage, wouldn't we?''If you could find that key to the hidden cisterns' door, then we'd be one step closer to reaching the upper tiers. It must be somewhere near the Wrights' Fellow-hall that it was lost.''Ah, ${PLAYER}, I knew you would find it! While you have been searching, I have spoken with the others, and Gelwen and Glatham have asked if they can come along.

'Would you lead the three of us into the cisterns? Ah, but perhaps you should speak to Gelwen first.''This shall be a grand adventure, ${PLAYER}!''Then we shall meet within the hidden entrance to the cisterns? Good.''I hope my sister is right about the Secret Walker. But if she is going in there, then I will go, too!''What will we find, I wonder? Do you think a passage to the Fourth Circle truly exists?''I must confess, it is stranger and more wonderful than I had even imagined.''Oh... This is where all the water is!''See, Glatham? The Secret Walker didn't appear and the passage DID go through, and look! Do you see where we are? The Finding Place is very near. What fortune! We must go over to it at once!

'Come, ${PLAYER}. You will see for yourself!''Well, now my luck's taken a turn for the better!''Imagine, the Finding Place so near to the secret passage. We must go over to it at once.''The Finding Place! I wonder what we'll find in it this time.''What is it? What did you find?''Can I see?''What is this?'

Bergil takes the letter and examines it.

'Oh, by Queen Beruthiel's cats! It's a letter Landath was meant to deliver. He must have lost it. How did it end up here? Well, that's the wonder of the Finding Place.

'Never mind that. Let us go tell the others we have found a way up - and get Landath his letter. Maybe there's even still time for him to deliver it!''I plan to go through the secret passage as often as I can. The Fourth Circle! I do hope some of the poets or minstrels or stage players will still play, even though these are times of war.''Maybe Gelwen is right and the Secret Walker is just a tale. But how can we be sure?''We have set more than one thing right on this adventure, ${PLAYER}, and I am glad. But most of all, I am glad we can reach the Finding Place once again. We boys and girls have become used to looking in there - and the things we would find! Lost trinkets, sweets, a coin or two.

'I would have felt doubly ashamed, if I had cut all them off from that!

'But look at Landath over there, puzzling over the letter! I do wonder when Himnir's sweet treats will arrive. You must join us when they do.''Oh! Now that I am here, my doubts seem larger and my certainty smaller than it did before. But I shall be brave... so long as you lead the way before us. You are the grown adventurer and we are but children, after all, ${PLAYER}!''Gelwen is just over there. You really should speak with her before we go.''So you are ${PLAYER}. It is a pleasure to meet you. Bergil has told us of your adventure together and his plan.

'The others all think that the Secret Walker lives in the cisterns and are afraid to set foot inside. I think they are wrong, and that the Secret Walker is nothing but a story made to scare little girls and boys.

'In addition, I wish more than anything to see inside the cisterns. I imagine it must be wondrous and beautiful. Therefore, my brother and I wish to go with you. If you agree, then let us meet within the door.'Some of the slaves the Corsairs use to row their boats have been left in manacles around the area. Find them all and free them of their chains to set back any chance of a Corsair escape.

This quest starts with <rgb=#FFFF00>empty</rgb> Merit Rating.

<rgb=#00FF00>Merit Gain:</rgb>
* Free fettered ship-slaves
* Free all of them as swiftly as possibleFind and free ship-slaves who are manacled throughout the area.Liberated ship-slaves (${VALUE}/6)<rgb=#FF0000>Quest will finish on Corsair defeat.</rgb>Lady Vanyalos insists that the gardens and arbors of Imloth Melui recall the grandeur of Gondor in its youth, and wants you to remind her of their varied beauties.Lady Vanyalos has asked you to appreciate the many beautiful sights within Imloth Melui.Find the shaded path that overlooks the River EruiFind the Erui overlook, south-east of the Hall of the Gentle HandFind the bridge by the source of the Erui, north-west of Imloth MeluiFind the tall stone steps in the northFind the central fountainLady Vanyalos is in her hall on the north-east rise of Imloth Melui, waiting for you to return with descriptions of her city.Return to Lady Vanyalos in her hall'While you tread the paths of Imloth Melui, do not keep your eyes upon your feet! These fair arbors and gardens recall the grandeur of my kingdom's past. I have walked them many times since my youth, and to remember them is the sweetest respite.

'I ask  you to take note of the loveliest sights you see here. When you return to me, you may recount them and so I will relive the pleasures I knew, through your fresh eyes.'Lady Vanyalos listens intently as you describe your exploration of her city. When you are finished, she sighs happily.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I think I will sleep now, and perhaps I shall dream of the places you have described to me. I am quite transported, in time if not in place, to the years of my youth, when I saw those sights beneath sun-filled skies, with a sun-lit heart.'Heartened by your tales of the Sister of the Gilrain, the people of Lebennin hope to draw her forth and beg her aid.Melawen and Lendithil can be found in Malbarth.

Arvaeth has asked you to tell the people of Malbarth of your supposed meeting with the fabled Sister of the Gilrain.Tell Melawen the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of your encounter with RoamingstarTell Lendithil the <rgb=#FF0000>story</rgb> of your encounter with RoamingstarArvaeth can be found to the north-west of Malbarth in Lebennin.

You have told the folk of Malbarth and should now return to Arvaeth near the banks of the Gilrain.Talk to Arvaeth by the GilrainThe pile of river-stones can be found on the banks of the Gilrain to the north-west of Malbarth.

Arvaeth has asked you to disturb the pile of river-stones in an attempt to draw Roamingstar forth once more.Disturb the pile of river-stonesArvaeth can be found to the north-west of Malbarth along the banks of the Gilrain in Lebennin.

Roamingstar did not come to the river's edge. You should speak to Arvaeth about what is to be done.Talk to ArvaethBarchir can be found in Malbarth in western Lebennin.

Although you could not call Roamingstar forth, Arvaeth still believes your tale. You should return to Barchir.Talk to Barchir in Malbarth'It has been told that there were once Sisters who watched over the lands of Lebennin, each of them inhabiting one of our great rivers. Five Sisters there were, but long has it been since any have shown their faces to our people.

'The Sister of the Gilrain is said to watch over our lands here in Malbarth, and few venture into the forest up-river for we consider them sacred. In your time at Linhir, did you learn of the Sisters?'

You tell Arvaeth of your meeting with Roamingstar and the power she wielded over the river Gilrain.

'I... even I began to doubt, ${PLAYER}. If you speak true, this will be a time of great upheaval and rebirth in Lebennin. Go back to the others! You must tell them of our Sister's return!''You are the first we have known of in ages who claims to have seen one of the Sisters, much less spoken to one.

'If you could call her forth before my folk, I do not think the darkest night could break our spirits.

'Disturb the pile of stones we have placed at the river's edge and perhaps she will honour us all by revealing herself!''Do not worry, my friend.

'I still believe you and I would have my folk do the same. I shall tell them of her return to our lands and inspire hope in my kin.

'I think it is time you returned to Barchir, ${PLAYER}... the war in the east only worsens with each passing moment and you are needed there.''The Sisters have returned?

'I am still not certain I can believe one so new to our lands, but I wish it true.

'Now then, we must speak of the conflict in the east.'Dindal fears the Orc raiding parties that come out from Harlond. Though they are small, they may discover Lossarnach's weak points and report back to the larger force.There are wooded areas west of the Harlond and the road leading up to it.

Dindal has suggested that you start smoky fires at old camp-fire sites in wooded areas near the Harlond, in order to lure Orc raiding parties to you in small groups.Start smoky fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.

You should return to Dindal and let him know that his plan worked.Talk to Dindal'I will tell you what I fear most. It is not the Orc-host below us, for they look north. No, it is the raiding parties I have seen. Though small in numbers, what they may glean and report back... where we lie undefended and un-pillaged, what farm remains yet unburned... these are troublesome thoughts.

'There are abandoned scouts' camp-fires in the wooded groves along the mountain's feet. If you built smoky fires in these, you might draw small parties of Orcs towards you, and dispatch them before they could go farther south.''The fires worked as I hoped? This is wonderful news. You have made the Orc host blind and deaf to our lands to the south.'Discover the Beacons of Central & Eastern Gondor.Discover the Beacons of Central & Eastern Gondor.Discover EilendothDiscover Dol BrannorDiscover AnglebedDiscover SirthancDiscover MinlosIorlas has been tasked with tidying up the baths at the Southern Great Guest-house. He is upset to receive such a lowly task but is glad to have your company in getting the job done as quick as possible.The Southern Great Guest-house is near the Citadel.

You should seek out the baths in the Southern Great Guest-house.Seek out the baths in the Southern Great Guest-houseIorlas can be found at the Southern Great Guest-house near the Citadel.

You should speak to Iorlas.Speak with IorlasThe Southern Great Guest-house is near the Citadel.

You should collect dirty cloths from the baths.Collect dirty drying cloths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Southern Great Guest-house is near the Citadel.

You should clean the cloths in a bucket.Wash the cloths in a bucket (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Southern Great Guest-house is near the Citadel.

You should rinse the cloths in a water bucket.Rinse the cloths in a water bucket (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iorlas can be found at the Southern Great Guest-house near the Citadel.

You should speak to Iorlas.Speak with Iorlas'You are correct, I am Iorlas. What brings you to the Gate of the Citadel?'

You explain Ormatar's orders and Iorlas looks increasingly displeased.

'While I appreciate your visit, I can't say I appreciate these orders from Ormatar. This is a disgrace, but I must accept any orders from him. Still, a guard of the Citadel is not usually on cleaning duty. What did I do to deserve this?'

You explain that the Citadel staff is short-handed and Ormatar needs guards to help out.

'I see. Well, perhaps you wouldn't mind coming with me then. The work will go quicker with the two of us. Let us meet at the baths in the Southern Great Guest-house when you are ready.''If we must do this, then so be it.''Welcome to the baths of the Southern Great Guest-house. It is a rather lovely area when you do not have work to do. I bet you my brother gets all the easy jobs from Ormatar. He is probably sitting at The Splintered Shield, drinking a pint with his Halfling friend. I'm not even supposed to be in the Citadel today. It was only Ormatar's chore that brought me here.

'Well, I suppose we should get to it then.''We finished! I shall complain about my day to my brother the next time I see him. I apologize for taking my frustration out on you. These are difficult times and I feel like I'm often ignored by both my family and superiors.'Concerned by the unusual tactics of the Haradrim, Lady Terenis hopes you and Lord Angbor can uncover their vile designs before it is too late.Lord Angbor can likely be found somewhere near the Crossings of Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.

Lady Terenis has asked you to speak to Lord Angbor about the Haradrim forces near the Erui.Talk to Angbor near the Crossings of EruiHalach can be found in south-eastern Upper Lebennin along the Anduin.

Angbor has asked you to secure the southern settlements of Upper Lebennin and uncover the plans of the Haradrim before rejoining him in Lossarnach.Travel south to HalachSurvivors may be found somewhere within Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have arrived at the ruined settlement of Halach, and should now search for survivors.Search the ruins of Halach for any survivors'As I said, I believe this is a matter best left to you and Lord Angbor. The Haradrim pose a dire threat to the people seeking refuge in Tumladen as well as all that dwell within Lossarnach. We must discover what has divided their forces near the Erui!

'Lord Angbor is a man of battle, and I trust he will know what is best. He has since departed Tumladen, but you may find him by the Crossings of Erui if he and his men have not yet crossed into Lossarnach.

'May you be swift, ${PLAYER}.''Ah, ${PLAYER}. What has kept you?'

You tell Lord Angbor of the Haradrim's unusual behaviour at the beacon Minlos and Lady Terenis's concerns.

'If their forces became divided at the river, perhaps more of their number have fled into the trees in the south. I know of a settlement to the south called Halach... but my men and I will not travel so far south as we advance to the east. Yet, for once I agree with the Lady, the Haradrim in Upper Lebennin must be defeated if we are to leave these lands behind.

'I ask that you travel to Halach and aid the people there if you are able. It seems we must part ways again, my friend, but let us hope that our paths will align in Lossarnach!''Few come willingly to Halach these days, traveller.

'The Haradrim seek to oust us from our homes, but they shall not succeed... not while I or the rest of the folk that remain still draw breath.

'If you will help us, we would be honoured to count a ${CLASS} among our number.'Read the plaques on the statues of kings and stewards in Minas Tirith.Read the plaques on the statues of kings and stewards in Minas Tirith.Complete The Line of Kings deedComplete The Stewards of Gondor deedRead the plaques on the statues of the stewards of Gondor.Read the plaques on the statues of the stewards of Gondor.Find the plaque of Steward Mardil VoronwëFind the plaque of Steward EradanFind the plaque of Steward HerionFind the plaque of Steward BelegornFind the plaque of Steward Húrin IFind the plaque of Steward Túrin IFind the plaque of Steward HadorFind the plaque of Steward BarahirFind the plaque of Steward DiorFind the plaque of Steward Denethor IFind the plaque of Steward Boromir CharnFind the plaque of Steward Cirion GwaedhirFind the plaque of Steward HallasFind the plaque of Steward Húrin IIFind the plaque of Steward Belecthor IFind the plaque of Steward OrodrethFind the plaque of Steward Ecthelion I MinasturFind the plaque of Steward EgalmothFind the plaque of Steward Beren IthrondilFind the plaque of Steward Beregond BelechestFind the plaque of Steward Belecthor II OrndilFind the plaque of Steward ThorondirFind the plaque of Steward Túrin IIFind the plaque of Steward TurgonFind the plaque of Steward Ecthelion II ThandirThandor suspects that someone in the abandoned district knows the location of Lorvegil, and has asked you to find him.The bandit leader can be located in the abandoned district to the north-east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should negotiate with the bandit leader.Negotiate with the bandit leaderThandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.

You should speak with Thandor.Talk to Thandor'Every group has men who know about all sorts of rumour and gossip. These ruffians are some of the only witnesses left to the fall of the city, so I'm sure that one of them knows something about where Lorvegil is hiding.

'If you can enter the abandoned district that's located in the east-garth of Pelargir, then I'm sure you'll find someone who has more information. They might not hand it over right away, but I suspect you could remedy that problem.''Ah, so the fancy Lord sends his little stooge to parley? You're making me laugh!

'Sure I know where your precious little noble is hiding out. But I ain't saying a thing unless the price is right!

'Oh you didn't come to bargain? Guess we'll have to settle this the only other way!''So that's where he is hiding. I can only imagine what will go through his head when he realizes how easily these curs sold him out for nothing. I guess even traitors can't buy loyalty.

'We will need to make preparations if we are to apprehend him. I shall offer my counsel to Faltharan, and hope that he accepts it. I thank you for your service to this city, ${PLAYER}.'Aside from a few guards, all occupants of Pelennor Fields have been evacuated except for one very stubborn farmer.Talfadan can be found at Pel Dúven, north-east of the South-gate.

You should try and talk some sense into Talfadan.Speak with TalfadanFarming tools can be found around Pel Dúven.

You should gather the farming tools for Talfadan.Collect farm tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF0000>Look around</rgb> for any more farm tools.<rgb=#FF0000>Look around</rgb> for any more farm toolsThe last farm tool is located in the fields at Pel Dúven.

Collect the final farm tool for Talfadan.Collect the final farm tool for TalfadanTalfadan is at Pel Dúven.

Return to Talfadan with the farm tools.Bring the farm tools to Talfadan'I am hoping you have a moment to assist me. I have too few men to turn their attention to every problem arising on the southern Pelennor.

'I have just gotten word that not everyone has been evacuated from the farms in Pelennor. It seems there is one farmer, a very old and stubborn man, who refuses to leave one of the nearby farms.

'You must convince him to retreat to Minas Tirith. It is too dangerous right now to risk a trip past the Harlond to Imloth Melui!''What's that?! I'm not leaving this farm! I've been farming here since before you were born! You'll have to drag me out of here, I tell you!'

The farmer calms down a little after you explain the grave danger he is about to face.

'Well, I don't see anything off in the distance. Hmm, you do seem like you're telling the truth though. Tell you what, if you help me finish my work then maybe I'll think about heading over to the White City.

'That's correct. Help me finish putting away my tools. Then we'll talk.''What took you so long? Did you step on a rake?'

You ask Talfadan if he saw the Haradrim that just tried to attack the farm.

'Oh, so that's what was going on there. I suppose that isn't a good thing, having the farm attacked and all. Back when I was a boy, no one ever attacked this farm. What's this land coming to?!'Grazadhal doesn't like that you showed up late and orders you to traverse the city to assist captains in their reach for favour from the Dark Lord.Orc captains can be found in the main strongholds of the Morgul army.

You should speak with the other Orc captains of the Morgul army.Listen to Dulglok give you ordersListen to Shíktarb give you ordersListen to Khúrhosh give you orders'You're late maggot! We already have a hold on this city. Soon those foolish men will run away or die by my sword!

'What?! You're still standing here. Go get some order from the other war-leaders or I'll send you on a mission to your death! Har, har!''What's this?! Another measly recruit?! Bah, I don't have time for you.

'Better make yourself useful or I'll deal with you myself!''Of course I'm Shíktarb. Do you see anyone else of importance around here?

'You want to work for me and kill those rotten men, I'll work you to the bone!''Those pesky men are just on the other side of the river! I've held this post by myself before and I'll do it again if I have to!

'If you want to stick around, better make yourself useful!'The slain body of a Sûhalar leads you on the trail of a mysterious Sûhalar slayer.The slain Easterling can be found on the roadside in Talath Anor.

You should investigate the body.Investigate the bodyTolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.

You should speak with Tolwin.Speak with TolwinThis Easterling had definitely been slain recently, but by whom and are they still nearby?Whoever slew this Sûhalar warrior managed to strike him dead with one blow!'The people look up to me here but I am just a boy. Perhaps it is in my blood since father was the lord of Cair Andros.'

You ask Tolwin about his excellent fighting techniques.

'I come from a family trained well in the art of war. I learned combat from a very early age. Still, it was not enough against such a powerful man as the one they call The First Blade.'The battle in the Ettenmoors is endless. Captain-General Tordúr bids all speak with him before venturing into the badlands beyond the safety of Glán Vraig. There are rewards to be had for the battles ahead.Speak with Captain-General Tordúr.Speak with Captain-General Tordúr'Before you venture back out, ${PLAYER}, visit Captain-General Tordúr. He offers rewards for those willing to fight in this harsh land.''${PLAYER}, it is good that you have come. The land beyond the stairs of Glân Vraig teems with enemies. We must remain diligent in our battle against them lest they breach our walls and ravage the civilized lands.

'If you wish to earn armaments commissioned for the defenders of these lands, take this and meet the enemies on the field of battle. Your efforts will not go unrewarded.'Corsair scouts have snuck up from behind and spotted our position. If they can get off three blows of their horn, reinforcements will come running! (Three scouts, one after the other, will attempt to blow their horn three times.)

This quest starts with <rgb=#FFFF00>empty</rgb> Merit Rating.

<rgb=#00FF00>Merit Gain:</rgb>
* Defeat scouts before third horn-blow 
  (with as few horn-blows as possible)Keep scouts from blowing their horns three times.Defeated scouts (${VALUE}/3)<rgb=#FF0000>Successful alarms raised: (${VALUE}/3)</rgb>Rathon has been tasked with maintaining many of the cisterns in Minas Tirith by himself but continues to work towards helping his fellow Gondorians where he can.Mushrooms can be found within the cisterns.

You should collect mushrooms for Rathon.Collect mushrooms from the cisterns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Rathon.Speak with RathonThe Foodmongers' Fellow-hall on the First Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should bring the mushrooms to a rations chest outside of the Foodmongers' Fellow-hall.Bring the mushrooms to the rations chest'I do not know if you have been to any of the Minas Tirith food stores as of late but just one look at them and you will see that they will not feed the city for a long war. Nearby farms are now burnt by the enemy or inaccessible. Now look at me, I sound like a doomsayer!

'Never mind all that talk of gloom. Sometimes you can find hope in the most unlikely of places. There is particular, tasty, white mushroom that usually only grows in the caves of Mount Mindolluin. Now they grow in the cisterns! I suspect the cave-lizards may have helped spread the mushrooms from the caves high above us to the cisterns. Perhaps they have done us some good after all! This mushroom has been growing so well in the cisterns that I believe we can start harvesting it. Would you be kind enough while you're in the tunnels to pick some?''What a harvest! Great work! I had already let the Foodmongers' Fellow-hall know about the mushrooms. They have set up a collection box in front of their guild hall. If you would kindly take the mushrooms there, the guild will then dry them and prepare them for the food stores.'With the Ruthless Dead and the Orcs working side by side, Arvaethor tasks you with causing disorder in the mountain pass encampment.Ruthless Dead and Orcs can be found in the mountain pass encampment in the north-western part of Ringló Vale.

Defeat Ruthless Dead and Orcs in Dâr Matum.Defeat Ruthless Dead at Dâr Matum (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orcs at Dâr Matum (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ruthless Dead captainArvaethor can be found near a mountain pass encampment in the north-western part of Ringló Vale.

You should speak with Arvaethor.Speak with Arvaethor'Can you feel the chill in the air? It is not a coldness but something much more evil.

'This old mountain pass is crawling with the Dead and Orcs. I shall have your back and guard the base of the pass while you ascend the old ruins. I know not what we will find up there. Good luck my friend!''So there is another crevasse into the mountain atop of the old ruins. What ever is raising the Orkish forces and rallying the dead must be dwelling within.'Having assisted the Free Peoples in their battle against the war-host of Angmar, you have earned much respect. The respect you earn entitles you to receive rewards from Quartermaster Ash at Glân Vraig.Quartermaster Ash is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors.

Ash sent you to earn tokens of valour by assisting members of the Free Peoples.'Do you see this? This is my Orc-cleaver. I was given this by Captain-General Lainedhel himself. That's right, this weapon was cooled in the rapids of the Noisewater in Rivendell. It barters for roughly one-hundred and ten beryls. It's got a sturdy oaken shaft and hardened Elf-steel blade. With me on the job, it's ready to fight at any moment.

'Now I know you are wondering how you can come by such a masterful piece of work. Well, I'll tell you: Valour. You prove your valour to the Free Peoples, and I'll see that you're fairly rewarded. No, you can't touch my blade. Your primitive mind wouldn't understand the relation of woods and alloys... things like magic.

'You want one of these types of weapons, you will need to earn it. Return to me when you've acquired enough tokens of valour, and we'll talk.''You got them all... excellent work! This key opens the chests behind me. I know what you're thinking: "What am I supposed to do? Open one chest, what?"

'I can solve this for you simply. The key will only open one chest. You want to open more, you need more keys. You want more keys... you go through me. You got that?

'All right. These are treasures found while we fight this war. Do yourself a favour and don't ask from where they came.'In the absence of Gilgír, the Lord of Anórien, Dúneth and Tolwin vow to rebuild Talath Anor.Tolwin can be found in the hall at Crithost.

You should speak with Tolwin.Speak with TolwinCeveneth is in the hall at Crithost.

You should speak with Ceveneth.Speak with CevenethIngold can be found at the North-gate.

You should return to Ingold and speak with him about your adventures in Talath Anor.Speak with Ingold'I know you must depart, for the enemy marches south from Cair Andros towards Minas Tirith. You must defend the White City from the forces of Mordor. Do not fear, we shall be able to hold our own at Crithost.'

You vow to Dúneth and all the people of Talath Anor to return after the battle and help her retake Cair Andros. You do not know when you will be able to fulfill this promise but you assure her that you will keep it.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Your vow means much to me. It is what Gilgír would have done and would have wanted. I shall await your return, brave ${RACE}. Please make sure to speak to Tolwin before you leave.''${PLAYER}, you were gone longer than expected. You say you were able to help establish a Gondorian stronghold in Crithost? That is good news.

'While Cair Andros may be lost, we still hold a patch of ground in Talath Anor. Slowly we will push the enemy back.

'Perhaps it would be wise of you to return to Minas Tirith. I am sure there are those in the city that could use your aid. I shall remain here to hold the North-gate for the arrival of the Rohirrim.''You would not believe it but those saplings you brought back are growing better in Crithost than they were in the orchard! I'll see to it that these fields are as beautiful and plentiful as they once were.

'It's a shame you have to leave so soon but I do understand. This is a hard time for everyone in Gondor and the White City needs as many able warriors as they can get.

'Good luck and don't be a stranger around here in more peaceful times!''I shall always remember this day. You have taught me much, ${PLAYER}, in our short time together. I shall continue to practice my fighting techniques until we meet again.

'Thank you again for your assistance in finding my mother and reuniting me with the family I still have. You should make sure to speak with Ceveneth before you head south. Farewell, my friend.'Borhador asks for you to tend to the beacon of Eilendoth.The beacon of Eilendoth is located south-west of Ethring in Ringló Vale.

You should climb the hill to the beacon.Climb the hill to the beacon of EilendothThe beacon of Eilendoth is located south-west of Ethring in Ringló Vale.

Defeat spiders at Eilendoth.Defeat spiders at Eilendoth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The beacon of Eilendoth is located south-west of Ethring in Ringló Vale.

You should speak with Authest, the caretaker at Eilendoth.Speak with Authest'When my son Dervorin answered the call in my stead, I promised to keep the beacon of Eilendoth burning bright in his absence. The beacon's light signifies my son's safe return. I fear the darkness that swept over the land is choking the beacon's flame. The air we breathe is growing stale. If the flame falls, surely we are next.

'The beacon has been slowly waning. I see it dim with each passing day. Will you tend to the beacon? I will be grateful if you are able to restore its light to the former brilliance I remember. I assure you, Ethring could use the light in this hour.''I thought my time had come! I have not seen such creatures of that size before!'Arodor asks you to survey the damage done by the Morgul-host.Faramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath.

You should speak with Gladhir at Faramir's Look-out.Speak with GladhirFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath.

You should look at Osgiliath from Faramir's Look-out.Faramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath.

You should talk to Mírthel at Faramir's Look-out about what you saw.Speak with MírthelFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath.

You should look at the Morgul Vale from Faramir's Look-out.Faramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath.

You should talk to Arodor at Faramir's Look-out about what you saw.Talk to Arodor'The enemy gather all around us, yet we remain hidden. We are cut off from the Rangers of Northern Ithilien and those in Osgiliath. Speak with the other Rangers here and see for yourself what has become of this land.''${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. My patrol and your errand have brought us to the same place.

'This flag of Gondor, you see here, we fly as a beacon of hope to those trapped in Osgiliath. I hope that Faramir and his garrison are still alive. Look at the destruction down there in Osgiliath.''I was not sure I would see you again, but Gladhir speaks highly of you. He and I came to the cross-roads following a Haradrim chieftain. We lost him after he entered Osgiliath. Now my gaze has turned to the Morgul Vale, and the lands beyond. Look at the red skies of Mordor. The unearthly glow frightens me.''Now that you have spoken to the other Rangers here and have seen the destruction for yourself, you can understand how dire the situation is. Perhaps you will be able to assist us in devising a plan of action?'Túmir the merchant needs to retrieve a shipment of wine for Calembel, but Corsairs got between him his goal.The wine cellar is located in the village of Gaerlond.

You should enter the wine cellar.Enter the wine cellarThe drunk corsairs can be found in the wine cellar in Gaerlond.

You should defeat the drunk corsairs.Defeat drunk Corsairs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wine can be found in the wine cellar in Gaerlond.

You should retrieve any unopened wine bottles for Túmir.Retrieve any unopened wine bottles for TúmirTúmir can be found in the village of  Gaerlond.

You should return to Túmir with the bottle of wine.Return to Túmir with the bottle of wine'Yes, hello there kind adventurer. The name's Túmir. Perhaps you could help me out. I was on my way to Calembel but I needed to pick up a shipment of wine from a man in Gaerlond first. Misfortune struck this town and now Corsairs are between me and the wine cellar.'

You are suspicious of this Túmir fellow, but wish to see him on his way and out of conflict.

'I assure you I have already paid the man in full for the wine. I am not... dishonest. I know roads that others do not. You needn't worry about my safety in travelling to Calembel.

'Will you help retrieve my wine before those unruly Corsairs consume it all?''Just one bottle? I see. What was your name again?

'Thanks, ${PLAYER}, I guess.... Well I must be going now.'With the siege now fully underway, the group calling itself the Withered Tree has become even more brazen. The Council of Gondor has tasked you with helping curb its rise.Húrin is in the besieged city, in the Dome of the Sun.

Lamlor believes you should ask Húrin to change the pass-words for the gates in the upper Circles of the city.

<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Talk to Húrin in the besieged city, in the Dome of the SunYou carry new pass-words for the Gate of the Citadel, the Gate of Stones, and the Gate of Stars.

Húrin has sent you to deliver the new pass-words for the gates in the upper Circles of the city.

<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Deliver the new pass-word to Linharn at the Gate of the CitadelDeliver the new pass-word to Garthor at the Gate of StonesDeliver the new pass-word to Doronir at the Gate of StarsYou carry new pass-words for the Gate of the Citadel, the Gate of Stones, and the Gate of Stars.

Húrin has sent you to deliver new pass-words for the gates in the upper Circles of the city.

<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>Destroy the parchment containing the new pass-wordsSome of the citizens of Gondor in the Fourth Circle may actually be supporters of the Withered Tree.Investigate the Fourth Circle of the city for supporters of the Withered TreeSome of the citizens of Gondor in the Third Circle may actually be supporters of the Withered Tree.Investigate the Third Circle of the city for supporters of the Withered TreeSome of the citizens of Gondor in the Second Circle may actually be supporters of the Withered Tree.Investigate the Second Circle of the city for supporters of the Withered TreeLamlor, the Captain of Tidings and Spy-master of Gondor, has come down to the gate in the First Circle.Talk to Lamlor at the City Gates, in the First Circle'The siege is well and truly begun, ${PLAYER}. We must hope that our preparations were enough, and that the gate stands strong. It should hold the enemies outside at bay for some hours, I hope, but it is the enemies within our walls that concern me right now.

'Look at the model of the city, and the scroll that now decorates it. This message is the work of the Withered Tree. 'The End Has Come?' That may be so, but I am going to ensure that the Withered Tree reaches its end before we do! Some member of that group gained access to the Dome of the Sun and committed this act while we were busy elsewhere.

'I am the Captain of Tidings, and I send forth errand-riders throughout the city and to other parts of Gondor, but that is not my only title. I am also the Spy-master of Minas Tirith, and I know how a group like the Withered Tree operates. They must have gained some of the pass-words for the upper Circles of the city. Húrin must change the pass-words, ${PLAYER}. We have not used the current set for as long as usual, but in time of war three hours may seem like days! Ask him for new pass-words, and give them to the guards at the gates in the upper Circles. Then find members of the Withered Tree in the lower Circles and make them cease their hateful whisperings! I will meet you in the First Circle when you have proved successful.''Captain of Tidings is not my only title. I am also the Spy-master of Minas Tirith, and I know how a group like the Withered Tree operates. They must have gained some of the pass-words for the upper Circles of the city. Húrin must change the pass-words, ${PLAYER}. We have not used the current set for as long as usual, but in time of war three hours may seem like days! Ask him for new pass-words, and give them to the guards at the gates in the upper Circles. Then find members of the Withered Tree in the lower Circles and make them cease their hateful whisperings! I will meet you in the First Circle when you have proved successful.''I have already written a new set of pass-words for the gates into the upper Circles of the city. Show them to the guards and then destroy this parchment. Perhaps that will hinder the movement of the Withered Tree into the upper levels.

'After the pass-words have been set, Lamlor wants you to find members of the Withered Tree urging dissent in the lower Circles? If you will be able to recognize them, I suppose. They have become more brazen in recent days, and now that the siege has begun I suppose they have nothing more to lose. They may be obvious to you now, ${PLAYER}.

'Go with haste, and remain loyal to the Council and to the Steward!''Show those pass-words to the guards and then destroy this parchment. Perhaps that will hinder the movement of the Withered Tree into the upper levels.

'After the pass-words have been set, Lamlor wants you to find members of the Withered Tree urging dissent in the lower Circles? If you will be able to recognize them, I suppose. They have become more brazen in recent days, and now that the siege has begun I suppose they have nothing more to lose. They may be obvious to you now, ${PLAYER}.

'Go with haste, and remain loyal to the Council and to the Steward!''Already a new pass-word? Very well, ${PLAYER}. I recognize Húrin's mark, and I will see to it that no one passes this gate save those who know the pass-word: <rgb=#00FF00>Light of Hope</rgb>.

'It is an appropriate pass-word. May we still possess that of which it speaks when the night ends!''I believed we would soon need new pass-words. This is Húrin's mark, and now I will recognize only the new pass-word: <rgb=#00FF00>Flame of Victory</rgb>.

'I hope it is our victory, and not the victory of Mordor, that this pass-word presages!''A new pass-word, already? I think the time for pass-words is behind us, ${PLAYER}! The Orcs of Mordor will not turn away from my gate because they lack the pass-word! But this is Húrin's mark, and I am bound to obey. The new pass-word will be: <rgb=#00FF00>Triumphant</rgb>.

'But whose triumph will it be, I wonder?''Supporters of the Withered Tree may be lurking within the lower Circles of the city. Search among the citizenry for such dangerous men!''The Steward is a fool! He has sold the city to our enemies, and now he asks us to die for him? None of us will see the dawn!

'Die, ${PLAYER}, and know that the Withered Tree has ended your tale!''Supporters of the Withered Tree may be lurking within the lower Circles of the city. Search among the citizenry for such dangerous men!''How will we survive the coming storm? Can there be any hope?''There is no hope for us! The Council of Gondor and the Steward have failed, and doomed this city to fall! Can you not hear the harsh cries from beyond the walls?

'We should have listened to the Withered Tree, and cast these leaders from the highest level of Minas Tirith! Perhaps then we would have been spared!''Supporters of the Withered Tree may be lurking within the lower Circles of the city. Search among the citizenry for such dangerous men!''The armies of the Enemy press close about the walls! How can there be any victory against such numbers?''We must open the gates! Have you not seen the parchments that the Withered Tree has placed throughout the city? The host of Mordor will spare us if we open the gates! The Orcs only want the Steward and the Council; they will allow the common folk to live if we let them in!

'It is wisdom! We must open the gates! I will kill you if you try to stop me!''Will the gates hold? I have never seen such evil, not in all my days!''You found supporters of the Withered Tree throughout the lower Circles of the city? I knew you would, ${PLAYER}. There are more and more of them with every passing hour! I have been kept quite busy keeping them away from the gate. Can you believe they think they will find mercy with the armies of Mordor? They are disloyal and foolish both!

'Keep fighting for Gondor, ${PLAYER}, and I will do the same, 'gainst any and all foes!'Saddened by the harm inflicted on the Gilrain's banks, Roamingstar hopes to heal the lands of Gondor before confronting the Ruthless Dead.A bucket can be found on the banks of the Gilrain in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

Roamingstar has asked you to aid her in healing the lands of Dor-en-Ernil by using the waters of the Gilrain.Search for a bucket near the mere outside Roamingstar's gladeWar-torn earth can be found in and around Roamingstar's glade.

Roamingstar has asked you to aid her in healing the lands of Dor-en-Ernil.Heal war-torn earth near Roamingstar's glade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.

You have healed the earth wounded by the war in Gondor and should now return to Roamingstar.Talk to Roamingstar'I have brought you here because I sense goodness within you, ${RACE}. You seek an end to the conflict that ravages my lands and burdens my people, as do I.

'Few still hold sincere belief in my sisters and fewer still have looked upon me in many long years. Of those that did... one came to regret it and I feel the shame still.

'Now these wounds lay bare as the Men from Umbar pollute and defile my lands. My waters can heal their destruction, but I cannot do this alone. Aid me, and I shall aid you in turn!''You have done well to heal the wounds of Men, ${PLAYER}. These outsiders have no love for our lands or the people within and will not stop until it all lies wilted and dead, but I shall do all I can to hold them back from the innocent.

'In all I have witnessed, few other times have come with such destruction and bloodshed. Let us hope that this one shall soon come to an end....'Someone within Dol Amroth has sold the city out and sided with the Corsairs.The traitor is likely hanging around near the Great Hall.Find and defeat the traitorFandmau prepares the defence of Tírith Rhaw against the Free Peoples.Slaughter the Free Peoples within the bounds of Tírith Rhaw.

Fandmau seems unimpressed with your capability, but you can show him that you are more of a soldier of Angmar than he.Slaughter the Free People in Tírith Rhaw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})If Fandmau was killed or Tírith Rhaw was lost, make your way to War-tyrant Akúlhun at Gramsfoot.

Fandmau's fears were unfounded. You repelled the attack and scored a great victory over the Free People. You should return to him with your report.'The people are coming. Pests with pointy sticks and arrows. We're not ready, I keep telling the tyrant. We only have you pathetic wretches to stand against them.

'We need your bodies, either to cast at the enemy as they draw near... or to stack in the entry way to seal it shut. I've seen you fight, and we'll not last with you on the defence, or so says I.

'The tyrant thinks otherwise and bids me offer you favour should you defeat a goodly number of the enemy when they come rushing to the tower. Stand against them and earn his favour... or prove me right, and we'll toss your body in the hall to stop their progress.''Proving my point about you already, standing here talking instead of preparing for battle. You are a hopeless wretch!''Survived! We survived, and you did well. I was wrong... wrong and you proved it.

'You'll earn favour, oh yes you shall, but only the favour which I offer. This victory will be mine, maggot. Your part was such a pittance!''Fandmau is a whimpering sod. I've a mind to flay him and hang his skin from the gates of Gramsfoot.

'You survived against the foe and took many lives as they stormed the tower. That, at least, earns you a reprieve from Malenhad, worm.'The Haradrim in Upper Lebennin have taken much from the people of Halach, and now these folk would see it returned.Haradrim archers can be found to the east and north-east of Halach in Upper Lebennin.

Gorhir has asked you to recover goods stolen by Haradrim archers in their last raid against Halach.Recover stolen goods from Haradrim archers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gorhir can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin.

You have recovered many of the stolen goods and should now return them to Gorhir in Halach.'We have endured numerous assaults by the Haradrim now, traveller.

'Many of our number were killed in their earliest attacks, and more still fled to Tumladen, but I shall not be moved. However, their archers are swift on their feet and in the midst of the last assault, they stole many goods of great import to us, including some of our food-stores. Our people are determined, but we cannot maintain a defence if we are starved.

'If you can recover them from the archers, we shall be able to hold out for weeks to come.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I shall see these goods brought to the others at once.

'We shall hide them away in secret places the next time the Haradrim dare attack Halach, for they cannot steal what they cannot find!'West of Tol Ascarnen, across the Hoardale River, the Orcs make their main keep. It is here that Lieutenant Solvi believes the Orcs have stolen precious food stores moved into Tol Ascarnen during the initial push by the Free Peoples, and he wants them back.Food-sacks might be found on the Orcs, trolls, and goblins in the Ettenmoors.

Lieutenant Solvi advised you to search Grothum and Dâr-gazag for more plentiful amounts of the food-sacks, but also said that the Ongbúrz and Snowreap may have some on their persons.'Ho there, ${CLASS}, you look like the sort who might help me fix some of the problems we found soon as we took this fortress. We and the Orcs fight here often, and we sometimes get beat back from within only to return later.

'During the last siege, it seemed like a score of Orcs stormed over me and got to our stores. We lost a good number of supplies in that assault, and we need to get them back. I've heard tell that the Orcs, trolls, and even the goblins are walking about with the food-sacks on their person. Hobbits need it too, those poor folk down the river a pinch.

'Slaughter the Orcs in the area and look for the food-sacks. I've heard tell you can find mountains of the stolen food at their camp, Dâr-gazag, in the west or maybe some up north near the goblin's village of Grothum.''I may seem a bit harsh, ${PLAYER}, that is true. But I want to see that we do what must be done to see this battle won. You helped us more than you know, and for that, I am grateful.

'Speak with Quartermaster Ash to learn of the importance of these tokens.'Tirith Rhaw is once again under the control of the Free Peoples. The forces here are still meagre, and a strong show of force from the Enemy could mean that the tower is lost as quickly as it is taken.Glân Vraig lay to the south and east of Tirith Rhaw.

After taking Tirith Rhaw away from the Enemy, the army of the Free Peoples sent you to Glân Vraig to request reinforcements for the tower.Inform Captain-General Tordúr that Tirith Rhaw needs reinforcements'Our victory could be short-lived if reinforcements are not sent from Glân Vraig. The Enemy will return quickly, and we do not have the forces to slow their progress to the Captain-General.

'I need you to make your way to Glân Vraig to inform Tordúr that we hold the tower and that we need reinforcements, or we will not hold.

'Go swiftly and do not suffer defeat.''Be swift. We must reinforce the tower quickly.''Your message is well-received. I will dispatch forces to Tirith Rhaw at once.'Mírthel asks you to speak with Gladhir about the Haradrim plans in Southern Ithilien.Gladhir can be found on the bridge to Bâr Húrin in Southern Ithilien.

You should speak with Gladhir.Speak with GladhirDerufin and Duilin can be found in Bâr Húrin.

You should speak with Derufin and Duilin.Speak with DerufinSpeak with DuilinAnborn and Thurindol can be found inside the keep at Bâr Húrin.

You should speak with Anborn and Thurindol.Speak with AnbornSpeak with Thurindol'Return to Gladhir and tell him of the Haradrim scaling the cliffs. I shall continue to monitor the situation and thwart their efforts until others arrive. Take care.''This is indeed dire. I do not wish to make you tarry longer than need requires if you do indeed have important news for Lord Faramir. I will muster nearby Rangers to put an end to the Haradrim plans to scale the cliffs. Pressing further into South Ithilien will be difficult. You should make your way to Bâr Húrin, the main stronghold of the Rangers south of Osgiliath. 
 
'You will not be welcomed there as warmly as you might wish or deserve, I am afraid. Anborn, leader of Bâr Húrin, is distrustful of outsiders, perhaps to a fault. I do not think he will turn you away, however. He did not turn away two others, like you, who came recently to Ithilien. If you take a little time to earn his trust, I feel sure he will assist you. 
 
Have hope, for I know you will find Faramir. May our paths cross again, ${PLAYER}.''My brother and I come from across the river. We're preparing to hunt a simply grand beast. Have you heard of the Mûmakil? They are giant, tusked creatures from lands south of here.'

You ask Derufin about Anborn.

'You can try talking to Anborn but I don't know how far you'll get. He admires our skill with the bow, but it ends there. You may have better luck with Thurindol. That Thurindol is a pleasant fellow, wouldn't you agree, Duilin?''Greetings, adventurer. Have you come to hunt wild game in Emyn Arnen?'

You ask Duilin about Anborn.

'If you're looking for Anborn, he's at the keep. He seems awfully busy though. He doesn't even have the time to hunt with us! Isn't that right, Derufin?''Stranger, you are bold to come and ask me where my leader is. You should not even be in these lands. But you speak Gladhir's name, so I will allow you here for now. It will take more than that to earn my trust, however.''Duilin and Derufin? Anborn allows those two to stay, I think, because they amuse our fellow Rangers with their cheerful antics. There is little to lighten our hearts in these days. They cheer us, but they are of little use. I hope that you may prove otherwise, for we are in need of some extra hands in Bâr Húrin, presently.'A little thief has just stolen a priceless bracelet from a noblewoman!The child has run off somewhere.

Follow the child to get the bracelet for the noblewoman.Follow the childThe child is in his hiding place.

You should scold the child for stealing.<rgb=#FF0000>Scold</rgb> the childThe noblewoman can be found near Pipers' Bend on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should return the bracelet to the noblewoman.Return the bracelet to the noblewoman'You, kind ${RACE}! Some errand-boy ran into me in the tunnels just now and it seems my bracelet has suddenly gone missing! I chased him towards Pipers' Bend but can't find the thieving child! The bracelet is a family heirloom and I must have it back!'

You spot the child thief and assure the woman that you will retrieve her bracelet and give the child a stern talking to.'Oh, thank you very much! I was afraid I would never see this bracelet again. It was my mother's, and her mother's before.

'I shall continue on my way to the Houses of Healing where I am currently training. If you have not already visited the Sixth Circle, there are some beautiful gardens to be admired. I do recommend a peaceful rest for the mind now and again, even in these dreadful times.'Anborn sends you on your way to the last known location of Faramir's camp.The ruins of Tuntham can be found north-east of Bâr Húrin.

You should travel to Tuntham and learn if Faramir is still there.Travel to TunthamThe ruins of Tuntham can be found north-east of Bâr Húrin.

You should locate the cairn on the western side of the ruins and look around.The ruins of Tuntham can be found north-east of Bâr Húrin.

You should locate the cairn on the northern side of the ruins and look around.Faramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath.

You should travel to Faramir's Look-out.Travel to Faramir's Look-outFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath.

You should speak with a Ranger at Faramir's Look-out.Speak with Arodor'Ithilien is a large stretch of land. Faramir travels constantly to visit Ranger camps and to keep us abreast of enemy movements. It has been many days since we last saw him, but I know that he had established a look-out in the ruins of Tuntham. You will find the ruins north-east of here, past Brangobel.

'Whether Faramir is there still, none in Bâr Húrin can say. If you arrive at the ruins and find them empty, do not fret. We Rangers leave cairns to share knowledge with each other after we have left. Stay strong in these dark days, my friend.''Greetings. I am guessing you are the traveller who has been helping Rangers around Southern Ithilien. Your deeds precede you, ${CLASS}. I am Arodor, commander of Faramir's Look-out.

'You seek Faramir? As you can see, he is not here. He had gone commanding a garrison in Osgiliath when the Morgul-host attacked the city. We've yet to make contact with anyone inside the city.'Ceveneth is in need of supplies if she is to continue to help repair the villages defences and to care for the wounded.Branches and deer can be found in the woods east of Crithost.

You should obtain some woods for repairing barricades and deer hides for making slings for the wounded.Collect branches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect deer hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ceveneth can be found in the hall of Crithost.

You should speak with Ceveneth.Speak with Ceveneth'If you have a moment, I am in need of supplies. I need more deer hides for making slings and casts for the wounded.

'Also, I could use more wood to construct additional barricades for Crithost. Do you think you could gather some for me? There are some woods east of here that should have what I am looking for.''You are most generous with your time. I shall put these supplies to good use around the village, my friend. You can count on me to help those in Crithost as much as I can.'A pair of drakes have roosted on the ruins of a small island off the coast of Dol Amroth, terrorizing the Gondorian fishermen.The drakes must be vanquished to protect the city.

A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Aduial.'Tol Aduial is a small island, just off the coast of Dol Amroth. You can see it from the cliffs near the Great Hall. Long has it been an outpost of the city, where we watched all manner of boats enter the bay. That is where we would intercept our enemies and ensure it was only allies who passed on to the city.

'The Corsairs have taken it as their own, and are choking off our fishermen and supplies. To make it worse, they have brought a pair of drakes with them. Fearsome beasts.

'There is a small boat in the harbour that will take you there. Once there, keep your eyes open. I am sure there is more to deal with than just those drakes. Be warned, you will want friends with you.'Avanc fill the coastal waters. With the right 'encouragement' they will swarm. True hunters of Gondor are able to dispatch of swaths of the beasts within a few very short, intense, moments.Placing the bait will cause the avanc to swarm.Place the baitThe challenge has begun. Dispatch as many avanc as you can before the time expires.Defeat swarming avanc (${VALUE}/20)Before time expiresCorsairs have started setting up on this small island, only a stone's throw from Dol Amroth. While not large enough to mount an assault from, they control the waters passing by and can spy on any activity happening within the port city.The corsairs must be cleared from the island.Clear the groups of Corsairs (${VALUE}/6)The corsairs have used the camp-fires to communicate with their ships by smoke signal.Sending a bunch of random patterns of smoke will confuse the corsair ships.Smoke signals sent (${VALUE}/6)The Corsairs have set up cages at several spots around the island, holding small animals captive.Cages can be found on the shorelines of Tol Fennas.

Dimlas asked you to free animals from cages on Tol Fennas. A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Fennas.Destroy cages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dimlas is in Dol Amroth.

Dimlas will be pleased to hear you freed many animals.'The Corsairs have been raiding Tol Fennas for food and supplies heavily these past few days. They've been catching more than they can eat and have set up small cages around the island, holding the creatures where they were caught.

'Freeing the creatures from the cages will disrupt the Corsairs' food supply, cause them confusion and delay in having to hunt them again, and hopefully save the animals as well.

'Take a boat from the harbour to Tol Fennas. Search the shorelines for cages and free the animals within.''In a few days' time we will need to return again, perhaps to free the same animals. But for now, they are safe and the Corsairs are delayed.'The Corsairs have set up Makham Jurrar, a lumber and shipyard camp on the north side of Tol Fennas.Corsairs can be found at Makham Jurrar, the lumber and shipyard camp on the north side of Tol Fennas.

Glíreth asked you to venture to Makham Jurrar and disrupt the lumber camp there. A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Fennas.Defeat Corsairs at Makham Jurrar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glíreth is in Dol Amroth.

Glíreth will be pleased to hear the workforce at Makham Jurrar has been noticeably reduced.'On the north side of Tol Fennas the Corsairs have set up a lumber camp, Makham Jurrar. The trees from the island are being brought there and felled. I believe they are using them to build a fleet of smaller vessels, just large enough to cross the channel and land in Belfalas. A fleet for a massive assault.

'Head to the island. You can use a small boat in the harbour. Find this camp and defeat the Corsairs within.''It is hard to build ships and fell lumber without men. Good work.'The Corsairs have set up a lumber and shipyard camp on Tol Fennas, west of Dol Amroth.Boats can be found at Makham Jurrar, the lumber and shipyard camp on the north side of Tol Fennas.

Glíreth asked you to venture to Tol Fennas and destroy the boats being constructed there. A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Fennas.Destroy boats at Makham Jurrar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glíreth is in Dol Amroth.

Glíreth will be pleased to hear the boats at Makham Jurrar have been destroyed.'The Corsairs are building boats at Makham Jurrar, a small camp on the north side of Tol Fennas. They are not large themselves, but launched from some of the bigger craft, they could carry a great many Corsairs to shore, even in the shallows.

'Find this camp and destroy the boats that are currently being constructed. You can take a craft from the harbour here in Dol Amroth to get to the island.''Fewer boats means fewer Corsairs on shore. Good work.'Corsairs have set up a small camp on the west side of the island. Clearing out the camp will help to stem the tide.The Corsair hunters are at Makham Hosh, on the west side of Tol Fennas.

Glíreth asked you to find a Corsair hunting camp on Tol Fennas and defeat those within. A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Fennas.Defeat Corsairs at Makham Hosh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glíreth is in Dol Amroth.

Glíreth will be pleased to hear the Corsair hunters have been thinned.'The Corsairs have been very active recently and started encroaching on these lands more and more. The large island to the west, Tol Fennas, they are using as a base of operations.

'Makham Hosh, a camp on the west side of the island, is being run as a hunting camp. They are catching and killing anything on the island they can find to use as food. We rely on that island as a source of meat during the longer winters.

'Use a small boat from the harbour to take yourself out to the island. When you get there, find the camp and defeat any Corsairs you find within.''More will come, I have no doubt of that, but you have at least saved some of the wild-life for a time.'The Corsairs are cutting down the trees on Tol Fennas in order to build more ships and boats.Planting locations can be found all over Tol Fennas.

Dimlas asked you to go to Tol Fennas and plant seeds to grow new trees. A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Fennas.Plant seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dimlas is in Dol Amroth.

Dimlas will be pleased to hear a new crop of seeds has been planted.'The trees on Tol Fennas are quite important. The wildlife that lives there relies on them for food and shelter. Their roots also keep the island from slipping into the waters during the more violent storms.

'The Corsairs that have settled there are cutting them down without care or concern. While I want to stop them from being able to build more ships, preserving the island is very important as well.

'Use a small boat in the harbor and head to the island. Once there, find some suitable locations and plant some seeds so we can begin growing a new crop of saplings.''This is a start. We will have to be vigilant to ensure these ones are left to grow.'The ravens' eggs at the peak of Tol Fennas must be protected if the birds are to survive.Raven eggs can be found in nests on the heights of Tol Fennas.

Dimlas asked you to head to Tol Fennas and gather raven eggs. A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Fennas.Venture to the the heights of Tol FennasRaven eggs can be found in nests on the heights of Tol Fennas.

Dimlas asked you to head to Tol Fennas and gather raven eggs.Eggs gathered (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather eggs before the Corsairs canDimlas is in Dol Amroth.

Dimlas will be pleased with the number of eggs you saved.'The ravens on Tol Fennas are very important to us. They are messenger birds and often used in hunting.

'I have heard the Corsairs are raiding the ravens' nests and stealing their eggs. Those eggs are then being used for breakfasts and not for hatching.

'Use a boat in the harbour and head to Tol Fennas. Once there, ascend to the heights and find the nests. You'll need to be quick, once you grab the first egg the Corsairs will surely notice.''We can get a full clutch from this many eggs. I will see to it they are properly cared for and hatched right here in Dol Amroth. When the island is ours again they shall return home.'The Corsairs have spread snares all over Tol Fennas to try and catch the smaller creatures.Snares can be found on Tol Fennas.

Dimlas asked you to head to Tol Fennas and remove the snares the Corsairs have placed. A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Fennas.Collect snares (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dimlas is in Dol Amroth.

Dimlas will be pleased to hear some snares have been removed.'Every animal contributes a purpose and a value to all the others. When one is removed the others will suffer.

'The Corsairs have spread snares all over Tol Fennas to try and catch the rabbits and squirrels and other small creatures. These creatures allow the forests to grow and the larger creatures to exist.

'Take a boat from the dock to Tol Fennas. Once there, remove any snares you find. I expect they will not be hard to find.''I am sure they will place more, but every day and bit we can delay them is a victory for us.'Some of the Corsairs at the hunting camp are diseased. Once defeated, their bodies must be treated to protect the local flora and fauna.Sick Corsairs are at the Makham Hosh, the hunting camp on the west side of Tol Fennas.

Glíreth asked you to defeat the sick Corsairs at the hunting camp and treat the bodies. A boat in the harbour of Dol Amroth can take you to Tol Fennas.Defeat and treat sick Corsairs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Glíreth is in Dol Amroth.

Glíreth will be pleased to hear the sick Corsairs have been cleansed.'The Corsairs from the south have a diet very different from ours. Their ailments are different as well. Some of the ones we have spotted have looked very sick, in a way that troubles me.

'The sick at Makham Hosh, the hunting camp, could do great harm. If they were to be eaten by the bears of the island, the disease could lie dormant, waiting to strike until we ate the bear next winter.

'Find the sick ones at the hunting camp, dispatch them, and then treat their bodies with this lacquer; it should prevent the disease from spreading to any animals or plants.''We will have to be vigilant in our application of this lacquer, but if we are, I feel our safety from the Corsair diseases is assured.'Tolwin asks for assistance as he patrols Talath Anor, searching for his mother who has been missing since minions of Mordor invaded the stronghold of Cair Andros.Tolwin is in the hall at Crithost.

You should speak with Tolwin.Speak with TolwinTolwin wishes for your help in his search for his missing mother, Dúneth.

You should complete a number of tasks in Talath Anor, using the whistle to call your friend for help if you become separated.Complete: The Search for Dúneth ContinuesComplete: Dismantling Their EffortsComplete: Protecting the WoodsComplete: The Doorstep of Cair AndrosUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedYou should speak with Tolwin.Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated'We can not delay further. We must work together to take back this land and find my mother, who may still be alive out there. I am certain The First Blade wants all of Talath Anor to burn. I have looked into his eyes and saw what he is capable of. He has murdered innocents with no remorse. He will leave nothing to chance.

'I feel that Crithost's defences are sufficient for the time we will be away. Ceveneth and the Cair Andros guards will manage without us.''Call me to your side when you wish to depart.''I thank you for your aid in finding my mother. Still, there is much to do.'Your war-host claims to have enough metal now that the mine is in-service and under your control, but the picks used by the goblins are dulled with time and the wood rots out from their hands.Kindling can be found in the Grimwood.

Taskmaster Bárzqhosh tasked you with garnering enough wood to repair the picks used to pull ore from the Isendeep.'The mine spills ore from every new scar we open in its walls, but the tools our slaves use grow weaker with every swing.

'There is a place, far to the south, where the wood is strong. Go there, to the Grimwood. Find healthy stocks of wood and bring them to us. They need only be better than roots. Some may call it kindling, but the wood will prove sturdy enough for our purposes.

'Make haste, ${RACE}. We must continue our assault and drive the enemy from this land!''We will go about refitting the tools now and see that the mine gives up ore at a faster pace. This shall fuel our war-machine, and we shall crush our opponents with ease.

'For the glory of Angmar! For the Great Eye!'The corsairs have started packing up and moving the tools used by the craftsmen.The tools should be recovered so the craftsmen can return to work.Recover tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find ancient treasure in Angmar.Find ancient treasure in Angmar.Find ancient treasure in AngmarFind Central Gondor's treasure that has been lost or stolen.Find Central Gondor's treasure that has been lost or stolen.Find Central Gondor's lost treasureFind Eastern Gondor's treasure that has been lost or stolen.Find Eastern Gondor's treasure that has been lost or stolen.Find Eastern Gondor's lost treasureFind ancient treasure in Evendim.Find ancient treasure in Evendim.Find ancient treasure in EvendimFind ancient treasure in Forochel.Find ancient treasure in Forochel.Find ancient treasure in ForochelFind ancient treasure in Southern Mirkwood.Find ancient treasure in Southern Mirkwood.Find ancient treasure in Southern MirkwoodFind lost treasure in The Misty Mountains.Find lost treasure in The Misty Mountains.Find lost treasure in The Misty MountainsFind ancient treasure in The North Downs.Find ancient treasure in The North Downs.Find ancient treasure in The North DownsTyrant Trintrû at Tol Ascarnen is deserving of praise and tribute. The tribute which the tyrant desires most is the flesh of Men.Men can be found throughout the Ettenmoors.

Quartermaster Apsduf ordered you to gather Man-flesh as tribute to the Tyrant at Tol Ascarnen.'Pay attention to everything I say, wretch, else I'll stretch your hide from the west bridge of this island to the east bridge. Our leader, Tyrant Trintrû, is deserving of our praise and our tribute. Time for you to pay your tribute, dog.

'The one thing, above all else, that Tyrant Trintrû desires is Man-flesh. So you will oblige him. You will go into the wild, find the Men at their holdings or wandering through the wood, ripe for picking, and you will cut their legs from their bodies.

'Bring their legs back to me, and I will see that the Tyrant knows you have paid him proper tribute! Go now, worm!''For the glory of Angmar, Mordirith, and the service of Lugburz! You serve your masters well, cur!'Defeat many Trolls in Old Anórien.Defeat many Trolls in Old Anórien.Defeat many Trolls in Old AnórienDefeat many Trolls in Old Anórien.Defeat many Trolls in Old Anórien.Defeat many Trolls in Old AnórienPatrol the Ettenmoors in search of the enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the EttenmoorsPatrol the Ettenmoors in search of the enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the EttenmoorsPatrol the Ettenmoors in search of the enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the EttenmoorsPatrol the Ettenmoors in search of the enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the EttenmoorsPatrol the Ettenmoors in search of the enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the EttenmoorsPatrol the Ettenmoors in search of the enemy. You must patrol for 60 minutes. After 60 minutes you will be returned to your post.Patrol the Ettenmoors.Patrol the EttenmoorsTurtles are the bane of the Dol Amroth fishermen. They eat the bait, and even sometimes the fish on the hook itself! Catching some and dispatching of them will aid the food supplies of the beleaguered Gondorian city.Swamps are north of Calembel, north-east of Dol Amroth.

Torchuil asked you to go fishing for turtles in the swamps north of Calembel and to dispatch of any you caught.Fish up and defeat the turtles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Torchuil is in Dol Amroth.

Torchuil will be pleased to know the turtles have been thinned.Speak to Torchuil'Ever seen a swamp turtle? They're rascally creatures, the ones out here. Eat the bait from your hook without you even knowing. Why, I've even heard tale of one who would eat the fish right off the hook while you were trying to reel it in. Would wait for you to do all the hard work and then swoop in at the end and steal your dinner.

'They're also dangerous creatures, with jaws that can snap a man's leg clear in half. I love just about everything in the water, even some of the things from the true depths, but turtles we cannot tolerate any longer.

'Head to the swamps north of Calembel, to the north-east of here, and spend some time fishing. When you get a turtle on the line, pull hard and make sure that it comes ashore. When it does, take care of it. There are a lot of them out there in the shallows, so make sure you clear out a couple.''I'm sure the fresh tide will bring in more, but for now we should be able to get a couple of hours of unmolested fishing in. Thank you.'Uglash has implored you to return to your trainers and learn how better to equip yourself for the battles to come. He has sent you to your trainers to learn more.Uglash has asked you to return to your trainers and learn more about what it takes to become a true soldier in the war against the Free Peoples.

The trainers are back where you started your life as a Warg. Speak with Gruglok.Return to your trainers and learn how to train your skillsHaving spoken to Gruglok, you should now talk to the Corruptor to learn about traits.Talk to Zagfra, a Corruptor of GramsfootNow that you have (presumably) equipped some traits, speak with the Corruptions Trainer to learn more about Corruptions in Monster Play.Talk to HoitgothNow that you have learned how to best equip yourself in Monster Play, speak with Uglash again for final instructions.Talk to Uglash to finish the tutorial'Return to your trainers. They can help you fight without getting squashed like an insignificant slug. Hurry! The war doesn't stop just because you aren't ready for it.''Well, it is about time someone knocked some sense into you! Now stop your howling and pay attention! Pups have no place in this army!

'Good! Now talk to me again if you wish to purchase skills, then speak to the Warg Corruptor.'

<rgb=#00FF00>In Monster Play, you will earn </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Infamy</rgb><rgb=#00FF00> and </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Commendations</rgb><rgb=#00FF00> by defeating the Free Peoples. As you accrue </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Infamy</rgb><rgb=#00FF00>, your rank (level) will increase, granting you access to additional skills, traits, and characteristics. You can then purchase these from your trainer with </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Commendations.</rgb>

<rgb=#00FF00>Speak with the trainer again if you wish to purchase additional skills and traits.</rgb>'Speak up. My ear is still bleeding from your constant howling.  

'If you purchased some traits from your trainer, then you can equip them with me.'

<rgb=#00FF00> You have a Corruption ready to be equipped. To equip traits and Corruptions speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and Corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections. </rgb>'So you think you are smart enough to understand the concept of trade-offs?  Then you are a bigger fool than most give you credit for. Corruptions will grant you incredible powers, but you can only use a handful at a time.  Choose wisely.'

'Uglash wishes to speak with you again.'

<rgb=#00FF00> Corruptions offer the players the ability to raise certain stats in exchange for lowering other ones. This is available for players who wish to specialize even further than their Monster Player class allows.</rgb>'Good, you are still alive! Hopefully you've learned a thing or two about how to keep yourself from being meat for the slugs. 

'There are many things that need to be done to win this war. Speak with the soldiers around the totem behind me to help in the war effort. You can also view the state of the war in the tent up on the hill. Some of the warriors up there may have things for you to do from time to time as well.

'Now quit staring at me with that vacant look in your eyes and get out there and fight!'As a new recruit to face the army of Angmar, you are welcome in the Ettenmoors. You have learned much in your travels and will be prepared to enter the fray of battle quickly.Make your way from the fountain to the front of this encampment to the north. There you should meet Captain-General Tordúr who leads this expedition in the Ettenmoors.Introduce yourself to Captain-General Tordúr'Well met. It is good to see new faces willing to come to the front and do battle against the enemy of the Free People. As you are newly arrived, you should introduce yourself to Tordúr, who stands near the stairs that lead from this safe haven in the Ettenmoors. He commands the forces here and will want to help you get started in this harsh land.

'Please, go and visit him now.''Another new recruit? You are most welcome in this host ${PLAYER}.

'Do not be surprised that I know your name. Your deeds echo across the land and long have we wanted to have your abilities added to the warriors in these forsaken lands.'

The Elf offers a broad smile.

'Let us get you prepared. Over there, just to my left are vendors who will sell you gear that will aid you here. The land here is afflicted and our smiths work hard to provide our warriors with gear to overcome that affliction. It is with this audacity that we can remain in this fight. Else, it appears that our morale falters.'You are nearly prepared for battle, but the Captain-General has one more task for you before he sends you into the fray.Travel out of Glân Vraig by the path along the cliffside to the east of Captain-General Tordúr and make your way to Ost Ringdyr.Arrive at Ost RingdyrYou have discovered the keep of Ost Ringdyr. You should now use the skill <rgb=#FFFF00>Return to Glân Vraig</rgb> to quickly return to the main encampment.Use the skill <rgb=#FFFF00>Return to Glân Vraig</rgb>You have returned to Glân Vraig. Speak with Captain-General Tordúr and let him know that you are prepared to fight in the battle for the Ettenmoors.'To the east, behind the foliage and stones, there is a path that leads to the keep of Ost Ringdyr. We keep a relic of power within those walls.

'I want you to travel there to see why we fight. I have provided you with a map showing a quick path back here to Glân Vraig. Go now with haste and return by way of the map, so that I know you are prepared for the battle to come.

'Travel along that path to the east and stay close to the cliffside so you do not fall down into the proper battlefield.''It is good to know that there are those like you, willing to come and fight for this land. We will remain resolute in this battle. The armies of Angmar will not press into the south, and it is by our force of arms combined that we shall see this through.

'You are prepared as best as I can see. Go forth.'Uglash wants you prepared to fight for Mordirith and tasked you with trying out your skills before sending you off to fight the enemy in the Ettenmoors.You are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy.

<rgb=#00FF00>Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are <rgb=#FFFF00>marching</rgb>. You will need to disable the skill <rgb=#FFFF00>March!</rgb> to begin attacking or use other skills.</rgb>Successfully use <rgb=#FFFF00>Intimidating Shout</rgb> on a target dummyYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy.

<rgb=#00FF00>Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are <rgb=#FFFF00>marching</rgb>. You will need to disable the skill <rgb=#FFFF00>March!</rgb> to begin attacking or use other skills.</rgb>Successfully use <rgb=#FFFF00>Cleave</rgb> on training dummy Kelsen, Jalessa, or Light training-dummy OrionYou have used both a ranged and a melee skill on a target dummy and should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.Report back to Uglash'Let us see what you can do. Behind the totems are effigies of the enemy. Go to them. Use your skills against them and return me when you have struck blows upon the false enemies that we train against. Return to me when this task is done.''Ha! Don't you feel special, you little wretch? Oh... I hit a training dummy, look at me!

'Pathetic!

'Out there, in the 'moors, the enemy hits back! And most time they don't use pillows filled with feathers. Except maybe the rat-folk. Oh... and them rat-folk is good eatin'.'

Uglash seems lost in thought for a moment.

'Oh... what? I've got no more to teach you - for now.'Uglash wants you prepared to fight for Mordirith and tasked you with trying out your skills before sending you off to fight the enemy in the Ettenmoors.You are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy.

