'Out there, in the 'moors, the enemy hits back! And most time they don't use pillows filled with feathers. Except maybe the rat-folk. Oh... and them rat-folk is good eatin'.'

Uglash seems lost in thought for a moment.

'Oh... what? I've got no more to teach you - for now.'It is time to put all you have learned together and return to War-tyrant Akulhún for your orders.Uglash can prepare you for the fight to come no longer. He advised that you speak with the War-tyrant and begin your battles in the Ettenmoors.Return to Akulhún for your newest orders'There is little else that I can do to prepare you for what is beyond that gate.'

Uglash laughs.

'Time to prove yourself. Go to the War-tyrant. Tell him you are ready.''Listen well, Uruk. There are expectations that I have of you and our race. You should lead - from the back. Whipping these lesser creatures into a frenzy and making sure that the taste of flesh stays fresh in their gullets.

'You are prepared. Do not fail...'

He leans in close.

'Or I'll skin you myself.'Uglash has implored you to return to your trainers and learn how better to equip yourself for the battles to come.Uglash has asked you to return to your trainers and learn more about what it takes to become a true soldier in the war against the Free Peoples.

The trainers are back where you started your life as an Orc.Return to your trainers and learn how to improve your skillsHaving spoken with Dagalúr, you should now talk to the Corruptor to learn about traits.Talk to Ashrokil, the Corruptor of GramsfootNow that you have equipped some traits, speak with the corruptions trainer to learn more about corruptions in Monster Play.Talk to DurglobNow that you have learned how to best equip yourself in Monster Play, speak with Uglash again for final instructions.Talk to Uglash to finish the tutorial'Return to your trainers. They can help you fight without getting squashed like an insignificant slug. Hurry! The war doesn't stop just because you aren't ready for it.''Well, it's about time someone knocked some sense into you! Now shut your gob and pay attention! This isn't some weak-armed, sunken-chest game we are playing out here.

'Good. Now, talk to me again if you wish to purchase traits, then speak with the Corruptor.'

<rgb=#00FF00>In Monster Play, you will earn </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Infamy</rgb><rgb=#00FF00> and </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Commendations</rgb><rgb=#00FF00> by defeating the Free Peoples. As you accrue </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Infamy</rgb><rgb=#00FF00>, your rank (level) will increase, granting you access to additional skills, traits, and characteristics.  You can then purchase these from your trainer with </rgb><rgb=#FFFF00>Commendations.</rgb>

<rgb=#00FF00>Speak with the trainer again if you wish to purchase additional skills and traits.</rgb>'Can I help you? No? Great.

'Oh, you're still here?  Well then, if you purchased some traits from your trainer, then you can equip them with me.'

<rgb=#00FF00> You have a corruption ready to be equipped. To equip traits and corruptions speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections.</rgb>'So you think you are smart enough to understand the concept of trade-offs?  Then you are a bigger fool than most give you credit for. Corruptions will grant you incredible powers, but you can only use a handful at a time.  Choose wisely.'

'Uglash wishes to speak with you again.'

<rgb=#00FF00> Corruptions offer the players the ability to raise certain stats in exchange for lowering other ones. This is available for players who wish to specialize even further than their Monster Player class allows. </rgb>'Good! You are still alive! Hopefully you've learned a thing or two about how to keep yourself from being meat for the slugs. 

'There are many things that need to be done to win this war. Speak with the soldiers around the totem behind me to help in the war-effort. You can also view the state of the war in the tent up on the hill. Some of the warriors up there may have things for you to do from time to time as well.

'Now quit staring with that vacant look in your eyes and get out there and fight!'Now that you are known to be a warrior in the Ettenmoors, you should prepare by acquiring the gear that suits you. The Captain-General warned that there is an affliction in these lands that only the gear specifically crafted for battle here will overcome.Make your way to the Medium Armour Quartermaster just to the west of Tordúr and purchase the gear you need to survive and thrive in the Ettenmoors.Speak with the Medium Armour Quartermaster and learn about <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity</rgb>Now that you are versed in the need for the gear that unlocks <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity</rgb>, return to Captain-General Tordúr.'As a ${CLASS}, you should speak with the Medium Armour Quartermaster. They will have the gear you need to survive, and hopefully thrive, here in the Ettenmoors.''Greetings, ${CLASS}. Welcome to the Ettenmoors. Please, look through my wares and purchase all of the gear that you can. There is a vile pall that blankets this land. Our smiths have discovered a way to make wares that will allow those with stout hearts to overcome the miasma through sheer will, but this gear seems to be the only means by which we can focus.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Surviving in the Ettenmoors requires the acquisition of <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity,</rgb> a special attribute unlocked with the gear you purchase here and earn throughout play within the Ettenmoors. You should spend a little coin to acquire your first suit of armour and accessories so that you can fully participate in the Ettenmoors.</rgb>'If you are truly prepared, then there is only one more step to complete before you should enter the battle for the Ettenmoors.'Now that you are known to be a warrior in the Ettenmoors, you should prepare by acquiring the gear that suits you. The Captain-General warned that there is an affliction in these lands that only the gear specifically crafted for battle here will overcome.Make your way to the Light Armour Quartermaster just to the west of Tordúr and purchase the gear you need to survive and thrive in the Ettenmoors.Speak with the Light Armour Quartermaster and learn about <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity</rgb>Now that you are versed in the need for the gear that unlocks <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity</rgb>, return to Captain-General Tordúr.'As a ${CLASS}, you should speak with the Light Armour Quartermaster. They will have the gear you need to survive, and hopefully thrive, here in the Ettenmoors.''Greetings, ${CLASS}. Welcome to the Ettenmoors. Please, look through my wares and purchase all of the gear that you can. There is a vile pall that blankets this land. Our smiths have discovered a way to make wares that will allow those with stout hearts to overcome the miasma through sheer will, but this gear seems to be the only means by which we can focus.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Surviving in the Ettenmoors requires the acquisition of <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity,</rgb> a special attribute unlocked with the gear you purchase here and earn throughout play within the Ettenmoors. You should spend a little coin to acquire your first suit of armour and accessories so that you can fully participate in the Ettenmoors.</rgb>'If you are truly prepared, then there is only one more step to complete before you should enter the battle for the Ettenmoors.'Now that you are known to be a warrior in the Ettenmoors, you should prepare by acquiring the gear that suits you. The Captain-General warned that there is an affliction in these lands that only the gear specifically crafted for battle here will overcome.Make your way to the Heavy Armour Quartermaster just to the west of Tordúr and purchase the gear you need to survive and thrive in the Ettenmoors.Speak with the Heavy Armour Quartermaster and learn about <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity</rgb>Now that you are versed in the need for the gear that unlocks <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity</rgb>, return to Captain-General Tordúr.'As a ${CLASS}, you should speak with the Heavy Armour Quartermaster. They will have the gear you need to survive, and hopefully thrive, here in the Ettenmoors.''Greetings, ${CLASS}. Welcome to the Ettenmoors. Please, look through my wares and purchase all of the gear that you can. There is a vile pall that blankets this land. Our smiths have discovered a way to make wares that will allow those with stout hearts to overcome the miasma through sheer will, but this gear seems to be the only means by which we can focus.'

<rgb=#00FF00>Surviving in the Ettenmoors requires the acquisition of <rgb=#FFFF00>Audacity,</rgb> a special attribute unlocked with the gear you purchase here and earn throughout play within the Ettenmoors. You should spend a little coin to acquire your first suit of armour and accessories so that you can fully participate in the Ettenmoors.</rgb>'If you are truly prepared then there is only one more step to complete before you should enter the battle for the Ettenmoors.'Malavin, the emissary of Angmar, directed you to return to where you began your journey in the Ettenmoors to speak with the corruptor there.Malavin sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Lenathron the corruptor.Return to your spawning den. Speak with Lenathron the Corruptor'Now that you have chosen a clan you must learn how to further strengthen and enhance yourself so that you are more than a distraction against the enemy. Return to the location you arrived and speak with Lenathron. They will show you the power that corruption can provide.''Greetings, broodling. Freshly arrived and visited the emissary? Allow me to assist you. I can aid in your survival and skill in the coming battles.'

The spider swipes at you.

'Consider this a lesson. Speak with me again to continue your lessons.'

<rgb=#00FF00>To equip traits and Corruptions speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and Corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections.</rgb>Malavin, the emissary of Angmar, directed you to return to where you began your journey in the Ettenmoors to speak with the corruptor there.Malavan sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Ashrokil the corruptor.Return to your spawning den. Speak with Ashrokil the Corruptor.'Now that you have chosen a clan, you must learn how to further strengthen and enhance yourself so that you are more than a distraction against the enemy. Return to the location you arrived and speak with Ashrokil. They will show you the power that corruption can provide.''Always good to see the real warriors here in the Ettenmoors. I can help you survive, slaughter, even thrive in this war. You will need my help.'

The Orc swipes at you.

'Consider this a lesson. Speak with me again to continue your lessons.'

<rgb=#00FF00> After completing this quest, you will have your first corruption. To equip traits and Corruptions speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and Corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections. </rgb>Malavin, the emissary of Angmar, directed you to return to where you began your journey in the Ettenmoors to speak with the corruptor there.Malavan sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Zagfra the Corruptor.Return to your spawning den. Speak with Zagfra the Corruptor.'Now that you have chosen a clan, you must learn how to further strengthen and enhance yourself so that you are more than a distraction against the enemy. Return to the location you arrived and speak with Zagfra. They will show you the power that corruption can provide.''The emissary told me she would send the newest pups my way. Well pup, I am here to enhance your ability to survive and slaughter in this unforgiving land.'

The Warg swipes at you.

'Consider this a lesson. Speak with me again to continue your lessons.'

<rgb=#00FF00>After completing this quest your will have your first corruption. To equip traits and Corruptions, speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and Corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections. </rgb>Malavin, the emissary of Angmar, directed you to return to where you began your journey in the Ettenmoors to speak with the corruptor there.Malavin directed you to return to Cinaid near the front gate of Gramsfoot. He will aid you further in preparing to battle throughout the Ettenmoors.'Acquainting yourself with the different clans is the first step in blooding yourself on the battlefield. To further your preparations return to the front gate and speak with Cinaid. He will further instruct and prepare you for the battle ahead.

'Again, sister, welcome to the fight. Let the true children show these lesser creatures how wars should be fought.''I am pleased to see you still here, mistress of darkness. The lessons I have to teach are manifold and important. They will aid you greatly in this foetid land.'

He pauses a moment.

'I think it is time to properly prepare you.'

<rgb=#00FF00> After completing this quest, you will have your first corruption. To equip traits and Corruptions speak again with the Corruptor. Select the available traits and Corruptions from the list and drag them into the empty trait slots. When you are finished, confirm your selections.</rgb>Having entered the Ettenmoors as a spider, you need to learn your way around. Follow your orders and do not get yourself killed by the Free Peoples who lurk around every corner.Tolothdal has ordered you to get into the fight already. She wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south.  Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.Get your orders from Chief Guard DuthúrzYou are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the camp to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.Return to safety and speak with Uglash'You have just been hatched, broodling, but already you must play an important role. Mordirith has sent you here to aid in the war against the Free Peoples. We have no time to waste. You must go get your feet wet now, all of them.

'Head down the hill and out the front gate and speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz. He will have orders for you. We must share our web with interesting allies to be victorious. Now go!''What are you doing here, recruit? You aren't ready to step foot out here! Why do they keep sending me fodder? I need trained soldiers. Get back in the base and learn something before a Burglar stealth kills you!

'Return to the camp now and speak with Uglash! Come back to me when you've learned a thing or two about fighting out here.''Pitiful fool. 

'You've passed the first test. You follow orders blindly even when it means certain death. Well done.  Now let us see if you can learn more obvious thoughts like "the Orc with the bigger sword wins."'Having entered the Ettenmoors as a spider, you need to learn your way around. Follow your orders and do not get yourself killed by the Free Peoples who lurk around every corner.Tolothdal has ordered you to get into the fight already. She wants you to go speak with Chief Guard Duthúrz outside the gate to the south. Leave the camp and speak with him immediately.Get your orders from Chief Guard DuthúrzYou are deemed unworthy by the Chief Guard. Speak with Uglash inside the base to learn more about what you need to survive the Ettenmoors.Return to safety and speak with Uglash'You have just been hatched, broodling, but already you must play an important role. Mordirith has sent you here to aid in the war against the Free Peoples. We have no time to waste. You must go get your feet wet now, all of them.

