You should speak to Mírthel near Ost Sarram.Speak with Mírthel'First among all things, we must find what became of Mírthel. It will be fastest to divide our search in two. I will continue up the road to the bridge. You go and search the southern cliffs and among Ost Sarram, which lie upon them.'"Ssh! The Haradrim will hear us. What business have you in this land?'

You explain that Gladhir sent you in search of him.

'I see. It is fortunate you arrived when you did. I have discovered how the Haradrim were able to gather in such great number here without our being aware. They have been constructing ladders along the cliffs to bring men and supplies over the Emyn Arnen. Without the ladders, they would need to pass through a chokepoint on the Harad road, which is closely watched. Needless to say, we must hinder these schemes immediately.''Good work! That will surely slow the Haradrim down enough that we may alert more Rangers to the situation.'Cangoras tasks you to deliver important supplies to Arthon at the Armoury.Arthon is at the Armoury.

You should bring the supplies to Arthon.Bring the supplies to Arthon quicklyDeliver supplies before the enemy attacks the Armoury'I have important supplies that need to be delivered to the Armoury as soon as possible. Please take these supplies to Arthon immediately.

'The defence of the Armoury depends on it!''Good work, bringing these vital supplies to me so quickly. Now we shall be able to arm another guard in the defence of the Armoury.'Arvaethor has asked you to scout out a nearby lumber camp for any survivors.The lumber camp is located east of Ethring in Ringló Vale.

You should search the Lumber camp for any survivors and defeat any Orcs.Defeat Orcs in the lumber camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Salvage tools from the lumber camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and speak with any survivorsSpeak with Arvaethor.Speak with Arvaethor'Those who live in Ethring make their way from the trees in our Vale. This mother of ships helped build a great naval fleet for Gondor many years ago. Recently our lumber camps have been pillaged and burnt. If we do not make this wood safe again, I fear the few townspeople left will not have the money to acquire provisions from passing merchants.

'There is one lumber camp not too far from here. I was on my way to investigate it before we met. I fear I am too late but let us hope for survivors.'The man beckons you to come closer and whispers words into your ear.

'I... tried to stop them *cough* but there... were too many. They came from across... the river.... *cough* and leading them... was... a...'

His words trail off as he passes.'What did the dying man say? So there is an Orc camp across the river? This is more serious than I thought. Once, centuries ago, the Orcs of the White Mountains were a plague upon the Vale. The people of the Vale were victorious after much bloodshed and drove them back under the mountain. I myself thought the Orcs were destroyed until I saw one with my own eyes just two days ago.'Complete the epilogue of Central Gondor.Complete the epilogue of Central Gondor.Complete the epilogue of Ringló ValeComplete the epilogue of Dor-en ErnilComplete the epilogue of LebenninDefeat Azruthor and his forces in Tarlang's Crown.Defeat Azruthor and his forces in Tarlang's Crown.Defeat Azruthor and his minions in Tarlang's CrownRead the plaques of landmarks used by those living in Minas Tirith to store provisions and valuables.Read the plaques of landmarks used by those living in Minas Tirith to store provisions and valuables.Find the Keep of the Keys plaqueFind the Lower Stores plaqueFind the Vaults of Rynd Mírath plaqueFind the Middle Stores plaqueFind the Upper Stores plaqueFind The Coffer-house plaqueDeep in the Mines of Moria, forces of Angmar and the Free People clash for control of a dwarf-hall.If you are willing, speak with Tordúr and make your way to the Heart if Baranzibar. Fight the forces of Angmar there.Speak with Tordúr to travel to the Heart of BaranzibarFight against the encroaching forces of Angmar in the depths of Moria.Complete a battle within the Heart of BaranzibarWith the battle complete, you should return to Tordúr and tell them of your effort.'Our allies from Moria tell of a concerning development in their mines. All manner of foul beast from Angmar infiltrated a place called the Heart of Baranzibar and move to claim this mine with rich deposits of ore. They ask that we forestall some effort here in the Ettenmoors to curtail Angmar's advance in Moria. Will you answer the call?''There will be few others who will make the journey with you. Be safe and do all you can to thwart the incursion.''It matters not if you won, but that you fought. We must all do our part and we will fight in those depths until the force of Angmar plague them no more. Good effort, ${PLAYER_NAME}.'Deep in the Mines of Moria, forces of Angmar and the Free People clash for control of a dwarf-hall.A simple task. Speak with Uglash to travel to the Heart of Baranzibar in Moria. There, fight off the Free People who would take this treasured hall away from your allies.Speak with Uglash to travel to the Heart of BaranzibarFight against the encroaching Free People in the depths of Moria. Speak with again to make the journey swiftly.Complete a Battle in the Heart of BaranzibarAfter fighting in the depths of Moria, there is only one thing left to do. Speak with Uglash and tell them how the battle went.'Scouts found a hold in Moria where we can mine for material to make better weapons of war! We need adventurous sorts to go down into the dark and keep the Free People away from this find. You willing to fight, maggot?''Good choice. I always prefer volunteers to forcing you maggots into something you'll just get squashed doing. Now, get into the dark and destroy those Free People.''You fought. That is enough... for now. The Free People will keep attacking the Heart of Baranzibar. We will not relent.'The corsairs brought rats with them, very hungry rats.The rats must be dealt with to save the food supplies in the warehouse.Defeat rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})As a reward for the efforts of the most recognized, noble, and persistent in the Ettenmoors, the Captain-Generals have commissioned a set of cloaks to be made and distributed to those who have achieved the rank of Lieutenant and better.Speak with Quartermaster Ash again and choose your reward for your continued efforts in the Ettenmoors.Speak to Ash at Glân Vraig'It seems not long ago that you stood there before me asking me how you get your hand on an Orc-cleaver like mine; all wide-eyed and timid in awe of this incredible specimen. Now look at you, a veteran in your own right, capable of standing with me - well, near me anyway, as I look down from on high at all the other new recruits looking to make their mark here in the Ettenmoors.

'You were scared like they are; we were all scared, but that doesn't mean we are cowards. We can face down the Orcs, and the spiders, and Wargs, and even the uruks, we can take them and now you can look good killing them.

'The Captain-Generals have seen fit to make some new cloaks for you all. All you need to do is choose and the cloak is yours. The Captain-Generals have limited the supply and I cannot hand too many out, so you should act quickly.''Looks like you have come back to make a decision. So, what is it going to be?'As a reward for the efforts of the most vile, depraved, and ignoble curs fighting in the Ettenmoors, the War-Tyrants have commissioned new honourifics for those having achieved the rank of Lieutenant and better.Speak with War-tyrant Akúlhun again to choose your reward for your continued efforts in the Ettenmoors.Speak to War-tyrant Akúlhun at Gramsfoot'I remember the first time I set eyes on your frail body; unscarred, unmarred by battle as if a newborn plucked from suckling. Now, I look upon you are recognize a seasoned warrior who has tasted the flesh of Men, dwarves, hobbits, and Elves. A hero to our cause!

'We have names for people like you, and you get to choose which you shall be known by. Just talk to me again and tell me which name we shall call you!''What will it be, former maggot?'As a reward for the efforts of the most recognized, noble, and persistent in the Ettenmoors, the Captain-Generals have commissioned new monikers to be bestowed on all who have achieved the rank of Lieutenant and better.Speak with Quartermaster Ash again and choose your reward for your continued efforts in the Ettenmoors.Speak to Ash at Glân Vraig'What's in a name? Some folks think that they hold power, some think that you can just choose your own. I've seen some ridiculous names in my time and that's not including all the Elves that I have been forced to deal with. Fortunately, the Captain-Generals are better at working out titles.

'In their wisdom they have given me leave to bestow new honourifics on the deserving. You take a look at them and let me know which one you would like.''Looks like you have come back to make a decision. So, what is it going to be?'Believing that they will lead his people to ruin, Jajax hopes to weaken the forces of the Heirs of Castamir in Hata Kebir.Half-trolls and men devoted to the Heirs of Castamir can be found in Hata Kebir in south-eastern Lebennin.

Jajax has asked you to help him weaken the forces of the Heirs of Castamir before they can cause further harm to Umbar.Defeat Half-trolls in Hata Kebir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn rowing boats in Hata Kebir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Corsairs and Haradrim in Hata Kebir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Jajax can be found at your side or can be called with your horn.

You have greatly weakened the forces of Hata Kebir and should now speak to Jajax.Talk to Jajax'I wonder if the others see what I do, ${PLAYER}...

'There will be no victory for Umbar no matter the outcome of this war, my friend. We have left our people at Mordor's mercy, and the closer we draw to victory in the east is the closer we draw to our own ruin. As I see it, these Heirs are pretenders, and none of them will rule even the smallest plot of land in the coming days. If we are to remain free of Mordor's oppression, the Heirs must fail in this war.

'Come, the men here are among their most devoted - let us break their morale before they can cause more harm to Umbar.'You may not believe me, but some of those were fine men... just lured to folly by the words of the Heirs.

'There remained no time or means to sway them from their foolishness, my friend, but I curse the Heirs for leading them down this path.

'Come now, there is still more to be done.'Hoping to confront the thief before the words on the stolen scroll can be spoken, Maenir directs you to the Old Archives.Gúldil can be found just inside the Old Archives in the tunnels of the Fifth Circle.

Gúldil has asked you to confront the thief in the Old Archives.Talk to GúldilGúldil can be found just inside the Old Archives in the tunnels of the Fifth Circle.

You have defeated the fell power summoned by the scroll and cleared the Archives of danger. You should now speak to Gúldil.Talk to GúldilMaenir can be found on the first floor of the Houses of Lore in the Fifth Circle.

You should inform Maenir that the scroll is destroyed and the fell power within it banished.Talk to MaenirMithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should inform Mithrandir of what you encountered in the Old Archives.Talk to Mithrandir'Ah yes, there was one man interested in our gathered knowledge of languages. He was holding a scroll, but I thought nothing of it at the time as most who come through here are studying one thing or another. I do not wish to appear rude, but he seemed to be a bit of a haggard fellow.'

You inform Gúldil that this man is likely a thief and has taken a prized trophy from the Houses of Lore.

'I take it back, ${PLAYER}. Rude or not, he had the look of a thief and that is why I have kept such a close eye on the entrance since he arrived!

'I can show you the way to our collection of works on the languages of Men, but I leave it to you to deal with him.''Come - let me lead you through the archives.''I heard a great calamity in the back of the Archives! Have you dealt with the thief?'

You inform Gúldil that you were able to confront the thief, but he was slain by some manner of fell spirit.

'A spirit? In the archives? Nonsense! If you happened to use too much force and slew that thief, I will not speak against you - you have my word.

'Nevertheless, I am glad this matter has been resolved, even at such a cost.''I am glad to see you return, ${PLAYER}. Were you able to find the scroll?'

You tell Maenir that the scroll burned after the thief read it aloud, but omit further details.

'Ah, I suppose it resolved itself then - I am sorry to have taken so much of your time.

'You have my thanks for seeking the scroll, even if it came to naught. All I would ask of you now is to return to Mithrandir and tell him that we need not worry any longer.''I am gladdened that you were able to destroy both the original and the transcript of the scroll, but the skill to summon a creature as foul as a rogmul by words alone is outside the power of most Men.

'It is likely that one of the Nazgûl had a hand in devising this plan, and judging by the chosen language, I believe it to be the High Sorcerer of Harad - a Man long succumbed to his Master's will. Unknowingly, the warrior who brought it to the city only worked to lay the foundation for the Enemy's ruinous plans. You did well to banish the rogmul, but I fear it is not the last we shall see of it.

'It shall not be long before I call upon you again, ${PLAYER}. Let us be prepared for the coming of the Enemy!'Cranniel, a passing merchant, could use a rest, while her dog, Shell, could use a walk.Shell the dog sits next to Cranniel.

You should see if the dog is ready for a walk.Use your whistle to see if Shell is ready to walkUse the whistle to summon your new friend for a walkWalk Shell along Cape Road, which runs along the coast of the Cape of Belfalas.Walk Shell along the Cape RoadUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedWalk Shell along Cape Road, which runs along the coast of the Cape of Belfalas.Continue walking Shell along Cape RoadUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedWalk Shell along Cape Road, which runs along the coast of the Cape of Belfalas.Walk further along Cape Road with ShellUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedWalk Shell along Cape Road, which runs along the coast of the Cape of Belfalas.Keep walking along Cape Road with ShellUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedWalk Shell along Cape Road, which runs along the coast of the Cape of Belfalas.Make your way back along Cape Road with ShellUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedWalk Shell along Cape Road, which runs along the coast of the Cape of Belfalas.Keep walking Shell back along Cape RoadUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedWalk Shell along Cape Road, which runs along the coast of the Cape of Belfalas.Continue walking Shell back along Cape RoadUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedWalk Shell along Cape Road, which runs along the coast of the Cape of Belfalas.Take Shell back to CrannielUse the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedFinish your walk with Shell.Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separatedCranniel is located near the lighthouse on the Cape of Belfalas.

You should speak with Cranniel.Talk to Cranniel'That is my dog Shell. She loves travelling everywhere with me. It looks like she wants to go for a walk! I am taking a break, but if you would like to take Shell for a walk, and if Shell would like to take a walk with you, you are more than welcome!'

Cranniel turns to Shell.

'Do you want to walk with this nice ${RACE}? You are a good dog! Yes, you are!''I hope she was no problem for you. She is a sweet dog, though starting to get on in years. Age certainly does not stop me from loving her though!'Shell wags her tail and looks about ready for a stroll by the sea.It looks as if Shell has had a good walk and is ready for a nap.Soldier Gazlup prepares for an assault against Lugazag by the Free Peoples.Defeat the enemy within the walls of Lugazag.

The enemy will fall as they crash against the walls, provided you stand against them as they attempt to crash the walls.Defeat the Free Peoples at Lugazag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Soldier Gazlup is at Lugazag. If the tower was lost to the enemy or Soldier Gazlup was beaten during the fighting, make your way to Gramsfoot and speak with War-tyrant Akúlhun.

You should return to Gazlup and report of your victory.'Our strength is in numbers, whelp. This has always been a truth. The Free Peoples will come, and they will crash upon these walls in an effort to drive us from this place.

'If they succeed, then our commanders at Dâr-gazag will know we are weakening, and all of our lives will come into question. Stand against the foe within these walls. Strike them down, and we shall have favour with Angmar!

'Fail us... and we will ship you north to work in the sulfur marsh. Fight and defeat the enemy within the borders of Lugazag!''Prepare yourself, maggot. This tower needs a solid defence!''We defeated them, for a while at least! They will not soon return to face us here at Lugazag, but still we must remain ever vigilant as they will return.

'For now we earn a reprieve. Return to me in time, and we shall stand in defence of Lugazag again!''You fought well at Lugazag. We must hold that tower at all costs. If it falls, the enemy will be too close, and we will need to commit forces to recovering it.

'You have earned this, but do not revel in your victory. Fight on for Angmar!'A lone Orc prowls the lost paths of the Dead Marshes, fell and stealthy.The Lone Orc Hunter Sorzúr wanders alone through through the Dead Marshes, disdaining any path. 

