Return the weapons to Erchar.Talk to Erchar at his encampment'During our escape to the wild, we made haste by dropping many of our heavier weapons. For this my men are without sufficient arms to defend themselves on the return to Linhir.

'${PLAYER}, will you retrieve some Corsair weapons for my men so that they make it to Linhir with their lives?''These weapons will do nicely. Put them in the barrel beside me.''The size of that creature.... How did it ambush us?!

'It is no man. This much is certain. Perhaps these half-trolls are an experiment of Sauron, and a gift to the Haradrim.

'Now we know that the enemy is searching for us. With these weapons, my men can defend themselves from any additional scouts sent our way.

'Let us turn our attention to Herion.'The corsairs have stolen many weapons from the armoury.The weapons must be recovered.Recover weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})To wage a war, one needs weapons. To sustain a war-machine, one needs the items to drive the war-machine.Wood can be found in the Grimwood Forest, and metal can be found in the Isendeep Mine.

Chieftain Torbok directed you to support the war effort by stripping the mines and forest bare.'I look about me and know that this wood is corrupt, and still the life that dwells here pains me. We are fighting a war and each day we gain or lose ground, and yet life still teems here! I have learned hatred, ${PLAYER}. I have learned to slaughter and destroy and in this wood, where corruption has so long held sway, I am not at peace.

'We need more weapons. We need more wood to fire the furnaces at Dol Dínen and within Carn Dûm. We need molten metal to forge our blades!

'Tear down this forest, scour the land in the north. Bring me fire, bring me molten metal to make the weapons this war so desperately needs!''Fuel for the fires and metal for the blades. This war will not end until we fill the land. We shall stand atop a heap of corpses as high as the central spire of Carn Dûm, ${PLAYER}.

'Then shall the Great Eye see that we are his greatest servants! Then shall Mordirith and his servants kneel to the Uruk!'Scout enemy camps scattered throughout West Gondor.Scout enemy camps scattered throughout West Gondor.Discover TingobelDiscover TathrendalfDiscover the Bandit EncampmentDiscover Abedec's WatchDiscover HashadîrDiscover Makham MijannDrawn to Tarlang's Crown by Azruthor, the Ruthless Dead now strike fear into the enemies of the Heirs of Castamir.The Dead can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown.

