Ulf has asked you to recover stolen gold and spoils of war from the Variags in hopes that he might barter for information with one of their number.Collect spoils and gold from Variags in Taur Drúadan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ulf can be found beyond the Eastern Blockade in Taur Drúadan.

Ulf has asked you to meet him beyond the Eastern Blockade between the Variag and Orc forces in hopes that he might barter with one of the Variags.Burnoth can be found at his camp among the War-stead of the King's Men in in Taur Drúadan.

You aided Ulf in recovering vital information from the Variag lord, and should now report back to Burnoth before continuing your journey.Talk to Burnoth at his camp in Taur Drúadan'We have had much time to ponder our course, but tracking our foe shall prove difficult no matter the choice.

'Many of our kinsmen have started through the winding paths of this forest, but we cannot follow them - not yet. We must learn more of our foe before we reach the Pelennor Fields, and on that, we are all agreed.

'Hutha and I shall speak more on what else can be done, but for now, perhaps it is best that you hear Ulf out. Ulf has devised a cunning, but unlikely plan - yet, I believe with your aid, it may succeed.

'Speak to him, and aid him if you might!''Ah, ${PLAYER}. I have heard talk of these Variags we have encountered in our journey, and I have devised a plan that might allow us to gain more information about the cur that slew Léofdag. 

'Rumours are spreading that some of their number seem to have a tenuous allegiance with the Enemy. It is the thought of our scouts that they are sell-swords, and have no true interest in the fates of Gondor or Rohan.

'If that is so, it may be possible to barter with a chief among them who knows more of our foe. Steal away the coins and spoils that the Variags have amassed, and bring them to me within their blockade. For my part, I shall find one of their chiefs and compel him to hear out our offer.

'I know as well as you that these men are not to be trusted, but I would not lose a chance to learn more of Léofdag's killer. Fear not... if they do not accept our barter, we shall fight our way out side by side.''Ah, that ought to be enough...

'Let us see what our friend here thinks of our offer!''I must admit, it puzzles me that one of the Enemy's men would surrender one of his allies for a modest bounty. Perhaps it is the way of these Variags... no true loyalty other than to their own wealth.

'I know not if he spoke true, but we have no other course at the moment but to trust his words.

'If this traitor intends to reunite with his master on the Pelennor, we must ride at once and keep a close watch on our kinsmen!'Artamir, son of Ondoher, was lost in a great battle against the Wainriders and his accursed brother, Faramir, has long searched for him within the lands of the Wastes.The Dead Marshes can be found to the west and north of Ondoher's Folly.

Faramir believes his brother might be found somewhere in the Dead Marshes to the west of Ondoher's Folly. You should search for any sign of Artamir, son of Ondoher.Faramir can be found on the plains south of Ondoher's Folly.

You did not discover any sign of Artamir or any spirit that might appear to be him. You should now return to Faramir.Talk to Faramir, son of Ondoher'In all the years I have wandered these lands, I have never learned of the true fate of my brother. When I awoke from what I learned to be my death, I saw a great force of Wainriders moving westward and then southward, but I could not follow them from these lands. Did my brother stand against them? Did he fall as I did?

'Search the low-lands to the west of this hill. If my brother fled the battlefield alive, he would have taken such a path. If not, perhaps... he too has been cursed.

'Please do this for me, ${PLAYER}, and tell me if you discover any sign of him. I must learn the truth of his fate.''I know of his brother's fate, ${PLAYER}, so perhaps it would be best if I told him. Do as he asks, but I shall work to soften the blow he shall soon be dealt.''In all my time here, I could not face the truth of my fate...

'Father and Artamir have found the peace they deserved in death, but I... I deserve no such comfort. Father laid his curse upon me, and I do not think ill of him for it. I failed him as a son and heir, and I shall remain alone and bound to this land far longer than it took me to realize my folly.

'I thank you for offering the truth to me, sorrowful as it may be.'As the Host of the West approaches the Black Gate, a sense of despair has taken root in even the hardiest warriors.Legolas can be found on the north-western ramparts of Haerondir.

Echil has asked you to speak to the Elves at Haerondir as their resolve has not visibly faltered. You should speak to Legolas first.Talk to Legolas at HaerondirElladan and Elrohir can be found on the eastern ramparts at Haerondir.

You have spoken to Legolas, but he has not experienced what Echil described. You should now speak to Elladan and Elrohir instead.Talk to Elladan and Elrohir at Haerondir'It has been a long march, ${PLAYER}...

'I can speak only for myself, but I am prepared for what may come when we reach the Black Gate. If my death awaits, I shall welcome it in the service of Gondor and of King Elessar. Even still, it is a weight to bear... and each man here bears it.

'I have seen much in these last days that I never imagined, and I am sure more still awaits beyond my sight. For all of these unknown joys or ills, I have not seen the Elves in this company falter even once. Whether they fear or not as Men do, they seem charmed.

'I wonder what eases them so in such times, and I wonder if it might offer some comfort to our company. Would you speak to them, my friend?''What is it, my friend?'

You tell Legolas of Echil's sense of wonder about the Elves at Haerondir, and how he wishes that he and the other Men might be so at ease as well. Legolas chuckles to himself, and Gimli scoffs quietly beside him.

'Your Ranger friend is perhaps too eager to think such things of the Elves. Isn't he, Gimli?

'It is not a lack of fear that drives me forth, but a sense of duty to Aragorn and to our kin in the Host. You and I have shared this long journey together and fear has not yet broken us even if it has lingered at every step of our adventures.

'These Men are the bravest of this Age, and I would not see them falter now. Victory can be won over the Enemy, and none would know that better than the sons of Elrond.

'Why don't you speak to them, ${PLAYER}? I wonder what they would make of Echil's talk of fearless Elves!''What troubles you, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Elladan and Elrohir of Echil's hope that the Elves in the Host of the West are without fear. Elladan stifles a laugh, but Elrohir is unable to hold back. Before Elladan is able to speak, Elrohir quickly interjects.

'I am sorry, my friend. Were that the truth, he would be the first to know! These Men should not think so little of themselves!'

Elladan gestures to Elrohir to be silent and begins to speak.

'No, there is no hidden bravery within us, my friend. Perhaps we benefit from knowledge of the past, but in matters of the Enemy, fear is ever present. The Ringbearer's quest is unlike any errand in the time of our father and the alliance of Men and Elves.

'You say these Men are fearful, but they still march forth knowing their doom. That is the truest bravery, and they must be made to see it.'There is much to be done in the Towers of the Teeth.The Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills.

