You should speak with Rhadrog.Speak with Rhadrog‘I hear Anborn is sending you to Nuiharn. While you're there, can you do me a favour? There is a shrub that grows amongst the ruins, silver-coloured and scraggly.  We call it hauntreek.  It is valuable to us because it glows an eerie blue colour when burned. Why do we want that? I'll explain when you return.

'Gather some hauntreek for me, and burn them in the braziers around Haerondir. The colour of the flames will change before your eyes!’‘I believe I owe you an explanation, ${PLAYER}. Have you noticed that no Orcs lurk in the ruins near Haerondir, as they do in all the other ruins in the Noman-lands? This is no accident. We have tricked those cowards into thinking that Haerondir is haunted! One of the ways we do this is with those blue-coloured flames you attended to earlier. Let me show you another way we spook them.'The Rangers know the lands of Ithilien well, and use their mastery of it to scare off encroaching foes who are easily unnerved in the shadows of Gondor's garden.Orcs and Khundolar searchers can be found throughout central and north-central North Ithilien.

Rhadrog has asked you to scare the forces of Mordor that are searching North Ithilien for the Rangers. You should <rgb=#FF00FF>roar</rgb> at the searchers while you remain hidden from their sight.Spook Mordor searchers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Spook Khundolar searchers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhadrog can be found at Henneth Annûn in north-central North Ithilien.

You have unnerved many of the Enemy's forces in North Ithilien and should now return to Rhadrog.Talk to Rhadrog'Ithilien may be beset by foes, my friend, but we have not yet lost the advantage.

'Our foes are large in number, but lacking in resolve. They do not share our knowledge of these lands and there remain many things in the dark of these woods that might strike fear into the heart of an Orc.

'It is that fear we must prey on, ${PLAYER}. The breaking of branches, a chirp that breaks the silence, and the howl of a great beast... our foes have quailed before them all.

'Orcs and Khundolar alike search the lands surrounding Henneth Annûn, and they are fearful of what lurks in the shadows of Ithilien.

'Seek their searchers in the lands around Henneth Annûn, and let loose a cry while you remain hidden from their sight. The fear we can instill in them is greater to our cause than any amount of bloodshed.''If we are so fortunate, those Orcs and Khundolar shall return to their masters with news of terrible, unseen things lurking in Ithilien.

'Regardless of our true strength, our company shall appear to be innumerable and ever-watching.

'You have done well, my friend.'Fire and slaughter blanket the Pelennor Fields as the Riders Three draw closer to their foe's whereabouts.Foes can be found across the Pelennor Fields.

