A burial within the lands of the Enemy seems an unlikely task, so you resolve to burn the dead before the Orcs can further dishonour them.It was a sorry fate that befell those slain at Ondoher's Folly, but no longer can the Orcs of Mordor defile and mock them in death.The trolls of Mordor and Minas Morgul that turned to stone in North Ithilien now serve as an unexpected source of a valuable moss.Sun-touched Morgul-trolls can be found in the hills surrounding Henneth Annûn.

Ereblen has asked you to return to the sun-touched Morgul-trolls you found previously and scrape patches of moss from them.Scrape moss from sun-touched Morgul-trolls in North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ereblen can be found in Henneth Annûn.

You have gathered a suitable amount of moss from the sun-touched trolls and should now deliver it to Ereblen.'Do you remember the trolls we found in the wilds of Ithilien, ${PLAYER}? The ones that had turned to stone?

'Some of our company have since returned to the sites where you discovered them, and they all appear to have encouraged the growth of a peculiar moss upon them! We harvested a small amount and were able to extract it into a healing salve.

'It is unlike any of the mosses we have encountered in Ithilien... could a troll from the Dead City truly give way to something so helpful to my kinsmen?

'Seek out the sun-touched trolls, my friend, and scrape the moss from them. Do not harvest it all - for I am certain we shall have further use of it in the coming days.''This is just enough! You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.

'I wonder what the Dark Lord would think if he knew his own trolls were of great aid to the healers of Gondor!'With their foes slain and the wealth of the Khundolar in their grasp, the Variags have decided to return to Khand once their final errand is finished.Jarl Gurthilm can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.

Jarl Gurthilm has offered you payment for the aid you gave to him and his men. You should discuss your choice with him.Complete A Just Reward - Honour AloneComplete A Just Reward - Spoils of WarJarl Gurthilm can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.

You have made your choice and should now speak to Jarl Gurthilm before parting ways.Talk to Jarl Gurthilm'It is done, ${PLAYER}. They have paid the price for our service, and more still for their betrayal!

'Lord Zarhal Kôz shall send no more men after us, and any among the Khundolar who would dare to track us will not soon find us in these lands again.

'My dealings with the Dark Lord are finished, as are those of my men. We shall not fight for a Master who does not honour our way.'

Jarl Gurthilm's eyes turn to the Mountains of Shadow and a scowl flashes across his face before he turns back to you.

'However, there remains the matter of your share.... You are free to take it, should you so choose. I understand if you would prefer to keep our dealings secret, so you may also refuse it and I shall send you on your way with basic supplies for your troubles.

'I would be a fool to turn down a larger cut, but I'm a man of principle.'

'I leave the choice to you.''With that sorted, I think it is best for my men and me to return to Khand now.

'Our battle is finished and our vengeance done, and we desire no greater role in this War. You keep the company of many great warriors, but do not underestimate the Dark Lord's power. In victory or defeat, I hope that you can escape his wrath.

'Off with you, ${PLAYER}. Your allies might think less of you if you continued to travel with men such as us... and rightfully so!'

With a smirk on his face, Jarl Gurthilm gestures for you to leave.With their foes slain and the wealth of the Khundolar in their grasp, the Variags have decided to return to Khand once their final errand is finished.Drúgred can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.

You have chosen to forgo your share of the gold, but Drúgred will offer you a meagre amount of supplies in return.Talk to Drúgred'So what shall it be, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Jarl Gurthilm that while his offer is generous, you do not wish to accept your share of the gold.

'I had a suspicion, and a small amount of hope, that you would refuse my offer. Your sense of duty is unfailing, ${CLASS}, and none should think less of you for honouring it. 

Besides, I shall have the shares sorted anew without yours, and my men and I shall be the richer for it!

'Speak with Drúgred, and he shall give you something to help you on your way. Not gold, mind you... but we're not heartless.''You do not want your share?'

Drúgred's eyes wander to the nearby piles of gold, and he appears dumbstruck by your decision.

'Truly, our ways are different... but I cannot begrudge you. You have done much for us, and that is to be commended. You have the bearing of a great warrior, and your allies are lucky to count you among them... even if their cause is nigh hopeless.

'Here, take these supplies. We can finish our journey without them, and you still have a battle to fight.'With their foes slain and the wealth of the Khundolar in their grasp, the Variags have decided to return to Khand once their final errand is finished.Blothára can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.

You have chosen to accept your share of the gold, and Blothára can deliver it to you when you are prepared.Talk to Blothára'So what shall it be, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Jarl Gurthilm that you would be glad to accept your share of the Khundolar's gold.

'You surprise me, ${CLASS}... perhaps we're more alike than I thought. There was a light in your eyes during the battle with the Khundolar, and not all of it came from the shimmering gold...

'If that is your wish, consider it done! Blothára has divided the shares, and yours is in his keeping. Speak to him, and it is yours!

'If our paths are so strange and winding as to cross again, you would be welcome among our company.''You'll take your gold?

'I must admit, I wagered a small portion of my share that you would refuse it. I suppose there's more sorting to be done then... Gurthilm must be delighted.

'We do not battle without the promise of rewards, and with all you have done, you should consider doing the same!'

'As promised, here is your share.'The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien alike have great need of your aid in studying and collecting the numerous plants and herbs of Middle-earth.The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien alike have great need of your aid in studying and collecting the numerous plants and herbs of Middle-earth.Complete Herbalism quests in North Ithilien and the Wastes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien alike have great need of your aid in studying and collecting the numerous plants and herbs of Middle-earth.The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien alike have great need of your aid in studying and collecting the numerous plants and herbs of Middle-earth.Complete Herbalism quests in North Ithilien and the Wastes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien alike have great need of your aid in studying and collecting the numerous plants and herbs of Middle-earth.The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien alike have great need of your aid in studying and collecting the numerous plants and herbs of Middle-earth.Complete Herbalism quests in North Ithilien and the Wastes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien alike have great need of your aid in studying and collecting the numerous plants and herbs of Middle-earth.The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien alike have great need of your aid in studying and collecting the numerous plants and herbs of Middle-earth.Complete Herbalism quests in North Ithilien and the Wastes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Discover the interiors of great structures of Osgiliath.Discover the interiors of Osgiliath buildings.Journey to the Dome of StarsJourney to the Osgiliath Houses of HealingJourney to the Palace of EldacarJourney to the Osgiliath CulvertsAlthough the battle is ended, Thurindol fears that the Enemy will soon muster more of his forces against Gondor within North Ithilien.Bâr Aroth can be found on a hillside to the north of the Cross-roads in North Ithilien.

Thurindol has asked you to assess the Enemy's presence in North Ithilien before you continue your journey to the refuge.Patrol the hill-top to the north of Bâr ArothPatrol the foot-hills of the Ephel Dúath to east of Bâr ArothPatrol the shores of the Anduin to the north of OsgiliathThurindol can be found at Aelin Veren.

You have scouted the lands surrounding Bâr Aroth and should bring news to Thurindol at Aelin Veren.Talk to Thurindol at Aelin Veren'After the great battle, we had much to consider, my friend.

'The Orcs claimed Bâr Aroth and from the north, the Khundolar struck and made inroads from Dagorlad.

'Where the rest that fled the battle have gone I do not know for certain, but I fear many may have found new refuge within North Ithilien.

'In these dark times, I count myself fortunate to have your trust and I give you mine in return.

'I would ask that you search the shores of the Anduin to the west, the hill-top to the north of Bâr Aroth, and the foot-hills of the Ephel Dúath, the Mountains of Shadow, for signs of our foes.

'When you have finished your patrol, meet me to the north at the old baths of Aelin Veren, and it is there we shall speak more on what is to be done in the coming days.''While I am gladdened that many Orcs failed in their crossing of the Anduin, I fear we will not soon see the last of the Enemy's wraiths and their terrible, flying beasts.

'We shall have to use greater caution in our movements, lest we be discovered from above. For my part, I am glad that you remained hidden from their sight, my friend.

'I shall bring these tidings to captain Anborn at Henneth Annûn.'After learning of the intentions of the Black Númenórean, Burudagath the Bloodletter, you and Artamir have decided to return to Haerondir and warn the Host of the West of their new danger at Ondoher's Folly.Haerondir can be found to the south of Ondoher's Folly in Dagorlad.

You have learned much from the spirit of Faramir and should now deliver a warning to the Host of the West at Haerondir.Return to Haerondir with Artamir's warningLaeglaw can be found in Haerondir.

You have returned to Haerondir and have been spotted by Laeglaw and Mincham. You should speak to Laeglaw.Talk to Laeglaw at HaerondirAnborn can be found at Haerondir.

You have returned to Haerondir too late, and now Laeglaw fears Anborn has sent his men on a foolish errand. You should speak to Anborn and ask what you can do to aid him.Talk to Anborn at Haerondir'I have outstayed my welcome in these lands, I think. I have found my mind unsettled and my thoughts drawn to my own death.

'This is no place for one such as me, ${PLAYER}. Twice you have helped me to realize my own peril, and I hope I shall not have need of a third opportunity.

'As much as I desire to spend more time speaking with Faramir of his life, our duties are to the Host of the West - and it is my duty to no longer impede them.

'All we have learned of the foes we now face... it goes beyond my knowledge and beyond my skill. Those we left behind at Haerondir, though... they could stand against them. Let us return there and tell them of what we have learned!

'I shall ride as swiftly as I am able, and I would ask that you do the same. Without your voice, I fear they shall not heed my warnings....''You have returned to us so late, ${PLAYER}, and I am afraid you have much to answer for in the eyes of captain Anborn. Artamir's errand may have endangered our entire cause, and for what? The chance to speak to a spirit?

'His foolishness may cost us more than time. You see, we returned to Haerondir after you departed and spoke to Anborn of your efforts to rescue Artamir from his delusions. He thought long on the matter and then chose his course. You must understand, my friend, Anborn sent an entire company to find you and Artamir on the battle plain. You have returned, but we have heard naught from them....'

You express regret at the effort put forth to ensure your return, but urge Laeglaw to understand that you have come with grave tidings about the foes lurking in Dagorlad and the coming battle with the Dark Lord at the Black Gate.

'I see, but Anborn has requested your presence at once upon your return, so I leave those matters to him.''${PLAYER}, I am glad you have returned to us. Yet, I must disagree with the course Artamir and you have taken. Such reckless actions could have led the Enemy to Haerondir or endangered the entire host, but they have not... and for that I am grateful.

'Do not mistake my concern for anger, my friend, but I would urge you to dissuade Artamir from any other adventures he might think to embark upon. Given the length of your absence, have you returned with any news of our foes?'

You inform Anborn of the designs of the Black Númenórean, Burudagath the Bloodletter, and warn him against possible encounters with more hostile fell spirits upon the battle plain.

'These are grim tidings, and they are made all the worse by the looming battle. I shall do what I can to prepare us should these evils come to Haerondir. As for you, my friend, I have a new task - one with which Artamir shall not be involved.'It is uncertain if there can ever truly be peace between the peoples of Gondor and Harad, but the Haradrim prisoners have offered their aid to the Men of Gondor for the sake of their kinsmen.Chan-két Doloi can be found at Aelin Veren in central North Ithilien.

Maendal has asked you to speak with Chan-két Doloi about his knowledge of the Enemy's plans.Talk to Chan-két DoloiMaendal can be found at Aelin Veren in central North Ithilien.

You have spoken to Chan-két Doloi and should now return to Maendal.Talk to Maendal'It is time we hear what their war-master knows. If he has not spoken true, the blood of his fellows shall be on his hands alone.

'With the Southrons routed at the Cross-roads and Cirith Negen, our foes shall now mainly strike from the north. The Enemy's plans for Dagorlad interest me greatly as any force rallied there could soon spill into Ithilien and beyond. These are fragile times, my friend... a misstep now could spell doom for the Host of the West and for Gondor.

'I would question him myself, but he might more readily offer his knowledge to you after all you have done for his people here. Go, and speak to him again and tell me what you learn.''I have not deceived you or these Rangers, ${CLASS}. I wish to return to Harad, and I will tell you whatever it is you require to allow me and my men to depart in peace.'

You ask about the Enemy's plans in Dagorlad, and to hear any other information Chan-két Doloi might have about the movements of the Enemy's forces in the coming days.

'The Dark Lord rallies all loyal to him to Dagorlad and the Black Gate... Orcs, Easterlings, and even more of my people. He awaits the arrival of a great host and lays many traps for them even now.

'As for the movements of his forces, I know of a company of Easterlings - the Khundolar - that have been ordered to hamstring the host as it passes through these woods. I do not know what they plan, but I would keep a careful watch on their forces. They are brutal beyond understanding, and would never surrender to you or any other.

'The Orcs of Mordor shall likely be driven to enter these lands as well, but they will be largely held in reserve in the Black Land until the Dark Lord has use for them. If their numbers seem great now, you shall have much to fear in the days ahead.

'That is all I know, ${PLAYER}. Tell the Rangers what I have told you, and urge them to lead us back to our homeland.'

Chan-két Doloi studies your face for a moment, and then speaks again.

'You are a curious ${RACE}, and I am pleased to have spoken so much with you. Let us hope that there are better days ahead for both of our peoples.''These are ill tidings, but I am heartened to know some of what awaits us, and gladder still that the Southron spoke true.

'I shall send a small company south with the prisoners, and bring them to the Crossings of Poros. If their brethren move against my men in their travels, they have been ordered to slay any and all attackers. It is a harsh measure, but this is a tenuous peace, and it is clear from the war-master's own words that his people are divided.

'What we have learned today could prove vital to the Host of the West, and I shall send one of my men to deliver word to Anborn at once!

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}. Let us hope we can stand together again in the days to come!'No longer wishing to involve his people in the affairs of the Dark Lord, Chan-két Doloi, a war-master of Harad, hopes to negotiate an uneasy peace.Maendal can be found at Aelin Veren.

Chan-két Doloi has offered his knowledge of the Enemy's plans in exchange for the ability to warn his people not to pass through North Ithilien or raise arms against the Rangers. You should speak to Maendal about his plan.Talk to MaendalIdeal banner locations can be found along the road, in southern North Ithilien.

Chan-két Doloi has offered knowledge of the Enemy's movements in exchange for warning his people not to pass through North Ithilien.Plant banners of Far Harad to warn away Haradrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Chan-két Doloi can be found at Aelin Veren, in central North Ithilien.

You have planted the warning banners of Far Harad and should now return to Chan-két Doloi.Talk to Chan-két Doloi'I know you wish to understand why I ordered my men to stand down.

'I ordered our surrender because I know that our people cannot win this war - not for ourselves, and not for the Dark Lord. I speak not for the others among my kin, and I do not claim falsely that the conflict between our peoples is ended. There have been many years of hatred between us, and old wounds are not so easily soothed.

'We have known the Rangers to be unforgiving of their foes, but we still draw breath... at least for now.

'I have kept several banners of Far Harad bundled in my armouring. They are borne into many battles, yes, but in my homeland they serve another purpose. You see, they are often used to mark areas of strife or of dangerous weather and winds. If you were to plant them along the southern roads of these lands, those that beheld them would be warned to turn back.

'In return, I will offer what I know of my people's plans in Dagorlad and of the Dark Lord's designs in the coming days of the War. I cannot promise that all will heed the warning banners, but if the captain of these Rangers wishes to see fewer of my people in his lands, he should consider it.''I do not know if I trust him, ${PLAYER}...

'It could lessen the burden on the Host of the West and leave Ithilien clear of their people. If it is a ruse, they could lead the Enemy's forces to our position.

'If this truly means that fewer Southrons will attempt to pass through Ithilien, I must allow it. Raise the banners as he asked, but begin the trail far to the south from Aelin Veren. Even if they follow it, they will not discover us, and if the Southron spoke true, they will turn about at the sight of them and have no need to continue northward.

'Be swift, my friend, for I desire to learn what the Southron knows of the Enemy's designs in Ithilien.''Were it any but you among these Men, I would not trust that the task had been finished. These Rangers have treated us better than I believed they would, but I shall not trust them - not this day, nor any day in the future.

'You have done me and my people a great favour, and I shall not forget that.

'All I wish for now is the chance to return home with my men and leave this War behind.'Mablung has suggested that you take Faroth with you on your adventures. Will you accept?Talk to Faroth if you would like to take him with you.Talk to Faroth'Excellent ranging, ${PLAYER}. The Noman-lands and the Host of the West are safer for your actions. 

'And of course, we must thank Faroth! 

'You two seem to have quite the bond. Would you care to take him with you? I am certain he would make an excellent adventuring companion.'You have decided to take Faroth on your adventures into the Wastes and beyond. Faroth looks thrilled!Torngroth, the last of the Ranger refuges to fall, has fallen into the hands of the Enemy, and those that aided in its defence are now lost or slain.Collect the Ranger's broochThe brooch can be found on the ground within Torngroth.

You have discovered a worn Ranger's brooch within Torngroth and should collect it before returning to Henneth Annûn.Collect the Ranger's broochHenneth Annûn can be found in north-central Ithilien.

You have collected the brooch and should now return it to someone in Henneth Annûn.While exploring Torngroth, you have discovered an ornate brooch in the abandoned Ranger hideout. It is unclear to whom the brooch belongs or if they yet live, but perhaps it would be best to deliver it to the Rangers at Henneth Annûn.'I know this brooch, my friend.

'It belonged to my brother... and at last his fate is clear to me. Although the Rangers held that refuge for many years, the Enemy discovered the location of Torngroth and we were forced to battle our way out. In our flight, we became separated and he never made it to Henneth Annûn.

'I have mourned for him ever since, but now I wonder... what drew him back to Torngroth?

'Ah, well, that is a matter for another time. I shall keep his brooch close, ${PLAYER}. You have my thanks.'Mablung has asked you to meet with the Variag Jarl Gurthilm who has expressed a wish to parley.Jarl Gurthilm can be found in after-battle Osgiliath.

You should find the Variag Jarl and learn what he wants.Meet with GurthilmYou should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.Talk to MablungCollect supplies and payment scattered around the encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.Collect supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather confiscated treasure (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Jarl Gurthilm can be found in after-battle Osgiliath.

You should bring the payment to Variag Jarl and make sure he keeps to his promise.Bring the payment to GurthilmYou should talk to Mablung, who can can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.Talk to Mablung'How much do you know of the Variags, my friend? We have had little contact with these men from the east. They seem fell but not mindlessly bloodthirsty, and from what I have been able to gather, care more for gold than honour or fealty.

'This is not idle gossip. A Variag Jarl, who goes by the name of Gurthilm, has made signs that he wishes to parley with someone from the Host of the West. While I trust him little, he claims he intends no harm. 

'Would you go and meet this Jarl Gurthilm, and learn, if you can, his true designs?''Are you the one they sent? Good, then I will only say this once.

'My men and I are breaking our pact with the Easterlings and, indeed, wish to sever all ties with Mordor. We have no quarrel with Gondor or the men of the West. We ask only safe passage. We plan to make our way back towards Khand, but to make such a journey, we require gold and supplies.

'As a token of good will, we will divulge the location of a large group of enemies you seek. What say you?'

You tell Gurthilm that you will discuss the Variag's proposal with others. He nods a curt assent.'The culverts, of course! It has been impossible to search both the city and the culverts thoroughly. We used all we could spare on the ruins above-ground and have neglected those under-passages completely!

'While I am not surprised they threatened you, this knowledge was worth their brutish dealings.''He breaks his troth and sells his former allies' lives for his own? There is no honour in such a man. 

Mablung lets out a sigh.

'I do not understand these lawless men nor do I trust them. But I would know the location of these enemy encampments. Yes, I deem it worth the price.

'Very well. Collect the supplies and gold they seek. You should find what you need here within our camp. But ${PLAYER}, if they cross us, you are under no obligation to keep them from harm!''You have done as we asked. This is good. It means we trust you enough to work with you. The hidden encampment is located right beneath your feet.

'Now you have your information. Be on your way and give us safe passage. Do not cross us though. We do not take kindly to such treachery.'Thurindol asks for you to collect samples of the water within the maggot-holes of Skoironk.Standing water can be found within the caverns of Skoironk.

You should collect samples of the water within the caverns for Thurindol.Thurindol can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.

You should speak with Thurindol.'It is still unclear if these maggots are the architects of these caverns or if machines bore these tunnels.

'Would you collect water samples from the caverns so that I may study them?

'We may be able to ascertain more about these unnatural structures from the waters which seep through the rock of the hills.''Let us see these samples.'

Thurindol holds one sample in each hand, peering into the glass phial as he holds each up to the smoke-masked sun.

'This sample is from near the entrance, is it not? While it is filthy, it is not as toxic as the waters around us in the slag. No doubt then, a product of Orc occupation. Now, this other sample is interesting. The water here is much purer. I believe our initial thought, that the maggot creatures were the ones who dug these holes, is indeed the correct assumption. This is very interesting and I look forward to learning more once the battle concludes.

'What troubles me, though, is that every maggot you have encountered thus far seems to only be in the larvae stage. Once fully grown, these creatures could potentially be terrifying.'After acquiring the sample of trollstrife, Mílgamel is curious to learn of the state of the water and soil in the Wastes, as well as that of any plants that still cling to life.Soil and mushrooms can be found somewhere within the southern reaches of the Dead Marshes or upon the battle plain. The Slag-hills can be found due east of Haerondir.

Mílgamel has asked you to seek samples of mushrooms, soil, and the brackish waters of the Slag-hills. You should obtain these samples and then return to her.Collect hardy mushrooms in the Wastes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect samples of blasted soil in the Wastes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect a sample of water at the Slag-hillsMílgamel can be found at Haerondir.

You have gathered the samples that Mílgamel requested and should now return to her at Haerondir.'While I work with the trollstrife you recovered for me, I would have you explore the Wastes further.

'It is plain to see that these lands have laid barren for many long years, but even among this desolation I have seen the trunks of trees and felt the soft crack of mushroom caps under my feet as we travelled to Haerondir.

'Search the lands surrounding Haerondir for samples of soil and mushrooms if you would.

'If I have need of the good, I shall also have need of the very worst the Wastes has to offer us... so collect a small phial of water from the run-off surrounding the Slag-hills to the east.

'Hurry now, ${PLAYER}. I would prefer my research to be finished before the battle is joined!''Ugh, what is that horrid smell?'

You eagerly hand the phial of slag-water to Mílgamel.

'This is hardly water at all! Look, ${PLAYER}, it has little bits of... something floating all about in it.

'None of that will do, but let me see the mushrooms and the pouches of soil you gathered! Yes, yes, these are lovely. The soil is thin and unhealthy, but it clings to life... and these mushrooms, I do not know if anything could stop them.

'Come now, we have to attempt to cross-breed them with the plants of Ithilien!'Anborn recalls bringing Gollum forth to be questioned by Faramir shortly after his capture, and his fears for the journey of the Halflings and the gangrel-creature.Anborn can be found within Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.

Anborn has offered to tell you more of the strange Halflings and their time among the Rangers.Listen to Anborn's taleAnborn can be found within Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.

Anborn has finished his tale, and you should now ask him if there remains any more to tell.Talk to Anborn'This is the last I saw of them until we parted ways in the forest. I can share what I remember, for these memories will not soon be forgotten.

'It was a strange discussion, and though I do not know the context, perhaps you can guess at it and relay the tale to the friends of the Halflings.

'Faramir asked me to bring the gangrel-creature to him so that he could question it, and so I did.''I have more yet to tell. Are you ready to hear of it, ${PLAYER}?''The night passed without incident. I was glad to be rid of the gangrel-creature when Faramir led them away in the morning.

'I cannot fathom what could have passed between Captain Faramir and the Halfling to make my lord grant them free passage in Ithilien, but all that I witnessed between them led me to believe that it was some strange, important errand. I trust my lord's judgment.

'I wish I had better news to tell you of your friends. They seemed hale enough ere they departed, but, as I said, they made for an evil place...the pass of Cirith Ungol.'Too many visiting well-wishers around the Houses of Healing are getting in the way of the healers' work and need to be shooed away.Torchún has asked you to disperse visiting well-wishers inside and outside the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Disperse well-wishers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Torchún outside of the Houses of Healing and let him know you have dispersed a number of visiting well-wishers.Return to Torchún'A great flood of well well-wishers has been flooding the Houses of Healing, ${PLAYER}. I would swear there are three of them to every wounded soldier! They must be turned away - the healers and herbalists are tripping over them to tend the patients!

'Would you go inside and outside the Houses of Healing and shoo away as many as you can?''You have sent a good number of them away? You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'Among the Orcs at Ondoher's Folly, you have glimpsed an unusual sight: a shade of a long-dead warrior of Gondor.The accursed warrior can be found wandering Ondoher's Folly in north-western Dagorlad.Attempt to talk to the accursed warrior at Ondoher's FollyThe accursed warrior can be found wandering Ondoher's Folly in north-western Dagorlad.

You have encountered the shade of an accursed warrior wandering the hill of Ondoher's Folly. You should attempt to speak to him.Attempt to talk to the accursed warrior at Ondoher's FollyAs you explore Ondoher's Folly, an unusual sight drifts into view.

In the distance, the shifting shade of a Gondorian warrior floats around the temple-hill, seemingly beneath the notice of all nearby Orcs of Mordor.

It is unclear if this shade is a cursed Man of Gondor or a fell spirit holding a form familiar to you, but something compels you to investigate.You approach the shade and attempt to speak with him, but it does not respond. His gaze remains fixed directly ahead of him, and he almost seems unaware of your presence.

Amid the sounds of nearby Orcs, the shade begins to shriek in a harsh tone.

'Father! I am sorry! Forgive me, I beg you! Brother... Artamir! Do not stay silent! Father will hear your words!'

Just as swiftly, the shade falls silent again.Complete quests in the Houses of Healing after the battle of the Pelennor Fields.Complete quests in the Houses of Healing after the battle of the Pelennor Fields.Complete -- Interlude: A Dream of Cold and SilenceComplete -- Interlude: A Secret ReturnComplete -- The Hands of a HealerAfter the Battle of the Pelennor Fields, Imrahil has summoned you to aid the great city of Minas Tirith.The horse to after-battle Minas Tirith can be found in the Threshold of the City, or in Minas Tirith pre-battle.

Take the horse to after-battle Minas Tirith so that you may meet with Imrahil.The horse to after-battle Minas Tirith can be found in the Threshold of the City, or in Minas Tirith pre-battle.

Take the horse to after-battle Minas Tirith so that you may meet with Imrahil.Take the horse to Minas Tirith, After the BattleImrahil can be found just outside the walls of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Imrahil.Speak with ImrahilThe Battle of the Pelennor Fields is at an end and Gondor has seen victory on this day. However, the city of Minas Tirith has succumbed to much death and destruction. Imrahil, Prince of Dol Amroth, has summoned you to his side as he begins the task of rebuilding the White City.'Ah, ${PLAYER}, I am glad you were able to come so quickly to aid the efforts here. There is much to be done.'The Rangers of Ithilien do not often show mercy to their foes, but to hold prisoners demands a certain watchful care.The river that flows through Aelin Veren can be found in central North Ithilien.

Maendal has asked you to fill water-skins in the eastern waters of the river flowing through Aelin Veren before giving them to the prisoners.The Haradrim prisoners can be found at Aelin Veren, in central North Ithilien.

You have returned with the filled water-skins and should now offer them to the Haradrim prisoners.Maendal can be found at Aelin Veren in central North Ithilien.

You have offered a water-skin to each of the prisoners and should now speak to Maendal.Talk to Maendal'${PLAYER}, a few of the Southrons have complained of thirst. I do not doubt it,  but I will not send my Rangers away from their sides. We still know little of their purpose here, and I dare not offer them the chance to slay us while our numbers are thinned.

'Still, I would not deny a prisoner such care, even one as hated as a Man of Harad. To the east of Aelin Veren lies the source of this river, beneath a great waterfall.

'I would ask that you take these water-skins and fill them there. When you return, offer them to the prisoners and let us hope it's enough to calm them for a time.

'If we are so fortunate, perhaps they may be more inclined to tell us of the Enemy's plots in Ithilien.''I did not expect such treatment from these Rangers....''Why even bother, ${RACE}?''An odd sort, these Men....

'We have heard they never take prisoners, and yet, here we are.

'Thank you, ${RACE}. This water soothes my ills....''You have my thanks. I have no love for these Men, but if bloodshed can be avoided this day, I shall do what I must.''I hope it is enough to soothe their thirst for a time, ${PLAYER}.

'I do not wish to offer them more than we can spare our own, but water is plentiful in these lands.

'Let us hope such a gesture gives them pause should they wish to attack us yet.'There is much to do to aid the people in Minas Tirith after the Battle of the Pelennor Fields.People who need aid after the battle may be found either in the First Circle of the city or in the Houses of Healing in the Sixth Circle.

You have been asked to aid the people of Minas Tirith as they recover from the Battle of the Pelennor Fields.

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will fail any Aiding Minas Tirith quests not yet completed for the day.</rgb>Complete quests in aiding Minas Tirith after the battle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'There is much to be done in Minas Tirith as we pick up the pieces. Though this was a victory, it was only nearly won.

'Many need help within the city walls. Much of the first tier has been bombarded by the Enemy and the Houses of Healing are over capacity as they treat the injured and dying. Can I count on you to assist those in need?'

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will fail any Aiding Minas Tirith quests not yet completed for the day.</rgb>Fearful of a young apprentice being miseducated by Galathir, Ioreth has asked you to join her on a daunting task.Galathir can be found in the House of Remedies within the Masters' Tier of Minas Tirith (After-battle).

Ioreth has asked you to speak with Galathir for she fears he might mislead a young apprentice in his tutelage.Talk to Galathir in the House of RemediesMílgamel can be found in the House of Remedies within the Masters' Tier of Minas Tirith (After-battle).

Galathir has given his apprentice, Mílgamel, a daunting task, and he has asked that you aid her in completing it.Talk to Mílgamel in the House of RemediesMílgamel can be found along the central causeway in Osgiliath (After-battle).

Mílgamel has asked you to meet her in Osgiliath before embarking on her survey of Ithilien.Meet Mílgamel near the remains of the Great Bridge in Osgiliath (After-battle)Mílgamel can be found on the central causeway in Osgiliath (After-battle).

You have found Mílgamel and should now speak to her about her plans for surveying Ithilien.Talk to Mílgamel in Osgiliath (After-battle)Mílgamel can be found at your side or summoned by horn.

Mílgamel has asked you to aid her in surveying the greater lands of Ithilien. You should bring her to each location she mentioned and confer with her once there.Mílgamel can be found at your side or summoned by horn.

Mílgamel has finished her initial survey and has asked to be escorted to Henneth Annûn. You should speak to her once you arrive at Henneth Annûn.Mílgamel can be found at Henneth Annûn.

You have escorted Mílgamel to Henneth Annûn and should now speak to her about what is to be done next.'Do not misunderstand me, ${PLAYER}. Galathir still possesses great skill as a healer, but he has lost sight of his shortcomings. In my long years in Minas Tirith and Imloth Melui, I have never found a shortage of new skills to learn and new draughts and tinctures to use in my work, from new trial and old lore alike. But Galathir has grown reliant on his own concoctions for his patients, and where one ill is healed another often takes its place.

'He has taken a new apprentice - a young woman by the name of Mílgamel. The poor girl has no idea that she might receive such misguided instruction! It is one matter for a certain draught or salve to seem the clear choice, and quite another entirely for it to truly be so. Indeed, there are many uses for Everworth, Trueleaf, Snagbane, Blushblade, Settlegang...'

Recalling that you have a certain urgency to your task, Ioreth trails off and pauses briefly.

'I have heard tell that Mílgamel shall soon make for Ithilien. Perhaps you would accompany her on your own journey back to the king's side, and while you do, help her see all she has to learn there, and not only that which Galathir has pre-ordained she should see. For they say that place was once the garden of all Gondor, and what forgotten herbs and herblore may await there, just as when I told Mithrandir of the old saying that the hands of the king... ah, but I see I am needed.

'Talk to Galathir and convince him of your worth in this task, and then speak to her. We shall make a great healer of her yet!''What do you want? Can you not see there are still many near to death and in need of tending? Even my healers are taking ill from lack of rest!

'If idle chatter is your wish, begone. If you have need of my ear, speak!'

You tell Galathir of your desire to accompany Mílgamel on her survey of Ithilien.

'So you have heard I am sending her off, have you? No matter. You know of her task? Certain herb-stores vital to my most trusty medicines dwindle near to nothing. If these can be found where herbalists long dared not tread, then she must make a thorough harvest. Mind you! I do not wish Mílgamel distracted by any strange roots and leaves we have no use for and which might prove harmful in the extreme! 

'You will find Mílgamel in the House of Remedies ready to ride to Ithilien. She knows her course, ${CLASS}...so keep her from harm. I cannot afford the loss of another healer.

'Now leave me!''Excuse me, what is it that you want? I'm quite busy enough in my studies and have little time to speak.'

You introduce yourself to Mílgamel and inform her that you are to be her guide for Galathir's task.

'Oh! I am so sorry... I've been a mite overwhelmed by Galathir's demands as of late. He is a wise teacher, but his tasks are often far more daunting than he thinks them. Perhaps he has forgotten what it was like to be a novice...

'He has charged me with surveying our lands in the aftermath of the battle. I have taken careful note of the twenty-three leaves, flowers, and roots he wishes me to search for... but I can think only of what I shall see in the ruins upon the Anduin, in lost Ithilien, and beyond! I must calm myself. I can see Master Galathir frowning at me even now. I must stay true to my task!

'My survey is to begin in Osgiliath, but it shall stretch far beyond it. If you are to be my guide, I ask that you meet me near the old bridge in Osgiliath. I can ride that far, but I would prefer to do my survey on foot.''Oh, I almost didn't hear you over the roaring water!

'In all my days, I have never crossed the Great River... and I wanted to spend some time looking upon it before you arrived. All that lies ahead is known to me only through distant gazes, travellers' tales, and old maps.

'I know it as a land of striking beauty, even at a distance, but I know that there is an unseen danger lurking within it - else the Rangers would have naught to do but rest. 

'Ah, but rest does not come easy these days...

'My brother was gravely wounded in the battle, and I tended to him in the Houses of Healing after he was taken from the Fields. I have never felt so powerless in my life, ${PLAYER}. Master Galathir and the lady Ioreth helped ease his pain, but his wounds were too many and too great. He lasted the night, but by dawn death had claimed him.

'I have kept his blade in my keeping, and I shall wield it if ever the need arises...'

Mílgamel pauses for a moment and stares into the rushing waters below.

'In addition to list of herbs, Master Galathir has given me a strict list of locations to direct my survey... perhaps some of them are familiar to you?'

Mílgamel hands you the list. The list mentions the old Houses of Healing in Osgiliath, the ruins of Bâr Aroth and Aelin Veren as well as the island fortress of Cair Andros in Ithilien, and mostly troublingly, the road into Imlad Morgul. At the end, it makes a note that the Rangers have been made aware of Mílgamel's passage into Ithilien and shall make arrangements at Henneth Annûn.

'Ah, so you do know them! Let us get started then, shall we?''Not in all my days have I seen such gorgeous lands, ${PLAYER}! I have heard much of Ithilien, but the tales all fall short in conveying its true beauty. I am proud to report that I have identified many of the herbs Master Galathir seeks... but I could not help take note of the many, many strange plants I had never before set eyes upon. Some stirred memories of drawings I had seen in musty tomes within the Old Archives, and I cannot help but wonder what powers some of these might possess... but I can see Master Galathir frowning down at these foolish thoughts of mine!

'I hope the Rangers do not mind my brief company here in their... cave. I don't mean to disparage their choice of refuge, but it is a cave.

'Yet, I can't deny there's a homely warmth to it... perhaps I'll take a few notes about Henneth Annûn for my own keeping.'Even in the harsh terrain of the Noman-lands, life, though it hardy and few, still flourishes.Hauntreek can be found in the ruins of Nuiharn, west of Haerondir.

