You have had a strange encounter with a shade of Gondor and should now tell Artamir about what you have seen and heard.Talk to Artamir at Tham DurlanThe accursed warrior has appeared at Tham Durlan in Dagorlad.

You have told Artamir of the strange connexion between him and the accursed warrior, and now the shade has appeared at his side. You should try to uncover the shade's purpose in coming to Tham Durlan.Talk to the accursed warrior at Tham DurlanArtamir can be found at Tham Durlan in Dagorlad.

The accursed warrior has not spoken to you since his arrival, but offered Artamir a grim warning. You should talk with Artamir about what is to be done.Talk to ArtamirHis words still fresh in your memory, the shade floats silently before you.

The shade wailed the name Artamir, and spoke as if Artamir were his brother. Without pausing to consider the absurdity of what you are about to speak, you tell the shade that a man named Artamir is among your company in the ruins to the south.

A puzzled expression washes over the shade's face, and his gaze swiftly shifts to meet your own. However, before speaking a word, he vanishes.'You say a spirit of some kind knew my name, ${PLAYER}? That he called out for an Artamir?

'I have had quite enough dealings with spirits for my liking, I'll have you know. There must be some mistake...

'You see, it is common in Gondor to honour our ancestors by bestowing their names upon our children, and even within Minas Tirith, I know no fewer than two others bearing my name. If I am recalling correctly, I even once told you of old King Ondoher's son named Artamir.

'No, no. That man cannot be me, my friend. How long has this spirit lingered in the Wastes? How many have fallen since he met his own end?'

Artamir begins to trail off as a look of horror appears on his face.

'D-do not move, ${PLAYER}!'The shade stares at you, but remains silent.

After a moment, he turns to Artamir and begins to speak.'Wainriders? They have not been a threat to Gondor, much less seen at all, for hundreds of years now. Perhaps this spirit has mistaken the Easterlings for their old ancestors, else I cannot say. To have silently watched for so long, it is possible he has lost his understanding of the passing peoples and creatures of these lands.'

Artamir's face still betrays his fear, but you sense a renewed resolve rising within him.

'Fate and chance drove me to the Dead Marshes, and now they have guided me thus. I... I shall resist them no longer. I may not be the man this spirit seeks, but his knowledge of these lands and our enemies may be turned to our benefit. I... I believe I know this spirit's identity, my friend, but more questions still linger... and answers seem unlikely unless he and I speak alone.'The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien have need of your aid, and offer great rewards in return for your continued service.Quests for the herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien can be found at the Camp of the Host and within Henneth Annûn.You should complete quests for the herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien.

Quests for the benefit of the herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien can be found at the Camp of the Host and within Henneth Annûn.Complete quests for the herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The herbalists of Minas Tirith and Ithilien have continued need of your aid.You have triumphed over the Men of Harad, shattered their leadership, and thrown down their vile standards.Complete the deeds in Blood of the Black Serpent.Complete the deeds in Blood of the Black Serpent.Complete the deed Blood of the Black Serpent -- Tier 1Complete the deed Blood of the Black Serpent -- Tier 2Complete the deed Challenge: Fall of the Two PrincesGladhir has asked you to stop the Haradrim camped in the hills from discovering Haerondir and threatening the Host of the West.You should find the Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha, located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills.Enter Dûm BohaYou should find and defeat Rujateng at Dûm Boha.Defeat RujatengComplete Quest: The Eyes and The BlindComplete Quest: Beneath the SnakeComplete Quest: Dwindling RationsComplete Quest: The Poisoned MindYou should return to Gladhir, who can be found at Haerondir.Return to Gladhir'${PLAYER}, it is good to have you here with us on the doorstep of the Enemy. After you left Osgiliath, the other Rangers and I had little difficulty finding and defeating the last Orcs hiding amongst the city ruins.

'Now then, to the matter at hand. As you may have heard, the Enemy does not venture into the ruins of Haerondir, for they believe it haunted. In truth, this is not the case. It is an appearance we keep up so that we may occupy this most northern look-out for Gondor undisturbed.

'Not long ago, Haradrim set up camp just over the western hills. We have noticed their patrols widen as each day passes. While we have been able to trick the Orcs for many years, I fear the Haradrim are shrewder foes.

'We must stop this camp from spreading and uncovering the truth about Haerondir. Would you take on this task while we guard the western gate from assault?''With all you have done for us, both past and present, no reward could suffice. I am glad to have you as a trusted ally, ${PLAYER}.

'I believe the Haradrim will no longer pose a threat to Haerondir. From what our look-out, Dornach, was able to surmise, their numbers should not be able to fully organize until well after the Host of the West passes their camp.

'We need not fear any ambush from that direction, at least, thanks to you.'Defeat many spiders and beasts in North Ithilien.Defeat many spiders and beasts in North IthilienDefeat many spiders and beasts in North IthilienDefeat many spiders and beasts in North Ithilien.Defeat many spiders and beasts in North IthilienDefeat many spiders and beasts in North IthilienDefeat many spiders and beasts in North Ithilien.Defeat many spiders and beasts in North IthilienDefeat many beasts in Far Anórien.Defeat many beasts in Far Anórien.Defeat many beasts in Far AnórienDefeat many beasts in Far Anórien.Defeat many beasts in Far Anórien.Defeat many beasts in Far AnórienAfter securing the lands of Ithilien, the time has come to rejoin the Host of the West at their encampment on the border of Dagorlad, the battle plain.Aragorn's camp can be found far to the north of Henneth Annûn on the southern border of Dagorlad.

Anborn has asked you to rejoin Aragorn and the Host of the West at his encampment to the north.Travel to Aragorn's camp on the border of DagorladMithrandir and Damrod can be found within Aragorn's encampment on the border of Dagorlad.

You have arrived at Aragorn's encampment and should now speak to your allies.Talk to Mithrandir at Aragorn's campTalk to Damrod at Aragorn's campAragorn can be found in his encampment on the border of Dagorlad.

You have spoken to Damrod and Mithrandir and should now speak to Aragorn.Talk to Aragorn'The Host of the West has passed northward, and even now they make camp on the border of Dagorlad.'

'The pass of Cirith Negen has been made safe, the roadway north is clear, but the lands of Dagorlad are steeped in the Enemy's corruption.

'The Host of the West shall have need of you in the coming days - of this I have no doubt. Although my men are familiar with the lands of Dagorlad, its harsh terrain and wide plains make it deadly to those who do not move with care. By sharp stone, Orc, or worse terrors of the Black Land, death follows closely upon the battle plain.

'Bear this in mind, ${PLAYER}, for it is there you and the Host of the West will challenge the Dark Lord. I ask that you rejoin them as swiftly as you are able and travel to their camp to the north.

'If you see Damrod, please speak to him on my behalf. A great test lies before us... and we must not fail.''We stand on the border between Gondor and Sauron's wastes, and if any among us would turn back, now is the final moment.

'I do not blame those that would turn from the coming battle. It shall cost most or all of our lives, but if Frodo can finish his quest, a victory over Sauron would be worth them all.

'We must stand together as one against the Dark Lord when the time comes, and I trust that you will be at my side. We have travelled far in service of the same quest, my dear friend, and now we must see it done!''The Dark Lord knows well of our approach, and we shall soon learn what manner of trap he has devised for us before the Black Gate. Let us hope that he remains blind to the trap we have laid in turn... and even moreso that our chance victory might be won.

'We are nearing the end of our journey, ${PLAYER}, and Aragorn will soon have need of us all.''${PLAYER}! For a moment, I was afraid you had left our company behind! It was a foolish worry, but fear has a smothering presence so close to the Black Land.'

Damrod shifts uneasily, but is quick to hide his concern.

'This is it, my friend... soon we shall pass from the lands of Gondor onto the battle plain, Dagorlad.

'While the Rangers and I often patrol the lands of Dagorlad, the Enemy cannot mistake our purpose in mustering so many to its border.

'We have fought through exhaustion, and now we must draw up our weapons once more. I am glad that all of us shall stand together as we march on the Black Gate.'There is much to do beneath the Slag-hills.There is much to do beneath the Slag-hills.Complete Skoironk: Driver of FearComplete Skoironk: Vile TunnelsComplete Skoironk: Complex PastComplete Towers of the Teeth: Guardian of the TeethComplete Towers of the Teeth: Foundation of ShadowComplete Towers of the Teeth: A Brush with DarknessThere is much to be done in the Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha.The Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha is located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills.

