You have routed the Khundolar ambushers and uncovered their grisly handiwork. You should return to Jarl Gurthilm.Talk to Jarl Gurthilm'We have been betrayed, ${PLAYER}...

'We were paid half our share to travel to the fields of Gondor, and now, the Khundolar have sent assassins to slay us before we could return home. Only the Lord that bought our blades could have arranged such an ambush, and his name is Zarhal Kôz.

'He is a coward among Easterlings, but his wealth grants him all the power he desires. He offered us the remainder of our share upon our return, but it's clear that he didn't intend for us to survive long enough to demand the rest of our gold.

'My men will hold this position, but we have need of a scout... and after all, you are still in our service!

'Search the surrounding lands for signs of the Khundolar or their assassins. Then we shall see about taking our gold back, and then taking quite a bit more!

'And then, ${CLASS}, you shall have a reward fitting of a King!''Oh, the fool he is... I will not suffer such an insult to my people and my skill!

'You send a pitiful band of assassins to slay warriors of Khand? Hah! You have sent flies to destroy a foundation of steel!

'This is no longer about returning home... I shall not rest until Zarhal Kôz lies dead at my feet and his riches are in my keeping!'There is much to do while travelling through the lands of Far Anórien.There is much to do while travelling through the lands of Far Anórien.Complete Explorer of Far Anórien deedComplete Quests of Far Anórien deedComplete Slayer of Far Anórien deedThere is much to do while travelling through the lands of The Wastes.There is much to do while travelling through the lands of The Wastes.Complete Explorer of The WastesComplete Quests of The WastesComplete Slayer of The WastesComplete Enemies Beneath the HillsThere is much to be done in the maggot-hole caverns of Skoironk.The maggot-hole caverns of Skoironk are located in the Slag-hills.

