You have done what you could to calm the Rangers of Ithilien at Aelin Veren and should now speak to Maendal.Talk to Maendal'I can sense my men's trust of the Southrons has already begun to splinter. After such a brazen attack, I must confess that I, too, share some of their apprehension towards the prisoners.

'If we truly think ourselves the better Men, we cannot give in to fear so easily. The prisoners themselves have done nothing to suggest that they harbour the desire to break free, and they have heeded our commands without question.

'I would ask for your aid in calming my men. They are uneasy, and I do not wish them to do something ill-considered - even against such an old foe of our people.

'Speak to them, and I shall do the same.''I shall offer them no quarter if their kinsman attack us again, but I will not have my men give in to fear on mere suspicion.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Let us hope it does not come to that.'Defeat many Easterlings in North Ithilien.Defeat many Easterlings in North Ithilien.Defeat many Easterlings in North IthilienDefeat many Easterlings in North Ithilien.Defeat many Easterlings in North Ithilien.Defeat many Easterlings in North IthilienDefeat many Easterlings in North Ithilien.Defeat many Easterlings in North IthilienÉomer has heard that Elfhelm wishes to meet with you on a private matter.Elfhelm wants to meet you in the Old Guest-house on the First Circle of after-battle Minas Tirith.Find Elfhelm in Minas TirithYou should talk to Elfhelm in the Old Guest-house in after-battle Minas Tirith.Talk to ElfhelmElfhelm has asked you to search the after-battle Pelennor for Éowyn's sword.Find the hilt of Éowyn's swordYou should talk to Elfhelm, who can be found in the Old Guest-house on the First Circle of after-battle Minas Tirith.Talk to ElfhelmYou should talk to Éomer, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Éomer'${PLAYER}, Elfhelm has come to me. He has said that he wishes to speak with you. It was peculiar as usually he speaks with great detail. While I do not know what it is that Elfhelm seeks you for, it did sound urgent. You should speak with him as soon as you are able.

'He did tell me one thing - he wants to meet you at the Old Guest-house in Minas Tirith.''My friend, I have an important task for you, one which I cannot entrust to any man of Rohan. You know that Lady Éowyn was on the battlefield and now she rests, recovering, in the Houses of Healing. I am in need of her sword. Yes, the sword with which she fought and killed the Witch-king.

'It still remains somewhere on the Pelennor. I have searched and searched for the sword but could not find it. It could not have strayed far from the spot where the Witch-king was slain. The sword was broken in combat, so I am certain no one took it to wield in the battle. I am hoping you might succeed where I could not. Will you try?'You explain the story of the sword of Théodred, and how it came to be here.

'This is an exceptional tale. Théodred's death was cruel and untimely. Now he has been avenged, and, through the hands of my sister, Théodred was there for his father. I shall tell this to all the men of Rohan. This will surely boost their spirits and this hilt shall be a prized relic of Rohan.''You found it! What good fortune! You see, ${PLAYER}, this is no ordinary sword. I gave this to Éowyn when she refused to stay behind in Rohan. Yes, I knew that she was riding to Gondor with us. I kept her secret. Now I must share with you another secret. This is the sword of Théodred, Théoden's son.

'Yes, the sword of the late King's son, wielded by the King's niece, slew the greatest enemy upon the battlefield. Théoden's death was avenged in many ways. Éowyn's brother, Éomer, must know the truth of this. Take the sword to him.'Candúr is concerned with the number of Orcs residing within Skoironk.Mordor bruisers can be found within Skoironk.

