You should report back to Húrin.Speak with Húrin'The weapons of the Enemy dealt many great blows to the city, and we find ourselves concerned with the growing threat of ruins aflame. If left unchecked, these fires could reduce the lower reaches of Minas Tirith to nothing!

'This task is arduous enough that I have tasked Rathon, the Warden of the Wells, with command over the efforts to quell the flames. Seek him out for assistance, ${PLAYER}, as I'm sure he could use someone with your level of insight.''Without access to the cisterns, we are left with scarce amounts of water, and very few measures for controlling the blaze. However, we do have an abundance of fine sand, which should prove adequate for our needs.

'As we already collected much of it into rucksacks, seek out whatever bags you can locate, and use them to smother the flames.''Rathon is a clever sort. I wouldn't have expected the Warden of the Wells to rely on minerals as his solution.

'We've calmed the flames for now, but new threats will likely emerge. As long as we remain aware of the danger that still exists within the city, then we will overcome this dark chapter.'Defeat many foes in Cair Andros.Defeat many foes in Cair AndrosDefeat many foes in Cair AndrosDefeat many foes in Cair Andros.Defeat many foes in Cair AndrosDefeat many foes in Cair AndrosDefeat many foes in Cair Andros.Defeat many foes in Cair AndrosDefeat many foes in Dûm Boha.Defeat many foes in Dûm Boha.Defeat many foes in Dûm BohaDefeat many foes in Dûm Boha.Defeat many foes in Dûm Boha.Defeat many foes in Dûm BohaDefeat many foes in Fushaum Gund.Defeat many foes in Fushaum Gund.Defeat many foes in Fushaum GundDefeat many foes in Fushaum Gund.Defeat many foes in Fushaum Gund.Defeat many foes in Fushaum GundDefeat many foes in Lang Rhuven.Defeat many foes in Lang Rhuven.Defeat many foes in Lang RhuvenDefeat many foes in Lang Rhuven.Defeat many foes in Lang Rhuven.Defeat many foes in Lang RhuvenDefeat many foes in Ondoher's Folly.Defeat many foes in Ondoher's Folly.Defeat many foes in Ondoher's FollyDefeat many foes in Ondoher's Folly.Defeat many foes in Ondoher's Folly.Defeat many foes in Ondoher's FollyEven after the great battle on the Fields of Pelennor, foes have sought refuge in the depths of Osgiliath.Defeat many foes in Osgiliath.Defeat many foes in OsgiliathEven after the great battle on the Fields of Pelennor, foes have sought refuge in the depths of Osgiliath.Defeat many foes in Osgiliath.Defeat many foes in OsgiliathDefeat many foes in Osgiliath.Defeat many foes in OsgiliathDefeat many foes in Skoironk.Defeat many foes in Skoironk.Defeat many foes in SkoironkDefeat many foes in Skoironk.Defeat many foes in Skoironk.Defeat many foes in SkoironkDefeat many foes in the Towers of the Teeth.Defeat many foes in the Towers of the Teeth.Defeat many foes in the Towers of the TeethDefeat many foes in the Towers of the Teeth.Defeat many foes in the Towers of the Teeth.Defeat many foes in the Towers of the TeethThe stream that flows over Henneth Annûn is of great import to the Rangers and to the lands of Ithilien.The stream of Henneth Annûn passes over the refuge from the east, and flows westward through the Field of Cormallen.

Laeglaw has asked you to gather water from various points of the stream of Henneth Annûn in order to determine if the Enemy's forces have poisoned it.Laeglaw can be found in Henneth Annûn.

You have filled water-skins at various points along the stream of Henneth Annûn and should now return to Laeglaw.'Have you a moment, ${PLAYER}?

'The heavy palls of the Black Land have laid above Ithilien for far longer than the rest of Gondor, and the ashy, sour air that rises over the Ephel Dúath all too often sweeps into our lands. Worse still are the foul rains that cascade down those black slopes... for they bring with them a blight.

'This blight has spread into our waters in the past, aided by raiding parties of Orkish defilers. Now, more than ever, it is necessary that the stream of Henneth Annûn remain free of Mordor's poisons.

'This is our only refuge from the onslaught of Mordor's forces, and without fresh water, our company is doomed to failure.

'Here, take these water-skins. Fill them in the Forbidden Pool, in the stream as it passes through the Field of Cormallen to the west, as well as within the stream's source along the Ephel Dúath to the east.

'I have no reason to believe the water is blighted, but I must be certain.''By your account, the Enemy's poisons have not seeped into the stream, but I shall test the water you gathered to be certain.

'Even without knowing the location of Henneth Annûn, the Enemy could flush us out by poisoning the streams of Ithilien. We are fortunate they have not yet had the forethought to do so.

'Very good, ${PLAYER}.'Discover the great forge machinery still churning in Udûn.Discover the great forge machinery still churning in Udûn.Angbor has been tasked with arming the men who will march east, and is short of the swords required.You should smith some weapons at the forge in Aragorn's Pavilion, on the after-battle Pelennor.Forge blades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The cooling bucket is located next to the forge in Aragorn's Pavilion, on the after-battle Pelennor.

