You have retrieved the Orcs' orders, but a curious phrase in the Black Speech of the Orcs has left Laeglaw vexed. He has asked you to have Mincham aid in its translation.Talk to Mincham at Tham Durlan'I have a favour to ask of you, my friend. One of our own, Laeglaw, has set out to scout the hill of Ondoher's Folly. He fears a company of Orcs lay in wait and seek to encircle the Host as it draws closer to the Black Gate.

'Laeglaw was firm in his desire to scout the hill, but these lands are hostile to us all. We cannot risk scouting alone any longer - for the Enemy's forces may be arrayed against us just out of sight. Thus, I bid the Ranger Mincham accompany him in his patrol.

'${PLAYER}, I know that you and the Ranger have crossed paths many times, and I trust that he shall be of aid to Laeglaw - especially with his knowledge of the Enemy's language. Patience also seems to be a virtue of his, as a lore-master of sorts named Artamir begged to follow him out to Ondoher's Folly, and he was gracious enough to escort the fellow there. The man is no warrior, and it troubles me that he might endanger their cause through carelessness.

'As far as I know, they have travelled to ruins due north of here. The ruins are known as Tham Durlan, but with so little left intact, it is difficult to tell them from any other. Meet them there, and aid Laeglaw and Mincham if you are able... and keep a close watch on Artamir for me.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}.

'Do not worry - I have learned my lesson from the time I spent in the Dead Marshes!

'It is a sorry fate that befell the Steward, though, is it not?''${PLAYER}! Keep your head low and your voice lower lest we alert the Orcs nearby....

'I have not come alone, but Mincham and I cannot defend against their numbers. As for the lore-master, Artamir does not even have a weapon to wield! He imagines this some sort of careless expedition, I think. I hope he realizes his folly soon, but not by an Orkish blade!

'Most of their forces are gathered up ahead upon the hill of Ondoher's Folly, but a small outpost lies to the north-east just over this ridge. We know little of their intent, but I worry they aim to endanger the Host of the West before it reaches the Black Gate - even if their Master wishes otherwise.

'We must learn more of their purpose at Ondoher's Folly, but I shall not risk a direct attack until we know more. Travel to their outpost and see if you can discover anything from the Orcs encamped there.''What have you learned of the Orcs' plans, ${PLAYER}? Were you able to recover any orders from them?'

You show Laeglaw the orders, but his face twists in concentration when he sees the phrase in the Black Speech.

'Our foes to the north are great in number as we expected, but I am left with more questions. The identity of this Bloodletter is unknown to us. They also have many unfortunate prisoners in their keeping, but we do not know what or where this "Faltor-shík" could be. It troubles me, my friend. Much of this writing is in Westron - for what purpose is a single phrase in the tongue of the Orcs?

'I assumed that bringing along a lore-master such as Artamir might have been of great help to us for such a chance find, but the man seems repulsed at the mere mention of the Black Speech. The poor fellow should have stayed back at Haerondir....

'It seems Maendal was wise to ask for Mincham's aid after all -- the Ranger is well-learned in the languages of the Enemy. Bring this missive to Mincham and see what he can make of it.''Bah! The Ranger knows the Black Speech?

'I knew he was a queer fellow! No self-respecting man would learn such a vile tongue, I say!''What is this missive you bear?'

You explain to Mincham that you have need of his knowledge of the Black Speech once more. He takes the orders from you, and begins to read it. When he reaches the phrase in the Black Speech, he suddenly halts.

'By my reading of these orders, I understand Ondoher's Folly and Faltor-shík to be the very same, and it seems the Orcs have made something far worse of that hill than a mere strategic holding. That phrase, Faltor-shík, it... it means the Fane of Screaming. Such a name... it affords new significance to the grim structures that tower over the hill.

'It is not merely an Orkish encampment, my friend, but a temple of slaughter.'Húrin leads the grim task of collecting the remains of comrades catapulted into Minas Tirith by the Enemy.You should pick up an unfilled barrel so that you can collect any scattered remains found on the outer walls in Minas Tirith.Pick up an unfilled barrelYou should use the unfilled barrel to collect any scattered remains that you can find on the outer walls of Minas Tirith.Collect scattered remains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Húrin can be found outside the front gates of Minas Tirith.

You should deliver the filled barrel to Húrin.Deliver the filled barrel to Húrin'During the siege, the enemy sought to intimidate us by volleying the remnants of our fallen brethren into the city. Our people kept their resolve, but we would like to put those remains to rest.

'We were able to clear most from the streets, but word has come to me that some still linger on the outer walls, and my hope is that you will be able to locate and collect the last of our fallen.''Even in the wake of carnage, I still cannot believe what the people of this city have endured. The enemy used every vile tactic that they could, but the will of Gondor did not break. I only hope that we can give these fallen a comfortable rest, and that Mordor's treachery sits at our heels.'As the Rangers led the Halflings through Ithilien, they spoke freely and prepared an ill-fated ambush for a company of Haradrim.Mablung can be found in Henneth Annûn.

Mablung has offered to tell you what he remembers of the Halflings and their time in Ithilien.Listen to Mablung's taleMablung can be found in Henneth Annûn.

Mablung has finished his tale, and you should now ask if he knows more of the Halflings.Talk to Mablung in Henneth Annûn'Ah, ${PLAYER}. These have been long days, and when first we met, such a tale was far from the front of my mind. The Enemy's designs for southern Ithilien and Osgiliath were pressing matters, and ones that could have changed the fate of the battle on the Pelennor had they not been addressed.

'Even though it has only been but a few days, I swear I can still hear the Halflings and their creature scurrying about Henneth Annûn...'

Mablung studies your face and detects a hint of confusion.

'Ah, but perhaps I am skipping ahead! Anborn told you of our first encounter with the Halflings, yes, but the day was not yet done. We were tasked with keeping the Halflings under our protection, but our plans to ambush a company of Southrons soon went awry... and thrust us unwittingly into the skirmish!''Are you ready to hear my tale?''That is all I recall, my friend. Upon Faramir's return, he led the Halflings to Henneth Annûn with our company.

'By their appearances, it had been a lengthy time since their last supper... or a bath for that matter. Samwise calmed a bit in the refuge, but something seemed to tug at Frodo. Alas, Lord Faramir alone would know of such things, for he spent much time in private with the Halflings beyond our hearing.

'There eventually came the question of how to deal with their elusive gangrel-companion, but I shall leave that tale to Anborn...'Find Haradrim supplies abandoned from the Battle of the Pelennor Fields.Find Haradrim supplies abandoned from the Battle of the Pelennor Fields.Find Haradrim supplies scattered across North IthilienÉomer, King of Rohan, has decided to investigate the slain fell-beast of the Witch-king.You should talk to Éomer, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to ÉomerYou should talk to Éomer, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Éomer'${PLAYER}, I have decided that before we take further action, we must dispose of the vile corpse of the Witch-king's fell-beast.

'I feel a shudder of revolt every time I look upon it, remembering how my uncle and king died there, and how my sister Éowyn nearly fell, too, battling the Witch-king. The men shun it as well, and whisper that it is ill luck to let your gaze linger on the dead beast. It should be purged.''Let me know when you are ready and I shall fetch Mithrandir to accompany us. He has mentioned some concern with the corpse and wishes to oversee its disposal.''I am sure that loremasters of Gondor will learn much from studying the head of that foul creature. I hope only that the risk does not outweigh the reward.'Mablung wishes for you to travel to Haerondir and assist the Rangers there.Travel to Haerondir in the Noman-lands, north of the Camp of the Host.Travel to HaerondirAnborn can be found at Haerondir in the Noman-lands.

You should talk to Anborn.Talk to Anborn'${PLAYER}, Anborn and a handful of others have moved ahead to Haerondir, our fort in the Noman-lands. You can see it from here; it is the large ruin to the north. They will likely need any help you can spare preparing for the march into enemy territory.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! Good to see you. I take it Mablung sent you our way. We can surely use the assistance.'Mablung has asked you to venture into the Noman-lands ruins with Faroth and search for hidden Orkish traps.Venture into the Noman-lands with Faroth, find hidden Orkish traps, and destroy them. They can be found in the many ruins throughout the Noman-lands.

Faroth must be present to find the hidden Orkish traps. If you lose track of him, use the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.Destroy hidden Orkish traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mablung can be found at the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.

You should return to Mablung and tell him that many of the Orkish traps were destroyed.Return to Mablung'Scouts returning to camp have brought word of Orkish traps in and among the ruins the entire way between here and Nuiharn. It is one of these that I guess gave Faroth his small wound. He was lucky and nimble. Our marching soldiers may fare far worse if they stumble on them.

'Take Faroth with you and destroy as many as you can find. If I am not mistaken, he will keep a keen eye and nose out for them now.''I thank you for your efforts, ${PLAYER}. Too many Rangers have found themselves in peril because of those traps, Faroth included!'Thurindol is concerned that even with your efforts thus far, Orc leaders could still mobilize their forces below ground quickly.Orcs can be found within the caverns of Skoironk.

You should defeat Orc Lieutenants within Skoironk.Defeat Orc Lieutenants in Skoironk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated Orc Lieutenants within Skoironk.Completed'Even if we are able to defeat the Orcs gathered beneath the hills, their leaders will only raze and enlist many more foul creatures. You must seek out the lieutenants skulking around beneath these forsaken lands, and put an end to their command.'You have defeated the Orc Lieutenants within the caverns of Skoironk and caused disorder among the growing number of Orcs hiding below the Slag-hills.Reach Level 1 with the Allegiance: Hobbits of the CompanyReach Level 1 with the Allegiance: Hobbits of the CompanyMablung has asked you to defeat  enemies still lurking in Osgiliath.Defeat enemies hiding in Osgiliath.Defeat enemies in Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.Talk to Mablung'I am certain that there are enemies still out there in Osgiliath. Search the city and find these craven lurkers. We must clear the city of foes if we are to truly reclaim Osgiliath for Gondor.''Good work. Though I fear there may be more. Mírthel has spotted movement among the shadows on his watch. Still, you have made a dent! And yet we must not lower our guard.'The paths of the Riders Three and Reeve Fastred align as they move against Crúmgam and his traitorous agent.Fastred can be found at Kings' End.

Burnoth has asked you to speak to Fastred about Crúmgam.Talk to Fastred at Kings' EndFastred can be found at Kings' End.

Fastred has asked you to accompany him and the Riders Three into battle against Crúmgam. You should speak to him when you are prepared.Talk to FastredThere are many things to be done before the day is won on the Pelennor Fields.

Note: You must complete Book 6, Chapter 8 of Volume IV to advance this objective.Battle on the Pelennor Fields until the day is wonThe Riders Three can be found at the Threshold of the City.

The battle is won. You should now speak to the Riders Three, and learn of what they faced after your paths diverged.Talk to Burnoth at Minas TirithTalk to Hutha at Minas TirithTalk to Ulf at Minas Tirith'${PLAYER}, Reeve Fastred also seeks this Crúmgam. He would have us come together to seek out this sorcerer and Léofdag's murderer.

'He spoke of the sorcerer's arrival in the Sutcrofts not long ago, and of his vile designs to unmake the Eastemnet before the war came to the Hornburg. Fastred harbours a wild ire, but we must proceed carefully if he speaks true of Crúmgam's power.

'For my part, I shall balk not at a chance to avenge my fallen friend, but the Enemy's power must not be underestimated.

'Fastred wishes to speak with you before we depart. Tarry not, for this opportunity shall not long last.''${PLAYER}! What a time for our paths to cross once again! I can think of no better ${CLASS} to join me and the Riders in this task.

'Remember you that foul man, Crúmgam? He sought to break apart my family and defile the lands of the Sutcrofts, but we drove him from the very heart of Snowbourn. But nay, he did not die... 

'Such are evil things that they slink away until the day favours them! Oh, but he is mistaken, my friend - for I shall lay my vengeance upon him!

'He has found himself emboldened amid this onslaught of the Enemy and came forth when the wraith felled Théoden King. He has since travelled south, but I have kept his trail. One of our kinsmen also slipped away with his forces and remained unharmed... if that is not the man you and your fellows seek, I know not who else it might be.

'Come with us, my friend. Let us end these treacherous men!''Come, ${PLAYER}. There is vengeance to be had!''What a day this has been, ${PLAYER}...

'Our foes were without end, and yet we triumphed against them. Léofdag is avenged, and my brothers and I can now rest without the fear of a traitor lurking among the ranks of our people.

'Out from the darkness a new dawn has burst forth, but what it shall bring... I know not.

'A rest is well-earned, but we cannot linger long while the Enemy contemplates his defeat. Another battle lies just beyond the horizon... I only hope we are prepared.''So this is the great ram the Enemy used to penetrate the gates of the City? It is both impressive and dreadful - a masterwork of the Enemy's evil.

'We could not have defeated that traitor without your aid, my friend. I am gladdened that dear Léofdag is avenged, and that another enemy of our people lies broken on the field.

'Does the light burn your eyes too, ${PLAYER}? In our journey to the fields, I had begun to wonder if the skies would ever clear again.

'Let us hope that it promises better days to come...''Ah, ${PLAYER}...

'It is good to see you... here at the battle's ending. Léofdag's murderer is slain and the day is won!

'My brothers and I felled this troll as it made for the gates of the City, but I am afraid my strength is spent. Worry not for me - it is nothing that rest and healing cannot cure! 

'Once we see the rest of the field swept of foes, I shall take a trip to the baths or to a fine bed. When next a battle calls to us, I trust you shall fight at my side!'You have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire armour for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire armour for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire armour for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire armour for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire provisions for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire provisions for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire provisions for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire provisions for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire weapons for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire weapons for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire weapons for the Host of the WestYou have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid those who march.You must acquire weapons for the Host of the WestSomeone has posted a task to collect bubbling goo. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire bubbling goo.Wanted: Bubbling Goo from the North Ithilien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in North Ithilien.Wanted: Bubbling Goo from the North Ithilien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect burnt ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire burnt ears.Wanted: Burnt Ears from the North Ithilien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in North Ithilien.Wanted: Burnt Ears from the North Ithilien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect mould skins. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire mouldy skins.Wanted: Mouldy Skins from the North Ithilien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in North Ithilien.Wanted: Mouldy Skins from the North Ithilien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect prismatic carapaces. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire prismatic carapaces.Wanted: Prismatic Carapaces from the North Ithilien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in North Ithilien.Wanted: Prismatic Carapaces from the North Ithilien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect reeking filth. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire reeking filth.Wanted: Reeking Filth from the North Ithilien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in North Ithilien.Wanted: Reeking Filth from the North Ithilien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect worn furs. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire worn fur.Wanted: Worn Fur from the North Ithilien region. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in North Ithilien.Wanted: Worn Fur from the North Ithilien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.On the eve of his final assault against the Dark Lord, Aragorn's thoughts turn to Minas Tirith and the wounded.Ioreth can be found in the High Hall within the Masters' Tier of Minas Tirith (After-battle).

Aragorn has asked you to return to Minas Tirith and learn of the fates of the wounded as well as what further havoc may have been wrought by Galathir's overeager hands.Talk to Ioreth in the High Hall'Have you a moment, ${PLAYER}? 

'With such a journey ahead, I count myself and this host fortunate to have you here at my side. Yet my thoughts stray back to Minas Tirith... and to those we left behind. Many dear friends and strangers alike now fight their own battles against illness and injury.

'It was with great sadness that I could not tend to them all, but the greater matters of the Dark Lord and the Ring-bearer's hidden quest have called me away. I know not if I shall ever return to Minas Tirith, and I worry for the fates of those we left behind if I fall in our final gambit.

'Do you remember the Master Herbalist we encountered during my brief time in the City? The one called Galathir? He was unfit for his post and could have caused great harm to those in his care, but I had not the means to send him from the Houses of Healing... not without declaring myself.

'I ask that you return to the Houses of Healing in Minas Tirith and speak with the healer Ioreth. Ensure that she keeps Galathir's ruinous tinctures from the wounded, and have her be my eyes in the High Hall. 

'She will heed my words, even if they are delivered in my stead. You are one of the swiftest riders among my ranks, and I entrust this task to you alone.

'Go with haste, my friend. Once you have returned, we can continue planning our course into the Wastes.''You have come at the request of the king?'

You inform Ioreth that Aragorn has not yet claimed that title, and then tell her of his concerns about Galathir's healing practices.

'Whether he claims the title or not, I know him for what he is. He has the hands of a healer, and none but a king could work kingsfoil into such a potent medicine - and I would know! Still, it troubles me that he has grown concerned about Galathir's methods. Not precisely because I disagree, mind you, but because I did not think it would be so plainly noticed!

'I cannot send Galathir away, but I can help prevent him from treating any more of the wounded with Everworth. It is the least I can do for my king!

'However, there remains one other matter of concern regarding Galathir... and his new apprentice.'Galathir is giving patients Draught of Everworth, which Aragorn believes may be harmful.Aragorn has asked you to remove any of Galathir's Draught of Everworth infusions that have been left near patients in the House of Rest and the House of Remedies in the Houses of Healing.Remove Draughts of Everworth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aragorn can be found in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should bring the harmful Draughts of Everworth to Aragorn, as he asked.'If I stood here as crowned liege and not in hooded stealth, that herb-master, Galathir, would know something of my displeasure! He has decided, I cannot fathom how, that Draught of Everworth is what wounded soldiers most need - when that is farthest from the case. At best, it will add to their suffering and at worse... but let us not speak of that. 

'Alas, cloaked diplomacy is the thing of the day, so I must enlist your help, friend. I have had Galathir shooed from this hall, but I cannot keep him from the others. Will you follow Galathir and his herbalists, and gather up the infusions wherever he has placed them?'You hand Aragorn the infusions you gathered.

'This many? If that man does not let up... but now is not the time. I thank you, ${PLAYER}. I will see these dealt with swiftly.'The Houses of Healing are running low on basic supplies needed to treat the wounded.Scour Minas Tirith for clean cloths and bittercap moss.Gather clean cloths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather bittercap moss (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Place the supplies you have gathered in a supply bin in either the High Hall, House of Remedies, or House of Rest, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Torchún can be found outside the Houses of Healing on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should return to Torchún and let him know the supply bins have been replenished.Return to Torchún'The number of wounded have been so great that the Houses of Healing have run short of some basic supplies. Have you time to forage about Minas Tirith, ${PLAYER}? We are in need of clean cloths for bandaging and bittercap moss for cleaning wounds. If you are able to gather these things, you should leave them in one of the supply bins in the High Hall, House of Remedies, or House of Rest.''We are resupplied with clean cloths and bittercap? That is a great relief. You have my thanks!'Corunir hopes that you will be able to find Golodir before he comes to harm.You have come with Corunir to an outpost on the Pelennor where the fighting has been thick.Talk to CorunirGolodir has gone ahead. Can you find him before it is too late?Find GolodirGolodir felled the mighty Thrúgrath, but his body is broken and he will not survive.Talk to GolodirCorunir mourns the loss of his friend on the Pelennor.Talk to Corunir'We... we cannot stay here, ${PLAYER}.''Amegil did not repent of the words he spoke to Golodir, but he did tell me which way he seemed to go: here, to this encampment of Orcs. We may yet find Golodir, if we hurry!''I am satisfied... ${PLAYER}. If the Gondorians... know of what they speak... then my death... will see Mordirith defeated....

'Corunir... my friend... when this war is over... I ask that you ensure... safety for Wenda....'

Golodir is quiet for a long moment. When he finally speaks again, it is for the last time.

'It is enough... for me... to die thinking of Lorniel... as I always...''He is gone. I... I do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}.'After the question of whether they should go into Mordor, Gandalf announced he had something - or rather some-place - to show Pippin and Merry.Gandalf has led you to Bâr Thorenion in North Ithilien, cut into a high place above Cormallen. 

You should talk to Gandalf to hear more about Bâr Thorenion.Talk to GandalfGandalf has invited everyone to step in and see Bâr Thorenion. You should talk to Merry and Pippin and hear what they think of it all.Talk to MerryTalk to PippinExplore Bâr Thorenion with Merry and Pippin.Explore the central courtyardExplore the side quartersExplore the north passageExplore the southern passageExplore the kitchensTalk to Pippin in the central courtyard, now that you have all explored Bâr Thorenion.Talk to PippinHelp Pippin and Merry gather the things needed for a makeshift meal.Collect some straw (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect some plates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Ithilien Wine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect provisions crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect some kind of light (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the things you collected to the table.Pippin and Merry have come running back with their own findings.Talk to PippinJoin Merry and Pippin in enjoying the makeshift meal.Enjoy the meal'What a remarkable place Gandalf found for us. Amazing to think that it is ours! Can you imagine what it will look like after the Gondorians have tidied it up? I should like to chat with them and make sure some of our things are placed in some of the rooms and that the kitchens in particular are restored, if anything.

'My, but listen to me! A meal, some good company, and something to do and think about is welcome in this odd, free time after we won. But I hope old Gandalf doesn't think he's fooled us into forgetting about Mordor. We should still very much like to go. ''This place, Bâr Thorenion, is yours by royal decree of the kingdom of Gondor. You might think this is some jest of our old friend Aragorn, but in truth it was the soldiery and the rangers of Ithilien who petitioned him that it be so.

'I have brought you here prematurely, I confess. I know not how many men will be here tomorrow to make the place somewhat more habitable. I thought, however, you should like to see it sooner, so you could make your own plans.

'It will serve as a fine residence, indeed, for the time that you dwell here in Gondor before heading back Shireward. And, with any luck, it will keep you out of trouble and away from some of your more foolish notions -- for a few days, at least, if we are lucky.

'Well, come on then. Let us step inside!''Go on, see what you can see. As I said, some Men of Gondor will be by tomorrow to make the place a bit more livable.''Well I suppose we really ought to have a look around, and see what we can see, hadn't we?''Is this considered a common home by the Big Folk around here? It is bigger than any house we ever saw in Breeland, and I dare say the whole of the Smials would fit in this one main hall!''I don't know if either of you observed the fact, but it so happens that we have everything we need for a simple makeshift meal - beginning with this old table someone happened to leave right here.

'I know that I could use a bite to eat. What about you two?

'There are crates of food and some bottles of old wine with the seals intact. Some light, a bit of straw for a seat, and a few plates will help. If you gather those, ${PLAYER}, Merry and I will work on cups, knives, and anything else we can muster up.''You scrounge up some light, a bit of straw for a seat, and a few plates will help, ${PLAYER}. Merry and I will find what else we need and meet back around this table.''All this running about and scrounging has got my stomach rumbling right and proper.''There we are. A meal, all laid out. Fine work, friends! 

'Well, don't just stand about. Let us eat!'Anborn recalls bringing Gollum forth to be questioned by Faramir shortly after his capture, and his fears for the journey of the Halflings and the gangrel-creature.Anborn can be found in Henneth Annûn.

Anborn is telling you what he recalls of the night he brought the gangrel-creature to be questioned.Listen to Anborn's taleAnborn can be found in Henneth Annûn.

Anborn is telling you what he recalls of the night he brought the gangrel-creature to be questioned.Listen to Anborn's tale'That is all I recall of that night, my friend.'You have crossed the noxious plains of Dagorlad with the Rangers Faeron and Mincham, scouting the lands through which Aragorn's host must pass.Mincham is ahead of you on the rocky slope.Talk to Mincham on the rocky slopeFaeron has returned from scouting the ridge.Talk to Faeron on the rocky slopeEager to learn the Enemy's secrets to help Aragorn and the Host of the West, Faeron wants to enter Narchost.Follow Faeron to NarchostThe entrance to Narchost is temporarily unguarded.Enter Narchost and remain alertYou have entered Narchost and do not have long before the Orc patrol returns.Talk to Faeron inside NarchostYou have entered Narchost and do not have long before the Orc patrol returns.You have entered Narchost and do not have long before the Orc patrol returns.Make your way to the upper levels of Narchost.
<rgb=#FF0000>Do not be seen by any of your foes!</rgb>You have entered Narchost and do not have long before the Orc patrol returns.Talk to Mincham inside NarchostYou have entered Narchost and do not have long before the Orc patrol returns.Eavesdrop on the conversation without being seenYou have overheard a conversation between Khôgath the Render and his minion Fulak, but it is not safe to linger within Narchost.Talk to Faeron inside Narchost'We have to get out of here!''We have picked our way across the tumbled stones and parched dust of Dagorlad, but all we have found is an inhospitable land. None live here, for what man could? The Orcs keep watch on this place, for it lies on the border of their master's fell country.

'Faeron has gone ahead to see what lies beyond the ridge. When he returns, we will turn back and tell Aragorn what we have seen: a dead land, watched by his enemies, through which we must pass nonetheless.''From the top of the ridge I could see a good distance, and I marked the movement of many Orcs crawling hither and yon across the plain. But near at hand, a great tower rises from the rocks and spies the approach. I know the place from Aragorn's maps: it is Narchost, one of the Towers of the Teeth.

'As I watched, a door in the tower opened and a great patrol of Orcs marched out on some mission. They made for Mordor, but if we hurry we might be able to enter the tower before they return. We might learn something of value for Aragorn, but we must seize this chance while we have it!

'Once the Orcs return the opportunity will be lost! Hurry!''I would not have been able to forgive myself if we let this chance pass untaken, ${PLAYER}, but now that we are inside my resolve wavers. Let us learn what we can and then depart!

'If there are any secrets to be found that will be of value to Aragorn, they will be on the upper levels of the tower. We must make our way upwards, but do not be seen by any of the guards that still lurk within! It is important that our passage remains unnoticed!

'Mincham and I will follow in the shadows. You must find a way to reach the upper levels of the tower without being seen! Do not approach the guards or we will all be imperiled!''I hear foul mutterings ahead, ${PLAYER}, and know them for what they must be: the vile Black Speech used by the creatures of Mordor. It is a language I have learned to understand, though the study pained my ears and my heart both.

'Let us move closer and I will try to translate the words for you and Faeron. Remain still out of sight! We must not be noticed, or I fear we will not leave this tower alive!''Mincham's study of that foul language has borne fruit, ${PLAYER}, and we have learned what we can: the armies of Mordor have orders to allow Aragorn to come to the gate! What terrible fate does the Enemy have in mind for the Host of the West?

'I hope Aragorn finds this knowledge useful, but now we need to escape from this place and return to his camp. We can no longer stay here!'The Riders of Rohan have joined the battle, but on the fields of the Pelennor, great deeds go hand in hand with death.Guthláf is on the fields of the Pelennor, ready to ride as his king commands.Talk to Guthláf on the field of battleThe battle rages before the White City.Ride with Guthláf and stand with the kingDeath has come to the Pelennor, and even kings cannot stand against it forever.Guard Théoden during his last momentsDeath has come to the Pelennor, and even kings cannot stand against it forever.Guard Théoden during his last momentsThéoden has come to the end of his road, but he has a final request of you.Talk to ThéodenThéoden requested that you pick up the banner of Rohan where it fell, and give it to Éomer.Pick up the fallen banner where it fell from Guthláf's handThéoden has asked you to give the banner to Éomer.Give the banner to Éomer, as Théoden requestedRemain on guard as Éomer remembers the fallen.Remain on guard'For glory and honour! Let us ride to Théoden King and make safe the fields before the city!''I have come to the end... of my road... ${PLAYER}. But Rohan will go on...'

Théoden nods weakly.

'Pick up the banner... where it fell... and give it to Éomer. He must lead now...'Éomer silently takes the banner from you and lifts it to the sky.Angbor has spoken to Aragorn and Mithrandir about an important matter concerning the Morgul Vale.Talk to Mithrandir.Talk to MithrandirSet fire to the noisome flowers.Set fire to noisome flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Mithrandir.Talk to MithrandirTalk to Mithrandir at the overlook.Talk to MithrandirLet Mithrandir execute his plan.Let Mithrandir execute his planTalk to Aragorn.Talk to Aragorn'Let us return, my friend. We have done what we could, and should tarry no longer.''The smoke of their burning is foul, ${PLAYER}, but it will pose less harm than leaving those evil blooms would have done. Let us press forward!''We must not tarry here. That dark citadel was once Minas Ithil, the Tower of the Moon, but it has not been called by that name for a terrible span of years. It is the fortress of the Nazgûl now, and none dare go that way.

'Thanks to the power and wisdom of Mithrandir, our work this day will make it more difficult for our foes to assail Gondor by this road, and that is a work done well.''Our destination lies further ahead, ${PLAYER}, but I ask that you take a moment to hear my counsel.

'The flowers that line the road have fallen to some corruption, prey for some dark force. I suggest that we burn these evil blooms in order to prevent their spread beyond the vale into Ithilien and Gondor.''That is the city of Minas Morgul. Once it was Minas Ithil, the Tower of the Moon, but no longer. Do you see the arched structure that crosses the river to the east? That is the bridge we must destroy if we are to keep the foes from the Morgul Vale from crossing into Ithilien.

'Let us rejoin Aragorn, ${PLAYER}.'As the Rangers led the Halflings through Ithilien, they spoke freely and prepared an ill-fated ambush for a company of Haradrim.Mablung recalls standing at the Halflings' camp-site.

Mablung is telling you more of the tale of the Halflings in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Listen to Mablung's taleMablung recalls guarding the Halflings and speaking to them of their plans.

Mablung is telling you more of the tale of the Halflings in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Listen to Mablung's taleMablung recalls the Southrons breaking through the trap.

Mablung is telling you more of the tale of the Halflings in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Listen to Mablung's taleMablung recalls the wild Mûmak and the aftermath of the battle.

Mablung is telling you more of the tale of the Halflings in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Listen to Mablung's tale'That is all I have to tell, my friend.'Mithrandir has taken an interest in the slain fell-beast that once served as the steed of the Witch-king of Angmar, Lord of the Nazgûl.Talk to Mithrandir near the corpse of the fell-beast.Talk to Mithrandir by the carcass of the fell-beastWrap the head of the fell-beast in the heavy cloth given to you by Mithrandir.Wrap the fell-beast head in the clothNow that you have wrapped the head of the foul steed in heavy cloth, Mithrandir asked that you burn the corpse of the fell-beast.Burn the carcass of the fell-beastTalk to Éomer on the Pelennor.Talk to Éomer by the burning carcass of the fell-beastTalk to Mithrandir near the corpse of the fell-beast.Travel to the Houses of Lore with Mithrandir and deliver the head of the fell-beast to the scholars there.Travel to the Houses of Lore with MithrandirStand by as Mithrandir speaks with the scholars of the Houses of Lore.Remain alert while Mithrandir speaks with the scholars at the Houses of LoreTalk to Mithrandir in the Houses of Lore.Talk to Mithrandir in the Houses of Lore'You should return to Aragorn's Pavilion, if you are finished here.''The carcass of the fell-beast still mars the field at which it breathed its last, and it remains a foul reminder of the villain it bore. It must be removed.

'I had thought to do so quickly and without ceremony, but a number of scholars from the city beseeched me, wishing to preserve some part of the creature for their study. Take this heavy cloth and wrap the head in it, so it may be safely transported to these scholars.

'We will then burn the body, for it cannot be allowed to fester here at the site of Théoden King's ending.''The dead beast and its foul master have both been cleansed from the Pelennor, and for that you have my thanks, but the memory of them lingers.

'I would have seen both head and body burned, but if it is Gandalf's wish that the head be preserved for scholarly study, I will not gainsay him.''Let us away to the Houses of Lore, ${PLAYER}, and we will bring with us our freshly-wrapped burden. May the cloth shroud the eyes of any who see us pass, for such a burden will work fear in the hearts of folk of the city, even if its days of rending and tearing are done.

'The greatest evil it poses now is against the nose, ${PLAYER}. Let us deliver it to the scholars with this advice: keep it not in an enclosed space; rather, let the place of its study be an airy one, and dispose of the foul-smelling relic when you have learned all you can of it!''Thank you for your help with this unpleasant burden, ${PLAYER}. Such creatures are bred in the darkness of Mordor, and little is known of them, save that they are raised in corruption and used for evil. They are fed vile meats and treated unkindly, and have proved fitting steeds for the Enemy's most powerful lieutenants.

'Can they teach us anything more? Perhaps our friends here will learn something valuable from this study, and perhaps not. But I am glad to have given them the opportunity for such learning, if there is a chance it might be had.'The paths of the Riders Three and Reeve Fastred align as they move against Crúmgam and his traitorous agent.Burnoth is standing on the field near Kings' End.

You have arrived at the last location where Fastred sighted Crúmgam, and should now talk to Burnoth.Talk to BurnothThe ambushing foes can be found just ahead.

You have begun your search for Crúmgam, but foes now harry your advance. You must defeat them!Defeat the ambushing foesFastred and the Riders Three are searching the fields outside Kings' End.

You have survived an ambush and should now resume your search for Crúmgam.Search the charred fields for signs of CrúmgamCrúmgam's flames are upon one of the charred fields outside Kings' End.

Vile flames have sprung to life and must now be quenched.Defeat the seeking flamesFastred is running through the charred fields outside Kings' End.

You have witnessed Crúmgam's sorcery and should now search the nearby area for Crúmgam.Follow Fastred as he seeks CrúmgamCrúmgam is standing before the pyre outside Kings' End.

You have found Crúmgam and beside him stands a man bearing the armour of the King's knights - a traitor deep within the heart of Rohan.Confront CrúmgamBrodwulf is standing near the pyre outside Kings' End.

Crúmgam has fled, leaving the traitor to his fate. You should defeat Brodwulf and avenge Léofdag.Defeat Brodwulf and avenge LéofdagBurnoth is standing near the pyre outside Kings' End.

You have defeated the traitor, Brodwulf, and should now speak to Burnoth.Talk to Burnoth'No victory comes easy this day, my friend.''Crúmgam is nowhere to be found, my friend, but fear not! It is difficult to move unnoticed through such a battle and he cannot have gone far.

'Fastred spoke of the sorcerer's mastery of flame - we must proceed carefully or he shall too soon sense our approach and send whichever magics he commands against us.

'Let us go now before these fiends slip away!''The traitor is slain, but Crúmgam has escaped with his vile sorcery.

'In his wake, he has left the Reeve slain and Ulf wounded. We must retreat to safer ground, and heal what we may. The body of the Reeve must be borne to the gates of the city - I shall not leave him here among the dead!

'Come!'As the Second Age approached its end, Elrond stood with the Last Alliance against the forces of Sauron and won a decisive victory that led to the Dark Lord's defeat.Elrohir and Elladan are telling you the tale of the Last Alliance's victory at the Battle of Dagorlad. You should follow along and listen as Elrohir begins the tale.Listen to Elrohir's tale of the Battle of DagorladThe Last Alliance gathered at a great bulwark in Dagorlad and prepared to strike against the armies of Mordor.Follow the Last Alliance into battle against the armies of MordorElrohir and Elladan are telling you the tale of the Last Alliance's victory at the Battle of Dagorlad. You should follow along and listen as Elladan continues the tale.Listen to Elladan's tale of the Battle of DagorladElladan is describing the trials of the Last Alliance as they drew closer to the Black Gate.Follow the Last Alliance across the flaming trench toward MordorElrohir is describing the courage of Gil-galad and Elendil in the face of the Ringwraiths.Listen to Elrohir's tale of the Last AllianceElrohir is describing a great battle between the Ringwraiths and the commanders of the Last Alliance.Follow Gil-galad and Elendil into battle against the RingwraithsElrohir is nearing the end of his tale. You should continue to follow along.Listen as Elrohir concludes the tale of the Battle of DagorladElrohir has finished his tale of the Battle of Dagorlad.Listen to Elrohir's final remarks'Quite the tale, my friend, was it not?''In an age long-ended, a great battle was fought upon Dagorlad between the numberless armies of the Dark Lord and the Last Alliance of Elves and Men. For years, they clashed upon the battle plain, and each momentary victory and defeat dimmed the hope of the war ever coming to an end.

'After many trying battles, the Last Alliance pressed southward and approached the Black Gate of Mordor. Yet, the nearer they drew to the Black Land, the more foes the Dark Lord sent forth.

'But lo, Elendil the Tall and High King Gil-galad of the Noldor possessed much wisdom and valour, and soon the plans were drawn for a final assault against the Black Gate.

'The Last Alliance assembled at a great bulwark and it was there they made their stand against Sauron and his armies.'Victories over the Dark Lord's servants would not come easily for long...

'Although Orcs and evil Men fell in scores upon the battle plain, Sauron soon loosed his nine greatest servants upon the Last Alliance. Once they were Men, but twisted by the Rings given to them by the Dark Lord, they grew stretched and withered into unseen forms. As the corruption of the Rings consumed them, these Men grew beyond death itself! For in truth, the Dark Lord held their Rings and thus tethered them to service and life unending. Even if they were struck down, they were not slain -- merely banished for a time!

'Many names have been bestowed upon them by those who have beheld their terrible shapes: Dwimmerlaik, Dúrchir, Gwetherain, and Nazgûl. In the tongue of Westron, their name is perhaps the most precise -- Ringwraiths!''Although many of their kin fled before the Ringwraiths, Gil-galad and Elendil did not falter. Gil-galad held close the mighty spear, Aiglos, and Elendil bore the blade, Narsil -- the very sword that was broken, reforged, and wielded anew by King Elessar! They fought as one and cut through the Dark Lord's forces with a fury unlike any the Elves or Men had ever witnessed.

'They soon stood before the Black Gate itself, but the battle would not be won so easily!

'Alas, the Ringwraiths and a vast army of Orcs had gathered beneath the dark ramparts of the Black Gate, and they sought to stand between the Last Alliance and their Master!'And so, the Battle of Dagorlad drew to a close...

'The Last Alliance won a decisive victory over the Dark Lord and banished his mightiest servants back to the Black Land. The might of Men and Elves proved the greater that day, and let us hope it shall prove true once more!

'Although the fighting within Mordor lasted over seven more years before Sauron himself was finally defeated, this battle turned the tide in a war that many thought unwinnable.

'Yet many victories and defeats still laid ahead...'The armies of Mordor converge on the slag hills as Aragorn and the Host of the West prepare for the final assault.Aragorn is atop the eastern slag hill, ready to engage once more with the enemies that approach.Talk to Aragorn atop the eastern slag hillThe eastern slag hill has come under heavy attack, and Aragorn calls his kinsmen to him for the final defence.Stand your ground and defend AragornAragorn has asked you to find Calenglad where he fell, if you can, and ease his pain.Find Calenglad where he fell on the battlefieldAragorn has asked you to make your way to the western slag hill and to help soldiers caught in the middle of the fighting.Golasgil of Anfalas has been caught between the slag hills and needs your help.Talk to Golasgil between the slag hillsGolasgil has been thrown to the ground by a great Olog, and now the beast seeks to finish what it began.Defeat the Olog that crushed GolasgilGolasgil has been mortally wounded.Talk to Golasgil where he liesYou have heard Pippin's voice from above the din of battle. He needs your help!Find Pippin atop the western slag hillBeregond is atop the western slag hill, calling for help.Talk to Beregond atop the western slag hillPippin lies beneath a great Olog atop the western slag hill.Check on Pippin where he liesThe battle rages all around you, and Beregond intends to rally the forces to keep fighting until the end.Talk to Beregond atop the western slag hill'My kinsmen and these others have cast back all of the enemy's advances to this point, ${PLAYER}. We must not fail now!''I will stay here and guard Calenglad's body from our foes, ${PLAYER}. You are needed to the west, between the slag hills, for the soldiers there are hard-pressed! Go, quickly!''Oh no! Help me!''We have to do something about those flying beasts, or there will be no one left to carry on the fight!

'Follow me, ${PLAYER}! We must find some archers!''I cannot see you, friend... everything is... darkness...

'I know I do not... do not have long. Fight on... fight on...

'If there is a day to come... after this... look to the people... of Anfalas. Tell them... tell them their lord...''The halfling... he saved my life! I was stunned and fell beneath the press of battle, but even as the great troll reached out to end my life, Peregrin stabbed it with his blade!

'He slew the beast, but it fell upon him and I fear he is dead!''There is no end to this onslaught, ${PLAYER}! As long as we remain divided, we are weak. We must move as a group if we are to stand long.

'We must fight back to King Elessar before it is too late!''Do not... give up... ${PLAYER}. Remember...'

Calenglad coughs weakly, but he smiles despite the pain.

'From above... I saw light. It cannot... be quenched...

'The new age...'There is little time to mourn those lost at Pelennor, but Aragorn knows that some time must be spared to remember the fallen.Speak with Éomer on the Pelennor.Talk to ÉomerPick up the torch for lighting the pyre.Pick up the torchUse the torch to light the pyre.Light the pyreListen to Éomer as he speaks the names of the fallen.Listen to the record of the fallenYou are overcome by the loss of many great warriors.<rgb=#FF0000>Mourn</rgb> the loss of your fellow warriorsSpeak with Éomer on the Pelennor.Talk to ÉomerPick up the stone for Snowmane's cairn.Pick up the stone for Snowmane's cairnPlace the stone on the cairn that marks Snowmane's grave.Place the stone on the cairn for SnowmaneListen to Éomer speak.Remain alert while Éomer speaksSpeak with Éomer on the Pelennor.Talk to ÉomerEnter the Tower of Ecthelion.Enter the Tower of Ecthelion with ÉomerSpeak with Éomer inside the Tower of Ecthelion.Talk to ÉomerWalk with Éomer to pay respects to Théoden.Walk with Éomer to Théoden's bedsidePay your respects to Théoden King.<rgb=#FF0000>Mourn</rgb> for Théoden KingSpeak with Éomer at the Tower of Ecthelion.Talk to Éomer'I am ready to depart. We should find what rest we can before our next tasks begin.''This is never easy, ${PLAYER}, but it is important. If we are to go on, we must take some time to remember those we have lost. These men died for Gondor, for Rohan, for every land in which dwell the good-hearted. We have constructed a great pyre, and by its light we will remember our fallen.

'Will you accept the task, and the honour, of lighting the pyre? Once it is burning we will begin.''The pyre will burn until morning, and the heat of the burning will carry our grief into the night sky.

'There is another creature of nobility we should remember: Snowmane, the steed of the king. Come, let us mark the spot where he died and we have buried him.''Morning has come. Let us return to the city and climb to the Citadel. I would visit my uncle where he lies in state, and pay my respects to him.''We have arrived, ${PLAYER}. My heart is full of sorrow, but I would look upon my uncle's visage and think upon his life and deeds even so.''I have said all I can, and now the rule of Rohan will be mine alone. It is a heavy burden. I hope to live up to my uncle's example, but it will not be easy. Still, I will do my best for the people of Rohan!

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I am ready now to depart.'The forces of Mordor prepare for a final attack on the fields of the Pelennor.You have found Horn in the midst of battle, but the bloodshed is taking its toll on him.You have fought alongside Horn, but the horrors of battle are taxing his courage.Talk to Horn on the battlefieldTalk to Horn on the battlefieldYou have become held by a powerful and evil force, unable to move!Stand against the forces of evilCrúmgam must pay for his crimes against the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.Defeat Crúmgam and his alliesCrúmgam has been defeated, but not without sacrifice.Talk to CalengladYou have found Aragorn and the Grey Company on the battlefield as they prepare to confront Gothmog.Stand with Aragorn as he confronts GothmogGothmog has fled the battlefield, leaving Aragorn and the Grey Company to mourn the slain he leaves behind.Talk to Aragorn'Let us make for the city, ${PLAYER}. I have lost too many friends today.''${PLAYER}, I have not seen you since the morning, and I feared the worst! We have a brief reprieve for now, but it will not last long. I have seen such horrors... so many good men lost...''${PLAYER}, I have not seen you since the morning, and I feared the worst! We have a brief reprieve for now, but it will not last long. I have seen such horrors... so many good men lost...''I could not move, ${PLAYER}... it was fell sorcery, and... I was powerless...'

Horn's breath comes raggedly, and there are tears in his eyes.

'Halros sprang to my defence, and took the blows that were meant for me. He died in my place... there was nothing I could do...''There is no time to mourn, ${PLAYER}! We have to find Aragorn, for I fear he has gotten too far ahead and may become surrounded by his foes if we do not aid him!''There is too much sorrow on this field, ${PLAYER}. Gothmog flees, and my anger will follow him, but this is not the day he will pay for the hurts he has caused us.''This young Ranger, this Halros, is able to do his duty without questioning it? Did I ever have that strength? I know that is what is expected of me, and I came here to prove it, but...

'If I was more like him, would I be able to fight on this field without regret? It weighs me down, even as I know why I must fight. But so many have died, and still the hosts of Mordor pour onto the plain! I thought I could protect Nona and our child from harm, but I see now that there is no hope of that. There are too many evils arrayed against us!''The enemies that pour forth from Mordor will not stop until they have slain every last one of us, ${PLAYER}. They will not stop even then, for there is no mercy in their hearts. They will kill even women and children, the old and the infirm.

'I do not regret my decision! I will fight to make Nona and our child safe, and if I never see them again I will go to my grave knowing that I did what I could. I do not fight for glory or for honour. I fight for time, not for myself but for those I love!'You have come with Legolas, Gimli, and a number of Rangers to the northern side of Cirith Negen in order to disrupt the Orc and Easterling ambush.Gimli is standing off the road north of Cirith Negen, waiting to attack the enemy ambushers.Talk to Gimli north of Cirith Negen<rgb=#FF0000>Do not get too close to Cirith Negen before the Rangers are in position</rgb>You have met up with Dagoras in the woods north of Cirith Negen.Talk to Dagoras north of Cirith Negen<rgb=#FF0000>Do not get too close to Cirith Negen before the Rangers are in position</rgb>Your attack on the Orc leader at Cirith Negen will be the signal for Dagoras and the other Rangers to begin the full assault.Attack the Orc leader at Cirith Negen to signal the other RangersYou need to survive until the Rangers can finish their attack!Survive combat until the Rangers can attack!The Rangers have launched their attack!The tables have been turned!You and the Rangers have turned the tables on the ambushers at Cirith Negen.Talk to Dagoras north of Cirith Negen'Let us return to Aragorn and report of our success.''We have come the long way 'round Cirith Negen, ${PLAYER}, and now we are in position to surprise the Orcs and Easterlings before they can attack Aragorn's host.

'We will descend upon them in full-throated fury, and send them screaming back to their own lands, or to death!''The Rangers are in position, ${PLAYER}, and so too are the Elves. Now we just need someone to give the signal to attack.

'Why don't you walk down the road behind Cirith Negen and let our enemies know they have been outmaneuvered? The time for stealth is over, now that we are ready to launch the attack!''We have victory! The enemy has been dispersed, and will no longer pose a threat to the Host of the West!

'Thank you for your heroism, ${PLAYER}! I must thank your friend Gimli as well, both for the swing of his axe and the stillness of his tongue during our approach. I know that dwarves enjoy to bellow, and keeping his quiet must not have been easy!

'We have all done a service for Aragorn this day. I am glad to have made the road safe for the host.'On the very doorstep of Mordor, Aragorn commands Sauron to come forth and surrender.Aragorn is at the Morannon, the Black Gate of Mordor, and prepares to challenge Sauron.Talk to Aragorn outside the Black GateAragorn has decided to call for the surrender of Sauron, and wishes for you to stand with him.Stand with Aragorn as he defies the Dark Lord SauronThe Mouth of Sauron has presented tokens for the perusal of the company.Stand with Aragorn as he defies the Mouth of SauronMithrandir has asked you to make Pippin hold his tongue lest he endanger the negotiations with the Mouth of Sauron.Talk to Pippin and keep him quietThe Mouth of Sauron mocks the Host of the West, and prepares the terms of Aragorn's surrender. Remain alert.Listen to the demands of the Mouth of SauronMithrandir has asked for you to speak with him while he considers Sauron's terms.Talk to MithrandirMithrandir asked you to retrieve the items presented by the Mouth of Sauron.Collect the short-swordCollect the Elf-cloakCollect the mithril-shirtYou have taken the items that belonged to Frodo and Sam, and Gandalf has defied the Mouth of Sauron.Stand with the Host of the West in defiance of Mordor'All is still and silent, but I do not trust this emptiness. Do not be fooled by the quiet! There are eyes upon us, though we see them not.

'Let us ride nearer, and I will call for Sauron's surrender.''${PLAYER}! Surely you must recognize those items! That's Frodo's mail-shirt, the one he had from Bilbo! The grey cloak has an elven-brooch pinned to it, like the one I had from Lórien. And that's Sam's sword, or I'm a Boffin!

'How did this terrible Messenger come to have those items, ${PLAYER}? What happened to Frodo and Sam?'

You silence Pippin with a look, but he is crestfallen and his outburst cannot be taken back.'Steel your heart for the trials ahead, ${PLAYER}. That Sauron has either Frodo or Samwise in captivity seems certain, but you must have noticed, as I have, that this Messenger speaks only of one prisoner, not of two.

'And yet, those items are unmistakable and were in the possession of both our hobbits. I do not want this vile Messenger to keep them. I will distract him, ${PLAYER}, and I want you to retrieve these items in memory of our friends.'Aragorn has called for a council of the captains at his pavilion in order to decide what must be done.Aragorn is inside his pavilion with many of the captains who fought at Pelennor.Talk to Aragorn inside the pavilionMithrandir is holding council inside Aragorn's pavilion on the Pelennor.Talk to Mithrandir inside the pavilionPrince Imrahil is holding council inside Aragorn's pavilion on the Pelennor.Talk to Imrahil in the pavilionAragorn and the captains of the armies are meeting to decide their next course.Observe the council of the captainsMithrandir is holding council inside Aragorn's pavilion on the Pelennor.Talk to Mithrandir inside the pavilionAragorn and the captains of the armies are meeting to decide their next course.Observe the council of the captainsAragorn is inside his pavilion with many of the captains who fought at Pelennor.Talk to Aragorn inside the pavilionAragorn and the captains of the armies are meeting to decide their next course.Observe the council of the captainsAragorn is inside his pavilion with many of the captains who fought at Pelennor.Talk to Aragorn inside the pavilion'We must determine the numbers we will need. There is work still to do before we set forth.''The captains who fought on Pelennor are here now, ${PLAYER}, and it is time to begin.''You remember the words of Denethor, ${PLAYER}. In them I think there is much we might learn.''If we cannot achieve victory, would you advise us to hide behind our walls, enduring siege after siege until we can last no longer?''There are some considerations that may slow his hand. The Ring can only be wielded by one, rather than by many. Sauron will expect a struggle among those who seek to wield it. He waits until one among us seeks to become greater than the others, and that is when he will act, seizing the advantage of our disarray.

'His Nazgûl still fly overhead, seeking signs of our movement. He has not forgotten the sword of Elendil, and now he has seen it reforged. His first assault was turned back and his greatest Captain slain. The winds of fortune have begun to blow in our favour.

'For the first time, doubt has begun to gnaw at him.''Legolas is right. We seek to capture Sauron's attention and keep it fastened upon us for as long as we can, but do not misunderstand.

'If we march to the Black Gate, there will be nothing to keep him from sending the considerable forces within Mordor to crush us completely and without mercy. We will buy time for the Ring-bearer to complete his mission, but there will be no more time for us.

'Any who go with me on this last march should know he goes to his death. There will likely be no returning from this. Still, I consider it my duty to try.''We do not need a great force to march on the Black Gate. This is not an army with designs on victory. We will determine the numbers we bring east and the numbers we leave behind.

'May this be the right choice, ${PLAYER}. I would rather die doing my part to bring about a new age than to do nothing and know the new age will never come.'The Eagles have come to the aid of the Host of the West, and the tide of battle has turned!Aragorn is on the slag-hill as the Battle of the Morannon rages all around him.Talk to Aragorn on the slag hillMithrandir is on the slag-hill before the Black Gate.Talk to Mithrandir on the slag-hillRemain on your guard!Remain on your guard!Mithrandir is on the slag-hill before the Black Gate.Talk to Mithrandir on the slag hillLandroval has set you down upon the slope of Mount Doom while the Eagles circle the Mountain and seek for Frodo on the far side.Find Frodo on the slopes of OrodruinYou have found Frodo and Sam on the slope of Mount Doom, but you do not have long before the slope will be engulfed in flame!Talk to Samwise Gamgee on OrodruinYou must stand on the edge of the outcropping if Gwaihir and his kin are to see you!Walk to the edge of the outcropping... there is little time to spare!'Gwaihir and the Eagles will keep the Nazgûl occupied, but the battle still rages upon the ground, ${PLAYER}! Let us press the advantage given to us by our winged allies and set the Orcs upon their heels!''Do you sense that? Something is amiss, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot discern what it might be. Some new artifice of the Dark Lord may be revealed to us!

'Stay near to me!''Frodo has fulfilled the Quest of the Ring, and he may still live! We must act quickly, ${PLAYER}, or he will never come alive from the Black Land. If Gwaihir and his brother will bear us into Mordor, we may yet come to Frodo in time!

'Gwaihir, Lord of Eagles! Two times have you borne me, my friend, and this will be the last and the most needed! If your brother Landroval will bear ${PLAYER}, we will have the best chance of finding Frodo before he is overcome!

'Fly now to Orodruin! Fly now to Mount Doom!''${PLAYER}! Is that... is that you...?''${PLAYER}... is that... really you...?'

Sam looks at you with bleary eyes; his exhaustion is apparent, and he seems to disbelieve that you are really standing here.

'We can't... go any further.... We got this far... but...'

Sam reaches into one of his pockets and withdraws a small item. He presses it into your hand.

'Where there's... life... there's hope...' he says.With the Witch-king now dead, a new commander has taken control of the enemy forces on the Pelennor Fields.Ingbert is on the Pelennor Fields just ahead of you.

You have begun your foray from King's End to discover the Enemy's new commander and should now talk to Ingbert.Talk to IngbertIngbert is battling on the Pelennor Fields.

Ingbert has asked you to join him in searching for the Enemy's new commander.Battle across the Pelennor FieldsDuilin and Derufin are scouting ahead and attempting to slay the Mûmakil.

You should stand back and allow them to weaken the beasts before proceeding.Stand back as Duilin and Derufin clear a pathThe Orc encampment is ahead.

Duilin and Derufin have been slain by the Haradrim and their Mûmakil. You should flee into the nearby Orc encampment.Flee to safety in the Orc encampment!The Hillock lies to the south-east of Minas Tirith.

Ingbert has decided that the best course is to reach the Hillock and make a stand against the Enemy's reinforcements there. You should follow him.Reach the Hillock with IngbertImrahil and his Swan-knights can be found to the north of the Hillock on the Pelennor Fields.

Imrahil is under attack! You and Ingbert should come to his aid.Aid Imrahil and his Swan-knightsThe Hillock is due south of your position.

Ingbert and Imrahil have begun their journey to the Hillock. You should accompany them.Reach the Hillock with Imrahil and IngbertOrolang is standing at the cross-roads to the north of the Hillock.

You have found your path blocked by a dreadful wraith and must defeat him if you are to reach the Hillock.Defeat OrolangImrahil is at the cross-roads to the north of the Hillock.

You should speak to him about what is to be done.Talk to Imrahil'Gothmog! These are ill tidings, ${PLAYER}. We must meet Éomer upon the Hillock - I only hope we are enough to stand against Gothmog's forces.''I know not who could command such a force in the absence of the Witch-king.

'These fields churn with battle and blood, but we must learn more of this new commander. Who could lead so many with nary an ebb in the flow of battle?

'He shall surely come forth from Osgiliath as so many of his reinforcements have, but we cannot afford to hold here and allow his forces to overwhelm us.

'Let us move to a more fortified position and hope that we might learn of his identity.''This wraith speaks ill of the dead - I shall not believe what he claims! Eärnur is lost to the Enemy's trickery... and to his own brashness. Such troubles are not for this day... when such a battle surrounds us even now.

'I saw a bold rider of Rohan and his company rush by to the south as we fought on. Éomer, they called him, chanting and slaying as they rode. A great fury had taken him, for he and his kinsmen screamed of death and destruction to be done upon our foes.

'If we are to survive the Enemy's renewed strength and the might of Gothmog, we must rally at Éomer's side atop the Hillock.'Anborn recalls the tense exchange when the gangrel-creature came unbidden to the Forbidden Pool beneath Henneth Annûn.Faramir, Anborn, and Frodo came to the overlook of Henneth Annûn.

You should listen to Anborn's tale.Listen to Anborn's taleAnborn and Frodo travelled down to the Forbidden Pool.

