You should listen to Anborn's tale.Listen to Anborn's tale'And that is all I have to say on the matter, my friend.'With renewed spirit, Éomer, king of Rohan, has decided to send Elfhelm to lead an attack against a band of Haradrim who has fled into Talath Anor.Enter the destroyed farm.Enter the destroyed farmDefeat enemies at the farm alongside Elfhelm and his men.Defeat enemies alongside Elfhelm<rgb=#FF0000>Elfhelm must survive</rgb>Pursue the Haradrim.Pursue the Haradrim<rgb=#FF0000>Elfhelm must survive</rgb>Talk to Elfhelm at the river crossing in Talath Anor.Talk to Elfhelm'There is nothing more we can do. Most of the Haradrim forces gathered in Talath Anor are now defeated. Let us return to Aragorn's Pavilion.''${PLAYER}, I thank you for lending your hand in combat and for your invaluable knowledge of Talath Anor and the Haradrim. It has made this ride a success, as we no longer need worry about a Haradrim ambush near Minas Tirith. I am concerned about Cair Andros however. We should tell Éomer and Aragorn of what we have seen.'With the Enemy alerted, the Faint-hearted are left with no choice but to retake the island with haste.Fight through Cair Andros with Duinhir and his men.Fight through Cair Andros with Duinhir and his men<rgb=#FF0000>Duinhir must survive</rgb>Defend your ground in hope that additional support arrives to aid in the fight.Defend your ground<rgb=#FF0000>Duinhir must survive</rgb>Defeat the four lieutenants of Cair Andros as you fight along side Tolwin, Dúneth, and Duinhir.Defeat SárgrishDefeat ThaukbagDefeat HurshálaDefeat Ursajun<rgb=#FF0000>Duinhir must survive</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Dúneth must survive</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Tolwin must survive</rgb>Talk to Tolwin and Dúneth.Talk to TolwinTalk to DúnethWalk together to the prow of Cair Andros.Walk together to the prow of Cair AndrosTalk to Duinhir.Talk to Duinhir'Come, there is much to do in securing this island.''${PLAYER}! It is good to see you again! You kept your word, like you said you would. You vowed to help retake my home for my family. I have trained and waited for this day ever since you departed Crithost. Now, let us reclaim the rest of Cair Andros!''I knew in my heart that I would see you again. I knew it was you when I saw the smoke of battle rising from off the island. We rushed over as quickly as we could muster. I wanted to be there on the day that Cair Andros once again belonged to Gondor. I want to help restore the home of my dearly departed husband, Gilgír.''I see your friend Dúneth and the boy Tolwin. You have done much to improve their lives as they faced devastating hardship.

'I, too, should thank you for lifting my own shadow. I was wholly overcome with sorrow for the loss of my sons. I could not see my hands held out before me. What folly! Instead of honouring their sacrifice, I tarnished my name and theirs.

'I am not fool enough to think that Cair Andros will undo my mistakes. No, my friend, I shall need to take charge in the future. I shall make sure that those from Harad will pay for the crimes against Gondor and against my family.'Jarl Gurthilm and his company have travelled to the stronghold of Uya Hujûm to deal their vengeance upon Zarhal Kôz and the Khundolar.Jarl Gurthilm is standing with his men in Uya Hujûm.

You have come with the Variags to Uya Hujûm and should now speak to Jarl Gurthilm.Talk to Jarl GurthilmZarhal Kôz can be found somewhere within Uya Hujûm.

You have arrived in Uya Hujûm and should now battle through the encampment until you find Zarhal Kôz.Fight your way through Uya Hujûm and find Zarhal KôzZarhal Kôz can be found deep within Uya Hujûm.

You have discovered Zarhal Kôz's whereabouts and should now confront him with the Variags.Confront Zarhal KôzZarhal Kôz can be found deep within Uya Hujûm.

Zarhal Kôz has called forth his men and now attacks. You should defeat him.Defeat Zarhal Kôz and his men'The day is won, ${CLASS}. Let us begone from this place!''Are you prepared, ${CLASS}?

'The blades of my men have tasted much of the blood of the Khundolar, but our foe eludes us still. A coward to the last, I do not doubt!

'We shall press onward into the mountainside... and soon there shall be nowhere left for him to hide!

'Ready your arms and let us go.'Anborn will not soon forget the doughty little Halflings who gave such cheek to his captain, Faramir.The Rangers of Ithilien were patrolling to the north-east of Henneth Annûn.

Anborn is telling you a tale of strange travellers in Ithilien. You should listen closely.Walk with the Rangers of IthilienThe Rangers of Ithilien spied the barren camp-site and moved to investigate.

