You have defeated every Orc in Ondoher's Folly and should now confront Burudagath.Confront Burudagath the BloodletterYou are trapped in the Fane of Screaming at Ondoher's Folly.Attempt to free yourself from Burudagath the BloodletterThe Wainriders have come to Ondoher's Folly and are now confronting Burudagath the Bloodletter.Observe the confrontation between Zhan Ashû and BurudagathZhan Ashû is addressing you before the Wainriders return to Dol Acharn.Remain on guard as Zhan Ashû speaksBurudagath has survived his encounter with the Wainriders, but appears to be severely wounded.Listen to BurudagathFaramir can be found at Ondoher's Folly.

Burudagath has been defeated and Faramir has reappeared within the Fane of Screaming at Ondoher's Folly.Talk to Faramir inside the Fane of Screaming at Ondoher's Folly'It is done, ${PLAYER}. My father's memory is no longer defiled and the Bloodletter's grip on the Wastes is broken...''Although I have spent many years upon this hill, never once have I raised a weapon against the Orcs. They came to regard me as nothing more than some sort of twisted amusement for their Master, and in time, I began to believe it myself.

'You have freed me from such delusions, my friend. It may have been folly for me to join the battle long ago, but to flee this fight could bring ruin to Gondor -- to my people!

'${PLAYER}, we must rid the hill of Orcs and leave none but the Bloodletter to the Wainriders. If they encounter even one Orc that is loyal to him, it may reveal our deception... and that is a chance we can ill-afford to take.

'We must move now! I shall do what I can to aid you!''I am filled with sorrow that I could not aid you further before the battle's end, ${PLAYER}, but I am glad the Wainriders arrived in time to draw his attention from you. It seems the folly of my past has been answered this day -- perhaps it was once true that my allies were fated to a greater end without my hand in battle, but no more!

'As I look at my father's banner now, I see the might of a Gondor that once was... and may be again. For all the defilement Burudagath brought upon it, it resisted any final destruction. Gondor itself must now press onward through the darkness in much the same way, it seems.

'We have won a great victory this day... but I believe it time I leave this place and its painful memories behind.

'Go, return to your friends in the ruins and tell them of our victory. I shall see you again soon enough, ${PLAYER}...'The battle may be over, but many of those wounded during the fighting still fight for their lives.Pippin is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Pippin in the High Hall of the Houses of HealingMerry suffers from a malady the Gondorians call the Black Shadow. He is on a bed in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, still caught in the throes of a terrible dream from which he cannot wake.Examine Merry and complete 'Interlude: A Dream of Cold and Silence'Pippin is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Pippin in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing'I was hoping to find you, ${PLAYER}. A messenger from the Houses of Healing was seeking you on behalf of Peregrin the Halfling. You should go to him in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing and learn why he summons you thither.

'Doubtless you would have seen him sometime today, in any event, for I know you have been doing much throughout the city to help in the aftermath of the battle.''There you are, ${PLAYER}! Your feet carry you throughout the city with so much haste that I despaired of finding you! Indeed, I had nearly resolved to sit here and wait until your errands brought you once more to this Circle of the city.

'Peregrin the Halfling desired to see you. He is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing.'Merry has grown very pale, and cannot wake. The Black Shadow comes from the Nazgûl, and he was very near indeed to their leader. Will it now cost him his life?'Look at him, ${PLAYER}. He is so pale! What will I do if he dies?''I wish there was something we could do for Merry. I will stay here by his side until I think of something!

'You should keep helping out in the city. I will let you know if I think of anything that might help cure him and these other wounded soldiers of the Black Shadow once and for all!''A messenger from the Houses of Healing was seeking you on behalf of Peregrin the Halfling. You should go to him in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing and learn why he summons you thither.''Peregrin the Halfling desired to see you. He is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing.''I am so glad you are here, ${PLAYER}, but I am afraid that not even you can help now! They tell me that the leechcraft of Gondor is the finest in Middle-earth, but no one seems to be able to do anything for Merry. He is caught in the throes of some terrible malady. They call it the Black Shadow, and many of the soldiers that came near to the terrible Riders suffer from it too.

'Merry is so pale! He seems caught in a dream, but sometimes he cries out in his sleep. I wish there was something we could do for him!'The words of Ioreth compelled Mithrandir to seek for one who might be able to heal those suffering from the Black Shadow.Mithrandir has come down out of the city to speak with you.Talk to Mithrandir outside the cityPass through the gates and make your way up through Minas Tirith to the Houses of Healing without being seen by Knowing Scholars who might see through your disguise.Sneak through the city to the Houses of HealingAvoid Knowing ScholarsPrince Imrahil of Dol Amroth is outside the Houses of Healing.Talk to Imrahil outside the Houses of HealingYou have entered the Houses of Healing at the behest of Mithrandir.Enter the Houses of Healing with Imrahil and MithrandirFaramir is in the south-eastern sick-room of the Houses of Healing.Examine Faramir in the Houses of HealingÉowyn is lying in a bed two rooms to the north of Faramir's room in the Houses of Healing.Examine Éowyn in the Houses of HealingMerry is in the north-western room of the Houses of Healing.Examine Merry in the Houses of HealingIoreth might know where you can find some athelas.Ask Ioreth for athelasIoreth has never heard of athelas. Could it be she would know it by another name?Ask Ioreth for kingsfoilMithrandir is in the Houses of Healing.Talk to Mithrandir in the Houses of HealingYou greet Mithrandir warmly and ask him how the folk of the city fare in the aftermath of the battle.

'The uninjured are slowly waking from the horrors of the siege, and before long they will return to their daily lives. But many soldiers and townsfolk lie in the Houses of Healing, suffering from the wounds of battle and the greater hurts inflicted by the Nazgûl. Some of the healers remark that if there were a king in Gondor, as of old, these wounds might be healed through his skill.'

You tell Mithrandir that you did not wish to upset the delicate situation in Minas Tirith by entering the city without the invitation of its Steward.

'If you do not go to the Houses of Healing, there might be no Steward by nightfall that could offer you such an invitation, Aragorn! Faramir needs your healing-arts, as do many others. You might save them still if you enter the city in disguise. Avoid Knowing Scholars who might see you for who you are, and the political situation should be unharmed. I cannot command you to do this, but I do request it as your friend, and as a friend of Gondor.''Aragorn! I was told you did not wish to enter the city. I am glad you have done so, for Mithrandir claims that in you alone may rest the only hope for recovery of the sick that lie within.

'Let us attend to them at once, and may he prove correct in this belief!'You study Faramir's face closely, and note that he is covered in sweat. His forehead glistens, and he burns feverishly. He breathes shallowly, and the rise and fall of his chest is very difficult to detect without close scrutiny.

The son of Denethor seems close to death. If nothing changes, and soon, he will join his father by nightfall.Éowyn is held in the grip of a troubled sleep, but a grey shadow has crept over her features and she is very pale. You have heard whispers of the Black Shadow that comes from the Nazgûl, and it seems to have settled very heavily upon her.

Her shield-arm is broken, but the healers have tended to it with all their skill, and it seems to your eyes that it will heal in time. The state of her sword-arm is more troubling, for it seems that there is no life in it, though the bones are not broken.Merry suffers troubled dreams. Like Éowyn, he pierced the Lord of the Nazgûl with his weapon and the encounter worked a grievous harm upon him. A grey pall has settled upon his face, and the Black Shadow stifles his breath.You ask Ioreth if there might be some athelas to be had in the storerooms.

'We have healing herbs of many varieties, but of course never as many as we might wish, especially not with so many needing our help! It has been some time since a carrier from Lossarnach has come, and our stock of cemenduril liquor is very low. But I am afraid I do not know of any herb by the name of athelas. I can ask the herb-master. He knows the old names.'You tell Ioreth that some folk also know athelas by another name: kingsfoil.

'Kingsfoil? Say you so? My sisters claimed it to be naught but a weed! Now that you mention it, I have noticed that it does give off a sweet smell when its flowers are disturbed. It is somehow a wholesome smell, if you understand what I mean. I did wonder why any king would wish such a plant to be named so, and not one more brightly-coloured or eye-catching.''If she finds any athelas in the city, she will bring it back here with haste. And if there is none to be found, I will ride to the woods near Lossarnach and bring back the plant myself!

'It is good that you came here, Aragorn. May it not be too late for our friends, and for the others who suffer in the grip of the Black Shadow. If Ioreth runs as quickly as her tongue, she will be back with athelas before the sun moves another step in the sky!'The Houses of Healing are full, and the healers are having a difficult time seeing to the needs of the wounded.Ioreth is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Ioreth in the High Hall of the Houses of HealingGandalf is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Gandalf in the High Hall of the Houses of HealingGandalf is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Gandalf and complete 'Interlude: A Secret Return'Gandalf is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Gandalf in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing'The healers have sent messages throughout the city, calling for any who might be able to aid the sick and wounded quartered in the Houses of Healing. Go to the ward where Faramir lies, in the High Hall, and Ioreth will set you upon some useful task.''I bear a message from the healers, seeking any who might be able to provide assistance within the Houses of Healing! Go at once to Ioreth in the High Hall and she will find a use for you. I saw her last by Faramir's bedside.

'If you can help the healers to make Faramir well, you should do what you can! I have heard troubling whispers about Steward Denethor, but I will not repeat them here. At the very least I will tell you that Faramir must recover, or Minas Tirith will be at risk of further grief!''Faramir burns with a fire that consumes him from within! What will we do if he should die? If only Gondor still had a king. Minstrels used to sing of the Kings of Gondor, saying of them that their hands were the hands of healers, and by that trait would they be known. But there has not been a King in Gondor for many years.''Did you hear the words of Ioreth? She speaks of songs only half-remembered in these modern days, and I do not doubt that she often refers to such tales, but her words on this day have stirred me as if from a stupor!

'The hands of the King are the hands of a healer? Gondor has not had a King for many years, but these are times of change and it could be that one such worthy is indeed close at hand! Ioreth, men may well remember your own words in the days to come!

'You know who I mean, ${PLAYER}! Speak to me with haste and we will fetch him!''The recollections of Ioreth may prove a boon for our suffering friends, ${PLAYER}. I must go at once in search of he who may prove to have the healer's touch!''We must trust in Aragorn now, for time is growing short. If there is any kingsfoil to be found within this city, may it be found while it might still be used to good effect!

'I know that Aragorn did not wish to enter the city before the right time, but without his healer's skill I fear that these wounded might never recover. Now there is some hope, though it be slight.

'Now go and find kingsfoil, wherever it might be found!''The healers have sent messages throughout the city, calling for any who might be able to aid the sick and wounded quartered in the Houses of Healing. Go to the ward where Faramir lies, in the High Hall, and Ioreth will set you upon some useful task.''I bear a message from the healers, seeking any who might be able to provide assistance within the Houses of Healing! Go at once to Ioreth in the High Hall and she will find a use for you. I saw her last by Faramir's bedside.

'If you can help the healers to make Faramir well, you should do what you can! I have heard troubling whispers about Steward Denethor, but I will not repeat them here. At the very least I will tell you that Faramir must recover, or Minas Tirith will be at risk of further grief!''We are pulled in so many directions, ${PLAYER}! How can we hope to address the needs of so many wounded? So many suffer in the aftermath of the battle, Faramir not least of all!

'There he lies, and he burns with a fire that consumes him from within! What will we do if he should die? If only Gondor still had a king. Minstrels used to sing of the Kings of Gondor, saying of them that their hands were the hands of healers, and by that trait would they be known. But there has not been a King in Gondor for many years.'Even as the Men of Gondor and Rohan take stock of the devastation from yesterday's battle, the need to gather plans and press onwards cannot wait.Imrahil can be found just outside the main gate of after-battle Minas Tirith. You can travel there from the Threshold of the City on the Pelennor battlefield and from pre-battle Minas Tirith. 

You have been summoned by Imrahil for an important task.

<rgb=#FF0000>The travel horses at pre-battle Minas Tirith are only available if you've completed Volume 4: Book 6, Chapter 8: On a Field of Red of the Epic. Alternatively you may get to the after-battle Minas Tirith from a Minas Tirith stable master.</rgb>Imrahil can be found just outside the main gate of after-battle Minas Tirith. You can travel there from the Threshold of the City on the Pelennor battlefield and from pre-battle Minas Tirith.

You have been summoned by Imrahil for an important task.

<rgb=#FF0000>The travel horses at pre-battle Minas Tirith are only available if you've completed Volume 4: Book 6, Chapter 8: On a Field of Red of the Epic. Alternatively you may get to the after-battle Minas Tirith from a Minas Tirith stable master.</rgb>Talk to Imrahil just outside of after-battle Minas TirithAragorn can be found in his pavilion on after-battle Pelennor.

You should learn what plans Aragorn has and what help he might need.Talk to AragornAngbor and Éomer can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on after-battle Pelennor.

You should ask Angbor and Éomer whether their men are ready to march.Talk to ÉomerTalk to AngborYou have been summoned by Prince Imrahil, who stands just outside the main gate of after-battle Minas Tirith.'${PLAYER}, I thank you for coming. While there is much work yet to be done in the City, you and I are now needed elsewhere: at Aragorn's pavilion upon the Pelennor, where we must take stock of the day and plan for the future.

'Come, I will meet you there. We shall see what Aragorn has to say.''Ah, ${PLAYER}, I have need of your assistance. We have won the battle, but the Enemy is far from true defeat. You understand this as much as anyone.

'We must act swiftly and decisively. We are soon to embark on our most arduous and perilous journey yet, I think. I hope you will come with me, but first I must ask you to bring word to Éomer and Angbor that our forces, such as they are, must be prepared to march.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I saw you speak with Aragorn and guess at what he asks.

'Many Rohirrim have died this last day. If we were to stop now, their deaths would surely be for naught. I am rightful king of Rohan now and my men will do as I bid. Tell Aragorn I raise my sword with his and that when he blows his horns we will come to the call.''It is good to see you again. A true ${RACE} of honour and nearly as fearless as I.'

You relate Aragorn's request.

'I have trusted Aragorn since the moment I saw Thorongil return to Linhir. Come, there is much to be done if we are to move an army.'You have been summoned by Damrod to the Camp of the Host in Northern Ithilien, where he hopes that you will be able to assist the Rangers of Ithilien in their tasks.Damrod can be found at the Camp of the Host in Northern Ithilien.

You have been summoned by Damrod to aid the Rangers of Ithilien as they make preparations for the march to the Black Gate.Damrod can be found at the Camp of the Host in Northern Ithilien.

You have been summoned by Damrod to aid the Rangers of Ithilien as they make preparations for the march to the Black Gate.Talk to Damrod at the Camp of the HostMablung can be found at the Camp of the Host in Northern Ithilien.

Mablung commands the Rangers of Ithilien stationed at the Camp of the Host and will be able to give you orders.Talk to Mablung at the Camp of the HostYou have been summoned by Damrod, who requests your presence at the Camp of the Host in Northern Ithilien.

You should meet with Damrod as soon as you are able.'${PLAYER}, my friend. You received my message.

'With the conflicts in Ithilien behind us, I trust you are well enough rested to press forward. The Host of the West prepares for the final leg of this journey. It will be perilous as the terrain is unkind and the enemies numerous. Since we know these lands better than any ally of Gondor, Aragorn has sent the Rangers of Ithilien ahead to ensure safe passage.

'If you are able to lend us your arms, Mablung is coordinating the Rangers from the Camp of the Host. Speak with him if you would. I am sure he will be glad to see you.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. Damrod sent you? There is indeed much to do before we can be sure the path to the Morannon, the Black Gate of Mordor, is clear and free of threat.

'We would be grateful for your help in this task. Our numbers are small, and  I consider you as much a Ranger as myself.'A force of Khundolar Easterlings has invaded North Ithilien, bringing soldiers and weapons of war to wield against the Host of the West.Uya Hujûm can be found in north-eastern North Ithilien.

Tordoron has asked you to assault the Khundolar encampment of Uya Hujûm.Defeat Khundolar at Uya Hujûm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn Khundolar banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Khundolar ration-barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Khundolar trebuchets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tordoron can be found in the northern wilds of North Ithilien.

You have routed the Khundolar encamped in North Ithilien and should now report to Tordoron.Talk to TordoronAnborn can be found at Henneth Annûn.

You have routed the Khundolar threat within North Ithilien and should now return to Anborn.Talk to Anborn at Henneth Annûn'In my scouting, I have listened secretly to passers-by and have heard them refer to the camp in their tongue as Uya Hujûm.

'To assail it shall be no easy task...

'The Khundolar encampment is well-defended by their soldiers and they have armed themselves with trebuchets. I have not been able to discern how far their encampment stretches into the slopes of the Mountains of Shadow, but the pass they have claimed is of considerable length and shall be an arduous course.

'To ensure the Khundolar can no longer pose a threat to Ithilien and the Host of the West, we must thin their numbers, dismantle their siege weaponry, and destroy their supplies.'

Tordoron cracks a wry smile.

'I would trust no other among us but you with this task, ${PLAYER}.''The Khundolar are routed... and flee in fear to Dagorlad?'

Anborn's face betrays a mix of disbelief and joy.

'You have done a great service to the Rangers, my friend. Through your efforts, our stores are renewed and my men better protected. Ithilien itself heals with greater vigour.

'I think, perhaps, it is time that you rejoin your allies in the Host of the West. By my thinking, to deprive them of one of your skill would be a grave mistake.

'Let us talk more of your journey, and of the road ahead.''You have done it, my friend! I saw a few of their number flee back into Dagorlad as you returned. I do not think they expected to encounter a ${CLASS} of your skill!

'They will certainly come again, but for a time, we are free of the Khundolar's presence in North Ithilien.

'Now then... you should return to captain Anborn in Henneth Annûn and tell him of what you have done. If only I were there to see his face when you tell him of the Khundolar!'Rhadrog has asked you to use the Haerondir Horn in certain places around Haerondir, and to use it to scare nearby curious Orcs.Use the Haerondir Horn at horn-blowing spots in Haerondir.Blow Haerondir Horn at horn-blowing spots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Curious Orcs can be found outside of Haerondir.

Use the Haerondir Horn to spook curious Orcs who have wandered too close to Haerondir.Rhadrog can be found in Haerondir.

You should speak with Rhadrog.Speak with Rhadrog'Another way we keep those Orcs out of here is with the use of eerie-sounding instruments. Here's one of them: the Haerondir Horn! There's a few places in Haerondir that have excellent acoustics. Go blow the horn in those places, and after that, see if you can find any curious Orcs that have strayed too close. Sneak up behind them, and blow the horn! Keeping the fear in them keeps us safe. I'll admit, it's also a bit of fun, but don't tell Anborn I said that.''I told you it was fun! Orcs are such cowards. Haerondir should remain unbothered by them for the time being. Should we return from the coming battle, and I remain hopeful we will, we will not find this ruin has become a stronghold for any remaining Orcs!'Aragorn has tasked Bergil with finding enough athelas, also known as kingsfoil, to treat every soldier afflicted with the Black Shadow.Search Minas Tirith for any kingsfoil growing wild.Find wild-growing kingsfoil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the kingsfoil you have found back to Bergil, outside of the Houses of Healing on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.'I am to find kingsfoil leaves - living if I can and as much as possible. But truly, I do not know how I will find another single leaf! Does it grow in the cracks somewhere? I am sure I've seen it here or there, but I know not where! I am driving myself mad, thinking how often I walked past that very shape of leaf. 

'Will you help me? I fear to think what that Aragorn fellow will do with me if I do not. That kingsfoil must be about, must it not?  In cracks and greenswards, there must be some, somewhere!''What is this? Wild sprigs of that athelas? Oh, you are a miracle-worker, ${PLAYER}. I will take this to that hooded Aragorn, immediately.'Aragorn has tasked Bergil with finding enough athelas, also known as kingsfoil, to treat every soldier afflicted with the Black Shadow.Ask people in Minas Tirith for any dried kingsfoil leaves they may have.Ask around for kingsfoil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the dried kingsfoil you have found back to Bergil, outside of the Houses of Healing on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Bring the kingsfoil to Bergil'What a bind I am! I found that hooded Aragorn a few dried leaves of kingsfoil or, what does he call it, athelas? Well, now he wants more. The old man who gave me those leaves has not any more. Will you help me? Somewhere about here, someone must have a few more dried leaves!''You were able to find some dried kingsfoil? By the kings of old, you have saved my hide! I will bring it to that Aragorn directly.'As she prepares to depart for Haerondir, Mílgamel asks for your aid in finding a sample of Trollstrife - the mysterious lichen that you discovered during your adventures in Ithilien.Trollstrife can be found on the sides of trees in the Noman-lands.

