'They took the road eastward toward the Slag-hills and were to move northward onto the battle plain to search for you and Artamir between the hills.

'I would suggest you begin your search upon the battle plain itself. Let us hope the Enemy's forces have heeded their Master's orders and have not brought an ambush upon my men.

'When you find them, send them back to Haerondir by our safest paths. They will know the way.''Do you believe my words now? Have you seen your allies fall now to unseen blades?

'Tread carefully, ${CLASS}...

'The Wainriders have claimed the site of their greatest defeat and now defile it with their very presence. You and any other Living that seek to pass through these lands have much to fear from their return.'The Rangers know much of the lands and history of Ithilien and have dedicated themselves to its protection even in times of war.Henneth Annûn can be found in north-central North Ithilien.

Mablung has asked you to hear the reports of recently-returned Rangers to help guide his plans to defend Ithilien.Mablung can be found in Henneth Annûn.

You have heard the reports of his Rangers and should now deliver them to Mablung.Talk to Mablung'After I sent you on your patrol, I sent several other Rangers to track our foes in the further reaches of Ithilien. 

'Many of them went to the north, a few to the west, and a few to the east. The border of Dagorlad has always been contested, but our foes have been emboldened by their Master's rage and pour across it in greater numbers than we have previously weathered.

'It has been some time, and I would hope that my scouts have all returned by now. I would ask that you gather their reports and deliver them to me.

'Search for my scouts in Henneth Annûn and hear what they have learned of our foes.''These reports are troubling, and much will need to be done to ensure our foes cannot gain more of a hold in Ithilien.

'The Khundolar are a terrible foe... for they are unlikely to surrender in direct combat. If we are to rout their forces in Ithilien, it must be through total defeat. 

'The Orcs of Mordor are more easily spooked, but their numbers are endless and the Dark Lord drives them further into Ithilien each day.

'To be free of even one of our foes would be a great boon to our cause!'As the Second Age approached its end, Elrond stood with the Last Alliance against the forces of Sauron and won a decisive victory that led to the Dark Lord's defeat.Elrohir can be found at Haerondir.

Elladan and Elrohir have offered to tell a tale of a great victory over the Enemy. You should speak to Elrohir when you are ready to hear the tale.Talk to ElrohirElrohir can be found at Haerondir.

Elladan and Elrohir have finished their tale of the Battle of Dagorlad. You should now speak to Elrohir.Talk to Elrohir at Haerondir'${PLAYER}, I believe all who wish to hear the tale have arrived by now. I can see men of Rohan, Gondor, and Ithilien gathered about... and still I can sense the unease in them.

'Elrohir and I shall do our best to ease it, but I cannot promise it shall be enough. Each of us shall be called to confront our fates soon enough, and it is likely some of us shall be more fortunate than others. But none should dwell on such things...

'As for the tale, it shall be a story of the Battle of Dagorlad's final hours and of my father's triumph over the servants of the Dark Lord. It is a lengthy tale, but my brother and I shall make sure the message of hope is not lost in its telling.

'Elrohir shall begin at your request, so when you believe everyone is ready, you should speak to him.''Let us begin, ${PLAYER}.''I have told it as best I can, ${PLAYER}. I hope it is enough to give these men comfort before we confront the Dark Lord.

'I must admit, I left out some of the more dreadful scenes that father described in the battle and embellished a few details... but I believe the full account is best left for times of peace and reflection. These men needed a tale of hope, and so that is what I told.

'It shall be as it was -- Elves and Men shall stand together again! Let us hope victory can be won once more and that the Ring of Power meets its final doom!'Angbor has been tasked with arming the men who will march east, but requires more metals to meet the demand for weapons and armour.Veins of ore can be found around the base of Mount Mindolluin.

You should mine the base of the mountain for ore.Collect ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The forge is located in Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.

You should bring the ore to the forge.Place the ore in the forgeYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Angbor'When last we spoke, near Pelargir, I expected to arrive before the battle began, or at least in the midst of it. But alas, the Enemy struck swiftly while I encountered setbacks and obstacles.

'Perhaps I will tell you more of my journey some time. Right now, we must see that the men who will march to the Black Gate are well outfitted and provisioned for the journey. Currently our weapons and armour supplies run low, but ore from the mountain should help us forge more blades and helmets. Will you collect some ore for the smithy?''Excellent work! This should give us at least a dozen more blades, if not more!'The herbalists of the Houses of Healing are unable to mix medicine fast enough for the healers tending the ill and wounded.The Houses of Healing can be found on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Look for trueleaf, blushblade, and snagbane within the High Hall, House of Remedies, or House of Rest.Gather trueleaf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather blushblade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather snagbane (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mixing tables can be found in the High Hall, House of Remedies, or House of Rest, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Find a mixing table and combine the ingredients into edledhim.Ioreth stands in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should return to Ioreth in the Houses of Healing and let her know you have prepared more edledhim.Return to Ioreth'The medicines are not ready. We have too few herbalists and too many wounded, by far! But here you are, just standing about. And to my eye, that means you have not enough to do. Well! If you wish to do some good instead of getting in the way, you will help the herbalists mix medicines. Edledhim, also called Sorrowfew, is needed most right now.

'Of course, they will be too overwhelmed to give you instruction, so let me see to that. First, you will need to gather up some Trueleaf, Blushblade, and Snagbane. Then you must find a mixing table, mix them together in the correct proportion, and place them in phials. Do you understand? Good then. Off with you!''There you are again! Still standing about? Oh, I see, so you've gone and mixed a batch of edledhim? Well, I am glad someone in these halls is doing their part!'Aragorn has decreed that everyone shall break for the remainder of the day and mourn those lives lost in the battle of the Pelennor Fields.You should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to AragornYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Speak with Aragorn'The dead have all been accounted for. The missing have been found. Now is the time to mourn those who fought to the end, and fought so bravely for this great kingdom.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Come. It is time.''Now we rest, for soon the march to the Black Gate will begin.'Even in the harsh terrain of the Noman-lands, life, though it hardy and few, still flourishes.Blighted Marsh-lurkers can be found throughout the marshlands for the Wastes.

