You have gathered the moss and should now deliver them to Arodor.'It would seem that strange things grow on the edge of the foul marshes. Legolas has told me of a moss you encountered growing on the backs of Marsh-lurkers. We believe this moss to have special properties that can cull toxic fumes, straight from the surrounding air.

'If you are willing, find some of this moss and bring it back here to me. I should be able to develop an elixir from the moss.''Thank you, my friend. Our company shall put this strange moss you bring us to good use. I hope that it will aid us in the days to come.'Desperate to hold their last refuge, the Rangers of Ithilien devise a plan to use the natural defences of Ithilien's wildlife against the Enemy.Shimmering river-toads can be found along the shores of various streams and ponds in North Ithilien, especially to the north-east of Henneth Annûn.

Rhadrog has asked you to defeat toads in North Ithilien and harvest their slime for use by the Rangers.Collect toad-slime from shimmering river-toads (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhadrog can be found in Henneth Annûn.

You have carefully gathered a great deal of toad-slime and should now return to Rhadrog.Talk to RhadrogWorkbenches can be found within the deepest caverns of Henneth Annûn.

You have gathered phials of toad-slime and should now use it to coat arrow-heads for the Rangers of Ithilien.Rhadrog can be found in Henneth Annûn.

You have coated many arrow-heads in toad-slime and should now report back to Rhadrog.Talk to Rhadrog'There is a matter which has left a few of us uneasy, my friend.

'Upon our return, a great troll was wandering near the eastern entrance to Henneth Annûn. In sunlight, no less! We struck at it from the shadows, but it fled before we could deal a killing blow.

'We do not know if it learned of the refuge's entrance or was passing by chance, but we cannot afford to be exposed to the Enemy.

'To that end, I have devised a plan to protect us if another troll draws too near. There are toads within Ithilien that produce a curious slime. It is not a threat to the lives to man or beast, but it produces a strange sensation and floods one's vision with illusory forms.

'With such a slime on our arrow-heads, we shall have little to fear from even the largest of the Enemy's forces. While they are being deceived by their own eyes, they will be easier to track and slay before they can return to their masters.

'Seek these toads, and carefully harvest their slime in these phials. Once you have filled them, return to me, and I shall instruct you further.''Yes, that looks to be enough.

'Now then, take those phials to one of our workbenches and apply the slime to our arrow-heads.

'Do work carefully, my friend. I would not want you to stumble into the falls!''We shall be well-prepared the next time a troll strays too close to Henneth Annûn. Even if we do not slay it before it flees, I doubt it shall be of any help to its master for some time.

'Excellent work, my friend.'The soil of North Ithilien is rich, even in times of war. The Rangers of Ithilien hope that simple efforts will aid in preserving the land in years to come.Seeds can be found on the Field of Cormallen and in the surrounding woods.

Ereblen has asked you to gather many seeds from the Field of Cormallen and then plant them in the lowlands of North Ithilien.Collect horsetail seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect oxlip seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect vetchling seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fertile soil can be found in the lowlands of North Ithilien to the west and south of Henneth Annûn.

You have gathered many seeds and should now plant them throughout North Ithilien.Ereblen can be found to the west of Henneth Annûn.

You have planted many seeds and should now return to Ereblen.Talk to Ereblen'Could you hold a moment, ${PLAYER}?

'Since I have asked you to harvest the flowers and herbs of Ithilien, I must also task you with planting new seeds. It may seem a foolish errand with the Enemy's forces looming so near to us, but if we are to fight for a bright future in Gondor, we will have need of Ithilien's bounty.

'To the west lies the Field of Cormallen, a verdant field wreathed by of some of Ithilien's most striking trees and flowers.  Seeds of many kinds can be found amongst the grass, especially those of oxlip, horsetail, and vetchling.

'The seeds should be very easy to find... oxlip seeds resemble those of a maple tree, vetchling seeds appear nearly identical to chestnuts, and horsetail seeds are indistinguishable from acorns.

'Gather many of them and then plant as many as you are able in the lowlands surrounding the Field of Cormallen.

'Once you have done this, return to me.''The many flowers and herbs of Ithilien are of great value to us, as well as the people of Gondor. For that reason, we tend them very carefully. Where any are claimed by hand or death, another is planted by our company.

'You have helped ensure that the lands of Ithilien will remain vibrant even in the face of the Enemy, and you have my thanks.'With the Host of the West on the march, Angbor has been given orders to proclaim the King's return.Morgul lurkers can be found in the wooded land south of the after-battle Cross-roads.

You should proclaim the King's return to any Morgul Orcs lurking nearby.Tell Morgul lurkers of the King's return (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Morgul lurkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.Talk to Angbor'Stay a moment, ${PLAYER}. Aragorn has asked me to make his coming known to what Morgul Orcs have regrouped in nearby Ithilien, so that word may be spread among their loathsome kind. If it were you who stood before them and proclaimed the true king of Gondor returning, I vouch it would strike some fear into their hearts. It might even put some bravery into the chests of my men here at the Cross-roads!''Exemplary work. I am certain they ran like the cowards they are.'After abandoning the Battle of the Pelennor Fields when defeat was inevitable, a company of Variags seeks to return to Khand and put the war behind them.Talk to Jarl GurthilmJarl Gurthilm can be found among his company on the banks of the Anduin in south-western North Ithilien.

You have encountered a familiar party of Variags camped within North Ithilien and should speak to their Jarl.Talk to Jarl GurthilmThe Field of Cormallen can be found far to the north in the north-western reaches of North Ithilien.

Jarl Gurthilm has asked you to keep the Orcs and Easterlings in North Ithilien at bay as he and his men travel. He expects a report on your efforts near the Field of Cormallen.Meet Jarl Gurthilm at the Field of CormallenJarl Gurthilm and his company must be somewhere nearby the Field of Cormallen.

You have arrived at the Field of Cormallen, but the Variags are nowhere to be found. You should search nearby for Jarl Gurthilm's company.Search for Jarl Gurthilm's company near the Field of CormallenJarl Gurthilm and his company can be found to the east of the Field of Cormallen.

You have found Jarl Gurthilm and his company and should now speak to him.Talk to Jarl GurthilmWhile exploring the shores of the Anduin, you have discovered a company of Variags camped upon its bank.

Upon closer inspection, you realize it is none other than Jarl Gurthilm and his men.

Despite your terse interactions in Osgiliath, his men do not appear immediately hostile and he gestures for you to approach.'Why have you come here? Have you come to test our threats? As I said before, we have no quarrel with Gondor and no quarrel with you.

'Our only concern now is a swift return to Khand. The supplies you traded in Osgiliath are of great use to us, but the gold shall not avail us until we are home and far from the reach of Mordor.

'The Khundolar know nothing of our plan to return to Khand, and indeed, it would be best for the both of us if they did not learn of it. The Lord that offered us gold in exchange for our services is an unscrupulous fellow, and I would prefer to keep his attention elsewhere. The Orcs and Khundolar that inhabit these lands are no friends of ours, and for that reason we shall keep to the western shores of the Great River.

'I have a proposal for you, ${CLASS}. Keep the Easterlings and Orcs distracted, and we shall see you well-rewarded. We do not expect to be free of encounters with them, but to have fewer to deal with would be a great boon for my company.

'Offer me your name and your services or depart and trouble us no more.'

You give your name to Jarl Gurthilm and accept the offer to keep the Enemy's forces at bay, knowing that the Rangers work to the same end.

'Those that seek to deceive my company do not live long enough to realize their mistake. I have not misjudged you, have I?

'We shall expect to see you again and hear your report near the Field of Cormallen. If you do not know it, I would suggest you look for a ring of vibrant trees surrounding a meadow. If beauty were gold, this land would be among the richest.'Jarl Gurthilm and his company look visibly shaken as you approach, though they have tried not to appear so.

'This... was no chance encounter. I do not blame you for failing to keep these men from my company, for they were searching for us... and us alone.

'You shall have your reward yet, but I must alter our arrangement in light of these events.

'Do not fear any treachery on my part, ${PLAYER}, for your reward does not lie in question. In fact, it can only grow greater!'The Rangers of Ithilien often use traps to capture deer for venison, but to ensnare an encroaching Orc in times of war would be an even greater prize.Ideal trap locations can be found around the eastern entrance to Henneth Annûn.

Rhadrog has asked you to lay traps for deer and Orcs alike in the lands around Henneth Annûn.Lay traps around Henneth Annûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rhadrog can be found in Henneth Annûn.

You have laid many traps on behalf of the Rangers of Ithilien. You should now return to Rhadrog.Talk to Rhadrog in Henneth Annûn'Could you aid me with something, ${PLAYER}?

'In the haste of our return, my brethren and I have forgotten to set traps around Henneth Annûn. These traps provide us an easy source of meat from the nearby beasts, and also keep wandering foes from straying too near to the refuge.

'I know it might seem a simple task, but if the war continues as it does, we shall have need of more meat and materials.

'The falls protect the western border of Henneth Annûn, so it is best to lay the traps to the south and east.

'I await your return.''The traps are laid then?

'I shall send one of our number on patrol to check them soon. At best, we shall have more meat and leather for our needs, and at worst, some unfortunate Orc will meet its end.

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'The terrible flowers you and Mithrandir encountered in Imlad Morgul have sprung forth anew and now spread beyond the valley of the Dead City.Noisome flowers can be found along the road into Imlad Morgul.

Mithrandir has asked you to return to the border of Imlad Morgul and cull the noisome flowers that have begun to spread into Ithilien.Burn noisome flowers outside Imlad Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mithrandir can be found at the Camp of the Host on the border of the Wastes far to the north in North Ithilien.

You have burned the noisome flowers outside Imlad Morgul, and you should now return to Mithrandir with news of your success.Talk to Mithrandir at the Camp of the Host'${PLAYER}, grim tidings have been delivered to me by one of Aragorn's rear scouts. The noisome flowers we burned within Imlad Morgul have grown anew and now spread beyond the shadowed vale.

'They cannot be allowed to spread beyond Imlad Morgul, else the lands of Ithilien may also succumb to their taint. If flame cannot hinder them, I fear that we may leave behind greater troubles for Gondor.

'I would ask that you return to the border of Imlad Morgul and burn them once again. If they return again, it seems our only course shall be to continue pruning them.''You have done well to burn those noisome flowers. Let us hope their rampant growth shall be lessened for a time.

'I shall call on you again if I receive word from the South, my friend.'Anborn has asked you to clear out the Orcs camped at Nuiharn.Anborn has asked you to defeat the Orcs and their leader Bloglok camped in the ruins of Nuiharn.

Nuiharn can be found in the hills to the north-west of Haerondir.Enter the Orc camp at NuiharnAnborn has asked you to defeat the Orcs and their leader Bloglok camped in the ruins of Nuiharn.

Nuiharn can be found in the hills to the north-west of Haerondir.Defeat Orcs in Nuiharn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Bloglok (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Anborn in Haerondir.Return to Anborn‘We've found an Orc camp not far from here, in the ruins of Nuiharn. They do not appear to be making a move toward the Camp of the Host, but it would be unwise to let them linger nearby. The last thing we need is to be ambushed on the road or flanked from the rear while we march to the Black Gate. We have learned that the Orc Captain Bloglok leads this camp. Head to Nuiharn and end this threat.'‘Good to hear that Bloglok and his followers are no longer a threat to the Host of the West. Now we can focus on the road ahead.’Although they have not been seen for hundreds of years, the Wainriders of the East have shaped the history of Gondor in both victory and defeat.Faramir can be found outside Ondoher's Folly.

Faramir has asked to tell you the tale of the Wainriders in the Wastes. You should speak to him when you are ready to hear it.Talk to Faramir, son of Ondoher outside Ondoher's FollyArtamir can be found outside Ondoher's Folly.

You have heard Faramir's tale of the Wainriders and should now speak to Artamir.Talk to Artamir outside Ondoher's Folly'I must admit, my friend, I am still vexed by Faramir's insistence on the threat of Wainriders upon the battle plain.

'The Wainriders have not been a threat to the peoples of Gondor in over a thousand years, and yet Faramir speaks of them as a foe with which we shall soon contend. The might of the Easterling clans has diminished much since their earlier, more unified days, and it seems unlikely to me that they have suddenly reforged a kinship that broke over many long years.

'He has asked to speak with you, and I do not doubt his words shall again concern the Wainriders.

'See what you make of his claims, ${PLAYER}. The Wainriders are dead and gone, but so too was Faramir, son of Ondoher....''If you are to survive long in these lands, ${CLASS}, you must first learn the history of the Wainriders as I and my father once did.

'The hatred between Gondor and the Wainriders is a tale of fathers and sons. Our lands were stolen and reclaimed through the passing of the years, but the Wainriders shaped the line of Kings in a way that no other foe could equal.

'After losing his own father to their hordes, King Calimehtar, father of my father, rode against the Wainriders in vengeance. With the help of the North-men, he devastated their ranks, broke their wains and chariots, and slew them upon the hill to the east - a hill which came to be known as Dol Acharn. Such a victory brought peace to Gondor for many years, and Calimehtar never again had to contend with the Wainriders before his death.

'Peace, such as it is, is always short-lived. Calimehtar's son and my father, King Ondoher, was forced to meet them in battle. Alas, you are aware of the loss Gondor suffered as a result.

'Artamir here has told me much of the days that followed the King's death as well as my own. He tells me that the Wainriders made camp to the south-west, but were ambushed and slain to the last by a vast army under the command of a man named Eärnil. He claims that Eärnil soon became king of Gondor, even in the face of the claim made by my sister's husband, King Arvedui of Arthedain. What tales he has told me of these new days...

'Ah, but now the past has risen to confront the present. Fate is a curious thing, ${PLAYER}... is it not?'This... cannot be! If the Wainriders again roam the battle plain, they may meet the Host of the West on the field. Their hatreds will not have dulled with time, and they shall strike at those that bear the king's banner with a vengeance renewed.

'We must bring word to Haerondir and soon!'Thai-chât, an archer of Harad, has pivotal information regarding the fate of a Mûmakil that disappeared into the wilds of Ithilien after an ill-fated attack at Cirith Negen.Marrow-root can be found within Aelin Veren and among the stony foot-hills of the Ephel Dúath.

Thai-chât has asked you to seek marrow-root in the ruins of Aelin Veren as well as along the Ephel Dúath, as he hopes it can be used to lure his Mûmak out of the lands of North Ithilien.Collect marrow-root in North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lokhu-achi can be found somewhere among the wilds of North Ithilien far to the south-west of Cirith Negen.

Thai-chât has asked you to discover the location of his pet Mûmak, Lokhu-achi, before luring him from the lands of Ithilien.Find Lokhu-achi in the wilds of North IthilienThe Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien.

You have discovered Lokhu-achi's location and now should crack marrow-root and smear it on stones to lure this Mûmak to the western reaches of North Ithilien and the Nindalf.The Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien.

Lokhu-achi is now following you. You should lead the Mûmak to the edge of the Nindalf.The Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien.

Lokhu-achi is still following you. You should lead the Mûmak to the edge of the Nindalf.The Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien.

Lokhu-achi is still following you. You should lead the Mûmak to the edge of the Nindalf.The Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien.

Lokhu-achi is still following you. You should lead the Mûmak to the edge of the Nindalf.Thai-chât can be found at Aelin Veren, in central North Ithilien.

You have sent Lokhu-achi beyond the lands of Ithilien and should now return to Thai-chât.Talk to Thai-chât'Come close, ${RACE}, for I do not wish to alarm the Rangers with what I must tell you. You see... I neglected to tell our captors of my companion and dear friend, Lokhu-achi.'

Thai-chât's voice shrinks to a whisper.

'Lokhu-achi is a Mûmak of sixteen years, and I cared for him after his mother was felled by disease in his earliest months. Lokhu-achi endured and grew mighty, weathering illness and battles alike, and he was to be brought into the war at long last. It was an honour to see him bear the brilliant armouring of my people, but those who rode him into battle did not make it far into these lands...

'Their company was ambushed at Cirith Negen, and there they were slain to the last... save for Lokhu-achi. He cast off his armouring, wild in anger and confusion, and trampled all beneath him as he fled the mountain pass.

'I believe he lives still, ${CLASS}, but there remains no way for him to escape the lands of the Rangers alive - not without aid. The Rangers will not trust our bond, and they will slay him unless he departs from here.

'There is a pale root that grows among the foot-hills of the black mountains, and it is known to my people as marrow-root. When cracked, it gives off a strong, sweet odour to which the Mûmakil are drawn. I have seen it among the ruins here, and in the foot-hills to the east. He fled far to the south-west of Cirith Negen, but I know no more of his flight. Once you have gathered the roots and discovered his whereabouts, crack the roots on moss-laden stones and lead him into the marshlands far to the north-west.

'I know not if he shall be left in peace there, but anywhere is safer for a Mûmak than the lands of the Rangers.'As you approach Lokhu-achi, he makes no attempt to attack or flee. In fact, the beast seems docile... and perhaps a bit hungry. Lokhu-achi's trunk meanders about you, searching curiously for the marrow-root you bear.

You offer what little remains of the marrow-root you gathered to Lokhu-achi, and as he chews it, he shakes his head about in an almost playful gesture.

You point towards the marshlands to the north-west, and Lokhu-achi seems to understand your command.

Lokhu-achi gently brushes you with his trunk, nearly knocking you off your feet, and then begins to wander into the shallows of the marsh.'While I am saddened that I may not see my dear companion again, I am glad that he has left behind the lands of those who would do him harm.

'Lokhu-achi is a resilient Mûmak, and I am certain he shall find his way to Harad or Dagorlad in time - whenever he should choose to return from his journey.

'You have done me a great honour, ${RACE}.'There are some enemies bearing orders from Mordor within the Tower of the Teeth.The Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills.

You should intercept more orders from Uruks and Black Númenóreans within the Towers of the Teeth.Collect Orders from Mordor in the Towers of the TeethThe Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills.

