You should talk to Angbor.Talk to Angbor'We are preparing to march soon. We must start packing the supplies that we will need on this journey to the Black Gate. Collect supplies from around the pavilion, then pack them in crates on one of the carts.''Good, good! Now we are one step closer to marching east.'Éomer fears any enemies remaining near its walls might find a way into Minas Tirith and do harm there, and has asked you to patrol its perimeter.Head to the north section of the outer wall of after-battle Minas Tirith.Head to the north section of the outer wall of Minas TirithPatrol the outer wall of after-battle Minas Tirith.Head south to continue patrolling the outer wall of the cityPatrol outside the main gate of after-battle Minas Tirith.Head south to patrol outside the main gate of the cityHead south to continue patrolling the outer wall of after-battle Minas Tirith.Continue south on patrol along the outer city wallHead to the southern point of after-battle Minas Tirith's outer wall.Patrol the southern part of the outer wall of Minas TirithYou should talk to Éomer, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Éomer'There are many ways to sneak into the City unnoticed. After we set forth for the Black Gate, too few eyes will be keeping watch and even fewer swords and bows will be defending it. Please patrol the outer walls of Minas Tirith and vouchsafe no remaining enemies loiter there.''Good, I am glad that very few foes still dare to come close to the city walls.'The battle-cats of the Khundolar are fierce predators trained to slay Men and beasts alike. Loosed upon the wilds of North Ithilien, they now threaten the native creatures.Ravenous battle-cats can be found to the west of Henneth Annûn.

Ereblen has asked you to defeat wandering battle-cats brought to North Ithilien by the Khundolar in the hope that they will no longer prey on Ithilien's wildlife.Defeat ravenous battle-cats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ereblen can be found to the north-west of Henneth Annûn.

You have defeated the wandering battle-cats and should now return to Ereblen.Talk to Ereblen'Have you seen the cats of the Khundolar lurking nearby, ${PLAYER}?

'They are terrible beasts bred only to maim and kill the enemies of their masters. When those enemies are absent or hidden away like my brethren, the battle-cats sate their hunger on any creature they can find.

'The lands of Ithilien are wild, yes, and beasts know the many ways through the shadows of these woods, but the battle-cats are trained to outpace and outsmart them. I have even heard tell they have the strength to slay the bears of Ithilien.

'I would ask that you defeat them before they can cause great harm to the order of beasts in Ithilien. Worse yet, their keen noses might lead them to our refuges.

'You will find them to the north, but be wary, my friend.''The Dark Lord may not care for the health of his lands, but Ithilien must remain verdant and wild. Having such a predator lurking in our wilds would not bode well for any of us.

'It is unfortunate that the Khundolar have raised their cats in such a way, but it cannot be helped now. And too much is at stake....

'You have my thanks.'The Orcs at Fushaum Gund must not be allowed to rally and attack before the Host of the West even finishes its march.The Orc encampment of Fushaum Gund is located on the eastern slopes of the Slag-hills.

You should destroy battle horns and tools in the Orc encampment to hamstring any rallying cry.Enter the enemy encampment of Fushaum GundThe Orc encampment of Fushaum Gund is located on the eastern slopes of the Slag-hills.

