You should return to Éomer King with the artifacts you found.Return to Éomer King'${PLAYER}, may I ask a favour of you? Old tales among my people tell of the time before we settled in Rohan. We called ourselves the Éothéod, then, and Guthláf believed it was through this land that our ancestors came, down from the Vale of Anduin, all the way to the Riddermark, where we saw the goodness of the land and made our home.

'While you are out assisting the Rangers in the Noman-lands, will you keep an eye out for any intact sign or remnant of the forebears of the Rohirrim? It would mean much to possess some such piece of our distant past.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We have precious little from the time of our forefathers. The Eorlingas will fight in our ancestors' name in the great battle to come.'You have proven yourself invaluable to the Host of the West and have done much to aid Gondor and its people. For this, Aragorn now counts you among one of his top commanders.You must earn Respected standing with the Host of the WestThe recently-abandoned refuge of Torngroth has been claimed by the Orcs of Mordor and they now stand between the Rangers and valuable supplies.Torngroth can be found far to the north of Henneth Annûn.

