t them to earn a reward suitable for a collector in Far Anórien.Wanted: Worn Furs from the Far Anórien region.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Small bands of enemies still roam the Pelennor Fields, threatening all who venture forth.You should defeat any enemies you find on the after-battle Pelennor.Defeat foes on the Pelennor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should talk to Éomer, who can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Éomer'Even now, enemies still roam the Pelennor. If it is to be safe again for the Gondorian farmers who tend the land, we must defeat these remaining foes. I want the Pelennor safe before we march eastward.''Thank you, ${CLASS}. Each passing day, the Pelennor fades from the hands of the enemy and returns to the kingdom of Gondor.'Many of Sauron's forces lay in hiding throughout the wreckage, and need to be cleared to reduce any further threats.Signs of Morgul Lurkers can be found throughout the First Circle in Minas Tirith.

