You should return to Legolas.Return to Legolas'${PLAYER}, I look out upon this land and feel a deep sorrow. Where Ithilien is beautiful, the Wastes are blighted and cursed. Evil's taint seeks always to spread, and we must not let that happen. Go out into the Noman-lands and take a closer look. Remove the blight wherever you find it.''Thank you for your help, ${PLAYER}. It may seem like your efforts mean little, but I have hope that one day, whether we be here to see it or not, this land will return to its original splendor.'In years past, the Rangers held many refuges within the lands of North Ithilien from which to combat the Enemy's forces. Now, only Henneth Annûn remains and the rest lie abandoned or in the hands of the Enemy.Thurindath can be found far to the south-east of Henneth Annûn, Adab Dolen can be found to the north of Henneth Annûn, and Torngroth can be found far to the north-west of Henneth Annûn.

Mablung has asked you to scout the old Ranger refuges of Thurindath, Adab Dolen, and Torngroth. You should seek them out and take note of what you discover.Patrol the abandoned refuge of ThurindathPatrol the abandoned refuge of Adab DolenPatrol the abandoned refuge of TorngrothMablung can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.

You have scouted the abandoned Ranger refuges and should now tell Mablung of what you discovered.Talk to Mablung'For many years, the Rangers held refuges throughout the lands of Ithilien. However, as the Enemy regained his terrible might, we began to lose our footholds one by one... and now only Henneth Annûn remains. Our hidden refuge of Torngroth held long against the Enemy's forces - outlasting both Thurindath and Adab Dolen, but it, too, fell.

'I wonder what has become of them since we were forced to abandon them. With all we have endured in the great battle, can we now hope to reclaim what was lost?

'I would ask that you scout them, my friend. Torngroth can be found along a river-bed far to the north-west, Thurindath to the north, and Adab Dolen along the Mountains of Shadow far to the south-east.

'Go with haste, and tell me what you uncover. The time of the Rangers is not yet ended!''What have you to report, ${PLAYER}?'

You inform Mablung of the massive size of the spiders in Thurindath, the relatively untouched state of Adab Dolen, and your suspicion that Orcs have claimed Torngroth.

'I see. I shall send my Rangers to Adab Dolen at once. If we can reclaim one of our northern refuges, it shall aid us greatly in keeping the Enemy from crossing into Ithilien from Dagorlad. However, to have spiders and Orcs lurking within our lost refuges is another matter. The loss of Torngroth was a tremendous blow to our company, and I would see it returned to us.

'We do not have the time to reclaim them now, but I shall have my scouts keep a careful watch on both Torngroth and Thurindath.'Thurindol has a plan, but needs black powder from the scrap scattered about the Slag-hills in order to proceed.Black powder may be found within the rubble surrounding the Slag-hills.

You should collect black powder for Thurindol.Search rubble for black powder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thurindol can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.

You should return to Thurindol with the black powder you gathered.'The odds may be great against us, but it does not mean that I am ready to give up. I have a plan that will allow us to traverse the hills unnoticed.

'Search the slag for any black powder. There may be some within the rubble, thrown out the gate from the scrap mounds in Udûn.''Ah excellent. Yes, this powder is just what we need. I suppose you would like to know what this plan entails then?'The siege of Minas Tirith has left the lower tiers in utter ruin, trapping many Gondorians who tried to flee.You should free any trapped Gondorians that you come across in the First Circle in Minas Tirith.Free trapped Gondorians (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Imrahil can be found outside the front gates of Minas Tirith.

You should speak with Imrahil.Speak with Imrahil'Even though the siege weapons of Mordor have been silenced, the city continues to crumble in their wake. Many of the surviving citizens of Gondor have found themselves at the mercy of a ceaseless tide of slag and debris, and we do not have enough resources to search under every corner of the wreckage.

'We have already begun our rescue efforts, but I would ask for your assistance in the rescue of any Gondorians that still remain buried.''It seems that the damage to the lower city is far more extensive than we thought. We may have to divert traffic from these areas in order to avoid further crises.

'It pains me to see so many who failed to flee during the siege, but hope remains strong as long as we continue our rescue efforts. I thank you for your continued service to the people of Gondor, ${PLAYER}.'Orcs of Mordor dwelling in the caverns below the mountains are up to many nefarious activities.

