You have defeated many of the encroaching Mordor Firestarters. You should speak to Thurindol with news of your success.Talk to  Thurindol'${PLAYER}, these brush fires are no mere accident. My rangers report more Mordor Orcs crossing into North Ithilien, many of which bear torches.

'I believe the Enemy has sent these firestarters to scorch the land. Now that the Dawnless Day has ended, North Ithilien's new growth shows promise. And the Enemy will do everything to snuff out hope. 

'But we must act first. We must snuff out these firestarters before their flames engulf the region! You will find these torch-bearing enemies near the Fields of Cormallen.''The Dark Lord sees North Ithilien's new growth as a sign of his waning reach.

'We must do everything we can to help these lands heal. In such dark days, we must act as sentinels of hope, defending whatever promising growth we can. 

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'Candúr believes there are Black Númenórean sorcerers gathering within the Towers of the Teeth.Black Númenórean sorcerers can be found within the Towers of the Teeth.

You should defeat Black Númenórean sorcerers.Defeat Black Númenórean sorcerers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Candúr, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.Return to Candúr'Thurindol has spoken to me about the foes gathered within the towers of Carchost and Narchost. He believes some Black Númenóreans dwell there, and that some of them are perhaps sorcerers. I have seen their ilk, and know they are well beyond dangerous when armed and fully prepared. Let us strike at them whilst they are neither of these things, ${PLAYER}.''With the Black Númenóreans in the Towers defeated, we may just yet stand a chance. Yet still, peril is all around us.'Mablung has asked you to track down a vicious Warg known as The Stalker with the help of Faroth. He is lurking somewhere in the Noman-lands.Warg tracks can be found near the Camp of the Host.

