You should return to Mablung and tell him you have defeated Múgbakh, The Stalker.Return to Mablung'${PLAYER}, I have one last mission for you and Faroth.

'There exists an especially terrible Warg in these lands, feared by Man and Orc alike. To them, he is Múgbakh, but we Rangers call him The Stalker. He is known for stalking and toying with men for leagues before ultimately ambushing them and taking their life.  

'Our attempts at hunting him down have all failed. However, we did not have the keen nose of Faroth at our disposal. Go, track down The Stalker and end him for good.''At last, The Stalker is dead! On behalf of all the Rangers of Ithilien: thank you. We can rest easier knowing we are no longer being hunted by that fiend.'The Rangers of Ithilien had much to contend with before Osgiliath fell to the forces of Mordor, but nothing more curious than a strange group of travellers in Ithilien.Anborn can be found in Henneth Annûn.

Mablung has asked you to speak to Anborn about the strange travellers that passed through Ithilien before the battle brought them to Osgiliath.Talk to Anborn in Henneth Annûn'Being back in Henneth Annûn has stirred my memories, ${PLAYER}...

'Before you and I met in Osgiliath, our company was stationed here and Lord Faramir still held command. Through my years in Ithilien, I have encountered both beauty and terror, but surely nothing stranger than what we found one night. 

'We discovered two Halflings and their strange pet-creature! I swear it is true! They spent time amongst our company and spoke much to Lord Faramir in hushed tones... but we came to know them as best we could.

'I have some tales to tell of their time here, but I did not overhear as much as Anborn in our initial encounter with them.

'If you wish to know how we came to find them, you should ask Anborn to tell you the tale.''You wish to know of the strange company that passed through Ithilien?

'In truth, I wish I had more to tell. A few among our number spent time with them, but their stay was brief and their purposes were kept secret... except to Lord Faramir.

'I can describe what I beheld during their time here, but you will have to speak with the others if you desire to know more.'Amidst the growing turmoil within North Ithilien, great spiders have come down from the Ephel Dúath and seized the long-held Ranger refuge of Thurindath.Defeat spiders and destroy spider-websSpiders and their webs can be found within the old Ranger refuge of Thurindath in south-eastern North Ithilien.

You have discovered the refuge of Thurindath overrun with great spiders and their webs. You should defeat them and clear the refuge of their webbing.Destroy spider-webs in Thurindath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat spiders in Thurindath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mablung can be found at Henneth Annûn.

You have cleared the old Ranger refuge of Thurindath of spiders and their webs, but you should inform the Rangers of what you discovered.Talk to Mablung at Henneth AnnûnYou have discovered the Ranger refuge of Thurindath overrun with large spiders and thick, sticky webbing. It is unclear how long the spiders have held the refuge since the Rangers of Ithilien abandoned it, but they must be driven off if the Rangers are to retake this key foothold in North Ithilien.

You should defeat the spiders and destroy their webs before reporting back to the Rangers at Henneth Annûn.'While I am glad you have driven them from Thurindath, I worry what their presence in Ithilien could portend.

'Long have rumours passed among my men of a great spider living in the heights of the Ephel Dúath, but the tale is so old... and so unthinkable.

'You have travelled to the forests of Mirkwood, have you not? Could such a creature lurk just beyond our sight?'Angbor has been tasked with arming the men who will march east and wishes to deliver new armour to the soldiers.You should bring the armour to the soldiers in and around Aragorn's Pavilion, on the after-battle Pelennor.You should talk to Angbor, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Angbor'I tell you, my friend, the Haradrim are a devious foe. Do you know they were planning an assault from the south? By good fortune, my men and I intercepted them on our own northward march. I will not bother you with the details, but needless to say, my men and I stood our ground.

'Ah, so, it seems the smiths have some new armour for our men! Would you be a kind ${CLASS} and deliver it?''The gleam of new-forged armour should breathe courage and pride into any soldier's heart. May fear take hold of no man.'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Complete Slag-hillsComplete Quests of the Slag-hillsThurindol requires more information on the structures within the Slag-hills, and wishes for you to survey the territory.Good vantage points can be found around the Slag-hills.

You should survey the Black Gate and the Towers of the Teeth.Survey the Black GateSurvey the base of NarchostSurvey the tower of NarchostSurvey the base of CarchostSurvey the tower of CarchostYou should return to Thurindol, who can be found at the small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.Return to Thurindol'While you are out among the Slag-hills, would you be kind enough to survey the Enemy strongholds of Carchost, Narchost, and the Morannon?

'It is imperative that we have the latest movements of the Enemy.'You relate to Thurindol what you saw.

'The Morannon has not changed? That is as I expected. The movements you describe around Narchost are interesting. I do not know what to make of it. And Carchost is heavily guarded, you say? That must mean there is something of great importance within the tower now.'Aragorn wishes to do something to lift the spirits of the remaining soldiers.Golasgil can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.

Lord Aragorn has asked you to talk to Golasgil.Talk to GolasgilYou can find soldiers and kegs in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.

Golasgil has asked you to gather soldiers and kegs of ale.Collect kegs of ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golasgil can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.

You should speak with Golasgil and tell him the kegs and soldiers have been gathered.Talk to GolasgilJoin Golasgil and the men in toasting to those who fell on the Pelennor.<rgb=#FF00FF>Toast</rgb> with Golasgil<rgb=#FF00FF>Cheer</rgb> at GolasgilJoin Golasgil in singing Authlin's Song to lift the hearts of the gathered men.<rgb=#FF00FF>Sing</rgb> with GolasgilGolasgil can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.

The celebration has gone off without a hitch. Now you should talk to Golasgil.Talk to Golasgil'${PLAYER}, while those of faint hearts have departed, I feel we must do something for the men who remain. They have lost so much already, and this may be our last true chance to bolster their spirits before we move into the Enemy's territory.

'I would have you speak with Lord Golasgil. With so few Lords of Gondor left, I will need him to bear more of the burden of leadership. I know he will show a brave face in front of his men if I ask it of him.''Lord Elessar has asked me to do something for the men? I will do my best, if my king wishes it. This would have been a task better suited to someone like Forlong, but alas, it falls to me.

'He is not mistaken. Gondor has lost much already, but we all know that if we do not act now, we will lose everything. What would Forlong have done?

'I have an idea. Gather the men from around camp, and some kegs of ale. Then, meet me back here. We will celebrate one last time before we march bravely into the Enemy's maw.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. The men and ale are gathered. Here goes nothing.''Well, my spirits are certainly lifted! We will march to our destiny with a song in our hearts. For Gondor and for all the Free Peoples. I think Forlong would not be ashamed of us, ${PLAYER}.'Jubuya, a sorcerer of Harad, has offered to tell the Rangers of his homeland and culture in exchange for leniency.The Haradrim prisoners can be found at Aelin Veren in central North Ithilien.

After questioning Jubuya, he has asked you to speak to his fellows about their lives in Harad.Talk to Thai-châtTalk to Daugha-tûmJubuya can be found at Aelin Veren in central North Ithilien.

You have spoken to the other prisoners and should now speak to Jubuya once more.Talk to Jubuya'I shall answer your questions, ${RACE}.

'In truth, I know little of our purpose here... only that our war-master bade us surrender to these forest-men. You call them Rangers, do you not? A strange name, I think.

'We had long been stationed in the lands of Dagorlad, but travelled southward to reach the battle on the fields. Many of our number were slain at Cirith Negen by the Rangers, and soon we were few. I learned of Gondor's victory from the Rangers, but know little else of the battle.

'If this is our fate, I wish only to learn more of that great battle and then return home with my brethren. I would ask to hear more of the battle, but first, you should speak to my brethren of it... they are eager to hear of it.''You know of the great battle? Tell me what happened - I beg you. What of the Men of Harad?

You tell Thai-chât of the Black Serpent's doom at the hands of Théoden King and of the three Mûmakil who fell in their assault against the walls of Minas Tirith.

'So much death... if only we had abandoned the Dark Lord long ago. Cruel is a master who sits behind black mountains and steep tower-walls, feeling nothing as his soldiers are slaughtered.

'I no longer wish to be a part of this war... I wish only to return to Harad.

'I have heard all I can bear. Leave me, ${RACE}!''What know you of the battle on the fields of Gondor?'

You tell Daugha-tûm of deeds great and small on the Pelennor Fields. You speak of the death of Théoden King, the triumph of your allies against the Witch-king of Angmar, and of the sacrifices of great warriors before the Enemy's forces.

'The Rangers spoke of a wraith garbed all in red, who thought himself protected from weapons of war, yet he fled the field in fear. How can one who need not fear death be cowed before the armies of Gondor? They cannot be so mighty!

'If the Dark Lord has such servants in his command, how lowly must we be in his sight?

'I hunger for battle with the Men of Gondor, and yet, this is an ill-fated path for my people. We shall be used to the last, and what glory shall we have when all of us are gone?

'This battle must be ended, ${PLAYER}. It must... if ever we are to return home in peace.''I have waited patiently for you to tell them of the battle, and now I ask that you tell me what you told them.'

You tell Jubuya of the battle on the Pelennor Fields. You tell him of the shattering of the gates of Minas Tirith and of Grond. You tell him of the Witch-king of Angmar and of Gothmog's flight. You tell him of the Black Serpent's death, and of Théoden King who fell soon after. He listens attentively, and bares a sad smile when your tale comes to an end.

'So my King and his sons are slain, then. They would not have wished for death to find them any other way, ${RACE}.

'Regardless of this war's outcome, much will change in my homeland. The lands of Harad are unforgiving, but beautiful. If ever there is peace between our peoples, or if you remain such a bold adventurer, I believe you would feel at home in the wilds of Harad and among the warm winds of our deserts and jungles.

'If there were the time, I would tell you more of it, but I can sense these Rangers no longer appreciate our conversation.'After seeing the weight of the burden resting on the soldiers in the Host of the West, Elladan and Elrohir seek to inspire hope by telling them a tale of victory over the Enemy.Bands of soldiers, Rangers, and warriors can be found throughout Haerondir.

Elladan has asked you to gather the soldiers of the Host of the West stationed in Haerondir in the hope that he and his brother might ease their worries through the telling of an old victory over the Enemy.Elladan can be found on the eastern ramparts of Haerondir.

You have gathered many soldiers, rangers, and warriors and should now return to Elladan and Elrohir.Talk to Elladan at Haerondir'${PLAYER}, my father's tales can do much to inspire hope and awe. Elrohir and I have heard them many times, and they are known to us now perhaps even more clearly than to our father after these long years.

'His tales are full of both glory and despair, but certain moments carry with them no sadness even in the face of loss. He told us many tales of the battles during the Last Alliance, and while no moment can match the joyous defeat of the Enemy at the end of the Second Age, there are others that might inspire those in times such as these.

'My mind is drawn to father's tales of the Battle of Dagorlad. It was a great and terrible battle that raged for many long years, and even after victory was won many more passed before the Ring was cut from the Dark Lord's finger. Even still, it was a victory that marked a turning point in what to many seemed a hopeless war against Sauron. Men, dwarves, Elves, and even the High Elves stood fast against the Enemy's forces and though many were lost in the fighting, they pushed forth and threw down the Black Gate.

'It is a tale of victory against great odds, and it seems we march to a battle that shall be much the same. Brother, can you think of a greater tale to tell these men?'

Elrohir shakes his head and seems pleased with Elladan's choice.

'Gather the men of Haerondir, my friend, and let them hear of glory from us!''You have done well, my friend! I see many have come to hear our father's tales, and we shall soon begin.

'Let us hope it can bring some comfort to these men before we make for the Black Gate!'With an abundance of seeds and seedlings in the care of the Rangers, they now seek to heal the wounds dealt to Ithilien by the Enemy.Fertile soil can be found throughout Ithilien, especially above Henneth Annûn and near the ruins of Aelin Veren, Thargelon, and Bâr Tarnaher.

Ereblen has asked you to plant various seeds in the fertile soil of North Ithilien.Plant seeds in fertile soil in North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ereblen can be found in Henneth Annûn.

You have planted all the seeds and should now return to him in Henneth Annûn.Talk to Ereblen in Henneth Annûn'With all the seeds we have gathered recently, it has become of great import that we see them planted as soon as we are able. The Enemy's forces have been routed for the moment, and we must seize this opportunity.

'Here, my friend. Take these seeds and patrol the lands surrounding Henneth Annûn and the old ruins of Ithilien. It is there you shall find the most fertile soil, and it is there that these seeds should be planted.

'Go with haste, and we shall speak again soon.''You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}. The forces of the Enemy shall not relent, and neither shall we.

'If you would offer your aid on the morrow, I shall have need of it again!'Angbor has successfully provided armour to the soliders but is uncertain of the armour's quality.Soldiers with new armour can be found in the sparring area in Aragorn's Pavilion, on the after-battle Pelennor.

