Soldiers are ready to spar with you in an effort to improve their skills and test their armour.Talk to another soldier at the sparring area in Aragorn's pavilionSoldiers with new armour can be found in the sparring area in Aragorn's Pavilion, on the after-battle Pelennor.

Soldiers are ready to spar with you in an effort to improve their skills and test their armour.Talk to another soldier at the sparring area in Aragorn's pavilionYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Angbor'I tell you, the Haradrim were dauntless. My men and I held against wave after wave of them until I saw that we must gain some advantage or be worn down to defeat. I led a charge and drove them back to the river, where my archers rained down arrows upon their rafts as they came across. It was thus that we rebuffed them, though not without great effort.

'The men here on the Pelennor are wearied, but still they must train. Will you go down to the sparring area and put their new armour to the test? They could surely gain from a combat tip or two from such a seasoned campaigner as yourself.''This armour fits well. Let us see how it holds to combat.''I am sure this armour is impenetrable.''I will spar with you when you are ready.''How did the armour hold up? Good, good! I hope that their spirits stay high in the days to come.''Are you certain this armour will protect me from a Morgul blade?''Let us spar and see how this armour holds up in combat.'Aragorn has asked you to make a reckoning of those who fell in the Battle of the Pelennor Fields.Ask Duinhir, Gléowine, Wídfara, Gamling, and Cutha about what they saw of the battle yesterday. They can all be found among the tents of Aragorn's Pavilion.Talk to DuinhirTalk to WídfaraTalk to GléowineTalk to GamlingTalk to CuthaAragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.

You should return to Aragorn and tell him what you learned.Talk to  AragornAragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.

Help Aragorn survey the battlefield for the missing and presumed dead of Gondor.Complete -- The Aftermath: Dervorin and RossaranComplete -- The Aftermath: Forlong, Golasgil, and HirluinComplete -- The Aftermath: Ingold and TurgonComplete -- The Aftermath: Duilin and DerufinComplete -- Book 7, Chapter 2: The Council of the CaptainsYou should speak with Rossaran, Dervorin, Golasgil, and Ingold, who can all be found in Aragorn's Pavilion, upon the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to RossaranTalk to DervorinTalk to GolasgilTalk to IngoldYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to AragornAragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.

Help Aragorn survey the battlefield for the missing and presumed dead of Rohan.Complete -- The Aftermath: Elfmar, Harding, and TorferthComplete -- The Aftermath: The Valiant RohirrimYou should talk to Éomer and Nothmar, who can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to ÉomerTalk to NothmarYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Aragorn'Théoden, Fastred, Golodir, Halbarad are but a few of the names of those who fell on the battlefield yesterday. Many more of the fallen remain uncounted, and we cannot mourn, remember, or honour them while this is so. 

'Please, my friend, go about the pavilion and see what you can learn of the battle. More took place here than any one account can comprehend.''I can not help you. I still heavily bear the loss of my sons.''${PLAYER}, my friend. I have been looking for Harding. He and I were fighting side by side, only to get separated in the fray in the late morning. I thought that we would meet again here at the pavilion, but alas, he is nowhere to be found.''I stayed by the side of Théoden King even after his passing and helped escort his body to Minas Tirith. When I heard that Aragorn had set up an encampment on the Pelennor, I rode out to join him.''I am sure you fought bravely in battle. How I survived the ordeal, though, I cannot say. This old body has seen more combat than most. I suppose I am very lucky to still be alive.''${PLAYER}, it has been long since we last spoke. I was unable to ride with the rest of my brethren into battle for it took longer than expected to depart. I can assure you that Beaconwatch is safe in my absence though.

'I expected to make good time on the ride south, only to be thwarted by a group of Uruk-hai. I believe they were tracking the rest of the riders so I diverted my path from theirs to throw them off the trail.

'I rode into battle towards the end, and did my best to take out as many Orcs as I could.''Hm... that yielded less than I had hoped. No matter. Can I rely on you to find those still missing or presumed dead?

'Let me think a moment on what must be done.''Thank you again for your assistance. I see everyone here preparing for a march to the east. I want to join them on this journey and help where I can.''I thought I was done for out there. I could only think about how I had let my family down. Now I have been given another chance. I will follow Aragorn to the Black Gate. Let Gondor take the offensive against these Mordor foes.''I still cannot believe that Forlong and Hirluin are both dead. These are hard, hard times for Gondor.''Surely it does not surprise you that I stood at my post until the very last, when you came for me? This great City I cherish and would defend with my life. It will be hard to leave it behind if I march with you. I will do as Aragorn commands, though.''It is good to see some of the men of Gondor whom we feared lost returned to us... even as my heart is heavy with those we know now to be dead.

'It is time we turned our efforts to the Rohirrim unaccounted for. I have spoken with Lord - I should say King Éomer and have the names of those you should seek.''It is a sad day. Many of the finest warriors I have known are slain. I take heart, however, that they live on in their descendents and their heroic deeds. May both go on for many generations to come.''I tried my hardest to bring Herefara and Herubrand back to the City. Their deaths at the hands of Gothmog's Orcs was a cruel and unwelcome demise. May I repay you many times over for your assistance out there, ${PLAYER}.''The dead and missing we sought are all accounted for, it seems. I thank you for your assistance in this matter. It is of great importance that the men who fought and died here receive all the honour and diligence that Gondor can grant them.'Aragorn has asked you to find Dervorin and Rossaran, both presumed to be missing in combat.Search for Dervorin and Rossaran on the after-battle Pelennor.Find DervorinFind RossaranAragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.

You should return to Aragorn now that Dervorin and Rossaran are found.Talk to Aragorn'Dervorin, son of Borhador, and Rossaran, a Swan-knight under Imrahil's command, are unaccounted for. You should search for them at once.''Thank the stars. It is good to see you. Though I am pinned, I do not believe my leg is broken. If you would assist me, I should be able to make my way back.''You appeared just in time. These Haradrim refused to surrender and, wearied as I am, I fear I might not have handled them on my own.

'I must see my wife Bruidis again. It is what keeps me going. I shall meet you back at the pavilion, my friend.''Both Dervorin and Rossaran are safely returned. I have seen them with my own two eyes. How relieved I am!'Help identify the bodies of Duilin and Derufin among those recovered from the field.You should speak with Duinhir, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to DuinhirSearch among the slain for Duilin and Derufin's bodies.Identify DuilinIdentify DerufinAragorn can be found in his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.

You should return to Aragorn now that you have identified Duilin and Derufin.Talk to Aragorn'Many corpses have been recovered from the field, some nearly beyond recognition. I fear that Duilin and Derufin, who were trampled by a Mûmak, may be among them. Would you ask Duinhir if he is willing to identify his sons?''I thank you, ${PLAYER}. I understand that it was a difficult task, but you have shown both discretion and courtesy in seeing it through.'You gently explain that Aragorn has asked Duinhir to identify his sons' bodies.

'I cannot. I have seen so much death. To see theirs... You came to know them well in these last days, did you not? Will you go in my stead?'Aragorn has asked you to find Elfmar, Harding, and Torferth, all presumed to be missing in combat.Elfmar, Harding, Torferth were last seen somewhere on the Pelennor Fields. Look for them there, after the battle.Find ElfmarFind HardingFind TorferthYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Aragorn'Éomer has informed me that Elfmar, Harding, and Torferth are all missing. While they were all seen on the battlefield, none have reported in to Éomer since we established victory. Find them quickly. I am counting on you.''This is grim indeed. Such great lives lost to evil that lies just beyond those mountains. That is why we march, ${CLASS}. Not just for Gondor, but for Elfmar, Harding, Torferth, and all that fell to the darkness of Mordor.'Aragorn has asked you to find Forlong, Golasgil, and Hirluin, all presumed to be missing in combat.Search for Golasgil and Hirluin on the after-battle Pelennor.Find GolasgilFind HirluinSearch for Forlong on the after-battle Pelennor.Find ForlongForlong lies dying on the after-battle Pelennor.

Blow Forlong's horn to summon Thorongil.Blow Forlong's hornYou should talk to Aragorn, who stands by Forlong on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Aragorn'Forlong, Golasgil, and Hirluin all were lost in the tempest of yesterday's combat. What befell them is unknown, though I fear the worst for Forlong, who was last seen charging at full fury towards a line of Sûhalar.

'Please search for them along the wreckage on the Pelennor.''The Enemy were everywhere. I did my best to fend them off but I was separated from my allies. I was able to hide here and lose them after I fended off a party of Orcs who tried to ambush me. 

'You say it is safe to return now? I will go.''I thank you. I bid my old friend a last farewell, too late and yet just in time. I have this memory now, and I shall hold it close to my heart always.''My friend, I am dying. But you could see that for yourself, I suppose. Ah, the good times... the adventures. What I wouldn't give for one more draught of that wine...'

Forlong coughs and tries to laugh through the pain.

'Ah, my friend. Forget wine. Would that I could see Thorongil once more. I would swear... ugh! You must forgive me. I would swear I saw him upon the field of battle beneath the banner of the king. What delusions come upon us when our deaths are nigh!

'And yet, if it were him and he had returned in the hour of glory. Here, take my horn. If Thorongil truly is returned, he will know its sound. He will come. I... ugh! I am sure of it.'Aragorn has asked you to find Ingold and Turgon, both presumed to be missing in combat.Search for Ingold and Turgon on the after-battle Pelennor.Find IngoldFind TurgonAragorn can be found in his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.

You should return to Aragorn now that you have found Ingold and Turgon.Talk to Aragorn'Ingold, Captain of the Out-wall, and Turgon, Captain of the South-gate, both remain missing. Imrahil felt sure they had retreated into the City before the start of the battle, but now it seems it was not so. You must add their names to those you seek upon the Pelennor.''You have come to assist me in defending the wall? Small Orc groups still linger in pockets. There is much to be done! Why do you stand there? Have you something to say?'

You explain to Ingold that he has been missed and should return to Aragorn's pavilion.

'I will go at once. Surely there I shall find others who will join me in wiping out every last threat to the Rammas wall.''Ingold has returned, but what of Turgon?'

You tell Aragorn that Turgon was slain.

'Ah, I see. This is grievous news. I have heard much of his heroic deeds at the South-gate and all he did to ensure my safe passage in the fields.'Aragorn has asked you to find the bodies of many Rohirrim who fell in combat, and to search for Nothmar, who was last seen making towards the city.Grimbold, Déorwine, Dúnhere, Guthláf, Herefara, and Herubrand died on the Pelennor. Nothmar is missing.

Search for the valiant Rohirrim on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle.Find GrimboldFind DéorwineFind DúnhereFind GuthláfFind HerefaraFind HerubrandFind NothmarYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Aragorn'Éomer has provided me a list of names of those known Rohirrim who were slain by the enemy on the Pelennor.'

You explain that you saw Nothmar on the Pelennor with Herefara and Herubrand.

'It seems that Nothmar is still missing. We thought he was in the city but word has come back that he never made it. Please look for him while you are out there. He may yet still be alive.''I tried to make it to the city with Herefara and Herubrand. Their deaths were heavy upon me. Slain by foul Orcs! I am hurt, my ankle twisted. I can walk but do not have the strength to carry my friends any further. I did not want to leave their side; not with Orcs roaming about. Thank you for coming and helping finish this task I set out to accomplish.''I am glad to hear that Nothmar is safe and that his wounds are not serious. The Rohirrim are great warriors. We will need as many as we can muster in the coming days to both protect the city and march with us to the Black Gate.'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Complete Volume IV, Book 8: The Black GateReach Level 1 with the Allegiance: The Court of Lothlórien.Reach Level 1 with the Allegiance: The Court of LothlórienThe Wainriders have claimed the hill of Dol Acharn, but they must be challenged if you are to stand between them and the Host of the West.Dol Acharn can be found in eastern Dagorlad.

Faramir has asked you to approach the hill to confirm his suspicions about the Wainriders. You should scout the hill carefully.Attempt to approach the hill-top of Dol AcharnFaramir can be found due west of Dol Acharn in Dagorlad.

You attempted to reach the hill-top of Dol Acharn but found your efforts repelled by an unseen force that sapped your will to press onward. You should return to Faramir and tell him of what you have experienced.Talk to Faramir near Dol Acharn'Your friends can rest easy for the moment, ${CLASS}, but rest shall not soon come to me.

'Even in this form beyond death, I have done naught to stop the countless horrors I have witnessed, and I can bear it no longer. This fallen man of Númenor, Burudagath, perverts the banner of my father and kills without mercy... and the Wainriders that rose in answer to the strife in these lands have slain the men of your company with fear alone. These two foes stand in defiance of Gondor on the hills of Dagorlad... and there remains no force to stop them.

'Yet, I believe that I have found a means to set our foes upon each other.

'However, such a ruse demands swaying the attention of the Wainriders... and that shall be no simple task.''It is as I feared... it seems only the Wainriders themselves can stand upon the hill without succumbing to fear.

'I had hoped you would not encounter such resistance from the Wainriders before even confronting them, but it seems our cause grows more desperate.

'I may know a way to allow you to travel onto Dol Acharn without hindrance, but it shall not be an easy task.'Mílgamel is concerned with a decaying corpse of one of the animals brought in from the wilds. She believes Cair Andros may hold the key.Phials of poison can be found on Uruks and Orcs in Cair Andros.

You should collect phials of poison.Collect phials of viscous poison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect phials of refined poison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A workbench can be found at Henneth Annûn.

You should bring the phials of poison to Henneth Annûn for study.Study the phials of refined poison at Henneth AnnûnA workbench can be found at Henneth Annûn.

You should bring the phials of poison to Henneth Annûn for study.Study the phials of viscous poison at Henneth AnnûnMílgamel can be found at Henneth Annûn.

You should take the poisons and what you have learned to her.'The Rangers brought back a mangled animal corpse from the wilds. It was struck with an arrow of Orkish design.

'The peculiar thing is not the arrow, but the state of the animal's body. The corpse is sickened and in a rapid state of decay. The Rangers say the ground surrounding the animal was devoid of flora.

'This is all very concerning. Perhaps it was unwise to pass Cair Andros by, after all. The forces from Mordor at Cair Andros must be coating their arrows with something most vile. Something not seen upon the Pelennor Battlefield (or else I would recognize it), and therefore, perhaps, concocted here in North Ithilien! It is not why Master Galathir sent me, or an inquiry he would approve of, but I must know what this substance is.

'I shall not accompany you to Cair Andros, as my lack of skill in combat would only slow you down - and endanger myself - but I beseech you, go and gather what you can of this poison, so we may study it.''A moss you say? That is no lichen of which I ever heard! And so my wonderment grows, and I find myself drawn to stray from the confining course Master Galathir has set for me. Yet if I do all he asks - then what study I make beyond it is no concern of his, do you not agree?'

She meets your eye with a new boldness in hers.

'Let us suppose for a moment that this grey lichen is most deadly and is the main ingredient used in making the poison. Indeed, I recall that I have read of poisonous mosses before. It would not be a stretch. And if we suppose, as well, that the lichen grows native somewhere within these lands east of the Anduin, there is hope we may learn more about it.'The flowers and herbs of Ithilien have many potent medicinal uses, and gathering them would aid the Host of the West as well as the wounded of Gondor and Rohan.Lush oxlip, horsetail, and vetchling can be found nearby Ereblen in north-western Ithilien.

Ereblen has asked you to gather lush oxlip, horsetail, and vetchling, so that you might learn more of their uses.Collect lush horsetail (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect lush oxlip (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect lush vetchling (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ereblen can be found to the west of Henneth Annûn.

You have harvested many of Ithilien's flowers and herbs, and you should now return to Ereblen.'In the wake of the great battle, the healers of Gondor and Rohan alike are strained and their stores will soon run low if we do not help replenish them.

'Gondor has long been a source of various remedies and tinctures, and nearly all of them through the use of the flowers and herbs that grow in Ithilien. This task has not often fallen to the Rangers in recent years, but the need is great now, and we must all do our part to ease the ills of the wounded.

'Among the most common of Ithilien's herbs and flowers are oxlip, horsetail, and vetchling. Each can be ground into a beneficial extract that can then be combined into powerful medicines by skilled healers.

'Search nearby for the lushest of these plants and bring them to me. Once you have gathered them, return to me and we can speak on how to harvest their extracts.''Excellent work, my friend. You have gathered them just as swiftly as I'd hoped! With a careful hand, you can grind these flowers into useful extracts. Here...'

Ereblen takes the bundles from you, and begins to grind them in a small mortar.

'There are many plants in the gardens of Ithilien, and some are much rarer than the rest. However, all of them are of great worth to healers of Gondor, so look closely and harvest as many as you can as you explore these lands.

'Now then, there are a few among our number that have been tasked to make swift trips to the White City. If you give them the phials you have collected, they may be able to offer you something of use in return. Our swift-riders can be found at the Cross-roads to the south, in Henneth Annûn, and far to the north among our camps on the border of Dagorlad. Your aid could make a tremendous difference in the aftermath of the great battle, so I would urge you to bring those phials to them as soon as you are able.'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Barter vendors for extract phials can be found at the Cross-roads, Henneth Annûn, and Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.</rgb>There is much to be done in the Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha.The Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha is located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills.

You should defeat Haradrim look-outs and half-troll executioners.Enter the enemy encampment of Dûm BohaThe Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha is located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills.

You should defeat Haradrim look-outs and half-troll executioners.Defeat Haradrim look-outs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat half-troll executioners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated many Haradrim look-outs and half-troll executioners.CompletedHalf-trolls and look-outs are gathered in Dûm Boha in great number. They seem to be waiting for something. Defeat enough of them to throw their plans into disarray.You have defeated many foes gathered at Dûm Boha. This will surely throw the Haradrim into disarray and give the Host of the West a better chance of making it to the Black Gate.Aragorn learns of a group of the Enemy, camped inside the island fortress of Cair Andros.Duinhir and soldiers of Gondor can be found at the Host of the West encampment, on the border of North Ithilien and Dagorlad.

You should speak to some of those who have expressed concern with marching to the Black Gate.Speak to Duinhir at the Host of the West encampmentSpeak to a scared warriorSpeak to the uncertain warriorSpeak to the injured warriorAragorn can be found at the Host of the West encampment, on the border of North Ithilien and Dagorlad.

You should speak with Aragorn.Speak with Aragorn at the Host of the West encampmentDuinhir can be found at the Host of the West encampment, on the border of North Ithilien and Dagorlad.

You should speak with Duinhir.Speak with DuinhirDamrod can be found to the north-east of Cair Andros at Caladuil.

You should speak to Damrod.Speak with DamrodCair Andros is an island fortress in the Anduin River, bordering North Ithilien and Talath Anor.

You should scout the entrance of Cair Andros.Scout the entrance of Cair AndrosDuinhir can be found near Cair Andros.

You should speak to Duinhir.Speak with Duinhir near Cair Andros'${PLAYER}, might I speak with you one moment? As we have passed through Ithilien, I look at these men and I see a horror growing behind their eyes. As we rest upon the border of Dagorlad, I have heard whispers of those unable to carry on, of those unable to move or bear arms.

'I ask of you, seek out these men, and speak with them. Find what it is that stricken them so. I fear the closeness of Mordor is enough to bring most men to a halt.''Aragorn asks of me to lead the assault on Cair Andros? You know that I would do as he asks, and I shall do this for him as well. I shall see to it that Cair Andros returns to Gondor. I will lead these men to see that they do not die, that they see their loved ones again. Blackroot Vale shall not be a place of shame, but a place of heroic memories, befitting for the likes of Duilin and Derufin.

'If you are to join us, I shall arrange for the ranger Damrod to guide us through the lands south-west of here. Let us depart soon. You may want to speak with Damrod when we arrive near the island fortress.''Did you pass through Cormallen as the rest of us did? The beauty of the area certainly renewed the spirits in these faint-hearted men.

'We are close to Cair Andros now. Would you mind scouting the entrance to see what these men are up against? Report back to Duinhir for I must return north-east. I hope that we shall see each other again soon. Good luck.''I see, these are young men with little time in battle, farmers who till the land, longing for their loved-ones, and those who still grieve amongst all the bloodshed they have witnessed.'

Aragorn looks around the encampment with gazing eyes that are both commanding yet full of pity.

'Men, listen to me. If you are not able to tread further, then go! I ask of you on this day, keep your honour and do not run! Instead, make way south-west for Cair Andros. It is still held by the Enemy. Lessen any shame, retake the island fortress, and hold it to the very last!'

The men understand and nod. Aragorn turns back to you and speaks in a softer tone.

'Many of these men who depart are not leaders, nor could I ever ask them to lead. Duinhir however, is a lord. You are Duinhir's friend. Speak with him and see if he is willing to lead these men to Cair Andros for me. You may assist him, if you wish, but I need you back here as soon as you are able.''Alas, my friend, I can not bring myself to look past the deaths of my sons. I know their recklessness saved us in battle. I know that if they had not learned how to take down the Mûmakil, we would not be standing here today. Still, it pains me so to see such potential lost for all time. I can not keep going, knowing that my death would certainly be the undoing of my dear Rosfin.''Brave ${RACE}, I have only heard of Mordor in tales from my mother, to keep me out of trouble, when I was a young lad. I am not much older now, as you can see. I am frightened, to be honest.''I am just a farmer from Lossarnach. I know the land, not war. If I pick up my sword, I will surely perish here.''The wind sweeping down the cliffs sounds of voices. I can not sleep for Mordor taunts me. The hand of death, ever reaching out towards me. My legs refuse to move out from Ithilien. Once we cross the border, my time of this world is at an end. I am sorry.''The entrance is heavily guarded. I suppose we shall need to be as stealthy as we can be before a full-on assault is possible.'With the Host of the West on the march, Angbor has been given orders to mend the Statue of the Fallen King.You should talk to Arandol, who can be found by the statue at the after-battle Cross-roads.Talk to ArandolThe statue is at the after-battle Cross-roads.

You should remove the Orkish poles placed around the Statue of the Fallen King.The statue is at the after-battle Cross-roads.

You should break the defiled head upon the Statue of the Fallen King.Break the defiled statue headThe statue is at the after-battle Cross-roads.

You should retrieve the original head of the Statue of the Fallen King.Retrieve the statue's original headThe statue is at the after-battle Cross-roads.

You should place the original head upon the Statue of the Fallen King.You should talk to Arandol, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.Talk to Arandol'When you are able, speak with Arandol near the Statue of the Fallen King. He is in charge of the statue repairs and will be able to put you to work in assisting our efforts here.''Yes, I am Arandol. As you can see, the repairs are behind schedule. Orcs have defiled the statue, removed the head, and scrawled unintelligible markings all over it.

'First those Orkish poles will need to be removed, then that vile head must come down. If you are able, the statue's original head should be retrieved and placed back atop its shoulders.'You completed all those tasks? One alone would have put us ahead of schedule! Perhaps we shall be allowed to march on from this place, thanks to you!'With the Host of the West on the march, Angbor has been given orders to mend the Statue of the Fallen King.Suitable stone can be found in and around after-battle Osgiliath. Suitable water can be found along the Anduin nearby.

You should collect some stone for mending the Statue of the Fallen King and water for washing away the scrawls and filth.Collect suitable stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect clean water (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should talk to Arandol, who  can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.The statue is at the after-battle Cross-roads.

You should clean the Gondorian posts around the Statue of the Fallen King.Clean Gondorian posts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The statue is at the after-battle Cross-roads.

You should clean the Statue of the Fallen King.You should talk to Arandol, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.Talk to ArandolYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the Cross-roads.Talk to Angbor'There is still much to be done before this statue is repaired. Our workers are in need of some good stone to fill the cracks. Would you retrieve some for us? You should be able to find suitable stones in Osgiliath, along the banks of the Anduin.

'While you are at the river's edge, you might also take up some good water, with which to clean these foul scrawlings off the statue.''Ah, the statue has come along nicely. I am certain you were a great help and an example to the men.''These stones will do nicely. You have a keen eye. I will give them to the builders. If you would not mind, use some of that water you collected to clean the posts around the Cross-roads. Then use the remaining water to clean the scrawls from the statue itself.''Look at that. It were as if the army of the Enemy never laid hands upon the statue! Please let Angbor know that we are nearly finished here and might march with the Host of the West when they depart. I thank you again for you help.'The hill once known as Ondoher's Folly has been fortified into a horrific shrine of the Enemy where Orcs torture and kill their prisoners.Orcs can be found throughout Ondoher's Folly in north-western Dagorlad.

Laeglaw has asked you to assault the hill of Ondoher's Folly and defeat the Orcs who have claimed it.Defeat Orcs at Ondoher's Folly (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Laeglaw can be found due north of Haerondir at Tham Durlan.

You have defeated many of the Orcs at Ondoher's Folly and should now return to Laeglaw.Talk to Laeglaw at Tham Durlan'What did the Ranger make of that missive, ${PLAYER}?'

You inform Laeglaw that Faltor-shík translates to "the Fane of Screaming" and what Mincham takes that to mean. His face is aghast for a moment, but he is able to summon his words once more.

'The Fane of Screaming... is this truly the name they have bestowed upon the site of our king's fall? If the Orcs sought to provoke us through insults, I shall let them consider this a victory... but it will be their last.

'It has been long since we moved against the Orcs in the Wastes directly, and I believe it likely an assault would catch them by surprise. I no longer doubt your place among the Rangers, my friend, for you have done much to aid my company and I trust that you would do so again.

'For the sake of our king's memory and for the fallen, ride to Ondoher's Folly and put an end to those Orcs!''Once those Orcs are gone, I would much like to study the location of King Ondoher's fall.

'Steward Denethor's dream has come to pass through the leader of this Host, but I wonder yet why Ondoher's banner came so clearly to his mind.''You have done well, my friend.

'With this accomplished, the Orcs at Ondoher's Folly should no longer pose a threat to the Host of the West or to any that still remain in their thrall.

'Let us hope it was enough, ${PLAYER}.'Although the Wastes have long laid desolate, Mílgamel holds hope that these barren lands can again be restored to their long-vanished beauty.The planting boxes can be found near Mílgamel in Haerondir.

Mílgamel has asked you to plant the flowers and herbs she carried from Ithilien in the soil of Dagorlad you brought to Haerondir. She also wishes for you to re-plant the mushrooms in the soil.Plant Mílgamel's plants and the mushroom samples in the soil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mílgamel can be found at Haerondir.

You have planted the various mushrooms and herbs in the soil you gathered and should now speak to Mílgamel.Talk to Mílgamel at HaerondirMílgamel is at Haerondir.

Mílgamel has added a splash of the slag-water to one of the planting boxes, and has asked you to wait with her and observe the results.Wait with MílgamelMílgamel can be found at Haerondir.

The slag-water ruptured the planting box and dripped into the soil at Haerondir. You should speak to Mílgamel.Talk to Mílgamel'That's right, ${PLAYER}... we are going to try to cross-breed the plants of the Wastes with those of Ithilien.

'Even if the Wastes never recover, we can save their unique plants and grow them within Ithilien if they are of need to us.

'I have set three planting boxes around this chamber, and I would first have you fill half of them with soil you gathered from the battle plain. I have already filled one half of each with soil from Ithilien. Next, you should plant my samples of Oxlip, Vetchling, and Horsetail alongside these hardy mushrooms you discovered.

'This way we shall see if they can live alongside one another in each variety of soil.

'I may still have a use for the slag-water you brought me, but that can wait...''Ah, wonderful!

'Now then, I'll add a splash of this sickly water you brought to one of them and we can observe the results.'

Mílgamel walks to the central planting box and upends the phial of slag-water.

'There! Now let us see what happens...''Ah, perhaps a minute was too long! Look, the slag-water has eaten right through the planting box...

'The others do not appear to have had such a reaction, though, and that is heartening.

'I do not know if the Wastes can ever truly be healed, but I am certain they cannot while the Enemy still looms ahead. Go, rejoin your company. I shall tend to these and see them safely transported away from these lands.

'If you ever find yourself in Minas Tirith again after this war, I am certain I shall have much to tell you!'An Orc captain remains on the Pelennor, determined to fight to the last and bring as many Men down with him as he can.Shumug can be found roaming the after-battle Pelennor.

You should find and defeat the Orc captain Shumug.Defeat ShumugYou should talk to Éomer, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.Talk to Éomer'We fought and we died on this field, the men of Rohan and Gondor. We fought and by some great miracle seized the day from the arms of an overwhelming foe. 

'But the battle is finished and it is a new dawn, so how is it that some foes linger yet upon the Pelennor? I have received word of one Orc captain who seems bent on fighting to the last, taking as many of our men as he can with him. I am weary of death, ${PLAYER}. Will you find this captain and put an end to him?''This is good news you bring. No more battle-weary men shall die by the hands of Shumug. I commend you, brave ${CLASS}.'Narthavron, master smith of the Noldor, has a proposition for you. For your help in purging the corruption of this land, he will craft powerful equipment for you.High-enchanters can be found in many camps around Gorgoroth, including the Udûn Foothold.

Purchase the Flame of Ancalamír from one of the High-enchanters.Purchase the Flame of Ancalamír from one of the High-enchantersFinnoth Sharp-wind can be found at the Udûn Foothold.

You should talk to Finnoth Sharp-wind.Talk to Finnoth Sharp-windYou can purchase the Flame of Ancalamír from one of the High Enchanters.

Use the Flame of Ancalamír to reduce the Morgul-steel Dagger to Motes of Enchantment.Use the Flame of Ancalamír to disenchant the Morgul-steel DaggerNarthavron can be found in the Udûn Foothold.

You should talk to Narthavron.Talk to Narthavron'Did you feel the change in the wind upon crossing the Black Gate, ${PLAYER}? Everything in this accursed land is tainted. The earth, the water, even the air.

'Allow me to introduce myself. I am Narthavron, master smith of the Noldor. I was present when the Last Alliance broke into this valley and defeated Sauron's army. I was filled with sorrow and anger seeing the atrocities they had committed here, and have made it my life's work to find a way to purge the corruption. I now believe I have the right tool to achieve this.

'I have recovered one of the adamants of old, the Flame of Ancalamír. It will unravel many items throughout Middle-earth into different components that I have named "Embers of Enchantment", "Figments of Splendour", and "Motes of Enchantment". What do you think? I thought those names might help bring a little more light into this dark place. Anyway, after I break the objects down, I am then able to use some of those components to fashion extraordinary equipment. I have a feeling you will be instrumental in the Conquest of Gorgoroth, and as such will be encountering many of these special items in your travels. I have a proposition for you.

'I will allow you use of the Flame. My assistants, the High-enchanters, will help you. You need only touch one of these objects to the Flame and it will be reduced to one of these components.  I believe that dwarf over there has been scavenging through the Orcs' forges. Perhaps he is willing to let go of something for this purpose. Find a piece of equipment, touch it to the Flame, and then return to me.''Aye, the Elf's right. I am seeking anything of value that might have been left behind. The Orcs were churning out thousands of blades and armour pieces from these forges, but most of them are foul Morgul-steel. Nothing I want anything to do with!

'Here, take this dagger I found. It's worthless to me! And tell that Elf he's better off leaving this sort of thing to the dwarves!''The Flame of Ancalamír has performed as expected, then? Excellent.

'In your travels, should you find equipment for which you have no use, I ask that you destroy it with the Flame and give the results to one of my assistants. They will reward you with powerful items of my own making, free from the foulness of this land.

'Good luck, and safe travels, friend.'Anborn recalls the tense exchange when the gangrel-creature came unbidden to the Forbidden Pool beneath Henneth Annûn.Anborn can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.

Anborn has offered to tell you more of the Halflings that passed through Ithilien.Listen to Anborn's taleAnborn can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.

You have listened to Anborn's tale and should now ask if he knows more of the Halflings.Talk to Anborn in Henneth Annûn'Do you wish to hear more of my tale?

'We returned from the battle with the Haradrim, and Faramir spoke long with the Halflings. He seemed convinced by their tale, and agreed to invite them into the sanctuary of Henneth Annûn. They spoke quietly as we walked through the woods, beyond our hearing, and more yet once we reached the cave.

'It was my duty to scout the way, and it was then that I saw the gangrel-creature. I took it to be some wretched squirrel or shadow-creature out of Mirkwood, but I did not shoot it, for Faramir does not permit the needless slaying of beasts.

'I told Faramir what I saw, and the Halflings listened with interest. Then I went out to guard.''Do you wish to hear more, ${PLAYER}?''I led the creature back to Henneth Annûn, but kept him under guard as Lord Faramir commanded.

'We did not yet know the Halflings' purpose in Ithilien, but the gangrel-creature had committed a serious offence in the eyes of the Rangers, and he had to answer for it.

'I have but a small bit more to tell, ${PLAYER}. When you wish it, I shall share the ending of the tale with you.'In the absence of the Rangers of Ithilien during the Battle of the Pelennor Fields, North Ithilien has been overrun with the forces of the Enemy.Orcs and Easterlings can be found throughout North Ithilien.

Orcs and Easterlings pose a grave threat to the Rangers of Ithilien and the Host of the West. You should defeat them to aid in the protection of Gondor's lands.Defeat Orcs and Easterlings in North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many Orcs and Easterlings in North Ithilien.CompletedWhile adventuring in North Ithilien, you have come upon many of the Enemy's forces in the old ruins of North Ithilien and in the foot-hills of the Ephel Dúath.

The Enemy's forces suffered a setback in Gondor, but the Dark Lord is far from bested.

You should defeat the Enemy's forces in North Ithilien and make clear the way for the Host of the West.You have defeated many of the Enemy's forces in North Ithilien and made clear the way for the Host of the West.

While their numbers will likely return in time, you have routed them for the moment.The healers have brought Aragorn some kingsfoil, and now he hopes to use it to heal the wounded.Aragorn is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Aragorn in the High Hall of the Houses of HealingAragorn is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Aragorn and assist him with healing the woundedGandalf is inside the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, located on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.Talk to Gandalf in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing'It seems that folk have been ransacking their cupboards and closets in search of a flowering weed, ${PLAYER}. Do you know anything about this?

'If you speak with Aragorn in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, perhaps he can tell you if enough was found.''I have come from the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, and I am sworn to keep secret the goings-on within. But I can tell you that your presence is requested!''I am weary, but there is no time to rest. Time is short for each of them, but for Faramir most of all.''Those Aragorn has seen to will heal, in time. Now he will attend the hurts of the others that rest in these Houses of Healing, and only then will he return to his pavilion outside the city.

'These wounded are fortunate indeed that Aragorn came to this city, and that Ioreth remembered that doggerel from her youth. The hands of a healer, indeed!

'For now, our friends must rest. But it is good to know that they will recover from their hurts and be themselves once again.''It seems that folk have been ransacking their cupboards and closets in search of a flowering weed, ${PLAYER}. Do you know anything about this?

'If you speak with Aragorn in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, perhaps he can tell you if enough was found.''I have come from the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, and I am sworn to keep secret the goings-on within. But I can tell you that your presence is requested!''Some kingsfoil has been found, but it remains to be seen if it will be enough. I may need someone to help me as I move from bedside to bedside, ${PLAYER}. Will you be that ${RACE}?'Minas Tirith's healers are overwhelmed by the number of wounded soldiers in need of care.The Houses of Healing can be found in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Go to the High Hall, House of Remedies, or House of Rest and tend to patients.Attend to patients (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ioreth can be found in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

You should let Ioreth know that you have treated many patients, although there were some possessed of a strange ailment you were unable to treat.Return to Ioreth'You there, idle hands! Are you well and able? Then why, I should like to know, are you standing about? There are soldiers, grievously wounded, in every one of the Houses of Healing and scant few healers to attend to them. Not enough by half!

'Why, has the sun ever shined on a slower wit? Go. Make the rounds. Help attend to those who need attending to!''What is that? You've gone the rounds and treated some of the wounded? I knew there was a fine head on those shoulders the moment I saw you!

'Now, about this malady that will not be healed.... You are not the first who has spoken of it, nor, I fear, the last. Into deep slumber they fall, colder and colder. What will come of it, I cannot say. Nothing good, that much is clear.'Mablung, Captain of the Rangers of Ithilien, would like you to find the source of the howling sound that has been bothering the men in the Camp of the Host.He thought it sounded like it was coming from the hills to the west of the Camp of the Host, in the Noman-lands.

Mablung has asked you to find the source of the howling sound.Find the source of the howling soundThe source of the howling sound was actually an injured hound.

You should find a way to calm the injured hound.<rgb=#FF00FF>Calm</rgb> the frightened houndMablung can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.

The hound has returned to the Camp of the Host. You should return to Mablung and tell him of your success.Return to MablungMablung would like you to work with Faroth to complete quests in the Noman-lands.

If you should get separated from your hound, blow the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.Complete quest 'Sniff Them Out' with FarothComplete quest 'Hidden Dangers' with FarothMablung would like you to work with Faroth to complete quests in the Noman-lands.

If you should get separated from your hound, blow the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.Complete quest 'Stalker of the Scrublands' with FarothMablung can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.

Now that Faroth's work in the Noman-lands is finished, you should return to Mablung.Talk to MablungFaroth deserves some praise from all his hard work! Why don't you give him a pat?

If you should get separated from your hound, blow the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.<rgb=#FF00FF>Pat</rgb> Faroth because he's a good dogTalk with Faroth to part ways for now.

If you should get separated from your hound, blow the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.Say good-bye to Faroth'Did you hear that, ${PLAYER}? That howling sound has been spooking the horses and making the men uneasy.

'We have not yet located the wretched beast, but I know I would like to see the noise ended. The more sleep we get before the march, the better.

'Let me know if you find it while you're out in the Noman-lands. It sounded as if it was coming from the hills west of here.'You have found the source of the howling sound! It's not a fearsome beast at all, but a scared and possibly injured hound. Does he belong to the Rangers?

You should try to calm it down and then return to Mablung.'Very good! You two have completed all the work I have for you this day. Faroth has proved himself quite capable, hasn't he? He deserves some praise!''So this was the source of the howling. Ah, Faroth, old boy! When you went missing, we thought you were gone for good.'

Mablung looks closely at the hound. 

'He must have run afoul of those Orkish traps. It must have been a lucky scrape, for he is well on better already. I think he will be on the look-out for those from now on!

'In truth, I have work for this little Ranger. He has taken a liking to you, it seems. Perhaps you would go with him on his rounds in the Noman-lands, ${PLAYER}?'Faroth looks up at you happily. It seems he enjoys life as a Ranger hound!In his time wandering the Wastes, Faramir has learned the identity of the true master of Ondoher's Folly: a vile Black Númenórean bearing a perverted banner of Gondor.The cage-waggons can be found to the south-east of Ondoher's Folly.

Faramir has asked you to dismantle the cage-waggons making for Ondoher's Folly and free any slaves you encounter. He also hopes you can learn the identity of the true master of Ondoher's Folly.Damage wheels on Mordor cage-waggons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Free slaves from the cage-waggonsArtamir can be found to the south outside Ondoher's Folly in Dagorlad.

You damaged the cage-waggons and learned much of the master of Ondoher's Folly, but you were unable to rescue any slaves. You should return to Artamir and tell him what has happened.Talk to Artamir outside Ondoher's Folly'It is time you learned of the greatest insult dealt against me and my family...

'When my father fell on the hill above, his banner was paraded by the Wainriders and the Orcs as the rest of his company fell. Our foes chased them as they fled into the marshes, and for many years I saw naught of my father's heraldry.

'Not long ago, a man returned to the hill bearing the banner... but it had changed. Age had worn it thin, but what remained was perverted into something between the familiar and the horrid. With the banner unfurled, he called forth the first of the slaves the Orcs had captured in Ithilien... and one by one he tortured and beheaded them beneath my father's banner as the others watched. After all were slain, the bodies were defiled in such terrible ways... I cannot speak them.

'This man dishonours the memory of my father, Ondoher, and twists it to suit his own cruelty. His name is unknown to me, but the Orcs must know it well... for they avert their eyes in his presence.

'If you wish to aid me, learn what you can of this man and free the poor men that have fallen into his hands. The slaves and prisoners are drawn by cage-waggons to the hill along a rough pathway to the east.''So the banner of Ondoher did survive! What a shame that it has been used to such an end...''The Orcs slaughtered them in their cages... like beasts. How horrid...

'Our foe may be of Númenórean blood, but he is no man. Burudagath the Bloodletter... who would hold such a title willingly?

'If he is the true master of Ondoher's Folly, the Host of the West should remain vigilant. You slew so many at Ondoher's Folly, but still their numbers do not dwindle... and this Burudagath seems to hold sway over them all.

'Mincham learned from Orcs and evil Men that the Enemy wishes us to come to the Black Gate safely, but how can such words be trusted now?

'Ruse or not, my friend, I believe only one course remains.'Reach Level 1 with the Allegiance: The Kingdom of GondorReach Level 1 with the Allegiance: The Kingdom of GondorAs the last remaining refuge of the Rangers of Ithilien, the secrecy of Henneth Annûn has never been more critical to the continued presence of the Rangers in North Ithilien.Henneth Annûn can be found in north-central North Ithilien.

Mablung has asked you to patrol around the borders of Henneth Annûn for possible threats to the refuge.Mablung can be found in Henneth Annûn.

You have scouted the lands surrounding Henneth Annûn and should now report back to Mablung.Talk to Mablung'Our enemies have come closer to Henneth Annûn each day, and unless we act to keep them from it, we shall be discovered before long.

'There are many ways for our foes to approach Henneth Annûn, but thankfully, very few through which they could enter. I would have you scout the far reaches of Ithilien surrounding Henneth Annûn for any sign of our foes.

'Their whereabouts in Ithilien are mostly known to us, but they move deeper into the woods with each passing hour and we cannot chance them drawing too close, especially after Rhadrog's encounter with that troll...

'With our other refuges fallen, any task that draws us into Ithilien risks leading our foes back to the refuge. Go swiftly, and take care that you are not followed.

'I shall await a report upon your return.''I am relieved that our foes have not encroached any more closely, but I do not trust that we are free of them. They will come again, and we must be ready for them.

'Dornach means well, but I shall speak to him about using more caution while scouting. Even the slightest rustle can expose our position, and to be exposed means to be slain.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Find cairns marking a forgotten path through the Entwash.Find cairns marking a forgotten path through the Entwash.Find cairns in the EntwashAngbor receives word that it is time to march onward to North Ithilien.You should talk to Mablung, who can be found in after-battle Osgiliath.Talk to MablungYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.Talk to AngborYou should talk to Thurindol, who can be found in North Ithilien near the after-battle Cross-roads.Seek out Thurindol in North Ithilien'The road through North Ithilien will be difficult. We must rely on Lord Faramir's Rangers to lead us among those hills safely. Why don't you speak with Mablung in Osgiliath about this?''The Rangers of Ithilien are here to do our part in the march. You remember Thurindol, do you not? He has been scouting in North Ithilien for some time now. I have arranged for him to meet you near the Cross-roads. You are to travel with him ahead of the Host of the West.

'First, however, you should speak with Angbor and relay these plans.''Good, good! I am glad we shall have the Rangers for guides. Please go on ahead. I will remain here and make sure all our supplies and men are accounted for and ready to march. We shall meet again soon, I am sure of it.''${PLAYER}, thank you for meeting me here. Much has happened since you passed through South Ithilien. For our parts, we Rangers have ever moved, striking at the Enemy where we might. Bâr Húrin, alas, could not be defended and was lost. Men, too, we have lost, but I shall not dwell on that now.

'Come, we have much to discuss if we are to shepherd an army through the lands of North Ithilien.'Aragorn hopes there are still Rangers of Ithilien hidden within Osgiliath who could help guide his army on their northward march.Search for Rangers of Ithilien within after-battle Osgiliath.Search for Rangers in OsgiliathGladhir, Mírthel, and Arodor can be found at the main Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.

You should speak with the other Rangers.Talk to ArodorTalk to GladhirTalk to MírthelYou should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the main Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.Talk to Mablung'${PLAYER}, we are to march shortly. Is it true, as I have heard, that you are known to the Rangers of Ithilien? Will you search for any who might still hide among the ruins of Osgiliath? It is my hope that they might help guide us through Ithilien and on to the Black Gates of Mordor.''${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. When last we spoke, Osgiliath was lost to the Enemy and war was at the doorsteps of Minas Tirith. We have watched the tides of battle turn from atop the Dome of Stars. We slew coward Orcs as they fled the battle, attempting to take shelter in the ruins. 

'But tell me, what word do you bring out of the White City? Why came you here?'

You tell Mablung of the battle and Aragorn's plans to march to the Black Gate.

'If this is the path they will march, then there is much to be done here in Osgiliath first. But before we speak of those matters, talk to the other Rangers here with me - Gladhir, Mírthel, and Arodor in particular. It has been too long and they will surely be glad to speak with you again.''Well met, ${PLAYER}! When I saw the darksome clouds finally give way, I shed my fears of the evils lurking in the Morgul Vale. I feel in my heart these great lands are not truly threatened any longer.''I still cannot thank you enough for rescuing me on your journeys. It seems the secret of my capture did not stay a secret for long. Many a good-natured jest has been made at my expense. Still, I have kept true to my oath and given my all to thwarting the Enemy at every turn.''It is good to have you back upon the eastern banks of the Anduin. It was my honour to scout events of the battle before Minas Tirith and report back to Mablung. Many of us wished to join the fray, but wisdom and discipline counseled we few would better serve Gondor here. And truly, many a hurried messenger and routed, retreating foe fell to our hands.''Now then, let us speak of securing Osgiliath. We have done much to sweep the foes from this place, but some remain. While they do, they are a threat to the rear flank of Aragorn's host, to the guard of Minas Tirith, and to my men here. To truly purge our enemies here, we will need your help, my friend.'With Osgiliath safe for passage, Mablung sends you on to assist Angbor at the Cross-roads.You should travel to the Cross-roads, which lie east of after-battle Osgiliath.Travel to the Cross-roadsYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.Talk to Angbor at the Cross-roadsView the statue at the after-battle Cross-roads.You should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.Talk to Angbor'A vanguard of Lord Aragorn's Host has passed through Osgiliath and gone on to the Cross-roads. Angbor, Lord of Lamedon, leads these men in securing that place and preparing the way. I deem it is an undertaking that will require many hands.''As you can see, the Orcs defiled the statue. It is hard work, restoring hope when you have none of your own. Would you help these men out, and raise their spirits as they restore the statue? What do you say?''Ah, ${PLAYER}, here we are, so close to the dreaded stronghold! If I did not have my orders from Lord Aragorn, I would march up to the gates of Minas Morgul and rap at the bars with my blade. Let them know fear for a change!

'That is how I feel, yet my men still tremble and seem downcast when they glance that way. Have I told you how, when I ousted the Haradrim from Lossarnach, not a single of my men died? It is true.

'Take a look at that statue up there. My men are restoring it rightfully to a symbol of hope.'Aragorn does not have time to identify and treat all the victims of the Black Shadow.Find patients suffering from the Black Shadow in the High Hall, House of Remedies, or House of Rest, and mark them for Aragorn.Aragorn stands in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.

Return to Aragorn and let him know that you have marked out those suffering from the Black Shadow.Return to Aragorn'There is not time, not time by half! I might treat all those suffering from the Black Shadow, but I fear I shall never find them before it is too late. 

'Will you go before me, ${PLAYER}, and lay a marker by all those afflicted? These are the signs: a deep slumber and cold to the touch. Attend closely and you shall know them. The speed that would grant me may well be the difference between life and death.''You have placed the markers? You are an irreplaceable ally, ${PLAYER}! I will be with them as swiftly as I am able.'With the claims of the Variags confirmed, Mablung has asked you to defeat the enemies hiding within the culverts of Osgiliath.The enemy hideout is in the culverts beneath the ruins of after-battle Osgiliath.

You should enter the culverts and find the enemy hideout.Search the culverts for the enemy hideoutThe raiding party hides in the culverts of after-battle Osgiliath.

You should defeat the Morgul raiding party.Defeat foes in the culverts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat KamábhilYou should return to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.Return to Mablung'Gladhir has just returned, and confirms that there are enemies hiding in a section of the culverts we had thought to be collapsed. The Variags were true to their word. I suppose it is up to us, then, to honour our half of the deal and let them pass unharmed through North Ithilien. I will send word.

'${PLAYER}, take to the culverts. Defeat the forces gathered there and make sure they do not have the strength to make trouble for the Host of the West.''Good work. You have helped us secure Osgiliath and made safe passage for the Host of the West. I commend your work.'Many useful supplies still exist within the First Circle of Minas Tirith and would be welcome by those who need it in the Houses of Healing.You should find and collect any loose supplies that you may come across in the First Circle of Minas Tirith.Collect supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The supply cart can be found near the City Stables in the First Circle of Minas Tirith.

