You should speak with Bregdal.Speak with Bregdal when next you meet'There are many of the Enemy encircling our hold on this ground. We must defeat some of them if we are to press on. Let us push through their numbers and break their rank!''Word from the Rohirrim captains is that we are pushing south! I am sure we will get separated, but perhaps we will fight together again upon this battlefield. Keep your wits about you, my friend!''${PLAYER}, I wish we could meet again under more ideal conditions. The tone is grim here and our forces dwindle. You must have heard of Théoden King's passing. If misery has a face, it is surely this battle. Still, we press on.'In the thick of battle upon the fields of Pelennor, Bregdal, Errand-rider of Gondor, hopes to assist you in any way he can.The Gloom of Nurn can be found in the Silent Street instance.Defeat the Gloom of NurnStay near Gandalf.Let events transpireGandalf and Peregrin Took can be found in the Silent Street instance.Speak with GandalfSpeak with Peregrin TookBregdal can be found at Kings' End.

You should speak with Bregdal.Speak with Bregdal at Kings' End'I have just gotten word that there is fighting within the city walls, and I have seen a fell-beast circle over the city! ${PLAYER}, you know the city much better than most. Take to Minas Tirith with what warriors you can muster. We must protect Denethor. If the line of Stewards breaks, all hope is lost for Gondor. I wish to stay here and fight by the side of the Men of Rohan. Quickly now!'

<rgb=#FF0000>It is recommended playing the Silent Street instance with a large fellowship. You can access the instance from the Instance Join panel.</rgb>'I shall make sure that Faramir sees safe passage from here to the Houses of Healing. ${PLAYER}, you are no doubt needed on the Pelennor. Make haste there, old friend!''So it has come to this. It saddens me to have seen his fall into madness. Denethor was a good man.''What is that, Denethor has burned himself alive?! What a terrible tragedy! I am glad that Faramir still lives, be it barely. Now let us hope his wounds can be healed so that the line of Stewards does not break!'In the thick of battle upon the fields of Pelennor, Bregdal, Errand-rider of Gondor, hopes to assist you in any way he can.The Enemy can be found at Kings' End, upon the fields of Pelennor.

