After accepting the quest "The Caretaker", you should shoo away the goats.Complete The CaretakerCompleted.CompletedThe enemy you just defeated was carrying strange machine parts. You ponder if there are more parts out there in Udûn, held by the enemies who still dwell near the forges.With the defeat of Búktavul the caretaker, perhaps it was best to not mess around with all the broken machines in Udûn. You never know what else could be lurking in the Gearworks.With the last machine repaired, it seems that nothing interesting has happened. Just then, you swear you hear the sound of goats off in the distance. Perhaps you should investigate.With all the machine parts you have gathered, there must be many machines in Udûn that are not working properly. Perhaps you should seek out these broken machines and try to repair them.Annoth desires to tell you the tale of his ancestors, the Thandrim, who kept watch on Mordor from fortresses within the Black Land for more than a thousand years.It is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Talk to Annoth during his recounting of the taleIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Listen to Annoth's account of the ThandrimIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Talk to Annoth during his recounting of the taleIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Listen to Annoth's account of the ThandrimIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Talk to Annoth during his recounting of the taleIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Listen to Annoth's account of the ThandrimIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Talk to Annoth during his recounting of the taleIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Listen to Annoth's account of the ThandrimIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.Talk to Annoth during his recounting of the tale'Now you know the tale.''I have heard tales of the bravery of the Thandrim for all my life: they were a shining light of Gondor's goodness, blazing within the shadows of Mordor. See them now, where they stand, defiant and bold!''Three only there are, but they are figures out of nightmare. Two are the beings we have come to know as the Nazgûl, the Ringwraiths of Sauron.

'The third may have been a Man, once, but through the foul sorceries of his master in the Dark Tower, he has become something else. He is Ugrukhôr, the Captain of the Pit. He comes now to Durthand with an offer.''Should they have refused? Every man there knew Ugrukhôr for a liar, but the pit of despair into which they had fallen could not be surmounted. They had been hardy men, once, but a year of starvation and fear must have taken its toll. No doubt their fear was made stronger by the presence of the Nazgûl, but I can understand the draw of even the faintest of hopes in that dark pit.

'The Thandrim surrendered to Ugrukhôr. Durthand was lost.''The Thandrim cast aside their weapons, and beneath Ugrukhôr's watchful gaze they march to the Morannon, now held by the Orcs. The gate opens. Sixty men, all that remained of the Thandrim, pass through the Gate.

'At a signal from Ugrukhôr, the archers on the walls fill the air with death.''That is the story of the Thandrim, ${PLAYER}. Only Halannon survived, and his account is kept in the archives of Minas Tirith. It is Trenarn Bronad, the Survivor's Tale.'You have been summoned by those who seek to enter Mordor.Mithrandir can be found near the Black Gate

You have been summoned by Mithrandir, who wishes you to enter Mordor on his behalf.Mithrandir can be found near the Black Gate

You have been summoned by Mithrandir, who wishes you to enter Mordor on his behalf.Talk to Mithrandir near the Black GateSador can be found at the Black Gate

You have been summoned by Sador, whose company has entered Mordor.Talk to Sador at the Black GateYou have been summoned by those who seek to enter Mordor.

You should meet at the Black Gate as soon as you are able.'I cannot abandon my post here at the Black Gate. Aragorn has tasked me with keeping tally on those who enter Mordor, and passing what information we have learned on to him. Yet there are affairs in Udûn that must be looked after, which go unattended.

'You are going that way? Perhaps you could be of some help.''All is not quiet in Mordor, my friend. I need someone like yourself to be my eyes upon the wreckage of Sauron's domain.

'Aragorn has appointed Sador, a captain of Gondor, to watch over the Black Gate. Others lead an expedition into Mordor. While you are not obligated, I ask of you to join the company. Speak with Sador if you are willing to brave the plateau of Gorgoroth.'Aganbâr the Cruel, Overseer of Mornaur, keeps his workers hard at task despite the fact that the war is lost.Defeat Overseer Aganbâr the Cruel in Mornaur, on the south slope of Udûn.Defeat Aganbâr the CruelDefeated Aganbâr the Cruel.CompletedAganbâr the Cruel, Overseer of Mornaur, keeps his workers hard at task despite the fact that the war is lost. What plans or orders he follows, no good can come of these machinations.You have defeated Aganbâr the Cruel, Overseer of Mornaur, who kept his workers hard at task, no matter Sauron's fall.Many forgeworkers are still hard at work, smithing weapons in Mornaur. They should be stopped before those fell instruments are used against Gondor and the Free Peoples.Defeat Forgeworkers in Mornaur, on the south slope of Udûn.Defeat Forgeworkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated many Forgeworkers in Mornaur.CompletedForgeworkers are still hard at work in Mornaur, smithing weapons. They should be stopped before those fell instruments are used against Gondor and the Free Peoples.You have defeated many Forgeworkers in Mornaur, slowing the creation of weapons that might be used against Gondor and the Free Peoples.Many fresh weapons have already been smithed in Mornaur, meant to be used against Gondor and the Free Peoples.You should destroy weapon crates throughout Mornaur, on the south slope of Udûn.Destroy weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroyed many new-forged weapons in Mornaur.CompletedMany fresh weapons have already been smithed in Mornaur. These should be destroyed before they may be used against Gondor and the Free Peoples.You have destroyed many weapons newly forged in Mornaur -  before they could be used against Gondor and the Free Peoples.Captain Lachír left with a search party yesterday and has not returned. He left some men searching among rubble for treasure, before continuing east.The first soldiers left behind saw Captain Lachír and his party heading east along the central road of Udûn, before turning north.

