'Speak your purpose or die!

'Very well then!''Narchraw has escaped then? This outcome may be the most favourable to all. It is very likely that Narchraw will return to his realm in Nan Ogol, the fell-vale in the far western reaches of Mordor. He may try to retake his former throne.'

You ask Lômazar about the creature known as Narchraw.

'It is difficult to explain in this tongue. He is neither man nor beast. He is both, yet something different.'Oppressed by Zôreth and now by the Order of the Eye, the Stout-axes of Lûghash have long fought for their survival as slaves of Mordor.Slain Stout-axes and cultists of the Order of the Eye can be found surrounding Lûghash.

Dréri has asked you to bury slain Stout-axes outside Lûghash and avenge the fallen by defeating cultists of the Order of the Eye.Bury Stout-axes slain by the Order of the Eye (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dréri can be found at the Stout-axe barracks within Lûghash.

You have defeated many cultists of the Order of the Eye and buried the Stout-axes slain by them. You should now return to Dréri.Talk to Dréri in Lûghash'Hail, ${PLAYER}! So finally you come to Lûghash, eh?

'It is not a very fitting a home for dwarves, but the Mistress has kept us from the Deathless and the others of her kin. Or so she did until Sauron fell....

'Now this ridiculous "Order of the Eye" won't leave us be! They actually believe he'll come back again! A foolish lot, they are!

'If they were harmless, I'd leave them to their fantasies, but now they have come to the Spire. They have tortured and killed my kin all to gain Mistress Zôreth's knowledge of Sauron's artifacts. What would we know? We are her servants - not her trusted allies and advisors!

'If you wish to aid me, bury my kin upon the fields surrounding Lûghash. They deserve that final honour!

'Come to think of it... if those cultists are still snooping about outside, bury them as well. Even if he does come back again, I don't want them to be around to see it!''May those Men rot upon the plains for what they have done! We may serve Mistress Zôreth, but we are not slaves to all the fools of Mordor! A fire burns within us yet!

'My kin have been given a final honour, and for that, I offer you my thanks.'Lômazar explains that he does not know Krassa-phûrsa's task nor where she can be found.An Orc under the command of Dulgabêth might be found somewhere in Dor Amarth, perhaps spying on those who travel on the road south-west of Lûghash.

