You should speak to Lômazar.Talk to Lômazar'You wish to seek more knowledge about Krassa-phûrsa, the Bringer of Tears. I cannot help you. While I have seen the wraith before, she is a mystery. She follows her own will and serves Dulgabêth with devotion, but it is in her own, secretive ways.''Gar! How would I know what that wraith seeks, ${RACE}?!''I saw the wraith! She went towards the north! Don't kill me!''Gar, she went up to the hills. The ones with the towers. No one goes there.''Looks like she's still looking for something, you filth.'While Krassa-phûrsa is withering from her defeat, you conclude that neither of you have found what you seek. Your only solace is in the defeat of this adversary. When able, you should return to the Ruins of Díngarth.'I know not what Krassa-phûrsa seeks. As I stated, she is a mystery. I do know the hills of Ered Lithui are a place of shadow that no Orc will set foot upon. There may be ancient, forgotten items there. If Krassa-phûrsa knew of something in the hills, it is remembered only by her.'The Order of the Eye has seized what remains of Barad-dûr in search of its secrets, and the Order now holds the Dark Lord's prisoners as its own.Seekers, torturers, and wardens of the Order of the Eye can be found throughout the ruins of Barad-dûr.

While searching for Váskmun Greytooth in the ruins of Barad-dûr, you have discovered a large assemblage of cultists serving the Order of the Eye. You should defeat them.Defeat Order of the Eye seekers in Barad-dûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Order of the Eye torturers in Barad-dûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat an Order of the Eye warden in Barad-dûrYou have stood firm against the Order of the Eye in Barad-dûr, and defeated many of their number.CompletedWhile searching for King Váskmun Greytooth in the bones of Barad-dûr, you have discovered a large assemblage of cultists serving the Order of the Eye. Some of them appear to be frantically searching the crumbling dungeons and halls of the Dark Lord's tower, while others have still held to their duties as torturers and wardens in service of Sauron.

You should defeat them and weaken their grip on the ruins of Barad-dûr.You have loosened the grip of the Order of the Eye on the bones of Barad-dûr as well as that of any prisoners still held in the dungeons of the Dark Lord.

