You have arrived at the main gate of the Oath-taker's Horn. You should use the gate mechanism and call forth the Firehorns to deliver Gimli's message.Call forth the Firehorns and deliver Gimli's messageGimli can be found along the causeway outside the Oath-taker's Horn.

You were brutally attacked by the Firehorns, and they threatened the Dwarves of Durin's Folk. You should talk to Gimli and tell him what has happened.Talk to Gimli outside the Oath-taker's Horn'This is not as simple a matter as it was with the Dourhands.... These Firehorns are not cruel or evil in their hearts, but the promise of a dwarf-ring's power has begun to chip away at their good sense!

'You and I saw what the Ring did to Frodo, even in the short span of months he bore it before our paths were forced apart! If Váskmun was forced to wear it in the dungeons of Barad-dûr during his imprisonment and then deprived of its power by Sauron, his mind may have withered into an obsession! Although, being a dwarf, I think he may have fared a bit better than Gollum!

'${PLAYER}, I do not wish to raise arms against Váskmun and his folk if it can be helped!

'Váskmun may not allow us inside the Oath-taker's Horn, but that does not mean we cannot come to the doors of the Spire! Ha!

'Go to the hidden gate of the Oath-taker's Horn and summon the Firehorns! Deliver them an invitation for King Greytooth to meet us upon the field!

'When that is done, we shall speak of peace... and of having some better dwarf-sense!''The Firehorns did what now? They attacked you... and they threatened my folk?'

Gimli's face flushes with anger.

'Well, that settles it! The time for talk is ended!'It remains uncertain if all the dwarves within the Oath-taker's Horn wish to follow King Greytooth in his quest to recover the dwarf-rings, but Gimli holds hope that a few might instead wish to ally with Durin's Folk.Intimidated Stout-axes can be found throughout the Oath-taker's Horn.

Gimli has asked you to rescue any of the Stout-axes that do not wish to follow King Greytooth in his quest to recover the dwarf-rings and offer them a new home as part of Durin's Folk.You have freed many of the intimidated Stout-axes from the Oath-taker's Horn.Completed'Hold a moment, ${PLAYER}.

'You surely saw as I did that some among the Stout-axes seemed unsettled by the King's command that we be cast out from the Spire. What will become of them? Shall they be met now with threats and curses? Perhaps they shall even be unfairly marked as traitors!

'I cannot speak for King Dáin, but I would offer the Stout-axes a new home among my folk. We shall have need of hardy dwarves now that Sauron has fallen!

'If you find any who still name themselves Stout-axes in the Oath-taker's Horn, aid them and offer them my promise that they shall find refuge in the halls of Durin's Folk.'You have done well to free the Stout-axes from the Oath-taker's Horn. It is likely that King Váskmun Greytooth will lead the Firehorns to ruin in his search for the dwarf-rings.

Instead, you have offered the few remaining Stout-axes a new chance at freedom among Durin's Folk.Overjoyed by the return of their King, Váskmun Greytooth, the Stout-axes of Lûghash have asked you and Gimli to share your tales of valour among the Free Peoples that they might learn more of the world beyond Mordor.Gimli can be found on the central level of Lûghash.

King Váskmun Greytooth desires to hear Gimli's tales of valour. You should join Gimli in recounting your adventures in Middle-earth.Talk to Gimli in LûghashSpakorth can be found along the causeway outside Lûghash.

You have been cast out of Lûghash by King Greytooth and the Firehorns. You should speak to Spakorth.Talk to Spakorth on the plains of Dor Amarth outside Lûghash'This is a day of celebration, indeed! My people are united once more, and today we cast off the shackles by which Sauron himself bound us!

'You and Gimli have done my people a great honour, and one that shall not soon be forgotten by my folk.

'As a dwarf of the eastern mountains, I have always wished to learn more of the west. Ah, but such things could not be asked of the Dark Lord! I know not the reasons why, but Sauron was not over fond of dwarves, you see!

'But, such questions can be asked now! How came you to Mordor, ${PLAYER}? What trials have you and Gimli faced and overcome?

'Let us hear your tales of valour!''Tales of valour, eh? I think we have a few we could tell.... Hah!

'Let's get on with it then!''I am ashamed that I could not resist Zôreth, ${PLAYER}! I am ashamed that I could not even sense her deception—that she could spy upon the Stout-axes through my very eyes and work our ruin!

'I have failed you and I have failed Gimli. Leave me if you wish—it is the fate I deserve!'

Spakorth notices that you make no effort to leave, and smiles weakly.

'What sort of dwarf is so easily swayed by the power of evil? I suppose that is a foolish question to ask now....

'Zôreth may have planned to use me in her search of the Rings of Power, but now King Váskmun has forsaken us all for Manthríf!

'If this is the way of the Firehorns, I want no part in it!'Hithgol asks for you and Legolas to assess if Aiglos is at all retrievable in its current location.The wounded devoted can be found near Aiglos.

You should confront the wounded devoted from the Order of the Eye.Confront the wounded devotedRabôkhor, high priest of the Order of the Eye, can be found in Dor Amarth.

You should find and defeat Rabôkhor.Find and defeat RabôkhorCollect a corrupted trinketAiglos can be found in Dor Amarth.

