You should bring the ward fragments to Isnír.Bring the ward fragments to IsnírThe carven rock focuses a beaming gaze upon you. Strange sounds begin to echo in your head. There is a grinding of rocks, a pick-axe strikes and voices echo through a cavern.

A driving pain seems to emanate from the watching stone and seize your head and chest. Images swirls through you and time seems to stop. You close your eyes yet you can still see. Everything looks different as if you are seeing the world through another's eyes.

Before you is Nargroth, but it is not ripped apart by the flames and fires of Mount Doom. There are dwarves and men on scaffolding working on walls in the cavern. Some have stopped working and instead gaze upon a doorway that is much, much older.

The images fade and you hear an explosion and screams. Those sounds fade as well. The stone is silent and has released you from its grasps. You are uncertain if the watching stone has shown you this memory of Nargroth for a purpose. Perhaps you will be able to search for some of the remnants of the ancient seal you saw in the vision.'Greetings, my name is Isnír. I have been summoned from Gondor to help those with questions of history and lore here in Udûn. Have we met before? I do not think so but I am much better with books than with faces you see.'

You give Isnír the fragments that you have collected.

'Now what have we here? Hmm, these indeed look old, quite old! Give me a few moments to look over them with some detail. I may be able to tell you more about them. I must read through a few passages of this text over here. I shall only be a moment or two.'A strange watching stone stands alone in the fiery landscape of Talath Úrui.Darkwaters can be found in pools around Talath Úrui.

You should defeat Darkwaters gathered at each of the pools in Talath Úrui.Defeat Darkwaters at Ashronk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Darkwaters at Krulronk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Darkwaters at Gakhronk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Darkwaters at Zagronk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The watching stone can be found in Talath Úrui.

You should return to the watching stone.Return to the watching stoneAs you approach the large carven stone, a strange, translucent mist starts to fill the air. The colours around you start to fade as if you are seeing a dream through someone else's eyes.

The unmoving stone seems to turn towards you. As it does, the air begins to feel damp and humid. Drops of water roll drown the face of the carven stone like tears down the face of a small child. Soon, everything is covered in a fine layer of cool mist.

Suddenly a string of words come to you: 'Cleanse, Ashronk, Krulronk, Gakhronk, Zagronk.'

Are these places that you know? It seems as if someone is speaking these thoughts to you.

As you start to ponder these words, the colour returns and the water vanishes. It is replaced by the expected, dry, scorched earth, created by the Ghâshghurm.

You believe the stone requires something of you.The carven stone does not move. There is a stillness in the air.

Again a mist envelopes you and the colours and light seems to fade. This time, the mist grows into a dense, dry fog until you can see nothing in front of you.

Images start to form in the fog. You see a young child fall playing in a field of arid grasslands. She stumbles and falls into a well. Time passes and you see the girl's parents mourning over the well. Time continues to pass, more rapidly this time. The arid plains become burnt. A mountain appears and bursts into flame. A vile statue is built over the well.

Suddenly, everything is returned to as it was. Ash and wind blow through the lifeless terrain.Akhrûn is not able to turn her back on her fellow Nurnhoth still imprisoned by servants of Naerband, and asks for your help in freeing them.Orodir is located next to Naerband.

You should enter the encampment.Enter OrodirOrodir is located next to Naerband.

