You should talk to Málmi.Talk to Málmi in Erebor, in the Hall Under the MountainCopper and calamine ore can be found nearby in Erebor.

You should collect a chunk of copper ore and a chunk of calamine ore.Collect copper oreCollect calamine oreMálmi the Ore Trader can be found in Erebor.

You should talk to Málmi.Talk to MálmiRísta can be found in Dale.

You should talk to Rísta.Talk to RístaDagrun can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.

You should talk to Dagrun.Talk to Dagrun'Mervárth stopped by earlier to congratulate me on my new position and asked for your help if you can spare a moment. He should be in the Trade Commission Headquarters if you would like to go speak with him.''${PLAYER}! Great to see you, as always! Listen, I want to get Dagrun something special in honour of becoming Master. If you're willing to do the work for me, we can say it's a gift from both of us! Keeping her on my good side is imperative to my success!

'So, I have an artisan lined up for the job. Her name is Rísta and her shop is in Dale. You will need to bring her a brass ingot from Erebor and some wood for carving. Not a huge piece, about so big?'

He holds his hands about three feet apart to show the size.

'Try the docks here in Lake-town for that. Please hurry, I'm so excited to see the look on Dagrun's face!''Mervárth needs some wood? Why? No, nevermind, I don't want to know what he's up to. Unfortunately, we are out of wood. You're going to have to go get some from the forester north of here. Good luck, he can be a bit prickly.''What do you want? A small amount of wood? Not worth my time. You can go take something from the scrap pile. Be quick about it.''Hail, friend. Here for a brass ingot? I can smelt you one right away. I will need you to choose one ore of copper and one of calamine from the table here.'Málmi takes the ore from you. You watch as he swiftly transforms the rocks into a bar of pure metal. He hands it to you.

'Since this is part of a gift for the Master of Lake-town, I will not charge you for my services. Give her my regards and tell her Lake-town has friends in Erebor!''Ah, you must be Mervárth's friend. I just need the wood and brass to get started.'

You hand her the brass ingot and the piece of wood, and then watch as she begins to transform them. The wood is carved into a likeness of Dagrun, in a particularly heroic pose, and the brass hammered into a base. To finish the piece, Rísta engraves the base to say "The Greatest Master." She sees your reaction as you read it and chuckles.

'That was what Mervárth asked to be engraved! I believe that's just the kind of relationship he has with Dagrun. It is done and already paid for in full. You may take it to Dagrun.''What is this? A gift from Mervárth?'

You hand her the statuette. She looks confused until she reads the engraving and then bursts out laughing.

'Mervárth! He likes to give me a hard time for being humble. "You're Master of all of Lake-town now, throw your weight around a little!" This will go on my desk as a reminder of my station and a reminder that I should do something nice for Mervárth one of these days. Thank you for your part in this, ${PLAYER}.'Gimli, son of Glóin, has returned to Erebor from the lands of Mordor and now seeks to ensure peace between the Dwarves of Durin's Folk and the Stout-axes of Dor Amarth.King Thorin III can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

Gimli has offered an impassioned plea for the Stout-axes to be accepted as friends and kin to Durin's Folk. You should hear King Thorin's judgment on the matter.Hear King Thorin III's judgmentGimli can be found near King Thorin's throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

King Thorin III has passed his judgment on what is to be done regarding the Stout-axes. You should now speak to Gimli.Talk to Gimli'Well, then.'

Gimli approaches King Thorin III and begins to speak.

'Hail, Thorin III, King Under the Mountain! I come before you today to ask for your wisdom and mercy. In my adventures beyond the Black Gate of Mordor, I discovered a clan of dwarves known as the Stout-axes. They are a hardy folk, but they have been beset by tragedy at many turns. They have lost their ancestral home, much as we of Durin's Folk have in the past, and they have suffered under the Dark Lord and his servants. Their leader of old, King Greytooth, succumbed to what power lingered in the Rings once wielded by the greatest Kings of the dwarves and led the remainder of his folk down a dark path to ruin.

'The Stout-axes were thus sundered, but I have come north with those who survived and they did not lose hope that kindness could be found beyond the mountains of Mordor. Their number is small, and they have no home beyond these lands. I beg you, King Thorin, offer them a place among us and they will offer their knowledge, compassion, and skill to Durin's Folk.'

Gimli finishes speaking and looks to King Thorin.'Gimli, son of Glóin, I have known your father and your family for many years.

'I have heard your words, and I will bear my judgment. As you well know, the Dale-lands are filled with refugees of the East -- and among them, the unfortunate cousins of the hated Jangovar. Regardless of their heritage, I see their plight for what it is.

'I trust your words, Gimli, and I would not deny those oppressed by Mordor. The Stout-axes shall have shelter within Erebor, and be welcome as friends of Durin's Folk. However, these are difficult times. Sacrifices have been made by each of the Kingdoms of the North, and more still will have to be made before we have healed the ills of the War. If the Stout-axes are to dwell among us, they must earn their place among our folk and share their knowledge of the Enemy and the lands beyond.

'You may inform the Stout-axes that they have found a new home in Erebor, but see to it that they offer their skills to all in need.''Hah! It is as I'd hoped, ${PLAYER}.

'Ambassador Spakorth and his folk will be so grateful. They will understand what a King of the dwarves ought to be!

'Now then, as for earning their place....'Peace has come to the kingdom under the mountain, but now, as the dust settles, all is not quiet or peaceful in King Thorin Stonehelm's court.You have received a letter from King Thorin Stonehelm, asking you to return to him in Erebor and assist him with another matter.Atli Spider-bane has requested an adventurer to mine a mysterious ore in Kâm Lagúrz, the Brokencleft.Glowing ore can be found inside Kâm Lagúrz, the Brokencleft.

You should mine the glowing ore for Atli Spider-bane.Mine glowing ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A note hangs on the board, signed by Atli Spider-bane:

'I spotted a glowing ore I've never seen before in the Kâm Lagúrz, the Brokencleft. If any of you are brave enough to venture inside, bring me some samples!'The merchants of Dale believe your presence in the markets will be good for business.You should visit and be seen at the various market areas and tavern in Dale, salute merchants, congratulate happy shoppers, assist indecisive shoppers, and calm angry shoppers on the way.<rgb=#FF00FF>Salute</rgb> Dale merchants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF00FF>Calm</rgb> angry shoppers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF00FF>Congratulate</rgb> happy shoppers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF00FF>Assist</rgb> indecisive shoppers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Visit the Upper Markets, northVisit the Upper Markets, southVisit the Jolly Bell tavernVisit the Lower Markets, westVisit the Lower Markets, centralVisit the Lower Markets, southYou should return to Rótha, who can be found inside the Great-keep in Dale.Return to Rótha'${PLAYER} - do I have that right? The - hhhem! - merchants of Dale have watched you in your service to Dale, and we have noted the good impression you have made on the folk of Dale.

'Indeed, the impression was strong enough that we feel your very presence in Dale's markets would do much for commerce. In fact - hhem! - if it were not too much of an imposition... might we ask you to go about Dale's markets, salute some merchants, talk to those buying here and there?''If it would not be too much trouble, the merchants of Dale would - hhem! - greatly appreciate your making an appearance in the upper markets, the lower markets, and the Jolly Bell tavern. Also, be sure to stop to speak with and encourage some merchants and shoppers along the way.''${PLAYER}! I have already heard many reports of your presence in the markets and the kind and wise words you spared for merchants and shoppers alike.

'You will truly always be welcome here in Dale!'Help Master Dagrun disprove the rumours that she is descended from Othur, the notorious Master from the time of Smaug and Bard the Bowman.The crests and old Isgird can be found about Lake-town. The old Master's chest can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.

You should find representations of Dagrun's and Othur's family crests, speak to old Isgird, and check the old Master's chest to verify that Othur's stolen treasure is not there.Find Dagrun's family crestFind Othur's family crestTalk to old IsgirdSearch the Master's safeA crowd of people have gathered near the Master's manor in Lake-town.

You should present your findings to the curious crowd of people.Quelled suspicions of Dagrun's bloodline.Completed'The rumours of my relation to Othur are pernicious, but easily disproved. The proof must be very clear, however, for we seek to persuade not judges, but fishermen and stevedores.

'First, you will need to find a crest of my own family and that of Othur's. They are, of course, not the same. Second, you must speak with Isgird, who is the oldest living person in Lake-town. She knows everyone. Lastly, search the old chest in the manor for Othur's treasure. It is foolish, I know, but some say it is still there.''Dagrun? The new Master of Lake-town? Why yes, of course I had heard! I am not deaf, you know, and many a little bird comes to my sill. Such a sweet child Dagrun was, I remember well. Sweet and kind, much like her mother before her.

'Married the boatman, named... no, but I've forgotten that. He was a boatman, though, much like her father. Not rich, but proud and hard-working. Boatman and fisherman, both families, as long as anyone could recall.'You have successfully quelled suspicions of Dagrun's bloodline to the people of Lake-town.One of the raft-elves has been kidnapped by smugglers in Esgaroth-of-old. Rescue him before it's too late!The captured raft-elf is somewhere in Esgaroth-of-old.

