Hear more from Queen Regent Erna.Hear Erna's remonstranceThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale.

Bryn has grown tired of listening and speaks out of turn.Hear Bryn speakThe Queen Regent and her sons stand within the Great-keep in Dale.

Bryn has grown tired of listening and speaks out of turn.Talk to King Bard IITalk to Queen Regent Erna'The fulfillment of justice has not yet run its course. This Athálrik acted as Prince Bryn's sword-thegn, and so Bryn in some part is answerable for the wrongs that have come to pass.

'It has not escaped my notice that Bryn has been elsewhere since these developments began coming to light. No, ${PLAYER}, I do not want your help in finding him. I know Bryn and Dale well enough for that. But while I am dragging my youngest son by the ear back to this spot, I hoped you might help me in another way.

'Namely, I would ask you to gather some things: a gold coin of Dale from the coin-changers, which you may redeem in my name, Ilon-ôtin, otherwise known as Snakewood, from traders in the lower markets by the eastern gate, and a dwarf-craft puzzle box from the upper markets.''While I drag my youngest son Bryn back here, I ask you to find me these three things: a gold coin of Dale from the coin-changers, which you may redeem in my name, Snakewood from the mercantile traders near the eastern gate, and a dwarf-craft puzzle box from the upper markets.''In the Queen Mother's name? Of course. Here you are.''A puzzle box? For the Queen Regent? Here, this is my finest. Take it with my compliments to Her Majesty!''You know as well as I do, Bryn, that you had better hear mother out.''Oh, it's you.''Here, Bryn. Our friend ${PLAYER} has come bearing - Bryn, attend to me when I speak!

'If you do not wish to be treated as a child, you must not sulk and act like one. You have exercised our authority, name, and coin upon a man who has done harm to the very substance of Dale. I do not charge you with more than errant judgment, but I do insist that you understand what harm has been done.

'Would you, ${PLAYER}, present us with the item from the upper markets?''I see. This is going to be one of those talks.''You recognize this manner of toy, Bryn? No, I see from your face you would feign forget. Yet I recall you begging me for one every trip through the market, not three years past.

'Its design is truly ingenious, is it not? Have you ever considered, however, how it came to be? They are as common as cobble-stones in Dale, and ever beloved of children, but in truth, they are guests here whose story spans leagues.

'Indeed, it was not fashioned within our kingdom at all, but in Erebor by some nimble-fingered dwarf. And with what did he craft it? ${PLAYER}, would you present us with the material you found in the lower markets?''I see. This is going to be one of those talks.''I see. This is going to be one of those talks.''Ilon-ôtin, or Snakewood, is beloved of carvers far and wide, for it is strong, handsome, and easily worked. Do you know in what forest Snakewood grows? Nor do I, save that it lies far to the east, though perhaps not so far as Rhûn.

'It was introduced into Dale's lower markets by an Easterling trader, not so very unlike those poor dispossessed souls who make camp across the River Running.

'What, one might ask, has Dale to do with any of this? ${PLAYER}, will you show us the final item?''She misses the point, as she always does.''Enough, Mother. You need not go on so. Nor did you need a mummer's act to make your point, which is plain enough. Dale thrives on trade. I cannot count how many times you have told me so.

'You have told me, too, that Dale's livelihood needs protecting, and that is the very reason I had Athálrik - but how could I ever have known how things would happen across the river? It cannot have been Athálrik's fault, no matter what you say. At least, he never would have started it. He swore to me. He swore...

'And how you and Bard cannot see how these throngs of dirty, tattered, dispossessed threaten that, what with more of them pouring into our vale day after day - I see by your face I will not be heard. No man's death is on my hands. That is all I will say.''Oh, Bryn. This would have gone better for you if you had heard mother out and nodded your head. Why must you always increase your troubles when you might lighten them?''If all you take from my instruction is that trade is vital to Dale, you have understood nothing. These dirty dispossessed, as you call them, are buyers, sellers, and guests of Dale. All the kingdoms touched by our roads are not strangers to us, but kin. Calamity in their lands is hardship in ours. You have come to think as the Jangovar do, and so you become as they are, seeing a wolf disguised in every sheep. You will find neither peace nor profit thus.

'I see, however, that I will impress nothing more on you, at the present. You will go across the river yourself, bearing clothes and provisions to the refugees. Until you do, you are in my ill-favour and all coin and privileges are from you withdrawn.

'You must forgive us, ${PLAYER}, for subjecting you to this scene. I hope you will take not as a slight, but as a sign of the trust and favour you have earned in Dale. No thanks would be enough for the good you have done, and you will always be welcome here in Dale.''She misses the point, as she always does.''The coin you paid Athálrik to strut about as your sword-thegn came, of course, from our coffers. Most likely, it entered them from a road toll upon the Easterling trader, as merchant stall fees from our clever-handed dwarf, and any number of other levies made upon the commerce of Dale.'By completing this quest, you will automatically complete the Abyss of Mordath discovery, tier 1, and tier 2 raid deeds.'Deeds! Get your Abyss of Mordath Raid Deeds here!

'Talk to me one more time, and they're all yours!''Deeds, incoming!'Someone - or something - has come to dwell in Caras Tilion.You should stand by Oroniel's side and face the dweller of Caras Tilion.Talk to OronielRadagast can be found at the tree nursery just outside of Felegoth.

You should tell Radagast about what you have encountered at Caras Tilion.Talk to Radagast'Whatever - whoever this dweller of Caras Tilion may be, he is aware of our presence already, I feel certain of it. If we tarry, he will be upon us.

'The wisest counsel would have you leave me, with my injured leg, and go to Felegoth for aid. But I see in your face you have no intention of such a cautious course.''Do you feel the air getting colder? He approaches! Prepare yourself!''This man you encountered in Caras Tilion is hair-raising, indeed, by your account. However, you must take me at my word that no one man holds the power to corrupt a river so.

'Nay, even the Dark Lord himself, in the guise of the Necromancer, could not have done so in mere days. Long have I watched the dark workings of Dol Guldur and their effect upon these forests, and I know it to be so.'A small number of Dale-folk are speaking out loud against the Easterling refugees and clouding the minds of many others.You should publically deter discontented Dale folk who are speaking against the refugees.Talk to discontented Dale-folk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Gaumar, who stands within the Great-keep in Dale.Return to Gaumar'In market stalls and street corners, some few murmur against the dispossessed from Rhûn, and their talk clouds the minds of others. 

'If you, a hero of the war and a symbol of goodness, would address those malcontents, it would change many minds among the folk of Dale.''Every discontented rabble-rouser you dissuade in Dale will keep a dozen others from turning against the refugees.''Do not doubt it, ${PLAYER}, you have changed many minds in Dale today.'Discover the notable landmarks of Agarnaith.Discover the notable landmarks of Agarnaith.Discover the Lair of the Gloom-lordDiscover Bhol RûdhDiscover Viznak's hideoutDiscover Faltor GâmDiscover Kala-gijakDiscover the Agarnaith Ranger campDiscover SeregostDiscover Mokál RukhThere is still much to do in Agarnaith.There is still much to do in Agarnaith.Complete More Pesky CrittersComplete Hunt the NerbygComplete Hunt GámnakurComplete Hunt the Ash-clawsComplete Enemies in SeregostComplete Hunt the Sudden WhelmerComplete Banners of the Lady of BlightComplete Hunt Shâkrum the RipperComplete Reclaiming Agarnaith: Mokál RukhComplete Reclaiming Agarnaith: Orodruin Guard-towerThere is much to do in assisting the Conquest of Gorgoroth in Mordor.There is much to do in assisting the Conquest of Gorgoroth in Mordor.Complete Celebrated in the Conquest of GorgorothComplete Enemy to Fushaum Bal southComplete Enemy to Fushaum Bal northComplete Known to the Red Sky ClanThe Easterling refugee encampments need more food and firewood than they can gather.The camps of the Easterling refugees are east and across the river from Dale.

You should help the refugees by gathering firewood and blue berries for them.Collect berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect firewood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enkárvo can be found in the Dorwinion camp, east and across the river from Dale.

You should bring the berries and firewood you gathered back to Enkárvo.'It is challenging enough to manage the needs of Dale, but I continue to hear reports of failing fires and food-stores among the refugees of Rhûn.

'They have grown fond of the berries that grow nearby, and there is plenty of wood to be harvested for a warm fire. I would ask that you assist them in their efforts to gather both.

'Aid them in collecting as much as you are able, and perhaps they shall sleep free of worry for a night.''You have done so much for us. Your help and humility are beyond reckoning, ${PLAYER}!'Wolves still attack the Easterling refugees when they stray from their camps.You should defeat wolves in the areas around the refugee encampments, east and across the river from Dale.Defeat wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should speak to Komúsi, who can be found in the Dorwinion camp, east and across the river from Dale.Talk to Komúsi'I have heard troubling reports that the refugees of Rhûn are beset by wolves. I will not see the dispossessed left to die, especially through the inaction of leadership.

'Travel out to their encampment and cull the wolves that harry them. Let them know that they are safe in our lands.''I am glad the Queen Regent of Dale has not forgotten us or our plight. The wolves will fall back into the deep trees and not bother us, at least for a spell.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Orphón believes that Akshir alone is the reason why the Jangovar remain in the Dale-lands.You should enter the Jangovar encampment of Urûshoba, south-east of Tay Yoldash in the Dale-lands.Return to the Jangovar camp of UrûshobaYou should attack the Jangovar encampment of Urûshoba, which is located south-east of Tay Yoldash in the Dale-lands.Defeat enemies in Urûshoba (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy weapons in Urûshoba (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat AkshirErna can be found in the Great-keep in Dale.

You should return to Queen Regent Erna with news of your fight with Akshir.Return to Erna'I learned some things about these Jangovar, ${CLASS}, before I slipped away and hid. Do you not think it strange that they cling to the Dale-lands, days and days after their defeat? Know that it is all Akshir. Others wish to leave. Again and again, he refuses. I heard one Jangovar grumble how his reasons change, but ever he insists they must stay.

'I cannot answer the riddle of why, but I think if Akshir were gone, the Jangovar might soon return to the East and leave this valley alone.'The boy's lower lip trembles.

'What did you say became of this Akshir? It is only that you ended abruptly, and I wish to know.'You tell the Queen Regent and the young King all you learned and did. After a grave pause, Erna speaks.

'You have done well, very well in the service of Dale, ${PLAYER}. Yet it is clear that some deep scheme is afoot, and it runs deep through this land.''Whatever you hoped to gain was for naught, ${RACE}. The work is nearly done, and you have hindered little, for all your meddling!'After discovering several suspiciously empty barrels of ale, Snállar hopes to uncover the source of the theft.Barrel-racks can be found throughout the Hall Under the Mountain.

Snállar has asked you to knock on various barrels of ale to try to expose the ale-thieves in Erebor.Snállar can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain.

You have driven off several ale-soaked cave-claws in the Hall Under the Mountain and should now return to Snállar.Talk to Snállar'Have you a moment?

'In just two days, I've lost nearly twelve barrels of ale to thieves. It's always the same! I find the barrel emptied with a great big hole bored into the bottom of it!

'There's treachery afoot here, and I think those dratted cave-claws are to blame again. Always sticking their noses where they don't belong!

'Knock on some of the barrels and give them a fright. That ought to drive them off!''Greedy little burrowers, that lot! Well, that ought to teach them not to meddle with our ales....

'And to think I'd considered requesting new barrels made of iron! Bah! It would turn my finest beers to swill!'There are many to assist in the conquest of Gorgoroth.There are many to assist in the conquest of Gorgoroth.Complete Durin's Folk AllegianceComplete Court of Lothlórien AllegianceComplete Hobbits of the Company AllegianceComplete Kingdom of Gondor AllegianceOroniel fears the corruption along the river Rhachló might be more widespread.You should patrol along the river Rhachló, looking out for any beasts corrupted by its waters.Defeat corrupted Huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat corrupted bears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat corrupted wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat corrupted boars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat gloomwaters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Oroniel has returned and can be found further south along the banks of the Rhachló.

You should reconvene with Oroniel and discuss how next to proceed.Meet up with Oroniel'${PLAYER}, I shall bring this poor soul back to Felegoth. I am certain he will recover under a healer's care.

'Will you survey more of the river's length, keeping an eye out for animals that might have been affected by the river as well? The effect of the waters on some beasts is not sleep... but madness. I shall meet you again, further upstream, as soon as I am able.''The sleeping Elf is in good care, though he has not yet wakened. What news have you?'

Oroniel listens closely as you tell her.

'It is as I feared then. The waters' corruption grows stronger and affects the surrounding land. We must continue upstream.'Ambassador Sparkorth of the Stout-axes wishes to thank King Thorin III and pledge his people to the service of Durin's Folk.Ambassador Spakorth can be found before King Thorin III's throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

Ambassador Spakorth has asked you to accompany him to address King Thorin in Erebor.Talk to Ambassador Spakorth before King Thorin III's throneKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

Ambassador Spakorth has thanked King Thorin III for his mercy and offered the services of the Stout-axes to Durin's Folk.Talk to King Thorin III'${PLAYER}! I am glad you and Gimli are here with us. It has been a bit... overwhelming.

'We will continue to aid Durin's Folk in their efforts to rebuild Erebor and heal the lands surrounding it, but I would like to speak to the King Under the Mountain. I am grateful for the aid that you and Gimli have provided my folk, but I wish to express my thanks to a King who is worthy of his title.

'Will you meet me before his throne?''Hail, King Thorin III! Hail, King Under the Mountain!'

Ambassador Spakorth bows deeply before King Thorin III.

'I am Spakorth of the Stout-axes. Once I was counselor to Váskmun Greytooth, the former King of my folk, but his madness and greed led him from reason to ruin. We are a people without a leader, and though I now speak for my folk, I do not desire to lead them. I ask that of you, King Thorin.

'Servitude is still so fresh in our minds. We have always served the greater powers of Mordor, and once again, we are bereft of the guiding hand of a King. I offer my people to you... to serve Durin's Folk for the kindness you have shown us.

'The Stout-axes shall be true friends to Durin's Folk. I promise you this!''Your words are appreciated, Spakorth of the Stout-axes.

'Durin's Folk are honoured to have you and your kin among us, and do not take my request for aid to mean that the Stout-axes will once again serve at the will of an oppressor. You are our friends and our guests, and I will not allow any to say otherwise.

'What you have endured is now a matter of the past. I bear no judgment against you or your kin for the crimes of your King and those he turned to his will. We of Durin's Folk have endured many hardships as well, and when the time is right, I shall tell you of them.

'Now, I must turn my attention to Erebor and to restoring the Kingdoms of the North.'Raft-elves from Loeglond are missing. Lorndúr believes they may be in great danger and would like you to go find them.Injured Raft-elves can be found along the Forest River between Felegoth and Loeglond.

You should seek out the missing Raft-elves and tend to their wounds if needed.Find and heal injured Raft-elves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lorndúr can be found in Loeglond.

You should talk to Lorndúr.Talk to Lorndúr'Ever since the thievery of Felegoth's shipments was thwarted, I have sent several of my Raft-elves to ensure the arrival of each new shipment. They have not returned again, and I grow worried.

'If not Orcs, I fear the agents of the Weeping Warrior may have attacked them. Find them and tend any wounds they may bear before sending them back to Loeglond!''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Even with the War ended, we must be vigilant and prepared to face the foes that remain.'The Easterling refugee encampments need more food and firewood than they can gather.The camps of the Easterling refugees are in the hills east of Dale.

You should help the refugees by gathering firewood and blue berries for them.Collect berries  (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect firewood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Enkárvo can be found in the Dorwinion camp, in the hills east of Dale.

You should bring the berries and firewood you gathered back to Enkárvo.'Many are our needs, but food and warmth are first among them. There is good wood among the trees and a blue berry we have found that is good for eating, but we cannot seem to gather either.

'I would not beg your help in such menial tasks... but any of these things you happened to gather would be gratefully received!''You have done what I could not ask of you. Your help and humility are beyond reckoning, ${PLAYER}!'Sangemêkh Turáh yearns for tangible proof that the Chayasír once dwelled by the Long Lake in the Dale-lands, long ago.You should search for Chayasír potsherds in the soil throughout the Dale-lands.Search for Chayasír potsherds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Sangemêkh Turáh, who can be found in the Dorwinion refugee camp, in the hills east of Dale.Return to Sangemêkh Turáh'I know from song-memory that our people dwelled here once, in this valley, many, many years ago. And though I have no doubt the memory is true, still some part of me yearns for proof I might touch with my hand.

'As you go here and there around the Dale-lands, would you look for traces of the Chayasír? There might be potsherds among the soil. The memories sing of fine clay vessels, ornate patterns about the rims, where we dwelled around the Long Lake.

'Will you tell me what - if you are able to find? It would mean much to me, ${PLAYER}.'You recount the places that you discovered potsherds among the soil.

'I knew it to be true and yet, somehow, what you found still fills me with wonder. I may only hope that our condition improves here, so that I may tour this valley and see these sights for myself. 

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Wolves still attack the Easterling refugees when they stray from their camps.You should defeat wolves in the areas around the refugee encampments, east and across the river from Dale.Defeat wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Komúsi, who can be found in the Dorwinion camp, in the hills east of Dale.Return to Komúsi'Though the pack leader is gone, wolves still harry us when we wander too far from our camps. If you would fell some more of them, ${PLAYER}, you will scare the rest away... at least for a time.''Please, defeat some of the wolves beyond our camps so that they will not dare to come so close.''The wolves will fall back into the deep trees and not bother us, at least for a spell. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'One of the raft-elves of Loeglond has become convinced a thief is somehow stealing from their supplies.You should talk to Sírithon, who can be found in Loeglond.Talk to SírithonYou should inventory the supplies and rations in Loeglond.Take inventory of supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Take inventory of provisions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sírithon can be found at Loeglond.

You should speak with Sírithon about the various missing supplies.Talk to Sírithon'While it is my task to oversee trade in Loeglond, it is all too much for one Elf to handle. I have delegated some tasks to Sírithon. He oversees the inventory and storing of provisions within Loeglond's bounds. 

'He has become increasingly agitated of late, convinced that a thief moves somehow undetected among us. I can hardly see how. No Wood-elf could be a thief! Any dwarf or Man would be watched closely enough, after Sírithon's talk of thieves, if not before!

'Would you speak with Sírithon and see if you can put his troubled mind to rest, one way or another?''Lorndúr sent you? Did he say he thought I was out of my wits? I tell you, there is a thief - though I have nothing to prove my convictions, as of yet. If only I had time to make a count of provisions. Though trade is stopped, somehow my work goes on. 

'Will you lend me a hand in counting supplies? It's hardly work suited for an adventurer like yourself... but it may lead us to that thief.''Now this is interesting. No common provisions were taken. They are the first thing a petty Lake-town thief would steal. 

'But sundry items are indeed missing, so my suspicions were no lapse of wits. Foresters' axes, rope, lumber, chisels? What do these have in common? Their value is little. They are but tools of our common labour. Strange, indeed!'After stoking the ire of the Herald of Winter, Karazgar has fled the North. The peoples of Eryn Lasgalen, Erebor, and the Dale-lands must now prepare to face a new foe.Piles of stone blocks can be found in Erebor, logs can be found in the halls of Felegoth, crates of rations can be found throughout Dale, and barrels of water can be found in Lake-town.

King Thorin III has asked you to aid the peoples of the North in preparing for battle against Vethúg Wintermind.King Thorin III can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain.

You have mistaken King Thorin's jest for an actual task. You should return to King Thorin.Erna can be found in Dale, Dagrun can be found in Lake-town, and Thranduil can be found in Felegoth.

King Thorin III has asked you to deliver a message of warning to the other strongholds of the North and ask that they prepare their defences as best they can before Vethúg Wintermind strikes.Talk to ErnaTalk to DagrunTalk to ThranduilKing Thorin III can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain.

You have warned the leaders of the strongholds of the North to prepare for the coming of Vethúg Wintermind as King Thorin asked. You should return to King Thorin.Talk to King Thorin III'I have thought long on what is to be done, ${PLAYER}. If Hrímil Frost-heart soon sends Vethúg and her hordes against us, we of Durin's Folk shall not shy from battle.

'You see, Vethúg Wintermind was known to us long before Smaug. He drove my forefathers from Thikil-gundu and left it a frozen ruin. Such a fate will not befall Erebor!

'We withstood the evils of Smaug and Bolg, and we shall withstand this!

'You have done many great deeds for Durin's Folk, my friend. And here now is a task befitting such a warrior! I would ask that you travel the lands of the North, and gather the resources of each of its peoples. We shall have need to share them if the battle is to be won.

'Swiftly now, ${PLAYER}!''Hah! Such trickery does not befit me now that I am King Under the Mountain, ${PLAYER}.

'You have always been eager to help those in need, but we have peoples enough to prepare our defences and fill our stores, and they can handle such tasks.

'As for you, my friend, you have become something of an emissary to the peoples of the North. I would ask that you inform Queen Erna, Master Dagrun, and King Thranduil of what we have learned. Our friendships must be held close in such times, and, at least in regard to the coming battle, there will be no secrets between us. Tell them what you have learned of the Herald of Winter, and tell them that Vethúg shall soon come to seek his misguided vengeance upon the peoples of the North. Urge them to do whatever they can to prepare for battle, and inform them that Erebor shall again welcome those who cannot fight into the safety of its halls.

'When you have done as I have asked, return to me at once.''So the Herald of Winter was not the cold-drake in the rumour-monger's tale, but a different cold-drake named Hrímil Frost-heart? And now her spawn comes to set siege to the Dale-lands?

Erna lets out a wry, desperate chuckle.

'I shall have to have a word with King Thorin about this! I fail to see the difference between the rumours and our new circumstances....

'All of Karazgar's plots have come to pass. I care not that he is wounded and lost. He has turned Hrímil's ire upon us, and we shall suffer her wrath in his stead. The young King shall face the same test as his namesake, but he is not ready to bear such a burden. Who can ever be truly ready to face such a challenge? What else can we do but prepare?

'I shall rally every able warrior of Dale and send my people to the safety of Erebor when the time comes. It seems the arrows must be nocked once more....

'Go on, ${PLAYER}! There is much to be done and little time to speak!''It is my truest regret and sorrow that some of my people aided Karazgar in his plots.

'Perhaps now they will understand their folly.... for we shall all suffer the consequences of their foolishness. They have drawn the ire of this Hrímil Frost-heart to our lands, and now I fear that Lake-town will again bear the most grievous wounds at the hands of her offspring. Instead of flames, we shall be frozen along with the waters of the Long Lake! We cannot rebuild our homes and resettle our people on the Lake every time a new foe comes to the North! Sooner or later, we shall run out of places to flee!

'I will offer what I can to the folk of Dale and Erebor. We have plentiful stores of water and food to be shared, but I am afraid I cannot spare a single warrior. All of this business has riled the folk of Lake-town, and my guards are needed here to keep order.

'I am sorry I cannot offer more, ${PLAYER}. We of Lake-town will prepare as best we can.''I knew well of the cold-drake that ravaged the Ered Mithrin, ${PLAYER}, but never have I known his name. Vethúg Wintermind... so he is the hated spawn of Hrímil Frost-heart!

'Whether we are granted days, weeks, months, or mere hours to prepare remains unknown, but the King Under the Mountain speaks true -- Vethúg will come. We know little of Hrímil's forces and what Vethúg may bring to bear upon this realm, but it is clear from your vision that her hordes are not limited to dragon-kind. There is no ill will between us and Durin's Folk, but we have all battled and suffered greatly to repel the forces of the Enemy. Terrible wounds are still borne by my kin, and I cannot muster such a force as the one that repelled the Orcs and Easterlings before Erebor.

'I shall send the warriors and archers I can to defend this realm, but I fear it will take more than our combined armies to overcome such a foe. Let us hope it is enough....''So it is done? Good.

'I will not allow Vethúg to displace Durin's Folk again, ${PLAYER}. We of the North battled together in unfriendly times and triumphed over Smaug and the armies of Bolg, but this time it shall be different. Durin's Folk, the Men of Dale, and the Elves of Eryn Lasgalen have no quarrels between them. There is no treasure to divide, no weregild withheld in stubbornness, and no treachery between us. We stand united against Vethúg Wintermind and so too shall we stand against Karazgar and Hrímil Frost-heart.

'At last, the Dwarves of Durin's Folk shall have our vengeance... Vethúg will fall!'


<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'An Unexpected Summons'</rgb>Pressing news has come to King Bard II.The messenger stands before King Bard II, inside the Great-keep in Dale.

You should hear the messenger's tidings.Talk to the messengerKing Bard II, Queen Regent Erna, and Prince Bryn stand discussing the messenger's tidings in the Great-keep in Dale.

You should hear what Prince Bryn has to say in response to the messenger.Talk to Prince BrynKing Bard II, Queen Regent Erna, and Prince Bryn stand discussing the messenger's tidings in the Great-keep in Dale.

You should hear what King Bard II and his regent mother, Erna, have to say in response to Prince Bryn and the messenger.Talk to Queen Regent ErnaTalk to King Bard IIYou should talk to the messenger who stands before King Bard II in the Great-keep in Dale, and learn where you must go to investigate the report of violence.Go with the messengerYou should speak to Enkárvo, the man of Dorwinion, in the refugee camp, across the river from Dale.Talk to Enkárvo'I must think long on all you have told me, ${PLAYER}. But a messenger has come with grave and pressing news, to judge by his face.

'Let us hear the tidings, then.''M'lord. There has been an incident - an outbreak of violence of some sort in one of the refugee camps. I can say little else, I am afraid, but if 'tis true, the lives of Dale-folk may be imperiled this very moment.''Word has come only that there was violence of some kind in one of the refugees' camps. I know nothing else, save that the matter is most urgent.''Even now, my sword-thegn Athálrik is patrolling the refugee encampments to ensure that no such violence or conspiracy can fester among the Easterlings. If there has been some incident, he will quell it.''I told you both, my sword-thegn is more than capable of handling the matter.''Word has come only that there was violence of some kind in one of the refugees' camps. I know nothing else, save that the matter is most urgent.''Let us err on the side of overabundant caution in this matter. We have just heard how our people's sentiments toward the Easterlings seeking refuge are delicate, at best.

'If some row between the refugees has broken out, or one has gone and attacked one of the Dale-folk, it must be swiftly dealt with.

'I deem that we should dispatch our new friend, the ${CLASS}, to assist Athálrik in whatever way is needed.''Athálrik? Now you have sent him and his fellows to go among the refuge-seekers, Bryn? Did you not even think to mention this to me or to Mother?

'${PLAYER}, if the Queen Regent wishes you to go then I, too... wish it.''Come with me, then, ${CLASS}. I will lead you to where the incident was said to have happened, and take the swiftest path.''Will you go with our messenger and see that no one comes to harm, ${PLAYER}? I have utmost faith in you.''I am sure you will arrive and find Athálrik has already subdued whichever of the Easterlings have caused this stir.

'But do go. Perhaps Mother and Bard will finally believe me!''Here then, this is my home. Oh, not my true home in Dorwinion, which might be destroyed, for all that I know. But this is as much home as I have, and you are my guest. My hearth is yours, and here no harm shall befall you.

'But you have come here for a purpose, and not for pleasantries! I have asked that you judge carefully what happened in the lower camp. Will you do so and hear me out?'Some spiders, at least, remain in Mirkwood, and they bear a grudge against the Elves.Thranduil can be found in Felegoth.

You should talk to Thranduil about the attack on the Elves at the caravan.Talk to ThranduilYou should collect sap from trees in Eryn Lasgalen that the Elves have already tapped for sap collection.Collect sap from trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The last place anyone saw spiders was near the caravan that was attacked.

You should use the sap to lay a trap for the spiders.The last place anyone saw spiders was near the caravan that was attacked.

You should wait and watch the trap to see if any spiders come.Wait and watch the trapThranduil can be found in Felegoth.

You should speak with Thranduil about the failed trap.Talk to ThranduilThe sap can be taken from corrupted Huorns throughout Eryn Lasgalen.

You should collect corrupted sap for a second attempt at laying a trap.Collect corrupted sap from Huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A good place for a trap might be closer to Felegoth, near the main road that runs through Eryn Lasgalen.

You should use the corrupted sap to lay a trap for the spiders.Set up another trap to catch a spiderCatch a spiderThranduil can be found in Felegoth.

You should bring the spider leg to Thranduil.The Beorning takes a deep breath.

'Ah... forgive me. My wits are returning. Grant me one more calming breath and I will tell my tale as it should be told. There. Now, then.

'When the Elf-king closed off his realm, I was still within it, and therefore unable to return home. By good fortune I was in the company of these poor Elves, with whom I had traded many years and knew well. They kindly offered to lead me to Felegoth, where I might bide my time. 

'Thither we were going when, here on the path and without warning, spiders descended all about us! Me, they ignored - but fell upon each and every Elf with a strange and silent fury. 

'What I tell you is true. Look into my eyes. Look at the nature of their wounds. Come, we must go to Felegoth and tell the Elves of this!''Hállkell has told me his story. His face is an honest one and I do not suspect him of deceit. Rather, instead, I find myself recalling things far in the past. Yes, it was many years ago... a great spider, strong and cunning and filled with malice. Iphantemel we called her, and she was nearly my match. I was stung, and in return gave her a grievous wound. At that, she fled... and though I hunted her many years, I never more than glimpsed her. She was wily, as I have said, and laid many traps for me.

'That was long ago, but such an ambush as Hállkell describes might well be her doing. Such malice against Elves and Elves alone I could also believe. And perhaps, due to the wound I dealt her, she was unable to flee with all the others of her wretched kind.

'I know how we may test this hunch. Alone among the spiders of Mirkwood, Iphantemel and all her spawn crave the sap of trees, and drink it as you might water. Would you return to the wood and gather some sap? You will find taps here and there, set by my foresters. It is time that we laid a trap of our own.''It did not work? Was I wrong in my suspicion? Let me think.

'That is it. The sap was too pure. The forest becomes Green-leafed once more, and Mirkwood no longer. It will be the old, befouled sap they hunger for. Seek out corrupted Huorns, for their blood is a most vile sap. Then we shall learn if Iphantemel hides somewhere within these woods.''Mark the colouring upon this leg. Yes, they are strikingly like the markings upon Iphantemel. I am convinced this was indeed one of her brood. If the pure sap of cleansed trees does not sate them, they must be driven as much by hunger as by malice.'As the North awaits the coming of Vethúg Wintermind, King Thorin III has received an urgent and unexpected summons from Ravenhill.King Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

King Thorin III has received an urgent summons from Dís, the Keeper of Ravenhill, and has asked you to accompany him to Ravenhill. You should talk to King Thorin III when you are prepared.Talk to King Thorin IIIKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

You travelled to Ravenhill and witnessed the return of the raven-chief, Arcah. King Thorin pledged to honour the old ways of friendship between Durin's Folk and the ravens of the North, and in return, Arcah sent her ravens to spy upon the plots of Karazgar and Vethúg Wintermind.Talk to King Thorin III'It has been quiet of late, ${PLAYER}, but it brings me no comfort.

'Vethúg Wintermind will come. He may arrive this very day, on the morrow, or perhaps months shall pass before at last he reveals himself. For that reason, I have spent many nights in wakefulness pondering the fate of Thikil-gundu in the Grey Mountains. Is that the fate that shall befall Erebor? Will the folk of Dale and Eryn Lasgalen soon know all too well the cold that overtook us in the North?

'It does me no good to dwell on such thoughts, and indeed, there are more pressing matters this day.

'Dís, the Keeper of Ravenhill and sister of Thorin Oakenshield, sent me an urgent summons requesting my presence at Ravenhill. It is a strange request, I think. There is no ill will between the ravens and Durin's Folk, but we have grown distant since the days of Roäc the raven-chief. His descendants are not known to me, and I do not think any in this realm have seen a raven of his stock in many years.

'I would ask that you accompany me to Ravenhill, ${PLAYER}. If we have need to return swiftly to Erebor, we shall ride together.''Let us depart for Ravenhill, ${PLAYER}.''Patience will serve us well, ${PLAYER}.

'Arcah possesses the wisdom of Roäc -- of this, I am certain. Her ravens are fewer in number, but their eyes remain keen in matters of spying. With their aid, we might sooner learn the truth of the visions you were granted.

'Why has Vethúg not yet come to Erebor? What does Karazgar seek in Dol Guldur? And how has he travelled so many miles in so short a time?

'We have sent the ravens forth, and we must now wait upon the tidings of their return.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'The Lady and the Mirror'</rgb>Many foes await those who dare enter Anglach, the Great Foundry.Ongdrágh, Master of the Mines can be found deep within Anglach.

You should defeat Ongdrágh, Master of the Mines.Defeat Ongdrágh, Master of the MinesCandúr can be found at the Udûn Foothold.

You should return to Candúr and apprise him of your efforts.Talk to Candúr'Reports have come in that enemy forces are gathering within Anglach. Ongdrágh, Master of the Mines, has returned to rally the Captain of the Pit's remaining soldiers. They must be quelled before they become a greater threat to our mission.

'When you are ready, I will direct you to Anglach.''There is no time to waste. The enemy's forces swell within Anglach. Are you prepared to depart?''With Ongdrágh dealt with, the forces within Anglach will fall into disarray. I thank you for your assistance.'Many foes await those who dare enter the fortress of Durthang, home to the Captain of the Pit.Candúr can be found in Udûn.

You should talk Candúr.Complete Durthang: Army of the PitCompleted Durthang: Army of the Pit.CompletedAn urgent notice hangs from the board:

'Uruk-hai have been spotted in Durthang. A brave adventurer is needed to defeat foes within the fortress. Seek out Candúr in Udûn to learn more.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Durthang: The Dark Spire to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>You have successfully braved the fortress of Durthang and defeated many Uruk-hai there.Defeat the numberless hordes of Shelob's offspring in Lhingris.Defeat the numberless hordes of Shelob's offspring in Lhingris.Defeat Shelob's lesser broods in LhingrisDespite uncovering evidence that Karazgar may still lurk in Eryn Lasgalen, King Thranduil has turned his attention to his hated foe of old: Iphantemel.King Thranduil can be found in Felegoth.

King Thranduil has asked you to accompany him and his warriors to Torech Emel in an effort to put an end to the blight of Iphantemel.Talk to King ThranduilKing Thranduil can be found in Felegoth.

You have defeated Iphantemel and forever banished her blight from Eryn Lasgalen. You should talk to King Thranduil.Talk to King Thranduil'It has been mere days, ${PLAYER}, but I have learned much of things that were beyond our sight. My scouts have travelled much of Eryn Lasgalen and they have discovered far more than what we sought.

'It seems the Old Mother, Iphantemel, has become trapped in Torech Emel by the excess of her own appetite. It was she that bound Caras Tilion and blighted Mirkwood before Sauron hid within Dol Guldur. It was she who wounded me in that failed battle of old!

'Do not think I have forgotten your purpose in coming here. I have great reason to suspect that the Weeping Warrior remains in my realm, but that matter must be set aside for the moment. If I have guessed Karazgar's true purpose in returning to Eryn Lasgalen, he will not find what he seeks. Indeed, there shall be time enough to find him when this task is done.

'Iphantemel must be brought low and her blight forever banished from Eryn Lasgalen!''The time has come! We must put an end to Iphantemel!''You have done well to aid me and my kin, ${PLAYER}. While a few of Iphantemel's children may linger in the forest, the last great evil of Mirkwood is no more.

'As for the matter of Karazgar, I believe he has returned to seek something within Caras Tilion. I will not send you there - not yet, for this is a matter of great import to me and me alone.

'I shall search the ruins myself, and when I have need of you again, I will call upon you.'


<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Karazgar's Gambit'</rgb>Banners bearing the symbol of Lhaereth the Stained fly in Seregost's courtyards and terraces. They should be destroyed in defiance.Banners of the Stained can be found in Seregost's courtyards and terraces.

