<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Barad-dûr: Realm of the Black Word to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>'These rare texts should be studied by the Lore-masters of Minas Tirith. I will give these tomes to Isnír for study.'A wealth of lore awaits those who brave the Bones of Barad-dûr.

<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest.</rgb>Defeat Kathanûl.Defeat KathanûlYou should return to Candúr and apprise him of your efforts.Talk to Candúr'Within the bones of Barad-dûr lie many secrets and strange objects collected by Sauron during his reign of Mordor. If we were to penetrate the ruined tower's defences, we may just yet be able to obtain some of these lost relics. Many I am sure rightfully belong to Gondor. I fear the Barad-dûr is still under command of those who serve the Black Word. Are you willing to risk a dive into the Sauron's ruins for Gondor?'

<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest. This quest can be completed with one or two adventurers.</rgb>'Careful now on your journeys.''You have slain one of the Black Word's knights? I praise you for your valiant efforts.'A wealth of lore awaits those who brave the Bones of Barad-dûr.

<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Barad-dûr: Realm of the Black Word to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>Defeat Black Númenóreans in Barad-dûr.Defeat Black Númenóreans in Barad-dûrDefeat Black Númenóreans in Barad-dûr.Defeat Black Númenóreans in Barad-dûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Candúr.Talk to CandúrA wealth of lore awaits those who brave the Bones of Barad-dûr.

<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Barad-dûr: Realm of the Black Word to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>'You have done well, friend. Your efforts will be duly noted!'Defeat many beasts in Dor Amarth.Defeat many beasts in Dor Amarth.Defeat many beasts in Dor AmarthDefeat many beasts in Dor Amarth.Defeat many beasts in Dor Amarth.Defeat many beasts in Dor AmarthDefeat many scavengers in Udûn.Defeat many scavengers in Udûn.Defeat many scavengers in UdûnDefeat many scavengers in Udûn.Defeat many scavengers in Udûn.Defeat many scavengers in Udûn.Defeat many scavengers in UdûnThose discontented with the newly-arrived refugees have been leaving angry scrawls throughout Dale.You should find angry scrawls on walls and doors throughout Dale and remove them.Remove angry scrawls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Gaumar, who stands within the Great-keep in Dale.Return to Gaumar'The discontent of Dale-folk over the new-arrived refugees has not abated, ${PLAYER}. Now angry scrawls have begun appearing on walls and doors around Dale: a bell with arrows pointing away. The meaning is clear enough to us.

