<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires Barad-dûr: Realm of the Black Word to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>You have successfully braved the Bones of Barad-dûr and defeated many Black Númenóreans there.The forces of Gundabad have made a pact with the Herald of Winter, and now occupy much of the Glimmerdeep.Find the dead ends.Find the dead endsThere is much to do while adventuring in Agarnaith.There is much to do while adventuring in Agarnaith.Complete Slayer of AgarnaithComplete Explorer of AgarnaithComplete Quests of AgarnaithThere is much to do while adventuring in Dor Amarth.There is much to do while adventuring in Dor Amarth.Complete Slayer of Dor AmarthComplete Explorer of Dor AmarthComplete Quests of Dor AmarthComplete deeds in Gorgoroth.Complete deeds in Gorgoroth.Complete Explorer of GorgorothComplete Quests of GorgorothComplete Slayer of GorgorothThe spider-haunts of Lhingris present the adventurers of Middle-earth with both great challenges and great rewards.The spider-haunts of Lhingris present the adventurers of Middle-earth with both great challenges and great rewards.Complete Slayer of LhingrisComplete Explorer of LhingrisComplete Quests of LhingrisThere is much to do while adventuring in Talath Úrui.There is much to do while adventuring in Talath Úrui.Complete Slayer of Talath ÚruiComplete Explorer of Talath ÚruiComplete Quests of Talath ÚruiComplete many deeds in Eryn Lasgalen, Dale-lands, and Erebor.Complete many deeds in Eryn Lasgalen, Dale-lands, and Erebor.Complete: Explorer of the NorthComplete: Quests of the NorthComplete: Slayer of the NorthThere is much to do while adventuring in Udûn.There is much to do while adventuring in Udûn.Complete Slayer of UdûnComplete Explorer of UdûnComplete Quests of UdûnLong before the great cold-drake Vethúg Wintermind froze the halls of Thikil-gundu, the Longbeards delved the Steel Keep in the depths of the Grey Mountains.The halls of Thikil-gundu delve deep into the Wrathhorn.Discover Durûz-mazal, the Chamber of FacesDiscover Bekâr-mazal, the Arming-chamberDiscover the Smithies of Kall-khebâbDiscover Balb-gundu, the FrostdelfDiscover Zashar-tûmun, the Ruin-dwellingsDiscover the Feast-house of Amrâg-zaharDiscover the Lore-trove of Afhân-binnînDiscover the Depths of AkhatârDiscover Razûkh-zahari, the Room of RainDiscover Thikil-nesad, the Steel SeatDiscover the Hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khaltDespite the efforts of the Elves, the Taurogrim have returned to Tholkát in Eryn Lasgalen.Taurog-dens can be found in Tholkát in northern Eryn Lasgalen.

You should destroy Taurog-dens in Tholkát.Destroy Taurog-dens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thranduil can be found in Felegoth.

You should talk to Thranduil.Talk to Thranduil'The Taurogrim have returned out of the lingering shadows of Eryn Lasgalen, and they seek to overrun Tholkát once more.

'Go, destroy their dens and drive them off!''Thank you, ${CLASS}. We must ensure that the Taurogrim never regain a foothold in Eryn Lasgalen.'Urudanî, the mysterious flame-wraith under the command of Borangos the horror, has been seen many times, entering and exiting the prison fortress of Naerband. Her work with Thraknûl, Sauron's former the chief torturer, lies within the dungeons of the Direhold -- the results of their work more would surely aid the great Rogmul.Complete the deed Dungeons of Naerband -- Tier 1Complete the deed Dungeons of Naerband -- Tier 2Complete the deed Challenge: Take a Turn on the RackComplete the deed Dungeons of Naerband: Lost LoreComplete the deed Dungeons of Naerband: Flame-slayerComplete the deed Dungeons of Naerband: Ghâsh-hai-slayerComplete the deed Dungeons of Naerband: Scourge-slayerNow that the Lake-town Smugglers are no longer a threat, it is time to consider the empty position of Master. Join Dagrun as she prepares for an important dinner.Frekur, Orgrand, Rikolf, Maeriel, and Hoskuld can be found in Lake-town.

You should talk to Frekur, Orgrand, Rikolf, Maeriel, and Hoskuld.Talk to FrekurTalk to OrgrandTalk to RikolfTalk to MaerielTalk to HoskuldDagrun is waiting for you near the Master's manor.

You should talk to Dagrun.Talk to DagrunDagrun is waiting for you near the Master's manor.

You should talk to Dagrun.Complete: The Deadly DinnerDagrun can be found in the Master's manor.

You should talk to Dagrun.Talk to Dagrun'I didn't think you would get anything else out of Skótmun, but it was worth a try. We know more than enough to lock him away for a long time. Now I have something else to speak to you about, ${PLAYER}.

'The Elders will choose the next Master tonight. Everyone considered for the position is invited to a feast. I have just received my invitation, and it says here that I can bring one guest. I would like that guest to be you.

'Oh, I know about you, ${PLAYER}. World-traveller, war hero, known to the Kings of Rohan and Gondor, known to the Elves of Mirkwood, Rivendell, Lórien, and the Dwarves of Erebor! Friend of Wizards! All of that aside, you have aided us in bringing the most notorious villain in Lake-town to justice! Yes, you will be a very impressive guest, indeed.

'Before the event, I suggest you go around town and meet the others who are being considered as the next Master. I believe they are Frekur, Orgrand, and Rikolf. Oh, there will be an ambassador from the Elves and one from the dwarves present as well. Once you are done, meet me at the Manor. Wear something fitting for the occasion!''Who are you, and why are you interrupting my work? Oh, yes, you're Dagrun's guest for the dinner. Hmph. I don't know what all the fuss is about, you seem awfully common to me. Yes, yes, I will see you tonight. Go away now, I'm very busy.''What have we here? I don't believe we've been introduced, friend. I am Orgrand, a humble servant of the people. Ah, you're Dagrun's guest for tonight, aren't you? My, you must have some wonderful tales to tell! Oh, but save them for tonight. I'm afraid I am already late for my appearance at the brand new orphanage, dedicated to those lost when the Easterlings attacked. Good to meet you, the pleasure was mine!''Oh, hello there. Dear, we have a guest.''Mae govannen, friend. I am Maeriel, ambassador of the Woodland realm, sent to make sure the King's interests are represented in the election of the new Master. All the peoples of this region, whether they be Elf, dwarf, or Man, are connected. We must make sure the Elders of Lake-town remember this. We will talk more tonight.''Well met! I am Hoskuld of Durin's Folk, here by King Thorin III's orders to make sure Erebor's interests are known to the Lake-town Elders.

'I will be truthful with you, ${PLAYER}. We have heard some rumblings of dissent and talk of Lake-town seceding from the Kingdom of Dale! That is absolutely not something we dwarves want, as both Dale and Lake-town are important in the greater trade network! I will make sure these Men understand that secession cannot happen if they want to keep receiving goods from the Lonely Mountain!''There you are - and right on time. I must thank you again for accepting my offer. The folk we dine with tonight think highly of themselves and highly of their stations. Such airs are not to my taste, but it will not do to offend. No, we must smile and nod. Are those your best garments? Then let us get on with this.''Ready to go inside?''I can hardly believe this is real, ${PLAYER}. So many killed right in front of our eyes. And then, I was named Master! I believe it will take some time to digest everything that just happened, but time is something I can no longer afford to lose. I must rise to this challenge and lead the people of Lake-town. I will not let my home be plunged into chaos in the wake of all this.

'I don't think this is over, either. The murderer could not have acted alone. Someone is trying to cause strife in the Kingdom of Dale. Please, keep your eyes open, and be careful.'A small number of Dale-folk continue to speak out against the Easterling refugees and cloud the minds of many others.You should publically deter discontented Dale-folk who are speaking against the refugees.Deter the discontented (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Gaumar.Talk to Gaumar'In market stalls and street corners, a misguided few still murmur against the dispossessed from Rhûn, and their talk clouds the minds of others.

'If you, a hero of the war and a symbol of goodness, would address those malcontents, it would change many minds among the folk of Dale.

'Even if not all of their minds might be turned, it would do well to make those from Rhûn feel more welcome.''I fear it will not be the last reminder they need, but do not doubt your efforts, ${PLAYER}. You have changed many minds in Dale today!'Due to recent events, King Thranduil Swiftstream has decided to close the Woodland Realm to outsiders. This has caused some friction among his people, especially the Raft-elves. Thranduil would like you to report to Loeglond to see what can be done to ease these tensions.Thranduil has asked you to head to Loeglond.

You should leave Felegoth.Leave FelegothGalion wishes to speak with you inside Felegoth.

