You should talk to Lorndúr.Talk to Lorndúr'Since I have closed my realm to trade and travel, there has been unrest and murmuring among the raft-elves who dwell along the river. Although my judgment was measured and with good reason, I deem I may not have considered all that I should.

'Will you travel to Loeglond and speak to Lorndúr? Tell him that I will weigh re-opening trade with Lake-town, should the route be made completely safe.'You explain to the despondent Elf that King Thranduil has agreed to re-open trade if it can be made perfectly safe. He looks relieved.

'What excellent tidings you bring, ${CLASS}!  If we can re-open trade, my kin can finally return to the waters. Your aid would help us overcome the many difficulties we now face.''Hold, ${PLAYER}. Hear me before you go farther.  Without open trade between Lake-town and Dale, the raft-elves are idle and purposeless. 

'But that is not all. There is talk among the river reeds of the ending of the age. Some wonder if King Thranduil and the other High Elves will leave us to sail west. Some argue they should. Fear not - we are Elves, all of us, though our kindred never looked upon the farther shore. There will be no treason or treachery, though other ills may come of it.

'Put the raft-elves back to work and there will be little time for such talk, and much good will shall be restored.’You have discovered the entrance to Glimmerdeep.To earn this deed, you must discover the entrance to Glimmerdeep.Discover the entrance to GlimmerdeepGrants completion of deed: Discovery: GlimmerdeepBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Discovery: Glimmerdeep'Now, my little fellows, where be you a-going to, puffing like a bellows? What's the matter here then? Tell me what's your trouble!

