<rgb=#FF0000>The Trail of Rust quest arc will continue after completing the Refugees in Dale quest arc which begins with King Bard II in Dale.</rgb>Complete the <rgb=#FF0000>Refugees in Dale quest arc</rgb>You should talk to Erna, who can be found in the Great-keep in Dale.Talk to Queen Regent ErnaThe Easterling refugees can be found throughout Dale.

You should speak with the Dorwinion and Chayasír Easterlings who have come within Dale's walls.You should reassure the concerned Dale-folk that they are not in danger from the Easterling refugees.Distressed Dorwinions can be found in Dale.

You should comfort Dorwinions, still in shock from the devastation in the east and the difficulties of acceptance from some of those in the city of Dale.You should talk to Queen Regent Erna, who can be found within the Great-keep in Dale.Return to Erna'From what you say, there can be no doubt that this Easterling - Utûkel - was one of the Jangovar who recently assailed the folk of this valley.

'Though the remnant of that army lingers on the far shore of the Long Lake, the brunt of their campaign was against Dale, where the crown of our people is seated. We would be remiss if we did not send word of this to the young king there.

'And what better emissary could be found than you, ${PLAYER}? Yes, I think you had better go and tell them what you have learned. You will want to find the Great-keep, in the north part of Dale.''I've had enough of your kind of help, ${RACE}. Speak to my brother or mother if you must hold your nose so high up in the air.''After careful consideration, we have decided to allow the Dorwinion and Chayasír who seek refuge into the city. Some have chosen to remain in their camps across the river, and this, too, we shall permit.

'My concern is for those we have welcomed within our walls, however. Will you go among them and see they are faring well, and being treated as guests should be?''At last Dale helps us and lets us within its walls. I say we should do what we can to help them, little though it be. Me, myself, I have always cared for animals. Why, in my home, far away, the farmers would bring whatever old hounds or young calves were sick, and I would look after them.

'If there are any animals that need looking after in Dale, I offer my help.''Before I fled my home, I farmed the land. Oh, how dry the soil was there. Hard work it was, farming that soil! But we knew many tricks, we did, to make things grow. I look in wonder on this green land with its running water! Still, I bet you I might teach these farmers a few of my tricks all the same.''I judge from your dress that you have known battle and have journeyed far. Am I right? The Chayasír journey too, even before we fled the devastation in Rhûn, but battle we have shunned. Unlike the Jangovar, with their lies of killing glory and red-eyed gods!

'Me? I am a humble mender of clothes. Dale have shown themselves to be no Jangovar, and I would gladly give my talents to them.''A darkness came in the East, and it was no longer safe there. So I took my children with me and we fled, side by side with so many others. I am weary beyond belief, and my heart cries out every time I think what my children have come through. And yet it also cries with joy that I still have them with me.

'I will make a new life here and travel no more, if the people of Dale allow it.''I am a worker and carver of wood. We Chayasír come to these lands hoping for a new life. How happy I would be to carve and work wood for the people of Dale.''I hope these Easterlings leave soon. I certainly do not welcome them here.''Many of the Chayasír and Dorwinion lost their homes in Rhûn. They are strong to be able to lose everything and carry on. I do not think I would be able to do that if I lost Dale.''We have done all we can, for now, I think, for these poor peoples from Rhûn. I hope many of them will make this place their home, and that we shall come to grow together as flowers in a field.'With harp in hand, Hithlos looks to lift people's spirits within the caverns of Felegoth.Wine can be found within Felegoth's wine cellar.

You should fetch some wine.Retrieve wine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Wood Elves can be found in Felegoth.

You should give wine to Elves within Felegoth.Many Elves live within the halls of Felegoth.

You should dance with some of the Elves.Hithlos can be found in Felegoth.

You should talk to Hithlos.Talk to Hithlos'Do you feel the swell in the air and the cheer within these halls? Hmm, yes I also feel as though something more is missing. Perhaps the Elves could use some wine and dancing. I shall continue to play. If you would, make haste to the wine cellar in Felegoth and procure some wine for the Wood Elves.''Now, everyone is merry and my joyous music brings light into the cavern halls. I thank you. Please continue listening to my music for as long as you wish. You are a kind ${RACE}.'Someone has posted a task to collect Bristled Fur. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire Bristled Fur.Wanted: Bristled Fur from the Strongholds of the North. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: Bristled Fur from the Strongholds of the North.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect Petrified Branches. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire Petrified Branches.Wanted: Petrified Branches from the Strongholds of the North. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: Petrified Branches from the Strongholds of the North.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Elves of Lothlórien seek relics from Mordor.Gather lost relics.Gather lost relicsGather lost relics.Gather lost relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A collection box can be found in the Court of Lothlórien.

Bring the relics to the Court of Lothlórien.The Elves of Lothlórien seek relics from Mordor.You have brought the Elves of Lothlórien a great gift from your journeys through Mordor.Ingold, a soldier of Gondor, has scouted Dor Amarth and is concerned with the growing numbers of foes gathering at the encampment of Fushaum Tûm.Ingold has asked you to defeat the Rogmul Emissary visiting Fushaum Tûm and to defeat those who may be persuaded by the Nameless creature.Defeat the Rogmul EmissaryDefeat foes in Fushaum Tûm (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'I did not believe my own eyes when I saw a nameless creature of flame enter Fushaum Tûm. It must be another one of these emissaries from Nargroth that I have heard about. We can not let Fushaum Tûm and Nargroth join forces. It would spell doom for the Gondorian presence here.'A notice is pinned to the board, signed by Ingold:

