Langhár sniffs the air.

'Ah, a familiar scent on the wind! Follow me, and stay close, lest you find yourself lost in these woods!''We have the Beorning. Now, we need to retreat, quickly! We will soon be swarmed by Taurogrim! I will have to return later with a stronger force.'Authi Gem-cutter has asked for your help with bringing his grievance against Khîl Tale-spinner before the king.King Thorin has chosen to hear Authi Gem-cutter's grievance, but he will not do so at his throne.Talk to Hrostyr, King Thorin's personal guardKing Thorin has chosen to go among his people for the hearing of Authi's complaint.Accompany Authi as he presents his case before King ThorinKing Thorin has chosen to go among his people for the hearing of Authi's complaint.Listen to Khîl's response before the kingKing Thorin has chosen to go among his people for the hearing of Authi's complaint.Talk to King ThorinKing Thorin has chosen to go among his people for the hearing of Authi's complaint.Listen to the judgement of King ThorinAuthi has heard the king's judgement and now wishes to speak with you.Talk to Authi'I suppose we should be going, ${PLAYER}. Let us return to my home and perhaps we can make sense of this.''This is highly irregular. Why does the king choose not to hear this grievance at his throne? Would he not be more comfortable at his high seat?''Khîl seeks to flatter me, but I am too wise a king to fall prey to such a tactic. I named my son Durin for my own reasons, and I do not feel the need to share them with Longbeards or with Zhélruka. He stays now in Járnfast with my brother Náin, Lord of the Iron Hills, and he will be king after me. If he is to be anything else is certainly beyond the sight of this Zhélruka.'

King Thorin strokes his beard, and you might detect a slight upturn among his whiskers. Does he smile in spite of Khîl's flattery or because of it?

'Durin the Deathless come again? Hmm. Imagine that!''The king ruled in my favour. Why then do I feel as if he also ruled against me? Did I win or did I lose?'The Green Lady once dwelled in the heights of the Emyn-nu-Fuin, but that was long before the darkening of Mirkwood.Tárasánë is in the Pristine Glade.

