All of King Thorin's guests have arrived, and now the feast can begin. You should talk to King Thorin.Talk to King Thorin III'Enough talk! Let us eat, ${PLAYER}!''It is a day of great celebration for Durin's Folk, ${PLAYER}. All around us the halls of Erebor echo with laughter and merriment!

'As well they should! This day, we honour our friends and our kin, and we proclaim our victory over the Enemy and those that followed him.

'Come, my friend. Let us join the others at my table!''It is a fine work, is it not? I did not choose it for you on a mere whim!'

King Thorin glances at the remaining empty seats at his table.

'Ah, but a few of my guests are still absent. I sent word to Spakorth and his warriors, but I do not know if they understood my meaning. I am certain they are about in the Hall, but I wish for them to join me at my table. Spakorth and his kin are our new friends and allies, and I would not deny them a warm welcome to Erebor.

'Would you seek out Spakorth and his kin? Send them here, and we shall soon be able to begin our feast!''Oh! ${PLAYER}, how good it is to see you!

'It has been quite the celebration already, don't you think? I have never heard such songs or seen such... dances, but I am pleased to be welcome among Durin's Folk. Do you wish to join us?'

You inform Spakorth that he, Dréri, and Náth have been summoned by the King Under the Mountain and have been granted seats at his table.

'Of course we accept his invitation! It would be a great honour to feast with King Thorin, and to thank him again for the kindness he has shown my people.

'Dréri! Náth! Come with me!''Hail, ${PLAYER}!

'I am glad to see you here at our table. You are a fine adventurer and ever a friend to those in need, and your presence here is well-earned. You are not unlike my Gimli, except you were courteous enough to attend at the time King Thorin requested.

'I know Gimli is here in the Hall, but I have not seen him in some time. I think he has gone off with Dori and Nori, but who can say? Will you find him and send him here? For that matter, send Dori and Nori as well!

'We cannot wait all day to begin the feast!''Oh, ${PLAYER}, I did not realize we had been speaking for so long!

'You see, I have been talking to Dori and Nori about my adventures, and I had just mentioned the book I discovered in the halls of Khazad-dûm. It concerns their brother, Ori, and Balin's expedition, but I should not tell such stories on a day of celebration. It is not the time for such things....

'We shall go to join the King Under the Mountain at his table at once! All of this talk has made me hungry!''Thank you for gathering my folk, ${PLAYER}. There is little sense in having a feast if there is no one with which to share it.

'This is a fine assemblage of friends and kin, but one of my guests has still not arrived. It was he I hoped to see most of all, for his long absence from his people should be ended.

'Let us wait just a few more moments more on his arrival, and then we shall begin the feast.''It brings me great joy to see the many Dwarves of Durin's Folk and our kin from the East united as one. If we do not recognize and celebrate such times of peace, it is certain they will be lost to us evermore.'

King Thorin III pauses for a moment.

'Ah... I have spoken enough! Let us share in this feast together!'Having found convincing proof, Sírithon devises a plan to catch the Loeglond thief.Patrol Loeglond.Check on the trap.Check on the trapTalk to Sírithon.Talk to SírithonInvestigate the noises.Investigate the noisesReturn to the trap.Return to the trapTalk to Sírithon.Talk to Sírithon'It would seem that Esgaroth may house our thief.''Not one movement or sign of an intruder?'

Before he can speak again, shouting erupts from the other end of Loeglond.

'What is that commotion? ${PLAYER}, go quickly. See what it is!''We laid our trap so carefully, only to be fooled by a ruse! These are sly and attentive thieves, indeed, ${PLAYER}.

'Sly - but not stealthier than the eyes of an Elf, ${PLAYER}. Not quite! For as we returned, I caught a glimpse - no more than a glimpse, though alas - of some shadowed figure fleeing the cart! The direction they fled, however, was plain as day. They fled towards Esgaroth.'You have tracked Athálrik to his retreat in the highlands west of Lake-town.You should look for Athálrik, eastward from Víthog.Find AthálrikYou should look for Athálrik, eastward from Víthog.Find AthálrikFollow the sounds eastward.Find AthálrikYou have found Athálrik. Now confront him.Confront AthálrikPursue Athálrik.Pursue AthálrikDefeat Athálrik.Defeat AthálrikYou should search Athálrik for the Chayasír's memory-cloth.Search Athálrik'You will find him between here and the bluffs to the north-east that overlook the Long Lake. That is where he roams. I do not follow him, no. I leave him to himself and his moods.'You find the memory-cloth clutched in his hands.Erna is worried about her son Bryn who has become more and more distant and aggravated.Try to speak with Bryn.Talk to BrynFollow Bryn and meet his friend.Follow Bryn to meet his friendListen to Bryn's exchange with Akshir.Listen to Bryn's exchange with AkshirBeckon Bryn to you.<rgb=#FF0000>Beckon</rgb> Bryn to youListen to the Weeping Warrior.Listen to the Weeping WarriorTalk to Bryn.Talk to Bryn'Though I can barely face my family right now, I know that we should return and tell them of rust-man and of what evil deceits he is capable.''What do you want of me, ${PLAYER}? Have you come to mock me again, or to shame me before my mother and brother?

'Look around you. Beyond Dale's walls, our kingdom hangs by a thread. We say the Easterlings are our vanquished foes, and yet they roam freely through the Dale-lands. We say many things that are wrong. My friend has shown me much, and my eyes are opened now. He has shown me how much I could accomplish if I were king instead of Bard.

'I see that mocking look in your eye. You think me a child. You disbelieve me. Come with me then and you'll meet him for yourself. Then he can explain it. Oh, he does so, so much better than I do!''Who was that - that deathly creature? What had Akshir to do with him? And why did it sound as if he were taking orders from him? Tell me, ${PLAYER}! Akshir would take orders from nobody - he is wise and...

'Oh! What a fool I have been. And to think he had near convinced me to kill my own brother. Did you see? He gave me the knife to do it with. Bah! I can barely look at the awful thing. What sorcery did Akshir cast upon me? What shall I do? Flee in exile and never return?'

You speak gently to Bryn, and convince him to return home, be brave and honest, and confess the truth.

'That is the thing that most terrifies me, ${PLAYER}, and so it must be the brave and right one.'Sigrun knows of Thorog and will lead the way to examine the dragon's corpse.Examine the corpse of Thorog.Examine the corpse of ThorogExamine the rust spot.Examine the rust spotExperience the vision.Experience the vision'Not much to see here but some old bones. You are ready to leave already?'You have obtained the disguise of a Nurnhoth slave, and now seek to infiltrate the meeting of the Masters of Mordor at Amon Thaur.You have come in disguise to the base of Amon Thaur. Will Dulgabêth's knights permit you to gain access to the meeting?Present yourself to the Knight of Dulgabêth at Amon ThaurOther slaves have already arrived. You should climb the stairs at Amon Thaur and join them.Climb the stairs at Amon Thaur and look for other Nurnhoth slavesYou can see other slaves to the south-east of the landing, among the pillars of Amon Thaur. You should join them in order to avoid arousing the suspicion of the enemy.Join the Nurnhoth slaves to the south-east, among the pillars of Amon ThaurYou can see other slaves to the south-east of the landing, among the pillars of Amon Thaur. You should join them in order to avoid arousing the suspicion of the enemy.Talk to the Nurnhoth slaveYou have infiltrated the meeting of the Masters of Mordor at Amon Thaur, on the slopes of Mount Doom.Observe the meeting of the Masters, and remain beneath their noticeYou have infiltrated the meeting of the Masters of Mordor at Amon Thaur, on the slopes of Mount Doom.Observe the meeting of the Masters, and remain beneath their noticeYou have infiltrated the meeting of the Masters of Mordor at Amon Thaur, on the slopes of Mount Doom.Observe the meeting of the Masters, and remain beneath their noticeLhaereth has summoned one of the Nurnhoth slaves.Talk to the Nurnhoth slaveThe slave dropped a pouch when he died, and now Laereth calls for you to bring it to her.Pick up the fallen pouch where it liesYou collected the fallen pouch, and now Lhaereth wants you to bring it to her.Lhaereth has commanded you to remain where you are.Observe the meeting of the Masters, and remain beneath their noticeDulgabêth and his knights have been betrayed. You should escape down the stairs and away from Amon Thaur before it is too late for you to get away!Escape down the stairs without being discoveredDulgabêth and his knights have been betrayed. You should escape down the stairs and away from Amon Thaur before it is too late for you to get away!Escape down the stairs without being discovered'You did not arrive with the others. Do you not fear the lash?

'Ha! It is no concern of mine! Climb the stairs and look for the others of your kind, if you dare! Dulgabêth will deal whatever punishment he deems sufficient. I look forward to the music of your screams, slave.

'Now go! Go!'Yadêphal looks at you with disinterest, but there is no recognition in his eye. The clothes you wear blind Dulgabêth's emissary to your identity. He does not know you.

'Move along, slave!' he barks at you.'I do not... feel well...

'What did the Mistress... give to me...?''I... I cannot...

'Something is... wrong...'Lhaereth barely looks at you as she takes the pouch from your hands.

'Stay here, slave. I may have further use for you,' she says, an unmistakable air of menace in her voice.You have descended a secret stairway into a hidden wing of the dungeons of Dol Guldur, where intense shadow covers its lost chambers.Intense shadow blankets the area. What evils might this forgotten chamber have held before the fall of Sauron?Cross the bridge and explore the room beyondA powerful presence has left its mark upon this chamber, and fell voices whisper of the past.Witness the shadowy impressions evil has left upon this chamberThere may be more to discover within this Room of Voices.Examine objects within the Room of VoicesA powerful presence has left its mark upon this chamber, and fell voices whisper of the past.Witness the shadowy impressions evil has left upon this chamberThere may be more to discover within this Room of Voices.Examine objects within the Room of VoicesA powerful presence has left its mark upon this chamber, and fell voices whisper of the past.Witness the shadowy impressions evil has left upon this chamberSomeone is approaching from the western passage!Cautiously investigate the western passageSomeone is approaching from the western passage!Cautiously investigate the western passageYou thought her dead, but somehow Sigileth of the Hidden Guard is still alive!Talk to Sigileth in the Room of Voices'Is it really you, ${PLAYER}? I feared all my companions among the Hidden Guard were dead, but here you stand!

'I made a place of my own in these dungeons and levied terror upon their fell inhabitants in the name of my Lady. Let us return to my secret lodgings before we press through the Room of Voices, and I will collect the few belongings I left behind. I could not pass through its deep shadow on my own, but together I believe we can.

'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}.'Although Galadriel remains doubtful that Karazgar has returned to the ruins of Dol Guldur, she has mustered a company to aid you in your search for the Weeping Warrior in the depths of Dol Dhannen.Karazgar may be found somewhere within the ruins of Gostador.

You have returned to Dol Dhannen in search of Karazgar and have descended into Gostador. You should search for Karazgar.Search for signs of Karazgar in GostadorA powerful presence has left its mark upon this chamber, and fell voices whisper of the past.Witness the shadowy impressions evil has left upon this chamberThere may be more left to discover within the Room of Voices.Examine objects within the Room of Voices in GostadorA powerful presence has left its mark upon this chamber, and fell voices whisper of the past.Witness the shadowy impressions evil has left upon this chamberThere may be more left to discover within the Room of Voices.Examine objects within the Room of Voices in GostadorA powerful presence has left its mark upon this chamber, and fell voices whisper of the past.Witness the shadowy impressions evil has left upon this chamberSigileth is standing at the edge of the Room of Voices in Gostador.

You have witnessed many events of Karazgar's past, but did not find Karazgar in Gostador. After waiting for a time, Sigileth has come to find you.Talk to Sigileth in the Room of Voices'Are you ready? Let us climb from this ruin, and leave this place behind evermore!''What has happened, ${PLAYER}? Did Karazgar escape by some secret path?'

You explain to Sigileth that shadowy impressions revealed much of the history of Karazgar and Sauron in Dol Guldur. After the impressions were interrupted when you first came to Gostador and discovered Sigileth, you were meant to return and witness the last remnants of the Necromancer's evil lingering within the Room of Voices.

'I am not certain I understand, but I believe your words. Karazgar is an elusive foe, but it seems something of his mind was revealed to you. Let us hope there is an advantage to be gained from it!

'The Orcs that remain here have grown hungry and wild. If you have found what you sought, we should leave this place.'You have come with Thorin's Company, his sister Dís, and Gandalf the Wizard to ensure the Arkenstone still remains entombed with Thorin Oakenshield within Mazal Akrâz, the Chamber of Glory.Gandalf is waiting to speak with you at the top of Mazal Akrâz, the Chamber of Glory.Talk to Gandalf at the top of Mazal AkrâzGandalf agreed to meet you by the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield, at the bottom of Mazal Akrâz, the Chamber of Glory.Descend the steps in Mazal Akrâz and make your way to the tomb of Thorin OakenshieldDís stands by the tomb of her brother and her sons, in Mazal Akrâz, the Chamber of Glory.Talk to Dís in Mazal AkrâzThe dwarves of Thorin's Company, his sister Dís, and Gandalf have come to Mazal Akrâz to see if the Arkenstone remains within.Remain alert while Gandalf and the dwarves open the tombGandalf is by the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield, in Mazal Akrâz.Talk to Gandalf in Mazal AkrâzRelieved that the Arkenstone remains with Thorin, Gandalf wishes to say a few words to you and to the dwarves.Listen to the words of GandalfRelieved that the Arkenstone remains with Thorin, Gandalf wishes to say a few words to you and to the dwarves.Listen to Gandalf's lecture on the evolution of wordsGandalf is by the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield, in Mazal Akrâz.Talk to Gandalf in Mazal AkrâzGandalf is by the tomb of Thorin Oakenshield, in Mazal Akrâz.Listen to the words of Gandalf'Thank you for suggesting this excursion, ${PLAYER}. I enjoyed seeing my kin again, though they be gone these many years. You will always be welcome at Raven-hill whenever you wish to visit me.

'As for your wizard, he talks too much. Leave him behind when you come to visit.''It seemed appropriate for Dís to go on ahead and for the rest of us to follow along behind. Her brother Thorin and her sons Fíli and Kíli lie entombed within, and while our purpose here is one of importance, I do not wish to work any disrespect upon the fallen.

'I will meet you at the bottom, ${PLAYER}. Keep watch upon your footing.''I have explored many of the dwarf-holds that stand still in Middle-earth, but few can compare to the grand chambers within and beneath the Lonely Mountain. Look about you at Mazal Akrâz, and know that its beauty and grandeur is deserved by those who rest within!''The Battle of Five Armies claimed the lives of Thorin Oakenshield and his nephews Fíli and Kíli. All three of them fought bravely and well, and without their courage things that day might have gone differently. We owe them each a debt, even today, so many years later.''We must take a brief rest, and then we will be off again. Do not wait on my account, ${PLAYER}! I will be along shortly. These steps are perilous for the young, but what can be done? Nothing. I show them as much patience as I am able, and I ask you to do the same.''I wanted to say something to you, ${PLAYER}, but I have not seen an opportunity before now. I wish to thank you for the aid you supplied to my son Bósi during the expedition of the Iron Garrison to Khazad-dûm. It has ended in failure, to his grief and shame, but that does not eliminate the efforts you and other good-hearted folk supplied to him in their attempted conquest.

'I thank you on his behalf. We will not forget the Iron Garrison; neither will we forget those who fought alongside our dwarves in the darkness of that kingdom, though it remain lost.''Bifur and Bósi tell me you fought alongside my son when the Iron Garrison failed. I thank you for standing by him, ${PLAYER}.'

Bofur stands silently for a moment, gazing away into the darkness of Mazal Akrâz.

'I had hoped he would live a long life, and when his days were spent at last he would be put to rest beside me and our kin in the Blue Mountains, but that is not to be. Instead he departs soonest, and lies now in a tomb even grander than this, for he rests in Khazad-dûm. Alas for Brogur, alas for my son! He was a finer dwarf than I, and had more to offer his people.''Mazal Akrâz was delved deep, fashioned with the labour of our finest dwarves, for Thorin and his nephews deserved a grand tomb. But it cannot hold a flickering candle to the glory of Khazad-dûm, where my son now adventures! The reports I have heard from Bósi and the Iron Garrison fill me with pride, and I delight at their successes!''It has been some time since my son Brogur has written to me of his adventures with the Iron Garrison in Khazad-dûm. By all accounts, the avenues and halls of that kingdom make for beautiful sights like no other!''Thorin was my cousin. I hope he rests well, and still keeps the Arkenstone safe. He came to regret some of the words he spoke to Bilbo; in the end he repented of them and they parted in kindness. We all thought it right that the Heart of the Mountain be laid to rest with Thorin. The disagreements concerning its disposition came later.''I and my retinue arrived during the Battle of Dale, and joined the fighting with great relish. This visit to the tomb of my cousin fills me with more worry than did the exertion of that battle. If the Heart of the Mountain does not lie within, what then will we do?

'Bah, we will soon know. We are near to the platform.''I am ready, ${PLAYER}. Let us see what there is to see.''It eases my heart to know the Arkenstone remains with Thorin, but this means the decline of his people's craft-skill must have another cause. A wizard's guess is not the same as any other's, ${PLAYER}, and it is the guess of this wizard that the loss of the dwarf-rings might be to blame for this decay. The ring Angya, called Handórm by the dwarves, was taken from Thráin by Sauron and must have perished in the fall of Barad-dûr.''From Dál-haim came Dálheim, which passed then to Dale-home, and is now Dale. Geirjarn became Girion, whose necklace caused much trouble between Thranduil of the Wood and the dwarves of the Mountain. Of all my many names, that which I wear in the North was not first; even that came from Wandalb, for Frumgar called me the Elf of the Wand, not knowing my true nature. Wood, Lake, Mountain, and Stone... each has their own words, and even when they speak of the same thing they may not find understanding.'

Gandalf looks at you closely, a curious look in his eye.

'${PLAYER}, what if the artifact for which we seek, this Bugdatish, never existed at all? Since this journey began neither friend nor foe have learned aught of it. No sign of this relic can be found. What if Ugrukhôr seeks an artifact that never was? Words can mean different things in different contexts, my friend, and even a small change can greatly affect a word's meaning. Can it be that Ugrukhôr does not look for that which we assumed?'You have been summoned by Galadriel, Lady of Lórien, to discuss matters concerning the kingdoms of the north.Galadriel can be found either at the Court of Celeborn or in Caras Galadhon.

You should speak with Galadriel.Galadriel can be found either at the Court of Celeborn or in Caras Galadhon.

You should speak with Galadriel.King Thranduil can be found in Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen. A swift horse in Southern Mirkwood will bring you to Tham Taerdol in Eryn Lasgalen, not far from the Elvenking's halls. Find such a swift horse in the ruins of Ost Galadh, in Emyn Lûm.Speak with King Thranduil in the halls of Felegoth, in Eryn LasgalenYou have been summoned by Galadriel, Lady of Lórien, to discuss matters concerning the kingdoms of the north.

You should meet Galadriel either at the Court of Celeborn or in Caras Galadhon.'King Thranduil of the Woodland realm and I met in council. We spoke of the northern kingdoms and their peoples: the Elves that walk Felegoth's cavernous halls, the Men of Dale and those who dwell by the Long Lake, and the dwarves that live beneath Erebor, the Lonely Mountain. Much evil and darkness has left those lands, but it has not left them untouched.

'I ask that you do your part to restore peace to the north. Speak with Thranduil in the halls of Felegoth. You can find a swift horse to the lands of the Elvenking by going to the ruins of Ost Galadh in Emyn Lûm, located in Southern Mirkwood. A horse will bear you swiftly to Tham Taerdol, and in the woods to the north-east you will find Felegoth.''King Thranduil of the Woodland realm and I met in council. We spoke of the northern kingdoms and their peoples: the Elves that walk Felegoth's cavernous halls, the Men of Dale and those who dwell by the Long Lake, and the dwarves that live beneath Erebor, the Lonely Mountain. Much evil and darkness has left those lands, but it has not left them untouched.

'I ask that you do your part to restore peace to the north. Speak with Thranduil in the halls of Felegoth. You can find a swift horse to the lands of the Elvenking by going to the ruins of Ost Galadh in Emyn Lûm, located in Southern Mirkwood. A horse will bear you swiftly to Tham Taerdol, and in the woods to the north-east you will find Felegoth.''Hail, ${PLAYER}. I have been expecting your arrival.'You have been tasked with retrieving the great eagle egg while keeping it safe from cracks or punctures. The safety of the egg is of the utmost importance, which is sure to be compromised in the hands of a stone-giant.The dangerous snow-covered paths twist up the mountain side in front of you.

