<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires The Burning Mountain: Blood Wings to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>You have successfully braved the mountain and defeated many Merrevail there.King Thorin III hopes to restore the Lonely Mountain to its former glory, but deadly conflicts and an inexplicable loss in crafting skill have plagued the Dwarves of Durin's Folk.King Thorin III and Bráthi can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain. Dís can be found at Raven Hill, to the south-west of Erebor.

King Thorin III has asked you to aid him in restoring Erebor and unifying the Stout-axes and Longbeards.Aid Bráthi with 'Essays of Old'Aid Dís with 'The Ravens of the North'Aid King Thorin III with 'Forging Trust'King Thorin III can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain.

You have done much to aid King Thorin and his folk, and you should now return to him.Talk to King Thorin III'Long have I known the troubles hindering Erebor, and time has not abated any of them.

'My father, Dáin, strengthened our alliances and brought great wealth to the North, but before the end of his reign, he felt that something unknowable had begun to slip beyond his grasp. In truth, our crafts grew cruder and simpler, and monuments once majestic and without equal in this realm now stood in silent mockery of our declining skill. We have felt this loss for many years now, but alas, it was not the only cost we have borne with the passing of the years. Dís tends the ravens as she always has, but they do not speak to Durin's Folk as they once did. It is habit alone that keeps her at Raven Hill; our friendship of old with the ravens has faded to naught. And now, these Stout-axes come to Erebor seeking refuge and freedom from the oppressors of Mordor, and still a few among us would deny their own kin and cousins!

'These are troubles enough for any King Under the Mountain, but it falls to me to resolve them, so resolve them I shall!''You have done much for Durin's Folk, ${PLAYER}.

'We have had little time to celebrate our victories or acknowledge the sacrifices made to achieve them, and I would take this day to honour them.

'When the War was ended, I sent missives far and wide to all the Dwarves of Durin's Folk. Let us hope that many travelled to join us for this day of revelry!'The merchants of Dale believe your presence in the markets will be good for business.You should visit and be seen at the various market areas and tavern in Dale, salute merchants, congratulate happy shoppers, assist indecisive shoppers, and calm angry shoppers on the way.<rgb=#FF00FF>Salute</rgb> Dale merchants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF00FF>Calm</rgb> angry shoppers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF00FF>Congratulate</rgb> happy shoppers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF00FF>Assist</rgb> indecisive shoppers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Visit the Upper Markets, northVisit the Upper Markets, southVisit the Jolly Bell tavernVisit the Lower Markets, westVisit the Lower Markets, centralVisit the Lower Markets, southYou should return to Rótha, who can be found inside the Great-keep in Dale.Return to Rótha'I have not forgotten you, ${PLAYER}!

'Indeed, the impression was strong enough that I feel your continued presence in Dale's markets would do much for commerce. In fact - hhem! - if it were not too much of an imposition... might we again ask you to go about Dale's markets, salute some merchants, talk to those buying here and there?''If it would not be too much trouble, the merchants of Dale would - hhem! - greatly appreciate your making an appearance in the upper markets, the lower markets, and the Jolly Bell tavern, and stopping to speak with and encourage some merchants and shoppers along the way.''Ah -hhem!- I think you have made quite the impression on the folk of Dale. I think they have grown used to your presence in the markets!'

'Do not forget to come back!'There is still much to do in Gorgoroth.There is still much to do in Gorgoroth.Complete Bhol Rûdh: Siege of CorruptionComplete Bhol Rûdh: Trail of BloodComplete Bhol Rûdh: Ancient LightsComplete Barad-dûr: Realm of the Black WordComplete Barad-dûr: Ruins of DarknessComplete Barad-dûr: Lore of the PastCompleted Kála-murg: The Final StandCompleted Kála-murg: The Hoards of UngolCompleted Kála-murg: The Silken GiftCompleted The Burning Mountain: Blood WingsCompleted The Burning Mountain: Red SkiesCompleted The Burning Mountain: Black FireCompleted Durthang: The Dark SpireCompleted Durthang: Army of the PitCompleted Durthang: Order of the PitIn the aftermath of the War of the Ring, the Kingdoms of Erebor, Eryn Lasgalen, and Dale struggle to rebuild and restore their former splendour.Quests to aid the Strongholds of the North can be found in Dale, Erebor, Felegoth, Lake-town, Loeglond, and Ravenhill.

Dale, Erebor, and Eryn Lasgalen are in need of aid to restore their Kingdoms to their former splendour. You should aid them.Complete quests to aid Dale, Erebor, or Eryn Lasgalen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'In the past, it is possible that my folk were too proud to admit our need for friends and allies. I would not have us make the same mistake.

'Although our needs are great, Erebor is not alone in facing the troubles of this time. The North has suffered greatly, and the kingdoms of Men and Elves shall have need of one such as you. 

'Aid them, and we shall all be the stronger for it.''It is no longer so simple a matter to live beyond the realms of Men and dwarves. If Eryn Lasgalen is to ever truly heal, we shall have need of our allies' trust and might.

'It is true that Eryn Lasgalen has great need of your aid, but I would also ask that you see to the needs of the peoples of Dale and Erebor in restoring their lands and kingdoms.''The strength of the North is determined by each of its peoples, and we can ill-afford to be unprepared for the conflicts that lay ahead.

'Aid the peoples of Dale, Erebor, and Eryn Lasgalen in their hardships, and I shall see that your efforts are rewarded.'In the aftermath of the Battle of Dale, the Dwarves of Erebor have grown curious of newly-exposed veins of ore.Newly-exposed veins can be found in rocky areas surrounding Erebor.

Bráthi has asked you to investigate newly-exposed veins of gold around Erebor. If you recover any dwarf-gold, he has asked you to deliver it to him.Collect chunks of dwarf-gold from newly-exposed veins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bráthi can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain.

You have uncovered a substantial amount of dwarf-gold in the newly-exposed veins outside Erebor and should now return to Bráthi.'Hail, ${PLAYER}!

'I have heard much of your skill in battle, but have you a keen eye? It is said that new veins of golden ore have revealed themselves in the aftermath of the battle. Hah! Perhaps we should be the slightest bit grateful to those Easterlings after all!

'Search rocky areas around Erebor, and see what you can find! If you uncover anything, deliver it to me, and I shall see that King Thorin knows well of your contributions to Durin's Folk.''Well, what do you know? It seems Erebor's roots spread even further than we thought!

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}! I shall inform King Thorin at once!'Roaming the burning plains of Dor Amarth, Rotwing patrols with her handlers.Rotwing can be found patrolling Mordor.

