The raven you found may know where Vethúg and Karazgar have gone in the wake of the attack on Erebor. You should talk to Arcah and learn what it saw.Talk to ArcahKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

You have learned that Karazgar passed into the Grey Mountains in pursuit of Vethúg Wintermind. You should inform King Thorin of what you learned.Talk to King Thorin III'It is good to look upon you once more, ${PLAYER}.

'Vethúg Wintermind was a cunning foe, but his defeat was a great victory for Durin's Folk. When he fled the battle, I believe he flew for Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep, but where he has gone matters not. If his wounds have not yet ended him, they soon will!

'As for Karazgar, it seems his plots have come to naught... or so he would have us believe. I received word that Karazgar passed near to Ravenhill shortly after the battle against Vethúg was ended. He moved silently among the trees, but even still, Arcah's people spied him from above and said that he made for the Grey Mountains.

'Why did he not come to Erebor to claim his prey? I want to know his purpose in taking that path!''Ah, ${PLAYER}, I have tidings both good and ill.

'Karazgar has gone from the North, and his followers have departed in his wake. When the battle turned, he followed the cold-drake into the Grey Mountains. Vethúg Wintermind must seek to heal his hurts in the Steel Keep of old, but he shall have little time to rest from battle.

'I do not think that the strife between Karazgar and Vethúg is ended. In the mind of one who tames dragons, a weakened foe would be an easier one to break. Who can say if such things will come to pass?

'Tell King Thorin what I have told you and the North shall again know peace.''Hail, ${PLAYER}.

'What did you learn of Karazgar's plots in the North?'

You tell King Thorin III that Karazgar has travelled into the Grey Mountains in pursuit of the wounded Vethúg Wintermind.

'Hah! Let him go! Karazgar and Vethúg can bring each other to ruin. I will not involve Durin's Folk in their squabbling any longer! We have defended Erebor! We have defended our home! If Vethúg still dwelt upon the hoards of Thikil-gundu, it is there he can die with the knowledge that he was bested. The sacrifices of Dáin I and Frór have been avenged!

'Now, I must put an end to my kinsfolks' wild thoughts of reclaiming Thikil-gundu....'

<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Trouble Under the Mountain'</rgb>One of the Beornings has been found, but Sterkist is still missing. Langhár needs your help rescuing him from the clutches of the Taurogrim.The Taurogrim took Sterkist further north.

You should look for Sterkist.Find any sign of SterkistLanghár has run further into the woods, to the north.

You should find Langhár.Find LanghárSterkist has been taken by the Taurogrim!

You should save Sterkist!Speak with Langhár and complete "Deep in the Darkening Wood"You have escaped the Taurogrim and rescued Sterkist.

You should talk to Langhár and Sterkist.Talk to LanghárTalk to SterkistYou have escaped the Taurogrim and rescued Sterkist.

You should talk to Thorlind.Talk to Thorlind'There is no time to delay, ${PLAYER}. I saw them take Sterkist further north. We must pursue them! Go, I will be right behind you.''Hurry, we must save Sterkist!''We appear to be safe, for now. You are quite the fighter, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for helping Sterkist. It is about time we move on and return home, I think.''Thank you for your help, friend. I cannot say I expected to be kidnapped by mythical wood-trolls on this journey! Our task was to trade with the Elves of Felegoth and then return. Oh, that reminds me, I think many of the things from our cart are scattered about the woods....''The Beornings may catch their breath here for a short time, but should not tarry long. I will keep watch, but must soon return to Felegoth. We are still near to danger.

'The Taurogrim have returned and at a time when the spiders have all but vanished. I do not think this a coincidence. They were a dangerous enemy of my people long ago, and we must not allow them to return to force unfettered. I have some more work for you, friend, while we are near to their encampment.

'After you have ensured the Beornings are safely at the Forest Gate, you should report this threat to King Thranduil. I will return myself after I am finished here.''Sterkist is through here, I am certain! We will surely have to face the Taurogrim inside. Come with me!'The lore-master Fróthi ponders the theft of the dragon-tooth necklace from Erebor.You should speak with Fróthi, who can be found in Erebor.Talk to FróthiYou should speak with the lore-master Fróthi, who can be found in Erebor.Talk to Fróthi'No Dwarf of Erebor would do such a thing as steal that necklace. Not a one! But I couldn't vouch for those Stout-axes. Could you?'

You tell Fróthi that you saw Karazgar holding a dragon's tooth.

'Then we know our thief! I am relieved that I need not think poorly of our cousin-dwarves. We know our thief, and how formidable a foe he is, but we do know little of what he is after.''Hm... yes, I would like to see that one tooth we still possess. Come. Perhaps we will gain some insight into the matter.''There can be truth in visions, ${CLASS}, though their proper meanings may be riddle-like. 

'Hm... yes, I think you ought to follow this path where it leads. I do not know what you will find, but I feel certain the journey will hold answers.'When the Taurogrim attacked the Beornings, the supplies from their cart were scattered all over the forest. Help the Beornings gather the lost items so they can return to their home.The Beornings' supplies are scattered in Eryn Lasgalen.

You should gather the lost supplies.Collect honey jars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect lembas bread (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect sacks of seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect crates of honey cakes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect barrels of cream (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sterkist can be found at The Forest Gate, on the western edge of Eryn Lasgalen.

You should talk to Sterkist.Talk to Sterkist'When we were first ambushed by the Taurogrim, our horse was spooked and our cart was overturned. The horse and cart are both fine, but many of our supplies are missing. I suspect the Taurogrim have taken some of them. While you are helping Thorlind deal with these wood-trolls, would you keep an eye out for anything we may have lost? Meet us at The Forest Gate once you have gathered them.'Sterkist checks a list from his cart and nods approvingly.

'This seems to be everything that was missing! Thank you, ${PLAYER}'After spending countless years within Thikil-gundu, Vethúg Wintermind, comes to seek a new vengeance upon Durin's Folk.King Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

King Thorin III has received word that Vethúg Wintermind draws near to Erebor. When you are prepared, you should speak to the King under the Mountain.Talk to King Thorin IIIKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.

You have triumphed over Vethúg Wintermind, but at great cost. You should speak to King Thorin III.Talk to King Thorin III'The time draws near, ${PLAYER}.

'My scouts have returned bearing ill tidings. Vethúg Wintermind, son of Hrímil Frost-heart, flies for Erebor from the Grey Mountains. He and his brood approach the mountain even now, and I have sent as many warriors as I can spare to guard the gates of Erebor. Many of the Dale-folk have sought refuge within Erebor, and the Elvenking has sent a company of his finest archers to aid us. Thikil-gundu still bears the cold scars of his ire for Durin's Folk, but I will fight to my last breath to ensure Erebor does not come to such an end. All have made ready for the coming of Vethúg, and this time, he will not take us by surprise. We of Durin's Folk will strike him down!

'When you are prepared, we shall join with my warriors before the gates of Erebor.''The time has come, ${PLAYER}.''It is over, ${PLAYER}. 

'We of Durin's Folk have claimed our vengeance upon one of our greatest foes! Vethúg Wintermind, son of Hrímil Frost-heart, fled the battle gravely wounded and shamed in defeat! Whether he lives still or not, he will not trouble my kinsfolk again!

'Many fought and died bravely before the gates of Erebor, but their sacrifices were not in vain. When the time comes, they shall be laid to rest in tombs of stone.

'There will be many tales told and songs sung of this day, my friend! But where has Karazgar gone? Has his plot now failed?'


<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Rust and Rime'</rgb>Defeat the many Scourges of Mordor.Defeat the many Scourges of Mordor.Defeat the many Scourges of MordorDefeat the many Scourges of Mordor.Defeat the many Scourges of Mordor.Defeat the many Scourges of MordorStrong enemies still roam Gorgoroth.Strong enemies still roam Gorgoroth.Complete Rotwing, Scourge of Dor AmarthComplete Spitpyre, Scourge of Talath ÚruiComplete Gristlebite, Scourge of LhingrisComplete Bolvág the Cursed, Scourge of AgarnaithComplete Nuzdum, Scourge of UdûnComplete Uiliúr, the Ancient EvilThranduil's chief hunter, Thorlind, has also been on Iphantemel's trail.You should talk to Thorlind, in Felegoth, about what he has found.Talk to ThorlindThorlind has spotted spiders harvesting sap along the river-banks of the Rhachló.

You should seek out the spiders that Thorlind found.Find the spiders by the RhachlóThorlind has spotted spiders harvesting sap along the river-banks of the Rhachló.

You should approach one of these sap-harvesting spiders.You should talk to Thorlind by the banks of the Rhachló.Talk to ThorlindThe trail of spider blood begins near the banks of Rhachló and will hopefully lead right to the den of Iphantemel.

You should track the wounded spider.Track the wounded spiderSearch for Iphantemel's denYou should talk to Thorlind where he stands just outside Torech Emel.Talk to ThorlindYou should return to Thranduil in Felegoth.Talk to Thranduil'While you sought proof by way of trap, I bade my chief hunter, Thorlind, to search these woods he knows so well for other signs of the spider Iphantemel. He, too, has just returned and bears tidings we should hear.''Far and wide have I wandered through our woods, and now I well and truly believe the spiders have gone. This should be glad news, but instead it troubles me. At long last, when I was full weary and on the brink of giving up, I happened upon a group of spiders by the banks of the Rhachló, gathering sap from a gnarled and wounded tree.

'They were too great in number and I dared not go closer, but with your help we might come closer and learn more, either by capture or chase.''Hold, ${PLAYER}. The spider flees, but look closely. The wound you have given it has in return given us a trail of blood to follow. If we keep our distance, we might follow this fleeing spider back to Iphantemel's den.''I think we have found what we sought, ${PLAYER}. See how webs entangle the way ahead. Yea, I can even hear her brood moving to and fro down there.

'Come, we should report back to King Thranduil. The brood is too much for the two of us alone.''Torech Emel is where old Iphantemel hides? I wonder how long the ancient thing has hidden there, where no Elf's foot ever treads. She will be on her guard, I do not doubt, but we know she may be provoked.

'Let us make preparations against her brood.'Explore Seregost's exterior courtyards and terraces.Explore Seregost's exterior courtyards and terraces.Explore Eastern CourtyardExplore Western CourtyardExplore Western TerraceExplore Eastern TerraceExplore Overlook TerraceExplore Chaydash BridgeExplore Mokál Rukh TerraceSmugglers have holed up in Esgaroth-of-old, using it as a base for mixing their prohibited goods into legitimate shipments. The Long Lake won't be safe again until they are removed.Esgaroth smugglers can be found in Esgaroth-of-old.

You should defeat Esgaroth smugglers.Defeat Esgaroth smugglers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mervárth can be found outside Esgaroth-of-old.

You should talk to Mervárth.Talk to Mervárth'You look like you can handle yourself in combat, ${CLASS}. While you're looking for that Elf, you should clear out as many of these smugglers as you can. If the Long Lake is ever going to be safe for traders again, they need to be removed!''Well, now I know for sure I can count on you in a fight! Good work! There's a few more smugglers in Lake-town that I'd love for you to meet....'Defeat many shades and armours in Eryn Lasgalen.Defeat many shades and armours in Eryn Lasgalen.Defeat many shades and armours in Eryn LasgalenDefeat many shades and armours in Eryn Lasgalen.Defeat many shades and armours in Eryn Lasgalen.Defeat many shades and armours in Eryn LasgalenGroups of Ghâsh-hai have been spotted securing structures near Nargroth, in Talath Úrui.Ghâsh-hai can be found at Magh Nûl and Magh Groth.

