You should defeat the wood-trolls!Defeat Taurogrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Langhár is in a small glade north of the path in Eryn Lasgalen.

You should talk to Langhár.Talk to Langhár'This is very troubling, ${PLAYER}. I will follow this blood trail and try to find Glenneth. You must continue on without me. If this is as it appears, the Beornings are in terrible danger.''So, the Elves sent you to find us? You are a friend, then. Good. Something took my brother, Sterkist. I... I think it may have been the Taurogrim. But those are just supposed to be a myth, meant to scare children away from the forest, aren't they? It matters not. Sterkist needs our help.''There is no mistake. These are the Taurogrim of legend. Why have they suddenly returned to Mirkwood?'Deep within Seregost, Lhaereth the Stained keeps her plague cauldrons. They contain a new, more virulent Great Plague, which she intends to release upon the realms of the Free Peoples. As you and the Rangers Faeron and Rhadrog are the few innoculated to the plague, you must enter the Court of Seregost as a small strike team and attempt to disrupt Lhaereth's plans.Complete the deed The Court of Seregost -- Tier 1Complete the deed The Court of Seregost -- Tier 2Complete the deed Challenge: Khílnat, the Silent ShadeComplete the deed The Court of Seregost: Lost LoreComplete the deed The Court of Seregost: Morroval-slayerComplete the deed The Court of Seregost: Orc-slayerComplete the deed The Court of Seregost: Black Númenórean-slayerExplore the dark caverns and web-shrouded passes of Lhingris.Explore the dark caverns and web-shrouded passes of Lhingris.Discover the MorgaiDiscover Rath CailDiscover Ceber DúathDiscover Dath NethrynDiscover Kâm LagúrzDiscover Amon RûthDiscover Torech UngolDefeat many spiders in Lhingris.Defeat many spiders in Lhingris.Defeat many spiders in LhingrisDefeat many spiders in Lhingris.Defeat many spiders in Lhingris.Defeat many spiders in LhingrisRoaming the lava lake of Talath Úrui, Spitpyre patrols its domain.Spitpyre can be found patrolling Mordor.

You have encountered the threatening Spitpyre. Roaming the lava lake of Talath Úrui, the beast patrols its domain.Defeat SpitpyreSpitpyre can be found patrolling Mordor.

You have encountered the threatening Spitpyre. Roaming the lava lake of Talath Úrui, the beast patrols its domain.Defeat SpitpyreYou have defeated Spitpyre.CompletedYou have encountered the threatening Spitpyre. Roaming the lava lake of Talath Úrui, the beast patrols its domain.You have slain Spitpyre and vanquished a threat to the safety of all those who brave Mordor.Explore the strongholds of Lhingris upon the jagged slopes of the Mountains of Shadow.Explore the settlements of Lhingris upon the jagged slopes of the Mountains of Shadow.Discover Kála-murgDiscover LugvargDiscover NelegrothDiscover Iant AngosDiscover Cirith UngolDiscover Fennas GostDiscover the dwarf-markers spread across the Dale-lands.Discover the dwarf-markers spread across the Dale-lands.Discover the dwarf-markers spread across the Dale-landsYou have agreed to do some chores for Captain Álarr in exchange for access to the murder location. Place notices around Lake-town for the guards.The stack of notices is in the guards' barracks in Lake-town.

You should take the stack of notices.Take the stack of noticesNotices can be posted in places all around Lake-town.

You should post notices around Lake-town.Post notices in Lake-town (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Captain Álarr can be found in the guards' barracks in Lake-town.

You should talk to Álarr.Talk to Álarr'I need someone to go around town posting notices. That someone is now you! Take the stack from over there and put them up anywhere that looks appropriate.''Yes, yes, I'm sure you did a wonderful job. What do you want, a pat on the head and a biscuit?'There is still much to do in Talath Úrui.There is still much to do in Talath Úrui.Complete A Fighting ChanceComplete Hoarded GoodsComplete Halting the MovementComplete Mysteries of the GhâshghurmComplete Shrine of the Ghâsh-haiComplete Infiltrating ThorzhafComplete The Conquest of Talath ÚruiComplete Reclaiming Talath Úrui: The Western GhâshghurmComplete Reclaiming Talath Úrui: The Gates of NaerbandComplete Reclaiming Talath Úrui: The Eastern GhâshghurmEnkárvo has encouraged you to talk to the Easterling refugees so you can judge the truth for yourself.You should talk to refugees of Dorwinion and the Chayasír in their camps in the hills to the east of Dale.You should return to Enkárvo in the Dorwinion refugee camp, in the hills east of Dale.Return to EnkárvoThe wolves can be found south and east of the refugee camp hills.

You should find and defeat wolf pack leader Tungváka, and a number of his pack, to stop them from being bold enough to attack the Easterling refugees.Defeat TungvákaDefeat wolves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Enkárvo in the Dorwinion refugee camp, in the hills east of Dale.Return to Enkárvo'When you haggle over the cost of goods in the market, neither haggler is fully to be believed. This we know. And yet, there is a true and fair worth to the goods, and when the haggling is done, it is hopefully found. But how do you know that truth? You hear both sides.

'Why do you not go among my people and among the Chayasír, and hear our sides of the story? The two camps are close, and when you are done, maybe you can judge the truth for yourself.''The camps of the Chayasír and of Dorwinion are not far from each other. You should go and talk with the people of both, and maybe you can judge for yourself.''When first we arrived in this vale, some number of us ventured down to the river's edge, so we might wash the mud from our cloaks and fill our water-gourds.

'There, kneeling by the cool waters did we look up and behold the high tower of Dale, its walls and bridges and houses huddled like a herd of sheep.

'But no gates or doors could we see from our place on the river, as if Dale had turned its back. Little did I dream that day how true this thought might be!''Many carts full of goods have I known from Dale, though until we fled I lived all my life in far Dorwinion.

'Many a merchant of Dale have I known, fair of speech and manner, come down the long roads to trade with us.

'So tell me now, if you can, how they have forgotten us now that we are at their doors? How they have forgotten their fair speech and the hospitality with which we treated them?

'Tell me, when they rise in the morning, how can they look their children in the eyes?''Some among us may complain of their lot - but is that not always so? So we do not lay about in a palace upon cushions of silk! Many leagues we walked, dogged by hunger, harried by sickness, robbed and beaten. And always the terror of what devastation lay behind us, never knowing whether it followed us, and how fast.

'Here we have found food and rest for our weary feet. We have come so far. Surely we can overcome the obstacles before us.''There is a name whispered in fear among our tents: Athálrik. Have you heard this name? He and his men come among us, chests puffed out. They shove those who have not offended. They take what is not theirs. They accuse us of things we never imagined.

'And suppose we struck back? We are not so helpless against a handful of men, armed though they be. If we struck back, would the Men of Dale believe we did so in defence? No, no. That is not the way.''Why have we fled so far from our homes in Rhûn? Have you not heard of the great devastation that happened there? Some say it was a blazing fire that rose up out of the earth, consuming all. Others, a darkness coming down from the sky, a thousand, thousand night-black red-eyed crows.

'I did not see it with my own eyes, I confess. They say none who did escaped with their lives. But when peoples, not just of Dorwinion, but beyond came fleeing in droves past our homes, we fled, too.

'Had you seen the terror in their eyes, you would have done the same!''We are Chayasír, and so we wander. But never so long, so ceaselessly and wearyingly have we wandered. I have seen such wonders as I never imagined!

'From the ruin we fled and came over high mountains. We were very near the tops when they shook, shook mightily. We fell to our feet, all of us, and watched amazed as the snows flowed cascading like thundering rivers down onto the foothills below.

'Then we came to the sea, the waters roiling and the sands lined with a great wreckage of ships. There was fire among them, and whether they came from strife among men, or great storms, or some other cause, I cannot say.

'We did not tarry. We went on.

'Over green lowlands we travelled, and then up into high dry-lands, swept cold by wind. There the earth had been opened up as if from a wound, and we could not see into the depths.

'Armies we saw, gleaming and orderly, as if going off to war. Then we saw other soldiers, wounded and dirtied, wandering as if lost. Sometimes they robbed us, or beat us. Other times, they went on by.

'At long last we have come here. Our Sangemêkh says this is a homecoming and that we will stay here, at least for now. And so we rest, and mourn all we have lost, and think in wonder over all that we have seen.''We Chayasír dwelt in this valley once, many lives of Women and Men ago. So it is sung by our Sangemêkh, our Song-Mother, of how before we wandered we settled around the Long Lake.

'How long have these Dale-folk lived here? If they continue to prove unworthy of this fair and bounteous land, perhaps it is they who should wander and the Chayasír should take it back!''Have you heard the tale of the War in Mordor? Let me tell you, for I have heard all about it. The armies of Gondor blew their horns and the gates crumbled before the blasts. Then the Red King vied in battle, one on one, with the White Sage. At their blows, the earth trembled! When the Red King struck, the sky darkened. When the White Sage landed a blow, the mountain burst into flame.

'Though he took a grievous wound, the White Sage prevailed and claimed the Red King's crown. All the Orcs of Mordor perished on the spot and a thousand thousand birds descended from the skies to pick at their bones.

'That is what I heard, and I swear that it is true!''You have spoken with some people in the camps? Good. But before you judge the truth, I would ask you to witness the dangers we face out here. Every night we hear the howling of wolves, and betimes they grow bold and attack.

'We fend them off with fire and bow as we may, but always we see the form of a great, grizzled pack leader beyond our reach. Tungváka we have begun calling him. Defeat him, and the wolves would surely lose their boldness, and keep away from our tents.

'I think you will find Tungváka among his pack, down in the ravine east of here, among the trees.''Look for the wolf ancient Tungváka and his pack in the low ravine south and east of here. They are the wolves who have grown bold enough to try and attack us.''Tungváka is defeated? You have done a great good. But here is Komúsi. Your face tells me the tidings are not happy.

'What has happened?'Defeat many Taurogrim in Eryn Lasgalen.Defeat many Taurogrim in Eryn Lasgalen.Defeat many Taurogrim in Eryn LasgalenDefeat many Taurogrim in Eryn Lasgalen.Defeat many Taurogrim in Eryn Lasgalen.Defeat many Taurogrim in Eryn LasgalenThe Abyss of Mordath has sunken into the deepest depths of the Black Pits of Mordor and now Sauron's greatest secrets are laid bare.The Order of the Eye has entered the Abyss of Mordath to seek vengeance upon King Váskmun Greytooth and lay claim to the lost artifacts of the Dark Lord. They have pursued the Firehorns into the depths of the Black Pits of Mordor.Descend into the Black Pits of MordorThe Order of the Eye has crossed the Abyss dividing the Black Pits into a towering structure built into the foundations of Barad-dûr.Cross the Abyss and pass into Thol Shíkug, the Screaming DeepThe Order of the Eye has laid claim to Thol Shíkug and descended into Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling. They must be defeated if you are to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and Firehorns.Defeat the Order of the Eye in Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling, and ascend the Black Stairs of DurshnúlAs Sauron willed for King Greytooth and the Firehorns to pass unhindered deeper into the Mordath, Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, stands in your path. You must overcome him to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and his folk.Defeat Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, and enter the Ring-prisons in pursuit of the FirehornsKing Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed. You must force King Greytooth to see reason or defeat him before he can lay claim to the Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.Confront King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns in Glurnákh, The Pit of GreedYou have completed the Abyss of Mordath on Tier 1 and prevented the Dwarf-rings from being wielded to any evil end.Completed: Abyss of Mordath (Tier 1)'It seems our paths once again converge, ${PLAYER}!

'We battled through the ruins of Barad-dûr, and hitherto, we have silently pursued the Order of the Eye into these depths. Both Megoril and I have known "believers" of their kind before...for they first rose after Sauron's defeat upon the slopes of Orodruin. Fate proved their beliefs to be true, and now they will never be turned from the hope that Sauron shall once again return.

'However, their presence here appeared both unannounced and unwanted, and we believe it might be turned to our advantage. They have passed through the Black Pits, crossed the Abyss itself, and battled deep into the foundations of Barad-dûr all while chanting their hatred of an accursed foe - one they call: Greytooth. I know not what dispute they have with this Greytooth, but from their wild shouts and chants, I fear it concerns the Rings of Power. Even with their power fading, the Rings remain a symbol of status and strength to those that dwell in these lands.

'Do what you must to combat the Order and keep the forces of this Greytooth from the Rings, and we shall search for any sign of Thelaron. If he yet lives, he must be hidden in the depths of the Mordath.

'We cannot face so many foes alone, but we have found secret ways through these depths. If you find your way into the deeper chambers of the Mordath, we can help you return to them swiftly.

'Let us hope we both find what we seek in this Abyss, friend.'


