With Dagrun's reputation improved, now would be a good time to speak to the Men of Lake-town about Smaug's bones, on behalf of the Master.You should speak with Dagrun, who can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.Talk to Dagrun'You're not one of those lot, then? Good. Why they wish to dredge up those bones and bearing them here to New Lake-town, I can't say! It was that dragon, after all, as set Old Lake-town ablaze. Or have they somehow forgotten the tales of their grandmams? 

'If you think you can make some sense of such rot and bother, go talk to Stafhild, over there. At the very least, he'll try to tell you why they believe the things they do.''Why bring the bones here? Well, they're doing no one any good out there in the Lake, for one. And they have great value, or so I've heard tale. They could bring great wealth to Lake-town. Or put them up somewhere, and travellers like yourself will come from leagues away just to see them.

'Don't you lecture me of that rot about ill luck. Why, that's a real bit of Smaug at the Dragonbone Inn... isn't it? I've always thought so, at any rate. The clear thing is, whoever begun this talk was thinking with their head for a change, and that's just the sort of thing Lake-town needs.

'Really, someone ought to bring a petition to the Master!''I have dwelled all my life among the folk of Lake-town, and never has the gossip in the market been so pernicious and full of lies as these last days.

'Why, they say I am of the bloodline of Othur! You know of Othur, do you not? He was Master of Lake-town in the time when Bard the Bowman was not yet king and Smaug slept, then awoke. Othur stole from Lake-town and fled, and his name is one of infamy and shame. They say his stolen wealth was not lost, but that I have it now and conceal it from all.

'This is all nonsense, of course! But if I am to assist you in your puzzle, I must ask you to assist me in mine. I should not be at all surprised if they were somehow linked.''Thank you once again, for all you have done, ${PLAYER}. You have been most helpful in assisting the best interests of Lake-town.''Ah, ${PLAYER}. This has been an eventful day for you and for me and for Lake-town, has it not? But what is it? Is there some other matter about which you wish to speak?'

You tell her briefly of the strange puzzle you followed from Loeglond, to Esgaroth, and finally to Lake-town.

'Your problems and my own are much akin, friend. It would seem, new as I am as Master, that I have more than my fair share of opposition, and it has taken the form of such grumbling in the street as you have witnessed over Smaug's bones.'Beorning travellers and an Elf scout are missing in the forest. Thorlind, the chief hunter of Felegoth, is concerned that something troubling is afoot.Thorlind can be found on the path south of Felegoth.

You should find Thorlind.Find Thorlind on the path south of FelegothThorlind can be found on the path south of Felegoth.

You should talk to Thorlind.Talk to Thorlind'May I ask for your assistance, ${CLASS}? A matter has been brought to my attention, and I could use the aid of someone battle-tested, like yourself.

'I am Thorlind, chief hunter of Felegoth. This is the situation: A pair of Beorning traders, siblings I believe, were present in Felegoth when King Thranduil ordered the realm closed. They left, taking the path west, but never reached The Forest Gate. I then sent one of my scouts, Glenneth, to find them. She, too, has gone missing. I fear they did not simply lose their way in the forest.

'Meet me on the path south of here. We will follow their trail and see where it leads us.''Ah, there you are. Ready to begin?'Having found convincing proof, Sírithon devises a plan to catch the Loeglond thief.Supplies can be found in Loeglond.

You should gather supplies to bait a trap.Collect supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There is an unused supply cart in Loeglond.

You should bait the cart with supplies.You should talk to Sírithon, who can be found in Loeglond.Talk to SírithonYou should talk to Sírithon, who can be found in Loeglond.Talk to Sírithon'I will tell you how my suspicions of a thief first arose: every morning, as I made my rounds, I would find things slightly moved from where they were. So slight was the shifting and rearranging that it only tickled my mind for some days. 

'Then, two days ago, I laid a coil of rope in a particular position upon some other tools. The next morning, there was no mistaking it: the rope was two hands shifted to the side.

'Therefore, we must conclude our thief steals by night. Come, help me lay a trap. This part, I would not dare without your help! First we must gather supplies and lay them in the unused supply cart.''Good work. You are a worthy ${CLASS}. Now let us wait for nightfall.''The ruins called Esgaroth-of-old, were once a town of the Dale-men. Very little remains, and what does is now covered over with marsh reeds and the waters of the Long Lake. Who hides in such a dreary and desolate place, and what aim do they pursue out there? I wonder! Our thief is real, but grows stranger every time we learn something new.'Legolas has devised a plan for defeating the Nelegroth Broodmother and requests an adventurer's aid.Ungol Weavers can be found in one of the caverns of Torech Ungol, beneath Nelegroth.

