'I have located a particularly elusive foe, the Brood-mother of Nelegroth. She does not reveal herself easily, but I have seen the local Orcs leaving their dead at an offering stone for her. It is then that she leaves her lair to feed. I suspect if you slay some of the Ungol spiders nearby and leave them on that stone, she will appear. Then, you can strike her down and rid Lhingris of another powerful enemy.'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Complete Volume IV, Book 9: The Ring of PowerComplete The Black Book of Mordor: Chapter 6Ingold, a soldier of Gondor, has scouted Dor Amarth and is concerned with the growing numbers of foes gathering at the encampment of Fushaum Tûm.Ingold has asked you to defeat the leaders of Fushaum Tûm.Defeat Thorakó, the HewerDefeat Shatúrro, the Spear'The encampment of Fushaum Tûm concerns me. There seems to be a large presence of Olog-hai there. I ask you to find those in command at Fushaum Tûm and defeat them.'A notice is pinned to the board, signed by Ingold:

