Dís has suggested that renewing the old practice of offering shiny trinkets to the ravens might aid in rebuilding a friendship between Durin's Folk and their kind.Collect Jangovar trinkets for the ravens of Ravenhill (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dís can be found at Ravenhill.

You have gathered many trinkets from the Jangovar and should now deliver them to Dís.'What do you want?'

You politely explain King Thorin's wish to rebuild a friendship with the ravens.

'Ah, so he thinks he might put all to rights now, does he? He did not seem so concerned about the minds of the ravens when Dáin was King Under the Mountain. He must know the truth of it. You see, the line of Carc nears its end. Roäc is dead, his children are dead, and now Arcah, daughter of Croär, is all that remains. I tend her lesser kin as best an old dwarf may, but she is the last chief of the great ravens, and it has been many years since we last spoke in the forgotten ways of Durin's Folk.

'She has gone elsewhere... beyond my sight. I do not know if she will ever return, but if the King Under the Mountain wishes to heal the wounds of time and once again share true friendship with the ravens, it will be no simple errand.

'I can speak with them if they would still hear me, but they will not listen without the offerings that once adorned their homes. I have seen sparkling trinkets borne by the Easterlings come to the North, and I believe the ravens may find them to their liking.

'Bring me those trinkets, and we shall see if the ravens still desire friendship with Durin's Folk.''I cannot give the King Under the Mountain what he seeks... not without time.

'The ravens must decide if such an offering pleases them, and perhaps one day the younger Dwarves of Durin's Folk will witness the return of Arcah and the friendship that was lost.'The old forester Víthog will lead you to Athálrik, where you can confront him for his accused crimes.You should talk to Víthog, the old forester in the highlands west of Lake-town.Talk to VíthogYou should talk to Víthog, who has approached after your confrontation with Athálrik.Talk to VíthogYou should bring the memory-cloth back to Sangemêkh Turáh, in the refugee camps in the hills east of Dale.You should return Queen Regent Erna, in the Great-keep in Dale, with the news that Athálrik chose death over justice.Return to Erna'Aye, I know his visits home are not to me, though I am the closest thing to family Athálrik ever had. I know also he has been troubled of late. Troubled as I have ever seen him. 

'My eyes are still keen, and I see as much that is good as is stern in your face. I will take you to him. I hope you will do him some good. Ah, but what am I? I am an old man and I am given to worry.''Come then, let me lead you to the place Athálrik goes. Whatever is troubling the lad... I hope you do him some good.'The Queen Regent and young king listen to your account.

'The news you bear is grave indeed. It is troubling that Athálrik could not be brought to face due and proper justice.

'However, I judge your dealings in the matter honest, and your course of action the necessary one. And for your service in the protection of Dale, we thank you.''Did you think I would run and hide in the timbers? I saw all, aye, and heard as well. The lad has come to a bitter end. It fills me with sorrow, but I hold nothing against you, ${CLASS}.

'There was always anger in Athálrik's heart... but not such anger as this. What put that there? Ah, I may never know. I have seen much sorrow in my life, and I have never known a true cause to any of it.''The Bilitang? You have returned it to us? Ah, ${PLAYER}. This means more than you can know. You have restored what is most prized to us. You have also restored our faith in the good-will and honesty of Dale.

'You must know that the twisted, faltering strength Athálrik gained from the memory-cloth was a misuse. It is not a weapon, nor was it meant to be anything of the kind. It is a long song of memory, woven by Sangemêkh after Sangemêkh across many lives of the Chayasír, and the song gives strength. A strength meant to sustain, and bring together, and give hope. In truth, I do not think many would become as Athálrik did, handling the Bilitang un-trained. I think there must have been some sour knot within his heart from long before.

'But thanks to you, all is right again.  You may go and tell the Regent Queen in Dale that she will see no more trouble from the Chayasír.'The Jangovar encampment of Urûshoba struggles to rebuild enough to set siege to the Dale-lands once more.Siege engines and banners can be found in the encampment of Urûshoba.

You should destroy siege engines and banners.Destroy Jangovar banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy siege engines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have destroyed many siege engines and banners.Completed'It would appear the Jangovar have begun to rebuild Urûshoba once again. The strategic location of their encampment has been nothing but trouble for the peoples of the North, and we cannot allow them to regain a foothold in the Dale-lands.

'Travel to Urûshoba, throw down their banners, and ruin their siege equipment. Do this, and you will have my thanks.'You have destroyed many siege engines and banners in the Jangovar encampment of Urûshoba. You have dealt a terrible blow to the Jangovar's efforts to rebuild.The time to strike at the heart of Seregost has come. Meet with Faeron to discuss how you can help.Complete: The Bloody WatchersFaeron is waiting for you at the Agarnaith Ranger camp.

You should talk to Faeron.Talk to FaeronFaeron and Rhadrog are somewhere inside Seregost.

You should find the Rangers.Find the Rangers in SeregostFaeron is outside the Court of Seregost, in Agarnaith.

You should talk to Faeron.Talk to FaeronTalk to RhadrogComplete: The Court of Seregost.Complete: The Court of SeregostComplete: The Court of Seregost - Tier 2Faeron can be found at the Agarnaith Ranger camp.

You should talk to Faeron.Talk to FaeronWord has reached you that Faeron of the Grey Company has a plan for penetrating the defences of Seregost, and has asked for you by name. You should return to Agarnaith and see how you can help.'Ah, ${PLAYER}! Per usual, your timing is uncanny. The threat of Lhaereth's plague still exists, and the time to act is now. I hear you have discovered another way into Seregost. Is this true?'

You explain that the Watching Stones in Seregost consider Lhaereth an enemy as well, and have allowed you safe passage to and from Seregost. 

'Watching Stones? Can we really trust such fell beings? We must take the risk.

'Here is my plan. I have gathered some soldiers, and more will be coming. They will move into Kala-gijak and create a bulwark there. My hope is that this will trigger an attack from the majority of the forces left in Seregost, and distract Lhaereth from our true intentions.

'That is where we come in. We cannot risk a full invasion, even if that were possible, because of the plague. Only the three of us are inoculated against it, and even then, I am unsure if we will survive direct exposure to it in a concentrated form.

'We have no choice. The threat to our homelands is too great. We will form a small strike team and enter this den of evil ourselves. Gather some companions, be sure they are inoculated themselves, and meet us in Seregost. We will find a way to Lhaereth's throne room, and do what we can to end this threat. 

'And no, I will not allow Viznak to come this time. He is but a child, after all.''I believe this is it, ${PLAYER}. Are you prepared to face the horrors within?''Here we are again, ${PLAYER}. I had hoped we wouldn't need to return to Seregost, at least not so soon! Alas, we must steel our hearts and put on our bravest faces. All the Free Peoples are counting on us now.''The day is won! You should be proud, ${PLAYER}. We would never have been successful without you. 

'The defeat of Dulgabêth and the departure of Lhaereth will mean another shakeup in the power structure of Mordor. This can only be good news for the Free Peoples!

'I am certain this is not the last we have seen of Lhaereth the Stained. Her threat made that abundantly clear. We should celebrate while we can, but keep a wary eye out for her in our future travels in Mordor.'The Sangemêkh Turáh and several other Chayasír were taken hostage by the Jangovar.Find and rescue Sangemêkh Turáh from the Jangovar camp, on the eastern side of the Long Lake.Rescue Sangemêkh TuráhYou should talk to Turáh in the Jangovar camp, on the eastern side of the Long Lake.Talk to Sangemêkh TuráhFind and free the other Chayasír captives in the Jangovar camp, on the eastern side of the Long Lake.You have freed Turáh and the other Chayasír and should meet them back at the refugee camps, in the hills east of Dale.Meet Turáh back at the camps'Terrible news, Enkárvo! Several people from my camp went down to the river, Sangemêkh Turáh among them. There, Jangovar scouts surprised them and took them hostage.

'Do they think we have wealth? Whatever did they hope to gain?

'Oh, ${PLAYER}. We are able enough to defend ourselves and our own. But we are common folk, and the Jangovar are hardened soldiers. We dare not move against them, not if all of us marched against them.

'But you might. We have heard of your deeds. Would you rescue our Sangemêkh and people from the Jangovar?''I thank you, stranger. But I am not the only one taken by the Jangovar. Will you find my people and free them, also?

'I will make my way out. Do not fear for me. I think the trouble you are raising in their camp will serve as plenty distraction. I am not helpless or unarmed, thank the earth, and one or two posted guards shall not hinder me, I assure you.''Free the other Chayasír taken by the Jangovar. Do not worry over me. I will meet you back at our camp-site.''There she/he is - our daring rescuer. How I wish I could sing this memory into the weave... but, alas! I cannot.

'You look puzzled, , and I realize there is much I should explain to you.'Defeat the three scourges of Eryn Lasgalen and the Dale-lands.Defeat the three scourges of Eryn Lasgalen and the Dale-lands.Complete: Kalabrazân, Scourge of the Dale-landsComplete: Urdâr, Scourge of the Dale-landsComplete: Gloomthorn, Scourge of Eryn-LasgalenAn old tome found in Erebor leads to the mystery of The Secret Stone. What does it mean?King Thorin III can be found at his seat in Erebor.

You should bring the tome to King Thorin III.Collect the dusty tomeKing Thorin III can be found at his seat in Erebor.

You should bring the tome to King Thorin III.Talk to King Thorin IIIA tome rests on this bench, left behind by someone.  It seems ancient, like it might just turn to dust if handled too roughly. Several pages have been torn out and are missing. A poem is written on the page that was left open:

Beneath the Misty Mountains, deep,
The ancient shadows hold their keep.
Came Durin King, his crown of stars,
To carve new halls, claim kingdom ours.
Above the dwarf-made forges glow,
While unknown dangers lurk below.

For many thousand years it slept,
In darkened depths, where fell-things crept.
And then, one day, the stone was found,
Dark as night, and perfectly round.
Its beauty beckons but a glance,
But ensnares the mind in a trance.

Many were lost, driven insane,
And then we unearthed Durin's Bane.
From Moria, the Longbeards flee
In hand, the stone-that-should-not-be.
By King Thráin's orders, it is sealed,
By secret door never revealed.

Just the line of Durin may know,
Of Secret Stone, born of shadow.
Heed this warning, do not seek it,
This fell thing you cannot outwit!
The stone must remain locked away
Do not seek the hidden doorway!

King Thorin III is in the line of Durin. Perhaps he would be willing to share more about this Secret Stone.'What have you brought me, ${PLAYER}?'

He takes the tome from you and gently leafs through the pages. Realization suddenly lights his eyes.

'Abnubuzûr! The Secret Stone! Where did you find this, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell him you found it left on a bench here in Erebor.

'I can hardly believe my eyes! Knowledge of the stone was passed down from my father, but its location has been lost. I believe my people took the Stone with them when they fled Moria, but not even I know where this secret door can be found.''Tome? What Tome? I'm sorry, I know nothing about it. Perhaps you should ask King Thorin.'As the unrelenting forces of Ungol pour from the mountain, few Orcs remain in Lhingris.Candúr can be found in Udûn.

