You have gathered many stones from the slopes of Erebor and should now deliver them to the Stout-axe rune-carvers in Erebor.You have delivered many crude stones to the Stout-axe rune-carvers.Completed'It has been a joy to be among the Dwarves of Durin's Folk. Each day here brings new wonders!

'They seem to have taken a liking to our fondness for rune-stones, and I would not deny them more examples of our crafting skill. If you were to gather loose stones from the slopes of Erebor, our rune-carvers could shape more of them into rune-stones.

'Gather as many as you can bear, and bring them to our rune-carvers. They will know what to do!'As Ambassador Spakorth asked, you delivered many stones of Erebor to the Stout-axe rune-carvers. Through their skill, they will be able to create impressive rune-stones for King Thorin III and Durin's Folk.The Dale knight Athálrik may have stolen a prized and powerful Bilitang, or 'memory-cloth', from the Chayasír.You should talk to Sangemêkh Turáh, who stands by Enkárvo in the Dorwinion refugee camp, across the river east of Dale.Talk to Sangemêkh TuráhYou should return to the Great-keep in Dale and relate the accusations against Athálrik.Accuse Athálrik in DaleYou should look for Athálrik on Wardman's Way, which lies west of the canal on the southern side of Dale.Look for Athálrik on Wardman's WayYou should talk to the man who caught your eye on Warden's Way in Dale and learn if he knows of Athálrik's whereabouts.Question KeldaYou should look for Athálrik in the Burnwater House in Lake-town.Look for Athálrik  in the Burnwater House in Lake-townYou should look for the old forester Víthog by his cabin, up in the hills west of Lake-town.Look for the old forester VíthogYou should defeat the ambushers you encountered while looking for the old forester Víthog, whose cabin is up in the hills north-west of Lake-town.You should continue looking for the old forester, Víthog, whose cabin is up in the hills west of Lake-town.Look for the old forester VíthogYou have found Víthog chopping wood by his cabin, in the hills west of Lake-town.

You should talk to Víthog and ask if he knows of Athálrik's whereabouts.Talk to Víthog'Yes, it is time to explain the root of our recent troubles and the cause of my people's anguish and ire.

'That ruffian, Athálrik, has done a harm greater than he knows. At first, he pleased himself with simply parading through our camps, knocking things over and cuffing children on the ears. But soon his swagger grew greater. He began suspecting us of imagined crimes, rooting through our belongings and taking what caught his eye. He beat any who stood in his way, then any who so much as looked him in the eye.

'And then, one day, he took what was most prized of the Chayasír: my memory-cloth,  or in our tongue, Bilitang. That with which I sing the memories of our mothers and fathers, and of their mothers and fathers before them.

'At last, we fought back. We knew no good would come of it, but he had gone too far. You have seen what followed, and we will not set foot in that ruined camp again.''I implore you, go to the young king and regent mother, and help them see the truth of what Athálrik has done.''See, mother? ${PLAYER} is returned. Let us hear what was found.''Yes, milady. He is sometimes seen on Wardman's Way.''${PLAYER}. You have returned from the camps of the Easterling refugees. What was your finding? Is the dispute settled?'

Choosing your words carefully, you relate what you have seen and learned, building the case against Athálrik.

'Justice should shield all who are wronged within our kingdom and spare none who trespass our laws. But ours is an orderly justice. He must be brought before us.

'And where is Bryn when he's wanted? Athálrik was his man. Gaumar, what do you know of the knight's whereabouts? He is seen sometimes on Wardman's Way? That is a quiet by-street west of the canal on the south end of Dale. ${PLAYER}, will you look for him there, and bring him before us?''Go find Athálrik, ${PLAYER}, and bring him before us, so that he may answer for the charges claimed against him. You may find him on Warden's Way.''Indeed, where is my brother Bryn when he's wanted? I should like to hear him answer for this.''Go find Athálrik, ${PLAYER}, and bring him before us, so that he may answer for the charges claimed against him. You may find him on Warden's Way.''Athálrik? Aye, he can be found here some days. More often than not, though, he's gone off the way of Lake-town.

'Didn't know that, did you? For all the talk, few do. But I swear it's true, he is no man of Dale. And down on the Long Lake, his name is not spoken of with very much respect, I have heard tell.

'If you venture to Lake-town, you'll find him in the Burnwater House, like as not. Only, if you do... don't mention it was me who told you.''If you venture to Lake-town, I think you will find Athálrik in the Burnwater House. Only don't tell him I sent you there.'The woman spits.

'Athálrik? That wet fish? Aye, he was here. Leering and lumping like he was too good for the wood he walked on. Well haven't I known him since back when, and was I going to take such guff?

'We had words then, he and I. Broke three good plates, knocked me to the ground, and stomped off.

'If I were you, I'd let him go, and good riddance. But I can see you're determined and I think I know where he must have gone. To the old forester, Víthog, whose cabin is up in the hills, west of here.

'That's where he'd always go in such moods, and I'll drink the Long Lake if it's not where he's gone now.''When Athálrik was under a black cloud, he would always be found up in the north-west hills, with the old shepherd. That is where you will find him now, I'll warrant.''Athálrik? Yes, yes! I have seen the lad quite often, lately, as a matter of fact. He takes the time from his important post in Dale to come home.

'Ah, but it is not me he comes for. I know the truth of it, no matter what he says. Athálrik does not believe my eyes are still as keen as they are, nor does he know how little I sleep at night.

'He meets with his men, sometimes. Always serious, always gathered around - around I don't know what. Sacks or coffers or some such. Other times, he comes alone, and the man in that horrid mask appears. They never talk long. I could hardly tell you where that other man comes from, or how he goes. Makes the hairs stand up on the back of my neck to look at him!''The memory-cloth Athálrik stole is a danger to him and not to him alone. Many lives of women and men are remembered within it. The memories are potent and hold great power. If he listens to them untrained, it may grant him strength. It may fill him with sorrow or with fury. It will almost surely drive him mad.

'It is for the memory-cloth that the Jangovar abducted me, but of course, I have it not. Athálrik does.

'As you have seen, we are not welcome within the walls of Dale, but you are, ${CLASS}. I implore you, go on our behalf to the young king there. Help him see the truth of what Athálrik has done.'Explore Talath Úrui's water reserves.Explore Talath Úrui's water reserves.Discover AshronkDiscover KrulronkDiscover GakhronkDiscover ZagronkCrawling out of the shadows of Eryn Lasgalen, the Taurogrim have returned to Tholkát in force.Taurogrim can be found in Tholkát in northern Eryn Lasgalen.

You should defeat Taurogrim in Tholkát.Defeat Taurogrim in Tholkát (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thranduil can be found in Felegoth.

You should talk to Thranduil.Talk to Thranduil'I have received reports that more of the Taurogrim have revealed themselves. As I feared, they have returned to Tholkát in force.

'Once more, I must ask that you defeat them or drive them off before they gain a new foothold.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. It seems we shall have to be more vigilant in our watch of Eryn Lasgalen, so the Taurogrim can never again return.'Górsim the vault-keeper agrees to help you find the necklace made from Scatha's teeth.You should have a drink while you wait for Górsim, in Erebor.Drink some aleGórsim can be found at one of the older vaults in Erebor.Search for GórsimYou should talk to Górsim, who can be found down in the vaults in Erebor.Talk to GórsimYou should speak with the lore-master Fróthi, who can be found in Erebor.Talk to Fróthi'Fine, fine! It's the teeth of Scatha you want to see, then? Oh, don't you worry, I know right where to find them. And you are lucky you found me. Those are in the old vaults. Hardly any dwarf knows the way back there, other than me! And if Fróthi sent you, I am happy to show them off. I would not mind taking a look at the old things, myself, now that I think of it.

'I will return shortly. Please, drink some while you wait. No, no, I insist. In fact, I will be offended if you do not!''And now what are you doing down here? This is all wrong, all of it. Do you see? This is the sack that held the necklace, and by Smaug's bones, it is empty but for a single tooth. 

'Oh, this is not good. You must go and tell Fróthi at once!''The necklace, stolen? That was a piece of our history, ${CLASS}. This is a serious grievance!'The last remaining spiders in Northern Mirkwood are in Torech Emel.Torech Emel is found in the north-western reach of Eryn Lasgalen.

You should defeat any spiders you come across in Torech Emel.Defeat spiders in Torech EmelTorech Emel is found in the north-western part of Eryn Lasgalen.

