You should talk to Kunchat.Talk to Kunchat'Kúlkhur tells me you did the tasks you were given without complaint. That is a good start, but how would you like to separate yourself from the rest of the weaklings here? Jangovar prove themselves by defeating their betters in combat. Then they become the betters. If you succeed and climb the ranks, perhaps Akh-gulûkh will notice you. But you must start at the bottom rung of the ladder. Find Jáldor, and challenge him to a duel. If you succeed, perhaps some less menial tasks will open up for you. The duels are not meant to be to the death, but, accidents happen....'

He laughs cruelly.'You wish to challenge me, Chayasír? You will end up dead, fool!''Ah, here is my busy little Chayasír. I hear more good things from Yólkhon. How would you like to climb the ladder higher? Go find Sháwat and challenge him. I do not think he will be much trouble for you.''A Chayasír weakling challenges me? I will break your bones!''Chayasír, Otkóz tells me you have helped us prepare Er Shamol for an attack. This is good. We should be able to hold off the dwarves now. As a reward for your hard work, I will tell you the name of the Man you must defeat next: Bakhíl. He is known to be dishonourable in duels, so consider yourself warned! I would hate to lose my pet Chayasír now.''A challenger? Good, I was growing bored!''Haha! Chayasír, I am impressed! I will spread word of your triumphs!''You surprise me, Chayasír. I did not know your kind had such martial prowess. Report to Otkóz now. He will have more work for you.''Good, good! Jáldor was a fool, and I am glad to be rid of him. Report to Yólkhon. If you can complete his tasks, I may tell you who next you can challenge.'You have been sent to ensure that Utterby's defences are prepared for a dwarf attack.Tuhâl would like to speak with you.

You should talk to Tuhâl.Talk to TuhâlCrude defences can be found at the entrances to Utterby.

You should secretly sabotage the Jangovar's defences.Sabotage crude defences (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should talk to Otkóz. who can be found inside Utterby.Talk to Otkóz'Chayasír, the dwarves may launch a retaliatory strike after our raid on Hammerstead. I need someone to go check that our defences are in order. You have proved trustworthy enough, so I am sending you. Get to it.''You know what I am thinking, friend? That this would be a good opportunity for sabotage! While we 'check' these defences, perhaps we should also weaken them, very subtly, of course.''So? Is it done?'

