Bofur has discovered another trail of hoof-prints leading onto the Men Angrún to the west of Óinsbridge. You should follow them.Follow the path of hoof-prints leading away from ÓinsbridgeThe raven can be found atop an obelisk along the Men Angrún to the west of Óinsbridge.

The path of hoof-prints led down the Men Angrún, but it appears that one of Arcah's ravens has perched atop an old obelisk along the dark road. You should direct the raven to fly to Dori at Óinsbridge.Direct the raven to fly to Dori at ÓinsbridgeDori can be found at Óinsbridge.

You have directed the raven to fly to Dori at Óinsbridge. You should now return to Dori.Talk to Dori at Óinsbridge'It is time, ${PLAYER}. We have spent long enough in the ruins of Tharrazhâr!

'While I and the others set out on the journey to Óinsbridge, I would ask that you speak to Ingór, son of Vékun. I have felt many eyes upon us here, and I fear that my attempt at deception has not gone unnoticed. And so, I would have you tell Ingór that I seek my brother, Nori. It is the truth, and it should put his mind at ease. I seek not for wealth or glory... only for my lost kin.

'When that is done, ride for Óinsbridge. It is there we will reunite and take our next rest.

'Óinsbridge lies to the south beyond the forest, but the Thornholt is home to many dangers. Do not stray from the dark road!''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}.

'I do hope my kinsfolk have held their tongues in regards to your Kámbrada companions. From what Dori has told me, Náth and Dréri and the rest of their kinsfolk knew great hardship in Mordor before they came to dwell in the Lonely Mountain. Enough hardship, I think, that mere insults would do naught to wound them. Perhaps I am not so resilient, but I find the greatest insult to be dishonesty.

'Tell me, ${PLAYER}. Have you had any luck in finding heirlooms of the Longbeards or have you come to tell me the truth of Dori's little expedition? What is it you truly seek?'

You tell Ingór of Dori's lost brother, Nori, who travelled into the Grey Mountains against the will of his kin and the King under the Mountain.

'I see. Perhaps I have judged Dori too hastily....

'There is a byword among the Zhélruka. Its true meaning cannot be shared, but it speaks of one who is governed by a doomed obsession. Those unlucky few "seek the Citadel". For Dori's sake, I hope his brother does not seek the Citadel.

'You may go, ${PLAYER}. May you find Nori before death or madness takes him.''At last, we have come to Óinsbridge.

'It is a fine respite from the gloom of the Thornholt, but the western reaches of the forest still lie ahead of us. If Nori and his expedition took rest here, it is likely that some sign of their passage has been left behind. And so, I have asked the others to search for signs of the expedition, ${PLAYER}. Would you join them?

'Oh, and do not be afraid to cross to the other side of the Forest River! The bridge may have fallen into disrepair, but it is still sturdy enough to bear the weight of a few dwarves and a ${RACE}, I think!''Ah, ${PLAYER}. Does Dori wish me to return?'

You explain that you followed a path of hoof-prints from the abandoned camp-site to Bofur.

'O! Those tracks were mine! Or my goat's, rather! You see, I found the old camp-site as well, but when I began to search the road I discovered tracks leading deeper into the forest. They are not unlike those of the goats of Erebor, and so, I think they belong to Nori and his expedition.

'It is likely they continue on the road ahead for some distance, but who can say if Nori has taken a less-travelled path through the Thornholt?

'If you were to follow them, we might learn if the path of the expedition strayed from the Men Angrún.

'Go on ahead, ${PLAYER}! I will keep watch!'The raven perches silently....'You have found one of Arcah's ravens, ${PLAYER}! Very good!

'What else did you find?'

You tell Dori that you found an abandoned camp-site in Óinsbridge, and that you believe Nori and his expedition rested a night before passing through the western reaches of the Thornholt.

'My brother and his expedition have kept quite the pace! Were I not so cross with him, I might be impressed!

'Once I have heard what Arcah's raven has to tell, we'll be off!'Stráhek the Stout retreated after encountering a wizard in Thornholt while collecting supplies.You should search the Thornholt woods, south of Skarháld, for the odd wizard Stráhek the Stout encountered.Search for the wizard in the woodsThe wizard stands among the wood of Thornholt, south of Skarháld.

You should talk to the not so odd, actually familiar wizard in the woods.Talk to Radagast'The Wizard! I saw him while collecting wood in Thornholt. He beckoned me closer, but I know better than to trust a strange wizard among the trees. He is dangerous, he must be! I, Stráhek the Stout, have too many expeditions to go on and wealth to gain to meet my end at the hands of some mad wizard!

'You may go see what he wants, if you wish to throw your life away. Not I!''${PLAYER}! It is good to see you. Did that odd dwarf tell you I was here? What a strange fellow. I do not know whether I gave him a fright or offence. I had hardly started speaking when he turned and marched off. I really could have used some help!'A deadly Gundabad Reaver roams the west, near Rushgate.A deadly Gundabad Reaver roams the west, near Rushgate.Defeat the Gundabad ReaverA deadly Gundabad Reaver roams the west, near Rushgate.Defeat the Gundabad ReaverA deadly Gundabad Reaver roams the west, near Rushgate.CompletedA deadly Gundabad Reaver roams the west, near Rushgate.You have defeated a Gundabad Reaver. The Ungoledain would have been wise to avoid a threat this deadly.A mix of Ungoladan and Gundabad weapons are strewn about the ground.A mix of Ungoladan and Gundabad weapons are strewn about the ground. It would be beneficial to investigate and discover who was the victor.Find the enemies that left these weapons behindA mix of Ungoladan and Gundabad weapons are strewn about the ground.Find the enemies that left these weapons behindA mix of Ungoladan and Gundabad weapons are strewn about the ground.CompletedA mix of Ungoladan and Gundabad weapons are strewn about the ground. It would be beneficial to investigate and discover who was the victor.It appears the Ungoledain have been having their issues with the Gundabad on their journey to Rushgate.Threkmóth and his folk have taken the poison-protecting potion in preparation for the assault on the Ungoledain... and possible rescue of Vaskorn.You should talk with Threkmóth, in Skoghús, and let him know you are prepared for the journey to Kêr Bréin.Speak with ThrekmóthYou should talk to Threkmóth back at Skoghús, the Thornholt.Talk to Threkmóth'The honey cakes are cooling, and we are as prepared as one could imagine. Come, let us deal with these Ungoledain like the nest of hornets... or, I suppose, web of spiders that they are!''Enough talk. Now we act! We Beornings will make quick work of these spider-folk, just you wait!''You fought well, ${RACE} and we drove the Ungoledain out of Thornholt. I fear that I am responsible for the injury to Vaskorn. I - I was preoccupied and did not weigh the threat with the gravity it deserved. He now lies silent, my hope is the brown wizard's protection will also heal him.'The Ungoledain are defeated and have fled, but you are not quite out of the woods just yet.Threkmóth asked you to check on Vaskorn's condition.Talk to VaskornThrekmóth can be found in Skoghús, in the south of Thornholt.

Vaskorn is not feeling well. You should return to Threkmóth and update him.Talk to ThrekmóthRadagast can be found in the north of the Thornholt woods.

With Vaskorn's condition not improving, Radagast should be notified in case there is something he can do for the Beorning.Talk to RadagastYou should return to Stráhek the Stout in Skarháld and tell him what took place in the woods.Talk to Stráhek the Stout in Skarháld'${RACE}, we have successfully driven the Ungoledain from Thornholt. That is as good a reason to celebrate as any, however I cannot bring myself to so much as look at those honey cakes, while Vaskorn is ill. I feel quite ill myself with remorse.

'Could you go check on him, and see if there is any improvement in his condition?''Th... th... thank you, ${PLAYER}. I see now what a fool's errand I was on, alone and without protection from the spider-folks' poisons.

'I... I am not well. Not feeling well. I fear none of my folk have the art to treat this poison. Will you go back to Radagast and ask what he c... could do for me?''Spider-folk, poison, honey cakes? What kind of madness is this? You think I want to go in Thornholt now? I trust you less than that wizard after this tale you have spun. 

'I'll simply have to convince some other poor drak to go and gather that wood. It's as simple as that.''Worse rather than better? It is as I feared. I do hope the brown wizard can help him.''I am quite relieved to hear that the Ungoledain have fled Thornholt. I might hope we shall not see their faces again, but I fear that is too much to ask. 

'I may have an idea of how to heal the sickened Beorning. I will stop by myself and visit. You have done more than enough for the Beornings of Skoghús, and all the beasts of this wood, ${PLAYER}.

'Oh, and if you should cross that peculiar dwarf in your travels, tell him he may gather wood from the forest's edge, I certainly won't turn him into a toadstool or any sort of animal.'The dwarf Agátur may have the knowledge needed to follow Etterfang's lost trail.Agátur can be found in Skarháld.

You should ask Agátur about under-maps of the Grey Mountains.Talk to AgáturClimbing gear can be found in Skarháld.

You should collect climbing gear for the journey to Stormwall.You should talk to Agátur in Skarháld.Talk to Agátur'You should speak with Agátur. He has studied many dwarf-maps, in which our surveyors have drawn the faults and crevices under many mountains.''I am always happy speaking on the old under-mountain maps, ${PLAYER}. Only the most skilled of dwarf surveyors can make them. It takes great care and precision! If you can believe it, many such maps were made and kept from the distant days when Durin's Folk called these cold Grey Mountains our home. Indeed, I brought some with me, knowing they might be of use.

'You wish to know of spider-paths that touch upon the Glimmerdeep? Let me see. Yes, there were many spider-tunnels beneath these peaks. However... the only ones to touch on Glimmerdeep cut straight across the mountain into Stormwall. You may be in luck! 

'Hum... yet do not judge your luck, perhaps, until you have found your way there and inside. Mountains shift and rocks fall, after centuries! You will want to take some climbing gear with you when you go.''You are well prepared now, but I have grim news. Word has spread through the Zhélruka of the Stave that you seek. Except the words have been twisted and now many believe the entrance to Thafar-gathol lies within the Stormwall! Blast these Zhélruka! Five of their kin left Skarháld just moments ago.'Drake eggs litter the landscape of the Withered Heath.You should destroy any drake eggs that you find on the Withered Heath.Destroy drake eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroyed many drake eggs.CompletedDrake eggs litter the landscape of the Withered Heath. Destroying the eggs within these ancient drake breeding grounds should lessen the impact of dragonkind in the Grey Mountains.You have successfully destroyed many drake eggs on the Withered Heath. The Zhélruka will surely be thankful of your efforts.Vútro the West-wind ran afoul of the Weeping Warrior and barely escaped with his life.Bótuz Frostblood is on the upper level of Skarháld.Talk to Bótuz Frostblood on the upper level of SkarháldBótuz Frostblood is on the upper level of Skarháld, and he plans to lead a party of dwarves in search of the Weeping Warrior.Talk to Bótuz Frostblood and join the search for KarazgarBótuz Frostblood is on the upper level of Skarháld.Talk to Bótuz Frostblood on the upper level of Skarháld'It was... he of the terrible mask... the Weeping Warrior!

'He held a knife to my throat... and gave me a message...'

Vútro closes his eyes, overcome with the pain of his wound.

'Karazgar wants to speak... with Bótuz....''Karazgar wants to speak... with Bótuz....''Before today, Vútro was one of our finest scouts, able to outrun even the West Wind. Alas for Vútro! This wound will keep him from the wild lands. A scout that cannot walk the wilderness is of no use to me or to my people.

'The Weeping Warrior is known to us, ${PLAYER}, even in the distant lands from which we came. His reputation for cruelty is unmatched; he has long had designs on the North, and has troubled both Longbeards and Zhélruka in pursuit of it. Even so, I do not fear him. I will bring a small force of my finest warriors for two purposes: as a wise exercise of caution, and also as a demonstration of our power. Perhaps Karazgar will decide he does not wish to oppose the Zhélruka in these mountains, and will leave us in peace.

'I would have you come with us, ${PLAYER}, but your friend Durin must remain behind. I gave him a task suited to his abilities, and at any rate this meeting will be too dangerous for an unproven king's son.''Vútro will tell us where he encountered Karazgar, and we will find the Weeping Warrior. Let us hear what he has to say, and if it is not to my liking he will regret it!''Karazgar thinks to frighten us with words, but he overestimates their power. Have I not told you that words mean little to me, and only actions earn my respect? Let Karazgar speak. We will blunt his words with hammers, and cut his intentions with our axes!

'The Zhélruka will prevail!'Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, has promised to bring war to Skarháld, and Bótuz Frostblood wants you to ready the defences.Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld.Talk to Durin inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of SkarháldDurin asked you to count the weapons and armour currently stored inside the keep of Skarháld, as well as to assess the quality of the siege defences on the upper level outside the keep.Tally the weapons stored inside the keep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tally the armour stored inside the keep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Assess the quality of the siege defences outside the keep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld.Talk to Durin inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of SkarháldDurin has requested that you send Zhélruka craftsmen inside the keep to repair the siege defences.Send Zhélruka craftsmen to repair the siege defences (${NUMBER}/4)The mountains shake! What is happening?The mountains shake!Durin is inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld, which has been shaken to its foundations.Talk to Durin inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of SkarháldThe mountains shake! What is happening?The mountains shake again!Bótuz Frostblood is inside the keep of Skarháld.Talk to Bótuz Frostblood inside Tharrazhâr, the keep of Skarháld'Even so, I do not think Karazgar's words are without meaning. He will attack Skarháld as he promised, and we will need to repel him. Go to your friend Durin inside the keep and help him assess our equipment. I want to ensure we have weapons and armour enough for my Zhélruka when Karazgar does attack.''Karazgar will attack Skarháld as he promised, and we will need to repel him. Go to your friend Durin inside the keep and help him assess our equipment. I want to ensure we have weapons and armour enough for my Zhélruka when Karazgar does attack.''I heard some of the Zhélruka talking, ${PLAYER}. Is it true that Karazgar has promised three assaults upon Skarháld? This inventory of the supplies has become much more important than it was mere hours ago! Have you come to assist me?

'I would appreciate it if you could tally the weapons and armour contained in the side rooms, and to inspect the siege defences outside the keep. We will need to know what deserves the most attention if we are to prepare in time for Karazgar's return.''I would appreciate it if you could tally the weapons and armour contained in the side rooms, and to inspect the siege defences outside the keep. We will need to know what deserves the most attention if we are to prepare in time for Karazgar's return.''I feared it was so, for the siege defences seemed in a poor state, even to my casual eye. Speak to some of the craftsmen here in the keep and see if they can repair the ballistae or produce a greater supply of heavy arrows to be set with them.

'I hold no authority over these dwarves, but I hope they will understand the importance of these suggestions! My teachers impressed upon me the need for suitable preparations; it is much better to mourn the lost time after a victory than it is to mourn a lost battle!''Speak to some of the craftsmen here in the keep and see if they can repair the ballistae or produce a greater supply of heavy arrows to be set with them.''Did you feel that? What is happening?''What is happening? The very mountains shake beneath my feet!''The mountains shake as if caught in a great gale! Has the Weeping Warrior worked some sorcery upon us?'Karazgar has not given the Dwarves of Skarháld enough time to prepare. He launches the first of his promised attacks, seeking to attain his goals with a single throw.Bótuz Frostblood wants you to keep an eye on Durin during the defence of Skarháld.Talk to Durin inside the keep and defend SkarháldDurin is outside the keep on the upper level of Skarháld.Talk to Durin on the upper level of SkarháldThe death of Bótuz Frostblood threatens to leave the Zhélruka at Skarháld in disarray. One of his lieutenants must rise to lead his fellows.Durin is outside the keep on the upper level of Skarháld.Talk to Durin on the upper level of Skarháld'Are you ready, ${PLAYER}? Tell Durin that even he must fight! If Karazgar is behind this, we will make him regret it!''To battle! We will find Karazgar's weaknesses and exploit them! Imkhih sabkyûd, ${PLAYER}!''Keep an eye on your friend and ensure he does not embarrass himself!''Karazgar toys with us, ${PLAYER}, as a cat does with a mouse! He had the advantage, but he did not press it. The first of his promises has been fulfilled, and claimed the life of Bótuz Frostblood. With one deadly strike, Karazgar has left the Zhélruka here without their leader. Who now will lead them? Who now will organize the defences?''The first of Karazgar's promises has been fulfilled, and claimed the life of Bótuz Frostblood. With one deadly strike, he has left the Zhélruka here without their leader. Who now will lead them? Who now will organize the defences?''Bótuz was supposed to lead us here in the Grey Mountains! What are the Zhélruka going to do now? Who will lead us on this venture now that the Frostblood is dead?'

Inek the Brash clenches his fists and lives up to his name.

'It has to be me! No others of his lieutenants are suited to the task! Kópat is a scholar, much good may it do us here, and Dóbrokh may be a fine warrior but he does not command respect the way Bótuz did. It falls to me to manage the defences. It can be no one else!

'Bótuz thought you a worthy ally, ${PLAYER}. Will you work with me to make this stronghold safe, and to take revenge upon the Weeping Warrior? If you will vouch for the Longbeard prince, he is welcome to join hands with the Zhélruka in these two purposes.''Will you work with me to make this stronghold safe, and to take revenge upon the Weeping Warrior? If you will vouch for the Longbeard prince, he is welcome to join hands with the Zhélruka in these two purposes.''If I once believed the ill fortune of the Zhélruka had been exaggerated by the bards, I do no longer! The loss of Bótuz Frostblood must be a grievous injury to them, and I confess that it pains me also. Would Bótuz and the others who died during Karazgar's attack still be alive if I had not lowered my weapon in the Ironfold? Would they still live if I had kept them from crossing the Dale-lands? Ah, I will not dwell upon it. What was done is done, and might have been worse.

'It is good to hear that Inek will take up the mantle of leadership and ready his people for another attack. Karazgar promised to come to Skarháld three times? How much worse will be the following assaults, if this was merely the first? It bodes ill, ${PLAYER}.

'I know the Zhélruka do not care for me. Nay, do not seek to deny it! It is true. I am unproven. Did I count myself ready when we battled the Easterlings outside Utterby back in the Ironfold? That counted for naught, or less than naught! To do battle against Karazgar, in defence not only of my people but of another... that is where my true glory lies. We will stand with Inek and his Zhélruka to repel whatever Karazgar sends against us, and perhaps afterward I will feel my name deserved. It will be my honour to stand with them and with you, ${PLAYER}. There is much we must do if we are to be ready. The first promise is fulfilled. When the next comes, we must be ready. We have no choice.'Stormwall was once a great crafting-hall of the dwarves in the Grey Mountains.Collect valuable trinkets.Collect valuable trinketsYou should search Stormwall for any valuable trinkets.You should bring the various trinkets to Hórin in Skarháld.Stormwall was once a great crafting-hall of the dwarves in the Grey Mountains. Perhaps some craft-work of old still lingers, lost amongst the rubble in these once great halls.'You bring me wondrous gifts. These were found in Stormwall? Though I still do not trust you, I admire that which you have done for the Zhélruka.'Deep within Stormwall lies a fiery secret, slumbering in the shadows.Complete the Caverns of Thrumfall Instance.

The Caverns of Thrumfall Instance can be found in the Instance Finder panel on the Specific tab under Non-Scaling Instance - Grey Mountains.You should talk to Agátur in Skarháld.Talk to Agátur'Hórin vouches for Drengur. He is not a dwarf known to spin tales. This means that Etterfang yet lives. The Zhélruka are already organizing for an attack. You should join them. They are not as well prepared for such a fight as you are, ${CLASS}.''You will go? Good. See that the world is rid of Etterfang at last.''You return once more. Marvels stacked upon marvels. And Etterfang is finally slain? Then Borin's quest is at long last done. I wonder what will become of this Stave the Zhélruka found. I wonder if their fabled lost citadel is quite as near as they hope. Ah, but only time will tell.'The Ungoledain aren't the only threat to be wary of to the west. Strange Orcs have fled Thrikil-gundu in great numbers.You should find and defeat Orcs west of Thornholt.Locate the scouting OrcsYou should find and defeat Orcs west of Thornholt.You have found and defeated Orcs west of Thornholt.CompletedThe Ungoledain aren't the only threat to be wary of to the west. Strange Orcs have fled Thikil-gundu in great numbers.Many of the strange Orcs in the west have been defeated.The defeated Ungoledain have retreated and are thought to be heading to Rushgate. Follow their tracks and look around to see where they are regrouping.Look towards the west for any Ungoladan activity.Continue to head west and scout for Ungoladan activity.Continue to head west and scout for Ungoladan activity.Enter Rushgate and scout for Ungoladan activity.Radagast can be found in the north of the Thornholt woods.

Return to Radagast and let him know what you've seen here in Rushgate.Talk to Radagast'It appears the Ungoledain have already been spotted heading towards Rushgate. We can't be sure if this was a small group of them or if their ranks are in far greater numbers to the west.

'Track the Ungoledain, ${PLAYER}. Do not engage them though, if you can avoid it. They are in retreat and we want to keep an eye on them to see what they plan next.''It seems the Ungoledain are moving out of Ered Mithrin. While I'm sure this isn't the last we've heard of them, I think it's safe to rest easy for now.'Creatures of flame block the path leading to Stormwall.You should defeat dragon-kind on the path to Stormwall, which lies north-east of Skarháld.Defeat dragon-kind on the path to Stormwall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Examine the slain hartExamine the slain bearExamine the slain wolfYou should search for the entrance to Stormwall, high in the mountains north-east of Skarháld.Search for the entrance to StormwallStormwall lies high in the mountains northeast of Skarháld.

You should defeat enemies in Stormwall and find the source of all these beasts.Defeat foes in Stormwall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the source of all these beasts within StormwallStormwall lies high in the mountains north-east of Skarháld.

You should examine the spider corpse you found in Stormwall.Examine the spider corpseIt would seem the body of the slain Zhélruka was indeed attacked by dragon-kind. Further up the path to the Stormwall, you hear the cries of an angered drake fighting some animal.Vaskorn has gone off to deal with the Ungoledain single-handedly and without protection from the poison. Threkmóth concedes this may have been a mistake.You should return to Radagast, in the Thornholt woods, to collect the potion which will guard against the Ungoladan-poison.Get the potion from RadagastYou should return once again to the Beorning camp of Skoghús, in the south of Thornholt, and let Threkmóth know you have Radagast's potion.Return to ThrekmóthYou should deliver the poison protection to Fiskvat and Hunulf, Threkmóth's neighbours.You should return to Threkmóth, now that you have given Radagast's potion to Fiskvat and Hunulf.'You think it was reckless to send Vaskorn by himself? Well... perhaps so. My mind was very much on my baking, you see, and it seemed sensible enough at the time. 

'Every once in a while, one Beorning is not enough for the task. I do not think we are too late. We should help him. He thinks very highly of you, ${RACE}, so I will trust you. You have seen what we are up against, after all. You may lead us to their camp.

'Here is my plan: you return to the brown wizard and bring back this potion of his, while I will get the others prepared for the outing.''Your timing is remarkable, ${PLAYER}. The honey cakes have just finished baking. I may set them to cool properly while we deal with these bothersome Ungoledain.

'You may give the poison protection to Fiskvat and Hunulf, while I set the honey cakes out to cool. We share a fence, and therefore trust.''Threkmóth is not a bad sort, really, though sometimes I think he cares more for honey cakes than his folk, or anyone else for that matter.''Your help is most welcome, ${RACE}. Vaskorn is my brother. I would have run off to stand by his side sooner, if I had known.''I suppose I should take this potion too, hadn't I? Well, then. Preparations are nearly complete, I should say.''The smell is horrible, I confess, but it will do the trick. Take it, and you and Threkmóth's folk will be well-shielded while fighting the Ungoledain.

'Do be sure to consume it before you strike. I am far from certain of its powers to cure the poison after the fact.

'Now go, and fortune smile upon you.'Fierce cold-drakes and frost grims roam in numbers upon the Withered Heath and must be defeated.You should defeat any fierce cold-drakes and grims that you find while exploring the Withered Heath.Defeat fierce cold-drakes and frost grimsYou should defeat any drakes that you find while exploring the Withered Heath.Defeat fierce cold-drakes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat frost grims (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated fierce cold-drakes and frost grims.CompletedFierce cold-drakes and frost grims roam in numbers upon the Withered Heath and must be defeated if the Grey Mountains are to ever be safe.You have successfully defeated many of the cold-drakes and frost grims that roam the Withered Heath. The Zhélruka will surely be thankful of your efforts.Fearing that Nori has met with a terrible end at the hands of Karazgar or the mysterious dwarf-wights within Thikil-gundu, Dori and Company must muster the courage to enter the Steel Keep.Dori can be found atop Stánbalk, the Stone Wall.

You have found evidence that Nori has gone into Thikil-gundu, and Dori now seeks to find his brother before Karazgar or the mysterious dwarf-wights can bring any harm to him.


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must complete the instance 'Thikil-gundu' on its solo difficulty to advance this quest.</rgb>Dori and Nori can be found in the Keep of Tharrazhâr.

You have repelled Karazgar and rescued Nori from the depths of Thikil-gundu, but many mysteries linger about the fate of the Steel Keep. You should talk to Dori and Nori.'This cannot be!'

Dori stares at Nori's axe in disbelief.

'Has my brother gone into Thikil-gundu without the aid of his own expedition? Has Karazgar devised some cruel purpose for him?

'But what if... what if he has been taken like the others? No! I will not believe such things!

'We will enter Thikil-gundu together, ${PLAYER}, and we will find my brother!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must complete the instance 'Thikil-gundu' on its solo difficulty to advance this quest.</rgb>'I will not allow my brother to meet with such a fate, ${PLAYER}. I swear it!''Our journey is over, ${PLAYER}... at least for the moment!

'Nori thinks himself a disgraced dwarf, but these hurts will heal in time! He has adventured as few dwarves have in their lives! Was I disappointed in my brother? Was I fearful that he had led himself to certain doom? Of course I was! But... he is my brother! Even if the King under the Mountain will not forgive Nori as I have, this will not be the end of our adventures!

'There is a fire in the hearts of Durin's Folk! An unquenchable flame! And you have proven yourself among us, my friend. 

'We have forced Karazgar out of Thikil-gundu, and that is enough! Even so, there is some unseen evil lurking in our delving of old... and many questions linger in my mind.

'But this day, we honour the lost here among the halls of Tharrazhâr!''I cannot atone for what I have done, ${PLAYER}. I have disobeyed the King under the Mountain, I have deceived my brother... and for what? Naught, I say!

'Even the gold we found is no boon to my people! There is a curse upon Thikil-gundu... and nothing in the halls of the Steel Keep has gone untouched by it!

'Once I was renowned among Durin's Folk... a hero of the Lonely Mountain! Am I now to be known as the foolish, old dwarf who dreamt of treasures lost?

'No... I will not let this be the end of it!'Threkmóth and his folk have taken the poison-protecting potion in preparation for the assault on the Ungoledain... and possible rescue of Vaskorn.The Ungoledain appear to be ready for an attack. Fight them off as you continue to search for Vaskorn.Search for VaskornVaskorn appears to be unconscious, but alive.Protect Vaskorn from Ungoledain attackersThe Ungoledain have begun to retreat, but left behind a vicious spider shade to fight you.Defeat the spider shade'We have accomplished what we set out to do, now honey cakes await!'Before the dwarves at Skarháld have had the chance to properly prepare, Karazgar launches the first of his promised attacks upon the fortress.The fortress of Skarháld is under attack! Durin raced ahead and already engages in battle at the bottom of the stairs.Catch up to Durin at the bottom of the stairsDurin fights against the onslaught of dragon-kind at the upper courtyard of the fortress and needs your help.Talk to Durin in the upper courtyard of the fortressDurin has seen that the dwarves operating the siege defences are in need of help, and asked you to attend to them.Climb the central platform and assist the dwarves operating the siege defencesThe drakes and other dragon-kind have begun to overwhelm Skarháld. Durin calls for you to help him turn the tide.Talk to Durin in the upper courtyard of the fortressBótuz Frostblood fights among his people in an upper courtyard of the fortress, but the drakes and other dragon-kind do not relent.Fight alongside Durin at SkarháldDurin is in the courtyard of Skarháld. Most of the dragon-kind army has retreated.Talk to Durin in the courtyard at Skarháld'Karazgar left us no time to prepare! But how has he brought these drakes and dragons to bear against us? Let us drive off these winged beasts and prove to the Weeping Warrior that dwarves cannot be intimidated so easily... neither Longbeard nor Zhélruka!''What do we do? I know what we must not do... we must not give in to despair! But anyone can see there are too many drakes and not enough dwarves to repel them. Think! We must think! How can we drive them away from the fortress? What would Uncle Náin do? Bah! I cannot think of anything!

'Come with me, ${PLAYER}! I saw Bótuz Frostblood fighting down below. Let us go to him and see if he has a plan!''It is done, ${PLAYER}. Karazgar could have slain us all, killed to the very last dwarf, but he chose to spare us instead. Hah! It is no mercy. He seeks to use fear as a weapon against us.

'Alas for Bótuz Frostblood! We must not let the Zhélruka despair at his loss, or the fortress is as good as fallen. I tell you dwarves are resilient. May we prove it!'Deep within Stormwall lies a fiery secret, slumbering in the shadows.Defend yourself against the dragon-kind.Defend yourself against the dragon-kind!You should speak with the dwarf.Talk to the dwarf'Now let us leave this place!'The dwarf catches his breath.

'I... I am surprised to be alive, and surprised to see a ${RACE} in Stormwall. I am Drengur. Have you come to search for me and my companions? I fear they are all dead. We were ambushed on the path. I ran into the ruins and found myself in an old spider cave. Little did I know that those beasts dwelled there as well!

'I was lost, hiding myself from worms and drakes. And then... and then I saw her. A dragon, slumbering in the caves! It is true! We must leave this place at once. I only escaped the tunnels thanks to your distraction.'Bótuz Frostblood and his warriors have left Skarháld in search of Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior.Bótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.Talk to Bótuz FrostbloodBótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.Search for Karazgar with Bótuz and his warriorsBótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.Remain alert for any treachery by KarazgarKarazgar has asked to speak with you.Talk to Karazgar, but remain alert for treacheryBótuz Frostblood and his Zhélruka have crossed Óinsbridge in search of Karazgar.Remain alert for any treachery by KarazgarBótuz Frostblood has some words for you now that Karazgar has departed.Talk to Bótuz Frostblood'Let us return to Skarháld. If these words signify anything more than idle boasting we should prepare for Karazgar's attack.''Remain on your guard, my warriors, and keep watch for Karazgar. He will not surprise us as he surprised Vútro.''I have taken the measure of these Zhélruka, but you... you are a curiosity to me.'

Even behind his mask, you feel the piercing eyes of Karazgar upon you. The urge to draw your weapon and cease their study rises in your heart, a sensation made more unpleasant by this lingering doubt: does this urge come from you or from the Warrior himself? If Karazgar notices your struggle, he gives no sign of it when next he speaks.

'There is a smell about you, ${PLAYER}, the odour of all your kind. But there is something else, too: the reek of subservience. I know the Master you serve. I have cast off the shackles that once bound me, and now I shall take what is mine. Why should you not do the same?''Karazgar speaks nonsense. He is one man, too cowardly to show his face. Without his fell Master he is nothing. Let him come to Skarháld once, twice, thrice, it matters not how often. The Zhélruka will make him regret the visits. Aye, even the Longbeards will oppose him!'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Adventure to Level 120Built by the dwarves and stolen by dragons, Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep, has borne witness to a tragic and terrible history.Rust-stained writing can be found in Thikil-gundu and among the Ered Mithrin.

