'I will speak with Hórin. If Etterfang yet lives, she is a mortal enemy to both the Longbeards and the Zhélruka! We must act before the beast awakes!'Stormwall was once a great crafting hall of the dwarves in the Grey Mountains.Find old crafting tools.Find old crafting toolsYou should search for old crafting tools in Stormwall.Find old crafting tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the crafting tools to Hórin in Skarháld.Stormwall was once a great crafting-hall of the dwarves in the Grey Mountains. Perhaps some of the trusty tools used to craft great and wondrous items still linger in these crumbling halls.'Why, look at these. They are not unlike the tools our own smiths use... fashioned by their ancestors, perhaps. See how they have weathered the years intact! One might still use them. I believe we shall.'Orc-kind have claimed the Glimmerdeep and work to mine its wealth.Weaken Orkish scaffolding.Weaken Orkish scaffoldingYou should weaken Orkish scaffolding in Glimmerdeep mine.Weaken Orkish scaffolding (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Weakened Orkish scaffolding.CompletedOrc-kind have taken over the Glimmerdeep and work to mine its wealth. The scaffolding they have built allows the miners to scale to unreachable sections of the mine, and must be destroyed. If enough scaffolding is weakened, it may eventually collapse under its own weight.You have weakened much of the Orkish scaffolding in the Glimmerdeep and successfully helped to hinder the mining operation.A band of half-orcs and ruffians loyal to one called Sharkey has begun to dredge the Gladden Fields with equipment left behind from Saruman's failed search for the Ring.Half-orcs and ruffians can be found at Sharkey's Slough in the Gladden Fields.

