You should examine the waters to see if anything has changed.Examine the waters around Rhosgobel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Radagast can be found at Rhosgobel.

You should talk to Radagast.Talk to Radagast'It is just speculation, of course it is. It may be nothing. Let us hope it is nothing!

'But for now, I need to work a magic of protection in order to keep safe my home of Rhosgobel and all of Laerlad while I am away. There is a calm in the woods now; do you hear it? There used to be an old song in these woods, a song that I heard once but have now forgotten. It was sung by all the rivers and streams here in Laerlad, but now it has gone into hiding. If you listen closely enough in the quiet woods you might hear it.

'It was a song of protection, of course it was. I can remember its name, Tauralindalë. If it were to be sung again, perhaps it could keep Laerlad and Rhosgobel well hidden from danger.''What a beautiful song, ${PLAYER}. Yes, I remember it now. The rivers and the streams shall cloud the minds of those who hate, but those who have kindness in their hearts will always find their way.''Of course it worked, my friend! You see the waters shimmering? That is the true gift of the waters. It is the gift that will fool hate and spread kindness throughout the forest.'The old stone walls of Blómgard should be rebuilt and reinforced in order to better defend the village.Field stones can be found near the edge of the woods in Laerlad.

You should gather field stones for Evorik.Gather field stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Crumbling walls can be found in Blómgard.

You should place the stones next to the crumbling walls in Blómgard so the Woodfolk may repair them.Evorik can be found in Blómgard.

You should talk to Evorik.Talk to Evorik'My folk have built sturdy wooden palisades to protect the village, but I fear it will not be enough. There are some old stone walls along the eastern side of the village. If we were to gather more stones from the forest's edge, we could repair the wall. Would you gather up some field stones for us so we could use them to repair the wall, and safe-guard the people of Blómgard?''I thank you for your service to Blómgard. No, do not concern yourself with building the walls! We shall see to it. I would not have you think we needed you to do everything for us! Gathering the stones was enough.

'This old wall was not built by us Woodmen. All I know is that when the wall was once maintained, the forest-demons kept afar. 

'With the old wall mended, I see the village safe, and my spirits lift.'A tribe of Orcs known as the Shapag-hai has invaded the Gladden Fields, polluting its marshlands and threatening the inhabitants of the Vales of Anduin.Lúlstrok can be found in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields.

