You should travel to Ainhard's homestead.Talk to Ainhard'Skalla, the one in command here at Vegbár, asked for help in this goblin matter, and Grimbeorn sent me. I was just about to ask Skalla what the situation is. Would you care to join me?''After you, ${PLAYER}.''Ah, Langhár. Grimbeorn sent you? And who is this outsider with you?'

You introduce yourself and explain that you would like to help with the goblin situation.

'Hmm. If Langhár can vouch for you, I see no issue. Woodmen living south of here have been reporting goblin activity in increasing numbers. Speak to the Beornings nearby and see what you can piece together.''Goblins? None here. The Old Ford has been rather quiet of late.''I have not seen any goblins myself, but several Woodmen spoke of goblin attacks at Waldfast. I have not heard from some of the people living to the South, and I cannot leave my post; will you please report this to Skalla?''Greetings, ${CLASS}. With what can Hertha, Keeper of the Pass, help you? Here to pay the toll?'

She gently chuckles. You explain that you are helping Langhár investigate some reports of goblin activity.

'Ah, you are here on goblin business? I did see some outsiders head toward the goblin gate not long ago, and then the next day, there was evidence of many goblins leaving. That is all I know. 

'The High Pass itself has been quiet. I do hear some very esteemed guests are on their way, however! Very exciting.''Outsiders entering Goblin-town, many goblins leaving, and now reports of homes south of Vegbár under attack. You say you are here to help, so now I am asking you to make good on your word. We have not heard from the forester Ainhard in some time. Go to his home and see if he still lives! We must discover why the goblins have left Goblin-town and now threaten the lands to the south.''Who goes there? Get away from me, villain!'

Ainhard is clearly rattled from whatever happened here. You do your best to calm him down.

