'Let me know when you are ready to continue our search, ${PLAYER}!''Give me a moment, I need to think. What are these goblins up to?''We should return to Vegbár and inform Skalla of the Great Goblin's presence here, and what we have learned about Gundabad's activities! You go on ahead, I will meet you there.''${PLAYER}, you have returned. Tell me what you have learned of the goblins.'

You explain the situation to Skalla: Hobgoblins from Gundabad have deposed the Great Goblin and taken over Goblin-town. The Great Goblin survived, destroyed the village of Waldfast, and now seeks to build up a host of goblins in order to retake his throne. Skalla's eyes grow wide.

'And here we thought the goblins were just getting creative with their raiding! This is a serious situation, ${PLAYER}. This Great Goblin was happy enough to stay in his mountain tunnels and grow fat while his underlings squabbled over scraps, but the hobgoblins are another matter entirely. They are aggressive, vicious, and if reports from the North are true, they are most loyal to the Herald of Winter.

'A unified Gundabad and Goblin-town is an immediate threat to the people of the Vales. If we do not act quickly, a flood of goblins will wash over us, and few will survive. We simply do not have the numbers to combat such a massive force.'Despite your belief that Úbil the Snatcher will never again return to the Vales of Anduin, Atta fears that the creature still lurks in the caves of Woodsedge.Wards should be placed to the north and south of Hultvís at Fil Sulmog, the Old Ford, the eastern ford to Avabárg, and the den of the Hól-budlan slightly north of Málvang. The Sorrow-well lies to the north-west of Hultvís.

Atta has asked you to place carved wards throughout Woodsedge to ensure the Snatcher will never return to the Vales of Anduin. He has also asked you to place a ward at the Sorrow-well, the last known refuge of the Snatcher in Woodsedge and a cave thought to bear a curse against the Woodmen.Set a warding totem at Fil SulmogSet a warding totem at the Old FordSet a warding totem at the eastern ford of AvabárgSet a warding totem at the den of the Hól-budlanThe Sorrow-well can be found to the north-west of Hultvís.

