You should search The Scholar's Abode for Grár's Key.Find Grár's KeyNáin can be found in Járnfast.

You should return to Náin.The entrance to the Howling Pit can be found beyond the last mithril door, deep within Járnfast.

You should seek the entrance of the Howling Pit.Seek the entrance of the Howling PitThe entrance to the Howling Pit can be found beyond the last mithril door, deep within Járnfast.

You should examine the entrance of the Howling Pit.Examine the entrance of the Howling PitNáin can be found next to the Howling Pit.

You should talk to Náin.Talk to Náin'Rukhûsh-minam, the Howling Pit. Three doors protect Járnfast from Rukhûsh-minam. Only one door remains locked and sealed. I have checked and the seal to that final door has not broken. There must be something wrong with Grár's Seal.

'The brave Dwarf Grár sacrificed himself to collapse the opening to the Howling Pit. The Seal of Grár has remained intact ever since, covering the pit. There are only two ways to open the final door. One is to break the seal, and doing so would most certainly lead to our doom. The second is to retrieve Grár's key. Yes, the doors can be opened with a secret key, stored for safe keeping within Erebor.

'Take this writ with you. It will explain the urgency to this matter to anyone who may find it odd of your actions. Seek out the scholar's abode of Mazalu Ugshar. The key remains hidden within. Hurry ${PLAYER}, time is of most importance!''Halt. By order of King Thorin III, Mazalu Ugshar may only be accessed by Erebor's lore-masters until the situation in the Grey Mountains is resolved.'

You hand Glóthin the writ from Náin.

'A writ from the Lord of the Iron Hills? Aye, this is no ordinary writ but a pact between Náin and King Thorin III. I am sorry to keep you. Please continue and accept my apology. We have all been on edge since Karazgar decreed his intentions against those of us in the north.''I am glad you have found Grár's key and returned quickly. I was worried that over the years, it may have been lost within the caverns of Erebor, but we must not tarry. While you were gone we have felt rumblings in Járnfast. Doom comes ever closer.

'Meet me at the entrance to the Howling Pit as soon as you are able.''It is as I feared. The final seal has been torn and will need mending. The mending will take time as working with mithril is not easy. The hole is small which explains why we are not seeing the true horrors that lie below.'Orcs and goblins living in Shathur-munzu appear to be subservient to the Wargs. They should be eliminated.Defeat Orcs and goblins in Shathur-munzuOrcs and goblins subservient to the wargs can be found inside Shathur-munzu.

You should defeat any Orcs and goblins you find.Defeat Orcs and goblins in Shathur-munzu (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed.CompletedYou see Orcs and goblins inside Shathur-munzu, but unlike their usual relationship, these appear to be subservient to the wargs. Perhaps it is because of the presence of Ránulur. You believe that you should eliminate these goblins, regardless of the chain of command, as they pose a threat to the people of Arhaim.You have defeated many of the Orcs and goblins subservient to Ránulur's warg pack. This should make them less of a threat to the people of the Vales, and make a dent in the clearing of Shathur-munzu.By completing this quest, you will automatically complete the discovery deeds for Glimmerdeep, Stormwall, and Thikil-gundu (the Steel Keep).'Deeds! Get your Grey Mountains Instance cluster discovery deeds here!

'Talk to me one more time, and they're all yours!''Deeds, incoming!'The Protectors of the Vales have a small quantity of Motes available.Talk to the Protectors of the Vales to trade Gúlmarks for Motes.

