<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will remove 55 Gúlmarks.</rgb>Radagast is concerned that the Ungoledain may have come to Laerlad because they are searching for Rhosgobel.Radagast can be found in Blómgard.

You should talk to Radagast.Talk to RadagastRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel.

You should talk to Radagast.Talk to Radagast at Rhosgobel'Do you remember what that Ungoladan warrior Lóbruth said to you? He said his leader was answering a call, and that they were all hearing voices of some kind from the shadows! Did you find this leader at Côs Braen? No, of course you did not.

'Here is my guess, ${PLAYER}, and while it is supposition only, I believe you did not encounter this leader because she was away searching for the source of this mysterious call! After I departed Rhosgobel, when the woods grew too dangerous even for a Wizard, many spiders descended upon Rhosgobel. They took over the old Elf-ruins and turned it into a vile den of spiders. Could something about those spiders be calling the Ungoledain leader to Rhosgobel? Let us return to my home as soon as possible, and find out for ourselves!''Quickly now, we must get to Rhosgobel at once!''Mam Murgwid, Mam Murgwid. Mam Murgwid?

'This is not a name I have ever heard before. I have learned enough about the Ungoledain to know they refer only to the late Iphantemel as "Mother." Their pets are the last of Iphantemel's brood. It seems to me there is nothing left for the Ungoledain here. Mam Murgwid must be something else.

'They travel south, as do all the spiders that left Mirkwood. Could they be answering the same call? Oh dear, ${PLAYER}, this is very bad. Why have I not realized this until now? Their true mother must be calling to them. Not Iphantemel, no, not at all! Shelob calls to them. Shelob!'Complete Helegrod - Dragon WingComplete 'Helegrod - Dragon Wing (Tier 2)' at levelComplete Helegrod - Dragon WingComplete 'Helegrod - Dragon Wing (Tier 3)' at levelHéolka poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.Héolka poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.Defeat Héolka, Scourge of the Withered HeathHéolka poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.Defeat Héolka, Scourge of the Withered HeathHéolka poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.CompletedHéolka poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.Héolka, Scourge of the Withered Heath has been defeated and you have significantly weakened the infested Withered Heath.Orcs have attacked many traders on the road in Duskenvale and stolen their supplies. The trader Lúfred has asked you to retrieve the wares.Orcs have stolen many traders' wares by ambushing them on the road to Arhaim.

You should collect the stolen supplies from the Orc camp Brafulug.Collect stolen supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have retrieved the stolen supplies from the Orc camp.

You should return to Lúfred at the Beorning watchpost to inform him.Talk to Lúfred'Several of the carriers I sent to Arhaim have not returned. I suspect the 'Orc activity' these Beornings mentioned was their attacks on my men! The Beornings will not allow me to cross and reclaim my stolen goods. If you are heading in there to deal with the Orcs, will you please keep an eye out for any of my supplies?''Thank you, ${CLASS}. At least I am able to recoup some of my losses. A shame that lives were lost to those brutes.'The Ungoledain feast on tainted foods that would make most ill.Tainted barrels can be found at Côs Braen in Laerlad.

You should destroy any tainted barrels you find.Destroy tainted barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroyed many tainted barrels at Côs Braen.CompletedThe Ungoledain feast on tainted foods that would make most ill. These barrels of tainted provisions must be destroyed.You destroyed vile Ungoledain provisions at Côs Braen, hindering the Ungoledain's plans in Laerlad. The Woodmen of Blómgard will be thankful for your efforts.Hládek the Hoary poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.Hládek the Hoary poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.Defeat Hládek the Hoary, Scourge of Thikil-gunduHládek the Hoary poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.Defeat Hládek the Hoary, Scourge of Thikil-gunduHládek the Hoary poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.CompletedHládek the Hoary poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.Hládek the Hoary, Scourge of Thikil-gundu has been defeated. You have removed a significant threat.The forester Ainhard's hounds ran into the woods and became lost when the goblins passed through. He has asked for your help tracking them down.Ainhard's three hounds, Hrában, Skádda, and Grymil, can be found somewhere in the forest near his home.

You should find Hrában, Skádda, and Grymil and send them home.Find HrábanFind SkáddaFind GrymilThe forester Ainhard lives south of Vegbár.

You should talk to Ainhard.Talk to Ainhard'My hounds ran off when those terrible goblins scurried through here. They must be so frightened, alone in the woods! Not the goblins, my hounds!

'They will respond to their names if you call to them, I am sure. They are Hrában, Skádda, and Grymil. Please, you must find them and send them home before the goblins come back!''Oh thank you, thank you, ${PLAYER}! My sweet hounds are back home, and now they will be safe from those monsters out there. When I feel all is clear, I will bring them to Vegbár.'The wilds are no longer safe, so the village of Arhaim cannot freely hunt the deer there. Braving the wilds to provide them food will surely earn you their favour.To gain the favour of the villagers of Arhaim, you have been asked to hunt deer in Duskenvale.

You should collect venison from the deer in Duskenvale.Collect venison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Goslim can be found in the village of Arhaim in Duskenvale.

You should bring the collected venison to Goslim.Talk to Goslim'You wish to earn the trust of the village? Very well. As a people, we live off the land. Hunters who enter the dangerous wilds to feed the village are highly esteemed here. If you enter the forest and hunt deer for us, you may win the favour of the people.''Thank you, traveller. The forest has become dangerous, and hunting is no longer safe. This venison will feed us for several days. I will tell the others how you bravely entered the wilds to hunt on our behalf.'Fearing that Nori has met with a terrible end at the hands of Karazgar or the mysterious dwarf-wights within Thikil-gundu, Dori and Company must muster the courage to enter the Steel Keep.Dori can be found in Thikil-gundu. If you have become separated, you may call him and the rest of the company by using your horn.

You have come to Thikil-gundu in search of Nori. You should now speak to Dori in Thikil-gundu.Talk to Dori in Thikil-gunduThe hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt can be found in the centre of Durûz-mazal, the Chamber of Faces.

Dori has directed you and the rest of the company to search the hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt for signs of Nori.The smithies of Kall-khebâb can be found in the eastern halls of Thikil-gundu.

