You should talk to Baradal about what just occurred.Talk to BaradalShathur-munzu can be found west of Arhaim, in the wilds of Duskenvale.

You should find Shathur-munzu.Find Shathur-munzuBaradal can be called to your side with Baradal's summoning horn.

You should talk to Baradal.Talk to Baradal'Finish any other business you have in the village. Then, we will head into the forest to find Shathur-munzu. Let us see if these 'demons' are real.''Whenever you are ready, ${PLAYER}.''This cart is mostly empty, and misses both horse and owner. Someone may have headed toward Shathur-munzu in search of dwarf-gold. These tracks seem fairly recent; perhaps the ones who made them are still alive. We should head into the forest and search for them.''We found him too late. Unfortunate, but he did not heed the warnings of the villagers. I have heard many tales of greed twisting the hearts of Men.

'There must be some evidence nearby as to the identity of the 'demon' who did this. And perhaps the horse who pulled that cart is still alive.'Baradal is slightly shaken by the sudden death of the horse.

'We are not alone out here! There are deep claw marks in its hide! Be on guard! The poor horse. He loyally followed his master into danger and met an undeserved fate.

'Wait... look at these tracks! I believe the demons feared by the Woodmen are simply wargs. We are more than capable of handling this threat. We should proceed to Shathur-munzu at once.''The size of this paw print is rather alarming. Was this left by the 'Shadow Hunter'? Weapons at the ready, ${PLAYER}.'Radagast has travelled to the Woodmen village of Hultvís, seeking your assistance with strange shadows lurking in the Gladden Fields.Radagast can be found at Hultvís.

You should talk to Radagast.Talk to Radagast at HultvísRadagast can be found at Hultvís.

