<rgb=#00FF00>If you are interested in following the storyline of the Black Book of Mordor, Chapter 10 will bring you naturally to the Vales of Anduin. Chapter 9 is available by speaking with Durin on the upper level of Skarháld.</rgb>'Absolutely not. My decision has nothing to do with the King of the Greenleaves and everything to do with my people. However, I permit you to stay for as long as you need. I am not unkind.''${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. My father has sent me to the Vales of Anduin to resolve a trade dispute. When King Thranduil declared no one leave or enter Eryn Lasgalen, trade between the Elves and the Beornings was halted. Now he wishes to resume trade, for Elves, Men, and dwarves all rely upon this. The security of the north depends on Beornings and their willingness to trade. If you and Gandalf are headed to see Grimbeorn, perhaps you would speak to him of the reopening of trade between the Beornings and Elves. If there is one fact that I know of Grimbeorn, it is that he does not welcome guests. If we were to all greet him together, the task I was sent to do would surely fail.'King Thranduil wishes to resolve a trade dispute in the Vales of Anduin so that he may continue to provide assistance to the Men, Elves, and dwarves of the north.Legolas can be found at the Forest Gate between Eryn Lasgalen and the Vales of Anduin.

You should talk to Legolas about King Thranduil's request to open the trade route through the Beorning-lands in the Vales of Anduin.Talk to Legolas at the Forest Gate in Eryn LasgalenLegolas can be found at the Forest Gate between Eryn Lasgalen and the Vales of Anduin.

You should talk to Legolas about King Thranduil's request to open the trade route through the Beorning-lands in the Vales of Anduin.Talk to Legolas at the Forest Gate in Eryn LasgalenGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorninglands of the Vales of Anduin.

You should talk to Grimbeorn.Talk to GrimbeornKing Thranduil requires your assistance in the Vales of Anduin. Thranduil has deemed Eryn Lasgalen safe and has opened the western road from Felegoth to the Vales of Anduin. He wishes for trade to continue between the Elves and Beornings. This was met with resistance from Grimbeorn, the leader of the Beornings, for reasons unknown. King Thranduil requires this dispute to be resolved hastily and diplomatically. The Elves, Men, and dwarves of the north all rely heavily upon trade. The security of the north is at stake.'${PLAYER}, you have received my father's request. It is good to see you again. Your assistance in this delicate task is most appreciated. Now, it would be unwise for both of us to travel to the Beorninghús to meet with Grimbeorn together. He does not welcome guests and I do not wish for my task to fail. Would you speak with Grimbeorn? I wish to scout Eryn Lasgalen, and make sure roads are truly safe. Come find me again once you have Grimbeorn's answer.''Absolutely not. My decision has nothing to do with the King of the Greenleaves and everything to do with my people. However, I permit you to stay for as long as you need. I am not unkind.'Defeat many beasts in the Ironfold.Defeat many beasts in the Ironfold.Defeat many beasts in the IronfoldDefeat many beasts in the Ironfold.Defeat many beasts in the Ironfold.Defeat many beasts in the IronfoldDefeat many wicked Easterlings in the Ironfold.Defeat many wicked Easterlings in the Ironfold.Defeat many wicked Easterlings in the IronfoldDefeat many wicked Easterlings in the Ironfold.Defeat many wicked Easterlings in the Ironfold.Defeat many wicked Easterlings in the IronfoldFor those visiting the Beorninghús, it is important to help in the daily work of Beornings.The vineyard can be found west of the Beorninghús.

