You should bring the jam to Gírta.Gírta asked you to make jam from scratch: a difficult task, but one which the Beorning matriarch believes you can accomplish. Perhaps it would be best to begin by picking grapes in the orchard.'This is a splendid jam. You have done well! It will spread well on crusty bread, or perhaps I will add it to a dessert. There are always plenty of possibilities to be found for a tasty jam!'Káldbak poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.Káldbak poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.Defeat Káldbak, Scourge of the Withered HeathKáldbak poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.Defeat Káldbak, Scourge of the Withered HeathKáldbak poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.CompletedKáldbak poses a great threat to all that enter the Withered Heath.Káldbak, Scourge of the Withered Heath has been defeated and you have significantly weakened the infested Withered Heath.Hithril of the Elves of Lórien is concerned about the shadowy waters that surround the sunken ruins of Kidzul-kâlah.Weapons taken from the Gladden Fields into Kidzul-kâlah should be destroyed before they can be used for some foul purpose.Destroy shunned swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The dredging machines stand like forgotten hulks in the Gladden Fields, idle now, but not always. Once there was a time when they sifted soil and mud, and drew weapons and armour-pieces from long ago to light. Someone or something has taken these unearthed treasures into Kidzul-kâlah, whether for grave robbery or some other purpose I cannot say. But if that purpose be foul, as I think it must, they should be found and destroyed.'Hithril of the Elves of Lórien is concerned about the shadowy waters that surround the sunken ruins of Kidzul-kâlah.Some creature stirs the shades of Kidzul-kâlah to wakefulness, and it must be defeated.Defeat the Bonds of the Drowned'Shades have been seen in the Gladden Fields before now, but never in such number. Someone or something stirs the shades of Kidzul-kâlah to wakefulness, ${PLAYER}, and makes fast the bonds that keep them here. Whatever creature this may be, it must be defeated.'Hithril, of the Elves of Lórien, is concerned about the shadowy waters that surround the sunken ruins of Kidzul-kâlah.Darkwaters menace the drowned ruins of Kidzul-kâlah, and must be defeated.Defeat Kidzul darkwaters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat shadow-grims (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The ruins of Kidzul-kâlah are surrounded by ice-cold waters, but nothing chills the heart quite like the evil that rises from that still pond. Shadowy darkwaters will menace the Vales of Anduin if they are not defeated. Do you understand me, ${PLAYER}?'Hithril of the Elves of Lórien is concerned about the shadowy waters that surround the sunken ruins of Kidzul-kâlah.Brooches of the fallen have been taken to Kidzul-kâlah, and should be reclaimed from those who deserve them not.Collect brooches of the fallen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The dredging machines in the Gladden Fields unearthed many items from the swamp, ${PLAYER}: weapons, armour-pieces, and other trinkets. Some of these have made their way to Kidzul-kâlah, and it offends me to think that brooches and jewels of personal significance were removed from those who perished wearing them. Reclaim these, if you can.'Driven from Tríubad by the Taurogrim, the Woodmen hope to repel the wood-demons from their remaining settlements in Woodsedge.Taurogrim can be found throughout Tríubad in Woodsedge.

Believing it might cleanse the Vales of Anduin of their evil, Clothar has asked you to burn the remains of fallen Taurogrim at Tríubad.Defeat Taurogrim and burn their remains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have burned the remains of many of the Taurogrim at Tríubad.Completed'Perhaps Tríubad is lost, but the wood-demons cannot come to Hultvís! They must be stopped, and I believe I know how it can be achieved!

'It was said in tales of old that the Thyrsir could not truly be slain. If one of the wood-demons fell to the axe, its mouldering remains would give rise to more of its kind. Only when they were put to flame could their evil be ended. Demons they may be, but they are demons wrought of wood, and that means they must fear fire!

'If you are to overcome the wood-demons, you must swiftly burn their remains after defeating them. For each of our sakes, let us hope the tale spoke true!'With the Taurogrim defeated and their twisted forms burned, the familiar crackling of firewood echoes through Tríubad. Although you suspect that the Taurogrim will soon return, you have done well to aid the Woodmen.Defeat many leaders in the resource instances of Ered Mithrin.Defeat many leaders in the resource instances of Ered Mithrin.Defeat many leaders in the resource instances of Ered MithrinDefeat many leaders in the resource instances of Ered Mithrin.Defeat many leaders in the resource instances of Ered Mithrin.Defeat many leaders in the resource instances of Ered MithrinCowardly goblins are lurking in the forest near the homes of Woodmen. They wait patiently for their chance to break in and steal whatever they can.Cowardly goblins can be found in the forest near the Woodmen homes.

