You should collect the pages to complete the song.Collect Page 1Collect Page 2Collect Page 3Collect Page 4Collect Page 5Collect Page 6Collect Page 7Collect Page 8Collect Page 9Collect Page 10Completed.CompletedYou have found a verse of what appears to be a Woodfolk song, perhaps written down by a scholar passing through the Vales. You might be able to complete the song if you find all of the missing verses.After a fair amount of searching, you have completed the song. This seems to be a song the Woodfolk sing to their children to warn them away from the marshes. The song itself is quite old, and has been passed down verbally for many generations. Could it be that Old Mad Ubb was based on a real person, perhaps 'Úbil the Snatcher,' a figure of whom the Woodfolk still speak? The unpleasantness of which Old Mad Ubb is accused in the doggerel strikes you as familiar, somehow.Verses of an old song can be found scattered around the Vales of Anduin. Perhaps you can complete it if you find them all.Old-elven parchments can be found scattered throughout the Vales of Anduin.

You should collect the pages to complete the song.Collect Page 1Collect Page 2Collect Page 3Collect Page 4Collect Page 5Collect Page 6Collect Page 7Collect Page 8Collect Page 9Completed.CompletedYou have found a verse of what appears to be ancient Elven song, perhaps written down by those Elves who once lived in the forest. You might be able to complete the song if you find all of the missing verses.After a fair amount of searching, you have completed the song. This seems to be the full text of a very old song about the woods and waters of the Wilderland. The song itself is quite old, and may have been all but lost, if not for your efforts.Lúbtul poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.Lúbtul poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.Defeat Lúbtul, Scourge of Thikil-gunduLúbtul poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.Defeat Lúbtul, Scourge of Thikil-gunduLúbtul poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.CompletedLúbtul poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.Lúbtul, Scourge of Thikil-gundu has been defeated. You have removed a significant threat.Goblins are still lurking in the forest near Ainhard's home, waiting for an opportunity to steal from him.Goblin looters can be found stealthily skulking near Ainhard's homestead.

