You should talk to Langhár.Talk to Langhár'Be on your guard, ${PLAYER}. I can still smell some goblins lurking nearby. I suspect they are waiting for us to leave, so they can kill Ainhard and steal from what remains of his home. We will show those cowardly vermin what happens to those who cross the Beornings!''Be on your guard, ${PLAYER}. I can still smell some goblins lurking nearby. I suspect they are waiting for us to leave, so they can kill Ainhard and steal from what remains of his home. We will show those cowardly vermin what happens to those who cross the Beornings!''Hah! That will teach them. The rest should scurry like rats back to the holes from which they crawled!'Marzlok poses a great threat to all that attempt to remove resources while under his watch in Glimmerdeep.Marzlok poses a great threat to all that attempt to remove resources while under his watch in Glimmerdeep.Defeat Marzlok, Scourge of GlimmerdeepMarzlok poses a great threat to all that attempt to remove resources while under his watch in Glimmerdeep.Defeat Marzlok, Scourge of GlimmerdeepMarzlok poses a great threat to all that attempt to remove resources while under his watch in Glimmerdeep.CompletedMarzlok poses a great threat to all that attempt to remove resources while under his watch in Glimmerdeep.Marzlok, Scourge of Glimmerdeep has been defeated. You have removed a significant threat.Sharkey has entrusted the newest excavation in the Gladden Fields to the most loyal and cunning of his followers.Collect medallions of loyalty from Sharkey's MenMedallions of loyalty are carried by the highest-ranking brigands and half-orcs in the warrens of Tûn Melen.

You have discovered curious medallions carried by the brigands and half-orcs in the warrens of Tûn Melen. Emblazoned with an 'S', they denote proven loyalty to Sharkey. You should strip them from their bearers and keep them to return to Radagast.Collect medallions of loyalty from Sharkey's Men (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected a few medallions of loyalty from Sharkey's Men in the warrens of Tûn Melen.CompletedAfter encountering a number of Sharkey's Men in the warrens of Tûn Melen, you have noticed that some of them bear curious medallions emblazoned with an 'S', signifying their loyalty to Sharkey.

You should collect these medallions from Sharkey's Men and keep them to deliver to Radagast.You have collected several medallions of loyalty from Sharkey's Men. With their bearers defeated, you have disrupted Sharkey's efforts to gain a stronger foothold in the Vales of Anduin.In the darkness of the Sorrow-well, you have discovered a curious trinket left behind by one of Úbil the Snatcher's victims.Atta can be found in Hultvís.

You have discovered a trinket bearing the name of Atta's long-deceased sister, Amelina. You should deliver it to Atta at once.Radagast can be found somewhere in Hultvís.

After Radagast came to Hultvís, he spoke to Atta about the Snatcher. Overcome with emotion at the return of his sister's trinket, Atta has vowed to spend his remaining days travelling Middle-earth.Find Radagast in HultvísRadagast can be found standing beside Ríkmar in Hultvís.

You have found Radagast in Hultvís and should now speak to him.Talk to RadagastIn the deepest recesses of the Sorrow-well, you have discovered a small, stone trinket in the shape of a bear. The moisture in the cavern has eroded the trinket, but as your fingers pass over it, you feel a number of shallow grooves on the back. Flipping it over, you discover the worn outlines of an inscription.

After examining it for a time, you are able to make out the old writing carved into the trinket. It reads: "For Amelina".

You should return the trinket to Atta.'You did not tell me you were a friend to the Wizard, ${PLAYER}!

'Radagast told me he had come to Hultvís on your behalf, and he knew at once that I was the man he sought. He spoke to me of your adventures together in distant lands, but he also told me what became of the Snatcher... Gollum... the hól-budlan once named Sméagol.

'I learned it was Radagast himself who drove Sméagol from Avabárg, but the creature escaped into the wilds and fled under the mountains for many years. When his power to walk unseen was stolen from him, he returned to the Vales... and that was when he stalked Hultvís once again. Not long after Beorn saved me, his kinsfolk drove the creature from the Vales and Sméagol was too fearful of their wrath to return. Radagast said what was taken from him gnawed at him greater than any hunger, and that he spent the rest of his days in pursuit of what was stolen from him... a simple trinket, Radagast said.

'Although at first I questioned his wisdom and how he could have come to know such things, I came to believe his words. Radagast is a Wizard, after all! His tale has done much to ease my mind, but I am sorry to have sent you on an unnecessary errand all the same. I am even more sorry that I did not trust your words... but you must understand what I have endured. What a sorry creature Sméagol became... he has my pity, but he is undeserving of forgiveness. If he had not perished in flames, I....'

Atta suddenly glances at the stone trinket you hold.

'But... what is that you have there, ${PLAYER}?'

You hand Amelina's trinket to Atta. In disbelief, Atta examines the trinket and runs his fingers along the old inscription. Atta clutches the trinket to his chest and begins to weep.

'Amelina... my dear sister. She was taken so long ago... but after all this time, part of her still lives. I will carry her memory with me always, ${PLAYER}.

'Do not worry for me, ${PLAYER}. You find the Wizard and I will set out to thank Grimbeorn for his father's kindness. After that, well... my sister and I will have much travelling to do.

'I am old in my years, but there is time for me yet!''Well, well... I thought I might find you here, ${PLAYER}. And I had time enough to tend to another matter while I awaited your arrival!'

'Although I spared old Atta many of its chapters, the tale of Sméagol seemed to offer him some measure of comfort. The minds of Men too often fall prey to fear and despair, and Atta was no different. His childhood was one of great pain and loss and it shaped him as he grew older. Indeed, until this very day, Atta lived his life in fearful vigilance... and he denied himself the chance to travel beyond the woods' edge.

'But, my friend, I believe Atta has always had a great strength within him.

Radagast chuckles to himself.

'Indeed, he only needed a Wizard and a kind-hearted ${RACE} to show him!'Waldfast, a tiny Woodfolk village in the Wolf-denes, has been taken over by goblins. Langhár would like you to remove the goblin threat.Goblins have taken over the village of Waldfast in southern Wolf-denes.

