<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest.</rgb>Defeat Helghúr in Óinsbridge.Defeat HelghúrYou should return to to Stráhek the Stout in Skarháld and let him know of your victory at Óinsbridge.Talk to Stráhek the Stout'Remember how I was afraid of that wizard in the woods? Well I tell you those woods are no good! Apparently those spider-folk are back and they're very upset! I can't possibly retrieve resources in Óinsbridge knowing they're around!

'We need to drive them out of Óinsbridge! Are you... well, will you go do it?'

<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest.</rgb>'Could you leave as soon as possible? The Ungoledain pose a great threat to Óinsbridge.''You have dealt a significant blow to the Ungoledain once again, ${PLAYER}. Their numbers have been weakened... for now.'Since the days of Atta's youth, the terrible creature that haunted Avabárg has passed into legend and it is now known by a more fanciful name among the children of Hultvís.Children of the Woodmen can be found in Hultvís.

Unwilling to speak more of it himself, Atta has told you to ask the children of Hultvís about a creature named Ubb.Atta can be found in Hultvís.

You have spoken to the children of Hultvís about Ubb, and you have learned much of the legend of the Snatcher. You should return to Atta.Talk to Atta'Many in Hultvís think me mad, but the children believe me!

'They have heard the old tales from their mothers and fathers... those sinister rhymes that speak of Old Mad Ubb. A creature come out of the night to punish children for their misdeeds? Nonsense!

'But... buried within the fables their parents tell them of Ubb, there are truths of which I dare not speak.

'Ask the children of Hultvís about the one called Ubb!''Do you believe them, ${PLAYER}?

'If you knew as I do... you would.'Swarming gnats and pesky flies in the Beorning-lands are hard to bear, even for a Beorning.Vale-flies and biting vale-gnats can be found in the Beorning-lands.

