You should talk to Langhár.Talk to Langhár'Those goblins nearly destroyed poor Ainhard's home! I feel for the poor man, living by himself out here. Perhaps we can spare a few moments and help clean up the mess.''That is much better. Now Ainhard will have less to clean up on his own when he returns from Vegbár.'Audvak of the Woodmen is concerned about the gloom that has descended upon Avabárg.Audvak can be found at Hultvís in Woodsedge.

You should speak to Audvak.Complete 'Avabárg: Sunken Gloom'Complete 'Avabárg: Source of Gloom'Complete 'Avabárg: Buried Omens'Complete 'Avabárg: Wayward Bones'Audvak can be found at Hultvís in Woodsedge.

You should speak to Audvak.Talk to Audvak'A gloom has come to Avabárg. Can you see it cast upon the middle of the Anduin, good ${RACE}? What omens it brings, I know not. What I can say is this: the Woodmen have not stepped foot upon Avabárg in quite some time, for only misfortune has followed when Avabárg is inhabited. The misfortunes of Avabárg are so gruesome, I can not speak of them further. This gloom, however is of a different misfortune. We Woodmen have never seen anything as such. I fear if we do nothing, we may bring upon ourselves the greatest misfortune the Woodmen have ever seen. I ask of you to investigate Avabárg for us, ${PLAYER}.''Good luck, friend. Avabárg has become home to a dreadful gloom, and you should tread within its walls with caution.''It seems my worries were well-founded, ${PLAYER}! You found the spirit within Avabárg, and sent it away in defeat? May it stay gone, and the gloom with it!

'Thank you for lending the Woodmen your aid.'Hithril of the Elves of Lórien is concerned about the shadowy waters that surround the sunken ruins of Kidzul-kâlah.Hithril can be found at Hultvís in Woodsedge.

You should speak to Hithril.Complete 'Kidzul-kâlah: Dark Waters'Complete 'Kidzul-kâlah: Bonds of the Drowned'Complete 'Kidzul-kâlah: Battles Past'Complete 'Kidzul-kâlah: The Fallen'Hithril can be found at Hultvís in Woodsedge.

You should speak to Hithril.Talk to Hithril'The darkness that has settled upon the Gladden Fields comes in some part from the dwarf-ruins of Kidzul-kâlah, inaccessible for so long but once more open. I have observed both an anger and a sadness in the shades that now wander the swamp, but I cannot speak of their source, for I do not know it. Look to Kidzul-kâlah and you may learn what drives them, ${PLAYER}, and in that flooded fortress you may do some good on behalf of the people here, as well.''Few know what lurks within Kidzul-kâlah, for it has been flooded and inaccessible for so long. Good fortune to you, friend!''A dwarf fortress attracts danger to it, ${PLAYER}, either abandoned or occupied. Kidzul-kâlah should have remained inaccessible, but once opened, it is good to meet its danger outright... as you have done! We are grateful for your efforts on our behalf, and on behalf of all those who dwell in the Vales of Anduin.'The Beorning Ragnild is concerned about the threat posed by the wargs of Duskenvale and the dwarf ruins of Shathur-munzu.Ragnild can be found at Hultvís in Woodsedge.

