Many of the Shapag-hai that remain in Woodsedge have gathered at Fil Sulmog. From the safety of their encampment, they launch raids against passing traders and unwary travellers. You should defeat them before they bring more harm to the people of the Vales.Defeat Shapag-hai in Woodsedge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many of the Shapag-hai at Fil Sulmog.CompletedA tribe of Orcs known as the Shapag-hai escaped the final battles of the War and fled into the hills of Woodsedge. Although they are seemingly few in number, they pose a great threat to unwary travellers in the Vales of Anduin. If trade and travel between the Beorning-lands and Woodsedge is to be renewed, the Shapag-hai must be defeated and their raids put to an end.You defeated many of the Shapag-hai who escaped into the hills of Woodsedge. With their numbers thinned, it is unlikely they will be able to continue to launch raids on traders and travellers in the Vales of Anduin.Before the coming of Hrímil Frost-heart and her spawn, Vethúg Wintermind, the Steel Keep was home to both the Longbeards and Zhélruka over the course of many long years. In the wake of Vethúg's defeat at Erebor, Nori set forth with a small company to reclaim the lost hoards of Thikil-gundu. However, great wealth is not all that remains hidden in its frozen halls, and the Dwarves of the North shall soon have to contend with the true master of Thikil-gundu if what was lost might still be reclaimed.Before the coming of Hrímil Frost-heart and her spawn, Vethúg Wintermind, the Steel Keep was home to both the Longbeards and Zhélruka over the course of many long years. In the wake of Vethúg's defeat at Erebor, Nori set forth with a small company to reclaim the lost hoards of Thikil-gundu. However, great wealth is not all that remains hidden in its frozen halls, and the Dwarves of the North shall soon have to contend with the true master of Thikil-gundu if what was lost might still be reclaimed.Complete 'Delver of Thikil-gundu'Complete 'Lost Lore of the Dwarf-holds: Thikil-gundu'Complete 'Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep -- Tier 1'Complete 'Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep -- Tier 2'Complete 'Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep -- Tier 3'There is much work to be done, if the Zhélruka hope to settle in the formidable Grey Mountains.There is much work to be done, if the Zhélruka hope to settle in the formidable Grey Mountains.Assist the ZhélrukaAssist the ZhélrukaAssist the ZhélrukaThere is much work to be done, if the Zhélruka hope to settle in the formidable Grey Mountains.Lend a hand in Skarháld by assisting Stráhek the Stout and by completing Wanted Pebbles quests.

