You should talk to Garsind in Arhaim.Talk to GarsindThe belongings of the victims of the wargs can be found scattered in Shathur-munzu. You believe the people of Arhaim would be grateful to have them back.'I recognize many of these items, ${PLAYER}. Some from unwary hunters, some from treasure-seekers, some from valiant fools seeking to end the threat. This one...'

She opens one of the satchels, and pulls out a battered cloth doll.

'This belonged to my son's daughter. She slipped away one evening and was lost to the forest. He knew her lost, and went seeking vengeance against the Shadow Hunter, so this tragedy would never befall anyone else. He was never seen again, leaving two more children fatherless.

'This place has known so much grief it has become a part of the very earth. Everyone living in Arhaim has lost someone. We carry on the best we can, despite these sorrows. You have done us a great service by bringing back these mementos. You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'Ohtar, Esquire of Isildur, has noticed some of the provisions in Díngarth have become spoiled from sitting too long in the stores.Spoiled food can be found in Díngarth.

You should remove any spoiled food found in Díngarth.Remove spoiled food in Díngarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ohtar can be found in Díngarth.

You should talk to Ohtar.Talk to Ohtar'This is embarrassing, friend.

'The siege has dragged on for so long that Díngarth is no longer in the centre of the fighting; the war continues further to the east. We have seen fewer and fewer soldiers within these walls, but ours is still a strategic fortification and must be occupied. The attention of the commanders lies elsewhere, however, and some small things have gone neglected.

'What are these small things? Well... some of the provisions have spoiled, and the meat we kept here at Díngarth has rotted. We do not need for our soldiers to be sickened by turned meat! Go and search the provisions for any which has gone bad and dispose of it.''You are sure that you have disposed of all the spoiled food? Good, good!

'I understand that Orcs have been known to feast on spoiled and rotten meat, but that is not something Isildur would allow for his own soldiers, and as his esquire I have taken it upon myself to see they do not have to do so!

'That was a lot of spoiled food, friend. Do we have any provisions at all left in Díngarth? We will need to do something about that....'The soldier Calion wants to give those who sacrificed their lives in battle a proper burial.Slain warriors can be found in Arandor.

You should bury the bodies of any slain warriors you come across.Bury the bodies of slain warriors in Arandor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Buried many slain warriors in Arandor.Completed'The march from Díngarth to Adambel has become a sad one, and my eyes well up just to think on't. The bodies of our friends and fellow soldiers are strewn about the battlefields, for none have taken the time to give them a proper burial. What haste can there be when our siege has lasted for so long, and shows no sign of stopping? 

'We must honour them, and show that they are remembered, and died not in vain. The war has taken its toll, yet we keep fighting! Let us give them proper burials. We must take the time for that, at least, or we are no better than the Orcs.'The bodies of the slain will be given a proper burial, and you know that this small toil will have a great effect upon the morale of the soldiers who still live and fight for the Great Alliance.Many farm animals in the Vales of Anduin are upset and could use kind and calming hand.Upset animals can be found throughout the Vales of Anduin.

