You should talk to Aflur Smokebeard.Talk to Aflur Smokebeard'I have not seen anything strange but have certainly felt something strange beneath my feet. The miners have felt it, too. There are rumblings coming from within the mines. Everyone refuses to work as they fear a cave in. I do not blame them. What could be causing this strange shaking below?! You must find out for us.''Creatures in the mines?! If these creatures are as vicious as you say, no one should be allowed to enter the Hammerstead mines. I will make sure the gates to the mines remain locked and guarded until Náin orders us to reopen them.'You have repelled the half-orcs and ruffians in the Gladden Fields, but it is your discovery of Sharkey's true identity that will be of greatest interest to Radagast.Radagast can be found in Hultvís.

You have discovered Sharkey's identity and made safe the Gladden Fields. You should return to Radagast in Hultvís.Talk to Radagast in Hultvís'I owe you my life, ${PLAYER}. 

'I'll make for Blómgard with the goods that Sharkey - er, Garmog - and his demons stole and see if they don't belong to any of my kinsfolk there. I suppose I'll have to build a new waggon, but I can look after myself now.'

Tautila turns to leave, but quickly turns back.

'Don't you worry about me. You should get back to Hultvís and tell Radagast all about Sharkey!''Ah, good! I am glad you've returned, ${PLAYER}. You have been a great help to me!

'My sparrow delivered the water sample you gathered to me, my bunting told me of your victory over the Orcs, but my thrush lost sight of you. I'd begun to worry that Sharkey proved a more formidable foe than I'd been led to believe! Is Sharkey defeated?'

You explain to Radagast that the leader of the ruffians in the Gladden Fields was an old half-orc named Garmog, who impersonated Sharkey in an attempt to amass a small fortune from the lost relics of the Gladden Fields.

'A half-orc? I had heard he was a Man, but now it seems that neither is true. Who is Sharkey?'

You tell Radagast that Saruman is Sharkey. Radagast falls silent for a long while.

'Gandalf told me that the Onodrim have imprisoned Saruman in Orthanc. Is that not so?

'When there is time at last, I will ride to Orthanc and question him myself!'Ríkmar has heard troubling stories concerning Blómgard, a small Woodman settlement in the southern reaches of Laerlad.Blómgard can be found at the edge of the southern wood of Laerlad in the Vales of Anduin.

You should travel to Blómgard and see if you could be of any help there.Travel to Blómgard in LaerladOdahild can be found in Blómgard.

