You should talk to Odahild, the leader of Blómgard.Talk to Odahild, leader of BlómgardRadagast can be found in Blómgard.

You should talk to Radagast.Talk to Radagast'Listen well, ${RACE}. I have heard troubling rumours from the south, and I would share them with you. They may be the falsest of lies, but then again they might be true. I cannot judge, so I leave it to you.

'These tales come from Blómgard, a village to the south, in Laerlad. They speak of shadows in the night and a frightful scuttling sound upon the roofs of the village. Now, I have not spoken with their leader Odahild since the Elves gave these woods to us, but she is not one to speak falsely. There are good men and women in that village, and if we can save them from this creeping danger we should do so! And if these are just tales, well, at least we will know for certain.''Yes, I am Odahild, the leader of this village. The tales you have heard of scuttling shadows in the night are true, every word of them, and they have brought a number of adventurers here seeking to learn more.

'They brought this Wizard hither as well. He says you are a friend of his. Perhaps, then, you could kindly ask him to leave? He brings only ill omens with him on this visit!''We always meet in less than ideal circumstances, ${PLAYER}! Have you noticed? I certainly have. Do you know that some folk believe my arrival actually draws these problems with them? Preposterous, I know, but people do think so nevertheless!'Campanula Chubb has heard the tale of adventurers braving The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu and would like you to bring her evidence of this terrible place.Forged Rift-iron Coins can be earned by defeating Thrâng once per day during the Summer Festival in Boss From The Vaults: Thrâng.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest can only be advanced on Tier 2 of Boss From The Vaults: Thrâng. In addition, this quest can only be completed once per Summer Festival.</rgb>Collect Forged Rift-iron Coins from Thrâng (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Campanula Chubb can be found at the Party Tree in the Shire.

You have collected a number of Forged Rift-iron Coins and you should now deliver them to Campanula Chubb.'Hello there! Enjoying the Summer Festival? Say, if you're feeling brave, I've got a job you would be perfect for!

'One day, I was enjoying a meal and a drink at the Green Dragon, and I overhead a Minstrel spinning some tales. He told the story of a group of Rangers and adventurers entering a great rift in the foul lands of Angmar, and facing all matter of horrors. They say the pit was so deep the ground itself was red-hot like iron in a forge, and it was home to fire giants and flaming Orcs!

'Flaming Orcs! Can you believe it? I couldn't, either, but then, he pulled out a most unusual coin. It was dark, and had a peculiar sheen. Rift-iron, he said it was, made from the metal and obsidian from that horrible place. That piqued my interest!

'I'm hearing whispers that the Rift has opened again, and adventures like yourself are braving the depths. If you bring me some of these coins as proof of this tale, I will reward you for your efforts!'You hold out the coins you have gathered. Campanula accepts them, a wide grin spreading across her face.

'These are surely the same coins that I saw that day in the Green Dragon! So the tale was true! Thank you, adventurer, for braving that terrible place for the sake of this old hobbit's curiosity!

'Here, take this gift. It's the least I can do. Enjoy the rest of the Summer Festival!'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Complete Ered Mithrin Dragon-kind SlayerComplete Quests of the Dwarf-holdsComplete Friend to the Grey Mountains ExpeditionDiscover new and rare iron veins in the Ironfold.Discover new and rare iron veins in the Ironfold.Discover new and rare iron veins in the IronfoldLost spirits move throughout the old dwarf ruins of Kidzul-kâlah.Kidzul-kâlah can be found alongside the Gladdenmere.

