<rgb=#FF0000>Noffer must be present to find the truffles.</rgb>Collect truffles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ingelfled can be found in the village of Arhaim in Duskenvale.

You should bring the truffles and Noffer to Ingelfled.Talk to IngelfledNoffer can be called with the pig whistle.

You should talk to Noffer and offer him a truffle.Offer a truffle to Noffer'Allow me to introduce my trusty partner, Noffer! He is a pig with a job, and he's very good at his job.

'To the south, where the river bends, you will find a place where the wild boars lie around and wallow in the mud. The reason they like this spot in particular is what can be found beneath the earth: delicious truffles! The boars can smell them, and know where to dig. We learned that pigs can be trained to find them as well. Noffer here is very good at sniffing them out.

'Why don't you take Noffer for a walk and see if he can find any truffles for you?''Here, take this whistle. If you lose track of him, he will come running when he hears it. Take good care of him.''These look delicious. Good work, ${PLAYER}! And good work, Noffer! Here, why don't you give him one as a reward for his hard work?'Noffer grunts happily as he gently takes the truffle from your hand. He trots back to Ingelfled with the truffle in his mouth and begins munching away at it.Hundreds of years ago, a terrible creature dwelt within the ruins of Avabárg and devoured those unfortunate enough to cross its path.Spirits can be found in Avabárg.

Atta has asked you to travel to Avabárg and put to rest the spirits of the unfortunate Woodmen that were taken by a terrible creature long ago.Put spirits to rest in Avabárg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Atta can be found in Hultvís.

You have defeated many of the spirits in Avabárg.Talk to Atta'Before the creature came to dwell at the woods' edge, it first made its home in the ruins of Avabárg. It was long after the North-men abandoned the old keep, but long ago just the same. Yea, long before even my grandfather was born....

'In the depths of Avabárg, the creature hid from the only thing it feared: the light. But in the dark of the night, it would creep forth. On some nights, the creature would merely sit atop the walls of Avabárg and peer across the river with its unblinking eyes. On others, it would sneak across the Anduin and... through some devilry, it would conceal itself from sight as it drew near to our villages. My people were taken from their homes... from their beds... and always the trail led to Avabárg. When my ancestors found gnawed bones in the depths of Avabárg, they could no longer deny what we feared. Our people were not only taken... they were devoured. 

'I do not know what changed the mind of the creature, but it came to fear Avabárg and so it abandoned the islet. Yet its foul deeds are not forgotten to the stones of that old keep! The spirits of those who met their ends in Avabárg still linger... and they cannot rest.

'Please, ${PLAYER}, help them to find peace!''The creature does not age as Men do, ${PLAYER}. As many of my ancestors grew old and died, it only grew more gaunt and wicked.

'Avabárg remains a place of great sorrow, and I'm grateful you have put the spirits of my ancestors to rest.'

Atta appears overcome with emotion.

'May they never be forgotten!'Sharkey is said to reward those who find suitable treasure in the Gladden Fields, but it is certain that he punishes those who fail him.Stolen treasures can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen.

Tautila told you Sharkey's Men have been stealing and collecting odd objects to impress Sharkey. He has asked you to recover the stolen 'treasures'.Tautila can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen.

You have recovered a strange collection of items stolen by Sharkey's Men in the Gladden Fields. You should return to Tautila.'Wait... I must ask one more thing of you.

'I don't know what Sharkey wants with these old tunnels, but I have heard the others speak of relics and lost fortunes to be found in the marshland. Whatever they find out in the Gladden Fields, they bring down here for Sharkey. I don't know if they mean to impress him or not, but nothing they've stored here seems particularly valuable... or even useful.

'But if you gather up what they've stolen, they'll have nothing to show Sharkey and we can see that it stays that way.'Tautila looks over what you have found and a weak smile spreads across his face.

'It might not be much, but at least Sharkey will never have it.'The Shapag-hai looted many provisions in the final days of the War, and Hárskor fears they will not soon depart the Vales of Anduin unless their supplies are destroyed.Spoiled provisions can be found throughout Fil Sulmog.

