You should return it to its rightful place in the Crown Chamber.Return the stone to its pedestalThe vision shows you an oval stone on this pedestal. This fourth stone must be out there somewhere, waiting for you to find it. You swear you can hear faint whispers, bidding you to look closer at the illusion.You have found the key to this chamber's lock, but judging by the charred bones and blast marks, you should not attempt to use it right away. Below the lock, a rune-stone adorns the door, its carvings glowing an ominous red. If you are going to safely open the door, you will need to find some way to remove the rune-stone.'Hello, ${PLAYER}. What brings you all the way down here?'

You ask Márus if he knows anything about removing rune-stones set up as traps on doors and describe the state of the chamber you found.

'Oh ho, that's quite clever! You know, I have heard of some of our forefathers using rune-stones to protect their vaults from intruders. Aye, let me try to remember the specifics.'

He spends a few minutes mumbling to himself, lost in thought.

'Right! I remember now! I should be able to help you, but it will be tricky! To dismantle the trap, you will need a powerful rune-stone of your own to protect yourself from the searing flames. I can craft that for you with the right reagents, but, you will also need to track down the original chisel used to carve the rune-stone! Aye, the ancient dwarf-craft is not easily undone. Here, let me write this down for you. Good luck in your search. I fear a chisel that old may be gone forever!'

He quickly jots down a list on a piece of paper and hands it to you:

To Make Rune-stone:
- Powerful fire-enchanted chisel
- Copper and obsidian rune-stone base
- Polished dwarrowgleam

- Don't forget the original chisel!'Did you find the chisel?'

You show him the ancient chisel and hand over the rest of the items on his list. His eyes light up.

'By Durin's Beard! This truly is a chisel of the First Age! Just look at the craftsmanship! If nothing else, thank you for sharing this with me, ${PLAYER}. Ah, if only it were not so urgently needed. I will get started on your rune-stone now.'

He gets to work on the rune-stone. A short time later, it is complete.

'Here you are. This will protect you, and allow you to dismantle the rune-stone. Ah, to do that, all you need to do is hold the chisel directly in the middle of the stone, and hit it with something. A hammer, the base of a sword, anything heavy will do. It should be that simple!'A ghost seems to be terrorizing the children of Blómgard.According to Odulf, the ghost of Old Mad Ubb is somewhere in Blómgard.

You should search the barrels and crates to make Odulf feel better.The squirrel can be found in Blómgard.

You should pick up the squirrel.Pick up the squirrelOdulf can be found in Blómgard.

You should show the squirrel to Odulf.Show the squirrel to OdulfVulmar can be found in Blómgard.

You should <rgb=#00FF00>scold</rgb> Vulmar.<rgb=#00FF00>Scold</rgb> VulmarRadagast can be found in Laerlad.

You should bring the squirrel to Radagast.'Oh my, a ${CLASS}! That is what you are, is it not? My name is Odulf and I need your help! My brother Vulmar says there is a ghost in Blómgard. Not just any old ghost though, no! It is the ghost of Old Mad Ubb! I saw it, I saw it! Well, I saw a barrel or a crate move, I did! Please catch the ghost, ${CLASS}! Please, oh please, will you?''Oh, that Vulmar! I'd wager he caught that squirrel and put it in there to make me think Old Mad Ubb was on the loose! Vulmar is always trying to trick me!'

Odulf starts to cry, but then he wipes his eyes and the sniffles stop.

'Do you know something? I think I have seen that squirrel before. He is friends with that funny man in brown who lives around here. You should bring him the squirrel! He probably misses his friend. I know I would! I wouldn't miss Vulmar, though, not at all! Let him find new friends if he seeks to keep tricking the ones he already has! I think you should scold Vulmar first, and then find the man in brown!''Why, look who you found! What good fortune! I have been searching for this little one everywhere. Well, not everywhere, I suppose, for I found him not. Together, perhaps, we searched everywhere!

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I would say my friend here needs to be a little more careful. Indeed, I will say it! You should be more careful where you scamper off to, little one!''Why look who you found! I have been searching for this one everywhere. Thank you ${PLAYER}. My friend needs to be a little more careful, I would say.'While waiting for Grimbeorn's answer, Legolas recalls a recent story told to him by King Thranduil.Legolas can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to LegolasLegolas can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas at the Beorninghús'We have some time before Grimbeorn sends his reply, ${PLAYER}. While we wait, perhaps I can tell you a story of something that happened recently, but that you missed? You were kept busy with other events of some importance, as I am sure you will recall, but great deeds were performed here among the Vales of Anduin. My father Thranduil told me of his recent visit here, after the war, and I can speak of it to you, if you like.''Since we have some time, let me tell you the story that my father Thranduil told to me.''Grimbeorn is possessed of a gruff demeanour, but he cares much for the Vales of Anduin and the people who live there. If he sees that we care for them as well he may be more willing to reopen the trade route with Felegoth.'Battle is about to erupt outside of Vegbár. The Beornings can only hope the goblins will do enough damage that the small force of Beornings can overwhelm the survivors.The stage is set for a battle between the goblin forces.

