You should talk to Odahild.Talk to OdahildThe wounded Ungoladan warrior can be found in Blómgard.

You should talk to the Ungoladan and learn what you can.Talk to the wounded Ungoladan warriorRadagast can be found in Blómgard.

You should talk to Radagast.Talk to Radagast'There is something strange about these spiders, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot put my finger upon what it might be. They are hiding somewhere in Laerlad, I can tell you that, and I can tell you too that we have to help these people! You because you are an adventurer, and me because, well, I owe them that. Let us leave it at that, and speak no more of my faults for now. Oh, it is a worrisome thing to remember!'

Suddenly, you hear shouts from the eastern side of the village.

'They are on the attack again! You must defend the village. Go now, quickly and hastily and with great speed, ${PLAYER}!''You have done Blómgard a good service, for the village is defended and we are safe... for now, at least. You say that you have done this in the name of Radagast? Perhaps we will let you and Radagast stay here until this threat is no more.

'My guards have informed me that one of the injured spiders tried to escape, and he tracked the beast. Before it could disappear into the thick of the woods, it turned into some sort of... well, into some sort of man! We captured the wounded beast and have kept it under guard.'

You explain that this creature could be one of the Ungoledain, a group of skin-changers from Mirkwood who worship spiders and hold them to be sacred.

'If you know of these creatures, it seems to me that you are the one to speak with our captive.''Lóbruth cares not what some ${RACE} wants. He listens only to Mengris, our Tásakh, and will follow her to death or end of world. Voice in shadows, it tells her where to go. Woodmen are in the way, says Tásakh. Pah! It matters little to Lóbruth. If Mengris says slay you all, then you must die!''The Ungoledain, yes, that would explain a great deal... a great deal indeed! It seems I owe the Woodmen for not one failing but for two! Firstly, I abandoned Rhosgobel, leaving the Woodmen to face the harsh blades of war on their own. I had my reasons, of course I did, but looking back on it I question if they were worthwhile enough to leave the Woodmen so unprotected.

'And secondly, well, now they face an enemy of my own creation! Yes, ${PLAYER}, you did not mishear me. I am responsible, in part, for the creation of the Ungoledain. I made them, and though it was not on purpose, I should have known better! Looking back, it could have been so easily avoided!'Varthmath wishes to explore the ruins of Kidzul-kâlah and learn more about the strange shadows stalking the Gladdenmere.The dwarf mine of Kidzul-kâlah can be found along the southern edge of the Gladdenmere.

You should investigate the old ruins for Varthmath.Explore the mine entrance of Kidzul-kâlahExplore the lower aqueducts of Kidzul-kâlahExplore the upper aqueducts of Kidzul-kâlahExplore the water-house courtyard of Kidzul-kâlahExplore the water-house overlook of Kidzul-kâlahExplore the mountain pass in the GladdenmereExplore the insides of Kidzul-kâlah's ruinsComplete 'Shade Over Kidzul-kâlah'Complete 'The Chambers of Kidzul-kâlah'Varthmath can be found at the old dock in the south-east side of the Gladdenmere.

You should talk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere.Talk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere'It is kind of the Elves to assist us in learning more about the troubles that plague the Gladdenmere. I have conversed with our new companions and they agree we should investigate the ruins of Kidzul-kâlah. We will explore and observe the old dwarf mine, and return in safety. Do you agree?''What have you to report, ${PLAYER}? I see, this is all very strange. The waters flow with curious currents, and the dead keep close to those waters? I have not encountered anything like that before! Kidzul-kâlah was once part of Moria, yes? I believe it, for walking in that place caused me no end of unease, and so it is here! The bridge was destroyed recently, you say? Hmm.

'We will need to stay here longer if we are to learn more. Perhaps the Elves will lend us a boat with which we can cross the Gladdenmere.'Deep under Járnfast, chief fortress of the Iron Hills, is a place where the red stone once cracked, revealing a horrible abyss beneath the Dwarf-halls.Náin can be found at the entrance to the Howling Pit in Járnfast.

