You should talk to Skalla.Talk to Skalla'I am not sure I have ever seen Skalla so concerned. There must be something we can do....'

Langhár trails off, lost in thought. A wry smile suddenly crosses her face.

'I have a crazy idea, ${PLAYER}, but it might just work. So, we have two goblin hosts to deal with, not enough Beornings to deal with either, and in the middle of it all the hobgoblins and the Great Goblin plan to fight it out? If their forces are closely matched, they might just kill each other off, and all we would have to do is mop up the survivors!

'Based on what you saw in Waldfast, I think the Great Goblin is at a disadvantage in numbers. Perhaps we should even the odds?

'I have some ideas for what we can do to pull this off. While you are dealing with things in Goblin-town, I am going to visit some good friends and see if I can get their help. Ask Skalla if he can help get you inside.''Yes, I can get you inside. Let me know when you are ready.''Good to see you in one piece, ${PLAYER}. How fared your mission into Goblin-town?'

You tell Skalla that you believe you were able to even the odds between the hobgoblins and the Great Goblin. You also saw the hobgoblin warlord, Shárnakh, while you were inside.

'Shárnakh. At least we have a name for our enemy now. If you were successful, and it sounds like you were, the Great Goblin will want to press his advantage while he has it, before more forces from Gundabad arrive.

'Langhár has not yet returned, and was rather mysterious about where she was going. I hope you are ready to face the goblins without her.''Yes, I can get you inside. Let me know when you are ready.''So, you wish to enter Goblin-town. I overheard your plans. This seems incredibly risky, but I will not stop you. It may be our only path to success.

'I have a scout stationed near the Goblin-gate. She will be able to get you near to where the hobgoblins have holed themselves up. Find her.'Varthmath wishes to explore the wilds of the Gladdenmere and learn what lurks in this formerly-inaccessible valley.The wilds of the Gladdenmere rest on the northern edge of the River Gladden.

You should explore the wilds of Gladdenmere for Varthmath.Explore the worm-hold of Kidzul-kâlahExplore the stone-giant fortExplore Gladdenmere isleComplete 'Trophies of the Mountain'Complete 'Trophies of Stone'Complete 'Giants of the Gladdenmere'Complete 'Beasts of the Mountain'Complete 'Unfortunate Orcs'Varthmath can be found in the Gladdenmere.

You should talk to Varthmath.Talk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere'Look upon the hills across the Gladdenmere. I swear to you: I saw them move! Do you suppose it was the stone-giants who dwell there? Could it be they blocked the path to the Gladdenmere? Perhaps it was an errant rock-toss that cleared the path they once impeded! We should investigate the other side of the Gladdenmere and learn more. I have no quarrels with stone-giants but they are not known to be friendly. The Elves have provided a boat when you are ready to cross the water.''Then I was right when I guessed the stone-giant presence on the far side of the Gladdenmere! It appears the spirits of the dead intruded upon the domain of the stone-giants, and in turn the giants destroyed the bridge in order to keep them away. No wonder the stone-giants that you encountered were so frenzied! I shall return to Grimbeorn at once and relay to him what we learned here. Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}.'Grimbeorn looks to the skies for assistance in the Vales of Anduin.Grimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands.

You should talk to Grimbeorn.Talk to GrimbeornThe Carrock can be found on the western edge of the Beorning-lands in the Vales of Anduin.

You should seek out Varthmath atop the Carrock.Travel to the CarrockThe Carrock can be found on the western edge of the Beorning-lands in the Vales of Anduin.

You should seek out Varthmath atop the Carrock.Talk to Varthmath atop the CarrockAnórohir is on the Carrock.

You should be polite to Anórohir.Cordially <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> to AnórohirAnórohir can be found atop the Carrock.

You should travel to the Eyrie with Anórohir.Travel to the Eyrie with AnórohirGwaihir the Wind-lord can be found at the Eyrie.

You should be polite to Gwaihir.Cordially <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> to GwaihirGwaihir the Wind-lord can be found at the Eyrie.

You should talk to Gwaihir.Talk to Gwaihir the Windlord'Ah, I believe Grimbeorn awaits us with his reply. Speak to the lord of the Beornings and learn what he has to say. Let us hope it will be good tidings for my father and for the Elves of Felegoth.''${PLAYER}, there you are. I have requested a summons. Anórohir has agreed to take only one of us up to the Eyrie. I think it should be you, for you are a friend of Gandalf, and that may help the Great Eagles decide to side with us!

'I would recommend that you speak with courtesy to the Eagles. Consider a proper bow at the outset, and be sure to make use of as fine speech as you are able!''Our paths cross once again, ${RACE}. I saw you once in the Garden of Galadriel, and now you fly high above your station to the very Eyrie of my people. It is most curious to me that you keep turning up, small one.''I have made my decision. The Elves say they will help us, but only rarely do I see them leave the shelter of the woods, and I hesitate to call on them for aid. The dwarves and Men that live in the north have their own problems, as do we, and neither can be a help to the other while his own lands remain unsecured!

'I have not spent this time idly, ${PLAYER}. No, there is a solution, and it lies on the very edge of my land. On the edge... and upwards! I speak of the Great Eagles' Eyrie. Those noble birds have aided my people before, and they may do so again.

'You are a friend of Gandalf the Wizard, and he is one who has the respect of the Eagles. Speak to Gwaihir the Wind-lord on behalf of my people and request their aid. I will send Varthmath ahead to call upon the Eagles for a meeting.'Many useful plants grow along the river Anduin. Ingelfled has asked you to gather some to help the village of Arhaim.Anduin moss and river reeds can be gathered from the river-banks of the Anduin in Duskenvale.

You should collect Anduin moss and river reeds.Collect Anduin moss (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect river reeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ingelfled can be found in the village of Arhaim in Duskenvale.

You should deliver the moss and reeds to Ingelfled.Talk to Ingelfled'Hello there. Have you come to help the village? I have a task for you, if you are willing.

'Much of the nearby flora is valuable to us, in one way or another. I am low on two items in particular: reeds and moss from the nearby river-bank. The reeds can be dried and woven into baskets and mats. The moss can be soaked in medicine and applied to wounds. If you could gather some of both, I would be very appreciative! You can get to the river quickly by taking the path east through the hills. Perhaps the fishermen at the docks could also use your help.'Ingelfled carefully inspects the reeds and moss clumps you gathered.

'These will do nicely, thank you ${PLAYER}. Since you did so well on this task, I have another for you! This one involves my portly friend here.'

She pats the pig sitting next to her.The stones must be returned to their rightful places in the Crown Chamber.An illusion has appeared before you in the Crown Chamber.

You should inspect the illusion of the second stone.Inspect the illusion of the second stoneThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.Find the second stoneThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.Find the second stoneYou have found a hidden chamber in the Mountains of Shadow, but a Nameless entity stands in your way.Talk to the EmissaryThe Emissary has asked you to find the "Remnants of the Fallen Ones" and return them.Find the first remnantFind the second remnantFind the third remnantFind the fourth remnantFind the fifth remnantFind the sixth remnantFind the seventh remnantYou have collected the remnants for the Emissary.

You should return to the Emissary and 'Speak the Words'.Talk to the Emissary and 'Speak the Words'You have found one of the missing stones!

You should return them to their rightful place in the Crown Chamber.Return the stone to its pedestalThe vision shows you a pear-shaped stone on this pedestal. This second stone must be out there somewhere, waiting for you to find it. You swear you can hear faint whispers, bidding you to look closer at the illusion.The Nameless being towers over you, but shows no hostility. As it turns its gaze towards you, you feel the hairs on the back of your neck stand on end. It slowly moves its hand in your direction, as if waiting for you to hand something to it. A booming voice fills your mind.

'Bring me the remnants. Remnants from the fallen ones. Prove your worth.'

It continues to hold out its hand to you.You place the remnants in the Emissary's still open hand. They absorb into its flesh and disappear. You once again hear the booming voice inside your head.

'Now, you must speak the words.'

The Emissary senses your confusion and emits a low rumbling sound that you think might be laughter.

'You cannot understand the whispers. Your mind is closed. Seek the Mighty Ones, and speak the words when you are ready.'The time has come to see what lies inside Shathur-munzu. Whatever awaits, your goal is to clear it of danger for Lady Arwen's arrival.The time has come to enter Shathur-munzu.

You should complete 'Instance: The Shadow Hunter.'Complete 'Instance: The Shadow Hunter'Completed.CompletedBaradal is somewhere inside Shathur-munzu. She may be in danger.

You should find Baradal.Find BaradalBaradal is locked inside a cage in Shathur-munzu, injured and in danger.

You should attempt to break open her cage.Attempt to break the lockCompleted.CompletedSomewhere inside Shathur-munzu, an Orc holds the key to Baradal's cage.

You should find and defeat the Orc jailor.Defeat the Orc jailorAcquire the crude iron keyNow that you have the key, you should return to Baradal's cage and try to open it.Open the strong lockBaradal has been freed from her cage.

You should talk to Baradal.Talk to Baradal'This must be Shathur-munzu. We know not what lies inside, but it is my charge to clear it of anyone or anything that would bring harm to Lady Arwen. When you are ready, we will enter.''Wait, do you hear that?'You find yourself in a den of wargs and Orc-kind. Baradal is nowhere to be seen, and it is very likely she is in grave danger.

You should make your way through Shathur-munzu and find her before it is too late. Be wary; Ránulur the warg chieftain, or the 'Shadow-hunter', as he is known to the locals, may still be near.Baradal is barely conscious. She stirs as you approach.

'${PLAYER}...? Where am I?'

She is still dazed from the warg attack. You should find a way to get her out of this cage before Ránulur returns.It seems this lock is too sturdy to be opened by force. You will need to find the key. It is probably being carried by an Orc or goblin somewhere inside Shathur-munzu.'${PLAYER}, I think I am recovering my senses. What has happened?'By your hand, a terrible Nameless entity has been released. By your hand, he must fall.The Shadowed King must be found and defeated, but first, you must find Frethi.

You should return to the Crown Chamber in the Foundations of Stone.Return to the Crown ChamberFrethi has left you a note in the Crown Chamber.

