You should find the Shadowed Cave in the Foundations of Stone.Find Frethi near the Shadowed CaveThe Shadowed King awaits within the Shadowed Cave.

You should complete Askâd-mazal, the Chamber of Shadows, on any difficulty.Complete Askâd-mazal, the Chamber of ShadowsThe Shadowed King has been vanquished!

You should return to King Thorin and inform him of your victory.Talk to King Thorin'${PLAYER}, I charge you with defeating that... fiend! The Shadowed King must not be allowed to live! Since it was by your hand he was released, it is only fitting that it be by your hand that he fall!

'Return to Moria at once, find Frethi, and track down the Shadowed King. We cannot allow him to release Throkhâr his master!'There is a note here with your name on it. It reads:

${PLAYER}, I am fine! My injuries were not severe. I went looking for the Shadowed King. I believe he has entered the Shadowed Cave! It is open! Meet me there as soon as you can!

Frethi'There you are! This is the Shadowed Cave. It has been sealed for as long as anyone can remember, as far back as our records, and farther! I have never seen it like this! It cannot be a coincidence that this would open just as the Shadowed King is let loose! He must be inside! Quickly, let us go after him!'You tell King Thorin of your victory over the Shadowed King, and he smiles with pride and relief.

'Thank you for your bravery, hero. You have undoubtedly saved us from a terrible fate. This incident has proven yet again that we must be ever watchful, for there are still terrible evils lurking in the depths, and secrets yet to be uncovered. We at least know the name of one now: Throkhâr. May the day never come that I must send you to defeat THAT monster.'Wargs from the north hide in the far reaches of the Beorning-lands.Ylgraf can be found on the northern edge of the Beorning-lands.

You should defeat wargs and burn animal carcasses found at Ylgraf.Enter YlgrafYlgraf can be found on the northern edge of the Beorning-lands.

You should defeat wargs and burn animal carcasses found at Ylgraf.Defeat wargs at Ylgraf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burn animal carcasses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated wargs and burned animal carcasses.CompletedWargs from the north have made a hiding-place among the rocks at Ylgraf in the Beorning-lands. These beasts from Gundabad will be a danger to the peaceful folk of the vales and should be dealt with immediately.You defeated many wargs at Ylgraf and destroyed their food, sending the creatures of Gundabad a message that they are unwelcome among the Vales of Anduin. The folk of the Beorning-lands are safer now for your efforts here.When Atta was a boy, the creature known as the Snatcher returned to the Vales of Anduin and once again sought to prey on the weak and helpless.Atta can be found in Hultvís.

