You should talk to Grimbeorn.'The darkness has spread across the mountains into formerly peaceful valleys, and these lands of mine are no exception. Orcs and wargs spy on my people from among the trees. Goblins creep from their holes in greater numbers than ever before. Even the beasts of the wood are angered... not just by strangers, but by me, once their trusted friend and companion!

'Speak to my kin in the vales, and every one of my people will confirm I speak the truth, and that it needs addressing! Once you have spoken to them, journey north to the edge of the Floodfells and find signs of the danger that creeps ever nearer to my home.''Look around you, and tell me what you see. You see peace, and you see safety! It is not easily won, and even less-easily kept! My husband, Grimbeorn, fought many battles to make it so, and he has shown no sign of stopping any day soon. Let the darkness beware!

'I am Gírta, matron of the Beorninghús. My husband and our kin will fight to protect this way of life from each danger that threatens. If you search for such dangers, you will find them nearby.''Greetings again, ${PLAYER}. I waited at the Forest Gate until the Elves finally allowed me to pass through, a process that took much longer than I liked! I did not wish to anger my sire, so I did not complain very much to the Elves about their obvious reluctance to open the way.

'I have not left the Beorninghús since I returned. Langhár's stories about the Wolf-denes have filled me up with caution, and I do not plan to venture past the vineyard.''I am called Varthmath. I have recently come home after travelling in the Misty Mountains, where my people once lived. Alas for the dwarves and the Orcs, for their wars drove us out and now it is no longer safe to return. A pox on the cursed halls of Moria! So many evils have come out of the darkness of that place that now the mountains are lost to us. I do not know if it will ever be safe to return there.''I was shown kindness by the Elves of Felegoth, as I would not have expected. I told Grimbeorn my story of the foes that ambushed me, and of the evil that lurks within the Elf-woods. They say they have cleansed the forest, but I hold that no Beorning should take the risk. It is still "Mirkwood" to me.''These trophies are certainly respectable, though they were not in life! Ha!

'They show what I expected them to show: that although the war may be done, its soldiers remain a threat to the Vales of Anduin. The trade route must remain closed, for the safety of my people.'The Beornings of Vegbár must keep constant watch on both the High Pass and Goblin-town, and can do neither with their buildings and walls in disrepair.Skalla has asked you to gather fallen timber to repair the buildings in Vegbár.

You should collect fallen timber from the area surrounding Vegbár.Collect fallen timber (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Skalla can be found in Vegbár, the Beorning outpost in the Wolf-denes.

You should talk to Skalla.Talk to Skalla'While you are out there talking to the others, would you do us a favour? We need timber for repairs to our buildings and walls. The goblins could attack at any time, and we must be ready for it. Find timber from fallen trees nearby and bring it to me.''These will do. I have another task, if you still wish to help.'Langhár has been sent to the Wolf-denes to help deal with the goblins there. Sterkist believes she would be happy to accept your help in the matter.Vegbár, the Beorning outpost in the Wolf-denes, can be found south-west of the Beorninghús.

You should travel to Vegbár to find Langhár.Travel to VegbárLanghár can be found somewhere in Vegbár.

You should talk to Langhár.Talk to Langhár'${PLAYER}! Good to see you again! How go the adventures?'

You tell Sterkist about all of your travels since the last time you saw him.

'Oh my, that all sounds rather harrowing! I think my adventuring days are behind me, friend. One near-death experience is plenty! Grimbeorn keeps me busy enough around here as it is. He is never especially pleased to have guests! I, on the other hand, am happy to meet new friends from far-away lands.'

He chuckles to himself, and then suddenly remembers something.

'Oh! Langhár will want to see you again since you are here! She was sent to the Wolf-denes to help deal with the goblin problem. You should go see her if you have time!''${PLAYER}! Good to see you again, friend! What brings you to Vegbár? Not here to pay the toll are you? Ha ha!'

You tell her that Sterkist sent you, and mentioned something about goblin problems.

'Oh, Sterkist, always worried about his sister! Indeed, there are often goblin problems this close to Goblin-town. This time, however, they are not of the usual sort. This time they may be worse.'After discovering a number of dredging machines left in disrepair, Sharkey's Men have hastened their search of the Gladden Fields for lost treasure.Relic-hunting tools and dredging machine mechanisms can be found at Sharkey's Slough in the centre of the Gladden Fields.

You have discovered that Sharkey's Men have been using a variety of tools in addition to Saruman's old dredging machines to search for lost relics in the Gladden Fields.Destroy relic-hunting tools at Sharkey's Slough (0/10)Relic-hunting tools and dredging machine mechanisms can be found at Sharkey's Slough in the centre of the Gladden Fields.

