Tautila has asked you to find and, if necessary, defeat his traitorous kinsfolk who have joined Sharkey's Men.Tautila can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen.

You have found or defeated all of the traitorous Woodmen in service to Sharkey. You should return to Tautila.Talk to Tautila in the warrens of Tûn Melen'Listen to me....'

The imprisoned Woodman gestures for you to approach and begins to whisper.

'My name is Tautila. I was raised in Hultvís, but it has been many years since I last dwelt there. You see, I am a travelling merchant and something of a scholar among my people... or at least I was until those demons and ruffians ambushed me on the road!

'When they brought me to Sharkey's encampment, I understood why I was taken. I learned then that a few of my kinsmen had willingly joined Sharkey, and they knew I was well-learned in the tales of the hól-budlan. Sharkey told me to guide him to the old tunnels or he would slay me where I stood. I did as I was told. What choice did I have?

'But the others... they had a choice! They have abandoned the old ways for greed, and they will never again be welcome among the Woodmen. Not if I have any say in it!

'When I was taken, I saw five of them. Find them and defeat them before they can sway more of my people into the service of Sharkey!''Tautila ought to keep his mouth shut. I told Sharkey we should've killed him!

'As for you, well... Sharkey wouldn't be too happy if he found out folks were poking their noses about in the warrens.''Do not speak to me as if you know my troubles... Sharkey looks after us better than that old fool Ríkmar ever did.

'And he'll pay a fine price for your head, too!''Sharkey told us that the swamp held treasures each worth more than a kingdom, but we have toiled for weeks and found nothing.

'Ah, but that weapon of yours looks worth a fair share of gold. Give it to me!''I had hoped some of them might realize their folly, but I had no such hope for Hathus.

'Like many of my kinsmen, he lost a great deal in the war, but he couldn't resist the chance to change his fortunes. We were all desperate, but to have fallen so low as to side with Sharkey? Unthinkable!

'Sharkey is no more than a demon in the skin of a Man. I only wish the others had seen that!'Discover ancient dwarf treasure caches in Ered Mithrin.Discover ancient dwarf treasure caches in Ered Mithrin.Discover ancient dwarf treasure caches in Ered MithrinDiscover the many dwarf mining caches in the Ironfold.Discover the many dwarf mining caches in the Ironfold.Discover the many dwarf mining caches in the IronfoldDiscover the many hidden caches in the Vales of Anduin.Discover the many hidden caches in the Vales of Anduin.Discover the many hidden caches in the Vales of AnduinAlthough his rule of Moria came to a well-deserved end, the cruel banners of Mazog are now flown by the Shapag-hai in the Gladden Fields.Banners of vengeance can be found at Lúlstrok in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields.

You have discovered the cruel banners of Mazog being flown by the Shapag-hai. You should burn them.Burn banners of vengeance at Lúlstrok (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have burned many of the cruel banners flown in Mazog's name by the Shapag-hai.CompletedAs you press deeper into Lúlstrok, you notice that the banners flown by the Shapag-hai bear a striking resemblance to those once flown by Mazog and his Pûlpum in Moria. If the legacies of Mazog and his cruel forebears, Bolg and Azog, are ever to be ended, the banners of the Shapag-hai must be burned.Although it cannot avenge the hurts done to the dwarves by the Orcs of Moria, you have done well to burn the cruel banners flown in Mazog's name by the Shapag-hai.Sterkist has been tasked with collecting mushrooms, only to realize that the mushrooms he seeks might lead him a little further astray than he would like.Mushrooms can be found north of the Beorninghús.

