You should bring the medallions to Varthmath.Many of the stone-giants that walk the Gladdenmere wear medallions of polished stone. These crafted discs would be greatly prized by Grimbeorn or the other Wilderfolk of the Vales of Anduin. You should collect some of these medallions from any stone-giants you defeat.'Ah, fine trophies, indeed! Grimbeorn and the Wilderfolk will be proud to bear these medallions. Our work in the Gladdenmere grows closer to its end. You have done well!'Concerned that the defences of Hultvís are still weakened, Ríkmar hopes to learn why shipments of lumber from the small forester's village of Tríubad have stalled.Tríubad can be found by travelling eastward from Hultvís and following the footpath into the hills of Woodsedge.

Ríkmar has asked you to find missing woodsmen and learn what has been slowing their efforts to rebuild Hultvís. Ríkmar believes the missing woodsmen can likely be found somewhere near Tríubad.Find the missing woodsmen and learn what happened at TríubadClothar can be found along the footpath to the south-east of Hultvís.

You have discovered two of the woodsmen of Hultvís and their damaged cart along the road to Tríubad. You should ask them what has happened.Talk to ClotharSeasoned lumber and tanned hides can be found at Tríubad.

Clothar and Vilibald have asked for your help in recovering the resources they were forced to leave behind when they fled Tríubad.Collect seasoned lumber (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect tanned hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Clothar's axe can be found somewhere near the pond at Tríubad.

Clothar claims that his axe was stolen by an angry tree-demon and has begged you to retrieve it.Find Clothar's axe and defeat the tree-demon of TríubadClothar can be found along the road to Tríubad.

You have recovered the lumber and hides Clothar and his kinsmen were forced to abandon at Tríubad, and you have also recovered Clothar's family axe. You should return to Clothar.Ríkmar can be found in Hultvís.

You have aided the woodsmen of Tríubad in repelling the Taurogrim and recovering their lost resources. You should return to Ríkmar with these good tidings.Talk to Ríkmar'If that were only the end of our troubles!

'A few of my people dwell in a village in the hills called Tríubad. All who dwell there are woodsmen, and here in the Narrows, such a skill is very valuable. I tasked my people in Tríubad to deliver a supply of lumber and hides to Hultvís with great haste. It is urgent that our fences be repaired and our roofs mended, but I have heard naught from the people of Tríubad in days.

'If some trouble has come to Tríubad, my people there may be in dire need. I would ask that you follow the road to Tríubad and learn what has happened!''I do not know you, traveller, but you would be wise to turn back. The Thyrsir... they have returned!'

You note Clothar's concern, and you then ask about the nature of the Thyrsir.

'They were wood-demons of legend, or so I thought! It is said the Elves long ago drove them from the forest, but how have they now come to be here in the vales? A shadow must still dwell in the forest! My cousin, Vilibald, and I only narrowly escaped the Thyrsir at Tríubad, but now... we have few hides and even less lumber left to bring to the chieftain.'

Clothar pauses and lets out a deep sigh.

'A great tree-demon followed in the wake of the Thyrsir, and though I tried to hew it, it wandered away with my axe still embedded in its trunk! That is the axe of my father and of my father's father, and now I have failed them and it is kept by a demon!

'But... if you do not fear the Thyrsir as we do, perhaps you could reclaim what was lost at Tríubad! Would you do this for me?''You've really done it, haven't you? You even got my father's axe back from that rotten tree-demon!'

Clothar looks in disbelief at the lumber and hides you place onto the cart. You approach Clothar and hand his axe back to him.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, and don't you worry about us! Vilibald and I can bear it the rest of the way.

'Tell the chieftain that we'll be back to Hultvís in no time!''What was keeping the woodsmen of Tríubad, ${PLAYER}? Did they meet with some trouble?'

You tell Ríkmar of the Thyrsir, known to you and the Elves of Eryn Lasgalen as the Taurogrim, and of the misadventure that befell the woodsmen before you aided them. You explain that Clothar and Vilibald will soon deliver a number of hides and planks of lumber to Hultvís.

'While I am concerned that the wood-demons have returned to the forest, I'm pleased that Hultvís will soon be better defended. When Clothar and Vilibald return, I will set my people to the task of repairing the fences and other damage the Orcs caused during the war.

'You are a brave ${CLASS}, and we are fortunate to have you here with us in Hultvís... if only for a time.'Orcs from the Gladden Fields ventured too far up the River Gladden and into the hands of giants.Orc corpses can be found in the northern reaches of the Gladdenmere.

You should search Orc corpses for relics.Search Orc corpses in the Gladdenmere (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect excavated relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Varthmath can be found in the Gladdenmere.

You should bring the excavated relics to Varthmath.These Orcs must have worked the dredging machines of the Gladden Fields until curiosity or greed led them to stray from their tasks and up the River Gladden, towards the halls of Kidzul-kâlah. It would seem they encountered stone-giants along the way and met an early end. Some of these Orcs might still hold relics they took from the Gladden, which you could now recover.'You found these on the corpses of Orcs? It would seem the giants of the Misty Mountains have done some good for once! How odd to think that such an out-of-the-way place, no more than wilderness, really, might become home to so many ancient artifacts!

'I do not know what is important and what is not. How could I? But perhaps I will take these relics to the Elves. They are sure to know what to do with them.'Mirkwood spiders still lurk in the recesses of Laerlad, threatening all those who dwell in the Vales of Anduin.Spiders can be found in the woods of Laerlad.

