You should speak with the recruit.Speak to the new recruitTake the new recruit with you as you assist those in Díngarth.Assist Gelvira at DíngarthAssist Radigond at DíngarthAssist Hildvar at DíngarthUse the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separatedTake the new recruit with you as you assist those in Echad-in-Edhil.Assist Durin IV at Echad-in-Edhil with: Heraldry of Durin IVAssist Durin IV at Echad-in-Edhil with: Sauron's Presence Upon Parth DaenathDefeat foes in Parth Daenath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separatedTake the new recruit with you as you assist those in Adambel.Assist Huneric at Adambel with: Heraldry of The ThíudaAssist Huneric at Adambel with: Turning DefectorsDefeat foes in Arandor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separatedDefeat enemies in Emyn Duir.Defeat foes in Emyn Duir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separatedSpeak to the new recruit.Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separatedAfter so many years besieging Mordor, the Great Alliance is still in need of new recruits. Upon entering Díngarth you receive a missive: you have been entrusted with a new soldier in hopes that you can mentor and train the young man. You should seek him out as soon as you are able.'Are you the one sent to train me? I look forward to learning all that you know! I was but a child when the war began, but now I am a man grown. Is it true that an Easterling horde is on its way?

'Oh, I almost forgot, I have a note for you. I have been waiting here so... I may have already read it. I hope you do not mind! It says that many great warriors have joined the battle and we should assist them. I am ready to leave, whenever you are ready!''Thank you, my friend. I have learned much in the time that we have spent together. I am now to report to Hildvar to continue my combat training. I am sure that we will soon fight side-by-side, and let our foes beware!'Huneric, Lord of the Thíuda, has noticed forces gathering at Mokh Darga and wishes to halt the imminent raid before it can form.Soldiers can be found sleeping in their tents in Adambel.

