You should talk to Hildvar.Talk to Hildvar'Have you come to train? Good, I could use someone like you: someone who has seen battle recently! The men who survived the fighting against the Ghâzab Bôron are too exhausted from the pitched retreat to even stand, and most of the soldiers we found here at Díngarth are unfit to take to the battlefield! If they cannot fight in a skirmish upon the Corpse-fields, how can they hope to survive the coming of the Storm of Wrath?

'Spar with these soldiers and teach them the techniques that have allowed you to survive upon the battlefield. I will watch and give you some recommendations after you have finished sparring. After all, I have seen battle with Huneric, Lord of the Thíuda, and I have picked up some of his techniques!''I am ready to spar, my friend!''I have killed ten Orcs! How many have you bested?''I am happy to spar with you, friend!''You handled yourself well against eight of the soldiers under my command. It is important to anticipate your enemies' actions before they happen; otherwise you will always be reacting, and not setting the pace of the combat. When you know your enemy well, you can counter their blow before they even make the attack!

'These are the words of my father, and I have seen the truth in them for myself. Heed them well and you will never know defeat!''Go easy on me. I just recovered from an injury.''I am in need of the practice. I hope to learn much under the command of Hildvar.''I would rather rest than spar, but Hildvar is looking this way! I suppose we should begin.''I have not seen combat in quite some time. Prepare yourself!''Let me see your skills. I am a quick learner!'Huneric, Lord of the Thíuda, has spied Easterling defectors roaming the Corpse-fields of Parth Daenath.Easterling defectors can be found in Parth Daenath.

You should attempt to convince the Easterling defectors to turn on the Enemy.Huneric can be found at Adambel.

You should talk to Huneric.Talk to Huneric'The Ghâzab Bôron is nearly here. I saw that horde with my own eyes, and I know the terror it will inflict upon our fighting men when it arrives. Rumour of its approach has already spread throughout the camps of this Alliance, and I fear word has also passed to the encampments of our foes.

'Some Easterlings have departed their own camps. Do they desire to join the Storm of Wrath? Find them on the Corpse-fields and confront these Easterlings! Perhaps they can be made to turn back, and mayhap take up arms against their former allies.''You convinced a number of Easterlings to assist us? That is far better than the alternative, for otherwise their numbers might swell the ranks of the Ghâzab Bôron! The Enemy will not know who is friend and who is foe. Can it be that the greatest weapon might prove to be the sword of uncertainty? Still, I must say... a good, sharp blade can be useful as well!'Many evil Men gather at the encampment of Urshúlagar, prepared to do the bidding of Sauron.Urshúlagar can be found in Emyn Duir.

