'What sort of spirit could hate us so much that it seeks to corrupt the very waters we need to rely upon for life and health? The very worst kind: darkwaters! These hateful shades have descended upon the rivers of Imlad Morgul, and they stir a deadly malaise into the waters, making them quite unfit to drink.

'Take the time to slay darkwaters along the river, and I will reward you for helping clean the waters.'At the suggestion of a bounty posted in Rath Dúath, you defeated darkwaters along the river. The poster of the bounty believed this would help to cleanse the waters, making them safe to drink, but you believe the corruption lies deeper. Whatever role the darkwaters played in tainting the river, theirs was not the only source of the foulness that grips it.A bounty notice asks you to hunt down prominent Orcs in Rath Dúath.Strong Orcs can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should defeat Morgul Captains and warg-masters.Defeat Morgul Captains in Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Morgul warg-masters in Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated strong Orcs.CompletedThe bounty notice reads:

'We need someone to do something about the Orcs. Not just the rank-and-file warriors, though. We need you to defeat the leaders, the intelligent Orcs that give out the orders to all the rest. Those are the ones that have the potential to cause us the most grief.

'There's a reward in it for you if you can slay some of the higher-ranking Orcs: Morgul Captains and warg-masters.'You defeated some of the stronger, more high-ranking Orcs in Rath Dúath. The disarray should prove useful to those who find themselves tasked with cleansing evil from the valley.A bounty notice asks you to hunt down Skrithras and his pack of dire-horns terrorizing Rath Dúath.Dire-horns can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should find and defeat Skrithras, along with other dire-horn goats.Defeat dire-horns in Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat SkrithrasDefeated dire-horns.CompletedThe bounty notice reads:

'You want to fight Orcs? You want to fight wargs? These are worthy foes, but they are not the worst of the threats in Rath Dúath. Read on, if you dare!

'We need someone to do something about the goats. These are not ordinary goats. These are dire-horns! They do not customarily attack travellers, but lately a powerful beast seems to have organized the things into an aggressive fighting force. Perhaps he learned it from the wargs? Hunt down these dire-horns and their pack-leader and make Rath Dúath a place where we need not fear even the goats!

'There will be a reward in it for you, of course, as well as the personal satisfaction that you are not afraid of goats.'You defeated the dire-horn herd and their leader Skrithras, ensuring that the Rath Dúath will be a little safer for the people who must journey there.

The identity of the bounty-poster remains secret, but you suspect he must have been a farmer, someone who raised livestock before becoming tasked with the mission of cleansing Imlad Morgul. His notice seemed to indicate that he was personally insulted that Skrithas had turned the goats into creatures of evil. Whoever he may have been, your work here must have eased his heart.A bounty notice asks you to hunt wargs across Rath Dúath.Warg packs can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should defeat pack leaders and pack wargs.Defeat pack leaders in Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat pack wargs in Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated warg packs.CompletedThe bounty notice reads:

'Where once there was a single large warg pack prowling the forests near Rath Dúath, something has changed, and several wargs have broken off to lead their own, smaller packs. These are unafraid to challenge folk on the road, and they can cover a greater distance than before.

'Hunt these packs and teach them we will not run from them. We will fight!'You reminded the warg packs that threaten folk travelling through Rath Dúath that theirs is not the only strength in the valley.After the defeat of Sauron, Isildur faced a number of challenges during the two years preceding his death on the Gladden Fields and the loss of the One Ring.The shade of Isildur is on Tol Send.Talk to the shade of Isildur on Tol SendGandalf is on Tol Send, deep in thought.Talk to Gandalf on Tol SendGrimbeorn is at the Beorninghús.

Gandalf thinks you should return to the Beorninghús and speak with Grimbeorn.Talk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús'Sauron was defeated, but at great cost. Elves and Men wept for their lost kings, for the like of Gil-galad and Elendil would never come again. But there was joy too, for the war was ended and none could see the sorrows of the Age to come. The Ring should have been destroyed on that day, but it was not. Isildur took the Ring as payment for the death of his father and the travails of his people, an heirloom of his house and a record of their triumph over evil.

'The several kindreds that composed the Alliance returned to their homelands, nursing their grief and holding dear the memory of their triumph. We believed Sauron was gone forever, and it was not so.''In the chamber I see a white stone, and a rotating beacon. But what does this vision signify?''Yes, my friend, I know what chamber Isildur describes. Many pieces fall now into place for me, for as Lendelen I knew many things and saw much. It is as if a room that was sealed to me has been flung open, and while the pain is unwelcome the knowledge is not. I deem it a worthy trade, though Glorfindel regrets the necessity.

'This I believe, ${PLAYER}. It was known to Sauron's servants that Isildur perished in the Gladden Fields. They scoured the swamplands hereabout in search of the Ring, but they found it not. In time, his bones were recovered and borne away to places of great evil, perhaps to the very Houses of Lamentation it is said lie hidden somewhere within Mordor. What unholy rites were performed with his remains? I hazard no guess, but in time perhaps even the servants of Sauron tired of this villainy, and his bones were brought to some chamber where they, in time, were forgotten.

'The white stone Isildur describes must be the Vandassar of Dúath, which stood in Minas Ithil until the forces of Sauron captured that city during the Second Age. It was moved to Barad-dûr at the direction of the Witch-king, hauled on a great waggon pulled by hill-trolls into Gorgoroth. It was in the Dark Tower that the Bright Company broke the spells upon it. After the war, when the Alliance razed Barad-dûr to its foundation, the Vandassar must have been returned to Minas Ithil. So that explains the white stone, but what of the rotating beacon? Indeed, there was a beacon of some note in that city, kept in an upper chamber atop Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon. It seems to me the bones of Isildur came to lie within the tower. If his shade is to find rest, these bones must be recovered.

'But let us not now dwell upon that task. We have been some time away from the Beorning-lands, and Grimbeorn may worry at our absence. We should return to him and assure him we still have need of his hospitality. I desire also to return to my study of the Black Book of Mordor, for I see now that some things I long held to be certain were perhaps not so, and I wonder at some avenues of learning I might have dismissed too readily.''We have been some time away from the Beorning-lands, and Grimbeorn may worry at our absence. We should return to him and assure him we still have need of his hospitality. I desire also to return to my study of the Black Book of Mordor, for I see now that some things I long held to be certain were perhaps not so, and I wonder at some avenues of learning I might have dismissed too readily.''You again? And here I hoped you might have gone, and taken Wizard and Elves with you! It was a pleasant thought, but now it is dashed!''My memory is less certain of the years following the defeat of Sauron, ${PLAYER}. Gultháva's enchantment still enwreathes my mind, and I find it difficult to clearly recall the events that transpired. There were two years of peace, that I know, and during those years the kingdom of Gondor was restored to order. Vows were taken before the Oath-stones, and a tomb made for my father at Amon Anwar. It was to be a hallowed place.

'At last it was time for me to take up my father's place on the high throne in the North. My queen and my youngest son waited for me in Rivendell, where they marked the time during the war, so I chose not to sail. With a company of knights, my sons, and the heirlooms of my house, I rode north... to my death and the death of my sons. We were all of us betrayed. You have agreed to help me avenge this treachery, ${PLAYER}, but I do not see the face of my betrayer, and cannot remember what befell. In my mind's eye I see only a chamber with a white stone, beneath a rotating beacon, but all is hazy, as if I look from a great distance.

'I do not know what this vision signifies. Gultháva's enchantment releases its grip upon my mind but slowly, and leaves only mystery in its wake.'Grimbeorn has not forgotten that Gandalf and the Elves are relying upon his hospitality, and he has some chores for you.Firewood can be found near the base of trees in the Beorning-lands, and Orcs and wargs still threaten the peace of the Beornings.Collect firewood from the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orcs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat wargs in the Beorning-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grimbeorn is waiting for you at the Beorninghús.Grimbeorn has not heard from the Elves at the Forest Gate in some time, and despite his reticence to restart trade with the Elves, he worries about the silence.Go to the Forest Gate on the edge of Eryn LasgalenThindrif is at the Forest Gate.Talk to Thindrif at the Forest GateThindrif invited you to search the corpses of the Orcs for some clue as to why they attempted to pass through the Forest Gate.Thindrif is at the Forest Gate.Talk to Thindrif at the Forest GateThindrif thinks one of the Orcs might have escaped into the Beorning-lands during the commotion.Search the Beorning-lands for the missing Orc's hiding-placeYou found a crumpled note clutched in the hand of the Orc that fled through the Forest Gate.Read the crumpled note you found on the missing OrcGandalf is inside the Beorninghús.'As long as they remain, you must continue to perform the chores I ask of you. We have need of firewood, for so near to the mountains the nights can be cold even in summer. And there are still Orcs and wargs about, despite your efforts of the other day! Put an end to their raids, and teach them a lesson about persistence!

'Carry out these chores and I will allow the Wizard and the Elves to stay a little longer.''Gather up more firewood and put an end to the Orc and warg raids, and I will allow the Wizard and the Elves to stay a little longer at the Beorninghús.''Yes, very good, fine. You have done the chores I asked you to undertake, and earned the Wizard and the Elves a few more days of hospitality.

'There is something else, however. It is not a matter of real concern, but I find I have not heard from the Elves at the Forest Gate in some time, and I wonder if it signals some trouble for my folk? If it does, I would have this problem resolved early rather than late. Go to the Forest Gate and make certain the Elves have things well in hand. If they don't, be sure to tell them so!''I have not heard from the Elves at the Forest Gate in some time, and I do not like it. I do not desire their company, but they do owe me the courtesy of telling me when there is trouble on the border of my lands!''A raiding party of Orcs sought to leave the forest by way of the Gate, ${PLAYER}. You can see what happened to them. It is curious indeed for Orcs to challenge us on the road. Did they not know our quivers held their doom?

'They did seem driven by some desperate haste. Search the bodies, and you may learn what caused them to dare the Gate, to their sorrow.''These Orcs did seem driven by some desperate haste. Search the bodies, and you may learn what caused them to dare the Gate, to their sorrow.''Did you find anything that might explain why the Orcs dared attempt the passage of the Forest Gate? Their need must have been great to challenge us, and they paid dearly for it.

'Wait a moment. Did you say you searched the bodies of four Orcs? That is most peculiar, friend. By my bow, I would swear the raiding-party consisted not of four Orcs but five. Can it be that one of these creatures slipped through the Forest Gate while we were distracted by the others?

'Search to the south in the Beorning-lands for our missing Orc! There may be some tracks you can follow to his hiding-place, if you make haste!''Search to the south in the Beorning-lands for our missing Orc! There may be some tracks you can follow to his hiding-place, if you make haste!''You found our missing villain? Did he have anything to tell us of his purpose in Eryn Lasgalen?''The Elves allowed an Orc to cross through the Forest Gate? Bah! I am pleased to hear you tracked him down.

'The Wizard is inside.''Oh, you have returned. What is it?'

Gandalf's expression is troubled, and he seems distracted by something.

'Falch Gurth? No, I have never heard of it before. That is not important right now. I need to speak with you, ${PLAYER}.'The Kergrim of the Morgul Vale have taken control of the old burial houses Gondor had once constructed for Minas Ithil.Dáru Lagúrz can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should destroy defiled bones and altars of sacrifice in Dáru Lagúrz.Destroy defiled bones and altars of sacrifice in Dáru LagúrzDáru Lagúrz can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should destroy defiled bones and altars of sacrifice in Dáru Lagúrz.Destroy defiled bones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy altars of sacrifice (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroyed many defiled bones and altars of sacrifice in Dáru Lagúrz.CompletedAt the Broken Houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim have defiled a sacred place housing the resting dead. Now it is a place filled with their vile altars, where they conduct horrid rituals. Everything the beasts have constructed here must be destroyed if the dead are ever to know peace.You have destroyed altars and bone piles in Dáru Lagúrz. Those who seek to cleanse the Morgul Vale of the evil that grips it will give thanks for your deeds this day, for it is a beginning, though there is still more to do.The Kergrim of the Morgul Vale have taken control of the old burial houses Gondor had once constructed for Minas Ithil.Kergrim can be found at Dáru Lagúrz in Rath Dúath.

