You should return to the broken-down dwelling to further your investigations.Return to the ramshackle dwellingDefeat the treacherous spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated the watching stone's grip on your mind.CompletedTo your surprise, you spy a small cabin precariously resting in the hills of the Morgul Vale. It looks as if the cabin is occupied by a family, but is that not strange? Men have not lived in the Morgul Vale for many years. Perhaps it is worth investigating this ramshackle cabin and those who dwell there.The child says nothing.You have overcome the deception of the spirits housed within the forgotten watching-stone. Their purpose remains unknown to you, but you feel certain you must not underestimate the malice of this place.The child looks around slowly before clearing his throat, as if he has uttered not a word in years.

'My doll. I must have my doll returned. It is all I have. Where could it be? Find it, please.'Those in the conquest of Gorgoroth and those in fealty to Gondor work together to cleanse the Morgul Vale and the fortress of Minas Morgul of the evils that inhabit them.Echad Uial can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should travel to Echad Uial.Travel to Echad UialDamrod and Thurindol can be found at Echad Uial.

You should talk to Damrod and Thurindol.Talk to DamrodTalk to ThurindolComplete quests in Rath Dúath to establish a hold in the area.Complete quests in Rath Dúath to establish a hold in the area (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Damrod can be found at Echad Uial.

You should talk to Damrod.Talk to Damrod'${PLAYER}, I did not think to see you again. I heard that urgent matters took you away from the conquest of Gorgoroth and sent you far to the north. Well, much has transpired while you were gone, my friend. The Masters of Mordor have turned their attention upon the Dead City. I know not why, but their power has grown and whatever reasons they have for coming to Minas Morgul must be fell purposes indeed! We have come to stop them before they achieve... whatever it is they seek to achieve.

'We found Faramir in good health, commanding the Rangers of Ithilien. They entered the Morgul Vale, and it is their design to cleanse the city of evil and reclaim it for King Elessar. Faramir established an encampment, Echad Uial, nearer to the city. If you should travel there, they will be glad to have your aid.''${PLAYER}! You earned my respect and it has not wavered; word of your deeds in Gorgoroth and in the northern lands has made its way back to me and to the other Rangers of Ithilien. And here we now meet upon the very doorstep of Minas Morgul! That is incredible, my friend, and yet I should not have doubted our paths would lead us here, where there is evil to be faced. Is that not what we do, time and again? It is indeed!

'Faramir has regained his health, a gift of time and some say the healing powers of King Elessar himself, and he has led us here. There is a camp now, Echad Uial, and from there he plans to cleanse the city of its evil, and reclaim it for Gondor. Damrod travels with him and will be pleased to speak with you. Return to me when Damrod sees fit to release you!''Welcome to Echad Uial, ${PLAYER}. Within any wood, we Rangers know how to travel at speed while remaining hidden; I find myself much more at home here than I did in the barren Wastes, where we last spoke. Come, we have much to discuss.' 

You and Damrod share stories and the account of your recent adventures.

'Then you will assist us here in Rath Dúath, for now? Good! You have not changed, my friend. I am glad to hear it, for we have need of you here. Did you think otherwise?''${PLAYER}, you have returned! I'll wager your journey to the north was a success if you have returned to assist us at this hour.

'While we successfully secured Talath Úrui, fumes and fire aside, the memory of that place still unsettles me. Borangos has remained hidden, but I saw tendrils of his thought everywhere, and his servants still haunted me. Now they are gone, and it is as if they never were. Where did they go, and for what purpose?

'Pressing matters in the Morgul Vale drew us hither, and I must leave Talath Úrui behind. I will try not to dwell upon it, but still I worry. Let us aid Faramir with his task here, and we will turn to the matter of vanished Borangos when the city is cleansed!

'I am glad you are here.''You have done much to assist us in Rath Dúath, and I thank you for your efforts. Still, the Morgul Vale is filled with unspeakable dangers. Both the hills and the city must be faced and conquered if we are to banish this evil and cleanse the vale of the corruption that has seized it for so long.'Arodor, under the command of Faramir, seeks to learn more about the noisome flora in Imlad Morgul.Noisome flowers can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should burn noisome flowers in Rath Dúath.Burn noisome flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burned noisome flowers in Rath Dúath.Completed'I am glad to find you well after the war, ${CLASS}. There is much to be done here!

'Have you seen, or perhaps I should say smelled, the noisome flowers that bloom throughout Rath Dúath? Some say they were bred by the Witch-king to sicken those who travel through Imlad Morgul. I do not know if that is true, but... it seems plausible. He hated us, and why should he not? We proved the greatest threat to him, did we not? I heard he died at Pelennor, and no doubt we had a great deal to do with that!

'Well, his flowers remain, and I fear the effect they may have upon the Rangers. Would you be willing to burn any noisome flowers you come across on your travels? You would be doing all of us a great service, friend.'You have burned many of the noisome flowers that grow throughout the Rath Dúath, but the wilds of Imlad Morgul remain treacherous. You must still exercise caution, but the Rangers of Ithilien will be pleased by your efforts all the same.Arodor, under the command of Faramir, seeks to learn more about the many poisonous threats upon the forest floor of Imlad Morgul.Noisome fungus and poison mushrooms can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should burn noisome fungus and destroy poison mushrooms in Rath Dúath.Burn noisome fungus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy poison mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Burned noisome fungus and destroyed poison mushrooms in Rath Dúath.Completed'Ever since I stood look-out over the city of Osgiliath, my mind was captured by the strange wonders of the Morgul Vale. My eyes kept turning that way, for I have been gripped with the fear of it for all my life, ever since I was just a boy. And that was right and proper, for it is a site of evil, and one should be wary of such places.

'But now Faramir has returned to lead the Rangers of Ithilien hither, and I must find my courage. Indeed I have, for I see now that the known evil is less frightening than that which is unknown. I see that Rath Dúath is home to many varieties of noisome plants and fungal growths; this is nature, not sorcery! Some of the fungal growths spew deadly fumes, which certainly pose a danger to those who travel through the valley. If you come across any of these deadly varieties, destroy them! We will all thank you for it.'You burned and destroyed many species of poisonous mushrooms that plague the Morgul Vale, but the threat is not ended forever; their spores live on in the winds, and it will be a long time before the valley might be truly free of them. But you have made a start, and lessened some of the danger.A nameless woman requires food to feed her family in the harsh land of the Morgul Vale.Bats and crawlers can be found in Rath Dúath.

The strange woman has asked you to gather meat from bats and crawlers.Gather worrisome meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The strange woman can be found back at her cabin.

