You should destroy perches and food sacks at Shakam Moz.Destroy food sacks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy perches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroyed many perches and food sacks at Shakam Moz.CompletedIt is said that the winged folk feast upon the slain and the living, free-folk and evil servants alike, and they keep the food they do not consume at once in sacks tied to pikes, where they rot for days. Destroy these sacks and the perches from which the winged creatures observe the path to Lhingris, picking out their prey.You destroyed many of the crude perches and merrevail provisions scattered along the cliff-side. Those who fight on behalf of Gondor to cleanse the Morgul Vale surely thank you for your efforts.High above Imlad Morgul, in an outpost secured by Lhaereth the Stained, merrevail and mervyl watch over the pass to Minas Morgul, consuming all who cross their path.The enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Gondor.Claim the first encampment for GondorThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Gondor.Claim the first encampment for GondorThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Gondor.Claim the second encampment for GondorThe enemy controls this location. You should claim this area for Gondor.Claim the final encampment for GondorClaimed this area for Gondor!CompletedHigh above, Lhaereth's forces control the peak that looks over both the Rath Dúath and Lhingris. It is important that this vantage point does not remain under the wing of Lhaereth the Stained. You decide to climb the peak and claim it for those who fight for Gondor against evil.You successfully claimed this area for Gondor, and sent a message to the forces that serve Lhaereth the Stained: Gondor will not stand idly by while she sweeps her vile wings across the Morgul Vale.The Kergrim of the Morgul Vale have taken control of the old burial houses Gondor had once constructed for Minas Ithil.Kergrim can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should defeat kergrim in Rath Dúath and seek out Dáru Lagúrz.Seek out Dáru LagúrzDefeat kergrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Broglok can be found in Dáru Lagúrz.

You should defeat Broglok.Defeat Broglok, overseer of Dáru LagúrzShalgoth fled to Gorthad Nûr.

You should follow Shalgoth.Follow the path to Gorthad NûrThurindol can be found outside Gorthad Nûr.

You should talk to Thurindol.Talk to Thurindol outside Gorthad Nûr'The kergrim must congregate somewhere in the Morgul Vale. But where?

'Hmmm... what if they gather at the old Gondorian burial houses that our scouts spotted when we entered the valley? I shiver at the thought of those beasts feeding on the dead, but there are likely to be many good men laid to rest in those old crypts, and the kergrim will not respect their sanctity as we would! You should head towards the charnel houses and defeat any kergrim you find on the way. I will join you when I can.''Stay low, my friend. I saw that fiend you chased. Shalgoth entered the tomb ahead.'Thurindol requires assistance in discovering what is killing nearby Orc sentries of Minas Morgul.Orc sentries and corpses can be found in Rath Dúath.

You should defeat Orc sentries and examine any Orc corpses that you find.Examine the Orc corpse on the road to Minas MorgulDefeat Morgul sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Another Orc corpse can be found closer to Echad Uial in Rath Dúath.

You should seek out another Orc corpse to examine.Seek out another Orc corpse in Rath DúathFootprints can be found leading away from the Orc corpse.

You should follow the footprints.Find the creature that is attacking OrcsThurindol can be found at Echad Uial in Rath Dúath.

You should talk to Thurindol.Talk to Thurindol at Echad Uial'I should be glad to see a dead Orc lying upon the road, yet instead I am concerned. The Orc was not killed by one of our own. It would seem that someone hunts Orcs in the Morgul Vale. Another Orc? A mysterious friend? More investigation is required to determine if the killer poses a threat to us. Examine the body and search for more sentries of Minas Morgul. We must get to the bottom of this.''Kergrim, you say? I have heard only tales of these beasts, but they sound vicious and unpleasant. I am thankful that you were able to fend them off, but that is not the end of it. Now we must devise some course of action to deal with the kergrim! The safety of our outpost is at stake.'A strange woman seeks to help you cure that which plagues the Morgulduin River.The urns Rauniel seeks can be found in the hills of eastern Rath Dúath and from outside the barrows of Gorthad Nûr.

You should retrieve the urns for Rauniel.Retrieve the urn from the hills of eastern Rath DúathRetrieve the urn from outside the barrows of Gorthad NûrComplete: Dwelling in the HillsVessels for the water of the urns can be found upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath.

You should pour water into the vessels for Rauniel.Rauniel can be found by the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath.

You should talk to Rauniel.Talk to Rauniel by the bridge to Eithel Gwaur'You are the first I have met who wishes to seek a cure for my river. Yes, I am the keeper of these waters, or once I was. That was long ago, when it was known as the Ithilduin. Now I am but a prisoner of the Witch-king, and endless tears of agony befoul the waters I love. It is not physically that I stand before you; my appearance here is only a creation of your mind. This projection of my thought has stolen the full extent of my power. Can you assist my escape from the watery prison of Eithel Gwaur?

'First you must collect the urns of pure water that remain hidden in Rath Dúath. They will break the wards that prohibit my escape. They are located at one end of the bridge to Eithel Gwaur. Please hurry.''You have done as I asked; I can sense it. Still, there is more to be done if I am to be free and restore the river to its former glory.'Arodor seeks to know more about the Morgulduin River. He is specifically interested in finding a way to cure its putrid waters.The Morgulduin River runs through Rath Dúath.

You should find tributaries into the Morgulduin and sample the water there.Gather water from a northern tributary into the MorgulduinGather water from a southern tributary into the MorgulduinSample water from a tributary into the MorgulduinSample water from another tributary into the MorgulduinThe Morgulduin River runs through Rath Dúath.

You should sample the water of the Morgulduin, further upstream, past its tributaries.Gather water from the Morgulduin, further upstreamSample water from the Morgulduin closer to its sourceRauniel can be found by the banks of the Morgulduin in northern Rath Dúath.

You should speak to the mysterious woman.Speak to Rauniel by the banks of the Morgulduin'Faramir has asked me to continue studying the waters of the Morgulduin, but I have yet to learn what might be causing this corruption. You helped me retrieve river samples once before, might you do the same again? I am certain we will find the answers if we work together. Does a tributary passing through the city taint these waters, or does the problem lie near the river's source? Would you take water samples from nearby tributaries into the Morgulduin and a sample closer to the river's source for me? I would be most grateful for your assistance, my friend.''What interest have you with this river? Speak now, ${RACE}.'Rauniel, the maiden of the Ithilduin, needs your assistance in destroying the wards that block her escape from a treacherous prison.The urn Rauniel seeks can be found at Shakam Moz in the hills of eastern Rath Dúath.

You should retrieve the urn for Rauniel.Retrieve the urn from Shakam MozThe final vessel can be found upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath.

You should pour water into the vessel for Rauniel.Rauniel can be found upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath.

You should talk to Rauniel.Talk to Rauniel upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur'Noble ${RACE}, there is but one more ward on the far side of the bridge. The urn you seek has been recently taken by merrevail, but they know nothing of the urn's significance. Scale the eastern peak and retrieve the final urn. We have come this far, have we not? I have no one else to assist in my freedom. You must seek out the final urn.''Again you are successful? I did not think you possessed such resolve, fair ${CLASS}. I am glad you are the one to rescue me. Still, there is more to be done before I am able to escape my bonds.'Mírthel has asked you to hunt some of the local wildlife and assess whether their meat can be eaten by the Rangers.Mírthel has asked you to hunt some of the wildlife in Cirith Ungol to assess the edibility of the meat.

You should hunt deer and dire-horns for their meat.Collect venison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect dire-horn meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mírthel is waiting for you to return with the meat.Talk to Mírthel'Might I ask for your assistance while you are here?

'As you may have guessed, supplying our small expedition has been difficult. We brought what we could carry up the Straight Stair, but it will not last long. Going forward, we must choose between finding a source of sustenance here among the darkness and corruption, or send someone to fetch more rations from Captain Faramir's camp, and that is a treacherous journey. Obviously, the former is preferable.

'I have seen some deer and goats while scouting the area. Would you please hunt some of them, so I can assess if the meat is edible?'Mírthel recoils as you hand him the meat. The smell is quite foul.

'Ah... not so edible, then. A shame. The deer are too sickly for our consumption, and the goats have succumbed to a fell sort of corruption that enables them to survive in this evil place.

'Thank you for your efforts all the same. I will dispatch one of our Rangers for more rations.'There are many unhatched spider eggs in Taurlingol. Atli suggests you deal with them before they become a problem.Many unhatched spider eggs can be found in Taurlingol.

You should destroy spider egg sacs.Destroy spider egg sacs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Atli can be found on a hill near Taurlingol.

You should talk to Atli Spider-bane.Talk to Atli Spider-bane'Those woods are crawling with spiders, aye, but you know what else? Spider eggs! Squash those little devils before they hatch!

'What? Do you think spiders fight fair? Of course not! Deal with them before they become a problem!''Did you squish those eggs? Good! One destroyed egg now is one fewer spider later!'Celeborn asks you to close the many winding passages created by Ungwetári's spawn under the Mountains of Shadow.Many small passages exist within Torech Ungol, allowing the spiders and gredbyg to come and go.

You should block these small passages to trap Shelob's brood.Block small passages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Beneath these mountains, there are many sprawling tunnels carved by Ungwetári and her brood. If we come across any small exits, we should close them to pen the spiders in. The Gilgelair will block the larger passages.'Gandalf has continued his study of the Black Book of Mordor, and he has much to tell you.Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, waiting to divulge what he has learned from his study of the Black Book of Mordor.Talk to Gandalf and complete 'Instance: The Picture Painted'Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, shaken by what he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor.Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús'I suspected there was something I missed in the Black Book... and I was right. I could not place my finger upon it, but something stirred within the recesses of my mind, and I found a new avenue of study worth following.

'Will you hear me, ${PLAYER}? Things are not as we believed.''Give me your attention, and do not let it wander; you must know what I have learned. I have made a worrisome discovery.''Gothmog has been responsible for much sorrow in each of his guises, ${PLAYER}. It seems too that his fate is interwoven with yours, for even the tale of Vóin is not free of his corruptive touch, though it be written almost a thousand years ago. Gothmog has been a long-simmering font of evil; he can no longer remain unchallenged. It is time at last to put an end to him.

'These past few years revealed to us that which we did not know: King Eärnur was not slain when he rode to Minas Morgul to confront the Witch-king; he was instead transformed into Mordirith, a thrall of the Lord of the Nazgûl. It was by Mordirith's hand that the shadow fell upon Angmar, but he was opposed by Golodir the Ranger and Narmeleth of Lindon, to say nothing of a certain ${CLASS} of my acquaintance. Mordirith's designs were broken, but his spirit persevered and he was given a new guise, and a new task. He would command Sauron's armies in war, second only to his old master, the Witch-king of Angmar.

'But the Witch-king was slain at Pelennor, as few only might have dared hope, and Gothmog's confidence in his own invulnerability was shaken. He fled the field, escaping to Imlad Morgul and sealing the roads in or out of that vale. While Sauron thrived, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth had worries enough to occupy their attention, and Gothmog could be set aside. But now a new fear presents itself to me. Gothmog has had time now to lick his wounds and search the valley for artifacts that might reverse his fortunes. What terrible sorceries might he have discovered?'According to Gandalf, the problem posed by Gothmog has become too serious to bear. Your road leads now to Imlad Morgul, where the creature that was once King Eärnur now lurks.Fennas Gost, the Dread Door on the outskirts of Gorgoroth, provides access to Imlad Morgul.Travel to Fennas Gost on the outskirts of Imlad MorgulAn injured Ranger at Fennas Gost has called to you, hoping to prevent you from suffering as he has.Talk to the injured Ranger at Fennas GostEchad Uial is west of Fennas Gost, in Imlad Morgul.Find Echad Uial in Imlad MorgulBeregond is at Echad Uial in Imlad Morgul.Talk to Beregond at Echad UialBeregond asked you to defeat foes throughout Rath Dúath, and to scout the terrain by <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb>ing at several important landmarks within Imlad Morgul.Defeat foes throughout Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Faramir, Prince of Ithilien, can be found near the Bridge of Gúliant in Imlad Morgul.Talk to Faramir at the Bridge of Gúliant<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Fennas Gost on the outskirts of Imlad Morgul when you accept this quest.</rgb>

'King Elessar has charged Faramir, Prince of Ithilien, with cleansing the evils from Imlad Morgul. Find his men at Fennas Gost, the Dread Door on the western bounds of Gorgoroth, and aid them with their mission. They will not be able to stand alone against Gothmog, but your help may tip the balance in their favour.

'Remember, my friend: Minas Morgul was once the tower of Minas Ithil, a jewel of Gondorian art and culture, but it has spent long centuries corrupted by the Nazgûl and Sauron's other terrible servants. None can say what dangers you will find within, but I trust that if any ${RACE} has the courage to face them, you do.''Be careful, friend! We are hard-pressed here!''Be careful, friend! We are hard-pressed here, and attacks can come at any time, without warning!

'It was at Prince Faramir's command that we forced open the Dread Door, and we paid dearly for it. Many of my brethren did not survive the initial attack, but now we hold it against whatever evils try to retake it; we will not risk dishonouring the memory of our fallen by giving it back!

'We established a camp to the west, and you may find the Prince there. Do what you can to help us, for we have need of strong allies and do not dare turn anyone away!''Welcome, my friend.''We established a camp to the west, and you may find the Prince there. Do what you can to help us, for we have need of strong allies and do not dare turn anyone away!''I bid you welcome to Imlad Morgul. Ha! Do I say "welcome?" This is not a welcoming place, and indeed it must be the least-such I have ever seen!

'Even so, it is my honour and my joy to serve here at the command of King Elessar, for it was his mercy alone that allows me to still draw breath. My crime could not be forgiven: I spilled the blood of my fellows and for that a Guard of the Citadel deserves death. Because I acted to save the life of my lord Faramir, the king named me an exile, and charged me with the further protection of Faramir's life. I do not gainsay the king's wisdom, nor would I, but neither am I blameless. I bear my guilt with me, and strive every day to serve King Elessar and Prince Faramir.

'It is the king's command that Minas Morgul be utterly destroyed and the valley cleansed. I do not know how this might be accomplished, but I will do whatever I can to make it so! Thus do I welcome you to Imlad Morgul, ${PLAYER}, strange though it seem!

'My prince has not found it easy to shake his roots as a Ranger; even now he walks somewhere in the valley, despite our warnings. I ask you to find several places from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at Minas Morgul and at the Bridge of Gúliant, and also to defeat our foes along the Rath Dúath. Take the road west until you emerge from the trees; there is a short stone pillar by the side of the track from which you can study the walls of the city. Faramir intended to survey Gúliant, and you may find him there when you have accomplished these tasks.''It is good to see you. This was once the Bridge of Ithiliant, but no longer. Now it is called by another name: Gúliant.''My prince has not found it easy to shake his roots as a Ranger; even now he walks somewhere in the valley, despite our warnings. I ask you to find several places from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at Minas Morgul and at the Bridge of Gúliant, and also to defeat our foes along the Rath Dúath. Take the road west until you emerge from the trees; there is a short stone pillar by the side of the track from which you can study the walls of the city. Faramir intended to survey Gúliant, and you may find him there when you have accomplished these tasks.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I will not say this is a pleasant place, but I know that once it was. This was Imlad Ithil, and nowhere else in Gondor could rival its beauty when the Ithilduin river sparkled in the moonlight like a vein of silver threaded between dark cliffs. When Isildur came to these shores with his father and brother, he was so taken by the beauty of this valley that he built a citadel beneath the slopes of Achathras, tallest peak of the Ephel Dúath. Minas Ithil he called it, and Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent Moon, rose from its topmost level.

'But that was long ago, and the Lord of the Nazgûl coveted the valley and the citadel sheltered within. Twice the Witch-king seized the city. The first time, he possessed it only until the Last Alliance of Men and Elves came south and fought the war that ended the Second Age. Minas Ithil remained under the control of Gondor for centuries, and although it would never again attain the heights it had known under Isildur, it drew the imaginations of poets, artists, and minstrels from all over the kingdom.

'That all came to a sad end with the second of the Witch-king's assaults upon the city. When the Nazgûl captured Minas Ithil for the second time, that name could no longer describe the citadel. It became Minas Morgul, the Tower of Sorcery, and so it would stay.'Gandalf has made a worrisome discovery while continuing his study of the Black Book of Mordor.Gandalf speaks to you of the discoveries he made while studying the Black Book.Talk to GandalfVóin writes of his adventures in the Grey Mountains, where he encountered Magoldir the Elf and the two became fast friends.Move through the twisting passage until you reach the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of MemoryGandalf is in the Grey Mountains as they are depicted by the Halls of Memory.Talk to Gandalf in the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of MemoryGandalf is in the Grey Mountains as they are depicted by the Halls of Memory.Listen to the words of Gandalf concerning his discoveriesTwo thousand years following his survival of the Siege of Barad-dûr, Magoldir adventured in the Grey Mountains... but he did not travel alone.Examine the indistinct figuresTwo thousand years following his survival of the Siege of Barad-dûr, Magoldir adventured in the Grey Mountains... but he did not travel alone.Listen to the words of Gandalf concerning his discoveriesTwo thousand years following his survival of the Siege of Barad-dûr, Magoldir adventured in the Grey Mountains... but he did not travel alone.Examine the indistinct figure that remainsGandalf is in the Grey Mountains as they are depicted by the Halls of Memory.Listen to the words of Gandalf concerning his discoveries'I should have known, ${PLAYER}. I should have read the signs.''From my earlier study of the Black Book, we learned of Vóin's encounter with Magoldir the Elf in the Grey Mountains and their subsequent friendship. Unremarkable, perhaps, and yet we marked it, for an air of mystery surrounds this tome; both the circumstances in which it was found and the writing between its black covers fill me with intrigue and unease in equal measure.

'From the shade of Isildur we learned somewhat of Magoldir the Elf, and few of his deeds seemed notable. It is no slight to him, merely the truth that his most significant achievement appears to be his survival; nearly two thousand years passed before his name surfaced anywhere, and that in the Black Book.

'What, then, of Magoldir's inclusion? Why did Vóin see fit to write of this Elf?''What has Vóin to say about this meeting? Listen well, ${PLAYER}.'The time has come to enter Torech Ungol, confront Rûkhor the Pale Herald, and discover if Shelob yet lives.Felgúr has continued ahead to Torech Ungol, and is waiting at the top of the Winding Stair.

You should climb the Winding Stair and find Felgúr.Talk to FelgúrFelgúr has tracked his people to the top of the Winding Stair.

You should talk to Felgúr, and be ready for a fight.Complete 'Instance: She Who Walks in the Darkness'Celeborn and Legolas are outside Torech Ungol, at the top of the Winding Stair.

You should talk to Celeborn and Legolas.Talk to CelebornTalk to LegolasCeleborn has asked for your help containing the spiders in Torech Ungol.

You should help Celeborn with 'Re-forming the Snare' and 'Caging the Spiders'.Help Celeborn with 'Re-forming the Snare'Help Celeborn with 'Caging the Spiders'Celeborn can be found outside Torech Ungol.

You should talk to Celeborn.Talk to CelebornCeleborn has asked you to swiftly return to the rangers in Echad Taerdrim.

You should return to the rangers and talk to Mablung.

Speak to Legolas to return there quickly.Talk to Mablung'Felgúr continued on while you were searching the camp. Fear not, I did not lose track of him. He is at the top of the Winding Stair. It is from there we will enter Torech Ungol.

'I am wary of travelling together up the stair. If these Bloodless Uruks have set up an ambush, that is where they will attempt it. We will be in the open and without footing. I will stay back and cover you. Go on and find Felgúr.''They are near. I can smell them. I smell HIM. The Pale Herald.''They are coming. I hope you are ready for a fight.''It has been some time since my last encounter with Ungwetári. Time has only made her more dangerous, more ravenous. Her wound has only increased her aggression and inflamed her hatred. We must do what we can to contain her and the Gúrzyul Rûkhor. To do nothing is to allow calamity.''You must tell me everything, ${PLAYER}.'

You tell Legolas of Rûkhor giving Felgúr back his skin-changing, the encounter with Shelob, and Rûkhor's final taunt. Legolas takes a moment to carefully consider everything.

'I believe his plan was to use Felgúr and yourself to lure Shelob out. He knew you would try to run, and perhaps she would follow you out of Torech Ungol into the Morgul Vale. But, he could not have anticipated Celeborn's appearance.

'Yes... I believe it is Rûkhor's aim to rouse Shelob from her underground lair so she may devour all in her path. His enemies, and his rivals. As ever, this all distills down to the former servants of the Dark Lord squabbling for control of his fading empire....''Lord Celeborn speaks true. The Rangers must be made aware of what transpired here. Let us return to Mablung as swiftly as we are able.'

<rgb=#FF0000>You will swiftly travel to Echad Taerdrim!</rgb>You quickly inform Mablung of all you learned in Kaslokroz and of what occurred in Torech Ungol. Mablung looks both distressed and awe-inspired.

'Wait, wait, hold a moment! Let me see if I have this right. Rûkhor wants to rouse the wounded Shelob from her lair so she eats everyone and everything, and when she goes back to sleep he wants to take Mordor for himself. That is a terrible, terrible plan! And, not only that, but he convinced the Ungoledain to lead him right to her, and he gave Felgúr back his skin-changing? Then that poor fool went after Shelob, she ATE him, and almost ate you as well, but Celeborn, the Lord of Lórien himself, stepped in to save you?'

You nod and confirm that is the summary of what transpired. He takes a moment to steady himself.

'What a day, ${PLAYER}. What a day. I will send for reinforcements at once and move all available scouts to keep watch on Torech Ungol. No one will come or go without our knowledge. When Celeborn is ready to confront Shelob, we will stand with him.''Our efforts will hold the spider-horde in Torech Ungol, for now. Soon we must pursue Ungwetári herself, but until then I ask you and Legolas to return to the Rangers of Ithilien and inform them of Rûkhor's plot. We will soon need a small force to enter the deep tunnels: Remmorchant, the Net of Darkness. That is where we will meet the spider-queen. That is where I will end this. I will send for you when the time is right.'Legolas has identified the leaders of the Bloodless Uruks in Kaslokroz and would like your help eliminating them.Legolas has identified the leaders of the Bloodless in Kaslokroz.

You should defeat Draulush, Mangath, and Narnagír.Defeat Draulush the BloodyDefeat Mangath the ImperviousDefeat Narnagír the White-arrow'I have identified the lieutenants of these Bloodless Uruks in Kaslokroz. I hear them issuing orders to the others, and hear their names on the wind: Draulush, Mangath, and Narnagír. You know what must be done, ${PLAYER}.'Strange orbs filled with blood and sorcery dot Kaslokroz, a camp of the Uruk-hai.Blood orbs can be found in Kaslokroz, an Uruk-hai camp.

You should destroy the blood orbs.Destroy blood orbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have destroyed the blood orbs in Rûkhor's camp.

You should report your success to Legolas near Kaslokroz.Talk to LegolasYou have found a strange orb filled with what you believe is blood in Kaslokroz. It gives you an uneasy feeling; perhaps it is used by The Pale Herald for his dark sorceries. You decide that destroying it, and others like it, is probably in your best interests.You tell Legolas of the strange blood orbs you destroyed in Kaslokroz.

'Unusual. I have not heard of these before, but I suspect they are in some way related to his sorcery. Perhaps it is a vessel for when a living host is unavailable. You did well to destroy them, ${PLAYER}.'Legolas has asked you to defeat any Ungoledain priestesses you find in Cadar Skûs, as they are the ones who claim leadership of the clan.Legolas has asked you to defeat Ungoladan devoted in Cadar Skûs.Defeat Ungoladan devoted (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated the highest ranking Ungoledain at Cadar Skûs.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'From my observations, it is clear Ungoledain society is matriarchal, and those highest in the social ladder are the priestesses of Mam Murgwid. We should find and defeat them to sow confusion in their ranks.''From my observations, it is clear Ungoledain society is matriarchal, and those highest in the social ladder are the priestesses of Mam Murgwid. We should find and defeat them to sow confusion in their ranks.''Those that devote themselves to the worship of Ungwetári will forever be our enemies. If they ever learn this lesson, the bloodshed can be spared.''Those that devote themselves to the worship of Ungwetári will forever be our enemies. If they ever learn this lesson, the bloodshed can be spared.'Legolas has asked you to thin the ranks of the Ungoledain at Cadar Skûs.Unoledain have set up camp in Cadar Skûs, a small village in western Cirith Ungol.

You should defeat Ungoledain in Cadar Skûs.Defeat Ungoledain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Many Ungoledain have been defeated this day.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'While we seek a living prisoner, I have little sympathy for Men who ally themselves with the spiders, an ancient enemy of my people. Do not spare any who refuse to surrender to you.''While we seek a living prisoner, I have little sympathy for Men who ally themselves with the spiders, an ancient enemy of my people. Do not spare any who refuse to surrender to you.''I am always impressed by your skills in battle, ${PLAYER}. We have done well thinning their numbers.''I am always impressed by your skills in battle, ${PLAYER}. We have done well thinning their numbers.'Gladhir has asked you to help exterminate the many pests found in Cirith Ungol.Gladhir has asked you to defeat any insects you come across in Cirith Ungol.Defeat insects in Cirith Ungol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gladhir can be found in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.

You should talk to Gladhir.Talk to Gladhir'I have need of your strength and your will, if you can spare the time.

'We have come to a foul land, corrupted by the dark river below, and ravaged by howling winds above. To make matters worse, we are constantly harassed by the local pests! The incessant buzzing is driving me mad! Please, do me a favour and take care of any insects that cross your path!''You return! I can tell you were successful; the noise is much reduced! Thank you for your service, ${PLAYER}. One fewer pest out there is one fewer in our food stores later.'Gladhir has told you of a massive grodbog queen high in the cliffs of Cirith Ungol. You will need allies, but defeating her will surely curb the flow of gredbyg in the area.The grodbog queen Maeganc can be found somewhere in the cliffs of Cirith Ungol.

You should defeat Maeganc and collapse the nearby tunnel to Torech Ungol.Defeat MaegancCollapse the grodbog tunnelGladhir came be found in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.

You should talk to Gladhir.Talk to Gladhir'${PLAYER}, we recently discovered the location of a massive grodbog queen high in the cliffs. I described her to Legolas; he grimaced and said the name "Maeganc". Perhaps he has encountered her before? The Elves can be quite... cryptic. 

'Regardless, I believe she is the source of the gredbyg closest to the camp, and therefore a threat to us. If you are able, I would ask that you and your companions find her and eliminate her before she finds us and does the same! While you are there, please look for a tunnel that may have allowed her passage from Torech Ungol. I do not expect the gredbyg would have travelled such a distance overland; they must have burrowed through the rocks beneath! If you find this tunnel, collapse it, or more gredbyg will come through.'You inform Gladhir that Maeganc has been vanquished and the tunnel to Torech Ungol collapsed.

'Excellent work, ${PLAYER}! I knew I could count on one as skilled as you. You are a breath of fresh air in this putrid land! With the quelling of the gredbyg threat, we can worry about the other creatures present here, for I believe they are more sentient and may prove the graver threat.

'We will no doubt be relying on you more before this expedition is over. Be safe out there. Between the heights, and the beasts, and the venomous things, this is one of the most treacherous places I have ever had the displeasure of visiting....'Long ago, Celeborn used the Gilgelair to hold Shelob in Torech Ungol. Today, those star-glasses will be replaced.Broken Gilgelair can be found inside Torech Ungol.

You should replace the broken Gilgelair.Replace the broken Gilgelair (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Celeborn can be found outside Torech Ungol, at the top of the Winding Stair.

You should inform Celeborn you have replaced the Gilgelair.Talk to Celeborn'When first I found Shelob hiding among these mountains, I was able to restrain her within Torech Ungol with the Gilgelair, glasses filled with the Light of Eärendil. I suspected that Sauron destroyed them when he came to Mordor in the Second Age. It must be true, as the broken glasses remain inside. Now that he is gone, we must restrain Ungwetári and her children. This is the first step to finally defeating the Spider-queen. Take the Gilgelair, and replace the ones that Sauron destroyed.''It is done? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I pray these hold her until we are ready to enter Remmorchant.'Trap-door spiders make their home along the Winding Stair, waiting to ambush anyone who passes by.Trap-door ambushers can be found along the Winding Stair in Cirith Ungol.

You should defeat trap-door ambushers.Defeat trap-door ambushers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed.CompletedYou have discovered trap-door spiders dwelling along the Winding Stair, waiting to ambush anyone who passes by. Defeat these ambush predators before they claim any further victims.You have successfully cleared the stair of ambushing spiders, which will allow the Rangers of Ithilien safe passage in the future.Mírthel has asked you to deliver supplies to Rangers in the field in Cirith Ungol.The crate of Ranger supplies can be found in Echad Taerdim.

You should collect the supplies to take to the Rangers in Cirith Ungol.Collect the Ranger suppliesRangers of Ithilien can be found in the western cliffs of Cirith Ungol.

You should deliver supplies to any Rangers you find. Mírthel said there were five.Deliver supplies to the resting RangerDeliver supplies to the famished RangerDeliver supplies to the tracking RangerDeliver supplies to the ill RangerDeliver supplies to the nervous RangerMírthel can be found in  Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.

You should talk to Mírthel.Talk to Mírthel'${PLAYER}, while you are out there with Legolas, keep watch for my fellow Rangers. Five of our company are already afield and would appreciate some fresh supplies.''I was expecting Mírthel to come with supplies, not you, ${PLAYER}! Thank you for your efforts, friend!''Thank you, friend. I was growing quite famished, and have not been able to find anything edible in these wilds. The plants and animals are all tainted!''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I have been attempting to follow these tracks, but it is very difficult. The others joke that the men leaving them must have sprouted wings and flew, but that cannot be, can it?''Ugh. The foul stench from the river below carries all the way up here. I shall have to return to camp soon, before I am seriously ill from the fumes! Thanks to your supplies, I should be able to make it back on my own.''Oh, ${PLAYER}! You startled me. This area is crawling with gredbyg, and it has me a bit on edge. Thank you for the supplies, but I may return soon for the sake of my own sanity.''It is done? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I am sure they were pleased to see a friendly face in this harsh land, especially one bearing fresh rations!'Goblins and white Uruk-hai pledged to Rûkhor the Pale Herald threaten the expedition into Cirith Ungol.Rûkhor's forces are camped in Kaslokroz in Cirith Ungol.

You should defeat Rûkhor's uruks and goblins.Defeat Rûkhor's forces in Kaslokroz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Legolas can be found near Kaslokroz, Rûkhor's encampment.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'These white Uruks must be the Bloodless, as Rûkhor called them. We would do well to defeat as many as we can now, while we have the element of surprise on our side. I believe that Rûkhor uses the goblins as fodder for empowering his Uruk-hai forces, making them a strategic target as well. Enter Kaslokroz and defeat as many of Rûkhor's forces as you can.''Excellent work as always, ${PLAYER}. By removing the fuel to power his dark sorcery, and the forces who benefit from it, we have dealt a blow to the Pale Herald's strength. However, we should not let our guards down yet. The Gúrzyul should never be underestimated.'Legolas has come to Cirith Ungol to address some unfinished business. What has become of Shelob, her brood, the Mirkwood spiders, and the tower of Cirith Ungol?The Straight Stair marks the start of your journey into Cirith Ungol.

You can find it through a pass just behind Halhir, who is stationed along the Morgul-road.Find the Straight StairEchad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol under command of Mablung, can be found at the top of the Straight Stair.

You should travel to Echad Taerdim.Find Echad TaerdimLegolas can be found at Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to LegolasLegolas believes the first course of action is to gather information from the Rangers of Ithilien stationed at Echad Taerdim.

You should talk to Mablung, Mírthel, and Gladhir.Talk to MablungTalk to MírthelTalk to GladhirLegolas is waiting for you in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. It gladdens me to see a friendly face on the road! Legolas has asked for you. He is waiting at Mablung's camp just ahead. To reach it, just take this pass behind me and head up the Straight Stair. Be warned, if you are headed into Cirith Ungol, there will be many stairs and steep climbs in your future! And, of course, there's the spiders. Many, many spiders.'

He shivers at the thought, and bids you farewell.'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. How have you fared since our last meeting? I am certainly glad for the help of Legolas and yourself. You are among the most skilled ${CLASS}s I have ever met.

'Our goal in Cirith Ungol is to try to establish a knowledge of any threats to Ithilien that may still exist in this place. Specifically, where the spider presence is, their numbers, and if the Orcs have any forces here. Indeed, despite Shelob's apparent defeat, we have already established that the spiders linger still. As of yet, we have found no evidence of Shelob herself, living or dead, but have found many of her brood.

'We know not the situation in the tower. I sent some Rangers to approach as close as they could to it, which is not especially close, for the path is treacherous and spider-infested. They reported they could detect little Orc activity on this side of the tower. I do not know if they have simply moved the garrison closer to Dor Amarth, or if they have abandoned the tower entirely.

'We also noticed when we set up camp here that someone, likely an uruk based on the size of the prints, had passed this way very recently, heading east toward the tower. Mírthel and Gladhir may have more information for you.''Good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! I am afraid I have little time to catch up. We have come to a dangerous place, and there is much to be done. I can share what information I have.

'There is very little spider presence on the west side of Cirith Ungol, which does not surprise me as we believe they are mainly coming from Torech Ungol itself. However, we have found one puzzling thing for which I have no explanation: in several places, we have found sets of footprints—alike that of Men both in shape and size—that seem to disappear mid-stride! The others are speculating that they sprouted wings and flew! I am not sure I believe that, but it is certainly worth looking into. See if you can find some of these footprints to the north-west.''Greetings, ${PLAYER}! How have you fared since the Battle of the Black Gate? I have done some scouting myself, and can tell you what I saw.

'The spider presence is dense to the east, as expected. They continuously flow out of Torech Ungol like a foul stream. Among them are also several horrible varieties of gredbyg. None of this is surprising, but in the north-east I found a forest completely overwhelmed by webs, and a large brood of spiders that seemed to be separating themselves from the ones in Torech Ungol. Make of that what you will!''Welcome to Cirith Ungol, ${PLAYER}. I have much unfinished business to manage here, and I would appreciate the help of a skilled and trusted friend such as you.

'When we last left the tower of Cirith Ungol, it was besieged by spiders; if the Gúrzyul failed to reinforce the garrison, the tower might fall to the spiders, and that would unleash the spiders upon Gorgoroth, and perhaps the larger world! I have heard no reports of spider activity beyond Lhingris, so perhaps the Orcs prevailed. We will have to investigate.

'There is also the matter of the Mirkwood spiders. When my father faced our old enemy Iphantamel, she said that all of her daughters had left her. We suspect that they may have come here, at the call of their true mother.

'Finally, we must discover if Ungwetári yet lives. As valiant as Master Samwise is, I do not believe she would have succumbed to such a small wound, though it was inflicted by a courageous heart. She is ancient and powerful.

'There is much to do. We should begin by questioning the Rangers of Ithilien. They have begun scouting the area, and may already have some answers to our many questions.'You relay to Legolas all of the information the Rangers shared with you.

'Interesting. I am glad to have such skilled Rangers at our disposal. They have saved us a great deal of time.'

Legolas' attention briefly drifts away as he considers all you have said.

'Several mysteries now need to be unravelled. Why did the Uruk-hai pass this way? Did they come from the city or somewhere else? If they were headed to the tower, does that mean the pass from the east is no longer accessible to them? What are these spiders that sequester themselves from the others? What do these strange footprints mean, where Men can suddenly disappear mid-stride? We have much to consider, and much ground to cover.'Legolas has asked that you come to Cirith Ungol when you are able to assist him with some unfinished business.Halhir can be found somewhere along the Morgul-road, somewhere to the west.

You should find Halhir.Talk to Halhir'${PLAYER}, Legolas has requested your assistance with a matter of great importance in Cirith Ungol. I was asked to send you his way, if you are able. Mablung and a few others have set up camp somewhere in the cliffs, but I do not know how to find the camp myself. Halhir should be stationed on the Morgul-road in that area; just follow it west and you should come across him eventually. He should be able to direct you further.'Halhir waves as you travel down the road. He smiles as you approach.

'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! I see Legolas's call has reached you!'Iphantemel's own daughters hide in Taurlingol, attempting the retain control of the Mirkwood spiders.The Daughters of Iphantemel are lurking somewhere in Taurlingol.

You should defeat Lhothbad, Iárvereth, and Saeriel.Defeat LhothbadDefeat IárverethDefeat SaerielLegolas can be found on a hill near Taurlingol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'The spider you defeated with Atli, Aegarach, was a daughter of Iphantemel herself. If one is here, her sisters will be as well. They are known to me: Lhothbad, Iárvereth, Saeriel. Terrible all. I speculate that they are the reason that some of the Mirkwood spiders have separated themselves from the rest. Perhaps they are attempting to retain control of their brood. Regardless, these sisters must be hunted down. They are responsible for the deaths of many of my people.''You have given my people a great gift with the deaths of these horrible monsters. Their deaths have been avenged.'The other children of Shelob, the Gredbyg, have also taken up residence in Torech Ungol.Many gredbyg have responded to the call of Shelob and taken up residence in her lair.

You should defeat gredbyg inside Torech Ungol.Defeat gredbyg in Torech Ungol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Legolas is standing by outside Torech Ungol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'Beyond the spiders, it seems that various gredbyg have also responded to the call of Shelob and taken up residence in Torech Ungol. Do not let your guard down; they are also dangerous in great numbers.''Did you defeat the gredbyg? Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. I know not how many more there are, or how deep they live inside. They may be Ungwetári's children, but they are unlike the spiders in many ways, and pose different threats.'Atli knows there is only one solution when you enter a spider-infested forest.You have entered a forest overwhelmed with spiders in Cirith Ungol.

You should defeat many spiders in Taurlingol.Defeat spiders in Taurlingol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Atli can be found on a hill near Taurlingol.

You should talk to Atli Spider-bane.Talk to Atli Spider-bane'You know what you have to do, ${PLAYER}. The only good spider is a dead spider, and since I'm injured, I leave it to you! Go into that accursed forest and kill the spiders!''So, how many did you kill? 15? Eh, not bad. I suspect you'll add to that count before you're finished in Cirith Ungol!'You have discovered much in Cirith Ungol, and the time has come to regroup with the Rangers of Ithilien.Legolas wishes to return to Echad Taerdim with an injured Atli Spider-bane.

You should speak with Legolas near Taurlingol to begin the journey.Complete Instance: Ambush at Echad TaerdimLegolas has returned to Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to LegolasFelgúr has been taken prisoner, and is being kept in Echad Taerdim.

You should talk to Felgúr.Talk to FelgúrFelgúr has asked you to propose a deal to Mablung on his behalf.

You should talk to Mablung in Echad Taerdim.Talk to MablungAtli Spider-bane is resting at Echad Taerdim.

You should see how Atli is faring after Rûkhor's assault.Talk to AtliLegolas can be found in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'When you are ready, let us depart for Echad Taerdim. Atli needs rest, and his wounds need to be better-tended than I can manage out here. I am also curious to hear if Mablung has learned more from our Ungoladan prisoner.''Come, let us return to Echad Taerdim.''The Pale Herald has finally made his appearance. We must be cautious. A Gúrzyul is already a formidable opponent, but something about his Uruks unnerved me. Did you notice it as well, ${PLAYER}? They possessed the foul aura of dark sorcery. I must think on our next steps. If you would, please make sure the others were unharmed in the assault.'Felgúr stares at the ground, grimacing. His former matriarch's words must have affected him. As you approach, he looks up and speaks, his voice almost cracking with emotion.

'I must speak with you, ${CLASS}! Rûkhor will betray my people, I am sure of it! But they will never accept me as I am now.

'I want to make a deal with the one in charge here! Tell that Mablung I will help him find my people and the Pale Herald if he helps me find a new life among Men. I can no longer hear the call of Mam Murgwid, but I can still sniff out my own kin.''Yes, I heard what the Ungoladan said. He was practically shouting! His suggestion is worth consideration. He is of little threat to us now that the enemy knows our location. He cannot skin-change and attack us himself, after all. Furthermore, several of my Rangers were injured in Rûkhor's attack and we are short-handed. Perhaps I can also pity someone who has lost everything....

'Fine. You can tell Felgúr he has a deal. Just make sure you keep an eye on him. He has not earned my trust, just a jot of leniency.''You have returned. Forgive me, but I overheard most everything. It is a small camp.

'I am not sure I agree with Mablung's decision regarding the Ungoladan, but perhaps he can be of use to us.'

He turns to Felgúr and speaks just loud enough for him to hear:

'I will be watching you, Ungoladan. If you betray us, you will find an arrow between your eyes.'

Felgúr looks terrified and nods enthusiastically. Legolas turns his attention back to you.

'Atli's account of the tower is also troubling. It may have completely fallen to the spider-horde since we departed. The time has come for us to head towards the Winding Stair and Torech Ungol. We must race to find Rûkhor and the Ungoledain before their wicked plans reach fruition.''Good to see you came out of that attack unscathed, ${PLAYER}. I am no worse off myself, just the gnawed leg from earlier.'

He chuckles and then groans, stroking his injured leg. You ask him how he came to Cirith Ungol and if he knew anything of the tower.

'Ah... after you departed Lhingris, I worked up the courage to enter the tower myself. It was the site of a massacre! Dead Orcs and spiders everywhere, not much of anything alive inside. I continued on and found the gate wide open. I can tell by the look on your face that you know the gate of which I speak! Yes, I entered Torech Ungol itself! Barely made it out alive, but I slew a great many spiders while I could! I then found my way to that cursed forest, Taurlingol. Easier pickings, until that big one chanced upon me and my leg, thinking to have us both for dinner. Heh!

'I will stay here for now. The Rangers are gracious enough hosts. Get out there with Legolas and slay some more spiders for me! As for the tower, hmm, I think the spiders have surely overtaken it by now. If the Orcs and their evil masters attempted to re-take it, they must have failed.'The time has come to track the Ungoledain and Rûkhor the Pale Herald with the aid of Felgúr.Legolas has asked you to unbind Felgúr and send him on his mission.

You should talk to Felgúr in Echad Taerdim.Talk to FelgúrFelgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain.

You should travel with Felgúr.Find the Ungoledain with FelgúrFelgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain.

You should travel with Felgúr.Find the Ungoledain with FelgúrFelgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain.

You should travel with Felgúr.Find the Ungoledain with FelgúrFelgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain.

You should travel with Felgúr.Find the Ungoledain with FelgúrLegolas has appeared near an Uruk camp in eastern Cirith Ungol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to LegolasFelgúr would like to speak with you.

You should talk to Felgúr.Talk to FelgúrLegolas has asked you to find evidence of Rûkhor's plans in Kaslokroz.

You should find written orders to the Uruk lieutenants.Find Rûkhor's first orders to ZabothakFind Rûkhor's second orders to ZabothakFind Rûkhor's third orders to ZabothakFind Rûkhor's fourth orders to ZabothakLegolas is waiting near Kaslokroz.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'It is time for Felgúr to make himself useful. Have him track down his kin. I will be watching from nearby, but will keep to the shadows.'You untie Felgúr and let him know it is time to begin tracking down the rest of the Ungoledain. He looks around sheepishly, still not entirely trusting of the Rangers or of Legolas. When he is at least mostly convinced he is not about to be shot full of arrows, he nods to you.

'I will find them! Let us start by heading east.''Hold, friend. It seems we are on the right track. There is no sign of the Ungoledain, but we did find Rûkhor's uruks. I propose we investigate the camp while we are here. Perhaps we can glean some clue as to Rûkhor's abilities and his motivation for seeking Ungwetári.''Are you going in there? Eh, that was not part of my bargain. I do not think I can fight those big white Orcs without the power of the Spider. I do not smell my kin here. I might wait with the Elf, or continue the search. You can find me later.'Zabothak, my most loyal servant.

Belzagar has sent word. The tower must be reinforced at once or be lost to the spider-horde. Rally with Ugrukhôr's forces and re-take the tower, or Shelob may be set loose upon Gorgoroth or the Morgul Vale. Do not fail me.Zabothak,

Fear not, my servant. I lay the blame for this defeat on the traitor Ugrukhôr. If he had delivered the forces he promised me, the tower would be secure. His excuses do nothing but tire me. We owe no allegiance to the Lady of Blight. I care nothing for the false king Gothmog. I will be formulating a new plan. Stand by to receive new orders.Zabothak,

I have had an epiphany. Perhaps Shelob is not a problem we can solve. Perhaps she is not a problem at all.

Rally the Bloodless. We will enter the Morgul Vale. We will enter Torech Ungol. We will find Her Ladyship Ungwetári and rouse her from her den.Zabothak,

Thus far, we have been unable to locate Shelob's den in the maze of tunnels in Torech Ungol, but we may finally have a solution. The scouts have located a tribe of primitive Men recently arrived to the west. They have been seen skin-changing into spiders! I believe these may be the Ungoledain that Karazgar mentioned. And if they have come all the way here... perhaps they also hear the call of the Spider-queen. Prepare for a delegation.'What have you learned, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Legolas of the orders you found in the uruk camp.

'Rûkhor is using the Ungoledain to seek Ungwetári? To what end? Does he intend to try to control her? Surely he is not so foolish. But it is true: pride seems a common flaw among the Gúrzyul.

'If Rûkhor and the Ungoledain were not at this camp, they must have already left for Torech Ungol. We do not know Rûkhor's plan, but if he succeeds in rousing Ungwetári, she will be unleashed upon all of us! I cannot fathom the terrible rampage he may incite. Her ravenous hunger will never be sated!

'We must hurry after them. We have no other choice.'Legolas wishes to next investigate the spider-infested woods in eastern Cirith Ungol, Taurlingol.According to the Rangers, the spider-infested forest of Taurlingol can be found in eastern Cirith Ungol.

You should find Taurlingol.Find TaurlingolAs you entered Taurlingol, you heard someone shouting.

You should find the source of the shouting.Find the source of the shoutingYou have found Atli Spider-bane in combat with a giant spider of Taurlingol.

You should help Atli defeat the spider!Help Atli defeat the spiderAtli has moved to a safe location nearby.

You should find and talk to Atli Spider-bane.Talk to Atli Spider-baneLegolas is tending to Atli Spider-bane's injuries on an overlook near Taurlingol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to LegolasLegolas has asked for your assistance with tasks in Taurlingol.

You should complete 'The Daughters of Iphantemel,' 'The Trees of Taurlingol,' 'Before They Become a Problem,' and 'The Only Solution.'Help Legolas with 'The Daughters of Iphantemel'Help Legolas with 'The Trees of Taurlingol'Help Atli with 'Before They Become a Problem'Help Atli with 'The Only Solution'You should inform Legolas of your success defeating the Mirkwood Spiders.

Legolas can be found on a hill near Taurlingol.Talk to Legolas'I doubt there is much else to learn here, ${PLAYER}. I would like to continue on with our mission. We should next investigate the spiders to the east. The Rangers report the spiders there isolate themselves from the spiders of Torech Ungol. I suspect I may know their reasons for this, but I would like to confirm my suspicions with my own eyes before I share my thoughts.

'I will bring the Ungoladan prisoner back to Echad Taerdim. Mablung may wish to question Felgúr himself. I will meet you near the spider-infested forest, Taurlingol.''Oof, thanks for the assistance, ${PLAYER}. And Legolas is here as well! I am happy to see some faces with fewer than eight eyes! It also helps that you're not trying to devour me. Haha! Erk....'

Atli doubles over and grabs his leg. His injuries seem to be worse than he let on.

'Aye, she chewed up my leg something fierce. Oh, don't worry about me, I will be fine. I just need to rest a bit....''I apologize for not arriving sooner, ${PLAYER}. I did see the spider you fought, and my suspicions were proven correct: these are the Mirkwood spiders, Iphantamel's own brood. This forest is too small to hold all that vanished from Eryn Lasgalen, however. Perhaps some have already entered Torech Ungol. I admit I do not fully understand the quarrelling between spiders. It matters not. The old enemy of my people has been found, and we must deal out vengeance upon them.

'I must tend to Atli's wounds, thus I must rely on you to venture into Taurlingol and slay my enemies for me. I know that you are capable of this task.'

You ask Legolas how he and Atli are acquainted. He allows the briefest hint of a smile to cross his face.

'Ah, I encountered him when we were last in Lhingris, in a very similar situation, in fact. He was engaged in combat with several very large brood-mothers, and I stepped in to assist him. I believe he was embarrassed, and accused me of "stealing his kill".

'But that is quite absurd!''Well done, ${PLAYER}. With the death of Iphantamel's daughters, the rest of the spiders will likely disperse into Cirith Ungol. I will return to track and kill them myself, one by one. For now, we must escort Atli to Echad Taerdim. He should be able to travel on his wounded leg, but it is not safe to remain here.'Shelob's lair has become infested with her spider children. Legolas has asked you to thin their numbers.The spider-horde has completely overrun Torech Ungol.

You should defeat spiders in Torech Ungol.Defeat spiders in Torech Ungol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Legolas is standing by outside Torech Ungol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'From Frodo and Sam's accounts, Torech Ungol should be empty. They found no living beings inside save Ungwetári herself. That is no longer the case, as she has recalled all of her children from the wider world. I do not know if she has done this for sustenance, protection, or loneliness. I cannot pretend to fathom the mind of such an ancient and evil being as she. It matters not, the spiders are a threat and must be thinned before we enter deeper into the tunnels.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Atli will be happy to hear there are fewer spiders in the world. Alas, there will be many more to slay in our near future. The horde is nigh unending.'Legolas has captured an Ungoladan by the name of Felgúr. He has much to tell you.The Ungoladan that ambushed you has regained consciousness.

You should talk to the Ungoladan.Talk to the UngoladanFelgúr has a tale to tell about a dark man who came to lead his people astray.

You should talk to Felgúr to hear the tale.Complete Instance: The Pale HeraldFelgúr has one last thing to say to you.

You should talk to Felgúr outside Cadar Skûs.Talk to FelgúrLegolas would like to discuss this new information with you.

You should talk to Legolas outside Cadar Skûs.Talk to Legolas'He appears to be regaining consciousness. Speak to him, and we will determine if he has any use to us alive.'The Ungoladan groans, clearly in pain from his knock on the head. He realizes what has just happened and grimaces. You ask him if he might answer some questions for you. He sneers and looks away, only to see the Elf-prince's icy glare. He quickly changes his mind and speaks.

'I am Felgúr. Ask your questions.'

You ask him why he did not change into a spider, and why the Ungoledain are here in Cirith Ungol. He looks away. Is he... ashamed?

'I tried to avenge our fallen leader, Mengris Tásakh. The brown one stole my skin-changing. My people turned on me! They tried to eat me! I am nothing without the Spider, but I follow my people. I have no other life. We are here because we follow the call of Mam Murgwid. We must be close now. The others are entranced by it, but I can no longer hear the call. The Spider has left me....'

You turn to Legolas, to gauge if he has heard enough. Felgúr quickly speaks up again, fearing for his life.

'There is one other thing I must say! My people are being led astray by an outsider. A dark one! You must listen!''Please, hear what I must say!''I do not trust this "Pale Herald", but I am exiled and can do nothing. Kill me if you want. I have no fear of death now.''He was surprisingly forthcoming! He must have understood that only useful information could stay our blades. It troubles me greatly that the Gúrzyul Rûkhor is here in Cirith Ungol. Perhaps the situation in the tower is worse than we thought.

'I believe Felgúr may be of further use to us. We should take him back to Echad Taerdim.'Legolas has decided to first pursue the tracks the Rangers believe to be left by "winged men".The mysterious footprints of which the Rangers spoke can be found north-west of Echad Taerdim.

You should find the footprints with Legolas.Find the mysterious footprintsLegolas would like to talk to you about these strange footprints.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to LegolasYou have discovered evidence of an Ungoledain presence in Cirith Ungol.

You should follow the tracks to find the Ungoledain.Find the UngoledainLegolas would like to speak to you about the Ungoledain camp you discovered.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to LegolasYou have discovered an Ungoledain camp within Cirith Ungol. Legolas has decided a prisoner may yield some useful information.

You should attempt to take an Ungoladan prisoner within Cadar Skûs.Attempt to take an Ungoladan prisonerLegolas would like to speak with you.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to LegolasLegolas would like to regroup in a safer location.

You should find a safer spot to talk south of Cadar Skûs.Find a safe place to regroup near Cadar SkûsYou are being ambushed!

Defeat the attacker!Defeat the attacker!The Ungoladan attacker has been defeated.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'I would like to begin with these mysterious "winged men". While the spiders are likely the most pressing concern, I do not want to travel into the more dangerous areas of Cirith Ungol with an unknown enemy still out there. Come, let us travel to the cliffs to the north-west and see if we can find the tracks for ourselves.''I understand what the Rangers meant; the footprints of a Man, and then suddenly...'

Legolas goes silent. His eyes dart around, closely examining the prints.

'I think I see what they could not. The footprints do not disappear, they merely change shape! I am not surprised that the Rangers could not see the footprints of a spider, but they are an old enemy of my people and I know them well. I believe you have already encountered Men who can become spiders, have you not, ${PLAYER}? We have uncovered the presence of the Ungoledain!

'Let us continue in the direction of these tracks. We may find the skin-changers higher in these mountains.''These are indeed the Ungoledain. I spoke with Radagast about these strange skin-changers when we were last in the Vales of Anduin. He said they were following the call of one they named Mam Murgwid, and it was his belief that might be Ungwetári herself. There is much I do not understand, but if these Men choose to ally themselves with the spiders, then they are my enemy, and yours! But because they are Men, we should attempt to take one as a prisoner and bring our captive back to Echad Taerdim. An interrogation may yield useful information.''Something is wrong. It is as if they cannot hear us at all and are completely entranced by some unseen force. I do not believe we will be able to capture one while they are in this state. We should do what we can to reduce this threat to the Rangers. When we are finished let us regroup in a safer area nearby.''This foolish Ungoladan was easily dispatched... perhaps too easily. Why did he not shift into his spider form? It matters not; we desired a prisoner and now we have one.'The Mirkwood spiders have only recently arrived, but already they taint the forests in Cirith Ungol.Mirkwood spiders have killed and webbed many trees in Taurlingol.

You should burn webbed trees.Burn webbed trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Legolas can be found on a hill near Taurlingol.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'The Mirkwood spiders have only been in Cirith Ungol a short time, and yet they have already begun to destroy the forest. They suffocate and hollow out trees to use as shelter for their broodlings. The dead trees must come down.'We could do nothing for the trees that were already killed, but by culling the spiders, we may yet save the living forest.'Legolas has asked you to destroy the Ungoladan totems in Cadar Skûs.Legolas has asked you to destroy spider totems in Cadar Skûs, for fear they may be conduits for foul magic.Destroy spider totems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have destroyed many spider totems in Cadar Skûs.

You should talk to Legolas.Talk to Legolas'I have seen the totems the Ungoledain carve in the likeness of "Mam Murgwid"; the face they give to the voice in their minds. I worry these are no mere statues, but perhaps a vessel for their foul magic. We should tear down those we come across in Cadar Skûs.''I have seen the totems the Ungoledain carve in the likeness of "Mam Murgwid"; the face they give to the voice in their minds. I worry these are no mere statues, but perhaps a vessel for their foul magic. We should tear down those we come across in Cadar Skûs.''Thank you for humouring me, ${PLAYER}. Even if the totems are not conduits for magic, you have still removed their gruesome images from the world, a favourable outcome.''Thank you for humouring me, ${PLAYER}. Even if the totems are not conduits for magic, you have still removed their gruesome images from the world, a favourable outcome.'Gothmog's forces have several valuable supply stores located within their encampment. Dolenthol asked you to destroy the supplies, creating a distraction that might serve of some use to the Rangers.Supply stores can be found throughout Gothmog's camp.

You should destroy the supply stores to create a distraction for Dolenthol.Destroy supply stores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have destroyed several supply stores located throughout Gothmog's camp.

You should return to Dolenthol and inform him of your success.Talk to Dolenthol'Scattered through the camp are several stockpiles of supplies. If we were to destroy these stores, we might cause sufficient distraction for us to withdraw from the area.

'Would you see this done, friend? Venture deeper into the camp to create this distraction, and we will have our chance!''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Your efforts will have created sufficient confusion for us to withdraw from the area.'Few among the River Hobbits have journeyed as far from home as you, but even after all your adventures, there are few things that would bring you more comfort than returning to Misthallow.Journey back to Misthallow and complete 'Farewell Lyndelby'Faramir, Prince of Ithilien, has been kept busy maintaining the watch on Minas Morgul.The entrance to Minas Morgul is located at the end of the road south of the Bridge of Gúliant.

Faramir asked you to do battle with the foes you find in the Dead City.Find the main entrance to the city of Minas MorgulDefeat foes within Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Passage between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul can be found north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë.Climb the ramp between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul, north-west of the Song-house of LindalírëYou found a mortally-wounded Morgul cultist on the ramp between the second and third tiers of Minas Morgul, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë.Talk to Nâlunitir on the ramp between the second and third tiers of the city, north-west of the Song-house of LindalírëFaramir intended to return to Echad Uial. You should find him there and tell him what you learned from the dying Morgul cultist.Return to Echad Uial and find FaramirFaramir is at Echad Uial, waiting for you to report on what you encountered in the Dead City.Talk to Faramir at Echad UialMithrandir has made the journey to Echad Uial.Talk to Mithrandir at Echad Uial'When I was just a boy, my brother Boromir and I had the finest teachers in all of Gondor. They told us tales of noble Elendil, wise Isildur, and bold Anárion, and our days were spent reenacting their most heroic deeds. But of all these tales, it was the fall of Minas Ithil to the Lord of the Nazgûl that most moved my brother's heart. I can still hear his voice recounting it to me on a stormy afternoon, ${PLAYER}, and though the tale is a sad one the recollection is welcome to me.

'"An army of Orcs came to the gates," I can hear him say, "but they were met by a hail of stones. The lord of the city, a great captain named Egalmoth, sent out sorties to sow confusion upon the Orcs and delay their plans. The Witch-king himself sought to breach the gates, but could not; years before and at the request of the King of Gondor, the wizard Curunír placed powerful enchantments upon them, and they held against the Witch-king's evil sorceries. But Egalmoth knew his men could not outlast the forces arrayed against them. At dawn of the appointed day, he sounded his war-horn and led his men on their mounts through the gates, forming a wedge to drive the enemies to either side or trample them underfoot. They rode to the bridge; see the light on their faces as they approach, knowing freedom is near! But it was not to be so, for as they neared the Ithiliant, the bridge sundered, its pieces falling into the river. Egalmoth could go no further, but he despaired not. He commanded his men to turn their backs to the raging river, and they charged once again... straight toward the Orc armies and their fell commanders. So died Egalmoth, but the tale of Egalmoth's Onslaught fills our hearts with joy even today, for we know that he died in service of Gondor, and so we remember him."'

Faramir smiles, remembering his brother's love for this tale. Then he sighs wistfully, and scuffs the stones with the toe of his boot.

'The Nazgûl had weakened the supports of the bridge, so ensuring Egalmoth could not escape that way. Boromir was always quick to point out that it was a strategy they had learned from Isildur, for the son of Elendil had used that very tactic against them when he first escaped Minas Ithil. Theirs was not a mindless evil, ${PLAYER}. Let us be glad they are gone.

'Yes, the Nazgûl are slain with Sauron, but others might still work his evil within the Dead City. South of here, the road climbs up to Minas Morgul. Go there and learn what you can of the situation inside. Defeat whatever foes you find there in memory of the hero Egalmoth, and in memory of my brother too.''Other servants of Sauron might still work his evil within the Dead City. South of here, the road climbs up to Minas Morgul. Go there and learn what you can of the situation inside. Defeat whatever foes you find there in memory of the hero Egalmoth, and in memory of my brother too.''Scout the ramp between the second and third tier of Minas Morgul, north-west of the Song-house of Lindalírë, and learn what dangers lurk within the Dead City.''If you've come to plunder Minas Morgul, you've arrived too late! The coward Gothmog sealed himself away in the tower, but he has minions roving the city, searching for whatever treasures might have been left behind. A doomed search! In the Valley of the Secret Shadow he might have found a useful weapon, but his Orcs cannot find the way.'

The cultist laughs, despite the pain of her wounds, and the blood staining her garb grows a deeper shade of red.

'My master Dolguzigir knows the path, but he will not tell Gothmog. Let the coward waste away in the tower... if he lives that long! More than one enemy desires his blood, and I have seen servants of at least two already. They say the Captain of the Pit will not rest until he has taken Gothmog's head, but he will have a rival for it; I heard Lhaereth the Stained hates Gothmog even worse than she hates your kind or mine, and that is no small amount! Look what... her merrevail did to me!

'Well, I have had my last jest, and I am ready to die. Let them kill each other. They deserve...''Well, did you learn anything that might be of use to us?''So we are not the only ones taking an interest in Minas Morgul. From your report, it sounds as if Ugrukhôr and Lhaereth have both sent their forces to the city, and Gothmog still commands a significant portion of the Orcs within. Furthermore, this Morgul cultist spoke of one called Dolguzigir, about whom I have heard little. These interests may not align with each other, for now, but we cannot take the risk that they might set aside their differences. Any of these foes will slay us without a second thought.

'The Valley of the Secret Shadow? I do not like the sound of that. Perhaps Mithrandir will know something of this place.''Perhaps Mithrandir knows something of this Valley of the Secret Shadow.''Hmm... the Valley of the Secret Shadow? That is Thuringwath, but its location is unknown to me, and to any good folk, I should expect. Do you remember the Orcs that challenged the Forest Gate on the edge of Eryn Lasgalen? The note you found mentioned a hidden pass named Falch Gurth and a secret enchantment. It is possible these spells masked the way to Thuringwath.

'But I have come here for another reason. I have uncovered developments most interesting from my study of the Black Book of Mordor.'Unwilling to remain behind in the Vales of Anduin, Mithrandir has come to Echad Uial with the Black Book of Mordor.Mithrandir is at Echad Uial, waiting to discuss what else he has learned from the Black Book of Mordor.Talk to Mithrandir in Echad Uial and complete 'Instance: The Sword and the Stonemaiden'Faramir is at Echad Uial.Talk to Faramir at Echad UialBeregond is at Echad Uial.Talk to Beregond at Echad Uial'Let us not delay. I will tell both you and Prince Faramir what I have learned, if you and he have the time and the interest to listen.''Faramir, I must ask that you not pepper me with questions while I tell you both the tale, or it will take much longer! Trust that ${PLAYER} will explain to you anything you do not understand. A Wizard's time is valuable and I cannot spend all day relating my discoveries to you.

'Are you both ready to listen? Very good.''That is the latest of my discoveries from the Black Book. What else lies between these leather covers, I wonder?''That is quite a tale! One day you will need to tell me where you found this curious tome, ${PLAYER}. The sigil on its face cannot be mistaken for anything save the Eye of Sauron, which marks it as an artifact of evil. How then came it to tell the tale of King Eärnur? Nay, not even so, for he was not yet king. But still, little is recorded of the years before he followed his father Eärnil to the throne. To find such an account in a book bearing the mark of Mordor is troubling to me.

'But Eärnur's doomed adventure into the citadel now called Durthang has brought to mind a recent conversation. Beregond spoke to me of someone with an interest in that place. Speak to my captain and ask him what happened to the man with the shield. A Man of Ithilien he was, but I confess I do not know his name. He was here at the camp, but I have not seen him since I returned.''Eärnur's doomed adventure into the citadel now called Durthang has brought to mind a recent conversation. Beregond spoke to me of someone with an interest in that place. Speak to my captain and ask him what happened to the man with the shield. He was here at the camp, but I have not seen him since I returned.''The man with the shield? Aye, I remember him. I did not much like the look of him, though.'Beregond charged the soldier Annoth with some tasks around Echad Uial, but Annoth has set his own plan in motion.Beregond charged Annoth with a number of duties to perform by the tent surrounded with crates in Echad Uial, to the north-west of his position.Look for Annoth by the tent north-west of Beregond in Echad UialDagoras is in Echad Uial.Talk to Dagoras at Echad UialDagoras saw Annoth studying the map in Echad Uial, to the west.Examine the map on the table to the west in Echad UialThe location Annoth marked on the map is north-west of Minas Morgul, up in the mountains. That may be where he has gone.Travel to the location Annoth marked on the map, north-west of Minas Morgul, up in the mountainsAnnoth may have climbed the stairs leading to Cirith Ungol. But when did he pass this way, and did he survive?Look for Annoth further along the rocky pathAnnoth is among the rocky crags within sight of the bottom of the Winding Stair.Talk to Annoth among the crags not far from the base of the Winding StairAnnoth asked you to search for signs of Ugrukhôr up the path to the north-east, among the crags.Search for some sign of Ugrukhôr among the crags to the north-east of AnnothYou found a crumpled parchment in the hand of Ugrukhôr's captain. What secrets lie within?

The soldier Annoth will be interested to see the report you found.Bring the report to Annoth not far from the base of the Winding StairYou found a crumpled parchment in the hand of Ugrukhôr's captain. What secrets lie within?

Gandalf will be interested to see the report you found. Return to the Wizard at Echad Uial.'What did he name himself? Annoth, I think he was called. He carried a broken shield around with him, and it seemed to me he repaired it as best he could with leather straps. The thing was barely holding together, and looked as if it would fall apart at the first blow of an enemy's weapon. Irresponsible.

'I set him to conducting an inventory of the rations and water for the camp, but he has not reported back to me. Go find him, will you? He should be somewhere by the tent to the north-west, among the crates.''I set him to conducting an inventory of the rations and water for the camp, but he has not reported back to me. Go find him, will you? He should be over by the tent surrounded with crates, to the north-west.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! Our work is never done, is it? Ah, I would not have it any other way, my friend, and I suspect neither would you.

'But you are here seeking the Ithilien Ranger with the broken shield? I wondered why he carried it around with him, but I did not ask. He seemed particularly interested in the map on the table over there, just to the west.''The man with the broken shield seemed very interested in the map on the table over there.''He marked a location on the map with a dagger? Well, if I were seeking this man I would check that location first!

'But you do not need my advice, ${PLAYER}. You have adventures in the wild to spare, and nearly as many as me!''He marked a location on the map with a dagger? Well, if I were seeking this man I would check that location first!

'But you do not need my advice, ${PLAYER}. You have adventures in the wild to spare, and nearly as many as me!''Hail, friend! It has been many days since last we saw each other. I trust you are well?''It is good to see you, my friend, for it means the Khundolar you brought out of Gorgoroth has not yet sunk his dagger into your back! I urge you now as I urged you then: keep Ayorzén the Wily at arm's length, for he cannot be trusted!'

You ask Annoth why he failed to complete the inventory with which Dagoras entrusted him, and the Ranger grimaces.

'You make your point sharply, and it wounds me! I do feel badly about shirking that duty, but I had little choice in the matter. I overheard from some of the scouts that Ugrukhôr himself had been seen west of Cirith Ungol, and that he made for Minas Morgul! I have not given up my quest to avenge the Thandrim, ${PLAYER}. I will make the Captain of the Pit pay for his crimes against them, though they be a thousand years distant. Let Ugrukhôr fear the descendant of Halannon the Survivor! I will let no other task hinder me in my vengeance.

'But it seems the reports were false. He has not come himself, so far as I have seen, though his Orcs stalk among the crags. Will you search for some sign of him up the path to the north-east? Then I will return to my duties.''It seems the reports were false. He has not come himself, so far as I have seen, though his Orcs stalk among the crags near the tower. Will you search for some sign of him among the crags to the north-east? Then I will return to my duties.''What does Ugrukhôr's captain have to say to his master?'

Annoth studies the crumpled note.

'These words are full of fear, ${PLAYER}. It seems the Masters of Mordor have more worries than King Elessar or Prince Faramir alone, or indeed the two of us; they fear the treachery of their allies. Listen: "If Gothmog has found a weapon to use against the spider-folk and their mistress, he keeps it to himself in his tower."

'The promise of such a weapon will surely draw Ugrukhôr to Minas Morgul! Let us be grateful that the Ungoledain did not slay every member of this Orc raiding-party, for word of this should still reach the Captain of the Pit through the survivors of that band. He will come for Gothmog and for this weapon, and I will be ready. The Thandrim will be avenged!

'You should bring this report back to the camp. Tell them what we have learned, and that Ugrukhôr knows Fennas Gost is closed to him. Instead he sends small raiding parties into Imlad Morgul by way of Torech Ungol, as I suspected!''Annoth shirks one duty and seeks to avoid punishment by providing useful tidings? I have seen it before, but I am not his commander and it is not my place to levy judgment. But I would caution him against pursuing vengeance with such single-minded purpose. He would not be the first to make such a mistake, nor I fear the last.

'But this report does help me piece together some of what I believe Gothmog has been up to while we were occupied with other matters.'Two forces of Orcs are fortifying the outer ring of Minas Morgul. Thornaran has asked you to defeat warriors in either camp.Two Orc armies inhabit the Circle of Wrath in Minas Morgul.

You should venture forth and defeat Orcs from either army.Defeat Orcs from either army in the Circle of Wrath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Thornaran and tell him you successfully defeated Orcs in Minas Morgul.Talk to Thornaran'Hail to you, and well-met! Our position in the city is a precarious one, and I hope you will be able to help us keep it! The outer ring of Minas Morgul is inhabited by two different armies of Orcs, and each of them stands in the way of the work we must do.

'Would you defeat troops from either encampment as you encounter them, thereby helping us ensure we can accomplish our mission here? Good, good!''You defeated Orcs from one of the armies in the Circle of Wrath, or dare I hope... from both? I am pleased to hear it, and to offer you my thanks.'Zhar Dushgoi lies east of Barad Angarth in the outer ring of Minas Morgul. Thornaran asked you to seek out and defeat its Orc captains.A powerful host of Orcs makes camp within Zhar Dushgoi.

You should seek out one of the captains in Zhar Dushgoi and defeat him.Defeat one of Gothmog's captains in Zhar DushgoiReturn to Thornaran and inform him that you defeated an Orc captain in Zhar Dushgoi.Talk to Thornaran'East of here lies Zhar Dushgoi, an Orc encampment that has proven quite a thorn in our side already. Within that camp, several captains serve to keep their subordinates in line. Would you venture into the area and defeat one of the captains? I do not care which! Any of them will do!''You did very well, my friend! Those Orcs are sure to miss that captain. Please accept my thanks.'Two forces of Orcs fortify the outer ring of Minas Morgul, and their goblin scouts are a threat to all who seek to move within the city.Two Orc armies inhabit the Circle of Wrath in Minas Morgul.

You should venture forth and defeat goblin-scouts within the encampments.Defeat goblin-scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Thornaran and tell him you defeated goblin-scouts in the Circle of Wrath.Talk to Thornaran'Goblin-scouts. I hate them, you hate them, what more needs be said? They are a threat to our position here, and must be defeated. Will you see it done? I am not particular: scouts from either encampment will do.''There are fewer goblin-scouts about? Then I am pleased! I cannot stand them, and now I need not! The Circle of Wrath remains dangerous, but it will be easier for the Rangers to move about unseen, which is very important. Please accept my thanks.'Two forces of Orcs fortify the outer ring of Minas Morgul. Thornaran asked you to seek out sergeants for either army, and defeat them.Two Orc armies inhabit the Circle of Wrath in Minas Morgul. 

You should venture forth and defeat sergeants in either encampment.Defeat Orc sergeants in either encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Thornaran and tell him you defeated Orcs in Minas Morgul.Talk to Thornaran'Minas Morgul is as dangerous a place as any I have dared to go! The outer ring, the Circle of Wrath, is currently home to two Orc armies. Each of these plays host to sergeants who organize small bands of warriors that train in the art of many different kinds of weapon. We cannot allow that, of course.

'Will you venture into either of these encampments and defeat sergeants as you encounter them? It would be a big help to us.''I'd like to see those sergeants try to train anyone in the art of combat now! No, I take that back. I have heard the Dead walk on the upper tiers, and in this city such a thing seems almost possible! But I am glad the sergeants' training days are done... for now, at least. Brrrr!

'Please accept my thanks. It is most appreciated.'From Zhar Skator, one of Ugrukhôr's captains commands an Orc army in the Circle of Wrath.A powerful host of Orcs camps within the Circle of Wrath, in Zhar Skator.

You should seek out and defeat one of the Orc-captains.Defeat one of Ugrukhôr's captains at Zhar SkatorYou should return to Thornaran with news of your victory over the Orc-captain.Talk to Thornaran'Our position here? Precarious, my friend!

'To the west of here lies Zhar Skator, an encampment of the Orcs, from which several captains keep the lesser Orcs in line. If something were to happen to one of these captains, those under their command might become unruly and disorganized....

'Do you understand me? I see that you do.''You defeated an Orc-captain? Ah, I can hear the tumult from here! Very well-done, my friend! I wager they will be more disorganized after that, just wait and see!'Orcs have fortified the outer ring of Minas Morgul, to the east. Thin the ranks of the Orcs in this area, so the Rangers can proceed further into the Dead City.The Orcs that threaten the Rangers can be found to the east of Barad Angarth.

Deplete the Orc forces as you make your way further into the encampment.Defeat Orcs to the east of Barad Angarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Inform Dorgam that you have defeated some of the forces surrounding his position. He is east of Barad Angarth.Talk to Dorgam within the Orc encampment'Thank you for your offer of aid in this dark time; we have greater need of it than ever! Two Orc armies have begun to fortify their positions within the outer tier of Minas Morgul, putting a stop to our forward advance.

'I sent two Rangers, Dorgam and Dolenthol, westward into the city. They will attempt to gain more information about the area, but could still use your assistance to defeat any of the Orcs you might encounter.

'Please reduce their numbers as we seek to learn more about the dangers that await us within the city.''Thank you for the help, ${PLAYER}.

'Now that you have thinned the numbers of some of the forces surrounding us, we should find it easier to seek out information concerning our entrenched foe.'Shakfut is in command of Ugrukhôr's troops in Zhar Skator, west of Barad Angarth. If he is driven off, the remaining forces might push towards Gothmog's troops.Shakfut is currently leading Ugrukhôr's troops in this area. He has been able to prevent his forces from pushing towards Gothmog's encampment on the western side of the Circle of Wrath.

