You should talk to Damrod.Talk to Damrod in Barad Angarth'Faramir has commanded me to lead a group of Rangers into the Dead City. I would like you to assist us, ${PLAYER}. There are many challenges that await us within its walls, but the very first awaits us without! We must find a safe way into the city.

'I fear the most direct route, by way of the main gate, may not be the best choice. Our numbers are few and the foes arrayed against us are many. I would like you to patrol the outer wall and search for weaknesses; perhaps there may be some secret entrance, heretofore undetected. There may be some way for us to enter the city while remaining beneath the notice of those who dwell there.''I thank you, ${PLAYER}, for leading the charge. We have successfully secured the tower of Barad Angarth. This will be our first base of operations in Minas Morgul, but likely not the last! From here we will work towards retaking the Dead City.''You have returned from patrolling the outer wall of Minas Morgul? What have you found?'

You tell Damrod of the small hatch you discovered at the base of one of the towers.

'I believe this may be our best option for entering the city. That tower is called Barad Angarth. Our scouts have spied Orcs patrolling the very top of the tower, and when night blankets the Vale they have seen the flicker of firelight in the windows. We should expect some resistance inside, but I think they will be unprepared for our attack. Quickly let us gather what is needed and prepare to take hold of Barad Angarth!'Damrod has asked you to investigate the invading Orc army fortified in Zhar Skator, the western half of the Circle of Wrath in Minas Morgul.Damrod has asked you to destabilize the Orc forces by completing several tasks in the western half of the Circle of Wrath.

You should complete quests in Zhar Skator.Help Damrod in Barad Angarth with 'Twice the Threat'Help Damrod with 'The Enemy of my Enemy'Dolenthol can be found somewhere amongst the fortifications in Barad Angarth.

You should talk to Dolenthol.Find DolentholDolenthol has asked you to venture further into Zhar Skator and learn more about Ugrukhôr's forces.

You should help Dolenthol with 'Word Among Ugrukhôr's Forces'.Help Dolenthol with 'Word Among Ugrukhôr's Forces'Return to Dolenthol in Zhar Skator with a report of what you overheard from Ugrukhôr's forces.Talk to DolentholDolenthol has asked for assistance destabilizing Ugrukhôr's forces in the Circle of Wrath.

You should help Dolenthol with 'Confronting Shakfut' and 'Spoil the Supplies'.Help Dolenthol with 'Confronting Shakfut'Help Dolenthol with 'Spoil the Supplies'You should return to Dolenthol and inform him of your progress.Talk to DolentholDamrod is standing by in Barad Angarth, awaiting word on Ugrukhôr's forces.

You should talk to Damrod.Talk to Damrod'The information you gathered was of the utmost importance. I agree with Dolenthol, our best hope of breaking this siege may be to turn the Orc armies against each other.

'My scouts tell me the Orcs have begun to gather in the western reaches of the Circle of Wrath. If we strike quickly, we might destabilize their forces; with strategy we may goad them into lashing out against Gothmog's forces.

'Head west, and see if you can assist Dolenthol in destabilizing the Orc army gathered there.''Hello again, ${PLAYER}. We have learned that the invading Orc army is under the command of the Gúrzyul Ugrukhôr. Clearly, there is very little unity among the former servants of Sauron.

'I do not know why they have not pressed their attack on Gothmog's forces. It seems they entered the city, and then halted. Do they anticipate reinforcements? We must know more before we can act.

'Please venture further into Ugrukhôr's encampment and gather information about the stalemate between the two forces.''Ugrukhôr ordered his forces to enter the city, but they were unable to break through to the next tier and have stalled. The march has left their supplies depleted and strained the morale of the Orcs. A handful of the bigger ones are keeping the others in line, and for now they await further instructions. I believe I know what we must do.

'Drive off the Orc captain Shakfut, and destroy nearby supplies so we can foment dissent among Ugrukhôr's forces.''It appears your work was successful! Ugrukhôr's forces are preparing to retaliate against Gothmog's Orcs.

'It would be wise for us to leave the area before they mobilize. Our plan will fail if they realize it was the Rangers of Ithilien that instigated the attack! We should head back to Barad Angarth and inform Damrod of our success.''Come with me. I will lead us back to Barad Angarth unnoticed.''Your work bears fruit, ${PLAYER}! Ugrukhôr's Orcs have moved to attack Gothmog's forces, and truthfully they do so as an unorganized mob, without discipline. If we tread carefully, we may be able to deal decisive blows to both armies!'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Complete Interlude: Blood of AzogDamrod has asked that you enter the fray between Gothmog and Ugrukhôr's forces and defeat each army's captain.Complete 'The Harrowing of Morgul' on any difficulty.

Use the Instance Finder to enter this instance.Complete 'The Harrowing of Morgul' on any difficultyWith the defeat of both Shaktur and Dargásh in Zhar Dushgoi, the Rangers are able to reach deeper into Minas Morgul.

You should speak to Damrod and inform him of your victory.Talk to Damrod'The battle between the Orcs has begun, and an opportunity has presented itself. The captains of both armies have made themselves known. If we are able to defeat both of them, the Orcs will be leaderless and collapse into an unruly, undisciplined mob! We will then be able to move further into Minas Morgul.

'Now that we have identified the captains of the two clashing armies, Shaktur and Dargásh, we should set our plan into motion. Good luck out there, ${PLAYER}. The Rangers of Ithilien are with you!''We must defeat both Shaktur and Dargásh in Zhar Dushgoi if the Rangers are to move further into the city!''With Shaktur and Dargásh defeated, we can now press on deeper into Minas Morgul. We can also provide secure supply lines and further reinforcements to the Rangers who have already climbed higher into the city.

'Your work has allowed us to gain a foothold in this dreadful city, and we cannot thank you enough.'Pages of a letter can be found scattered across Cirith Ungol. Perhaps you can complete it if you find them all.Ancient pages can be found scattered throughout Cirith Ungol.

