You should talk to Celeborn.Talk to CelebornYou have found what appears to be a page of a letter. It seems quite ancient, written in an elvish script with a deft hand on paper that should have long ago decomposed. Perhaps you can find other pages in Cirith Ungol and complete the story.The story is complete. This letter was clearly written for Galadriel by her husband Celeborn, but you are unsure quite how old it is. Perhaps if you bring it to Celeborn, he will be able to answer your questions.You show Celeborn the ancient pages you found in Cirith Ungol. He looks amused.

'Thousands of years later, a letter sent but never delivered re-appears. Just as the subject of the letter has re-appeared herself. I wrote this in the early days of the Second Age. Thangorodrim had fallen. I, with the aid of the Bright Company, hunted down Morgoth's living servants, of which the spawn of Ungoliant were counted. My request for aid did eventually reach Galadriel, through other means, and the star-glasses received. Ungwetári was bound by the Gilgelair for only a few hundred years, before Sauron came to Mordor and freed her.

'When I return to Lórien, I will deliver this letter to Galadriel. I believe she will be pleased to finally receive it.'Orcs flying the banner of Gothmog have remained behind their fortifications for some time. Dolenthol has asked you to find out more information about the tactical situation in the encampment and report back to him.Dolenthol has asked you to find good vantage points throughout the Orc encampment from which you might listen to Orkish conversation and learn the reason they do not fight each other.Return to Dolenthol and inform him about the conversation you overheard from Gothmog's forces.Talk to Dolenthol'We must gather information about Gothmog's army. It has fortified this location for quite awhile, content not to mount an attack upon the Orc army to the east. I cannot say what the reason might be, but if we were to learn the cause of it we might make some advantage of it.

'Locate several high vantage points and try to overhear their conversation. We might learn the reason for their reluctance!''The Orcs that rally to Gothmog's banner have been ordered not to push an attack of any kind, and to fortify and defend this location instead? Curious, and it would be a shame if they were unable to carry out these orders.

'Perhaps we can find some way to disrupt this plan of theirs!'Supplies are running low in Ugrukhôr's encampment, but they might always run lower....Supplies are running low in Ugrukhôr's encampment, west of Barad Angarth.

You should seek out and destroy the supplies.Destroy Ugrukhôr's supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You destroyed some of the supplies in Ugrukhôr's camp.

You should return to Dolenthol and inform him of your victory.Talk to Dolenthol'Greetings, friend. As you reported, it seems that Ugrukhôr's forces are running low on supplies. If we were to destroy the few supplies that remain, we might sufficiently enrage the Orcs into attacking Gothmog's forces. And wouldn't that be a pity?

'Go forth and destroy the supplies that you find, and we will see if I am right.''With the supplies destroyed, the Orcs become more and more aggressive. In point of fact, they may begin to raid Gothmog's encampment to seize the supplies they now lack!

'Well done, I say. Well done to both of us.'Damrod has asked that you find and support two Rangers that have gone westward into the outer tier of Minas Morgul.Damrod has asked that you assist the Rangers in Zhar Dushgoi.

