Scout several locations within the camp and you may gain additional information about your foe.Scout northern fortifications to the west of Barad AngarthScout central fortifications to the west of Barad AngarthScout southern fortifications to the west of Barad AngarthDolenthol awaits your findings in the field.

You should locate the Ranger and make your report.Talk to Dolenthol'Greetings to you, ${PLAYER}. Your assistance has been most appreciated to this point, but I must ask: are you willing to assist our cause for a little longer?

'I sent Dolenthol ahead to scout the area, but he could use your eyes on this mission as well. Join him and see what further information you might uncover.''Thank you for the information you learned while scouting the fortifications. It seems Ugrukhôr has sent his warriors to this location, and they will become an imminent threat.

'Accept this token of thanks for your work.'Gothmog's forces have built a series of fortifications throughout the area.  Dorgam asked you to destroy them.Barricades inside the city will jeopardize the Rangers' attempts to infiltrate Minas Morgul, and should be destroyed.

Report to Dolenthol when the work is done.Destroy barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Locate Dolenthol and inform him that you destroyed several barricades in the area.Talk to DolentholGothmog’s forces have constructed a series of barricades throughout the area. They will hinder attempts to infiltrate and disrupt the enemy forces within Minas Morgul, and must be destroyed.'Your assistance is most welcome! With these barricades destroyed, it will be easier for our forces to slip without notice past unfriendly eyes.'Orcs under the banner of Ugrukhôr have settled in Zhar Skator. Listening to their conversations may prove beneficial.Ugrukhôr's forces have been engaged in heated conversation west of Barad Angarth. 

You should find a good location to listen to the conversation of Ugrukhôr's warriors.Ugrukhôr's forces have had heated conversations west of Barad Angarth, in Zhar Skator.

You should find a good location from which you might overhear the conversation of Ugrukhôr's warriors.Dolenthol will want to hear what you learned from the Orkish conversations.Talk to Dolenthol'Now that we have made our way into this encampment, we must gather more information about the situation here. What might be their next course of action, and how might we use it to our advantage? If you find locations from which you can overhear their conversation, we might learn a thing or two about the plans of these Orcs.''It is good to hear that many of the Orcs desire to do battle against Gothmog's forces. We should use this information to our advantage.'Dolenthol calls for help to destroy the caches of Morgul steel blades that can be found throughout the Circle of Sorrow.Morgul blades can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.

You should destroy any Morgul blades that you find.Destroy Morgul blades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dolenthol can be found in Barad Orhant.

You should talk to Dolenthol.Talk to Dolenthol in Barad Orhant'The Nazgûl had formidable blades made out of Morgul steel, a terrible ore found here in the Vale. I have seen the Dead in Minas Morgul, wielding those same blades. You know as well as I that these dangerous weapons must be destroyed. Let us search the Circle of Sorrow for such weapons and dispose of them.''It concerns me that we fought the merrevail while we sought to destroy the Morgul blades. Are they tasked with stealing the blades from the Dead or did they make a pact of some sort with them? We should investigate this matter further.'Some of the Rangers of Ithilien have taken ill as Arodor frantically searches for a remedy to this strange Morgul ailment.Medicine can be found in Barad Orhant.

You should gather medicine for the ailing Rangers.Gather medicine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sick Rangers can be found in Barad Orhant.

You should treat the sick Rangers.Arodor can be found in Barad Orhant.

You should talk to Arodor.Talk to Arodor in Barad Orhant'There is an urgent matter to which we must attend. As we press further into the Dead City, some of the Rangers have taken ill. At first it was a trifle of an illness, but now, some Rangers are unable to perform their duties. I believe something noisome is to blame, be it the flowers or mushrooms, or some other sinister growth.

'We must devise some remedy. Let me think on this while you gather what medicinal supplies we brought into the city. Quickly now, see to those ailing Rangers!''Thank you for treating some of the Rangers. This is but a temporary solution. I would not be surprised if more of us also fall victim to this Morgul ailment. We must search for a remedy.'Some of the Rangers of Ithilien have taken ill as Arodor continues his search for a remedy to this strange Morgul ailment.Resilient mould, glimmering salt, and Agarnaith fruit can all be found in Minas Morgul.

You should recover these ingredients.Find a bit of resilient mould (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find a speck of glimmering salt (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find some Agarnaith fruit (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A mortar and pestle can be found at Barad Orhant.

You should grind up the ingredients.A mortar and pestle can be found at Barad Orhant.

