<rgb=#FF0000>It is recommended to have the quest The Circle of Wrath underway.</rgb>Secure the towerTalk to one of the Rangers.Talk to one of the RangersBarad Orhant, otherwise known as the Tower of the Treegarth, must be captured in order to enter the Circle of Sorrow and reclaim Minas Morgul.'We have secured the tower!'Dolenthol needs your help to find and confront the vile wraith who commands the Dead in Minas Morgul.Talk to Dolenthol.Talk to DolentholKeep close to Dolenthol and remain alert.Keep close to Dolenthol and remain alert<rgb=#FF0000>Dolenthol must survive</rgb>Defeat Thargaun and the Morroval.Defeat ThargaunDefeat the Morroval<rgb=#FF0000>Dolenthol must survive</rgb>'Thargaun is not truly defeated. I saw a true death on Pelennor with the defeat of the Witch King. No, something else keeps Thargaun bound here. It is a deeply fell sorcery.''They are nearby. We must be careful so as not to alert Thargaun to our presence.'Dolenthol calls for aid in finding and confronting the vile wraith who commands the Dead in Minas Morgul.Dolenthol can be found in Barad Orhant.

You should talk to Dolenthol.Talk to Dolenthol in Barad OrhantDolenthol can be found in Barad Orhant.

You should talk to Dolenthol.Talk to Dolenthol in Barad Orhant'Since we came to the Circle of Sorrow, I have felt as if something were watching all of us. When drowsiness takes me I hear whispered voices and a single name. The name is "Thargaun."'

You tell Dolenthol that you have also heard this name before but it was not in a dream. It was the rumour of an alliance between someone called Thargaun and the vile kergrim of Imlad Morgul.

'Thargaun may be the one who commands the Dead in Minas Morgul. If he were willing to make a pact with such creatures as the vile kergrim, a pact with the merrevail could be just as likely. We must seek out this Thargaun and put a stop to his plans.''Thargaun is near. The darkness grows as he approaches. Let us find him, and quickly!''We have thwarted Thargaun's plans concerning the merrevail. I believe the winged beasts will need to be dealt with, and soon. Their numbers are many and more flock to Minas Morgul each day.'Away from the Shrouded Forge, the Dead take the path that is forced upon them.Fell path-finders can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.

You should defeat any fell path-finders that you find.Defeat fell path-finders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated many fell path-finders in Minas Morgul.CompletedAway from the Shrouded Forge, the Dead take the path that is forced upon them. Fell path-finders follow the stream of spirits to their destination, allowing nothing to stand in their way. You should defeat these path-finders to allow the Rangers of Ithilien to move about the city with fewer worries.You have defeated many fell path-finders in the Circle of Sorrow. The Rangers of Ithilien will be pleased with your efforts.Damrod wishes to gather the pendants of Cargûl who wander the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.Cargûl can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.

You should collect pendants from them as they fall.Collect Cargûl pendants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Damrod can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul.

You should bring the pendants collected from the Cargûl to Damrod.'Dolenthol tells me that the merrevail are grasping anything they found throughout the Circle of Sorrow, and winging them away for some foul but unknown purpose. Now, I have seen Cargûl wearing vile pendants, and I think we should keep them from the clutching talons of the merrevail. Find them and bring them back to me, and I will destroy them.''I thank you for these, ${PLAYER}. I will have these vile pendants destroyed immediately. You have done the Rangers of Ithilien a great service.'Damrod wishes to patrol the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul to assess the difficulties that the Rangers of Ithilien will have to overcome.Damrod has asked you to scout the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.Find Búrzangh, the Shrouded ForgeFind Dâr Grazadh, the Hall of RotFind the Song-house of LindalírëScout the western side of the Circle of SorrowScout the north-eastern side of the Circle of SorrowScout the north-western side of the Circle of SorrowDamrod can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul.

You should talk to Damrod.Talk to Damrod in Barad Orhant'You are truly an experienced ${CLASS}, and no stranger to adventure or danger. This is why I ask you to scout the Circle of Sorrow for us. We must learn what difficulties we are to face and what obstacles we must overcome. Search the many places and buildings upon the Circle of Sorrow, and then report back to me with whatever you have learned.''You have learned a great deal about the Circle of Sorrow... and most of it unpleasant. It would seem all these locations, the Hall of Rot, the Shrouded Forge, and the Song-house, all work together to procure a legion of the Dead to serve Minas Morgul. I will send Rangers to these locations with the hope that this plan will be thwarted.'Damrod wishes to gather the sigils of the gaunt-men who wander the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.Gaunt-men can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.

You should collect their sigils from them as they fall.Collect gaunt-man sigils (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Damrod can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul.

You should bring the gaunt-man sigils to Damrod.'I have heard the accounts from Dolenthol that merrevail have been seen collecting blades made of Morgul steel from the Circle of Sorrow. I would not be surprised if the merrevail also seek other trinkets of evil within the city. I have seen the gaunt-men carry terrible sigils with them. We should search out and destroy these sigils before the merrevail are able to get them.''I thank you, ${PLAYER}. I will have these vile sigils destroyed immediately. You have done the Rangers of Ithilien a great service, but I suppose that is nothing new. All the same, thank you once again.'Damrod wishes to defeat the many shades and spirits that haunt the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.Shades and fell spirits can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.

You should defeat any shades and fell spirits that you find.Defeat shades in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat fell spirits in Minas Morgul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Damrod can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul.

You should talk to Damrod.Talk to Damrod in Barad Orhant'We must lessen the numbers of fell spirits who wander upon the Circle of Sorrow. I ask you to defeat any of the spirits and shades that you see as you venture out into Minas Morgul. Beware, for they are treacherous and will seek to do you harm!''You have done the Rangers of Ithilien a great service, but there is still more to be done if we are to cleanse the shadow from this corrupted city.'Dolenthol calls for aid in purging the fell sorcery that continues to infect the old song-house of Lindalírë.The Song-house of Lindalírë can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.

You should free the bound spirits held within the theatre.Dolenthol can be found near the Song-house of Lindalírë.

You should talk to Dolenthol.Talk to Dolenthol near the Song-house of Lindalírë'The paths of the spirits travel to the old Song-house of Lindalírë. There they are tortured and corrupted, by what I do not know and cannot say. We should travel to the old song-house and free those who have yet to be taken by the sorcery of Minas Morgul. We must be careful, for the Circle of Sorrow is full of ghastly horrors!''${PLAYER}, over here, let us rest a moment!

'I must speak to you about something, and perhaps you already have your suspicions about me. I would expect no less from an old friend like you!'

The gruffness in Dolenthol's voice departs.

'It is your friend, Éowyn.'

She briefly reveals her face to you, confirming that she speaks the truth.

'I thought to insist to Faramir that I travel to the Morgul Vale with him, but decided otherwise at the realization that he would be overcome with worry for my safety. What preoccupations does the arrival of love bring to the hearts of men! He must focus on his own task, and not on the safety of his beloved. As at Pelennor, I have come in secret! Until now, the Rangers believe me to be only a new and eager recruit. I reveal this to you because I know you will keep my secret.'Dolenthol calls for aid in purging the fell sorcery that enwreathes the Circle of Sorrow.Moon Tower wraiths can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.

You should defeat the Moon Tower wraiths and sever their shackles.Defeat the Moon Tower wraiths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dolenthol can be found in Barad Orhant.

You should talk to Dolenthol.Talk to Dolenthol in Barad Orhant'Good ${CLASS}, may I have a word with you? We have accomplished much upon the Circle of Wrath together. Perhaps it best if we continue our work upon this Circle of Sorrow.

'I believe there is still good to be found in this corrupted city. Take for example the walking wraiths who were once guarding the Tower of the Crescent Moon in Minas Ithil. They serve darkness only because they know not their past. We should lay to rest these guards, so they can find peace. Do you agree with this plan, ${PLAYER}?''The old guards have been laid to rest, and slowly Minas Ithil is restored. Still there is much more to do upon this Circle of Sorrow, my friend.'Arodor wishes to learn more about the Morgul-sheen, the strange glow of the Dead City.Dust of Morgul-sheen can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.

You should gather dust of Morgul-sheen.Gather dust of Morgul-sheen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arodor can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul.

You should bring the dust to Arodor.'Now that the most pressing task is dealt with, I can now continue to study the strange sorcery that envelops these lands.

'I wish to learn more about the glow of the Dead City, the Morgul-sheen. Would you search the Circle of Sorrow for dust of the same colour as the Morgul-sheen? Perhaps a study of this dust will help us to learn more about the sorcery and the glow both.''What fascinating dust you have given to me, ${PLAYER}. It is not unlike the dust that gathers upon the furniture of an abandoned house, but see how it glows.'

Arodor throws a small bit into the air.

'Look! It does not catch the slight breeze in here, but floats, as if it were bound by some other force! It may take time, but I will continue to study the Morgul-sheen. You have my word.'Dornach leads the effort to reclaim the Circle of Despair, once known as the Circle of Mirth, from the forces of Gothmog in Minas Morgul.Dornach can be found in the Circle of Despair.

