<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.</rgb>Aid Dornach and complete 'The Will of Ugrukhôr'Aid Dornach and complete 'Tears of Minas Ithil'Dornach can be found in the Circle of Despair.

You are aiding Dornach in securing the Circle of Despair.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.</rgb>Aid Dornach and complete 'Unstilled Waters'Dornach has returned to Barad Arthir.

After securing the Circle of Despair, Dornach asked you to meet him and Candúr in Barad Arthir. You should return to them.Meet Dornach in Barad Arthir'Once this was the Circle of Mirth, ${PLAYER}, but it does not seem so now. There are strange things afoot in this Circle of Despair.

'I saw Ugrukhôr's Orcs quail before shades of the Dead, and I do not blame them. Something terrible has happened here, for the Dead cackle and weep in equal measure. Those that laugh seem the cruelest spirits, and those that cry seem fearful even in death.

'If some knowledge of Ugrukhôr's plans can be gleaned from these Orcs, I will consider our efforts fruitful, but I would much like to know what terrible fate has befallen these shades of Gondor.'Pale, twisted roots of an unknown lineage grow within the Garth of Angáth and threaten the unwary.Twisted pale-roots can be found in the Garth of Angáth in the Circle of Despair.Burn twisted-pale roots in the Garth of AngáthTwisted pale-roots can be found in the Garth of Angáth in the Circle of Despair.

You have encountered twisted pale-roots in the Garth of Angáth and should burn them, lest their corruption linger in Minas Morgul.Burn twisted-pale roots in the Garth of Angáth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})As you explore the Garth of Angáth, you notice a number of pale, twisted roots thrashing in the gardens.

These white roots seem a twisted mockery of the White Tree of Gondor, but it is unlikely they possess such a lineage as the seedling of Nimloth, which once grew tall and mighty in Minas Ithil and was burned many years ago.

Even so, you would be wise to set flame to these wild roots and put an end to the vile creations of the Nazgûl.Stained merrevail have invaded Minas Morgul and taken over the Circle of Madness.Stained merrevail have taken over the third tier in Minas Morgul, the Circle of Madness.

