Candúr has asked you to travel to Taen Orwath and aid the Rangers of Ithilien preparing to venture into Thuringwath.Travel to Taen OrwathCuilion can be found at Taen Orwath.

One of the Rangers at Taen Orwath appears to have been awaiting your arrival. You should talk to Cuilion.Talk to Cuilion'I have received troubling news from Taen Orwath.

'It seems that Gothmog had plans beyond Minas Morgul. Word has spread of a place named Thuringwath. It is believed that the deathly cleft, Falch Gurth, that runs through the Mountains of Shadow might lead to it.

'I do not know what might be found in Thuringwath, but from what I have heard, it is nothing good. We have twice-walked bravely through the lands of the Enemy, my friend, but something about this leaves me uneasy. What need has evil to conceal itself in the lands of the Dark Lord?

'When you are prepared, ride for Taen Orwath. I hope my dread is for naught, ${PLAYER}.''I'd hoped it would be you, ${PLAYER}.'<rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers.</rgb><rgb=#00e4ff>This deed is for Legendary Servers</rgb>Adventure to Level 130While you worked to secure the Circle of Despair, Prince Faramir led a company of Rangers of Ithilien into the Circle of Death.You should complete quests in the Circle of Death and aid Faramir in his plans.Complete quests in the Circle of Death (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aid Prince Faramir in 'A Waxing Moon'Candúr can be found in Barad Arthir.

You have aided Prince Faramir and secured the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul.Talk to Candúr in Barad Arthir'While you worked to secure the Circle of Despair, we worked to fortify the defences of Barad Arthir.

'It is unlikely Gothmog will be able to muster enough forces to breach the walls of the tower, but I have seen more surprising things in my time. We shall remain vigilant.

'After you left the tower, Prince Faramir led his company into the Circle of Death. I believe the Prince means to prepare a final assault against Gothmog, but he has kept his plans hidden... even from me.

'Once you have secured the Circle of Despair, please return to me.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}, and I hear Prince Faramir has changed his mind regarding the Dead City.

'It would be a shame to let Minas Ithil fall to its final ruin by the hand of Gondor, I think. It is good he believes so as well.

'These are glad tidings, but alas, there is another matter to discuss.'Thuringwath, the Valley of Secret Shadow, has remained hidden among the slopes of Ephel Dúath since the Second Age of the world.Mithrandir can be found in Falch Gurth.

Mithrandir has asked you to accompany him into Thuringwath. You should talk to Mithrandir when you are prepared.Talk to MithrandirMithrandir can be found in Thuringwath.

You have passed through Falch Gurth into Thuringwath with Mithrandir. You should talk to Mithrandir.Talk to Mithrandir in Thuringwath'I am told that beyond this darkness lies Thuringwath, the Valley of Secret Shadow.

'It is difficult to believe the Enemy could have hidden such a place so near to Minas Ithil of old, but it is that uncertainty which has led me here.

'Have the Enemy's works crumbled to naught behind a veil of shadow? Or does some evil still dwell beneath the notice of Gondor?

'I must know the truth of it, but I do not wish to walk alone. Will you accompany me, ${PLAYER}?''Come, ${PLAYER}.''It is worse than I feared, ${PLAYER}.'After repelling many of Ugrukhôr's forces, the Rangers of Ithilien saw one of his Uruk-hai make for Bâr Maenath.Bâr Maenath can be found in the western reaches of the Circle of Death.

Maendal has asked you to track one of Ugrukhôr's Uruks into Bâr Maenath and defeat it.Enter Bâr MaenathThe trail of blood leads through Bâr Maenath.

You discovered a puddle of black blood trailing off into Bâr Maenath. You should follow it and defeat the Uruk that escaped Maendal and his men.Follow the trail of black blood through Bâr MaenathYou have found Ugrukhôr's uruk slain in Bâr Maenath.Completed'Dolenthol sent you?

'A few of us have some minor injuries, but we'll be back on our feet soon enough.

'It was Ugrukhôr's Orcs that waylaid us, all right. Look at them... none of the Morgul-pallor that you'd see in Gothmog's Orcs. One of his uruks ran into the old treasury rather than fight us off, but I'm not keen on letting it catch us by surprise once it catches its breath.

'We'll go rejoin the Prince's company, but you ought to search Bâr Maenath and make sure that uruk's not going to trouble us anymore!'The Rangers of Ithilien need not fear the return of this uruk, but Ugrukhôr's forces still swell within the Dead City.Within Aufaltor, many rune-inscribed urns of shadow rest among the Dead. Mithrandir may have an interest in them, for historical record.Rune-inscribed urns can be found at Aufaltor in Thuringwath.Collect rune-inscribed urns at AufaltorRune-inscribed urns can be found at Aufaltor in Thuringwath.

You have discovered numerous urns bearing runic inscriptions in Aufaltor. You should collect a number of them for Mithrandir.Collect rune-inscribed urns at Aufaltor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected many rune-inscribed urns at Aufaltor.Within Aufaltor, many rune-inscribed urns of shadow rest among the Dead. The urns are not of Gondorian-make, and though you can not read the runes, you shudder as your mind inevitably wanders to imagining whatever profane rituals the previous residents here may have carried out.

The vile inscriptions they bear may be of interest to Mithrandir.You stow the rune-inscribed urns.

Once your exploration of Thuringwath is finished, you plan to deliver them to Mithrandir.A small company of Rangers of Ithilien passed through what Taurdir described as a 'wall of shadow' in Falch Gurth.The 'wall of shadow' can be found to the south of Torgris in Falch Gurth.

