Mithrandir has asked you to cast a stone into the shadows of Falch Gurth. You should pick up a nearby stone and cast it into the darkness.Cast a stone into the shadows of Falch GurthMithrandir can be found within Falch Gurth.

After casting a stone into the shadows of Thuringwath, it appears to be gone from the world. You should talk to Mithrandir.Talk to Mithrandir'We didn't make it far the first night.

'A dark cloud, like some unearthly wall of shadow, appeared in our path. Only Nidhlas was brave enough to reach out into the darkness, but he withdrew his hand almost at once. It was as if a deathly chill had taken hold of his arm!

'I thought that was going to be the end of it, but Nidhlas insisted that we make camp... and so we did. The rain fell cold, and we had too few tents. Many of us took ill in the night, but Nidhlas led the rest beyond the shadows at first light.

'See for yourself, ${PLAYER}. It is some old devilry, I think!''It is most curious, is it not?'

Mithrandir does not turn to face you, and his eyes remain transfixed on the 'wall of shadow' Taurdir described.

'As I expected, the enwreathment spells the Nazgûl used to conceal the pass have faded. But, I did not expect to encounter this sort of sorcery.

'May I ask something of you, ${PLAYER}? It might seem a trifle, but take a stone and cast it into the shadows.''Hmmph.'

Mithrandir turns to face you.

'It is no mistake that our paths have crossed again, my friend.'Nagli Want-kin has many duties at Khadâsh-gâra, not the least of which is caring for his beloved aurochs, Lapis.A bucket of water can be found along the Greylin near Khadâsh-gâra.

Nagli Want-kin has asked you to aid him in bathing his beloved aurochs, Lapis. You should fetch a bucket of water as he asked and use it to bathe Lapis.Pick up the bucket of water by the GreylinNagli Want-kin can be found at Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade.

You have bathed Lapis and she seems to be very happy about it. You should talk to Nagli.Talk to Nagli Want-kin'Do you see that aurochs over there? That's Lapis!

'She's been with me ever since I set off on my own. One of my favourite parts of my day is giving Lapis a bath. Why don't you give it a try today instead?

'Fetch the bucket I left down by the Greylin and bring it back here. Then... just douse her with water! It's that simple.''Now I know it seems a bit crude, but trust me, she loves it!

'I hope you enjoyed that little bit of fun!'Sorrow has overtaken Váko, who cannot bring himself to find his fallen brother's axe.Váko has asked you to help him recover his brother's axe. Taking the axe may catch the attention of the Orc Borbák.

The axe can be found somewhere in Dursh Hûl.Reclaim the dwarf-axeDefeat Borbák the ShearerBorbák has been defeated and the dwarf-axe reclaimed.

You should return the axe to Váko in Amdân. He waits for you in the Zhélruka camp.'You nearly gave me a scare. It was foolish of you to sneak up on me in enemy territory; I thought you were an Orc.

'No matter, it is not your fault I have tarried here. There is an Orc that I seek, Borbák -- a vile creature who dragged my brother into Dursh Hûl and cut off his beard before... before...

'I-I cannot muster the courage I need to enter the camp. I do not know what business you have in that accursed place, but please find his axe. It is of dwarf-make, easy to spot among the Orcs' filth. Take it, and I'm sure Borbák will make himself known.

'I shall return to Amdân in the meantime and wait in the Zhélruka camp.''You found my brother's axe and avenged him? This means more to me than you know.

'My brother's body is lost, but his axe I will leave here, in memory of him. It is not much, but it is enough.'The War of Three Peaks has begun!Zudramdân can be found in Elderslade.

