He will want to hear about the Angmarim orders you found.'Soon after we began investigating Gáfin's death, scouts reported Angmarim activity nearby. The Angmarim appear to be searching for something, but can't venture close enough without meeting the pointy end of a dwarf-blade. They're too craven to attack us openly, but they aren't welcome!

'I'd wager a couple have settled themselves behind Annâk-khurfu, while others watch the path leading up here. You won't have to look far. Find out why they're skulking around -- while getting rid of them, of course.''The Trév Dúvardain -- the Hill-men who ally with Angmar? Aye, I can see now why Aighrig would shroud her actions from us. Still, if the Angmarim are hunting her down, her alliances are clear. We ought to help her.'Defeat many beasts in Câr Bronach.Defeat many beasts in Câr Bronach.Defeat many beasts in Câr BronachDefeat many beasts in Câr Bronach.Defeat many beasts in Câr Bronach.Defeat many beasts in Câr BronachAzhorns crush enemies upon the battlefield and must be dealt with in order to win this war.Azhorns can be found upon the battlefield.

