<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will swiftly travel to Khur Azan when you advance this quest.</rgb>Glóin has made his decision: he must send message-ravens to Skarháld and to the Lonely Mountain bearing word of this new Lord of Gundabad.Runerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge in the village of Limlók.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in LimlókThe box of scrolls is near the task board in Limlók.Take some small parchments from the box of scrollsGlóin is in the centre of the village, preparing his ravens to carry messages to Skarháld and the Lonely Mountain.Find Glóin and his ravens in the centre of LimlókGlóin is in the centre of the village, preparing his ravens to carry messages to Skarháld and the Lonely Mountain.A young Beorning child stands nearby, fascinated by Glóin and the messenger-ravens.Talk to VídarYrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.

According to her son Vídar, Yrsa has tasked him with scouting outside the village once a week.Talk to Yrsa Spearwife in LimlókYrsa told you to scout the wild lands south of Limlók with her son Vídar. You will find the Beorning boy at one of three different spots: to the south-east, south, or south-west of the village.Talk to Vídar at one of his three favourite scouting locationsYrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.Talk to Yrsa Spearwife in LimlókThe dwarves have gathered behind Runerik and Yrsa's lodge to release the messenger-ravens.Find the dwarves behind Runerik and Yrsa's lodgeImák is behind Runerik's lodge to watch the release of the messenger-ravens.Talk to Imák behind Runerik's lodgeThe messenger-ravens will bear word of the new Lord of Gundabad to Durin at Skarháld and to King Thorin in the Lonely Mountain.Watch the departure of the messenger-ravensRunerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge in the village of Limlók.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge in Limlók'I am troubled by this news that Gorgar, brother of Mazog, now rules in Gundabad, but do not mistake me! I do not fear him. The line from which he springs has long troubled Durin's Folk, but have we not laughed last in every case? We are not unprepared to deal with Gorgar, now that we know we must.

'We must send messages to Durin in Skarháld and to King Thorin at the Lonely Mountain, warning them of Gundabad's new leader. It is for this very purpose I brought messenger-ravens with me on this journey, ${PLAYER}, though I did not guess at the content of the messages they needs must bear!

'Will you ask Runerik for some parchment upon which I can write these messages of warning? I brought the birds, it is true, but I seem to have left my papers behind.''Will you ask Runerik for some parchment upon which I can write these messages of warning? I brought the birds, it is true, but I seem to have left my papers behind.''I do not understand why your friend is so concerned about the one called "Gorgar the Ruthless." One Orc is much the same as any other, in my experience and that of my kind.

'But I can spare some parchment for him to write the frightened warnings he wants to send back home. There is a box of paper near the task board, and my people use its contents to post requests and other messages on the board. You can give him some parchment from that box, if you must.''There is a box of parchment near the task board, and the people of Limlók use its contents to post requests and other messages on the board. You can give him some parchment from that box, if you must.''Did you find the parchment you needed?'Glóin is focused on preparing the ravens. He has not noticed you.'Ah, these will do nicely, thank you. I need to decide how to phrase this message, and then copy it onto each of these papers. I need to...'

Glóin looks up with barely-disguised irritation.

'I need to concentrate, and this child has peppered me with questions ever since I began! Yes, yes, I told you once! This one is Vaka, and this one is Telgja. Their names mean Vigilant and Cutter, if you must know.'

Glóin masters his tone, and speaks again to you.

'And this one here is Hjála, which means Chatter, and I daresay he and this Beorning child have much in common! Can you keep this child entertained while I prepare these messages, ${PLAYER}? I need to think, and these constant questions are not helping!''I need to think, and these constant questions are not helping!''Do they fly very high? How do they know where to go? What's the farthest they've ever flown before?'

Vídar pauses for air, and you manage to interject a question. The child considers it briefly.

'Have I any chores that need doing? Well, yes, I suppose. I am nearly a man grown, after all, and Mother says it is my job to scout outside Limlók once a week. I will go do that now, if you will let her know! You have already met her, yes? Her name is Yrsa.

'All right, I am leaving now. But I want to learn more about the ravens when I get back!''I am almost ready to go!''It is true, I told Vídar that as he grows into a man he must shoulder further duties around the village. That includes scouting the wilderness outside Limlók, but I did not expect him to choose to do so immediately after an attack by an Orc raiding-party!

'He has always been a bold boy. I should have expected it, after all! Perhaps you can ease a mother's worries by finding him on his patrol and ensuring he does not run into harm? There are three places he enjoys to scout, to the south-east, south, and south-west of the village. Look for him at one of these locations and safe-guard Vídar, and I will remember your good-hearted assistance.

'It will also keep him out from underfoot your dwarves, which I know they will appreciate. Vídar always has so many questions.''Find Vídar on his patrol and ensure he does not run into harm. There are three places he enjoys to scout, to the south-east, south, and south-west of the village. Look for him at one of these locations and safe-guard Vídar, and I will remember your good-hearted assistance.'The bear cub snorts in your direction, but you cannot guess at its meaning. Is this Vídar? You hope so, both for your sake and his!'Vídar returned and spoke of your prowess! Thank you for keeping an eye on him, ${PLAYER}.'

You are relieved to learn that the bear cub was Yrsa's son Vídar after all. On the journey back to Limlók you had not been entirely certain.

'Your friends have gathered behind the lodge to release the messenger-ravens. You should join them.''Your friends have gathered behind the lodge to release the messenger-ravens. You should join them.''Are they ready or not? What is the delay?''The messages are sent. Now it is up to the Longbeards to do what must be done. I will decide for myself whether to continue with this endeavour.''The ravens have been sent? Fine, fine.'

Runerik's brows crease with a new thought.

'I should have read the messages before your dwarf friend released the ravens. He has not called an entire company of dwarves here, has he?'All dwarves everywhere are threatened by the presence of a new Lord of Gundabad. Glóin's warning must reach them!Glóin is behind Runerik's lodge, and from there you heard a great commotion. What has happened?Talk to Glóin behind Runerik's lodgeSome of the ravens were shot from the sky by Orc archers! You have to retrieve them from the White Mare and learn if any of Glóin's messages escaped the Floodfells.Venko is at the north-western point of the White Mare.Talk to Venko at the north-western point of the White MareSome unexpected visitors have come north-west of the White Mare, across the river from your dwarf companions. Why have they followed you here?Confront the unexpected visitors north-west of the White Mare, across the riverRunerik stands before some of his assembled people north-west of the White Mare, and demands to speak with you.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard north-west of the White MareFlood-broom can be found alongside rivers and streams throughout the Floodfells. Runerik also wants his wife Yrsa to examine unspent arrows carried by Orcs in the area, and has asked you to collect some.Collect flood-broom by rivers in the Floodfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect unspent arrows from Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Yrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.Runerik Knotbeard will meet you inside the lodge to treat the injured messenger-ravens.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard inside his lodge in LimlókRunerik has prepared a pot of boiling water in the north room, and he wants you to add the flood-broom you collected to it.The flood-broom will take some time to steep in the boiling water.Wait for the flood-broom tea to properly steepThe flood-broom tea is now prepared, and waits for you to bring it to Runerik.Collect the flood-broom tea inside Runerik's lodgeRunerik is inside his lodge, tending to the wounded messenger-ravens.'I have been more than welcoming up to this point, but if a whole troop of dwarves come to Limlók....'

Runerik's further complaint is halted by the sound of sudden commotion behind the lodge.

'What is that noise? Your companions do not sound pleased about something, ${PLAYER}.''What was that noise? Your companions do not sound pleased about something.''We have a problem, ${PLAYER}. As my ravens flew above the White Mare on their errand, arrows sped from the ground and brought them down! I do not know if any of my birds survived this assault, or if any of the messages will reach their destinations.

'Go to the White Mare, north of here, and recover the fallen ravens. We must know which of them did not escape the Orkish volley.''Go to the White Mare, north of here, and recover the fallen ravens. We must know which of them did not escape the Orkish volley.''We are being watched. No, not by Orcs.

'They are to the north-west, across the river. Go see what they want, ${PLAYER}.

'I don't like it.''Why have they come here? I do not like it.''Your ravens... do they still live?'

Runerik gently takes the birds from you and sniffs their wounds.

'They are grievously wounded, and will die if they are not treated. But I understand one of the ravens escaped the arrows of the Orcs, and winged away with the message it bore? Does your interest in these poor creatures then end? They are of no more use to you; do you then discard them?'

You make clear that you want to heal Hjála and Vaka of their hurts, if you can.

'If this is true, you will collect some of the herb we call flood-broom. It grows beside rivers and streams in the Floodfells, and possesses healing properties that may help. Collect too some unspent arrows from the Orcs. My wife will inspect them back in Limlók, and she may learn from them something of which I can make use when healing these ravens.''If you wish to aid your injured, you will collect some of the herb we call flood-broom. It grows beside rivers and streams in the Floodfells, and possesses healing properties that may help. Collect too some unspent arrows from the Orcs. My wife will inspect them back in Limlók, and she may learn from them something of which I can make use when healing these ravens.''You brought me some arrows from the Orcs? Let me see them.'

Yrsa inspects the arrows, sniffing the arrowhead and grimacing.

'Yes, these are coated with a thin poison. It is not enough for such foes to injure or maim, they seek to attack their enemies from the inside as well! My husband instructed you to gather flood-broom? That tells me he suspected poison, for that herb has effectively treated such vile substances for us before. But it is good to know for certain.

'He has brought your birds inside the lodge. Find him there and tell him the arrows used by the Orcs in this area are poisoned, as he believed.''My husband brought your birds inside the lodge. Find him there and tell him the arrows used by the Orcs in this area are poisoned, as he believed.''I will meet you inside.''Poison? Yes, I thought so.

'I have set some water boiling by the fire in the north room. Add the flood-broom to it and let it steep for a little while.

'You did gather the flood-broom, did you not?''I will feed this tea to the ravens, and with luck it may halt the poison. I have done what else I could for them, and with rest it is to be hoped they will recover.

'I am pleased you did not abandon these creatures when they were of no more use to you. I admit I expected worse of you, and of your dwarf allies.'Runerik thinks you may be able to develop one of your latent abilities, and wants you to consult with his wife Yrsa for further instruction along that line.Yrsa is inside the lodge, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Yrsa Spearwife inside her lodgeYrsa has asked you to try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> her skills.<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Yrsa Spearwife inside the lodgeYrsa is inside the lodge, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Yrsa Spearwife inside her lodgePractice makes perfect! Yrsa has asked you to once again try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> her skills.Once again <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Yrsa Spearwife inside the lodgeYrsa is inside the lodge, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Yrsa Spearwife inside her lodgeYrsa has asked you to try and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Glóin's skills. The old dwarf should be somewhere outside in Limlók.Find Glóin in Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skillsGlóin is in Limlók, wondering why you have been studying him so closely.Talk to Glóin in LimlókGlóin wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Imák's skills. Imák is on the western side of Limlók.Find Imák on the western side of Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skillsImák is in Limlók, and he wants to know why you have subjected him to such scrutiny.Talk to Imák in LimlókImák wants you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Venko's skills. Venko is by the south-east entrance of Limlók.Find Venko by the south-east entrance to Limlók and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> his skillsVenko is in Limlók, and he is suspicious of the recent attention you have given him.Talk to Venko in LimlókThe real test of your appraisal ability will be to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge.<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> Runerik Knotbeard outside the lodgeRunerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge and interested to know your appraisal of his skills.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge in Limlók'Are you surprised to learn I possess such skill in the healing arts and mastery of herb-lore? You should not be. Were you to exercise your powers of observation, you should be able to discern such skills in others. Indeed, I believe it is a latent ability you already possess.

'Yrsa can tell you more. Consider such training as she can provide a repayment for aiding my son Vídar with his chores. Aye, he told me you were an able fighter, and was pleased to have the company.

'My wife came inside to inquire about the ravens. Find her in the other room and see what she can teach you.''My wife came inside to inquire about the ravens. Find her in the other room and see what she can teach you.''You wish to learn the art of appraisal, by which you may determine the skills and abilities of the people you meet? It is not difficult to learn the basics, but it does take some practice if you are to become a master of observation. The trick is to relax your eye and consider every aspect of your subject as a unified whole: every detail is in some way related to the larger sum that is your subject.

'Try it on me, ${PLAYER}. Look at me and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> my skills, and I will tell you if you succeed to my satisfaction.''Try it on me, ${PLAYER}. Look at me and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> my skills, and I will tell you if you succeed to my satisfaction.'Yrsa waits for your assessment of her skills and abilities. You consider what you have learned.

<u>Yrsa Spearwife, Beorning Woman of Limlók</u>
<rgb=#FFFF00>Skin-changing:</rgb> 95
<rgb=#FFFF00>Observation:</rgb> 90

She sighs as your provide your account, but there is humour in it.

'You say I have great skill at skin-changing? Whatever gave you that idea? Ah, it is only a jest. Try it once again, and perhaps you can notice details you missed before. The signs are there for one who knows what to seek. <rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> me once again, and concentrate.''Try once more, and perhaps you will notice details you missed before. The signs are there for one who knows what to seek. <rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> me once again, and concentrate.'Yrsa waits patiently for your second assessment. You consider what you have learned.

<u>Yrsa Spearwife, Beorning Woman of Limlók</u>
<rgb=#FFFF00>Skin-changing:</rgb> 95
<rgb=#FFFF00>Observation:</rgb> 90
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 80
<rgb=#FFFF00>Resolve:</rgb> 90

She nods, pleased at your success.

'You have done well, ${PLAYER}, and will improve with time and practice! Why not try this on your dwarf friends next? If they are like others I have known, they will be interested in your appraisal of their talents. You may find it useful to learn of their strengths and weaknesses, as well, for there is little doubt that danger still lies ahead of you all.

'After you have done that, perhaps you can impress my husband with your newfound talent.''Why not try this on your dwarf friends next? If they are like others I have known, they will be interested in your appraisal of their talents. You may find it useful to learn of their strengths and weaknesses, as well.''Yes? To what do I owe such scrutiny?'

<u>Glóin, Hero of the Lonely Mountain</u>
<rgb=#FFFF00>Axe-wielding:</rgb> 80
<rgb=#FFFF00>Fire-making:</rgb> 95
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hardiness:</rgb> 90
