<rgb=#FF0000>This quest can be completed weekly.</rgb>'I must thank you once again for all that you do for us. Those are all the Motes I have for now. Perhaps I will have more soon.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Completing this quest will remove 30 Copper Coins of Gundabad.</rgb>Mother Amma needs more crystals to study.Howlers' Notch is north-west of Annâk-khurfu.

Mother Amma has asked you to collect more of the fell crystals.Collect strange crystals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mother Amma is in the forge at Annâk-khurfu, in southern Elderslade.

You should bring the crystals to Mother Amma.Talk to Mother AmmaThe chest is located near the forge at Annâk-khurfu.

Mother Amma has asked you to place the foul smelling crystals in a chest.Mother Amma is in the forge at Annâk-khurfu.

You should talk to Mother Amma.Talk to Mother AmmaGunvald is in Annâk-khurfu.

Mother Amma has asked you to pass a message along to Gunvald.Talk to GunvaldMother Amma is in the forge of Annâk-khurfu.

Gunvald has asked you to give his thanks to Mother Amma.Return to Mother Amma'My initial examination of the crystal you brought me is troubling, ${PLAYER}. We need to learn more, but I require a larger amount to study.

'I have heard tell of more of these fell stones in the Warg camp, Howlers' Notch. Bring me what you find, that we might uncover their secrets.''Ugh. I thought I was accustomed to the stench of these rocks by now, but with so many in one place it is nearly overwhelming.

'Ah, yes. These stones hold even more of the corruption than the first you brought hither. I suppose that explains the... enhanced smell.

'Put them into that chest there, will you? That should help keep the fumes contained while I study each one.''Whew! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. That was worse than sour sulfur.

'I shall need some time to examine the crystals you brought. Go now and tell Gunvald to keep his scouts away from these abominations, then return to me.''I was wondering what that smell was. Thank you for the information, ${PLAYER}. I will let my scouts know to give these crystals a wide berth. Please thank Mother Amma for me.''That Gunvald is a solid rock. Always has the proper amount of courtesy.'The sorceress Brágha Fellwinder has gone to Caivád Sâr, where she intends to teach her fellow Angmarim how to make more of the corrupted Wargs.Brágha Fellwinder has gone to the tower of Caivád Sâr, in central Elderslade.

You should defeat Brágha Fellwinder before she can pass on the knowledge of the crystals and the corruption her spells bring.Gunvald is in Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.

Return to Gunvald.Talk to Gunvald'The sorceress must be stopped.''Let's go!''Good job, my friend. This knowledge is best forgotten.'An Orc has been tampering with the dwarves' water supply and needs to be stopped.Dági has asked you to go to the next set of collection buckets and stop the Orc.

The buckets are in an area that overlooks the Mirrormere, to the south-west of Ashmargathâl.Go to the next locationThe Orc has not touched these buckets yet, but is most likely nearby.

You should feign ignorance about the Orc's presence and pretend to collect snow.Pretend to collect snowDefeat the Orc responsibleThis specific Orc will trouble Dági no longer.

He waits for you at Ashmargathâl.Talk to Dági'This Orc must have been studying my movements. Unfortunate, but at least I know their next destination: an area that overlooks the Mirrormere, to the south-west of us. No need to follow the road for long.

'A lone soldier would seem like an easy victory to any Orc. And when this Orc tries to sneak up behind you, you'll show them that you're not as easily fooled!

'In the meantime, I ought to start hiding the other buckets....''Well then, that's that! From now on, I'll be vigilant about the locations I pick. Retrieving the buckets will be much more of a chore, but I'd rather that the Orcs never find out about our water supply.'After coming to Azanulbizar at long last, King Thráin has called the Kings of the Seven Houses to council at Amdân.Dáin can be found at Amdân.

Dáin has learned that King Thráin intends to call a council of the Kings of the Seven Houses at Amdân and has asked you to join him. You should talk to Dáin.Talk to DáinDáin can be found at Amdân.

After attending the council of the Kings of the Seven Houses, you took rest before the battle ahead. You should talk to Dáin.Talk to Dáin at Amdân'According to my father, King Thráin intends to call the Kings of the other Houses to council this evening.

'The sons of the other Kings and lords have been invited as well, so being the grandson of the Lord of the Iron Hills, so have I!

'You may not be of my blood, but you are my brother, Hermáth. A great battle awaits us on the morrow, and we must be prepared for it.

'Will you accompany me to the council?''What do you say, Hermáth? Will you join me?''Ah, Hermáth! I did not sleep as well as I'd have liked, but I hope you got some rest.

'Amdân is all a-bustle this morn, and it seems some of our cousins have already set out. I am eager to join the battle, but I will heed King Thráin's orders—father made certain of that!'Misthallow is home to a fierce breed of larger hunting cats which stalk the hill and valleys in search of prey.   These vile evil creatures hunt for sport — toying cruelly with their victims — instead of merely for food.Mishallow is home to a fierce breed of larger hunting cats which stalk the hill and valleys in search of prey. These vile evil creatures hunt for sport — toying cruelly with their victims — instead of merely for food.Defeat Anduin Hunters throughout MisthallowFierce hunting cats, known to the locals as Anduin Hunters, stalk the hills and valleys along the Langflood. These foul creatures are renown in the area for toying cruelly with their victims before ending their lives.

Defeat these creatures where you find them in the Misthallow.Defeat Anduin Hunters in Misthallow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed.CompletedThe hunting cats of Misthallow have grown larger and fiercer than many of their kind, and they stalk the hills and valleys along the Langflood in search of prey. They are held in the grip of some vile evil, and hunt not for food but for sport, toying cruelly with their victims before ending their lives. You should defeat these malicious beasts before their hunt begins anew.You have put an end to the vile sport of the Anduin Hunters, making more safe the lands along the river. The folk who live and adventure in Misthallow would give you their heartiest thanks if they knew the torture they would have faced in the grasp of the hunters, and that you saved them from it.The Wargs of Azanulbizar must have their ranks thinned before the major battle takes place.Wargs can be found at Gadh Ujáf and Zagâf Muzug.

Valdi has asked you to defeat Wargs and their sires.Defeat NaurnashDefeat KhakrankDefeat Wargs in Azanulibizar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Valdi can be found in Amdân.

You should talk to Valdi.Return to Valdi'We shall now strike the source! The fiercest and most deadly of the Warg champions are all kin, results of numerous litters produced by two past champions, Naurnash and Khakrank. Defeating the sires and thinning the pack will go a long way to removing their evil from Azanulbizar.''You have defeated the Wargs and their sires? Well done, friend. We have dealt a solid blow to the enemy this day.'The gladiatorial pits of Umbar Baharbêl serve several important purposes: entertaining the masses, keeping their attention focused, and meting justice upon those who break the laws of the city.Complete 'Dahâl Huliz, The Arena -- Tier 5'Hoping to put an end to Azog's plots at the warding-spire of Atrad-zarakh, Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu have made for the slopes of Bundushâthur.Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu can be found at Ashmargathâl, far to the north of Amdân on the slopes of Bundushâthur.

