The Kings of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu have asked you to scout Târ-kútoz and defeat Azog's forces at Atrad-zarakh.Scout Târ-kútozGoblins and bats can be found at Târ-kútoz and within the warding-spire of Atrad-zarakh. Trophy-bones can be collected from Orcs and some goblins.

You should aid the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu by defeating the goblins and bats dwelling at Târ-kútoz. You should also collect trophy-bones for the Haban'akkâ.Defeat goblins at Târ-kútoz and Atrad-zarakh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat bats at Târ-kútoz and Atrad-zarakh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect trophy-bones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have done much to hinder Azog's forces at Târ-kútoz and Atrad-zarakh.

You should raise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Atrad-zarakh.Raise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Atrad-zarakhYou have done much to aid the dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu at Atrad-zarakh.Completed'What do you say, Hermáth? The journey will be long, but hardship has not stopped us yet!

'Will you aid our kin and cousins at Ashmargathâl?''Yes, Longbeard? Do you bring word from King Thráin?'

King Shâlim Nightcloak looks to you. You inform King Shâlim that you have come to aid the dwarves on Bundushâthur.

'At least someone means to do what must be done then! I grow tired of these Zhélruka and Kámbrada. Not their warriors, mind you, but Usk and Vélat. For dwarves I thought to be sworn enemies, they seem to grow closer friends with each passing hour. That is all well and good, but it seems they have forgotten there is a war to be won!

'The Abnúzhu have slain many Orcs this day, and we will slay many more before its end. I would not leave this battle empty-handed, friend. Orc-bones can make for fine trophies!''If King Thráin means to bolster us only with a single warrior, I hope he has chosen wisely!'

King Usk stares you down, and then chuckles to himself.

'I welcome any aid you would give us, Longbeard. After all, Vélat and his Zhélruka have spun enough tales to last three wars, but if we intend to rout our foes, someone must do the fighting. A-ha!

'Among the Orcs at Atrad-zarakh, their smaller cousins have proven difficult to overcome. Between the bat-tenders and those wielding their crude explosives, it has made our approach much more challenging than I had hoped.

'Do what you can, and that is enough!''What is this? Does King Thráin not trust us in our task?'

King Vélat smirks.

'I jest, Longbeard! Between the Zhélruka and the Abnúzhu, we have things well in hand. Oh, and I must admit that my friend, Usk, and his Kámbrada have played a part in our success as well. Hah!

'Ashmargathâl was an easy prize to win, but Atrad-zarakh still teems with our foes. It would be far easier to look ahead without those accursed bats flitting about our heads!'Although the battle on Bundushâthur is not yet ended, your efforts have done much to aid the Dwarves of the Kámbrada, Zhélruka, and Abnúzhu.Defeat many of the Dead in Câr Bronach.Defeat many of the Dead in Câr Bronach.Defeat many of the Dead in Câr BronachDefeat many of the Dead in Câr Bronach.Defeat many of the Dead in Câr Bronach.Defeat many of the Dead in Câr BronachProgress through Cloudyhead Pass is impeded by a dangerous hail of arrows, shot from enemies on the ledges above.Archers can be found on the western overpass above the Cloudyhead Pass.

You should defeat archers and relieve them of their weapons.Collect Orkish arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Moria overpass-archers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy bow stands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Valdi is located in Amdân.

Bring the arrows to Valdi.'Archers are hindering our attack upon the ruins and Orc camp at the far end of the pass. They rain down arrows into the gorge from the overpass above. Thus far, they have repulsed our attempts to capture their position, for a company of dwarves presents a large target. A single dwarf, however, could get close enough without being seen to defeat them. Take them down from their perches, Hermáth, and relieve them of any weapons you might find.''Excellently done! Our army will be able to progress through the pass more safely now.'Much to the horror of the Gabil'akkâ, Gorgar the Ruthless has discovered a means to spread strange, noxious fumes upon the war-fell of Azgh-buzru.Noxious cauldrons can be found across Azgh-buzru, especially among siege installations.

Dréri has asked you to destroy noxious cauldrons at Azgh-buzru.Destroy noxious cauldrons at Azgh-buzru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dréri can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks.

You have destroyed many noxious cauldrons at Azgh-buzru and impaired Gorgar's usage of this vile weaponry. You should report to Dréri at Drenghól.Talk to Dréri at Drenghól'${PLAYER}! It is good to see you, but keep your head down!

'Have you seen a cloud upon the war-fell? Dare not to stray too close to it! It is death itself... a fire that consumes all breath and burns within! Oh, that such a weapon did not exist!

'I have spied them gathering it in cauldrons beside their trebuchets across Azgh-buzru.

'Destroy as many cauldrons as you can, and when that is done, report to me at Drenghól!''Through all my years in Mordor, I witnessed many terrible things. I had hoped that such terrible creations could not be found so far from the Black Land.

'We cannot hope to undermine the craft of this new weapon, but we can work to slow its deployment on the battlefield. And that is enough!'You have studied Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar in its entirety.You have studied Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar in its entirety.Complete Explorer of AzanulbizarComplete Quests of AzanulbizarComplete Slayer of AzanulbizarThere is much to do while adventuring in Câr Bronach.There is much to do while adventuring in Câr Bronach.Complete Explorer of Câr BronachComplete Quests of Câr BronachComplete Slayer of Câr BronachThere is much to do while adventuring in Deepscrave.There is much to do while adventuring in Deepscrave.Complete Explorer of DeepscraveComplete Quests of DeepscraveComplete Slayer of DeepscraveComplete many deeds in Elderslade.Complete many deeds in Elderslade.Complete: 'Explorer of Elderslade'Complete: 'Quests of Elderslade and War of Three Peaks'Complete: 'Slayer of Elderslade'There is much to do while adventuring in Gloomingtarn.There is much to do while adventuring in Gloomingtarn.Complete Explorer of GloomingtarnComplete Quests of GloomingtarnComplete Slayer of GloomingtarnComplete deeds in Imlad Morgul and Mordor Besieged.Complete deeds in Imlad Morgul and Mordor Besieged.Complete The Reclamation of Minas IthilComplete Explorer of Imlad Morgul and Mordor BesiegedComplete Quests of Imlad Morgul and Mordor BesiegedComplete Slayer of Imlad Morgul and Mordor BesiegedComplete many deeds in Misthallow and the Floodfells.Complete many deeds in the Wells of Langflood.Complete: Explorer of the Wells of LangfloodComplete: Quests of the Wells of LangfloodComplete: Slayer of the Wells of LangfloodThere is much for the White Company to accomplish in reclaiming Minas Ithil from the remnants of Sauron's forces.Defiled bones can be found in Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.

