You should deliver Náin the Slakeless's war orders to the Zhélruka Soldiers.'Take these orders. I am giving the best Zhélruka warriors important missions. These missions, if successful, are certain to turn the tides of war! Deliver them at once, ${PLAYER}. For Gundabad!'The Filth-well of Eithel Gwaur is the source of the corruption that has long tainted the flowing waters of the Ithilduin, giving to them a new name: Morgulduin, River of Sorcery.Complete 'Eithel Gwaur, the Filth-well -- Tier 1'Complete 'Eithel Gwaur, the Filth-well -- Tier 2'Complete 'Eithel Gwaur, the Filth-well -- Tier 3'Complete 'Eithel Gwaur, the Filth-well -- Slayer'Behind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Complete Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow -- Tier 1Complete Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow -- Tier 2Complete Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow -- Tier 3Complete Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow: Kergrim-slayerComplete Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow: Wight-slayerFar under Mount Gundabad lies the Den of Pughlak, the realm of the deepest of the deep toads.Delve deeper.Delve deeperDefeat Kordkoth.Defeat KordkothDelve deeper.Delve deeperDefeat Pughlak.Defeat PughlakFar under Mount Gundabad lies the Den of Pughlak, the realm of the deepest of the deep toads.Delve deeper.Delve deeperDefeat Kordkoth.Defeat KordkothDelve deeper.Delve deeperDefeat Pughlak.Defeat PughlakFar under Mount Gundabad lies the Den of Pughlak, the realm of the deepest of the deep toads.Delve deeper.Delve deeperDefeat Kordkoth.Defeat KordkothDelve deeper.Delve deeperDefeat Pughlak.Defeat PughlakFar under Mount Gundabad lies the Den of Pughlak, the realm of the deepest of the deep toads.Delve deeper.Delve deeperDefeat Kordkoth.Defeat KordkothDelve deeper.Delve deeperDefeat Pughlak.Defeat PughlakThyra, daughter of Runerik and Yrsa, seeks to fill some of the dwindling food supplies in Limlók.Fish may be found in nets along a river in the Floodfells.

You should gather any fish that you find.Gather fish from nets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather nuts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A crate for the fish can be found in Limlók.

You should put the fish in a crate.'I am Thyra. Sighild is my twin sister. Now, a question for you: Have you lately seen the stores in Limlók? They are nearly empty. I blame all you outsiders. Oh, you want to replenish our dwindling stores? Then you should gather fish and nuts for us. 

'Yes, some of us Beornings do eat fish. Grimbeorn does not, but when you live where the cows and fields are plentiful, you need no fish to survive. The Floodfells can be a harsh place at times, but still does it provide well for us. The fish that reside in the rivers nearby are a resource, just as the nuts that grow on the trees and bushes.'With few clues as to what Gáfin discovered before he died, hunting down the Orc commander Uflúk for information may be the next best option.Rékkur has suggested bringing Aighrig with you to the Orc camp.

Aighrig stands before the stairs to Annâk-khurfu.Talk to AighrigThe Orc camp Zarkul-sulûn is located west of Annâk-khurfu.

Aighrig believes that Uflúk can be lured out if you find a war horn to use in the camp.Use war horn and defeat UflúkUse the whistle to summon Aighrig to your sideUpon defeating Uflúk, you found a report among his belongings.

Discussing this report with Aighrig may reveal something.Use the whistle to summon Aighrig to your sideRékkur awaits your return at Annâk-khurfu, to the east of Zarkul-sulûn.

Aighrig has asked you to bring the report to him.'Maybe we'll learn something if we set our sights higher.

'It's clear that Gáfin was killed by Orcs. According to the scouts, the Orc Uflúk commands the camp Zarkul-sulûn, to the west. If anyone has the information Gáfin was trying to bring back, it would be Uflúk.

'But I wouldn't ask for you to venture forth alone. This could be another chance for Aighrig to prove herself to us, if she is willing!''I was just feeding Lúkhag. She has been very brave lately. But yes, I would be happy to aid you in your hunt.

'I do not think a commander such as Uflúk will be caught off-guard wandering around. There must be a war horn in the Orc camp that we can use to trick him into emerging.''This report details the health of bats under Angmarim care. They are raising and training bats for the Orcs -- perhaps this is what Gáfin discovered....'

A troubled expression falls upon Aighrig's face.

'The one who wrote this report is someone named... Latharn. ${PLAYER}, I recognize that name -- it belongs to an Angmarim who is an accomplished beast-tamer. But that is all I know.

'I believe I know where the Angmarim are raising their bats. May I ask you to bring this report to Rékkur? I am sorry, but I must investigate alone.''Lúkhag flew off not too long ago -- and where is Aighrig? This doesn't bode well.'

Rékkur patiently listens to your account of what happened before reading through the report you found.

'Why does Aighrig require such secrecy? Though I suppose we can only wait for her....

'The Orcs had a hand in Gáfin's death, and now the Angmarim might have too. Gáfin, my old friend, what did you get yourself into?'Gorgar the Ruthless keeps many curious beasts in his thrall. Among them, the frost-tusks possess size and might beyond that of any mere Orc, but they are reluctant to be stabled.Frost-tusks can be found hitched to posts in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.

Rádek has asked you to free frost-tusks from their hitching posts in an attempt to sow discord at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.Free frost-tusks from hitching posts in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rádek can be found near the gates of Mount Gundabad.

You have freed several frost-tusks from their hitching posts at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. You should return to Rádek.Talk to Rádek'Zhúdo sent you, did he? I assure you... I have my task well in hand.

'You have fought beside the Commander before, haven't you? Glóin's tasks are wise in the way of war, and I mean him no disrespect, but he does not think like a Zhélruka.

'I have learned much of the forces at the encampments here before the old gates. I have marked every weakness in their defences, noted every loose stone on the steps of Gundabad, but such things are obvious to those who wish to see them. No, to think like a Zhélruka would mean to see the Orcs' misplaced trust in their own beasts!

'The frost-tusks these Orcs keep are proud, mighty beasts... not mere pets! They have been trained well enough, but they would sooner wander off without those posts tying them down. And that is the way of the Zhélruka!

'Free these frost-tusks from their would-be masters and we shall see if they truly wish to serve Gorgar!''Hah! That's what those Orcs get for trying to break a frost-tusk!

'No matter how well-trained they might seem, a frost-tusk never truly answers to anyone but itself! Now... it is true that there are some awfully wicked frost-tusks, but I knew these weren't that sort. It's in their eyes, after all!

'Very good, my friend.'You have discovered the entrance to Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold.Discover the entrance to Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold.Discover the entrance to Amdân Dammul, the Bloody ThresholdGrants completion of deed: Discovery: Amdân Dammul, the Bloody ThresholdBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Discovery: Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold'Now, my little fellows, where be you a-going to, puffing like a bellows? What's the matter here then? Tell me what's your trouble!

