Bring the arrows and pouches to Edash.Return to Edash'A strange and fell ailment has befallen our soldiers. Even the smallest wound has left them stricken by some unnatural illness. I suspect poison is to blame, but I need more of the foul stuff to study. Time is pressing down on our brethren, so you must hurry.

'Make your way to Rung-shakam and gather samples of the poison. Check their arrows and look for pouches of the stuff. It dries quickly and flakes into powder, so I suspect they must carry it with them into battle. Anything you might do to thin their ranks will also help.''Good, good. You have brought me many samples. We must work quickly if we are to save their lives.'As the one in charge of collecting usable water, Dági might work faster this time with your help.You should check on and collect melted snow from Dági's collection buckets.

He placed the buckets at a snowy overlook to the south-east of Ashmargathâl, just off the road in Tharkh Shathur.Check on the water-collection bucketsThe collection buckets have been tampered with.

Checking the surrounding snow for clues may point you to the right direction.Examine the disturbed snow for tracksDági at Ashmargathâl will want to know about the Orc footprints you found.Talk to Dági'Greetings, friend! I was just about to head out to fetch water. We haven't got a good source of water here, so collecting snow in buckets is our only choice. I can't set up the buckets here -- on account of the foot traffic -- so instead I have groups of buckets at a few different locations close by.

'Of course, retrieving them can be a pain when working alone. If you'd like to help me, we'll get our water much faster!

'Follow the road south-east through Tharkh Shathur, and you'll see a snowy overlook before long. I have some buckets set up at the top. Watch out for the wild animals there!''So you saw Orc tracks too, did you? Ugh. Depriving us of our water, or worse. We'll have to put a stop to this, lest we die of thirst instead!'Nagli Want-kin has invited you to share in a day of the simple life he and the other Want-kin have long sought.Bráthur, Dúghild, Gaustaf, and Nagli Want-kin can be found at Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade.

