You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at AzanulbizarAs you sift through the first few pages of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs, you notice the author has written a foreword.'It was at the behest of Dáin, my dear friend and King Under the Mountain, that I embarked upon writing a complete account of the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs. For too long, Durin's Folk had endured hardship after hardship, and it did not seem proper to dwell on such a sorrowful chapter in our history.

'Where my own memory and experiences did not serve the tale, I enlisted the accounts of others, chief among them the sons of Fundin and Gróin, and by his own request, King Dáin. For this, they have my truest gratitude.

'As a final note, I have laboured to construct this tale that the reader might see it through mine own eyes. If I should interject on occasion, it is only to make clear certain details or include aspects of the tale learned long after the war's end.'

Beneath the foreword, you notice a dedication.

'For Durin'The northern settlement of Limlók needs its defences fortified, supplies replenished, and surrounding lands made safe.Yrsa Spearwife, Thyra, Sighild, and Trygvar can all be found in Limlók.

You should assist each of them with their tasks.Assist Yrsa Spearwife with "Protecting Limlók"Assist Trygvar with "Walls of Bramble"Assist Sighild with "Spies From Gundabad"Assist Thyra with "Depleted Stores"Runerik Knotbeard can be found in Limlók.

You should talk to Runerik Knotbeard.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók'Yrsa has informed me that we do not need your help to keep Limlók safe. I am inclined to disagree. Oh, how I miss the years before the Orcs and Wargs came. In those days we could leave Limlók vacant all day while we wandered about the wilds. I would prefer a return to that peace we knew before my time's end.

'Seek out my kin in Limlók and assist them. They will be reluctant, but I have put you to work and my word is the rule here. Report back to me when you have finished your tasks.''Hmm, perhaps you are useful after all. Vaskorn has informed me of your deeds in the Thornholt and now I might have to start trusting you. Ha!'Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, wishes to learn more about Fram's history and the decisions that he made in life.Framsburg can be found in Misthallow.

