You should bring the furs to Aboki.Talk to Aboki'Make yourself useful! Our brethren may be trying to hide shivers behind beards, but I can tell they feel the biting wind through their mail. If you can bring me fur pelts, I can make blankets and line the clothing of our brave warriors.

'You will find bears, wolves, and Wargs outside these walls. The latter may or may not have pelts we can use, but you may get lucky! Anything we can do to thin their ranks is always worth it as well.''These are fine furs indeed. Once we get the stench off them, they'll be made into blankets, cloaks, lining, and other items to protect our army from this biting chill.'Dwarf scouts who have pressed further towards the walls of Gundabad need support.Scout Borghild is somewhere in north-west Elderslade.

Gunvald has asked you to bring orders to Borghild and lend what support you may.'You have done much to thin the ranks of the enemy, ${PLAYER}! Our scouts have thus been able to slip closer to the walls of Gundabad. If you are still able to help, bring this scroll to Scout Borghild, and lend her what help she may need.''Well met. If Gunvald sent you, then you have my trust as well.'The Shadow-roost of Gath Daeroval is home to Khatlob, the Brood-mother of the winged beasts ridden by the Nazgûl. She and her vile egg-clutch must be destroyed or there will never be an end to the terror of the fell beasts.Cannoth has a plan.Talk to CannothDefeat Khúrthak the Rent.Defeat Khúrthak the RentTalk to Cannoth further up the path.Talk to Cannoth further up the pathReach the outcropping above and destroy the fell beast eggs before they hatch.Fell beast eggs destroyed (${VALUE}/4)<rgb=#FF0000>Fell beast eggs hatched (${VALUE}/4)</rgb>Defeat Khatlob the Brood-mother.Defeat Khatlob the Brood-mother'The cliffs above are home to Khatlob, Brood-mother of the fell beasts. She and her spawn have been mostly contained by the Orcs, but a new clutch of eggs is about to hatch, and I fear the newly-spawned beasts will not long remain at Gath Daeroval. We must put an end to Khatlob and her brood, or our people will never be safe, in Imlad Morgul or elsewhere.

'Some of Khatlob's caretakers remain, led by an olog known simply as Khúrthak the Rent. He possesses the keys we will need to gain access to the spawning ground. While you face Khúrthak, I will attempt to enter the Rookery.

'One last thing, friend. Khúrthak and his fellow ologs are possessed of a furious rage, and only a soothful vapour can calm their fury. I will give you a set of phials containing this vapour, but there are more in the chest next to me. If an olog enters that state, throw one of these phials at him and he will be calmed.''Past the gate and further up the path you will find Khatlob's roost. Hurry! The eggs are getting near to hatching! Find the nests and throw their contents off the edge to the rocks below!'The Shadow-roost of Gath Daeroval is home to Khatlob, the Brood-mother of the winged beasts ridden by the Nazgûl. She and her vile egg-clutch must be destroyed or there will never be an end to the terror of the fell beasts.Cannoth has a plan.Talk to CannothDefeat Khúrthak the Rent.Defeat Khúrthak the RentTalk to Cannoth further up the path.Talk to Cannoth further up the pathReach the outcropping above and destroy the fell beast eggs before they hatch.Fell beast eggs destroyed (${VALUE}/4)<rgb=#FF0000>Fell beast eggs hatched (${VALUE}/4)</rgb>Defeat Khatlob the Brood-mother.Defeat Khatlob the Brood-mother'The cliffs above are home to Khatlob, Brood-mother of the fell beasts. She and her spawn have been mostly contained by the Orcs, but a new clutch of eggs is about to hatch and I fear the newly-spawned beasts will not long remain at Gath Daeroval. We must put an end to Khatlob and her brood, or our people will never be safe, in Imlad Morgul or elsewhere.

