'One last thing, friend. Khúrthak and his fellow ologs are possessed of a furious rage, and only a soothful vapour can calm their fury. I will give you a set of phials containing this vapour, but there are more in the chest next to me. If an olog enters that state, throw one of these phials at him and he will be calmed.''Past the gate and further up the path you will find Khatlob's roost. Hurry! The eggs are getting near to hatching! Find the nests and throw their contents off the edge to the rocks below!'High above the Morgul Vale in a cleft in the side of Achathras, Gath Daeroval is home to the Shadow-roost of the fell beasts.Complete 'Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roost -- Tier 2'The Shadow-roost of Gath Daeroval is home to Khatlob, the Brood-mother of the winged beasts ridden by the Nazgûl. She and her vile egg-clutch must be destroyed or there will never be an end to the terror of the fell beasts.Cannoth has a plan.Talk to CannothDefeat Khúrthak the Rent.Defeat Khúrthak the RentTalk to Cannoth further up the path.Talk to Cannoth further up the pathReach the outcropping above and destroy the fell beast eggs before they hatch.Fell beast eggs destroyed (${VALUE}/6)<rgb=#FF0000>Fell beast eggs hatched (${VALUE}/2)</rgb>Defeat Khatlob the Brood-mother.Defeat Khatlob the Brood-mother'The cliffs above are home to Khatlob, Brood-mother of the fell beasts. She and her spawn have been mostly contained by the Orcs, but a new clutch of eggs is about to hatch. I fear the newly-spawned beasts will not long remain at Gath Daeroval. We must put an end to Khatlob and her brood, or our people will never be safe, in Imlad Morgul or elsewhere.

'Some of Khatlob's caretakers remain, led by an Olog-hai known as Khúrthak the Rent. He possesses the keys we will need in order to gain access to the spawning ground. While you face Khúrthak, I will attempt to enter the Rookery.

'One last thing, friend. Khúrthak and other Olag-hai are possessed of a furious rage, and only a soothful vapour can calm their fury. I will give you a set of phials containing this vapour, but there are more in the chest next to me. If an Olog-hai enters that state, throw one of these phials at him and he will be calmed.''Past the gate and further up the path you will find Khatlob's roost. Hurry! The eggs are getting near to hatching! Find the nests and throw their contents off the edge to the rocks below!'High above the Morgul Vale in a cleft in the side of Achathras, Gath Daeroval is home to the Shadow-roost of the fell beasts.Complete 'Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roost -- Tier 3'High above the Morgul Vale in a cleft in the side of Achathras, Gath Daeroval is home to the Shadow-roost of the fell beasts.Complete 'Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roost -- Tier 3'Defeat fell beasts within Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roostDefeat fell beasts within Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roostDefeat fell beasts within Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roostDefeat Olag-hai within Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roost.Defeat Olag-hai within Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roostDefeat Olag-hai within Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roostEdash has confirmed the poison that coats the enemy's arrows. Time is running out to craft the antidote.Twistbeard can found on rocks in Azanulbizar.

Edash has tasked you with gathering twistbeard moss.Collect twistbeard moss (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Edash is located in Amdân.

Bring the healing moss to Edash.Return to Edash'I have inspected the samples you brought and it is as I suspected. Which is both good and very, very bad. Bad, because left untreated every single one of these warriors will perish. Good, because I know the antidote.

'It shall not be a pleasant task for you, but their lives hang in balance. A moss grows in this valley, Asfurtarg, sometimes called twistbeard. Bring me as much as you can find, and do be quick about it!''Yes, yes. Excellent. Bring it here! Time runs short!'Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Complete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore -- Tier 3Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Faeron is standing by inside the Halls of Black Lore.

