'Whenever you are ready, we will proceed.'Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Defeat the Vision of Past Adventures.Defeat the Vision of Past AdventuresDefeat the Vision of Fallen Foes.Defeat the Vision of Fallen FoesDefeat Dolguzigir, the Dark ArchivistDefeat Dolguzigir, the Dark ArchivistWithin Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Complete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore -- Tier 1Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Defeat the Vision of Past Adventures.Defeat the Vision of Past AdventuresDefeat the Vision of Fallen Foes.Defeat the Vision of Fallen FoesDefeat Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Defeat Dolguzigir, the Dark ArchivistWithin Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Complete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore  -- Tier 2Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Defeat the Vision of Past Adventures.Defeat the Vision of Past AdventuresDefeat the Vision of Fallen Foes.Defeat the Vision of Fallen FoesDefeat Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Defeat Dolguzigir, the Dark ArchivistWithin Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Complete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore  -- Tier 3Defeat many of the shades and fell spirits within the Halls of Black Lore.Defeat many of the shades and fell spirits within the Halls of Black Lore.Defeat many of the shades and fell spirits within the Halls of Black LoreDefeat many dark cataloguers and dark curators in the Halls of Black Lore.Defeat many dark cataloguers and dark curators in the Halls of Black Lore.Defeat many dark cataloguers and dark curators in the Halls of Black Lore.A missing severed hand, a mysterious illness, and a ghost?The fallen statue is located in Amdân.

Look for clues near the broken statue.Search for cluesExamine the footprintsThe wall is near the broken statue in Amdân.

Look for more clues along the wall.Search for cluesThe gap in the wall is in Amdân.

Follow the trail of the thief.Search for cluesThromur can be found in Amdân.

Talk to Thromur.'Three guards for one shift, hmmm. And one of them is ill, you say? That is very interesting, for my own reason for not being alert last night... well, was exactly the same as his. I wonder if some illness is spreading through the camp. That would be a disaster, with all of us in such close quarters. I am fine today, however. I also thought it was something I ate.

'And what is this about Zebena seeing a ghost?! Nonsense. There must be some other explanation! Please, my friend, examine the area where this so-called ghost was seen. There must be more to this!''You look like you have found something! Please tell me it's a severed hand.'Defeat many giants in Câr Bronach.Defeat many giants in Câr Bronach.Defeat many giants in Câr BronachDefeat many giants in Câr Bronach.Defeat many giants in Câr Bronach.Defeat many giants in Câr BronachRúzat, Agátur, and Náth wish to gather gifts for the Beornings so they will be more inclined to assist them in the North.Agátur can be found in Limlók.

You should talk to Agátur.Talk to Agátur in LimlókWargs can be found in the Floodfells.

You should gather pelts from Wargs in the Floodfells.Gather Warg pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Runerik Knotbeard can be found in Limlók.

You should present the Warg pelts to Runerik Knotbeard.Agátur can be found in Limlók.

You should talk to Agátur.Talk to Agátur in Limlók'Do my eyes deceive me? It is the kind ${CLASS}, ${PLAYER}! Indeed, you must remember the humble Rúzat, once again at your service!'

You explain to the three dwarves that you have heard of their heroics, accompanying the Beornings from Thornholt to Limlók.

'Why, you already know of our journey then, or at least some of it? Word travels quickly in the Vales, does it not? If Grimbeorn knows of our plight, surely he will accept our plea!'

Agátur grumbles at Rúzat.

'I suppose you find it odd to see a Longbeard, a Stout-axe, and a Zhélruka travelling together, no? I will let Agátur explain in detail, for he says that I rarely arrive at the point of the conversation in a timely fashion. Ha, maybe, maybe, my friend!''${PLAYER}, it is good to see you well. It was not long after you left Skarháld that Náth here and some others travelled from Erebor to assist us. Alas, our efforts took a turn for the worse. Some blamed a lack of leadership. Others were blamed for a failure to work together. I believe it was Gundabad that caught us off our guard.

'Skarháld is still well-defended, but for how much longer? The raiding parties from out of Gundabad are emboldened, and their numbers grow stronger with each passing day. What leadership there was at Skarháld sent emissaries from each clan to entreat the Beornings for assistance. We decided first to seek out the Beornings in the Thornholt at Skoghús. I am glad we got there when we did, or they would have all been slaughtered by an approaching warband!

'That was when we realized these Beornings have had no contact with the Vales in years. We offered to escort them to safety as a gesture of goodwill towards their people. Only hardship was found on our journey here. The path may never be clear of the evil that dwells in those woods!

'Now we await word from Grimbeorn. I hope he and the Beornings will aid us.

'Hmm, perhaps there is something we can do. I have heard that Beornings like good trophies as gifts, accepting them as a show of respect and goodwill. Yes, some Warg pelts would do, would they not? Would you mind gathering some Warg pelts for us? We are still resting from our arduous journey.''Is this a trophy from the dwarves? Why do they not present it to me themselves? I suspect they are a lazy bunch!

'Grr, I am not impressed, and yet it does not matter if I am or not! They should not be trying to impress me, for it is Grimbeorn whose approval they need, and that is an even greater challenge! Only Grimbeorn can make a pact for all Beornings to abide by. There is none other, so do not waste your time on me, ${CLASS}.''Well, I am out of ideas! I suppose we should just assist the Beornings as best we can, and wait here for Grimbeorn's reply. I do not like waiting. It makes me quite restless. Unless.... Hmm, I may have an idea, everyone!'Many particularly troublesome goblins still lurk in the Wells of Langflood.Many particularly troublesome goblins still lurk in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat Blade-slaverDefeat the Wound-skewerDefeat the Death-spearDefeat the Mighty StingerDefeat the Tracking DaggerDefeat the Angry ChaserDefeat Earth-splitterDefeat Marsh-reaverDefeat Raging MaulerDefeat Crag-slaverDefeat Shadow-ripperDefeat the Beast MasterDefeat Bone-chewerDefeat Bear-cleaverDefeat Drudge-stomperDefeat the Gangly SlicerDefeat Pine-cleaverDefeat Forest-stalkerDefeat Skull-cookerDefeat Blood-spillerMany were the goblins slain during the Battle of Azanulbizar.Many were the goblins slain during the Battle of Azanulbizar.Learn of the goblins slain at AzanulbizarMany were the goblins slain during the Battle of Azanulbizar.Many were the goblins slain during the Battle of Azanulbizar.Learn of the goblins slain at AzanulbizarBehind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Defeat Shalgoth.Defeat ShalgothFind the horrid creature that the kergrim have raised.Find the horrid creature that the kergrim have raisedDefeat Gurzhorn.Defeat GurzhornBehind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Complete the quest Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow -- Tier 1Behind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Defeat Shalgoth.Defeat ShalgothFind the horrid creature that the kergrim have raised.Find the horrid creature that the kergrim have raisedDefeat Gurzhorn.Defeat GurzhornBehind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Defeat Shalgoth.Defeat ShalgothFind the horrid creature that the kergrim have raised.Find the horrid creature that the kergrim have raisedDefeat Gurzhorn.Defeat GurzhornBehind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Complete the quest Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow -- Tier 2Behind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Defeat Shalgoth.Defeat ShalgothFind the horrid creature that the kergrim have raised.Find the horrid creature that the kergrim have raisedDefeat Gurzhorn.Defeat GurzhornBehind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Complete the quest Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow -- Tier 3Behind the broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz, the kergrim conduct horrid rituals from within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Complete Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow -- Tier 3Defeat many kergrim within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Defeat many kergrim within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Defeat many kergrim within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrowDefeat many wights within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Defeat many wights within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow.Defeat many wights within Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrowThere are many occupants of the hidden village of Lyndelby who are curious to meet with you.Mountain flowers can be found west of Lyndelby.

You should gather Misty Meadow marigolds for Badehild Bolga.Collect Misty Meadow marigolds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Planters can be found in Lyndelby.

You should plant the flowers you collected.Badehild Bolga can be found in Lyndelby.

You should talk to Badehild Bolga.Talk to Badehild Bolga in Lyndelby'It's nice to meet you. I am Gísla's daughter, Badehild! Lyndelby has been busy and lively since you arrived. It does feel like a festival today, does it not? I love the mountain flowers that grow near Lyndelby. Have you seen them? If we collect some and decorate the town, it will feel even more like my favourite festival of the year... Mountain Day! It's the first really nice day of the year after the winter ends. On that day, we spend the whole day outside, just enjoying the lovely weather, the lovely company, and very lovely meals!''Well look at that, Lyndelby is looking quite festive! Call me Hildi from now on. That is the name all my friends call me. You earned it, friend!'There are many occupants of the hidden village of Lyndelby who are curious to meet with you.The Misty Howler can be found near Lyndelby.

You should defeat the Misty Howler for Clodar Túcca.Find and defeat the Misty Howler!Clodar Túcca can be found in Lyndelby.

You should talk to Clodar Túcca.Talk to Clodar Túcca in Lyndelby'Thank you for entertaining my wife, Fastrada. My name is Clodar Túcca. I have been too scared to leave my home lately. Can you hear the howling?! That's the Misty Howler! A terrible wolf that comes down from the mountains just to howl and terrorize me! That wolf terrifies me so! It does not frighten you at all?! Could you scare away the Misty Howler for me, then?''The howling stopped! I am not going to ask you how you accomplished such a feat. I'll just be glad that I can go out around Lyndelby in peace, not having to worry about the Misty Howler sneaking up behind me or eating my food! Or me! Thank you, stranger!'There are many occupants of the hidden village of Lyndelby who are curious to meet with you.Chickens can be found in Lyndelby.

You should catch chickens for Erma Túcca.Erma Túcca can be found in Lyndelby.

You should bring the chickens to Erma Túcca.Talk to Erma Túcca in Lyndelby'Good to meet you. I am Erma Túcca, and I keep our livestock happy and healthy. I've run into a bit of a problem, though. It seems I may have left the gate to the chicken's pen open just a bit. Now my chickens are all roaming around Lyndelby. This normally is not a problem, but it is feeding time and none of the chickens came when I called. I don't want them to starve, and I have to be here in case they come back! Please, could you help find my chickens?''Well look at that! You got my birds back to me, all safe and sound! You're so gracious, stranger, helping us and doing such nice things. Grandmother Maddy was right about you.'There are many occupants of the hidden village of Lyndelby who are curious to meet with you.The gazebo can be found in the village centre.

You should get on stage!Head to the Lyndelby gazeboThe gazebo can be found in the village centre.

You should get on stage and sing!The gazebo can be found in the village centre.

You should get on stage and tell a story!The gazebo can be found in the village centre.

You should get on stage and show off your strength!Fastrada Túcca can be found in Lyndelby.

You should talk to Fastrada Túcca.Talk to Fastrada Túcca in Lyndelby'I wasn't going to meet you, stranger, no matter how many others found you to be helpful or pleasant. Then I heard that you're quite strong, performing all sorts of tasks for the village. I also heard that you know some stories and songs that I do not know. That was what convinced me. I'm Fastrada Túcca. No, no, do not tell your story here and now! You must perform for the whole town. Come, let us go to the gazebo in the town's centre!''A lovely story, wonderful song, and my, how strong. I have not been this entertained in many, many years. I do hope you will stay a while longer. You must have more songs and stories to share with us?'There are many occupants of the hidden village of Lyndelby who are curious to meet with you.A freshly baked pie can be found in Lyndelby.

You should deliver the pie to Madelgard Túcca.Pick up the pie from the tableA freshly baked pie can be found in Lyndelby.

You should deliver the pie to Ogiva Túcca.Pick up the pie from the tableA freshly baked pie can be found in Lyndelby.

You should deliver the pie to Erma Túcca.Pick up the pie from the tableGísla Bolga can be found in Lyndelby.

You should talk to Gísla Bolga.Talk to Gísla Bolga in Lyndelby'Is Ubbo off fishing again? Then who's going to handle today's pie deliveries?! Hmmm, will you? That would be very kind of you! I baked these pies for Madelgard, Ogiva, and Erma. They are fresh and hot, and need to be delivered immediately. You can only carry one pie at a time though! They're fragile and if one were to drop on the ground... I shudder even at the thought!''All the pies have been delivered and not a single slice dropped? I'm very relieved to hear that! Oh, my apologies. In my haste to have the pies delivered, I forgot my manners. My name is Gísla Bolga, and it's a pleasure to make your acquaintance! I have been told that I bake the best pies in all of Lyndelby. Pie delivery day is always stressful. Pies are my trade, but they're also an art form after all. I would hate to see even one slice go to waste! Thank you for helping out. I'll make sure Ubbo delivers twice the pies tomorrow!'There are many occupants of the hidden village of Lyndelby who are curious to meet with you.A barrel of Lyndelby Northern Leaf can be found in Lyndelby.

You should try the Lyndelby Northern Leaf.Try the Lyndelby Northern LeafA barrel of Hubo's Berry-bear can be found in Lyndelby.

You should try Hubo's Berry-bear.Try Hubo's Berry-bearA barrel of Old Eagle Wings can be found in Lyndelby.

You should try Old Eagle Wings.Try some Old Eagle WingsHeldric Túcca can be found in Lyndelby.

You should talk to Heldric Túcca.Talk to Heldric Túcca in Lyndelby'Oh, hullo. You met my wife, Maddy, or Madelgard as she most likely introduced herself, yes? My name is Heldric Túcca! Pleased to meet you! Now, perhaps you could help me out with something. Here before you are three barrels, each with their own variety of Lyndelby pipe-weed. Oh, have you heard of pipe-weed before? How interesting! I bet the pipe-weed you have tried is not prepared the Lyndelby way! Ha, why not try some of each with me and see which you like best!''Did you have a favourite? Yes, it is hard to decide. I like them all very much!'

Heldric whispers to you.

'The secret is that we ferment them in a mix of our ale and mountain mineral water. You seem the type to keep a secret, so I trust you won't be telling anyone!'There are many occupants of the hidden village of Lyndelby who are curious to meet with you.Veins of gems can be found near Lyndelby.

You should gather the gems for Húbald Túcca.Gather Misty Mountain gems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A grindstone can be found in Lyndelby.

