You should talk to Valaric Túcca.Talk to Valaric Túcca at the picnic'Hullo, my name is Valaric Túcca and it's nice to meet you. I have a question, well, maybe two questions! Actually, I have many questions about life outside of Lyndelby. Um, first, how would you like to go on a picnic? Come on! We'll find a perfectly delightful spot! Well, it doesn't really need to be delightful or perfect. Any ol' adequate picnic spot will do. Oh! I know a good place. Grab the blanket and basket and meet me there.''Thanks for coming on this picnic with me, ${PLAYER}. It sure is nice to talk to someone new for once. Sorry for dragging you all the way out here, but if I'd started asking these questions while we were still in town, there'd be no end of gossip about me leaving. I don't want to leave Lyndelby! I am just very curious, is all.

'Anyhow, here's my first question....''How very interesting, I dare say!

'Now then, I have another question for you....''Another great story of the lands beyond. My, I never imagined so much was out there!

'I do have one last question for you, if you do not mind....''You've shared with me such fascinating of stories about life outside of Lyndelby. Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for giving me so many things to think and dream about!'There are many occupants of the hidden village of Lyndelby who are curious to meet with you.Pesky mountain-shrews can be found in Lyndelby.

You should defeat the shrews for Vilihad Túcca.Boot pesky mountain-shrews off the fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Vilihad Túcca can be found in Lyndelby.

You should talk to Vilihad Túcca.Talk to Vilihad Túcca in Lyndelby'Vilihad Túcca is my name and farming is my life! I love to work in the fields. The freshest crops are the best to eat after all, and you can't get fresher than just picked, Ha! My wife, Ogiva, tells me you enjoy helping us folk out. Hmm, well how do you feel about shrews? Oh, I know how I feel about them! I hate them! That's right, they're always running around my fields, devouring my lettuce. How am I supposed to eat the food I grow if it's ruined before I pick it?! If you could boot them off the fields for me, I would be most grateful!''The shrews are all gone?! Oh, misty mountain mornings, you are certainly a helpful stranger! I shall never forget you! Call me Villo from now on. That's what my friends call me!'One of the Want-kin, Gaustaf, has found joy in panning the Greylin for gem-stones and other interesting baubles.The Greylin runs south out of Ered Mithrin to the east of Khadâsh-gâra.

Gaustaf has asked you to pan the Greylin in several locations and bring him what you find. You should pan the Greylin.Gaustaf can be found at Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade.

You have found a few small gem-stones and interesting pebbles from panning the Greylin. You should return to Gaustaf.'I must admit, this is the best place we've made camp so far. Nagli has truly outdone himself!

'Sheltered from the chill air... and the Orcs, and in sight of such a beautiful river—what more could I ask for?

'Have you walked along the Greylin, ${PLAYER}? It has proven a site of many interesting finds of late... at least for me!

'Here, why don't you take my pan and try your luck in its waters? Go on!''Well, let's have a look at what you found....'

Gaustaf looks over your collection of small gem-stones and pebbles.

