You should talk to Léothred at Framsburg.Talk to Léothred elsewhere at Framsburg'Ah, are you feeling well-rested? Good, then we can begin another day's delving into Rohirric history! Now we shall explore what I see as a crucial time for the Éothéod. Haldend remained their lord, but he had neither sons nor brothers to continue his line! Come, let us depart.''As you can see, these were most uncertain times for my people. There was hope, however!''Haldend did have a daughter, however, and she proved the salvation of her people. Théodwyne Sternbrow was a formidable woman, a shield-maiden who towered over, and could easily best, many of the Éothéod's finest warriors. She slew several trolls, faced giants, and hunted Wargs in the wild.

'Perhaps we should slay a few giants, trolls, and Wargs to better understand Théodwyne's might!'There is much for the White Company to accomplish in reclaiming Minas Ithil from the remnants of Sauron's forces.Gondorian scrolls can be found in Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore.

