You should report back to Skarding.Talk to Skarding Wargsbane at Thokvist'Worry not about Egraedir. While he cares only for Eagle-kind, he is not wicked. Do not be fooled by his mien! He may offer help, but none will come from my brother; he considers all but the Eagles to be lesser than he.

'I can be no more assistance to you on the ground. Speak with Skarding about where to proceed, and with what.''${PLAYER}, I have found the patrol. The brutes return to Lumrog. Let us survey the place from on high, for here we are too surrounded by mist. I do not know what lurks in Lumrog, but something there protects the chieftain Gúrbarash from my claws.'You explain to Egraedir that a fire has been lit on one of the nearby hills.

'Yes, I see it. It was most likely set by those vile trolls. I do not like the way they cut down and burn the forest! By the time you get there, worthless and slow, the entire hilltop will be scorched from base to crest! I shall put it out.''Ha, you played a good trick upon Egraedir. No, I do not think he would ever work with Gundabad. He hates Orcs as much as Fanglind does. Egraedir is more of a fool, really. He knows not the time for play and the time for work... that is something all Beornings know. My work, it seems, is never done....'

Skarding looks into the mist, clutching his gifted Warg pelt. He mutters quietly to himself.

'Soon... soon my work will be finished.'History, etched in the stones of time, can be looked at from many views and read with just as many interpretations.The Carrock can be found in the Beorninglands.

