You should travel to Limlók.Talk to Léothred at Limlók'You are heading to Limlók, yes? I will accompany you. It would seem the story I seek follows the same path. Might we stop at the Carrock on our way? I would very much like to see for myself. There is some Rohirric history there as well, if you can believe it.''For a time the folklore of the Ai-thúda held that it was Fram, not the Dwarf-king Durin, who first beheld the Lonely Mountain, though no tale among Durin’s Folk mentions him. There may be some truth in this claim. I still wonder, which story is true? I fear the story of Fram may have been embellished in places over the years.''This seems a good enough place to rest for a bit.'Defeat many hobgoblins in Elderslade.Defeat many hobgoblins in Elderslade.Defeat hobgoblins in EldersladeDefeat many hobgoblins in Elderslade.Defeat many hobgoblins in Elderslade.Defeat hobgoblins in EldersladeThe members of the ill-fated scouting party must be remembered and honoured for their heroics and sacrifice.Shakal-atrâd can be found in central Elderslade.

