His face is stern, but it does little to mask the tears dried upon his cheeks.'Nár is right.

'All among my Haban'akkâ have earned a night's rest, but far too many of our kin and cousins shall not wake again. Let Khazad-dûm bear witness to their deeds, both great and small.

'And so, we shall not return to Amdân tonight. Durin himself shall watch over us!''Oh, Hermáth... I wish I did not have to speak of it.

'But I will say what I must.''I crossed the threshold, and the First Hall laid before me....'At first, King Thráin says nothing.

After a moment, he straightens his beard and turns to the other survivors.'At last our work is done, but it rings hollow, my friend.

'Many were lost in the fighting, but now even the dale itself lies barren and lifeless. I weep for my father, Náin. I wish he knew how soon victory would come after he fell. Along with the rest of our kin, he too will be burned, but he will remain in my mind as the proud dwarf he was!

'Our friends and cousins mourn their losses, and I would not leave them to grieve alone. I have paid my respects to each of them. I am certain they would welcome any words of comfort from you as well, Hermáth.

'Once that is done, you ought to talk to Thorin. I believe we need only await King Thráin before this grim task is finished.''Ah, Hermáth, I think we are ready to light the final pyres.

'Although I am not certain as to his reasons, I believe my father has gone down to Kheled-zâram. We all mourn in our own ways, I suppose, so perhaps he seeks the wisdom of the First Crafter. Alas, this duty is his alone!

'Would you go find him and tell him that we are prepared?''Yes?'

King Thráin appears lost in thought, his gaze fixed upon the dark waters of Kheled-zâram. You tell him the final pyres are prepared, and that Thorin has sent for him.

'So be it.''It is time we honoured our fallen as best we can.

'We have stripped them of their mail, taken their weapons, and now we give their bodies to the flame. Bolg and the Orcs will never make trophies of them.

'To burn the dead is not the way of any of our peoples, but it must be done, and we must hold those we lost dear to our hearts and memory.

'Let us honour them together.''My heart is heavy, friend. I wish it hadn't come to this....''Ah, you return. But where is my father, Hermáth?'

You explain that King Thráin sent you to inform Thorin that he would arrive shortly, despite his leg-wound.

'He is stubborn as ever, I see. We will wait, then.'

You and Thorin wait for a time, until finally King Thráin begins to shuffle up the ramp to the central pyre.

'There he is!'Durin was last seen travelling north-east with a single companion. Do they journey to the Anvil of Winterstith? And for what purpose?Glóin stands among the warriors of the Longbeard army before the Anvil of Winterstith.Talk to GlóinGlóin and the warriors of the Longbeard army marvel at Durin's secret departure from Skarháld.Listen to the questions of the LongbeardsGlóin is worried for the prince of the Longbeards, and has asked you to slowly approach Durin and learn why he came to Winterstith.Carefully approach DurinDurin stares into the sheet of ice at Winterstith, muttering quietly.Listen to Heilar's accountDurin stares into the sheet of ice at Winterstith, muttering quietly.Gently break Durin's reverie, if you canYou have managed to break Durin's reverie at the Anvil of Winterstith, but he still speaks slowly, as if waking from a deep sleep.Talk to DurinDurin has managed to shake free of his reverie, seeing for the first time the Longbeard army from the Lonely Mountain.Listen to Durin as he addresses the great force of LongbeardsThe Zhélruka Mírkuz followed on the heels of the Longbeard army during its march from Skarháld, and now he has interrupted Durin's speech.Talk to MírkuzNewly-resolved, Durin addresses the Longbeard army before the Anvil of Winterstith.Listen to Durin as he addresses the great force of LongbeardsMírkuz has listened to the words of Durin with growing displeasure and worry, and now he wishes to voice his concerns to you.Talk to Mírkuz'Can you not feel the power in the air, ${PLAYER}? My warriors will not know defeat, and soon, yes... soon we will walk in Gundabad once more, and cast out the Orcs that fill it!''Do you see him down the hill there? At least he is not unguarded, for Heilar stands with him. But what purpose brought them hither with no word to anyone?''This is... Winterstith? What am I doing here?'

Durin shakes his head to clear it. His eyes refocus upon you, and he no longer speaks as if he were submerged in the deep water of sleep.

'I remember leaving Skarháld, and calling for Heilar to accompany me, but my purpose for doing so has fled. It seemed so clear to me, like the great sheet of ice before us, but now it is clouded over and hazy. It is lost to me. There was a voice; that much I do remember. It drew me here. If you had not disturbed me I might have learned what it wanted!'

You remind Durin of the need for caution: Hrímil Frost-heart dwells somewhere behind the ice, sealed within the Anvil of Winterstith, and the speech of dragons is known to have a strange power.

'Do you take me for a fool? I would have known if this was dragon-speech. It cannot have been the voice of Hrímil, ${PLAYER}. No, I think this was something else. Many are the dwarves, Longbeard and Zhélruka alike, who have reported a fascination with the Anvil throughout the years. Many of them were kings. Can it be that it is now my turn to accept this kingly aspect?'

Durin nods to himself, and his face shines as he sees the Longbeard army behind you.'I followed this great array of Longbeards here from Skarháld, for I do not like it and did not trust it. I like what I am hearing from their prince even less!

'You need use no force, ${PLAYER}. I am of the Zhélruka and fear nothing, neither ${RACE} or dwarf. Nor do I fear kings or princes such as he.''I do not like it, ${PLAYER}. I fear the prince's words on this day will echo throughout the mountains until they reach unfriendly ears.

'Who can say what evil might be done as a result of this Longbeard's newfound course?'After King Thráin and his vanguard set out to assault the gates of Khazad-dûm, a sudden revelation threatens to raise tensions between the Longbeards and the Zhélruka at Amdân.Thromur can be found at Amdân.

