Shálun aided Thorin, but was dealt a fatal blow by Urro One-hand. You should talk to Shálun.Talk to Shálun'Stay with... me... a moment, won't you?''There he is, Hermáth.

'Let us see what Shálun has to say for himself!''I know not of what he speaks.

'If there is more to this tale, I would hear it. And preferably before we come to blows!''Oh, so now you want to hear what I have to say?'

Shálun glances derisively at Thromur.

'So long as you keep that one away from me, I'll tell you whatever you want.

'I am no thief! Will you hear my tale?''I... I did not mean for that. Nor did I wish for Frerin's death. I only wanted... no matter.

'I will make this right, Thromur. I must!''What has happened?! The vanguard is in retreat!

'Come, we must find Frerin!''Fundin was a friend of my master's....

'From the looks of it, he was far from the only dwarf who fell in the vanguard's retreat. I fear for master Frerin, but I also fear for King Thráin and what remains of his vanguard.'

Thromur glances at the ground, his eye pausing at a few spots.

'There are many tracks leading to the south-east, and not all of them were made by dwarves. If the Orcs are in pursuit, we must aid the King and our kinsfolk before it is too late!''No. I... we are too late. What have I done?'

Shálun steadies himself.

'To lose a son is a pain no father should bear... not once, and certainly not twice.''You have... my thanks, but I did not... see you in the vanguard. Did my father send for you?'

As Thorin tries to catch his breath, you explain that you came on another errand, but chose to aid the vanguard when you discovered what had befallen them.

'If you and your Zhélruka friend had not arrived when you did, I... things may have gone differently. I am not defeated yet, though.

'And Urro must pay for slaying my brother!''We have done it... but I don't even know your names, my friends.'

You introduce yourself and Shálun. Amidst the battle around you, Thorin smiles slightly.

'You have my thanks, Hermáth... and you also, Shálun. Your deeds this day will not be forgotten among the Zhélruka, nor shall they be among the Longbeards—that I promise to you!

'Stay with Shálun, Hermáth. His eyes grow dark, and the comfort of a friend would do his spirit well.

'As for me, I....''Hermáth... is that you?'

Shálun coughs and blood dribbles from his lip.

'Is... Urro... slain? What... of the Longbeard... prince?'

You tell Shálun that Thorin slew Urro and survived. Shálun smiles weakly.

'I... told Thromur... I would... make it right. Didn't... I?'After coming to Azanulbizar at long last, King Thráin has called the Kings of the Seven Houses to council at Amdân.Dáin can be found at Amdân.

