After listening to Thráin's council with the Kings of the Seven Houses, Dáin has beckoned you. You should talk to Dáin.Talk to Dáin'Rest well, Hermáth. I shall see you in the morn!''I think we're in luck, Hermáth.

'It doesn't sound like it's started yet, but we'd better hurry over!''I hope my father did not think me imprudent in my concern, Hermáth.

'I could tell he, too, was displeased that the Iron-folk would be held in reserve, but a dwarf of his station would not dare say as much. At the very least, I seem to have amused our elders and some of the Kings!

'I fear we have a long day ahead of us on the morrow, my friend. Let us sleep while we might!'Grimbeorn seeks word of the situation in the Wells of Langflood.Talk to Rúzat.Talk to RúzatJourney to Ered Mithrin with the dwarves.Journey to Ered Mithrin with the dwarvesDefeat the ambushers.Defeat the ambushers<rgb=#FF0000>Agátur must survive</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Náth must survive</rgb><rgb=#FF0000>Rúzat must survive</rgb>'I am grateful that you decided to accompany us!

'Now then, let us make for Skarháld. I do not think I would fare well in any further ambushes today!''I am ready. Let us continue on the path to Ered Mithrin.'Léothred and Fróthi have finally uncovered the truth of how Fram died and who killed him.Talk to Léothred.Talk to LéothredListen to Fróthi and Léothred's tale.Listen to Fróthi and Léothred's taleTalk to Fróthi.Talk to Fróthi'If only we had known then what we know now. To think of the added prosperity that both our peoples unknowingly abandoned.''Fram set out towards Scatha's hoard, as he often did. On this journey he had no intention of taking riches, however. His only goal was to confront Karazgar....''The bodies of the dwarves were nothing more than another misdirection by the devious Karazgar. He wanted nothing more than to stoke the fires of mistrust in the north.'The raiding-party from Gundabad had designs upon the peaceful Beorning village of Limlók... but where has it gone?Venko is ready to speak with the Beorning chieftain at the village of Limlók and learn if he has seen the missing raiding-party from Gundabad.Talk to Venko at LimlókVenko wishes to speak with the village chieftain of Limlók to learn what befell the raiding-party from Gundabad.Meet with Runerik, the village chieftain of LimlókRunerik believes his town has nothing to fear from the missing raiding-party, but your companions want to check Limlók's exterior fences just to make sure.Examine the south-eastern fence of LimlókExamine the eastern fence of LimlókExamine the north-eastern fence of LimlókExamine the north-western fence of LimlókExamine the south-western fence of LimlókRunerik Knotbeard stands outside his home in Limlók.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his house in LimlókRunerik does not believe his village is any more susceptible to danger than is usual for his people.Follow Runerik KnotbeardThe raiding-party has attacked the village of Limlók from multiple directions at the same time!Find Imák and protect him from the OrcsFind Venko and protect him from the OrcsThe raiding-party has attacked the village of Limlók from multiple directions at the same time!Return to Glóin in the village square and protect him from the OrcsThe raiding-party that threatened the safety of Limlók has been defeated, thanks to your efforts and those of your companions, as well as those of the people who dwell there. One Orc remains alive, but he will soon die of his wounds.Listen to Glóin's wordsThe raiding-party that threatened the safety of Limlók has been defeated, thanks to your efforts and those of your companions, as well as those of the people who dwell there. One Orc remains alive, but he will soon die of his wounds.Talk to Natsatúg before he dies of his wounds'Farewell to the worms who raided my town, and to the vermin who led them. None shall mourn.

'I thank you for your aid and that of your companions, ${PLAYER}. It was well-given.''We will speak to the chieftain and learn what he knows of the raiding-party. For there to be no sign of it, given the dying words of Thrúgord, seems most peculiar to me.''I take it you have seen no sign of this raiding-party? How surprising.''These Orcs are canny, ${PLAYER}! They set fires along the outskirts of the village at the same time, in order to thin out the defenders.

'But they did not account for us!''This attack is better-planned than I expected from the Orcs! They set fires on opposite sides of the village at the same time, forcing us to split the defences!

'I hate to say it, but these Orcs may work better together than we do!''Our companions are safe? That is good to hear, my friend! Let us finish off the Orcs here and the village will follow suit!''Enjoy... the days you have left... for they are few!'

Natsatúg coughs weakly and blood spreads from his wounds, soaking his armour.

'The time of the dwarves... is nearly ended! The Lord of Gundabad... the Lord of Gundabad...'

Natsatúg closes his eyes, and with his last exhalation he breathes a name.Lúkhag has led you to Dûn Traikh, presumably where she last saw Aighrig.Lúkhag is waiting for you on the road leading to Dûn Traikh.Approach LúkhagLúkhag appears to know where she's going, but will need you to defend her.Defend LúkhagLúkhag has led you to Aighrig, who has come to Dûn Traikh alone.Talk to AighrigAighrig is determined to find Latharn.Defend AighrigAighrig has stopped in front of the tower and has something to say.Talk to AighrigAighrig seems intent on confronting the Angmarim at the tower's entrance.

She has asked you not to attack them unless it's in self-defence.Observe the confrontationThe conversation between Latharn and Aighrig has not ended peacefully.Defend AighrigLatharn has been defeated.

You should check on Aighrig.Talk to Aighrig'Back to Annâk-khurfu, then. I have had enough of this place.'Seeing that you've caught up, Lúkhag continues flying towards Dûn Traikh.'Have you seen that island in the middle of the lake, ${PLAYER}? Grytholm, it is called, home to the bats of this region. I once considered it peaceful, but the Angmarim have taken over the cave on the island since, twisting bats to do their bidding. Gáfin must have discovered this before he died.

'I came here in search of Latharn, the one who wrote the report we found in Zarkul-sulûn. Join me if you wish, but I will continue with or without you.''Stay your hand. Please, do not attack them unless they attack first. I hope it does not come to that, but....''The Angmarim had my father in their clutches from the start.... I should have known that he would believe them to the bitter end. May the earth reclaim his bones and find some use for him.

'I will not apologize for coming here on my own, as it was my burden to bear. Still, I appreciate your help; I did not think you would trust me after learning of my past.

'Let me know when you are ready to depart. Rékkur ought to know the truth behind Gáfin's death.'Hoping to aid King Thorin in guiding the Prince to victory, Hersegg, grand-daughter of Hermáth Stormhammer, has offered to tell you the tragic tale of Nár.Hersegg can be found at Azanulbizar.

