You should go to that location and see if you can find the mearh.Seek out the mearh that Léothred saw in the mistLéothred can be found at Thokvist.

You should talk to Léothred.Talk to Léothred at Thokvist'Before we travel further north, I have been thinking about some moments in the history of the Ai-thúda that intrigue me. Have you heard of the mearas? They are a breed of wild horse, white in colour, that was once known to live in Misthallow. The path of the mearas crossed with my people's own many times. North of here, between the Twainmantle and Reikfoss falls, Frumgar first beheld a herd of wild, silver-coated horses running upon the folde. This was the first sighting of the mearas, the mighty steeds with whom the fates of the Ai-thúda would ever after be entwined.

'Perhaps we should go looking for sign of the mearas ourselves?''Do not worry that we have returned empty handed. I will admit that fresh tracks are much more than I would have expected to....'

Léothred trails off, surveying the mist.

'Do you see that? Something silver, yonder in the mist?''Ah, it escaped a closer gaze! Still, we have witnessed something special, just as Frumgar had. Taking the sight of the beautiful beasts as an omen, Frumgar settled his people in these hills. There my people built for themselves a new home. It was a mighty fortress called Fasthálla. From time to time, I can see its shadow above the mist, yonder.'A letter has arrived from Léothred, the Rohirric historian.Léothred can be found at Hlithseld.

You should talk to Léothred at Hlithseld.Talk to Léothred at HlithseldAgátur hands you a letter.

'Léothred wanted me to give this to you when I saw you next.'

The letter is brief:

'${PLAYER}, I am still in Misthallow and wish to talk with you, as soon as you are able.

'Léothred.''Ah, you got my letter.'Captured dwarves are being forced to forge weapons for the enemy in Dûn Traikh!Dwarf-captives can be found in the Angmarim town of Dûn Traikh, in western Elderslade.

You should free dwarf-captives before they are forced to make weapons for the enemy.Zádokh Flint-eye can be found at Drenghól.

You have freed the dwarves in Dûn Traikh. Return to Zádokh Flint-eye for your reward.Return to Zádokh Flint-eye'Our scouts have returned from Dûn Traikh with troubling news. The Angmarim have managed to capture a number of our allies and plan to force them to forge dwarf-made weapons! Free the captives, ${PLAYER}. Dwarves must not be used to arm our enemies, nor shall we leave any of our brethren in their grasp.''Those you freed returned here and spoke highly of your deeds. You have done us a great service on this day, friend.'Whether they were lost in the heat of battle or fell when their wielder was slain, countless weapons litter the battlefield in the War of Three Peaks.Dwarf-make weapons can be found on the battlefield around Zudramdân in the War of Three Peaks.

You have discovered a number of dwarf-make weapons lost in the fighting during the War of Three Peaks. You should collect them for the Gabil'akkâ.Collect dwarf-make weapons lost in the War of Three Peaks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lági Helmbiter can be found at Ifbar-athrâkh.

You have recovered many dwarf-make weapons lost during the War of Three Peaks. You should deliver them to Lági Helmbiter.As you continue in your efforts to aid the Gabil'akkâ, you have discovered a number of weapons of dwarf-make strewn across the battlefield around Zudramdân.

It is likely the Gabil'akkâ will have need of them as the War of Three Peaks draws nearer to the gates of Mount Gundabad, and it would be a great insult to allow the weapons of the dwarves to fall into the hands of Gorgar the Ruthless and his Orcs.

You should collect many dwarf-make weapons and deliver them to Lági Helmbiter.'Ah, good!

'I shall see that these are wielded into battle once more. Those brave dwarves who gave their lives shall be avenged in Durin's name!'Little is known of the time following the defeat of the False King of Angmar, but the forces of the Iron Crown have come to dwell in the shadow of Mount Gundabad.Angmarim scrolls and tomes can be found in the tower, Tûr Ágal, at Caivád Sâr.

Múta has asked you to collect Angmarim scrolls and tomes from the forces of the Iron Crown at Caivád Sâr.Collect Angmarim scrolls in Tûr Ágal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Angmarim tomes in Tûr Ágal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Múta can be found outside Caivád Sâr in northern Elderslade.

You have collected many tomes and scrolls from the forces of the Iron Crown at Caivád Sâr. You should deliver them to Múta.'Oh, and one more thing!

'This settlement is of particular interest to the Gabil'akkâ. After all, we had not expected to encounter forces of the Iron Crown in our march on Gundabad.

'We do not know why they have chosen to return to these lands, but Commander Glóin believes it wise to learn their purpose in Elderslade. I have seen Angmarim bearing scrolls and tomes into their tower, and I think they might allow us the chance to learn more of what the Iron Crown has done since Angmar again fell into ruin.

'Find your way into their tower and recover whatever information you can!''Now, let's see....'

Múta looks over the scrolls and tomes you've collected.

'Hmmph. All this talk of False Kings and secret rifts... it is too much to read on my own!

'You've done well, though. I'll see that these are brought to our allies at Annâk-khurfu.'Within the encampment of Lumrog, Orcs and hobgoblins serve foul hill-trolls that make this place home. If these creatures are dispatched, the trolls will find it difficult to maintain their presence in Misthallow.Within the encampment of Lumrog, Orcs and hobgoblins serve foul hill-trolls that make this place home. If these creatures are dispatched, the trolls will find it difficult to maintain their presence in Misthallow.Defeat Orcs or hobgoblins in LumrogThe encampment of Lumrog echoes not only with the heavy footfalls of hill-trolls, but also with the shrieks and cries of their servants and allies. If these Orcs and hobgoblins are slain, the trolls will find it difficult to maintain their presence in Misthallow.Defeat Orcs or hobgoblins in Lumrog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed.CompletedThe encampment of Lumrog echoes not only with the heavy footfalls of hill-trolls, but also with the shrieks and cries of their servants and allies. If these Orcs and hobgoblins are slain, the trolls will find it difficult to maintain their presence in Misthallow.Without their lackeys, the hill-trolls will find it difficult to maintain their presence in Misthallow. Lumrog has been made safer, if not completely safe, by your efforts.The sound of heavy footsteps shakes the rocks around an encampment of Lumrog. Hill-trolls have settled here and they pose a danger to those in the area.The sound of heavy footsteps shakes the rocks around an encampment of Lumrog. Hill-trolls have settled here and they pose a danger to those in the area.Defeat hill-trolls in LumrogLumrog has long been a home to a group of hill-trolls in Misthallow. The sound of their heavy footsteps shakes the rocks around their encampment striking fear into the hearts of the nearby residents.Defeat hill-trolls in Lumrog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed.CompletedHill-trolls have settled in the Misthallow, and the sound of their heavy footsteps shakes the rocks around their encampment. These creatures pose a danger to any who draw too near to Lumrog and should be defeated.The sound of the trolls stomping around Lumrog has quieted some, thanks to your efforts. Lumrog will never truly be safe, but you have lessened the danger these massive creatures pose for the residents of Misthallow, and that is a good deed.The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has need of your assistance in securing a foothold outside of Gundabad.Hlóthi has requested your aid in completing several tasks outside of Gundabad for the Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: In order to advance this quest, you must complete any four of the required quests.</rgb>Complete 'March on Gundabad: Securing the Slade'Complete 'March on Gundabad: Healing Hands'Complete 'March on Gundabad: Resupplying the Forces'Complete 'March on Gundabad: Torching the Trenches'Complete 'March on Gundabad: Siege Upon Siege Engines'Complete 'March on Gundabad: Pilfering Orkish Orders'Complete 'March on Gundabad: Raising Morale'Locate Hlóthi and inform him of your progress.Talk to Hlóthi'Hail!

'The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has need of your assistance in securing a foothold outside of Gundabad.

'There are several places where we could use your assistance in Elderslade.

'Might you assist us on the battlefield?'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: In order to advance this quest, you must complete any four of the required quests.</rgb>'While there is more to do to assist the war effort, your help has been noted, and we greatly appreciate it.

'Thank you kindly.'The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has need of your assistance in the ongoing war effort.Hlóthi has asked for your assistance in the war effort. The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has requested that you assist the war effort.Complete missions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Your assistance in completing several sorties for the Gabil'akkâ has been greatly noticed.Speak to Hlóthi'The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has need of your assistance in the ongoing war effort.

'Before you, there are a wide array of missions that are required to assist in our cause.

'Seek out and complete these missions and return for a token of our esteem.''Your assistance in the war effort has been paramount to our preparation. Thank you kindly.'Numerous wounded soldiers have been stranded on the battlefield, unable to receive aid.You can find injured soldiers scattered across enemy territory, beyond the dwarves' trenches at Ifbar-athrâkh. More soldiers have been stranded in Azgh-buzru, but Hlóthi has suggested bringing allies if you go there.

You should tend to these soldiers' wounds so that they may return to safety.Tend to (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}) injured soldiersThe soldiers you tended to will seek treatment from the healers.

Hlóthi in Annâk-khurfu will want to know that you've honoured his request.Talk to Hlóthi'There's fear of fever in the trenches, and that's one enemy we can't defeat with steel. But our healers are unable to treat the wounded that have been stranded on the battlefield.

'Find these injured soldiers in the enemy territory that lies beyond our trenches at Ifbar-athrâkh. Do what you can to ease their suffering so that they may return on their own.

'You may be more fortuitous in this endeavour if you strike out north-east to Azgh-buzru, but bring your allies if you decide to do so.''You have saved their lives, and the lives of others. We'll have a better chance now of staving off illness in the trenches.'Intercepting Orkish correspondences will give the Gabil'akkâ insight into the plans of the enemy.Orkish orders can be found across the War of Three Peaks.

You should gather Orkish orders to help the Gabil'akkâ's cause.Collect elite Orkish orders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Orkish orders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hlóthi is in Annak-khurfu in southern Elderslade.

Return to Hlóthi.'While you are out among the enemy, keep your eyes open for any correspondences that might give to us some insight into their operations. Anything you can find could give us the edge when we plan our attacks.''Excellent work, ${CLASS}. These may just give us the advantage we need!'War affects not just the body, but also the mind. The horrors of the War of Three Peaks have caused some Gabil'akkâ soldiers to lose hope.The dwarf-trenches have been dug along the main road towards Gundabad.

Hlóthi has asked that you sing to disheartened soldiers in the trenches, so that you may bolster their spirits.You have sung songs for several disheartened soldiers and bolstered their spirits.

Hlóthi in Zarkul-sulûn is waiting for you to report back.Talk to Hlóthi'If we are to win this war, our soldiers being in low spirits won't do! Are you up to the task of singing to them, ${PLAYER}?

'You must have heard many songs during your travels. Perhaps you could bolster our soldiers' spirits with a few. Go forth and bring some light to our disheartened soldiers in the trenches.''The war may be far from over, but your singing has allowed our soldiers to forget their sorrows, if only for a little while. Thank you.'Delivering fresh supplies to the scattered Gabil'akkâ battalions is paramount to the war effort.There are empty supply crates in Shakal-atrâd, Ifbar-athrâkh, the trenches, and on the docked boat. You should deliver the supplies and replenish the crates.

Shakal-atrâd lies to the north-east of Zarkul-sulûn, and Ifbar-athrâkh is close to the forward-most dwarf trench. The dwarf-trenches can be found along the main road towards Gundabad, and the boat near the lake's south-eastern shore.Replenish supply crates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have distributed fresh supplies among the Gabil'akkâ.

Hlóthi awaits news in Zarkul-sulûn.'We've received a fresh shipment of supplies that requires distribution among our battalions.

'Deposit these in the supply crates in the trenches and on the boat docked at the lakeshore, as well as the crates in Shakal-atrâd and Ifbar-athrâkh.''You've assisted us in keeping the pressure on our foes, and for that, the Gabil'akkâ thanks you.'Foes in the War of Three Peaks must be defeated to help the Gabil'akkâ press forward to Gundabad.Foes can be found throughout the War of Three Peaks.

