'Take one of the nearby powder kegs and burst them into the heavens. You shall have to make quick work of this task, however, as the fuses will not last forever.''Haha! Tell me, were they scrambling for safety? Great job, friend.'You have solved the mystery of the Secret Stones and the Shadowed King!Complete 'The Shadowed King'Mozbuk the Hobgoblin delights in feasting upon unwary travellers in Misthallow. Only by facing him with might and courage can his reign of terror be ended.Unwary travellers in Misthallow have long been preyed upon by a foul hobgoblin known as Mozbuk. Through courage and force of will, you may put an end this reign of terror.Find MozbukMozbuk the Hobgoblin delights in feasting upon unwary travellers in Misthallow. Only by facing him with might and courage can his reign of terror be ended.Defeat MozbukCompleted.CompletedTales of Mozbuk the Hobgoblin have spread far and wide, striking fear into the hearts of all who hear them. It is said that only by facing him with might and courage can his reign of terror be ended, and you think you might be just the ${RACE} to accomplish it.You put an end to the villainous tales of the hobgoblin Mozbuk, who did not seem quite as fearsome as you expected. Still, you are certain that the end of his story will not spread as quickly as did his legend, and Mozbuk will remain a frightful visage with which parents will frighten misbehaving children. At least Mozbuk himself will do no more harm in Misthallow, no matter what his legend might accomplish elsewhere.Defeat many merrevail and mervyl in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many merrevail and mervyl in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many merrevail and mervyl in Imlad MorgulDefeat many merrevail and mervyl in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many merrevail and mervyl in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many merrevail and mervyl in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many merrevail and mervyl in Imlad MorgulAid the Kharum-ubnâr and complete every mission they offer you in service of Prince Durin as he prepares to reclaim Mount Gundabad.Aid the Kharum-ubnâr and complete every mission they offer you in service of Prince Durin as he prepares to reclaim Mount Gundabad.Complete 'Mission: Respite in Zarkul-sulûn'Complete 'Mission: Wrath of the Frost-heart'Complete 'Mission: Securing the Redhorn'Complete 'Mission: Trinkets of the Lost Garrison'Complete 'Mission: Defilers in the Dale'Complete 'Mission: Enemies at the East-gate'Complete 'Mission: Standards of Khazad-dûm'Complete 'Mission: Claws of Gabilshathûr'Complete 'Mission: Trouble at the High Crag'Complete 'Mission: Keepers of the Narrow Way'A frantic Lúkhag has returned without Aighrig.Lúkhag hangs from a tree in front of Annâk-khurfu.

You should go to her and see where she'll lead you.Approach LúkhagYou should inform Rékkur of what you've learned about Gáfin's discovery.Talk to Rékkur'Lúkhag flew back while you were gone and pestered me to no end! I believe she wants to lead me somewhere, but I can't abandon my post, nor does she seem to trust anyone other than us.

'Please follow her, ${PLAYER}. I have a feeling that you'll find Aighrig at the end of all this.'Lúkhag chirps in affirmation before leading you away from Annâk-khurfu.

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'You've returned, and in one piece! Aighrig doesn't seem to be herself, but I won't ask you what happened; she can tell me herself if she wishes.'Hoping to aid King Thorin in guiding the Prince to victory, Hersegg, grand-daughter of Hermáth Stormhammer, has offered to tell you the tragic tale of Nár.Hersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in Erebor, the Lonely Mountain.

Hersegg has offered to tell you Nár's tale as transcribed by her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hersegg.Talk to HerseggHersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in Erebor, the Lonely Mountain.

You have heard Hersegg's telling of Nár's tale as transcribed by her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hersegg.Talk to Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar'So you wish to hear the tale of Nár? I must warn you, ${PLAYER}, it is quite grim — even for a retelling!

'Ah, but first....'

Hersegg glances around Akrâz-zahar, making careful note of the dwarves still present.

'Ah good, it seems Frithgeir has taken him home. Nár is an old dwarf, and though it is no fault of his own, he is often forgetful and confused in his mind. It is as if the stones of a great mosaic were scattered upon the floor — all of the pieces remain in some form or another, but what it once depicted is lost.

'Even so, neither I nor anyone else in this hall would tell the tale in his presence!'

Hersegg lifts a small volume from her hip and flips through its pages, stopping at one page in particular.

'Let us begin.''Are you ready to hear the tale of Nár, ${PLAYER}?''As for Nár, there is far more to be said of his tale, but I shall tell it as briefly as I might.

'Nár was brought to Thráin in Zudrugund and there told his tale, and spoke the name of Azog, which all Longbeards have held with hatred ever since. All Thrór's court wept at the tidings, and tore their beards, then looked to Thráin who sat down heavily upon his father's throne and was silent.

'Breaking the silence, Thorin said, "You are King now, Father. What is your will? How shall we answer this outrage?"

'All around the court, hands went to sword-hilt and axe-handle, and brows lowered darkly. But still Thráin sat quiet, and did not move. Seven days he remained thus, still as a stone, saying no word. Then, as a storm long gathering that breaks upon the mountainside, he arose, eyes ablaze, and cried: "This cannot be borne!"

'From Thráin's yearning for vengeance arose the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, called simply the War of the Dwarves and Orcs in our memory. Ah, but that is another tale!'Explore the several natural curiosities to be found within the Wells of Langflood.Explore the various natural curiosities to be found within the Wells of Langflood.Explore TithrozExplore Reikfoss of GreylinExplore the TwainmantleExplore VeithhólExplore Scraper's CloughExplore the Cabed RhimdathAfter discovering a number of intact Orkish arrows left behind at Zarkul-sulûn, Rádek has devised a plan to 'return' them to the Orcs of Gundabad.Intact Orkish arrows can be found scattered in the ground at Zarkul-sulûn.

Hoping to arm Zhélruka archers, Rádek has asked you to collect intact Orkish arrows from the ground at Zarkul-sulûn.Collect bundles of intact Orkish arrows at Zarkul-sulûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Zhélruka archers can be found at Zarkul-sulûn.

You have collected the Orkish arrows and should now deliver them to Zhélruka archers at Zarkul-sulûn.Rádek can be found at Zarkul-sulûn.

You have armed the Zhélruka archers and should now report back to Rádek.Talk to Rádek'Bah! The Orcs at Zarkul-sulûn were weak!

'I am as pleased as Glóin that we have gained a new foothold, but many battles still await us.

'Look around you, ${PLAYER}. Countless Orkish arrows litter the ground and many of them are still intact. There is a tradition in my family to always return a lost weapon to its rightful owner. In the case of the Orcs of Gundabad, it seems only fitting that the keen-eyed archers of the Zhélruka 'return' them.

'Find as many intact arrows as you can. I will see that each Orc shall have one in their time!''Do not worry, ${PLAYER}.

'We Zhélruka will make sure every last arrow is returned to Gorgar and his Orcs! Hah!'Goblin-assassins of Gundabad stalk the battlefield around Zudramdân and seek to put an end to unwary dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ.Gundabad goblin-assassins can be found on the battlefield around Zudramdân.

Goblin-assassins of Gundabad stalk the battlefield around Zudramdân and seek to put an end to unwary dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ. You should defeat them.Defeat goblin-assassins on the battlefield around Zudramdân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many of the goblin-assassins of Gundabad stalking the battlefield around Zudramdân.CompletedWhile aiding the war effort in Elderslade, you have been ambushed by a goblin-assassin of Gundabad.

Hardier than the others of their kind fighting in the War of Three Peaks, these goblins wield their hidden blades for Gorgar the Ruthless and have been sent forth to slay the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ before they can march to the gates of Mount Gundabad.

You should defeat as many of these goblin-assassins as you can in the War of Three Peaks.You have defeated many of the goblin-assassins of Gundabad stalking the battlefield around Zudramdân. With the goblins routed, the Gabil'akkâ can now press onward to Mount Gundabad unhindered by hidden blades.Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ have been captured and brought to Bagûd-mekhem where they shall soon be slain by the Orcs loyal to Gorgar the Ruthless.Captured dwarves can be found at Bagûd-mekhem.

After receiving word that dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ have been captured and brought to Bagûd-mekhem, Dréri hopes to see them freed before they are slain. You should free captured dwarves at Bagûd-mekhem.Free captured dwarves at Bagûd-mekhem (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dréri can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks.

You have freed a number of captured dwarves at Bagûd-mekhem. You should report your success to Dréri.Talk to Dréri at Drenghól'${PLAYER}, I have an urgent task for you!

'Through your efforts, we have gained significant ground at Azgh-buzru. However, I have just received word that several of our warriors were captured in battle and taken to Bagûd-mekhem.

'If I have learned one thing about Gorgar, it is that he does not suffer unneeded prisoners. Once the amusement of his Orcs is sated, dwarves who are not deemed useful to him are slain and beheaded.

'We cannot allow that fate to befall any more dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ! Go to Bagûd-mekhem and free our allies before it is too late!''Ah! You return.

'The dwarves you freed from Bagûd-mekhem were sent to recover at Zarkul-sulûn. I am told they will all survive, but I know well enough that not all wounds are so easily healed.

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'The supply of twistbeard is running low for the soldiers at Ashmargathâl. Swamped with responsibilities, Lúka finds herself asking for aid.Lúka has asked you to collect some twistbeard.

Twistbeard can be found on rocks in Tharkh Shathur, to the south-east of Ashmargathâl.Collect twistbeard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected all the twistbeard you could find.

You should return to Ashmargathâl and give the twistbeard to Lúka.Talk to LúkaLúka has asked you to clean the wounds of injured scouts.

The scouts are resting around Ashmargathâl.You should let Lúka know that you have cleaned the scouts' wounds.Talk to Lúka'I'll begin studying this sapper-bomb right away -- the materials used for its construction might give us a clue as to where they're being made. From what Mekhnet found out, a goblin named Thraunákh crafts these bombs. We don't know where he's located, but his sapper-bombs have spread throughout the Orc camps.

'However, if I study this bomb, I'm afraid I won't have time to pick twistbeard. I thought I'd picked enough yesterday but... our supply dwindles.

'Could you help me collect some? I usually find twistbeard on rocks in Tharkh Shathur, south-east from here. If you follow the road, you won't miss it.''I'll make sure this twistbeard is usable; in the meantime, could you clean the wounds of a few of our injured scouts? The last thing I want is for infection and fever to sweep through our ranks.''Thank you. Now that I do not have to worry about our twistbeard supply, we can continue focusing on the problem of the sapper-bombs.'Unsatisfied with his progress, Halvar has decided to scrounge around for more ingredients.Halvar has asked you to retrieve some dried meat from a rations crate, but he's not sure which one.

The crates can be found around Ashmargathâl.You should deliver the dried meats to Halvar, who's waiting by one of the camp-fires in Ashmargathâl.Dági can be found somewhere in Ashmargathâl.

To complete the dish, Halvar would like for you to ask Dági for some beer.Ask Dági for beerHalvar is waiting by one of the camp-fires in Ashmargathâl.

You should bring the beer to him.'Hermáth -- this harthrót is, without a doubt, the worst thing I've ever had the displeasure to cook. It is tough and refuses to soften no matter what I try. Small wonder that nobody has used it before!

'But we aren't in a position to choose. Even if I must cook it for hours on end, I will not let this plant defeat me!

'Still, there must be more we can add to this dish. I have some dried meat stored in... erm... well, it's in one of the rations crates around the camp. Could you help me find some?''Pairing this meat with the harthrót might just work, but... argh, there's just something missing, something... oh, I don't know, let's just throw some beer in! See what happens!

'I don't have beer on hand, but Dági does. He should be nearby; ask him if we could take some.''Well... normally I'd rather save my alcohol for special occasions, but if Halvar is trying to make our food taste good, then count me in! Here you go -- best of luck!''All right then, shoo! I have work to do.'

Halvar begins to cobble together the ingredients you gave him. After a while, he calls you over.

'Hermáth, this... this isn't bad. I'll have to keep working on it. It's nowhere near the level of food I could make back home, but it's a start. Here, have a taste!

'See? We've created something good, my friend.'With Rúzat, Agátur, and Náth waiting for word from Grimbeorn, they set their restless minds to the old Dwarf-ruins of Sundergrót.Náth cam be found in Limlók.

