You should talk to Rúzat outside of Sundergrót.Talk to Rúzat outside of Sundergrót'The old Dwarf-hold of Sundergrót! It is nearby to the west, is it not? Let us explore the ruins. Perhaps we can find something useful there! I am sure the Beornings of Limlók will be pleased with us leaving their village for a while! Náth, what do you say?''Ah yes, Sundergrót. I have been studying the northern dwarf-holds during my time in Erebor. Sundergrót is an old structure, but it should be well-preserved; know you not how impressive is dwarf-craft? I agree with Agátur that it would be worth a survey. I know many have their eyes on Gundabad, and I do not blame them for that! But there are other Dwarf-holds still worth surveying, and not just the Mountain-home! Come, let us depart.''Náth wishes to have Sundergrót surveyed for minerals to see if the depths are rich enough to return to for mining. Make this your primary concern, but watch out for goblins. There are plenty lurking about! Anything you could do to thwart them would be much appreciated, my friend!''Ah, we all return and the survey was a great success! I believe we have found Sundergrót to remain a useful dwarf-hold! We must bring this knowledge back to Skarháld with us!''I thank you for clearing the old watch-posts, my friend! You have done a great service to us, and to the Beornings. The fewer the goblins in the Floodfells, the better, no? Ha, now let us continue with the survey mission!

'I have taken a glance inside Sundergrót and I am sure you can guess what it is I saw in there! Oh, that is correct, my friend: many more goblins lurking inside. Bah, too many for only the four of us. If we are crafty, we should be able to survey all of Sundergrót and thwart whatever plans those goblins have with the old dwarf-hold. Now let us continue on our mission.''Bah, this place is crawling with goblins! Did you see the old ruins on our way from Skerabrygg to Sundergrót? Aye, Stramvárth and Egvárth, those old watch-posts are called. I would recommend we scout them ourselves and take care of any goblins lurking about the old ruins. You can not be too careful!'Defeat many Orc-kind in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many Orc-kind in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many Orc-kind in Imlad MorgulDefeat many Orc-kind in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many Orc-kind in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many Orc-kind in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many Orc-kind in Imlad MorgulMany were the Orcs slain during the Battle of Azanulbizar.Many were the Orcs slain during the Battle of Azanulbizar.Learn of the Orcs slain at AzanulbizarMany were the Orcs slain during the Battle of Azanulbizar.Many were the Orcs slain during the Battle of Azanulbizar.Learn of the Orcs slain at AzanulbizarDefeat many Orcs in Elderslade.Defeat many Orcs in Elderslade.Defeat Orcs in EldersladeDefeat many Orcs in Elderslade.Defeat many Orcs in Elderslade.Defeat Orcs in EldersladeDefeat many Orcs in Gloomingtarn.Defeat many Orcs in Gloomingtarn.Defeat many Orcs in GloomingtarnDefeat many Orcs in Gloomingtarn.Defeat many Orcs in Gloomingtarn.Defeat many Orcs in GloomingtarnThe Orcs of the Ufúrzrak, Azog's clan, dwell within and without the old kingdom of Khazad-dûm.Ufúrzrak Orcs and thrug-hai can be found at Muru Azog, before the East-gate of Nud-mekhem at Azanulbizar.

