You should defeat the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog.Defeat Ufúrzrak Orcs at Muru Azog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ufúrzrak thrug-hai at Muru Azog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many Orcs of the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog.CompletedEncamped in the very shadows of Nud-mekhem, the East-gate, the Orcs of the Ufúrzrak have laid claim to Khazad-dûm in the name of their chieftain, Azog. Determined to keep hold of their would-be realm, countless Orcs of the Ufúrzrak, including the vicious and powerful thrug-hai, have gathered before the East-gate.

You should defeat the Orcs and thrug-hai of the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog.Although the halls of Khazad-dûm still teem with Orcs, you have done much to thin the numbers of the Ufúrzrak and weaken Azog's hold on Azanulbizar.An Orc has stolen Oda's sole set of armourer's tools.The Orc who stole Oda's tools retreated to Târ-kútoz, the Orc camp to the west of Ashmargathâl. However, Oda does not know which Orc is responsible.

You should defeat Orcs to see which one has her tools.Defeat the Orc who has Oda's toolsYou have found Oda's tools.

You should return them to her at Ashmargathâl.'One of those Orcs stole my tools! Supplies are scarce up here, and those are the only tools I've got to work with. But there's no way I can follow him into that camp; I'm just an armourer! Argh, I'll be damned if a single Orc ruins our soldiers' armour!

'You're able to fight, aren't you? If you're going west into Târ-kútoz, could you help me find the culprit? I can't say I know which Orc took my tools, but if you find dwarf-made armourer's tools, those are mine.''Finally! I can continue working, the soldiers can get their armour repaired, and the Orcs can't lay their nasty hands on my tools. If you ever need your armour repaired, feel free to come to me!'There is always work to be done at the Beorninghús.Wild berries can be found in the Beorninglands.

