You should bring them to Thrúthug at Drenghól.'Been waitin' for a shipment of healing supplies, but I haven't seen nor heard any sign of it. Scouts reported Orcs carrying the crates off to their camp, Hanksar-mokh, to the west. And now I have more injured dwarves than supplies to spare.

'I'm thinkin' you can get the supplies back, though. Whatever is left in those crates should be easy enough to carry on your own.

'I'd wager the Orcs keep the supplies close at hand while resting at their camp-fires.''Nicely done. I'll put these to good use.'Dwarf-bodies litter the battlefield around Durin's Stone. Their arms and armour must not fall into the hands of the enemy.Fallen dwarves are strewn across the field near Durin's Stone.

