Bring the arms and armour to Dráttur.Return to Dráttur'The field around Durin's Stone has seen much bloodshed. The fallen from each side lie piled upon each other, food for the carrion birds. The enemy keeps watch on the field and are rearing to fight. They would swiftly attack and overwhelm a group sent to collect our slain comrades. One quick, nimble dwarf, however, might be able to retrieve their arms and armour without rousing our foes.

'Go forth; gather helmets, shields, and swords from our brothers. The Orcs must not be allowed to steal their arms and armour.''A grim task, this. We shall collect the bodies of our brothers when there is more time, and honour their deeds.'After completing your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you have decided to reflect upon some of what you have learned.The Azanulbizar Reflecting Pool can be found at Amdân.

