You have reflected upon one of the tales of Azanulbizar as recounted by Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at AmdânAfter completing your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar, you have decided to reflect upon some of what you have learned.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Completing any of the following at the Azanulbizar Reflecting Pool will advance this quest: 'Nár's Tale', 'Council of the Seven', 'Bonds of Oak and Iron', 'The Lord of Moria', or 'A Final Reckoning'.</rgb>'I thank you, dear reader, for reflecting upon my writings once again. It was not a simple task to recount them, but it was my duty on behalf of Durin's Folk.

'It is my hope that like the many-faceted gem, new details and considerations will reveal themselves to you as you further explore these tales!'A wax-sealed letter, delivered in haste, contains a personal request from Glóin, father of Gimli and hero of the Lonely Mountain.Glóin can be found in the war-room at Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.

You should talk to Glóin.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: Mission Recruiters are available to deliver you there with haste. Mission Recruiters can be found at Thorin's Gate, Gondamon, Bree-town, The Twenty-first Hall, Othrikar, Gabilshathûr, Glóin's Camp, Hrimbarg, Galtrev, The Dolven-view, Magh Ashtu, Járnfast, Erebor, and Minas Tirith (Midsummer).</rgb>Talk to Glóin at Annâk-khurfu${PLAYER},

Despite our many triumphs, the War of Three Peaks has taken a great toll. To some among the Gabil'akkâ, victory seems no closer than it did when Prince Durin first swore his oath before the Anvil of Winterstith.

Gorgar, son of Bolg, still eludes us. Wittingly or not, that accursed cold-dragon, Hrímil Frost-heart, allowed him to escape his doom. It is little comfort that there is no love lost between the two of them, for their hatred of dwarves might prove enough to set aside their enmities at least for the moment. All is not lost, and I stand by my words, but it is difficult for the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ to see the battle on the threshold of Gundabad as anything but a costly setback. And, to the mind of Prince Durin, an unforgivable defeat.

Although he has not said it aloud or so plainly, Prince Durin has set his thoughts upon vengeance. In truth, he contemplates a great offensive to breach the gates and reclaim Mount Gundabad at all cost. I will not overstep the bounds of my station, but I am an old enough dwarf to know that the hunt for vengeance might prove just as deadly as any weapon our foes might wield against us.

Prince Durin knows well the worth of your counsel, and I believe that together you and I might convince him to weigh the wisest course to this war's end. And so, I humbly request that you return to Annâk-khurfu.

Let us speak soon, my friend.

-Glóin'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you received my letter? I suppose in times of war nothing is certain, so I am thankful for that at least!'As Celeborn leads a company of brave adventurers into the depths of the Remmorchant seeking to bring about the final defeat of his ancient foe Ungwetári, Rûkhor the Pale Herald enacts his vile plan to unleash the unending hunger of Shelob the Great upon all of Middle-earth.As Celeborn leads a company of brave adventurers into the depths of the Remmorchant seeking to bring about the final defeat of his ancient foe Ungwetári, Rûkhor the Pale Herald enacts his vile plan to unleash the unending hunger of Shelob the Great upon all of Middle-earth.Complete 'Remmorchant, the Net of Darkness -- Tier 1'Complete 'Remmorchant, the Net of Darkness -- Tier 2'Complete 'Remmorchant, the Net of Darkness -- Tier 3'You were one of the first adventurers to enter the Remmorchant and triumph over Shelob the Great, last child of Ungoliant.You were one of the first adventurers to enter the Remmorchant and triumph over Shelob the Great, last child of Ungoliant.Be among the first to fully complete Remmorchant, the Net of Darkness on Tier 3You were one of the first adventurers to enter the Remmorchant and triumph over Shelob the Great, last child of Ungoliant.You were one of the first adventurers to enter the Remmorchant and triumph over Shelob the Great, the last child of Ungoliant.Be among the first to fully complete Remmorchant, the Net of Darkness on Tier 2As Celeborn leads a company of brave adventurers into the depths of the Remmorchant seeking to bring about the final defeat of his ancient foe Ungwetári, Rûkhor the Pale Herald enacts his vile plan to unleash the unending hunger of Shelob the Great upon all of Middle-earth.As Celeborn leads a company of brave adventurers into the depths of the Remmorchant seeking to bring about the final defeat of his ancient foe Ungwetári, Rûkhor the Pale Herald enacts his vile plan to unleash the unending hu