ood, the horrific daughters of Shelob, lurk within the tunnels of the Remmorchant.Defeat GragaragDefeat GuruthangDefeat GamnagolThe Queensbrood, the horrific daughters of Shelob, lurk within the tunnels of the Remmorchant.The Queensbrood, the horrific daughters of Shelob, lurk within the tunnels of the Remmorchant.Defeat GragaragDefeat GuruthangDefeat GamnagolDaughter of Shelob and queen of all Gredbyg, Thossulun the Massive is a formidable foe. You must defeat her to cease the endless tide of insects plaguing your allies.Daughter of Shelob and queen of all Gredbyg, Thossulun the Massive is a formidable foe. You must defeat her to cease the endless tide of insects plaguing your allies.Defeat Thossulun the MassiveDaughter of Shelob and queen of all Gredbyg, Thossulun the Massive is a formidable foe. You must defeat her to cease the endless tide of insects plaguing your allies.Daughter of Shelob and queen of all Gredbyg, Thossulun the Massive is a formidable foe. You must defeat her to cease the endless tide of insects plaguing your allies.Defeat Thossulun the MassiveDaughter of Shelob and queen of all Gredbyg, Thossulun the Massive is a formidable foe. You must defeat her to cease the endless tide of insects plaguing your allies.Daughter of Shelob and queen of all Gredbyg, Thossulun the Massive is a formidable foe. You must defeat her to cease the endless tide of insects plaguing your allies.Defeat Thossulun the MassiveAlthough Khazad-dûm was abandoned long ago, remnants of its splendour might still be found in Azanulbizar.Although Khazad-dûm was abandoned long ago, remnants of its splendour might still be found in Azanulbizar.Learn of AmdânLearn of GabilthurkhuLearn of Labam-gairuLearn of Khur AzanLearn of Kibil-nâlaLearn of Tharkh ShathurLearn of AshmargathâlLearn of Atrad-zarakhLearn of Tharkh BarazLearn of Anlakh-zelegLearn of Tharkh ZigilLearn of ZirakazhârLearn of Kheled-zâramLearn of Durinul’abanLearn of Nud-mekhemOn the snowy slopes of Barazinbar, goblin warg-riders guard the blockade at Zaghúth.Warg-riders of Moria can be found at Zaghúth.

You should defeat Warg-riders of Moria at Zaghúth.Defeat Warg-riders of Moria at ZaghúthWarg-riders of Moria can be found at Zaghúth.

You should defeat Warg-riders of Moria at Zaghúth.Defeat Warg-riders of Moria at Zaghúth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many Warg-riders of Moria at Zaghúth.CompletedWhile exploring the heights of the Redhorn Pass, you have come across the Orkish encampment of Zaghúth. Within Zaghúth, a small company of Warg-riders of Moria keep watch on the pass and ensure that no unwanted guests enter the realm of Azog.

You should defeat the Warg-riders of Moria at Zaghúth.Although the Redhorn Pass remains blocked, your defeat of the Warg-riders of Moria has loosened the Orcs' grip on Barazinbar.The Beorning Langhár is weary of spies encroaching upon Zarkul-sulûn and wishes to defeat them before they learn of the dwarves' war plans.Goblin spies can be found near Zarkul-sulûn.

You should recover notes from goblin spies.Recover notes from goblin spies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Langhár can found at Zarkul-sulûn.

You should talk to Langhár.Talk to LanghárA fire pit is located at Zarkul-sulûn.

You should burn the goblin notes in the fire pit.'Hail, ${PLAYER}. I have not the time to ask of your adventures since last we met in the Wolf-denes. While I would very much like to hear those stories, they will have to wait.

'We have noticed goblin spies about, lurking in the shadows. The enemy is trying to steal our plans of war. We can not let this happen. Let us find these goblin spies and take back any notes they have collect thus far.''Good, you recovered all the notes? Now then, let me see these. There is not much information on these scrawls but there is enough to be useful to the enemy. I have seen enough. Go and burn it.'Explore the various ruined structures to be found within the Wells of Langflood.Explore the various ruins that dot the hills and valleys throughout the Wells of Langflood.Find SundergrótFind the White MareFind SkerabryggFind Hengi's LeapFind FramsburgFind LumrogFind StramvárthFind EgvárthFind DúnabryggGori Stonesetter wishes to walk among the ruins his ancestors built ages past.Gori Stonesetter can be found in Amdân.

Gori has asked you to accompany him to the bridge that crosses the Kibil-nâla.Talk to Gori to travel to the ruinsGori Stonesetter can be found in Amdân.

Gori has asked you to talk with him in Amdân.Talk to Gori'I heard that you are heading east, towards the Kibil-nâla. I am Gori Stonesetter, Master Architect. An ancestor of mine worked to build bridges and buildings about the valley in ages past, when Khazad-dûm was still ours.

'I wish to examine the nearby ruins, but I need someone with a strong arm to mind my back. If you are of a mind to help, I would greatly appreciate it.''Let us travel the old ways of our forefathers!''Long have I desired to stand under those arches, and on those bridges. You have given me a wonderful gift on this day, my friend. You have my thanks.

'There is much work to be done, but first this damnable war must be won. Let us hope that the damage from the conflicts to come are minimum. We have much to learn from those who built before.'A celebration is in order after the fall of Lumrog and Gúrbarash's cowardly flight.Skarding can be found at Thokvist.

You should talk to Skarding.Talk to Skarding Wargsbane at ThokvistFanglind can be found at Thokvist.

You should talk to Fanglind.Talk to Fanglind at Thokvist'While I must remain vigilant over the passes of Misthallow, tonight we celebrate our victory! I have called upon my friends and kin to join us!''Let us show you what it means to be a Beorning. Run wild with us, ${PLAYER}!''Greetings, ${PLAYER}. No, I have not seen Skarding since last night. Do not worry. He spends more time in the woods than at Thokvist. I am sure he will return soon enough.

'It was indeed a pleasure to fight by your side. Now I understand the high praise you have received from my brethren. Perhaps we shall meet again. Until that day, farewell, my good ${RACE}.'The Orcs of Gundabad carry many orders into battle, but the most closely-guarded plans of Gorgar the Ruthless are held by his trench-commanders.Gundabad trench-commanders and Orkish orders can be found in the trenches around Zudramdân in the War of Three Peaks.

In addition to seeking to intercept a missive from Gorgar the Ruthless, Agnar Brokentooth has also asked you to collect Orkish orders from the forces of Gundabad.Collect Orkish orders in the trenches around Zudramdân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect a missive from a Gundabad trench-commanderAgnar Brokentooth can be found at Ifbar-athrâkh.

You have collected many Orkish orders and also recovered a missive from Gorgar the Ruthless. You should deliver them to Agnar Brokentooth.'If I have learned anything about Gorgar the Ruthless, it is that he is cunning in his misdirection.

'The orders held by many of his Orcs are often partly or wholly untruthful, and they exist only to confound the plans of Gabil'akkâ.

'However, my scouts have reason to believe that a few among his forces bear missives written by Gorgar's own hand, and I do not doubt them. It is rumoured that these missives are held by the trench-commanders of Gundabad, but I cannot say for certain if they all carry them.

'I have a task for you, ${PLAYER}.

'In addition to collecting orders from the Orcs on the battlefield, you are to find one of these missives and deliver it to me here in Ifbar-athrâkh. If these missives are indeed Gorgar's will, we might learn what few truths can be gleaned from the others Orcs' orders.''You were able to find one of the missives? That is excellent news!

'Now, let me have a look at this....'

Agnar studies the missive you've recovered and compares it to a few of the Orkish orders you collected.

'Ah-ha! There are many inconsistencies between the missive and the other orders, but each mentions the passage called Ushkútoz we recently discovered beneath Zudramdân. It seems that Gorgar plans to send one of his most-trusted lieutenants to Ushkútoz to oversee the destruction of Ifbar-athrâkh and the routing of the Gabil'akkâ.

'This may be just what we need to break the stalemate! I shall prepare a plan of attack at once!'Thyra, daughter of Runerik and Yrsa, seeks to save the creatures of the Floodfells from the Wargs who stalk the wilds.Goats in trouble may be found in the Floodfells.

You should save any goats who are in trouble.Save goats from Wargs in the Floodfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Warg encampment of Ujâk-fulug is located in the Floodfells.

You should seek out Ujâk-fulug.Find the Warg encampment of Ujâk-fulug in the FloodfellsThe Warg encampment of Ujâk-fulug is located in the Floodfells.

You should burn any goat corpses at Ujâk-fulug.Burn goat corpses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The Warg menace is only getting worse. Do you hate Wargs as well? It looks like we share a common interest after all! The worst of it is how the goats of the Floodfells have suffered at the fangs of the beasts that came over the mountains. 

'Would you patrol the Floodfells in search of any goats in trouble? It would mean a lot to me. If you do venture to Ujâk-fulug, I hear that the hillside is painted in corpses of slain animals. Burn the goat corpses you find, will you? Let us deny the Wargs their spoils. Grr, I will rip the throat out of the next Warg that assaults Limlók!'Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, wishes to learn more about the great worm, Scatha, whose history weaves closely with that of the great warrior, Fram.Léothred can be found at Hlithseld.

You should talk to Léothred at Hlithseld.Talk to Léothred at HlithseldLéothred can be found at Hlithseld.

You should talk to Léothred at Hlithseld.Talk to Léothred at HlithseldLéothred wishes to return to Framsburg.

You should talk to Léothred at Framsburg.Talk to Léothred at Framsburg'My friend, ${PLAYER}. I am glad that you are here. I have been pondering the well known Rohirric tale of Fram and Scatha. While I am certain that the tale is true, I have often questioned some of Fram's actions. If you would continue to be my guide in the north a little while longer, I would be ever so grateful, for I wish to continue learning and writing the story of my people.

'Fram is but half the tale I wish to learn more about. What of Scatha, the worm? Perhaps it was the dwarves’ arrival in the Grey Mountains that awoke Scatha from slumber. Perhaps it was the coming of the Ai-thúda, and the slaughter and flight of the Gundabad Orcs after Angmar’s fall. I believe that answers will lie in the north.'

<rgb=#00FF00>While it is not required, it is recommended that you have completed Léothred's journey through the Wells of Langflood before beginning the The Folly of Scatha and Fram.</rgb>'Scatha’s bite carried a flesh-rotting poison, such that Fram was forced to cut off his own father’s sword-arm to save his life. Even after this maiming, Frumgar remained sickly and weak for the rest of his days.

'Come, let us return to Framsburg. There is more to learn in the ruins there.''This truth is certain. A year after Durin’s folk departed the Ered Mithrin to follow King Thráin to Erebor, the great long-worm spilled forth from his secret cavern. Angry and ravenous, Scatha attacked the Ai-thúda, ravaging their herds and scorching Fasthálla itself with his destructive breath.''Fasthálla once stood here. Now we can only see the ruins of Framsburg, built upon Fasthálla's ruins, after Scatha's attack.'The Beorning Varthmath knows that supplies are limited in battle and wishes to scavenge the battlefield for weapons to repair.Broken swords can be found scattered across the battlefield.

You should collect any broken swords that you find.Collect broken swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Varthmath can be found at Zarkul-sulûn.

You should give the broken swords to Varthmath.'${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. When Grimbeorn declared that we were to assist the dwarves, I knew that I must come here. During my time in Moria, I learned a great many things from the dwarves. Now I look to repay their hospitality by fighting along side them. If we make it to Gundabad, I am going in with them.

'For now, I am focused with assisting the forge-workers, but they have informed me that metal to forge is becoming scarce. We should find more metals on the battlefield. Would you be able to traverse the battlefield and collect any broken weapons that you come across?''Thank you for these broken swords, ${PLAYER}. This will keep the forge workers busy for a while and keep weapons in our hands during battle!'Explore the many dreadful and worrisome locations to be found within Cirith Ungol.Explore the many dreadful and worrisome locations to be found within Cirith Ungol.Explore the Straight StairExplore the Winding StairExplore Echad TaerdimExplore Cadar SkûsExplore Torech UngolExplore the RemmorchantExplore TaurlingolExplore KaslokrozThe scout Laugi needs assistance completing his survey of the nearby enemy camp.Zarkul-sulûn is in southern Elderslade.

Laugi has asked you to scout Zarkul-sulûn.Scout the lower campScout the east portion of the campScout the southern section of the campExamine the back of the campGunvald is in Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.

You have enough information to make a report to Gunvald.Talk to Gunvald'If Gunvald sent you, then he must trust you. I must return to our base and get this scratch tended to or my wife will never let me hear the end of it.

'I was on my way to scout the camp ahead when I was beset upon by the enemy. Will you go scout ahead and report your findings to Gunvald?''Ah, you return! Laugi told me you were checking into the camp for us. My thanks. What have you found?'Explore the many places of fear and dread that can be found within Minas Morgul, the Dead City.Explore the many places of fear and dread that can be found within Minas Morgul.Explore Barad Angarth, the Gate-wardens' KeepExplore Barad Orhant, the Tower of the TreegarthExplore Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' SpireExplore Barad Arthir, the Lofty Watch-fortExplore the Song-house of LindalírëExplore Roz Dagalur, the Fiend-houseExplore Búrzangh, the Shrouded ForgeExplore Dâr Grazadh, the Hall of RotExplore Ghashan-kútot, the Hall of Black LoreExplore the GloomwatersExplore the Garth of AngáthExplore Bâr MaenathExplore Uialrond, the Dome of EveningExplore the Wracking-hallExplore Gath DaerovalExplore Barad Cúron, the Tower of the Crescent MoonExplore Zhar DushgoiExplore Zhar SkatorExplore the many locations where danger might lurk, and where good-hearted folk might oppose it, within Rath Dúath.Explore the many locations where danger might lurk, and where good-hearted folk might oppose it, within Rath Dúath.Explore Annon MorgulExplore the GúliantExplore Eithel Gwaur, the Filth-wellExplore Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrowExplore Estolad LânExplore Echad UialExplore Râkh MathánExplore Banám LugaunExplore Shakam MozExplore Dáru Lagúrz, the Broken HousesExplore Taen OrwathWith Thrain's scouts recovering, their duties must be taken up by another.Locations to be scouted can throughout Azanulbizar.

