You should place the spears in the empty barrels.'Claw and fang are enough for me to win most any fight. I am no fool though. Sometimes a spear is a much needed weapon when the odds are against you, or the hunt is too dangerous! For that reason, we Beornings of the Floodfells have hidden caches of spears throughout the lands. Go south, to the cave Tithroz, and find the spears within. It is our largest cache. There should be many spears inside; many more than you would be able to carry.'Defeat many spiders and insects in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many spiders and insects in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many spiders and insects in Imlad MorgulDefeat many spiders and insects in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many spiders and insects in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many spiders and insects in Imlad Morgul.Defeat many spiders and insects in Imlad MorgulDefeat many spiders and insects in Gloomingtarn.Defeat many spiders and insects in Gloomingtarn.Defeat many spiders and insects in GloomingtarnDefeat many spiders and insects in Gloomingtarn.Defeat many spiders and insects in Gloomingtarn.Defeat many spiders and insects in GloomingtarnSighild, daughter of Runerik and Yrsa, seeks to put an end to the Orc spies skilfully patrolling the Floodfells.Gundabad spies can be found in the Floodfells.

You should defeat any Gundabad spies that you find.Defeat Gundabad spies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Oh, I am Sighild. Thyra is my twin sister. Have you heard that spies from Gundabad watch Limlók even now? I can never seem to spot them, but I know they are across the river, skilfully patrolling the Floodfells. We must defeat them to prevent the arrival of more raiding parties.'Dwarf-corpses litter the battlefield around Durin's Stone. Their arms and armour must not fall into the hands of the Orcs.Fallen dwarves can be found at Durin's Stone.

You should collect arms and armour from fallen dwarves at Azanulbizar.Collect dwarf-helmets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect dwarf-shields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect dwarf-swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Thorin can be found at Amdân.

You have collected a great deal of arms and armour from the fallen. You should deliver them to Thorin at Amdân.'Many of our kin lay dead beneath the eyes of Durin's Stone, but I would not allow them to be defiled and dishonoured. The Orcs pick at the dead, pilfering arms and armour wrought by the skilled hands of our ancestors. Nay! Not just those of Durin's Folk, but of all Seven Houses!

'I ask that you gather helmets, shields, and swords from our fallen brethren that they do not fall into the hands of Azog and his Orcs.''Our brethren must not be forgotten, my friend. We must honour their deeds and sacrifice through all days to come!'Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Within Minas Morgul, a great repository of evil knowledge stands: The Halls of Black Lore. To gain the information you seek, you must enter and face Dolguzigir, the Dark Archivist.Complete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore -- Tier 1Complete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore -- Tier 2Complete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore -- Tier 3Complete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore: Slayer of the Archivist's AssistantsComplete Ghashan-kútot, the Halls of Black Lore: Slayer of SpiritsAmong the hills of Azanulbizar, deadly Wargs vie for the privilege of being steed to the Orc-chieftains.Warg champions can be found in eastern Azanulbizar.

