You should assist Langhár and Varthmath.Assist Langhár at Zarkul-sulûnAssist Varthmath at Zarkul-sulûnLanghár can be found at Zarkul-sulûn.

You should talk to Langhár.Talk to Langhár at Zarkul-sulûn'${CLASS}, I must speak with you of an urgent matter. Scouts have spotted what seems to be a raiding party, heading in our direction from the east! It appears that the enemy seeks to ambush us from behind! I do not know how they were able to get around our lines, but we must confront the raiders immediately! They can not be allowed to cross the River Drekvath.''Why, ${PLAYER}, have you come to welcome us to the battle? How very kind of you! We are people of our word. If Grimbeorn declares that the Beornings will assist our allies in their time of need, that is what we will do! We are here to help you win this war. Come, let us not waste another moment!''This is a good enough place to assist as any. Some of my kin have ventured elsewhere but do not fear. I have respect for them all in battle.

'Speaking of battle, These dwarves could use some of my deadly Beorning hunting spears. A perfect throw will slice any Orc in twain! Here, take these spears and distribute them to the dwarves at Shakal-atrâd.''Upon first inspection, the spear seems crude to an untrained eye. Hmm, then you feel the balance and notice the deadly sharp tip. This is fine craftsmanship!''You should assist those of my kin who are here at Shakal-atrâd with me. They may need assistance in their tasks. Time is never on one's side in battle.''Skarding walks his own path. You know this. I never worry, for he is the greatest Beorning warrior. Search for him on the battlefield, as I am sure that is where he went. He may welcome your assistance, though I am certain he does not need it.

'Once you have assisted Skarding, locate Langhár and Varthmath at Zarkul-sulûn. They may have need of your assistance.''Thank you ${PLAYER} for all that you have done to assist our efforts in battle. We will prevail soon enough, this I know!'The island of Grytholm is deeply entrenched within enemy territory, but Aighrig may have a plan.You should discuss plans with Aighrig.

She stands before the stairs to Annâk-khurfu.Talk to AighrigThe cave Tithzagáf is located on the island of Grytholm, to the north-west of Annâk-khurfu.

