Halvar spends the next few hours experimenting alone and muttering to himself.The Great Alliance of Elves and Men stood in defiance of Sauron for long years of siege, but even their greatest heroes came to fear his deadliest servants. These were the Nazgûl, and their number was Nine.Once he was a great king in lands far to the east, accustomed to rule and unwilling to bend the knee to any other. But then came a giver of gifts and a promiser of power, and upon accepting these lures, the great king changed. No longer did he rule his lands with mercy, and neither did he remain in his own kingdom. He became Rhûn's bane, and by that name came he to be known as the Bane of Rhûn, and elsewhere.Defeat the Bane of Rhûn in Mordor BesiegedOnce he was a great king in lands far to the east, accustomed to rule and unwilling to bend the knee to any other. But then came a giver of gifts and a promiser of power, and upon accepting these lures, the great king changed. No longer did he rule his lands with mercy, and neither did he remain in his own kingdom. He became Rhûn's bane, and by that name came he to be known as the Bane of Rhûn, and elsewhere.Defeat the Bane of Rhûn in Mordor BesiegedOnce he was a great king in lands far to the east, accustomed to rule and unwilling to bend the knee to any other. But then came a giver of gifts and a promiser of power, and upon accepting these lures, the great king changed. No longer did he rule his lands with mercy, and neither did he remain in his own kingdom. He became Rhûn's bane, and by that name came he to be known as the Bane of Rhûn, and elsewhere.The Bane of Rhûn, defeated but enduringThe Great Alliance of Elves and Men stood in defiance of Sauron for long years of siege, but even their bravest heroes came to fear his deadliest servants. These were the Nazgûl, and their number was Nine. They stalked the battlefield of Mordor Besieged, and were its most dangerous scourges.

Once he was a great king in lands far to the east, accustomed to rule and unwilling to bend the knee to any other. But then came a giver of gifts and a promiser of power, and upon accepting these lures, the great king changed. No longer did he rule his lands with mercy, and neither did he remain in his own kingdom. He became Rhûn's bane, and by that name came he to be known as the Bane of Rhûn, and elsewhere.The Bane of Rhûn suffered defeat on the battlefield of Mordor Besieged, but it was not to be a lasting death... not while Sauron endured. The Nazgûl would return, for his was an existence beyond ending.Complete a study of the key moments in Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar.Complete a study of the key moments in Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar.Complete 'Council of the Seven'Complete 'Bonds of Oak and Iron'Complete 'The Lord of Moria'Complete 'A Final Reckoning'It is at the Battle of Azgh-buzru that the coming days of the War of Three Peaks are to be decided. The Gabil'akkâ must rout the forces of Gorgar the Ruthless and the Frost-horde or all hopes of mounting an attack on the gates of Mount Gundabad are lost.Dréri, Mézto, and Órug can be found among the forces of the Gabil'akkâ at Azgh-buzru.

