You have aided Náin the Slakeless and the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ in overcoming the garrison at Bagûd-mekhem. You should report to Náin with news of your victory at Bagûd-mekhem.Talk to Náin the Slakeless at Drenghól'It does the Gabil'akkâ no good to call it by any other name... the battle of Azgh-buzru is upon us!

'When we marched to the war-fell, my company numbered in the hundreds, but our losses have been great. What I intended to be a sudden, brutal attack against the Orcs of Gundabad was repelled by their machines of war, and our advance has stagnated into a bloody stalemate. Ground is gained and lost in the span of hours, so much so that I must bare my shame and admit Gorgar has claimed the advantage... at least for the moment. Indeed, he owes much to his defences both within and without Mount Gundabad, but they cannot hold forever!

'I need you to find three of my warriors in the field: Dréri, Mézto, and Órug. I believe you know them. I tasked them with discovering weaknesses in Gorgar's defences, and I would have you exploit those weaknesses.

'Into battle, ${PLAYER}! For the glory of the Gabil'akkâ!''You have done well, ${PLAYER}.

'The others informed me of the aid you brought them... and not a moment too soon, it seems. Gorgar's forces have been hindered greatly by your hand, but the battle is not yet ended.

'After conferring with Dréri, Mézto, and Órug, our path is clear. The time has come to press the attack!

'I shall send as many of my forces as I can spare into the field to occupy Gorgar's forces, but it is you who shall lead the attack on Bagûd-mekhem!''The Battle of Azgh-buzru is won!

'From what I have heard, Bagûd-mekhem has already fallen into disarray. Without Narg-and-Mauz to lead them, it is unlikely they shall ever reforge even the most tenuous alliance. Now those Orcs will prove no match for us proud dwarves... and I suppose not for a ${RACE}.

'The Gabil'akkâ shall see that Bagûd-mekhem is rid of Orcs once and for all, but none of this would have been possible without you, ${PLAYER}!

'Let Gorgar lick his wounds while he can for his own defeat is soon to come!'The Great Alliance of Elves and Men stood in defiance of Sauron for long years of siege, but even their greatest heroes came to fear his deadliest servants. These were the Nazgûl, and their number was Nine.In later days, the Black Blade of Lebennin was oft-seen stalking among the hills and forests of Western Gondor, striking fear into the hearts of Men with both deadly countenance and fearsome sword. For those few who did not flee, his words poured like honey into their unwilling ears and drove them to terrible acts of evil. This may have proved his worst and most effective weapon.Defeat the Black Blade of Lebennin in Mordor BesiegedIn later days, the Black Blade of Lebennin was oft-seen stalking among the hills and forests of Western Gondor, striking fear into the hearts of Men with both deadly countenance and fearsome sword. For those few who did not flee, his words poured like honey into their unwilling ears and drove them to terrible acts of evil. This may have proved his worst and most effective weapon.Defeat the Black Blade of Lebennin in Mordor BesiegedIn later days, the Black Blade of Lebennin was oft-seen stalking among the hills and forests of Western Gondor, striking fear into the hearts of Men with both deadly countenance and fearsome sword. For those few who did not flee, his words poured like honey into their unwilling ears and drove them to terrible acts of evil. This may have proved his worst and most effective weapon.The Black Blade of Lebennin, defeated but enduringThe Great Alliance of Elves and Men stood in defiance of Sauron for long years of siege, but even their bravest heroes came to fear his deadliest servants. These were the Nazgûl, and their number was Nine. They stalked the battlefield of Mordor Besieged, and were its most dangerous scourges.

