You should talk to Léothred at Avabárg.Talk to Léothred at Avabárg'I hope that I am not a burden to you. I could use a companion on my travels. It is a boon to my research that you accompany me with your current knowledge of these lands and your skill in combat. I have heard the north can be a harsh place at times.

'Now then, I suppose we'd best be off. The story of the Rohirrim begins, in many ways, at Avabárg.''Let us defeat these Orcs and honour the hardship endured by the Horse-folk for so many years.''Frumgar was victorious. It was said, however, defeat only stoked the Orcs’ thirst for blood. Thirteen years later the Orcs returned to raze the Ai-thúda's lands and sack Avabárg.''In many ways the story of my people begins with King Marhári, of the Northmen. Disaster befell the Thíuda during the Battle of the Plains against the Wainriders. When King Marhári fell in that battle, his son Marhwini led the survivors on a long journey in search of a new home, ultimately resettling here.

'Marhwini’s people, the Ai-thúda or Horse-folk, were not well satisfied dwelling in the Vales. They desired open country where they could ride and graze their herds. Their scouts found this in the Floodfells, but Marhwini deemed it too rough and untamable a land, and too close to the threat of Angmar, to halt with his war-weary people.''Here Marhwini built the hall of Avabárg and named it the chief fortress of the Ai-thúda. This was not the safest of places, though. The coming of the Horse-folk roused the Orcs of Hithaeglir, who attacked them again and again over the next century. Both Marhwini’s son Forthwini and his grandson Forthári fell in battle to the Orcs, leaving only Forthári’s youngest son as heir.''Forthári’s youngest son was Frumgar, a boy of twelve, now Chieftain of the Ai-thúda. While still a youth, Frumgar became a hero of his people, befriending both the Longbeard Dwarves and the Wizards Gandalf the Grey and Barandil the Brown.''Frumgar even received an ancient sword of Westernesse, which he named Wrothbláda, from Curunír the White. With these allies he defeated the Orcs in battle at the age of seventeen.'Léothred and Fróthi look to unearth a piece of lost history in Elderslade.Fróthi brought Scatha's tooth with him to Annâk-khurfu.

