After learning of their arrival at Bagûd-mekhem, Órug has asked you to defeat the lieutenants of Gorgar.Defeat Lieutenant BauzmátDefeat Lieutenant GádhmalDefeat Lieutenant OgarbukÓrug can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks.

You have defeated lieutenants Ogarbuk, Bauzmát, and Gádhmal at Bagûd-mekhem. You should report to Órug.Talk to Órug at Drenghól'${PLAYER}, I have received word that Gorgar has bolstered his presence at Bagûd-mekhem.

'It seems three of Gorgar's most trustworthy lieutenants have been sent to oversee his forces and lead a new front against the Gabil'akkâ. It remains unclear if Gorgar is even aware of the alliance between his forces and the small contingent of the Frost-horde gathered within Bagûd-mekhem.

'If there are troubles between them, so be it. Nevertheless, the defeat of his lieutenants is of utmost importance!''It is done? Good!

'Let that be a lesson to Gorgar and his Orcs!'Within the twin encampments of Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh, terrible siege-engines stand ready to fire on any who would dare to approach Mount Gundabad.Orkish trebuchets and ballistae can be found in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.

Darfin has asked you to destroy the siege-engines deployed in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. You should destroy Orkish trebuchets and ballistae.Destroy Orkish trebuchets at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Orkish ballistae at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have destroyed many Orkish trebuchets and ballistae at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.Completed'Oh, thank goodness you've come!

'I was on my way to report that I found a number of Orkish trebuchets and ballistae among the outer defences of Gundabad, and then some sneaky little goblin caught sight of me. After that, well, the odds were against me!

'You know as well as I that a proud dwarf does not surrender! But... it is not an admission of defeat to buy one's self time to think! I broke my bonds not one minute after the Orcs threw me in this cage, but escaping this filthy camp will take more than just strength.

'Why don't you destroy some of those siege-engines? That ought to get the Orcs riled up... and distracted enough to take their eyes off me!

'Do not worry! I'll find somewhere safe... just not here!'You have destroyed many Orkish trebuchets and ballistae at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.

