You should talk to Léothred in Erebor.Talk to Léothred in Erebor'Now that we have safely arrived at Erebor, I would very much like to have a look around the grand hall under the mountain.

'When Thráin’s herald returned to Erebor with the necklace, Wandalb had accompanied the herald to speak on the Ai-thúda’s behalf. I assume that the Grey Wizard did all he could to help ease the tensions between the two people.''Wandalb remained at Erebor for weeks afterward, pleading for Thráin to see reason, but the Dwarf-king never again spoke to him or counted him friend. It was a dark time.

'It makes me wonder if the necklace was cursed!''It is said that when Thráin received the gift of Scatha's teeth, he was furious. He believed Fram's missive to be a taunt, and would not be moved even by the Grey Wizard's most cunning words. He cast the necklace aside, proclaiming that such trinkets were poor substitutes for his people's birthright, and sent Wandalb away.'The worm nesting grounds of Nathból prevent those who seek to journey up the river towards Wyrmsgráf.The nesting grounds of Nathból can be found in Elderslade.

