You should destroy the worm nests found in Nathból.Destroy the worm nests found in Nathból (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have destroyed many worm nests in Nathból.CompletedThe worm nesting grounds of Nathból prevent those who seek to journey up the river towards Wyrmsgráf. If some of the nests are destroyed, perhaps the route towards Wyrmsgráf will become safer to travel.You have destroyed many worm nests in Nathból. The path towards Wyrmsgráf is safer to explore.The Great Alliance of Elves and Men stood in defiance of Sauron for long years of siege, but even their greatest heroes came to fear his deadliest servants. These were the Nazgûl, and their number was Nine.The Great Alliance of Elves and Men stood in defiance of Sauron for long years of siege, but even their greatest heroes came to fear his deadliest servants. These were the Nazgûl, and their number was Nine.Complete "The Bane of Rhûn, Scourge of Mordor"Complete "The Forsaken Reaver, Scourge of Mordor"Complete "The Gloom of Nurn, Scourge of Mordor"Complete "The Grim Southron, Scourge of Mordor"Complete "The High Sorcerer of Harad, Scourge of Mordor"Complete "The Woe of Khand, Scourge of Mordor"Complete "The Black Blade of Lebennin, Scourge of Mordor"Complete "The Cursed Rider, Scourge of Mordor"Complete "The Witch-king, Lord of the Nazgûl, Scourge of Mordor"Grants completion of deed: The NineBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing The Nine'Now, my little fellows, where be you a-going to, puffing like a bellows? What's the matter here then? Tell me what's your trouble!

