You should find Rauniel inside Eithel Gwaur and save her.Arodor can be found at Echad Uial in Rath Dúath.

You should talk to Arodor.Talk to Arodor at Echad Uial'Eithel Gwaur lies beyond this bridge. The old cisterns have remained hidden for many years, but the passage is always guarded. Defeat those who guard the path and meet me upon the steps to Eithel Gwaur. Only there can you set me free.''Ah, ${PLAYER}, have you returned with the water samples? You were gone for so long I feared the worst! What befell while you undertook that task?'

You tell Arodor of your confrontation with the evil Gwaurodel and the beast's deception.

'Are you certain this Gwaurodel was the cause of the Morgulduin's blight? I can not thank you enough for seeing this through to the end, for that proved no simple task after all! Not only have you found what manner of corruption befouls the waters, you put an end to the horrid creature that was its cause. That was nobly done, my friend!

'It may be a long while before the river is truly clean, for Gwaurodel deprived the waters of its true keeper, the river maiden of the Ithilduin, and the beast befouled them for so long. It will take time before these cruel injuries are undone.''You have defeated the guards with ease. Now is the time to free me from this prison! You have done as I asked and cleared a path for my escape. Now I can guide you to my cage. Follow me inside, noble ${RACE}.'Aid those who seek to carry out the reclamation of Minas Ithil.Aid those who seek to carry out the reclamation of Minas Ithil.Complete The Trial of DeathComplete Imlad Morgul -- The ReclamationComplete Vale of Sorcery: The Trial of DeathSighild, daughter of Runerik and Yrsa, seeks to put an end to the packs of Wargs still roaming the Floodfells.Gundabad pack-leaders and Gundabad pack-hunters can be found in the Floodfells.

You should defeat the Gundabad pack-leaders and Gundabad pack-hunters.Defeat Gundabad pack-leaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Gundabad pack-hunters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Wargs, I hate them. Skarding hates them more, but I hate them almost as much! They have no regard for the creatures of the wilds. They kill animals for amusement! It sickens me. Their packs roam the lands between Khilbakh and Ylgraf. We must reclaim these lands from the Wargs. They have no right to the Floodfells.'The goblins of Sundergrót have set up a secret meeting within the old dwarf ruins.Sundergrót can be found in the Floodfells.

You should talk to Agátur outside of Sundergrót.Talk to Agátur outside of SundergrótRúzat, Agátur, and Náth can be found at Limlók.

You should talk to the three dwarves.Talk to Rúzat at LimlókTalk to Agátur at LimlókTalk to Náth at Limlók'${PLAYER}, something bothers me about the goblins in Sundergrót. I know not what, but something is amiss! Agátur looks as if he has something to say. Spit it out, my friend!''I overheard some goblins talking while I was in Sundergrót. At the time, I did not think much of it, but perhaps I should revisit what it was I heard.

'Do you find it odd that the goblins work and camp as if they are commanded, yet there is no commander in sight? Yes, well, I heard a few goblins talking about an important meeting that is soon to happen in Sundergrót. Could this meeting be with this mysterious, absent commander? I say we find this meeting, and learn what is really going on here!''It is always a pleasure to receive assistance from the great ${PLAYER}. I hope our paths cross once more, my friend!''Aye, it looks like my curiosity was warranted. I am glad that we stopped those goblins from joining forces with Gundabad.''Thank you for your assistance on our survey mission. I hope that you will return to Skarháld with us. Please, bring us word from Grimbeorn as soon as you hear something.'Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, seeks to complete the journey his ancestors took north, from the Vales of Anduin through Misthallow.Thokvist can be found in the south of Misthallow.

You should travel to Thokvist.Travel to Thokvist in MisthallowLéothred can be found at Thokvist.

