'Urgh... apologies. I got too close to a group of Angmarim while scouting, thinking they'd never catch me. Well, they dragged me to Dûn Traikh. Then one of them claimed my sword -- forged by my own mother -- for himself!

'But I'm in no state to challenge him. If you're planning to head west and enter the camp, find the quartermaster, Akhún. He's rather irritable when his fellow Angmarim try to take weapons without his permission. Make enough noise with those weapons, and he'll come running!''Ah... thank you, ${PLAYER}. I don't think I could have lived with myself, knowing that Akhún would've drawn the blood of my people using my mother's blade.

