You should talk to Runerik Knotbeard.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók'Speaking of Vaskorn, he has recovered fully from his injuries. I knew that he would. He is eager to patrol the wilds. I will tell you what I told him, for I fear an assault upon Limlók may be imminent. I need you to find any of these raiding-parties before they find the village!

'Speak to Vaskorn before you set out, ${PLAYER}.''Keep a hushed tone about you, ${PLAYER}. I hear the tread of Warg-paws: over the hill, within the valley of Misthallow. They come this way. Should we retreat and warn the village? If we run, we will lose sight of this band, and an unseen threat can be the more dangerous. No, we must stand our ground. I have fled too often of late. No more.''Our victory was for Hunulf. Our success was for elder Threkmóth. Until now, I felt lost, thrust from my quiet life in the Thornholt, a sudden victim of death and conflict. But I am now newly-resolved: I shall remain in Limlók and help protect this village. If Limlók is not kept safe, how will my Skoghús ever be so?''What? A Warg made it through Misthallow? Skarding is either in trouble or he has been overwhelmed... and I am sure he is not in trouble.''Yes, I am healed and ready to assist Runerik. Let us patrol the wilds of the Floodfells in search of any of these raiding parties. I will patrol the southern route and round the western hill towards the northern pass. You patrol the northern route past the horse rocks. We will meet up at the northern pass.'The Orcs have dug out winding tunnels in the shadow of Zudramdân, further defiling the dwarf-ruin.The Ushkútoz Trenches can be found underneath the scorched ruins of Zudramdân.

