You should return to Sárgo.Return to Sárgo'Some of our brethren have not returned from scouting. One group was investigating Orc camps, while the other was looking into the Wargs. I fear for their safety, Hermáth. Please look for them and bring them back, if they still yet live.''This is fine work you have done today, friend. Those you freed owe you their life.'A fearsome two-headed troll named Grush-and-Flak has been routing a wide array of troops throughout the countryside. Find the creature and drive it from the battlefield.A fearsome two-headed troll Grush-and-Flak has been attacking a wide array of troops throughout the countryside. Find the creature and drive it from the battlefield.Defeat Grush-and-FlakThe fearsome two-headed troll Grush-and-Flak has been attacking a wide array of troops throughout the countryside. Find the creature and drive it from the battlefield.Defeat Grush-and-FlakLet Hlóthi know that Grush-and-Flak has been driven off.Speak to HlóthiWithin the troops pushing towards our encampment, the monstrous two-headed troll Grush-and-Flak has battered the forces of the Gabil'akkâ throughout the region. This horrific beast is said to have consumed several patrols during its reign of terror.'The fearsome two-headed troll Grush-and-Flak has been routed, bringing some stability to the region.

'Thank you kindly for this dangerous work.'Hoshkhor, the Cruel Barb, has become known to the gathered forces of Gabil'akkâ. This foul creature has routed several patrols throughout the area, and has hindered supply lines for the war effort.Hoshkhor, has become known to the gathered forces of Gabil'akkâ. This foul captain has routed several patrols throughout the area and has hindered supply lines for the war effort.Defeat HoshkhorHoshkhor has become known to the gathered forces of Gabil'akkâ. This foul creature has routed several patrols throughout the area and has hindered supply lines for the war effort.Defeat HoshkhorHoshkhor has become known to the gathered forces of Gabil'akkâ. This foul creature has routed several patrols throughout the area and has hindered supply lines for the war effort.Speak to HlóthiHoshkhor has become a scourge throughout Elderslade. The Gabil'akkâ has learned to fear the creature as the field turns cold in its presence.

