You should talk to Fanglind.Talk to Fanglind at Thokvist'Hmm, I can not allow any more of my kin to leave Limlók, but I must know what troubles Skarding in Misthallow. ${PLAYER}, you have proven yourself resilient and defended my home. Is it too much to ask one more task of you? Will you travel to Misthallow and seek out Skarding Wargsbane? You may find him at Thokvist where he often resides.

'${PLAYER}, I can see now why Grimbeorn trusts you.''Runerik has sent you? These must be trying times. Do not speak to me of Ujâk-fulug. I am even less pleased than you about the Wargs who escaped my wrath and made for the Floodfells. It would have not been so, if not for Gúrbarash and those cursed trolls who blockade half the valley!'

The Eagle perched at Thokvist eyes you closely.

'It seems you have something to add, Fanglind?''Yes, I know who you are, ${PLAYER}. I have heard about you from Lord Gwaihir! With what knowledge of you I have, I know your assistance will be a boon to us in ousting this Gúrbarash. No good can come from a Gundabad chieftain in these lands.'Eager to erode the alliance between the forces of Gorgar the Ruthless and Hrímil Frost-heart, Mézto has devised a plan to turn Orc against Orc.Cold-whelplings can be found at Bagûd-mekhem.

Mézto has asked you to slay cold-whelplings in Bagûd-mekhem and set their remains upon fires tended by the Orcs of Gundabad.Collect the remains of cold-whelplings at Bagûd-mekhem (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fire-pits can be found at Bagûd-mekhem.

Mézto has asked to slay cold-whelplings in Bagûd-mekhem and set their remains upon fires tended by the Orcs of Gundabad.'Cook' cold-whelpling remains in fire-pits at Bagûd-mekhem (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mézto can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks.

You have done as Mézto asked and sown division between the forces at Bagûd-mekhem. You should report your success to Mézto.Talk to Mézto at Drenghól'Ah, ${PLAYER}!

'You and I both know there is no love lost between the Orcs of Gundabad and those wild Orcs of the Frost-horde. Why should we not turn their mutual distrust to our advantage?

'I have heard that several cold-whelplings have begun to roost with their Orkish allies in Bagûd-mekhem. I do not know the appetites of Orcs, but perhaps if a few of these whelplings were "cooked" by Gorgar's Orcs... things might not seem so friendly between them and the Frost-horde.

'Do you understand? Slay as many cold-whelplings as you can and toss them in the fire-pits tended by Gorgar's Orcs!''Hah! It would be quite a joy to see the face of the first Orc who discovers what we've done!

'Alas, my imagination will have to suffice....

'You've done well. That is all, ${PLAYER}.'Grimbeorn knows the threat in the north moves ever closer to the lands and people he has sworn to protect.Hunulf can be found at the front gate of the Beorninghús.

