You should talk to Runerik Knotbeard.Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in LimlókGrimbeorn peers toward the front gate of the Beorninghús.

'Now what?! Another guest?! We have not the time for this. ${PLAYER}, see what they want, then send them on their way.'Hunulf is far from his dwelling in the Thornholt. He looks badly injured.

'${PLAYER}, is that you? Please listen.... I travelled from the Thornholt with Vaskorn, Threkmóth, and three dwarves. We came to warn of the growing threat. The warbands in the mountains grow more fearsome by day.... We made it to Limlók.... The village is not safe. They need help.'

Hunulf coughs and looks too weak to move.

'I was ambushed on my journey here. I narrowly escaped those wargs....'

Hunulf falls silent.'Hunulf, my kin! I did not recognize him at the gate and now this news you bring pains me. Hunulf was an outsider, but kin all the same. We must see that his death was not in vain. You are willing to help, ${CLASS}? I will gladly accept this kindness. Here, take this candle. Light it for Hunulf at the Carrock. If you take the scholar with you, that is your decision. Just see to it that he does not die. I wish for no more deaths of those in my lands who I have sworn to protect. Those in Limlók seek aid. You must go north.''This is horrible. I did not think I would be imposing myself upon the Vales in such a trying time. If Grimbeorn allows me to continue, then continue I shall. Do not worry, ${PLAYER}. I will not get in your way!''Ba! I can not believe Grimbeorn sent you alone. Hmm, if you do not get in the way and do as you are told, perhaps you might be useful.'The Gabil'akkâ has secured Zudramdân in Elderslade.Agátur the Boastful has asked you to plant banners along the road leading to Zudramdân.

