You should talk to Náth at Zudramdân.Talk to Náth at Zudramdân'I have just received word that the Gabil'akkâ have secured Zudramdân, to the north! This is indeed a victory, as Zudramdân is a strategic point for staging an assault against Gundabad. You must travel to Zudramdân immediately, as we will need as many warriors there as is possible. On your way there, place some banners along the road to bring strength to all in the Gabil'akkâ!

'I believe that our friend, Náth, was one of the group that took Zudramdân. If you see him, give him my thanks!''The taking of Zudramdân was barely a battle, ${PLAYER}. Most of the Orcs just fled, instead of fighting. If you ask me, I found it quite odd. I would be grateful if you were to defeat some Orcs in Elderslade. Those who fled Zudramdân could not have gotten far.''Good work, ${PLAYER}. We will hold onto Zudramdân for as long as we can. I am weary of the growing numbers of Orcs by the walls of Gundabad. I see more with each passing hour.'As the Want-kin bid you farewell, the conflict in Elderslade grows greater just beyond Annâk-khurfu.Annâk-khurfu can be found to the west of Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade.

Nagli Want-kin has suggested that you rejoin Durin's army at the dwarf-ruins of Annâk-khurfu. You should travel to Annâk-khurfu.Travel to Annâk-khurfuAnnâk-khurfu can be found to the west of Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade.

You have arrived at Annâk-khurfu and you should now enter the old ruins in search of Glóin.Find Glóin in the old keep of Annâk-khurfuGlóin can be found in the war-room of Annâk-khurfu.

You have found Glóin in the old keep of Annâk-khurfu. You should speak to Glóin.Talk to Glóin at Annâk-khurfu'Indeed, but that is only a wishful thought.

'You have a duty to Durin and his army to see this march to its end, and I would not have you break an oath on my account. Most of the dwarves I have seen pass through the Slade have mustered at Annâk-khurfu. I overheard one of them speak the name Glóin. Is this name known to you?'

You tell Nagli that Glóin is an old friend and a commander of the army passing through Elderslade.

'It is there you must go then—to Glóin and your allies.

'Beware the dangers that lie beyond our little encampment, ${PLAYER}. May good fortune be with you!''Ah, ${PLAYER}! I had begun to wonder where you'd gone.

