As you inspect Krúmpug's hand, you notice he bears a crude missive of sorts written in goblin-scrawl. Much of it is illegible, but you note the mention of a "Great Goblin". This name is unfamiliar to you. Could this be referring to Azog or was this goblin sent to treat with the Orc-chieftain on behalf of another master?

You decide to bring this trophy to Elgur, a skilled taxidermist of the Landorrim, that it might be preserved once the war is ended.'What is this now?'

Elgur inspects Krúmpug's hand and unfurls the crude missive it holds.

'The Great Goblin, eh? Aye, it could be Azog, but I wouldn't be so sure. If this war's taught us anything, it's that worse things are often hiding just out of sight. I'll make certain that Thráin sees this!'After encountering the elusive great-bat, Muzbuk, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Haban'akkâ of Thráin.Elgur can be found at Amdân during the Battle of Azanulbizar in T.A. 2799.

