You have succeeded in defeating Kraznákh and undermining Gorgar's plans to keep the Gabil'akkâ locked in a bloody stalemate. You should talk to Agnar.Talk to Agnar Brokentooth at the western entrance to Ushkútoz'According to Glóin, it seems the advance of the Gabil'akkâ has stalled upon the battlefield. The enemy is too deeply-entrenched around Zudramdân and regrettably, their defences have held against our assaults. We have found ourselves in bloody stalemate, and I have no doubt this is what Gorgar sought all along.

'Gorgar has all of his Orcs, all of his defences, and all of his tricks to bring to bear against us from Mount Gundabad. There is no Erebor for us to retreat to in Elderslade—our only defences are our axes and these old ruins, and we have meagre supplies if we hope to outlast the enemy.

'A stalemate means only one thing, ${PLAYER}, and that is the defeat of the Gabil'akkâ.

'Hope is not yet lost, though. My scouts have discovered weaknesses in the Orcs' defences at Zudramdân, namely a trench-tunnel known as Ushkútoz that they use to swiftly move forces to either side of the old ruins. With your aid and a bit of luck, we might turn Gorgar's overconfidence to our advantage.

'Glóin speaks highly of you, ${PLAYER}. Let us see if his faith is not misplaced!

'There is much to be done!''The moment is at hand, ${PLAYER}. This may be our only chance!''I have received word that Kraznákh has arrived at Ushkútoz. If we are to break this stalemate for the Gabil'akkâ, we must act before the chance is lost!

'Lági and Reithvald will infiltrate the western entrance to Ushkútoz, and we shall take the eastern entrance, ${PLAYER}. Where our paths converge, we will find Kraznákh and his Orcs. No matter what happens, they must not be allowed to escape!

'Are you prepared, my friend?''Our victory was hard-fought, ${PLAYER}, but... we have triumphed.

'Without Kraznákh to lead Gorgar's forces at Ushkútoz, the Gabil'akkâ will soon overrun their position. And we shall claim far more than Zudramdân this time!'

Agnar holds his axe aloft and points it at Mount Gundabad.

'Old Glóin was wise to send you to aid us, my friend. We could not have done it without you!'Aighrig, the person who led you to Gáfin's body, has asked you to help her prevent further Orkish attacks on dwarf supply trains.Aighrig keeps watch at the overlook near the Greylin River.

You should let her know when you are ready to help with her task.Talk to AighrigGundabad scouts roam near the road east of Annâk-khurfu.

The scouts are responsible for signaling attacks on dwarves' supply trains. Defeating them may make the road safer.Defeat Gundabad scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Use the whistle to summon Aighrig to your sideThere are fewer Orcs near the road now, thanks to your efforts and Aighrig's.

