Lúka will want to know everything that's happened.Talk to Lúka'I'll admit Mekhnet seems to be doing better, but she insists on re-entering Târ-kútoz with you, which I cannot abide. It was my fault that she -- '

Mekhnet clears her throat.'I made mistakes that night as well -- I wasn't careful enough. But blaming ourselves won't change the past. There isn't anything to forgive, Lúka.

'Hermáth, let's pay the Orcs a visit. I've got matters to settle with a certain goblin.''You're back! Of course I was worried, but that is different from harbouring doubt. I had faith that you two would return. As I have faith that we can now better handle the Orcs of Târ-kútoz.

'Thank you, Hermáth. I hope we all can meet again someday, when this war will be nothing more than mere memory.''Are you ready?'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>One cryptic note has led to a scout's corpse and another note, answering nothing but creating more questions. Who has been sending these?The messenger wants you to follow the road east, past the Hárveg Bridge. Before the road cuts into the Greylin River, there is an overlook to the south.

