You should talk to Thurindol.Talk to ThurindolYou have done much to aid those allies of the White Company in Imlad Morgul. Thurindol, a Ranger of Ithilien calls upon you to lead the charge in reclaiming Imlad Morgul from the dark grasp surrounding the once proud city of Minas Ithil. You should speak to Thurindol, Ereblen, and Tordoron at Echad Uial as soon as you are able.'${PLAYER}, you have heeded my call, as I knew you would. You are a faithful ally to the Rangers of Ithilien.

'Faramir has given me orders to begin the long and arduous task of cleansing the Morgul Vale. Our hope is for this valley to once again be a part of Ithilien and Gondor. I shall be focused on the Dead City of Minas Morgul, while my fellow Rangers, Ereblen and Tordoron will focus on the whole of the Vale. There are many tasks in the days ahead.

'Our first task is to retrieve Lhaereth's book on her Great Plague. I am sure it can still be found within the Hall of Black Lore. Will you retrieve the book for us?''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. Injury from the Battle at the Black Gate prevented me from joining the Mordor expedition. Now that my injuries have healed, I have been called upon by Thurindol to assist in the reclamation of Minas Ithil. I am ready to provide every skill that I have mastered since becoming a Ranger of Ithilien.

'Speak with me if you wish for tasks and rewards in assisting with the reclamation of Minas Ithil.''My good friend, ${PLAYER}! I was hoping we would one day adventure together again! I have been quite busy since we last parted, securing Ithilien. When the White Company entered Imlad Morgul, I knew I must follow, so I pleaded with Captain Faramir to reassign me. I am here to follow Thurindol's orders and assist any Ranger in need.

'Speak with me if you wish for tasks and rewards in assisting with the reclamation of Minas Ithil.''You make a grave mistake if you have come to kill me, ${RACE}. What will that accomplish, hmm?

'What? You want a book from my master's archives?! What a foolish request!'

You raise your weapon at the Black Númenórean.

'Ah... perhaps we could arrange a trade. You see, a book from the archives went missing last night. If you retrieve it for me, I could transcribe this book of Lhaereth's that you seek and give you a copy? All I know is that the doors to the archives remain locked. Whoever stole the book enters without a use for doors. Be quick, for I am not certain how long my offer for a trade will stand, ${CLASS}.'The Black Númenórean has been slain very recently. It is uncertain by whom, or what. The pages of the books you hold must have been important if both Thargaun and Dolguzigir both desire possession of the book. Perhaps you should bring the pages to Thurindol for closer inspection.'I can see now that breaching the archives may be more difficult than I previously thought. However, these pages you have collected bring me hope. I believe these pages may hold the key to defeating the dark sorcery that sits upon the city. It will not be possible to truly reclaim Minas Ithil until this veil of sorcery is lifted.'For those reclaiming Minas Ithil from the grasp of darkness, a trial of death has begun.The Altar of Death can be found in the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul.

