You should find out what happened to this group of Orcs.Talk to the injured OrcThurindol can be found at Echad Uial.

You should talk to Thurindol.Talk to Thurindol'Our best scholars bring word of their findings. They have only studied and learned some of the secrets buried within the first of the five pages. It would seem the sorcery that protects the Dead City is bound to five artifacts. The scholars are unsure as to what these artifacts are but they have learned that one sits within the Circle of Wrath. Perhaps a trip is in order?'The surly Orc is close to death, yet still manages to insult you.

'Is the weak ${CLASS} finally going to kill an Orc?! How brave of you! What, you want the orb too?! I knew it was valuable! That's why me and the others meant to bring it to Nurn. Matriarch would know what to do with it! Now look at me. I'm about to die to some lowly ${RACE} and those blasted Ghâsh-hai are to blame for everything! Said something about presenting it to their fire goddess, Urudanî. Toasted maggots, the lot of them! I don't got much longer. If you want to kill those Ghâsh-hai for me, they headed east on this here road.''Your search took you to Talath Úrui? This is all unexpected. These Orcs who fled were not following orders. Perchance to have found it just when we began searching for this artifact ourselves.'

You tell Thurindol about trial you had to overcome in order to destroy the artifact.

'I see, you have undergone a terrible trial of wrath in order to destroy the first orb of shadow that empowers the Dead City with dark sorcery. I fear there may be additional trials to overcome if we are to destroy all five artifacts.'A hidden entrance called Bagûd-mekhem, the Gate of Wind, lies just east of Gundabad. Zhurmat, with his fearsome mount the horrible two-headed troll Groz-and-Ulk, leads a force that threatens the Gabil'akkâ below.Complete 'Shakalush, the Stair Battle -- Tier 1'Complete 'Shakalush, the Stair Battle -- Tier 2'Complete 'Shakalush, the Stair Battle -- Tier 3'Complete 'Shakalush, the Stair Battle: Orc-slayer'Complete 'Shakalush, the Stair Battle: Hobgoblin-slayer'Complete 'Shakalush, the Stair Battle -- Tier 4'Complete 'Shakalush, the Stair Battle -- Tier 5'After discovering that Gorgar's forces have begun to claim trophies from fallen dwarves, Mézto seeks vengeance on behalf of the Zhélruka of the Gabil'akkâ.Dwarf-beards are kept as trophies by Orcs at Azgh-buzru. Medallions are carried by Orcs, trolls, and goblins loyal to Gorgar the Ruthless at Azgh-buzru.

Mézto has asked you to reclaim dwarf-beards taken as trophies by the forces of Gundabad. In addition, Mézto has asked to you collect the crude medallions carried by those loyal to Gorgar the Ruthless.Collect 'medallions' of Gorgar at Azgh-buzru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect dwarf-beard trophies at Azgh-buzru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mézto can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks.

You have collected many trophies from the forces of Gundabad. You should deliver them to Mézto at Drenghól.'${PLAYER}! What are you doing here? Leave me to my work!'

Mézto takes a crude medallion from a fallen Orc. You notice what appears to be a severed dwarf-beard gripped in his other hand.

'Gorgar is cunning... for an Orc. His slimy ilk have ripped and torn the beards from my fallen kin and kept them as trophies. Trophies! There can be no greater insult!

'If the Lord of the Iron Hills has sent you, I shall not scoff at the prospect of spilling more Orc-blood. Reclaim what they have taken from us, and collect their own 'medallions' in kind. If Gorgar wishes to count the dead, he shall suffer to find scores of his own among them!

'Say what you will of the Longbeards and these Stout-axes, I see the fury of the Zhélruka in their hearts! Is it in yours as well?

'When our vengeance is done, let us meet in Drenghól. Go!''Is your vengeance done? May you have found as much joy in it as I did.

'Give me what you have collected and I shall see that all of it is borne to Zarkul-sulûn.

'I shall not forget what you have done for the Zhélruka this day.'Few have encountered Otgand the Vile and lived to tell the tale of him, but on one matter they all agree: you do not want to encounter Otgand.Few have encountered Otgand the Vile and lived to tell the tale of him, but on one matter they all agree: you do not want to encounter Otgand.Find Otgand the VileFew have encountered Otgand the Vile and lived to tell the tale of this foul creature. Seek him out and end this scourge of Misthallow.Defeat OtgandCompleted.CompletedFew have encountered Otgand the Vile and lived to tell the tale of him, but on one matter they all agree: you do not want to encounter Otgand. The worm has feasted upon at least a score of travellers unfortunate enough to find themselves lost among the rocky crags of Misthallow during the last six months, and in that time he has grown larger and bolder than before. You should put an end to vile Otgand before anyone else is lost to his insatiable hunger.Otgand will no longer stalk the rocky crags of Misthallow. In time, the stories of him will fade, and few will believe that he feasted upon at least twenty travellers in only six months.

'How could one creature eat so many?' they will ask in disbelief.
'How big did he grow? How vile was he, in the end?' they will marvel.

'So very vile,' some may reply. 'Just ask , for she/he was there.'Trygvar, son of Runerik and Yrsa, seeks brambles to strengthen Limlók's fortifications.Brambles can be found in the Floodfells.

You should gather brambles for Limlók.Gather brambles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Brambles should be placed around Limlók.'Aye, you must be the outsider. If father Runerik says you are welcome, then I have no trouble with you. Mother Yrsa says I should reinforce the palisades with brambles. I have gathered all the brambles to be found nearby. Would you gather the brambles found further from Limlók and apply them to the fortifications?'Some needed secondary supplies may be found in Imlad Morgul.<rgb=#FF00FF>These items may be found by defeating foes in Imlad Morgul instances. Different instances will yield different types of items.</rgb>Collect crafter's steel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect worn trinkets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should deliver the items you collected to Tordoron in Echad Uial.'While you are out there helping our efforts, we are in need of some lesser resources that are difficult to find.

'If you come across any crafter's steel, or worn trinkets, will you gather them for us? Our crafters have been asking for these items in particular.''You have returned with the items I asked of you? You have my thanks.'Some needed secondary supplies may be found in Imlad Morgul.<rgb=#FF00FF>These items may be found by defeating foes in Imlad Morgul instances. Different instances will yield different types of items.</rgb>Collect deep-lichen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect smoothed stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should deliver the items you collected to Tordoron in Echad Uial.'While you are out there helping our efforts, we are in need of some lesser resources that are difficult to find.

