You should talk to Madelgard Túcca.Talk to Madelgard Túcca in Lyndelby'No, your eyes do not deceive you. This is the last village of the Holbytlan. We have watched over Lyndelby and its inhabitants for as long as they have lived here. They are a quiet people, and Lord Gwaihir had taken a liking to their kind. The Holbytlan are shy, however. You may look around the village, but I wouldn't expect even their leader to greet you, ${PLAYER}.''I am Grandmother Madelgard Túcca, and you are quite the stranger! I'm only talking to you because you are the friend of an Eagle. We have great respect for the Eagles, but not much for... what are you? ${RACE}?! Hmm, perhaps you could earn more respect if you do something nice for Lyndelby. You see, I have been noticing snooping goblins nearby. If you send them away, I might rest a bit easier at night!''You sent those goblins running?! To be honest, I did not expect you to help us at all! It would seem the rest of the village is now working up the courage to meet such a helpful and peculiar stranger, such as yourself. Perhaps you would also like to meet the rest of us? We can be a shy people, but we will warm to you in time.''Oh, I am glad that the whole village was able to meet you! Well, all but two, I think. Yes, they went up into the mountains to explore some time ago. Following in the footsteps of the Fallohide. Anyhow, I would say you have been most helpful to Lyndelby. It nearly felt as one of our festivals, what with all the buzz in the air from having you around!'Defeat many beasts in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many beasts throughout the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many beasts throughout the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many beasts in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many beasts throughout the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many beasts throughout the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many Orcs and goblins in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many goblins and Orcs in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat goblins and Orcs in the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many Orcs and goblins in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many goblins and Orcs in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat goblins and Orcs in the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many Trolls and Hobgoblins in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many Trolls and Hobgoblins in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat Trolls and Hobgoblins in the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many Trolls and Hobgoblins in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many Trolls and Hobgoblins in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat Trolls and Hobgoblins in the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many wargs in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many wargs in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many wargs in the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many wargs in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many wargs in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many wargs in the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many Wood-trolls in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many Wood-trolls in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many Wood-trolls in the Wells of LangfloodDefeat many Wood-trolls in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many Wood-trolls in the Wells of Langflood.Defeat many Wood-trolls in the Wells of LangfloodThe cave of Tithroz is home to winged beasts that feast upon the unwary when they leave the safety of its darkness behind.The cave of Tithroz is home to winged beasts that feast upon the unwary when they leave the safety of its darkness behind. They should be slain before they leave Tithroz again.Defeat bats within TithrozThe bats that live in Tithroz should be slain before they can descend upon a village in the Floodfells with their sharp fangs and grasping claws.Defeat bats in Tithroz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed.CompletedThe cave of Tithroz is home to winged beasts that feast upon the unwary when they leave the safety of its darkness behind. These excursions were once rare, but as folk move more freely about the Floodfells, these deadly flights have become more common. They should be slain before they leave Tithroz again.You defeated many of the winged beasts that haunt the shadowy ceilings and corridors of Tithroz, keeping their deadly fangs and grasping claws from the folk of the Floodfells.Someone has posted a task to collect disgusting filth. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire disgusting filth.Wanted: disgusting filth from Imlad Morgul. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: disgusting filth from Imlad Morgul.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect night-touched furs. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire night-touched furs.Wanted: night-touched furs from Imlad Morgul. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: night-touched furs from Imlad Morgul.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect toughened skins. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire toughened skins.Wanted: toughened skins from Imlad Morgul. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: toughened skins from Imlad Morgul.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Someone has posted a task to collect tufted ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire tufted ears.Wanted: tufted ears from Imlad Morgul. Collect them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: tufted ears from Imlad Morgul.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Free folk have long sought rare roots and other necessities of life amongst the foliage of Grazadh-gropor.  Wood-trolls jealously protect this place from all whom approach it.Grazadh-gropor has long been home to foul wood-trolls. Free folk seek to forage beneath its dark canopy for roots and other necessities of life. Defeating the wood-trolls throughout the area would be a boon to those living nearby.Defeat wood-trolls in Grazadh-groporDefeating wood-trolls throughout Grazadh-gropor would bring help to free folk who need the roots and herbs throughout the area to survive.Defeat wood-trolls in Grazadh-gropor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed.CompletedWho would live in Grazadh-gropor?

