You should defeat bats and destroy their perches at Búshatap.Defeat bats and destroy their perches at BúshatapBúshatap can be found in Máttugard.

You should defeat bats and destroy their perches at Búshatap.Defeat bats at Búshatap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy bat perches at Búshatap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeated bats and destroyed their perches at Búshatap.CompletedBúshatap, one of the last bat enclaves in Máttugard, is now a training ground for goblin bat-riders. Breeding is done here as well to selectively produce the largest bats for riding. Destroying the bat perches present at Búshatap should assist in culling the great numbers of these winged beasts in Máttugard.With many bats defeated and their perches destroyed at Búshatap, you have done much to assure the safety of all those who enter through the Noble Gate into Máttugard to reclaim Gundabad.It is time for the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ to break through the icy wall with which Hrímil Frost-heart blocked the entrance to Gundabad.Prince Ingór asked you to collect some picks and shovels from inside Zarkul-sulûn and deliver them to some of the Zhélruka standing idle within the fortress.Collect picks and shovels from a barrel within Zarkul-sulûnIdle Zhélruka can be found throughout the fortress of Zarkul-sulûn, waiting for you to give them picks and shovels to use to break through the ice in front of Gundabad.Distribute picks and shovels to idle Zhélruka inside Zarkul-sulûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Prince Ingór is waiting to hear that his people have been given the supplies needed to break through the ice blocking the entrance to Gundabad.Talk to Prince Ingór in Zarkul-sulûnDurin is eager to gain access to Gundabad, and believes that the ice will not long stand before the combined efforts of his Longbeards and Prince Ingór's Zhélruka.Talk to Durin in Zarkul-sulûnDurin is eager to gain access to Gundabad, and believes that the ice will not long stand before the combined efforts of his Longbeards and Prince Ingór's Zhélruka. When you are ready, he will go with you to the gates of Gundabad.Talk to Durin and travel with him to the gates of GundabadDurin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, inside the mighty court of Máttugard.Talk to Durin at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard'I am pleased we understand each other.

'Know this, ${PLAYER}. While my Zhélruka do not fight for nothing, neither do they expect their home in Gundabad to be given for nothing! No, they will pay for it with the blood they have already spent and with tomorrow's sweat on their brows. They will do their part, as I do my own.

'Gather some picks and shovels from a barrel within the fortress and distribute them among my people. They will remain idle no longer, but will help Durin's own folk to break through the ice that blocks the entrance to Gundabad. The work will go more quickly with the strong arms of my people set to the task!''Gather some picks and shovels from a barrel within the fortress and distribute them among my people. They will remain idle no longer, but will help Durin's own folk to break through the ice that blocks the entrance to Gundabad. The work will go more quickly with the strong arms of my people set to the task!''Gather some picks and shovels from a barrel within the fortress and distribute them among my people. They will remain idle no longer, but will help Durin's own folk to break through the ice that blocks the entrance to Gundabad. The work will go more quickly with the strong arms of my people set to the task!''You have armed my folk with the picks and shovels I requested? Good. The dragon's ice will not keep us from our rightful home for much longer.''The dragon's ice will not keep us from our rightful home for much longer!''I doubt not that my Longbeards and Ingór's Zhélruka will break through the ice into Gundabad in short order. Are you prepared to help us, ${PLAYER}? We will march together.''Let us march now to Gundabad, where we will carve a passage through the ice! Neither Orc nor dragon will hinder us!''At last I set foot within the Mountain-home! The mission of the Gabil'akkâ is fulfilled, despite the perils set before us! No victory is beyond my reach, ${PLAYER}!'Durin is pleased to have gained access to Gundabad, but he knows the dwarves must fortify their position inside the mountain if they are to keep it.Glóin is north of Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard, down one level.

Durin put Glóin in charge of scouting the mighty court, and asked you to aid him with his task.Glóin asked you to defeat several different enemies lurking within Máttugard, and to search for relics from the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, when last the dwarves occupied Gundabad.Defeat cave-claws or deep-claws in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat bats or gredbyg in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat cave-beasts in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search piles of debris for artifacts from the Sixth War of Dwarves and OrcsGlóin is north of Maergrind in Máttugard.'Ah, I see the warning in your eye, my friend. Let me ease your worries: I know there is much yet to do, and Gundabad is not yet fully-reclaimed. But we have made a start, and is that not sometimes the most difficult of a journey's steps?

'I set Glóin to observe the northern approach to Maergrind. Find him and see what he thinks of our defensive position here... and if it be lacking, help him to improve it until the old warrior is satisfied!''I set Glóin to observe the northern approach to Maergrind. Find him and see what he thinks of our defensive position here... and if it be lacking, help him to improve it until the old warrior is satisfied!''There you are, ${PLAYER}. Prince Durin sent you to me? Would you mind telling me of his demeanour? Did he seem rather... overfull of confidence to you?'

Glóin strokes his beard.

'We have gained the entry-halls, that is true, but we did the same during the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, when I was just a lad. We claimed the upper halls and part of the Welkin-lofts, and King Thráin called for Dwarrowmoot. At that grand meeting of the dwarves, the first held here in four thousand years, it was decided that a garrison would be left to hold the mountain; the greater portion of our armies departed for the last battle of that war, at Azanulbizar. But the garrison was too small, for we needed as many warriors as we could levy, and Gundabad was again lost.

'The prince is young, and while he knows what happened he did not stand in Máttugard then. We must guard against this overconfidence, ${PLAYER}, if we can. Let us defeat the beasts that threaten our presence in these halls and impress upon Durin that there are dangers enough to keep the Gabil'akkâ occupied! Gundabad is not won yet.

'If you happen to find any relics or weapons from the Sixth War, I would be very interested in seeing them. I imagine most such artifacts have been looted by Orcs during the intervening years, but perhaps one or two items of interest remain in the debris.''Let us defeat our foes in these halls and impress upon Durin that there are threats enough to keep the Gabil'akkâ occupied! Gundabad is not won yet.

'If you happen to find any relics or weapons from the Sixth War, I would be very interested in seeing them. I imagine most such artifacts have been looted by Orcs during the intervening years, but perhaps one or two items of interest remain in the debris.''What have you got there? You found this sword here in Máttugard? Let me read these runes and learn if this weapon saw service during the Sixth War!'

Glóin takes the sword from you and puzzles over its runes.

'Hmmm... let's see.... According to these, this blade belonged to a Longbeard by the name of Dolgur Hardroot, a member of the garrison that remained in the Mountain-home when war took the rest of us away. No doubt he fought well against the forces that surged back into Gundabad, but he did not survive their attack.

'This is a fascinating find, ${PLAYER}. During the Sixth War we did not advance far beyond the halls of Máttugard and the Welkin-lofts, for there were more pressing needs elsewhere. But today our goal is Gundabad, and we cannot leave the further halls unexplored and unconquered. The deeper we go into the mountain, the more danger we will find. Dolgur Hardroot would understand, and be pleased. I will find a place of honour for his lost weapon.'Master smith, Grámi Hornhelm, wants Máttugard cleaned up and looking more a city and less a tomb.Stone trolls can be found west of Maergrind.

You should destroy any of the stone trolls that you find.Destroy intact stone trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy broken stone trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grámi Hornhelm can be found at Maergrind in Máttugard.

You should talk to Grámi Hornhelm.Talk to Grámi Hornhelm'Since you are traversing Máttugard, might you have some time to clean up the place? It has been a long while since dwarves last occupied these halls. Máttugard is in a decent enough shape due in part to the ingenuity of the dwarves' mirror traps. A cave-troll caught in the trap's light will immediately turn to stone! No dwarf-city should have troll statues scattered about. They should be removed! As you know, trolls are not very bright, thus many have been caught in the mirror traps over the years.''Ah, Gundabad looks more like a city now! Still there is dust to clear away and much more work to be done.'The dwarf-outpost of Imrêkh-guthlu borders the heavily-fortified Orc stronghold of Deepscrave in Gundabad.Imrêkh-guthlu can be found in the southern reaches of Máttugard, near Deepscrave.

