You should talk to Belg Thickshanks.Talk to Belg Thickshanks'Ah ${PLAYER}, have you been practicing your smithing since we met in the Ironfold? Good, good! Grámi Hornhelm had asked me to accompany him to Gundabad, so that is why I am here. I will forge what is needed!

'I hear the halls of Máttugard are littered with the bones of dwarves long since dead. These dwarves must have died during a battle long ago and I know it is custom to burn the dead in times of war. We can not burn their bodies here inside the Noble Gate but we could add their bones to the forge! I can not think of anything better to honour these dwarves than to forge them into a great weapon crafted by Grámi Hornhelm and myself!''You have done well, and Máttugard feels a bit more inviting too! Do not worry, I will forge a fine weapon to honour the legacy of all those dwarves who have fallen in the quest to retake Gundabad. You have my word!'Durin, Prince of the Longbeards, and Ingór, Prince of the Zhélruka, have commanded their forces to break through the ice that blocks passage into Gundabad.Durin wishes to observe the progress made by the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ outside the gates of Gundabad.Talk to Durin outside the gates of GundabadDwarves of the Gabil'akkâ work to break through the ice that blocks passage into Gundabad.Talk to Bósi, former leader of the Iron GarrisonTalk to Stóthkell, forge-master of the Iron GarrisonTalk to Venko of the ZhélrukaTalk to Imák the Stout-axePrince Ingór desires to wield a sword, not a pick-axe, in service of the effort to gain entrance to Gundabad.Talk to Prince Ingór at the ice outside Gundabad<rgb=#FF0000>Durin and Ingór must not be defeated!</rgb>Rúvaran's forces have been routed, and now Durin is eager to return to the work of breaking through the ice before Gundabad.Talk to DurinDurin is eager to pass beyond the ice and into Gundabad.Follow DurinDurin stands on the landing before the gates of Gundabad, eager to pass into the Mountain-home.Talk to Durin on the landing outside GundabadThe gates of Gundabad lie before you, atop the stairs.Climb the stairs and pass through the gates into GundabadAt long last, Durin has entered the Mountain-home.Talk to Durin inside Gundabad'There is much to be done.''This way, my friend. See how my dwarves labour at the ice? Nothing stands long before my people when they set their minds and muscles to overcoming it!''Put your back into it, fellows! This unnatural ice cannot keep us from our goal, and it will not!

'Already I hear the ice cracking, ${PLAYER}! It will not be long before we are through!''I ordered some of my own fellows to bring up torches, and with their help we will weaken this ice. Have I not personally seen strong metal bend and twist in the forges of the Heart of Fire? I have, ${PLAYER}. So too will it be here.

'This may be a dragon's ice, but it is ice all the same.''Prince Ingór ordered that I help break through the ice alongside these Longbeards, but even without that command I would do it. Let them see the Zhélruka hold true to their word.

'Even now cracks begin to form deep in the ice! We will soon be through!''I toiled long in Mordor, ${PLAYER}, but this is not the same.

'It is much colder up here.''My folk toil no less than Durin's Longbeards, and I beam with pride to hear no complaint! But my skill is with the sword and not with the pick-axe. There must be another way I can aid this effort.'

The Zhélruka prince falls silent, listening closely.

'Do you hear that, ${PLAYER}? Our foes deliver just such a use for my talents!''I daresay we won't see him again, but if we do he will regret it. Let Ingór keep watch for him. You and I will return to the ice and help as we may.''This is it, ${PLAYER}. Nothing stands in our way.

'Let us climb the rest of the way and pass into Gundabad, the Mountain-home of my people!''I can hardly believe it, ${PLAYER}, and yet here we stand.

'Gundabad at last!'Although over two hundred years have passed since the Haban'akkâ of Thráin set siege to Máttugard during the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs, memories of that fateful battle have never left the mind of Hermáth Stormhammer.King Thráin can be found at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset.

