You should talk to Voina at Zidir-nesad.Talk to Voina at Zidir-nesad'We need to find out what happened here and where Gazathrug is. Let us search the outpost. Perhaps Gazathrug left a clue to his whereabouts.''Wait, ${PLAYER}, do you hear that? Someone is coming!''It would seem that a large number of Zhélruka venture to the Steepset, following Prince Ingór, no doubt. Well, we should tell someone about the hobgoblins and Orcs fighting each other. I'm sure there is a high ranking Zhélruka commander around here somewhere!

'Before you go, I just wanted to thank you for accompanying me on this adventure. It turned out somewhat differently than I expected, but I suppose that is the way of adventuring, is it not? I might stick to exploring Máttugard, for now, but if you decide to explore deeper into Gundabad, I will understand. Best of luck to you, ${PLAYER}.''The hobgoblins and Orcs are at odds? Why am I not surprised to hear that? Their pact has been tenuous at best since the war began! I will make sure no hobgoblins get past the Steepset!'Agátur the Boastful asks you to seek out Kurthár, a terrible cave-beast found in Máttugard.Kurthár and cave-beasts can be found in Máttugard.

You should defeat cave-beasts.Defeat KurthárDefeat cave-beasts in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect the claw of Kurthár for AgáturAgátur can be found at Steepset in Máttugard.

You should bring the claw of Kurthár to Agátur.'Hmm, have you seen the beast, ${PLAYER}? Bah, I speak of Kurthár, the mighty cave-beast! Kurthár is a terrible menace in Máttugard. The beast has ransacked multiple supply carts and must be stopped! Find Kurthár and bring me its claw. Only then shall I rest easily.''Oh ho! This is the claw of Kurthár indeed! Many at Steepset will rejoice to see this beast no more when travelling through Máttugard. You have done a good deed, ${PLAYER}.'The passage of Brúvraum has become a vile insect hive where gredbyg have claimed this area in Máttugard.Grodbog grubs can be found at Brúvraum in western Máttugard.

