You should burn the poisonous mushrooms.Burn the poisonous mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The passage of Brúvraum has become a vile insect hive where gredbyg have claimed this area in Máttugard. Growing around the hives are a variety of poisonous mushrooms. Máttugard is not the place for this invasive fungus, and for that the mushrooms should be destroyed.Glóin has asked you to aid the dwarves of the Iron Garrison he sent to scout the further reaches of Máttugard.You will find Bósi along the southern side of the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.Look for Bósi south of the great pit in MáttugardYou have found Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard, studying a troll that has been turned to stone.Talk to Bósi south of the great pit in MáttugardThe mirror mechanism south of the great pit once kept the trolls at bay, but now it is filth-covered and non-reflective. Bósi asked you to clean the dirty mirror to the south-east and restore its troll-hindering potential.Find the dirty mirror of which Bósi spoke to the south-eastThe mirror mechanism to the south-east once kept the trolls at bay, but now it is filth-covered and non-reflective. Bósi asked you to clean the dirty mirror and restore its troll-hindering potential.Clean the mirror south-east of Bósi's locationNow that you cleaned the mirror as he requested, you should return to Bósi in Máttugard, north-west of the cleaned mirror.Talk to Bósi to the north-west in MáttugardBósi directed you to the west, where he spoke of more mirrors in need of cleaning.Clean the eastern mirror mechanism at Vâr NuchurBósi directed you to the west, where he spoke of more mirrors in need of cleaning.Clean the south-western mirror mechanism at Vâr NuchurBósi directed you to the west, where he spoke of more mirrors in need of cleaning.Clean the mirror mechanism north-west of Vâr Nuchur, and down a levelSearching for mirrors to clean, you have found Bósi's son Bori north-west of Vâr Nuchur.Talk to Bori north-west of Vâr Nuchur'The prince has charged me with sending dwarves to scout the further reaches of Máttugard. There is no shortage of eager explorers among both the Longbeards and the Zhélruka, to their credit! I confess to a certain hesitation when it came to sending forth dwarves who fought with the Iron Garrison in Moria, but Bósi assured me that they were fully-prepared to face the dangers ahead. I believe him, but perhaps you can follow him and make certain my trust is not misplaced?

'Bósi and some of his kin went to the west, planning to skirt the southern side of the great pit.''Bósi assured me that the dwarves who fought for the Iron Garrison were fully-prepared to face the dangers ahead. I believe him, but perhaps you can follow him and make certain my trust is not misplaced?

'Bósi and some of his kin went to the west, planning to skirt the southern edge of the great pit.''Over here, friend!''Look at this, ${PLAYER}! Even so far underground, this troll has been turned to stone by the ingenious workings of dwarves! By the clever use of mirror mechanisms, my people redirected sunlight through the halls of Máttugard, and at some point during the long years of the mountain's abandonment, this troll ran afoul of the trap! We saw much the same in Moria, did we not?

'The device that ensnared this troll has become encrusted with dirt and filth, and no longer reflects the light as once it did. Can you clean it of grime and restore the mirror's effectiveness?''The device that ensnared this troll has become encrusted with dirt and filth, and no longer reflects the light as once it did. Can you clean it of grime and restore the mirror's effectiveness?''The device that ensnared this troll has become encrusted with dirt and filth, and no longer reflects the light as once it did. Can you clean it of grime and restore the mirror's effectiveness?''Ah, very good! That is a start. There are other similar mechanisms throughout the halls. I sent Bori looking for them, but it would not surprise me to learn that he became distracted from the task and instead went in search of enemies to slay. Follow in his steps and restore the mirrors he has not, ${PLAYER}!

'I intended for him to clean the mirrors to the west.''I sent Bori looking for other mirrors to restore, but it would not surprise me to learn that he became distracted from the task and instead went in search of enemies to slay. Follow in his steps and restore the mirrors he has not, ${PLAYER}!

'I intended for him to clean the mirrors to the west.''There you are! I should have known you would adventure here, and fear nothing!''I sent Bori looking for other mirrors to restore, but it would not surprise me to learn that he became distracted from the task and instead went in search of enemies to slay. Follow in his steps and restore the mirrors he has not, ${PLAYER}!

'I intended for him to clean the mirrors to the west of here.''I should have known you would adventure here, ${PLAYER}, for it seems you truly fear nothing! My father sent you to help me clean these mirrors? I have already restored this one, but still I appreciate the company.

'Whenever I see one of these devices I marvel at it, here no less than in Moria where first I beheld such a thing. For my ancestors to have made a weapon of light in this fashion... that is truly a feat of craft and skill!''I sent Bori looking for other mirrors to restore, but it would not surprise me to learn that he became distracted from the task and instead went in search of enemies to slay. Follow in his steps and restore the mirrors he has not, ${PLAYER}!

'I intended for him to clean the mirrors to the west.'Bori wonders whether any of the trolls that were turned to stone by the mirror mechanisms throughout Máttugard might have kept treasure-hoards nearby, and wants you to investigate.Bori has two locations in mind that might once have served as troll-hoards full of treasure. The first is a short distance to the south of his position.Bori has two locations in mind that might once have served as troll-hoards full of treasure. The second is far to the east, beyond the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.Líkmund is standing by this one-time troll-hoard, waiting to hear of your discoveries.Talk to Líkmund outside the grodbog-infested troll-hoard, to the north-westLíkmund thinks the goblins lurking in the shadowy reaches of Máttugard might have coins they stole during their occupation of Gundabad.Collect coinpurses from goblins throughout Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Líkmund asked you to bring the coinpurses to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind in partial payment of his gambling debt.Bróin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.Talk to Bróin at Maergrind, the Noble Gate'The sight of all these trolls turned to stone in the halls of Máttugard has raised in me a curiosity, ${PLAYER}. When these creatures were petrified, what happened to their treasures? Might there be valuables hidden away in their hoards? The contents of such a hoard, once ill-gotten, might be cured of that defect when found by good-hearted folk such as us!

'I have a few spots in mind that might once have served as possible troll-hoards. Will you investigate and see if any treasures remain? Try searching a short distance to the south, and once you have done that try looking far to the east, beyond the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.''I have a few spots in mind that might once have served as possible troll-hoards. Will you investigate and see if any treasures remain? Try searching first to the south, and afterwards look far to the east, beyond the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.''I have a few spots in mind that might once have served as possible troll-hoards. Will you investigate and see if any treasures remain? Try looking first to the south, and then afterwards far to the east across the great pit, friend.''Hallo there, friend. Are you also looking for treasure?

'The gredbyg have moved into this tunnel, but it seems to me it was once a troll-hoard. What valuables might still remain inside?''Did you find anything? Alas, neither did I. If this was once a troll-hoard, it is no longer, for Orcs or others of similar ilk have looted it of whatever treasures it once might have held. A pity... that looter could have been me! Just a jest, ${PLAYER}.

'But I do owe Thettmárr a rather sizeable debt, and I could have used these treasures to pay him. He graciously offered to play me in one more game of Hammers and Bones, so that I could win back my losses... but that was five games ago! Now I am so deep in his debt, and my luck has turned so poor, that I do not trust myself to approach the gambling-table ever again!

'I have seen goblins sneaking about. Do you think you could wrest some of their coin-purses from them? You would be making these halls more safe for the Gabil'akkâ, and at the same time you would be helping me with my own problem, ${PLAYER}. That way everyone is happy, except for the goblins, and what ${RACE} should care about the happiness of goblins? Once you have found three coin-purses, bring them to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind for me, and I will be in your debt. Figuratively-speaking, that is!''Do you think you could wrest coin-purses from the goblins? You would be making these halls more safe for the Gabil'akkâ, and at the same time you would be helping me with my own problem, ${PLAYER}. That way everyone is happy, except for the goblins, and what ${RACE} should care about the happiness of goblins? Once you have found three coin-purses, bring them to Thettmárr at Maergrind for me, and I will be in your debt. Figuratively-speaking, that is!''Bring those coin-purses to Thettmárr, south-west of Maergrind. It will likely not satisfy my whole debt, but I wager it will be a good start!

'You know what I mean, ${PLAYER}!''What have you brought to me, ${PLAYER}? Oh, I see. Líkmund thinks to satisfy his gambling debt to me with these goblin coin-purses? These coins are filthy. Yuck.

'There is good coinage mixed with the bad, but can I tell you something? Líkmund and I have been playing Hammers and Bones for many months now, and I have never seen a streak of ill fate like the one under which he labours now. He cannot seem to win, and I cannot seem to lose. I have begun to wonder if my friend might be cursed!

'I will accept these coins in partial satisfaction of Líkmund's debt to me, but I would consider it paid in full if he simply promised never to play Hammers and Bones ever again! There is something unnatural about his poor luck at that game, and I fear it may spill over into the rest of his life, or affect our efforts here in Gundabad!''I hope that Líkmund's ill fortune will not affect our efforts here in Gundabad!''Oh, I am sorry, my friend. I am just a little unsettled by the strange familiarity which surrounds me. I remember Thettmárr and Líkmund arguing over games of Hammers and Bones while we sought to reclaim Moria. We were, all of us, members of the Iron Garrison, and we thought to restore the Dwarrowdelf to prominence and glory.

'It was not to be. So many were lost...'

Bróin's voice trails away, and you know he is thinking of his father Brogur, who perished during the escape from Khazad-dûm. Then he shakes his head and looks you in the eye.

'But Gundabad is not Moria, and the Gabil'akkâ will not share the fate of the Iron Garrison. I should not be troubled by the reminder that Thettmárr and Líkmund played their game in Moria, and they play it here too; I should be heartened that they both live to play it still! Thank you for providing a kindly ear, ${PLAYER}. I will be all right now.'With the first foothold of the dwarves in Gundabad assured, Prince Durin calls for the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to ascend to the Steepset.Durin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.Talk to Durin at MaergrindDurin has called for the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to ascend to the Steepset.Talk to Durin and ascend to the Steepset with the Gabil'akkâDurin stands atop the Steepset, considering the progress of his people as they seek to reclaim the halls of Gundabad.Talk to Durin at the SteepsetStáli the Hewer is at the Steepset.Talk to Stáli the Hewer at the Steepset'But enough of my own troubles! I was supposed to send leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to join the prince as he climbs to the Steepset. Yes, he counts you in that number... and why should he not? You have already proven a great help to us in this campaign, and surely will in the days to come!

'Report to Durin at Maergrind, my friend, and I will join you once I find these few others.''Report to Durin at Maergrind, my friend, and I will join you once I find these few others.''Bróin found you, then? Very good. I know it was your appraisal of the lad that he weathered the hardships faced by the Iron Garrison in Moria and emerged from them no worse for wear, but all the same I have seen fit to assign him simple, easy tasks, for now. I will turn no dwarf away who vows his aid, but I do not wish to break such valuable implements with uncareful use.

'He is a bearer of messages, for now. That is a useful service, and as we acquire more victories perhaps the shadow of Khazad-dûm that blankets him will shrink.

'But I had Bróin send you to me for a purpose! Are you ready to climb with me to the Steepset, the High Seat of the Lord of Gundabad?''Then let us no longer delay! I am eager to stand atop the Steepset and behold the great hall of the dwarves from that place of honour and history!''I am saddened by the loss of the Zabad'ibîn, but I am not surprised. Who knows how long ago the clutching fingers of the Orcs might have prized them from their settings in the Steepset, and to what vile hole they might have been brought?

'But it is my hope that the light of the Zabad'ibîn will remain undimmed, and perhaps their shining radiance will guide us to them! They may yet emerge, and when they do I will place them once more atop the Steepset, a treasure of the Mountain-home restored.''It is my hope that the light of the Zabad'ibîn will remain undimmed, and perhaps their shining radiance will guide us to them! They may yet emerge, and when they do I will place them once more atop the Steepset, a treasure of the Mountain-home restored.''Listen here, ${PLAYER}. I overheard the words of Prince Durin, and they stirred in me a desire to find the Zabad'ibîn, no matter the danger. Once they are found, I will gift them to the prince and earn myself a noble place in the annals of Gundabad's reclamation!'Explorers in Gundabad will need a way to light their path as they search the ancient depths beneath the mountains.Crystals and metal ingots can be found near the forge in Vérnozal.

You should collect crystals and metal ingots to make crystal torches.Collect crystals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect metal ingots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A forge can be found in Vérnozal.

You should forge crystal torches for dwarf explorers at the forge.Dwarf explorers can be found in Vérnozal.

You should give the crystal torches you forged to the dwarf explorers.Rúzat can be found at Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to Rúzat.Talk to Rúzat'Ah, good ${CLASS}! If you are going to explore Gundabad, you might want to take the advice of humble Rúzat! I have seen the pit of Ablak-zibdîn and know its depths and far-flung corners are dark indeed. You and other explorers must make sure to have some proper light! Here, take these plans for a crystal torch. You should be able to find what you need to make them in the Hall of Vérnozal. If you would be kind to make more than you need, I am sure the other explorers would be grateful to receive one. I would make these torches myself but my crafting skills are not anywhere near the prowess of great ${PLAYER}!''Ah, you have constructed the torches well from my plans! Thank you for giving them to the other explorers. It is always an honour to work together!

'Take care when exploring Gundabad, my friend. I will be going no further than Máttugard for now. My services are needed here.'A small group of greedy Dourhands has been captured by the hobgoblin forces in Máttugard.Captured Dourhands can be found at Sadauk-kala in western Máttugard.

You should free the captured Dourhands.Free the captured DourhandsCaptured Dourhands can be found at Sadauk-kala in western Máttugard.

You should free the captured Dourhands.The freed Dourhands can be found near Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to one of the freed Dourhands.Talk to one of the freed DourhandsStolen supplies can be found at Sadauk-kala in Máttugard.

You should recover the stolen supplies.Recover stolen supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The freed Dourhands can be found near Steepset in Máttugard.

You should bring the supplies to one of the freed Dourhands.You find a few of greedy Dourhands who have been captured by the hobgoblin forces here in Sadauk-kala. It is only a matter of time before the hobgoblins obtain useful information from the Dourhands, and they would certainly use what they learn against those who seek to reclaim the Mountain-hold. You decide to rescue the Dourhands.The group of Dourhands looks weary. One musters enough effort to speak up for the rest.

'Thank you, ${CLASS}. We are indebted to your kindness. I hate to ask more of you but, well, we are traders, and all of our goods to trade were stolen by those hobgoblins that captured us! Would you be able to retrieve our supplies, good ${CLASS}? It is all we have.'You return the supplies to the Dourhands. They look relieved to have their trade-goods returned.

'We have very little to offer to repay such an act of kindness. I am sorry. All we can offer is our word that our barter prices will be fair! We thank you again, brave ${CLASS}.'Explorers in Gundabad will need a good meal or two as they search the ancient depths beneath the mountains.Cured pork and hearty vegetables can be found at the feast hall in Vérnozal.

You should collect cured pork and hearty vegetables.Collect cured pork (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect hearty vegetables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})An oven can be found at the feast hall in Vérnozal.

You should cook shchi for dwarf explorers at the oven.Dwarf explorers can be found in Vérnozal.

You should give the shchi you cooked to the dwarf explorers.Rúzat can be found at Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to Rúzat.Talk to Rúzat'Ah, good ${PLAYER}! I would recommend that you do not venture too far into Gundabad on an empty stomach, my friend! You should try my shchi! Ah, I do not have anymore though.

'Well, you could make some more! I will tell you how and I am sure the ingredients for it can be found inside the Hall of Vérnozal. If you would be kind to make more than will fill you, I am sure the other explorers here would be grateful to receive some shchi too.''It is good, is it not?! Ha, yes of course it is good! May it keep your belly full and the bellies of all the explorers full as well. I will try to make some more before I see you again, my friend!'Varthmath seeks to learn more about the frenzied stone-claws in Máttugard.Varthmath can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset, in Máttugard.

