You should travel to Ronglagam.Travel to RonglagamRonglagam can be found south-east of Zidir-nesad in Máttugard.

You should defeat stone-claws and collect samples at Ronglagam.Defeat stone-claws at Ronglagam (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect bones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect dirt samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Varthmath can be found near Ronglagam in Máttugard.

You should bring the samples to Varthmath.'${CLASS}, I will see to the destruction of these runes you have given me. You have my word.

'Now, I have just recently been informed about something that might interest you and your Beorning friend. There seems to be more frantic stone-claws nearby in a large burrow called Ronglagam. It might be worth investigating as Ronglagam is not far from the foundation of the Steepset. Dwarf-made buildings are as sturdy as they come, but nothing can last from the continuous gnawing of the stone-claws.''I am glad that the runes will be dealt with. The new information that Voina has given us is concerning. Could there be more strange runes on this side of Máttugard as well? We should travel towards the burrows of Ronglagam as soon as we are able and collect some more samples.'Varthmath inspects the samples of the stone-claw burrows.

'Hmm, nothing seems tainted or poisoned here. You would not know that from the way these stone-claws are acting, though!'An accident involving a supply cart has left the dwarves' supplies strewn about Máttugard.Supplies can be found in northern Máttugard.

You should recover supplies.Recover supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Dargumë can be found at Asbaj-khîrfin.

You should bring the supplies to Dargumë.'I ventured out here in Máttugard to hunt for treasure. It is a passion of mine, you see. I would already be out there hunting for it if it were not for the fact that I am still awaiting my tools and supplies. There was a supply cart travelling behind us. The supply cart met an unfortunate accident and all that it carried, including my tools and supplies, tumbled out and fell a great distance!

'If you are able, would you locate the fallen supplies for me? I would be most grateful to be reunited with the tools I need to hunt for treasure!''I see, some of the crates broke during the fall. Hopefully, if I sort through what you did manage to recover, I will soon enough find my tools and supplies. Treasure hunting awaits after all! Thank you, ${CLASS}!'Voina, a high ranking Zhélruka warrior, believes that the Angmarim and the hobgoblins have formed some sort of pact.Sadauk-kala can be found in western Máttugard.

You should travel to Sadauk-kala.Travel to Sadauk-kalaSadauk-kala can be found in western Máttugard.

You should defeat enemies at Sadauk-kala.Defeat enemies at Sadauk-kala (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sadauk-kala can be found in western Máttugard.

You should confront the Iron Crown emissary.Summon and confront the Iron Crown emissarySadauk-kala can be found in western Máttugard.

You should confront the Iron Crown emissary.Summon and confront the Iron Crown emissaryVoina can be found at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset, in Máttugard.

You should talk to Voina.Talk to Voina'Upon the highest bridge within the encampment of Sadauk-kala, my scout witnessed an emissary of the Iron Crown speak at length with high-ranking captains of the hobgoblin forces here in Máttugard.

'I worry what this could mean. We already know the hobgoblins are devoted to the Frost-horde. Have the Angmarim cut their ties to Gorgar's forces as have the hobgoblins? Does Angmar seek an alliance with Hrímil Frost-heart? I do not know what is in store for us as we delve deeper into Gundabad, but I do know this Iron Crown Emissary remains at Sadauk-kala, and may be our best chance to learn about this new arrangement between our enemies.''You were not able to learn anything new from the Angmarim? That is all right, ${PLAYER}. Even had we captured the emissary alive, I doubt he would have spoken any truth to us.

'But we have learned something: we can now say for certain that the Angmarim and the hobgoblins work together in some capacity. There is only one way to learn more about what plans they share for Gundabad and that is for us to venture into the Pit of Stonejaws.''Have you come to bargain? No, there is naught you have that the Iron Crown desires. You have come to declare fealty then? You would make a fine servant.

'I see then. You have not come here to speak, only to act. Just as you acted against those with whom I speak, I shall also act, and act with resistance. You shall learn no more from me than you already know, determined and foolish ${RACE}!'Bráthi the master prospector is searching for precious geodes in Gundabad.Various rocks can be found next to Bráthi at Zidir-nesad.

You should choose the correct rock.Various rocks can be found next to Bráthi at Zidir-nesad.

You should pick up the correct rock.Pick up the correct rockYou should crack open the rock that you picked up.Crack open the rock that you picked upBráthi can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset.

You should show the geode to Bráthi.Show the geode to Bráthi'Greetings again, skilled ${CLASS}. I have come to Gundabad in search of rare geodes. You have a keen eye. Perhaps you wish to assist me in the search for geodes?

'Good! There is much of Gundabad to search! Before you begin searching Gundabad for these prized stones, I would first like you to show me what you know of geodes. Next to me there are three rocks. I would like you to pick out the stone with a geode inside. When you have picked up the correct stone, you will need to crack it open to reveal the geode within.''Ah, you have done well! I can see your skills and keen eyes have only improved since last we met. I believe you are ready then.

<rgb=#00FF00>'Throughout Gundabad you will find many round rocks that contain geodes within. I recommend searching for the following stones: granite, basalt, rhyolite, limestone, and sandstone.</rgb>

'I ask of you to search and collect them when you are able and return with what you find. I will make your endeavours worth your while too, as I have much to trade for such exquisite geodes.

'Good hunting, ${PLAYER}!'Gazathrug's fear of losing the Upper Reaches of Máttugard are quite warranted.Talk to Hetbrúda.Talk to HetbrúdaFind a good location to spy on the Orcs.Find a good location to spy on the OrcsListen to the Orc factions.Listen to the Orc factionsDefeat the remaining hobgoblins.Defeat the remaining hobgoblinsTalk to Gazathrug.Talk to GazathrugDefeat Gazathrug.Defeat Gazathrug'Come, ${PLAYER}, let us continue to the Steepset. While at Imrêkh-guthlu I overheard that dwarves had secured Zidir-nesad.''We need to hide. Quickly, behind the large mirror!''Come closer, ${RACE}.

'I should've died by those hobgoblins. Your interference was warranted, however. The hobgoblins would have reported back of my loss and too soon would these halls of Vok-kasol fall to the Frost-horde. You made sure they didn't make it, and for that I commend you.

'Now, I must die with honour and for Gorgar. I can't die slowly upon this stone. No, I must be killed in combat. Grant me this last wish, ${RACE}.'Durin desires to see with his own eyes the Steepset, the High Seat of the Lord of Gundabad.Durin stands with his personal guard Hrostyr not far from the Steepset, and he waits to speak with you.Talk to Durin in the court below the SteepsetDurin asked you to clear the stairs leading to the Steepset of foes. Once you have accomplished this, he will rejoin you at the top of the stairs.Clear the stairs leading to the Steepset of foesNow that you have cleared the stairs of his foes, Durin can climb to the Steepset.

He waits to speak with you at the top of the stairs.Talk to Durin atop the stairs near the SteepsetDurin stands before the Steepset, the High Seat of the Lord of Gundabad.Hear the words of Durin before the SteepsetDurin stands by the Steepset, mourning for what has been lost.Talk to Durin by the Steepset'The reclamation of Gundabad has begun. That will have to be enough... for now.''The stairs to the Steepset are just to the south of us, ${PLAYER}. Before we ascend, Hrostyr and I will make safe this court. I do not ask you to follow us! With the Red Axe I will make short work of the creatures here, and with Hrostyr to guard my flank I will fear no injury.

'This is the task I have for you, my capable friend: I ask that you clear the stairs of our foes. Once you have accomplished that, Hrostyr and I will join you at the top and we will approach the Steepset together.''The Steepset is just ahead, ${PLAYER}.

'We will stand together, and show that none can oppose us!''Glóin mourns for the Zabad'ibîn, and he is not alone. Seven sacred jewels they were, brilliant and scintillating even in the dark, and they were housed in the very stone of this throne for centuries. But that was long ago, and the Zabad'ibîn have been stolen away during the years of our absence by persons unknown.

'I did not truly expect to find otherwise, but the sight of this plain stone is like a dagger in my heart, ${PLAYER}, and it would be the same for any Longbeard. Recovering the gems and returning them to their pride of place in the Steepset would mean a great deal to me, for it would signal that treasures long thought lost could come back to us.'Something stirs the creatures of Máttugard from within the caverns, deep under the Mighty Court.Talk to Varthmath.Talk to VarthmathExplore the cave and learn of what stirs the beasts in Máttugard.Search the cave for what stirs the beasts in MáttugardDefeat the frenzied beasts guarding the ritual obelisk.Defeat the frenzied deep-clawDefeat the frenzied grodbogDestroy the ritual obelisk.Destroy the ritual obelisk'That obelisk was certainly a creation of the Angmarim. Come, let us return to the Steepset and report what we have found.''The cavern is vast. Well, shall we continue then?'Within the Great Court of Máttugard lies the strange Plaque of the Moon.A lit moon mirror must be somewhere in Máttugard.

