You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti Graver'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. Last we spoke, I was at work on the Dáinlik. My work there is finally complete, so I followed Náin the Slakeless to Elderslade. Now here we are in Gundabad, where my skills as a foreman of great dwarf-works can be put to use once again.

'Before us stands the throne of Zidir-nesad, once the seat of the Lord of Gundabad but now in ruin and disrepair. I have been researching all there is to know about the Steepset, and I believe with the correct materials we can fully rebuild the throne of Zidir-nesad. Will you assist me in this task?''We have done it! The throne of Zidir-nesad has been rebuilt!'

Rísti Graver inspects the throne with a keen eye.

'Hmm, while it has been rebuilt, it has not been restored. The seven sacred gems are still missing. Without those gems, the throne will never be made completely whole. If I learn of the whereabouts of any of these gems, I will be the first to let you know. I am sure that together, in time, we will be able to fully restore this seat, just as we will be able to reclaim Gundabad.'After encountering the elusive cold-worm, Forsting, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Reclaimers of the Mountain-hold.Belga Defthand can be found at Steepset in Máttugard.

You have acquired a trophy from an elusive foe in Gundabad. You should deliver it to Belga Defthand, a skilled taxidermist of the Longbeards.Deliver Forsting's tail to Belga Defthand at SteepsetAfter encountering the elusive cold-worm, Forsting, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Reclaimers of the Mountain-hold.

As you inspect Forsting's tail, you wonder if the etched scars upon the scales signify some status of the beast within the Frost-horde.

You decide to bring this trophy to Belga Defthand, a skilled taxidermist of the Longbeards, so that it might be preserved once Gundabad is reclaimed.'What have you brought me now?'

Belga Defthand inspects Forsting's tail closely, holding it up to the light at Steepset.

'Ah, this shall make a fine trophy! I shall preserve this rare find. Let us hope fewer of the Frost-horde shall trouble us in the days to come!'The sacred Jewel of Amnâd has been found.Rísti Graver can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard.

