You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti GraverRísti Graver, the greatest foreman of the Ironfold, has learned the location of the sacred Jewel of Amnâd. While the jewel has been found, it will take a skilled hero to recover it and return it to the throne! You should seek out Rísti Graver as soon as you are able.'I thank you for retrieving the Jewel of Amnâd, one of the seven sacred jewels of Zidir-nesad. I have been researching the jewel since its discovery, but to see it restored fills me with a feeling of triumph I can hardly explain, even to you.

'Behold its light green radiance! This gem symbolizes the will of the dwarves to achieve whatever they set their minds and muscles to accomplish... let it be a sign to all those who struggle against overwhelming odds, and give them the strength to persevere! The return of this jewel shall undoubtedly give us the will to continue our quest and see the Mountain-home reclaimed.''The sacred Jewel of Amnâd! It has been found, right here in Máttugard, but no one can say how to reach it! I ask you to find a way to retrieve it.'Whether or not Shúkurz is lying, the possibility of dwarf prisoners should be investigated.Múta can be found outside Gazat-fark, located on the lowest level of Deepscrave and to the south-east of Aslíf.Talk to Múta outside of Gazat-farkFour dwarf smiths are being held at Gazat-fark.

One has been spotted on the ground level, and the other on the second floor. The others may be trapped in Durbángh -- behind the doors on the second floor.You have rescued the dwarf smiths.

You should return to Náin in Aslíf on the upper tier.Return to Náin in AslífYou have returned to Aslíf and should talk to Féli.Talk to FéliYou should talk to Shúkurz and see what he has to say.Talk to Shúkurz'I've sent Múta to scout Gazat-fark and make sure it isn't a trap. You'll find it on the lowest level of Deepscrave, in the south-east. By the time you arrive, she'll be there.

'If you find any information on the location of Dhúrstrok, let me know straightaway. It's time we stopped looking around aimlessly, and started acting.''${PLAYER}, you made it. It seems Shúkurz was telling the truth after all. Einar here has seen two dwarves already -- one on the ground level, and another up the stairs. The other two haven't been spotted yet, but I've noticed Orcs going in and out of a door on the second level. The remaining dwarves might be in there.

'While you rescue the dwarves, I'll go in and try to obtain any information I can get my hands on. Once the last dwarf is out, I'll help them find their way back. Good luck.''My apologies, I didn't mean for you to see us have such a heated discussion. Lord Náin believes we are wasting our time with Shúkurz.

'Múta just returned with the smiths. Her search around Gazat-fark did not reveal anything new, nor anything that contradicts Shúkurz's claims of Dhúrstrok requiring more weapons. If anything, she found information that supports his claims.

'If they need those weapons, then the smiths' rescue will not go unnoticed. Perhaps we could use this to our advantage somehow....

'Shúkurz -- what say you? If you tell us where Dhúrstrok is, we'll let you go.''I -- I've been lying, I don't know where Dhúrstrok is. Didn't want to give that angry dwarf over there an excuse to execute me. So fine, I'll help you, but what choice have I got?'Náin's fate is in your hands.Shúkurz has returned with a wealth of information.

You should talk to Múta and formulate a plan.Talk to MútaDhúrstrok is located in the catwalks north-east of Aslíf. The catwalks can be reached through the lift.

Múta will meet you inside Dhúrstrok.Find DhúrstrokComplete 'Assault on Dhúrstrok' on any difficulty.

Use the Instance Finder to enter Assault on Dhúrstrok.Complete 'Assault on Dhúrstrok' on any difficultyYou have rescued Náin and brought him back safely to Aslíf.

You should talk to him.Talk to Náin in Aslíf'Náin's trapped behind a door with two locks. The goblin Mozrúk holds one key, and a troll named Gâdh-and-Shum holds the other.

'Watch out when you're dealing with Mozrúk. He's one of those bat-riders -- got an arsenal of explosives he creates himself.

'Gâdh-and-Shum is a mystery, but there are rumours of him dealing with magic. Even his own kind thinks there's something... unnatural with him.

'They each work in separate wings of Dhúrstrok. I don't know what they're going to do with that dwarf, but you better act fast. He didn't look so well when I saw him.''You've done your part, Shúkurz. Féli will see to it that you and your party are escorted safely out of Gundabad.

'${PLAYER}, it looks like we'll want a small group of people for this job -- rescuing Lord Náin will go faster. If you have allies who can rally to us quickly, bring them along; if not, we'll work together instead.

'When you're ready, take the lift in the north-east all the way up to the catwalks. Find Dhúrstrok; I'll meet you there.''I am in your debt, ${PLAYER}. I let anger overtake me and cloud my senses. It was unbefitting of me as a leader -- nay, as a dwarf. I selfishly put my own thirst for revenge above the concerns of the Gabil'akkâ.'

He absentmindedly reaches for his beard before realizing that it's no longer there. A tired sigh escapes him.

'At least I have paid dearly for my actions.'Stáli the Hewer has charged his apprentice Eskil Bloodthumb with searching the caverns of Deepscrave for the Zabad'ibîn, the lost jewels of the Steepset.Eskil Bloodthumb is at the entrance to Deepscrave from Máttugard, south-west of the Steepset.Find Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to Deepscrave, south-west of the SteepsetStáli the Hewer's assistant, Eskil Bloodthumb, stands at the entrance to Deepscrave.Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to DeepscraveEskil Bloodthumb has asked you to observe his fighting style so you can give him pointers about his combat form.Observe Eskil's fighting formEskil has dropped his axe, fumbling it while trying to show off his fighting form for you.Pick up Eskil's fumbled axeEskil Bloodthumb stands at the entrance to Deepscrave, weaponless and ashamed of his clumsiness.Give Eskil back his axeWorried that he lacks the necessary training to successfully investigate Deepscrave, Eskil Bloodthumb has asked you to find a teacher at Maergrind willing to help him hone his skills.Eskil Bloodthumb is still at the entrance to Deepscrave, waiting for the news that you found him a teacher.Talk to Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to DeepscraveStáli the Hewer is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate.Talk to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind, the Noble Gate'It is my hope to find one of the Zabad'ibîn, and... no! Why should I aim so low? Say instead that I shall be the one to find all seven of the sacred stones, and let the name Stáli the Hewer echo in every dwarf-hall from here to the Blue Mountains!

'Now that I have spoken the dream aloud, I detect in it a flaw. How am I to deliver seven such valuable stones to Prince Durin? Each of the Zabad'ibîn should be carefully-handled, and I should fear to drop one when the time comes to pass them into the prince's hands....

'Ah-ha! A solution comes. I will not deliver the stones into Durin's care individually, but rather fashioned into a larger work of art! But what? Perhaps a statue of the prince himself, holding aloft one or more of the gems? Mayhap the statue can wear a belt with the seven stones embedded within? Worry not! These problems can be solved.

'There is the small matter of finding the Zabad'ibîn. I sent my assistant Eskil Bloodthumb to search Deepscrave for works of dwarf-art that might be recovered from the Orcs. Find him and tell him he is to also search for these gems!''I sent my apprentice Eskil Bloodthumb to search Deepscrave for works of dwarf-art that might be recovered from the Orcs. Find him and tell him he is to also search for these stones!''Oh, hullo there, friend.''I sent my apprentice Eskil Bloodthumb to search Deepscrave for works of dwarf-art that might be recovered from the Orcs. Find him and tell him he is to also search for these stones!''Oh, hullo there, friend. My master sent me to search Deepscrave for valuable works of dwarf-art he might restore, but I have heard from scouts that the caverns crawl with foes, and the Orcs have a village there.'

You tell Eskil that Stáli has asked him to search also for sign of the Zabad'ibîn that were lost from the Steepset, and the artist's assistant frowns again.

'Oh my. Yes, I will do my best, although I am not very practised at the combat arts. Actually... you are an accomplished adventurer. Do you think you could observe my... fighting style, my combat form, whatever it is you heroes look for... and tell me what I might be doing wrong?

'Thank you so much, my friend! Watch closely and tell me what I need to improve!''Ah. Thank you, yes. Sorry.'

Eskil looks down at the ground, dejected and ashamed.

'Am I being sent to my death, ${PLAYER}? Reports from Deepscrave make it sound a den of foes, crawling with Orcs and goblins, and you have seen what happens to me when I seek to wield an axe! I am apprenticed to Stáli and must do as he orders, but if I venture into Deepscrave as I am now, I will surely perish, and my master will need another apprentice.

'I know you are busy with your other duties, but do you think you could find a dwarf at Maergrind that might instruct me in the ways of combat? What I need is a good teacher: skilled and patient both!''I know you are busy with your other duties, but do you think you could find a dwarf at Maergrind that might instruct me in the ways of combat? What I need is a good teacher: skilled and patient both!''Eskil Bloodthumb seeks a trainer in the arts of war? I have seen him following that imperious sculptor through the halls of Máttugard, a cowed and shrinking figure! He is no warrior. Not yet, at least.

'I and my axe will make him a worthy addition to the Gabil'akkâ, much as his master carves unhewn stone into figures of royal shape! By my training's end he will fear nothing... but not before. Bring him my first lesson: "get away from Deepscrave! You are not ready for such a place as that!"

'Tell him too that once he has returned to a place of safety I will find him for a second lesson. A dead dwarf is no help to his master or his prince, and with my help he will not become one!''I am too busy to provide such teaching. I am sorry.''I forge metal into weapons, I do not refine inexperienced dwarves into warriors!

'Find someone else!''You expect me to teach a young Longbeard how to fight? He would not survive the experience, I assure you, even had I the time to spend.

