'The Berg-beam remains strong, then? Good, good! For the Pillar of the Mountain to retain its stability even after so many centuries of Orc degradation seems a marvel to me. But perhaps it should not surprise me so, for I feel the presence of some enchantment upon the Mountain-home: an enchantment that preserves it from Orkish abasements. Have you not noticed the remarkable resilience of the walls of Gundabad, an unwillingness to suffer the marks of Orc-filth?

'That may be so, but still the Orcs have lived beneath the mountain for many years, and the refuse in which they dwelt may hold useful information for those seeking to combat them. Scour their homes and persons in Deepscrave for useful records, and bring them to me when your search is done.''Orcs have lived beneath this mountain for many years, and the refuse in which they dwelt may hold useful information for those seeking to combat them. Scour their homes and persons in Deepscrave for useful records, and bring them to me when your search is done.''You found a great deal of information among the dwellings of the Orcs, I see! I shall peruse these as soon as I am able. I am not accustomed to... so much reading, and in such unpleasant Orkish handwriting, no less!

