Rékkur in Aslíf will be glad to hear the news.Talk to Rékkur in Aslíf'Every now and then, the Orcs at Durshulot will mount coordinated attacks against us. These attacks have not been overwhelming or difficult to deal with, but there must be a reason why the Orcs are holding back. I suspect the purpose of these attacks is to tire us out, make us waste our resources before the longer fight ahead.

'But two can play this game. Go north-west on the middle tier to Durshulot and destroy their weapons.''The job is done, then? Perhaps we guards can finally get some rest! Thank you -- I'm sure I speak for everyone here when I say that.'Gorgar's forces flock to Durshulot, waving his banners proudly. Rékkur has an idea for what to do with them.Durshulot lies on the middle tier to the north-west of Aslíf.

Rékkur believes that burning the Orkish banners at Durshulot will diminish the morale among Gorgar's forces.Burn Orkish banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rékkur is stationed in Aslíf and will want to hear that the deed is done.Talk to Rékkur in Aslíf'The banners hanging in Durshulot mock us. The Orcs believe that those banners, and Gorgar himself, remain untouchable.

'We may not be able to deal with Gorgar today, but we can burn those banners at the very least. Head north-west to Durshulot. Show the Orcs that they are mistaken!''Magnificent job, my friend. I could see the smoke from here. And who knows? Perhaps we'll get our hands on Gorgar soon enough!'Goblins have been stealing books from Gundabad, but why?Durshulot Book-nabbers can be found in Deepscrave.

Some of the goblins of Deepscrave seem to be carrying lumpy sacks. You should investigate their contents.Collect a sackDurshulot Book-nabbers can be found in Deepscrave.

Some of the goblins of Deepscrave seem to be carrying lumpy sacks. You should investigate their contents.Collect sack of books (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lore-master Rúni can be found at Aslíf in Deepscrave.

