You hand him the sack of books.

'Goblins are not really known to be collectors of books or avid readers, are they? A scout returned earlier with a similar story to yours. Apparently they are collecting books on behalf of someone named Gâdh! I am incredibly curious to know what they have been up to!'Though she can no longer hunt alone, Elta still wishes to claim her final bounties in Gundabad.Elta has offered to split the bounty for defeating Kaupur at Kordh Gúrat.

Kordh Gúrat lies on the level below the middle tier, to the south-west of Aslíf.Lure out and defeat KaupurElta is waiting in Aslíf for your return with the "armour."'Ah, a ${CLASS}, aren't you? Would you like to help an old hunter?

'I came to Deepscrave to help the Gabil'akkâ with a few bounties. I'm no longer as quick as I used to be, but I refuse to retire! To complete my final jobs within Gundabad itself... I would be happy enough to retire afterwards.

'If you'd like to split the bounties with me, you'll have to carry out the actual hunting. I've done my part of the job already -- tracked the targets down across Deepscrave myself. There are a few names to cross off my list, starting with the first target, Kaupur.

'Go south-west and down a level from the middle tier to Kordh Gúrat. Use this steak to catch Kaupur's attention. Oh, and bring back his armour, would you? I'm sure the Gabil'akkâ would be interested.''I see you've managed to retrieve the drake's scales. These creatures that we hunt threaten the Gabil'akkâ, but parts of them may also be useful.

'Hm? What did you think I was sending you off to fight? I simply name my targets after folks I don't like... I named that cold-drake after a former friend with a very cold personality. Appropriate, no? It's incredible that we befriended each other in the first place!

'But enough about that. Should you still be interested in this line of work, I have more bounties to share.'Finding the final creature on Elta's list might be trickier than it seems....Elta has suggested to wait and see if Bothin will appear.Wait with EltaBothin has not appeared.

You should talk to Elta and come up with a different plan together.Talk to EltaElta has asked you to find Bothin alone.

You should venture into the cave Skrizagáf, on the eastern side of Shataz-kordh.Find signs of BothinYou should continue looking for signs of Bothin in Skrizagáf.You have found a dead Orc in Skrizagáf.

You should examine the corpse.Examine the Orc corpseYou should pretend to steal the Orc corpse and trick Bothin into emerging.Lure out and defeat BothinYou have defeated Bothin and obtained its hide.

Elta waits for you outside of Shataz-kordh.'As you were burning the corpses, I was thinking of what to call the worm. A bit tricky, but I believe the name I've chosen fits well: Bothin, named after an old hunting partner of mine who was lazy to the bone. You've already shown more competence than he ever did, and I am not someone who is easily impressed!

'Now, let's wait for Bothin to emerge. Make sure to keep its hide at least mostly intact; we'll want to hand that over to the Gabil'akkâ.''If we wait any longer, my beard will become whiter than it already is! Perhaps there are more Orc corpses in the worm-cave, Skrizagáf? You must've passed by its entrance by now -- it's on the eastern side of Shataz-kordh.

'Entering the worm-cave Skrizagáf might be the only option. You'll have to go alone -- with these old bones, I'd be more of a burden than a boon, but I'm sure you can manage. Good hunting.'The Orc's body has sustained large bite marks that could not have been inflicted by most of the worms here. This corpse must be what's encouraging Bothin to stay inside the cave.

Bothin hasn't made an appearance, but pretending to steal its food may enrage it into emerging.'Heh, I was starting to wonder when I'd have to go in myself! No, no, I jest.

'Though our partnership was brief, I could not have asked for a better hunting partner. You honour me, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps we'll meet again -- but now, it's time for me to retire!'Only one bat in Dalugronk is capable of carrying Orcs, and it's next on Elta's list.The Orc village Dalugronk is located on the lowest level of Deepscrave, to the north-east of Aslíf.

The Orc beast-masters may have bait that you can use to lure out the bat Sumri.Obtain bat bait from an Orc beast-masterYou have obtained bait to lure Sumri out.Lure out and defeat SumriYou have defeated Sumri.

Elta waits for you nearby to the north-west, watching the worm nest Shataz-kordh.'The next target is a giant bat in the Orc village Dalugronk, to the north-east at the bottom level of Deepscrave. The Orcs there are trying to ride bats like the goblins, but only one can carry them. Not well enough to fly far, but I'd hate to find out what can happen next. I suppose I'll name it... Sumri.

'Luckily, Sumri is a disobedient beast; the Orc beast-masters must coax it with spiders. You could find a few spiders from some of the beast-masters and then lure Sumri out yourself.

'Once you're done, meet me outside the village -- I'll be nearby to the north-west, watching the worm nest Shataz-kordh.

'Curious about the bat's name? Well, let's make a deal: bring me the bat's fur, and I'll tell you.''Hrm... perhaps I should not have named such a strong creature after my old teacher. He always hovered over my shoulder, you see. Well, who's the one working with the Gabil'akkâ now? Heh.

'Anyways, the scouts will keep an eye on the village to make sure we don't have bat-riding Orcs on our hands anytime soon. I hope we won't; bat-riding goblins are enough of a nuisance!

'I've got one more name on the list. You won't have to venture far.'Vatug-ronk, home to the fiercest Orcs in Gundabad, also plays host to a number of trolls who are tougher than average.Defeating the trolls of Vatug-ronk as quickly as possible before they cause deaths on the battlefield would be best.Defeat trolls in Vatug-ronkDefeating the trolls of Vatug-ronk as quickly as possible before they cause deaths on the battlefield would be best.Defeat trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of trolls in Vatug-ronk.CompletedVatug-ronk, home to the fiercest Orcs in Gundabad, also plays host to a number of trolls who are tougher than average. Defeating them as quickly as possible before they cause deaths on the battlefield would be best.You have defeated a number of trolls in Vatug-ronk. The less the Gabil'akkâ has to deal with the trolls, the better.With the Orc taken as prisoner, Náin and Féli prepare to interrogate him.Náin waits for you in Aslíf.Talk to NáinNáin has asked to speak with you in Aslíf.Talk to Náin'I understand the value in listening, at least; perhaps the Orc will accidentally let go of important information. I'll tolerate his presence for now. But the moment he ceases to be useful, I will not hesitate to bring the Black Mattock down upon his head.

'Come, then. Let us hear what he has to say.''Keep your wits about you.'

<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>'Gorgar's pride must know no bounds if he is boastful enough to claim that he killed my father. Hah! As if that wretch could have ever laid a finger on him!

'My people might never see justice done for what the Orcs have wrought upon us. But if we defeat Gorgar, then I can see at least a small amount of justice done for my family. To put an end to the line of Azog once and for all... my grandfather and my father would rest easier, knowing it is over.'Light is scarce in Deepscrave. The lanterns around 'Abad-nuhbu have gone unlit for too long.Thrúthug has asked you to light the lanterns near the main staircases circling 'Abad-nuhbu.

Half of the lanterns can be found above Aslíf on the upper tier, and half below.Light lanterns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have lit the lanterns.Completed'Came up from Aslíf to try and help Felgar here. Can't say it was easy finding my way up and down the main staircases circling 'Abad-nuhbu through all that darkness. There're lanterns near the stairs, but the Orcs have snuffed 'em out.

'You headed down? Maybe you could light the lanterns along the way. Half of 'em are above Aslíf on the upper tier, and half below.

'It'd be nice if getting lost in the dark became the least of my worries.'With fresh flames dancing at their cores, the lanterns now hold the shadows at bay. Here, the darkness of Deepscrave does not feel so suffocating.

Perhaps, in time, the dwarves shall see the rest of Deepscrave illuminated and claim it as their home once more.Deepscrave is below Máttugard, in Gundabad.Féli can be found in Aslíf, on the upper tier of Deepscrave.

You should seek him out.Talk to Féli in Aslíf'If you are seeking Deepscrave, it is not far from here. You can find it by travelling south. Tread carefully, for very few dwarves have yet to venture within the deep shaft.

'If you do venture there, you should first seek out Féli, an advisor to Náin the Slakeless. Náin has led a group of dwarves into Deepscrave just recently; they should be on the upper tier, in Aslíf.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! It is good of you to join our expedition; there is much to do. Should you seek to help us, Lord Náin might have just the task.'Náin has never been one for inaction, and Shúkurz deserves an apology.Náin has asked you to help him apologize to Shúkurz.

Shúkurz is preparing for the upcoming journey in an old home at the base of Buzra-salân, north of Aslíf.Talk to ShúkurzYou have delivered Náin's apology to Shúkurz.Completed'There is one last thing I would ask of you. Years of bloodshed and bitterness may exist between our people, but I did not judge Shúkurz's character correctly. I would like to apologize, though I know my presence causes him undue stress. I would not approach him myself if he did not wish it.

'Would you mind sending my apologies to him? Féli told me that Shúkurz and his party are hiding in an old home at the base of Buzra-salân in the north. I will not pretend such a small gesture will make things better, but it's a start.

'You do not have to tell me his response; I trust that you'll honour my request.''That Náin fellow apologized? To me? Strange times we're living in. It's not like I had much of a choice, agreeing to help you folks. But if he could find it in him to apologize, maybe there's something for us Orcs in the future other than war.

'We'll be on our way soon enough. I wonder what's out there....'You have delivered Náin's apology to Shúkurz. An uncertain future stands in the way of Shúkurz and his people, but they may yet find peace.After encountering the elusive ukhrash, Gurlázg, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Reclaimers of the Mountain-hold.Belga Defthand can be found at Steepset in Máttugard.

You have acquired a trophy from an elusive foe in Gundabad. You should deliver it to Belga Defthand, a skilled taxidermist of the Longbeards.Deliver Gurlázg's claw to Belga Defthand at SteepsetAfter encountering the elusive ukhrash, Gurlázg, you have claimed a trophy that may be of value to the Reclaimers of the Mountain-hold.

As you inspect Gurlázg's claw, you take care to not get yourself caught in its mighty grasp.

You decide to bring this trophy to Belga Defthand, a skilled taxidermist of the Longbeards, so that it might be preserved once Gundabad is reclaimed.'What have you brought me now?'

Belga Defthand inspects Gurlázg's claw closely, holding it up to the light at Steepset.

'Ah, this shall make a fine trophy! I shall preserve this rare find. There are many strange creatures living within the depths of Gundabad. Perhaps you will find them all!'Seeking notes from the Orcs in Dalugronk may grant some insight into the current morale of Gorgar's forces.Orkish notes with useful information may be scattered around Dalugronk.Find Orkish notes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found a number of Orkish notes, each with varying degrees of usefulness to the Gabil'akkâ.

Féli in Aslíf will be interested to hear of your findings. Aslíf is on the upper tier of Deepscrave.Talk to Féli in AslífIn barely-decipherable handwriting, this note mentions the writer's doubts about the future of Dalugronk. Worms from Skrizagáf have taken over part of the village, chasing out the Orcs and killing those who get too close. To make matters worse, hobgoblins often come to raid the villagers. Gorgar has not extended any support to his people.

While this note may not be considered valuable intelligence, it does grant some insight into the current morale of Gorgar's forces. There may be other similar notes with useful information scattered around Dalugronk.'These notes paint a grim future for the Orcs here. They seem to be beset on all sides by hostile forces, including our own. Perhaps more Orcs will abandon Gorgar, in time.

'Regardless, thank you for recovering these notes. I'll pass them on to the scouts to examine whether there is more information to be gleaned from here.'The sacred Jewel of Abnâh has been found.Rísti Graver can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti GraverRísti Graver can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti GraverNakhauga can be found in Deepscrave.

You should collect the Jewel of Abnâh from Nakhauga.Defeat NakhaugaRetrieve the Jewel of AbnâhSummon NakhaugaThe Throne of Zidir-nesad can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard.

You should add the Jewel of Abnâh to the Throne of Zidir-nesad under Rísti Graver's supervision.Rísti Graver can be found at Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti GraverRísti Graver, the greatest foreman of the Ironfold, has learned the location of the sacred Jewel of Abnâh. While the jewel has been found, it will take a skilled hero to recover it and return it to the throne! You should seek out Rísti Graver as soon as you are able.'I thank you for retrieving the Jewel of Abnâh, one of the seven sacred jewels of Zidir-nesad. I have spent so long studying the meaning of these gems, but to finally see this one restored lightens my heart and fills me with a happiness I find difficult to explain.

'How blue shines the light reflecting from it! This gem symbolizes the grand traditions of the dwarves, and reminds us to remember the places from which we came. The return of this jewel will undoubtedly boost the spirits of all who see it, letting them know the rightness of our cause. The Mountain-home welcomes we who come back to it.''The sacred Jewel of Abnâh! It has been found in the Deepscrave, upon the crown of a greedy Orc named Nakhauga whose fingers on the sacred stone cannot be further allowed! I ask you to retrieve it.'Scout-master Ausma has entered Shakhajât on her own, and though her apprentices were ordered to stay put, they are determined to come to her aid.You should consult Klúso and Molkha.Talk to KlúsoTalk to MolkhaKyrstig is waiting to hear what the other scouts have decided.Talk to KyrstigIt is time to venture inside the fort with your scout allies.Meet the Scout Trio outside ShakhajâtKyrstig has a plan.Talk to KyrstigYou should search for the way to the throne room.Find the throne roomThe throne room awaits you and your allies!Complete 'Instance: To Ausma's Aid'Ausma has been rescued from the clutches of Warlord Dushtalbúk!

You should talk to Ausma in Bárgstad.Talk to Scout-master Ausma'I don't know what to do! Am I wrong to think Ausma is in trouble? She probably told us to stay here for a good reason.... No, I think we should go after her! The four of us can make it through that fort! But I don't want to make this call on my own. Will you ask Klúso and Molkha what they think?''Kyrstig wants to go in after Ausma? I am with her, of course! Stout-axes do not abandon their own!''Kyrstig wants to go after Ausma? Well, I applaud her bravery, but it seems risky to storm the hobgoblin fort with so few of us. And Ausma clearly ordered us to stay here. Hmm....

'All right, I'll do it, but if we get in trouble for disobeying her orders, you'll be the one to shoulder the blame!''This must be the throne room! We might have to fight Warlord Dushtalbúk as soon as we enter. Are you ready?''And here we are, back at camp, all safe and sound.'

Ausma sighs deeply, clearly unhappy about the outcome of her mission.

'Honestly, my pride is more wounded than my body, but I will have to sit out on some of our upcoming missions. I will ensure Shakhajât has an adequate watch, and station myself in Vérnozal to oversee the Gabil'akkâ's operations. You and my apprentices have more to do, however! When it is time to make our move on the hobgoblins, I will send word to you to find Hórin. Until then, go, explore Gundabad, and win many battles for us!''It's decided then! The three of us will move towards Shakhajât. Come meet us when you're ready, and we will launch our attack!''Good, you're here! Are you ready to tear this place apart? Ausma must have gone to the throne room. We can't go the same way as last time. Trust me, I already checked: the hobgoblins removed the stairs! So, we're going to have to go through the front door, and through a lot of foes beside! If we make enough noise out here, maybe the distraction will help Ausma!'Kyrstig has asked you to defeat the Angmarim cultists in Akhaldarâg tombs.Akhaldarâg is on the south-west side of the Pit of Stonejaws.Defeat Angmarim in Akhaldarâg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kyrstig is scouting near Akhaldarâg.Talk to Kyrstig near Akhaldarâg'We have to do something about these Angmarim cultists! They will raise every fallen dwarf in these tombs if we don't stop them... so stop them we must!''Did you thin their numbers? Good! We may not be able to stop them by ourselves, but we must not allow these atrocities to continue!

'The Angmarim will pay for this bold villainy!'Fúsi Gem-cutter has requested your help with an unorthodox plan.You can find foul meat from ukhrâsh throughout the Pit of Stonejaws.Collect foul meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should lure out the massive ukhrash from its pond north of Bárgstad.Fúsi is at Bárgstad in the Pit of Stonejaws.

Now that you have collected the massive chitin, you should bring it back to Fúsi.Talk to Fúsi Gem-cutter'${PLAYER}! I hope you have been well. We Gem-cutters are here to help! There may not be much use for rings and bracelets in time of war, but we're plenty resourceful folk; I know I can put my craft-skill to some other use.

'Have you seen the strange shelled creatures that crawl hereabouts? They look a bit like crabs, but they are much larger. Their strange and bulbous eyes fill me with unease, I don't mind telling you. The Orcs call them 'Ukhrâsh.'

'Well, I have had a thought, and that thought is this: perhaps we could use their shells to fashion useful articles for the war effort: shields, armour, who knows what else? But the shells of the small ones aren't thick enough to serve. Fret not! I have caught glimpses of a huge one! Only glimpses. I think it spends most of its time underwater, but I have a feeling that one's shell will be worth its weight in gold! I doubt you'll catch it out in the open, but perhaps you can lure it out with meat from the smaller uhkrâsh in the Pit of Stonejaws. I am hoping the big one is both scavenger and cannibal!'You present the massive ukhrash shell to Fúsi.

'My goodness, ${PLAYER}! What a monster that must have been! I will be able to make something sturdy from this chitin, or my name is not Fúsi Gem-cutter! I mean, this is no gemstone, but my abilities are more wide-ranging than my name would suggest! And so it is with you, my friend.

'Thank you for your help!'Prince Durin has ordered the Gabil'akkâ to push further into Gundabad in opposition to the hostile Orc-defenders.Prince Durin has returned with you to Máttugard.Talk to Durin in MáttugardDurin ordered Bósi of the Iron Garrison to scout the further reaches of the Mountain-home, and has asked you to meet up with them at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard.Find Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of MáttugardBósi is at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws.Talk to Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of StonejawsBósi's son Bori has gone to search the crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws, and could use your assistance to the north-west.Defeat creatures in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find Bori to the north-west in the Pit of StonejawsTalk to Bori in the Pit of StonejawsBori asked you to search more of the crypts along the westward path, which eventually turns north and slopes upward.Bori has agreed to meet you by the upper crypts, further north in the Pit of Stonejaws.<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Máttugard when you accept this quest.</rgb>

'Then let us return! The conquest of the Mountain-home will wait no longer!''Threats remain here and there within Máttugard, but for the most part we have secured these halls and I do not fear they will be retaken. The time has come to push deeper into Gundabad. To that end I have ordered scouts to survey the further reaches: beyond Deepscrave to the west and north from Máttugard into the Pit of Stonejaws. Perhaps you can work to accomplish the second of these?

'You proved a good friend to Bósi of the Iron Garrison, so I ask you to meet up with him at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws. Help him to survey that cavern and the tombs housed within, the better to expand the foothold of the Gabil'akkâ in Gundabad. I will await report of your success, ${PLAYER}!''You proved a good friend to Bósi of the Iron Garrison, so I ask you to meet up with him at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard. Help him to survey that cavern and the tombs housed within, the better to expand the foothold of the Gabil'akkâ in Gundabad. I will await report of your success, ${PLAYER}!''Hail, friend!''Welcome, my friend! Are you here to lend us your aid? I must give my thanks to the prince when next we return to Máttugard, for you have always been a great help to us in each of our endeavours.

'My son Bori went on ahead to seek for the Houses of Rest, the tombs of our people. They are said to line the walls of the Pit of Stonejaws, and I am interested to see them as well, but something else has drawn my attention: a great city in the pit, home not to the bones of our ancestors but to more recent, and unwelcome, arrivals. I will take a small party of Longbeards to appraise this city. Perhaps you can bring my son to join us after he learns if the Houses of Rest are free of Orcs?

'Bori went to the north-west, and will be pleased for you to join him. Beware of the creatures that have made their homes here, and destroy any that threaten your safe passage!''Bori went north-west, and will be pleased for you to join him. Beware of the insects that have made their homes here, and destroy any that threaten your safe passage!''Hail, friend! Are you here to study the tombs in the Houses of Rest? Well, it is not truly a scholarly mission that brought me hither; my father expects me to learn if the Orcs have defaced the tombs here during their long residence. But I am also interested in learning the names of the dwarf-families that lie here entombed, and thought I could accomplish both errands at once!

'Let us climb a little higher, ${PLAYER}. The path west of here eventually slopes upward to the north, near more of the crypts.''Let us climb a little higher, ${PLAYER}. The path slopes upward to the north, near more of the crypts.''I find that Orc-sword quite curious. Did they fight among themselves for the privilege of ransacking the Houses of Rest?'

'As I climbed past the crypt-entrances, I tried to read the names of the families entombed within. It was not an easy task, for most of them have faded with the passage of the years, and I could not make many of them out.

'I saw markers for the Line of Arnvíth... the Line of Félag... Yngvi's Line...'

Bori stands up straight and rubs his chin.

'Perhaps the faded letters prevented the Orcs from disturbing the timeless sleep of the dwarves that lie within. For that let us be grateful. If the Orcs believed these dwarves had names of importance, they might have cracked open their tombs in search of wealth.

'I see signs that much else in the Pit of Stonejaws, and throughout the Mountain-home, was plundered and defaced. But how can this be so? Legend tells us that such villainy should have been prevented!'Bori is interested in the legends and history of Gundabad, and wants your help to learn as much of them as he can.Bori has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws, which contains the crypts of the many dwarf-families that were laid to rest over the years.<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the Pit of StonejawsBori is by the upper crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws.Talk to Bori by the upper crypts in the Pit of StonejawsBori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance to the south-west.Clear rubble from the entrance to the south-westBori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance.Clear rubble from the entrance to the south-westBori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance.Clear rubble from the entrance to the south-westTogether, you and Bori have cleared the rubble away from the room to the south-west, and can now gain entrance.Explore the room you have unearthed from the rubbleA broken mosaic decorates one wall of this chamber.Examine the broken mosaic in Zul-mazalBori is in Zul-mazal.Talk to Bori in Zul-mazalBósi is outside the fortress of Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.Find Bósi outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of StonejawsBósi is outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.Talk to Bósi outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws'Many are the great stories that have come down through the ages to us, ${PLAYER}. They stir our passions and fill us with dwarf-pride. One of these tales concerns these very tombs: according to legend, the lords of Gundabad will one day rise from their crypts and walk once again among the living. When they see the evils perpetrated by the Orcs in Gundabad, they will unleash their wrath upon those who despoil the great dwarf-halls, slaying their enemies from sunrise to sunset. Then, when their day of reckoning is done, the great lords will return to the Houses of Rest and slumber again for eternity, the Mountain-home made free of their foes.

'<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws, ${PLAYER}, and tell me what you see.''<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> out over the Pit of Stonejaws, ${PLAYER}, and tell me what you see.''Perhaps it is just a legend, after all. How could the dead lords of Gundabad stand by and watch for so many years, and do nothing?'

Bori sighs and turns his attention to the rubble-choked passage behind you.

'Can you help me shift some of those rocks aside? I would like to take a look inside that room. It may be a tomb or memorial of some kind, and perhaps the debris kept the Orcs out even as it blocks our own passage.''What awaits us within? I will follow after you, friend!''Will you look at that!''The rubble that blocked the way into this room must be of fairly recent vintage, for it did not prevent someone from looting the stones from the mosaic on the opposite wall. Orcs or goblins, no doubt; they have no love for fine dwarf-art, and would seize any opportunity to despoil such a thing as that. It is a pity we cannot tell what it might once have shown.

'It does remind me of a mosaic that once stood in the throne room of the Hall Under the Mountain, and which Stáli the Hewer had begun to restore. I wonder if this is similar to that one? He will be interested to see this, even as incomplete as it is. Curse the Orcs for their damage! This mosaic might once have been a great work of art, but like so much else in Gundabad it has been ruined by their hateful efforts.

'But we can do nothing about it for now. Let us return to my father, far below in the Pit of Stonejaws.''Here, friend, and keep quiet.''We can do nothing about the damage to this room for now. Let us return to my father, far below in the Pit of Stonejaws.''Here, friend. Let us keep our voices quiet while we make our plans.'The Dwarves of the Iron Garrison plan to combat the denizens of Shakhajât in the Pit of Stonejaws.Bósi has asked Imák and Bróin to draw the defenders of Shakhajât out into the open.Talk to Imák outside ShakhajâtTalk to Bróin outside ShakhajâtBósi is outside Shakhajât. Given Bróin's discomfort with the plan, perhaps you should volunteer in his stead?Talk to Bósi outside ShakhajâtBósi has agreed that you can carry out Bróin's part of the plan: climbing either the left or right slope around the fortress and using a discarded horn of battle to draw forth some of the hobgoblins from Shakhajât.Now that you have carried out your part of the plan, you should join the dwarves inside Shakhajât.Meet up with Bróin inside ShakhajâtBróin is inside Shakhajât and desires to speak with you.Talk to Bróin inside ShakhajâtBróin has seen a dwarf-woman fighting in the fortress and wants you to check on her while you combat the forces inside Shakhajât.Talk to the dwarf-woman Bróin saw within ShakhajâtDefeat hobgoblins in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The dwarves have made their presence known to Bósi's satisfaction and are now ready to meet up outside Shakhajât.Talk to Fastrith outside ShakhajâtBori is waiting to meet up with you outside Shakhajât.Talk to Bori outside Shakhajât'If we are to advance from Máttugard, we will need to do something about the city the Orcs have established here. Shakhajât, it is called, and long has it stood among the broken teeth of the Pit of Stonejaws. It was here that Bolg mustered the force that met its end before the gates of the Lonely Mountain in the Battle of Five Armies, but I do not know what it is like within its walls today.

'We need to draw the attention of its defenders so some of us can get inside and cause some trouble! Who volunteers? Imák? Bróin? Will the two of you blast a great signal upon horns of battle, drawing forth the hobgoblins that reside within the city?''We need to draw the attention of its defenders so some of us can get inside and cause some trouble! Who volunteers? Imák? Bróin? Will the two of you blast a great signal upon horns of battle, drawing forth the hobgoblins that reside within the city?''If you need a distraction, I am your dwarf. I can make enough noise the defenders of Shakhajât will think five armies approach, and all of them dwarves!''I suppose I can cause a distraction... if I must. Yes, I can... I can do it.''What's that, ${PLAYER}? You wish to draw the eyes of the defenders away on your own? We do not need three teams to do this.

'Very well, you and Imák will fashion a suitable distraction, and the rest of us will sneak into Shakhajât as a group. Climb either the left or right slope that extends around the fortress and find one of the discarded horns of battle with which to draw hobgoblin attention.''You and Imák will fashion a suitable distraction, and the rest of us will sneak into Shakhajât as a group.''Our fellowship is not the only one to have infiltrated Shakhajât, ${PLAYER}. Other dwarves have arrived, including a dwarf-woman of no small ferocity! I watched her engage in combat with a hobgoblin and as I beheld her prowess my own fears evaporated! Will you make sure she fares well enough in the courtyard ahead?'

You assure Bróin you will find her, but if she is as fierce as he says, you are certain she will be fine.

'Aye, she was most striking... and struck her foes with abandon, too! Impress her by slaying the hobgoblins, our shared foes, and making the Pit of Stonejaws safer for all of us!''Will you find her and make sure she fares well enough within the walls of the city?''Hearty greetings to you, ${PLAYER}! Can you imagine my brother Eskil in such a place? I can... but not for long. It is better that I am here!'

You tell Fastrith that she has an admirer in Shakhajât, and he sent you to check on her.

'An admirer? Well now! I trust that he's no Orc or hobgoblin? A fine dwarf, you say? Better and better! But this is no place for such idle talk. I will meet you outside the city once your business here is concluded, ${PLAYER}.''I will see you in the courtyard to the south when you are done here, friend.''I am glad to see you made it back outside, ${PLAYER}, as did these others!'

You ask Fastrith why she ventured inside Shakhajât, and whether she needs your help escaping the contract with Stáli, as did her brother. She laughs in response.

'No, my droll friend! My master Stáli did not send me here. His instructions were simple: "Find me the Zabad'ibîn," he said. I reckoned they would be more likely found in dangerous places than in peaceful ones. A search of the chief-stead seemed in order. I found no gemstones, but there were plenty of Orc-skulls against which I tested the sharpness of my axe. Would that I had replaced my brother in his apprenticeship before this! Such fighting really gets the blood flowing, doesn't it?

'Perhaps Stáli will eventually teach me the ways of sculpture, but until then I think I will adopt axe-handling as my trade!''Stáli may one day teach me the ways of sculpture, but until then I think I will adopt axe-handling as my trade!''Did I hear her correctly? She is apprenticed to Stáli the Hewer, the sculptor from Erebor?

'That is a curious coincidence, is it not?'Bori believes that Stáli the Hewer would be interested in the mosaic you found in Zul-mazal, and suggested that his apprentice Fastrith Hawkfeast take a look on behalf of her master.Fastrith Hawkfeast is outside Shakhajât.Talk to Fastrith outside ShakhajâtFastrith is outside Shakhajât, waiting for you and Bori to bring her to Zul-mazal to examine the interesting mosaic.Talk to Fastrith and travel with her to Zul-mazalImák is standing in Zul-mazal, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Imák in Zul-mazal'How odd that we should discover a broken mosaic on the same day we encounter an apprentice to one renowned for the study and restoration of such works of art?

'Stáli the Hewer will surely be interested in examining our discovery, ${PLAYER}. Does his apprentice care to see it, and confirm if I am right?''Stáli the Hewer will surely be interested in examining our discovery, ${PLAYER}. Does his apprentice care to see it, and confirm if I am right?''A broken mosaic? I can certainly take a look. With Shakhajât apparently free of any of the Zabad'ibîn, I have the rest of the day free.

'Let me know where to go, ${PLAYER}.''Lead on, my friend!''Hmm. There's something about this chamber, ${PLAYER}, and it's not the hobgoblins. Well, it's not just the hobgoblins.'

Imák sniffs the air.

'Yes, there is something peculiar about the air in here. You know my sense of smell is highly refined, do you not? Well, something here is a bother to it, and I don't like it.'Gráfar Splitstone needs your help clearing out a den of beasts.Tunnels in the north-east side of the Pit of Stonejaws contain many cave-claws and deep-claws.Defeat cave-claws and deep-claws in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gráfar Splitstone waits to hear about your efforts against the cave-claws.Talk to Gráfar Splitstone'Oh, I could use your help, ${PLAYER}. We Gem-cutters have come to assess the ore and minerals in the Pit of Stonejaws, but this place is crawling with beasts and things look to be difficult. We found some tunnels on the north-eastern side of the Pit of Stonejaws that look rich with veins and precious gems, but they are thick with cave-claws and their deep-claw cousins. Do you think you might spare the time to clear them out for us?''Did you clear out those beasts? Good! I have never liked cave-claws, you know. And they seem to be everywhere!

'Now I, Gráfar Splitstone, can get to work doing what I do best!'Kyrstig has asked you to stop the kergrim from consuming the dwarf-corpses in the Akhaldarâg tombs.Kergrim can be found throughout the Pit of Stonejaws.Defeat kergrim in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kyrstig is scouting near Akhaldarâg.Talk to Kyrstig near Akhaldarâg'The kergrim and Angmarim seek to control the tombs in Akhaldarâg, but neither of them must be allowed to win the contest! Each group is vile in its own way, but the kergrim turn my stomach. Defeat as many as you can, and keep them from feasting upon the fallen!''You have slain many kergrim? Good work, ${PLAYER}! I think kergrim may be my least-favourite of the creatures that dwell beneath the mountains. Aye, even worse than Orcs! That's how much I dislike the vile creatures!'Stazg Vozag, the main out-camp in the Pit of Stonejaws, receives messages from hobgoblins elsewhere in Gundabad.Scraps of paper inside the out-camp might hold information intended for the hobgoblin leadership... but they might be intercepted by a daring adventurer.Collect the first hobgoblin reportCollect the second hobgoblin reportCollect the third hobgoblin reportCollect the fourth hobgoblin reportCollect the fifth hobgoblin reportKlúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.Talk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag'While I've been watching, I've seen quite a few runners come and go with scraps of paper to deliver to Captain Zúrthrug. I assume they are then passed on to the warlord and his closest advisors. Some of this intelligence is probably still in the camp, and will be useful to the war effort!

'Intelligence? In hobgoblins? Bah, there has to be a better word. Well, it will do for now.''What did you find?'

You hand the parchments to Klúso. He quickly reads the messages, squinting at the crude Orc-scrawls.

'Some of these tidings are old, but some of this is news to me. It is interesting to hear that some lose faith in Gorgar... I wager we can take advantage of that, and wouldn't that be quite the Beard Bonus?

'I'll make sure these get to Ausma!'Molkha has seen the drakes carrying injured Zhélruka into Borkordh, probably intending to feed them to their young!Injured dwarves must be rescued from Borkordh, the drake nest on the south-east side of the Pit of Stonejaws.Help injured dwarves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Molkha is scouting outside Borkordh.Talk to Molkha outside Borkordh'I've seen the drakes carrying dwarves into the cavern below. They might have been my fellow Zhélruka, and although I can't be certain... I think they were still alive! I suspect the drakes intend to feed them to their young.

'Please! Help them if you can, before they are eaten alive!''Did you rescue those dwarves? They all made it out alive?

'Oh, thank the First Crafter! And not just him, of course. You have my thanks as well, ${PLAYER}!'Molkha believes you should break as many unhatched drake eggs in Borkordh as you can.Drake eggs can be found throughout Borkordh, on the south-east side of the Pit of Stonejaws.Break drake eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Molkha is scouting outside the drake-nest of Borkordh in the south-east corner of the Pit of Stonejaws.Talk to Molkha outside Borkordh'There are a lot of unhatched eggs down there in Borkordh, and I think it will be best if we keep them that way! Drakes grow up fearsome and dangerous, and their favourite breakfast is unwary dwarf!

'I enjoy eggs for breakfast, myself. But I won't be eating these, ${PLAYER}, absolutely not! Go break the drake-eggs and make the Pit of Stonejaws safer for the Gabil'akkâ.''It is as I always say, ${PLAYER}: if you want dwarves to live long, satisfying lives full of hearty breakfasts of eggs and bacon, you can't be afraid of a few drakes.

'Something like that, anyway. Well-done, my adventuring friend.'Bori has suggested that you bring Fastrith to inspect the broken mosaic in Zul-mazal in order to see if her master Stáli the Hewer would be interested in it.Fastrith has come to Zul-mazal.Talk to Fastrith Hawkfeast in Zul-mazalFastrith and the other dwarves stand in Zul-mazal, discussing the broken mosaic on the wall.Listen to the dwarves discuss the broken mosaic in Zul-mazalBored by the discussion, Imák has called for you to speak with him. He believes danger is near.Talk to Imák in Zul-mazalA hobgoblin prey-catcher has found the entrance to Zul-mazal, and before he was slain he alerted his band to your position. You and the dwarves must ready your defence!Return to Zul-mazal with Imák and ready the defenceBori and the other dwarves prepare to defend Zul-mazal from the hobgoblin hunting-pack.Talk to Bori in Zul-mazalYou and the dwarves have defended Zul-mazal from the hobgoblin hunting-party.Remain alert for any further threats to the dwarves'That was well-fought, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps these Longbeards can take care of themselves after all... so long as there is a Stout-axe nearby to lend a hand!''This mosaic must have been quite lovely, once! I have only been apprenticed to Stáli the Hewer for a short time, but I am certain he will want to see this!''Something smells foul, ${PLAYER}. Let them study that mosaic... we should look around for the source of this unsettling odour.

'I think danger is near.''These hobgoblins do not know who they have chosen for dancing partners!

'Let us show them the mistake they have made!'Scout-master Ausma has charged you and her three apprentices with dismantling the Angmarim forces in the Pit of Stonejaws.Kyrstig waits to speak with you.Talk to KyrstigKyrstig has pointed out the first tomb on the left in Akhaldarâg as yours.

You should enter the tomb.Enter the dwarf-tombThe dwarf-tomb contains Angmarim possessed of evil intent.Clear the tomb of AngmarimKyrstig needs your help.Talk to KyrstigIt is time to confront Loknashra!Confront LoknashraYou should defeat the dwarf-wights in the tomb.Defeat the Dwarf-wights'I have a bad feeling about this. We should get back to camp, and quickly!''Our first real mission without Ausma! Finally, a chance to show our mettle! When you're ready, we'll split up and hit all of these tombs at once, clearing out the Angmarim we find inside. This will only work if we clear them at the same time, or else some of the cultists might get away and warn the others. Once each of our tombs is cleared, we are to return to camp straight away! Everyone ready?''I need your help over here! I found Loknashra! I can't defeat her by myself, but perhaps the two of us have a chance! Follow me!'Scout-master Ausma intends to find a way deep into Shakhajât in order to learn more about Warlord Dushtalbúk and his advisors.Ausma is pleased with your progress so far.Talk to Scoutmaster AusmaYou should follow Ausma.Follow Scout-master AusmaEnter ShakhajâtAusma is continuing to explore, and will need your help.Talk to Scout-master AusmaYou should eavesdrop and see what can be learned.Listen to the conversation'Let's get out of here before we're seen. We can talk about what we just learned back at camp.''Good, we managed to get this far unseen. We're on the west side of the pit now. I noticed there are quite a few catwalks and scaffolding on the exterior of Shakhajât. I have a hunch we'll be able to use them to find another way inside the fort. Are you ready to move in?''Well, we're inside now, but who knows where? Stay close to me, and keep to the shadows. Let's see if we can't find the warlord.'The scouts Kyrstig, Molkha, and Klúso have stormed the hobgoblin fortress Shakhajât to rescue their master, Ausma. But it is unclear if they are too late, or if their help is needed at all.The plan to rescue Ausma begins with Kyrstig.Talk to KyrstigYou need to find Ausma.Find AusmaStand by with the Scout TrioAusma is frozen in a block of ice!Break ice block (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have to escape!Escape with Ausma'Come on, let's get back to camp. I need some time to lick my wounds and wallow in my failure.''Ausma must be in here if she went after Dushtalbúk. I hope you're ready for a fight.'Scout-master Ausma has asked you to deal with any hobgoblins that cross your path while you complete your initial reconnaissance.Scout-master Ausma has asked you to defeat any hobgoblins you come across while looking for Shakhajât.

You should defeat hobgoblins in the Pit of Stonejaws.Defeat hobgoblins in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many hobgoblins in the Pit of Stonejaws.

You should talk to Scout-master Ausma at Bárgstad.Talk to Scout-master Ausma at Bárgstad'One more thing, ${PLAYER}. While you scout the way to Shakhajât, slay any hobgoblins that cross your path. This will keep them from reporting back to their masters in the fortress and also give you a warm-up for the battles to come. This task serves two purposes, and that is even better than one!''This is just the beginning, ${PLAYER}. If these are the hobgoblins outside the fort, imagine how many must lurk within!'Molkha has been sent to investigate a frost-drake nest in the Pit of Stonejaws.Molkha has been sent to find the frost-drakes inside the Pit of Stonejaws.

You should find Molkha somewhere in the tunnels east of Bárgstad.Find MolkhaMolkha needs your help.Complete 'Quelling the Horde'Complete 'If You Want to Make a Hearty Egg Breakfast...'Complete 'Food for Their Young'Complete 'Frost-bound Nest-tenders'Find information about LoknashraYou should return to Molkha.Talk to Molkha'Because the frost-bound hobgoblins rule the Pit of Stonejaws, it is very likely there is a Frost-horde presence here as well. The drakes are the masters in that relationship, after all. I have sent Molkha to find the drakes and observe them. Look for her on the eastern side of the pit. If she has succeeded in finding them, do what you can to disrupt the drakes. When we eventually assault Shakhajât. We're better off if the Frost-horde doesn't come to fight on the side of the hobgoblins.''Ah, ${PLAYER}. Keep your voice down. The cave ahead teems with frost-drakes and their spawn! I expect Ausma sent you to see if I had found the drake-nest and if I had, to deal with them at once. Well, I have, so you should!''Ack! No, stay away! Wait, you not hobgoblin? You maybe... help me? Me don't want to end up drake food!'

The goblin senses your distrust, and changes his tactics.

'Please, wait! I'll make trade! Warlord sent me here for thieving, but I kept some of the shinies. You take, and you let me go, yes?'

You agree to the deal, and cut the goblin loose. The goblin cackles gleefully and produces a red crystal from under his belt. He holds it out to you, and you allow him to place it in your hand.

'Here! I took this from big hobgoblin lady. She not nice. You take, I go!'

Something feels off about the crystal, besides the stink of goblin upon it. You think Ausma should see this.'I saw you fighting in there. I guess Ausma was right about you. You certainly are skilled! But what did that goblin give you?'

You show Molkha the strange red crystal. She gingerly takes it from you, and winces. She holds it up to one ear, listening carefully. Her eyes widen. She then hands it back to you.

'I can hear... screaming? Whatever this is, I don't want it! You should take it to Ausma right away. If Loknashra had it, it probably came from the Angmarim!'Molkha thinks you should keep an eye out for the advisors to Warlord Dushtalbúk while you storm Shakhajât.Warlord Dushtalbúk's advisors should be defeated if you can find them within Shakhajât.Defeat Margzasht the CrusherDefeat Núlnazt the Keen-eyedDefeat Akúlog of the HoarfrostMolkha waits for your report about the warlord's advisors.Talk to MolkhaTalk to Molkha'If you want to head back into Shakhajât, we should keep an eye out for those hobgoblin advisors we saw with Dushtalbúk. They will be much easier to deal with if we catch them on their own!''While we're in Shakhajât, we should keep an eye out for those hobgoblin advisors we saw with Dushtalbúk. They will be much easier to deal with if we catch them on their own!''We did it! Fighting by your side truly is exhilarating. I feel like the four of us could even take on Dushtalbúk himself!''The advisors are dead, then? I knew you could manage it, ${PLAYER}. I never doubted you for a moment, let alone two or three!'Molkha has spotted several hobgoblins inside Borkordh, tending the drake nests.Hobgoblin nest-tenders can be found in the drake-nest of Borkordh in the south-east side of the Pit of Stonejaws.Defeat hobgoblin nest-tenders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Molkha is scouting outside Borkordh.Talk to Molkha outside Borkordh'I've seen some hobgoblins down in the drake nest. They seem rather subservient, tending to the eggs and nests like... well, like nannies! Imagine having to tend to little babies with teeth like those infant drakes have! No thank you!

'You should defeat those hobgoblins while they're busy. Such nannies and the infants in their care are enemies of the Gabil'akkâ, and dangerous to dwarves!''Tending to drake nests seems like it would be dull work most of the time... until it's suddenly not, and you find yourself having to calm down a grumpy infant drake that doesn't want to nap! I wonder how the warlord chooses who gets assigned that task?'Hobgoblin sentries patrol the road near the out-camp of Stazg Vozag.Hobgoblin sentries patrol the roads near Stazg Vozag.Defeat hobgoblin sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Klúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.Talk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag'There are several sentries on the roads around here, coming and going from the out-camp. Removing them will hinder any schemes the hobgoblins might think up, and also lower the chance that one of them might stumble upon our own camp.

'You know what to do, ${PLAYER}.''You cleared the roads? Good work. At the very least it will be easier to sneak out of here when we're done.

'Oh yes, my friend. We are just getting started!'Molkha believes clearing the drake nest in the Pit of Stonejaws would be the best course of action.Worms and drakes in the Pit of Stonejaws present a dangerous threat to the dwarves.Defeat drakes and worms in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Molkha is scouting outside the drake-nest of Borkordh in the south-east corner of the Pit of Stonejaws.Talk to Molkha near Borkordh'The Scout-master is right. We should clear out as many drakes in the Pit of Stonejaws as we can before we assault Shakhajât. If we do not, we risk facing two enemy forces at once, and no one wants that!

'Well? Go on, then!''Those drakes will no longer be a problem? Hmmm.

'Perhaps I was wrong about you, ${PLAYER}. You do seem able to hold your own in combat!'Gráfar Splitstone has warned you of a deadly foe lurking in the north-eastern corner of the Pit of Stonejaws.Dulkoth the Slicer lurks somewhere in the tunnels in the north-eastern corner of the Pit of Stonejaws.Defeat Dulkoth the SlicerGráfar Splitstone waits to hear of your encounter with Dulkoth the Slicer.Talk to Gráfar Splitstone'While I was scouting those tunnels in the north-east corner of the Pit of Stonejaws, I ran afoul of a creature that could only belong to legend... and yet my father brings word of another such beast, in lands far to the south. Can you believe it?

'This creature is a massive cave-claw with a bright and shining golden horn! It nearly sliced me in two! Keep an eye out for him if you're over there. He's quite aggressive, and is sure to become a danger to the Gabil'akkâ if someone doesn't do something.

'And that someone is you, ${PLAYER}! Deny it if you can!''You encountered the giant cave-claw with the golden horn, and lived to tell the tale? Excellent work, ${CLASS}!

'I wonder how many of these creatures stalk the roads beneath the mountains? One fewer, it is true, but the wonders and curiosities that burrow in the earth can hardly be counted.

'We must be wary, for such denizens might develop a taste for dwarf... and my people are also known for burrowing!'Klúso has a plan to deal with the towers near Shakhajât.Large towers in front of Shakhajât will serve as fine targets for Klúso's smoke bombs.Place smoke bombs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Klúso will want to hear how well his plan to hide your movements is proceeding.Talk to Klúso'I have had an idea, inspired by one of Ausma's inventions! Here, you will need these.'

He places a heavy sack in front of you, and opens it to reveal several large metal canisters full of blasting powder.

'These look big, I know, but the mixture is specially-formulated to produce smoke instead of flames. We can set these off around the big towers in front of Shakhajât and the billowing smoke will mask our movements!''I have had an idea, inspired by one of Ausma's inventions! Here, you will need these.'

He places a heavy sack in front of you, and opens it to reveal several large metal canisters full of blasting powder.

'These look big, I know, but the mixture is specially-formulated to produce smoke instead of flames. We can set these off around the big towers in front of Shakhajât and the billowing smoke will mask our movements!''Look at those mighty columns of smoke! The sentry at the top of each of those towers must be furious! Haha!''Did the smoke bombs work? Huge columns of smoke, you say? Excellent! I am eager to try them out myself in the future!'Fúni Gem-cutter has asked you to collect crystal samples from the Pit of Stonejaws.Exposed crystals can be found throughout the Pit of Stonejaws.

You should hit exposed crystals with Fúni's pick and collect the crystal samples that break off.Collect samples from exposed crystals in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected samples of the crystals found in the Pit of Stonejaws.

You should return to Fúni Gem-cutter in Bárgstad.Talk to Fúni Gem-cutter'${PLAYER}! It is good to see you again! We Gem-cutters have returned after a long time away, eager to join the Gabil'akkâ. We are not truly warriors, but perhaps we can help in other ways... and if we do not, my wife Amma will never let me hear the end of it!

'She believes the Pit of Stonejaws contains a large number of crystals, and she sent me here to collect some samples. "Yes, of course!" I said to her, but now that we are here I see this area is quite dangerous; see how it swarms with beasts and hobgoblins? Can I ask you to bring me back some crystal samples for examination? You may even borrow my pick!''Oh, look at all these beautiful crystals! Hand them over so I may examine them more closely.'

He takes out a bright glass and carefully inspects the crystal samples.

'Hmm. I do not believe these are the same as those the Angmarim corrupt. See how beautiful they are, and how they shine even in the dim light! Our craft is sure to benefit from this cavern's crystals. Thank you for doing the leg-work, ${PLAYER}.'Kyrstig has given you the difficult task of storming the hobgoblin fortress of Shakhajât and facing its defenders.Shakhajât is well-defended by hobgoblins, so there will be no shortage of enemies for you to face inside.Defeat hobgoblins in Shakhajât (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kyrstig will want to hear how many hobgoblins you faced in Shakhajât.Talk to Kyrstig'There's still plenty of work to do in Shakhajât if you're up for it! Get in there and fight those hobgoblins!''It's time to storm Shakhajât! Let's take out as many hobgoblins as we can on the way!''Good fighting, ${PLAYER}! We surely dented their numbers. Not bad for a day's work, if I say so myself!''How goes the fight, ${PLAYER}? You took down how many? Really? Good work!'Hobgoblins working from the out-camp of Stazg Vozag pose a grave danger to the dwarves in the Pit of Stonejaws.The out-camp of Stazg Vozag is slightly north-east of the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.Defeat hobgoblins in Stazg Vozag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat the fearsome Captain Zúrthrug, about whom the whispers gatherKlúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.Talk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag'I'm afraid you're going to have to get your hands dirty, ${PLAYER}. To disrupt this camp, you're going to have to fight the hobgoblins and the one in charge here, a wholly unpleasant fellow by the name of Captain Zúrthrug. He's a real bad sort, if half of the things I've heard whispered about him are true.

'But you need not fear any of that. You're a hero, aren't you? This out-camp will be just a footnote in your legend, when all is said and done, and no one will remember Captain Zúrthrug at all!

'Good luck!''See? I knew you could handle it. Didn't doubt you for a moment! The hobgoblins will soon notice that their out-camp has been, well... cleared out... and if we play our runes right, they will blame it on the Orcs!

'They did not know they were dealing with a master of Hammers and Bones, but so they are! And my skill at the runic dice translates onto the battlefield, see if it does not!'Orc spies surround the out-camp of Stazg Vozag, carrying swords of jagged metal.Orc-spies near Stazg Vozag carry the weapons Klúso will need for the plan.Collect weapons from Orc-spies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Klúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.Talk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag'This camp has drawn a lot of attention from those who are not on friendly terms with the hobgoblins. I've spotted quite a few Orcs spying from the shadows. The weapons they carry will be vital to giving the damage you're about to do the proper framing!

'Yes, we're going to make this look like an Orc plot, rather than the work of dwarves! I hope your acting is up to the challenge, friend! Actually, perhaps I will teach you a thing or two about it. I have received many compliments for my ability to throw my voice, making it seem as if I am speaking from some distance away.

'Your part in this play will be to collect weapons from the Orc-spies hereabout, and then I will scatter them around to make it look like the Orcs ambushed this camp. What can go wrong? Nothing, ${PLAYER}. Nothing can go wrong.''Ah, good work! I'll place these next to some of the defeated hobgoblins to set the scene. Let the master show you how it's done!'Ausma has decided that stopping the Angmarim cult from raising the entirety of the Houses of Rest in undeath is to be top priority.It is time for you to carry out Ausma's plan.Complete 'Instance: The Apprentices Attack'Troubling portents abound! Where is Ausma?Talk to KrystigTroubling portents abound! Where is Ausma?Find a clue to Ausma's whereaboutsKyrstig awaits your unhappy tidings.Talk to Kyrstig'I have seen enough to make a decision: this Angmarim cult has become our top priority. There are many Longbeard ancestors entombed in the Houses of Rest, and we cannot allow them to be drafted into an army of the dead. I am sending you and my apprentices to deal with this matter at once. You will split up and attack each tomb at the same time, preventing any of these Angmarim snakes from slithering away! I will keep watch on Shakhajât in the meantime, and warn you should the hobgoblins move to assist the cultists. Have you any questions?''When you are ready to depart, the four of you will attack at once. We will nip this wight problem in the bud.''Molkha and Klúso were right! Ausma is gone! Look around and see if you can find any sign of where she went. I really hope something horrible hasn't happened....'My scouts,

Your attack on the Angmarim has proven distraction enough to set my own plan into motion. I am going into Shakhajât alone. If we are fortunate, I will return with the warlord's head. You three are to stay put!

AusmaYou show Kyrstig the note left by Ausma.

'She went in there by herself, and told us to stay here! But is that really the right thing to do?'Klúso has been sent to investigate the hobgoblin out-camp called Stazg Vozag.Klúso is east of Out-camp Stazg Vozag, spying on the hobgoblins.

You should find Klúso and help him however you can.Find KlúsoKlúso needs your help.Complete 'Sentries from the Out-camp'Complete 'Swords in the Shadows'Complete 'Storming Stazg Vozag'Complete 'Enemy Intelligence'Find information about LoknashraKlúso is east of Out-camp Stazg Vozag, spying on the hobgoblins.Talk to Klúso'Klúso has been sent to keep watch on Stazg Vozag, the hobgoblin out-camp. We know this is where runners from elsewhere in Gundabad deliver their missives and receive their marching orders, rather than entering Shakhajât itself. It seems the warlord takes his precautions very seriously. You should meet up with Klúso and hear what he has discovered.'Klúso is startled as you approach, but he manages to slap a hand over his mouth before he can make a sound.

'Oh, ${PLAYER}, it's just you! I thought I was about to catch an Orc-dagger in my back! Hahaha... give me a moment to calm my heart!

'So Ausma sent you to get my report, hmm? Well, she was right that this is where the hobgoblins receive messages from elsewhere in Gundabad. Because of that, this camp has drawn the attention of spies, and I don't mean us! Ausma didn't specifically tell me not to do this so... I have an idea. You could do a lot of damage to the hobgoblins if you attack this camp, and because of the suspicion present on both sides, the warlord might assume it was the Orcs doing the backstabbing and not us dwarves! What do you say to that? Smart, eh?'By order of Warlord Dushtalbúk,

All raids on the Angmarim settlements are to cease immediately. The Frost-bound and the Cult of Drugoth are negotiating a deal. Anyone who has a problem with this should report to Loknashra at their own risk!'Great work out there, ${PLAYER}. I'll run around and place these Orc-swords before returning to camp, completing the ruse. I think we might actually pull this off! What do you have there?'

You show Klúso the orders you found in the out-camp.

'Hmm, you'd better bring those to Ausma right away.'Scout-master Ausma thinks the time is right to enter Shakhajât with stealth and learn more about the hobgoblin leadership.Ausma is ready to infiltrate the fortress.Complete 'Instance: The Inner Circle"You have successfully infiltrated Shakhajât.

You should talk to Scout-master Ausma in Bárgstad.Talk to Scout-master Ausma'Now that we have the location of Shakhajât, we need to gather more information. Specifically, it will be valuable to know how many hobgoblins are stationed in the fortress, and which ones serve as advisors to the warlord. We also need to know Dushtalbúk's plans, both to plan a battle strategy and in order to catch him alone....'

She flashes you a wicked grin.

'There's no way around it: we are going to sneak inside. I hope you still remember the stealthy skills I taught you in our previous adventures together!''Let me know when you're ready to move out. I'm eager to get started!''Good work on a successful infiltration! I am pleased to learn that the Orc and hobgoblin relationship remains tense; we can exploit that. Still, this bargain with the Angmarim is concerning. Are they trying to make an alliance with Hrímil? She has previously shown animosity to Sauron's servants. Perhaps they need a good word from the hobgoblins to get in the good graces of the Frost-horde? We will need to find out.

'Finding Dushtalbúk's throne room is a good first step, but it is going to be hard to catch him alone. We should continue investigating the surrounding area, and see what we can find out about this Angmarim plot.'Scout-master Ausma and her apprentices have arrived in the Pit of Stonejaws to investigate the hobgoblins' seat of power.Scout-master Ausma has asked you to introduce yourself to her apprentices.

You should talk to Kyrstig, Molkha, and Klúso in Bárgstad.Talk to KlúsoTalk to KyrstigTalk to MolkhaNow that you have met the new scouts, you should decide upon your course of action in the Pit of Stonejaws.

You should talk to Scout-master Ausma in Bárgstad.Talk to Scout-master AusmaSomewhere in the heart of the Stonejaws is the hobgoblin fort Shakhajât.

You should find Shakhajât and help Ausma with "Just a Warm-up".Find ShakhajâtHelp Scout-master Ausma with "Just a Warm-up"You have located the hobgoblin fort in the Pit of Stonejaws.

You should talk to Scout-master Ausma in Bárgstad.Talk to Scout-master Ausma'Welcome to the Pit of Stonejaws, ${PLAYER}. We have reason to believe that the hobgoblin seat of power lies within these jagged caverns. We also believe that their leader, Warlord Dushtalbúk, and his advisors are currently here, holed up in their fort to avoid the growing unrest between the enemy forces.

'Our mission here is to locate their fort, discover the scope of their power, and if we are very fortunate indeed, slay the warlord himself. The timing is vital. If we can remove Dushtalbúk from the table before the hobgoblins and Orcs reconcile their differences, they may be unable to organize again before we deal a decisive blow and win this war. 

'Because of this mission's importance, Prince Durin has personally asked me to oversee it. You, ${PLAYER}, will also be instrumental in our success. I have not come alone, however. I have taken on three apprentices that I would like you to meet. I have been teaching them the ways of stealth and of the dagger. Go, introduce yourself. I expect they will be excited to meet you, for they have heard tell of your exploits!''So you are ${PLAYER}? I am Klúso of the Stout-axe clan! Ausma has told me much of your skills. I look forward to seeing them in action myself!''You must be ${PLAYER}! I have heard a great deal about you! I am Kyrstig of the Longbeards. I am eager to fight beside such a renowned ${CLASS}!''${PLAYER}, was it? I am Molkha of the Zhélruka. The others seem quite excited to work with you. If your presence betters our chance of surviving this dangerous mission, I suppose I am pleased as well!''My apprentices are an interesting assortment, to be sure. They show promise but lack experience, which I hope to correct during this mission. But enough of the pleasantries. We have work to do.

'We arrived only slightly ahead of you, giving us the time to make camp but little else. Our next step is reconnaissance. I will send you and those three out into the caves to scout different areas of the Stonejaws. Your first mission is this: find the hobgoblin fortress known as Shakhajât. Do not stray too near, lest you ruin the advantage of our surprise!''All warmed up, ${PLAYER}? What do you have to report?'

You tell Ausma that Shakhajât lies at the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws, little more than a dagger's throw from Bárgstad.

'Good work. Now for the next step: locating our warlord.'Krystig has been sent to investigate the ancient dwarf-tombs in the Pit of Stonejaws.Kyrstig should be scouting somewhere near Adkhât-zahhar, the Houses of Rest, on the western side of the Pit of Stonejaws.

