You should talk to Kyrstig.Talk to Kyrstig'We know from ancient lore that Adkhât-zahhar, the Houses of Rest, should be somewhere in the Pit of Stonejaws. These tombs are said to hold the long-dead lords of Gundabad, certainly an important and hallowed place to the Longbeard dwarves. I have sent Kyrstig out to find them, and investigate if they have been disturbed by Angmarim or hobgoblins. You should be able to find her somewhere on the western side of the Pit of Stonejaws.''${PLAYER}! I need help here! The Angmarim are committing atrocities in the Houses of Rest! I have witnessed them stealing the fallen dwarves from their resting places and bringing them back to life as wights! And in the places the Angmarim aren't, the Kergrim are ransacking the tombs and EATING the dead! This is horrible, and though I was told to just watch and not interfere, I cannot in good conscience allow this to go on!'

You ask Kyrstig if she has seen Loknashra or heard any mention of her from the Angmarim.

'The female hobgoblin? No, I have not seen her, but I have heard the Angmarim speaking about her. It sounded like they were teaching her something? You should look around and see if you can find out more.'Children of Drugoth,

It is of vital importance that we build a strong alliance with the frost-bound hobgoblins. Loknashra is the key to that end. Instruct her in our ways as best you can.

Ugarad the Harbinger'We have done what we can for now. We need to inform Ausma of the Angmarim's activities here! I will return to Bárgstad as soon as I can get away without being seen.'Ausma has sent her apprentices to several points of interest around the Pit of Stonejaws to investigate the plans of the hobgoblins and Angmarim.Scout-master Ausma's apprentices have been sent to points of interest around the Pit of Stonejaws.

