You should talk to Monathár.Talk to Monathár'Be them our brothers or not, those hillmen who remain loyal to the Iron Crown have chosen a different road. Pleas and reason do not sway them from their needless subjugation. I speak of those at Tâg Fógarrach with both anger and sadness, ${RACE}.

'If their conditions become unbearable, perhaps they will flee or change their ways. I know not. If you venture to Tâg Fógarrach, burn their supplies. Those supplies are nothing more than thinly veiled gifts of loyalty from the Iron Crown.''Even if just one hillman retreats from Tâg Fógarrach to join us at Eiricháv, then I will consider your work a success. I thank you for assisting us.'In the barrows of Skáilag, sorcerers of the Iron Crown work to raise the remains of the Hill-men of Rhudaur into the service of Angmar once again.Skáilag can be found to the east of Grúmachath.

Rethvárd has informed you that the sorceress, Fláthail, endeavours to raise the Hill-men of Rhudaur at Skáilag. You should travel to Skáilag and defeat Fláthail.Travel to SkáilagFláthail can be found within the barrows of Skáilag.

You have arrived to find Skáilag overrun by wights and other fell things. You should defeat Fláthail.Defeat Fláthail at SkáilagYou have defeated Fláthail at Skáilag.Completed'As you might imagine, most of us Dourhands no longer look kindly on those who dare to practise necromancy or other fell sorceries.

'However, there is a barrows to the east where the Angmarim seek to raise the Hill-men of Rhudaur into their service once more. A sorceress, Fláthail, leads them in this task, but she has not yet completed her work—much to the disappointment of the High Priestess, Ásachal.

'If you would help both of our peoples, put an end to her before the Dead overwhelm all of Câr Bronach.'With the defeat of Fláthail at Skáilag, the Iron Crown's plot to raise their ancient servants, the Hill-men of Rhudaur, has been undone. Your efforts have done much to ensure the success of the Zhélruka expedition in Câr Bronach.In the caverns of Toll Oivas, sorcerers of the Iron Crown animate the remains of bats into spies for Angmar.Toll Oivas can be found to the west of Grúmachath.

Rethvárd has informed you that the sorcerer, Iärcagar and his pet, Uiagal, lead the Angmarim gathered at Toll Oivas. You should travel to Toll Oivas and defeat Iärcagar and Uiagal.Travel to Toll OivasIärcagar and Uiagal can be found within the cavern of Toll Oivas.

You have arrived to find Toll Oivas overrun by bat-wights and other fell things. You should defeat Iärcagar and Uiagal.Defeat Iärcagar at Toll OivasDefeat Uiagal at Toll OivasYou have defeated Iärcagar and Uiagal at Toll Oivas.Completed'It seems the Iron Crown is not content to bend other peoples' to its will. Within the cavern of Toll Oivas, the sorcerer Iärcagar has devised a means of binding fell spirits to the remain of bats.

'If the Iron Crown can animate flying spies to keep watch on us and Mount Gundabad itself, we shall never be able to free ourselves of their influence.

'Toll Oivas lies to the north-west from here. And while you are there, deal with his pet... Uiagal.

'Iärcagar must be slain before the skies grow dark with bat-wights!'With the defeat of Iärcagar and Uiagal, the Iron Crown's plans to use bat-wights as spies against the Gabil'akkâ and the Orcs of Mount Gundabad have failed. Your efforts have done much to ensure the success of the Zhélruka expedition in Câr Bronach.Desiring trophies from their conquest of Câr Bronach, the Zhélruka at Grúmachath will provide a bounty for bone amulets from the Dead that roam Câr Bronach.The Dead can be found in Câr Bronach.

A bounty posted by Lísek promises a bounty for the collection of bone amulets from the Dead in Câr Bronach.Collect bone amulets from the Dead in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lísek can be found at Grúmachath.

You have collected a sufficient number of bone amulets and should now deliver them to Lísek for a bounty.A bounty posted at Grúmachath reads:

'WANTED: Bone amulets claimed from the Dead that roam Câr Bronach. Our warriors desire trophies to commemorate the success of Prince Ingór's expedition in Câr Bronach and the reclamation of the Mountain-home. A fine bounty shall be offered for every twelves amulets collected. Glory to the Zhélruka!

-Lísek'


<rgb=#FF000>NOTE: This bounty may be completed up to three times for additional rewards.</rgb>'Ah-ha! These amulets will make fine adornments and serve as a grim reminder of the fate that awaits those who would oppose the Zhélruka!

'Here is your bounty, as promised.'After failing to break the hill-ram, Crótharc, Rádek of the Zhélruka promises a bounty for any warrior who can present him Crótharc's horns as a trophy.Crótharc can be found somewhere in the eastern reaches of Câr Bronach.

A bounty posted by Rádek promises a bounty for the horns of the mighty hill-ram, Crótharc, in Câr Bronach.Defeat Crótharc and collect his hornsRádek can be found at Grúmachath.

You have claimed Crótharc's horns as a trophy and should now deliver them to Rádek for a bounty.A bounty posted at Grúmachath reads:

'After slaying no fewer than three—nay four—Zhélruka in the course of attempts to break him, I desire the horns of Crótharc as wergild for my fallen brethren. Crótharc was last seen roaming the eastern hillsides of Câr Bronach. Approach him with great care, lest you meet your doom! For the Zhélruka!

-Rádek''A bittersweet end, but the only one I could abide. Do not worry, friend, Crótharc did not actually slay any of my kin. But I was bested by a ram! I couldn't simply write out the truth of my failure for all to see—I had to employ my greatest skill: exaggeration! You understand, do you not?

'I only wish Crótharc had tolerated my saddle, but I could not be made to look a fool before my kin and kindred! A mighty, stubborn, but unwise ram he was—'twould have been better for the both of us if we had seen eye to eye!

'Take this for your troubles, friend. You have spared me a great deal of embarrassment and given me a trophy to carry home from this war!'Desiring to learn the plans of the Iron Crown, the Zhélruka at Grúmachath will provide a bounty for war dispatches retrieved from the Angmarim in Câr Bronach.Angmarim can be found in Câr Bronach.

A bounty posted by Mézto promises a bounty for the collection of war dispatches from the Angmarim in Câr Bronach.Collect war dispatches from the Angmarim in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mézto can be found at Grúmachath.

You have collected a sufficient number of wicked daggers and should now deliver them to Mézto for a bounty.A bounty posted at Grúmachath reads:

'WANTED: The war dispatches carried by the Angmarim in service of the Iron Crown in Câr Bronach. Although these missives have proven difficult to obtain, they are invaluable to our efforts to topple the remnants of Angmar and provide vital information as to the plans of those who now dwell within Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire. For the Zhélruka! For the Gabil'akkâ!

-Mézto'


<rgb=#FF000>NOTE: This bounty may be completed up to three times for additional rewards.</rgb>'I shall see that Prince Ingór is apprised of what we learn from these missives. At long last, the Iron Crown shall be stopped by the Zhélruka—and our long war with Angmar ended!

'You have done much to aid the Zhélruka this day, my friend. Here, take this bounty.'Desiring to deprive the hillmen of Câr Bronach of their weapons, the Zhélruka at Grúmachath will provide a bounty for wicked daggers retrieved from evil hillmen in Câr Bronach.Evil hillmen can be found in Câr Bronach.

A bounty posted by Lísek promises a bounty for the collection of wicked daggers from evil hillmen in Câr Bronach.Collect wicked daggers from evil hillmen in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lísek can be found at Grúmachath.

You have collected a sufficient number of wicked daggers and should now deliver them to Lísek for a bounty.A bounty posted at Grúmachath reads:

'WANTED: The wicked daggers of hillmen loyal to the Iron Crown in Câr Bronach. Too many of our warriors have suffered grievous wounds at the hands of the hillmen. Slay them, and lay claim to their weapons that they might never again be wielded against the Zhélruka!

-Lísek'

<rgb=#FF000>NOTE: This bounty may be completed up to three times for additional rewards.</rgb>'Better to keep these daggers in our hands than allow the hillmen to wield them against us. What sorry lapdogs they are to grovel at the feet of the so-called masters of a dead kingdom!'

'Here is your bounty, as promised.'Fuisach of the Trév Dúvardain finds the air in Eiricháv quite unacceptable.Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.

You should clear the mould from Eiricháv.Clear the mould from Eiricháv (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.

You should talk to Fuisach.Talk to FuisachFuisach coughs and shakes his head.

'There is something about the air in Eiricháv. It does not feel right. I believe there may be mould on the cave walls. Would you search out and dispose of any mould that you find in the cave?''The air already feels better! Yes, I believe you have found the problem! Thank you!'Imák insists that he can smell the odour of magic about the chamber of Zul-mazal, and believes it may be the doing of Angmarim cultists.Imák has asked if Fastrith and Bróin wish to investigate the dealings of the Angmarim cultists in Câr Bronach.Talk to Fastrith in Zul-mazalTalk to Bróin in Zul-mazalImák has suggested that you meet up at the Witch-gate, which can be found at the connexion between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach.Meet up with Imák at the Witch-gate between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr BronachImák stands at the Witch-gate between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach.Talk to Imák at the Witch-gate'It is the unpleasant stench of ritual that I smell, ${PLAYER}, the distinctive odour of magic: the smell of a spell lingers about this chamber. I suspect it is the doing of Angmarim cultists such as those the scouts have spied lurking about the vale of Câr Bronach.

'What say you others? Will you come with us and hinder the workings of these Angmarim? If they have conducted some evil in this chamber we will make them tell us!''What say you others? Will you come with us and hinder the workings of these Angmarim? If they have conducted some evil in this chamber we will make them tell us!''I believe I will remain here, ${PLAYER}, if that is all right with you. There is still much to be learned about this mosaic, though it lacks so many of its stones.

'Perhaps Bróin will keep me company?''I would go with you, ${PLAYER}, but someone should really stay with Fastrith and keep her company while she studies the mosaic. Wouldn't you say? It would be a lonely business otherwise!''Bah! Let them stay if they want. If they could smell the distinct aura of magic that hangs upon this chamber they would not wish to stay, but few noses can boast of such perception as mine possesses!''We have arrived. This is the Witch-gate.''We have arrived. This is the Witch-gate.

'Scouts report that the vale beyond is crawling with Angmarim cultists. I do not know much of this people, but I understand you have adventured in their realm? What can you say of them?'

You briefly describe your adventures in Angmar, and Imák nods sagely.

'Aye, it sounds dreadful. Guard against such bewitchment as they seek to bring against us, and we will stand strong, ${PLAYER}. They are servants without a master now, and we will scatter them like dried leaves. You fear them not, and neither shall I!'Imák believes the mountain passes of Câr Bronach have been overrun by Angmarim cultists that threaten the mission of the Gabil'akkâ in Gundabad.The Iron Pass is located in the north-western reaches of Câr Bronach, and Imák wants you to make the road there as safe as you can while investigating the enemy presence on that route to Angmar.Scout the Iron Pass in the north-western reaches of Câr BronachTalk to Imák at the Iron PassDefeat beasts in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Having scouted the Iron Pass, Imák thinks you should now do the same for the Narrow Way, the southern pass into Elderslade. He also wants you to continue your efforts to make the mountain paths safe for the Gabil'akkâ.Scout the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and EldersladeDefeat beasts in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have met up with Imák at the Narrow Way only to discover that a former companion also shows an interest in the situation at Câr Bronach.Talk to Imák at the Narrow WayYour former companion Venko has also come to investigate the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade.Talk to Venko at the Narrow WayVenko gave you a crumpled piece of parchment that he wrestled from one of the Angmarim, and is waiting for you to read it.Read the crumpled parchment given to you by VenkoVenko has asked you to show the crumpled parchment to Imák.Venko is waiting to hear your thoughts at the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade.Talk to Venko at the Narrow Way'I do not know these lands, but I studied the maps of the Gabil'akkâ and learned enough of them to plan our next steps. We should head north through Câr Bronach and see the state of the Iron Pass; no doubt it has been well-travelled in the months since the fall of Angmar Reborn.

'It is not just the Angmarim that haunt these slopes. Let us slay the beasts that threaten our passage as we make for the Iron Pass.''We should head north-west to the Iron Pass and slay the beasts that block our way.''It is just as I said! This road may once have been little-travelled, but since their kingdom fell, the Angmarim have passed this way in great numbers.

'Cultists fled this way, but I do not think they came alone. If the Men of Angmar are like those I knew in Mordor, I am sure they filled their pockets with as much wealth as they could carry. I do not begrudge them that, though such riches are surely tainted by evil, and woe to those who seek to spend them! No, what worries me, and should worry you, is what else these cultists might have brought out of Angmar when their kingdom fell. Did they bring with them artifacts of fell power, relics of the Witch-king's rule? They might have brought anything from their defeated kingdom, ${PLAYER}.

'Let us go back the way we came, and study the southernmost pass for similar signs. Any beasts that dare to threaten us will regret it, and serve as a warning to the Angmarim that fled to Câr Bronach!''Let us go back the way we came, and study the southernmost pass for similar signs. Any beasts that dare to threaten us will regret it, and serve as a warning to the Angmarim that fled to Câr Bronach!''Over here!''Look who it is, ${PLAYER}! Our old friend Venko!'

Imák lowers his voice.

'The three of us did not always get along, it is true. But I confess that the several days since we adventured together have made me miss this old Zhélruka. What tidings does he have for us?''What news does the old Zhélruka have for us?''Hail, friends! It is good to see you again. I trust you are here on the orders of Prince Durin? I myself was sent here by command of Prince Ingór, but I see no reason we should not join forces, as we did in the Wells of the Langflood, if our goals align and we work not at cross-purposes.

'I was set upon by cultists of Angmar when I first came to Câr Bronach, but after a bit of sword-work I freed myself. From the body of my captor I took this!''Read the report I took from the Angmarim who thought to capture me, ${PLAYER}, and show it to Imák. I would know what both of you make of it.''Ah-ha! I knew it! Did I not tell you so, ${PLAYER}? The Angmarim that fled to Câr Bronach brought an artifact of evil with them!''The Angmarim that fled to Câr Bronach brought an artifact of evil with them!''We are in agreement, then? The cultists brought something out of Angmar, and we need to keep them from using it for some evil purpose!

'I am sure both princes would agree on this, ${PLAYER}. Let us work together to end the danger this poses for the Gabil'akkâ!'From the tainted lake of Eiglinn and other pools of spell-dross, shadow-grims have risen from the remnants of the Iron Crown's fell sorcery in Câr Bronach.Defeat shadow-grims at EiglinnShadow-grims can be found at Eiglinn in Câr Bronach.

Summoned forth from the remnants of the Iron Crown's sorcery, shadow-grims roam the tainted lake of Eiglinn.Defeat shadow-grims at Eiglinn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many shadow-grims at Eiglinn.CompletedUpon the frozen lake of Eiglinn, you have discovered countless shadow-grims summoned forth by the remnants of the Iron Crown's sorcery in Câr Bronach. If the way through Câr Bronach is ever to be made safe for travellers, these shadow-grims must be banished and the pollution of Eiglinn by the Iron Crown must be undone.

You should defeat shadow-grims at Eiglinn.Although it shall take time for the sorcery of the Iron Crown to fade from Câr Bronach, you have done well to banish the foul shadow-grims at Eiglinn.After escaping her imprisonment at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate, Múta intends to join the Zhélruka expedition at Grúmachath.Grúmachath can be found to the north-east of the Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.

