<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Múta, use the horn she gave you to summon her to your side.</rgb>Travel to Grúmachath with MútaMúta can be found at your side.

You have arrived at Grúmachath. You should talk to Múta.


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Múta, use the horn she gave you to summon her to your side.</rgb>Talk to MútaMúta can be found at Grúmachath.

After arriving at Grúmachath, Múta ran off toward the centre of the encampment. You should join Múta by the camp-fire at Grúmachath.Join Múta by the camp-fire at the centre of GrúmachathMúta can be found at Grúmachath.

You have found Múta speaking to the Zhélruka in charge of Grúmachath. You should talk to Múta.Talk to Múta at GrúmachathMézto can be found at Grúmachath.

You have found Múta speaking to the Zhélruka in charge of Grúmachath, Mézto. You should talk to Mézto.Talk to Mézto at Grúmachath'After I was captured, I spied some Zhélruka to the north-east. It was an unintended benefit of being imprisoned so high up, it seems!

'According to what little the Gabil'akkâ knows of this region, there is an old Angmarim settlement in that direction known as Grúmachath. Perhaps that is where the Zhélruka have made camp... or perhaps not, but anywhere is better than staying here.

'Let's go, ${PLAYER}. I will show you the way!''Ah, here we are at last!'

Múta looks around Grúmachath and spies several Zhélruka standing around a camp-fire.

'That looks to be the dwarf in charge, ${PLAYER}. I will go announce us!

'Come on over in a moment!''There you are, ${PLAYER}. I was just telling Mézto about the hardship we encountered in our journey to Grúmachath.

'In exchange for our aid, the Zhélruka are willing to give us quarter and supplies as needed. That is kindness enough for me, my friend, but why don't you speak to Mézto yourself?''Câr Bronach has drawn the attention of all sorts, it seems. Perhaps Prince Durin did not wish to be left out!

'As I said to Múta, you may aid us and make camp among us, but in matters of this expedition, I will answer only to the orders of Prince Ingór. Is that understood?'Originally intending to join the Zhélruka expedition in Câr Bronach, Múta and her scouts quickly became separated after being ambushed by Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.

After being discovered by Dourhands at the Witch-gate, Múta was captured and the rest of her scouts were scattered. You should find Múta.Find Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gateMúta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.

Múta has been captured and imprisoned by the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. You should talk to Múta.Talk to Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gateDourhands can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.

In preparation for her escape, Múta has asked you to collect orders from the Dourhands at the Witch-gate. You should defeat the Dourhands and collect their orders.Collect orders from the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.

You have collected orders from the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. You should deliver them to Múta.Múta's weapons can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.

Múta has asked you to return her weapons to her before attempting an escape. You should collect Múta's weapons.Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.

You have recovered Múta's weapons. You should deliver them to Múta.'Before we set out, Múta warned us that some new purpose has kindled the spirits of the Dourhands and that they serve one of their own sworn to the Iron Crown: Brathar Crack-helm. We made every preparation... or so we thought.

'No sooner had we passed through the Witch-gate than we were caught in a trap! Múta was captured by the Dourhands, but I do not know what has become of Kársa or Uzvát. Alas, ${PLAYER}, I'm in no condition to mount a rescue.'

'I'm afraid you will have to manage that, my friend.'

As Gárjan braces his leg, you notice a lengthy gash in the armour covering his thigh.

'Bah, it looks worse than it is! At the very least, I can make it back to Bárgstad on my own to tell Ausma what has happened.

'Do not let these Dourhands get the last laugh, ${PLAYER}. Múta must be freed before it is too late!''${PLAYER}! What are you doing here?!'

Múta's voice shrinks to a gruff whisper.

'I didn't expect for help to be sent so soon, but given the circumstances, I'm more than happy to be wrong! When the Dourhands ambushed us, I saw Kársa and Uzvát escape to the east. But have you seen Gárjan?'

You tell Múta that Gárjan escaped and that he now intends to warn Ausma and Lord Glóin of the danger beyond the Witch-gate.

'It seems our efforts to foil the Iron Crown in Elderslade did not go as unnoticed as we hoped. After the Dourhands threw me in this cage, I overheard them mumbling about new orders from Brathar. Unfortunately, they were wise enough to continue their conversations where I couldn't eavesdrop on them.

'Why don't you see if some of them have been foolish enough to keep their orders on hand? I'll keep trying to free myself in the meantime!''Did you find anything?'

You hand the orders to Múta. As she reads them, her eyebrows raise and lower a few times. After a moment, she scoffs.

'Bah! If these orders are to be believed, we and the Zhélruka have our work cut out for us. From what I can tell, the Iron Crown, as well as their Dourhand and Hill-men allies, now serve one named High Priestess Ásachal. I cannot be certain of it, but I would not doubt she is a descendant of the corrupt Men of Westernesse! It seems the Iron Crown has laid claim to that fortress across the valley—the Drearspire, they call it. It is said they seek something called "Crûn Nasgadh", but I cannot glean anything else about it from these orders. Is it some sort of artifact? A spell of old Angmar? Whatever it is, I'm certain it won't be good for us or the Gabil'akkâ if they find it!

'Things are more urgent than they seemed, ${PLAYER}. Will you fetch me my weapons? The Dourhands took them and set them on a table over there—just out of my reach. I've an idea on how to escape from this cage, but I'd feel a lot better about it if I wasn't unarmed.''You have them? Give them here, my friend!'

As Múta examines her axe and dagger, a smile forms at the corner of her mouth.

'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}. It'll be time to put them to use soon enough!'Encamped at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate, the Dourhands loyal to the Iron Crown dutifully guard the pass to Câr Bronach.Destroy banners of the Dourhands at Mur Shatraug
