You should talk to Soltakh of the Trév Gállorg in Eiricháv.Talk to Soltakh of the Trév Gállorg in Eiricháv'While we have managed to take Grúmachath, our numbers are too little to succeed against the Angmarim and Dourhands. If the Gabil'akkâ is to succeed in Câr Bronach, we may need some allies. I have sent my best scout, Uzvát, to seek out potential allies in the mountains. My hopes were not high.

'To my surprise, Uzvát returned with word of a group of hillmen working against the Angmarim. They work from a secret cave, high upon the slopes to the north. You and Uzvát are to return to Eiricháv and offer our assistance. We must show these hillmen that the Zhélruka are willing to work with them to hurry their cause.''This is the cave of Eiricháv, ${PLAYER}. I have already made an initial contact with the group. It seems your name precedes you, as a couple of the hillmen seem to already know who you are. They are expecting you within, my friend.''It has been a long while, ${PLAYER}. I would wager that you did not expect to see those of the Trév Dúvardain and the Trév Gállorg working as one. Yet, here we are.

'You have met our leader, Domongart, before. He is on an urgent mission of diplomacy in the north. That is all that I can say. I have heard from Uzvát that you wish to assist us in our efforts. You have assisted me in the past. I know that you will be able to do so once more, old friend.

'The Trév Duvárdain have been sundered by choice. Many remain loyal to the Iron Crown. Those here see the folly in servitude. Assist us in our efforts here and then we will consider returning the favour to assist the Zhélruka.''You have done well. We thank you for your assistance. Just as you have already done, I continue to make a name for myself in these lands.'A lone stone-giant has been spotted sitting upon the old ruins of Crágan Bris.Crágan Bris can be found in the hills west of Hlídborg in Câr Bronach.

You should travel to Crágan Bris.Travel to Crágan BrisCrágan Bris can be found in the hills west of Hlídborg in Câr Bronach.

You should talk to Skálgrund at Crágan Bris.Talk to Skálgrund, the Exile at Crágan BrisCrágan Bris can be found in the hills west of Hlídborg in Câr Bronach.

You should feed the rams at Crágan Bris.Crágan Bris can be found in the hills west of Hlídborg in Câr Bronach.

You should talk to Skálgrund at Crágan Bris.Talk to Skálgrund at Crágan BrisMézto and be found at Grúmachath in central Câr Bronach.

You should return to Mézto.Return to Mézto with what you have learned'A memory has come to me, ${PLAYER}. I did not think much of it at the time. Now, in light of what you have learned, I believe there is something else worth investigating before you return to Mézto. The day after the Angmarim visited the stone-giants, we saw our first and only movement from the encampment of Hlídborg. Two giants left the camp. One was Hraubrek, Chieftain of the Grímklettar, who marched off to the north with purpose. We were unable to follow. The second was a stone-giant who stomped away from the encampment in anger. He headed towards the old ruins of Crágan Bris.

'Those old ruins might be worth investigating.''Go away!

'What?! You are still here?!

'You can ask me all the questions you you want. It does not mean that I will answer them!

'How could I even trust you? I can not even trust my own kind to make the right decisions. I can only trust these goats. If the goats trust you, then maybe I will answer a question for you.''You have done as I asked, and the goats seem to find you acceptable. I will answer your question.

'Why am I here you ask? Crágan Bris was once a great settlement of my people. It is all I have left. You do not know much about Câr Bronach, I see. Then I will explain. This is where my ancestors came from. We once had a great city where the Drearspire now stands. Our home was taken from us by Men and we were chased away. Hraubrek wanted to reclaim our land. That is why we have returned. I followed Hraubrek because I believed in his wisdom. Now I am lost, for Hraubrek allies with our enemy. All our alliances have ended in death. How will this one be any different?!

'I have answered your question, now leave me be.''${PLAYER}, have you returned! I was starting to wonder where you had gotten to!

'So the Grímklettar ally with the Dourhands, but not the Angmarim? I find this confusing! We know the Angmarim and the Dourhands work together! There is more at hand in Câr Bronach then I thought! Someone is driving a wedge in this alliance.'The stone-giant encampment of Hlídborg remains the last giant-hold upon the slopes of Câr Bronach.Hlídborg can be found in south east Câr Bronach.

You should travel to Hlídborg.Travel to HlídborgHlídborg can be found in south east Câr Bronach.

