You should talk to Kúzun.Talk to Kúzun at Leitstáth'The rumours of a barricade on the eastern edge of Câr Bronach have proven to be false. What we found when we arrived was a group of stone-giants, encamped on the nearby slopes. We have watched them, waiting for them to strike or prepare for war. Instead, they sit idle.  They were recently visited by the Angmarim. We were not able to eavesdrop, and as such, we do not know what conversation transpired.

'If you were able to infiltrate Hlídborg, I am sure we would find some evidence of Angmarim influence over the stone-giants.''Dourhands! Are you sure?! Why would the stone-giants be in league with the Dourhands?

'Kúzun, what do you make of this revelation?''This certainly would explain their inactivity, if they ally with the Dourhands instead of the Angmarim. The Dourhands must have arranged a pact with the Grímklettar under cover of night, and after, the Angmarim left the stone-giants be.

