You should destroy altars and supplies at Agal Dûn.Destroy Angmarim altars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Iron Crown supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Within Agal Dûn, the fortress of horror, Angmarim of the Iron Crown watch over Câr Bronach. Behind its wall, Angmarim gather supplies and altars for their vile rituals. In steps to reclaim Câr Bronach, these supplies and altars must be destroyed.Ordered by Prince Ingór to learn more about the Angmarim presence in Câr Bronach, Venko is pleased to adventure with you and Imák once again.Venko believes there is more to learn from the messages carried hither and yon by Angmarim cultists within Câr Bronach. He wants you to wrest from them any such missives.Defeat Angmarim cultists or Trév Duvárdain in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/8)Venko believes there is more to learn from the messages carried hither and yon by Angmarim cultists within Câr Bronach. He wants you to wrest from them any such missives.Defeat Angmarim cultists or Trév Duvárdain in Câr Bronach (7/8)You retrieved a set of orders from one of the cultists you faced in Câr Bronach, and should read it to learn what you can of their movements and plans for the mountain passes.Read the orders from MagithVenko is outside Tâg Fógarrach. No doubt the Zhélruka will be pleased to see the set of orders you recovered from the Angmarim cultist you defeated.Venko saw something disturbing to the south-east, just behind Tâg Fógarrach, and he has asked you to investigate. Whatever he saw, the vision seems to have shaken the Zhélruka's composure.Investigate the mountainside to the south-east, behind Tâg Fógarrach, and learn what could have shaken Venko's composureVenko saw something disturbing by the mountainside to the south-east, behind Tâg Fógarrach, and he has asked you to investigate. Whatever he saw, the vision seems to have shaken the Zhélruka's composure.Someone watchesVenko is outside Tâg Fógarrach, disturbed by whatever it was he saw.Talk to Venko outside Tâg FógarrachImák is south-west of Tûr Fúar, stroking his beard thoughtfully.Talk to Imák south-west of Tûr Fúar'The Angmarim are up to something in Câr Bronach, that much is clear. Defeat as many of the cultists as you can find, and I will do the same. Some of them are bound to carry reports from which we can learn more of their plans, and with good fortune we may learn where they brought this artifact!''Defeat as many of the cultists or their Trév Duvárdain allies as you can find, and I will do the same. Some of them are bound to carry reports from which we can learn more of their plans, and with good fortune we may learn where they brought this artifact!''Defeat as many of the cultists or their Trév Duvárdain allies as you can find, and I will do the same. Some of them are bound to carry reports from which we can learn more of their plans, and with good fortune we may learn where they brought this artifact!''Hmmm? What?'

Venko appears quite distracted, his attention distant. At last he notices your presence and turns confused eyes on you.

'Oh, I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. I thought I saw... well, someone that couldn't be there. Can you... can you go to the south-east, just behind Tâg Fógarrach, and see if there is anything to see?''I thought I saw... well, someone that couldn't be there. Can you... can you go to the south-east, just behind Tâg Fógarrach, and see if there is anything to see?''Did you... did you see anything, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Venko that you felt eyes upon you, but the watchful presence did not show itself to you. His brow creases with worry and with thought.

'I thought I saw my younger brother Dúsek. He stood there, just by the mountainside, and watched me in silence. I called out to him, but he did not answer. I called again, though I knew it was for naught, for Dúsek is dead and will never see Gundabad. Did we not honour him at the Reikfoss, ${PLAYER}, both he and my eldest brother Lékhun, slain by the Frost-horde?

'Dúsek could not be here, and yet he was, in appearance just as I remember him. What can it mean, my friends?''Dúsek could not be here, and yet he was, in appearance just as I remember him. What can it mean, my friends?''Do not be fooled by such sentimental apparitions, Venko! I feel in my heart this has something to do with the rituals of the Angmarim being conducted in their vile tower. This has the stench of foul magic upon it, and I wager they are somehow to blame. We must not fall for their tricks!'Imák believes that the troubling presence that so disturbed Venko might be the result of a ritual being conducted by the Angmarim in Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire. The Stout-axe thinks the three of you should investigate, despite the danger.Imák believes that the troubling presence that so disturbed Venko might be the result of a ritual being conducted by the Angmarim in Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, and he wants you to investigate.Talk to Imák and sneak into the Drearspire of Tûr FúarVenko is north of the Witch-gate.Talk to Venko north of the Witch-gateImák and Venko are prepared to depart Câr Bronach, and want to travel with you to the Witch-gate.Return to the Witch-gate with Imák and VenkoYou once again feel the watchful presence.Someone watchesImák stands at the Witch-gate, a haunted expression on his face.Talk to Imák at the Witch-gateVenko is at the Witch-gate, waiting to speak with you about what you saw.Talk to Venko at the Witch-gate'If the vision that so troubled Venko is the result of some Angmarim ritual, I think I know just where we will find the source of it. What do they call their tower? Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire? If those orders you recovered are to be believed, it may be that the complement of guards promised by Magith the Scather has not yet been dispatched to fortify the tower.

'Let us sneak inside and put an end to whatever magic these cultists think to unleash. We will all be the better for it, and Venko not least of all!''The Drearspire awaits us. Are you ready?'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'We need to bring word of the Angmarim intention to break the wards on the Gloomingtarn. Let us climb the path to the Witch-gate itself and then we will bring this urgent message together!''We need to bring word of the Angmarim intention to break the wards on the Gloomingtarn. Let us meet up at the Witch-gate and then we will bring this urgent message together!''What is wrong, ${PLAYER}? What did you see?'

You tell Imák you recognized a figure from your past, who could not possibly be there.

'I believe you, for I also saw someone impossible. I saw a dwarf-woman named Anorta, who I knew during my captivity in Mordor. I escaped from the Black Land, but Anorta did not. She is dead. She could not be here... and yet I saw her standing just ahead, just as I remembered her.''This time I saw my eldest brother, Lékhun, and he seemed just the same to me as he did in life. What did the watchful presence show to you, ${PLAYER}? Who did you see?'

You tell Venko that you beheld a Ranger named Amdir, who suffered a grievous, corrupting injury from a Nazgûl's blade when you adventured in Bree-land. He nods solemnly.

'He is dead, or worse than dead? Then he cannot be here... and yet you saw him. There is some strange force at work in these mountains, but it is not the work of the Angmarim. It is something else.'You have come with Imák and Venko to Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, to learn if an Angmarim ritual is behind the curious happenings within Câr Bronach.Imák and Venko wait for you on the hill upon which the Drearspire stands.Imák and Venko hope your presence in the Drearspire will go unnoticed as you investigate the Angmarim interest in the tower.Follow Imák and Venko toward the DrearspireVenko stands before a side entrance to the Drearspire, considering its suitability for your purpose.You have entered the Drearspire with Imák and Venko, in search of answers: what villainy have the Angmarim conducted within Câr Bronach?Enter the Drearspire with Imák and VenkoYou have entered the Drearspire with Imák and Venko, in search of answers: what villainy have the Angmarim conducted within Câr Bronach?You have entered the Drearspire with Imák and Venko and should search the tower for answers.Explore the Drearspire with Imák and VenkoInside the Drearspire, Venko has called for you to halt.Talk to Venko inside the DrearspireYou have entered the Drearspire with Imák and Venko, and now you have the opportunity to eavesdrop on some of the Angmarim who remain in the tower. Perhaps you will learn what these evil folk seek to accomplish within Câr Bronach, and elsewhere.

You must not be seen by the Angmarim cultists.Eavesdrop on the discussion between the cultists in the Drearspire<rgb=#FF0000>Avoid being seen by the Angmarim cultists</rgb>'Our investigation has borne fruit, ${PLAYER}: it seems the strange occurrences within Câr Bronach are not entirely understood by the Angmarim cultists themselves.

'But there is reason for us to leave this tower, and with haste! The Angmarim leader Rúvaran now possesses an artifact with which he hopes to break the runes on Gloomingtarn, where stand the still waters of the sacred lake of Durin!

'We will set aside the mysteries of Câr Bronach for now. Rúvaran and his Angmarim must be opposed!''The snow has begun. It is not yet very heavy, but if it gets worse perhaps it will mask our approach.

'Let us try to do this without fighting, if we can. I wager the answers we seek will be on an upper level of the tower, and the further we can get without making noise, the more we will learn.

'Will this be a problem, Brawler?''The snow has begun. It is not yet very heavy, but if it gets worse perhaps it will mask our approach.

'Let us try to do this without fighting, if we can. I wager the answers we seek will be on an upper level of the tower, and the further we can get without making noise, the more we will learn.

'Agreed? Good.''Still we have seen no guards, and it seems to me we might have walked right up to the front door of the tower, if that was our wish! We have either been very fortunate to this point... or it is a trap.

'Let us use this side entrance. It may allow us to surprise any Angmarim that might lie in ambush for us within the Drearspire.''Still we have seen no guards, and it seems to me we might have walked right up to the front door of the tower, if that was our wish! We have either been very fortunate to this point... or it is a trap.

'Let us use this side entrance. It may allow us to surprise any Angmarim that might lie in ambush for us within the Drearspire.''A tower of this size could hold a battalion of Angmarim, ${PLAYER}, and our prior scouting revealed that recently it did! Where then have the cultists gone?

'Let us proceed, and let caution be the watch-word.''A tower of this size could hold a battalion of Angmarim, ${PLAYER}, and our prior scouting revealed that recently it did! Where then have the cultists gone?

'Let us proceed, and let caution be the watch-word.''I hear the voices of Angmarim from just ahead, ${PLAYER}. Let us advance, slowly, and see if we can eavesdrop on their conversation. Let us remain out of sight and we may learn what they seek to do here in Câr Bronach, and elsewhere.'

He turns to address your Stout-axe companion.

'Imák, you stay here and guard the path of our escape, in the event we need it. But we will try to avoid being seen by these villains.

'Come, ${PLAYER}, and make as little noise as possible!'Múta suggests pushing further into the Drearspire, for Brathar Crack-helm has been truthful in his word, thus far.Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.

