After returning to Abkân'aban, Thrástan revealed himself to be a servant of the First Crafter named Tamindur the Forge-servant. You talk to Tamindur.Talk to TamindurHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn.

After gathering your allies and speaking with Tamindur, you are ready to depart for Watchers' Roost. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Abkân'abanHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

After departing from Abkân'aban, you have returned to Watchers' Roost. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Watchers' Roost'In light of what has happened here at Abkân'aban, I shall soon have to speak to Prince Durin.

'That a servant of the First Crafter would reveal himself to us is too unbelievable a tale to send by any missive! Only my voice might lend it any credibility... and even so, the Prince may have to see with his own eyes!

'Let us not trouble our new benefactor, ${PLAYER}. Our gratitude is enough, I think, and there are greater matters in this world for one of such power to lend his aid.

'You should speak to the others here and see if they are ready to depart. When that is so, come speak to me again!''I hardly know what to say, ${PLAYER}...'

Spall gazes up at the White Stone Forge where Tamindur now stands watch.

'I have seen more in one day than I dreamt of seeing in a lifetime.

'As for me, my survey will continue unhindered now that the Iron Crown have been driven out of Gloomingtarn. Who knows what other secrets lie hidden for us to discover? I, for one, relish the chance to find them!

'When Lord Stormhammer wishes to depart, I shall be prepared.''What an adventure, ${PLAYER}!

'From the Lonely Mountain to Elderslade and now to the very heart of Mount Gundabad... I am grateful our paths crossed when they did. Perhaps I was a bit too eager to confront the Iron Crown, but it all worked out in the end, didn't it?'

Hersegg smirks and looks to Tamindur.

'A victory hard won... and secured with as near a miracle as I've ever seen! The First Crafter himself must watch over us here in Mount Gundabad!

'I will be ready to depart in just a moment, my friend. Why don't you go and see if Spall is ready to set out?''You need not fear my wrath, ${PLAYER}. Approach, and let us speak!

'Long ago, when the Shaper's work was finished, I was bidden to rest beneath Mount Gundabad. In time, I awoke as Thrástan; different in form, but alike in mind and spirit to walk among Durin's Folk. In my long years of solitude, the two diverged, but I am now restored.

'At long last, my vigil nears its end and a new Age is soon to dawn. But fear not, I shall ward the Stone of Awakening from all evil that would seek to master it until I am called back to the Uttermost West.

'Yet many trials lay ahead for you, little one.''Is everyone prepared to depart? Very good, ${PLAYER}.

'Let us return to Watchers' Roost and, at last, we can set about undoing the damage the Iron Crown has done to Gloomingtarn!'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will swiftly travel to Watchers' Roost after advancing this quest.</rgb>'Ah, ${PLAYER}, it seems our journey through Mount Gundabad shall have more than its fair share of surprises!

'My expedition and I will see to repairing the damage left by the Iron Crown, and we shall set the echo-horns across this great cavern into alignment once more. The warding-runes may never again repel our foes, but when the Mountain-home is ours again and evermore, I hope we find we have no need for them!

'I am certain Prince Durin and the others shall have need of your aid in the Clovengap and beyond, but I thank you for all you have done here, my friend. Without your aid, the secrets of our ancestors may well have been forgotten!

'Baruk Khazâd! For Gundabad!'Much to Spall's surprise, Hermáth Stormhammer has permitted him to begin his survey of Gloomingtarn. However, Hermáth Stormhammer also wishes to learn what has become of his warriors, Lokur and Vithin, who led companies into the ancient tunnels of Gloomingtarn.Spall can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

Hermáth Stormhammer has permitted Spall to conduct a survey of Gloomingtarn on the condition that you accompany him. You should talk to Spall.Talk to Spall at Watchers' RoostVithin and Lokur can be found in Glittengrof and Ormgren, respectively. Spall can be found at your side.

Hermáth Stormhammer has permitted Spall to conduct a survey of Gloomingtarn on the condition that you accompany him and also aid the expeditions in Glittengrof and Ormgren. You should aid Spall with his survey and receive reports from Lokur and Vithin, two warriors of Hermáth Stormhammer's expedition.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.</rgb>Talk to Vithin and assist the expedition in GlittengrofTalk to Lokur and assist the expedition in OrmgrenAid Spall with 'Surveying Glittengrof'Aid Spall with 'Surveying Ormgren'Spall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn.

You have helped Spall complete his survey of Glittengrof and Ormgren. You should talk to Spall.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.</rgb>Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

You have assisted Lokur and Vithin with their expeditions into Glittengrof and Ormgren, and Spall has completed the first part of his survey of Gloomingtarn. You should return to Watchers' Roost and talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Watchers' Roost'Now then, ${PLAYER}...

'I know this will come as some surprise, but my granddaughter has not shied from voicing her misgivings about your companion. However, I believe I see something of myself in him. Spall is a curious dwarf and he is well-learned in the history of the dwarves. Indeed, Spall might prove invaluable to this expedition. I was hesitant to allow him to begin his survey unaccompanied, but with you here, I see no reason to keep him from his studies!

'Besides, I need your help with another matter, my friend. After we established camp here at Watchers' Roost, I sent two companies to investigate some of the old passages of Gloomingtarn. One of my warriors, Vithin, led his company to Glittengrof, and another, Lokur, led his to Ormgren. My scouts spied a few glass-spiders near the entrance to Glittengrof, but I know little of Ormgren. Unfortunately, neither company has returned or even sent word—be it good or ill. Needless to say, I have become concerned. Either they have made some great discovery, or some terrible fate may have befallen them. If you find them in the course of Spall's survey, aid them as best you can. I would not leave any of my warriors behind!

'Go, ${PLAYER}, and tell Spall that he may begin his survey in Glittengrof and Ormgren—so long as you accompany him!''Lord Stormhammer has given me permission to begin my survey of Gloomingtarn? And you will accompany me? How wonderful!

'I had hoped to begin my survey at Abkân'aban, the great Stone of Wakening, but upon further thought, I suppose that is better left for last. Yes, Glittengrof and Ormgren shall be fine places to begin my studies!'

Spall begins to collect his things into his pockets and picks up a nearby axe.

'If it is all right with you, ${PLAYER}, I would like to set off at once!''By Durin's beard, you startled me! Did Lord Stormhammer send you?'

Vithin catches his breath and begins to whisper.

'Aye, I'm Vithin, but I'm afraid I cannot leave—not yet. Glittengrof and its crystals are indeed beautiful, but that doesn't mean much if it's overrun by spiders! Even worse, I've lost most of my company in these blasted webs!

'I can't just leave them! Will you aid me?''You are a friend of Prince Durin's, are you not? Oh, thank you for coming to my aid!'

'We arrived expecting to find an old, abandoned delving to mine, but instead we've found what must be thousands of glow-worms! If we intend to reclaim Ormgren, it will take more than my axe and a small company of miners to do it!

'Will you aid me? I shall send word to Lord Stormhammer as soon as I can!''Although I can hardly believe it myself, I think we're finished here.

'I could not have done this without you, my friend. Your name will no doubt feature prominently in my notes about Gloomingtarn—whenever I should actually finish writing everything down!

'These surveys have given me much to consider, ${PLAYER}, and some very fine things to study! If you wish to explore Glittengrof or Ormgren further, I am certain you will be up to the task. As for me, I'm going back to Watchers' Roost!

'Farewell!''Ah, ${PLAYER}. You have returned not a moment too soon!

'Spall spoke highly of your aid in his survey, but I must ask something of you now as well.'Believing that no dwarf could have entered Mount Gundabad between the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs and the arrival of the Gabil'akkâ, Hermáth Stormhammer is determined to learn how Thrástan came to dwell in Gloomingtarn.Thrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

After you and Hersegg discovered an old dwarf alone in the caverns of Gloomingtarn, Hermáth Stormhammer has asked you to talk to Thrástan and uncover how he came to dwell in Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Thrástan.Talk to ThrástanThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

Thrástan seems unaware of your presence. You should hail Thrástan and attempt to get his attention.<rgb=#FF00FF>Hail</rgb> Thrástan and try to get his attentionThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

Thrástan has turned to look at you. You should talk to Thrástan.Talk to ThrástanThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

Thrástan has become distraught in his attempt to answer your questions. You should try to calm Thrástan and urge him to continue trying to remember.<rgb=#FF00FF>Calm</rgb> Thrástan and urge him to continueThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

Thrástan does not appear to be able to answer your questions. You should talk to Thrástan.Talk to ThrástanHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

Before you could learn much from Thrástan, the old dwarf appears to suffer from some unseen ailment. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer'To my knowledge, there is not a single dwarf among the Gabil'akkâ named Thrástan!

'You see, ${PLAYER}... unless Thrástan was with us before the Iron Crown captured him, it is nearly impossible that he should have found his way this deep into Mount Gundabad. Even when the Haban’akkâ breached the Mountain-home during the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs, we ventured no further than Máttugard. Even King Thráin deemed the Deepscrave too perilous to cross, and after all, Azog had yet to be slain!

'Perhaps he entered in the years that followed, but to elude the Orcs as far as Zâram-mekhem on his own is beyond the skill—or luck—of any dwarf I have ever known! Or that he could have dwelt here since the time of Durin the Deathless? Impossible! Only Durin himself was so long-lived among the Dwarves!

'I cannot make any sense of it, my friend. If he is truly of Durin's Folk, Thrástan must answer for himself!

'Question Thrástan, ${PLAYER}, speak to him, and learn what you can!'Thrástan does not appear to notice your presence.

He mumbles inaudibly to himself for a moment and then falls silent.Thrástan raises his hand to greet you, but remains silent. You ask Thrástan how he came to dwell within Mount Gundabad. After a long pause, he begins to speak, but his voice is gravelly and weak.

'I... I do not remember.'

You ask Thrástan if he was among the Haban’akkâ of Thráin during the Sixth War of the Dwarves and Orcs. He shakes his head solemnly, but his face betrays a pained expression.

'The memories... it is as if they are not mine. Even this name... I gave it to myself. It... was so... long ago....''I... am sorry. I wish I could... remember, but I... cannot. A chill... has taken... these old bones.'

Thrástan shivers uncomfortably.

'I have... been too long... from the Shaper's hearth.''What were you able to learn from Thrástan, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Hermáth Stormhammer what little knowledge you gleaned from Thrástan's words. You mention that the dwarf appears to be suffering from a strange ailment, but you suspect that he wishes to travel to Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening.

'Ah, I see. I am afraid I now only have more questions on my mind! As for the Shaper's hearth... could Thrástan be speaking of the White Stone Forge?'At Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening, the Angmarim of the Iron Crown seek to master the white forge of Durin the Deathless, forever defiling the hallowed caverns of Gloomingtarn.Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost.

Determined to both repel the Iron Crown and escort Thrástan to the White Stone Forge, Hermáth Stormhammer has asked you to accompany him and his warriors to Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth StormhammerHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn.

After defeating Allaban the Collector at Abkân'aban and the revelation of Thrástan's identity, Hermáth Stormhammer wishes to speak with you. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Abkân'aban'Although we still do not know the truth of how Thrástan came to dwell in Mount Gundabad, I am inclined to aid him—especially now that he seems to have taken ill. If any good can come from his return to Abkân'aban, I shall not keep him from it! Let us—'

A scout's sudden arrival interrupts your conversation. The scout hands Hermáth a missive, and Hermáth begins to read it. After a moment, his brow furrows in concern.

'It seems we were fated to travel to Abkân'aban this day, ${PLAYER}. I have just received word that the Angmarim of the Iron Crown have gathered their forces and now make for the Stone of Wakening!

'To cede the sacred place of Durin's awakening to these wicked Men—it would be unthinkable! Let us go—all of us—and put an end to the Iron Crown's plans for Gloomingtarn!''There is no time to waste, ${PLAYER}. Are you prepared?''I am not certain what we just witnessed, ${PLAYER}. Had I not seen it with my own eyes, I would never have believed it!

'That one of the servants of the First Crafter would come to our aid in our hour of need...'

Hermáth Stormhammer's eyes are wide with awe.

'What better omen of success could Prince Durin and the Gabil'akkâ have wished for?'Imák and Venko think you should return to the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ with news of both the Angmarim cultists' plans and the peculiar visions the three of you experienced in Câr Bronach.Venko is at the Witch-gate, waiting to speak with you before the three of you depart for Maergrind, the Noble Gate.Talk to Venko and travel to MaergrindDurin is at Maergrind, enraged by both Gorgar's attack and the words of the Orc leader.Talk to Durin at Maergrind, the Noble Gate'There is something about Gundabad that is affecting us in this fashion, ${PLAYER}, but what it might be is beyond this Zhélruka's ken. I do not like it, and I do not trust it. I have no need for Imák's sense of smell to tell you the odour of this is foul!

'But for now we should return to Durin and Prince Ingór, and tell them of the Angmarim's efforts to use the Máltagar to break the wards on Gloomingtarn. Speak to me if you are ready, and we will hurry back to Máttugard!''Let us away, and at once! Such riddles as these worrisome visions pose must wait until we have more time to ponder them and fewer urgent concerns!''A thousand curses upon him! Gorgar will pay for this attack, and he will pay in blood!'Gorgar's attack has left many dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ dead or wounded. If the conquest of Gundabad is to be successful, Prince Durin and those loyal to him must recover from this defeat, and resist despair.Búkk is at Maergrind.

Durin asked you to collect salves and bandages from Búkk with which to heal the hurts of those dwarves who are not already beyond help.Talk to Búkk at MaergrindLongbeards and Zhélruka were wounded during Gorgar's attack, and many of them require treatment for their wounds.Búkk is at Maergrind.

You have treated the dwarves you could, and should now return the remaining supplies to Búkk.Durin is at Maergrind, furious at Gorgar's attack and grieving for the slain.Talk to Durin at MaergrindSlagvi is at Maergrind.Talk to Slagvi at MaergrindDurin is at Maergrind.Talk to Durin at MaergrindSlagvi is at Maergrind.Talk to Slagvi at Maergrind'Vengeance will have to wait, though it pains me to say so! We must do something about our dead and wounded.

'Where is Búkk? We have need of your salves and poultices, your slings and bandages! ${PLAYER}, find Búkk! Fire and flames, pox and bother! Where is Búkk?''Where is Búkk? We have need of your salves and poultices, your slings and bandages! ${PLAYER}, find Búkk! Fire and flames, pox and bother! Where is Búkk?''I am here, I am here!

'Gorgar will not escape retribution for this attack, but I fear we have sustained such losses that we may lack the fighters to hold the son of Bolg responsible! No, that cannot be. It must not be!

'Take these salves and bandages and bring them to any dwarves who need them. So many dead, so many wounded... I hope this will be enough, but I fear it will not be.''Take these salves and bandages and bring them to any dwarves who need them. So many dead, so many wounded... I hope this will be enough, but I fear it will not be.'Prince Ingór refuses the bandage.

'I need it not,' he insists.'Thank you for your quick action, friend. This haste may yet save some of our wounded from succumbing to their injuries and joining the list of the slain.

'Líkmund... Stóthkell... Thettmárr... too many dead at Gorgar's command.''Thank you for your quick action, friend. This haste may yet save some of our wounded from succumbing to their injuries and joining the list of the slain.''I am still angry, ${PLAYER}, do not mistake me! But my rage, once white-hot, has cooled to a slow-burning ember. I will not allow it to push me into recklessness. Gorgar will pay for this, if not today then on the morrow. But you have a report for me from the vale of Câr Bronach? Tell me what you learned there; I will not let Gorgar's attack divert or delay our plans, and I would know what you discovered.'

You tell Durin that Angmarim cultists intend to use an artifact they rescued from Barad Gúlaran during the fall of Angmar Reborn to break the wards on Gloomingtarn.

'That cannot be allowed! That place is sacred, and must be protected from the cultists and Gorgar both! If you are willing, I ask you to go with Bósi of the Iron Garrison and put an end to that Angmarim mission.''Yes, Slagvi, what is it?''My prince, I hope you will forgive this interruption and grant me this boon: may I accompany ${PLAYER} on this task? I mourn for Stóthkell who perished at Gorgar's hands, and I wish to see to the safety of Gloomingtarn and the Wakening Stone that lies within. It is what the forge-master would want, and I desire to do right by his memory.''Will you grant me this boon, my prince?''Aye, Slagvi. Do this in memory of Stóthkell, and honour him. I will send Bósi to assist the two of you later.

'The Angmarim cannot be allowed to despoil the ground where my ancestor Durin first awoke. Keep them from staining Gloomingtarn with their steps or their foul magic, ${PLAYER}.''Stand strong against Orc and cultist alike, and avenge Forge-master Stóthkell.''Thank you, my prince.

'${PLAYER}! The reason I must ask to accompany you brings me no joy, but I am grateful that you and the prince allow it. It should be Forge-master Stóthkell who safe-guards the Gloomingtarn, but he cannot, and I must do it in his stead.'Slagvi wants to honour the memory of Stóthkell by protecting the sacred lake of Gloomingtarn from the Angmarim, and has volunteered to accompany you there.Slagvi asked to meet with you at the entrance to Gloomingtarn from Deepscrave, where he fears the rune-stones warding passage to that sacred cavern may be threatened.Meet up with Slagvi at the entrance to Gloomingtarn from DeepscraveSlagvi stands beside the rune-stone wards at the entrance to Gloomingtarn.Talk to Slagvi at the entrance to GloomingtarnStudying the stones on either side of the entrance may reveal what happened to the wards that once blocked passage to Gloomingtarn.Slagvi stands at the entrance to Gloomingtarn, beside the broken wards.Talk to Slagvi at the entrance to GloomingtarnSlagvi asked you to defeat any Angmarim cultists you find lurking within the cavern of Gloomingtarn.Defeat Angmarim cultists within Gloomingtarn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Slagvi stands beside the lakeshore in the vast cavern, deep in thought.Talk to Slagvi by the lakeshoreSlagvi has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> toward the Stone of Wakening, the island that stands in the lake.<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> toward the island that stands in the lakeSlagvi stands beside the lakeshore in the vast cavern, deep in thought.Talk to Slagvi beside the lake in GloomingtarnThe Wakening Stone stands in the middle of the lake in Gloomingtarn.Cross to the island and find the White Stone Forge and the Black Stone AnvilIt is said that Durin himself constructed the White Stone Forge and the Black Stone Anvil in the days after he first awoke.Examine the White Stone Forge on the island in the lakeSlagvi has come to the Stone of Wakening, and he is not happy.Talk to Slagvi on the Stone of Wakening'We will find the entrance to Gloomingtarn beyond the Orc-infested cavern of Deepscrave, to the west. Let us journey there and see if the warding-runes have kept the cultists from gaining entrance to that sacred site.''We will find the entrance to Gloomingtarn beyond the Orc-infested cavern of Deepscrave, to the west. Let us journey there and see if the warding-runes have kept the cultists from gaining entrance to that sacred site.''I fear we may be too late.''I fear we may be too late, ${PLAYER}. Examine the warding runes and tell me what you see.''I fear we may be too late. Examine the warding runes and tell me what you see.''It is as I feared: they have somehow modified the runes, sapping them of their power. They are now only ordinary stones, and Gloomingtarn lies open to the cultists, that they may walk where they will, and spoil what they wish.

'We must follow them inside, and teach them they are not welcome! Let us enact the vengeance of Stóthkell, and of all the dwarves who revere this place, upon the intruders!''We must follow the cultists inside, and teach them they are not welcome! Let us enact the vengeance of Stóthkell, and of all the dwarves who revere this place, upon the intruders!''This is the cavern where Durin the Deathless awoke, ${PLAYER}, first of all the dwarves. Do you see the island in the lake? <rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> across the water, and tell me what you see.''Do you see the island in the lake? <rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> across the water, and tell me what you see.''The island in the lake is called the Stone of Wakening, for it is said that Durin awoke there, first of all the dwarves. He built an anvil of black stone and a forge of white brick, and the sound of his hammer echoing over the water called forth the ancient fathers of the dwarves. They stood on the shore of the lake, observing his work.

'Stóthkell would have loved to stand here, ${PLAYER}. He spoke of it often, and my heart is aggrieved to know now that he never will.

'Let us cross to the Wakening Stone and see the black anvil and the white forge on his behalf. The bridge is just to the south.''Let us cross to the Wakening Stone and see the black anvil and the white forge on his behalf.''Let us cross to the Wakening Stone and see the black anvil and the white forge on his behalf.''I cannot believe this! The White Stone Forge is here, as it should be, but the Black Stone Anvil has been taken away by unknown villains! This is a grievous insult!

'Stóthkell would die of a broken heart had he lived to see it!'Slagvi has sworn vengeance upon the Angmarim cultists that removed the Black Stone Anvil from the island of Durin's awakening.Slagvi has demanded that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim as payment for their theft of the Black Stone Anvil.Defeat Angmarim in Gloomingtarn (${NUMBER}/101)Slagvi has demanded that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim as payment for their theft of the Black Stone Anvil.Defeat Angmarim in Gloomingtarn (6/101)Slagvi is standing on the Stone of Wakening, the island in the middle of the Gloomingtarn lake.Talk to Slagvi on the island in the lakeBósi and some other Longbeards have come to the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.Meet up with Bósi and the other Longbeards on the lakeshoreBósi is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.Talk to Bósi on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn'It must have been the cultists from Angmar! Did I say they would pay for their intrusion into Gloomingtarn? That was nothing compared to this insult! The villains who hauled away the Black Stone Anvil will suffer the wrath of the dwarves and all who call them friend! I will not sleep until those responsible are slain!

'You will aid me in this, yes? I ask that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim cultists in Gloomingtarn! That will show them the reach of our anger, and still it will only be the start!''The villains who hauled away the Black Stone Anvil will suffer the wrath of the dwarves and all who call them friend! I will not sleep until those responsible are slain!

'You will aid me in this, yes? I ask that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim cultists in Gloomingtarn! That will show them how serious we are!''The villains who hauled away the Black Stone Anvil will suffer the wrath of the dwarves and all who call them friend! I will not sleep until those responsible are slain!

'You will aid me in this, yes? I ask that you slay one hundred and one Angmarim cultists in Gloomingtarn! That will show them how serious we are!''We stand upon sacred ground, my friend.''I have decided... reluctantly... that such slaughter will not prove a salve for the hurt done my people, though the villains who stole the Black Stone Anvil deserve such dealings. Let us instead learn where they have taken it, that we may recover it and restore it to this sacred ground. Many more than one hundred and one cultists may fall before we accomplish this, and I will not weep for them.

'But I see that Bósi and his kin have arrived on the lakeshore. Let them know the Black Stone Anvil has been stolen, but tell them gently; they suffered a great deal in Moria, and this insult will grieve them no less than it does me.''I see that Bósi and his kin have arrived on the lakeshore. Let them know the Black Stone Anvil has been stolen, but tell them gently; they suffered a great deal in Moria, and this insult will grieve them no less than it does me.''We stand upon sacred ground, my friend.''I am saddened by the theft of the Black Stone Anvil, but I think we can recover it. Mark my words: forging-hammers will once again ring against it, echoing throughout the caverns of Gundabad. We will make certain of it, not only to honour Durin the Deathless who built it, but also for the memory of Stóthkell the Forge-master, who fell in Máttugard.

'My son thinks he knows where the Black Stone Anvil was taken.'After discovering that the Iron Crown have begun to capture and tame ukhrâsh, Hersegg has devised a plan to set the would-be pets of the Angmarim against them.Ukhrash-traps can be found at Lochan Dúv in Gloomingtarn.

Hersegg has asked you to free ukhrâsh from traps at Lochan Dúv in the hope that releasing them will hinder the plans of the Iron Crown in Gloomingtarn.Free ukhrâsh from traps at Lochan Dúv (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hersegg can be found in Gloomingtarn.

You have freed many ukhrâsh from traps at Lochan Dúv and sent the Iron Crown into disarray. You should talk to Hersegg.

<#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use her horn to call her to your side.</rgb>Talk to Hersegg'Do you see those traps, ${PLAYER}? It looks like those Men have been capturing the ukhrâsh to use them against us!

'I don't know how they've managed to control them, but it must be some old sorcerers' trick of Angmar. To actually tame an ukhrash? You might as well try to tame the sea!

'If we were to free the ukhrâsh, we might overwhelm them before they discover what's happening right under their noses! Come on!''Hah! That ought to teach them.

'If you treat ukhrâsh like that, you're bound to end up on the wrong end of their claws!'A group of goblins in Gloomingtarn has been seen acting in a very peculiar way.Influenced goblins can be found in northern Gloomingtarn.

You should defeat influenced goblins.Defeat influenced goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The entrance to the Den of Pughlak can be found in the Gloomingtarn.

You should further explore where the influenced goblins are camped.Further explore where the influenced goblins are campedComplete 'Den of Pughlak' on any difficulty.

Use the Instance Finder to enter the Den of Pughlak.Complete 'Den of Pughlak' on any difficultyOrti can be found at Watchers' Roost in the Gloomingtarn.

You should return to Watchers' Roost and talk to Orti.Talk to Orti'If you are busy with other matters, do not trouble yourself with what I am about to say, ${CLASS}.

'There is something peculiar across the tarn. I have spied a small band of goblins acting more strange than even goblins ought to act! They seem to wander up and down the shoreline in a trance. Perhaps they have an encampment in a nearby cave, and search the shore for something to eat?

'As I have said, if curiosity takes you across the lake to find answers, I am glad. There are certainly more important tasks at hand in the Gloomingtarn, however.''I was starting to wonder where you have gone off to? What did you find that had you across the tarn for such a length in time?!

'A giant toad had poisoned the goblins' minds?! I would have never guessed that to be the answer! All of your talk about this cavern of deep toads, and a broken, nameless shrine has me rethinking my curiosity, ${CLASS}.

