You have explored the Iron Crown encampment at Durthuzâram and recovered a scroll-case. You should return to Hersegg.'As I was saying, ${PLAYER}...

'Your companion, Spall, was quite determined to continue his survey, and so I allowed him to continue onward to Abkân'aban. However, I did not send him alone. Hersegg and a few of my warriors accompanied him northward to Lugun-nâla, the ancient span to the Stone of Wakening. I am certain our warriors are more than a match for the Iron Crown, but I grow concerned that more of these Men of Angmar are arriving in Gloomingtarn with each passing hour.

'As much as Spall may wish to continue his survey with you at his side, I am afraid I now have a greater need for your aid. I ask that you join Hersegg and my warriors at Lugun-nâla, ${PLAYER}. Do let Spall know that I regret depriving him of his companion, but I am certain he will understand.

'Be swift, my friend. The Iron Crown cannot be allowed to lay claim to Gloomingtarn!''Ah! There you are, ${PLAYER}!

'I was beginning to wonder if Lord Stormhammer forgot to mention where I'd gone, but no matter. Look out across the lake, my friend. Isn't Abkân'aban beautiful?'

Spall gestures to the massive island which rises out of the waters of Durthuzâram. His eyes are aglow with excitement and awe.

'It is the Stone of Wakening! It is said that it was upon those stones where Durin the Deathless first awoke—first of the Seven Fathers. What a sight to behold! Few Longbeards have been so fortunate to make such a pilgrimage, but would you accompany me?'

You tell Spall that Lord Stormhammer has asked you to aid Hersegg and the other warriors.

'I see. That is a shame, my friend, but I do understand. I shall continue my studies here then for a time before crossing the span, but I do hope you get to visit the Stone before you depart Gloomingtarn.''All right, ${PLAYER}. It's time we figured out just what the Iron Crown are after!

'Before you arrived, I spotted a small encampment to the north. It seems the Iron Crown have a few such camps leading down into Gloomingtarn from the Clovengap, but this one appears to be the largest of them—aside from Lochan Dúv. Although we haven't been able to recover any of them, I have seen the Angmarim of the Iron Crown carrying scroll-cases.

'If they didn't stop after stealing the Black Stone Anvil, who knows what else they might seek to pilfer? Scout the encampment to the north and see if you can't find one of those scroll-cases, ${PLAYER}. We've got to know what they're up to and what they've found!''What did you find, ${PLAYER}? Ah, give that here!'

Hersegg opens the scroll-case and begins reading the notes and research collected by the Iron Crown in Gloomingtarn.

'Oh, I don't like the sound of this at all!'After spying a mysterious shimmering in the tide-pools of Skelstrand on the western shore of Durthuzâram, Orti has become convinced that the dark lake conceals ancient treasures.Tide-pools can be found at Skelstrand in Gloomingtarn.

Orti has asked you to pan the tide-pools of Skelstrand for the source of a mysterious shimmer he spied from Watchers' Roost. You should pan the tide-pools of Skelstrand.Orti can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

Despite seeing the shimmers Orti described, panning the waters of Durthuzâram has not yielded anything. You should return to Orti.'Have you been down to the tide-pools at Skelstrand, ${PLAYER}? I haven't myself, but not for lack of trying. Those blasted ukhrâsh keep chasing me off every time I get close!

'You see, I swear I've seen something shimmering in those shallow tide-pools, but no one believes me! You don't doubt my eyes, though, do you?

'Here, take my pan, and go see for yourself. When you return with the hidden treasures of Durthuzâram, the others will see!''You saw it, right? So, what did you find?'

You tell Orti that you saw the faint shimmering in Durthuzâram, but panning the waters yielded nothing of note.

'A-ha! I may not have been exactly right, but I knew my eyes were not deceiving me. Perhaps it's some sort of illusion or enchantment set long ago by Durin or... dare I say, even the First Crafter!

