You decide to bring this trophy to Belga Defthand, a skilled taxidermist of the Longbeards, so that it might be preserved once Gundabad is reclaimed.'What have you brought me now?'

Belga Defthand inspects Gullush's legs closely, holding them up to the light at Steepset.

'Ah, this shall make a fine trophy! I shall preserve this rare find. There are many strange creatures living within the depths of Gundabad. Perhaps you will find them all!'After arriving at Zâram-mekhem, Spall has discovered that passage through Gloomingtarn is fraught with danger. Undaunted, however, Spall is determined to aid Hermáth Stormhammer's expedition and bear witness to the site where Durin the Deathless awoke in Mount Gundabad.Hersegg can be found at Zâram-mekhem in Gloomingtarn.

Spall hopes to join Lord Hermáth Stormhammer's expedition at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. You should talk to Hersegg on his behalf.Talk to Hersegg at Zâram-mekhemHersegg and Spall can be found at Zâram-mekhem in Gloomingtarn.

In exchange for your aid in combating the Orkish presence in Gloomingtarn, Hersegg has indicated that she is willing to escort Spall to Watchers' Roost. You should aid Hersegg and Spall.Aid Hersegg with 'Gorgar's Curse-breaker'Aid Spall with 'Echoes of the Ancestors'Watchers' Roost can be found in Gloomingtarn, along the thoroughfare between the Deepscrave and the Clovengap.

After hindering the Orcs encamped at Drúkala, Hersegg told you to join the rest of her grandfather's expedition at Watchers' Roost. You should travel to Watchers' Roost.Follow the thoroughfare through Gloomingtarn and travel to Watchers' RoostHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.

After arriving at Watchers' Roost, you have spotted Hermáth Stormhammer among the warriors of the Gabil'akkâ. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Watchers' Roost'It seems I had even more reason to send word to you than I first thought, ${PLAYER}.

'Do you see these runes, my friend? They read: "ALL MUST DEPART EXCEPT THE ELDEST HOUSE. DEATH AWAITS THE UNWELCOME." Not the most inviting, and for good reason! See what happens when some wicked Men render them powerless?

'Hersegg tells me that the Orcs' encampment lies directly in our path... or at least right beside it! As I am certain one as well-informed as you will have heard, Hersegg's grandfather, Lord Hermáth Stormhammer, has led an expedition into Gloomingtarn. Although it was said to have faced Orkish resistance upon passing through Zâram-mekhem, the Gabil'akkâ was able to secure a foothold deeper within the hallowed caverns—at an old overlook known as Watchers' Roost.

'That is where I wish to go, my friend. And now that you have come, perhaps Hersegg will finally allow me to begin my studies!''I must thank you for coming as soon as you did, ${PLAYER}. I have found myself in a bit of a bind.

'When my grandfather sent me to escort a new arrival to Watchers' Roost, I expected to find a capable warrior—not a lore-master of the Lonely Mountain. I mean him no insult, but a journey through the Ironfold is a much different task than the reclamation of the Mountain-home. I have no doubt that Spall means well, but as Prince Durin himself knows, the situation in Gloomingtarn is far more dire than we had hoped.

'The warding-runes were sapped of their ancient power by some fell artifact of Angmar, and without their protection, the Orcs and some wicked Men of the Iron Crown have invaded Gloomingtarn. Although we overcame the Orcs in our first encounter with them on our way to Watchers' Roost, they have bolstered their numbers from the Deepscrave and made camp at Drúkala.

'I am capable enough of escorting Spall on my own, but without some sort of distraction, I fear we will be waylaid by the Orcs before we reach our destination. As you might expect, Spall and I each have our own ideas of what might prove most effective in repelling the Orcs from Gloomingtarn. If you would combat the Orcs at Drúkala, I shall escort Spall and see that he can begin his studies in earnest at Watchers' Roost.

'And when you have finished with the Orcs, you should follow the thoroughfare and join us at the Roost. It is quite the sight to see, my friend!''Ah, it is good to see you, ${PLAYER}!

'Hersegg informed me that you would be along soon enough. I trust the Orcs have been dealt with for the moment?'

You tell Hermáth Stormhammer of your efforts to combat the Orcs at Drúkala.

'It will not stop them for long, I fear, but it has bought us time—and that is enough. For there is much to be done to reclaim Gloomingtarn, my friend, and I would not turn away one as skillful as yourself!'Much to the dismay of the Gabil'akkâ, the glass-spiders in Glittengrof have begun to prey upon unwelcome visitors—dwarf and goblin alike.Wriggling webs can be found in Glittengrof.

Vithin has asked you to aid in the rescue of several Longbeard guards who were captured by the glass-spiders now dwelling in Glittengrof. You should rescue the Longbeard guards.Rescue Longbeard guards from webs in Glittengrof (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Vithin can be found in Glittengrof in Gloomingtarn.

You have successfully rescued all of the Longbeard guards captured by the glass-spiders. You should return to Vithin.Talk to Vithin in Glittengrof'Before we realized what was happening, we were overrun. Although I managed to escape, several of my guards were dragged away and bound them in webs. I am ashamed that I could not rescue them myself, but if I had been captured, aid may have come too late.

'But now you are here, my friend! Would you aid me in rescuing my guards from the spiders' webs?

'I must admit, ${PLAYER}, these spiders are quite the sight. But as the survivors of the Iron Garrison have told me, they are no less dangerous than their cousins in Moria!''Very good, ${PLAYER}! It seems a shame that their webs aren't as crystalline as the spiders themselves or I'd be inclined to leave them up once we reclaim Gloomingtarn!

'I've ordered the guards you rescued back to Watchers' Roost. There is still much to be done, but I wager they've earned themselves a short rest!'The sacred Jewel of Adnâkh has been found.Rísti Graver can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti GraverRísti Graver can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti GraverPiles of muck can be found in Gloomingtarn.

You should sift through the muck for the Jewel of Adnâkh.Sift through the piles of muck (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Piles of muck can be found in Gloomingtarn.

You should sift through one last pile of muck for the Jewel of Adnâkh.Sift through one last pile of muckThe Jewel of Adnâkh can be found in Gloomingtarn.

You should collect the Jewel of Adnâkh.Collect the Jewel of AdnâkhThe Throne of Zidir-nesad can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard.

You should add the Jewel of Adnâkh to the Throne of Zidir-nesad under Rísti Graver's supervision.Rísti Graver can be found at Steepset in Máttugard.

You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti GraverRísti Graver, the greatest foreman of the Ironfold, has learned the location of the sacred Jewel of Adnâkh. While the jewel has been found, it will take a skilled hero to recover it and return it to the throne! You should seek out Rísti Graver as soon as you are able.'You have restored the Jewel of Adnâkh to its proper place! You did clean away the muck from it before setting it in the throne, I hope? Ah, I see it shining brightly there, of course you did.

'This jewel represents nature, not just the natural environment in which wild things grow but also the natural state of all beings, ${PLAYER}. It is the nature of the dwarves to persevere, and so we will, until all of Gundabad is made safe from our enemies. The light that shines from the Jewel of Adnâkh will remind us who we are and who we remain as we explore the deep places beneath Gundabad, and that is good.''Word has reached us here at the Steepset that the sacred Jewel of Adnâkh was recently dredged up in Gloomingtarn, unbeknownst to the goblins doing the dredging! I ask you to locate the jewel and retrieve it before the sacred stone becomes lost once more!'Angmarim have been spotted skulking about the western tiers of Skarashulg, in Clovengap.Angmarim can be found in south-west Clovengap.

Gunvald has asked for you to defeat the Angmarim who are among the Wargs in south-west Clovengap.Defeat Angmarim in south-west Clovengap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Afárr is in Hagbuth, in the south-eastern Clovengap.

You should tell Afárr you defeated the Angmarim.Talk to Afárr in Hagbuth'I am glad to hear that you are helping Mother Amma with the Warg problem. My scouts report Angmarim among the upper tiers as well.

'Do what you can to lessen their foothold among the forests of Clovengap and then report to Afárr in Hagbuth, across the river. He shall reward you for your time and efforts.''${PLAYER}, is it? I am Afárr. Welcome to Hagbuth. Not much to look at now, but we have driven the enemy soundly from this part of the tier.

'Excellent work. It seems the tales about you are true.'Klátha's heart has turned against Nósni, but he's not ready to give up.Klátha is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar.

Nósni has asked you to speak to Klátha once more.Talk to KláthaNósni is located in a garden north of Bazanmanar.

You should talk to Nósni.Talk to NósniThe fireworks are located in a garden north of Bazanmanar.

You should light the fireworks.Light the fireworksNósni is located in a garden north of Bazanmanar.

You should talk to Nósni.Talk to NósniKlátha is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar.

Nósni has asked you to speak to Klátha for a final time.'This is all my fault. I have a very good reason for having had Klátha stationed here, and it has naught to do with whether she can defend herself. However... well, I suppose I never shared with her that reason.

'My friend, if you would help me once more, please tell Klátha that I am sorry, and if she will gaze towards the river, she will understand why I asked she be moved to this camp.

'After you speak with her, come find me in the gardens below.''You again?'

You give Klátha the message from Nósni.

'Look towards the river? Hmm. I suppose I can do that. Not that it will matter, of course. But I suppose I can.''Hello, hello! Now the truth will out. You see, I know that Klátha's favourite thing is fireworks. I arranged to purchase special ones from Feredis of Minas Tirith herself!

'I have been waiting for the right moment to set them alight for Klátha. I had her moved here so she wouldn't miss the display, but... well, the delivery was very late and... oh. I can of course see how she would think I was trying to protect her. It was supposed to be a surprise, but... well, I suppose things have dragged on with no real news from me. I was so focused on my plan that I lost sight of how confusing my actions must have been.

'Well, will you help me light these fireworks? It may not be enough to redeem myself, but I have to try.''Oh, ${PLAYER}. That was spectacular! And probably the first time fireworks have ever graced these halls. If that did not win her love, at least may it grant me her forgiveness. Would... would you check on her for me? See whether I am allowed to speak with her again?''Welcome back, friend. Yes, yes. I saw the display. And one of the merchants came by to apologize to Nósni for the late shipment. Nósni had me moved here for the spectacular view, did he not? He has always been so thoughtful in his deeds, but foolish with the timeliness of his words.

'Hmmm. They were quite the thing, weren't they. I suppose I might find it in my heart to forgive him.'Slime and unnatural plants choke the once-majestic fountains about Bazanmanar.The foetid fountain pools are located near Bazanmanar.

Golodhril has asked you to bring her samples of the plants from the foetid pools.Collect plant samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golodhril is located in Bazanmanar.

You should bring the plant samples to Golodhril.Kurdushâlak runs the length of Clovengap.

Golodhril has asked you to collect clay from the banks of Kurdushâlak.Collect clay from KurdushâlakGolodhril is located in Bazanmanar.

You should bring the clay to Golodhril.Bring the clay to GolodhrilGolodhril's workbench is located in Bazanmanar.

You should mix the clay with the ingredients in the mortar on Golodhril's workbench.The foetid pools are located near Bazanmanar.

Golodhril has asked you to add drops of the antidote to the foetid pools.Treat foetid pools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golodhril is located in Bazanmanar.

You should give Golodhril the good news.'At the bottom of the nearby stairs, there are multiple fountains whose pools are clogged with something foetid and foul. Go and fetch me some of the plants, that I might study them with my own eyes.''You bring plants from the pools? Ech, smells almost as bad those sarrowstones Mother Amma is forever crushing. Give it here then, let me see.

'It is as I expected. The plants are indeed causing the pools to turn sour. Fortunately, I know the remedy! Go on down to Kurdushâlak, the river what cuts through the centre of the gap. On its banks, you will find clay. Bring the clay to me and we shall craft an antidote for the pools.''Did you fall in? Do you have the clay?'

You show her the wet clay.

'Excellent! This will serve perfectly. Take the clay to the workbench and mix it with the ingredients in the mortar. When you are done, add a few drops to the pools and the waters shall run clear once more!

'Ah - if you do not mind, that is. My sister has informed me that I am not to order you around.''You finished cleaning the pools? Wonderful! It is essential that the dwarves have clean drinking water, lest their conquest of this place continue to draw out.'Within the crumbling ruins of Clovengap lie pulsing nests, full of wasp larvae.The wasp hive can be found in south-western Clovengap.

Borghild has asked you to deal with the wasp infestation in the nearby ruins.Destroy wasp nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Clovengap fire-flies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Clovengap hornets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Borghild is in western Clovengap.

You should let Borghild know that you have completed the task of defeating the wasps.Return to Borghild'Hail, ${CLASS}. We meet again, and what fortuitous timing you have.

'North of here are some old ruins which have been overrun with wasps. As you know, my eyes are my weapons. I implore you - take care of as many of the insects as you can, and put their nests to the torch.''Excellently done! We make a good team, eh?'Caches of foul-smelling crystals have been hidden in the overgrown forests of Clovengap.Caches of corrupted crystals can be found in central Clovengap.

You should destroy any caches of sarrowstone crystals you come across.Destroy crystal caches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mother Amma is in Bazanmanar in north-eastern Clovengap.

You should let Mother Amma know you have taken care of the crystals.Return to Mother Amma'Most of the journal makes little sense, but this page here mentions a stash of… hmm, they must have no word for what he was trying to say. Stench rock? Oh, this phrase means something to you?

'Go on then, do what you need with your rocks, and give me some time to translate the rest of these ramblings.''Bless me, the stench you carry could shear the beard off Durin himself.'Bori of the Iron Garrison thinks the Angmarim may have hauled the Black Stone Anvil out of Gloomingtarn, and if you hurry you may be able to find and retrieve the ancient artifact before they do it some harm.Bori is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.Talk to Bori on the lakeshoreBróin is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.Talk to Bróin on the lakeshoreFastrith is on the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn.Talk to Fastrith on the lakeshoreBori is waiting by the lakeshore in Gloomingtarn for you to agree to his plan.Talk to Bori by the lakeshore and travel with him in search of the Black Stone AnvilBósi is in Clovengap, north-east of the tunnel to Gloomingtarn.Talk to Bósi in Clovengap, north-east of the tunnel to Gloomingtarn'Bori believes it must have been hauled on ropes north to Clovengap, although the purpose for which the cultists would put it remains a mystery to him, and to me.

'Hear him and see if you agree.''Hear what Bori has to say and see if you agree, friend. I think he is right on this.''It is no easy matter to move such a thing, ${PLAYER}, and legend says of the Black Stone Anvil that it was heavier than other such tools. That solidity imbued weapons hammered upon it with similar qualities, and it is said that no weapon Durin ever crafted upon the Black Stone Anvil and in the White Stone Forge could be turned away, unless it be by armour forged from the same.

'If the Angmarim have taken it, they must have taken it across the lake by boat, and hauled it north on ropes into Clovengap. We would have seen signs of its passage had they dared take it south or east, and we did not. I suggest we investigate Clovengap, and perhaps we will learn for what purpose the cultists sought to steal such a relic of our history.

'Is my cousin with us? Will Bróin consent to leave Fastrith behind? This expedition will be dangerous.''Clovengap is bound to be dangerous, and each member of this expedition would do well to heed it.''I see no reason to leave Fastrith behind if she is willing to risk the dangers. If Bori were to look around him, he would see no sign of hearth or home nearby... we are far from the Lonely Mountain, and I say Fastrith has already proven herself more than his equal in courage!'

Bróin's eyes flash dangerously, and you wonder for how long this declaration has been brewing.'I have said my say.''I hear you, cousin, and I insist that I meant no disrespect.''I think I will come along. After all, if I do not keep Bróin from stumbling into the dangers that wait for him in that direction, who will do so? There is also the matter of my apprenticeship: I have not yet searched Clovengap for the Zabad'ibîn sought by my master, and it is only a matter of time before he gets it into his head that they must surely lie within.

'Lead on, I say!''I did not mean to offend, and I hope I have not. Let us all remain friends as we venture into Clovengap!'

Bori lowers his voice and speaks only to you.

'They cannot be helped, ${PLAYER}. He is smitten beyond aid, and she is reckless to a fault. I do not know which is more hopeless! We will have to keep our eyes on them as we adventure, for their safety, and ours! Anyway... onward!''How can I fear to adventure in Clovengap when I have not yet seen it? It could be lovely!''Bori should not speak of what he does not understand. It is a fault of his!''The wargs will return, and in greater numbers. We must remain cautious while we set up camp, and be ready for anything.'The Longbeards of the Iron Garrison comb the gardens of Akrakír for the missing Black Stone Anvil, hoping to find the ancient artifact before it is put to some terrible purpose by their enemies.Bósi has asked you to search a number of locations within Clovengap for the missing Black Stone Anvil, and to defeat the wargs charged with protecting the area from intruders.Defeat wargs in Clovengap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Investigate the old vineyard of MaranazhârInvestigate the sounds coming from Dashat-zaharInvestigate the Angmarim presence at GaranashmarBósi is at his camp not far from the south-western entrance to Clovengap.Talk to Bósi in Clovengap'While we work, perhaps you can quiet some of the warg-voices that trouble the stillness, ${PLAYER}. Ránulur's brothers and sisters will not abandon their efforts to avenge him upon us; would we, in their position? You know we would not.

'I ask that you also keep your eyes open for the missing Black Stone Anvil, or some sign of its passage. Be not blinded by the beauty of the once-verdant ladder-gardens! We are here for a purpose, and should see it done.'

Bósi chuckles.

'I know you would not be distracted so, ${PLAYER}. I was speaking more to myself than to you. Not since Khazad-dûm have I seen such beautiful terraces, and... ah, it does not matter. Good fortune go with you, my friend. When you return perhaps we will know where next to search.''Quiet some of the warg-voices that trouble the stillness, and also keep your eyes open for the missing Black Stone Anvil, or some sign of its passage.''You are back, and sooner than I expected! What did your explorations teach you of this place? Was there any sign of the object of our search?'Bósi is concerned about the frozen northern reaches of Clovengap, and believes you should investigate to learn if it has become a lair for Hrímil Frost-heart.The northern reaches of Clovengap may have become home to Hrímil Frost-heart, and Bósi wants you to investigate... carefully. He suggested you make your way through Frósthel on the left side of the Ladder-gardens to reach the frozen river-bed.Investigate the frozen reaches of Clovengap, to the north-westA disorganized array of Orkish footprints has drawn your attention.Examine the booted footprints in the icy channelBósi is in the south-west portion of Clovengap, waiting to hear what you learned during your investigation of the frozen reaches.Talk to Bósi in the south-western portion of ClovengapBróin has called for your attention in Clovengap.Talk to Bróin in ClovengapBróin asked to meet with you atop the terrace to the west, a short distance away from the others.Talk to Bróin atop the terrace to the west, in ClovengapBróin has asked to see the red pebble you found.'It seems the northern reaches of Clovengap have been iced over and frozen, a sure sign Hrímil Frost-heart has chosen that place for her lair, or that she has spent time there for another reason. What that might be I cannot guess, but I deem it important we learn what we can of it!

'Investigate that frozen place and keep a close eye for any clues that might shed light upon her intentions in Clovengap! Did the Angmarim bring the Black Stone Anvil there, hoping to present it to the dragon? I cannot see what use she might have for it, but the minds of dragons have always been impenetrable to the dwarves, and to me in particular!

'To reach the frozen river-bed in the northern reaches of Clovengap, make your way through Frósthel on the left side of the Ladder-gardens.''Investigate that frozen place and keep a close eye for any clues that might shed light upon the dragon's intentions in Clovengap.

'To reach the frozen river-bed in the northern reaches of Clovengap, make your way through Frósthel on the left side of the Ladder-gardens.''Investigate that frozen place and keep a close eye for any clues that might shed light upon the dragon's intentions in Clovengap.''You found the prints of Orkish boots in the snow outside the rimed passage? That tells me that Gorgar's Orcs may speak with Hrímil Frost-heart from time to time... and that is not good for the Gabil'akkâ.

'But I cannot say I know the significance of this red pebble you found. It was crushed beneath an Orkish heel? Perhaps that means it is of no significance to our enemies either, and will at least pose us no danger.

'I will need to think about this. And still no sign of the Black Stone Anvil!''Hmm. Why should the Orcs meet with the dragon? Do they hatch some plan to push the Gabil'akkâ back out of Gundabad?''Can we talk, ${PLAYER}? No, not here. Let us meet... over there, atop the terrace to the west.''Thank you for agreeing to speak with me.''Yes, my friend, this is perfect!'

He catches himself abruptly and lowers his voice, looking nervously toward the rest of your party.

'Thank you for agreeing to speak with me, ${PLAYER}. I do not know if you noticed, but I have become quite fond of Fastrith, and I have been trying to put together a present for her, a sign of my affection.'

You assure Bróin that you had noticed, and so had everyone else, except perhaps Fastrith herself. He grumbles something that you don't quite make out.

'I thought I might find one or all of the Zabad'ibîn for her, but the more we adventured in Gundabad the less likely that began to seem to me. Instead I have been trying to collect enough colourful stones with which she could finish the mosaic in Zul-mazal. Do you think she would like that? I have been picking up likely pebbles wherever I find them, and this one appears just right.'Bróin has noticed that the foes of the Gabil'akkâ often pick up these coloured stones scattered throughout Gundabad, and he thinks you might help him with his own goal while still helping the overall effort of his people.Bróin has asked you to collect any colourful stones you find from the enemies you face on behalf of the Gabil'akkâ throughout Gundabad.Collect blue stones from enemies in Gloomingtarn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect red stones from enemies in Clovengap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect green stones from enemies in Deepscrave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect yellow stones from enemies in the Pit of Stonejaws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect black stones from enemies in Câr Bronach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect white stones from enemies in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bróin is at Maergrind in Máttugard, eager to see how many stones you were able to find.Durin is at Maergrind in Máttugard.Talk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard'I am not the only one who has found these pebbles to be of interest! Many of the enemies we have faced in Gundabad also seem attracted to the colourful stones, and I have noticed that some of them carry such pebbles on their persons as they travel on their various errands through every region of the caves.

'Could you collect for me such of these pebbles as you can find, ${PLAYER}? Do not go out of your way for them, but as you complete tasks for Prince Durin and defeat the foes of the Gabil'akkâ, search their bodies for suitable colourful stones and add them to the pouch in which I collect them. It will be easy, and you will be helping not only the Gabil'akkâ but also your good friend Bróin! It is not just one excellent purpose... but two!

'Thank you, my friend. I will owe you a favour for each pebble you find! Is that not worth something? I will meet you in Máttugard when you have filled the pouch with stones.''Could you collect for me such of these pebbles as you can find, ${PLAYER}? Do not go out of your way for them, but as you complete tasks for Prince Durin and defeat the foes of the Gabil'akkâ, search their bodies for suitable colourful stones and add them to the pouch in which I collect them. It will be easy, and you will be helping not only the Gabil'akkâ but also your good friend Bróin! It is not just one excellent purpose... but two!

'Thank you, my friend. I will owe you a favour for each pebble you find! Is that not worth something? I will meet you in Máttugard when you have filled the pouch with stones.''Perfect! I can tell from the heft of this pouch that you found many of the stones I sought, and indeed you have found more than any of the others who gathered pebbles for me!

'Aye, I asked some others to gather colourful stones, ${PLAYER}. Did you think you were the only one? It is such a large mosaic, and so many stones are missing! But you are my favourite, and have done the best, good ${RACE}.

'Perhaps you should check in with Prince Durin? There was quite a commotion a short time ago. I think something has happened.''You have come back at just the right time, ${PLAYER}.

'While you were away... my guards caught a prisoner.'The Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ have caught a goblin sneaking around Máttugard, and now he is their prisoner.Eskil and Trausti are keeping watch over the captive goblin north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.The goblin Glúrkub has been imprisoned by the Gabil'akkâ.Talk to Glúrkub, the captive goblin north of MaergrindTrausti is keeping watch over the captive goblin north of Maergrind.Talk to Trausti north of MaergrindThe goblin Glúrkub has given you information concerning the hobgoblin who took Trausti's axe, but can he be trusted? According to Glúrkub, the hobgoblin can be found living in a dwelling south-east of the fortress of Shakhajât.Trausti stands south-east of the fortress of Shakhajât, pleased to have retrieved his axe.Talk to Trausti in ShakhajâtDurin is keeping an eye on the captive goblin north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.Talk to Durin north of Maergrind in MáttugardThe goblin Glúrkub is encaged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.Talk to the goblin Glúrkub north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard'Our captive is a goblin of Gundabad. The guards caught him creeping in the shadows near the Steepset, no doubt on an errand of evil for Gorgar. He would have been slain out of hand if he had not been recognized, but that recognition will only stay the executioner's axe for a short while.

'They have him in a cage north of Maergrind, down one level. Speak to those who watch him, and perhaps he will tell us something of use. We have no need for goblins, but our need is even less if they can tell us nothing.''They have our goblin prisoner in a cage north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard. Speak to those who watch him, and perhaps he will tell us something of use. We have no need for goblins, but our need is even less if they can tell us nothing.''I know this goblin, ${PLAYER}. Do you remember when Stáli the Hewer sent me into Deepscrave in search of the Zabad'ibîn, and I was captured by the Orcs? This goblin was my jailor! He it was that kept the hobgoblins from killing me! And then you and Trausti freed me from that place.

'The guards were not happy, but I convinced them he seemed a figure of importance. They have jailed him, for now, but they are not happy about it! In truth I am not sure myself. Is this some trick?''Eskil prevailed upon the guards to spare this goblin's life, for now, but I am less forgiving. One of his friends made off with my favourite axe, the one bearing Lofrík's golden tooth, and the loss of that precious memento has me inclined to take this goblin's head in payment!''This goblin kept me captive in Vatug-ronk, but he also kept his friends from visiting death upon me. Why would he creep so near to the Gabil'akkâ?''That was no ordinary axe, ${PLAYER}, and this goblin is responsible for its theft! He should die for its loss.''The axe! The axe! I knew it was important, I did! Something special about it? Glúrkub knows where it is! Maybe let him free if you find it?

'Hobgoblin who took the axe very mean, very nasty, bad sort. But Glúrkub knows where he lives! In Shakhajât, that's the place. Knock on his door south-east of the fortress proper! And when Shoshraf answers, take the axe right from him!

'Then you'll know Glúrkub is a very helpful goblin, and you'll set him free? Ah, we'll talk when you get back, yes we will. Think about it? You'll think about it.''Hobgoblin who took the axe very mean, very nasty, bad sort. But Glúrkub knows where he lives! In Shakhajât, that's the place. Knock on his door south-east of the fortress, and when he answers, take the axe right from him!''Do you suspect a trap, as I do? Good ${RACE}! We will see about this hobgoblin, but if the captive has lied to us, we will come back at once and separate his head from his shoulders!

'Shakhajât, he said? Let us go knock on the doors, ${PLAYER}, and woe to the hobgoblin that answers!''Shakhajât, he said? Let us go knock on the doors, ${PLAYER}, and woe to the hobgoblin that answers!''By Durin's Beard, he was telling the truth! It feels good to have my axe back in hand, ${PLAYER}, for once again I feel that Lofrík is with me, though he died outside Moria. What was wrong has been set right, though it took a goblin's help! What would Lofrík say to that, I wonder?

'He would say that a bad deed is not entirely undone by a good one, ${PLAYER}. Let us bear that in mind when we return to the prisoner.''What was wrong has been set right, though it took a goblin's help! What would Lofrík say to that, I wonder? He would say that a bad deed is not entirely undone by a good one! Let us bear that in mind when we return to the prisoner.''Trausti has his axe again? That is good, ${PLAYER}, but I caution you and any others who speak to the prisoner not to trust everything he says. He may mix truths in with falsehoods in order to mislead us... indeed, I would expect nothing else.

'And yet, if we bear that in mind he may provide the Gabil'akkâ with useful information. Ask him where he came from, and why he was creeping around near the Steepset.''Our prisoner may mix truths in with falsehoods to mislead us.''It was just as I said, wasn't it? Yes, it was, I can tell! Glúrkub will be so very helpful to you, as long as you keep him safe.

'Yes, safe! Safe from both dwarves and Orcs! Do you agree? Think about it? Think about it. And then I will tell you my tale.'The goblin Glúrkub has a tale to tell, but whether or not he can be trusted is up to you and to the Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ.The goblin Glúrkub wants to tell you his side of the story. He is caged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.Talk to the prisoner and experience 'The Divided Loyalties of Glúrkub the Goblin'Glúrkub is caged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.Talk to GlúrkubPrince Durin is furious, enraged with Glúrkub's story.Talk to Durin by the cage'My tale is a long one, yes, long and sad. But you will hear it, yes? You will see it? Put yourself in my shoes, walk around and see from my side?

'Maybe then you will know Glúrkub tells the truth, and Glúrkub can be trusted?

'Maybe then you let me go?''My story begins before your army came to Urbhármok, before this war of the dwarves. Hear it now, and know Glúrkub not to blame. Glúrkub just doing his best.''That is my tale, and every word of it is true. Every word! Now you trust Glúrkub? Now you let him go?''I swear it is all true!''The lies of this goblin cannot be believed!'

Durin's face is a thundercloud. He is angrier than you have ever seen him.

'I have not been controlled by the voice of Hrímil Frost-heart! I am no dragon's puppet!'Durin is beside himself with rage at Glúrkub's story, and refuses to believe that he has been made a dragon's puppet.Durin has ordered you to kill the goblin prisoner.Kill GlúrkubGlóin is standing by the cage, eyeing Durin warily.Talk to Glóin by the cageDurin is furious at the words of Glúrkub and at Glóin's betrayal of his commands.Talk to Durin by the cageDurin has calmed himself somewhat, but the prince still disbelieves the goblin's story.Talk to Durin by the cageGlóin is by the cage in Máttugard.Talk to Glóin by the cageGlúrkub is encaged in Máttugard.Talk to GlúrkubDurin is by the cage holding Glúrkub.Talk to Durin by the cage'Lies, all of them lies! This goblin claims that I am under Hrímil Frost-heart's control, obeying her command to reclaim Gundabad? Impossible! Unthinkable!

'${PLAYER}! I command you to slay this goblin where he stands!''You will obey my order! Slay him where he stands!''The goblin is our prisoner, my prince. He is helpless, and cannot be killed in this fashion.

'It is beneath you to command ${PLAYER} to do this, Durin.''A cage can be arranged for you as well, Glóin, and for all who speak against me! Your age will not save you from captivity, or from cruel treatment! I am your prince!

'Do you question that I am Durin the Seventh? For no Durin could ever be subject to Dragon-compulsion! If you believe the lies of this goblin, you deny the very foundation upon which this conquest is based!

'Speak now, Glóin! Speak, and seal your fate!''It cannot be true. It cannot.'

Durin breathes heavily, studying the faces of the dwarves nearby, his brow creased in thought.

'Gorgar asked "are you the same as I am?" What did he mean by that? What did he see? Did he recognize some compulsion in me, a compulsion he shares? Have we both been ensnared by the Dragon's voice?''My prince, I am sorry. If you deem my words worthy of punishment, I will accept it without objection. You are my prince, and if I live to see it you will be my king when your father no longer rules in Erebor.

'You are Durin the Seventh, and no Dragon-trick can change that. I will follow wherever you lead.''It is true: when Hrímil says "time to jump," Gorgar says "how high you want?" But maybe she not trust her power over him. She summons Gorgar not to her lair, but to another place, called Lugroz by the Orcs.

'When he go see her, she make him leave fancy hammer behind. She scared of it, for some reason. Glúrkub not know why: hammer small, but Dragon very big! But she not like it. He leave it on weapon-rack near path to the summit, and when he done meeting with her he come down mountain and take it back. Any who dare touch it would die by Gorgar's hand, but none have because none risk it!'Durin's breath still comes in ragged hitches, but he has for the moment mastered the fury that so seized him. He glowers at the encaged goblin with undisguised hatred, but now his expression contains something else: curiosity.

'If Hrímil has the power to command Gorgar, why would she not allow him to wield the mithril hammer in her presence? She cannot fear he would use it against her, not unless she doubted her hold upon him. Does she fear the mithril hammer itself? That is very interesting, ${PLAYER}, and I see in it an opportunity.

'Let this guide our next move. It will be dangerous, but it may yield treasure commensurate with the risk.'Durin thinks you should investigate the Welkin-lofts and see what you can learn about the relationship between Gorgar the Ruthless and Hrímil Frost-heart.Orcs prowl the Welkin-lofts, and Durin has asked you to defeat those you find there.Defeat Orcs in the Welkin-lofts (${NUMBER}/6)Orcs prowl the Welkin-lofts, and Durin has asked you to defeat those you find there.Defeat Orcs in the Welkin-lofts (5/6)The path to the summit can be found atop a snow-covered terrace in the south-eastern heights of the Welkin-lofts.Find the path to the summit in the south-east heights of the Welkin-loftsA weapon rack stands by the path to the summit, as Glúrkub described.Examine the weapon rack by the path to the summitYou need to find a hiding place nearby! Perhaps one could be found in the stand of trees to the north-west.Find a hiding place nearby, perhaps in the stand of trees to the north-westDurin is north of Maergrind and down one level, by the cage holding Glúrkub in Máttugard.Talk to Durin by the cage north of Maergrind, in MáttugardGlúrkub is encaged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard.Talk to Glúrkub in Máttugard'The Orcs may call it Lugroz, but to us those high places are known as the Welkin-lofts. Climb up there, slaying any of the Orcs you encounter, and see if the path to the summit is as Glúrkub described.

'If there is no such weapon-rack, we will know his story for what it is: full of lies. But if he does tell the truth, and there is such a place for Gorgar to leave the mithril hammer when he is summoned by the Dragon... well, in that case, see if there is a hiding place nearby. I may have the beginning of a plan.''Climb to the Welkin-lofts, slaying any Orcs you encounter, and see if the path to the summit is as Glúrkub described. If there is a place for Gorgar to leave the mithril hammer when he is summoned by the Dragon... well, in that case, see if there is a hiding place nearby. I may have the beginning of a plan.''Climb to the Welkin-lofts, slaying any Orcs you encounter, and see if the path to the summit is as Glúrkub described. If there is a place for Gorgar to leave the mithril hammer when he is summoned by the Dragon... well, in that case, see if there is a hiding place nearby. I may have the beginning of a plan.''Climb to the Welkin-lofts, slaying any Orcs you encounter, and see if the path to the summit is as Glúrkub described. If there is a place for Gorgar to leave the mithril hammer when he is summoned by the Dragon... well, in that case, see if there is a hiding place nearby. I may have the beginning of a plan.''Climb to the Welkin-lofts, slaying any Orcs you encounter, and see if the path to the summit is as Glúrkub described. If there is a place for Gorgar to leave the mithril hammer when he is summoned by the Dragon... well, in that case, see if there is a hiding place nearby. I may have the beginning of a plan.''Climb to the Welkin-lofts, slaying any Orcs you encounter, and see if the path to the summit is as Glúrkub described. If there is a place for Gorgar to leave the mithril hammer when he is summoned by the Dragon... well, in that case, see if there is a hiding place nearby. I may have the beginning of a plan.''So it is as Glúrkub said? Then we will proceed with the plan.

'It is this: when next Gorgar goes to meet with the Dragon, you and Glúrkub will steal the mithril hammer from the weapon rack when Gorgar leaves it behind. If the goblin carries out his part in the plan, I will release him. In this way he will earn his freedom, and we will deprive Gorgar of his most deadly weapon, the hammer with which he slew Stóthkell and so many others.

'Can you accomplish this, ${PLAYER}? I trust no other with this important task.''This is the plan. When next Gorgar goes to meet with the Dragon, you and Glúrkub will steal the mithril hammer from the weapon rack when Gorgar leaves it behind. If the goblin carries out his part in the plan, I will release him. In this way he will earn his freedom, and we will deprive Gorgar of his most deadly weapon, the hammer with which he slew Stóthkell and so many others.''I already told the important dwarf I agree to the bargain. What else would I do? Think about it? No one likes a cage, goblin or dwarf. And I know, because I used to close the cages and not open them! But that's not important now, no it isn't. I have been so helpful, haven't I?

'Glúrkub can command Gorgar's Orcs to leave the fancy hammer undefended. It will be easy, you will see. And then freedom for Glúrkub!'Glúrkub and Durin have come to an arrangement by which the goblin can earn his freedom, but only if he provides the Gabil'akkâ with trustworthy aid and information.Glúrkub is encaged north of Maergrind and down one level, in Máttugard, prepared to undertake his end of the bargain.Talk to Glúrkub and travel with him to the Welkin-loftsDurin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, having fulfilled his end of the agreement with Glúrkub.Talk to Durin at Maergrind, in Máttugard'The Dragon calls Gorgar to meet with her almost every night since she came to the mountain. If we go now, we might be ready for next audience! No sense waiting... and not just because cage is cramped!''Time to go? Yes, time to go, don't want to be late. Glúrkub spent enough time in cage. Too much!''I did not want to hear the words of Glúrkub, ${PLAYER}, for they made me question many things I had long taken for granted. I thought the desire to reclaim Gundabad slept within the breast of any Longbeard; how could it not? To hear that the voice of a Dragon might have commanded it of me... I could not believe it.

'But it is one thing to hear a command, and it is another to obey. Hrímil may think she motivated the dwarves to strike against Gundabad too soon, the easier for her to destroy us, but she did not. It was the voice of a dwarf that I heard beyond the Anvil of Winterstith, ${PLAYER}, a dwarf-voice that drowned out the words of the Dragon. I will listen to that voice, and no other, and it spoke of victory in Gundabad.

'Depriving Gorgar of this mithril hammer is simply the first step. Next we will deprive him of his armies, and then we will take his life. And then we will come for his Dragon-master. She fears this hammer? Then let it be her undoing!'Beneath the crumbling arches of ancient vineyards prowls a deadly beast. Has the corruption of the sarrowstones spread to this already formidable foe?Nósni is located in Hagbuth.

Mother Amma has asked you to speak to Nósni.Talk to NósniClovengap mist-stalkers and sabre-tooth cats can be found in the vineyards in eastern Clovengap.

Mother Amma has asked you to look into whether the Angmarim have managed to corrupt the sabre-tooth cats that prowl Maranazhâr.Search for signs of corruptionDeadly sabre-cats prowl the Maranazhâr vineyards in eastern Clovengap.

Look for more clues as to whether the Angmarim have managed to corrupt the sabre-tooth cats.Continue searching for signs of corruptionIn the crumbling vineyards of Maranazhâr, you have discovered an Angmarim waggon.

The Angmarim have intentions of creating abominations out of the already fierce sabre-tooth cats! You should defeat the Angmarim!Examine the waggonThe Angmarim experiments were going to take place in the vineyards.

With the Angmarim sorceress Iuvár defeated, you should look for clues about their experiments.Search for cluesMother Amma is in Hagbuth, in south-eastern Clovengap.

You should tell Mother Amma what you found in the vineyards.'The journal you found is full of the rantings of a mad man. It will take me some time to unravel what he has been up to, but I was able to make out that he has been placing more of his crystals around other creatures in the Gap, in hopes of afflicting them with the same power and madness.'

She shows you a page of the book.

'Look here. That is no Warg, but a sabre-tooth! ${PLAYER}, you must find the crystals and destroy them. We need not make sword-mouthed cats even more dangerous. Speak to Nósni, about where the beasts are lurking.''What have you found?''Aye, I have seen the creatures of which you speak. They glide in and out of the mists like unholy shadows, striking with talons and fangs the size of my arms! Be careful if you go pursuing those cats. You will find them north of here, among the crumbling arches of the old vineyards.'This appears to be an account of the sorceress Iuvár's attempts at using the crystals on the sabre-tooth cats of Clovengap.

'We are being sent back to the vineyards with more crystals. Bruidalg insists I keep trying, no matter how many of my underlings the blasted cats devour. He gave me an adjustment to the ritual at least, so perhaps this time we shall have more luck.'

As you flip through the pages, a familiar looking piece of torn paper flutters loose.The torn fragments have been pieced together to form a map! But there is yet one more piece to this puzzle....Tuzugrák and the hobgolins can be found holed up in Anatrâd.

Lore-master Rúni has asked you to defeat Tuzugrák and his hobgoblin captains, and to bring back the stolen candle.Defeat hobgoblin captains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat TuzugrákRecover the candleLore-master Rúni is in Bazanmanar, in the north-east Clovengap.

You should bring the candle to Rúni.'The fragments you brought me are most assuredly a map, but it seems there is yet one more piece to this puzzle. This passage here mentions an ensorcelled candle whose flame is used to find a hidden door. Sadly, the candle seems to have been stolen by a hobgoblin leader named Tuzugrák.

'Tuzugrák and his ilk are holed up in Anatrâd, the ruins north of here. Go, retrieve the candle, and defeat Tuzugrák and his captains.''Excellent work, friend. Not only have you retrieved the candle, but you have put a sizable dent in the enemy's forces! Well done, well done.'The Angmarim sorcerers are experimenting on their own people with the corrupted sarrowstone crystals.The Angmarim priest can be found in north-western Clovengap.

You should find and defeat the priest who is working to corrupt the deserting Angmarim.Defeat CrágachaMother Amma is in Bazanmanar, in north-east Clovengap.

You should bring the new fragment to Mother Amma.'I know not why I am always surprised and horrified anew by the lengths the Angmarim will go to with their experiments, but this passage in the journal made my beard curl. Listen here:

'"Crágacha has retreated back to her hole in the ruins, claiming the drakes she was working on are too powerful and deadly to be controlled. She had the audacity to suggest her tests on the drakes were a success and that maybe she could head back to the surface. Coward! Imbecile! Traitor!

'"My master has demanded more tests. More more more tests. My master in the muck. The bones are leaking. Leaking leaking. I told Crágacha that she was not done. Not done with the bones and the tests and the muck. She is now testing the crystals and the magic leaking leaking much magic spells the bones --"'

Mother Amma breaks off, scanning the page and muttering.

'He goes on rambling for some time... what matters is that we know where they are holed up. Head over to the Angmarim camp and stop this madness!''Welcome back, friend. Were you able to defeat Crágacha?'Having run out of test subjects within Clovengap, the maddened Angmarim have turned on their own.Missing scouts can be found in Gadh Ujáf, Zagâf Muzug, and Rung-shakam.

You should look for, and rescue, the missing scouts.Mother Amma is in Bazanmanar, in north-east Clovengap.

You should tell Mother Amma that you freed the Angmarim deserters.Return to Mother AmmaMother Amma's face is dark as she reads from the journal.

'"The traitorous prisoners, the ones who tried to get away. Like she tried to get away. They are being tested now! Tested for the master in the muck. Muck muck...."'

Mother Amma shakes herself, and closes the book with a snap.

'They are using the crystals and sorceries on their own people, ${PLAYER}. We must stop them before they are successful! Free who you can, if possible. They are the enemy, but no one deserves that fate.''Good work, friend. May they find a way to be of use to their people as the Men rebuild.'The source of the crystals' corruption has been located, but what lies in wait in the muck?The source of the crystals' corruption has been located, but what lies in wait in the muck?Mother Amma is in north-eastern Clovengap.

You should tell Mother Amma that the threat has been defeated.Return to Mother Amma'The torn page pieces have helped me make sense of some of the ramblings. The fragments turned out to be a map, leading to the origin of the crystals! Look here! See those lines? Those are dragon bones, or I'm beard lice. Obviously I will be joining you in order to study and recover what I may.

'I have pieced the fragments together for you on the table, and we have the candle. Speak with me when you are ready to go. Oh, and you may wish to bring along some friends with you. Who knows what truly waits in the crystal cavern.''Let's go!''Well done, my friend. May this be the last we see of these foul sorceries.'Mother Amma suspects the corruption uncovered in Elderslade has spread to Clovengap.Crystal-encrusted Wargs can be found in south-western Clovengap.

Mother Amma has asked for you to defeat crystal-encrusted Wargs and to bring her crystal samples.Defeat crystal-encrusted Wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect corrupted crystals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mother Amma is in Stókkset, in Clovengap.

You should bring the crystal sarrowstone sample to Mother Amma.'Welcome to Stókkset, friend. There is much work to be done. I had hoped that the crystals we destroyed in Elderslade were the only ones, but scouts in Clovengap bring reports of Wargs and other creatures with the fell sarrowstones embedded in their very skin!

'Defeat what abominations you come across, and bring me samples of their crystals. I fear we may be dealing with something new… something far more dangerous.''Oh, hoo! I see the stench of the crystals has not improved. Let us see what you have brought.'Beneath the crumbling arches of ancient vineyards prowls a deadly beast. Has the crystal corruption altered this already formidable foe?Clovengap mist-stalkers and sabre-tooth cats can be found in the vineyards.

Nósni has asked you to bring back furs from Clovengap mist-stalkers and fangs from the deadly sabre-tooth cats of Clovengap.Collect mist-walker pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect sabre-tooth fangs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nósni is in Hagbuth in north-east Clovengap.

Bring the furs and fangs to Nósni.'If you will not be talked out of avoiding the beasts, you may as well do away with any you come across. Bring back their hides and fangs. The tailor, Klátha, will use the furs to clothe our warriors and families, while the deadly fangs make for good weapons.''Ah, you return! And with such fine furs and fangs as well.'Someone has been experimenting on the Wargs of Clovengap and creating even more dangerous abominations.Warg dens can be found in western Clovengap.

Mother Amma has asked for you search for clues around the Warg dens.Search for cluesClues can be found in the upper tiers of south-west Clovengap.

You should continue to look for clues as to how the crystal-encrusted Wargs are being created.Search for more cluesClues can be found in the upper tiers of south-west Clovengap.

You should continue to look for clues as to how the crystal-encrusted Wargs are being created.Search for the testing siteThe Angmarim camp is in south-west Clovengap.

You have discovered an Angmarim camp where a sorceress is conducting experiments on the local Wargs.Defeat the Angmarim sorceressSearch the testing campClues can be found in the upper tiers of south-west Clovengap.

You should continue to look for clues as to how the crystal-encrusted Wargs are being created.Search the testing campMother Amma is in Hagbuth, in south-eastern Clovengap.

You found a fragment of torn paper and a journal detailing sarrowstones experiments. You should bring the journal and paper fragment to Mother Amma.'As I suspected, the crystals you collected are different from those we saw in Elderslade. We must uncover this new weaver of fell magic who has been enhancing the sarrowstones and using them to create these terrible beasts.

'See if you can find the location where the Wargs are being enchanted. One of the scouts said she saw cages in the tiers above their dens. Search for anything that might help us discover who is behind these abominations. I will meet you in Hagbuth, on the upper tier across the river.''Welcome back, friend. What have you discovered?'Tucked away high above the fields of Clovengap, wounded warriors await assistance.Thyfli is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar.

Golodhril has asked you to bring a bundle of healing plants to Thyfli.'I am still studying two of the plants, but I do recognize one of them! What we were calling daewath is known in your language as duskenshade, and it is known to provide relief to those who are injured.

'If you're still of a mind to help, will you bring this bundle to Thyfli? He is stationed in a small camp north of here, where the wounded are being watched over.''Ah, well met, friend. You bring something from the Elf-lady? Oh! Duskenshade? Well bless me. My great-grandmother called this plant "lanzaskâd." It will do much to ease the suffering of our fallen brothers and sisters. You have my thanks.'Garânashmar, the ancient homestead of Forstóri's Line, has been overrun by Angmarim.Garânashmar perches above Kurdushâlak, in north-western Clovengap.

Gerja has asked you to investigate Garânashmar.Investigate GarânashmarAngmarim intruders can be found in Garânashmar.

While investigating Garânashmar you found some old coins. Their features are worn down by time, but perhaps you could find others with clearer markings.Collect old coins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gerja is in Bazanmanar in north-eastern Clovengap.

You should bring the old coins to Gerja.'Across the river Kurdushâlak, tucked into the curve of the gap's walls, is Garânashmar, the ancient homestead of Forstóri's Line. Forstóri and his kin were the caretakers of Clovengap in ancient days. The markets they oversaw brought them wealth, some of which they invested back into the improvement and upkeep of the gap. Some of their gold went to the building of Garânashmar. An estate that housed their families and friends, and which served as sentinel over the river and cavern.

'Cross the river and explore Garânashmar, that we may add its location to our map.''What have you found?'Angmarim sorcerers weave foul magic up and down the length of Clovengap. They must be stopped before they are able to create any more of their corrupted abominations.The Angmarim priest can be found in north-eastern Clovengap.

You should find and defeat the priest who is working to corrupt the worms.Defeat MádathDefeat worms in Clovengap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Investigate Mádath's experimentsMother Amma is at Bazanmanar, in north-east Clovengap.

You should bring the new fragment to Mother Amma.'It appears that Fioth and Iuvár were also working under the command of Galachán. As we suspected, Brágha Fellwinder was not the only one mixing fell magic with the corrupted sarrowstone crystals.

'According to the journal, there are experiments taking place up and down Clovengap. We have found and defeated two of his underlings, but more yet remain. We must stop them before they are successful, ${PLAYER}!

'An Angmarim named Mádath was tasked with corrupting the worms that have taken up residence in the northern end of Clovengap. Head there next friend, and let us hope that their efforts were in vain.''Welcome back. Were you able to defeat Mádath?'

You inform her of what you found. She laughs so loudly and long at the image of Mádath hiding from the worms that she can barely breathe.Clovengap plants with special properties are written of in ancient tales.The three plants can be found in central Clovengap.

Golodhrim has asked you to collect samples of three plants.Collect daewath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect fingloth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect elialas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golodhril is located in Bazanmanar.

You should bring the flowers you collected to Golodhril.'You have my gratitude for your assistance with the fountains. I wonder if I might ask you for further help. I have read about three rare plants that grew here in Clovengap. One of them is said to cure stomach ailments, and I believe it could be useful for our eventual sailing trip to the West.'

She lowers her voice, glancing to be sure her sister is not listening.

'Sadorwen does not do so well with the rocking of boats, which is no doubt why she agreed to put off going for as long as we have. Sadly, my book is unclear on which plant has this property. The three plants are called daewath, fingloth, and elialas in Sindarin.'

She shows you a page with the image of three flowers, with illegible writing next to them.

'Gather some of each for me and bring them back here… ah, please.''You come bearing plants? Lovely! Let us see what we have.'You have come with Glúrkub to the Welkin-lofts to steal the mithril hammer wielded by Gorgar the Ruthless, and perhaps earn the goblin captive his freedom.Glúrkub stands among the trees not far from the hiding place you scouted.Talk to Glúrkub in the Welkin-lofts<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>Glúrkub stands in the hiding spot near the path to the mountain's summit.Talk to Glúrkub in the hiding spot<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>Glúrkub stands in the hiding spot in the Welkin-lofts.Listen to Glúrkub explain the plan<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>Glúrkub has asked you if he can trust Prince Durin, and if you think the prince will let him go.Answer Glúrkub's question: can the goblin trust Prince Durin?<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>Glúrkub is in the hiding spot in the Welkin-lofts.Listen to Glúrkub<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>Glúrkub has asked you what password he should use to call you forth from hiding if he gets into trouble.Answer Glúrkub's question: what password should he use to call you from hiding if he gets into trouble?<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>Glúrkub is in the hiding spot in the Welkin-lofts.Listen to Glúrkub and wait for Gorgar to climb to the peak<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>Glúrkub is in the hiding spot in the Welkin-lofts.Talk to Glúrkub<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot too early!</rgb>Glúrkub has gone to execute his part of the plan: stealing the mithril hammer from the guards Gorgar left behind. You should remain in the hiding spot and not emerge unless Glúrkub gets into trouble and shouts the password.Watch Glúrkub carry out the plan<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot until Glúrkub shouts the password!</rgb>Glúrkub has gone to execute his part of the plan: stealing the mithril hammer from the guards Gorgar left behind. You should remain in the hiding spot and not emerge unless Glúrkub gets into trouble and shouts the password.Watch Glúrkub carry out the plan<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the hiding spot until Glúrkub shouts the password!</rgb>Glúrkub has seized the mithril hammer and raced back to the hiding spot, where he waits to speak with you.Talk to GlúrkubYou and Glúrkub successfully carried out the plan to steal the mithril hammer and should now return to Prince Durin.Return to Prince Durin with Glúrkub and the mithril hammerGlúrkub has delivered the mithril hammer to Prince Durin, as he promised to do. How will the prince now respond?Talk to Prince DurinGlúrkub has delivered the mithril hammer to Prince Durin, as he promised. The goblin now waits to speak with you.Talk to GlúrkubPrince Durin has commanded that Glúrkub be given safe passage away from Gundabad, and asked you to escort the goblin from Elderslade.Escort Glúrkub from GundabadYou have safely escorted Glúrkub past the dwarf-lines and out of Gundabad.Talk to Glúrkub outside Gundabad'I will not lie to you, ${PLAYER}: I am glad to see him go. Glúrkub was of some help to the Gabil'akkâ, but it could very easily have gone otherwise.'

You ask Glóin if he feels eyes upon the two of you, and he shakes his head.

'I cannot say I do, my friend, but that means little. As the years pass I find more and more things similarly passing my notice! It would not surprise me to learn that Dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ watch us from afar, pondering our escort of Glúrkub to safety.'

You give Glóin a nod but keep your silence; the watchful presence has already departed, and you do not wish to worry the old dwarf unnecessarily.'We almost there, ${PLAYER}. You will see how helpful Glúrkub can be, and then your prince will let him go.

'How funny: Glúrkub must steal a thing to earn his freedom!''This where we wait. Gorgar will be along soon, and after he leaves the shiny hammer behind, that is when Glúrkub earns his keep, and won't be kept any longer!''Now is my turn, ${PLAYER}.

'Remember! Do not leave hiding spot until you hear me say password!''I am sorry about that, ${PLAYER}... I forgot the password!

'But all is well now.''You have done well, ${PLAYER}... you and the goblin both.'

Durin studies the clean, angular lines worked in the mithril of the hammer, marvelling at the ease with which he hefts the weapon.

'Remarkable, my friend, truly remarkable. Gorgar will not be pleased to lose this! Let him howl his anger to the skies, while he can, for with this he will be undone, and every dwarf that suffered at his hands will be avenged!'

Durin looks up from his study of the mithril hammer and considers the goblin standing before him.

'Now to the matter of the goblin. Your kind are enemies of me and mine, Glúrkub, and you served our hated foe; you would have seen us all slain, if you could.

'But you did not, and through your efforts you have aided the cause of the Gabil'akkâ. So too have you performed a great service to me personally, for the delivery of this mithril hammer has lifted my spirit and given to me a weapon unrivalled. For your service on my behalf I will grant you what you have said you sought: safe passage through the lines of war, and the freedom to establish your own dwelling far from Gorgar and his people, somewhere beyond the lands of my folk.

'${PLAYER} will see you brought through the lines, and where you go afterward is up to you. These are my thanks, and they are all you will receive, for I am unaccustomed to speaking words such as these to goblins.''I not know what to say, ${PLAYER}. I did not think dwarf-prince would honour agreement. Glúrkub happy to be wrong!

'Lead the way, friend ${RACE}. Sooner Glúrkub far from here, the better!''Thank you for bringing me this far, ${PLAYER}. I will go rest of the way from here.

'Glúrkub look forward to life far from Gorgar, Hrímil, and Gundabad!'You and the dwarves have followed the trail of the Angmarim into Clovengap, where you hope you will find some sign of the Black Stone Anvil's passage.Bósi stands by the entrance to Clovengap.Talk to Bósi near the entrance to ClovengapThe dwarves have discovered the corpse of a warg among the mist-laden grasses of Clovengap.Examine the warg corpseBori and the other dwarves gather around the warg corpse you found near the entrance to Clovengap.Talk to Bori by the warg corpse in ClovengapThe dwarves have discovered the corpse of an Angmarim cultist not far from the first body you encountered in Clovengap.Examine the corpse of the Angmarim cultistThe dwarves discuss the violence that has been done here in Clovengap; what does it mean for the safety of your travelling party?Listen to the dwarves discuss the situation in ClovengapThere are wolf-voices on the wind, and it seems the dwarves do not have long to prepare before the wargs attack!Talk to Bósi in ClovengapYou have fended off the wargs... for now.Remain alert for the return of the wargs'We should make camp before another warg-pack finds us. They will not have forgotten the death of Ránulur upon the very threshold of the Mountain-home. That was the doing of dwarves, but it was Gorgar that commanded the warg-chieftain to battle. Until we have a better foothold in Gundabad, this is their territory... not ours.

'But one day it will be ours again.''Remain alert, ${PLAYER}. None of us must be blinded by the beauty of Akrakír, for we are here to learn where the Angmarim have stolen the Black Stone Anvil of my people!''This warg was not slain by dwarf-axes or swords, then? Aye, I see the scorch marks. Fire it was that killed this beast.'

He faces Bósi and raises his voice.

'I will lead us from here, father! Follow me!''You too, ${PLAYER}. Wargs are as smart as they are ferocious, and I expect this hunting-pack to attempt to encircle us.

'They may attack from any direction, and we must be prepared to defend ourselves!'Deep in the ground, in crystal-laden, foetid pools, an ancient evil spreads corruption.Lore-master Rúni waits for you by the falls in western Clovengap.

You should talk to Rúni.Talk to RúniThe waterfall is in eastern Clovengap.

Rúni the Lore-master believes there is a hidden cave behind the nearby waterfall. You should find the cave.Find the crystal caveThe source of the corruption is deep in the Min Návaid cave in Clovengap.

You should uncover the source of the corrupted sarrowstones and put an end for good to the terrible experiments of Bruidalg the Bloodletter.Defeat Bruidalg the BloodletterThe secret tunnel is within the crystal cave, Min Návaid.

The journal spoke of a secret tunnel whose entrance can be revealed by the light of the candle. With the Angmarim High Priest defeated, you should look for the secret tunnel.Find the secret tunnelPraushod the Foetid lies deeper within Min Návaid.

You should summon Praushod the Foetid by striking the corrupted crystals.Summon Praushod the FoetidThe dragon bones are in Min Návaid.

Lore-master Rúni has asked you to investigate the cave for dragon bones.Investigate the dragon bonesLore-master Rúni is in the crystal cave.

You should tell Lore-master Rúni that the deed is done.Talk to Rúni'Do not worry about me. I shall stay on a while longer to study these bones. Go now, and tell Mother Amma that Praushod and Bruidalg have been defeated.''I shall be right behind you, friend! Well, probably more at a distance, really.''Well done, friend! And these bones! Amazing! Ancient and seemingly the source of the corruption.

'I shall stay on a while longer to study these bones. Go now, and tell Mother Amma that Praushod and Bruidalg have been defeated.''See yonder waterfall? The mad man's journal says that behind it lies the entrance to a cave. It is from here that the sarrowstones are harvested. This is the source of the corruption, friend! I would come to help you, but as you know, I am useless with weapons. I shall be right behind you, however! Good luck!

'Ah, I nearly forgot! Take the candle with you! The journal says that by its light, the way shall be revealed.'Glúrkub has a tale to tell... but how much of it can be believed?Muzmák is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Muzmák in DurshulotMuzmák gave you the names of three similar-minded residents of Durshulot who might help you escape from the growing conflict beneath Gundabad.Talk to ShulgolbTalk to LumbagTalk to ZogmaukMuzmák is waiting to speak with you.Talk to Muzmák in DurshulotAn unexpected visitor has interrupted your plans.Remain alert during Gorgar's inspectionGorgar has chosen you for some unknown purpose.Talk to Gorgar the RuthlessGorgar has need of a goblin to acquire a valuable treasure for him.Carry out Gorgar's planGorgar believes there is a mithril treasure in the room on this side of the rock-fall.Collect the mithril treasure sought by GorgarAcquiring the mithril hammer for Gorgar was only the beginning.Continue working for GorgarGorgar the Ruthless has sent you to command the loyalty of Ránulur, Chieftain of Wargs.Command Ránulur to fight on behalf of GorgarYou served Gorgar faithfully and well.Carry out the wishes of Gorgar the RuthlessThe War of Three Peaks is underway!Talk to Muzmák during the War of Three PeaksYou ran far from the battle-lines, eventually finding yourself on distant snowfields.Continue your flight from the warYou have run with Muzmák from the War of Three Peaks... but how far will be enough?Talk to Muzmák as he catches his breathHrímil Frost-heart has emerged from her icy prison behind the Anvil of Winterstith!Survive the reemergence of Hrímil Frost-heartMuzmák stands in silence upon the snowfield.Talk to Muzmák'Are you sure this plan of yours is going to work, goblin? I'm taking a real risk siding with you, and it'll be our heads if we're discovered!

'The dragon who commands the hobgoblins might be trapped behind the Anvil of Winterstith, but that has not decreased their numbers here! They're pushing us out, Orcs and goblins both! I don't like it. And why hasn't Gorgar stood up to them? Bah.'

Muzmák peers around suspiciously and lowers his voice.

'So the plan is still on? We'll join the next raiding party heading south, and once free of the mountains we'll slip away? We'll set up somewhere far from Gundabad, far from Gorgar, and far from these accursed hobgoblins? All right. I've chosen three others who might join us. Speak to them and see what you think, goblin. Their names are Shulgolb, Lumbag, and Zogmauk, and they're all here in Durshulot.''You're part of Muzmák's gang, eh? If we get found out I'm tellin' Gorgar it was all his idea. Are you all right with that, Glúrkub?

'Then I'm in. Gorgar is losing his power to the hobgoblins, day by day. Won't be good for any of us to still be here when he loses the last of it!''Count me in, Glúrkub. This place won't be safe for us when the hobgoblins take over!

'Who plans to lead the raiding-party we will join? Natsatúg? Ah, that is good to know. It won't be easy, but I think I can get my hands on some of the badges his boys wear when they leave the mountain. You know the ones, with the thunderclouds on 'em?

'We'll blend right in, and when we're safely in the country we'll slip away for our better lives. It's a good plan.''I could join your little band, it's true.

'Or I could turn you and your friends in for traitors and cowards!''Are they with us? Ah, I wondered about Zogmauk. At least he has been dealt with before he could cause us any more -'

Muzmák suddenly stops speaking.

'What is that? Someone comes!''I need you to come with me, goblin. You are just what I need for my purposes.'

Gorgar scowls at the line of goblins, every one of whom wears a relieved expression.

'I have seen the glint of mithril inside an old tomb, but the entrance is sealed by a great rock-fall. No Orc can make it through the opening, and it might be too small for most goblins. But you, I think, will serve. You will bring me this treasure, and be rewarded by Gorgar the Generous.''What did you say? A great force of dwarves approaches the mountain? Even now they near Elderslade, and Gorgar commands that I fight on his behalf?''We are taking a big risk trusting you again, Glúrkub. How are we to know you don't plan to trick us, and turn us in to Gorgar?

'Pox and maggots, there's nothing for it. We'll fight through the dwarf-lines and make for freedom... and if you betray us, Glúrkub, I'll see that you die for it!''This is... this is not far enough....

'We have to... we have to keep going....''If what the Dragon has said is true... the dwarves are doomed to fail. Do we flee from certain victory, Glúrkub?'

Muzmák stares into the sky.

'We should return to Gundabad. I do not know what ever compelled us to leave. That is our place. The new Lord of Gundabad commands it.'An eager architect asks assistance acquiring details of Clovengap.Dashât-zahar is in western Clovengap.

You should search for Dashât-zahar, an old market.Search for the old marketGerja Defthand is in south-west Clovengap.

You should let Gerja Defthand know what you found in the old market.'Welcome to Clovengap! I am Gerja Defthand, Master Architect and head of the restoration project for this area of Gundabad. Yes, yes. I am aware that we have not yet taken back the gap, but as our victory is a given, it is never too early to start planning. If you are of a mind to help, I would greatly appreciate it!

'Over the centuries, time and the gap’s unsavoury occupants have destroyed the gardens and farms. However, dwarf-hewn stone remains solid. We may discover once again the locations of these lost marvels.

'Let us start locally. The records state that north of here, burrowed into the very mountain itself, was a marketplace, Dashât-zahar. Will you go and survey the area? I am drawing up a map for our forces and I believe the location could be useful as a camp.''Do not be deceived by the current conditions of Clovengap. Ancient records state that this area was once tiered gardens, markets, and parks. The author of said records wrote of vineyards, lush fields for livestock, and gardens of fruit bearing trees, herbs, and ornamental plants.'Welcome back! Did you find Dashât-zahar?'The passing of Hrímil has greatly altered the landscape of Clovengap. Are there still signs of the fields and fortresses beneath the ice?The new locations are in northern Clovengap.

You should search for the Amgaruslun Falls, the ruins of Anatrâd, the look-out, and Frósthel.Search for AnatrâdSearch for the fields of FrósthelSearch for the look-outSearch for the Amgaruslun FallsGerja Defthand is in Bazanmanar, in north-east Clovengap.

You should let Gerja Defthand know what you found.'Since you are heading north, you may as well try to find these last few places. The Amgaruslun Falls and the ruins of Anatrâd. Even further north, now covered in rimefrost by the passage of Hrímil, was Frósthel. These were large fields by the side of the river, where livestock once grazed on lush grasses.

'There is also mention of a look-out, near to the tunnel that leads to the Welkin-lofts. I cannot make out the name, but see if you can find any clues about where that may have been as well.''Ah, you return! What have you found, friend?'A hopeless romantic finds hope in the forest beneath the mountains.Klátha is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar.

Nósni has asked you to bring the furs to Klátha.Talk to KláthaThe pile of furs is next to Klátha, in northern Clovengap.

You should add your furs to the pile.Klátha is located in Bazanmanar.

You should let Klátha know you have added your furs to the pile.Speak to KláthaNósni is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar.

Klátha has asked you to give her message of refusal to Nósni.Return to Nósni'The fangs and furs you brought me are perfect, friend. If you do not mind doing me another favour, would you be so kind as to bring the furs to the Lady Klátha? She will craft them into finest things! Klátha is stationed in a camp north of Bazanmanar. I shall meet you there as well.''Let me guess, furs from Nósni.'

Klátha sighs and rolls her eyes.

'Very well, add them to the pile, if you must.''I know you meant no harm, friend, but please tell Nósni that I have no interest in speaking with him until he apologizes for what he did. A pile of furs, no matter how fine, will not change my mind.'

Klátha huffs and refuses to say anymore.'I shall meet you in the camp north of Bazanmanar!''What did she say? She was delighted, right?'Nósni's display of affection has managed to turn his intended's heart to ice. He needs help before the door to love closes forever!Mother Amma is located in Bazanmanar.

Nósni has asked you to ask Mother Amma whether she knows why Klátha is angry.Talk to Mother AmmaNósni is located in a camp north of Bazanmanar.

You should let Nósni know what Mother Amma said.Return to Nósni'I cannot believe this has happened. My efforts to win Klátha's heart have instead driven her against me! I have no idea why she is so cross.

'Perhaps someone else has a clue for us. Please, friend, speak with Mother Amma. I have seen Klátha and Amma whispering to each other. Let us hope the clue to her anger has been shared.''Greetings, my friend!'

You share Nósni's predicament with her. Mother Amma chuckles and shakes her head.

'Klátha has every right to be upset with Nósni! He had her moved from this camp to the one up north. She is most cross that he thinks she cannot take care of herself, and that she needs protecting.''That fool! I can take care of myself just fine.''What did Mother Amma say? What have I done?'

You tell Nósni what Mother Amma said.

'Protecting her? Cannot take care of herself? Oh, by Durin's beard. This is terrible.'A vicious Warg prowls the upper tiers of Clovengap, blocking access to enemy camps in the ruins beyond.The Warg prowls the highest tier in western Clovengap.

Borghild has asked you to deal with a vicious Warg who blocks the army's progress.Find and defeat the WargNakrovak is in eastern Clovengap.

Nakrovak, a crystal-encrusted Warg, has asked you to listen to her tale.Speak to NakrovakNakrovak's cubs are held prisoner in eastern Clovengap.

Angmarim sorcerers have cubnapped Nakrovak's litter! You should defeat the Angmarim!Defeat the cub-snatchers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nakrovak's cubs are held prisoner in eastern Clovengap.

With the Angmarim defeated, you should release the Warg cubs.Rescue the Warg cubsNakrovak is in eastern Clovengap.

You have freed Nakrovak's cubs. You should ensure they all made it back to her safely.Return to Nakrovak'One of the scouts reported a vicious Warg who prowls the upper tiers north of here. She blocks access to enemy camps in the ruins beyond. Defeat her, so that our armies may march on the Angmarim unhindered.''I am Nakrovak. My mate and I were captured many moons ago by Men in robes. They chanted over us and pierced our hides with crystals. The pain and the ensorcelled crystals drove my mate mad.

'The crystals had a different effect on me, however. My mind grew clearer. My body stronger. Rage and hunger were once all I knew. Now, there is sorrow, grief, and… something else I cannot explain. A softness….

'I managed to get away from my captors, but they found my den, weakened me with poison, and stole my cubs. As you have seen, I am not yet at my full strength.

'I dare not wait for the effects of the poison to wear off, for my cubs are in danger. Please, rescue them, and we will leave this place and go far away from two-legged peoples and their sorceries.''I owe you a great debt, ${RACE}. My intention is that our paths never cross again. If they do, however, and you require assistance, I will be there.

'My children and I will leave Clovengap once I have recovered.''Stay your hand, ${RACE}. I am in no shape to fight you.

'I can see that you are a formidable foe, and you seem not to be associated with the scum who stole my cubs. Listen to my tale, then decide whether I should be destroyed.'Golodhril has narrowed her study down to two of the plants you collected for her in Clovengap.The test subjects are located at Bazanmanar.

Golodhril has asked you to speak to her various test subjects.Talk to Mother AmmaTalk to RúdinTalk to Gerja DefthandTalk to Málur KeenwordGolodhril is located at Bazanmanar.

You should report your findings to Golodhril.'My friend, you have done much for my sister and me. If you would do me one last favour, I would greatly appreciate it. I studied the two remaining plants you gathered for me and created two concoctions. While you were gone I had our friends here sample each and now all that remains is to determine the results! Please, go see how they have fared.''Well met! Oh yes, you can tell Golodhril that I have noticed that my beard is softer. Please do give her my thanks and let her know I'd like that recipe!''You tell that fool of an Elf that if she splashes me again with any of her so called concoctions that I will have her relocated to the camp north of here.

'But since you are here, I might as well admit that yes, my beard is feeling quite fine now. That is no excuse, however!''Ah, you come from Golodhril? I cannot say as I have noticed much of a change, no.''I have not noticed a change, no. My beard has always been gloriously soft, though, so who really could tell?''You return! How fared our experiment?'

You give her the results.

'Ah hah! Excellent! I gave Málur and Gerja the second phial which means... ${PLAYER}! We have done it! The second phial must then be the quellwort!

'Oh my friend, thank you ever so much for all of your help! Our journey to the West encroaches, but now perhaps Sadorwen's passage will be that much gentler.'Málur Keenword has finished his translation of the madman's journal.Málur is located in Bazanmanar.

Mother Amma has asked you to see how far Málur Keenword has come in deciphering the journal.Talk to Málur KeenwordThe journal is on the table beside Málur in Clovengap.

You should pick up the translated journal.Pick up the translated journalMother Amma is in Bazanmanar.

You should bring the translated journal to Mother Amma.'The sarrowstone crystal you collected from the Wargs is akin to the ones we saw in Elderslade, but there is something else going on here. The colour is new and it... feels different. Blah, the stench remains just as vile, however. Now then, where is the madman’s journal?'

You tell her that Málur Keenword is working on it.

'Well, go over and see what he has discovered.''Aye, I finished my translation. I am none too happy about what I found in these pages. Unholy and fell dealings with evil creatures, muck monsters, dragons, and abominations of nature.

'The journal and its translation are on the table. You tell Mother Amma to be careful. This madman is not acting alone.''What news do you bring? Málur has completed the translation? Well, let us have a look.'Ages ago, a great sundering shook loose the ceiling of this massive cavern. Once opened to the sky, Clovengap became an emerald swath of tiered gardens, unique among the dwarves. Gone now are those gardens, replaced by dark forests and thick mists, in which prowl those with murderous intent.Wargs can be found in western Clovengap.

Gunvald has asked for your assistance in thinning the Warg packs in Clovengap.Defeat Wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gunvald is in a camp in the south-western area of Clovengap.

You should let Gunvald know you have culled the Warg population of Clovengap.Return to Gunvald'At one time, orchards, farms, and vineyards filled these terraces. Now they lie fallow, forests of fruitless trees filled with feral creatures.

'To the north of this camp, Warg dens litter the tiers. The creatures impede our ability to move forward. Do what you can to thin their ranks, my friend. We will reclaim these gardens!''Good work! We shall drive them all from our ancestral home!'A deadly fungus spews poisons on the banks of the Kurdushâlak.Smothercap can be found in northern Clovengap.

Golodhrim has asked you to destroy smothercap mushrooms.Destroy smothercap mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Golodhril is located in Bazanmanar.

You should tell Golodhril that you have removed many of the smothercap mushrooms.Return to Golodhril'I would ask your help once more while I examine the plants you brought me. A scout returned recently with word of a strange mushroom that releases toxic fumes when one draws near.

'From their description, this can be no other than smothercap. In small doses it… ah, never mind that. The fungus is deadly. When you are out in the frozen fields north of here, keep watch for the mushrooms, friend. Oh, and - I encourage you to destroy them from a distance.''Welcome back! I hope you did not suffer overly much in this task.'The hobgoblins of Anatrâd have filled their pockets with stolen gems from Tharrkirîn for the last time.Anatrâd lies in north-western Clovengap.

You should recover the stolen gems from the hobgoblins of Anatrâd.Collect stolen gemsAnatrâd lies in north-western Clovengap.

You should recover the stolen gems from the hobgoblins of Anatrâd.Collect stolen gems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gerja is in Bazanmanar in north-eastern Clovengap.

