'The next location to find is Danakh-khêj. One of my ancient texts contains part of a song about meeting a beloved in a lush sward of grass under the mountain, the two gazing at the stars together. Should you find an enormous fountain, you shall know you are in the right place.''So the fountains still flow? Ah, my mind wanders to what it must have been like. Dwarves of all ages, relaxing and enjoying the day, chatting together on the benches, the fountains splashing merrily. We shall return it to its glory, my friend.'This dwarf-made memorial stone is weathered but has stood strong against time and the elements. The runes read, 'Rest well, Azagh Gamz, my fierce warrior.'

