Sadorwen has suggested that you help Golodhril.Return to Golodhril'Oh, hello! You are that hero of the realm, ${PLAYER}, correct? My, it must be wonderful to be free to wander Middle-earth in search of adventure and glory.

'I am Golodhril. My sister Sadorwen and I have come to see the fabled Forest Beneath the Mountain!'

She sighs and slumps.

'Sadly, we have seen barely anything save rocks and weeds. I am a prisoner of my tyrannical sister! Perhaps you could speak with her, and tell her that Clovengap is nowhere near as dangerous as she fears.''Mae govannen, friend. I see my dear sister still chafes at her imagined bonds.'

Sadorwen chuckles lightly.

'Golodhril is merely a few centuries old. She has not yet experienced all that ones such as ourselves have. I promised her that we could visit the places she reads about before we set sail for the West. However, I did not agree to allow her to become drake food.

'With your experience and skills, you could easily help her with some of the tasks she has set for herself. I am sure you are busy; however, you will no doubt pass by the weeds and vines she seeks. If you are interested, why not offer to go in her place for now.''She continues to treat me like a child, I see. Very well, I suppose I will accept your service.'With your assistance, Gerja has created a detailed map of Clovengap. The war will go more smoothly now, thanks to your scouting.The map is on a table beside Gerja in Bazanmanar.

