'Look here, he wrote, "The way is secret, secret is the way. Only with the four shall the secret way be secret no more." Bruidalg continues on, rambling about, "The bones, the bones are leaking. The master is in the muck, the master and the bones and the crystals. All in the muck, dragons in the mire. Never will I breathe clean air again."

'Fascinating, no? Could there be a dragon here in Clovengap? Aside from our frosty lady, that is. But another, perhaps? A second dragon?! Mired in the muck somewhere? By Durin's beard, this is too exciting.

'Oh! I almost forgot. The journal mentions experiments on some of the frost-drakes that followed Hrímil into Clovengap. They have taken up residence at Frósthel, a set of ruins across the river. You go deal with that, and I shall have a look at the fragments you brought me.''Ah! You return. Tell me of the drakes!'High above the River Kurdushâlak an ancient collection of stone from across Gundabad waits to be discovered.Tharrkirîn is in northern Gundabad.

