'I will meet you at Bazanmanar, north of here.'Much of the wording has faded with time, but it seems to be a poem describing the sundering of Gundabad, and the crumbling of the ceiling of Clovengap and of Nâtatharr, the Ceiling Rock, crashing to the ground below alongside countless other pieces. The latter were used in the construction of the tiers and ramps of Clovengap.Much of the wording has faded with time, but it seems to be a poem describing the sundering of Gundabad, and the crumbling of the ceiling of Clovengap and of Nâtatharr, the Ceiling Rock, crashing to the ground below alongside countless other pieces. The latter were used in the construction of the tiers and ramps of Clovengap.'Welcome back! Did you find Nâtatharr? Was it enormous?'Ages ago, a great sundering shook loose the ceiling of this massive cavern. Once opened to the sky, Clovengap became an emerald swath of tiered gardens, unique among the dwarf-holds. Gone now are those gardens, replaced by dark forests and thick mists, in which prowl those with murderous intent.Mother Amma is in Stókkset, in south-west Clovengap.

