You should find Bagud-dum.Find the entrance to the dwarf-fort of Bagud-dumHórin can be called with the summoning horn.

You should talk to Hórin.'We have done all we can here. Klúso will keep an eye on Thyrstáth. It is time to continue our search for Dushtalbúk, Loknashra, and the staff. Let us continue up the Father's Path. We should find Kyrstig, the last of Ausma's apprentices, somewhere nearby. Keep an eye out for her flare.''${PLAYER}! Good to see you again. Welcome to Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold. This is a place of much historic significance for all dwarves. Within these walls, the great Dwarrowmoots take place, where the Kings of all the clans are called together to make important decisions, like declarations of war!

'I brought a few dwarves up here to set up a staging area to the higher peaks. It's not much, but please use it should you need to rest. Oh, and one more thing... I saw the hobgoblins!''Loknashra is making secret deals with the Angmarim? What are they doing that she does not want Dushtalbúk to know about? Finding her and the staff have just become an even more pressing matter! Come, we must continue up the path and find this fort Kyrstig mentioned in her report.''This must be the place. I hate to see such a grand dwarf-fort taken over by Men of evil. We should discuss our plan of attack.''Are you ready to receive my report?'Náth has warned you of a dangerous predator lurking nearby.Náth has told you about a huge white sabre-cat lurking somewhere near Fellgát.

You should find and defeat the sabre-cat known as Héormuth.Defeat HéormuthYou have successfully defeated the sabre-cat menacing the dwarves in Fellgát.

You should talk to Náth.Talk to Náth in Fellgát'${PLAYER}, I need your help. Right after she first set out, Molkha encountered something in the snow that gave her quite a scare. She came running back to camp, and after we were able to calm her down she told us she could not make out exactly what it was, and that all she saw was a sudden flash of white against a dark tree-trunk. 

'After she left camp again I saw it with my own eyes: a huge white sabre-cat with long and glistening fangs! I'm worried it might still be out there, stalking her! If you see it, well... you know what to do. I'm afraid Molkha might not be as fortunate a second time!'You present Náth with Héormuth's fang. His eyes widen.

'Will you look at that? Any beast with fangs that sharp, and that large, could have proven fatal to any of us travelling alone out there. Thank you for slaying the beast, ${PLAYER}, and for making the Welkin-lofts a little safer for us.

