You should talk to Hórin.'Here is the plan. We are going to enter Thyrstáth, request an audience with the ice-giant chieftain, and attempt to sway them over to the side of the Gabil'akkâ. I am more warrior than diplomat, but I will do what I can! Keep your guard up in the event this goes poorly.

'But ${PLAYER}? Try not to start a fight... unless we really need one.''Well, here goes nothing!''I may have been wrong about most giants having honourable natures... that was downright duplicitous! It is time to go on the offensive! If they want to ally with the Frost-horde and the Angmarim, well, they have declared themselves our enemies. And let them regret it!''We've done enough here. Let's leave, and quickly, before more hobgoblins, or giants, or Angmarim come looking for us.''Come, let's return to Klúso. He's probably worried about us!''${PLAYER}! I was about to come looking for you! What happened?'

You tell Klúso about the ice-giant's trap, and your assault on Thyrstáth with Hórin.

'Ah. So much for diplomacy! It changes little. What is one more enemy to defeat before we can reclaim Gundabad? But there is this too: should we be worried about that staff falling back into the hands of the Angmarim?''Klúso is correct. For the Angmarim to so intently pursue that staff means you were right to keep it from them. All we can do now is continue up the mountain, and hope we can track it down again.'The bodies of fallen dwarves have been taken to Mullach Cagar, where they are used in rituals to create wights.You have found dwarf bodies are being used in Angmarim rituals to make wights.

