You should return to Molkha.Talk to Molkha'While you are investigating Mullach Cagar, I know Hórin will want you to defeat as many of the Angmarim stationed there as you can. We do not know what they are up to, but I guarantee you it is not in our best interests to let it continue!

'Put an end to their evil and it will benefit the Gabil'akkâ, ${PLAYER}!''I knew you could handle them on your own! Good work, ${PLAYER}.'Dréri has asked you to set up camp-fires in Fellgát to keep the cold away.Dréri has asked you to look around the nearby area for firewood.

You should collect fallen branches near Fellgát.Collect fallen branches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Now that you have some firewood, you should build camp-fires in Fellgát.Build camp-fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The camp-fires in Fellgát have been assembled, but now they need to be set alight.Light camp-fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The camp-fires have been lit, protecting Fellgát from the chill of the mountains.

You should talk to Dréri.Talk to Dréri'Now that our tents are set up, we need to get the camp-fires ready. The howling wind and high altitude keep it mighty cold here, and it would not do for us to freeze solid in the middle of the night!

'I need you to look for suitable firewood outside the walls of Fellgát. While you do that, I will mark places for you to make the camp-fires.''Ah, I'm warmer already! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. If you haven't already done so, you should talk to Náth. I'm sure he has some work for you as well.'Náth has asked you to keep an eye out for predators in the Welkin-lofts.Náth has asked you to defeat any predators you find in the wilds near Fellgát.Defeat Welkin-lofts predators (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have hunted predators near Fellgát, and made it a little safer for the dwarves.

You should talk to Náth.Talk to Náth'While you're up here, keep an eye peeled for prowling beasts in the high places. I've seen a few wolves and cats creep a little too close to the camp for my comfort. I have even seen some of the cold-worms going in search of easy meals, and once a drake swooped out of the sky not twenty feet ahead of me, and lifted a mountain ram off the ground as if it were nothing!

'It would be wise for us to lessen the numbers of these predators before the reinforcements arrive and we have even more dwarves to safe-guard. It isn't easy to watch your back when you also need to keep one eye on the sky, ${PLAYER}!''Did you cull some of the more dangerous beasts? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I'll sleep a little better knowing you taught those predators this is not the place for them to seek a dwarf-dinner... or if they do, it will cost them dearly!'The Angmarim have gifted the Frost-horde with a number of dwarf-wights to act as guardians of their nests in Flogalith.The Angmarim have given dwarf-wights to the drakes in Welkin-lofts.

You should defeat dwarf-wights in Flogalith.Defeat dwarf-wights in Flogalith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have slain many wights guarding the drake-nest. You should report your success to Molkha.

Molkha can be found on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.Talk to Molkha in the valley'The Angmarim have gifted a number of dwarf-wights to the drakes of Flogalith, and these unhappy creatures now serve as nest-guardians. If you find yourself at Flogalith you must slay the wights! We cannot allow this insult to stand! It is the least we can do to honour these dwarves, though they perished long ago.''Did you end the unhappy servitude of those long-dead dwarves? We may not be able to give them a proper burial, but we have done what we can. At least they are no longer the slaves of the Frost-horde.

'Thank you for this, ${PLAYER}.'Ancient ward-runes protect Ibdêkh-buzru from Orc-kind invaders. The runes be protected from the Angmarim.Kyrstig believes the Angmarim may have tampered with some of the ward-runes around the Thing-fold.

You should repair the warding runes around Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold.Clean warding runes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kyrstig can be found near Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold.

You should talk to Kyrstig.Talk to Kyrstig'Ibdêkh-buzru is protected from Orc-kind by ward-runes, placed thousands of years ago by the ancestors of the Longbeards. The wards in Gloomingtarn have already been defaced and dismantled by some device of the Angmarim, and I fear they could do the same here!

'While you're looking around the Thing-fold keep an eye out for the wards, and scrape away any modifications the cultists might have made to them.''Thank you for cleaning up the evil modifications the Angmarim attempted to make to the warding runes, ${PLAYER}. No doubt they will not abandon such attempts, but for now the Thing-fold will remain protected.'Dréri has asked you to help prepare Fellgát for use as a base of operations.Dréri has asked you to take down the hobgoblin tents and clean up hobgoblin refuse in Fellgát.Take down hobgoblin tents (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Clean up hobgoblin refuse (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Now that the camp has been cleared, you should set up the packed tents.

You should unpack and set up tents in Fellgát.Set up your packed tentSet up Kyrstig's packed tentSet up Molkha's packed tentSet up Klúso's packed tentSet up Hórin's packed tentSet up Dréri's packed tentSet up Náth's packed tentFellgát is now cleared of hobgoblin structures and ready for dwarf use.

You should talk to Dréri.Talk to Dréri'Hello again, ${PLAYER}! Has Hórin given you our battle-plan for the Welkin-lofts? Good, good. We have some work ahead of us. The cold and the lack of resources this far up the mountain-side will make things difficult for us; we need to ensure our camp is fully-stocked and shielded from the elements!

'Our first order of business is to clear out the tents the hobgoblins left behind, and clean up their filth. It will not be pleasant work, true, but it needs to be done. While you are working on that, I will unpack our own tents and set them down here. Then you can prepare them for dwarf-use. We need shelter if we're going to survive up here.''Good work, ${PLAYER}! Fellgát looks like a proper camp already. Hórin made sure to pack an extra-large tent for you. That was smart of him, but the rest of us would have laughed to see your feet sticking out the end of a dwarf-tent!

'The frost-bite would have been no laughing matter, of course.'The hobgoblin forces have not yet been found, so they must be at the very peak of the mountain. The time for battle is soon at hand.Hórin has gathered the dwarf reinforcements and is waiting for you at the stairs to the ruins of Uzdarulzahar.

You should meet Hórin and complete 'Instance: The Warlord's Gambit'.Climb the Father's Path and meet up with Hórin by the steps leading to the ruins of UzdarulzaharHórin is waiting for you at the gate of Uzdarulzahar.

You should talk to Hórin.Talk to Hórin at UzdarulzaharThe Battle of Uzdarulzahar has begun!

You should complete objectives in Uzdarulzahar and find and assist your dwarf allies.Complete 'Hobgoblins at the Highest House' for HórinComplete 'Dwarves in Arms' for HórinFind and assist Dréri with his opponentFind and assist Náth with his opponentFind and assist Klúso with his opponentFind and assist Kyrstig with her opponentFind and assist Molkha with her opponentHórin needs your assistance defeating Hárkyrta the Frigid in Uzdarulzahar.

This will be a difficult fight! Use the battle horn at the gate of Uzdarulzahar to summon the scout trio if they have left your side.Assist Hórin by defeating Hárkyrta the Frigid(Optional) Use the battle horn to summon the scout trioThe drake has been slain! You should talk to Hórin.

Use the battle horn at the gate of Uzdarulzahar to summon the scout trio if they have left your side.Talk to Hórin at UzdarulzaharThe battle has been won!

You should return to Fellgát and talk to Hórin.Talk to Hórin in Fellgát(Optional) Talk to Hórin at Uzdarulzahar to quickly travel to Fellgát'As we have yet to come across them in our travels up the mountainside, the hobgoblin forces can only be in one place: at the end of the Father's Path, the ruins of Uzdarulzahar at the very peak. I will return to the Thing-fold and send for our reinforcements. They will have arrived at Fellgát by now. Dréri, Náth, Molkha and Klúso will escort them. Kyrstig and I will then travel to just outside the ruins. Meet us there when you are prepared to battle Warlord Dushtalbúk!''Everyone is gathered and the reinforcements have arrived. Are you ready for battle, ${PLAYER}?''That was not how I expected this battle to begin, but the tide has turned in our favour! The others have already joined the fight. Find them, and join me up ahead. I will need everyone's help to defeat the elder drake! For the Zhélruka!''Come, ${PLAYER}, let us return to Fellgát. I desire the warmth of a camp-fire and the taste of an ale-flagon!''Your work cleaning up Fellgát truly paid off, my long-suffering but never-complaining friend! I am glad to have a proper camp to return to after a fierce battle.

'You fought bravely, ${PLAYER}, and though the day is won, I cannot help but dread what must next be done: Hrímil Frost-heart must be defeated. Gorgar and Dushtalbúk are but pawns to the Dragon, and now fully under her control! If anything, the Orcs and hobgoblins are even more dangerous now, for they work in unison rather than tearing at each others' throats. However, our campaign in Gundabad has had no small effect, and I suspect Hrímil will now pull back her forces to protect her lair. For all her haughtiness, she must be feeling rather cornered.

'The unknown factor in all of this is Loknashra. Hrímil was unable to control her, due to whatever dark magic the Angmarim instilled in her, and she spoke of revenge. I have a feeling she will soon make some move, and we must be ready for it... whatever form it takes.

'But enough of doom and gloom! We will face those foes another day. For now, rest, and drink with me! A cheer, for ${PLAYER}! For the Gabil'akkâ!''Right on time, ${PLAYER}! The battle is won! Our forces can deal with the rest of these hobgoblins. It is time we returned to Fellgát.'The Thing-fold is a landmark of great historic significance for the dwarf-clans. It is a location where dwarf-kings have met to discuss matters of grave importance for thousands of years.Seven statues representing the Great Moots can be found in Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold.

You should examine the statues.Examine the statue of The First Great MootExamine the statue of The Second Great MootExamine the statue of The Third Great MootExamine the statue of The Fourth Great MootExamine the statue of The Fifth Great MootExamine the statue of The Sixth Great MootExamine the statue of The Seventh Great MootKyrstig can be found just outside Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold.

You should talk to Kyrstig.Talk to Kyrstig'This grand structure behind me is Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold. This is where the kings of all the dwarf-clans met to discuss matters of grave importance throughout all the long history of the dwarves. There have been six Great Moots held at the Thing-fold, and we can learn about each of them by studying the monuments here.''Did you explore the Thing-fold? Magnificent, isn't it? I'm curious about that seventh statue. Was a seventh moot foretold, but has yet to happen? Hmmm. Well, perhaps it will happen in our lifetime, and I can be here to see it in person!'Two siblings of Vethúg Wintermind have been found living in the Welkin-lofts, and the dwarves have placed a bounty on their heads for the protection of the Gabil'akkâ.Molkha has asked you to slay Fólnith the Pale and Grimdóth the Bitter, siblings of Vethúg Wintermind.

One can be found at the top of Flogalith, the other flies over the frozen lake and will need to be lured from the sky.Defeat Grimdóth the BitterPlace a fresh ram to lure Fólnith the Pale from the sky and defeat himThe two elder drakes have been slain! You should report your success to Molkha.

Molkha can be found on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.Talk to Molkha in the valley'Those two massive drakes I saw speaking with the Angmarim are apparently a breeding pair, lord and lady of the cliff-nest Flogalith. Do you know what Hórin has also told me they are?

'They are the siblings of Vethúg Wintermind, children of Hrímil Frost-heart herself! Hórin says it's his personal mission to burn every branch of that cursed family tree, and I say we help him do it!

'I do not think you can slay them alone, ${PLAYER}, despite your considerable skill, but if you do manage to destroy them I know you will receive a handsome reward.''You have done the deed? It is good to know there are two fewer of Hrímil's vile children in the world, for the evil in their hearts posed a great danger to all those who do not claim such parentage as theirs. I trust you will know what to do should you encounter any more of her foul brood!'The Angmarim have been allowed passage into Welkin-lofts by the Frost-horde, but for what purpose did they come to these high peaks?The Angmarim have made camp south of Fellgát.

You should find Mullach Cagar.Find Mullach Cagar, the Angmarim camp south of FellgátYou have discovered the Angmarim camp of Mullach Cagar.

You should search the camp for clues to the Angmarim's purpose here.Search inside the tents at Mullach CagarYou have found a strange staff in Mullach Cagar.

You should investigate it more closely.Examine the mysterious staff on the table in the Angmarim tentYou have found a mysterious staff in the main tent of Mullach Cagar. You feel it must be a powerful evil artifact.

You should destroy the mysterious staff.Destroy the mysterious staffThe staff has completely rebuffed your attack.

You should investigate the staff again.Once again examine the mysterious staff on the table in the Angmarim tentThe mysterious staff cannot be destroyed through any means you currently have at your disposal.

You have decided you must take the mysterious staff with you.Take the mysterious staff from the table in the Angmarim tentYou now have the mysterious staff in your possession. The nausea and paranoia it causes is slowly increasing.

You should return to Hórin and Molkha on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.Talk to Hórin in the valley'Our next objectives should be to investigate what the Angmarim are up to, and to do whatever damage we can to the nest of drakes above us. Molkha has located an Angmarim camp to the south-east, not far from here, called Mullach Cagar. I trust you, mighty ${PLAYER}, can handle a small group of Angmarim on your own. I am going to stay here with Molkha to attack this nest of drakes. If you would prefer to handle the drakes yourself before we move on, I will not stop you! Most importantly, I need you to find some evidence of why the Angmarim chose to come all the way up to the Welkin-lofts in the first place. They risked much to get this far.'This ornate staff has been placed in a prominent position in this central tent, surrounded by a runic circle and many-faceted crystals. What ill-intentioned ritual were the Angmarim performing here?

Standing beside the staff makes you feel unpleasantly queasy; you are overcome with a sensation of great distrust. The purple glow of the gem mounted atop the staff fills your vision and you are falling, falling....

You snap from your reverie. This is an artifact of evil, and you should destroy it if you can.The staff remains unbroken.

You cannot leave it in the possession of the Angmarim, for they will use it for some evil purpose. You must take it with you. Perhaps Hórin will know of a place where this artifact can be made safe?'${PLAYER}, you return! Did you find anything in Mullach Cagar? Wait... something about your demeanour has changed. What has happened?'

You show Hórin the staff. His eyes widen and his skin blanches.

'What in the name of the First Crafter is THAT?'

You explain that you found it in the Angmarim camp and believe it to be a powerful artifact of evil. You tell him too that it resisted your efforts to destroy it.

'Well, I think you were right to take it. We can't let the Angmarim keep such an artifact of evil. But I am no expert on the subject of fighting such magic! Who knows what might be unleashed if we did manage to destroy it? I think it might just be best for you to hold onto it for now. You are the most powerful among us, and we don't have time to cart it off to your Wizard-friend Gandalf! We have a war to fight!'Hórin is leading an expedition into the peaks of Welkin-lofts to search for Warlord Dushtalbúk and Loknashra.Hórin has asked you to help Dréri and Náth prepare the camp for incoming reinforcements.

You should complete quests for Dréri and Náth.Complete quests in the Welkin-lofts for Dréri and Náth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fellgát has been cleaned up and is ready for more dwarves.

You should talk to Hórin in Fellgát.Talk to Hórin'We have come to these high peaks in search of the hobgoblin leader Warlord Dushtalbúk and his advisor Loknashra. Ausma's scouts spotted them leaving the Stonejaws and marching in this direction with a sizeable troop of soldiers. We do not know their goal here, or why they left the safety of their stronghold, but this is an opportunity we cannot pass up! If we catch Dushtalbúk out in the open on these mountain slopes, we can deal a major blow to Hrímil's forces.'

His face hardens, and he looks towards the sky, still haunted by his previous experience with the Dragon.

'We must defeat the leaders of the Orcs, hobgoblins, and whatever else remains under her sway before engaging Hrímil directly. She is more than enough for an entire army to handle on her own, trust me.

'Judging by the state of this place, we are on the right track. The hobgoblins must have passed through here and abandoned this camp. We cannot pass on such an advantageous defensive position for our own base of operations, so I must ask you to help clean up this mess. I know this is beneath your station, ${PLAYER}, but we are short-handed. Reinforcements will be arriving shortly, so this place needs to be in better shape! Dréri and Náth will take charge of this effort.

'In the meantime, Ausma's apprentices Kyrstig, Molkha, and Klúso have gone ahead to locate the hobgoblin force. It is a shame Ausma could not join us herself, but she is still injured from her attack on Dushtalbúk. After we sort this place out, you and I will go looking for the hobgoblins.''Good work, ${PLAYER}! Fellgát looks much more like a proper camp now, and worthy of the Gabil'akkâ! Dréri and Náth will stay here until reinforcements arrive and we locate the hobgoblins, but you and I have some mountain-trekking to do.'Snow-beasts have made their home in Grymmclúd, the Roaring Stones.A pack of snow-beasts has been discovered in Grymmclúd, near the Clovengate.

You should defeat snow-beasts and their pack-leader, Stormbár, in Grymmclúd.Defeat StormbárDefeat snow-beasts in Grymmclúd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kyrstig can be found near Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold.

You should talk to Kyrstig.Talk to Kyrstig'I discovered a pack of vicious snow-beasts living in a craggy area near the Clovengate. I have taken to calling it Grymmclúd, or the Roaring Stones, because you can hear the echoing roars from quite far away. So? What are you waiting for?'

Kyrstig looks at you expectantly.

'I don't need to convince you that a pack of dwarf-eating beasts so near the road is dangerous, do I? Please clear the place out, ${PLAYER}!''Did you clear out those snow-beasts? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Snow-beast ambushes are not a pretty sight, and now our reinforcements need not fear one. They will have enough to worry about with all these hobgoblins and Angmarim around!'The ancient dwarf-fort known as Bagud-dum has been taken over by the Angmarim. There they plan to perform an ancient ritual which might reveal their true motives.Hórin is standing by outside Bagud-dum.

You should speak to Hórin and complete 'Instance: The Secret Ritual'.Talk to Hórin outside Bagud-dum and go with him to investigateHórin has dragged you out of Bagud-dum.

You should talk to Hórin.Talk to Hórin just outside the door to the keep in Bagud-dumThe Angmarim cultists have taken over the dwarf-fort Bagud-dum.

You should complete objectives in Bagud-dum to prevent their plans from reaching fruition.Complete 'Apprentices of the Cult' for HórinComplete 'Spirits and Summoners' for HórinFind Loknashra inside the keep of Bagud-dumHórin is waiting for you outside Bagud-dum.

You should talk to Hórin.Talk to Hórin outside Bagud-dum'This must be where most of the Angmarim travelled. This is a large camp! No sign of Loknashra out here, though... she must be inside. I do not know what horrors the Angmarim have waiting for us inside, but we have to find that staff before they complete whatever evil ritual they mean to do within! We must sneak inside, and quickly!''We will enter Bagud-dum when you are ready.''Did you find Loknashra?'

You tell him that Loknashra has vanished, but you did what you could to hinder the efforts of the Angmarim.

'Where could she have gone? Well, if she lives, I'm sure we'll find out soon enough. There are other matters to attend to for now. We are nearly at the very peak of the mountain, and as we have not yet run into Warlord Dushtalbúk and his host, there is only one place left he is likely to be.''${PLAYER}? Can you hear me? ${PLAYER}! Oh thank the Valar, you are returning to consciousness! After that blast, I wasn't sure I would be able to drag you out in time. Fell spirits began to churn the very air inside that fort! I am not sure what happened after that... Is Loknashra still alive?'

You tell Hórin you aren't sure, but you want to find out and take action against the Cult of Drugoth.

'You want to go back in there? Truthfully I am not surprised! Go be a hero, then. I will wait for you here. Go find Loknashra, and bring her down if you can!'Klúso, another of Ausma's apprentices, has witnessed a disagreement about what to do concerning the local ice-giants.Hórin thinks the best course of action is to continue higher into the Welkin-lofts in search of Ausma's apprentices.

You should continue south and find Klúso.Find Klúso near Bazan-medanKlúso can be found near Bazan-medan.

You should talk to Klúso.Talk to Klúso near Bazan-medanKlúso is ready to give his scouting report.

You should talk to Klúso and complete 'Instance: The Tipping Point'.Talk to Klúso and hear his reportKlúso can be found west of Bazan-medan.

You should talk to Klúso.Talk to Klúso near Bazan-medanHórin can be found next to Klúso, west of Bazan-medan.

You should talk to Hórin.Talk to Hórin near Bazan-medanA battle between the Orcs and hobgoblins has erupted in the ice-giant settlement of Thyrstáth.

You should complete objectives in Thyrstáth for both Klúso and Hórin.Complete 'Three Faction Battle!' for KlúsoComplete 'The Unyielding and the Overwhelming' for KlúsoCall Hórin and help him with 'Caught In The Middle'You should talk to Hórin.

Use the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.Call Hórin and talk to himYou have defeated the Orcs and hobgoblins, and possibly earned some favour with the ice-giants.

You should find the door to the main keep, in the south-eastern reaches of Thyrstáth.Find the door to the main keep in south-east ThyrstáthYou should talk to Hórin.

Use the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.'For now, we should continue up the mountain. We still need to find the hobgoblins and the rest of the Angmarim. Let's continue south and find the Father's Path again and see where it leads. Molkha will head back to Fellgát, and join us again when we find the hobgoblins. Klúso should be the next scout we come across. Hopefully he has some more information for us. Keep that staff safe, and let me know if you start hearing voices in your head, or if any other horrible things start happening!''${PLAYER}! You have come just in time! Warlord Dushtalbúk was just here, and you are going to want to hear this!''It was just a short while ago. I was scouting this area, when I suddenly heard something...''I'm quite fortunate none of those Orcs or hobgoblins spotted me. Even if they are at each other's throats, they have one thing in common: they share a hatred of dwarves! Dushtalbúk and most of the hobgoblins continued up the mountain, but some of them are just ahead, fighting the Orcs! What should we do? Those ice-giants did not seem particularly friendly, either!''I did not expect the Orc and hobgoblin feud to erupt right in front of us! This is a golden opportunity! We can take down both forces while they're distracted fighting each other. As for the giants... perhaps we can convince them to side with us instead of the Frost-horde. You have made alliances with giants in the past, yes? It is risky, but on occasion they have proved an honourable people. Klúso, stay here and watch for Orc or hobgoblin reinforcements. Come, ${PLAYER}, we have work to do!''We've done all we can out here. Let us make for the entrance to the main keep of Thyrstáth. With luck, our actions may have earned some good will from the ice-giants, and we can negotiate with their leader.''This is it. I hope you're ready for some dwarf-diplomacy!'The leaders of the Orc and hobgoblin factions battling in Thyrstáth may not be able to defeat each other, but you are more than a match for them.The leaders of the Orc and hobgoblin armies battle each other in Thyrstáth.

You should defeat Nargákh the Unyielding and Ufmazat the Overwhelming.Defeat Nargákh the UnyieldingDefeat Ufmazat the OverwhelmingUse the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.

You should talk to Hórin.Call Hórin and talk to him'The two leading the Orc and hobgoblin forces are known as Nargákh the Unyielding and Ufmazat the Overwhelming. They both think very highly of themselves, but I have seen them enter single-combat with each other several times, and it always ends in a draw, with both retreating.

'I have a feeling you will be more than a match for them both!''Hah! "The Unyielding?" "The Overwhelming?" Neither was true!

'How do they come up with these titles?'While the Orcs and hobgoblins are busy fighting each other, they won't be expecting an attack from you!The Orcs and hobgoblins are engaged in a battle in the ice-giant settlement.

You should defeat Orc-kind in Thyrstáth.Defeat Orc-kind in Thyrstáth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Use the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.

You should talk to Hórin.Call Hórin and talk to him'Bah! I wish I could crack some Orc-skulls with you, but I understand the need to watch the road. We wouldn't want their reinforcements to come up from behind and flank you, after all.

'Kill a few for me, won't you?''Hah! They didn't expect us! It is always a pleasure to fight by your side, ${PLAYER}.'A runner from Scout-master Ausma has found you. Your orders are to assist Hórin in the peaks of the Welkin-lofts!Ausma has sent word that the hobgoblins are moving into the Welkin-lofts.

Your orders are to assist Hórin with tracking them down. You will find Hórin at a camp in the northern reaches of the Welkin-lofts called Fellgát.Talk to Hórin in Fellgát, a camp in the northern reaches of the Welkin-lofts'${PLAYER}! I have new orders from Scout-master Ausma for you! She says that Warlord Dushtalbúk and Loknashra have left Shakhajât with a host of hobgoblins, and are moving toward the Welkin-lofts. You are to meet Hórin and assist him as soon as you are able!

'Look for him in the northern reaches of the Welkin-lofts, at a camp called Fellgát.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! Ausma's runner must have found you. Welcome to the top of the world!'Hórin has discovered that the ice-giants in Thyrstáth keep treasures of the ancient Gundabad dwarves in their hold.Plundered dwarf treasure can be found inside the giant-hold of Thyrstáth.

You should collect plundered dwarf treasures.Collect plundered dwarf treasure (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Use the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.

You should talk to Hórin.Call Hórin and talk to him'While we were making our way through Thyrstáth, I spotted a chest of dwarf-make. The giants must have stolen it from one of our ancient holds in Gundabad! I say we recover such treasures as we can on our way out!''For how long have the giants hoarded these dwarf treasures? I am glad to restore them to their rightful holders, though their original owners be long-dead. These artifacts belong to dwarves, not giants, and we will ensure in dwarf-hands they stay from now on!

'Thank you for the help, ${PLAYER}.'Crithon is concerned by the increased population of badgers surrounding the river leading to Pelargir.Crithon has asked you to drive away badgers around the river Erui south-west of Imloth Melui.Shoo badgers around the river Erui away (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The badger problem has been addressed. You should report your progress to Crithon.

Crithon is in Imloth Melui.Talk to CrithonCrithon has asked you to deliver your report to Arlach.

Arlach can be found in Arnach.Talk to Arlach'Ah, stranger! Please, if you could spare a moment.

'We are well under way with restoration efforts in Gondor, rebuilding after the war as you know. I have been overseeing the restoration of farmland. I am a bit concerned about the increased population of badgers gathering to the south-west. Normally, these animals are harmless, but they are burrowing and digging much deeper and more frequently around the banks of the river Erui.

'I foresee this having long term effects on the farming efforts in Arnach. Could you aid me in driving them away? We would be most grateful.''Yes. It seems the badgers have been driven off for now. They will eventually return, I'm afraid.

'I imagine the farmers in Arnach should be pleased by this news. We will have to make plans for the future if the badgers continue to pester the river Erui.'

Crithon puts up his hand.

'Ah, could you please deliver a message to Arlach in Arnach?

'He is the one who specifically posted this request.''Huh? Oh, did Crithon send you?'

Arlach keeps busy in his work.

'That man gets on my nerves. I posted about the badger problem a long time ago, but I suppose he did follow through with it after all. If only that were the only thing hindering progress in these farmlands.

'This problem is a little bit more urgent and I would prefer not to involve Crithon.'After a long journey, Othor has arrived at Pelargir with a rag-tag group of Corsairs.According to Othor, there is a food stall run by Haradrim towards the southern end of West Pelargir.

You should find it.Find the food stall run by HaradrimYou have found the food stall in West Pelargir.

You should talk to Jódha to order food.You have found the food stall in West Pelargir and given your order.

You should wait for Jódha to finish cooking.Wait for Jódha to finish your orderJódha has finished cooking your food.

You should talk to her at her food stall in West Pelargir.Talk to JódhaYou have retrieved the food for Othor, Nasar, and the other Corsairs.

You should return to them near the West Pelargir gates.Return to Othor near the West Pelargir gatesNasar waits near the West Pelargir gates.

He seems to want to talk to you.'${PLAYER}, what a surprise! I'm glad to see you again, now that those dark days are behind us.

'Ah -- yes, that's Nasar. I'm not sure if he would remember you on account of his drunkenness when you met him. As for how we've wound up here... that is a long story. Suffice to say that my men and I could not extract any useful secrets from him, even after he imbibed all the ale you collected. And with the aid of some shared drinks, we befriended each other instead.

'Actually, would you lend me your ear? I'm unfamiliar with Pelargir, and while my presence seems to put the residents at ease, my Corsair companions are also fresh faces to the city. Walking around freely would not go well. But after such a long journey, I was hoping to raise our spirits with some food.

'I've heard there is a food stall run by Haradrim somewhere south of here, near the docks. Would you mind ordering something for us?''What are you doing, feeding an army? Ah, I jest! The food will be ready in a moment; just wait right there.''Here you go. If your small army is still hungry afterwards, do come back!'For about ten seconds, Nasar squints at you with a look of intense concentration. His eyes then light up, and a grin spreads across his face.

'Hah! I remember you! Othor didn't think I would, but I do! How could I forget the one who supplied me with all of that ale? Ah, here, let me help you distribute the food....

'Othor hasn't told you why we came to Pelargir, has he? After the war, I went searching for other wayward Corsairs, and he came along to protect me. Not that I needed the protection, of course, but he's a good sort to have around!

'That's how we all found each other. We may be stranded here with no ships to take us home, but at least we are not alone.'The defender at Minlos beacon tells you that trouble is brewing at Tumladen.The defender at Minlos beacon has asked you to speak to Cúdor in Tumladen.

Cúdor can be found at Tumladen to the west of Minlos beacon.Talk to CúdorCúdor has informed you of an Orc party which has begun to corrupt the bears of Grafeleg.

Grafeleg can be found north of Tumladen.Defeat Grafeleg bears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Grafeleg fugitives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat a Grafeleg matron (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat ZagrazgYou should tell Cúdor that the threat in Grafeleg has been addressed.

Cúdor can be found in Tumladen.Talk to Cúdor'${PLAYER}, I have an additional request if you would be so kind.

'While we've secured the road to Tumladen, I have also received word that trouble is afoot.'

The defender looks westward.

'Please follow the road to the west to Tumladen and speak to Cúdor. He will surely fill you in on what is happening.''Ah, so you must be ${PLAYER}.

'I was notified of your imminent arrival. I won't waste your time.

'To the north of Tumladen, there is a cave known as Grafeleg. It is a well known bear den in these parts. Most of the townsfolk keep away from it.

'Our scouts chased a party of Orcs to the cave giving us the most unexpected of outcomes: the Orcs have begun to use and corrupt the bears for their own nefarious purposes. We cannot allow this to continue in such close proximity to Tumladen.

'Go to Grafeleg, and defeat the Orc captain Zagrazg and the Grafeleg matrons. If this unlikely alliance is to grow, it will only mean the worst of trouble on our doorstep.''A job well done, ${PLAYER}.

'With Zagrazg gone and the Grafeleg clear, the townsfolk can walk freely in peace.

'Tumladen thanks you this day.'Asórkho regrets his actions during the war.Asórkho has asked you to hunt some more boars for fresh meat.

You can find boars in the boar wallow north-east of Halach.Hunt boars for fresh meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have obtained a good amount of fresh boar meat.

You should return and talk to Asórkho near the boar wallow.Asórkho has given you preserved meat to give to the townsfolk of Halach, and asked you to keep his identity a secret.

You should return to Irodon in Halach.'You found me in the middle of preparing meat from a previous hunt. I came here for more fresh meat, but I confess that hunting tires me quickly, and I am at my limit today.

'If you wish to help, could you hunt some of the boars here?''A mighty hunter, you are. I shall take this fresh meat to preserve for another delivery. If you intend on returning to the townspeople, please give them these meats I have finished preparing.

'I expect they are waiting for your answer to their question. It is... a difficult situation. If you must give them an answer, I would ask that you keep my homeland a secret. I am loath to show my face, for more reasons than just shame, but... I only want to be kind. I hope they will understand. And perhaps I will reveal myself, in time.''A harmless person who wishes to stay a secret for now? I admit that, had anyone else told me this, I would've grown warier. But your words hold weight here. I trust you.

'May this person find the courage to come forth one day. I'd like to thank them for all they've done.'Kúmri would like your help gathering berries so that he may have something to present to Onjópo in Pelargir.Kúmri has asked you to pick some berries outside of Ost Anglebed.

Find tart berries in the fields east of Ost Anglebed.Collect tart berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found enough tart berries to satisfy Kúmri.

Deliver the tart berries to Kúmri.Talk to Kúmri'Traveller.'

He dips his chin in a casual greeting.

'I must say, you look familiar. Perhaps we've seen each other on the road, or maybe even in battle. If so, it's good to see you again. If not, then it's a pleasure to meet you.

'Either way, my name is Kúmri, and I am hoping to travel to Pelargir. Word has reached my ears of a popular eatery by the ship-yards run by others who were left behind like me. There is berry that grows in this area that I'd like to bring with me. If they're cooking what I think they're cooking, I could see this fruit pairing well with those flavours. May I ask you to harvest some for me? My arm, you see—'

He extends his arm, slowly, until he winces and pulls it back.

'It's still healing.''Did you try one as you gathered them? They're terribly sour, aren't they?

'Thank you for doing me this kindness. Come see me in Pelargir, won't you?'You found an abandoned waggon with traces of a vile ichor that reminds you of the same substance found in Thaurisgar.You found an abandoned waggon with phials of a familiar substance. This could be the mode of transport Indagir used.

You should search the waggon to support your theory.Search the waggonThis seems like the same substance you encountered in Thaurisgar. There is a trail of broken phials.

