Inside the waggon are scattered phials of a green ichor that look eerily similar to you.

Beside the waggon is a spilled phial. There could have been a struggle here.'Huh? Who are you?'

The waggon driver rubs his eyes and tries to focus on you.

'My waggon?'

The driver nods his head.

'Some fellow requested a ride all the way to Linhir. I was happy to oblige, but I noticed the phials he was carrying with him had a very pungent and off putting odour. I questioned him about it and he got defensive and hit me... tried to steal the waggon. One of the patrols noticed and gave chase. So he grabbed what he could of his quarry and ran off. I don't know where he is.

'I am sorry.'Though there is no ship to take the Corsairs home, hope is not lost.Celebros has asked you to bring some sealed orders and a lockbox to Captain Thandor.

He stands watch near the East Pelargir gates.You still have papers to deliver to Nasar and his companions.

You should return to them near the West Pelargir gates.'Unfortunately, the war consumed most of our seafaring resources. We cannot spare a ship for your friends to return home. Do not fret; I may have a solution. If I can provide the materials and funds necessary, the Corsairs could work with our shipwrights to repair a damaged ship rather than build a new one entirely... and I daresay both groups could learn new things from each other.

'Please, wait right here. I must retrieve something.'

Celebros disappears into the manor. A while later, she returns with what looks like a collection of papers and a sturdy lockbox.

'Would you deliver these orders and the lockbox to Captain Thandor? He stands watch near the East Pelargir gates.

'And once that is done, please give your friends these papers, and let them know they are most welcome here. I would be happy to discuss the matter with them further.''Lady Celebros' lockbox? She did not tell you what this was for, did she? Then I suppose I shall find the answer here...'

As Captain Thandor reads the orders, he raises an eyebrow.

'Well... I was not expecting her to part with her heirloom just to fund this endeavour... but it is a noble cause, and I am glad to see it.

'I shall take things from here. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''Lady Celebros agreed to meet with us? And these papers with the seal of Sirgon -- now we may wander freely about the city. Despite every grudge she could hold against us... I can hardly believe it. We've found our way home.'

The soft smile on Nasar's face slowly transforms into a grin.

'No doubt the shipwrights of Pelargir have things to teach us, but I assure you, they shall not be the only ones teaching!'Deep in the Pit of Stonejaws, a grand tomb holds the remains of the many ancient dwarf-lords of Gundabad. The necromancer Loknashra, now empowered with the spirit of Drugoth, has returned to raise an army and claim her vengeance upon all those who wronged her.Find and speak to Kytstig at the entrance of The Houses of Rest.Talk to KyrstigPick up the summoning hornDefeat the risen dwarf-lordsDefeat LoknashraDefeat the wight of Vethúg Wintermind'That hobgoblin was formidable enough before she possessed the spirit of a Gauntlord in addition to her own! I think we need to hurry. I definitely saw Loknashra come in here, and she has no doubt already set to work disturbing the rest of my ancestors. Come on, let's go! Be brave, Kyrstig, be brave!'Deep in the Pit of Stonejaws, a grand tomb holds the remains of the many ancient dwarf-lords of Gundabad. The necromancer Loknashra, now empowered with the spirit of Drugoth, has returned to raise an army and claim her vengeance upon all those who wronged her.Complete 'Adkhât-zahhar, the Houses of Rest -- Tier 1'Deep in the Pit of Stonejaws, a grand tomb holds the remains of the many ancient dwarf-lords of Gundabad. The necromancer Loknashra, now empowered with the spirit of Drugoth, has returned to raise an army and claim her vengeance upon all those who wronged her.Defeat the risen dwarf-lordsDefeat LoknashraDefeat the Wight of Vethúg WintermindDeep in the Pit of Stonejaws, a grand tomb holds the remains of the many ancient dwarf-lords of Gundabad. The necromancer Loknashra, now empowered with the spirit of Drugoth, has returned to raise an army and claim her vengeance upon all those who wronged her.Complete 'Adkhât-zahhar, the Houses of Rest -- Tier 2'Deep in the Pit of Stonejaws, a grand tomb holds the remains of the many ancient dwarf-lords of Gundabad. The necromancer Loknashra, now empowered with the spirit of Drugoth, has returned to raise an army and claim her vengeance upon all those who wronged her.Defeat the risen dwarf-lordsDefeat LoknashraDefeat the Wight of Vethúg WintermindDeep in the Pit of Stonejaws, a grand tomb holds the remains of the many ancient dwarf-lords of Gundabad. The necromancer Loknashra, now empowered with the spirit of Drugoth, has returned to raise an army and claim her vengeance upon all those who wronged her.Complete 'Adkhât-zahhar, the Houses of Rest -- Tier 3'Deep in the Pit of Stonejaws, a grand tomb holds the remains of the many ancient dwarf-lords of Gundabad. The necromancer Loknashra, now empowered with the spirit of Drugoth, has returned to raise an army and claim her vengeance upon all those who wronged her.Complete 'Adkhât-zahhar, The Houses of Rest -- Tier 3+'Deep in the Pit of Stonejaws, a grand tomb holds the remains of the many ancient dwarf-lords of Gundabad. The necromancer Loknashra, now empowered with the spirit of Drugoth, has returned to raise an army and claim her vengeance upon all those who wronged her.Defeat the risen dwarf-lordsDefeat LoknashraDefeat the Wight of Vethúg WintermindBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete the Adkhât-zahhar, the Houses of Rest, tiers 1 and 2 instance deeds.'Deeds! Get your Adkhât-zahhar, the Houses of Rest Deeds here!

