The farming community of Glaniath lies north of this Corsair camp; perhaps you can find the rightful owner there.'My, what a surprise! Those Corsairs forced me into handing over several sacks of Glaniath's harvest. We can't recover everything, but I daresay your actions may have caused them to think twice about doing so again!'With the sudden return of the Iron Crown to the Witch-king of Angmar's ancient capital of Carn Dûm, a tenuous peace is broken and the lingering grip of the Enemy begins to close around the Hill-men of Angmar and the now-diminished Council of the North.With the sudden return of the Iron Crown to the Witch-king of Angmar's ancient capital of Carn Dûm, a tenuous peace is broken and the lingering grip of the Enemy begins to close around the Hill-men of Angmar and the now-diminished Council of the North.Complete 'Angmar Reborn, Chapter 1'Complete 'Angmar Reborn, Chapter 2'Complete 'Angmar Reborn, Chapter 3'Complete 'Angmar Reborn, Chapter 4'Complete 'Angmar Reborn, Chapter 5'With the return of the Iron Crown and its loyalists among the now-splintered Trév Duvárdain to Carn Dûm, a tenuous peace was broken and old foes of the Trév Gállorg sought new dominion over Angmar.Nekhtan can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar.

Soltakh has asked you to speak to Nekhtan about the recent rite of Clúcath between the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain. You should talk to Nekhtan.Talk to Nekhtan at Bail AvarcNekhtan can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar.

