'Talk to me one more time, and they're all yours!''Deeds, incoming!'Once the seat of the Witch-king of Angmar, the dread citadel of Gwathrenost casts a long shadow upon the city of Carn Dûm. All but abandoned after the Steward of Angmar was deposed, the remnants of the Iron Crown have crept forth from the shadows, seeking to master a lost artifact of the Witch-king and reclaim dominion of Angmar.Imprisoned Hill-men can be found at Gwathrenost.

Raith has asked you to free Hill-men that have been imprisoned by the Iron Crown from Gwathrenost.Raith can be found at Bail Avarc.

You have freed many of the Hill-men imprisoned by the Iron Crown from Gwathrenost. You should return to Raith.Talk to Raith at Bail Avarc'${PLAYER}!

'The Iron Crown has imprisoned tribesmen of the Trév Gállorg and the exiles of the Trév Duvárdain within the walls of the Witch-king's citadel. It is said they are kept confined within the heights of Gwathrenost and under constant watch.

'If we do not act swiftly, it will not be long before they become bódraillan—the oath-thralls of the Iron Crown!'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel.</rgb>'You have my truest thanks, ${PLAYER}. It is a great relief that you were able to free so many of our tribesmen and the good-hearted exiles of the Trév Duvárdain before the Iron Crown could work their evil upon them.

'To become one of the bódraillan is a terrible fate....'Once the seat of the Witch-king of Angmar, the dread citadel of Gwathrenost casts a long shadow upon the city of Carn Dûm. All but abandoned after the Steward of Angmar was deposed, the remnants of the Iron Crown have crept forth from the shadows, seeking to master a lost artifact of the Witch-king and reclaim dominion of Angmar.Iron Crown repositories containing scrolls of forgotten history can be found at Gwathrenost.

Raith has asked you to search the Iron Crown's repositories at Gwathrenost for scrolls of forgotten history, as the oppression of the Witch-king of Angmar and the Iron Crown has done much to obscure the true history of Angmar.Collect scrolls of forgotten history in Gwathrenost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Raith can be found at Bail Avarc.

You have collected several scrolls of forgotten history from the repositories at Gwathrenost. You should deliver them to Raith.'Have you a moment, ${PLAYER}?

'The Iron Crown keeps many repositories within the walls of Gwathrenost, and it is rumoured they contain scrolls that tell of the true history of Angmar. What such knowledge might mean for our people I cannot say for certain, but we shall have time enough to reckon with it after the Iron Crown is driven out of our lands.

'If you intend to brave the Witch-king's citadel, would you search for some of these scrolls?'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel.</rgb>'What have you found?'

You hand the scrolls to Raith and he hurriedly reads over them.

'It seems every day I learn more about the history of our people, my friend. Who can say what other lost knowledge might still remain hidden in Gwathrenost? That is a question for another day, I think.

'I thank you for your aid, ${PLAYER}.'Once the seat of the Witch-king of Angmar, the dread citadel of Gwathrenost casts a long shadow upon the city of Carn Dûm. All but abandoned after the Steward of Angmar was deposed, the remnants of the Iron Crown have crept forth from the shadows, seeking to master a lost artifact of the Witch-king and reclaim dominion of Angmar.Banners of the Iron Crown can be found at Gwathrenost.

Raith has asked you to destroy banners of the Iron Crown at Gwathrenost.Destroy banners of the Iron Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Raith can be found at Bail Avarc.

You have destroyed many of the Iron Crown's banners at Gwathrenost. You should return to Raith.Talk to Raith at Bail Avarc'It is a terrible sight to see so many banners of the Iron Crown again flying within Carn Dûm. We have done what we can to tear them down throughout the city, but the banners at Gwathrenost are too well-defended.

'Will you aid us, friend?

'If the Iron Crown is to be overthrown at last, the symbols of their oppression must be torn down!'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel.</rgb>'You have done well, ${PLAYER}.

'With each banner we burn and each symbol of the Witch-king we cast down, the grip of the Iron Crown loosens!'Gorhir looks out for his fellow labourers.There are thirsty labourers working in Halach.

Gorhir has asked you to bring water-skins to them.You have finished delivering water-skins to thirsty labourers in Halach.

You should talk to Gorhir at the pier.Talk to Gorhir'${PLAYER}! I've just refilled these water-skins. Could you hand them out to the thirsty folk around town?''Many thanks. Everyone is eager to rebuild, but that cannot happen in just a day. Our work must be slow and steady, and while we work, we must take care of each other.'The Battle of Uzdarulzahar has begun, and the hobgoblin forces must be defeated.The Battle of Uzdarulzahar is underway!

You should defeat hobgoblins in Uzdarulzahar.Defeat hobgoblins in Uzdarulzahar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The battle proceeds!Completed'The hobgoblins have succumbed to the Voice of the Dragon, but that has not made them any less dangerous! Go and defeat them before they overwhelm us!'You have defeated many hobgoblins in Uzdarulzahar, turning the tide of battle in favour of the Gabil'akkâ!King Elessar has summoned you to the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith, where he wishes to discuss his plans with you.Glindor has brought you to the Tower of Ecthelion, where King Elessar and Queen Arwen await you.Talk to Glindor in the Tower of EcthelionKing Elessar is ready to speak with you about his plans.Talk to King Elessar in the Tower of EcthelionKing Elessar and his advisors discuss his plan to tour the kingdom and heal the hurts caused by the war.Listen to the discussion of King Elessar's plansThalhír, the Warden of Laws, is in the Tower of Ecthelion and has been called to answer whether the Heirs of Castamir remain a threat to the peace of Gondor.Talk to Thalhír in the Tower of EcthelionKing Elessar and his advisors discuss his plan to tour the kingdom and heal the hurts caused by the war.Listen to the discussion of the Heirs of CastamirQueen Arwen is in the Tower of Ecthelion and wishes to speak with you about a special task.Talk to Queen Arwen in the Tower of EcthelionKing Elessar is in the Tower of Ecthelion, waiting to hear if you will agree to this new plan.Talk to King Elessar in the Tower of Ecthelion'Another adventure begins, ${PLAYER}, of a sort. It will not take long to learn if the Heirs of Castamir are truly gone, and when we have done so Elessar can tour his kingdom.

'Let us start by journeying to the Harlond, my friends. The south-harbour is nearest to the city, and from there we can proceed west in search of news.''King Elessar and Queen Arwen will see you now.''We accomplished much good in the fight against Mordor and the forces of Sauron, ${PLAYER}, and prevented the triumph of terrible evil! The War of the Ring, for so I have heard it called in the days since its ending, has left its mark upon us and upon our lands. Our victory came at great cost, and the losses suffered in its achievement still wound those of us who remain. Perhaps they always will. And yet, if I can ease the hurts of my kingdom, I would do it. Can I count upon you to help me with this aim?'

You assure Elessar that you are with him, and he smiles.

'I knew our minds would be alike in this. This, then, is my purpose: I wish to travel my kingdom, from town to town, speaking with the people. I wish to hear what it is they lack, and to provide it; I wish to know how the war has injured them, and do what I can to repair those injuries. I want my people to know that their King is with them, not a distant figure in the Tower of Ecthelion, but a man who knows them and will strive every day of his life to prove he is worthy of Gondor.

'I want to tour the kingdom, and see what I can do to heal the hurts of the war.''I hesitate to mention it, my King, for I understand the majority of your people are overwhelmed with happiness at both the successful conclusion of the war and with your marriage to the Queen. I do not wish to spoil the broth of positive sentiment by dwelling upon the inclusion of one or two poor ingredients, and those in such tiny quantities.'

Thalhír clears his throat and looks uncomfortable.

'But there have been whispers of discontent in the city following your happy marriage, my King. Few perhaps, but some. I am sure they will disappear in time, as did those of the supporters of the Withered Tree, but as of yet they remain. I have heard tell from other members of the Council that people in the lower circles of the city speak wishfully of the Heirs of Castamir, praying for their return and believing they soon will.''My husband so greatly desires to speak with his people and mend the pain of the hurts they suffered that I fear he will give no thought to his own protection, ${PLAYER}. I turn then to you, and to those others who hold him dear!

'I ask this of you, ${PLAYER}, and of my husband's boon companions: Legolas of Eryn Lasgalen and Gimli the Dwarf, of Erebor. Where Elessar wishes to venture, I ask that you three travel first, with your ears listening and your eyes sharpened. Look for any sign that the Heirs of Castamir remain a danger to the kingdom or to the King, and make the path he plans to travel as secure as you may.

'Only this will ease the burden of my heart.''You will do as my Queen requests? I think it will prove unnecessary, but I do not want my bride to worry if it might be prevented! Nor do I want my people to wait for any help I might have offered.

'It is not an easy riddle to solve, ${PLAYER}, but I think I have the answer. The three of you will go ahead of me to visit the towns and cities of my kingdom, keeping watch for any sign of the Heirs of Castamir or their supporters, as Arwen requests, but you will go not only in search of danger. You will also go as my emissaries, and to begin my own mission of aid, doing what you can to help the people with their concerns.

'When you have determined the Heirs of Castamir are of no real danger to myself or the kingdom, you will return to me and I will depart with my own travelling companions to further your work. If this will satisfy my Queen and my Council, then I suppose I must be content with the delay. It will be a balm to my spirit to know that you three, at least, will have begun my mission to heal the kingdom of its hurt.'With the shard of Tauressar destroyed, the oath-thralls freed, and the last remnants of the Iron Crown brought to ruin, a new day—uncertain, yet hopeful—dawns in Angmar.Crannog can be found at Fail-á-Khro.

You have followed Crannog and the Trév Gállorg to Fail-á-Khro to parley with the Trév Duvárdain. You should talk to Crannog.Talk to CrannogThe Trév Gállorg have gathered to Fail-á-Khro to parley with the Trév Duvárdain.

You should listen as Crannog addresses the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain.Listen as Crannog addresses the Trév Gállorg and the Trév DuvárdainThe Trév Gállorg have gathered to Fail-á-Khro to parley with the Trév Duvárdain.

You should witness the parley between the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain.Witness the parley at Fail-á-KhroCrannog can be found at Fail-á-Khro.

The parley has concluded. You should talk to Crannog.Talk to Crannog'Come, my friend. Let us return to Aughaire. It will do my heart good to see it once more.''You are welcome among us, ${PLAYER}, but this is a matter we must see to ourselves.

'There has not been such a parley between the Trév Gállorg and Trév Duvárdain in many years, and I do not know what it will mean for either of our peoples. I have not forgotten the misdeeds of the Trév Duvárdain under Domongart's rule, but Soltakh was among them, and he has changed. Though he is Trév Gállorg now, in truth, he is of both tribes—and that gives me hope that we might one day unite again.

'It has been long enough. It is time, my friend.''It is ended, ${PLAYER}.

'It lasted longer than I expected, but that is not unwelcome. Much remains to be settled in the days to come, but we will meet and overcome those challenges. The Trév Duvárdain have splintered, but I do not begrudge them their use of that name. It belongs to them, and I would not take it from them. Whether our tribes will unite in kinship as we did long ago remains uncertain, but that is a question for another day.

'Let us rejoice in our freedom!'After the fall of Mordirith and abandonment of Carn Dûm, the tribesmen of the Trév Duvárdain grew increasingly divided, leading many to forsake the Iron Crown. However, many still remained among the Trév Duvárdain, and either ignorant or wilfully blind to the true wickedness of the Iron Crown, they followed them to Mount Gundabad.Finrúth is prepared to tell the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.

You should talk to Finrúth.Talk to FinrúthFinrúth is recounting the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.Listen to Finrúth's taleFinrúth is ready to continue the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.

You should talk to Finrúth.Talk to FinrúthFinrúth is recounting the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.Listen to Finrúth's taleFinrúth is ready to continue the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.

You should talk to Finrúth.Talk to FinrúthFinrúth is recounting the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.Listen to Finrúth's tale'None of us will be spared... not the Trév Duvárdain, not even the rest of the Iron Crown!''My tale begins at Bálach Iaran, the Iron Pass....

'It was said that the reach of the Witch-king of Angmar stretched into the East during his reign. There sat a fortress known as Agal Dûn, and the Angmarim meant to claim whatever secrets laid forgotten within it. Above the fortress, legend spoke of a broken spire piercing the sky—Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire—and it was believed that powerful tools of sorcery might be found within it.

'All among the Angmarim had plans to find the power they sought. With a tool stolen from Barad Gúlaran, one among them thought to ascend to the now-vacant throne of Angmar. The tool he bore was called Máltagar, the Fell Graver, and it was possessed of some unearthly magic. Whispers and visions of the Dead came to all who drew too near to Máltagar, and its wickedness seemed to grow as if it were feeding upon us.

'It was borne across Bálach Iaran and we of the Trév Duvárdain followed the Iron Crown to Câr Bronach....''We pressed on to Agal Dûn, and it seemed for a time that the Angmarim of the Iron Crown meant to dwell within the old fortress.

'It had become like another Carn Dûm, and I began to wonder why they were so intent on returning to Angmar at all. We had left our foes behind, had we not?

'But it was never enough for the Angmarim, and their work had to continue....''In secret, the Iron Crown had sought for something far more powerful.

'Beneath Tûr Fúar, a terrible artifact had laid nigh-forgotten, but not to High Priestess Ásachal. In her studies, she had learned many things of Angmar at the time of its downfall and of the Witch-king's many evils that never came to light. Although nothing spoke so plainly of what she would find, I suspect she knew the nature of it. And she wanted it—that she might succeed where the Witch-king of Angmar had failed.

'One of her ilk, Rúvaran, was the man who stole Máltagar and with it, they meant to wrest the power of the Witch-king into their own hands. Her work took her often into the depths of Tûr Fúar, but none seemed to know where she laboured.

'I decided that I would find out....'You have infiltrated a meeting of supporters of the Heirs of Castamir, and should learn what you can of their operation and their plans to undermine the rule of King Elessar.A supporter of Castamir stands inside an abandoned home and bars your passage.Talk to the Castamir supporter inside the abandoned homeMaethon is somewhere within the abandoned homes taken over by supporters of the Heirs of Castamir.Find Maethon somewhere within the abandoned homes of LinhirMaethon is within one of the abandoned homes of Linhir now used by supporters of the Heirs of Castamir.Talk to MaethonMaethon asked you to introduce yourself to some of the supporters of Castamir in the cellar of the abandoned home.Maethon is in the cellar of an abandoned home in Linhir.Talk to MaethonSupporters of the Heirs of Castamir secretly meet in a cellar in Linhir.Observe the meeting of the Castamir supportersTumúldo Fierce-water, emissary from Umbar, is interested to speak with you.Talk to Tumúldo Fierce-waterSupporters of the Heirs of Castamir secretly meet in a cellar in Linhir.Observe the meeting of the Castamir supporters and the emissaries from UmbarMaethon is in the cellar of an abandoned home in Linhir.Talk to MaethonSupporters of the Heirs of Castamir secretly meet in a cellar in Linhir.Observe the meeting of the Castamir supporters and the emissaries from UmbarMaethon is in the cellar of an abandoned home in Linhir.Talk to MaethonSomething has happened upstairs!Follow Maethon upstairs and learn what has happenedTumúldo Fierce-water has been grievously wounded, a deadly blade buried in his back.Examine Tumúldo Fierce-waterTumúldo Fierce-water lies dying, attacked by the supporters of Castamir.Hear what transpiredNakási Wave-reaper desires vengeance upon the Heirs of Castamir, and has challenged you to stand with her against them.Talk to NakásiTumúldo Fierce-water is on the very precipice of death.Hear the final words of Tumúldo Fierce-water'None of these vermin remain alive in this place, Tumúldo. You are avenged upon them.'

Nakási turns her eyes to you.

'Let us leave this place. Go ahead of me; I will carry the body of my husband. He deserves to rest forever in the Sea, and not in these vile houses of stone.''Maethon vouches for you, but you had better be on your finest behaviour while you are with us, ${PLAYER}. If you put a single toe out of line you will wish you hadn't.

'Praise the memory of Castamir, and all his heirs.''You found the right place! I am delighted for you to join us, my friend. To have another member of Elessar's court among our number seems almost too great a gift to be believed, but I will not turn it down!

'The meeting is soon to begin.''Introduce yourself to my friends, ${PLAYER}, and then we will begin.''Is it true you are close to the King? That will be useful indeed.'

You tell him that Maethon mentioned another member of Elessar's court is a supporter of the Heirs of Castamir. He studies you carefully.

'Aye. But you have yet to earn my trust, and until you do I will speak no more of those who should remain secret, for now. It should bring you joy to hear that the King is not as safe as he believes himself to be, and we may soon have the victory we seek.''Do not think you are one of us just because Maethon invited you to this meeting, ${PLAYER}. You have not yet proven yourself to me.

'I spoke with a gossipmonger in town who says that King Elessar has already departed Minas Tirith, and he travels this way! Perhaps you will soon have a chance to prove yourself to me after all.''I have nothing to say to you. Count yourself fortunate I do not cut you down where you stand. You may have deceived Maethon, but I am not fooled by this part you play, ${RACE}.''Ah, do not trouble yourself overmuch. They will warm up to you when they learn how useful you will be to us.

'I hope Elessar has enjoyed his kingship, for it nears its end!''It is said that when Balakhôr the Scourge met his end, it was at the hands of Dead Men that he met it. They say it was the King Elessar who commanded the killing blow, but others stood nearby: an Elf... a dwarf... a hero who bore the name ${PLAYER}.

'I had no love for Balakhôr, ${PLAYER}. Nakási and I preyed upon the ships he sent forth from Umbar before he came to power, but afterward, when we did not cease our roguery, he took one hand from each of us. They were ours to keep, and so we did, though we replaced them with these made of metal.'

Tumúldo raises his left hand, and it shines in the dim light of the cellar.

'The hands he cut from us were preserved, and now they decorate the cabin of our ship, each forever clasping the other, a sign of our love... and also of our desire for vengeance. Your part in the death of Balakhôr has robbed us of that vengeance.''I don't understand how this could have happened! We heard no word from the Heirs of Castamir who remained in Umbar, but I believed they would send messages as soon as they could. From where sprang this Kindred of the Coins, and how could they so easily overthrow our folk? The Heirs of Castamir were so established in the city... I cannot understand it....

'What has become of Saklaphêl, the widow of Balakhôr, or of Balakhâd his son? What are we now to do?''We have friends across the kingdom, hidden in plain sight. If we can rally the people of Gondor to our side....

'Aye, it could be done, ${PLAYER}. The folk of Gondor do not wish to be ruled by Elessar and his Elf-queen; nor do they wish to be made subservient to Umbar! If the Kindred of the Coins thinks to challenge us for the rule of Gondor once our plans bear fruit and King Elessar is slain, perhaps they will find we are not so easily conquered. I have to believe this is the way it will be.'Tumúldo Fierce-water lies on the cold stone floor in a pool of his own blood, a Gondorian blade buried in his back. His wife Nakási kneels by him, her eyes burning with fury and with unshed tears.'No, there is something about you that is different. You are not with this rabble, even as they seek to court you. Tumúldo and I know well that achieving a goal can at times mean you must ally with your enemies.

'Are you willing to die with these folk? Or will you stand with me to repay their treachery? The next one they stab in the back might be you, or it might be a friend, or it might be a lover. Tumúldo was all of these to me.''Nakási, my love... you were right...

'Gondor... must die...

'The Song...'Prince Durin has asked you to accompany Mótsog to the peak, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.You have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.Talk to MótsogYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.Talk to Mótsog on the slopeYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.Talk to Mótsog on the slopeYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.Talk to Mótsog beneath the peakYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.Confront Hrímil Frost-heartTwo leaders of the Angmarim have blocked your way up the slope to Hrímil Frost-heart, and they must be defeated if Mótsog is to reach the dragon.Defeat Ailgar and RúvaranYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.Confront Hrímil Frost-heartGorgar has succumbed to the voice of the dragon. He must be defeated if Mótsog is to face Hrímil Frost-heart.Defeat Gorgar the RuthlessAs the sun sets behind distant hills, Mótsog's time on this world draws near its end.

The dragon still lives.Stand with Mótsog'Durin's forces have opened an aisle for us. We must pass through it, and climb the mountain!

'Let none stand in our way.''It is a long way to the summit, friend of Durin. We cannot stop now.''We are nearly there.'

Mótsog looks out over the yawning brink, unconcerned by the great height. The waning light of day occupies his every thought.

'I will face the dragon, but I will need you to stand against her minions. Can you do this?'With the return of the Iron Crown and its loyalists among the now-splintered Trév Duvárdain to Carn Dûm, a tenuous peace was broken and old foes of the Trév Gállorg sought new dominion over Angmar.Nekhtan has offered to recount the tale of the rite of Clúcath.

You should talk to Nekhtan.Talk to NekhtanNekhtan is recounting the events of the rite of Clúcath between the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain.Listen to Nekhtan's tale of the rite of ClúcathNekhtan has concluded the tale of the rite of Clúcath.

You should talk to Nekhtan.Talk to Nekhtan'If only that was the end of the tale....''It is tradition that Clúcath is held at Fail-á-Khro. There, atop that hill and within sight of the Cairn of Honour, countless rites have been held through the long years of Angmar.

'After the Trév Duvárdain took the Stone of Clúcath from the Cairn of Honour, it was our duty to answer their challenge, and so we did. Crannog called upon us—his mightiest warriors—to accompany him to Fail-á-Khro.

'With our blades honed and our provisions for the journey prepared, we set out from Aughaire.''After Clúcath was ended, we had no choice but to return to Aughaire. What else could we do?

'Few spoke on the journey home, and I think we all feared what might befall us in the days that followed.

'But nothing happened. Perhaps we had been mistaken, I thought.'Ugarad the Harbinger intends to perform a secret ritual to impart the strength of the Gauntlord Drugoth to Loknashra of the Frost-bound. You and Hórin must stop this ritual before it is too late!Hórin is ready to stop the ritual taking place in Bagud-dum.

You should talk to Hórin.Talk to HórinThe Angmarim are attempting a ritual that will empower Loknashra!

You should defeat the approaching fell spirits!Defeat the approaching fell spiritsThe Angmarim are attempting a ritual that will empower Loknashra!

You should defeat the cultists performing the ritual!Defeat the Angmarim cultists'Ugh, my head! We made it outside. Are you all right?''We must find Loknashra quickly, before this ritual can be completed!'Durin has called for Dwarrowmoot, a gathering of the dwarves that will decide what can be done to wrest Gundabad from the claws of Hrímil Frost-heart.Prince Durin stands at the Thing-fold to begin the Dwarrowmoot for which he has called.Talk to DurinThe Dwarrowmoot has begun.Observe the DwarrowmootThe Dwarrowmoot has been interrupted by the dragon!Remain on your guard!The Dwarrowmoot has been interrupted by the dragon!Remain on your guard!Hrímil has escaped on powerful wings, making for the high peak, but her terror is plain to see.Stand with the dwarvesThe Dwarrowmoot came to a sudden end, but Durin has made a decision: it is time to face the dragon and reclaim the Mountain-home!Talk to Durin'Wish me good fortune in this, ${PLAYER}.''The Dwarrowmoot is over, ${PLAYER}. Now we have no choice.

'All will be decided in the moments to come!'You have reached the end of the Father's Path, and Warlord Dushtalbúk must be ahead. His reason for marching to the mountain's peak is about to be revealed....Hórin is standing by with the dwarf forces.

You should talk to Hórin.Talk to HórinYou have tracked the hobgoblins to the end of the road.

You should follow Hórin and find the hobgoblins.Find the hobgoblinsYou have tracked the hobgoblins to the end of the road.

You should follow Hórin and find the hobgoblins.Follow Hórin to the hiding spotYou have found Gorgar at the end of the road. He must be the hobgoblins' reason for coming here!

You should watch and listen as events unfold!Listen to the conversationThe hobgoblins will soon be upon you!

You should return to the Gate of Uzdarulzahar and summon your forces!Return to the Gate of UzdarulzaharThe hobgoblins will soon be upon you!

You should blow the horn to summon your forces!Blow the horn to summon your forces!The hobgoblins will soon be upon you!

You should wait for your forces to arrive!Wait for your forces to arrive'The hobgoblins and our own forces are approaching! Be ready for a battle!''We don't know what we're walking into here, so I will hold back the main force for the moment, but this is the end of the road! Dushtalbúk MUST be up here. The two of us are going to go ahead, and sound the horn when we want our forces to advance.'Sant Lhoer, known as the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm, is a dank place teeming with deadly plants, trees, and flowers, the likes of which have rarely or never been seen before in Middle-earth. Beyond the foetid, beryl-green waters which flow through Sant Lhoer, rise immense glass structures, including Bâr Heledh, the Glass House. It is here that the sorceress Oganuin plies her craft, experimenting upon creatures, plants, and people alike. To what end, and for what purpose? One can only assume the darkest of designs.Rhúnelleth has suggested that you speak with Dolág, whose brother went missing while scouting the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm.

Dolág is at Bail Avarc, near Carn Dûm.Talk to DolágDetermined to rescue her missing brother, Dolág has asked you to meet her at the entrance of Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens.

The Poison Gardens are located in Carn Dûm.Talk to Dolág within Sant Lhoer, the Poison GardensDolág has met you inside the gate of the Poison Gardens and is waiting for you to press on. You should look for her missing brother.Enter Sant Lhoer and search for some sign of MálruvWhile exploring Sant Lhoer, you have come across a glass gazebo. You should search inside for signs of Málruv.Search the gazeboWithin Sant Lhoer you have come across an Angmarim sorcerer, Cráthair, and his companion, the Jorthkyn Tarkka-oka. The latter is like nothing you have ever seen before. This must be one of Oganuin's foul experiments! You should defeat the pair.Defeat CráthairDefeat Tarkka-okaWithin an iron and glass gazebo in Sant Lhoer, you were set upon by Tarkka-oka and his Keeper, Cráthair. Upon their defeat, you found an iron key.

Dolág has joined you in the gazebo and is waiting to speak with you.Talk to DolágYou have discovered an iron key on the body of Cráthair. Dolág thinks it may unlock a gate she saw on the northern end of the Poison Gardens.

You should search for and unlock the north gate.Search for the north gateYou leave the Poison Gardens behind and make your way towards enormous structures of iron and glass. You should continue searching for Málruv.Continue searching for MálruvYou have discovered massive glass and iron greenhouses within Sant Lhoer. Wait for Dolág to catch up to you and then speak with her.Wait for, and then talk to, DolágYou stand before Bâr Heledh, the Glass House of Carn Dûm. Within its metal and glass walls the sorceress Oganuin practices her fell crafts, creating abominations and twisting living things towards unnatural ends. You must defeat her and search for signs of Málruv.Defeat High Cultivator OganuinYou have found Málruv, and rescued him from the machinations of the Angmarim sorceress, Oganuin. You should speak with Málruv.Talk to MálruvAfter defeating the sorceress Oganuin, you rescued Málruv and saw to his well-being. His worried sister is now waiting to speak with you.

You should talk to DolágTalk to DolágDolág waits to speak with you at Bail Avarc, near Carn Dûm.Talk to Dolág at Bail Avarc'Beyond the iron gates of Sant Lhoer lie deadly gardens and glass houses full of fungi spewing forth noxious spores. Some of the plants within the Poison Gardens can kill one in an instant! Beyond the gardens, across the teeming rivers of green liquid, is Bâr Heledh, where an Angmarim sorceress is said to be experimenting upon plants, creatures, and free-folk alike. There are things which should never be attempted, and I fear she has gone far beyond that limit. I beg you to put an end to her endeavours.

'Before you venture into Sant Lhoer, you should speak with Dolág. Her brother Málruv was attacked and she tracked his captors here. She is nearly grieved enough to go in for him by herself, but if she did so, I fear she would not return.

'Please, offer her your aid if you are able.''What sort of a vile world is it that we live in?''Who are you? I do not know you. Rhúnelleth sent you? The Elf meddles and has not stopped pestering me since I arrived here.'

She sighs and collects herself.

'In fairness, I have appreciated her concern, and she kept me from rushing into that foul place without a plan. I have scouted at the gates of the Poison Gardens, and I see much movement beyond its metal bars. I doubt I could proceed against so great a number of enemies, but you look formidable enough to give me some bit of hope.

'If you will lead the way, I will follow close behind. Perhaps Málruv can be found within! Let us meet then, in Sant Lhoer.''Won't you aid me in freeing my brother from the Iron Crown?''You came! I... admit I did not actually expect you to.'

She is silent a moment, and when she speaks again, her shoulders are set more firmly.

'My gratitude runs deep. Let us go forth then, but take care. The waters here are foul and have a fell look about them. I shall follow behind.''What has happened to this giant? It looks nothing like the Jorthkyn I have encountered before. There is something strange going on with the creatures in this garden. The Orcs and trolls, and now the Jorthkyn - they all seem to be twisted, grotesque mutations. This is surely Oganuin's doing, if Rhúnelleth is to be believed. The Elf will be glad to know you put an end to this abomination of nature.'

You show her the iron key you found.

'A key! Now that must be for the gate to the north. I could see it far over the poison waters. Let us make our way there.''Look there, beyond the glass walls! There is some queer light flickering within. We have found Bâr Heledh, where Rhúnelleth says Oganuin is creating the creatures you have been fighting. Could my brother be within as well?

'Collect yourself, for I doubt not that she will have more fearsome surprises waiting.''I... greet you with joy, Southron. The things she planned for me....'

He shudders.

'You were just in time!''Words alone can not express my relief. Come, let us leave this foul place. Meet me back at Bail Avarc. I wish to get my brother to safety.''Welcome back, my new friend. Málruv is safe now, thanks to you. Though he is well in body, the horrors he saw within Bâr Heledh will stay with him all his days, I fear.

'However, I now have hope that people like you will help to create a new world where good folk are safe once more.'Determined to defeat Hrímil Frost-heart and reclaim Mount Gundabad once and for all, Prince Durin leads the Gabil'akkâ to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.Following the death of their chieftain, Hrungrod, at the hands of the dwarves, the heirs of Thyrstáth have pledged themselves into the service of Hrímil Frost-heart.Defeat the Heirs of ThyrstáthEnter AbnankâraFallen under the sway of Hrímil Frost-heart's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk leads the Orcs of Gundabad in defending the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.Defeat Thrall-lord DushtalbúkAfter suffering an unexpected defeat atop Mount Gundabad, Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, retreated to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra to tend her wounds and prepare for the final confrontation with Durin.Defeat Hrímil Frost-heartYou have completed the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra on Tier 1.Completed: Into the Hiddenhoard (Tier 1)'It is time, ${PLAYER}. Abnankâra lies just ahead, but to gain entry to its halls and its deepest chambers, we must overcome Hrímil's mightiest guardians. To win this final victory will be a difficult and costly task, but it is one we must undertake. If we do not stop Hrímil Frost-heart before she recovers from the wounds dealt to her by Motsóg, we may never have such an opportunity again. Such a thing must not come to pass!

