en spotted in the Pit of Stonejaws!

'I have had my scouts keep an eye out for her after she disappeared from the Welkin-lofts, clearly changed from that Angmarim ritual you and Hórin beheld. She had completely vanished from Gundabad, until now! Kyrstig has just sent word that there is new activity in the Houses of Rest, and she witnessed hobgoblins there first-hand! I want you to go with her and investigate the Houses of Rest. I have a feeling that Loknashra has returned to enact her vengeance upon us, and we must put an end to her plan before it is too late! Go, find Kyrstig with haste!''${PLAYER}! I have urgent news: Loknashra has been spotted in the Pit of Stonejaws!

'I have had my scouts keep an eye out for her after she disappeared from the Welkin-lofts, clearly changed from that Angmarim ritual you and Hórin beheld. She had completely vanished from Gundabad, until now! Kyrstig has just sent word that there is new activity in the Houses of Rest, and she witnessed the hobgoblins there first-hand! I want you to go to the Pit of Stonejaws and meet her outside the Houses of Rest. Investigate them with her. I have a feeling that Loknashra has returned to enact her vengeance upon us, and we must put an end to her plan before it is too late! Go, find Kyrstig with haste!''${PLAYER}! Did Ausma send you to assist me? Good. To be frank, I was afraid to go in there alone! This place was pretty quiet when last I scouted these tombs, but there has been a flurry of activity here of late. And it's not the Angmarim, it's the hobgoblins! If I had to venture a guess, I would say Loknashra has taken leadership of the hobgoblins that were spared the control of the Dragon Voice, and has sent them to the tombs. Hórin did say she swore revenge on everyone, right? I think they might be eager to turn our resting ancestors into their foot-soldiers!

'We have no other option but to go in there and stop her. It would take too long to wait for reinforcements. You're coming with me, right?''We really were just in time, ${PLAYER}! Can you imagine if the newly-restored Vethúg Wintermind was permitted to wreak havoc on our forces? The war would have been over... and not in our favour! It is a pity Loknashra escaped, but I don't think we'll see her again anytime soon. I hope not, anyway.

'You should return to Ausma and tell her what happened. I will stay here for now and make sure we didn't miss any wights or hobgoblins. And please thank her for sending you my way. I wouldn't have been able to do this without you!''We really were just in time, ${PLAYER}! Can you imagine if the newly-restored Vethúg Wintermind was permitted to wreak havoc on our forces? The war would have been over... and not in our favour! It is a pity Loknashra escaped, but I don't think we'll see her again anytime soon. I hope not, anyway.

'You should return to Ausma and tell her what happened. I will stay here for now and make sure we didn't miss any wights or hobgoblins. And please thank her for sending you my way. I wouldn't have been able to do this without you!''${PLAYER}! Tell me everything! Are the Houses of Rest free of evil?'

You tell Ausma of Loknashra's return, the unnatural animation of the dwarf-lords, Vethúg Wintermind's resurrection as a wight, and Loknashra's ultimate defeat.

'By the Valar! You were just in time to prevent a catastrophe! I am filled with amazement that you were able to defeat the newly-risen Vethúg Wintermind with so few! I am concerned to hear that Loknashra escaped, but she and Drugoth will need time to regain their power. They are certain to be off the table for the remainder of this war. For now, our top priority must be the defeat of Hrímil Frost-heart. One of us will send for you when we are ready to strike at the dragon's lair!'Berion would like your help speaking with tradespeople around town.Berion has asked you to speak with some tradespeople on his behalf.

Talk to tradespeople in Ost Anglebed.Talk to EithrielTalk to RaithgamTalk to BrechanYou have spoken with the tradespeople only to learn that none can take on an apprentice. You'll have to deliver the bad news to Berion.

Talk to Berion in Ost Anglebed.Talk to Berion'Excuse me. My name is Berion. I believe you saw me earlier, sitting by the front gate.

'I've been a soldier ever since I was tall enough and strong enough to hold a spear. I can't imagine doing anything else in life, but I can't carry on being a guardsman anymore.

'I was thinking of seeking apprenticeship with one of the tradespeople here in Ost Anglebed. If one of them accepts me, I may quit the guard knowing I'll still be able to provide for myself.

'Could you speak with the smith, the baker, and the tanner while I meet with others? We can meet back here later.'His face falls when you deliver the news.

'I had forgotten about that incident with Brechan. Ah, well, I suppose there's nothing to do but speak with the sergeant. Thank you for trying, friend.'Eithriel laughs at you.

'Do I want an apprentice? I wake up before the cocks crow and move my own weight in dough twice over before dawn rears its head. Of course I want an apprentice!

'The trouble is, I haven't coin enough to hire one.

'You tell Berion that I'm sorry, and to come see me for some free bread if he ever needs it, assuming his pride will allow it.'The smith makes a long, low growling sound that you think might have been speech.

'My father regretfully declines to take any new apprentices at this time,' his daughter translates.

The old man grunts an affirmative.'Berion needs work, you say? Need I remind him that the last time he came to visit me he didn't make it within fifteen feet before the smell of the tannery stole the lunch from his stomach?'Grodris returns to defend her brood in the Isendeep. Defeat her and gain power for your side of the battle in the Ettenmoors.Grodris, the matron of the Wintersebb, now stalks the Isendeep mine in the Ettenmoors.

