You should mine crystals for Bráthi.Mine crystals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bráthi can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset.

You should return to Bráthi with the crystals that you have mined.'I have recently discovered a new crystal deposit in Gundabad. These crystals are rare and should be mined before they are collected or destroyed by our enemies. Will you mine these crystals for me?''Thank you! These crystals are indeed rare and a beauty to behold! What wonders are in Gundabad!'Rescued from the Battle at the Pelennor Field, a great mûmak works alongside the Temámir Dwarves to repair the harbour.Dingási has asked you to bring a crate of carrots from the Harlond's provisioner and bring it back to the mûmak.

The crate is next to the provisioner, in the Harlond, and the mûmak is north of the Harlond's walls.Pick up the crateYou should let Dingási know that Lokhûr is happily munching away at the carrots and other vegetables you brought from the provisioner.

Dingási is in the Harlond.Return to Dingási'Welcome to the Harlond. I can tell by your bearing that you are also not of these lands. My name is Dingási and I am in charge of the rebuilding the Harlond.

'Have you seen our great mûmak? One of the men here rescued her after the battle at the Pelennor Fields, and she's been a great help to us, moving the large blocks that we are using to repair the wall and buildings. She has a larger appetite than nearly any creature you shall ever meet, I promise you! If you have time, bring a crate of carrots from the provisioner, will you? She is due for a break and a treat.''She's a beauty, isn't she? We shall have to bring her south when the weather turns cold again, but for now, Lokhûr gets green fields and bushy trees to explore.''Did you hear that? You have made her happy! Most excellent!''She's a beauty, isn't she? We shall have to bring her south when the weather turns cold again, but for now, Lokhûr gets green fields and bushy trees to explore.'The citizens of Umbar Baharbêl are wary of outsiders, but they no longer consider you a threat to their livelihoods, and you are welcome in the City of the Corsairs—at least for the moment.You must earn Neutral standing with the the Citizens of Umbar BaharbêlAfter the Battle of the Pelennor Fields, the stores of potions held at the Hall of the Gentle Hand were drained to meet the demands of the wounded soldiers returning from war. Though the lands are calmer, there are still ingredients whose locations are difficult or dangerous for common folk to access.Atharon has asked you to gather ingredients for potion making while you are searching the forest.

Fuingil and lethelin can be found in the forest and caves west of Imloth Melui.Collect fuingil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect lethelin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the plants and mushrooms to Atharon.

Atharon is in the Hall of the Gentle Hand in Imloth Melui.'Since you will be out in the forest, might I impose upon you another task as well? We have run low on both fuingil and lethelin, both of which can be found west of the city. Fuingil, also known as nightstar, is a mushroom which grows in dark places like caves, and lothelin is a plant which loves to spread across the forest floor. Both are essential in many of the potions we make here in the Hall.

'Please gather what you can and bring it back to me, and I shall reward you for your time.''These are quite good! They will make fine ingredients for our potions.'A young woman stands distraught that her father has lost his purpose in life after suffering the consequences of war.Sadrien has asked you to deliver a message to Halgúr at his homestead south of Imloth Melui.Talk to HalgúrHalgúr is ignoring you. Perhaps you can learn more by searching his homestead.Examine the rubbleThe homestead looks to have been ransacked.Investigate the food storesAll the edible food has been taken. The rest has been left to rot.Check on Halgúr's suppliesThe supplies have not seen much use. Halgúr seems to be working aimlessly.Investigate Halgúr's materialsThe materials have been destroyed. They will not see any use.Examine the ruinsPart of Halgúr's homestead has collapsed. Something terrible must have happened. Speak to Halgúr.Talk to HalgúrHalgúr does not wish to speak to you anymore. Perhaps Sadrien in Imloth Melui has more information on what transpired at the homestead.Talk to SadrienSadrien asks you to find Melnith's retreat east of Imloth Melui.Investigate Melnith's retreatInform Halgúr of Melnith's retreat. Halgúr can be found at his homestead south of Imloth Melui.Talk to HalgúrHalgúr is still not willing to listen. He needs to be encouraged in some way.Beckon Halgúr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have convinced Halgúr to meet you at Melnith's retreat.Talk to HalgúrHalgúr has a renewed sense of hope for the world. Inform Sadrien back in Imloth Melui.Talk to Sadrien'Could you spare a moment? You look as though war has painted a stroke on you. The war has taken the heart of my father. He idles in his work and has very little reason to speak to me. Could you possibly deliver a message?'

The young woman hesitates for a moment before whispering a message into your ear to deliver.

'His name is Halgúr. You can find his homestead south of Imloth Melui.''Leave me be, wanderer. I have no words for you.'

The man continues to bury himself in his work ignoring you.'What business do you have rummaging through my things? Leave at once!'

Halgúr has become agitated. Reminding him of the sorry state of his homestead has seemingly reopened a wound or a memory he would rather forget.'I must apologize. I knew he would be reluctant to speak to you.

'I had hoped that your experience in the war would still his fervour. His will to continue on with meaning was lost... along with my mother.'

Sadrien steels herself before continuing.

'After the war, many parties retreating would often trouble us on the way to Pelargir. My father's homestead was raided, ransacked and pillaged of anything valuable. He tried to stand his ground, but those brigands chose to ruin his home. My mother Melnith was inside when the building collapsed.

'So you see, reminding him of that moment may have angered him. There is something you should see.'

Sadrien tells you of a place Melnith used to frequent daily.

'Most of the time, when I would visit, my mother would be away. Father thought she was visiting the markets. So I followed her one day, at a distance. I never got too close, but there is a spot in the forest she visits daily. Perhaps there is something there that could help you.'The wolf mother seems to have been injured and cannot fend for herself. The wolf cub seems to be in high spirits, unaware of its mother's condition. It appears, from the food remnants and empty water dishes, Melnith frequented this cove daily to check on the wolf and cub.

Halgúr should be informed of this immediately.'Have I not suffered enough? Must you trouble me so?! My wife is lost to me. There is nothing left for me in this world!'

Halgúr begins to well up.'My beloved Melnith. So kind. So gentle. It is no wonder she spent many a twilight away tending to this area.'

Halgúr examines a ribbon on the wolf mother's neck.

'Nathemel. That is the name Melnith gave to this wolf mother.''Thank you so much for everything you've done, traveller. My father has a renewed sense of spirit and vigour. He has found purpose once again. Even I had no idea my mother tended to a wolf mother, but now we both have renewed purpose. We shall both endeavour to maintain the beauty of this land.'At the foot of the snowy peaks of northern Lower Lebennin, rumours of a terrifying beast haunting the woods have emerged to coincide with news of a hunter gone missing.Malbír has asked you to look for signs of his missing friend, Gúrayin, who was last seen heading north of Zarsatrâd.Search for GúrayinWhile searching for Gúrayin in Lower Lebennin's forest, you came across some dwarf-sized footprints. You should continue to follow the footprints and look for signs of Gúrayin.Continue searching for GúrayinAt the foot of a snowy mountainside you found a scrap of blue fabric. You should investigate the fabric.

The fabric is in Lower Lebennin, north of Zarsatrâd.Investigate the fabric scrapAs you leaned in to examine the scrap of blue fabric, a terrible beast roared and rushed forward to attack! You are sure that Gúrayin did not survive their encounter with the snow-beast. You should let Malbír know what you found.

Malbír is at Zarsatrâd.Return to Malbír'Greetings, stranger. Tell me, have you seen my friend, Gúrayin, on your travels? No? Ah, more's the pity. I am quite worried about him. He went hunting yesterday and has not yet returned. No one else is concerned, but I swear I saw an enormous beast in the woods north of here and I am worried.

'Will you keep your eyes open for any sign of my friend? I would greatly appreciate it! You will know him by his blue cloak!''Your grave expression tells me that you have no good news to share.'

