'Talk to me one more time, and they're all yours!''Deeds, incoming!'Lágsaith's disinterest in mentioning the sewers' health hazards bothers Avlath.Use the Instance Finder to enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty.Enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficultyPiles of unidentifiable filth can be found in 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.'

You should destroy them.Destroy unidentifiable filth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lágsaith has recounted, in excruciating detail, the disgusting filth she and her comrades encountered while in the sewers.

You should tell Avlath in Bail Avarc.Talk to Avlath in Bail Avarc'A fresh face. You must be Lágsaith's latest victim, or will be soon. She usually saves her dramatic retellings for children, but even passing travellers will not be spared.

'The sewers expedition was not nearly as exciting as she makes it out to be. She completely skips over the "boring bits," as she would call them, for the sake of "better pacing." Thus she neglects to mention the filth we burned along the way.

'The children ought to know that infection and plague is no laughing matter. Make sure Lágsaith does not forget this either!'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.</rgb>'Lágsaith actually mentioned the filth this time? Then I'm satisfied. I didn't mean to sound so harsh earlier, but she wields power with her words, power that can be used for good.

'May her story remind the children to keep themselves healthy, for followers of the Iron Crown are not the only threats we face.'As Eávair and Borgach attempt to solve the issue of cleansing the sewers, Náchtan directs his efforts towards spreading information -- and hopefully, gaining some answers.Use the Instance Finder to enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty.Enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficultyFoul liquid can be found in 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.'

You should collect some samples.Lágsaith has described the foul liquid running through the sewers in vivid detail.

You should tell Náchtan in Bail Avarc.'You are a traveller, no? Have you ever seen anything like this before?' He procures a few phials of viscous, violently green liquid.

'The Iron Crown did not maintain their sewers very well. We gathered samples from there for further studying, but Eávair and Borgach -- ' He nods to the two women nearby who are in deep discussion. ' -- are still figuring out how to break down and cleanse it. These impurities must be harming the land in ways we do not understand.

'Lágsaith loves to recount our expedition, though she does not linger on the details. Stories spread by word-of-mouth can cover larger distances than we ourselves can travel. If she described the foul liquid to more travellers such as yourself, someone with new information might come forward and help us in our endeavours.

'Should you seek her out for the full account, make sure to remind her of this.'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.</rgb>'It is good to hear Lágsaith honoured your request. Maybe she will eventually recount these details on her own, without needing reminders. In the meantime, Eávair and Borgach will do what they can, while I keep an ear to the ground.'The layout of Carn Dûm's sewers is a mess. Aighrig's map is a work-in-progress, but it might also help you visualize Lágsaith's story better.Use the Instance Finder to enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty.Enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficultyMapping points can be found in 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.'

You should find them to complete the map of the sewers.Thanks to Aighrig's map, Lágsaith's tale became a little less confusing to follow.

You should return the map to Aighrig in Bail Avarc.'After our adventures in the east, it is strange to see you here in my homeland, ${PLAYER}. But you are a welcome sight.'

Lukhag chirps in affirmation.

'I am sure Lágsaith wishes to regale you with the tale of our expedition, so I will not keep you for long. But perhaps knowledge of the sewers' layout will allow you to appreciate her retelling more.' She hands you a map that has been sketched in a careful hand. 'I traced our steps while we were down there. Lágsaith would never admit this, but she needed the help; her sense of direction is atrocious.

'You may borrow the map until Lágsaith is finished with her retelling.'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.</rgb>'I trust that the map helped? It is rudimentary to be sure, but useful as well. Without it, we may have been lost forever.' A small smile cracks through Aighrig's serious countenance. 'I jest. But returning home would have been more difficult.

'The map only displays a fraction of the full sewer system. It is my hope that we will complete it on future expeditions. There is still much work to be done, after all.'Sant Lhoer, known as the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm, is a dank place teeming with deadly plants, trees, and flowers, the likes of which have rarely or never been seen before in Middle-earth. Beyond the foetid, beryl-green waters which flow through Sant Lhoer, rise immense glass structures, including Bâr Heledh, the Glass House. It is here that the sorceress Oganuin plies her craft, experimenting upon creatures, plants, and people alike. To what end, and for what purpose? One can only assume the darkest of designs.You have entered the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm, Sant Lhoer.

You should use the nearby summoning horn to call an ally, Forba, to your side.Pick up the summoning horn and call Forba to your sideYou should explore Sant Lhoer and look for the sorceress Oganuin.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You can use the 'Call Forba' skill to call Forba to your side in Sant Lhoer.</rgb>Search for Oganuin within Sant LhoerWithin Sant Lhoer you have come across an Angmarim sorcerer, Cráthair, and his companion, the Jorthkyn Tarkka-oka. The latter is like nothing you have ever seen before. This must be one of Oganuin's foul experiments! You should defeat the pair.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You can use the 'Call Forba' skill to call Forba to your side in Sant Lhoer.</rgb>Defeat Tarkka-oka and CráthairWhen you defeated Tarkka-oka and Cráthair, you acquired the key to the North Gate.

You should unlock the North Gate and continue on.

