'Talk to me one more time, and they're all yours!''Deeds, incoming!'Within the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm grow numerous plants, twisted and corrupted by the foetid waters of the rivers that flow through the area.Rhúnelleth has asked you to collect water samples from the Poison Garden and the Glass House.

The Poison Garden and the Glass House are in Carn Dûm.Collect water samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the water samples you collected to Rhúnelleth.

Rhúnelleth is located at Bail Avarc, outside of Carn Dûm.'I am curious about the waters that flow through Sant Lhoer, Carn Dûm's Poison Gardens. They are less potent than those of the rest of the city, thankfully, but they seem also to possess other attributes, both corrupting and empowering to the plants and creatures near to them.

'Take these phials and bring me samples from the flowing streams, that I might study the effect Helchgam's defeat has had. Take care that you do not let the waters touch your skin! Who knows what poisons yet lurk in those depths?'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens.</rgb>'Ah, you return! Come, let me see what the phials contain.'The Angmarim sorceress Oganuin has locked herself in Bâr Heledh, the Glass House within Carn Dûm, where she has been experimenting on plants, creatures, and monsters alike. Her creations skulk between the shadows in the gardens of Sant Lhoer.Dolág has asked you to collect samples of flesh from the creatures within Carn Dûm's Poison Garden and the Glass House.Collect flesh samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected the samples of flesh that Dolág requested. You should give these messy bits to her as quickly as possible.

Dolág is located at Bail Avarc, outside of Carn Dûm.'Oganuin has locked herself in her Glass House, where she and her followers experiment on plants and creatures alike. I have seen some of the Orcs that she has wrought her trials upon and the results have stricken me to the core.

'I know of a master hunter who wishes to study the flesh of the creatures she has altered. Bring me samples from creatures within her Poison Gardens and the Glass House. Knowledge of what she has done may help us to stop and even reverse the process.'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens.</rgb>'Ah, you return. A grisly task I set you upon, I know. Give to me the samples you gathered. I will bring them to my friend, and perhaps he will have some insight into what atrocities are being committed behind those dirty glass walls.'Within Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm, grow numerous plants, twisted and corrupted by the foetid waters of the rivers that flow through the area. Should these aberrations manage to make their way out of their dank garden, they could threaten the other plants, creatures, and peoples of Middle-earth.Galasdil has asked you to destroy any witch's crown plants that you might find within Sant Lhoer, the Poison Garden.

Sant Lhoer is in Carn Dûm.Put witch's crown to the torch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have put to torch many witch's crown, and Galasdil will be happy to hear of your efforts.

Galasdil is located at Bail Avarc, outside of Carn Dûm.Talk to Galasdil'Mae govannen. My name is Galasdil, and I was travelling through Nan Amlug when I came across a plant so strange I paused my journey in order to study its origin. My investigation led me through the wasted lands of Angmar, to here - the gates of Carn Dûm.

'Within Carn Dûm's Sant Lhoer grow numerous plants, twisted and corrupted by the foetid waters of the rivers that flow through the area. Among these is the corrupted witch's crown, whose seeds carry lightly upon the winds. Even now, I see small fluffs of seed floating through the dank air!

'If you are brave enough to venture into the Poison Gardens, put any of these plants you see to the torch. They must not be allowed to spread throughout Middle-earth!'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens.</rgb>'Welcome back. I can see by the smoke that lingers about you that you have been successful. May it be that your actions will keep these terrible creations from spreading into Angmar and beyond.'Unbeknownst to the Men of Cardolan, Sarch Vorn, an ancient temple of the Edain, has long served as the resting place of a malevolent spirit of the Elder Days known only as Hithrengor, the Grey Fear. Roused by the return of the Witch-king of Angmar, the Grey Fear has awoken from its slumber to once again spread terror and death across the ravaged lands of Cardolan.You have arrived at Sarch Vorn, the Black Grave.

You should collect the summoning horn. It will allow you to call Gorwen to your side at Sarch Vorn.Collect the summoning horn and call Gorwen to your sideThe Dead have overrun Sarch Vorn.

You should journey deeper into Sarch Vorn and search for Hithrengor, the Grey Fear.

