It would be safest to destroy them.Hopefully this action will diminish the powers of the Ruthless Dead, but only time will tell.A toymaker and souvenir crafter asks for assistance fetching a special, sunken, item.Tawardan has asked you to retrieve lengths of black sails from the sunken ships in the bay of the Harlond.Retrieve waterlogged fabric (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should bring the waterlogged sail fabric to Tawardan.

Tawardan is in the Harlond.'Hello, hello! If you have come looking for one of Tawardan's famous toy ships, you are sadly out of luck, my friend. I have only two left, and they have already been purchased.

'Oh, you are not here to shop? More's the pity for you! You could be taking home one of my handmade Corsair ships! The perfect souvenir to help you remember your time in the Harlond! Have you been out to see the sunken ships? King Elessar himself swept into this harbour with an army of the Dead! My toy ships are made with black sails whose cloth was gathered from those very ships!'

He dramatically deflates, sighing heavily.

'Alas, I have run out of fabric. You see, there were a few ships close enough to the dock from which I was able to reach out and tear free large swatches. Now, however, the remaining sails lay sinking into the bay, and I am not a strong swimmer. Say, if you would be willing to swim out and gather more fabric for me, I would be happy to pay you!''You did it! I hope you aren't too waterlogged yourself. Now I shall be able to make many sails, which means many boats, which in turn means - many happy customers!'The people of Lossarnach have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Lossarnach (King's Gondor).Complete quests in Lossarnach (King's Gondor)The people of Lower Lebennin have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Lower Lebennin (King's Gondor).Complete quests in Lower Lebennin (King's Gondor)The people of Upper Lebennin have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Upper Lebennin (King's Gondor).Complete quests in Upper Lebennin (King's Gondor)In the depths of Thaurisgar, countless foul and twisted experiments roam the shadows--the terrible legacy of Aniochán the Harrower. Before the fall of Carn Dûm, Aniochán worked tirelessly to outdo his rivals and win the favour of the Steward of Angmar. Chief among his tools in shaping his fell creations was a curious ichor known only as the Bile of Ifrinn. Thought to be lost after a disastrous experiment claimed Aniochán's life, now this foetid and vile substance is in danger of being let loose into the world.Thaurisgar houses many a foul and twisted creature and the vile ingredients of Angmarim alchemy. You should investigate all that this apothecary contains.Explore the halls of ThaurisgarThe doors to the lower levels of Thaurisgar seem to be locked.

