You should defeat the twins.Defeat Kurja and KârsijaBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete the Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary, tiers 2 through 4 instance deeds or quests.'Deeds! Get your Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary Deeds here!

'Talk to me one more time, and they're all yours!''Deeds, incoming!'Torvendor is a Ranger from the North who has come as part of a vanguard to keep whatever festers in Carn Dûm from escaping into the outside world. Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary is home to some of the foulest and twisted creations.Torvendor has asked you to cleanse Thaurisgar of vile remnants.

Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary is in Carn Dûm.Destroy vile phial of bile (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Thaurisgar creatures (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have put down as many foul creatures as you could within the Thaurisgar. Torvendor should be informed immediately.

Torvendor is located at Bail Avarc, outside of Carn Dûm.Return to Torvendor'Greetings, traveller.

'I come from the North. We need your assistance in the apothecary. According to our scouts, the place has been left abandoned. Defeat whatever manner of fell creature that runs wild within, and destroy any evidence of foul experimentation you find.'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary.</rgb>'You're alive. Good.'

Torvendor looks down and sighs in relief.

'To be honest I did not expect you to survive. I have lost many scouts trying to gain more information about the creatures within.

'We have much ahead of us if we are to keep whatever vile creations still linger within. But I am grateful nonetheless for the work you've done.'Thaurisgar serves as genesis to some of the most twisted experiments and fell creations by Aniochán the Harrower. It must be studied before countermeasures can be put into place.Baranoth has asked you to collect any research notes that remain in tact within Thaurisgar.

Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary is in Carn Dûm.Collect research notes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})These research notes should be enough for Baranoth to examine.

Baranoth is located at Bail Avarc, outside of Carn Dûm.'Mae govannen, adventurer. I am Baranoth. I have come to assist in the cleansing of this foul place. While others would have you destroy any trace of defilement, I would have you aid me in understanding the very nature of what they sought to achieve here.

'There can be no guarantee that whatever twists the creatures in the apothecary has been contained within. We must endeavour to understand the corruption. If you find any notes of alchemical nature within, I urge you to preserve them and bring them to me. It is not only of academic import, but also imperative we discover the depths with which their alchemy has fallen.'


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: To advance this quest, you must use the Instance Finder (Ctrl+J) to enter Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary.</rgb>'You have returned. It is good to see that you have survived such a treacherous journey.

'These research notes are promising indeed. Whatever vile and foetid aspirations this Aniochán had, will see shadow and crumble along with this place.'Thama Aklam has become home to a number of brigands.Approach the camp at Thama Aklam to determine possible goings on.Discover the camp of Thama AklamThama Aklam has become home to a number of brigands, many of whom are bored and hope for a fight worthy of their skills.

Defeat brigands in Thama Aklam.Defeat brigands in Thama Aklam (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat brigand leaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many brigands in Thama Aklam.CompletedAs you approach the brigand camp, you begin to hear rumblings of frustration and discontentment.

'It's been days since we had a good scrap,' you hear one complain.

Perhaps you could satiate their boredom with a light scuffle or twelve.You have tussled with many bandits. Perhaps they will be less inclined to start trouble along the road.A secret weapon to wield against the drakes has been brought to you!Scoutmaster Ausma has sent you a special crossbow to help you take down flying cold-drakes.

You should use the Drake-slayer crossbow to defeat flying cold-drakes.Pick up 'The Drake-slayer'Defeat flying drakes with 'The Drake-slayer' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The drake-slayer has lived up to its name!

You should talk to Hórin in Fellgát after the battle is over.Talk to Hórin in Fellgát'${PLAYER}! I'm glad I found you in time. The Scoutmaster sent me to deliver this: a special crossbow she has crafted that should be very effective against aerial drakes! You will need these as well.'

The scout hands you a bundle of black-metal bolts. They are covered in sharp barbs.

'It's called "The Drake-slayer!" Make it live up to its name!''What have you there, ${PLAYER}? A crossbow?'

You hand Hórin the Drake-slayer and tell him the story of its making and of its success during the battle.

'Clever Ausma! Did she develop these black bolts herself as well? Hmm... Perhaps this is the key to defeating Hrímil once and for all...?'A shy librarian of Imloth Melui has gone missing, along with numerous invaluable medical texts from the Hall of the Gentle Hand.Merenir has asked you to speak with Chief Healer Brunil in Imloth Melui's Hall of the Gentle Hand.Talk to BrunilBrunil has asked you to pick up the encrypted note.

The note is next to Brunil, in the Hall of the Gentle Hand.Pick up the noteBrunil has asked you to bring a note written in a medical shorthand to Atharon, who she thinks can decipher the script.

Atharon is in the potions wing of the Hall of the Gentle Hand.Upon reading the encrypted note, Atharon has suggested that you check the market to speak with merchants Rendis mentioned she was going to see.

You should talk to the bag maker and the provisioner in the Imloth Melui market.Talk to BrenionTalk to TherienAfter speaking with Therien and Brenion, you gained some information about Rendis's actions the day she disappeared. You should let Atharon know what you've learned.

Atharon is in the Hall of the Gentle Hand.Return to Atharon'Welcome to Imloth Melui. If you are here to help, I ask that you seek out Chief Healer Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand. She has been asking for help with something.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! I heard you were quite instrumental in assisting with the defence against the Enemy. I wonder if I might press you into service for something less grandiose, yet just as important to me.

'One of my staff has gone missing. Rendis oversaw the care of the medical texts here in the Hall. She always took her job very seriously, so I was quite surprised when she vanished one day, along with many important texts.

'I took her for a traitor, but I recently found a note she left behind which might explain her disappearance. Unfortunately, it is written in a medical shorthand unfamiliar to me. Will you take the note to her old teacher? You can find him in the potions wing here in the Hall. He may be able to translate it for us. You will find the note on the table, just there.''Aye, Rendis came by. Haven’t seen her for some time though. She bought seeds and quite a few sacks of grains, breads, and dried meats... and vegetables enough for a feast! Carted it all away without even inviting me to whatever party she was throwing. Now that I think of it, perhaps she wasn’t the one throwing the party. You see, her living quarters were off that way, but she carted off that way!'

The merchant points first towards the east and then to the west.'Rendis? Why I haven’t seen 'er in weeks. A fortnight at least... maybe longer, maybe. She was looking for a sturdy bag. Brought a few books of different sizes along - trying 'em out for size, she was. Went with what I call the Big Brown Sack. Sturdy straps on that one. Good for hiking and over-nighting. And books too, apparently. Not sure why anyone would need so many books as all that.

'Say - can I interest you in a bag? How's about a sack?''Why hello. Yes, I am Atharon. You say you may have a clue to the whereabouts of Rendis? Well, give it here.'

You hand over the encrypted note, which he squints at, nodding.

'This is written by Rendis, but I am not sure it helps much. 'Tis merely a list of items she planned to purchase from the market! See here, she planned to speak with Therien and Brenion. Why don’t you seek them out and see what Rendis wanted? They may have some idea of her whereabouts.''You return! Tell me what you discovered. Is Rendis found?'Explore the enemy encampments and strongholds within Clovengap.Explore the enemy encampments and strongholds within Clovengap.Explore Dashât-zaharExplore GarânashmarExplore FrósthelExplore AnatrâdExplore MaranazhârExplore SkarashulgExplore Min NávaidExplore the remnants of the Church of the All-seeing in Umbar Baharbêl.Explore the remnants of the Church of the All-seeing in Umbar Baharbêl.Find Mâkhda Khorbo, the Fane of the All-seeingFind the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Sail-havenFind the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Upper WardFind the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Tor-gardensFind the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Lower WardThe Hill-men of Angmar and their allies work to oppose the remnants of the Iron Crown who dwell again within the walls of Carn Dûm.You should aid the Hill-men of Angmar and work to oppose the Iron Crown in Carn Dûm.

