'Talk to me one more time, and they're all yours!''Deeds, incoming!'Prince Durin believes he has discovered where Hrímil Frost-heart has made her lair within Mount Gundabad: the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.Náin and his company can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.

Believing that an ancient Greymaul treasury known as the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra had long laid hidden in Mount Gundabad, Prince Durin has asked you to join Náin and his company at Amgaruslun in the Clovengap. You should meet up with Náin and his company at Amgaruslun.Meet up with Náin and his company at Amgaruslun in the ClovengapNáin can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.

After arriving at Amgaruslun, you have found Náin's company hard at work excavating what appears to be an old passageway deeper into Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Náin.Talk to Náin at AmgaruslunThe Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found beyond the frozen falls of Amgaruslun in the Clovengap.

According to Prince Durin, the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found beyond Amgaruslun in the Clovegap. You should see if the dwarves of Náin's company have broken through the ice concealing the passage to the ancient Greymaul treasury.Náin can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.

The dwarves' hard work has borne fruit. You have discovered the passage to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You should return to Náin.Talk to Náin at AmgaruslunThe Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found in the Clovengap.

Náin has asked you to muster your allies and aid Prince Durin in confronting Hrímil Frost-heart in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.


<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must complete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra' on any difficulty Tier to advance this quest.</rgb>Complete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'Prince Durin can be found at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset.

You have triumphed over Hrímil Frost-heart at the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You should talk to Durin at Zidir-nesad.Talk to Durin at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset<rgb=#00FF00>It is recommended, but not required, that you complete The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves before playing 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'.</rgb>

'There are those who believe that Hrímil Frost-heart has abandoned Mount Gundabad. I say they are wrong! It is true she has fled, but only deeper into the Mountain-home—to Abnankâra!

'Does that name sound unfamiliar to your ear? It should, my friend. It is known to none who still live, save for me, and that is only because I share the memories of the Durins who came before me!

'Not long after the Greymaul Rebellion was ended and Motsóg came to dwell in solitude in the caverns deep beneath the Mountain-home, he confessed a secret to me—to the Durin I was then. Before that ruinous war between our peoples, he had set the Greymauls upon a great task: to delve a hidden treasury within the depths of Mount Gundabad. It was named Abnankâra, the Hiddenhoard, and it would have been the jewel of Motsóg's kingdom. Had the Greymauls succeeded in their plot to steal the wealth and mithril of Khazad-dûm, it is certain the spoils would have come to rest at Abnankâra.

'Whether it was by some sense of duty or mere curiosity, I—when I was Durin the First—heeded Motsóg's words and found the hidden way to the gates of Abnankâra. I strode within its halls only once, and when I had seen all that I meant to, I sealed it behind me—leaving the few, ill-gotten riches of the Greymauls to be forgotten. And so it has been for many Ages of the world!

'It lies still in the Clovengap, my friend, and in my heart, I am certain that that is where Hrímil Frost-heart has gone. I have sent my uncle, Náin, ahead with a small company to seek for the Hiddenhoard.

'Will you aid him, my friend? Will you see our long struggle for the conquest of Mount Gundabad to its end?'<rgb=#00FF00>It is recommended, but not required, that you complete The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves before playing 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'.</rgb>

