'Whether it was by some sense of duty or mere curiosity, I—when I was Durin the First—heeded Motsóg's words and found the hidden way to the gates of Abnankâra. I strode within its halls only once, and when I had seen all that I meant to, I sealed it behind me—leaving the few, ill-gotten riches of the Greymauls to be forgotten. And so it has been for many Ages of the world!

'It lies still in the Clovengap, my friend, and in my heart, I am certain that that is where Hrímil Frost-heart has gone. I have sent my uncle, Náin, ahead with a small company to seek for the Hiddenhoard.

'Will you aid him, my friend? Will you see our long struggle for the conquest of Mount Gundabad to its end?''My uncle Náin has gone to seek the old passage to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. Travel to the Clovengap and join him, my friend!''I can hardly explain it, my friend. How could Durin know of such a passage? Could it be true?'

Náin absent-mindedly strokes at the air beneath his shorn beard before lowering his hand.

'You know of what I speak, ${PLAYER}. When Durin told me that he had proclaimed himself to be Durin the Seventh—Durin the Deathless reborn, I must admit I balked at his words. Durin confided in me, and he spoke of visions and of ancient memories that returned to him deep within Mount Gundabad. And so, you must imagine my disbelief when he told me that Hrímil had made a lair for herself in an old Greymaul treasury—the so-called Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. Such a thing should not even exist!

'Yet, with each swing of those pick-axes, I find myself more convinced.'

Náin glances over his shoulder at the dwarves of his company picking away at the ice of Amgaruslun.

'It has been some time, my friend. Why don't you see if we have broken through?'Go on ahead, my friend, and see if we have broken through!''You say you heard a voice on the wind? It can be no other—we have found the lair of Hrímil Frost-heart!

'I shall send word to Durin at once, my friend. If ever I doubted his words, I have now all the proof I sought. Alas that the Black Mattock was lost in the Deepscrave! This will have to do....'

Náin hefts a war-mattock of the Iron Hills in his hand.

'In the meantime, ${PLAYER}, I would ask that you gather your strongest allies to Mount Gundabad. When you are prepared, we shall see what awaits us within Abnankâra!

'Even with the combined might of the Gabil'akkâ behind him, Durin shall have need of you—and of them—if victory is to be won!''Even with the combined might of the Gabil'akkâ behind him, Durin shall have need of you and your strongest allies if victory is to be won!''Many are the songs that will be sung of this day, my friend. At long last, Hrímil Frost-heart is dead and Mount Gundabad is ours. And I would be remiss to overlook the role you played in our victory, ${PLAYER}!

'With Hrímil's death, our conquest of the Mountain-home is all but certain. Gorgar is slain, and the line of Azog is ended. The Orcs and their wild cousins from the North have fallen into disarray, and it is my firm belief that those who linger within Gundabad will be routed in the days ahead.

'Even so, I grieve the loss of my uncle, Náin, and it is with great sorrow that I shall have to deliver word of his death to my father, King Thorin. My heart aches, too, that he was so soon to follow my grandfather, Dáin, in death.

'May his deeds and his memory never be forgotten! Long live Náin—slakeless, now and evermore!'Atop the towers of the great wall, Rammas Echor, fly the black banners of King Elessar. Time, weather, and war have ripped and shredded their once proud edges.Othanar has asked you to speak with Langwen, who has been asking for assistance.

Langwen can be found by a fountain in one of the gardens in the Harlond.Talk to LangwenLangwen has asked you to replace shredded banners atop the towers of Rammas Echor in the Harlond. You should pick up the nearby bag full of banners.

The bag is next to Langwen, in the Harlond.Pick up the bag full of bannersLangwen has asked you to replace shredded banners atop the towers of Rammas Echor in the Harlond.Replace tattered banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have taken down the tattered banners and replaced them with proud black flags bearing the white tree of Gondor. You should let Langwen know that her new banners fly from the towers' heights.

Langwen is in the Harlond.'Welcome to the Harlond! Word travelled ahead that you might be coming to lend a hand. As you can see, the city is working to pick itself up after being nearly razed to the ground by the Morgul-host. I would ask that you speak with Langwen, as she has asked me twice today already to send help her way.''Well, it's about time Othanar sent someone to help me. I am indeed Langwen, weaver and seamstress.

'At the moment, I am working to replace the banners which are atop the wall. Time, wind, and war have shredded their edges, and I am wont to replace them with fresh versions. The towers of Rammas Echor are reached by long flights of stairs, however, and though my fingers are yet nimble, the same cannot be said for my knees. Will you take up these new banners and replace any you find which might be ruined?''Have you done it then? Ah yes, I can see from here our king's banners flying true once more. I know there are more yet to replace, but these old hands can only work so fast. You have my thanks!'Not too long ago, a group of Trév Duvárdain defeated an Iron Crown sorcerer in the sewers of Carn Dûm. The tale is, as Lágsaith would have many believe, a rather strange one.Complete 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty.

Use the Instance Finder to enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin'.Complete 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficultyLágsaith has concluded her tale.

You should talk to her in Bail Avarc.Talk to Lágsaith in Bail Avarc'You wish to hear the tale, eh? Well, I suppose I could grant you the privilege.

'Once my dear Aighrig returned from the east, our little group began hunting down those who still believed in the Iron Crown. We tracked one such fool named Gárvadach into the sewers of Dûn Bándrath -- or Carn Dûm, as it's otherwise known. Apparently, he sought to capture and tame a beast of some sort. Rumours of terrible monstrosities lurking beneath the city come and go, but...'

Lágsaith leans in for a conspiratorial whisper. 

'I assure you, some of them have been very true. After all, why would the Iron Crown care about how their sorceries have poisoned the wildlife?'

She grins, then leans back. 

'Gárvadach may have been a fool, but anyone who perceives the world as something to be conquered is dangerous. The land does not forgive such arrogance, nor does it forget.

'And so, the six of us pursued him....''I would say that the story has come to a close, but the fate of our large rat friend remains shrouded in mystery. May it find some modicum of peace out in the wild -- preferably far, far away from the Iron Crown.

'Thank you for indulging me, friend. I've told this tale numerous times already, but I don't think I'll ever grow tired of it. Watching people react with smiles and laughter is enough for me. After all, what's the harm in some light-hearted fun amidst such dark days?

'Was I lying about the large rat? Well...' 

Lágsaith gives you a wink. 

'That's for me to know and for you to guess. If you think it would help you form a decision, come back again for another retelling!''Down we travelled into the depths of the old sewers of Carn Dûm....'A lonely dog sits on a pier in Pelargir, always watching the horizon.You have found a lonely dog in East Pelargir.

A nearby guard, Handir, has called out to you.Talk to HandirYou have found a lonely dog in East Pelargir.

A nearby guard, Handir, has called out to you.Talk to HandirHandir has given you some meat with which to feed the lonely dog.You have fed the lonely dog.

You should talk to Handir.Talk to HandirThe dog watches the horizon, only sparing you a quick glance at your approach. Then she returns to her vigil.'Hail, friend. I'm afraid nothing can distract that dog from watching the sea. On many mornings, I find that she has beaten me here! Sometimes she only leaves that spot once the moon has risen.

'I decided to come prepared today with meat, just in case the dog was hungry. How about you take some to her?''Well, would you look at that! Even the most stalwart of guards must take a break from their duty every now and then.'

Handir's smile fades as he continues gazing at the dog. 'I wonder what she is searching for. Did she lose something? Someone? Perhaps her master left home for the war and never returned.

'I suppose I ought to start asking around, see if anyone recognizes the poor beast. And if not... well, my family has room for another member!'Explore the markets of Umbar Baharbêl.Explore the markets of Umbar Baharbêl.Find the Dawn MarketFind the SaltlanesFind the FisherfoldFind the Rovers' YardFind the Grand MarketFind the Waterway MarketFind the Stonecliff MarketFind the Dusk MarketAfter speaking with a couple of merchants in Imloth Melui, Rendis's intentions have become clearer. The path she chose to tread is one of danger, however, and it's unclear whether she or the precious tomes she carried away have survived.Atharon has suggested that Rendis may be hiding out in a nearby cave. You should search the forest west of Imloth Melui.Search the hillside for cavesWhile searching the hills west of Imloth Melui, you have come across a cave-mouth. You should explore the cave for any sign of Rendis or her books.Search for RendisRendis has been found and has promised to return to the city of Imloth Melui. She has asked you to inform Brunil of her whereabouts and plans.

Brunil is in the Halls of Healing, in Imloth Melui.Return to Brunil'Bags full of books, seeds, and a cart of food? I know for sure there were no parties or gatherings around the time she vanished, as we were preparing for potential invasion!

'Just a moment - the merchant said she headed off west? Could she have... hmmm. There is a cave in that direction that Rendis has mentioned before. She was always insisting that the dry air within would be beneficial to some of our mouldier books.... But... you don’t think...?

'Please, ${PLAYER}, the cave is west of here, someplace between Imloth Melui and Tumladen. You should take the south road out of the city and pass through the forest. I wish I knew more, but please, search for her there?''Hiding in a cave? All this time? What a fool that girl is. I insist you find her and bring her back at once. Come to think of it, even if you just return with the stolen books, that's fine with me. Hmph!''Who- who are you?'

You explain that Brunil and Atharon have sent you to find her.

'Brunil and Atharon? They yet live? Oh, what a happy day this is! Uh, on that topic... what day is it, exactly?'

Her mouth drops open with shock as you tell her the date.

'How did so many days, nay, weeks pass? And you say that the war is over, and the Enemy is no longer a threat? My goodness. I came up here with some of our more essential medical texts, you see. I was sure the Morgul-horde would soon be on our doorstep and that Imloth Melui would fall to their flames. My beloved books... well, they are such important texts. I could not risk them, you see. I only meant to stay for a bit. I really did mean to check back and see if it was safe to return. Only, I suppose I got distracted reading.'

She sighs, looking wistfully about the cozy cave.

'Well, I suppose it is time to make my way back. Thank you for bringing me this news. I shall take some time to pack up my things. Please let Brunil and my teacher know that I am returning.'This is 'Gondorian Herbology,' a book on remedies made from plants and herbs found across Gondor.This slim, unassuming book is entitled, 'Poisonous Plants of Pelennor and Beyond.'The binding of this slim book shows signs of heavy use, and its pages are dog-eared and creased. The title is 'Midnight in the Garden,' and its contents are enough to make one's cheeks redden.The cover of this book reads 'To Break and to Bind,' and seems to be about setting bones and how to make splints.The binding of this ancient book is cracked and warped with age. Its title has been worn away and lost with time, but its pages are full of drawings displaying organs and other things that are possibly better left inside one's body.This appears to be a compendium of various ancient texts, and presents and overview of medicine as it was practiced in ages long past. Flipping to a random page, you pause as you read a suggestion for applying spoiled sheep's milk mixed with week-old fish guts directly to a wound.'You return! What news of Rendis?'

You let her know that the librarian is safe, and on her way back to the city with the medical tomes.

'Holed away in a cave and lost track of time? That fool of a girl was always getting lost in a book! Well, I am equal parts annoyed and relieved. I will let Atharon know to expect her back. He and I will have a very stern talk with Rendis about all of this.

'I suppose this is the best possible outcome I could have hoped for. You have my thanks.'This is 'Gondorian Herbology,' a book on remedies made from plants and herbs found across Gondor.This slim, unassuming book is entitled, 'Poisonous Plants of Pelennor and Beyond.'The binding of this slim book shows signs of heavy use, and its pages are dog-eared and creased. The title is 'Midnight in the Garden,' and its contents are enough to make one's cheeks redden.The cover of this book reads 'To Break and to Bind,' and seems to be about setting bones and how to make splints.The binding of this ancient book is cracked and warped with age. Its title has been worn away and lost with time, but its pages are full of drawings displaying organs and other things that are possibly better left inside one's body.This appears to be a compendium of various ancient texts, and presents and overview of medicine as it was practiced in ages long past. Flipping to a random page, you pause as you read a suggestion for applying spoiled sheep's milk mixed with week-old fish guts directly to a wound.The townspeople of Halach have been receiving help from someone, but no one knows who.Irodon has asked you to investigate a boar wallow to the north-east of Halach.Investigate the boar-wallow near HalachYou have found a Haradrim man near the boar wallow.

You should talk to him.Talk to Asórkho near the boar wallow'${PLAYER}, welcome! As you can see, we've been hard at work rebuilding our home. My heart should feel light, but ever since the war's end, I have been troubled by a string of mysteries.

'For the past few months, every now and then, someone has been leaving sacks of supplies at our doorsteps. Preserved boar meat, cut firewood, all harvested from the wild. The strange thing is, we don't know who is responsible. Of course, we were suspicious at first, but nothing about the supplies thus far has seemed amiss. I hope that the culprit is not a malicious person, but we cannot be too careful.

'Now, I suspect the meat we have been receiving has been hunted from a nearby boar wallow, to the north-east. Perhaps our culprit is there right now. But very few people here would be able to defend themselves out there, and they are all busy protecting Halach.

'Would you investigate the wallow for us?''Please, put down your weapons, ${CLASS}. I mean you no harm, and I am alone. My fellow soldiers fled long ago.

'You have come looking for me at the behest of the townspeople, yes? Rather, you have come looking for the one gifting them supplies. It is not much, compared to what my comrades and I raided from them during the war. But this is... repentance, I suppose.

'I will return home eventually, but not before I see some of the harm undone.'Stragglers driven from the Battle of the Pelennor Fields have scattered throughout Lossarnach. Though their numbers have been decimated, they still stand to pose a threat and must be eliminated.Horndir has asked you to deal with the Orc presence at Taustrok before it grows in strength enough to threaten the Harlond.

The Orcs have gathered at a small camp, north-west of the Harlond.Defeat Orcs at Taustrok (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Horndir know that you have defeated many of the Orcs who were gathering and trying to regroup north-west of the Harlond.

Horndir is in the Harlond.Return to Horndir'Greetings. I am Horndir, captain of the guard here in the Harlond. I hear you are looking to lend aid and were of great help during the war. Stragglers driven from the Battle of the Pelennor Fields have scattered throughout Lossarnach. Though their numbers have been decimated, they still stand to pose a threat and must be eliminated.

'North-west of the Harlond, my scouts have reported a group of Orcs. They must be dealt with, lest they grow in number and become a danger once more.''Thank you for the help. We are all looking forward to more peaceful days.'Dingási suspects that the supply chain may have been corrupted with more of the poor-quality stone. You are tasked with travelling to Arnach to check on the inventory stored there.Dingási has asked that you travel south to Arnach, and speak with Kholnedák, the supervisor in charge of the town's storage and shipping of stone.

Kholnedák can be found in Arnach.Talk to KholnedákKholnedák has asked you to meet her near the northern farms in Arnach.Talk to Kholnedák near the northern farmsKholnedák has asked you to investigate the bandit camp Aegollant, and to search for signs of the shoddy stones.

Aegollant is in Lossarnach.Search Aegollant for shoddy stonesWithin the ruins of Aegollant, you have found piles of the shoddy blocks which were snuck into the dwarves' superior piles of stone.

You should investigate the blocks.Examine the stoneWhile inspecting the shoddy stones in Aegollant, you were set upon by brigands. One of the bandits dropped a crumpled note, the details of which Kholnedák will be eager to read.

Kholnedák is in Arnach.'Glad am I that you have destroyed so many of those shoddy blocks, yet troubled too, that there were so many. I have had my workers check the stores we have here, and there were indeed more of the poor blocks mixed in among the ones of greater quality.

'I ordered the inferior blocks destroyed, but I need to trace the dilution of our stock to see from whence they came. Will you go south to Arnach and speak with my colleague, Kholnedák? Have her check the town's stores to see if they too have been infiltrated.''Greetings, stranger. You come from Dingási? You are timely, as I was readying to send word that we had a partial wall collapse here.'

As you inform her of the bad blocks her face grows troubled.

'Dire news indeed, and I feel the fool for not having noticed if our stock was tainted. I will check the stores immediately! Our stone is currently stored within a local barn. Meet me near the northern farms.''You return! Tell me, what did you find?''Ah, ${PLAYER}, it is as we feared. Our stock within has also been seeded with poor quality stone. If I were a betting dwarf, and I am, I would say that we might find some answers in Aegollant, where a group of bandits has set up camp.

'Down the hills and across the road they linger, attacking passersby on the road and stealing from the town when they can. The Captain of the Guard, Baranor, has been planning to rout the swine, but his forces are stretched a bit thin at the moment.

'You seem like you can take care of yourself. Why not search their camp? Look for more of these blocks, or any other clues that might tell us who is responsible for the deception.'An Elf surveys building materials in an effort to hasten the progress with which the land is restored.Himril has asked you to travel to Arnach to the south and search for building materials.Collect building materials (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})All of these building materials should account for what is missing from Himril's records. You should return to Himril.

Himril is in Imloth Melui.'Greeting, traveller. Welcome to Imloth Melui.'

She files through papers, showing you little concern.

'I am surveying the land, and the damage done to it is spread far and wide from here to Pelargir.

'We seem to be missing a few crates of building materials. If you are keen to lend your aid, could you perhaps visit Arnach to the south and see if there are any materials that have been left behind?

'Our efforts to restore Gondor are vast, and a few items being unaccounted for is nothing new.'Himril takes full account of all the materials you delivered.

'Many thanks, traveller.

'This should account for the missing materials from my ledger. You may go on your way.'A fresh shipment of building materials has arrived in Halach.Gorhir has asked you to take a crate to Irodon, who is supervising rebuilding efforts in the centre of Halach.

You can take the crate from the pile next to Gorhir.Pick up a heavy crate from the pileYou've delivered the crate to Irodon.

You should confirm with Gorhir at Halach's harbour.Talk to Gorhir'Look at all of these crates, ${PLAYER}! Filled to the brim with building materials, too!

'Would you mind taking this one over to Irodon? He should be supervising rebuilding efforts in the centre of town.''Would you mind taking this crate over to Irodon? He should be in the centre of town.''Thank you, friend! I expect Gorhir will want to know the materials have been delivered.''You hauled such heavy cargo without even breaking a sweat. Impressive work!'Reniaril is concerned that Dindal's Overlook has been overrun by remnant Orcs.Reniaril has asked you to defeat any Orcs you find along the path to Dindal's Overlook.

Dindal's Overlook can be found east of Imloth Melui.Defeat Orcs in Dindal's Overlook (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should inform Reniaril that Dindal's Overlook has been cleared of remnant Orcs.

Reniaril can be found south of Imloth Melui and north-east of Arnach.Talk to ReniarilReniaril beckons you to her.

'You look like you can take care of yourself.'

She studies you intently, while being aware of her surroundings.

'My name is Reniaril. I'm in charge of patrols along these roads. We could use someone of your ability if you could help. Imloth Melui has got its hands full with restoration efforts, and we have supplies being carted all along these roads. Sometimes these supplies get lost. I'm concerned that Dindal's Overlook has been overrun by remnant Orcs. I used to oversee the supply routes from there but I can no longer patrol in peace.

'Just follow the road east until you see a path through the forest to the north into the cliffside. Perhaps you could do us all a favour and clear the way.''I could hear the cries of the Orcs all the way from here.

'So the deed is done then. Hopefully we won't have to deal with anymore stray Orcs in the area. With so many fleeing from the war, it can be difficult to track them all down.

'Thank you for your service.'A battle-worn soldier would like your help to disperse the Ruthless Dead.A battle-worn soldier has offered you the chance to defeat the Ruthless Dead in the Ruins of Ethillorn, south of Linhir.

Defeat the Ruthless Dead.Defeat Ruthless Dead (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ruthless Dead berserkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated many of the Ruthless Dead, and should report to the battle-worn soldier standing outside the Ruins of Ethilllorn south of Linhir.

Talk to the soldier outside the Ruins of Ethillorn.Talk to the battle-worn soldier outside the Ruins of EthillornA battle-worn soldier stands guard outside the Ruins of Ethillorn. Dirt marks his face. Sweat mats down his hair in clumps. There are scrapes across his armour, as if some beast tried to claw the heart from his chest.

But he's beaming as you approach him.

'Hail, traveller!'

You feel his eyes assess your worth, and when he judges you a capable adventurer, he beams wider.

'I have been tasked with dispersing the Ruthless Dead from within the walls of Ethillorn. I am in the middle of a respite, but if you would like a turn, you are more than welcome.''To test myself against such strange beings is an honour and a privilege, is it not?

'Thank you for your aid. I will tend to whatever remains in due time.'Jódha needs some help preparing for a rush of customers at her food stall.Jódha has asked you to pick some savoury herbs outside of Pelargir.

Find herbs in the fields west of Pelargir.Collect savoury herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found enough herbs to satisfy Jódha.

Deliver the savoury herbs to Jódha.Talk to JódhaAn affable woman pulls you aside.

'You there! Are you looking for work?'

You begin to answer, but she doesn't let you finish.

'Of course you are!'

She pushes a cloth-lined basket into your hands.

'There is an herb that grows outside the western gate of Pelargir. It has broad leaves and a distinct smell, like the rind of a sour fruit. I would go get it myself, but as you can see we have a lot of hungry customers to feed.'

She leans in and whispers in a conspiratorial tone.

'Onjópo is a great cook, but he doesn't do well under pressure. I need to make sure he doesn't burn anything.'

She sends you off with a wink.With a sweep of her arm, Jódha gestures to the line of hungry patrons waiting in front of the grill.

'We started out feeding just the shipbreakers and shipbuilders, but before we knew it half of Pelargir has come lining up for our food! We never expected to be so popular. Thank you for the herbs. They're one of the most important ingredients in our marinade.

'You'll... keep that a secret, won't you?'Experience the story of 'The Song of Waves and Wind'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 1'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 2'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 3'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 4'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 5'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 6'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 7'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 8'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 9'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 10'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 11'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 12'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 13'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 14'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 15'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 16'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 17'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Chapter 18'Complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind, Epilogue'Thama Aklam has many coffers in it, likely home to ill-gotten gains.Thama Aklam is host to many suspicious coffers.

Inspect coffers in Thama Aklam.Discover the camp of Thama AklamThama Aklam has become home to a number of brigands.You have inspected many coffers.You spy some coffers in Thama Aklam that are probably filled with ill-gotten gains.

Investigate these coffers to see what has been keeping the brigands so busy.You open the chest, anticipating gold and glittering jewels, but are instead met with the sight and smell of an old, mouldy shirt.

Why would anyone keep this?At first glance, the chest appears empty, but a seasoned adventurer knows that looks can be deceiving.

You knock on the bottom of the chest. It rings hollow.

Aha! A false bottom.

You pry it open with your fingers to reveal a hidden compartment that is also...

Empty.Within this coffer is a small supply crate.

You pry open the lid, revealing a strongbox.

The strongbox, in turn, contains a thick canvas sack.

You peer into the bag only to find a small chest.

You open the chest, expecting to find something precious, something worth something to anyone, but it is empty.

And then you realize, the containers were the real treasures all along.Among the mundane items in this coffer, you find a stack of neatly folded papers.

Perhaps these are missives, plans for attacking nearby settlements or travellers on the road.

A cursory examination reveals them instead to be love letters -- poorly written love letters best not read by anyone. Ever.'After a thorough inspection of their coffers, you can safely conclude that these brigands are either largely inactive or largely ineffective.'Bráthi the Master Prospector seeks to halt those who wish to destroy the rare treasures of Gundabad.Stone-smashers found throughout Gundabad.

You should defeat stone-smashers for Bráthi.Defeat stone-smashers in Gundabad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search for signs of stone-smashersDefeat many stone-smashers in Gundabad.Completed'${PLAYER}, stone-smashers threaten all of the rare treasures and mineral deposits in Gundabad! We must defeat these brutes before they destroy what makes Gundabad a place of beauty and wonder!'You have defeat many stone-smashers in Gundabad and greatly assisted Bráthi and all those who seek to conquer the Three Peaks and reclaim the Mountain-home.Once the seat of the Witch-king of Angmar, the dread citadel of Gwathrenost casts a long shadow upon the city of Carn Dûm. All but abandoned after the Steward of Angmar was deposed, the remnants of the Iron Crown have crept forth from the shadows, seeking to master a lost artifact of the Witch-king and reclaim dominion of Angmar.Gurkrak keeps watch on Gwathrenost and brutally dispatches those foolish or daring enough to enter the Witch-king's citadel unbidden.

You must defeat Gurkrak and enter Gwathrenost.The Castellan's chambers can be found atop a set of winding stairs within Gwathrenost.

You must find the Castellan's chambers and defeat Castellan Obáshurz if you are to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.Ascend Gwathrenost and enter the Castellan's chambersOne of the last remnants of the reign of the Steward of Angmar, Castellan Obáshurz tends Gwathrenost and dutifully serves his masters: High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd.

You must defeat Castellan Obáshurz.Defeat Castellan ObáshurzTham Mornarcham can be found atop Gwathrenost.

You must ascend Gwathrenost and reach Tham Mornarcham to confront the leaders of the Iron Crown.Ascend Gwathrenost and enter Tham MornarchamHigh Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd await in Tham Mornarcham, the Seat of the the Witch-king.

High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd must be defeated before they can wield the shard of Tauressar to subjugate the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.Defeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain ClaghórdSevered from the Vandassar of Rhudaur, the shard of Tauressar is possessed of a terrible enchantment capable of swaying the hearts and minds of those who swear oaths upon it—willingly or not.

You must destroy the shard of Tauressar.Destroy the Shard of TauressarWith the destruction of the shard of Tauressar and the final downfall of the Iron Crown, a new day dawns in Angmar.

You have completed 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel' on Tier 1.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Gwathrenost, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Monday, Thursday, and Saturday.</rgb>Completed: Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel (Tier 1)'There it is, ${PLAYER}. Whether it is called Tûr Dúvar, Gwathrenost, or countless other names, it is the dark citadel of the Witch-king of Angmar. But you know it well, don't you?

'From what we have learned, High Priestess Ásachal has stolen a shard of the ancient Oath-stone of Rhudaur, Tauressar, and brought it to Angmar that she might wield its power as her own. It is said that it was corrupted by the hand of the Witch-king himself, and that oaths sworn upon it bind the wills of its victims to the Oath-stone. Even so far from the battle in the south-lands, our tribes learned of the Witch-king's doom. Does Ásachal truly mean to master the Oath-stone in his absence? It must be destroyed before it is too late!

'Although we cannot be certain, it is likely the shard is now kept in the highest chambers of Gwathrenost. We have cleared the way, my friend. It is up to you now!'


