You should bring the gems to Zádokh Flint-eye at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset.The scout gives you a missive from the Zhélruka, seeking precious gems from Gundabad.'Very good, ${CLASS}. I will see to these gems and make sure that Prince Ingór gets his fair share.'Though the repair crew has worked tirelessly to shore up the walls and crumbled buildings of the Harlond, time, weather, and underlying issues can still lead to instabilities.Birási has asked you to inspect the braces supporting walls and other stonework at various sites in the Harlond.Examine the first siteExamine the second siteExamine the third siteExamine the fourth siteExamine the fifth siteExamine the sixth siteYou have examined Birási's assigned inspection sites. You should let him know what you found.

Birási is in the Harlond.Return to Birási'Hail, ${CLASS}. You must forgive me for not rising to greet you, as I am not steady enough yet on my feet. My name is Birási, and it falls to me to do a daily check of the integrity of the various buildings and walls across the Harlond. Many are the bolsters we have placed to brace the damaged stones, but stone shifts as weather and time work their ways.

'I was inspecting this location when a stone came loose and struck me on the head. I should wear my helmet, I know. I was in a rush, though. Do not tell Dingási, eh?

'I am in no shape to continue today's inspections, but if you have the time, I could pass this task on to you. 'Tis an easy one, and I can tell you what to look for. I do advise you wear your helmet. What say you?''You return! What have you found?'

You tell him which spots look like they need immediate attention.

'Ah, thank you! I will send workers to these locations once my head stops spinning. With a reminder for them to all wear their helmets. Ooof.'Shoddy stones have found their way into the stockpiles in Arnach - the work of someone named Garaphir. He must be stopped, lest he continue to taint the dwarves' supply chain and reputation.The crumpled note you found mentioned someone named Garaphir, who Kholnedák thinks can be found in Imloth Melui.

She has recommended that you go to Imloth Melui and speak with the Captain of the Guard, Merenir.Talk to MerenirMerenir has suggested that you look for Garaphir in the market district in Imloth Melui.Talk to GaraphirYou managed to find Garaphir in the marketplace, but he fled when you drew near.

You should pursue Garaphir through Imloth Melui.Pursue Garaphir through Imloth Melui!After a brief chase through Imloth Melui, Garaphir has collapsed on a tall stair-case, panting for breath.

You should talk to Garaphir.Interrogate GaraphirAfter collapsing on one of Imloth Melui's incredibly tall set of stairs, Garaphir was more than willing to point the finger at his employer, the noble, Maengar.

You should look for Maengar at his warehouse in Imloth Melui, and look for proof he was behind the infiltration of shoddy stones.Examine Maengar's warehouse for evidenceRealizing he was found out, Maengar attacked you to keep his secrets safe. He was no match for you, however, and has been defeated. You should collect his accounts book and bring it to Merenir.

The accounts book is in Maengar's warehouse.Pick up the accounts bookYou should bring the accounts book to Merenir in Imloth Melui.Return to MerenirMerenir mentioned that someone had been looking for you while you were dealing with Maengar. You can find Kholnedák in Imloth Melui.'The note that you found mentions someone named Garaphir, who is moving on to Imloth Melui. The gang you encountered in Aegollant was to report to him once they had finished moving this shipment of stone into our warehouse.

'We must find out who is behind this! I recommend you go to Imloth Melui and speak with the Captain of the Guard, Merenir. He may know something of this Garaphir.''Garaphir? Yes, I know of him. In fact, I wish his name had come to my attention less lately. He's an awful brute who has no qualms about trying to swindle the good folk of this town.

'You should try looking for him in the market. I think I saw him slink that way earlier.''${PLAYER}! Glad am I to see you, friend. Dingási sent me to check on things up here, but it seems like you have already handled the situation.'

You hand her the journal and explain Maengar's involvement and demise. She flips through the pages, shaking her head.

'Handled it, you certainly have! My, my. I thank you for your continued help! Those slabs of soft-stone Maengar was trying to slip in could have led to structural damage at best, and loss of life at worst. You have done a great service to Gondor and the Dwarves of Furukzahar, my friend. I will let Dingási know that the threat to our reputation - ah, and the danger of shoddy stone work, is over.''All right, I'll talk. Oof, my aching side! Bah, why are there so many steps?! This blasted city is too hilly, ouch, huff.

'Wait, wait, I said I'll talk. You are wasting your time with me anyhow! I'm just the middle man! You really want Maengar. He paid me to organize the shipment of his stone down to Arnach and the Harlond.

'He's at his warehouse, in the western part of the city, but you had best leave him be! He won't go down without a fight, and he has plenty of protection. Now leave me be! I was just doing my job!''So, Maengar was behind the shoddy stone? That does not surprise me, but I am saddened that someone would try to profit in a way that could cause harm to others. I am sorry that you had to deal with him, but glad that you did.

'While you were busy with Maengar, a dwarf named Kholnedák came 'round looking for you. You will find her just over there.'Nestled within the forest of northern Lower Lebennin, is the dwarf-outpost, Zarsatrâd. The outpost serves as a waypoint for the Dwarves of Furukzahar as they move supplies of heavy stone from the Aban-bazan quarry.Tinído has asked you to bring a crate of chisel tips north to the dwarf-outpost of Zarsatrâd.Pick up the crate of chisel tipsYou should bring the crate of chisel tips to Irzeben.

Irzeben is in northern Lebennin, at Zarsatrâd.'Well met! I am Tinído, Master of Procurements. You seem like a capable and curious sort. Have you been up to Zarsatrâd? 'Tis a small outpost south of Furukzahar which serves as a waypoint between the 'Aban-bazan quarry and Pelargir.

'If you are heading in that direction, I would ask you to bring along this crate of chisel tips. I would do it myself, but I am already running behind due to this swindling merchant wanting to haggle over every minuscule detail. Bring the crate north to my supervisor, Irzeben, and he will reward you for your efforts.''Hail and well met! You say you come from Pelargir with the crate Tinído was supposed to be procuring? Aye, supposed to procure and thence return with straightaway. His love for the Pelargir mead bogs him down once more.

