You should talk to Rísti Graver.Talk to Rísti GraverRísti Graver, the greatest foreman of the Ironfold, has learned the location of the sacred Jewel of Abhâr. While the jewel has been found, it will take a skilled hero to recover it and return it to the throne! You should seek out Rísti Graver as soon as you are able.'Thank you for retrieving the Jewel of Abhâr, ${PLAYER}, for the orange light that shines from this gem symbolizes reason, and if there is one quality that best describes the dwarves, it is that one!

'It is true, my friend. I hope you do not think all dwarves act without thought, for when something is of great importance to our people, I assure you there is much consideration that goes on, just beneath the surface. Indeed, some dwarves may do much of their thinking out loud, as it seems your friend the Dourhand may have done.

'I am glad you endured the tasks of Mangur Bentpenny, my friend, for now the Jewel of Abhâr has been restored to its proper place in the throne! And that is reason enough!'

Rísti Graver chuckles to himself.

'Just my little joke, ${PLAYER}. Thank you again.''The sacred Jewel of Abhâr has been found... but there is a problem. It has been found by a Dourhand, Mangur Bentpenny, in the Welkin-lofts! I ask you to find a way to retrieve it from this Dourhand without causing too unpleasant an incident.''What is it you want, stranger? The Jewel of Abhâr? Bah, is that what this stone I found is called? Sounds important! Sounds even more important if you've come asking about it, I think!

'Do you expect me to just give it to you? I lay claim to it after all, found it fair! If you want this jewel, then what are you going to do for me? Hmm, let me think....'

'Aha! Yes, yes, I've got just the thing! I've always wanted the horn of a silver drake! They are rare beasts, but I've seen one or two here in the Welkin-lofts. You get me the horn of a silver drake, and then... then we'll talk. Not before!''What? You got the horn of a silver drake?'

Mangur Bentpenny mumbles under his breath.

'This fool should be dead.'

Mangur Bentpenny clears his throat and continues speaking to you.

'Hmm, I can see you really are serious about this jewel. Your desire to own this gem makes it more valuable, however. The price has gone up! The horn you gave me is not a fair trade. I need something more....

'Ah, Iron Crown treasures! My friends and I have been trying to acquire the Iron Crown treasures hidden in the Welkin-lofts, but to no avail! If you can find and bring us these hidden treasures, then I will relinquish the jewel to you. You have my word... again!''My, this is a lot of treasure! Look at all these trinkets and gems! I almost feel badly, trading you this one jewel for all of this treasure... but a deal is a deal!

'Have your jewel and be on your way. Hmm, I might just pack it in. With all these riches, I could find a quiet mountain and live out the rest of my days in peace....

