'You know, I think it is time you spoke to Garvir.'Shegai knows that the dwarves who report to him have taken to playing games instead of working.Yared stands by the stacks of crates in north-western Furukzahar.Talk to YaredThe rock-scrapers demanded by Shegai will be in one of the crates of tools near Yared in Furukzahar.Search crates of tools until you find the rock-scrapersYared is by the crates of tools in north-western Furukzahar.Talk to Yared'We each responded differently to Hámisar's command that the gates of Furukzahar be shut when Gondor went to war. Some, such as myself, continued to do our work without interruption, knowing that one day the storm-clouds would pass and we would be needed again. Others, including some of the dwarves who work for me, turned to games to pass the time. Have you heard of this ridiculous Stacking Game they invented?

'Ah, I understand it, even as I think it is needlessly frivolous in such times as we live in. I allow them to pass the time as they see fit... so long as they quickly respond when I have a task for them! And this is the case today. Will you find Yared somewhere here in Furukzahar and tell him that an order has come in for additional rock-scrapers? He can give them to you and you can bring them back to me... for a reward, of course.''Will you find Yared somewhere here in Furukzahar and tell him that an order has come in for additional rock-scrapers? He can give them to you and you can bring them back to me... for a reward, of course.''My friend ${PLAYER}! I am glad you have returned! You are always welcome here! But what brings you hither?

'Shegai asks for rock-scrapers? Oh, yes, they are around here somewhere. They will be in one of these crates, if you don't mind helping me search for them.''The rock-scrapers are around here somewhere. They will be in one of these crates, if you don't mind helping me search for them.''I could have sworn they were in one of these crates, ${PLAYER}.'

Yared toys with the end of his beard as realization dawns.

'Uh oh.'Gladion has invited you to dine with his family again.Gladion has invited you to join him and his family for dinner.

Talk to him when you're ready to go inside.Talk to GladionSupper has concluded and Gladion has moved outside for some fresh air.

Speak to Gladion in the field next to his house.Talk to Gladion'Before you leave, we would love if you could join us for dinner. Surely even you must need a rest after such hard labour?'You relay what Limril said to you.

'Ah, I see. I was afraid I had made some misstep.'

He sighs and runs his hand down his face.

'It has been a trying several months. We have all taken my brother's death very hard. Limril and I try to keep our spirits up especially in front of the children. As you can see, this does not always work.''Limril will be delighted to see you.'Yared has remembered in which crate the rock-scrapers demanded by Shegai were packed.Someone needs to check the highest crate used in The Stacking Game for the rock-scrapers demanded by Shegai.Check the highest crate used in The Stacking Game for rock-scrapersYared is waiting for you to descend and speak to him.Bring the rock-scrapers to YaredShegai is in the Armoury of Furukzahar.'I think the rock-scrapers were stored in the pivotal crate we used in The Stacking Game, ${PLAYER}... but none of the rest of us can get up there to retrieve them! You are the only one who can retrieve them for us!

'We are all counting on you... again!''None of the rest of us can get up to the highest crate to check it for rock-scrapers! You are the only one who can do this!''You did it! Thank you for retrieving the rock-scrapers for us!

'Can I ask another favour? When you bring these tools to Shegai, will you please not tell him that The Stacking Game made finding the rock-scrapers more difficult? He does not approve of it, and while I usually lose the game I would still miss it if he forbade us from playing it.''When you bring these tools to Shegai, will you please not tell him that The Stacking Game made finding the rock-scrapers more difficult? He does not approve of it, and while I usually lose the game I would still miss it if he forbade us from playing it.''These are the rock-scrapers I requested, and I thank you for them. Now tell me: did Yared cooperate? Did he know where these could be found, and was able to retrieve them quickly and easily?

'Ah, nevermind. I know Yared and the other dwarves who work for me think I disapprove of their games, but I would not make them stop playing them. I know how important such things are for the smooth running of the fortress! What matters is that when work comes in, it is accomplished without hesitation or delay... and here it has been.

'But do not tell Yared what I have said to you! Let him and the others think they are getting away with something. If fear that I might take away their Stacking Game keeps them sharp, who am I to dull them by letting slip that it is fine? If that must be the relationship between worker and supervisor, so be it.'

Shegai hums a brief tune, and then laughs.

'If I were not their supervisor, however, and was invited to play, I tell you I would stack my crates the highest! I was very skilled at such things when I was young.'Annoyingly aggressive avanc have been causing issues along the banks of the rivers in Lamedon.Drambor has asked you to search for his missing pack at one of the waterfalls between the beacons and Calembel.

