Maeron is in the Calembel barracks.Bring the crate to MaeronMaeron has asked you to distribute tonics to wounded soldiers in the Calembel barracks.You should let Maeron know that have brought healing potions to many of the wounded soldiers in the barracks.

Maeron is in the Calembel barracks.'Good day to you, ${CLASS}. I am Eliaril, one of the healers of Calembel. If you are making your way up the hill to Calembel, may I impose upon you to bring a crate of  Cemenduril tonics to the barracks? Many soldiers came back from the war wounded, and the potions aid in their healing.

'Bring the crate to Maeron, and he will show you what is to be done.''Done already? Have you considered a position at a healing house? You seem to have the touch. My thanks for your assistance.''Welcome to the Calembel barracks, ${CLASS}. You bring tonics from Eliaril? Excellent. While you're here, you might as well pass them out to the wounded soldiers. I could use all the help I can get.'King Elessar and Queen Arwen's journey westward will next pass into Dor-en-Ernil and the Ringló Vale.Caebar is by the eastern entrance of the town of Linhir, in King's Gondor.Talk to Caebar by the eastern entrance of Linhir, in King's GondorCaebar made a list of the most common complaints of Linhir's townsfolk: foes in Dor-en-Ernil, pests in the town, burned timbers in Linhir, and listening to the concerns of the people.Defeat pests in Linhir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hear the concerns of NimdolHear the concerns of MaerielHear the concerns of ForcharnCaebar is by the eastern entrance of the town of Linhir, in King's Gondor.Talk to Caebar by the eastern entrance of Linhir, in King's GondorBarad Rill is located to the south-west of Linhir, at the southern point of the peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.Travel to Barad Rill, the grand lighthouse in Dor-en-Ernil, in King's GondorCaebar stares at the ruin of Barad Rill at the southern peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.Talk to Caebar in view of Barad Rill, in King's GondorCaebar gave you a sketch of the lighthouse of Barad Rill, seen in happier days.Examine the sketch of Barad Rill given to you by CaebarCaebar stares at the ruin of Barad Rill at the southern peninsula of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.Caebar has a renewed interest in facing the foes of Gondor that prowl Dor-en-Ernil or the Ringló Vale, in King's Gondor.Defeat enemies of Gondor in Dor-en-Ernil or the Ringló Vale, King's Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Caebar's hometown of Ethring is located in the Ringló Vale, north of Dor-en-Ernil, in King's Gondor.Travel to the southern entrance of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale, King's GondorUilin stands at the entrance of Ethring, glaring at you and Caebar.Talk to Uilin at the entrance of Ethring, in King's Gondor'I have sent the rest of the travelling party on to Linhir with instructions to aid the people there. Your report that supporters of the Heirs of Castamir maintained a presence in that city is worrisome to me; perhaps if we can give the townsfolk what help they need we will help reduce support for any of that sort who remain.

'I told Caebar to make a list of notable tasks. Meet up with him in Linhir and learn the content of his catalogue of things that need doing. Afterwards, he is to guide the company through Dor-en-Ernil and into the Ringló Vale. Arwen and I will meet up with you there, or in Lamedon if we meet with delays.''I told Caebar to make a list of notable tasks. Meet up with him in Linhir and learn the content of his catalogue of things that need doing. Afterwards, he is to guide the company through Dor-en-Ernil and into the Ringló Vale. Arwen and I will meet up with you there, or in Lamedon if we meet with delays.''Oh, ${PLAYER}, I am glad to see you, for I am at the end of my wits! The King instructed me to make a list of things we might do to aid the people of Linhir, but everyone I asked had a different idea of where to start! Some are concerned about the foes that still stalk Dor-en-Ernil, to the west of the river. Others claim the pests that inhabit the town have gotten out of control in recent weeks, others say the burned timbers that remain in Linhir pose a risk to the health of the citizenry, and some... well, I think some folk just want to talk.

'I don't know with which of these things you want to start, but the King did say we were to be comprehensive on his behalf! I will see to the burned timbers, but perhaps you can tackle the other items on the list?''Everyone I asked had a different idea of where to start! Some are concerned about the foes that still stalk Dor-en-Ernil, to the west of the river. Others claim the pests that inhabit the town have gotten out of control in recent weeks, others say the burned timbers that remain in Linhir pose a risk to the health of the citizenry, and some... well, I think some folk just want to talk.''You took care of everything on the list? You are good at this, aren't you?

'The King asked me to direct everyone through Dor-en-Ernil and into the Ringló Vale, where he and Queen Arwen will rejoin us. I don't know why he chose me for this task... do you think he knows that I was born in Ethring? I might have mentioned it to you once when he was nearby, but surely he would not remember a thing like that!

'The grand lighthouse of Barad Rill is on our way, and I would not mind stopping to see it before we continue on to Ethring. I visited it when I was just a boy and found it most impressive. I heard a disturbing rumour that the lighthouse sustained some damage during the war, but perhaps that talk was exaggerated? I hope so, at any rate.''It is worse than I expected.''The grand lighthouse of Barad Rill is on our way, and I would not mind stopping to see it before we continue on to Ethring. I visited it when I was just a boy and found it most impressive. I heard a disturbing rumour that the lighthouse sustained some damage during the war, but perhaps that talk was exaggerated? I hope so, at any rate.''It is much worse than I expected, ${PLAYER}. What manner of devilry did the Corsairs of Umbar harness to knock down such a structure as the grand lighthouse? But more than that: how could they bring themselves to do it?

'I did not bring much of my artwork with me when I left for Minas Tirith to join the service of the City as a scribe, but I did bring one piece: a sketch I made of this lighthouse when I was just a boy. Here, you can see it if you like.''I made that sketch of Barad Rill in much happier days.''Ah, thank you, ${PLAYER}. The sketch is painful now, but I will keep it close as a reminder of what the enemies of Gondor will not hesitate to take from us. It lifts my spirits to see the construction effort! But I wish it were not necessary.

'As we make our way north through Dor-en-Ernil to my hometown of Ethring, let us face whatever foes we encounter with courage and strength, for the King and for Gondor.''As we make our way north through Dor-en-Ernil to my hometown of Ethring, let us face whatever foes we encounter with courage and strength, for the King and for Gondor.''As we make our way north through Dor-en-Ernil to my hometown of Ethring, let us face whatever foes we encounter with courage and strength, for the King and for Gondor.''So you're back, are you?''So you're back now, Caebar, now that Ethring doesn't need you? Your mother will weep to hear it.

'And who is this stranger? You have the look of an Elf-friend, and that is not a popular thing to resemble in these days.'Caebar has returned to his hometown of Ethring at the King's direction, but the homecoming is not a pleasant one.Caebar has returned home to Ethring, but it is not a pleasant homecoming.Talk to Caebar at the entrance of EthringCaebar's mother's house is to the north across the bridge and to the right, in the village of Ethring, in King's Gondor.Find the home of Caebar's mother, SirdisCarlong blocks the way into the home of Caebar's mother, Sirdis.Talk to Carlong in front of Sirdis's houseCaebar stands outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor.Talk to Caebar outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's GondorCaebar wants you to listen to the concerns of Ethring's villagers.Caebar stands outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's Gondor.Talk to Caebar outside his mother's house in Ethring, in King's GondorThe town of Calembel is north-west of the Ringló Vale, in Lamedon, King's Gondor.Travel to the entrance of Calembel in Lamedon, King's GondorGarthaben calls excitedly to you south-east of the entrance to Calembel.Talk to Garthaben south of Calembel, in King's GondorGalengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts is in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor.Enter Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's GondorGalengam is inside his crowded shop in the south-west corner of Calembel, in King's Gondor.Talk to Galengam inside his shop in Calembel, King's Gondor'Caebar left us to make his own way in the world. He could have returned when war seemed unavoidable, but instead he left his mother to fend for herself. Poor Sirdis is fortunate that her brother was here to take care of her, and the rest of the town did what we could.

'Where was Caebar when the skies turned dark and the sun never rose? He was away in the White City, feasting and drinking fine wine while the rest of us suffered! He spared not a thought for Ethring, and now when things are good he wants to return? Let him try, that's what I say. We have not forgotten.''Where was Caebar when the skies turned dark and the sun never rose? He was away in the White City, feasting and drinking fine wine while the rest of us suffered! He spared not a thought for Ethring, and now when things are good he wants to return? Let him try, that's what I say. We have not forgotten.''It is true that I left home before war seemed certain, but how could I have known how bad things would get? I worried about home every day...'

Caebar casts his eyes to the ground.

'I should have come back before now. My family and my friends had to endure the darkness Sauron sent before his armies, just as I did, but they had to do it without the armies of Minas Tirith near at hand. I understand why Uilin is upset. I should go to see my mother, ${PLAYER}. Our house... her house... is to the north, across the bridge and to the right.''I should have come back before now. My family and my friends had to endure the darkness Sauron sent before his armies, just as I did, but they had to do it without the armies of Minas Tirith near at hand. I understand why Uilin is upset. I should go to see my mother, ${PLAYER}. Our house... her house... is to the north, across the bridge and to the right.''She doesn't want to see you, Caebar. You had better find somewhere else to go.'

Carlong looks at you appraisingly.

'You're with the new King, just as Caebar seems to be? You can keep moving, same as my nephew. We here in Ethring know the Elves are behind putting this Elessar on the throne, and we're not going to let them interfere with life in the Ringló Vale. When Caebar left, it broke his mother's heart... but it broke again when he became a puppet of the Elves. She doesn't want to see him.''She doesn't want to see him.''My uncle Carlong may be right about me, but he is wrong about the King. King Elessar is a good man, and he wants what is best for Gondor!

'I don't have time to be upset about this, ${PLAYER}. I was given a task by my King, and I am going to see it done. Let us do what we can for the folk of Ethring, and perhaps my mother and my uncle will see that King Elessar is not a pawn of the Elves or of anyone else!''I don't have time to be upset about this, ${PLAYER}. I was given a task by my King, and I am going to see it done. Let us do what we can for the folk of Ethring, and perhaps my mother and my uncle will see that King Elessar is not a pawn of the Elves or of anyone else!''You should just return to your King, and take Caebar with you. This is no longer his home.''You are not wanted here, and neither is my nephew.''Did anyone... did anyone want our help, ${PLAYER}?'

Caebar appears more defeated than you have ever seen him, and you ask what has happened.

'I told my uncle I would leave, if that is what my mother truly wants, but that I would like to retrieve some of the sketches I had left inside when I departed for Minas Tirith. He said... he said when I was gone, my mother burned them all.'

Caebar sighs heavily, and raises his head.

'There is nothing left for me here, and the King and Queen have not arrived. We should move on to Calembel. The King said he might rejoin us in Lamedon.''There is nothing left for me here, and the King and Queen have not arrived. We should move on to Calembel. The King said he might rejoin us in Lamedon.''It is for the best that Caebar move on. His mother already has... she was forced to do so when he departed.''The King and Queen have come to Calembel! It is true, they are here with their entire retinue! I saw them going to speak with Galengam!

'Look for his shop to the north-west, inside the city, and you might catch a glimpse of them. Imagine that: the King and Queen, here in Lamedon! I never would have expected them to travel so far from Minas Tirith, and yet I saw them with my own eyes!''The King and Queen have come to Calembel! It is true, they are here with their entire retinue! I saw them going to speak with Galengam!

'Look for his shop to the north-west, inside the city, and you might catch a glimpse of them. Imagine that: the King and Queen, here in Lamedon! I never would have expected them to travel so far from Minas Tirith, and yet I saw them with my own eyes!''If there was ever any doubt that I sell only the finest of goods, let that doubt now be dispelled! I am to be the personal merchant of the King and Queen of Gondor themselves, as always I dreamed!'King Elessar has decided to answer the invitation of the Dwarves of Furukzahar, stronghold of the Temámir in the White Mountains.Queen Arwen is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, in King's Gondor.Talk to Queen Arwen at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's GondorGimli is at the dry dock in south-eastern Pelargir, in King's Gondor.Talk to Gimli at the dry dock in Pelargir, King's GondorSékhel stands guard outside the entrance to Furukzahar.Travel to the entrance of Furukzahar in the White Mountains north of Pelargir, in King's GondorThe dwarf Sékhel stands guard at the entrance to Furukzahar.Talk to Sékhel at the entrance to FurukzaharKing Elessar stands outside the entrance to the Temámir fortress of Furukzahar, in the White Mountains.Talk to King Elessar outside the entrance to Furukzahar, in King's GondorThe Dwarves of Furukzahar expect a gift from those who visit them, and the guard Sékhel suggested that you hunt the game to be found in the valley for that purpose.Hunt animals in the valley outside Furukzahar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The dwarf Sékhel stands guard at the entrance to Furukzahar.Sékhel, the guard outside Furukzahar, has regretfully informed you that King Elessar is not yet permitted inside. He will have to wait a little longer.Wait until Sékhel says King Elessar is permitted inside FurukzaharGimli has grown impatient and is not pleased at being made to wait outside the entrance to Furukzahar.Talk to Gimli outside the entrance to FurukzaharSékhel, the guard outside Furukzahar, has regretfully informed you that King Elessar is not yet permitted inside. He will have to wait a little longer.Wait until Sékhel says King Elessar is permitted inside FurukzaharKutúkh has emerged from the stronghold of Furukzahar.Talk to Kutúkh at the entrance to Furukzahar'But I sadly admit that staring at the ships under construction will not speed up the process. Gondor must now depend on the skill of her craftsmen and the quality of their work, and her King must look to other matters. If the Kindred of the Coins turns its gaze upon our shores in the next few months, we will need Gondor's fleets, buildings, and quays repaired... but we will also need to repair the bonds of friendship between Gondor and her neighbours.

'Let us accept the invitation of the Dwarves of Furukzahar, ${PLAYER}. We will visit them in the White Mountains and negotiate a fair arrangement between their people and my kingdom. We may need true-hearted allies in the days to come, and Gondor's stone-work could use the attention of such as these dwarves. What does my Queen say to this proposal?''Let us accept the invitation of the Dwarves of Furukzahar. What does my Queen say to this proposal?''My husband speaks the truth: if ties of friendship are neglected, they can slip loose entirely. It sounds to my ear that the affection between the people of Gondor and the Dwarves of the White Mountains is already strained, and threatens to become worse.

'The King should take a smaller party than the one with which he left Minas Tirith. You should go with him, ${PLAYER}, and Gimli, and I suggest too that he bring the company's scribe, Caebar. Should any records be drawn about the meeting between my husband and the ruler of Furukzahar, Caebar will have the tools necessary.

'The rest of the company will stay for a few days in Pelargir, but we will rejoin your small band at Ost Anglebed, and continue onward together.''The King should take a smaller party than the one with which he left Minas Tirith. You should go with him, ${PLAYER}, and Gimli, and I suggest too that he bring the company's scribe, Caebar. Should any records be drawn about the meeting between my husband and the ruler of Furukzahar, Caebar will have the tools necessary.

'The rest of the company will stay for a few days in Pelargir, but we will rejoin your small band at Ost Anglebed, and continue onward together.''You will want me along on this mission, of course. The Dwarves of Furukzahar are not Longbeards, but you cannot best a dwarf when it comes to speaking with other dwarves! They will want to hear what I have to say, even as they spare not a moment for the King of Gondor.

'It's true that you don't see Temámir in the North very often, but they did answer the call of the Sixth War of Dwarves and Orcs, and suffered losses as severe as any other house. Their stronghold of Furukzahar is hidden in a cleft of the White Mountains to the north of Pelargir? Then let us be off, and see if the hospitality of the Temámir is to be as noteworthy as their wisdom!''The stronghold of Furukzahar is hidden in a cleft of the White Mountains to the north of Pelargir? Then let us be off, and see if the hospitality of the Temámir is to be as noteworthy as their wisdom!''Welcome to Furukzahar, stronghold of the Temámir in the White Mountains. All are welcome within, of course, but affairs of state are such that the arrival of the King of Gondor demands a little extra preparation! I ask that you wait until I hear word from my brethren inside that you may enter.

'I do not wish to inconvenience you... but it is also customary to bring a gift when you arrive here. Perhaps some meat from the game that is to be found in this valley? I do not wish to impose a burden upon you, but it will be my great shame if I were to allow you inside without such a gift, and you were thought to be discourteous. I cannot allow that to happen, if it might be prevented!''I do not wish to inconvenience you... but it is also customary to bring a gift when you arrive here. Perhaps some meat from the game that is to be found in this valley? I do not wish to impose a burden upon you, but it will be my great shame if I were to allow you inside without such a gift, and you were thought to be discourteous. I cannot allow that to happen, if it might be prevented!''We are here on a mission of friendship, ${PLAYER}, and therefore we will do what custom and tradition demand of us. Let us hunt some of the wild game to be found in this valley, and may the Temámir enjoy what bounty we can bring to them.

'I trust the game animals of this vale are plentiful, Sékhel of Furukzahar?''Let us hunt some of the wild game to be found in this valley, and may the Temámir enjoy what bounty we can bring to them. I trust the game animals of this vale are plentiful, Sékhel of Furukzahar?''I hope the dwarves will accept these gifts from us in the spirit of their custom, and as tokens of friendship from Gondor.''Yes, this gift will do nicely. It is good you have done as my people expect, and our ruler Hámisar will be pleased to learn that the King of Gondor does not think himself above such customs as we hold in Furukzahar.'

Sékhel permits himself a small smile, and then shakes his head regretfully.

'However, it pains me to tell you that we are not yet ready to allow the King of Gondor inside. You will have to wait a little longer.''If the Dwarves of Furukzahar think to test my patience, I am determined to pass the test, ${PLAYER}. Give no sign of displeasure, my friend, and we will weather this challenge.''This is ridiculous! How long must we wait until they permit Elessar to go inside?''Do dwarves usually make people wait this long?''This is intolerable! How long do they intend to make us wait? We did not come here to be made to stand on the doorstep like common peddlers! Should any Temámir come to Thorin's Halls, would they be kept outside for the merest whim? I think they would not!'

Elessar gives Gimli a meaningful look, and the dwarf glowers at him.

'I am sorry, my friend, but this endless waiting is intended as an insult! You cannot see it? Did they not invite the King of Gondor to visit them? Or did they do so in order to slight you in this fashion? No Longbeard would stand for it, and I should think the King of Gondor would have more demands upon his time than would allow him to waste such time as this!''And still we wait! With whom do these dwarves think they are dealing? This is Elf-like behaviour, if you ask me!

'Perhaps you will refrain from telling Legolas I said that, friend? But this is ridiculous!''If the dwarves think to test our patience, I am determined not to fail the challenge, ${PLAYER}. Please make sure Gimli says nothing we will regret.''Do dwarves usually make folk wait like this?''Allow me to convey Hámisar's deepest apologies for the wait. He is of course delighted to meet with the King of Gondor and his companions, and regrets only that the meeting has not happened before now.'King Elessar has been invited to visit Furukzahar, a stronghold of the Temámir dwarves in the White Mountains.The ruler of Furukzahar awaits you and the King of Gondor in his throne room in the north-western reaches of the fortress.Find Hámisar in the throne room of FurukzaharHámisar rules Furukzahar from his throne room in the north-western reaches of the fortress.Talk to Hámisar inside the throne room of FurukzaharHámisar has invited you to meet the people of Furukzahar while he speaks with King Elessar.Explore the armoury of FurukzaharExplore the kitchens of FurukzaharExplore the rooms south of the throne room in FurukzaharTalk to Asitám in FurukzaharTalk to Gúlkhu in FurukzaharTalk to Zimikál in FurukzaharKing Elessar and Hámisar of the Temámir speak together in the throne room of Furukzahar.Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of FurukzaharKing Elessar and Hámisar of the Temámir speak together in the throne room of Furukzahar.Talk to Hámisar in the throne room of Furukzahar'You may enter. Hámisar awaits you within.''Hámisar awaits you within.''Welcome, King Elessar, to the stronghold of Furukzahar. How shameful that our folk have remained neighbours for so long without you coming to visit us here. I mourn that it took the fighting of a war to bring us together... but at least something did so.'

Hámisar turns his attention to you.

'I gave my greeting to the King, but of course his companions are welcome here as well! He and I have matters to discuss concerning the ongoing relationship between our peoples and how the Temámir can best aid in the rebuilding of his kingdom. I would not think to bore you with such matters! I hope you will explore the beautiful corridors of Furukzahar and meet with my folk.''Enjoy the sights of Furukzahar while the King of Gondor and I speak about the ongoing relationship between our peoples.''Enjoy yourself, my friend. I will ask Caebar to stay and document the proceedings, but you and Gimli are free to meet with Hámisar's people.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I did not expect the King of Gondor to accept the invitation to visit Furukzahar so swiftly! It reflects well upon him for respecting the will of Hámisar, and upon you for bringing word to him with such haste!

'I hope you enjoy your stay here, and that King Elessar and ruler Hámisar are able to arrive at a fair and equitable arrangement that will enrich both of their folk.''What has brought you to Furukzahar? I hope you do not think to involve us in your wars? The Temámir of Furukzahar have always welcomed visitors from the other dwarf families, but Hámisar shut the gates for a reason. He did not intend to invite Gondor's war to our doorstep.''I ask that you wander elsewhere, stranger. There's nothing for you here.''Hámisar and I have come to an arrangement for the continued relations of his people and mine, ${PLAYER}. During the discussion... something revealed itself to me.'

Elessar holds your gaze with a stern eye.

'Hámisar spoke to me of a group arising in Umbar, across the Bay of Belfalas. He says they call themselves... the Kindred of... something. What was it?''What did they call themselves? The Kindred of... the something?''They are called the Kindred of the Coins, Elessar, but feel no shame at forgetting it. The name is fresh in my mind, for a member of their company visited Furukzahar some weeks ago with a proposal for me.'A member of the Kindred of the Coins brought a proposal to Hámisar of Furukzahar in recent weeks.King Elessar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of FurukzaharThe guest rooms of Furukzahar are on the eastern side of the fortress.Find the guest rooms provided for Elessar's party on the eastern side of FurukzaharKing Elessar's small travelling party waits in the guest rooms provided by Hámisar.Talk to King Elessar in the guest rooms of FurukzaharTalk to Gimli in the guest rooms of FurukzaharTalk to Caebar in the guest rooms of FurukzaharYou experienced a sensation of dread near a door located south of the throne room in Furukzahar, and King Elessar thinks you should investigate further.Investigate the suspicious door south of the throne room in FurukzaharGangur Farwend, a Longbeard visiting from the north, has quietly called for your attention.Talk to Gangur Farwend by the suspicious door in FurukzaharGangur Farwend has information for you, but he will only share it if you meet with him inside the armoury of Furukzahar.Talk to Gangur Farwend inside the armoury of Furukzahar in the north-eastern reaches of the fortressKing Elessar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar on the eastern side of the fortress.Talk to King Elessar in the guest rooms of FurukzaharElessar gave you the sketch Caebar made of Khôltekh the Cunning from Gangur's description.Examine the sketch of Khôltekh the CunningCaebar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar.King Elessar is in the guest rooms of Furukzahar on the eastern side of the fortress.Talk to King Elessar in the guest rooms of Furukzahar'This messenger was named Khôltekh, and he claimed that the Kindred of the Coins had overthrown the servants of Sauron who ruled in Umbar. Now they name it a Free City, and seek allies to defend themselves from those who preferred the old order of things... and from Gondor, it must be said.

'It was a proposal of peace and friendship that Khôltekh brought to me. I do not wish to become involved in the affairs of Umbar, so while I did not immediately refuse, nor did I give him the enthusiastic agreement he desired. I sent him on his way, but if he was disappointed he did not show it when he departed. That was a fortnight ago, and he is likely back in Umbar by now.

'But we have spoken now for such a time that my throat is parched and my eyes weary. Accept a guest room and remain here for the night. There is no need for you to depart as speedily as did Khôltekh, after all. A room will be provided for you on the eastern side of the fortress, King Elessar, and I trust your companions will take their rest in comfort. What say you to this?''Accept a guest room and remain here for the night. There is no need for you to depart as speedily as did Khôltekh, after all. A room will be provided for you on the eastern side of the fortress, King Elessar, and I trust your companions will take their rest in comfort. What say you to this?''We will accept your gracious offer of hospitality, Hámisar, and I thank you for dealing with the emissary of the Kindred of the Coins as you say. Gondor does not wish for war, and if Umbar does not offer violence, we will have no need to respond with such.

'Come, my friends. We will retire to our guest rooms and leave Hámisar to think upon the matters we discussed. No doubt he values the friendship of Gondor, and understands the importance of such a relationship for Furukzahar, and for his people.''Let us retire to the rooms Hámisar has provided.''Please enjoy the hospitality of Furukzahar. Your guest rooms are on the eastern side of the fortress.''I do not like this, ${PLAYER}. Hámisar is hiding something. I think he would have preferred not to speak to us of the Kindred of the Coins, and had we left him the choice he would not have spoken of them at all. I believe this Khôltekh came to Furukzahar, but I am less certain the meeting was as Hámisar presented it.

'We should remain on our guard while we are here. Something about this situation does not feel right.''That Hámisar is lying to us. I don't know about what, or why he seeks to deceive us, but I can see it as plainly as you can see the beard on my handsome face.

'I knew there was something afoot when he made us wait so long on the doorstep! It was not mere discourtesy... it was villainy of some kind! We have yet to discover what type of villainy, perhaps... but villainy nonetheless!

'Do you think it has something to do with the unpleasant sensation of dread we felt by that door south of the throne room, ${PLAYER}? What is Hámisar keeping in that chamber?''Do you really think Hámisar is lying to the King? Why would he risk such a dangerous deception? You don't think he's in league with the Kindred of the Coins, do you?

'I am just a scribe, ${PLAYER}, and not especially accomplished at that. I am not an adventurer or a hero like you; I left my home in Ethring a few months before the outbreak of war. Ever since I came to Minas Tirith and the service of the City, I have become embroiled in great events I find myself unable to comprehend.

'It is all very overwhelming to me. What is Hámisar keeping from the King?''What is Hámisar keeping behind that suspicious door, ${PLAYER}? Perhaps you can investigate further, but do try not to draw attention to yourself.''I knew there was something going on when they made us wait on the doorstep for so long. Did I not tell you so?''I feel as if I struggle to stay afloat in deep water, and something tries to pull me under. I have felt this way for most of my time in the employ of the King, and the Steward Denethor before him!''You are a companion of the King of Gondor? Have we met? My memory for faces is not what it once was, and I am far from my home. I am here visiting, but I believe I have information you should know.

'Quietly! We should not speak here. Let us meet inside the armoury, across the water to the north-east. There will be fewer unfriendly ears to hear what I have to say, and the noise of the forges should help to hide our conversation.''Not here! We should speak inside the armoury, across the water to the north-east. The noise will help to hide our conversation.''When I first arrived here, the Temámir showed me a great deal of hospitality, and Hámisar gave me his personal welcome. I was most impressed, for while I have been warmly greeted at every dwarf-hold I visited on my travels, Furukzahar outshone them all. But then it all changed.

'A few days ago, an emissary from the Kindred of the Coins arrived. His name you know, for Hámisar told it to you, but he withheld his epithet and the folk to whom he belongs. His full name is Khôltekh the Cunning, and he is a dwarf of the Temámir who hails from some distant land. And yet it was not from Umbar he came, or at least not directly; he came from the west. From conversations I overheard I understand that he received delivery of some artifact from the north, and he brought it with him to Furukzahar.

'Hámisar told you this emissary of the Kindred departed, but I think he is still here; it is the dread of the artifact he bears that you sensed outside the door where he shelters. I do not know why the Temámir became so cold to me after he arrived, or why their leader lies to the King of Gondor, but I thought you should know. I will speak with King Elessar briefly, if it can be arranged in secret, but I think you should all leave this place before it is too late. Furukzahar may not be safe for you.''Hámisar told you this emissary of the Kindred departed, but I think he is still here; it is the dread of the artifact he bears that you sensed outside the door where he shelters. I do not know why the Temámir became so cold to me after he arrived, or why their leader lies to the King of Gondor, but I thought you should know. I will speak with King Elessar briefly, if it can be arranged in secret, but I think you should all leave this place before it is too late. Furukzahar may not be safe for you.''Gangur Farwend was just here, ${PLAYER}, and he told me what he said to you. I asked him to describe Khôltekh, and he did the best he could... he did say his memory for faces is not what it used to be. Caebar sketched a drawing from the description. Here it is.''You should examine the sketch Caebar made of Khôltekh the Cunning.''Once you have studied the sketch, you can give it back to Caebar.''My hand shook as I drew the sketch, ${PLAYER}. I do not know if I am properly cut out for such an adventure as this! I hope you and the King find the drawing useful. Will you now know Khôltekh the Cunning if you see him?

'If you will not, the fault lies with me... I apologized to the King, for I am only an amateur artist, but he would not hear it. He is too good for such as I am.''This is all so overwhelming. How did I come to be here?''We have no choice now, my friends. We should get as much rest as we are able. Whatever Hámisar thinks to keep from us, whether it is the continued presence of Khôltekh the Cunning in Furukzahar or some other deception, we cannot reveal it if he chooses to keep it hidden.

'We will depart in the morning. Rest for now... but lightly.'The time has come for Elessar and his companions to leave Furukzahar and rejoin the larger company.Hámisar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.Talk to Hámisar in the throne room of FurukzaharKing Elessar is in the throne room of Furukzahar.Talk to King Elessar in the throne room of FurukzaharThe Hall of Ost Anglebed is to be found south-west of Furukzahar, in King's Gondor.Rejoin Elessar's travelling party outside the Hall of Ost AnglebedThe Hall of Ost Anglebed is to be found south-west of Furukzahar, in King's Gondor.Talk to Glindor outside the Hall of Ost Anglebed'It is time for us to take our leave, Hámisar of Furukzahar. We thank you for your gracious hospitality, and for your continued friendship. The efforts of your folk on behalf of mine in the days to come will not be forgotten.''May there be continued friendship between the Temámir and the people of Gondor.''I share your hopes for the future, King Elessar of Gondor, and have this to say as well. As you return to your kingdom and continue the journey about which you spoke yestereve, let caution guide your steps. There are snakes in the grass everywhere.

'Indeed, even some dwarves may hold treachery in their hearts, and give voice to things they ought not. I had to send one such troublemaker from Furukzahar this very morning; the Longbeard Gangur Farwend is no longer welcome within these walls.

'But it is different for you and your companions, King Elessar! You, of course, are welcome to return at any time should you wish to discuss the continuing relationship of our folk. But remember what I said: beware of snakes in the grass, for they are more likely to strike when you expect it not.''Remember what I said: beware of snakes in the grass.''Fear not, Hámisar. I will remember your words.'

Elessar gives you a knowing look.

'Come now, my friends. We shall rejoin the rest of our travelling party at the Hall of Ost Anglebed, to the south-west.''Come now, my friends. We shall rejoin the rest of our travelling party at the Hall of Ost Anglebed, to the south-west.''It's terrible, just terrible!''It's terrible, ${PLAYER}, just terrible! Queen Arwen is nowhere to be found!'Queen Arwen has disappeared, and none know where she might be found.You should ask around Ost Anglebed and learn if anyone knows where the Elf-queen has gone.Ioreth told you she saw someone wearing a cloak much like Queen Arwen's walking to the north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river.Find Queen Arwen in King's GondorQueen Arwen is deep in conversation with Roamingstar, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.Talk to Queen ArwenRoamingstar stands beside Queen Arwen, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.Talk to Roamingstar, Maiden of the GilrainRoamingstar stands beside Queen Arwen, north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.Wait for a new arrivalKing Elessar has rejoined his Queen north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor.Talk to King Elessar north-west of Ost Anglebed, in King's Gondor'I beg you, ask around Ost Anglebed and find the Queen! The King will never forgive us if we have allowed some harm to befall her!''Someone in Ost Anglebed must know where the Queen has gone!''I am sorry I cannot help you, ${PLAYER}! I was deep in conversation with Aphadaer and Grethril a few hours ago, and we only learned the Queen was missing when we returned from our walk! It was such a nice stroll, it was, with the flowers all in bloom... Aphadaer presented me with the finest one he could find, and...'

Ioreth trails off, a faint blush colouring her cheeks.

'Do you know, I think he might be sweet on me? Can you imagine? Oh, to be young again! But now that you mention it, while we were out I did see someone wearing a cloak very similar to the one the Queen prefers walking north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river. Do you think she might have gone that way?''I have not seen my sister today, but I am not yet worried. Arwen can take care of herself, if the need arises.

'She will be fine.''The Queen is gone? What do you think might have happened to her?

'Do you think she will be all right? What will happen now to Gondor?''I have not seen Queen Arwen today. I hope she is safe!

'Have you spoken with Ioreth? She sees more than you might think, and may know where the Queen has gone!''We must not immediately expect foul play, ${PLAYER}. The Queen is likely to be fine.

'But we should speak with those of our company who may have seen her lately, perhaps Grethril, Aphadaer, or Ioreth. They are often together, and may have observed without notice what happened to Arwen.''I have spoken with the folk up here, and none have seen the Queen. Perhaps you should search the lower levels of the city.''Now that you mention it, while we were out I did see someone wearing a cloak very similar to the one the Queen prefers walking north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river. Do you think she might have gone that way?''Ioreth saw someone wearing the Queen's cloak walking to the north-west of Ost Anglebed, in the direction of the river? You should hurry after her, and see for certain!''But I hope you will heed my words, Maiden of the Gilrain, and trouble yourself not overmuch. A life is lived as it is lived, and if we grieve for all that has transpired, or for all that will, we could not bear the sorrow. Let it not weigh too heavily upon you, dear one.'

Arwen turns to see you, and smiles.

'I hope I did not worry the company too greatly, ${PLAYER}, but I did not want to burden Roamingstar with the tramping feet of my husband's entire retinue. There were things to be said in private, and I felt certain I could return before Ioreth finished her chattering. I saw her from afar and it seemed she had only recently begun. Even from such a distance I believe she might have become rather enamoured of the groom who keeps the horses.''There were things to be said in private. I hope the rest of the company did not worry overmuch about me.''Arwen has shown me a kindness of the sort I had thought vanished from the world, ${PLAYER}. I do not know what to say.''If I wore my Ranger garb I could have approached without making any noise, but these garments are much less suited for walking in the wilderness. I hope I did not frighten Roamingstar with my tramping! Arwen has spoken to me of her desire to meet the Maiden of the Gilrain, and I did not wish to interrupt.

'But I have need of you, my friend.'A frazzled farmer needs help looking after her livestock.Alagiel has asked you to check the chickens of Lothgobel for eggs.Tell Alagiel that you have checked all the chickens for eggs.Talk to Alagiel'I have much too much to do. If you have experience being a farmhand I would welcome your help.

'I need you to check the chickens to see if they have laid any eggs. I promised Old Grathir I would deliver him half a dozen eggs but with all my other work I don't have time to chase down my birds.''Thanks! Set down the eggs over there. Now if you'll excuse me I have some goats to feed.

'Once I find where they've gone. Oh dear....'It is time to confront Dravron.Dervorin is going to confront Dravron over his taxes, or lack thereof.

