Talk to Dornach at the lumber camp east of Ethring.Talk to Dornach'In our absence, the local wolves have grown bold. I cannot have them harassing my crews while they work.

'I would be grateful if you could discourage the wildlife from approaching us.''I hope your actions have sufficiently dissuaded the vale-wolves from approaching us.'

They dismiss you with a nod.The most delicious mushrooms in the Blackroot Vale can be found in the caverns of Lhingroth, but so can the spiders of Tarlang's Peaks.Silkencaps, a pale mushroom native to the Blackroot Vale, can be found in the caverns of Lhingroth in the hills to the south-east of Sardol.

Sidharan has asked you to collect silkencaps from the caverns of Lhingroth, but he has warned you that spiders dwell in Lhingroth. You should collect the silkencaps and deliver them to Sidharan in Sardol.Collect silkencaps in Lhingroth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sidharan can be found in Sardol.

You have collected many silkencaps from the caverns of Lhingroth. You should deliver them to Sidharan in Sardol.'Ho there! It was ${PLAYER}, right?

'I remember the last time you were here—all that nasty business with spiders and the Dead! But that is in the past, and now, we have welcomed some of our proud bowmen back to Sardol. I only wish more of them had made it home from the War....'

Sidharan pauses for a moment and sighs.

'There are joys still be found, though, and one of mine is a delicious mushroom stew that my neighbour Garthwen makes every so often. Garthwen's a brilliant cook, though she's far too modest to say as much. For her stew, she uses a mushroom native to the Blackroot Vale that we call a silkencap on account of its pale hue. The trouble is that silkencaps only grow in a few places, but they are most plentiful in Lhingroth. I don't think I need to remind you that the spiders of Tarlang's Peaks can also be found within those caverns, but Garthwen's supply has run out. It may not be as dire a problem as the Dead or the Corsairs, but I would appreciate your aid just the same, my friend. Little joys are what keep us together, after all.

'Would you collect some silkencaps for me and Garthwen?''Ah, you have them. Thank you!

'That ought to be enough to make a few pots of stew at least. Venison is pleasant enough, I'll admit, but I prefer a bit of variety in my meals. You understand, don't you? And there truly is nothing quite like these silkencaps!

'Here, ${PLAYER}, I actually still have a little left over from the last time I was able to sneak a few mushrooms out for Garthwen. I hope you enjoy it... and thank you for not forgetting about us, my friend.'Children of the Blackroot Vale often dare each other to approach the Stone of Erech, heedless of old warnings and the true danger that the Ruthless Dead now pose to them.Thendor, Glamion, and Randis can be found at the Hill of Erech, to the west of Lancrath in the Blackroot Vale.

Berthalend has asked you to find Thendor, Glamion, and Randis before they endanger themselves at the Hill of Erech.Find Thendor, Glamion, and Randis at the Hill of ErechThendor and Glamion can be found at the foot of the Hill of Erech near Lancrath, in the Blackroot Vale.

You have found Thendor and Glamion, but Randis does not appear to be with them. You should talk to Thendor and Glamion.Talk to Thendor at the Hill of ErechTalk to Glamion at the Hill of ErechRandis can be found at the Hill of Erech, in the Blackroot Vale.

Thendor and Glamion believe Randis is trying to fulfil her dare: to touch the Stone of Erech. You should find Randis.Find Randis at the Hill of ErechRandis can be found at the Stone of Erech, in the Blackroot Vale.

You have found Randis near the Stone of Erech, but she is clearly uneasy. You should talk to Randis.Talk to Randis at the Hill of ErechBerthalend can be found in Lancrath, in the Blackroot Vale.

You have convinced Randis, Thendor, and Glamion to return to Lancrath. You should talk to Berthalend.Talk to Berthalend'Hail, friend.

'I don't believe we spoke the last time you were in the Vale, but I remember your face. I am Berthalend, a simple craftsman of Gondor. And you are?'

You introduce yourself and inform Berthalend that you are one of King Elessar's emissaries.

'Ah, I did not realize you worked in service of the King! Might I ask a small favour of you? You see, some of the children in Lancrath have taken to daring each other to do this and that, and it is usually harmless fun. However, I overheard one of the older girls, Randis, talking about the Stone of Erech. You have been to the Vale before, ${PLAYER}, so surely you know what lurks on the Hill of Erech. Such a dare could lead them into grave danger!

'Randis set off with two young boys named Thendor and Glamion. Would you go find them? Tell them to come home before it is too late!''R-Randis wouldn't listen!'

Thendor is clearly afraid, and his voice barely rises above a whisper.

'I don't want to do the dare anymore! I want to go home!'

You comfort Thendor and try to encourage him to return to Lancrath with Glamion.'I was going to go with Randis, but then Thendor got scared, so I didn't want to leave him alone!'

Glamion appears visibly nervous.

'Randis said she wasn't going to come back until she touched the Stone, but it's been a long time....'

You tell Glamion to take Thendor back to Lancrath, and that you'll find Randis.

