You should talk to Boradan at Amon Lontir.Talk to Boradan'Hail, friend. Judging by your hurried steps, you seem to have much on your mind.

'Why not stay a while and take in the view? The sight of Edhellond to the north is always calming.''Whenever I look at Dol Amroth, a part of me still believes that I will see Corsair ships marring the bay. Despair often overtook me during the war, and I wondered how the city would fall.

'Our troubles are not over, and indeed, some scars may never heal. But we are still here, are we not? We are still here.

'May there be happier days ahead for you, ${PLAYER}. And should you find yourself plagued by dark thoughts, you are always welcome to return here.''Too many of my waking hours have been spent watching Edhellond with dread in my heart. We would have been no match for the Corsairs there. Perhaps that is cowardly of me to admit, but it is the truth.

'And yet, when I look out towards Edhellond now, I feel hope. Did you hear that the Elves are turning the harbour into a garden? May it remain a safe haven forevermore.

'But Edhellond is not the only place I'd like to point out -- behold Dol Amroth to the west.'Although Tingobel has been rebuilt, bowmen now stand guard to prevent the Orcs or any other foe from threatening the new peace in the Blackroot Vale.Newly-crafted arrows can be found in a barrel near Boradan's forge in Tingobel.

Boradan has asked you to collect his newly-crafted arrows and deliver them to the bowmen in Tingobel. You should collect the newly-crafted arrows.Collect the newly-crafted arrows in TingobelBowmen can be found throughout Tingobel in the Blackroot Vale.

You have collected the newly-crafted arrows from Boradan. You should deliver them to the bowmen in Tingobel.Boradan can be found in Tingobel.

You have delivered the arrows to the bowmen in Tingobel. You should return to Boradan.'I must thank you again for your efforts to wrest Tingobel from the Orcs during the War. Once Lord Duinhir and his men returned, the Orcs could scarcely defend themselves and fled into the mountains.

'I'm told that Lord Duinhir has ordered some of his men to remain in Tingobel lest the Orcs return. To that end, I've just finished crafting another batch of arrows, and it would be a great help if you could deliver them to the bowmen here in Tingobel. I don't believe that the Orcs will dare to return now that Tingobel is rebuilt and so well-defended, but if they do, we will be prepared. I will not lose my home a second time!

'Take as many as you can carry from this barrel and bring them to our bowmen.''Very good, ${PLAYER}.

'I've still got a great deal of work ahead of me, but I am glad to be back here in Tingobel. Lancrath and its people were very kind to us when Tingobel fell, and I will never forget that, but my place is here—at my home and at my forge!'One type of flower in Edhellond has been dying out in the months since the war's end.Cellineth has given you a bag of seeds to plant into empty flower beds.

You can find these flower beds scattered around Edhellond.Plant seeds into empty flower beds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have filled every flower bed you could find with seeds.

You should return your bag of seeds to Cellineth in Edhellond.'Mae govannen, traveller! Would you like to plant some flowers? I have seeds to spare.

'The Corsairs unwittingly carried the seeds of some foreign weed with them when they landed on these shores. As a result, many flowers of one type have withered. I wish to plant more.'

Cellineth lowers her voice. 'Breniriel does not quite believe my seeds will survive, but she has not stopped me. If you ask me, I'd say she hopes to be proven wrong.

'Ah, now I've said too much.' Cellineth winks, then returns her voice to normal. 'At any rate, I've already prepared a number of flower beds around Edhellond for you. Go forth!''Perhaps the next time you return, you shall see the fruit of your labours. And perhaps Breniriel will not be as dour!'The scout Dolvir kept a collection of Elf-relics from Edhellond safe during the war. Now that the war has passed, it is time to return them.Gilanor has asked you to deliver the Elf-relics to Lathlorn in Edhellond.

