'I wonder if you might do me the favour of speaking with Nosseth and Naremil in the Library of Saphadzîr. Ask them to show you anything that might be relevant about Rohan and its leaders. Do not tell them that it is I who asks. We do not need to start tongues wagging for no reason.''Ah! It appears you managed to find me some books! Thank you! I look forward to reading them as time allows.''Good day to you. You wish to learn about the geography and history of Rohan? We have few books that will tell you tales of those fields of green, as theirs is an oral history.

'Were you to find anything, it would be on the second floor, southern end of the building.''Greetings, ${CLASS}. You come seeking books on Rohan's lords and ladies? We have few, if any, I am afraid. What you find may be recorded in conversations about treaties and trade between our two countries.

