You should deliver them to him outside of Ost Amondal, in southern Belfalas.'Bah! Just as I expected! I knew it was just a matter of time.'

The stranger glares at you and then lets out a breath, deflating.

'My apologies, I am only about to lose my entire supply of goods to cursed adventurers like you who are sure to come wandering by now that the roads are open. Say, I don't suppose you are looking for some coin?

'These roads used to be known to only a few, and I have used them for years to transport my goods across Belfalas. I had been using the nearby ruins as a way point, where I would stash goods, but now that it's overrun by worms, I cannot get near enough to retrieve them. If you go fetch my crates for me, I will make it worth your time. Just... hurry up before anyone else comes along, will you?''Hurry, now hurry! Bring them to me! Ah, thank you. Thank you. What a burden this has become. I will sadly have to pass along the increased cost of supply to my buyers, alas.'Though Dol Amroth is no longer under siege, the wharf master has noticed odd happenings being reported on ships docked in the bay.Annúngil has asked you to inspect ropes and pins on the Rosigil.

The Rosigil is moored in the Dol Amroth bay.Examine the first pinExamine the second pinExamine the third pinExamine the fourth pinExamine the fifth pinExamine the sixth pinExamine the first rope bundleExamine the second rope bundleExamine the third rope bundleYou should let wharf master Annúngil know that you have examined many pins and piles of rope on the Rosigil.

The wharf master is on a dock in the Dol Amroth bay.Return to the wharf master'Ah, ${PLAYER}, was it? I am Annúngil, master of the wharf here in Dol Amroth. I heard you were instrumental in helping to break the siege on Dol Amroth. When word came of King Elessar's victory at Pelargir, the Corsairs here turned tail and sailed away fast as could be. We gave chase to some of them, of course, but mostly we were simply happy to see them go.

'However, in recent days, odd things have started failing on the ships that are docked here. Rigging pins slip their posts and tightly woven ropes snap like yarn. I have begun to suspect that we did not chase all of the enemy from our bay. I wonder if you might be able to assist. I need someone who can discreetly inspect pins and ropes on the ship moored here. Someone who will not let whoever is behind this know we're on to them. If you can, I would greatly appreciate the help.''You return! What did you find?'

You tell her about the smoothly filed pins and threadbare rope.

'I knew it! Someone is deliberately trying to sabotage our ships!'An investigation revealed that many of the post pins and bundles of rope on the Rosigil and docks were intentionally damaged. They must be replaced, for if left in their current state they could endanger the crew.Wharf master Annúngil has asked you to replace the damaged ropes and pins on the Rosigil. You should pick up the box of pins and bundles of new rope.

