'If you wish to replace the flowers, there is one type you may find near the piers here that has soft, pink petals. It was Lhinnedhel's favourite kind. Indeed, I believe it is a beautiful flower.''This means more to me than you will ever know -- and I am sure Lhinnedhel would have said the same, had he witnessed this.

'May kindness follow wherever you may go, traveller. And thank you.''Ah... I am sorry, I cannot help you. You ought to discuss the matter of the vase with Calendorion; it concerns him, after all.

'I last saw him at one of the piers, gazing out towards the bay.''Talk to Calendorion about replacing the flowers. He is at one of the piers, looking out towards the Bay of Belfalas.

'I apologize, I can say no more; his story is not mine to tell.''My apologies, I have no answer for you. Calendorion would have a better idea of which flowers to pick for the vase.

'You may find him at one of the piers in Edhellond, watching the bay.'An investigation revealed that someone has been sabotaging Dol Amroth's ships, and their identity must be uncovered!The wharf master has asked you to speak with Londring to see if anyone has come by to borrow tools or use the workbench.

