The wharf master is on the docks in Dol Amroth's bay.Return to Annúngil'Stripping those pins was not an easy task, and the file needed to grind down that metal isn't one that just anyone would have. You should go talk to Londring, the blacksmith. Ask him if anyone has come by recently, asking to borrow tools or to use a workbench. He's a king's man and I trust him, so you may as well.''Yes, I know who you're looking for. I did not catch his name, as his breath reeked so much of ale that I refused to entertain anything past refusing to lend or sell him a horse until he dried up. Cursed me out something fierce, he did.

'He stomped off towards Harper's Court, probably to find more ale.''Ah, yes. I know exactly of whom you speak. He came by here earlier, asking to use the workbench. He had a sack full of pins on which he wanted to grind the threads down. 

'We got into quite the heated argument when I tried to suggest he purchase nails instead of trying to make them from perfectly good screws. He spat at my feet and told me he was off to see someone about a horse and that after today he'd never have to look at my ugly face again. Very rude. Many think I'm quite fair, you know. Hmph.''Yârlag, eh? I do not know the name, but from what you said, it sounds like he was a Corsair who either stayed behind or was left behind when his crewmates fled.

'Glad am I that you put an end to his meddling, ${PLAYER}.'Traces of the Corsairs' occupation of Edhellond persist in the form of an invasive plant.Breniriel has asked you to pull any invasive weeds you find in Edhellond.Pull invasive weeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have pulled all the weeds you could find.

You should talk to Breniriel in Edhellond.Talk to Breniriel'Mae govannen. Have you seen these weeds around Edhellond?' Breniriel holds up a fistful of what appears to be a bristly plant. 'I have studied many native plants, and not once have I ever seen one similar to this. Neither animal nor pest will eat the weeds, and they steal the resources that our garden requires. Doubtless the seeds accompanied the Corsairs on their long voyage here.

'If Cellineth's new flowers are to thrive, then I must uproot every weed here.

'Will you help me?''Now Cellineth's flowers have a better chance at survival. That is more than enough for me.' 

Breniriel offers a faint smile. 

'Thank you.'Makham Mijann may not be fully abandoned.Halnith has sighted smoke rising from a lit camp-fire in Makham Mijann. You should investigate.

