Nendath stands to the south of Makham Mijann.Use the whistle to summon Kakhât to your sideReturn to Halnith at NendathUpon arriving at Nendath, Kakhât barked at you.

You should check on him.Use the whistle to summon Kakhât to your sideYou should tell Halnith what you found at Makham Mijann.

She stands guard at Nendath.Talk to Halnith'For the last few days, smoke has been rising from Makham Mijann, perhaps from a single camp-fire. I can't imagine anyone would be eager to hide out in an abandoned Corsair war-camp, unless they held some sort of ill intent.

'Obviously, I cannot leave my post, but I see that you're quite familiar with adventuring. Will you investigate in my stead?''Nothing you can do will hurt me, stranger. I'll be gone soon. Curse the warmongers that took me so far from home. May the seas take them all! May they --'

Whatever the Corsair intends to say next devolves into a series of dry, rattling coughs.

'Still listening to this dying man's last words? Then...' With a trembling hand, he reaches out to pet his war-hound. 'Take this whistle, and Kakhât will follow. He was never made for war. He doesn't deserve the same sad end that I do.

'Leave me, Kakhât. Go.'Kakhât sniffs your hand. Before the hound leaves his master's side, he looks to him -- for further commands, perhaps. But the Corsair utters no more words.Kakhât abruptly trots over to Halnith's side and lies down. Something tells you that even if you used the whistle to call him, he would simply refuse to listen.'Had I known what was happening at that camp-fire... but I did not, and he was beyond help. To die nameless and forsaken in an unfamiliar place... I only hope your actions gave him some semblance of peace.'

Halnith reaches down to gently pet the hound, who only responds with a tired thump of his tail.

'I daresay he's found his new home.' A smile breaks across Halnith's face. 'Guarding the beacon doesn't sound like such a lonely task anymore.'Much to the dismay of the people of Lancrath, a pack of wolves has made a den in the woodlands near Tarlang's Neck.Wolves can be found in Eryn Asgath near Tarlang's Neck in the Blackroot Vale.Defeat wolves in Eryn Asgath (0/12)Wolves can be found in Eryn Asgath near Tarlang's Neck in the Blackroot Vale.

You have discovered the den of the wolves that recently invaded the Blackroot Vale. You should defeat them and make safe the road through Tarlang's Neck.Defeat wolves in Eryn Asgath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of wolves at Eryn Asgath.CompletedTo the south-east of the Hill of Erech, you have discovered the wolf den of Eryn Asgath. Whether these wolves crept in from Lamedon or some hidden refuge in the hills, their presence in the vale has posed a continued threat to the hamlet of Lancrath and to all who would seek to travel the road through Tarlang's Neck.

You should defeat wolves in Eryn Asgath to aid the people of Lancrath and make safe the road through Tarlang's Neck.You have defeated a number of wolves at Eryn Asgath and made safe the road through Tarlang's Neck. Through your efforts, you have eased the fears of the good people of Lancrath and they will rest more soundly knowing that wolves do not stalk the vale so near to their homes in the night.Gerech the Addled wishes for you to find a cursed child that roams Langstrand.Gerech the Addled has asked you to help with a cursed child who seems to be a sign for imminent doom to Anfalas.

The cursed child can be found in the bluffs to the south-west.Find the cursed childThe Huntsman refuses to give up the cursed child. You should intimidate them and scare them away.Scare the huntsman awayThe Huntsman has been scared away. You should reason with the cursed child.Talk to EndelaEndela has revealed to you the terrible treatment she suffered. You should confront Gerech.

Gerech the Addled can be found in Barad Faen.Confront Gerech the AddledGerech forced your hand and has been defeated. You should tell Endela she is free.

Endela can be found in the bluffs to the south-west.Talk to Endela'You! You can help, yes you can!

'My search for this cursed child has ended! They are here to bring eternal ruin to Anfalas! The prosperity of the Langstrand is in your hands!

'Every single huntsman I have sent to end this imminent doom upon us has not returned, but I see you! You look very capable....'

You look at the stranger with elevated skepticism.

'Please, time is of the essence! The trail ends here, among the bluffs of Anfalas to the south-west!''Please don't hurt me!'

The woman recoils at your approach. But you raise your hands in surrender.

'A cursed child you say? I'm no child. But I have been running from hunters all my life.

'I was told the circumstances of my birth were extraordinary by Gerech. When my mother passed, he took me in, but I was treated poorly, and subjected to horrible experiments for his own esoteric pursuits of knowledge.

'Apparently my existence is akin to a curse upon Anfalas. When I grew older, I managed to escape and have been on the run since.

'I don't know whether I am cursed or not, but I'm done running. Would you help me gain my freedom?''You return to me empty handed. I placed all my faith in you to prevent the doom of Anfalas!'

You inform Gerech that the woman must go free.

'Never! You have no idea what you have done! You will be the doom of us all!''I cannot thank you enough for what you have done. This is the start of something new.

'I have not been able to live peacefully without a shadow looming over me for quite some time.

'I am in your debt, good stranger.'A carpenter in Melgobas is fretting over the fact that his friend hasn't arrived yet.Govach has asked you to find his friend Dardreg at the lumber camp north of Melgobas.Find Dardreg at the lumber campYou found Dardreg at the lumber camp in Anfalas.

You should talk to him.Talk to Dardreg'So many boats to fix and no wood to use... this isn't ideal. Where in the world is Dardreg?

'Ah -- you, traveller! Did you happen to travel here from the north -- past a lumber camp? My friend Dardreg told me he'd join me in Melgobas soon, but it's been days since I arrived. The Corsairs can't have raided the camp... right?

'Could you make sure he's all right? Surely the trees here can offer the same quality of wood that he seeks!''Govach sent you, didn't he? Hah! That man never stops worrying about me. I simply don't wish to leave empty-handed. The trees in Fleetmire have good wood, and there are folks in Melgobas who cannot travel as far as I can for such quality.

'Unfortunately, the Corsairs -- or rather, their actions -- have been a persistent thorn in my side. Thanks to their excessive woodcutting there, the bog-lurkers have become aggressive.

'I'm no fighter; I'd sooner find my death trying to wield my axe against anything that breathes, but you seem to be capable of defending yourself.'Anoch's sister has gone missing. The only clue you have is that she left for the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor, armed with her father's knife.The location Anoch described sounds like the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor, which lies west of Melgobas.

You should try and find Hedra there.Find Hedra near the wreck of the Kêl TezhorYou've found Hedra outside the wreck of the Kêl Tezhor.

You should talk to her.Talk to Hedra'Hedra told me she was going west, where there's a lot of Corsairs. The Corsairs already took Father... I don't want them to take her too!

'Please, please, can you find her? I want her to come home. I'm scared.'Startled, the girl whirls to face you, knife in hand. 'Who are you? What do you want?!'

As you explain, she lowers her knife.

'I should've known Anoch would tell someone eventually. The truth is, I... I wanted to avenge Father. Those Corsairs took him away and I couldn't even do anything about it. I thought, maybe if I muster up the courage to fight them off, they'd leave us alone forever. It sounds silly, doesn't it? Me, fighting all of those men...

'And I want to. I want to run in screaming and tear them apart. I'm so angry. But I'm also so scared. I've never hurt anyone. I don't want to hurt anyone. But they hurt Father. He must be dead by now.

'What am I supposed to do?'Luingil is concerned about the fauna that presents a natural obstacle along their journey to Iáphel.Luingil has asked you to clear the road north of Neekerbreekers and lynx.Defeat Neekerbreekers in Springer's Close (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat lynx in Loxhall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have cleared a path on the central road to Iáphel in Pinnath Gelin.

You should report your progress to Luingil in Echad Lendir.Talk to Luingil in Echad Lendir'We find ourselves at a crossroads, quite literally. My companions and I were on our way to Iáphel when one of our own expressed concern over their waggon. Naturally, we set up camp here so we could address their concerns before moving forward.

'Our scouts tell of a menace of local fauna that could present trouble for our party.

'You look as though you are handy with steel. Could you perhaps do us a courtesy and clear a path for us?''This should suffice. We are not so defenceless ourselves.

'But with the numbers along the road sufficiently reduced, we should manage on our own.

'Thank you, traveller, for your much needed assistance.'Gella has asked you to gather some white and purple flowers for a crown she is making.Gella asked you to gather lavender anemones near the pond and white anemones near the keep in Lond Cirion.Collect lavender anemones near the pond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect white anemones near the keep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Hello! I'm Gella! You look like someone who is good at helping. I am making a gift for my sister, Amardis, but I could use some help gathering the last of what I need for it.

'There are the prettiest lavender flowers around the pond just behind me... but mum is afraid I will fall in if I get too near! Oh, and the white ones near the keep up the road would be lovely too, they are her favourite!

'I'll be so grateful!''Hooray! These flowers are so pretty!'

You hand her the lavender and white flowers as her eyes light up with joy.

'Now I can finish my special crown, and I know Amardis will love it! Mum says she has been unwell and must rest. Mum fears her health does not improve, but with this crown, I am certain she'll be on her feet in no time!

'Thank you!'Arthiel said you might find Tirneldir near the fish traps to the south. Investigate to see if you can find out what happened to them.Arthiel has not seen Tirneldir for some time and told you he may be at his fish traps to the south of Lond Cirion.Search for Tirneldir at the fish traps outside the southern gateSearch for Tirneldir at the fish traps outside the southern gateThere was no sign of Tirneldir at the fish traps just outside of the southern gate in Lond Cirion, he may be at other traps nearby.Check the area for signs of TirneldirYou have found Tirneldir outside of the southern gate in Lond Cirion. You should speak with him as he appears injured and scared.Speak with TirneldirTirneldir has asked you to return to Lindil back near the northern gate in upper Lond Cirion.Return to Lindil'Thank ye kindly for allowing me a moment, friend.

'Aye, I had seen Tirneldir here but he left a bit back to check on his fish traps, and I've not seen him since.

'You can find his traps along the shore outside of the city gate to the south, near a scorched building.

'Luck be with ye in finding him, and I hope no shadows darken their tale.''Oh thank you, kind soul!

'Tirneldir has come back, and now he rests. Though wounded, the healers say he'll mend.

'Your kindness will not fade from our memories, be assured of that.''Please help! I beg of you!

'Corsairs are on my tail!'A body is found in the middle of the road through Barad Faen. Hadorion is investigating, and needs your help to catch the perpetrator.Hadorion has asked you to search the body and see if you can find what he could not.Search the corpseYou found traces of a green ichor on the victim's clothes. You should report to Hadorion.

Hadorion can be found in Barad Faen.Talk to HadorionHadorion has asked you to question the townsfolk of Barad Faen for more information on the mysterious ichor.Talk to the careful merchantThe concerned merchant has told you the substance is foreign. You should question more townsfolk to see if they have noticed anything suspicious come through.Talk to the anxious womanThe woman has told you of someone new to town that seems distressed. You should search for them.Talk to the distressed manThe man has told you that his waggon was hijacked before arriving in Barad Faen and abandoned along the western exit of Barad Faen.Search the abandoned waggonYou found a shard of glass stained with the foul smelling ichor. You should return to Hadorion.

Hadorion can be found in Barad Faen.Hadorion wishes to speak to you in private, follow him into his hearth.Follow Hadorion into the cabin'What happened here you ask? I'd like to know myself.

'Our men fallen in war, our shores given to the want of Corsairs, land, bridge, and dwelling ravaged by hatred and time. I'm used to all of that, but the sudden end of a man in the middle of the road so close to home, with no sight of Corsair, ship, or pillaging? A dark foreboding indeed... more so than what has wrought these lands for as long as I can remember.

'Perhaps you can find what I could not?''You found the victim's clothes stained in a green ichor? That seems to line up with what I found as well.

'It has a fell odour to it also. You should investigate amongst the townsfolk and see if anyone has seen this substance before.''A foul smelling green ichor? We have none of that here in Barad Faen.

'Most of our draughts are for mending and treating injuries. I cannot say such a substance comes from here.''Do I have anything suspicious to report? Why, of course!

'All manner of foul play is afoot! Corsairs are harrying the shores. Animals are pestering our foragers!

'Well, there is one person I do not recognize here, and they seem very anxious.

'I couldn't tell you where to find them, but if they look out of place and disturbed, chances are you have found your quarry.''What is it?!'

The man is startled by your presence.

'I've done nothing wrong! I was just passing through!

'On my way to Lond Cirion, I was. My waggon was hijacked just up the road before arriving here.

'A foul smelling substance? Of course! The person who hijacked my waggon reeked of it.

'I ended up here a day later to find my waggon abandoned on the town's western exit. Surely you will find more of that wretched substance.''Hmmm. This shard of glass is intriguing.

'It is... familiar to me, or rather, I've heard of this before.''There is more to discuss.'Hadorion has happened upon more information during his investigation.Hadorion wants you to check on a new camp that has been erected to the north.Investigate the camp-siteYou found a strange note with barely visible markings. Bring it back to Hadorion.

Hadorion can be found in his cabin in Barad Faen.'Some new information has shed some light on these new happenings. I shall try to glean more information from the sash you brought back.

'Recently, while out hunting, the folk have noticed a camp in the hills to the north. It has always been empty according to their reports, but there is evidence of recent use.

'As with all cases, this cannot be mere coincidence. It suggests that whoever we are dealing with will not be here for long.''What's written on this note is barely readable, but this last line here is of concern: "It is time." It seems we are out of time. Whatever they were planning to do, they plan to do soon.

'I think I may have everything I need to solve this case.'Hadorion has completed his investigation and needs your help to solve the case.Hadorion wants your help preventing the culprit from making an escape by sea.Solve the case of the Vile TrailHadorion wants to speak to you about further options pursuing Khâshap.

