Hadorion can be found in his home in Barad Faen.'This ichor... it is grotesque and foul in smell. A certain result of fell experiments. I've only heard rumours of such a thing... ghastly abominations roaming the halls of Carn Dûm.

'Of course, I have no experience with this, but my friend was so curious about the depths of that place he decided to venture there. Torvendor was his name.

'I can only assume that whatever lay waiting in those halls has now found its way here to us. I have a new lead.

'One of the townsfolk spotted a suspicious figure running off towards the western road at night. See if you can pick up their trail and follow it to whatever ends.

'I'll be here.''This sash, it is unlike the ilk of Corsair we see that typically trouble these shores.

'Fortunately, it gives us our next clue.'Defeat many beasts in Outer Gondor.Defeat many beasts in Outer Gondor.Defeat many beasts in Outer GondorDefeat many beasts in Outer Gondor.Defeat many beasts in Outer Gondor.Defeat many beasts in Outer GondorKing Elessar has offered the help of his companions in the defence of Anfalas, and that includes any assistance you can provide to Lady Marra's scouts.Lady Marra's scouts can be found outside Lond Cirion to the north, east, and south.Talk to Borion north of Lond CirionTalk to Galleth on the beach south of Lond CirionTalk to Gilvenel on the hill east of Lond CirionNow that you have aided the scouts, you should return to Lond Cirion.Return to Lond Cirion to report of your successesCaebar is in the central yard of Lond Cirion. He seems worried about something.Talk to Caebar in the central yard of Lond Cirion'Lady Marra's scouts patrol the lands hereabout in search of Corsair raiding parties, and I have offered to them the assistance of my travelling companions, many of whom are deadly with weapons of every sort. I count you in this number, ${PLAYER}, and would greatly appreciate your aiding the scouts as they seek such foes as trouble Anfalas.

'The scouts have gone in three directions: to the north, the east, and to the south.''Lady Marra's scouts patrol the lands hereabout in search of Corsair raiding parties, and I have offered to them the assistance of my travelling companions, many of whom are deadly with weapons of every sort. I count you in this number, ${PLAYER}, and would greatly appreciate your aiding the scouts as they seek such foes as trouble Anfalas.

'The scouts have gone in three directions: to the north, east, and south.''You are here to help oppose the enemies of Anfalas? I am pleased to hear it, for I surprised a number of Corsairs creeping about those rocks, and I believe they will soon return!''Corsairs sometimes try to approach Lond Cirion from this beach, so we must remain always vigilant.''Corsair scouts have been spotted inland, and we must always remain on our guard.''Oh, I am glad you have returned, ${PLAYER}. King Elessar asked for me to attend to some business about an hour from now, and I am consumed with worry about what it might be. I am trying not to be nervous, but it is... well, it is difficult.'King Elessar has called upon Caebar to provide a service for Lond Cirion, and the scribe is worried about it.Caebar is in the central yard of Lond Cirion, where he has confided in you that he is worried about the service King Elessar has asked him to provide.Talk to Caebar in the central yard of Lond Cirion and accompany him to the KingLady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond CirionKing Elessar is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of Lond CirionLady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion'Will you accompany me, my friend? The King did not prohibit it, so far as I know, and I cannot imagine he would not allow you to be present at... whatever this duty turns out to be!

'I would just feel better if you were there, ${PLAYER}. Tell me you will come with me.''Thank you, my friend! I will not forget this!

'Let us meet with King Elessar at the appointed hour, and until that time comes I will try not to worry overmuch.''I am sorry, but it was very hard to hear these things. My husband was a man of great bravery and courage, and a generous heart, but to think of him writing these things, alone, without first taking my advice...

'I will shed no more tears. I wish this letter had not been read here today.'

Marra falls silent, her face a mask.Marra stares forward and says nothing.'I have to ask you something, Marra, and I do not wish to give you offence or cause you any further upset... but I feel that I must ask it.'

Elessar fixes his gaze upon the Lady of Anfalas. When next he speaks, his voice is gentle, but his eyes are stern.

'Why did you break the seal upon your husband's last wishes, Marra? The parchment was not found only today, as you suggested. The paper was in your possession ever since Golasgil departed, and you knew its contents before now.''Why did you break the seal upon your husband's last wishes, Marra?''I am grateful for your discretion earlier, my King, for Coruchon would seek any advantage he could from this, and Golasgil would never forgive me should a widow's weakness endanger Orgolas's claim!

'But I broke the seal and read my husband's last wishes out of fear that he would do as he has indeed done: granted to his son and mine that cursed ship, Wave-hunter! How often did he speak of his intention for Orgolas to follow in his own steps, and become a great mariner like his father? Too often, and every time it cut me deeply! The Wave-hunter was harboured upstream in Pinnath Gelin during the war, to protect it from the Corsairs, and I have refused to summon it back here to keep Orgolas as far from its threatening decks as I can!

'When I saw such a bequest had been made, I did not know what to do. But I cannot disobey the command of the King of Gondor. Hindering Golasgil's wishes was bad enough, but I fear for my son's safety! He is so young, my King. You must understand.'Lady Marra has entreated the King to forbid her son from leaving Lond Cirion.Queen Arwen has something she wishes to say to Lady Marra.Talk to Queen Arwen in the main hall of Lond CirionLady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond CirionDaeram is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.Talk to Daeram outside the keep of Lond CirionOrgolas is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.Talk to Orgolas outside the keep of Lond Cirion'I gave you my thanks for not speaking what you suspected in front of Coruchon, King Elessar, but you will have my thanks a hundredfold if you do this now: I entreat you to forbid Orgolas from leaving Lond Cirion, no matter what his father has gifted to him. Already it is nearly impossible to keep him from sneaking beyond the walls, but perhaps a command from the King of Gondor would stay his steps?''I gave you my thanks for not speaking what you suspected in front of Coruchon, King Elessar, but you will have my thanks a hundredfold if you do this now: I entreat you to forbid Orgolas from leaving Lond Cirion, no matter what his father has gifted to him. Already it is nearly impossible to keep him from sneaking beyond the walls, but perhaps a command from the King of Gondor would stay his steps?''I understand this request you have of my husband, Marra, but I fear you may do more harm with the asking of this boon than you will prevent. Your son will not be kept from leaving your home if that is the purpose of his heart. Though the command be in the King's voice, Orgolas will know who wrote the words, and that knowledge can only breed resentment.

'You say Golasgil was a fine mariner, and I do not doubt he was! But what I have learned of your husband from my own is that he cared deeply for the people of Anfalas, and did not sail from them, or from you, without great need. Perhaps if Orgolas understood the cares and concerns of the folk he will rule when he comes of age, he will make the same choice, and the Wave-hunter will remain at its dock.

'This, then, is my suggestion: let your son come with our travelling party as we journey to Pinnath Gelin. It is my belief that Orgolas will see this land with new eyes, and he will grow into the responsibility he must one day have.''This is my suggestion: let your son come with our travelling party as we journey to Pinnath Gelin. It is my belief that Orgolas will see this land with new eyes, and he will grow into the responsibility he must one day have.''I do not know.'

Marra looks from the Queen to the King, and back again.

'What if this journey gives life to embers that might otherwise have been cooled? I do not see how such an adventure could prevent that which I fear for my son.

'But if you permit Daeram to also join your travelling party, that he may attend my son and keep him safe, I suppose I cannot refuse.''If you permit Daeram to also join your travelling party, that he may attend my son and keep him safe, I suppose I cannot refuse.''I am surprised to learn that Lady Marra has agreed to allow Orgolas to depart with the King and Queen, but Pinnath Gelin is not far from here. I will do what I can to keep the boy safe among the green hills. Perhaps he will be less likely to slip my watch if he feels that he is on an adventure, and need not go in search of another one himself!''I am surprised to learn that Lady Marra has agreed to allow Orgolas to depart with the King and Queen, but Pinnath Gelin is not far from here. I will do what I can to keep the boy safe among the green hills. Perhaps he will be less likely to slip my watch if he feels that he is on an adventure, and need not go in search of another one himself!''Is it true? I am to depart with the King's party for Pinnath Gelin? That is wonderful news! That is where the Wave-hunter is currently docked, ${PLAYER}! Are we going to see the ship that my father left to me?'The time has come for you to rejoin King Elessar on the road to Anfalas.You planned to rejoin King Elessar south of the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor, on the road into Anfalas.Travel south of the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor, and rejoin Elessar on the road to AnfalasKing Elessar is on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor.Talk to King Elessar on the road to Anfalas, in King's GondorTalk to Queen Arwen on the road to Anfalas, in King's GondorThe town of Melgobas is to the west along the coast in Anfalas.Travel to the town of Melgobas, in AnfalasAnoradan is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas, in Anfalas.Talk to Anoradan in Melgobas'I bid you farewell, then, and I will try to master my grief and that of my people. But King Elessar would do well to remember that not all the folk of Gondor are as stern or as cold as the Elves he loves, and if he does not take care his kingdom may slip away. And when it does, if it does, it may not be to the fires of the Corsairs but to the fury of his own people. You tell him that, ${PLAYER}. He has my loyalty, for I am sworn to Gondor, but these are true words I speak, and he would do well to heed them.''King Elessar would do well to remember that not all the folk of Gondor are as stern or as cold as the Elves he loves, and if he does not take care his kingdom may slip away. And when it does, if it does, it may not be to the fires of the Corsairs but to the fury of his own people. You tell him that, ${PLAYER}. He has my loyalty, for I am sworn to Gondor, but these are true words I speak, and he would do well to heed them.''Thank you for going on my behalf to Morlad, ${PLAYER}! How fares the Lord of the Blackroot Vale and his wife and people?'

You give your account of the grim sentiment that pervades the Vale, and the words of its ruler. Elessar nods.

'Duinhir and Rosfin suffered much during the war, and the wound that is the loss of their sons can never truly be mended. I knew it was so, but I let my other concerns guide me and erred by sending you there. I should have gone as well, ${PLAYER}. On my return journey, after we see Anfalas, I will go to the Vale and speak with them personally.''This is the road to Anfalas, ${PLAYER}, westernmost fief of my husband's kingdom. He has spoken to me of its ruler Golasgil, who marched to the defence of Minas Tirith with a number of soldiers and his household guard. He perished at the Battle of the Morannon, moments before the defeat of Sauron, and Elessar grieves that he sacrificed so much and never saw the victory for which he died.

'I understand he asked you to bring to his people word of his bravery in the face of death?''I will go to the Blackroot Vale and hear Duinhir's concerns myself after we have returned from Anfalas.''Golasgil asked you to bring word of his death to his people? If it will bring comfort to them, I encourage you to do this.''Who are these fine folk?''Who are these fine folk?'The people of Melgobas are endangered by more than just the Corsairs that drew the King to Anfalas.Corsairs and lynx threaten the folk of Anfalas in the vicinity of Melgobas.Defeat lynx near Melgobas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Corsairs near Melgobas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Anoradan is in the town of Melgobas.Talk to Anoradan in MelgobasDaeram is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas.Talk to Daeram in Melgobas'The King and Queen have come to Anfalas? I never thought I would see such a day as this, for the Langstrand is so far from the White City and it seemed we were just as distant from their minds, if not further! It must be they were impressed by the swords and spears that Lord Golasgil brought to bear during the war. He is greatly missed.'

You tell the man that Golasgil fought bravely on behalf of the King, and brought honour to Anfalas. He smiles and holds up a hand.

'I rejoice to hear you say so, stranger, but it is unnecessary. His quality was well-known to his people, and though his son Orgolas is still young, there are none who doubt he will grow to be his father's equal. But do you bring pleasing words alone, or are you here to help us? We could use assistance thinning the lynx hereabouts, and the Corsairs have been even more of a problem of late.''Are you here to help us? We could use assistance thinning the lynx and dealing with the Corsairs hereabouts, you know.''You took care of the beasts that threaten Melgobas, lynx and Corsairs both? Perhaps the King and Queen knew what they were doing when they brought you with them to visit the Langstrand!

'But there may be something more serious afoot than even those foes. A guard has come to Melgobas from Lond Cirion, and he looks worried. Perhaps he will share with a member of the King's travelling party what has brought him here?''There may be something more serious afoot than even such foes. A guard has come to Melgobas from Lond Cirion, and he looks worried. Perhaps he will share with a member of the King's travelling party what has brought him here?''You have come with the King's travelling party? If you have the trust of King Elessar, I suppose you have more than earned my own. I hope I do not step wrong by telling you this, or the Lady Marra will have my head.

'I am seeking Orgolas, the young heir of Lord Golasgil. He has gone missing.'Daeram was sent from Lond Cirion to search for the missing heir of Anfalas.Daeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south, down below the fishing village of Melgobas.Search along the beach at the bottom of the steps in MelgobasDaeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south of Melgobas.Search for Orgolas along the beach to the eastDaeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south.Search for Orgolas further east along the beachDaeram is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas.Talk to Daeram in MelgobasKing Elessar stands in Melgobas, considering Orgolas's disappearance.Talk to King Elessar in MelgobasBarad Faen is west of Melgobas, in Anfalas.Meet up with King Elessar outside Barad Faen, in AnfalasKing Elessar kneels outside Barad Faen, studying the ground. It seems the life of a Ranger can be hard to escape!Talk to King Elessar outside Barad FaenKing Elessar has found tracks of some sort outside Barad Faen.Examine the tracks outside Barad FaenTracks indicate Orgolas might have climbed Barad Faen.Search for Orgolas atop Barad Faen'This is not the first time Orgolas has slipped his keepers' watch and escaped to tour the countryside, but with the Corsairs still harrying the coast... I need not tell you that once harmless excursions have become more dangerous than before.

'Will you help me look for him? Search along the beach to the south and I will ask around the fishing village to learn if anyone has seen him of late.''Will you help me look for Orgolas, Golasgil's young heir? Search along the beach to the south and I will ask around the fishing village to learn if anyone has seen him of late.''Will you help me look for Orgolas, Golasgil's young heir? Search along the beach to the south of Melgobas and I will ask around the fishing village to learn if anyone has seen him of late.''Will you help me look for Orgolas, Golasgil's young heir? Search along the beach to the south of Melgobas and I will ask around the fishing village to learn if anyone has seen him of late.''You found no sign of the boy? No one around the village has seen him of late. I cannot return to Lond Cirion without him!''I cannot return to Lond Cirion without him! Where can he have gone?''Do not despair before there is need, my friend. We have seen no sign of Orgolas, but neither is there evidence that he ran afoul of danger.'

Elessar strokes his chin and gazes out over the waves.

'Is there a tall watch-tower of some sort along the coast? Golasgil's heir might have climbed such a tower in order to get a better view of the Corsair ships out in the bay. Such a sight might be difficult for a young boy to refuse, if my own childhood is to be any indication!''Is there a tall watch-tower of some sort along the coast? Golasgil's heir might have climbed such a tower in order to get a better view of the Corsair ships out in the bay. Such a sight might be difficult for a young boy to refuse, if my own childhood is to be any indication!''Aye, this is just the sort of place I expected.''Aye, this is just the sort of place I expected. What do you make of these tracks, ${PLAYER}?''What do you make of these tracks?''I believe we will find our quarry atop Barad Faen, ${PLAYER}.''What do you want? I am not ready to return to Lond Cirion, and you cannot make me! I have not yet even seen any of the Corsair ships up close!'You have found Orgolas, the son of Golasgil and heir to Anfalas. The question now is what should be done with him?King Elessar stands by Orgolas, at Barad Faen.Talk to King Elessar at Barad FaenLond Cirion is to the west of Barad Faen.Travel to the entrance of Lond CirionOrgolas is at the entrance of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.Talk to Orgolas at the entrance to Lond CirionDaeram is at the entrance to Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.Talk to Daeram at the entrance to Lond CirionThe main hall of Lond Cirion is located just inside the entrance to the keep.Find the main hall of Lond CirionLady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.Talk to Marra in the main hall of Lond CirionMarra suggested you become familiar with the layout of Lond Cirion and those who reside there.Find the Lond Cirion library inside the keepFind a guardsman on the bridge north-west of Lond CirionFind Orgolas by the docks of Lond CirionTalk to Coruchon in the library of Lond CirionTalk to Aerhant on the bridge to the north-west of Lond CirionTalk to Orgolas by the docksKing Elessar is in the main hall of Lond Cirion, speaking with Lady Marra.Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of Lond Cirion'Wait... who is that man? Is he... King Elessar? My mother brought me to the King's wedding this summer, but I only saw him from afar, and we did not stay long. Can he really have come to Anfalas?'

You tell Orgolas that Elessar joined the search to find him, and the boy's eyes widen in amazement.

'Truthfully? He came here to seek me? I cannot believe it! I simply must show him to my home! Yes, I will return to Lond Cirion, and at once! King Elessar! Mother will be so surprised!''I simply must show King Elessar to my home! Yes, I will return to Lond Cirion, and at once! The King of Gondor! Mother will be so surprised!''Lead on, young master Orgolas. ${PLAYER} and I will follow you to Lond Cirion.

'It is located to the west, ${PLAYER}, and was named Ciryalondë by the Men of Númenor who settled there during the Second Age. It is the oldest Númenórean settlement in Gondor, but its original name fell out of use and now it is Lond Cirion. It was Golasgil's ruling seat, and now his widow Marra holds it until their son comes of age.''Lond Cirion is located to the west, ${PLAYER}, and was named Ciryalondë by the Men of Númenor who settled there during the Second Age. It is the oldest Númenórean settlement in Gondor, but its original name fell out of use and now it is Lond Cirion. It was Golasgil's ruling seat, and now his widow Marra holds it until their son comes of age.''This way, my King! My home is to the west!''Here we are! Now, you've probably seen impressive places on your journey across Gondor, and Minas Tirith is of course very large... but my teachers say that Lond Cirion is older than all of them! Let me show you around, King Elessar!''Daeram always spoils my fun. That is the duty with which my mother always charges him, anyway!''Master Orgolas is very excited, but you and the King should make yourselves known first to the Lady Marra. It would be proper.

'She will be inside the hall.''Master Orgolas is very excited, but you and the King should make yourselves known first to the Lady Marra. It would be proper.

'She will be inside the hall.''You and your travelling party are welcome to Lond Cirion, King Elessar, and all of you will enjoy the hospitality of my house. Please feel free to explore the Anfalas as you wish, but know that the Corsairs of Umbar trouble the long shore, even despite the war's ending; my guards cannot ensure your safety if you stray near the coast.

'But I understand this ${RACE} was present when my husband fell? Would you... would you speak to me of what befell my dear Golasgil in the King's service?'

You speak of Golasgil's bravery before the Black Gate of Mordor, and that you repaid with death the great Olog that gave him his mortal wound, moments before the defeat of the Dark Lord Sauron. Marra's eyes brim with tears, but she wipes them away with her sleeve and her expression hardens.

'So near to the end, then? I worried it might have been so. What need was there for my husband to die, if the Men of the West were so near to their victory? My Golasgil had not the attention of Sauron; he was but one man among hundreds. Whose sword-arm failed to slay the Olog that killed my husband before it could reach him, ${PLAYER}? Was it yours? Was it the King's?

'You may leave me, ${PLAYER}. I have words to speak to Elessar, but they are not for your hearing. See the comforts of Lond Cirion, and know that Golasgil will not enjoy them again.''You may see the rooms of Lond Cirion and meet its people while I speak with the King. I have much to say to him.''The King has come here to resolve the line of succession, hasn't he? Golasgil's heir is too young to rule, and has ceded some of his authority to his mother Marra, but there are some in Lond Cirion and elsewhere who believe she is not fit to govern in these trying times, and she still in mourning.

'There is another matter of some curiosity, stranger. It is known that before he departed for the war, Golasgil prepared a parchment containing his last wishes... but it cannot be found. I have spoken with Marra about this, and she brushes away my questioning. There is something untoward going on. You should tell the King, for the safety of Anfalas is affected, and that imperils the kingdom.''I saw you and King Elessar when you arrived at Lond Cirion in the company of young master Orgolas. He is a frequent visitor to this bridge, and often wants news from me concerning distant lands.

'The news is poor, of late. Corsair ships are often seen along the coast, and they endanger the fisherfolk and peasantry of Anfalas. Do they not know the war is over?''Ho there, ${PLAYER}! I come here often to watch the soldiers training! One day I hope to have as much martial prowess as they do! I will be as good a fighter as my father was. Nay, I shall be even better!

'Mother says the war is over, but Aerhant showed me a ship far off in the bay that must have been full of Corsairs sailing from Umbar. I hope they are not all dealt with before I have finished my sword-training!''The Lady Marra and I have come to an understanding, ${PLAYER}, and she knows we did as much for her husband as we could, and mourn with her that it was not enough. She has my promise that we will work to defend her people, as Golasgil desired.'Defeat many Corsairs in Outer Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in Outer Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in Outer GondorDefeat many Corsairs in Outer Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in Outer Gondor.Defeat many Corsairs in Outer GondorWith her hands full tending to her mother's injuries, Avri finds herself unable to check on her crab traps.Avri has asked you to check the crab traps she placed at Lithengris.

Lithengris is located south-east of Sadrech's Camp.Check crab traps at Lithengris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})None of the crab traps held any crabs.

You should check the last crab trap at Lithengris.Check the last crab trapYou have recovered a bucket full of crabs from the Corsair.

