Marra can be found in Lond Cirion.Talk to Marra in Lond Cirion'Ever since the war, the lands have been emptied of our most seasoned and hearty folk.

'Guard duties have been delegated to garrisons mostly made up of new recruits with barely any field experience.

'Lond Cirion to the west of here remains harried by straggler Corsairs in Khatsûr.

'They grow bold and encroach further towards Lagorduin. Would you help them by repelling the Corsairs?''Ah, ${PLAYER}, I am glad to see you well.

'Lond Cirion is grateful for your aid in driving back the Corsairs of Umbar for they have long troubled our shores.

'With the war ended, and many lost, we can only depend on those left behind to be up to the task. I too am personally grateful that you were able to help our new recruits. Your wisdom and martial discipline is appreciated.

'Now, if there is nothing else?'Lornion needs your help making the stew for the day's meal.Lornion has asked you to gather meat from dun oxen to the east as well as vegetables and spices from crates at the top of the northern lift.Collect meat from dun oxen east of Lond Cirion (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather vegetables and spices near the docks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Lornion at The Brew and Bounty Tavern in Lond Cirion with the stew ingredients.Lornion has asked that you ask Hithudor for some bowls near the training grounds behind the tavern, at the docks.Get bowls from the training grounds cookObtain a crate of bowls behind Hithudor near the training grounds at the docks.Pick up the crate of bowlsReturn to Lornion in The Brew and Bounty in Lond Cirion.'Greetings, friend. I'm in a right mess, ya see. The ol' Brew and Bounty is in a pickle, and not the tasty kind! We are missing the supplies I need for today's grub. I was planning a stew, but we are all out of the meat and veggies.

'Ye look like you have some know-how in adventurin'. Would you be able to lend a hand and gather what I need? It would sure mean a lot to the workers down here on the docks.

'Out the eastern gate of Lond Cirion, ye can find some dun oxen who will provide plenty of meat and ye can find some veggies and spices in the supplies at the top of the northern lift nearby. Gatherin' up those would make for a fine stew.''Bless ye for bringin' back the stew ingredients. You've proven yourself a most solid individual, you have! But, lo and behold, we're still in a bit of trouble. We're lackin' bowls, can ye believe it? Bowls we need to serve the meal, no less!

'If ye could do me one more favour adventurer and run off to the training grounds outside near the water. Ask the cook there, Hithudor, if they have any layin' about that they can spare. I'd be in yer debt, friend.''Well met, adventurer. What can I help you with?'

You tell the cook of the situation at The Brew and Bounty and their need for bowls.

'Bowls, ye say? Not a worry at all. We got more bowls than we know what do with. You can find a whole crate of 'em near the wall back here. If ye need more, just holler. Always happy to help the other folk here and Lornion is good folk.''Well yer a sight for sore eyes. Back with a whole crate of bowls!

'Done our humble tavern a mighty favour ye have. The stew will be flowing and they'll be singing yer praises for this!'The Corsairs have left behind some perfectly fine logs, and Dardreg refuses to see them go to waste.Dardreg has asked you to collect freshly-cut logs left behind by Corsairs.

These logs can be found scattered around Fleetmire, south-west of the lumber camp.Collect freshly-cut logs at Fleetmire (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have gathered a good amount of logs.

You should bring them back to Dardreg, who waits for you at the lumber camp.'If you'd like to make some coin, why not help me? A group of Corsairs passed through Fleetmire recently, south-west of here. They procured more wood than they could carry, so they simply left the logs behind to rot.

'Bring those logs back to me, and I'll consider the job done!''The bog-lurkers were no match for you, eh? I suppose I ought to start learning a thing or two about dealing with them... or those Corsairs! Ah, but first... Govach must be worried sick, waiting for me.

'I'll be on my way, then. Thanks, ${CLASS}!'Siliveth would like you to check on her friends who are sequestered in Echad Lendir.

