'Could you find Luingil in Echad Lendir and lend your aid to our travels?''Ah, so Siliveth sends you to check on us?

'So she does care after all.

'We are doing quite well actually. We've set up camp and are currently waiting for our companion to fix their waggon before progressing on our journey to Iaphel.

'Actually, there is something with which we could use assistance, if you are able?'One of Iáphel's coopers awaits a delivery of recovered flotsam.Miruhir has asked you to move recovered flotsam from where it is stacked by the fence to Tregeth, who waits in town.

Collect recovered flotsam.Pick up the stack of planks in IáphelTalk to Tregeth'Most of the wood being produced in Gondor is reserved for the rebuilding of homes and the construction of a new fleet of ships, or so I hear. This makes it hard to source wood for the barrels we need to store and age the wine. My clever cooper, Tregeth, has found a creative solution — reusing flotsam that has washed ashore. Some labourers from Lond Cirion brought some to the vineyard yesterday morning and left it by the entrance to town. Could I ask you to bring it the rest of the way to her? Set it down right beside her, in front of the fence post that runs beside her home.''Ah, there's my delivery! It has been difficult to source quality wood as of late, so using recovered flotsam will help me keep up with production. Perhaps the wine aged in the barrels I'll make will be briny and taste of the sea, because that is what everyone wants -- salty wine.'Across the green hills of Pinnath Gelin, scouts work alongside, and many times ahead of, the local knights. Theirs is a small, but tightly organized group. Thus, when one of their number misses an appointed time to report in, tensions rise.Lúmar is concerned that his fellow scout hasn't reported back after making a trip north of Iáphel. Igerna was last seen heading to Elbery Farm in Pinnath Gelin, to speak with Húrwen.

You should speak with Húrwen.Talk to HúrwenHúrwen spoke with Igerna, who continued on towards the mountains in search of more goblins.

You should look for signs of Igerna in northern Pinnath Gelin.Search for IgernaWhile searching for Igerna, you discovered that goblins have made a camp at the foot of the mountains.

You should continue looking for Igerna in the goblin camp in north-western Pinnath Gelin.Search the camp for IgernaA freshly made cave has been blasted into the mountainside by goblins. You should search the cave.

The cave is in north-western Pinnath Gelin.Search the cave for IgernaIn a newly dug cave north of Iáphel, you found a shredded pack. Does it belong to Igerna?

You should bring it to Lúmar in Ost Arndir to find out.'Well met. I am Lúmar, scout commander for the Knights of the Green Hills. And you - well, your reputation precedes you. The knights have spoken your name with cheer around many a fire. I pray I can charge you with a small task. My fellow scout, Igerna, went north to look into troubling reports of goblin activity. Alas, she missed her deadline for reporting back, and I can wait no longer before pressing on to Ost Arndír.

'Will you follow in her footsteps and see if she requires aid? She's one of the most capable scouts we have, and it's unlike her to be tardy. Head to Elbery Farm and speak with Húrwen. Igerna planned to checked on her.''${PLAYER}! You return without Igerna, I see.'

You hand him the pack, and a worried recognition passes across his face.

'This is a troublesome outcome indeed. Why would Igerna leave her pack behind? The leather is shredded, but thankfully there is no blood to be found. Perhaps she made an escape!''Igerna? Aye, she came through here, but she's gone on up north. She said she heard that goblins have been spotted blasting up the side of the mountain!'With its defender lost at war, Munadhor Farm in Pinnath Gelin has been overrun by beasts and brigands.Megorneth has asked you to drive away thieves who have come to plunder her farm.

Corsairs can be found at Munadhor Farm.Defeat Corsair raiders at Munadhor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Corsair sneaks at Munadhor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Megorneth know that you have defeated many Corsairs at Munadhor Farm.

Megorneth is at Munadhor Farm in Pinnath Gelin.Return to Megorneth'Who are you?! Here to plunder our farm too, are you?'

The younger woman places a gentle hand on the elder's arm and tries to sooth her. Cúronel says, 'I do not think they're one of the thieves, mother. I think they may be here to help.'

The elder woman glares up at you, saying, 'If that's the case, go kill as many of the thieves as you can! We may not be able to live here anymore, but I won't see our farm plundered!''I am sorry about my mother - well, she was my husband's mother. He was a knight but... he did not return from the war.

'Megorneth has been full of rage since, and having our farm overrun by all sorts of beasts and brigands has done nothing to alleviate her pain. I thank you for your help.''Are they gone? Have you done it?'

When you tell her of your deeds, Megorneth slumps with relief, but her eyes lose none of their venom.

'They had it coming! I hope you were thorough!''I am sorry about my mother - well, she was my husband's mother. He was a knight but... he did not return from the war.

'Megorneth has been full of rage since, and having our farm overrun by all sorts of beasts and brigands has done nothing to alleviate her pain. I thank you for your help.'The vineyards of Pinnath Gelin are renowned for producing the finest wines and spirits. One of this year's delicate crops is playing host to a most unwelcome guest.Lúmar has asked you to search for signs of Igerna and speak to Nordach at Winbury.

Winbury is in northern Pinnath Gelin.Talk to NordachNordach seems to know where Igerna is, but won't share the information until you have helped clear his vineyards of an infestation of beetles.

You should defeat beetles at Winbury, in northern Pinnath Gelin.Defeat beetles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Nordach know that you have helped to clear the Winbury vineyards of beetles.

Nordach is at Winbury.Return to Nordach'I must stay here to receive reports from the rest of my scouts. We are working hard alongside the Knights to ensure that the king's visit is untroubled. Will you go east to Winbury and speak with Nordach? He may have seen or spoken with Igerna!''Stay where you are! We don't need any more trouble here!'

You assure Nordach that you're here to help and tell him that Lúmar sent you.

'He must be looking for Igerna, eh? She's not here, and I wish she was. My fields have been infiltrated by enormous beetles! They are eating up my precious grapes. You get rid of them for me, and I'll tell you what I know about Igerna.''Thank goodness you came when you did! My harvest would have been devastated for the entire year, otherwise!

'Right, I can breathe now and give you the answer you're looking for.'A family of farmers has been dealing with boars encroaching on their land.You have been tasked to hunt boars for food.

The boars in question may be found at the Farrowfold, south-west of Cornworth.Hunt perturbed wild boars in the Farrowfold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have done as Branach asked. Return to him.

Branach can be found at his farm, Cornworth, north-east of Farrowfold.'Sausages, roasts, grilled chops, braises, butter-basted herbed tenderloin, these are the things I would be eating right now if someone were to harvest some boars from where they've made their dens to the south-west. Watch out for the aggressive ones, however! They are usually covered in flies, and not fit to eat. Their perturbed cousins should be perfect for this, and plenty edible.'

He smiles at you and gestures his head in the direction he just indicated.

'I would pay such an adventurous person with coin.'

He winks.

Perhaps you should go hunt some boars.'This will keep us fed through the harvest. Thank you.'Boar belly is a fatty cut of meat which, when cured with spices and herbs, is added to many popular dishes in Pinnath Gelin.Cúronel has asked you to bring her boar belly meat from healthy boars and to put down diseased boars at her farm, Munadhor Farm in Pinnath Gelin.Collect boar belly (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Put down diseased boars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should return to Cúronel with the boar belly pieces that you gathered.

Cúronel is at Munadhor Farm, in central Pinnath Gelin.'Greetings, traveller. I am Cúronel, and I am sorry I can not welcome you fully to our farm. It has sadly been overrun by boars and brigands, and without my husband about to help drive them off, we have had to abandon our home. I have come here with my husband's mother to see if they've moved on, but no, they've made themselves quite at home... at our home.

'If you are going on ahead, will you bring me back cuts of boar meat? The fatty belly meat, in particular. I can prepare it so that it will last a good long time, and help see us through this. But take care, some of the boars seem to be ailing and their meat would be foetid. Just put those ones down, but bring boar belly from the others.''You come bearing boar belly? Ah, how wonderful. I would not have been able to gather so much on my own. I will make mother's favourite dish tonight with some of this, and prepare the rest for curing.

'You have my thanks!''I like braised boar belly, but mother likes when I prepare it with herbs and wine, and roll it with twine and then bake it until crispy. I admit, I do also enjoy it prepared as such. At least these boars will be useful, especially if we can drive them out before they do too much damage.'Left unchecked, the Ronkrúm goblin horde will continue to crawl out from the depths of the mountain, onto the rolling green hills of Pinnath Gelin.Igerna has asked you to gather barrels of the goblins' black powder.

Barrels can be found in the camp outside, as well as inside, the cave at Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin.Collect barrels of black powder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})With a hefty supply of dangerously explosive barrels of black powder, you are ready to seal off some of the goblins' tunnels.

You should start with the south-western tunnel, in the cave in Pinnath Gelin.Blow up the south-western tunnelThe black powder did a fine job of blocking the south-western tunnel. You should move on to the western tunnel and blow that one up as well.

The western tunnel is in the Krauzhaf cave in Pinnath Gelin.Blow up the western tunnelWith both the western and south-western tunnels blocked, you have but one left.

You should blow up the north-western tunnel in the Krauzhaf cave in Pinnath Gelin.Blow up the north-western tunnelYou have battled your way through Krauzhaf and blown up the three tunnels that the Ronkrúm goblins were using to crawl out of the mountain.

Igerna is waiting to speak with you outside the Krauzhaf cave, in Pinnath Gelin.'Much as I wish to be free of this dank place, we still have work to do. From what I've overheard, this tribe of Ronkrúm goblins recently tunnelled to the surface, and if we don't send them back underground they shall continue to spill over into Pinnath Gelin.

'These wretched louts are industrious, but lazy creatures, and they rely heavily on their black powder to blast open new tunnels in the mountainside. We can use this against them! Go and gather cases from around the cave and their camp outside. Then, delve deeper into the mountain until you find the places from whence they come. Between sealing these off and the punishment you shall be dealing out, they will be hesitant to continue their plans to surface.

'My wound is troubling, but I think I can walk now. I shall meet you outside the cave when you are done.''I heard the explosions from here! May that make them think twice about coming to the lands of Gondor.'Word of the Ronkrúm goblin incursion must be brought to Ost Arndír.Igerna has sent you on to Ost Arndír with her report of the goblin incursion.

You should bring the report to Lúmar and let him know what you and Igerna have been doing.'Word of the goblins must be brought to Ost Arndír, but my wound will make my journey a slow one. I beg of you one last boon – bring this report to Lúmar. He needs to know about the threat of the goblins. The knights will take it from here, ${PLAYER}.''You return! With the scent of black powder about you, but looking none the worse for wear. Did you find Igerna?'

You hand him the report and explain what you found. He takes it from you and reads it gravely.

'It seems we owe you great thanks for your actions in Krauzhaf and across Pinnath Gelin. I shall send knights to deal with the remaining goblins, and a horse for Igerna, that she might not have to walk all the way back.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You are true to your reputation, and lucky we are that you arrived when you did.'Orgolas is very excited to join King Elessar's travelling party as he journeys into Pinnath Gelin.King Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond CirionThingast has a reputation for being haunted, and the folk of Lond Cirion will appreciate if you face some of the dangers there as you journey north.Defeat beasts or spirits in Thingast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Iáphel is located north of Thingast, in Tûm Rost.Travel to the entrance of Iáphel in Tûm RostGrethril is at the entrance of Iáphel in Tûm Rost.Talk to Grethril by the entrance to IáphelGwindir is north-west of the entrance to Iáphel.Talk to Gwindir north-west of the entrance of IáphelVine trellises can be found on the western side of Iáphel.Pick grapes from the vines at Iáphel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gwindir is waiting for you to return with the grapes you picked.Gwindir offered you three of the wines stored nearby.Select wines for the King's company (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Grethril will know how best to store the wine bottles. She is by the entrance to Iáphel.King Elessar is in Iáphel.Talk to King Elessar at Iáphel'Do you think there will be fighting? They say the war is over, but from the tower I saw Corsair ships off in the distance, and the guards report that they sometimes send raiding parties inland to slay and to steal!

'I have studied the maps, you know, and the road to Pinnath Gelin leaves Lond Cirion to the west. It passes through Thingast before turning north, and folk say Thingast might be haunted! I will have my sword at the ready. Will you tell King Elessar that I am not afraid?''I have studied the maps, you know, and the road to Pinnath Gelin leaves Lond Cirion to the west. It passes through Thingast before turning north, and folk say Thingast might be haunted! I will have my sword at the ready. Will you tell King Elessar that I am not afraid?''Young Orgolas says the road we must take through Thingast may be haunted? I have not heard this before, though it is true that folk once dwelled there and now only their ruins remain. They were called the Orodhoth by the Dúnedain, but they had another name for themselves that I cannot recall.

'As we travel through Thingast, let us remain alert for any dangers that might threaten the safety of the company: spirits, beasts, or raiding Corsairs. Two of these seem more likely to me, but I will not discount the possibility that the folk of Anfalas know more about these lands than we do, and Thingast may truly by haunted by shades. I tell you I have had my fill of spirits.'

Elessar smiles.

'My companion Hirluin was lord of Pinnath Gelin, ${PLAYER}, and he and I adventured with Forlong in days long ago. Forlong would say he could never have his fill of spirit, and Hirluin would laugh and laugh; no room could be empty of cheer that had the two of them in it. But they are gone now, and cheer seems hard to come by. At least the memory of their jesting remains with me, and I cherish it.''As we travel through Thingast, let us remain alert for any dangers that might threaten the safety of the company: spirits, beasts, or raiding Corsairs. Two of these seem more likely to me.''As we travel through Thingast, let us remain alert for any dangers that might threaten the safety of the company: spirits, beasts, or raiding Corsairs. Two of these seem more likely to me.''Do you have a moment for me, ${PLAYER}? I know we have come to Pinnath Gelin for matters most serious, but I beg a small boon of you and the King, for we have come to a place of which I have heard a great deal, and all of it good!

'This is Iáphel in Tûm Rost, and word of the high quality of its grapes has reached the ears of wine-lovers across all of Gondor, even in distant Minas Tirith. Do you think you might see if one of the vintners here might gift us a bottle or two of their finest? I do not know what it is that makes the wine here so renowned, but this is like to be my only chance to sample it!''This is Iáphel in Tûm Rost, and word of the high quality of its grapes has reached the ears of wine-lovers across all of Gondor, even in distant Minas Tirith. Do you think you might see if one of the vintners here might gift us a bottle or two of their finest? I do not know what it is that makes the wine here so renowned, but this is like to be my only chance to sample it!''Welcome to Iáphel, the most fruitful field among all the green hills of Pinnath Gelin! I understand your company came to Tûm Rost by the road from Anfalas? You saw, then, how dry that land can be, despite how near to the Sea it lies? I will of course gift to the King and his party some bottles of our finest wine, for you must all be so parched!

'Our land is quite different than the Langstrand to the south. Where that is a place of dry, salt-scarred cliffs, ours is a green, rainy country. The mist off the Sea comes to the mountains as low clouds, leaving fog in the hollows; it gives to our grapes a rich, full taste, and the wine we make from them is without compare!

'Aye, we will gift you some bottles. But first I ask that some among your company help us with our work. Not the King or Queen, of course! But we have grapes to pick, and you surely will not refuse when such quality wine is to be the reward?''We will gift you some bottles. But first I ask that some among your company help us with our work. Not the King or Queen, of course! But we have grapes to pick, and you surely will not refuse when such quality wine is to be the reward?''You have done very well with the work! Should you wish to aid us in the future, I would not refuse the assistance! But I suppose the King has other tasks for you.

'I set aside some bottles for your company. Bring them to the King's provisioner, and be sure to tell her that if she wishes to purchase more for the cellars of Minas Tirith, the vintners of Iáphel will give her a fair price. The King should have the finest of wines for his table. Don't you agree?''I set aside some bottles for your company. Bring them to the King's provisioner, and be sure to tell her that if she wishes to purchase more for the cellars of Minas Tirith, the vintners of Iáphel will give her a fair price. The King should have the finest of wines for his table. Don't you agree?''I set aside some bottles for your company. Bring them to the King's provisioner, and be sure to tell her that if she wishes to purchase more for the cellars of Minas Tirith, the vintners of Iáphel will give her a fair price. The King should have the finest of wines for his table. Don't you agree?''Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}!

'No, we cannot open these now! We must save them for the right time! I am certain they will live up to their reputation, but if we were to drink them now, in the field, we would truly be wasting the opportunity to enjoy them! Perhaps when the King's business in Pinnath Gelin is done.

'Where does he intend next to travel?''Where does the King intend next to travel?''Yes, I am ready to continue onward, ${PLAYER}. Our next destination is Ost Arndír, stronghold of the Lord of the Green Hills. It was the keep of my friend and companion Hirluin the Fair, but I understand after his death at Pelennor his daughter now rules from that seat.'King Elessar's next destination is to be Ost Arndír in Pinnath Gelin.The entrance to Ost Arndír is to the north-east of Iáphel, in Pinnath Gelin.Travel to the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír, north-east of IáphelHebron is outside the northern entrance to the keep of Ost Arndír.Talk to Hebron outside the keep of Ost ArndírThe Lady Nauriel is inside the main hall of Ost Arndír, located upstairs inside the keep.Talk to Lady Nauriel in Ost ArndírNauriel's son Thorongil's room is to the north-east, through the door on the right.Find Thorongil's room inside the keep of Ost ArndírThorongil is in his room north of the main hall, inside the keep of Ost Arndír.Talk to Thorongil inside his room in the keep of Ost ArndírOrgolas is in Thorongil's room in Ost Arndír.Talk to Orgolas in Thorongil's room inside the keep of Ost ArndírHebron is outside the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír.Talk to Hebron in Ost ArndírAccording to Hebron, various dangers can be found in the vicinity of Ost Arndír, and the folk of the town would appreciate you helping deal with them.Defeat foes throughout Pinnath Gelin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hebron is outside the northern entrance of the keep in Ost Arndír.Talk to Hebron outside the northern entrance of the keep in Ost ArndírThorongil is outside the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír.Talk to Thorongil outside the keep of Ost Arndír'Hirluin's daughter is named Nauriel, and she is high in the order of knights that protects Pinnath Gelin; it is the tradition in this land that women may also wield sword and sceptre. She is married to Carandolion, who is the brother of Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale, though I recall the two are quite different in temper. The son of Nauriel and Carandolion is named Thorongil, and must now be about ten years old.'

Elessar nods.

'Yes, I am afraid Hirluin spoke often of our campaign in Umbar, and while it has been many years since I wore the name "Thorongil," his grandson was given that name in remembrance of me. I would prefer you not speak of it to Nauriel or her son. There must be few in Outer Gondor these days who know the warrior Thorongil and the King Elessar for the same man, and I would like to keep it that way.

'Ost Arndír is to the north-east of Iáphel. Let us travel there now before Grethril burdens our pack-horses with more bottles of wine than we need. To speak honestly, this may have happened already.''I am afraid Hirluin spoke often of our campaign in Umbar, and while it has been many years since I wore the name "Thorongil," his grandson was given that name in remembrance of me. I would prefer you not speak of it to Nauriel or her son. There must be few in Outer Gondor these days who know the warrior Thorongil and the King Elessar for the same man, and I would like to keep it that way.

'Ost Arndír is to the north-east of Iáphel. Let us travel there now before Grethril burdens our pack-horses with more bottles of wine than we need.''Welcome.''Welcome to Ost Arndír, home of the Lady Nauriel, Knight of the Green Hills and Lord of Pinnath Gelin. She awaits you inside the hall.''Welcome to Ost Arndír, home of the Lady Nauriel, Knight of the Green Hills and Lord of Pinnath Gelin. She awaits you inside the hall.''I am pleased to see you among the Green Hills, King Elessar and Queen Arwen! You and all your company are welcome to stay for as long as it pleases you. Know that there are dangers still in Pinnath Gelin, for Haradrim fighters were transported here on Corsair ships during the war, and my knights have not yet found them all. Raiders from Umbar, too, have come up the rivers in small boats and harry our people. But I see warriors among your company, and if they exercise caution they should fear little.

'I understand you have brought Golasgil's heir Orgolas with you on this visit? My son Thorongil will be delighted to entertain a boy of his own years! Perhaps this ${RACE}, ${PLAYER}, will show Orgolas to my son's chambers? You will find them to the north-east, through the door on the right.''I understand you have brought Golasgil's heir Orgolas with you on this visit? My son Thorongil will be delighted to entertain a boy of his own years! Perhaps this ${RACE}, ${PLAYER}, will show Orgolas to my son's chambers? You will find them to the north-east, through the door on the right.''Hello. So you are a ${CLASS}? Are you a good one?'

Thorongil dismisses your answer with a casual wave, and turns to Orgolas.

'I am going to train to be a knight when I'm old enough. It won't be very long from now, just a year or two! I have already been practicing my sword-play with sticks and with implements from the kitchens. Do you want to see? We can pretend to duel, and whoever wins gets to be the King of Outer Gondor. I wager King Elessar will be very impressed with us!''I have been practicing my sword-play. I am already very skilled, ask anyone!''Back home in Lond Cirion, Aerhant often lets me climb the tower and look out over the Sea, and I have seen a great many Corsair ships going here and there across the waves! Once when the sky was clear I thought I could see all the way to Umbar, but he said that wasn't possible. But I have very sharp eyes, just like my father did, and he was a great mariner and fought bravely at the Black Gate of Mordor.

'I will be fine, ${PLAYER}. You can go now.''I will be fine, ${PLAYER}. You can go now.''Ah, ${PLAYER}, you are looking for something to do while the King and Queen speak with Lady Nauriel? I am glad to hear it, for there is always something that needs doing in and around Ost Arndír.

'Can I ask you to deal with any of the foes that encroach upon our lands? There is no shortage of threats throughout many of the Green Hills.''Can I ask you to deal with any of the foes that encroach upon our lands? There is no shortage of threats throughout many of the Green Hills.''You have taken care of some foes of Pinnath Gelin? I am grateful for your service on behalf of Ost Arndír and the Lady Nauriel. I see why the King has made you a part of his travelling company!''What is this tumult?''Do you often befriend liars, ${PLAYER}, and encourage them to speak untruths? Because Orgolas here has told me something surprising, and there is no way it could be true!

'He says that King Elessar adventured with my grandsire Hirluin in Umbar, many years ago, and that he is the "Thorongil" for whom I was named!'Thorongil is eager to show his new friend the sights and sounds of Pinnath Gelin, and to make a memorable first impression.Orgolas is outside the keep of Ost Arndír.Talk to Orgolas outside the keep of Ost ArndírThe boys have run off on their adventure.There is no stopping themDaeram is inside the kitchens of the keep in Ost Arndír.Find Daeram at the keep's kitchens in Ost Arndír and tell him where the boys planned to goOrgolas and Thorongil intended to go to the Wave-hunter, docked to the east on the lake in Pinnath Gelin.Find Orgolas and Thorongil near the Wave-hunterOrgolas is near the Wave-hunter, peering up at the rigging.Talk to Orgolas near the Wave-hunterDaeram is near the Wave-hunter.Talk to Daeram near the Wave-hunterYou should cross onto the deck of the Wave-hunter in order to get Thorongil to come down.Cross onto the deck of the Wave-hunterFrom the deck of the Wave-hunter you should <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for Thorongil to come down.Thorongil is high above your head in the rigging of the Wave-hunter.Wait for Thorongil to come downThorongil stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter.Talk to Thorongil on the deck of the Wave-hunterOrgolas stands near the Wave-hunter.Talk to Orgolas near the Wave-hunterThe northern entrance to the keep of Ost Arndír is west of the Wave-hunter.Return to the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír, west of the Wave-hunterHebron is outside the keep of Ost Arndír.Talk to Hebron outside the keep of Ost Arndír'He is just making it up! One look at the King tells me he could not be old enough to have been of fighting age when my grandsire Hirluin adventured in Umbar! To think Orgolas believes I would fall for such falsehoods! I tell you I am smarter than that!''Orgolas must think I know nothing at all if he believes I will fall for this falsehood!''But it is true! I am not lying! I heard King Elessar say he was the very same Thorongil that adventured with Hirluin and Forlong in Umbar so many years ago! It is true! Tell him, ${PLAYER}! I wish Thorongil would believe me! But he is going to take me to see the Wave-hunter where it sits at dock, and I do want to see the ship my father left to me, so...'

You tell the boys they should not go alone, but they pay you no mind.'What? Orgolas has left the keep with Nauriel's son? Already? We only just arrived! How can he have already slipped my watch and disappeared?'

You tell Daeram that the boys intended to see the Wave-hunter where it is docked, and he breathes a sigh of relief.

'That is not far from here to the east. Quickly now!''Look there!''That is not far from here to the east. Quickly now!''I told him not to do it, but he would not listen to me. Now he is halfway up the rigging of the Wave-hunter, even though I told him he should not climb it! It is my ship, ${PLAYER}, given to me by my father, and Thorongil should do what I say, and not what I forbid, concerning it!''He should not be up there! The Wave-hunter is my ship!''What if he falls, ${PLAYER}? At least Orgolas had sense enough to stay on solid ground! I am not burdened with the duty of protecting Thorongil.

'Still... I do not want him to fall. But thank the Valar it is not Orgolas up there. Lady Marra would cook me on a spit and serve me to her guests.''We should get him to come down, if we can.''He should not be up there!''We should get him to come down, if we can.''He should not be up there!''You worry too much, ${PLAYER}. I was not in any danger, but even if I was I would not be afraid. I am no coward!

'I was named for the great hero Thorongil, sword-brother of my grandsire Hirluin and mighty hero of Gondor! He warred with Umbar, many years ago, and I have heard from the men-at-arms of Ost Arndír that even today the Umbarrim tremble when they speak his name! I am going to follow in his footsteps as soon as I am old enough to become a Knight of the Green Hills. And that is the truth, unlike whatever lies Orgolas insists on telling! To think King Elessar might be the same man as Thorongil of old? Pig slop!

'I tire of this ship, anyway. Orgolas's mother sent the Wave-hunter here during the war, and it did not even see any fighting! What a waste that is!''I tire of this ship. It bores me.''Thorongil and I are about the same age, but I think he is... I don't know...'

Orgolas kicks a small stone into the water, and the ripples run up against the side of the Wave-hunter before dispersing.

'He is rather childish, isn't he? He says he will soon become a Knight of the Green Hills, but I think he is too rash, and too unthinking, and too... I don't know. A proper knight should not be any of those things, ${PLAYER}! He does not give a thought for any of his people, and speaks only of his own glory. And I was telling the truth about King Elessar!

'I suppose we should return to Ost Arndír.''I suppose we should return to Ost Arndír.''The boys are safe? Thank the Valar!

'A scout has just arrived from Tûm Rost, driving his horse beyond exhaustion. The Corsairs have attacked in force!'Tûm Rost has been attacked by Corsair raiders, and now the folk of Pinnath Gelin must spring to its defence.Nauriel is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.Talk to Nauriel in Ost ArndírKing Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.Talk to King Elessar in the main hall of the keep of Ost ArndírKing Elessar hopes to bring his own fighters to join the defence of Tûm Rost against the Corsair raiders.Talk to King Elessar in the keep of Ost Arndír and join the defence of Tûm RostNauriel is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.Talk to Nauriel in the main hall of the keep of Ost ArndírKing Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír.Talk to King Elessar in Ost Arndír'The Lady Nauriel prepares a response to deal with the Corsair raiders. Hurry now to her side, for there is little time to waste if we are to save the folk of Tûm Rost!''The Lady Nauriel prepares a response to deal with the Corsair raiders. Hurry now to her side, for there is little time to waste if we are to save the folk of Tûm Rost!''A number of Corsair ships have sailed in secret up the Hathollant river, and now they pillage the farms and villages of Tûm Rost. I will dispatch our soldiers at once. Are you with us, Elessar?''I will dispatch our soldiers at once. Are you with us, Elessar?''We will fight alongside you to defend the Green Hills, Nauriel. Count my warriors among your number!

'Are you prepared for this, ${PLAYER}? Tell me when you are ready to depart for Tûm Rost.''Then let us depart for Tûm Rost with all haste!''This outrage cannot stand! I will wage such war upon the Corsairs that they will not sail within sight of Gondor for a thousand years! I will call to arms every knight that has ever raised sword within Pinnath Gelin to follow me and rescue my son!''I will slay every Corsair that thinks to keep my son from me!''I think there is reason to believe the Corsairs will not harm Thorongil, Nauriel. They will see value in keeping him alive to use in a potential bargain with Gondor. If we act rashly we might endanger the boy's life; we must not risk that.

'I want to send someone to follow the ships. We must track them from shore, and see where they sail. It is not certain they will return directly to Umbar, and if they put in at a cove along the Langstrand we may be able to rescue Thorongil before he is brought back to the Kindred of the Coins.

'What say you, ${PLAYER}? Are you prepared for a chase?'King Elessar directed you to hurry south along the coast of Anfalas, in pursuit of the fleeing Corsair ships.King Elessar wants you to travel with haste to the coast near Thingast, south-west of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.Travel to the southern coast of Thingast, south-west of Lond Cirion, in AnfalasFrom this location on the coast you should <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the water in search of the fleeing Corsair ships.Another location on the coast to the west may allow you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the water in search of the fleeing Corsair ships.Arasdil stands nearby, and has something to say to you.Talk to Arasdil on the coast of ThingastArasdil told you he saw Corsair activity at the haunted grove to the south-west before the ships sailed toward Pinnath Gelin.Search the grove to the south-west for sign of the CorsairsA high quality bow rests on a stone within the grove here.Examine the high-quality bow on the stone blockYou feel the sudden sensation of being watched.Remain on your guardA mighty Ent stares at you from within the curious, deep wells of his eyes.Talk to the Ent in the shady grove'I want you to return to Anfalas as quickly as you can, my friend, and to look for sign of the retreating Corsair ships from the coast of Thingast. If it can be managed, we need to know what direction they sail as they leave the river.

'We will follow after you, but a larger company must move more slowly than one ${RACE}. Once you determine the direction of the Corsair ships, you will find me at Lond Cirion. Go with utmost haste, my friend! Much depends on what you can learn of their course.''I want you to return to Anfalas as quickly as you can, my friend, and to look for sign of the retreating Corsair ships from the coast of Thingast. If it can be managed, we need to know what direction they sail as they leave the river.

'We will follow after you, but a larger company must move more slowly than one ${RACE}. Once you determine the direction of the Corsair ships, you will find me at Lond Cirion. Go with utmost haste, my friend! Much depends on what you can learn of their course.''My son is depending upon your haste, ${PLAYER}. Do not fail him.''I want you to return to Anfalas as quickly as you can, my friend, and to look for sign of the retreating Corsair ships from the coast of Thingast. If it can be managed, we need to know what direction they sail as they leave the river.

'We will follow after you, but a larger company must move more slowly than one ${RACE}. Once you determine the direction of the Corsair ships, you will find me at Lond Cirion. Go with utmost haste, my friend! Much depends on what you can learn of their course.''My son is depending upon your haste, ${PLAYER}. Do not fail him.''I want you to return to Anfalas as quickly as you can, my friend, and to look for sign of the retreating Corsair ships from the coast of Thingast. If it can be managed, we need to know what direction they sail as they leave the river.

'We will follow after you, but a larger company must move more slowly than one ${RACE}. Once you determine the direction of the Corsair ships, you will find me at Lond Cirion. Go with utmost haste, my friend! Much depends on what you can learn of their course.''My son is depending upon your haste, ${PLAYER}. Do not fail him.''Fleeing Corsair ships? No, I have not seen anything of that sort today, for I have only just arrived from Melgobas. You say they would be coming down the river?

'Doubtless these are not the tidings you need, but I did see your ships going up-river a few days gone. From hiding I watched their crew come ashore, bearing torches and shouting commands. They visited the haunted grove to the south-west... foolish idea, of course, that's a place decent folk don't go, and still haven't! Who would count a Corsair decent, after all?

'Anyway, they were inside for just a quarter of an hour or so, and when they emerged they reboarded their ships and sailed up the river. I told the town guard back home, so do not think I haven't done my share! But I am just a fisherman, and even the guardsmen knew better than to get mixed up with two ships of Corsair raiders!

'You think they might keep a secret store of goods or weapons in that grove? Strangdene it is called, and I tell you again it is haunted. You won't see me creeping about in there, and if you've more wisdom than foolish courage, you won't go inside either! Good day to you.''I have not seen these Corsair ships return, but I did see them going up-river a few days gone. From hiding I watched their crew come ashore, bearing torches and shouting commands. They visited the haunted grove to the south-west... foolish idea, of course, that's a place decent folk don't go, and still haven't! Who would count a Corsair decent, after all?

'Anyway, they were inside for just a quarter of an hour or so, and when they emerged they reboarded their ships and sailed up the river. I told the town guard back home, so do not think I haven't done my share! But I am just a fisherman, and even the guardsmen knew better than to get mixed up with two ships of Corsair raiders!

'You think they might keep a secret store of goods or weapons in that grove? Strangdene it is called by my people, and I tell you again it is haunted. You won't see me creeping about in there, and if you've more wisdom than foolish courage, you won't go inside either! Good day to you.''I have not seen these Corsair ships return, but I did see them going up-river a few days gone. From hiding I watched their crew come ashore, bearing torches and shouting commands. They visited the haunted grove to the south-west... foolish idea, of course, that's a place decent folk don't go, and still haven't! Who would count a Corsair decent, after all?

'Anyway, they were inside for just a quarter of an hour or so, and when they emerged they reboarded their ships and sailed up the river. I told the town guard back home, so do not think I haven't done my share! But I am just a fisherman, and even the guardsmen knew better than to get mixed up with two ships of Corsair raiders!

'You think they might keep a secret store of goods or weapons in that grove? Strangdene it is called by my people, and I tell you again it is haunted. You won't see me creeping about in there, and if you've more wisdom than foolish courage, you won't go inside either! Good day to you.''You there... small one...

'Have you come here to Tumbamálë... to bring tidings of my friend... Nestinanessornë...?'The Ent Leafshade might know what transpired when the Corsair ships came this way, but getting him to tell you about it might be challenging.The Ent Leafshade is at the grove of Tumbamálë.Talk to Leafshade at TumbamálëThe Ent Leafshade is at the grove of Tumbamálë.Talk to Leafshade at Tumbamálë and learn what you can from the EntThe Ent Leafshade is at Tumbamálë, and he has much to say.Talk to Leafshade at TumbamálëKing Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep of Lond Cirion, and should hear what you learned from Leafshade.Talk to King Elessar inside the main hall of the keep of Lond Cirion'There have been many strange happenings... of late...' the Ent rumbles. He slowly turns his head to look past the trees of the grove, and falls silent. After a long moment, he seems to realize you are still here. A long, windy sigh escapes from his mouth.

'It is most unusual... for so much to happen... to the Ents,' he murmurs, sleepily.

'I am called...' he begins, and after a time you realize that the sound rolling out among the twigs and branches of the grove, making them restless, is actually a long name spoken languidly in Old Entish.

'But you may call me Lathlum... or Leafshade...' he continues, his voice little more than a sigh.'But you did not know Ferien, hm? No, you would not have. The lives of Ents are measured differently, hoom, hoom. Months! Months are the blink of an eye, or less, hm! I was thinking of Ferien when I carried this wounded creature, this Elf, back here to my home. I did not know if he would live, hoom. For Ferien I would try to save him. In time he did recover his strength, hm, hm, and that is when I named him Nestinanessornë, which is sapling-who-is-healed in the words Ferien taught to me.''Yesterday I saw... the ships return...

'They sailed south until they disappeared... over the horizon...'

Leafshade's words rise in intensity until their booming shakes the branches of the trees of Strangdene.

'I hope you will... ensure Nestinanessornë is safe...'

Leafshade ceases his trumpeting, and quiet returns once again to Tumbamálë.

'He is... a friend...' he murmurs. 'So many others went away...'

You assure Leafshade that you will do what you can to help him, but the Ent says nothing more.You cannot tell if Leafshade remains awake or if he has heard your words.'We have only just arrived at Lond Cirion, ${PLAYER}. Did you learn where the ships are bound?'

You tell Elessar that the Corsair ships left the river and sailed south until they disappeared over the horizon.

'So Nakási does make for Umbar. I was not certain that would be so. It seems she knows the value of her captive to the Kindred of the Coins. But something else troubles you, my friend. I can see it in your expression.'

You tell Elessar, more briefly than it was told to you, of Leafshade's account of the past few months. The King puts a comforting hand on your shoulder.

'Your friend Corudan lives, ${PLAYER}, but he is in need of rescue. As it happens, we were already planning such a mission, for young Thorongil must be freed from his imprisonment as well. I feel in my heart this is the way it must be: both of these captives are being brought to Umbar, the City of the Corsairs. A small party of adventurers might infiltrate the city and rescue Thorongil and Corudan where a larger group must surely fail. I want you to lead this small party, my friend. I know you are the right choice for this task, though it prove most dangerous.

'You say that Corudan's sister Sigileth intended to investigate his disappearance near Helm's Deep? I will send a message to Erkenbrand that she be found and told of these new tidings.'Leafshade appears in no hurry to speak any further, so you ask about the Elf-bow in the centre of his glade.

'Hrum, hoom! That is the bow of my friend, Nestinanessornë! He left it here when he... went away.'

The Ent sighs heavily, the breeze of his exhalation rustling the leaves of the trees.

'There was a gathering of my folk some... what is the word your kind would use, hm? Months, hoom. Some months ago. On my return, I came across a dying creature suffering from a poisoned wound. He reminded me of an old friend, an Elf I once knew. Ah, Ferien. Hm, hoom. She lived among the beeches, and sang so beautifully. Hoom...'

Leafshade stands in silence, his story unfinished, and you wonder if you should prompt him to continue.King Elessar has given you an important duty, and he believes your leadership will be crucial in the weeks ahead.Orgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion.Find Orgolas in his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond CirionOrgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion.Talk to Orgolas inside the keep of Lond CirionYou try to gather your thoughts and tell Orgolas what he needs to hear.Gather your thoughts concerning GolasgilYou remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas and father of Orgolas.Consider your memory of Golasgil in Minas Tirith before the siege of the White CityYou remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas and father of Orgolas.Consider your memory of Golasgil on the Pelennor Fields after the battleYou remember Golasgil, Lord of Anfalas and father of Orgolas.Consider your memory of Golasgil during the Battle of the Black GateOrgolas considers what you have told him of his father Golasgil, who perished at the Black Gate of Mordor.Wait for Orgolas to consider what you have told himOrgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion.Talk to Orgolas inside the keep of Lond CirionOrgolas is inside his bedroom, upstairs in the keep of Lond Cirion, and he has made up his mind.Talk to Orgolas inside the keep of Lond CirionKing Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion'I know I can rely on you for this, ${PLAYER}, but you will need a ship to carry you and the crew you choose to bring to Umbar. I have already spoken with Orgolas about this, and have given the heir of Golasgil a number of things to consider, but as you will lead the expedition across the Bay you should be the one to hear what he has decided.

'I believe you will find him in his bedroom somewhere upstairs.''I know I can rely on you for this, ${PLAYER}, but you will need a ship to carry you and the crew you choose to bring to Umbar. I have already spoken with Orgolas about this, and have given the heir of Golasgil a number of things to consider, but as you will lead the expedition across the Bay you should be the one to hear what he has decided.

'I believe you will find him in his bedroom, somewhere upstairs.''Oh, it's you.''We cannot choose the times that call upon us, can we? Someone needs to rescue Thorongil, and I suppose it falls to me. I am not a warrior or a sailor, but how... how hard can it truly be? I have watched the men training, and I can swing a sword nearly as well as they can. And the Wave-hunter has a crew who will do the actual sailing, I trust...'

Orgolas chews his lower lip with worry, and you are reminded he is only twelve years old.

'I don't... I don't know what to do, ${PLAYER}. I want to help, and to prove that I am strong and brave enough to do what my father would want of me... but I also know I cannot leave my mother alone. I share some of the blame for Thorongil's capture. Should I not also be responsible for helping rescue him, if such a thing might be possible?'

Orgolas sighs unhappily.

'The King asked me "What would your father tell you?" but I confess that I don't know. Do you... do you have any idea what my father Golasgil would want me to do? What would he say to me?'You remember Golasgil standing in the White City before battle was joined on the Pelennor Fields, unafraid of the hard times ahead, trying to remember the words of an old travelling song.You remember finding Golasgil on the Pelennor Fields after the great battle, surrounded by the corpses of the Orcs that ambushed him. You recall too the look on his face when he learned how many of his friends perished before the walls of Minas Tirith, but such sorrow did not keep him from marching to the Black Gate with the Men of the West when his King required it.You remember Golasgil at the Battle of the Black Gate as he stood face to face with the mighty Olog that would give him his mortal wound, and you recall his final words.

'If there is a day to come after this,' he said, 'look to the people of Anfalas. Tell them their lord...'

You cannot say for certain what the Lord of Anfalas intended, for then he died, only moments before the fall of the Dark Lord Sauron and the rout of Mordor's armies. You relay his father's words to Orgolas, and Golasgil's heir rubs at a smudge on the floor with his shoe.'My father's last thoughts were not for himself, or for what he was about to lose, but for the folk of Anfalas, so far away? How can that be true, ${PLAYER}? He left us behind to go to the war. If he truly cared would he not have remained here?'

You remind Orgolas that his father counted his family, his son, and his wife among those people of Anfalas he sought to protect, and it was on their behalf that he followed the King to war. Orgolas sighs again.

'Is that what you are telling me? To be a good ruler, you have to put the needs of your people ahead of your own? Is that what it means to be the son of the Lord of Anfalas? Is that what it means to be the heir of Golasgil? But it is so difficult. Thorongil would cast all that aside and charge off to battle, hoping to achieve glory, and before today I might have done the same. But I am not a fighter, not yet, and if I were seized by Umbar as was Thorongil... what would that mean for the people of Anfalas? I have to stay here. I have to help my mother and be here for my people. My father was a great mariner, and a mighty warrior, but I have not yet grown into the man he was. I must serve my people in another way.''The Wave-hunter was given to me by my father, and if he had not died in service of Gondor, one day he would have taught me to be a great mariner, as he was. But that was not meant to be. Instead, I give command of the Wave-hunter to you until Thorongil is returned safely to his hall. Use it well and wisely, and may the memory of Golasgil go with you, and fill the sails with wind to speed you on your journey! When Thorongil is rescued, and the threat of the Corsairs is ended, perhaps you will teach me what you have learned of sailing, and I will drive the Wave-hunter upon the Great Sea.

'But that will be in days yet to come! For now I must find how to protect the folk of Anfalas I will one day rule, and that is a lesson I will learn from my mother.''I am pleased with the decision of Orgolas, ${PLAYER}. I will not say I expected it with complete certainty, but I believed the son of Golasgil was enough like his father to arrive there after some deliberation. The folk of Anfalas will be in good hands once the Lady Marra instructs her son about what she has learned of rule: a considerable amount!

'But our paths must now diverge, my friend. I charge you with the rescue of Thorongil and of Corudan, and look forward to your successful return aboard the Wave-hunter. Do try not to fan anew the flames of war with Umbar, ${PLAYER}. This must be a mission carried out in secret.''I will remain behind to help protect Anfalas and Pinnath Gelin from further attack by the Corsairs, for that is the best way for me to aid my people... but the King is right that someone must sail to Umbar and rescue Thorongil, if it can be done in secret. He has chosen you for this, ${PLAYER}, but you need a ship.'

Orgolas stands at attention and studies you seriously.

'The Wave-hunter was given to me by my father, and if he had not died in service of Gondor, one day he would have taught me to be a great mariner, as he was. But that was not meant to be. Instead, I give command of the Wave-hunter to you until Thorongil is returned safely to his hall. Use it well and wisely, and may the memory of Golasgil go with you, and fill the sails with wind to speed you on your journey! When Thorongil is rescued, and the threat of the Corsairs is ended, perhaps you will teach me what you have learned of sailing, and I will drive the Wave-hunter upon the Great Sea.

'But that will be in days yet to come! For now I must find how to protect the folk of Anfalas I will one day rule, and that is a lesson I will learn from my mother.'King Elessar is about to leave Anfalas with his travelling party, but he has entrusted you with a different mission of grave importance.You should speak with the members of the travelling party who will leave Anfalas in the company of King Elessar.Talk to Queen Arwen at Lond CirionTalk to Ioreth at Lond CirionTalk to Grethril at Lond CirionTalk to Aphadaer at Lond CirionTalk to Glindor at Lond CirionTalk to Líniel at Lond CirionLady Marra is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.Talk to Lady Marra outside the keep of Lond CirionKing Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.Talk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond CirionCaebar waits for you in the library of Lond Cirion, inside the keep.Return to the library of Lond Cirion inside the keepCaebar is in the library of Lond Cirion, inside the keep.Talk to Caebar in the library of Lond Cirion'The Wave-hunter was harboured upriver in Pinnath Gelin to protect it from the Corsairs during the War of the Ring; a decision that must have rankled Golasgil even as he saw the need for it. The ship's crew is likely eager to sail again, and you will need their talents and knowledge of the Bay to bring you to Umbar in secret.

'But your arrival at the City of the Corsairs will only be your mission's beginning, ${PLAYER}. To that end, I suggest you add to the Wave-hunter's complement of sailors such folk as you can trust or as have a stake in the quest's successful conclusion. You will not be able to keep Nauriel away, I think, and as a Knight of the Green Hills her combat prowess may be of use to you. Legolas and Gimli will go with you gladly, of course, and I think Sirgon of Pelargir will be no less eager to sail again; his knowledge of the Bay and of the folk that dwell along its shores may prove valuable. If you believe that Corudan's sister Sigileth will begin her search for him at Helm's Deep, the messages I have dispatched to Erkenbrand should reach her, and she will likely make her way to Gondor as soon as she can.

'There is another you should add to your crew, my friend, but I advise you to watch him carefully. I speak of the Corsair Jajax. It may be helpful to have him near as you adventure in Umbar... if you can trust him. Now bid farewell to the travelling company, ${PLAYER}, for we each have our own roads to walk and it may be some time before we see each other again.''Now bid farewell to the travelling company, ${PLAYER}, for we each have our own roads to walk and it may be some time before we see each other again.''Good fortune go with you, ${PLAYER}, and may you rescue the young heir of Pinnath Gelin from his captivity.

'You need not take my advice, but if you have a willing ear I might suggest that you bring my brothers with you when you assemble your crew. Elladan and Elrohir remained behind to aid the folk in Pinnath Gelin for a few days, but I know that they would be happy to accompany you when they have done there what they wanted.''Dearie me, ${PLAYER}, do take care of yourself! I hope the things I have heard about the City of the Corsairs are untrue, for it sounds a frightful and violent place! How do Corsairs behave when they are at home? I cannot even imagine!'

You tell Ioreth that your mission is supposed to be a secret, and she gives you a dramatic wink.

'My lips will remain sealed. You can count on me!'

She suddenly smacks her forehead with one palm.

'It is going to be very warm there. You will need to dress for the weather! A change of clothes may be warranted, ${PLAYER}! Umbar, can you imagine?''I understand you are leaving us, ${PLAYER}? Good luck to you, and to young Thorongil, the heir of Pinnath Gelin! I hope you are right, and the Corsairs will not harm their young captive. I would volunteer to come with you if I was not charged with maintaining the provisions for the King's travelling party, but what use could I be on such a quest? I am no fighter.

'But I do know food, ${PLAYER}. The fruits of Umbar are apples, dates, figs, grapes, melons, and plums. Vegetables include beets, cabbage, eggplant, fennel, onions, and turnips. The diet of the Umbarrim contains a great deal of fish and shellfish, but also beef, goat, mutton, and poultry, in lesser quantities.

'I don't suppose that helps you at all? I will miss you, friend.''You are leaving us on a secret errand, ${PLAYER}? Ioreth says you go to rescue young Thorongil from the Kindred of the Coins? No, do not seek to deny it! We both know it is true.

'If you do encounter any members of this Kindred, do not stay the killing stroke! They need to be taught not to interfere with the rule of Gondor.'

You tell Aphadaer you hope to rescue Thorongil without undue bloodshed, and he snorts.

'I am sure that is your hope, but nothing so risky was ever accomplished without bloodshed. When it proves impossible, you will remember my words, I warrant.''Farewell, ${PLAYER}! Líniel and I will watch out for the King on his return to Minas Tirith. You take care of yourself, for my heart tells me you are about to be in far greater danger than the rest of us!''I hope you know what you are doing, ${PLAYER}. Ioreth says you plan to sail to Umbar, and most of what I have heard of that place is... frightening. The King says Sauron is gone, and I have no reason to think he is wrong about that, but Sauron was worshipped for a long time in the City of the Corsairs. Can you be certain his cult is gone?

'Glindor and I will do what we can to keep the King safe. I hope the crew you assemble for your mission will do the same for you!''I feel it will be some time before we see each other again.''I may have misjudged both you and the King, ${PLAYER}. I felt certain the two of you would encourage my son Orgolas to follow in his father's footsteps, luring him away from Anfalas and into danger... but you have done the opposite. I am surprised.

'My heart goes out to Nauriel and to her husband. I hope you are able to rescue their son from the Corsairs who have stolen him away. If Golasgil were here, I know he would welcome you aboard the Wave-hunter... indeed, he would have set sail at once, as soon as he had a course to follow!

'Good fortune go with you and with the crew you choose. Long have I borne resentment for my husband's ship in my heart, but now I place upon its wooden frame my most fervent hope that you will return soon and safely, with young Thorongil in tow.''My heart goes out to Nauriel and to her husband. I hope you are able to rescue their son from the Corsairs who have stolen him away. If Golasgil were here, I know he would welcome you aboard the Wave-hunter... indeed, he would have set sail at once, as soon as he had a course to follow!

'Good fortune go with you and with the crew you choose. Long have I borne resentment for my husband's ship in my heart, but now I place upon its wooden frame my most fervent hope that you will return soon and safely, with young Thorongil in tow.''So this is farewell.'

Elessar clasps your arm and looks into your eyes.

'You sail into dangerous waters, ${PLAYER}, and in Umbar you will be beyond my help. Rescue young Thorongil, and Corudan, and return to Gondor as soon as you may. I leave the choice of your crew to you, but I have asked my scribe Caebar to assemble some notes on folk who might be well-suited for the task. Speak to him in the library of Lond Cirion and hear his suggestions.

'Good-bye, my friend. I will see you again, but it may be many days hence, and far from here. Haste and good fortune go with you!''You sail into dangerous waters, ${PLAYER}, and in Umbar you will be beyond my help. Rescue young Thorongil, and Corudan, and return to Gondor as soon as you may. I leave the choice of your crew to you, but I have asked my scribe Caebar to assemble some notes on folk who might be well-suited for the task. Speak to him in the library inside the keep and hear his suggestions.

'Good-bye, my friend. I will see you again, but it may be many days hence, and far from here. Haste and good fortune go with you!''This is really happening? When the King asked me to accompany you to Umbar, I thought he was joking. I thought he said it in jest! But it was not so.

'I will do my best, ${PLAYER}. You have shown me kindness, and I will do what I can in return. But do not ask me to steer the ship! I would fetch us up upon the rocks, or on a reef, or...

'Oh, I feel suddenly faint.'Elessar has charged you to carry out a dangerous rescue mission to the City of the Corsairs, and for that you will need a willing crew.Caebar has written some notes about potential crew-members for the Wave-hunter. Consult the book on the table in the library of Lond Cirion, and let it guide you as you assemble your crew.Complete 'The Crew: Knight of the Green Hills'Complete 'The Crew: The Boon Companions'Complete 'The Crew: The Sea-longing Lord'Complete 'The Crew: She Who Remained'Complete 'The Crew: The Corsair Jajax'Recruit any other members of the crew you wishCaebar has written some notes about potential crew-members for the Wave-hunter. Consult the book on the table in the library of Lond Cirion, and let it guide you as you assemble your crew.

When you are satisfied with the crew you have assembled, return to the library of Lond Cirion and speak with Caebar.Talk to Caebar in the library of Lond Cirion when you are satisfied with your crewRecruit any other members of the crew you wish'I will be fine in a moment. Let me just... breathe for a bit.'

Caebar rubs his eyes and steadies himself.

'All right, ${PLAYER}. To business, to business. The Wave-hunter already has a complement of sailors, and they will best know how to bring us to Umbar, but you will want to fill out the crew with trusted and accomplished folk. After all, there will still be a rescue to manage once we arrive at the City of the Corsairs! King Elessar suggested several additions to the crew, and if you deem these enough we can sail as soon as you have returned with them: Lady Nauriel of Pinnath Gelin, the boon companions Legolas and Gimli, Lord Sirgon of Pelargir, Corudan's sister Sigileth, and the Corsair Jajax. I have compiled notes on each of these, and on others who might be willing to sail with us on the Wave-hunter. Consult my notes in the book on the table there, and may it prove useful as you assemble your crew.''The Wave-hunter already has a complement of sailors, and they will best know how to bring us to Umbar, but you will want to fill out the crew with trusted and accomplished folk. After all, there will still be a rescue to manage once we arrive at the City of the Corsairs! King Elessar suggested several additions to the crew, and if you deem these enough we can sail as soon as you have returned with them: Lady Nauriel of Pinnath Gelin, the boon companions Legolas and Gimli, Lord Sirgon of Pelargir, Corudan's sister Sigileth, and the Corsair Jajax. I have compiled notes on each of these, and on others who might be willing to sail with us on the Wave-hunter. Consult my notes in the book on the table there, and may it prove useful as you assemble your crew.''Have you assembled a crew for the Wave-hunter?'

You tell Caebar about the crew you have recruited for the mission to Umbar, and he nods.

'They sound quite capable, ${PLAYER}. I think you have done very well, and I am glad to have been of service. I suppose it is nearly time for us to depart.'Chittering and feral growls have been heard in a once-quiet forest outside of Ost Arndír.Serric has asked you to reduce the cave-claw infestation in the nearby mountains.

Cave-claws have been spotted at the foot of the mountainside west of Ost Arndír.Defeat cave-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Serric know that you have lessened the number of cave-claws at Rasping-crag.

Serric is in Ost Arndír.Return to Serric'Someone needs to do something! I just got back from trying to gather firewood in the woods west of the city and you will not believe what I found. Cave-claws! They've burst through the mountainside and are infesting the forest. Someone needs to take care of those vermin before they multiply! Before they come down into Ost Arndír itself!'

Serric shudders at the thought and looks at you impatiently.'You did it? Oh, thank you so much. Ugh, those creatures make my stomach turn.'A herd of oxen grazes upon the green hills of Pinnath Gelin.You have been tasked to hunt dun cows for food.

Oxen can be found on a hill called Glaerendalf, to the west.Hunt dun cows for meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Locrin's brother Branach will be pleased to receive the meat you collected. He waits for you at the farm of Cornworth.'Many of our hands did not return from the war, and each of us still on the farm has to work twice as hard as before! We need some hearty meals to keep us going. A herd of oxen grazes on the hill of Glaerendalf to the west of here. Will you hunt some of the dun cows there for their meat? Do not try it with any of the bulls, for their meat is likely as tough as they are!

'Once you have accomplished that, can you bring the meat to my brother Branach on our farm of Cornworth? The farm is to the south-west of here.''Many thanks, friend! Locrin was right to send you here to help! All of us here at Cornworth appreciate what you have done for us.'The island of Loeg Thangalf has become home to ferocious dread-turtles, whose shells may well serve to provide protection and armour for the Knights of the Green Hills.Maelvír has asked you to bring back shells from the dread-turtles inhabiting a nearby island.

You can hunt dread-turtles on the island of Loeg Thangalf, in Pinnath Gelin.Collect turtle shells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})With multiple dread-turtle shells in hand, you should return to Maelvír.

Maelvír is at Mereham, in central Pinnath Gelin.'Hello, hello! Ooh, a ${CLASS}. Most excellent! You're just who I need!

'Ah, let me explain. I am Maelvír - armourer for the Knights of the Green Hills. I heard that dread-turtles have moved onto the nearby island of Loeg Thangalf. Isn't it exciting? That is, you see, I am very interested in learning more about their armoured shells. Bring some back, and I shall reward you. What do you say?''Welcome back, welcome back! Ah, do you have them? Oof, you certainly smell like you do.'Branach would like you to feed acorns to wild boars so that they might take on a more unctuous flavour.Scatter acorns for the nearby boars to eat.

The boars may be found to the south-west of Branach's farm, near the Hallothant.Scatter handfuls of acorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have done as Branach asked. Return to him.

Branach can be found at his farm, Cornworth, north-east of Farrowfold.Talk to Branach'I heard a rumour that pigs fed on acorns taste delicious. I've had some of the other farmers send me the acorns they collect on their lands. Could you try placing them around the boar dens? I would do it myself, but the last time I got close to them they tried to gore me, and I am not interested in giving them another chance to do that.

'I would reward you handsomely for an investment in my gastronomic future.''I realize now that I'll have to scatter more acorns myself after you leave. Unless... you wouldn't be planning to stay in the area for the next few weeks? No?'

He takes a bracing deep breath.

'Perhaps if I hurl the acorns from a great distance then immediately run....'There are broken sections of fence in Iáphel that need mending.Miruhir has asked you to repair fences around a section of vineyard in Iáphel.

The broken fences can be found on the western hill of Iáphel.Repair sections of fence (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should tell Miruhir that you have finished repairing the fence.

Miruhir can be found in Iáphel.Talk to Miruhir'Recent storms have damaged sections of fence around the vineyard. Animals have taken advantage of these gaps to sneak onto the grounds and feast on the fruit. One time a sheep managed to get into the wine. I spent the next hour watching an apologetic shepherd coax the drunk critter back to the rest of the flock. As amusing as that was, it's probably for the best that it doesn't happen again.''Thank you. Another thing off my mind.'Among the rocks that line the banks of a crashing waterfall, a strange ore has been discovered. Getting to it, however, will take some skill.Alêtifa has charged you with gathering ore and thinning the number of wood-trolls blocking the way to the nearby waterfall.

Wood-trolls and ore can be found in north-western Pinnath Gelin.Collect flood-iron (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat wood-trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should let Alêtifa know that you have cleared some of the wood-trolls out of the area and bring her the ore you gathered.

Alêtifa is waiting by the banks of the Hathollant, in north-western Pinnath Gelin.'Stop! Do not go that way, lest you fancy fighting the very trees themselves. I am Alêtifa, and I am come north, following hints that a previously unknown ore was to be found in the rocks about the waterfall at the top of this stream.

'Little did I know, wood-trolls infest these parts. I haven't been able to get any closer, but you look like someone who might be able to. I shall reward you if you clear out some of those overgrown weeds and bring me back what ore you might find.''Well look at you. You survived! And with a sack of ore for me to examine? Ahh, may your beard grow thick and lush. Give it here then!'Most of the Haradrim in Pinnath Gelin wish for nothing more than to return home, but a rogue captain wishes to continue a pointless fight.Torthril has asked you to help Upokhir and his allies within Pahor Boha.

Pahor Boha can be found in the south-east of Pinnath Gelin.Complete 'Upokhir's Allies'Complete 'Rescue at Pahor Boha'Complete 'Scouting Pahor Boha'You to have aided completed the tasks that Torthril and Upokhir have given you and should speak with them again.

Upokhir and Torthril can be found at Ost Arndír.Talk to Upokhir'Greetings. I am Torthril, a captain of Ost Arndir. My friend here is Upokhir, a warrior of Harad. You might wonder why Upokhir is still in Gondor now that the war is over. So does he.'

'I would like nothing more than to leave these lands,' Upokhir says. 'Almost all of my fellows feel the same, but our captain refuses to give the order to withdraw! He and his lieutenants have delusions of winning glory through a pointless conflict. They do not care how many lives will be wasted.'

Torthril looks to you. 'We will deal with this Captain, but I need time to muster a force to march on Pahor Boha. In the meantime, Upokhir's people continue to suffer, but you could help.''I cannot thank you enough for what you have done. Torthril says that her troops will be ready to move by tomorrow night. I must admit their sympathy for the plight of my fellows is touching. I was worried that Gondorians would be loath to risk their lives on behalf of my people, but the soldiers here at Ost Arndir at least appear to be honourable people. Wish us luck my friend, and I wish you luck on your continued journeys. If you one day find yourself in my homeland, I hope I will be there to greet you.'Derva has garlic scapes for Miruhir.Derva has asked you to deliver garlic scapes to her friend Miruhir.

You can find Miruhir in Iáphel.Talk to Miruhir'When you return to Iáphel, could I bother you to deliver a token of our gratitude to Miruhir? We harvested some garlic scapes the other day. Their aroma and flavour speak to the season, and he is an accomplished cook. I'm sure he would appreciate the fresh ingredients.''For me? Oh these are beautiful.'

He takes a bite of one raw and smiles.

'Chopped fine and cooked in butter, this will go lovely over some roasted fish. Thank you for bringing me these.'News has reached the scouts of goblins slithering their way out of dank tunnels under the mountains about Pinnath Gelin.Lúmar has asked you to lessen the number of goblins present in Pinnath Gelin.

You should look for goblins north of Iáphel, in Pinnath Gelin.Defeat goblins in Pinnath Gelin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have dealt a blow to the goblins in Pinnath Gellin. You should let Lúmar know that you lessened the threat you found.

Lúmar is in Ost Arndír.Speak to Lúmar in Ost Arndír'Igerna went north following reports of goblin activity at the nearby farm. This news is quite troubling, if true. If you happen to come across any of the foul creatures, reducing their numbers would do much to lessen their threat to Pinnath Gelin.''It is most concerning that you came across so many goblins. Let us hope this is the only instance of them in our land, but I fear it is not so.'Miruhir has many tasks that need doing in and around his vineyard.Miruhir has asked you to help with many tasks around the vineyard.

Complete quests in and around Iáphel.Complete 'Vineyard Pests'Complete 'A Delivery for the Cooper'Complete 'Fence Repair'Complete 'The Crows of Iáphel'You have completed all the tasks that Miruhir gave you.

Speak with him in Iáphel.Talk to Miruhir'If you have come to purchase wine, I am afraid most of it is spoken for. Merchants from Minas Tirith have bought up my entire existing stock and almost all the product of the coming harvest. How much wine can one city drink?

'What I can offer you is work. There is plenty to do and not enough hands for the doing.'You have completed all the tasks that Miruhir has set before you. He looks so happy he could hug you. He doesn't because you are sweaty, he is sweaty, and despite his gratitude he doesn't know you that well.

'What a gift you have for odd jobs! Could I convince you to stay on? Even for another day or so? Ah, you have other places to be. I understand.'

He tries not to look too disappointed but he is a forthright man who wears his heart upon his sleeve.Miruhir wishes to send some wine to his friend, Derva.Miruhir has asked you to deliver wine to his friend, Derva, at the farm to the north.

Deliver wine to Derva.Talk to Derva'If you plan to venture north in the near future, might I ask you to bring a bottle of wine to my friend, Derva? We often make time to visit each other, but work at the winery is hungry for my time.

'Please give it to her with my apologies.''Oho! I was beginning to wonder when Miruhir would come calling. He's busy at the vineyard you say? I wish I could say that's surprising but that man is in love with his work. That's alright. He'll make time for me sooner than later. He never makes me wait too long.'Leafshade has agreed to tell you the story of how he met Nestinanessornë, and what happened afterward.Nestinanessornë lies upon the stone table in Leafshade's grove.Talk to NestinanessornëLeafshade and Nestinanessornë discuss what befell the Elf, and how he came to be in the Ent's care.Listen to the conversation of Leafshade and NestinanessornëLeafshade remembers his conversations with Nestinanessornë.Talk to LeafshadeLeafshade and Nestinanessornë discuss what befell the Elf, and how he came to be in the Ent's care.Listen to the conversation of Leafshade and NestinanessornëNestinanessornë has collapsed in Leafshade's grove, seeking to go to the aid of his friends.Talk to NestinanessornëLeafshade and Nestinanessornë discuss the Elf's need to leave the Ent's grove.Listen to the conversation of Leafshade and NestinanessornëNakási Wave-reaper and her Corsairs have come to Leafshade's grove.Talk to Nakási Wave-reaperNakási Wave-reaper poses a threat to Leafshade and to Nestinanessornë.Observe the confrontation between Nakási Wave-reaper and LeafshadeLeafshade is ready to conclude his tale.Talk to Leafshade'Where... where am I? What happened to me?

'I remember the marching ranks of the Orcs! My friends... I have to warn my friends... and the defenders of Helm's Deep...

'But... but how did I come to be here? Pain... I remember a pain in my side...''You are one of the long-lived ones, like my friend Ferien, hoom. But even poison can bring the Elves low, if it is of a bad sort. The poison used by these burárum, these Orcs, is of a very bad sort indeed. Any others struck by their arrows would have died at once, and never known there was poison to survive. An Elf might last a little longer, but without my Entish medicine you would have perished too. You are, hoom, lucky? Ents do not believe in such a thing, but Ferien used to speak of it to me, hoom, toom. Oh, she did!

'If I had not seen you on my return journey, you would surely be dead now. You have Ferien's luck, little Nestinanessornë. You slept for a long time, and will need to sleep longer if you are to be fully healed. What did Ferien used to say to me? "You are not... out of the woods yet...?" Hoom, boom, toom! Imagine that, Nestinanessornë, hm, hm, hm.''You have to... have to let me go, Leafshade.

'My friends need me! Horn... Nona... ${PLAYER}... Gléowine...

'I tried to stand, and walk, but my body... still too weak...''Why should we not burn this grove as a message to the folk of Gondor who live in Anfalas? We have set fire to their ships, but the ships come from elsewhere and are manned by crews selected by the Prince of Dol Amroth and by the King, far away in the White City.

'I say we burn this grove to show they are not safe in their homes. The waves bring us even to their shores, and they are not safe from us.''Nestinanessornë left with them, and sailed away on one of their ships. I did not want to fight, and I am glad, hoom, glad that I did not have to.

'But I hope my friend... is safe. He was not yet fully recovered from his wound, and could not hope to oppose the people of the ships... if it came to fighting.'

Leafshade stares at you with half-lidded eyes. He seems nearly ready to fall asleep once again.Corsairs have raided the grassy hills and fields of Tûm Rost, threatening the village and vineyards of Iáphel with destruction.King Elessar has brought his soldiers to bear against the Corsair raiders that threaten Iáphel.Talk to King Elessar outside IáphelKing Elessar has asked you to go with the Swan-knight Rossaran to drive the Corsairs from northern Iáphel.Talk to the Swan-knight Rossaran in IáphelSearch for Corsairs hiding behind the northern buildings of Iáphel.Find and defeat Corsairs hiding behind the northern buildings of Iáphel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rossaran is waiting to hear your report among the northern buildings of Iáphel.Talk to Rossaran among the northern buildings of IáphelGimli remained in the main square of Iáphel to root Corsair raiders from out of hiding.Talk to Gimli in the main square of IáphelYou and Gimli have caught up with King Elessar by the shore, down the hill from Iáphel.Talk to King Elessar by the shoreKing Elessar has asked you to search along the shoreline for sign of Corsairs that did not take to their boats.King Elessar has asked you to search along the shoreline for sign of Corsairs that did not take to their boats.Search along the shoreline for any sign of hidden CorsairsKing Elessar has asked you to search along the shoreline for sign of Corsairs that did not take to their boats.Search along the shoreline for any sign of hidden CorsairsWhat has brought Orgolas to this place? He was supposed to remain in Ost Arndír!Talk to Orgolas outside his hiding-placeYou should listen to Orgolas's story.Listen to Orgolas explain what befell ThorongilYou should listen to Orgolas's story.Talk to OrgolasKing Elessar wears a thoughtful expression as he waits for you to speak to him.Talk to King Elessar by the shore'This attack is a personal affront to me, ${PLAYER}, for this land is not just under the protection of Lady Nauriel and the Knights of the Green Hills, but it falls also within my purview as the King of Gondor! The people of Iáphel will not be endangered while I still live to prevent it!''Would that I had a company of mounted swan-knights with which to sweep the Corsairs from this place! You and I will have to do, ${PLAYER}, and we must be up to the task. That is the command of the King!'Gwindir, the vintner of Iáphel, sits in a widening red pool and stares at you with glassy eyes, his clothes red-stained. You ask if he is injured, and he shakes his head.

'This is not blood,' he says. 'It is worse! My finest bottles were smashed beyond repair and their contents drained! I pray the King still has the bottles we gifted to him. They are irreplaceable now.'

Gwindir falls silent.'I stayed behind, ${PLAYER}, and I was right to do so: some of the Corsair raiders hid themselves around the square and thought to attack Elessar from the rear. But there may be more! We should follow after him and see if any other villains had the same idea.''I do not fully understand it, ${PLAYER}. The main Corsair ships must be anchored further down the river, for most of the raiders rowed here in secret, piloting small boats. Why then would they set fire to the hillside as they approached Iáphel, giving away their presence before they reached the village that was their destination?'

You suggest to Elessar that perhaps the Corsairs wanted to inspire fear in the hearts of the villagers, and he nods.

'Perhaps that is the answer. Still, it is good to hear that most of the villagers remain unharmed. We drove the Corsairs back to the river and most of them fled in their small ships. They may seek to return once they have licked their wounds, but I think it more likely they will not attack Iáphel again for some time.

'We should search along the shoreline and ensure that no Corsairs remain here in hiding. It is possible we overlooked some of the fleeing pillagers in our charge down the hill.''I'm sorry! I'm sorry!' Orgolas stammers nervously, overcome with fright. 'I told Thorongil it was wrong, and we should not follow the warriors, but he said if we didn't that my father Golasgil would know his heir to be a coward! And I am no coward, ${PLAYER}, but...''The Reaper of the Waves? I think we know this captain, ${PLAYER}.

'Nakási has reason to hate Gondor, and she told you herself that she planned to wreak vengeance upon my kingdom. It would not surprise me to learn she planned to raid every village along the river's edge in Pinnath Gelin, but the abduction of Thorongil caused her to change this plan. He may prove a useful hostage for the Kindred of the Coins.

'But I am getting ahead of myself. Right now we must bring this unwelcome news to Thorongil's mother Nauriel, and then perhaps we can do something to prevent Nakási from escaping Outer Gondor with Thorongil in her custody.''One of the Corsairs, a huge lout with muscles like I have never seen, lifted Thorongil up by one arm and dangled him over the river. "Is this one of those halflings I have heard about?" he asked, and Thorongil spat curses at him and said he was named Thorongil and would have all the Corsairs put to death if they didn't unhand him. They laughed at that, oh, did they ever! I can still hear the laughter, it's terrible!

'But there was something about that name they didn't like. "Thorongil, you say?" the big fellow asked, drawing his sword. I think he would have killed Thorongil then and there, but an Elf among the Corsairs said something to him and his face became like a storm cloud. I couldn't really hear it from where I was hiding, but I think the Elf was saying the captain would want to keep Thorongil onboard her ship.

'The big lout put his sword away and hauled Thorongil onto their boat and they rowed out into the river and then they were gone. I know it was wrong and we shouldn't have come here! But I didn't know how to get out of it, and then it was all over and it was too late! The way they spoke about their captain... it fills me with terror even now!''We are fortunate, my friend. Most of the villagers are unharmed, for the Corsairs set the hillside aflame as they climbed up to the village, and the folk of Iáphel did not delay; they took shelter among these buildings at the first sign of the Corsair approach. Once we have put out the fires, most of the danger should be over.

'Just before you returned, I heard the dwarf Gimli shouting back in the main square. You should ensure he has all in hand; it could be more of the Corsairs hid themselves and thought to do some mischief when our backs were turned.'Loeg Thangalf island, once home to an ancient Elven family, has been overrun by deadly dread-turtles. There are few who would dare their sharp beaks or brave their shores. One such hopeful hero may need a bit of rescuing.Andrethil is frantic with worry over her missing child, Dorach, who she think may have gone to the nearby island to challenge its fierce dread-turtles.

You should head to Loeg Thangalf and look for Dorach.Search for DorachWhile searching Loeg Thangalf you managed to find Dorach, who is eager to speak with you.

Loeg Thangalf is in northern Pinnath Gelin.Talk to DorachYou rescued Dorach, but she's worried about the sword she dropped on the north-eastern part of the Loeg Thangalf. You should retrieve the sword and return it to her.Search for Dorach's swordOn Loeg Thangalf you found a small sword that had been dropped by Dorach.

You should bring the sword to Dorach at Mereham, in central Pinnath Gelin.You have returned Thumb-cleaver to Dorach, and her mother, Andrethil is waiting now to speak with you.

Andrethil is at Mereham in central Pinnath Gelin.Talk to Andrethil'Help! Oh, have you seen my baby? My little girl, Dorach, is missing! That fool of a child is always wandering off pretending to be a knight like her older sister. I only looked away from her for a moment and she was gone!

'Her sword is missing too, and I fear she's gone on to challenge the turtles on Loeg Thangalf. I tried to explain to her that they are enormous, fierce creatures, and not at all the small turtles she's seen in the river nearby, but I fear that made her all the more determined. Oh please find my girl!''You found it! You found Thumb-cleaver! Oh thank you, thank you! I... think I'm going to train a bit closer to home from now on, until I'm at least taller than those turtles.''I wanted to name my sword something fierce, like Foe-cleaver or Goblin-head-lopper, or something. But, the first time I drew it I cut my thumb right badly on its edge and my sister named it Thumb-cleaver on me and even laughed when she bound me up! I miss her. And I miss my sword. I hope you find it soon!''Oh, hullo. Did mother send you? Thanks for clearing a path through those awful turtles. When mother said they were bigger, I never thought… well, I can get home on my own now, but please – I lost my sword! It was a gift from Cangwen, and she always says a knight doesn't leave their sword on the ground, but when the turtles showed up I stabbed at one of them and it got stuck in the shell, and and and…'

She sniffles and wipes at her eyes.

'Please find Thumb-cleaver! I think I ran here from over that way.'

She waves an arm towards the north and swallows.'Words alone cannot express my thanks to you, traveller. I hope she's learned her lesson. I might not be able to keep her from following in Cangwen's footsteps, nor would I want to, but hopefully she'll be more careful going forward.

'There's bravery and then there's… well, this was a learning experience, I suppose. Oh my poor girl, I am so glad she's home safe.'Igerna managed to elude the goblins in a cave where her shredded pack was found and made visits to a couple of the local farmers. She was most recently seen heading north once more, chasing rumours of the goblins' origins, however she has not been seen for a few days.Varbris said that Igerna went north to try to find from whence the goblins have been coming.

You should search the mountains north of Ritherstad in Pinnath Gelin for any signs of goblins or Igerna.Search for IgernaWhilst searching for Igerna, you discovered that goblins have made another camp at the foot of the mountains.

You should continue looking for Igerna in the goblin camp, in northern Pinnath Gelin.Search the camp for IgernaAt the foot of the mountains, a well-carved cave has been allowing the Ronkrúm goblin tribe access to Pinnath Gelin. You should search the cave for Igerna.

The cave is at Krauzhaf, in north-eastern Pinnath Gelin.Search the cave for IgernaIgerna is waiting to speak with you in the goblin cave, in north-eastern Pinnath Gelin.Talk to Igerna'Igerna went north from here, towards the mountains, a few days ago. I hope she's safe and unharmed, but I fear the worst.

'You should head that way if you're still determined to find her.''Happiest of greetings upon you, ${CLASS}! You have no idea how good it is to see a face that's not of goblin-kind. I pray you are friend and not foe?'

You explain that Lúmar sent you and her shoulder slump with relief, but then she winces at some pain in her side.

'Umph, excuse me for not rising, my injury pains me greatly.'You have happened upon a farmer who is offering prizes for completing fishing challenges.Madern has invited you to participate in a fishing contest.

Catch two fish in as many minutes while standing near the designated marker.Catch fat fish (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Before time expiresYou have caught two fish within the time limit.

Talk to Madern on the road between the farm, Wetcroft, and the western bank of Nen Eilen.'Welcome one and all to the most exciting -- and only -- fishing contest in Pinnath Gelin! My name is Madern and it is my joy in life to promote the love of fishing. To that end, I offer prizes to any who can pass my fishing challenges. Are you angler enough to win? Please say yes. I worked so hard on this and no one is participating.

'You are? Excellent! Your first challenge is to run to the lone banner down by the water and catch two fish in two minutes! What are you waiting for? I've already started counting!'Madern claps for you as you, winner that you are.

'You've passed the first challenge! Congratulations. Are you ready for the next one?'You have happened upon a farmer who is offering prizes for completing fishing challenges.Madern has challenged you to catch a beast of a fish along the north-western banks of Pinnath Gelin near a scarecrow.

Catch the mysterious fish.Catch the legendary fishYou have caught an impressive fish.

Talk to Madern on the road between the farm, Wetcroft, and the western bank of Nen Eilen.Madern lowers her voice as if to share a secret.

'For generations, the people of Pinnath Gelin have whispered of a creature that lives in Nen Eilen. They say it was once a fish like any other, but it feasted upon something unnatural, something foul, then it in turn became something unnatural, something foul. It lurks through these blessed waters, waiting for its time to strike.

'Unless of course, a bold angler such as yourself plucks it from the depths.

'There is a scarecrow north of here along the lakeshore towards Ost Arndír. There have been sightings of the beast in the water. Catch it, but be prepared to defend yourself.

'Why a scarecrow you ask? I ran out of banners.'You show her the strange fish you caught.

She takes a minute to study it, occasionally poking it with the back end of a spatula she has lying around.

'It's weird,' she pronounces. 'It's not the legendary fish, but it's big enough and funny to look at. That's worth a prize I think.'

She smiles and hands you your winnings.

'Congratulations my friend. You've passed all the trials I have to offer. Go forth and spread the joy of fishing to every corner of Middle-earth -- the safe corners of Middle-earth. I'm not telling you to go fishing in Mordor!'

She makes herself laugh for a full thirty seconds.

'Wait... you say you've already been there?'You have happened upon a farmer who is offering prizes for completing fishing challenges.The farmer Madern hosts a fishing contest on the western bank of Nen Eilen.

'The fish at the lone banner are eager to bite but are worth only one point.
'The fish at the spot marked by two banners are a bit more shy but are worth two points apiece.
'The fish at the spot marked by three banners are not so easily persuaded to take any sort of bait, but a fish caught there is worth three points!

Catch five points worth of fish in three minutes.Earn points (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Before time expiresYou have caught enough points' worth of fish within the time limit.

