Varbris is at Ritherstad.Return to Varbris'Igerna came through here a few days ago and hasn't returned. She headed off to Ritherstad, even though I tried to warn her that it's been overrun by goblins! Can you believe it? This used to be a quiet place to live.

'I can see in your eyes that you're determined to follow after her. Like Igerna, you seem capable, but, well, I thought she was also and she has yet to return. Good luck, then! Keep your eyes open for Varbris. That fool also refuses to fall back to some place safe and is probably lurking around his farm getting into trouble with the goblins.''Ahaha! You did it! I saw my girls running for the hills. They'll be safer out there for now, and I will remove myself to Ost Arndír to ask for more help. You have my thanks.''Who are you? Have you come to help? Ah, Igerna? Yes, she came through here. She's since moved on to try to find the source of the goblins, leaving me here to defend my farm on my own! Well, truth be told, she directed me to flee to Ost Arndír, but I shan't let my home be overrun!

'What do you say? Will you help me deal a blow to these scum?'

When you agree, Varbris' shoulders slump with relief.

'You have no idea how relieved I am to hear that! Now here's my plan: these goblins are here for my cows! I love these daft girls dearly, but they are far too unworried about our new guests. Go into the fields and give 'em a right good smack right on the rump! They'll run off a ways to safety.'Many dissenters have been imprisoned at Pahor Boha. Upokhir would have you rescue them.Upokhir has asked you to rescue some fellow dissenters in Pahor Boha.

Pahor Boha can be found in the south-east of Pinnath Gelin.You to have rescued the imprisoned warriors within Pahor Boha and should report your success.

Talk to Upokhir in Ost Arndir.Talk to Upokhir'While I was able to escape the camp and come here to seek aid, many of my fellows were not so fortunate. I would ask you to free them. Their imprisonment is unjust, but I also fear they would become hostages when Torthril marches on Pahor Boha.''Thank you for rescuing them. Had any of the other warriors helped them, they would have suffered repercussions.'Torthril has asked you to scout the defences at Pahor Boha.Torthril has asked you to scout the Pahor Boha's entrances.

Pahor Boha can be found in the south-east of Pinnath Gelin.Scout the south-west gateScout the south-east gateYou to have scouted Pahor Boha's defences and should report your success.

Talk to Torthril in Ost Arndír.Talk to Torthril'If we are to mount an assault on the camp, it would be good for us to know its defences. Upokhir has already drawn a detailed map for me, but you are more experienced with fighting alongside Gondorians. As someone familiar with our tactics and strengths, I would appreciate your perspective. Scout Pahor Boha's entrances and report back to me on what you find.''Thank you for report. I will review your findings with my lieutenants and adjust our plans accordingly.'Branach has asked you to exterminate an overgrowth of sickle-flies.Branach has asked you to defeat sickle flies.

The sickle-flies in question can be found to the south-west of Branach's farm, Cornworth.Defeat gelin sickle-flies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have done as Branach asked. Return to him.

Branach can be found at his farm, Cornworth, north-west of Gnatstead.Talk to Branach'Every summer, swarms of sickle-flies plague the coast of the Lagorduin south-west of here. They're awful pests.'

He bares his arm, which sports a row of awful raised welts.

'Their bites and stings are so itchy! This is torture. I would appreciate if you culled some of them.''Thank you for squashing those disgusting pests!'From a hill overlooking a large farm, a woman waits for help recovering her stolen coin.Húrwen has asked you to search for sacks of coin that her father secreted about her farm.

Elbery Farm is located in north-western Pinnath Gelin.Recover buried coins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have recovered multiple sacks of coins from Elbery Farm.

You should bring the sacks of coin to Húrwen, who is waiting on the road west of Elbery, in Pinnath Gelin.'Are you going down to my farm, Elbery? I am Húrwen, and yes, it is mine, but alas it's completely overrun with goblins. I came back to see if they'd moved on, but the wretched things are still there. I wonder if you could help me. When word came that goblins were sighted in the area, my father... well, you see, he's got a troubled mind and I'm afraid he took all the money in our coffers and buried it about the property in an effort to "keep it safe."

'I know I'm taking a big risk here, asking a stranger to recover it for me, but you're my only hope of getting back my coin before the goblins start wondering what's under the freshly dug earth.

'Please, bring me back any coin you find, and I'll give you a share of it in return.''You actually did it! I saw you taking on those wretches too. I had a good feeling about you - glad am I that I trusted my gut! Give them here then, and I shall be sure to keep them away from my dear addled Father.'Igerna has been found alive, but injured and captive. Her freedom must be gained, but the door to her rusted metal cage sits firmly locked.Igerna has asked you to find the key to her cage. She suggests the overseers may be the ones to carry the keys.

Goblin overseers can be found throughout the cave and in Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin.Retrieve the key to Igerna's cageAfter battling through the halls of Krauzhaf, you recovered an iron key that looks like it will fit the lock on Igerna's cage door.

You should unlock Igerna's cage, in the cave at Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin.Unlock Igerna's cageYou have unlocked Igerna's cave, and she is now waiting to speak with you.

Igerna is in a cave in Krauzhaf, in northern Pinnath Gelin.Talk to Igerna'If I could, I would hug you, but the door to my cage is locked tight. I have only seen it unlocked with keys the overseers have. Hunt them down until you find the key.''Freedom! Thank you, my new friend. I have been trapped in there for days.'Elladan and Elrohir will be welcome aboard the Wave-hunter, if they can be convinced to join your crew.Elladan and Elrohir went in search of Corsairs near Iáphel, intending to find any of the raiders who might have hidden after the attack.Find Elladan somewhere in Tûm RostFind Elrohir somewhere in Tûm RostElladan and Elrohir will have returned to Ost Arndír by the time you get there.Talk to Elladan in Ost ArndírElrohir is at Ost Arndír, waiting to speak to you.Talk to Elrohir in Ost Arndír'Queen Arwen's brothers? Aye, they spoke of tracking down Corsairs who might have hidden after the raid upon Tûm Rost. I do not know exactly where they might have gone since, but you should begin your search for them somewhere near Iáphel.''I do not know exactly where the Queen's brothers might have gone since, but you should begin your search for them somewhere near Iáphel.''I tracked a party of Corsairs to this hillside, and I think they are readying their response. Let us face them and ensure the safety of Iáphel!''Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}! I came here in search of Corsairs, but I think they ran afoul of another foe. Be ready for anything!''My brother and I remained behind to deal with the Corsair threat when Elessar left, for we believed the folk of the Green Hills might still be endangered. Grief can render incapable even the stoutest of hearts. That is true even of the Elves!

'I will be pleased to join your crew, ${PLAYER}. I have little love for ships, but for adventure I have a great fondness. Speak to my brother and see if he is of the same mind.''Speak to my brother and see if he is of the same mind.''I went in search of Corsairs and found goblins instead, ${PLAYER}. Will it be the same on our voyage to Umbar? Who knows what unexpected adventures will await us there? I have never been to that land, and I am filled with excitement at the prospect of seeing it for myself!

'I will be pleased to join the crew of the Wave-hunter, my friend. We will be there when the time comes to depart.'Caebar believes Gangur Farwend, the dwarf who warned you about Khôltekh the Cunning during your stay at Furukzahar, might be willing to join your crew.Kutúkh told you that Gangur Farwend mentioned stopping at the outpost of Zarsatrâd to the south before continuing his journey.Find Gangur Farwend at Zarsatrâd, to the south of FurukzaharGangur Farwend is at the outpost of Zarsatrâd, south of Furukzahar.Talk to Gangur Farwend in ZarsatrâdThe dwarves at Zarsatrâd agreed to tell Gangur Farwend something about the strange gemstone he saw at Furukzahar if he aided them by defeating beasts near the outpost, and you agreed to help.Defeat foes of the dwarves near the outpost of Zarsatrâd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gangur Farwend is at the outpost of Zarsatrâd, south of Furukzahar.Talk to Gangur Farwend in ZarsatrâdGangur Farwend stormed from Zarsatrâd after being embarrassed by the dwarves there. It looked to you as if he was heading in the direction of Erynos, but he likely wishes to stay away from people.Find Gangur Farwend somewhere to the south-east of ZarsatrâdGangur Farwend is south-east of Zarsatrâd and north of Erynos, in King's Gondor East.Talk to Gangur Farwend north of Erynos, in King's Gondor East'Do I know where Gangur Farwend went after he left Furukzahar? You are going to have to remind me who that is.'

You tell Kutúkh that he was a Longbeard that departed shortly after the arrival of King Elessar. The dwarf strokes his beard and contemplates your description.

'Yes, I remember him now. Hámisar sent him from the fortress in disgrace, as I recall. You should not waste any time seeking one such as he, for he is a bad penny and will bring you nothing but trouble. If you insist upon it, perhaps so you can make him a better dwarf, I believe he mentioned stopping at Zarsatrâd before continuing his journey. Zarsatrâd is the outpost to the south. Good day to you.''I remember Gangur Farwend now. Hámisar sent him from the fortress in disgrace, as I recall. You should not waste any time seeking one such as he, for he is a bad penny and will bring you nothing but trouble. If you insist upon it, perhaps so you can make him a better dwarf, I believe he mentioned stopping at Zarsatrâd before continuing his journey. Zarsatrâd is the outpost to the south. Good day to you.''Oh, I know you.''Do I know you? I don't have a very good mind for faces.'

You remind Gangur that he warned you about some suspicious dealings within the Temámir fortress of Furukzahar, and he nods.

'Yes, I remember now. I am pleased that my words proved some help to you, although as you can see I am no longer welcome there. Ah, it is fine. I have always been a traveller, and the hospitality of Furukzahar was not especially to my liking.'

He lowers his voice.

'You remember Khôltekh the Cunning? He carried a talisman on his person, and it shone in a very curious way, as if it contained a gem possessing unusual qualities. I have mentioned it to some of the dwarves here, in a roundabout way so as not to give away my interest, and they say they will tell me more if I help eliminate some of the beasts nearby. Would you like to help me accomplish this?''Khôltekh the Cunning carried a talisman on his person, and it shone in a very curious way, as if it contained a gem possessing unusual qualities. I have mentioned it to some of the dwarves here, in a roundabout way so as not to give away my interest, and they say they will tell me more if I help eliminate some of the beasts nearby. Would you like to help me accomplish this?''I told the dwarves here we did as they requested, and they laughed at me! "A special gemstone? What makes you think we would tell an outsider like you anything?" they said! They called me too trusting! Me! Gangur Farwend!'

You try to calm him down and ask if he will be interested in joining your crew, but you have only just brought it up when he interrupts.

'I am not in the mood for conversation, ${PLAYER}! I cannot stay in this place! They are laughing at me even now, behind my back!''Yes?''They laughed at me, ${PLAYER}. Why would they do that? What is it about that gemstone that they do not want to share with outsiders?'

Gangur strokes his beard, deep in thought.

'The Temámir of Furukzahar did not want you to know they were visited by an emissary of the Kindred of the Coins, and they kept the details of what he spoke about a secret from you and from the King of Gondor. Then the Dwarves of Zarsatrâd dodged my questions about the gemstone that emissary carried. Why? What were you saying earlier, ${PLAYER}? Something about a voyage?'

You tell Gangur, once again, about your mission to Umbar and your desire for him to join your crew. This time he thinks it over.

'I have come a long way from my home already... what is another hundred miles, even if those carry me across the Bay? The answers I seek may lie in Umbar with the Kindred of the Coins. I will join you, ${PLAYER}! I must learn about the unusual gem carried by Khôltekh the Cunning, and the reasons for his folk to maintain such secrecy when asked about it! I will be there when you begin your voyage!'Caebar has an interest in learning more about Leafshade, and while the Ent is unlikely to join your crew, perhaps he will know of something that might be of use to you.Leafshade thinks an old sailor might have sailed away with his friend Gwallang, a songbird of the Limlinn species. If you could find him, Leafshade's whistle will apparently remind the bird from where he came.Find Leafshade's friend Gwallang the LimlinnSirgon is in his manor's room of keepsakes.Talk to Sirgon in his room of keepsakes about the caged songbirdThe caged songbird at the far end of Sirgon's room of keepsakes may be Gwallang.The caged songbird certainly appeared to recognize the whistle. Sirgon has given you permission to open the cage and free the bird.Open the cage and free the songbird in Sirgon's room of keepsakesLeafshade the Ent is in Tumbamálë, in south-western Anfalas.Talk to Leafshade in TumbamálëGwallang is in Tumbamálë, and apparently wants to tell you something.Talk to Gwallang the Limlinn in TumbamálëLeafshade is in Tumbamálë.Talk to Leafshade in Tumbamálë'Hrum, hoom... you have come back again, little one? Have you returned to Tumbamálë to bring me news of Nestinanessornë?'

You tell Leafshade that you are looking for crew-members to sail with you to Umbar, and you hope to rescue both Nestinanessornë and the young heir of Pinnath Gelin from the Kindred of the Coins. Leafshade exhales heavily, shaking the leaves of his grove.

'Hoooooooom...'

When the leaves finally settle, Leafshade speaks again.

'I do not like boats, hoom, toom. My friend Nestinanessornë sailed away on one such vessel, but it is not the first time I have lost a companion to the branches-that-float. Another friend of mine, Gwallang the Limlinn, built a nest here in Tumbamálë, but a wooden boat passed nearby and he flew over to it. He never, hoom, never came back. Ferien told me long ago that sailors sometimes take birds with them on their voyages. Perhaps it was the same with Gwallang.'

Leafshade slowly extends a long arm down to you. After a moment you realize he is holding a small wooden whistle.

'If you find Gwallang... blow this whistle and remind him of Tumbamálë. It may be he has, hrum, forgotten.''I do not like boats, hoom, toom. A friend of mine, Gwallang the Limlinn, built a nest here in Tumbamálë, but a wooden boat passed nearby and he flew over to it. He never, hoom, never came back. Ferien told me long ago that sailors sometimes take birds with them on their voyages. Perhaps it was the same with Gwallang. If you find him... blow the whistle I gave you and remind him of Tumbamálë. It may be he has, hrum, forgotten.''What is it, my friend? Ask me anything and it shall be yours.'

You ask Sirgon how he came to possess the songbird caged at the far end of his room of keepsakes.

'Oh, it was years ago, now. I sailed to speak with my friend Belondor of Langstrand about some matter or another, I confess that I cannot bring it so easily to mind. He is dead now, drowned among the Shield Isles; a story for another time! But I do remember that as we sailed along the coast of Anfalas, that bird flew across the water to my vessel and settled upon one of the ropes! He was a boisterous little fellow! At first I thought he was there for the fish my crew had caught that day, but he quite ignored them. He stayed on the ship for that entire voyage, and as he did not disturb any of the crew I kept him onboard for other journeys as well. Now he keeps me company here at home.'

You tell Sirgon about the possibility that the songbird might be Gwallang, a friend of Leafshade, and that the Ent gave you a whistle to call him home.

'Oh, I see. I will miss the little fellow, but I do not want to keep him a prisoner here if he wishes to be elsewhere! Well do I know what it is to be kept from the place where sings your heart! Go to him and blow the whistle; perhaps he will stay here, but if he does not I will be pleased to set him free.''I will miss the little fellow, if he is the friend of this Leafshade, but I do not want to keep him a prisoner here if he wishes to be elsewhere! Well do I know what it is to be kept from the place where sings your heart! Go to him and blow the whistle; perhaps he will stay here, but if he does not I will be pleased to set him free.''He did seem to recognize the whistle? Then by all means set him free, my friend.''I hope my little friend has found freedom and happiness. I enjoyed my time with him, and the sound of his song.''You found my friend Gwallang, ${PLAYER}, hoom, toom, boom!

'He has quite a story to tell, hm, hm!''He would like to speak to you, hoom, toom.'Gwallang jumps around, chirping and trilling. After several minutes of this, Leafshade rumbles in satisfaction and calls you over to him.Gwallang trills a lovely song.'Hm, hm, hm. My friend Gwallang the Limlinn says that he misses travelling, and his happiest days were spent accompanying Sirgon the Sailor on his voyages. Hoom! Happier than spending time with me?'

Gwallang trills for a moment, and then Leafshade continues.

'He says he was very disappointed when Sirgon left the seafaring life behind him, hoom. He desires to accompany you, if you will have him. Hm, hm! Perhaps when your voyages are done, my friend will return to Tumbamálë? But until then he desires to go with you.'King Elessar suggested that you recruit the Lady Nauriel for the mission to Umbar.Nauriel's sword and shield have been made ready for the voyage, and can be found on the lowest level of Ost Arndír.Retrieve Nauriel's sword from the armoury in Ost ArndírRetrieve Nauriel's shield from the armoury in Ost ArndírNauriel's husband Carandolion is on the lowest level of Ost Arndír.Nauriel is in the main hall, on the upper level of Ost Arndír.'Every day that passes brings my son further into danger, ${PLAYER}. There must be no more delay.

'I will join the crew of the Wave-hunter so I may ask the Kindred of the Coins to return Thorongil, but I will ask only once. If they refuse I will bloody my sword and dent my shield on their carcasses! They have remained unused for too long, anyway. My husband Carandolion always speaks of the need for patience, and for thinking things through, but see where that has gotten us! Our son stolen away by enemies of Gondor! Well, they have made an enemy of Nauriel, and she does not forgive as readily as Gondor. Recruit the crew you think we will need for the voyage, ${PLAYER}, but remember the need I have for haste.

'Will you retrieve my sword and shield from the armoury on the lower level? I have had the sword sharpened and the shield reinforced since the Corsairs raided Tûm Rost, and they should now be ready for me.''Will you retrieve my sword and shield from the armoury on the lower level? I have had the sword sharpened and the shield reinforced since the Corsairs raided Tûm Rost, and they should now be ready for me.''My husband was looking for you. Return to the lowest level and find him.''I am no fighter, ${PLAYER}, but that does not mean I do not want my son safely returned to his home. My wife has always been the firebrand, and she has temper enough for the both of us! But she matches it, nay, she exceeds it, with her martial skill. There are none more deadly in all the Green Hills with a blade than she!

'I am unlike my brother, you know. Duinhir rode to Minas Tirith with trumpets and banners, and when he came back he did so without his sons, for they were of fighting age. My Thorongil was not, but he has been taken away all the same, and now I must rely upon my dangerous wife to retrieve him. Do I risk losing them both? These are the thoughts that keep me awake at night, ${PLAYER}.

'I will remain here to oversee Pinnath Gelin while Nauriel is away, but my thoughts will sail alongside her as she rides the waves to Umbar. I will give her a favour to carry into battle, so she knows her husband's heart goes with her.''I will remain here to oversee Pinnath Gelin while Nauriel is away, but my thoughts will sail alongside her as she rides the waves to Umbar. I will give her a favour to carry into battle, so she knows her husband's heart goes with her.''Thank you for bringing me my equipment, ${PLAYER}, and for speaking with my husband. I will carry his favour into battle on behalf of our son Thorongil, should battle prove necessary. My husband would be the first to tell you he is no fighter, but I love him all the more for it. I do our fighting for us, and without regret.

'Carandolion will see that Pinnath Gelin does not suffer in my absence, and when I return I will return with our son, and only his father will celebrate more loudly and happily than I.

'I will await your command, and the rest of your crew, at the Wave-hunter.'King Elessar suggested that you recruit Corudan's sister Sigileth for the mission to Umbar.If you really expect Sigileth to pass through the Paths of the Dead, you should look for her on the road to the Dark Door, north of Morlad in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor West.Look for Sigileth somewhere on the road to the Dark Door, north of Morlad in King's Gondor WestThe Swan-knight Rovalang stands by the road to the Dark Door, in King's Gondor West.Talk to Rovalang by the road to the Dark Door in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor WestThe Swan-knight Rovalang asked for your help making safe the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor West.Defeat foes in the Blackroot Vale, King's Gondor West (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Swan-knight Rovalang stands by the road to the Dark Door, in King's Gondor West.Talk to Rovalang by the road to the Dark Door in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor WestSomeone approaches from the direction of the Dark Door.Wait for the newcomer to arriveSigileth has come to the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor West, in search of her brother Corudan.Talk to Sigileth on the road to the Dark Door in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor WestThe Swan-knight Rovalang stands by the road to the Dark Door, in King's Gondor West.Talk to Rovalang by the road to the Dark Door in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor West'I am pleased to see you again, ${PLAYER}. King Elessar sent word that he will come in person to the Blackroot Vale after all, and I believe I have you to thank for that. It is important for the folk of Morlad and the wider Vale to see their king. But what brings you here now?'

You ask Duinhir if an Elf-warrior named Sigileth has come to Morlad, and he says that he has not seen anyone by that name or description come from the south. You shake your head, and tell the Lord of the Blackroot Vale that Sigileth would likely come from the north. He marvels at you in surprise.

'From the north? Does that mean you expect this Elf-warrior to come through the Paths of the Dead? I have not seen her, at any rate. If you go to the Dark Door perhaps you will intercept her on her way, but I find this hard to believe.''You really expect this Elf-warrior to come through the Paths of the Dead? I have not seen her, at any rate. If you go to the Dark Door perhaps you will intercept her on her way, but I find this hard to believe.''Greetings to you.''What brings you once again to the Blackroot Vale, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Rovalang that you are waiting for a friend to arrive, and you plan to ask her to join your crew on a secret mission to Umbar. The swan-knight nods, and looks as if he has some questions to ask. Then he smiles.

'I will not press you any further on this, my friend, for a secret mission should remain secret, no matter how intriguing it may be for me to hear more of it! While you wait for your friend to arrive, perhaps you will help me with my own task? I have been ordered to make safe the Blackroot Vale, and I could use your help with that, as before and as always!''While you wait for your friend to arrive, perhaps you will help me with my own task? I have been ordered to make safe the Blackroot Vale, and I could use your help with that, as before and as always!''Thank you, my friend. It is always a pleasure to work alongside you!

'But wait... someone comes!''This is quite a tale!''I did not expect to see you on the road, ${PLAYER}. I would have found you, just as we will now find my brother Corudan!'

You ask Sigileth if she truly passed through the Paths of the Dead on her way to the Blackroot Vale, and she looks at you quizzically.

'I am no stranger to places of evil, my friend; my stay beneath the dungeons of Dol Guldur has seen to that. I was untroubled by the Paths of the Dead; any of the spirits that still dwell beneath the Mountain chose not to hinder my passage... a wise choice. Now, tell me what you have learned of Corudan's whereabouts. Time is wasting.'

You tell Sigileth, briefly, of what you know of her brother's captivity by Nakási Wave-reaper and the Kindred of the Coins, and of your plan to rescue him.

'Your ship is docked at a lake to the west? I will meet you there, and sail with you to Umbar. My brother will be freed from captivity and death, just as I was when you thought me dead on the stairs of Dol Guldur. Let us not delay.''I will meet you at your ship when the time comes to depart.''This sounds like quite the adventure, ${PLAYER}! I would go with you, but I am commanded by my Prince to make safe the Vale, and I have never desired to do other than that.

'Good fortune go with you on your voyage, my friend. I hope you accomplish all that you set out to do.'King Elessar suggested that you recruit Legolas and Gimli for the mission to Umbar.Elestren has a home in Melgobas and may know how to make a sea-sickness remedy for Gimli.Talk to Elestren in MelgobasLangstrand wild-flowers can be found north of Melgobas, in the grass alongside the road. Crawlers, oxen, and crabs can be found outside the village.Collect Langstrand wild-flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect beast parts from crawlers, crabs, or oxen near Melgobas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Elestren has a home in Melgobas and is waiting for you to return to her with the flowers and beast parts she requested.Legolas is outside the home of Elestren in Melgobas.Talk to Legolas in Melgobas'I know why you are here, my friend, and of course I will agree to sail with you into danger! I hope you did not expect me to refuse! But I have set foot upon one too many boats for my liking in these past few months, ${PLAYER}. I simply do not like them. Show me a dwarf who does and I will be very surprised!

'The folk hereabout say that the Bay is generally calm... generally... but I know that even the calmest waters can shake a boat to its very foundation. Do I say foundation? A boat has no such thing, and tosses and turns at the merest whim of the waves! Sea-sickness is a concern, friend.

'Legolas inquired on my behalf, seeking a remedy for it, and learned that an herbalist in Melgobas may prepare a suitable concoction. Will you go there and see if it is ready, and you may also ask the Elf if he desires to join your crew as well. I assume he will, but you should ask him yourself.''Legolas inquired on my behalf, seeking a remedy for it, and learned that an herbalist in Melgobas may prepare a suitable concoction. Will you go there and see if it is ready, and you may also ask the Elf if he desires to join your crew as well. I assume he will, but you should ask him yourself.''A sea-sickness remedy? You are the second person to ask for such a concoction today. The first was an Elf, and I will tell you what I told him: the effectiveness of such an elixir varies depending upon the person who takes it, and what works for one may not work for another. I do not give back the purchase price in the event you are dissatisfied!

'I sent the Elf to collect some Langstrand flowers and beast parts from the creatures hereabout, and while he has not yet returned, if you perform the same task as he the work may be finished more quickly. I make use of parts from crawlers, aurochs, and crabs in the various unguents and potions I create, and will appreciate any you bring back to me.''I sent the Elf to collect some Langstrand flowers and beast parts from the creatures hereabout, and while he has not yet returned, if you perform the same task as he the work may be finished more quickly. I make use of parts from crawlers, oxen, and crabs in the various unguents and potions I create, and will appreciate any you bring back to me.''Thank you for bringing me these; they will not all be used in the same mixture, but I assure you they will all be used in something! Your friend returned shortly before you did, and I have given him the sea-sickness remedy I promised. I give to you the same warning I gave him: it may not have the desired effect upon the dwarf for whom it is intended! It truly does vary based on the individual, and if it does not work as you expect it is not a failing of the potion, or of she who brewed it!

'But I hope it does help him. Sea-sickness is not a pleasant thing for anyone.''I hope my remedy does help your dwarf friend. Sea-sickness is not a pleasant thing for anyone.''I hope possession of this remedy will ease the turmoil of Gimli's stomach when the Wave-hunter sets out! He may not even need to ingest it, if he knows it is near-at-hand and might be taken if necessary. I will not tell him of the chance that it will do nothing, unless he asks directly. I will not lie to my friend, but this information can do no good in advance and may instead do harm.

'There was no need for you to come all this way to speak with me, ${PLAYER}! I of course will join you on your mission. The sea-longing has me and will not abate, but I understand the Wave-hunter will remain in the Bay and not pass out into the Great Sea. There are still things for me to see and to do before I begin that last voyage, and I count high in that number aiding you in the rescue of young Thorongil from the clutches of the Kindred of the Coins.

'I will be pleased to join your crew, my friend. Both I and Gimli will meet you by the Wave-hunter when you are ready to depart.'King Elessar suggested that you recruit the Corsair Jajax, if you think he can be trusted to help.Prince Imrahil's scouts reported seeing Jajax near Abadec's Watch to the south-east of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor West.Find Jajax at Abadec's Watch, south-east of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor WestJajax stands outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West.Talk to Jajax outside Abadec's WatchYour rescue of Daxamat from Abadec's Watch will require you to defeat the Corsairs camped inside.Defeat Corsairs inside Abadec's Watch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Daxamat is being held prisoner inside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West.Free Daxamat inside Abadec's WatchYou have freed Daxamat from his bonds.Wait for Daxamat to escapeJajax stands outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West.Talk to Jajax outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor WestDaxamat stands outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West.Talk to Daxamat outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor WestJajax stands outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West.Talk to Jajax outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West'I did not expect you to return to Dol Amroth so quickly, ${PLAYER}. And where is the King?'

You tell Prince Imrahil about Nakási Wave-reaper's raid upon the Green Hills and her seizure of young Thorongil. When you speak of King Elessar's suggestion that you assemble a crew to rescue the heir of Pinnath Gelin, the Prince grasps the hilt of his sword.

'I can leave at once. You have but to say the word and I will voyage with you to Umbar Baharbêl, the City of Sails! The Kindred of the Coins will not stand long against us, for they will know my face and my reputation! But... you are not here to recruit me for your mission, are you? I can tell from your expression that the King wishes this to be a more secret quest. Yes, I see the need for it. I apologize for getting carried away. Who does the King suggest?'

You say that you are considering the Corsair Jajax for your crew, and the Prince is overcome by a coughing fit.

'What? Tell me you are not serious about this, ${PLAYER}! This Jajax is a Corsair, and will betray you at the first opportunity, if he has not already! My scouts report that he has gone in the direction of Abadec's Watch, south-east of Dol Amroth, likely to meet with those of his fellows encamped there. They are a danger to Gondor, and always will be! I hope you know what you are doing. If the King believes this is the right course I will not speak against it.''This Jajax is a Corsair, and will betray you at the first opportunity, if he has not already! My scouts report that he has gone in the direction of Abadec's Watch, south-east of Dol Amroth, likely to meet with those of his fellows encamped there. They are a danger to Gondor, and always will be! I hope you know what you are doing. If the King believes this is the right course I will not speak against it.''Look who has turned up!''Well look who turned up, and just in time!

'I have learned what happened to Dax, my friend, and I was just about to go inside and rescue him... but now that you are here I see the blessing of happy chance is upon me! I have always been one of the lucky ones, ${PLAYER}; that is why I have lived so long!

'Now get in there, kill his captors, and keep my brother alive. We'll talk once you've done that... and not before.''Now get in there, kill his captors, and keep my brother alive. We'll talk once you've done that... and not before.''Are you here to help?''${PLAYER}! Are you here to rescue me? Please say that is what brings you here, for otherwise I fear I might die bound to this post, and that would make my brother very displeased, I am sure of it!'

You tell Daxamat that Jajax waits for him outside Abadec's Watch, and untie him.

'Thank you for this! I will not forget it!''I told you I was lucky, ${PLAYER}. All I had to do was wait, and you rescued my brother for me! How very fortunate. The stars truly smile upon Jajax... they always have, and they always will! Now what brought you in search of me?'

You tell Jajax that you are assembling a crew to sail to Umbar to rescue the kidnapped heir of Pinnath Gelin from the Kindred of the Coins, and you want him to join you. When you have finished, Jajax laughs, but his laughter is free of mirth.

'Why would I do this? What could you possibly offer to me that would make it worth my while to return to Umbar while it is under the control of the Kindred? I told you what happened when Dax and I returned there! No. My answer is no. You will sail to Umbar without us.''No. My answer is no.''Wait.'

Daxamat stares off into the distance, as if gathering his courage.

'I will join you, ${PLAYER}, if you will have me. I fear the Kindred of the Coins, but I fear the Heirs of Castamir more, and they still have supporters throughout these lands; the Corsairs here in Abadec's Watch belong to that number. They imprisoned me as a traitor to the Heirs, and would do so again if given the chance.

'My brother says he is the lucky one, but I think in recent days I have had the best fortune in our family, for your path brought you here to rescue me. I cannot be certain you will be near the next time, unless I go with you on your ship. Count me among your crew, ${PLAYER}.''I will join your crew, ${PLAYER}. I will be there when the voyage begins.''So that is the way of it, Dax?'

Jajax scowls at you.

'My brother has always been one who follows, ${PLAYER}. First he served Balakhôr the Scourge as a deckhand on the Night-jewel, and then he served Azgarzôr his brother until we slew him, and only then! Always Dax needs someone to tell him what to do! Well, I am different.'

The Corsair's scowl deepens.

'Jajax is a captain, not a crew-member! He gives the commands! He is the one who leads!'

Jajax shakes his head at his brother and gives you a curt wave with one hand.

'This is where we part ways, ${PLAYER}. I will find a crew and a ship of my own. May my brother serve you better than he served the Heirs of Castamir! Without me to keep him in line, I believe your ship will be doomed. A pity, that! A pity! Farewell.'Caebar believes the merchant Galengam might prove a useful member of the crew, if he can be convinced to join your cause.Galengam's notices can be found throughout Calembel, in King's Gondor West.Collect Galengam's notices throughout Calembel, in King's Gondor West (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The brazier by the southern entrance to Calembel, in King's Gondor West, will be an effective way to dispose of Galengam's notices.Bandron, standing nearby, has attracted your attention.Talk to Bandron by the brazier in Calembel, in King's Gondor WestGalengam is inside his shop in Calembel, in King's Gondor West.Talk to Galengam inside his shop in Calembel, in King's Gondor West'Well now, this is quite a surprise! What brings you back to Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, ${PLAYER}? Did the King come with you? I saw an increase in visitors to my shop after his previous visit, and I look forward to any future return he might make!'

You tell Galengam the purpose of your visit: that you are recruiting crew-members for a dangerous journey to Umbar so you may rescue the kidnapped heir of the Green Hills. The merchant adjusts the hat upon his head.

'Ah, I see why you have come to me. Who else would have the extensive knowledge of provisions and supply necessary for such a voyage? But what would be my payment for providing such a service? Answer not so quickly! I have the answer: this will permit me to open up new markets across the Bay! What new goods will I be able to acquire? The mind truly reels at the possibilities!

'I accept! There is one small complication, however. I had some of my workers put papers up all over town advertising my status as the King's Own Merchant and detailing the movement of my shop to Minas Tirith, but if I am to join you on your ship I will not be able to make the move just yet. The posters must come down! Burn them in a brazier here in Calembel after you have removed them. I cannot join your crew until this is done!''There is one small complication. I had some of my workers put papers up all over town advertising my status as the King's Own Merchant and detailing the movement of my shop to Minas Tirith, but if I am to join you on your ship I will not be able to make the move just yet. The posters must come down! Burn them in a brazier here in Calembel after you have removed them. I cannot join your crew until this is done!''I had some of my workers put papers up all over town advertising my status as the King's Own Merchant and detailing the movement of my shop to Minas Tirith, but if I am to join you on your ship I will not be able to make the move just yet. The posters must come down! Burn them in a brazier here in Calembel after you have removed them. I cannot join your crew until this is done!''Excuse me, I could not help but notice that you have gone and burned up all the notices my son and I were ordered to put up around town. It took us all morning to do, and now you've gone and ruined all that work! What is the meaning of... the meaning of...'

The man pauses.

'${PLAYER}? It IS you! It has been a long time since our paths crossed! I did not expect to see you again, let alone for you to work at cross-purposes to me and my son! Galengam had us putting up those notices to advertise that his shop will be moving to Minas Tirith. Why have you taken them down?'

You tell Bandron that Galengam will be sailing with you to Umbar, and therefore his other plans have been halted for now. The waggon-driver's eyes light up, and despite his age he dances a merry jig on the cobblestones.

'What wonderful tidings you bring! My son will be delighted to hear it as well: at last we will have a break from Galengam's orders! He is always sending us all over Gondor, ${PLAYER}, with nary a rest in-between each journey. Do you think you could make this voyage take as long as possible, and give my boy and I a true holiday? Endless thanks to you, my friend!''What wonderful tidings you bring! My son will be delighted to hear it as well: at last we will have a break from Galengam's orders! He is always sending us all over Gondor, ${PLAYER}, with nary a rest in-between each journey. Do you think you could make this voyage take as long as possible, and give my boy and I a true holiday? Endless thanks to you, my friend!''You have removed all the notices? Good, good! There are new markets to discover and new goods to acquire, and when we do return I shall become even more profitable than I had previously expected!

'It will be an honour to profit from your mission, ${PLAYER}! I mean, it will be an honour to aid you with the provisions you need to conduct a successful voyage. I will be ready when you are set to depart, my auspicious friend!'King Elessar suggested that you recruit Sirgon, former Lord of Lebennin, for the mission to Umbar.Sirgon already packed his trunk, and he wants you to carry it to him from the southern dining room.Pick up Sirgon's trunk in the southern dining roomSirgon is inside his keepsake room in the northern part of his manor.Talk to Sirgon inside his room of keepsakesCelebros and Faltharan are in Sirgon's manor, and will want to speak to you.Talk to Faltharan in Sirgon's manorTalk to Celebros in Sirgon's manorSirgon is inside his keepsake room in the northern part of his manor.Talk to Sirgon inside his room of keepsakes'You return from your tour of Gondor with the King, and so quickly? What brings you back to my manor with such haste, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Sirgon of what befell young Thorongil of Pinnath Gelin, and of the mission to bring him safely back from Umbar. His eyes light up and he eagerly grasps your hand.

'I will be delighted to join your crew, my friend! I confess to you that thoughts of the Sea have occupied my dreams, and even my waking thoughts have dwelt upon it! Ever since I spoke with King Elessar and stepped down as the Lord of Lebennin I have desired to sail once again! My son Faltharan will take up the charge of rebuilding the vessels of the Gondorian navy; he is already well-acquainted with what must be done.

'I have a further confession: I have already packed my trunk, hoping beyond hope that a ship would have need of an old sailor for its crew. By the Valar, it has come to pass! Will you bring the trunk in here for me? It is in the southern dining room of my manor.''I have already packed my trunk, hoping beyond hope that a ship would have need of an old sailor for its crew. By the Valar, it has come to pass! Will you bring the trunk in here for me? It is in the southern dining room of my manor.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}! Tell me about the ship we will be sailing to Umbar! Ah, it has been too long!'

You tell Sirgon what you know about the Wave-hunter, little as it is, and he nods eagerly.

'Golasgil of Anfalas was a mariner of great skill and ability. I knew him well, and we sailed together more than once. I believe he was as I am: a man of the Sea, but one whose duties called him away from the waves, to his great regret. I remember him fondly. It is right that his prized vessel will bear us to Umbar on the King's mission.

'My wife and son will want to speak to you. They think I am too old to be of use, but I tell you they are wrong.''My wife and son want to speak to you. They think I am too old to be of use, but I tell you they are wrong.''I understand you will sail with my father to Umbar on a mission of some secrecy, ${PLAYER}? No, I do not ask for any of the details. I think I have expected him to depart ever since I agreed to take over his duties as Lord of Lebennin. At least this seems to be on the King's behalf; my mother told me privately that she feared my father might sneak aboard a merchant ship and vanish in the night, just to set sail again. I do not think he would go so far... but it is better this way, I think.

'Do what you can to keep him safe, my friend. He is not the man he was in his youth, when he freely sailed the Bay of Belfalas at the Steward's command, and challenged Corsair ships among the waves.''My husband believes he is still the same man he was when he commanded the fleets of Gondor, but it is not so. Time marches onward, and while his mind is as sharp as ever it was, my Sirgon has lived long since those days.'

You ask Celebros if she wishes for you to withdraw your request, and she shakes her head.

'I do not ask this of you, for I know he can be of great help to you and to King Elessar; I do not say he should remain behind, for I believe it would do him an injury, ${PLAYER}. Aye, being left behind while others sail again on such an urgent mission would deal him a grave hurt, perhaps his last.

'He is a sailor, my Sirgon, and he has always been a sailor. He must go with you. But do keep a watchful eye on him, ${PLAYER}. I do worry, even as I know he cannot stay.''I will continue to perform my duties as Lord of Lebennin while my father sails with you on your voyage. Please return him safely at the end of your mission, ${PLAYER}!''Please watch out for my husband on your voyage. I do worry, even as I know he cannot stay.''It will be just like the old days, ${PLAYER}, when I sailed the waves and risked life and limb against the harsh elements! Oh, you never feel so alive as when you stand on the deck of a ship; any mariner will tell you so!

'I will meet you beside the Wave-hunter when you are ready to depart. I look forward to meeting the rest of your crew, my friend! Together we will rescue young Thorongil, and no Corsair shall prevent us... and live!'The Swan-knight Rossaran will be a good addition to the crew of the Wave-hunter, if his wife Bruidis can be convinced to permit it.The Swan-knight Rossaran left Tadrent heading north-east.Talk to Rossaran north-east of Tadrent, in King's Gondor WestWild-flowers grow in the camp of Makham Mijann, north of Tadrent, in King's Gondor West.Collect Belfalas wild-flowers from the camp of Makham Mijann (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Swan-knight Rossaran is just outside the eastern entrance of Makham Mijann, in King's Gondor West.Rossaran's wife Bruidis is at Tadrent, in King's Gondor West, and she will have the final word on whether her husband joins the crew of the Wave-hunter.Talk to Bruidis at Tadrent, in King's Gondor WestThe Swan-knight Rossaran is at Tadrent in King's Gondor West, preparing for the voyage.Talk to Rossaran at Tadrent, in King's Gondor West'Greetings to you, ${PLAYER}. There is, as always, much work to be done here!

'You seek my husband Rossaran? I believe he departed Tadrent and headed to the north-east. Look for him there if you wish to speak with him.''You seek my husband Rossaran? I believe he departed Tadrent and headed to the north-east. Look for him there if you wish to speak with him.''What brings you back to these lands, ${PLAYER}? I believed you would spend longer than this in Outer Gondor with the King.'

You tell Rossaran what befell young Thorongil in Pinnath Gelin, and of the Wave-hunter's need for a loyal crew to rescue him. The swan-knight rubs his chin, thinking deeply.

'I want to serve my King in this, ${PLAYER}, but I have only just returned to my wife Bruidis after being long away. I do not think she will be pleased if I leave her again so soon!

'Perhaps you will help me gather some flowers for a bouquet? I will present them to her and she may be agreeable to this plan. I will, however, defer to her judgement in this, no matter what decision she arrives at. She is my wife, and I will not defy her wishes. You must understand, my friend.

'I have seen wild-flowers growing throughout the camp of Makham Mijann, just to the west.''Perhaps you will help me gather some flowers for a bouquet? I will present them to her and she may be agreeable to this plan. I will, however, defer to her judgement in this, no matter what decision she arrives at. She is my wife, and I will not defy her wishes. You must understand, my friend.

'I have seen wild-flowers growing throughout the camp of Makham Mijann, just to the west.''Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}. I will go now to Tadrent and speak with my wife, and if she is in a warm mood perhaps she will permit me to join your crew. You should follow along afterwards and see if we were successful in this.

'If she does not permit it, I must refuse your offer. I hope you understand.''I will go now to Tadrent and speak with my wife, and if she is in a warm mood perhaps she will permit me to join your crew. You should follow along afterwards and see if we were successful in this.''You! ${PLAYER}!'

Bruidis holds your gaze with her eyes, but before you can speak any words in your defence, she laughs.

'My husband Rossaran came here moments ago with a bouquet of flowers, thinking that would be enough for me to say he can sail away with you to Umbar, a fool on some other fool's errand. Aye, I say "fool," for I know my dear Rossaran: he is brave and courageous, but he does not think things through as he should. For example: he believed a bouquet of flowers would so warm my heart that I would allow him to leave my side again, and so soon after he returned from the War! Can there be any other word for that than fool?'

You apologize to Bruidis for asking her husband to join the crew of the Wave-hunter, and she looks at you curiously.

'I did not say he could not join your crew, ${PLAYER}. I said he could not leave my side. That is why I am coming with you! Even now I have sent him to collect some supplies for the journey. Speak to him and see what he thinks of this; I believe you will find he is agreeable.''I did not say he could not join your crew, ${PLAYER}. I said he could not leave my side. That is why I am coming with you! Even now I have sent him to collect some supplies for the journey. Speak to him and see what he thinks of this; I believe you will find he is agreeable.''You came here for one crew-member, ${PLAYER}, but now you have two! To speak truthfully, I think my wife Bruidis may be a better addition to the crew than I, myself! She is a master of strategy and brilliant in tactical matters. In fact, I believe she made only a single mistake in her lifetime to this point, ${PLAYER}... marrying me! But I am glad for it.

'We will be there when the Wave-hunter begins its voyage.'Pesky birds are feasting on wine grapes in Iáphel.Miruhir has asked you to shoo away birds that are eating valuable wine grapes at his vineyard in Iáphel.

Shoo away birds.You should tell Miruhir that you have shooed the birds away.

Miruhir can be found in Iáphel.Talk to Miruhir'I have a sickle-fly problem and a bird problem. You would think the birds would eat the sickle-flies for me but no, that would be too convenient.

'The crows have seen fit to roost amongst the trellises along the western slope of the hill, just outside Iáphel's walls. Please shoo them away for me.''I know they will be back tomorrow, but thank you all the same.'In a newly blasted cave, you found a pack, shredded and rumpled, on the floor. Could it belong to the missing scout? Its contents may shed some much needed light upon her whereabouts.Lúmar has asked you to search through the shredded pack that you found for any information that might tie it to Igerna.

You can search through the pack on the table next to Lúmar, in Ost Arndir.You should search through the pack for clues.

The pack is on the table next to Lúmar, in Ost Arndír.Search the packYou should continue searching through the pack for clues.

The pack is on the table next to Lúmar, in Ost Arndír.Continue searching the packWhile searching through Igerna's pack, you found a hastily scrawled note addressed to Lúmar. You should read the note.

The note is on the table next to Lúmar, in Ost Arndír.Read the hastily scrawled noteLúmar is waiting to speak with you about what was written on the note you found.

Lúmar is in Ost Arndír.Speak to Lúmar'The pack you brought looks familiar to the one Igerna uses. Will you search through it to see if you can find anything of import? You can use the table here to do so.''I fear Igerna has been captured or assaulted, given the state of this bag. What did you find?'Lúmar,

I was right, there are goblins in Pinnath Gelin! They've been hounding me for hours, but I managed to slip their grasp thus far. I overheard one mentioning a farm with lots of four legged, spotted, dinners walking around. I can only imagine this is referring to Varbris's poor cows. I must go first to Winbury and see what fate has befallen Nordach. I will leave this message with - wait, something draws near

---

The message abruptly cuts off.With local farms under various forms of attack, wine makers in Pinnath Gelin have had to become resourceful in their methods.Leithiel has asked you to distract a swarm of bees with some honey. You should pick up the jar of honey.

The honey is next to Leithiel at Bergraw in Pinnath Gelin.Pick up the honey potYou should place the honeypot a ways away from the barrel of grapes.

A good spot for the honeypot can be found at Bergraw in Pinnath Gelin.Place the honeypotCollect yeastYou should bring the yeast you've collected to Leithiel at her vineyard in Pinnath Gelin.'Hello and welcome to Bergraw! We produce Pinnath Gelin's prized Calengaran. Bottles were sent up to the table of the king and his lady themselves for the wedding! Have you tried it?

'Yes, we pride ourselves on our wine, however this season's batches are in serious peril. So much has been going strangely lately on our Green Hills. Talk of goblins and Southrons. Something happened to Cornworth Farm and I haven't been able to get yeast from them for months! I've had to make due with yeast made from our very own grapes. It'll change the flavour, but will still be Bergraw worthy, of course. Only problem is, I can't get near the barrel the yeast is growing in to collect it! One bee sting could mean my death – my own gran had her throat close up because of it, many years back. We've all been careful since.

'Maybe you can help. I have some honey to distract the bees with, but you'll have to be quick! Take up that honey there, bring it a distance away from the barrel of grape yeast, and then make a run for it! You should be able to gather yeast in time, before they get back. I'm… nearly sure of it!''Whew, you hustled like a bee was in your britches for sure! Haha! Did you get the yeast then? Let's have it, shall we?'Derva needs you to defeat wood-trolls and harvest mushrooms in the forest north-west of her farm.Derva has asked you to defeat wood-trolls and pick mushrooms.

Wood-trolls and the mushrooms she seeks can be found in the woods to the north-west.Defeat Gelin warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Gelin lobbers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather woody mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'What we don't grow here we forage from the woods to the north-east. Or at least we used to until some wood-trolls moved in. They used to be fewer in number and stayed closer to the water. Something pushed them farther up hill and I don't know what.

'Normally I would be happy to live and let live, but over the past few nights I've noticed a few of them straying from the woods and getting closer to the farm than I'd like. I petitioned Ost Arndír for aid but it seems they are busy with some Haradrim lingering to the south-east.

'Could I ask you to go into the woods and erm, discourage them from venturing too close? Oh and while you're there, if you see any white mushrooms could you pick them for me? They are the backbone of my summer stew recipe and I haven't been able to pick any myself on account of the wood-trolls.'Derva brushes some woodchips and twigs from your shoulder.

'You had a little something on there. I take it the wood-trolls have been dealt with?'

You nod and hand over the basket of mushrooms. She lifts them to her nose and inhales.

'I've missed that musty smell. Thanks, adventurer. I hope your future journeys treat you well.'Though their foolhardy captain leads with an iron fist, Upokhir counts many brave warriors as trusted allies within Pahor Boha.Upokhir has asked you to deliver plans to his trusted confidants in Pahor Boha.

Pahor Boha can be found in the south-east of Pinnath Gelin.You to have delivered plans to Upokhir's trusted confidants within Pahor Boha, and should report your success.

Talk to Upokhir in Ost Arndír.Talk to Upokhir'Many of my people are too afraid of our captain to challenge him directly, but I am here on behalf of many others who wish to see all our people return home safely. When Torthril leads her people into battle, my allies can coordinate with her forces and hopefully we can eliminate the captain with as little bloodshed as possible. To this end, I would ask you to deliver word to my allies.'

Upokhir provides you with detailed descriptions of his trusted allies.

'Deliver these letters to them so they can begin their preparations.''Thank you for passing them my messages. I am glad to hear they are still well. I look forward to celebrating with them after putting this dark chapter behind us.'Sickle-flies plague Iáphel.Miruhir has asked you to defeat sickle-flies to the north-west of the vineyard.

Defeat sickle-flies near Iáphel.Defeat vineyard flies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should tell Miruhir that you have dealt with sickle-flies.

Miruhir can be found in Iáphel.Talk to Miruhir'A swarm of sickle-flies have made a home in the fields to the north-west. Sometimes they stray into the vineyards and spoil my grapes and bite my people! Could you help rid me of those pests?'Miruhir shivers as you tell him how you dealt with the sickle-flies.

'I would have taken care of them myself if they didn't upset my stomach so. They are disgusting to behold, and the very sound they make is like a millstone against my ear. Thank you for your aid.'Defeat many beasts in the Shield Isles.Defeat many beasts in in the Shield Isles.Defeat many beasts in in the Shield IslesDefeat many beasts in the Shield Isles.Defeat many beasts in the Shield Isles.Defeat many beasts in the Shield IslesKiria's goods were lost during a recent attack from bog-lurkers.Kiria asked you to retrieve any stolen goods to which the bog-lurkers may have taken a liking.

They can be found at Basha Ghând to the north-west.Collect stolen supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You seem to have collected all of the supplies that the bog-lurkers lifted from Kiria. You should return to Kiria.

Kiria can be found in Mâr Naphra.Talk to Kiria'No one told me about the bogs. I came here to sell honest goods in exchange for honest money, but since those creatures attacked my waggon, I don't have any goods to sell!

'I'm going to take a massive loss if I can't unload this product here. Could you possibly help me retrieve my items? I am sure those creatures are keeping them. They didn't much care if I ran away and seemed to only want what was in the waggon.

'Coincidentally, I only care about what was in the waggon as well....''Oh I thought I'd never get my supplies back! Many thanks to you.

'Now I can continue with my trade.'Ahuz is concerned about the wine casks he was transporting that were lost during a recent storm on the isles.Ahuz has asked you to retrieve his lost wine casks. His boat ran ashore to the west of Mâr Naphra.Collect wine casks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have successfully collected all of Ahuz's wine casks. You should return them. Ahuz can be found in Mâr Naphra.'Not that it's any of your business, but my wine is gone! All the trouble I've been through just trying to smuggle such acquired delectables to Umbar... I should be paid a king's ransom!

'You look fairly capable. If you're lookin' to make some coin, I'm lookin' for someone to retrieve what I've lost!''Well, would you look at that. You came through!

'I promise not to harass upstanding, tight-strapped fellows like yourself from now on. You all can be quite useful!'The time has come for you and your trusted crew to depart for Umbar on the Wave-hunter.The Wave-hunter is docked on the lake outside Ost Arndír.Travel to the Wave-hunter where it is docked in Pinnath GelinNauriel readies for the voyage of the Wave-hunter where the ship is docked in Pinnath Gelin.Talk to Nauriel beside the Wave-hunter in Pinnath GelinSigileth readies for the departure of the Wave-hunter.Talk to Sigileth beside the Wave-hunter in Pinnath GelinSirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, lost in his thoughts, as he prepares for the voyage.Talk to Sirgon on the deck of the Wave-hunter'The rest of your crew must have arrived at the Wave-hunter by now, and they surely wait for you to join them. Yes, I am coming too. I hope that the brave men and women you have recruited will have courage enough to spare some for me, for the spectre of this voyage fills me with trepidation!

'I will be fine, ${PLAYER}. I have to be. Lead on!''Lead on! The Wave-hunter is docked on the lake to the east of Ost Arndír, in Pinnath Gelin.''Time is wasting.''The sailors were up before dawn, making the ship ready to sail, but it seems that was still not enough! When will be the last of these unending delays? My son is still in the hands of the Kindred of the Coins, and must be rescued with all speed!

'My husband will see to the safety of Pinnath Gelin while I am away, but as you are the one King Elessar has chosen for this mission, you will be responsible for the lives of all those aboard the Wave-hunter, ${PLAYER}. I care not for my own life; I care only for that of my son Thorongil. Bring me to his captors and I will do what is necessary.''You may be responsible for the lives of all those aboard the Wave-hunter, ${PLAYER}, but I care not for my own. I care only for that of my son Thorongil. Bring me to his captors and I will do what is necessary.''It seems we are once again to be the Hidden Guard, ${PLAYER}, journeying in secret to rescue a captive. Nay, for this time the captives number two, and one of them is my own brother. Let it be a consolation to us that the place we must go can shelter no evil as great as that which lurked within the walls of Dol Guldur.

'I do wish I had my knives for this mission. Lanchigil and Egnassigil would make short work of the Kindred of the Coins, although I understand Elessar is hopeful we can return Thorongil and Corudan without bloodshed. I think that is unlikely.

'I have been training with this blade, just in case. I have not yet given it a name.''I understand Elessar is hopeful we can return Thorongil and Corudan without bloodshed. I think that is unlikely.

'I have been training with this blade, just in case. I have not yet given it a name.''I rose with the dawn and helped the sailors prepare the Wave-hunter for its voyage. Thank you once again, and a million times more, for allowing me to sail with you, my friend. I feel alive again, and the feel of the deck beneath my feet has given back to me the vigour of my youth!

'To sea, to sea! At last!'Now that your preparations have been made, it is time for the voyage of the Wave-hunter and the completion of your secret mission.Sirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, eager for the ship to set sail.Talk to Sirgon and give the order for the ship to set sail to UmbarDaxamat has left the ship and awaits your orders.Talk to Daxamat at Voyage's End in the Shield IslesSomeone watches you from the tree line to the west of the Wave-hunter.Confront the men watching you from the tree line to the westTwo residents of the Shield Isles watch you with suspicion in their eyes.Talk to Mattân to the west of the Wave-hunterTalk to Ozâl to the west of the Wave-hunterCaebar stands by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Talk to Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles'Are you ready to give the order? None but you can give it, ${PLAYER}!

'Is it time to leave your familiar shores behind?''Very well, my friend!

'Ready the sails! It is time for the Wave-hunter to ride the river down to the sea, and then to make for the City of the Corsairs!'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'We are lucky to be alive, ${PLAYER}. The storms that arise in the Bay of Belfalas can be fearsome, and these isles are often lashed by the worst of them. Ours is not the first ship to run aground on these isles, and I cannot believe it will be the last.

'I have been to one of the southernmost islands in this chain before. Zamarzîr it was called. My brother and I sheltered for a time among the freebooters who live there, but Jajax did not want to stay, and I could not remain by myself. We were very young then, only children; it must have changed in the years since.

'But our arrival has attracted some attention. Look, among the trees! These isles are not deserted, ${PLAYER}, and the men who live here may seek to do us harm.''Our arrival has attracted some attention. Look, among the trees! These isles are not deserted, ${PLAYER}, and the men who live here may seek to do us harm.''What?''What?''These isles are not deserted, ${PLAYER}, and the men who live here may seek to do us harm.''The storm chewed up your ship and spat you out, stranger... but it must not have liked the taste of you. Most of the ships devoured by Shedax Khîn arrive upon the Shield Isles in more pieces than this, and with fewer survivors.

'Shedax Khîn? That is the Umbari word for the rocks that surround the island of Bakhjâd. It means "the Grinding Jaws," and theirs is the smile that welcomes strangers to these isles. But someone else must smile upon you and upon your crew, for while your ship will not sail again, you have your life, and that is more than some retain when they come here.''Mattân and I listened to the driving rain of the storm last night and it told the two of us a new wreck would decorate the islands this morn. We arose early, before any others, and came here in haste... but we were rewarded with disappointment. The isles have their new decoration, aye. But the Grinding Jaws did not finish their meal, and too many survivors guard the wreck.

'There will be little for us to salvage today. But I tell you this: life in the Shield Isles is hard, and not all who arrive here as you have can endure it. You survived the storm, but will you survive the week? Will you survive the day?

'Oh, it is no threat, stranger. I am simply making conversation.''You are more fortunate than most who come here, stranger.''An unguarded wreck is free to all who dare search it. Perhaps Mattân and I will come back tomorrow.''I knew I did not like sailing, ${PLAYER}! How can it be that Sirgon missed it? A sailing-ship is a hateful thing, as unpleasant a creation as I have ever known!'

You remind Caebar that were it not for the strong hull of the Wave-hunter and its brave crew, he would not have survived the storm. Caebar shakes his head.

'Yes, yes,' he mumbles. 'I suppose it could always be worse. But I am done with ships! You mark my words, ${PLAYER}! From this day forward I will take the land-road, no matter how out of the way it may run!'Eager to obtain a secure foothold from which to continue the mission, some of the Wave-hunter's crew have scattered across the Shield Isles and must be found.Each member of your crew has gone in search of some way to help, but now many of them are scattered across the various islands that make up the Shield Isles.Complete 'The Isles: Sirgon the Explorer'Complete 'The Isles: The Knight Nauriel'Complete 'The Isles: Gimli and Legolas'Complete 'The Isles: Keen-eyed Sigileth'Complete 'The Isles: The Corsair Daxamat'Caebar is by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Talk to Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield IslesSirgon is interested in your conversation with Caebar.Think it overSirgon has joined you and Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Talk to Sirgon by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles'Waiting for the rain to end was a burden for some of the crew, and of that number many of them have already gone to scout the neighbouring isles. Nauriel declared she could not wait, and pressed through the trees to the south, and I saw Sigileth wading through the waves to the south-east of here in search of... I know not what. Does she think the ship carrying her brother to Umbar ran afoul of the rocks as we did? As for Gimli and Legolas, I heard the Elf calling for Gimli to follow him to the south-east in search of game animals, but I do not know how far they might have travelled. I think they may have gone as far as Zamarzîr.

'The rest of the crew may be scattered across any of the Shield Isles, ${PLAYER}! We need them to return so we can decide what to do next!''Nauriel declared she could not wait, and pressed through the trees to the south, and I saw Sigileth wading through the waves to the south-east of here. As for Gimli and Legolas, I heard the Elf calling for Gimli to follow him to the south-east in search of game animals, but I do not know how far they might have travelled. I think they may have gone as far as Zamarzîr.''Many members of the crew have returned to the Wave-hunter, ${PLAYER}, and I know we have you to thank for that! Did their scouting turn up anything of use to us?'

You tell Caebar what you learned about the Widow Saklaphêl and the Heirs of Castamir, and the bounty she has placed upon the leadership of the Kindred of the Coins. He smiles wryly.

'I suppose that might be one way to complete our mission: get one of these bounty-hunters to slay the folk responsible for capturing Thorongil and Corudan, and mount a rescue mission during the ensuing chaos. What were the names of the targets? Azagath the Sea-shadow, Belondor of the Fleet-fast, and Hármelak Golden-hand? They sound... lovely.''What is it?''I am sorry to interrupt, ${PLAYER}. But... I overheard you speaking with Caebar, and I thought I heard the boy speak a name that... well, a name I have not heard in many years.

'Did you speak the name Belondor? Or have I misheard you?'

Caebar shrugs apologetically and responds that "Belondor of the Fleet-fast" was listed as one of the bounties for which Saklaphêl would pay a valuable reward. Sirgon nods, a haunted look in his eye.

'I see. It couldn't be... and yet perhaps it could.'Defeat many Corsairs in the Shield Isles.Defeat many Corsairs in the Shield Isles.Defeat many Corsairs in the Shield IslesDefeat many Corsairs in the Shield Isles.Defeat many Corsairs in the Shield Isles.Defeat many Corsairs in the Shield IslesDefeat many crabs in the Shield Isles.Defeat many crabs in the Shield Isles.Defeat many crabs in the Shield IslesDefeat many crabs in the Shield Isles.Defeat many crabs in the Shield Isles.Defeat many crabs in the Shield IslesTarshiah laments about the growing population of kergrim threatening the coast off Bakhjâd.Tarshiah has asked you to help cull the population of kergrim on the coast west of Mâr Naphra.Defeat kergrim on the island south-west of Bakhjâd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Now that the task is complete you should report back to Tarshiah.Talk to Tarshiah'We've got a good thing going aroun' 'ere, and I don't want to screw it up, but these kergrim are presentin' a huge problem for us and our clientele. If we can't get this population under control, we'll take huge losses.

'Why don't you make yourself useful, and get out there? Fight, and take care of the kergrim population count.''That's it then. A job well done.

'So long as we keep their numbers from going out of control, they shouldn't be a nuisance to this town.'Defeat many Dead in the Shield Isles.Defeat many Dead in the Shield Isles.Defeat many Dead in the Shield IslesDefeat many Dead in the Shield Isles.Defeat many Dead in the Shield Isles.Defeat many Dead in the Shield IslesZîrar Tarka, the Shield Isles, serve as Umbar's bulwark against the storms that often trouble the Great Sea, but so too do they often prove the doom of unwary sailors, as countless ships have run aground on its coasts—their wrecks caught in the grinding jaws of the Shedax Khîn.Zîrar Tarka, the Shield Isles, serve as Umbar's bulwark against the storms that often trouble the Great Sea, but so too do they often prove the doom of unwary sailors, as countless ships have run aground on its coasts—their wrecks caught in the grinding jaws of the Shedax Khîn.Complete Explorer of the Shield IslesComplete Quests of the Shield IslesComplete Slayer of the Shield IslesExplore settlements and other important points of interest in the Shield Isles.Explore settlements and other important points of interest in the Shield Isles.Find Voyage's EndFind HalraxFind KafagurFind Phadâl BimaiFind AklâradumFind IrkhadârDefeat many dragon-kind in the Shield Isles.Defeat many dragon-kind in the Shield Isles.Defeat many dragon-kind in the Shield IslesDefeat many dragon-kind in the Shield Isles.Defeat many dragon-kind in the Shield Isles.Defeat many dragon-kind in the Shield IslesExplore Zîrar Tarka, the Shield Isles of Umbar.Explore Zîrar Tarka, the Shield Isles of Umbar.Complete Denizens of the Shield IslesComplete Perils of the Shield IslesComplete Treasure-seeker of the Shield IslesNow that your preparations have been made, it is time for the voyage of the Wave-hunter and the completion of your secret mission.Caebar stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter, already concerned about something.Talk to Caebar on the deck of the Wave-hunterCaebar is worried that Daxamat will fall, and he has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> the Corsair to come down.Spirits are light as the Wave-hunter begins its voyage to Umbar.Wait with your crewSirgon stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter as its voyage begins.Talk to Sirgon on the deck of the Wave-hunterSirgon recommended that you speak with the crew-members you recruited for the voyage as the Wave-hunter sails to Umbar.As he said he would, Caebar prefers to remain below decks.Talk to Caebar below decks in the Wave-hunterCaebar has suggested you go above and take in the fresh air.Go back up on deckSigileth stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter.Talk to Sigileth on the deck of the Wave-hunterSome members of your crew discuss the situation that awaits them in Umbar.Listen to the concerns of your crewDaxamat has agreed to tell you what he can about the City of the Corsairs.Talk to Daxamat and learn about UmbarCaebar is below decks, waiting to hear how the crew is enjoying the voyage.When you have learned enough, find Caebar below decksSirgon calls for you as the storm rages outside and the Wave-hunter is tossed on wild seas.Talk to Sirgon inside the Wave-hunterThe storm rages!Go up on deck and weather the stormLegolas calls for your help.Talk to Legolas on the deck of the Wave-hunterThrown from the ship during the storm, you have washed ashore and must now return to the Wave-hunter.Find the Wave-hunterWaterlogged but alive, you have found where the Wave-hunter ran aground on the Shield Isles.Meet with Sirgon'I know I suggested that you recruit the Corsair Jajax for the crew and he refused the offer, but I was under the impression that his brother Daxamat would be a little less... I don't know... a little less wild, perhaps? But he is clambering all over the Wave-hunter as if he has not a care in the world, and without the slightest thought that he might fall from any of these perches, each more perilous than the last!

'Will you <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for him to come down? He is making me nervous!''I have not felt this youthful in years! Our course leads down the Lagorduin to the Bay of Belfalas, and then we will truly be on our way.

'Like young Caebar, not all of the Wave-hunter's crew have before been at sea. I suggest that you speak with the folk you recruited and learn how the river-passage treats them. The waters in the Bay will be more unruly than this, and if the rocking in Lagorduin disturbs them it may be helpful to know, and guard against further upset! I understand the dwarf Gimli has in his possession a remedy for seasickness? He may need to share it, with Caebar at least, and perhaps with others!''I am all right now, ${PLAYER}. It was simply the sight of Daxamat clambering out over the railing of the ship that made me feel queasy. I think I will remain below decks for the rest of the voyage, unless you need me above. I cannot imagine you will. The sailors of Anfalas seem very capable.''The one who abducted my son Thorongil, this Nakási Wave-reaper... you said you know who she is?'

You tell Nauriel of the cellar encounter between Nakási and the Heirs of Castamir that resulted in the death of her husband Tumúldo. Nauriel stares at you with narrowed eyes.

'She will have no sympathy from me. Bad things happen. If she does not return my son to me, unharmed, I will send her to see her husband at once. I may do this anyway. Let her and her masters beware: a Knight of the Green Hills does not grant mercy without good reason... and the mother of an endangered child never does.''I have been thinking about something, my friend. So much good stone is covered by rivers and by lakes... and by the Sea as well, I imagine! What precious gemstones lie hidden down there, out of our reach? Is that the secret of the Temámir? Do the arid lands of their birth yield such valuables to them more easily than ours? And yet they still need water to drink....

'I look forward to learning how it is done when we arrive in Umbar. The gemstone worn by Khôltekh the Cunning is an intriguing mystery, but it is one I intend to solve!''Oh, excuse me, ${PLAYER}, I did not mean to be rude. I was contemplating the bridge over the Lagorduin: such an impressive feat of stonework!

'The City of the Corsairs has been many things over the years, but for some of that time it was a sea-haven of Númenor. There must be architectural wonders there too, and I am eager to see them. My wife Bruidis cares less for such things. Where is she now? She has gone below decks, intending to assess our stock of supplies. I told her the voyage itself should not take more than a few days, but still she wanted to ensure we have food and water enough.

'I told you before, did I not? I am a swan-knight, and my martial skill is well-developed; but my wife Bruidis is the strategist of the family. If there is thinking to be done, she is the one to do it!''I have never been to Umbar, ${PLAYER}, and neither has my brother... unless he has somehow managed to escape my notice and had some adventure about which he has told me nothing! But I find that unlikely.

'I wonder if Elves live among the sea-folk that call Umbar their home? I will have to put this question to the Corsair Daxamat sometime in the next few days. It could be he has seen Elves in the city or along the cape during his time there, before the Kindred came to power.'Gwallang the Limlinn hops excitedly up and down, occasionally cracking the shell of a snail he has caught on the railing of the Wave-hunter. He seems very happy to be sailing with Sirgon again.'This blade has to earn its name, ${PLAYER}. I cannot give it a name that might prove to be the wrong one! Weapons are like children, or so I have heard it said.

'The Elves of Lórien called my brother Corudan "the River-walker," for he was often away from home, exploring the lands up and down the Anduin. Will this adventure now make him "the Sea-strider," or "the Bay-rider?"

'I will have to tell him this when we rescue him. He will laugh to hear it, once he is safe.''I have not yet needed the seasickness remedy you and Legolas procured for me, ${PLAYER}, but all the same I believe I will stay below decks for now. Do you think I should share it with Caebar? I will have it ready if he asks me for it, but I do not want to give it all away, just in case.

'We are not yet out in the Bay, after all. Legolas says he expects the rocking of the ship to become more pronounced when we leave the river behind us.''I have given some thought to our voyage, ${PLAYER}. I believe the City of the Corsairs must remain a bustling port-city, despite the defeat of Balakhôr the Scourge and the Heirs of Castamir during the War of the Ring. Do you think the arrival of the Wave-hunter can go unnoticed when we draw near the port?

'I cannot decide if it is more or less suspicious of us to arrive by night. Perhaps some of Golasgil's sailors will give me their opinions.''How fares my husband Rossaran? No doubt he gawks at the scenery through which the ship passes?

'Oh, he is a dear man. Two things he loves besides me, ${PLAYER}: faithfully serving his King, and marvelling at the great feats performed by the prospectors and stonemasons of Gondor. Sometimes I wonder if he should have been born a dwarf!

'But I have been checking our store of food and water, and it seems that we should have enough for the voyage to Umbar and back. The Wave-hunter is well-prepared for the journey; I confess to you that it is our arrival at the City of the Corsairs that now most concerns me!''This ship is unlike those of my people, ${PLAYER}. No, I do not intend that to be an insult! Even a ship made of rough-hewn timber is still to be prized if it stays afloat and keeps you from a watery grave! I think it is simply the way of the Men of Gondor to value the use of a thing higher than the beauty of its form.''What's that? Oh, nothing. I am just thinking.

'What goods do you think the people of Umbar might value? If I were to establish a market along the docks of the city, what things would fetch the highest price? Will items from Gondor be considered valuable or worthless, ${PLAYER}? I cannot decide! At least I will have a few days to think it over.''Thank you for keeping me company, ${PLAYER}, but I will not ask you to remain below decks for the whole voyage! Feel free to go above and take in the fresh air.''The voyage is well underway, and now our thoughts turn to our arrival at the City of the Corsairs. What will we do if the Kindred of the Coins greets us at the dock, ${PLAYER}? I said we would once again become the Hidden Guard, but there is very little that will be hidden about our mission if our foes see us arrive from atop the walls or from the watch-towers of Umbar.''I am not much of a teacher. My brother Jajax is the talker in the family.

'But I hope to be a help to you. What do you want to know?''I am not much of a teacher, but I hope to be a help to you. What do you want to know?''Thanks for checking in on me, ${PLAYER}. You say the Corsair Daxamat spoke about what we can expect when we reach Umbar? I should have liked to hear that... assuming it was good news!'

You tell Caebar what you learned, and he nods.

'A little good and a little bad, then? It sounds to me as if we have our work cut out for us when we arrive. At least the sailing has been easy. I expected worse!''The storm rages and the seas are wild! We have to take down the sails, or the wind will tear our masts to splinters! The sailors and the Elves have gone above, but I cannot tell if they are still alive!''The sails have been taken down, but we are not yet safe! There is a presence in the wind, and it seeks to batter our ship beneath the waves!'Defeat many kergrim in the Shield Isles.Defeat many kergrim in the Shield Isles.Defeat many kergrim in the Shield IslesDefeat many kergrim in the Shield Isles.Defeat many kergrim in the Shield Isles.Defeat many kergrim in the Shield IslesBalidan expresses that he severely misjudged the life of a pirate. He desires your help in planning an escape.Balidan has asked you to collect some spare parts for his escape. The parts can be found within Mâr Naphra's off-limits storage.Find spare oars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect pillaged rations (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have successfully collected everything Balidan needs to make his escape. Deliver them to the meeting point.

Balidan is waiting on the coast south-west of Mâr Naphra.'You... look different. Not like them. Those filthy scoundrels. I never thought life would be like this. When I first set out for the isles....

'I've underestimated just how cruel and rough the life of a pirate is. Your life is constantly at risk and people walk all over you.

'But I've a plan. They don't take kindly to deserters but I've a boat near the western coast. If I could get the necessary supplies to make her sea-worthy I might just be able to be free.''You made it, and you have the things! I'll finally be able to go home! I can't thank you enough, stranger. These are dark times indeed, but the light shines forth where it can!'The wandering soul cannot rest peacefully. There must be something keeping it in this realm.The wandering soul seems to be muttering to itself. Perhaps you should search the vicinity for any clues as to its identity.Search the nearby satchelAn herbal satchel found by the wandering spirit leaves trail leading to the north-west.Follow the trail north-westThe trail led you to a wrecked boat in the shallows. It must have run aground during a horrible storm.Search the wreckageSearching the wreckage, you find a water-logged journal. Perhaps this can help the wandering spirit.Examine the water-logged journalThere seems to be a trail of jetsam leading away from the first trail of herbs.Track the scattered jetsamMore and more debris scatters the more south you wander.Find the next pile of debrisAs the trail narrows, it leads you further into the shallows.Find the next sign of jetsamThe trail is getting thinner and harder to track. You must be getting closer.Find where the trail endsSearch for the final clueThe locket you found contains a small sketch of two people locked in an embrace. One of the people bears a striking resemblance to the wandering spirit. You should return this to the lost soul.

Heshla can be found south-east of the wreckage.'The bright canopy...

'Razed by shrieks of light...

'A violent storm...

'Thrashing to...

'A loud crash...

'A point of no return...''My... locket.

'My beloved.

'I am unable to return...

'This is who I am...'Erothai is concerned that the bog-lurkers are becoming more aggressive, heightening the threat of attacks on Mâr Naphra.Erothai has asked you to clean up the bogs to the north so that Mâr Naphra maintains such a high status as an establishment.Defeat bog-lurkers in Basha Ghând (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You've done all you can to clear the bogs. You should talk to Erothai and give your full report.

Erothai can be found in Mâr Naphra.Talk to Erothai'You seen them nasty creatures out in the bogs to the north? Filthy. Disgusting.

'Takes away from our most reputable establishment, wouldn't you agree? I'm looking for strong folk such as you to clear them out. They're gettin' aggressive and we can't have them roaming about causing the most prestigious clientele discomfort.

'Do what you can, eh?''That ought to raise the reputation of Mâr Naphra. The fewer of these filthy creatures roaming about the vicinity, the better.

'Of course, a reward for honest work!'Explore enemy encampments and the dangerous wilds of the Shield Isles.Explore enemy encampments and the dangerous wilds of the Shield Isles.Find Basha GhândFind Khataj MârsaFind BâkhabarFind Ghax-hophraFind Jeb LiphaFind Dor PherkhaFind Maj KhibiFind InjakhûrFind Bax GarâkhFind Ghar JâdamFind Dar GrekhûlFind Baj KhatûgComplete quests in the Shield Isles.Complete quests in the Shield Isles.Complete quests in the Shield IslesDefeat foes in Zîrar Tarka, the Shield Isles of Umbar.Defeat foes in Zîrar Tarka, the Shield Isles of Umbar.Complete Beast-slayer of the Shield Isles (Advanced)Complete Corsair-slayer of the Shield Isles (Advanced)Complete Crab-slayer of the Shield Isles (Advanced)Complete Dead-slayer of the Shield Isles (Advanced)Complete Dragon-kind Slayer of the Shield Isles (Advanced)Complete Kergrim-slayer of the Shield Isles (Advanced)Rumours of a treasure cache that once belonged to a Corsair captain have reached your ears.Kotheret Glint-grin told you about the rumoured treasure. Whether the treasure is real, she cannot say.

It may have been buried somewhere in Bax Garâkh, east of Mâr Naphra.Search for the rumoured treasure in Bax GarâkhYou have discovered the possible location of the treasure cache.

You should dig into the sand mound.Dig into the sand moundYou've discovered what appears to be the treasure Kotheret told you about.

You should try to open it.Try to open the treasure chestTrying to open the treasure chest caused an angry shade to attack you.

Now that you've vanquished it, you should try to open the chest again.Open the treasure chestThe contents of the treasure were more troubling than valuable: an intact skull, and a metallic tooth like Kotheret's.

You should return to her in Mâr Naphra and seek answers.Find Kotheret Glint-grin in Mâr NaphraKotheret Glint-grin seems to have vanished from Mâr Naphra.Completed'A ${CLASS}, are you?' The woman grins widely, revealing a metallic tooth. 'The sort who seeks out grave danger in the spirit of adventure? I'd wager you'll want to hear what I have to say, then.

'When you've stuck around Mâr Naphra for as long as I have, you pick up all sorts of... interesting stories. One story has fragmented into naught but rumours: a bloodthirsty Corsair captain, a cache of buried treasure...

'Many an ambitious soul has ventured east to Bax Garâkh in search of this treasure. Whether they've been successful, I cannot say I know. Perhaps the treasure does not exist after all.

'Ah, I've taken up enough of your time. Watch yourself, traveller. Not everyone here is as friendly as I.'The amount of coins in the chest barely comes close to what you were expecting -- or rather, hoping for.

What truly catches your attention, however, is the preserved skull that sits among the coins. It greets you with an eternal, lipless smile.

Hidden among the shining coins is a metallic tooth, one that looks eerily similar to Kotheret Glint-grin's...Kotheret Glint-grin seems to have vanished from Mâr Naphra. You may have your suspicions about what you discovered, but it seems your questions will never be put to rest.Rossaran and Bruidis have a plan to help those who were wounded during the storm and the Wave-hunter's arrival on the Shield Isles.Bruidis is by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Talk to Bruidis by the Wave-hunter on the Shield IslesBruidis sent you to look for herbs, flowers, and tree bark at several different locations throughout the Shield Isles.Collect scraggly herbs from the nearby beach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect wild-flowers from the isle near Voyage's End (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect tree-bark from the large grey tree west of Bruidis (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bruidis is by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Talk to Bruidis by the Wave-hunter on the Shield IslesThe tub of water where Bruidis plans to brew the salve is to the south-east, near the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.The tub of water where Bruidis plans to brew the salve is to the south-east, near the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.The tub of water where Bruidis plans to brew the salve is to the south-east, near the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Rossaran is on the Wave-hunter where it has run aground in the Shield Isles.Talk to Rossaran on the Wave-hunter in the Shield IslesThe tub of water where Bruidis plans to brew the salve is to the south-east, near the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Bruidis is by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Talk to Bruidis by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles'Many of the sailors who crewed the Wave-hunter sustained injuries during the storm, and Bruidis wants to prepare a salve that will help make them more comfortable while they recover. She has set me to fish, for apparently this salve has need of fish-scales, but there are other ingredients to be gathered. Speak to her and she will tell you what else she needs, if you are of a mind to help.''My wife Bruidis wants to prepare a salve that will ease the sailors' recovery. She has set me to fish, for apparently this salve has need of fish-scales, but there are other ingredients to be gathered. Speak to her and she will tell you what else she needs, if you are of a mind to help.''Rossaran has enlisted you to help me gather the ingredients I need to brew the salve? He is a good man, my husband. But you would have offered to help me anyway, would you not? I think I am a good judge of character, not just of husbands but of friends, as well.

'This salve requires herbs tough enough to grow on the nearby beach, flowers nourished by the damp air blanketing this isle, and several pieces of tree-bark, which you should be able to take from a large grey tree I saw to the west. Bring these ingredients back to me and I will tell you about the next steps.''This salve requires herbs tough enough to grow on the nearby beach, flowers nourished by the damp air blanketing this isle, and several pieces of tree-bark, which you should be able to take from a large grey tree I saw to the west. Bring these ingredients back to me and I will tell you about the next steps.''You found the things I need! I am very pleased to hear it, ${PLAYER}!

'Now you need to steep each of the ingredients in the tub of water I have prepared to the south-east: the herbs the longest, followed by the flowers, and finally the tree-bark. After you have added each of these things to the water, speak to Rossaran and obtain as many fish-scales as he can give you, and add those to the tub last of all.''Now you need to steep each of the ingredients in the tub of water I have prepared to the south-east: the herbs the longest, followed by the flowers, and finally the tree-bark. After you have added each of these things to the water, speak to Rossaran and obtain as many fish-scales as he can give you, and add those to the tub last of all.''Now you need to steep each of the ingredients in the tub of water I have prepared to the south-east: the herbs the longest, followed by the flowers, and finally the tree-bark. After you have added each of these things to the water, speak to Rossaran and obtain as many fish-scales as he can give you, and add those to the tub last of all.''Now you need to steep each of the ingredients in the tub of water I have prepared to the south-east: the herbs the longest, followed by the flowers, and finally the tree-bark. After you have added each of these things to the water, speak to Rossaran and obtain as many fish-scales as he can give you, and add those to the tub last of all.''My husband should have enough fish-scales by now.''Your timing is just about perfect, ${PLAYER}, for I have finished scaling the fish I caught. Here you go.

'What next? You need to add the scales to the water tub? Go on, then.''I hope I caught enough fish-scales for Bruidis's purposes.''Add the fish-scales to the tub of water, if you would.''All done? Very good, and thank you!

'The salve will take awhile to steep, but once it is prepared I will have Rossaran bring it around to the injured sailors. You have done more than enough, and we appreciate every bit of it! But do not let me distract you any further... there is surely work to be done elsewhere on the Shield Isles, and I know the Lady Nauriel wants nothing to delay the rescue of her son from the Kindred of the Coins!

'But I know a thing or two about such things, and we will want the members of the crew to be as rested and comfortable as they can be when the time comes to mount the rescue. Injured men fight poorly, no matter how brave they may be when hale, or during peacetime.

'Thank you once again, ${PLAYER}. We will not forget that you helped us... all of us!'Elladan and Elrohir have rescued a resident of the Shield Isles from danger, and he may share useful information with you if you help him further.Elladan and Elrohir have saved Yahîm from danger, and he waits to speak with you in Bakhjâd.Talk to Yahîm by Elrohir in BakhjâdYahîm has asked you to retrieve his sword from the kergrim den where he lost it, and to slay any of the creatures you can.Defeat kergrim among the ruins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Retrieve Yahîm's sword from the kergrim-infested ruinsYahîm waits for you to return his sword to him near his home by the water on the eastern side of Mâr Naphra.Elladan and Elrohir have returned to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.Talk to Elladan at Voyage's EndTalk to Elrohir at Voyage's End'My brother and I thought to scout Bakhjâd and avoid the attention of the Corsair settlement we discovered in the island's interior, but it was not long before we heard the sound of someone calling for help from within the ruin atop this hill. We could not remain idle, ${PLAYER}, you understand. We went to investigate and only then discovered that he was clearly a Corsair; by most accounting he is a foe of our mission, but we could not leave him to be devoured by the kergrim that threatened him.

'We saved him and brought him back here. Have we done wrong?''We saved him from the kergrim and brought him down here, though he is a Corsair and a foe of our mission. Have we done wrong?''You are a friend of these Elves? I am not accustomed to speaking with such as they, but I cannot deny that if they had not come along I would now be dead.

'My name is Yahîm, and I am not one to refuse aid when it is offered! It is true: I am a Corsair, and Mâr Naphra is my home, but I confess I am currently without a ship. If you hold a grudge against my kind, I understand it, but we are not currently at sea. On land can we not remain friendly?

'I appreciate the timely intervention of these Elves, and I do not mean to be ungrateful... but when I followed them to safety I left my sword behind. If you will return to the kergrim-infested ruin atop this island and retrieve my sword for me, I will see that you are rewarded. The Elves seemed more interested in what I might know than what valuables I might give to them, if you take my meaning. I will tell you what I know about the Heirs of Castamir and the Kindred of the Coins... if you bring my sword to me at my home by the water on the eastern side of Mâr Naphra. Unless I have misjudged your intent, that is what you want to know, is it not?

'If you will do this, can I ask for one more favour? Slay some more of the kergrim for me, will you? They are disgusting creatures, spreading filth and disease, and they should not remain among the old ruins. It is not right.''If you will return to the kergrim-infested ruin atop this island and retrieve my sword for me, I will see that you are rewarded. I also ask that you slay some more of the kergrim for me. They are disgusting creatures, spreading filth and disease, and they should not remain among the old ruins. It is not right.''Watch yourself among the wrecks, ${PLAYER}. The kergrim are dangerous.''Yahîm said you should bring his sword to him at his home by the water on the eastern side of Mâr Naphra. It may be he will know something useful about the Heirs of Castamir or the Kindred of the Coins. Once you have spoken with him, we will meet you back at the Wave-hunter.''Thank you for returning my sword to me. How would I make my living without it?'

Yahîm lowers his voice, and looks to either side before continuing in a hushed tone.

'The life of a Corsair is not what it once was, I confess it. I blame the Heirs of Castamir for that, but when I do so I make sure not to do so loudly, or when not in the company of those I know well. I make an exception for you and for your Elf companions, for if you cannot trust those who save your life, who can you trust?

'I promised you knowledge. Here it is: after the death of Balakhôr the Scourge in Gondor, his widow Saklaphêl thought to claim the rule of Umbar, acting as regent through their young son Balakhâd, but the rioting in the streets and the rise of the Kindred of the Coins caused her to abandon both that plan and the city; she fled to the Shield Isles, and now lives in exile here in Mâr Naphra. None see her. She issues orders to her servants through Galadaith, her spokesman. Supporters of the Heirs of Castamir believe she will organize the remaining Corsairs and attack the city and the Kindred who control it.

'But I have heard there is a reason she cannot. Some say Balakhâd died during the fighting when the city fell, but others say that the Kindred hold him hostage, and Saklaphêl dares not attack the city for fear he will be slain.

'Once again I thank you and those Elves for the rescue, and for the return of my sword. I hope my information is of help to you.''Once again I thank you and those Elves for the rescue, and for the return of my sword. I hope my information is of help to you.''This is a very strange adventure, ${PLAYER}, where we must save our foes and rely upon what they can tell us to free our friends. My head spins, but I think Elrohir and I did the right thing. We could not leave Yahîm to be devoured by the kergrim, whether his allegiance is to the Heirs of Castamir or not. Corsair or no, he is still a Man, and he needed help.

'My brother feels the same, I am certain of it.''What did Yahîm have to say about the Heirs of Castamir and the Kindred of the Coins? Elladan and I would have rescued him no matter what information he had to share... but if his information is useful then so much the better.'

You tell Elrohir what the Corsair had to say, and he mulls it over for a moment.

'He does not know if the son of Balakhôr and Saklaphêl is alive and held by the Kindred of the Coins, but I think we have seen enough to know that they are the type to take prisoners. It could be Thorongil and Corudan and Balakhâd are all being held in the same dungeon, the easier to keep an eye upon them. The Kindred can then use each of them as leverage upon their respective families and friends.

'It is interesting, too, that Saklaphêl fled to Mâr Naphra. At least we will know from where the Heirs of Castamir might be organized, should they once again become a threat. It is worth keeping an eye upon, anyway. As if there was not enough to do already!

'Thank you for helping us with Yahîm, ${PLAYER}. Elladan and I will see what else we can help with around here.'Galengam has not been in the Shield Isles for long and the merchant is already up to something.Galengam has asked you to clear away some of the dense vegetation near his gathered supplies.Clear away concealing vegetation (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Galengam is north of Halrax.Talk to Galengam outside HalraxGalengam has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at several vendors within Halrax, to assess the level of his competition.Galengam is north of Halrax.Talk to Galengam outside HalraxSalamanders and toads can be found east of Halrax in the Shield Isles, and Galengam believes their legs might prove delicious for his customers... or for the crew of the Wave-hunter.Collect salamander legs on the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect toad legs on the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Galengam has returned to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.'There you are, ${PLAYER}. The mark of a truly great merchant is how well he responds to adverse conditions, and I plan to prove I am the finest in all the world, no matter the challenge with which I am confronted!

'That vegetation will become a problem if it is not cleared away. Will you do that for me?''That vegetation will become a problem if it is not cleared away. Will you do that for me?''Yes, thank you. Now the sunlight should dry out these supplies, and I can sell them at the market in Halrax as soon as they stop dripping.'

You ask Galengam if he really believes he can sell the supplies he took from the Wave-hunter, and he responds with a breezy laugh, apparently misunderstanding your question.

'I can sell anything, ${PLAYER}! Am I not the King's Own Merchant? But you raise a good point. Perhaps you should <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the vendors within Halrax and see what I will have to face for competition. I am only concerned with those vendors who have stalls along the main road that leads into the city; worry not about those up the hill.''Perhaps you should <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the vendors within Halrax and see what I will have to face for competition. I am only concerned with those vendors who have stalls along the main road that leads into the city; worry not about those up the hill.''What level of competition will I face at the market within Halrax?'

You tell Galengam about the type of goods you saw for sale within the town, and his forehead creases with thought.

'I planned to sell the goods we brought with us on the ship, ${PLAYER}, for I believed the residents here would believe them to be unusual... but I think now that will not be sufficient. I have heard that salamander legs and toad legs can be considered something of a delicacy, if they are prepared correctly. I understand you will find the raw ingredients for such a feast to the east of here, and while you see about collecting those, I will find out how to prepare them. Meet me back at the ship when you have enough salamander and toad legs, and perhaps we can corner the market on these goods. And if not, well, I assume the crew of the Wave-hunter will want something to eat.

'It is a shame not to sell the supplies I hauled all the way here, but it will take too long for them to dry out, and I need the coin coming in as soon as possible!''I have heard that salamander legs and toad legs can be considered something of a delicacy, if they are prepared correctly. I understand you will find the raw ingredients for such a feast to the east of here, and while you see about collecting those, I will find out how to prepare them. Meet me back at the ship when you have enough salamander and toad legs, and perhaps we can corner the market on these goods. And if not, well, I assume the crew of the Wave-hunter will want something to eat.''No one will tell me the right way to prepare toad or salamander legs! The folk of these isles must know I would drive them right out of business if they shared the secret with me... which of course I would, so they are right to worry!

'I will keep these legs you have brought me in a barrel of seawater until I learn the secret. I will not give up! Am I not the King's Own Merchant?

'In the meantime, keep an eye out for other mercantile opportunities, ${PLAYER}. I know we are here to rescue the young heir of Pinnath Gelin, but there is no reason we cannot make a little coin on the way, is there? No, there is not!'Gangur Farwend is lucky to be alive, but his experience has left him all the more eager to accomplish his mission.Gangur Farwend has asked you to retrieve the pick-axe and satchel he lost when he fell overboard. Additionally, he wants you to bring him rock samples from the island onto which he washed ashore.Retrieve Gangur's pick-axe from the coast nearbyRetrieve Gangur's satchel from the coast nearbyCollect rock samples from the island where Gangur came ashore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gangur Farwend waits for you to bring him his items on the island where he washed ashore.Gangur asked you to defeat worms and drakes in the high places of an island to the south, and to search their lair for corroded rock samples that might prove interesting to him.Defeat worms or drakes in the high places of the island south of Gangur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect corroded rock samples on the island south of Gangur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gangur Farwend has returned to the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles and waits for you to bring him the corroded rock samples he requested.'Is that you, ${PLAYER}? Oh, I am glad to see you. I am drenched through to my skin, and as my clothes dry I can feel the salt left behind. It is not pleasant, but I am lucky to be alive! Why did I allow you to talk me into this voyage?'

You tell Gangur that you are relieved to see he still lives, for it was believed that he was lost overboard during the storm.

'That is exactly what happened. I know it was foolish of me to go up on deck during the storm, but I feared the ship would fill with water and I would have no hope of survival if I remained below deck. There was a tremendous wave and I was swept overboard. Someone was looking out for me, but I cannot imagine why. More deserving dwarves than I have been favoured by the First Crafter. I thought I was sure to drown, and I saw... well, never mind what I saw. I cannot believe it, myself.

'I lost my pickaxe and my satchel. I was fortunate enough to wash ashore; perhaps they have fetched up along one of these islands too. Do you think you could look for them for me? While you look for those, could you also retrieve some rock samples for me from the islands hereabout? I am curious about something. I will be... well, I will be right here. I am still too water-logged to go anywhere.''I know it was foolish of me to go up on deck during the storm, but I feared the ship would fill with water and I would have no hope of survival if I remained below deck. There was a tremendous wave and I was swept overboard. Someone was looking out for me, but I cannot imagine why. More deserving dwarves than I have been favoured by the First Crafter. I thought I was sure to drown, and I saw... well, never mind what I saw. I cannot believe it, myself.

'I lost my pickaxe and my satchel. I was fortunate enough to wash ashore; perhaps they have fetched up along one of these islands too. Do you think you could look for them for me? While you look for those, could you also retrieve some rock samples for me from the islands hereabout? I am curious about something. I will be... well, I will be right here. I am still too water-logged to go anywhere.''You found my things! I was holding them when I went overboard, so it make sense to me that they would arrive along roughly the same coastline as I did. They are in better shape than I am, that is for certain. I will need to dry them out in the sun all the same, but they are no worse for wear.

'I was hoping these rock samples you brought me would have some hint of sparkle in them, but while there are salt-crystals embedded within them, there is little else of value. And yet I saw...'

Gangur falls quiet.

'I heard the calls of some lizards or worms coming from the heights of the island to the south. How about you look to combat those creatures and retrieve some more rock samples from their lair? I think I am just about dried out enough to make my way back to the ship, and I will meet you there when you have fulfilled this last request of mine.''I heard the calls of some lizards or worms coming from the heights of the island to the south. How about you look to combat those creatures and retrieve some more rock samples from their lair? I think I am just about dried out enough to make my way back to the ship, and I will meet you there when you have fulfilled this last request of mine.'Gangur turns the corroded rock samples you retrieved over and over in his hands, but his scowl deepens the longer he looks at them.

'These rocks are like the others. The only difference is they are melted by the corrosive breath of the drakes. I admit it is not what I was hoping to see. I thought Khôltekh the Cunning might have gotten the shiny material that was embedded in his medallion from these islands, but if so its location remains a secret.'

He sighs heavily and then looks at you with a more open expression than you are accustomed to seeing on his face. He seems almost haunted.

'When I fell in the water I swallowed too much sea-water, and I felt the life leaving me. I cannot tell you now if my eyes were open or shut, but I believed them to be open, and before the blackness took me... I saw it.'

Gangur pauses, as if gathering the strength to go on. You let him wait until he is ready to continue.

'It was a great shelled beast, all tentacles and siphons, and its spiral shell was encrusted with the shining jewel of my dreams, glimmering like an opal but with every facet a riot of colour. Huge the creature was, but it paid me no mind even as it filled the great expanse of my vision. And then it was gone.

'Was this the dream of a dying dwarf, ${PLAYER}? Maybe it was. But I cannot forget the sight of it. That vision will haunt me to my last day... I know it.

'Thank you for listening to my story, but please do not tell anyone else of it. I will try to put it from my mind and help with the mission... as much as I can.'Gimli and Legolas have begun to gather food to help your crew survive among the Shield Isles, and they could use your help.Various beasts of the Shield Isles can provide your crew the food necessary to their survival.Collect meat from beasts of the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gimli is at the northern tip of the island of Zamarzîr.Legolas is at the northern tip of Zamarzîr.Talk to Legolas at the northern tip of ZamarzîrLegolas has felled a number of birds throughout Zamarzîr, and asked you to retrieve their meat and his arrows.Retrieve meat and arrows from felled birds throughout Zamarzîr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Legolas intended to return to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.Gimli has returned to the Wave-hunter, in the Shield Isles.Talk to Gimli at Voyage's End'I have not seen islands like these before, ${PLAYER}... they are very different than the lands with which I am familiar! By Durin's Beard! Am I to believe that the folk who live here are used to the heat and the damp, and would find their lack in the North uncomfortable even as I am accustomed to it? That is a wonder to me.

'Legolas and I departed the wreck of the Wave-hunter not to see the sights, of course, but to hunt for game animals of the Shield Isles. The Elf is still out hunting; he should be back before too long. When we have found enough meat to bring back, we will both return to the ship. Would you like to help us in our hunt? Of course you would!''Legolas and I departed the wreck of the Wave-hunter not to see the sights, of course, but to hunt for game animals of the Shield Isles. When we have found enough meat to bring back, we will return to the ship. Would you like to help us in our hunt? Of course you would!''How fares the hunt?''Ah, you did very well, my friend! I will add the meat you gathered to that which I collected, and when we return the crew will be very pleased.

'How did Legolas fare in his hunt? He kept his attention upon the trees, seeking for birds to bring down with his bow-skill and his fine Elf-arrows. He will be very embarrassed if we bring back more meat than he does! If that is so we can say we all shared equally in the task.

'But you and I will know the truth of it, ${PLAYER}. Ha ha ha!''How did the Elf fare on his own hunt? Did he prove as successful as we did?''Gimli's jesting is at an end, ${PLAYER}, for I did bring a number of birds to earth. Once we find where they fell the dwarf will see that there will be plenty of meat for the crew of the Wave-hunter.

'Can I ask you to retrieve the birds and the arrows with which I felled them? You will find them along the route I took back here, to the south-west. Each bird took but a single arrow, my friend. My aim remains true, even among the trees of these islands and from such distance as necessity required I shoot.

'We will see you back at the Wave-hunter when you have done this.''Can I ask you to retrieve the birds and the arrows with which I felled them? You will find them along the route I took back here, to the south-west. Each bird took but a single arrow, my friend. My aim remains true, even among the trees of these islands and from such distance as necessity required I shoot.

'We will see you back at the Wave-hunter when you have done this.''Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}. Our crew will eat well for as long as they must remain here among the Shield Isles, and that eases my mind. I am sure it eases yours as well.

'I should tell you something I observed while I was on the hunt. I felled a number of the birds I saw winging among the trees of Zamarzîr, the southern island... but there was one target that I could not bring myself to down. It was a mighty creature, and though I saw it from a great distance it appeared to me of tremendous size. It brought to my mind the Great Eagles Gwaihir and his brother Landroval.

'I did not release my arrow. Whatever the creature may have been, something told me not to harm it. I do not know if it would give us the same treatment, ${PLAYER}. Walk carefully if you tread again on Zamarzîr, just in case.''Walk carefully if you tread again on Zamarzîr, just in case. I do not know if that mighty creature is a friend or a foe.''The crew of the Wave-hunter will have food to eat tonight, thanks to the three of us, ${PLAYER}!

'Did Legolas tell you about the great bird he witnessed from afar? I told him it is probably not one of the Great Eagles, because while the flight for one such as Gwaihir or Landroval would not be as long a journey as it was for us, what reason would they have to make it? No, it must be something else. I say he should have filled it with arrows, because anything as large as he describes likely feasts upon anything smaller, and we surely qualify!

'I hope in this case I am wrong, and Legolas will not regret his choice to spare this creature. But if it was up to me I would not have hesitated. The Longbeards have little patience or mercy for monsters, and such a giant bird sounds like a monster to me until it proves it is a friend, as the Eagles have done.

'I say remain wary, ${PLAYER}!'Gwallang the Limlinn seems to be searching for a new home among the dangerous Shield Isles.Meat from the nearby beetles on the western side of the island may help feed Gwallang the Limlinn.Collect meat from the beetles north of Jeb Khâtel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gwallang the Limlinn is on one of the north-western islands of the Shield Isles.Gwallang the Limlinn flew to the south-east, and you should look for him among the islands to the west of Voyage's End.Find Gwallang the Limlinn among the islands west of Voyage's EndGwallang the Limlinn is among the islands west of Voyage's End.Talk to Gwallang the Limlinn among the islands west of Voyage's EndThe ground beneath Gwallang has proved unstable!Help GwallangGwallang the Limlinn flew to the south-east, and you should look for him along the coast of Zamarzîr.Find Gwallang the Limlinn along the coast of ZamarzîrGwallang the Limlinn is along the coast of Zamarzîr in the Shield Isles.Talk to Gwallang the Limlinn along the coast of ZamarzîrGwallang the Limlinn hops up and down before flying to several nearby trees and testing their branches, scrutinizing the bark and leaves closely with his tiny, sharp eyes. You can't be quite sure, but it feels to you as if he is looking for a suitable place to build a nest!

If so, he'll want easy access to meat. Perhaps the meat of nearby beetles on the western side of the island will suffice. You should bring some to him and see if he likes it.Gwallang the Limlinn might like meat from the nearby beetles on the western side of the island.Gwallang pecks at some of the beetle meat, but it is impossible to gauge his reaction. After a few bites, he flutters into the air and peers away southward. Something in that direction seems to bother him.Gwallang chirps a welcome at you.Gwallang perches atop a sandy mound, chirping happily at you. He peers around at the surrounding area, taking it all in, apparently deciding if this is a good place to build a nest.Gwallang chirps at you.As you arrive, a huge shadow passes overhead, blanketing the immediate area in darkness. Gwallang jumps up and down with fright. He shakes out his feathers, and while you cannot understand his language the message is clear: the Shield Isles are not a suitable place for him to build a nest.

Gwallang's journey will continue, and perhaps when you leave the Shield Isles the next place he tries will be free of noise, bog-lurkers, and giant birds.Sigileth wants to search the various wrecks that populate Shedax Khîn to ensure none of them carried her brother to his death.Sigileth asked you to search several of the shipwrecks at Shedax Khîn in search of her brother.Sigileth is further south of the wrecks you investigated in Shedax Khîn.Talk to Sigileth further south of the wrecks you investigated in Shedax KhînSigileth handed you a note she found within a bottle discovered on one of the wrecks in Shedax Khîn.Read the note Sigileth discovered inside a bottle in one of the wrecks of Shedax KhînSigileth is south of the wrecks you investigated in Shedax Khîn.'Our ship was more fortunate than some of the vessels torn apart by the Grinding Jaws, ${PLAYER}. See where the hulks lie, their hulls smashed upon the rocks, their masts ripped away? Did the ship which carried my brother toward Umbar fall prey to a similar fate?

'Search the wrecks in this lagoon for any sign that the ships of Nakási Wave-reaper or her ally Tatháta succumbed to the rocks of Shedax Khîn. I hope and believe they did not... but for Corudan's sake we must be certain.''Search the wrecks in this lagoon for any sign that the ships of Nakási Wave-reaper or her ally Tatháta succumbed to the rocks of Shedax Khîn. I hope and believe they did not... but for Corudan's sake we must be certain.''I found a bottle wedged into a crack on the deck of that nearby ship, ${PLAYER}, the cork still held in place. Inside there was a parchment with writing upon it. Read it and tell me what you think.''Read the note I gave you and tell me what you think.''By our search of these wrecks we know the ship that carried my brother Corudan to Umbar did not suffer the same fate as they. The sailor who wrote this note, Phêlex, may be dead, and his love Khâsha will never know what evil befell him, but my brother lives still. One is beyond our reach, but the other is not.

'I know the Corsairs of Umbar by their evil reputation, and while the Kindred of the Coins may bear a different name and pretend to be something else, the manner of their crimes seems to me the same. Phêlex suffered at the hands of Corsairs; was what happened to my brother at the hands of Nakási Wave-reaper and her Kindred any different?

'We can do nothing for he who wrote this letter, or for Khâsha who waited in vain for his return, but my brother is not yet beyond saving. There is hope our search for him will continue, and end with success. That is hope enough for me, ${PLAYER}.'Sirgon wants to make use of his experience sailing around the Shield Isles to help you learn the geography with which you must now deal.Sirgon has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> over your surroundings at three separate locations: the beach across the lagoon to the south of Sirgon, the beach to the north-west of the Wave-hunter, and the beach on the western side of the island.Sirgon is located at Voyage's End on the Shield Isles.Talk to Sirgon at Voyage's End'Do not look so crestfallen, my friend! You must see that the Valar smile upon the Wave-hunter, and upon our voyage! We have our lives, after all, and the successful conclusion of your mission still lies ahead! This is not an ending, but a beginning! I have lost friends to the rocks that guard the Shield Isles, it is true... but today the strong hull of the Wave-hunter and the resilience of his crew has delivered us here safely. Rejoice for that, and celebrate the good fortune and the blessing of the Powers that aided in its accomplishment!

'I have not set foot upon this island chain in many years, but it will take me only moments to refamiliarize myself with them. If you will go to several locations and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb>, your report may help me remember the geography of these islands. Perhaps you can start at the beach across the lagoon to the south, a beach to the north-west of the Wave-hunter, and the beach on the western side of this island.''I have not set foot upon this island chain in many years, but it will take me only moments to refamiliarize myself with them. If you will go to several locations and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb>, your report may help me remember the geography of these islands. Perhaps you can start at the beach across the lagoon to the south, a beach to the north-west of the Wave-hunter, and the beach on the western side of this island.''What did you see, my friend?'

You tell Sirgon what you saw from each of the locations you scouted, and he nods agreeably.

'Aye, it is coming back to me now. Let us see what I can remember.

'This island chain is a rocky archipelago composed of numerous isles running from north-west to south-east, but three of these are larger than the others. The southernmost island is the largest, Zamarzîr, and it lies in view of the cape upon which Umbar stands. It is a place of jungle and mountain, and when I served the Steward of Gondor in years past it was the haunt of pirates and freebooters. We left it alone as much as we could, for it was a dangerous place.

'The middle island is nearest to us, and it is Bakhjâd. The jagged rocks that surround Bakhjâd are responsible for the reputation of this place as the bane of sailors, for the dangerous currents surrounding the Shield Isles sweep strong ships and braver men to their dooms. I have lost good friends to those rocks, which the men of Umbar call Shedax Khîn. I understand that there may be a settlement somewhere in the centre of Bakhjâd, but I have not seen it.

'The northern island is uninhabited. I believe it is called Jeb Khâtel, but the steep cliffs surrounding it make it inaccessible from the coast.

'This is a place of adventure, ${PLAYER}! If we meet the challenge it sets before us, we are certain to survive and see the successful completion of our mission!'Daxamat knows the danger of being stranded on an island without any supplies, and is eager to avoid that unfortunate fate.Barrels float in the water not far from the Wave-hunter, and other supplies have fetched up upon the nearby coastline.Collect floating barrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect ship supplies along the coast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Daxamat stands by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.'Tell me what I can do to help, ${PLAYER}. I should have tried to keep the crew from scattering across the isles, but I did not think to say anything until it was too late!'

You ask Daxamat what he believes can be done now to ensure that the loss of the Wave-hunter does not spell the failure of your mission, and he scratches his chin. 'Many of our supplies fell overboard when the Wave-hunter ran aground,' he mumbles. 'Perhaps we should recover what we can?'

You agree with the Corsair's assessment, and encourage him to help you recover the lost supplies.

'Yes! One step at a time. I can manage that. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We will retrieve the supplies we can. Some of them may be floating just offshore, but others may have fetched up along the coasts of the nearby islands.''I will help you retrieve the supplies that fell overboard when the Wave-hunter ran aground. Some of them may be floating just offshore, but others may have fetched up along the coasts of the nearby islands.''This is a good start, is it not? I will bring the supplies we recovered inside the Wave-hunter to protect them from the wind and the rain. We will be glad to have them if we must remain on the Shield Isles for some days, and the weather here is changeable.

'I told you that Jajax and I grew up on the island of Zamarzîr, to the south-east, among the freebooters. There was a settlement there called Halrax, home to thieves and cutpurses, and it could be violent at times but it was home. I might have stayed there forever and known nothing of the wider world, but when Jajax decided to leave I went with him, and did not look back.

'I wish my brother were here. I wonder what he is up to now?

'Ah, never mind, ${PLAYER}. I have to bring these supplies inside. There will be time for thinking later on, I do not doubt it. Right now is the time for survival!'Nauriel has no patience for any delays, and has come to Mâr Naphra in search of information that will help her rescue her son Thorongil from the Kindred of the Coins.Nauriel stands by a posted notice outside Mâr Naphra.Examine the posted notice outside Mâr NaphraNauriel stands outside Mâr Naphra, considering the bounty posted on the Kindred of the Coins by the Heirs of Castamir.Talk to Nauriel outside Mâr NaphraIf you are to get an audience with Saklaphêl, you will need to attract the attention of the residents of Mâr Naphra.Defeat aggressive residents of Mâr Naphra, and make it noisy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Have you made enough of a commotion in Mâr Naphra?Wait for someone to notice the ruckus you createdA man called Galadaith has called for you from atop a tall building on the western side of Mâr Naphra.Talk to Galadaith from atop the tall buildings on the western side of Mâr NaphraNauriel waits for you outside Mâr Naphra.Talk to Nauriel outside Mâr Naphra'I could not wait, ${PLAYER}. My son Thorongil is still a captive of the Kindred of the Coins, and I care not the nature of the delay that keeps me from him... I will defy it and see it overcome! Neither storm nor foe will keep me from him.

'I have learned the name of this settlement. It is Mâr Naphra, and from the sounds coming from within it is a place where vile sea-brigands gather to fight and drink and gamble. But look at this! It appears it is also a haven for the Heirs of Castamir and those who support them. Just see who has posted a bounty of interest to us outside the village!''The name of this settlement is Mâr Naphra, and from the sounds coming from within it is a place where vile sea-brigands gather to fight and drink and gamble. But look at this! It appears it is also a haven for the Heirs of Castamir and those who support them. Just see who has posted a bounty of interest to us outside the village!'Heed these words, and profit by them!

For the CAPTURE or DEATH of each of the following leaders of the so-called "Kindred of the Coins," the generous Heirs of Castamir offer the following rewards:

<rgb=#FFFF00>Azagath the Sea-shadow</rgb> --- five chests of gold phârzi, and two of silver gîmli

<rgb=#FFFF00>Belondor of the Fleet-fast</rgb> --- one chest of gold phârzi, and one of silver gîmli

<rgb=#FFFF00>Hármelak Golden-hand</rgb> --- her weight in silver gîmli, multiplied by five hundred

Know that the CAPTURE or DEATH of any others who claim to belong to the Kindred of the Coins will be rewarded. Speak with Galadaith within Mâr Naphra for more information.

So it is ordered,

Saklaphêl, Wife of Balakhôr the Scourge and True Ruler of Umbar Baharbêl and the Surrounding Lands'It has been said in the Green Hills that the enemy of one's enemy may be a friend, for awhile, and so it seems it is today. The Heirs of Castamir were a dire threat to Gondor, but if the widow of Balakhôr the Scourge intends to reward mercenaries for slaying the serpents who took my son, I cry "do so!" and without hesitation!

'The Shield Isles may teem with bounty-hunters now, and their victory may be ours also, for without these leaders the Kindred must fall. Learning the identity of the mercenaries Saklaphêl has hired for this purpose can only be to our benefit.

'Are you prepared to make some noise within Mâr Naphra, ${PLAYER}? If you take on the role of a deadly and dangerous bounty-hunter who fears nothing, I believe the one called Galadaith may invite you to speak with Saklaphêl directly. Go cause some trouble... let us see what happens.''Are you prepared to make some noise within Mâr Naphra, ${PLAYER}? If you take on the role of a deadly and dangerous bounty-hunter who fears nothing, I believe the one called Galadaith may invite you to speak with Saklaphêl directly. Go cause some trouble... let us see what happens.''Has Galadaith noticed you yet? He surely must have!''I have not seen you before, stranger. From the commotion downstairs I take it you have a taste for trouble? An expensive taste that could be satisfied with some gold phârzi or silver gîmli? Did you see the bounties posted outside the village? If you have a disregard for danger and some skill in combat, as I deem you do, it may be of some interest to you. What do you call yourself?'

You think it over carefully, and give your answer.

'"The ${CLASS}," you say? Well, your name will spread across all of the Zîrar Tarka if you claim one or more of the bounties!'

You ask Galadaith if you could speak with the wealthy patron who ordered the bounty so you may ask her who else has already taken on the task, and he shakes his head.

'The widow Saklaphêl sees no one. You do your business with me, friend. But I can tell you that a number of dangerous sorts have already announced their intentions to claim some or all of the bounties. If you are new to the Isles you may not know them, but their reputations speak for themselves. You would be wise not to delay any longer than you have to, or you will miss your chance. Some of the deadliest bounty-hunters in this part of the world seek Saklaphêl's reward, and most have reasons of their own to hate the Kindred who rule now in Umbar Baharbêl. Good luck to you, ${CLASS}.''A number of dangerous sorts have already announced their intentions to claim some or all of the bounties. If you are new to the Isles you may not know them, but their reputations speak for themselves. You would be wise not to delay any longer than you have to, or you will miss your chance. Some of the deadliest bounty-hunters in this part of the world seek Saklaphêl's reward, and most have reasons of their own to hate the Kindred who rule now in Umbar Baharbêl. Good luck to you, ${CLASS}.''How did you fare within Mâr Naphra, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Nauriel about your meeting with Galadaith, and what you learned about the bounties issued by Saklaphêl.

'I would be very interested to learn more about these bounty-hunters, for we might make use of them when the time comes to rescue my son from the Kindred of the Coins. Whether they will provide a distraction only, or can be used to remove some of the pieces from the table entirely, remains to be seen. But it appears we have some new friends to make.

'Keep your eyes open, and I will see you back at the Wave-hunter when I am finished scouting around here.'Javish is troubled by a group of renegade Corsairs who refuse to play nice with rules of Mâr Naphra.Javish has asked you to initiate negotiations between a renegade Corsair group which poses a threat to the status quo in Mâr Naphra.

The meeting location should be among the shallows to the south-east.Talk to Adranax at the agreed upon locationAdranax planned to betray Javish all along. Javish should know that you had no choice but to defend yourself.

Javish can be found in Mâr Naphra.Talk to JavishJavish has no choice but to take Adranax's actions as an act of sedition. He asks that we punish the Corsairs before they can cause further chaos.

Khataj Mârsa can be found south-east of Mâr Naphra.Defeat Corsairs in Khataj Mârsa (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Corsairs at Khataj Mârsa have been punished. You should report to Javish your success.

Javish can be found in Mâr Naphra.Talk to Javish in Mâr Naphra'The rules here are simple. You follow them, and your life ain't forfeit.

'Seems we got ourselves a crew of Corsairs who think they're better than the lot of us. I reckon we will need an outside party to resolve matters.

'I've already set up the parley. Adranax is going to meet you at a cove south-east of Mâr Naphra.''What do we have here? You mean to tell me that Javish couldn't show up himself?

'This is going to make things difficult. instead of betraying my good friend Javish, I've got to end some poor lackey's life.

'This isn't personal, friend.''Well, I should've seen that coming. Could never trust a Corsair, eh?

'Anyways, I reckon we have no choice but to nip this in the bud. There's a reward in it for ya. Pay Khataj Mârsa a visit and take care of them before they cause more trouble for Mâr Naphra, would ya?''It didn't have to come to this. Us pirates need to stick together. If we don't, that'll be the best of us.

'I appreciate you sticking your neck out. It was a difficult task, but you proved your worth.'Find the many treasure caches hidden or left forgotten in the Shield Isles.Find the many treasure caches hidden or left forgotten in the Shield Isles.Find treasure caches in the Shield IslesHûrlub the Bellower does not seem to be hostile at all. He is agitated by the barbs of what seems to be spiders.Hûrlub the Bellower seems like a gentle creature. He has asked you to defeat spiders in Maj Khibi.Defeat spiders in Maj Khibi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The spiders should be less likely to bother Hûrlub now. You should speak to Hûrlub in Phadâl Bimai.

Phadâl Bimai can be found at the northern coast of Jeb Khâtel.Talk to Hûrlub the Bellower'You fight good, small thing.

'You not afraid of Hûrlub. Maybe Hûrlub make friend?

'Many leg ones. Crawlies. So many, they bully me. Keep Hûrlub from food.

'Can small thing make many leg ones no more?''Many legs gone?

'You did for Hûrlub? You friend me now. Hûrlub is happy.

'Ask a thing of Hûrlub. You have.

'This thing? It is done. Hûrlub not need big swing. Old toy.'You came across a man, defeated not by battle, but by a strange hammer jutting out of a stone.The rogue was tasked with delivering this hammer to the leader of Halrax, Ithurga.Pick up the hammerYou have successfully removed the strange hammer from the stone. According to the man, you should deliver the item to Ithurga.

Ithurga can be found in Halrax.The man's breathing is laboured, huffing and puffing against the large hammer, trying in vain to move it.

'Don't mind me.... I am here... on behalf of... Ithurga. He runs things... around Halrax.'

The man stops his efforts and wipes his brow, taking some time to compose himself.

'I'm supposed to remove this silly ornament and bring it to him.

'Myth and legend, and all that spooky stuff. Me? I don't believe it, but whatever the boss wants, he gets.'

The man moves to begin his struggles again, but stops to consider you.

'You reckon you can lift this?'The seasoned rogue studies you and notices something in your possession.

'Well, well, well. Seems my faithful minion failed. What did you do to him? Judging by that hammer there, you either took it from him or took it for him.'

You explain the situation to him.

'I suppose I should thank you for bringing me the hammer? That is, of course, if you arrive here with auspicious tidings and intend to release it to me.'Nargo is looking for help in patching up the dock at Halrax. He needs assistance in repairs and materials.Nargo asked you to harvest palm wood from the forest outside of the city and then repair the planks on the dock.Collect palm timber (${NUMBER}/6)Repair the damaged dock planks (${NUMBER}/10)You chopped down some nearby trees to collect palm timber and repaired the planks on the dock. Return to Nargo, on the Halrax docks, with the news.'The sea is a voracious beast consuming wood at a rate only surpassed by fire. Every day, I toil to repair this dock. Each night, when I slumber, I dream of hammering nails. And each morning, I awake to find more rot chewing away at the docks.

'I grow weary, friend. Could you help? I need palm wood from the trees in the wood to the east of the town. Can you collect those and repair the damaged planks?''I need palm timber from the woods surrounding Halrax. The trees are pliable and survive longer along the harsh sea-shore. Then, if you do not mind, repair the damaged planks along the dock.''What you have done for me may seem like that much effort. It is a great relief to me not having to deal with that monotonous life, even for a few moments. Thank you, friend.'You delivered what seems to be a replica of a forgotten myth.Ithurga suspects this is a replica and wants you to confirm all the rumours about this hammer from the town's residents.All the witnesses had varying tales, but a professor has told us Shereb knows of this hammer.

You can find Shereb in the most isolated part of Halrax.Confirm witness accounts 7/8You've gathered all the information you can from the townsfolk of Halrax. You now have a lead. You should talk to Ithurga.

Ithurga can be found in Halrax.Talk to Ithurga'You have my gratitude for helping my man out there. I'm afraid it was for naught.

'It's as I feared. It's a replica. There have been numerous accounts from the folks in town of having seen this thing.

'The only issue is that by all those accounts, none lead here.

'Why don't you go around and confirm all of the reports? Else we done all this for a novel trinket and nothin' more.''A mythical hammer? Dunno know what yer talkin about.

'If ye be needin' a smithy, we gots plenty.''A large hammer? I seen that, yea. Massive one isn't it?

'You'll find plenty of stolen goods and contraband in the shallows, I reckon.

'Lots of people lose their stuff around those parts all the time. I'm sure you can find your hammer there.''A mythological hammer, you say? Well, I have my fair share of tools working on cultivating the harsh land that is these islands.

'But never had a need for a giant hammer. Nope. Just me and my herbs.''A hammer? You think I get out lookin' for hammers?

'I only have one job in this town and that's not to look for hammers.''A hammer? Well, if I recall correctly, I heard tale in the tavern of a man passing through the shallows coming from the north.

'Talk of a wild freak of nature swinging around a hammer. Sadly, I have no more information for you.''A giant hammer? Well, you must be talking nonsense.

'That is the stuff of legend here on the isles. No one has seen the real one in ages.

'If I recall the texts correctly, it was Marâkh, Mother of Tempests. But honestly, a hammer controlling the storms? I am unconvinced such a weapon exists.''You're looking for Marâkh, Mother of Tempests?

'That is quite the endeavour you've undertaken. You know, many historians will argue the very existence of such a thing... but I place evidence high on my list, and where there is the mark of such a weapon existing, I cannot be but consumed by the possibilities.

'My good friend, who does most of the travelling so that I may have the most accurate information, may have something for you. His name is Shereb.

'You can find Shereb in the most isolated parts of Halrax.''I knew you'd be here sooner or later.

'The town stirs at the possible mention of Marâkh, Mother of Tempests.

'But this isn't a weapon you can just go and retrieve. It's risky.

'In case I can't convince you to give up your chase - there exists an island in Jeb Khâtel, past the shallows to the north-west.

'I warn you, this will not be journey free of hardship. Prepare yourself accordingly.''I knew it.

'There were definitely several inconsistencies in many of the reports of this hammer's existence.

'So now our best lead takes us up north to Jeb Khâtel.

'I must ask you this last favour, because though the journey seems fraught with danger, I see in you a capable leader.

'Come back with this hammer, or come back alive. I will not allow another blind rush into darkness, with your life being forfeit.'Anyâmat harbours aspirations of being a great shanty-man.Anyâmat has worked hard to write new verses for a shanty and would love to show them off to you.

Talk to Anyâmat in Halrax.Talk to Anyâmat'${PLAYER}, I'm glad you are here. I have had much to think about after our adventures.''${PLAYER}, it's good to see you again. I had hoped I would have a new shanty to share with you, but despite our adventures, when I began to write, the words did not come to me.

'After the rush of excitement wore off, all I felt was tired and worn out. The small cuts I earned from fighting that big crab sting, and my legs ache from dashing about the island. And then I thought, what if the sailor's life is not for me?

'But then I thought of the freebooters we met, how welcoming and giving they were. I had expected them to be rough around the edges. Are my perceptions of life at sea shaped by tall tales and silly stories?

'Have I been chasing a false ideal?

'Thank you for travelling with me today and for keeping me safe. I did not get what I wanted out of today, but maybe that is all right.

'May our paths cross again.'Muzmák wants to attempt something he's never done before: record a story.Muzmák has asked you to hunt beetles in Ghax-hophra for beetle shells.

Ghax-hophra can be found north of Kafagur.Hunt beetles in Ghax-hophra for shells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You've collected a wide variety of colourful beetle shells.

You should bring them back to Muzmák at Kafagur.'${RACE} -- Shúkurz says you're the one who did us a good turn back in Gundabad. Thanks for that.

'How did we get here? Well, it's a long story, one I can barely believe myself. I'm getting tired of repeating it, though, so I think I ought to put it on paper. But to do that, I need to make pigment first.

'Say, if you're looking to help... there's a beetle warren to the north called Ghax-hophra. There's got to be plenty of beetles with colourful shells there that I can use.''Well, would you look at that! Plenty of different colours to work with here.

'I've never done this sort of thing before. After all, there's no time to create anything nice when you're being forced to fight and survive all day.

'I'm glad for this change of pace. It suits me better.'A resident of Halrax has lost something precious to him. No, not that precious.Etinan has asked you to find the necklace his partner gave him on the beach of Baj Khatûg.

Baj Khatûg is an island off the eastern shore of Zamarzîr.Find Etinan's necklaceYou have found the necklace and should return it to Etinan.

Etinan can be found in Halrax.As you approach the man you notice that he seethes with wrath so smouldering it would make even the most hot-headed Rune-keeper blush.

'Ah how could this be?! I could have sworn I was wearing it when we left the beach! Could I have left it there somehow?

'Adventurer! Could I ask something of you? I was at Baj Khatûg with my dearest Zimâr this morning. There, he presented me with a beautiful necklace. I cannot find it now, and I'm terrified that I may have somehow left it on the beach! I'm to meet with him at the tavern tonight. He can't know that I lost it. Could you find it for me?

'What does it look like? The gemstone is blue like his eyes and cut sharp like his clever wit! In the sun, it shines as bright as his smile!

'Also it's on a sort of brown leather cord. Metal necklace chains irritate my skin.''Ah, the knot on the cord must have come undone and slipped off my neck! Thank you so much for retrieving it for me.'To be accepted in Halrax, you must appease Ithurga, the stolid leader of the settlement.Ithurga wants you to collect debts from residents holding back their tithes. He directed you to scout the town for Methen, Akubis, Dagan, and Yigo to collect their debts.Collect Methen's debtCollect Akubis's debtCollect Yigo's debtCollect Dagan's debtYou collected the four debts. Return to Ithurga at his abode in lower Halrax.Ithurga directed you to purchase a bag of coins that matter to him from the vault-keeper in Halrax. The vault is in the upper ward of the township. Return to Ithurga with your tithe.'Good, I'm grateful for the understanding.
 
'Respect amongst the citizens of Halrax is earned and lost through deed and effort. Some folks test my resolve by eschewing their tithe and letting that debt grow too long. If you want to prove your value to Halrax, see these debts collected. Yes?''I don't know where you'll find them all. I know they frequent different parts of the township and are derelict in their tithes. Do this for me, and you'll be on your way to being accepted here in Halrax.''You'll not be the last lackey that Ithurga sends to pry the tithe from my hands. But you'll surely be my latest victim. Let's get this over with, you worthless cur.''Ithurga has some nerve in sending a fresh-faced arrival like you to collect my debt. This place is supposed to be about respect and decency. And he treats me like this? No offence, stranger, but this doesn't end well for you.''I feel bad for you, stranger. You've no idea the bee nest you've just struck. This matter ends only one way. You trampled underfoot. Draw your weapon of choice. The least I can do is give you a sporting chance.''Well, this is galling. Have you even bought into Halrax yet? Have you paid your tithe yet? Or is this a ploy by Ithurga to get you into the plan? Oh, I understand now.'

He laughs.

'Brilliant plan, Ithurga, send the new fish from the sea to do the work of those who've paid the price. Fine. Take my debt.''You return and look no worse for wear. I heard about Dagan.'

He shrugs.

'Unfortunate. Dagan's crew is worse off without him, but he made his choices, lived, and died as he wanted.

'Dagan's untimely death is not the matter at hand, however. We must discuss your future here.

'You've done what I asked, but to finalize the deal and earn protection through the thoroughfares of Halrax I need your tithe.

'Visit the vault-keeper here in town and exchange your coin for a bag of coins that matter to me.''Excellent. You've done well, friend. You are free to move throughout Halrax without fear of being accosted. I'll ensure that everyone learns of the change in your status.

'Now that we've come to an understanding. There is something further I ask of you.'The increase in wounded Kafagur hunters has left Kúlthrak bereft of spider-web bandages.Spider-webs can be found at Maj Khibi, north-west of Kafagur.Collect spider-webs at Maj Khibi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You've collected enough spider-webs.

You should bring them back to Kúlthrak at Kafagur.'After treating so many injured hunters, I've barely got enough spider-web left to cover Nargai's wounds.

'If you've got the guts, head north-west to Maj Khibi and grab me some. And try not to get injured yourself; I don't want to have to treat you too.''Oh, good. You made it back in one piece, too.

'Nargai will be back on their feet in no time.'Zagdúr will need to be convinced that you mean no harm to the people of Kafagur.You should complete quests in Jeb Khâtel to win the Orcs' trust.You have helped the inhabitants of Kafagur.

You should return to Zagdúr in Kafagur and talk to her.Talk to Zagdúr in KafagurAccording to Zagdúr, a Man was sighted outside of Kafagur.

You should talk to the guard Grúshul for more information.Talk to Grúshul'Shúkurz's friendship with you means something to me, but I require some more convincing.

'Should you wish to stay in Kafagur, then help my people. Prove to me that you are someone worth trusting.

'If not, then heed my warning: leave us be.''You have proven that you are worthy of my trust, ${CLASS}. Now I would call upon you to aid us.

'The guards have sighted a strange Man outside Kafagur -- perhaps the outlander you spoke of before. Shúkurz left in hopes of talking to the man peacefully, but he has not returned.

'Grúshul will have more information.''Here to help your friend?

'We saw the Man sneaking around near the trees, but he fled after Shúkurz tried to approach. Then the fool ignored my protests and ran after him!'You accepted a bounty to eliminate the dread Akraz the Vile for violating a tenuous truce.Seek Yitro at his home in lower Halrax and let him know that you are interested in assisting in bringing the Uruk Akrax the Vile to justice.Speak with Yitro at his home in lower HalraxYitro directed you to find a secluded spot east and north out of Halrax in which to feign weakness to draw out Akraz the Vile.Find a secluded location east outside of HalraxFind and eliminate Akraz the VileYitro awaits word of your battle against Akraz the Vile at his home in lower Halrax. Return to him.Bounty: Akraz the Vile

An Uruk named Akraz the Vile threatens to destroy the truce between the freebooters of Halrax and the Kafagur Orcs. His actions include waylaying travellers, preying on the weak and weary, robbery, and murder. 

Interested parties should seek guidance from Yitro at his home in lower Halrax.'It's good to see that my post is drawing some interest. The matter is simple. Akraz the Vile lives up to his name. He stalks the paths east and north of our township, preying on the tired or weary travellers, waylaying them, robbing them, or worse, leaving them for dead.

'We made a truce with the Kafagur Orcs, and if this menace isn't brought to heel, then that truce could soon break.

'Head out east and north, and feign weakness in a secluded area. You will draw the villain out.''We're better off with the likes of Akraz removed. We want to find a way to live in peace, but some still want to burn the world. You've done a good thing today.

'You earned this.'You accepted a bounty to hunt the salamander Nakhrûd to recover a locket and deliver proof of the beast's defeat.The bounty requests the recovery of a silver-inlaid locket and proof that the best, Nakhrûd, was slain. Nakhrûd is said to nest among its brood to the east of Halrax.After a quick battle, you dispatched Nakhrûd and took its fang, recovered the locket, and prepared to return to Hannax in the town of Halrax.Bounty: Nakhrûd

Bring a precious silver-inlaid locket lost near the creature's lair and proof of the salamander's defeat to Hannax in Halrax. Nakhrûd makes its lair among its brood to the east of Halrax.'Oh ho! Look at that locket.'

His demeanor suddenly shifts.

'Oh, and the salamander's fang. The locket belonged to my late mother. This locket's been in the family for generations, and you're the one to recover it for me. So, you're the one who'll reap the reward. It's not much, but it's all I have.

'I hope you understand. You're so kind.'Sirgon's joy of exploring the Shield Isles has soured a little with the arrival of some new information.Sirgon has asked to meet you to the west so he can discuss something with you.Find the location to the west where Sirgon wants to talk with youSirgon is west of Voyage's End, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Sirgon on the rocky outcroppingSirgon has fallen silent.Wait for Sirgon to gather his thoughtsSirgon is west of Voyage's End, ready to continue his tale.Talk to Sirgon on the rocky outcroppingSirgon has fallen silent once again.Wait for Sirgon to gather his thoughts once againSirgon is west of Voyage's End, ready to conclude his tale.Talk to Sirgon on the rocky outcropping'Let us not speak of it here. Meet me to the west of here, ${PLAYER}.

'It may be I am worried for nothing, and it is not the same man. But my heart says it must be.''Let us not speak of it here. Meet me to the west.''Thank you.''Thank you for indulging me in this, ${PLAYER}. I owe you so much for allowing me to join the crew of the Wave-hunter and come with you on this voyage. I would follow you to the very ends of the earth, know that I would, and never complain or say to you a cross word. I have always done my duty as I saw it, first for the Steward of Gondor and then for the King Elessar, and now for you, as the leader of this mission. So I will not still my tongue now, and I will tell you the source of my fear. May it prove without base!

'The name spoken by the young scribe: Belondor. I knew a Belondor when I was a young man. He was born in Anfalas and grew up along the Langstrand, and we both served at the command of the Steward Denethor. Belondor and I were well-nigh inseparable, and together sailed this very Bay of Belfalas and up the coast of Gondor to more distant shores. He was at my wedding, by the Valar, and gave the toast before all the gathered company! Celebros had me keep the stuffed birds he gave us for a wedding-gift in my hall of keepsakes, even when later events made their reminder a painful one.

'We rose in the estimation of the Steward. Even as I was made master of the fleets of Gondor, Belondor was named Warden of the Firth, and worked faithfully to keep the city of Umbar under guard, its pirates quelled and under control. He was an empathic guardian of the city, fair and just to the Umbari people, and they loved him. But this love proved to have a cost.''The Steward Denethor came to believe that Belondor cared more for the people of Umbar than he did for his native Gondor, and he distrusted the man he had named Warden of the Firth. He believed Belondor had fallen under the sway of the Church of the All Seeing, a religion that had at the time a small, though growing, presence in the city of Umbar. This was impossible to believe, and even today I do not believe it, but the Steward had other reasons to distrust Belondor.

'My old friend had fallen in love with an Umbari noblewoman named Mêshka. I do not know how the Steward came to learn of this, but the rumours eventually came even to the White City. There must have been spies aboard one or more of Belondor's ships, or lurking in the court of Mêshka's home... but I cannot say for certain. When paired with Belondor's recent missives, which counseled mercy and fairness for the Umbari people, these whispers painted a clear picture of betrayal that the Steward of Gondor could not disbelieve.

'He commanded the master of his navy to pursue the traitor Belondor, relieve him of his duties, and bring him back to Gondor. I could not refuse the command, ${PLAYER}.''I am not a man for whom deceit comes easily, ${PLAYER}, but I could not think my old friend a traitor without good cause. On any other day, a call to dinner at my manor-house would have been the signal for a time of merriment and joyful reunion, but on this day it was a lure. Belondor answered the summons, for he had no reason to suspect the orders given to me by the Steward Denethor. Over dinner I asked him where lay his loyalties... and his answer did not dispel my worries.

'"They lie with Umbar Baharbêl, the City of Sails, my old friend," he said to me. "They lie with my Mêshka, to whom I am betrothed. And only then do they lie with Gondor. Can a man not serve three loves equally in his heart, if he is wise and fair?"

'"The Steward Denethor does not think so," I told him, and our raised voices would have proven to me that our friendship was at an end, even if the drawn swords had not followed. Each of us sustained injuries in that duel, and Belondor fled through the shadowed streets of Pelargir to where his ship lay moored. For three days I pursued him in my own vessel across the tumultuous Bay, when at last he dared draw too near the Grinding Jaws; among the rocks of Shedax Khîn his ship perished. Some of his crew we rescued, but of Belondor there was no sign, and I believed him drowned, lost at sea. The Steward Denethor praised me for the pursuit, but I mourned lost Belondor, and cursed the duty that made me drive my friend to his death. But I cursed it silently, for still I served the Steward.'Belondor is not the first wayward voyager to return from death among the Shield Isles, and he will not be the last.Nauriel has returned to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles and will surely have a plan.Talk to Nauriel at Voyage's EndNauriel believes you should ask the folk who live in Halrax, on the island of Zamarzîr, what they know about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl.Daxamat has come to Halrax in search of more information, and can be found at the bottom of the hill on the eastern side of the city.Talk to Daxamat on the eastern side of Halrax, at the bottom of the hillManadhon, the bartender at Halrax, may be willing to tell you about Driftwood, one of the bounty hunters hired by Saklaphêl.Nauriel is back at the Wave-hunter, waiting for information about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl.Talk to Nauriel at Voyage's End'The Belondor that belongs now to the Kindred of the Coins may not be the same man... but in my heart I know he must be. Did he survive the wreck of his ship during my pursuit, and come to make a desperate living upon the wild Shield Isles? He did not hold hatred for Gondor in his heart before that night, whatever the Steward may have believed, but afterwards...? No man could do otherwise.

'I cannot know by what paths he returned to Umbar, but when he did it seems he found others who shared his mind. Did he rise through the ranks of the Kindred, or perhaps he was there at its founding? Now, at least, he holds a position with enough standing to warrant one of Saklaphêl's bounties!'

Sirgon stares at you unhappily.

'I was so pleased to sail again, ${PLAYER}. I had consigned these feelings of guilt to the past, and let the passing of the years dull their pain. But if Belondor did not drown on that night, if he now leads the Kindred of the Coins that hold Thorongil and your Elf-friend captive... I fear that the history between us may put both of those lives in greater danger than we believed. And all because I thought I missed the Sea... but I earned my own share of guilt upon the waters, ${PLAYER}. I had thought it gone, but it is never truly gone, is it?'

You tell Sirgon that it is the mission of the Wave-hunter to rescue Nauriel's son Thorongil and your friend Corudan from the Kindred of the Coins, no matter who comprises its membership. He nods, reluctantly.

'Aye. It must be so. But you must tell the Lady Nauriel what I have told you. If her son may be further endangered by this account, she deserves to know of it.''I must ask you to tell the Lady Nauriel what I have told you. If her son may be further endangered by this account, she deserves to know of it.''You have the look of someone who bears bad tidings, ${PLAYER}, but with our current situation as it is I cannot imagine what could be worse.'

You tell Nauriel, briefly, of Sirgon's belief that "Belondor of the Fleet-fast" may have once been a friend of his. She raises an eyebrow at you and puts her hand on the hilt of her sword, toying with the favour tied there by her husband Carandolion.

'It matters not to me, ${PLAYER}, unless Sirgon thinks to stand with the Kindred of the Coins against us when the time comes to rescue my son. Do you think he might?

'But that is still some time away; we must first leave these islands and reach the City of the Corsairs. Daxamat and some others of the crew have gone to the settlement of Halrax on the southern island of Zamarzîr to see what they can learn of the bounty-hunters Saklaphêl has likely employed. Can I ask you to also speak with residents of Halrax about this? Once we have learned what we can about them, we may be able to make use of them in our rescue of Thorongil, as we discussed.''Daxamat and some others of the crew have gone to the settlement of Halrax on the southern island of Zamarzîr to see what they can learn of the bounty-hunters Saklaphêl has likely employed. Can I ask you to also speak with residents of Halrax about this? Once we have learned what we can about them, we may be able to make use of them in our rescue of Thorongil, as we discussed.''Nauriel sent you here to ask for information about Saklaphêl's bounty-hunters? How did you fare?'

You reluctantly tell Daxamat that the folk of Halrax were less than helpful. He puts a reassuring hand on your shoulder, and then quickly removes it.

'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}. I did have more success than you, but remember that I did grow up here! There are not many folk who remember me, but there are a few. I learned from them that perhaps a dozen bounty-hunters met with Saklaphêl's man Galadaith, but of that number only three seemed serious about it. One of these I heard talk about even when I was just a child: the Blade-twist, who must be an old man by now, surely. The other is a woman, Cruel Dancer, and of those I spoke to she is believed to have the greatest chance of actually claiming any of the bounties.

'It seems the Blade-twist and Cruel Dancer have already departed the islands, but the third bounty-hunter may still be here. He is a man they call Driftwood, and he lives here in Halrax. Perhaps you can speak to Manadhon, the man who tends the bar here, and learn where we can meet with Driftwood? You are certain to redeem yourself in the eyes of the crew, ${PLAYER}! Oh... my apologies!''It seems the Blade-twist and Cruel Dancer have already departed the islands, but the third bounty-hunter may still be here. He is a man they call Driftwood, and he lives here in Halrax. Perhaps you can speak to Manadhon, the man who tends the bar here, and learn where we can meet with Driftwood? You are certain to redeem yourself in the eyes of the crew, ${PLAYER}! Oh... my apologies!''When I suggested that one of Saklaphêl's bounty-hunters might help us with our rescue of my son, I did not envision you asking one of them to join the crew, ${PLAYER}. If this Driftwood proves himself useful, that is one thing... but if he did not even set forth for the City of the Corsairs already, how serious can he be about opposing the Kindred of the Coins?

'But I will trust your decision.'Without the right ingredients, Shulgolb's and Uzhún's cooking plans are in a spot of trouble.Complete two tasks for Shulgolb at Kafagur.Complete Quest 'Cooking Catastrophe: Drake Eggs'Complete Quest 'Cooking Catastrophe: Beetle Larvae'You've helped Shulgolb collect enough ingredients.

You should talk to him at Kafagur.Talk to Shulgolb at KafagurShulgolb has given you the ingredients that Uzhún requires.

Uzhún can be found at Kafagur.'Thanks for gettin' us out of Gundabad. It's nicer here, and I don't have to fight anymore. I just help Uzhún cook food!

'Though, times have been tough lately. We wanted to cook something to improve morale, but Uzhún forgot to ask the hunters to gather ingredients again. Now there aren't enough hunters to help. I'd go myself, but... I don't think I'm ready for that.

'Would you mind helpin' us one more time?''Think Uzhún'll want to get their hands on these ingredients and start cookin'.

'Bring the ingredients over to 'em, would you? It's only right -- after all, you're the one who did the hard work, not me.''Thank you -- Shulgolb told me what you were up to. We can finally get started!

'Now, where did I put my....'Shulgolb's and Uzhún's dish calls for beetle larvae.Shulgolb has asked you to collect larvae from beetle nests on Ghax-hophra.

Ghax-hophra is located north of Kafagur.Collect larvae from beetle nests on Ghax-hophra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You've collected a good amount of beetle larvae.

You should bring them to Shulgolb at Kafagur.'Those beetles in Ghax-hophra have nests full of tasty little grubs. Just head north of Kafagur, and you'll see what I mean!''This'll do! Hope the beetles didn't give you too much trouble. I've heard they can be nasty.'Shulgolb's and Uzhún's dish calls for drake eggs.Shulgolb has asked you to collect drake eggs from nests in Jeb Lipha.

Jeb Lipha is located east of Kafagur.Collect eggs from drake nests in Jeb Lipha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You've collected a good amount of drake eggs.

You should bring them to Shulgolb at Kafagur.'The drakes to the east in Jeb Lipha are a tough lot, but their eggs are worth the trouble, I promise! Just be careful -- they guard those nests closely.''Wow! How many drakes did you have to fight to get these?'One final, tiny issue needs to be resolved before Uzhún and Shulgolb can get cooking.Uzhún has asked you to search for their salt pouch.

It must be in one of the provision barrels around Kafagur.Search provision barrels for Uzhún's salt pouchYou've found Uzhún's salt pouch.

They wait for you at Kafagur.'My salt! My dried sea-weed! I just brought the pouches here, I know I did. Unless I didn't?

'Maybe they're still in the provisions barrels around Kafagur. I'll send Shulgolb to find the sea-weed -- you can look for my salt pouch.''Excellent! At least our bellies will be full for a while, and our moods lifted! That has to count for something, even with everything going on.

'Thank you, ${RACE}.'Itho has arrived at Raghda-gûn's nest to take an egg for himself.While you were searching for Berkha, Itho arrived to try stealing one of Raghda-gûn's eggs for himself.

Speak to Raghda-gûn's friends to discover the story of what transpired.Talk to AnathAnath has asked you to meet Nekhama in Halrax.Talk to Nekhama in Halrax'This fool threatened to shoot me with a crossbow if I did not turn over one of my eggs. As you can see, things did not proceed as he expected.''Me? I'm an old friend of Raghda-gûn's here. I heard about this piece of flotsam asking around about roc eggs the other day. I didn't think much of it until one day I come out of the pub and he's not in his usual spot. Something feels wrong about it, so I gather Nekhama here–'

Nekhama grunts.

'–and I come to see Raghda-gûn. You know, just in case. Turns out we didn't have much to worry about here as this fool has as much sense as he does hygiene.'

Nekhama grunts again, but this one sounds like it might have been a laugh.

'Is he alive? He is, merely stunned by the thrashing we gave him. Hmm? Curious about who he meant to steal the egg for? Ah so are we. Tell you what, Nekhama here will carry this sea-sponge back to Halrax.'

Nekhama grunts disapprovingly.

'Meet her there later today and see if she hasn't learned anything. I'm going to stay a while longer and speak to my friend.'The woman stands outside the pub looking impatient. She spots you, thrusts a letter into your hands, and returns inside. She does not invite you to follow her.

The letter is written in shockingly beautiful handwriting:

The would-be child thief has been dealt with. Before his demise, he mentioned the name of someone in Umbar who seeks rare 'animals' to own. If you find yourself in the city of Umbar, seek out Tatháta. She could be an ally in your hunt for this scoundrel.Hazâl, appalled at the treatment of the buildings within the town, enlists your aid to remedy the situation.Find the defaced walls throughout Halrax and clean them to restore their beauty.Clear graffiti from the walls (${NUMBER}/6)Having cleaned the graffiti from the walls in town, you should return to Hazâl near her home by the docks in Halrax.Speak with Hazâl near the dock in HalraxHazâl asked that you search the south-eastern dock of Halrax for the vandal responsible for defacing the walls throughout the town.Find the Corsair vandal and ask him to stopYou confronted the Corsair vandal, and after issuing a threat and attacking you, he ran when it was clear you would defeat him. Return to Hazâl and inform him that the vandal should no longer be a problem.Speak with Hazâl near the docks in Halrax'I apologize if I seem on edge. There is an issue in this town that vexes me greatly. Some people show no respect for property. I am speaking of the act of defiling the walls of our homes. Someone is purposefully defacing the beauty of the buildings.

'Each day, I clear the walls of the filth spread on them, and each day, they return.

'Would you help me clean the walls and perhaps help me find the culprit?''Thank you for cleaning the walls for me. I need to confide something to you. While you were busy about town, I overheard a knave speaking about damaging the walls and laughing about his actions amongst friends. I wonder, can you address this and make him see his folly?

'I saw him, only a few moments ago, headed down the south-eastern dock.''How dare you accost me about some foolish old sketches? What does it matter if they are on the walls? They are just walls. There is no value to them. We live here now, and we will do as we please. You need to learn that lesson.

'I find pain teaches a student best.''The coward. I expected nothing less. We should preserve our buildings and respect them. Our works stand a test of time that no man ever has, and we have not begun to build.

'In time, we will cover the the isles with these rugged and enduring buildings. They will survive in a climate as hostile as the Shield Isles. I thank you for your efforts, friend.'Raghda-gûn has realized she may not be best suited to care for little Berkha.Raghda-gûn has realized she may not be best suited to care for little Berkha, and has arranged for you to take him with you.

Speak to Berkha at Raghda-gûn's nest, Aklâradum, atop a cliff south of Halrax.Talk to Berkha'${PLAYER}, I begin to suspect that I may not be best suited to care for young Berkha here. The life of a Roc and the life of a duck are so very different. He seems to have taken a shine to you, however. Would you be interested in taking him on your travels? The wind has brought me stories of a far away place known as the Shire. I hear it is ever peaceful. Perhaps you could take him there some day?'

You look at Berkha, who quacks at you. How could anyone say no to that?

'Well, he at least seems amenable to the idea,' Raghda-gûn says.

'Berkha, it has been a treat to have you around. You do not seem to listen to my wishes and your ability to hunt for prey is lacking, but you were at least amusing. May your belly always be full and your feathers clean.'The little duck waddles away from Raghda-gûn, but he doesn't make it more than a few feet before he looks back at the one who took him in.

'Quack!'

The single word could not hope to capture the depth of his gratitude or his love, but it will have to do.Anyâmat harbours aspirations of being a great shanty-man.Anyâmat thinks it would be a great idea to pick fights with random freebooters so that she might experience the rough and tumble life of a sailor.

Willing freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.Defeat freebooters (0/8)The first freebooter you spoke to wasn't interested in fighting. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.

Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzir.Talk to AnyâmatThe first freebooter you spoke to isn't interested in fighting. Try challenging one of her friends.

Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.Challenge freebooters (0/8)The second freebooter you spoke to isn't interested in fighting. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.

Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.Talk to AnyâmatThe second freebooter you spoke to wasn't interested in fighting. Anyâmat has decided to change strategies and wants to make friends with these freebooters instead.

Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.Make friends (2/4)The third freebooter gave you and Anyâmat some grilled fish. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.

Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.Make friends (3/4)
Talk to AnyâmatAnyâmat wants to make friends with all four freebooters on this little island.

Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.Make friends (3/4)Anyâmat has made unexpected friends with the freebooters she was intending to instigate! Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.

Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.Make friends (4/4)
Talk to Anyâmat'Why don't we start by challenging some freebooters to a fight? Nothing speaks to rugged life at sea like pointless brawling!''A fight? Now why would I do that? I have only just met you! Come, join me and my friends for some tea.''Well that didn't go as I expected,' Anyâmat says as she sips from the offered cup. 'Free tea though. Maybe we can challenge one of the other people here?''Ah, such lovely weather we have been enjoying as of late. It makes me want to sing!'

The freebooter strikes up a joyful song. Anyâmat doesn't know the words, but she harmonizes beautifully with the man. She may not have success writing lyrics, but doesn't lack for singing talent.'This is not going how I expected. Maybe we should give up on trying to pick a fight and make friends instead.''I know we look like rough folk, but that is what happens when you spend all day in the sun and having your face chapped by salty sea air!'

He laughs, no, guffaws at himself.

'Are you hungry? The sea has been generous and there is plenty of food to share.'Anyâmat speaks through a mouthful of grilled fish.

'I should go around talking to strangers more often! Instead of fighting you they give you free tea and fish and sing with you. I really like these folks. Come, let's meet the last of their company.''Hello--oooh!' 

The woman's greeting is interrupted by a yawn. 

'Sorry about that. I had coffee too late in the day yesterday. I went to sleep late and am still waking up.'

Anyâmat shares her desire to be a shanty-man, and the sleepy freebooter's lips curl into a smirk.

'If it is inspiration for songs you seek, I can tell you about my own travels on the sea.'

Anyâmat quickly agrees, and the sleepy freebooter proceeds to tell the most bawdy and violent tales one could tell. By the end of the stories, Anyâmat is frozen stiff by shock.

She thanks the woman for her time, and the two of you beat a hasty retreat.'As lovely as this has been, I do think a real sailor should get into a scrap. If these fine folk won't fight with us, I have heard rumours of a strange creature we could go bother....'The little bird, Berkha, has gone missing! His mother, Raghda-gûn, has bid you find him.Raghda-gûn asked you to find Berkha in Irkhadâr, the caldera lake in Zamarzîr.

Irkhadâr is north of Aklâradum.Raghda-gûn asked you to find Berkha in Irkhadâr, the caldera lake in Zamarzîr.

Irkhadâr is north of Aklâradum.Find BerkhaBerkha announced his presence at the shore of Irkhadâr.

Speak to Berkha.Talk to BerkhaYou have found little Berkha and should take him back to Aklâradum.

Aklâradum is on a cliff to the south of Irkhadâr.Talk to Raghda-gûn'I hate to ask this of you, but could you track down Berkha? I would normally have a friend go search, but the turmoil in recent months has seen many rocs find new perches in calmer seas.

'Hmm? Do I not have a mate to help protect my nest? Alas, he is no longer with me.

'What? No he's not dead. His mother is ill so he went to go care for her. What did you think I meant?

'Anyway, please go find Berkha. Perhaps he went down near the caldera lake where I first found him.'The duckling tilts his head at you, as if quietly asking 'Why were you swimming around in that lake?'

When you reach down to pick him up, he happily leaps into your arms.

He's had his fun. It's time to return to Raghda-gûn.As you approach, Berkha cradled safely in your arms, you see that Raghda-gûn has more guests. One of them, a familiar greasy looking man, lies dazed on the ground, his vacant eyes fixed on the sky above. The other two you may have seen in passing on the streets of Halrax.

'Berkha!' Raghda-gûn shouts as you approach. 'What have I told you about going off on your own?'

Berkha quacks and nips at your sleeve.

'We will speak later, young man.'

Raghda-gûn fixes her clever eyes on you.

'You have my thanks. Now, I believe you know this gentleman taking up space on the ground?'Though pleased with your assistance regarding the matters facing the town of Halrax, Ithurga warns that not everyone is happy with the news that you made such inroads with the Kindred.Ithurga told you that the good you've done in Halrax will attract unwanted attention. He returned your tithe and told you to distribute it to the freebooters to gain favour.You distributed your tithe to the freebooters. Return to Ithurga at his home in Halrax.Speak with Ithurga at his home in HalraxIthurga asked if you will travel to Umbar. Tell him your intentions.

<rgb=#FF0000>Use the emote /yes for yes or the emote /no for no.</rgb>Tell Ithurga you will not travel to Umbar (<rgb=#FF0000>/no</rgb>)Tell Ithurga that you will travel to Umbar (<rgb=#FF0000>/yes</rgb>)Ithurga seems pleased with your response and wishes to speak with you one more time.Speak with Ithurga at his home in Halrax'Truth is ${PLAYER}, the favour you curried with the Kindred will bring you undue attention. A newcomer hoisting their sail so quickly is grounds for suspicion. It's best to make amends before the elders start whispering in the shadows.

'Take your tithe and distribute it to some of the freebooters. It will curry favour with them. Be wary. The rumours will spread, and your welcome will end.''It's rare that you meet someone like you, my friend. I must admit that I am surprised by your resolve and honesty. Tell me, will you travel to Umbar Baharbêl? The city, I mean.''Listen, ${PLAYER}. What you did for Halrax, for me... there aren't many as honest in all the world. Not at least that I've seen.

'Here.'

He hands you a sack of gold coins.

'You will need this more than I, and I can't keep your coin if you don't mean to stay. Not after all you've done.

'Go with the southern wind in your sails, my friend.'Tanim directed you to hunt jungle-beasts throughout the Shield Isles for their horns. They fetch a good price in Umbar City.Head into the wild lands of the Shield Isles and search for Ghar Jâdam, Sekbiri, or Bâkhabar jungle-beasts. Collect their horns ands return to Tanim at Halrax.Collect sekbir-horns (${NUMBER}/12)You slew several beasts in the Shield Isles and collected their horns. Tanim awaits your return at his home in Halrax.'Tanim is my name. I'll not attempt to deceive you with some sad story about an ailing child, sibling, mother, or other nonsense. I'll tell you straight what and why I want what I want.

'In Umbar Baharbêl, there is a newfound freedom. That freedom comes with opportunity, and I am seizing mine. You see, people will pay for any foolish notion or thought. Want to look younger, be strong, or faster? Enterprising scholars will brew you a potion or two to fit your needs. Those scholars need a product, and you can get me the product I need.

'Jungle-beast horns. Tales tell of their mystical qualities, and I aim to make my coin while I can. Would you help an honest man?''You'll find the beasts I seek all over the Shield Isles. After collecting twelve sets of their horns, return them to me.''Yes, this is a fine selection of horns. A little polish and a spit-shine, and they'll be ready to ship into the city. You've helped me, friend. Let me line your pockets as you've lined mine.'Shúkurz has abandoned all caution to try and reason with a strange Man.Shúkurz has left behind a trail of footprints leading out of the northern side of Kafagur.

You should follow it.Follow the trail of footprints out of KafagurYou have found Shúkurz and Phocas outside Kafagur, near the northern side.

You should talk to Phocas.Talk to PhocasYou have found Shúkurz and Phocas outside Kafagur, near the northern side.

You should talk to Shúkurz.Talk to ShúkurzShúkurz has asked you to talk to him back in Kafagur.Talk to Shúkurz in Kafagur'No matter how much I'd like to send more guards after Shúkurz, it'd only make things worse with that Man. But you're different; I'm sure he's the kind who'd trust you over an Orc.

'It won't be hard for you to track down Shúkurz. See that trail of footprints, leading out of the village? Heh, I bet he was a lousy scout in Gundabad.''I am sorry, ${CLASS}; I followed you from Mâr Naphra to find Kafagur. I had believed that it was a camp full of dangerous Orcs. Clearly, I was mistaken, and this investigation was faulty from the start.

'It's true that I am not from Umbar, but rather, Gondor. I... do not know if I can tell you what led me here, but you have my word: I will not harm the Orcs.

'Whether they believe me is another matter entirely. Though, after I judged them so rashly, I do not know if I deserve that trust.''Phocas doesn't seem like the bad sort. After all, he was willing to stop running long enough to listen to me. I'm sure we'll figure things out.

'I've got more I want to tell you, but I ought to take Phocas back to Kafagur first. I'll see you there.''Thanks for making sure I was all right, ${PLAYER}. Grúshul's right; I acted like a fool. Even during our journey out of Gundabad, we stuck to the wilds because we knew Men would kill us if they saw us. I should have been scared of Phocas.

'But... I remembered how we got out of Gundabad in the first place. With your help, and the help of others. I remembered Náin, and how he apologized to me.

'I guess I wanted to believe that sort of thing could happen again. Maybe it can.'The bodies of fallen Kafagur hunters lie scattered around Dor Pherkha.It might be worth reclaiming the fallen hunters' belongings and returning them to Kafagur.Retrieve belongings from fallen hunters at Dor PherkhaFallen hunters can be found around Dor Pherkha.

You should retrieve their belongings.You have retrieved a number of belongings from fallen hunters at Dor Pherkha.

You should venture north-west to Kafagur and bring what you've collected to the hunter Rúkbag.The bodies of fallen Kafagur hunters lie scattered around Dor Pherkha. A number of them must hold personal effects, as well as salvageable equipment. It might be worth reclaiming such items and returning them to Kafagur.'This means more than you know. I'll see to it that my fellows' belongings are treated with care.

'Thank you.'There aren't enough uninjured hunters in Kafagur able to hunt for fresh supplies in Jeb Lipha.Rúkbag has asked you to hunt in Jeb Lipha, east of Kafagur.

The hunters require phials of acid from drakelings, as well as hide from the larger drakes.Hunt drakes in Jeb Lipha for hide (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hunt drakelings in Jeb Lipha for phials of acid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You've collected enough supplies for the Kafagur hunters.

You should return to Rúkbag at Kafagur.'We need more phials of acid and drake hide for our equipment, but we lack enough uninjured hunters able to travel east to Jeb Lipha.

'If you're willing, would you hunt in our stead? It's easier to procure acid from the drakelings, but the best and toughest hide comes from the larger drakes.''Many thanks. The fresh supplies will help us enormously during these trying times.'Kúlthrak is in need of spider venom for wound-numbing purposes.Kúlthrak has asked you to hunt down spiders for venom.

Spiders can be found at Maj Khibi, which is located north-west of Kafagur.Collect venom from spiders at Maj Khibi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected enough spider venom.

You should give the phials to Kúlthrak at Kafagur.'I used up the last of my spider venom on Nargai. Their pain has dulled for now, but that won't last if I don't get my hands on more venom.

'If you're up to the task, hunt down some spiders for me, yeah? There're plenty of them north-west of us at Maj Khibi.''This is plenty. Thanks, ${CLASS}.'Echoes of the violence that the Gundabad Orcs experienced run deeper than mere wounds.Nargai has asked you to find and talk to Zogmauk in Kafagur.

They suggested clearing your throat to alert him to your presence first.You have caught Zogmauk's attention.

You should talk to him in Kafagur.Talk to ZogmaukZogmauk has asked you to return to Nargai with some fruit and his apologies.

Nargai can be found in Kafagur.'My injuries? Oh, I'm fine. Getting fixed up right now, aren't I? I'm more worried about Zogmauk, really. Think I scared him -- that's how I landed in this situation.

'He ran away after, but I'm sure he's still somewhere in Kafagur. If you bump into him, make sure he's all right. Just... cough to catch his attention first. He's probably still on edge.''Oh. Didn't expect to see you again. Good thing you didn't try to tap me on the shoulder just now -- that was Nargai's mistake.

'It's too quiet here. Nothing like Gundabad. If this were Gundabad, someone would've already cut me down by now. I guess that's why I hid after I hurt Nargai. The only way to survive there was to look out for yourself. But now....

'Take some of this fruit to Nargai, will you? Tell them I said sorry. Maybe I'll be brave enough to say that to their face later.''Thanks for checking on Zogmauk. Glad he's doing all right -- or, about as all right as he can be.

'I hope he realizes that he doesn't have to fight anymore. That there's more to living than surviving.'Upon arriving on the island, the boatman at the dock warned you to be cautious and directed you to the healer in the outpost.Speak with the healer at the stalls within the outpost of Bel Inzûl.Speak with healer standing near the stalls at Bel Inzûl'Best to make whatever business you have here quick, my friend. There are terrors lurking around this island that turn the innards of men to jelly - just by sight. Talk with the healer if you want to know more.''It was good of the boatman to warn you. There are things on this island that are terrifying and cruel. We do our best to stay away. This port ensures that goods are moving across the townships... we do not linger here long.

'If you have companions, I would bring them with you if you choose to take on the bounties we've posted on the wall around the corner. Otherwise, friend, do yourself a favour and stay within the confines of this outpost - for your safety.'A dead Corsair, bound by a curse upon a chest found in the salamander's lair in Zamarzîr, seeks assistance finding rest.A shade of a dead Corsair begged for help in finding peace.Speak with the shadeThe shade wants you to find his body, collect the stolen treasure, and return the gold to the chest. The shade believes that this will set him free.Collect the stolen goldThe shade reappeared and warned that you must return the treasure to the chest or suffer the same fate. Return to the open chest in the salamander grotto and restore the treasure.The treasure is whole, and the shade remains. It seems to beckon to you.'The chest lured me in with riches. The thought of a better life. The hope of a bright tomorrow.

'The gold was cursed. Look upon me. This is the fate of any who would steal this treasure.

'I long for rest. Can you help me find peace?''My body lies south-east, across the water, in the centre of a small island. Collect the gold. Place it back in the chest so that I may rest.''You have my thanks. I feel free. I can rest.'Melitara enlisted your aid in keeping her furrier business afloat.Hunt down jungle-beasts throughout the Shield Isles. Skin their corpses, and when you have enough, return to Melitara at Halrax for payment.Collect pelts from sekbiri on the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/16)You collected enough pelts to meet Melitara's current demand. You should return to her at her station in Halrax.Melitara thanked you for collecting the furs and mentioned shining some previously stretched hides. She once again asked for your aid.Shine the stretched hides (${NUMBER}/4)Your work on the hides is complete, and they look great. Melitara wants to speak with you.'Are you looking to make some coin and willing to spend a little time helping someone who is a little on in years?

'My mind is as sharp as steel, but my body... my body is starting to show my age. Not as able as I once was to roam the wilds hunting down jungle beasts for their pelts. And yet, there is still brisk demand for my wares.

'I'll pay if you can help. What do you say?''These furs are fine, yes. I would have hunted more animal types to get a wider variety, but since you are helping me, I think these shall do nicely.

'One more thing, if you don't mind. These skins need curing. I have hides that need stretching, and my back is aching fiercely. Could you spare a few more moments to help me?''You'll find the hides just here behind me. Please, be a dear, and help me.''I've not seen a shine that good in quite a while. My customers will surely be pleased with these. Only a few years ago, I'd have done the same, not as quickly, but as well.

'Thank you for all that you've done for me. Please take this as my way of thanking you.'The sabre-tooth known as Hedâkha has been a thorn in Kafagur's side for too long.Rúkbag has asked you to find Lumbag.

She last saw him at Dor Pherkha, south-east of Kafagur.Find Lumbag at Dor PherkhaYou have found Lumbag hiding at Dor Pherkha.

You should talk to him.Talk to LumbagLumbag has given you some raw boar meat that might lure out Hedâkha.

You can find a good spot to place the bait somewhere in Dor Pherkha.Hedâkha has been defeated.

You should check on Lumbag at Dor Pherkha.Talk to Lumbag'During our last hunt at Dor Pherkha, the sabre-tooth Hedâkha overwhelmed us. So many fell. I ran back here, but one of the newcomers -- Lumbag, I think his name is -- stayed behind. I told him that trying to prove himself was stupid, but maybe that was low of me.

'Could you venture south-east and make sure he's still alive? I don't doubt his skills, but trying to act like a hero isn't going to land him in a good place.'Lumbag lets out a shaky breath -- almost like he's been holding it this entire time, waiting for you to return.

'It's gone... heh. Rúkbag was right; I couldn't fight Hedâkha alone after all. After I saw it tear through everyone...' He gulps.

'Thanks for the help. I'll return to Kafagur to rest.''Shhh! There're a bunch of things here that want to hurt me and I'm trying to think.

'Oh, hang on -- you can be part of my plan! Look.'

He triumphantly waves around a slab of raw boar meat.

'I hunted myself some bait! Just find a good place to set it down and lure out Hedâkha. A beast like that should be no problem for you, right? ...Right?'Manadhon, the bartender of Halrax, has given you a lead on the man called Driftwood.Manadhon told you the man called Driftwood might be found on the lower level of Halrax, on the south-western side of the inlet.Find Driftwood on the lower level of HalraxThe man called Driftwood is deep in his cups on the lower level of Halrax, on the south-western side of the inlet.Wait for Driftwood to acknowledge your presenceDriftwood stands suddenly, knocking his chair to the floor.Talk to Driftwood on the lower level of HalraxSigileth has joined you in Halrax.Talk to Sigileth in HalraxDriftwood stands on the lower level of Halrax.Talk to Driftwood on the lower level of HalraxMany Corsairs throughout the Shield Isles support the Heirs of Castamir, and Driftwood has asked you to continue his work of making things difficult for them.Defeat Corsairs throughout the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Having defeated many supporters of the Heirs of Castamir throughout the Shield Isles, you should return to the Wave-hunter.Return to Voyage's End and check on your crewDriftwood stands by the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.Talk to Driftwood at Voyage's End'Aye, I know the man called Driftwood. Leastways, I know him as much as any other who lives in Halrax. You don't ask questions about folk who end up in Zîrar Tarka. This is a place for lost things, and some of those things don't want to be found, if you take my meaning.'

You tell Manadhon that you might have information of interest to Driftwood, and a friend to the man would help you find him.

'Maybe that's so and maybe that isn't, but this is not a place for friends, stranger. He is here most every night, drinking, and he is generous with his coin. Perhaps that makes us friends after all.

'But he is a man grown, and he does not need me to protect him. He lives on the lower level of Halrax, on the south-western side of the inlet, if you need to speak with him so badly. But I don't want anyone coming back here and causing trouble if he doesn't want to speak to you.''But Driftwood is a man grown, and he does not need me to protect him. He lives on the lower level of Halrax, on the south-western side of the inlet, if you need to speak with him so badly. But I don't want anyone coming back here and causing trouble if he doesn't want to speak to you.''No... it cannot be!'

Driftwood stares at you with astonishment, the ale-inspired cloudiness of his eyes draining away.

'You... ${PLAYER}... I cannot believe it! I never thought... I never thought I would see you again.'

There can be no mistake. This is Horn of Rohan, though months of hard living on the road and in the wild have weathered his clothes. His face is still familiar, but the war and its worries have left their marks upon it, and he seems more aged than you remember.

'What brings you to the Shield Isles, ${PLAYER}? You have not let down your own folk, as I have, surely? I cannot imagine that. You were always stronger in mind than I was, with courage to spare. It is the truth, and we both know it. And Nona was... Nona was stronger than both of us. But... what do you have to say of yourself? You are not running away from something. You were always running... toward.'

Before you can gather your thoughts to speak, someone steps close behind you. She stares at Horn with a hard look in her eyes, and you know you must introduce her.

'This is Sigileth,' you say.'Sigileth... the sister of Corudan!''It is true, Corudan is my brother, and he needs our help.'

Sigileth stares at Horn, daring him to speak, but he wisely keeps his silence.

'I have heard of your adventures with ${PLAYER}, Horn of Rohan, and with my brother, and I have been told of the choice you made when the Battle of Pelennor Fields was ended. It is not my place to judge whether your choice was well-considered or ill-thought, and I will not do so.

'But I will ask this of you. Did you consider my brother Corudan to be a friend? Did you think you knew him? This, then, is my last question.

'Would Corudan come to your aid, if your positions were reversed? Or would he give in to cowardice, and run away, leaving the hard work to others?''Would Corudan come to your aid, if your positions were reversed?''I believed Corudan's sister Sigileth was dead, ${PLAYER}, and that she perished within Dol Guldur before we adventured in Rohan. But no, she is alive and seems eager to shame me on his behalf! Have you learned what happened to Corudan at Helm's Deep? You had better tell me what happened to him, and quickly, for I think his sister may be about to stick me with her famous knives, and right now I confess I might deserve it!'

You tell Horn what you know about Corudan's captivity by the Kindred of the Coins and your mission to Umbar. When you have finished, he rubs his eyes.

'After the Battle of Pelennor Fields, I wandered without purpose. I came to this land because I did not want to get involved, but even that proved a lie. I called myself Bymerë at first, and told myself Horn was dead. But as I lived here, drowning my old sorrows with ale and trying to forget what I had done and what I had been, I saw crimes I could not forgive; as I opposed them I took on a new name: Driftwood. I believed the Heirs of Castamir might again threaten Gondor... and if they had victory there, would not Rohan be next? So I made things difficult for them, as I could. I thought I might gain an audience with Balakhôr's widow if I claimed to have slain one of her enemies, and so end the threat of the Heirs of Castamir.

'Most of my plans ended in the bottom of a mug of ale, ${PLAYER}. When I was Horn, and fought alongside friends, it was different. Driftwood is alone, and accomplishes nothing. It is useless.'

You tell Horn that it could be different, and he shakes his head.

'This is my place now. I spend my days fighting Corsairs and my nights here, drowning in my cups. I suggest you defeat the Corsairs of the Shield Isles, for the sake of our past friendship, and then return to your ship. Horn is dead; only Driftwood remains, and he cannot help you.''This is my place now. I spend my days fighting Corsairs and my nights here, drowning in my cups. I suggest you defeat the Corsairs of the Shield Isles, for the sake of our past friendship, and then return to your ship. Horn is dead; only Driftwood remains, and he cannot help you.''I have changed my mind, ${PLAYER}. Sigileth is right: were our positions reversed, Corudan would stop at nothing to come to my rescue or yours.

'I will join you in this, my old friend, if you will have me. The Shield Isles are a place for lost and broken things, but perhaps such things need not stay lost forever, and maybe with friendship they can be repaired. I will join you once again... for Corudan, and to keep the Kindred of the Coins from endangering Gondor, Rohan... and other, more distant lands.

'I spoke truly when I told you Horn was dead. I am Driftwood now, and would have your crew call me by this name. I hope this is agreeable to you, my friend. And one more thing: you might have told me Sigileth no longer possesses her famous knives! I might have thought more clearly in Halrax if I knew I was not in danger of being sliced open!'

You assure Driftwood that while she no longer possesses Lanchigil and Egnassigil, Sigileth has been practicing with her new blade, and even without a name she could still do considerable damage with it.

'Oh,' he responds. 'Perfect.'Manadhon, the bartender of Halrax, has given you a lead on the man called Driftwood.Manadhon told you the man called Driftwood might be found somewhere to the east in Halrax.Talk to Driftwood on the upper level of HalraxCorsairs throughout the Shield Isles carry money-purses that Driftwood recovers and donates to Manadhon.Collect money-purses from Corsairs throughout the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Driftwood has directed you to bring the money-purses to Manadhon on the upper level of Halrax.Having satisfied Driftwood's request, you should return to the Wave-hunter.Return to Voyage's End and check on your crewDriftwood stands by the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.Talk to Driftwood at Voyage's End'Aye, I know the man called Driftwood. Leastways, I know him as much as any other who lives in Halrax. You don't ask questions about folk who end up in Zîrar Tarka. This is a place for lost things, and some of those things don't want to be found, if you take my meaning.'

You tell Manadhon that you might have information of interest to Driftwood, and a friend to the man would help you find him.

'Maybe that's so and maybe that isn't, but this is not a place for friends, stranger. He is here most every night, drinking, and he is generous with his coin. Perhaps that makes us friends after all. But he is a man grown, and he does not need me to protect him. He was just here, moments ago, if you need to speak with him so badly. He went off to the east. But I don't want anyone coming back here and causing trouble if he doesn't want to speak to you.''This is not a place for friends, stranger. He is here most every night, drinking, and he is generous with his coin. Perhaps that makes us friends after all. But he is a man grown, and he does not need me to protect him. He was just here, moments ago, if you need to speak with him so badly. He went off to the east. But I don't want anyone coming back here and causing trouble if he doesn't want to speak to you.''You are the one who is looking for me? By my guess you are from the ship that ran aground north of Bakhjâd in the recent storm... a more common occurrence of late than it has been. I have not seen you before, and Driftwood makes it his business to see people before they see him, if you take my meaning. The Shield Isles are a place for the lost, and most lost things prefer to stay that way. Why do you seek me?'

You tell Driftwood that you are interested in Saklaphêl's bounties upon the Kindred of the Coins, and that you understand he might share that interest.

'Perhaps, stranger, and perhaps not. If you think I desire the wealth of the reward, you are mistaken. In a past life I stole more coins than you could spend in a lifetime, not the gold phâraz or the silver gîmil of Umbar, but the currency of Gondor; that life is finished. Now I rob only those who steal from others, and give every coin to folk in need.

'If we are to do business, I want to know you share my mind. Continue my work, stranger, and take the money-purses from Corsairs here in the Shield Isles. Bring them to Manadhon here in Halrax when you have finished. He will know the use to which this stolen money should be put.

'But I am content to remain here. There is little you could offer me that I need.''If we are to do business, I want to know you share my mind. Continue my work, stranger, and take the money-purses from Corsairs here in the Shield Isles. Bring them to Manadhon here in Halrax when you have finished. He will know the use to which this stolen money should be put.

'But I am content to remain here. There is little you could offer me that I need.''You have brought me these money-purses at the direction of our mutual friend Driftwood, have you not?'

You tell Manadhon that he is correct, and Driftwood believed the bartender would know what to do with them.

'I do, for it is the same every week. Driftwood comes here with his pockets full of money-purses he has taken from Corsairs, and I use the coin to support the folk of Halrax who have nothing, giving them food, giving them drink, and making the ill-gotten wealth of the Corsairs serve a beneficial purpose. Why does he do this? He has not said, but I have pieced together a little of it.

'I think he used to be a robber himself, stealing from wealthy merchants somewhere in Gondor. He knows his way around ships, so perhaps he plied his trade along one of the rivers in Gondor. But something went wrong. Or maybe he just tired of the life and sought to leave it behind. But for all his intentions, and despite taking a new name, Driftwood is still a robber, and still he steals... but he tells himself it is different.

'I do not know. I try not to pry.''I think Driftwood used to be a robber himself, stealing from wealthy merchants somewhere in Gondor. He knows his way around ships, so perhaps he plied his trade along one of the rivers in Gondor. But something went wrong. Or maybe he just tired of the life and sought to leave it behind. But for all his intentions, and despite taking a new name, Driftwood is still a robber, and still he steals... but he tells himself it is different.

'I do not know. I try not to pry.''I told you there was little you could offer me that I need, stranger, but I may have been wrong.

'I have not always been proud of the life I chose, but at least I can say that I chose it. I followed the path I was on until I decided it was not for me, and then I took another path. But your arrival at this place, and the words you spoke to me, have made me realize that the road I followed was not the straight way I envisioned; instead it twisted and curved through the wild in a way I did not expect... only to rejoin the earlier path I had been on, the one I thought I left behind.

'Stealing from the Corsairs and giving their money-purses to Manadhon for the support of those in Halrax who need it... that is a small thing, and small things are insufficient. I need a truly different path, ${PLAYER}, and I believe you are the sort to cut your own way through the wild. I will accompany you as you face the Kindred of the Coins, for I believe you herald the truly different path I have been seeking.

'If you will respect my privacy and ask no questions of my past, Driftwood is with you.'Fearsome beasts roam along a part of Halrax's northern coast.A fierce sekbir stands above the rest.Discover Ghar JâdamA fierce sekbir stands above the rest.

Defeat the sekbir brute in Ghar Jâdam.Defeat the sekbir bruteA woman in a grey cloak wipes her blade against the fur of the slain sekbir.

'You see, it is one thing to fight a person either on a killing field or in a duel. It is another thing entirely to fight a beast that is twice as large as you, three times as heavy, and cares not for how good your form is. You cannot intimidate it with fancy bladework, nor trick it, not unless you possess some sorcery of which I am unaware.'

A woman in tattered armour and threadbare boots shakes her head. 'Just me and my blade. No special tricks here.'

Grey Cloak inclines her head towards a particularly nasty looking creature. 'I believe that is the strongest of them here. Do you think you can take it down?'

Threadbare Boots grins and slashes through the air a few times, warming up her wrist. 'After watching you, I think I know just what to do.'You and Ithurga have confirmed that the replica was likely a misdirect and the real hammer is still out there.Ithurga explained that he has deduced the final location of Marâkh, Mother of Tempests. It is in an island in northern Jeb Khâtel.Find the island of legendYou have found a long path up a tall peak. The journey will be dangerous.Climb to the top of the peakThe giant seems to be agitated by something stuck in its eye.Talk to Hûrlub the Bellower'After thinking about the reports you gathered and putting them together with what I know of this Marâkh, Mother of Tempests, I believe our best guess is an island in the north Jeb Khâtel. It is said to be such a perilous journey that not even the heartiest of freebooters dare travel there.

'Again, I must caution, your life is more important than some old relic. Do not be hasty in this regard.

'Go to the island in Jeb Khâtel. Learn what you can, and retrieve Marâkh. If you cannot do this, escape as quickly as possible. Live to tell the tale.''You are small thing. Why do you come here?

'You not afraid? Everyone afraid. All stay away. Hûrlub always alone.

'Crawlies! Crawlies hurt Hûrlub! Hûrlub cannot sleep!

'Many leg ones. Always bully Hûrlub.'

Hûrlub frowns.The Roc, Raghda-gûn, has taken in a little bird of another species.Raghda-gûn asked you to gather insects to feed to her little adoptee.

Insects can be found underneath little stones scattered around the Raghda-gûn's nest.Gather insects (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have gathered enough insects to feed little Berkha.

Return to Raghda-gûn.Talk to Raghda-gûn'This would not be the first time someone's foolish greed brought trouble to my nest or danger to myself or one of my young. I appreciate your warning. I must nurse these eggs, which gives me less freedom to watch for interlopers.'

You can't help but notice the duck waddling around her nest.

'Ah, the chick here? Say hello to our guest, little Berkha! Say hello! Ah, he's shy. You know how children that age can be.

'I found him alone not far from here. I do not know what became of his family, but if I did not adopt him as my own he surely would have died on these harsh isles. Though my kind are a far sight from his flock, surely our differences cannot be insurmountable. If you would like to be helpful to me, could you gather some insects for him to eat? I fear he is too small to be hunting on his own.''Berkha? Our new friend has brought you some delicious morsels to eat! Berkha? Oh dear. I lose track of him for five minutes and already he finds a way to escape....'A man named Phocas seems intent on tracking down Orcs in Jeb Khâtel.Phocas has asked you to head north to Jeb Khâtel and find the Orcs that dwell there.Find the Orcs of Jeb KhâtelYour presence in Kafagur has not gone unnoticed, but many of the Orcs seem unwilling to talk to you.

You should find someone who is willing.Find someone in Kafagur who is willing to talk to youYou've found an Orc in Kafagur named Grúshul who wishes to speak with you.

You should talk to her.Talk to GrúshulGrúshul has given you permission to meet with the elder, Zagdúr.

You should find her in Kafagur.Find Zagdúr in KafagurYou have found Kafagur's elder, as well as a familiar Orc by her side -- Shúkurz.

You should talk to him.Talk to ShúkurzZagdúr has politely interrupted your reunion with Shúkurz.

You should talk to her in Kafagur.Talk to Zagdúr'Hail, stranger. You're not from around these parts, are you?

'Have you, by chance, ventured north to Jeb Khâtel and encountered Orcs? I've heard nothing beyond mere whispers, but it is my duty to find them. Alas, everyone here is rather... tight-lipped on the matter.

'If you manage to locate these Orcs, I'll happily pay you for the information.''You aren't the first outsider who's found their way here. But you'd better make sure you don't become the last, you hear? Try anything funny, and we'll gift you an arrow to the throat.

'If you've got important Mâr Naphra business, head up the hill and talk to our elder, Zagdúr. She'll sort you out.''Well, stranger, if you are friends with Shúkurz, then I can push aside some of my wariness for now. What brings you to Kafagur?'

You tell her of the Man in Mâr Naphra who sent you to look for the Orcs.

'Judging by his words, he is an outlander like you -- far from home, and far from his friends. The few in Mâr Naphra who trade with us would never tell him of Kafagur.

'I shall inform our guards to watch out for this man, in case he harbours ill intentions. As for your intentions, however...''${PLAYER}?! You're the last person I expected to see here!

'Don't worry -- Zogmauk, Lumbag, Muzmák, and Shulgolb made it out of Gundabad safely with me. We only just recently arrived ourselves! Some of the folks here weren't too keen on us staying, but we got that all smoothed out. And -- 'A stranger has offered you coin for stealing a Roc's egg.Itho has asked you to steal a roc's egg, a most heinous act.

You should warn any rocs you find. Rocs may found at Aklâradum, a cliff south of Halrax.Talk to Raghda-gûn'Hello there, stranger. Fancy making some coin? I have a job for only the most capable of adventurers, and you have just the right kind of look about you.

'Have you heard of a roc? Vicious, nasty creatures they are. Massive birds with talons like daggers, beaks strong enough to pierce the hull of even the sturdiest ships.

'Well, I represent a wealthy buyer who is interested in acquiring one of these beasts for himself. Fancies if he raises the thing from birth, it'll be loyal. Could you imagine? The power of a roc tamed.

'So here's the job: Go to the roc's nest south of here and nab one of their eggs. Bring it back to me, and you'll have enough coin to live comfortably for the rest of your life anywhere in the world.'

As you recall, Rocs are intelligent creatures, not the mere beasts that this brigand claims them to be. It may be worth warning the nearby rocs that someone has designs on their eggs.'Finally, a visitor who has the sense to address me with any respect. I greet you. You may call me Raghda-gûn. You come bearing a warning for me? I will hear it.'Sekbiri have attacked Zamarzîr. A local guard would like to cull down their numbers to prevent another attack from happening.A worried guard at the gate of Halrax has asked you to cull down the sekbir population in their den on the north side of the island.

Sekbiri may be found at Ghar Jâdam to the north of Zamarzîr.Defeat sekbiri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'You there, with the sword. Or is that an axe? Or a big rock? I can't see very well. Anyway, you look tough.

'Some of the sekbiri from up north strayed close to the gate last week. Thankfully no one got hurt. Well, except for Itho and nobody likes him anyway.

'The town's promised some funds to the idiot -- I mean brave soul -- who's willing to cull down their numbers.'Hûrlub the Bellower was grateful for your help with the spiders and has given you Marâkh, Mother of Tempests.Hûrlub has given you the tempest hammer and explains that he must rest now.'You take old toy. Hûrlub no need anymore.

'Hûrlub just want sleep. Hûrlub and you are friend now.

'See you.''Is this... it? This is the fabled Marâkh, Mother of Tempests?

'It is quite exquisite. Clearly crafted by a talented smith, but I feel nothing from it. If this thing once wielded the power to control the storms of the seas, it does not seem to possess it now.

'Alas, it is just a novel trinket, but we will display it nonetheless! It is a part of the history of the isles. Perhaps one day, it shall grace us with its power, and we shall make safe the isles from its burden of being a graveyard of ships.

'You have my eternal gratitude.'Eshen requested your aid in collecting obsidian and flowers from the rim of the Irkadâr Caldera.The rich soil around the Irkhadâr Caldera, south of Halrax, promotes the growth of beautiful flowers called, ekhwar. The heat from the volcano long ago forged bits of deldêja desired by the artist Eshen.Collect chunks of deldêja from the Irkhadâr Caldera (${NUMBER}/8)Collect bundles of ekhwar from the Irkhadâr Caldera (${NUMBER}/10)You collected the deldêja chunks and ekhwar flowers Eshen asked you to acquire. Return them to the artist at his home in Halrax.Eshen asked that you place the flowers into the dye pot near the oven so that he can begin his work.You placed the flowers into the dye pot. All that remains to do is speak to Eshen.Speak with Eshen'I've longed for a time to give my calloused hands a rest. Here, in Halrax, I finally have that time and an inclination to pursue something new and creative. A fever recently slowed my pace, forcing me to abandon my goal of scouring the Irkhadâr Caldera for the precious obsidian and beautiful flowers that ring the hollow.

'Would you be willing to go there and help me? I need the obsidian because all the artists use the sea-glass. Sea-glass isn't inspiring. Sea-glass is insipid.''Do you see how pure the deljêda is? It gleams so brightly at the edges and swallows the light as you move toward its centre. It's beautiful. Thank you for getting this for me.

'The ekhwar, too. Beautiful. Please place them in the pot over by the oven. I will begin my work immediately.''Magnificent, friend. I shall be known all across Shield Isles as the greatest artist. You have set me on a path toward success, and I thank you dearly for your aid.

'Now, I must begin. The muse strikes me.'Anyâmat harbours aspirations of being a great shanty-man.Anyâmat has asked you to help her become a great shanty-caller by bringing her along for some adventures.Wait a momentAnyâmat has asked you to help her become a great shanty-caller by bringing her along for some adventures.

While in Zamarzîr, use Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory to summon Anyâmat to your side.Summon Anyâmat with the whistle and complete 'Fightin' Freebooters'Anyâmat has asked you to help her become a great shanty-caller by bringing her along for some adventures.

While in Zamarzîr, use Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory to summon Anyâmat to your side.Summon Anyâmat with the whistle and complete 'What if We Fight a Giant Crab?'Summon Anyâmat with the whistle and complete 'Zamarzîr Treasure Hunt'Anyâmat has asked you to help her become a great shanty-caller by bringing her along for some adventures.'O'er the waves, we shall set sail...

'To the horizon with the help of a tail... wind.

'No no that's terrible!

'Oh! You! Hello! My name is Anyâmat, the greatest shanty-man there ever was! Or at least, that's what they will call me some day. You see, I have such a deep love of song and the romanticism of sailing, but aside from the trip from Minas Tirith to here, I will confess I don't have much sea-faring experience.

'What if I were to follow you around and observe you on your adventures? Perhaps that will provide the inspiration I need!'

She hands you a small whistle.

'Use this to call me as you travel about Zamarzîr. Oh, we are going to have so much fun together!''Well I think that's quite enough adventure for me. I had a lovely time but I don't know how you have the energy to do this every day! This ought to give me enough inspiration to come up with new lyrics.

'I'm going to take that whistle back from you now and head back to Halrax. Come find me when next you're in town.'The dwarf emissary asked for a bond of secrecy, recorded your response in a ledger, and then informed you of his purpose in Halrax.Bekhel enlisted you to search for signs of the Temámir ship near the settlement of Halrax. You recall the bond you made to keep their motivation secret.Search the shore of the islands south-west for the Temámir shipWhile searching for the Temámir vessel, you discovered a wounded Temámir sailor stranded on the shore.Speak with the dwarfMulûg sent you toward the Corsair ship that set upon his vessel and stole the shipment bound for Umbar Baharbêl.Find the Corsair ship beached on the shoreYou found the Corsair's ship. You also found the captain. Confront him and find the cargo.Face the Corsair captainYou can see nothing that looks like a shipment on the shore. Perhaps the cargo you seek is on the deck.Board the Corsair ship and search the deckWith the captain dispatched and his crew eliminated the cargo is yours.Collect the Temámir cargoBekhel and his entourage arrived while you fought the captain. You hear them on the shore nearby.Bekhel thanked you for your assistance in recovering the stolen shipment and dispatched you to Halrax to inform Ithurga that Halrax is beyond suspicion and well-liked by the Kindred of the Coins.Speak with Ithurga at his home in Halrax'Call me Bekhel.

'Your leader is wise to be concerned. Our arrival is fraught.

'A Temámir ship of glorious craftsmanship beyond any other in the Umbari fleet went missing. My lord received an urgent missive mentioning that the vessel was under pursuit as it neared Halrax.

'When it did not arrive soon after the delivery, we left the city to learn its fate. Thus far, the people in Halrax have proven evasive and suspicious. We grow increasingly aware of their lack of allegiance.

'You seem to be wiser. Perhaps you can aid us. Will you look for the ship?''Ho there! Do not fuss over me. I look worse than I feel. The rest of my crew didn't fare as well. Worse, we lost our shipment when the Corsairs set upon us.

'Halrax is not far from here. I was making my way there to beseech Ithurga's aid. Your arrival is auspicious. The dreaded Corsairs are beached to the west just a little further. I'd travel with you but for my knee.

'I'll continue toward Halrax and dispatch Bekhel and his guard to meet you at the ship. I fear I'd only hinder you in a fight.

'Go now and tell the Corsair dog of a captain, Mulûg sent you.''You'll be leaving that crate right where it is, and I'll claim anything on your person as payment for any crew-mates you slaughtered!''I am pleased you proved trustworthy. I will have the shipment if you would. We will take this scoundrel back to Umbar Baharbêl with us. His penance will be to serve in the pit for as long as Khôltekh deems necessary.

'Return to Ithurga and tell him he is beyond suspicion, and you saw this to its acceptable resolution. In fact, tell Ithurga that the Kindred look favourably upon Halrax. You have proven a worthy ally this day.''Favoured by the Kindred? What did you do for them? No, don't tell me what you've done. It's better if I don't know. You've lifted a weight off of my shoulders, ${PLAYER}.'

He beams.

'Favoured by the Kindred. I almost want to return your tithe. I have a better idea.'The arrival of a dwarf emissary and his entourage from Umbar Baharbêl unnerves Ithurga. He asked that you deal with the visitors.Ithurga's concern over the arrival of an emissary and his entourage from Umbar might be an ill-omen and asked that you enquire after his purpose in Halrax.Find the dwarf emissary and his companyAs you searched Halrax's docks, you spied the dwarf and his entourage. Make your introductions and enquire why they are in Halrax.Introduce yourself to the dwarf emissary and ask why he is in HalraxYou have a decision to make. Learn why the dwarf is here in Halrax and bind yourself to secrecy or refuse and fail in the task Ithurga assigned.Give the dwarf your word of secrecyYou made your intention clear. The dwarf is prepared to inform you of his purpose in Halrax. Speak with him.'Yours is not the only unexpected arrival, friend.

'Shortly before you arrived, an emissary from the Kindred of the Coins came by ship. Since he landed, he's been asking questions... questions that give me leave to think he's not wholly here for appearances.

'I run this place proper-like and want no trouble with the Kindred. As the newest friendly-type in town, why not make your acquaintance with them?''I'm not sure where you can find the dwarf and his company. I only know that they are somewhere within the town. Why not search near the docks to start?''Forward. Very forward. I'll be honest, it's refreshing, given the welcome we've received since our arrival. People outside of Umbar Baharbêl have not yet come to trust the Kindred of the Coins. A sadness, I am afraid.

'As for why we have come to Halrax, I am afraid that I cannot share this news with you unless you bind yourself to secrecy.

'Are you willing to bind yourself in such a way?''Very well.'

The dwarf nods to a member of his entourage who scribbles something into a ledger.Halrax, a lively town of pirates and freebooters, is nestled on the isle of Zamarzîr in the Shield Isles.Ithurga is outside his home atop the hill in Halrax.

After arriving in Halrax on the isle of Zamarzîr, a freebooter instructed you to speak with Ithurga, the Grey Rogue.Talk to Ithurga, the Grey Rogue'Newcomers need to speak with Ithurga. If you're not willing to make that effort, then you'd best consider shoving off to another port on the Shield Isles, stranger. You'll find Ithurga outside his home at the top of the hill.''It's good that you came to see me, stranger. As you learned, my name is Ithurga. I oversee Halrax. I maintain its operations and its people's safety. I'm sure you understand that strange faces make people wary.

'They become warier when they see idle hands belonging to those faces. If you want to be welcome here, do your part and show the locals that you mean well. Understand?'Anyâmat harbours aspirations of being a great shanty-man.Anyâmat thinks it would be a great idea to fight a giant crab named Shelly.

Shelly may be found on Baj Khatûg, an island off the eastern shore of Zamarzîr.Defeat ShellyShelly has fallen! Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.

Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.Talk to Anyâmat'I once overheard a sailor tell a story wherein she faced down a ferocious beast. Let us seek out the most horrifying creature these isles have to offer! There is a giant crab on a small island east of here. I hear folks have nicknamed it Shelly. Let's go fight it!''What a fearsome beast! Its hands were like spiked gauntlets! You were lucky I was around to help or you'd have been in a lot of trouble.'Large crabs roam a beach on the north-east side of Halrax.Oversized crabs have taken over the beach of Baj Khatûg east of Zamarzîr.Discover Baj KhatûgOversized crabs have taken over the beach of Baj Khatûg east of Zamarzîr.

Defeat crabs.Defeat crabs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'I don't know if I want to eat one of those things.' The woman in threadbare boots grimaced at the hard-shelled creatures.

The woman in a grey cloak put on a smug smile. 'Yes you do. You just don't know it yet.'

'They look like they'll be crunchy.'

'You remove the shell, you dolt. The meat inside is as sweet and tender as anything you've ever had.'

'They're scary to look at,' Threadbare Boots said.

'Then don't look at them,' Grey Cloak retorted, her patience cleaving paper thin. 'Trust me, a little butter and some sour fruit and you'll be happy as a clam.'

'I don't like clams either.'Anyâmat harbours aspirations of being a great shanty-man.Anyâmat would like to dredge for buried treasure on Baj Khatûg.

Baj Khatûg is an island off the eastern shore of Zamarzîr.Dig at the first spotAnyâmat would like to dredge for buried treasure on Baj Khatûg.

Baj Khatûg is an island off the eastern shore of Zamarzîr.Dig at the second spotAnyâmat would like to dredge for buried treasure on Baj Khatûg.

Baj Khatûg is an island off the eastern shore of Zamarzîr.Dig at the third spotAnyâmat would like to dredge for buried treasure on Baj Khatûg.

Baj Khatûg is an island off the eastern shore of Zamarzîr.Dig at the fourth spotYou've found things that could be considered treasure. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next.

Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.Talk to AnyâmatAnyâmat holds a shovel aloft as if it were some prize.

'Treasure! I'm always hearing about sailors looking for treasure that's washed ashore.'

They thrust the shovel into your hands.

'I will tell you where to dig. I am a very lucky person and tend to have a good sense for these sorts of things.''Do you think this is the owner of the boots?' Anyâmat wonders aloud as she stares at the skull.

'Maybe... that is enough treasure hunting for today.'Keteph wants to create a feast to celebrate with his family and friends the freedom granted under the reign of the Kindred of the Coins. He bid you to collect fine crab meat from the crabs on the western shores of the Cape.Keteph asked you to make your way south and west of Jax Phanâl along the shore to find and collect delectable crab meat from the crabs there for a feast he means to prepare for friends and family.'If the magistrate vouches for you, then I am willing to accept your assistance.

'I desire the delectable meat from crabs crawling along the shoreline to the north, west, and south-west of our outpost. I mean to serve a feast for friends and family to celebrate our newfound freedoms.

'Sadly, that freedom only pertains to the outpost itself! The road south is endangered by Haradrim, and I will risk neither life nor limb. But you... you look like a seasoned combatant.

'I know the task is a menial one, but will you collect the meat for me?''Yes. Yes, these shall do. I will prepare a proper feast with these offerings. I am in your debt. Let me offer you something for your efforts.'Tankho asked you to deal with a creature that watches the moving trees in Jâghimsa, the forest to the north of Rhakatâb. He also asked that you collect tree sap while you are there.Make your way north and east through the woods in the shadow of the mountains outside of Rakhatâb and search for evidence of the creature the workers say dwells at Jâghimsa. Collect the sap from the moving trees within the wood.Search for the creature that defends the woods of Jâghimsa'I could use your help, ${PLAYER}. The workers complain that the woods north and east of Rakhatâb are haunted, cursed, or worse. They said that a creature, like a living tree, stalks the woods and harries their attempts to get the sap, logs, branches and other needs we have from the woods.

'You have proven able and I would request that you investigate the woods for this... herder. While there, could you help me complete the quota of sap from the trees there? The sap from the living woods there are vital to our ship repair and maintenance efforts.''This sap is exactly what we need. You also were able to find and eliminate the creature? Excellent. This will help to set the workers' minds at ease and likely improve their productivity.

'This is for your effort. Thank you.'A very simple task lies before you. Head to the north and east of the fort and collect logs and branches suitable to keep the fires of Rakhatâb alight.Tankho needs logs and branches collected from Jâghimsa, the forested area to the north and east of the fort of Rakhatâb.'Our workers keep suffering injuries. Is it exhaustion or the perils of the wild? I cannot say. I am tasked with keeping the fires burning, but at the volume these fires must burn, I cannot keep pace.

'What say you? Will you help me put some logs on the fire? I wish I had something more exciting for you to do, for you seem an adventuring sort! Alas, all I require is enough fuel for the fires to stay lit. The wooded area to the north-east should have some logs and branches suitable for my purpose.''This should do for a while. I know this is not the grandest work, but know that it is appreciated. We are building something special here, one fire at a time. Or so I am told.'Taphis has asked you to help get the forges ready to operate fully again.Taphis asked that you assist in the maintenance of the forges to help get them back to working at full capacity. Forges can be found throughout Rakhatâb.Grease the gears (${NUMBER}/5)Stoke the forge fires with the bellows (${NUMBER}/5)Repair the pulleys (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You greased the gears, stoked the flames, and fixed the pulley system; time to return to Taphis and let her know what you have done.'Our forges are almost back to full strength! The fires of the forges are a light for all of Umbar, and might be seen from as far away as Umbar Baharbêl itself! Can you help us finish the task and get these forges fully working again?

'You will find forges throughout the outpost of Rakhatâb.''So much around here needs maintenance, and it is my job to keep it all working. I must tell you, I am tired. If you are willing to help, multiple hands will make the work quick. The gears, fires, and pullies are all just around here.''We did it, ${PLAYER}! The forges of Rakhatâb are at full strength again! At least for now. No telling how long it will last. For the moment though, let us enjoy our successes!'Stúkha told you to search the beach for a particular crab, then subdue the crab and return it to him at his post in Jax Phanâl.Make your way to the north from the dock along the shoreline and look for an ancient and enormous crab there. It is called Imkhâs the Cleaver. Defeat the crab and return it to Stúkha.Find and challenge Imkhâs the CleaverYou defeated Imkhâs. Collect the crab, which now hides in its shell, and return her to Stúkha at the crest of Jax Phanâl.'Stalking the shore to the north and west, Imkhâs the Cleaver stalks and terrorizes travellers. Do not be deceived. Imkhâs is no ordinary foe. It is a crab of extraordinary size and strength. Many have fought the creature, and many have fallen or never returned.

'Perhaps you will be the lucky one to retrieve the creature for me. Are you willing?''This crab is Imkhâs? It looks pitiful. It must be sad that you defeated it. I would be also, should you ever best me in a battle. You have done as I asked and given me what I needed. Thank you, friend. This creature has a purpose. You will see. I will train it to be stronger than it is now, and it will entertain the masses in Umbar Baharbêl.''Do you fear the hunt ahead? If not, head out of the city to the west and hug the shoreline north in search of the great crab, Imkhâs. Defeat the creature and return it to me. Alive.'Imkhâs the Cleaver stands before you prepared to fight.Khôltekh's emissary, Girgish, directs you to a soldier on watch duty that has reported the Haradrim further encroaching upon the city's limits.Girgish instructed you to visit Guard Nimish at the southern entrance of the Jax Phanâl outpost. Guard Nimish regularly informs the emissary of goings on along the southern road. Today, Girgish would like you to fetch the guard's latest report.Collect the report from NimishNimish provided you a report on the latest movements by the Haradrim. Deliver the report to Girgish.'At the southern end of the outpost there is a guard who stands watch by the name of Nimish. Nimish is invaluable for he possesses a keen eye and pays close attention to details.

'He delivers a report to me on a regular basis. I ask that you retrieve this for me today... if you are willing.''Hurry along. We must know what the Haradrim are up to so we can best counter their movements.''Odd that Girgish sent someone else to collect this report. You fit the description that I was given perfectly, though. Please tell her that the Haradrim are getting more brazen. We do not have the force to stand against them if they organize their banners and press an attack upon the outpost.

'Everything is detailed in my report.'The emissary takes the note from you and looks it over. She audibly clicks her tongue and then speaks.

'Interesting. I had hoped that the rumours were untrue, for one shipment intercepted is one too many. We shall need to respond.'Ayaluk explained that he discovered reports from all of the masters of the different disciplines in the fort and asks that you have them pledge that the information he came upon is true.Ayaluk says that he collected written requests from the different masters in the fort. He asked that you get their verbal agreement that they submitted these reports and requests and come back to him.Gain Tankho's pledgeGain Kharishah's pledgeGain Beliash's pledgeGain Hûzo's pledgeYou have gained the pledge of all the masters that they will bear witness to filing these reports. It is time to return to Ayaluk.Return to Ayaluk at his family home in RakhatâbTake the evidence supplied to you and deliver it to Foreman Nûrut in Rakhatâb.Speak with Foreman Nûrut in Rakhatâb'Each foreman submitted reports of accidents, disappearances, and deaths, requesting the effects of the victims to be returned to their families, yet none of the families were compensated. Go to the different masters in the fortress and explain everything to them and gain their pledge that their reports were accurate.

'I would go, but I know I am being watched.''I will not send this information on to the foreman until I have the pledge of witnesses from the masters. It is our custom that there are those to bear witness against the accused and I will see that I follow our ancient rules. But, please, make haste.''Yes, I have submitted those reports to the overseer. How were they never fulfilled? You have my pledge that I will bear witness.''Most recently, I sent a request to have pay sent to the family of a man who lost his arms in a terrible accident. He has not been seen since. I thought he simply returned home! I will stand witness to this.

'If the family was not recompensed and the man is missing there is something terrible at work.''Of course I have sent requests on behalf of injured or slain workers. How is it that nothing has been done to help their families? I pledge to stand witness.''I must supply reports when there are any incidents on site. How did you learn that nothing is being done about them? It does not matter. What matters is that you have my pledge. I will bear witness.''This is what we needed. Here, take these notes to the foreman and inform him there are witnesses who will pledge that these reports were never acted upon. Go quickly. I dare not leave for fear of retribution.''This is unconscionable! These lives have been damaged or lost! Their sacrifices were brushed away in the past, but the Kindred of the Coins pledged they would not allow such as this to happen here. This matter must be addressed.'Defeat many beasts in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat beasts throughout the Cape of UmbarDefeat many beasts in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many beasts in the Cape of UmbarAyaluk is concerned about his brother. He went missing several days ago after a visit from a collector of debts.Ayaluk is concerned that the overseer in Rakhatâb has injured or killed his brother Zûfan.You discovered that there was a missing pack, oil lantern, and trail rations taken from the home.Speak with Ayaluk in RakhatâbZûfan likely went to the place where the siblings used to hide as children, north from the city and then west along the cliffs near the shoreline. Go there and ensure that the brother is well.Find Ayaluk's brother ZûfanZûfan likely went to the place where the siblings used to hide as children, north from the city and then west along the cliffs near the shoreline. Go there and ensure that the brother is well.Witness the tragedyUlanor found Zûfan before you and exacted the blood price for his debts. You need to deliver this sad news to Ayaluk.Bring the sad news to Ayaluk in Rakhatâb'I wonder if you might help me. It is a delicate matter.

'My brother Zûfan has been shaving down his coins, you see, giving the overseer less than her share. I told him not to, but he said he would never get caught. He started doing it for some of the other workers as well.

'Well, this morning I heard a rumour that the overseer caught on to these ruses, and now my brother has vanished. Even if he has run away, I just want to know he's all right. He may be a fool, but he is family.

'Go to our home and see if you can find any clue to where he went. Please, ${PLAYER}, can you help me?''He took enough to survive for some time out in the wild. There is a place we used to go as children. It is north, outside the fort here and then west down toward the shoreline. He must have gone there. Please, see if he is well.''Thank you for trying. The fool knew the risks. I warned him.'

Tears well in his eyes.

'I am going to build a cairn for my brother down at the shoreline. I will try to remember our days of happiness and laughter. Feel free to visit me there.'Ayaluk asked you to return to the foreman to thank him for his aid and concern.Ayaluk asked that you return to the foreman and express his heartfelt thanks.Speak with Foreman NûrutThe foreman was not at his post. Where could he have gone? You hear a nearby whisper that there is a new overseer; perhaps you should go and check.Find and speak with Nûrut'I want to thank the foreman for his assistance. I know that my brother always held him in high regard and he was the only person in this encampment, aside from you, I felt I could trust.

'Could you tell him how grateful I am for the help he provided to us?''It appears that the news reached the ears of the Kindred of the Coins before we captured the overseer. Word arrived with a contingent bearing Rothog's symbol and colour. They took the overseer away and departed; they have already set sail toward the city. It is likely to be a sentence to the pits for the overseer.

'For me, as you can see, I am in a new arena of my own. I pledge, my friend, to do right by the workers here. I will see the work done and do my best to protect them all.

'Thank you, deeply, for your guiding hand in this difficult time. You have proven your worth to us and that service is well remembered, ${PLAYER}.'Keteph's culinary ascent continues. Demand for his stuffed crab shells has increased, and he asks yet again that you help him to acquire more materials for a new recipe.Keteph's continued success weighs upon him, and he makes another request of you regarding the crabs that walk the shores south and west of the outpost of Jax Phanâl. He asks that you gather meat, shells, and claws from the crabs and then return to him at Jax Phanâl.Collect intact crab claws (${NUMBER}/8)Collect crab shells (${NUMBER}/8)Collect delectable crab meat (${NUMBER}/8)Keteph's continued success weighs upon him, and he makes another request of you regarding the crabs that walk the shores south and west of the outpost of Jax Phanâl. He asks that you gather meat, shells, and claws from the crabs and then return to him at Jax Phanâl.'If I had a large enough stick, my friend, I would be driving customers away with swift swings. Alas, I have a mind meant for cooking and so my destiny is to be this outpost's chef.''With the right mix of herbs, spices, and other additives I will create a true feast fit for those loving this crusty critter. Thank you again for your assistance.''You can find crabs along the shoreline. Please, if you don't mind.'The Ledger-keepers maintain the Books of Balance informing the Kindred of the Coins of the honour gained by the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl. Your name is now entered in the Books of Balance.Zarai offered to provide you with details about the ledger-keepers. Listen to her tale to learn why this organization exists.Speak with Zarai the Ledger-keeper in Jax PhânalThe keeper thumbs through pages of scrawl, finally resting her finger on an entry, unmistakably your name.

'Nary a misstep since you arrived on these shores. Reports contend that you are a capable ${CLASS} with many talents. You have a penchant for heroism, a quality some find noble, and you appear outwardly compassionate.

'Your legend, thus far, is unstained by controversy or misdeed. Let us see you keep it this way, yes?

'If you wish to know more about the ledger-keepers, why we are here, why we are necessary, and how we came to be, I will explain it to you.'

She nods.

'But I warn you. Our history is... complicated. Our reason for being, while rooted in the dark past, looks to the promising future.''In the past, our role was to track the actions of those who would oppose the tyranny of the Heirs of Castamir. We did so in secret. We traded information we acquired to the counsel of leadership in exchange for freedom from the lash or the gallows.

'When the Heirs fell, and the Kindred of the Coins came to power, they chose a new path for our talents... one that we quite prefer.'

She offers a genuine smile.

'We fully embrace the need to understand the deeds undertaken for - and against - our burgeoning society. In their wisdom, the Kindred enable us to honour good deeds done for the citizens of Umbar.

'You will find that the people of Umbar will provide you with coins long held as the currency of our land. These coins are little more than keepsakes. We call them ûr in the singular and ûri in the plural. If you wish, you can exchange these coins with us, and we will track your undertakings in our records so that you earn respect, honour, and gifts representative of our culture.

'If you do not choose to use the coins, it will not matter. We will remain ready to track and memorialize efforts undertaken for Umbar Baharbêl and her people. We will record your efforts only when you choose that we should.'

She nods.

'Until you earn our trust more completely, this is all I can say.'Concern over the new powers in control of Umbar and their potential relationship to the Haradrim or the Church of the All-Seeing cause the Order of the Eagle to maintain watch over threats from Umbar Baharbêl.Harthabor is need of assistance to contact his leader in Umbar Baharbêl. Speak with him to learn more.Speak with HarthaborThe sea-hawk sits atop a roof through the archway and east of Harthabor in Jax Phanâl. Find a method to draw the bird down, collect its message, and return it to the agent.Pick up a scrap of meat from the plaza near the sea-hawkThe flat stone on the rampart to the north-east may prove a suitable place to lure the sea-hawk from its perch.Place the scrap of meat on the flat stone to the north-eastYou drew the bird down from its perch and should now remove the message from its leg.Retrieve the message from the sea-hawkHarthabor is waiting to see the message you retrieved.The Watcher on the Wing waits dutifully for you to give it a message to bring back to Achardis. Bring the note and tie it to her leg so she may return it to the Order of the Eagle's leader in Umbar Baharbêl.The bird is away. Harthabor awaits your return in Jax Phanâl. Go to the agent and inform him that all went well.'The threat of the Kindred of the Coins cannot remain unknown. After the fall of the Mâkhda Dahak-'

He shakes his head.

'Forgive me. I am Harthabor, and you should call that place Mâkhda Khorbo, my friend. My folly was not using the local vernacular. Do better than me.'

He begins again.

'After the fall of the Mâkhda Khorbo and the Heirs of Castamir, whispers and warnings from eagles throughout Umbar ceased. Worse, we lost contact with our leader in Umbar City.'

He stops and shakes his head again.

'The citizens call it Umbar Baharbêl, and so should you.

'Can you see why I need your aid?''We set forth to reestablish contact with the leader of the canaries in Umbar Baharbêl, but we were ill-prepared. Missteps and affronts to changes in custom abound. Many of our names are etched in their ledgers, and I know they are not written there because of our heroism.

'Through this archway to the east, I saw a sea-hawk perched atop a roof. That is a courier, I am sure of it! Every day, that bird arrives and perches there looking for something. I have seen a scrap of paper affixed to its leg! It likely seeks the eagle that used to watch this outpost, and has a message to deliver.

'I cannot approach it without drawing attention to me, but you have committed no offence and breached no customs. You can act as our eagle here.

'Coax the bird from its perch and obtain that scrap, then return to me.''That sea-hawk? We call her Watcher on the Wing. She's oft up there waiting for a scrap of meat to fall off a careless plate. She doesn't care much what kind of meat it is. She's harmless, as birds go.''That's the Watcher on the Wing. She's a vigilant bird. She perches at that spot each day she's here. Nary moves unless it's for a scrap of food or a shiny bauble. She's lovely though, isn't she?''I am sure there is a way to draw the bird down from that height so you can take the message it carries.''Ah, thank you for this, friend! The fall of the Heirs and the rise of the Kindred diminished Achardis's capacity to gather information, yet she persists, and still she awaits requests from us. This bird network of hers... she calls them the Watchers on the Wing.'

He produces a small note and hands it to you.

'We need to send this message back to her. Bind the message to the sea-hawk's leg; it will do the rest. Return to me after the Watcher on the Wing has left.'The sea-hawk looks up expectantly, and you fasten the return message to its leg.'Now, my friend, we wait. I thank you. Your effort and attention averted the disaster, or worse, that my folly would have wrought.

'I hope to see you again soon.'You gently remove the paper tied to its leg. The sea-hawk does not seem to mind, and in fact appears to be very comfortable exchanging the information for the delicious dinner you set before it.Concerns over the new powers in control of Umbar and their potential relations to the Haradrim or the Church of the All-Seeing cause the Order of the Eagle to maintain watch over threats from Umbar Baharbêl.Speak with Harthabor at Jax Phanâl and help him obtain the response from the leader in Umbar Baharbêl. Avoid unneeded contact as you make your way to and through the outpost.Speak with Harthabor along the outer wall at Jax PhanâlThe sea-hawk sits atop a roof through the archway and east of Harthabor in Jax Phanâl. Find a method to draw the bird down, collect its message, and return it to the agent.Pick up a scrap of meat from the plaza near the sea-hawkThe flat stone on the rampart to the north-east should prove a suitable place to once again lure the sea-hawk from its perch.Place the scrap of meat on the flat stone to the north-eastYou drew the bird down from its perch and should now remove the message from its leg.Retrieve the latest message from the Watcher on the WingOnce again, the bird dutifully descended from the roof-top and delivered its message. Deliver to the agent without being seen.The Watcher on the Wing waits dutifully for you to bring the return message.Harthabor waits for you to return.Friend,

The Watcher on the Wing returned. I require your aid at Jax Phanâl. Please make haste and do not draw attention.'I am glad to see you again, ${PLAYER}. The Watcher on the Wing returned at sunset last evening. We need to obtain its latest message.''I know the risk I place upon you, but we must ensure that we find out all we can from the leadership in Umbar Baharbêl. Please coax the courier again and get the latest communication from our leader in the city.''What does the Watcher on the Wing have for us today?

'I see: our leader is alive and still obfuscated from the Kindred of the Coins. Though it appears her reach diminished after the fall of the Heirs of Castamir, she maintains enough sway in the city to provide us with these details. I will work toward finding a way to get her the aid she requires.'

He scribbles a note.

'Attach this to the courier, as before. I will work on getting you into the city to meet with our leader, Achardis.''Send the message back with the courier. I must find a way to get you into the city and to our leader.'You tie the return message to the sea-hawk's leg and it peers up at you with beady eyes.You remove the latest message from the leg of the Watcher on the Wing.'Once again we must wait. When it is safe for Achardis to meet with you, she will let us know. Until then we must remain beneath the notice of any who might wish her harm.'The Ledger-keepers maintain the Books of Balance informing the Kindred of the Coins of the honour gained by the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl. Your name is now entered in the Books of Balance.Zarai has a concern that she needs to address. Speak with her in Jax Phanâl.Speak with Zarai at her post in Jax PhanâlZarai provided a general area east along the mountains where a courier lost their delivery. She requires that the satchel reaches Aphamâr, the ledger-keeper of Rakhatâb.Find the satchel along the foot of the mountains to the south-eastWith the satchel recovered you should deliver it to the ledger-keeper Aphamâr in Rakhatâb. You were told she usually stands across the path from the stable-master.Deliver the runed leather satchel to Aphamâr in RakhatâbAphamâr is not where you expected to find her. Núrut of Rakhatâb likely knows her whereabouts. Find and speak with the dwarf near their office at the crest of Rakhatâb.Find Aphamâr in Râhal Ghol, the upper ward of Umbar Bahârbel.${PLAYER},

We hope this message finds you well. Your efforts throughout Umbar Baharbêl fill our pages with credibility and nobility unseen in these lands for ages. We are pleased that an ally like you is in our midst.

It is for this reason that I write to you. Your proven capacity for both compassion, discretion, and swift reciprocity are needed. At your earliest convenience, please return to me at Jax Phanâl. There is a matter of import I wish to discuss.

Zarai
Ledger-keeper of Jax Phanâl'It is fortuitous that you return to me. I sent you a letter. I was unsure if it reached you. That is of no matter now.'

She pauses and shifts uncomfortably.

'You prove yourself daily to Umbar Baharbêl. There is a matter that recently came to my attention. I would ask for your aid if you are willing to provide it.''Our roles, while necessary, breed discontent with some areas of the populace. Some believe, incorrectly, that our records detail all actions undertaken within Umbar Baharbêl and that we expose or trade secrets to the guards or Kindred's enforcers. Some believe we still serve the Heirs of Castamir.

'Neither is true.

'We humbly do our work as a form of penance for the years of torment wrought upon the populace. Self-preservation is a powerful motivator.

'Because of this, our couriers and aides sometimes find themselves the target of ire or worse.

'A courier travelling south toward Rakhatâb was assaulted and lost one of our ledgers during the attack. The courier is well. You needn't concern yourself with their welfare. I require your attention on the ledger.

'While escaping an assailant, the courier stumbled off his mount and ran east toward the mountains. Along the way, he dropped the pack containing my latest ledger. I no longer require the book; I need it delivered to my colleague Aphamâr at Rakhatâb. She usually stands across the path from the stable-master in Rakhatâb.

'Can you do this?''Find the satchel somewhere to the south-east beside the mountains and deliver it to Aphamâr. She should be amongst the workers in Rakahtâb.''Aphamâr is not at her post in Rakhatâb. I cannot say what occurred. Please inquire with the Núrut of Rakhatâb about Aphamâr's whereabouts. We must deliver this ledger.''Aphamâr is not at her post in Rakhatâb. I cannot say what occurred. Please inquire with the Núrut of Rakhatâb about Aphamâr's whereabouts. We must deliver this ledger.''Aphamâr hasn't graced the walkways of Rakhatâb for nearly a moon. Ulanor, the overseer, found her presence untenable.

'Last I heard, Aphamâr returned to Umbar Baharbêl and took residence in the Upper Ward. You may find her there.''If Aphamâr returned to Umbar Baharbêl, she will be in Rahâl Ghol. That is the uppermost ward in the city. Hurry and deliver the ledger to her.''You are a friend, a warden of merit, and a courier too.

'My time at Rakhatâb unceremoniously ended nearly a month ago. Ulanor's sway there will abate. Time and the pits judge all who transgress the Kindred in Umbar Baharbêl; her time will come.

'I have expectantly waited for this delivery from our usual courier. Strangely, you are here, but your legend in Umbar Baharbêl grows as swiftly as the tides in storm.

'For now, ${PLAYER}, this is all I require. When the time is right, we will call upon you again.'The Ledger-keepers maintain the Books of Balance informing the Kindred of the Coins of the honour gained by the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl. Your name is now entered in the Books of Balance.Aphamâr, dwelling in the upper ward called Rahâl Ghol in Umbar City, wants to speak with you about your ledger.Speak with Aphamâr at Rahâl Ghol in Umbar BaharbêlAphamâr showed you respect in bowing to your deeds within Umbar. She asks that you accept a gift from the Ledger-keepers and requests that you bow to convey your thanks.Bow to Aphamâr in a show of respect and honourAphamâr is at Rahâl Ghol, the Upper Ward of the city.${PLAYER},

I invite you to join me at Rahâl Ghol. We are to acknowledge the efforts and strides you make to assist and aid the people of Umbar Baharbêl.

Please attend to my request as soon as you can.

Gratefully,

Aphamâr
Ledger-keeper'Your timing matches your ledger; impeccable.

'I recently sent a message to gain your attention. I am pleased to see it was unnecessary and that you returned to me of your own accord. Let us speak.''I want to thank you for understanding and trusting our process, friend. We occupy a tenuous position in the new structure implemented by the Kindred of the Coins.

'Some feel our presence causes more harm than good. Others slowly recognize the value of documenting the merits undertaken by the people here. Regardless of your feelings, you abide by our requests and honour the folk who commend you using the ûr they provide.

'We want to formally recognize your contribution to Umbar Baharbêl and the defence of her people. The city and her people need defenders and supporters like you to continue aiding us in emerging from the darkness that once enveloped our lands.

'The Kindred of the Coins is a shining beacon where once only shadow stood. You, friend, contribute to the development of our society.

'I bow to you, ${PLAYER}, as a sign of respect and gratefulness.

'It is our custom that if you accept this sign, you should bow to show the same respect to my office.''You adhere to our customs, defend our people, and bring no harm to the land. Your legend among the newly freed populace of Umbar Baharbêl grows, and so do your responsibilities.

'Thanks be to you, ${PLAYER}.'Concerns over the new powers in control of Umbar and their potential relations to the Haradrim or the Church of the All-Seeing cause the Order of the Eagle to maintain watch over threats from Umbar Baharbêl.Harthabor is pleased with all of the work you've done for the Order of the Eagle. He asks that you speak to him so he can provide details about how you can meet with Achardis.Speak with Harthabor on the outer wall of Jax PhanâlYou were told to travel to the Fleet-fast docks and then head east into the Lower Ward to find Achardis's bath-house, located on the northern side of the ward.Friend,

Passage is secured. Make haste to Jax Phanâl. I will see you on your way. Opportunity is not a lengthy visitor.'Your continued efforts to help us ensure that the influence of the Kindred of the Coins is not shaped by external hands have earned you an audience with Achardis.''Find your way to the Fleet-fast docks in Umbar Baharbêl. From there, travel east into the Lower Ward and find Achardis's bath-house. It is located on the northern side of the ward.''Welcome, eaglet, you have proven an able and trustworthy ${RACE}. I am Achardis.

'The people of Umbar Baharbêl call me Oma.

'I watch over them, in my way, and keep them safe. There are still many threats that linger from the rule of the Cult of the All-Seeing and the Haradrim of Ordâkh. We are lucky to have an ally like you to assist us. I know that this shall continue to be a relationship that benefits us all.'Nauriel is ready to continue with the reason for the voyage: the rescue of her son Thorongil from the Kindred of the Coins in Umbar.Caebar is at the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.Talk to Caebar at Voyage's EndMembers of your crew have gone ahead to the Cape of Umbar, located south-east of the Shield Isles.Travel south-east of the Shield Isles to the Cape of UmbarGimli is at the Cape of Umbar, waiting for direction.Talk to Gimli on the Cape of UmbarLegolas is at the Cape of Umbar, waiting for your suggestions about how to proceed with the mission.Talk to Legolas on the Cape of Umbar'The sailors believe that the Wave-hunter is not damaged beyond repair, but it will still take too long to repair the hull and make the ship seaworthy. He may sail again, but we cannot afford to wait.

'We must take the over-land route to the City of the Corsairs, ${PLAYER}. We cannot risk any further delay.''The sailors believe that the Wave-hunter is not damaged beyond repair, but it will still take too long to repair the hull and make the ship seaworthy. He may sail again, but we cannot afford to wait.

'We must take the over-land route to the City of the Corsairs, ${PLAYER}. We cannot risk any further delay.''Travelling to the City of the Corsairs by land will take longer, but I do not think we have any other choice. We can reach the Cape of Umbar by travelling south-east along the Shield Isles, for the Cape lies beyond the island of Zamarzîr.

'What do you think, ${PLAYER}? When we arrive on the mainland we should stop and discuss our approach to the city. I am unfamiliar with the geography of the over-land route, as are most of the crew. It would have been different if the Wave-hunter had not run aground, but there is nothing to be done about that now.''Travelling to the City of the Corsairs by land will take longer, but I do not think we have any other choice. We can reach the Cape of Umbar by travelling south-east along the Shield Isles, for the Cape lies beyond the island of Zamarzîr.''Here we are!''Here we are!

'How much longer do you think we have to go? I had thought to see the City of the Corsairs when we arrived on the mainland, but it is not yet in view.''How much longer do you think we have to go? I had thought to see the City of the Corsairs when we arrived on the mainland, but it is not yet in view.''The Cape of Umbar. We have made it to the final leg of our journey, ${PLAYER}. We are almost at the end of our mission.'

Legolas gives you a wry look.

'Almost, I said. There is more walking to be done, much to Gimli's displeasure. I tried to lighten his mood by offering to find him some Umbari coins, the silver gîmli, but he did not seem amused by that either.'You have made the crossing to the Cape of Umbar from the Shield Isles and should now turn your attention toward reaching Umbar Baharbêl.The settlement of Jax Phanâl is to the east.Enter the settlement of Jax PhanâlJâkin is in the settlement of Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.Talk to Jâkin in Jax PhanâlDriftwood has accompanied you to Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.Jâkin is in the settlement of Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.Talk to Jâkin in Jax PhanâlThe Haradrim that were pushed out of Jax Phanâl have a camp to the south where they keep the things they stole.Defeat Haradrim at Grijâti south of Jax Phanâl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Retrieve Umbari Book of HistoryRetrieve Umbari Book of RomanceRetrieve Umbari Book of FloraYou recovered the stolen books and should bring them back to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl.Driftwood has accompanied you to Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.Nauriel has made the crossing from the Shield Isles to the Cape of Umbar, and you should speak with her outside Jax Phanâl.Talk to Nauriel outside Jax Phanâl'This is not the road we expected to take to the City of the Corsairs, ${PLAYER}, but it is now the one we must walk. Let us ask someone in the nearby settlement how best to reach Umbar Baharbêl. The conclusion of King Elessar's mission awaits us there... but we cannot complete this quest until we reach the city.''Let us ask someone in the nearby settlement how best to reach Umbar Baharbêl. The conclusion of King Elessar's mission awaits us there... but we cannot complete this quest until we reach the city.''You have come to Jax Phanâl with a curious group, stranger. I hope you and your friends will cause no trouble here, for if you do, the Kindred of the Coins will see that it is the last trouble you make. Umbar Baharbêl has been made a Free City once again, and under the rule of the Kindred the Haradrim of the Great Southern Empire have been driven out of Jax Phanâl and other villages along Umbarkhîl, the Cape of Umbar. The Empire of Ordâkh has no claim upon us, and never will again. They plundered our valuables when they fled, and even now they muster their warriors at a camp to the south. They have no interest in some of the things they stole... they wanted only to deprive us of them.'

Jâkin studies your face carefully.

'Are you a helpful sort? Or do you only wish to learn what you can and move on, leaving we who struggle here behind when we are not useful to you? Few come to Jax Phanâl without reason, and fewer still leave the Shield Isles without some ill intent. I wonder what my silence might be worth to you? There must be some who would be interested to hear of your little group of travellers. Unless you are a helpful sort. Then it might be different.''Are you a helpful sort? Or do you only wish to learn what you can and move on, leaving we who struggle here behind when we are not useful to you? Few come to Jax Phanâl without reason, and fewer still leave the Shield Isles without some ill intent. I wonder what my silence might be worth to you? There must be some who would be interested to hear of your little group of travellers. Unless you are a helpful sort. Then it might be different.''I think we should help this man, ${PLAYER}.

'He is not wrong, for in other lands we have done as he said: moved on when we learned what we could, remaining only for as long as we needed to learn where next to journey. Now, it was war! So I do not think we could have done otherwise! But if we can help the folk of Jax Phanâl and also keep our presence hidden from those who watch for us, I believe we should.

'What would Jâkin have us do?''Jâkin uses us cleverly, ${PLAYER}. I recognize the tactic from my days of... banditry.

'But he is not wrong about this: his silence will aid us more than an errant word to the wrong folk, and if we might accomplish some good for the people here at the same time, how should I put it? Everyone wins, or at least no one loses more than anyone else, which is a start, and for me a change.

'What would he have us do?''You are a helpful sort, then? I smile to hear it!

'When the magistrate's forces drove the Haradrim from Jax Phanâl, the occupiers fled with whatever valuables they could find, but they were not... how would you say it? Choosy. Some of them stole books of great value to me personally, and I would have them back. These are not worth any great amount of Phârzi or Gîmli, but they do contain stories and accounts that are very dear to me, and I want them back.

'The Haradrim will have them at their camp to the south. Retrieve my books and defeat any of the warriors you must, and you will prove yourself a helpful sort.''The Haradrim will have them at their camp to the south. Retrieve my books and defeat any of the warriors you must, and you will prove yourself a helpful sort.''I am most grateful for this service you have provided this day! These books are very dear to me, and I could not bear to think of them in the hands of the Ordâkhim, never to be read again. They did not know the worth of the treasures they stole from us!

'You are a friend to the Free City of Umbar; I see that now. I will tell none of your arrival here. The merchant road runs along the coast southward to Rakhatâb, where it turns north and passes by a small fishing village, Khûtra. Umbar Baharbêl lies just beyond the hills past the village, the shining jewel of Umbarkhîl. Go in peace, and with my best wishes for your health and happiness.''You are a friend to the Free City of Umbar; I see that now. I will tell none of your arrival here. The merchant road runs along the coast southward to Rakhatâb, where it turns north and passes by a small fishing village, Khûtra. Umbar Baharbêl lies just beyond the hills past the village, the shining jewel of Umbarkhîl. Go in peace, and with my best wishes for your health and happiness.''It is... almost like it used to be, isn't it?'

He gazes out past the buildings of Jax Phanâl, and you know he is thinking of Nona. He catches you looking at him and gives you a brief smile.

'Well, thank you for listening to me, ${PLAYER}. Let us return to the shore and see if the rest of the crew has made the crossing.''Thank you for taking my advice, ${PLAYER}. When every party gets something of value, you can be assured they will each stand by the bargain. I learned this on the river, in my old life, and it was a useful lesson.

'Let us return to the shore and see if the rest of the crew has made the crossing.''So this is the Cape of Umbar? The Corsair Daxamat tells me his people call it Umbarkhîl, and it is a land of beauty? For him it may be. For me I see only the land of the folk who stole my son Thorongil away. The sooner we get to the City of the Corsairs, the sooner I will have my vengeance.'

You remind Nauriel that the mission is to rescue Thorongil, not to take revenge, and she gives you a cool look.

'The Corsair Daxamat also says there can be two ways to say the same thing, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps it is the same with this.'Nauriel is eager for you to continue along the coast road toward the City of the Corsairs. Your first stop will be at Rakhatâb along the southern promontory.Rakhatâb is located on the southern promontory of the Cape of Umbar.Travel south along the coast to RakhatâbA crowd gathers around a body on the ground in Rakhatâb.Talk to the woman in the crowdA crowd gathers around a body on the ground in Rakhatâb.Talk to the man in the crowdThe body of an aged man lies dead on the ground in Rakhatâb.Examine the body of the victimA guard has called for you to step away from the body, and glares at you with distrust.Talk to the guard in RakhatâbDaxamat stands by the crowd in Rakhatâb.Talk to Daxamat by the crowd in RakhatâbFolk in the crowd believe one of the Corsairs from the camp to the north-east, up the coastline, may be responsible for the brazen murder in Rakhatâb.Defeat Corsairs in the Cape of Umbar and at Kan Skûrja, north-east of Rakhatâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Daxamat is outside Rakhatâb, waiting to hear what you learned from the Corsairs.Talk to Daxamat outside RakhatâbDaxamat runs off to distract the guards.Wait for Daxamat to run offThe coffer containing evidence taken from the victim of the murder in Rakhatâb is outside the keep, to the south-east.Search the evidence coffer outside the keep in RakhatâbYou agreed to meet with your crew outside Rakhatâb on the south-eastern beach to examine the evidence you retrieved.Meet up with your crew on the beach to the south-east of RakhatâbSirgon is at your meeting spot outside Rakhatâb.Talk to Sirgon outside RakhatâbDaxamat has arrived at your meeting spot south-east of Rakhatâb, and you should show him the evidence you retrieved from the coffer.'No matter what awaits us at the end of the journey, there are still miles to go before we reach it. What is the name of the next settlement along the merchant road to the south? Rakhatâb?

'Then it is to Rakhatâb we must go.''What is the name of the next settlement along the merchant road to the south? Rakhatâb?

'Then it is to Rakhatâb we must go.''Murder! Murder!'

The woman tears her gaze from the body lying on the ground and seems to see you for the first time.

'Is nowhere safe anymore? This poor man was slain, right here in the open! I did not get a good look at the man who stabbed him, but he was tall, I do know that. And bearded! He had a great dark beard! One of the Corsairs who camp up the shore to the north-east, I think he was! He must have come here to Rakhatâb with evil in his heart, and death in his mind!

'Did anyone else see this man? Oh, it is terrible!''Did anyone else see this man? Oh, it is terrible!''A tall man, with a dark beard? I cannot say I saw him.

'But this man was just minding his own business, and I heard him cry out as he fell. He was a stranger to Rakhatâb, that is true, but he has been here for a day or two. Why, I think I spoke to him yesterday, but I cannot remember what he was asking about. We spoke about recent events, I seem to recall, and about how the Kindred of the Coins has been dealing with the warriors of Ordâkh that refuse to leave our lands... but the murderer was not one of the Ordâkhim.

'And now this man is dead! Such things were not supposed to still happen after Ordâkh was driven from Umbar! The Kindred promised us peace, and for the most part they have delivered it!''This man was just minding his own business; I heard him cry out as he fell. He was a stranger to Rakhatâb, that is true, but he has been here for a day or two. Why, I think I spoke to him yesterday, but I cannot remember what he was asking about. We spoke about recent events, I seem to recall, and about how the Kindred of the Coins has been dealing with the warriors of Ordâkh that refuse to leave our lands... but the murderer was not one of the Ordâkhim.

'And now this man is dead! Such things were not supposed to still happen after Ordâkh was driven from Umbar! The Kindred promised us peace, and for the most part they have delivered it!''You there! Stay back. No, I do not suspect you in this, for I saw you arrive. But it is not impossible for the murderer to have had help, so you make sure you keep yourself out of trouble. Guardsmen of Rakhatâb will be watching you.

'Did you say you heard a Corsair might have done this? A tall man, with a dark beard? I am not surprised. Even after the rise of the Kindred of the Coins in Umbar Baharbêl, many of the Corsairs refused to swear oaths of peace and loyalty to the new order. Some of them are camped even now to the north-east along the coast, and sometimes they adventure here to Rakhatâb to cause problems for the workers.

'Might one of them murdered this man? I think it likely.''Did you say you heard a Corsair might have done this? A tall man, with a dark beard? I am not surprised. Even after the rise of the Kindred of the Coins in Umbar Baharbêl, many of the Corsairs refused to swear oaths of peace and loyalty to the new order. Some of them are camped even now to the north-east along the coast, and sometimes they adventure here to Rakhatâb to cause problems for the workers.

'Might one of them murdered this man? I think it likely.''Something smells fishy, ${PLAYER}. If my brother were here he would say "it is the right of a Corsair to do as he likes!" and think nothing of it, but there is something about this situation that feels wrong to me. Perhaps I am just not as bold a Corsair as my brother.

'But the camp of Corsairs to the north-east lies in our path. Perhaps we can help the people here by thinning their numbers, and when we return they may have captured the one who did this. What do you say to this idea?''The camp of Corsairs to the north-east lies in our path. Perhaps we can help the people here by thinning their numbers, and when we return they may have captured the one who did this. What do you say to this idea?''I think we have made life a little more safe for the folk of Rakhatâb, but something still bothers me about the murder of that aged man. Why would one of the Corsairs at Kan Skûrja commit such an act? He was a recent arrival to Rakhatâb, much like we are, and yet they did not depart their encampment to threaten us. Did he possess something they wanted? The guards took the victim's belongings away, and unless we hurry they will put the evidence in a coffer within the keep.

'I have had an idea. I will go keep the guards occupied. You find the evidence coffer and retrieve the old man's belongings from it before they can finish bringing it into the keep!. We may find a clue among them. Let us meet up on the beach to the south-east of the city after you are successful!''What have you found, ${PLAYER}? Was Daxamat right? Is there any motivation for the victim's murder to be found among his belongings?'

You unfold the possessions you retrieved from the evidence coffer and study each in turn, handing them to Sirgon after examination.

'A note signed by someone named Galadaith? "There is no information I can give that you have not already been provided, but I assure you that if you offer proof of the deed, you will receive the reward to which you are entitled." That is a familiar name, but why?

'And a knife with a curious insignia on the handle. Is this a snake that coils around itself? See how it goes around the hilt? What does this mean?''If there are clues to be found among his belongings, I do not understand them.''I kept the guards talking for as long as I could manage, but I had to leave before they became suspicious. They believe without question that one of the Corsairs from Kan Skûrja is responsible. I see that your own errand was as successful as mine! What have you discovered?'

Daxamat takes the note and the knife from you, and almost drops them.

'What is... no... it cannot be. I know this symbol! This is... this is the knife wielded by The Blade-twist! I have heard tales of him ever since I was a child... but now he is slain, and will collect no further bounties.

'This... this is bad, ${PLAYER}. We knew the identity of three bounty-hunters hired by Saklaphêl to slay the Kindred of the Coins: The Blade-twist, our own Driftwood, and Cruel Dancer. I think Cruel Dancer seeks to eliminate her competition.'The bounty-hunter Cruel Dancer may be seeking to eliminate her competition and claim the bounties on the Kindred of the Coins for herself, which endangers Driftwood and any who associate with him.Driftwood is outside Rakhatâb.Caebar is at the meeting spot outside Rakhatâb.Talk to Caebar outside RakhatâbThe village of Khûtra is north-east of Rakhatâb along the coast road that runs to the City of the Corsairs.Travel to the village of Khûtra, north-east of RakhatâbBôdo is unsure what to make of your arrival to his village.Talk to Bôdo in KhûtraYou were asked to collect things that may help Khûtra survive the famine with which it has been gripped in recent days.Collect driftwood along the beach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect crab legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bôdo waits for you to return to him in the village of Khûtra.Bôdo told you a woman was looking for you, and could be found atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra.Find the woman Bôdo described atop the rocks north-east of KhûtraA woman has asked to speak with you atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra.Talk to the woman north-east of KhûtraCruel Dancer moves swiftly, and then she is gone.Remain alertGimli waits for you north-east of the village of Khûtra.Talk to Gimli north-east of the village of Khûtra'There is one other who expressed an interest in the bounties posted by Saklaphêl, ${PLAYER}. Cruel Dancer will not know whether Driftwood's interest was real or just a pretense. He may now be in danger, and so may any who associate with him.''Cruel Dancer will not know whether Driftwood's interest was real or just a pretense. He may now be in danger, and so may any who associate with him.''We have been through danger before, ${PLAYER}, and I have seen the horrors of war first-hand. What can Cruel Dancer do to me that I have not already suffered?

'Still, we should remain alert. I would prefer she leave us alone. I looked into Saklaphêl's bounties not so I could claim one, but so I could learn what the Heirs of Castamir and the Kindred of the Coins were each, separately, hoping to accomplish, and whether that would endanger the lands across the Bay of Belfalas. I did not think such an inquiry would lead to anything like this, or a reunion with you!

'I am grateful for the latter, of course.''I do not think Cruel Dancer needs to worry that I might steal her bounties from her, but she has no way of knowing that.

'I will remain alert, and I recommend that you do the same. She is notorious, in her own way, and if half of what I have heard of her is true... we may be in some trouble, ${PLAYER}. The murder of The Blade-twist has the effect of removing one of her competitors, but it is also a message to us, a warning to stay out of her way.''What do we do now?'

Caebar looks around nervously, and then surprises himself with a sudden laugh.

'I know the answer, of course. We continue our journey. Our road leads to Umbar Baharbêl, and it seems there is a fishing village between here and the city, a village named Khûtra.

'I do not think I am becoming any braver, ${PLAYER}, but it may be this adventure is making me more used to living through dangerous situations. Let us hope that continues to be so!'

He looks around again.

'But if you see Cruel Dancer lurking about, you will be sure to tell me, won't you?''I know what we do. We continue our journey. Our road leads to Umbar Baharbêl, and it seems there is a fishing village between here and the city, a village named Khûtra.'This is a poor time to visit this village, stranger. Ever since the great quake shook these lands and the temple on the hill sunk into the earth, an evil has taken the lands hereabout. Famine has come to Khûtra, and disease, and... suspicious folk.'

He stares at you meaningfully. You ask if anyone who has come to the village lately might have inquired about a group such as yours, and he raises an eyebrow.

'Could be so. Could be maybe not. I would have to ask some of my neighbours, and while I'm asking I'm not bringing crab legs back to Khûtra, or collecting driftwood along the shore with which we can smoke the meat and improve the flavour. With the famine going on, that's one of the only reliable sources of food around here, and it is barely edible.''I would have to ask some of my neighbours for the information you want, and while I'm asking I'm not bringing crab legs back to Khûtra, or collecting driftwood along the shore with which we can smoke the meat and improve the flavour. With the famine going on, that's one of the only reliable sources of food around here, and it is barely edible.''You did as I asked? This surprises me, stranger.

'The answer to your question is that yes, you are not the only visitor to recently arrive at Khûtra. A woman there was, and she asked about folk such as those with whom you travel. I saw her again only moments ago, atop the rocks to the north-east.

'I think she is waiting for you to go to her.''You are not the only visitor to recently arrive at Khûtra. A woman there was, and she asked about folk such as those with whom you travel. I saw her again only moments ago, atop the rocks to the north-east.

'I think she is waiting for you to go to her.''We meet again, ${PLAYER}. It is a pleasure to speak with you, as it was before. But you did not know my name then, did you?'

The woman flings one arm dramatically outward and holds the back of her other hand over her eyes.

'Murder! Murder! Is nowhere safe anymore? This poor man was slain, right here in the open! Oh, it is terrible!'

She lowers her arms to her sides and laughs long and loudly.

'It is remarkable how simple it is to make people see what they want to see. I had all the folk of Rakhatâb believing they saw a tall bearded Corsair stab a man to death, right there in the open. Oh, the murder was real enough, and The Blade-twist did not see it coming. Weep not for him. No bounty-hunter should live as long as he did and remain in service. I will have the good sense to hang up my own knife before there is more life behind me than ahead.

'But I wanted to speak with you for a particular reason, ${PLAYER}. I would like to declare for ourselves a truce, and to work together where that is possible. The Blade-twist would share neither money nor information, and slay me with as little regard as I slew him; and that is familiar to me, and in this business that is right. But I observed you speaking with the man called Driftwood in Jax Phanâl, and I could not understand it. For what purpose did he ask you to help the people of that settlement? Not only for their silence. There was something else. I find that most interesting.

'Let us consider the Kindred of the Coins our mutual foe, then? I will help you find them, ${PLAYER}. The bounties belong to me... but it seems to me that you seek them for... other reasons. So long as our aims do not conflict, you may count Cruel Dancer among your allies... if not among your friends. It seems to me you may have friends enough. I trust you chose them carefully?''Who was that woman, ${PLAYER}?

'What? Cruel Dancer? You are joking!'The road to Umbar Baharbêl runs by two places of significance for the region: the temple of Sauron and the wreckage of Calatirion. Either may pose the threat of watchful guards.The Dead that linger near the ruined temple of Sauron to the east will endanger any who travel to the City of the Corsairs.Defeat the Dead outside the ruined temple of Sauron (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sirgon has come as near to the ruined temple of Sauron as he wishes.Talk to Sirgon outside the ruined temple of SauronThe wreckage of Calatirion on the hill of Kharn Arâx can be found to the south-west.Travel south-west where you can have a view of the Calatirion's wreckageLegolas looks up at the wreckage of Calatirion, musing about what he has been told of its history.Talk to Legolas in view of the wreckage of CalatirionYour crew plans to meet on the road to Umbar Baharbêl, and you should join them.Meet up with your crew further ahead, beside the road to Umbar BaharbêlDaxamat stands by the road to Umbar Baharbêl with the rest of your crew.Talk to Daxamat by the road to Umbar Baharbêl'If Cruel Dancer will help us track the location of the Kindred of the Coins, I suppose we cannot turn down her help... but I do not like it! And yet no one asked for my thoughts on the subject, ${PLAYER}, did they?

'But I was looking for you. Several members of the crew were speaking with the folk of Khûtra, and there was a lot of talk about problems further up the road. Some form of festering blight has taken hold of the land to the north-east, and before you can say "best leave well enough alone," Sirgon volunteered to do something about it. He is probably up there right now!

'You should go deal with the Dead that have been reported near the ruins of the temple, ${PLAYER}, unless you think Sirgon can handle himself. Afterward you might want to check on Legolas. He said something about seeing an old tower that fell down in this area some years ago. He said the name of it, but who can remember the Elf-names for such things? It is not like dwarf-names! Now those are easy to recall!''You should go deal with the Dead that have been reported near the ruins of the temple, ${PLAYER}, unless you think Sirgon can handle himself. Afterward you might want to check on Legolas. He said something about seeing an old tower that fell down in this area some years ago. He said the name of it, but who can remember the Elf-names for such things? It is not like dwarf-names! Now those are easy to recall!''Ah, I had thought to help the people of Khûtra with their difficulties, but as I approached the temple I could not bring myself any nearer than this. Thank you for helping them combat these evils.'

Sirgon sighs heavily, a sound you have become accustomed to ever since the man who was once the Lord of Lebennin came ashore upon the Shield Isles.

'I quail at the sight of the Dead, ${PLAYER}, but there is something I fear even more than such as they, and it is a fear that takes the shape of a Man. I fear the meeting with Belondor that surely awaits me in the city ahead. I fear what he will have to say to me, but worst of all: I fear that I may deserve it.

'The Steward Denethor gave me the command to bring Belondor to justice, but I did not refuse it. When I believed I drove him to his death I felt the shame and the guilt of that pursuit, but to learn that he rose from the waves, that he survived... my shame and my guilt are doubled. Nay, they are trebled. And now he is one of those who leads the Kindred of the Coins against Gondor!

'I am sorry. I will pull myself together. I will be fine. You say Legolas intended to visit the wreckage of a tower? I believe that is Calatirion, on the hill of Kharn Arâx, to the south-west.''I am sorry. I will pull myself together. I will be fine.

'You say Legolas intended to visit the wreckage of a tower? I believe that is Calatirion, on the hill of Kharn Arâx, to the south-west.''There it lies. Calatirion.''This was the beacon-tower of Calatirion, ${PLAYER}, constructed by Elendil as a mighty monument of Númenor. I have heard tales from Glorfindel of the Vandassar that stood within it for much of its history, Airessar, as clear as crystal, shining so brightly it could be seen even from far off in the bay.

'I know it was destroyed by the Bright Company to loosen Sauron's bonds upon the Men of Harad during the War of the Great Alliance. The tower itself survived that battle, and would stand for almost three thousand more years, but it would not stand forever. When the Church of the All-Seeing came to Umbar in the vanguard of the Empire of Ordâkh, there were servants of that church who resented that which Calatirion represented; they were the Nazgûl, with the Forsaken Reaver at their head. With sorcery he and his allies toppled the tower, and the memory of that day has lived on in whisper ever since. Even Glorfindel wished not to speak of it, but he told me the name by which folk of Umbar recall that day: Mût Tadaul, the Death of Light.

'The Forsaken Reaver must have perished with his master when Frodo cast the Ring into the Cracks of Doom, ${PLAYER}. But Calatirion remains toppled. It is a reminder to me that evil deeds are not undone by the destruction of those who wrought them.

'We should continue to the east and then north along the road. We have almost reached the city.''There our destination lies!''We are almost there!

'The journey nears its end... and we are still alive, which is more than I expected, if I am being honest with you!'Explore the settlements, outposts, fortresses, and other points of interest in the Cape of Umbar.Explore settlements and other important points of interest throughout the Cape of Umbar.Find Jax PhanâlFind RakhatâbFind Jid PhêsiFind KhûtraThe foreman wants to confront the overseer with the evidence of her covering-up and pocketing the personal effects of those suffering ill fates in Rakhatâb. He asked you to first collect Ayaluk to stand witness.Nûrut directed you to inform Ayaluk that he will confront the overseer and that the brother is expected to stand witness. Find Ayaluk at his family home in Rakhatâb.Inform Ayaluk that the overseer will be brought to justiceAyaluk was not within his hovel. You discovered a small pool of fresh blood in his stead. Deliver this news to the guard.Report the news to Foreman NûrutUlanor is taking Ayaluk to the Corsairs for some evil purpose. Stop her and save Ayaluk.Find Ulanor and rescue AyalukWith the overseer apprehended and Ayaluk safely returned to Rhakatâb you should make your way to the foreman and inform him of the good news.Speak with Foreman Nûrut at Rakhatâb'We cannot allow this to continue. I will bring the matter to the master of the guard.

'Return to the young dwarf and tell him that we will seek justice! Ask that he meets us here so that we may go together to confront the overseer; for his brother and the families of those that the overseer harmed within this fortress.''Hear me, friend. The master of the guard informed me that the overseer left her post and headed east toward the Corsair camp with a prisoner. It appears that Ayaluk's fear of being watched was correct.

'I can only hope that we can get to him in time. The master of the guard said he can spare none to pursue the overseer, but they will follow after you when he can.

'Make haste east toward the Corsair camp and track down the overseer. If you can, rescue the lad.''I will not stand idly by while Umbar withers from within. The Heirs of Castamir were right: the Old Ways are best! We should return to them before we allow scoundrels who do not pay their debts to ruin our future. You fool. You and this meddlesome dwarf obstruct me for the last time. Prepare to die!''The guards informed me that that overseer was apprehended. You managed to also save the lad. We are indebted to your service, but this work is not yet done.'Defeat many Corsairs and pirates in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many Corsairs and pirates in the Cape of UmbarDefeat many Corsairs and pirates in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many Corsairs and pirates in the Cape of UmbarDefeat many crabs along the shores of the Cape of UmbarDefeat many crabs along the shores of the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many crabs along the shores of the Cape of UmbarDefeat many crab along the shore of the Cape of UmbarDefeat many crabs along the shores of the Cape of UmbarDefeat many crabs along the shores of the Cape of UmbarThe overseer of Rakhatâb asked you to collect the debt owed by five Umbari workers.Ulanor instructed you to collect debts from five workers that are behind on their credit. Something seems off. The workers are in the nearby area.Collect debts from sullen indebted workers (${NUMBER}/5)The worker expressed that there is no way that he could pay his debts and that he wanted you to speak with the foreman. You can find Foreman Nûrut in Rakhatâb.Speak with Foreman NûrutThe foreman directed you to the shoreline surrounding Rakhatâb to search for a monstrous crab that defends a great treasure. Once you have recovered the treasure, you are to take it and sell it to a merchant with a penchant for very fine things in Rakhatâb.With enough coin to pay the overseer you should return to her in western Rakhatâb and tell her that the worker's debts were paid in full.'Nûrut tells me that you're a person who gets things done. I'm glad you were able to help him with his menial tasks. Perhaps you will be equally skilled at helping with mine: five workers that have gone into debt.

'We have given these workers many freedoms and much coin for their work. Every bit that we give them, every amount of credit we extend... they abuse! Many have spent more coin than they are given. We don't forget or forgive debts here.

'You should know this: if their debts are not paid in coin and on time, we will settle their debt to us in blood. Either way, the debt will be paid.''I have nothing to give. They already bled me drier than a stone and forced me to work many hours without compensation or food. If I had no other mouths to feed at home, I would make my way back to the sea or to the city. Please, can you speak to the foreman about this?''That's what she asked of you? I know those workers; they don't have the coin. They've used it on food, family, and rebuilding.'

He thinks.

'I may have an answer that saves their hides and pays the overseer her coin.

'To the south and east of here along the shoreline there is a Great Crab. It is rumoured to guard a large pearl.

'There is a merchant here, a collector of beautiful and rare things. I happen to know she will pay handsomely for that pearl.

'Please, ${PLAYER}, bring back the pearl to the merchant over yonder and give the proceeds to the overseer. These men will owe you their lives.''What is this?'

She looks the pearl over.

'My patron will be pleased to acquire this.'

She produces a pouch, hefty with coins. You can hear them jingling.

'This is more than adequate payment for this... bauble. Take it.'The overseer holds the bag in one hand weighing it, measuring it.

'A little more than expected. Good. They know their place.

'However the debts are paid, they are paid. It is good that today these laggards chose coin over blood.

'Thank you for bringing this matter to a close.'Explore enemy encampments and the dangerous wilds of the Cape of Umbar.Explore enemy encampments and the dangerous wilds of the Cape of Umbar.Find GrijâtiFind SúlstrokFind JâghimsaFind Kan SkûrjaFind Ghadir SûdFind KâshtabilFind Gherja MûtFind BêkhmolFind IdwadârFind Taj-kâtaFind Jêbel LakhaFind HâtaphorFind BâlakhatDefeat the dead in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many of The Dead in the Cape of UmbarDefeat many of the Dead in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat the Dead in the Cape of UmbarOnce beneath the rule of the ruthless Heirs of Castamir, the Cape of Umbar emerges from a shadowy chrysalis as a land reborn. The citizens struggle with newfound freedom, the sins of the past, and a desire to cling to the rites and customs of their culture, as they are guided by the hands of Kindred of the Coins.Once beneath the rule of the ruthless Heirs of Castamir, the Cape of Umbar emerges from a shadowy chrysalis as a land reborn. The citizens struggle with newfound freedom, the sins of the past, and a desire to cling to the rites and customs of their culture, as they are guided by the hands of Kindred of the Coins.Complete Explorer of the Cape of UmbarComplete Slayer of the Cape of UmbarComplete Quests of the Cape of UmbarKeteph's feast was a success, but now there is a demand for his cooking that he did not anticipate. He needs more crab meat, and asks you to help with the newfound demand for his skills.Keteph requested you return to the shore to collect more ingredients. His feast was successful, and his culinary skills are in high demand! The people require a new recipe to sate their hunger, and the key ingredient is crab. Head to the shores south and west of Jax Phanâl, collect delectable crab meat crab shells and return them to him.'You again, thanks be to all! I am in a bind, my friend. You see, my feast was a success. Too much a success!

'I simply cannot meet the demand I am seeing for this recipe by myself! I wonder, would you be willing to help me get more of the precious crab meat from the crabs along the shore?''These will do nicely. I know it seems foolish to look at such success as an unwanted gift. Mind you, I am pleased, and the new wealth will suit me and mine well. Please return, I will undoubtedly have more work for you.'A mining foreman asked you to assist with a cave-in that occurred within a cave near Rakhatâb. The cave is east of the fort.To the east of Rhakatâb on the southern slope of the mountains there is a mining cave that suffered a cave-in. Go there and rescue the miners trapped behind the rubble.Speak with Hûzo to travel to Jid PhêsiThe miners are safe, and you escaped the mine. Return to Hûzo and tell him that the mine is either unsafe or home to something that will make it unsafe for his miners to continue working there.Return to Hûzo at the common in Rakhatâb'You assisted me before, and I have need with someone with your skills again. There is a cave not far from here along the southern edge of the mountains to the east. We have workers there, extracting metals for the forges. There's been a cave-in; many lives are in the balance. Please, can you help them?''I wish only for the safe return of the workers. The metals that they mine are important, but not as much as their lives are worth... to me and to them, at the least, if not to the overseer! Please, make haste!''Something was shaking the mine shaft?

'A creature? The earth? No, you are correct. It should not matter what was shaking the mine. We should not return there. I will seek the council of the overseer to determine what should be done.

'Please, take this for your efforts, ${PLAYER}.'Explore the Cape of Umbar.Explore the cape of Umbar.Complete Dangers in the Cape of UmbarComplete Citizens of the Cape of UmbarComplete Treasure-seeker of the Cape of UmbarTagar directs you toward a camp of goblins to the south-east of the outpost. The goblins threaten food supplies on Jax Phanâl by organizing raids against those living there.

Tagar wants retribution.The goblin encampment of Súlstrok is found to the south-east of Jax Phanâl at the foot of the mountains. Most goblins there wear bandanas. Collect the bandanas and return them to Tagar.'To the south-east, by the foot of the mountains, camps a goblin-mob that once rode aboard Umbar's ships. The Kindred of the Coins ousted some of them, but some of the creatures linger still. Those villains are killing my sheep! I want proof that the goblins are slaughtered. Will you go to their encampment of Súlstrok and collect the goblins' bandanas so I will know the job is done?''So you are capable of besting goblins and saving my sheep! The magistrate did well to send you to me. I will sleep better knowing that so many of the goblins have been dealt with. Thank you.'Stúkha bids you take his banner to a camp in the east where the goblin pirates make their home. Challenge the leader, defeat him, and the goblin will make its way to Jax Phanâl.You are to head south-east to Súlstrok, an encampment of goblins once loyal to the Corsairs. Once there, you are to plant the banner given to you to call forth one of the strongest goblins. This will enable a ritual combat. Win, and the goblin will surrender to the emissary in Jax Phanâl.With Shakfut Slit-throat defeated you can now return to Rothog's emissary in Jax Phanâl and inform him of your victory.'In the east, there are goblins who once sailed the seas with us. There is one among them who knows the banner of the lords.

'Go to their camp and plant the banner I give you. This will start a ritual fight between you and the goblin I seek. When you have won, the goblin will come to me. It is their way.''You will find the goblin encampment of Súlstrok to the south-east in the shadow of the cliffside. Search within the camp for the ritual circle. Plant the banner I gave you and defeat the leader in ritual combat. When it is done return to me.''A challenge? With Rothog's banner, no less. Very well. I will honour the ritual, gut you like a fish and slit your throat to fill our bellies.

'This will prove a wonderful exercise.''I sent Shakfut on to the city. He will make a great fighter in the gladiator pits. You have done well and earned your reward.'The forge-master has asked you to go to the hills to the north or east of Rakhatâb and bring back goat fat for greasing the machines.Goats with thick layers of fat are found in the hills north or east of Rakhatâb. Goats from either location will do for the forge-master's needs. When you have collected the fat return to Kharishah in Rakhatâb.'Welcome to Rakhatâb! Yes, I've a task that needs doing, if you're able. In order to run these great forges, we need large amounts of goat fat, and we've been running dangerously low for weeks now. Without it, our forges can't fire, and nothing gets built.

'Will you help us? There are many goats in the hills north or east of here. Bring back as much of their fat as you can. You'll be rewarded for it, and you'll have my thanks.''Enough goat-fat for at least a week! This will keep the wheels of the forge moving for certain. You have earned my thanks, and your coin-purse has surely become... fat. Ha! Ha ha ha!

'Just my little joke, friend. We do what we must.'The chef in Jax Phanâl requires assistance with his second recipe after completing his successful feast.Assist the chef of Jax Phanâl with his second recipe.Complete the quest 'Burgeoning Business'The chef in Jax Phanâl requires assistance with his first recipe after completing his successful feast.Assist the chef of Jax Phanâl with his first recipe.Complete the quest 'Demand Absent Supply'Keteph is off to the City of Umbar after Khôltekh's emissary recommended that the guild-masters there try his creation. A new hire now stands in his place with a message for you.Keteph is no longer within the outpost of Jax Phanâl. He hired an assistant to work in his place and has left you a letter to explain what transpired.Read Keteph's letter'Keteph said that you were likely to return. I have something for you if you want to read it.''We are all immensely proud of Keteph. More, we are all so pleased to see that the Kindred is rewarding us for efforts like this one. It is so refreshing to see after so many years of horrid subjugation.'Defeat many Haradrim in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many Haradrim in the Cape of UmbarDefeat many Haradrim in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many Haradrim in the Cape of UmbarHûzo asked that you enter the mine to free the workers trapped within.Rescue the miners trapped by the collapsed shafts throughout the mine.Escape before the mine collapsesYour rescued the miners, but the mine is shaking violently. Make your way out of the mine.Escape the mine before it collapses!You agreed to assist Ayaluk in obtaining proof of the overseer's wrongdoing in Rakhatâb.Meet Ayaluk at the edge of the building near the overseer's chambers.Speak with Ayaluk at a building near Ulanor's chambersAyaluk asked you to distract the guard while he sneaks into Ulanor's office to find proof of her wrongdoing.Distract the guard by clearing your throat <rgb=#00FF00>/ahem</rgb>Distract the guard with a <rgb=#00FF00>/hail</rgb>When the guard starts walking again, distract him by waving <rgb=#00FF00>/bye</rgb>Keep the guard distracted for one full minuteYou distracted the guard well enough for Ayaluk to search and escape. Return to his hiding spot near the building east of Ulanor's office.Speak with Ayaluk near his original hiding spot'Let's make haste and do not be seen.''I only need you to distract the guard for a few moments while I search the office. Distract the guard however you can. Annoy them if you must. Wave bye, hail them, clear your throat at them. Anything to keep them occupied.''What I found is worse than I feared. I need some time to review this information. Meet me at my home. Now I must go!'Defeat lions in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat lions in the Cape of UmbarDefeat many lions in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many lions in the Cape of UmbarGirgish instructed you to venture to the Haradrim encampment of Grijâti to rescue captives taken in the attack on the caravan.

The Haradrim camp of Grijâti is west of the road that goes south from Jax Phanâl.You must head south along the road and then make your way west toward the Haradrim encampment of Grijâti to search for the captives taken from the attack on the caravan. Rescue the eight travellers and return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl.You successfully rescued eight of the caravan captives. Return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl and tell her of your success.Return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl'We must respond, but Nimish is correct that we do not have the forces to spare in a direct confrontation with the Haradrim. By the looks of you, you might be able to handle such a force on your own... is it true?

'Our people are in danger, and I believe you wish to make a name for yourself here? If that is the case, then please, save the captured prisoners held against their will in the Haradrim camp of Grijâti to the south. It is west off the road, along the beach.''You will find an encampment of Haradrim west of the road that runs south of town, near the shore. I know you will use caution in rescuing the citizens of our settlement.''Every one of the citizens you saved paid a visit to either the magistrate or myself, and each of them spoke highly of your valour. In turn, I gathered rewards to repay the considerable risk you undertook on their, and our, behalf.'As a new arrival, you should seek the counsel of the outpost's magistrate.New arrivals must meet with the magistrate. The magistrate is at the crest of Jax Phanâl north of the stable-master, beyond the first right through the arch and at the top of the stairs. Visit Magistrate Zebulo now.Speak with Magistrate Zebulo at the crest of Jax Phanâl'New arrivals should meet with the magistrate. You can find Magistrate Zebulo at the crest of Jax Phanâl, in the heart of the city. From the stable-master, travel through the north gate and turn right through the central arch. Take the stairs up to the crest of the outpost.''New arrivals should meet with the magistrate. You can find Magistrate Zebulo at the crest of Jax Phanâl, in the heart of the city. From the stable-master, travel through the north gate and turn right through the central arch. Take the stairs up to the crest of the outpost.''New arrivals should meet with the magistrate. You can find Magistrate Zebulo at the crest of Jax Phanâl, in the heart of the city. From the stable-master, travel through the north gate and turn right through the central arch. Take the stairs up to the crest of the outpost.''New arrivals should meet with the magistrate. You can find Magistrate Zebulo at the crest of Jax Phanâl, in the heart of the city. From the stable-master, travel through the north gate and turn right through the central arch. Take the stairs up to the crest of the outpost.''A visitor from abroad, eh? Your arrival is most fortuitous. Let us speak plainly.'Rothog's emissary bid you prove your strength by venturing into the wilds. You'll need to survive the vile disease spread by the midges throughout the land.Along the shoreline and plains of the western part of the Cape of Umbar are sea-flies that carry terrible illnesses. To prove that you can survive in the lands, an emissary of one of the Kindred of the Coin instructed you to go get bit by the stinging sea-flies.Become infected by stinging sea-flies (${NUMBER}/6)You survived! The sea-flies certainly are aggressive, and their bite does carry some vile illness. You should return to the emissary in the outpost of Jax Phanâl in the north-west of the Cape of Umbar.Return to Stûkha at Jax Phanâl'You are new. You want to prove your worth to me, emissary of the mighty Rothog?

'You will do this by surviving the wilds in our lands. To the south along the shore, across the plains, forests, and into the hills are insects with a ravenous appetite.

'They bite. They sting. They spread disease. Survive? Return to me and I will test you again.''The sea-flies can be found near sand, soil, and grass. They do not travel too near the foot of the mountains. Find them and prove that you can survive our land, then I may offer you more.''You prove heartier than most. You may well be able to assist me with my requests.'

He looks you over.

'No worse for wear. You want a reward, I presume?'Beliash ensures the fair treatment of the workers at Rakhatâb. He asked you to deliver some extra food to hungry workers and to raise the spirits of dispirited workers in the fort.Make your way through the fort to feed the hungry workers and spread coin to those who have become dispirited with the work and schedules they must maintain.Your work is done. Head back to Beliash in Rakhatâb and let him know what you have done.Tell Beliash you did as he asked'Only a few months freed and already the yoke begins to feel heavy again. Yes, we are free, but the overseer does her best to make certain that we have little of comfort, and no time to enjoy our freedom. The workers suffer for her ill-treatment. Some are being starved, and all are dispirited!

'I managed to get some extra food, and I have a few coins to spare. Could you see that the food is delivered to those that are hungry, and use the money to cheer up those who appear crestfallen?''Food in their bellies and bolstered spirits. It may seem a small thing, but it is a sliver of hope.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. They are good, hard workers. They just are pushed too hard. Once we get through these lean times, I know things will get better. They have to get better.'Girgish wants you to send a message to the Haradrim in their camp to the south. You were tasked with attacking the enemy where they camp.Girgish provided you with a letter you should post within the Haradrim encampment located to the south and west of Jax Phanâl. She also instructed you to eliminate a number of the enemies within the camp so that the proper message is sent to the unwelcome squatters.Defeat Haradrim in the western Cape of Umbar (${NUMBER}/18)Post the message to the Haradrim in the camp of GrijâtiWith the grisly aspect of the task done and the message to the Haradrim posted, it is time to return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl.Return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl'In the past, messengers were sometimes returned to the places from which they came with... let us say "injuries," and let that speak volumes. We want to avoid that sort of thing going forward, but there are times when swords and axes must deliver messages for us. If you are willing, I would like to employ your weapons against our foe: defeat the Haradrim at their camp of Grijâti and post this letter I have written as a warning to them should they remain.''I would have parleyed with the Haradrim were they amenable. Alas, they attacked our people and forced our hand. Head to the south and east and deliver the message we must convey.''I will confide to you that this was not the way that I wanted these issues resolved. I would rather have found a peaceful solution to this matter.'

She sighs.

'The Haradrim proved too inflexible, and attacking our citizens along the road was simply a step too far. May our future days require less violence than this.'Tagar wants you to find proof that the goblins are attacking food sources for the outpost of Jax Phanâl. Gather evidence from the goblin encampment along the mountains to the south and east of Jax Phanâl.Tagar believes that the goblins are attempting to starve the people of Jax Phanâl. He asked that you look for proof in their camp of Súlstrok to the south and east of the outpost.Gather tufts of fur from slain goats at Súlstrok (${NUMBER}/10)Tagar believes that the goblins are attempting to starve the people of Jax Phanâl. He asked that you look for proof of this sort in their camp to the south and east of the outpost.'I know that the goblins are doing more than just harassing our people. I need proof to share with the guards. If we gather enough evidence against the goblins, we can convince Zebulo that we must act.

'I beg you, go to their camp of Súlstrok and search for signs that they are slaughtering the goats that we need for food, and if they are not stopped they will starve us when winter comes!''I knew you would find evidence that the goblins slaughter our food sources for mere sport. I will see these reach the guards. In time, perhaps the magistrate will act.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''Along the mountainside to the south and east of Jax Phanâl is a large camp of scheming goblins. Go there and find tufts of bloody goat fur so that I can prove this goblin-guilt to the guards here in the outpost.'Complete quests in the Cape of Umbar.Complete quests in the Cape of Umbar.Complete quests in the Cape of UmbarKhôltekh's emissary wants you to find the destroyed delivery caravan and the manifest it was carrying. Once recovered, you are to find the items listed within the Haradrim camp.The guard's report suggested that the caravan was ambushed by the Haradrim while travelling the south road. Search along the road for signs of the ambushed caravan.Find the ravaged caravanYou have discovered the caravan. It was clearly ambushed, the cargo stolen, and all occupants are missing. You should set about finding the manifest.Collect the caravan manifestThe manifest lists the items aboard as eight crates of food, an ornate cruet meant as a gift, a sealed document case, and twelve ornate weapons. Perhaps the Haradrim have them within their camp to the east. You should venture there in search of these items.'The goods and materials the Haradrim stole from the caravan cannot remain in their possession. I must admit that the news of their robbery came as a surprise, and I was caught without the manifest of goods on the caravan. While you assist me with these efforts, could you find the site of the attack and locate the manifest, if it survived? Once you have done that, I ask that you recover whatever materials might be salvaged from the Haradrim camp.''Could you find the site of the attack and locate the manifest, if it survived? Once you have done that, I ask that you recover whatever materials might be salvaged from the Haradrim camp.''It appears that you have recovered every article taken from the caravan. This is a triumph, ${PLAYER}. I would not have expected such good fortune even had I organized a party of our own guards. Even then it is likely something would have been missing.

'This is no slight against those within the outpost, just that I believe they are not as careful with the belongings of others as they should be.

'Your efforts are deserving of a reward.'Nûrut directed you to speak with the young worker and see how he is faring.Nûrut asked you to check in on Ayaluk and see if he is well and if he is satisfied with the outcome of the investigation and efforts to expose the overseer's crimes.Find Ayaluk at his home and speak with him'We should ensure that the young dwarf you rescued is well. There is little more that we can do to ease the pain that he surely feels, but the capture of the overseer should bring him some peace.''Justice will be served. That the overseer will meet the fate she deserves must be enough to honour my brother's memory. For the future, I hope that those chosen to take the lead in our rebuilding efforts will exercise care and good dealing! I would rather see the light that dawns on our lands than to dwell upon the shadow that obscures our past.'Tankho asks that you again assist him with the task of collecting sap from the huorns, and timber from the woods to the north of Rakhatâb.Go to Jâghimsa, the woods north-east of Rakhatâb, and collect sap from the huorns and fallen logs from the trees there. Then return to Tankho at Rakhatâb.'Our ships will always have need for sap to patch the hull, and the fires here burn at all hours, so there is always a need for wood.

'If you can help with this, I will see that you are rewarded.''We will put all of this to use. We do not desire to waste any of the resources that we can garner here at Rakhatâb.

'Here, this is for your efforts.'Rothog's emissary sent you into the hills and wilds in search of the matriarch and patriarch of the wild goats that make the western Cape of Umbar their home. You are to apply a sedative to them, defeat them and return them to the emissary at Jax Phanâl.Head into the wilds of the western Cape of Umbar. Search the plains, hills, and mountain edges for the goat sire and dam. Weaken them and use the toxin on them docile. When you've captured both goats, deliver them to Stúkha at the crest of Jax Phanâl.Challenge Rûnax in the hills of the Cape of Umbar WestChallenge Shâba in the hills near Jax PhanâlYou've captured both goats. Deliver them to Stúkha at the crest of Jax Phanâl.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: The rams will find their way if you become separated.</rgb>Deliver the pair of goats to Stúkha at the crest of Jax Phanâl'In the hills, mountains, and sometimes the plains there are two goats standing tall above others in the herd. They are the sire and the dam.

'They mate each season and raise their young. They are known for their strength. We want them for our pit entertainment.

'When you find them, I ask that you defeat them after using this sedative upon them. It will ensure that they do not die, but fall into slumber.

'Collect them then after they fall into this slumber and return them to me.''In the hills, mountains, and sometimes the plains there are two goats standing tall above others in the herd. They are the sire and the dam. When you find them, I ask that you defeat them after using this sedative upon them. It will ensure that they do not die, but fall into slumber. Collect them then after they fall into this slumber and return them to me.'Rûnax appears to dislike you disturbing his stroll.Shâba is perturbed you spoiled her walk.'My friend, you return to me victorious.

'This pair will serve us well and bring joy to those who watch the battles in Umbar.

'Your assistance in this matter is most welcome. Please accept this gift. I am grateful that you've proven so useful to me.'Defeat foes throughout the Cape of Umbar.Defeat foes throughout the Cape of Umbar.Complete Beast-slayer of the Cape of Umbar (Advanced)Complete Crab-slayer of the Cape of Umbar (Advanced)Complete Dead-slayer of the Cape of Umbar (Advanced)Complete Lion-slayer of the Cape of Umbar (Advanced)Complete Corsair and Pirate Slayer of the Cape of Umbar (Advanced)Complete Worm and Salamander Slayer of the Cape of Umbar (Advanced)Stúkha handed you a banner and instructions to taunt the Haradrim at their encampment in order to draw out and defeat their strongest fighter.

The Haradrim camp of Grijâti can be found south of Jax Phanâl and west of the road.Make your way to Grijâti, the Haradrim camp south-east of Jax Phanâl. Once there, find the ritual circle and plant the banner to draw out and challenge the strongest of the Haradrim warriors.You defeated the Haradrim leader, and he said he would honour the pacts of the past. You should return to Stúkha at Jax Phanâl.'Haradrim raiders still linger in our lands to the south, encamped at a place they name Grijâti. The strongest among them will enter into single combat with anyone who plants my banner. It is a sign of respect, but also a ruse, as I will not be the one fighting!'

The emissary winks and laughs heartily.

'You will fight in my stead! Defeat the raider and he is bound to honour the treaties of our past by making his way to me here at Jax Phanâl.''Plant the banner at the circle in Grijâti and the Haradrim raid-leader will think I have invoked a ritual battle. The terms are to allow them to leave our lands or grant them access back to our outpost. Defeat him, and he will come here, ashamed. Simple.''This trickery will not go unpunished! I will have my revenge, and our people will have what is rightfully ours. Our service to the Heirs and to the Church of the All-Seeing cannot be forgotten! The Empire of Ordâkh remains vital and alive... as you will soon not be!''Consider me impressed. The Haradrim will serve as good entertainment in Dahâl Huliz, the grand arena of the gladiators in Umbar Baharbêl! You have done well.'Elbatra asked you to bring back some large, ornate sea-shells from the coast.Elbatra asked that you go to the shoreline and gather up ornate sea-shells. She cautioned that you should be wary of the creatures that roam the shore; specifically, the crabs. Gather the shells and return them to Elbatra at Rhakatâb.'You seem like you can handle yourself. I have a special request. I collect exotic sea-shells, the larger and more ornate the better. Unfortunately, the best specimens seem to be located along beaches infested with crabs.

'I would love to add to my collection. The sea-shells on that beach shine like no other. Would you bring me back some exquisite ones? I would pay you quite well for the trouble.''Beautiful, are they not? So many in the city desire things of beauty, but have no drive to do the menial tasks like collecting the items necessary to make their baubles. What fortune then there is in finding one such as yourself. Willing to do anything for a bit of coin and recognition.

'Your payment.'You discovered a note written in a strange cipher on the body of Sûbodal. Deliver it to  Girgish, Khôltekh's emissary.You discovered a note on the body of the Haradrim sorcerer. You cannot make any sense of the symbols used on the note but can reason that it is writing of some type. This is likely something that Girgish should see. Return it to her at Jax Phanâl.The note appears to be written in a complex cipher. This is something that you have never seen before in your travels. Perhaps the emissary will know more of what this means. You should deliver the note to them.She takes the note.

'What is this?'

Glancing over the parchment, she clicks her tongue.

'Curious. This is not a cipher with which I am familiar. It is good that you brought this to me. I will investigate this matter. Thank you for your effort.'Girgish informs you that a Haradrim leader has been identified at Grijâti, the camp to the south-west. She directed you to eliminate the sorcerer, Sûbodal, and also to speak with Rothog's emissary to ensure that you eliminate all of the Haradrim leadership.You are to travel south and west into the Haradrim camp of Grijâti once again. This time, however, you are seeking the sorcerer Sûbodal, one of the Haradrim leaders. You are to eliminate him and return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl when the effort is complete.Defeat Sûbodal, the Haradrim sorcerer at GrijâtiThe sorcerer is slain. You should return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl and tell her of your success.Return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl'As grim as you may find this, we must remove the leader of these Haradrim before they can reorganize. The longer we keep them in disarray, the better.

'My counterpart Stúkha, an emissary of Rothog the Storm, works to defeat the strongest of the Haradrim; if you have not spoken with him – you should before you head out there.

'Are you willing to assist me again?''You will find the Haradrim sorcerer I speak of within the confines of the encampment to the south-west of Jax Phanâl. He will be smart enough not to just wander the camp without a guard of some sort. The last reports mentioned that he sleeps in a different tent each night in order to avoid detection.''You have done what was needed. I commend you, ${PLAYER} and thank you for your assistance. The death of the sorcerer was necessary to protect the lives of the folk who live in this outpost.

'Here is a reward for your efforts on our behalf.'Girgish represents Khôltekh, a leader of the Kindred of the Coins. She has requested that you make yourself known to some of the citizens in Jax Phanâl.Girgish directed you to make your way around the outpost of Jax Phanâl to familiarize yourself with the citizens dwelling here. She then bids you return to her after meeting all the important folk in the outpost.Speak with Gadnith in the easternmost outer courtyardSpeak with the innkeeper at the central outer courtyardSpeak with the dock-master on the shore west of the outpostSpeak with the auctioneerSpeak with Ledger-keeper Zarai at the courtyard in Jax PhanâlHaving spoken with important members of the town, you should return to Khôltekh's emissary and let her know that you now have introduced yourself to those she recommended you meet.Return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl'A new face. I hope that it will remain a friendly one.'

She offers a wry smile.

'Time will tell, of course. I assume that you met the magistrate; this is good. He will steer you in the right direction until you get your bearings. Until recently, our shores were less... hospitable to outsiders.

'I am Girgish, an emissary here at the behest of Khôltekh, a leader of the Kindred of the Coins who now rules in Umbar. I would have you introduce yourself to others in this outpost, If you are willing.

'I think you should meet our barber, innkeeper, stable-master, auctioneer, and ledger-keeper.

'Return to me once you have made their acquaintances.''You are not familiar to me. Perhaps that is a good thing. Ending up on the wrong side of the guards leads to poor marks by the ledger-keepers.

'By the look of you, you have been at sea. You should get some rest. Tend to your injuries and find a nice meal to eat.

'I am here to serve and watch. Please, leave me to my duty.''The emissary did well to send you to me, friend. Do you have need of a bed? Wine? Ale? Or perhaps a meal cooked in the style of the lands from which you hail? You need but ask and if it is within my power or the purview of this inn, I shall make it so. We are pleased that our land is more hospitable to those from abroad now that the Kindred watch over our people. We hope that this will bring about even greater commerce to our land, in time.''I am pleased to make your acquaintance and hope that you are finding our outpost as welcoming as we wish to make it, friend. This is a land reborn and her people celebrate the casting off of the yoke that restrained them.

'Tyranny is ended. We wake to a dream from a nightmare that lasted too long. The Kindred breathe life and liberty into the lands, and we are free to roam once again. Our roads are safer and travel and trade quicken their pace. Natural dangers remain, however: passage around the Cape is not always easy, and you may still prefer to visit the stables should you wish to journey to the fort at Rakhatâb, to the south! But you have my welcome all the same, should you have need of my service.''Come closer, friend, and look upon the wares that I oversee. All manner of goods, weapons, armour, and other such delights await you.

'A brisk trade returns to Jax Phanâl now that the tyranny of the past is ended. I will do my part to see that these items are safe-guarded. Once they are purchased, I return the profits to those who entrusted their goods to my care... for a modest fee, of course. I treat the goods under my care as I would my own children.

'That is, if I had any children!'

The barker laughs and returns to calling out auction details.'It is good you have come to me. First, I will require a name for the ledger so that the people will come to know you for all that you do in these lands.'

She awaits your response and then scribbles some notes in a writing style you do not recognize. She then continues.

'Very well, that is all I require of you for now. If you wish to know more, I can spare a few moments to explain the purpose of the ledger-keepers.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}.  

'I am pleased that you were able to make introductions around town. Now there are some matters that could use both your attention and your discretion.'Tagar once again enlists you to collect trophies from the goblins south-east of Jax Phanâl.Tagar asked that you return to the goblins' encampment south and east of Jax Phanâl in a further attempt to remove the goblin threat from the area. You are to collect twelve of the goblins' bandanas, and return them to Tagar at his dwelling.'We cannot seem to rid ourselves of these vile goblins. I would like you to go to their encampment to the south-east of Jax Phanâl, collect their bandanas and return them to me as proof of their defeat.''Excellent work, friend. It may take time, but I am certain that we will root out these goblins and make our lands safe, now that the Kindred are in charge.'Khôltekh's emissary suggests that you have done enough for the citizens of Jax Phanâl and directs you to the stable-master to journey to Rakhatâb to the south.Khôltekh's emissary directed you to the stable-master in Jax Phanâl to purchase a ride south along the road to Rakhatâb.Speak with the stable-master and ride to RakhatâbYou should take a stabled horse to the southern fortress of Rakhatâb. There you are to meet with the foreman, Nûrut. He has been told of your arrival and all the deeds you have done to assist the citizens of Jax Phanâl.Speak with Nûrut'Friend, thank you for what you have done here. I will tell you that even further along the cape you will find others in need of assistance and the skills you possess. If you desire it, I will pay for your passage to Rakhatâb, a citadel to the south where you can continue to assist the people of Umbar. No? I knew I liked you, ${PLAYER}. But even so, it is to the stable-master you will want to go if you are to make the journey to Rakhatâb.

'Know that the citizenry here will remember you. More importantly, it is I who will remember you and speak well of you to my lord. In a place such as Umbar, it is good to have friends in places both high and low. You are well on your way to acquiring both.

'Good travels to you.''I offer you my sincerest thanks. Your efforts to assist our outpost will be on the lips of the citizens here for years to come.

'An outsider, from lands afar, taking up arms against our former allies who are now foes! It is the mark of a hero to take on the woes of others, to assist those without the means to meet their struggles head on.

'You are such a hero as this. The people of Jax Phanâl know it, and in time perhaps all of Umbar shall know it too. Go now, and in peace. Good travels to you.''Thank you, friend. What you have done for the people here in Jax Phanâl will not be forgotten. We are learning to be free and what it means to breathe the air fresh and new.

'I know it seems that some of us are in a state of euphoria; perhaps we are. The shadow that long cast itself over these lands is no more; all around us there is light.'

She smiles.

'...and it seems that even outsiders can become our allies. Good travels to you. When you arrive in Rakhatâb speak with the overseer there. He has already been told that you are coming to their aid.''Greetings, ${PLAYER}.

'Your arrival was foretold. You have already earned a reputation as a folk hero among some of the workers here. What you did for the citizens of Jax Phanâl reverberates in the halls of stone to be found here.

'Welcome to Rakhatâb. We can only hope that your good nature and generosity will continue in our small, but bustling fort.'Nûrat asks that you search among the Haradrim for Gunjik, the warrior who stole a necklace from her. Haradrim can be found lurking in the wilds or encamped to the south.Nûrat asked you to make your way south along the road outside of Jax Phanâl and then turn west toward Grijâti, the camp of Haradrim there. Among the Haradrim is a warrior named Gunjik, who stole something precious from her. She wants it back.'Magistrate Zebulo sent you? He is either shrewd or foolish to send an outsider to help me.'

She shakes her head.

'I mean you no offence. It is just not a simple matter.

'When the Kindred of the Coins took control and freed us from the yoke of tyranny, many of the Haradrim fled lest they suffer the wrath of our new rulers. Some warriors of Ordâkh begrudgingly left on their ships; others made mischief in the outpost; more still set up a camp on the outskirts of the city.

'For a time I called one of them my love... but no longer! And in leaving, the knave stole something precious from me!

'I am ill-equipped to hunt him down. I have also heard that they are being bold enough to capture folk who venture too near Grijâti, their encampment to the south. That is where Gunjík will be hiding.

'Can you help?''Thank you kindly. It may not seem much, but it is all I have left of my mother. Had he made off with this for good I would have been filled with woe.'You arrived in Rakhatâb and met the foreman. The fort teems with activity and bustling workers, and there is much to be done. The foreman confides that not all is well and they are looking for some assistance with the many problems in their day-to-day lives.Assist Tankho with his needsAssist Beliash with his needsAssist Kharishah with his needsAssist Hûzo with his needsAssist Taphis with her needsAssist Ulanor with her needsYou addressed the concerns of the foremen in the fort and should return to Nûrut where you found him in Rakhatâb.Talk to Nûrut in Rakhatâb'Yours is a fresh face, and a welcome one. I will share with you some information about our fort and then, if you are willing, perhaps you will help with some of the issues faced by our workers?

'We are free, this is true. No whips lash our backs now, but our workers remain weary and hungry. Injuries, or worse, are frequent. These are only setbacks, of course, for ours is a land born anew.

'I coordinate the fort's efforts for the overseer. The other foremen here each have quotas that must be met... and they are falling behind. Meet first with them. Their names are Tankho, Beliash, Kharishah, Hûzo, and Taphis. After you have spoken with them, you should meet with the overseer about our schedule.''You are swift and true. I thank you for the assistance and hope you were not overly troubled by the requests made of you. Ours is a land in recovery, but soon our operations will return to their greatest efficiency!

'For now you have earned us a welcome respite from overwork.'The magistrate of Jax Phanâl is a pleasant man dealing with a good number of requests from the citizens in his outpost. Your arrival seems a good omen to him, and he asks that you assist him to address some of the lesser tasks to which he must attend.Whether he is sincere or not is debatable, but the magistrate of Jax Phanâl asked that you assist him in seeing to the needs of the populace of the outpost. There are five individuals needing assistance throughout Jax Phanâl.Assist Nûrat at the eastern-most courtyard of outer Jax PhanâlAssist Tagar at the central outer courtyard of Jax PhanâlAssist Keteph at the main courtyard of Jax PhanâlAssist Girgish at the crest of Jax PhanâlAssist Stúkha at the crest of Jax PhanâlYou completed the tasks set before you by the citizens of Jax Phanâl. Return to Magistrate Zebulo at the crest atop the stairs in eastern Jax Phanâl to inform him of your success.Speak with Magistrate Zebulo at the crest of Jax Phanâl'I will call you friend until I have a reason to do otherwise.'

He offers a broad smile. 

'I wonder, friend, would you be willing to help our outpost? Our newfound freedom comes with its fair share of... difficulties. My daily tasks keep me busy, and I find myself with neither the time nor assistants to address the concerns of my citizens.

'Would you be willing to assist me?''I promise you, friend. It is not a lack of desire to help all of the citizens here, it is simply the demands on my time are too great! If you are willing to assist me, I will see you rewarded well.''I will admit, my friend, that I did not know if you would be a willing agent for me. You have proven my apprehension unfounded. I am grateful. Would that every visitor to our outpost was so willing to aid us.'Find the many treasures hidden or forgotten through the Cape of Umbar.Find the many treasure caches lost or forgotten throughout the Cape of Umbar.Find treasure caches in the Cape of UmbarHûzo asked you to check the stone supports around the town for signs of wear and to repair any cracks.Hûzo asked that you look at the support beams around the fort for signs of wear or cracking. If you find any, Hûzo asked you to repair the damaged supports.Repair damaged supports (${NUMBER}/6)Nearly all of the supports you examined were damaged or in a state of disrepair. You should return to Hûzo and inform him of this discovery.'The foreman sent word that you helped in Jax Phanâl. I appreciate that, friend. There's another thing you could help us with, if you will.

'One of the stone supports collapsed last night. Two of my best workers died in the accident. These structures are old and weak, but we cannot stop our work to fix them; the overseer has threatened to cut our rations even further if our progress slows.

'Would you check the other supports by walls and archways for signs of wear, and reinforce any cracked supports you find? You'd have the gratitude of both myself and my workers.''That many? We must be working too quickly to repair them as we should. We will need to pay closer attention, if we can, or we will suffer for it! And if we suffer, the work suffers! But I cannot speak these words to the overseer.

'Thank you. This means more to me and the workers than you can know. I do not intend to bury any more of my men.'Ayaluk asked you to distract the guards who watch over the overseer's office in the fortress. He is certain that there is something untoward happening here.Ayaluk  asked you to meet him near the entry of the overseer's office.Speak with Ayaluk and complete 'Instance: Whispers of the Forge'After assisting Ayaluk he returned to his family home with haste. He directed you to speak with him there.'Friend, I have had a change of heart. The overseer here in Rakhatâb brings too much harm. My brother should not have been killed. I have watched the comings and goings of individuals with whom the overseer meets, and I believe that there is some rot here that must be cut out. I intend to slip into her chambers, get whatever information I can, and report it to certain folk who can do something about it.

'I only require a distraction long enough to cover my efforts. Will you help me?''We will wait for Ulanor to be on the long part of her walk. You distract the guard and I will slip in and out of her chambers to get the proof we need.''These notes are clear. The overseer is hiding something and we need the help of others if we are to expose it!'Defeat many worms and salamanders in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many worms and salamanders in the Cape of UmbarDefeat many worms and salamanders in the Cape of Umbar.Defeat many worms and salamanders in the Cape of UmbarDefeat many "rats" in Umbar Baharbêl. Not every villain and ruffian of the city names themselves sworn to the Heirs.Defeat many "rats" in Umbar Baharbêl. Not every villain and ruffian of the city names themselves sworn to the Heirs.Defeat many "rats" in Umbar BaharbêlDefeat many "rats" in Umbar Baharbêl. Not every villain and ruffian of the city names themselves sworn to the Heirs.Defeat many "rats" in Umbar Baharbêl. Not every villain and ruffian of the city names themselves sworn to the Heirs.Defeat many "rats" in Umbar BaharbêlIn the aftermath of the Sea-stone Mutiny, Umbar Baharbêl was made a Free City, but there are whispers that Men loyal to the Heirs of Castamir still trouble the Sail-haven.Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, seeks for new guards to help safe-guard the Sail-haven in the aftermath of the Sea-stone Mutiny.Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower'You there!'

The harbour-guard glances downward and appears to begin reading off a small piece of parchment.

'By order of the Kindred of the Coins: the Captain of the Haven, Eshmun, requires assistance in rebuilding the Sail-haven and safe-guarding it from the enemies of Umbar. Heirsworn loyalists still plague the Free City, and they must be routed that the stain of the Scourge be finally cleansed from our lands. Fair compensation will be provided. If you wish to aid Umbar Baharbêl, report to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower at once!''Hail! I am Eshmun, harbour-warden and Captain of the Haven, and I was appointed to this station by the authority of Tumúldo Fierce-water—greatest, to my mind, of the Kindred of the Coins.

'Is there some matter that demands my attention, or have you merely come to admire the craftsmanship of the Umbari?'

You tell Eshmun that you have come to help rout those loyal to the Heirs of Castamir from Umbar Baharbêl.

'Is that so, stranger? I must admit, I am more accustomed to visitors perusing our markets than leaping at the opportunity to involve themselves in the affairs of the Kindred of the Coins, but I have been left little choice, it seems.'In the bustle of commerce on the streets, markets, and piers of Umbar Baharbêl, it is not uncommon for goods to accidentally end up in a canal or at the bottom of the harbour of the Sail-haven.Waterlogged crates can be found in the canals and in the harbour surrounding the Rovers' Yard in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

Galyat has asked you to retrieve waterlogged crates that have sunken into the canals and harbour of the Sail-haven.Retrieve waterlogged crates from the waters of Sail-haven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Galyat can be found near the Rovers' Yard to the east of the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have retrieved a number of waterlogged crates from the canals and harbour of the Sail-haven in Umbar Baharbêl. You should deliver them to Galyat.'It is just terrible! There are too many clumsy hands around at the Rovers' Yard, I think.

'In the past few weeks, I've seen more than a few crates end up in the waters of the harbour and these canals, and not even the Captain of the Haven seems interested in retrieving them. It is a disgrace, I tell you!

'If you can dredge up some of those sunken crates for me, I've some coin for you.''A-ha! Let's see what we have here!'

Galyat pries open one of the crates, and smiles.

'Everything seems to be intact, so as promised, here is your reward. It is the least I can do to repay you for your help, my friend.

'After all, ${PLAYER}, I never did say these were mine!'Heshra, the herbalist needs your help collecting diseased salamanders outside of Khûtra in order to find out more about this strange disease.Elder Roshat has told you to speak with Heshra, the herbalist in the Khûtra Elder Hall, about the disease overtaking Khûtra.Speak with Heshra, the herbalist, in the Khûtra Elder HallHeshra needs your help tracking down diseased salamanders west of Khûtra along the shore in order to find out more about this strange disease.'I still don't trust you, but you've done more for us than any outsider ever has.

'This disease... we have lost three of our own to it this week, and without the fishing....

'Our village herbalist thinks something can be done about it. Perhaps even a salve created to reduce its effects. But first he needs more samples of the dreadful stuff, and from animals, not fish for some reason. He's in the Elder Hall at the end of this road. Talk to him, he knows better than I of what he needs.

'Oh, and stranger – I've still got my eye on you.''Oh yes, more samples would be wonderful. I really need more animals that are afflicted, as I have plenty of fish. The fisher-folk just throw them outside my door. Dreadful smell. I've asked them not to anymore, but I suspect they do it for sport at this point.

'Would you go west of here along the shore and bring me back samples of the diseased animals you find? I know the salamanders have been affected. It's the stomachs I need in particular.''Yes, this is exactly what I need.'

He examines the samples you brought him.

'Just as I suspected! I don't think this will help the fish any, but I have plants here that can hopefully heal living versions of these animals. Give me a few minutes. Yes, honeywort in each....'Khûtra Elder Roshat has asked for your help culling the rising population of the dead near the Mâkhda Khorbo.Khûtra Elder Roshat has asked for your help culling the rising population of the dead near the Mâkhda Khorbo. The ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo can be found in the hills to the east of Khûtra.Defeat wights near the Mâkhda Khorbo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat spirits near the Mâkhda Khorbo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat decayed near the Mâkhda Khorbo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Elder Roshat in Khûtra.Return to Elder Roshat in Khûtra'It is fortunate that you are going out near the Mâkhda Khorbo. The dead have been getting more plentiful by the day. They are harrowing our merchants and folk passing to Umbar. If you could cull some of their number, you would have my thanks.''You have my thanks again. There was a rising tide of dead washing close to Khûtra. Because of you, my people can walk the pathways around Khûtra without fear.'The plan to draw out Khâshap has begun. With rumours beginning to spread, Hadorion aims to create chaos amongst Khâshap's rivals.Hadorion seeks to sow chaos amongst Khâshap's rivals by framing him for acts of aggression.Defeat Corsairs in the Gut (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Fake sashes planted (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You should tell Hadorion that you have created some chaos in the Gut and the fake sashes have been planted.

Hadorion can be found in the Lower Ward.'Now that the rumours are spreading, it is time to sow the seed of discord. 

'As I learned in Anfalas, Khâshap is prone to making mistakes when under duress. After some digging around and bribing the right people, I was able to learn that Khâshap does in fact have some rivals in the city. A rival Corsair group that, while not enthusiastic about snitching on a fellow, would have no choice but to respond to acts of aggression.

'This group routines the Gut, a part of the Lower Ward that is ill hospitable to outsiders. I've fashioned these sashes in the likeness of Khâshap's unique design. Let's just say, leaving it behind after roughing up a few of their number would work wonders towards turning their ilk against him.''This is the perfect storm. With the rumours spreading, and the chaos in the Gut - it is only a matter of time before Khâshap makes his move to clear his name.... and when he does, we will be there.

'Now, we wait.'Animals who have been kept in captivity require urgent aid.Gûshida has given you a formula which can help the animals.

Find the ingredients across the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Take a petal from a vibrant flowerPluck a clump of fragrant herbsPick a verdant leafYou have gathered most of the ingredients you need. Now you need fresh water and honey from a vendor that Gûshida recommended.

Gûshida's vendor is in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Gûshida's vendorYou have gathered all you need to create the remedy.

Use the remedy-making supplies from your inventory to create the remedy.Use the remedy-making kitYou have created enough remedy and should give it to the animals in Ezôti's hiding place.

Ezôti's hiding place is inside the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Give the cave-claw in Ezôti's Flat a dose of remedyGive the goat in Ezôti's Flat a dose of remedyGive the boar in Ezôti's Flat a dose of remedyGive the bear in Ezôti's Flat a dose of remedyYou have given doses of remedy to each animal, and they all seem better for it. You should report to Gûshida.

Gûshida can be found where you first met her in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Gûshida where you first met her in the Upper Ward'I know of a tincture that can wipe away even the heaviest lethargy. Take some herbs and edible flowers from the courtyards and gardens of the Upper Ward. Do not worry about getting permission. If you take only cuttings it will not be a problem. In Umbar, some things we share freely with each other.

'Once you have the herbs and flowers, grind them up with honey, mix that with water, and give them to the animals. A merchant I know on the south-eastern side of the Grand Market will help you do this. Meanwhile, I will report to my Lady.''Gûshida stopped by. She said you might need some honey and some water.

'Oh put your coin away. We all owe her a debt that would take a lifetime to repay.

'Here, you can use this remedy kit to mix the tincture you need.'Gûshida relaxes as you give her the good news.

'You have done well, ${PLAYER}.'Hadorion has been pursuing a Corsair by the name of Khâshap since he showed in Anfalas. His pursuit has led him to the city of Umbar.Hadorion plans to spread wild rumours about Khâshap in order to draw him out. The first step is to place these posters around the city to publicly paint a target on his back.Place posters in Lower Ward (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There hang posters all around the Lower Ward of the city. This should create a stir amongst the residents. You should tell Hadorion.

Hadorion can be found in the Lower Ward.Talk to Hadorion in the Lower Ward'We've made it to Umbar, ${PLAYER}.

'I tracked Khâshap all the way from the Langstrand through the Shield Isles. I believe he's made landfall here in Umbar, but we are among his cohorts so we must tread carefully. I have a plan to draw him out of hiding.

'What's more important to a Corsair and a cutthroat? Reputation. If we call into question that very reputation, they are bound to come forth in defence of it. We shall spread rumours of ill-gotten gains. Paint him as a betrayer to his people. We don't need anyone but Khâshap himself to believe in these rumours... and something tells me he will.''Tongues should start flapping. Whether or not it is believable should not matter.

'There exists within Umbar a healthy smattering of different allegiances. Now we wait for it to spread like a contagion.'Investigate the strange disease afflicting Khûtra's beasts and inhabitants.Speak with Elder Roshat about the strange disease afflicting Khûtra.Meet with Elder Roshat in Khûtra'A disease in Khûtra? Where do you hail from, stranger?''Where are you from, stranger? Not from Gondor, I presume. We have no need for their kind here.

'Help? We don't need help here, and certainly not from outsiders.

'If you want to help, go talk to my fisherfolk and get my people some fish that don't reek of death. Bah. Off with you.'Investigate the strange disease afflicting Khûtra's beasts and inhabitants.Meet with Elder Madag about the strange disease afflicting Khûtra.Meet with Elder Madag in Khûtra'We've heard troubling reports of an unnatural disease afflicting the people and beasts of Khûtra. Please, go to the village, investigate the disease and offer any aid you can.''You should speak to Roshat about the disease. He knows the most about it.'After purchasing the deed to the land upon which it sits from the Kindred of the Coins, Phenâsh hopes to demolish the ruins of the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Sail-haven.Rubble can be found at the ruined Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

Phenâsh has asked you to help clear the rubble at the ruined Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All.Destroy rubble at the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Phenâsh can be found at the ruined Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You attempted to destroy the rubble at the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All, but you were attacked by several frothing shrine-spirits. You should talk to Phenâsh.Talk to Phenâsh at the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All'You there! Interested in earning a tâm or three?

'You see this ruin here? I bought the land it stands on from the Kindred of the Coins, and I'd like to begin new construction as soon as I can. Alas, I have been trying to demolish this old shrine for nearly a week now, but my labourers keep walking out on their work. It's haunted, they say, as if such a thing could be true! How absurd!

'I've been here for nearly an hour now, and I've seen nothing of the sort. If you'd clear some of this rubble and help prove me right, I'll see to it that you receive a fitting reward.''No, do not speak. You do not need to tell me I was mistaken, ${PLAYER}. I saw those terrible things with my own eyes!'

Phenâsh covers his face with his hands, and sighs.

'I should have known, ${PLAYER}. Why else would they have sold this land for such a meagre price?'After helping to unload a ship, Tâbrim has reported that a strange creature escaped its crate and fled into the Sail-haven.The broken crate can be found near Tâbrim on the piers of the Sail-haven.

Tâbrim has asked you to examine the broken crate. You should inspect the broken crate.Examine the broken crateThe escaped creature can be found somewhere in the Sail-haven.

Tâbrim informed you that the creature tore up some stonework as it fled into the Sail-haven. You should follow the damaged stonework and see where it leads.Follow the trail of damaged stonework and find the escaped creatureThe cave-claw can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven.

You have found a fearful cave-claw, and it is clearly overwhelmed by its new home. You should carefully approach the cave-claw.Carefully approach the cave-clawSacks of potatoes can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven.

You have found the cave-claw, but it appears very uneasy. You should find something you can offer it to help calm it down.Collect a potato from one of the nearby sacksThe cave-claw can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven.

You have collected a fine potato, and you should offer it to the frightened cave-claw.Henok can be found in a small alley in the Sail-haven.

One of the Temámir, Henok, has arrived to collect his companion. You should talk to Henok.Talk to Henok'Did you see it? There is a beast loose in the Sail-haven!

'It burst out of that crate over there, and then it ran off into the Sail-haven. It was so swift that it even tore up some of the stonework as it went! I'm told that this shipment was for the dwarf, Henok, and if I've nothing to offer him, it won't be long before word reaches Khôltekh and the rest of the Kindred of the Coins.

'What am I going to do?! If Eshmun finds out, he'll have my head! Won't you help me?''Ah! You have found my new companion!

'I spoke to Tâbrim, and much the same as you I suppose, my path led me to this alley. It is all right, friend. I can handle this matter from here, and I think this cave-claw will find quite the pleasant home in the Shoreward Stone. I do thank you for helping to calm him down, though. It is quite the experience to walk the streets of Umbar Baharbêl, and if we are being honest, it can be a bit much for anyone!

'I must confess, though, I do not know your name. What is it?'

You tell Henok your name, and he smiles.

'Ah, well, that might be a strange name for a cave-claw, but we'll give it a try. You have my thanks!'As you approach the cave-claw, you can tell that it is deeply distressed and overwhelmed by its new surroundings in Umbar Baharbêl.

Deciding that it might be unwise to try to capture the creature yourself, you look about the alley and notice a few sacks of potatoes. You hope that offering it something in kindness might soothe the cave-claw's fears.Furious about the mutineers who stole her ship, Kenza wants you to help her retrieve her valuables from it.The ship docked to the east holds Kenza's valuables, but it also holds deadly mutineers.Collect shipboard treasures from Kenza's ship in the Fleet-fast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kenza is by the steps leading to the upper level in the Fleet-fast.'My ship has been overrun by mutineers, stranger. They will be dealt with, I assure, but time is short. You see, there is treasure still aboard the ship, and as it is MY ship the treasure is also mine by right.

'Will you fight your way onto my ship and retrieve my three chests of valuables? You will be rewarded, of course. My ship is docked to the east of here, and some of the ruffians and bruisers that now lurk here in the Fleet-fast were once members of my crew. Feel free to slay as many of them as it takes to retrieve my treasures.''Will you fight your way onto my ship and retrieve my three chests of valuables? You will be rewarded, of course. My ship is docked to the east of here, and some of the ruffians and bruisers that now lurk here in the Fleet-fast were once members of my crew. Feel free to slay as many of them as it takes to retrieve my treasures.''Is there anything more lovely than being returned treasure that belongs to you? I do not think so, my friend. I would have brought the chests with me when need drove me to escape from those worthless villains... but I will be truthful with you: mutinies may take awhile to form, but when they do happen they happen quickly.

'I am pleased to be reunited with these valuables. I will give you some valuable wisdom as reward: if you choose to captain a ship, do not hire a crew that believes themselves to be more deadly than you are!

'I think my former crew has now learned they were mistaken. Thank you for your assistance with them.'Elder Ilaya has asked you to go to Umbar Baharbêl, the City of Corsairs, to investigate rumours of the mistreatment of animals by a man named Ezôti. You should meet with Gûshida in the Upper Ward.Meet with Gûshida in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl about rumours relating to the mistreatment of animals.Meet with Gûshida in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl'We've heard troubling rumours from Umbar Baharbêl about animal mistreatment. I appreciate what you did here for Khûtra's animals, so I know you understand how important our duty is, to protect and respect them. Their lives are as sacred as our own.

'These rumours tell of a street charlatan. They call him Ezôti. His words are sweet but his deeds are dark. He parades animals around for show. He whips them until they do his tricks.' Ilaya spits on the ground, to show her displeasure.

'He does not understand the pact between humans and animals. He does not see them as we do. To him, they are just a means to buy coin and praise. Cheap entertainment, to be used and discarded.

'Go to Umbar Baharbêl, find Gûshida. She can be found in the Upper Ward of the city. She is like you and I. She understands animals. She is looking to expose Ezôti and end his crimes. You've done much to help us and the animals here. Please, find Gûshida, and help the animals there. They don't have much time.''Ilaya sent you? Then I know you have a pure heart and devotion to animals. It is good that you've found me. We have much to talk about.'There is a large wounded salamander that needs to be healed with the salve given to you by Heshra, the herbalist. The salamander can be found west of Khûtra.Elder Ilaya has asked you to heal a large wounded salamander with the salve given to you by Heshra. The beast can be found west of Khûtra.Administer the salve to Nekarkul on the shore to the westElder Ilaya has asked you to heal a large wounded salamander with the salve given to you by Heshra. The beast can be found west of Khûtra.Return to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra.Return to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra'There is a great wounded salamander to the north of here that has been stricken with this dangerous affliction. Healing it will help not only the beast itself, but also ensure its many young are protected from this scourge.

'Will you go and heal this beast?''Let that be a lesson to you. Nature gives no quarter, and expects none in return. A wounded beast is still savage, and nature only recognizes strength and ferocity. Fortunate, then, that its ferocity was more than matched by yours.'A strange man puts on a 'show' in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Ezôti has asked you to find and paint a rock that looks reasonably like a roc egg.

Search for a suitable rock outside the Gate of Songs in the north-eastern wall of Umbar Baharbêl.You have inspected some rocks that did not fit the requirement.

Inspect one last rock outside the gates of Umbar Baharbêl.Inspect rocks outside the city beyond the Gate of Songs (2/3)You have found the perfect sized rock. Now to paint it so it looks like a roc's egg.

Paint the rock outside the gates of Umbar Baharbêl.Paint the rockYou have painted a rock to look like a roc's egg. It's time to deliver it back to Ezôti.

Deliver the fake roc's egg to Ezôti in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Pick up the 'egg' outside the north gate of Umbar BaharbêlYou have delivered the 'egg' to Ezôti.

Report back to Ezôti in the Upper Ward.Talk to Ezôti'What is it that makes finding good associates so difficult? Take for example one of my previous fellows, a man named Itho. I paid him quite a large sum to fetch me an egg, a single egg! One egg! And I have not had word from him in days. How hard can it be to retrieve a roc's egg?

'I begin to think he ran off with my money, but would he dare? How could he dare such a thing? Now, a lesser man would fall into despair over this betrayal, if that is indeed what it is... but Ezôti is no lesser man, is he? The show must go on, as they say. To that end, I need you to find an egg-shaped rock, paint it to look like a roc's egg, and bring it back here. And no one needs to know! Look for one outside the city, beyond the Gate of Songs in the north, where no one will see what you are up to.''This is perfect! This looks exactly like a roc egg!

'At least, I assume it does. I have never seen one myself. But I believe that it must look exactly like this... how could it not?'The travelling merchant Labóni has lost a precious family heirloom to the ruffians of Umbar.Labóni has asked you to investigate The Eastern Stores and retrieve his family heirloom.

The Eastern Stores can be found on the east side of the Lower Ward in the Cistern.Find the hidden store-roomYou have found the Eastern Stores. The family heirloom must be hidden within.Find Khatrâxi, the RaindropYou found The Eastern Stores and have obtained Khatrâxi, the Raindrop. You should return to Labóni.'Please, if you have a moment!

'I came here seeking a new venture, and while business has been somewhat doing well, I have lost something very precious!

'It is something that is quite priceless: a family heirloom. Certainly it is not part of any merchandise I would be selling.

'I have asked around and apparently the Corsairs keep their valuables in a place called the Eastern Stores, but this does not seem to be a place open for the public. It is not very heavily advertised....

'I have managed to secure a lead, however. The entrance to this store-house should be on the eastern side of the Lower Ward, in the Cistern.''Ah there it is!

'The raindrop is a priceless heirloom that our family has kept for generations. We come from a long line of merchants, and this raindrop was the first piece of jewellery ever purchased with our family's fortune.

'I thank you from the bottom of my heart for returning such a precious artifact to me!'Ikha asked you to recover shiny baubles stolen from residents of the Lower Ward by ruffians in the Gut.Stolen baubles can be recovered from enemies in the Gut, located in the Lower Ward.Recover stolen baubles from enemies in the Gut (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ikha is in the Lower Ward.'Do you believe folk should be safe from villains, stranger? It is true that the people who dwell in the Lower Ward of Umbar Baharbêl do not have as much wealth as the noble ones who dwell across the city in the Upper Ward... but what they do have is no less precious to them. For it to be stolen...

'It is a grievous crime to do such a thing, but that is just what the villains who lurk in and around the Gut have done! If you will find these ruffians and retrieve from them the shiny baubles they have stolen, my family and my friends will not forget it.''Find the ruffians who lurk in the Gut and retrieve from them the shiny baubles they have stolen. My family and my friends will not forget it.''I know these baubles are not of any real value; most of them are mere painted glass. But they belong to my friends and my neighbours and my family, and in the Lower Ward even such things can bring happiness. I hope to do just that when I return these things to their owners.

'Thank you for retrieving them, my friend. They are only baubles... but they ought not be stolen.'Gûshida and Nekhama stand where you expected to find Ezôti.Ezôti is nowhere to be found, but Gûshida and a familiar face from the Shield Isles are here.

Speak to Gûshida and Nekhama in the Upper Ward.Talk to Nekhama across the way from Gûshida'Ezôti has been dealt with by our mutual friend Nekhama. As you have done us a favour, I will share with you that both Nekhama and I are agents of Tatháta the Beast. Her work with the Kindred of the Coins means that weeks can go by without either of us speaking with her... but we know she would approve of the work you helped us do this day.

'Speak with Nekhama. She has something for you.''Good work,' she says. 'The animals have all been rescued, and they will no longer suffer in such a situation as Ezôti imposed upon them. For myself I have chosen to adopt "The Razor of Belfalas." Once I cleaned away all the mud and sea-weed that Ezôti had used to disguise him, it became clear that the Razor was a rather ordinary turtle. And yet he is not ordinary, not truly, for he is very friendly, and loves people! He seems rather taken with me, and I confess I am quite fond of the old fellow too.'

She holds out a flame-coloured coin for you to take.

'Should you ever need a favour, redeem this coin with myself or Gûshida.'

She smiles, and says nothing further. You suppose the meeting is done.Your mission nears its end. Thorongil and Corudan are sure to be held somewhere within Umbar Baharbêl, just down the coast road.The crew separates and prepares to enter the city by different paths.Wait for your crew to disperseYou will enter the city by the Beacon Gate, which provides entrance to the north-western area of the city.Enter Umbar Baharbêl by the Beacon Gate, which leads to the Sail-havenCaebar has entered Umbar Baharbêl by the Beacon Gate on the north-western side of the city.Talk to Caebar by the Beacon GateYour crew has split up to search Umbar Baharbêl for information that will aid in the rescue of Thorongil and the completion of your mission.Complete 'The City: The Eyes of Nauriel'Complete 'The City: Sirgon's Wound'Complete 'The City: Sigileth's Curiosity'Complete 'The City: Elves, Dwarves, and Trouble'Complete 'The City: The Short Straw'Caebar said he would meet you at one of the markets in the Sail-haven when you have learned what your crew discovered.Talk to Caebar at a market in the Sail-haven'I am no strategist, ${PLAYER}, but even I know we are likely to attract unwelcome attention if we approach the city as a group. What do you think?'

You advise your crew to split up and enter the City of the Corsairs by separate gates.

'That is a good idea! We will all meet up after we have learned what we can inside the city. Until then, farewell! And be careful!''So this is the City of the Corsairs. I am a long way from home.''So this is the City of the Corsairs. I am a long way from home, ${PLAYER}.'

Caebar frowns, and you know he is remembering the cold welcome he received from his family and the other folk of Ethring.

'I suppose my home is not what it used to be. I am here at the command of King Elessar, and to help my friends as I can. For those two purposes... I would travel anywhere.

'The rest of the crew will be somewhere within the city now, searching for information that will aid us in the rescuing of Thorongil and your Elf-friend. You will need to search the several districts of the city if you are to find them, I think: the Fleet-fast, the Upper and Lower Wards, and the Sail-haven, at least! I will see you at one of the markets in the Sail-haven when you have learned what there is to be learned!''The rest of the crew will be somewhere within the city now, searching for information that will aid us in the rescuing of Thorongil and your Elf-friend. You will need to search the several districts of the city if you are to find them, I think: the Fleet-fast, the Upper and Lower Wards, and the Sail-haven, at least! I will see you at one of the markets in the Sail-haven when you have learned what there is to be learned!''I hope the rest of the crew learned something valuable, ${PLAYER}, for I have had a hard time of it. I leaned out over one of the railings and studied the Citadel of Winds from afar, but that place seems to be a fortress, and impregnable. I cannot think of any way we will get inside, if that is where the Kindred of the Coins is holding the prisoners.

'I am sorry, I am feeling rather out of sorts. Someone bumped into me right before you arrived, and I almost fell. Folk should watch where they are going!'Mânobaz is feeling ostracized by his cohorts even after helping to plunder and raid.Mânobaz has asked you to steal a portion of spoils that is rightfully his from the The Eastern Stores.

The Eastern Stores can be found on the east side of the Lower Ward in the Cistern.Find the hidden store-roomYou have found the Eastern Stores. The plunder should be stored within.Collect Mânobaz's plunder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected a good amount of spoils. Perhaps this is enough for Mânobaz.

Mânobaz can be found next to the Black Anchor.'Can you believe this nonsense?

'I go and help these so called friends sack and plunder, and they go and take all the spoils for themselves! I was instrumental in securing that loot, and I deserve a portion of it!

'What do you say? Would you help me take back my fair share? I'm not saying to rob them clean, I am an honest and fair individual myself. I just have to look after my enterprises is all.

'Now, there's a secret store-room where all the ne'er-do-wells keep their prized possessions. It's in the Waterways Market just outside of the Gut. It is sure to be guarded. No need to be specific, just grab whatever you can and bring it back to me.''Well, would you look at that. You did it! You've gone and collected quite a haul.

'I have to admit, I did not think you'd do it, but you are a fair and honest individual now aren't you? And us fair and honest individuals must uphold the strictest code of fairness!

'You've got yourself a friend in Umbar!'A strange man puts on a 'show' in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Ezôti has asked you to place flyers advertising his show all around the Upper Ward.

But because Ezôti is terrible, do not do a good job. Place flyers in poorly visible spots around the Upper Ward.Hang up flyers... but place them poorly (${NUMBER}/16)You have placed a number of Ezôti's flyers. That is enough, and you should burn the rest in a fire.Does Ezôti need so many flyers posted?Instead of distributing more flyers for Ezôti, you have decided to burn them in a fire. The open flame on the south-eastern corner of the Grand Market in the Upper Ward should suffice.Throw the remaining flyers into a fire on the south-eastern corner of the Grand MarketYou have no more flyers left to place. Will Ezôti wonder how you accomplished the task so quickly? Probably not.Talk to Ezôti in the Upper Ward'As excellent as I am, I am but one man... and that one man can only be in one place... at one time!

'If only I could walk the whole of the city to spread word of my show, the docks themselves would buckle beneath the weight of my vast audience! But no... residents of the lower streets of the city do not have the coins I need to make the show worth my time! We will focus our efforts upon the Upper Ward only. Take these posters, and place them upon the walls of the Upper Ward. Only the denizens of such a prestigious quarter have the refined taste to appreciate my talents. And their coin purses often shine with gold instead of silver....'

You resolve to place the posters in areas with poor visibility and little foot traffic. Ezôti does not deserve to be rewarded with large crowds.'Wonderful work, assistant! With all sixteen of those flyers posted in high-visibility areas with great foot traffic throughout the Upper Ward, my next show is sure to be an even bigger success than my previous one! My upcoming success burns like a fire, bright and hot, and I have myself to thank for that!

'And you too, of course. You have contributed a small portion, I suppose.'Defend Umbar Baharbêl.Defend Umbar Baharbêl.Complete Heirsworn-slayer of Umbar Baharbêl (Advanced)Complete "Rat"-catcher of Umbar Baharbêl (Advanced)A self-proclaimed community representative stands over a ransacked stall.A self-proclaimed community representative asked you to fight the brigands responsible for attacking the House of Twisted Vines in the Upper Ward.

Upstart brigand fighters can be found outside the Raven and Albatross in the Upper Ward.Defeat upstart fighters outside the Raven and Albatross (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat upstart crossbowmen outside the Raven and Albatross (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated enough of the upstarts to make them think twice about disrupting the Upper Ward again. Tell Dehêbix of your success.

Dehêbix can be found in the Upper Ward.Talk to Dehêbix outside the House of Twisted Vines'In Umbar Baharbêl, we care for our own. It is true in most districts of the city, but it is more true in the Upper Ward than anywhere else. If a merchant loses his stall or his goods to the actions of an undesirable few, the others band together to see that he is made whole, and the wrongful parties are... dealt with. That is why we must do something about the upstarts who have taken over the Raven and Albatross. They tried to send a message to the proprietor of this inn, the House of Twisted Vines, by ruining some of his prized trellises, as you can see. But this cannot go unpunished.

'I am a representative of the community here in the Upper Ward, and my name is Dehêbix. I speak for myself, but more importantly I speak for the community. For the sake of its people you will tell me what you know about these upstarts.

'You did not see the attack? Then I shall count upon you to mete out the justice that is required. The upstarts that did this can be found fortifying the Raven and Albatross here in the Upper Ward. They will not be afraid to kill you, I am afraid, but the community will reward you if you risk this danger.''My associates have sent word of your deeds to me, and I approve. Those upstarts will think twice before crossing the Golden Queen again, and if they do they know what will happen to them.

'Did I not say before that I am an agent of Lady Hármelak? I believe I made it clear to you that I represent the community of the Upper Ward, and if you are to spend time here you must know, or must learn, this simple truth: Lady Hármelak IS the Upper Ward. It is her coin that remunerates you now, and her favour you have earned. Cherish it, for it is of great value.'Khûtra Elder Ilaya has asked for your help in healing some of the afflicted animals surrounding Khûtra.Khûtra Elder Ilaya has asked for your help in healing some of the afflicted wild goats surrounding Khûtra. The goats can be found in the hills north of Khûtra.Return to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra.Return to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra'Now that we have a salve for these animals, our important work can begin in earnest.

'It is important that we heal any nearby diseased prey animals. Healing the wild goats in the hills north of Khûtra will ensure that if any predator should eat them, this cycle of death is ended.

'Will you help us?''You have our gratitude, and that of the beasts'. Nature works best when we all work together harmoniously. You are a fine example of that.'Shikavi is concerned that her child is romanticizing the life of a Corsair and may travel down a path she cannot follow.Shikavi has asked you to try and reach Kina and help him see the realities of pirate life.Talk to Kina in the GutKina has run away disinterested in what you have to say leaving you to deal with his friends.Defeat Kina's guardsYou handled Kina's supposed friends, but they ran away in the process. You should tell Shikavi.Talk to Shikavi'Kina has convinced himself that he will one day rule the Corsairs and even this city. I cannot reach him. I am accused of not being supportive and pushing him away... but I know for a fact these Corsairs do not care for Kina. They use him as a slave with promises of space on one of their boats and a share of spoils.

'I have seen how they treat Kina. Would you please help me get through to him?''Oh my, Kina. How could you?

'I hope you are all right. I did not think it would be so dangerous to speak to my child.

'This is far more serious than I could have ever imagined.'Shikavi is convinced that Kina is in far deeper than she could ever fear.Shikavi has asked you to appeal to the authority of the captain of the crew of which Kina pretends to be a member.

Captain Hûmaraz can be found on the south-east end of Lower Ward.Confront HûmarazYou have slain Hûmaraz, but Kina ran away again, his feelings hurt by what once was his idol. You should check in with Shikavi.

Shikavi can be found outside of the Black Anchor Tavern.Talk to Shikavi'This has to end here. I fear for my child's life. If he continues down this path, there is only death in his future. And an early one!

'Could you please help convince the captain of Kina's crew to let him go? That is the only way.

'They may even respect this approach more. If Kina will listen to anyone, it's his captain.

'The Captain makes the deepest part of the Gut his home, in the south-east end of the Lower Ward.''You wish to take Kina from this crew? Kina is no more than a cabin boy, but a good one.

'He listens and obeys, fetches me drinks, and brings me worthy tithings. He is my personal errand-boy and I have no intention of giving him up.

'For this insubordination, I will have your head!''Good, you are here! Don't worry! Kina is safe with me. He is crying in his room.

'I don't know what you did or how you did it. But Kina has quit the crew and returned to me. I hope that his stories of fancy with the Corsairs have ended.

'Nonetheless, you have brought him home and I thank you.'A man named Ezôti has assembled a fearsome collection of animals for his menagerie in the Upper Ward, and it is the talk of many folk in the Sail-haven.Ezôti can be found by Bith Gabâr in the Upper Ward.'Have you heard about the many animals that have been put on display in the menagerie of the Upper Ward? A man called Ezôti has gathered a number of fearsome creatures; just thinking about them fills me with dread!

'He is to be found by Bith Gabâr in the Upper Ward. When I am done with my work I will go there right away!''Have you heard about the many animals that have been put on display in the menagerie of the Upper Ward? A man called Ezôti has gathered a number of fearsome creatures; just thinking about them fills me with dread!

'He is to be found by Bith Gabâr in the Upper Ward. When I am done with my work I will go there right away!''Another interested set of eyes? Indeed, indeed! Rumour of my creatures has spread far and wide, but none so far as that concerning my latest acquisition!'The Yâshalam family's emissary, Miritah, has asked you to retrieve a family heirloom, a necklace, from the ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo.Search the ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo for a heavy, ornate necklace that the Yâshalam family lost. The ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo can be found in the hills east of Khûtra.  Then bring it back to the Yâshalam Family Emissary, Miritah.'You seem uniquely equipped for a task that requires some... delicacy. The Yâshalam family lost something years ago that was taken to the Mâkhda Khorbo. We have reason to believe this family heirloom, a necklace, is still there in the ruins. Unfortunately for us, the dead are more at home than the living in the Mâkhda Khorbo.

'If you could retrieve this item for us, there would be a handsome reward for you. Not a word to anyone, though. Any rumours that leak out about the Yâshalams or this necklace would... displease the Lady Yâshalam.''Thank you for retrieving this. It is priceless to the Yâshalam family. If anyone asks, nothing was found in the ruins, and we never asked for this. I'm sure you understand.

'A curse? No, I think not. To commune with the dead is a privilege, not a curse, and one my family has not had in far too long.'The Fathomwell cisterns provide water for the rest of the city, but that is no reason for local fishermen to avoid plumbing its depths for their dinners.Tarax is across the Fathomwell from Hûmaz.Talk to Tarax on the other side of the FathomwellHûmaz is across the Fathomwell from Tarax.Talk to Hûmaz on the other side of the FathomwellTarax is across the Fathomwell from Hûmaz.Talk to Tarax on the other side of the FathomwellHûmaz is across the Fathomwell from Tarax.Talk to Hûmaz on the other side of the Fathomwell'Greetings, stranger. I would ask you to keep your voice down, but I do not think that will make a difference today. The fish have not been biting.

'This is the Fathomwell, where water from the bay runs into the great cisterns for use by the folk of Umbar Baharbêl. The fish swim in and become disoriented, which makes for good fishing for me and my companions. Most of the time.

'Perhaps not today. Will you cross to the other side of the Fathomwell and ask Tarax if he is having more good fortune on that side of the pool?''How is the fishing over here? Why do you ask?'

Tarax looks at you suspiciously for a considerable length of time, paying no attention to the line he has cast into the Fathomwell. You note that he appears to get not so much as a nibble.

'If Hûmaz thinks he is going to do better than I am, he is better off staying where he is. You go tell him that.''He says I should stay here? Hmm... I don't trust those words.

'Does that mean he is having more luck on that side than I am over here, or does that mean he is looking out for my own interests and believes I must be getting more fish upon my hook on this side?

'Perhaps you will go back to him and see if he is hiding anything from us? Is it possible he caught a great deal of fish and has hidden them somewhere nearby?''You are back again? Hûmaz thinks I have caught a great number of fish and have them hidden somewhere nearby? It does make sense. After all, he did that very thing himself the other day! I was so furious when I discovered it!

'Yes, this happens a lot. We come to the Fathomwell every morning, and some days he catches more fish than I do, and sometimes I have better luck than he, and often we send a helpful stranger back and forth across the pool to inquire about the other's fortunes. There really is no end to it... at least until the sun goes down, and then we each go back to our homes and it all starts again the next day.

'I suppose I would miss it. But it seems today we are equally-matched in ill fortune.''So he has no secret pile of fish today? That is good to know.

'Yes, we have been coming to the Fathomwell for years and years. My father brought me here when I was just a boy, and he would tell me stories of the city and its history. My favourites were always the ones with fighting, like when bloodthirsty Thorongil attacked and set the city aflame. Did you know not even the waters of Fathomwell could put out the fires? They burned for days, my father said.

'Tarax loved those stories too. I had forgotten! We used to fish on the same side of the pool, but at some point we became so competitive that we could not do that any longer. Ah, this is not an uncommon mood for me on days when the fish aren't biting!

'Thank you for helping me as you have. I appreciate it.'Umaris has asked for your help feeding the village using the large, fierce crabs south of Khûtra. Perhaps Elder Roshat will see your value once you've helped the village.Large crabs can be found to the south-east of Khûtra. Go there and return with crab meat to feed the hungry villagers.'Help from outsiders? And you were sent by Roshat? He must be getting truly desperate.

'It's true we could use all the help we can get. Our lures are as good and our hands as quick as ever. It's the trout themselves that have changed. They have turned a pallid, slimy green, afflicted with some terrible disease. We know not why. Some of the hands have taken to calling it the stench, for obvious reasons. We cannot eat or sell any of the fish we catch, it makes any who eat it violently ill.

'I'll be honest with you, moreso than perhaps Roshat was – we really could use your help. We rely on the fish to fill our bellies and our coin pouches. I know Roshat has suspicions about the source of the disease, but he won't trust outsiders unless he sees your value.

'I don't know how to heal our fish, but I know how you could help fill our bellies and perhaps gain his trust. There are crabs to the east of here, along the shore, just beyond the village. They seem to be immune to the stench, at least so far. However, they fight back more than we gentle fisherfolk can handle.

'Would you go to the east and bring us back some crab to feed our people?''I am grateful. We are proud folk, but I'm not too proud to admit my people will have full bellies tonight thanks to you. You might want to talk to Elder Roshat again.'The Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl is filled with skilled shipmen who toil to better the Free City in the aftermath of the Sea-stone Mutiny.Hungry shipmen can be found throughout the Sail-haven, especially on its piers and near its canals.

Zemirah has asked you to deliver meals to hungry shipmen in the Sail-haven.Zemirah can be found at the Sailors' Guild-hall in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have delivered meals to many of the shipmen labouring in the Sail-haven. You should return to Zemirah.Talk to Zemirah at the Sailors' Guild-hall'It is a miracle what we can accomplish now that Balakhôr and the Heirs have been overthrown, but we must not push ourselves too hard too swiftly as we work to build a new Umbar Baharbêl. It is a credit to the work ethic of our shipmen that the Sail-haven looks scarcely different than it did before the War—or the Mutiny, for that matter. As the new master of the sailors' guild, it is my belief that meals should sometimes be provided at the expense of the guild's coffers. Let our shipmen keep their wages for their own!

'To that end, I have prepared a number of meals for hungry shipmen in the Sail-haven, but I simply do not have the time to deliver them myself. If you could deliver them on my behalf and offer some words of encouragement to our shipmen, I would be most grateful.

'What do you say, ${PLAYER}?''You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.

'Hopefully, I'll be able to deliver some meals myself in the future, but I'm certain they all appreciated your help as much as I did!'Ibzan is concerned for The Black Anchor. The Corsairs have made it difficult for the tavern to entertain guests and also turn any profit.Ibzan has asked you to take back casks of mead stolen from Corsairs in the Gut.Collect casks of mead from the gut (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have taken back as many casks as you can from the Corsairs of the Gut.'The Black Anchor will soon go under.

'At first this was a premiere establishment for all of the people of Umbar, but now Corsairs and pirates from the Gut have started crossing boundaries. Their presence makes it harder for us to not only entertain our guests, but to turn a profit.

'They take casks of mead freely as though it is owed to them. If I cannot take these casks back, I will not be able to keep the mead flowing for paying customers!

'Would you be willing to help?''I cannot believe this. You actually did it! You are something else, friend.

'Now we will not only be able to keep the mead flowing, but I will be able to turn a profit this night.

'I am eternally grateful to you!'Now that the fish are healthy again, Umaris has asked for your help feeding the village. Bring her a mix of healthy fish for a reward.Now that the fish are healthy again, Umaris has asked for your help feeding the village. Bring her a mix of healthy fish for a reward.'Now that the fish are healthy again, would you consider joining us in the great pursuit? We'll give you a fair share on anything you catch!''I am grateful for these. We always need more good quality fish such as these, so come back tomorrow if you fancy a little more coin.'Ahûzath is concerned about the state of Umbar with swaths of freebooters and Corsairs roaming around.Ahûzath has asked you to clean up all the detritus in the Gut.Clean up the detritus (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have cleaned up most of the mess in the Gut. You should tell Ahûzath about this.Talk to Ahûzath'We would love to share our culture, but that is not very easy to do now. These freebooters and scoundrels roam the city as if they own the land. They leave behind debris and detritus and create an ill look for the city. Our businesses cannot thrive in such an environment.

'Would you help clean up the detritus around Râhal Bakh? There is an area that is most troubled by this mess. We call it The Gut because that is where all the ruffians leave their waste.''Did you actually do this? I was just complaining into the wind. I did not actually believe someone would try to clean up the Gut.

'The Corsairs and pirates will most likely take it as an insult and probably leave even more waste behind... but I cannot blame you for a good deed.

'Thank you for listening to my ramblings and acting upon it.'Heshra has asked you to bring him large quantities of the ingredients he needs for the improved healing salve.Heshra has asked you to procure large quantities of ingredients he needs from Ziriha, the merchant. She can be found near the fishing pier.Talk to Ziriha, the merchantGive dried ingredients to Heshra in the Elder Hall.Give dried ingredients to Heshra, the herbalistAdminister salve to afflicted Khûtra villagers. They can be found on the rocks just outside of Khûtra, to the east.Return to Heshra the herbalist in the Elder Hall.Return to Heshra, the herbalist'That last salve proved the key. Can you help me gather enough ingredients that we may heal our fish, our animals and our people? We need large quantities of calendula and delphinium. I have the other ingredients here. I happen to know the local merchant, Ziriha, has large quantities dried.''Heshra has found a cure? That is joyous news indeed. Here, take all the ingredients you need, with my blessing. No, no keep your coin. It's bad business to make a profit off any of this suffering.''Ahh yes, fine quality, as usual. Just a moment, let me add this to what I already have. Here, take this. Please, our afflicted are below here, on the rocks just outside the village. Not a moment to spare! Give each some of the salve, and they should be back on their way to good health.''I can't thank you enough for what you have done here. Please, take what is left and go see Elder Ilaya. She oversees all our livestock. I'm sure she would appreciate some help tending to the afflicted animals.'Speak to Elder Ilaya about administering the improved salve to the livestock in Khûtra.Elder Ilaya has asked that you administer the improved salve to the afflicted goats and pigs in Khûtra. The goats can be found outside the Elder Hall.You should administer the salve to diseased pigs in Khûtra. They can be found in a pen outside the Elder Hall.Administer salve to sullen diseased pigAdminister salve to boisterous diseased pigAdminister salve to despondent diseased pigAdminister salve to glum diseased pigAdminister salve to scheming diseased pigAdminister salve to happy diseased pigReturn to Elder Ilaya outside the Elder Hall.Speak with Elder Ilaya'You have a cure from Heshra? It's about time. Our animals are suffering just as much as our people, and between you and I, I prefer the company of the goats.

'Please, help the afflicted goats and pigs here on their way back to good health.''Thank you. It warms my heart to see the animals romping, full of energy again. Seems you're running low on that salve. You should see if Heshra has made any more, and then go see Umaris.'Umaris has asked you to distribute the salve to the best fishing spots in Khûtra.Speak with Umaris, the fisher. She can be found by the fishing pier.Speak with Umaris, the fisherUmaris has asked you to distribute the salve to the five best fishing spots in Khûtra. These fishing spots start on the fishing pier and then move west along the shore.Release the salve into fishing spots around Khûtra (${NUMBER}/5)Return to Umaris by the fishing pier.Return to Umaris'You need more? What a welcome problem. Yes, I've been quite busy. For the fish? You'll need lots. Here, take what I have. I'm making more as fast as I can. You'll want to see Umaris next, I expect.''Thank you. You have done much for Khûtra. We won't soon forget. I won't soon forget.

'Roshat is asking after you, you should see what he wants.''That foul smelling mixture is the cure? As you say. Here. let me mark our five best fishing spots. Release the salve there, and it should, in time, filter down into the fish. There are several spots here on the pier, and then more along the beaches to the west.'Satisfied that the Heirsworn have been routed from the Sail-haven, at least for the moment, Eshmun has invited you to accompany him to the Bloody Eagle to celebrate this victory and toast to brighter days ahead.The Bloody Eagle is a tavern located to the east of the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

Eshmun has asked you to meet him at the Bloody Eagle to celebrate your victory over the Heirsworn in the Sail-haven. You should meet Eshmun at the Bloody Eagle.Meet Eshmun at the Bloody EagleEshmun can be found in the Bloody Eagle, a tavern located to the east of the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have found Eshmun in the Bloody Eagle. You should talk to Eshmun.Talk to Eshmun in the Bloody EagleAkurga's spear can be found behind the bar in the rear of the Bloody Eagle.

Eshmun has asked you to examine Akurga's spear in the Bloody Eagle.Examine Akurga's spear in the Bloody EagleAkálam can be found behind the bar in the rear of the Bloody Eagle.

After inspecting Akurga's spear, you have caught the attention of the tavern keep of the Bloody Eagle, Akálam. You should talk to Akálam.Talk to Akálam in the Bloody EagleAkálam is telling his tale of the bane of Umbar in the Bloody Eagle.

After speaking with Akálam, you believe you know the identity of the bane of Umbar. You should continue to listen to his tale.Listen to Akálam's tale of the bane of UmbarAkálam can be found behind the bar in the rear of the Bloody Eagle.

Akálam has nearly concluded his tale of the bane of Umbar. You should talk to Akálam.Talk to Akálam in the Bloody EagleKhôltekh the Cunning can be found in the Bloody Eagle, in the Sail-haven.

After listening to Akálam's tale, you heard a chuckle at the end of the bar in the Bloody Eagle, and it appears that Khôltekh the Cunning, one of the Kindred of the Coins, was amused by some aspect of Akálam's tale.Talk to Khôltekh the Cunning in the Bloody EagleEshmun can be found in the Bloody Eagle, a tavern located to the east of the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

After having an uncomfortable talk with Khôltekh the Cunning, you decide you should return to Eshmun in the Bloody Eagle.Talk to Eshmun in the Bloody Eagle'I must thank you, ${PLAYER}. If only for a day, you have helped me to drive the Heirsworn from the Sail-haven, and I say that is worthy of celebration!

'To that end, I would ask that you meet me in the Bloody Eagle. It is one of Umbar's many taverns, but fortunately, it is not so far from here. In fact, it is just to the east of this tower! There is something else I would like to show you there—something of great importance to me and the older sailors of Umbar.'

'But when that is done, we shall toast to your victory over the Heirsworn and to the future of Umbar!''Ah! I hope it was not too much trouble to find me, ${PLAYER}.

'I do not often come to the Bloody Eagle—or any tavern for that matter—but since I was made Captain of the Haven, I have found myself here on more than a few occasions. You see, its proprietor is a man named Akálam, and many years ago, his father, Akurga, was the Captain of the Haven. To this day, Akurga's spear still hangs behind the bar, and I find it a comfort to look upon it—to remember what it is that I strive to protect and the sacrifices we must make for Umbar.

'Why don't you go and see it for yourself? It has quite the storied history, my friend, and if Akálam catches you looking at it for long enough, you're likely to hear the lot of it!''You wish to know about that spear, do you?'

Akálam glances at the spear, and in the flicker of the light, you catch sight of old burns upon his face.

'Do you know the tale of the bane of Umbar? He was like a half-giant among Men—dark-haired with eyes of grey—a great captain from some distant, unknown land.

'That spear belonged to my father, Akurga, or so it did until the bane of Umbar came to our city....'Akálam's tale continues.

'And so, he came to Umbar like a spectre in the night. It was said that his blade was wreathed in flame, for the ships of the Sail-haven were set alight in his wake, and the harbour burned as if the water itself had turned to blackest pitch.

'Many were those who fell before him and his fleet, but none fought as bravely as my father, Akurga. He was Captain of the Haven on that dark night, and it fell to him to repel these interlopers lest all of Umbar be overthrown. Alas, before my own eyes, the villain slew my father at the doors of the Harbour-master's Tower. I was only a boy then, and rushing out from the doors, I stepped over my father to take up his spear. It seemed then that our enemy hesitated, and in that moment, I drove the spear into him with all of my might. Fleeing into the flames, he withdrew with his fleet, and he was never seen again.

'And surely I dealt him a mortal blow, for had I not truly killed him, would not he have returned to avenge himself upon us?''I later learned that the bane of Umbar was said to be named Thorongil—the Eagle of some accursed star, in the tongue of the Elves—but it matters not.

'None in Umbar Baharbêl need fear his return. Thorongil is dead, and the blood on my father's spear is all the proof of that we shall ever need!''That was quite the tale, wasn't it?'

Khôltekh chuckles to himself.

'Akálam seems quite sure of himself, and from what I can tell, the people of Umbar have no reason to doubt him. After all, he is the hero that slew Thorongil, the bane of Umbar, and he bears the scars to prove it! I wonder, though. What about you? What do you think happened to Thorongil, ${PLAYER}?'

Khôltekh looks into your eyes, and his face no longer betrays any amusement.

'You know what I think? Perhaps he became a King!'

Khôltekh laughs.

'Better warn old Eshmun, eh?''Is everything all right, ${PLAYER}? You were over there for quite some time, and I saw that you caught Khôltekh's attention.'

You tell Eshmun that you are fine, but that Khôltekh was a bit unusual.

'As one of the Kindred of the Coins, I respect what he has done for Umbar, but I must admit, I find him to be an odd fellow—charming, to be certain—but I'm never quite sure what he's after when I speak to him. I much prefer to let Tumúldo deal with him, to be perfectly honest.

'Here, my friend, let us toast to the future of Umbar.'

Eshmun hands you a mug, and you notice that it is not filled with ale, but instead with water.

'I know it is not the tradition, but I find ale to be a luxury of younger Men, and when you have been a sailor for as long as I have, you know the true worth of water.

'And so, I toast to you, ${PLAYER}, and to the future of Umbar Baharbêl! May the Free City endure until the end of all days!'

You and Eshmun toast.

'I ought to get back to the Harbour-warden's Tower, my friend. If you ever need anything, you know where to find me!'Although most were slain or routed during the Sea-stone Mutiny, several crews of Corsairs still loyal to the Heirs of Castamir have found unlikely refuge in Umbar Baharbêl.Heirsworn Corsairs can be found around their ships at the northern and southern piers of the Sail-haven, as well as at the southern ship-yard of the Sail-haven.

Eshmun has asked you to defeat Heirsworn Corsairs in the Sail-haven.Defeat Heirsworn Corsairs in the Sail-haven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have defeated many of the Heirsworn Corsairs troubling the people of the Sail-haven. You should return to Eshmun.Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower'According to Zemirah and Ahûd, the Heirsworn have taken up on the more distant piers of the Sail-haven.

'One Heirsworn is a problem that can be handled with a hidden blade in the shadows of a tavern or by a raucous crowd in the market, but these are traitor crews—crews still captained by Balakhôr's most loyal followers. Even so, they have made their intentions clear and I would be a fool to ignore them. With the murder of Râmax, there can be no hope for peace between us. Tumúldo has put his faith in me, and I do not intend to let him down.

'Where the Heirs of Castamir are concerned, brutality must be met with brutality, for that is the only language that they understand. But, do you understand, ${PLAYER}? Until the last of them are routed or slain, I say that the Sea-stone Mutiny is not ended!''I trust you have succeeded, ${PLAYER}.

'The Heirsworn should have been grateful enough that they escaped the bloodshed of the Mutiny with their lives, but they cannot let go of their delusions. The Scourge is dead, and so are the other masters of the Heirs of Castamir. Umbar Baharbêl is a Free City, and its people will not go quietly back into servitude!'Defeat many Heirsworn in Umbar Baharbêl.Defeat many Heirsworn in Umbar Baharbêl.Defeat many Heirsworn in Umbar BaharbêlDefeat many Heirsworn in Umbar Baharbêl.Defeat many Heirsworn in Umbar Baharbêl.Defeat many Heirsworn in Umbar BaharbêlIn the wake of a brazen murder committed by the Heirsworn, Eshmun, the Captain of the Haven, intends to deliver swift and terrible retribution upon those still loyal to the Heirs of Castamir in Umbar Baharbêl.Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, has asked for your aid in ridding Umbar Baharbêl of those still loyal to Balakhôr the Scourge and the Heirs of Castamir.Complete 'The Scourge's Captains'Complete 'Stealing From Their Own'Complete 'Heirs To Naught'Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have done much to rout the remnants of the Heirs of Castamir in the Sail-haven. You should talk to Eshmun.Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower'When I was made Captain of the Haven, Tumúldo said it had to be me—Kindred of the Coins or not, he knew I could keep watch on the Sail-haven. Like it was with poor Râmax, I have known Tumúldo since he was a boy, and though our friendship has been a complicated one at times, we have grown to trust each other without question.

'Before Tumúldo departed on his voyage, he told me to do whatever I must to protect Umbar Baharbêl and its people from those who still put their faith in Balakhôr the Scourge. While these Heirsworn may not fly the black sails of old, they are still at war—only instead of with Gondor, who was too mighty for them to overcome, they have turned their hatred upon their own. I have seen Umbar changed again and again through turmoil in the course of my life, but we have never been so close to true freedom. The Heirsworn cling to the past, and their grip loosens with each passing day, but how many more must be injured—or killed—before they are finally only a memory? I say none! We shall pry each of their fingers loose until their grip is broken, and when that is done, Umbar Baharbêl shall truly be a Free City!

'You are a hale adventurer, and though I do not know your journey, I know that you share my hatred of those who call themselves the Heirs of Castamir. Let us work together and put an end to them, once and for all!''You have done very well, ${PLAYER}.

'When Tumúldo returns from his voyage, I ought to introduce him to the ${CLASS} who drove out the last of the Scourge's Men in the Sail-haven!'A strange man puts on a 'show' in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Ezôti has revealed where he keeps his captive animals. Share this information with Gûshida.

Gûshida is in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Gûshida across the way from EzôtiGûshida told you to meet her at Ezôti's hiding place.

Ezôti's hiding place is inside an unassuming flat in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl, to the north-east.Meet with Gûshida inside Ezôti's FlatEzôti's captive animals are in poor condition. Gûshida has asked you to help check on them.

Ezôti's hiding place is inside the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Check on the cave-clawCheck on the goatCheck on the boarCheck on the bearYou have inspected the animals and should report back to Gûshida.

Gûshida can be found in Ezôti's hiding place in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Gûshida inside Ezôti's FlatEzôti smiles at you for a little too long, an already uncomfortable pause becoming longer and more awkward with each passing second. Finally he says 'I think I can trust you with a most important task. I have many animals in my care.'

He leans closer to you. His breath smells of good fish and bad milk.

'...Or should I say "our" care? That is right! I am entrusting you with the care of my animals. Go to where I house my precious friends in the Upper Quarter. Feed and water them.'You share the animals' location with Gûshida.

'Good work! I will tell my associates we are on our way to rescue the animals. I will meet you inside Ezôti's Flat in the Upper Ward, north-east of here.'The air is thick with an amalgam of stenches. Gûshida pinches her nose with a thick cloth.

'Quickly! Help me check on them!''This is no natural exhaustion. I suspect Ezôti has given them something to make them sluggish, and less capable of escape. The fiend!'A merchant needs help evaluating the quality of his goods.A merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags.

His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.Smack the bags of rice (0/5)A merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags.

His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.Smack the bags of rice (1/5)A merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags.

His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.Smack the bags of rice (2/5)You have found a bag of rice that does not pass muster. Pick it up and drop it next to the injured merchant.

The injured merchant can be found outside the Monger's Guild-hall in the Upper Ward.Pick up the bag of bad riceA merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags.

His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.Smack the bags of rice (3/5)A merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags.

His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.Smack the bags of rice (4/5)You have inspected all the rice and should report back to the injured merchant.

The injured merchant is outside the Monger's Guild-hall in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to the injured merchant outside the Monger's Guild-hall'Ugh, I hurt my back recently, and now I cannot lift the sacks of rice I ordered. I need to check them in case I need to send any of them back to my supplier, but I can't easily move from this spot. Could you do it for me? No, you don't need to open the sacks. Just give them a whack. You'll know by the feel and the sound if the bag is good or not.

'The sacks were unloaded by the Wharf-gate between the Sail-haven and the Upper Ward. There is an alley on the Sail-haven side of the gate where my men leave them. I need them to bring the sacks all the way here next time, if my back is not better, but I know they will not want to do that unless I pay them more... and that would be very difficult to do unless my fortunes change!''Only one sack of bad rice so far? I hope the others are good.

'You will return there to check the rest of them?''Oh good! So there was only the one bag that did not pass the smack test? Good. I will return it and ask that my coin be returned to me... when I am able to, of course. For now, I will sit here and enjoy the breeze.'Khâshap has fled into the bustling Streets of Râhal Bakh where he has the protection of his cohorts.Khâshap has fled deeper into the Streets of Râhal Bakh. Catch up to him before it is too late.Pursue KhâshapKhâshap has left his champion Utho to deal with you.Defeat Utho the GrasperKhâshap continues his escape to another gate. But it seems he is out of options.Continue the pursuitThe pursuit of Khâshap has led you to a dead end. He has no choice but to take a stand.Defeat KhâshapKhâshap at long last has been stopped. The engine of the apothecaries will no longer reach his masters, and the crisis averted.

You should speak to Hadorion.Talk to Hadorion'This is it. It's now or never. He has nowhere left to hide.

'But this is also his home turf. We face some tough odds. But I am sure you have faced far worse.

'If he manages to deliver the phial, there's no telling what the consequences may be. Do not stop for anything. Bring him to justice!''I swear that man had nine lives. Every step of the way he used his minions as shields and would slip off into the night.

'Today was a good day. Not only did we solve the case, but we stopped an even larger plot from manifesting.

'Thank you. I could not have done this without you.'Usham was frightened by spiders outside the city and has asked for your help.Usham ran afoul of spiders to the east of the city, and he asked for your help recovering the satchel he dropped here when he fled.Defeat spiders east of the city (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Usham's satchel where he dropped it east of the cityUsham is outside the Dampstone Inn.Bring the satchel to Usham outside the Dampstone InnUsham asked you to set his satchel down on the table outside the inn.Place Usham's satchel down on the table outside the innUsham is not happy.Talk to Usham outside the Dampstone InnUsham no longer wants his satchel, and has asked you to leave it outside the city. Just to the north-east of the Dampstone Inn should be far enough.Leave Usham's satchel in the wild north-east of the Dampstone InnNow that you have done as he asked, you should return to Usham outside the Dampstone Inn.Return to Usham outside the Dampstone InnMaisha has called for your attention outside the Dampstone Inn.Talk to Maisha outside the Dampstone Inn'Far to the east of the city I ran afoul of... afoul of...'

Usham shudders.

'Do I have to say it? Spiders! Terrible things! In my haste to escape, I left my satchel behind. Will you go back there and retrieve it for me? And perhaps you will defeat some of the creatures that frightened me so?''In my haste to escape, I left my satchel behind. Will you go back there and retrieve it for me? And perhaps you will defeat some of the creatures that frightened me so?''You rescued my satchel from the spiders? Thank you, friend. Can you set it down on that small table over there?''Can you set my satchel down on that small table over there?''There... there was a spider hiding in my satchel? It must have hitched a ride when I was travelling toward the city, and thought to surprise me when I least expected it! These creatures will stop at nothing to terrify me! I am lucky that I dropped the satchel when I did! Why did I ever send you to bring it back to me?'

You ask Usham what he would like done with his satchel now. He gazes at you in horror.

'Keep it? Are you mad? I do not want it anymore! Take it outside the city and leave it there!''Keep it? Are you mad? I do not want it anymore! Take it outside the city and leave it there!''Your friend is gone. He said he was going to sign up with one of the caravans and go with them to a land far from here, where spiders will no longer menace him.'

She grins at you.

'He left before I could tell him about any of the great beasts that I have heard live in and beyond the vast deserts... much worse than any of the spiders you find around here! Oh well. He will see.

'Good day to you.'It is finally time to confront Khâshap.Khâshap plans to confront the rumours head on by appearing before the Gut. Hadorion believes we should spring the trap now.Attend Khâshap's assemblyKhâshap has gathered his Corsairs and makes his escape into the back alleys of the Lower Ward. He must be stopped here before he delivers the phials of Ifrinn to his master.Confront KhâshapKhâshap has fled into the back streets of the Gut. Hadorion believes this is the final chance. Khâshap is cornered.Talk to Hadorion'Let us make preparations to begin our pursuit! We have him cornered!''He has escaped again!

'The man is either lucky or very good at pretending to be. Either way, the pursuit doesn't stop. This is his destination, after all.

'We must pressure him into making one final mistake.

'The man has nine lives. I won't lie to you. We are severely outnumbered.

'But we must keep our eyes on the prize. Khâshap is within our grasp!'Shajât has a sad story to tell, and he has asked you to help him with his myriad woes.Shajât's former captain, Jidâlo, is outside the Broken Pillar Tavern in the Lower Ward.Talk to Jidâlo outside the Broken Pillar Tavern in the Lower WardThe Ballast's former ship-mates can be found in the vicinity of the Broken Pillar Tavern, in the Lower Ward.Talk to the Ballast's former ship-mates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Shajât is outside the Lower Ward, in the Sail-haven.Excited to begin his new life, Shajât agreed to meet you outside the Swain's Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.Find the Swain's Guild Hall in the Lower WardShajât stands outside the Swain's Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.Talk to Shajât outside the Swain's Guild HallShajât lost the coins given to him by his ship-mates to ruffians in the Gut, and if you don't recover them for him no one will.Retrieve Shajât's coins from ruffians in the Gut (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Shajât stands outside the Swain's Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.'My name is Shajât, and I have a sad story to spin. Will you hear it?

'I was a sailor on a ship, a good ship, and together the crew and I delivered cargo up and down the coast. It was the life for me: seeing new lands and distant shores, meeting interesting people and seeing their faces light up with delight when they received the goods they wanted or needed! I loved it!

'And the camaraderie! That crew was like my family. They called me "The Ballast." A term of endearment, you know?

'It was the best week and a half of my life. But now Captain Jidâlo has sent me away! Will you find him and beg for me to be allowed to join his crew again? He should be at the Broken Pillar Tavern in the Lower Ward with the rest of the crew.''But now Captain Jidâlo has sent me away! Will you find him and beg for me to be allowed to join his crew again? He should be at the Broken Pillar Tavern in the Lower Ward with the rest of the crew.''Shajât sent you? Who is that?'

You tell the captain that Shajât also may have been called "The Ballast," and he groans.

'Oh, I see. Do you know why we called him the Ballast? He may not understand this, being so unused to a mariner's life, but ballast is a heavy material, usually iron, lead, or stone, placed in the hold of a ship to keep it steady. When used as a name for someone onboard a ship... it means that person is useless.

'He was just terrible, friend. During the days he was with us we encountered enough ill fortune and bad luck to fill a year. He tied the wrong knots, scrubbed the wrong floors, emptied the wrong pots, read the wrong weather signs, pointed out dangerous shoals as safe and safe shoals as dangerous. I have never seen someone less-suited to shipboard life. So I sent him away.

'We did not mean to hurt his feelings. Boys! I say we pass around the hat and raise some coin for the Ballast to begin a new life. Every man should put in some coin... and make his donation with the certainty that it will keep the Ballast as far from our ship as might be managed!''Every man should put in some coin... and make his donation with the certainty that it will keep the Ballast as far from our ship as might be managed!''They raised these coins... for me?'

Shajât's eyes water with grateful tears.

'I told you my former ship-mates were like family to me! "Ballast!" they said to me, "we have never had a voyage like this before!"

'But it is time to set a new course. I will go to the Swain's Guild Hall, in the Lower Ward. I understand that is from where some of the caravans across the desert depart, and that is the new profession I have chosen for myself. I will see you there, friend!''I will go to the Swain's Guild Hall, in the Lower Ward. I understand that is from where some of the caravans across the desert depart, and that is the new profession I have chosen for myself. I will see you there, friend!''You are not going to believe this, friend... but as I made my way here I was accosted by ruffians, and they stole the coins given to me by my former shipmates! Alas!

'The ruffians apparently make their home in a place called the Gut. Do you know where that is, and do you think you might retrieve the money for me? It would be a shame for the hopes of Captain Jidâlo and his crew to be dashed in this fashion! What will they think of their Ballast then?''The ruffians apparently make their home in a place called the Gut. Do you know where that is, and do you think you might retrieve the money for me? It would be a shame for the hopes of Captain Jidâlo and his crew to be dashed in this fashion! What will they think of their Ballast then?''You retrieved my coins? I am so grateful, my friend! Now my new life can begin!

'I do not understand how such things can keep happening to me, but I am ready to join one of the caravans and see what adventures await me across the sands! It will be a new beginning for the Ballast... and I have you and my good crew-mates to thank for it!'Kenza wants you to deal with the mutineers that cost her the command of her ship.Many of the ruffians in the Fleet-fast conducted a mutiny against Kenza and she wants you to deal with them.Defeat ruffians in the Fleet-fast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Fleet-fast bruisers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kenza is by the stairs leading to the upper level in the Fleet-fast.Talk to Kenza in the Fleet-fast'My former crew turned out to be mutineers and ruffians, all of them! They must think I perished when they threw me overboard, and I would not survive the swim back to shore. So they are not only dishonourable, but they are fools too! Now they haunt this area of the Fleet-fast, and they stay here in great enough number that the guards fear to engage them in battle.

'But I do not fear them, and neither do you, do you, my new friend? Some of them are tougher than they appear, but that will not be a problem for you, will it?''Now my former crew haunts this area of the Fleet-fast, and they stay here in great enough number that the guards fear to engage them in battle.

'But I do not fear them, and neither do you, do you, my new friend? Some of them are tougher than they appear, but that will not be a problem for you, will it?''I heard the fighting from here, friend, and it was like beautiful music to hear the panic in the voices of those mutineers. You have done very well by me. Perhaps when I recover my ship you will sail with me?

'Ah, I am already thinking of assembling a new crew, only days after my previous mates mutineed against me? I am truly a romantic at heart, my new friend. It has always been a problem.

'Thank you for your help with those ruffians and bruisers. We are more deadly than they are, and now they know it.'Mêdi wants you to put an end to the reign of terror caused by a Corsair villain on the loose in the Lower Ward.A challenge bell can be found to the south-east of Mêdi in the Lower Ward.Ring the challenge bell to the south-east of MêdiYou have rung the challenge bell and should wait for your challenge to be answered.Wait for your challenge to be answeredAnother challenge bell can be found further to the south-east in the Lower Ward.Ring the next challenge bell further to the south-eastYou have rung the challenge bell and should wait for your challenge to be answered.Wait for your challenge to be answeredThe last challenge bell can be found to the north of the previous one, in the Lower Ward.Ring the last challenge bell to the northYou have rung the challenge bell and should wait for your challenge to be answered.Wait for your challenge to be answeredMûtahir stands near the last challenge bell.Talk to Mûtahir by the last challenge bellMêdi is to the west of the last challenge bell, in the Lower Ward.Talk to Mêdi in the Lower Ward'A Corsair named Mûtahir has kept this area of the Lower Ward trembling in fear of him ever since he returned to the city. So certain of his combat prowess is he that he has string up bells throughout the Gut, and has invited anyone who believes they can best him to ring one of these bells.

'He has knocked a number of challengers senseless in the week since he left the bells. If you think you can put an end to his tyranny, one of the bells is to the south-east of here. He has others throughout the Gut as well, but he has never failed to respond to a challenge.''Mûtahir has knocked a number of challengers senseless in the week since he left the bells. If you think you can put an end to his tyranny, one of the bells is to the south-east of here. He has others throughout the Gut as well, but he has never failed to respond to a challenge.''Yes, I am Mûtahir, but I do not think I want to fight you.

'As a matter of truth, I believe I will take down all of the bells I have strung up around the Lower Ward. It seemed a good way to make a name for myself, and indeed I have now done so... but I fear that were I to engage you in battle I would, perhaps, find myself defeated. And I do not think that would add very much to my legend.

'I will leave the inhabitants of the Lower Ward alone, stranger. They will face no more challenges from Mûtahir. You have my word.''I will leave the inhabitants of the Lower Ward alone, stranger. They will face no more challenges from Mûtahir. You have my word.''You challenged Mûtahir and survived to tell the tale? This is very impressive!

'Thank you for putting an end to his reign over the Gut! The folk of the Lower Ward feared to walk the streets when he was known to be out and about. I can still hear the tinkling of the bells....

'But no longer! Thank you, my friend!'Zadok hoped to turn money lending into a profitable venture in a new city. Umbar, it seems, was not that city.Zadok has asked you to help him collect on a few debts so that he can at least have enough to return to Gondor.

Zadok's clients can be found wandering around Black Anchor, and the Baths.Collect from Râhal scoundrelCollect from Râhal lazy-bodyCollect from Râhal drunkardYou have managed to collect debts from some of the Corsairs in the Gut. This should help Zadok make a respectable getaway.Talk to Zadok'What do you want?

'I am at my wit's end. I cannot possibly make up for all the money I have lost. I thought this city and a new clientele would help me make big profits as a money-lender, but these ruffians don't understand lending terms or even the notion of paying back what's borrowed!

'In addition, they extort me constantly for more hand-outs. If I am to make it out of here and start over, I'll need help with collecting debts from these low-lifes.

'Could I hire you to be my muscle and perhaps intimidate a few of my clients into paying their debts?''My money! You managed to get some of it back, and there is even some interest on top of it.

'You either took more than what was owed, or these people are familiar with the concept of loans after all.

'Perhaps I should rethink my business model rather than running away with my tail tucked between my legs.

'Thank you, traveller!'Zadok has re-organized his business efforts in Umbar. Perhaps he can make it work after all.Zadok has asked you to help him collect a debt from a respectable proprietor in the Gut.Confront the successful proprietorYou have bested the successful proprietor. You are free to collect his treasures.Collect the treasure chestYou have the money that was promised to Zadok. You should return it to him.'I have been thinking about how I could actually make a profit here in Umbar.

'Sure, the usual clientele are not used to the notion of debts, but with your help, I can set an example in the city and perhaps even The Gut!

'There is a proprietor here who took out a massive loan in hopes of striking it rich, same as me. They have a healthy reputation in the Gut. If we could set an example with such a figure, debts would surely be paid on time and with interest.''You want my money? Do you know who you are talking to?

'You have made a big mistake this day! No one touches my money but me!''Perfect! It's even in the same chest in which he hauled it away.

'This man was obviously quite the businessman. It seems he was able to make some money on top of the initial investment that I made.

'I can't thank you enough, traveller. Perhaps one day I will be lucky enough to serve your needs. Of course you are entitled to a massive discount on interest.'Khûtra Elder Roshat has instructed you to head north from the village into the hills to search for elderberries and wheat. You are to collect them and return to him.Khûtra Elder Roshat asks that you search for food for his village.

Berries and wheat can be found to the east of Khûtra.Harvest sheaves of wheat (${NUMBER}/6)Collect elderberry bunches (${NUMBER}/10)Return the food to Khûtra Elder Roshat.Return the food to Elder Roshat in Khûtra'We have more need of supplies, and you've shown a small talent for finding foodstuffs. I wonder if you might find some more food for my village?

'Would you go to the north and collect some elderberries and wheat? The harvesting itself should be easy, but the hills there have many dangers.''You have my people's thanks. Their bellies will once again be full tonight because of you. You're more resourceful than you look.'Nâjah heard there were surplus goods stored inside the Fleet-fast, and she knows they could be put to better use in the Lower Ward.Surplus goods can be found outside two store-houses located in the Fleet-fast.Retrieve surplus goods from outside the southern store-house (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Retrieve surplus goods from outside the western store-house (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nâjah is outside the entrance to the Fleet-fast from the Lower Ward.'There are two store-houses in the Fleet-fast, stranger, to the south and to the west, and they are full of supplies. How many rations do the guards of the Citadel require? Not as many as they keep for themselves, I can tell you that. My friend says that there is such a surplus at each of these store-houses that crates and chests are even kept outside! The guards won't miss those, if you take my meaning.

'Bring me some of these surplus supplies and I will see that they are given to people who really need them: the people of the Lower Ward. They do no good for anyone if they simply take up space within the Fleet-fast. Remember, there are store-houses both to the south and to the west of the Stûna, the great dock of the ships in the water's centre. You should retrieve surplus goods from both.''Bring me some of the surplus supplies and I will see that they are given to people who really need them: the people of the Lower Ward. They do no good for anyone if they simply take up space within the Fleet-fast. Remember, there are store-houses both to the south and to the west of the Stûna, the great dock of the ships in the water's centre. You should retrieve surplus goods from both.''You have done a good thing this day. I will put these goods to... good use.

'It is very good, my friend. It should not trouble the ear to hear one say so.'Elder Roshat asks that you deal with raiders west of Khûtra in order to prove worthy of a greater task.Elder Roshat asks that you deal with Jerath and his raiders. Their camp can be found along the road west of Khûtra.Defeat raiding Corsairs in their camp (${NUMBER}/10)Defeat Jerath in the raider camp and retrieve his cutlass. Then return to Elder Roshat in Khûtra.'It seems you are not entirely without worth,' Elder Roshat says.

'The stench is not our only problem. We have been raided multiple times by Corsairs camped south of here. Their leader, Jerath, was cast out of Khûtra for petty thievery. He has borne a grudge ever since, descending from the hills and harrying our people.

'These raiders always attack from the west. Find their camp and wipe them out. From the look of you, I doubt you'd survive a brush with them, but if you did deal with these raiders, perhaps you'd prove worthy of a larger task.

'Bring Jerath's cutlass back to me as proof of his demise.''You're not dead. Couldn't be your skill. Fortune must follow you closer than most.'Yosarin has challenged you to relax. Can you do it?Yosarin asked you to sit in the baths nearby and relax. She does not think you will be able to do it!Yosarin challenged you to remain in the baths for two minutes, enjoying the water and not thinking about your daily cares.Relax within the baths without leavingYosarin is by the baths in the Lower Ward.Talk to Yosarin in the Lower Ward'Welcome to the Baths of Kadax, traveller! Can you find it in yourself to relax within their soothing waters? You need not submerge, but if it does help you to do so and you can hold your breath, I encourage you to do what comes naturally!

'This is my challenge: can you enter the baths, <rgb=#00FF00>sit</rgb>, and then empty your mind of all the day's stressful workings? Can you relax for even two minutes? If you can, I will reward you... but such a practice can be its own reward, I assure you!

'However, if you leave the baths too soon... I will not be surprised, but I will be disappointed.''This is my challenge: can you enter the baths, <rgb=#00FF00>sit</rgb>, and then empty your mind of all the day's stressful workings? Can you relax for even two minutes? If you can, I will reward you... but such a practice can be its own reward, I assure you!

'However, if you leave the baths too soon... I will not be surprised, but I will be disappointed.''I am impressed with you, my relaxed friend! I did not think you would be able to do this!

'Folk are always running here and there at great speed, their errands bringing them from one corner of the city to the other, and then back again. But is it not important to slow down, take a deep breath or two, and enjoy the experience of living?

'It is, my friend, it is! I encourage you to do so more often! And come back to the Baths of Kadax whenever you like!'Charzâd stands by the old observatory above the city, musing about the stars in the sky and the sand in the desert.Charzâd asked you to collect sand from several different locations outside the city.Collect sand from the spider-haunted ruins east of the cityCollect sand to the west of one of the farms outside the cityCollect sand from the hills north-east of the farms outside the cityCollect sand south-east of the farms outside the city, near the riverCharzâd is by the old observatory above the city, waiting for you to return to her with your discoveries.'From this observatory, scholars in Umbar Baharbêl once gazed at the skies above, studying the night sky for wisdom. How distant was that age of knowledge? Too long ago for one lifetime, my friend; the observatory was destroyed, and has fallen into ruin in the years since.

'But I have dreamed about the things you might have seen from its balconies and from the rooftop viewing platforms. Will you do something for me? I am a scholar of sorts myself, but my subjects are more terrestrial than those of the folk who once worked in the building above us. Will you take this small leather bag and fill it with sand from several locations east of the city? I will reward you for this work, of course.''Will you fill the bag I gave you with sand from several locations east of the city? I will reward you for this work, of course.''Thank you for doing as I asked, my friend. Did you observe that the sand you collected from each location possessed its own characteristics?'

You tell Charzâd that some of the sand was damp and some was dry; some was coarse and some was fine; some of the sand was brightly-coloured.

'And yet they were all, in the end, still sand?' Charzâd answers with a raised eyebrow. 'It reminds me of how I envision the stars in the sky. From our position here they all seem to be the same: twinkling dots of light, like jewels affixed to the heavens. But look at this!'

Charzâd reaches into the small leather bag and removes a handful of the sand you gathered. She opens her palm and lets the sand fall, where the individual particles drift and float restlessly on the breeze.

'Like stars,' she says. 'How different might the stars be from each other if we could only see them up close? Might the scholars at the observatory above us have learned the answer if they were not slain, the observatory not shuttered, and their work not lost? I think they might have.

'Thank you for doing this for me, my friend. Not everyone would! I know: I asked them. But take this for your trouble and your time.'Heshra is investigating the source of the disease afflicting Khûtra. He has asked you to investigate the marsh near Khûtra for anything unusual.Heshra has asked you to investigate the marsh east of Khûtra near the shore for anything unusual.Investigate suspicious areas in the marshReturn to the herbalist Heshra in the Elder Hall.Return to Heshra, the herbalist'I think I might have something. It's hard to tell... much of what they ate is now mush. One of the few things these animals all share is honeywort in their stomachs.

'There is a marsh to the east of here along the shore that is thick with the stuff. Hopefully you will find more answers there.

'There must be some malady or evil presence causing this disease that emanates from there. Please, go there and see what you can find.''A dead end. That is quite unfortunate. Still, we must try to heal these animals, and our people, regardless.'Heshra has asked you to collect various herbs for a simple salve to treat the disease.Heshra, the herbalist, has asked you to collect various herbs for a simple salve to treat the disease. These herbs can be found in the hills north of Khûtra.Administer the simple salve to the afflicted villagers. They can be found on the rocks just outside Khûtra, to the east near the shore.Return to Heshra the herbalist in the Elder Hall.Return to Heshra, the herbalist'I have a recipe that I believe could work to bring our people back to good health.

'Unfortunately, the hills around Khûtra are no longer safe for us to gather the herbs I need. Would you perhaps help? If you collect these herbs, I can prepare them into a salve to try to heal our animals and people. We may not know how to prevent this affliction, but we may yet stop it from spreading further.

'Please, collect the herbs I need. You can find most of them growing in the hills to the north. Our village depends on it.''Fine quality there. Just a moment....

'There we are. Don't mind the smell! It confirms its potency. Please, give this to the afflicted villagers. They are below us, just past the farthest house to the east, on the rocks before the shore. If it works as it should, their pallid nature should fade and they should get more lively in minutes.

'I pray it does for all our sakes.''No change? That is ill news. We are no closer to finding the source of this disease or how to stop its spread.'Heshra has asked you to test various healing salves on diseased goats in Khûtra.Speak with Ziriha the merchant about the rare ingredients Heshra needs. She can be found near the fishing pier.Talk to Ziriha the merchant and acquire rare ingredientsHarvest sponge mushrooms that grow in the hills east of Khûtra.Administer the new salves to afflicted goats. They can be found outside the Elder Hall.Administer first experimental salve to diseased goatAdminister second experimental salve to a diseased goatAdminister third experimental salve to a diseased goatReturn to Heshra the herbalist in the Elder HallReturn to Heshra, the herbalist'I had hope that the old recipe would be successful, but this disease is unlike any I've seen before. Small wonder then, that the simple salve didn't work.

'Everything is not lost, however. Using the herbs you've brought and some of my own, I can create several new salves. We shouldn't give these to the villagers, no telling what effect they might have. Goats are close enough. Gather these ingredients from the merchant Ziriha, would you? I need several rare ingredients for the new salves.''Heshra sent you? Let me see the list. Yes, you're in luck, I happen to have everything he wants. Well, everything except this mushroom here. That you'll have to find on your own. I believe it grows in the ruins in the hills east of here, near the Mâkhda Khorbo.''Ahh, excellent quality lavender, as well. Thank you. Just a moment as I finish these....

'There! Three new salves. I admit these are a bit of a stab in the dark, but we don't have much to go on, do we?

'Will you give each of these salves to some of the local afflicted animals? If any of them improve, it could be a vital clue for us in fighting this dreadful disease.''The goat got better? The last salve? The calendula... of course, I know where this blight is coming from!

'Roshat! I know where the disease is coming from!'Determined to pillage the Free City before making their escape to the Shield Isles or more distant shores, the Heirsworn have taken to robbing merchants and raiding the markets of Umbar Baharbêl.Stolen goods can be found on ships crewed by Heirsworn Corsairs in the Sail-haven.

Eshmun has asked you to recover goods stolen from Umbari merchants and from the markets of Umbar Baharbêl.Recover stolen goods from the Heirsworn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have recovered many of the goods stolen by the Heirsworn in the Sail-haven. You should return to Eshmun.'I am troubled by Ahûd's account, ${PLAYER}.

'It does not take long for small thefts to grow into larger ones, especially if such crimes go unpunished. What troubles me most, though, is that the Heirsworn see no contradiction in their actions. Those who supported the Heirs of Castamir would claim to be the most loyal to Umbar, and yet, they would pillage their own city and set Umbari merchants on a course to ruin. Weak-minded cowards!

'These are desperate Men who have abandoned whatever principles they claimed to have under the leadership of the Scourge, and it falls to us to set things right. If Ahûd spoke true, it is likely the Heirsworn have loaded the stolen goods onto their ships here in the harbour.

'I ask that you recover them before the Heirsworn set off!''You have done well, ${PLAYER}.

'I will speak to the merchants of the Sail-haven and see that these goods are returned to them. Let this be a lesson to the Heirsworn that desperate plots do not bear fruit!'A strange man puts on a 'show' in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.A woman attending the show is trying to get your attention.

Speak to the woman across the way in the Upper Ward.Talk to Gûshida across the way from EzôtiGûshida has asked you to pretend to befriend Ezôti in order to gain information from him.

Speak to Ezôti in the Upper Ward.Talk to Ezôti in the Upper Ward'Come one, come all! Gaze upon the terror that is the Razor of Belfalas! A twisted creature from the very depths of the sea! Marvel at its frightening visage, and gasp at its every sudden movement!

'But fear not, for I, Ezôti, have tamed this beast.''Can you believe this nonsense? How foolish must these people be to believe his tales? That is a normal sea turtle he's painted and dressed in sea-weed! The poor creature looks miserable.'

She tears her gaze away from the spectacle and gives you an appraising look.

'I have an associate in Zîrar Tarka, Nekhama by name. She wrote to me of an adventurer who looks very much like you... an adventurer who deals honourably with others. Might you be the very one of whom Nekhama spoke?

'Can I rely upon your help to deal with this charlatan? That turtle is not the only creature he has paraded before the crowds he attracts. Before we deal with him, we must rescue his poor captives. Ezôti knows my face and is wary of me, but you might pretend to befriend this man, and then you could learn where he keeps his "pets."''Yes, yes, now that I am finished with my show, I have time to speak with you. Hmm? An assistant? Why yes, I could use an assistant....

'It is to be expected that someone as talented as myself would come to command the respect of others! How can I not have seen it before now? My good friend, it would be an honour and a privilege for you to work alongside me, and I have the very task upon which to set you.'The Lower Ward is bustling with chatter. The trap is set. Rumours abound that Khâshap plans to defend his honour before finally making his way to his master.Khâshap plans to confront the rumours head on by appearing before the Gut. Hadorion believes we should spring the trap now.

Meet Hadorion outside the Stonecliff Market in the Gut.Talk to Hadorion outside the Stonecliff MarketKhâshap has gathered his cohorts to clear his name. He must be stopped here and now.Crash Khâshap's AssemblyKhâshap has fled into the alleys of the Gut under the protection of his Jephai Corsairs. Find Hadorion at the entrance of the Stonecliff Market to discuss our next move.Talk to Hadorion at the Stonecliff Market entrance'Everything we've done up until now has led to this moment.

'The whispers around every corner are speaking of the trespasses of Khâshap.

'His first mistake, he has made it publicly known that he plans to address The Gut to clear his name. It's our chance to spring the trap and capture him for good.''We shall stop him here! Let us make haste!''It looks like the market is bustling. No doubt everyone has gathered to hear Khâshap's testimony regarding all of our allegations. Let us confront him once and for all!''We have no choice but to give chase. The Gut is filled with Jephai Corsairs meant to hinder us at every turn. We will have to pursue Khâshap into the depths of the Gut to wherever he flees. You must be prepared to deal with whatever the Jephai throw at us!'Driftwood asked you to leave him alone with his thoughts for a time, and you should respect his wishes.Driftwood asked you to give him some time to think in peace.Leave Driftwood alone with his thoughtsDriftwood has likely wandered the surrounds outside the city. You should look for him and see how he is feeling.Talk to Driftwood somewhere outside the city'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}, but I am not really in the mood for talking right now. Do you think you could give me some time to walk outside the city? I would like to be alone with my thoughts for now.''I need some time to be alone with my thoughts for now.''I have been thinking, ${PLAYER}... I think I may have been wrong.

'These past few months have been difficult. I abandoned my kingdom, my friends, and the woman I love, and I thought it was for their own good. I punished myself for the weakness I saw in myself, and I believed my wife and kingdom would be better off without relying on such a man as I am. Horn perished on the Pelennor, and Driftwood was born. But that death, and that birth... they changed nothing. I told myself it was right, but it was not.

'I am done with being alone. I think once our mission is concluded... I might be brave enough to see Nona again. Will you go with me when that time comes?'

You tell your friend that you will, and he smiles grimly.

'I do not think she will be happy to see me, ${PLAYER}. I may need you to convince me to go through with such a meeting, if my courage fails me. But for now I intend it.'Gwallang the Limlinn has come a long way from his home, and now is the time for him to either make a nest or give up on the idea.The fruit trees far to the south-east, by the farms outside the city, are of interest to Gwallang the Limlinn.Gwallang has arrived and hops around excitedly on a rock by the tree.The haystack to the north-east might provide the materials Gwallang will need to construct his nest.Collect a fistful of grass and hay from the haystack to the north-eastGwallang's potential nesting place is by the lone tree to the south-west of the haystack.Gwallang seems very pleased with his new nest.Talk to Gwallang by his new nestGwallang the Limlinn flutters briefly out of sight and then returns with a small item clutched in one of his feet. He drops it on the ground and you pick it up. Surprisingly, it appears to be Leafshade's whistle, which you had not known the Limlinn had brought with him.

He flies into the air and faces toward the distant fruit trees to the south-east, near the farms, and you understand that he wants you to find a good place for him to build a nest somewhere near those trees, and to call him with the whistle when you have found one. It will be a hike, because you cannot fly as the Limlinn does.You understand that he wants you to find a good place for him to build a nest somewhere near the fruit trees to the south-east, by the farms, and to call him with the whistle when you have found one.Gwallang hops around excitedly, and you know he likes your choice of location for his nest. Now he needs a fistful of grass or hay with which to build it, if you can find such a thing nearby.Gwallang hops around excitedly, and you know he likes your choice of location for his nest. Now he needs a fistful of grass or hay with which to build it, if you can find such a thing nearby.Gwallang waits expectantly for you to construct his nest for him.Gwallang flies in a grand circle around your head, chirping all the while. At last he lands safely in his nest and sings a trilling song, and you know that he enjoys the location and the smell of the sea-breeze. He seems very happy, but you imagine that his happiness is partially due to the knowledge that if the desire to explore the seas comes upon him again, he has ready access to any of the vessels docked in the City of the Corsairs, and any of them can take him on exciting adventures... should the mood strike him.

Gwallang chirps happily at you, and you know you have made a friend for life.Gimli and Legolas have begun their investigation into the Kindred of the Coins in the Sail-haven.Gimli asked you to speak with nearby dock-workers about the Kindred of the Coins.Gimli asked you to speak with nearby dock-workers about the Kindred of the Coins.Talk to dock-workers in the Sail-haven about the Kindred of the CoinsGimli asked you to speak with nearby dock-workers about the Kindred of the Coins.Talk to dock-workers in the Sail-haven about the Kindred of the CoinsLegolas stands in an alley in the Sail-haven.Talk to Legolas in the Sail-havenThe office of the harbour warden is in the tall blue tower out in the water south of the Sail-haven.Find the office of the Harbour Warden in the tall blue towerThe Harbour Warden's assistant is outside the tall blue tower located in the water south of the Sail-haven.Talk to Eshmun's assistant outside the tall blue tower south of the Sail-havenGimli and Legolas stand across the bridge from the Harbour Warden's tower.Talk to Gimli across the bridge in the Sail-havenTalk to Legolas across the bridge in the Sail-haven'I never thought I would say something like this, but these Corsair vessels simply do not compare to the Wave-hunter. Now that was a fine ship! Ah, what has happened to me, ${PLAYER}? I have been beside the water for too long! I will be dreaming about the gulls next, like poor Legolas! No, it is only a jest. I like good strong earth beneath my feet, and always will!

'Legolas and I have been trying to speak to the dock-workers in the Sail-haven, but they have not been very helpful to us. Perhaps you will have more good fortune than we have. If we could aid our mission here with suspicious glances, we would have the victory already and be halfway back to Gondor by now! I do not think these folk see many Longbeards here, and Elves are even more rare.''Legolas and I have been trying to speak to the dock-workers in the Sail-haven, but they have not been very helpful to us. Perhaps you will have more good fortune than we have. If we could aid our mission here with suspicious glances, we would have the victory already and be halfway back to Gondor by now! I do not think these folk see many Longbeards here, and Elves are even more rare.''There was a time when asking questions would get you brought to the temple on the hill by the Church of the All Seeing. Be glad those times are past, stranger.

'But I have nothing to say to you. Just be glad the Kindred of the Coins rules us now, and not the Empire of Ordâkh.''Legolas and I have been trying to speak to the dock-workers in the Sail-haven, but they have not been very helpful to us. Perhaps you will have more good fortune than we have. If we could aid our mission here with suspicious glances, we would have the victory already and be halfway back to Gondor by now! I do not think these folk see many Longbeards here, and Elves are even more rare.''Questions like this are like to get you in trouble, stranger, and sooner than you might be prepared for!''Have you had good fortune or ill so far, ${PLAYER}?''It is said "Wherever Elves and dwarves go, trouble is sure to follow."

'I am not saying I agree with it, but this is something you will hear in Umbar, if you keep your ears open. There are other whispers, as well: that Tumúldo Fierce-water got himself killed in Gondor, and his wife Nakási burned the White City to the ground to avenge him. I do not know the truth of it. Why, Tumúldo is probably still alive. He has disappeared before for weeks at a time, and I do not believe something just because I heard someone say it.

'The two of them are beloved by the folk of the Sail-haven, and have been ever since they helped us cast off the yoke of Ordâkh and the Church of the All Seeing. If something has happened to the two of them, Harbour Warden Eshmun will know of it. His office is in the tall blue tower to the south. I cannot guarantee he will speak to such as you... but you may find it valuable to try.''The people here do not know some of what we know, ${PLAYER}, and I recommend we keep it that way. If it became clear that some of the rumours they have dismissed are true... let us say it may become more difficult for us to accomplish our mission.

'We should speak with this Harbour Warden and learn what we can of Nakási's whereabouts. She knows you by sight, and will not have forgotten your face. She could make things very difficult for us.''We should speak with this Harbour Warden and learn what we can of Nakási's whereabouts. She knows you by sight, and will not have forgotten your face. She could make things very difficult for us.''Yes, what is it?''Yes, what is it? Eshmun is too busy to speak with just anyone, but I am his assistant and can aid you with any of your needs, so long as it is in the power of the Harbour Warden to grant it. What do you want?'

You ask the Harbour Warden's assistant what he knows about the ship of Nakási Wave-reaper. He seems about to answer quickly, and then catches himself. He thinks for a moment.

'Do you know something? I have not seen Nakási or Tumúldo in some time. There have been whispers about them down in the Sail-haven, but now that you mention it... it is rather strange that they have not come to see Eshmun in the past few days. Their ship is hard to miss! Usually it is docked right over there.

'Is that all? Good day to you, then.''I have not seen Nakási or Tumúldo in some time, actually.''Where has Nakási Wave-reaper gone? I do not like this, ${PLAYER}.

'They say Elves and dwarves cause trouble? I say vengeful widows are more likely to cause trouble than we are, and that trouble will be worse!''Gimli and I will keep our eyes open for some sign of Nakási Wave-reaper, ${PLAYER}. It is true that she may cause difficulty for us if she finds us before we locate the ones she took captive.

'We will not relax our vigilance.'Galengam has wasted no time and is ready to open his market stall in Umbar Baharbêl.Galengam has asked you to put up notices for his new stall to the south, within the Sail-haven.Post notices for Galengam's market stall (0/3)Galengam has asked you to put up notices for his new stall to the south, within the Sail-haven.Post the notices for Galengam's market stall (1/3)Galengam has asked you to put up notices for his new stall to the south, within the Sail-haven.A richly-dressed man has commented on the notice you just posted.Talk to the richly-dressed man staring at the notice you just postedThat man was Azagath Sea-shadow, the leader of the Kindred of the Coins!Wait for Azagath to leaveAzagath said he would visit Galengam's market stall to the north. Is Cruel Dancer nearby? If she kills her target now, you might never see Thorongil again!Galengam's market stall is to the north, in the Sail-haven.Talk to Galengam at his market stallGalengam's market stall is to the north, in the Sail-haven.Talk to Azagath Sea-shadow at Galengam's market stallAzagath Sea-shadow moves away and is lost in the crowd.Wait for Azagath to leaveGalengam's market stall is in the Sail-haven.Talk to Galengam at his market stall'The principles of buying and selling hold true no matter where you go in this world, ${PLAYER}. Have I not proved this to you already?

'But I will do so again! I give to you this stack of notices advertising the new market stall I have opened. If you post these around the Sail-haven for me, perhaps to the south, soon the customers will swarm my goods and you will have to save me from drowning... drowning in gold phârzi and silver gîmli, that is!''Post those notices around the Sail-haven for me, perhaps to the south, and soon the customers will swarm my goods and you will have to save me from drowning... drowning in gold phârzi and silver gîmli, that is!''Post those notices around the Sail-haven for me, perhaps to the south, and soon the customers will swarm my goods and you will have to save me from drowning... drowning in gold phârzi and silver gîmli, that is!''Post those notices around the Sail-haven for me, perhaps to the south, and soon the customers will swarm my goods and you will have to save me from drowning... drowning in gold phârzi and silver gîmli, that is!''Post those notices around the Sail-haven for me, perhaps to the south, and soon the customers will swarm my goods and you will have to save me from drowning... drowning in gold phârzi and silver gîmli, that is!''A man from Gondor has opened a new market stall in the Sail-haven?' the man asks you. As you tell him that is true, something about his manner strikes you as odd. You ask him if he has an interest in goods from Gondor, and he smiles.

'I do, my new friend. Why should that be unusual? We have had our differences, Umbar and Gondor, but my land desires only to maintain the stability it has earned. It has been different in Gondor, but it should not remain so, should it? My Kindred believes that peace between our lands is possible... if Gondor will meet us along that path. What did you say you were called?'

You answer with your name, and he responds with another charming smile.

'Enjoy your stay in Umbar Baharbêl, ${PLAYER}. Let Azagath Sea-shadow be the first to welcome you to his land. I will not be the last, I warrant. We are a friendly people, as you are certain to discover. Now I will go to see the goods your merchant friend has to sell.'

This man is Azagath, leader of the Kindred of the Coins!'I told you the customers would come here in droves, ${PLAYER}! None can resist my rare and valuable goods, or my name is not Galengam! The coin will be rolling in before this day's end!

'This man is my first customer, and...'

Galengam lowers his voice to a hushed whisper.

'...and see how finely he is dressed! This man has money to spend, and I will see to it that he spends most of it at my stall, and no others!''Please take your time, my wealthy friend! You are certain to see something you will want!''The overland route from Gondor has been treacherous of late, and few merchants have come to my city during the months following the conclusion of the war. Did you come by ship?'

Galengam happily chatters away, describing a dangerous voyage across the bay and a brief stay in the Shield Isles. Azagath nods sagely.

'You have done very well to make the journey up Umbarkhîl, for the Cape has had its own share of troubles of late: famine, blight, and unsavoury types among them. You are to be commended for bringing your wares this far. 

'I must be about my own business now, but allow me to extend the welcome I gave to ${PLAYER} to you as well, Galengam. I hope you will find the custom in my city to your liking! Farewell, my friends. Perhaps I will see you again.''My first customer was not a customer at all, for he did not buy anything. Disaster! No, I must try and stay positive. Perhaps he will tell his other wealthy friends. Why are you staring at me like this, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Galengam that the richly-dressed man was Azagath Sea-shadow, leader of the Kindred of the Coins, and that if Cruel Dancer had seen him out and about in the Sail-haven she would have likely killed him where he stood. Galengam frowns.

'We should be glad that she did not see him, then. That would have been quite bad for business! Really, ${PLAYER}, I think your priorities are somewhat askew. You will never make it as a merchant in this world if you have such trouble remembering what is important!'Gangur Farwend is frustrated to learn that the dwarf-quarter of the city, the Shoreward Stone, is shut to outsiders.Gangur Farwend is feeling frustrated.Wait to see what happensCarver Gírma has called for your attention.Talk to Carver Gírma outside the Shoreward StoneCarver Gírma offered to speak with you and Gangur Farwend at the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast.Find the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west of the Shoreward Stone, in the Fleet-fastGangur Farwend is eager to speak with Carver Gírma at the Old Bastion Inn.Talk to Gangur Farwend at the Old Bastion InnCarver Gírma is at the Old Bastion Inn.Talk to Carver Gírma at the Old Bastion InnGangur Farwend is at the Old Bastion Inn.Talk to Gangur Farwend at the Old Bastion Inn'I thought I would find the answers I sought in the dwarf-quarter of the city, but now I see that it is shut to outsiders! I have come so far to learn about this gemstone... must I be turned away by these Temámir as I was by Hámisar of Furukzahar? Interolerable, that's what this is!''What is it?''Listen to me, my friends. I understand you have come a long way to be here, and that you were hopeful to see inside the Shoreward Stone?

'Regretfully, I do not possess the authority to permit it. But if you will meet me by the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast, perhaps I can show you the hospitality you deserve? I do not want the good name of the Temámir besmirched in this fashion, if I might prevent it!''If you will meet me by the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast, perhaps I can show you the hospitality you deserve? I do not want the good name of the Temámir besmirched in this fashion, if I might prevent it!''Lead on, my friend.''Carver Gírma has agreed to answer any questions I might have, ${PLAYER}, and I must admit that this is a much finer reception than that I was given in Furukzahar! The Shoreward Stone may be off-limits to me, but if he gives me the answers I seek I will forgive that refusal, and harbour no hard feelings about the matter!

'Then let me ask the first question. I understand that one member of the Kindred of the Coins is a Dwarf of the Temámir who goes by the name Khôltekh. He wears a medallion of some kind, and this medallion sparkles with a most unusual shine, the like of which I have never seen in any jewel buried within the earth. What is this material, and where may it be found? I have never seen anything like it... not while awake, in any case!''I understand that one member of the Kindred of the Coins is a Dwarf of the Temámir who goes by the name Khôltekh. He wears a medallion of some kind, and this medallion sparkles with a most unusual shine, the like of which I have never seen in any jewel buried within the earth. What is this material, and where may it be found? I have never seen anything like it... not while awake, in any case!''You speak of Abâshal, my new friend! It can be no other! Some call it "sea-opal," but unlike other jewels the iridescence that gives it value can shine with every colour of the rainbow, and the forces involved in its shaping can cause even those to shift in truly remarkable fashion! You will typically find it cut into small jewels or fashioned into flat panels, if you find it at all; it is most rare, and its naturally-occurring form is brittle. Only the finest of stone-workers can mould it effectively. I blush to tell you I am one such craftsman. The knowledge is known only to few.

'The Empire of Ordâkh and the Church of the All Seeing that they brought with them to Umbar believed the ornamentation of Abâshal to be blasphemous; almost overnight as much of the jewel as could be salvaged was removed from the city and hidden away in secret vaults. When the temple collapsed at the moment of the Dark Lord's fall, it seemed clear the time of his church and the dominion of Ordâkh was ended. The Kindred of the Coins adopted Abâshal as a sign of not just wealth, but of defiance to foreign rule. You will not be surprised to learn that each of the Kindred's leaders possesses a medallion such as that you saw on Khôltekh's person, each one inlaid with a small piece of Abâshal.''It is my pleasure to speak of Abâshal! It has been a secret of my people, but as it grows in importance for Umbar I cannot avoid speaking of it to those who would hear more. That would not be right!''Abâshal, the sea-opal! At last I have a name to apply to the most beautiful gemstone on which I have ever laid my eyes!

'I will have many more questions for my new friend here, ${PLAYER}. Do not let me keep you! I am disappointed the Shoreward Stone must be closed to outsiders, but I am delighted to know that not all of the Temámir guard their tongues as closely as the others I have met!

'I will remain and speak with Carver Gírma for a time. Abâshal! I would learn as much about it as I can!'Sigileth overheard someone mention the name "Khâsha." Is it possible this could be the same Khâsha mentioned in the note you found in the Shield Isles?Sigileth wanted you to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for mention of Khâsha to the north, outside the Black Anchor Tavern in the Lower Ward.Sigileth wanted you to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for mention of Khâsha further north, outside the Cat's Grin Tavern in the Lower Ward.You think you have overheard the name "Khâsha" and should ask the Lower Ward resident for more information.Talk to the Lower Ward resident outside the Cat's Grin Tavern about KhâshaSomeone named Khâsha lives to the north-east, in the Lower Ward.Find the Khâsha who lives in the Lower WardKhâsha lives in the Lower Ward, north-east of the Cat's Grin Tavern.Talk to Khâsha in the Lower WardSigileth is helping you investigate the mystery of Khâsha in the Lower Ward.Talk to Sigileth in the Lower WardYou were told you might find Phêlex near the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.Find Phêlex outside the Guild Hall in the Lower WardPhêlex is by the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.Talk to Phêlex by the Guild Hall in the Lower WardSigileth has come with you to meet with Phêlex in the Lower Ward.Talk to Sigileth by the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward'When I became She Who Remained, and haunted the dungeons of Dol Guldur, I often heard voices and names from my past. I believed this was due to the dreadful nature of those midnight vaults or the terrible artifacts held within them... but it is possible it was... just me.

'I think it has happened again. While I walked here in the Lower Ward, I thought I heard the name "Khâsha." It may be this is a common Umbari name, but is it also possible someone may speak of the woman to whom the note we found in the Shield Isles was addressed?

'Will you go north and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for further mention of this name outside the Black Anchor Tavern? If we have learned the fate of Khâsha's lost love, should we not tell her of it?''Will you go north and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for further mention of this name outside the Black Anchor Tavern? If we have learned the fate of Khâsha's lost love, should we not tell her of it?''Will you go further to the north and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> outside the Cat's Grin Tavern for mention of this name? If we have learned the fate of Khâsha's lost love, should we not tell her of it?''Khâsha? Why yes, I do know a Khâsha! She is a friend of mine.

'She lives to the north-east, here in the Lower Ward, if you seek her.''Khâsha? Why yes, I do know a Khâsha! She is a friend of mine.

'She lives to the north-east, here in the Lower Ward, if you seek her.''Yes? I am called Khâsha. Can I help you with something?'

You tell Khâsha about the discovery you made on the Shield Isles of a bottle that contained a note addressed to someone with her name, and that if she is the Khâsha in question it properly belongs to her. She takes the note from you and studies it. When she finishes reading the message, she folds it up and puts it back inside the bottle. She looks at you carefully before she speaks again.

'My husband's name is Phêlex... and he is very much alive.''My husband's name is Phêlex... and he is very much alive.''Phêlex is alive? Those are surprising tidings, for it sounded from his note as if he was about to be slain by the Corsairs that boarded his ship. How did he manage to escape?''Phêlex is alive? It sounded from his note as if he was about to be slain by the Corsairs that boarded his ship. How did he manage to escape?''My husband's name is Phêlex... and he is very much alive. Find him by the Guild Hall and he will tell you the story... if you can be trusted.''Khâsha sent you to me? For what purpose? If I can help you I will, but I do not believe we have ever met before. I think I would remember it!'

You tell Phêlex that you found a bottle among the Shield Isles with a note inside it, and his mouth drops open with surprise. You show it to him and he reads it with interest.

'I never thought to see this again, stranger. You see... I wrote this note almost thirty years ago, when my ship was boarded by Corsairs. I did not think to escape alive, and indeed none others of the crew survived. But I... I am not proud of this, but I threw myself upon their mercy, and they took me into their crew. For more than twenty-five years I lived on that ship, raiding and pillaging, living the life of a Corsair, a brigand of the waves. I am not proud of it... but I was alive, and I intended to stay alive.

'I returned at last to my Khâsha. It would have been a short reunion, and bittersweet, had I not befriended a smuggler by the name of Tumúldo Fierce-water. He encouraged me not to sail with Balakhôr, one of the Heirs of Castamir, and in that way he saved my life, for all who followed Balakhôr to Gondor perished in the war. Ever since that day I have supported the Kindred of the Coins. Loyalty to any others, and the life of a Corsair, are both behind me now.

'I ask you to understand, stranger. I lived a criminal's life, yes, but it was the only life I had available to me. Tumúldo understood that, and so did Khâsha, and now I dedicate my life to serving each of them. It really brings me back, seeing that note in its bottle, but I was a different man when I wrote it, and I have become a different man than the man I became afterward.''I ask you to understand, stranger. I lived a criminal's life, yes, but it was the only life I had available to me. Tumúldo understood that, and so did Khâsha, and now I dedicate my life to serving each of them. It really brings me back, seeing that note in its bottle, but I was a different man when I wrote it, and I have become a different man than the man I became afterward.''It is not our place to judge this man. Have we not all done what we must to survive? She Who Remained is no stranger to need, and neither are you, ${PLAYER}. Will it be the same with my brother? Perhaps it will.

'I will continue searching for information that will help us with our mission, but it is good to know the conclusion to the mystery of the note we found in the bottle in the Shield Isles. I was curious, and now that curiosity has been satisfied.'Sirgon is reluctant to face his unpleasant history with Belondor of the Kindred, but he knows that he must.Sirgon has asked you to speak to residents of the Upper Ward so you may learn where Belondor now lives.Sirgon has asked you to speak to residents of the Upper Ward so you may learn where Belondor now lives.Talk to residents of the Upper Ward and learn where Belondor livesYou learned that Belondor's wife Mêshka was recently spotted on her way south, perhaps to one of the markets of the Upper Ward or in the Sail-haven.Talk to Mêshka at one of the markets in the Upper Ward or in the Sail-havenYou learned that Belondor's wife Mêshka was recently spotted on her way to one of the markets in the Upper Ward or the Sail-haven.Wait for Sirgon to arriveMêshka stares at Sirgon coldly.Talk to Mêshka at one of the markets in the Upper Ward or the Sail-havenMêshka hurries away.Wait for Mêshka to leaveMêshka and Belondor live to the north-east, in the Upper Ward.Meet with Mêshka at her home in the Upper WardMêshka and Belondor live in the north-eastern reaches of the Upper Ward.Talk to Mêshka at her home in the Upper WardSirgon seems to ignore the nearby guards, and keep his eyes on Mêshka.Talk to Sirgon outside Mêshka's home in the Upper WardMêshka and Belondor live in the north-eastern reaches of the Upper Ward.Talk to Mêshka at her home in the Upper WardMêshka and Belondor live in the north-eastern reaches of the Upper Ward.Wait for Mêshka to leaveSirgon stands outside the home of Mêshka and Belondor in the Upper Ward.Talk to Sirgon outside Mêshka's home in the Upper WardSirgon has been banished from the Upper Ward. You should speak with him to the south-west, in the Sail-haven.Talk to Sirgon to the south-west, outside the Upper Ward'I must confront my old friend Belondor, ${PLAYER}. I cannot put it off any longer, or I will never face it. No, do not seek to dissuade me! I am resolute. If you are a friend, you will aid me in this.

'The woman Belondor loved was a noblewoman of the city, and she was called Mêshka. I believe her home must be somewhere within the Upper Ward, and the folk within may tell us where she lives with Belondor. It is a gamble, of course: the two may dwell now within the Citadel of Winds, as befits a leader of the Kindred and his wife. But it might not be so, and folk of the Upper Ward may tell us.''The woman Belondor loved was a noblewoman of the city, and she was called Mêshka. I believe her home must be somewhere within the Upper Ward, and the folk within may tell us where she lives with Belondor. It is a gamble, of course: the two may dwell now within the Citadel of Winds, as befits a leader of the Kindred and his wife. But it might not be so, and folk of the Upper Ward may tell us.''I cannot help you. I am sorry.''I know nothing that will help you. You have my apologies.

'Now move on.''Belondor? Aye, he is the Master of Fleets, and when he is not at sea you will usually see him walking through the Fleet-fast, down by the shore. He is a good man, well-loved by his people. They say he was instrumental in organizing the overthrow of the Church of the All Seeing and the casting off of our Ordâkhai shackles... but that is just what I heard.

'I can tell you no more than this.''The woman Belondor loved was a noblewoman of the city, and she was called Mêshka. I believe her home must be somewhere within the Upper Ward, and the folk within may tell us where she lives with Belondor. It is a gamble, of course: the two may dwell now within the Citadel of Winds, as befits a leader of the Kindred and his wife. But it might not be so, and folk of the Upper Ward may tell us.''I have not seen Belondor today, but you just missed his wife Mêshka! She was heading south toward the Sail-haven. She may have been bound for the market of the Upper Ward that is on the way, or one of those in the Sail-haven, and if you hurry you might still catch her.''I have not seen Belondor today, but you just missed his wife Mêshka! She was heading south toward the Sail-haven. She may have been bound for the market of the Upper Ward that is on the way, or one of those in the Sail-haven, and if you hurry you might still catch her.''Yes, can I help you with something? What is it?''I do not care for your choice of friend, stranger.'

Mêshka addresses Sirgon with hatred in her voice.

'You are bold to come here, Sirgon of Gondor, but foolish. My husband suffered much at your hands and those of your master. For you to come here now...'

She falls silent.

'Not here. You will come to the home I share with Belondor, and there we will speak. It is the north-east, here in the Upper Ward.''I was not certain you would dare come here.''I was not certain you would dare come here. But since you have, you will hear my words before you and your friend die.'

Mêshka holds up her hand, signaling to her guards that they should await her command.

'For years after Sirgon drove my intended to his death, I lived a life of mourning. Believing he died at sea, I married, and it was a marriage of great happiness... at least until its ending, when my husband was seized by the Church of the All Seeing and burned alive, sacrificed to its Dark Lord.

'Why do I tell you this? I tell you this so you will know I am no wilting flower. I have been forged of tough steel, hardened by fire and by the salt-spray. There is a reason Belondor was my first intended, for he is the same: made durable by his experiences.

'For he did not perish beneath the waves when Sirgon pursued him through the rocks of Shedax Khîn. He survived as a castaway among the Shield Isles, sun-scorched and bitter, until he was taken aboard an Ordâkhai galley. In time he came to Umbar and served in the Fleet-fast, becoming one of its dedicated defenders, but the rule of the Heirs of Castamir rankled him.

'He began a friendship with Azagath the Sea-shadow and others who would come to supplant the Heirs. This Kindred of the Coins rules wisely and fairly, unlike either the Heirs of Castamir or the Steward of Gondor. What final words have you to say, Sirgon? Will you beg the forgiveness of my husband? I will give your words to him, if they please me.''What final words have you to say, Sirgon? Will you beg the forgiveness of my husband? I will give your words to him, if they please me.''I do not beg for forgiveness, Mêshka, for I know forgiveness is not deserved. If there is a message to give from me to your husband Belondor, it would be this: the wound I suffered the night we duelled after dinner was mortal. It was not a deep cut, not physically, but that wound has stayed with me since that night.

'I will not beg for forgiveness, or say that following the command of the Steward Denethor protects me from your reprisal. But know that I was forever changed by what I did to your husband Belondor, though I did not know it. But now I see that I was.

'I believed I missed the sea, and sailing, and traced my miseries to giving up that life. But I see now that it was my friendship with your husband that I truly missed, and the innocence of my youth before I committed the act by which I am now forever judged, and judge myself. If this is the wound that is to slay me now, I welcome it. I ask that you spare ${PLAYER}, who had no part in earning this, but I will not run from it.'Mêshka stares at Sirgon for a long moment... and then motions for her guards to stand down.

'We were all wounded on that night, Sirgon, and none of us knew how deeply. Your words ring true to me. I have spent years dwelling upon my hatred of you for the treatment suffered by Belondor at your hands, and at the hands of Gondor, and though that land is ruled now by a King and not a Steward, I believe in my heart that it would be no different if those events happened today and not long years ago. I did not forgive you then, and I do not forgive you now.'

Mêshka shakes her head, and for the first time today you see her smile.

'But men are weak, Sirgon. Know this: when the streets of Umbar Baharbêl filled with soldiers of Ordâkh and the Heirs of Castamir sailed with the Corsairs to Gondor, my husband Belondor weighed his hatred for Gondor against them... and he dispatched a ship for Pelargir, bearing a warning for you. I counselled against it, but it seems it did not matter, for the ship never arrived. No doubt it was sunk by the Heirs, and no warning ever came to you.

'My first husband was a good man, slain by Ordâkh. My second husband, Belondor, helped to overthrow those who killed my first, and he established a new order in Umbar, the Kindred of the Coins, which will usher in an era of prosperity and peace. If he has any fault, it is that he forgives too readily, and is pleased to forget the sins of Gondor if it means Umbar will have a fresh beginning; this is not a fault that I share! Therefore I give you your life, Sirgon, but I banish you from the Upper Ward. If I see you return I will order my guards to slay you where you stand. Now begone. Our business here is done.''I have... much to think about, ${PLAYER}.

'Let us leave the Upper Ward. I believe Mêshka was serious, and it is not safe for us to remain here.''I have... much to think about, ${PLAYER}.

'Let us leave the Upper Ward. I believe Mêshka was serious, and it is not safe for us to remain here.''I have spent our journey from the Shield Isles fearing a confrontation with Belondor, ${PLAYER}, but it seems I should have more feared his wife Mêshka! I warrant that she is more fierce than he is! I hope I have not endangered our own mission here. He will learn from her that I am in the city, that is true, but the personal nature of our conversation may mask that I came here at the command of King Elessar. Perhaps that will prove a helpful distraction for the Kindred of the Coins when the time comes to rescue the captives?

'I have much to think about. Thank you for helping me with this, my friend, and I am sorry to have brought you into danger. It could... it could have gone worse. But it did not. My apologies all the same, ${PLAYER}.

'I will continue seeking out information... just not within the Upper Ward of the city.'Nauriel has asked you to learn the guard assignments within the Fleet-fast as she prepares a plan to gain access to the Citadel of Winds.Nauriel asked you to linger by the clay jar to the south-west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.Linger by the clay jar to the south-west, in the Fleet-fastNauriel asked you to linger by a clay jar so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.Observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fastNauriel asked you to linger at a clay jar further to the west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.Linger by a clay jar further to the westNauriel asked you to linger by a clay jar so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.Observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fastNauriel asked you to linger by a clay jar further to the west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.Linger by the clay jar further to the westA suspicious guard of the Fleet-fast has called you over to him.Talk to the Fleet-fast guardNauriel waits for your report where you left her, to the north-east outside the Fleet-fast.Talk to Nauriel to the north-east, outside the Fleet-fast'The Fleet-fast is just beyond this gate, ${PLAYER}, and it seems to be guarded. Still, if we are to rescue my son we will need to penetrate its defences. Can I ask you to become my eyes in there, and for you to linger by certain of the clay jars that stand at major cross-roads within the Fleet-fast? When you do, be sure to note the number of guards and the patrol routes they take as they pass by.

'This information will help us craft a plan for making our way through the Fleet-fast when the time comes to rescue my Thorongil.''Can I ask you to become my eyes in there, and for you to linger by certain of the clay jars that stand at major cross-roads within the Fleet-fast? When you do, be sure to note the number of guards and the patrol routes they take as they pass by.

'This information will help us craft a plan for making our way through the Fleet-fast when the time comes to rescue my Thorongil.''You there! You cannot just linger like this in the Fleet-fast! Do not make me haul you away to the Gaol, for I will do it.'

You ask the guard if any visitors are ever permitted into the island citadel, and he laughs.

'Oh yes, folk are allowed inside! But those folk need to have a personal invitation, and you don't have the look of someone who's likely to have that. Unless Azagath invites you himself, I think you had better keep moving.'

You ask if Azagath ever comes out of the citadel, and the guard raises an eyebrow.

'He does, for he is beloved by the people and sometimes walks among them... but if any harm should befall him on one of these strolls I will look for you first, so you had better not try anything.

'No lingering in the Fleet-fast! I will not tell you again!''If any harm should befall Azagath on one of these strolls I will look for you first, so you had better not try anything. No lingering in the Fleet-fast! I will not tell you again!''From your report it appears the Fleet-fast is well-patrolled by guards loyal to the Kindred of the Coins, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps Cruel Dancer would be able to get inside the Citadel of Winds, but for the rest of us... I will need to think of some other way.

'An invitation by Azagath himself seems... unlikely. I will keep thinking.'Daxamat has learned that his good friend Itûr, currently held in the gaol in the Fleet-fast, may have volunteered for something unwise.A guard stands watch outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast.Talk to the Guard of the Gaol in the Fleet-fastDaxamat stands outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast.Talk to Daxamat outside the gaol in the Fleet-fastThe various match-ups for the arena can be found in the Tor-gardens.Examine the arena match-ups in the Tor-gardensYou should see how bad things may be for Itûr by speaking to people familiar with the arena in the Tor-gardens.Daxamat is outside the arena in the Tor-gardens, considering his friend's likely fate if he faces Rothog the Storm in battle.Talk to Daxamat outside the arena in the Tor-gardensOnly the guard outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast can save Itûr now.The Guard of the Gaol has gone inside to speak with Itûr.Wait for the guard to come back outsideThe Guard of the Gaol has gone inside to speak with Itûr.Wait for the guard to come back outsideThe guard of the gaol has finally come back outside.Talk to the Guard of the Gaol in the Fleet-fastDaxamat stands outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast.Talk to Daxamat outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast'I asked around the city for information about... ah... the matter that brought us here. But I learned something else!

'A good friend of mine, and Jajax's too, is locked up in the gaol here. His name is Itûr, and he got up to much the same things as my brother and me. When my brother and I returned to the city, it was Itûr who helped me escape from the notice of Khôltekh. It seems Itûr was not so fortunate.

'Do you think you might ask the guard of the gaol if Itûr is in good spirits, and when he may be released?''Do you think you might ask the guard of the gaol if Itûr is in good spirits, and when he may be released?''You are fortunate you spoke to me today, and so am I... for my coin-purse is feeling a little light. Who did you want to hear about?

'Itûr? Yes, I know this prisoner. He was a Corsair that managed to avoid sailing to the war with all the rest, which means he sails under lucky stars... but his good fortune must have run out, because he robbed the wrong person and ended up in the Fleet-fast Gaol.

'But he is not to be here long. I understand he has agreed to trial by combat in the Dahâl Huliz, the arena of the gladiators. If he is victorious there he will be released. If he is not... well, he will no longer take up any wall-space in the gaol, if you understand my meaning.''Itûr? Yes, I know this prisoner. He was a Corsair that managed to avoid sailing to the war with all the rest, which means he sails under lucky stars... but his good fortune must have run out, because he robbed the wrong person and ended up in the Fleet-fast gaol.

'But he is not to be here long. I understand he has agreed to trial by combat in the Dahâl Huliz, the arena of the gladiators. If he is victorious there he will be released. If he is not... well, he will no longer take up any wall-space in the gaol, if you understand my meaning.''Trial by combat? Itûr was no martial novice when I knew him, but he was never especially skilled in combat. I think his success in the arena will depend upon the Hûlaz against whom he is matched.

'Let us go to the arena and see if they have posted the match-ups for the upcoming contests.''Itûr was no martial novice when I knew him, but he was never especially skilled in combat. I think his success in the arena will depend upon the Hûlaz against whom he is matched.

'Let us go to the arena and see if they have posted the match-ups for the upcoming contests.''Oh no. If Itûr must face Rothog the Storm in the arena, he has no hope for survival!''Rothog the Storm? He is my favourite of all the Hûliz who fight in the arena! How can you not have heard of him?

'He is a mighty half-troll who began as a ferocious pit-fighter and rose to command a ship and crew of his own; the Crow-feeders, they were called, for a great mass of carrion birds followed in their wake. When Rothog crossed Balakhôr the Scourge, he found himself once again consigned to the arena, forced to fight his former crew and friends. Balakhôr thought he would die... but Rothog survived for more than a year, sometimes fighting as many as ten bouts in a week!

'He became the favoured champion of the people, and though Balakhôr commanded the master of the arena to execute the half-troll and be done with him, she refused the command. "Fight him yourself, if you wish so badly to see him dead!" I heard she answered.

'But before he could, Balakhôr sailed to his death in Gondor. And now Rothog belongs to the Kindred of the Coins... but he still fights in the arena, because he enjoys it!''Who are the two combatants about whom you speak? Rothog the Storm?

'You need not tell me the other name. Rothog never loses!''I was in the stands of the arena the night of the rebellion, when the Kindred of the Coins came to power and cast off the shackles of Ordâkh and the Church of the All Seeing, when the Heirs of Castamir lost their grip on Umbar.

'The ground shook, and we saw flames erupt away across the harbour. Rothog had been put to work fighting the few of his Crow-feeders that remained alive, as well as Men who had defied the Heirs. But that all changed when the whispered rumours became facts proclaimed: Mâkhda Khorbo, the temple of Sauron, had fallen. Rothog turned to face his opponents in the arena, and he spoke a single word. From where I stood I could not hear it, but as it was repeated by others it grew in volume and intensity, until the echo of that one word shook the very foundations of the arena.

'The word was "Hêlsi," and when the uprising of the Kindred was completed, Azagath Sea-shadow found Rothog the Storm sitting in the seats reserved for the Heirs of Castamir, surrounded by their half-eaten bodies. The half-troll did not join the Kindred of the Coins at once, but in time he did, and the people of the city love him. He still fights in the arena as often as he can, but now he does it for himself, and no other.

'What does "Hêlsi" mean? It means "Freedom."''My friend Itûr has to withdraw his request for trial by combat! There is no possible way he can best Rothog the Storm in the arena! Perhaps if he was matched against someone else he would have some hope of victory... but Rothog is the most dangerous Hûlaz to ever fight in the Tor-gardens! Itûr could not have drawn a shorter straw than this!

'Take my money-purse, ${PLAYER}, and hurry back to the gaol! There is no time to waste! We have to get the guard to allow Itûr to withdraw his request!''Hurry back to the gaol! There is no time to waste! We have to get the guard to allow Itûr to withdraw his request for trial by combat!''What's this? Back so soon?'

You press Daxamat's money-purse into the guard's hands and he tests its weight.

'You want me to see if your friend will withdraw his request for a trial by combat? That is not usually done, stranger. What makes you think he should?

'Ah. Rothog, eh? I understand now! I will see what I can do.''I ran as quickly as I could, but you still got here before me. I take it the guard is speaking to Itûr?''Here he is!''I am happy to report that your friend has withdrawn his request for trial by combat. He does not want to remain imprisoned... but when I told him he had drawn Rothog as an opponent, he was unable to speak. Through the stammering I was able to discern that he preferred remaining a guest of the gaol for awhile longer. "Until Rothog has retired," he may have said, but if I were a wagering man I would not expect that to happen any time soon. The half-troll Master of the Tor-gardens loves fighting that much, even when there is no need for it.

'Our business is now done. I thank you for the donation to the Fleet-fast.''Thank you for the... donation. The Fleet-fast will make use of it.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I know Itûr wanted to be set free, but I also know he would prefer to be alive than to face an unwinnable battle, and Rothog's reputation in the arena speaks for itself.

'I do hope you will take pity upon me if I need coin in the future. I gave the last of my money away as part of this endeavour, after all. It was worth it, was it not?

'Aye, surely it was worth it. But keep me in mind at meal-times, ${PLAYER}, or I will waste away to nothing.'Bruidis has taken on the responsibility for appraising the defences of the Fleet-fast, since her husband Rossaran's armour stands out too much for him to move about freely in this part of the city.Bruidis has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> the defences of the barracks, and the eastern and western ends of the bridge that spans the Fleet-fast.Bruidis is located by the south-eastern gate in the Fleet-fast.Talk to Bruidis by the south-eastern gate in the Fleet-fastRossaran is to the north of the Fleet-fast, in the Lower Ward.Talk to Rossaran in the Lower Ward'The Fleet-fast is well-defended, ${PLAYER}, and it will prove nearly impossible for one of us to walk around while remaining undetected. There are a number of places of interest that we should <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> for their military readiness. Can I ask you to conduct such an appraisal of the barracks and both the eastern and western ends of the bridge that spans the Fleet-fast?

'I would ask my husband Rossaran to do this... but his swan-knight armour makes him stand out even more than you do! He took only a dozen steps within before he was pulled aside by one of the guards. You are more likely to escape their notice.''The Fleet-fast is well-defended, ${PLAYER}, and it will prove nearly impossible for one of us to walk around while remaining undetected. There are a number of places of interest that we should <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> for their military readiness. Can I ask you to conduct such an appraisal of the barracks and both the eastern and western ends of the bridge that spans the Fleet-fast?

'I would ask my husband Rossaran to do this... but his swan-knight armour makes him stand out even more than you do! He took only a dozen steps within before he was pulled aside by one of the guards. You are more likely to escape their notice.''What have you learned of the defences within the Fleet-fast, ${PLAYER}?'

You give your report to Bruidis and she thinks it over.

'I see. If I believed most of the Corsairs' martial forces had perished at Pelargir, it seems that the Kindred of the Coins has rebuilt them enough to man the Fleet-fast, at least, very effectively. A frontal assault upon the Citadel of Winds is, in my opinion, out of the question.

'I could not utilize Rossaran effectively in the Fleet-fast, so I sent him to conduct his investigation within the Lower Ward. Seek him out in the Lower Ward to the north and find out what he learned while he was there.''I could not utilize Rossaran effectively in the Fleet-fast, so I sent him to conduct his investigation within the Lower Ward. Seek him out to the north and find out what he learned while he was there.''Bruidis suggested I find some garb that would allow me to pass undetected within the Fleet-fast, but I refused her; it was not easy, but I do not want to skulk about in secret! If my swan-knight armour is not welcome here, then neither am I!

'She was not pleased about it, but she sent me into the Lower Ward to learn what I could about our opponents. I cannot say that what I have discovered will be of use to us, but I was able to learn how the people feel about some of the various leaders among the Kindred of the Coins.

'Azagath and Belondor are both well-loved by the people, who give them a large portion of the credit for the Sea-stone Mutiny. That is the name given to the overthrow of the Heirs of Castamir and the Church of the All Seeing, when the oppressors of the Empire of Ordâkh were cast out of the city.

'Hármelak, the Golden Queen, is respected more than she is loved. She is one of the wealthiest people in Umbar, but the folk of the Lower Ward distrust her riches; many of them believe she is indifferent to their plight, and would not spend a single coin on their behalf.

'Rothog the Storm is considered a champion of the Lower Ward, for no one lives there who has not heard of his exploits in the arena, or of the manner with which he dispatched many of the Heirs of Castamir during the Mutiny. They love him... but they fear him as well.

'Of the others I was not able to learn very much. I hope this information is of as much use to you as the recounting of the Fleet-fast's defences are to Bruidis! We shall see, I suppose. I will keep looking, ${PLAYER}.'You found Driftwood wandering through the Upper Ward, wrestling with himself about a personal matter.Driftwood has asked to you meet you in the Tor-gardens.Meet up with Driftwood in the Tor-gardensDriftwood is by the arena in the Tor-gardens.Talk to Driftwood outside the arena in the Tor-gardensDriftwood asked you to speak with visitors to the Tor-gardens about what the future might hold for such a man as he.Driftwood is by the arena in the Tor-gardens.Talk to Driftwood in the Tor-gardens'I do not know why I came to the Upper Ward; something compelled my feet to bring me hither. I find myself eyeing the upper stories of the manors and mansions of this district, and wondering if the windows might be unlocked, the balcony doors unbarred. It is a remnant of my old life that brings these thoughts to me, a relic of the brigand once I was.

'I should not remain in this district. It is not safe for me to stay here. Let us continue on to the Tor-gardens, ${PLAYER}. There we will speak, and I will find it easier to resist my more dangerous impulses.''I should not remain in this district. It is not safe for me to stay here. Let us continue on to the Tor-gardens, ${PLAYER}. There we will speak, and I will find it easier to resist my more dangerous impulses.''This place is better for me.''Old habits are the hardest to lose, ${PLAYER}, and in another life I preyed upon the wealthy merchants and nobles who sailed upon the River Anduin. I relieved them of their wealth, at least, and in some cases of their lives as well. Even today I feel the pull of that life, though I have spent the years since then seeking to leave it behind me.

'What might have happened had I succumbed to that pull again? Had I climbed through one of the windows of a mansion in the Upper Ward and stolen the valuables I found within, would I be seized by the guards? Would I have been brought to yon building, there to fight and die for my crime? Would that have been right?

'I am curious about this, friend. Ask some of the folk nearby what might have happened to me in that case. I am interested to know.''What might have happened had I succumbed to that pull again? Had I climbed through one of the windows of a mansion in the Upper Ward and stolen the valuables I found within, would I be seized by the guards? Would I have been brought to yon building, there to fight and die for my crime? Would that have been right?

'I am curious about this, friend. Ask some of the folk nearby what might have happened to me in that case. I am interested to know.''This is most unusual. You want to know what might happen to a friend of yours that commits a crime, such as theft or burglary? If he is not caught by the guards and slain at once, it is true that he might request a trial by combat in the arena, where he would need to face one of the Hûliz. These are the gladiators who make their living in the arena by dealing death, and unless your friend is very skilled, he is not like to survive it.

'His chances decrease to near zero if he has the misfortune of drawing Rothog the Storm for an opponent. He is the deadliest fighter I have ever seen!

'I would advise your friend not to steal. This ending, to me, seems most likely: death for him, and for any who aid him!''You ask what might happen to a friend of yours that steals? I can answer this very simply for you. Is he of the nobility? For if he is a nobleman, I say he is likely to escape judgement. If he is from the Lower Ward, I do not like his chances. Consider Hármelak, the Golden Queen! Her family has always been wealthy, but you cannot tell me that all of her dealings are and have ever been aboveboard!

'What is your friend's station in life? That will determine not only if he can commit his theft and live, but also how rich a lifestyle he will be able to maintain... and the duration of it!''You want to know what will happen to your friend if he begins a life of theft and burglary? I do not have enough information to answer this for you. The reason? I do not know how skilled he is at this trade!

'Yes, I call it a trade. If you speak to others about this matter, they will tell you he will be caught or killed by the guards, or be sent to face Rothog the Storm in the arena, or fall to his death from an upper balcony when he seeks to escape notice. But I say differently.

'I think if he is well-practiced at the art of thievery, he might well escape and live a long and full life feasting upon the fruits of his labours! It can be so in other areas... why not burglary as well?''What did visitors to this place have to say about my future, ${PLAYER}? To what ending do they believe I will come to when I breathe my last?'

You recount the words of the folk with whom you spoke, and Driftwood listens intently.

'They are all right, my friend, and they are all wrong. How can this be so? It is because you asked them what would happen if I gave in to my thieving impulses and returned to my past life, and I do not doubt that I would arrive at one of those endings if I did.

'But it is possible for a man to change, even one such as I am. I strive every day to prove it. It is not easy. But it is worth it.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. None of those endings are mine today... and for today that is enough.'Elladan and Elrohir were approached by a man in the Lower Ward who claimed to have information for them, but the brothers are not certain he can be trusted.Elladan is by the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward.Talk to Elladan at the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower WardElladan and Elrohir have decided to investigate the man's information, meeting him beside one of the farms outside the city.Talk to Elrohir by one of the farms to the east, outside the cityElladan and Elrohir agreed to meet you back outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward of the city.Talk to Elrohir outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower WardTalk to Elladan outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward'My brother and I were walking through the Lower Ward of the city when a man approached us and said he had information for the two of us. I do not know if he speaks the truth, but we should hear what he has to say. If we are watched, we will be watchful too. It is the wise course, is it not?''I do not know if this man speaks the truth, but we should hear what he has to say, should we not?''I told Elrohir I do not trust this man... but that is not enough for us to refuse him.

'I suspect he would need many men indeed to get the better of us. Will you join us when we go to speak with him? He suggested a location far to the east, beside one of the farms outside the city.''Will you join us when we go to speak with this man? He suggested a location far to the east, beside one of the farms outside the city.''We are about to see if this is a trap, ${PLAYER}. But what is of most interest to me is learning if the predator is actually the prey, as I suspect may be the case. These Men likely do not have much occasion to see Elves, after all.''The Heirs of Castamir, in league with the Empire of Ordâkh and the Church of the All Seeing, ruled this city for many years... but now their star has fallen so low that their supporters consist mainly of brigands and lawless toughs. They are no match for such as we are, ${PLAYER}, but they do not yet understand it.''So it was a trap, but it turns out it was a trap in which the ones who set it were the first caught. That is a pity for them, but perhaps it will teach other supporters of the Heirs of Castamir not to cause trouble for us in the days to come.

'Their mention of "Elves from the oasis" is very interesting! I have not heard of Elves living across the southern desert before. I would learn more about them, and I am sure Elrohir feels similarly! It is most intriguing.'In the aftermath of the Sea-stone Munity, the waters of the Sail-haven have been befouled by filth and the corpses of those found to still harbour loyalties to the Heirs of Castamir.Disgusting harbour-filth and the bodies of Heirsworn traitors can be found in the waters of the Sail-haven.

Eshmun has asked you to help cleanse the waters of the Sail-haven by clearing it of filth and the bodies of Heirsworn traitors.Remove disgusting harbour-filth from the waters of the Sail-haven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Remove Heirsworn traitors from the waters of the Sail-haven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have done a great deal to cleanse the waters of the Sail-haven. You should return to Eshmun.Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower'It is a great shame of mine that the harbour has been left in such disarray since the Mutiny's end. There are vast patches of filth floating in the water, and it seems that almost every morning, I wake to the news that another Heirsworn traitor has 'mysteriously' found their way into the waters of the Sail-haven.

'As Captain of the Haven, I have many duties that demand my attention, and as obvious a problem as this is, I simply have not had the time or men to spare to see to it. I know what I ask of you, so I will see to it that you are well-compensated for this task.

'Will you help me to cleanse the harbour?''It is unpleasant work, but I am afraid it is necessary, especially in the wake of the Mutiny.

'It will not be long before the rest of the Heirsworn are routed or slain, but I only hope that some of my kinsmen will give more careful thought to where they dispose of them. After all, these are our waters!'You have healed Khûtra. Now Roshat is throwing a feast, and you are the guest of honour. Don't be late!Pick up wheat from Gadir, the farmer. He can be found along the road to the Elder Hall.Pick up sheaf of wheat from Gadir, the farmerPick up jugs of khôrob from Ziriha, the merchant. She can be found by the fishing pier.Pick up jugs of khôrob from Ziriha, the merchantPick up fish from Umaris, the fisher. She can be found by the fishing pier.Pick up fish from Umaris, the fisherDeliver ingredients to Ekhmun, the cook. He can be found near Ziriha.Return to Elder Roshat in the centre of Khûtra.Talk to Elder Roshat about the feast'I am astounded. I misjudged you, and perhaps I misjudged the other travellers venturing through here. You are a boon to Khûtra, and I wish I had seen it sooner.

'You must let this foolish old man set accounts right. Come! We will prepare a feast in your honour!

'The only thing I ask of you is to help us with the preparations! Would you mind collecting some of the food? Gadir, down the road, has some wheat as a start.''Here, take this wheat for the feast. You collected it anyway. It is only right that it goes to the feast. Sincerely, thank you for everything you've done.''Here, take all the khôrob I have left. You've earned it.''Here we are. The first healthy fish we've caught in a month. Take them, with our thanks. You'll want to bring the ingredients to Ekhmun, the cook - he's just over there, talking to Ziriha.''That's a welcome sight. More food than I've seen in a fair few nights. Thanks for gathering all this! Leave it to me - I'll have everything ready before you can spit.''Come on, come on! Down to the Elder Hall! Everything's been laid out, time to try the best food Khûtra has to offer.'You have healed Khûtra. Now Roshat is throwing a feast, and you are the guest of honour. Don't be late!Take your place as the guest of honour where the feast has been laid out.Take your place as the guest of honourListen to Elder Roshat, then cheer with him.Listen to Elder Roshat, then cheer with himZuhûr just wants apricots. Is that too much to ask?Zuhûr asked you to speak with merchants at the Waterway Market and find out if anyone has any apricots for her to purchase.Zuhûr is at the Waterway Market, looking for apricots.Talk to Zuhûr at the Waterway MarketThe Dawn Market is located east of the city walls.Zuhûr is on a bench by the Waterway Market in the Lower Ward.'I am looking to buy apricots, which is usually a very easy task here in the Waterway Market. But I have not had any luck so far today! Will you help me find a market stall with the fruits for sale?''Will you help me find a market stall with the fruits for sale?''Apricots? Sadly, while I usually carry these items, I am completely out of them today. Can I interest you in some oysters, or some of my delicious beans? They were picked just this morning, you know.''Apricots? I do wish I had some of those to sell you, but sadly I do not.

'These are not the same taste, but I recommend you purchase some of my millet, rice, or chickpeas. They will form the basis of a delicious meal, and if you do happen to find apricots here in the Waterway Market, the fruits will be a welcome addition... but not the main course.''Apricots? No.

'Dates, figs, and grapes, however? Yes and yes and yes! Why not purchase some of those instead? They are just as good, I assure you!''I never have apricots for sale. I am sorry.

'The reason for that is simple: any that come into my possession are eaten immediately! I love the taste of them, you know, and buy them for myself at every opportunity. I tend to clear out the full supply of the fruits here at the Waterway Market most weeks.

'I apologize.''No apricots for sale anywhere?

'I am not ready to give up. Can you check at the Dawn Market, outside the city? It is located outside the eastern wall of Umbar Baharbêl, but it is too far for me to walk in these shoes. Will you take this money and purchase apricots for me if there are any to be found there?

'I need to find someplace to sit down while you do this. My feet are killing me.''I am not ready to give up. Can you check at the Dawn Market, outside the city? It is located outside the eastern wall of Umbar Baharbêl, but it is too far for me to walk in these shoes. Will you take this money and purchase apricots for me if there are any to be found there?''Apricots? Of course! What sort of merchant would I be if I did not have such things? They were not picked today, so I hope you can excuse some light bruising, but they were plucked from their trees just yesterday. I still have them because not everyone with a taste for apricots always wants to make the journey outside the city to the Dawn Market. There is a vendor in the Waterway Market who visits my stall every few days... you are fortunate she has not yet appeared today!''May those apricots bring you joy... and may they bring you back to me to buy more of them when they are gone!''You found me some apricots at the Dawn Market? I am pleased, really. Do not mistake me! But I have done so much walking around today, and I am so very tired. I do not really want the apricots anymore. Now what I want is new shoes!

'But no, the money I might have spent on shoes went to apricots. I might as well enjoy them. Thank you for your help, my friend. I think I will just sit here and enjoy the fruits of your labour.'Despite the success of the Sea-stone Mutiny, several captains still loyal to Balakhôr the Scourge have managed to entrench themselves in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Medêshi, Grizagâr, Jakham, Krûha, Sikaru, and Akhâd can be found throughout the Sail-haven, either upon the decks of their ships in the harbour or lurking at one of the local taverns.

Eshmun has asked you to find, confront, and defeat Balakhôr the Scourge's loyal captains in Umbar Baharbêl.Confront AkhâdConfront SikaruConfront KrûhaConfront JakhamConfront GrizagârConfront MedêshiEshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have defeated all of Balakhôr the Scourge's loyal captains in the Sail-haven. You should return to Eshmun.Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower'After you returned, I sent my guards to investigate the rumours Zemirah spoke of, but unfortunately, the situation is far worse than I expected.

'From what I have learned, six of Balakhôr's captains remain in the Sail-haven: Medêshi, Grizagâr, Jakham, Krûha, Sikaru, and Akhâd. How they all managed to survive the Mutiny is a mystery to me, but the Kindred of the Coins cannot abide traitors in Umbar Baharbêl. I am told that some of them can be found on the decks of their ships at the edges of the harbour, but others may still haunt the local taverns.

'Need I tell you what must be done, ${PLAYER}? Confront them, and slay them to the last!''It is done? Excellent!

'It will take more than the Mutiny and time to wash away the stain of Balakhôr the Scourge, but you have done well to rid the Free City of his few remaining captains.

'May their names and deeds be forgotten!''Oh? One of the old man's lackeys finally grew a spine?'

Akhâd sneers at you and slams his mug onto the table. After a tense moment, he barks at one of the tavern-workers.

'Another round when this is done!''What is this? You think I answer to you or that old fool, Eshmun?'

Sikaru glares at you.

'No, you were dead the moment you stepped onto my ship!''YOU! I know you!'

Krûha stares at you as if he has seen a ghost.

'I was at Pelargir, ${CLASS}, but you don't remember me, do you? I know you serve the King of Gondor—that Elf-loving pretender! If you think the people of Umbar hate me, just wait until they learn who you really are!''Who are you to speak to me? Some foreign puppet of the Kindred?'

Jakham smirks at you.

'I should cut your tongue from your mouth!''I've lost, have I? Balakhôr is dead? You know nothing, ${CLASS}, and I will not be moved. Not by Eshmun, and certainly not by you!'

Grizagâr scowls at you, and chuckles to himself.

'The Sail-haven is ours by right!''You dare threaten me? I've killed better than you for far less, ${CLASS}.'

Medêshi glares at you and gestures to the others at the tavern.

'Let these fools relish their so-called victory because when the Scourge returns—Balakhôr or no—we shall have Umbar for our own!'Two wine shop owners suspect each other of dishonest business practices.Akhmâra asked you to investigate her business rival.

His shop, The Drowned Prince, can be found in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Read the manifest at The Drowned Prince in the Sail-havenThere is nothing suspicious in The Drowned Prince's latest shipping manifest. Perhaps a conversation with its proprietor would yield some clues.

The proprietor, Mutâz, can be found outside his shop in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Mutâz at the Drowned Prince in the Sail-havenMutâz said that Akhmâra is the one guilty of underhanded business practices and has asked you to investigate her.

Search for clues around Akhmâra's shop, The Full Belly, in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Read the manifest at The Full Belly in the Upper WardThe Full Belly's import manifest looks shockingly similar to its rival's.

Akhmâra can be found outside her wine shop, the Full Belly, in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Akhmâra at The Full Belly in the Upper WardAkhmâra plans to confront her brother, Mutâz, at his shop.

Go to The Drowned Prince in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl to witness the confrontation.Talk to Akhmâra at The Drowned Prince in the Sail-haven'He is cheating! I know he is cheating! I don't know how he is cheating but I will figure it out. Or maybe you will.

'I am Akhmâra, owner of the finest wine shop in town, and my rival Mutâz is a liar and a cheat and a good-for-nothing! Please, kind stranger, help me uncover the nature of his misdeeds and I will repay you.'In hasty, chunky handwriting, you read the following:

1 cask Mereham Rose 3014
1 cask Bergraw White 3012
2 casks Winbury Red 3013
1 cask Iáphel Red 3014

All goods paid for
- Captain Nishak'How is business? It is wonderful! Wine is equally welcome at celebrations and commiserations, and there is no shortage of either in the city. It... could be better, though. My rival, Zâkh Okhon, the Full Belly, is stealing some of my customers away. Its owner is a liar and a cheat and a good-for-nothing! I know she is hiding something.

'I heard a rumour that she waters down her wine. I implore you on behalf of all honest businesspeople and wine-lovers everywhere... find out what she's doing, and how she's doing it!'In familiar, chunky handwriting, you read the following:

1 cask Mereham Rose 3014
2 cask Bergraw White 3012
1 casks Winbury Red 3013
2 cask Iáphel Red 3014

All goods paid for
- Captain Nishak'What do you think you are doing? I asked you to investigate The Drowned Prince, not my own shop! Now tell me, what tricks is my dolt of a brother employing?'

Now that you think of it, she and Mutâz do share a resemblance.

'Yes, we are twins! What of it? Our parents left us these shops after their passing. He and I could not agree on how to run them so we each took one shop for ourselves, and I swear I will not rest until I prove to him that my ways are better!'

You share that both the twins are ordering the same goods from the same suppliers in almost the same quantities.

'What? That is absurd. His wine tastes like swill, and I sell only the finest vintages! That is IT! I am going down there myself and getting to the bottom of this!''You know, if we place one large order with Nishak, we could negotiate for a better price than if we ordered separately...' Mutâz says. 'I wonder what other costs we could trim if we worked together?' Akhmâra asks. Finally the two notice you have arrived.

'Oh, your job is done. My brother and I have business to discuss. Come see me if you need to buy wine!'

'No, come see me!' Mutâz interjects.

Akhmâra wheels on him. 'What? No. Come to me. I met you first and my wine tastes better because it is not kept as hot as the roof-tops at noon.'

'I do not keep my wine too hot!' Mutâz protests.

You have your reward. Perhaps you should escape this argument before you get drawn into it any further.Elder Roshat has tasked you with going into the hills to the east, near the Mâkhda Khorbo, to a cliff where purple honeywort grows. Heshra is convinced that is where the disease originates. Find the source of the disease and seal it up if you can.Talk to Elder Roshat in the Elder Hall.Talk to Elder RoshatElder Roshat has asked you to go to the hills east of Khûtra, to the cliffs facing south near the ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo and investigate the source of the disease.Investigate the southern cliffs near the Mâkhda KhorboA noxious blight is seeping from these broken stones. Patch up the stones and seal the wellspring!Patch the stones seeping noxious blight (${NUMBER}/3)Talk to Heshra, the herbalist in the Elder Hall.Talk to Heshra, the herbalist'Stranger, you said you wanted to aid us. If ever an oath was to be uttered, now is the time. If you are who you say you are, and you can help us, your name will be sung through the halls of Khûtra long after you've passed through here.

'Will you help us? Will you help us heal Khûtra?''The blight is sealed! That is welcome news indeed! That will dry the source of evil coming into Khûtra. Now we just need to heal Khûtra's afflicted. Hurry, we've not a moment to lose!''This terrible disease must be coming from the ruins of the Mâkhda Khorbo. Go to the hills east of here, to the ruins. The air there is thick with malevolence, and the dead roam free. I am sure that this must be the source of all our trouble. Please, investigate the ruins. Find and seal up the source of this malady!'A memorial to the victims of the Church of the All-Seeing could use a cleaning.A young man is cleaning a memorial by himself. Help him.

The memorial can be found in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Clean the first dirty spotA young man is cleaning a memorial by himself. Help him.

The memorial can be found in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Clean the second dirty spotA young man is cleaning a memorial by himself. Help him.

The memorial can be found in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Clean the third dirty spotYou have helped a young man clean the memorial. He seems ready to speak to you.

Speak to Nadiph in the Upper Ward.Talk to Nadiph by the memorialNadiph expressed a desire for help in cleaning the memorial. Perhaps you could secure pledges of assistance from people around the plaza.

Talk to passersby around the plaza in the Upper Ward.Talk to the shopkeep in the Grand MarketTalk to the man running errandsTalk to the idle guardsmanTalk to the energetic youthYou were unable to secure regular assistance from anyone nearby, but perhaps it would cheer up Nadiph to know you tried.

Return to Nadiph in the Upper Ward.Look for NadiphA young man stands in front of a memorial to those murdered by the Church of the All-Seeing. He seems to be cleaning it. Perhaps you should join him in his work.'I appreciate your help, stranger. This memorial is meant to honour those murdered by the Church of the All-Seeing, but as you can see, most of the folk here pretend it does not exist. I do not fault them for that! The memory of what happened here can be unbearably painful. I wish only that I had some help in keeping it clean on days when you are not nearby and offer your help.''I see good Nadiph working so hard every day. I would help him, but I must care for my shop and cannot take the time away.''That is a nice thing for that man to do, but I am here from the Lower Ward. Even if I wanted to help, I could not make the journey every day.''I cannot so easily abandon my post, but I will do what I can when I can.

'Whenever that may be. I promise nothing to you, you understand.''I do not think so. Sorry.

'Perhaps someone else will do it? I cannot be your only choice for this chore, surely?'When you return, Nadiph is nowhere to be found, but there is a fresh stain atop the memorial. You wipe it clean with a scrap of cloth left behind for that purpose.

You could not fix Nadiph's problem, but you tried to help. That will have to be enough this time.Appointed as Captain of the Haven by the Kindred of the Coins, Eshmun seeks to preserve the peace in the Sail-haven and make safe the Free City of Umbar Baharbêl.Zemirah is at the Sailors' Guild-hall, Ahûd is at the northern shipyard, and Râmax is at the southern shipyard.

Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, wants to assess the threat of the Heirsworn following the Sea-stone Mutiny.Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.

You have spoken to Zemirah and Ahûd, but Râmax was slain by the Heirsworn in the Sail-haven. You should report to Eshmun.Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower'Before I took up this station, the Captain of the Haven and many of his harbour-guards were loyal to Balakhôr the Scourge and the Heirs of Castamir. Nearly all of them were slain in the Mutiny, but as you might imagine, having fewer men has made my efforts to rebuild the Sail-haven far more difficult—and I will not be made to look the fool when Tumúldo Fierce-water returns from his voyage!

'Rumours abound of the Heirsworn and their plots in Umbar, but aside from the few that hurl insults from the decks of their ships in the harbour, I see no greater plan at play in the Free City. I only know what I have seen with my own eyes, and to speak plainly, I am not the young sailor I once was!

'To that end, I would ask that you speak to Zemirah, the new master of the sailors' guild, as well as Ahûd and Râmax, the foremen of the ship-yards in the Sail-haven. If there is an imminent threat to Umbar, they will know of it.''Greetings!

'Have you come seeking to join the sailors' guild? I must admit, you do not look the sort at a glance, but our membership is... thinner than it was before the Mutiny. If not for that reason, then speak quickly, for my time is not idly spent. What do you need?'

You inform Zemirah that Eshmun hopes to assess the threat of the lingering Heirsworn in the Sail-haven.

'The Heirs of Castamir had many supporters in Umbar and a great many of them were members of the sailors' guild. In fact, my predecessor was one of Balakhôr the Scourge's most ardent followers, but I digress. I have done what was necessary to put my house in order, if you understand my meaning, but it is no secret that the Scourge's loyal captains still maintain a foothold in the Haven. From what I have heard, they find shelter on the decks of their ships, cowering behind their crews, or in the taverns of the Sail-haven. That is all I know, ${PLAYER}.''Yes?'

You tell Ahûd that Eshmun hopes to assess the threat of the lingering Heirsworn in the Sail-haven. In addition, he wishes to learn if they have troubled the work at the ship-yards of Umbar Baharbêl. Ahûd nods and smirks.

'Tumúldo chose wisely, I think. Age has not slowed Eshmun in the least, and though he might seem a kindly old man at first glance, he is every bit as vicious as his predecessor. The only difference between the two of them is that Eshmun fights for the people of the Free City... and, of course, that he did not end up in the waters of the harbour with a spear through his back.

'Nevertheless, I can say with certainty that none of the Heirsworn have troubled this ship-yard. I have only employed shipmen from the sailors' guild since the Mutiny, and even so, I have conducted routine inspections of these ships at every stage of their construction. I have seen the Heirsworn cowering at their ships at the edges of the harbour, but aside from petty theft and harassment, they pose little threat to our work here in the Sail-haven. It seems they mean to pillage the city and scatter like rats before the Kindred can slay the last of them. I say let them! Death would be a kindness for them—let them suffer their shame in exile!''Râmax has been murdered? This is intolerable!'

Eshmun's demeanour darkens.

'He was a good man. None who survived the Mutiny should have met with such an end, but still those craven louts cut him down for the crime of helping to rebuild the Sail-haven. I trust that Zemirah and Ahûd were confident in their judgements, but such a violent action taken against the people of Umbar—against the Kindred of the Coins—cannot go unanswered!'Brûdo is catering a gathering of Umbar's elite and would benefit from an extra set of hands, after you wash them of course.Renowned head-cook Brûdo needs help catering a party for Umbar's elite. Start by washing your hands.

A hand-washing basin can be found near Brûdo.Wash your hands in the wash-basinNow that your hands are clean, speak to Brûdo to receive instructions.

Brûdo can be found at the bath-house in the Upper Ward.Talk to BrûdoNow that your hands are clean, pick up the first tray of food and take it to table three.

The tray of food is on the table next to Brûdo.Carry the tray of food to table threeYou have made your first delivery. Speak to Brûdo to learn what to do next.

Brûdo can be found at the bath-house in the Upper Ward.Talk to BrûdoBrûdo told you to clean the dishes off tables four, five, six, and seven, near the dancing man.

Brûdo still needs your help in the Upper Ward.Clean up dirty dishes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have gathered the soiled plates. Bring them to Brûdo.

Brûdo can be found in the bath-house of the Upper Ward.Brûdo has asked you to deliver a special semolina cake to a guest.

Brûdo can be found at the bath-house in the Upper Ward.Deliver the semolina cake to the guestYou have completed all your tasks and should speak to Brûdo.

Brûdo can be found at the bath-house in the Upper Ward.Talk to Brûdo'You there! Can you carry plates and trays of food without spilling them everywhere? Good. I need help. One of my workers is sick today, but this party must be a success. The elite of the city are gathered here and I will not give any of them an excuse to complain about my food or my service! Wash your hands and take this tray of food to table three.''Good. Your hands are clean. I wish we had time to do something about your clothing, but we do not. Pick up that tray of meat and bring it to table three. It is the one on the other side of the fountain.

'Those... those... carnivores! They have been hounding me for their meal!''Next, I need you to clean off the dishes from tables four, five, six, and seven. Those tables are near the man in green, with the purple sash... you see him? He is over there, making a fool of himself with his silly dancing. There is no music! What is he dancing to? The tune is of his own making... and I say it is his own madness!'Brûdo takes the dirty dishes from you and sets them down on the table.

'I have one last task for you. One of the guests... it is his birthday! I wish I had known in advance so I could have prepared something special, but this semolina cake will have to do. He is the merchant at the long table just to the east! Please bring it to him. Tell him it is a gift from the chef.''You performed better than I expected! If your pockets are ever light, come to me. I will find more work for you. It is always somebody's birthday after all!'

He smirks.

'The regular fellow will likely not be sick tomorrow, I suppose. But still, what I said is true. You will be welcome whenever it is someone's birthday.'Kâsho has challenged you to execute his exercise regimen: making several circuits around the amphitheatre.Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (0/3)Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (0/3)Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (0/3)Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (1/3)Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (1/3)Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (1/3)Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (2/3)Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (2/3)Kâsho suggested that you make several circuits around the amphitheatre.Run a circuit around the amphitheatre (2/3)Kâsho is at the amphitheatre outside the city.Talk to Kâsho at the amphitheatre'This is a grand place for concerts and gatherings of large groups, it is true... but it also serves another purpose.

'A few months ago, I was drowsing on one of the seats here when the sun rose. To my great surprise, who should I see descending the steps but Tatháta the Beast herself, kinswoman of the Lower Ward? She is a towering, imposing figure; if you have ever seen her, you know she is not a woman with whom you should trifle! But on this morning she was not alone: she was walking two of her great hounds, the ones named Nûdil and Jôzi, around the amphitheatre. They worked up quite a sweat, the three of them, conducting great circuits of the structure.

'And it gave me an idea: if I did as Tatháta did, would I develop into as physical a specimen as she? So I have been coming here and walking down the steps, across the way, up the steps again, and following the curve of the seats back here. You should do the same! Why not make three circuits of the amphitheatre, friend? Be sure to start by running down the steps to begin!''Is that not a tremendous way to begin your day, my friend? I have found it to be so, ever since I adopted this means of exercise!

'I have not seen Tatháta or her hounds out this way in several weeks. Perhaps they are at sea again on some errand of the Kindred. There was a time she would walk through the Lower Ward and you could observe the crowds parting before her and her dogs wherever she went. They were friendly and would not bite, of course... although the same might not be said for Tatháta!

'Just a little joke, my friend. Perhaps you will do me the favour of keeping that one to yourself. But you are welcome to come back and run or walk around the amphitheatre whenever you like!'Jewellers purchase baubles found from sea-wrecks gathered by the sea-hawks that collect the shiny objects for their nests. Collect some of the dirty baubles for Luthana.Luthana requested that you search for sea-hawk nests far to the north for baubles and trinkets stolen from shipwrecks. She will use the baubles to satisfy her patrons in Umbar Baharbêl.Collect dirt-encrusted baubles from sea-hawk nests (${NUMBER}/14)You collected enough baubles to satisfy Luthana's patrons in Umbar Baharbêl. Deliver the baubles to her at the expedition camp in the south-eastern area of the Cape of Umbar.'Sea-hawks scavenge shore and shoals for materials to build their nests. The birds find baubles and curiosities within the wrecks along the sand bars to the north and store the treasures in their nests. Some of those baubles may have value to the jewellers in Umbar. Find encrusted keepsakes in the sea-hawk nests and return them to me here at the encampment.''Go north beyond the city of Umbar into the hills that meet the shore. Examine sea-hawk nests for signs of baubles or keepsakes and collect them. Return anything you find to me, and I will reward you for what you discover.''I will clean these items and separate those with value for shipment to the city's jewellers. I want to thank you for doing this. This effort is above and beyond what I am required to do. It earns me favour with the guild and the Kindred. This effort provides favour to the people of Umbar for you.'Khânai suggested that the scholars of Umbar are trying to cultivate a brood separate from the nest in the desert. To do so, the scholars require a matron and hope that collecting some eggs might yield what they desire.An inventive answer to the dangers presented in harvesting spider-silk is to control the brood in the city. Khânai asks that you collect spider eggs from the nest in the desert so she can deliver them to the scholars and outfitters.Collect spider-eggs (${NUMBER}/12)After collecting enough eggs from the spider's brood lair, you should return them to Khânai at the Hunter's camp in the Cape of Umbar.'Scholars and outfitters in Umbar City concocted a plan to produce silk at reduced risk to people like us. They desire to gather enough eggs from the brood mother in the desert nest to cultivate a brood within the city.

'Should they succeed, perhaps our lives would be less fraught with danger. I will carefully package and deliver the spider eggs if you will collect them for me.''I dare not ask the scholars how many spiders hatch from these eggs. I will leave the rearing of these crawling menaces to those with a stronger stomach. I will focus on the worms that stalk the sand. They intrigue me more than anything with legs.''You will find spider eggs within the nest in the desert to the north. Be careful not to disturb the brood matron watching over the unborn menaces.'Luthana requested that you make your way north to the hills that stretch to the shore. She suggested that there is an area there where bog-lurkers nest. She asked that you collect the legs and the seeds from their backs.North in the hills beyond Umbar Baharbêl, you will find bog-lurkers nesting in the fields as you approach the shore. Hunt the bog-lurkers for their legs and seeds.Collect bog-lurker legs (${NUMBER}/32)Collect bog-lurker seeds (${NUMBER}/16)North in the hills beyond Umbar Baharbêl, you will find bog-lurkers nesting in the fields as you approach the shore. Hunt the bog-lurkers for their legs and seeds.'There is a nest of bog-lurkers north beyond the city. I cannot say that the lurkers are a menace, only that the cooks of Umbar prize the seeds you can pluck from their backs. Their legs, too, are a delicacy enjoyed widely in the city.

'Because of these facts, they become the target of hunters. You will be paid if you join in this hunt.''Do not fret for the lurkers. They will recover. We have long hunted them and used them as a food source. We are careful not to reduce their population too far. We strike a balance with them and allow them to recover.''Travel north beyond the city to where the hills and shore meet. You will find a nest of bog-lurkers there. You may also find some that wandered away from the nest. Hunt them for their legs and the seeds on their backs.'Luthana directed you to the north in search of sea-hawk feathers. Jewellers in Umbar City use them as adornments for many of their creations and pay those who collect them in the wild.Luthana's patrons in Umbar Baharbêl use sea-hawk feathers when creating some jewellery. She asked that you do your best to collect moulted feathered from their nests and from live creatures if you must.Collect sea-hawk feathers from nests or birds (${NUMBER}/14)You collected enough feathers for Luthana. Return to the hunter's expedition in the south of the Cape of Umbar and deliver the feathers to her.'I prefer if you can acquire feathers without killing the sea-hawks. There should be feathers that the birds lose in the process of moulting. If you do not find enough in the nests, you may have to kill the birds to meet our quota.

'Find the birds in the hills north of Umbar proper and far north from this encampment. I need fourteen pristine feathers returned to me.''Go north and do your best to find the pristine feathers in sea-hawk nests. If you must, kill the birds and collect the pristine feathers. When you collect enough to meet the quota return them to me here at the expedition encampment.''These shall do nicely. There are some jewellers who adorn their earrings, necklaces, and other jewellery with feathers. They pay a fair price for the trouble we incur to gather the feathers. I thank you for taking care to harm as few sea-hawks as you could.'The healers of Dâr Tabib await fresh medical supplies.Chakâr has asked you to deliver medical supplies to healers in and around Dâr Tabib.

Dâr Tabib is located in the south-west area of the Tor-gardens.You have finished distributing medical supplies among the Dâr Tabib healers.Completed'I have some fresh medical supplies that need to be distributed among the healers in and around the building.

'Could you assist me with this task? I would be happy to pay you in advance.'You have finished distributing medical supplies among the Dâr Tabib healers, and in the process, alleviated some of their stress.After receiving a surplus of book copies, the scholars of the Tor-gardens are looking to give them away.Bashem has asked you to send books to Chakâr at Dâr Tabib.

Dâr Tabib is located in the south-west area of the Tor-gardens.Talk to Chakâr at Dâr TabibChakâr has asked you to give the books to listless patients in and around Dâr Tabib.

Dâr Tabib is located in the south-west area of the Tor-gardens.You have delivered the last of the books to the patients of Dâr Tabib.Completed'Will you be passing through the south-west part of the district? I meant to bring some books to Chakâr at Dâr Tabib, but...' He frowns at the stack of papers in front of him. 'I have some research to attend to, unfortunately.'

'People all over the city have been kind enough to donate books to us in our recovery efforts. Some are common enough that we can spare copies for the healers' patients. I am sure they would be thankful for something to chase away their boredom.''Bashem must be just as busy as us to send someone in his stead!

'The patients who remain bore grievous injuries from the fighting months ago and must stay under our supervision. As you can imagine, there are very few sources of entertainment here, and many have become listless. Some cannot leave their beds. Others can only wander around the apothecary grounds to break up the monotony.

'Would you mind handing out the books? It would do our patients some good to see a new person rather than the same healers every day.'You have delivered the last of the books, granting the patients of Dâr Tabib a bit of joy amidst the struggle of healing.What's left of the academy and scriptorium still haunts the Tor-gardens.It's possible that things of note are still buried under rubble at Kamîr Kateb.

Kamîr Kateb is located in the north-western corner of the Tor-gardens.Search through rubble in Kamîr KatebYou found a damaged ink bottle near the ruins of Kamîr Kateb.

You should show it to Rimâti at the Pot and Quill.'It was not so long ago when enforcers of the All-Seeing guarded the north-western ruins. Having the Heirsworn as our new neighbours is an improvement, but not by much.

'Kamîr Kateb held untold amounts of historical knowledge; surely there must be something left in the rubble still. Something the Church would have never considered important enough to be destroyed.

'If you discover anything of note there, please let me know. It may be foolish of me to hope for, but this city has already lost so much. Hope is all that keeps us going.''What is left of the ink looks dull brown, but I do not think it started out as this colour. The years and the elements have not been kind.

'The label on the bottle... much of it has fallen off, and the script on it has faded. But these are Ordâkhai characters, not Umbari ones.

'This was not a pigment of Umbari origin -- that much is certain.'Caebar has had a close encounter with Cruel Dancer, but did not realize it at the time. What has the dangerous bounty-hunter discovered that may be of use to you?Caebar handed you the note he discovered in his pocket, and you should read it.Read the note Caebar discovered on his personCaebar is in the Sail-haven.Talk to Caebar in the Sail-havenCruel Dancer spoke of crocodiles outside the city, and Caebar believes she means the ones that can be found to the south-east.Find the camp of crocodiles to the south-east of the cityCruel Dancer spoke of lamps in the night, somewhere near the crocodiles.Find the lamp nearest the crocodiles, on the rocks to the westThe toppled lamp to the west of the crocodiles merits some examination.Examine the toppled lampAnother lamp lies to the west.Examine another toppled lamp to the west along the rocksSomeone watches you from the rocks to the west of the line of lamps.Confront the person watching you to the west of the line of lampsCruel Dancer is west of the line of lamps, standing upon the rocks overlooking the river.Talk to Cruel Dancer by the coil of rope'Why are you staring at me like that?'

You encourage Caebar to check his belongings, concerned that he might have fallen victim to a pickpocket. He frantically searches his clothes for his money-purse.

'Here it is, thank goodness; but as light as it ever is, I am sorry to say. But what is this?'

He retrieves an unfamiliar scrap of parchment from one of his pockets, and his eyes go wide as he reads the message written on it.

'It is a message from Cruel Dancer!' he whispers, handing it to you.'I gave you the note! What do you think it means?''Do you think it means she's found a way to the prisoners? Lamps in the night? Crocodiles?'

Caebar thinks it over.

'I heard the crocodiles to the south-east of the city have been a problem for merchants trying to go that way. Maybe that is where we should start? But it sounds like only one of us should go? That must be you, right? Tell me that you think she means you!'

You assure Caebar that you will investigate the crocodiles outside the city by yourself, and he should continue his efforts in the Sail-haven. He breathes a sigh of relief and wishes you well.'I heard the crocodiles to the south-east of the city have been a problem for merchants trying to go that way. Maybe that is where you should start?'I am glad you received my message. I wondered after I left it if perhaps I was too subtle for the scribe to realize it had been given to him.

'Our shared purpose is almost complete, ${PLAYER}. The line of lamps indicates the way to a secret harbour used by certain members of the Kindred of the Coins. I have reason to believe your prisoners are held within, and several of the bounties upon the Kindred are ripe for me to claim.'Cruel Dancer has located the grotto where two members of the Kindred of the Coins seem to harbour their ships: Tatháta the Sea-beast and Nakási Wave-reaper.The coil of rope by Cruel Dancer will allow you to reach the lair Cruel Dancer discovered.Use the coil of rope and climb down to the secret grottoYou rescued one prisoner from the Kindred of the Coins, and your friends now recover at the amphitheatre east of the city.Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city'Here is what I know of this secret harbour. It has been the berth of the ship belonging to Tatháta the Sea-beast, but ever since Nakási Wave-reaper's husband perished in Gondor, she has used it for her own ship as well. I do not know for what reason she chooses not to dock in the city proper, but I believe we will find both vessels in the harbour when we descend.

'The way is treacherous, but we can use this rope to descend to the ledge we must take. It is narrow, with only room for one of us to pass at a time. Once you reach the far side of the ledge, there is a ladder that descends to the hidden harbour where our two targets keep their ships. You can go first down the rope... I will be right behind you.'Despite your misgivings, you know that this may be your best chance to reach the Kindred's prisoners undetected. You resolve to remain alert in case Cruel Dancer attempts any treacherous action.'The way is treacherous, but we can use this rope to descend to the ledge we must take. It is narrow, with only room for one of us to pass at a time. Once you reach the far side of the ledge, there is a ladder that descends to the hidden harbour where our two targets keep their ships. You can go first down the rope... I will be right behind you.''I still cannot believe it, ${PLAYER}! I never believed I would see you again... and yet here you are, such a great distance from where we parted! It is truly remarkable, and I delight that our reunion has come to pass!'You have rescued a friend from the Kindred of the Coins. Has the experience changed him, or have those he left behind changed in his stead?Corudan looks around eagerly.Wait for Driftwood to arriveDriftwood greets Corudan warmly.Talk to Driftwood at the amphitheatre east of the cityCorudan is pleased to see his friends again.Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the cityDriftwood remains silent.An awkward silence fills the airCorudan looks at you carefully.Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the citySigileth is at the amphitheatre east of the city.Talk to Sigileth at the amphitheatre east of the city'You must have had many adventures since we parted, my friend! What brings you all the way to the land of Umbar? Many months and more miles have passed since I saw you last at Helm's Deep, in Rohan!'

You tell Corudan, briefly, about some of the experiences you have had since his departure. He asks if you know how Leafshade fared after he went away, and you say as far as you know the Ent remains in good health and spirits. He smiles fondly.

'I am glad. I do not doubt that he could have survived any attack by Nakási or Tatháta if he was roused to battle, but I feared for the creatures of his grove and the trees for which he cared. I know the Ents are fearsome when enraged... but I cannot help but think something is lost when they are called to fight. Something in them is wounded. It is true for Men and Elves, in my experience, and I think it may be so for the Ents as well. They are meant for peace, for the care and tending of things that grow.

'I went with the Corsairs so they would not force Leafshade into battle. I sought to exert my influence upon them, and while I was not wholly successful I think it was for the best. Save for my words I fear the boy Thorongil would not have lived to reach Umbar.''Horn, my friend! It is good to see you!''I see you found our wayward Elf, ${PLAYER}! It is about time Corudan joined us again, wouldn't you say?''It is about time Corudan joined us again, wouldn't you say?''Horn, my friend! It is good to see you! I see you have shared in ${PLAYER}'s recent adventures, and I wish only that I could have done so as well!

'But where is Nona? Surely she is here too? I cannot imagine she would be content to sit out such a fight as we all have now before us?''I see... I am sorry.'

Corudan stares at you carefully, and you try to tell him with your eyes that Nona is alive but her feelings toward Horn have cooled in recent months. The silence is finally broken by Sigileth.'I am saddened to have missed your recent adventures, my friends, but I am pleased we are now reunited.''My purpose for joining this adventure has now been satisfied, but I will not have it said that I abandoned the mission when it was half-done. My brother has been rescued from the Kindred of the Coins, as I knew he would be, but they still hold the young heir of Pinnath Gelin captive.'You have rescued a friend from the Kindred of the Coins. Has the experience changed him, or have those he left behind changed in his stead?Corudan is eager to hear what befell his friends... but you do not know how to tell him some of the mournful things that transpired.Think about what to tell CorudanCorudan waits for you to speak.Talk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the citySigileth is at the amphitheatre east of the city.Talk to Sigileth at the amphitheatre east of the city'You must have had many adventures since we parted, my friend! What brings you all the way to the land of Umbar? Many months and more miles have passed since I saw you last at Helm's Deep, in Rohan!'

You tell Corudan, briefly, about some of the experiences you have had since his departure. He asks if you know how Leafshade fared after he went away, and you say as far as you know the Ent remains in good health and spirits. He smiles fondly.

'I am glad. I do not doubt that he could have survived any attack by Nakási or Tatháta if he was roused to battle, but I feared for the creatures of his grove and the trees for which he cared. I know the Ents are fearsome when enraged... but I cannot help but think something is lost when they are called to fight. Something in them is wounded. It is true for Men and Elves, in my experience, and I think it may be so for the Ents as well. They are meant for peace, for the care and tending of things that grow.

'I went with the Corsairs so they would not force Leafshade into battle. I sought to exert my influence upon them, and while I was not wholly successful I think it was for the best. Save for my words I fear the boy Thorongil would not have lived to reach Umbar.

'But where are our other friends, ${PLAYER}? Do you not still adventure with Horn, Nona, and Gléowine?''Why do you hesitate, my friend? What has happened?'

Sadly you tell Corudan of Horn's death before the walls of Minas Tirith during the Battle of Pelennor Fields. The Elf remains silent for a long moment. When at last he speaks, his voice is choked with emotion and he does not sound like himself.

'Horn always possessed more courage than he believed himself to have, ${PLAYER}. I hope that Nona holds his memory dear. Know that I will. I know this too: Gléowine must record the name of our friend in song, for he fought for Rohan, and though I was not there I know he fought with courage on behalf of his friends and for his kingdom.'

You tell Corudan that Gléowine did intend to include Horn in the song he composed of the battle, and the Elf smiles. After a moment Sigileth speaks up.'I am saddened to have missed your recent adventures, my friend, but I am pleased we are now reunited.''My purpose for joining this adventure has now been satisfied, but I will not have it said that I abandoned the mission when it was half-done. My brother has been rescued from the Kindred of the Coins, as I knew he would be, but they still hold the young heir of Pinnath Gelin captive.'Tevurin requested that you recover two types of hides from the saltwater crocodiles on the shores of the Cape of Umbar, the soft underbelly skin and the coarse hide of the back.Tevurin directed you to the shore south and east of the expedition camp in search of crocodile skins. He needs the soft underbelly skins and the tough hides from the backs of the crocodiles there.Collect crocodile underbelly skins (${NUMBER}/6)Collect tough crocodile hides (${NUMBER}/6)You collected the soft underbelly and tougher hides of crocodiles. Take the hides and return to Tevurin at the hunter's expedition in the southeast of the Cape of Umbar.'It must come as no surprise that the thick hide of the crocodile that protects the top side of their bodies can also be used as a fine defence for our warriors. What is not as obvious is the value of the soft underbelly.

'Many of the more affluent members of the city desire bags, or water-skins made of that skin; and so, I will ask that you go to the shore in search of complete skins of each type. Six of each, to be precise.''These will do nicely. The size is close to the same, and I can see that you did your best to minimize the damage when we fought the creature. You have my thanks for fulfilling this request.''Crocodiles stalk the shore south and east of the expedition encampment. I need to collect both the tough hide from the backs of the crocodiles and their soft underbelly. Return to me when you have those hides.'Head north to where the hills meet the shore, and search the nests of the sea-hawks for unfertilized eggs. Collect fourteen eggs from the nests and return them to Luthana at the expedition encampment in the eastern part of the Cape of Umbar.North, beyond Umbar city, where the hills roll into the shore, sea-hawks soar above the land. They build nests in the crags and trees. They lay eggs prized by the chefs of Umbar. Collect the eggs and return to Luthana at the expedition camp.Collect sea-hawk eggs from nests (${NUMBER}/14)Your efforts to collect sea-hawk eggs proved fruitful. All you need do now is return your precious cargo to Luthana at the hunter's expedition in the south-eastern portion of the Cape of Umbar.'Epicureans in the city desire sea-hawk eggs for their unique flavour and size. The birds make their nests north beyond the city, where the hills roll into the shore. Go north and seek out the sea-hawk nests, collect fourteen eggs from their nests, and return them to me.''You will find eggs in sea-hawk nests north along the shore and the hills. Collect fourteen eggs and return them to me here at the encampment.''Thank you for collecting these. I will deliver the eggs to the cooks' guild. The leadership will distribute them to their chefs. Those who pay will enjoy them in breakfast feasts throughout the city.'Alchemists within the city of Umbar use the glands from the worms in the crags to strengthen or modify many of their potions. You were asked to collect several of the glands from the creatures to the north-west of the city.You were instructed to head north and west of the expedition encampment to find the intact fire-glands in the throats of the worms there. When gathered, you should return the glands to Abido at the expedition camp.Collect worm fire-glands (${NUMBER}/6)You recovered the intact fire-glands from the worms in the eastern area of the Cape of Umbar. Return your collection to Abido at the hunter's expedition in the south-east of the Cape of Umbar.'North and west of our encampment and beyond the city bounds you will find a collection of worms in the craggy hills. I have a request for the glands within their throats that give them their fiery disposition and abilities.

'Our alchemists make use of them in many ways and pay my patron for their acquisition. I will need six pairs of intact fire-glands to offer you payment.''Look at these fine specimens. Excellent work.

'I wonder. Did you see the beast, Nejagil, while you were hunting the worms in the crags? It is said that the beast makes its home among the lesser worms there. I am sorry, my preoccupation with the beast often distracts me from my duties.'

He sighs.

'Ah yes, my duties. You have completed the task I set before you and so you should receive your reward. Please, accept this with great thanks.''You will find the worms among the craggy hills north and west of here beyond the bounds of the city proper. Hunt the worms there for their fire-glands and return them to me when you have six pairs of unmarred glands.'Abido expressed that the common folk have a less refined palette than those of the higher castes in the city. They do not desire more than the simple meat of boars to fill their bellies.While you hunt the crags and other areas of the eastern cape of Umbar, Abido asked that you collect wild hog haunches to help feed the masses in the city.Collect wild hog haunches (${NUMBER}/12)You collected enough haunches to satisfy Abido's needs. Return the haunches to him at the hunter's expedition in the south-east of the Cape of Umbar.'Not everyone can partake in affluent meals and delicacies. For many of the commoners the best meal is one that is simply… fresh, hot, or something heartier than fruits or vegetables.

‘For them, I am asked to gather meat from the wilds hogs of the hills and plains to the north of our camp and the city. This seems a simple order.''As requested, so delivered. Enough meat to feed a family for a month. The guilds and the Kindred are doing much to provide for the citizens. I do believe that this is admirable. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''Wild hogs can be found throughout the eastern Cape of Umbar. When you encounter and kill them collect their haunches. The meat there can be used to feed the populace of the city.'As foul as the task may seem, it is a necessary one for the outfitters of Umbar: the collection of excrement from wild beasts throughout the Cape of Umbar for the production of tannins.Abido asked you to help him obtain twenty heaps of dung to send back to outfitters in the city. It matters only that the dung comes from wild hogs or buffalo that make the crags and desert of the Cape of Umbar their habitat.Collect heaps of dung (${NUMBER}/20)Your task is complete, and none too soon. Return the dung to Abido at the hunter's expedition in the south-east of the Cape of Umbar.Abido shakes his head.

'I admit that this is an ignoble request. Outfitters in the city, who provide and create leathers for the populace, require a certain amount of an item....'

He pauses and sighs.

'They require dung. The dung of boars or wild buffalo; the source does not truly matter. It is a crucial ingredient in the process to create the tannins used to tan hides. I am to obtain twenty heaps for delivery to the city. If you are willing to undertake this request, you will be paid very well.''I am surprised that I did not sense your arrival. Given the task you have just completed for me I thought I would have sensed you from a great distance. Strange that, yes? As promised, a generous reward for such a terrible request.''Wild hogs and buffalo can be found north of this encampment. They wander the crags, the desert, the savannahs. Wherever you find them, you are certain to find what I need you to... pick up.'Despite those who would try to destroy it, Umbar's past survives.Rimâti has invited you to join her at the Shrine to He-Who-Sees-All.

You can find the shrine at the southern end of the Tor-gardens.Talk to Rimâti at the Shrine to He-Who-Sees-AllRimâti has given you dyed banners to hang up at the Shrine to He-Who-Sees-All.Hang banners on flag-poles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have hung up the banners.

You should talk to Rimâti.'I cannot surmise much else from this ink bottle without dedicated study. Unfortunately, having more questions than answers is only natural in my vein of research. History is always fragmented and difficult to piece together -- the Church's burning of our archives only exacerbated our restoration attempts.

'But I did not come to the Tor-gardens to sulk about research! I have a wrecked shrine to further deface.

'Why not join me there? Should you spot a blight of black among the buildings to the south, you will know you have found the shrine.''There you are. Behold!'

Rimâti reaches into a sack and pulls out a banner. At first glance, the banner is simply pink. But then the cloth shifts, and you realize at certain angles, the colour transforms -- blue, then purple, then pink again.

'The scholars and I spent months researching this pigment. Bidulêkh, it is called -- Dawn-sheen. When Kamîr Kateb burned down, the recipe burned with it. The scribes and scholars who would have held that knowledge met their ends at the Church's hands.

'I came to the shrine to hang up the banners, but...' She gestures to the flag-poles before you and grins. 'Would you like to do the honours instead?''For as long as I can remember, our buildings were always draped in black. The Church did not allow any other colours to be displayed. A silly thing to concern themselves with, perhaps, but hasn't it always been about control?

'That is why the scholars and I continue to do our research. With every colour we return to the city, we spit in the faces of tyrants who tried to control us... and come what may, the people of Umbar will endure.'You have found the hidden harbour used by two members of the Kindred of the Coins, and hope to rescue the hostages contained within.Cruel Dancer has come with you to the hidden harbour.Talk to Cruel Dancer in the hidden harbourThe nearest of the ships you should investigate is to the west.Board the nearest ship to the west in the hidden harbourYou have boarded the first ship and should wait for Cruel Dancer to join you.Wait for Cruel Dancer to join you aboard the shipCruel Dancer stands aboard the deck of one of the ships moored within the hidden harbour.Talk to Cruel Dancer aboard the shipCorsairs loyal to the Kindred of the Coins have learned of your presence in the hidden harbour!Defeat the Corsair defenders aboard the ship while Cruel Dancer searches below deckCruel Dancer has returned from her search of the first ship's interior.Talk to Cruel Dancer aboard the first ship in the hidden harbourHaving found no one within the first ship, Cruel Dancer believes the hostages you seek may be aboard the second ship moored within the hidden harbour.Follow the walkways to the second ship moored within the hidden harbourCorudan is a captive aboard the second ship, but he is still alive.Talk to Corudan aboard the second ship moored within the hidden harbourWait for the captain of the ship to arrive.Wait for the ship's captain to arriveTatháta the Beast stands upon the deck of her ship.Talk to Tatháta the Beast aboard her shipCruel Dancer engages Tatháta the Beast in conversation aboard the second ship moored within the hidden harbour.Witness the confrontation between Cruel Dancer and Tatháta the BeastThe conversation has become a violent conflict!Defeat Tatháta and her crewCruel Dancer has chased after Tatháta the Beast, but your priority must be to rescue Corudan.Talk to Corudan aboard the second ship moored within the hidden harbour'You should follow the walkway to the west and investigate the first of the ships docked within this hidden harbour. I will circle around and come to it from the water, so we will have the advantage of surprise upon any members of the Kindred onboard the ship.''I hear folk inside the ship, and even now we have attracted their notice. They approach from within.

'I will search below deck while you keep them busy up here.''There were no prisoners within this ship, ${PLAYER}. If your mission is to succeed, and if I am to claim the bounties I seek, we must hope the prisoners and their captors are aboard the second of the ships docked within this harbour.

'Follow the walkways to the second ship. I will approach that vessel by water as I did this one, and maintain the element of surprise.''${PLAYER}... is that you? I cannot believe it!

'But you must be careful! I hear Tatháta coming back!''Who are you to stand so boldly upon the deck of my ship? There are few indeed who would dare such a thing, for I have sent most of those to watery graves.

'${PLAYER}? I have heard this name before now; Nakási has spoken of you to me. I am surprised you are still alive. Were she still here, instead of in the Citadel of Winds with the hostage from Pinnath Gelin, she would no doubt skin you alive. She will be disappointed to learn she missed you.

'But why are you here? You cannot have come all the way to Umbar Baharbêl to take Nestinanessornë from us. It amused Nakási to take him aboard our ships, but he says little enough to us, and when he does speak his talk is mostly nonsense and riddles. The lions like him, which has kept him alive this long, but if they should get hungry I believe they will like him both less and more.'

Tatháta smiles languidly.

'I can speak in riddles too, you see?''I still cannot believe you came to rescue me, ${PLAYER}... are our friends here too?'

You tell Corudan that you will recount your adventures to him just as soon as you untie him and bring him safely from Tatháta's hidden harbour. With a grin, you say that Sigileth will be very pleased to see him alive and unharmed. He blinks at you with surprise.Tevurin needs you to collect soft and tough hides from the crocodiles along the shores of the Cape of Umbar.Tevurin explained that the fatty layer between the crocodile's skin is difficult to obtain, but used by the craftsmen to keep their crocodile hide specialties supple. He asked that you spend some time collecting the fatty layer of the crocodiles from along the shore south and east of the expedition encampment.Collect fatty crocodile viscera (${NUMBER}/8)Tevurin explained that the fatty layer between the crocodile's skin is difficult to obtain, but used by the craftsmen to keep their crocodile hide specialties supple. He asked that you spend some time collecting the fatty layer of the crocodiles from along the shore south and east of the expedition encampment.'Though there is not much to the layer of fat on a crocodile, when distilled with water and some herbs it is the best solution with which to tan, treat, and maintain the armour-refined hides that craftsmen create.

'I have need for eight phials of the fatty layer between the muscle and sinew of the crocodiles. I will furnish you the phials, you will need to collect the viscera.''Excellent work. Once the outfitters get hold of this they will turn it into a softener that will keep their product flexible and strong for years. They will earn a larger amount of coin than you or me. At least we are paid for our efforts.''You will find the crocodiles along the shoreline to the south and east. Finding crocodiles with enough fat upon their frames may prove difficult. When you have collected the fat I require please return to me.'Khânai asked that you carve the haunches off the water buffaloes you slay in the Cape of Umbar. Cooks in Umbar City prize their meat in their banquet dinners.Make your way into the plains, desert, or savannah to find water buffalo. Slaughter the beasts; carve haunches off their bones and deliver the meat to Khânai at the expedition camp. You will find them north, east, and west from the hunter's encampment.Collect buffalo haunches (${NUMBER}/14)Make your way into the plains, desert, or savannah to find water buffalo. Slaughter the beasts; carve haunches off their bones and deliver the meat to Khânai at the expedition camp.'Water buffalo haunches provide several cuts of meat for the cooks of Umbar City to use in banquet dinners and feasts. They desire that we deliver a great deal of the haunches to them.

'As you hunt the buffalo, cut the haunches from the bone and deliver them to me. I will pay you for your effort and send the meat to the cooks in the city.''These haunches are expertly removed from the water buffalo. It is clear that you have undertaken tasks like this before. I will see that the cook's guild in Umbar becomes aware of your contributions.

'Please accept this reward for the assistance you provided.''You will find water buffalo roaming the savannahs, plains, and deserts here in the Cape of Umbar. Collect the haunches from the beasts and return them to me here at the camp.'Most of a crocodile can be eaten. Tevurin does not seem to be overly concerned about what kind of meat you obtain so long as it is from the crocodiles on the shore of the sea to the south and east.Tevurin directed you to make your way south and east to the shoreline to hunt crocodiles for meat. Chefs in Umbar Baharbêl use the meat to cook for the masses.Collect crocodile meat (${NUMBER}/14)You collected what you believe is about a stone's worth of crocodile meat. Return the meat to Tevurin at the hunter's expedition in the southeast of the Cape of Umbar.'Nearly all of the crocodile can be eaten, so I will not require any particular portions of the beasts for this request. We have only been tasked with acquiring meat.

'To be exact, I will need a stone's worth of crocodile meat. The meat will need to be unspoiled, but otherwise any crocodile meat should suffice.''Yes, this will do. It feels about the full weight of a stone. Thank you for your assistance.''I need about a stone's worth of crocodile meat. You can find them along the shore to the south and east of the expedition camp.'Speak with the expedition assistants to learn about the birds of prey and bog-lurkers on the Eastern Cape of Umbar. Though limited in use, there remains value in hunting these creatures. The assistants in the expedition camp will tell you more.Speak with the expedition assistants to learn about the birds of prey and bog-lurkers on the Eastern Cape of Umbar. Though limited in use, there remains value in hunting these creatures. The assistants in the expedition camp will tell you more.Speak with Zerkho about the fauna in the hillsSpeak with Dorshet about the fauna in the hillsYou spoke with Zerkho and Dorshet. They do not think that there is a threat from the seahawks and bog-lurkers you hunt in the north. Return to Luthana in the expedition camp.'The hills and plains that meet the sea teem with an abundance of fauna, natural and corrupt. Cooks in the city use bits gathered from uncorrupted creatures to supplement the food served throughout the city.

'My role is to organize the collection and distribution of the materials the cooks require and reward any who aid in the effort. Discuss with Zerkho and Dorshet the benefits gained from gathering materials and the danger inherent to meeting the requests.''Speak with Dorshet and Zerkho. Their knowledge provides advantages in harvesting the materials my patrons require.''As you climb the hills far to the north and west of this expedition, you will see signs of uncorrupted fauna. Seahawks soar on the warm air rising from the land as it fights with cool breezes from the sea. Bog-lurkers, often mistaken for reeds or detritus, wander in large numbers.

'Cooks in Umbar draw the most value from these creatures.

'Sea hawks lay large flavourful eggs that epicures devour by the dozen. The profit gained exceeds the risk presented by disturbing the sea hawk's nests.

'Bog-lurker legs are a delicacy for the thin shaft of gelatinous meat drawn forth when boiled and the salty broth that remains after. Last, the seeds found on the lurker's back grow to stock our vegetable and spice stores.''I have no desire to harm the sea hawks making their nests in the northern part of the Cape of Umbar. Unlike the culinarians, I do not wish to steal their young. I want only to recover what they lose and what they find that was lost.

'I am sorry. I do not mean to be cryptic. The sea hawks lose their feathers, naturally and unnaturally. The sea hawks also find baubles and bits from shipwrecks.

'My patrons in the city desire these commodities and pay well for any who deliver them.''Zerkho and Dorshet do not believe that there is a threat posed by the sea hawks and bog-lurkers as you attempt to relieve them of their limbs and eggs. I respect their knowledge but question that advice. I would use caution, friend.'Tevurin asked you to make your way to the east and north along the shore to find and kill Omkâru, a legendary ancient crab.Tevurin advised that a legendary ancient crab stalks the shores north and east of the expedition encampment. He asked that you help earn accolades by finding and defeating the creature.Defeat Omkâru and collect its clawYou found the crab Tevurin spoke of and battled it to the death. You took its claw as a trophy and should return the claw to Tevurin at the hunter's expedition in the south-east of the Cape of Umbar as proof of your deed.'When I signed on to the expedition, I hoped to seek my own fortune as a hunter of the magnificent. Now, I am mired in the details of delivery and collection for the union and my dreams are filled with numbers of deliveries and counts for collection.

'I do not mean to complain. After all, you helped me as much as you have, friend. You see, there is an ancient crab rumoured to stalk the shores to the north and east of where we are camped.

'Any who find this creature and collect a trophy from it will be met with great accolades, I am sure. I wonder, would you be interested?''My friend, you have done something that several have dreamed of, but none, until now, have ever achieved. I can offer you very little in the way of reward for such a feat; certainly not enough to honour this achievement, but please accept this reward.''If the rumours are true, the crab makes its way along the shoreline east of here.'Khânai suggests that the water buffalo dwelling in the areas within and near the desert to the north of the expedition have hides that are best for tents. The citizens of Umbar prize the larger hides, and she asks that you acquire some for her.Khânai directed you to scour the lands surrounding the encampment but more near the savannah and desert for the water buffalo. You are to collect hides from the defeated beasts and return them to her at the expedition encampment.Collect water buffalo hides (${NUMBER}/12)With the hides collected and safely stowed, it is time to return to the hunter's encampment outside of Umbar Baharbêl to deliver the hides to Khânai.'The blistering heat of the sun burns flesh and draws water from our skin. To protect ourselves from the danger that the sun presents, we use tents and other items to shield our heads. The buffalo that roam the outskirts of the desert have large hides conducive to these purposes. I ask that you hunt and skin the beasts for their hides and then return them to me.''A fine collection. I will return this to my patron in the city, and they shall be made into useful abodes for the populace.'Tevurin asks that you make your way to the shoreline to hunt the crocodiles there for their pristine teeth.Tevurin directed you to the shore south and east of the expedition camp in search of pristine crocodile teeth. He requires ten incisors to satisfy his quota.Collect sets of crocodile incisors (${NUMBER}/10)Tevurin directed you to the shore south and west of the expedition camp in search of pristine crocodile teeth. He requires ten incisors to satisfy his quota.'As you now know, teeth from the crocodiles can be used in many of the craftsman works from the simplest fastener to ornate pieces that embellish the self.

'I must collect ten crocodile incisors... if you are willing to make the effort.''An excellent hunt and find, friend. Each of these is nearly identical to the other. I do hope that finding them was not too difficult. I know that an order as specific and yet broad as perfect is less than ideal, but you appear to have understood the request, perfectly.''You will find the crocodiles along the beach to the south and east of our expedition encampment. I require their incisors and a perfect set of incisors.'Copies of historical texts have been stolen from a dyer visiting the Tor-gardens.Rimâti's scholarly texts may have been scattered around the ruins of Dâr Jeraf.

Dâr Jeraf can be found in the north-western corner of the Tor-gardens.Collect scholarly texts at Dâr Jeraf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected (hopefully) all of Rimâti's scholarly texts.

You should return them to her at the Pot and Quill.'Stay clear of Dâr Jeraf to the north-west, if you can. The Heirsworn there stole my belongings. Not that they would deem any of it valuable -- I was only carrying historical texts on pigments. Copies, I mean, not the originals!

'You see, I have been attempting to recreate colours that were lost during the Church's rule. The scholars spent innumerable hours copying those texts for me, and I do not wish to see their efforts go to waste.

'The texts must have been left to scatter to the winds. Should you find any, please return them to me!''Not a page is missing! Thank you... and I am sure I speak for the scholars as well!'Hides collected from the wild hogs strewn throughout the eastern stretches of the Cape of Umbar can be turned into simple leathers used for clothing and more. You were asked to help in the collection of these hides.You will find wild hogs throughout the crags and moors of the eastern Cape of Umbar. Kill them and collect their hides for Abido.Collect wild hog hides (${NUMBER}/10)You will find wild hogs throughout the crags and moors of the eastern Cape of Umbar. Kill them and collect their hides for Abido.'When hunting the wild hogs of the eastern Cape of Umbar, we are cautious to leave little waste. The hides of the wild hogs, as an example, can be used to outfit our populace, make satchels or packs and much more. My patrons request that I oversee the collection of a good number of these hides. If you are willing to assist then there is payment to be made.''A simple request fulfilled. You are proving very capable and prompt. Perhaps we could convince you to stay with us and assist us beyond a day or two?'

He laughs.

'No, I know well the call of adventure and would not wish this style of life on you, friend.''While hunting the wild hogs throughout the eastern areas of the Cape of Umbar, be certain to collect their hides for me. My patron will pay for meeting a quote of ten.'Delona informed you that though this seems like a hunt for sport, the purpose of the Umbari hunt is to supply the city with vital resources. They then asked if you wanted to join in the efforts and you complied.Delona asked you to work with the various hunters and experts within the expedition camp to meet the needs of the craftspeople in Umbar city.Assist Khânai with the spice flow into Umbar BaharbêlHelp Luthana meet epicurean desiresHelp Tevurin achieve his personal hunting goalHelp Abido achieve his hunting dreamYou completed several tasks for the various hunters and experts within the expedition camp. Return to the expedition leader, Delona, and inform her of your efforts.Speak with Delona'Here in the wilds outside of our city, we find a great deal of fauna that provide the craftspeople within our city with vital materials to their professions. It does not matter why you come to this encampment, only that you are here; and if you are willing and capable of assisting us in gathering resources and eliminating the greater threats that stalk the dunes, shores, prairies, and hills surrounding Umbar Baharbêl.''Each of the hunters informed me of your successes. This is an accomplishment that even the few who dedicate themselves to such a lifestyle achieve. You should feel a great deal of pride in your success. For all you have done, you have earned this.

'Please, return to us again, friend. We are here at the behest and employ of the crafters of Umbar and welcome the assistance and company of individuals with skills that assist us.

'You have proven capable and personable; two qualities that we prize. Thank you again.'You have learned that the term used for a group of crocodiles is a bask, and that there is an ancient crocodile that makes its way onto shore to bask in the sun daily. You were asked to gain proof of defeating the massive crocodile and bring it to Tevurin.Tevurin directed you to look along the sands near the shore east of the expedition camp in search of the great ancient crocodile, Ghadamût. Defeat the crocodile and collect its jaws.Defeat Ghadamût and collect its mawTevurin directed you to look along the shore south and east of the expedition camp during the day in search of the great ancient crocodile, Ghadamût. Defeat the crocodile, collect its jaws, and return it to Tevurin.'During the sunlight hours it is said, a great crocodile of immense size and age makes its way to the beaches to sit and rest in the sun among the bask of crocodiles.

'Some have fought the creature only to be rescued near death from its jaws. Others have gone on the hunt and disappeared. I had wanted to make my mark as shore hunter by claiming its jaws as a trophy, but alas - my duty now is the daily effort of scribing and counting.

'Perhaps this is a pursuit you will find appealing.''This is a feat that I did not think possible.''The massive beast is often seen basking in the sun on the beaches east of here. It is said to lay in the sun and appear asleep. Do not let its sedentary behaviour fool you. Be cautious too, as it is said to defend the bask from hunters.'In the north-west, beyond the city and amongst the crags where the worms make their lairs, sands are stained black from oil that seeps through the surface. You were asked to collect a few sacks of the sand and return them to the expedition camp.Make your way to the worm habitat in the north-west crags. Search there for patches of black sand and collect three bags for Abido at the expedition encampment.Collect bags of tar sand (${NUMBER}/3)You searched the area and found three full bags of tar sand. Return the filled sacks to Abido at the hunter's expedition in the south-east of the Cape of Umbar.'In the habitat where you find the worms, there are sands that bubble with crude smelling oil. The sand is thick and heavy, drawing down most anything too large and heavy to stand upon it.

'There are those in the city proper, however, who prize these sands. For when treated correctly, they can harness the power of fire with it for days at a time.

'I ask that you fill three sacks with the sand and return it to me.''I am told that the scholars have learned to press the sand to draw out the natural oil within. They use it in lamps, torches, and all manner of things that burn. I have heard tell that the Kindred are planning to make even greater use of the extract. How, I do not know.

'Your payment is well earned. Here, my friend. Would that I could leave these bounds and journey with you.''You will find the sands I speak of in the hills where the worms lurk. They are north-west beyond the city. Collect some of the sand and return it to me.'Khânai suggested that you should converse with the experts visiting the expedition from the city to learn more about the vale and the threats across the desert to the east and north.Khânai made sure you understood that you should speak with the advisors visiting the encampment to learn what is hunted for in the desert and the dangers that the flora and fauna present.Speak with the outfitter, KarbahSpeak with the scholar, MallaxSpeak with ZerkhoHaving spoken with the advisors, you should return to Khânai and let her know that you are prepared to deal with the flora and fauna of the desert.Speak with Khânai at the Hunter's Expedition Camp'The land to the east of the city and north of this encampment is barren and desert-like. There lay a wasteland where trees grow sparsely and danger lurks within the sand.

'Terrible creatures sift through the sand, spin it about them as they blow across the landscape, or, worse, lay traps to ensnare the unobservant.

'Above all else, one must be alert and informed when entering those lands.

'I advise consulting with the experts here within the expedition camp for their guidance and direction to understand why we hunt in the desert and what you should expect if you make your way there.''In the desert land east of Umbar Baharbêl, there is a great brood of spiders weaving deep nests and webs to ensnare beasts as large as water buffalo. It is these spiders that the aristocracy prizes. Not for anything other than the webbing and silk that the spiders weave.

'When worked through looms, the spider-silk can be turned into beautiful fabrics that are then dyed and manufactured to the specifications made by the great tailors of the guilds and sold to the well-to-do.

'Be warned, the spiders are foul creatures with a penchant for blood. And, sadly, they are very good at obtaining what they desire. You must simply be better at keeping yourself alive.''The reasons to hunt in the desert waste are many. As a scholar, the main reason that I choose is knowledge.

'We seek to understand the secrets of spider's weaving webs. We wish to know why the frill about a lizard's neck repairs itself as does a salamander's body. These mysteries are the puzzles that drive us back into the desert when we know the dangers are great.''Khânai sent you to learn about why the chefs of Umbar desire us to explore and ravage the already ravaged desert land to the east of the city, eh?

'I will tell you, then. Across the desert grows an abundant array of aromatic and potent spices that give many of the dishes enjoyed by our aristocracy. It is for this reason that we send so many adventurers into the wastes.

'There are enemies there: grim winds that carry the spice, and worms that sift the sand to move, leaving spice in their wake, or, carrying the spice within themselves. These are each viable targets for the collection of the spices we desire.

'But be wary, the magical nature of the grim and the violent nature of the sand-worms should not be underestimated.''What the advisors teach you is learned from books and speeches. What I will tell is from experience of my own and that of travellers who make their way through the unforgiving desert.

'When there is a question of your safety move to the rocks.

'When your journey is beginning make sure to drink your water.
 
'Share your water with others only if they are trusted or of your kin.

'Do not linger on the hot sand too long.

'Now... you are as prepared as can be.'Scholars in Umbar believe the membranous tissue of a lizard frill and the ability of salamanders to regenerate missing tails and limbs might help them reinforce their potions. They need more samples to study.Foray into the desert and obtain lizard frills from the reptiles there. You will need to travel north from the expedition camp. Once harvested, return the frills to Khânai at the encampment.Collect lizard frills (${NUMBER}/14)Foray into the desert and obtain lizard frills from the reptiles there. You will need to travel north from the expedition camp. Once harvested, return the frills to Khânai at the encampment.'There are oddities in nature that scholars believe are worth studying. The frilled lizards in the desert are among the natural creatures that Umbari scholars find fascinating.

'The thin membranous frills around the lizard's neck heal even if ruptured or removed. This regeneration is not unique among lizard-like creatures in Umbar. The process by which the membrane repairs itself is unknown; but our scholars are working toward understanding.

'We must help their efforts by acquiring lizard frills and delivering them to the city.''I do not care for the wanton slaughter of animals. I find it cruel and inhumane. However, I do support studying nature's mechanisms to comprehend how we might harness the natural powers and strength all around us.

'I believe this is the goal of our scholars, so I continue to support these efforts. Thank you for your assistance.''Scattered across the desert, plains, and savannah in the eastern Cape of Umbar, you will find the frilled lizards in adequate numbers. Obtain fourteen frills from about their necks and deliver them to me here.'Abido, inspired by the ease with which you accomplished all of the tasks he laid before you, asks for assistance in seeing his dream through. He wants you to hunt and slay Nêjagil.Abido, excited at the prospect of seeing Nêjagil, wants you to return to the black sands in the crags north-west of Umbar City to find and slaughter the beast. Collect its tail and return to him at the expedition encampment.Defeat Nêjagil and claim its tailAbido, excited at the prospect of seeing Nêjagil, wants you to return to the black sands in the crags north-west of Umbar City to find and slaughter the beast. Collect its tail and return to him at the expedition encampment.'I heard from another aspirant aiding me that they saw Nêjagil roaming the black sands at night. They told me they engaged the beast but were forced to flee the confrontation because it overpowered them. It chirped loudly, they said, so loudly that it shattered their ears.'

He shakes his head.

'Would that I could leave my post during the day to hunt down the beast.

'I wonder, would you hunt the beast? You've proven so able thus far with everything before you. Certainly, you are twice the adventurer as this other aspirant. You could slaughter the beast, collect its tail as a trophy and return it to me so that I might see something of the beast for my time in the wilds.''It is everything I expected and more. Even now the flesh knits back together. Forgive my excitement. You see, the tail of the salamander is exceptional. You have defeated a creature that many have feared for years.'You should find Nêjagil stalking near the black sands in the crags north-west of Umbar City. Please, as an enthusiast who wanted nothing more than to face the beast will you claim that glory in my stead?'Desert spice, used in many dishes enjoyed by the people of Umbar, requires collecting and sifting sand where desert fauna deposit spice. Khânai asked that you obtain spice for her.Seek spice from the sand-storms and sand-worms in the desert north of the expedition camp. Collect twelve sacks of desert spice and return them to Khânai.Collect sacks of spice (${NUMBER}/12)Having recovered the spice that Khânai requested, it is time to return the sacks of freshly gathered herbs to her at the Hunter's encampment.'Chefs in Umbar say that the blend of spices used to enhance the flavour of their dishes is more important than the collection of any other ingredient. The spice blend is rare and found only in the desert. Worse still is the method for collecting the spice.

'To obtain desert spice, you must eliminate the carrier. Strange winds streaking across the desert or sand-worms are known to be spice carriers. Seek them out in the desert land to the north and return to me when you've gathered twelve sacks full.''Once delivered, the cook's guild will further refine and separate the spice from the silt. The guild can include the spice in their recipes, package it for sale, and teach others the processes of refining the product.

'You completed the work asked of you. The guild will know that it was you that furnished the spice. Here is your reward.''Make your way to the desert and collect pouches of spice from the sand-storms and sand-worms. You will find them north in the desert sands.'You visited Tevurin, the shore hunter, and were instructed to speak with his assistants to learn more about the fauna that make the shoreline of the eastern Umbar Cape their home.Tevurin asked that you visit the three expert assistants to learn about the crocodiles and other creatures that make the beaches of the Cape of Umbar their home. When you have learned what the experts know, you are to return to Tevurin so that he can provide you further direction.Speak with the engraver DorshetSpeak with the cook ZerkhoSpeak with the outfitter KarbahYou spoke with the visiting specialists from Umbar Baharbêl. Return to Tevurin and tell her that you are prepared for her requests.'Greetings. It appears that the overseer of this effort has found another set of hands to help us meet the quotas we are asked to meet. If this is true, then I would have you see my three assistants to learn about the fauna, specifically the crocodiles, that dwell along the shore here in the eastern stretch of Umbar.

'Once you have absorbed the knowledge that my associates possess, return to me so that I can set you about the many tasks that we have.''Bones from creatures we once hunted among the waves are carved by some jewellers, but it is a hobby that the seaborne warriors practice that brings value to something other than the bones of the saltwater crocodiles; their teeth.

'Crocodile teeth are larger than most and make carving easier. When sealed properly they make fine thong fasteners as well as ornamentation for outfits or jewellery.''Though it does not spring to mind when you think of food, there is some value in the flesh of the crocodile. The meat is tough, gamey, and requires some preparation, but there are delicacies that are enjoyed by many throughout the region.

'There are no prime cuts that come from the crocodile, but the meat can be dried, or prepped and turned into trail rations and some other tasty treats that are crafted by guild masters in the city.''You spoke with Tevurin, eh? Then you want to know about the salties and the value of their hide? Valuable. Very valuable. The hide is thick and scaly, but pliable enough to mould and shape as you need. True masters of the craft make fine leathers, cops, bracers, belts, and helms from the hide of the beasts.

'Further, the thin layer of fat that one can peel from the sinewy muscles and hide can be boiled down into an oil that helps to maintain the pliability of the hide during processing.''Take note of what you were told. The wilds of Umbar can be very dangerous.'Abido instructed you to speak with the expert assistants to learn more about the salamanders and boars that roam the hills to the north and west of the camp and city.You were instructed to consult with the experts in the camp to learn about the animals that you would hunt across the crags and moors in the eastern Cape of Umbar. They can be found in the encampment.Speak with ZerkhoSpeak with KarbahSpeak with MallaxYou should now have an understanding of how the people of Umbar will use the various items gained from a hunt in the crags and moors of the Cape of Umbar. Return to Abido and speak with him.Speak with Abido'Oh, hello, welcome, excuse me.'

The man seems confused.

'Forgive me. I was told the position here would be in the field. I have spent a good deal of time adjusting to the demands put upon me in organizing details and hunts rather than the pursuits I originally intended.

'If you would, consult with the experts here for details on the importance of the creatures you will be hunting.''Worms and salamanders, in any of the forms they take here in the Cape of Umbar, are not for eating. Their flesh and meat is poison to us. The boars that wallow in the mud pools along the hills of Umbar have meat decent enough for normal fare. No cook would ever use the meat for delicacies. Innkeepers and the commoners, on the other hand will happily purchase the meat for modest meals.''The worms and salamander that make the north and west reaches of their habitats have no value to an outfitter. The wild hogs of the moorlands have two uses. Their hides and coats, can be refined by skilled foresters and made into something used by outfitters like myself. Additionally, their dung is a critical component in the process of creating the tannins that we use to cure and treat the hides of nearly all animal leathers....''I do hope that my peers explain that the worms and salamanders have no value to them or their patrons, but to me and my patrons, they are a critical and vital creature. From the glands just behind their tongues, to the natural springs of tar that is their habitat; there are uses for the creatures.''You see my problem?'

He shakes his head.

'I signed onto the expedition with intent of heading into the wild, myself. I wanted to slay these creatures and earn my own glory.'

He stares off into the sky.

'There is such glory to be had in the city if you are the one who finds and defeats the great salamander, Nejagil.'

He shakes his head as if pulling himself out of a daydream.

'Look at me now, a manager of goods and service.'In the city of Umbar, the outfitters refine the silken webs of the desert spiders into fabric and dye it for use by the aristocracy. Khânai asked that you collect silks from webs and spiders to supply the outfitters in the city.Make your way north into the desert and collect thick silk webs from the spiders there. Be cautious; the spiders are cunning in their nests.Collect strands of spider-silk (${NUMBER}/16)Return the silk to Khânai at the expedition camp. She will be pleased that you helped her meet the quote placed upon her.'Merchant or magistrate, if you are a leader in Umbar, you dress in fineries offered by the outfitters who learned to refine the heavy silk of desert spiders into fine fibres and fabric.

'For those like you and me, not destined to walk the halls of leadership, we work to collect the materials that outfitters and tailors use to adorn the leaders with the trappings of their offices.

'Use caution when collecting the silk from the spiders in the desert. They are known to entrap many travellers and beasts who stumble like newborn calves through their nests.''I am impressed with the care you took in harvesting this silk. Too often, I will find frayed fibres dragged through the dust and dirt. Few understand that such carelessness ruins much of the material, reducing the price the silk earns when sold at market.

'Your efforts will earn top prices. Your reward reflects the care you took.''Search for a large nest of spiders on the western edge of the desert to the north. Take care not to disturb too much at once, lest you face the wrath of the brood.'The Heirsworn threaten the scholars who congregate at the Pot and Quill.Shûba has asked you to defeat a number of Heirsworn.

Heirsworn can be found in the ruined area of the Tor-gardens, to the north-west.Defeat Heirsworn at Dâr Jeraf and Kamîr Kateb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated a number of Heirsworn.

You should report back to Shûba at the Pot and Quill.Talk to Shûba at the Pot and Quill'Those Heirsworn have some nerve lingering in the city. The scholars who come to my establishment have suffered enough; they do not need more reasons to fear for their safety!

'If you decide to teach those fools a lesson, well... I would be happy to pay you. It is hard to miss them -- they lurk around the wreckage of the old academy and scriptorium to the north-west.''I can only hope the Heirsworn will stop darkening my doorstep from now on. If they continue pushing their luck, they shall find themselves at the bottom of a watery grave.'You learned that the scholars in Umbar City are attempting to discern how the spiders can create the silk used to construct their webs. They want to collect spider glands to further their understanding.Collect spider glands from the spiders in the nest on the western edge of the desert north of the expedition camp. When you've collected sixteen of the glands, return the glands to Khânai.Collect spider glands (${NUMBER}/16)Khânai instructed you to obtain sixteen glands from the spiders in their camp in the eastern stretch of the Cape of Umbar, and you have completed this task. Return the glands to her for your reward.'I've another request from the scholars of Umbar. An interest in learning the secrets of nature inspires scholars to learn the secret of spinning spider-silk. Scholars believe that careful study of spider glands will provide insight into how the natural process of spinning webs takes place.

'Our task requires we obtain eight pairs of undamaged glands to assist in the scholars' research.''Such strange-looking organs. I don't know what I expected them to look like... I only know that this does not meet my expectations.

'I shall see these delivered. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.''You will find the spider's brood in the nest on the edge of the desert north of the expedition. Kill the spiders and collect the glands behind the spinnerets where they release their webs.'Akûshu is concerned about the horses' distress while the caravan is stranded.Akûshu has asked you to find crunchy vegetables for the horses to snack on to relieve their distress. Crunchy vegetables can be found along the river-bank just south of Eshadûr.Collect crunchy vegetables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected crunchy vegetables for the horses at the stranded caravan to snack upon. You should give one to each horse.You have given each horse at the stranded caravan a crunchy vegetable to snack upon. You should talk to Akûshu.Talk to Akûshu'I know that when I feel distressed I find myself wanting a snack. I recall seeing some crunchy vegetables along the river-bank just south of Eshadûr. Would you mind gathering some for the horses if you can find them? The vegetables, I mean. The horses are right here.''Would you mind gathering some crunchy vegetables for the horses?''You have the vegetables? Go ahead and give one to each horse.''Wonderful! Look at how happy they all are now. It is good to meet someone else who loves horses. Thank you, ${PLAYER}!'Mizâdi is ready to assault Kûr Anzar with her Hamâti warriors. Aid her in the battle for Kûr Anzar by defeating Barkhûshim and planting banners for Renewed Hamât in Kûr Anzar.Meet with Mizâdi outside the gates of Kûr Anzar to begin the assault.Speak with Mizâdi outside Kûr Anzar to begin the assaultMake your way through Kûr Anzar, tearing down Barkhûshim banners and replacing them with banners for Renewed Hamât. Defeat All-seeing cultists throughout Kûr Anzar.Defeat All-seeing in Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Restore Mizâdi's standard throughout Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Make your way to Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar.Make your way to Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr AnzarSpeak with Mizâdi outside the tower of Kûr Anzar.Speak with Mizâdi outside the tower of Kûr Anzar'Our time has come. Okhíso and his foul Barkhûshim will rue the day he forced us from Kûr Anzar. A red dawn comes, friend. Will you aid us in our assault on Kûr Anzar?''He must be inside. We must pursue him! We will not let him escape justice!''They will fear our blades this day!

'For this is the last night they will enjoy the spoils of their ill-gotten gains in Kûr Anzar. The Barkhûshim will not live to see the breaking of the skies in dawn's light tomorrow. For it will be a blood-red dawn, a triumphant dawn. And what a glorious and terrible day it will be!'Okhíso has fled inside the tower of Kûr Anzar. Mizâdi seeks your help in pursuing him and bringing his tyrannical reign to an end.Speak with Mizâdi outside the tower in Kûr Anzar when you are ready.Speak with Mizâdi outside the tower in Kûr Anzar when you are ready to goSpeak with Mizâdi inside the tower in Kûr Anzar.Speak with Mizâdi inside the tower in Kûr Anzar'Quickly! Okhíso went inside the tower! We must go after him - he must not escape!''We must put these fires out, and save as many as we can!''We must go now, before he slips our grasp!'Kûr Anzar is aflame! Stamp out the straw fires and save as many residents as you can!Speak with Mizâdi inside the tower in order to help Kûr Anzar from going up in flame!Speak with Mizâdi about her plan to save Kûr AnzarSpeak with Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar.Speak with Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar'A curse upon Okhíso! He could not even die with dignity, instead stubbornly trying to take half of Kûr Anzar with him. I must think, and quickly.''We've done it! We've saved Kûr Anzar, ${PLAYER}! This is all I have wanted, friend. I have long wished for peace in my homeland and to restore Hamât to its former glory. There is still much to do, and a great many battles still to be won, but I have learned we must savour the wine of victory when it is proffered.

'Thank you for all you have done, for Hamât, and for me, my friend. Numûru has told me he is composing an epic ballad of your deeds. I believe even I will join in on that chorus.''Quickly, you stamp out the straw fires you see and rescue as many trapped residents as you can find. I will rally my troops to rout the rest of this accursed Barkhûshim force. Without its head, I believe it will fold quickly and without much further bloodshed.'Surodith, an Adúrhid warrior, has asked for your help culling the population of diseased boars and servals near Vartúlin, in Shakhdag and Tir Katar.Surodith asks you to cull afflicted boars and servals plagued by the Lâg Dávrit in Shakhdag and Tir Katar. Shakhdag is north-west of Vartúlin. Tir Katar is directly north of Vartúlin.Cull diseased boars in Shakhdag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cull diseased servals and caracals in Tir Katar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Surodith in Vartúlin and report your success.Speak with Surodith in Vartúlin'The Lâg Dávrit has swept through Favrathór, the forest of bone. The beasts of the forest have not been spared either, afflicted with some disease the hateful men of the south brought with them.

'It is a heavy weight on my heart, but these afflicted animals - particularly the boars of Shakhdag and the servals of Tir Katar - need to be culled from their groups, lest the whole population become afflicted. Please, help us trim the population of afflicted boars and servals north of Vartúlin, but spare any healthy beasts you see. We will rely on them to repopulate Favrathór, whenever we can reverse the effects of the Pale Blight and restore Favrathór back into Laithór, the Emerald Wood.''Thank you. It grieves me to ask for your blade to wound any animal, but it is for the good of the greater forest, that Favrathór may flourish again.'Khôltekh has asked you to help him find and catch Sêkhta. He believes Sêkhta is an archivist, a historical scholar working and living in the Tor-gardens.Speak with Khôltekh about his plan.Speak with Khôltekh about his planMove over to the right of the group of archivists.Move over to the right of the group of archivistsDefeat the false archivists!Defeat false archivists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Khôltekh.Speak with Khôltekh'I'm going to try something - move around that group of nobles to the right a bit and watch who moves.''Khmêg! He got away. Sêkhta was this close, and now he's slipped from my grasp again.

'No - wait. Wait! I know where he's going. I've solved his riddle! I know where the candle is!'Girhâzi has an idea for how to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of the lost library of Dubarâkh, and she needs your help.Talk to Girhâzi when you are ready to question Khûldim Umûn again.Complete Instance: A Captive AudienceYou and Girhâzi succeeded in getting Khûldim Umûn to tell you where the lost archive is. You should talk to Girhâzi.Talk to Girhâzi'I think I know how to get him to tell us where the archive is.'

Girhâzi has a mischievous grin and looks excited about her idea.

'It is worth a try, anyway. We will talk to him together. Let me know when you are ready to go.''Are you ready? Just go along with whatever I am saying.''Ha! That was as fun as I thought it would be. You did well! Thank you for that. I must say though, I still do not trust him, and it would be just like him to lead us into a trap. Sometimes though, walking into a trap is what must be done.

'I will go personally, as I would never send Dumûri to do a thing that I would not do myself. And I will bring Khûldim along so that whatever fate befalls us will be his fate as well.'

You ask Girhâzi how she knew you were at the Pelennor and the Black Gate. She gives you a hearty laugh and a wink.

'I didn't! Until now.'Amalíbi tasks you with recruiting the author of the letter to treason against the Ordâkhai. You are to accompany rebels to complete this task.Amalíbi asked that you accompany her forces to confront the captain near a waystation along the road from Jirush to the Wrackwade.Complete Instance: A Changing WindYou confronted the captain and learned the Ordâkhai are splintered and near total revolt. You left the captain in the hands of Sigénik and returned to Ghalburu to speak with Amalíbi.'It is clear from this letter the man cares deeply for his partner and child. Love of one's children is a potent motivator. Even the threat of loss can drive the humble to inspired acts.'

She pauses.

'The author of this letter is known to us. He often leads a small contingent to a way station between the Wrackwade and Jirush. His patrol is small but well-armed.

'I believe if we can separate this man from his patrol, we can speak with him. Perhaps we can persuade him to assist us for the price of his life and freedom.

'Will you help again?''Sigênik will meet you at the north side of the gate from the Wrackwade. He will monitor you, but will not assist. His involvement must remain unknown to ensure his safety.

'You will return to me when you have completed this task.''Sigénik pried more information from the captain after you departed. We have a course of action.

'${PLAYER}, your involvement is a more potent boon than expected. Of course, we will need to test the captain's information. If he proves reliable, then we shall need guidance on the proper way to manoeuvre our enemies towards certain hostility.'Horse traders Khâmi and Akûshu are stranded at Gha Nêkha, in the desert south-west of Eshadûr, with a broken waggon wheel.Khâmi has asked you to take their broken wheel to Iridír to have it repaired. You should pick up the waggon wheel.Take the broken wheelYou have the broken waggon wheel. You should find someone in Iridír who can repair it.The wheelwright, Aranbir, says he will make time to fix the waggon wheel if you fill in for his absent apprentice.Complete Quest: Mending the WheelYou have completed the work of the absent apprentice, and Aranbir says the wheel is repaired. You should pick up the wheel to bring it back to Khâmi at Gha Nêkha, the outpost in southern Ambarûl.Take the repaired wheelYou have taken the broken wheel to Iridír and had it repaired. You should return it to Khâmi at Gha Nêkha, south-west of Eshadûr.'Hashtal-gûr stranger! Please, would you lend us aid? I am Khâmi, and that is Akûshu with the horses. We are horse traders and came to Ambarûl in search of customers interested in purchasing our fine animals. We were led to believe that the Ordâkhai were defeated here, but that is not true! They have entirely taken over Eshadûr!

'These days, Ordâkhai are more likely to steal our horses than buy them. So we turned around to instead go to Iridír, but curse it all, one of our waggon wheels broke! Now we found ourselves stranded. Thankfully, we were near enough to this outpost to make it here.

'If you have kindness in your heart, would you take our wheel to Iridír and find someone to repair it? We cannot leave the animals and supplies unattended, and neither of us wants to be left alone here, trapped between Ordâkhai têshu and the Usan-kûni.''Would you take our wheel to Iridír and find someone to repair it? We cannot leave the animals and supplies unattended, and neither of us wants to be left alone here.''Hashtal-gûr, stranger. What do you need?'

You give the broken wheel to the wheelwright and ask if it can be repaired. The man examines the wheel.

'I am for certain capable of repairing this. What is less certain is if I have the time. I am busy and my worthless apprentice says he is too tired to work today. But I will offer you a deal. Do a few of the lad's chores, and I will make time for this wheel, and do it for free to boot.

'What say you?''Do a few of my layabout apprentice's chores, and I will make time to fix this wheel.''The wheel! Níkhu, it looks as good as new! Thank you ever so much, friend. We will soon be on our way, thanks to you.'Amalíbi sends you to Nangar for a bit of guidance on how best to use this information. Nangar suggests that a retaliatory post placed within the encampment overlooking Jirush may serve the rebels well.Amalíbi sent you to speak with Nangar about what you found and how best to proceed with this new knowledge. Return to Jirush and inform Nangar of all that transpired.Return to Jirush and speak with Nangar about AmalíbiNangar believes Jombahok can be incited by Khârdu's words. He asks that you visit Zidemel to have the proper ink made to draft a curse from Khârdu toward Jombahok.Speak with Zidemel and learn what is needed for inkZidemel sent you to the quarry north-west of Jirush to collect drams of scorpion blood to distill and create ink to create a proper curse.Collect drams of scorpion blood (${NUMBER}/8)You acquired the eight drams of scorpion blood Zidemel needs to make the ink. Return the scorpion blood to Zidemel at Jirush.Zidemel sent you to Malgat. Find him at his hovel in Jirush.Speak with Malgat about the next stepsMalgat explained that Khârdu often pays travelling hunters bounties to clear beasts from the wastes of Khûd Zagin. He asks that you acquire a bounty posting and return it to him to validate Khârdu's handwriting.Collect a bounty post written by KhârduYou found a posting near the Ordâkhai encampment south and east from Jirush. You assume it is written by Khârdu. Return the bounty posting to Malgat for confirmation.Read the posting if you wishMalgat confirmed the posting was written by Khârdu. He then directed you to deliver the ink and posting to Nangar for further instruction.Nangar is pleased with all you have done. He requests that you take the ink and the posting to Galamê. Galamê will use the ink and posting to create an Ordâkhai curse in Khârdu's hand.Galamê states he can replicate Khârdu's writing. The papyrus he has, however, is not the same quality as Khârdu uses, and to make the curse authentic he needs papyrus from the farmer, Sûlmur in Ambarûl.Speak with Sûlmur to request a sheaf of her papyrusSûlmur provided you with a sheaf of papyrus and asked for Galamê's patronage. She then pledged her sword and asked you to request the swords of Khûd Zagin, should they overcome their Ordâkhai oppressors.Galamê returns a letter to you written in Ordâkhin. He tells you it will incite violence between the two captains and asks that you deliver it to Nangar.Nangar trusts the efforts of the other elders and appreciates your role in acquiring the letter. He puts his faith in you and the other elders and sends you to Amalíbi for the final decision.'We must foment the aggression these two Ordâkhai captains harbour toward one another. The response to Jombahok needs to be subtle and pointed. A slight so cutting that Jombahok commits too much to bringing down Khârdu.

'I would like you to discuss this with Nangar in Jirush. I think the best action is a 'personal' response from Khârdu. For this, however, we will need to enlist other members of Jirush.

'Go west along the road to Jirush and tell Nangar of our plan and gain his guidance.'You share the details of your excursions for Amalíbi with Nangar. He ponders for a long moment.

'I believe our leader is correct. The response should be personal. A slight against Jombahok from Khârdu presented plainly and openly. It must be something that outs the former as a scoundrel to his men. The unrest within Jombahok's ranks ensures no choice but retaliation.

'Seek Zidemel's counsel on the best ink for an Ordâkhai curse. While you undertake the collection of whatever Zidemel requires, I will discuss with the other elders. Our time to unite and rise is nigh.''A curse, you say?

'A true curse? Or, a curse of words? These are very different. If you desire a curse of words, use scorpion blood. It is acrid. The blood burns papyrus rather than staining it like ink. When dry, it looks like caked blood. The meaning of letters written in such a manner is unmistakable - hatred.

'I know the method to distill the blood in this manner. I will need eight drams of their blood. The scorpions wander the arid lands north-west of Jirush or the crags of the buried quarry to the north-west.''Yes, yes, these will do nicely. A moment, please.'

Zidemel adds the blood to a crucible, mixes in an herb, and applies heat. He stirs briefly and then tilts the crucible, emptying its contents into an ink-well.

'Take this, ${PLAYER}. I have done my part. Now, please, leave me. I want to know no more of what is to come. I have a higher calling for which to prepare. You are to speak with Malgat now.''I did not expect aid from the north, ${PLAYER}. It is humbling that you are willing to do so much for people you hardly know.

'Travelling caravans often look to make a little extra coin, and the Ordâkhai have coin to spare. I will admit, in the past, I have directed others to take work from Khârdu. He is fond of posting bounties for pelts or meat from the desert-dwelling beasts. You will find them on the pilings and pitons surrounding his encampment in the south-east. Collect one and return it to me so that I can validate the writing is in his hand.''Unmistakable, yes? He signed the document himself. He refuses to pass work like this to his subordinates. He is a very predictable man. Likely, that predictability is the precise reason for Jombahok's easy removal of Khârdu.

'I am pleased the rebellion has found a method to turn the men against one another. Now, we must all execute our parts. Take this letter to Nangar. He awaits you at his home.''Your assistance is welcome by all the elders now. Each prepares for the coming strife before our freedom.

'You have the ink, and you have the writing example. Take these to Galamê. He will write the letter to spark the fire to engulf our enemy and open the way to our freedom.'Galamê studies the posting.

'I can match the writing, both in script and tone. However, I cannot match this papyrus. It is a finer craft than I have access to here in Jirush.

'Good fortune though, ${PLAYER}. North, in Ambarûl, there is a papyrus farmer named Sûlmur. The quality of her papyrus matches this posting. I expect the Ordâkhai captains purchased it from her.

'Go to her and collect a sheaf of papyrus and return it to me. I can then pen a response that will incite a battle between the northern and southern encampments.'You explain your need to Sûlmur. She hands you a sheaf of papyrus.

'If we are to know freedom, we must band together. I cannot head south to aid the Khûdi, but I can supply you with a small amount of my papyrus.

'Tell those who fight in the south. Should we drive our enemy out first, they will have our swords. Should they prevail, I beg they bring theirs to the north to aid us. And, when we are free, I shall expect their patronage.''Sûlmur's papyrus is impeccable. When we are free of the Ordâkhai and trade resumes in earnest, she will have my coin. Give me a moment, and I will pen a divisive letter to start a conflict.'

Galamê works quickly and quietly. Then hands a letter to you written in Ordâkhin.

'Nangar will need to trust me. The letter carries more weight if it is in Ordâkhin. I pledge, on my life, these words will drive the captains to blows.''Trust.'

Nangar smiles weakly.

'If I pass this letter to Amalíbi, and the words written by Galamê are a warning to the Ordâkh, then we are all as good as dead.'

He pauses.

'If I pass this letter to Amalíbi and the words written do incite the captains to violence, we may know freedom in my lifetime.'

He pauses again.

'My heart is heavy, and my mind swirls with myriad possibilities.'

He hands the letter back to you.

'Deliver the letter, ${PLAYER}. I vouch for Galamê. We must trust one another. All of us.'Amalíbi takes the letter and looks it over.

'What is this, ${PLAYER}? I cannot understand this. Nangar places his trust in a translator who served the Ordâkhai. Can we be so sure this is not some communication to doom us all?'

She closes her eyes. You utter one word in response, 'trust.'

'Trust? Yes. I trusted you. So, I shall trust Galamê.'You must move quickly into Angar Aragín to save Numûru!Speak with Razâl outside the tower in Kûr Anzar when you are ready.Speak with Razâl when you are ready to goSpeak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh.Speak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh'I can't believe they've taken him! We must hurry inside the Angar Aragín as well, before they torture him or attempt to sacrifice him to their dark lord.''You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}. To have two of my bravest - and most foolhardy - soldiers returned to me relatively unharmed is a boon I cannot repay.

'This night did not happen as I had imagined, but still the Barkhûshim were weakened, their stores and defences depleted. Okhíso is as weak as he will ever be. Now is the time for us to strike.''We must rescue Numûru. There's not a moment to lose!'Your scouting mission to Eshadûr revealed that the Ordâkhai are preparing waggons full of explosive powder for an attack.The Ordâkhai waggons in Eshadûr, south of the Ikorbân River, must be destroyed to protect Dumûri control of the Wrackwade.Destroy powder-laden waggons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have successfully destroyed the Ordâkhai powder-laden waggons in Eshadûr. You should now travel to the Wrackwade and talk to Ningêna, the Dumûri captain. The Wrackwade is a river crossing east of Iridír.Talk to Ningêna at the Wrackwade'To the south and east is a floating bridge at a crossing called the Wrackwade. From there we can govern passage into Ambarûl from the east by the waterway, and from the south through Khûd Zagin. The Ordâkhai have been contesting us for control of the Wrackwade, but there have only been small daily skirmishes so far.

'I suspect the Ordâkhai have decided that if they cannot control the Wrackwade, then nobody can. I think those waggons are for destroying our makeshift bridge there. We will be completely cut off from the rest of Shâgana if they succeed. We cannot allow this to happen!

'Please, if you think you are able, return to Eshadûr and destroy that black powder! After you have done this, you should go to the Wrackwade and inform the Dumûri captain there, Ningêna, of what has occurred. If you feel you are capable of helping her further, please do so. She is the widow of my son, Tâlax, and is truly like a dumûri; a daughter, to me.''Return to Eshadûr and destroy that black powder! After this is done, you should go to the Wrackwade and inform the Dumûri captain there, Ningêna, of what has occurred.''Hashtal-gûr, friend. I am glad you are here. Is there news from Iridír?'

You update Ningêna on recent events and tell her about the black powder waggons and your quest to destroy them. Once you are done, she studies you for a moment before responding.

'A foreigner does all this for the Ambarûli? You are a mysterious one, that is certain. But I cannot say that I am not grateful!'Defeat Shalblúg and his band of Orcs encamped near the top of Kûr Anzar.Defeat the Orcs encamped in Fotak-dâr near the top of Kûr Anzar, including their leader, Shalblúg. Kûr Anzar is located east of Urmâkh.Defeat Orcs in the Fotak-dâr camp within Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Shalblúg in Fotak-dârReturn to Numûru in Urmâkh with news of your triumph.Return to Numûru in Urmâkh'In my latest scouting excursion, I saw something troubling, ${PLAYER}. The Barkhûshim have allied themselves with a group of Orcs. They make their camp near the top of Kûr Anzar.

'I know not what foul cause would lead to such an allegiance, but we need to eliminate this threat as we move through Kûr Anzar. You have already done much for Renewed Hamât, but I would ask this of you. Please, defeat the Orcs in Kûr Anzar, so that we may move our citizens back there once this battle is over.

'Oh, and be careful. I saw a particularly large Orc ordering the others around. I heard one of the others call him Shalblúg. If you can, he should be your main target.''You defeated them! Excellent! We will sing of your exploits yet, my friend. You have my thanks for this, just another of your many valorous deeds you've accomplished here in Imhûlar.'Raphûz does not believe the woman is cursed by evil spirits and blames himself for her running into danger. He is torn between the promise he made to his parents and the obligation he feel he has to Ashâmi.Raphûz requested your advice. You should speak with him about his concerns and confusion.Speak with Raphûz about his concernsRaphûz explained his concerns and asked you to give him your advice.Tell Raphûz <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, you would follow your heartTell Raphûz <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, you would keep your promiseRaphûz wants to explain his decision. Speak with him at his home in Jirush.Speak with Raphûz at his home in Jirush'She is not cursed, friend. You and I both know this. Her father's superstitions aside, I drove her away.

'I would speak to you about advice on what to do.''Allow me a moment to speak, and then I will ask you a sincere question.'

He breathes in deeply.

'I made a terrible mistake. In my attempt to draw Ashâmi's attention, I drove her away. She would rather flee all she knows than be forced to speak with me at her father's behest.

'He told me she headed to the south, into an Elven grove long lost to the darkness.

'I have a new choice, my friend, duty and heart.

'Duty... the promise to my mother to seek amends for my father's name requires I stay with the Phetekâri.

'My heart begs me to seek Ashâmi, to forgo my promise and see to the life's journey without honouring my promise.

'If the choice were yours, my friend. Would you follow your heart?''From the explorations I track, I know the location is south of Jirush, hidden in a craggy depression in the land. I will go there and find Ashâmi and tell her my intent. If she rejects me, I will return and beg the Phetekâri to forgive my transgression.

'If she accepts my apology, I will have no need to return. This is my decision.'After your limited efforts in Shonith, Tharashil is moved to offer a gift to the men of Shâgana. She asks you to help her prepare the gift.Tharashil gave you an empty phial and sent you to the oasis, near the three sister trees, to collect water. She then told you to visit Aítarshun and Filadal. She suggested they would know what to do once you explained why you were there.You filled the phial with Shonith oasis water. Visit Aítarshun and Filadal and tell them why Tharashil sent you. Tharashil stated they will understand what they need to do.Aítarshun and Filadal both held the water and spoke words. You do not understand the meaning or the ritual, but both seem to believe this will aid the Men of Khûd Zagin in a time of need. Return the water to Tharashil.Tharashil returned the water to you with a warning and instruction. You are to deliver the water to Amalíbi. Tharashil does not believe Amalíbi will understand the value but believes in time she will.'You are generous and kind. I misjudged you upon your arrival. Your selfless acts are indicative of a noble spirit. I see the wisdom of the Men of Khûd Zagin in sending you as their latest emissary.

'I am bound to my people, our land, and our fate. I cannot pledge an alliance. I will, however, provide the men a gift due to your assistance here in Shonith.'

She hands you an empty phial.

'Collect water from the oasis near the three sister trees, and present it to Aitarshun and Filadal. They will know what to do. After you speak with them, return the dram of water to me, and I will provide further instructions.''Collect water from the oasis in the phial I provided. Then, speak with Aítarshun and Filadal. They will understand the meaning of this gift.''Collect water from the oasis in the phial I provided. Then, speak with Aítarshun and Filadal. They will understand the meaning of this gift.''What is this? A gift from Tharashil?'

He offers a smile.

'It is an oath.'

He presses his hands around the dram and whispers a word you cannot hear.

'I think, when the time is right, this will be of great use to the men of Khûd Zagin.'She looks at the dram and nods.

'Tharashil offers aid of another sort to the men. You did well to earn a measure of trust.'

She covers the dram with her hand and whispers and imperceptible word.

'When the time is right, this will aid the men of Khûd Zagin.'Tharashil takes the dram of water in her hands and whispers an imperceptible word.

'This water, blessed and taken from the oasis, is a remnant of the Kintai and Khûd Zagin. Present it to Amalíbi. She will rebuke us for not aiding her and value the gift less than she should. In time, she will learn its value or pass it to another who will understand.

'You earned this gift for the men of Khûd Zagin. You earned our favour. You earned our thanks. If there are more like you in this world, perhaps our time is not yet over.''You have proven there are people in this world who are pure of heart and intent. Perhaps all is not as we expected. Thank you for your aid, ${PLAYER}.''She sends me water? I need warriors, not water.'

You explain Tharashil's reasoning. A look of acceptance and understanding creeps onto Amalíbi's face as you speak.

'Leadership is filled with fraught decisions. If there is a purpose for this water, we shall learn it. For now, we wait for the seed we planted to take root.

'Thank you for trying, ${PLAYER}.'Hármelak has kept a close watch upon Khôltekh's dealings in Umbar-môkh, and she wants to ensure that his power does not threaten her own.Sharûla's manor can be found in the north-east reaches of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens.Talk to Sharûla outside her manor in the Upper WardSharûla has invited you to study the documents and ledgers she has provided for Hármelak's perusal.Examine Sharûla's ledgersExamine Sharûla's papersSharûla stands outside her manor in the north-east reaches of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens.Talk to Sharûla outside her manor in the Upper WardHármelak is inside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, waiting for your report of Sharûla's accounts.Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja'And thus the one who gave aid to my esteemed friend Khôltekh... was you after all, ${PLAYER}. Many are my eyes and ears throughout Umbar Baharbêl and beneath the surface in Umbar-môkh, and they relayed to me the aid you provided him in the matter of Sêkhta. It was a messy business, I am told. He would be a dangerous foe, would he not?

'But so it is with all of us within the Kindred, and it is important that any who think to oppose us realize it. There is a noblewoman of the city on whom I have kept watch, but of late she has had fewer coins with which to support the Kindred. Her name is Sharûla, and she keeps a manor in the north-eastern area of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens. Speak with her there and consult her ledger. She will likely be expecting someone to call upon her on my behalf, for it is the regular time for her tithe to come due.''We should not wish to disturb the honourable Sharûla overlong. She keeps a manor in the north-eastern area of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens. Speak with her there and consult her ledger. She will likely be expecting someone to call upon her on my behalf, for it is the regular time for her tithe to come due.''I am honoured to welcome an emissary of the Kindred! I expected your arrival, so I have had my servants bring my ledgers and these papers outside for your convenience. You are free to examine them, of course, but I can assure you that the Golden Queen will find all is in order, and my expected tithe is the correct amount. If anything I am giving more to the Kindred than others of my station... but it is my pleasure and I am not given to complain!''Do not convey any discontent to any... interested parties; I am too happy to express my gratitude. Hármelak will find that I am most accommodating! Examine my ledger and these papers at your leisure!''I thank you for your doubtless precious time, as I have little of my own. Can I count upon you to speak favourably of my situation to Hármelak?''As she requires. Tell Hármelak that Sharûla is her patient servant, as always.''A wealthy noble free of suspicious secrets is a suspicious sort indeed. Sharûla is hiding something. I am certain of it.'Hármelak has asked you to procure clear records from the smugglers of Tâkhdar that might shed some light on Sharûla's misdeeds.Smugglers within Tâkhdar, the Cellars of Umbar-môkh beneath the city, may possess records that will shed light upon Sharûla's misdeeds.Collect clear and straightforward records from smugglers within Tâkhdar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hármelak is inside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, waiting for you to return from Tâkhdar with proof of Sharûla's misdeeds.'We shall appear content, for a time. Then we will return to Sharûla and uncover her secrets.

'Word has come to me that she may have some connexion with smuggling activity in Tâkhdar, the Cellars of Umbar-môkh. If you engage with some of those who participate in these unlawful activities, you may recover some clear records that will connect Sharûla with their smuggling operation. This will make it easier for us to move against her, ${PLAYER}.''I have ears and eyes everywhere. Word has come to me that Sharûla may have some connexion with smuggling activity in Tâkhdar. If you engage with some of those who participate in these unlawful activities, you may recover some clear records that will connect Sharûla with their smuggling operation. This will make it easier for us to move against her, ${PLAYER}.''Yes? Speak.'

Hármelak studies the confused records you recovered from the smugglers in Tâkhdar. She looks up at you with disappointment on her face.

'Nothing here connects obviously-enough to Sharûla, but this does not change the fact that she is keeping something from us. It simply means that she is better at hiding it than she appeared.'Hármelak has not given up on proving that Sharûla has committed some misdeed, and the Golden Queen wants your continued aid in service of that aim.Hármelak wants you to return to Sharûla's manor in the north-eastern Upper Ward, on the edge of the Tor-gardens... but this time she wants you to return unannounced.Return to Sharûla's manor unannounced and unheraldedSharûla's steward, Zakhâz, guards the entrance to her manor in the Upper Ward.Talk to Zakhâz outside Sharûla's manorZakhâz appears to be struggling with a difficult decision.Wait for Zakhâz to make his decisionSharûla's steward, Zakhâz, guards the entrance to her manor in the Upper Ward.Talk to Zakhâz outside Sharûla's manor'Perhaps, should you darken her door unannounced, any enshrouded secrets might come to light.

'Earlier she was expecting an emissary from me, but now she is not. Let us see what Sharûla does when you make an unheralded call upon her, ${PLAYER}. She will not be prepared for you, and may let something slip.''We must take care of this matter. Return to Sharûla's manor in the north-eastern corner of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens. Let us see if she betrays her secret when you make an unheralded call upon her, ${PLAYER}.''Forgive this servant's confusion, but the tithe is not yet ready. Is Lady Hármelak upset with us? Oh no, I hope we have done nothing to draw her ire!'

You assure Zakhâz that as long as he speaks honestly, and has nothing to hide from the Kindred, that Hármelak will treat him and the lady of the house fairly.

'I... I... I...' he says, clearly grappling with some unsaid worry.'I beg your kind discretion, lest my lady's ire affect my stewardship. But I cannot remain silent any longer!

'I fear that Lady Sharûla desires to inflict harm upon the people of the city and upon the Kindred of the Coins!'Sharûla's steward Zakhâz told you that the lady of the house possesses a second, secret residence in Umbar-môkh beneath the city.According to Zakhâz, the entrance to Sharûla's second, secret residence is located in Tâkhdar, south of the stairs to Dâr Laja.Find Sharûla's second, secret residence in TâkhdarSupporters of Azagath Sea-shadow come and go frequently throughout Sharûla's secret residence.Defeat Azagath loyalists in Sharûla's secret residence (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A lockbox in the middle of Sharûla's secret residence may contain evidence of her support for Azagath Sea-shadow.Search the lockbox in Sharûla's secret residenceHármelak is in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja. She will be pleased to see the documents you recovered that suggest Sharûla has continued funding Azagath's assorted ventures.Zakhâz pauses for a long moment, steeling his resolve.

'You know that Azagath Sea-shadow has apparently revealed himself a traitor to the Kindred? I believe that Lady Sharûla has taken in with a crowd of supporters who desire that he be reinstated to a position of power in the city! She keeps a second, secret residence in Umbar-môkh where she meets with these loyalists and plots to overthrow the remaining members of the Kindred, including Lady Hármelak! I can keep silent no longer!

'The entrance to her secret residence is in Tâkhdar, south of the Meeting-hall stairs. Please, my friend... please show mercy to my lady. She has been led astray by the venomous whispers of those who follow Azagath. I know she will repent of her misdeeds.''Once again, I beg your kind discretion, lest my lady's ire affect my stewardship. The entrance to her secret residence is in Tâkhdar, south of the Meeting-hall stairs. Please, my friend... please show mercy to my lady. She has been led astray by the venomous whispers of those who follow Azagath. I know she will repent of her misdeeds.''News of your perilous encounter and Sharûla's treachery fast reached Dâr Laja. It is precisely as I believed it to be: there are treacherous forces arrayed against us and against the city.

'Azagath has fled, but his supporters remain, and they can do us harm. Khôltekh faced his own opponent, but Sêkhta was a single foe. My opponents endanger all of Umbar Baharbêl, ${PLAYER}. You will help me root them out and end their villainy.

'But I must prepare, and make my plans. When next you return to me we will learn the extent of Sharûla's traitorous reach. She may not be the only member of her class whose wealth is a mask for the corruption beneath, a gilded veneer on something distasteful. Until then, keep watch. The shadow cast by Azagath has grown long in the city, and beneath it.'Concerned about the possibility that others among the residents of Umbar Baharbêl might seek to assist Azagath Sea-shadow, Hármelak wants her guards to be equipped with better weapons.Hármelak's order of fresh swords for her personal guardsmen is ready to be picked up inside the Swain's Guild-hall.Collect Hármelak's order of shiny swords from the Swain's Guild-hall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Jaith stands guard outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja. He is waiting to receive the swords Hármelak ordered from the Swain's Guild-hall.Hármelak is inside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, waiting for your report that her swords have been delivered.Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja'The corruption might run deep, but we shall remain composed for the public. We know that Sharûla met with supporters of Azagath in her secret residence beneath the city, and funded some of the Sea-shadow's dealings; perhaps it was her wealth that enabled him to escape the Kindred's justice, ${PLAYER}.

'I did not remain idle during these past few days. If we are to remain safe here in the Meeting-hall, I need my guardsmen to have the finest equipment made for them. To that end, I ordered four swords to be made, and they are ready to be collected.

'Go now to the Swain's Guild-hall and retrieve these swords. Once you have them, give them to Jaith outside Dâr Laja and he will distribute them among my guards.''You must not delay. Go now to the Swain's Guild-hall and retrieve the swords I have ordered. Once you have them, give them to Jaith outside Dâr Laja and he will distribute them among my guards.'Jaith appraises the collection of shiny swords you have brought.

'These swords seem well-made, but are they really any better than the ones already wielded by Lady Hármelak's personal guardsmen? The only difference I can see is that these are much shinier.'Jaith nods in recognition.'What is it? You have collected the swords I commissioned from the Swain's Guild-hall? Good. It was a costly order, but the price of security is a price I will not balk at... not when treachery has taken root in my city, and beneath it.'Hármelak has heard there might be associates of Sharûla in the market of Kheb Hanût beneath the city, and she wants you to root them out.Hármelak asked you to speak to merchants in the market of Kheb Hanût in north-west Tâkhdar and learn if any of them share Sharûla's loyalty to Azagath.Talk to Dayêri in Kheb HanûtHármelak asked you to speak to merchants in the market of Kheb Hanût in north-west Tâkhdar and learn if any of them share Sharûla's loyalty to Azagath.Talk to Nagamûn in Kheb HanûtHármelak asked you to speak to merchants in the market of Kheb Hanût in north-west Tâkhdar and learn if any of them share Sharûla's loyalty to Azagath.Talk to Okhmath in Kheb HanûtHármelak asked you to speak to merchants in the market of Kheb Hanût in north-west Tâkhdar and learn if any of them share Sharûla's loyalty to Azagath.Talk to Lashêm in Kheb Hanût'Foes of the city will be dealt with... harshly. Now that my guardsmen are better-equipped, they will apprehend Sharûla and bring her to me. No, you do not need to wait, ${PLAYER}. I have something else for you.

'I believe some of Sharûla's associates are vendors in the market of Kheb Hanût, beneath the city. Speak to these merchants and determine their loyalties, if you can. It may be they will let something slip that will connect them to Sharûla or to Azagath.

'If anyone asks you to lend your aid to them, I suggest that you do. They may reveal their true hearts to you in a moment of gratitude.''It is our duty to care for the people of Umbar. If we are to fulfil this duty, we must learn if Sharûla's corruption extends to the merchants of Kheb Hanût.''And at what cost to me do these kind favours arrive? The Golden Queen never does anything for free, or so it is said.

'I will not be in her debt. Not for any sum!''And at what cost to me do these kind favours arrive?''No, no, no, nothing needed, nothing desired, nothing hoped! I simply wish to not draw the attention of the Golden Queen, lest she take offence at me and send me to the gaols, or worse!''No, no, no, nothing needed, nothing desired, nothing hoped!''If ever I needed a favour from Hármelak Golden-hand, have her douse me in water and face my body towards the sea. On that day it will be already too late for me!''If ever I needed a favour from Hármelak Golden-hand, have her douse me in water and face my body towards the sea.''I am honoured to be thought of at all by a member of the Kindred! Just a few days ago I had the pleasure of speaking with one of the Temámir, a friend of Kinsman Khôltekh himself! And now to be greeted politely by an emissary of Hármelak, the Golden Queen? These are remarkable days indeed!'The merchant Lashêm has a request to make of you concerning some of his parcels that were "misplaced."Lashêm's parcels were "misplaced" by a number of smugglers operating out of Sâl Bajat, and he needs you to recover them and teach the miscreants he will not be intimidated.Defeat smugglers operating in Tâkhdar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Recover Lashêm's misplaced parcels in Sâl Bajat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lashêm is waiting for you to deliver his misplaced parcels to him at Kheb Hanût, in Tâkhdar.'In times of unrest, one must rely on healthy trade. Kinswoman Hármelak must know this as well, for she is the most wealthy merchant in all these lands, is she not?

'I have become modestly successful in the trade of dried squid, a staple of the Umbari diet, but recently some of my parcels have been misplaced. Well, I say "misplaced," but in truth they have been stolen and carried into Sâl Bajat. The smugglers nearby must believe they can use my goods to great profit, which has left me in a predicament.

'Will you help me deal with these villains and recover my misplaced parcels? I would not trouble the Lady Hármelak with this personally, of course, but you are here, after all...''In times of unrest, one must rely on healthy trade. Will you help me deal with those smugglers and recover my misplaced parcels? I would not trouble the Lady Hármelak with this personally, of course, but you are here, after all...'Lashêm smiles broadly as you approach.

'You recovered my parcels! I thank you, friend. The dried squid contained within will bring me a fair profit, and I will raise a toast to the Golden Queen when I have a moment to do so.'Hármelak moves to maintain order in Umbar-môkh as she does in Umbar Baharbêl above.The sound of approaching footsteps echoes throughout Kheb Hanût.The sound of approaching footsteps!Hármelak's guards hold Lashêm at swordpoint.Talk to Hármelak's guardsmanLashêm stands in disbelief, surrounded by guardsmen.Talk to Lashêm in Kheb HanûtHármelak is in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja. Perhaps she will explain to you why Lashêm has been apprehended.Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja'What is this?''Grab him! This man is wanted for questioning by the Kindred of the Coins, ${PLAYER}. He is a known associate of a traitor to the city who has confessed to their ill deeds; they used their mercantile connexions to transport weapons through Umbar-môkh and into the city above. Their plan was to arm dissidents with these weapons and to ambush Lady Hármelak and the other members of the Kindred!''Grab him! Keep him from escaping!''On my life and livelihood, I did not know of any plan, any ambush! These are lies, lies! I know nothing about a conspiracy such as this! What villain claims to work with me? I have done nothing of the sort! I love Lady Hármelak, and the Kindred, with all of my heart!'

Lashêm stares at you with wild eyes, desperate to escape the snare in which he is caught.

'Search my parcels! Every one contains dried squid, and nothing else! Someone is seeking to destroy my good reputation! ${PLAYER}, my friend, tell Lady Hármelak I am innocent of this! Please, you must!'Lashêm stands in stunned silence. Only the words of Hármelak can free him now.'Poor timing for an ambush indeed, if these whispers of revolt prove true. There are eyes on us now.'

You ask Hármelak why she sent her guardsmen to apprehend the merchant Lashêm, and tell her that he did not seem obviously guilty of the crimes. She stares back at you steadily.

'Did you check the bottom of those crates, ${PLAYER}? Beneath the piles of dried squid, someone could have hidden anything. It is safer this way. After all, he admitted he spoke with a friend of Khôltekh only days ago. What might have been the topic of conversation, do you think?'

You ask Hármelak if Sharûla's confession truly implicated the merchant Lashêm, and she waves a hand.

'You have still not learned the way of things in this land, ${PLAYER}. There is gold here, it is true, but an outward appearance is not always the truth, as Sharûla's misdeeds teach us and I told you before. Sometimes a thing possesses only the veneer of wealth and status, the thinnest gilded surface, and it hides something much uglier.'

As Hármelak bids you farewell, you consider the meaning of her words and think she may be right: there is something ugly at work in Umbar.A small moment of peace has given Mizâdi time to speak with Amalíbi, to see the consequences of her decisions.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír when you are ready to go.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír when you are ready to goSpeak with Mizâdi in Iridír.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír'Everything is so calm in this moment, I scarcely recognize it. These past few days have been a whirlwind. I have not had a chance to stop the winds and listen, to find peace.

'I would have words with Amalíbi. She said many things in that hall, and I agree with all of them. Many of the things I said I do not agree with, but such is passion. I have many mistakes for which I must atone. Would you accompany me to see her?''I hear her words, but I do not yet feel them. Perhaps in time I will.

'Thank you, friend. Your presence has been a constant comfort, and one for which I am quite grateful.''Let us go then, to Amalíbi's encampment, to mend what wounds we can.'The battle has been won, but this victory tastes bitter: Bârshud intends to cut through all of Khûd Zagin and Ambarûl with his army. Warn Amalíbi in Ghalbûru and Girhâzi in Iridír of his advance.Warn Amalíbi at Ghalbûru's highest point about Bârshud's advance. Ghalbûru is located within Khûd Zagin, in the Ikorbân Valley.Warn Amalíbi in Ghalbûru about Bârshud's advanceWarn Girhâzi in Iridír about Bârshud's advance. Iridír is located within Ambarûl, in the Ikorbân Valley.Warn Girhâzi in Iridír about Bârshud's advanceSpeak with Mizâdi in Iridír.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír'What a fool I was. Letting Bârshud cloud my emotions and stoke this fire. I should have seen his plan for what it was.

'Quickly, you must warn Amalíbi in Ghalbûru and Girhâzi in Iridír. I have had some words with each and both are hearty and passionate fighters who want what is best for Shagâna.

'I will finish here and then leave with Razâl and Numûru for Iridír. I will meet you there. We will have much to discuss, I'm afraid.''Oh now the Shâra will deign to meet with me? Now that my soldiers are bloodied, dead, scattered to the winds and lost in the Khûd? Where was this Shâra when I sent out my request for aid?

'I will meet her in Iridír, if only so she knows the full weight of her mistake.

'She will hear my fury, have no doubt in that.''Thank you, friend, for speaking with them and convincing them both to meet. We shall now gather in the hall, and quickly, as time is not our ally.''Bârshud has just toed the line into fair Ambarûl. We were just about to convene a war council on our response to this aggression.

'Of course we will meet with Mizâdi, and Amalíbi. We will accept all the help we can get in repelling this invasion.'Nukûsh the blacksmith has asked for your help in accomplishing his daily tasks, as his apprentice has joined Mizâdi's warriors.Acquire iron ore and wood from outside Urmâkh to the east for Nukûsh, the blacksmith in Urmâkh.Mine iron ore for smithing (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Pick up wood for Nukûsh's forge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring gathered wood and ore to Nukûsh in Urmâkh.Feed the wood into the fire in the forge.Feed the wood into the fire in the forgeCollect the swords Nukûsh has forged for deliver to Numûru.Collect Nukûsh's newly forged swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Deliver Nukûsh's newly forged swords to Numûru in Urmâkh. Numûru can be found by Urmâkh's eastern gate.Speak again with Nukûsh in Urmâkh.Speak with Nukûsh in Urmâkh'The fires are hot and there's work to be done! My apprentice ran off, off to join Mizâdi's band, he did. I don't mind a good war, but not when it hurts the forge. How am I supposed to make blades for Mizâdi when there's no one to help gather ore for the swords and collect wood for the fires?

'You want to help? Well there may be some good left in this world after all. You can start by gathering some wood and ore, we have plenty of both outside of Urmâkh, to the east. Watch out for the jackals, they've been roaming closer and closer to the city proper.''Ah, that's enough to get me ahead for once. You move quick. You remind me of myself at a young age. Nice enough for you to help an old man with his tasks. I appreciate it. Anytime you want to come back, there's a spot at the forge for you.''There you are. Well you've gathered plenty of both at least. Leave them there, I'll take care of the ore. Add the wood to the fire, it's getting low. Then you can bring these swords to Numûru. Hope you don't mind sweating, there's no loafing here.''My thanks to you. It's been fair too long since we had fresh blades. These will cut the Barkhûshim quite well, and any others who draw Mizâdi's ire. Give my regards, and that of the Subuzûri, to Nukûsh.'Angârmu has asked you to recover his beloved pet who has yet to come home.Angârmu has asked you to help him find his missing pet, Ershûr.Find the camp that Angârmu mentionedLook for Angârmu's pet, Ershûr, at the camp.Find Angârmu's beloved pet, ErshûrReturn to Angârmu in Malgâma near Zikrum-dûl with his beloved pet, Ershûr.'A visitor! A welcome sight! I ask of you to find my beloved pet. My beloved Ershûr. He wandered somewhere I know not.

'He must be at the camping spot! Yes! That is his favourite spot. Ershûr must have ran off to go there. But I can not go, I must stay here.

'You must go to his camping spot near the river to the south-east for me and find dear Ershûr. Find him, and bring him back to me so that I can keep him safe.

'And tell him... tell him I miss him dearly.''You found him! My sweet Ershûr. I have missed you!'

Angârmu takes the rock from you and hugs it with a wide smile on his face.

'You are a true friend. To me and my dear Ershûr. Thank you. I can now be certain he is safe from harm.'As you make your way behind the secret door, more of Sêkhta's forces rise to stop you!Fight off Sêkhta's forces!Defeat Sêkhta's men (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search for clues about Sêkhta and his true identity.Find Sêkhta's clothesFind Sêkhta's booksFind Sêkhta's noteKhôltekh has asked you back to his house once more, so he can think on the riddle of this key and access to Dâr Sêkhta.Accompany Khôltekh to his study.Accompany Khôltekh to his studyListen to Khôltekh's thoughts on the key.Listen to Khôltekh's thoughts on the keyAsk Khôltekh about his thoughts on the matter.Ask Khôltekh about his thoughts on the matterListen to Khôltekh's explanation.Listen to Khôltekh's explanationListen to Khôltekh's explanation.Listen to Khôltekh's explanation'I have bad news, ${PLAYER}. I've solved our riddle.'Belondor has asked you to go to Umbar Baharbêl's Fleet-fast ward and handle two problems for him.A group of ruffians is causing trouble in the Fleet-fast near the Soldiers' Mess-hall. You should go there and teach them a lesson.Defeat Fleet-fast ruffians (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})At the nearby docks in the Fleet-fast, there is a dispute going on at one of the ships. A fruitmonger and a deck-steward are arguing about fruit shipment. You should find where they are.Find Râkariz and the deck-stewardYou have found Râkariz and the deck-steward arguing about the shipment of fruit. You should inspect the fruit to see its condition.Inspect the shipment of fruitYou have inspected the fruit in question, and it is indeed rotten. You noticed a stamp that indicated the fruit came from Khûtra. You should confront the fruitmonger Râkariz.Talk to RâkarizYou have inspected the fruit and confronted Râkariz with the knowledge that provisions from Khûtra have somehow been corrupted after the fall of Mâkhda Khorbo. You should return to Belondor and tell him what you learned.Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja'${PLAYER}, I'm glad you are here. I have a few concerns with which I was hoping to receive your assistance.'

Belondor looks excessively tired but clearly has no intention to rest.

'I am tied up here in Dâr Laja, hearing the concerns of the people and doing my best to help them. Meanwhile, I'm also expected to handle issues in the Fleet-fast when I am not at sea. Much of my fleet is out patrolling the coast, looking for signs of Azagath and Nakási. I was hoping you would be available to handle something for me.

'I have received reports of ruffians on the docks, causing trouble in the area near the Soldiers' Mess-hall. I would like you to go there and... discourage them from doing that.'

He gives you a wink that makes it clear he wants you to rough them up.

'Umbar is a land of tough people and sometimes this is the only way to get your point across. Not far from that same area, there is a dispute going on that I would like you to investigate. One of our ships is preparing for departure and was bringing provisions aboard when the deck-steward noticed that all of the newly purchased fruit was rotten. The fruitmonger, a man named Râkariz, argues that the fruit was fine when he sold it to us.

'I would like you to inspect the fruit shipment for me and determine who is in the right. I recommend dealing with the ruffians first though, as they are the more pressing matter.'The fruit is indeed rotten and inedible. You notice a stamp indicating that the fruit originated in Khûtra.'I will tell you the same thing I have been telling everyone! I am not at fault! The fruit was good when I unloaded it. It must have been mistreated by the Fleet-watch.'

You tell Râkariz that you noticed that the fruit came from Khûtra. You have been there and happen to know that Khûtra has been plagued with disease and sickness since the collapse of Mâkhda Khorbo. You can see in his eyes that he has been caught, but he says nothing else to you.'Is everything settled, then?'

You tell Belondor that you handled the ruffians, and that the fruit was likely rotten before it even left Khûtra.

'Khûtra, you say? Yes, I have heard about their issues there. Thank you for clearing this up. I appreciate your help as always, ${PLAYER}.'Belondor would like to start a Widows-and-Orphans fund and has asked for your help in retrieving his savings.Belondor has asked you to enter Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl, and locate his secret cache of savings.Find the location Belondor describedYou have found the location Belondor described as the location of his hidden cache. You should retrieve the treasure.Collect Belondor's cacheYou have collected Belondor's secret cache from its hiding place in Ilmabiri. You should bring it to Belondor in Dâr Laja.'I have oft been thinking about the suffering that continues in this city, ${PLAYER}. The Empire of Ordakh, the Church of the All-seeing, and the Heirs of Castamir have all ruled here with an iron fist, and that fist was covered in blood. Though many of the Corsairs lost at the Harlond were not good people, many in the city are still suffering from the loss of loved ones.

'That is why I have decided to use my personal savings to seed a fund that will help support those left behind. They suffer needlessly, and I will do what I am able for those who are innocent. This savings of mine is not held in a bank. I have kept it hidden should Mêshka and I need to flee the city again.

'It is always good to have a backup plan, but it bothers me greatly knowing that I have treasures hidden away doing nothing when it could be helping people in need. I would like to entrust to you the task of retrieving it,  as there are dangers involved that I have no doubt you can handle. The coffer is located in the north-east part of the sewers. I will mark its location on your map.''There it is. You have done a good deed today, ${PLAYER}. Thank you. This will go a long way to ease their suffering.'Mêshka has asked for your help with a secret project.Mêshka has requested that you meet her at the Fleet-watch Tavern, located at the southern end of the Fleet-fast, across from the Old Bastion Inn.Talk to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch TavernMêshka is commissioning a memorial for the crew of the Rebuke and has asked for your assistance in choosing a location.Scout near the Sailors' Mess-hallScout the gate near the Parade GroundScout between the Gate of Sorrows and the StûnaScout near the Fleet-gateScout near the Lord's GateYou have scouted several possible locations for Mêshka. You should return to her at the Fleet-watch Tavern at the southern end of the Fleet-fast to tell her your findings.Talk to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern'While you were gone Mêshka came to visit and she said she would like to meet with you. She wouldn't tell me what it was about, but I didn't get the feeling that she plans to have you killed. I wouldn't worry,' he says with a chuckle, '...too much.'

'She said that you will be able to find her at the Fleet-watch Tavern in the Fleet-fast. Be safe!''${PLAYER}, I admit that I am a little surprised to see you. I would not blame you if you had no desire to associate with me.'

She cocks an eyebrow and gives you a measuring look.

'I will not apologize, however. You must understand that I will do whatever is necessary to protect my husband and his interests.'

She takes a casual sip of her wine before continuing.

'Speaking of his interests, he told me that you have been assisting him of late, so you have probably noticed that he avoids what needs to be done; prioritizing trivialities while Azagath and Nakási escape without consequences. They must be found, and they must be made to pay the price for their betrayal. For this to happen, we must awaken Belondor so he sees things as they are, not as his pain tells him. He loves passionately, but he hurts with the same intensity. He has been hiding from himself behind his work, not allowing himself to feel his grief.

'I am commissioning a memorial in tribute of the crew of the Iskánta, Belondor's ship. Rebuke, in the Westron tongue. Will you help me with this? I have several locations around the Fleet-fast in mind but have not been able to decide. Would you visit each location and tell me your opinion of them?''You return with opinions, I hope?'

You tell the noblewoman your opinion on each location.

'Thank you for your time and thoughts. I will take them into consideration.'While talking with Mêshka, she notices that you are being watched.Mêshka has spotted that the two of you are being watched. She suggests you confront the man at the Fleet-watch Tavern at the south end of the Fleet-fast.Confront the person spying on youTabrím, a member of the Order of the Eagle has asked you to bring an offer to Belondor.Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja'Be careful, ${PLAYER}. We are being watched. Is he here to spy upon you or me? Since you are the one who is armed, confront him, and see what he wants.''Hoi there, ${PLAYER}. Yes, I know who you are. You can call me Tabrím.'

The man gazes at you for a moment with an expression you can't read.

'I understand that you have the ear of Belondor of Langstrand, and you are a friend of the king. I am from the Order of the Eagle and would like you to present Belondor with an offer. We have uncovered some information on the whereabouts of Azagath Sea-shadow and Nakási Wave-reaper.

'We would share this information with Belondor in exchange for him agreeing to meet with an emissary of Prince Imrahil. He need not agree to anything other than to meet and to listen. Will you do this?''Welcome back! I see you have survived your meeting with my wife,' Belondor says jokingly.

You quietly tell him of the offer from the Order of the Eagle and his expression darkens.

'No. I cannot have my loyalty to Umbar called into question. What information could they have, I wonder?'

He sighs and you see the exhaustion return to his features.

'I need some time to think about it.'Belondor has asked you to go to the Fleet-fast on his behalf and collect dues from the merchants there.Talk to the traders in the Fleet-fast and collect their dues.Collect dues from the fruit peddlerCollect dues from the cloth dealerCollect dues from the fishmongerCollect dues from the Old Bastion InnkeeperCollect dues from the Fleet-watch TavernYou have collected the dues from the traders in the Fleet-fast. You should return to Belondor in Dâr Laja.Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja'I have another task for you, should you be willing.'

You quietly ask Belondor if he has decided whether or not to accept the offer from the Order of the Eagle.

'I have not. There are many things to consider. The cost may outweigh the benefit. Speaking of costs, life goes on and there are still things that need doing in the Fleet-fast.

'Traders that are permitted to sell their goods and services within the Fleet-fast are required to pay regular dues to be allowed to do so. When I am not at sea, this is something I like to do personally. It is good to be seen and to meet them in person, but the additional workload brought on by the re-opening of Dâr Laja has been taxing.

'You would be helping me a great deal if you would collect these dues for me. If any of them give you trouble, I guarantee that a little bit of rough handling will convince them that paying you is as good as paying me.''Oh yes, of course! Here you are.''Where is Belondor? I will not pay you, outlander!''Oh yes, I have it right here.''Is it time for dues again already? Here, this should cover it.''Do you mistake me for a fool? I don't give money away to strangers!''Excellent, I knew I could count on you ${PLAYER}.'Mêshka has requested your help again at the Fleet-watch Tavern at the south end of the Fleet-fast.Meet with Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern.Talk to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch TavernMêshka has asked you to visit each of the surviving family members of the crew of the Rebuke and invite them to the memorial she arranged.Talk to Ansham, Talkênza's wifeTalk to Bekhír, Khalmôz's sonTalk to Okhâb, Hâkraph's brotherTalk to Pârnakh, Mairan's motherTalk to Imâra, Sallax's wifeYou have invited the families of the slain crew members of the Rebuke. You should return to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern.Talk to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch TavernEverything for the memorial has been prepared. You should talk to Mêshka when you are ready to attend.Talk to MêshkaThe memorial is now complete. It looks like Belondor wants to talk to you.Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja'I don't know what this is about, but now I grow suspicious. Mêshka says she would like to meet with you again at the Fleet-watch Tavern. Off with you, before I decide to have you followed,' he says with a wink.'${PLAYER}, I am glad you made it! The memorial is almost ready to go. The last bit of business that needs to be tended to is the invitations. Here is a list of surviving family members of the crew that reside in the city. Please pay each of them a visit and invite them to the memorial. In the meantime I will see to the finishing touches and collect Belondor. Return to me here when you are ready.''A memorial? How thoughtful. Of course, I will be there.''I will do anything for Belondor and Mêshka. Allow me to go get cleaned up, and I will be there.''A memorial? You know, I think that would be very nice. Yes, you can count on me to be there.''How generous of them to pay for a memorial! Yes, I would love to go and see it.''I suppose I should sober up then, eh?'

She laughs without joy.

'Yes, I will attend.''Everyone has been invited? It seems we are all ready then. Talk to me again when you are ready to go.''Are you ready? Let us get this over with.''This is not how I expected today to go, my friend.'

Belondor forces a small smile, and looks you in the eye.

'I will meet with the Order of the Eagle, and see what they have to offer.'Belondor has agreed to a clandestine meeting with the Order of the Eagle and has asked you to accompany him.Travelling separately, Belondor has asked you to meet Tabrím and himself in Umbar-môkh at a place in Tâkhdar; the Cellars, east of Tilmakhím.Find the meeting place in Tâkhdar; the CellarsYou have arrived in Umbar-môkh, where you are to join Belondor in meeting with Tabrím. You should talk to Belondor.Talk to Belondor in Umbar-môkhYou have arrived in Umbar-môkh, where you have joined Belondor and Tabrím. You should see what Tabrím has to say.Talk to TabrímTabrím has revealed that the Order of the Eagle knows that Azagath and Nakási were preparing to travel by land, not by sea. He put forth the Order's theory that the two went to Mâkhda Khorbo to retrieve something. Identifying what that was should help reveal their destination. You should talk to Belondor.Talk to Belondor'${PLAYER}, I would like you to come with me to this meeting. I don't truly think Prince Imrahil has evil intentions, but in my heart, I don't think I will ever be able to forget that the Steward of Gondor, whom I served faithfully, ordered my death and sent a man I loved like a brother to do it. The experience has made me cautious, to say the least.

'If you will accompany me, we should travel separately to not arouse suspicion. I am to meet this Tabrím fellow in Umbar-môkh at a place in Tâkhdar; the Cellars, east of Tilmakhím. Meet us there.''I am relieved you made it. Let us hear what this spy for Gondor has to say.''Thank you for agreeing to our offer. I was not sure you would accept, but I am grateful for it. We can work out the details of the emissary at a later date. Enough time has been wasted already, and the longer we wait, the further away the Sea-shadow gets.'

Tabrím speaks calmly, like a man in full control, but you can see that he is sweating nervously.

'This is what the Order has learned. Azagath and Nakási were seen outside of the city, gathering supplies for a journey overland, which is why your scout ships have found nothing. We have a theory that when you... they fled to Mâkhda Khorbo, it was no mere coincidence that they went to a temple of Sauron.

'We believe it is possible that they went to the temple to retrieve something.  Some evil relic perhaps. Some knowledge or power that they needed. If you happen to know - or can find out, what they went to Mâkhda Khorbo for, it would surely reveal where they went.''This is unexpected news, ${PLAYER}. I was shortsighted and had assumed they would have fled by sea. I also assumed that the only purpose of going to Mâkhda Khorbo was its convenience. I was not privy to any plan they had.

'I see now that they planned to use me, and my crew as a delaying tactic all along, else I would have known of their plans.'

A new sense of resolve settles over Belondor, and he nods to himself.

'It is unavoidable. ${PLAYER}, we must return to Mâkhda Khorbo and see what we can learn there. I had hoped to never set foot in that evil place again, but visiting that place only in my nightmares will not help us. Would you accompany me? We should go now before my courage fails me.'Belondor has asked you to accompany him as he returns to Mâkhda Khorbo in search of clues leading to Azagath and Nakási.Belondor is ready to face his fears and return to Mâkhda Khorbo. He has asked you to accompany him.  You should talk to him when you are ready.Talk to Belondor in Umbar-môkh; the NeathsAfter returning to Mâkhda Khorbo with Belondor, you discovered that Azagath and Nakási took from the temple a map of inland areas east of Umbar. You should talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall.Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja'Are you prepared to accompany me to Mâkhda Khorbo? Let me know when you are ready. I want to be finished with this business.''Are you ready ${PLAYER}? Let us make haste before my courage fails me.''Thank you my friend for all you have done. I cannot imagine what scheme they have put in motion, but they must be stopped whatever it is. There will be hard work ahead of us, but Azagath and Nakási will pay for their betrayal.'Mizâdi requests your presence in investigating a strange report she has received from her scouts.Speak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh. Urmâkh can be found in Imhûlar, which is within the Ikorbân Valley.Speak with Mizâdi in UrmâkhSpeak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh. Urmâkh can be found in Imhûlar, which is within the Ikorbân Valley.Speak with Mizâdi in UrmâkhMizâdi, Shâra of Renewed Hamât, requests your presence in Urmâkh. She calls for your aid in investigating a disturbing report she has received from her scouts to the south.'Thank you for your haste in seeking me out. I received a disturbing report from one of my scouts that I would discuss with you.'Another messenger from southern Imhûlar has come to call on Mizâdi with dire news.Speak with the scout Nimasi in Kûr Anzar.Speak with Nimasi in Kûr AnzarTake the banner Nimasi has brought from the south.Take the banner Nimasi has brought from the southGive the strange banner to Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar.Get Numûru's opinion on the situation.Get Numûru's opinion on the situationSpeak with Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar.Speak with Mizâdi in Kûr AnzarLet Nimasi know Mizâdi's decision.Let Nimasi know Mizâdi's decisionRelay Nimasi's gratitude to Mizâdi.Relay Nimasi's gratitude to Mizâdi'It appears one of my scouts has a message for me near the western gate. Would you receive them and see to their message?

'My mind is still more a whirling storm than I'd like to admit from our trip to Esh-kimâkhi.''Hashtal-gûr, favoured outsider. I would request an audience with my Shâra, though I know it not proper. The situation I find myself in is that dire.

'The scout who brought you news of a southern incursion not so long ago, Surâsh? She is one of the scouts with which I patrol. She has herself now vanished. We were supposed to meet at a certain hilltop two nights ago. In her place I found this strange banner. I believe it to be the same standard you found with her not long before. She told me the story.

'Would you ask the Shâra if she can spare some forces to investigate Surâsh's disappearance? We southern scouts are being picked off one by one like zizani. I fear the worst for Surâsh, and, if I'm honest, for myself.''So strange. This is indeed the same banner you and Surâsh brought me. Who could be doing this?

'I need to think on this for a moment. You should ask Numûru his feelings on the matter.''What an interesting story! This is a simple matter, indeed. Nothing that some skull-crushing can't fix and quickly, if I do say so myself.

'Were it up to me, and not my queen, I would accompany this scout south, find the blasted fools scattering their distasteful and ugly artistry hither and yon, and split them in twain with a good iron blade. I know Mizâdi prefers me here in Kûr Anzar, however, to assist with the rebuilding.

'Perhaps you can see to the skull-crushing this time, ${PLAYER}?''I should hope there will be no need for skull-crushing, Numûru's wishes notwithstanding.

'You were able to quickly find the missing scouts last time, so I believe you, ${PLAYER}, are the perfect one to go with Nimasi. Hopefully this conclusion is a happier one than that of the other scouts. Will you help Nimasi?

'If so, please, tell Nimasi you will go down to the south to investigate this disappearance.''I knew our Shâra was both just and benevolent! Please thank her for me, and thank you, for your eloquence in relaying this need.

'I will meet you just outside of Zahûmakh, the marsh to the south. That's where I found the new standard, and should be where we start our investigation for her.

'I will ride out now, and meet you down there. Please thank the Shâra for me.''You are the one to be thanked, not I. You will be the one going into danger, so my gratitude is with you for that. As it has each time you have braved your skin for ours.

'As to Nimasi and Surâsh, I must look after my people, or what kind of Shâra am I?'Raphûz informed you he must move south along the dry river to a place called the Crossing of Sílabal or the Wrackwade. He wants to sit and speak with you again.Raphûz wants to sit with you and discuss over a smoke and food about all that has transpired since his arrival in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete the Instance: A New PostRaphûz was gone in the morning, having headed south to the Wrackwade. Find him there to see how he fares.Speak with Raphûz at his post in Wrackwade'In my excitement over the news of the revenge wrought in my father's name, I forgot to tell you I was reassigned to an outpost south-east of Iridír along the dry river near the Crossing of Sílabal, also called the Wrackwade. I will leave as soon as I am prepared.

'Should you find yourself in the encampment there, visit me. I will treat you to a meal and a smoke.''Let us enjoy the night while we can. Tomorrow will take me further into these lands, and who is to know my fate.''Did you see? She is as beautiful and free as she appeared from a distance. She thanked us for caring for and nursing her fawn back to health. My friend, I confess I am at a loss for words. She said 'Khûd Zagin, the land to the south.' I must consult with the people of this camp and learn their ways.

'I would very much like to speak with her again.'Malgat explained he needed some time to complete a gift for you. He asked to wait for some time and then return to him for your reward.Malgat offered to provide you a gift. You only need wait a little while for him to finish his work. Adventure elsewhere for a few minutes and then return to him in Jirush.Let Malgat complete his workEnough time has passed. Malgat is likely done with the work on your gift. Make your way to his location in Jirush to claim your gift.Return to Malgat at his home in Jirush to receive his gift'You inspire me, ${PLAYER}. I shall begin my work on a reward suitable for the efforts you undertook for me and all Jirush. Please return to me when you are able. It will take me only a short while to do what I must. I promise the reward is worth the wait.''It is good to see you again, friend. Please, allow me a few more moments and I will have my work completed.''As I said, you inspired me. I created not one, but three works. Please take your time and choose the one you feel is most fitting for you.

'Again, friend, thank you for assisting our outpost.'Malgat asked if you would help him with a personal task. He misses the adventure of his youth and asks you to help him recapture a small piece of that wonder.Malgat asked you to recover the corpse of the Eldest of Samarsûg in the marshes in northern Khûd Zagin, the corpse of Shûhuz from a den west of Jirush, and the corpse of Grigazug from the ruined temple Is Dara west of Jirush.Collect the Eldest of Samarsûg's corpseCollect Shûzhuz's corpseCollect Girgazug's corpseYou defeated the Eldest of Samarsûg, the jackal Shûhuz, and the scorpion Girgazug. You collected their corpses, as Malgat requested. Return to Malgat and give him the corpses.'Forgive me, ${PLAYER}. I wish not to impose more upon you, but I must ask if you will do one thing for me.

'In my youth, I made my way as a hunter. Much of what I earned passed to the Ordâkhai, but I kept some to teach myself a trade beyond skinning and sewing. Cleaning, curing, and stuffing the fauna of these lands. I would, in my twilight, enjoy this.

'Would you help an old man meet his twilight years with a smile? If so, seek out the Eldest of Samarsûg, a crocodile the north, the jackal known as Shûhuz, and the scorpion in the temple ruin of Ish Dara known as Girgazug. I will also need six slivers of jade found among the many mines in Khûd Zagin.''I would like to reward you for all you have done. It will take a short while. I will ask you to return to me if you are willing.'Thórvilon, leader of the Kintai in Vartúlin, has asked you to gather fresh Sarláshi shoots from Róthirin, that they may grow into Sarláshi trees and be fashioned in Veróthi one day.Gather Sarláshi shoots from the grove of Róthirin. Róthirin is located east of Vartúlin.Gather Sarláshi shoots from Róthirin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Vartúlin and plant the Sarláshi shoots at well-lit spots around Vartúlin.Plant Sarláshi shoots in Vartúlin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Thórvilon in Vartúlin.'Lidath mâd. There is much we must do to maintain what we have here in Vartúlin. I presume you've noticed the red-leafed trees around us? They are Sarláshi trees, with which we make Veróthi. Our Veróthi are living links to the Kintai who have undergone Trothúl, the Wearying. We give them the reverence and respect Men have for their entombed dead in sarcophagi.

'Our Veróthi require fresh Sarláshi trees with which to grow. Vartúlin's trees no longer produce shoots, as they are near the end of their life cycle, as are we who tend them.

'There is an area west of here with younger Sarláshi trees. This is the grove of Róthirin. I must warn you however, there are vengeful Curthádi spirits, Kintai who became wrathful or vengeful at the despoiling of the forests, who roam Róthirin. It is no longer safe for the Kintai to venture there. You, however, have the bearing of one who can handle yourself in a fight.

'It is our ancestral duty to plant more Sarláshi trees here in Vartúlin, that we have enough for all the Kintai Elves who undergo Trothúl. Go to Róthirin and gather us fresh Sarláshi shoots, that they may be replanted here in Vartúlin and grow into full Sarláshi trees. I am trusting you with something quite sacred to us, ${PLAYER}. I know you will not let me down.''It warms my heart to see the Sarláshi shoots flourishing as they are. Thank you for respecting and following our traditions. One day I too will undergo Trothúl - I hope someone with your care and fastidiousness tends to my Veróth.'Water buffalo that roam throughout the eastern span of the Cape of Umbar grow in value. Khânai offers payment for collecting haunches and hides from the beast. She resides at the expedition camp.Collect buffalo hides (${NUMBER}/12)Collect buffalo haunches (${NUMBER}/12)Khânai at the expedition camp desires more buffalo haunches and hides. Her patron in Umbar City sees an increase in the value of the beast and wants more to maximize their profit.'Water buffalo are the choice of the moment in Umbar City. My patron demands that more haunches and hides be collected and delivered to them. Will you venture into the desert and plains in search of the buffaloes, claim their hides and haunches, and return them to me?''This meets my quota and will satisfy the request from my patron. I am pleased that this relationship between us works so well. Please, return tomorrow. I am certain that there will be more activities that need meeting.''Head north toward the desert or beyond into the savannah. You will find the buffalo in those areas. Hunt them for their haunches and hides and return what you collect to me.'Artar Ildarthos has asked you to help buy time for the Adúrhid at Vartúlin by going to Ghât Lor and defeating many of the Ordâkhai making war on the Adúrhid.Destroy fortifications and defeat Ordâkhai at Ghât Lor. Ghât Lor can be found east of Vartúlin.Defeat Ordâkhai at Ghât Lor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Artar Ildarthos at Vartúlin with news of your triumph.Return to Artar Ildarthos at Vartúlin with news of your triumph'The southern men make war on my people, outsider. I know not why, only that it is how it always has been. If not Men, then Orcs. If not Orcs, then Men. We wish to exist, and they seem to wish we didn't. Others of my kin worry about Trothúl, the Wearying that comes with age to my people. I have never worried about it. I have a duty, to my warriors and to my people to protect them. I will not fade until the threats to my people are removed. So perhaps I will live forever. That was a joke my friend, don't look so serious.

'The southern Men, who call themselves Men of Ordâkh, have made camp east of Vartúlin. They are quite dug in, with strong fortifications, based on what Surodith has told me. If you wish to help us, send them a strong message. Defeat a contingent of them at Ghât Lor. That will buy us time to make fortifications here, designed to repel any attack they make on us. Please, go to Ghât Lor and teach the southern Men a valuable lesson - that they reap the discord they have sown.''I am relieved. I can breathe easier now. We have some time to finish our defensive preparations here. Thank you for your actions defending us - please, relax here in Vartúlin. You have proven yourself to me and the Adúrhid.'Raphûz, grateful for your assistance in recovering his pack, asks you to join him for tea and a smoke by the fireside.Raphûz asked you to join him for tea and a smoke at the Tale-warden encampment near Telperiën's Wall.Complete the Instance: A Promise KeptYou learned much about the young man you helped. You should say your farewell in the shadow of Telperiën's Wall.'Thank you again for your assistance with my pack. I was foolish to think Kizeri would cut me loose for such a simple transgression. I know I said I have nothing to offer your kindness, but I remembered I have some fine tobacco from Umbar I can share. We can sit and share. If you wish, we can sit and talk for a while.''Join me? We can share the fire, my tobacco, and I will prepare some tea.''Thank you for listening and sharing my tobacco. I am unsure what my future holds. I am glad we spoke. You have a good ear for conversation.'You have retaken Kûr Anzar! Now is the time to celebrate! Help the local vendors and Kûr Anzar residents get settled upon their return to the city.Use the back gate of Kûr Anzar, then find the vendors down the hill and beckon them to follow you inside.Beckon the merchant Galpêsh outside the walls of Kûr AnzarFind the merchants of Kûr Anzar down the hillSpeak with Numûru at the top of Kûr Anzar.Speak with Numûru at the top of Kûr AnzarSpeak with five vendors at the top of Kûr Anzar and offer your aid.Speak with GalpêshSpeak with HâdimaSpeak with UrguSpeak with MulnûriSpeak with MâkhburClean up rubble piles for Urgu and hang posters for Mulnûri.Clean up rubble piles for Urgu (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hang posters for Mulnûri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Mizâdi at the top of Kûr Anzar.Speak with Mizâdi at the top of Kûr Anzar'Thank you for all you have done. There are many citizens waiting outside the back gate to come back in and begin to reclaim their lives here in Kûr Anzar.

'Would you go out there and beckon them in? Let them know the danger has passed and they can set up their stalls, reclaim their homes and begin their lives here again.''There is still much to be done, and yet more to be celebrated! Please, help the vendors set up their wares and make both the residents and vendors feel welcome again.''It is so good to be home again. Help? No, no, no. I need nothing from you. I'm too excited for help... in a good way.''So much to do, so little time. Help? No, nothing I need, my dear. I'm just so glad to see people smiling again around here. At least I think they are smiling. Surely they are! It's hard to tell through the soot.''How is one supposed to turn a decent profit with all this rubble everywhere? Yes, you can help me. Get some of this rubble cleared away. My clothes are far too fine to be in a war.''Something you can do for me? Absolutely, get the word out. Mulnûri will not be beat, cannot be beat on these prices or this quality. Look at these tunics. You will find no higher quality anywhere in Shagâna. Umbar can only marvel at these textures, this softness, they cannot come close to matching me.

'Everyone needs to know. It's for the public good!''Help, for me? Unless you can get the smell of fire or this blasted soot out of the air, you cannot do anything for me. Why did I let my wife convince me to come back here? Blasted wars, terrible for business, and one's nose.''Thank you for your help setting up and helping usher in some of old Kûr Anzar.

'The people of Kûr Anzar will now look to us for a sense of normalcy. A warm belly and a new tunic may not seem like much, but they are more than many have had here in Kûr Anzar in some time.'Ashâmi and Raphûz discussed the threat the cultist made and want to consult with the Elves of Shonith. They hope you will visit them there.Raphûz and Ashâmi intend to leave Urmâkh to return to Lathagwid. They ask that you go to Shonith to share your description with Lathagwid. She may know the foe you witnessed. Lathagwid can be found near the oasis in Shonith.Speak with Lathagwid at Shonith and describe what you sawLathagwid could not recall a foe in all her long life. She told Ashâmi and Raphûz there is a dead land north of Imhûlar but could recall nothing more. Seek out Ashâmi in Shonith to speak with her about Lathagwid's response.Speak with Ashâmi in the oasis of ShonithAshâmi is frightened and inspired by what she heard and what you have seen. She asked for time to think apart from Raphûz and determine the path she wishes to follow. She hopes Raphûz feels the same. Seek Raphûz in Shonith.Speak with Raphûz in the oasis of Shonith'${PLAYER}, we intend to speak with Lathagwid. The Elves of the Shonith Oasis have lived in these lands so long they have forgotten more than they remember.

'Perhaps they can explain what the cultist meant by the words lost to time. Perhaps they cannot.

'If they can help us, they will.

'Meet us there, and we will gain Lathagwid's guidance.'Lathagwid holds your gaze.

'Ashâmil and Raphûz shared their information with me. The language of the letter I would not read here. The repercussions to the oasis could be grave.

'They told me you saw something at a great distance.'

You describe what you saw.

'I cannot recall anything like this in my life. Our tales do not recount such things.

'Alas, ${PLAYER}, much of our history dissipated as the oases died and the land corrupted. I told Ashâmi and Raphûz about the dead lands to the north.

'I remember one name, Maurush. It is a place where you may find refuge. A place you may find horror. A place where you may find answers.

'This is all I know.''Lathagwid will not leave. She cannot recall seeing an enemy as you described in her lifetime.

'She told me she cannot help. She told me this path be mine to walk or leave. I told Raphûz I needed time to think.

'My bones still shake when I think of the words the cultist spoke as we defeated him. I felt the evil passing over me.

'There is some greater evil beyond the Ordâkhai. I want to face that evil and drive it away. I want to live for myself and the greater good of the world.

'I only hope that Raphûz will feel the same.'Raphûz looks tired.

'Hello, my friend.

'Ashâmi asked for time to think. My decision was an easy one. I have learned my father's homeland has people who are fierce, independent, and beautiful.

'I have learned the people of the north need not be our enemy.

'When the cultist spoke, I felt the shadow of true evil. Something shook me deeply.

'These things changed me. I cannot cast my eyes toward a goal that does not safe-guard all. There is some great work at hand. I will go to Maurush and seek to discern the evil we face.

'I hope Ashâmi and I can do this together.'Sûzakh has given you directions to a hideout where you can learn more about the situation in Urash Dâr.Reach Ub Nishir, the camp to the north of Maurûsh and speak with GalâmkaReach Ub Nishir to the north of MaurûshSpeak with Galâmka in Ub Nishir.Speak with Galâmka'${CLASS}, what could ever bring you to Urash Dâr? There are many dangers here. The demon-pit has been opened and I myself intend to flee.

'If you wish to go forth, I urge you to go to Ub Nishir, just north of Maurûsh, and speak with Galâmka there. He will know more and will be in need of your help.

'As for Maurûsh itself, you must stay clear of it. It has been overrun by Orcs and other monstrosities. If you follow the road on the western side of the stronghold, you may find a safe route to Ub Nishir.

'Good luck.''Greetings, ${CLASS}, what brings you to Ub Nishir?'

You inform Galâmka that you were sent by Sûzakh.

'Ah, Sûzakh. So that is what became of him. As for you, if you wish to help, you are welcome to stay in Ub Nishir.'Girhâzi has asked you to prove that you are not her enemy by defeating Ordâkhai soldiers.There is an Ordâkhai camp to the north-east of Iridír. You have been asked to go there and collect proof that you have defeated eight soldiers.Collect trinkets from defeated Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected proof that you have defeated eight Ordâkhai soldiers. You should bring the trinkets to Girhâzi in Iridír.'Who are you, that visits our land?'

The imposing woman scrutinizes your appearance and looks curious, but you get the impression that she has no love for foreigners.

'I am called Girhâzi and I am chieftain of the people here. It is my duty, and that of my Dumûri, to defend this land from the tyranny of our oppressors from the Southern Empire of Ordâkh. I have heard that you from other lands call us all "Haradrim", as though we are one people, but that is not so.

'Over one hundred years ago the Ordâkhai swept through Shagâna, conquering land after land and subjugating the native peoples. For generations, they have demanded our servility. They profit from our labour and steal our sons and husbands, sending them into war.'

As she lifts her chin, you can see anger, grief, and defiance in the woman's eyes.

'But no more. Never again. If you wish to speak to me, you must prove you are not our enemy. To the north, on the west side of the stream that runs through Iridír, you will find a camp of Ordâkhai soldiers who have thus far managed to escape our wrath. Go there and defeat them. Bring me proof that you have defeated at least eight, and I will speak with you further.''I will not speak with you further until you prove you are not our enemy. To the north, on the west side of the stream that runs through Iridír, you will find a camp of Ordâkhai soldiers. Bring me proof that you have defeated at least eight of them, and I will speak with you further.''You return from your task. Do you bring evidence of your deeds?'

You hand Girhâzi the trinkets taken from the defeated Ordâkhai. She looks them over briefly, and you see a genuine smile.

'It is good to have you here. In Ambarûl, we do not have enough friends in other lands. We will need them if we are to survive. Thank you.'Kalkhadra's sister, Agalûnu, has gone to the haunted forest of Arwáth and has not returned.Kalkhadra asked you to go to Arwáth and check on Agalûnu. Arwáth is a forest in the northernmost reaches of Ambarûl.Find AgalûnuYou have found Agalûnu. You should talk to her and see if she is all right.Talk to Agalûnu'Pardon me, traveller! I need someone to help me, but the Dumûri say it is not urgent! My sister, Agalûnu, has gone missing! All right, so she went on purpose but has not returned. She went north to Arwáth. Nobody goes to Arwáth. It is a forest haunted by tortured spirits!'

The woman is very distraught and is anxiously wringing her hands.

'She said the trees there have wood that is better for woodworking and would be worth a fortune. I told her not to go, but she said, "I am no pashâg!" and that she would return in three days. That time has passed, and she has not returned! Did she anger the spirits? Did bandits attack her? Please, go to Arwáth and see if she is well. Nobody else will do it!''Oh, thank you for stopping, stranger! Please, I am injured and need some help.''My sister has gone to the haunted forest in the north and has not returned. Please, go to Arwáth and see if she is well. Nobody else will do it!'Avadhril asks you to look for seeds untouched by the Lâg Dávrit. She has previously had good luck scavenging unblemished seeds near Shakhdag and Tir Katar, among the wild servals and boars.Avadhril asks you to gather acorns and berry seeds untouched by the Lâg Dávrit in Shakhdag and Tir Katar. Shakhdag is north-east of Vartúlin. Tir Katar is directly north of Vartúlin.Gather unblemished acorns in Shakhdag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather unblemished berry seeds in Tir Katar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Avadhril in Vartúlin with the seeds you've gathered.'There is much to be done, if your hands are willing. The Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight, has swept through our great forests. What once was Laithor, the great Emerald Wood, has been sapped dry, trees turned as bone and plants turned to ash. We now call these woods Favrathór, the forest of bone. But life still struggles to find its way, even within this dying land.

'As the Artar Grove-tender, I am responsible for tending and caring for the woods around you. As you can see, I am doing a quite poor job of it. These hands, though still skilled, are lined with more than experience and slower than they used to be. But more importantly, the Lâg Dávrit has made all of us grove-tenders quite powerless. It has ossified the great trees of the ancient forest. We few who remain do what we can to combat it.

'I have been known to scavenge seed, untouched as of yet by the Pale Blight. I plant it here in Vartúlin, that we might transplant these trees and bushes into greater Favrathór when the time is right. I have had good luck with finding unblemished acorns and berry seeds to the north, in both Shakhdag and Tir Katar. However, the beasts of the area have also suffered from the Pale Blight, many becoming sickened and frenzied. I dare not scavenge there anymore, for fear I shall not return. But I am no warrior. You seem much more capable. If you are willing, would you go there and gather more seeds? It is imperative to the forest that we gather and nurture new, unblemished life here in Vartúlin.''Some recent days are difficult, outsider. So many of my kind have faded, so many long held friends have become faded memories. Sometimes when I hear the wind blow through these trees I feel I can hear their voices. It sounds like they are calling out to me, calling me home. But it is not my time yet. It is not my time yet...

'This helps. Knowing we can still make a difference in our little corner of Favrathór, it aids me in shouldering this lonely burden. Thank you.'Amarêkh has asked you to go north to Tilmakhím for a new book.Amarêkh has asked you to go north to a place called Tilmakhím, the Cross-roads. There the bookseller Ephrâti should have the book "A Smouldering Fire" for Amarêkh.Talk to the bookseller Ephrâti in TilmakhímEphrâti has asked you to deal with the rat menace.Defeat Tilmakhím rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Ephrâti the bookseller.

Ephrâti can be found in Tilmakhím in Takhdâr.Return to Ephrâti the booksellerReturn to Amarêkh in Mekab-kuphâr, in southern Khabârkhad, with the book.Return to Amarêkh in Mekab-kuphâr with the book'It gets so boring down here. These other guards aren't the best conversationalists, you know. I wonder, would you be able to obtain a book for me?'

She leans in close, as though to tell you a secret.

'There's a specific one I'm after. "A Smouldering Fire." It's very... academic.

'There's a bookseller to the north, just outside Khabârkhad in an area called Tilmakhím, the Cross-roads.

'Here, take a few coins for the bookseller. Would you be able to get this book for me?''I have the book, but I don't want your coin. All day long I deal with the rats.

'It's rats this, rats that. They get in the books, my hair, they get in everything. I've tried to make the best of it.

'Ephrâti, they said, just eat the rats. Make the best of a bad situation.

'Have you tried rat soup? I have, it's disgusting. Please just deal with the rats.''You've thinned their number? Excellent. Here is the book you requested.

'Maybe tonight I'll finally stop dreaming of a gallant rat prince to take me away to his rat kingdom, where all the houses are made of discarded grain and the carriages spin on wheels of ale cheese.'

She stops abruptly.

'Never mind. My dreams are my own business. Kindly take the book and be off with you.''You found it! Oh, thank you!

'Now I don't have to be so dreadfully bored here.

'Ephrâti? Yeah, she can be a bit dramatic. And a terrible cook. Her rat soup is awful.'Talmûri has asked for your help investigating claims of a poisoned water source in the area. She suspects it may be the work of Ekhamâti soldiers.Talmûri has asked for your help investigating claims of a poisoned water source in the area. Travel north-west to the mouth of the river to see if you can find any clues as to the cause of the tainted water.Reach the mouth of the riverYou arrived at the mouth of the river Talmûri told you about. Investigate the area and see if you can find any clues as to what may be causing the water to be poisoned.Investigate tracks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You arrived at the mouth of the river Talmûri told you about. Investigate the area and see if you can find any clues as to what may be causing the water to be poisoned.You found tracks near the mouth of the river Talmûri told you about. They pointed further upstream. Follow the river to see if you can find any more indications of the poison's source.Search further up the riverYou found more tracks along the river. Investigate them to see what you can learn.Investigate tracks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You found more tracks along the river. Investigate them to see what you can learn.You found more tracks that point even further upstream. You have to be getting close now. Follow the river to find the source of the poison.Continue your search up the riverYou discovered the source of the poisoned water to be rotting animal carcasses. Remove them to stop river's water from being tainted.Remove animal carcasses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Talmûri in Burukíri and let her know it wasn't Ekhamâti soldiers poisoning the river, it was only animal carcasses that began to rot in the water.Return to Talmûri in Burukíri'Oh, ${CLASS}. I am glad to see you. We are in need of help from someone with your skills.

'There is a river to the north-west of here, and there have been claims that the water coming from it is being poisoned. With the recent attacks by Bârshud II, farmers here fear it may be the work of Ekhamâti soldiers. We would not stand a chance against them if the rumours are true. Can you investigate the river and see if you can find anything?''You have returned! Did you find the source of the poisoned water?'

You inform Talmûri of the dead animals you found and that you removed them.

'Animal carcasses you say? So it was not Ekhamâti soldiers after all? That is a relief to hear, and I am glad you were able to remove them. Our waters should flow clean again soon. Thank you, kind ${CLASS} for all your help.'Raphûz recalled a tale told by his father. An Ordâkhai warlord bested him in combat and took a trophy of his hand and sword. Raphûz's father always wanted vengeance and now there is a chance.Raphûz directed you to an Ordâkhai camp north-east of Iridír. He believes that Dhómok Umûn, the warlord who stole his father's sword and arm, is there. In addition, you can help the people of Ambarûl by thinning out the Ordâkhai.Defeat Ordâkhai warriors at Omboha (${NUMBER}/12)Defeat Dhómok UmûnRecover Raphuz's father's swordYou found Dhómok Umûn and defeated him, recovering Raphûz's father's sword. Return the sword to Raphûz at the settlement of Iridír.'My father lost his arm when he refused to give Dhómok Umûn — a cruel Ordâkahi warlord who took limbs, eyes, and tongues from those he deemed insolent — a shipment of grain bound for a different settlement. Umûn took my father's sword as a final insult.

'Fate shines on me, friend. Dhómok Umûn leads an encampment of Ordâkhai threatening Iridír. Still, fate is cruel. I am not a capable enough warrior to face such a foe. His encampment is small, just north of the waterfall's source where you collected the berries.

'I feel shame in asking. Could you confront the warlord and recover my father's sword?''I heard tell warlord Dhómok Umûn, the man who maimed my father and stole his sword, is at the Ordâkhai camp of Omboha. Will you go there and defeat this man and see if you can recover my family sword?''This - this is my father's sword? You found Umûn and defeated him.'

Raphûz's eyes well with tears.

'My father is avenged. This is a step on the path to restoring his name. I do not know if I can ever repay you for this. You must think me a coward.

'Please, take this small reward for what you have done. I must write this event into my journal.'Raphûz decides to pursue wealth and asks you to help him determine if there are truly riches near Jirush he can acquire to pay Igbâl's price.Raphûz has chosen to pursue the cost Igbâl put on pursuing Ashâmi's hand. He wants to learn all he can from the people of Jirush about the Tomb of Nirgambâr before he ventures there.Learn about the Tomb of Nirgambâr from denizens of Jirush (${NUMBER}/6)You visited many of the inhabitants of Jirush and enquired about the Tombs of Nirgambâr. It sounds like a terrible place. You should return to Raphûz at his camp in Jirush with the information.'My friend, while I recuperated from the wounds received by the teeth and tusks of the boar, my mother shared the story of how my father won her over.

'It was a simple tale. My father proved he would do anything for her and her love by meeting each challenge her father placed before him. I will do the same.

'I intend to learn about Nirgambâr from the people of Jirush. Will you aid me as you did in the encampment outside of the Wrackwade?'You explain your desire to learn the dangers of Nirgambâr.

'Like the temple that overlooks this outpost, the tombs have always been. None alive remember who built them. None in this outpost dare to enter the place.'You explain your desire to learn the dangers of Nirgambâr.

'What more do you need to know? It is a tomb. The Dead there should rest, and yet they stir. Evil is in that place.'You explain your desire to learn the dangers of Nirgambâr.

'None from this outpost would dare venture there. Some say that the spirits of the once thriving land fled into the bodies of the dead after the land was laid waste. They were quiet for centuries. In recent times, the dead stir. More recently, they move onto the land from deep within the tombs.'You explain your desire to learn the dangers of Nirgambâr.

'There is an abundance of wealth within the deepest chambers. Thieves and robbers enter there all the time to acquire relics to sell to the Ordâkhai or to sacrifice at the temple above Jirush. No good comes from that place.'You explain your desire to learn the dangers of Nirgambâr.

'The superstitious among us do not speak of the tombs. It is where the dead are meant to rest. They do not.'You explain your desire to learn the dangers of Nirgambâr.

'Nirgamâr is a place of horror. The Dead walk the land and the catacombs beneath. None who live remember when those halls were ancient. Perhaps the tombs are as old as the stars or older. All we know is the tombs are unnatural and evil.'You tell Raphûz what the inhabitants of Jirush told you of Nirgambâr.

'Yes. I heard the same. A place of evil. If this is where I must go to earn Igbâl's respect, then I shall.'Amalíbi devised a plan to test the captain's information. She provided you some details and sent you off to the task while she and her rebels prepare another part of the plan.Amalíbi sent you north-west to the Ordâkhai encampment to obtain sashes from the warriors, and a sounding horn from one of the mustering tents. You are to return to her at Ghalbûru after acquiring the items.Obtain Ordâkhai warrior sashes from the Ordâkhai camp north of Jirush (${NUMBER}/4)Collect an Ordâkhai sounding hornYou acquired the sashes and the sounding horn. Return to Amalíbi and show her you have the items.Amalíbi directed you to the outskirts of the Ordâkhai encampment in the south-east and find the staged attack Amalíbi's forces provided. Place the sashes on the defeated Ordâkhai.With the sashes placed, you should find a spot where you can watch what transpires when you blow the sounding horn.After blowing the horn, Captain Khârdu recognized the horn as Bosóta's. You need to speak with Bosóta and tell him to explain the tale to plant the seeds of rebellion among the Ordâkhai.Speak with Bosóta in your hiding spotThe ruse was successful and Bosóta Dôlo played his part well. You should return to Amalíbi and inform her of the success.'I am willing to test the information Bosóta supplied us. I ask that you go to the Ordâkhai fort overlooking Jirush to obtain a sounding horn and sashes from four soldiers there.

'I will have others from my number prepare a position near the Ordâkhai encampment to the south-east. When you return with the sashes and horn, we will discuss what further must be done.''We want to set the Ordâkhai at odds. We need the sashes worn by the men serving Jombahok at the encampment north of Jirush. Collect the sashes and horn from there and return to me.''You did well to keep blood off the sashes, and the horn is in good repair. While you were at your task, I moved the bodies of the courier and his companions to the outskirts of Khârdu's encampment to the south-east.

'Take the sashes and the horn to that location. Place the sashes on the corpses and find Bosóta nearby and conceal yourself.

'Once settled, blow the horn. Speak with Bosóta to have him leave the hiding place, and if his mettle holds, he will play the ruse well enough to convince Khârdu of our deception and return to his captain's ranks.

'I warn you, this subterfuge is not without risk, and it is only the first step on a long path to absolution and retribution for my people.''Bosóta did not mislead us. It is as I expected, ${PLAYER}. Love is a force more powerful than self-preservation. One will do anything for those they love. Now we must counter this defection and ruse with another to raise Jombahok's hackles, setting him and Khârdu toward an irrevocable confrontation.''I will play my part. I no longer wish to make war and this will set the steps in motion to returning to my family in the south.

'Tell your leaders that I will not betray them.'Zidemel asked you to assist Zidek of Jirush. The man lost his sight when the Ordâkhai burned his home and slaughtered his family. He seeks vengeance.Zidek asks that you head into the wild where the crebain used by the Ordâkhai roam freely to slaughter the birds and steal their eyes. He believes if the proper sacrifice is made, his sight will return.Collect craban eyes from the wastes of Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/10)You slaughtered many of the crebain and collected their eyes. Return to Jirush, in central Khûd Zagin, and deliver them to Zidek as he listens to Zidemel preach in Jirush.'Are you the person Zidemel said would come? I pray you are. My eyes are useless. Ordâkhai flames destroyed my family, my home, and my sight. Zidemel says if I give a gift of the enemy's eyes to the desert, the Ishími will speak kindly of me to the king. When the king returns, so will my sight.

'The enemy sees through eyes in the sky. The eyes of the craban. The carrion eaters who scour the lands to the south and all around us. Fetch me ten pairs of their eyes that I may please the king.''The crebain gather in a large murder north-west of Jirush. Hunt them for their eyes so I may see again.''My vengeance is complete. I will know the gift of sight again. I will keep these safe until he returns. Zidemel was right to send you to me.'A child of the Sail-haven has lost her dog after it ran into the sewers chasing a rat. Lebíthi has asked you to keep an eye out for the dog while you traverse Ilmabiri.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail if you are defeated or log out. If this occurs, it will be removed from your quest log and you will need to accept it again.</rgb>You have been asked to stay on the look-out for a lost nether-hound as you travel through Ilmabiri.Find the lost dog, HírkhaYou have found Hírkha, a lost nether-hound as you travelled through Ilmabiri. You should introduce yourself to her.Introduce yourself to HírkhaYou have found Hírkha, a lost nether-hound as you travelled through Ilmabiri. After introducing yourself to her, she seems willing to follow you. You should lead Hírkha to Kruha-sûrja, the guard post in the northern part of the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Lead Hírkha back to LebíthiYou have found Hírkha, a lost nether-hound as you travelled through Ilmabiri and have led her to safety at the guard post Kruha-sûrja. You should talk to Lebíthi.Talk to Lebíthi'While you are travelling through the tunnels, I have a favour to ask of you. A girl has lost her dog, Hírkha. They were walking through the Sail-haven when the hound took off, chasing a rat. She believes the dog followed the rat into the sewers and has not seen Hírkha since. If you happen to see a nether-hound on your trek through Ilmabiri, there is a small reward for her return.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail if you are defeated or log out. If this occurs, it will be removed from your quest log and you will need to accept it again.</rgb>'You found her! This is such good news!

'I will be honest with you that I did not expect her to be found alive. She is lucky to not be inside the belly of a crocodile! I will see that she is returned to her owner. Hírkha must have been very brave to survive down here. Thank you for her rescue!'You've been asked to cull the number of spiders to the north of Mekab-kuphâr, in Nishabêt.North of Mekab-kuphâr there is an area infested with spiders. You've been asked to thin their number, lest they over-run Khabârkhad and spill out into greater Umbar-môkh.Defeat Khabârkhad spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to the Temámir Guard Captain Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr, the Temámir outpost in the southern Khabârkhad.Return to the Temámir Guard Captain Nûru'You look quite capable. We have need of some assistance, if you're willing.

'North of here is an encampment of monstrous spiders. Their numbers are growing, their brood multiplying in the dark with no Man or dwarf to pare them back. Their reach has expanded to the point they've been attacking my patrols here in the southern crypts.

'Please, we need their numbers thinned, before more of my Temámir fall to these terrible beasts. Will you help us?''I am grateful. If those spiders got any closer, they might over-run our encampment. You've assured the safety of many Temámir this day.'Raphûz asks you to meet him at Igbâl's, once again. He intends to provide the merchant with the riches he acquired in exchange for an opportunity to court Ashâmi.Raphûz wants you to meet him at Igbâl's home in Jirush when he presents the merchant with the treasure he acquired from Nirgambâr.Meet Raphûz at Igbâl's home in JirushRaphûz is engaged in discussion with Igbâl. Galamê motioned to you. You should speak with Galamê at Igbâl's home in Jirush.Speak with Galamê in Igbâl's home in JirushGalamê informed you that Ashâmi went missing soon after you and Raphûz departed for Nirgambâr. He suggested you speak with your friend Raphûz at Igbâl's home to see what he learned and to help him.Speak with Raphûz in Igbâl's home in JirushGalamê overheard Raphûz's comment and motioned you to attend him.Speak with Galamê at Igbâl's home in JirushGalamê's warning was clear. If Raphûz makes a scene here, he will create enemies where he does not want them. Speak to the young man in Igbâl's home.Speak with Raphûz at Igbâl's home in JirushRaphûz wisely chose to continue his conversation out of earshot of Igbâl, Ardub, and Tâlsari. He waits your arrival at his home in Jirush.Speak with Raphûz at his home in JirushRaphûz is polishing a golden coin bearing an unfamiliar emblem.

'This is the last of the coins I wanted to polish before meeting with Igbâl. If you will, meet me there. I want you by my side when he provides his blessing.''Raphûz handed the gift to Igbâl and is listening now to a familiar tale. His daughter, stricken mad with an Aladi curse, fled when her father confessed to sending you and Raphûz to Nirgambâr.

'See there, they are done speaking. You should attend your friend.'Raphûz appears flummoxed.

'He says she is mad. Not angry, insane. He took my gift, then told me she ran off to the south under the sway of the same Aladi that ensorcelled her mother.

'He is a charlatan.'

Galamê shoots a glance at the two of you and beckons you.Galamê speaks in a hushed tone.

'You and Raphûz are fortunate Igbâl did not hear Raphûz's outburst. I advise you to take your friend and make your leave before other ears hear his words.

'I will smooth down any ruffled feathers that may rise from Raphûz's outburst. Now go before you do more harm.'

You notice Ardub and his wife Tâlsari paying close attention to Raphûz.You alert Raphûz to the attention his outburst provoked. He lowers his voice as he responds.

'Perhaps we should discuss this elsewhere. I am too bothered by these events to hold my tongue. Meet me back at my hovel, here in Jirush.''Igbâl explained to me what transpired when we left.

'Ashâmi fought with her father and told him her hand was not his to give. He said this is a sign she is under the sway of an Aladi.

'More superstition. She is independent, nothing more.

'I slighted her terribly in making this decision. Her father only wanted wealth for himself.

'I am embarrassed, ${PLAYER}.'Nangar enlisted you to aid in a distraction while he steals information from the Ordâkhai encampment overlooking Jirush.Nangar directed you to meet him beneath the Ordâkhai camp on the plateau by following a hidden path at south-western edge of the plateau. You will help provide a distraction for him.Go to the location Nangar described beneath the Ordâkhai encampmentNangar signaled you when you arrived beneath the Ordâkhai encampment. You should speak with him.Speak with Nangar at the foot of the hidden pathNangar stole into the encampment and vanished from sight. You are to assault the Ordâkhai encampment providing him a distraction long enough to go about finding their plans.Defeat Ordâkhai dôla (${NUMBER}/2)Defeat Ordâkhai jackal-keepers (${NUMBER}/4)Defeat other Ordâkhai warriors at the encampment north of Jirush (${NUMBER}/14)You fought back the Ordâkhai and, hopefully, provided Nangar enough time and distraction to acquire the plans. Return to the hidden path at the south-western foot of the plateau beneath the Ordâkhai encampment to speak with him.Return to the foot of hidden path beneath the Ordâkhai encampmentNangar waits for you along the hidden path beneath the Ordâkhai encampment. Speak with him to learn how successful you both were in your actions.After speaking with Nangar near the Ordâkhai encampment, he asked to speak with you more openly at this home in the relative safety of Jirush.'I trust you enough, ${PLAYER}, that I am willing to enlist your assistance in a matter requiring direct conflict against the fortress to the north-west.

'I need a distraction... one loud enough and long enough to provide me cover to sneak into the encampment and out again unseen.

'If you are willing, I know of a secret path into the encampment. Meet me at the top of the path beneath the Ordâkhai structure on the plateau. You will find it north of Jirush.''I will meet you near the secret path at the south-west foot of the plateau beneath the Ordâkhai encampment.''Sneak into the base and defeat the dôla — the captains — the lieutenants, and the other soldiers within. While you create the commotion, I will steal behind the walls and try to find plans drafted by the keep lord Jombahok.''We should move quickly. You provided me enough time to acquire a selection of notes, and I hope the plans I sought. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Return to me at my home in Jirush where we can speak in relative safety.''I have only begun looking through the notes I recovered, but there is promise in this discovery. I could not have succeeded without your involvement, ${PLAYER}. Thank you.'Zidemel asked you to assist Meliri, an elderly woman of Jirush. She is haunted by the memory of her husband and the ignominy he faced at the hands of an Ordâkhai warlord.Meliri asked you to go to Nirgambâr to retrieve the hand bones and finger-bones of wights. She and Zidemel believe it will quiet the restless spirit of her dead husband and absolve her in preparation for the return of a great king.Collect wight finger-bones from the Dead at Nirgambâr (${NUMBER}/5)Collect wight hand bones from the Dead at Nirgambâr (${NUMBER}/10)You collected the hand bones and fingerbones of the wights at Nirgambâr. Return to Meliri listening to Zidemel preach in Jirush and give them to her.'Zidemel sent you? Then my hope returns.

'Years ago, my husband crossed an Ordâkhai warlord and lost his hand as punishment. Zidemel said the terrors seeking me at night will end, and my absolution will come when I restore what my husband lost.

'A hand, you see, made anew from the grim walkers risen in the west at Nirgambâr. Collect the hand and finger-bones of the walking dead at Nirgambâr, that I may stitch my husband a new hand.''Please help me, ${RACE}. My husband's spirit haunts my dreams. I believe he will rest if I restore his hand. You can find all you need from the Dead in Nirgambâr to the north-west.''I will stitch the hand together with sinew and thread. Thanks to you, I will make my offer. My husband will rest, and I will be cleansed and prepared for the return of our king.'Filadal wants to recover her mother's necklace from the oasis north-west of Shonith and to bring vengeance on the wrathful spirits that drove her from the oasis before she could say good-bye.Filadal told you of being forced to leave the oasis north-west of Shonith as her mother was set to fade. She fled, and only saw her mother surrounded by wrathful spirits before reaching her final rest. She wants a keepsake and vengeance before she fades.Collect Filadal's Mother's necklaceAvenge Filadal's mother by defeating wrathful spirits (${NUMBER}/8)You recovered the necklace from near one of the trees in the old oasis and defeated a good number of the wrathful spirits there. Return the necklace to Filadal.'I know Tharashil has no time for me or Aítarshun. I am touched she sent you to aid me and him.

'She does not know the weight I carried out of the old oasis to the west. My mother is there, still. She will dwell there forever, as I will in this oasis.

'I left her to fate, rooted, as I am now, to a spot she could not depart. The wrathful spirits swarmed her as she fell to final slumber, and I left.

'I did not look back. Now, friend, I want to claim something of hers. Her tomb's location will be obvious. Her necklace is there.

'I should like to know that some of the wrathful spirits there met a final fate.'A tear falls from her eye.

'This means the world to me, friend. You are selfless. I have no words but ones of thanks for what you did for me.'Your efforts to support Shâra Mizâdi and her forces in Idagâl earn you great favour with Hamât Renewed.You must earn Acquaintance standing with Hamât RenewedYour standing with the Adúrhid improves and earns you a gift from the Ikorbâni Elves.Your continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.Reach Acquaintance tier with the AdúrhidYour continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.Visit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a giftYour continued efforts to aid the Kintai Elves brings great joy to them. You should visit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a gift from the Elves of the oasis.'We are pleased you have proven so noble.

'We do not open our lands to many, as we have little left. To see that you are willing to aid us is a portent. We hope it is a portent of a change for the better. Though we know our fates our chosen.'Your continued efforts to support Mûr Ghala earns you greater favour with the City of Zajâna.You must earn Acquaintance standing with the City of ZajânaYou continue to prove your valour, nerve, and measured assistance to the Hunter's Guild of Mûr Ghala.You must earn Acquaintance standing with the Hunter's Guild of Mûr GhalaYour standing among the Ikorbâni earns you a gift. Return to Kildûg at Iridír to claim your reward.You have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.Reach Acquaintance tier with the IkorbâniYou have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.Visit Kildûg at Iridír to claim a giftYour efforts to assist the Ikorbâni are noted among the people. To recognize your efforts, the leaders of the Shagâni at Iridír wish to honour you with a gift and thanks.'You are true to your word. We recognize all you have done with this simple offering. We would provide you more if you are willing to part with Ghín.

'If you wish, speak with Nêkhur and see what we offer.'Your continued efforts to support the Ikorbân Valley earn you greater favour with the Shagâni people.You must earn Acquaintance standing with the IkorbâniYou continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Ikorbân.You must earn Acquaintance standing with the KintaiYou continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Sul Madásh.You must earn Acquaintance standing with the Kintai of Sul MadáshYour standing among the Tale-wardens earns you a gift. Return to one of their members' quartermasters to be rewarded.Visit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Reach Acquaintance tier with the PhetêkariVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Visit Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate to claim your giftVisit a Tale-warden's assistant at Iridír, Jirush, or UrmâkhYour standing with the Phetekâri grows. You should visit one of their assistants at Telperiën's Gate, Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a well-earned gift.'The secrets of the land, its history, and its people become clearer with every effort you undertake for us. We want to recognize your contributions.

'Please accept one of these fine gifts provided to us by Captain Rothog as a reward for your efforts.

'Be certain to speak with Shulêga. She has other gifts from Captain Rothog.''Please accept one of these fine gifts provided to us by Captain Rothog as a reward for your efforts.

'Speak with one of our quartermasters to see what other gifts Lord Rothog offers.'Your continued efforts in Shagâna inform the Tale-wardens of the people, history, and tribulations of the land. The records of the Ikorbân Valley's history grow due to your efforts.You must earn Acquaintance level with the Tale-wardensYour continued efforts to support An Shêru earns you greater favour with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh.You must earn Acquaintance standing with the Temámir of Jiret-menêshRaphûz informed you he is moving south across the Bridge of Sílabal to a new post. Before his departure he wants to talk over a smoke.Raphûz asked you to join him for a smoke and conversation in the Wrackwade camp.Complete Instance: Across the IkorbânAfter a good conversation and a full night, Raphûz moved on to Khûd Zagin. You should seek him at Jirush.'My friend, I move south across the Bridge of Sílabal tomorrow. Tonight, if you will, join me so we may speak one last time before I make this new journey.

'I grow weary of my choice to chase my parent's wishes. Then, there is the hope that I may see Ashâmi again.''Join me in the evening by the fire. We will share another smoke and discussion.''It is good to see you well, my friend. I pray your journeys have not changed who you are. For you are the best of us.'Gûzinir asked you to go to Ashâgir and see if there is anyone there in need of help.Gûzinir has asked you to go to Ashâgir and see if there are any refugees remaining there as they may be in need of help.Reach the Ashâgir hideout in the cliffsYou found the refugees who remained in Ashâgir. Ask one of them if the are in need of help.Speak with a nearby Ashâgir refugee'Hello stranger, you must be the ${CLASS} of which Galâmka spoke.

'I am Gûzinir, and if you are willing, I have a request for you. If you find yourself near Ashâgir to the west, could I ask of you to search around the hideout there to see if anyone remains? I fled when the Orcs arrived and found myself here, but my friends may still be there and may be in need of your help.''Hello ${CLASS}, what brings you here?'

You explain to them that you were sent by Gûzinir.

'I see. We remained because we know what to expect here and wanted to rebuild. We did not wish to risk new dangers elsewhere. Though I am glad to hear that they are well.'Khôltekh has asked that you return any valuables you see in Deshûkh.Khôltekh has asked that you return any valuables you see in Deshûkh, the Blood Market to him, so that he may return them to the families from which they were stolen. Deshûkh is located in Dil-irmíz, south-east of Mekab-kuphâr.Recover treasure caches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, the Hall of the Kindred.Return to Khôltekh in the Hall of the Kindred'It's not only our people these scoundrels have captured, it's also our treasure. Raiding parties along the coast of the Cape of Umbar have made off with countless caches, spoils of this shadow war we are fighting with those in Umbar-môkh, the Undercity.

'That same smuggler's market where the Umbari nobles were taken - Deshûkh, the Blood Market  - it is likely to have many of these misbegotten treasures as well. While these are certainly not so precious as our citizens' lives, coin is still precious. There is much to rebuild here in Umbar, and many families who have pled with us to have their treasures returned to them.

'You would be doing a great service to us by returning any treasure you find in Deshûkh. Will you lend us your aid?''As I said, this coin is not as precious as lives, but it will surely help many rebuild theirs. You have my thanks.'After introducing yourself to Sigênik in Khûd Zagin, he tests your attention to detail as you meet the most important people in Jirush.Sigênik instructed you to meet each of the elders of Jirush, and to pay special attention to their greetings. One among them, the elder directly supporting the rebels, will greet you differently. The first elder to meet is the wealthy merchant, Igbâl south and east of Sigênik.Speak with the wealthy merchant, Igbâl at his home in JirushIgbâl would not speak with you. His translator suggested you speak with him instead. He stands very near Igbâl within Igbâl's home.Speak with Igbâl's translator, GalamêWith your introduction to Igbâl concluded you should seek Elder Zidemel. He is a zealot who can be found tending a flock of adherent in the outpost. He preaches near the fountain in the outpost mall.Speak with the Elder Zealot, ZidemelYou met with the Elder Zealot Zidemel. You should now turn your attention to find the elder Nangar. He is the outpost's main caretaker. He lives at a home south-west of the northern entrance to Jirush.Speak with the Elder Carpenter, NangarYou met with Nangar. Something about the meeting was different than it was with the others. What was it? You should think about that as you prepare to meet Malgat at his home east of first free standing arch from the northern entrance of Jirush.Speak with the Elder Hunter, MalgatYou met with the four elders and introduced yourself as Sigênik instructed. Now that you are known to the Elders of Jirush. Return to Sigênik near the northern entrance to Jirush. He will likely prepare you for your test.Return to Sigênik near the north entrance at Jirush'To prove your sincerity and ability, I have a simple task. The elders overseeing the continued functions of the outpost do so for reasons selfish or selfless. One among them allies with our cause.

'The others we bear no ill, but their mettle is not strong enough to withstand an Ordâkhai whip, and our trust cannot be misplaced.

'Meet with the elders. They will each provide a gift of water, as is customary. One will gift you the water differently than the others. We shall test your perception when you return.

'Fair?'Igbâl regards you with disdain. Still, a servant brings you water, as is custom. The man near Igbâl clears his throat and beckons you.'My Lord Igbâl offers you water and welcome. You come to our outpost from afar, and we offer you fair warning. Jirush is a difficult place to live. My Lord's desire is to return Jirush to the glory of our ancestors, a trading post grander than the caravansaries you will undoubtedly see throughout the land.

'He works with the other elders here to see that we can outlast the occupation from the south. The cost is of no matter to him.

'Should you decide to remain in our homeland, perhaps we can find use of your services. You will be handsomely paid for your effort.'Elder Zidemel opens his eyes as you approach. A servant approaches with a gift of water.

'Have you come to hear the tale of our returning king? Do you hear his voice in the wind, too? The wheels of prophecy turn.

'Soon, he shall return and lay low the enemy who so long forced our obedience and subjugated our wills.

'The faithful adherents who allay the spirits of their ancestors shall know his glory and light. Have you ventured to our lands to know his grace, foreigner?

'If you be an enemy, know that we shall root you out and lay you low when our king arises. But, if your intentions are noble, perhaps you can assist the infirmed with settling the debts of their souls.'Nangar regards you with a smile. He motions to a nearby table with flagons of water.

'Drink your fill, stranger. You are welcome here if your weapon does not draw the blood of our people. I am Nangar. I see to the upkeep of the outpost, and as you can tell, I need assistance.

'Our enemies assail us from the north and the west. They leave us open to desert crawlers and creatures when they reduce our defences and steal our supplies. But we persist, and perhaps with some help from those from afar, we may thrive.'Malgat looks at you as you approach and nods to a servant. The servant brings you an offering of water.

'Another foreigner passing through our land? Do you mean harm? Or are your intentions genuine?'

He pauses.

'Time will tell your tale, I think.

'I am Malgat. I keep our food stores as best I can and outfit the caravans that pass through with what materials the desert offers... or I used to before time left the telling of my tale to others.

'If your intention here is genuine, you are welcome.''I welcome your return, ${PLAYER}. You have met the elders and now I think I am prepared to test you.'Defeat many All-seeing in Imhûlar.Defeat many All-seeing in Imhûlar.Defeat many All-seeing in ImhûlarDefeat a great many All-seeing in Imhûlar.Defeat many All-seeing in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many All-seeing in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many All-seeing in ImhûlarYour continued efforts to support Shâra Mizâdi and her forces in Idagâl earn you greater favour with Hamât Renewed.You must earn Ally standing with Hamât RenewedYour renown grows among the Kintai of Sul Madásh.You honour the Kintai and assist them with the efforts to preserve Adagím. You should return to their settlement of Sul Madásh to speak with the quartermaster to be recognized for your efforts.Reach Ally standing with the Kintai of Sul MadáshYou honour the Kintai and assist them with the efforts to preserve Adagím. You should return to their settlement of Sul Madásh to speak with the quartermaster to be recognized for your efforts.Speak with Aralath at Sul MadáshYour renown grows among the Kintai of Sul Madásh. Return now to the Quartermaster—they have readied a boon in thanks for your labours.'You stand as a bulwark against the blight. With each harvest, hope is kindled anew. We are strengthened by your aid, and you shall not go unrewarded.'Your standing with the Adúrhid improves and earns you a gift from the Ikorbâni Elves.Your continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.Reach Ally tier with the AdúrhidYour continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.Visit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a giftYour continued efforts to aid the Kintai Elves brings great joy to them. You should visit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a gift from the Elves of the oasis.'We find you an interesting ally. We are not accustomed to finding allies, but we are very pleased that we have an ally in you.

'Our offerings are meager, I fear, but they are gifted with the same measure of kindness you have shown us.'Your continued efforts to support Mûr Ghala earns you greater favour with the City of Zajâna.You must earn Ally standing with the City of ZajânaYou continue to prove your valour, nerve, and measured assistance to the Hunter's Guild of Mûr Ghala.You must earn Ally standing with the Hunter's Guild of Mûr GhalaYour continued efforts to support the Ikorbân Valley earn you greater favour with the Shagâni people.You must earn Ally standing with the IkorbâniYour standing among the Ikorbâni earns you a gift. Return to Kildûg at Iridír to claim your reward.You have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.Reach Ally tier with the IkorbâniYou have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.Visit Kildûg at Iridír to claim a giftYour efforts to assist the Ikorbâni are noted among the people. To recognize your efforts, the leaders of the Shagâni at Iridír wish to honour you with a gift and thanks.'I am pleased that you are such a staunch supporter of our people. For too long we suffered and lost much of who we were as a people.

'Thanks to you and your efforts our culture will return. Please accept this gift.

'If you would like to see what else we offer speak with Nêkhur.'You continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Ikorbân.You must earn Ally standing with the KintaiYou continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Sul Madásh.You must earn Ally standing with the Kintai of Sul MadáshYour standing among the Tale-wardens earns you a gift. Return to one of their members' quartermasters to be rewarded.Visit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Reach Ally tier with the PhetêkariVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Visit Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate to claim your giftVisit a Tale-warden's assistant at Iridír, Jirush, or UrmâkhYour standing with the Phetekâri grows. You should visit one of their assistants at Telperiën's Gate, Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a well-earned gift.'With the small number of Phetekâri making the journey into the Ikorbân Valley, we did not expect to obtain and catalogue so much information this quickly. It is only through your assistance we obtained this knowledge.

'If you continue to deliver the wealth of information you gather, you will overwhelm our capacity to catalogue everything you find. This is a fine problem to have and Captain Rothog will be very pleased.

'Please, take one of these as a gift for your continued assistance. Shulêga can furnish you with more rewards and materials to obtain more knowledge from the ruins scattered throughout Shagâna.''If you continue to deliver the wealth of information you gather, you will overwhelm our capacity to catalogue everything you find. This is a fine problem to have and Captain Rothog will be very pleased.

'Please, take one of these as a gift for your continued assistance. Visit a quartermaster for other rewards.'Your continued efforts in Shagâna inform the Tale-wardens of the people, history, and tribulations of the land. The records of the Ikorbân Valley's history grow due to your efforts.You must earn Ally standing with the Tale-wardensYour continued efforts to support An Shêru earns you greater favour with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh.You must earn Ally standing with the Temámir of Jiret-menêshZildug has shared with you the secret locations of his favourite fishing spots.The first fishing spot is on a bridge crossing a stream east of Arwáth. You should go there and try catching a fish.Find the first fishing spotYou have found the first fishing spot Zildug described. You should equip your fishing rod and see if it is as good a place to fish as Zildug says.Catch a fish at the first spotThe second fishing spot is south along the same stream as the first. You should go there and try catching a fish.Find the second fishing spotYou have found the second fishing spot Zildug described. You should cast a line and see if it is as good a place to fish as Zildug says.Catch a fish at the second spotThe third fishing spot is a dock on the Ikorbân, far to the south-east past the Wrackwade. You should go there and try catching a fish.Find the third fishing spotYou have found the third fishing spot Zildug described. You should throw the old bait and hook and see if it is as good a place to fish as Zildug says.Catch a fish at the third spotYou caught a fish at each of the three locations Zildug recommended. You should return to Iridír and show your catch to the fisherman.'You have been such a help to me, ${PLAYER}. I will show my appreciation by sharing with you where my new favourite fishing spots are! You know how to fish, yes? They are a secret, so do not tell anyone else. If you go fishing there, come back and show me what you caught. I would be very interested to see!

'The first location is on a bridge in a nice, shady spot! You will find it crossing the stream east of Arwáth, the haunted grove. The second fishing spot is south along the same stream, and is also a bridge in a nice, cool, shady place! The third is a fishing dock on the Ikorbân, and is very far to the east. If you continue to follow the main road past the Wrackwade, you will eventually come by it. It does not have shade though, so bring a big hat!''${PLAYER}! You return! Níkhu, look at those lovely fish! I am very impressed. You are an excellent fisher. Did you enjoy the spots? Ambarûl is a beautiful land full of beautiful things to eat.'An envoy from Khûd Zagin crossed the Wrackwade looking for an audience with Ningêna. Ningêna has no time or resources to spare the envoy and asked you to intervene.Ningêna asked you to speak with the Khûdi envoy in the encampment. She cannot spare her time or any of her people to address the envoy's needs. You can find him not far from her location.Speak with SûkalSûkal provided you a coin and a general direction to the road south over the Wrackwade to reach Jirush, and a man named Sigênik. Sigênik is a contact for the rebels in Khûd Zagin.'I have neither patience nor time for beggars. Nor do I have resources to spare for anyone who comes asking for handouts or assistance. The Khûdi Rebels sent me a messenger whom my people must save from an Ordâkhai raiding party near the bridge, and the man still seeks an audience from me several days hence.

'He is either a fool or desperate.'

She sighs.

'Perhaps a bit of both. I do not have the time or the resources to assist them. If you are as earnest as you seem, maybe you can help them. You will find him to the east near a hut.''Ningêna sent you?

'Forgive me. My name is Sûkal, and I am here at the behest of my people. I am from Khûd Zagin. More properly, I am from the outpost Jirush, the 'Swords' Cross' along the 'Road of Riches.' My people have thrown off the yoke of oppression from our Ordâkhai masters in the south, but their retribution has been swift and terrible.

'I see you are not from our lands. The times are dire, and the Ambarûli struggle with their own difficulties. We have been forced into hiding and seek help in ridding our land of our oppressors. If you would be an ally, take this coin and find Sigênik at Jirush. They will test your mettle and integrity.

'I cannot promise wealth or power, and I pray your intentions are noble.

'When the battle dins, cross the Wrackwade and follow the road south to Jirush. Be wary of Ordâkhai patrols. I thank you.'As you reveal the coin to the man, he holds up a hand.

'The first lesson you must learn is discretion. There is an appearance of freedom here, but ever watchful are the eyes of the Ordâkhai on the rise to the north-west.

'We struggle for the future of our land and people. Our leaders are few, hidden, for their safety and their families. The few who remain here are vigilant in their watch and defence. You bear a gift we sent north to our cousins in Ambarûl. If they sent you here, then you shall be tested.

'Prove your value and integrity, and we welcome your assistance. Do not, and suffer the fate of our enemies.'Khôltekh has taken you into his trust, for now. He's asked you to accompany him to his house to speak more about his plans for Umbar.Introduce yourself to the important-looking dwarf standing in Khôltekh's entry room.Introduce yourself to the important-looking dwarf standing in Khôltekh's entry roomListen to the conversation between Khôltekh and Inîk Jewel-brow.Listen to the conversation between Khôltekh and Inîk Jewel-browSpeak with Khôltekh about Inîk Jewel-brow.Speak with Khôltekh about Inîk Jewel-browListen to Khôltekh explain his plans for the Umbar-môkh.Listen to Khôltekh explain his plans for the Umbar-môkhListen to Khôltekh explain his plans for the Umbar-môkh.Listen to Khôltekh explain his plans for the Umbar-môkhSpeak with Khôltekh about his plans for the Umbar-môkh.Speak with Khôltekh about his plans for the Umbar-môkh'I intend to purge Umbar Baharbêl of its shadows, wherever they may hide. Will you help me, ${PLAYER}?’'That went well. I expected much worse. Come with me.'Ilzhâna, a cheerful but suspicious trader of unknown wares, has asked you to thin the number of smugglers, who she insists are not business rivals.Smugglers can be found throughout Tâkhdar.

Ilzhâna has asked you to thin the number of smugglers stalking Tâkhdar and interfering in her trade. She insists it's for the safety of the cellars, not because they are business rivals.Defeat smugglers in Tâkhdar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ilzhâna can be found at Tilmakhím on the western side of Tâkhdar.

Return to Ilzhâna with news of your exploits.Speak to Ilzhâna'My honest and most helpful friend, might you lend a hand once again? Trade flows like heady wine now that you have returned my stolen crates! My good business, however, has attracted covetous gazes. You have no doubt seen ruffians and smugglers about. They are no business contacts or rivals of mine, I assure you! Certainly no friends of mine, nor yours! If you were to rid Tâkhdar of some small number, I am sure no one would miss them.''Have you convinced any of those smugglers to leave Tâkhdar, my favourite future customer? I am certain no harm shall befall you, what with those shiny weapons you bear!''So you return! Then you encountered no trouble persuading those brigands to depart? No, no, I do not recall asking you to slay any such fine business folk. But if you did, it cannot be helped, ah ha! How truly terrible such ruffians assaulted you, leaving you no choice but to fight back and end their own business ventures.

'You are too good to this honest trader. Too good indeed! Take this with my eternal gratitude.'Aítarshun explained he failed to honour an oath to a man he knew. He knows the man's spirit is not at rest and wants to make amends before his time in the world is done.Aítarshun asked you to help him fulfil an oath forsaken to a man who perished in the ruined khanâg north of Shonith. He gave you a phial of oasis water and bid you deliver it to the shade.The shade faded from existence. The man is at peace, though it was displeased with Aítarshun. Return to the Elf at Shonith and tell him what occurred.Inform Aítarsun at Shonith his oath is fulfilled'Tharashil does too much. I am pleased she found you.

'I will tell you my tale and leave you a choice.

'Once, long ago, I made an oath to a man at a khânag north of this oasis. I made this oath after he risked his life for mine when an Ordâkhai soldier cast me off my oryx while I rode across the wild.

'When the man called me to see my debt through, I was unable. He perished at the hands of the Ordâkhai. I have mourned his passing and my failure since.

'He walks the ruins of the khanâg north and west of here and I would see him set to rest. I give this gift of water. Take this gift to his spirit.'The shade halts its moaning and looks at your gift.

'Water. Water was his pledge. Water was his oath. He did not come when I called. I thirsted. I choked on the sand. I died.

'Now, as he passes from the world, he fulfils his oath.'

The spirit tilts the water back as if drinking.

'As I fade, so shall he....''All is as it should be. He is right. I made an oath to that man. I made an oath that I did not honour, and so I needed to make amends before I could fade, and I have; thanks to you.

'Return to Tharashil. Tell her I am prepared.'Zidemel asks you to assist his adherent, Andur. Andur wishes to extend his lineage. His family was all murdered by the Ordâkhai, and Zidemel told him of a way to live on.Zidemel the zealot told Andur his bloodline would live on if he provided the desert a hefty gift of blood. Andur asked that you collect the blood of sand-sifters so that he can fulfil this gift.Collect drams of sand-sifter blood (${NUMBER}/10)You ventured into the desert and collected ten drams of sand-sifter blood for Andur. Return the blood to Andur at Jirush. He is listening to Zidemel preach in the centre of the outpost.'Who are you?'

You tell the man and explain that Zidemel sent you.

'Zidemel found someone to help me with penance? Blessed are his words.

'Listen well, ${PLAYER}. I am Andur, the last of my bloodline. My brothers, sisters, and all their children are dead at the hands of the Ordâkhai. Zidemel said my family would live on if I gift a patch of the desert the blood of its sons and daughters mixed with mine.

'The desert sand-sifters to the south-east are the true daughters and sons of the desert. Collect drams of their blood that I may extend my lineage.''The Ordâkhai took my family from the world. I will not die the last of my lineage. Please, ${RACE}, help me. The sand-sifters gather in number south-east of Jirush. With their blood my lineage may live on.''I thank you for this gift, ${PLAYER}. I shall make my last trek into the desert and mix my blood and theirs. I will ensure my lineage does not pass into history with my death because of your actions this day.'Endunâm wants to recreate a dish his grandmother used to make but does not have all the ingredients he needs.Endunâm has asked you to collect beans found along the road travelling north-east to the old salt mines. He also needs pork loins from wild boars and fresh herbs, both from Shegdush far to the east.Collect pork loins from fen-wallowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect beans (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect fresh herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected the meat, beans, and herbs for which Endunâm asked. You should bring the ingredients to him in Iridír.Bring the ingredients to Endunâm in Iridír'Tell me lûkal, have you any interest in tasting Ambarûli cuisine? I am trying to recreate a dish my grandmother used to make, but I do not have all the ingredients. I will tell you what - if you bring me the ingredients, I will give you a plate! Then you can say you have had some of the best food in the world!'

The man laughs heartily and grins.

'What say you, friend? I need some snap beans. They grow on vines to the north-east along the road to the old salt mines. I will need loins from fen-wallowers. There are many of them far to the east in Shegdush. You can also find fresh herbs that I think will be perfect for this dish in Shegdush. The sooner you get them, the sooner we can eat!''I need some fresh herbs, beans, and meat from fen-wallowers. The sooner you get them, the sooner we can eat!''Lûkal, you are back! Have you the ingredients? Yes, there they are! Perfect!'

You watch as Endunâm expertly prepares the ingredients and adds a sauce filled with spices, garlic, and onions. He puts the ingredients in a large cooking pot and places it in the oven. As it simmers, the smell is enticing and it starts to feel like it's been forever since you last ate.

Endunâm finally takes the pot from the oven, inspects his handiwork, and gives it a taste.

'Mmm. Quite good, but not exactly the same. I am getting closer though!  Here, have a bowl and I will give you some to take on the road. Thank you for your help lûkal, be safe in your travels!'Nashôn has asked you to investigate an area of Ilmabiri beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. There have been reports that lead him to believe that there is an encampment of homeless children there and he is concerned for their welfare.Travel to the western areas of Ilmabiri and locate the camp of homeless children.Find the camp Nashôn describedYou have located the camp Nashôn described, but he was mistaken. This is not a camp for children.Defeat goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have discovered a camp of goblins inside Ilmabiri. You should look around the camp for clues explaining why they are here.Investigate the goblin campYou have discovered a camp of goblins inside Ilmabiri. While investigating the camp, you have spotted a note.Read the noteYou have discovered a camp of goblins inside Ilmabiri. While investigating the camp, you have spotted a note indicating that they have recently come from Súlstrok to attempt to rescue their leader, Shakfut Slit-throat, from the fighting pits of the arena.Talk to Nashôn'Umbar Baharbêl is a rough city that has seen more than its fair share of war and loss. Sail-haven residents have reported petty crimes committed by small, shadowy figures spotted lurking near sewer entrances late at night. I believe that at the western end of Ilmabiri, there is an encampment of the city's homeless children. People have been referring to them as Mâtrikhai, the Unseen Ones.

'Foetid, dank sewers are no place for a child. Would you mind scouting the encampment out and seeing how they fare? I'm not sure we would be prepared to move them immediately, but we may be able to re-direct some supplies in the meantime.'You're unable to read the majority of the messy scratch on the note but manage to discern that the goblins hail from Súlstrok, to the west of Umbar Baharbêl. They are here in an attempt to stage a rescue of their leader, Shakfut Slit-throat, who has gone to the arena to fight as a gladiator.'Goblins!?  Are you quite sure they were not children?'

You explain that you fought some, and found a note that explains their presence.

'This is very unexpected, to say the least. Thank you for discovering this. I will pass the information along to my Captain.'Baziphâr is likely still hiding in Tâkhdar, below Dâr Laja.

Baziphâr has agreed to return home, but you have a sneaking suspicion he needs to be scolded into compliance.Baziphâr is likely still hiding in Tâkhdar, below Dâr Laja.

Find Baziphâr and scold him for hiding below the city.Search for Baziphâr below Dâr Laja in TâkhdarBaziphâr is likely still hiding in Tâkhdar below Dâr Laja.

Find Baziphâr and scold him for hiding below the city.Scold Baziphâr and convince him to return homeBaziphâr is still hiding in Tâkhdar below Dâr Laja.Speak with BaziphârHanâth is waiting at The Din of Arms in the Tor-gardens, in the western side of Umbar Baharbêl.

Hanâth will surely be grateful to hear her husband has returned home.Speak with Hanâth'Are we drinking one last time together? No? You said my wife is... hm. You and I are friends, but we will not be if you tell me to go home. The scolding I shall receive! No, no, I cannot bear it.

'But you are right, of course. No, I need no assistance. I will... err, find my way there myself, yes. Do not help me! I will be... elsewhere, ho ho!''My husband has still not returned home! You cannot trust a word that faithless man says. I am sure he is still drinking in this city's underbelly!''My husband has still not returned home! You cannot trust a word that faithless man says. I am sure he is still drinking in this city's underbelly!''You have found my husband? He has not yet arrived. Perhaps his drunken self has gotten lost? Please hurry! I miss that besotted fool and I do not wish him robbed further blind!''Here I am, just as I have promised you to tell my wife... it is near enough, is it not?

'My wife... I cannot join her inside the Din of Arms! The owner and I have a.... misunderstanding. Tell her I will be at home. No, I swear! I will be at home. I need to... lie down.''I will go home once I see you have spoken to my wife. I do not want you to send hounds after me if you fear I have vanished. But please do not take too long. My head hurts.''Baziphâr is at our house? You are certain? He has promised? I am so glad to hear. Thank you for returning my troublesome man home to me. I know he is a handful, but he is my handful. I should go home now to tend to his no-doubt-aching head, and remind him to stop harassing customers and businesses! Who does that, anyway?'Khôltekh believes that Sêkhta is stealing the Candle of Umbar, a ship docked in the Sail-haven. Help him apprehend Sêkhta!Speak with Khôltekh on the dock.Speak with Khôltekh on the dockMove to stop Sêkhta and his men from commandeering The Candle of Umbar.Move to stop Sêkhta from commandeering The Candle of UmbarDefeat Sêkhta's guards!Defeat Sêkhta's guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Sêkhta's honour guard!Defeat Sêkhta's honour guardDefeat Sêkhta's honour guard!Defeat Sêkhta's honour guardListen to Khôltekh confront Sêkhta.Listen to Khôltekh confront SêkhtaListen to Khôltekh confront Sêkhta.Listen to Khôltekh confront SêkhtaSpeak with Khôltekh on the dock.Speak with Khôltekh on the dock'There they are - quickly, we must stop them from boarding that ship!''The ravings of a madman.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We have done much for Umbar, both above and below-ground this day. My guard will take care of this mess.

'Let me buy you a drink. Umbar will sleep peacefully tonight because of your deeds... and mine, of course.'Dalagín, the Dumûri captain, has asked you to fetch the arrows she ordered from the fletcher.More arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The fletcher, Tínsha, can be found at the east end of the crafters' wharf.Talk to TínshaMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. Tínsha has requested that you bring her a crate of arrowheads from Gurtum, the arrowsmith. The smithy can be found at the north end of the crafters' wharf.Find the smithyMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The fletcher has requested that you bring her a crate of arrowheads from the arrowsmith.Talk to GurtumMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The arrowsmith, Gurtum, has given you leave to take a crate of arrowheads to the fletcher, Tínsha.Carry the crate of arrowheads to TínshaMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. Gurtum, the arrowsmith, has given you leave to take a crate of arrowheads to the fletcher. Tínsha. Tínsha is at the east end of the crafters' wharf.Talk to TínshaMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The fletcher has given you leave to take the tub of arrows to the Dumûri captain, Dalagín. Dalagín is near the archers' towers on the west side of Iridír.Bring the arrows to DalagínMore arrows are needed for the defence of Iridír. The fletcher has provided a tub of arrows that you brought to Dalagín. You should talk to her.Talk to Dalagín'It takes many arrows to remind the Ordâkhai that they do not want to come to Iridír. I have ordered additional arrows from Tínsha, the fletcher, but have not been able to spare anyone to get them. Would you mind? Tínsha is at the east end of the crafters' wharf.''Go find Tínsha, the fletcher, and pick up the arrows I ordered.''You say you are here to retrieve arrows for the Dumûri? I will give them to you if you do me one favour. I am running low on arrowheads. I do not make them myself, they come from Gurtum, the arrowsmith who casts them in iron and sharpens them. Go to Gurtum and bring me a crate of arrowheads, and I will give you the arrows.''Go to Gurtum, the arrowsmith, and bring me a crate of arrowheads. Then I will give you the arrows.''Come to pick up for Tínsha, have you? There's a crate ready to go just there. Help yourself to it.''Ah, there are my arrowheads! Thank you for getting them for me. You may take that tub of arrows there to the Dumûri.''There you are, I was beginning to think you got lost. Thank you for bringing the arrows. We will put them to good use.'Ashâmi is tasked with going to the a serval den to kill a diseased serval there. She asks you to meet her there to assist her.Ashâmi was attacked by a serval and gravely wounded in her youth. She asks for your help against the diseased serval she is tasked to kill to prove herself to Numûru. The serval camp is east of Urmâkh.Meet with Ashâmi near the serval den east of UrmâkhAshâmi greeted you when you arrived outside of the serval den near Urmâkh. She waits for you to say you are ready to assist in hunting the diseased serval, Kanagir.Complete Instance: Ashâmi's ChallengeAshâmi completed her task at Tir Katar. Return to her home in Urmâkh and discuss her next steps.Ashâmi's resolve is apparent.

'I was ten when the serval attacked me. My father put the beast down immediately. My wounds became infected. I nearly died. My father wanted the wounds to heal on their own.

'My mother took me to Lathagwid. It was only with her care I survived.

'My fear of these cats is great. I think I shall need a bit of Raphûz's confidence. Maybe your help.

'The serval's den is east of here, in central Imhûlar. Will you meet me there?''Let us use caution as we search for the beast, Kanagir. Something in this forest fills me with dread.''When Raphûz completes his task, we will speak with you.

'Your help was invaluable today. I understand why Raphûz regards you so well and has such faith in you, ${PLAYER}.'Defeat Anâkhi within Ashunûg, the Fane of the AccursedDefeat Anâkhi within Ashunûg, the Fane of the AccursedDefeat Anâkhi within Ashunûg, the Fane of the AccursedWe have discovered a dangerous cult of usan-kûni worshippers hiding in our own back-yard. They call themselves Anâkhi, and have made their home inside Ashunûg, a salt mine in northern Ambarûl that has long been abandoned. We are only recently freed of Sauron, the All-seeing, and must not allow this new cult to take hold. The Anâkhi scorpion worshippers must be driven from our lands.A fierce brute is guarding the way deeper into the mines of Ashunûg.

Defeat Eshêgur the Reaper.Defeat Eshêgur the ReaperA group of Anâkhi cultists stand at the passage even deeper to the mine, guarding something important. Their rituals must be stopped.

Defeat the Anâkhi Ensemble.Defeat Anâkhi EnsembleA monstrous scorpion dwells deep within the mine of Ashunûg. This must be the Anâkhi's idol, and it must be destroyed before it can bring terror to the nearby lands in Ambarûl.

