Defeat Nâkhugir.Defeat NâkhugirWe have discovered a dangerous cult of usan-kûni worshippers hiding in our own back-yard. They call themselves Anâkhi, and have made their home inside Ashunûg, a salt mine in northern Ambarûl that has long been abandoned. We are only recently freed of Sauron, the All-seeing, and must not allow this new cult to take hold. The Anâkhi scorpion worshippers must be driven from our lands.Complete 'Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Tier 3'Belondor has asked you to check on a group of guards from the Fleet-fast that he has sent into the sewers under the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. Citizens have reported a problem with crocodiles coming out from the sewers and troubling them, but Belondor believes that this is just a symptom of a larger problem below.You have been asked to check on a group of guards that were sent into the sewers beneath the Sail-haven. Their post can be found by entering Umbar-môkh through a door between The Wharf-gate and The Fisherfold.Find the guard post in the sewersYou have been asked to check on a group of guards that were sent into the sewers. You should introduce yourself to Nashôn, who appears to be in charge.Talk to Nashôn'It is good to see you again, my friend. I heard you have been helping with various tasks around the city, and I wanted to thank you for that. It's important for keeping the peace that citizens don't lose faith in the Kindred after... recent events.'

A darkness begins to creep onto the man's face before he shakes it off and returns to the present.

'Since the re-opening of Dâr Laja, some of the residents of the Sail-haven have come to me with their troubles, as they currently have no representative on the council. They tell me of crocodiles coming out of the city sewers and causing trouble in the streets. Apparently, someone has lost a beloved pet.

'I have dispatched a few guards from the Fleet-fast to go there and assess the situation. I suspect that there is more going on down there than just wandering beasts. I happen to have some familiarity with these tunnels, as it is where Mêshka and I were forced to hide for a time to escape the fires of the All-seeing's priests. The beasts in the tunnels underfoot are content to stay there so long as they are not disturbed. Something else is causing this.

'If you would like to continue giving aid to the people of Umbar Baharbêl, I am eager to receive a report from my soldiers there. You can find them by entering Umbar-môkh through a door between The Wharf-gate and The Fisherfold.''Hoi there, traveller! What is it that brings you to Ilmabiri, the home of fierce beasts, foul smells, and now three brave soldiers?'

You introduce yourself and tell him that Belondor has sent you to check on them and ask if they need any help.

'${PLAYER}! That is so kind of you! We are still setting up our post here. I have decided to call it Kruha-sûrja, which in your tongue means Bastion Against the Beasts. Do you like it? We would certainly not refuse your help.'Defeat Rumók the Blood-spiller in Thûr Hin.Defeat Rumók the Blood-spiller in Thûr Hin.Defeat Rumók the Blood-spillerSlay many Ordâkhai foes throughout the Ikorbân Valley.Slay many Ordâkhai foes throughout the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Ambarûl (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Khûd Zagin (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Imhûlar (Advanced)Defeat many bats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat many bats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat many bats in the Umbar-môkhDefeat a great many bats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat many bats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat a great many bats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat a great many bats in the Umbar-môkhHaving found Bârshud's new location, the formidable fortress of Dun Shûma in Khud Zagin, Mizâdi asks you to gather supplies and help rally the local people for one last assault to rid Shagâna of Bârshud for good.Speak with Sârgud, the blacksmith in Iridír.Speak with Sârgud, the blacksmith in IridírGather ore for Sârgud in the hills north-east of Iridír.Collect ore for Sârgud in the hills north-east of Iridír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the ore to Sârgud in Iridír.Gather shields from Sârgud, the local blacksmith.Gather shields from Sârgud's table (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather supplies and provisions from around Iridír.Gather supplies from around Iridír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the supplies and shields to Numûru in Iridír.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír.Speak with Mizâdi in IridírSpeak with Girhâzi and Amalíbi in Iridír.Speak with Girhâzi in IridírSpeak with Amalíbi outside Iridír, in her encampmentSpeak with Mizâdi in Iridír.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír'My scouts have excellent news, ${PLAYER}. We've found where Bârshud's army is located. He is in southern Khûd Zagin, at a place known as Dun Shûma. What he is doing there, we have no idea. But this is our chance. Before he fortifies his position and brings all his forces to Dun Shûma, we have time to strike him quickly.

'If we can defeat him, it should cause his army to scatter to the winds. We could have peace in Shagâna, friend, real peace for the first time in a very long time.

'But first we need to prepare for this battle. Could you gather shields and supplies for our warriors, and then bring them to Numûru? You might start with the local blacksmith, Sârgud.''You want shields? Everybody wants shields. Sârgud is so popular all of the sudden.

'For Mizâdi? Oh a Shâra wants them. Well, of course. Of course. Sârgud do this, Sârgud do that. Every day it's the same.

'I have many orders, friend. Many orders. I love Shagâna as much as anyone, but even the Shâra cannot cut the line.

'I'll tell you what I can do. Sârgud performs miracles, you'll see! I have some shields almost ready. You gather me some more ore from the north-eastern hills to replace what I used here, and I will give the Shâra these shields. Yes, Sârgud's amazing. I know, I know, you don't even need to tell me.

'Get me that ore and you can have the shields.''Thank you for swiftly gathering those supplies, and for dealing with Sârgud. What a headache.

'Now we need to assess whether the others are ready as well. If they are, we will leave at first light tomorrow and make our way south to Dun Shûma. You should speak with Girhâzi and Amalíbi to ensure they and their fighters are ready to leave so soon.''Yes, we will be ready. You can count on us.''Yes, what warriors I have that can still fight will be ready at dawn's light. Tell Mizâdi we will see this through to the end.''Oho, these shields are well made! Sârgud is lucky that his boasts are equal to his craft. And look at this! This is enough for our Subuzûri to feast on for a fortnight. We shall not go hungry with this much grain!

'I will take those off your hands. You should speak with Mizâdi, I believe she has another ask of you.''Excellent. Tomorrow is the day, ${PLAYER}. Tomorrow is the day Bârshud's reign of terror ends in Shagâna.''Ah, yes. That should do nicely. See how good Sârgud is at both smithing and negotiation? Here are your shields. Only the best for the Shâra.'Mizâdi has tracked Bârshud to the fortress of Dun Shûma in Khûd Zagin. The time has come to meet Bârshud in pitched battle and defeat him for good.Journey to Khûd Zagin and meet with Mizâdi outside of Bârshud's fortress, Dun Shûma.Journey to Khûd Zagin and meet with Mizâdi outside of Dun ShûmaSpeak with Mizâdi outside of Bârshud's fortress, Dun Shûma when you are ready to go.Speak with Mizâdi when you are ready to goSpeak with Mizâdi in Khûd Zagin on the hilltop outside of Dun Shûma.Speak with Mizâdi in Khûd Zagin on the hilltop'The crucial hour has arrived, friend! Meet us outside of Dun Shûma, ${PLAYER}. There we will end Bârshud's reign of terror, and drive him out of Shagâna for good.''This is a good spot to rest a moment. We will gather here and then press on into the fortress proper.''Let us press into Dun Shûma. For glorious victory!''Bârshud is close, I can feel it. It is time we drove him out of Shagâna for good.

'Come on, ${PLAYER}! For Shagâna, and for Hamât!'Push into Dun Shûma and end the threat of Bârshud!Speak with Mizâdi to begin the assault.Speak with Mizâdi to begin the assaultSpeak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma in Khûd Zagin.Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma'We are close enough that I can taste victory, ${PLAYER}. I would see this Bârshud answer for his crimes against the peoples of Shagâna. He thinks me a fool and a child? We shall soon see which one of us is the fool.''We must celebrate this victory, but I know my celebration shall be bittersweet. I meant to see the end of Bârshud, but he has survived. If left alone, he will regain an army and make war on Shagâna once more. I must think more on this, but Shagâna is not safe - cannot be safe - whilst Bârshud still breathes.

'But that is a matter for another day. Now we should gather the others and celebrate this victory, incomplete as it feels to me. We have driven Bârshud out of Shagâna, and destroyed his fighting force, and that is cause enough for rejoicing today.''We are as ready as we'll ever be. Now we must confront Bârshud and end this fight!'The time has come to fight for Maurûsh and retake the stronghold from the Orcs. All the preparations are complete and Galâmka is ready to lead the charge.The preparations are complete and Galâmka is ready to begin the battle to retake Maurûsh.Speak with Galâmka when you are ready to beginSpeak with Galâmka about the battle.Speak with Galâmka'The day has come. Today, we will retake our home!'

'We are as prepared as we can be for the fight ahead. I feel the determination in every one of our hearts. Some of us may not see tomorrow, but know that we all fight for our home, for what is ours! We fight to show these Orcs that these are our lands and they will not drive us from them!

'Let us go now. Let us retake Maurûsh from the monsters who defile it!

'With me my friends! Into Maurûsh and into the fires of battle!'Galâmka takes a moment before looking up at you to speak.

'Maurûsh is lost.'

Galâmka pauses again.

'There was such hope after all we had done. After all you had helped us to achieve. We fought our hardest, but it was all for nothing. None of us expected that monster to be there. He must be one of them who came from the demon pits. I did not expect them to have such power.

'We may have lost this fight, but Maurûsh is still our home. We must take our time to heal and recover, but this is not the end of our struggle.

'Thank you for standing with us, ${PLAYER}. At the very least, thanks to you, those of us here still remain to fight another day and will continue to fight until our final breath.''The day has come. Today, we will retake our home!'

'We are as prepared as we can be for the fight ahead. I feel the determination in every one of our hearts. Some of us may not see tomorrow, but know that we all fight for our home, for what is ours! We fight to show these Orcs that these are our lands and they will not drive us from them!

'Let us go now. Let us retake Maurûsh from the monsters who defile it!

'With me my friends! Into Maurûsh and into the fires of battle!'Khânah has a growing concern with the kergrim below the cliffs in Tûkurdul and asks you to get rid of them.Khânah has asked you to get rid of the kergrim in Tûkurdul at the bottom of the cliffs to help make the hideout safer for the people who remain.Defeat kergrim near Ashagir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Khânah and let him know that the hideout will now be safe from the kergrim.Return to Khânah and update him on the kergrim'Greetings, ${CLASS}. I am glad to see an adventurer such as yourself.

'I have been keeping track of the kergrim in Tûkurdul below and I begin to worry for our safety. The cliff itself is our only defence, and with the lift destroyed we would be unable to escape should they choose to attack.

'I ask that you travel down into Tûkurdul and thin out the number of kergrim in the area. It would make us much safer here in Ashâgir if you would.''You have returned. I have noticed less activity as of late from down in Tûkurdul. I am to believe that this is your doing.

'We shall be much safer now because of what you have accomplished here. I thank you.'Thórvilon has given you the honour of being a tree-bearer for the Adúrhid. You are to transplant the first young tree saplings into the greater forests of Adagím.Speak with Culvair the grove-tender in Vartúlin.Speak with Culvair the grove-tender in VartúlinCollect rich soil from around Vartúlin.Collect rich soil from around Vartúlin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Go to Ulthral's nursery and carefully remove tree saplings for planting in the greater forest.Carefully gather the tree saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Go to the where the forest of Favrathór meets the edge of Vartúlin. Go to the edge of Vartúlin then march east and north around the rock formation. Plant the tree saplings there.Go to the edge of Vartúlin then march north around the rock formationPlant the young tree saplings in the forest just outside Vartúlin.Plant the tree saplings in Favrathór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Thórvilon in Vartúlin.'I have a final task for you, my friend. Though this is less a task, and more an honour befitting all you have done for us. You are to be an Adúrhid tree-bearer.

'The first young tree saplings we have grown resistant to the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight, are ready to be transported out of Vartúlin and into the forests of Adagím proper. I have instructed the grove-tenders that you are the one to be given the honour of doing this. Speak with Culvair, one of our grove-tenders. He will explain more deeply. And, once more, thank you for all you have done for us, ${PLAYER}.''You have borne the first of many trees back to the forests of Favrathór. It is not again Laithór, the Emerald Wood, nor will it be for many years. But we have hope now, because of your actions.

'The Adúrhid use 'Tree-bearer' to denote someone who has done great works for the lands near their home. Though you are not Adúrhid, you have done great works near our home. You should know that not many outsiders get to wear this title. But for you, we will make a special exception. You may wear this name with pride.''Thórvilon told me you are to be our tree-bearer? It is quite the honour. Almost never given to an outsider. Thórvilon must think quite highly of you.

'Well, your task is simple enough. Gather rich soil into this sack from throughout Vartúlin. Then come back here and carefully remove these young tree saplings you see. You are then to replant them in greater Adagím. Dig a small hole out, replant them and then cover their roots with the rich soil you collect. They are to be about 20 paces east, beyond the edge of Vartúlin. This will allow us to check them easily, to ensure they are truly hardy enough to withstand the Lâg Dávrit. Off with you then.'Deep within Harkhaphâr, the Nêpharai are led by Umâr. Seek him out and defeat him.Locate Umâr within Harkhaphâr and defeat him.Defeat UmârReturn to Dabôr the Breaker in Hulzidâr and inform him of Umâr's demise and the recovery of the journal.Return to Dabôr the Breaker in Hulzidâr and present him with the journal'Your work thus far in fighting the Nêpharai has been instrumental to our survival. The leader of the Nêpharai, Umâr organized and led the revolt, and was personally responsible for the death of a number of the refugees. His leadership endangers our people, and he must pay for what he has done.

'Seek him out and dispatch him for his misdeeds.''This journal is most disturbing. It seems that Umâr was not working alone, and was in fact sponsored to lead this revolt. I fear that The Storm may have more enemies throughout the court than he realizes. I will pass this journal along. Your hard work has put Hulzidâr on secure footing for a good deal of time.'Yâshri has requested that you help recover items of value from Ghâr Mejet.Find and recover valuable goods scattered amongst the Dead in Ghâr Mejet.Recover valuable goods (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Yâshri with the valuable goods.

Yâshri can be found just north of Ghâr Mejet.Return to Yâshri with the valuable goods'Scattered throughout this cursed place are bits and baubles that can be sold topside so that our small settlement can afford supplies and food. While this is dangerous work, it is necessary for our people's survival.

'If you are brave enough, could you scour the area and recover some of these objects?''Your work is excellent, and these valuable goods will go a long way to support our cause. I cannot express my thanks greatly enough, as now my family and friends have food to eat for the coming months.'After news of the assaults led by Bârshud II reached Iridír many of Ashnân's farm-hands fled to seek a safer place for them and their families. In the chaos they abandoned their tools and Ashnân needs your help gathering them up.Ashnân needs your help gathering the tools abandoned by the farm-hands in Burukíri. He suggested checking behind the house first.Check behind the house for any abandoned toolsYou spotted some abandoned tools behind the house in Burukíri. Gather them so they can be returned to Ashnân.Gather abandoned shovels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ashnân needs your help gathering the tools abandoned by the farm-hands in Burukíri. He said to check by the beehives next.Check by the beehives for any abandoned toolsYou spotted some abandoned tools near the beehives in Burukíri. Gather them so they can be returned to Ashnân.Gather abandoned axes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ashnân needs your help gathering the tools abandoned by the farm-hands in Burukíri. Ashnân thinks there may be some left by the mill.Check around the mill for any abandoned toolsYou spotted some abandoned tools near the mill in Burukíri. Gather them so they can be returned to Ashnân.Gather abandoned shovels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather abandoned axes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Ashnân in Burukíri and give him the abandoned tools you were able to recover.Return to Ashnân in Burukíri'Hello, my friend. If you are willing I am in need of some help. When word of the assaults led by Bârshud II reached the people here in Burukíri some of my farm-hands fled the area with their families to find somewhere safer.

'I do not condemn their decisions, but in the chaos when they fled my farm-hands abandoned the tools they had in their hands. I need them back and accounted for. This is where you come in!

'If you have the time, I ask that you check around Burukíri for abandoned tools. The places that the farm-hands worked were behind the house, near the beehives, and around the mill. I would suggest checking there first.''My tools! Thank you my friend. I can now make sure the work is getting done in Burukíri, and the people here will be ready for the coming fight.'Galâmka has asked you to gather weapons from the Orcs in Maurûsh to help arm the fighters in Ub Nishir.Using the information from the scouting report gathered from Emlû, Galâmka has asked you to take weapons from the Orcs in Maurûsh so they can arm themselves.Seize Orc weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir with the weapons you have retrieved in Maurûsh.'Now that you are here, we can begin. Emlû gave his life for this valuable information and it saddens me that you found him the way that you did. His report that you were able to retrieve details of locations within Maurûsh where the Orcs are keeping their weapon stores.'

Galâmka indicates to locations on the map where Emlû claimed there are weapons.

'I need you again to make your way into Maurûsh, and take what weapons you can from these locations. This would be would of great use to arm the fighters here.''You return with weapons! You are a true help, my friend.

'This day you have furthered our cause yet again as well as ensured that Emlû's death was not in vain. We all thank you for that.

'Come back when you can. We still have more to do before we can strike back in Maurûsh, but we are growing stronger by the day.'Defeat the leaders of the cultists spread throughout Jâx Ugikh. Ghamêla and Hênakh have long been a scourge to this place for some time.Defeat the leaders of the cultists spread throughout Jâx Ugikh. Locate and defeat Ghamêla and Hênakh.Defeat GhamêlaDefeat HênakhInform Azrât in Kên Taghlim and let her know that Ghamêla and Hênakh have been defeated.Talk to Azrât in Kên Taghlim'While many of the cultists near Jâx Ugikh represent a threat to those who dwell in this place, there are two powerful leaders who endanger all of our encampments below the city. Ghamêla and Hênakh have driven their followers to horrific acts that endanger this entire portion of the catacombs.

'Can you travel to Jâx Ugikh, locate Ghamêla and Hênakh and drive them from this place?''Ghamêla and Hênakh have long been a scourge in this place. It is said that many refugees and people attempting to eek out a life beneath the city have fallen victim to their cruel whims.

'While not safe, these foul cultists should take a good deal of time to reorganize after losing their leadership.

'Thank you. You have saved many countless lives this day, and my expedition is safe because of it.'Demand for boar hides and meat in the city grows steadily. Abido requests that you collect hides and meat from boars to meet the orders placed by his patrons.Abido asked that you make your way throughout the eastern Cape of Umbar in search of boars to collect their hides and meat.Collect boar hides (${NUMBER}/12)Collect boar haunches (${NUMBER}/12)You collected hides and haunches from the boars in the wilds of eastern Cape of Umbar. Deliver the haunches and hides to Abido at the hunter's expedition camp in south-eastern Cape of Umbar.'My patron asked for more boar meat and hides. The commoners eat well because of our efforts. Shall we continue our enterprise where you collect the beast's loins and skin and I ship it on to the city?''As long as there is demand for the boars I will have work for you, friend. You are a swift hand at this and I am grateful for that fact. As always, here is your payment for the job you've done.''You will find the boars strewn across the crags and hills throughout the eastern Cape of Umbar. Collect their hides and haunches and return them to me here at the encampment.'Defeat many boars in Ambarûl.Defeat many boars in Ambarûl.Defeat many boars in AmbarûlSlay many boars throughout the Ikorbân Valley.Slay many boars throughout the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Boar-slayer of Ambarûl (Advanced)Complete Boar-slayer of Imhûlar (Advanced)Defeat a great many boars in Ambarûl.Defeat many boars in Ambarûl.Defeat a great many boars in AmbarûlDefeat a great many boars in AmbarûlDefeat many boar in Imhûlar.Slay many boar in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Slay many boar in ImhûlarSlay a great many boar in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Slay many boar in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Defeat a great many boar in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many boar in ImhûlarA bounty posted by Bôgalekh to go to Ghâs Hejai in the north and reduce the number of Hakâri in the area.You accepted a bounty notice asking you to reduce the number of Hakâri in Ghâs Hejai. It can be found to the north of Jadambor.Reach the Hakâri camp to the north of JadamborYou accepted a bounty notice asking you to reduce the number of Hakâri in Ghâs Hejai. It can be found to the north of Jadambor.Defeat Hakâri within Ghâs Hejai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have culled the number of cultists.Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have culled the number of cultistsThe bounty notice reads:

We can not let the cultists rebuild their strength here in Dil-irmíz.

Any willing adventurers need only to go north to Ghâs Hejai and defeat any you encounter. If you succeed, return to Zûfan here in Jadambor and he will reward you for your efforts.

They can be dangerous. You may want to bring some companions.You inform Zûfan about the completed bounty.

'Great work ${CLASS}. I know they will return soon enough, but the longer we can keep fighting them back thanks to the likes of adventurers like you, the better.

'Be sure to check the board for more requests, we need all the help we can get down here.'A bounty has been posted with a request to go to Jalkhûl in the south and cull the number of spiders in the area.You accepted a bounty notice asking you to reduce the number of spiders in Jalkhûl. It can be found to the south-east of Jadambor.Reach Jalkhûl to the south-east of JadamborYou accepted a bounty notice asking you to reduce the number of spiders in Jalkhûl. It can be found to the south-east of Jadambor.Defeat spiders within Jalkhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have culled the number of spidersInform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have culled the number of spidersThe bounty notice reads:

