Reward offered to any individual that puts down the bog-lurker dubbed 'Drâghru'. This dangerous creature is unusually large and aggressive. It has been determined to be a threat to the people of Umbar Baharbêl that must be dealt with. See Nashôn to collect this bounty.'Ah, you have defeated the infamous Drâghru? Thank you! Here is some coin for your trouble.'The infamous Orc Kaursu has killed many Hamâti warriors from his perch in Kûr Anzar. You are to defeat him and return to Numûru with his vile armour.Mizâdi Shâra, Queen of Renewed Hamât, has posted a bounty seeking skilled soldiers to defeat the infamous Orc Kaursu, slayer of over fifty Hamâti warriors, and return to her Hand, Numûru, with his armour. He keeps his council with the Barkhûshim in Kûr Anzar.Defeat Kaursu and collect his vile armourBring Kaursu's vile armour to Numûru in Urmâkh to collect your reward.Bring Kaursu's vile armour to Numûru in UrmâkhThe bounty notice reads:

On behalf of the Queen of Renewed Hamât, Mizâdi Shâra, you are asked to seek out and defeat the infamous Orc Kaursu. Kaursu has been seen inside Kûr Anzar and is known to be allies with the vile Barkhûshim stationed there. Kaursu has killed more than fifty Hamâti warriors, using their skulls and bones as vile trophies upon his very armour.

The proof of his death shall be his chest-piece and pauldrons, that we may lay our fallen soldiers to rest properly. Bring the vile armour to Numûru, Hand of the Queen in Urmâkh for a proper reward.'You defeated Kaursu? Some of our finest warriors were broken by his blade. You aren't one to be trifled with, it seems. Thank you. These warriors deserve better than to be worn by a monster. We can give their remains a proper resting place now.'A bounty notice asks you to defeat Kigrush, the leader of a brigand group attacking refugees. He is reported to be found in Zikrum-dûl to the east.A bounty notice in Ub Nishir has asked for someone to defeat ruthless leader of a group of brigands in Zikrum-dûl to the east known as Kigrush.Defeat KigrushReturn to Neshurga in Ub Nishir north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have completed the bounty and defeated Kigrush.Return to Neshurga and inform him of Kigrush's defeatThe bounty notice reads:

'A group of brigands has been betraying our agreement here in Urash Dâr and they must be stopped. They are working out of Zikrum-dûl and are led by the a ruthless man named Kigrush.

'Put an end to him and speak to Neshurga in Ub Nishir when you do.''I am glad to hear of the end of Kigrush. He broke our agreement to work together against the Orcs who ravage this land and instead choose to prey on the refugees fleeing from the chaos.

'The road through Zikrum-dûl will now be safer thanks to you. Take this, ${CLASS}.'Morutágya Clan has called for the death of the morroval known as Legwêna.Legwêna is located in the western side of Ilmabiri; the Wells.Defeat the morroval LegwênaYou have defeated the morroval, Legwêna. You should return to Porókho at his camp in Hêbatokh to claim your reward.Talk to PorókhoThe bounty notice reads:

Wanted: The slaying of the morroval known as Legwêna. Do not attempt unless you are an experienced warrior. She has killed some and injured many. Morutágya wants her head! See Porókho for reward.

Scrawled underneath this in another handwriting is an additional message that reads:

Please do not actually bring us a head. That is gruesome.
-Eshéra'Oh-ho!  You have slain Legwêna? This is good news! You did not bring her head though? That is ok. I will reward you anyway.'Usakâr's bounty asks you to find the marsh-strider Luhum-gêna and teach her a lesson in the consequences of thievery, as she stole Usakâr's favourite hat.Usakâr's bounty asks you to teach Luhum-gêna in Zahûmakh a lesson for stealing and eating his hat, then go to Dag Usakâra, located south of Urmâkh, to claim your reward.Teach Luhum-gêna in Zahûmakh a lessonFind Usakâr near his home of Dag Usakâra, located midway between Urmâkh and Vartúlin, and tell him about Luhum-gêna's defeat.Find Usakâr near his home and report Luhum-gêna's defeatThe bounty notice reads:

On behalf of Usakâr, who makes his home amongst these woods, you are entreated to use your sternest words and teach Luhum-gêna, protector of the marshes of Zahûmakh, a quite stringent lesson. Luhum-gêna stole my favourite hat. It was good in both the hottest days and the coldest nights. Close-knit, quite fine stitching. Just snatched it off my head, she did.

It was a really nice hat. I was quite fond of it. The manners on these marsh-lurkers leave much to be desired. Teach this one a thing or two about the consequences of thievery. Find me after it's done. I'll find you a suitable enough reward.'You killed Luhum-gêna? The hat? Oh yes, I had quite forgotten about that sign. Bit harsh, don't you think? I only meant to give her some harsh words when I saw her next. Lost in translation I suppose. No sign of the hat, was there? No? Ahh, what a pity.

'Still, you managed to teach her the consequences of thievery, if a bit more permanently than I intended. For that I have a reward for you. What is it that the blasted Men use for coin? Ah, here's some. Thank you, I suppose.'You accepted a bounty for defeating the proto-beast dwelling in the north-western stones of Bel Inzûl.Gather a fellowship and make your way to the north-western stones of Bel Inzûl. Defeat the Bel Inzûl proto-beast.Defeat the Bel Inzûl proto-beastYou defeated the menace in the north-western stones. Return to the healer at the outpost on Bel Inzûl to claim your reward.Speak with the healer at the outpost on Bel InzûlBounty: Bel Inzûl Proto-beast

A proto-beast, lord of the jungle, stalks the stones in the north-western areas of Bel Inzûl.

Slaughter the menace and return to Bel Inzûl's healer for reward.

Do not go alone.'With the menace of the stones gone, it will be easier to harvest the cast of crabs there.

'We thank you, friend. Killing the creature makes our efforts on the island much safer.'You accepted a bounty for defeating the proto-crab that nest in a wreck in the northern section of the island.Gather a fellowship and make your way to the western side of Bel Inzûl. Defeat the Bel Inzûl proto-crab.Defeat the Bel Inzûl proto-crabYou defeated the menace on the northern shore. Return to the healer at the outpost on Bel Inzûl to claim your reward.Speak with the healer at the outpost on Bel InzûlBounty: Bel Inzûl Proto-crab

