'Your prerogative. Come back tomorrow to see if you were right.''Let us see which, if any, foremen had a worker accident yesterday.''All right, I will mark this down. Come back tomorrow to see if you won.'Defeat many dead in Imhûlar.Defeat many Dead in Imhûlar.Defeat many Dead in ImhûlarDefeat a great many Dead in Imhûlar.Defeat many Dead in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many Dead in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many Dead in ImhûlarDefeat many Dead in Kamrabezûr.Defeat many Dead in Kamrabezûr.Defeat many Dead in KamrabezûrDefeat a great many Dead in Kamrabezûr.Defeat many Dead in Kamrabezûr.Defeat a great many Dead in Kamrabezûr.Defeat a great many Dead in KamrabezûrDefeat many Dead in Khabârkhad.Defeat many Dead in Khabârkhad.Defeat many Dead in KhabârkhadDefeat a great many Dead in Khabârkhad.Defeat many Dead in Khabârkhad.Defeat a great many Dead in KhabârkhadDefeat a great many Dead in KhabârkhadDefeat many dead in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many dead in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many dead in Khûd ZaginDefeat a great many dead in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many dead in Khûd Zagin.Defeat a great many dead in Khûd Zagin.Defeat a great many dead in Khûd ZaginYou have left no task unfinished, no stone unturned, and no foe undefeated in each wing of 'The Temple of Utug-bûr'.Utug-bûr is home to long-hidden vaults delved deep into the stone, hidden by sorcery since the end of the First Age. The Thardúth, one of Morgoth's powerful agents, bred the great Elder Orcs known as the Utûgi. Its denizens have remained in a sorcerous slumber for millennia, but have now awakened, and their lair opened anew with the passing of the threat of Sauron.Complete 'Explorer of the 'Temple of Utug-bûr' - Tier 1'Complete 'Explorer of the 'Temple of Utug-bûr' - Tier 2'Complete 'Explorer of the 'Temple of Utug-bûr' - Tier 3'Complete 'Bane of the Blood-spiller'You have proven yourself by scouring the Isle of Storms, braving the Streets of Râhal Bakh, enchanting the crowd in the arena of Dahâl Huliz, and surviving the Depths of the Mâkhda Khorbo. None can question your tenacity and determination, and by completing all these deeds, you have earned great favour throughout Umbar Baharbêl.Complete the deeds of the Umbar Instances.Complete 'Deeds of The Streets of Râhal Bakh'Complete 'Survivor of The Isles of Storm'Complete 'Vanquisher of Dahâl Huliz, The Arena'Complete 'Deeds of the Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo'The Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat but remains a place of great interest for those seeking artifacts of evil. When Azagath Sea-shadow fled from the Citadel of Winds in the company of his comrades Belondor and Nakási Wave-reaper, his purpose was not escape alone. What treasure of the Dark Lord's might he have wrested from those buried ruins? Its identity remains unknown, but your pursuit of Azagath played a role in fracturing the bonds between some of these Kindred.The Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat but remains a place of great interest for those seeking artifacts of evil. When Azagath Sea-shadow fled from the Citadel of Winds in the company of his comrades Belondor and Nakási Wave-reaper, his purpose was not escape alone. What treasure of the Dark Lord's might he have wrested from those buried ruins? Its identity remains unknown, but your pursuit of Azagath played a role in fracturing the bonds between some of these Kindred.Complete The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 1Complete The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 2Complete The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 3The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- The Evil WithinThe Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- The Evil BelowIn the aftermath of the Sea-stone Mutiny, Umbar Baharbêl has been freed from the Heirs of Castamir and their rulers in the Empire of Ordâkh. Under the governance of the Kindred of the Coins, a council of seven chosen by the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl, the City of the Corsairs struggles to be reborn as a Free City—with tidings of hope and treachery found in equal measure as its people step out from the darkness that was cast upon them long ago by the Dark Lord, Sauron.In the aftermath of the Sea-stone Mutiny, Umbar Baharbêl has been freed from the Heirs of Castamir and their rulers in the Empire of Ordâkh. Under the governance of the Kindred of the Coins, a council of seven chosen by the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl, the City of the Corsairs struggles to be reborn as a Free City—with tidings of hope and treachery found in equal measure as its people step out from the darkness that was cast upon them long ago by the Dark Lord, Sauron.Complete Quests of Umbar BaharbêlComplete Explorer of Umbar BaharbêlMushêndu, a local farmer, has asked for your help repairing the local well. He believes there may be something trapped inside it.Examine the well for signs of disrepair.Examine the well for signs of disrepairRemove the small stones clogging the drain-ways of the well.Remove the stones clogging the drain-ways of the well (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Examine the well once more.Examine the well once moreSpeak to Mushêndu in Urmâkh about what to do next.Ask Mushêndu in Urmâkh what you should doAcquire a large, smooth stone of the right size from outside Mushêndu's farm. Mushêndu's farm is located just outside Urmâkh to the north-west.Find a large, smooth stone outside Mushêndu's farmUse the smooth stone to bash the stuck rock inside Urmâkh well back down.Use smooth stone on stuck rock inside Urmâkh wellSpeak with Mushêndu in Urmâkh.Speak with Mushêndu in Urmâkh'The well won't run. It's been dry for a week now. It's no good for my crops or my chickens... to say nothing of the people of Urmâkh.

'We have to walk miles to the nearest river, and the jackals are only getting fiercer. It's a real danger for us. Would you take a look at the well? I think something may be stuck inside, but I don't see as well as I used to, it's all inky darkness in there for me.''Rocks! Of course it's rocks. Well, if rocks are to get us into this mess, it's rocks that will get us out of it, sure enough.

'There are many large, smooth stones just outside Urmâkh, near my farm to the north-west. Gather one that seems the right size and bash that rock back down the well. That should do it.''I knew it! Rock gets you into a mess, a rock will get you out of it. That's what my dad always said, anyway.'You have been tasked with defeating dangerous creatures and helping those in need throughout the Umbar-môkh.Defending the Umbar-môkh quests are available from Bôgalekh and Zûfan in Jadambor, from bounty boards in Ilmabiri and Dil-irmíz, and from defeating spiders, bog-lurkers, and shades in Dil-irmíz to collect supplies required by Kavíra, the healer.Complete Defending the Umbar-môkh quests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed many Defending the Umbar-môkh quests aiding in the defence of the Umbar-môkh.Completed'We must reclaim the Umbar-môkh for all of Umbar!

'We need your aid in helping defend our position here and in defeating dangerous enemies throughout the Umbar-môkh. We can reward your valiant accomplishments with treasure to match. Will you help us?'Your efforts have truly assisted those who work to reclaim the Umbar-môkh from the forces that would harm it. You will certainly be rewarded for your accomplishments.Tibira told you of bandits robbing travellers on the road and asked for your help.Tibira has asked you to deal with the bandits that have placed a barricade along the road west of Western Khanâg.Locate the bandits hindering travellersTibira has asked you to deal with the bandits that have placed a barricade along the road west of Western Khanâg.Defeat Khûdi bandits (${NUMBER}/4)Tibira has asked you to deal with the bandits that have placed a barricade along the road west of Western Khanâg. One of the bandits is surrendering. You should talk to him.Talk to the Khûdi banditTibira has asked you to deal with the bandits that have placed a barricade along the road west of Western Khanâg. One of the bandits surrendered and has agreed to meet you outside of Western Khanâg, near the southern gate.Meet Andur near the gate to Western KhanâgTibira has asked you to deal with the bandits that have placed a barricade along the road west of Western Khanâg. One of the bandits surrendered and has agreed to meet you outside of Western Khanâg, near the southern gate. You should talk to him.Talk to AndurTibira has asked you to deal with the bandits that have placed a barricade along the road west of Western Khanâg. One of the bandits surrendered and has entered Western Khanâg, promising to do only honest work. You should return to Tibira and talk to her.Talk to Tibira'Tell me, stranger, are you a warrior? I only ask because I and many other traders here need help. Bandits prey upon trade caravans like packs of hungry jackals. It is so bad that many people will not even attempt to trade with us anymore because it is not worth the risk.

'The bandits have become so bold as to set up a camp with barricades along the road where they charge travellers a 'tax'. They beat and rob anyone who does not pay them willingly, and the Ordâkhai do nothing. If you wish to be of help to the Khûdi, we can offer you a small reward to rid us of them. They are along the road to west, at the crest of a hill.''Please! Do not strike me down! I do not wish to fight you!'

You lower your weapon and allow the man to speak.

'I only joined them recently and have committed no crimes! I was in the army but the rations are shrinking and our pay comes late, if it comes at all, these past few months. I am no fool and can see that the empire wanes. I abandoned my post, thinking I would return home. These men came across me in the desert and I acted friendly with them so they would not kill me. They had food and water, and I was desperate.

'Please... spare me. Spare me and I will serve you! Ah, I see on your face that this is distasteful to you. What would you have me do? Tell me and I will do it! I am a good man, I swear.'

You tell him to meet you outside of Western Khanâg, and the man nods to you.

'Thank you. My name is Andur and I will meet you at the village gate.''I thank you for your mercy. I hope to find honest work here. You have done so much for me already, but I must ask - please do not tell anyone here of my past. If the people here knew I was with the bandits, they would either kill me or turn me out. In this land, I would not live long on my own.'

You agree and tell the man to stay out of trouble.

'Yes, I will. Of course! Thank you!''Ah, there you are! Did you take care of those bandits?'

You tell her there are no longer bandits at the camp along the road.

'It is a shame that we get more help from strangers than from the Ordâkhai têshu. You have the gratitude of not just myself, but all of the merchants here. Here is something for your trouble.'Shalâra has told you that jackals killed her baby. Following a short discussion, you have offered to cull the jackal population to a more reasonable number.You should defeat jackals in Khûd Zagin in an effort to prevent further tragedies, such as the one Shalâra has suffered.Defeat Khûdi jackals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated jackals in Khûd Zagin in an effort to prevent further tragedies, such as the one Shalâra has suffered. You should return to Shalâra in Western Khanâg.Talk to Shalâra in Western Khanâg'My baby!'

The distraught woman continues crying.

'Jackals killed my baby!'

She looks up at you.

'You. You will help me, yes? Jackals roam these lands unchecked, free to go wherever they wish and to eat whoever they want.'

You ask her how you can help. Her wet, bloodshot eyes lock onto yours.

'I want you to wipe them out. All of them.'

After you have recovered from your choking fit, you tell her you will not do that, but could cull some of the animals if they are too aggressive and numerous.

'I will take what I can get. You have offered me more than anyone else has. Thank you.''You have slain some of them? Thank you for avenging my baby. I know that it is what my precious Boots would have wanted. I am grateful.'The merchant Muntâkh has asked you to undo the desecration of tombs by grave robbers in Sektakhâb, so that the dead may find some peace.The merchant Muntâkh has asked you to undo the desecration of tombs by grave robbers in Sektakhâb.Restore badly desecrated tombs in Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Restore desecrated tombs in Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to the merchant Muntâkh in Mekab-kuphâr, the Temámir outpost in the southern Khabârkhad.Return to the merchant Muntâkh in Mekab-kuphâr'Can you spare a moment? It's awful - absolutely awful - what those people have done.'

You ask him what people and to what he's referring.

'The grave robbers. They've been in Sektakhâb. No wonder the dead are agitated. I'd be too if they smashed my home and disturbed my slumber. They have been desecrating the tombs there, they are all in disarray. All for a few pieces of coin or gold.

'The dead are too much for me for deal with, or I'd restore them myself. But you look like you can handle yourself. Would you go there and restore the tombs? Bring the dead some dignity and peace?''I am grateful. My heart goes out to those poor souls. The dead deserve dignity, and peace. Because of you, they shall have it once again.'The Elf-lord Glorfindel fights valiantly during the Dagor Carlanthir.Glorfindel asked you to hold the Elf-stone aloft near Elladan and Elrohir, who fight their enemies in the middle of the river to the north-west during the Dagor Carlanthir.Glorfindel asked you to hold the Elf-stone aloft near Legolas, who fights on the western side of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.Glorfindel asked you to hold the Elf-stone aloft near Sigileth, who fights during the Dagor Carlanthir by the northern waterfall that hides Utug-bûr.Sigileth fights beside Silirtas during the Dagor Carlanthir by the waterfall that hides Utug-bûr.Talk to Sigileth during the Dagor CarlanthirGlorfindel fights to the south of Sigileth and Silirtas during the Dagor Carlanthir.'I saw how the warriors of Ambarûl responded when you invoked the name of their great hero, ${PLAYER}. Let us similarly inspire the Elves!

'Take this Elf-stone and hold it aloft in the company of the Eldar! May it shine as a beacon against the darkness that threatens to spill from Utug-bûr!''Hold aloft the Elf-stone I gave you in the company of the Eldar! May it shine as a beacon against the darkness that threatens to spill from Utug-bûr!''The Orcs fear and hate the light of the Elf-stone you carry, even as it renews my own determination to triumph!

'I returned as quickly as I could with some of the Avabár-kintai, and they fight bravely in defence of their groves and their people. But you should know something, ${PLAYER}.

'Balakhâd was not yet fully-recovered from his injuries, but he followed my small band of Kintai reinforcements here from Shonith. I saw him at times from a great distance, pursuing us as we came north. I know not where he is now, but he may watch the battle from afar, waiting to see which side prevails.''Balakhâd was not yet fully-recovered from his injuries, but he followed my small band of Kintai reinforcements here from Shonith. I saw him at times from a great distance, pursuing us as we came north. I know not where he is now, but he may watch the battle from afar, waiting to see which side prevails.''Thank you for bringing the light of the Elf-stone to bear during the battle!

'We will fight on! We have no choice but to prevail!'Khôltekh fights for Umbar during the Dagor Carlanthir.Goblin-spies creep along the edges of the fighting during the Dagor Carlanthir.Goblin-spies creep along the edges of the fighting during the Dagor Carlanthir.Defeat goblin-spies during the Dagor Carlanthir (4/5)You caught sight of Balakhâd fighting a goblin-spy to the south during the Dagor Carlanthir.Find Balakhâd south of Mithrandir's position during the Dagor CarlanthirYou have found Balakhâd on the edge of the fighting during the Dagor Carlanthir.Talk to Balakhâd to the south of Mithrandir's position during the Dagor CarlanthirOverwhelmed by the sight of such evil, Balakhâd flees from the battle.Wait for Balakhâd to escapeKhôltekh is on the eastern bank of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.Talk to Khôltekh during the Dagor Carlanthir'You have heard that knowledge is power? It is true: battles are won by the side that obtains the most intelligence.

'Hunt the goblin-spies that scamper throughout the battlefield, ${PLAYER}. They should pose little danger to you, but while they live they can deliver messages to their masters. We must stop the delivery of these messages if we wish to attain the upper hand in this battle.''Hunt the goblin-spies that scamper throughout the battlefield, ${PLAYER}. They should pose little danger to you, but while they live they can deliver messages to their masters. We must stop the delivery of these messages if we wish to attain the upper hand in this battle.''Hunt the goblin-spies that scamper throughout the battlefield, ${PLAYER}. They should pose little danger to you, but while they live they can deliver messages to their masters. We must stop the delivery of these messages if we wish to attain the upper hand in this battle.''Oh!''When Sigileth the Elf came to the oasis to speak with the Kintai, I listened to the message she brought. She spoke of the great evil waking in these canyons, but I did not expect...'

Balakhâd's eyes are wide as he stares about himself at the boiling mass of Orcs.

'I wanted to see it for myself... but no longer! No longer!''You have slain some of the goblin-spies? Good. Attacking an enemy's sources of knowledge may at times be more effective than wounding them directly.

'Knowledge is power, ${PLAYER}. Never forget that!'Legolas and Gimli seek to patch holes in the defensive line during the Dagor Carlanthir.Legolas asked you to stand your ground before the waterfall to the north-west.Hurry to defend the waterfall north-west of LegolasYou must defend the north-west waterfall and not leave it until enough time has passed!Defend the north-west waterfall until time is up<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the north-west waterfall or you will fail the quest!</rgb>Gimli fights to the south-east during the Dagor Carlanthir.Talk to Gimli during the Dagor CarlanthirGimli asked you to stand your ground at the waterfall to his south-east.Hurry to defend the waterfall to Gimli's south-eastYou must defend the waterfall to the south-east of Gimli, and not leave it until enough time has passed!Defend the south-eastern waterfall until time is up<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the south-eastern waterfall or you will fail the quest!</rgb>Legolas fights during the Dagor Carlanthir.Talk to Legolas during the Dagor Carlanthir'There are not enough of us to maintain a complete defensive line, ${PLAYER}! See you not the holes in our defence?

'Go to the waterfall ahead of me to the north-west and try to fill the gap there! You must battle the enemies that seek to take advantage of our limited numbers. Do not leave that spot until you have stayed there long enough to make a difference! Afterward you should find Gimli and see if he knows of a similar gap in our defensive line!''Go to the waterfall ahead of me to the north-west and try to fill the gap there! You must battle the enemies that seek to take advantage of our limited numbers. Do not leave that spot until you have stayed there long enough to make a difference! Afterward you should find Gimli and see if he knows of a similar gap in our defensive line!''I cannot be everywhere at once, ${PLAYER}! You will have to fill the gaps in our defences! Legolas had the same idea? Then you can assure him it was a good one, for I have a sharp mind for such things!

'But go to the waterfall to my south-east and defend it until you have made a difference, as you did at the other!''Go to the waterfall to my south-east and defend it until you have made a difference!''Let us hope your defensive work at those locations showed the Orcs the folly of seeking to slip past our line! The battle shows no sign of nearing its end, but I have not yet begun to tire.

'I am certain Gimli would say the same!'Rahâzi returned from Ambarûl with a force of Dumûri warriors, and now the Dagor Carlanthir rages all about them.Girhâzi stands her ground north of her daughter during the Dagor Carlanthir.Talk to Girhâzi during the Dagor CarlanthirDumûri warriors fight bravely during the Dagor Carlanthir.Rahâzi fights to the south during the Dagor Carlanthir.Talk to Rahâzi to the south during the Dagor Carlanthir'The Dumûri of Ambarûl will neither back down nor retreat! We will not relinquish a single step to these foes!

'${PLAYER}! Find my mother somewhere to the north and learn from her one of the great tales of Old Shagâna! To hear those names recounted will inspire the Dumûri to greater heights of combat prowess when they need it most!''Find my mother Girhâzi to the north and learn from her one of the great tales of Old Shagâna! To hear those names recounted will inspire the Dumûri to greater heights of combat prowess when they need it most!''We will not know defeat! We must triumph or the lands that lie behind us will suffer terrible torments at the hands of these vile creatures!

'Rahâzi is right in this, ${PLAYER}: our people should be reminded of the great heroes that came before us! Sing a song of the great hero Shurug-nîn to the fighting Dumûri and they will fight more fiercely than ever before!

'The melody is not as important as the words themselves! Sing of Shurug-nîn as she fought the great dragon Akhízi, the Winged Terror! Sing of Shurug-nîn's powerful allies among Elves, both the ancient Kintai of the Emerald Wood and the more distant Elves who gifted her the mighty sword Orotheg! Sing of how she slew Orcs by the thousands! These names from our great histories will inspire the Dumûri who hear them!''Our people should be reminded of the great heroes that came before us! Sing a song of the great hero Shurug-nîn to the fighting Dumûri and they will fight more fiercely than ever before!

'The melody is not as important as the words themselves! Sing of Shurug-nîn as she fought the great dragon Akhízi, the Winged Terror! Sing of Shurug-nîn's powerful allies among Elves, both the ancient Kintai of the Emerald Wood and the more distant Elves who gifted her the mighty sword Orotheg! Sing of how she slew Orcs by the thousands! These names from our great histories will inspire the Dumûri who hear them!''These songs of our great hero Shurug-nîn have stirred my heart, and those of the other Dumûri!

'The melody was unfamiliar, ${PLAYER}, but we knew the words! They have done as my mother wished, and our people fight more fiercely than before!

'What named the Wizard this battle? Dagor Carlanthir? To my people it will be the Sabûdamar, the red-rush battle, and perhaps it will one day number among the great songs of the Ambarûli!'Rothog fights ferociously during the Dagor Carlanthir.Rothog asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>point</rgb> at specific Orc spy-masters on the high ground to tell Húrshauk who to attack.<rgb=#00FF00>Point</rgb> at Krazlak, the Orc-spymaster on the high ground above the western bank of the riverHúrshauk charges toward Krazlak!Wait for Húrshauk to attack the target you indicatedRothog asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>point</rgb> at specific Orcs on the high ground to tell Húrshauk who to attack.<rgb=#00FF00>Point</rgb> at Gadrúth, the Orc-spymaster on the high ground above the eastern bank of the riverHúrshauk charges toward Gadrúth!Wait for Húrshauk to attack the target you indicatedRothog fights in the centre of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.Talk to Rothog during the Dagor Carlanthir'Have you yet broken a sweat? I am instructing these Orcs in the folly of facing the Kindred of the Coins and their allies!

'Húrshauk hungers for direction, ${PLAYER}! There are spy-masters working for the Orcs, and they call out battle plans from the high ground to the south, beyond where stands the Wizard. Find these Orc spy-masters and <rgb=#00FF00>point</rgb> them out to Húrshauk so he can disrupt their plans!''Húrshauk hungers for direction, ${PLAYER}! There are spy-masters working for the Orcs, and they call out battle plans from the high ground to the south, beyond where stands the Wizard. Find these Orc spy-masters and <rgb=#00FF00>point</rgb> them out to Húrshauk so he can disrupt their plans!''Together you and Húrshauk have disrupted our opponent's battle plan! Well done, ${PLAYER}!

'Victory cannot be far away now!'Sirgon may not possess the physical strength of his youth, but still he fights during the Dagor Carlanthir.Orcs in service to the Utûgi charge across the battlefield during the Dagor Carlanthir.Defeat Urâshi warriors during the Dagor Carlanthir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Urâshi skirmishers during the Dagor Carlanthir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Sirgon fights along the north-western bank of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.Talk to Sirgon during the Dagor Carlanthir'I am not as young as once I was, but I can still fight!

'I will not have Belondor return from his city with reinforcements to see me cowering behind the line of battle! Let us slay as many Orcs as we can, ${PLAYER}, and protect the lives of our friends and the homes we left behind!''Let us slay as many Orcs as we can, ${PLAYER}, and protect the lives of our friends and the homes we left behind!''There is no end to these creatures! Good!

'That means there is still glory to be won, and we will win it!

'I have not engaged in combat like this for years, ${PLAYER}! I will not let down my friends! For Lebennin and for Gondor!'After listening to the details of this "Dead Pool" you decided to speak with Othax and give him your honest opinion of this practice.Othax does not seem to think that there is anything wrong with taking advantage of those who suffer grievous injuries while working at Rkhatâb. You are going to give him your honest opinion of this practice.Show your anger to Othax (<rgb=#FF0000>/angry</rgb>)Tell Othax of the immorality of this practice (<rgb=#FF0000>/talk</rgb>)Admonish Othax for this unwholesome practice (<rgb=#FF0000>/no</rgb>)You made your displeasure with this practice known to Othax and he seems to still want to say something to you. Speak with Marjadi at the commons in Rakhatâb.Speak with OthaxOthax was unapologetic and defensive about his decision to continue running the game. He suggested that you speak with another worker in the rest area to get her opinion. Make your way to her and let her know of your disapproval of this practice.Speak with Marjadi at the commons in Rakhatâb'Here to make your choice of foremen?'

He looks at you expectantly.

'What is it?''Taking a chance like this is not for everyone. I will not justify myself to you. The way we find humour is ours. Be gone and do not speak with me again. Maybe you should visit Marjadi here in the rest area. She might appreciate your ramblings.''I have nothing more to say to you. You do not share in the humour that allows us to keep smiling in the wake of the difficulties we face. Be gone.''Othax has long found a way to profit from the misfortune of others. As one of the unfortunate workers who was injured I thank you for standing up to that fool. I will tell others of your morality and spread tale of your nobility. Please return to me tomorrow.'The Ordâkhai maintain an encampment on the south side of the Wrackwade, from which they launch attacks at the Dumûri of Sûru.Ningêna has asked you to go to Khetsok, the Ordâkhai camp on the south side of the Wrackwade in Ambarûl, and defeat some of the soldiers there.Defeat Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated Ordâkhai soldiers at Khetsok, the Ordâkhai camp on the south side of the Wrackwade. You should return to Ningêna at Sûru.Talk to Ningêna'If Girhâzi sent you to help us, who am I to argue? Welcome to Sûru. Here we camp not only to maintain control of the crossing, but we are also building a permanent outpost. From here we can keep watch upon both the crossing and the roads. The road going south-east is blocked by a landslide currently, but that will not always be so. People are working to clear it.

'The Ordâkhai test our defences almost daily. They have their bivouac across the river, and though we hold the bridge itself, they watch upon the road from the other side, so we still cannot truly use it. We will need to clear them out in time, but for now, we are content to hold this ground with minimal losses and make progress on our fortress. Or we were, anyway, before hearing your news that they were frustrated enough to try destroying the floating bridge.

'It would seem that the time of action is upon us. My best Dumûri are resting after a skirmish that lasted long into the night. You appear to be a talented warrior. If you think yourself capable it would be good of you to visit the Ordâkhai camp across the bridge and remind them that we are not weak.''It would be good of you to visit the Ordâkhai camp and remind them that we are not weak. Defeat some of the Ordâkhai soldiers at Khetsok and return to me.''You defeated their soldiers and look none the worse for wear. Well done ${PLAYER}!'Bâzadur needs your help discovering the cause of the supplies going missing from their camp in Ashâgir, and wants you to investigate.Bâzadur has asked for your help investigating the stolen supplies in Ashâgir. He has suggested inspecting the supplies themselves first to see if you can find out anything.Investigate the supplies in Ashâgir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Bâzadur and inform him of what you found while searching the supplies.Return to BâzadurBâzadur has asked you to look for additional clues around the hideout in Ashâgir.Look for clues near the supply cartLook for clues at the nearby sheltersLook for clues at the nearby rubbleReturn to Bâzadur with the information you have gathered from your investigation in Ashâgir.Return to Bâzadur in AshâgirBâzadur suggests you investigate a hideout they know of down near Ningûdu, as there may be more clues to the whereabouts of the supplies there.Search for a hideout near NingûduInvestigate the corpse found at the hideout in Ningûdu, near Ashâgir, for the missing supplies.Investigate the corpseRecover the stolen supplies at the hideout in Ningûdu, near Ashâgir.Recover stolen supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return the recovered supplies to Bâzadur in the hideout in the Ashâgir camp.'Ah, hello there. I see that you have found your way up to Ashâgir, ${CLASS}. I am Bâzadur, the leader of this small group.

'This is fortunate timing for your arrival. If you are willing, there is a problem here that needs an outsider's help.

'We have but few resources left here so we must make everything last. Unfortunately, some of our supplies have gone missing, and no one will say a word.

'Would you investigate this matter for me in secret until we know more? I suggest you start by checking the supplies themselves for any clues as to who the thief might be. You can find the supplies nearby in the camp.''Did you find out anything while investigating the supplies?'

You tell Bâzadur what you found.

'I see. Not much to learn from that, as expected. They could not have vanished!

'Might I trouble you to check around for any other clues you might find in the camp? There must be something.''You have returned. Did you find any new information about the missing supplies?'

You tell Bâzadur about your discoveries around the camp.

'Is that so? It seems our thief may have made away with our supplies, and it could have been anyone here. The burned notes lead me to believe they intend to sell our supplies for their own gain.

'With the lift broken it would not be an easy task to take the supplies far from here. I know of a hideaway, down near Ningûdu at the bottom of these cliffs, near the water to the north-east. The area is overrun with foul kergrim, though this spot I speak of would be a perfect place to hide.

'I ask that you go and investigate the hideout and see if you can learn anything more. If we cannot recover these supplies we may need to abandon this place.''Ah! You return in one piece. Have you found anything?'

You give Bâzadur the supplies and describe the body of the thief you found. 

Bâzadur's expression turns to a frown.

'The man you describe, it matches the description of Surdukas. It must have been him then who took our supplies. He wished to flee this place and this must have been his attempt to do so. He might have succeeded if the kergrim had not gotten to him first.

'I will tell the others. Even though he stole from us, I am sorry for his fate. He was a friend. I thank you for all you have done for us this day.'Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Find Kûr AnzarFind VartúlinFind UrmâkhFind Tûl Zakana, the Well of ForgettingFind the Tombs of Esh-kimâkhiFind the Watcher of UrmâkhFind Dag UsakâraFind KûgrunFind Nâmbadir, the Span of PrincesExplore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Khûd Zagin in the Ikorbân Valley.Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Khûd Zagin in the Ikorbân Valley.Find JirushFind ShonithFind the Tombs of NirgambârFind the Span of DanagírFind Menundâri-enFind GhalbûruFind Western KhanâgFind Ruined KhanâgExplore friendly settlements, structures, canyons, and other important points of interest in Urash Dâr in the Ikorbân Valley.Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Urash Dâr in the Ikorbân Valley.Find Ub NishirFind NêruzigFind Ilzag KhûlFind ShengarâshFind the Channel of BâdizalFind the Falls of IlûrituFind AshâgirFind Sûr AkilFind MalgâmaFind Utug-bûrDefeat many diseased animals in Imhûlar.Defeat many diseased animals in Imhûlar.Defeat many diseased animals in ImhûlarDefeat a great many diseased animals in Imhûlar.Defeat many diseased animals in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many diseased animals in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many diseased animals in ImhûlarHênok has asked you to defeat Khadimâl and stop the ritual in Ghâs Hejai.After informing Hênok of what you discovered you have been asked to return to Ghâs Hejai in Dil-irmíz.Discover the ritual location in Ghâs HejaiKhadimâl must be stopped before they complete their ritual within Ghâs Hejai in Dil-irmíz.Defeat Khadimâl and stop the Hakâri ritualReturn to Bôgalekh in Jadambor in Dil-irmíz and inform them of your triumph over the Hakâri.Return to Bôgalekh in Jadambor'Your findings are troubling indeed, ${CLASS}. It appears the cultists are planning something nefarious.

'It is clear that the Hakâri are preparing to enact a ritual and these notes you gathered have mention of a Khadimâl, who is to perform it.

'Go now and infiltrate the gathering and defeat this Khadimâl. We must disrupt this ritual before it can reach its completion, for the consequences of its completion could be dire.

'I will make haste to Jadambor and inform Bôgalekh of this threat. Return to her once you have stopped the ritual.''Ah, ${CLASS}, it gladdens my heart to see you return unharmed. Hênok told me of what you discovered in Ghâs Hejai.

'I am relieved to hear that you have been able to stop this Khadimâl, and prevent their ritual from taking place.

'Your courage and resolve have spared us from the clutches of this threat for now. Accept this as a token of our gratitude for all you have done to help us this day.'To the south, the Nêpharai have made a small encampment known as Harkhaphâr. There are several dwellings that have been hastily constructed. Find them and destroy them.Search Harkhaphâr and destroy the largest dwellings in an attempt to push them elsewhere in the catacombs.Destroy dwellings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Bâkhadir located just north of Harkhaphâr and inform him of your progress.Talk to Bâkhadir outside of the camp'The Nêpharai have begun to build out their settlement in Harkhaphâr. Search the camp and destroy the largest dwellings in an attempt to push them elsewhere in the catacombs.''With the Nêpharai buildings destroyed, perhaps this should encourage them to avoid us and move elsewhere.'Defeat Ordâkhai within Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Ordâkhai within Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Ordâkhai within Dun Shûma, The King's FortressThe hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Menûn Shûma III. The ancient ruin is said to hold many historical treasures of the kingdoms of Shagâna. Though Bârshud has retreated, his Umûni still stand opposed to Mizâdi's quest to claim the Crown of Hamât.Defeat Weaponmaster Mâkhragab and Ushdâla, Lady of the Pride in Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Weaponmaster MâkhragabDefeat Ushdâla, Lady of the PrideDefeat Zidunâm, the Spirit-caller in Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Zidunâm, the Spirit-callerThe hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Menûn Shûma III. The ancient ruin is said to hold many historical treasures of the kingdoms of Shagâna. Though Bârshud has retreated, his Umûni still stand opposed to Mizâdi's quest to claim the Crown of Hamât.Defeat Weaponmaster Mâkhragab and Ushdâla, Lady of the Pride in Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Weaponmaster MâkhragabDefeat Ushdâla, Lady of the PrideDefeat Zidunâm, the Spirit-caller in Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Zidunâm, the Spirit-callerThe hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Menûn Shûma III. The ancient ruin is said to hold many historical treasures of the kingdoms of Shagâna. Though Bârshud has retreated, his Umûni still stand opposed to Mizâdi’s quest to claim the Crown of Hamât.Complete 'Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress -- Tier 1'The hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Menûn Shûma III. The ancient ruin is said to hold many historical treasures of the kingdoms of Shagâna. Though Bârshud has retreated, his Umûni still stand opposed to Mizâdi's quest to claim the Crown of Hamât.Defeat Weaponmaster Mâkhragab and Ushdâla, Lady of the Pride in Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Weaponmaster MâkhragabDefeat Ushdâla, Lady of the PrideDefeat Zidunâm, the Spirit-caller in Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Zidunâm, the Spirit-callerThe hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Menûn Shûma III. The ancient ruin is said to hold many historical treasures of the kingdoms of Shagâna. Though Bârshud has retreated, his Umûni still stand opposed to Mizâdi’s quest to claim the Crown of Hamât.Complete 'Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress -- Tier 2'The hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Menûn Shûma III. The ancient ruin is said to hold many historical treasures of the kingdoms of Shagâna. Though Bârshud has retreated, his Umûni still stand opposed to Mizâdi's quest to claim the Crown of Hamât.Defeat Weaponmaster Mâkhragab and Ushdâla, Lady of the Pride in Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Weaponmaster MâkhragabDefeat Ushdâla, Lady of the PrideDefeat Zidunâm, the Spirit-caller in Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress.Defeat Zidunâm, the Spirit-callerThe hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Menûn Shûma III. The ancient ruin is said to hold many historical treasures of the kingdoms of Shagâna. Though Bârshud has retreated, his Umûni still stand opposed to Mizâdi's quest to claim the Crown of Hamât.Complete 'Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress -- Tier 3'The hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Menûn Shûma III. The ancient ruin is said to hold many historical treasures of the kingdoms of Shagâna. Though Bârshud has retreated, his Umûni still stand opposed to Mizâdi's quest to claim the Crown of Hamât.Complete 'Dun Shûma, The King's Fortress -- Tier 3'You must help turn the tide of battle and finish this fight, as there is a much greater fight happening west of Imhûlar.Defeat Ekhamâti forces around you and tend to the wounded Subuzûri in Nisigurûm.Defeat Ekhamâti warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ekhamâti look-outs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ekhamâti champions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tend to wounded Subuzûri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Mizâdi on the battlefield outside Nisigurûm in southern Imhûlar.Speak with Mizâdi on the battlefield outside Nisigurûm'He played me for a fool. Damn my temper. It feels sometimes like a flame that consumes the rest of me whole. We need to end the threat here, and then we need to warn the others as quickly as possible. I thought there more forces in reserve, but clearly he only left a small portion of his army.

'Please, help finish the fighting here, and then I have an even more important task for you.''This is not the real battle. I need to warn the leaders of Khûd Zagin and Ambarûl. They are in terrible danger.'Defeat many Ekhamâti in the Ikorbân Valley.Defeat many Ekhamâti in the Ikorbân Valley.Defeat many Ekhamâti in the Ikorbân ValleyDefeat a great many Ekhamâti in the Ikorbân Valley.Defeat many Ekhamâti in the Ikorbân Valley.Defeat a great many Ekhamâti in the Ikorbân Valley.Defeat a great many Ekhamâti in the Ikorbân ValleyYour continued efforts to support Shâra Mizâdi and her forces in Idagâl and Pahar Hatokáli earn you great esteem with Hamât Renewed.You must earn Esteemed standing with Hamât RenewedThe Quartermaster has asked that you gather your allies and travel to The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr to put an end to the evils there.The evils within The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr must be stopped.

Complete three Umbar or Ikorbân raids on tier 2 or higher.Complete Umbar or Ikorbân raids on tier 2 or higher (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to the Temple of Utug-bûr Quartermaster with proof of your victory.Return to the Temple of Utug-bûr Quartermaster'Greetings, ${CLASS}.

'An evil plagues the lands of Umbar and Ikorbân and we cannot allow it to spread.

'I ask that you gather your allies and travel to The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr and defeat the evils who lurk in their halls. Do this, and I can provide you with a reward to match your efforts.''I have heard of your deeds in The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr.

'Please accept this as a token of my thanks to you and your companions.'Ghâr Mejet is a vile place within the underground. Explore its chambers and report your findings to Yâshri.Ghâr Mejet is a vile place within the underground. Explore its chambers and report on your findings.Explore the south-western chamberExplore the south-eastern chamberExplore the north-eastern chamberExplore the north-western chamberThe main chamber of Ghâr Mejet is the vilest place in the area. Explore its chambers and report on your findings.Explore the main chamberInform Yâshri of your findings.Talk to Yâshri outside of Ghâr Mejet'We do not know much about Ghâr Mejet. While we know the restless dead haunt this place, we have yet to explore the area more closely.

'Could a capable adventurer such as yourself explore its chambers and report on your findings?''This information should be useful for any future forays and as a warning to those who might wander too closely to this place.

'Your work has saved the lives of our peoples, and I cannot thank you enough.'Thoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Ambarûl in the Ikorbân Valley.Explore Ambarûl in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Dangers in AmbarûlComplete Scouting AmbarûlComplete Treasure-seeker of AmbarûlThoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Khûd Zagin in the Ikorbân Valley.Explore Khûd Zagin in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Dangers in Khûd ZaginComplete Discovering Khûd ZaginComplete Treasure-seeker of Khûd ZaginYou have proven yourself by conquering what lies within the primeval darkness of the Temple of Utug-bûr.Complete each wing of 'The Temple of Utug-bûr' at Tier 1.Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Dhórgruth -- Tier 1'Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Thûr Hin -- Tier 1'Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Inner Sanctum -- Tier 1'You have proven yourself by conquering what lies within the primeval darkness of the Temple of Utug-bûr.Complete each wing of 'The Temple of Utug-bûr' at Tier 2.Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Dhórgruth -- Tier 2'Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Thûr Hin -- Tier 2'Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Inner Sanctum -- Tier 2'You have proven yourself by conquering what lies within the primeval darkness of the Temple of Utug-bûr.Complete each wing of 'The Temple of Utug-bûr' at Tier 3.Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Dhórgruth -- Tier 3'Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Thûr Hin -- Tier 3'Complete 'Temple of Utug-bûr: Inner Sanctum -- Tier 3'Thoroughly explore every settlement, canyon, cave, camp, marsh, lair, and point of interest in the Ikorbân Valley.Thoroughly explore every settlement, canyon, cave, camp, marsh, lair, and point of interest in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Explorer of AmbarûlComplete Explorer of Khûd ZaginComplete Explorer of ImhûlarComplete Explorer of Urash DârExplore the Umbar-môkh.Explore the Umbar-môkh.Complete Reclaiming KhabârkhadComplete Reclaiming IlmabiriComplete Reclaiming KamrabezûrComplete Reclaiming TâkhdarComplete Reclaiming Dil-irmízThoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Urash Dâr in the Ikorbân Valley.Explore Urash Dâr in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Dangers in Urash DârComplete Discovering Urash DârComplete Treasure-seeker of Urash DârThoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Explore Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Dangers of ImhûlarComplete Discovering ImhûlarComplete Treasure-seeker of ImhûlarNeshurga has asked you to go investigate Utug-bûr because he needs more information on what they are up against in Urash Dâr.Reach the Utug-bûr scouting location that Neshurga described.Reach the Utug-bûr scouting locationScout Utug-bûr from the location that Neshurga described.Scout out Utug-bûr to gather informationReturn to Neshurga in Ub Nishir with the information you've gathered on Utug-bûr.Return to Neshurga in Ub Nishir'Yes? You must be the ${PLAYER} of which Galâmka spoke. I am Neshurga.

'I am in need of your assistance. We do not know much about our enemy that came from this Utug-bûr, this demon-pit. We have only seen these monsters when they took Maurûsh from us.

'If you would, I ask that you travel to Utug-bûr and learn what you can. Along the river are hills that you may find a good vantage point, but I suggest you keep your distance from the gates of Utug-bûr, that is more danger than it is worth.''Ah, ${CLASS}, what have you learned of the demon-pits?'

You inform Neshurga of what you learned while scouting Utug-bûr.

'So there are even more of these monstrous creatures pouring from Utug-bûr. That is what I feared, and it appears we are losing the battle everywhere. Thank you for bringing this information to me.'Talmûri informed you that farmers in the area have spotted Ekhamâti scouts hiding in the marshes nearby. She asks that you stop them before they can bring information back to the enemy.Talmûri informed you that farmers in the area have spotted Ekhamâti scouts hiding in the marshes nearby. She asked that you stop them before they can bring information back to the enemy.Defeat Ekhamâti scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Talmûri in Burukíri and let her know you have dealt with the scouts in the marshes.Return to Talmûri in Burukíri'Glad to see you. I have heard some troubling news, and so I must ask for your help.

'Other farm-hands have spotted Ekhamâti scouts in the marshes just to the north of here. You must stop them before they can bring any reports back to their leaders. It would endanger us all if they succeed.''I am relieved to see you return!

'I know that more Ekhamâti will show themselves in time, but you have given us peace of mind for now. Thank you friend.'Tafikh has challenged you to a game of Facts and Fictions, believing that you do not know enough about the people of Umbar Baharbêl and the Kindred of the Coins.Tafikh is waiting to ask you her first question.Talk to TafikhQuestion One:
Belondor, Kinsman of the Fleet-fast, is married to an Umbari woman named Khâsha.Tafikh is waiting to ask you her second question.Talk to TafikhQuestion Two:
Azagath Sea-shadow has been known to walk through the markets of Umbar Baharbêl.Tafikh is waiting to ask you her third question.Talk to TafikhQuestion Three:
The Church of the All-Seeing prized the sea-opal Abâshal, and used it to decorate its places of worship.Tafikh is waiting to ask you her fourth question.Talk to TafikhQuestion Four:
The Sea-stone Mutiny, during which the Heirs of Castamir were overthrown, began in the Upper Ward of the city.Tafikh is waiting to ask you her fifth question.Talk to TafikhQuestion Five:
The name of this land comes from the word Umbru-mâra, which means 'Fruitful Land.'Tafikh is amazed that you answered all of her questions correctly.Talk to Tafikh'Ah, you came back! I did not know if you would. Does this mean you are prepared to play my game of Facts and Fictions? It will truly test how much you know about the Kindred of the Coins and the city of Umbar Baharbêl. But be warned: if you fail to answer a question correctly, it will be some time before I allow you to play again. It is only fair.

'Here is how to play. Behind me you will see the ruined structure that was the Shrine of He-Who-Sees-All. The shrine is now mere rubble, as it should be; it stands as a testament now to the evils that the Empire of Ordakh inflicted upon us. To the south-east, on the left side of the ruin, I have erected a red canopy. There is a similar canopy to the south, on the right side of the ruin; that one is made of green cloth.

'I will make a series of five statements. If the statement is true, you will stand under the green canopy. If the statement is false, you will stand under the red canopy. Return to me after each answer to hear the next statement. However, if you get one wrong you will need to begin my game again from the top... after spending a period of time mourning your lack of knowledge. Are you ready? Speak to me to begin.''Then let us begin.

'Belondor, Kinsman of the Fleet-fast, is married to an Umbari woman named Khâsha.''Well?''Very good. A lucky guess. Next question.

'Azagath Sea-shadow has been known to walk through the markets of Umbar Baharbêl.''Well?''Yes. This next one will not be easy.

'The Church of the All-Seeing prized the sea-opal Abâshal, and used it to decorate its places of worship.''Well?''Fine, you got it. How about this one?

'The Sea-stone Mutiny, during which the Heirs of Castamir were overthrown, began in the Upper Ward of the city.''Well?''You think you are smart? Then let us see your mastery of the language! This is the last question.

'The name of this land comes from the word Umbru-mâra, which means 'Fruitful Land.'''Well?''I must admit I did not think you would defeat my game, but you have proven a master of Facts and Fictions! Well done, stranger! May you continue to use your knowledge of our land and our city to better the lives of its people! I must give you the reward I thought to keep for myself, for you have bested me in this contest as few before have done!'Tharashil explains the oasis is the Elves' home and those under care require assistance in leaving the world. They work to keep memories and the trees alive, and they ask for aid.Tharashil asked you to go to the dead oasis to the north-west to collect keepsakes and dormant seeds from the oasis. They safe-keep them for the memory of those who faded.Collect oasis seeds from the dead oasis (${NUMBER}/6)Collect oasis keepsakes from the dead oasis (${NUMBER}/6)You collected the oasis seeds and keepsakes. Return them to Tharashil at Shonith to show your intent to assist the Elves.'Our fate lies here in this oasis. Once, our number covered this region with splendour and wonder. We will not fade without trying to restore what we lost. To the north-west, there is a remnant of one of our oases. The desiccated trees appear dead. They are dormant. Some seeds still live. Where once we walked, our keepsake remains.

'If you would collect some of those sleeping seeds and remnants of our past and return them to me, I shall be grateful.''We will safe-guard the mementos and seeds you recovered. We may fade from the world, but there will be a memory of us in the trees.

'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'Turizi has asked you to slay some of the wild cats worrying his mother.Servals and caracals can be found prowling about the rice fields of Ekagar in Ambarûl. You should defeat some and bring their pelts to Turizi.Defeat wild cats and collect their pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated servals and caracals prowling about the rice fields of Ekagar. You should bring their pelts to Turizi behind the farmhouse.'I have another trouble you could help me with, should you be willing. There are wild cats that live in the untamed lands in the north. At least, that is where they should be living. Of late they have been prowling our fields and frightening my mother as she goes about her work.

'If you are willing to slay some of the vexing animals, let us not be wasteful. Bring me their pelts and I will put them to good use this next winter.''Of late wild cats have been prowling our fields and frightening my mother. If you are amenable, slay some of them and bring me their pelts.''Ah, the pelts! Thank you, my friend. Life can be trying here in Ambarûl and I cannot abide waste. These will help someone greatly when the seasons change.'Paguri in Ub Nashir has asked you to gather feathers from nearby birds so that she can replenish her stock of arrows.Paguri in Ub Nishir has asked you to gather feathers from birds in Urash Dâr so that she can replenish her stock of arrows.Gather pristine feathers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the pristine feathers back to Paguri in Ub Nishir.'Ah, an adventurer. Could I trouble you for some help?

'I am the fletcher here and I am working to build our supply of arrows. We will need all that we can get if we mean to retake Maurûsh.

'If you happen upon any feathers from the creatures here in Urash Dâr, I would be glad to take them off your hands. I do not have the time myself to track them down with the work that must be done.

'Only ones remaining in pristine condition will suffice.''These are flawless! I thank you adventurer.

'I will make some fine arrows with these.'Ningêna would like more meat added to their stockpile at Sûru.Shegdush, located east of Sûru, has a sizable wild boar population. You should go there and hunt fen-wallowers for Ningêna.Collect fen-wallower meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have hunted fen-wallowers and collected their meat. You should bring it to Ningêna in Sûru.'I have learned that being a commander is not just planning for battles. Keeping your warriors well-fed is key to victory. A hungry army is less effective and could lead to desertions. We are not low on supplies, but I want to shore up our meat reserves. Fen-wallowers live in a place east of here that we call Shegdush. If you wouldn't mind doing so, hunting some and bringing back the meat would be helpful.''Fen-wallowers live in a place east of here that we call Shegdush. If you wouldn't mind doing so, hunting some and bringing back the meat would be helpful.''${PLAYER}, you return with meat! I will see that it is cured for storage. Thank you!'Mizâdi has asked you to assist the local Ambarûli in procuring supplies to feed the soldiers gathered in Iridír.Speak with Zilêndu, a farmer in Ambarûl. Zilêndu can be found at Burukíri, an orchard north of Iridír.Speak with Zilêndu at BurukíriHarvest oranges and defeat zizani at Burukíri.Harvest oranges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat zizani (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Harvest grain in the northern field near the orchard in Ambarûl.Harvest grain in the northern field for Zilêndu (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Give the harvested grain and oranges to Zilêndu, the Ambarûli farmer.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír'A hungry army is half-defeated before they take the battlefield. There is plenty of food in the hills of Ambarûl, but with most of the able-bodied taking up arms to defend her, there are few hands left to pick and harvest the fruits of the soil.

'Would you go to the local orchard and help the farmers there gather grain and fruit to feed our army? Every bit helps to keep morale high and minds sharp, ${PLAYER}.''Ah, yes I could use the help, much as it shames me to say it. These legs have borne strides enough for three men. I have been blessed to work this land for many years, but now the years feel much heavier on my bones than they once did. I am glad for the aid.

'You can start by gathering fruit from the orchard. Beware of the zizani - every year they grow fiercer and seemingly larger. Anything you can do to reduce their number would be greatly appreciated. After that there is some grain that is ready for harvesting in the northern field.''You move with an enviable speed, that much is sure. I will add these to what my farm-hands gathered, and we will distribute them to Iridír on the next waggon. Thank you for your aid. This harvest would have taken us days without it.''I am heartened. A queen without an army is just a deluded fool, smitten with false confidence and capricious lies. But this responsibility cuts both ways. I must provide for those under my care. I am grateful to you, for making that responsibility a bit lighter for me this day.

'I know these food-stocks will aid us in our fight against this Bârshud.'Defeat many servals and caracals throughout Ambarûl.Defeat many servals and caracals throughout Ambarûl.Defeat many servals and caracals in AmbarûlDefeat a great many servals and caracals in Ambarûl.Defeat many servals and caracals in Ambarûl.Defeat a great many servals and caracals in AmbarûlDefeat a great many servals and caracals in AmbarûlSûlmur has trouble with aggressive crocodiles and Neekers lurking among the papyrus reeds.Sûlmur has offered you a reward for defeating crocodiles and zizani, what the locals call Neekers, in the papyrus fields at Mehêtur in Ambarûl.Defeat crocodiles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat zizani (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated crocodiles and zizani in the papyrus fields. You should return to Sûlmur north-east of the fields.Talk to Sûlmur'The reeds grow easily here, but one must tread carefully in the bog. There is no small amount of crocodiles and zizani among the reeds.  Verily, they seem to be more hostile of late. It is concerning. Are you a ${CLASS}? If you are apt to fighting, I would not complain if you were to rid me of the beasts! I can offer you a small reward for your trouble.''If you are apt to fighting, I would not complain if you were to rid me of the crocodiles and zizani in the marshes here in Mehêtur. I can offer you a small reward for your trouble.''Oh my, thank you! I will feel much safer doing my work now. It isn't much, but take this with my gratitude.'Gajóta, the cook at Hêbatokh, the Morutágya clan hideout, has asked you to do something about the rats that keep getting into their food stores.Sewer rats can be found throughout Ilmabiri, but may be more plentiful in Gedma-ghâr, on the eastern edge.Defeat Ilmabiri rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have slain many Ilmabiri rats. Return to Gajóta to let him know.Talk to Gajóta'Making yourself useful, are you? Why don't you do something more practical like helping me? Helping me helps all of us, as I'm the one keeping everyone fed!' 

Gajóta exclaims this loudly for all to hear. The other smugglers groan as if this is something they have heard many times before.

'Unfortunately, I am not only keeping my clansmen fed but the neighbours as well. Sewer rats keep getting into our food stores! I tell them we need to get a cat like on a ship, but do we have a cat? We do not.

'If you want to be of use to us, go find those filthy thieves and rid us of them.''Ah, the hero returns! Did you deal with those wretched things?'

You tell him you did.

'Very good! Now you have accomplished something of import. Here, you deserve some food for your trouble.'You have done what you can to help restore balance to Arwáth, for both the forest and the people who will now share the burden of caring for it.Shanthar has thanked you for all that you have done. He asked you to visit Agalûnu once more to check on her and tell her he will visit soon.Talk to AgalûnuYou have bid Agalûnu farewell and she asked you to tell her sister Kalkhadra in Iridír that she is all right.Return to Kalkhadra in Iridír'You have done well ${PLAYER}. There is much more to do, but perhaps with Agalûnu's assistance, I will be able to not only preserve this grove but expand it as well. You have done much to help, particularly in bringing Agalûnu and I together to talk. I now have an ally instead of an enemy.

'I will let you be on your way, but if you do not mind, would you check on Agalûnu? I have a few matters to attend to first, but please tell her I will visit soon and see if I can do anything for her injury. Farewell, ${PLAYER}.''${PLAYER}, you were gone for an age! Though I suppose it only felt that way because I am bored.'

The woman chuckles to herself and she appears to be in higher spirits as well as better health. You tell her that you are leaving, but Shanthar will soon visit.

'Oh! Well, I hope he feels guilty.'

She laughs again, holding up her wounded arm.

'But I will enjoy the company. It is not every day that I can talk to someone thousands of years old! I cannot even imagine such a life. Are you going back to Iridír? Can you please let my sister know that I yet live? Kalkhadra is likely beside herself with worry.''There you are! I was about to start marshalling a search party! Where is Agalûnu?!'

You tell Kalkhadra that her sister is injured but all right, and that an Elf of the Kintai is looking out for her. Kalkhadra's jaw drops.

'Surely you jest. Nobody has seen a Kinta in ages! Oh, Agalûnu... this is what she gets for not being properly afraid of things. You have my thanks for finding her.'Agalûnu's wound has re-opened and she worries about a possible infection.Agalûnu has asked you to collect healing herbs for a poultice. They can be found across the stream to the south-east.Collect healing herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected herbs to make a healing poultice for Agalûnu. You should mash them with the mortar and pestle near Agalûnu's tent.You have made a healing poultice. You should go to Agalûnu and apply it to her wound.You have made a healing poultice and applied it to Agalûnu's wound. You should talk to her and see how she is doing.Talk to AgalûnuAgalûnu must rest to allow her wound to heal. In the meantime, she asked you to return to Shanthar and reassure him that she intends to keep her promise to help him care for the forest. Shanthar is at his abode in Arwáth.Talk to Shanthar'${PLAYER}, I fear that travelling to visit Shanthar has caused my wound to re-open. It is terribly painful, and now I worry that it may fester. I know how to make a poultice, but I cannot gather the ingredients. I do not feel well at all.

'${PLAYER}, would you please collect some healing herbs? There should be some growing across the stream to the south-east. I have a mortar and pestle you can use to mash them.''Would you please collect some healing herbs? There should be some growing across the stream to the south-east. I have a mortar and pestle you can use to mash them.''Thank you so much ${PLAYER}. Hopefully, that will do to avert festering. I should continue to rest and allow my body to heal. I feel ashamed though. I told Shanthar that I would return and help him steward the forest. He will think I lied to him when I fail to return.

'On my honour ${PLAYER}, I was speaking true. I beg you to go to him and tell him of my condition and reassure him that I intend to keep my oath.''I beg you to go to Shanathar and tell him of my condition. Reassure him that I intend to keep my oath.''You return without Agalûnu?'

The Kinta looks irritated. You tell him of her injury and that she is resting. You also reassure him that she is determined to keep her promise to him once she has recovered. The Elf's brow furrows.

'I confess ${PLAYER} that I have not spent much time in the company of Men and I forgot that they do not heal with the ease of the Firstborn. I am no master of the healing arts, but I believe rest and your poultice should serve her well.

'It gladdens my heart to know she intends to keep her oath. I look forward to teaching others how to care for the grove. Never did I think anyone other than Kintai would be interested in doing such a thing.'Mizâdi has asked for your company in a visit to the grave of her husband, Eshtali.Gather flowers outside Kûr Anzar for Mizâdi's husband, Eshtali. You can find these flowers growing in the hills outside the back gate to the tower of Kûr Anzar.Gather flowers for Eshtali's tomb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the flowers to Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar.Bring the flowers to Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr AnzarSpeak with Mizâdi when you are ready to leave.Speak with Mizâdi when you are ready to leaveSpeak with Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar.'I would ask you for your company in a personal matter, ${PLAYER}. I will be visiting my husband's tomb today, to lay fresh flowers upon it. I wonder if you would accompany me, I could do with some fellowship.

'If you're willing, gather me some white flowers outside of Kûr Anzar. You will notice them by their striking petals, and strong fragrance. They were Eshtali's favourite flower, and mine.''Let us be on our way then to Esh-kimâkhi.''These are lovely, thank you. Are you ready to leave for Esh-kimâkhi?''I appreciated your company this day. I trust you will not repeat anything you heard today to anyone.

'This burden... this burden is not so great when it can be shared, even if for a moment. Thank you.'Raphûz learned the softer side of Shagâni courting and wants to work toward making an impression. He wants to collect hearty flowers from the river-banks west of Wrackwade, near Eshadûr, and a vase from the bandit encampment at Eshadûr.Raphûz asked you to make your way along the dry river-bed searching for marsh lilies. He also asked you to collect a vase taken by Ordâkhai bandits at Eshadûr to the north and west.Collect marsh lilies from the river-banks in Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/12)Collect a relic vase from EshadûrDefeat Ordâkhai bandits at Eshadûr (${NUMBER}/12)Raphûz awaits your return at Wrackwade with the vase, lilies, and news of the bandits' defeat. Return to him at the southern outpost of Ambarûl.'I would like to acquire something showing my softer side. A would-be merchant here lost a shipment of vases to an Ordâkhai patrol on the west side of the bridge. I learned there is a place along the banks of the dry river-bed where the heartiest flowers still bloom. I want to collect some and help the would-be merchant. Alas, my recent excursions with you drew the notice of other Phetekâri, and I cannot leave my post.

'Would you help me again, friend? I think a dozen flowers and a vase from the camp at Eshadûr, west and north across dry river will suffice.

'Perhaps you could punish the Ordâkhai as well.''They are as beautiful and hardy as described. Thank you for doing this, my friend. I am grateful. I am also certain the would-be merchant will be thankful for returning some of the product.

'I know the fighters here will rejoice in the thinning of Ordâkhai ranks. I continue to ask too much of you. Thank you, sincerely.'Galâmka has asked you to clear out the Orc scouts spotted nearby before they can discover the camp at Ub Nishir.Using the information from the scouting report gathered from Irkiri, Galâmka has asked you to clear out Orc scouts in the area to the south-east to prevent them from finding the camp.Defeat Orc scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have eliminated the Orc scouts.Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir'Ah, you are here. Let us get started.

'The report you gathered from Irkiri details the movements of the Orc scouts, and we must act fast. They are getting closer by the day to scouting out the location of Ub Nishir and we can not allow that to happen.'

Galâmka points to a location on his map to indicate the location of the scouts being tracked.

'You can find the scouting parties in this area, I ask that you clear them out and prevent them from scouting any further.''I hear reports that you have succeeded in eliminating the Orc scouts. That is heartening news, and I give my thanks.

'You have given us vital time to continue our preparations. I know that the Orcs will send more scouts in time, but we are safe for now.

'We still have much work to do here. I ask that you return when you can if you wish to help more with our efforts.'Your aid is requested in the continued efforts to help forge a new path for the peoples of the Ikorbân Valley.Complete missions throughout the Ikorbân Valley. Missions can be found in Iridír in Ambarûl, Urmâkh in Imhûlar, and Ub Nishir in Urash Dâr.Complete Ikorbân Valley missions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed many missions throughout the Ikorbân Valley, assisting the peoples of Shagâna.Completed'We must continue to forge a new path for all of the peoples of the Ikorbân Valley!

'If you are willing to lend your efforts several more times, I will be able to reward your accomplishments.'Your efforts have truly assisted those who work to improve the fortunes of the Ikorbân Valley. You will be rewarded for your efforts.Defeat many forsaken in Ilmabiri.Defeat many forsaken in Ilmabiri.Defeat many forsaken in IlmabiriDefeat a great many forsaken in Ilmabiri.Defeat many forsaken in Ilmabiri.Defeat a great many forsaken in Ilmabiri.Defeat a great many forsaken in IlmabiriEnârshan has asked you to defeat the leader of the nearby camp, Hazthak, and make the Falls of Ilûritu safe again.Enârshan has asked you to enter into Khûn Sagaz and use the challenge horn to call out Hazthak and defeat him.Reach Hazthak's tent in Khûn Sagaz to sound the challenge hornUse the challenge horn and call forth Hazthak to battle.Use the challenge horn to call forth HazthakDefeat Hazthak in Khûn Sagaz near the Falls of Ilûritu.Defeat HazthakReturn to Enârshan and let her know that you have defeated Hazthak and her falls should be safe for now.Return to Enârshan'It is time to end this and free Ilûritu, ${CLASS}.

'With their camp weakened, you can now take the fight directly to their leader, a foul Orc named Hazthak.'

Enârshan hands you a horn.

'Take this horn and use it to challenge Hazthak at his tent within Khûn Sagaz. You will find it in the centre of the camp. Even in his weakened state he will not be able to refuse a direct challenge.

'Bring an end to this monster and rid them from my waters.''I heard the horn from here. You must be returning victorious. I regret that I could not protect my falls alone, but I am grateful for what you have done, ${CLASS}.

'Please take this, and then leave these falls. I ask that you not speak of my presence as I must remain the myth the people believe me to be.

'You have my thanks. I wish you well on your adventures.'Avadhril has offered to show you how the Kintai tend to their groves. You are to work with Ulthral, one of the Kintai grove-tenders, in tending to the new shoots growing in Vartúlin.Ulthral has offered to show you how the Kintai nurture young plants. Your first task is to collect cinder to be used as a potent fertilizer. There should be some right outside Vartúlin to the east.Collect cinder from cinder piles outside Vartúlin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Ulthral about what to do next.Speak with Ulthral in VartúlinMix water and cinder in Ulthral's soil plot.Mix water and cinder to create fertile ground in soil plot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Ulthral in Vartúlin to collect small saplings for planting.Plant the small saplings in the holes in Ulthral's soil plot in Vartúlin.Plant the small saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Ulthral the grove-tender in Vartúlin.'There is much work to be done planting and growing, now that the Pale Blight can be properly combated. We could use your help, ${PLAYER}. If you wish to learn how we plant and tend to the forest, I and the other grove-tenders will show you. You will work with Ulthral, one of our grove-tenders on the high path above.

'First, however, we need to collect cinder from nearby cinder piles. It makes the soil fertile, and it is beneficial for new plants. There should be some right outside Vartúlin.''These new plants growing are so exciting! There is so much for us to do. We grove-tenders had our hands full just tending to the Veróthi and holding back the Pale Blight. Now we can focus on the fun part - growing new plants in rich soil. There is much to it - lend me a hand and I'll show you how we do it.

'This is perfect. Don't you just love that smell? It smells like home to me.

'Now we need to combine the cinder with a little water into each hole you see there. Then we'll fill the holes with small saplings.''That was perfect! We'll make a tree-bearer of you yet. Well, if Thórvilon allows it. For that you'd have to plant some of these saplings outside Vartúlin. But that was great! Just wait - just thirty years from now, this whole forest will be transformed.''Here. Be careful with them! These saplings are easily broken. Put one sapling in each fertile area you made.'Your continued efforts to support Shâra Mizâdi and her forces in Idagâl earn you greater favour with Hamât Renewed.You must earn Friend standing with Hamât RenewedYour standing with the Adúrhid improves and earns you a gift from the Ikorbâni Elves.Your continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.Reach Friend tier with the AdúrhidYour continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.Visit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a giftYour continued efforts to aid the Kintai Elves brings great joy to them. You should visit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a gift from the Elves of the oasis.'Your continued attention to our requests is truly noble, friend. We are pleased you seek the same paths we walk.

'Please accept this small token for our appreciation.'Your continued efforts to support Mûr Ghala earns you greater favour with the City of Zajâna.You must earn Friend standing with the City of ZajânaYou continue to prove your valour, nerve, and measured assistance to the Hunter's Guild of Mûr Ghala.You must earn Friend standing with the Hunter's Guild of Mûr GhalaYour standing among the Ikorbâni earns you a gift. Return to Kildûg at Iridír to claim your reward.You have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Irídir to receive a reward for your continued assistance.Reach Friend tier with the IkorbâniYou have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.Visit Kildûg at Iridír to claim a giftYour efforts to assist the Ikorbâni are noted among the people. To recognize your efforts, the leaders of the Shagâni at Iridír wish to honour you with a gift and thanks.'Your alliance with our people shows that many of tales of the north are without merit. Please accept one of these gifts and if you desire, purchase more from Nêkhur.'Your continued efforts to support the Ikorbân Valley earn you greater favour with the Shagâni people.You must earn Friend standing with the IkorbâniYou continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Ikorbân.You must earn Friend standing with the KintaiYou continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Sul Madásh.You must earn Friend standing with the Kintai of Sul MadáshYour standing among the Tale-wardens earns you a gift. Return to one of their members' quartermasters to be rewarded.Visit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Reach Friend tier with the PhetêkariVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Visit a Tale-warden's assistant at Iridír, Jirush, or UrmâkhVisit Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate to claim your giftYour standing with the Phetekâri grows. You should visit one of their assistants at Telperiën's Gate, Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a well-earned gift.'Captain Rothog bids us provide you another selection of rewards as recompense for your continued assistance.

'As always, for a small amount of Ghín, our quartermasters have other offers from Lord Rothog.''Our knowledge and collection of relics and writings grows due to your continued assistance in these lands.

'Captain Rothog bids us provide you another selection or rewards as recompense for your continued assistance.

'As always, for a small amount of Ghín, Shulêga can furnish you with the other selections you do not choose.'Your continued efforts in Shagâna inform the Tale-wardens of the people, history, and tribulations of the land. The records of the Ikorbân Valley's history grow due to your efforts.You must earn Friend standing with the Tale-wardensYour continued efforts to support An Shêru earns you greater favour with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh.You must earn Friend standing with the Temámir of Jiret-menêshGirnada, the quartermaster of Urmâkh, has asked for your aid in scavenging food and supplies for the hungry people of Urmâkh.Girnada, the quartermaster of Urmâkh, has asked you to gather supplies for the villagers in Shakhdag, as food and supplies are scarce in Urmâkh. Shakhdag is located just outside Urmâkh, to the west.Collect boar meat from healthy boars near Shakhdag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather healthy berries near Shakhdag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather sticks for kindling near Shakhdag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Girnada in Urmâkh with all you've collected.'I tell you we have great need of food and supplies here. I am just a humble quartermaster. I cannot spin rock into cloth, or sand into bread. Life is hard in Urmâkh, and has only gotten harder with this great influx of people fleeing Kûr Anzar. We do what we can, but supplies are scarce and with the forest afflicted as it is, our meagre sources of food have only grown more paltry.

'Truth be told, there are days I go without so the children can still eat. When we do engage in hunting parties, the mad beasts of the forest often bedevil us. I know there are berries and kindling to spare in Shakhdag, to the east, but the boar have gone mad and attack anyone on sight.

'We could very much use one such as you, with a talent for combat. Would you be able to hunt for some healthy boar meat, and scavenge for fresh berries and kindling? We are close to our breaking point, ${PLAYER}.'Girnada's eyes light up at the sight of all the boar you have brought her.

'Oh, thank you. You don't know how many this will help. It's surprising how few cares a person has when you have a warm hearth and a belly full of boar.'Trees have been felled to the north-east of Sûru for the building of the Dumûri fort. The logs have yet to be collected.Ningêna has asked you to collect logs and deposit them in a pile near the archers' towers at Sûru.Collect logs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected the logs. You should deposit them in a pile near the archers' towers at Sûru.You have placed the logs you collected at the building site. You should return to Ningêna.Talk to Ningêna'There is another thing you could do for me if you wish. Some trees have been felled north-east of here for the building of our fortress. These have not yet been collected. If you could gather them, there is a pile near the building site to which they may be added.''Some trees have been felled to the north-east for building our fortress. If you would gather them, there is a pile near the building site to which they may be added.''The logs were collected and have been added to the pile? Thank you ${PLAYER}, this will speed the builders' work nicely.'Angârmu has asked you to help him gather magical sand from places nearby for an enchantment meant to protect him from the Orcs roaming the area.Reach the locations where you can find magical sand for Angârmu's enchantment to the south-east near the river.Find the location of the magical sand to the south-eastGather handfuls of magical sand for Angârmu's enchantment at the location you found to the south-east near the river.Gather sand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Reach the location where you can find magical sand for Angârmu's enchantment to the north-east along the river.Find the location of the magical sand to the north-eastGather handfuls of magical sand for Angârmu's enchantment at the location you found to the north-east along the river's edge.Gather sand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Reach the location where you can find magical sand for Angârmu's enchantment further to the north-east along the river.Find the location of the magical sand to the north-eastGather handfuls of magical sand for Angârmu's enchantment at the location you found further to the north near the river's edge.Gather sand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Angârmu in Malgâma near Zikrum-dûl with the piles of gathered sand to complete their enchantment.'I am relieved you are here, visitor! Demons of the Dark Lord are near and you must help.

'I need sand. Not just any sand, but sand for my enchantment. My enchantment will hide me from the Dark Lord. Go and get me some. You will know it when you see it.

'It must be from three places, yes three. Along the river to the south of this place. You will find the sand I need there. Bring it to me before the demons come.''You are back and with my sand! I can begin my enchantment at once. Hand it over, hand it over!

You hand the sand you have collected over to Angârmu and he begins to look at it.

'This will do nicely, yes. I know not why you also brought me the rest of this sand, so unremarkable it is. Just ordinary sand I could have gathered by my feet. Though I can still be safe. Very safe. From the eyes of the Dark Lord.'

'Thank you visitor. You may go now.'Zildug told you about oysters that can be found in the Ikorbân River.Zildug has invited you to gather oysters for him. Oysters can be harvested in the shallows west of Iridír.Look in likely spots for oysters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have gathered oysters from the Ikorbân River shallows. You should bring them to Zildug in Iridír.'Níkhu! A traveller from the north! What an interesting time to be alive. Tell me traveller, where you come from, have you oysters? Today I am catching fish, but river oysters are a celebrated Ambarûli delicacy. Would you like to gather some? It is very easy. The water is shallow enough in places that all you have to do is pick them up!

'Go ahead, look around in the shallows and find some oysters. When you are done, I will take them off your hands. What is that? Am I trying to get you to do my work for me?'

The fisherman gives you a lighthearted laugh and winks at you.

'Well... yes. Will you do it?''Look around in the shallows to the west and find some oysters. When you are done, I will take them off your hands.''Ah, look at these beautiful oysters. Thank you for gathering them. It was easy, yes?'Ashâmi and Raphûz are unnerved by the last words of the cultist and want to gather proof to present Numûru proving the threat is real.Ashâmi and Raphûz, unnerved by the words of the cultist, want to collect evidence of a greater threat to present to Numûru. They ask you to search near Dûl Zidur, where the cultists are most numerous to search in all directions for signs of invasion.Near Dûl Zidur and the Bridge of Princes you saw an encampment of Orcs to the north. Among the Orcs, stood one of proportions more fitting of a troll: fearsome, vile, and terrifying. Return this information to Raphûz and Ashâmi at their home in Urmâkh.Present your findings to Raphûz at his home in UrmâkhHaving heard your report and deciphered the letter they discovered, Ashâmi and Raphûz send you to present the evidence to Numûru at his post in Urmâkh.Present the evidence to Numûru at his post in UrmâkhNumûru refuses to look to other threats while the Ordâkhai remain. He will not bring the information to Mizâdi. Speak with Ashâmi or Raphûz at their home in Urmâkh and ask how they want to proceed.Speak with Ashâmi at her home in UrmâkhRaphûz and Ashâmi nod in unison. Ashâmi speaks.

'We agree. We want to collect proof to deliver to Numûru. If the cultist's threat is real, there will be signs near their encampment.

'Raphûz and I will head to the Ordâkhai camp in the south. Will you go to the cultist camp east near the Bridge of Princes, called Nâmbadir in the Shagâni tongue?

'Look for signs of the threat and return here with your evidence. We will confer and present what we find to Numûru.'You shared your discovery of the Orc encampment to the north of the camp of cultists. Both Ashâmi and Raphûz seem unsurprised.

'We found a letter in a language I do not understand. I believe I deciphered one word - Orcs.

'We should take this information to Nurûmu.'Nurûmu looks at the letter and listens to your report on the cultist camp far to the east.

'None here can read this. Raphûz is a scholarly man, and he cannot read this. Orcs are a menace. Most fled when the temple-keepers vanished. If there is an encampment of Orcs near the bridge, they are just another enemy to face.

'As for your large Orc, you said it was a good distance away. You could be mistaken. Maybe it was a troll or some upright beast.

'We have an enemy we know now. We must focus on Kûr Anzar and not bother ourselves with what may be a threat from the dead lands in the north.

'The offer to join our number remains extended to your friends. I offer you the same. Your tenacity would be welcome.'You approach Ashâmi and Raphûz. They have been talking quietly.

'We cannot join them. We believe the threat from the east is real. Raphûz and I have been talking, and we have a course.'Shanathar has offered a lesson on Kintai forest stewardship.You have been directed to plant saplings in Arwáth, in the places where they have the best chance to grow.Plant saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have planted saplings in Arwáth where you feel they have the best chance to grow. You should return to Shanthar.Talk to Shanthar'Tell me, ${PLAYER}, would you be interested in understanding the forest? The first truth in restoring the land is that you must give more than you take away.

'You may fell a tree that is in decline. Doing so will allow the younger things that are beneath its canopy to grow. When a tree is removed, one should plant a sapling to replace it. This is good, but what is better, is planting many to replace it. It sounds overly simple when it is said out loud, but we have seen our beloved woods clear-cut by Men more than once.

'Go forth, into Arwáth and find the places where the sunlight touches the ground. There you should plant a sapling that will one day grow into a majestic tree.''Go forth and plant saplings that will one day grow into a majestic tree.''The saplings are planted? That is happy news. Thank you.'Defeat many gladiators in Kamrabezûr.Defeat many gladiators in Kamrabezûr.Defeat many gladiators in KamrabezûrDefeat a great many gladiators in Kamrabezûr.Defeat many gladiators in Kamrabezûr.Defeat a great many gladiators in Kamrabezûr.Defeat a great many gladiators in KamrabezûrDefeat many goblins in Ilmabiri.Defeat many goblins in Ilmabiri.Defeat many goblins in IlmabiriDefeat a great many goblins in Ilmabiri.Defeat many goblins in Ilmabiri.Defeat a great many goblins in Ilmabiri.Defeat a great many goblins in IlmabiriBefore dismissing you from her service, Meliri has one last job for you.Meliri handed you a crate of oranges and honey to deliver to a trader named Dashên in Iridír.'I have one final job for you, and then you must find work elsewhere, or I will run out of coin! Here is a crate of oranges and honey. Have you been to Iridír yet? I need you to take this to Iridír to the trader named Dashên. There is no need to collect my payment for it, as we have already agreed that he will send it to me later, and he should give you some coin for your trouble.

'You are a good worker. There are many skilled craftspeople in Iridír, and I do not think you will have much trouble finding a job. Girhâzi may also have use for your fighting skills, so you could also go talk to her. Off you go now!''Well, go on then. Those oranges aren't getting any fresher. Take the crate to Dashên in Iridír.''Hashtal-gûr, what can I do for you?'

You hand the man the crate given to you by Meliri.

'Ah, wonderful, I needed a restock of these. Thank you for bringing them. Did... did Meliri pay you already?'

You tell him that she did not.

'Humph. Well. I will just take it out of what I owe her for these. Thank you, my friend.'The Quartermaster has asked that you gather your allies and travel to The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr to put an end to the evils there.The evils within The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr must be stopped.

Complete three Umbar or Ikorbân raids on the highest tier.Complete Umbar or Ikorbân raids on the highest tier (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to the Temple of Utug-bûr Quartermaster with proof of your victory.Return to the Temple of Utug-bûr Quartermaster'Greetings, ${CLASS}.

'An evil plagues the lands of Umbar and Ikorbân and we cannot allow it to spread.

'I ask that you gather your allies and travel to The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr and defeat the evils who lurk in their halls. Do this, and I can provide you with a reward to match your efforts.''I have heard of your deeds in The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr.

'Please accept this as a token of my thanks to you and your companions.'Gêna would like to attempt some container gardening using soil from the dry river-bed of the Usâl.Gêna has asked you to go to the Usâl and fill four bags with soil from the dried river-bed.Collect sacks of dry river-bed dirt from the sediment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gêna has asked you to go to the Usâl and fill four sacks with soil from the dried river-bed. You have collected the soil and should bring it to Gêna in Western Khanâg.You have collected the sediment Gêna asked for and delivered it to her. She will put it in the planter with the seeds while you get a bucket of water from the well.Bring water from the well for the newly planted seedsThe planter has been filled with soil, seeded, and watered. You should talk to Gêna.Talk to Gêna'Hashtal-gûr, may I ask you a favour?

'Another traveller told me once that the soil from a dried river-bed is very good for growing fruits and vegetables. I have this large planter and would like to try it, but I am not brave enough to go to the Usâl. Would you be willing to go to the old river-bed and collect some soil for me? Four of these sacks should do.''You have the soil! Wonderful! I will take it and put it in the planter with my seeds while you get water from the well.''Thank you for all of your help, ${PLAYER}. It will be exciting to see if the traveller spoke true, and the soil from a dry river-bed is indeed better for gardens.'Defeat many gredbyg in Tâkhdar.Defeat many gredbyg in Tâkhdar.Defeat many gredbyg in TâkhdarDefeat a great many gredbyg in Tâkhdar.Defeat many gredbyg in Tâkhdar.Defeat a great many gredbyg in Tâkhdar.Defeat a great many gredbyg in TâkhdarMizâdi, Girhâzi, Rahâzi, Amalíbi, and Numûru have gathered outside Dun Shûma to discuss their victory and what is next for Shagâna.Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma when you are ready.Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma when you are readySpeak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma.Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma'This is a new day for Shagâna. For the first time in generations we Shagâni can control our own destiny. We have much to be thankful for. I have much to be thankful for. Please, join me in talking with the others. You have earned your place among us.''Finally, this is a gift for you, ${PLAYER}. You have been my steadfast friend and compatriot through all the events over these past several weeks, and for that I am eternally grateful.

'You will always have a welcome place in my halls, and in Shagâna, for everything you've done for her people, and for me. Thank you.''Let us meet with the others, before they all scatter to the winds and return to their homelands. This is a moment we need to remember, and cherish.'Urama, tired from a life of manual labour, has asked for your help on her rice farm.You have been asked to collect stalks of rice that are ready to harvest from the eastern fields at Ekagar.Collect rice stalks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected stalks of rice that were ready to harvest from the fields to the east. You should bring them to Urama by the trellis.'Hashtal-gûr traveller, what brings you to our lands?'

The old woman looks at you warily.

'I hope you are not here to cause trouble, as we have enough of that already. I am weary of it. Though to be fair, I was weary already! I have done this work my whole life, but harvesting rice is demanding. It is early yet in the season, but the food is needed. Many farms have been destroyed or abandoned because there are scant workers.

'You look rather fit, would you mind helping an old woman? In the fields to the east, you can find some rice that can be harvested. Collect the stalks and bring them to me while I rest.''Well, go on then. You can find some rice that can be harvested in the fields to the east. Collect the stalks and bring them to me while I rest.''Oh, you are back! And you bring bundles of rice with you.'

The woman's smile is positively beaming.

'Thank you so much for your help.  These must dry before threshing so don't worry, I won't ask you to do that part!'Nakûr is concerned about the parcels he has seen Corsairs hiding around the waterways of the Lower Ward, and wants you to investigate them.Hidden parcels can be found alongside the southern waterway that runs through the Lower Ward.Collect hidden parcels along the southern waterway in the Lower Ward (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Nakûr is located on the western side of the Lower Ward, near the southern waterway.'The vigilant eye cannot be taken by surprise, my friend. That is why I keep a close watch on anything that seems out of the ordinary, and why my neighbours believe I have been taken by madness. But it is not so!

'Why, just this afternoon I have learned that Corsairs have left parcels along the waterway that runs through the Lower Ward... this one right here! They must be stockpiling weapons so they can begin another rebellion, as they did before. The Sea-stone Mutiny began in the Lower Ward... who is to say these Corsairs do not intend to foment another uprising? This one would aim to overthrow the Kindred of the Coins!

'We cannot allow that to happen! Find the parcels these Corsairs have hidden along the waterway and return them to me so we may stop their plans before they get any further along!''Find the parcels these Corsairs have hidden along the waterway and return them to me so we may stop their plans before they get any further along!''You found the hidden parcels? Let us see what these Corsairs have secreted within!'

Nakûr gingerly opens the first parcel.

'This is... a hard biscuit and a small cloth bag. What is inside the bag?'

He tastes it and makes a face. 'Salt,' he says to you. 'It is cooking-salt.'

Nakûr opens the rest of the parcels, revealing more food, a number of copper buttons, and a few other household trinkets. The last parcel contains a small knit figure of a crocodile.

'This does not appear to be the beginning of a new rebellion, friend. I will return these parcels to the places you found them. I cannot say why these items were hidden in this fashion, but it seems we have stumbled upon a scheme most unusual. I will continue to keep my eyes open! For now you have my thanks, and this reward. But my vigilance will not lapse!'Urama has suggested you introduce yourself to her son, Turizi.Turizi has been troubled since returning home from the war in the north. You should talk to him behind the house at Ekagar.Talk to Turizi'Forgive me, I mentioned my son to you twice and have not introduced you! His name is Turizi and he is behind the house, to the south. He might enjoy meeting you. He was injured in the war and returned a man unlike the one who had left. Please, if you have time, mayhap you could talk to him? I think he feels very alone and maybe the company of someone worldly like yourself could do him some good.''Go ahead and introduce yourself to Turizi. He is not as surly as he looks, and could use a friend, I think. He should be behind the house, to the south.''Who are you!?'

The young man is clearly alarmed by your approach. You tell him you had been helping his mother with some farm chores and she asked you to introduce yourself to him. His shoulders relax, but he still holds suspicion in his eyes.

'My apologies. We don't see strangers in this land often, and when we do, they usually mean us harm. What brings you to our farm?'

You tell him that you often take the time to help others while you go about your travels.

'A noble undertaking, though you might find that there are more people in need of help in Ambarûl than you can handle.'The Adúrhid have posted a task to collect leathered sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire leathered sword sheaths for the Adúrhid.Wanted: leathered sword sheaths from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: leathered sword sheaths from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Adúrhid have posted a task to collect notched axes. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire notched axes for the Adúrhid.Wanted: notched axes from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: notched axes from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Adúrhid have posted a task to collect sand-baked hides. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sand-baked hides for the Adúrhid.Wanted: sand-baked hides from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sand-baked hides from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Adúrhid have posted a task to collect sand-scarred ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sand-scarred ears for the Adúrhid.Wanted: sand-scarred ears from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sand-scarred ears from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Adúrhid have posted a task to collect scorched goo. This can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire scorched goo for the Adúrhid.Wanted: scorched goo from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather it to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: scorched goo from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Adúrhid have posted a task to collect sun-bronzed claws. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sun-bronzed claws for the Adúrhid.Wanted: sun-bronzed claws from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sun-bronzed claws from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Ikorbâni have posted a task to collect leathered sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire leathered sword sheaths for the Ikorbâni.Wanted: leathered sword sheaths from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: leathered sword sheaths from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Ikorbâni have posted a task to collect notched axes. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire notched axes for the Ikorbâni.Wanted: notched axes from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: notched axes from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Ikorbâni have posted a task to collect sand-baked hides. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sand-baked hides for the Ikorbâni.Wanted: sand-baked hides from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sand-baked hides from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Ikorbâni have posted a task to collect sand-scarred ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sand-scarred ears for the Ikorbâni.Wanted: sand-scarred ears from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sand-scarred ears from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Ikorbâni have posted a task to collect scorched goo. This can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire scorched goo for the Ikorbâni.Wanted: scorched goo from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather it to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: scorched goo from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Ikorbâni have posted a task to collect sun-bronzed claws. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sun-bronzed claws for the Ikorbâni.Wanted: sun-bronzed claws from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sun-bronzed claws from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Phetekâri have posted a task to collect leathered sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire leathered sword sheaths for the Phetekâri.Wanted: leathered sword sheaths from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: leathered sword sheaths from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Phetekâri have posted a task to collect notched axes. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire notched axes for the Phetekâri.Wanted: notched axes from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: notched axes from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Phetekâri have posted a task to collect sand-baked hides. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sand-baked hides for the Phetekâri.Wanted: sand-baked hides from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sand-baked hides from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Phetekâri have posted a task to collect sand-scarred ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sand-scarred ears for the Phetekâri.Wanted: sand-scarred ears from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sand-scarred ears from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Phetekâri have posted a task to collect scorched goo. This can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire scorched goo for the Phetekâri.Wanted: scorched goo from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather it to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: scorched goo from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Phetekâri have posted a task to collect sun-bronzed claws. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire sun-bronzed claws for the Phetekâri.Wanted: sun-bronzed claws from the Ikorbân Valley. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: sun-bronzed claws from the Ikorbân Valley.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Malgat asked you to assist with some fundamental and menial tasks for the people of the outpost. He directed you to assist the tanner, Ashkab and the quartermaster, Nisami, with their needs.Malgat asked you to visit Ashkab and Nisami, the outpost's tanner and quartermaster, and help them with whatever was needed. They can be found in the outpost of Jirush.Assist the quartermaster Nisami with her taskAssist the tanner Ashkab with her taskYou aided both Ashkab and Nisami. With the work complete, you should return to Mallgat in Jirush near the northernmost standing arch and inform him of what you have done.Inform Malgat of your assistance to Nisami and Ashkab'Nangar is good to send you to me. While I look toward the future, I overlook the pressing needs of our community. We are few. Many are infirm or older than I am.

'The Ordâkhai were cruel masters who left nothing for our people. Their presence in the north strikes fear into many hearts. You look as though you have often faced and overcome fear.

'I ask that you help two in Jirush. The first is Ashkab. They help to shelter the masses. The second is Nisami. They see to feeding all they can. Help them and return them to me.''Have you finished the work offered by Ashkab and Nisami? If not, please find them and do whatever they ask. The outpost could use some younger, stronger arms, to handle some of the efforts.''Ashkab and Nisami seem pleased with your efforts. For this, I thank you, and I wish to become a little selfish with your time.

'Maybe you will consider doing something for me directly?'Munsubur has asked you to help him to gather pelts from jackals in Urash Dâr.Gather jackal pelts for Munsubur from the nearby jackal dens of Urgudag or Khazâda.Gather jackal pelts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the jackal pelts back to Munsubur in Ub Nishir near Maurûsh.'Adventurer, might I trouble you for your help?

'I must gather pelts for the people in need here in Urash Dâr. Many are fleeing from these Orcs pouring from the demon-pits. I have given them what I could, but it has not been enough. I am in need of more pelts from the jackals, but it is now a task too dangerous for a trader such as myself to accomplish alone.

'I ask of you to bring me any pelts you manage to gather. The jackals can be found to the west, in Urgudag, and to the east, in Khazâda.''You have returned and with the pelts in hand!'

You give Munsubur the jackal pelts.

'I can not thank you enough, adventurer. These pelts will help many during the cold nights as long as get them to those in need. The other traders here are unhappy with me for not making any coin with these pelts.'Uda is unhappy with the number of Orcs in the area and has asked that you help her to reduce it.Uda has asked you to slay Orcs in Urash Dâr to help her thin their numbers.Defeat Orcs in Urash Dâr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Uda at her camp and let her know you have reduced the number of Orcs in the area.Return to Uda at her camp near Utug-bûr'Adventurer, you seem worthy enough to join our efforts.

'The opening of the demon-pits nearby has unleashed hordes of Orcs into these lands, and we mean to push them back. I ask of you to help thin their numbers.

'They can be found throughout the area of Urash Dâr, though you may find a concentration of them in the camps to the north and east of here.''You have returned. I trust that means you have completed your task?

'Thank you, my friend. These lands are still dangerous, but I am glad to see people such as yourself helping our cause.

'I ask of you to continue to reduce their numbers, should you encounter any more.'Agalûnu was stuck by an arrow, shot by an unseen foe in Arwáth.Agalûnu has asked you to help her by finding who is responsible for wounding her. You should explore Arwáth in northern Ambarûl and seek out the culprit.Look for the person responsibleWhile searching Arwáth for who might have struck Agalûnu with an arrow, you spotted a strange Elf.  You should talk to him.Talk to the strange Elf'I was in the grove and someone shot me with an arrow! I did not think anyone else was here. Of the living, anyway. Thankfully the arrow hit nothing vital and I can dress the wound myself.

'I expect you are the capable sort, else you would not have come to these woods. Please, if you desire to help me, seek out who did this. Tread carefully friend, as those who say these woods are haunted speak true. I neither saw nor heard anything before I was struck, so be vigilant.''I was in the grove and someone shot me with an arrow! Please, seek out who did this.''Tell me, who treads upon this sacred grove of my people?'

The Elf has an ethereal quality about him and you find him unsettling, though you cannot determine exactly why. He is not like any other Elf you have met.Belondor has asked you to deliver a letter to Morutágya, the clan of smugglers that Tumúldo Fierce-water was the leader of, informing them of his death. Morutágya maintains a hideout in the southern part of Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Deliver Belondor's letter to the Morutágya clan, informing them of the demise of their leader, Tumúldo Fierce-water.'${PLAYER}, have I told you yet that I am grateful to have you as an ally? It means a lot that though you are a newcomer to this city, you take actions that are for the good of the common folk of Umbar. As you well know, I was a newcomer here once as well. It did not take me long to fall in love with the Umbari culture. The resiliency of the people, the bright colours, flavourful food, favourable winds, the blue seas... and of course, my beloved Mêshka, whom I can finally call my wife.

'Whether or not you love this city as I do, I still appreciate what you have been doing for its people, and feel ashamed to have once called you my enemy. You are a good person, ${PLAYER}.'

Belondor takes a deep breath as his posture changes and his demeanour returns to that of the Kinsman of the Fleet-fast and Captain of Fleets of Umbar Baharbêl.

'Speaking of your quality, I have another thing to ask of you, if you are willing. I am unsure if the kinsmen of Tumúldo Fierce-water are aware of his fate. Tumúldo was the leader of a clan, Morutágya. Smuggling has been the family business for generations. When Nakási returned to the city with a hostage instead of her husband, I don't think she took the time to inform their clan of his murder. Rumours abound, of course, but they are family and deserve to know the truth.

'If you would not mind delivering it, I have written a letter detailing everything I know about Tumúldo's death.'

You confess to Belondor that you were present in Linhir when Tumúldo Fierce-water was murdered. He raises his eyebrows in surprise.

'Is that so? I wouldn't tell them what you have just told me, or you may not walk away from the encounter without bloodshed. I've been told that they have a base of operations in the southern part of the Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven.''What is this, then? Who are you?'

You inform Porókho that you bring a letter from Belondor, Kinsman of the Fleet-fast, addressed to the Morutágya clan.

He takes the letter from you, reads it, and sighs, handing the letter over to Eshéra.

'So it is true. Tumúldo is dead, and Nakási has fled the city with the Sea-shadow, unlikely to return. Alive, anyway. We had our suspicions.'

The man's attitude quickly changes from sadness to anger.

'Curse all Men of Gondor, including this Belondor! They are as low as the wretched filth in these sewers.'

He spits on the floor to make his point.Keteph is undeterred by his failure and looks for a different bread he heard of from the North, rye. He requested that you collect several loaves of rye bread so he may try his recipe again.Keteph wants you to collect five loaves of rye bread for him. He intends to try to infuse his latest recipe with a different bread from the north. Rye bread requires a cook proficient in Ironfold cooking. Seek out a cook with this skill or trade for the bread at the auction house.Collect rye breads (${NUMBER}/5)You have five loaves of rye to deliver to Keteph in the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.'Failure is the first step on the road to success, friend. I will yet uncover the proper bread from the north to use with my latest dish.

'In fact, I have another idea. I hear there is a bread prized in the north that is darker in colour and filled with flavour from spices baked directly into the bread. I desire to try this bread next.

'Can you acquire five loaves of rye bread for me?''I will try the recipe again with a different bread. I am told that the rye bread of the north is tasty and distinct in colour. Can you obtain five loaves for me?'Keteph sniffs the bread deeply.

'Ah, that is a richer scent.'

He squeezes the bread and it crunches a bit under the pressure.

'Oh, that is a surprise! A good, thick crust. Yes, I think that this shall do nicely.'Keteph desires to hear fair criticism of his new dish. He enlists you to deliver sacks containing his new dish to the expedition leaders outside of Umbar to get their discerning opinions.Keteph wants discerning and brutally honest feedback from the workers of Rakhatâb. He asks that you deliver these free meals to the worker leaders there.You gathered the responses and critiques from the worker leaders in Rakhatâb. Return this information to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.'To be fair, my friend, I cannot determine if this is good. I need opinions I can trust before I present this to the aristocrats who so desire my dishes.

'The workers of Rakhatâb are honest to a fault. They will not hold back on telling you how bad or good the new dish is. Please bring this new recipe to them, gather their opinions, and then return to me with their feedback.''The workers of Rakhatâb are honest and forthright. I will get an honest opinion of this new dish from them. Please take it to them with haste.''I will never forgo an offer of a free meal. Especially on the pay that the kindred see fit to offer us here.'

She bites into the bread.

'It is a bit dry. I can taste a hint of saffron. This bread is too porous and flavourless. Still, a free meal is a free meal.'

She bites again.

'I am sorry, I cannot. This is awful.'Hûzo looks at you and cautiously accepts the sack.

'I am wary of those bearing free gifts. Alas, I am hungry, as are many in Rakhatâb. I will indulge you.'

He takes a bite of Keteph's new dish.

'Dry. Drier and drabber than a day along the shore with no water. I will eat it begrudgingly because the crab is delicious.''You come bearing a gift, and I will gladly accept.'

He takes a bite of Keteph's recipe.

He chews for a few seconds and swallows.

'Terrible, friend. Truly awful. This is not a gift. It is a curse.'Karishah tears the bready creation in half and takes a large bite.

'This bread is awful! It is bland. No spice, no taste. This is terrible.'

He spits the mouthful on the ground.

'I would not pay for this. Nor would I put in my body for free.'Beliash opens the sack and looks the bready gift over.

'Smells good.'

He takes a bite.

'Oh.'

His face contorts.

'This bread is the worst thing I have ever tasted. It mars the delicious crab and saffron in the dish. This is, perhaps, the worst thing I have eaten in a moon.'Keteph listens to you explain the harsh reactions of the workers in Rakhatâb. He then nods his head.

'I thought the same when I took a bite after you left. How you northerners use this bread as a means of sustenance is a wonder. It has no taste. Still, I think that I can make a marriage of northern heartiness and the delicacies of Umbar work well together.'Keteph, again, assembles his new recipe into sacks to deliver to others for testing. This time, he hopes the dish will meet the needs of the aristocrats who enjoy his creations.Keteph asked that you take his deliveries to the scholars and artisans keeping busy at the expedition camp to the south-east of Umbar Baharbêl. Most are employees of the aristocrats who will be the final arbiters of his latest creation.You received nothing but goodwill and words of encouragement from the denizens of the expedition camp. It appears that Keteph's recipe is complete. Return to him at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.'As I was assembling the recipe, the pleasing aroma of all the ingredients married in complete harmony. I am certain this is the fare I should deliver to the Epicureans of Umbar. Alas, I cannot be the sole determinant.

'${PLAYER}, I again ask you to aid me in determining if the dish is complete.
 
'To the south-east of the city proper, there is an encampment of scholars, adventurers, and hunters. They are representative of the many wealthy patrons in the city.

'Deliver this latest dish to them and return to me with their thoughts on the recipe.'He listens intently, as you speak. When you finish explaining the responses, he nods and claps his hands.

'It is as I expected. Very good. I took the liberty of preparing the final version of the dish while you were abroad. One final step now.''Make your way to the hunter's expedition south-east out of Umbar. Deliver my new dish and return to me with the responses.'Zerkho unwraps the satchel and sniffs the contents. He takes a moment.

'Aromatic.'

He bites into the bread and crab. He chews and swallows.

'This is exquisite. The crab is tender and moist. The bread is firm enough to hold the thinly sliced vegetables and saffron aioli. I have not eaten anything this delicious in some time.'Dorshet unwraps your delivery and lifts the bread from the top.

'It looks much like our wraps, only the bread is leavened and filled on the bottom.'

She covers the crab and aioli and takes a bite. A smile spreads as she chews.

'This is a very enjoyable dish. I am very pleased that you shared this with me.'Karbah looks at Keteph's new dish.

'It looks different than anything I have eaten before.'

She takes the food up and takes a small bite. She chews and smiles. She then takes a larger bite.

'This is very good. I am pleased. I shall enjoy this as I finish it. Thank you for sharing.'Mallax looks the item over.

'It appears plain. Nothing like the lavish dishes my patron is fond of consuming, but the aromatics are good.'

He takes the food up and bites into it. A glimmer of joy passes through his eyes.

'I am mistaken. This is a dish worthy of my patron and many others in Umbar. Thank you.'Delona looks the food over and takes a bite. She smiles as she places it back down.

'I could tell just by the weight and the smell that this would be delicious. It does not disappoint.

'The flavours are complex and balanced. The crunch of the vegetables and the succulence of the crab are perfect.

'This is a masterpiece.'Keteph is displeased with the look of the dish, thinking it is very bland. He asks that you get two vegetables: carrots and cabbages, so that he might mix his aioli with them to make a vibrant and flavourful topping for his new dish.Keteph asked you to find cabbages and carrots for his new dish. Apprentice farmers can grow carrots, and journeyman farmers can grow cabbages. Trade with a farmer or visit the auction house. Or, if you are lucky and patient, search the land for wild cabbages and carrots.Collect cabbages (${NUMBER}/5)Collect fresh carrots (${NUMBER}/5)Return the fresh carrots and cabbages to Keteph at Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.Keteph examines his newest creation.

'Oh, hello again, ${PLAYER}.

'I am just... not ready to share this with anyone. It looks bland. Very bland. Nothing leaps out to visually inspire the diner to reach for this dish. It needs colour and a crunch. It needs an earthen flavour to go along with the crab from the sea.'

He ponders.

'Cabbage and carrots! The green and orange will blend well, and I will add a saffron aioli to create a delectable dressing!

'Can you get me the cabbages and carrots, my friend?''Cabbages and carrots are both crunchy earthen vegetables with brilliant colours. Together, they will further enhance this dish. Please find a way to get me these fresh ingredients as quickly as you can.''Yes, these will do very nicely.'

He slices the vegetables up swiftly and mixes them with an aromatic liquid mixture.

'The colour pierces. This is an acceptable addition to the dish. Just one more moment, please.'Keteph's latest recipe is complete. He asks for your assistance one last time to deliver his creation to the Kindred at Dâr Laja.Keteph's latest recipe is complete. He asks for your assistance one last time to deliver his creation to the Kindred at Dâr Laja. Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall, is north of Swain's Guild-hall near the central crossroads of Umbar Baharbêl.The Kindred all seemed to enjoy the dish. You should return to Keteph and inform him of his success.'My friend, it is time you reveal my new creation to the true aristocracy, the Kindred of the Coin.

'Recently, they have taken residence in Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall. Please, take these four plates to them and share my latest creation.''You will find the Kindred holding open discussion and interviews at Dâr Laja. Please, take my dish to them. I desire to know what they think of my efforts.'Belondor looks the dish over.

'If it is crab, then it is from Keteph. If it is from Keteph, then it will be good. I will partake at a later time. But, I thank you and him for delivering this to me.'Harmelak smiles at you genuinely.

'A gift for me? How kind. It appears to be the latest dish from Keteph. That young man is quite the cook. All his dishes bring joy to the masses, not just the leaders of our fine city.

'Who would think that a poor cook from Jax Phanâl would rise so quickly through the ranks of our cook's guild? And yet....'

She smells the dish and then places it down nearby.

'Please give Keteph my thanks for this delivery. I shall enjoy it at my earliest convenience.'Khôltekh takes the plate and takes a hearty bite.

'I had heard a new dish would arrive from the famed cook, Keteph. Now, here it is.'

He smiles broadly.

'Let me tell you, friend. It does not disappoint. It is an achievement to satiate dwarf hunger as well as Keteph does. Please, when you return to him, give him my compliments.'Rothog looks at you and then looks at the dish. He smirks and pops the food into his mouth. He chews and swallows, and a broad smile crosses his face.

'Tell the cook that this is his best yet. In fact, tell him that I want to order this for my next feast with the gladiators. They will appreciate the flavours he uses here.

'I know not where the bread is from, but the tangy bits within it are truly delicious.'The Kindred all seemed to enjoy the dish. You should return to Keteph and inform him of his success.

'This pleased me greatly, ${PLAYER}.'

Keteph looks relieved.

'This will tide the aristocrats over for some time. The taste will grow stale. They will ask for something more and something fresh. I must continue to seek new ingredients or preparations to sate the never-ending desires of these epicureans.'

He sighs.

'For now, please take this. You have earned this and should feel free to share in my successes.'Keteph asks for your assistance in creating a dish that satisfies the desires of the Epicurean elite in Umbar. He desires a sturdy bread to support his latest creation.Acquire five loaves of barley bread from cooks through trade or auction and return them to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl. Apprentice cooks can bake <rgb=#00FF00>Barley Bread</rgb>.Collect five loaves of <rgb=#00FF00>Barley Bread</rgb> (${NUMBER}/5)Acquire five loaves of barley bread from cooks through trade or auction and return them to Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl. Apprentice cooks can bake barley bread.'Tastes in Umbar are fickle. The aristocracy constantly strives to find something new to tempt their stomachs and tantalize their desires.

'The source of the new flavour typically does not matter. My crab dishes, for example, were a mere play on traditional fare long-served in my hometown of Jax Phanâl.

'I have been thinking. In the north, you have leavened bread. Leavened bread is a treat we do not often see. Yet, I desire to use a taste of the northlands and the standard fare of my home to create a delicacy that will sate the desires of the epicurean elite in Umbar.

'I require bread from the north. I am told there is a grain growing wild and on farms those from the north call barley. We shall begin there. I will require five loaves of barley bread.

'Will you assist me?''Most excellent, my friend.'

He sniffs the bread and makes a face.

'Hmm, I expected something... more. This has almost no discernable scent. No matter, it is a taste of the north. Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.'

He beams brightly.Keteph asked you to further assist him in crafting a special new dish. He needs you to return to Jax Phanâl to retrieve his cruet.Return to Jax Phânal and speak with Phâredar to retrieve Keteph's family cruet.Collect Keteph's family cruet from Phâredar in Jax PhanâlPhâredar told you that Keteph's family cruet was stolen in a raid by goblins. She suggested that you go to the encampment in the south-east to acquire the cruet from the goblins.Collect Keteph's family cruetYou recovered Keteph's family cruet from the goblins. Return the cruet to him at Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.'I am very close to presenting this new recipe to the aristocracy, my friend. However, I require a reminder from home to ensure that the recipe ends with the desired result.

'I left Jax Phânal in such a hurry I forgot to take my grandmother's cruet. It is a precious family heirloom. While I have the one I crafted here, I would prefer to pay homage to my grandmother and use the family cruet for this recipe.

'Return to Phâredar in Jax Phânal. She will know where it is.''Return to Jax Phanâl and collect my family's cruet from Phâredar. She will know where to find it. When you have it, return it to me here.''Keteph's cruet, you say?'

She looks uncomfortable for a moment.

'That will be an issue. When Keteph went silent those weeks ago, I thought this would not matter. Now, it seems it does.

'As you know, Jax Phânal endures harassment by the goblins in the south-east. When their leader Shakfût was imprisoned, they raided the outpost under cover of night and stole many treasures.'

She sighs.

'Keteph's cruet was amongst the stolen items. You will need to visit their encampment and collect the cruet from whichever goblin carries it now.''The raiding goblins have an encampment far to the south and east of Jax Phanâl in the shadow of the mountains. You will likely find the cruet on one of the tougher goblins in that encampment.''Oh-ho! You are a dear associate, ${PLAYER}.

'This cruet has been in my family for generations. My grandmother claims it was hers. My father told me it was in our family long before. Losing this would have been a tragedy I could not endure.

'Let me have a moment, yes?'Defeat many insects in Ambarûl.Defeat many insects in Ambarûl.Defeat many insects in AmbarûlDefeat a great many insects in Ambarûl.Defeat many insects in Ambarûl.Defeat a great many insects in Ambarûl.Defeat a great many insects in AmbarûlYou must quickly ascend the tower of Kûr Anzar. Okhíso must not escape what justice demands.Go with Mizâdi up the tower stairs to confront Okhíso.Speak with Mizâdi to continue your ascent through the towerGo with Mizâdi up the tower stairs to confront Okhíso.Alert Mizâdi you are prepared to continueGo with Mizâdi up the tower stairs to confront Okhíso.Tell Mizâdi you are prepared to move forwardFinish your ascent and enter the tower room to confront Okhiso.Assist Mizâdi with her confrontation with OkhísoListen to Mizâdi and Okhíso.Listen to Mizâdi and OkhísoDefeat Okhíso's guards and archers.Defeat Okhíso and his guardsListen to Okhíso's dying words.Listen to Okhíso's dying wordsSpeak with Mizâdi in the tower.Speak with Mizâdi in the tower'Our ascent will not be without conflict. Stay close and we will reach Okhíso and bring the dog low.''Gird yourself, ${PLAYER}, Okhíso will now pay by my hand.''Come, ${PLAYER}, let us press our advantage and bring the fight to Okhíso!''We draw close to apex of the tower. Prepare yourself, ${PLAYER}, this scorpion will sting if we allow him the opportunity.''There will be time for talk later. We must get outside, and quickly. We must save Kûr Anzar and her people!'Okhíso, seeking to divert your attention, has set Kûr Anzar aflame. That was not enough to stay Mizâdi's blade but now the city needs to be saved. You must put out the fires and rescue trapped citizens in Kûr Anzar.Put out straw fires and rescue trapped citizens in Kûr Anzar.Put out straw fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Tend to wounded Kûr Anzar citizens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat All-seeing cultists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Meet Mizâdi back at the tower of Kûr Anzar.Meet Mizâdi back at the tower of Kûr AnzarGirhâzi has an idea for how to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of the lost archive, and she needs your help.Girhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh. You should talk to her.Talk to GirhâziGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.Listen to the conversationGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> at Khûldim UmûnGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.Listen to the conversationGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.<rgb=#00FF00>Flex</rgb> at Khûldim UmûnGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.Listen to the conversationGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.<rgb=#00FF00>Pose</rgb> for Khûldim UmûnGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.Talk to GirhâziGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.Listen to the conversationGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.<rgb=#00FF00>Challenge</rgb> Khûldim Umûn to trial by combatGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.Listen to Khûldim UmûnGirhâzi has a plan to get Khûldim Umûn to divulge the location of Dubarâkh, and has asked you to go along with whatever she is saying.<rgb=#00FF00>Clap</rgb> for Khûldim Umûn's decisionGirhâzi grins at you.

'Come, ${PLAYER}, we are done here for now.''Remember, just go along along with whatever I am saying.'Girhâzi signals that she wants to talk to you, but makes no effort to keep her words unheard by Khûldim Umûn.

'I was planning on ransoming him and sending him back to his family once we learned where the archive is, but if he is not going to tell us, what do you think of giving the people of Ambarûl what they want? Public executions are so distasteful though. We could even make it a fair fight, you against him. It would end the same.'Amalíbi arranges an opportunity to intercept the captain who sent the letter home as he escorts his men north toward the Wrackwade. You must intercept them and confront the captain.Sigénik awaits you near the gate north of Jirush.Speak with SigénikMake your way to the gate and await the arrival of Bosóta Dôlo.Enter the way-station and defeat Bosóta Dôlo and his escort. Engage them, defeat them, and then confront the captain.Speak with the captain after the battleBosóta Dôlo yielded. You should return to Sigénik with the information he provided.Speak with Sigénik north of the gateYou hand the captain the letter you retrieved from the courier.

'You killed the courier and our men, and you translated my letter. That was personal.'

He stifles a sob.

'I do not wish to die in this forsaken land. Spare my life so I can return to my partner in the south. Our leaders act without orders. They are independent warlords on the precipice of revolt.

'Jombahok, the commander in the north, exiled my commander Khârdu and separated us. Khârdu wants what I do, to leave this land and return home.

'If you can drive a further wedge between Khârdu and Jombahok, they will devolve into open warfare.

'I swear this on my life and the life of my love.''If this is true, we will get the further information we need from this man. Return to Ghalbûru and speak with Amalíbi. I will inform her what I learn.''Bosóta Dôlo, a captain of the Ordâkhai, will arrive at the small way-point to the south. Stay hidden by the gate and await his arrival. Then confront him with the information we gained from the envoy.'You must move quickly into Angar Aragín to save Numûru!Speak with Razâl inside the Angar Aragín.Speak with Razâl inside the Angar AragínGo with Razâl up the tower stairs to find Numûru and defeat All-seeing cultists.Go with Razâl up the tower stairs to find NumûruFolllow Razâl and defeat All-seeing cultists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#ff0000>Razâl must not falter</rgb>Free Numûru from his bonds.Free Numûru from his bondsSpeak with Numûru in the Angar Aragín.Speak with Numûru in the Angar AragínSpeak with Razâl in the Angar Aragín.Speak with RazâlAscend the stairs and defeat the Barkhûshim guarding the other prisoners.Ascend the stairs and defeat the Barkhûshim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the other prisoners.Find the other prisonersFree the prisoners.Free the first prisonerFree the second prisonerFree the third prisonerDefeat Karâshna Zíri.Defeat Karâshna Zíri'There's no telling what we may find here. I believe they bring the sacrifices upstairs to one of their dark altars. That is likely where we'll find Numûru and any other unfortunates they've gathered.''My thanks. The Barkhûshim seem to have an unhealthy appreciation for my blood. It does wonders for me. I think it would not work nearly so well for their dark lord, but they would hear none of it.

'They stuck me several times. It's fortunate you came when you did, or there would be precious little left of me to collect.

'I can manage my way out of here - there are others trapped above us. Please help them escape as well.''He is wounded. I will get him out of Kûr Anzar, leave it to me. Free those poor souls above us, they need your aid most now. Then meet us back in Urmâkh.'A small moment of peace has given Mizâdi time to speak with Amalíbi, to see the consequences of her decisions.Enter Amalíbi's encampment near Iridír.Enter Amalíbi's encampment near IridírListen to Mizâdi and Amalíbi's conversation.Listen to Mizâdi and Amalíbi's conversationSpeak with several of the wounded soldiers in Amalíbi's camp and ask if they require aid.Speak with Zagêli in Amalíbi's campSpeak with Gúrumkir in Amalíbi's campSpeak with Jínsa in Amalíbi's campHelp Amalíbi's wounded with their various needs.Gather fresh bandages for ZagêliFind a bottle of Khôrob for GúrumkirGive the fresh bandages to Zagêli and the Khôrob to Gúrumkir in Amalíbi's camp.Ask to hear Jínsa's storyListen to Jínsa's storyComfort Jínsa in Amalíbi's encampment.Comfort Jínsa in Amalíbi's encampmentLet Mizâdi know you have helped the wounded.Let Mizâdi know you have helped the woundedListen to Mizâdi and Amalíbi's conversation.Listen to Mizâdi and Amalíbi's conversationSpeak with Mizâdi in Amalíbi's camp.Speak with Mizâdi in Amalíbi's camp'Ah, it's good of you to ask. It's not much, but these bandages have frayed, and they are more dirt than cloth at the moment.

'Would you see if there are any fresh ones among the quartermaster's things? Nothing worse for the spirit than soggy dressings.''Oho, you've come to help us, have you? Aid us in our time of need? Well I have great need of you then, friend. Great need.

'The Umûn says I can't have any Khôrob. I know, it is a tragedy. Usually I'd just swipe it as soon as her back was turned, but with this bum leg, it makes any petty thievery a terrible bother. She thinks it makes for bad soldiers. I say it makes for the best soldiers. Or at least the happiest.

'What do you say? Can you make a bottle of Khôrob appear in these old hands?''You're helping those in the camp? That is very nice of you. I don't need much, I have a warm bedroll and enough bread to get by.

'Maybe I could tell you my story? These words in my head seem to weigh heavily on me, pressing me down. Unless you don't want to hear it?''I meant what I said. I will see these people restored to their homes. I will see them made whole.'

Mizâdi pauses, and her breath becomes hushed.

'I swear it.''Thank you. I can dress the wound myself. It's the little things that make the days a bit more manageable, don't you think?''Oho, you really did it! Yes, that's the stuff. Don't worry, the Khôrob belongs to all of us in the company, there's no actual thievery. I'd say you've done a great job here. This soldier will be very happy for the rest of the afternoon.''It is nice of you to ask. Very well, I will tell you of the attack that caused all this.''Thank you for hearing my story, friend. It helps.'The time has come for you and your companions to confront the Thardúth at Utug-bûr.Mithrandir and your companions prepare to confront the Thardúth.Talk to Mithrandir in front of the waterfallServants of the Thardúth await you at Utug-bûr.Confront Azagath in front of Utug-bûrAzagath Sea-shadow has suggested that his former allies among the Kindred of the Coins join his new cause.Talk to RothogTalk to KhôltekhYour companions stand opposed to Azagath Sea-shadow and the Thardúth he now serves.Remain on guard during the confrontation with AzagathYour companions stand opposed to Azagath Sea-shadow and the Thardúth he now serves.Remain on guard during the confrontation with Azagath'Steel your resolve, ${PLAYER}. We know not the precise nature of the evil we go to face... but we will face it all the same.''We have found our quarry, ${PLAYER}. The journey that brought us from Umbar Baharbêl as allies is at its end. We have found Azagath.

'But it seems someone else found him first.'Khôltekh glances at you briefly but says nothing. All of his attention is fastened upon Azagath.Raphûz wants to thank you for your aid and again invites you to sit with him for a discussion and a smoke.Raphûz is waiting for you to speak with him.Approach Raphûz's fireRaphûz made his way to the fireside and invited you to sit.<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> with RaphûzListen to Rapûz's storyRaphûz invited you to partake in his smoking device. Perhaps you should smoke your own pipe.Share a <rgb=#00FF00>smoke</rgb> with RaphûzWait for the conversation to endRaphûz finished his statement with a hearty laugh. You should laugh with him.<rgb=#00FF00>Laugh</rgb> with RaphûzWait for the conversation to endA woman emerged from the shadows. She speaks with confidence and asks why so many from the north travel into Shagâna.<rgb=#00FF00>Talk</rgb> with the woman and tell her why you are hereWait for the conversation to endThe woman introduced herself as Ashâmi. She asked for the deer. Raphûz appears stunned see if you can make him respond.Clear your throat to prompt Raphûz to respond with <rgb=#00FF00>/ahem</rgb>Wait for Ashâmi to take her leaveAshâmi left the fireside with the deer in tow. Raphûz watches her recede into the night.Speak with Raphûz to get his reaction'I do not understand. What did she mean, my friend? Ah, the hour is late. I should sleep. Thank you for lending your ear again.'Over tea and a smoke, Raphûz tells you why he joined the Tale-wardens and recalls the story of his family.Join Raphûz by the fire.Join Raphûz by the fireRaphûz offers a seat by the fire.<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> with Raphûz by the fireContinue conversing with Raphûz.Tell Raphûz you do not think him a fool with <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>Raphûz suggested you share his tobacco.Smoke with Raphûz's deviceYou used Raphûz's hookah, but the experience is different than smoking with your pipe.<rgb=#00FF00>Cough</rgb> at Raphûz, alerting him to your difficulty with his deviceYou continue listening to Raphûz's story. You should share a smoke with him using your pipe.<rgb=#00FF00>Smoke</rgb> with RaphûzThe evening grows long. Perhaps it is time to retire.Conclude your discussion with Raphûz<rgb=#00FF00>Bow</rgb> to Raphûz and take your leaveBefore moving to his new post in Khûd Zagin, Raphûz again asks you to join him for dinner and a smoke to continue your discussions.Raphûz waits for you by the fireside.Join Raphûz by the fireRaphûz invites you to sit and enjoy the warmth of the fire and share stories.<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> with Raphûz by the firesideRaphûz compliments you on your generosity and then pauses to smoke.Share a <rgb=#00FF00>smoke</rgb> with RaphûzRaphûz confessed to requesting a move to Khûd Zagin in hopes he would see Ashâmai again.Continue to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> to RaphûzYou are concerned about Raphûz and his pursuit of Ashâmi.Talk to RaphûzRaphûz seems to understand and have his mind in the right place.Nod <rgb=#00FF00>/yes</rgb> to Raphûz to acknowledge his wordsYou tell Raphûz he should take caution to not press the woman. She may not return his affection.

'I am aware, my friend.

'I only wish to make my case and prove my value to her. I am not fool enough to think I can change her mind should she reject me.'Balakhâd has agreed to tell you what befell him after he fled from Jirush and hid within the tombs of Nirgambâr.Balakhâd has more to tell you.Talk to BalakhâdListen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.Listen to Balakhâd's accountBalakhâd has more to tell you.Talk to BalakhâdListen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.Listen to Balakhâd's accountBalakhâd has more to tell you.Talk to BalakhâdListen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.Listen to Balakhâd's accountBalakhâd has more to tell you.Talk to BalakhâdListen to Balakhâd's account of his encounter with Azagath and Nakási within Nirgambâr.Listen to Balakhâd's account'Memories of my frightening escape from Jirush flashed before my eyes: the Ordâkhai barring Azagath's approach to my cell, the intruder raising his arms, the soldiers falling to the floor as his dark sorcery stole the very life from their bodies.

'I knew he would follow me, but I sought to get as far from his dreadful presence as I could.''Even through the haze of my fear, one thing was clear to me: Azagath and Nakási might have possessed a shared purpose, but their tolerance for each other began already to wear thin. Whatever they hoped to accomplish, every day that passed wore upon their alliance.

'In my desperation I hoped to take advantage of their eroding trust for each other, but I could think of no effective means of accomplishing it.''Nakási removed from her garment a small glass phial containing an oily substance that glittered even in the dim light of the chamber. I knew it for its terrible reputation: Narghâk, the Hungry Fire, longest-burning and deadliest of the alchemic weapons ever used in war throughout Shagâna and in Umbar.

'My father searched for stores of Narghâk that might have evaded destruction over the centuries, but he never found any. The last sages who knew the secret of its making were put to the sword a hundred years ago.

'Even so small a quantity of Narghâk as Nakási possessed has not been seen in Umbar for many years. I believed the Hungry Fire had left the world.''Even through the haze of my fear, the realization dawned upon me: not only do Azagath and Nakási not trust each other, every member of their ruling Kindred fears and distrusts the others.

'I did not believe I would live long enough to take advantage of this knowledge, but it brought to me a calm I never thought to feel again. The Kindred of the Coins that displaced the Heirs of Castamir will not much longer survive to rule Umbar. The seeds of their undoing are already planted, and they have done it themselves.

'The knowledge brought me peace, even as my new captors discussed the manner of my death.'Members of the Kindred of the Coins take petitions from nobles throughout Umbar. Rothog has summoned you to his chambers to hear one specific complaint.Rothog has summoned you to his chambers to hear a specific complaint from one of his nobles regarding one of the gladiators.Talk to RothogApproach Zarzíra Dawn-star to begin her petition.Speak to Zarzíra and witness the proceedingsSpeak to Rothog regarding Zarzíra Dawn-star's petitionSpeak to Rothog the Storm'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER} for witnessing the petition. Let us leave these chambers and return to Dâr Laja.''Let us see what she is to say regarding this situation. It should be most interesting.

'Tell her she may begin.''I am not sure why I must address this petition with the likes of you, but if I must, I will begin.''These accusations are most troubling. While I do not doubt that these incidents have transpired, I do feel that she may not be telling us everything. It would be good to investigate this further.

'Would you be willing to do so?'In order to prove their mettle Raphûz and Ashâmi were tasked by Numûru to prove their abilities while confronting their fears. Ashâmi must face a fearsome serval in Imhûlar.Ashâmi appears a bit shaken as she looks over the woods. You, too, have an uneasy feeling in these woods.Speak with Ashâmi to begin the huntThere has been no sign of the serval Numûru described to Ashâmi. The woods are eerily still and quiet.Speak with Ashâmi to continue the hunt for KanagirAshâmi stopped her search and looked back into the woods. Something still feels off.Speak with Ashâmi to continue the hunt for KanagirAshâmi looks shaken, but resolute. The serval pack attacked without warning. The serval Kanagir, as described, was not among them. You feel like you are being stalked.Speak with Ashâmi about how to proceedKanagir proved a true hunter. You and Ashâmi survived and should discuss a return to Urmâkh.Speak with Ashâmi'${PLAYER}, Raphûz speaks highly of your skill and how you helped him along his path to find me and his fate. I have seen how capable you are when you helped me with the Alad.

'Still, something here makes me uneasy. Do you feel it too?'

She breathes in deeply and sighs.

'Perhaps I should be more eager, like Raphûz. Come, let us hunt this creature.''Something is not right. Can you feel it?'

She looks around, listening intently and peering into the woods.

'If Raphûz were here, he would say, 'Is this another Shagâni superstition?''

She chuckles softly.

'I find his questions very amusing. He does not understand how much our superstitions kept us safe in the darkest of times. Our lives coming together as they have does seem to be something different.

'I never expected -'

She stops and points.

'Look, there. Let's go.'She scans the woods and speaks softly.

'I kissed him. It was spontaneous, something I never expected do.

'I have not often allowed anyone to get close to me.

'My mother's disposition, love of life, and attitude of defiance in the face of great oppression shaped me. I am who am I because of her. Her marriage to my father was arranged. I never understood how she came to care for him.

'But, Raphûz,-'

She stops, alerted to a sound.

'What was that?''We are not the hunters here, ${PLAYER}. This serval is cunning beyond normal measure. We must be cautious.

'We will not become prey.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}.

'You're a capable warrior. Raphûz is a good judge of character.'

She manages a smile.

'I confess, while we were fighting just now, I was thinking of how I must survive so I can return to him. It is a strange feeling to me. One with which I am not entirely comfortable.

'I am glad we had time to travel together. I understand why he sees you as such a trusted companion. Let us return to Urmâkh.'Nauriel has not forgotten the injuries done to her family by the Kindred of the Coins, and she wants to pursue Azagath and his fleeing allies as they attempt to escape the Citadel of Winds.Nauriel is within the great hall of the Citadel of Winds, ready to pursue Azagath and his allies.Talk to Nauriel in the Citadel of WindsUshu wants to speak to you in the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Ushu in the Citadel of WindsUshu has agreed to show you and Nauriel the passage through which Azagath and his allies fled.Follow Ushu and EnâtNauriel desires to chase after Azagath and his allies as they flee deeper into the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Nauriel in the Citadel of WindsNauriel desires to chase after Azagath and his allies as they flee deeper into the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Nauriel in the Citadel of WindsNauriel desires to chase after Azagath and his allies as they flee deeper into the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Nauriel in the Citadel of WindsNauriel is waiting to speak with you within the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Nauriel in the Citadel of WindsAzagath and his allies fled outside the Citadel of Winds by making use of the door at the bottom of the stairs.Follow Azagath's trail through the door and outside the Citadel of WindsNauriel has come with you outside the Citadel of Winds in pursuit of Azagath.Talk to Nauriel outside the Citadel of WindsAzagath and his allies have escaped from the island on which stands the Citadel of Winds.Follow Nauriel to the docks outside the Citadel of WindsThe nearby dock-worker may know where Azagath and his allies fled.Talk to the observant dock-worker outside the Citadel of Winds'For now they have escaped us, but not for long.''The guardsmen are in disarray. They speak of two groups: those loyal to Azagath and those who now question him. We should remain alert for the first, and learn what information we can from the second.'

Nauriel turns her gaze to the great hall, lingering briefly on the fountain in its centre.

'I wish you had waited for me to accompany you before you came here the first time, ${PLAYER}. Had you done so, we would not now need to make this venture... for Azagath's head would already be shorn from his body and I would be half of the way back to Pinnath Gelin!

'But what is done is done, and that undone remains undone. Let us speak to these women and learn if they support Azagath or oppose him.''When we aided you we did not think you intended to bring Gondorian sorcery to bear against the Kindred! We fled when the Corsair made your presence known to Azagath, but from the far side of the hall we witnessed the terrible creatures as they rose from the fountain. Where have they now gone? Do you plan to unleash them upon the city?'

You assure Ushu that the Five Sisters would not have harmed either her or her friends in any way, and now that Thorongil has been rescued they will not trouble the folk of the city. She considers your words.

'That is a comfort, but something yet confuses me. If these water-spirits answered to the call of Gondor, why were they dressed in Umbari garb? To my eye they were dressed as nobles of the city, and Enât told me the same.'

You tell Ushu that the Five Sisters did not appear that way to you, and she furrows her brow but does not seem surprised.

'For one thing to appear many ways is not unusual in these times. The Kindred of the Coins seemed to be one thing to us, and yet Azagath's words of late have cast another light upon it, a light fell and sickly.''Are you prepared, ${PLAYER}? We will likely face opposition from those still loyal to Azagath, and they will seek to keep us from reaching their master and his allies in the Kindred.

'Once we pass through this door, we must let none keep us from finding the treacherous leader of the Kindred of the Coins! Others of your crew will follow behind to keep Azagath from circling around us and escaping. Now let us fight!''The corridor to the south-east descends a long flight of stairs. Azagath and his allies must have gone that way!''Those warriors were guarding the north-east corridor, ${PLAYER}. That must be the way Azagath, Nakási, and Belondor fled.

'It is curious, but I see no one guarding the passage. Still, we must remain alert!''I do not have a good feeling about this. That door leads outside!

'${PLAYER}, we must hurry. We cannot allow Azagath to escape us!''No... no...

'This cannot be! Azagath and his allies cannot have escaped us!''I beg you! Have mercy upon me and my fellows! We had no choice! Nakási Wave-reaper threatened to skin us alive if we did not help them cast off with utmost haste! There was a terrible light in her eyes, and I think she would have done it!

'Belondor's crew is fiercely loyal, and they manned the oars without argument. Even when Azagath told them their destination, they did not balk at it as I would have done!'

You ask the dock-worker where the leaders of the Kindred intended to row, and he shudders.

'Across the water, stranger. They made for the Temple of the All-Seeing. They made for the Mâkhda Khorbo.'Mizâdi has tracked Bârshud to the fortress of Dun Shûma in Khûd Zagin. The time has come to meet Bârshud in pitched battle and defeat him for good.Speak with Mizâdi on the battlefield outside Dun Shûma.Speak with Mizâdi on the battlefield outside Dun ShûmaDefeat Ekhamati forces and destroy Ekhamâti tar pots as you move toward the hilltop.Defeat Ekhamâti at Dun Shûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy tar pots on the battlefield (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Take the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces.Take the hilltop from Ekhamâti forcesDefend the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces until reinforcements arrive!Defend the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces until reinforcements arrive<rgb=#ff0000>Mizâdi must not falter</rgb>Speak with Mizâdi in Khûd Zagin on the hilltop outside of Dun Shûma.Speak with Mizâdi on the hilltop outside of Dun ShûmaSet up camp on the hilltop outside of Khud Zagin.Set up barricades around the hilltop encampment.Set up barricades around the hilltop encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Now is the time for us to charge into battle and end the threat of Bârshud! Meet me on the hilltop!''Now that this hilltop has been won in hard-fought battle, we need to make our camp here and fortify it. Can you help set up the tents, tables and barricades we'll need to make this camp safe for everyone?'Push into Dun Shûma and end the threat of Bârshud!Make your way down the hilltop and toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi.Make your way toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with MizâdiMake your way toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi.Make your way toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with MizâdiDefeat Ekhamâti forces and treat the wounded Subuzûri at Dun Shûma.Defeat Ekhamâti forces at Dun Shûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Treat the wounded Subuzûri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#ff0000>Mizâdi must not falter</rgb>Enter the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma.Enter the inner courtyard of Dun ShûmaDefeat the Ekhamâti forces!Defeat the Ekhamâti forces<rgb=#ff0000>Mizâdi must not falter</rgb>Listen to Mizâdi and Bârshud II.Listen to Mizâdi and Bârshud IIDefeat the Mûmak!Defeat the MûmakSpeak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma.Speak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma'Bârshud has escaped! No! He was right here, and he slipped through my grasp!

'At least that monster was defeated. Thank you for that. I know not how many Subuzûri would have fallen had you not been here to slay the beast.'Fight with Galâmka to retake the stronghold of Maurûsh from the Orcs.Enter into the passage from Ub Nishir to begin the attack on the Orcs in Maurûsh.Enter the passage from Ub NishirFollow Galâmka through the passage to reach Maurûsh.Follow Galâmka through the passageOrcs have ambushed you inside the passage to Maurûsh. Defeat them!Defeat the OrcsYou have defeated the Orc ambush. Follow Galâmka as he leads you through the passage to Maurûsh.Follow Galâmka through the passageMore Orcs have spotted you and want to prevent you from reaching Maurûsh. Defeat them and continue the fight.Defeat the OrcsContinue following Galâmka through the passage to get to the stronghold of Maurûsh.Continue through the passageYou have arrived at the entrance into Maurûsh. Speak with Galâmka when you are ready to continue the fight.Speak with GalâmkaProceed out of the passage and into the stronghold of Maurûsh to continue the battle.Exit the passage into the stronghold of MaurûshThe fight in Maurûsh continues. You must push your way up the stairs to bring the battle to the leader of the Orcs.Defeat the Orcs guarding the stairsReconvene with Galamka at the top of the stairs in the stronghold of Maurûsh to bring the fight to the leader of the Orcs here.Reconvene with Galamka at the top of the stairsYou have made it to Râkdakul, the Utûgi who is leading the Orcs here in Maurûsh. He must be stopped so the stronghold can be reclaimed.Defeat Râkdakul and reclaim MaurûshRâkdakul and the Orcs proved too powerful. Escape Maurûsh back into the mountain passage!Escape Maurûsh back to the mountain passageRâkdakul and the Orcs proved too powerful. Escape Maurûsh back into the mountain passage!Escape Maurûsh back to the mountain passageGalâmka takes a moment to catch his breath.

'I did not expect the Orcs to have overrun this passage. No matter, we must press on.

'This is the entrance into Maurûsh. Here is where we will take our stand. Are you ready, friend?'Despite the comfortable accommodations given to you by Girhâzi, your sleep has been disturbed by strange dreams.The hallway outside the tower room in the Citadel of Winds swims from the recesses of your sleeping mind.Talk to Corudan in your dreamThe unnatural flames barring the way into the tower room high within the Citadel of Winds have disappeared, granting you passage.Enter the tower room in your dreamThough he has been dead for months, the image of Balakhôr the Scourge glowers at you from the other side of the tower room.Examine the image of Balakhôr the Scourge conjured by your dreaming mindFamiliar images and voices emerge from your dreaming mind.Listen to familiar voices conjured by your dreaming mindThe tower room in the Citadel of Winds swims from the recesses of your sleeping mind.Talk to Corudan in your dreamYou are gripped with a sense of unreality as an unfamiliar land coalesces before your sleeping eyes.Maintain focus as your dream continuesYou expected your dreaming mind to bring you a vision of the grove of Arwáth, but it is not so. It seems the course of your dream is not so easily-controlled.Examine the image of the Grim Southron conjured by your dreaming mindUnfamiliar images and voices emerge from your dreaming mind, of events you never could have seen.Listen to unfamiliar voices conjured by your dreaming mindYour dreaming mind conjures unusual images before you, with familiar voices emerging from unexpected places.Examine the scorpion conjured by your dreaming mindAn image from the darkest corner of the Morgul Vale swims from the recesses of your mind.Maintain focus as your dream continuesIn your dream the Wizard Mithrandir stands before an unpleasant statue in the Valley of the Secret Shadow.Examine the image of Mithrandir conjured by your dreaming mindThe dream feels so real to you.Witness the strange images conjured by your dreaming mindThuringwath swims hazily before your dreaming eyes.Talk to Mithrandir in your dream'${PLAYER}! Have you seen Sigileth? I have been calling for her ever since she came this way, but she has not responded!

'She will not turn back from this course!'Balakhôr appears as you remember him.

Months ago, before the end of the War of the Ring, the leader of the Heirs of Castamir stood on the deck of the Night-jewel, defying Aragorn and the Army of the Dead in what proved to be his final moments.'Where might Sigileth have gone, ${PLAYER}? She spoke of wishing to meet the Kinta Elves. Do you think she has gone to see Shanthar, the Elf-warden of Arwáth?'Somehow, your unconscious mind knows this wraith to be the Nazgûl known in the annals of Gondor as the Grim Southron... but he and the others of his kind perished with Sauron.

Is this a vision of the distant past, when the Nazgûl still lived?You suffer a feeling of unreality as Corudan's voice emerges from the body of the scorpion.

'She cautioned us that the creatures possess great reserves of patience,' he says.

'They might lie in wait for hours, hidden from careless observation, and strike without any warning.'Even seen through the haze of unreality conjured by your dreaming mind, you can see lines of care and worry on the Wizard's face. Some great effort has left its mark upon him, and his exhaustion is apparent in every movement.'For many days Megorlam whispered to me from the stone and I came to understand he was a prisoner. I know not the precise reason for which Sauron imprisoned him, though I might make a guess. The chains that bind him within this statue remain unbroken; the Dark Lord must have drawn upon another source to fashion those bonds. They survived his own defeat, to the sorrow of Megorlam.

'My struggle with the captive spirit has revealed this much, Taurdir: he possessed knowledge of some secret that even Sauron knew not. He taunted the Dark Lord with this secret, claiming that this power was beyond Sauron, impossible for even that terrible sorcerer to harness. "This power is beyond all living memory!" he said to Sauron, and great was the Dark Lord's anger. As I strove against Megorlam, he repeated these three words over and over again: "beyond living memory," he cried, "beyond living memory!"

'I believe Megorlam thought to ensnare me with the promise of knowledge, attempting to steal my powers and use them to break from his prison. I proved more capable than he expected, Taurdir, and he has relented in that effort, but I dare not speak to him again lest he overcome my defences.

'But his words trouble me, my Ranger friend. A power beyond Sauron...'Raphûz wants to prove his bravery and face his fear by seeking out the "largest boar in Ambarûl," Urushagân. He asked you to accompany him.Raphûz appears nervous. Speak with his to calm his nerves and begin your search for Urushagân.Calm Raphûz's nerves and begin the huntYou fought alongside Raphûz to the centre of the boar den. He looks as though he could use some reassurance. Speak with him.Speak with Raphûz and continue the huntRaphûz's confidence is building. He believes Urushagân must be further in the boar den.Speak with Raphûz to continue the huntRaphûz is undeterred by not yet finding Urushagân. He urges you to help him press onward.Speak with Raphûz to continue the huntAfter defeating the beast Raphûz wants to speak to you in a safer part of the area.Speak to Raphûz'I will steel my nerve, ${PLAYER}. I must overcome my fear.'

He swallows hard.

'All the same, I am glad you are here with me.''No, no friend. My resolve is stalwart. I only wonder which trail to follow to discover the beast.'

He looks at the paths and then chooses.

'Let us search there, friend.''We will find him yet. I can see another hollow on the rise above. Let us move swiftly.''Is this beast another Shagâni myth?'

He smirks.

'Come, I think there is another hollow above where the beast must be.''My friend, I could not have succeeded without you. I still will not stray so near to a boar that it could gore me without holding a weapon.

'But my fear of the creatures is diminished thanks to you.

'Please visit me in the Wrackwade, where I can thank you more formally.'Eshtali lies in the tombs of Esh-kimâkhi. In the fight to liberate Kûr Anzar, there was scarcely enough time to think, let alone mourn the dead. Now that the immediate threat is over, we mourn our fallen and remind ourselves why they still take such firm residence in our hearts.Join Mizâdi at Eshtali's tomb.Join Mizâdi at Eshtali's tombSpeak with Mizâdi by Eshtali's tomb.Speak with Mizâdi by Eshtali's tombPlace the flowers on Eshtali's tomb.Place the flowers on Eshtali's tomb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Listen to Mizâdi.Listen to MizâdiOffer comfort to Mizâdi.Offer comfort to Mizâdi'Please, place the flowers on the centre of his sarcophagus.''Thank you. Come, we should return to Kûr Anzar before dusk floods Esh-kimâkhi.'Belondor has suggested that Sirgon meet with him at the Hungry Deep Tavern, but it will be best if you and your crew attend the meeting as well... for the safety of all involved.Sirgon waits below the stairs that climb to the Hungry Deep Tavern.Talk to Sirgon below the Hungry Deep TavernYou have agreed to stand by Sirgon with much of your crew while he meets with Belondor.Climb up to the Hungry Deep Tavern with SirgonYou have agreed to stand by Sirgon with much of your crew while he meets with Belondor.Stand by Sirgon while he meets with BelondorBelondor wants to speak with you about the events that transpired beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo.Talk to Belondor at the Hungry Deep TavernYou have agreed to stand by Sirgon with much of your crew while he meets with Belondor.Stand by Sirgon while he meets with BelondorBelondor's wife Mêshka has arrived at the Hungry Deep Tavern, and she is not pleased to see that Sirgon has violated her ban upon returning to the Upper Ward.Talk to Mêshka at the Hungry Deep TavernYou have agreed to stand by Sirgon with much of your crew while he meets with Belondor.Stand by Sirgon while he meets with BelondorSirgon is compelled to speak on behalf of King Elessar.Talk to Sirgon at the Hungry Deep TavernRothog the Storm has questions for Belondor.Remain alert to see what Rothog will doBelondor wishes to speak with you at the Hungry Deep Tavern.Talk to Belondor at the Hungry Deep TavernRothog the Storm has something to say to you.'I appreciate you and the crew of the Wave-hunter agreeing to accompany me to this meeting with Belondor, ${PLAYER}.

'The Hungry Deep, and my fate, awaits me atop these steps.''Beneath the Mâkhda Khorbo he worked cruel magic, tearing the life from dear members of my crew, friends I have known for years. They died trusting me, Sirgon. They trusted I would bring them to safety, and trusted that their families would know they did not die for nothing.

'But Azagath spent their lives for no purpose! Their deaths were needless, and provided only the smallest of delays so the Sea-shadow could make his escape! He did not know those men, and he discarded them without thought... only I am left to suffer the grief of their loss.''I warned your friend Sirgon not to return to the Upper Ward! Does he think he remains out of reach and free from justice?

'Rothog has slain many such men who believed themselves to be untouchable, and for less reason that this. Belondor has not forgotten how easily Sirgon cast aside his long friendship and was rewarded for it! He followed the Steward Denethor's commands, and questioned them not!''I know my words are just words, Belondor, and I have given you little reason to believe them. But I speak this from my heart: King Elessar is a good man, and he desires only what is best for his people and for yours. He wants peace between Gondor and Umbar, and prosperity for both.

'I know this is so. He is not the same as the Steward Denethor. Can the Kindred of the Coins come to see this, if Azagath no longer controls them? Can you, and they, work alongside the kingdom of Gondor, and not against it? Can you join hands with King Elessar, if it means setting aside war and conflict?''I hope we have repaired something of the friendship we once possessed, Sirgon, but I am not ready to say the same of that between Gondor and Umbar. Your King has much to prove to us, for we have heard sweet words before, and were deceived. It will not happen again.

'The Kindred of the Coins will survive without Azagath and Nakási. It was larger than both of them. It is larger than all of us, for it is Umbar. Your King will need to realize that if he believes there can be peace between our lands.''What kind of bird was that?'

You tell Rothog that the bird's name is Gwallang, and he is a Limlinn from across the Bay of Belfalas.

'Gwallang. Limlinn. I have not heard these names before. He is brave for one so small.

'But I came here for two purposes: to fight, and to fetch. I am disappointed there was no fight, but now you will come with me.

'Hármelak wants to see you again.''Gondorians and Umbari are both alike in this: each of them uses too many words.

'I came here for two purposes: to fight, and to fetch. I am disappointed there was no fight, but now you will come with me.

'Hármelak wants to see you again.'Mizâdi, Girhâzi, Rahâzi, Amalíbi, and Numûru have gathered outside Dun Shûma to discuss their victory and what is next for Shagâna.Speak with Mizâdi at Dun Shûma.Speak with Mizâdi at Dun ShûmaListen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.Listen to the conversation between the leadersCheer with Mizâdi!Cheer with MizâdiContinue listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.Continue listening to the conversationContinue listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leadersListen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leadersGather pile of gifts Mizâdi brought.Give gifts to each of the leaders.Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leadersListen to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.Listen to Mizâdi speak to the other leadersBow out of respect to Mizâdi.Bow out of respect to MizâdiFinish listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.Finish listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leadersFinish listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders.Finish listening to the conversation between Mizâdi and the other leaders'Now that we are all gathered here, and the day has been won, I would have words and express my gratitude to each of you.''I am grateful. This axe has a fine balance, and look at that blade! The skulls we shall split with her!''We accept this horn in the spirit in which it is given. If Hamât ever needs our aid, know that we shall remain at the ready to offer our Dumûri to aid her as well.'A real Subuzûri blade! This is quite the weapon! I shall not always use it, but when I do, know that I will think of you. My thanks.''A saddle? Oh I see. Thank you. It has not been easy to come together with everything that has happened these past few weeks, but I thank you for this gift, and accept it in the spirit in which it is offered.'Within the halls of Dahâl Huliz, the gladiators make their home. Rothog has asked that you question Shaidal.Rothog has asked that you travel into the gladiator's residences and question Shaidal regarding the petition.Talk to ShaidalThe sounds of footsteps fill the halls, you are ambushed by attackers.Defeat ambushersSpeak to Shaidal about the attack and what he will need of you.Speak to Shaidal about the attack'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER}. Please tell Rothog of the attack and that I may have access to the evidence that would prove my innocence.

'Please convince him to allow you to look into the matter further, for I fear for my life and that of those whom I hold dear.''You are truly a worthy candidate, ${PLAYER}. I have heard your name whispered within these halls. There is rumour that Rothog has sent you to speak with me regarding an incident, and I would hope you would be willing to assist me.

'I will tell you that I am innocent of the crimes that have damned me to this place. You see, I worked for Zarzíra, and noticed there were some ill deeds happening within the house. I approached the captain of the guards regarding the deeds, and shortly afterwards, I was being accused of the brutal slaying of one of Zarzíra's competitors. I was saved from death by Rothog, only to be sentenced to  fight in the sands of Dahâl Huliz.

'While working for her, it was rumoured in her house that she kept excellent records of her business dealings and her exploits both legal and less than legal.

'While it is true that I did work with someone to recover those records, it was to prove my innocence and free me from here. Not for any other nefarious purpose....

'I think I hear something!''As you can see, Zarzíra has become most desperate. She has even sent her people in an attempt to silence me. I beg of you to speak to Rothog on my behalf, and ask if you could gather proof of my innocence.'Mêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is ready to begin.Mêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is almost ready to begin. You should talk to Mêshka.Talk to MêshkaMêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is ready to begin. You should take a moment to look at the mural.Admire the muralMêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. Everyone is present, and the memorial is beginning.Attend the memorialMêshka has commissioned a mural in memory of the fallen crew of the Rebuke. The families of the deceased mariners have tried to absolve Belondor of his feelings of guilt. Belondor wants to talk to you.Talk to Belondor'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER}. It was difficult to watch, but I think this has done exactly what I had hoped.''Thank you for your assistance with making this all come together, ${PLAYER}. When I first asked for your help, I was unsure of your intentions, or if you would even show. I must tell you though that I am glad you did. Belondor has told me that you have been aiding him, and I am glad for him to have a friend.

'It is my hope that this memorial will help him move past his current unease. He has not been kind to himself. He will not be able to do what he needs to in such a state.'As you approach Belondor, he looks haggard, older than you remember him being and is clearly troubled.

'${PLAYER}, I have a few things to take care of before I leave here, but I would like to speak with you later. Meet me back in Dâr Laja when it's convenient for you.'At the suggestion of Hármelak, the Golden Queen, you have uncovered a means of gaining access to the Citadel of Winds, where Azagath Sea-shadow must be holding Thorongil captive.You should pick up the bowl of sea-water and carry it across the bridge to the island, bringing it past the defences and up the hill into the Citadel of Winds. Do not drop the bowl or spill any of the water!Pick up the bowl of sea-water on the bridge to the Citadel of WindsThe other water-bearers stand to the south-east of the fountain inside the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Water-bearer Ushu south-east of the fountainSeveral members of the Kindred of the Coins guard their captive inside the Citadel of Winds.Eavesdrop upon the conversation of the Kindred of the Coins inside the Citadel of WindsSeveral members of the Kindred of the Coins meet with Jajax inside the Citadel of Winds.Eavesdrop upon the confrontation of the Kindred of the Coins with Jajax and his captiveAzagath has noticed you within the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Azagath Sea-shadow in the Citadel of WindsThe Kindred of the Coins has obtained a new, more valuable hostage: you!Survive the attention of the Kindred of the Coins in the Citadel of WindsThe bubbling fountain in the Citadel of Winds heralds the arrival of an unexpected presence.Witness the confrontationJajax's captive is in the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Jajax's captiveJajax is in the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Jajax in the Citadel of Winds'Now we must wait until we are dismissed. It is best to not attract any attention.

'Remain within these steps with the rest of us, and we will stay beneath the notice of anyone who might take offence at our listening.''I thought something was out of place. I see now that it was you, ${PLAYER}.

'You have come a long distance to be here. It is curious that none of my fellows thought to mention your presence to me. I do not believe you could have escaped Khôltekh's notice, or Hármelak's spies. Perhaps they tire of our continued association? I have experienced such disillusion before; some went willingly to the knife, but only later learned what it meant.

'Do you think to battle me now? Do you think you could best me in my own palace?''The Kindred of the Coins have fled deeper into their citadel, but our purpose is fulfilled, and Thorongil rescued. The power of the Five Sisters frightens Azagath; he was right to flee from them, and his allies beside him.

'And yet Roamingstar and her sisters cannot long remain this far from their homes. They have helped buy us a reprieve, and freedom for the Kindred's hostage, but that is all. If Azagath and his Kindred remain a threat, we cannot rely upon the Five Sisters to face it.''You are lucky I came along when I did, ${PLAYER}, for the Kindred of the Coins were only moments away from discovering you. I deem that I saved you from imprisonment at least, and death at most, and you would do well to reward my friendship with whatever valuables you might have at hand.'

You remind Jajax that the Kindred was quite oblivious to your presence until he called their attention to you, and he waves a dismissive hand.

'Ah, who can remember now? The important thing is that great deeds were done, and prisoners rescued, and the legend of Jajax has increased.'A great winged terror known to the people of Umbar as a Roc has been seen attacking ships sailing off the Cape of Umbar, swamping them with the winds from its vast wings and plucking the hapless crew out of the water. The lords of Umbar have requested that you find the nesting place of this monstrous bird and drive it from the Shield Isles. The Roc is believed to be roosting upon a deserted isle in the far reaches of the archipelago, once a haunt for pirates and brigands. Rumours say that they were driven out by strange and monstrous creatures, far greater in size than any beast should be....Defeat the great beast guarding the entrance to the caves of the Isle of Storms.Defeat KrizhmûlSomeone - or more likely something - has slain most the pirates who once frequented these caves and driven away any survivors. If you want to reach the Roc's aerie above, you're going to have to make your way past it....Defeat Urâbaz the MightyThe tunnels here howl with winds that blow down from the peak, making your progress treacherous - but it seems to be the only path leading to the Roc's aerie above.Defeat RaghârikA great winged terror known to the people of Umbar as a Roc has been seen attacking ships sailing off the Cape of Umbar, swamping them with the winds from its vast wings and plucking the hapless crew out of the water. The lords of Umbar have requested that you find the nesting place of this monstrous bird and drive it from the Shield Isles. The Roc is believed to be roosting upon a deserted isle in the far reaches of the archipelago, once a haunt for pirates and brigands. Rumours say that they were driven out by strange and monstrous creatures, far greater in size than any beast should be....Defeat the great beast guarding the entrance to the caves of the Isle of Storms.Defeat KrizhmûlSomeone - or more likely something - has slain most the pirates who once frequented these caves and driven away any survivors. If you want to reach the Roc's aerie above, you're going to have to make your way past it....Defeat Urâbaz the MightyThe tunnels here howl with winds that blow down from the peak, making your progress treacherous - but it seems to be the only path leading to the Roc's aerie above.Defeat RaghârikA great winged terror known to the people of Umbar as a Roc has been seen attacking ships sailing off the Cape of Umbar, swamping them with the winds from its vast wings and plucking the hapless crew out of the water. The lords of Umbar have requested that you find the nesting place of this monstrous bird and drive it from the Shield Isles. The Roc is believed to be roosting upon a deserted isle in the far reaches of the archipelago, once a haunt for pirates and brigands. Rumours say that they were driven out by strange and monstrous creatures, far greater in size than any beast should be....Defeat the great beast guarding the entrance to the caves of the Isle of Storms.Defeat KrizhmûlSomeone - or more likely something - has slain most the pirates who once frequented these caves and driven away any survivors. If you want to reach the Roc's aerie above, you're going to have to make your way past it....Defeat Urâbaz the MightyThe tunnels here howl with winds that blow down from the peak, making your progress treacherous - but it seems to be the only path leading to the Roc's aerie above.Defeat RaghârikA great winged terror known to the people of Umbar as a Roc has been seen attacking ships sailing off the Cape of Umbar, swamping them with the winds from its vast wings and plucking the hapless crew out of the water. The lords of Umbar have requested that you find the nesting place of this monstrous bird and drive it from the Shield Isles. The Roc is believed to be roosting upon a deserted isle in the far reaches of the archipelago, once a haunt for pirates and brigands. Rumours say that they were driven out by strange and monstrous creatures, far greater in size than any beast should be....Defeat the great beast guarding the entrance to the caves of the Isle of Storms.Defeat KrizhmûlSomeone - or more likely something - has slain most the pirates who once frequented these caves and driven away any survivors. If you want to reach the Roc's aerie above, you're going to have to make your way past it....Defeat Urâbaz the MightyThe tunnels here howl with winds that blow down from the peak, making your progress treacherous - but it seems to be the only path leading to the Roc's aerie above.Defeat RaghârikA great winged terror known to the people of Umbar as a Roc has been seen attacking ships sailing off the Cape of Umbar, swamping them with the winds from its vast wings and plucking the hapless crew out of the water. The lords of Umbar have requested that you find the nesting place of this monstrous bird and drive it from the Shield Isles. The Roc is believed to be roosting upon a deserted isle in the far reaches of the archipelago, once a haunt for pirates and brigands. Rumours say that they were driven out by strange and monstrous creatures, far greater in size than any beast should be....Defeat the great beast guarding the entrance to the caves of the Isle of Storms.Defeat KrizhmûlSomeone - or more likely something - has slain most the pirates who once frequented these caves and driven away any survivors. If you want to reach the Roc's aerie above, you're going to have to make your way past it....Defeat Urâbaz the MightyThe tunnels here howl with winds that blow down from the peak, making your progress treacherous - but it seems to be the only path leading to the Roc's aerie above.Defeat RaghârikA great winged terror known to the people of Umbar as a Roc has been seen attacking ships sailing off the Cape of Umbar, swamping them with the winds from its vast wings and plucking the hapless crew out of the water. The lords of Umbar have requested that you find the nesting place of this monstrous bird and drive it from the Shield Isles. The Roc is believed to be roosting upon a deserted isle in the far reaches of the archipelago, once a haunt for pirates and brigands. Rumours say that they were driven out by strange and monstrous creatures, far greater in size than any beast should be....Defeat the great beast guarding the entrance to the caves of the Isle of Storms.Defeat KrizhmûlSomeone - or more likely something - has slain most the pirates who once frequented these caves and driven away any survivors. If you want to reach the Roc's aerie above, you're going to have to make your way past it....Defeat Urâbaz the MightyThe tunnels here howl with winds that blow down from the peak, making your progress treacherous - but it seems to be the only path leading to the Roc's aerie above.Defeat RaghârikRaphûz asked you to accompany him to find and defeat Kushlâgur, the largest scoprion in Ambarûl.Raphûz appears ready to enter the scorpion nest. Speak with him to begin your hunt for Kushlâgur.Speak with Raphûz to begin the hunt for KushlâgurRaphûz looks nervous but resolved to defeat the scorpion Kushlâgur. You should speak with him before you continue.Speak with Raphûz to continue the hunt for KushlâgurDefeat KushlâgurYou successfully defeated Kushlâgur. See how Raphûz is doing.Speak with Raphûz to see how he is'I have seen smaller scorpions in my days in Umbar, nothing as large as these. We should be cautious as we approach. Who is to know how dangerous this Kushlâgur may be?''I will admit I am nervous. The sting of these creatures is painful. If I had not brought some draughts with me to counteract their sting, I do not think I could continue.

'Fortune is upon me though, you are my companion.'

He smiles at you.

'Let us end this creature.''I am exhilarated, ${PLAYER}. The danger was clear, but we fought like warriors and put the beast down. I could not have done this without you.

'Thank you, my friend.'In order to prove their mettle Raphûz and Ashâmi were tasked by Numûru to prove their abilities while confronting their fears. Raphûz must face a fearsome boar in Imhûlar.Raphûz prepares to enter the ruins where the great boar is said to stalk. Let him know when you are ready to proceed.Speak with Raphûz to begin the hunt for UrkhêruYou and Raphûz search the ruins for signs of Urkhêru but find nothing.Speak with Raphûz to continue the hunt for UrkhêruYou and Raphûz search the ruins for signs of Urkhêru but find nothing.Speak with Raphûz to continue the hunt for UrkhêruYou and Raphûz search the ruins for signs of Urkhêru but find nothing.Speak with Raphûz to continue the hunt for UrkhêruAfter a short advance through the ruins, Raphûz stopped and spotted the beast, Urkhêru. He appears to be awaiting your signal to conclude the hunt.Speak with Raphûz to engage UrkhêruYou found and killed Urkhêru. Raphûz looks pleased with your success. Speak with him.Speak with Raphûz'My fear of these beasts is much diminished. I have you to thank for this my friend. Let us make haste. I want to return to Ashâmi as quickly as we can.''Not here. No matter, we will find the beast.'

He looks at you and smiles.

'We have come far, you and I. To think, it was only a short while ago I feared these creatures so much. With your assistance I learned there is little to fear.

'Ashâmi finds my stories of travelling with you amusing. She is a marvellous woman.'

He stares off for a moment.

'Come, friend. We have a pressing matter at hand.''The beast is not here, my friend. It is proving very elusive.'

He smiles genuinely.

'I have something to confess, ${PLAYER}. On the road from Shonith to Urkmâkh Ashâmi, in a quiet moment, shared a kiss.'

He blushes.

'It was... amazing. In the quiet moments, even now as we hunt, I find my thoughts drifting to her. I only hope she feels for me as I feel for her.'

He shakes his head.

'Enough talk like this. Let us continue.''Another battle and story to enter into my journal. I never imagined my life to be filled with such adventure and challenges. I feel pride, my friend.

'Perhaps my first steps into the valley were for my parents and their legacy. Now, however, every step I take is my own. I have you, your advice, your assistance, and I daresay your companionship to thank.'

He chuckles.

'Come, let us return to Ashâmi.''My friend, I am beginning to think this large boar Numûru speaks of is another Shagâni myth.

'Were Ashâmi here, she would tell me, 'Raphûz you must exercise patience and understand the mysteries of Shagâna reveal themselves when they are prepared, not you.''

He grins.

'She is a very wise woman. We should continue, so I can get back to her.''There it is my friend, the beast they call Urkhêru. It is as Ashâmi says, patience in all things.

'Let us make this a merciful and quick kill. I wish to return to Urmâkh and check on Ashâmi.'Defeat the Orcs who tracked you to Enârshan's home.The Orcs have followed you to Enârshan's home. Defeat them and make safe the cave.Ready yourself for the OrcsOrcs have arrived at Enârshan's home. Defeat them before they can cause any damage.Defend against the attacking OrcsYou hear more Orcs coming. Defeat them before they can cause any damage.Defend against the attacking OrcsThere are more Orcs on the way. Their captain appears to be with them. Defeat them before they can cause any damage.Defend against the attacking OrcsYou do not hear any more Orcs. Enârshan's home is safe for now.Speak with EnârshanAshâmi and Raphûz share time with you.Raphûz and Ashâmi are sitting and talking. You should sit and join them.Join Raphûz and AshâmiAshâmi and Raphûz asked you to sit with them.You sat with your friend and the woman, Ashâmi. They seem to be talking more openly, learning about one another.Listen to the conversation between Ashâmi and RaphûzAs Raphûz and Ashâmi converse, you saw a figure approach. You should investigate.Respectfully leave the conversation by bowing to either Raphûz or AshâmiYou saw a shadow approach. You should investigate.Speak to the new arrival'Greetings, friend. I am Lathagwid. I wanted to thank you and to save you from what would become inescapable.

'It is fascinating to watch a watered seed germinate, but also tedious. Once our part is done, it is best to let them be.

'It is up to the seed to strive and grow.

'Let us let them speak.'Corudan has devised a desperate plan, and he needs your help and the assistance of Rothog the Storm to carry it out.Corudan needs your help if he is to reach the chamber deep within Ashâgir where the last stockpile of Hungry Fire was hidden.Talk to Corudan inside AshâgirDeep within Ashâgir, Rothog is ready to do his part.Talk to Rothog inside Ashâgir'Azagath and his Thardúth masters may not know why we have returned to Ashâgir, but if they marked our passage here they will try to stop us.

'We must be prepared for anything as we return to that sealed chamber, ${PLAYER}!''I know of this Narghâk, this Hungry Fire, only by its evil reputation. I will carry as many of the crates as I can safely hold, ${PLAYER}, but if they should come alight I will ensure neither you nor Corudan the Elf escape the burning.

'If I am to perish in a conflagration of Narghâk, so too will you. See that I do not.'Rothog has summoned you to his chambers as he confronts Zarzíra Dawn-star about her misdeeds.Rothog has summoned you to his chambers to confront Zarzíra Dawn-star about her misdeeds.Talk to Rothog the StormDefeat Zarzíra and her men as they attack you in the audience chamber.Defeat Zarzíra and her menSpeak to Rothog the Storm about Zarzíra's treachery.Speak to Rothog'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER}. With Zarzíra defeated and Shaidal well on his way to freedom, things seem to have worked out. Now please go, my people have some cleaning up to do.''Now you will see a matter of justice. While I am very confident about how this will go, do be wary, as this serpent seems to be willing to strike.''Zarzíra made a grave mistake so openly attacking you in my presence. I am overjoyed by your victory. You see, Zarzíra and her men were not worth me bloodying my blades, as they are so below me. But I commend you for your quick action.

'Rest assured, if Shaidal is successful in the task that I laid out before him, he will go free.

'Thank you again for helping solve what could have been a rather complicated situation!'Assist Razâl and Numûru on a mission into Kûr Anzar to weaken the Barkhûshim.Move closer to speak with Numûru and Razâl.Move closer to speak with Numûru and RazâlListen to Numûru and Razâl's conversation.Listen to Numûru and Razâl's conversationSpeak with Numûru outside Kûr Anzar.Speak with NumûruSpeak with Razâl outside Kûr Anzar.Speak with RazâlMove further into Kûr Anzar.Move further into Kûr AnzarMove further into Kûr Anzar.Move further into Kûr AnzarSabotage the Barkhûshim forces in Kûr Anzar by taking grain sacks, destroying weapon stands and defeating Barkhûshim sentries.Collect grain sacks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy racks of weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Barkhûshim sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Move to meet Numûru and Razâl outside the Angar Aragín, the tower of Kûr Anzar at the top of the city.Meet Numûru and Razâl outside the tower of Kûr AnzarSet fire to the barricades near the tower.Set fire to the barricades near the towerListen to Numûru near Angar Aragín.Listen to NumûruSpeak with Razâl near Angar Aragín, the tower of Kûr Anzar.Speak with Razâl'I will move ahead and clear our path.''I almost feel bad for the Barkhûshim, now that I've got Numûru a bit stirred up.

'I will also soften your resistance. My sword arm may be slow but it helps when the enemy doesn't see it coming. You should move through the city, taking back their ill-gotten grain stores and destroying their weapons as the opportunity arises. Make sure to defeat their sentries, lest they call out our presence here. 

'We will meet again at the top of Kur Anzar, near the Angar Aragín.''No! They've taken him!'Working with Nimasi, you have traced the banner attacks to a large camp in southern Imhûlar. Investigate the camp without being seen to discover the source of these attacks.Move to the main tent to determine who is leading this force of Ordâkhai.Move to the main tent inside the camp

<rgb=#ff0000>Avoid Ekhamâti Look-outs</rgb>Listen to Nimasi in the tent.Listen to NisamiListen to Bârshud's message to Mizâdi.Listen to Bârshud's message to MizâdiFlee the tent and find Surâsh.Flee the tent and find Surâsh before Bârshud changes his mindFree Surâsh near the front gate.Free Surâsh near the front gateKhûldim Umûn has informed Girhâzi that the Dubarâkh is inside an abandoned salt mine. You have been invited to join them as they search the caves for the lost library of Ambarûli culture and history.Khûldim Umûn has led you into a salt mine where he claims the Dubarâkh is hidden. You should talk to Girhâzi.Talk to GirhâziKhûldim Umûn has led you into a salt mine where he claims the Dubarâkh is hidden. You should follow Girhâzi and Khûldim.Accompany Girhâzi and KhûldimKhûldim Umûn has led you into a salt mine where he claims the Dubarâkh is hidden. You should follow Girhâzi and Khûldim.Defend yourself from the attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Listen to the conversationDefend yourself from the attackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Girhâzi'Well this is it, ${PLAYER}. Hopefully, this pashâg is telling the truth, though I doubt it. We have no other clues to go on, so we must hold on to hope.

'I do not like the idea of being trapped here with no escape. I will leave the Dumûri here to secure our exit. We can handle the Usan-kûni we will likely encounter in these caves.''That was unexpected, to say the least! Have you been hurt?

'We should leave here before more arrive. I do not know how many members this cult may have, and we are only two. Perhaps we can return later with more warriors to oust these cultists. For now, let us return to Iridír.'Belondor has asked you to accompany him as he returns to Mâkhda Khorbo in search of clues that may explain why Azagath and Nakási went there, as well as where they are going.You have arrived at the Iron Stairwell in Mâkhda Khorbo, where you and Belondor faced each other as enemies, and where his crew was slain by Azagath's dark magic. You should talk to Belondor.Talk to BelondorYou have arrived at the Iron Stairway in Mâkhda Khorbo, where you and Belondor faced each other as enemies, and where his crew was slain by Azagath's dark magic. You should talk to Belondor.Talk to BelondorYou have arrived at the Iron Stairway in Mâkhda Khorbo, where you and Belondor faced each other as enemies, and where his crew was slain by Azagath's dark magic. You should talk to Belondor.Talk to BelondorWithin Mâkhda Khorbo, Belondor has noticed that the gate previously blocking access to the stairs is now open. You should go up the stairs.Ascend the Iron StairwellYou have followed Belondor into an upstairs area. You should talk to Belondor.Talk to BelondorAs you enter this upstairs area, you discover that it is infested with bats. You should defeat bats.Defeat Ghâbekhid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You are in an area of Mâkhda Khorbo that Belondor says he saw Azagath and Nakási enter. You should search the area for signs of why they may have come here.Continue searching the areaYou and Belondor have spotted something at the end of this hallway. You should investigate what it is.Examine the itemAt the end of a hallway in Mâkhda Khorbo you and Belondor have found a tapestry on the wall that is a map. You should examine the map.Examine the mapYou have searched Mâkhda Khorbo and found the remains of a map, torn in half. You should talk to Belondor.Talk to Belondor'I think we have found what we came for. Let us leave this hateful place.''When last we were in this room together, we faced each other as enemies. How is it that it feels like an eternity ago, but also like it was just yesterday? I have been trying to push all of this from my mind, ${PLAYER}. It seemed like the only way I would be able to go on.

'But I see now that closing off my heart does them an injustice. They were family to me, ${PLAYER}, and I miss them with all of my heart. But is that not the danger any time you choose to love? I don't think I care much for the alternative.'This large map is an old and tattered tapestry. The right half of it has been cut and torn from what remains; and recently, by the looks of it. The lettering on it is written in a language with which you are unfamiliar.'I cannot read the script on this map, but I recognize it all the same. This is a map showing the Shield Isles and Cape of Umbar. The eastern half of the map has been taken. Surely if they are travelling overland, their journey is to the east.

'Maps themselves are not rare. Something must have been marked on that side of the map that they are trying to find. Considering the previous owners of the map, this indeed bodes ill.'Belondor places his hand on the ground where his crew fell, silent tears falling onto the stone floor.

'I blamed myself, ${PLAYER}, for being a fool. They trusted me with their lives and I failed them. I still hold myself responsible for my poor decisions, but I am not the one who killed them, and my hatred should be directed at Azagath and not myself.

'I knew him for many years. I thought him to be my friend. Men of a common purpose and a similar mind. What evil lurks inside him, I wonder, to give him the power to rip souls from bodies and command spirits like his puppets? And how did I not see it before?'Belondor stops for a moment and looks around. He mutters something to himself, and you can see on his face that something just occurred to him.'Prepare yourself for a fight ${PLAYER}. There are enemies ahead. They will not stay our search.'You have come with Rahâzi, Corudan, and Sigileth to the fortress above Jirush with the hope that you will be able to find Balakhâd and free him from Ordâkhai captivity.Rahâzi wants to go over the plan before you infiltrate the fortress above Jirush.Talk to RahâziYour part of the plan requires you to sneak inside the fortress and turn to the right to search for the prisoner.Sneak into the fortress and search the right side of the Ordâkhai campTatháta has come to the fortress above Jirush.Remain on your guard and listen to the newcomerTatháta has come to the fortress above Jirush.Talk to TathátaTatháta has come to the fortress above Jirush.Talk to TathátaTatháta has offered to answer a single question of yours.Ask Tatháta a single questionTatháta has agreed to answer a single question of yours.Listen to what Tatháta has to sayTatháta has answered your question, and the sound of distant shouting has brought your conversation with her to a close.Talk to TathátaThe time has come for you to leave the fortress before you are discovered by the Ordâkhai.Leave the fortress by the main gate before you are discovered by the Ordâkhai'Listen closely to the plan.

'I will make for the buildings opposite the entrance, and move from shadow to shadow. Corudan and Sigileth will pass through the main gate and search for their quarry on the left side of the fortress. And you will look for him on the right side, ${PLAYER}. I will give you some minutes before engaging the enemy... but you will not have very long!

'In days to come, may the Ordâkhai speak in hushed tones of our work tonight! Fortune smile upon us!''I have spent weeks hunting agents of the Heirsworn who seek to claim the bounties placed upon the Kindred of the Coins by the widow Saklaphêl. Agents such as you, ${PLAYER}.'

You deny that you are in Saklaphêl's employ. Tatháta eyes you closely.'You have had ample time to act upon the widow's orders, if you sought her bounty upon us. Have I not espied you from afar in the company of Kinsman Belondor, his back turned to you at length and without fear? And when I decided on that moonlit night mere days ago to put an end to both these questions and your life, was it not the arrival of Khôltekh and Rothog that stayed my attack? I am not often surprised, ${PLAYER}, but on that night your friendship with my allies was a startlement to me. No servant of Saklaphêl could deceive such as they for long.

'Why do you ally with the Kindred? Are we not enemies?'

You briefly describe your shared fear that Azagath and Nakási are using a map they took from the Mâkhda Khorbo to search for a buried evil of Sauron's somewhere east of Umbar. Tatháta nods slowly.'I will answer a single question. Choose your inquiry with care.''The sands have run from the hourglass, ${PLAYER}, and our conversation is ended. I am pleased I did not slay you. Your answers were most informative.

'Good-bye.'You have only moments before the entrance to Utug-bûr collapses. If you are to escape with Sigileth, you will have to act quickly.Corudan knows the need for haste if you are to rescue Sigileth.Talk to Corudan inside Utug-bûrYou can go no further inside Utug-bûr or you will be trapped forever with the Thardúth.Heed the words of CorudanYou can go no further without risking entombment with the Thardúth... but perhaps Sigileth will hear your voice if you call for her down the hallway!Choose your words with care and call for Sigileth to return to youYou are out of time! You must escape from Utug-bûr!Escape from Utug-bûr!<rgb=#FF0000>You have to reach the exit before the entrance collapses!</rgb>Days later, anxious eyes turn to the east and consider the army of soldiers approaching Umbar Baharbêl.Days pass, and a ruler in Umbar Baharbêl anxiously awaits newsJajax waits in Dâr Laja to hear news of what his brother Daxamat learned of the approaching army.Talk to your brother Jajax in Dâr Laja and tell him what you sawHármelak waits for tidings of the army that approaches the city, and your brother Jajax is not about to give her this news. It falls to you to do this, Daxamat.Talk to Hármelak inside Dâr Laja and tell her what you sawSeveral days ago, in the aftermath of the Dagor Carlanthir.Days earlier, in the aftermath of the Dagor CarlanthirYou cannot have imagined it! You know someone lives beneath the rubble!Break the rubble beside the collapsed entrance to Utug-bûrYou cannot have imagined it! You know someone lives beneath the rubble!Break more of the rubble beside the collapsed entrance to Utug-bûrYour quick action has unearthed Sigileth from the rubble that might have proved her tomb!Talk to Sigileth among the rubble beside the collapsed entrance to Utug-bûr'Hurry, ${PLAYER}! We have little time to waste!''What did you see, Dax? An army approaches Umbar Baharbêl?'

You tell Jajax that a great force of soldiers emerged from Ambarûl, drawing even with Telperiën's Wall, but they raised no banner and you could not discern their loyalties.

'Did you see ${PLAYER} among them? Or perhaps Belondor leads these men? Is this army the same that he took with him in haste... or is it an army of Heirsworn, come to take the city?

'I am not bringing Hármelak these tidings, Dax. I leave that to you!''What is it? I can see from your face you have tidings to share, but you fear they will be unwelcome. Speak them, and I will decide if it is so.'

You tell Hármelak that an army approaches the city, but you were unable to see who leads it, or what their intentions may be. Hármelak purses her lips, deep in thought.

'When Belondor asked to bring soldiers to battle in the lands to the east, I told him I needed time to think upon it; he waited not for my answer, but took the soldiers and marched within the hour. Such disrespect cannot be allowed... but it is said that when commanders of men taste victory in battle, they can at times desire more and more. If Belondor leads this returning army, will he think to use it to take control of this city?

'Or perhaps this is an army of Heirsworn. If Balakhâd escaped capture by the party sent to retrieve him, his survival could prove a beacon to his folk. Thinks he to overthrow the Kindred of the Coins? But from where could this army have come?'

You suggest to Hármelak that there may be a third possibility. She considers you carefully.

'What is this third possibility, tidings-bearer Daxamat?'

You suggest that the army may be tired from battle in the east, and the soldiers may simply want to return home. In this you see the guidance of ${PLAYER}, a hero who knows when to fight, and when not to fight. Hármelak weighs your suggestion.

'We will see if you are right, Daxamat. We will see. Send word to the scouts that whoever leads this army is to be brought before me at once!''I cannot believe it!''${PLAYER}...

'Has anyone... ever told you...

'You are such... a bother...'

Sigileth smiles up at you weakly.

'Thank you... my dear friend...' she murmurs quietly.Something stirs within the old keep of Maurûsh, but it is not the presence of the Ordâkhai that threatens Urash Dâr from behind its walls.Silirtas and Sigileth have come with you to investigate Maurûsh.Talk to Silirtas outside MaurûshThe Orcs remaining in Maurûsh seemingly abandoned much of their equipment at one of their camp-fires.Examine the abandoned possessions at the camp-fireSigileth and Silirtas stand unmoving in Maurûsh. What has happened to them... or to you?Examine SigilethSigileth and Silirtas stand unmoving in Maurûsh. What has happened to them... or to you?Examine SilirtasSome evil located deeper within Maurûsh may hold the key to freeing Sigileth and Silirtas from the ensnaring enchantment.Search deeper within Maurûsh for some way to free your friendsAn unusual creature, larger than the other Orcs you have seen, stands deep within Maurûsh. Or is this creature a product of the enchantment in which you have been snared?Examine the imposing creature worshipped by the OrcsA great weight lifts from your eyelids.Wait for answersSigileth stares at you with concern.Talk to Sigileth within MaurûshMithrandir has come to Maurûsh... but for what purpose has the Wizard travelled so far south?Talk to Mithrandir in MaurûshSome great evil pursues you! You have to escape from Maurûsh!Flee down the slope to the south to escape from Maurûsh!'Something drove the Ordâkhai from this place. Was it the Orcs... or was it something else? We should be careful, but we must learn these answers if we can.''${PLAYER}! Are you all right? You appeared to swoon for a moment, and you responded to nothing!'

You ask Sigileth if she or Silirtas heard the terrible voice that spoke to you, or saw the large and fearsome Orcs, and both Elves shake their heads.

'You were dazed for only moments, ${PLAYER}. How could you...?'

Sigileth's voice trails away to nothing, and she suddenly looks past you to the south.

'Someone approaches!''A terrible evil sleeps in this place, ${PLAYER}, and it is more dangerous than you can face alone! We cannot stay here!

'Quickly, now!'You have accompanied Corudan and Sigileth into a forgotten passage in the depths of Kamrabezûr, the vaults beneath Umbar Baharbêl, in search of Tatháta.Corudan stands in a forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.Talk to Corudan in the forgotten passageSigileth waits for you and Corudan in the forgotten passage.Talk to Sigileth in the forgotten passageThe passage shakes as a mighty beast charges toward you and your friends down the forgotten passage!Stand your ground!Corudan stands in a forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.Talk to Corudan in the forgotten passageDespite the appearance of the rampaging beast, Corudan and Sigileth have not abandoned their purpose to investigate the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.Follow Corudan and Sigileth down the forgotten passageJudging from the quantity of blood spilled on the floor of this chamber, the Umbari woman does not have long to live.Talk to the dying Umbari womanListen to what befell Cruel Dancer when she caught up to Tatháta in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.Listen to Cruel Dancer's storyCruel Dancer lies dying in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.Talk to Cruel Dancer and hear her last requestCorudan stands in the forgotten passage within Kamrabezûr.Talk to Corudan in the forgotten passage within KamrabezûrGalatâni asked that you bring her outside into the sunlight before she dies.Bring Galatâni into the sunlight before she diesGalatâni lies dying in the moonlight.Talk to Galatâni in the moonlightGalatâni does not have much time to live.Stand with Galatâni and observe her final momentsGalatâni has one more thing to say to you.Hear what Galatâni has left to say'She is gone. We should make a place for her here. Let us find stones with which to mark the grave before the sun rises.''This is the passage my sister discovered. Judging from the air in here, few have come this way, but there has been no sign of Tatháta elsewhere in Kamrabezûr. If we can trust the words of the unseen ones, the Terâsi, she may have fled to this forgotten corner and gone into hiding.

'I told Sigileth to wait, but she has gone ahead. Let us catch up to her, and quickly.''I hear movement ahead of us. Ready yourself!''I think we found the creature that escaped from the arena, ${PLAYER}. Let us hope it does no harm to the folk who dwell within Umbar-môkh!

'We will hunt it later. For now let us continue on in search of our true quarry!'The woman blinks up at you through bloodshot eyes and her face is familiar. You have found Cruel Dancer.

'${PLAYER}...' she manages, weakly. 'I do not have much... time... left to me...'Cruel Dancer shakes her head, but the motion causes her great pain and she winces.

'I was the... deadliest woman... in all these lands, ${PLAYER}. But my luck... my fortunes... they have abandoned me. Did it happen... when I killed the Blade-twist? Ever since then I have had ill fortune. I never... considered... that Tatháta might possess... such power...'

The dying woman gathers what remains of her strength.

'I want to confess to you something, ${PLAYER}. Will you... bring me into the sunlight? I have spent... too long in darkness... too long as Cruel Dancer. I would be Galatâni again... instead.''Yes, we can do as she asks. But I do not think she has very long left to her, ${PLAYER}. She may not survive the journey aboveground.

'Still... we will make the attempt.'Galatâni laughs weakly, a thin sound in the silence of the Umbari night.

'It was too much to hope for sunlight... I suppose,' she murmurs.

'I was not always as I am, ${PLAYER}. I was like you... an adventurer-for-hire, accomplishing the small tasks... that needed doing. It was a simple life, but a good one. There was food on the table for my husband, Jedûth, and my daughter Ashenâth. But it... did not last.

'My husband was accused... of stealing a vase from a wealthy nobleman, a man called Phirasâkh. He did not! I know he did not... but he was slain for the crime. I had to take on even more dangerous tasks to support my Ashenâth... even murder. That paid the finest of all, ${PLAYER}, but the first victim of my knife was the sweetest: Phirasâkh, the nobleman who falsely-accused my Jedûth. He deserved the death I gave to him.

'But I did not stop at Phirasâkh, for I had tasted the deadly nectar of death. I was away for longer and longer at a time; I told myself the coins I gave my neighbours to watch my daughter Ashenâth were all for her benefit. The name "Galatâni" no longer applied to me, for I had grown hard, and cold. I was now Hazêphen, "Cruel Dancer," and I delighted in the slaughter. Phirasâkh had deserved death. But he would not be the last, and some who died at the hands of Cruel Dancer deserved it less than he. Many did.

'It was best for Ashenâth that her mother remain only a memory... for I had grown addicted to... the danger, ${PLAYER}, and the sight of the blood I spilled. It had... become an obsession.'

She falls silent for a long moment, and you wonder if her life has ended, but then she coughs and sputters back to awareness.

'The city was not a place of safety... in those years. The Church of the All-Seeing saw its... enemies everywhere. The neighbours who watched after my daughter were taken in sacrifice to the Mâkhda Khorbo, and their home burned. On that day Ashenâth joined her father, but when I returned to the burned frame that had been a home there was no vengeance to be had. The Dark Lord worshipped by the Church of the All-Seeing was not like... not like Phirasâkh. I could not be certain He even lived, and if He did not live... could He be slain?

'I preyed upon the Church for a time, often for free, but when my coins ran out I had few choices left to me. I stopped returning to the burned husk where once I lived with my Jedûth and my Ashenâth. I only felt alive when I competed with other bounty-hunters for the most dangerous work I could find.''What bounties could be more dangerous... than those placed by Saklaphêl... on the Kindred of the... of the...'

Frustration and sadness war upon her face as she lies dying in the moonlight.

'If only... I could have chosen a different road. But that was... not to be. In my heart, I was... always... Hazêphen.'

Galatâni's voice is little more than a whisper now.

'Tatháta... kept me alive... for days... ${PLAYER}. With her terrible, secret power... she could have slain me... easily. But she had... she had questions. Questions about... you, ${PLAYER}...'Outraged that a Kinta Elf shot her with an arrow in an attempt to get her to leave Arwáth, Agalûnu has asked you to escort her into the grove to confront Shanthar.You have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should talk to Agalûnu.Talk to AgalûnuYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should stop and appreciate the beauty of the grove with Agalûnu.<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the beauty of ArwáthYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Agalûnu wants to talk to you.Talk to AgalûnuYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Agalûnu wants to talk to you.Talk to AgalûnuYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Shanthar has something to say to Agalûnu.Talk to ShantharYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should listen to their conversation.Listen to the conversationYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Agalûnu wants to talk to you.Talk to AgalûnuYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should listen to their conversation.Listen to the conversation'Come ${PLAYER}, let us return to my camp. I have much to think about, and I am also not feeling so well.''${PLAYER}, can you believe him? How galling!'

Agalûnu turns to Shanthar.

'I understand that you wish for solitude and to hoard this wood for yourself, but what I do not understand is why. Why should one Elf sit upon this grove like a dragon sitting upon piles of gold?''I did not expect this ${PLAYER}. Have I and my forebears really been party to the destruction of a forest that covered the entire Ikorbân Valley? That is just awful. I can see why this Elf would not like us overmuch!''Oh, ${PLAYER}, this place is so lovely! Just look at it!''It is a beautiful day, but we should not dally overmuch. Is that the Elf's abode just ahead?'Shanthar gazes at the woman, his expression unreadable.

'You know not of which you speak, child. I have sworn an oath to steward these grounds and protect them with my life. Why I have done so is none of your concern. What I do not understand is why Men insist on destroying everything beautiful in Middle-earth.

'Trees provide shade, they disrupt harsh winds, they protect the soil from the river. They provide homes to birds, squirrels and insects. They provide food for all. Long ago, this entire valley was a forest, dense with trees exactly like these. Then Men came and 'put them to use' as you would do. They are already in use, only you do not see it.'Corudan has asked to go with you to visit an old friend.After a lengthy journey, Corudan and your other companions stand outside the village of Lhanuch.Talk to Corudan outside LhanuchCorudan encouraged you to climb the hill into Lhanuch and ensure that your group will be welcome.Enter Lhanuch and climb the hillSuvulch stands partway up the hill in Lhanuch.Talk to Suvulch in LhanuchSuvulch told you Nona is further up the hill within Lhanuch, and will be delighted to see you.Find Nona up the hill near the summit of LhanuchNona sits by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch.Talk to Nona by the fire near the summit of LhanuchIt is a reunion of friends and adventurers near the summit of Lhanuch, but not everyone is welcome.Stand beside the fire with your friendsNona is prepared to become Wadu's Ghost and slay her former lover... but you cannot stand idly by.Talk to Nona and keep her from once again becoming Wadu's GhostYou prevented Nona from becoming Wadu's Ghost... but it was a close thing.Stand beside the fire with your friendsNona has called for you and the others to <rgb=#00FF00>sit</rgb> and reminisce about your adventures.<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> by the fire and reminisce about your adventuresYou and your friends sit by the fire and reminisce about your shared adventures.Reminisce about your adventures'This is Lhanuch, the village of the Uch-lûth from which Nona came? I am pleased to see it. She did not speak of it often, but when she did her voice was fond... despite her attempts to prevent it, I think.

'You had better go on ahead, ${PLAYER}. Nona's people will remember you. The rest of us will be considered... what was the word? Duvodiad? Yes, that was it.

'The rest of us may be duvodiad, but in Lhanuch I believe you will be welcomed.''I knew you would one day climb this hill and come again to Lhanuch, ${PLAYER}. I saw it in the Pool of the King only weeks after my daughter Nona departed, following the dream that carried her away to fight another kingdom's war. She returned months afterward with a broken heart and a child in her belly, and I thought you would return in the company of this man, this Horn who was the father of the child. But sun and moon rose and fell, and he never showed his face.

'My daughter sits by the summit of the village, by the fire on the right. She will be glad to see you. As for the others who wait below... who can say? If they do not speak the right words, they may learn the daughter of Suvulch can be even more dangerous than he is, and that is no small amount!''${PLAYER}, my dear friend! It is good to see you again at last! If you waited a few more months you might meet my son or my daughter... but I am glad you did not wait.

'No, I do not yet know what my child will be! When the days feel longest I wonder if Hildegard would tell me whether I am having a son or a daughter... but I cannot bring myself to return to the soothsayer's cave. If she had not spoken as she had, perhaps Horn...

'It does not matter. It has been months but my anger has not cooled. It is said the Uch-lûth love even more fiercely than they fight, and you should cross them in neither! Someone should have told that to Horn before he sent me away, the fool. Yes, I know he thought he was doing right. He was wrong, and should have listened.''Stand aside, ${PLAYER}. To return here, after sending me away... his wits are more addled than they used to be! How can you explain his presence here?'

Nona's eyes boil with fury, but your keen eyesight reveals that the hand holding her brother's sword trembles. She does not want to become Wadu's Ghost again, despite her words and the anger she has nursed for Horn since he sent her away from the war. If only there was some way for you to break the tension. You cast your thoughts back to the days you spent travelling with Horn and Nona, and then you have it.

You recount your cautious steps within the deserted village of Dunfast, in Wildermore, when Nona had left your little party, leaving you in the company of Horn, the minstrel Gléowine, and Corudan. The Elf felt eyes upon your group, and it was with heightened senses that the four of you crept towards the bush that seemed to contain the unwelcome and hostile eyes. Horn valiantly approached the bush, his hand upon his sword, prepared to face whatever evil lurked within...Corudan has asked to go with you to visit an old friend.After a lengthy journey, Corudan and Caebar stand outside the village of Lhanuch.Talk to Corudan outside LhanuchCorudan encouraged you to climb the hill into Lhanuch and ensure that your group will be welcome.Enter Lhanuch and climb the hillSuvulch stands partway up the hill in Lhanuch.Talk to Suvulch in LhanuchSuvulch told you Nona is further up the hill within Lhanuch, and will be delighted to see you.Find Nona up the hill near the summit of LhanuchNona sits by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch.Talk to Nona by the fire near the summit of LhanuchIt is a reunion of friends and adventurers near the summit of Lhanuch.Stand beside the fire with your friendsNona has set down the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepare.Examine the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepareNona is grateful for the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepare.Stand beside the fire with your friendsNona has called for you and the others to <rgb=#00FF00>sit</rgb> and reminisce about your adventures.<rgb=#00FF00>Sit</rgb> by the fire and reminisce about your adventuresYou and your friends sit by the fire and reminisce about your shared adventures.Reminisce about your adventures'This is Lhanuch, the village of the Uch-lûth from which Nona came? I am pleased to see it. She did not speak of it often, but when she did her voice was fond... despite her attempts to prevent it, I think.

'You had better go on ahead, ${PLAYER}. Nona's people will remember you. Caebar and my sister and I will be considered... what was the word? Duvodiad? Yes, that was it.

'The three of us may be duvodiad, but in Lhanuch I believe you will be welcomed.''I knew you would one day climb this hill and come again to Lhanuch, ${PLAYER}. I saw it in the Pool of the King only weeks after my daughter Nona departed, following the dream that carried her away to fight another kingdom's war. She returned months afterward with a broken heart and a child in her belly, and I thought you would return in the company of this man, this Horn who was the father of the child. But sun and moon rose and fell, and it was not you who first came to Lhanuch with tidings.'

Suvulch frowns, and you remember that he considers himself more gifted with weapons than with words.

'It was a minstrel, an old one with white hair and a solemn face. He said he served a king of the horse-lords who perished fighting the Dark Lord, and he had sad tidings for Nona. "Horn is dead," he said to her, and while she had raged with anger in the wordless months that passed, her fury was replaced all at once, and with sorrow. I wept with the two of them. Yes, even I! But I am her father, and I raised my Nona to be strong. Her tears showed to me how deeply she loved this Horn, even though she buried that love beneath the rage she held for him, and which he deserved! So I wept alongside them, and when the minstrel departed I embraced my daughter and I told her that I would never again say a cross word about the man Horn.

'I meant it even then, but in time I have come to understand he was a man of courage who believed he was not courageous, ${PLAYER}. That is a curious thing, and not common among the Uch-lûth. But perhaps not all can be as honest as Suvulch, who is certain of his courage and acts upon it every day.'

He roughly clasps your arm, and then points up the hill.

'My daughter sits by the summit of the village, by the fire on the right. She will be glad to see you.''${PLAYER}, my dear friend! It is good to see you again at last! If you waited a few more months you might meet my son or my daughter... but I am glad you did not wait.

'No, I do not yet know what my child will be! When the days feel longest I wonder if Hildegard would tell me whether I am having a son or a daughter... but I cannot bring myself to return to the soothsayer's cave. When Gléowine came to Lhanuch and told me of what transpired before the walls of Minas Tirith... it was as if I was hearing of it for the second time, seeing it again, feeling anew all the pain of it. So I will not return to Hildegard.

'Gléowine spoke also of your deeds, and I know Horn was avenged. I would have become Wadu's Ghost once more and done it myself, but you can see that I am somewhat occupied for now. So I thank you, and I know Horn does as well, and so does his child.'You need to seal the entrance to Utug-bûr before the Thardúth emerge and levy their full power against you.Grieving that the Thardúth had their origins as ancient Kintai, Silirtas greatly desires to do her part in sealing them away.Talk to Silirtas outside Utug-bûrYou and Sigileth have volunteered to place the Narghâk on the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr.Place Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (0/3)You and Sigileth have volunteered to place the Narghâk on the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr.Place Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (1/3)You and Sigileth have volunteered to place the Narghâk on the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr.Place Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (2/3)A sense of exhaustion has overcome you once again, as happened earlier when you journeyed within Maurûsh.Check on the group placing the Narghâk on the other sideThe ethereal voice speaks threatening words from within the confines of your mind.Listen to the threatening voice within your mindSilirtas is in grave danger! She must awaken at once!Awaken Silirtas from the enchantment that keeps her from movingAt the urging of his Thardúth masters, Azagath intends to do great harm to your friends.Prevent Azagath from inflicting great harm upon SilirtasAt the urging of his Thardúth masters, Azagath intends to do great harm to your friends.Prevent Azagath from inflicting great harm upon SilirtasAt the urging of his Thardúth masters, Azagath intends to do great harm to your friends.Prevent Azagath from inflicting great harm upon SilirtasThe Thardúth turn their attention elsewhere in the battle. The sorcerous exhaustion that troubled you has been lifted.Stand your ground'If the Thardúth were truly once of my people, I want to do my part in sealing them away, ${PLAYER}!

'I and Corudan will set the Narghâk to the right of the entrance. You and Sigileth can place the Narghâk on the left side. We will seal the entrance to Utug-bûr and these fallen Kintai will no longer trouble the world!'In desperation you call her name, but Silirtas remains frozen, unaware of the evil that threatens her.The Dumûri warriors Rahâzi and Surdûsha have suggested that you return with them to Iridír where you can speak of your shared triumph over the Ordâkhai remnant.Part of the way back to Iridír, Rahâzi has called for a halt.Talk to RahâziRahâzi and Surdûsha have triumphed over the Ordâkhai, but now a new threat emerges.Talk to RahâziStand your ground against Tatháta and protect the Dumûri warriors.Stand your ground against Tatháta and protect the Dumûri warriorsRothog the Storm has arrived, and his arrival may have saved you and the Dumûri warriors from Tatháta's wrath.Talk to Rothog the StormKhôltekh has arrived in Ambarûl.Talk to KhôltekhRothog and Khôltekh have arrived in Ambarûl, and they seek to gain permission from its people to carry out the mission they share with you.Observe the meeting of Khôltekh and RahâziRahâzi waits to speak with you before she departs.Talk to RahâziKhôltekh has some words for you before you continue on to Iridír.Talk to Khôltekh'Quiet! There it is again: the sound of voices. More of the Ordâkhai have come in search of their fellows, and now they seek to surprise us.

'Let us teach them to fear the defenders of this land!''Do you know what terrible creature makes this sound, ${PLAYER}? Your eyes tell me that you do!'

Hurriedly, you advise Rahâzi and Surdûsha to take defensive stances and prepare once again for battle.'What caused Tatháta to attack you, ${PLAYER}? She and I have faced each other in battle before, and when I tell you she is a deadly opponent you can believe me. Ours was a friendly competition, and it came to a draw, but in return she made a gift to me of Húrshauk here.

'I did not plan to bring Húrshauk with me on this adventure, but he has grown so large and so ferocious that no one at Dahâl Huliz dares to approach him without me. We could delay no longer, so my good friend accompanies me. That will not be a problem.''A number of difficulties threatened to delay us too long, ${PLAYER}, and it was decided we could wait no longer. The caravan driver and the warehouse master suffered our displeasure for the obstacles they placed in our way, and they will suffer even more in the days ahead, for Hármelak has a mind for punishment.

'At last we set out, and it would appear we arrived at a fortunate time. Who are these warrior-women, and can we count them friends to Umbar, and to the Kindred of the Coins?''I will hurry on to Iridír with Surdûsha and tell my mother about these newcomers, ${PLAYER}. If they are friends of yours, I believe she will give them leave to move freely within Ambarûl.''One more thing, ${PLAYER}, before we follow those warriors to their village and meet with their chief.

'I think it will be best not to mention that Tatháta is a member of the Kindred of the Coins. She currently works at cross-purposes to us, and while she may not be allied with Azagath, neither does she work to help us. It can give us no advantage to tell the people of this land that she is a member of Umbar's ruling council.

'Now let us proceed. We have traitors to find and a mission to complete, and I do not like to spend this long away from my city, and away from my other endeavours.'You have come with Sirgon of Lebennin to an upper level of the Citadel of Winds to meet with the Kindred of the Coins.You and Sirgon have been escorted to an upper level of the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Sirgon inside the Citadel of WindsHármelak and other leaders of the Kindred of the Coins await you in a tower room inside the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Hármelak inside the tower roomWithin a tower room inside the Citadel of Winds, the Kindred of the Coins discuss the days to come.Attend your meeting with the Kindred of the CoinsHármelak and other leaders of the Kindred of the Coins await you in a tower room inside the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Hármelak inside the tower roomThe Kindred of the Coins discuss the recent past with you and Sirgon in a tower room in the Citadel of Winds.Listen to the Kindred discuss the disappearance of BalakhâdBelondor wishes to tell you what the Kindred knows concerning Balakhâd's escape from the Citadel of Winds.Talk to Belondor inside the tower roomThe Kindred of the Coins discuss the disappearance of Balakhâd with you and Sirgon in a tower room in the Citadel of Winds.Listen to the Kindred discuss the disappearance of BalakhâdHármelak wishes to discuss with you the road ahead.Talk to Hármelak inside the tower roomThe Kindred of the Coins discuss the mission to pursue Azagath and Nakási.Listen to the Kindred discuss the adventure to comeSirgon has volunteered for the dangerous mission to pursue Azagath and Nakási into the wild lands of the east and south.Talk to Sirgon in the tower roomThe Kindred of the Coins discuss the mission to pursue Azagath and Nakási.Listen to the Kindred discuss the adventure to comeHármelak wishes to address you before you depart.Talk to Hármelak in the tower room'A new adventure begins, ${PLAYER}! The weight of the years has fallen from my shoulders, and I am ready to set foot upon the unknown road once again. Let us prove our mettle and that King Elessar chose his champions and his friends well and ably!''How many hallways and staircases must we take to arrive at our destination, ${PLAYER}? I have already lost the path back to the entrance, despite my best effort to remember it.

'What must the Kindred say to us that they cannot say in Dâr Laja, or in the main hall of this Citadel?''I am pleased the two of you accepted our invitation to meet. We have much to discuss about the days ahead, and I believe the decisions we make here today may affect the fortunes of both Umbar and Gondor.

'The people welcomed my Kindred with glad hearts, and cheered as we cast off the yoke placed upon our city by the Empire of Ordâkh and the Heirs of Castamir. But such a change was not without cost, and the coffers of the city are at a low ebb. I have contributed much of my own fortune to the effort, but even my own great wealth cannot support the city indefinitely.

'War is expensive. Our wish is to spend no further, unless we must. How does Gondor feel on this matter? Does this King Elessar desire peace? He must know the Corsairs of Umbar retain ships enough to make him suffer for any war he begins anew.''The Empire of Ordâkh and its Church of the All-seeing held Umbar in the grip of fear while the Heirs of Castamir carried out their commands, but that fear was founded upon terror of the Dark Lord and his powerful servants. When the great quake sundered his land of Mordor and caused the collapse of his temple, we who watched and waited knew our time had come. The number of our conspiracy was few, but we believed the people would join us when they witnessed the vulnerability of the Empire, and how near the Heirs of Castamir were to defeat. When no vengeful wraith emerged from the ruins of the temple or swept towards us from Mordor, the people knew Umbar could be theirs again.

'With a fleet from the south, Azagath Sea-shadow swept into the Gulf of Umbar. It was poorly-defended now, with much of its power gone to the coast of Gondor, captured or burned. The Umbari rose up in open revolt, thus beginning the Sea-stone Mutiny. Those of the Heirs who resisted were slain without mercy; others either lacked courage or possessed wisdom, and fled. Some of these were Saklaphêl, the widow of Balakhôr the Scourge, and a number of her personal guards. It is believed she hides now among the Shield Isles and seeks to retake the city and her husband's rule, but she has not the numbers.

'Not all of the Heirs were slain or escaped. Before he could take command of a ship and flee the Sail-haven, our forces captured Balakhâd, the twenty-year-old son of Balakhôr. We held him here in the Citadel of Winds, in this tower room, and counted him a valuable hostage.''Only members of the Kindred of the Coins knew the identity of the man we kept in this room, ${PLAYER}. Even the guards did not know. They were told he was awaiting execution for crimes against the city; their loyalty to the Kindred cannot be questioned. One day Balakhâd was safely imprisoned, as he had been for months, and then one day he was not. If the guards can be trusted, how did Balakhâd leave this tower room without being seen?'

Belondor shakes his head.

'The problem is more difficult than that, for the Citadel of Winds stands upon an island. Could he escape onto one of the ships, and flee that way? It is hard to imagine. But neither could he walk past the many guards posted on the island and then across the bridge back to the city without being seen.

'He is not the only person who seems to have disappeared that day. One of Azagath's servants, a water-carrier by the name of Sadûkh, cannot be found. Did he help Balakhâd to escape? And if so, where might he have hidden the son of Balakhôr now? It beggars belief that such an important figure for the Heirsworn can remain hidden for so long.''Azagath hid his true nature from us. None suspected his true allegiance lay with Sauron, and now he seeks to follow the map he took from the Mâkhda Khorbo to some unknown end. I say we cannot know his purpose in this, but can there be any doubt that such a map can lead only to sorrow for the people of Umbar Baharbêl?

'There was a time when Nakási Wave-reaper would not have followed Azagath on such an adventure, but I deem her mind is now clouded by the grief and rage that swirls within her breast. If the map taken by the two of them leads to some weapon of evil, can you say for certainty that it would not be used first against Umbar, and then against Gondor?

'I see two important purposes along the road ahead, ${PLAYER}: first we must prevent Azagath and Nakási from locating the evil they seek. Secondly, we must find Balakhâd, son of Balakhôr, and make him once again our captive. Only then will we reacquire our bargaining power over Saklaphêl and the Heirs of Castamir.

'These twin courses will bring the instruments of our will out of the city and into the wild lands of the east and south.''Are you with me, ${PLAYER}?'

You assure Sirgon that you will stand with him on this adventure, and he smiles broadly.

'I did not doubt it for a moment, my friend! I dare say the Elves will also wish to accompany us. I met each of them only days or weeks ago, but already I know them to be strong and capable, each in their own way. And I witnessed Sigileth's great courage when fortune ill and storm unnatural threw the Wave-hunter onto the rocks of the Shield Isles!

'Who else will accompany us?''Much will depend upon how well you perform upon this adventure, ${PLAYER}. I have not forgotten that the people of my city think highly of you, and believe you should join our Kindred. Let this quest serve as your trial, with Rothog, Belondor, and Khôltekh to serve as your judges. They will assess your performance and how you conduct yourself on behalf of our shared interests: those of Umbar, and those of distant Gondor.

'Prevent Azagath and Nakási from following their map to whatever evil Sauron left behind and making use of it against us. So too should you seek Azagath's former servant Sadûkh, if he seeks to rejoin his master. He may tell you what he has done with Balakhâd, son of Balakhôr the Scourge. If you can recover Balakhâd, alive, we may be able to end the threat posed by the Heirs of Castamir forever... and that will benefit not just Umbar but Gondor as well.

'The lands outside the city contain perils and dangers the like of which few among you have ever faced. It will take some time to prepare the caravan that will take you out of Umbar and into the lands where your prey has vanished. Come to Dâr Laja after this and we will make such preparations as you will need.'You have brought the leaders of Ambarûl, Khûd Zagin, and Imhûlar together in Iridír. Mizâdi has much to do before Girhâzi and Amalíbi trust her or her leadership.Join Mizâdi around the war table.Join Mizâdi around the war tableListen to the conversation.Listen to the conversationSpeak with Mizâdi in the war room.Speak with MizâdiGather the map from near the Subuzûri.Gather the map from near the SubuzûriSpread the map out on the table.Spread the map out on the tableListen to the conversation.Listen to the conversationListen to the conversation.Listen to the conversationSpeak with Mizâdi in the hall.Speak with Mizâdi in the hall'Thank you for coming, friend. It is quite the aid, let me tell you. I know not how to make my words persuade others, I haven't the talent. What's worse, it seems my passion has gotten the better of me again. I wish I had not said what I did to Amalíbi.

'Could you gather the map from near the Subuzûri guard and spread it on the table? Now that we are discussing tactics and troop movements I feel much more in my element.''The alliance proffered here is uneasy, and fragile, but it is there. Let us venture back outside into Iridír. We have preparations to make.'Armed with proof of Shaidal's innocence, you approach Rothog the Storm with your findings.Fight off the ambush awaiting you in Rothog's chambers.Defeat ambushersArmed with proof of Shaidal's innocence, you approach Rothog the Storm with your findings.Speak to Rothog the Storm and watch his reactionSpeak to Shaidal about his task.Speak to Shaidal about his task'I give you my thanks again ${PLAYER}. Your work has been excellent and revealed many problems for me. That being said, I may have work for you in the near future.''${PLAYER}, these rabble! How dare they invade my quarters?! There will be swift vengeance upon those who would do such a thing. I will have my guards take the bodies and feed them to the lions.

'Anyway, you had mentioned that you managed to gather information that might be of interest to me?''I am glad that I have an avenue to gain my freedom, but saddened that this treachery was not enough to gain it. I understand the ruling and will abide by it.

'Ragrekhûl is known to be a dreaded beast, I only hope that I may be capable of capturing the beast.'You, Raphûz, and Ashâmi are distracting the enemy forces from a main assault on Kûr Anzar.Speak with Raphûz to begin the assaultYour assault was successful, but the madness of the cultists weighs on Ashâmi and Raphûz. You should make haste and return to Urmâkh.Speak with Ashâmi to return to Urmâkh'We will do what must be done. Let us fight through the enemy and give the main force the distraction they need to retake parts of the ruins.''What did he mean, 'The Firstborn return from their long slumber?' What evil grows beyond Imhûlar? Let us return to Numûru with haste.'Intrigued by your discovery of a curious wall inside another salt mine tunnel, Amâsu has asked you to escort her there to see it for herself. Girhâzi, who would not want to be left out, is accompanying you.Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should talk to Amâsu.Talk to AmâsuAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should lead them to the odd wall you found.Lead Amâsu and Girhâzi to the odd wallAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should lead them to the odd wall you found.Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. With Girhâzi's help, you have thwarted an attack by giant scorpions. Amâsu would like to talk to you.Talk to AmâsuAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should lead them to the odd wall you found.Lead Amâsu and Girhâzi to the odd wallAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should lead them to the odd wall you found.Amâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. Girhâzi wants to talk to you.Talk to GirhâziAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should lead them to the odd wall you found.Lead Amâsu and Girhâzi to the odd wallAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. You should join them at the odd wall.Join Amâsu and Girhâzi at the wallAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. Amâsu wants to talk to you.Talk to AmâsuAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more, and have led them to the odd wall you found. You should listen to their conversation.Observe Girhâzi and AmâsuAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more, and have led them to the odd wall you found. You should listen to their conversation.Observe Girhâzi and AmâsuAmâsu and Girhâzi have followed you into the salt mine tunnels once more. After leading them to the odd wall you found, they were able to open the secret door, discovering the Dubarâkh. Girhâzi wants to talk to you.Talk to Girhâzi'This is very exciting, ${PLAYER}. I have not been on an adventure in many years! You should have seen me in my younger days. I was quite rough and tumble!

'Lead on, my dear. Do watch your step though, it seems there are a few usan-kûni in here.''Those usan-kûni are quite large! I am glad to have both you and Girhâzi here with me. Let us move quickly though. This does not seem like a place where we should dally.'Are we almost there ${PLAYER}? Amâsu wishes to travel quickly, but I believe we should slow down. She will not tell us if the journey is difficult for her. If we are close, I believe we should walk the rest of the way, for her sake.'

You assure Girhâzi that it is just ahead.'Níkhu, ${PLAYER}, we found it! I am stunned. I confess there was a part of me that believed it would never be found in my lifetime, and yet, here we are. This is a beautiful treasure trove of knowledge. The culture and history of Ambarûl has been preserved for us in this room. This will restore our sense of identity and help us to rebuild, to uphold our independence. Thank you, ${PLAYER}, you have done our people a great service, and we will never forget it.

'I will place guards here to ensure the safety of Dubarâkh, and you are always welcome to return here, should you desire it.''You are quite right that this wall does not look like the others in this mine. Do you truly think it may be a door, though? What do you suppose may open it? This a puzzle indeed!'Raphûz asked you to accompany him to find Ashâmi. He wanted to apologize to the woman and to help her.Raphûz is preparing for battle through the grove to find Ashâmi.Speak with Raphûz to begin the search for AshâmiYou and Raphûz discovered Ashâmai amongst a section of dead trees in the grove. She does not look happy to see you. Approach her and allow Raphûz to explain why you are here.Cautiously approach AshâmiYou approached Ashâmi in the ruined grove. Allow Raphûz and her to speak.Wait for Raphûz and Ashâmi to finish speakingAshâmi is concerned you and Raphûz are over-matched in the fallen grove. She warns that the Alad is a powerful creature and suggests you may not survive this attack.Defeat the Alad of Er-atûrAssist Ashâmi and Raphûz to defeat the AladAshâmi begins the grisly business of collecting a trophy from the Alad. Raphûz shifts nervously.Speak with RaphûzAshâmi finishes her task and she and Raphûz move to speak to one another. Allow them to have their conversation.Allow Ashâmi and Raphûz to finish their discussionAs Ashâmi begins to walk away, Raphûz looks at you excitedly and smiles. You should speak with him.Speak with Raphûz'Prepare yourself. We must use caution and haste as we search for Ashâmi. The reports I received about this dead land speak of fell and wrath-filled spirits. I will take the lead.'Ashâmi scowls.'We survived. I will have an opportunity to speak with her now.''Come, my friend, Shonith awaits.'Raphûz wishes to claim a treasure from a wealthy tomb in Nirgambâr. You agreed to assist him as he searches this place of the dead.In the shadow of an ancient tomb, Raphûz awaits your counsel.Raphûz awaits your counsel and assistance to beginYou ventured deeper into the ruins of Nirgambâr. Raphûz's resolve is holding, but he looks nervous.Raphûz paused his advance and looks in need of reassuranceAfter fighting through the dead, you and Raphûz see the treasure he seeks. A small cadre of guards stands between you and Raphûz's goal.Tell Raphûz you are ready to claim the chestYou fought your way through the Dead at Nirgambâr to obtain a chest containing riches for Raphûz. Raphûz stands near the prize and looks pleased.Speak with Raphûz'I am prepared if you are, my friend. I do not wish to linger near this place any longer than we must. I will admit, there is a sense of dread washing over me.''There is fear in my heart, yes. But your resolve strengthens mine, ${PLAYER}. We will find what we need and I prove my worth to Igbâl. I know this. We should press on.''There, my friend, do you see? A chest. Undoubtedly it holds the treasure we seek. I have not faced such enemies until now and I will not let these few more deter me from this prize.'

Raphûz adjusts his weapon.

'Come, ${PLAYER}. Let us finish this!''The wealth within should command Igbâl's attention. I could not have succeeded in this venture without your aid. Please, visit me at my camp in Jirush. I wish to speak more before I bring this to Igbâl, and prove myself worthy to court his daughter.'Sigênik led you to a secluded location out of sight and earshot of Jirush. He means to test your knowledge here.Sigênik is prepared to administer his test. Speak to him when you are prepared.Speak with Sigênik to begin your testSigênik awaits your response. He asked if Igbâl is the Elder who directly supports the rebellion in Jirush. You should give him your response.Tell Sigênik <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, Igbâl is the elder allied to the rebellionTell Sigênik <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, Igbâl is not the elder allied to the rebellionYou provided your answer to Sigênik's question about Igbâl. Speak with him again to continue your test.Speak with Sigênik to continue your testSigênik awaits your response. He asked if Zidemel is the elder who directly supports the rebellion in Jirush. You should give him your response.Tell Sigênik <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, Zidemel is the elder allied to the rebellionTell Sigênik <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, Zidemel is not the elder allied to the rebellionYou provided your answer to Sigênik's question about Zidemel. Speak with him again to continue your test.Speak with Sigênik to continue your testSigênik awaits your response. He asked if Nangar is the elder who directly supports the rebellion in Jirush. You should give him your response.Tell Sigênik <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, Nangar is the elder allied to the rebellionTell Sigênik <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, Nangar is not the elder allied to the rebellionYou provided your answer to Sigênik's question about Nangar. Speak with him again to continue your test.Speak with Sigênik to continue your testSigênik awaits your response. He asked if Malgat is the elder who directly supports the rebellion in Jirush. You should give him your response.Tell Sigênik <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, Malgat is the elder allied to the rebellionTell Sigênik <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, Malgat is not the elder allied to the rebellionYou provided all of your answers to Sigênik's questions. Speak with him to learn your judgement.'We should return. It is better that Ordâkhai eyes do not see us speaking.''As I said before, one of the Elders allies with our cause, and the other three are not our enemy. I will ask you only a few questions, and your honest answer will prove your value to us.'

He pauses.

'I will begin. Igbâl, the merchant who employs the translator... is he allied with our rebellion?''Zidemel, the man whose fervour for a prophecy, is he allied with our rebellion?''Nangar, the keeper of the walls, is he allied with our cause?''Malgat, the Elder hunter who stocks the larder and turns a profit from the desert fauna, is he allied with our rebellion?'Nangar's efforts to find Ordâkhai yielded an unexpected opportunity. A courier will carry a message meant for the captain of the Ordâkhai camp in the southern crags. He asks you to intercept the courier and seize the letters.Nangar suggested the courier carrying orders to the south will pass a ruined khanâg along the eastern road from Jirush. He suggested you ambush the courier and his escort there and seize the parcel he carries.Defeat the CourierYou recovered a single missive, written in Ordâkhin, from the courier. Take the letter to Nangar in Jirush.Nangar asked you to trust him and deliver the letter you recovered to Galamê. Galamê can, and will translate the letter.Nangar's words were true. Galamê made the translation quietly and did not ask how it was obtained. He handed a translation back to you alongside the original document. Return the messages to Nangar in Jirush.'Our attack brought fortune, ${PLAYER}. I saw a schedule of deliveries meant for the Ordâkhai encampment in the south-east. We have an opportunity to intercept their courier, steal the information they mean to share, and gain advantages where once there was none. For this, I am grateful. Now I must ask you to perform another service.

'Track down the courier along the road east from Jirush. You should set an ambush south and east of the ruined khanâg. Collect whatever you can from the courier and return their parcels to me.''The khanâg is on the east road out of Jirush. There should be plenty of spots to prepare an ambush for the courier. Make haste and recover what they carry.''This is written in Ordâkhin? I cannot understand what is on this papyrus.

'Now it is time for you to trust me. Take the letter to Galamê. He will translate it for you. He will be discreet, I am certain. Return to me when you have the translation.'Galamê arches a brow as you hand him the papyrus. He withdraws a quill and quickly writes a translation onto the page before passing the papyrus back.

'Return this to Nangar. It is not what he wanted. Still, the tree he shakes may yet yield fruit.''Galamê is correct on both counts. This letter is not as I expected. However, we can use the contents to our advantage.'Corudan has returned after months away, and he desires to catch up with lost friends.Corudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.Talk to Corudan and go with him on one more journeyCorudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.Talk to Corudan at the Harbour Warden's tower'Your mission has concluded, ${PLAYER}, and I am pleased it has ended happily! Now that it has, I can confess to you something.

'The physical hurt of the wound I suffered outside Helm's Deep pained me greatly, even as it would in time be healed by Leafshade's ministrations. But one pain remained even afterward: the pain of loss, of not knowing what befell my friends. As my body recovered, my heart dwelled on the uncertainty of what might be happening even then to you, and to Gléowine, and to Horn, and to Nona.

'Now that Thorongil of Pinnath Gelin has been rescued from the Kindred of the Coins... will you take one last journey with me, ${PLAYER}?''In the space before your adventures continue, my friend, I would ask to take one more journey with you.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Thank you, my friend.'Corudan has returned after months away, and he desires to catch up with lost friends.Corudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.Talk to Corudan and go with him to see a lost friendCorudan is by the Harbour Warden's tower.Talk to Corudan at the Harbour Warden's tower'Your mission has concluded, ${PLAYER}, and I am pleased it has ended happily! Now that it has, I can confess to you something.

'The physical hurt of the wound I suffered outside Helm's Deep pained me greatly, even as it would in time be healed by Leafshade's ministrations. But one pain remained even afterward: the pain of loss, of not knowing what befell my friends. As my body recovered, my heart dwelled on the uncertainty of what might be happening even then to you, and to Gléowine, and to Horn, and to Nona. I sorrow now to know that Horn perished on the Pelennor Fields... but other of our friends survive, and my heart goes out to them.

'Now that Thorongil of Pinnath Gelin has been rescued from the Kindred of the Coins... will you take one last journey with me, ${PLAYER}?''In the space before your adventures continue, my friend, I would ask to take one more journey with you.'

<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>'Thank you, my friend.'Shukûri in the Gorge of Woe has asked you to scout out the camps to the north near Utug-bûr and defeat any Orcs you find there.Shukûri has asked that you go to Sar-kidul and Ab-dâna to the north near Utug-bûr to see what you find and defeat any Orcs you encounter there.Defeat Orcs in Sar-kidul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orcs in Ab-dâna (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Shukûri in the Gorge of Woe to inform her you have reduced the number of Orcs in the camps near Utug-bûr.Return to Shukûri'${CLASS}, I need your help dealing with the dangers emerging from the demon-pit.

'Their numbers are many and we must put a stop to their advances. To the north of here, near Utug-bûr, you will find two of their camps by the entrance. Sar-kidul to the north-west and Ab-dâna to the south-east of it.

'If you are willing, I ask that you travel there and see what you can discover. Defeating any Orcs you see would be welcomed as well.''I am glad to see you have returned safely.'

You inform Shukûri of what you have seen at the camps near Utug-bûr.

'That confirms my fears. The threat here is overwhelming and may even threaten Gondor if we cannot halt or even slow their advance.

'I thank you for your help. We now know more about our foes.'Galâmka has information on the current state of Urash Dâr.Tell Galâmka <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, that you are not frightened and that you wish to help the people of Urash Dâr.Tell Galâmka <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>Speak with Galâmka now that he knows you are not too scared to help.Speak with Galâmka'All of Urash Dâr has been overrun by Orcs, and amongst them are these demons from Utug-bûr... a monstrous evil.

'The people here could use all of the help that be can managed, but I assure you it is a dangerous undertaking. I would understand if you are too frightened to help.''Aha! I am glad that you are so eager to help our cause!'

Galâmka laughs.

'As I have said, there are people from all over here. If you truly wish to help, I ask that you speak with them as they could use your help as well.'The Mâkhda Khorbo, the seat of adherents to the All-seeing eye, crumbled when the Dark Lord fell. Yet, within the Temple of Ash and Blood, ancient evil stalks the halls, seeps into every stone, and infests every living thing within; what reason is there to trespass here? You intend to discover why the Kindred of Coin came to this place.Azagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred.

Defeat Azagath's crew and pursue the Kindred through the fallen temple.Defeat Azagath's Sea-Shadow and his crewAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred.

Defeat Belondor and his crew to pursue Azagath through the fallen temple.Defeat Belondor and his crewAzagath Sea-shadow, Nakási Wave-reaper, and Belondor took their crews through the tunnel ahead. Pursue them and defeat the Kindred.

Defeat Umshûra the Glutton.Defeat Umshûra the GluttonAzagath Sea-shadow and Nakâsi Wave-reaper are missing. Belondor returns to Umbar Baharbêl in disgrace and you defeated Umshûra the Glutton, a foul denizen of the deep.

You have completed Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 1.

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You may keep this quest in your Quest Log to access each of the encounters in Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo, or you may abandon it to reset your progress. This quest will automatically reset on Monday, Thursday, and Saturday.</rgb>Completed: Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo -- Tier 1The woman looks at you anxiously.

'I know I ought not to be here. The Kindred swore us away. I saw three of them though. They pulled their launches up on the shore and entered this tunnel with their crews. They went straight on ahead.

'I know I'm not supposed to be here, but I know a bit about the temple. I used to work a dock here in my younger days. If you need to get deeper into the ruins, I can help you.

'If you can tell me the last room you entered, I can show you a shortcut through the nearby tunnels.'

